
#bookname=mw-1872 (sa-en)
#stripmethod=keep
#sametypesequence=h
#description=Data from https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de/ as on 2026-06-24

अ|अं|अः
अ 1. अ, the first letter of the alphabet; the<BR>first short vowel inherent in consonants.<BR>—अ-कार,<BR>अस्, m. the letter or sound अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ 2. अ, ind. an interjection of pity (Ah!).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ 3. अ (before a vowel अन्), a prefix cor-<BR>responding to Gr. ἀ, ἀν Lat. in, Goth. and Germ. un,<BR>Eng. in or un, and having a negative or privative or<BR>depreciative sense; e. g. एक one, अन्-एक not one;<BR>अन्त end, अन्-अन्त endless; पश्यत् seeing, अ-पश्यत्<BR>not seeing. Sometimes this prefix denotes com-<BR>parison. It is occasionally an expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ 4. अ, the base of some pronouns and pro-<BR>nom. forms; (substituted for इदम्, in अस्य, अत्र, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ 5. अ, the augment prefixed to the root<BR>in the formation of the imperfect, aorist, and con-<BR>ditional tenses, by some considered as connected with<BR>3. अ, and by others as connected with 4. अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ 6. अ, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu (especially as the<BR>first of the three sounds in the sacred syllable ॐ), also<BR>of Brahmā, Śiva, and Vaiśvānara; (अम्), n. Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अऋणिन्
अऋणिन् अ-ऋणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, free from debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश्
अंश् अंश्, cl. 10. P. अंशयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>divide, distribute; also occasionally A.<BR>अंशयते; also अंशापयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश|अंशः
अंश, अस्, m. a share, portion, part, party;<BR>partition, inheritance; a share of booty; earnest<BR>money; a fraction; the denominator of one; a<BR>degree of lat. or long.; N. of an Āditya; the<BR>shoulder or shoulder-blade, more usually spelt अंस,<BR>q. v. [cf. Old Germ. ahsala; Mod. Germ. achsel;<BR>Lat. axilla.].<BR>—अंश-करण, अम्, n. act of dividing.<BR>—अंश-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, one who has a share, an heir, a<BR>co-heir.<BR>—अंश-वत्, आन्, m. a species of the Soma plant.<BR>—अंश-सवर्णन, अम्, n. reduction of fractions.<BR>—अंश-स्वर, अस्, m. the key-note.<BR>—अंश-हर,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, or अंश-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who<BR>takes a share, a sharer.<BR>—अंशांश (˚श-अं˚), अस्, m.<BR>part of a portion (of a deity), a secondary incarnation.<BR>—अंशांशि, ind. share by share.<BR>—अंशावतरण<BR>(˚श-अव्˚), अम्, n. descent of parts of the deities;<BR>partial incarnation; title of sections 64 — 67 of the<BR>first book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशक|अंशकं|अंशकः
अंशक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, having a share; m. f. a<BR>co-heir, a relative; m. a share; n. a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशन|अंशनं
अंशन, अम्, n. the act of sharing or dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशनीय
अंशनीय or अंशयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितृ
अंशयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a divider, sharer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशल|अंशलः
अंशल. See अंसल next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशित
अंशित, अस्, आ, अम्, divided, shared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशिन्
अंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a sharer, co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशु|अंशुः
अंशु, उस्, m. a filament, especially of the Soma<BR>plant; end of a thread; a minute particle; a point or<BR>end; a garment, decoration; a ray, light, the sun; N.<BR>of a Ṛṣi or of a prince.<BR>—अंशु-जाल, अम्, n. a collec-<BR>tion of rays, a blaze of light.<BR>—अंशु-धर, अस्, m. the<BR>bearer of rays, the sun.<BR>—अंशु-पट्ट, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of cloth.<BR>—अंशु-पति, इस्, or -भर्तृ, ता, m. the<BR>lord of rays, the sun.<BR>—अंशु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, fibrous,<BR>rich in filaments; radiant, luminous; pointed; (आन्),<BR>m. the sun, the moon; N. of various persons, especially<BR>of a prince of the solar race, son of A-samañjas, grand-<BR>son of Sagara; (ती), f. the celestial river Yamunā; a<BR>plant, Hedysarum Gangeticum.<BR>—अंशुमति-फला, f.<BR>a plant, Musa Paradisiaca.<BR>—अंशु-माला, f. a garland<BR>of light, halo.<BR>—अंशु-मालिन्, ई, m. the sun.<BR>—अंशु-<BR>वाण, अस्, m. having rays for arrows, the sun.<BR>—अंशु-<BR>हस्त, अस्, m. having rays in his hand, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुक|अंशुकं
अंशुक, अम्, n. a leaf; cloth; fine or white cloth;<BR>muslin, an upper garment; a mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुल|अंशुलः
अंशुल, अस्, आ, अम्, radiant; (अस्), m., N. of the<BR>sage Cāṇakya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश्य
अंश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस्
अंस् अंस्, cl. 10. P. अंसयति, &c., = अंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस|अंसः
अंस अंस, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अम्), the shoulder,<BR>shoulder-blade; N. of a king; a share, see अंश;<BR>(औ), m. du. the two shoulders or angles of an altar<BR>[cf. Goth. amsa; Gr. ἄσιλλα Lat. humerus,<BR>ansa].<BR>—अंस-कूट, अस्, m. a bull's hump, the pro-<BR>tuberance between the shoulders of the Indian ox.<BR>—अंस-त्र, अम्, n. armour to protect the shoulder;<BR>a bow.<BR>—अंस-ध्री, f. a cooking vessel(?).<BR>—अंस-<BR>फलक, अस्, m. upper part of the spine.<BR>—अंस-<BR>भार or अंसे-भार, अस्, m. a yoke or burden put<BR>upon the shoulder.<BR>—अंस-भारिक or अंसे-भारिक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, or अंस-भारिन् or अंसे-भारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, bearing a yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसल|अंसलः
अंसल, अस्, आ, अम्, lusty, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस्य
अंस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्
अंह् अंह् (allied to अङ्घ्), cl. 1. A. अंहते,<BR>हितुम्, to go, set out, commence; to ap-<BR>proach: cl. 10. P. अंहयति, to send; to speak; to<BR>shine. [The rt. अंह् seems to have had originally<BR>another meaning, viz. to press together, strangle; =<BR>Gr. ἄγχω]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहति|अंहतिः
अंहति, इस्, f. (probably fr. the preceding rt., said<BR>to be here a substitute for हन्), anxiety, distress,<BR>trouble, illness [cf. Lat. ango]; a gift, (in this sense<BR>also अंहती, f.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहस्
अंहस्, n. (said to be connected with rt. अम्),<BR>anxiety, trouble; sin [cf. अघ, आगस्; Gr. ἄχνυμαι<BR>ἄχος, ἄγος].<BR>—अंहसस्-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of<BR>the perplexity, i. e. an intercalary month.<BR>—अंहस्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, sinful.<BR>—अंहो-मुच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>delivering from distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहिति|अंहितिः
अंहिति, इस्, f. a gift, donation. See अंहति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहु
अंहु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. strait, narrow; (उस्), m.,<BR>N. of an Asura; (उ), n. anxiety, distress; Pudendum<BR>Muliebre [cf. Gr. ἐγγύς Goth. aggvus; Lat.<BR>angustus, anxius, &c.].<BR>—अंहु-भेदी, f. having<BR>a narrow slit, having the pudendum divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहुर
अंहुर, अस्, आ, अम्, straitened, distressed; sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहूरण
अंहूरण, अस्, आ, अम्, distressing, sinful; (अम्),<BR>n. sin, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहोयु
अंहोयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. troublesome; freed from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रि|अंह्रिः
अंह्रि, इस्, m. a foot, the root of a tree [cf.<BR>अङ्घ्रि].<BR>—अंह्रि-प, अस्, m. a tree (foot-drinker).<BR>—अंह्रि-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a part of the foot between<BR>the ancle and the heel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्
अक् अक्, cl. 1. P. अकति, अकितुम्, to move<BR>tortuously, like a snake [cf. Gr. ἀγκή<BR>ἀγκαί, ἀγκών Lat. angulus]. Compare rt. अग्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक|अकं
अक, अस्, आ, अम्, moving tortuously; (अम्), n. pain,<BR>trouble, sin (also derived from अ, not + क, happiness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकच|अकचः
अकच अ-कच, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of hair,<BR>bald; (अस्), m., N. of Ketu, the dragon's tail or descend-<BR>ing node, the symbol of which is a headless trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकण्टक
अकण्टक अ-कण्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>thorns, troubles, difficulties, or enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकत्थन
अकत्थन अ-कत्थन, अस्, आ, अम्, not boastful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथ्य|अकथ्यः
अकथ्य अ-कथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unspeakable;<BR>not to be uttered or mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठ|अकनिष्ठः
अकनिष्ठ अ-कनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, not the<BR>youngest; elder, superior; (अस्), m. a deified Buddhist<BR>saint, Buddha.<BR>—अकनिष्ठ-ग, अस्, m. Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकन्या
अकन्या अ-कन्या, f. no virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकपीवत्|अकपीवन्त्
अकपीवत् अकपीवत्, आन्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पित|अकंपित|अकम्पितः
अकम्पित अ-कम्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, unshaken,<BR>firm; (अस्), m., N. of a Jaina saint, a pupil of the last<BR>Tīrtha-kara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्प्य
अ-कम्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर
अकर अ-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, handless, maimed;<BR>exempt from tax or duty, privileged; not acting; (आ),<BR>f. Emblic Myrobalan, Phyllanthus Emblica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरण|अकरणं
अकरण अ-करण, अम्, n. absence of action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणि|अकरणिः
अ-करणि, इस्, f. non-accomplishment, failure, disap-<BR>pointment (used in imprecations, e. g. तस्याकरणिर्<BR>एवास्तु, may he experience a failure !).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणीय
अ-करणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरुण|अकरुणः
अकरुण अ-करुण, अस्, आ, अम्, merciless, re-<BR>lentless.<BR>—अकरुण-त्व, अम्, n. harshness, cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्कश|अकर्कशः|अकर्क्कश
अकर्कश अ-कर्कश, अस्, आ, अम्, not hard,<BR>not rugged, soft, tender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्ण|अकर्णः|अकर्ण्ण
अकर्ण अ-कर्ण or अ-कर्णक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>without ears, deaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्ण्य
अ-कर्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not fit for the ears; not in<BR>the ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्णधार
अकर्णधार अ-कर्णधार, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>a helmsman, destitute of a pilot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तन|अकर्त्तन|अकर्त्तनः
अकर्तन अ-कर्तन, अस्, m, a dwarf (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्तृ|अकर्त्तृ
अकर्तृ अ-कर्तृ, ता, m. not an agent; an<BR>inferior agent.<BR>—अकर्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. condition of an<BR>inferior agent, a subordinate station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मन्|अकर्म्मन्
अकर्मन् अ-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, without work,<BR>idle; inefficient; disqualified for performing essential<BR>rites, destitute of good works; (in grammar) intransitive;<BR>(अ), n. absence of work; absence of essential observ-<BR>ances; improper work, crime.<BR>—अकर्म-भोग, अस्, m.<BR>renunciation of self-righteousness; enjoyment of free-<BR>dom from the fruits of action.<BR>—अकर्मान्वित (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, unoccupied, disqualified; criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मक|अकर्म्मक
अ-कर्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, (in grammar) intransitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्मण्य|अकर्म्मण्य|अकर्म्मण्यं
अ-कर्मण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, improper to be done;<BR>unfit for work; inefficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल
अकल अ-कल, अस्, आ, अम्, not in parts, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्क
अकल्क अ-कल्क, अस्, आ, अम्, free from sedi-<BR>ment; pure; sinless; (आ), f. moonlight.<BR>—अकल्क-<BR>ता, f. honesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्कन|अकल्कनः
