अकल्मष
अकल्मष अ-कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, sinless,<BR>faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्माष
अकल्माष अ-कल्माष, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of the fourth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्य|अकल्यः
अकल्य अ-कल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unwell, ill, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्याण|अकल्याणं
अ-कल्याण, अस्, आ, अम्, not prosperous, inauspicious;<BR>(अम्), n. adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकव
अकव अ-कव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. कु, q. v.),<BR>Ved. not contemptible, not bad.<BR>—अ-कवारि (˚व-<BR>अरि), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. not contemptible as an enemy,<BR>or to his enemies, or in his enemies; not having<BR>weak enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकवच
अकवच अ-कवच, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. without<BR>a coat of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0001-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकवि
अकवि अ-कवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. unwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकस्मात्
अकस्मात् अ-कस्मात्, ind. without a why or<BR>a wherefore, accidentally, suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्ड|अकांड
अकाण्ड अ-काण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘without a trunk,’<BR>causeless, unexpected.<BR>—अकाण्ड-पात-जात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dying as soon as born.<BR>—अकाण्ड-शूल, अम्,<BR>n. sudden attack of colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डे|अकांडे
अ-काण्डे, ind. causelessly, unexpectedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकातर
अकातर अ-कातर, अस्, आ, अम्, not down-<BR>hearted, cheerful, hearty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाम
अकाम अ-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, without desire<BR>or affection, without intention; unintentional, re-<BR>luctant; (in grammar) the Sandhi which causes the<BR>dropping of a final र् before a succeeding र्; (अस्), m.<BR>absence of desire or affection.<BR>—अ-काम-कर्शन,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. not disappointing desires.<BR>—अकाम-तस्,<BR>ind. unintentionally, unwillingly.<BR>—अकाम-ता, f.<BR>freedom from desire or affection or intention.<BR>—अ-<BR>काम-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, not smitten with desire or<BR>affection; free from desire, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकामिन्
अ-कामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, the same as अ-काम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाय|अकायः
अकाय अ-काय, अस्, आ, अम्, incorporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारण|अकारणं
अकारण अ-कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, causeless;<BR>(अम्), n. absence of a cause; ind. causelessly.<BR>—अ-का-<BR>रणोत्पन्न (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced spon-<BR>taneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारिन्
अ-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, inactive, not performing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्णवेष्टकिक
अकार्णवेष्टकिक अ-कार्णवेष्टकिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>not adapted for ear-rings. See कर्ण-वेष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्य|अकार्य्य|अकार्य्यं
अकार्य अ-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be done,<BR>impracticable, improper; (अम्), n. a criminal action.<BR>—अकार्य-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, an evil-doer; one who<BR>neglects his duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्ष्ण्य
अकार्ष्ण्य अ-कार्ष्ण्य, अम्, n. absence of<BR>blackness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाल|अकालः
अकाल अ-काल, अस्, m. a wrong or bad or<BR>inauspicious time; (अस्, आ, अम्), unseasonable.<BR>—अ-<BR>काल-कुष्माण्ड, अस्, m. a pumpkin produced out<BR>of season; a useless birth.<BR>—अकाल-कुसुम, अम्,<BR>n. a flower blossoming out of season.<BR>—अकाल-ज or<BR>अकाल-जात or अ-कालोत्पन्न (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>born or produced at a wrong time, unseasonable.<BR>—अकाल-जलदोदय (˚द-उद्˚) or अकाल-मेघो-<BR>दय (˚घ-उद्˚), अस्, m. unseasonable rise or clouds; a<BR>mist.<BR>—अकाल-वेला, f. unseasonable or unusual time.<BR>—अकाल-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, unable to bide one's time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाल्य
अ-काल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unseasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिञ्चन|अकिंचन|अकिञ्चनः
अकिञ्चन अ-किञ्चन, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>anything, utterly destitute, poor; disinterested; (अम्),<BR>n. that which is nothing, or worth nothing.<BR>—अ-<BR>किञ्चन-ता, f. voluntary poverty (as the duty of a<BR>Jaina ascetic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिञ्चनिमन्|अकिंचनिमन्
अ-किञ्चनिमन्, आ, m. destitution, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकितव
अकितव अ-कितव, अस्, m. no gambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिल्विष|अकिल्विषः
अकिल्विष अ-किल्विष, अस्, आ, अम्, sinless,<BR>faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकीर्त्ति|अकीर्ति|अकीर्तिः|अकीर्त्तिः
अकीर्त्ति अ-कीर्त्ति, इस्, f. bad repute.<BR>—अकीर्त्ति-<BR>कर, अस्, आ, अम्, disreputable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुण्ठ|अकुंठ
अकुण्ठ अ-कुण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, not blunted<BR>or worn out; fresh, vigorous, fixed.<BR>—अ-कुण्ठ-<BR>धिष्ण्य, अम्, n. heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुण्ठित|अकुंठित
अ-कुण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, = अकुण्ठ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुतस्
अकुतस् अ-कुतस्, ind. (usually found in<BR>composition), not from anywhere or any cause.<BR>—अ-<BR>कुतश्-चल, अस्, m. not moveable from any cause;<BR>a title of Śiva.<BR>—अ-कुतो-भय, अस्, आ, अम्, not afraid<BR>or threatened from any quarter, secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुत्र
अ-कुत्र or अ-कुत्रा, ind., Ved. nowhere, i. e. astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुत्सित
अकुत्सित अ-कुत्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, unreproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुध्र्यञ्च्|अकुध्र्यंच्
अकुध्र्यञ्च् अ-कुध्र्यञ्च्, अन्, ध्रीची, अक् (कु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">Page0002-b+ 68</a>]<BR>ध्रि for कुध for कुह = कुत्र), Ved. going no-<BR>where, coming to nothing; (Sāy.) fruitless, worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुप्य|अकुप्यं
अकुप्य अ-कुप्य, अम्, n. ‘not base metal,’<BR>gold or silver; any base metal, (see 3. अ at end.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुमार
अकुमार अ-कुमार, अस्, m. not a boy; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुल|अकुलः
अकुल अ-कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, not of a good<BR>family, low; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of<BR>Pārvatī.<BR>—अकुल-ता, f. lowness of family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुलीन
अ-कुलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, not of a good family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुशल
अकुशल अ-कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, inauspicious,<BR>evil; not clever; (अम्), n. evil, an inauspicious or<BR>evil word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुसीद
अकुसीद अ-कुसीद, अस्, आ, अम्, not wishing<BR>for interest or gain; (also अ-कुशीद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुसुम
अकुसुम अ-कुसुम, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of<BR>flowers or blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुह
अकुह अ-कुह, अस्, m. no deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूपार|अकूपारः
अकूपार अ-कू-पार, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably fr.<BR>अकू for अ-कु, not bad, not contemptible, and पार,<BR>opposite shore or limit), having a good issue or effect;<BR>unbounded; (अस्), m. the sea; the sun; the king of<BR>tortoises, who upholds the world; any tortoise or turtle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूवार
अ-कूवार = अ-कू-पार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूर्च|अकूर्चः|अकूर्च्च|अकूर्च्चः
अकूर्च अ-कूर्च, अस्, आ, अम्, guileless; (अस्),<BR>m. Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृच्छ्र
अकृच्छ्र अ-कृच्छ्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. absence<BR>of difficulty; facility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृच्छ्रिन्
अ-कृच्छ्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, free from trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत|अकृतं
अकृत अ-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, undone, un-<BR>performed; not made, uncreated; not prepared, not<BR>ready, incomplete; one who has done no works;<BR>(अम्), n. an unperformed act; an unheard-of action<BR>or crime; (आ), f. a daughter not placed on a level with<BR>sons.<BR>—अकृत-कारम्, ind. as has not been done be-<BR>fore.<BR>—अकृत-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, ungrateful.<BR>—अकृत-<BR>ज्ञ-ता, f. ingratitude.<BR>—अकृत-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having an unformed mind.<BR>—अकृतबुद्धि-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. ignorance.<BR>—अकृत-व्रण, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an expounder of the Purāṇas.<BR>—अकृतात्मन् (˚त-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having an unformed mind; not yet identi-<BR>fied with the supreme spirit.<BR>—अकृतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having one's object unaccomplished unsuc-<BR>cessful.<BR>—अ-कृतास्त्र (˚त-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, unpractised<BR>in arms.<BR>—अ-कृतैनस् (˚त-एन्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, innocent.<BR>—अकृतोद्वाह (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतिन्
अ-कृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, unfit for work, clumsy.<BR>—अकृति-त्व, अम्, n. unfitness for work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्य
अ-कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be done, criminal;<BR>(अम्), n. crime.<BR>—अकृत्य-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, evil-doer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्त
अकृत्त अ-कृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, uncut, unimpaired.<BR>—अकृत्त-रुच्, क्, क्, क्, possessing unimpaired splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्रिम|अकृत्रिमं
अकृत्रिम अ-कृत्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, inartificial,<BR>unfeigned, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्स्न
अकृत्स्न अ-कृत्स्न, अस्, आ, अम्, incomplete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृप|अकृपः
अकृप अ-कृप, अस्, आ, अम्, merciless, unkind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृपण|अकृपणः
अकृपण अ-कृपण, अस्, आ, अम्, not miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृश
अकृश अ-कृश, अस्, आ, अम्, not slender or<BR>emaciated; strong, full.<BR>—अ-कृश-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, ईस्, इ,<BR>enjoying full prosperity.<BR>—अ-कृशाश्व (˚श-अश्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृषीवल
अकृषीवल अ-कृषीवल, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>agricultural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्ट
अकृष्ट अ-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, unploughed,<BR>untilled; not drawn.<BR>—अकृष्ट-पच्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ripening in unploughed land, growing wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्णकर्मन्|अकृष्णकर्म्मन्
अकृष्णकर्मन् अ-कृष्ण-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, free<BR>from black deeds, guiltless, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेतन
अकेतन अ-केतन, अस्, आ, अम्, houseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेतु
अकेतु अ-केतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. shapeless,<BR>unrecognisable; (Sāy.) unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेश|अकेशः
अकेश अ-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोट|अकोटः
अकोट अ-कोट, अस्, m. the Areca or Betel-<BR>nut palm, (‘without a bend.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोपन
अकोपन अ-कोपन, अस्, आ, अम्, not irascible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोविद|अकोविदः
अकोविद अ-कोविद, अस्, आ, अम्, unwise, stupid,<BR>ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकौशल
अकौशल अ-कौशल, अम्, n. want of dexte-<BR>rity or skill; evil [cf. अ-कुशल].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्का
अक्का अक्का, f. a mother. [Supposed to be<BR>a term of foreign origin; cf. Lat. Acca.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त 1. अक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (part. of rt. अञ्च् or अञ्ज्<BR>in the sense ‘to go’), gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त 2. अक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (part. of rt. अञ्ज्),<BR>smeared over; diffused; bedaubed, tinged, characterized.<BR>It is often the last part of a compound word; as, रक्ताक्त,<BR>tinged with red or blood; (अम्), n. oil, ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ता
अक्ता, f., Ved. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्तु|अक्तुः
अक्तु, उस्, f. (m. ?), Ved. ointment; tinge, ray, light,<BR>star (?); dark tinge, darkness, night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्तोस्
अक्तोस्, अक्तुभिस्, ind., Ved. at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त्वा
अक्त्वा (ind. part. of rt. अञ्ज्), having besmeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्न
अक्न अक्न, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अञ्च्), bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्र|अक्रः
1. अक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. violent [Lat. acer?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्र|अक्रः
अक्र 2. अ-क्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 3. अ and rt. 1.<BR>कृ ?), Ved. inactive, bootless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रतु
अक्रतु अ-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. destitute of will<BR>or energy; powerless, foolish; (Sāy.) without sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रम|अक्रमः
अक्रम अ-क्रम, अस्, m. want of order,<BR>confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रविहस्त
अक्रविहस्त अ-क्रवि-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>not having bloody hands; (Sāy.) not having nig-<BR>gardly hands, not close-fisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रव्याद|अक्रव्यादः
अक्रव्याद अ-क्रव्याद, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-क्र-<BR>व्याद्, त्, त्, त्, not carnivorous, not eating flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रान्त|अक्रांत
अक्रान्त अ-क्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unpassed, un-<BR>surpassed, unconquered; (आ), f. the Egg plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रिय|अक्रियः
अक्रिय अ-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, without works;<BR>inactive, torpid; abstaining from religious rites; good<BR>for nothing; (आ), f. inactivity; neglect of duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रीडत्|अक्रीडन्त्
अक्रीडत् अ-क्रीडत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, not playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रूर|अक्रूरः
अक्रूर अ-क्रूर, अस्, आ, अम्, not cruel, gentle;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Kṛṣṇa's paternal uncle and friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोध|अक्रोधः
अक्रोध अ-क्रोध, अस्, m. suppression of<BR>anger, one of the chief virtues among Hindūs; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), free from anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोधन|अक्रोधनः
अ-क्रोधन, अस्, आ, अम्, free from anger; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a prince, son of Ayutāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लम
अक्लम अ-क्लम, अस्, m. freedom from fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिका
अक्लिका अक्लिका, f. the Indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्ट
अक्लिष्ट अ-क्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, untroubled;<BR>undisturbed; unwearied.<BR>—अक्लिष्ट-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>or अक्लिष्ट-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, unwearied in action.<BR>—अक्लिष्ट-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, unwearied in keeping<BR>religious vows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेश|अक्लेशं|अक्लेशः
अ-क्लेश, अस्, m. freedom from trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेद्य
अक्लेद्य अ-क्लेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, incapable of<BR>moisture, not to be wetted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्
अक्ष् अक्ष् (probably not a simple rt.,<BR>perhaps a kind of old Desid. form of rt.<BR>1. अश्), cl. 1. P. अक्षति, cl. 5. अक्ष्णोति, आनक्ष,<BR>अक्षिष्यति, अक्ष्यति, आक्षीत्, अक्षितुम् or अष्टुम्,<BR>to reach; to pass through, penetrate, pervade, embrace;<BR>to accumulate (to form the cube ?): Caus. अक्षयति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-a" target="_blank">Page0003-a+ 79</a>]<BR>यितुम्, आचिक्षत्, to cause to pervade: Desid. अचि-<BR>क्षिषति or अचिक्षति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0002-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष 1. अक्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. अश् or अज्?),<BR>an axle, axis, pivot, (in this sense also अम्, n.); a<BR>wheel, car, cart; pole of a car; the beam of a balance<BR>or string which holds the pivot of the beam; a snake;<BR>terrestrial latitude; the lower part of the temples<BR>[cf. Lat. axis; Gr. ἄξων Old Germ. ahsa; Mod.<BR>Germ. Achse; Lith. assis].<BR>—अक्ष-कर्ण, अस्, m.<BR>the hypotenuse, especially of the triangle formed with<BR>the gnomon of a dial and its shadow; (in astronomy)<BR>argument of the latitude.<BR>—अक्ष-ज, अस्, m. a dia-<BR>mond; a thunderbolt; a N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अक्ष-धुर्,<BR>ऊर्, f. the yoke attached to the fore part of the pole of<BR>a car.<BR>—अक्ष-धूर्तिल, अस्, m. a bull, an ox, i. e.<BR>yoked to the pole of a cart.<BR>—अक्ष-पीडा, f.,<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>—अक्ष-भाग, अस्, m. a degree of<BR>latitude.<BR>—अक्ष-भार, अस्, m. cart-load, carriage-<BR>load.<BR>—अक्षांस (˚ष-अं˚), अस्, m. a degree of<BR>latitude.<BR>—अक्षाग्र (˚ष-अग्˚), अम्, n. the end of<BR>an axle; the anterior end of the pole of a car; an<BR>axle.<BR>—अक्षाग्र-कील or -कीलक, अस्, m. a linch-<BR>pin; the pin which fastens the yoke to the pole.<BR>—अक्षा-नह्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. tied to a cart or its pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष 2. अक्ष, अस्, m. (said to be from rt. 1.<BR>अश्, a die for playing with; a cube; a seed of which<BR>rosaries are made (in compound words, like इन्द्रा-<BR>क्ष, रुद्राक्ष); a shrub producing that seed (Eleo-<BR>carpus Ganitrus); a weight called कर्ष, equal to 16<BR>māṣas; Beleric Myrobalan (Terminalia Belerica), the<BR>seed of which is used as a die; (अम्), n. sochal salt;<BR>blue vitriol (from its crystallized shape).<BR>—अक्ष-<BR>कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in dice.<BR>—अक्ष-ग्लह,<BR>अस्, m. gambling, playing at dice.<BR>—अक्ष-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, skilled in gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-तत्त्व, अम्, n.<BR>science of dice.<BR>—अक्षतत्त्व-विद्, त्, त्, त्, skilled in<BR>the principles of gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-देवन, अम्,<BR>n. gambling, dice-playing.<BR>—अक्ष-देविन्, ई, m. a<BR>gamester.<BR>—अक्ष-द्यू, ऊस्, m. a gambler, a dice-<BR>player.<BR>—अक्ष-द्यूत, अस्, m. a gambler, a dice-<BR>player; (अम्), n. gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-द्यूतिक, अम्,<BR>n. dispute at play.<BR>—अक्ष-द्रुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>hated by, i. e. unlucky at dice.<BR>—अक्ष-धर, अस्, आ<BR>or ई, अम्, one who has dice; (अस्), m. a plant, Trophis<BR>Aspera; see साखोत.<BR>—अक्ष-धूर्त, अस्, m. a game-<BR>ster, a gambler, i. e. a dice-rogue.<BR>—अक्ष-नैपुण or<BR>-नैपुण्य, अम्, n. skill in gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-परा-<BR>जय, अस्, m. loss in gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-पात, अस्, m.<BR>cast of dice.<BR>—अक्ष-पातन, अम्, n. act of casting dice.<BR>—अक्ष-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of dice, or (perhaps)<BR>favoured by the dice, lucky.<BR>—अक्ष-मद, अस्, m.<BR>intoxicating passion for dice.<BR>—अक्ष-मात्र, अम्, n.<BR>dice, anything as big as dice; the twinkling of an eye, a<BR>moment of time.<BR>—अक्ष-माला, f. a rosary, a string<BR>or necklace of beads, especially of the seeds of the<BR>Eleocarpus; a N. of Arunḍhatī, wife of Vasiṣṭha,<BR>from her wearing a rosary; (अस्, आ, अम्), or अक्ष-<BR>मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing a rosary of seeds.<BR>—अक्ष-<BR>राज, अस्, m. the king of dice, the die called Kali.<BR>—अक्ष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having dice, relating to<BR>dice, gambling; (ती), f. a game of dice.<BR>—अक्ष-<BR>वाम, अस्, m. an unfair gambler.<BR>—१. अक्ष-विद्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, skilful in gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>what has occurred in gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-शौण्ड, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, fond of gambling.<BR>—अक्ष-सूत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>string or rosary of Eleocarpus seeds.<BR>—अक्ष-स्तुष,<BR>अस्, m. Beleric Myrobalan.<BR>—अक्ष-हृदय, अम्, n.<BR>innermost nature of dice, perfect skill in gambling.<BR>—अक्षहृदय-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, perfectly skilled in<BR>gambling.<BR>—अक्षावपन (˚ष-आव्˚), अम्, n. a dice-<BR>beard.<BR>—अक्षावाप or अक्षातिवाप (˚ष-अत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the keeper of the dice, or of a gambling table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षक|अक्षकः
अक्षक or अक्षिक, अस्, m. the tree Dalbergia<BR>Oujeinensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष 3. अक्ष, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. अश्?), an organ<BR>of sense, an object of sense; (अस्), m. the soul; know-<BR>ledge, religious knowledge; the law; a lawsuit;<BR>a person born blind; N. of Garuḍa, of a son of<BR>Rāvaṇa, of a son of Nara, &c.<BR>—अक्ष-दर्शक, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">Page0003-b+ 76</a>]<BR>m. a judge, i. e. one who sees lawsuits; also अक्ष-<BR>दृश्, क्.<BR>—अक्ष-पटल, अम्, n. court of law; de-<BR>pository of legal document.<BR>—अक्ष-पाट, अस्, m. an<BR>arena, a wrestling ground, place of contest.<BR>—अक्ष-<BR>पाटक or अक्ष-पाटिक, अस्, m. a judge, i. e. ar-<BR>ranger of a lawsuit.<BR>—अक्ष-पाद, अस्, m. a follower<BR>of the Nyāya or logical system of philosophy; N. of<BR>the Ṛṣi Gotama.<BR>—अक्ष-वाट, see अक्ष-पाट.<BR> — 2. अक्ष-विद्, त्, त्, त्, versed in law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष 4. अक्ष, अम्, n. the eye, especially<BR>substituted for अक्षि at the end of adjective com-<BR>pounds, the fem. being अक्षी [cf. Gr. ὄσσο, ὄκκο<BR>for ὄξο Lat. oculus; Germ. Auge; Russ. òko].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षण
अक्षण अ-क्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, inopportune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षत|अक्षतं|अक्षतः
अक्षत अ-क्षत, अस्, आ, अम्, not crushed;<BR>uninjured, unbroken, whole; (अस्), m. Śiva; thrashed<BR>and winnowed rice which has been dried in the sun;<BR>barley; (अस्, अम्), m. n. an eunuch; (आ), f. a virgin;<BR>N. of a plant, Karkaṭaśriṅgī or Kankaḍaśriṅgī; (अम्),<BR>n. and (आस्), m. pl. whole grain, fried grain.<BR>—अक्षत-<BR>योनि, इस्, f. a virgin, an unblemished maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षत्र
अक्षत्र अ-क्षत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of the<BR>Kṣatriya caste, apart from the Kṣatriya caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षन्
अक्षन् अक्षन्, substituted for अक्षि, the eye,<BR>in the weakest cases, see Gram. 122 [cf. Goth. augan].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षण्वत्|अक्षण्वन्त्
अक्षण्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षम|अक्षमः
अक्षम अ-क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, unable to en-<BR>dure, impatient; incompetent.<BR>—अ-क्षमा or अक्ष-<BR>म-ता, f. impatience, envy; incompetence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षय|अक्षयः
अक्षय अ-क्षय, अस्, आ, अम्, exempt from<BR>decay, undecaying; (अस्), m., N. of the twentieth year<BR>in the cycle of Jupiter; (आ), f. the seventh day of<BR>a lunar month, if it fall on Sunday or Monday; the<BR>fourth, if it fall on Wednesday.<BR>—अक्षय-गुण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, possessing imperishable qualities; (अस्), m. Śiva.<BR>—अक्षय-ता, f. or अक्षय-त्व, अम्, n. imperish-<BR>ableness.<BR>—अक्षय-तृतीया, f. a festival, the third<BR>day of the bright half of Vaiśākha, which is the first<BR>day of the Satya-yuga, and secures permanency to ac-<BR>tions then performed.<BR>—अक्षय-पुरुहूत, अस्, m.<BR>Śiva.<BR>—अक्षय-मति, इस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—अक्षय-लोक, अस्, m. the undecaying world, hea-<BR>ven.<BR>—अक्षया-ललिता, f. festival observed by women<BR>on the seventh day of the second half of Bhādra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयिन्
अ-क्षयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, undecaying; (इणी), f., N. of<BR>Śiva's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षय्य
अ-क्षय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, undecaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षर|अक्षरं|अक्षरः
अक्षर अ-क्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, imperishable;<BR>unalterable; (अस्), m. a sword; Śiva; Viṣṇu; (अम्),<BR>n. a syllable; the syllable ॐ; a letter; a vowel, a<BR>sound; a word; speech; Brahma; final beatitude;<BR>abiding merit, religious austerity; sacrifice; right,<BR>justice; the sky; water; a plant (Achyranthes Aspera).<BR>—अक्षर-चञ्चु or अक्षर-चुञ्चु, उस्, or अक्ष-<BR>र-चण or अक्षर-चन, अस्, m. a writer, scribe.<BR>—अक्षर-च्छन्दस्, अस्, n. metre regulated by the<BR>number and quantity of syllables.<BR>—अक्षर-जननी,<BR>f. a reed or pen.<BR>—अक्षर-जीवक or अक्षर-<BR>जीविक, अस्, or अक्षर-जीविन्, ई, m. a scribe.<BR>—अक्ष-<BR>र-जुर्, ऊर्, m. a sage, one who knows and enjoys<BR>Brahma.<BR>—अक्षर-तूलिका, f. a reed or pen.<BR>—अक्षर-न्यास or अक्षर-विन्यास, अस्, m. array<BR>of syllables or letters, writing; scripture; the alphabet.<BR>—अक्षर-पङ्क्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, containing five syllables;<BR>(इस्), f., N. of a metre of four lines, each containing<BR>one dactyl and one spondee; also called पङ्क्ति or<BR>हंस.<BR>—अक्षर-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. entitled to a<BR>share in the syllables (of a prayer).<BR>—अक्षर-मुख,<BR>अस्, m. having the mouth full of syllables, a student,<BR>scholar.<BR>—अक्षर-विन्यास, see अक्षर-न्यास.<BR>—अक्षर-शस्, ind. syllable by syllable.<BR>—अक्ष-<BR>र-शून्य, अस्, आ, अम्, inarticulate.<BR>—अक्षर-<BR>संस्थान, अम्, n. scripture, writing.<BR>—अक्षराङ्ग<BR>(˚र-अङ्ग), अम्, n. part of a syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरक|अक्षरकं
अक्षरक, अम्, n. a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षर्य
अक्षर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to syllables or letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षान्ति|अक्षांति|अक्षांतिः|अक्षान्तिः
अक्षान्ति अ-क्षान्ति, इस्, f. impatience,<BR>jealousy, intolerance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षार|अक्षारः
अक्षार अ-क्षार, अस्, आ, अम्, free from facti-<BR>tious salt; (अस्), m. natural salt.<BR>—अक्षार-लवण or<BR>अक्षारालवण, अम्, n. natural salt; food that may be<BR>eaten at a season unfit for performing religious duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षि
अक्षि अक्षि, n. (fr. rt. 1. अश् or अञ्ज्? Instr.<BR>अक्ष्णा, Dat. अक्ष्णे &c., fr. अक्षन्, substituted for<BR>अक्षि in the weakest cases. At the end of comp.<BR>अक्ष is substituted, see 4. अक्ष), the eye; the<BR>number two; (ई), du., Ved. the sun and moon [cf.<BR>Lith. aki-s].<BR>—अक्षि-कूट or अक्षि-कूटक, अम्, n.<BR>the eyeball, the pupil of the eye.<BR>—अक्षि-गत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, visibly present, seen; hated.<BR>—अक्षि-गोल,<BR>अस्, m. the eyeball.<BR>—अक्षि-जाह, अम्, n. the root<BR>of the eye.<BR>—अक्षि-तारा, f. the pupil of the eye.<BR>—अक्षि-पक्ष्मन्, अ, n. the eyelash.<BR>—अक्षि-<BR>पटल, अम्, n. a coat of the eye.<BR>—अक्षि-पत्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, Ved. (falling into the eyes), hurtful; (त्), ind. as<BR>much as could fall into the eyes, a little.<BR>—अक्षि-<BR>भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, visible, perceptible, manifest, present.<BR>—अक्षि-भेषज, अम्, n. a medicament for the<BR>eyes, collyrium, &c.; (अस्), m. a tree, Red Lodh.<BR>—अक्षि-भ्रुव, अम्, n. the eyes and eyebrows to-<BR>gether.<BR>—अक्षि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, provided with eyes.<BR>—अक्षि-लोमन्, अ, n. the eyelash.<BR>—अक्षि-विकूणित,<BR>अम्, n. a glance, a look with the eyelids partially closed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिक|अक्षिकः
अक्षिक or अक्षीक, अस्, m. the tree Dalbergia<BR>Oujeinensis. See अक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिणी
अक्षिणी अक्षिणी, f. (fr. 3. अक्ष ?), one of<BR>the eight conditions or privileges attached to landed<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षित
अक्षित अ-क्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, undecayed, un-<BR>injured; undecaying; (अम्), n. water.<BR>—अक्षिता-वसु,<BR>उस्, m., Ved. epithet of Indra (possessed of undecaying<BR>wealth).<BR>—अक्षितोति (˚त-ऊति), इस्, m., Ved. epithet of<BR>Indra (granting permanent help).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिति|अक्षितिः
अ-क्षिति, इस्, f. imperishableness; (इस्, इस्, इ), im-<BR>perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षियत्|अक्षियन्त्
अक्षियत् अ-क्षियत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. not<BR>inhabiting, destitute of a dwelling, unsettled; (Sāy.)<BR>not decreasing (in riches).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिव|अक्षिवः
अक्षिव अक्षिव or अक्षीव, अस्, m. a plant,<BR>Guilandina or Hyperanthera Moringa; (अम्), n. sea salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0003-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

