अङ्गीकार|अंगीकार|अंगीकारः|अङ्गीकारः
अङ्गी-कार, अस्, m. agreement, promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकृत|अङ्गीकृतं
अङ्गी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, agreed to, promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकृति|अंगीकृति|अंगीकृतिः|अङ्गीकृतिः
अङ्गी-कृति, इस्, f. agreement, promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरि|अंगुरिः|अङ्गुरिः
अङ्गुरि अङ्गुरि, इस्, or अङ्गुरी, f. (for अङ्गुलि,<BR>q. v.), a finger; a toe.<BR>—अङ्गुरीय or अङ्गुरीयक,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a finger-ring; the ring-finger (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुल|अंगुल|अंगुलः|अङ्गुलः
अङ्गुल अङ्गुल, अस्, m. (for rt. अग् or अङ्ग्),<BR>a finger; the thumb; a finger's breadth, a measure<BR>equal to eight barley-corns, twelve aṅgulas making<BR>a vitasti or span, and twenty-four a hasta or cubit;<BR>(in astron.) a digit, or twelfth part; N. of the sage<BR>Cāṇakya.<BR>—अङ्गुल-प्रमाण or अङ्गुल-मान,<BR>अम्, n. the measure or length of an aṅgula; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), having the length of an aṅgula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलक
अङ्गुलक at the end of compounds = अङ्गुल, i. e.<BR>so many aṅgulas or fingers long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलि|अंगुलि|अंगुलिः|अङ्गुलिः
अङ्गुलि, इस्, or अङ्गुली, f. a finger; a toe; the<BR>thumb; the great toe; the finger-like tip of an ele-<BR>phant's trunk; the measure aṅgula.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-तो-<BR>रण, अम्, n. a sectarial mark on the forehead con-<BR>sisting of three fingers or lines shaped like an arch or<BR>doorway (तोरण), drawn with sandal or the ashes of<BR>cow-dung.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-त्र, अम्, n. or अङ्गुलि-त्राण,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. (?), n. a finger-protector, a contrivance<BR>like a thimble, used by archers to protect the thumb<BR>or finger from being injured by the bow-string.<BR>—अङ्गुलित्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, provided with such a<BR>finger-protector.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-मुख or अङ्गुलि-मुख,<BR>अम्, n. the tip of the finger.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-मुद्रा or<BR>अङ्गुलि-मुद्रिका, f. a seal-ring.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-मोटन,<BR>अम्, n. snapping or cracking the fingers.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-<BR>षङ्ग, अस्, m. contact of the fingers; act of finger-<BR>ing; (अस्, आ, अम्), sticking to the fingers.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-<BR>सन्देश, अस्, m. snapping or cracking the fingers as<BR>a sign.<BR>—अङ्गुलि-स्फोटन, अम्, n. snapping or<BR>cracking the fingers.<BR>—अङ्गुली-पञ्चक, अम्, n. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">Page0008-b+ 72</a>]<BR>five fingers.<BR>—अङ्गुली-पर्वन्, अ, n. a finger-joint.<BR>—अङ्गुली-सम्भूत, अस्, m. produced from or on<BR>the finger, i. e. a finger nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीक|अंगुलीक|अंगुलीकं|अङ्गुलीकः
अङ्गुलीक or अङ्गुलीय or अङ्गुलीयक, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. a finger-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठः|अङ्गुष्ठः
अङ्गुष्ठ अङ्गुष्ठ, अस्, m. (the smallest<BR>अङ्ग or limb?), the thumb; the great toe; a thumb's<BR>breadth, usually regarded as equal to an अङ्गुल.<BR>—अङ्गुष्ठ-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, or अङ्गुष्ठ-<BR>मात्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, having the length or size of<BR>a thumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुष्ठ्य|अंगुष्ठ्य|अंगुष्ठ्यः|अङ्गुष्ठ्यः
अङ्गुष्ठ्य, अस्, m. the thumb nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गूष|अंगूष|अंगूषः|अङ्गूषः
अङ्गूष अङ्गूष, अस्, m. (rapid in motion,<BR>fr. rt. अङ्ग् or अग्), an ichneumon; an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गोषिन्
अङ्गोषिन् अङ्गोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. re-<BR>sonant (?), praiseworthy (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग्य|अंग्य
अङ्ग्य अङ्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अङ्ग), be-<BR>longing to or connected with the limbs of the body,<BR>corporeal, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्|अंघ्
अङ्घ् अङ्घ्, cl. 1. A. अङ्घते, आनङ्घे,<BR>अङ्घितुम्, to go, set out, set about, com-<BR>mence; to hasten; to speak hastily, scold, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ|अङ्घः
अङ्घ (not in use, but equivalent to अघ), evil,<BR>sin.<BR>—अङ्घस्, अस्, n. sin.<BR>—अङ्घारि (˚घ-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. (an enemy to sin or evil), epith. of Soma, and of<BR>a particular altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घि|अङ्घिः
अङ्घि, or better अङ्घ्रि, इस्, m. a foot; the root<BR>of a tree [cf. अंह्रि].<BR>—अङ्घ्रि-नामक, अस्, m.<BR>or अङ्घ्रि-नामन्, अ, n. a synonym of अङ्घ्रि, a<BR>root.<BR>—अङ्घ्रि-प, अस्, m. (drinking with the foot<BR>or root), a tree.<BR>—अङ्घ्रि-पर्णी or अङ्घ्रि-वल्लि,<BR>इस्, or अङ्घ्रि-वल्लिका, f. a plant, Hedysarum Lago-<BR>podioides.<BR>—अङ्घ्रि-पान, अस्, आ, अम्, sucking his<BR>foot or toes (as an infant).<BR>—अङ्घ्रि-स्कन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. the ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्
अच् अच् (connected with अञ्च्, q. v.), cl.<BR>1. P. A. अचति, अञ्चति, -ते, आनञ्च, -ए,<BR>अञ्चितुम्, to go, move, tend; to honour; to make<BR>round or carved; to request ask; to speak in-<BR>distinctly. See 2. अचित, अचिष्टु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचक्र
अचक्र अ-चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having no wheels;<BR>immoveable; not vacillating; automatous (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचक्षुस्
अचक्षुस् अ-चक्षुस्, उस्, n. a bad or miser-<BR>able eye, no eye; (उस्, उस्, उस्), blind.<BR>—अ-चक्षुर्-<BR>विषय, अस्, आ, अम्, not or no longer within reach of<BR>the eyes, invisible.<BR>—अचक्षुष्-ट्व, अम्, n. blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचक्षुष्क
अ-चक्षुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of eyes, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचण्ड|अचंड
अचण्ड अ-चण्ड, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, not of a<BR>hot temper, gentle, tractable; (ई), f. a tractable cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचतुर
अचतुर अ-चतुर, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of<BR>four, having less than four; not cunning, not dexterous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचन्द्र
अचन्द्र अ-चन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, moonless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचपल
अचपल अ-चपल, अस्, आ, अम्, not oscillating<BR>or vibrating; unmoveable, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचापल्य
अ-चापल्य, अम्, n. freedom from unsteadiness,<BR>firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचर
अचर अ-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-चरत्, अन्,<BR>अन्ती, अत्, immoveable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचरम
अचरम अ-चरम, अस्, आ, अम्, not last, not<BR>least.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचल|अचलः
अचल अ-चल, अस्, आ, अम्, not staggering or<BR>moving, immoveable; (अस्), m. a mountain or rock;<BR>a bolt or pin; the number seven; N. of Śiva<BR>and of the first of the nine deified persons, called<BR>‘white Balas’ among the Jainas; (आ), f. the earth;<BR>one of the ten earths of the Buddhists.<BR>—अचल-<BR>कीला, f. the earth.<BR>—अचल-त्विष्, ट्, m. the Kokila or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR>—अचल-धृति, इस्, f. a metre of four<BR>lines, of sixteen short syllables each, also called<BR>Gītyāryā.<BR>—अचल-भ्रातृ, ता, m., N. of a Brāhman<BR>from Oude, who became one of the eleven heads of<BR>Gaṇas among the Jainas.<BR>—अचल-मति, इस्, m., N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">Page0008-c+ 72</a>]<BR>of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—अचल-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. chief of<BR>mountains.<BR>—अचलाधिप (˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, m. (king<BR>of mountains), the Himālaya.<BR>—अचला-सप्तमी, f.<BR>title of a book in the Bhaviṣyottara Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचारु
अचारु अ-चारु, उस्, वी, उ, not pretty, in-<BR>elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिक्कण
अचिक्कण अ-चिक्कण, अस्, आ, अम्, not smooth,<BR>rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित्
अचित् 1. अ-चित्, त्, त्, त् (fr. rt. चित्), without<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिकित्वस्
अ-चिकित्वस्, आन्, उषी, अस्, Ved. not knowing,<BR>ignorant of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित्त
अ-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unnoticed, unexpected; not an<BR>object of thought; inconceivable; destitute of intellect<BR>or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित्ति|अचित्तिः
अ-चित्ति, इस्, f., Ved. want of sense, infatuation; an<BR>infatuated man (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित्
अचित् 2. अ-चित्, त्, त्, त् (fr. चित् or चिति, a pile;<BR>rt. चि), neglecting the Agnicayana, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित
1. अ-चित, अस्, आ, अम्, not collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित
अचित 2. अचित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अच्), gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिष्टु
अचिष्टु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचित्र
अचित्र अ-चित्र, अस्, आ, अम् (not variegated),<BR>undistinguishable, indistinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्ता
अचिन्ता अ-चिन्ता, f. thoughtlessness, dis-<BR>regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्तित|अचिंतित
अ-चिन्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, not thought of, unexpected,<BR>disregarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्त्य|अचिंत्य|अचिन्त्यः
अ-चिन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, surpassing all thought or<BR>conception; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—अचिन्त्य-कर्-<BR>मन्, आ, आ, अ, having or performing inconceivable<BR>actions.<BR>—अचिन्त्य-रूप, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, possessing<BR>inconceivable beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिर
अचिर अ-चिर, अस्, आ, अम्, not of long dura-<BR>tion, brief; not of long date, recent.<BR>—अचिर-द्युति,<BR>इस्, f. or अचिर-प्रभा, f. lightning.<BR>—अचिर-प्रसूता,<BR>f. (having recently brought forth), a cow that has<BR>recently calved.<BR>—अचिर-भास्, आस्, f. lightning.<BR>—<BR>अचिर-मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, recently deceased.<BR>—अचिर-<BR>रोचिस्, इस्, f. or अचिरांशु (˚र-अं˚), उस्, f. or अचिराभा<BR>(˚र-आभा), f. lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरम्
अचिरम् or अचिरात् or अचिरेण, ind. not long, not<BR>for long; not long ago; soon, speedily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरा
अचिरा, f. the mother of the Jaina-saint Śānti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिष्टु
अचिष्टु अचिष्टु, Ved. See under 2. अचित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेतन|अचेतनः
अचेतन अ-चेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-चेतस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, destitute of consciousness, inanimate; (of men)<BR>inconscious, insensible, senseless, fainting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेतान
अ-चेतान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. thoughtless, infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचैतन्य|अचैतन्यं
अ-चैतन्य, अम्, n. unconsciousness; insensibility;<BR>senselessness, ignorance in spiritual things; that which<BR>is destitute of consciousness, i. e. the material world;<BR>matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेष्ट
अचेष्ट अ-चेष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, effortless, mo-<BR>tionless.<BR>—अचेष्ट-ता, f. loss of motion from faint-<BR>ing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचोदस्
अचोदस् अ-चोदस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. free from<BR>compulsion or external stimulus, spontaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छ|अच्छं|अच्छः|अछ
अच्छ 1. अ-च्छ, अस्, आ, अम् (not shaded or<BR>covered, fr. अ + छ for छद् or छाया, rt. छद्),<BR>pellucid, transparent, clear; (अस्), m. a crystal.<BR>—अच्छोद (अच्छ-उद), अस्, आ, अम्, having clear<BR>water; (आ), f., N. of a river; a covering or garment<BR>of Viṣṇu (?); (अम्), n., N. of a lake in the Himālaya<BR>formed by the river Acchodā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छाय|अछाय
अ-च्छाय, अस्, आ, अम्, without shadow, casting no<BR>shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छ|अच्छं|अच्छः|अछ
अच्छ 2. अच्छ, अस्, m. (corruption of ऋक्ष),<BR>a bear.<BR>—अच्छ-भल्ल, अस्, m. a bear; (भल्ल<BR>itself means ‘a bear.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छ|अच्छं|अच्छः|अछ
अच्छ 3. अच्छ or usually अच्छ, rarely अच्छम्,<BR>ind., Ved. to, towards (governing the accusative and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">Page0009-a+ 78</a>]<BR>rarely the locative). It is a kind of separable pre-<BR>position or prefix to verbs and verbal derivatives, as in<BR>the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0008-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छइ
अच्छ-इ, cl. 2. P. -एति, -तुम्, or अच्छा-गम्, cl.<BR>1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्तुम्, to attain, go towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छनक्ष्
अच्छ-नक्ष्, cl. 1. P. A., Ved. -नक्षति, -ते,<BR>-क्षितुम्, to go towards, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छनश्
अच्छ-नश्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -नशति, -शितुम्, to<BR>come near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छनी
अच्छ-नी, cl. 1. P., Ved. -नयति, -नेतुम्, to lead<BR>towards or to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छनु
अच्छ-नु, cl. 2. P., Ved. -नौति, -नवितुम् or<BR>-नुवितुम्, to call out to, to cheer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छपत्
अच्छ-पत्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -पतति, -तितुम्, and<BR>Caus. P. -पतयति, -यितुम्, to fly towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छवद्
अच्छ-वद्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -वदति, -दितुम्, to salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छावच्
अच्छा-वच्, cl. 2. P., Ved. -वक्ति, -क्तुम्, to invite.<BR>—अच्छा-वाक, अस्, m. ‘the inviter’, title of a par-<BR>ticular priest or Ṛtvij, one of the sixteen required to<BR>perform the great sacrifices with the Soma juice.<BR>—अच्छावाकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, referring to the Acchā-<BR>vāka; containing the word अच्छावाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छेत
अच्छेत (˚छ-इत), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. approached,<BR>attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छोक्ति|अछोक्ति
अच्छोक्ति (˚छ-उक्˚), इस्, f., Ved. invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छिद्र|अच्छिद्रं|अछिद्र
अच्छिद्र अ-च्छिद्र, अस्, आ, अम् (free from clefts<BR>or flaws), unbroken, uninterrupted, uninjured; (अम्),<BR>n. unbroken or uninjured condition, an action free<BR>from defect or flaw; (एण), ind. uninterruptedly, from<BR>first to last.<BR>—अच्छिद्र-काण्ड, अम्, n. title of a<BR>chapter of the Taittirīya-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—अच्छिद्रोति<BR>(˚द्र-ऊति), इस्, इस्, इ, affording perfect protection.<BR>—अच्छिद्रोध्नी (˚र-ऊध्˚), f., Ved. (a cow) having<BR>a faultless udder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छिद्यमान|अछिद्यमान
अ-च्छिद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, uncut, uncurtailed;<BR>not fragile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छिन्न|अच्छिन्नं
अ-च्छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, uncut, uncurtailed, uninjured;<BR>undivided, inseparable.<BR>—अच्छिन्न-पत्त्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (of a bird, or, in the Vedas, of an altar shaped<BR>like a bird), having the wings uncurtailed, uninjured;<BR>having uninjured leaves.<BR>—अच्छिन्न-पर्ण, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, having uninjured leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छेदिक
अ-च्छेदिक or अ-च्छैदिक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, not<BR>fit or needing to be cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छेद्य|अछेद्य
अ-च्छेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, improper or impossible to<BR>be cut, indivisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छुप्ता
अच्छुप्ता अ-च्छुप्ता, f. (not touched by sin),<BR>N. of one of the sixteen Vidyādevīs of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छोटन|अच्छोटनं
अच्छोटन अच्छोटन, अम्, n. hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युत|अच्युतः
अच्युत अ-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, what has not<BR>given way or fallen; firm, solid; imperishable, per-<BR>manent; not leaking or dripping; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; also of a physician; N. of a plant,<BR>Morinda Tinctoria; N. of a gift to Agni.<BR>—अच्युत-<BR>क्षित्, त्, m., Ved. having solid ground, an epithet of<BR>Soma.<BR>—अच्युत-च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. throwing down<BR>that which is fixed.<BR>—अच्युत-ज, आस्, m. pl. a class of<BR>Jaina deities produced by Viṣṇu.<BR>—अच्युत-जल्लकिन्,<BR>ई, m., N. of a commentator of the Amara-Koṣa.<BR>—अच्युत-दन्त or अच्युतन्त, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>ancestor of a warrior tribe called Ācyutadanti or<BR>Ācyutanti, though possibly the names refer to two<BR>distinct persons and tribes.<BR>—अच्युत-मूर्ति, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अच्युत-रुष्, ट्, f. inveterate hatred.<BR>—अच्युत-वास, अस्, m. the sacred fig-tree, Ficus<BR>Religiosa.<BR>—अच्युत-स्थल, अम्, n., N. of a place<BR>in the Pañjāb.<BR>—अच्युताग्रज (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, m.<BR>(Viṣṇu's elder brother), Balarāma; Indra.<BR>—अच्युतो-<BR>पाध्याय (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m. = अच्युत-जल्लकिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्
अज् अज्, cl. 1. P. (defect. verb, supple-<BR>mented fr. rt. वी), अजति, आजीत्, अजितुम्, to<BR>go, to drive, propel, throw, cast: Desid. अजिजिषति, to<BR>be desirous of driving [cf. Gr. ἄγω Lat. ago].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
1. अज, अस्, m. a drove; a driver, mover, instigator,<BR>leader; epithet given in the Vedas to Indra. Rudra,<BR>one of the Maruts, Agni, and the sun; in later works<BR>to Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Śiva, and Kāma (see also 2 अ-ज);<BR>the leader of a flock; a he-goat or ram [cf. Gr. αἴξ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-b" target="_blank">Page0009-b+ 81</a>]<BR>αἰγος Lith. ožys]; the sign Aries; the vehicle of<BR>the sun; N. of a descendant of Viśvāmitra, and of<BR>Daśaratha's or Dīrghabāhu's father; N. of a mineral<BR>substance; of a kind of rice; of the moon; (अस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a class of Ṛṣis; of a people mentioned in<BR>the Vedas; (आ), f., N. of Prakṛti or Nature, of Māyā<BR>or Illusion; a she-goat; N. of a plant whose bulbs<BR>resemble the udder of a goat.<BR>—अज-कर्ण, अस्, m.<BR>a goat's ear; a plant or tree, Terminalia Alata<BR>Tomentosa.<BR>—अज-कर्णक, अस्, m. the Śāl-tree,<BR>Shorea Robusta.<BR>—अज-कूला, f., N. of a town of the<BR>Bodhis.<BR>—अज-क्षीर, अम्, n., Ved. goat's milk.<BR>—अज-गन्ध, अस्, m. smell of a he-goat; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), smelling like a goat.<BR>—अज-गन्धा or अज-<BR>गन्धिका, f. shrubby basil, Ocymum Gratissimum.<BR>—अज-गन्धिनी, f. a plant, also called अजशृङ्गी,<BR>q. v.<BR>—अज-गर, अस्, m. (that swallows a goat), a<BR>huge serpent, probably boa constrictor; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—अज-गल्लिका, f. ‘goat's cheek,’ an infantile<BR>disease.<BR>—अज-जीव or अज-जीविक, अस्, m. ‘who lives<BR>by goats,’ a goat-herd.<BR>—अज-ता, f. a multitude of<BR>goats; the being a goat.<BR>—अज-त्व or अजा-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the being a goat.<BR>—अज-दण्डी, f. a plant, also<BR>called ब्रह्मदण्डी.<BR>—अज-देवता, आस्, f. pl. the<BR>25th lunar mansion.<BR>—अज-नामक, अस्, m. (named<BR>Aja or Viṣṇu), a mineral substance.<BR>—अज-प, अस्,<BR>m. a goat-herd.<BR>—अज-पथ, अस्, m. ‘goat's road,’<BR>probably synonymous with अज-वीथी, q. v.<BR>—अज-<BR>पद or अज-पाद, अस्, आ, अम्, goat-footed.<BR>—अज-<BR>पाद्, त्, m., Ved. epithet of the divinity called अज.<BR>—अज-पार्श्व, अस्, m. (having black sides like a<BR>goat), epithet of Śvetakarṇa's son Rājīvalocana.<BR>—अज-पाल, अस्, m. a goat-herd; N. of Daśaratha's<BR>father.<BR>—अज-भक्ष, अस्, m. ‘goat's food,’ N. of a<BR>plant, Varvūra.<BR>—अज-मायु, उस्, m., Ved. bleating<BR>like a goat.<BR>—अज-मार, अस्, m., N. of a tribe or a<BR>prince.<BR>—अज-मीढ or अज-मीऌह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Suhotra, the author of some Vedic hymns; of<BR>a grandson of Suhotra; surname of Yudhisṭhira.<BR>—अज-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, goat-faced; (ई), f., N. of<BR>a Rākṣasī.<BR>—अज-मेरु, N. of a place, Ajmir (?).<BR>—अज-मोद, अस्, m. or अज-मोदा or अज-मोदिका,<BR>f. ‘goat's delight,’ N. of various plants, common<BR>Carroway, the species called Ajwaen (Ligusticum<BR>Ajwaen), and especially a species of Parsley, Apium<BR>Involucratum.<BR>—अजर्षभ (˚ज-ऋष्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>best goat.<BR>—अज-लम्बन, अम्, n. antimony.<BR>—अज-<BR>लोमन्, आ, m. or अज-लोमी, f., N. of a plant, Cowage,<BR>Carpopogon Pruriens; (अ), n. goat's hair.<BR>—अज-वस्ति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a tribe; (अयस्), m. pl. the members of<BR>that tribe.<BR>—अज-वाह, अस्, m., N. of a district.<BR>—अज-वीथी, f. ‘goat's road,’ N. of one of the three<BR>divisions of the southern path, or one of the three<BR>paths in which the sun, moon, and planets move,<BR>comprehending the asterisms मूला, पूर्वाषाढ,<BR>and उत्तराषाढ.<BR>—अज-शृङ्गी, f. ‘goat's horn,’<BR>N. of a shrub, Odina Wodier, used as a charm and as<BR>a remedy for sore eyes, — the fruit resembles a goat's<BR>horn.<BR>—अज-स्तुन्द, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—अज-हा,<BR>f. Cowage, Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR>—अजा-कृपाणीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, like the goat and shears in the fable.<BR>—अजा-क्षीर, अम्, n. goat's milk.<BR>—अजा-गल, अस्,<BR>m. goat's neck.<BR>—अजागल-स्तन, अस्, m. nipple or<BR>fleshy protuberance on the neck of some Indian goats,<BR>and an emblem of any useless or worthless object or<BR>person.<BR>—अजा-जीव, अस्, m. (who lives by goats), a<BR>goat-herd.<BR>—अजा-तौल्वलि, इस्, m., N. of a Muni who<BR>lived on the milk of goats; (given by grammarians as<BR>an example of compounds in which the middle term<BR>is left out).<BR>—अजाद (अज-अद), अस्, m. ‘goat-eater,’<BR>the ancestor of a warrior tribe.<BR>—अजादनी (˚ज-अद्˚),<BR>f. a species of prickly night-shade.<BR>—अजान्त्री (˚ज-<BR>अन्˚), f. a pot-herb, Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR>—अजा-<BR>पयस्, अस्, n. goat's milk.<BR>—अजा-पालक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>tending goats; (अस्), m. a goat-herd.<BR>—अजाविक (अज-<BR>अव्˚), अम्, n. goats and sheep, small cattle.<BR>—अजाश्व<BR>(अज-अश्), अम्, n. goats and horses; (अस्), m. Pūṣan<BR>or the Sun who has goats for horses.<BR>—अजैकपाद्<BR>(अज-एक्˚), त्, m. epithet of Viṣṇu; of one of the<BR>eleven Rudras.<BR>—अजैडक (अज-एड्˚), अम्, n. goats<BR>and rams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजक
अजक, अस्, m., N. of a descendant of Purūravas;<BR>also of a king of Magadha; अजका or अजिका, f. a<BR>young she-goat; a disease of the pupil of the eye,<BR>small reddish tumours (compared to kids), protruding<BR>through the transparent cornea and discharging pus.<BR>—अजका-जात, अम्, n. the same disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन|अजनं|अजनः
अजन, अजनि, अजि, अज्म, &c., see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
अज 2. अ-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, not born, existing<BR>from all eternity; (अस्), m. Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Śiva,<BR>Kāma; (आ), f. Prakṛti or Nature, Māyā or Illusion<BR>(see also 1. अज, s. v. अज् and 1. अजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकव|अजकवं|अजकवः
अजकव अजकव, अस्, m. (etymology un-<BR>known), Śiva's bow.<BR>—अजकाव, अस्, अम्, m. n. Śiva's<BR>bow; (अस्), m. a venomous kind of vermin, cen-<BR>tipede or scorpion; (अम्), n. sacrificial vessel dedicated<BR>to Mitra and Varuṇa.<BR>—अजगव or अजगाव, अम्,<BR>n. Śiva's bow; the southern portion of the path of<BR>the sun, moon, and planets; N. of a snake priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजघन्य
अजघन्य अ-जघन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not last;<BR>not least.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजघ्निवस्
अजघ्निवस् अ-जघ्निवस्, आन्, उषी, अत् (perf.<BR>part. fr. rt. हन्), not having killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजटा
अजटा अ-जटा, f. a plant, Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta; also अजडा and अज्झटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजड
अजड अ-जड, अस्, आ, अम्, not torpid or<BR>stupid; (आ), f., N. of two plants; see अजटा and<BR>कपिकच्छु, Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR>—अजड-धी, ईस्,<BR>ईस्, इ, of a vigorous mind, energetic, bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजथ्या
अजथ्या अजथ्या, f. yellow jasmin (fit for<BR>goats ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन|अजनं|अजनः
अजन 1. अजन, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अज्.), Brahmā<BR>‘the agitator;’ (अम्), n. act of instigating or mov-<BR>ing.<BR>—अजन-योनि-ज, अस्, m. (born fr. अजन, i. e.<BR>Brahmā); N. of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनि|अजनिः
अजनि, इस्, f. a path, road; see also अजि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन|अजनं|अजनः
अजन 2. अ-जन, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जन्), desti-<BR>tute of living beings, especially of men; desert; (अस्),<BR>m. an insignificant person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजननि|अजननिः
अ-जननि, इस्, f. privation of birth, cessation of exist-<BR>ence; अजननिर् अस्तु तस्य, ‘may he cease to exist !’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्य|अजन्यं
अ-जन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, improper to be produced or<BR>born; unfit or unfavourable for mankind; (अम्), n.<BR>any portent or natural phenomenon unfavourable to<BR>mankind, as an earthquake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजप|अजपः
अजप 1. अ-जप, अस्, m. (rt. जप्), one who<BR>does not repeat prayers; a reader of heterodox works;<BR>(आ), f. the mantra or formula called haṃsa, which con-<BR>sists only of a number of inhalations and exhalations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजप|अजपः
अजप 2. अज-प, अस्, m. a goat-herd. See<BR>s. v. 1. अज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमीढ|अजमीढः
अजमीढ अज-मीढ, अस्, m. See s. v. 1. अज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजम्भ|अजंभ|अजम्भः
अजम्भ अ-जम्भ, अस्, m. (toothless), a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय|अजयः
अजय अ-जय, अस्, m. non-victory, defeat;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), unconquered, unsurpassed, invincible; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Viṣṇu; of a lexicographer; of a river; (आ),<BR>f. hemp; N. of a friend of Durgā; Māyā or Illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय्य|अजय्यं
अ-जय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, invincible, improper to be<BR>won at play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर|अजरः
अजर अ-जर, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जॄ), not subject<BR>to old age, undecaying, ever young; (आ), f., N. of two<BR>plants, Aloe Perfoliata and Jīrṇapañjhī.<BR>—अजरामर-<BR>वत् (˚र-अम्˚), ind. as if undecaying and immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरत्|अजरन्त्
अ-जरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, not suffering from old age,<BR>not decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरयु
अ-जरयु, उस्, उस्, उ, not subject to old age or<BR>decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरस्
अ-जरस्, another form for अजर, used only in<BR>some cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्य|अजर्य्य|अजर्य्यं
अ-जर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not friable, not digestible;<BR>not subject to old age or decay; (अम्), n. friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजवस्
अजवस् अ-जवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. not quick,<BR>inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0009-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्र|अजस्रं
अजस्र अ-जस्र, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जस्, ‘to injure’<BR>not to be killed or interrupted), perpetual.<BR>—अजस्रम्<BR>or अजस्रेण, ind. perpetually, for ever, ever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहत्
अजहत् अ-जहत् (pres. part. fr. rt. हा with<BR>अ), not dropping or losing (used in compounds).<BR>—अजहत्-स्वार्था, f., N. of a rhetorical figure, an<BR>elliptical use of words in which their original meaning<BR>is not dropped, as “white ones” for “white horses,”<BR>“lances” for “men with lances.”<BR>—अजहल्-लिङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. (in grammar) said of a noun not dropping its<BR>original gender, when used like an adjective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजा
अजा अजा, f. a goat; Prakṛti; Māyā. See s.v.<BR>1. अज, where the compounds of अजा will also be found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजागर|अजागरः
अजागर अ-जागर, अस्, आ, अम्, not awake, not<BR>wakeful; (अस्), a plant, Eclipta or Verbesina Prostrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजि|अजाजिः
अजाजि अजा-जि, इस्, or अजा-जी, f. (अजा with rt.<BR>जि?, that overcomes goats); Cumin seed, Cuminum<BR>Cyminum; Ficus Oppositifolia; Nigella Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अजात अ-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, unborn, not yet<BR>born, not yet developed.<BR>—अजात-ककुद्, त्, m. a young<BR>bull whose hump (ककुद्) is yet undeveloped.<BR>—अजात-<BR>पक्ष, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having undeveloped wings.<BR>—अजात-व्यञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, having an unde-<BR>veloped beard.<BR>—अजात-व्यवहार, अस्, m. having<BR>his majority unattained, a minor, a youth under fif-<BR>teen.<BR>—अजात-शत्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, having no enemy;<BR>having no adversary of equal standing; (उस्), m., N. of<BR>Śiva, of Yudhiṣṭhira, of a king of Kāśī, of a son of<BR>Śamīka, of a son of Vidmisāra or Bimbisāra, and con-<BR>temporary of Śākyamuni.<BR>—अजातानुशय (˚त-अनु˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having no regret.<BR>—अजातारि (˚त-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. (having no enemy), Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानत्|अजानन्त्
अजानत् अ-जानत्, अन्, अती, अत् (pres. part. of<BR>rt. ज्ञा with अ), not knowing, unaware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानि|अजानिः
अजानि अ-जानि, इस्, or अ-जानिक, अस्, m.<BR>having no wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानेय|अजानेयः
अजानेय अजानेय, better आजानेय, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>(from आजान, आजानि, birth, descent), of high breed;<BR>undaunted, fearless; (अस्), m. a horse of high breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजामि
अजामि अ-जामि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. not of kin,<BR>not related; unfriendly; (in grammar) not corres-<BR>ponding.<BR>—अजामि-ता, f., Ved. absence of connection,<BR>friendliness, or similarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजायमान
अजायमान अ-जायमान, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जन्),<BR>not being born, not subject to birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजि|अजिः
अजि अजि, f. (fr. अज्, q. v.), a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिका
अजिका अजिका, f. (fr. अजा), a young goat<BR>[cf. 1. अज].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजित|अजितं|अजितः
अजित अ-जित, अस्, आ, अम्, not conquered,<BR>unsubdued, unsurpassed, invincible, irresistible; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of an antidote, a poisonous sort of rat; N. of<BR>various persons, viz. Viṣṇu; Śiva; one of the Saptar-<BR>shis of the fourteenth Manvantara; Maitreya or a future<BR>Buddha; the second of the Arhats or saints of the<BR>present (Jaina) Avasrapiṇī, a descendant of Ikṣvāku;<BR>the attendant of Suvidhi, who is the ninth of those<BR>Arhats; (आस्), m. pl. a class of deified beings in the<BR>first Manvantara.<BR>—अजित-केश-कम्बल, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Brāhman.<BR>—अजित-बला, f., N. of a Jaina deity,<BR>who acts under the direction of the Arhat Ajita.<BR>—अजित-विक्रम, अस्, m. (having invincible power),<BR>epithet of king Candragupta the second.<BR>—अजितात्मन्<BR>(˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having an unsubdued self or spirit.<BR>—अजितापीड (˚त-आप्˚), अस्, m. having an unsurpassed<BR>crown; N. of a king.<BR>—अजितेन्द्रिय (˚त-इन्द्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having an unsubdued sensuous nature, whose<BR>passions are not controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिन|अजिनं
अजिन अजिन, अम्, n. (probably at first the<BR>skin of a goat, अज, with the hair on, then any skin<BR>which would answer the same purpose); the hairy<BR>skin of an antelope, especially a black antelope,<BR>which serves the religious student for a couch, seat,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">Page0010-b+ 73</a>]<BR>covering, &c.; the hairy skin of a tiger, &c.; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a descendant of Pṛthu.<BR>—अजिन-पत्त्रा or<BR>अजिन-पत्त्री or अजिन-पत्त्रिका, f. a bat.<BR>—अजिन-<BR>फला, f., N. of a plant (?).<BR>—अजिन-योनि, इस्, m.<BR>(origin of the skin), an antelope, deer.<BR>—अजिन-<BR>वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, clad in a skin.<BR>—अजिन-सन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. (who joins or prepares skins), a furrier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिर|अजिरं|अजिरः
अजिर अजिर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अज्), agile,<BR>quick, rapid; (अस्), m., N. of a snake priest; (आ),<BR>f., N. of Durgā, and of a river; (अम्), n. place to run<BR>or fight in, area, court [Lat. ager?]; the body; any<BR>object of sense, air, wind; a frog; (अम्), ind. quickly.<BR>—अजिर-वती, f., N. of the river on which the town<BR>Śrāvasti was situated.<BR>—अजिर-शोचिस्, इस्, m., Ved.<BR>having a quick light, glittering, epithet of Agni and<BR>Soma.<BR>—अजिराधिराज (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m., Ved. an<BR>agile emperor, epithet of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिराय
अजिराय, nom. A. अजिरायते, -यितुम्, Ved. to be<BR>agile or quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरीय
अजिरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, connected (by proximity or<BR>ownership &c.) with an ajira or court &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्म|अजिह्मं|अजिह्मः
अजिह्म अ-जिह्म, अस्, आ, अम्, not crooked,<BR>straight, straightforward, upright; (अस्), m. a frog, a<BR>fish; see अ-जिह्व, of which this may be a corruption.<BR>—अजिह्म-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going straight on; (अस्),<BR>m. an arrow.<BR>—अजिह्माग्र (˚ह्म-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a straight point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्व|अजिह्वः
अजिह्व अ-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, tongueless;<BR>(अस्), m. a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीकव|अजीकवं
अजीकव अजीकव, अम्, n. Śiva's bow. See<BR>अजकव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीगर्त|अजीगर्तः|अजीगर्त्त
अजीगर्त अ-जीगर्त, अस्, m. (that has nothing<BR>to swallow), N. of a Ṛṣi, Śunaḥśepha's father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीत
अजीत अ-जीत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ज्या usually<BR>makes जीन), not faded, not faint.<BR>—अजीत-पुनर्व-<BR>ण्य, अम्, n., Ved. (unfaded and recoverable), N. of a<BR>twofold rite to be performed by Kṣatriyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीति|अजीतिः
अ-जीति, इस्, f., Ved. unfadingness; freedom from decay,<BR>prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्ण|अजीर्णं
अजीर्ण अ-जीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जॄ), not de-<BR>composed; unimpaired; undigested; (अम्), n. free-<BR>dom from decay, indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्णि|अजीर्णिः
अ-जीर्णि, इस्, f. indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्णिन्
अ-जीर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीव|अजीवः
अजीव अ-जीव, अस्, m. (non-life), non-ex-<BR>istence, death; (अस्, आ, अम्), lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवत्|अजीवन्त्
अ-जीवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, not living, destitute of a<BR>livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवन
अ-जीवन, अम्, n. non-existence, death; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), destitute of a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनि|अजीवनिः
अ-जीवनि, इस्, f. non-existence, death; अजीवनिस्<BR>तस्य भूयात्, ‘may death befal him!’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवित
अ-जीवित, अम्, n. non-existence, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुगुप्सित|अजुगुप्सितः
अजुगुप्सित अ-जुगुप्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुर
अजुर अ-जुर or अ-जुर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt.<BR>जूर्), Ved. not subject to old age or decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुष्ट
अजुष्ट अ-जुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not enjoyed,<BR>unsatisfactory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुष्टि|अजुष्टिः
अ-जुष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. non-enjoyment, feeling of dis-<BR>appointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेतव्य
अजेतव्य अ-जेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, invincible,<BR>insuperable, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेय|अजेयः
अ-जेय, अस्, आ, अम्, invincible; (अम्), n., N. of an<BR>antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजैकपाद्
अजैकपाद् अजैकपाद् (अज-एक˚), त्, or अजै-<BR>कपाद, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of one<BR>of the eleven Rudras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजैडक
अजैडक अजैडक (अज-एडक^1), अम्, n. goats<BR>and sheep.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk. on 20161122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजोष
अजोष अ-जोष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not gratified,<BR>not yet satisfied.<BR>—अ-जोष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>easily gratified, never satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जुका अज्जुका, f. (in the drama) a cour-<BR>tezan; (corruption of अर्जुका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झटा
अज्झटा अज्झटा, f. a plant, Flacourtia<BR>Cataphracta. (Also अजटा and अजडा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झल|अज्झलं
अज्झल अज्झल, अस्, m. (corruption of<BR>उज्ज्वल?), a burning coal; (अम्), n. a shield (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञ|अज्ञः
अज्ञ अ-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अ and rt. ज्ञा),<BR>not knowing; ignorant, inexperienced; unconscious;<BR>unwise, stupid.<BR>—अज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n. or अज्ञ-ता, f.<BR>ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञका
अज्ञका or अज्ञिका, f. diminutive form for अज्ञा,<BR>an ignorant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञात
अ-ज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, unknown; unexpected; unaware.<BR>—अज्ञात-कुल-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, whose lineage and<BR>character are unknown.<BR>—अज्ञात-केत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having unknown or secret designs.<BR>—अज्ञात-<BR>भुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, eaten unawares.<BR>—अज्ञात-<BR>यक्ष्म, अस्, m., Ved. (insidious consumption?),<BR>N. of a disease.<BR>—अज्ञात-वास, अस्, आ, अम्, whose<BR>dwelling is unknown.<BR>—अज्ञात-शील, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose character is unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातक
अज्ञातक, अस्, आ, अम्, unknown, unaware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञाति|अज्ञातिः
अ-ज्ञाति, इस्, m. not a kinsman, not related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञात्वा
अ-ज्ञात्वा, ind. not having known or ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञान|अज्ञानं
अज्ञान अ-ज्ञान, अम्, n. non-cognisance;<BR>ignorance, especially (in philosophy) spiritual ignor-<BR>ance; not merely a negative, but an active principle,<BR>which consisting of the three Guṇas (fetters or qualities)<BR>सत्त्व, रजस्, and तमस्, and preventing the soul<BR>from realizing its identity with Brahma, causes self to<BR>appear a distinct personality, and matter to appear a<BR>reality; hence equivalent to Prakṛti or Nature, and<BR>termed a divine Śakti (power), synonymous with Māyā,<BR>Illusion; (अस्, आ, अम्), ignorant, unwise.<BR>—अज्ञान-तस्<BR>or अज्ञानात्, ind. unawares, ignorantly, inadvertently.<BR>—अज्ञान-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done inadvertently.<BR>—अज्ञान-त्व, अम्, n. or अज्ञान-ता, f. ignorance.<BR>—अज्ञान-बन्धन, अम्, n. the bond of ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानिन्
अ-ज्ञानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ignorant, unwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञास्
अ-ज्ञास्, आस्, m., Ved. not a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञेय
अ-ज्ञेय, अस्, आ, अम्, baffling or passing knowledge,<BR>unfit to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्म
अज्म अज्म, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अज्), Ved. career,<BR>march, battle [cf. ὄγμος].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्मन्
अज्मन्, अ, n., Ved. career, passage, battle; a house,<BR>a habitation [Lat. agmen].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्यानि
अज्यानि अ-ज्यानि, इस्, f., Ved. undecaying<BR>nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्येष्ठ
अज्येष्ठ अ-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, not the oldest<BR>or best; having no elder brother.<BR>—अज्येष्ठ-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, not behaving as the eldest brother ought to<BR>behave, or (अज्येष्ठ-वृत्ति) behaving like one who<BR>has no elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्र|अज्रः
अज्र अज्र, अस्, m., Ved. a field, a plain;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. agile, quick [Lat. ager; Gr. ἀγρός<BR>cf. अजिर].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्र्य
अज्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in or connected with<BR>a field or plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्विन्
अज्विन् अज्विन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. rt. अज्), Ved.<BR>active, agile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च्|अंच्
अञ्च् 1. अञ्च् (connected with अच्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 1. P. A. अञ्चति, -ते, आनञ्च, -ए, अञ्चि-<BR>ष्यति, -ते, अञ्चितुम्, to bend, curve, incline, curl;<BR>to reverence (with inclined body), to honour; to tend,<BR>move, go, wander about; to request: cl. 10. or Caus.<BR>अञ्चयति, -यितुम्, to unfold, make clear, produce:<BR>Desid. P. A. अञ्चिचिषति, -ते, to be desirous of bend-<BR>ing: Pass. अञ्च्यते or अच्यते, to be bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च्|अंच्
2. अञ्च् (at the end of compounds), turned to, going<BR>or directed towards; see अकुध्र्यञ्च्, अवाञ्च्, उदञ्च्,<BR>देवद्र्यञ्च्, &c. It may also mean honouring, see<BR>प्राञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च
अञ्च, अस्, m. (only used as the last part of com-<BR>pound words), curling, as in रोमाञ्च, sensation of<BR>the hairs of the body curling, thrill of rapture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0010-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चति|अंचतिः|अञ्चतिः
अञ्चति, इस्, m. or अञ्चती, f. wind; fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चन
अञ्चन, अम्, n. act of bending or curving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चल|अंचलं|अंचलः|अञ्चलः
अञ्चल, अस्, m. (perhaps also अम्), n. the border or<BR>corner of a garment, especially of a woman's garment,<BR>of a veil, shawl. (In Bengālī, a strip of country,<BR>district.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चित|अंचित|अञ्चितः
अञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, curved, curled, arched,<BR>handsome; gone, walked in; reverenced, honoured,<BR>distinguished.<BR>—अञ्चित-पत्त्र, अस्, m. lotus with<BR>curved leaves.<BR>—अञ्चितपत्त्राक्ष (˚र-अक्ष), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having lotus eyes.<BR>—अञ्चित-भ्रू, ऊस्, f. wo-<BR>man with arched or handsome eyebrows.<BR>—अञ्चित-<BR>लाङ्गूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a curved tail (as a<BR>monkey).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्ज्|अंज्
अञ्ज् अञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. A. अनक्ति, अङ्क्ते,<BR>आनञ्ज, अञ्जिष्यति or अङ्क्ष्यति, आञ्जीत्,<BR>अञ्जितुम् or अङ्क्तुम्, to apply an ointment or pig-<BR>ment, smear with, anoint; to decorate, prepare; to<BR>honour, celebrate; to cause to appear, to make clear,<BR>distinguish, represent; to be beautiful; to go: Caus.<BR>अञ्जयति, -यितुम्, आञ्जिजत्, to smear with; to speak,<BR>shine, to cause to go [cf. Lat. ungo].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जक|अञ्जकः
अञ्जक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vipracitti; of a son<BR>of Yadu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जन|अञ्जनं|अंजनः|अञ्जनः
अञ्जन, अस्, m. a kind of domestic lizard; N. of a<BR>fabulous serpent; of a tree; of a mountain; of a king<BR>of Mithilā; of the elephant of the west or south-west<BR>quarter; (अम्), n. act of applying an ointment or pig-<BR>ment, embellishing, &c.; black pigment or collyrium<BR>applied to the eye-lashes or the inner coat of the eye-<BR>lids; special kind or material of this pigment, as<BR>lamp-black, Antimony, an extract of Ammonium,<BR>Xanthorrhiza, &c.; paint, especially as a cosmetic;<BR>magic ointment; ink; night; fire. (In rhetoric)<BR>suggesting the special meaning alluded to in an ex-<BR>pression, as in a pun, &c.<BR>—अञ्जन-केशी, f., N. of a<BR>vegetable perfume.<BR>—अञ्जन-नामिका, f. a swelling<BR>of the eyelid, stye.<BR>—अञ्जन-वत्, ind. like collyrium.<BR>—अञ्जनाधिका (˚न-अध्˚), f. a species of lizard.<BR>—अञ्जनाम्भस् (˚न-अम्˚), अस्, n. eye-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनक|अंजनकः|अञ्जनकः
अञ्जनक, अस्, m. portion of the Vedas containing<BR>the word अञ्जन.<BR>—अञ्जनकी, f., N. of a medicinal<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जना|अंजना
अञ्जना, f., N. of Hanumat's mother; of Pravara-<BR>sena's mother.<BR>—अञ्जना-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—अञ्जना-वती, f. the female elephant of the<BR>north-east (or the west ?) quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनिक
अञ्जनिक, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with collyrium;<BR>(आ), f. a species of lizard; a small mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनी|अंजनी
अञ्जनी, f. a woman fit for the application of oint-<BR>ments, pigments, sandal, &c.; N. of two medicinal plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जल
अञ्जल, अञ्जलि, see s. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जस्|अंजस्
अञ्जस्, अस्, n., Ved. ointment, preparation (?);<BR>smoothness, sliding, speed (?); a good fit, adaptation (?);<BR>(according to others, आस्, आस्, अस्), level, straight,<BR>right.<BR>—अञ्जस्-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. drinking the Soma<BR>preparation.<BR>—अञ्जः-सव, अस्, m. rapid preparation<BR>of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जस|अंजस|अञ्जसः
अञ्जस, अस्, आ, अम्, straight, straightforward, honest;<BR>(ई), f., Ved., N. of a heavenly river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसा|अंजसा
अञ्जसा or अञ्जस्, ind. straight on, right, truly, justly;<BR>quickly, soon, instantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसायन
अञ्जसायन (˚सा-अय्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having a straight<BR>course, going straight on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसीन|अंजसीन
अञ्जसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. going straight on,<BR>straightforward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जि|अंजि|अञ्जिः
अञ्जि, इस्, इस्, इ, applying an ointment or pigment;<BR>ointment, brilliancy, unctuous, slimy; shining, bril-<BR>liant; (इस्, इ), m. n. the sexual organ, i. e. distinguishing<BR>the sex; (इस्), m. a sender, commander.<BR>—अञ्जि-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. coloured, bright, adorned.<BR>—अञ्जि-<BR>सक्थ, अस्, m. (a victim) that has coloured thighs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिन्
अञ्जिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. making clear or manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिव|अंजिव
अञ्जिव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. slippery, smooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिष्ठ|अंजिष्ठः|अञ्जिष्ठः
अञ्जिष्ठ, अस्, m., Ved. (highly brilliant), the sun;<BR>also अञ्जिष्णु, उस्, m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जल
अञ्जल अञ्जल (only at the end of com-<BR>pounds), another form for अञ्जलि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलि|अंजलिः|अञ्जलिः
अञ्जलि अञ्जलि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. अञ्ज्), the open<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">Page0011-b+ 76</a>]<BR>hands placed side by side and slightly hollowed, as if<BR>by a beggar to receive food; hence when raised to the<BR>forehead, a mark of supplication, reverence, salutation<BR>or benediction; a libation; a measure of corn, sufficient<BR>to fill both hands when placed side by side, equal to a<BR>kuḍava.<BR>—अञ्जलि-कर्मन्, अ, n. making the अञ्जलि<BR>or respectful salutation.<BR>—अञ्जलि-कारिका, f. an earthen<BR>doll, making the अञ्जलि; N. of a plant, probably<BR>Mimosa Natans.<BR>—अञ्जलि-पुट, अस्, अम्, m. n. cavity<BR>produced in making the अञ्जलि.<BR>—अञ्जलि-बन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. salutation with the अञ्जलि raised to the fore-<BR>head.<BR>—अञ्जली-क्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, (hands) placed to-<BR>gether to form the अञ्जलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिक|अञ्जलिकः
अञ्जलिक, अस्, अम्, m. n., N. of one of Arjuna's<BR>arrows; see कर्ण-पर्व, 4788; (आ), a young mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिक|अञ्जिकः
अञ्जिक अञ्जिक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Yadu.<BR>See अञ्जक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिहिषा
अञ्जिहिषा अञ्जिहिषा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>अंह्), desire of going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जी|अंजी
अञ्जी अञ्जी, f. a blessing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जीर|अंजीर|अंजीरं|अञ्जीरं|अंजीरः|अञ्जीरः
अञ्जीर अञ्जीर, अम्, n. a species of fig-tree<BR>(Ficus Oppositifolia); a fig. (In Bengālī) a guava.<BR>(अञ्जीर is a Persian word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्
अट् अट्, cl. 1. P. A. अटति, -ते, आट, अटिष्यति,<BR>आटीत्, अटितुम्, to roam, wander about (some-<BR>times with acc.), frequently used of religious mendicants:<BR>Intens. अटाट्यते, to roam or wander about zealously<BR>or habitually, especially as a religious mendicant:<BR>Desid. अटिटिषति, to be desirous of roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट
अट, अस्, आ, अम्, roaming, wandering; (आ), f. the<BR>act or habit of roaming or wandering about, especially<BR>as a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटक
अटक, अस्, ई, अम्, roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटन|अटनं
अटन, अम्, n. act or habit of wandering about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनि|अटनिः
अटनि, इस्, f. or अटनी, f. the notched extremity of<BR>a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटमान
अटमान, अस्, आ, अम्, roaming about, vagabond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवि|अटविः
अटवि, इस्, or अटवी, f. (place to roam in), a forest.<BR>—अटवि-शिखर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people or<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटविक|अटविकः
अटविक, better आटविक, अस्, m. a woodman, forester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटाटा
अटाटा, f. (habit of) roaming or wandering about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटाट्यमान
अटाट्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, roaming excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटाट्या
अटाट्या, f. (habit of) roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटाय
अटाय, nom. A. अटायते, to enter upon a roaming<BR>life, to become a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्या
अट्या, f. act or habit of roaming about as a religious<BR>mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनि|अटनिः
अटनि, अटवि, अटाट्या, &c., see under<BR>अट् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरुष|अटरुषः
अटरुष अटरुष or अटरूष or अटरूषक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the shrub Justicia Adhatoda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटल
अटल अ-टल, अस्, आ, अम्, not shaky, firm,<BR>solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट्
अट्ट् अट्ट्, cl. 1. A. अट्टते, आनट्टे, अट्टितुम्,<BR>to exceed, kill; cl. 10. P. अट्टयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to contemn, lessen diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट, ind. high, lofty, loud; (अस्), m. top-heavy (?),<BR>exceeding; shaking; injuring; N. of a Yakṣa; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. addition to a building, apartment on the<BR>roof, upper story; tower, buttress, back of a building;<BR>(corruption of हट्ट), a market, a market-place;<BR>(आ), f. overbearing conduct ?; (अम्), n. (corruption of<BR>अन्न ?), boiled rice, food; (अस्, आ, अम्), dried, dry.<BR>—अट्ट-पति-भागाख्य-गृह-कृत्य (˚ग-आख्˚),<BR>अम्, n. business of the house called the market-<BR>master's department (an office in Kashmir).<BR>—अट्ट-<BR>स्थली, f. (site of an अट्ट), a name.<BR>—अट्ट-हसित,<BR>अम्, n. loud laughter, a horse-laugh.<BR>—अट्ट-हास,<BR>अस्, m. idem; a name of Śiva.<BR>—अट्ट-हासक, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a shrub, Jasminum Multiflorum or Hirsutum.<BR>—अट्ट-हासिन्, ई, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—अट्ट-हास्य,<BR>अम्, n. loud laughter; a horse-laugh.<BR>—अट्टाट्ट-हास<BR>(˚ट्ट-अट्ट्˚), अस्, m. very loud laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टक|अट्टकः
अट्टक, अस्, m. an apartment on the roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टट्ट
अट्टट्ट, ind. very high, very loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टन|अट्टनं
अट्टन, अम्, n. a weapon shaped like a discus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टा
अट्टा, f. overbearing conduct (?), excess (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टाय
अट्टाय (nom. fr. अट्टा), A. अट्टायते (meaning<BR>doubtful), to be overbearing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टाल|अट्टालः
अट्टाल अट्टाल, अस्, or अट्टालक, अस्, m. an<BR>apartment on the roof, an upper story; (इका), f.<BR>a house of two or more stories, a lofty house, palace;<BR>N. of a country.<BR>—अट्टालिका-कार, अस्, m. a bricklayer,<BR>mason.<BR>—अट्टालिका-बन्ध, अस्, m. (in architecture)<BR>a kind of base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टिलिका
अट्टिलिका अट्टिलिका, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्णार
अट्णार अट्णार, अस्, m. a king of Kośala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्या
अट्या अट्या, f.; see under rt. अट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठ्
अठ् अठ्, cl. 1. P. A. अठति, -ते, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठिल्ला
अठिल्ला अठिल्ला, f., N. of a Prākṛt metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्
अड् 1. अड्, cl. 1. P. अडति, to endeavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्
अड् 2. अड्, cl. 5. P., Ved. अड्नोति, to per-<BR>vade, attain; various reading for अह् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अडकवती
अडकवती अडकवती, N. of a fabulous palace<BR>on Meru; also of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्ड्
अड्ड् अड्ड्, cl. 1. P. अड्डति, आनड्ड, अड्डितुम्,<BR>to join; to infer, argue, meditate, discern; to<BR>attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्डन|अड्डनं
अड्डन, अम्, n. a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्
अण् 1. अण्, cl. 1. P. अणति, आण, अणितुम्, to<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्
अण् 2. अण्, cl. 4. A. अण्यते, to breathe;<BR>another form of rt. अन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणक|अणकः
अणक, अस्, आ, अम्, insignificant, small, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणकीय
अणकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with what is<BR>insignificant, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणव्य|अणव्यं
अणव्य, अम्, n. a field of (अणु) Panicum Milia-<BR>ceum; see अणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणि|अणिः
अणि, इस्, m. or अणी, f. the point of a needle; the<BR>linch-pin; the pin or bolt at the end of the pole of<BR>a carriage; the corner or part of a house which serves<BR>for slaughtering; a bound, boundary, limit.<BR>—अणी-<BR>माण्डव्य, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi said to have been<BR>impaled on an अणि or linch-pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिमन्
अणिमन्, आ, m. (fr. अणु, q. v.), minuteness, fine-<BR>ness, thinness; atomic nature; the superhuman power<BR>of becoming as small as an atom; (अ), n., Ved. the<BR>smallest particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिष्ठ
अणिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अणु, q. v.), most minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणीयस्
अणीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (fr. अणु, q. v.), or अणीयस्क,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, more minute than usual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणु|अणुः
अणु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ, fine, minute, atomic; (उस्),<BR>m. an atom of matter; an atom of time; the<BR>54, 675, 000th part of a muhūrta (of 48 minutes);<BR>N. of a grain, Panicum Miliaceum; N. of Śiva;<BR>(उ), n. (in prosody) the fourth part of a mātrā.<BR>—अणु-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, very fine or minute, gentle.<BR>—अणु-तैल, अम्, n., N. of a medical oil.<BR>—अणु-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. or अणु-ता, f. minuteness, atomic nature.<BR>—अणु-भा, f. lightning.<BR>—अणु-मध्य-वीज, अम्,<BR>n. title of a hymn.<BR>—अणु-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>the size of an atom.<BR>—अणु-मात्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the size of an atom; containing the atomic<BR>elements (मात्रा) of the body.<BR>—अणु-रेणु, उस्,<BR>m. f. atomic dust (as seen in sun-beams).<BR>—अणु-रेणु-<BR>जाल, अम्, n. an aggregate of such atomic dust.<BR>—अणु-रेवती f., N. of a plant, Croton Polyandrum.<BR>—अणु-वेदान्त, अम्, n. title of a book.<BR>—अणु-<BR>व्रीहि, इस्, m., N. of a fine sort of rice.<BR>—अणु-शस्,<BR>ind. into or in minute particles.<BR>—अणू-भू, cl. 1. P.<BR>-भवति, -वितुम्, to become minute or atomic.<BR>—अणू-भाव, अस्, m. the becoming an atom.<BR>—अण्व्-<BR>अन्त, अस्, m. a hair-splitting question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुक|अणुकः
अणुक, अस्, आ, अम्, fine, minute, atomic; acute,<BR>clever, subtle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्व|अण्वं
अण्व, अम्, n., Ved. fine interstice or hole in the<BR>strainer used for the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्वी
अण्वी, f., Ved. a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0011-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुह
अणुह अणुह, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vibhrāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ठ्|अंठ्
अण्ठ् अण्ठ् or अठ्, cl. 1. A. अण्ठते,<BR>आनण्ठे, अण्ठितुम्, to go, move, tend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ठित|अंठित
अण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ड|अंडं|अण्डं|अंडः|अण्डः
अण्ड अण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. अम्), an egg,<BR>a testicle; the scrotum; the musk bag; Semen Virile;<BR>epithet of Śiva, from his being identified with the<BR>Brahmāṇḍa or mundane egg.<BR>—अण्ड-कटाह, अस्,<BR>m. the shell of the mundane egg.<BR>—अण्ड-कोटर-<BR>पुष्पी, f., N. of a plant, Convolvulus Argenteus (?).<BR>—अण्ड-कोश or अण्ड-कोष or अण्ड-कोषक,<BR>अस्, m. the scrotum.<BR>—अण्ड-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born<BR>from an egg; (अस्), m. a bird; a fish; a snake;<BR>a lizard; (आ), f. musk.<BR>—अण्डजेश्वर (˚ज-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. Garuḍa, the king of birds.<BR>—अण्ड-धर, अस्,<BR>m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—अण्ड-वर्धन, अम्, n. or<BR>अण्ड-वृद्धि, इस्, f. swelling of the scrotum, hydro-<BR>cele.<BR>—अण्ड-सू, ऊस्, f. oviparous.<BR>—अण्डाकर्षण<BR>(˚ड-आक्˚), अम्, n. castration.<BR>—अण्डाकार (˚ड-<BR>आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, egg-shaped, oval, elliptical; (अस्),<BR>m. an ellipsis.<BR>—अण्डाकृति (˚ड-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>egg-shaped, oval, elliptical; (इस्), f. an ellipsis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डक|अंडकः|अण्डकः
अण्डक, अस्, m. the scrotum; (अम्), n. a small<BR>egg, an egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डर
अण्डर, अस्, ई, अम्, N. or epithet of a tribe.<BR>—अण्डराय, nom. A. अण्डरायते, -यितुम्, to be-<BR>have like an Aṇḍara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डालु|अंडालुः|अण्डालुः
अण्डालु, उस्, m. a fish (full of eggs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डीर|अंडीरः|अण्डीरः
अण्डीर, अस्, m. a full male, a man; strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्|अन्त्|अंत्
अत् 1. अत्, ind. a prefix said to imply ‘sur-<BR>prise,’ probably a contraction of अति, meaning ‘extra-<BR>ordinary.’<BR>—अद्-भुत, अस्, आ, अम्, extraordinary,<BR>mysterious, wonderful; see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्|अन्त्|अंत्
अत् 2. अत्, cl. 1. P. अतति, आत, अतिष्यति,<BR>आतीत्, अतितुम्, sometimes A. अतते, &c., to<BR>go constantly, walk, run; to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन|अतनं|अतनः
अतन, अस्, m. a passer on; (अम्), n. act of<BR>passing on.<BR>—अतन-वत्, आन्, m. one who wanders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसि|अतसिः
अतसि, अत्क, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतज्ज्ञ
अतज्ज्ञ अ-तज्-ज्ञ (for अ-तद्-ज्ञ), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ignorant of (तत्) that, i. e. Brahma and the soul's<BR>identity with it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतट|अतटः
अतट अ-तट, अस्, आ, अम्, having no beach<BR>or shore, precipitous^1; (अस्), m. a precipice; the<BR>third hell.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतत्त्वविद्
अतत्त्वविद् अ-तत्त्व-विद्, त्, त्, त्, ignorant of<BR>(तत्त्व) the soul's identity with Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतत्त्वार्थवत्|अतत्त्वार्थवन्त्
अ-तत्त्वार्थ-वत् (˚त्व-अर्˚), आन्, अती, अत्, not con-<BR>formable with the nature of truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथा
अतथा अ-तथा, आस्, m., Ved. not such,<BR>different; saying अ-तथा, ‘not so,’ ‘no,’ refusing;<BR>careless.<BR>—अ-तथोचित (˚था-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>deserving of such (a fate), not thus deserving, not<BR>used to this (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथ्य
अ-तथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, untrue, unreal, not really so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतदर्ह|अतदर्हं
अतदर्ह अ-तद्-अर्ह, अस्, आ, अम्, not deserv-<BR>ing that; (अम्), ind. undeservedly, unjustly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतद्गुण|अतद्गुणः
अ-तद्-गुण, अस्, m. (in rhetoric) the use of pre-<BR>dicates not descriptive of the essential nature of the<BR>object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्त्र|अतंत्र
अतन्त्र अ-तन्त्र, अस्, ई, अम्, having no ropes<BR>or no (musical) strings; unrestrained; (अम्), n. not<BR>the object of a rule or of the rule under consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्र|अतंद्र
अतन्द्र अ-तन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-तन्द्रित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-तन्द्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, free from lassi-<BR>tude, alert, unwearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप
अतप अ-तप, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. तप्), not hot, not<BR>excited, not eager; cool; impassible, unostentatious;<BR>unemployed; (आस्), m. pl. a class of deities among<BR>the Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्
अ-तपस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or अ-तपस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>अ-तपस्य, अस्, m. one who neglects तपस् or the prac-<BR>tice of ascetic austerities; an irreligious character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्त
अ-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not heated, cool.<BR>—अतप्त-<BR>तनू, ऊस्, m., Ved. whose body or mass is cool.<BR>—अतप्त-तपस्, आस्, m. whose ascetic austerity has<BR>not been (fully or properly) endured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्यमान
अ-तप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, not suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतमिस्र
अतमिस्र अ-तमिस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, not dark,<BR>not benighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतमेरु
अतमेरु अ-तमेरु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not languid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क|अतर्कः
अतर्क अ-तर्क, अस्, m. an illogical reasoner;<BR>bad logic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कित
अ-तर्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, unconsidered, unthought of;<BR>unexpected; (अम्), ind. unexpectedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क्य
अ-तर्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, baffling or surpassing thought<BR>or reasoning.<BR>—अतर्क्य-सहस्र-शक्ति, इस्, m. in-<BR>comprehensibly endowed with a thousand powers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतल|अतलं|अतलः
अतल अ-तल, अम्, n. bottomless; N. of<BR>a hell beneath the earth; (अस्), m. Śiva.<BR>—अतल-<BR>स्पर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, or अतल-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, touching<BR>the अतल; bottomless; (or it may be अ-तल-स्पर्श,<BR>whose bottom cannot be touched or reached.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतव्यस्
अतव्यस् अ-तव्यस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. not<BR>stronger, not very strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस्
अतस् अतस्, ind. (ablative of the pronom.<BR>base अ, synonymous with अस्मात्), from this, than this;<BR>hence; henceforth, from that time; from this (or<BR>from that) cause or reason.<BR>—अत-ऊर्ध्वम्, ind.<BR>henceforth, afterwards.<BR>—अत-एव, ind. for this very<BR>reason; therefore.<BR>—अतः-परम्, ind. henceforth, fur-<BR>ther on.<BR>—अतो-निमित्तम्, ind. on this ground, for this<BR>reason.<BR>—अतो-न्य (तस्-अन्), अस्, आ, अत्, differing from<BR>this.<BR>—अतो-र्हम् (˚तस्-अर्˚), ind. for this object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस|अतसः
अतस अतस, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अत्), wind, air;<BR>the soul; a (missile) weapon; a garment made of the<BR>fibre of (अतसी) flax; (अम्), n., Ved. shrubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसी
अतसी, f. common flax, Linum Usitatissimum; Śaṇa,<BR>Bengal sun used as hemp, Crotolaria Juncea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसि|अतसिः
अतसि अतसि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. अत्), Ved. a<BR>wandering mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसाय्य
अतसाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be got by begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति अति, ind. [probably neut. of an obsolete<BR>adj. अतिन्, passing, going, beyond; see rt. अत् and cf.<BR>Old Germ. anti, unti, inti, unde, indi, &c.; Eng.<BR>and; Germ. und; Gr. ἔτι, ἀντί Lat. ante; Lith.<BR>ant; Arm. ti; Zend aiti]. As a prefix to verbs and<BR>nouns, expresses beyond, over; too far past; as अति-<BR>क्रमितुम्, to overstep.<BR>—अति-क्रम, transgression.<BR>When prefixed to nouns, not derived from verbs,<BR>it expresses beyond, surpassing; as अति-कश, past the<BR>whip; अति-मानुष, superhuman, &c.; see s. v.<BR>As a separable adverb or preposition (with acc.),<BR>Ved. beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति is often prefixed to nouns and adjectives, and<BR>rarely to verbs, in the sense excessive, extraordinary,<BR>intense; excessively, too; exceedingly, very.<BR>—अति-<BR>कठोर, अस्, आ, अम्, very hard, too hard.<BR>—अति-कथा,<BR>f. an exaggerated tale; (अस्, आ, अम्,), exaggerated;<BR>see also s. v.<BR>—अति-कर्षण, अम्, n. excessive<BR>exertion.<BR>—अति-कल्यम्, ind. very early, too early.<BR>—अति-कान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively beloved.<BR>—अति-काय, अस्, आ, अम्, of extraordinary body<BR>or size, gigantic; (अस्), m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—अति-कुत्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly despised.<BR>—अति-<BR>कुल्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. too bald.<BR>—अति-कृच्छ्र, अस्,<BR>m. extraordinary pain or hardship; extraordinary<BR>penance.<BR>—अति-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, overdone, exagge-<BR>rated.<BR>—अति-कृश, अस्, आ, अम्, very thin, emaciated.<BR>—अति-कृष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, very or too dark, very or<BR>too deep blue.<BR>—अति-क्रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively<BR>angry.<BR>—अति-क्रुष्ट, अम्, n. extraordinary cry or<BR>wailing.<BR>—अति-खर, अस्, आ, अम्, very pungent or<BR>piercing.<BR>—अति-गण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, having large<BR>cheeks or temples; (अस्), m., N. of the योग (or<BR>index), star of the 6th lunar mansion.<BR>—अति-गन्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having an overpowering smell; (अस्), m.<BR>sulphur; lemon-grass (Andropogon Schænunthes);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-c" target="_blank">Page0012-c+ 81</a>]<BR>the Champac flower (Michelia Champaca); a kind of<BR>jasmin.<BR>—अति-गन्धालु, उस्, m., N. of a creeper, Pu-<BR>tradātrī.<BR>—अति-गरीयस्, अस्, n. (compar. of अति-गुरु),<BR>a higher price.<BR>—अति-गर्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, very con-<BR>ceited.<BR>—अति-गहन, अस्, आ, अम्, very impenetrable.<BR>—अति-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, having extraordinary<BR>qualities.<BR>—अति-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, closely concealed,<BR>very mysterious.<BR>—अति-गुरु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ, very<BR>heavy<BR>—अति-गो, औस्, f. an excellent cow.<BR>—अति-<BR>ग्राह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, very acceptable; (अस्), N. of<BR>three successive libations made (or cups filled) at the<BR>Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR>—अति-चण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>violent.<BR>—अति-चरण, अम्, n. excessive practice.<BR>—अति-चापल्य, अम्, n. extraordinary mobility or<BR>unsteadiness.<BR>—अति-छत्त्र or अति-छत्त्रक, अस्, m.<BR>(extraordinary parasol), a mushroom; (आ), f. Anise,<BR>principally Anisum or Anethum Sowa; another<BR>plant, Barleria Longifolia.<BR>—अति-जर, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>(as a supplementary form) अति-जरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, very<BR>aged.<BR>—अति-जल, अस्, आ, अम्, well watered.<BR>—अति-<BR>जव, अस्, m. extraordinary speed; (अस्, आ, अम्), very<BR>fleet.<BR>—अति-जागर, अस्, आ, अम्, very wakeful; (अस्),<BR>m. the black curlew.<BR>—अति-जीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>aged.<BR>—अतिजीर्ण-ता, f. extreme old age<BR>—अति-जीव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, quite alive, very lively.<BR>—अति-डीन, अम्,<BR>n. extraordinary flight (of birds).<BR>—अति-तपस्विन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, very ascetic<BR>—अति-तीक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>sharp.<BR>—अति-तीव्र, अस्, आ, अम्, very sharp, pungent<BR>or acid; (आ), f. dūb grass.<BR>—अति-तृण्णस्, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>seriously hurt.<BR>—अति-तृप्ति, इस्, f. too great satiety.<BR>—अति-तृष्णा, f. excessive thirst, rapacity; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), excessively thirsty, rapacious.<BR>—अति-त्रस्नु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, very timid, over timid.<BR>—अति-दग्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, badly burnt; (अम्), n. (in medicine) N.<BR>of a bad kind of burn.<BR>—अति-दर्प, अस्, m. excessive<BR>conceit; N. of a snake; (अस्, आ, अम्), excessively con-<BR>ceited.<BR>—अति-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, very far-sighted.<BR>—अति-<BR>दातृ, ता, m. a very liberal man.<BR>—अति-दान, अम्, n.<BR>munificence.<BR>—अति-दारुण, अस्, आ, अम्, very terrible.<BR>—अति-दाह, अस्, m. great heat; violent inflamma-<BR>tion.<BR>—अति-दीर्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, very long, too long.<BR>—अति-दुःखित or अति-दुष्खित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>greatly afflicted, very sad.<BR>—अति-दुःसह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very hard to bear, quite unbearable.<BR>—अति-दुर्गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very badly off.<BR>—अति-दुर्धर्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very hard to approach, very haughty.<BR>—अति-<BR>दुर्लम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, very hard to attain or obtain.<BR>—अति-दुष्कर, अस्, आ, अम्, very difficult.<BR>—अति-<BR>दूर, अस्, आ, अम्, very distant; (अम्), n. a great<BR>distance.<BR>—अति-दोष, अस्, m. a great fault.<BR>—अति-<BR>धवल, अस्, आ, अम्, very white.<BR>—अति-धेनु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, distinguished for his cows.<BR>—अति-निद्रा, f.<BR>excessive sleep; (अस्, आ, अम्), given to (or over-<BR>powered by) excessive sleep; (अम्), ind. past (or<BR>after) sleeping time.<BR>—अति-निपुण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very able or skilful.<BR>—अति-नीच, अस्, आ, अम्, exces-<BR>sively low.<BR>—अति-पथिन्, अन्थास्, m. a better road<BR>than common.<BR>—अति-पद, अस्, आ, अम्, (in prosody)<BR>too long by one पद or foot.<BR>—अति-परोक्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, far out of sight, i. e. no longer discernible.<BR>—अतिपरोक्ष-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, (in grammar)<BR>having a nature that is no longer discernible, i. e.<BR>obsolete.<BR>—अति-पातक, अम्, n. a very heinous sin,<BR>incest.<BR>—अति-पुरुष or अति-पूरुष, अस्, m. a first-<BR>rate man or hero.<BR>—अति-पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, quite<BR>purified; refined to excess.<BR>—अति-पेशल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very dexterous or clever.<BR>—अति-प्रकाश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. very manifest, notorious.<BR>—अति-प्रगे, ind. very<BR>early.<BR>—अति-प्रणय, अस्, m. excessive kindness,<BR>partiality.<BR>—अति-प्रणुद्य, ind. having pushed far<BR>forward.<BR>—अति-प्रबन्ध, अस्, m. complete con-<BR>tinuity.<BR>—अति-प्रवरण, अम्, n. excess in choosing.<BR>—अति-प्रवृत्ति, इस्, f. issuing abundantly or too<BR>freely.<BR>—अति-प्रवृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, enlarged to<BR>excess, overbearing.<BR>—अति-प्रश्न, अस्, m. an ex-<BR>travagant question, a question regarding transcendental<BR>objects.<BR>—अति-प्रश्न्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be asked<BR>such an extravagant question.<BR>—अति-प्रसक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>or अति-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m. excessive attachment; un-<BR>warrantable stretch of a rule or principle.<BR>—अति-<BR>प्रसिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, very famous, notorious.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0013-a" target="_blank">Page0013-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—अति-प्रौढ, अस्, आ, अम्, full-grown.<BR>—अति-<BR>प्रौढ-यौवन, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the<BR>full enjoyment of youth.<BR>—अति-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>strong or powerful; (अस्), m. an active soldier; N. of<BR>a king; (आ), f., N. of a medicinal plant (Sidonia<BR>Cordifolia and Rhombifolia, or Annona Squamosa);<BR>N. of a powerful charm; N. of one of Dakṣa's<BR>daughters.<BR>—अति-बालक, अस्, m. an infant; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), childish.<BR>—अति-बाहु, उस्, m. ‘having extraordi-<BR>nary arms;’ N. of a Ṛṣi of the fourteenth Manvantara.<BR>—अति-बीभत्स, अस्, m. excessive aversion.<BR>—अति-<BR>ब्रह्मचर्य, अम्, n. excessive abstinence or con-<BR>tinence.<BR>—अति-भर, usually अति-भार, अस्, m. an<BR>excessive burden; excessive obscurity (of a sentence);<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—अतिभार-ग, अस्, m. a mule.<BR>—अति-<BR>भी, ईस्, m. (very terrific), lightning.<BR>—अति-भीषण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very terrific or formidable.<BR>—अति-भृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, well filled.<BR>—अति-भोजन, अम्, n. eating<BR>too much; morbid voracity.<BR>—अति-भ्रू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>having extraordinary eyebrows.<BR>—अति-मङ्गल्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, very auspicious; (अस्), m. a fruit, Ægle or<BR>Cratæva Marmelos.<BR>—अति-मति, इस्, f. haughtiness.<BR>—अति-मध्यन्दिन, अम्, n. the height of noon.<BR>—अति-मर्श, अस्, m. close contact.<BR>—अति-मान, अस्,<BR>m. great haughtiness.<BR>—अति-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, very<BR>haughty.<BR>—अतिमानि-ता, f. great haughtiness.<BR>—अति-<BR>मारुत, अस्, आ, अम्, very windy; (अस्), m. a hurricane.<BR>—अति-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, entirely liberated; quite<BR>free from sensual or worldly desire; seedless, barren;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a tree, Dalbergia Oujeinensis; of a<BR>creeper, Gærtnera Racemosa.<BR>—अति-मुक्तक, अस्, m.<BR>= the preceding; mountain ebony; a tree called<BR>Harimantha.<BR>—अति-मुक्ति, इस्, f. final liberation (from<BR>death).<BR>—अति-मूर्ति, इस्, f. ‘highest shape,’ N. of a<BR>ceremony.<BR>—अति-मैथुन, अम्, n. excess of sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>—अति-मोक्ष, अस्, m. final liberation<BR>(from death).<BR>—अति-मोदा, f. extraordinary fragrance;<BR>N. of a tree, Jasminum Arboreum.<BR>—अति-यव, अस्, m.<BR>a sort of barley.<BR>—अति-यश, अस्, आ, अम्, or अति-यशस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, very celebrated or illustrious.<BR>—अति-याज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘great sacrificer,’ N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—अति-युवन्,<BR>वा, वती, or ऊनी, व, very youthful.<BR>—अति-योग,<BR>अस्, m. (in medicine) excessive union, excess.<BR>—अति-रंहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, extremely rapid.<BR>—अति-<BR>रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, very red; (आ), f. one of Agni's<BR>seven tongues.<BR>—अति-रथ, अस्, m. a very great<BR>warrior fighting from a car.<BR>—अति-रभस, अस्, m.<BR>excessive or extraordinary speed.<BR>—अति-रसा, f. (very<BR>succulent); N. of various plants, as Mūrvā, Rāsnā,<BR>Klītanaka.<BR>—अति-राजन्, आ, m. an extraordinary or<BR>excellent king; one who surpasses a king [cf. also<BR>s. v.].<BR>—अति-रुचिर, अस्, आ, अम्, very lovely; (आ),<BR>f., N. of two metres, one a variety of the अति-<BR>जगती, the other also called चुडिका or चुलिका.<BR>—अति-रुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, very angry.<BR>—अति-रूप, अस्, आ,<BR>or ई, अम्, very beautiful; (अम्), n. extraordinary<BR>beauty.<BR>—अति-रोग, अस्, m. consumption.<BR>—अति-<BR>रोमश, अस्, आ, अम्, very hairy, too hairy; (अस्), m.<BR>a wild goat, or a kind of monkey.<BR>—अति-लक्ष्मी,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, very prosperous; (ईस्), f. extraordinary<BR>prosperity.<BR>—अति-लङ्घन, अम्, n. excessive fasting.<BR>—अति-लम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, very extensive.<BR>—अति-<BR>लुब्ध or अति-लोभ, अस्, आ, अम्, very greedy or<BR>covetous.<BR>—अति-लुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, closely attached<BR>or adhering.<BR>—अति-लोभ, अस्, m. or अतिलोभ-ता,<BR>f. excessive greediness or covetousness.<BR>—अति-लोम<BR>or अति-लोमश, अस्, आ, अम्, very hairy, too hairy.<BR>—अति-लोमशा, f. a pot-herb, Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR>—अति-लोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, very red.<BR>—अति-लौल्य, अम्,<BR>n. excessive eagerness or desire.<BR>—अति-वक्तृ, आ, री,<BR>ऋ, very loquacious.<BR>—अति-वक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>crooked or curved; (आ), f. one of the eight descrip-<BR>tions of planetary motion.<BR>—अति-वर्तुल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very or quite round; (अस्), m., N. of a grain or<BR>pot-herb.<BR>—अति-वात, अस्, m. high wind, a storm.<BR>—अति-वाद, अस्, m. extraordinary, i. e. abusive lan-<BR>guage; (reproof); N. of a Vedic verse recited on certain<BR>occasions.<BR>—अति-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, talkative.<BR>—अति-<BR>वालक, अस्, आ, अम्, childish; (अस्), m. an infant.<BR>—अति-वाहन, अम्, n. excessive toiling.<BR>—अति-<BR>विकट, अस्, आ, अम्, very fierce; (अस्), m. a vicious ele-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0013-b" target="_blank">Page0013-b+ 81</a>]<BR>phant.<BR>—अति-विपिन, अस्, आ, अम्, having many forests.<BR>—अति-विलम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, very dilatory.<BR>—अति-<BR>विश्रब्ध-नवोढा (˚व-ऊढा˚), f. a fond but pert<BR>young wife.<BR>—अति-विष, अस्, आ, अम्, exceedingly poi-<BR>sonous; counteracting poison; (आ), f. a very poisonous<BR>yet medicinal plant, Aconitum Ferox.<BR>—अति-वृद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. extraordinary growth or increase.<BR>—अति-वृष्टि,<BR>इस्, f. excessive rain.<BR>—अतिवृष्टि-हत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>injured by heavy rain.<BR>—अति-वेपथु, उस्, m. exces-<BR>sive tremor; (उस्, उस्, उ), or अतिवेपथु-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, trembling excessively.<BR>—अति-वैचक्षण्य, अम्,<BR>n. great proficiency.<BR>—अति-वैशस, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>adverse or destructive.<BR>—अति-व्यथन, अम्, n. in-<BR>fliction of (or giving) excessive pain.<BR>—अति-व्यथा,<BR>f. excessive pain.<BR>—अति-व्यय, अस्, m. lavish expen-<BR>diture.<BR>—अति-व्याप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, stretched too far<BR>(as a rule or principle).<BR>—अति-व्याप्ति, इस्, f. unwarrant-<BR>able stretch (of a rule or principle).<BR>—अति-शक्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or अति-शक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, very powerful; (इस्), f.<BR>or अतिशक्ति-ता, f. great power or valour.<BR>—अतिशक्ति-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, possessing great power.<BR>—अति-शङ्का, f.<BR>excessive timidity.<BR>—अति-शर्वर, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>dead of night.<BR>—अति-शस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, very excellent.<BR>—अति-शुक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, too bright.<BR>—अति-शुक्ल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very white, too white.<BR>—अति-शोभन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very handsome, distinguished.<BR>—अति-श्री,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, very prosperous.<BR>—अति-संस्कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, highly finished or adorned or educated.<BR>—अति-<BR>सक्ति, इस्, f. excessive attachment.<BR>—अतिसक्ति-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, excessively attached.<BR>—अति-सञ्चय, अस्,<BR>m. excessive accumulation, a hoard.<BR>—अति-सन्तप्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, greatly afflicted.<BR>—अति-सन्धेय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, easy to be settled or conciliated.<BR>—अति-समर्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very competent.<BR>—अति-समीप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very near.<BR>—अति-सम्पर्क, अस्, m. excessive sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>—अति-साध्वस, अम्, n. excessive fear<BR>or alarm.<BR>—अति-सान्तपन, अम्, n. a species of severe<BR>penance, inflicted especially for eating unclean animal<BR>food.<BR>—अति-सायम्, ind. very late or in the dusk.<BR>—अति-<BR>सिद्धि, इस्, f. great perfection or proficiency.<BR>—अति-<BR>सुजन, अस्, आ, अम्, very moral, very friendly, very<BR>respectable.<BR>—अति-सुन्दर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, very hand-<BR>some, very beautiful; (अस्, आ), m. f. a metre belonging<BR>to the class अष्टि, also called चित्र or चञ्चला.<BR>—अति-सुलभ, अस्, आ, अम्, very easily obtainable.<BR>—अति-सुहित, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively kind, over-<BR>kind.<BR>—अति-सृष्टि, इस्, f. an extraordinary or excel-<BR>lent creation.<BR>—अति-सेवा, f. excessive indulgence (of a<BR>habit).<BR>—अति-सौरभ, अस्, आ, अम्, very fragrant;<BR>(अम्), n. extraordinary fragrance.<BR>—अति-सौहित्य, अम्,<BR>n. excessive fondness, or the effect of it, e. g. being<BR>spoiled, stuffed with food, &c.<BR>—अति-स्तुति, इस्, f. extra-<BR>ordinary praise.<BR>—अति-स्थिर, अस्, आ, अम्, very stable<BR>or durable.<BR>—अति-स्थूल, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively thick,<BR>or stout, or big, or clumsy; excessively stupid.<BR>—अति-<BR>स्निग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, very smooth, very nice, very<BR>affectionate.<BR>—अति-स्पर्श, अस्, m. too marked contact<BR>(of the tongue and palate) in pronunciation.<BR>—अति-<BR>स्फिर, अस्, आ, अम्, very tremulous.<BR>—अति-स्वप्न,<BR>अस्, m. excessive sleep; (अम्), n. excessive tendency<BR>to dreaming.<BR>—अति-स्वस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, enjoying ex-<BR>cellent health.<BR>—अति-हसित, अम्, n. or अति-हास, अस्,<BR>m. excessive laughter.<BR>—अति-ह्रस्व, अस्, आ, अम्, ex-<BR>cessively short.<BR>—अत्य्-अग्नि, इस्, m. morbidly rapid di-<BR>gestion.<BR>—अत्य्-अद्भुत, अस्, आ, अम्, very wonderful.<BR>—अत्य्-अध्वन्, आ, m. a long way or journey, exces-<BR>sive travelling.<BR>—अत्य्-अमर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, quite out<BR>of temper.<BR>—अत्य्-अम्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, very acid; (अस्),<BR>m. a tree, Spondias Mangifera; (आ), f. a tree, a species<BR>of citron.<BR>—अत्यम्ल-पर्णी, f. having very acid leaves,<BR>N. of a medicinal plant or creeper.<BR>—अत्य्-अल्प, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very little.<BR>—अत्य्-अशन, अम्, n. immoderate<BR>eating.<BR>—अत्य्-अश्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, eating too much.<BR>—अत्य्-असम, अस्, आ, अम्, very uneven, very rough.<BR>—अत्य्-आदर, अस्, m. excessive deference.<BR>—अत्य्-<BR>आदान, अम्, n. taking away too much.<BR>—अत्य्-आप्ति, इस्, f.<BR>complete attainment.<BR>—अत्य्-आरूढि, इस्, f. mounting too<BR>high.<BR>—अत्य्-आशा, f. extravagant hope.<BR>—अत्य्-आहार,<BR>अस्, m. excess in eating.<BR>—अत्य्-आहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, eating<BR>immoderately, gluttonous.<BR>—अत्य्-आहित, अम्, n. great<BR>calamity; great danger; facing great danger; a daring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0013-c" target="_blank">Page0013-c+ 71</a>]<BR>action.<BR>—अत्य्-उक्ति, इस्, f. excessive talking; exaggera-<BR>tion; hyperbole.<BR>—अत्य्-उग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, very fierce;<BR>very pungent; (अम्), n. Asa Fœtida.<BR>—अत्य्-उच्चैस्,<BR>ind. very loudly.<BR>—अत्युच्चैर्-ध्वनि, इस्, m. a very<BR>loud sound; a very high note.<BR>—अत्य्-उत्कट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very imposing, immense, extraordinary.<BR>—अत्य्-<BR>उत्साह, अस्, m. (in medicine) excessive vigour or<BR>activity.<BR>—अत्य्-उदार, अस्, आ, अम्, very liberal.<BR>—अत्य्-<BR>उल्बण or अत्य्-उल्वण, अस्, आ, अम्, very conspicuous,<BR>immense, excessive.<BR>—अत्य्-उष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, very hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0012-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकथ|अतिकथः
