अति-ग्रह, अस्, m. act of overtaking or surpassing;<BR>one who takes or seizes to an extraordinary extent;<BR>(in philosophy) the same as अतिग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्राह|अतिग्राहः
अति-ग्राह, अस्, m. object of a ग्रह, i. e. of an<BR>apprehensive organ; there are eight such grahas, viz.<BR>प्राण, ‘inhaling or nose;’ वाच्, ‘speech;’ जिह्वा,<BR>‘tongue;’ चक्षुस्, ‘eye;’ श्रोत्र, ‘ear;’ मनस्,<BR>‘mind;’ हस्त, ‘hand;’ त्वच्, ‘skin:’ these have<BR>eight corresponding अति-ग्राहस् or objects, viz.<BR>अपान, ‘exhaling substance;’ नामन्, ‘name;’ रस,<BR>‘sap or taste;’ रूप, ‘form;’ शब्द, ‘sound;’ काम,<BR>‘desire;’ कर्मन्, ‘action;’ and स्पर्श, ‘touch.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्राह्य|अतिग्राह्यः
अति-ग्राह्य, अस्, m., Ved., N. of three successive<BR>libations made (or cups filled) at the Jyotiṣṭoma<BR>sacrifice; (very acceptable; see under अति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ
अतिघ अति-घ, अस्, m. (fr. अति and rt. हन्,<BR>‘very destructive’), a weapon, a bludgeon; wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ्न
अति-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. very or utterly de-<BR>structive; (ई), f., Ved. a happy state of utter oblivion<BR>or profound sleep obliterating all that is disagreeable<BR>in the past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ्न्य
अति-घ्न्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. overpowering, over-<BR>coming (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचमू
अतिचमू अति-चमू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, victorious over<BR>armies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर्
अतिचर् अति-चर्, cl. 1. P. -चरति, -रितुम्, to<BR>pass or pass by; to overtake, surpass; to transgress,<BR>offend, be unfaithful to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर
अति-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, transient, changeable; (आ),<BR>f., N. of the shrub Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचरण|अतिचरणं
अति-चरण. See s. v. अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचार|अतिचारः
अति-चार, अस्, m. act of passing, overtaking, sur-<BR>passing; accelerated motion, especially of planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचारिन्
अति-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, surpassing, transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचृत्
अतिचृत् अति-चृत्, cl. 1. P. -चर्तति, -तितुम्,<BR>to stick on, fasten together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचेष्ट्
अतिचेष्ट् अति-चेष्ट्, cl. 1. A. -चेष्टते, -टितुम्,<BR>to make extraordinary or excessive efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छन्द|अतिच्छंदः|अतिच्छन्दः
अतिच्छन्द अति-च्छन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, past<BR>wordly desires, free from them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छन्दस्|अतिच्छंदस्
अति-च्छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. past worldly desires,<BR>free from them; (आस्, अस्), f. n., N. of two extensive<BR>classes of metres; (अस्), n., N. of a particular brick in<BR>the sacrificial fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजगती
अतिजगती अति-जगती, f., N. of a genus of<BR>metres (belonging to the class अतिच्छन्दस्), of four<BR>lines, each containing thirteen syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजन
अतिजन अति-जन, अस्, आ, अम् (‘past men’),<BR>uninhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजात
अतिजात अति-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, superior to<BR>his parentage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजि
अतिजि अति-जि, cl. 1. P. -जयति, -जेतुम्, to<BR>conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजीव्
अतिजीव् अति-जीव्, cl. 1. P. -जीवति, -वितुम्,<BR>to survive; to surpass in the mode of living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितत
अतितत अति-तत, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अति-तन्), far-<BR>stretched, making one's self very big, conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितप्
अतितप् अति-तप्, cl. 1. P. -तपति, -तप्तुम्,<BR>to be very hot; to heat; to affect greatly: Caus.<BR>-तापयति, -यितुम्, to heat much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितराम्
अतितराम् अति-तराम्, ind. (compar. of अति),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">Page0014-b+ 71</a>]<BR>above in rank (with acc.); better, higher, more (with<BR>abl.); very much, exceedingly, excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितृद्
अतितृद् अति-तृद्, cl. 7. P. -तृणत्ति, -तर्दितुम्,<BR>to pierce, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितृप्
अतितृप् अति-तृप्, cl. 4. P. -तृप्यति, -तर्प्-<BR>तुम् or -त्रप्तुम्, to be or become satisfied, satiated<BR>or glutted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितॄ
अतितॄ अति-तॄ, cl. 1. P. -तरति, -तरितुम् or<BR>-तरीतुम्, to pass, cross, get over, overcome, escape;<BR>to attain: Desid. -तितीर्षति, to be desirous of crossing<BR>or overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितारिन्
अति-तारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, crossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितार्य
अति-तार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper or practicable to be<BR>got over or overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतित्यद्
अतित्यद् अति-त्यद्, surpassing that; (a<BR>fictitious compound coined by grammarians.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतित्वम्
अतित्वम् अति-त्वम्, surpassing thee; (a<BR>grammatical compound, see the last); अतित्वाम्, अति-<BR>त्वान् (acc. sing. and pl.), him that surpasses thee,<BR>them that surpass thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतित्वर्
अतित्वर् अति-त्वर्, cl. 1. A., occasionally P.,<BR>त्वरते, -ति, -रितुम्, to hasten greatly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथि|अतिथिः
अतिथि अतिथि, इस्, ई, इ, m. f. n. (etymology<BR>uncertain; if, according to native authorities, fr. rt. अत्,<BR>it would then first mean ‘a traveller;’ if fr. अ and<BR>तिथि, the first idea would be ‘one who has no fixed<BR>time for coming or staying;’ if from अति and स्था,<BR>‘one who has the pre-eminence over the members of<BR>the household’), a guest, entitled to hospitality; (इस्),<BR>m. wrath; N. of Agni or an attendant of Soma; N.<BR>of Suhotra, king of Ayodhyā, and grandson of Rāma.<BR>—अतिथि-क्रिया, f. hospitality, as (religiously) due to<BR>a guest.<BR>—अतिथि-ग्व, अस्, m. (‘to whom guests should<BR>go’), an epithet of Divodāsa.<BR>—अतिथि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>condition of a guest, hospitality.<BR>—अतिथि-देव, अस्,<BR>आ, or ई, अम्, treating the guest as a divinity.<BR>—अतिथि-<BR>द्वेष, अस्, m. inhospitality.<BR>—अतिथि-धर्म, अस्,<BR>m. title to hospitality.<BR>—अतिथि-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>entitled to hospitality.<BR>—अतिथि-पति, इस्, m. the host<BR>or entertainer of a guest.<BR>—अतिथि-पूजन, अम्, n. or<BR>अतिथि-पूजा, f. honourable and religious reception of<BR>a guest.<BR>—अतिथि-वत्, ind. like a guest.<BR>—अतिथि-<BR>सत्कार, अस्, m. honourable treatment of a guest.<BR>—अतिथि-सेवा, f. attention paid to a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिन्
अतिथिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. rt. अत्), Ved. travelling; (ई),<BR>m., N. of a king, also called Suhotra and Atithi, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदत्त
अतिदत्त अति-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a brother<BR>of Datta and son of Rājādhideya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदह्
अतिदह् अति-दह्, cl. 1. P., poet, also A.,<BR>-दहति, -ते, -दग्धुम्, to burn or blaze across; to<BR>burn or distress greatly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदा
अतिदा अति-दा, cl. 3. P. -ददाति, -दातुम्, to<BR>surpass in giving; to pass over or neglect in giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदान्त
अतिदान्त अति-दान्त, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदिव्
अतिदिव् अति-दिव्, cl. 4. P. -दीव्यति, -देवितुम्,<BR>to play high, lose at play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदिश्
अतिदिश् अति-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति, -देष्टुम्,<BR>to assign, make over, transfer: Pass. -दिश्यते, (in<BR>grammar) to be overruled or attracted or assimilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदिष्ट|अतिदिष्टः
अति-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, overruled, attracted, in-<BR>fluenced, inferred, substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेश|अतिदेशः
अति-देश, अस्, m. transfer, extended application,<BR>inference, analogy, overruling influence, assimilation;<BR>a rule providing for more than the usual rule; putting<BR>one thing instead of another, substitution; रूपाति-<BR>देश, such a rule as affecting the form of a word;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्,), overruling, previously stated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदीप्य|अतिदीप्यः
अतिदीप्य अति-दीप्य, अस्, m. (very brilliant),<BR>a plant, Plumbago Rosea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदृप्
अतिदृप् अति-दृप्, cl. 4. P. -दृप्यति,<BR>-दर्प्तुम् or -द्रप्तुम्, to be excessively conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदृश्
अतिदृश् अति-दृश्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -पश्यति,<BR>-द्रष्टुम्, to look beyond, look through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेव|अतिदेवः
अतिदेव अति-देव, अस्, m. a superior god;<BR>surpassing the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधन्वन्
अतिधन्वन् अति-धन्वन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>descendant of Śunaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधाव्
अतिधाव् अति-धाव्, cl. 1. P. -धावति, -वितुम्,<BR>to run or rush over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधृति|अतिधृतिः
अतिधृति अति-धृति, इस्, f., N. of a genus of<BR>metres belonging to the class अतिच्छन्दस्, and con-<BR>sisting of four lines, each containing nineteen syllables;<BR>(in arithm.) nineteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनम्
अतिनम् अति-नम्, cl. 1. P. -नमति, -नन्तुम्,<BR>to bend aside, keep on one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनामन्
अतिनामन् अति-नामन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>Saptarṣi of the sixth Manvantara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनाष्ट्र
अतिनाष्ट्र अति-नाष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, past danger,<BR>out of danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिचृत्
अतिनिचृत् अति-निचृत् or अति-निवृत्, त्, f., N.<BR>of a Vedic metre of three pādas, containing respec-<BR>tively seven, six and seven syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिद्रम्
अतिनिद्रम् अति-निद्रम्, ind. past sleeping<BR>time. See s. v. अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिष्टन्
अतिनिष्टन् अति-निष्-टन् (-निस्-तन्), cl. 8. P.,<BR>Ved. -तनोति, -नितुम्, to penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनी
अतिनी अति-नी, cl. 1. P. -नयति, -नेतुम्, to<BR>lead over or beyond, to help a person over anything;<BR>to allow to pass away: Intens. A. -नेनीयते, to bring<BR>forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनु
अतिनु अति-नु, Caus. -नावयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>turn away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनुद्
अतिनुद् अति-नुद्, cl. 6. P. A., Ved. -नुदति,<BR>-ते, -नोत्तुम्, to drive by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनेद्
अतिनेद् अति-नेद्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -नेदति,<BR>-दितुम्, to stream or flow over, to foam over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनौ
अतिनौ अति-नौ, औस्, औस्, उ, disembarked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपञ्चा|अतिपंचा
अतिपञ्चा अति-पञ्चा, f. a girl who is past five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपटीक्षेप
अतिपटीक्षेप अति-पटीक्षेप or अ-पटीक्षेप,<BR>अस्, m. omission of removing the theatrical curtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपठ्
अतिपठ् अति-पठ्, Pass, -पठ्यते, to be<BR>proclaimed, named or celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्
अतिपत् अति-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -तितुम्,<BR>to fall or fly by, past, beyond, over; to neglect: Caus.<BR>-पातयति, -यितुम्, to cause to fly by; to drag<BR>away; to make effectless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपतन|अतिपतनं
अति-पतन, अम्, n. act of falling or flying beyond,<BR>passing, missing, transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपतित
अति-पतित, अस्, आ, अम्, missed, transgressed, past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपात|अतिपातः
अति-पात, अस्, m. passing away, lapse; neglect,<BR>transgression; ill-usage, opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातित
अति-पातित, अस्, आ, अम्, quite displaced or broken;<BR>(अम्), n. (in medicine) complete fracture of a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातिन्
अति-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, overtaking, excelling in speed;<BR>(in medicine) running a rapid course, acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपात्य
अति-पात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or proper to be neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्त्र
अतिपत्त्र अति-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the Teak tree;<BR>another tree, Hastikanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपद्
अतिपद् अति-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते, -पत्तुम्,<BR>to go beyond (with acc.), jump over, neglect, trans-<BR>gress: Caus. -पादयति, -यितुम्, to allow to pass by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्ति|अतिपत्तिः
अति-पत्ति, इस्, f. going beyond, passing, lapse;<BR>क्रियातिपत्ति, the passing by of an action unaccom-<BR>plished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपन्न
अति-पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, gone beyond, transgressed,<BR>missed; past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपर|अतिपरः
अतिपर अति-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, having over-<BR>come his enemy or enemies; (अस्), m. a great enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपा
अतिपा अति-पा, Caus. P. -पाययति, -यितुम्,<BR>to give to drink in great quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपादनिचृत्
अतिपादनिचृत् अति-पादनिचृत् or अति-पाद-<BR>निवृत्, त्, f., N. of a Vedic metre of three pādas, con-<BR>taining respectively six, eight and seven syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपितृ
अतिपितृ अति-पितृ, -ता, m. surpassing his<BR>own father.<BR>—अति-पितामह, अस्, m. surpassing his<BR>own paternal grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपू
अतिपू अति-पू, cl. 9. P., Ved. -पुनाति,<BR>-पवितुम्, to purify by overflowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपॄ
अतिपॄ अति-पॄ, P., Ved. -पृणाति (?), Caus.<BR>-पारयति, -यितुम्, to convey across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रकित्
अतिप्रकित् अति-प्र-कित् or -चित्, cl. 3. A., Ved.<BR>-चेकिते, to be distinct or distinguishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रच्यु
अतिप्रच्यु अति-प्र-च्यु, cl. 1. A. -च्यवते,<BR>-च्योतुम्, to pass by: Caus. -च्यावयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause or allow to pass by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रणश्
अतिप्रणश् अति-प्र-णश् (rt. नश्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-णश्यति, -णशितुम् or -णंष्टुम्, to be deprived<BR>of (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रणी
अतिप्रणी अति-प्र-णी (rt. नी), cl. 1. P. -णयति,<BR>-णेतुम्, to lead past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रणुद्
अतिप्रणुद् अति-प्र-णुद् (rt. नुद्), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-णुदति, -ते, -णोत्तुम्, to press a person very strongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रमाण
अतिप्रमाण अति-प्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, past<BR>measure, immense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्राणम्
अतिप्राणम् अति-प्राणम्, ind. above life.<BR>—अतिप्राण-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, dearer than life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रेषित|अतिप्रेषितं
अतिप्रेषित अति-प्रेषित, अम्, n. the time<BR>after the ceremony in which the Praiṣa Mantras are<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिब्रह्मन्
अतिब्रह्मन् अति-ब्रह्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिब्रू
अतिब्रू अति-ब्रू, cl. 2. P. -ब्रवीति, -वक्तुम्,<BR>to insult, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभू
अतिभू अति-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्,<BR>to excel, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभाव
अति-भाव, अस्, m. superiority; overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभूमि|अतिभूमिः
अतिभूमि अति-भूमि, इस्, f. extensive land;<BR>culmination, eminence, superiority; excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभूष्
अतिभूष् अति-भूष्, cl. 10. A. -भूषयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to precede in adorning oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमनुष्यबुद्धि
अतिमनुष्यबुद्धि अति-मनुष्य-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, having a superhuman intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्त्य
अतिमर्त्य अति-मर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्याद|अतिमर्य्याद|अतिमर्य्यादः
अतिमर्याद अति-मर्याद, अस्, आ, अम्, exceeding<BR>the proper limit; (अम्), ind. beyond bounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमात्र|अतिमात्रं
अतिमात्र अति-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, exceeding<BR>the proper measure; (अम्), ind. or अतिमात्र-शस्,<BR>ind. beyond measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानुष
अतिमानुष अति-मानुष, अस्, ई, अम्, super-<BR>human, divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमाम्
अतिमाम् अति-माम् (acc. of अत्य्-अहम्, q. v.),<BR>him or her that surpasses me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमाय
अतिमाय अति-माय, अस्, आ, अम्, emancipated<BR>from Māyā or Illusion; finally liberated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमार
अतिमार अति-मार or अति-भार, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमित
अतिमित 1. अति-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, over mea-<BR>sured, beyond measure, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमित
अतिमित 2. अ-तिमित, अस्, आ, अम्, not moist-<BR>ened, not wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्त|अतिमुक्तः
अतिमुक्त अति-मुक्त and अति-मुक्तक, अस्, m.<BR>(rt. मुच्), N. of certain shrubs or trees; see under<BR>अति (surpassing pearls in whiteness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्ति|अतिमुक्तिः
अति-मुक्ति, इस्, f. final liberation. See under अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुच्य
अति-मुच्य, ind. part. having dismissed or given up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमृत्यु|अतिमृत्युः
अतिमृत्यु अति-मृत्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, overcoming<BR>death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिया
अतिया अति-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -तुम्, to<BR>pass by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियूयम्
अतियूयम् अति-यूयम् (nom. pl. of अति-त्वम्,<BR>q. v.), persons surpassing thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिराजन्
अतिराजन् अति-राजन्, आ, m. an extraordinary<BR>king; superior to a king.<BR>—अति-राजकुमारि, इस्, इस्<BR>or ई, इ, superior to a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिराजय
अतिराजय, nom. P. अतिराजयति, -यितुम्, to sur-<BR>pass a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिराज्ञी
अति-राज्ञी, f. (a woman) superior to a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरात्र|अतिरात्रः
अतिरात्र अति-रात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pre-<BR>pared or performed over-night; (अस्), m. an optional<BR>part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice; commencement<BR>and conclusion of certain sacrificial acts; concluding<BR>Vedic verse chanted on such occasions; N. of a son<BR>of Cākṣuṣa the sixth Manu.<BR>—अतिरात्र-सवनीय-<BR>पशु, उस्, m. the victim sacrificed at the Atirātra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरि
अतिरि अति-रि, neut. of अति-रै, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिच्
अतिरिच् अति-रिच्, Pass. -रिच्यते, to be left<BR>with a surplus, to surpass (in a good or bad sense<BR>with abl. or acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्त|अतिरिक्तः
अति-रिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, left with or as a surplus, left<BR>apart; redundant, unequalled.<BR>—अतिरिकत-ता, f. re-<BR>dundancy, &c.<BR>—अतिरिक्ताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a redundant limb or finger or toe; (अम्), n. a<BR>redundant limb or finger or toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेक|अतिरेकः
अति-रेक or अती-रेक, अस्, m. surplus, excess; redun-<BR>dancy; difference; (अस्, आ, अम्,), redundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेकिन्
अति-रेकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरुच्
अतिरुच् अति-रुच्, cl. 1. P. -रोचति, -चितुम्, to<BR>outshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरुच्
अति-रुच्, क्, m. a horse's fetlock or knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरै
अतिरै अति-रै, आस्, आस्, इ (‘exceeding one's<BR>income’), extravagant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलिहा
अतिलिहा अतिलिहा or अठिल्ला, f. (etymology<BR>uncertain), N. of a Prākṛt metre of four lines, each<BR>containing sixteen Mātras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवयम्
अतिवयम् अति-वयम् (nom. pl. of अत्य्-अहम्,<BR>q. v.), persons surpassing me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तन|अतिवर्तनं|अतिवर्त्तन
अतिवर्तन अति-वर्तन. See under अति-वृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवलित
अतिवलित अति-वलित, अस्, आ, अम्, well sur-<BR>rounded or covered (?), full of folds (?), well supplied (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवह्
अतिवह् अति-वह्, cl. 1. P. -वहति, -वोढुम्,<BR>to carry over or across: Caus. -वाहयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>let time pass, spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहन|अतिवाहनं
अति-वाहन, अम्, n. excessive toiling or enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहित|अतिवाहितः
अति-वाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, swifter than the wind;<BR>(according to Colebrooke) an epithet of the Sūkṣma-<BR>śarīra, also (according to Carey) of the Preta-śarīra, or<BR>misery-enduring body, which is of the size of a<BR>thumb; (अस्), m. an inhabitant of the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाह्य
अति-वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, practicable or proper to be<BR>passed (as time, &c.); (अम्), n. the passing of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवोढृ
अति-वोढृ, ढा, m. one who carries over or across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवास|अतिवासः
अतिवास अति-वास, अस्, m. fast on the day<BR>before performing the Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविद्ध
अतिविद्ध अति-विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. व्यध्),<BR>transfixed, badly wounded.<BR>—अतिविद्ध-भेषज,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, curing deep wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविश्व
अतिविश्व अति-विश्व, अस्, m. (‘superior to all<BR>or to the universe’), N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृत्
अतिवृत् अति-वृत्, cl. 1. A. -वर्तते, -तितुम्,<BR>to pass, surpass, cross; to get over, overcome; to<BR>transgress, violate, offend, especially by unfaithfulness;<BR>to pass away; to delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तन|अतिवर्तनं|अतिवर्त्तन
अति-वर्तन, अम्, n. a pardonable offence or mis-<BR>demeanour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तिन्|अतिवर्त्तिन्
अति-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crossing, passing; guilty of a<BR>pardonable offence or of pardonable irregularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृत्ति|अतिवृत्तिः
अति-वृत्ति, इस्, f. surpassing; hyperbolical meaning;<BR>(in medicine) excessive action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेल|अतिवेलं
अतिवेल अति-वेल, अस्, आ, अम्, passing its<BR>proper boundary, excessive; (अम्), ind. excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्याधिन्
अतिव्याधिन् अति-व्याधिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt.<BR>व्यध्), piercing, wounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्याध्य
अति-व्याध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, vulnerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्करी
अतिशक्करी अति-शक्करी or अति-शक्वरी, f. a<BR>class of metres of four lines, each containing fifteen<BR>syllables. It has eighteen varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्र
अतिशक्र अति-शक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, superior to<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशङ्क्
अतिशङ्क् अति-शङ्क्, cl. 1. A. -शङ्कते, -कितुम्,<BR>to suspect; to be concerned about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशय|अतिशयः
अतिशय अतिशय, &c. See under अति-शी<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशस्त्र
अतिशस्त्र अति-शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, superior to<BR>weapons or missiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशाक्वर
अतिशाक्वर अतिशाक्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, written in<BR>or connected with the Ati-śakvarī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशी
अतिशी अति-शी, cl. 2. A. -शेते, -शयितुम्, to<BR>precede in lying down; to surpass, excel, exceed;<BR>to act as an incubus, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशय|अतिशयः
अति-शय, अस्, m. pre-eminence, eminence; superi-<BR>ority in quality or quantity or numbers; advantageous<BR>result; one of the superhuman qualities attributed to<BR>Jaina Arhats; (अस्, आ, अम्), pre-eminent, superior,<BR>abundant.<BR>—अतिशयम् or अतिशयेन, ind. eminently,<BR>very.<BR>—अतिशयोक्ति (˚य-उक्˚), इस्, f. hyperbolical lan-<BR>guage; extreme assertion; verbosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयन|अतिशयनं
अति-शयन, अस्, आ, अम्, eminent, abundant; (अम्),<BR>ind. excessively.<BR>—अति-शयनी, f., N. of a metre of<BR>four lines, also called चित्रलेखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयित
अति-शयित, अस्, आ, अम्, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयिन्
अति-शयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, excelling, abounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायन|अतिशायनं
अति-शायन, अम्, n. act of excelling; excessiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायिन्
अति-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, excelling, abounding; excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशेत
अति-शेत, अस्, आ, अम्, excelling, exceeding; superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशीतम्
अतिशीतम् अति-शीतम्, ind. past the cold,<BR>after the winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशेष|अतिशेषः
अतिशेष अति-शेष, अस्, m. remainder, rem-<BR>nant, especially of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्रेष्ठ
अतिश्रेष्ठ अति-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, superior<BR>to the best, best of all.<BR>—अतिश्रेष्ठ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्रेयसि|अतिश्रेयसिः
अति-श्रेयसि, इस्, m. a man superior to the most<BR>excellent woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्लिष्
अतिश्लिष् अति-श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. -श्लिष्यति,<BR>-श्लेष्टुम्, to fasten or tie over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्व|अतिश्वः
अतिश्व अति-श्व, अस्, ई, अम्, superior to, or<BR>worse than, a dog; (आ), m., N. of a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिषेल्
अतिषेल् अति-षेल् (rt. सेल् or शेल्), Caus. P.<BR>-षेलयति, -यितुम्, to make one go to a great<BR>distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिष्कद्वरी
अतिष्कद्वरी अति-ष्कद्वरी, f. (rt. स्कन्द्),<BR>(transgressor), a dissolute woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिष्ठत्|अतिष्ठन्त्
अतिष्ठत् अ-तिष्ठत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, not stand-<BR>ing, unstable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिष्ठा
अतिष्ठा अति-ष्ठा (rt. स्था), cl. 1. P. -तिष्ठति,<BR>-ष्ठातुम्, to excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिष्ठा
अति-ष्ठा, f. precedence, superiority; (आस्), m. f.,<BR>Ved. or अति-ष्ठावन्, आ, m. or अतिष्ठा-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, superior in standing, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धा|अतिसंधा
अतिसन्धा अति-सन्-धा (-सम्-धा), cl. 3. P.<BR>A. -दधाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to overreach, de-<BR>ceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धम्|अतिसंधम्
अति-सन्धम्, ind. in violation of an agreement<BR>or of the settled order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धान|अतिसंधान|अतिसंधानं
अति-सन्-धान, अम्, n. overreaching, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धित|अतिसंधित
अति-सन्-धित, अस्, आ, अम्, overreached, cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धेय|अतिसंधेय
अति-सन्-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, easy to be conciliated<BR>or settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्व|अतिसर्वः|अतिसर्व्व
अतिसर्व अति-सर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, superior to<BR>all; (अस्), m. the supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसांवत्सर
अतिसांवत्सर अति-सांवत्सर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>extending over more than a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसाम्या
अतिसाम्या अति-साम्या, f. the sweet juice of<BR>the Bengal Madder, Rubia Manjith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृ
अतिसृ अति-सृ, Caus. P. -सारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to extend; to exert (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर|अतिसरः
अति-सर, अस्, m., Ved. effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसार|अतिसारः
अति-सार or अती-सार, अस्, m. violent straining at<BR>stool, dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारकिन्
अति-सारकिन् or अती-सारकिन् or अति-सारिन् or अती-<BR>सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, afflicted with dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृज्
अतिसृज् अति-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति, -स्रष्टुम्,<BR>to dismiss, abandon; to leave as a remnant; to remit,<BR>forgive; to give away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्ग|अतिसर्गः
अति-सर्ग, अस्, m. act of parting with, dismissal,<BR>giving away, granting permission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्जन|अतिसर्जनं|अतिसर्ज्जनं
अति-सर्जन, अम्, n. liberality, granting, engaging,<BR>a gift; sending out of the world, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृज्य
अति-सृज्य, ind. part. having dismissed, &c.; ex-<BR>cessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृप्
अतिसृप् अति-सृप्, cl. 1. P. -सर्पति, -सर्प्तुम्<BR>or -स्रप्तुम्, to glide over, get over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसेन
अतिसेन अति-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a prince,<BR>a son of Śambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौपर्ण
अतिसौपर्ण अति-सौपर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, superior<BR>to Suparṇa's or Garuḍa's (vision, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्त्रि
अतिस्त्रि अति-स्त्रि, इस्, इस् or ई, इ, surpassing a<BR>woman; Gram. 123. b. The feminine may end in ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहस्तय
अतिहस्तय अति-हस्तय, Nom. (fr. अति-हस्त),<BR>P. अतिहस्तयति, -यितुम्, to stretch out the hands; (fr.<BR>अतिहस्तिन्), to overtake on an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहिमम्
अतिहिमम् अति-हिमम्, ind. after the cold<BR>or the frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अती
अती अती (अति-इ), cl. 2. P. अत्य्-एति, -तुम्,<BR>to pass, elapse, pass over, overflow; to pass on; to<BR>get over; to defer; to enter; to overcome, overtake,<BR>outdo; to pass by, neglect; to overstep violate; to<BR>be redundant; to die: Intens. अतीयते, to overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीत|अतीतं|अतीतः
अतीत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone by, past, passed away,<BR>dead; having gone through, having got over or be-<BR>yond, having passed by, having neglected; negligent;<BR>passed, left behind; excessive; (अस्), m. modern N.<BR>of a particular Śaiva sect; (अम्), n. the past.<BR>—अतीत-<BR>काल, अस्, m. the past time or tense.<BR>—अतीत-नौक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, landed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीत्वरी
अतीत्वरी (˚ति-इत्˚), f., Ved. (transgressor), a bad<BR>woman.<BR>—अत्य्-अय, अत्य्-आय, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीक्ष्ण
अतीक्ष्ण अ-तीक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, not sharp,<BR>blunt, dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रिय|अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं|अतीन्द्रियः
अतीन्द्रिय अतीन्द्रिय (अति-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>yond the congnisance of (इन्द्रिय) the senses; (अस्), m.<BR>in the Sānkhya phil. the soul or पुरुष; (अम्), n.<BR>in the Sānkhya phil. nature or प्रधान; in the<BR>Vedānta phil. the mind or मनस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीरेक|अतीरेकः
अतीरेक, अतीसार। See under अति-रिच्,<BR>अति-सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव
अतीव अतीव (अति-इव), ind. exceedingly,<BR>very; excessively, too; quite; surpassing (with the<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव्र
अतीव्र अ-तीव्र, अस्, आ, अम्, not sharp, blunt;<BR>not pungent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुङ्ग
अतुङ्ग अ-तुङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, not tall, short,<BR>dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुन्द|अतुंद
अतुन्द अ-तुन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, not stout, thin,<BR>lank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुर
अतुर अ-तुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not liberal,<BR>not rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल|अतुलः
अतुल अ-तुल, अस्, आ, अम्, unequalled; (अस्),<BR>m. (destitute of weight), the Sesamum seed and plant.<BR>—अ-तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unequalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुष
अतुष अ-तुष, अस्, आ, अम्, without husks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुषारकर|अतुषारकरः
अतुषारकर अ-तुषार-कर, अस्, m. (having<BR>not cold rays), the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुष्टि
अतुष्टि अ-तुष्टि, इस्, f. displeasure, discontent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुहिन
अतुहिन अ-तुहिन, Ved. not cold; used in<BR>compounds, thus अतुहिन-धामन्, आ, or अतुहिन-<BR>रश्मि, इस्, or अतुहिन-रुचि, इस्, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूतुजि
अतूतुजि अ-तूतुजि, इस्, इस्, ई, Ved. not quick,<BR>slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूर्त|अतूर्त्त
अतूर्त अ-तूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not in a<BR>hurry; not outrun or outdone or obstructed; unhurt;<BR>(अम्), n. illimited space.<BR>—अतूर्त-दक्ष, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. having designs that cannot be obstructed (epithet<BR>of the Aśvins).<BR>—अतूर्त-पथिन्, अन्थास्, m., Ved.<BR>having a path that cannot be obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृणाद|अतृणादः
अतृणाद अ-तृणाद (˚ण-अद), अस्, m. (not an<BR>eater of grass), a newly-born calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृण्या
अतृण्या अ-तृण्या, f. a small quantity or<BR>short supply of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृदिल
अतृदिल अ-तृदिल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>fragile, solid, or ‘having no holes.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप
अतृप अ-तृप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्णुवत्|अतृप्णुवन्त्
अतृप्णुवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. insatiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्त
अ-तृप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unsatisfied, insatiable, eager.<BR>—अतृप्त-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, looking with eagerness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्ति|अतृप्तिः
अ-तृप्ति, इस्, f. unsatisfied condition, insatiability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृषित
अतृषित अ-तृषित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>thirsty, not greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृष्णज्
अ-तृष्णज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. not thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृष्य
अ-तृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. beyond the reach of<BR>thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृष्यत्|अतृष्यन्त्
अ-तृष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. not thirsting after,<BR>not greedy, not eager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्
अतेजस् अ-तेजस्, n. absence of brightness<BR>or vigour; dimness, shade, shadow; feebleness, dul-<BR>ness, insignificance; (आस्, आस्, अस्), or अ-तेजस्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or अ-तेजस्विन् ई, इनी, इ, not bright, dim, not<BR>vigorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतोषणीय
अतोषणीय अ-तोषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, impossible<BR>or improper to be pleased or appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्क|अत्कः
अत्क अत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. अत्), travelling;<BR>(अस्), m. a traveller; a limb or member; (Ved.) water,<BR>liquid; lightning; armour, mail; garment; N. of an<BR>Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्कील|अत्कीलः
अत्कील अत्कील or उत्कील, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of some Vedic hymns, a descendant of Viśvā-<BR>mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तलि
अत्तलि अत्तलि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तव्य
अत्तव्य अत्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. अद्), fit or<BR>proper to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ति|अत्तिः
अत्ति, इस्, m., Ved. an eater; f., see also s. v. अत्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ, ता, m. an eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ता
अत्ता अत्ता, f. (etym. uncertain, probably<BR>a word borrowed from the Deccan, occurring chiefly<BR>in dramas); a mother; mother's sister; elder sister;<BR>(in Prākṛt) a mother-in-law. See अक्का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ति|अत्तिः
अत्ति, इस्, or अत्तिका, f. elder sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्र
अत्त्र, अत्त्रि, अत्त्रिन्, अत्त्र, &c. See अत्र,<BR>अत्रि, अत्रिन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्न|अत्नं|अत्नः
अत्न अत्न, अस्, or अत्नु, उस्, m. (fr. अत्), the sun.<BR>अत्य, अस्, m., Ved. a courser, steed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंहस्
अत्यंहस् अत्य्-अंहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. beyond<BR>the reach of (or emancipated from) sin or evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्नि|अत्यग्निः
अत्यग्नि अत्य्-अग्नि, इस्, m. morbidly rapid<BR>digestion, see s. v. अति; (इस्, इस्, इ), surpassing fire.<BR>—अत्य्-अग्नि-सोमार्क (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, brighter<BR>than fire or the moon or the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्निष्टोम|अत्यग्निष्टोमः
अत्यग्निष्टोम अत्य्-अग्निष्टोम, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the optional second part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice;<BR>the Vedic verse chanted at the close of that cere-<BR>mony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यङ्कुश|अत्यंकुश
अत्यङ्कुश अत्य्-अङ्कुश, अस्, आ, अम्, past the<BR>(elephant-driver's) hook, unmanageable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यङ्गुल
अत्यङ्गुल अत्य्-अङ्गुल, अस्, आ, अम्, exceeding<BR>an aṅgula (finger's breadth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यतिक्रम्
अत्यतिक्रम् अत्य्-अति-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. -क्रामति,<BR>-क्रमितुम्, to approach for sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यनिल
अत्यनिल अत्य्-अनिल, अस्, आ, अम्, surpassing<BR>the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्त|अत्यंत|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यन्त अत्य्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, past its proper<BR>end or limit; excessive, very great or strong, &c.;<BR>endless, unbroken, perpetual; absolute, perfect; (अम्),<BR>ind. excessively, exceedingly; in perpetuity; absolutely,<BR>completely; to the end.<BR>—अत्यन्त-कोपन, अस्, आ,<BR>आम्, very passionate, outrageous.<BR>—अत्यन्त-ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, going or walking very much or very fast.<BR>—अत्यन्त-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, completely pertinent;<BR>always applicable.<BR>—अत्यन्त-गति, इस्, f. complete ac-<BR>complishment; (in grammar) the sense of ‘completely.’<BR>—अत्यन्त-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going or walking very<BR>much or very fast.<BR>—अत्यन्त-गुणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having<BR>extraordinary qualities.<BR>—अत्यन्त-तिरस्कृत-वाच्य-<BR>ध्वनि, इस्, f. (in rhetoric) a metaphoric or hyper-<BR>bolical use of depreciating language.<BR>—अत्यन्त-<BR>पीडन, अम्, n. act of giving excessive pain.<BR>—अत्यन्-<BR>त-वासिन्, ई, m. a Brāhman who perpetually lodges as a<BR>student with his teacher.<BR>—अत्यन्त-संयोग, अस्, m.<BR>(in grammar) immediate proximity.<BR>—अत्यन्त-सम्-<BR>पर्क, अस्, m. excessive sexual intercourse.<BR>—अत्यन्त-<BR>सुकुमार, अस्, ई, अम्, very tender; (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of grain, Panicum Italicum.<BR>—अत्यन्ताभाव (˚त-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. absolute non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिक|अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिकः
1. अत्यन्तिक or अत्यन्तिन, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>much or fast or far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिक|अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिकः
अत्यन्तिक 2. अत्य्-अन्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, too close,<BR>too near, very close; (अम्), n. too great nearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय अत्य्-अय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. इ with अति, see<BR>अती), passing, lapse, passage; passing away, perishing,<BR>death; danger, risk, evil, suffering; transgression, guilt,<BR>vice; getting at, attacking; overcoming, mastering<BR>(mentally); a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिक
अत्ययिक better आत्ययिक, अस्, आ, अम्, tempo-<BR>rary, occasional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिन्
अत्ययिन्, ई, इनी, इ, passing, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यराति
अत्यराति अत्य्-अराति, इस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Janantapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थ|अत्यर्थं
अत्यर्थ अत्य्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम् (beyond its<BR>proper worth), exorbitant, excessive.<BR>—अत्यर्थम्,<BR>ind. excessively, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्द्
अत्यर्द् अत्य्-अर्द्, cl. 1. P. -अर्दति, -दितुम्, to<BR>press hard, to distress greatly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्ह्
अत्यर्ह् अत्य्-अर्ह्, cl. 1. P. -अर्हति, -हितुम्, to<BR>excel in worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यवि
अत्यवि अत्य्-अवि, इस्, m., Ved. passing over<BR>or through the strainer, which consisted of sheep's<BR>wool or a sheep's tail (an epithet of Soma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यश्
अत्यश् अत्य्-अश्, cl. 9. P. -अश्नाति, -अशितुम्, to<BR>precede in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यष्टि|अत्यष्टिः
अत्यष्टि अत्य्-अष्टि, इस्, f. a metre of four<BR>lines, each containing seventeen syllables; the number<BR>seventeen.<BR>—अत्यष्टि-सामग्री, f. title of a particular<BR>book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यस्
अत्यस् 1. अत्य्-अस् (अति-अस्), cl. 2. P. -अस्ति, to<BR>excel, surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यस्
अत्यस् 2. अत्य्-अस् (अति-अस्), cl. 4. P. -अस्यति,<BR>-सितुम्, to shoot beyond or at, overpower (with<BR>arrows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यस्त
अत्य्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having shot beyond, having<BR>surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यहम्
अत्यहम् अत्य्-अहम्, surpassing me, (a ficti-<BR>tious word coined by grammarians.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यह्न
अत्यह्न अत्य्-अह्न, अस्, आ, अम्, exceeding a day<BR>in duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याकार|अत्याकारः
अत्याकार अत्य्-आ-कार, अस्, m. (rt. कृ), con-<BR>tempt, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याक्रम्
अत्याक्रम् अत्य्-आ-क्रम् (अति-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमितुम्, to walk past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचार|अत्याचारं|अत्याचारः
अत्याचार अत्य्-आचार, अस्, m. performance of<BR>works of supererogation; (अस्, आ, अम्,), negligent of<BR>or departing from the established customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यादित्य
अत्यादित्य अत्य्-आदित्य, अस्, आ, अम्, surpassing<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याधान|अत्याधानं
अत्याधान अत्य्-आ-धान, अम्, n. act of im-<BR>posing or placing upon; imposition, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यानन्दा|अत्यानंदा
अत्यानन्दा अत्य्-आनन्दा, f. morbid indiffer-<BR>ence (of a wife) to the pleasure of sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याय|अत्यायः
अत्याय अत्य्-आय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. इ with अति),<BR>transgression, excess; (अस्, आ, अम्), going beyond,<BR>transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यायत्
अत्यायत् अत्य्-आ-यत् (अति-आ˚), cl. 1. A. -यतते,<BR>-तितुम्, to make extraordinary efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याल|अत्यालः
अत्याल अत्य्-आल, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>Plumbago Rosea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याश्रमिन्
अत्याश्रमिन् अत्य्-आश्रमिन्, ई, m. (superior to<BR>the four Āśramas), an ascetic of the highest degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यास|अत्यासः
अत्यास अत्य्-आस, अस्, m. act of allowing to<BR>elapse; only used in the acc. as the concluding part of<BR>compound words, thus द्व्यहात्यासम्, after an in-<BR>terval of two days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ता
अत्युक्ता अत्य्-उक्ता or अत्य्-उक्था, f., N. of a<BR>class of metres of four lines, each containing two<BR>syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ष्
अत्युक्ष् अत्य्-उक्ष् (अति-उक्ष्), cl. 1.P. -उक्षति,<BR>-क्षितुम्, to surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्क्रम्
अत्युत्क्रम् अत्य्-उत्-क्रम् (अति-उत्˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमितुम्, to surpass, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युपध
अत्युपध अत्य्-उपध, अस्, आ, अम्, superior to<BR>any test, tried, trustworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युह्
अत्युह् अत्य्-उह्. See अत्य्-ऊह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूमशा
अत्यूमशा अत्य्-ऊमशा, ind. (etym. unknown),<BR>particle of abuse, used in comp. with अस्, भू, कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूर्मि
अत्यूर्मि अत्य्-ऊर्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. overflowing,<BR>bubbling over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूह्
अत्यूह् अत्य्-ऊह् (अति-ऊह्), cl. 1. P. ऊहति,<BR>हितुम्, to convey across. Spelt अत्य्-उह् in some<BR>forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूह|अत्यूहः
अत्यूह अत्य्-ऊह, अस्, m. close meditation; a<BR>gallinule, a peacock; (आ), f. a plant, Jasminum Vil-<BR>losum or Nyctanthes Tristis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यृज्
अत्यृज् अत्य्-ऋज् (अति-ऋज्), cl. 1. P. A. -अर्जति,<BR>-ते, -जितुम्, to convey across, admit; to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्येष्
अत्येष् अत्य्-एष्, cl. 1. P. -एषति, -षितुम्, to<BR>glide over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र 1. अ-त्र or Ved. अ-त्रा, ind. (fr. pro-<BR>nominal base अ substituted for एतद्; the word अत्र<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">Page0017-b+ 74</a>]<BR>being often used for the loc. case एतस्मिन्), in<BR>this matter, in this respect; in this place, here; at<BR>this time; there; then.<BR>—अत्र-दघ्न, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>reaching so far up, having this (or that) stature.<BR>—अत्र-भवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, honourable (used chiefly<BR>in dramatic language, to indicate a person who is<BR>present).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रत्य
अत्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with this place,<BR>produced or found here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र 2. अ-त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. त्रै), Ved. not<BR>enjoying (or not affording) protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र 3. अत्र, अस्, m. (for अत्-त्र, fr. rt. अद्),<BR>Ved. a devourer, demon; a Rākṣasa; (अम्), n.,<BR>Ved. food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि, इस्, m. (etymologically अत्-त्रि, fr. rt. अद्), a de-<BR>vourer; N. of a great Ṛṣi, author of a number of Vedic<BR>hymns; (in astronomy) one of the seven stars of<BR>the Great Bear.<BR>—अत्रयस्, pl. m. the descendants of<BR>Atri.<BR>—अत्रि-चतुरह, अस्, m. (the four days of Atri),<BR>N. of a sacrifice.<BR>—अत्रि-जात, अस्, m. the moon, said to<BR>have been produced by Atri's look; for अ-त्रि-जात, see<BR>below.<BR>—अत्रि-दृग्-ज, अत्रि-नेत्र-ज or अत्रि-नेत्र-<BR>प्रसूत or अत्रि-नेत्र-प्रभव or अत्रि-नेत्र-<BR>सूत, अस्, or अत्रि-नेत्र-भू, ऊस्, m. the moon; (in<BR>arithm.) the number one.<BR>—अत्रि-भारद्वाजिका, f.<BR>marriage of Atri and Bhāradvājī.<BR>—अत्रि-वत्, ind.<BR>like Atri.<BR>—अत्रि-संहिता, आ, or अत्रि-स्मृति, इस्, f.<BR>the code ascribed to Atri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन्, ई, m. a devourer, demon; a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रप
अत्रप अ-त्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रवस्
अत्रवस् अत्रवस्, ind. (a doubtful word),<BR>the year before last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रस्नु
अत्रस्नु अ-त्रस्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, or अ-त्रास, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिजात|अत्रिजातः
अत्रिजात अ-त्रि-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, (not born<BR>thrice, but twice); a man belonging to one of the<BR>first three classes [for अत्रि-जात, see s. v. अत्रि].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रैव
अत्रैव अत्रैव (अत्र-एव), ind. on this very<BR>spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्वच्
अत्वच् अ-त्वच्, क्, क्, क्, skinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्वरा
अत्वरा अ-त्वरा, f. freedom from or absence<BR>of haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ अथ or Ved. अथा, ind. (probably fr.<BR>pronom. base अ), an auspicious an inceptive particle,<BR>often not easily expressed in English; now; then;<BR>moreover; rather; certainly; but; else; what? how<BR>else ? &c.<BR>—अथ-किम्, ind. how else? what else?<BR>certainly, assuredly, sure enough.<BR>—अथ-किमु, ind.<BR>how much more; so much the more.<BR>—अथ-च, ind.<BR>moreover, and likewise.<BR>—अथ-तु, ind. but, on the<BR>contrary.<BR>—अथ-वा, ind. or; (when repeated) either<BR>or; or rather; or perhaps; what? is it not so? &c.<BR>—अथवापि (˚वा-अपि), ind. or, rather.<BR>—अथातस्<BR>(˚थ-अत्˚), ind. now.<BR>—अथानन्तरम् (˚थ-अन्˚),<BR>ind. now.<BR>—अथापि (˚थ-अपि), ind. so much the<BR>more; moreover; therefore; thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथो, ind. (has much the same meaning as अथ, and<BR>probably the same etymology), now; likewise; next;<BR>therefore.<BR>—अथो-वा, ind. the same as अथ-वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथरि|अथरिः
अथरि अथरि, इस्, or अथरी, f. (generally in<BR>the plural; etymology doubtful; said to be fr. rt. अत्,<BR>to go, or fr. an obsolete rt. अथ्), meaning doubtful,<BR>probably spark or flame having a pointed shape;<BR>(according to others) the point of a lance; (according<BR>to others) a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्य
अथर्य, अस्, m., Ved. lambent; moving con-<BR>stantly; or (according to some) pointed like a lance;<BR>or (according to some) shooting forth points like<BR>those of a lance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्य
अथर्य, nom. P. अथर्यति, Ved. to move con-<BR>stántly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्यु
अथर्यु, उस्, m., Ved. = अथर्य, अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वन्|अथर्व्वन्
अथर्वन् अथर्वन्, आ, m. (said to be fr. an<BR>obsolete word अथर्, fire), a priest who has to do with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">Page0017-c+ 76</a>]<BR>fire and Soma; a Brāhman; N. of the priest who is said<BR>to have been the first to obtain fire and offer Soma and<BR>prayers: he is represented as a Prajāpati, as Brahmā's<BR>eldest son, as the first learner and earliest teacher of<BR>the Brahma-vidyā, as the author of the Atharva-veda,<BR>as identical with Aṅgiras, as the father of Agni, &c.:<BR>epithet of Śiva, Vaśiṣṭha, Soma, Prāṇa; (आ, अ), m. n.<BR>the fourth or Atharva-veda, consisting chiefly of for-<BR>mulas intended to obviate the effects of any mistake<BR>or untoward incident attending the performance of<BR>a sacrifice.<BR>—अथर्वाणस्, pl. m. descendants of<BR>Atharvan, often coupled with those of Aṅgiras and<BR>Bhṛgu; the hymns of the Atharva-veda.<BR>—अथर्व-<BR>भूत, आस्, m. pl. (who have become Atharvans),<BR>epithet of the twelve Maharṣis.<BR>—अथर्व-वत्, ind.<BR>like Atharvan or his descendants.<BR>—अथर्व-विद्, त्, m.<BR>one versed in the Atharva-veda (a qualification essen-<BR>tial to the special class of priests called Brāhmaṇas).<BR>—अथर्व-वेद, अस्, m., N. of the fourth Veda, which<BR>strictly speaking is not a Veda at all, like the Ṛg,<BR>Yajur, and Sāma-vedas, but a collection of formulas<BR>to avert the consequences of mistakes or mishaps in<BR>sacrifices.<BR>—अथर्व-शिखा, f. title of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—अथर्व-शिरस्, n. = preceding; (आस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Mahāpuruṣa.<BR>—अथर्व-हृदय, अम्, n. title of<BR>a Pariśiṣṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व|अथर्वः|अथर्व्व
अथर्व, अस्, m., N. of Brahmā's eldest son, to<BR>whom he revealed the Brahma-vidyā. See अथर्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वण|अथर्वणः|अथर्व्वण|अथर्व्वणः
अथर्वण, अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वणि|अथर्वणिः|अथर्व्वणि|अथर्व्वणिः
अथर्वणि, इस्, better आथर्वणि, m. a Brāhman<BR>versed in the Atharva-veda; a family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरस्|अथर्वांगिरस्
अथर्वाङ्गिरस् (˚व-अङ्˚), आस्, m. a member of the<BR>sacerdotal race or class called अथर्वाङ्गिरसस्, m.<BR>pl., i. e. the descendants of Atharvan and of Aṅgiras;<BR>this latter word is also a name of the hymns of the<BR>Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाङ्गिरस|अथर्वांगिरस|अथर्वाङ्गिरसः
अथर्वाङ्गिरस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the preceding), con-<BR>nected with the sacerdotal class called Atharvāṅgiras;<BR>(अम्), n. the work or office of the Atharvāṅgiras;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the hymns of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाण|अथर्वाणं|अथर्वाणः
अथर्वाण, अम्, n. the work, i. e. ritual of the<BR>Atharva-veda.<BR>—अथर्वाण-विद्, त्, m. one versed in<BR>that ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वी
अथर्वी, f., Ved. (doubtful) not moving (?); pierced<BR>by a lance (?); surrounded by fire (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद् अद्, cl. 2. P. अत्ति, आद, अत्स्यति, अत्तुम्,<BR>to eat, devour; to destroy [cf. Lith. edmi;<BR>Slav. jamj for jadmj; Gr. ἔδω Lat. edo; Goth.<BR>rt. AT, pres. ita; Germ. essen; Eng. to eat;<BR>Arm. utem].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद्, त्, त्, त्, at the end of compounds, eating; as<BR>मत्स्याद्, त्, त्, त्, eating fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद|अदः
अद or अदक, अस्, आ, अम्, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्|अदन्त्
1. अदत्, अन्, अती, अत्, eating. (For अ-दत्, see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन|अदनं
अदन, अम्, n. act of eating; food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदनीय
अदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eaten, what may be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तव्य
अत्तव्य, अत्ति, अत्त्रि, अद्मन्, अद्य, अद्वन्, &c.,<BR>see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्ष
अदक्ष अ-दक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, not handy,<BR>unskilful, awkward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अदक्षिण अ-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, not handy;<BR>not right, left; not giving or bringing in a dakṣiṇā<BR>or present to the priest.<BR>—अदक्षिण-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>awkwardness; peculiarity of not bringing in a dakṣiṇā.<BR>—अदक्षिणीय or अदक्षिण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>entitled to a dakṣiṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदग्ध
अदग्ध अ-दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not burnt, not<BR>scorched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड|अदंड
अदण्ड अ-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, free from punish-<BR>ment; (अम्), n. impunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड्य|अदंड्य
अ-दण्ड्य or अ-दण्डनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>deserving punishment; exempt from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्|अदन्त्
अदत् 2. अ-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, or अदत्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, toothless. (For अदत्, see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्त|अदत्तं
अदत्त अ-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not given; given<BR>unjustly; not given in marriage; having given nothing;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">Page0018-a+ 72</a>]<BR>(आ), f. an unmarried girl; (अम्), n. a donation which<BR>is null and void.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्त्वा
अ-दत्त्वा, ind. not having given, without having<BR>given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्रया
अ-दत्रया, ind., Ved. not through a present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदद्र्यञ्च्|अदद्र्यंच्
अदद्र्यञ्च् अदद्र्य्-अञ्च्, अङ्, ईची, अक् (a word<BR>coined by grammarians, fr. अदस् + अञ्च्), inclining or<BR>going to that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन|अदनं
अदन अदन, अदनीय. See under अद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त|अदंत|अदन्तः
अदन्त 1. अ-दन्त or अ-दन्तक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>toothless; (अस्), m. a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त्य|अदंत्य
अ-दन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not suitable for the teeth;<BR>not dental; injurious to the teeth; (अम्), n. tooth-<BR>lessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त|अदंत|अदन्तः
अदन्त 2. अद्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (in gram.)<BR>ending in अत्, i. e. in the short inherent vowel अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्ध
अदब्ध अ-दब्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दम्भ् or<BR>दभ्), Ved. not deceived or tampered with, unim-<BR>paired, unbroken, pure.<BR>—अदब्ध-धीति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. whose works are unimpaired.<BR>—अदब्ध-व्रत,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. whose devotions or religious observances<BR>are unbroken.<BR>—अदब्ध-व्रत-प्रमति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. of unbroken observances and superior mind; of<BR>superior mind from having unbroken observances.<BR>—अदब्धायु (˚ध-आयु), उस्, m., Ved. having un-<BR>impaired vigour or pure food; leaving uninjured the<BR>man who sacrifices.<BR>—अदब्धासु (˚ध-असु), उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. having a pure life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

