अदू अ-दू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. dilatory, without<BR>zeal, not worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदून
अदून अ-दून, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दु), uninjured,<BR>unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूर
अदूर अ-दूर, अस्, आ, अम्, not distant, near;<BR>(अम्), n. vicinity.<BR>—अदूरे or अदूरात् or अदूरतस्,<BR>ind. (with abl. or gen.) not far, near; soon.<BR>—अदूर-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, situated at no great distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूषित
अदूषित अ-दूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, unvitiated;<BR>unspotted, irreproachable.<BR>—अदूषित-धी, ईस्, m. pos-<BR>sessing an uncorrupted mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृढ
अदृढ अ-दृढ, अस्, आ, अम्, not firm; not<BR>decided, irresolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृपित
अदृपित अ-दृपित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दृप्), Ved.<BR>not treated haughtily (?), not thoughtless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृप्त
अदृप्त, अस्, अ, अम्, Ved. not conceited, not vain.<BR>—अदृप्त-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, having not vain de-<BR>signs; sober-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृप्यत्|अदृप्यन्त्
अदृप्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. not conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्
अदृश् अ-दृश्, क्, क्, क् (rt. दृश्), sightless,<BR>blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्य|अदृश्यं
अ-दृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, invisible, latent; not fit to<BR>be seen.<BR>—अदृश्य-करण, अम्, n. act of rendering<BR>invisible; title of a part of a treatise on magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्यत्|अदृश्यन्त्
अ-दृश्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, invisible; (ई), f., N. of<BR>Vasiṣṭha's daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्ट|अदृष्टं|अदृष्टः
अ-दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, unseen, unforeseen; invisible;<BR>not experienced; unobserved, unknown; unsanction-<BR>ed; (अस्), m., Ved., N. of some venomous substance or<BR>vermin; (अम्), n. unforeseen danger or calamity; that<BR>which is beyond the reach of observation or conscious-<BR>ness; especially the merit or demerit attaching to a<BR>man's conduct in one state of existence (such as a<BR>former birth), and the corresponding (apparently arbi-<BR>trary) reward or punishment with which he is visited<BR>in another (which may be either the present life or a<BR>future birth); destiny, fate; luck, bad luck.<BR>—अदृष्ट-<BR>कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, one who has not seen practice.<BR>—अदृष्ट-काम, अस्, m. passionate attachment to<BR>an object that has never been seen.<BR>—अदृष्ट-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced or resulting from fate.<BR>—अदृष्ट-<BR>नर or अदृष्ट-पुरुष, अस्, m. (no third person<BR>or mediator being seen), a treaty concluded by the<BR>parties personally.<BR>—अदृष्ट-पर-सामर्थ्य, अस्,<BR>m. one who has not experienced the power of an<BR>enemy.<BR>—अदृष्ट-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, never seen<BR>before.<BR>—अदृष्ट-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having con-<BR>sequences that are not yet visible; (अम्), n. result or<BR>consequence which is not yet visible, i. e. hidden in<BR>the future.<BR>—अदृष्ट-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having an in-<BR>visible shape.<BR>—अदृष्ट-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, connected<BR>with or coming from destiny; lucky or unlucky;<BR>fortunate.<BR>—अदृष्ट-हन्, आ, m., Ved. destroyer<BR>of venomous vermin.<BR>—अदृष्टार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a transcendental object, metaphysical,<BR>having an object not evident to the senses (as a<BR>science).<BR>—अदृष्टाश्रुत-पूर्वत्व (˚ट-अश्˚), अम्,<BR>n. quality of never having been seen or heard before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टि|अदृष्टिः
अ-दृष्टि, इस्, or अ-दृष्टिका, f. a displeased or<BR>malicious look, an evil eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेय
अदेय अ-देय, अस्, आ, अम्, improper or unfit<BR>to be given; (अम्), n. an object which, in law, it is<BR>either not right or not necessary to give or surrender.<BR>—अदेय-दान, अम्, n. an illegal gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेव|अदेवः
अदेव अ-देव, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दिव्), not divine,<BR>not of divine origin, not referring to any deity; godless,<BR>impious; (अस्), m. one who is not a god.<BR>—अदेव-<BR>मातृक, अस्, आ, अम्, not having the gods as mothers,<BR>not suckled by any deity, i. e. not rained upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवक
अ-देवक, अस्, आ, अम्, not referring to or intended<BR>for any deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवता
अ-देवता, f. one who is not a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवत्र
अ-देवत्र or अ-देवत्रा, ind., Ved. not towards<BR>the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवयत्|अदेवयन्त्
अ-देवयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or अदेवयु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. indifferent to the gods, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदैव
अ-दैव, अस्, ई, अम्, not referring to or connected<BR>with the gods or with their action; not predetermined<BR>by them or by fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवृघ्नी
अदेवृघ्नी अ-देवृ-घ्नी, f., Ved. not de-<BR>structive to her brother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेश|अदेशः
अदेश अ-देश, अस्, m. (rt. दिश्), a wrong place,<BR>an improper place.<BR>—अ-देश-काल, अम्, n. wrong<BR>place and time.<BR>—अदेश-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, grown in a<BR>wrong place.<BR>—अदेश-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, out of place,<BR>in the wrong place, one absent from his country, an<BR>absentee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेश्य
अ-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, improper or unfit to be or-<BR>dered or advised or indicated; not on the spot, not<BR>present on the occasion referred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोमद
अदोमद अ-दोम-द or अ-दोम-ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. not occasioning inconvenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोमय
अदोमय अदो-मय, &c. See अदस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोह|अदोहः
अदोह अ-दोह, अस्, m. (rt. दुह्), season when<BR>milking is impracticable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोग्धृ
अ-दोग्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ (not milking), not<BR>exacting; considerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्ग|अद्गः
अद्ग अद्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अद्), a sacrificial<BR>cake, also called पुरोडाश; (according to others) an<BR>oblation of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्ट्
अद्ट् अद्ट् or अद्ड् अद्ड्. See. s. v. अट्ट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धा
अद्धा अद्-धा, ind. (fr. अद् or अ, this),<BR>Ved. in this way; manifestly; certainly, truly.<BR>—अद्-<BR>धा-तमाम्, ind., Ved. most certainly.<BR>—अद्धा-<BR>पुरुष, अस्, m., Ved. a veritable or true man.<BR>—अद्धा-बोधेय, आस्, m. pl. adherents of a parti-<BR>cular Śākhā or recension of the white Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धाति|अद्धातिः
अद्धाति, इस्, m., Ved. a wise man, a seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्ध्यालोहकर्ण
अद्ध्यालोहकर्ण अद्ध्या-लोह-कर्ण, अस्, आ, or<BR>ई, अम्, Ved. having ears quite red (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुत|अद्भुतं|अद्भुतः
अद्भुत अद्भुत, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps cor-<BR>rupted from अति-भूत, ‘exceeding that which is;’<BR>see 1. अत्), transcendental, supernatural, prodigious,<BR>wonderful, marvellous; (अस्), m. the marvellous<BR>(in style); surprise; N. of the Indra of the ninth<BR>Manvantara; (अम्), n. a marvel, a wonder, a prodigy.<BR>—अद्भुत-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, performing wonderful<BR>works; exhibiting wonderful workmanship.<BR>—अद्भु-<BR>त-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. possessing wonderful in-<BR>telligence.<BR>—अद्भुत-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>wonderful smell.<BR>—अद्भुत-तम, अम्, n. an extra-<BR>ordinary wonder.<BR>—अद्भुत-त्व, अम्, n. wonderful-<BR>ness.<BR>—अद्भुत-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>wonderful aspect.<BR>—अद्भुत-धर्म, अस्, m. a<BR>system or series of marvels or prodigies.<BR>—अद्भुत-<BR>ब्राक्मण, अम्, title of a portion of a Brāhmaṇa<BR>belonging to the Sāma-veda.<BR>—अद्भुत-भीम-<BR>कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, performing wonderful and fearful<BR>works.<BR>—अद्भुत-रस, अस्, m. the marvellous style<BR>(of poetry).<BR>—अद्भुत-रामायण, अम्, n. title of<BR>a work ascribed to Vālmīki.<BR>—अद्भुत-रूप, अस्, आ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">Page0019-b+ 76</a>]<BR>or ई, अम्, having a wonderful shape.<BR>—अद्भुत-<BR>शान्ति, इस्, m. or f. (?), N. of the sixty-seventh Pariśiṣṭa<BR>of the Atharva-veda.<BR>—अद्भुत-सङ्काश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>resembling a wonder.<BR>—अद्भुत-सार, अस्, m. the<BR>wonderful resin (of the Khadira tree, Mimosa<BR>Catechu); title of a book on the “Essence of Prodi-<BR>gies.”<BR>—अद्भुत-स्वन, अस्, m. (having a wonderful<BR>sound or voice), a N. of Śiva.<BR>—अद्भुतैनस् (˚त-<BR>एन्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one in whom no fault is visible.<BR>—अद्भुतोत्तरकाण्ड (˚त-उत्त्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work, an appendix to or rather an imitation of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—अद्भुतोपम (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>resembling a wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मन्
अद्मन् अद्मन्, अ, n. (fr. rt. अद्), Ved. eating;<BR>a meal; a house.<BR>—अद्म-सद्, त्, m., Ved. seated<BR>(with others) at a meal (?); seated at or busy in the<BR>preparation of a meal (?); a cook (?); a mother (?).<BR>—अद्मसद्य, अम्, n., Ved. the condition of an<BR>अद्मसद्.<BR>—अद्मसद्वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. fit to be<BR>a companion at a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मनि|अद्मनिः
अद्मनि, इस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मर|अद्मरः
अद्मर, अस्, आ, अम्, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
1. अद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or proper to be eaten;<BR>(अम्), n. food, anything eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य 2. अ-द्य or Ved. अद्या, ind. (fr.<BR>pronom. base अ, this, with द्य for द्यु, Lat. ho-die),<BR>to-day; now-a-days; now.<BR>—अद्य-दिन or अद्य-<BR>दिवस, अस्, अम्, m. n. the present day.<BR>—अद्य-<BR>पूर्वम्, ind. before now.<BR>—अद्य-प्रभृति, ind.<BR>from and after to-day.<BR>—अद्य-श्वीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>likely to happen to-day or (श्वस्) to-morrow; (आ), f.<BR>a female near delivery.<BR>—अद्य-सुत्या, f. preparation<BR>and consecration of the Soma on the same day.<BR>—अद्यापि (˚य-अपि). ind. even now, just now; to<BR>this day; down to the present time; henceforth.<BR>—अद्यावधि (˚य-अव्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, beginning or<BR>ending to-day; from or till to-day.<BR>—अद्यैव (अद्य-<BR>एव), ind. this very day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतन|अद्यतनः
अद्यतन, अस्, ई, अम्, extending over or referring<BR>to to-day; occurring or current to-day or now-a-days,<BR>modern; (अस्), m. the period of a current day, either<BR>from midnight to midnight, or from dawn to dark;<BR>(ई), f. (in gram.) the aorist tense from its relating<BR>what has occurred on the same day.<BR>—अद्यतन-<BR>भूत, अस्, m. the aorist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनीय
अद्यतनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, extending over or refer-<BR>ring to to-day; current now-a-days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यु
अद्यु अ-द्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. blunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्युत्
अद्युत् अ-द्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. destitute of<BR>brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यूत्य
अद्यूत्य अ-द्यूत्य, अम्, n., Ved. unlucky<BR>gambling; (according to others) the watch just before<BR>the dawn; (अस्, आ, अम्,), not derived from gambling,<BR>honestly obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव|अद्रवः
अद्रव अ-द्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, not liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव्य|अद्रव्यं
अद्रव्य अ-द्रव्य, अम्, n. a nothing, a<BR>worthless thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रि|अद्रिः
अद्रि अद्रि, इस्, m. (said to be fr, rt. अद्, but<BR>perhaps from अ not, and दॄ, to split, not liable to be<BR>split), a stone, a rock, a mountain; a stone for pound-<BR>ing Soma with or grinding it on; a stone for a sling,<BR>a thunderbolt; a mountain-shaped mass of clouds; a<BR>cloud (the mountains are the clouds personified, and<BR>regarded as the enemies of Indra); a tree; the sun;<BR>N. of a measure; the number seven; N. of a grandson<BR>of Pṛthu.<BR>—अद्रि-कर्णी, f. a plant, Clitoria Ternatea<BR>Lin.<BR>—अद्रि-कीला, f. the earth.<BR>—अद्रि-कृत-स्थली,<BR>f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—अद्रि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>from or found among rocks or mountains; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a plant, Saiṃhalī; N. of Pārvatī or Durgā;<BR>(अम्), n. red chalk.<BR>—अद्रि-जा, आस्, m., Ved. produced<BR>from (the friction of) stones.<BR>—अद्रि-जूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. excited by (the friction of) stones.<BR>—अद्रि-<BR>तनया, f. the mountain-daughter, i. e. Pārvatī; N.<BR>of a metre of four lines, each containing twenty-three<BR>syllables.<BR>—अद्रि-दुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. milked,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">Page0019-c+ 76</a>]<BR>i. e. expressed with stones.<BR>—अद्रि-द्विष्, ट्, m. the<BR>enemy of mountains or clouds, i. e. Indra.<BR>—अद्रि-<BR>नन्दिनी, f., N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—अद्रि-पति, इस्, m. the<BR>Himālaya as the lord of mountains.<BR>—अद्रि-बर्हस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. mountain-high.<BR>—अद्रि-बुध्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rooted in or produced on a rock or<BR>mountain.<BR>—अद्रि-भिद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. splitting mountains<BR>or clouds; (त्), m., N. of Indra.<BR>—अद्रि-भू, ऊस्, ऊस्,<BR>उ, mountain-born, found or living among mountains;<BR>(ऊस्), f. a plant. probably Salvinia Cucullata.<BR>—अद्रि-<BR>मातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. having a rock or moun-<BR>tain for a mother.<BR>—अद्रि-मूर्धन्, आ, m. the head<BR>or summit of a mountain.<BR>—अद्रि-राज्, ट्, or अद्रि-<BR>राज, अस्, m. Himālaya as the king of mountains.<BR>—अद्रि-वत्, आन्, voc. अस्, m., Ved. armed with<BR>stones or thunderbolts.<BR>—अद्रि-वह्नि, इस्, m. fire on<BR>or in a mountain or rock.<BR>—अद्रि-शय्य, अस्, m. having<BR>the mountain for his couch, i. e. Śiva.<BR>—अद्रि-शृङ्ग,<BR>अम्, n. a mountain-peak.<BR>—अद्रि-षुत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. prepared with stones.<BR>—अद्रि-संहत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. expressed with stones.<BR>—अद्रि-सानु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. lingering on the mountains.<BR>—अद्रि-<BR>सार, अस्, m. essence of stones, i. e. iron.<BR>—अद्रि-<BR>सार-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of iron.<BR>—अद्रीन्द्र<BR>(˚द्रि-इन्˚) or अद्रीस (˚द्रि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord of<BR>mountains, i. e. Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिका
अद्रिका, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रुह्
अद्रुह् अ-द्रुह्, ध्रुक्, क्, क्, or अद्रुह्वन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ (rt. द्रुह्), Ved. free from malice or treachery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोघ
अ-द्रोघ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. free from falsehood,<BR>true; (अम्), ind. without falsehood.<BR>—अद्रोघ-वाच्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, Ved. free from malice or treachery in speech.<BR>—अद्रोघावित (˚घ-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. loving<BR>freedom from malice or treachery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोह|अद्रोहः
अ-द्रोह, अस्, m. freedom from malice or treachery.<BR>—अद्रोह-वृत्ति, इस्, f. conduct free from malice or<BR>treachery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोहिन्
अ-द्रोहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, free from malice or treachery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वन्
अद्वन् अद्वन्, आ, आ, अ (fr. rt. अद्), eating;<BR>(used at the end of compound words.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वय|अद्वयः
अद्वय अ-द्वय, अस्, आ, अम्, not two, without<BR>a second, only, unique; (अस्), m., N. of Buddha;<BR>(अम्), n. non-duality, unity; identity, especially the<BR>identity of Brahma with the universe or with the<BR>soul, or of spirit and matter; the ultimate truth.<BR>—अद्वय-वादिन् or अद्वैत-वादिन्, ई, m. Buddha;<BR>a Jaina; one who teaches अद्वय or identity.<BR>—अद्वयानन्द (˚य-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author, and of a founder of the Vaiṣṇava sect in<BR>Bengal, who lived at the close of the fifteenth century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयत्|अद्वयन्त्
अ-द्वयत्, अन्, or अ-द्वयस्, आस्, m., Ved. free from<BR>duplicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयाविन्
अ-द्वयाविन्, ई, or अ-द्वयु, उस्, m., Ved. free<BR>from double dealing or duplicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वार|अद्वारं
अद्वार अ-द्वार, अम्, n. a place without a<BR>door; an entrance which is not the proper door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्विज
अद्विज अ-द्विज, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of<BR>Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीय|अद्वितीयः
अद्वितीय अ-द्वितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>second, sole, unique; matchless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्विषेण्य
अद्विषेण्य अ-द्विषेण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. द्विष्),<BR>Ved. not to be disliked; not malevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष|अद्वेषः
अ-द्वेष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not malevolent.<BR>—अ-<BR>द्वेष-रागिन्, ई, इणी, इ, free from malevolence and<BR>passionate desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषस्
अद्वेषस्, ind., Ved. without malevolence, without<BR>opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषिन्
अद्वेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, free from malevolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष्टृ
अद्वेष्टृ, आ, m. not an enemy; a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत अ-द्वैत, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of<BR>duality, having no duplicate; peerless; sole, unique;<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. non-duality; identity,<BR>especially the identity of Brahma with the universe<BR>or with the soul, or of spirit and matter; the<BR>ultimate truth; title of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—अद्वैतेन,<BR>ind. solely.<BR>—अद्वैताननद (˚त-आन्˚), अस्, m. =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">Page0020-a+ 76</a>]<BR>अद्वयानन्द, q. v.<BR>—अद्वैतोपनिषद् (˚त-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध|अधः
अध अध or अधा, ind., Ved. (much the<BR>same as अथ, used chiefly as an inceptive particle),<BR>now; then, therefore; moreover, so much the more;<BR>and, partly.<BR>—अध-अध, अस् well as, partly-partly.<BR>—अध-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, or अध-प्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ,<BR>Ved. pleased or glad then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधः|अध
अधः अधः, &c. See अधस्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन
अधन अ-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of<BR>wealth or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन्य
अ-धन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not richly supplied with corn<BR>or other produce; not prosperous; unhappy, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम अधम, अस्, आ, अम् (see etymology of<BR>अधर), lowest, vilest, worst; very low or vile or<BR>bad; often used at the close of comp., as in नरा-<BR>धम, the vilest or worst of men; (अस्), an un-<BR>blushing paramour; (आ), a low or bad mistress [cf. Lat.<BR>infimus].<BR>—अधम-भृत or अधम-भृतक,<BR>अस्, m. a servant of the lowest class, a porter.<BR>—अधमर्ण (˚म-ऋ˚), अस्, or अधमर्णिक,<BR>अस्, m. one reduced to inferiority by debt, a debtor.<BR>—अधम-शाख, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N.<BR>of a region.<BR>—अधमाङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚), अम्, n. (the<BR>lowest member), the foot.<BR>—अधमाचार (˚म-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, guilty of vile conduct.<BR>—अधमार्ध<BR>(˚म-अर्˚), अम्, n. the lower half, the lower part.<BR>—अधमार्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with or<BR>referring to the lower part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णा
अधमर्णा, अधमर्णिक, &c. See above, under<BR>अधम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर अधर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to come<BR>from अधस् or from a base अध्, whence अधस्<BR>may be derived), lower, inferior; tending down-<BR>wards; low, vile; worsted, silenced; prior; (अस्),<BR>m. the lower lip, the lip; (आ), f. the lower re-<BR>gion, nadir; (अम्), n. the lower part; a reply;<BR>Pudendum Muliebre [Ossetic, दलग्; Goth. dala-<BR>thrô; Lat. inferus].<BR>—अधर-तस् or अधर-<BR>स्तात् or अधरस्मात् or अधरात् or अधरेण, ind.<BR>below, beneath; in the lower region.<BR>—अधर-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, अम्, m. n. the lower neck.<BR>—अधर-<BR>काय, अस्, m. the lower part of the body.<BR>—अधर-<BR>पान, अम्, n. drinking the lower lip, kissing.<BR>—अधर-मधु, उ, n. the moisture of the lips.<BR>—अधर-स्वस्तिक, अम्, n. the nadir.<BR>—अधरा-<BR>मृत (˚र-अम्˚), अम्, n. the nectar of the lips.<BR>—अधरारणि (˚र-अर्˚), इस्, f., Ved. the lower of<BR>the two pieces of wood used in producing fire by<BR>friction.<BR>—अधरावलोप (˚र-अव्˚), अस्, m. biting<BR>the lip.<BR>—अधरोत्तर (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, lower<BR>and higher; worse and better; question and answer;<BR>nearer and further; sooner and later; upside down,<BR>topsy-turvy.<BR>—अधरोष्ठ or अधरौष्ठ (˚र-<BR>ओष्˚), अस्, m. the lower lip; (अम्), n. the lower and<BR>upper lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराक्
अधराक्, ind. beneath, in the lower region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराचीन
अधराचीन or अधराच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>अधराञ्च् आङ्, आची, आक्, Ved. tending downwards, to<BR>the nadir or the lower region, tending towards the<BR>south (or west ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरात्तात्
अधरात्तात्, ind., Ved. below, beneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीकृत
अधरी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, worsted; invalidated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीण|अधरीणः
अधरीण, अस्, आ, अम्, vilified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीभूत
अधरी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, worsted; invalidated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेद्युस्
अधरे-द्युस्, ind. the day before yesterday; on a<BR>previous day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेय
अधरेय, अस्, आ, अम्, inferior in quality or worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म|अधर्मः|अधर्म्म|अधर्म्मः
अधर्म अ-धर्म, अस्, m. unrighteousness,<BR>injustice, irreligion, wickedness; demerit, guilt; N. of<BR>a Prajāpati, son of Brahmā, husband of Hiṃsā or<BR>Mṛṣā; N. of an attendant of the sun; (आ), f. un-<BR>righteousness personified and represented as the bride<BR>of death.<BR>—अधर्म-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, practising<BR>wickedness.<BR>—अधर्म-तस्, ind. unrighteously, un-<BR>justly.<BR>—अधर्म-दण्डन, अम्, n. unjust punish-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-b" target="_blank">Page0020-b+ 80</a>]<BR>ment.<BR>—अधर्म-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made up of<BR>wickedness; downright wicked.<BR>—अधर्मात्मन्<BR>(˚म-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having a wicked spirit or dis-<BR>position.<BR>—अधर्मास्तिकाय (˚म-अस्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>category (अस्तिकाय) of अधर्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मिन्|अधर्म्मिन्
अधर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, unrighteous, wicked, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मिष्ठ|अधर्म्मिष्ठ
अधर्मिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, most wicked, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्य
अधर्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unlawful, contrary to law<BR>or religion, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधवा
अधवा अ-धवा, f. a widow (usually वि-<BR>धवा, without a husband).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्
अधस् अधस्, ind. (said to come from अध्,<BR>see अधर), below, down; in the lower region;<BR>beneath, under; from under (with acc., gen., and abl.);<BR>also applied to the lower region and to the Pudendum<BR>Muliebre [cf. Lat. infra].<BR>—अधस्-तरम्, ind. very<BR>far down.<BR>—अध-उपासन, अम्, n. sexual inter-<BR>course.<BR>—अधः-कर, अस्, m. the lower part of the<BR>hand.<BR>—अधः-काय, अस्, m. the lower part of the body.<BR>—अधः-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, put down, cast down.<BR>—अधः-कृष्णाजिनम् (˚ण-अज्˚), ind. under the<BR>black skin.<BR>—अधः-खनन, अम्, n. undermin-<BR>ing.<BR>—अधः-पद्म, अम्, n. (in architecture) a cer-<BR>tain part of the cupola.<BR>—अधः-पात, अस्, m. a down-<BR>fall.<BR>—अधः-पुष्पी, f. (having flowers looking<BR>downwards), N. of two plants, Pimpinella Anisum<BR>and Elephantopus Scaber (or Hieracium ?).<BR>—अधः-<BR>प्रवाह, अस्, m. a downward current.<BR>—अधः-<BR>प्रस्तर, अस्, m. seat or bed of turf or grass for<BR>person in a state of impurity.<BR>—अधः-प्राङ्-शायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, sleeping on the ground, towards the east.<BR>—अधश्-चर, अस्, m. a thief (‘creeping on the<BR>ground’).<BR>—अधः-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping on the<BR>ground.<BR>—अधः-शय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having a pecu-<BR>liar couch on the ground; (आ), f. act of sleeping on<BR>the ground and on a peculiar couch.<BR>—अधः-शिरस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, holding the head downward; head fore-<BR>most; (अस्), n., N. of a hell.<BR>—अधस्-तल, अम्, n.<BR>the room below anything.<BR>—अधस्-पद, अम्, n.<BR>the place under the feet.<BR>—अधस्पदम्, ind. under<BR>foot.<BR>—अधः-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, placed low or below;<BR>inferior.<BR>—अधः-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing below;<BR>situated below.<BR>—अधः-स्वस्तिक, अम्, n. the nadir.<BR>—अधो-ऽंशुक, अम्, n. a lower garment.<BR>—अधो-<BR>ऽक्ष or अधो-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (situated) below<BR>the axle or under a car; (अम्), ind. under the axle.<BR>—अधो-ऽक्ष-ज, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa; the sign Śravaṇā.<BR>—अधो-गण्टा, f. a plant,<BR>Achyranthes Aspera.<BR>—अधो-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone<BR>down, descended.<BR>—अधो-गति, इस्, f. or अधो-गम, अस्,<BR>m. or अधो-गमन, अम्, n. descent, downward move-<BR>ment, degradation.<BR>—अधो-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, going down-<BR>wards, descending.<BR>—अधो-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ = preced-<BR>ing.<BR>—अधो-घण्टा, f. a plant, Achyranthes Aspera.<BR>—अधो-ऽङ्ग, अम्, n. the anus, Pudendum Muli-<BR>ebre.<BR>—अधो-जानु, ind. below the knee.<BR>—अधो-<BR>जिह्विका, f. the uvula.<BR>—अधो-दारु, उ, n. the under<BR>timber.<BR>—अधो-दिश्, क्, f. the lower region, the nadir.<BR>—अधो-दृष्टि, इस्, f. a downcast look; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>having a downcast look.<BR>—अधो-देश, अस्, m. the<BR>lower or lowest part, especially of the body.<BR>—अधो-<BR>द्वार, अम्, n. the anus, Pudendum Muliebre.<BR>—अधो-नाभम्, ind. below the navel.<BR>—अधो-<BR>ऽपर, अम्, n. the anus.<BR>—अधोपहास (˚धस्-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m., Ved. sexual intercourse.<BR>—अधो-बन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. an under girth.<BR>—अधो-भक्त, अम्, n. a<BR>dose of medicine to be taken after eating.<BR>—अधो-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, lower.<BR>—अधो-भाग, अस्, m. the<BR>lower or lowest part, especially of the body.<BR>—अधो-<BR>भाग-दोष-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, curing or strengthen-<BR>ing the lower part of the body.<BR>—अधो-भुवन,<BR>अम्, n. the lower world.<BR>—अधो-भूमि, इस्, f. lower<BR>ground; land at the foot of a hill.<BR>—अधो-मर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. the anus.<BR>—अधो-मुख, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, having<BR>the face downwards; headlong; upside down; (अस्),<BR>m. Viṣṇu; (आ), f. a plant, Premna Esculenta; (अम्),<BR>n. a division of hell.<BR>—अधो-यन्त्र, अम्, n. the<BR>lower part of an apparatus; a still.<BR>—अधो-रक्त-<BR>पित्त, अम्, n. discharge of blood from the anus and the<BR>urethra.<BR>—अधो-राम, अस्, m., Ved. (a goat) having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">Page0020-c+ 74</a>]<BR>peculiar white or black marks on the lower part of<BR>the body.<BR>—अधो-लाम्ब, अस्, m. a plummet; the<BR>perpendicular; (अस्), m. the lower world.<BR>—अधो-<BR>वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, the same as अधो-मुख.<BR>—अधो-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, powerful in the lower<BR>regions.<BR>—अधो-वश, अस्, m. the bottom, Pudendum<BR>Muliebre.<BR>—अधो-वायु, उस्, m. vital air passing down-<BR>wards; flatulency.<BR>—अधो-ऽवेक्षि (अधस् + अव +<BR>ईक्षिन्), looking down.<BR>—अधो-ऽश्र-पित्त, see अधो-<BR>रक्तपित्त.<BR>—अधो-ऽश्वम्, ind. under the horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तन
अधस्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, lower, being underneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तात्
अधस्तात्, ind. the same as अधस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्ताद्दिश्
अधस्ताद्-दिश्, क्, f. the lower region, the nadir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधा
अधा अधा, Ved. See अध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधामार्गव|अधामार्गवः
अधामार्गव अधामार्गव, अस्, m. a plant,<BR>Achyranthes Aspera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधारणक
अधारणक अ-धारणक, अस्, आ, अम्, unable<BR>to support, unremunerative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधार्मिक|अधार्म्मिक|अधार्म्मिकः
अधार्मिक अ-धार्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, unjust,<BR>unrighteous, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधार्य
अधार्य अ-धार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit or improper<BR>to be held or carried or kept up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि 1. अधि, इस्, m. (better आधि, q. v.),<BR>anxiety, perplexity; f. a woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि 2. अधि, ind., as a prefix to verbs and<BR>nouns, expresses above, over and above, besides.<BR>As a separable adverb or preposition; (with abl.)<BR>Ved. over; from above; from; from the presence of;<BR>for; (with gen.) Ved. among; (with loc.) Ved.<BR>over; on; at; subject to; (with acc.) over, upon,<BR>concerning.<BR>—अध्य्-अधि, ind. on high, just above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक|अधिकं|अधिकः
अधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, additional; subsequent, later;<BR>surpassing (in number or quantity or quality), superior,<BR>more numerous; abundant; excellent; supernumerary,<BR>redundant; secondary, inferior; intercalated; (अम्),<BR>n. surplus; abundance; redundancy; hyperbole: ind.<BR>exceedingly; too much; more.<BR>—अधिकं-तु, more-<BR>over.<BR>—अधिक-क्षय-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, causing<BR>excessive waste.<BR>—अधिक-ता, f. or अधिक-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. addition, excess, redundancy, preponderance.<BR>—अधिक-तिथि, इस्, m. f. an intercalary lunar day.<BR>—अधिक-दन्त or अधि-दन्त, अस्, m. a redun-<BR>dant tooth which grows over another.<BR>—अधिक-दिन<BR>or अधि-दिन, अम्, n. an intercalated day.<BR>—अधिक-<BR>मांसार्मन् (˚स-अर्˚), अ, n. proud flesh in the eye;<BR>see अधिमांस.<BR>—अधिक-मास, अस्, m. an inter-<BR>calated month.<BR>—अधिकर्द्धि (˚क-ऋद्˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>abundantly prosperous.<BR>—अधिक-वाक्योक्ति (˚क्य-<BR>उक्˚), इस्, f. exaggeration, hyperbole.<BR>—अधिक-षा-<BR>ष्टिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (containing or costing) more than<BR>sixty.<BR>—अधिक-संवत्सर, अस्, m. an intercalated<BR>month.<BR>—अधिक-साप्ततिक, अस्, ई, अम् (containing or<BR>costing) more than seventy.<BR>—अधिकाङ्ग (˚क-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, having some redundant member or<BR>members; (अम्), n. belt worn over the coat of mail.<BR>—अधिकाधिक (˚ख-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, outdoing<BR>one another.<BR>—अधिकार्थ (˚क-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>exaggerated.<BR>—अधिकार्थ-वचन, अम्, n. exagger-<BR>ation, hyperbole,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मकर|अधिकर्मकरः|अधिकर्म्मकर
अधिकर्मकर अधि-कर्मकर, अस्, m. or<BR>अधि-कर्मकृत्, त्, m. an overseer of workmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकल्पिन्
अधिकल्पिन् अधि-कल्पिन्, ई, m., Ved. a<BR>sharp gambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार्म
अधिकार्म अधि-कार्म, अम्, n., N. of some<BR>place unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृ
अधिकृ अधि-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to place at the head, appoint; to aim at, regard;<BR>to refer or allude to; to superintend, be at the head<BR>of: A. -कुरुते, to be or become entitled to; to be<BR>or become superior to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरण|अधिकरणं
अधि-करण, अम्, n. the act of placing at the<BR>head or of subordinating government, supremacy,<BR>magistracy, court of justice; a receptacle, sup-<BR>port; a claim; a topic, subject; (in philosophy) a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">Page0021-a+ 77</a>]<BR>substratum; a subject (e. g. आत्मा is the अधि-करण<BR>of knowledge); a category; a relation; (in grammar)<BR>regimen, government, comprehension, location, the<BR>sense of the locative case; relationship of words in a<BR>sentence, which agree together, either as adjective and<BR>substantive, or as subject and predicate, or as two sub-<BR>stantives in apposition; (in rhetoric) a topic; a para-<BR>graph or minor section; (अस्, ई), m. f. one who has to<BR>superintend.<BR>—अधिकरण-भोजक, अस्, m. a judge.<BR>—अधिकरण-मण्डप, अस्, अम्, m. n. the hall<BR>of justice.<BR>—अधिकरण-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. a syl-<BR>logism or conclusion which involves others.<BR>—अधि-<BR>करणैतावत्त्व (˚ण-एत्˚), अम्, n. fixed quantity of<BR>a substratum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरणिक|अधिकरणिकः
अधि-करणिक or better आधिकरणिक, अस्, m.<BR>a government official; a judge or magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरण्य|अधिकरण्यं
अधि-करण्य, अम्, n. authority, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मन्|अधिकर्म्मन्
अधि-कर्मन्, अ, n. superintendence.<BR>—अधि-<BR>कर्मकृत् or अधि-कर्मकर, see s. v.<BR>—अधि-<BR>कर्म-कृत, अस्, m. person appointed to superin-<BR>tend an establishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्मिक|अधिकर्मिकः|अधिकर्म्मिक|अधिकर्म्मिकः
अधिकर्मिक, अस्, m. the overseer of a market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार|अधिकारः
अधि-कार, अस्, m. authority; office; government,<BR>rule, administration, jurisdiction; royalty, prerogative;<BR>title; rank; claim, right, especially to perform sacri-<BR>fices with benefit; privilege; ownership; possession;<BR>property; reference, relation; exertion, effort; a topic,<BR>subject; a paragraph or minor section; (in grammar)<BR>government; a heading-rule; (अस्, ई), m. f. having<BR>much to superintend.<BR>—अधिकार-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>established in an office.<BR>—अधिकाराढ्य (˚र-आढ˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, invested with authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिन्
अधि-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, possessing authority; en-<BR>titled to; fit for; (ई), m. a superintendent, governor;<BR>an official; a rightful claimant; a proprietor, master;<BR>one possessing the right of sacrificing; a man pro-<BR>ficient in the Vedānta; man as the lord of creation.<BR>—अधिकारि-त्व, अम्, n. or अधिकारि-ता, f. author-<BR>ity; rightful claim; ownership, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृत|अधिकृतः
अधि-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, placed at the head of;<BR>appointed; ruled, administered; claimed; (अस्), m.<BR>a superintendent, especially a comptroller of public<BR>accounts.<BR>—अधिकृत-त्व, अम्, n. the being engaged<BR>in or occupied with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृति|अधिकृतिः
अधि-कृति, इस्, f. a right, privilege; possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृत्य
अधि-कृत्य, ind. having placed at the head, having<BR>made the chief subject; regarding; concerning; with<BR>reference to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रम्
अधिक्रम् अधि-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. -क्रामति,<BR>-क्रमितुम्, to ascend, mount up to; to attack, scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रम|अधिक्रमः
अधि-क्रम, अस्, m. an invasion, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रमण|अधिक्रमणं
अधि-क्रमण, अम्, n. act of invading or scaling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षि
अधिक्षि अधि-क्षि, cl. 6. or cl. 1. P., Ved.<BR>-क्षियति or -क्षेति, -क्षेतुम्, to be settled in or<BR>over, rest upon; to inhabit, to obtain; (occasionally<BR>अधि-क्षिप् occurs for this rt. by mistake.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षित्
अधिक्षित् अधि-क्षित्, त्, m., Ved. a lord,<BR>ruler (fr. rt. 2. क्षि and not fr. अधि-क्षि above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षिप्
अधिक्षिप् अधि-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. -क्षिपति,<BR>-क्षेप्तुम्, to lay upon; to bespatter; to insult, abuse,<BR>scold; to superinduce (disease); (occasionally this rt.<BR>appears to be used by mistake for अधि-क्षि, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

