अधिराज
अधि-राज, अस्, or अधि-राजन्, आ, m. an emperor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्य|अधिराज्यं
अधि-राज्य or अधि-राष्ट्र, अम्, n. supremacy,<BR>imperial dignity; an empire; N. of a country.<BR>—अधिराज्य-भाज्, क्, m. possessor of imperial dig-<BR>nity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुक्म
अधिरुक्म अधि-रुक्म, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing<BR>gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुह्
अधिरुह् अधि-रुह्, cl. 1. P. or poet. A.<BR>अधि-रोहति, -ते, -रोढुम्, to rise above, to ascend,<BR>mount: Caus. -रोपयति, -यितुम्, to raise, place above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूढ
अधि-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, ascended, mounted.<BR>—अधिरूढ-समाधि-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged<BR>in profound meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

