अधिष्ठित
अधि-ष्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, settled; inhabited; super-<BR>intended; regulated; appointed; superintending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिस्त्रि
अधिस्त्रि अधि-स्त्रि, ind. concerning a wo-<BR>man or a wife.<BR>—अधि-स्त्री, f. a superior or distin-<BR>guished woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिहरि
अधिहरि अधि-हरि, ind. concerning Hari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधी
अधी अधी (अधि-इ), cl. 2. P. अध्य्-एति, -तुम्,<BR>to meet with, attain, notice, observe, understand; to<BR>mind, remember, care for, long for; to know, know<BR>by heart; to go over; study, learn, read, recite, de-<BR>clare; A. अधीते, to study, learn by heart, read,<BR>recite, declare: Caus. P. अध्य्-आपयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make one read or study, teach, instruct; Desid. of the<BR>Caus. अध्य्-आपिपयिषति, to be desirous of teaching:<BR>Desid. अधीषिषति, to be desirous of teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

