अधीष्ट|अधीष्टः
अधीष्ट अधीष्ट (अधि-इष्ट), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>solicited, honorary; (अम्), n. solicitation; honorary<BR>office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुना
अधुना अ-धुना, ind. (fr. the pronom. base<BR>अ, substituted for इदम्), at this time, now.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुनातन|अधुनातनं
अधुनातन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or extend-<BR>ing over the present time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुर
अधुर अ-धुर, अस्, आ, अम्, not laden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधूमक|अधूमकः
अधूमक अ-धूमक, अस्, आ, अम्, smokeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृत|अधृतः
अधृत अ-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not held, un-<BR>restrained, uncontrolled; (अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृति|अधृतिः
अ-धृति, इस्, f. want of firmness or fortitude; laxity,<BR>absence of control or restraint; incontinence; (इस्, इस्,<BR>इ), unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्ट|अधृष्टः
अधृष्ट अ-धृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. धृष्), not<BR>bold, modest; not put down, invincible, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्य|अधृष्यः
अ-धृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unassailable, invincible;<BR>unapproachable; proud; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधेनु|अधेनुः
अधेनु अ-धेनु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. yielding no<BR>milk or advantage; not nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्य|अधैर्य्य|अधैर्य्यः
अधैर्य अ-धैर्य, अम्, n. want or loss of<BR>calm self-command; paroxysm of excitement; excita-<BR>bility; (अस्, आ, अम्), deficient in self-command;<BR>swayed by excitement or violent feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधो
अधो अधो. See under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यंस
अध्यंस अध्य्-अंस, अस्, आ, अम्, (placed) on<BR>the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्त
अध्यक्त अध्य्-अक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. अञ्ज्),<BR>equipped, prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्ष|अध्यक्षः
अध्यक्ष अध्य्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, observable;<BR>exercising supervision; (अस्), m. an eye-witness; an<BR>inspector, superintendent; N. of a plant, Mimusops<BR>Kauki (क्षीरिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षरम्
अध्यक्षरम् अध्य्-अक्षरम्, ind. on the sub-<BR>ject of syllables; above all syllables (as the mystic ॐ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यग्नि
अध्यग्नि अध्य्-अग्नि, ind. over or by the<BR>nuptial fire, property given to the bride.<BR>—अध्यग्नी-<BR>कृत, अम्, n. property given to the wife at the<BR>wedding.<BR>—अध्यग्न्य्-उपागत, अम्, n. property<BR>received by a wife at the wedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यञ्च्|अध्यंच्
अध्यञ्च् अध्य्-अञ्च्, अङ्, ईची, अक्, tending up-<BR>wards, eminent, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यण्डा|अध्यंडा
अध्यण्डा अध्यण्डा, f., N. of two plants,<BR>Cowage (Carpopogon Pruriens) and Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधिक्षेप|अध्यधिक्षेपः
अध्यधिक्षेप अध्य्-अधिक्षेप, अस्, m. ex-<BR>cessive censure; gross abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधीन
अध्यधीन अध्य्-अधीन, अस्, आ, अम्, completely<BR>subject or dependent, as a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यय|अध्ययः
अध्यय अध्य्-अय or better अध्य्-आय, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. अधि-इ, see अधी), a lesson, lecture, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययन|अध्ययनं
अध्य्-अयन, अम्, n. reading, studying, especially<BR>the Vedas (on of the six duties of a Brāhman).<BR>—अध्ययन-तपसी, n. nom. du. study and penance.<BR>—अध्ययन-पुण्य, अम्, n. religious merit ac-<BR>quired by studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययनीय
अध्य्-अयनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or proper to be<BR>read or studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्ध|अध्यर्धः
अध्यर्ध अध्य्-अर्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, having an<BR>additional half, i. e. one and a half; (in compounds<BR>synonymous with) अध्य्-अर्धक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>amounting to or worth one and a half.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-<BR>कंस, अस्, अम्, m. n. one and a half kaṃsa; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), amounting to or worth one and a half kaṃsa.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-काकिणीक, अस्, आ, अम्, amounting to<BR>or worth one and a half kākiṇī.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-<BR>कार्षापण or अध्यर्ध-कार्षापणिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, amounting to or worth one and a half kārṣā-<BR>paṇa.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-खारीक, अस्, आ, अम्, amount-<BR>ing to or worth one and a half khārī.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">Page0023-b+ 74</a>]<BR>पण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, amounting to or worth one and<BR>a half paṇa.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>amounting to one foot and a half.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-<BR>प्रतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, amounting to one and a half<BR>kārṣāpaṇa.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-माष्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>amounting to or worth one and a half māṣa.<BR>—अध्य्-<BR>अर्ध-विंशतिकीन, अस्, आ, अम्, amounting to or worth<BR>one and a half score or thirty.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-शत<BR>or अध्यर्ध-शत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, amounting to or<BR>bought with one hundred and fifty.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-<BR>शतमान or अध्यर्ध-शातमान, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>amounting to or worth one and a half śatamāna.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-शाण or अध्यर्ध-शाण्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, amounting to or worth one and a half śāṇa.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-शूर्प, अस्, ई, अम्, amounting to or<BR>worth one and a half śūrpa.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-सहस्र<BR>or अध्यर्ध-साहस्र, अस्, ई, अम्, amounting to<BR>or worth one thousand five hundred.<BR>—अध्यर्ध-<BR>सुवर्ण or अध्यर्ध-सौवर्णिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>amounting to or worth one and a half suvarṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्बुद|अध्यर्बुदं
अध्यर्बुद अध्य्-अर्बुद or अध्य्-अर्वुद, अम्,<BR>n. a tumour, goitre (dating from the time of birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसो
अध्यवसो अध्य्-अव-सो, cl. 4. P. -स्यति,<BR>सातुम्, to undertake, grapple with, attempt; to<BR>determine, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसान|अध्यवसानं
अध्य्-अव-सान, अम्, n. determining; attempt,<BR>effort, exertion; energy, perseverance; (in rhetoric)<BR>concise and forcible language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसाय|अध्यवसायः
अध्य्-अव-साय, अस्, m. = the preceding; (in phi-<BR>losophy) mental effort, apprehension.<BR>—अध्यव-<BR>साय-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, or अध्यवसायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायित
अध्य्-अव-सायित, अस्, आ, अम्, attempted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसित
अध्य्-अव-सित, अस्, आ, अम्, mentally apprehended,<BR>ascertained, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवहनन|अध्यवहननं
अध्यवहनन अध्य्-अवहनन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>serving as an implement on which anything is peeled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यशन|अध्यशनं
अध्यशन अध्य्-अशन, अम्, n. eating too<BR>soon after a meal, before the last meal is digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्
अध्यस् अध्य्-अस्, cl. 4. P. -अस्यति, -सितुम्, to<BR>throw or place over or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्त|अध्यस्तं
अध्य्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, placed over; disguised;<BR>supposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्थि
अध्यस्थि अध्य्-अस्थि, इ, n. a bone growing<BR>over another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यह्
अध्यह् अध्य्-अह्, Defect. Perf. -आह, to<BR>address; to bless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याक्रम्
अध्याक्रम् अध्य्-आ-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. -क्रामति,<BR>-क्रमितुम्, to attack; to fix upon, occupy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यागम्
अध्यागम् अध्य्-आ-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to fall in with, meet with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याचर्
अध्याचर् अध्य्-आ-चर्, cl. 1. P. -चरति,<BR>-रितुम्, to bestride, occupy as a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याण्डा
अध्याण्डा अध्य्-आण्डा, f., N. of a plant.<BR>See अध्यण्डा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्म
अध्यात्म अध्य्-आत्म, अम्, n. the supreme<BR>spirit; (अस्, आ, अम्), own, belonging to self; (अम्),<BR>ind. concerning self or individual personality.<BR>—अध्य्-<BR>आत्म-चेतस्, आस्, m. one who meditates on the su-<BR>preme spirit.<BR>—अध्य्-आत्म-ज्ञान, अम्, n. or अध्य्-<BR>आत्म-विद्या, f. knowledge of the supreme spirit or<BR>of आत्मन्.<BR>—अध्य्-आत्म-दृश्, क्, or अध्यात्म-विद्,<BR>त्, m. a sage proficient in that knowledge.<BR>—अध्य्-<BR>आत्म-रति, इस्, m. a man delighting in the contem-<BR>plation of the supreme spirits or of आत्मन्.<BR>—अध्य्-<BR>आत्म-रामायण, अम्, n. a Rāmāyaṇa, in which every-<BR>thing is referred to the universal spirit; it forms part of<BR>the Brahmāṇḍa-Purāṇa.<BR>—अध्यात्म-शास्त्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—अध्यात्मोत्तर-काण्ड (˚म-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of the last book of the Adhyātmarāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मिक
अध्य्-आत्मिक or better आध्यात्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>connected with or relating to the soul or the supreme<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापक|अध्यापकः
अध्यापक अध्य्-आपक, अस्, m. (fr. अधि-इ, see<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">Page0023-c+ 74</a>]<BR>अधी), a teacher or professor, especially of sacred know-<BR>ledge; N. of a priest (?).<BR>—अध्यापकोदित (˚क-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. entitled an अध्यापक, styled a professor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापन|अध्यापनं
अध्य्-आपन, अम्, n. instruction or lecturing.<BR>especially on sacred knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापयितृ
अध्य्-आपयितृ, त्, आ, m. a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापित
अध्य्-आपित, अस्, आ, अम्, instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याप्य
अध्य्-आप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit or proper to be instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्य्-आय, अस्, m. a lesson, lecture, chapter; reading;<BR>proper time for reading or for a lesson; (at the close<BR>of comp. words) a reader, student, as वेदाध्याय, a<BR>reader or student of the Vedas.<BR>—अध्याय-शत-<BR>पाठ, अस्, m. an index of the One Hundred Chapters,<BR>N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यायिन्
अध्यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, studious, engaged in reading<BR>or study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारुह्
अध्यारुह् अध्य्-आ-रुह्, cl. 1. P., poet. A.<BR>-रोहति, -ते, -रोढुम्, to ascend, mount: Caus.<BR>-रोपयति, -यितुम्, to cause or order to mount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारूढ|अध्यारूढः
अध्य्-आरूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, mounted, ascended;<BR>(with the instr.) above, superior; (with the abl.)<BR>below, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोप|अध्यारोपः
अध्य्-आरोप, अस्, m. or अध्य्-आरोपण, अम्, n.<BR>act of making one mount or of raising; act of<BR>attributing, especially through mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपित
अध्य्-आरोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, falsely attributed; hy-<BR>perbolical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावस्
अध्यावस् अध्य्-आ-वस्, cl. 1. P. -वसति,<BR>-वस्तुम्, to inhabit, dwell in (with acc. or loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाप|अध्यावापः
अध्यावाप अध्य्-आ-वाप, अस्, m. (rt. वप्), the<BR>act of sowing or scattering upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाहनिक|अध्यावाहनिकं
अध्यावाहनिक अध्य्-आ-वाहनिक, अम्, n. that<BR>part of a wife's property which she receives when on<BR>a visit to her parents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यास्
अध्यास् अध्य्-आस्, cl. 2. A. -आस्ते, -सितुम्,<BR>to sit down or (of beasts) lie down upon, to settle<BR>upon; to occupy as one's seat or habitation; to get<BR>into, enter upon; to be directed to or upon; to<BR>affect, concern; to influence, rule; to cohabit with:<BR>Caus. P. अध्य्-आसयति, -यितुम्, to make (one)<BR>sit down: Des. अध्य्-आसिसिषते, to be about to<BR>get upon (a seat &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासन|अध्यासनं
अध्य्-आसन, अम्, n. act of sitting down upon;<BR>presiding over; a seat, settlement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासयोग
अध्यास-योग, अस्, m. (with Buddhists) a kind of<BR>meditation (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासित
अध्य्-आसित, अस्, आ, अम्, seated on; seated in the<BR>presidential chair; settled, inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासिन्
अध्य्-आसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sitting down or seated upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासीन
अध्य्-आसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, seated upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यास|अध्यासः
अध्यास अध्य्-आस, अस्, m. (rt. 2. अस्), impos-<BR>ing; erroneously attributing; an appendage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहरण|अध्याहरणं
अध्याहरण अध्य्-आ-हरण, अम्, n. or अध्य्-<BR>आ-हार, अस्, m. (rt. हृ), act of supplying (elliptical<BR>language); supplement; act of inferring or arguing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहरणीय
अध्य्-आहरणीय or अध्य्-आहर्तव्य or अध्य्-<BR>आहार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper to be supplied; proper<BR>to be argued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहृत
अध्य्-आहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, supplied, argued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषित
अध्युषित अध्य्-उषित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वस्,<BR>see 1. अधि-वस्), inhabited; obtained (?).<BR>—अध्य्-<BR>उषिताश्व or अध्यूषिताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince descended from Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट|अध्युष्टः
अध्युष्ट अध्य्-उष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. उष् =<BR>उच्छ् ?), coiled up three and a half times.<BR>—अध्य्-<BR>उष्ट-वलय, अस्, m. (snake) forming a ring coiled<BR>up three and a half times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट्र|अध्युष्ट्रः
अध्युष्ट्र अध्य्-उष्ट्र, अस्, m. conveyance<BR>borne or drawn by camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढ|अध्यूढः
अध्यूढ अध्य्-ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass.<BR>part. fr. rt. वह् with अधि), raised, exalted; affluent;<BR>abundant; (अस्), m. Śiva; (आ), f. a wife whose hus-<BR>band has married an additional wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूध्नी
अध्यूध्नी अध्य्-ऊध्नी, f. (fr. ऊधन् or ऊधस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">Page0024-a+ 74</a>]<BR>udder, with अधि), a tubular vessel above the udder,<BR>or above the scrotum, i. e. urethra (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूषिवस्
अध्यूषिवस् अध्य्-ऊषिवस्, आन्, उषी, अस् (perf.<BR>part. of rt. वस् with अधि), having inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूह्
अध्यूह् अध्य्-ऊह्, cl. 1. P. -ऊहति, -हितुम्, to<BR>lay on, overlay; to place upon, to raise above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूहन|अध्यूहनं
अध्य्-ऊहन, अम्, n. putting on a layer (of ashes<BR>or cinders).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यृध्
अध्यृध् अध्य्-ऋध्, cl. 5. P. -ऋध्नोति,<BR>-अर्धितुम्, to expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येतव्य
अध्येतव्य अध्य्-एतव्य or अध्य्-एय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (fr. rt. इ with अधि, see अधी), fit or proper to<BR>be studied or read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येतृ
अध्य्-एतृ, त्, आ, m. a student, reader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येष्यमाण
अध्य्-एष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fut. part.), intending<BR>to study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येध्
अध्येध् अध्य्-एध्, cl. 1. A. -एधते, -धितुम्,<BR>to increase, prosper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येषण|अध्येषणं
अध्येषण अध्य्-एषण, अम्, आ, n. f. (fr. rt.<BR>3. इष् with अधि), solicitation, entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रि
अध्रि अ-ध्रि, इस्, इस्, इ (rt. धृ), unrestrained,<BR>irresistible.<BR>—अध्रि-गु, उस्, plur. आवस्, m., Ved.<BR>irresistible; N. of a heavenly killer of victims; N. of<BR>a formula concluding with an invocation of Agni.<BR>—अध्रि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. irresistible.<BR>—अध्रि-<BR>पुष्पलिका, f. a species of the Pāṇ plant, Piper Betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रियमाण
अ-ध्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (pres. pass. part. of rt.<BR>धृ with अ), not held; not to be got hold of, not<BR>forthcoming, not surviving or existing, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुव
अध्रुव अ-ध्रुव, अस्, आ, अम्, not fixed, not<BR>permanent; uncertain, doubtful; separable, admitting<BR>of severance without disastrous effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुष|अध्रुषः
अध्रुष अध्रुष, अस्, m. quinsy, a kind of<BR>sore throat (etymology doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्
अध्वन् अध्वन्, आ, m. (said to be from अद्,<BR>‘to eat,’ द् being changed to ध्, or fr. rt. अत्), a<BR>road, way, orbit; a journey, course; distance; time;<BR>means, method, resource; the zodiac (?), sky, air;<BR>a place; a recension of the Vedas and the school up-<BR>holding it; assault (?). अध्वन् becomes अध्व, अस्,<BR>at the end of some compounds.<BR>—अध्व-ग, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, travelling; (अस्), m. a traveller; a camel, a mule;<BR>the sun; (आ), f. Gangā (the river).<BR>—अध्व-गत्, त्,<BR>m. a traveller.<BR>—अध्व-गत्य्-अन्त or अध्व-गन्त-<BR>व्य, अस्, m. measure of length applicable to roads.<BR>—अध्वग-भोग्य, अस्, m. (traveller's delight), N.<BR>of a tree (Spondias Mangifera).<BR>—अध्व-गमन,<BR>अम्, n. act of travelling.<BR>—अध्व-गामिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, wayfaring.<BR>—अध्व-गा, f. a plant, also called<BR>Svarṇulī.<BR>—अध्व-पति, इस्, m. (lord of the orbits or<BR>of the zodiac), the sun.<BR>—अध्व-रथ, अस्, m. a<BR>travelling car.<BR>—अध्व-शल्य, अस्, m. a plant, Achy-<BR>ranthes Aspera.<BR>—अध्वाधिप (˚व-अध्˚) or अध्वेश<BR>(˚व-ईश्˚), अस्, m. officer in charge of the police on<BR>the public roads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वनीन|अध्वनीनः
अध्वनीन or अध्वन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, speeding on<BR>a journey; (अस्), a traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वयत्|अध्वयन्त्
अध्वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. running, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर|अध्वरः
अध्वर अ-ध्वर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अ, not, and<BR>ध्वर, crookedness, injury), Ved. not crooked,<BR>unbroken, uninterrupted; durable; sound; intent;<BR>(अस्), m. a religious or liturgical service, a sacrifice,<BR>especially the Soma sacrifice; N. of a Vasu; of the chief<BR>of a family; (अम्), n. sky or air.<BR>—अध्वर-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. performance of the Adhvara or connected with<BR>it.<BR>—अध्वर-कल्पा, f., N. of an optional sacrifice<BR>(Kāmyeṣṭi).<BR>—अध्वर-काण्ड, अम्, n. title of the<BR>book in the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa which refers to<BR>Adhvaras.<BR>—अध्वर-कृत्, त्, m. performing an<BR>Adhvara.<BR>—अध्वर-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, intended for<BR>an Adhvara.<BR>—अध्वर-दीक्षणीया, f. consecration<BR>connected with the Adhvara.<BR>—अध्वर-प्रायश्चित्ति,<BR>इस्, f. expiation connected with the Adhvara.<BR>—अध्व-<BR>र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing the word Adhvara.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">Page0024-b+ 73</a>]<BR>—अध्वर-श्री, ईस्, m., Ved. glory (i. e. patron) of the<BR>Adhvara.<BR>—अध्वर-समिष्ट-यजुस्, उस्, n., N. of<BR>an aggregate of nine libations connected with the<BR>Adhvara.<BR>—अध्वर-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, or अध्वरे-<BR>ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. standing at (or engaged in)<BR>an Adhvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरयु
अध्वरयु, etymological substitute for अध्वरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरीय
अध्वरीय or अध्वर्य, nom. (fr. अध्वर), P.<BR>अध्वरीयति or अध्वर्यति, P. to be desirous of<BR>having an Adhvara performed; to institute one (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्यु, उस्, m. one who institutes an Adhvara;<BR>any officiating priest; technical name of a priest of a<BR>particular class (as distinguished from the होतृ, the<BR>उद्गातृ, and the Brahman classes). The Adhvarya-<BR>vas “had to measure the ground, to build the altar,<BR>to prepare the sacrificial vessels, to fetch wood and<BR>water, to light the fire, to bring the animal and<BR>immolate it.” Whilst engaged in these duties, they<BR>had to repeat, without interruption or mistake, the<BR>hymns of the Yajur-veda; hence that Veda itself is also<BR>called Adhvaryu or Adhvaryavas, and the latter word<BR>also means adherents of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—अध्वर्यु-<BR>काण्ड, अम्, n. title of a book of mantras or prayers<BR>intended for Adhvaryavas.<BR>—अध्वर्यु-क्रतु, उस्,<BR>m. sacrificial act performed by the Adhvaryu.<BR>—अध्वर्यु-वेद, अस्, m. the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वस्मन्
अध्वस्मन् अ-ध्वस्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. im-<BR>perishable (?); not causing to fall (?); unveiled, open<BR>to the light (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्त|अध्वांतं|अध्वान्तः
अध्वान्त अ-ध्वान्त, अम्, n. (not positive<BR>darkness), twilight, gloom, shade.<BR>—अध्वान्त-शा-<BR>त्रव, अस्, m. a plant, Cassia Fistula or Bignonia<BR>Indica (not an enemy to darkness, i. e. blossoming in<BR>the shade).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्
अन् 1. अन्-, occasionally अन अन-, (before<BR>a vowel) the substitute for 3. अ, or अ privative.<BR>(Before terminations commencing with vowels) the<BR>substitute for the pronominal base अ, as in अनेन<BR>(अन-इन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्
अन् 2. अन्, cl. 2. P. अनिति or Ved. अनति,<BR>आन, अनिष्यति, आनीत्, अनितुम्, to breathe,<BR>gasp, move, go, live [cf. Gr. ἄνεμος Lat. animus]:<BR>Caus. आनयति, -यितुम्: Desid. अनिनिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन|अनः
अन, अस्, m. breath, spiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन|अननं
अनन, अम्, n. breathing, living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंश
अनंश अन्-अंश, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-अंशिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, portionless; not entitled to a share in an<BR>inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंशुमत्फला
अनंशुमत्फला अन्-अंशुमत्-फला, f. a plan-<BR>tain (the same as अंशुमत्-फला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अनक अनक, अस्, आ, अम्, inferior = अणक,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनकदुन्दुभ
अनकदुन्दुभ अनक-दुन्दुभ, अस्, m. a name<BR>of Kṛṣṇa's grandfather.<BR>—अनक-दुन्दुभि or<BR>better आनकदुन्दुभि, इस्, m. a name given to<BR>Kṛṣṇa's father, Vasudeva; (a name said to be derived<BR>from the beating of drums at his birth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनकस्मात्
अनकस्मात् अन्-अकस्मात्, ind. not without a<BR>cause or an object; not accidentally, not suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष्
अनक्ष् अन्-अक्ष्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. or अन्-अक्ष,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, sightless, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षि
अन्-अक्षि, n. a bad eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षर|अनक्षरं
अनक्षर अन्-अक्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit to be<BR>uttered; unable to articulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षस्तम्भम्
अनक्षस्तम्भम् अन्-अक्ष-स्तम्भम्, ind. so<BR>as not to interfere with the axle-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगार|अनगारः
अनगार अन्-अगार, अस्, m. (houseless), an<BR>ascetic who has adopted a houseless or vagrant con-<BR>dition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगारिका
अन्-अगारिका, f. the houseless life of such an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्न
अनग्न अ-नग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, not naked.<BR>—अनग्न-ता, f. the not being naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नि|अनग्निः
अनग्नि अन्-अग्नि, इस्, m. non-fire; substance<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">Page0024-c+ 75</a>]<BR>differing from fire; absence of fire; (इस्, इस्, इ), re-<BR>quiring no fire or fire-place; not maintaining the<BR>sacred fire, irreligious; unmarried; dispensing with<BR>the use of fire; dyspeptic.<BR>—अन्-अग्नि-त्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or अन्-अग्नि-त्रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, not maintaining the<BR>sacred fire, irreligious (?); not enjoying Agni's pro-<BR>tection (?).<BR>—अन्-अग्नि-दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not burnt<BR>with fire; not burnt on the funeral pile (but buried);<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of manes.<BR>—अनग्नि-<BR>ष्वात्त, आस्, m. pl. = preceding; see अग्नि-दग्ध<BR>and अग्नि-ष्वात्त under अग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघ|अनघः
अनघ अन्-अघ, अस्, आ, अम्, sinless, innocent;<BR>faultless; handsome; (अस्), m. white mustard; N. or<BR>epithet of various persons, especially Śiva.<BR>—अन-<BR>घाष्टमी (˚घ-अष्˚), f., N. of the fifty-fifth<BR>Adhyāya of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्कुश|अनंकुश
अनङ्कुश अन्-अङ्कुश, अस्, आ, अम्, unrestrained,<BR>ungovernable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्ग|अनंग|अनङ्गं|अनङ्गः
अनङ्ग अन्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, incorporeal;<BR>(अस्), m. Love, N. of Kāma, the god of love, so called<BR>because he was reduced to ashes by a flash from the<BR>eye of Śiva, for having attempted to disturb his penance<BR>by filling him with love for Pārvatī; (अम्), n. the<BR>ether, air, sky; the mind, मनस्; that which is not<BR>the अङ्ग, q. v.<BR>—अनङ्ग-क्रीडा, f., N. of a metre<BR>of two verses, the first containing sixteen long syllables,<BR>the second thirty-two short ones.<BR>—अनङ्ग-देवी, f.,<BR>N. of a queen-consort of Kaṣmīr.<BR>—अनङ्ग-पाल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king's chamberlain at Kaṣmīr.<BR>—अन्-अङ्गम्-एजय, अस्, आ, अम्, not shaking the<BR>body (?).<BR>—अनङ्ग-रङ्ग, N. of an erotic work.<BR>—अनङ्ग-लेखा, f. a love letter; N. of a queen of<BR>Kaṣmīr.<BR>—अनङ्ग-शेखर, अस्, m., N. of a metre<BR>of four verses, each containing fifteen iambi.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अङ्ग-सेना, f., N. of a dramatic personage.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अङ्गापीड (˚ग-आप्˚) अस्, m., N. of a king of Kash-<BR>mīr.<BR>—अनङ्गासुहृद् (˚ग-अस्˚), त्, m. Kāma's<BR>enemy, i. e. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गक|अनंगकं|अनङ्गकं
अन्-अङ्गक, अम्, n. the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गुरि|अनंगुरि
अनङ्गुरि अन्-अङ्गुरि, इस्, इस्, इ, destitute of<BR>fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनच्छ|अनच्छः
अनच्छ अन्-अच्छ, अस्, आ, अम्, not pellucid,<BR>turbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनजका
अनजका अन्-अजका or अन्-अजिका, f. a miser-<BR>able little goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनञ्जन|अनंजन|अनञ्जनं
अनञ्जन अन्-अञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>collyrium or pigment or pain; (अम्), n. the sky,<BR>atmosphere; Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुह्
अनडुह् अनड्-उह्, ड्वान्, m. (fr. अनस्, a<BR>cart, q. v., and वह्, to drag), an ox; bull; the sign<BR>Taurus.<BR>—अनडुज्-जिह्वा, f. a plant, also called Gojihvā,<BR>Elephantopus Scaber.<BR>—अनडुद्-द, अस्, m. donor of<BR>a bull or ox.<BR>—अनडुही or अनड्वाही, f. a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुत्क
अनडुत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having oxen (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुह|अनडुहः
अनडुह, अस्, m., N. of the chief of a certain<BR>Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनणु|अनणुः
अनणु अन्-अणु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ, not minute<BR>or fine, coarse; (उस्), m. coarse grain, peas, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनत
अनत अ-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, not bent, not<BR>bowed down; erect; stiff; haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनति
अनति- अन्-अति-, not very-, not too-, not<BR>past-. (Words commencing with अन्-अति are so easily<BR>analysed by referring to अति, &c., that few need be<BR>enumerated).<BR>—अन्-अति-क्रम, अस्, m. moderation,<BR>propriety.<BR>—अन्-अतिक्रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to<BR>be avoided, not to be transgressed, inviolable.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अतिदृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not transparent, opaque;<BR>(or equivalent to अत्य्-अदृश्य), quite indiscernible.<BR>—अन्-अतिद्भुत, अस्, m., Ved. unsurpassed.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अतिवृत्ति, इस्, f. congruity.<BR>—अन्-अतिव्याध्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. invulnerable.<BR>—अन्-अत्यन्त-गति, इस्, f.<BR>the sense of “not exceedingly,” sense of diminutive<BR>words.<BR>—अन्-अत्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, unperishable, un-<BR>broken.<BR>—अन्-अत्युद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (equivalent<BR>to अत्य्-अन्-उद्य), quite unfit to be mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनदत्|अनदन्त्
अनदत् अन्-अदत्, अन्, अती, अत्, not eating, not<BR>consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्धा
अनद्धा अन्-अद्धा or (with part. उ) अन्-अद्धो,<BR>ind., Ved. not truly, not really; not clearly.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अद्धा-पुरुष, अस्, m., Ved. one who is not a true<BR>man, one who is of no use either to gods or men or<BR>the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्य|अनद्यः
अनद्य अन्-अद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not fit to be<BR>eaten; (अस्), m. white mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्यतन|अनद्यतनः
अनद्यतन अन्-अद्यतन, अस्, m. tense which<BR>is not applicable to the current day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिक
अनधिक अन्-अधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, incapable of<BR>being enlarged or excelled; boundless; perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकार|अनधिकारः
अनधिकार अन्-अधिकार, अस्, m. absence of<BR>authority or right or claim.<BR>—अनधिकार-चर्चा, f.<BR>intermeddling, officiousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारिन्
अन्-अधिकारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, not entitled to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकृत
अन्-अधिकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not placed at the head<BR>of, not appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगत|अनधिगतः
अनधिगत अन्-अधिगत, अस्, आ, अम्, not ob-<BR>tained, not acquired; not studied.<BR>—अनधिगत-<BR>मनोरथ, अस्, आ, अम्, disappointed.<BR>—अनधिगत-<BR>शास्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, unacquainted with the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगम्य
अन्-अधिगम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unattainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिष्ठान
अनधिष्ठान अन्-अधिष्ठान, अम्, n. want of<BR>superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिष्ठित
अन्-अधिष्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, not appointed; not<BR>present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीन|अनधीनः
अनधीन अन्-अधीन or अन्-अधीनक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>independent; (अस्), m. an independent carpenter who<BR>works on his own account, see कौट-तक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यक्ष|अनध्यक्षः
अनध्यक्ष अन्-अध्यक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, not ob-<BR>servable; destitute of a superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्ययन|अनध्ययनं
अनध्ययन अन्-अध्ययन, अम्, n. not study-<BR>ing; intermission of study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्याय|अनध्यायः
अन्-अध्याय, अस्, m. = the preceding; time when<BR>there is or ought to be an intermission of study.<BR>—अनध्याय-दिवस, अस्, m. a vacation day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन|अननं
अनन अनन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. अन्), breathing,<BR>living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननङ्गमेजय
अननङ्गमेजय अन्-अनङ्गमेजय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not leaving the body unshaken; see under अन्-अङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुज्ञात
अननुज्ञात अन्-अनुज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>agreed to, not permitted, denied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभावक
अननुभावक अन्-अनुभावक, अस्, ई, अम्, un-<BR>able to comprehend.<BR>—अननुभावक-ता, f. non-<BR>comprehension; unintelligibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभाषण|अननुभाषणं
अननुभाषण अन्-अनुभाषण, अम्, n. not<BR>repeating (for the sake of challenging) a proposition;<BR>tacit assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभूत
अननुभूत अन्-अनुभूत, अस्, आ, अम्, not per-<BR>ceived, not experienced, unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुमत
अननुमत अन्-अनुमत, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>honoured, not liked, disagreeable, unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुषङ्गिन्
अननुषङ्गिन् अन्-अनुषङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, not<BR>attached to, indifferent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुष्ठान
अननुष्ठान अन्-अनुष्ठान, अम्, n. non-ob-<BR>servance, neglect; impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननूक्त
अननूक्त अन्-अनूक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not recited<BR>or studied; not responded to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त|अनंत|अनन्तं|अनन्तः
अनन्त अन्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, endless, bound-<BR>less, eternal, infinite; (अस्), m., N. of many person,<BR>particularly of Viṣṇu; of Viṣṇu's couch, the snake<BR>king Śeṣa; of Śeṣa's brother Vāsuki; of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>of his brother Baladeva; of Śiva, Rudra, one of the<BR>Viśva-devas, the 14th Arhat, &c.; a plant, Sinduvāra,<BR>Vitex Trifolia; Talc; the 23rd lunar asterism, Śravaṇa;<BR>a silken cord tied round the right arm at a particular<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">Page0025-b+ 79</a>]<BR>festival; the letter आ; a periodic decimal fraction?; (आ),<BR>f. the earth; the number one; N. of various females,<BR>especially of Pārvatī; N. of various (perennial?)<BR>plants, particularly one also called Śārivā, Periploca<BR>Indica or Asclepias Pseudosarsa (or Asthmatica), the<BR>root of which supplies a valuable medicine; (अम्), n.<BR>the sky, atmosphere; Talc.<BR>—अनन्त-कर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, rendering endless, magnifying indefinitely.<BR>—अनन्त-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going or moving for ever<BR>or indefinitely.<BR>—अनन्त-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>boundless excellencies.<BR>—अनन्त-चतुर्दशी, f. the<BR>fourteenth lunar day (or full moon) of Bhādra, when<BR>Ananta is worshipped.<BR>—अनन्त-चारित्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Bodhisattva.<BR>—अनन्त-जित्, त्, m., N. of the<BR>fourteenth Jaina Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR>—अनन्त-ता, f. or अनन्त-त्व, अम्, n. eternity,<BR>infinity.<BR>—अनन्त-तान, अस्, आ, अम्, extensive.<BR>—अनन्त-तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>तीर्थ-कृत्, त्, m. the same as Anantajit.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>तृतीया, f. the third day of Bhādra, said to be sacred<BR>to Viṣṇu.<BR>—अनन्ततृतीय-व्रत, the twenty-fourth<BR>Adhyāya of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>दृष्टि, इस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—अनन्त-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of various persons, especially of a king of<BR>Kaṣmīr.<BR>—अनन्त-नेमि, इस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Mālava, a contemporary of Śākyamuni.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>पार, अस्, आ, अम्, of boundless width.<BR>—अनन्त-पाल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a warrior chief in Kaṣmīr.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अनन्त-मति, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR>—अनन्त-मायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>endlessly illusory or delusive or deceitful.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>मूल, अस्, m. a medicinal plant, also called Śārivā.<BR>—अनन्त-राम, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>राशि, इस्, m. (in arithm.) an infinite quantity; a<BR>periodic decimal fraction (?).<BR>—अनन्त-रूप, अस्, आ,<BR>or ई, अम्, having innumerable forms or shapes.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अन्त-अत्, आन्, अती, अत्, eternal, infinite; (आन्), m.<BR>(in the Upaniṣads) one of Brahmā's four feet, earth,<BR>intermediate space, heaven, and ocean.<BR>—अनन्त-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king.<BR>—अनन्त-वात, अस्,<BR>m. a disease of the head, somewhat like tetanus.<BR>—अनन्त-विक्रमिन्, ई, m., N. of a Bodhisattva.<BR>—अनन्त-विजय, अस्, m., N. of Yudhiṣṭhira's conch-<BR>shell.<BR>—अनन्त-वीर्य, अस्, m., N. of the twenty-third<BR>Jaina Arhat of a future age.<BR>—अनन्त-व्रत, अम्, n.<BR>ceremony or festival in honour of Ananta or Viṣṇu<BR>on the day of the full moon in Bhādra; title of the<BR>102nd Adhyāya of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अन्त-शक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, omnipotent; (इस्), m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—अनन्त-शयन, अम्, n. Travancore.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अन्त-शीर्षा, f., N. of the snake king Vāsuki's wife.<BR>—अनन्त-शुष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. possessing bound-<BR>less strength (?); endlessly blowing (?).<BR>—अनन्तात्मन्<BR>(˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. the infinite spirit.<BR>—अनन्ताश्रम,<BR>अनन्तेश्वर, &c., names of persons unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननतक
अननतक, अस्, आ, अम्, endless, boundless, eternal,<BR>infinite; (अम्), n. (among the Jainas) the eternal<BR>(i. e. the aggregate of spirit and matter); the infinite<BR>(i. e. infinite space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त्य|अनंत्य
अनन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, infinite, eternal; (अम्), n.<BR>infinity, eternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तर|अनंतर|अनन्तरं
अनन्तर अन्-अन्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>interior; having (or leaving) no interstice or interval<BR>or pause; uninterrupted, unbroken; continuous;<BR>immediately adjoining, contiguous; next of kin, &c.;<BR>compact, close; (अम्), n. contiguousness; Brahma,<BR>the supreme soul, as being of one entire essence; (अम्),<BR>ind. immediately after; after; afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरज|अनन्तरजः
अनन्तर-ज, अस्, m. (next-born), the son of a<BR>Kṣatriyā or Vaiśyā mother by a father belonging to<BR>the caste immediately above the mother's.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अन्तर-जात, अस्, m. = preceding; also the son of a<BR>Śudrā mother by a Vaiśya father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरायम्
अन्-अन्तरायम्, ind. without a break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरित
अन्-अन्तरित, अस्, आ, अम्, not separated by any<BR>interstice; unbroken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरीय|अनंतरीय
अनन्तरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, concerning (or belonging<BR>to) the next of kin, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तर्हित
अनन्तर्हित अन्-अन्तर्-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, (past<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">Page0025-c+ 73</a>]<BR>part. Pass. of अन्तर्-धा, q. v., with अन्), not con-<BR>cealed, manifest; not separated by a break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्द|अनंद|अनन्दः
अनन्द अ-नन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, joyless, cheer-<BR>less; (आस्), m. pl., Ved., N. of a purgatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्न|अनन्नं
अनन्न अन्-अन्न, अम्, n. rice or food unde-<BR>serving of its name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्य
अनन्य अन्-अन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, no other, not<BR>another, not different, identical; self; not having a<BR>second, unique; not more than one, sole; having<BR>no other (object), undistracted.<BR>—अनन्य-गति, इस्,<BR>f. sole resort or resource.<BR>—अनन्य-गति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>or अनन्य-गतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having only one (or<BR>no other) resort or resource left.<BR>—अनन्य-गामिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, going to no other.<BR>—अनन्य-चिन्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or अनन्य-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, giving one's<BR>undivided thought to, (with loc.).<BR>—अनन्य-चोदित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, self-impelled.<BR>—अनन्य-ज, अस्, m. epi-<BR>thet of Kāma or Love.<BR>—अनन्य-ता, f. or अनन्य-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. identity.<BR>—अनन्य-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>gazing intently.<BR>—अन्-अन्य-देव, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no other god.<BR>—अनन्य-निष्पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(requiring) to be accomplished by no other.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अन्य-पूर्वा, f. a female who never belonged to<BR>another, a virgin.<BR>—अनन्य-प्रतिक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having no other means of resistance or redress.<BR>—अनन्य-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, originating in or with<BR>no other.<BR>—अनन्य-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, thinking of<BR>the only one, i. e. of the supreme spirit.<BR>—अनन्य-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or अनन्य-मनस्क, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or अनन्य-मानस, अस्, ई, अम्, exercising undivided<BR>attention.<BR>—अनन्य-योग, अस्, m. not suitable to any<BR>others.<BR>—अनन्य-विषय, अस्, आ, अम्, exclusively<BR>applicable.<BR>—अनन्य-विषयात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, having the mind fixed upon one (or the sole)<BR>object.<BR>—अनन्य-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, closely attentive.<BR>—अन्-अन्य-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not carried off by<BR>another, safe.<BR>—अनन्यानुभव (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the teacher of Prakāśātman.<BR>—अनन्यार्थ (˚य-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not subservient to another object;<BR>principal.<BR>—अनन्याश्रित (˚य-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>having resorted to another; independent; (अम्), n.<BR>(in law) unencumbered property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यादृश
अन्-अन्यादृश, अस्, ई, अम्, not like others, singular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्वय|अनन्वयः
अनन्वय अन्-अन्वय, अस्, m. want of con-<BR>nexion; (in rhetoric) comparison of an object with<BR>its own ideal, (as, a lady-like lady.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्वित
अन्-अन्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, unconnected, inconsecutive,<BR>desultory, incoherent, irrelevant, irregular; not attended<BR>with, destitute of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनप
अनप अन्-अप, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकरण|अनपकरणं
अनपकरण अन्-अपकरण, अम्, n. (rt. कृ),<BR>not injuring; (in law) non-payment, non-de-<BR>livery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकर्मन्|अनपकर्म्मन्
अन्-अपकर्मन्, अ, n. or अनपक्रिया, f. = pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकार|अनपकारः
अन्-अपकार, अस्, m. harmlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकारिन्
अन्-अपकारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, innocuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकृत
अन्-अपकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, unharmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकर्ष
अनपकर्ष अन्-अपकर्ष, अस्, m. (rt. कृष्),<BR>m. non-degradation, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपग
अनपग अन्-अपग, अस्, आ, अम्, not departing<BR>from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपच्युत
अनपच्युत अन्-अपच्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>not fallen off, not declined; not displaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपजय्य
अनपजय्य अन्-अपजय्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जि),<BR>Ved. impossible to have its victorious character re-<BR>versed or neutralized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्य
अनपत्य अन्-अपत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, childless;<BR>Ved. causing childlessness, unpropitious; (अम्), n.<BR>childlessness.<BR>—अनपत्य-ता, f. childlessness.<BR>—अन्-<BR>अपत्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्यक
अनपत्यक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्रप
अनपत्रप अन्-अपत्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपनिहित
अनपनिहित अन्-अपनिहित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>not curtailed or mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपयति
