अनभिस्नेह
अनभिस्नेह अन्-अभिस्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>affectionate, impassible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिहित|अनभिहितः
अनभिहित अन्-अभिहित, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>named; (Ved.) not fastened; (अस्), m., N. of the<BR>chief of a Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभीशु
अनभीशु अन्-अभीशु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. unbridled;<BR>epithet of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यनुज्ञा
अनभ्यनुज्ञा अन्-अभ्यनुज्ञा (अभ्य्-अनु-ज्ञा),<BR>f. non-permission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यारूढ
अनभ्यारूढ अन्-अभ्यारूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>ascended, not mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्याश
अनभ्याश अन्-अभ्याश or अन्-अभ्यास, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, not near, distant.<BR>—अनभ्यासम्-इत्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, improper to be approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यास
अनभ्यास अन्-अभ्यास, अस्, m. want of prac-<BR>tice or skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्रक
अनभ्रक अन्-अभ्रक, अस्, m. ‘cloudless;’<BR>N. of a class of Bauddha divinities (generally in m.<BR>pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्रि
अनभ्रि अन्-अभ्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (requiring)<BR>no shovel or scraper; epithet of rain-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनम|अनमः
अनम अ-नम, अस्, m. one who needs not<BR>make a salutation to others; a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमस्य
अ-नमस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unworthy of a salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमितम्पच|अनमितंपच|अनमितम्पचः
अनमितम्पच अन्-अमितम्-पच, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(the same as मितम्-पच), not cooking what has<BR>not first been weighed, niggardly, miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमित्र
अनमित्र अन्-अमित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>enemies; (अम्), n. condition of having no enemies;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of various persons, particularly a king of<BR>Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमीव
अनमीव अन्-अमीव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. free from<BR>disease, well, comfortable; salubrious, salutary; sinless;<BR>(अम्), n. good health, happy state, comfort, pros-<BR>perity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनम्बर|अनंबर|अनम्बरः
अनम्बर अन्-अम्बर, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing no<BR>clothing, naked; (अस्), m. a Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनय|अनयः
अनय 1. अ-नय, अस्, m. bad management;<BR>bad conduct (gambling, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनय|अनयः
अनय 2. अन्-अय, अस्, m. evil course, ill<BR>luck; misfortune, adversity.<BR>—अनयङ्-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनरण्य|अनरण्यः
अनरण्य अन्-अरण्य, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Ayodhyā, said by some to have been Pṛthu's father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनरुस्
अनरुस् अन्-अरुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. not sore<BR>or wounded, healed, well, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्गल|अनर्गलं
अनर्गल अन्-अर्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>bars, free, licentious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ|अनर्घः
अनर्घ अन्-अर्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, priceless, in-<BR>valuable; (अस्), m. wrong value.<BR>—अनर्घ-राघव,<BR>अम्, n. title of a drama by Murāri, treating of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्य
अन्-अर्घ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, priceless, not to be had at<BR>any price; anything but valuable.<BR>—अनर्घ्य-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. pricelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थ|अनर्थः
अनर्थ अन्-अर्थ, अस्, m. non-value; a worth-<BR>less or useless object; disappointing occurrence, reverse,<BR>evil; nonsense; (अस्, आ, अम्), worthless, useless; un-<BR>fortunate; having no meaning; having not that (but<BR>another) meaning; nonsensical.<BR>—अनर्थ-कर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, doing what is useless or worthless; unprofit-<BR>able; producing evil or misfortune.<BR>—अनर्थ-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. uselessness, &c.<BR>—अनर्थ-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>minding useless or worthless things.<BR>—अनर्थ-नाशिन्,<BR>ई, m. (destroyer of evil), Śiva.<BR>—अनर्थ-बुद्धि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, having a nonsensical intellect.<BR>—अनर्थ-<BR>भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, malicious.<BR>—अनर्थ-लुप्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, freed from all that is worthless.<BR>—अन्-अर्थ-<BR>संशय, अस्, m. not a risk of one's money; safety of<BR>one's money or wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थक|अनर्थकं
अन्-अर्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, useless, vain, worthless;<BR>meaningless, nonsensical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थ्य
अन्-अर्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, worthless, useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्पण
अनर्पण अन्-अर्पण, अम्, n., Ved. non-sur-<BR>rendering, not giving up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्व
अनर्व अन्-अर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-अर्वन्, आ, आ,<BR>अ, Ved. not liable to be stayed or limited; unob-<BR>structed; irresistible; permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्विश्
अनर्विश् 1. अनर्-विश्, ट्, m., Ved. seated on<BR>the car (अनस्) or cart; a driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्विश्
अनर्विश् 2. अन्-अर्-विश्, ट्, m. (अर् for अरम्,<BR>rt. ऋ), one who fails to reach his destination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्शनि
अनर्शनि अन्-अर्शनि, इस्, m., Ved. N. of a<BR>demon slain by Indra; (etym. doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्शराति
अनर्शराति अन्-अर्श-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. giving<BR>of uninjurious things, one whose gifts do not hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्ह
अनर्ह अन्-अर्ह, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-अर्हत्, अन्,<BR>अन्ती, अत्, undeserving of punishment or of reward;<BR>unworthy; inadequate, unsuitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्ह्यता
अनर्ह्य-ता, f. condition of not being properly<BR>estimated; inadequacy, unsuitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनल|अनलं|अनलः
अनल अनल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अन्, q. v.), fire;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">Page0027-a+ 68</a>]<BR>Agni, the god of fire; digestive power, gastric juice,<BR>bile; wind; N. or epithet of Vasudeva; of a certain<BR>Muni; of one of the eight Vasus; of a certain monkey;<BR>N. of various plants, as Plumbago Zeylanica and<BR>Rosea, and Semicarpus Anacirdium; the letter र्;<BR>the number three; (in astron.) the fiftieth year of Bṛ-<BR>haspati's cycle; the third lunar mansion or Kṛttikā (?).<BR>—अनल-दीपन, अस्, ई, अम्, stomachic.<BR>—अनल-<BR>प्रभा, f. a plant, Halicacabum Cardiospermum.<BR>—अनल-प्रिया, f. Agni's wife.<BR>—अनल-वाट्त, अस्,<BR>m., N. of ancient Pattana.<BR>—अनल-साद, अस्, m.<BR>dyspepsia.<BR>—अनलानन्द (˚ल-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Vedantic writer, author of the Vedāntakalpataru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलङ्करिष्णु|अनलंकरिष्णु
अनलङ्करिष्णु अन्-अलङ्करिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>not given to the use of ornaments; not ornamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलम्
अनलम् अन्-अलम्, ind. not enough; in-<BR>sufficiently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलस
अनलस अन्-अलस, अस्, आ, अम्, not lazy, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलि|अनलिः
अनलि अनलि, इस्, m. a tree, Sesbana<BR>Grandiflora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनल्प
अनल्प अन्-अल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, not a little,<BR>much, numerous.<BR>—अनल्प-घोष, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>clamorous, very noisy.<BR>—अनल्प-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>greatly enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनव
अनव अनव, अस्, m., N. of a man or a<BR>tribe, = अनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवकाश|अनवकाशः
अनवकाश अन्-अवकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no opportunity; uncalled for (there being no “occa-<BR>sion” for it), inapplicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवगाहिन्
अनवगाहिन् अन्-अवगाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt. गाह्),<BR>not dipping into, not studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवगाह्य
अन्-अवगाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवगीत
अनवगीत अन्-अवगीत, अस्, आ, अम्, not made<BR>an object of a contemptuous song, not blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवग्रह
अनवग्रह अन्-अवग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, resistless;<BR>not to be intercepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवग्लायत्|अनवग्लायन्त्
अनवग्लायत् अन्-अवग्लायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved.<BR>not growing remiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवच्छिन्न
अनवच्छिन्न अन्-अवच्छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>intersected, uninterrupted; not marked off, unbounded,<BR>unlimited, immoderate; undefined, undiscriminated.<BR>—अनवच्छिन्न-हास, अस्, m. continuous or im-<BR>moderate laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवत्|अनवन्त्
अनवत् अन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. अन, see under<BR>rt. अन्), endowed with breath or life.<BR>—अनवत्-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. condition of being endowed with life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवतप्त
अनवतप्त अन्-अवतप्त, अस्, m. (among<BR>Buddhists) N. of a serpent king; N. of a lake, =<BR>Rāvaṇa-hrada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवद्य
अनवद्य अन्-अवद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, irreproach-<BR>able, faultless; unobjectionable; (आ), f., N. of an<BR>Apsaras.<BR>—अनवद्य-ता, f. or अनवद्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. faultlessness.<BR>—अनवद्य-रूप, अस्, आ or इ, अम्,<BR>of faultless form or beauty.<BR>—अनवद्याङ्ग (˚य-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, having faultless body or limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवद्राण
अनवद्राण अन्-अवद्राण, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. द्रा),<BR>Ved. not going to sleep, not sleepy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधर्ष्य
अनवधर्ष्य अन्-अवधर्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>not to be defied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधान|अनवधानं
