अनसूय
अनसूय अन्-असूय, अस्, आ, अम्, not spiteful,<BR>not envious; (आ), f. freedom from spite; absence of<BR>ill-will or envy; N. of a daughter of Dakṣa, and of<BR>one of Śakuntalā's friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयक
अन्-असूयक, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-असूयु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>not spiteful or envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूरि
अनसूरि अन्-अ-सूरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. not un-<BR>wise, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्तमित
अनस्तमित अन्-अस्तम्-इत, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>gone down; not subject to setting or declining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्थ|अनस्थः
अनस्थ अन्-अस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-अस्थि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, or अनस्थिक, अस्, आ, अम्, or अनस्थि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, boneless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कार|अनहंकार
अनहङ्कार अन्-अहङ्कार, अस्, m. (non-ego-<BR>tism), absence of or freedom from self-conceit, or<BR>the tendency to regard self as something distinct from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">Page0028-a+ 72</a>]<BR>the supreme spirit; freedom from pride; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>free from self-conceit or pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कृत
अन्-अहङ्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-अहं-वादिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, free from self-conceit or pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कृति|अनहंकृति|अनहङ्कृतिः
अन्-अहङ्कृति, इस्, f. = अन्-अहङ्कार; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>free from self-conceit or pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहन्
अनहन् अन्-अहन्, अस्, n. a day which is no<BR>day, an evil or unlucky day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अना
अना अना, ind., Ved. (inst. of pronom. base<BR>अ), hereby, thus, indeed; also said to be a substitute<BR>for अन् or अन, ‘not,’ in one or two words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकार
अनाकार अन्-आकार, अस्, आ, अम्, shapeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकारित
अनाकारित अन्-आकारित, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>claimed, not exacted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाल|अनाकालः
अनाकाल अन्-आकाल, अस्, m. unseasonable<BR>time; famine.<BR>—अनाकाल-भृत, अस्, m. a slave<BR>who became one voluntarily to avoid starvation in a<BR>time of scarcity; also spelt अन्नाकाल-भृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाश|अनाकाशः
अनाकाश अन्-आकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>transparent atmosphere, differing from it; opaque,<BR>dark; (अस्, अम्), m. n. air or atmosphere undeserving<BR>of its name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकुल|अनाकुलः
अनाकुल अन्-आकुल, अस्, आ, अम्, not beset;<BR>not confused; unperplexed, calm, consistent, regular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकृत
अनाकृत अन्-आकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unre-<BR>claimed, unreclaimable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रान्त|अनाक्रांत
अनाक्रान्त अन्-आक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unassailed,<BR>unassailable; (आ), f. a plant, Prickly Nightshade, So-<BR>lanum Jacquini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्षारित
अनाक्षारित अन्-आक्षारित, अस्, आ, अम्, unre-<BR>proached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्षित्
अनाक्षित् अन्-आक्षित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. not re-<BR>siding or resting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाग
अनाग अन्-आग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sinless;<BR>see अन्-आगस्; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागत|अनागतं
अनागत अन्-आगत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. गम्), not<BR>come, not arrived; future; not attained, not learnt;<BR>unknown; (अम्), n. the future.<BR>—अनागत-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, connected with or relating to the future.<BR>—अनागत-विधातृ, आ, m. (disposer of the future),<BR>provident; N. of a fish.<BR>—अनागताबाध (˚त-आब्˚),<BR>अस्, m. future trouble.<BR>—अनागतार्तवा (˚त-आर्˚), f.<BR>a girl who has not yet attained to puberty.<BR>—अन्-<BR>आगतावेक्षण (˚त-अव्˚), अम्, n. act of looking at<BR>that which is to come next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागति|अनागतिः
अन्-आगति, इस्, f. non-arrival; non-attainment, non-<BR>accession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम|अनागमः
अन्-आगम, अस्, m. non-arrival, non-attainment;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), not come, not present; (in law) not<BR>constituting an accession to previous property, but<BR>possessed from time immemorial, and therefore with-<BR>out documentary proof.<BR>—अनागमोपभोग (˚म-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. enjoyment of such property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागमिष्यत्|अनागमिष्यन्त्
अन्-आगमिष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, one who will not<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम्य
अन्-आगम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unapproachable, unattain-<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागामिन्
अन्-आगामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not coming, not arriving;<BR>not future, not subject to returning; (ई), m. epithet<BR>of the third among the four Buddhist orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागामुक
अन्-आगामुक, अस्, आ, अम्, not in the habit of<BR>coming, not likely to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागस्
अनागस् अन्-आगस्, आ, आस्, अस्, sinless, blame-<BR>less; conferring sinlessness or bliss.<BR>—अनागास्-त्व,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. sinlessness.<BR>—अनागो-हत्या, f. murder<BR>of an innocent person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचरण
अनाचरण अन्-आचरण, अम्, n. or better<BR>अन्-आचार, अस्, m. improper behaviour; departure from<BR>that which is customary or right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचार|अनाचारः
अन्-आचार, अस्, आ, अम्, or अनाचारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>improper in behaviour; regardless of custom or pro-<BR>priety or law; unprincipled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचार्यभोगीन
अनाचार्यभोगीन अन्-आचार्य-भोगीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unfit or improper for a spiritual teacher to eat or<BR>enjoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाज्ञप्त
अनाज्ञप्त अन्-आज्ञप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ज्ञा), not<BR>commanded.<BR>—अनाज्ञप्त-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, doing<BR>what has not been commanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाज्ञात
अनाज्ञात अन्-आज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, unknown,<BR>surpassing all that has ever been known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाढ्य
अनाढ्य अन्-आढ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not wealthy,<BR>poor.<BR>—अन्-आढ्यम्-भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, not be-<BR>coming wealthy; becoming poor (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातत
अनातत अन्-आतत, अस्, आ, अम्, not stretched<BR>or strung (as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातप|अनातपः
अनातप अन्-आतप, अस्, m. freedom from the<BR>blaze of the sun; shade; coolness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातुर|अनातुरः
अनातुर अन्-आतुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. free<BR>from suffering or weariness; well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मन्
अनात्मन् अन्-आत्मन्, आ, m. not self, an-<BR>other; something different from spirit or soul; (आ,<BR>आ, अ), not spiritual, corporeal; destitute of spirit or<BR>mind.<BR>—अन्-आत्म-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of spi-<BR>ritual knowledge or true wisdom.<BR>—अनात्म-प्रत्य-<BR>वेक्षा, f. (with Buddhists) reflection that there is<BR>no spirit or self.<BR>—अन्-आत्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, not<BR>self-possessed; (वत्), ind. unlike one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मक
अन्-आत्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, (with Buddhists) unreal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मनीन
अन्-आत्मनीन, आस्, आ, अम्, not adapted to self;<BR>disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्म्य
अन्-आत्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, impersonal; (अम्), n. want<BR>of affection for one's own family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्यन्तिक|अनात्यंतिक
अनात्यन्तिक अन्-आत्यन्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, not<BR>perpetual, not final; intermittent, recurrent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथ|अनाथः
अनाथ अ-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>master or natural protector; widowed; fatherless;<BR>helpless, poor; (अम्), n., Ved. want of a protec-<BR>tor, helplessness.<BR>—अनाथ-पिण्ड-द or अ-नाथ-<BR>पिण्डिक, अस्, m. (‘giver of cakes or food to the poor’),<BR>N. of a merchant, in whose garden Śākyamuni used<BR>to instruct his disciples.<BR>—अनाथ-सभा, f. a poor-<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद
अनाद अ-नाद, अस्, m. absence of sound (in<BR>pronouncing aspirated letters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिन्
अ-नादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाददान
अनाददान अन्-आददान, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादर|अनादरः
अनादर अन्-आदर, अस्, m. disrespect, con-<BR>temptuous neglect; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. not awe-<BR>struck, calm; indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरण|अनादरणं
अन्-आदरण, अम्, n. disrespectful behaviour, neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरिन्
अन्-आदरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, disrespectful, irreverent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादि|अनादिः
अनादि अन्-आदि, इस्, इस्, इ, having no begin-<BR>ning, existing from eternity.<BR>—अनादि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>state of having no beginning.<BR>—अन्-आदि-निधन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having neither beginning nor end, eternal.<BR>—अनादि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having no beginning.<BR>—अन्-आदि-मध्यान्त (˚ध्य-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having no beginning, middle or end.<BR>—अनाद्य्-<BR>अनन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, without beginning and without<BR>end.<BR>—अन्-आद्यन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, without beginning<BR>and end; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिष्ट
अनादिष्ट अन्-आदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, not indi-<BR>cated; not commanded or instructed; not allowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादीनव
अनादीनव अन्-आदीनव, अस्, आ, अम्, faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत|अनादृतः
अनादृत अन्-आदृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not respected,<BR>disrespected, despised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत्य
अन्-आदृत्य, ind. without respecting, regardless of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेय
अनादेय अन्-आदेय, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit or<BR>improper to be received, unacceptable, inadmissible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेशकर
अनादेशकर अनादेश-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, doing<BR>what is not commanded or not allowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्य
अनाद्य 1. अन्-आद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = अन्-आदि,<BR>having no beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्य
अनाद्य 2. अन्-आद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = अन्-अद्य,<BR>not eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्
अनाधृष् अन्-आधृष्, क्, क्, क् (rt. धृष्),<BR>Ved. not checking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्ट
अन्-आधृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unchecked, unim-<BR>paired, invincible, perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्टि
अन्-आधृष्टि, इस्, m. (‘superior to any check’), N.<BR>of a son of Śūra; also of a son of Ugraseana and<BR>general of the Yādava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्य
अन्-आधृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. invincible, not to<BR>be meddled with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानत
अनानत अन्-आनत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unbent,<BR>not humbled; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुकृत्य
अनानुकृत्य अन्-आनुकृत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. कृ<BR>with आनु for अनु), Ved. inimitable, unparalleled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुद
अनानुद अन्-आनुद, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दा with<BR>आनु for अनु), Ved. not giving way, unyielding,<BR>obstinate; unaided (?), unsurpassed in giving (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुदिष्ट
अनानुदिष्ट अन्-आनुदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. दिश्<BR>with आनु for अनु), Ved. unsolicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुपूर्व्य|अनानुपूर्व्यं
अनानुपूर्व्य अन्-आनुपूर्व्य, अम्, n. separation<BR>of the different parts of a compound word by the<BR>intervention of others; the not coming in regular<BR>order, tmesis.<BR>—अन्-आनुपूर्व्य-संहिता, f. the<BR>manner of constructing a sentence with the above<BR>tmesis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुभूति|अनानुभूतिः
अनानुभूति अन्-आनुभूति, इस्, f., Ved. inat-<BR>tention, neglect; (तयस्), pl. neglectful or irreligious<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापद्
अनापद् अन्-आपद्, त्, f. absence of misfor-<BR>tune or calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापन्न
अनापन्न अन्-आपन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, not realized,<BR>unattained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापान
अनापान अन्-आपान, अस्, m., N. of a prince,<BR>son of Aṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापि
अनापि अन्-आपि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having no<BR>kindred or friends (epithet of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापूयित
अनापूयित अन्-आपूयित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>stinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्त|अनाप्तः
अनाप्त अन्-आप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unattained, un-<BR>obtained; unsuccessful in the effort to attain or obtain;<BR>not apt, unfit; (अस्), m. a stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्ति|अनाप्तिः
अन्-आप्ति, इस्, f. non-attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्य
अन्-आप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unattainable, unobtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्लुत
अनाप्लुत अन्-आप्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, unbathed,<BR>unwashed.<BR>—अन्-आप्लुतङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, or ई,<BR>अम्, having an unwashed body^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाबाध
अनाबाध अन्-आबाध, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>obstacles or troubles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभयिन्
अनाभयिन् अन्-आभयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. fear-<BR>less (epithet of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभू
अनाभू अन्-आभू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. neglectful,<BR>disobliging, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभ्युदयिक
अनाभ्युदयिक अन्-आभ्युदयिक, अस्, ई, अम्, in-<BR>auspicious, ill-omened, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामन्
अनामन् अ-नामन्, आ, आ, अ, nameless; in-<BR>famous; (आ), m. the ring-finger.<BR>—अनाम-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. namelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामक|अनामकं|अनामकः
अ-नामक, अस्, आ, अम्, nameless, infamous; (अस्),<BR>m. the intercalary month; (अम्), n. piles, hæmorrhoids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिका
अ-नामिका, f. the ring-finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामय|अनामयं|अनामयः
अनामय अन्-आमय, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>disease, healthy, salubrious; (अस्), m. Śiva; (अम्), n.<BR>health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयत्|अनामयन्त्
अन्-आमयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. not causing pain,<BR>not hurting; (त्), n., Ved. health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयित्नु
अन्-आमयित्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. salubrious, curative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिन्
अनामिन् अ-नामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. unbending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाम्य
अ-नाम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, impossible to be bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिष
अनामिष अन्-आमिष, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>flesh; bootless, profitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामृण
अनामृण अन्-आमृण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>no enemy that can injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामृत
अनामृत अन्-आमृत, अस्, आ, अम्, immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायक
अनायक अ-नायक, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>leader or ruler, disorderly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत
अनायत अन्-आयत, अस्, आ, अम्, unchecked,<BR>unrestrained; not propped or supported; close, con-<BR>tinuous, unseparated; unextended, having no length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायतन
अनायतन अन्-आयतन, अम्, n. that which<BR>is not really a resting-place or an altar; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having no resting-place or altar.<BR>—अनायतन-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, = the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्त|अनायत्तः
अनायत्त अन्-आयत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, independent,<BR>uncontrolled.<BR>—अनायत्त-वृत्ति, इस् इस्, इ, having an<BR>independent livelihood.<BR>—अनायत्तवृत्ति-ता, f. in-<BR>dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायसाग्र
अनायसाग्र अन्-आयसाग्र (˚स-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having no iron point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास अन्-आयास, अस्, m. absence of ex-<BR>ertion, facility, ease, idleness, neglect; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>easy, ready; (एन), ind. easily.<BR>—अनायास-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, done readily or easily; (अम्), n. an infusion<BR>prepared extemporaneously (in medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायुध
अनायुध अन्-आयुध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. weapon-<BR>less; having no implements (for sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायुषा
अनायुषा अन्-आयुषा, f. or अन्-आयुस्, f., N. of<BR>the mother of Bala and Vṛtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायुष्य
अन्-आयुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not imparting long life,<BR>fatal to long life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारत|अनारतं
अनारत अन्-आरत, अस्, आ, अम्, eternal; (अम्),<BR>ind. eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारभ्य
अनारभ्य 1. अन्-आरभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, improper<BR>or impracticable to be commenced or undertaken.<BR>—अनारभ्य-त्व, अम्, n. impossibility of being<BR>commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारभ्य
2. अन्-आरभ्य, ind. without commencing: this is<BR>used in compounds in the sense ‘detached;’ thus, अन्-<BR>आरभ्य-वाद, अस्, m. a detached remark (upon<BR>sacrifices, &c.); अनारभ्याधीत (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, taught or studied or read as a detached subject<BR>(not as part of regular or authoritative treatise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भ|अनारंभः|अनारम्भः
अन्-आरम्भ, अस्, m. absence of beginning, non-<BR>commencement, not attempting or undertaking; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), having no commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्बण
अनारम्बण अन्-आरम्बण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>(for अनालम्बन) having no support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भण|अनारंभण
अनारम्भण अन्-आरम्भण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>without support (?), or intangible (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारुह्य
अनारुह्य अन्-आरुह्य, ind. not having sur-<BR>mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्य
अनारोग्य अन्-आरोग्य, अम्, n. sickness; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), unhealthy.<BR>—अनारोग्य-कर, अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, unwholesome, unhealthy, causing sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जव|अनार्जवं|अनार्ज्जव
अनार्जव अन्-आर्जव, अम्, n. crookedness,<BR>moral or physical; disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्तव|अनार्त्तव
