अनार्त्विजीन
अनार्त्विजीन अन्-आर्त्विजीन, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit<BR>or unsuitable for a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्य|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य अन्-आर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not respectable,<BR>vulgar, unworthy, inferior, bad, vile; destitute of<BR>Āryas; (अस्), m. not an Ārya.<BR>—अनार्य-कर्मिन्,<BR>ई, m. doing work unbecoming an Ārya or becoming<BR>only a non-Ārya.<BR>—अनार्य-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, of vile or<BR>unworthy origin; (अम्), n. Agallochum being a pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-b" target="_blank">Page0029-b+ 69</a>]<BR>duce of the country of Mlecchas or barbarians.<BR>—अन्-<BR>आर्य-जुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, practised, observed, or pos-<BR>sessed by men who are not Āryas.<BR>—अनार्य-ता, f.<BR>or अनार्य-त्व, अम्, n. vileness, unworthiness, baseness.<BR>—अनार्य-तिक्त, अस्, m. a medicinal plant, a kind<BR>of Gentian (Gentiana Cherayta Rox).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यक|अनार्यकं|अनार्य्यक|अनार्य्यकं
अन्-आर्यक, अम्, n. Agallochum or Aloe wood<BR>(Aquila Agallocha Rox).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्ष
अनार्ष अन्-आर्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, not referring or<BR>belonging to a Ṛṣi or to the genuine text of a Vedic<BR>hymn; e. g. the word इति, added for grammatical<BR>purposes in the Pada-pāṭha to certain words, which in<BR>the Saṃhitā-pāṭha are not followed by इति; not applied<BR>to a Ṛṣi, not added to his name, as an affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्षेय
