अनिष्पत्त्रम्
अनिष्पत्त्रम् अ-निष्-पत्त्रम्, ind. so that the<BR>arrow does not come out (on the other side), i. e. not<BR>with excessive force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिसर्ग
अनिसर्ग अ-निसर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, unnatural,<BR>unnaturally affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तब्ध
अनिस्तब्ध अ-निस्तब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not ren-<BR>dered immoveable or stiff; not paralysed; not fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तीर्ण
अनिस्तीर्ण अ-निस्तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>crossed over; not set aside; not rid of; unanswered,<BR>unrefuted.<BR>—अनिस्तीर्णाभियोग (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>(a defendant) who has not yet (by refutation) got<BR>rid of a charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीक|अनीकं|अनीकः
अनीक अनीक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. अन्),<BR>face; appearance, splendor; edge, point; front, row,<BR>array, march; army, forces; war, combat.<BR>—अनीक-<BR>वत्, आन्, m., Ved. having a face, or constituting the<BR>face, or occupying the front or foremost rank (epithet<BR>of Agni).<BR>—अनीक-विदारण, अस्, m. (shatterer of<BR>armies), N. of a man.<BR>—अनीक-शस्, ind. in rows or<BR>marching columns.<BR>—अनीक-स्थ, अस्, m. a warrior or<BR>combatant; an armed or royal guard, a sentinel; the<BR>trainer of an elephant, an elephant-driver; a mark,<BR>a sing, signal; a military drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकिनी
अनीकिनी, f. an army, a host, forces; a certain force;<BR>three Camūs or one-tenth of an Akṣauhiṇī, i. e. a com-<BR>plete army; 2187 elephants and as many cars, 6561<BR>horses, and 10935 foot; a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीक्षण
अनीक्षण अन्-ईक्षण, अम्, n. not seeing or<BR>looking at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीच
अनीच अ-नीच, अस्, आ, अम्, not low, decent,<BR>respectable; not pronounced with the Anudātta accent.<BR>—अ-नीचानुवर्तिन् (˚च-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, not keeping<BR>low company; (ई), m. a faithful lover or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचिदर्शिन्
अ-नीचि-दर्शिन्, ई, m., N. of a Bauddha saint (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचैस्
अनीचैस्, ind. not in a low voice, loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीड
अनीड अ-नीड, अस्, आ, अम्, having no nest<BR>or settled abode, i. e. incorporeal; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Agni or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीति|अनीतिः
अनीति 1. अ-नीति, इस्, f. impropriety, im-<BR>morality, injustice; impolicy, foolish conduct, indis-<BR>cretion.<BR>—अनीति-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, or अनीति-विद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>clever in immoral conduct or (fr. अ and नीतिज्ञ)<BR>ignorant of morality or policy, not politic or discreet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीति|अनीतिः
अनीति 2. अन्-ईति, इस्, f. freedom from a<BR>calamitous season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीदृश
अनीदृश अन्-ईदृश, अस्, ई, अम्, unlike, dis-<BR>similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीप्सित
अनीप्सित अन्-ईप्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, undesired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीरसन
अनीरसन अ-नीरसन (अ-निर्-रसन), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, not destitute of a waistband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश|अनीशः
अनीश अन्-ईश, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has not<BR>a lord or superior, paramount; powerless, unable;<BR>(अस्), m. Viṣṇu; (आ), f. powerlessness, helplessness.<BR>—अनीश-त्व, अम्, n. powerlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वर
अन्-ईश्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, without a superior; un-<BR>checked, uncontrolled, paramount; without power,<BR>powerless, unable; not belonging to the deity; athe-<BR>istical.<BR>—अनीश्वर-ता, f. or अनीश्वर-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>absence of a supreme ruler.<BR>—अन्-ईश्वर-वादिन्, ई, m.<BR>an atheist, one who denies a supreme ruler of the<BR>universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीह|अनीहः
अनीह अन्-ईह, अस्, आ, अम्, listless, indifferent;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a king of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहा
अन्-ईहा, f. indifference, apathy, disinclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहित
अन्-ईहित, अस्, आ, अम्, disagreeable, displeasing, un-<BR>wished; (अम्), n. displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीळ
अनीळ अ-नीऌअ, Ved. See अ-नीड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु 1. अनु, उस्, वी, उ. See अणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु 2. अनु, उस्, m., Ved. man; N. of a<BR>king, one of Yayāti's sons; (possibly) N. of a non-<BR>Āryan tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु 3. अनु, ind. as a prefix to verbs and<BR>nouns, expresses after, along, alongside, lengthwise,<BR>near to, under, subordinate to, with.<BR>(When prefixed to nouns, especially in adverbial<BR>compounds) it implies repetition, according to, seve-<BR>rally, each by each, orderly, methodically.<BR>(As a separable preposition, with accusative) after,<BR>along, over, near to, through, to, towards, at, according<BR>to, in order, agreeably to, in regard to.<BR>(As a separable adverb) after, afterwards, thereupon,<BR>again, further, then, next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक|अनुकः
अनुक अनु-क, अस्, आ, अम्, lustful (fr. अनु-<BR>कम्, q. v.; or, according to others, fr. 3. अनु with<BR>affix क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथ्
अनुकथ् अनु-कथ्, cl. 10. P. -कथयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to relate after (some one else); to repeat<BR>(what has been heard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथन|अनुकथनं
अनु-कथन, अम्, n. orderly narration, dis-<BR>course, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथित
अनु-कथित, अस्, आ, अम्, related, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकनीयस्
अनुकनीयस् अनु-कनीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, the<BR>next youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्
अनुकम् अनु-कम्, Caus. P. -कामयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक|अनुकः
अनु-क, अस्, आ, अम्, libidinous; see s. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकाम|अनुकामं|अनुकामः
अनु-काम, अस्, m., Ved. desire; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>according to one's desire, agreeable; (अम्), ind. as<BR>desired, at pleasure; wish after wish (?), after one's<BR>wish (?).<BR>—अनुकाम-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. fulfilling one's<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामीन|अनुकामीनः
अनुकामीन, अस्, m. one who acts as he pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्प्|अनुकंप्
अनुकम्प् अनु-कम्प्, cl. 1. A. -कम्पते,<BR>-पितुम्, to sympathize with, compassionate; Caus.<BR>-कम्पयति, -यितुम्, = the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पक|अनुकंपक
अनु-कम्पक, अस्, m. (sympathizer), N. of a king;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), (at the close of compounds) sympathizing<BR>with, compassionating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पन|अनुकंपन
अनु-कम्पन, अम्, n. or अनु-कम्पा, f. sym-<BR>pathy, compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पायिन्
अनु-कम्पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, condoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पित|अनुकंपित
