अनुचि 2. अनु-चि, cl. 3. P., Ved. -चिकेति, to<BR>remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचित
अनुचित 2. अन्-उचित, अस्, आ, अम्, improper,<BR>wrong, unusual, strange.<BR>—अनुचितार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. an unusual meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्त्|अनुचिंत्
अनुचिन्त् अनु-चिन्त्, cl. 10. P. -चिन्तयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to meditate, consider, recal to mind: Caus.<BR>to make to consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्ता|अनुचिंता
अनु-चिन्ता, f. or अनु-चिन्तन, अम्, n. thinking<BR>of, meditating upon, recalling, recollecting; anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्तित
अनु-चिन्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, recollected, recalled,<BR>thought of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्च
अनुच्च अन्-उच्च, अस्, आ, अम्, not high, low,<BR>humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्चैस्
अन्-उच्चैस्, ind. not aloud, in a low voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्चार
अनुच्चार अन्-उच्चार, non-pronunciation,<BR>skipping words. See उच्-चर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छाद|अनुच्छादः|अनुछाद
अनुच्छाद अनु-च्छाद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. छद्<BR>with अनु), a garment which hangs down, or probably<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">Page0033-b+ 70</a>]<BR>that part of the lower garment which hangs down<BR>in front from the waist to the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छित्ति|अनुच्छित्तिः
अनुच्छित्ति अन्-उच्-छित्ति, इस्, f. or अन्-उच्-छेद,<BR>अस्, m. (rt. छिद् with उद्), not cutting off, non-ex-<BR>tirpation, non-destruction, indestructibility.<BR>—अनुच्-<BR>छित्ति-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, possessing the virtue (or<BR>law) of being indestructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिन्दत्|अनुच्छिन्दन्त्
1. अन्-उच्-छिन्दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, not destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिन्न
अन्-उच्-छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, not cut off, unextirpated,<BR>undestroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छेद्य
अन्-उच्-छेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, indestructible, not<BR>severable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिद्
अनुच्छिद् अनु-च्छिद् (अनु-छिद्), cl. 7. P.<BR>-च्छिनत्ति, -च्छेत्तुम्, to cut along or lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिन्दत्|अनुच्छिन्दन्त्
2. अनु-च्छिन्दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, cutting lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिष्ट|अनुच्छिष्टः
अनुच्छिष्ट अन्-उच्छिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. शिष्<BR>with उद्), not rejected, pure (by austerity and devotion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छो
अनुच्छो अनु-च्छो (अनु-छो), cl. 4. P.<BR>-छ्यति, -छातुम्, to cut open or cut up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्
अनुजन् अनु-जन्, cl. 4. A. -जायते, -जनितुम्,<BR>to follow in being born or produced or arising; to<BR>take after (one's parents).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज|अनुजं|अनुजः
अनु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born after, later, younger; (अस्),<BR>m. a younger brother, a cadet; N. of a plant, also<BR>called Trāyamāṇa; (अम्), n., N. of a plant, also called<BR>Prapauṇḍarīka; (आ), f. a younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्मन्
अनु-जन्मन्, आ, m. a younger brother, younger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजात|अनुजातः
अनु-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, after-born, later, younger;<BR>taking after (the parents); after teething (?); born<BR>again, i. e. invested with the sacred cord; (अस्), m. a<BR>younger brother; (आ), f. a younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजनम्
अनुजनम् अनु-जनम्, ind. according to<BR>people, popularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजप्
अनुजप् अनु-जप्, cl. 1. P. -जपति, -पितुम्,<BR>to follow or imitate in muttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजल्प्
अनुजल्प् अनु-जल्प्, cl. 1. P. -जल्पति, -पितुम्,<BR>to follow in talking; A. -जल्पते, to entertain by<BR>conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजागृ
अनुजागृ अनु-जागृ, cl. 2. P. -जागर्ति,<BR>-जागरितुम्, to watch as an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजि
अनुजि अनु-जि, cl. 1. P. -जयति, -जेतुम्, to<BR>subdue: Desid -जिगीषते, to be desirous of subduing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजिघृक्षा
अनुजिघृक्षा अनु-जिघृक्षा. See under<BR>अनु-ग्रह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीव्
अनुजीव् अनु-जीव्, cl. 1. P. -जीवति, -वितुम्,<BR>to follow or imitate in living; to live for any one; to<BR>live by or upon something; to live submissively un-<BR>der: Caus. -जीवयति, -यितुम्, to restore to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीविन्
अनु-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living by or upon; dependent;<BR>(ई), m. a dependent, follower.<BR>—अनुजीवि-सात्-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, made wholly subservient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीव्य
अनु-जीव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be followed in living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजुष्
अनुजुष् अनु-जुष्, cl. 6. A., Ved. -जुषते,<BR>-जोषितुम्, to seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजॄ
अनुजॄ अनु-जॄ, cl. 4. P. -जीर्यति, or cl. 1. P.,<BR>Ved. -जरति, -जरितुम्, -रीतुम्, to follow in getting<BR>old or decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीर्ण
अनु-जीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, grown old or decayed after<BR>or in consequence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्झत्
अनुज्झत् अन्-उज्झत्, अन्, अन्ती or अती, अत्, not<BR>quitting, not leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्झित
अन्-उज्झित, अस्, आ, अम्, undiminished, unimpaired,<BR>not left or lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा 1. अनु-ज्ञा, cl. 9. P. rarely A. -जानाति,<BR>जानीते, -ज्ञातुम्, to permit, grant, allow, consent;<BR>to excuse, forgive; to authorize; to allow one to take<BR>leave, dismiss, bid farewell; to entreat; to behave<BR>kindly: Caus. -ज्ञापयति, -यितुम्, to request, ask<BR>permission, ask for leave, to take leave: Desid.<BR>-जिज्ञासति or -ते, to be willing to grant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
2. अनु-ज्ञा, f. or अनु-ज्ञान, अम्, n. assent, assent-<BR>ing, permission; leave to depart; allowance made for<BR>faults; an order or command.<BR>—अनुज्ञा-प्रार्थना<BR>or अनुज्ञैषणा (˚ज्ञा-एष्˚), f. asking permission,<BR>taking leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञात
अनु-ज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, assented to, permitted,<BR>allowed; ordered, directed, instructed; accepted;<BR>authorized, honoured; allowed to depart, dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापक|अनुज्ञापकः
अनु-ज्ञापक, अस्, m. one who commands or<BR>enjoins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापन|अनुज्ञापनं
अनु-ज्ञापन, अम्, n. or अनु-ज्ञप्ति, इस्, f. author-<BR>ization; issuing an order or permission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्येष्ठ
अनुज्येष्ठ अनु-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, next<BR>eldest; (अम्), ind. after the eldest, according to<BR>seniority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतक्ष्
अनुतक्ष् अनु-तक्ष्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -तक्षति,<BR>-क्षितुम्, -तष्टुम्, to sharpen or stimulate by<BR>offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतन्
अनुतन् अनु-तन्, cl. 8. P. -तनोति, -तनितुम्,<BR>to extend along, to carry on, continue, develop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्
अनुतप् अनु-तप्, cl. 1. P. -तपति, -तप्तुम्,<BR>to heat, to vex, annoy: Pass. -तप्यते or poet.<BR>-तप्यति, to suffer afterwards, repent; to desiderate,<BR>miss: Caus. -तापयति, -यितुम्, to distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्त
अनु-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, heated; filled with regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुताप|अनुतापः
अनु-ताप, अस्, m. repentance, heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापन
अनु-तापन, अस्, ई, अम्, occasioning remorse,<BR>repentance or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापिन्
अनु-तापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, penitent, regretting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर|अनुतरं
अनुतर अनु-तर. See अनु-तॄ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्क्
अनुतर्क् अनु-तर्क्, cl. 10. P. or poet. A.<BR>-तर्कयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to follow in thought, to<BR>regard as or take for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्ष|अनुतर्षः
अनुतर्ष अनु-तर्ष, अस्, m. thirst, wish,<BR>desire; a drinking vessel, one used for drinking<BR>spirituous liquors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षण|अनुतर्षणं
अनु-तर्षण, अम्, n. a vessel from which spi-<BR>rituous liquor is drunk; distributing liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतिलम्
अनुतिलम् अनु-तिलम्, ind. grain after grain<BR>(of Sesamum), i. e. very minutely or by grains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतिष्ठमान
अनुतिष्ठमान अनु-तिष्ठमान. See अनु-<BR>ष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतुन्न
अनुतुन्न अनु-तुन्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. तुद्),<BR>Ved. depressed or repressed (in sound), muffled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतूलय
अनुतूलय अनु-तूलय, nom. P. -तूलयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to rub lengthwise (with a brush or cotton?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतृद्
अनुतृद् अनु-तृद्, cl. 7. P. -तृणत्ति, -तर्दि-<BR>तुम्, to let go, let out; split, sever, open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतृप्
अनुतृप् अनु-तृप्, cl. 4. A. -तृप्यते, -तर्पि-<BR>तुम्, -तर्प्तुम्, -त्रप्तुम्, to take one's fill (or<BR>refreshment) after or later than another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतॄ
अनुतॄ अनु-तॄ, cl. 1. P. -तरति, -रितुम् or<BR>-रीतुम्, to follow across or to the end; to stretch<BR>lengthwise or prostrate: Pass. -तीर्यते, to be laid or<BR>lay one's self lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर|अनुतरं
अनु-तर, अम्, n. fare, freight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्क
अनुत्क अन्-उत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, free from regret,<BR>not regretting, self-complacent, not repenting of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्कर्ष
अनुत्कर्ष अन्-उत्कर्ष, अस्, m. inferiority,<BR>non-elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्त
अनुत्त अ-नुत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not cast<BR>down, invincible; (or, not moistened, = अन्-उत्त?).<BR>—अनुत्त-मन्यु, उस्, m. of invincible wrath, i. e.<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तम|अनुत्तमः
अनुत्तम अन्-उत्तम, अस्, आ, अम्, unsurpassed,<BR>incomparably the best or chief, excellent; not the<BR>best; (in gram.) not used in the उत्तम or first<BR>person.<BR>—अन्-उत्तमाम्भस् (˚म-अम्˚), अस्, n. (in<BR>Sāṅkhya phil.) indifference to and consequent absti-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">Page0034-a+ 72</a>]<BR>nence from sensual enjoyment, as fatiguing.<BR>—अन्-<BR>उत्तमाम्भसिक, अम्, n. indifference to and absti-<BR>nence from sensual enjoyment as involving injury to<BR>external objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तर|अनुत्तरं
अनुत्तर अन्-उत्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, chief, principal;<BR>best, excellent; without a reply, unable to answer,<BR>silent; fixed, firm; low, inferior, base; south,<BR>southern; (अम्), n. a reply which is coherent or<BR>evasive and therefore held to be no answer; (अस्), m.<BR>a class of gods among the Jainas.<BR>—अनुत्तर-योग-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n. title of the last of the four Bauddha-<BR>tantras.<BR>—अन्-उत्तरोपपातिक (˚र-उप्˚), आस्, m. pl.<BR>the same class of gods.<BR>—अनुत्तरोपपातिक-दशा,<BR>आस्, f. pl. title of a book treating of those gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तान
अनुत्तान अन्-उत्तान, अस्, आ, अम्, lying with<BR>the face towards the ground; not supine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्थान|अनुत्थानं
अनुत्थान अन्-उत्थान, अम्, n. (rt. स्था), the<BR>not rising, want of exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्थित
अन्-उत्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, not risen, not grown up<BR>(as grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्ति|अनुत्पत्तिः
अनुत्पत्ति अन्-उत्पत्ति, इस्, f. failure, non-pro-<BR>duction; (इस्, इस्, इ), or अन्-उत्पत्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, not<BR>(yet) produced.<BR>—अनुत्पत्तिक-धर्म-क्षान्ति, इस्,<BR>f. (with Buddhists) acquiescence in the state (and<BR>moral condition) which is still future, preparation for<BR>a future state.<BR>—अनुत्पत्ति-सम, अस्, आ, m. f. (in<BR>Nyāya phil.) arguing against a thing by trying to<BR>show that nothing exists from which it could<BR>spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पन्न
अन्-उत्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, unborn, unproduced;<BR>uneffected, unaccomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पाद|अनुत्पादः
अन्-उत्पाद, अस्, m. the not coming into existence;<BR>the not taking effect.<BR>—अनुत्पाद-क्षान्ति, इस्, f.<BR>acquiescence in not having to undergo another<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पादन
अन्-उत्पादन, अम्, n. not producing, non-pro-<BR>duction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पाद्य
अन्-उत्पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be produced or<BR>created, i. e. eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्साह|अनुत्साहः
अनुत्साह अन्-उत्साह, अस्, m. want of adequate<BR>effort; want of energy or determination; listlessness;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), deficient in determination.<BR>—अनुत्साह-<BR>ता, f. want of determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सुक
अनुत्सुक अन्-उत्सुक, अस्, आ, अम्, not eager,<BR>calm, retiring; moderate.<BR>—अनुत्सुक-ता, f. mode-<BR>rateness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सूत्र
अनुत्सूत्र अन्-उत्सूत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, not ano-<BR>malous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सेक|अनुत्सेकः
अनुत्सेक अन्-उत्सेक, अस्, m. absence of arro-<BR>gance or highmindedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सेकिन्
अन्-उत्सेकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not arrogant or puffed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदक
अनुदक अन्-उदक, अस्, आ, अम्, waterless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदग्र|अनुदग्रः
अनुदग्र अन्-उदग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, not lofty,<BR>low; not projecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदय
अनुदय अन्-उदय, अस्, m. non-rising, the<BR>not rising (of a luminary).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदित
1. अन्-उदित, अस्, आ, अम्, not risen, not appeared.<BR>(For 2. अन्-उदित, see next column.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर
अनुदर अन्-उदर, अस्, आ, अम्, thin, lank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदह्
अनुदह् अनु-दह्, cl. 1. P. -दहति, -दग्धुम्,<BR>to burn over again, to burn up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदा
अनुदा अनु-दा, cl. 3. P. -ददाति, -दातुम्, to<BR>give back, restore, give way, yield, grant, remit; to<BR>pay one out (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद
अनु-द, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. yielding, emulating<BR>others in giving, a follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदत्त
अनु-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, granted, remitted, given<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेय
अनु-देय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be given back or restored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेयी
अनु-देयी, f., Ved. restitution; a female follower<BR>or companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्त|अनुदात्तः
अनुदात्त अन्-उदात्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not raised,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">Page0034-b+ 72</a>]<BR>not elevated, not pronounced with the Udātta accent,<BR>grave; accentless, having the neutral general tone<BR>neither high nor low: the term अनुदात्त is used<BR>by Pāṇini both for the grave or non-elevated accent<BR>(explained by him as सन्नतर, q. v.) which im-<BR>mediately precedes the Udātta, and also for the<BR>general accentless, neutral tone, neither high nor low,<BR>explained as एक-श्रुति, i. e. the one monotonous<BR>ordinary intonation which belongs to the generality<BR>of syllables in a sentence; (अस्), m. one of the three<BR>accents to be observed in reading the Vedas, the<BR>grave accent.<BR>—अनुदात्त-तर, अस्, m. more than<BR>Anudātta, still lower in sound than Anudātta, i. e.<BR>the very Anudātta accent (or a syllable having this<BR>accent) which immediately precedes a syllable hav-<BR>ing the Udātta or Svarita accent, and is therefore<BR>more depressed than the ordinary Anudātta.<BR>—अन्-<BR>उदात्तादि (˚त-आद्˚), n. (in gram.) a nominal base<BR>of which the first syllable is Anudātta.<BR>—अनुदात्तेत्<BR>(˚त-इत्˚), त्, m. a verbal root having for its Anubandha<BR>the Anudātta accent to indicate that it takes the<BR>Ātmane-pada terminations only; also अनुदात्तोप-<BR>देश.<BR>—अनुदात्तोदय (˚त-उद्˚), अम्, n. a syllable<BR>immediately preceding the Anudātta accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार 1. अन्-उदार, अस्, आ, अम्, niggardly,<BR>mean; liberal, munificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार 2. अनु-दार, अस्, आ, अम्, adhered to<BR>or followed by a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदित
अनुदित 2. अन्-उदित, अस्, आ, अम्, unsaid, un-<BR>uttered, interdicted (see 1. अनु-उदित under अन्-<BR>उदय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिनम्
अनुदिनम् अनु-दिनम् or अनु-दिवसम्, ind.<BR>daily, every day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिश्
अनुदिश् अनु-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति, -देष्टुम्,<BR>to point out, to assign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिशम्
अनु-दिशम्, ind. in every quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेश|अनुदेशः
अनु-देश, अस्, m. a rule or injunction, especially<BR>one that points back to a previous rule; reference to<BR>something prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेशिन्
अनु-देशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pointing back, referring back;<BR>being the object of an Anudeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृभ्
अनुदृभ् अनु-दृभ्, cl. 6. P., Ved. -दृभति,<BR>-दर्भितुम्, to make into bundles or chains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृश्
अनुदृश् अनु-दृश्, cl. 1. P. -पश्यति, -द्र-<BR>ष्टुम्, to survey, behold; to keep in view or in mind,<BR>to foresee: Caus. P. -दर्शयति, -यितुम्, to show,<BR>tell, teach: Pass. -दृश्यते, to become or be visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर्शन|अनुदर्शनं
अनु-दर्शन, अम्, n. consideration, regard, refer-<BR>ence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर्शिन्
अनु-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, considering, foreseeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृष्टि|अनुदृष्टिः
अनु-दृष्टि, इस्, f., N. of the ancestress of Ānu-<BR>dṛṣṭineya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रष्टव्य
अन्-उद्रष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, capable of being ob-<BR>served, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदॄ
अनुदॄ अनु-दॄ, Pass. -दीर्यते, to break<BR>through after (another); to be scattered or confused<BR>(in consequence of the confusion of others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेहम्
अनुदेहम् अनु-देहम्, ind. behind the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदैर्घ्य
अनुदैर्घ्य अनु-दैर्घ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, longi-<BR>tudinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्गीर्ण
अनुद्गीर्ण अन्-उद्गीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, not vomited<BR>forth, not disdained; not spurned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धत
अनुद्धत अन्-उद्धत, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. हन्), not<BR>lifted up, humble, unsurpassed, unequalled, unopposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धरण|अनुद्धरणं
अनुद्धरण अन्-उद्धरण, अम्, n. (rt. हृ),<BR>non-removal; not offering, not establishing or proving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धार|अनुद्धारः
अन्-उद्धार, अस्, m. non-partition, not taking a<BR>share; non-removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धृत
अन्-उद्धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, non-removed, not taken<BR>away; uninjured, undestroyed; unoffered; undivided,<BR>unpartitioned; unestablished, unproved.<BR>—अन्-उद्-<BR>धृताभ्यस्तमय (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m. sunset (अभ्य्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-c" target="_blank">Page0034-c+ 70</a>]<BR>अस्तमय), taking place whilst the Āhavanīya fire<BR>continues (अन्-उद्धृत) unremoved from the Gār-<BR>hapatya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्भट
अनुद्भट अन्-उद्भट, अस्, आ, अम्, not exalted,<BR>unassuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्य
