अनुपूर्व|अनुपूर्वं|अनुपूर्व्व
अनुपूर्व अनु-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, regular,<BR>orderly, successive, from the preceding. अनुपूर्वेण<BR>or अनुपूर्व-शस्, ind. in regular order or succession,<BR>from the first, from the beginning, from above down-<BR>wards.<BR>—अनुपूर्व-केश, अस्, m. one who has<BR>regular hair.<BR>—अनुपूर्व-गात्र, अस्, m. one who<BR>has regularly shaped limbs.<BR>—अनुपूर्व-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, descended in a regular line.<BR>—अनुपूर्व-<BR>दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having regular teeth.<BR>—अनु-<BR>पूर्व-नाभि, इस्, m. having a regularly shaped navel.<BR>—अनुपूर्व-पाणि-लेख, अस्, आ, अम्, having regular<BR>lines in the hands.<BR>—अनुपूर्व-वत्सा, f. a cow<BR>which calves regularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

