अनुस्रयामन्
अनुस्रयामन् अन्-उस्र-यामन्, आ, m., Ved.<BR>not going (in a waggon drawn) by oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वान|अनुस्वानः
अनुस्वान अनु-स्वान, अस्, m. sounding con-<BR>formably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वार|अनुस्वारः
अनुस्वार अनु-स्वार, अस्, m. (rt. स्वृ), after-<BR>sound, the nasal sound which is marked by a dot<BR>above the line, and which always belongs to a preced-<BR>ing vowel.<BR>—अनुस्वार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having the<BR>Anusvāra.<BR>—अनुस्वार-व्यवाय, अस्, m. separation<BR>between two sounds caused by an Anusvāra.<BR>—अनु-<BR>स्वारागम (˚र-आग्˚), अस्, m. an augment consisting<BR>in the addition of an Anusvāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुह
अनुह अनुह, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Vibhrātra and father of Brahma-datta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहव|अनुहवः
अनुहव अनु-हव, अस्, m. (rt. ह्वा for ह्वे),<BR>Ved. inviting, stirring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहा
अनुहा अनु-हा, cl. 3. A., Ved. -जिहीते,<BR>हातुम्, to grant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहुङ्कृ|अनुहुंकृ
अनुहुङ्कृ अनु-हुङ्-कृ, cl. 8. A. -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to roar in imitation of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहृ
अनुहृ अनु-हृ, cl. 1. P. -हरति, -हर्तुम्,<BR>to imitate, to exhibit; A. -हरते, to take after (one's<BR>parents).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहरण|अनुहरणं
अनु-हरण, अम्, n. or अनु-हार, अस्, m. imi-<BR>tation; resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहरत्|अनुहरन्त्
अनु-हरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, imitating; (अन्), m., N.<BR>of a man (?); (the deriv. आनुहारति takes Vṛddhi in<BR>both members).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहरमाण
अनु-हरमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, imitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहारक
अनु-हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, imitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार्य|अनुहार्यः|अनुहार्य्य
अनु-हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be imitated; (अस्), m.<BR>monthly obsequies on the day of the new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहोड|अनुहोडः
अनुहोड अनु-होड, अस्, m. a cart (?); (the<BR>deriv. आनुहौडिक, takes Vṛddhi in both members.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुह्राद
अनुह्राद अनु-ह्राद or अनु-ह्लाद, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Hiraṇya-kaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक|अनूकं|अनूकः
अनूक अनूक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. अञ्च् with<BR>अनु), the backbone, spine; the back part of the<BR>altar; a former state of existence; (अम्), n. race,<BR>family; peculiarity of race, disposition, character; (आ),<BR>f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्य
अनूक्य, अम्, n. backbone; flesh on the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूकाश|अनूकाशः
अनूकाश अनू-काश, अस्, m. (rt. काश्), re-<BR>flection (of light), clearness; regard, reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्ष्
अनूक्ष् अनूक्ष् (अनु-उक्ष्), cl. 1. A. अनू-<BR>क्षते, -क्षितुम्, to sprinkle, bedew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचीन
अनूचीन अनूचीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अन्व्-अञ्च्),<BR>coming after, successive; अनूचीनाहम्, on the fol-<BR>lowing day.<BR>—अनूचीन-गर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, born in<BR>successive order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूच्य|अनूच्यं
1. अनूच्य, अम्, n., Ved. the board on the side of a<BR>couch. (For 2. अनूच्य, see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूच्यते
अनूच्यते अनूच्यते (˚नु-उच्˚), Pass. of अनु-<BR>वच्, q. v., p. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्त
अनूक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken after, recited after;<BR>occurring in the (sacred) text; studied; (अम्), n. =<BR>the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्ति|अनूक्तिः
अनूक्ति, इस्, f. mentioning after, repeated mention,<BR>repetition by way of explanation; study of the Veda.<BR>—अनूक्ति-त्व, अम्, n. state of requiring repetition<BR>or explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचान|अनूचानः
अनूचान, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to study; one so<BR>well versed in the Vedas and Vedāṅgas as to be able<BR>to repeat them; one who repeats his lesson after his<BR>master; well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूच्य|अनूच्यं
2. अनूच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूज्जि
अनूज्जि अनूज्-जि (अनु-उद्-जि), cl. 1. P. -जयति,<BR>-जेतुम्, to follow in being victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढ|अनूढः
अनूढ अन्-ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वह्), not<BR>borne, not carried; unmarried; (आ), f. an unmar-<BR>ried woman.<BR>—अनूढ-मान, अस्, आ, अम्, bashful.<BR>—अनूढा-गमन, अम्, n. fornication.<BR>—अनूढा-<BR>भ्रातृ, ता, m. the brother of an unmarried woman;<BR>the brother of the concubine of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूति|अनूतिः
अनूति अन्-ऊति, इस्, f., Ved. not helping, not<BR>coming to aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूत्क्रम्
अनूत्क्रम् अनूत्-क्रम् (अनु-उद्-क्रम्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमितुम्, to follow in going up or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूत्त
अनूत्त अनूत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for अनु-दत्त, rt.<BR>दा), given back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूत्था
अनूत्था अनूत्था (अनु-उद्-स्था), cl. 1. P.<BR>अनूत्तिष्ठत्, अनूत्थातुम्, of follow in rising;<BR>Ved. to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूत्पत्
अनूत्पत् अनूत्-पत् (अनु-उद्-पत्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-पतति, -तितुम्, to fly up after another (with acc.),<BR>raise one's self into the air, jump up afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूत्पा
अनूत्पा अनूत्-पा (अनु-उद्-पा), cl. 1. P., Ved.<BR>-पिबति, -पातुम्, to empty by drinking after an-<BR>other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदक|अनूदकं
अनूदक अन्-ऊदक, अम्, n. (for अन्-उदक),<BR>want of water, aridity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदस्
अनूदस् अनूद्-अस् (अनु-उद्-अस्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-अस्यति, -सितुम्, to toss up behind or after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदि
अनूदि अनूद्-इ (अनु-उद्-इ), cl. 2. P. -एति, -तुम्,<BR>to follow in going up or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदित
अनूदित अनूदित (˚नु-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम् (rt.<BR>वद्), spoken after, spoken according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्य|अनूद्यं
1. अनूद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken to afterwards<BR>or in reply to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्य|अनूद्यं
2. अनूद्य, ind. having said in reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्यमान
अनूद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken in reply to, ac-<BR>cording to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदे
अनूदे अनूद्-ए (अनु-उद्-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. अनूद्-<BR>ऐति, -तुम्, to follow in coming up or rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्देश|अनूद्देशः
अनूद्देश अनूद्देश (अनु-उद्˚), अस्, m. (rt. दिश्),<BR>describing, mentioning according to or conformably<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूधस्
अनूधस् अन्-ऊधस्, आस्, f., Ved. udderless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनून|अनूनं
अनून अन्-ऊन or अन्-ऊनक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whole, entire; having full power; not less, not infe-<BR>rior; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—अनून-गुरु, उस्,<BR>उस् or वी, उ, of undiminished weight, very heavy.<BR>—अनून-वर्चस्, आस्, m., Ved. having full splen-<BR>dor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनून्नी
अनून्नी अनून्-नी (अनु-उद्-नी), cl. 1. P. -नयति,<BR>-नेतुम्, to take out and fill after another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप|अनूपं|अनूपः
अनूप 1. अनूप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अप्, q. v., with<BR>अनु), situated near the water, watery, wet, a watery<BR>country; (अस्), m. pond, bank of a river; a buffalo;<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—अनूप-ज, अम्, n. moist ginger.<BR>—अनूप-देश, अस्, m. a marshy country.<BR>—अनूप-<BR>प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, marshy.<BR>—अनूप-विलास, अस्, m.<BR>title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप्य
अनूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in ponds or bogs (as<BR>water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप|अनूपं|अनूपः
अनूप 2. अनूप, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अनु-वप्), Ved.<BR>bestowing in order. (For. 1. अनूप, see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपदस्
अनूपदस् अनूप-दस् (अनु-उप-दस्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-दस्यति, -सितुम्, to fail (or become extinct) in<BR>consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपसदम्
अनूपसदम् अनूपसदम् (अनु-उप्˚), ind. at<BR>every Upasad (a kind of religious ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूबन्ध्य|अनूबंध्य
अनूबन्ध्य अनू-बन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. बन्ध्),<BR>Ved. to be fastened (as a sacrificial animal); see also<BR>अनु-बन्ध्य, p. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूयाज
अनूयाज अनू-याज. See अनु-याज, p. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूराध
अनूराध अनू-राध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing<BR>welfare, happiness; (आ), f. =अनु-राधा, q. v., p. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरु|अनूरुः
अनूरु अन्-ऊरु, उस्, उस्, उ, thighless; (उस्), m.<BR>the charioteer of the sun, the dawn.<BR>—अनूरु-सार-<BR>थि, इस्, m. whose charioteer is Anūru, i. e. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्जित
अनूर्जित अन्-ऊर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, not strong,<BR>weak; not proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्ध्व
अनूर्ध्व अन्-ऊर्ध्व, अस्, आ, अम्, not high, low.<BR>—अनूर्ध्व-भास्, आस्, m., Ved. one whose splen-<BR>dor does not rise, who lights no sacred fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूर्मि
अनूर्मि अन्-ऊर्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. not waving,<BR>not fluctuating; inviolable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूला
अनूला अनूला, f., N. of a river in Kāśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूवृज्
अनूवृज् अनू-वृज्, ट्, m. f. (?), Ved. a part<BR>of the body near the ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूषर
अनूषर 1. अन्-ऊषर, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. ऊषर<BR>with 3. अ as an expletive or denoting comparison),<BR>saline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूषर
अनूषर 2. अन्-ऊषर, अस्, आ, अम्, not saline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूषित
अनूषित अनूषित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वस् with<BR>अनु), living near another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूष्मपर
अनूष्मपर अन्-ऊष्म-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, (in<BR>gram.) not followed by a sibilant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूह
अनूह अन्-ऊह, अस्, आ, अम्, thoughtless,<BR>careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृक्क
अनृक्क अन्-ऋक्क. See अन्-ऋच् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृक्षर
अनृक्षर अन्-ऋक्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. thorn-<BR>less (as a path or a couch).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृच्
अनृच् अन्-ऋच्, क्, क्, क्, or अन्-ऋच, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not containing a verse from the Ṛg-veda, hymnless,<BR>not conversant with the Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृक्क
अन्-ऋक्क or अन्-ऋच्क, अस्, आ, अम्, containing no<BR>Ṛc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृजु|अनृजुः
अनृजु अन्-ऋजु, उस्, उस्, उ, not straight,<BR>crooked, perverse, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृण
अनृण अन्-ऋण, अस्, आ, अम्, free from debt.<BR>—अनृण-ता, f. or अनृण-त्व, अम्, n. freedom<BR>from debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृणिन्
अन्-ऋणिन् ई, इनी, इ, unindebted, free from debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृत|अनृतं
अनृत अन्-ऋत, अस्, आ, अम्, not true, false;<BR>(अम्), n. falsehood, lying, cheating; agriculture.<BR>—अनृत-देव, अस्, m., Ved. one whose gods are<BR>not true; playing unfairly (?).<BR>—अनृत-द्विष्, ट्, ट्,<BR>ट्, Ved. persecuting untruth.<BR>—अनृत-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, full of untruth, false.<BR>—अनृत-वदन, अम्, n.<BR>or अनृत-भाषण, अम्, n. or अनृताख्यान (˚त-<BR>आख्˚), अम्, n. speaking falsehood, lying.<BR>—अनृत-<BR>वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or अनृत-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, speaking<BR>untruth.<BR>—अनृत-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, false to vows or<BR>engagements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतिन्
अनृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who tells untruths, lying, a<BR>liar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतु|अनृतुः
अनृतु अन्-ऋतु, उस्, m. unfit season.<BR>—अनृतु-<BR>कन्या, f. a girl before menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृशंस
अनृशंस अ-नृशंस, अस्, आ, अम्, not cruel,<BR>mild.<BR>—अनृशंस-ता, f. mildness, kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेक|अनेकं
अनेक अन्-एक, अस्, आ, अम्, not one, many,<BR>much; separated.<BR>—अनेक-कालम्, ind. a long time,<BR>for a long time.<BR>—अनेककालावधि (˚ल-अव्˚), ind.<BR>long since.<BR>—अनेक-कृत्, त्, m. doing much, epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—अनेक-गोत्र, अस्, m. having more families<BR>than one, i. e. two, belonging to two families (or to<BR>one as an adopted son).<BR>—अनेक-चर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>gregarious.<BR>—अनेक-चित्त-मन्त्र, अस्, m. one whose<BR>counsels are many-minded.<BR>—अनेक-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>born more than once; (अस्), m. a bird.<BR>—अनेक-ता,<BR>f. or अनेक-त्व, अम्, n. muchness, manifold condi-<BR>tion.<BR>—अनेक-त्र, ind. in many places.<BR>—अनेक-<BR>धर्म-कथा, f. different exposition of the law.<BR>—अनेक-धा, ind. in various ways, often.<BR>—अनेक-<BR>धा-प्रयोग, अस्, m. using several times.<BR>—अनेक-<BR>प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking oftener than once; (अस्, आ),<BR>m. f. an elephant, because he drinks with his trunk<BR>and with his mouth.<BR>—अनेक-भार्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having more wives than one.<BR>—अनेक-मुख, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having several faces, having different ways.<BR>—अनेक-युद्ध-विजयिन्, ई, m. victorious in many<BR>battles.<BR>—अनेक-रन्ध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having many<BR>holes, weaknesses or troubles.<BR>—अनेक-रूप, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, multiform; of various kinds or sorts; fickle, of<BR>variable mind.<BR>—अनेक-लोचन, अस्, m. having seve-<BR>ral (three) eyes, N. of Śiva.<BR>—अनेक-वचन, अम्,<BR>n. the plural number.<BR>—अनेक-वर्ण, (in arithmetic<BR>compounded with various words to denote) many un-<BR>known quantities (colours representing x, y, z, &c.),<BR>e. g. अनेक-वर्ण-गुणन, multiplication of many<BR>unknown quantities. (Similarly, if for गुणन<BR>be substituted भजन ‘division,’ मध्यमाह-<BR>रण ‘taking away the middle term,’ व्यवकलन<BR>‘subtraction,’ सङ्कलन ‘addition,’ other algebraical<BR>processes may be expressed).<BR>—अनेक-वारम्, ind.<BR>many times, repeatedly.<BR>—अनेक-विध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of many kinds, in different ways, various.<BR>—अनेक-<BR>शफ, अस्, आ, अम्, cloven-hoofed.<BR>—अनेक-शब्द,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, expressed by several words, synonymous.<BR>—अनेक-शस्, ind. in great numbers, several times,<BR>repeatedly, by large numbers or quantities.<BR>—अनेका-<BR>कार (˚क-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, multiform.<BR>—अनेका-<BR>क्षर (˚क-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, polysyllabic, having<BR>more than one syllable.<BR>—अनेकाग्र (˚क-अग्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, engaged in various pursuits.<BR>—अनेकाच् (˚क-<BR>अच्), having more than one vowel or syllable (अच् in<BR>gram. being the technical term for vowel).<BR>—अने-<BR>कार्थ (˚क-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having more than one<BR>meaning (as a word).<BR>—अनेकार्थ-ध्वनि-मञ्-<BR>जरी, f. and अनेकार्थ-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. titles of<BR>two works on such words.<BR>—अनेकाल् (˚क-अल्), con-<BR>sisting of more than one अल् or letter (in the technical<BR>phras. of gram.).<BR>—अनेकाश्रय (˚क-आश्˚), अस्, m. or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">Page0043-a+ 69</a>]<BR>अनेकाश्रित (˚क-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (in Vaiśeṣika<BR>phil.) dwelling, abiding in more than one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाकिन्
अन्-एकाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not alone, accompanied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकान्त|अनेकान्तः
अन्-एकान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not alone and excluding<BR>every other, uncertain.<BR>—अनेकान्त-त्व, अम्, n. un-<BR>certainty.<BR>—अनेकान्त-वाद, अस्, m. scepticism.<BR>—अनेकान्त-वादिन्, ई, m. a sceptic; a Jaina, an<BR>Arhat of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकीकरण
अनेकी-करण, अम्, n. making manifold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकीभवत्|अनेकीभवन्त्
अनेकी-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being manifold, i. e.<BR>divided in two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकीय
अनेकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, having several.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेजत्|अनेजन्त्
अनेजत् अन्-एजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (rt. एज् with<BR>अन्), not moving, immoveable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेड|अनेडः
अनेड अन्-एड, अस्, m. (अन् being an expletive<BR>or denoting comparison), stupid, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेडमूक|अनेडमूकः
अन्-एड-मूक, अस्, आ, अम्, deaf and dumb; blind;<BR>wicked, fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेद्य
अनेद्य 1. अ-नेद्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. निद्), Ved.<BR>not to be blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेद्य
अनेद्य 2. अ-नेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अ and<BR>नेद्यस्, a contraction of नेदीयस्?), Ved. not near,<BR>infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेन|अनेनः
अनेन 1. अन्-एन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according<BR>to native authorities) sinless, faultless; (according to<BR>German scholars) without a variegated set (of horses).<BR>See एत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेनस्
अन्-एनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, blameless, sinless, not liable<BR>to error; N. of various personages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेनस्य
अन्-एनस्य, अम्, n. freedom from fault, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेन|अनेनः
अनेन 2. अनेन, अस्, m. (fr. इन and अन<BR>for अन्); this doubtful word may signify one who has<BR>no superior, ‘a sovereign or paramount lord;’ see इन<BR>and अन for अन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेमन्
अनेमन् अ-नेमन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. to be praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेव
अनेव अन्-एव, ind. otherwise (?), or (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेहस्
अनेहस् अन्-एहस्, आ, आ, अस् (fr. rt. ईह् with अन्),<BR>Ved. without a rival, incomparable, unattainable; un-<BR>menaced, unobstructed; (आ), m. time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्त|अनैकांत
अनैकान्त अन्-ऐकान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. एकान्त),<BR>variable, unsteady; (in logic) occasional, as a cause<BR>not invariably attended by the same effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्तिक|अनैकांतिक
अन्-ऐकान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, unsteady, variable, hav-<BR>ing many objects or purposes.<BR>—अनैकान्तिक-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. unsteadiness, uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैक्य|अनैक्यं
अनैक्य अन्-ऐक्य, अम्, n. (एक), want of<BR>oneness, plurality, the existence of many; want of<BR>union, anarchy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैपुण
अनैपुण अ-नैपुण or अ-नैपुण्य, अम्, n.<BR>unskilfulness. See आनैपुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैश्वर्य|अनैश्वर्य्य
अनैश्वर्य अन्-ऐश्वर्य, अम्, n. weakness.<BR>See आनैश्वर्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनो
अनो अनो, ind. no, not. (An unusual<BR>form of नो.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकशायिन्
अनोकशायिन् अन्-ओक-शायिन्, ई, m. not sleep-<BR>ing in a house (as a beggar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकह|अनोकहः
अन्-ओक-ह, अस्, m. not quitting the house, a tree;<BR>(ओक is for ओकस्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोङ्कृत|अनोंकृत
अनोङ्कृत अन्-ओङ्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not ac-<BR>companied by the holy syllable ॐ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोदित
अनोदित अनोदित (अन-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>addressed (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोवाह्य
अनोवाह्य अनो-वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be carried<BR>on a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौचित्य|अनौचित्यं
अनौचित्य अन्-औचित्य, अम्, n. unfitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौजस्य|अनौजस्यं
अनौजस्य अन्-औजस्य, अम्, n. want of<BR>vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौद्धत्य|अनौद्धत्यं
अनौद्धत्य अन्-औद्धत्य, अम्, n. freedom<BR>from haughtiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौपम्य
अनौपम्य अन्-औपम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unpa-<BR>ralleled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनौरस
अनौरस अन्-औरस, अस्, m. not one's own<BR>son, adopted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्|अत्|अंत्
अन्त् अन्त्, cl. 1. P. अन्तति, -तितुम्, to<BR>bind [cf. अन्द्, ईन्त्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त|अंत|अन्तं|अन्तः
अन्त अन्त, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अम् ?), end, limit,<BR>boundary, term; end of a texture; end, conclusion;<BR>end of life, death, destruction (in these latter senses<BR>sometimes neut.); a final syllable, termination; last<BR>word of a compound; pause, settlement, definite as-<BR>certainment, certainty; whole amount; border; near-<BR>ness, proximity, presence (e. g. ग्रामान्ते, in the<BR>neighbourhood of the village); inner part, inside; con-<BR>dition, nature; अन्ते, loc. c. in the end, at last; in the<BR>inside; अन्तम् at the end of a compound means<BR>‘as far as,’ thus उदकान्तम्, as far as the water;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), near, handsome, agreeable [cf. Goth.<BR>andeis, Theme andja; Germ. Ende; Eng. end:<BR>with अन्त are also compared the Greek ἄντα, ἀντί<BR>Lat. ante; the Goth. anda in anda-vaurd, &c.; and<BR>the Germ. ent, e. g. in entsagen].<BR>—अन्त-कर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, or अन्त-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, or अन्त-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, causing death, mortal, destructive.<BR>—अन्त-<BR>काल, अस्, m. time of death, death.<BR>—अन्त-कृत्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, making an end; (त्), m. death.<BR>—अन्तकृद्-दशा,<BR>आस्, f. pl. a sacred book of the Jainas, containing ten<BR>chapters.<BR>—अन्त-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going to the end,<BR>thoroughly conversant with.<BR>—अन्त-गति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>or अन्त-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going to the end, pe-<BR>rishing.<BR>—अन्त-गमन, अम्, n. the going to the<BR>end of something, finishing; the going to the end,<BR>dying.<BR>—अन्त-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going to the fron-<BR>tiers, walking about the frontiers.<BR>—अन्त-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, last born.<BR>—अन्त-जाति, see अन्त्य-जाति.<BR>—अन्त-<BR>तस्, ind. from the end, from the term; lastly, finally;<BR>in the lowest way; in part; within.<BR>—अन्त-दीपक,<BR>अम्, n. a figure in rhetoric.<BR>—अन्त-पाल, अस्, m. a<BR>frontier-guard.<BR>—अन्त-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, being at<BR>the end, last.<BR>—अन्त-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, standing at the<BR>end (of a word).<BR>—अन्त-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, delighting<BR>in destruction.<BR>—अन्त-लीन, अस्, आ, अम्, hidden, con-<BR>cealed.<BR>—अन्त-लोप, अस्, m. the dropping of the final<BR>of a word (in grammar).<BR>—अन्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having an end or term, limited, perishable; (-वत्),<BR>ind. like the end.<BR>—अन्तवत्-त्व, अम्, n. limited<BR>existence, perishableness.<BR>—अन्त-वह्नि, इस्, m. the<BR>fire of the end, by which the world is to be burnt.<BR>—अन्त-वासिन् or अन्ते-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling<BR>near the boundaries, dwelling close by; (ई), m. a<BR>pupil who dwells near or in the house of his teacher;<BR>a Cāṇḍāla (who lives at the end of the town).<BR>—अन्त-वेला, f. hour of death.<BR>—अन्त-शय्या, f. a<BR>bed or mat on the ground; death; the place for<BR>burial or burning; bier.<BR>—अन्त-सत्क्रिया, f. the fu-<BR>neral ceremonies.<BR>—अन्त-सद्, त्, m. a pupil (who<BR>dwells near his teacher).<BR>—अन्त-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>standing at the end; see also अन्तः-स्थ.<BR>—अन्त-<BR>स्वरित, अस्, m. the Svarita accent on the last syllable<BR>of a word; (अम्), n. a word thus accentuated.<BR>—अन्तादि (˚त-आदि), ई, du. m. end and beginning.<BR>—अन्तावसायिन् or अन्तावशायिन् (˚त-अव्˚), ई, m. a<BR>barber; a Cāṇḍāa; N. of a Muni or saint; see<BR>अन्त्यावसायिन्.<BR>—अन्ते-वास, अस्, m. a neighbour, a<BR>companion, a pupil.<BR>—अन्ते-वासि, ind. in statu pupil-<BR>lari; see अन्त-वासिन् above.<BR>—अन्तोदात्त (˚त-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the acute accent on the last syllable; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), having the acute accent on the last syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तक|अंतक|अन्तकः
अन्तक, अस्, m. border, boundary; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>making an end, causing death; (अस्), m. death; Ya-<BR>ma, king or lord of death.<BR>—अन्तक-द्रुह्, -ध्रुक्,<BR>क्, क्, Ved. offending or provoking destructive demons,<BR>or death, or Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकि
अन्तकि, इस्, m. wind (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तम|अंतम
अन्तम, अस्, आ, अम्, next, nearest, intimate (as a<BR>friend); Ved. last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तय
अन्तय, nom. P. अन्तयति, -यितुम्, to make an<BR>end of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अन्तिक, अन्तिम, अन्त्य, &c. See अन्तिक, p. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तः|अन्त|अंत|अन्तं
अन्तः अन्तः. See अन्तर् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःख्या
अन्तःख्या अन्तः-ख्या (अन्तर्-ख्या), cl. 2. P.,<BR>Ved. -ख्याति, -तुम्, to deprive of, keep back, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तम|अंतम
अन्तम अन्तम. See s. v. अन्त last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्|अंतर्
अन्तर् अन्तर्, ind. within, between, amongst,<BR>in the middle or interior; a particle of assent.<BR>(As a prep. with loc.) in the middle, in, between, in-<BR>to; (with acc.) between; (with gen.) in, in the middle.<BR>(When used at the end of a compound) in, into,<BR>in the middle of, between, out of the midst of [cf.<BR>Zend antarĕ; Lat. inter; Goth. undar].<BR>Sometimes अन्तर् is compounded with a following<BR>word like an adjective, meaning interior, internal,<BR>intermediate.<BR>—अन्तः-करण, अम्, n. the internal<BR>and spiritual part of man, the seat of thought and<BR>feeling, the mind, the thinking faculty, the heart,<BR>the conscience, the soul.<BR>—अन्तः-कल्प, अस्, m. a<BR>certain number of years (in Buddhism).<BR>—अन्तः-<BR>कुटिल, अस्, आ, अम्, internally crooked; fraudulent;<BR>(अस्), m. a couch.<BR>—अन्तः-कृमि, इस्, m. a disease<BR>caused by worms in the body.<BR>—अन्तः-कोटर-पुष्-<BR>पी, a various reading for अण्ड-कोटर-पुष्पी, q. v.<BR>—अन्तः-कोण, अस्, m. the inner corner.<BR>—अन्तः-<BR>कोप, अस्, m. inward wrath.<BR>—अन्तः-कोश, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. the interior of a store-room.<BR>—अन्तः-पट, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a cloth held between two persons who<BR>are to be united (as bride and bridegroom, or pupil<BR>and teacher) until the right moment of union is<BR>arrived.<BR>—अन्तः-पदम्, ind. in the middle of an<BR>inflected word.<BR>—अन्तः-परिधान, अम्, n. the in-<BR>nermost garment.<BR>—अन्तः-परिधि, ind. in the inside<BR>of an enclosure.<BR>—अन्तः-पर्शव्य or अन्तः-पार्-<BR>श्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being between the ribs (as flesh).<BR>—अन्तः-पवित्र, the Soma when in the straining-<BR>vessel (?).<BR>—अन्तः-पशु, ind. from evening till morn-<BR>ing (while the cattle is in the stables).<BR>—अन्तः-पात<BR>or अन्तः-पात्य, अस्, m. (in gram.) insertion of a<BR>letter; a post fixed in the middle of the place of<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—अन्तः-पातित, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्तः-पातिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, inserted, included in.<BR>—अन्तः-पात्र, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. the interior of a vessel.<BR>—अन्तः-पादम्,<BR>ind. within the Pāda of a verse.<BR>—अन्तः-पाल, अस्,<BR>m. one who watches the inner apartments of a palace.<BR>—अन्तः-पुर, अम्, n. the king's palace, the female<BR>apartments, gynæceum; those who live in the female<BR>apartments; a queen.<BR>—अन्तःपुर-चर, अस्, m.<BR>guardian of the women's apartments.<BR>—अन्तःपुर-<BR>जन, अस्, m. the women of the palace.<BR>—अन्तःपुर-<BR>प्रचार, अस्, m. the gossip of the women's apart-<BR>ments.<BR>—अन्तःपुर-रक्षक, अस्, m. or अन्तः-<BR>पुर-वर्तिन्, ई, m. or अन्तःपुराध्यक्ष (˚र-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. superintendent of the gynæceum, cham-<BR>berlain.<BR>—अन्तः-पुर-सहाय, अस्, m. belonging to<BR>the gynæceum (as an eunuch, &c.).<BR>—अन्तः-पुरिक,<BR>अस्, m. superintendent of the gynæceum; (आ), f. a<BR>woman in the gynæceum.<BR>—अन्तः-पूय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ulcerous.<BR>—अन्तः-पेय, अम्, n., Ved. supping up,<BR>drinking.<BR>—अन्तः-प्रकृति, इस्, f. the heart, the<BR>soul, the internal nature or constitution of a man.<BR>—अन्तः-प्रज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, internally wise, know-<BR>ing one's self.<BR>—अन्तः-प्रतिष्ठान, अम्, n. resi-<BR>dence in the interior.<BR>—अन्तः-प्रतिष्ठित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, residing inside.<BR>—अन्तः-शर, अस्, m. an internal<BR>arrow or disease.<BR>—अन्तः-शरीर, अम्, n. the inter-<BR>nal and spiritual part of man.<BR>—अन्तः-शल्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a pin or extraneous body sticking in-<BR>side.<BR>—अन्तः-शिला, f., N. of a river.<BR>—अन्तः-श्लेष,<BR>अस्, m. or अन्तः-श्लेषण, अम्, n., Ved. internal sup-<BR>port.<BR>—अन्तः-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, internally conscious.<BR>—अन्तः-सत्त्वा, f. a pregnant woman; the mark-<BR>ing nut (Semecarpus Anacardium L.).<BR>—अन्तः-सद-<BR>सम्, ind. in the middle of the assembly.<BR>—अन्तः-<BR>सार, अस्, आ, अम्, having internal essence; (अस्), m.<BR>internal treasure, inner store or contents.<BR>—अन्तः-<BR>सुख, अस्, आ, अम्, internally happy.<BR>—अन्तः-सेनम्,<BR>ind. into the midst of the armies.<BR>—अन्तः-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being in the midst or between; a term ap-<BR>plied to the semivowels, as standing between the con-<BR>sonants and vowels; (आ), f. the god of the vital<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-a" target="_blank">Page0044-a+ 80</a>]<BR>organs; an epithet of one of the Ṛg-veda mantras.<BR>—अन्तःस्थ-मुद्गर, अस्, m. (in anatomy) the<BR>malleus of the ear.<BR>—अन्तः-स्वेद, अस्, m. an ele-<BR>phant.<BR>—अन्तर्-अंस or अन्तरांस (˚रा-अं˚), अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. the part of the body between the shoul-<BR>ders, the breast.<BR>—अन्तर्-अग्नि, इस्, m. the interior fire,<BR>digestive force.<BR>—अन्तर्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, interior,<BR>proximate, related, being essential to, or having refer-<BR>ence to the essential part of the अङ्ग or base of a<BR>word.<BR>—अन्तरङ्ग-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, not essential<BR>to the base of a word, lit. beyond or external to it.<BR>—अन्तरङ्ग-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of<BR>an Antaraṅga.<BR>—अन्तर्-अवयव, अस्, m. an inner<BR>limb or part.<BR>—अन्तर्-आकाश, अस्, m. the sacred ether<BR>or Brahma in the interior part or soul of man.<BR>—अन्तर्-आकूत, अम्, n. hidden intention.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>आगम, अस्, m. an additional augment between two<BR>letters (in gram.).<BR>—अन्तर्-आगार, अस्, m. the interior<BR>of a house<BR>—अन्तर्-आत्मन्, आ, m. the soul, the inhe-<BR>rent supreme spirit; the internal feelings, the heart<BR>or mind.<BR>—अन्तर्-आत्मेष्टकम् (˚मन्-इष्˚), ind.<BR>in the space between one's self and the (sacrificial)<BR>bricks.<BR>—अन्तर्-आपण, अस्, m. a market inside (a<BR>town).<BR>—अन्तराय, see अन्तर्-इ.<BR>—अन्तर्-आराम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, rejoicing in one's self (not in the exterior<BR>world).<BR>—अन्तर्-आल or अन्तर्-आलक, अम्, n. inter-<BR>mediate space; अन्तराले, in the midst, in midway;<BR>(आल is probably for आलय).<BR>—अन्तर्-इन्द्रिय, अम्,<BR>n. an internal organ, of which there are four, viz.<BR>मनस्, बुद्धि, अहङ्कार, and चित्त.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>ईप, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. अप्), an island, a promontory.<BR>—अन्तर्-उष्य, अम्, n. (rt. वस्), Ved. a secret abode.<BR>—अन्तर्-गङ्गा, f. the Ganges, as supposed to com-<BR>municate under-ground with a sacred spring in Mysore.<BR>—अन्तर्-गडु, उस्, उस्, उ, unprofitable, useless (filled<BR>with worms).<BR>—अन्तर्-गत, &c.; see under अन्तर्-<BR>गम्.<BR>—अन्तर्-गर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, inclosing young;<BR>pregnant.<BR>—अन्तर्-गिरम् or अन्तर्-गिरि, ind. among<BR>the mountains.<BR>—अन्तर्-गुद-वलय, अस्, m. (in<BR>medicine) the sphincter muscle.<BR>—अन्तर्-गूढ-<BR>विष, अस्, आ, अम्, having hidden poison within.<BR>—अन्तर्-गृह, अम्, n. an inner apartment of the<BR>house; अन्तर्-गृहम् or अन्तर्-गेहम्, ind. in the<BR>interior of a house.<BR>—अन्तर्-घण, अस्, or अन्तर्-<BR>घन, अस्, m. a place between the entrance-door and<BR>the house; N. of a village.<BR>—अन्तर्-घात, अस्, m.<BR>striking in the middle.<BR>—अन्तर्-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, bred<BR>in the interior (of the body, as a worm).<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>जठर, अम्, n. the stomach.<BR>—अन्तर्-जन्मन्, अ,<BR>n. inward birth.<BR>—अन्तर्-जम्भ, अस्, m. the inner<BR>part of the jaws.<BR>—अन्तर्-जल-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going<BR>in the water.<BR>—अन्तर्-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, inborn, inbred,<BR>innate.<BR>—अन्तर्-जानु, ind. between the knees; (उस्,<BR>उस्, उ), being between the knees.<BR>—अन्तर्-ज्ञान, अम्,<BR>n. inward knowledge.<BR>—अन्तर्-ज्योतिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, having<BR>the soul enlightened, illuminated.<BR>—अन्तर्-ज्वलन,<BR>अम्, n. internal heat, inflammation.<BR>—अन्तर्-दग्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, burnt inwardly.<BR>—अन्तर्-दधन, अम्,<BR>n. the distillation of spirituous liquor, or a substance<BR>used to cause fermentation.<BR>—अन्तर्-दधान, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, vanishing, disappearing, hiding one's self<BR>[cf. अन्तर्-धा].<BR>—अन्तर्-दशा, f. a technical term<BR>in astrology.<BR>—अन्तर्-दशाह, अम्, n. an interval of<BR>ten days; so अन्तर्-दशाहात्, before the end of ten<BR>days.<BR>—अन्तर्-दाव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing<BR>fire.<BR>—अन्तर्-दाह, अस्, m. internal heat, or fever.<BR>—अन्तर्-दुःख, अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted in mind, sad.<BR>—अन्तर्-दुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, internally bad, wicked,<BR>vile.<BR>—अन्तर्-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, looking into one's<BR>own soul.<BR>—अन्तर्-देश, अस्, m., Ved. an interme-<BR>diate region of the compass.<BR>—अन्तर्-द्वार, अम्, n.<BR>a private or secret door within the house.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>धा, &c.; see. s. v. अन्तर्-धा, p. 45.<BR>—अन्तर्-ध्यान,<BR>अम्, n. profound inward meditation.<BR>—अन्तर्-नगर,<BR>अम्, n. the palace of a king.<BR>—अन्तर्-निविष्ट, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, gone within, being within.<BR>—अन्तर्-निष्ठ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, engaged in internal reflection.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>भवन, अम्, n. the interior of a house.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>भाव, &c.; see अन्तर्-भू, p. 45.<BR>—अन्तर्-भावना,<BR>f. inward meditation or anxiety; a technical term in<BR>arithmetic; rectification of numbers by the differences<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-b" target="_blank">Page0044-b+ 80</a>]<BR>of the products.<BR>—अन्तर्-भूमि, इस्, f. the inner<BR>part of the earth.<BR>—अन्तर्-भौम, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>in the interior of the earth; subterranean.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, sad, perplexed.<BR>—अन्तर्-मुख,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, going into the mouth; (अम्), n. a kind<BR>of scissors used in surgery.<BR>—अन्तर्-मुद्र (?), sealed<BR>inside; N. of a certain form of devotion.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, still-born.<BR>—अन्तर्-याम, अस्, m.<BR>the suppression of the breath and voice; a Soma liba-<BR>tion during this act.<BR>—अन्तर्-याम-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>the Soma libation Antar-yāma; the performing of<BR>such a libation.<BR>—अन्तर्-यामिन्, ई, m. checking or<BR>regulating the internal feelings; the soul; providence;<BR>the supreme spirit as regulating and guiding mankind;<BR>Brahmā.<BR>—अन्तर्-योग, अस्, m. deep thought, ab-<BR>straction.<BR>—अन्तर्-लम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, acute-angular;<BR>(अस्), m. a triangle in which the perpendicular falls<BR>within, an acute-angled triangle.<BR>—अन्तर्-लीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, inherent.<BR>—अन्तर्-लोम, अस्, आ, अम्, covered<BR>with hair on the inner side.<BR>—अन्तर्-वंश, अस्, m.<BR>the gynæceum; see अन्तः-पुर.<BR>—अन्तर्-वंशिक,<BR>अस्, m. superintendent of the women's apartments.<BR>—अन्तर्-वण, अस्, आ, अम्, situated in a forest;<BR>(अम्), ind. within a forest.<BR>—अन्तर्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>being in the interior.<BR>—अन्तर्-वती, Ved. or अन्तर्-<BR>वत्नी, f. a pregnant woman.<BR>—अन्तर्-वमि, इस्, m.<BR>flatulence, indigestion.<BR>—अन्तर्-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or<BR>अन्तर्-वसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, internal, included, dwelling<BR>in.<BR>—अन्तर्-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a Soma sacrifice.<BR>—अन्तर्-वस्त्र, अम्, n. an under garment.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>वाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, skilled in sacred sciences.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>वावत्, आन्, अन्ती, or अती, अत्, Ved. abounding inter-<BR>nally with precious things, hidden; (वत्), ind. in-<BR>wardly.<BR>—अन्तर्-वाष्प, अस्, m. suppressed tears;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), containing tears.<BR>—अन्तर्-वासस्, अस्, n.<BR>an inner or under garment.<BR>—अन्तर्-विगाहन, अम्,<BR>n. entering within.<BR>—अन्तर्-विद्वस्, वान्, उषी,<BR>वस्, Ved. knowing (the paths) between (earth and<BR>heaven); knowing exactly.<BR>—अन्तर्-वेग, अस्, m. in-<BR>ternal uneasiness or anxiety; inward fever.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>वेदि, इस्, इस्, इ, belonging to the inside of the sacri-<BR>ficial ground; (इ), ind. within this ground; (इस् or ई),<BR>f. the Doab or district between the Gaṅgā and Ya-<BR>munā rivers.<BR>—अन्तर्-वेश्मन्, अ, n. the inner apart-<BR>ments, the interior of a building.<BR>—अन्तर्-वेश्मिक,<BR>अस्, m. superintendent of the women's apartments.<BR>—अन्तर्-हणन, अम्, n. striking in the middle.<BR>—अन्तर्-हनन, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>हस्तम्, ind. in the hand, within reach of the hand.<BR>—अन्तर्-हस्तीन, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the hand or<BR>within reach.<BR>—अन्तर्-हास, अस्, m. laughing inwardly;<BR>suppressed laughter; (अम्), ind. with suppressed laugh.<BR>—अन्तर्-हित, see अन्तर्-धा, p. 45.<BR>—अन्तर्-हृ-<BR>दय, अम्, n. the interior of the heart.<BR>—अन्तस्-तप्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, internally heated or harassed.<BR>—अन्तस्-<BR>ताप, अस्, m. inward heat; (अस्, आ, अम्), burning<BR>inwardly, burning with passion.<BR>—अन्तर्-तुषार, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having dew in the interior.<BR>—अन्तस्-तोय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, containing water.<BR>—अन्तस्-पथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. going within the clefts or hollows (of moun-<BR>tains), being on the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तस्त्य
अन्तस्त्य, अम्, n. intestines, bowels, entrails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर|अंतर|अन्तरं
अन्तर अन्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the in-<BR>terior, interior; near, proximate, related, intimate;<BR>lying adjacent to; distant; different from; exterior;<BR>(अम्), n. the interior; a hole, opening; the interior<BR>part of a thing, the contents; soul, heart, supreme<BR>soul; interval, intermediate space or time; period;<BR>term; opportunity, occasion; distance, absence; dif-<BR>ference, remainder; property, peculiarity; weakness,<BR>weak side; representation; surety, guaranty; respect,<BR>regard; (at the end of compounds) different, other,<BR>another, e. g. देशान्तरम्, another country [cf.<BR>Goth. anthar, Theme anthara; Lith. antra-s,<BR>‘the second;’ Lat. alter]. अन्तरम् or अन्तर-तस्,<BR>ind. in the interior, within.<BR>—अन्तर-चक्र, अम्, n.<BR>a technical term in augury.<BR>—अन्तर-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing the interior, prudent, provident, foreseeing.<BR>—अन्तर-तत्, त्, त्, त् (rt. तन्), spreading death or<BR>destruction.<BR>—अन्तर-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, nearest;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 78</a>]<BR>immediate, intimate, internal; like, analogous; (अस्),<BR>m. a congenial letter, one of the same class.<BR>—अन्तर-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम्, nearer, more intimate.<BR>—अन्तर-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दा for दो), cutting or hurting the<BR>interior or heart.<BR>—अन्तर-दिशा, f. or अन्तरा-दिश्,<BR>क्, f. or अन्तर्-देश, अस्, m. an intermediate region or<BR>quarter of the compass.<BR>—अन्तर-पूरुष, अस्, m.<BR>the internal man, the soul.<BR>—अन्तर-प्रभव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of mixed origin or caste.<BR>—अन्तर-प्रश्न,<BR>अस्, m. an inner question; a question which is contained<BR>in and arises from what has been previously stated.<BR>—अन्तर-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्तर-स्थायिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, or अन्तर-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, interposed, in-<BR>ternal, situated inside, inward; separate, apart.<BR>—अन्-<BR>तरापत्या (˚र-अप्˚), f. a pregnant woman.<BR>—अन्त-<BR>राभर, अस्, m., Ved. (if fr. अन्तर and आभर)<BR>taking away intervals; (if fr. अन्तरा and भर)<BR>bringing into the midst or near; procuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरा|अंतरा
अन्तरा, ind. in the middle, in the interior, inside,<BR>within, among, between; on the way, by the way;<BR>in the neighbourhood, near, nearly, almost; in the<BR>meantime, now and then; for some time; (with<BR>acc. and loc.) between, during, without.<BR>—अन्तरांस,<BR>see under अन्तर्.<BR>—अन्तरा-भव-देह, अस्, m. or<BR>अन्तरा-भव-सत्त्व, अम्, n. the soul in its middle<BR>existence between death and regeneration.<BR>—अन्तरा-<BR>वेदि, इस् or ई, f. a veranda resting on columns.<BR>—अन्तरा-शृङ्गम्, ind. between the horns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीय|अंतरीयं|अन्तरीयं
अन्तरीय, अम्, n. an under or lower garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरे|अंतरे
अन्तरे, ind. amidst, among, between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरेण|अंतरेण
अन्तरेण, ind. amidst, between; (with acc.) within,<BR>between, amidst, during; except, without, with re-<BR>gard to, with reference to, on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्य|अंतर्य|अन्तर्य्य
अन्तर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरञ्ज्
अन्तरञ्ज् अन्तर्-अञ्ज्, cl. 7. P., Ved. -अनक्ति,<BR>अङ्क्तुम्, -अञ्जितुम्, to assume, take upon one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरय|अंतरयः|अन्तरयः
अन्तरय, अन्तराय, &c. See अन्तर्-इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराल|अंतरालं|अन्तरालं
अन्तराल अन्तर्-आल. See under अन्तर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरि|अंतरि
अन्तरि अन्तर्-इ, cl. 1. P. -अयति, -एतुम्, to<BR>come between; cl. 2. P. -एति, -तुम्, to stand in any<BR>one's way, to separate; to exclude from (with abl.);<BR>to pass over, omit; to disappear: Ved., Intens. or Pass.<BR>-ईयते, to walk to and fro between (as a mediator).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरय|अंतरयः|अन्तरयः
अन्तर्-अय, अस्, m. impediment, hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरयण
अन्तर्-अयण, अम्, n. going under, disappearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराय|अंतरायः|अन्तरायः
अन्तर्-आय, अस्, आ, अम्, going between; (अस्), m.<BR>intervention, obstacle, impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरित|अंतरित|अन्तरितं
अन्तर्-इत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone within, interior,<BR>hidden, concealed, screened, shielded; departed, re-<BR>tired, withdrawn, disappeared, vanished, perished, dead;<BR>separated, detached; impeded, hindered; (अम्), n. (?)<BR>remainder (in arithmetic); a technical term in archi-<BR>tecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्ष|अंतरिक्षं|अन्तरिक्षं
अन्तरिक्ष अन्तरिक्ष or अन्तरीक्ष, अम्, n.<BR>(either fr. अन्तर्, ‘within,’ and ईक्ष्, ‘to see,’ or fr.<BR>अन्तरि, loc., and क्ष, ‘dwelling within bodies;’<BR>क्ष being fr. rt. क्षि), the intermediate space be-<BR>tween heaven and earth; (in the Veda) the middle<BR>of the three spheres or regions of life; the atmo-<BR>sphere or sky; the air; talc.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-क्षित्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, dwelling in the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-ग or<BR>अन्तरिक्ष-चर, अस्, m. a bird.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-प्रा,<BR>आस्, आस्, m. f., Ved. filling the sky, irradiating the<BR>firmament; travelling through the atmosphere (?).<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-प्रुत्, त्, त्, त् (rt. प्रु for प्लु), Ved.<BR>floating over the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-लोक,<BR>अस्, m. the intermediate region or sky as a peculiar<BR>world.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-संशित, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened<BR>in the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>dwelling in the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तरिक्ष-सद्य,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. residence in the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>इक्षोदर (˚क्ष-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an in-<BR>terior as comprehensive as the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तर्-<BR>ईक्ष-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going in the atmosphere; (अस्),<BR>m. a bird.<BR>—अन्तरीक्ष-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, moving<BR>through the atmosphere.<BR>—अन्तरीक्ष-जल or अन्-<BR>तरिक्ष-जल, अम्, n. the water of the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्ष्य
अन्तरिक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, atmospheric, aërial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरुपाती
अन्तरुपाती अन्तर्-उपाती (-उप-अति-इ), cl. 2.<BR>P. -उपात्येति, -तुम्, to enter over a threshold or<BR>boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गम्|अंतर्गम्
अन्तर्गम् अन्तर्-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to go between (so as to exclude from, with<BR>abl.); to disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गत|अंतर्गत|अन्तर्गतं
अन्तर्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्तर्-गामिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, gone between or into, being in, included in; being<BR>in the interior, internal, hidden, secret; disappeared,<BR>perished; slipped out of the memory, forgotten.<BR>—अन्तर्गत-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, whose mind is<BR>turned inwards, engaged in deep thought, sad, per-<BR>plexed.<BR>—अन्तर्गतोपमा (˚त-उप्˚), f. a concealed<BR>simile (the particle of comparison being omitted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गा
अन्तर्गा अन्तर्-गा, cl. 3. P. -जिगाति, -गातुम्,<BR>to go between, separate (so as to exclude from; with<BR>abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दृश्
अन्तर्दृश् अन्तर्-दृश्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -पश्यति,<BR>-द्रष्टुम्, to look between or into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धा|अंतर्धा
अन्तर्धा 1. अन्तर्-धा, cl. 3. A. -धत्ते,<BR>-धातुम्, to place within, deposit; to receive within;<BR>to hide, conceal, obscure; to hide one's self: Pass.<BR>-धीयते, to be received within, to be absorbed; to<BR>be rendered invisible; to disappear, vanish; to cease:<BR>Caus. -धापयति, -यितुम्, to render invisible, to<BR>cause to disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धा|अंतर्धा
2. अन्तर्-धा, f. concealment, covering, disappearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धान|अन्तर्द्धानं|अंतर्धानं
अन्तर्-धान, अम्, n. disappearance, invisibility;<BR>अन्तर्धानम् इ or गम्, to disappear; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Pṛthu.<BR>—अन्तर्धान-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, disappeared.<BR>—अन्तर्धान-चर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>going invisibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धापित
अन्तर्-धापित, अस्, आ, अम्, rendered invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धायक|अंतर्धायक
अन्तर्-धायक, अस्, इका, अम्, rendering invisible,<BR>concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्धि|अन्तर्द्धिः|अंतर्धिः|अन्तर्धिः
अन्तर्-धि, इस्, m. concealment, covering, disap-<BR>pearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हित|अंतर्हित|अन्तर्हितं
अन्तर्-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed between, separated;<BR>covered, concealed, hidden, made invisible, vanished,<BR>invisible; hidden from (with abl.).<BR>—अन्तर्-हितात्-<BR>मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. epithet of Śiva (‘of con-<BR>cealed mind’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भू|अंतर्भू
अन्तर्भू अन्तर्-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्,<BR>to be (contained or inherent or implied) in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भव|अंतर्भव
अन्तर्-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, being within, inward,<BR>internal, generated internally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भवन
अन्तर्-भवन, अन्तर्-भावना, See s. v. अन्तर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भाव|अंतर्भावः|अन्तर्भावः
अन्तर्-भाव, अस्, m. the being included by, in-<BR>ternal or inherent nature or disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावित
अन्तर्-भावित, अस्, आ, अम्, included, involved, im-<BR>plied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भूत|अंतर्भूत|अन्तर्भूतः
अन्तर्-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being within, internal,<BR>inner.<BR>—अन्तर्भूत-त्व, अम्, n.; see अन्तर्-<BR>भाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भूमि|अन्तर्भूमिः
अन्तर्-भूमि. See under अन्तर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तश्चर्
अन्तश्चर् अन्तश्-चर् (अन्तर्-चर्), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-चरति, -ते, -रितुम्, Ved. -रध्यै to move be-<BR>tween, to move within.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तश्छिद्
अन्तश्छिद् अन्तश्-छिद् (अन्तर्-छिद्), cl. 7. P.<BR>-छिनत्ति, -छेत्तुम्, to cut off, to intercept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तस्
अन्तस् अन्तस् See अन्तर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ति|अंति|अन्तिः
अन्ति 1. अन्ति, ind. before, in the presence<BR>of, near; (with gen.) within the proximity of, to<BR>[cf. Lat. ante, Gr. ἀντί].<BR>—अन्ति-गृह, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>a house near one's own dwelling; a place before the<BR>house, the neighbourhood of the house.<BR>—अन्ति-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very near.<BR>—अन्ति-तस्, ind., Ved. from near.<BR>—अन्ति-देव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the presence<BR>of the gods, near the gods; playing against another,<BR>an adversary (at dice).<BR>—अन्ति-मित्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. near or at hand with friendship.<BR>—अन्ति-वाम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. near with wealth or loveliness.<BR>—अन्ति-षद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sitting near.<BR>—अन्ति-<BR>षुम्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. near with happiness or<BR>kindness.<BR>—अन्त्य्-ऊति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. near with help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
1. अन्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (with gen. or abl.) near, prox-<BR>imate; compar. नेदीयस्, superl. नेदिष्ठ; (अम्), n.<BR>vicinity, proximity, near, e. g. अन्तिक-स्थ, remaining<BR>near; (अम्), ind. (with abl., gen., or as last member<BR>of a compound) until, near to, into the presence of;<BR>(आत्), ind. from the proximity; near, close by; within<BR>the presence of; (ए), ind. (with gen. or as last mem-<BR>ber of a compound) near, close by, in the proximity<BR>or presence of; (एन), ind. (with gen.) near.<BR>—अन्तिक-गति, इस्, f. going near.<BR>—अन्तिक-ता, f.<BR>nearness, vicinity, contiguity.<BR>—अन्तिकाश्रय (˚क-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m. contiguous support (as that given by a<BR>tree to a creeper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिम|अंतिम|अन्तिमः
1. अन्तिम, अस्, आ, अम्, immediately following (in<BR>this sense a the last member of a compound, e. g.<BR>दशान्तिम, ‘the eleventh’); very near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिय
अन्तिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. near; (अम्), n. a proxi-<BR>mate place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ति|अंति|अन्तिः
अन्ति 2. अन्ति, इस्, f. an elder sister (in<BR>theatrical language). For 1. अन्ति, see last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिका|अंतिका
अन्तिका, f. an elder sister (in theatrical language;<BR>perhaps a corruption of अत्तिका); a fire-place; a plant,<BR>Echites Scholaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ती|अंती
अन्ती, f. an oven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अन्तिक 2. अन्तिक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अन्त),<BR>reaching to the end of, reaching to (e. g. नासान्तिक,<BR>reaching to the nose), lasting till, until.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिम|अंतिम|अन्तिमः
2. अन्तिम, अस्, आ, अम्, final, ultimate, last.<BR>—अन्ति-<BR>माङ्क (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, m. the last unit, nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्य|अंत्य|अन्त्यं|अन्त्यः
अन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, last in place, in time, or in<BR>order; immediately following (used as the last mem-<BR>ber of a compound, e. g. अष्टमान्त्य, ‘the ninth’);<BR>lowest in place or condition, undermost, inferior, be-<BR>longing to the lowest caste; (अस्), m., N. of the plant<BR>Cyperus Hexastachyus Communis; (अम्), n. the num-<BR>ber 1000 billions; the twelfth sign of the zodiac;<BR>the last member of a mathematical series.<BR>—अन्त्य-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. or अन्त्य-क्रिया, f. funeral rites.<BR>—अन्त्य-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, younger, latest born; of the<BR>lowest caste; (अस्), m. a Śūdra; a man of one of<BR>seven inferior tribes; a washerman, currier, mimic,<BR>Varuḍa, fisherman, Meda or attendant on women, and<BR>mountaineer or forester.<BR>—अन्त्यज-गमन, अम्,<BR>n. intercourse (between a woman of the higher caste)<BR>with a man of the lowest caste.<BR>—अन्त्य-जन्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, or अन्त्य-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, or अन्त्य-जातीय अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of the lowest caste.<BR>—अन्त्यजा-गमन,<BR>अम्, n. intercourse (between a man of the higher<BR>caste) with a woman of the lowest caste.<BR>—अन्त्य-<BR>धन, अम्, n. last member of an arithmetical series.<BR>—अन्त्य-पद or अन्त्य-मूल, अम्, n. (in arithm.)<BR>the last or greatest root (in the square).<BR>—अन्त्य-भ,<BR>अम्, n. the last Nakṣatra (Revatī); the last sign of<BR>the zodiac, the sign Pisces.<BR>—अन्त्य-युग, अस्, m.<BR>the last or Kali age.<BR>—अन्त्य-योनि, इस्, f. the lowest<BR>source; (इस्, इस्, इ), of the lowest origin.<BR>—अन्त्य-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, आ, m. f. a man or woman of the last<BR>tribe, a Śūdra.<BR>—अन्त्य-विपुला, f., N. of a metre.<BR>—अन्त्यावसायिन् (˚य-अव्˚), ई, इनी, m. f. a man or<BR>woman of low caste, the son of a Cāṇḍāla by a Ni-<BR>ṣādī, especially one of the following classes: Cāṇ-<BR>ḍāla, Śvapaca or executioner, Kṣattṛ, Sūta, Vaide-<BR>haka, Māgadha or bard, and Āyogava.<BR>—अन्त्याहुति<BR>(˚य-आह्˚), इस्, f. funeral oblation or sacrifice.<BR>—अन्-<BR>त्येष्टि (˚य-इष्˚), इस्, f. funeral sacrifice.<BR>—अन्त्य्-<BR>एष्टि-क्रिया, f. funeral ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यक|अंत्यकः|अन्त्यकः
अन्त्यक, अस्, m. a man of the lowest tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्र|अंत्रं|अन्त्रं
अन्त्र अन्त्र, अम्, n. (contraction of अन्तर;<BR>or fr. rt. अम्?: Gr. ἔντερον), entrail, intestine; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a plant, either Convolvolus Argenteus or<BR>Ipomœa Pes Capræ Roth (?).<BR>—अन्तर-कूज, अस्, m.<BR>or अन्त्र-कूजन, अम्, n. or अन्त्र-विकूजन, अम्,<BR>n. rumbling of the bowels.<BR>—अन्त्रन्-धमि, इस्, f.<BR>indigestion, inflation of the bowels from wind.<BR>—अन्-<BR>त्र-पाचक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, Æschynomene<BR>Grandiflora.<BR>—अन्त्र-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>entrails.<BR>—अन्त्र-वृद्धि, इस्, f. inguinal hernia,<BR>rupture.<BR>—अन्त्र-शिला, f., N. of a river.<BR>—अन्त्र-<BR>स्रज्, क्, f. a kind of garland worn by Nara-siṃha.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">Page0045-c+ 76</a>]<BR>—अन्त्राद (˚र-आद्˚), अस्, m. worms in the intes-<BR>tines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्द्|अंद्
अन्द् अन्द्, cl. 1. P. अन्दति, -दितुम्, to<BR>bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्द|अंदः|अन्दः
अन्द, अस्, m. binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दु|अंदुः|अन्दुः
अन्दु, उस्, f. or अन्दू, ऊस्, f. or अन्दुक or अन्-<BR>दूक, अस्, m. the chain for an elephant's feet; a ring<BR>or chain worn on the ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दिका|अंदिका
अन्दिका अन्दिका, f. (for अन्तिका, q. v.), fire-<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलय
अन्दोलय अन्दोलय, nom. P. अन्दोलयति,<BR>यितुम्, to agitate, to swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलन|अंदोलनं
अन्दोलन, अम्, n. swinging, oscillating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोलित
अन्दोलित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, swung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्द्रक
अन्द्रक अन्द्रक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्|अंध्
अन्ध् अन्ध्, cl. 10. P. अन्धयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to be or become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, blind; making blind, prevent-<BR>ing the sight, dark; (अम्), n. darkness; turbid<BR>water, water; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—अन्ध-<BR>कार, अस्, अम्, m. n. darkness.<BR>—अन्धकार-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, dark.<BR>—अन्धकार-सञ्चय, अस्, m.<BR>intensity of darkness.<BR>—अन्ध-कारित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>made dark, dark.<BR>—अन्ध-कूप, अस्, m. a well of<BR>which the mouth is hidden; a well over-grown with<BR>plants, &c.; a particular hell.<BR>—अन्धङ्-करण, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, making blind.<BR>—अन्ध-तमस or अन्ध-<BR>तामस or अन्धा-तमस, अम्, n. great darkness.<BR>—अन्ध-ता, f. or अन्ध-त्व, अम्, n. blindness.<BR>—अन्ध-तामिस्र, अस्, m. complete darkness of<BR>the soul; (अम्), n. a division of Tartarus, the second<BR>or eighteenth of the twenty-one hells; doctrine of<BR>annihilation after death.<BR>—अन्ध-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ,<BR>mentally blind.<BR>—अन्ध-पूतना, f. a female demon<BR>causing diseases in children.<BR>—अन्ध-मूषा, f.<BR>a small covered crucible with a hole in the side.<BR>—अन्ध-मूषिका, f., N. of a grass, Lepeocercis<BR>Serrata.<BR>—अन्धम्-भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्ध-<BR>भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, becoming blind.<BR>—अन्ध-<BR>रात्री, f., Ved. dark night.<BR>—अन्धालजी (˚ध-अल्˚),<BR>f. a blind boil, one that does not suppurate.<BR>—अन्-<BR>धाहि (˚ध-अहि), इस्, or अन्धाहिक, अस्, m. a blind<BR>snake, not poisonous; (इस्, इस्), m. f., N. of a fish,<BR>commonly called kucikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धक|अंधक|अन्धकः
अन्धक, अस्, आ, अम्, blind; (अस्), m., N. of an<BR>Asura, a son of Kaśyapa and Diti; N. of a descen-<BR>dant of Yadu and ancestor of Kṛṣṇa and his descen-<BR>dants; N. of a Muni.<BR>—अन्धक-घातिन्, ई, m. or<BR>अन्धक-रिपु, उस्, m. or अन्धकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. or अन्धकासुह्रिद् (˚क-अस्˚), m. epithet of Śiva,<BR>the slayer or enemy of the Asura Andhaka.<BR>—अन्ध-<BR>क-वर्त, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—अन्धक-<BR>वृष्णि, अयस्, pl. m. descendants of Andhaka and<BR>Vṛṣṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धस्|अंधस्
1. अन्धस्, अस्, n., Ved. darkness, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धिका|अंधिका
अन्धिका, f. night; a kind of game, blindman's<BR>buff; a woman of a particular character; one of the<BR>classes of women; a disease of the eye; another dis-<BR>ease; see सर्षपी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीकृ|अंधीकृ
अन्धी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>blind, to blind.<BR>—अन्धी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made or<BR>become blind.<BR>—अन्धीकृतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, blinded in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीगु
अन्धी-गु, उस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीभू|अंधीभू
अन्धी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्, to become<BR>blind.<BR>—अन्धी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धस्|अंधस्
अन्धस् 2. अन्ध, अस्, n. (fr. rt. अद्, to eat?;<BR>Gr. ἄνθος), food, Soma, ghee, boiled rice; herb in<BR>general herb of the Soma plant, Soma juice, juice;<BR>grassy ground. (For 1. अन्धस्, see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धु|अंधुः|अन्धुः
अन्धु अन्धु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. अम् or अन्ध्?),<BR>a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धुल|अंधुलः|अन्धुलः
अन्धुल अन्धुल, अस्, m., N. of a tree,<BR>Acacia Sirissa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्र|अंध्र|अंध्रः|अन्ध्रः
अन्ध्र अन्ध्र, अस्, m., N. of a people, pro-<BR>bably modern Telingana; N. of a dynasty; a man of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-a" target="_blank">Page0046-a+ 80</a>]<BR>a low caste, the offspring of a Vaideha father and<BR>Kārāvara mother, who lives by killing game.<BR>—अन्-<BR>ध्र-जाति, इस्, f. the Andhra tribe.<BR>—अन्ध्र-जातीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to this tribe.<BR>—अन्ध्र-<BR>भृत्य, आस्, m. pl. a dynasty of the Andhras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्न|अन्नं|अन्नः
अन्न 1. अन्न, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अत् or अम्?),<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्न|अन्नं|अन्नः
अन्न 2. अन्न, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अद्), eaten;<BR>(अम्), n. food or victual in general; food in a mys-<BR>tical sense, or the lowest form in which the supreme<BR>soul is manifested, the coarsest envelope of the su-<BR>preme spirit; boiled rice; bread corn; Ved. water;<BR>Viṣṇu; earth.<BR>—अन्न-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous<BR>of food.<BR>—अन्न-काल, अस्, m. meal-time, proper hour<BR>for eating.<BR>—अन्न-कोष्ठक, अस्, m. cupboard,<BR>granary; Viṣṇu; the sun.<BR>—अन्न-गति, इस्, f.<BR>the œsophagus, gullet.<BR>—अन्न-गन्धि, इस्, m. dy-<BR>sentery, diarrhœa.<BR>—अन्न-ज or अन्न-जात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, springing from or occasioned by food as the<BR>primitive substance.<BR>—अन्न-जल, अम्, n. food and<BR>water, bare subsistence.<BR>—अन्न-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. ob-<BR>taining food by conquest.<BR>—अन्न-जीवन, अस्, ई (?),<BR>अम्, living by food.<BR>—अन्न-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>having the vigour of food.<BR>—अन्न-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or अन्न-दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or अन्न-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>or अन्न-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, giving food; epithet of<BR>Śiva and Durgā.<BR>—अन्न-दान, अम्, n. the giving<BR>of food.<BR>—अन्न-देवता, f. the divinity supposed to<BR>preside over articles of food.<BR>—अन्न-दोष, अस्, m.<BR>a fault committed by eating prohibited food.<BR>—अन्न-<BR>द्वेष, अस्, m. want of appetite, dislike of food.<BR>—अन्न-पति, इस्, m. possessor of food, an epithet of<BR>Savitṛ, Agni, Śiva.<BR>—अन्न-पू, ऊस्, m., Ved. puri-<BR>fying food, epithet of the sun.<BR>—अन्न-पूर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, filled with or possessed of food; (आ), f. a goddess,<BR>a form of Durgā.<BR>—अन्न-पूर्वा (?), f., N. of Durgā.<BR>—अन्न-पेय, अम्, n., Ved. another name for the<BR>Vāja-peya sacrifice.<BR>—अन्न-प्रलय, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>ing resolved into food or the primitive substance after<BR>death.<BR>—अन्न-प्राश, अस्, m. or अन्न-प्राशन,<BR>अम्, n. putting rice into a child's mouth for the first<BR>time, after oblations to fire, a ceremony performed<BR>between the fifth and eighth month: it is one of the<BR>sixteen Saṃskāras mentioned in the second book of<BR>Manu.<BR>—अन्न-बुभुक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of<BR>eating food.<BR>—अन्न-ब्रह्मन्, अ, n. or अन्नात्मन्<BR>(˚न-आत्˚), आ, m. Brahma as represented by food.<BR>—अन्न-भक्ष, अस्, m. or अन्न-भक्षण, अम्,<BR>n. or अन्न-भुक्ति, इस्, f. eating of food.<BR>—अन्न-<BR>भाग, अस्, m., Ved. a share of food.<BR>—अन्न-भुज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, eating food; (क्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—अन्न-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made from food, com-<BR>posed of food or of boiled rice; (अम्), n. plenty of<BR>food.<BR>—अन्नमय-कोश or अन्नमय-कोष, अस्,<BR>m. the gross material body, that which is sustained by<BR>food (the sthūla-śarīra).<BR>—अन्न-मल, अम्, n. ex-<BR>crement; spirituous liquor.<BR>—अन्न-रक्षा, f. caution<BR>in eating food.<BR>—अन्न-रस, अस्, m. essence of food,<BR>chyle; meat and drink, nutriment, taste in distin-<BR>guishing food.<BR>—अन्न-लिप्सा, f. desire for food, ap-<BR>petite.<BR>—अन्न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of food.<BR>—अन्न-वस्त्र, अम्, n. food and clothing, the ne-<BR>cessaries of life.<BR>—अन्न-वाहि-स्रोतस्, अस्, n. the<BR>œsophagus, gullet.<BR>—अन्न-विकार, अस्, m. transform-<BR>ation of food; disorder of the stomach from indiges-<BR>tion; the seminal secretion.<BR>—अन्न-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>knowing food; possessed of food.<BR>—अन्न-शेष, अस्,<BR>m. leavings, offal.<BR>—अन्न-संस्कार, अस्, m. conse-<BR>crating of food.<BR>—अन्न-हर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, taking<BR>away food.<BR>—अन्न-होम, अस्, m. a sacrifice con-<BR>nected with the Aśva-medha.<BR>—अन्नाकाल, see<BR>अनाकाल.<BR>—अन्नाच्छादन (˚न-आच्छ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>food and clothing.<BR>—अन्नात्तृ (˚न-अत्˚), ता, m. or<BR>अन्नादिन् (˚न-आद्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating food.<BR>—अन्ना-<BR>द (˚न-अद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, eating food; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अन्नादन (˚न-अद्˚), अम्, n. eating<BR>of food.<BR>—अन्नाद्य (˚न-अद्˚), अम्, n. food in<BR>general, proper food.<BR>—अन्नाद्य-काम, अस्, m. de-<BR>sirous of food.<BR>—अन्नायु, or अन्नायुस् (˚न-आय्˚), उस्,<BR>m. living by food, desirous of food.<BR>—अन्नार्थिन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-b" target="_blank">Page0046-b+ 80</a>]<BR>(˚न-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, asking for food.<BR>—अन्ना-<BR>वृध् (final अ lengthened), त्, त्, त्, Ved. increasing<BR>food.<BR>—अन्नाहारिन् (˚न-आह्˚), ई, इणी, इ, eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नम्भट्ट|अन्नंभट्ट|अन्नंभट्टः
अन्नम्भट्ट अन्नम्भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Tarka-saṅgraha, or compendium of the<BR>Nyāya philosophy, especially the Vaiśeṣika branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्य|अन्यः
अन्य अन्य, अस्, आ, अत् (according to native<BR>authorities fr. rt. अन्, but more probably from a pronom.<BR>base अ or अन्), other, different; (with abl. or as the<BR>last member of a compound) other than, different<BR>from opposed to; another; another person; one of<BR>a number; अन्य अन्य or एक अन्य, the one, the<BR>other [cf. Zend anya; Armen. ail; Lat. alius; Goth.<BR>aljis, Them. alja; Gr. ἄλλος for ἄλ-ϳος cf. also<BR>ἔνιοι].<BR>—अन्य-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, loving another.<BR>—अन्य-कारुका, f. a worm bred in excrement.<BR>—अन्य-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्य-कारित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, done by another.<BR>—अन्य-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. an-<BR>other territory or sphere.<BR>—अन्य-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>अन्य-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going to another, adulterous.<BR>—अन्य-गोत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, of a different family.<BR>—अन्य-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, whose mind is fixed on<BR>some one or something else.<BR>—अन्य-चोदित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, moved by another.<BR>—अन्यच्-च (˚यद्-च), ind.<BR>and another, besides, moreover, on the contrary.<BR>—अन्य-ज or अन्य-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born of another<BR>(family, &c.), of a different origin.<BR>—अन्य-जन्मन्,<BR>अ, n. another birth, being born again, metempsy-<BR>chosis.<BR>—अन्य-ता, f. difference.<BR>—अन्यत्-काम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, desirous of something else.<BR>—अन्यत्-कृ, to<BR>make a mistake in reading, &c.<BR>—अन्यद्-अर्थ<BR>or अन्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having another<BR>meaning, purpose, sense.<BR>—अन्य-दुर्वह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, difficult to be borne by another.<BR>—अन्य-देवत<BR>or अन्य-देवत्य or अन्य-दैवत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having another divinity, i. e. addressed to another<BR>divinity.<BR>—अन्य-धर्म, अस्, m. different character-<BR>istic; characteristic of another; (अस्, आ, अम्,), having dif-<BR>ferent characteristics.<BR>—अन्य-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, one whose<BR>mind is alienated (from God).<BR>—अन्य-नाभि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, of another family.<BR>—अन्य-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>voted to something else, zealous in something else.<BR>—अन्य-पुष्ट or अन्य-भृत अस्, आ, m. f. the<BR>kokila or Indian cuckoo, supposed to be reared by<BR>the crow.<BR>—अन्य-पूर्वा, f. a woman previously pro-<BR>mised or betrothed to one and married to another.<BR>—अन्य-भृत्, त्, m. a crow (‘nourishing another;’<BR>the crow being supposed to sit upon the eggs of the<BR>kokila).<BR>—अन्य-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or अन्य-म-<BR>नस्क or अन्य-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose mind<BR>is fixed on something else, absent, fickle, versatile;<BR>having another mind in one's self, possessed by a<BR>demon.<BR>—अन्य-मातृ-ज, अस्, m. a half-brother, who<BR>has the same father but another mother.<BR>—अन्य-<BR>राजन्, आ, आ, अ, having another for king, subject to<BR>another.<BR>—अन्य-राष्ट्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, from another<BR>kingdom, belonging to another kingdom.<BR>—अन्य-<BR>रूप, अम्, n. another form; (एण), in another form,<BR>disguised; (अस्, आ, अम्), changed, altered.<BR>—अन्य-<BR>रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having another shape.<BR>—अन्य-<BR>लिङ्ग or अन्य-लिङ्गक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>gender of another (word, viz. of the substantive), an<BR>adjective.<BR>—अन्य-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, having another<BR>colour.<BR>—अन्य-वाप, अस्, m. the kokila or Indian<BR>cuckoo (‘sowing for others,’ i. e. leaving his eggs in<BR>the nests of other birds).<BR>—अन्य-वीज-ज or अन्य-<BR>वीज-समुद्भव or अन्य-वीजोत्पन्न (˚ज-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. (‘born from the seed of another’), an adopted<BR>son.<BR>—अन्य-व्रत, अस्, m., Ved. following other<BR>(than Vedic) observances; devoted to other (gods),<BR>infidel, unbelieving.<BR>—अन्य-शाखक, अस्, m. a<BR>Brāhman who has left his school; an apostate.<BR>—अन्य-सङ्गम, अस्, m. intercourse with another,<BR>adulterous intercourse.<BR>—अन्य-साधारण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, common to others.<BR>—अन्य-स्त्री-ग, अस्,<BR>m. going to another's wife, an adulterer.<BR>—अन्या-<BR>दृक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्य-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, or अन्य-<BR>दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, of another kind, like another.<BR>—अन्याधीन (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, subject to<BR>others, dependent.<BR>—अन्याश्रयण (˚य-आश्˚), अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">Page0046-c+ 81</a>]<BR>n. going to another (as an inheritance).<BR>—अन्या-<BR>श्रित (˚य-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, gone to another.<BR>—अन्यासक्त (˚य-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, intent on some-<BR>thing else.<BR>—अन्यासाधारण (˚य-अस्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>not common to another, peculiar.<BR>—अन्योढा (˚य-<BR>ऊढ्˚), f. married to another, another's wife.<BR>—अन्-<BR>योत्पन्न (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, begotten by another.<BR>—अन्योदर्य (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, born from<BR>another womb; (अस्), m. a step-mother's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यक
अन्यक, अस्, m. another, other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतम|अन्यतमः
अन्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, any one of many, either,<BR>any.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतर|अन्यतरः
अन्य-तर, अस्, आ, अत्, either of two, other, differ-<BR>ent; अन्यतर अन्यतर, the one, the other;<BR>अन्यतरस्याम्, loc. f. either way.<BR>—अन्यतर-<BR>तस्, ind. on one of two sides.<BR>—अन्यतरतो-दन्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having teeth on one side (only).<BR>—अन्य-<BR>तरे-द्युस्, ind. on either of two days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्
अन्य-तस्, ind. from another; from another mo-<BR>tive; on one side (अन्यतः अन्यतः, on the one,<BR>on the other side); elsewhere; on the other side, on<BR>the contrary, in one direction; towards some other<BR>place.<BR>—अन्यत-एत, एतस्, एनी, m. f., Ved. variegated<BR>on one side.<BR>—अन्यतः-क्ष्णुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sharp<BR>on one side.<BR>—अन्यतः-प्लक्षा, f., N. of a Lotus<BR>pond in Kurukṣetra.<BR>—अन्यतो-घातिन्, ई, m., Ved.<BR>striking in one direction.<BR>—अन्यतो-ऽरण्य (˚तस्-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n., Ved. a land which is woody here and there,<BR>or only on one side (?).<BR>—अन्यतो-वात, अस्, m. a<BR>certain disease of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्त्य|अन्यतस्त्यः
अन्यतस्त्य, अस्, m. opponent, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्य-त्र, ind. (equivalent to अन्यस्मिन्, loc.<BR>of अन्य), elsewhere, in another place (with abl.);<BR>on another occasion; (as last member of a comp.) at<BR>another time than; otherwise, in another manner;<BR>to another place; except, without [cf. Goth. aljathrô].<BR>—अन्यत्र-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, whose mind is di-<BR>rected to something else, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्य-था, ind. otherwise, in a different manner<BR>(with अतस्, इतस् or ततस् = in a manner different<BR>from this; अन्यथा अन्यथा, in one way, in another<BR>way); inaccurately, untruly, falsely, erroneously; from<BR>another motive; in the contrary case, otherwise [cf.<BR>Lat. aliuta].<BR>—अन्यथा-कार, अस्, m. doing other-<BR>wise, changing; (अम्), ind. otherwise, in a different<BR>manner.<BR>—अन्यथा-कृ, to act otherwise, alter, vio-<BR>late (a law), destroy (a hope), &c.<BR>—अन्यथा-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, changed.<BR>—अन्यथा-ख्याति, इस्, f. erro-<BR>neous conception of spirit; title of a philosophical<BR>work.<BR>—अन्यथा-त्व, अम्, n. an opposite state of the<BR>case, difference.<BR>—अन्यथा-भाव, अस्, m. alteration,<BR>difference.<BR>—अन्यथा-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, changed.<BR>—अन्यथा-वादिन् or अन्य-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speak-<BR>ing differently; (ई), m. speaking inconsistently; (in<BR>law) prevaricating or a prevaricator.<BR>—अन्यथा-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, altered, disturbed by strong emotion.<BR>—अन्यथा-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, wrongly defined,<BR>wrongly proved or established; effected otherwise, un-<BR>essential.<BR>—अन्यथासिद्ध-त्व, अम्, n. or अन्यथा-<BR>सिद्धि, इस्, f. wrong arguing, wrong demonstration;<BR>that demonstration in which arguments are referred<BR>to which are not the true causes.<BR>—अन्यथा-स्तोत्र,<BR>अम्, n. irony. — (From अन्यथा comes the nom. verb<BR>अन्यथय, P. अन्यथयति, -यितुम्, to alter.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्य-दा, ind. at another time; sometimes; one<BR>day, once; in another case [cf. Old Slav. inogda,<BR>inŭda].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदीय
अन्यदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यर्हि
अन्यर्हि, ind. at another time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्
अन्ये-द्युस्, ind. on the other day, on the following<BR>day; the other day, once.<BR>—अन्येद्युष्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, occurring every other day, daily, diurnal; (अस्),<BR>m. a quotidian fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य or अन्यो-ऽन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one another,<BR>mutual [this word is said to be fr. अन्यस्, nom. sing.<BR>m., and अन्य; cf. परस्पर. In most cases, ac-<BR>cordingly, it will be found that the first अन्य may be<BR>regarded as the subject of the sentence, while the<BR>latter assumes the acc., inst., gen., or loc. cases as re-<BR>quired by the verb; there are many instances, however,<BR>in which the first अन्य, originally a nominative, must<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">Page0047-a+ 73</a>]<BR>be regarded as equivalent to an oblique case]; अन्यो-<BR>न्यम् or अन्योन्य-तस्, ind. mutually.<BR>—अन्योन्य-<BR>कलह, अस्, m. mutual quarrel.<BR>—अन्योन्य-घात, अस्,<BR>m. mutual conflict, killing one another.<BR>—अन्योन्य-<BR>पक्ष-नयन, अम्, n. transposing (of numbers) from<BR>one side to another.<BR>—अन्योन्य-भेद, अस्, m. mutual<BR>division or enmity.<BR>—अन्योन्य-मिथुन, अम्, n. mu-<BR>tual union; (अस्), m. united mutually.<BR>—अन्योन्य-वि-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. mutual partition (of an inheritance).<BR>—अ-<BR>न्योन्य-वृत्ति, इस्, m. mutual effect of one upon another.<BR>—अन्योन्य-व्यतिकर, अस्, m. reciprocal action, re-<BR>lation or influence.<BR>—अन्योन्य-संश्रय, अस्, m.<BR>reciprocal relation (of cause and effect).<BR>—अन्योन्य-<BR>सापेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, mutually relating.<BR>—अन्योन्य-<BR>हाराभिहत (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (two quantities)<BR>mutually multiplied by their denominators.<BR>—अन्यो-<BR>न्यापहृत (˚य-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taken or secreted<BR>from one another, taken secretly.<BR>—अन्योन्याभाव<BR>(˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m. mutual non-existence, mutual<BR>negation, relative difference.<BR>—अन्योन्याश्रय (˚य-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m. mutual or reciprocal support, connec-<BR>tion or dependance; mutually depending.<BR>—अन्यो-<BR>न्याश्रित (˚य-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mutually supported<BR>or depending.<BR>—अन्योन्योक्ति (˚य-उक्˚), इस्, f. con-<BR>versation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यङ्ग|अन्यंग
अन्यङ्ग अ-न्यङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. spotless.<BR>—अ-न्यङ्ग-श्वेत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. white and<BR>without spot (as a sacrificial animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यच्च
अन्यच्च, अन्यतस्, अन्यथा, अन्यदा, अन्योन्य।<BR>See under अन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्या
अन्या अ-न्या, f., Ved. (न्या contracted fr.<BR>निया ?), not drying up (as the milk of a cow ?); or<BR>अन्या, f. of अन्य, other (the accent being altered ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अन्याय अ-न्याय, अस्, m. unjust or unlawful<BR>action; impropriety, indecorum; irregularity, disor-<BR>der.<BR>—अन्याय-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or अन्याय-वृत्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, acting unjustly; following evil courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिन्
अ-न्यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or अ-न्याय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unjust,<BR>improper, indecorous, unbecoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यून|अन्यूनः
अन्यून अ-न्यून, अस्, आ, अम्, not defective,<BR>entire, complete.<BR>—अ-न्यूनाधिक (˚न-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, not too little and not too much; neither de-<BR>ficient nor excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योकस्
अन्योकस् अ-न्य्-ओकस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, not remaining<BR>in one's own (ओकस्) habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्ष|अन्वक्षः
अन्वक्ष अन्व्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अक्ष,<BR>the eye, with अनु), following; (अम्), ind. afterwards;<BR>immediately after; directly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्षरसन्धि|अन्वक्षरसंधि|अन्वक्षरसंधिः|अन्वक्षरसन्धिः
अन्वक्षरसन्धि अन्व्-अक्षर-सन्धि, इस्, m.<BR>a kind of Sandhi in the Vedas, euphonic conjunction<BR>of a vowel and consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वङ्गम्
अन्वङ्गम् अन्व्-अङ्गम्, ind. after every<BR>member or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वञ्च्|अन्वंच्
अन्वञ्च् अन्वञ्च्, अङ्, ऊची, अक् (fr. rt. अञ्च् with<BR>अनु), following the direction of another, going after,<BR>following; lying lengthwise; अनूचि, loc. c. in the<BR>rear, behind; (अक्), ind. afterwards.<BR>—अन्वग्-भा-<BR>वम्, ind. afterwards; friendly disposed.<BR>—अन्वग्-<BR>भूय, ind. becoming friendly disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वती
अन्वती अन्व्-अती (अनु-अति-इ), cl. 2. P. -अत्येति,<BR>-तुम्, to follow in crossing or passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वध्यायम्
अन्वध्यायम् अन्व्-अध्यायम्, ind. according<BR>to the chapters (especially of the Veda), according to<BR>the sacred texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय अन्व्-अय, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. इ with<BR>अनु, see अन्व्-इ), following, succession; (अस्), m. con-<BR>nection, association, being linked to or concerned<BR>with; the natural order or connection of words in a<BR>sentence, syntax, construing; logical connection of<BR>words; logical connection of cause and effect, or pro-<BR>position and conclusion; drift, tenor, purport; de-<BR>scendants, race, lineage, family.<BR>—अन्वय-ज्ञ, अस्,<BR>m. a genealogist.<BR>—अन्वय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">Page0047-b+ 71</a>]<BR>a connection (as a consequence), following, agreeing<BR>with; belonging to race or family.<BR>—अन्वय-वत्,<BR>ind. in connection with, in the sight of.<BR>—अन्वय-<BR>व्यतिरेक, अम्, n. a positive and negative proposition;<BR>agreement and contrariety; species and difference;<BR>rule and exception; logical connection and discon-<BR>nection.<BR>—अन्वय-व्यतिरेकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, (in phil.)<BR>affirmative and negative.<BR>—अन्वय-व्याप्ति, इस्, f. an<BR>affirmative argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, connected (as a consequence).<BR>—अन्वयि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being a necessary<BR>consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्च्
अन्वर्च् अन्व्-अर्च् (अनु-अर्च्), cl. 1. P. -अर्चति,<BR>-चितुम्, to honour with shouts or songs of jubilee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्ज्
अन्वर्ज् अन्व्-अर्ज् (अनु-अर्ज्), cl. 1. P. -अर्जति,<BR>-जितुम्, to let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्तितृ
अन्वर्तितृ अन्व्-अर्तितृ, ता, m. (fr. अनु-अर्त्<BR>for अनु-अर्थ्), Ved. an inviter, one who allows to<BR>take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थ
अन्वर्थ अन्व्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>meaning obvious, intelligible, clear.<BR>—अन्वर्थ-ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. the literal acceptation of the meaning<BR>of a word (as opposed to the conventional).<BR>—अन्वर्-<BR>थ-सञ्ज्ञा, f. a term whose meaning is intelligible<BR>in itself (opposed to such technical terms as भ,<BR>घु, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वव्
अन्वव् अन्व्-अव् (अनु-अव्), cl. 1. P. -अवति,<BR>-वितुम्, to encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववकॄ
अन्ववकॄ अन्व्-अव-कॄ (अनु-अव˚), cl. 6. P.<BR>-किरति, -करितुम् or -रीतुम्, to scatter or strew<BR>about: Caus. P. -कीरयति, -यितुम्, to make one<BR>scatter about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववकिरण|अन्ववकिरणं
अन्व्-अवकिरण, अम्, n. scattering about succes-<BR>sively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववक्रम्
अन्ववक्रम् अन्व्-अव-क्रम् (अनु-अव˚), cl. 1.<BR>P. -क्रामति, -क्रमितुम्, to descend or enter in<BR>succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववगा
अन्ववगा अन्व्-अव-गा (अनु-अव˚), cl. 3. P.<BR>-जिगाति, -गातुम्, to go and join another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववचर्
अन्ववचर् अन्व्-अव-चर् (अनु-अव˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-चरति, -रितुम्, to insinuate one's self into, enter<BR>stealthily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववचार|अन्ववचारः
अन्व्-अवचार, अस्, m., Ved. descending and going<BR>after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववपा
अन्ववपा अन्व्-अव-पा, cl. 1. P. -पिबति,<BR>पातुम्, to drink after others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसर्ग|अन्ववसर्गः
अन्ववसर्ग अन्व्-अवसर्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सृज्<BR>with अनु and अव), letting down, slackening;<BR>friendly invitation; permission to do as one likes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसित
अन्ववसित अन्व्-अवसित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. सि<BR>with अनु and अव), fastened to, bound to, attached;<BR>see अनुवसित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववार्ज्
अन्ववार्ज् अन्व्-अवार्ज् (अनु-अव-अर्ज्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-अवार्जति, -जितुम्, to cause to go after or in a par-<BR>ticular direction; to visit with anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववे
अन्ववे अन्व्-अवे (अनु-अव-इ), cl. 2. P. -अवैति,<BR>-तुम्, to follow, walk up to or get into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववाय|अन्ववायः
अन्व्-अवाय, अस्, m. race, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववायन
अन्व्-अवायन, अम्, n., Ved. descending and going<BR>after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववेक्ष्
अन्ववेक्ष् अन्व्-अवेक्ष् (अनु-अव-ईक्ष्), cl. 1.<BR>A. -अवेक्षते, -क्षितुम्, to look at, inspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववेक्षा
अन्व्-अवेक्षा, f. regard, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वश्
अन्वश् अन्व्-अश् (अनु-अश्), cl. 5. P. A. -अश्नोति,<BR>-नुते, -अशितुम् or -अष्टुम्, to reach, come up to,<BR>equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका अन्व्-अष्टका, f. the ninth day in<BR>the latter half of the three months following the full<BR>moon in Āgrahāyaṇa, Pauṣa, Māgha, Phālguna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टक्य|अन्वष्टक्यं
अन्वष्टक्य, अम्, n. a Śrāddha or funeral cere-<BR>mony performed on the Anvaṣṭakās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वस्
अन्वस् अन्व्-अस्, (अनु-अस्), cl. 2. P., Ved. -अस्ति,<BR>to be at hand, to reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वस्त
अन्वस्त अन्व्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. अस्,<BR>अस्यति), shot along, shot; interwoven (as in silk),<BR>chequered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वह्
अन्वह् अन्व्-अह् (अनु-अह्), perf. -आह, to pro-<BR>nounce, especially a ceremonial formula (Gram. 384. b).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहम्
अन्वहम् अन्व्-अहम् (अनु-अहम्), ind. day<BR>after day, every day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाक्रम्
अन्वाक्रम् अन्व्-आ-क्रम् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. A.<BR>-क्रमते, -मितुम्, to ascend towards or to; P.<BR>-क्रामति, to visit in succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्या
अन्वाख्या अन्व्-आ-ख्या (अनु-आ˚), cl. 2. P.<BR>-ख्याति, -तुम्, to enumerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्यान|अन्वाख्यानं
अन्व्-आख्यान, अम्, n. enumeration; section;<BR>chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वागम्
अन्वागम् अन्व्-आ-गम् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-गच्छति, -गन्तुम्, to follow, come after: Desid.<BR>-जिगांसति, to wish or intend to follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वागा
अन्वागा अन्व्-आ-गा (अनु-आ˚), cl. 3. P., Ved.<BR>-जिगाति, -गातुम्, to follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचक्ष्
अन्वाचक्ष् अन्व्-आ-चक्ष् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 2. A.<BR>-चष्टे, Ved. Inf. -चक्षसे, to name after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचम्
अन्वाचम् अन्व्-आ-चम् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-चामति, -चमितुम्, to follow in rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचय|अन्वाचयः
अन्वाचय अन्व्-आचय, अस्, m. (rt. चि), laying<BR>down a rule of secondary importance after that which<BR>is प्रधान or primary; connecting of a secondary<BR>action with the main action (e. g. the conjunction च<BR>is sometimes used अन्वाचये.) — अन्वाचय-शिष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, propounded as a rule or matter of secon-<BR>dary importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचित
अन्व्-आचित, अस्, आ, अम्, secondary, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचर्
अन्वाचर् अन्व्-आ-चर् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-चरति, -रितुम्, to follow or imitate in doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाजे
अन्वाजे अन्वाजे (fr. अनु and अज्?), only used<BR>in connection with rt. कृ, e. g. अन्वाजे कृ, to sup-<BR>port, aid, assist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वातन्
अन्वातन् अन्व्-आ-तन् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 8. P.<BR>-तनोति, -नितुम्, to extend, spread; to overspread,<BR>extend over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादा
अन्वादा अन्व्-आ-दा (अनु-आ˚), cl. 3. A. -दत्ते,<BR>दातुम्, to resume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिश्
अन्वादिश् अन्व्-आ-दिश् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 6. P.<BR>-दिशति, -देष्टुम्, to name or mention afresh; to<BR>employ again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिष्ट
अन्व्-आदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, mentioned after or ac-<BR>cording to, employed again; inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादेश|अन्वादेशः
अन्व्-आदेश, अस्, m. mentioning after, a repeated<BR>mention, referring to what has been stated previously,<BR>re-employment of the same word in a subsequent<BR>part of a sentence, the employment again of the same<BR>thing to perform a subsequent operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधान|अन्वाधानं
अन्वाधान अन्व्-आधान, अम्, n. (fr. rt. धा<BR>with अनु and आ), putting fuel (on the three sacred<BR>fires), depositing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधि|अन्वाधिः
1. अन्व्-आधि, इस्, m. a bail or deposit delivered to<BR>a third person, see अन्व्-आहित below; a second deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेय|अन्वाधेयं
अन्व्-आधेय or अन्व्-आधेयक, अम्, n. property<BR>presented after marriage to the wife by her husband's<BR>family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्व्-आहित, अस्, आ, अम्, deposited with a person to<BR>be delivered ultimately to the right owner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधि|अन्वाधिः
अन्वाधि 2. अन्व्-आधि, इस्, m. (rt. ध्यै),<BR>repentance, remorse, melancholy reflection after (the<BR>commission of a bad act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाध्य|अन्वाध्यः
अन्व्-आध्य, अस्, m. a kind of divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वानी
अन्वानी अन्व्-आ-नी, cl. 1. P. -नयति, -नेतुम्,<BR>to lead to, to lead along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वानु
अन्वानु अन्व्-आ-नु, Intens., Ved. -नोनवीति,<BR>to sound through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वान्त्र्य|अन्वांत्र्य
अन्वान्त्र्य अन्व्-आन्त्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being<BR>in the entrails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायतन
अन्वायतन अन्व्-आयतन, अस्, आ, अम्, lati-<BR>tudinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायत्त
अन्वायत्त अन्व्-आयत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. यत्<BR>with आ and अनु), Ved. following after, in accordance<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायात्या
अन्वायात्या अन्व्-आयात्या, f. a deity invoked<BR>by the verb अन्व्-आ-या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारभ्
अन्वारभ् अन्व्-आ-रभ् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. A.<BR>-रभते, -रब्धुम्, to commence; to receive; to<BR>touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारब्ध
अन्व्-आरब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, in contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारभ्य
अन्व्-आरभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be touched, tangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भ|अन्वारंभः|अन्वारम्भः
अन्व्-आरम्भ, अस्, m. or अन्व्-आरमभण, अम्,<BR>n. touching, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भणीया|अन्वारंभणीया
अन्व्-आरम्भणीया, f. an initiatory ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारुह्
अन्वारुह् अन्व्-आ-रुह् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-रोहति, -रोढुम्, to follow or join by ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहण|अन्वारोहणं
अन्व्-आरोहण, अम्, n. (a widow's) ascending the<BR>funeral pile after or with the body of a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहणीय
अन्व्-आरोहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>Anvārohaṇa, or rite of cremation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाविश्
अन्वाविश् अन्व्-आ-विश् (अनु-आ˚), cl. 6. P. -विश्-<BR>अति, -वेष्टुम्, to enter, occupy, possess, engross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाश्रि
अन्वाश्रि अन्व्-आ-श्रि (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. P. -श्रयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to resort to, repair, to go (or come) up to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वास्
अन्वास् अन्व्-आस् (अनु-आस्), cl. 2. A. -आस्ते,<BR>-सितुम्, to follow in taking a seat; to be seated at or<BR>near or round; to be engaged in (especially in a reli-<BR>gious act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासन|अन्वासनं
अन्व्-आसन, अम्, n. sitting down after (another),<BR>service; regret, affliction; a place where work is done,<BR>a manufactory, a house of industry; an unctuous or<BR>cooling enema.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासित
अन्व्-आसित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to sit down after<BR>or alongside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासीन
अन्व्-आसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting down after, seated<BR>alongside of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वास्यमान
अन्व्-आस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being accompanied by,<BR>attended by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वास्था
अन्वास्था अन्व्-आ-स्था (अनु-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-तिष्ठति, -स्थातुम्, to go towards, to meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्य अन्व्-आहार्य, अस्, अम्, m. n. or<BR>अन्व्-अहार्यक, अम्, n. (rt. हृ), a certain gift<BR>presented to the priests; (अम् or अकम्), n. the<BR>monthly Śrāddha or funeral repast in honour of the<BR>manes, held on the day of new moon; according<BR>to Manu, it should be of meat eaten after the pre-<BR>sentation of a Piṇḍa or ball or rice.<BR>—अन्वाहार्य-<BR>पचन, अस्, m. the southern sacrificial fire, used in<BR>the Anvāhārya sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिक
अन्वाहिक अन्व्-आहिक, अस्, ई, अम्, daily, diurnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित अन्व्-आहित. See अन्व्-आधान, p. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वि
अन्वि अन्व्-इ (अनु-इ), cl. 2. P., Ved. -एति,<BR>-तुम्, -तवे, -तवै, to go after or alongside, to<BR>follow; to seek; to be guided by; to fall to one's share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्व्-अय. See s. v., p. 47, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वित|अन्वितः
अन्व्-इत or अन्व्-ईत, अस्, आ, अम्, joined, attended,<BR>connected with, linked to; having as an essential or<BR>inherent part, endowed with, possessed of, possessing;<BR>acquired, reached by the mind, understood; follow-<BR>ing; connected as in grammar or construction.<BR>—अन्व्-<BR>इतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a clear meaning<BR>understood from the context, perspicuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विति|अन्वितिः
अन्व्-इति, इस्, f. following after; food (as the com-<BR>panion of the body?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीयमान
अन्व्-ईयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विध्
अन्विध् अन्व्-इध् or अन्व्-इन्ध् (अनु-इन्ध्), cl.<BR>7. or cl. 1. A. -इन्द्धे or -इन्धते, -धितुम्, to kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्
अन्विष् 1. अन्व्-इष् (अनु-इष्), cl. 1. P. -इच्छति,<BR>-एषितुम्, -एष्टुम्, to desire, seek, seek after, search,<BR>aim at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्
अन्विष् 2. अन्व्-इष् (अनु-इष्), cl. 4. P. -इष्-<BR>यति, -एषितुम्, to go after, seek, search: Caus.<BR>-एषयति, -यितुम्, to seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्ट|अन्विष्टः
अन्व्-इष्ट or अन्व्-इष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, sought,<BR>required.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष|अन्वेषः
अन्व्-एष, अस्, m. or अन्व्-एषण, अम्, आ, n. f.<BR>seeking for, searching, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषक
अन्व्-एषक, अस्, इका, अम्, or अन्व्-एषिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, or अन्व्-एष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, searching, enquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष्टव्य
अन्व्-एष्टव्य or अन्व्-एष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>searched, to be investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्ष्
अन्वीक्ष् अन्व्-ईक्ष् (अनु-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A. -ईक्-<BR>षते, -षितुम्, to follow with one's looks, to keep<BR>looking or gazing, to keep in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्षण|अन्वीक्षणं
अन्व्-ईक्षण, अम्, n. or अन्व्-ईक्षा, f. reflection,<BR>meditation, searching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीप
अन्वीप अन्वीप, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अप्, q. v., with<BR>अनु), near the water; or (fr. rt. आप् with अनु),<BR>attainable; friendly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वृ
अन्वृ अन्व्-ऋ (अनु-ऋ), cl. 3. P. -इयर्ति,<BR>-अर्तुम् or -अरितुम् or -अरीतुम् (?), to follow; to<BR>follow in rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वृचम्
अन्वृचम् अन्व्-ऋचम्, ind. verse after verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वृध्
अन्वृध् अन्व्-ऋध् (अनु-ऋध्), cl. 6. P., Ved.<BR>-ऋधति, -अर्धितुम्, to carry out, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वे
अन्वे अन्व्-ए (अनु-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. -ऐति, -तुम्,<BR>to come after, to follow as an adherent or attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्
अप् अप् (in the Vedas used in sing. and<BR>plur., but in the classical language only in plur.), आपस्,<BR>f. water; air, the intermediate region; the star δ Virigi-<BR>nis. Sometimes, particularly in the Vedas, the आपः<BR>are considered as divinities. As the last member of a<BR>compound, अप् may become अप, ईप, ऊप. [Cf.<BR>Lat. aqua; Goth. ahva, ‘a river;’ Old Germ. aha,<BR>and affa at the end of compounds; Lith. uppê, ‘a<BR>river;’ perhaps Lat. amnis, ‘a river,’ for apnis; cf.<BR>also ἀφρός].<BR>—अप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. watery.<BR>—अपः-संवर्त, अस्, m. (Buddh.) destruction (of<BR>the world) by water.<BR>—अपां-वत्स, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>star (‘calf of the waters’).<BR>—अपां-नपात्, त्, or<BR>अपां-नप्तृ, ता, or अपां-गर्भ, अस्, or अपान्-<BR>नपात्, or अपो-नपात्, त्, &c., m., Ved., N. of Agni<BR>or fire as sprung from water.<BR>—अपां-नपत्रिय or<BR>अपां-नप्त्रीय or अपो-नपत्रिय or अपो-नप्त्रीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to Agni.<BR>—अपां-नाथ,<BR>अस्, m. the ocean.<BR>—अपां-निधि, इस्, m. the ocean.<BR>—अपाम्-पति or अप्-पति, इस्, m. the ocean; N. of<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>—अपाम्-पित्त or अप्-पित्त, अम्, n. fire; a<BR>plant.<BR>—अप्-कृत्स्न, अम्, n. deep meditation per-<BR>formed by means of water.<BR>—अप्-चर, अस्, m. an<BR>aquatic animal.<BR>—अप्-सरस्, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्त्य
अप्त्य, अप्य. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव
अपव, अप्सव्य, अप्सा. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सु
अप्सु, for words beginning thus. See अप्सु-.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्
अब्-, for words beginning thus. See अब्-इन्धन,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
अप अप, ind. (as a prefix to nouns and<BR>verbs, expresses) away, off, back, (opposed to उप,<BR>अनु, सम्, प्र), down (opposed to उद्).<BR>When prefixed to nouns, it may sometimes = the<BR>neg. particle अ, e. g. अप-भी, fearless; or may ex-<BR>press deterioration, inferiority, &c., e. g. अप-पाठ,<BR>q. v.<BR>(As a separable preposition or adverb, with abl.)<BR>away from, on the outside of, without, with the ex-<BR>ception of. It is separated only in the Vedas [cf. Gr.<BR>ἀπό Lat. ab; Goth. af; Eng. of].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरुण
अपकरुण अप-करुण, अस्, आ, अम्, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकलङ्क|अपकलंक|अपकलंकः|अपकलङ्कः
अपकलङ्क अप-कलङ्क, अस्, m. an indelible<BR>disgrace, a deep stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकल्मष
अपकल्मष अप-कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, stain-<BR>less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकष्
अपकष् अप-कष्, cl. 1. P. -कषति, -षितुम्,<BR>to scrape off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकाम|अपकामः
अपकाम अप-काम, अस्, m., Ved. aversion,<BR>abhorrence; abominableness; deprivation of what is<BR>dear; (अम्), ind. against one's liking, unwillingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकीर्ति|अपकीर्तिः|अपकीर्त्ति
अपकीर्ति अप-कीर्ति, इस्, f. infamy, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकुक्षि
अपकुक्षि अप-कुक्षि, इस्, m. a bad or ill-<BR>shaped belly (?). This word may also be used as a<BR>बहु-व्रीहि and as an अव्ययी-भाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकुञ्ज|अपकुञ्जः
अपकुञ्ज अप-कुञ्ज, अस्, m., N. of a younger<BR>brother of the serpent king Śeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृ
अपकृ अप-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to carry away, remove, drag away; (with<BR>gen. or acc.) to hurt, wrong, injure (any one): Caus.<BR>-कारयति, -यितुम्, to hurt, wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरण|अपकरणं
अप-करण, अम्, n. acting improperly; doing<BR>wrong; ill-treating, offending, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्तृ|अपकर्त्तृ
अप-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, injurious, offensive, hos-<BR>tile, inimical, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्मन्|अपकर्म्मन्
अप-कर्मन्, अ, n. discharge (of a debt); evil doing,<BR>improper conduct, wickedness; oppression, violence;<BR>laziness, incompetence; any impure or degrading act<BR>or rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकार|अपकारः
अप-कार, अस्, आ, अम्, acting wrong, offending;<BR>(अस्), m. wrong, offence, injury, hurt; wickedness;<BR>oppression, enmity.<BR>—अपकार-गिर्, ईस्, f. or अप-<BR>कार-शब्द, अस्, m. an offending or menacing speech.<BR>—अपकार-ता, f. wrong, offence.<BR>—अपकारार्थिन्<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, malicious, malevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारक|अपकारकः
अप-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, or अप-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>(with gen.) acting wrong, doing ill (to any one),<BR>offending, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत
अप-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done wrong, maliciously,<BR>offensively or wickedly committed; observed or<BR>practised as a degrading or impure act, as servile<BR>duties, funeral rites, &c.; (अम्), n. injury, offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृति|अपकृतिः
अप-कृति, इस्, f. oppression, wrong, injury; en-<BR>mity, opposition; any degrading or impure act or<BR>rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत्य
अप-कृत्य, अम्, n. damage, injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अप-क्रिया, f. delivery, clearing off (debts); offence;<BR>any impure act or rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत्
अपकृत् अप-कृत्, cl. 6. P. -कृन्तति, -कर्-<BR>तितुम्, to cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्
अपकृष् अप-कृष्, cl. 1. and 6. P. A. -कर्ष्-<BR>अति, -ते, -कृषति, -ते, -कर्ष्टुम् or -क्रष्टुम्,<BR>to draw off or aside, drag down, carry away, take<BR>away, remove; to omit, diminish; to put away; to<BR>anticipate something which occurs later (as a word of<BR>a sentence); to bend (a bow); to detract, debase,<BR>dishonour: Caus. -कर्षयति, -यितुम्, to remove,<BR>diminish, detract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्ष|अपकर्षः
अप-कर्ष, अस्, m. drawing or dragging off or<BR>down, detraction, deficiency, diminution, decay; low-<BR>ering, deterioration, depression; decline, degradation,<BR>inferiority, infamy; anticipated performance of a<BR>duty; (in poetry) anticipation of a word occurring<BR>later.<BR>—अपकर्ष-सम, अस्, आ, m. f. a sophism<BR>in the Nyāya, e. g. ‘sound has not the quality of<BR>shape as a jar has, therefore sound and a jar have no<BR>qualities in common.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षक
अप-कर्षक, अस्, इका, अम्, drawing down, de-<BR>tracting (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षण
अप-कर्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, taking away, forcing<BR>away, removing, diminishing; (अम्), n. taking<BR>away, depriving of; drawing down; abolishing, de-<BR>nying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अप-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn away, taken away,<BR>removed, lost; dragged down, brought down, de-<BR>pressed; low, vile, inferior; (अस्), m. a crow.<BR>—अप-<BR>कृष्ट-चेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, mentally debased.<BR>—अप-<BR>कृष्ट-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, of a low tribe.<BR>—अपकृष्ट-<BR>ता, f. or अपकृष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. inferiority, vileness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकॄ
अपकॄ अप-कॄ, cl. 6. P. -किरति, -करितुम्,<BR>रीतुम्, to spout out, spurt, scatter; to throw down;<BR>to scrape with the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकौशली
अपकौशली अप-कौशली, f. news, informa-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ति|अपक्तिः
अपक्ति अ-पक्ति, इस्, f. (rt. पच्), immaturity;<BR>indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्व|अपक्वः
अ-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, unripe, immature; undi-<BR>gested.<BR>—अपक्व-ता, f. immaturity; incompleteness.<BR>—अपक्व-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, of immature under-<BR>standing.<BR>—अपक्वाशिन् (˚व-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating<BR>raw, uncooked food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम्
अपक्रम् अप-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. -क्रामति, poet.<BR>A. -क्रमते, -मितुम्, to go away, fly, retreat, re-<BR>tire from; to glide away; to measure off by steps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम|अपक्रमः
