अपतानकिन्
अप-तानकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, affected with spasmodic<BR>contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपति|अपतिः
अपति अ-पति, इस्, m., Ved. not a husband<BR>or master; (इस्, इस्, इ), without a husband or master,<BR>unmarried.<BR>—अ-पति-घ्नी, f. not killing the husband.<BR>—अपति-ता, f. state of being without a husband.<BR>—अपति-पुत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, without a husband and<BR>children.<BR>—अ-पति-व्रता, f. an unfaithful or unchaste<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतिक
अ-पतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, without a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतीर्थ
