अपत्त्र
अपत्त्र अ-पत्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, leafless; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नीक
अपत्नीक अ-पत्नीक, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्य|अपत्यं
अपत्य अपत्य, अम्, n. (fr. अप or according<BR>to native etym. fr. rt. पत् with अ, because a family is by<BR>offspring prevented from falling into decay); offspring,<BR>child, descendant; a patronymical affix.<BR>—अपत्य-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of offspring.<BR>—अपत्य-<BR>जीव, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अपत्य-ता, f. state of<BR>childhood.<BR>—अपत्य-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving offspring;<BR>(आ), f., N. of various plants.<BR>—अपत्य-पथ, अस्,<BR>m. the vulva.<BR>—अपत्य-प्रथ्यय, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymical affix.<BR>—अपत्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed<BR>of offspring.<BR>—अपत्य-विक्रयिन्, ई, m. a seller of his<BR>offspring; a father who receives a gratuity from his<BR>son-in-law.<BR>—अपत्य-शत्रु, उस्, m. ‘having his de-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-a" target="_blank">Page0050-a+ 73</a>]<BR>scendants for enemies,’ a crab (said to perish in<BR>producing young).<BR>—अपत्य-साच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. ac-<BR>companied with offspring.<BR>—अपत्यार्थ-शब्द (˚य-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप्
