अपभर्तृ|अपभर्त्तृ
अप-भर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. taking away, de-<BR>stroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभाष्
अपभाष् अप-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भाषते,<BR>-षितुम्, to revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभाषण|अपभाषणं
अप-भाषण, अम्, n. abuse, bad words, vitu-<BR>peration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभू
अपभू अप-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्,<BR>to be absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभूति|अपभूतिः
अप-भूति, इस्, f., Ved. defect, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश|अपभ्रंशः
अपभ्रंश अप-भ्रंश or अप-भ्रंस, अस्, m.<BR>falling down or away; a bad fall; a corrupted word,<BR>a corruption; ungrammatical language, the most<BR>corrupt of the Prākṛt dialects. (The spelling अप-<BR>भ्रंस is incorrect according to some grammarians.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रष्ट
अप-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen away, corrupted<BR>(as a Prākṛt dialect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपम|अपमः
अपम अपम, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अप), Ved. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">Page0051-a+ 71</a>]<BR>most distant, the last; (अस्), m. the declination in<BR>astronomy; the ecliptic.<BR>—अपम-क्षेत्र, see<BR>क्रान्ति-क्षेत्र.<BR>—अपम-ज्या, f. the sine of the<BR>ecliptic.<BR>—अपम-मण्डल or अप-मण्डल or<BR>अपम-वृत्त, अम्, n. the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमन्यु
अपमन्यु अप-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, free from<BR>grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्द|अपमर्दः|अपमर्द्द
अपमर्द अप-मर्द, अस्, m. (rt. मृद्), what<BR>is swept away, dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्श|अपमर्शः
अपमर्श अप-मर्श, अस्, m. (rt. मृश्), touch-<BR>ing, grazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान|अपमानं|अपमानः
अपमान अप-मान, अस्, अम्, m. n. (rt. मन्),<BR>disrespect, contempt, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानित्र
अप-मानित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, dishonoured, disgraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानिन्
अप-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dishonouring, despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान्य
अप-मान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, disreputable, dishonourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्ग|अपमार्गः
अपमार्ग अप-मार्ग, अस्, m. a by-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्य
अपमित्य 1. अप-मित्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मि?),<BR>Ved. to be thrown away; see under अप-मे below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमुख
अपमुख अप-मुख, अस्, आ, अम् having the<BR>face averted; having an ill-formed face or mouth;<BR>(अम्), ind. except or without the face, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमूर्धन्
अपमूर्धन् अप-मूर्धन्, आ, आ, अ, headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृज्
अपमृज् अप-मृज्, cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि, -मार्-<BR>जितुम्, -मार्ष्टुम्, to wipe off, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्जन|अपमार्जनं
अप-मार्जन, अम्, n. cleansing; shaving, paring,<BR>chips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृष्ट
अप-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्यु|अपमृत्युः
अपमृत्यु अप-मृत्यु, उस्, m. sudden death,<BR>dying by some accident, not of sickness or decay; a<BR>great danger or illness, from which a person, contrary<BR>to expectation, recovers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृषित
अपमृषित अप-मृषित, अस्, आ, अम्, unin-<BR>telligible (as a speech).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमे
अपमे अप-मे, cl. 1. A. -मयते, -मातुम्,<BR>to change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्य
2. अप-मित्य or अप-मित्यक, अम्, n. debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अपयशस् अप-यशस्, अस्, n. disgrace, infamy.<BR>—अपयशस्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, occasioning infamy,<BR>disgraceful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपया
अपया अप-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -तुम्, to go<BR>away, to depart, fall off, go over to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयात|अपयातं
अप-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone away, having retired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयातर्व्य
अप-यातर्व्य, अम्, n. to be gone away (used im-<BR>personally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयान|अपयानं
अप-यान, अम्, n. retreat, flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयु
अपयु अप-यु, cl. 3. P., Ved. -युयोति, to<BR>repel, disjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर 1. अ-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, having nothing<BR>beyond or after, having no rival or superior.<BR>—अ-<BR>पर-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having nothing following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर 2. अपर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अप), posterior,<BR>hinder, later, latter (opposed to पूर्व and often<BR>occuring as the first member of a comp.); following;<BR>western; inferior, lower (opposed to पर); other,<BR>another (opposed to स्व); different (with abl.); dis-<BR>tant, opposite. Sometimes अपर is used as a con-<BR>junction to connect words or sentences, e. g. अपरञ्च,<BR>moreover. (अस्), m. the hind foot of an elephant;<BR>(आ), f. the west; the hind quarter of an elephant;<BR>the womb; (ई), f., Ved. the future times, future;<BR>(अम्), n. the future; the hind quarter of an elephant;<BR>(अम्), ind. in future, for the future; again, more-<BR>over; (एण), ind. (with acc.) behind, west, to the west<BR>of [cf. Goth. and Old Germ. afar; and the Mod.<BR>Germ. aber, in such words as Aber-mal, Aber-<BR>witz].<BR>—अपर-कान्यकुब्ज, अस्, ई, अम्, situated in<BR>the western part of Kānyakubjā.<BR>—अपर-काय, अस्,<BR>m. the hind part of the body.<BR>—अपर-काल, अस्,<BR>m. another or later period.<BR>—अपर-गोदान, अम्,<BR>n. (in Buddhist cosmogony) a country west of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">Page0051-b+ 77</a>]<BR>the Mahā-meru.<BR>—अपर-ज, अस्, m., Ved. born<BR>later, or at the end of the world (the destroying<BR>fire).<BR>—अपर-जन, अस्, m. an inhabitant of the<BR>west.<BR>—अपर-ता, f. or अपर-त्व, अम्, n. distance;<BR>posteriority (in place or time); opposition, contra-<BR>riety, relativeness; nearness.<BR>—अपर-त्र, ind. in<BR>another place; एकत्र, अपरत्र, in one place, in<BR>the other place.<BR>—अपर-दक्षिणम्, ind. south-<BR>west.<BR>—अपर-निदाघ, अस्, m. the latter part of<BR>the summer.<BR>—अपर-पक्ष, अस्, m. the latter half<BR>of the month, the other or opposing side, the defend-<BR>ant.<BR>—अपर-पक्षीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>latter half of the month.<BR>—अपर-परिचाल, आस्, m. pl.<BR>the western Pañcālas.<BR>—अपर-पर, आस्, or ए, आस्, आणि,<BR>pl. one and the other, various.<BR>—अपर-प्रणेय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, easily led by others, tractable.<BR>—अपर-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. existing after, succession, continuation.<BR>—अपर-<BR>रात्र, अस्, m. the latter half of the night, the end of<BR>the night, the last watch.<BR>—अपर-लोक, अम्, n. an-<BR>other world, paradise.<BR>—अपर-वक्त्रा, f. a kind of<BR>metre of four lines, having every two lines the same.<BR>—अपर-वत्, ind. like what comes after.<BR>—अपर-<BR>वर्षा, आस्, f. pl. the latter part of the rains.<BR>—अपर-<BR>शरद्, त्, f. the latter part of the autumn.<BR>—अपर-<BR>सक्थ, अम्, n. the hind thigh.<BR>—१. अपरस्-पर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one after another; continued, uniter-<BR>rupted.<BR>—अपर-स्वस्तिक, अम्, n. the western point<BR>in the horizon.<BR>—अपर-हेमन्त, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>the latter part of winter.<BR>—अपर-हैमन, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, belonging to the latter half of the winter<BR>season.<BR>—अपराग्नि (˚र-अग्˚), ई, m. du. the दक्-<BR>षिण, i. e. southern, and gārhapatya, i. e. western<BR>fire (of a sacrifice).<BR>—अपरान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, living at the western border; (अस्), m. the west-<BR>ern extremity, the country or the inhabitants of the<BR>western border; the extreme end or term; death.<BR>—अपरान्तक, अस्, m. the same as अपरान्त; N.<BR>of a song; (इका), f. a metre consisting of four times<BR>sixteen mātrās.<BR>—अपरान्त-ज्ञान, अम्, n. prescience<BR>of one's latter end.<BR>—अपरापर (˚र-अप्˚), आस्, or ए,<BR>आस्, आणि, pl. another and another, various.<BR>—अप-<BR>रार्क (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. the oldest known com-<BR>mentator of Yājñavalkya's law-book.<BR>—अपरार्क-<BR>चन्द्रिका, f. the name of his comment.<BR>—अपरार्-<BR>ध (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. the latter, the second half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्ण|अपराह्णः
अपराह्ण (˚र-अह्˚), अस्, m. afternoon, the last<BR>watch of the day.<BR>—अपराह्णतन or अपराह्-<BR>णेतन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or produced in the<BR>close of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेतरा
अपरेतरा (˚र-इत्˚), f. opposite to or other than<BR>the west, the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेद्युस्
अपरे-द्युस्, ind. on the following day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरक्त
अपरक्त अप-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, colourless,<BR>bloodless, pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरति|अपरतिः
अपरति अप-रति, इस्, f. (rt. रम्), stopping,<BR>ceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरव|अपरवः
अपरव अप-रव, अस्, m. contest, dispute;<BR>discord.<BR>—अपरवोज्झित (˚व-उज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from dispute, undisturbed, undisputed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर 2. अ-परस्पर, अस्, आ, अम्, not re-<BR>ciprocal, not one (by) the other.<BR>—अ-परस्पर-<BR>सम्भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, not produced one by the<BR>other; or (fr. 1. अपरस्-पर above), produced by<BR>an uninterrupted series (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराग|अपरागः
अपराग अप-राग, अस्, m. (rt. रञ्ज्), aver-<BR>sion, antipathy, enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराच्
अपराच् अ-पराच्, आङ्, आची, आक्, not averted,<BR>i. e. fronting, in front.<BR>—अ-पराङ्-मुख, अस्, आ, or<BR>ई, अम्, with unaverted face, not turned away; pre-<BR>senting a firm front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजित|अपराजितः
अपराजित अ-पराजित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. जि),<BR>unconquered, unsurpassed; (अस्), m. a poisonous in-<BR>sect; Viṣṇu; Śiva; one of the eleven Rudras; a<BR>class of divinities, constituting one portion of the so-<BR>called Anuttara divinities of the Jainas; N. of a<BR>sage; (आ), f. Durgā; a name applied to several<BR>plants, Clitoria Ternatea, Marsilea Quadrifolia, Ses-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">Page0051-c+ 72</a>]<BR>bania Ægyptiaca; a species of the Śarkari metre of<BR>four lines, each containing fourteen syllables.<BR>—अपरा-<BR>जिता-दिश्, क्, f. the north-east quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजिष्णु
अ-पराजिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, or अ-पराजेय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unconquerable, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध्
अपराध् अप-राध्, cl. 4. or 5. P. -राध्यति,<BR>राध्नोति, -राद्धुम्, to wrong (with gen.), to<BR>offend, sin; to annoy, prohibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्ध
अप-राद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, sinned; criminal, guilty;<BR>erring.<BR>—अपराद्ध-पृषक्त, अस्, or अपराद्-<BR>धेषु (˚ध-इष्˚), उस्, m. an archer whose arrows<BR>always miss the mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धि|अपराद्धिः
अप-राद्धि, इस्, f. wrong, mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धृ
अप-राद्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, offending, an<BR>offender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध|अपराधः
अप-राध, अस्, m. offence, transgression, fault; mis-<BR>take; e. g. अपराधं कृ, (with gen.) to offend any<BR>one.<BR>—अपराध-भञ्जन, अस्, m. the destroyer<BR>of sin, epithet of Śiva.<BR>—अपराधभञ्जन-स्तोत्र,<BR>अम्, n. a poem of Śaṅkarācārya, in praise of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिन्
अप-राधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, offending; criminal; guilty.<BR>—अपराधि-ता, f. or अपराधि-त्व, अम्, n. crimi-<BR>nality, guilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापरण
अपरापरण अ-परापरण, अस्, m. not having<BR>descendants or offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरामृष्ट
अपरामृष्ट अ-परामृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिकलित|अपरिकलितः
अपरिकलित अ-परिकलित, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>known, unseen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिक्रम
