अपोढ
अपोढ अपोढ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वह् with<BR>अप), carried off, removed, taken away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोत्कृष्
अपोत्कृष् अपोत्-कृष् (अप-उद्-कृष्), cl. 1. 6.<BR>P. A. -कर्षति, -ते, -क्रिषति, -ते, -कर्ष्टुम्,<BR>-क्रष्टुम्, to separate, disjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदक
अपोदक अपोदक (˚प-उद्˚) अस्, आ, अम्, water-<BR>less, water-tight; not watery, not fluid; (इका), f. a<BR>pot-herb, Basella Rubra or Lucida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदि
अपोदि अपोद्-इ (अप-उद्-इ), cl. 2. P. -एति,<BR>-तुम्, to go away altogether, to give way, to with-<BR>draw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदित्य
अपोद्-इत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be completely gone<BR>away from or left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोद्धार्य
अपोद्धार्य अपोद्-धार्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हृ<BR>with अप and उद्), liable to have something taken<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोनपात्
