अप्रमादिन्
अ-प्रमादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, careful, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमद
अप्रमद अ-प्रमद, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>pleasure, joyless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमय
अप्रमय अ-प्रमय, अस्, अ, अम्, Ved. un-<BR>limited, imperishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमा
अप्रमा अ-प्रमा, f. a rule which is no<BR>authority (see अ-प्रमाण); incorrect knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाण
अप्रमाण अ-प्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, immeasur-<BR>able, unlimited; without weight or proof, without au-<BR>thority; (अम्), n. a rule which is no standard of action.<BR>—अ-प्रमाण-विद्, त्, त्, त्, incapable of weighing<BR>evidence.<BR>—अप्रमाण-शुभ, आस्, m. pl. of immea-<BR>surable virtue; N. of a class of Buddhist divinities.<BR>—अप्रमाणाभ (˚ण-आभ), आस्, m. pl. of unlimited<BR>splendor; N. of a class of divinities in Buddhism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाणिक
अ-प्रमाणिक, अस्, आ, अम्, unauthorized; properly<BR>अ-प्रामाणिक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमित
अ-प्रमित, अस्, आ, अम्, unbounded, unmeasured;<BR>not proved, not established by authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेय
