अप्रवीण
अप्रवीण अ-प्रवीण, अस्, आ, अम्, unskilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवीत
अप्रवीत अ-प्रवीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unap-<BR>proached; not approaching (to impregnate); not im-<BR>pregnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवृद्ध
अप्रवृद्ध अ-प्रवृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not ex-<BR>cessively grown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवेद
अप्रवेद अ-प्रवेद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. difficult<BR>to be found or obtained; silent (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशक्त
अप्रशक्त अ-प्रशक्त, अ-प्रशक्ति, probably<BR>for अ-प्रसक्त, अ-प्रसक्ति, q. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्त|अप्रशस्तं
अप्रशस्त 1. अ-प्रशस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. शंस्),<BR>not praised, worthless, contemptible; not approved,<BR>forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्य
अ-प्रशस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not praiseworthy, not<BR>good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्त|अप्रशस्तं
अप्रशस्त 2. अ-प्रशस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. शास्),<BR>Ved. indocile, disobedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्त
अप्रसक्त अ-प्रसक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. सञ्ज्), not<BR>addicted, not attached to; moderate, temperate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्ति|अप्रसक्तिः
अ-प्रसक्ति, इस्, f. or अ-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m. non-<BR>addiction, non-attachment, moderation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसन्न|अप्रसन्नं
अप्रसन्न अ-प्रसन्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. सद्), not<BR>quiet, not clear, turbid, muddy; displeased, dissatisfied,<BR>unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाद|अप्रसादः
अ-प्रसाद, अस्, m. disfavour, disapprobation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाद्य
अ-प्रसाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be propitiated;<BR>unappeasable, implacable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसव|अप्रसवः
अप्रसव अ-प्रसव, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. सु or सू),<BR>not being prolific; (अस्), m. the not being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसूत
अ-प्रसूत, अस्, आ, अम्, not having offspring, bar-<BR>ren, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसह्य
अप्रसह्य अ-प्रसह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, intolerable,<BR>insufferable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्ध|अप्रसिद्धं
अप्रसिद्ध अ-प्रसिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not settled<BR>or established; unknown, uncelebrated; unusual, un-<BR>common, of no real existence, not current or generally<BR>known.<BR>—अप्रसिद्ध-पद, अम्, n. an obsolete<BR>word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुत|अप्रस्तुतं
अप्रस्तुत अ-प्रस्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, unconnected<BR>with, irrelevant, unsuitable to the time or subject; not<BR>principal, not being the chief subject-matter; acci-<BR>dental or extraneous; not ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्ताविक
अ-प्रस्ताविक, अस्, ई, अम्, irrelevant to the subject-<BR>matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहत|अप्रहतं
अप्रहत अ-प्रहत, अस्, आ, अम्, unhurt, in-<BR>tact; untilled, waste; uncultivated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहन्
अ-प्रहन्, आ, आ, अ, or अ-प्रहन्तृ, ता, त्री,<BR>तृ, not hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहित
अप्रहित अ-प्रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>stirred up, not sent out, unassailed (by foes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकृत
अप्राकृत अ-प्राकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not princi-<BR>pal; not original; special, particular; not vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राग्र्य|अप्राग्र्यं
अप्राग्र्य अ-प्राग्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, secondary,<BR>subordinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राचीन|अप्राचीनं
अप्राचीन अ-प्राचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, modern, re-<BR>cent; not eastern, western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञ
अप्राज्ञ अ-प्राज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, unlearned,<BR>ignorant; unconscious.<BR>—अप्राज्ञ-ता, f. ignorance,<BR>unconsciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राण|अप्राणः
अप्राण अ-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-प्राणिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, inanimate, lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राधान्य
अप्राधान्य अ-प्राधान्य, अम्, n. inferiority,<BR>subordination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्त|अप्राप्तः
अप्राप्त अ-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. आप् with प्र),<BR>unobtained; unarrived; unproved.<BR>—अप्राप्त-काल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, out of season, inopportune, ill-timed; un-<BR>der age; (अम्), n. an irregular debate.<BR>—अप्राप्त-<BR>यौवन, अस्, आ, अम्, not arrived at puberty.<BR>—अ-<BR>प्राप्त-व्यवहार or अप्राप्त-वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>a minor in law; under age, not of years to engage<BR>in law or public business.<BR>—अप्राप्तावसर (˚त-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, unseasonable, inopportune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्ति|अप्राप्तिः
अ-प्राप्ति, इस्, f. non-attainment, non-acquisition,<BR>scarcity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्य|अप्राप्यं
अ-प्राप्य, ind. not having found; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>unobtainable, unattainable, scarce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाणिक|अप्रामाणिकः
अप्रामाणिक अ-प्रामाणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, un-<BR>authentic, unwarranted, unauthoritative, unworthy of<BR>being trusted or believed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाण्य|अप्रामाण्यं
अ-प्रामाण्य, अम्, n. absence or insufficiency of<BR>proof or authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामिसत्य
अप्रामिसत्य अ-प्रामि-सत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मी<BR>with प्र), Ved. of unimpaired truthfulness; unalter-<BR>ably true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायत्य|अप्रायत्यं
अप्रायत्य अ-प्रायत्य, अम्, n. impurity, un-<BR>governableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायु
अप्रायु अ-प्रायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. assiduous,<BR>unceasing, not going forth (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायुस्
अ-प्रायुस्, उस्, m., Ved. not ceasing; with unde-<BR>parted life, with unimpaired or ever brilliant vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिय|अप्रियं|अप्रियः
अप्रिय अ-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, disagreeable,<BR>disliked; unkind, unfriendly; (अस्), m. a foe, an<BR>enemy; N. of a Yakṣa; (आ), f. a sort of skeat fish,<BR>Silurus Pungentissimus.<BR>—अप्रिय-कर, अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, or अप्रिय-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, doing an unkind-<BR>ness; unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR>—अप्रिय-भागिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, unfortunate.<BR>—अप्रिय-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ or<BR>अप्रियं-वद, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking unkindly or<BR>harshly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीति|अप्रीतिः
अ-प्रीति, इस्, f. dislike, aversion, unfriendliness, en-<BR>mity; pain.<BR>—अप्रीति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, unkind, ad-<BR>verse; disagreeable, offensive.<BR>—अप्रीत्य्-आत्मक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, consisting of pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेतराक्षसी
अप्रेतराक्षसी अप्रेत-राक्षसी, f., N. of a<BR>plant, Ocimum Sanctum; see अपेत-राक्षसी, p. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेमन्
अप्रेमन् अ-प्रेमन्, अ, n. dislike, aversion;<BR>(आ, आ, अ), unfriendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रैष
अप्रैष अ-प्रैष, अस्, आ, अम्, not invoked<BR>with a प्रैष (q. v.) mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रोषिवस्
अप्रोषिवस् अ-प्रोषिवस्, -वान्, -षुषी, -वत्<BR>(rt. वस्, perf. part.), Ved. not gone away, staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रौढ
अप्रौढ अ-प्रौढ, अस्, आ, अम्, not arrogant,<BR>timid, gentle; (आ), f. an unmarried girl, or one very<BR>recently married and not come to womanhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्लव
अप्लव अ-प्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, without a ship;<BR>not swimming.<BR>—अ-प्लवेश (˚व-ईश), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>unable to swim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्वा
अप्वा अप्वा, f. (fr. अप or fr. obs. rt. अप्?),<BR>disease; danger; the region of the throat or neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्स|अप्सः
अप्स 1. अप्-स, अस्, m., Ved. giving or<BR>yielding (अप्) water [cf. अप्-सा below].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्स|अप्सः
अप्स 2. अ-प्स, अस्, m., Ved. not destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सर|अप्सरः
अप्सर अप्-सर, अस्, m. water-goer, any<BR>aquatic animal (see etym. of next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्
अप्सरस् अप्सरस्, आस्, or अप्सरा, f. (fr. अप्,<BR>q. v., and rt. सृ, ‘going in the waters or between<BR>the waters of the clouds’); certain female divinities,<BR>who reside in the sky and are the wives of the Gan-<BR>dharvas; they have the faculty of changing their<BR>shapes, are very fond of bathing, and are said to have<BR>been produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR>—अप्स-<BR>रः-पति, इस्, m. Indra, lord of the Apsarasas.<BR>—अप्स-<BR>रस्-तीर्थ, अम्, n. a pool in which the Apsarasas<BR>bathe.<BR>—अप्सरा-पति, इस्, m. lord of the Apsarasas;<BR>N. of the Gandharva Śikhaṇḍin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सराय
अप्सराय, nom. A. अप्सरायते, -यितुम्, to behave<BR>like an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सव
अप्सव अप्सव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (if from<BR>अप्सस्) possessed of form or shape; (if from अप्)<BR>giving water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सव्य
अप्सव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for water, being in the<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सस्
अप्सस् अप्सस्, अस्, n. (fr. obs. rt. अप्), Ved.<BR>cheek; shape, beauty (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सा
अप्सा अप्-सा, आस्, m. (fr. अप् and rt. सन्), Ved.<BR>giving water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सु
अप्सु 1. अ-प्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. without food;<BR>not beautiful (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सु
अप्सु 2. अप्सु (loc. pl. of अप्, q. v.), in the<BR>water or waters. This word forms the first member<BR>of various compounds, thus:<BR>—अप्सु-क्षित्, त्, m.,<BR>Ved. dwelling within the clouds, in the region be-<BR>tween heaven and earth.<BR>—अप्सु-चरु, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. going in the waters.<BR>—अप्सु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or अप्सु-जा, आस्, आस्, m. f., Ved. born in the waters.<BR>—अप्सु-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. vanquishing between the<BR>waters or in the region of the clouds.<BR>—अप्सु-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of what is in the waters; mot<BR>losing one's nature in the water (e. g. the lightning<BR>does not lose his fiery nature in the clouds); con-<BR>taining the word अप्सु.<BR>—अप्सु-योग, अस्, m. the<BR>connecting power in water.<BR>—अप्सु-योनि, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. born from the waters.<BR>—अप्सु-वाह्, ट्, m., Ved.<BR>driving in water.<BR>—अप्सु-षद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. dwelling<BR>in the waters.<BR>—अप्सु-सोम, अस्, m. Soma in water;<BR>a cup filled with water.<BR>—अप्सु-संशित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. raised or excited in the waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल|अफलः
अफल अ-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, unfruitful,<BR>barren; vain, unproductive; deprived of virility; (अस्),<BR>m., N, of a plant, Tamarix Indica; (आ), f. the Aloe<BR>plant, Aloes Perfoliata; another plant, Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta.<BR>—अ-फल-काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, disinterested,<BR>not looking to beneficial consequences.<BR>—अफल-ता,<BR>f. or अफल-त्व, अम्, n. barreness, unprofitableness.<BR>—अ-फल-प्रेप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, one who desires no<BR>recompense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल्गु
अफल्गु अ-फल्गु, उस्, उस्, उ, not vain, pro-<BR>dictive, profitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफुल्ल
अफुल्ल अ-फुल्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, unblown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अफेन 1. अ-फेन, अस्, आ, अम्, frothless,<BR>without scum or foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अफेन 2. अ-फेन, अम्, n. (corruption of<BR>अहि-फेन, foam of a snake?), opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्ध|अबद्धं|अबद्धः
अबद्ध अ-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-बद्धक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम् (rt. बन्ध्), unbound, at liberty; un-<BR>meaning, nonsensical.<BR>—अबद्ध-मुख, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, foul-mouthed, scurrilous; mendacious.<BR>.1. अ-बध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unmeaning, nonsensical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धक|अबंधक
अ-बन्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, not binding; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धन|अबंधन
अ-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, without fetters, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्य|अबन्ध्यः
अ-बन्ध्य. See s. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्र|अबंध्र
अ-बन्ध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. without bonds or<BR>ligatures, falling asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध
अबध अ-बध, अस्, m. (rt. बध्), not killing;<BR>(आ), f. a segment of the base of a triangle, see अ-<BR>वध.<BR>—अबधार्ह (˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>worthy of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्य|अबध्यं
2. अ-बध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be killed, invio-<BR>lable; see also अ-वध्य.<BR>—अबध्य-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. immunity, sacredness of character, as, that of an<BR>ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धु|अबंधु
अबन्धु अ-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, without kindered,<BR>without companions, friendless.<BR>—अबन्धु-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. causing want of companions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबान्धव|अबांधव
अ-बान्धव, अस्, आ, अम्, having no relation or<BR>kindered, lone, unacknowledged, unowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्य|अबन्ध्यः
अबन्ध्य अ-बन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not barren,<BR>not unfruitful, fruitful, productive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल|अबलं|अबलः
अबल अ-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, weak, feeble, in-<BR>firm; (अस्), m., N. of a plant, Tapia Cratæva; N. of<BR>a king of Magadha; (आ), f. a woman; one of the<BR>ten Buddhist earths; (अम्), n. want of strength,<BR>weakness [with अबल have been compared, Goth.<BR>ubils, Them. ubila; Mod. Germ. uebel; Eng.<BR>‘evil]. — Abala-dhanvan, ā, ā, a, possessing a weak<BR>bow.<BR>—अबलाबल (˚ल-अब्˚), अस्, m. ‘neither power-<BR>ful nor powerless;’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलास
अ-बलास, अस्, आ, अम्, not consumptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलीयस्
अबलीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, weaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल्य|अबल्यं
अ-बल्य, अम्, n. weakness, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबहु
अबहु अ-बहु, उस्, उस्, or वी, उ, not many,<BR>few.<BR>—अबह्व्-अक्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, or अबह्व्-अच्,<BR>च्, च्, च्, having not more than two syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध|अबाधं|अबाधः
अबाध अ-बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, unobstructed,<BR>unrestrained; free from pain; (आ), f. segment of the<BR>base of a triangle [cf. अ-बधा under अ-बध above].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधक
अ-बाधक, अस्, ऐका, अम्, or अ-बाधित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unimpeded, unobstructed; unrefuted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध्य
अ-बाध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, improper to be opposed or<BR>pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबान्धव|अबांधव
अबान्धव अ-बान्धव. See अ-बन्धु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबालिश
अबालिश अ-बालिश, अस्, आ, अम्, not childish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबालेन्दु
अबालेन्दु अ-बालेन्दु (˚ल-इन्˚), उस्, m. full<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाह्य
अबाह्य अ-बाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not exterior,<BR>internal; without an exterior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिन्धन|अबिंधनः|अबिन्धनः
अबिन्धन अब्-इन्धन, अस्, m. ‘having (अप्)<BR>water for fuel,’ submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिभीवस्
अबिभीवस् अ-बिभीवस्, आन्, भ्युषी, अत्, or<BR>अ-बिभ्यत्, अत्, अती, अत्, Ved. fearless, confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्ध|अबुद्धः
अबुद्ध अ-बुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, unwise, foolish.<BR>—अ-बुद्ध-त्व, अम्, n. foolishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धि|अबुद्धिः
अ-बुद्धि, इस्, f. want of understanding; ignorance;<BR>stupidity; (इस्, इस्, इ), ignorant, stupid.<BR>—अ-बुद्धि-<BR>पूर्व or अ-बुद्धि-पूर्वक, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">Page0060-a+ 76</a>]<BR>preceded by intelligence; beginning with non-in-<BR>telligence; (अम्), ind. ignorantly.<BR>—अबुद्धि-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, unwise, ignorant, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्
अ-बुध्, भुत्, त्, त्, or अ-बुध, अस्, आ, अम्, stu-<BR>pid, foolish; (अस्), m. a fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्य
अ-बुध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not to be perceived;<BR>not to be awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्यमान
अ-बुध्यमान, अस् ,आ, अम्, not being awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध|अबोधः
अ-बोध, अस्, m. ignorance, stupidity; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>ignorant, stupid; puzzled, perplexed.<BR>—अ-बोध-ग-<BR>म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधनीय
अ-बोधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, unintelligible; not to<BR>be awakened or aroused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्न
अबुध्न अ-बुध्न, अम्, n., Ved. ‘having no-<BR>bottom or root,’ the air or intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ज|अब्जः
अब्ज अब्-ज, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अप् and rt. जन्),<BR>born in water; (अस्), m. the conch; the moon; the<BR>tree Barringtonia Acutangula; Dhanvantari, physician<BR>of the gods, produced at the churning of the ocean;<BR>N. of a son of Viśala; (अम्), n. a lotus; a large<BR>number of millions.<BR>—अब्ज-ज, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Brahmā (sprung at the creation from the lotus,<BR>which arose from the navel of Viṣṇu).<BR>—अब्ज-दृश्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, or अब्ज-नयन, अस्, आ, अम्, or अब्ज-नेत्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, lotus-eyed, having large fine eyes.<BR>—अब्ज-<BR>बान्धव, अस्, m. the sun (friend of the lotus).<BR>—अब्ज-भव, अस्, m. Brahmā, a Brāhman.<BR>—अब्ज-<BR>भोग, अस्, m. the root of a lotus.<BR>—अब्ज-योनि, इस्,<BR>m. epithet of Brahmā [cf. अब्ज-ज].<BR>—अब्ज-वाहन,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of Śiva, ‘carrying the moon’ on his<BR>forehead.<BR>—अब्ज-हस्त, अस्, m. the sun (represented<BR>as holding a lotus in one hand).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जा
अब्-जा, आस्, m., Ved. born in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जिनी
अब्जिनी, f. a multitude of lotus flowers.<BR>—अब्जिनी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जस्
अब्जस् अब्जस्, अस्, n. shape, beauty [cf.<BR>अप्सस्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जित्
अब्जित् अब्-जित्, त्, त्, त् (fr. अप् and rt. जि),<BR>Ved. conquering waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्द|अब्दः
अब्द अब्-द, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अप् and rt. दा),<BR>giving water; (अस्), m. a cloud; a year; the grass<BR>Cyperus Rotundus; N. of a mountain.<BR>—अब्द-तन्त्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of an astronomical work.<BR>—अब्द-वाहन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Śiva (? borne on a cloud or bearing the<BR>clouds).<BR>—अब्द-शत, अम्, n. a century.<BR>—अब्द-<BR>सहस्र, अम्, n. a thousand years.<BR>—अब्द-सार,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of camphor.<BR>—अब्दार्ध (˚द-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a half year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दया
अब्दया, ind., Ved. out of desire of giving water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दि|अब्दिः
अब्-दि, इस्, m., Ved. a cloud.<BR>—अब्दि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of clouds, giving water, im-<BR>pregnating (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दुर्ग|अब्दुर्गः
अब्दुर्ग अब्-दुर्ग, अम्, n. (see अप्), a fortress<BR>surrounded by a moat or lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्देवताक
अब्देवताक अब्-देवताक or अब्-दैवत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (see अप्), having the waters as divinities, prais-<BR>ing the waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धि|अब्धिः
अब्धि अब्-धि, इस्, m. (fr. अप् and rt. धा), a<BR>pond, lake; the ocean; sometimes used to denote the<BR>numerals 4 or (?) 7.<BR>—अब्धि-कफ, अस्, m. cuttle<BR>fish bone, being considered as the forth of the sea.<BR>—अब्धि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born in the ocean; (औ),<BR>m. the अश्विन्स्; (आ), f. spirituous liquor.<BR>—अब्धि-<BR>झष, अस्, m. a sea-fish.<BR>—अब्धि-द्वीपा, f, earth;<BR>an island surrounded by the ocean.<BR>—अब्धि-नगरी,<BR>f., N. of Dvārakā, the capital of Kriṣṇa.<BR>—अब्धि-न-<BR>वनीतक, अस्, m. the moon.<BR>—अब्धि-फेन, अस्, m.<BR>cuttle fish bone.<BR>—अब्धि-मण्डूकी, f. the pearl oyster.<BR>—अब्धि-शयम्न, अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu, sleeping<BR>on the ocean at the periods of the destruction and<BR>renovation of the world.<BR>—अब्धि-सार, अस्, m. a<BR>gem.<BR>—अब्ध्य-अग्नि, इस्, m. submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भक्ष|अब्भक्षः
अब्भक्ष अब्-भक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अप् and<BR>rt. भक्ष्), living upon water; (अस्), m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भक्षण|अब्भक्षणं
अब्-भक्षण, अम्, n. living upon water, a kind<BR>of fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भ्र|अब्भ्रं
अब्भ्र अब्-भ्र. See अभ्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मचर्य|अब्रह्मचर्य्य
अब्रह्मचर्य अ-ब्रह्मचर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>chaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मचर्यक|अब्रह्मचर्य्यकं
अ-ब्रह्म-चर्यक, अम्, n. incontinence, coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मण्य|अब्रह्मण्यं
अब्रह्मण्य अ-ब्रह्मण्य, अम्, n. act not<BR>proper for a Brāhman; an unbrahmanical or sacri-<BR>legious act; in theatrical language an exclamation,<BR>meaning ‘help!’ ‘to the rescue!’ ‘a disgraceful deed<BR>is perpetrated!’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मन्
अ-ब्रह्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. unaccompanied by de-<BR>votion or devotional hymns, wanting in knowledge<BR>or divine wisdom; separated from the Brāhmans.<BR>—अब्रह्म-ता, f., Ved. want of devotion or true<BR>divine knowledge.<BR>—अ-ब्रह्म-विद्, त्, त्, त्, not<BR>knowing Brahma or the supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्राह्मण|अब्राह्मणः
अ-ब्राह्मण, अस्, m. not a Brāhman; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), without Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्राह्मण्य|अब्राह्मण्यं
अ-ब्राह्मण्य, अम्, n. violation of sanctity, or of<BR>the duty of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रुवत्|अब्रुवन्त्
अब्रुवत् अ-ब्रुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, not speak-<BR>ing, silent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रूकृत|अब्रूकृतं
अब्रूकृत अब्रू-कृत, अम्, n. making (अब्रू)<BR>a growling; indistinctness of speech caused by shutting<BR>the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्लिङ्ग|अब्लिंगं
अब्लिङ्ग अब्-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. (see अप्), a सूक्त<BR>or verse addressed to the waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्विन्दु
अब्विन्दु अब्-विन्दु, उस्, m. (see अप्), a tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्
अभ् अभ्. See अम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्त
अभक्त 1. अ-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unbelieving,<BR>not devoted, not worshipping; not attached to, de-<BR>tached, unconnected with; not accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ति|अभक्तिः
अ-भक्ति, इस्, f. want of devotion to, want of faith,<BR>unbelief, incredulity.<BR>—अभक्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>undevoted to, unbelieving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्त
अभक्त 2. अ-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तच्छन्दस्
—अ-भक्त-च्छन्दस्, अस्, n. or अ-भक्त-रुच्,<BR>क्, f. want of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष|अभक्षः
अभक्ष अ-भक्ष, अस्, m. or अ-भक्षण,<BR>अम्, n. not eating anything, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्य|अभक्ष्यं
अ-भक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be eaten.<BR>—अ-<BR>भक्ष्य-भक्षण, अम्, n. eating of prohibited<BR>food.<BR>—अभक्ष्य-भक्षिन्, ईम्, इणी, इ, eating for-<BR>bidden food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभग
अभग अ-भग, अस्, आ, अम्, without enjoy-<BR>ment, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभग्न
अभग्न अ-भग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, unbroken,<BR>entire; uniterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभङ्गुर|अभंगुर
अ-भङ्गुर, अस्, आ, अम्, unbroken; firm; un-<BR>disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभज्यमान
अ-भज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, not being detached,<BR>associated, attended with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभद्र
अभद्र अ-भद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, not good, bad,<BR>wicked; (अम्), n. badness, sin, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभय|अभयं|अभयः
अभय अ-भय, अस्, आ, अम्, unfearful, not<BR>dangerous, secure; fearless, undaunted; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of Śiva; a son of Dharma; (आ), f. a plant, Termi-<BR>nalia Citrina; (अम्), n, absence or removal of fear,<BR>peace, safety, security; N. of a sacrificial hymn; the<BR>root of a fragrant grass, Andropogon Muricatum.<BR>—अभय-गिरि-वासिन्, ई, m. dwelling on the moun-<BR>tain of safety; N. of a division of Kātyāyana's pupils.<BR>—अभय-गिरि-विहार, अस्, m. Buddhist monastery<BR>on the Abhayagiri.<BR>—अभयङ्-कर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or अभयङ्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing peace of safety.<BR>—अभय-जात, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अभय-<BR>डिण्डिम, अस्, m. a war-drum.<BR>—अ-भय-द or<BR>अभयन्-दद or अभयम्-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>giving fearlessness or safety; (अस्), m. an Arhat of<BR>the Jainas; N. of a king, the son of Manusyu and<BR>father of Su-dhanvan.<BR>—अभय-दक्षिणा, f. promise<BR>or present of protection from danger; a gift to a<BR>Brāhman, which he may receive even from a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयदान
—अभय-दान or अभय-प्रदान, अम्, n. giv-<BR>ing assurance of safety or protection.<BR>—अभय-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. (a modern term), a written document<BR>or paper granting assurance of safety, a safe conduct.<BR>—अभय-वचन, अम्, n. or अभय-वाच्, क्, f.<BR>assurance of safety, encouragement.<BR>—अभय-सनि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. giving safety.<BR>—अभयानन्द (˚य-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभर्तृका
अभर्तृका अ-भर्तृका, f. an unmarried wo-<BR>man; a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव|अभवः
अभव अ-भव, अस्, m. non-existence; de-<BR>struction, end of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवनीय
अ-भवनीय or अ-भवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, what<BR>is not to be, what will not be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवन्मतयोग|अभवन्मतयोगः
अ-भवन्-मत-योग or अ-भवन्-मत-सम्-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. (in rhetoric) a defect in composition;<BR>want of harmony between the ideas, which are to be<BR>expressed, and the words by which they are expressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव्य
अ-भव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be, not predestined;<BR>what ought not to be, improper, inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्र
अभस्त्र अ-भस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, without bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्रका
अ-भस्त्रका or अ-भस्त्रिका or अ-भस्त्राका, f.<BR>a badly made or inferior pair of bellows. The former<BR>two are said to mean also, ‘a small woman who has<BR>no bellows.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग
अभाग अ-भाग, अस्, आ, अम् or अ-भागिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, not sharing or dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग्य
अ-भाग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unfortunate, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाव|अभावः
अभाव अ-भाव, अस्, m. non-existence, ab-<BR>sence; non-entity, negation, nullity, the seventh cate-<BR>gory in Kaṇāda's system; annihilation, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावना
अ-भावना, अम्, f. n. absence of judgment or<BR>right perception; absence of religious meditation or<BR>contemplation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावनीय|अभावनीयः
अ-भावनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be inferred or<BR>contemplated, inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावयितृ
अ-भावयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, not perceiving, not<BR>inferring, not comprehending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाविन्
अ-भाविन्, ई, इनी, इ or अ-भाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>what is not to be or will not be, not destined to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाषण|अभाषणं
अभाषण अ-भाषण, अम्, n. not speaking,<BR>silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभि
अभि अभि, ind. (a prefix to verbs and<BR>nouns, expressing) to, towards, into, over, upon.<BR>.(As a prefix to verbs of motion) it expresses the<BR>notion of moving or going towards, approaching, &c.<BR>.(As a prefix to nouns not derived from verbs) it ex-<BR>presses superiority, intensity, &c.; e. g. अभि-ताम्र,<BR>अभि-नव, q. v.<BR>. (As a separable adverb or preposition) it expresses<BR>(with acc.) to, towards, in the direction of, against;<BR>in, into, to; for, for the sake of; on account of; on,<BR>upon, with regard to; by, before, in front of; over.<BR>It may even express one after the other, severally;<BR>e. g. वृक्षम् वृक्षम् अभि, tree after tree [cf.<BR>Gr. ἀμφί Lat. ob; Zend aibi; Goth. bi; Old<BR>High Germ. bī].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक|अभिकः
अभिक, अस्, आ, अम्, lustful, libidinous; (अस्), m. a<BR>lover, a husband. Some regard this as derived from<BR>अभि-कम् [cf. अनिक].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितराम्
अभि-तराम्, अभि-तस्. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकम्
अभिकम् अभि-कम्, perf. -चकमे, -कमितुम्,<BR>to desire, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाम
अभि-काम, अस्, m. affection, desire; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>affectionate, loving, desirous, with obj. in acc. or gen.;<BR>(अम्), ind. with desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकामिक
अभि-कामिक, अस्, आ, अम्, voluntary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकम्प्|अभिकंप्
अभिकम्प् अभि-कम्प्, cl. 1. A. -कम्पते,<BR>-पितुम्, to tremble vehemently, to shake: Caus.<BR>-कम्पयति, -यितुम्, to stir, allure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्ष्|अभिकांक्ष्
अभिकाङ्क्ष् अभि-काङ्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. -काङ्क्षति,<BR>-षितुम्, to ask, request, long for, desire; to strive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षा|अभिकांक्षा
अभि-काङ्क्षा, f. longing, wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षित
अभि-काङ्क्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, longed for, wished,<BR>desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षिन्|अभिकांक्षिन्
अभि-काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, longing for, wishing,<BR>desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाल
अभिकाल अभि-काल, अस्, m., N. of a town;<BR>see Rāmāyaṇa II. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाश्
अभिकाश् अभि-काश्, Intens., Ved. -चाकशीति,<BR>-चाकश्यते, to illuminate, irradiate; to look on, to<BR>perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकुत्स्
अभिकुत्स् अभि-कुत्स्, cl. 10. P. A. -कुत्स्यति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to revile, to inveigh against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकुष्
अभिकुष् अभि-कुष्, cl. 9. P. -कुष्णाति,<BR>-कोषितुम्, to pull, to tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकूज्
अभिकूज् अभि-कूज्, cl. 1. P. -कूजति, -जितुम्,<BR>to twitter, warble, coo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृ
अभिकृ अभि-कृ cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to do with reference to or in behalf of; to procure,<BR>effect; to render, make: Desid. -चिकीर्षति, to wish<BR>to do; to long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकरण|अभिकरणं
अभि-करण, अम्, n. effecting; incantation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृति|अभिकृतिः
अभि-कृति, इस्, f., N. of a metre, containing one<BR>hundred syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृत्वन्
अभि-कृत्वन्, वा, वरि, m. f., Ved. magical; a<BR>magician, a spirit (producing diseases?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृष्
अभिकृष् अभि-कृष्, cl. 1. 6. P. A. -कर्षति,<BR>-ते, -कृषति, -ते, -कर्ष्टुम् or -क्रष्टुम्, to<BR>overpower, to pull-down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकॄ
अभिकॄ अभि-कॄ, cl. 6. P. -किरति, -करितुम्<BR>or -रीतुम्, to pour over, throw over, cover; to fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकॢप्
अभिकॢप् अभि-कॢप्, cl. 1. A. -कल्पते,<BR>-पितुम् or -प्तुम्, to be adequate to, to answer; to<BR>have the same meaning: Caus. -कल्पयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to put in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकॢप्त
अभि-कॢप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्नूय्
अभिक्नूय् अभि-क्नूय्, cl. 1. A. -क्नूयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to bemoisten, bedew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रतु
अभिक्रतु अभि-क्रतु, उस्, m., Ved. insolent,<BR>haughty (as an enemy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रन्द्|अभिक्रंद्
अभिक्रन्द् अभि-क्रन्द्, cl. 1. P. -क्रदति,<BR>-दितुम्, to shout at, roar at, to neigh or whinny at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रन्द|अभिक्रंदः|अभिक्रन्दः
अभि-क्रन्द, अस्, m. a shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रम्
अभिक्रम् अभि-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A., cl. 4. P.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमते, -क्राम्यति, -क्रमितुम्, to<BR>step or go near to, approach; to fly at, attack; to<BR>step upon; to undertake, begin: Caus. -क्रमयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रम|अभिक्रमः
अभि-क्रम, अस्, m. assault, attack; ascending,<BR>mounting; undertaking, attempt, beginning.<BR>—अभि-<BR>क्रम-नाश, अस्, m. unsuccessful effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रमण|अभिक्रमणं
अभि-क्रमण, अम्, n. or अभि-क्रान्ति, इस्, f.<BR>stepping near, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रान्त
अभि-क्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, approached; attacked,<BR>begun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रान्तिन्|अभिक्रांतिन्
अभि-क्रान्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has undertaken;<BR>conversant with (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रामम्
अभि-क्रामम्, ind. having stepped near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्री
अभिक्री अभि-क्री, cl. 9. P. A. -क्रीणाति, -णीते,<BR>-क्रेतुम्, to buy for a certain purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रुध्
अभिक्रुध् अभि-क्रुध्, cl. 4. P. -क्रुध्यति,<BR>-क्रोद्धुम्, to be angry with (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रुश्
अभिक्रुश् अभि-क्रुश्, cl. 1. P. -क्रोसति,<BR>-क्रोष्टुम्, to cry out at, call out to; to call to any<BR>one in a scolding manner; to lament with tears, to<BR>bemoan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रोशक|अभिक्रोशकः
अभि-क्रोशक, अस्, m. a reviler, one who calls<BR>out; a herald (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षत्तृ
अभिक्षत्तृ अभि-क्षत्तृ, ता, m., Ved. mur-<BR>derer, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षदा
अभिक्षदा अभि-क्षदा, f., Ved. (according<BR>to native interpretation) destroying, a destroyer. It<BR>is better, perhaps, to divide thus, अ-भिक्ष-दा, आस्,<BR>m. giving without having been asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षम्
अभिक्षम् अभि-क्षम्, cl. 1. A. -क्षमते,<BR>-क्षन्तुम्, to be gracious, propitious, to allow, to<BR>pardon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षर्
अभिक्षर् अभि-क्षर्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्षरति,<BR>-ते, -रितुम्, Ved. -रध्यै, to flow near or round,<BR>to pour on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षिप्
अभिक्षिप् अभि-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. -क्षिपति,<BR>-क्षेप्तुम्, to fling at (as the lash of a whip at a<BR>horse), to insult; to excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षिपत्
अभि-क्षिपत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिखन्
अभिखन् अभि-खन्, cl. 1. P. A. -खनति,<BR>-ते, -नितुम्, to dig up, to turn up (the soil).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्या
अभिख्या 1. अभि-ख्या, cl. 2. P., Ved. -ख्याति,<BR>-तुम्, to see, view, perceive; to cast a kind or gracious<BR>look upon any one, to be gracious: in later Sanskrit<BR>the rt. ख्या conveys the idea of telling, making<BR>known: Caus. -ख्यापयति, -यितुम्, to make known.<BR>.2. अभि-ख्या, f. look, view; splendor; beauty; fame,<BR>glory; notoriety; telling; calling, addressing; a name,<BR>appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यात
अभि-ख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, become known, mani-<BR>fested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यातृ
अभि-ख्यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. looking, super-<BR>vising, superintending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यान|अभिख्यानं
अभि-ख्यान, अम्, n. fame, glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्
अभिगम् अभि-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्-<BR>तुम्, to go near to, approach (with acc.); to follow;<BR>to meet with, to find; to cohabit, have intercourse<BR>with a woman; to undertake; to get, gain, obtain:<BR>Caus. -गमयति, -यितुम्, to cause to obtain, to<BR>cause to apprehend, to explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगच्छत्
अभि-गच्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, approaching, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगत
अभि-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, approached, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगन्तृ|अभिगंतृ
अभि-गन्तृ, ता, m. one who approaches, one who<BR>has intercourse with a woman; one who understands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम|अभिगमः
अभि-गम, अस्, m. or अभि-गमन, अम्, n. ap-<BR>proaching, visiting; sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्य
1. अभि-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be visited; accessi-<BR>ble; inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्य
2. अभि-गम्य, ind. having approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामिन्
अभि-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having intercourse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर|अभिगरः
अभिगर अभि-गर. See अभि-गॄ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्ज्
अभिगर्ज् अभि-गर्ज्, cl. 1. P. -गर्जति, -जितुम्,<BR>to roar at, to bawl at; to raise savage or ferocious cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्जन|अभिगर्जनं
अभि-गर्जन, अम्, n. ferocious roaring, uproar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

