अभिभव|अभिभवः
अभि-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, overpowering; (अस्), m.<BR>addition; prevailing, overpowering, excessive power,<BR>predominance; defeat, subjugation; disregard, disre-<BR>spect; humiliation, mortification, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवन|अभिभवनं
अभि-भवन, अम्, n. overpowering, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवनीय
अभि-भवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be overcome or<BR>surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावक
अभि-भावक, अस्, इका, अम्, or अभि-भाविन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, or अभि-भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, overpowering,<BR>surpassing, overspreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावन|अभिभावनं
अभि-भावन, अम्, n. causing to overcome, mak-<BR>ing victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभु|अभिभुः
अभि-भु, उस्, or 2. अभि-भू, ऊस्, m., Ved. one<BR>who surpasses, a superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूत|अभिभूतः
अभि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, surpassed, defeated, sub-<BR>dued, humbled; overcome, aggrieved, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभि-भूति, इस्, f. superior power, overpowering,<BR>defeating; disrepect, disgrace, humiliation; (इस्, इस्,<BR>इ), Ved. overpowering, superior.<BR>—अभिभूत्य-ओजस्,<BR>अस्, n., Ved. superior power; (आस्, आस्, अस्), having<BR>superior power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूय|अभिभूयं
अभि-भूय, अम्, n., Ved. superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूवन्
अभि-भूवन्, वा, वरी, m. f., Ved. superior,<BR>victorious over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमद्
अभिमद् अभि-मद्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -मदति,<BR>-दितुम्, to gladden, inebriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद|अभिमादः
अभि-माद, अस्, m. intoxication, inebriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद्यत्
अभि-माद्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being inebriated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद्यत्क
अभि-माद्यत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, partially intoxicated,<BR>half-drunk, stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्
अभिमन् अभि-मन्, cl. 8. A. -मनुते, -न्तुम्,<BR>to think one's self equal to, to think of self; cl. 4.<BR>A. and poet. P. -मन्यते, -ति, to assent to, approve<BR>of; to covet, desire; to consider, imagine, fancy, think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभि-मत, अस्, आ, अम्, admitted, assented to;<BR>agreed, accepted; wished, desired; honoured, re-<BR>spected; (अम्), n. desire, wish.<BR>—अभिमत-ता, f.<BR>agreeableness, desirableness; desire, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनस्
अभि-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the mind directed<BR>towards; desirous of, longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनाय
अभि-मनाय, nom. A. -नायते, -यितुम्, to be<BR>desirous of, to long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तव्य
अभि-मन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be considered; to<BR>be desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तु|अभिमंतुः|अभिमन्तुः
अभि-मन्तु, उस्, f. injuring, destroying.<BR>—अभि-<BR>मन्तोस्, ind., Ved. to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तृ|अभिमंतृ
अभि-मन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, admonishing, longing<BR>for, referring all objects to self, self-conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्यमान
अभि-मन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, conceiving, ima-<BR>gining, regarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमान|अभिमानः
अभि-मान, अस्, m. high opinion of one's self,<BR>self-conceit, pride, haughtiness, honourable feeling;<BR>consciousness; referring all objects to self (as the<BR>act of Ahaṅkāra or personality); conception, con-<BR>ceit; affection, love, desire; laying claim to; injury,<BR>hurting.<BR>—अभिमान-ता, f. pride, arrogance.<BR>—अभि-<BR>मान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, conceiving or having ideas<BR>about self; proud, arrogant.<BR>—अभिमान-शून्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, void of conceit, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानित|अभिमानितं
अभि-मानित, अम्, n. the condition of an egotist;<BR>copulation, sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभि-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, thinking of one's self, proud,<BR>self-conceited, arrogant; imagining; (ई), m., N. of<BR>a deity.<BR>—अभिमानि-ता, f. or अभिमानि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of self-conceitedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानुक
अभि-मानुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. striving to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्र्|अभिमंत्र्
अभिमन्त्र् अभि-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्र्-<BR>अयते, -यितुम्, to consecrate or accompany with<BR>Mantras or magic formulas; to address, invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रण|अभिमंत्रणं|अभिमन्त्रणं
अभि-मन्त्रण, अम्, n. calling out to, addressing,<BR>inviting; counselling; charming, consecrating; making<BR>anything sacred by a special formula, called अभि-<BR>मन्त्रण-मन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रित
अभि-मन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, consecrated, charmed;<BR>made sacred by a certain formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्थ|अभिमंथः|अभिमन्थः
अभिमन्थ अभि-मन्थ, अस्, m. ophthalmia,<BR>disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्यु|अभिमन्युः
अभिमन्यु अभि-मन्यु, उस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Manu Cākṣuṣa; of a son of Arjuna by Subhadrā;<BR>of two kings.<BR>—अभिमन्यु-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—अभिमन्यु-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर|अभिमरः
अभिमर अभि-मर, अस्, m. (rt. मृ), killing,<BR>slaughter; war, combat; treachery, danger from one's<BR>own party or friends; binding, confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्द|अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्द अभि-मर्द. See अभि-मृद्, p. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शन|अभिमर्शनं
अभिमर्शन See अभि-मृश् next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाति|अभिमातिः
अभिमाति अभि-माति, इस्, इस्, इ (rt. मा = मन्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">Page0066-a+ 72</a>]<BR>Ved. striving to injure, hurting, inimical; (इस्, इस्),<BR>m. f. striving to injure, hurting, plotting against; an<BR>enemy, foe.<BR>—अभिमाति-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. subduing<BR>enemies.<BR>—अभिमाति-षाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. conquering<BR>enemies.<BR>—अभिमाति-हन्, आ, m., Ved. striking, de-<BR>stroying one's enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमातिन्
अभि-मातिन्, ई, m., Ved. injuring; an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद|अभिमादः
अभिमाद अभि-माद. See अभि-मद् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमान|अभिमानः
अभिमान अभि-मान. See अभि-मन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाय|अभिमायः
अभिमाय अभि-माय, अस्, आ, अम्, perplexed,<BR>bewildered, stupid, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमिह्य
अभिमिह्य अभि-मिह्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मिह्),<BR>Ved. to be wetted (by urining upon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमीलित
अभिमीलित अभि-मीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, closed<BR>(as the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख अभि-मुख, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, with<BR>the face directed towards; turned towards, facing;<BR>going near, approaching; disposed to, intending to,<BR>ready for; taking one's part; nearly related to;<BR>friendly disposed; (ई), f. one of the ten earths of<BR>Buddhists; (अम्), ind. towards, in the direction of,<BR>in front or presence of, near to.<BR>—अभिमुख-ता, f.<BR>presence, proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखीकरण|अभिमुखीकरणं
अभिमुखी-करण, अम्, n. causing to turn the<BR>face towards, addressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखीभूत
अभिमुखी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being in presence<BR>of or facing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमूर्च्छित
अभिमूर्च्छित अभि-मूर्च्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, dis-<BR>tracted, utterly confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृद्
अभिमृद् अभि-मृद्, cl. 1. P. -मर्दति, -दि-<BR>तुम्, to oppress, to devastate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्ध
अभि-मर्ध, अस्, m. rubbing, friction; oppression,<BR>devastation of a country &c. by an enemy; war,<BR>battle; spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दन|अभिमर्द्दन
अभि-मर्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, oppressing; (अम्),<BR>n. oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दिन्
अभि-मर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, oppressing, one who de-<BR>vastates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृश्
अभिमृश् अभि-मृश्, cl. 6. P. -मृशति,<BR>-मर्ष्टुम् or -म्रष्टुम्, to touch, stroke, come<BR>in contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्श|अभिमर्शः
अभि-मर्श, अस्, m. or अभि-मर्शन, अम्, n.<BR>(less correctly) अभि-मर्ष, अस्, m. or अभि-मर्-<BR>षण, अम्, n. touching, contact; (अस्, आ, अम्), rub-<BR>bing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शक
अभि-मर्शक or (less correctly) अभि-मर्षक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, touching, coming in contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृष्ट
अभि-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, touched, rubbed, brought<BR>close to, grazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमेथिका
अभिमेथिका अभि-मेथिका, f. (rt. मेथ्),<BR>Ved. insulting or injurious speech; obscene expression;<BR>imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिम्लात
अभिम्लात अभि-म्लात or अभि-म्लान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (rt. म्लै), Ved. altogether withered, faded; de-<BR>cayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियज्ञगाथा
अभियज्ञगाथा अभि-यज्ञ-गाथा, f. a sacri-<BR>ficial verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिया
अभिया 1. अभि-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -तुम्, to<BR>go up to, approach, encounter, attack, assail.<BR>2. अभि-या, आस्, आस्, m. f. going up to, approaching,<BR>assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियात्
अभि-यात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत्, assailing, an assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियात
अभि-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, approached, attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाति|अभियातिः
अभि-याति, इस्, m. or अभि-यातिन्, ई, m. or अभि-<BR>यातृ, ता, m. an assailant, foe, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियान|अभियानं
अभि-यान, अम्, n. coming near, approaching, at-<BR>tacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायिन्
अभि-यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, coming near, approaching,<BR>attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाच्
अभियाच् अभि-याच्, cl. 1. A. or ep. P.<BR>-याचते, -ति, -चितुम्, to ask for, solicit, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाचन|अभियाचनं
अभि-याचन, अम्, n. or अभि-याच्ञा, f. asking for,<BR>entreaty, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाचित
अभि-याचित, अस्, आ, अम्, asked for, requested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुज्
अभियुज् 1. अभि-युज्, cl. 7. A. -युङ्क्ते,<BR>-योक्तुम्, to apply to, exert effort, make one's self<BR>ready; to encounter, attack, assail; to accuse; to hurt:<BR>Pass. -युज्यते, to be accused, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्त|अभियुक्तः
अभि-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, applied, intent on, dili-<BR>gent, absorbed in meditation, versed in; appointed;<BR>said, spoken; attacked by an enemy, assaulted, as-<BR>sailed; blamed, rebuked; (in law) charged, prose-<BR>cuted, a defendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुग्वन्
अभि-युग्वन्, आ, m., Ved. hurting, attacking; an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुज्
2. अभि-युज्, क्, f. attacking; an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुज्यमान
अभि-युज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being prosecuted<BR>(as a defendant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तव्य
अभि-योक्तव्य or अभि-योज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>reproved or rebuked; to be prosecuted, indictable;<BR>assailable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तृ
अभि-योक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, assailing, attacking; (ता),<BR>m. an enemy; a plaintiff, a claimant, a pretender, an<BR>accuser; a stronger party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोग|अभियोगः
अभि-योग, अस्, m. application; energetic effort,<BR>exertion, perseverance, learning; attack, assault, chal-<BR>lenging to fight, war, battle; (in law) a plaint, a<BR>charge, an accusation.<BR>—अभियोग-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>petition or writing of complaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगिन्
अभि-योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, intent upon, absorbed (in<BR>meditation); attacking; (ई), m. a plaintiff, a prose-<BR>cutor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोग्य
अभि-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, assailable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोजन|अभियोजनं
अभि-योजन, अम्, n., Ved. harnessing (one horse)<BR>on to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुध्
अभियुध् अभि-युध्, cl. 4. A. P. -युध्यते,<BR>-ति, -योद्धुम्, to fight against, to acquire by fight-<BR>ing, to conquer for (another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्ष्
अभिरक्ष् अभि-रक्ष्, cl. 1. P. or ep. A.<BR>-रक्षति, -ते, -षितुम्, to succour, to protect, to<BR>preserve; to govern or command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षा
अभि-रक्षा, f. universal protection, wide bene-<BR>volence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षित
अभि-रक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, protected, preserved,<BR>guarded; governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षितृ
अभि-रक्षितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, preserving, protecting,<BR>guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्ष्य
अभि-रक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be protected or go-<BR>verned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरञ्ज्|अभिरंज्
अभिरञ्ज् अभि-रञ्ज्, cl. 4. A. or Pass.<BR>-रज्यते, -रङ्क्तुम्, to be coloured, to be flushed<BR>with pleasure: Caus. P. -रञ्जयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरञ्जित
अभि-रञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, tinted, flushed, kindly<BR>affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरम्
अभिरम् अभि-रम्, cl. 1. A. -रमते, -रन्-<BR>तुम्, to delight in, to be delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरत
अभि-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased or contented with,<BR>satisfied; engaged in; attentive to; performing,<BR>practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरति|अभिरतिः
अभि-रति, इस्, f. pleasure, delighting in; occupation,<BR>practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरमण|अभिरमणं
अभि-रमण, अम्, n. delighting in, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरमणीय
अभि-रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be delighted in,<BR>delightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराम|अभिरामः
अभि-राम, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, delightful, agree-<BR>able, beautiful; an epithet of Śiva; (अम्), ind., see<BR>s. v. next col.<BR>—अभिराम-ता, f. or अभिराम-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. loveliness, beauty, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरम्भित
अभिरम्भित अभि-रम्भित, अस्, आ, अम्, ob-<BR>tained (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराज्
अभिराज् 1. अभि-राज्, cl. 1. A. -राजते,<BR>-जितुम्, to shine, be-brilliant.<BR>2. अभि-राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, reigning everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराज
अभि-राज, अस्, m., N. of a Burmese king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराष्ट्र
अभि-राष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who has gained<BR>dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराध्
अभिराध् अभि-राध्, Pass. -राध्यते, to be<BR>rendered propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरामम्
अभिरामम् अभि-रामम्, ind. referring to<BR>Rāma (see also under अभि-रम् last col.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुच्
अभिरुच् अभि-रुच्, Caus. P. -रोचयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to long for, desire, be inclined to, have a taste<BR>for, to like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचि|अभिरुचिः
अभि-रुचि, इस्, f. desire, delight, taste, relish, plea-<BR>sure; desire of fame, ambition; splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचित|अभिरुचितः
अभि-रुचित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, delighted, de-<BR>lighting in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचिर
अभि-रुचिर, अस्, आ, अम्, very pleasant, desirable<BR>or pretty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुत
अभिरुत अभि-रुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रु),<BR>sounded; cooed, vocal (as the voices of birds, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुह्
अभिरुह् अभि-रुह्, cl. 1. P. -रोहति, -रोढुम्,<BR>to ascend, mount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुह्य
अभि-रुह्य, ind. having ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप अभि-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, corresponding<BR>with; conformable to, congruous; in accordance with;<BR>pleasing, handsome, desirable, well formed, beautiful;<BR>wise, learned; (अस्), m. the moon; Śiva; Viṣṇu;<BR>Kāmadeva.<BR>—अभिरूप-पति, इस्, m. having an agree-<BR>able master (a rite) to secure such a master in the<BR>next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूपक
अभि-रूपक, अस्, आ, अम्, corresponding; pleasing,<BR>handsome; learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरोरुद
अभिरोरुद अभि-रोरुद, अस्, आ, अम् (Intens.<BR>of rt. रुद्), Ved. causing tears (of earnest desire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलक्षित
अभिलक्षित अभि-लक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, marked<BR>with signs, bearing marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलक्ष्य
अभि-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be marked or noted;<BR>(अम्), ind. towards a mark or aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलङ्घ्|अभिलंघ्
अभिलङ्घ् अभि-लङ्घ्, cl. 10. P. -लङ्घ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to jump across or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलङ्घन|अभिलंघन|अभिलंघनं
अभि-लङ्घन, अम्, n. jumping across or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलभ्
अभिलभ् अभि-लभ्, Desid. A. or poet. P.<BR>-लिप्सते, -ति, to desire to obtain, covet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलम्भन
अभि-लम्भन, अम्, n. obtaining transition (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलिप्सा
अभि-लिप्सा, f. desire of obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलष्
अभिलष् अभि-लष्, cl. 1. 4. P. -लषति,<BR>-लष्यति, -षितुम्, to desire or wish for, covet, crave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषण|अभिलषणं
अभि-लषण, अम्, n. craving after, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषणीय
अभि-लषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, desirable, to be coveted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषित
अभि-लषित, अस्, आ, अम्, desired, wished; (अम्),<BR>n. desire, wish, will, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाष|अभिलाषः
अभि-लाष or (less correctly) अभि-लास, अस्, m.<BR>desire, wish, covetousness, affection, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषक
अभि-लाषक, अस्, इका, अम्, or अभि-लाषिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, or अभि-लाषुक, अस्, आ, अम्, or (less cor-<BR>rectly) अभि-लासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wishing, desiring, de-<BR>sirous, covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाप|अभिलापः
अभिलाप अभि-लाप, अस्, m. (rt. लप्), ex-<BR>pression, word, speech; declaration of the object of<BR>a vow or religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाव|अभिलावः
अभिलाव अभि-लाव, अस्, m. (rt. लू), cutting,<BR>reaping, mowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलिखित
अभिलिखित अभि-लिखित, अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>scribed, inserted in writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलेखन
अभि-लेखन, अम्, n. writing upon, inscribing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलीन
अभिलीन अभि-लीन, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ली), ad-<BR>hering to, shrouding; embraced; embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलुप्त
अभिलुप्त अभि-लुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, disturbed,<BR>injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलुलित
अभिलुलित अभि-लुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, playful,<BR>unsteady; agitated, disturbed, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलूता
अभिलूता अभि-लूता, f. an insect, a kind of<BR>spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवच्
अभिवच् अभि-वच्, cl. 2. P. -वक्ति, -क्तुम्,<BR>to speak to, address; to tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवञ्चित
अभिवञ्चित अभि-वञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वञ्च्),<BR>cheated, deceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवत्|अभिवन्त्
अभिवत् अभि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing<BR>the word अभि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवद्
अभिवद् अभि-वद्, cl. 1. P. A. -वदति, -ते,<BR>-दितुम्, to address or salute with reverence: Caus.<BR>-वादयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to address or salute rever-<BR>entlty; to salute through another person; to play on<BR>an instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवदन|अभिवदनं
अभि-वदन, अम्, n. addressing, salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद|अभिवादः
अभि-वाद, अस्, m. reverential salutation; (for अति-<BR>वाद), opprobrious or unfriendly speech, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादक|अभिवादकः
अभि-वादक, अस्, इका, अम्, a saluter, saluting,<BR>offering salutation; civil, polite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादनम्
अभि-वादनम्, अम्, n. respectful salutation, including<BR>sometimes the name or title of the person so addressed<BR>and followed by the mention of the person's own<BR>name; salutation of a superior or elder by a junior<BR>or inferior, and especially of a teacher by his disciple;<BR>(in general it is merely lifting the joined hands to<BR>the forehead and saying अहम् अभिवादये, I salute).<BR>—अभिवादन-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, one who habitu-<BR>ally salutes, respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादयितृ
अभि-वादयितृ, ता, त्री, m. f. a respectful saluter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादित
अभि-वादित, अस्, आ, अम्, saluted respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादिन्
अभि-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, telling, enunciating, describing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद्य|अभिवाद्यः
अभि-वाद्य or अभि-वादनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>respectfully saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवन्द्|अभिवंद्
अभिवन्द् अभि-वन्द्, cl. 1. A. -वन्दते,<BR>-दितुम्, to salute respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवन्दन|अभिवंदनं
अभि-वन्दन, अम्, n. saluting respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवप्
अभिवप् अभि-वप्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -वपति,<BR>-प्तुम्, to join, come together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवयस्
