अभि-सरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going to meet, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्तृ
अभि-सर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, attacking, assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसार|अभिसारः
अभि-सार, अस्, m. attack, assault; meeting, rendez-<BR>vous; companion, follower; war, battle; a purificatory<BR>rite; going to meet a lover, an assignation, appoint-<BR>ment; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (ई), f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिका
अभि-सारिका, f. a. woman who goes to meet her<BR>lover or keeps an assignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिन्
अभि-सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going to meet, visiting,<BR>attacking; (इणी), f. a woman who keeps an assigna-<BR>tion or goes to meet her lover; N. of a species of<BR>the Triṣṭubh metre, in which two Pādas contain<BR>twelve instead of eleven syllables, and which therefore<BR>is said to approach another metre called Jagatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसार्यमाण
अभि-सार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृत्य
अभि-सृत्य, ind. having gone near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृज्
अभिसृज् अभि-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति, -स्र-<BR>ष्टुम्, to pour forth, to give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्ग|अभिसर्गः
अभि-सर्ग, अस्, m. creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्जन|अभिसर्जनं|अभिसर्ज्जन|अभिसर्ज्जनं
अभि-सर्जन, अम्, n. gift, donation; killing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृष्ट
अभि-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसेवन|अभिसेवनं
अभिसेवन अभि-सेवन, अम्, n. practising,<BR>cultivating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्कन्द|अभिस्कंदः|अभिस्कन्दः
अभिस्कन्द अभि-स्कन्द, अस्, m., Ved. as-<BR>sault; an assailant; (अम्), ind. by assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्थिरम्
अभिस्थिरम् अभि-स्थिरम्, ind. very firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्नेह|अभिस्नेहः
अभिस्नेह अभि-स्नेह, अस्, m. attachment,<BR>affection, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्फुरित
अभिस्फुरित अभि-स्फुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, ex-<BR>panded to the full (as a blossom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्मि
अभिस्मि अभि-स्मि, cl. 1. A., poet. P. -स्म-<BR>यते, -ति, -स्मेतुम्, to smile upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्यन्द|अभिस्यंदः|अभिस्यन्दः
अभिस्यन्द अभि-स्यन्द, &c. See अभि-<BR>ष्यन्द, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वयमातृण्णम्
अभिस्वयमातृण्णम् अभि-स्वयमातृण्णम्, ind.,<BR>Ved. on the brick (used in sacrifices and called) स्व-<BR>यम्-आतृण्ण (perforated in itself, i. e. full of holes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वृ
अभिस्वृ अभि-स्वृ, cl. 1. P., Ved. -स्वरति,<BR>-स्वर्तुम्, -रितुम्, to approve, praise, invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वर्
अभि-स्वर्, अर्, f., Ved. invocation; calling into<BR>(one's) presence; a hymn or song of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वर्तृ
अभि-स्वर्तृ, ता, m., Ved. invoking, praising, an<BR>invoker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहन्
अभिहन् अभि-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -तुम्, to<BR>thump at, strike, kill; to beat off, drive off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहत
अभि-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck; beaten; smitten;<BR>killed; humbled, subdued, broken down; obstructed;<BR>multiplied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहति|अभिहतिः
अभि-हति, इस्, f. striking; (in arithm.) multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहन्यमान
अभि-हन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being smitten, kill-<BR>ed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघात|अभिघातः
अभि-घात. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहव|अभिहवः
अभिहव 1. अभि-हव, अस्, m. (rt. ह्वे), in-<BR>vocation; (for 2. see under अभि-हु below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहूति|अभिहूतिः
अभि-हूति, इस्, f. invocation, worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहस्य
अभिहस्य अभि-हस्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. हस्),<BR>Ved. ridiculous, laughable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहास|अभिहासः
अभि-हास, अस्, m. jest, joke, mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित अभि-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अभि-धा,<BR>q. v.), held forth, said, declared, spoken; determined;<BR>spoken to, addressed, accosted; whispered, prompted<BR>to say; placed upon; (अस्), m., N. of a chief; (अम्),<BR>n. a name, expression, word.<BR>—अभिहित-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the state of being said or spoken; a holding forth,<BR>declaration; authority, test.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहिति|अभिहितिः
अभि-हिति, इस्, f. telling, manifesting, title. See<BR>अभि-धान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहु
अभिहु अभि-हु, cl. 3. P. -जुहोति, -होतुम्,<BR>Ved. -होतवै, to make an oblation, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहव|अभिहवः
2. अभि-हव, अस्, m. oblation, sacrifice. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहोम|अभिहोमः
अभि-होम, अस्, m. making the oblation of clarified<BR>butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहृ
अभिहृ अभि-हृ, cl. 1. P. -हरति, -हर्तुम्,<BR>to snatch away, carry off; to bring: Caus. P. -हार-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to make a sudden attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहर|अभिहरः
अभि-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying off, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरण|अभिहरणं
अभि-हरण, अम्, n. bringing near, conveying,<BR>robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरणीय
अभि-हरणीय or अभि-हर्तव्य or अभि-हार्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहर्तृ
अभि-हर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who snatches away,<BR>seizes, takes by violence; a ravisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहार|अभिहारः
अभि-हार, अस्, m. robbing, seizing anything in<BR>the owner's presence; a brisk attack; effort; arming,<BR>taking up arms; mingling together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुत्
अभिह्रुत् अभि-ह्रुत्, त्, त्, त् (rt. ह्वृ), Ved.<BR>bending, causing crookedness, acting injuriously; (त्),<BR>f. fall, defeat, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुति|अभिह्रुतिः
अभि-ह्रुति, इस्, f. causing to fall; defeat, damage,<BR>offence; offensive, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्वर|अभिह्वरः
अभि-ह्वर or अभि-ह्वार, अस्, आ, अम्, falling<BR>off; crookedness, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अभी 1. अ-भी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, without fear, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अभी 2. अभी (अभि-इ), cl. 2. P. अभ्य्-एति,<BR>-तुम्, to come near, approach; to go up to or<BR>towards (with acc.); to go along, go after; to go into,<BR>enter; to join; to go over to; to reach; to come<BR>to, to fall to one's share (with acc.); to get; to fall<BR>into: Ved. Intens. or Pass. -ईयते, to ask, request;<BR>सकाशम् or समीपम् अभी, to go near.<BR>1. अभीति, इस्, f., Ved. approach, assault. See next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत्वन्
अभीत्वन्, वा, वरी, m. f., Ved. approaching, at-<BR>tacking: also written अभीत्वर, अस्, ई, अम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यय|अभ्ययः
अभ्य्-अय. See s. v., p. 71, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक 1. अभीक, अस्, आ, अम् (= अभिक, q. v.,<BR>fr. अभि), longing after; lustful, libidinous; anxious,<BR>desirous; (अस्), m. a lover, a husband, a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक 2. अभीक, अम्, n. (fr. अभि-अच्; cf.<BR>अनूक, अपाक, प्रतीक), Ved. meeting together, close-<BR>ness, nearness; collision, combat, opposition; अभीके,<BR>ind. in the neighbourhood, at the same place or time,<BR>at the right time, just in time; in a moment, instan-<BR>taneously; (with abl.) from, out of; on account of,<BR>with regard to; from (in connection with verbs ex-<BR>pressing defending from, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक 3. अ-भीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. भी), fear-<BR>less; (अस्), m. a poet; a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्
अभीक्ष् अभीक्ष् (अभि-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A. -ईक्-<BR>षते, -षितुम्, to look towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्ण|अभीक्ष्णं
अभीक्ष्ण अभीक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (contraction<BR>of अभि-क्षण), repeated, frequent; constant, per-<BR>petual: (अम्), ind. repeatedly, again and again;<BR>perpetually, constantly; very, exceedingly; quickly.<BR>—अभीक्ष्ण-शस्, ind. repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीघात
अभीघात अभी-घात. See अभि-घात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीज्य|अभीज्यः
अभीज्य अभीज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. यज्), to be<BR>sacrificed to, one to whom sacrifice is offered: (अस्),<BR>m. a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत
अभीत अ-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, not terrified,<BR>fearless.<BR>—अभीत-वत्, ind. as one not afraid, fear-<BR>lessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीति|अभीतिः
2. अ-भीति, इस्, f. fearlessness. See last line first col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीन्ध्
अभीन्ध् अभीन्ध् (अभि-इन्ध्), cl. 7. A.<BR>-इन्द्धे, -इन्धितुम्, to surround with flames, to in-<BR>flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीद्ध
अभीद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, inflamed, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीपत्
अभीपत् अभीपत्, m. (fr. अभि and अप्;<BR>cf. अनूप), Ved. a pond or any spot in which water<BR>collects; favour (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीपतस्
अभीपतस् अभीपतस्, ind. (fr. rt. आप् with<BR>अभि), Ved. according to the event, at the right time (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सित|अभीप्सितं
अभीप्सित अभीप्सित, अस्, आ, अम् (ईप्स्, Desid.<BR>of rt. आप्; see अभ्य्-आप्), desired, wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सिन्
अभीप्सिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or अभीप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, de-<BR>sirous of obtaining, wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीम|अभीमः
अभीम अ-भीम, अस्, आ, अम्, unterrific, causing<BR>no fear; (अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमान
अभीमान अभी-मान, अस्, m. (rt. मन्),<BR>pride, &c. See अभि-मान under अभि-मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमोद|अभीमोदः
अभीमोद अभी-मोद, अस्, m. (rt. मुद्), joy.<BR>—अभीमोद-मुद् (only used in pl.), Ved. intense<BR>joy and pleasure; or अभी-मोदमुद्, excessively<BR>joyful (fr. irreg. intens. of rt. मुद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीर|अभीरः
अभीर अभीर, अस्, m. a cowherd; N. of a<BR>people; (ई), f. the language of this people; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a metre, containing four Pādas with eleven<BR>Mātrās in each Pāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरणी
अभीरणी अभीरणी, f. (rt. ईर्?), a kind of<BR>serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीराजी
अभीराजी अभीराजी, f. a kind of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अभीरु अ-भीरु, उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ, unterrific;<BR>fearless, undaunted; (उस्), m., N. of Bhairava or Śiva;<BR>(उस् or ऊस्), f., N. of a plant, Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—अभीरु-पत्त्री, f. a plant, the leaves of which are<BR>like those of the plant Abhiru (see above); the plant<BR>Abhīru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुण
अ-भीरुण, अस्, आ, अम्, unterrific, fearless, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलु
अ-भीलु, उस्, उस्, उ (for अ-भीरु), or अभीलुक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुच्
अभीरुच् अभी-रुच्. See अभि-रुचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलापलप्
अभीलापलप् अभीलाप-लप् (only used in<BR>pl.), Ved. discourse and talk; or अभी-लापलप्, talk-<BR>ing excessively, whimpering (fr. irreg. intens. of rt.<BR>लप्, cf. अभी-मोदमुद् last col.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवर्ग|अभीवर्गः
अभीवर्ग अभी-वर्ग, अस्, m. (rt. वृज्), circuit,<BR>compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवर्त|अभीवर्तः|अभीवर्त्त
अभीवर्त अभी-वर्त, अस्, m. (fr. अभि-वृत्,<BR>q. v.), Ved. existing everywhere, going towards, ap-<BR>proaching, attacking successfully; successful assault,<BR>victory; a hymn recited in attacking the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवृत्
अभी-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. abiding everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवृत
अभीवृत अभी-वृत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वृ),<BR>covered, surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशाप|अभीशापः
अभीशाप अभी-शाप, अस्, m. (rt. शप्), curse,<BR>imprecation. See अभि-शपन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशु|अभीशुः
अभीशु अभीशु or less correctly अभीषु, उस्,<BR>m. (rt. ईश् or 1. अश् with अभि?), Ved. rein, bridle; arm,<BR>finger; ray of light.<BR>—१. अभीषु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>splendid, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्
अभीष् अभीष् (अभि-इष्), cl. 6. P. अभीच्-<BR>छति, अभ्य्-एषितुम्, -ष्टुम्, to seek for, long for,<BR>endeavour to gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीच्छत्
अभीच्छत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषु|अभीषुः
अभीषु, उस्, m. attachment, love, lust, passion<BR>[cf. अभीशु above].<BR>—२. अभीषु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>attached, enamoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired; acceptable,<BR>dear, favourite, darling; optional; (आ), f. a mistress;<BR>betel.<BR>—अभीष्ट-ता, f. state of being desired.<BR>—अभीष्ट-देवता, f. beloved goddess, favourite<BR>deity.<BR>—अभीष्ट-लाभ, अस्, m. or अभीष्ट-सिद्-<BR>धि, इस्, f. the gaining a desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषङ्ग|अभीषंग|अभीषङ्गः
अभीषङ्ग अभी-षङ्ग, अस्, m. curse, im-<BR>precation. See अभि-षञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषया
अभीषया अ-भीषया, ind. (inst. case of<BR>अभीषा), fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषाह्
अभीषाह् अभी-षाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. over-<BR>powering; (ट्), f. immense power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्त|अभुक्तः
अभुक्त अ-भुक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. भुज्), un-<BR>eaten; unenjoyed, unused, unexpended; one who<BR>has not eaten, enjoyed or expended.<BR>—अभुक्त-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has not eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज्
अ-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. one who has not experi-<BR>enced or enjoyed, one who does not keep (a promise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुञ्जत्|अभुंजत्|अभुञ्जन्त्
अ-भुञ्जत्, अन्, अती, अत्, not eating; Ved. not allow-<BR>ing to enjoy; not protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न अ-भुग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, not bent,<BR>straight; well, free from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज
अभुज अ-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, armless, maimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुजिष्य
अभुजिष्य अ-भुजिष्य, अस्, आ, m. f. not a<BR>slave, not a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभू
अभू अ-भू, ऊस्, m. unborn; an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूत
अ-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, non-existent, whatever is not<BR>or has not been.<BR>—अभूत-तद्भाव, अस्, m. the<BR>coming into being of that which has not existed before.<BR>—अ-भूत-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, unprecedented.<BR>—अ-<BR>भूत-प्रादुर्भाव, अस्, m. the becoming manifest<BR>of what has not been before.<BR>—अभूत-रजस्, असस्,<BR>m. pl., N. of some deities supposed to have existed<BR>in the fifth Manvantara.<BR>—अ-भूत-शत्रु, उस्, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>having no enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूति|अभूतिः
अ-भूति, इस्, f. non-existence; want of power; poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमि|अभूमिः
अभूमि अ-भूमि, इस्, f. non-earth, anything<BR>but earth; no proper object, unfit place or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमिज
—अभूमि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in unfit or un-<BR>suitable ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूयिष्ठ
अभूयिष्ठ अ-भूयिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, few,<BR>scanty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूरि
अभूरि अ-भूरि, इस्, इस्, इ, few, some, several.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूष
अभूष अ-भूष or अ-भूषित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत
अभृत अ-भृत or अ-भृत्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not receiving hire, not hired, not paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृश|अभृशं
अभृश अ-भृश, अस्, आ, अम्, not much, little,<BR>few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अभेद अ-भेद, अस्, m. absence of difference<BR>or distinction; identity; not breaking, compactness,<BR>closeness of array; (अस्, आ, अम्), undivided, identical,<BR>alike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेदक
अ-भेदक, अस्, इका, अम्, not dividing, not dis-<BR>tinguishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्य|अभेद्यं
अ-भेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-भैदिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>not to be divided or broken or pierced; indivisible;<BR>(-यम्), n. a diamond.<BR>—अभेद्य-ता, f. indivisibility,<BR>impenetrability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तृ
अभोक्तृ अ-भोक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or अ-भोगिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, not enjoying, not using, abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तव्य
अ-भोक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be enjoyed or<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग|अभोगः
अ-भोग, अस्, m. non-enjoyment, not making use of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग्य
अ-भोग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्
अ-भोज्, क्, m., Ved. not affording enjoyment (to<BR>the gods, i. e. refusing to sacrifice).<BR>—अभोग्-घन्,<BR>आ, m., Ved. killing the stingy (who will not sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजन|अभोजनं
अ-भोजन, अम्, n. not eating, fasting, abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजित
अ-भोजित, अस्, आ, अम्, not fed, not feasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजिन्
अ-भोजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not eating, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अ-भोज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be eaten, prohibited<BR>as food, impure.<BR>—अ-भोज्यान्न (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one whose food is not allowed to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभौतिक
अभौतिक अ-भौतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, not ele-<BR>mental, not relating to or produced by the gross ele-<BR>ments, mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्नि
अभ्यग्नि अभ्य्-अग्नि, इस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Etaśa or Aitaśa; (इ), ind. towards the fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

