अभ्यर्दित|अभ्यर्द्दित
अभ्य्-अर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, distressed, oppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ध
अभ्यर्ध अभ्य्-अर्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अर्ध्<BR>for अर्द् with अभि, cf. अभ्य्-अर्ण), Ved. being on<BR>this side; proximate, near; increasing; (अम्), n. the<BR>being situated on this side, near.<BR>—अभ्यर्ध-<BR>यज्वन्, आ, m., Ved. granting gifts; increasing the<BR>worshipper's prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ष्
अभ्यर्ष् अभ्य्-अर्ष् (अभि-अर्ष्), cl. 1. P. -अर्-<BR>षति, -षितुम्, to flow near, to run near (with acc.);<BR>to cause to flow near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हणीय
अभ्यर्हणीय अभ्य्-अर्हणीय, अस्, आ, अम् (rt.<BR>अर्ह्), to be greatly honoured, venerable.<BR>—अभ्य्-<BR>अर्हणीय-ता, f. honourableness, honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हित
अभ्य्-अर्हित, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly honoured, venera-<BR>ble; fit, proper, becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यलङ्कृ
अभ्यलङ्कृ अभ्य्-अलङ्कृ (अभि-अलम्-कृ), cl.<BR>8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यलङ्कृत|अभ्यलंकृत
अभ्य्-अलङ्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकर्षण|अभ्यवकर्षणं
अभ्यवकर्षण अभ्य्-अवकर्षण, अम्, n. (rt.<BR>कृष्), extraction, drawing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकाश|अभ्यवकाशः
अभ्यवकाश अभ्य्-अवकाश, अस्, m. (rt. काश्),<BR>an open space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकॄ
अभ्यवकॄ अभ्य्-अव-कॄ (अभि-अव˚), cl. 6. P.<BR>-किरति, -करितुम्, -रीतुम्, to throw or cast on, to<BR>pour on, to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवचर्
अभ्यवचर् अभ्य्-अव-चर् (अभि-अव˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-चरति, -रितुम्, Ved. -तवे, -तवै, -रसे, -रध्यै,<BR>to press on, penetrate: Caus. -चारयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>send away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवतन्
अभ्यवतन् अभ्य्-अव-तन् (अभि-अव˚), cl. 8.<BR>P., Ved. -तनोति, -नितुम्, to extend along or to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवदान्य
अभ्यवदान्य अभ्य्-अवदान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>withholding gifts, not liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवदो
अभ्यवदो अभ्य्-अव-दो (अभि-अव˚), cl. 4. P.<BR>-द्यति, -दातुम्, to divide into pieces for any purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवधा
अभ्यवधा अभ्य्-अव-धा (अभि-अव˚), cl. 3.<BR>P. A. -दधाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to lay down on<BR>all sides, overlay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहित
अभ्य्-अवहित, अस्, आ, अम्, allayed, laid, e. g. dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवनम्
अभ्यवनम् अभ्य्-अव-नम् (अभि-अव˚), Caus.<BR>P. -नामयति, -यितुम्, to bow, incline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवनिज्
अभ्यवनिज् अभ्य्-अव-निज् (अभि-अव˚), cl. 3.<BR>P. A. -नेनेक्ति, -नेनिक्ते, -नेक्तुम्, to wipe or wash<BR>off, clean: Caus. -नेजयति, -यितुम्, to cause to wash<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवनी
अभ्यवनी अभ्य्-अव-नी (अभि-अव˚), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-नयति, -ते, -नेतुम्, to lead down, pour into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवपत्
अभ्यवपत् अभ्य्-अव-पत् (अभि-अव˚), cl. 1.<BR>P. -पतति, -तितुम्, to fly or fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवमन्
अभ्यवमन् अभ्य्-अव-मन् (अभि-अव˚), cl. 4.<BR>A. -मन्यते, -मन्तुम्, to despise, scorn, reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्द्|अभ्यवस्कंद्
अभ्यवस्कन्द् अभ्य्-अव-स्कन्द् (अभि-अव˚), cl.<BR>1. P. -स्कन्दति, -स्कन्तुम्, to jump up (or out ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्द|अभ्यवस्कंदः|अभ्यवस्कन्दः
अभ्य्-अवस्कन्द, अस्, m. or अभ्य्-अवस्कन्दन,<BR>अम्, n. impetuous assault, facing an enemy; striking<BR>so as to disable an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहृ
अभ्यवहृ अभ्य्-अव-हृ (अभि-अव˚), Caus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारयति
-हारयति, -यितुम्, to get one to oppose another; to<BR>cause one to take or eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहरण|अभ्यवहरणं
अभ्य्-अवहरण, अम्, n. throwing away or down;<BR>taking food, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार|अभ्यवहारः
अभ्य्-अवहार, अस्, m. taking food, eating, enjoy-<BR>ing; food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार्य|अभ्यवहार्य्य
अभ्य्-अवहार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, eatable, fit for eating;<BR>(अम्), n. food, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहृत|अभ्यवहृतं
अभ्य्-अवहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken (as food), de-<BR>voured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवास्
अभ्यवास् अभ्य्-अवास् (अभि-अव-अस्), cl. 4. P.<BR>-अस्यति, -सितुम्, to throw upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवे
अभ्यवे अभ्य्-अवे (अभि-अव-इ), cl. 2. P.<BR>-अवैति, -तुम्, to go down; to descend; to get an<BR>insight, to condescend; to perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवायन|अभ्यवायनं
अभ्य्-अवायन, अम्, n. going down, descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवेत
अभ्य्-अवेत, अस्, आ, अम्, descended, immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवेक्ष्
अभ्यवेक्ष् अभ्य्-अवेक्ष् (अभि-अव-ईक्ष्), cl. 1.<BR>A. -अवेक्षते, -षितुम्, to look at or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यश्
अभ्यश् अभ्य्-अश् (अभि-अश्), cl. 5. P. A. -अश्-<BR>नोति, -नुते, -अशितुम्, -अष्टुम्, to pervade, reach<BR>to, gain; to make one's self master of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यशन|अभ्यशनं
अभ्य्-अशन, अम्, n. reaching to, pervading,<BR>gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्य्-आश, अस्, m. reaching to, pervading; prox-<BR>imity, neighbourhood, result, consequence, prospect,<BR>hope of gaining; (अस्, आ, अम्), near, proximate<BR>(also written अभ्य्-आस). अभ्य्-आशम् or अभ्य्-आशे,<BR>ind. near (also written अभ्य्-आसे). अभ्याशाद्-आगत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, arrived from near at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्
अभ्यस् 1. अभ्य्-अस् (अभि-अस्), cl. 2. P. -अस्ति,<BR>to fall to one's share; to be over; to excel; to reign<BR>over, tyrannize over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्
अभ्यस् 2. अभ्य्-अस् (अभि-अस्), cl. 4. P. -अस्-<BR>यति, -असितुम्, to throw down, throw to, heap one<BR>on the other, accumulate, to shoot off at, to concen-<BR>trate one's attention in one direction; to repeat,<BR>practice, exercise; to study, read, recite; to learn by<BR>heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसन|अभ्यसनं
अभ्य्-असन, अम्, n. concentrating of the faculties<BR>of the mind in one direction; practice, exercise;<BR>repetition, study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसनीय
अभ्य्-असनीय or अभ्य्-असितव्य or अभ्य्-अस्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, to be studied, to be repeated or redupli-<BR>cated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्त|अभ्यस्तं
अभ्य्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, accumulated, practised,<BR>exercised; learnt by heart, repeated, studied; multi-<BR>plied; reduplicated in grammer; (अम्), n. the re-<BR>duplicated base of a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्यत्
अभ्य्-अस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, studying, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्य्-आस, अस्, m. repetition; practice, military<BR>practice, permanent or repeated exercise, discipline,<BR>use, habit, custom; repeated reading, reciting, study;<BR>learning by heart; education; practising archery; (in<BR>grammar) repeating twice, reduplication; the first<BR>syllable of a reduplicated radical; (in poetry) repeti-<BR>tion of the last verses of a stanza; (in arithmetic)<BR>multiplication: see also under अभ्य्-अश्.<BR>—अभ्यास-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, approached, gone near (see अभ्य्-आश<BR>above).<BR>—अभ्यास-ता, f. constant practice, use, habit.<BR>—अभ्यास-निमित्त, अम्, n. the cause of the redupli-<BR>cation in grammar.<BR>—अभ्यास-परिवर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>wandering about or near, for अभ्याश˚.<BR>—अभ्यास-<BR>योग, अस्, m. the practice of frequent and repeated<BR>meditation on any deity or on abstract spirit, re-<BR>peated recollection.<BR>—अभ्यास-व्यवाय, अस्, m. in-<BR>terval caused by the reduplication-syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासिन्
अभ्यासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, practising, repeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासे
अभ्यासे, ind. near; more correctly written अभ्याशे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूय
अभ्यसूय अभ्य्-असूय, nom. P. A. -असूयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to show indignation, to detract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूय
अभ्य्-असूय, अस्, आ, अम्, angry, vexed, impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्य्-असूयक, अस्, इका, अम्, detracting, a de-<BR>tractor, calumniator; envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूया
अभ्य्-असूया, f. detraction, envy, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमि
अभ्यस्तमि अभ्य्-अस्तम्-इ, cl. 2. P. -एति, -तुम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">Page0072-b+ 69</a>]<BR>or अभ्य्-अस्तङ्-गा, cl. 3. P. -जिगाति, -गातुम्, to go<BR>down or set (as the sun) during or with reference to<BR>(some act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमय|अभ्यस्तमयः
अभ्य्-अस्तमय, अस्, m. setting of the sun during<BR>or with reference to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमित
अभ्य्-अस्तमित, अस्, आ, अम्, one on whom the sun<BR>has gone down while asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकर्ष|अभ्याकर्षः
अभ्याकर्ष अभ्य्-आकर्ष, अस्, m. (rt. कृष्),<BR>a striking of the flat of the hand upon the breast in<BR>defiance (a practice common to wrestlers and pugilists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकाङ्क्षित|अभ्याकांक्षित|अभ्याकांक्षितं|अभ्याकाङ्क्षितं
अभ्याकाङ्क्षित अभ्य्-आकाङ्क्षित, अम्, n. a<BR>groundless complaint, a false accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकृ
अभ्याकृ अभ्य्-आ-कृ (अभि-आ˚), cl. 8. P. -क-<BR>रोति, -कर्तुम्, to draw near to one's self, attract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकारम्
अभ्य्-आकारम्, ind. by or in drawing near to one's<BR>self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याक्रम्
अभ्याक्रम् अभ्य्-आ-क्रम् (अभि-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>A., cl. 4. P. -क्रामति, -क्रमते, -क्राम्यति, -क्र-<BR>मितुम्, to step near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याक्रामम्
अभ्य्-आक्रामम्, ind. by or in stepping near or<BR>mutually, in stepping rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याक्रुश्
अभ्याक्रुश् अभ्य्-आ-क्रुश् (अभि-आ˚), cl. 1. P. -क्रो-<BR>शति, -क्रोष्टुम्, to assail with harsh language, to revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यात
अभ्याख्यात अभ्य्-आख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, accused<BR>falsely, calumniated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यान|अभ्याख्यानं
अभ्य्-आख्यान, अम्, n. a false or groundless ac-<BR>cusation, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम्
अभ्यागम् अभ्य्-आ-गम् (अभि-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-गच्छति, -गन्तुम्, to come near to, approach,<BR>visit; to come to, fall into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्य्-आगत, अस्, आ, अम्, come, arrived; (अस्), m.<BR>a guest, a visitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम|अभ्यागमः
अभ्य्-आगम, अस्, m. or अभ्य्-आगमन, अम्, n.<BR>approaching, arrival, visit, visitation; neighbourhood;<BR>arriving at or enjoying a result; rising, getting up;<BR>war, battle; encountering, striking, killing; enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागा
अभ्यागा अभ्य्-आ-गा (अभि-आ˚), cl. 3. P. -जि-<BR>गाति, -गातुम्, to come to, approach, arrive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागारिक|अभ्यागारिकः
