अभ्यायम्
अभ्यायम् अभ्य्-आ-यम् (अभि-आ˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-यच्छति, -यन्तुम्, to restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यायंसेन्य
अभ्य्-आयंसेन्य, अस्, m., Ved. to be restrained;<BR>to be made subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याया
अभ्याया अभ्य्-आ-या (अभि-आ˚), cl. 2. P. -याति,<BR>-तुम्, to come up to, attain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारभ्
अभ्यारभ् अभ्य्-आ-रभ् (अभि-आ˚), cl. 1. A. or<BR>P. -रभते, -ति, -रब्धुम्, to commence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारम्भ
अभ्य्-आरम्भ, अस्, m. beginning, commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारम्
अभ्यारम् अभ्य्-आरम्, ind. (rt. ऋ), near, at<BR>hand, by coming near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारूढ
अभ्यारूढ अभ्य्-आरूढ, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रुह्),<BR>ascended; gone up to; surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोह|अभ्यारोहः
अभ्य्-आरोह, अस्, m. or अभ्य्-आरोहण, अम्, n.<BR>going up to, ascending; transition from one place to<BR>another; progress; ascending in devotion, praying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहणीय|अभ्यारोहणीयः
