अभ्युत्क्रुष्ट
अभ्य्-उत्क्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, applauded with loud<BR>acclamations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्क्रोशन|अभ्युत्क्रोशनं
अभ्य्-उत्क्रोशन, अम्, n. loud acclamation.<BR>—अभ्य्-<BR>उत्क्रोशन-मन्त्र, अस्, m. a hymn of applause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्तॄ
अभ्युत्तॄ अभ्य्-उत्-तॄ (अभि-उद्˚), cl. 1. P., Ved.<BR>-तरति, -रितुम्, -रीतुम्, to cross over towards, pene-<BR>trate to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्था
अभ्युत्था अभ्य्-उत्-था (अभि-उद्-स्था), cl. 1.<BR>P. -तिष्ठति, -थातुम्, to rise, rise from a seat to do<BR>any one honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थान|अभ्युत्थानं
अभ्य्-उत्थान, अम्, n. rising from a seat through<BR>politeness; rising, elevation, obtaining a high position,<BR>gaining authority, dignity, respectability; sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थायिन्
अभ्य्-उत्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rising from a seat to<BR>do any one honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थित
अभ्य्-उत्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, risen, arisen, elevated,<BR>exalted.<BR>—अभ्युत्थिताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a prince descended from Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थेय
अभ्य्-उत्थेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be greeted reveren-<BR>tially, i. e. by rising from one's seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पत्
अभ्युत्पत् अभ्य्-उत्-पत् (अभि-उद्˚), cl. 1. P.<BR>-पतति, -तितुम्, to fly up to, jump up to: Caus.<BR>-पातयति, -यितुम्, to cause to fly up to (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पतन|अभ्युत्पतनं
अभ्य्-उत्पतन, अम्, n. springing or leaping against<BR>any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्सद्
अभ्युत्सद् अभ्य्-उत्-सद् (अभि-उद्˚), Caus. P.,<BR>Ved. -सादयति, -यितुम्, to destroy (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्सह्
अभ्युत्सह् अभ्य्-उत्-सह् (अभि-उद्˚), cl. 1. A.<BR>-सहते, -सहितुम्, -सोढुम्, to feel competent, to<BR>venture, to dare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्स्मि
अभ्युत्स्मि अभ्य्-उत्-स्मि (अभि-उद्˚), cl. 1. A. or<BR>poet. P. -स्मयते, -ति, -स्मेतुम्, to smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदन्
अभ्युदन् अभ्य्-उद्-अन् (अभि-उद्˚), cl. 2. P.<BR>-अनिति, -अनति, -अनितुम्, to breathe on or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदाहरण|अभ्युदाहरणं
अभ्युदाहरण अभ्य्-उदाहरण, अम्, n. (rt. हृ),<BR>an example or illustration of a thing by its reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदि
अभ्युदि अभ्य्-उद्-इ (अभि-उद्˚), cl. 2. P. -एति,<BR>-तुम्, to go up; to rise over; to happen; to engage<BR>in combat with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्य्-उदय, अस्, आ, अम्, rising; (अस्), m. the rise<BR>of luminaries (especially with reference to some other<BR>occurence), sunrise; beginning, commencing; ele-<BR>vation, increase, prosperity; happiness; good result;<BR>a festival, any religious celebration; accident, occur-<BR>rence.<BR>—अभ्युदयेष्टि (˚य-इष्˚), इस्, f., N. of a<BR>particular expiatory sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयिन्
अभ्य्-उदयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rising, arising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदित|अभ्युदितः
