अभ्यृछ्
अभ्यृछ् अभ्य्-ऋछ् (अभि-ऋछ्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-ऋच्छति, -छितुम्, to come to, to visit or afflict with;<BR>to strive against, to strive to overpower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यृञ्ज्
अभ्यृञ्ज् अभ्य्-ऋञ्ज् (अभि-ऋञ्ज्), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>-ऋञ्जति, -ते, -जितुम्, to stretch out the hand for, to<BR>hasten to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यृष्
अभ्यृष् अभ्य्-ऋष् (अभि-ऋष्), cl. 1. P. -अर्ष्-<BR>अति, -षितुम्, to flow or run towards a place; to let<BR>flow or run towards a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्ये
अभ्ये अभ्ये (अभि-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. -ऐति, -तुम्,<BR>to go near, to come to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्येत्य
अभ्य्-एत्य, ind. having approached, having come to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्येषण|अभ्येषणं
अभ्येषण 1. अभ्य्-एषण, अम्, n. (rt. 3. इष्),<BR>desiring, wishing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्येषणीय
अभ्य्-एषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्येषण|अभ्येषणं
अभ्येषण 2. अभ्य्-एषण, अम्, n. (rt. 1. इष्),<BR>going towards, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र्
अभ्र् अभ्र्, cl. 1. P. अभ्रति, अभ्रितुम्,<BR>to go; to err or wander about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र अभ्र (sometimes spelt अब्भ्र, ac-<BR>cording to the derivation अब्-भ्र, ‘water-bearer’),<BR>अम्, n. cloud; sky, atmosphere, ether, heaven;<BR>dust (?); talc, mica; gold; camphor; the ratan (Ca-<BR>lamus Rotang); Cyperus Rotundus; (in arithmetic) a<BR>cypher; [cf. Gr. ὄμβρος and Lat. imber.]<BR>—अभ्रं-<BR>लिह, अस्, आ, अम्, cloud-licking; what touches or<BR>sweeps the clouds; sky-scraper; (अस्), m. wind.<BR>—अ-<BR>भ्र-घन, अस्, आ, अम्, thickly covered with clouds.<BR>—अभ्रङ्-कष, अस्, आ, अम्, grazing (hurting) the<BR>clouds, very high; (अस्), m. air, wind, a mountain.<BR>—अभ्र-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. born from clouds,<BR>caused by vapours.<BR>—अभ्र-नाग, अस्, m. one of the<BR>elephants supporting the globe.<BR>—अभ्र-पिशाच or<BR>अभ्र-पिशाचक, अस्, m. sky-demon, N. of Rāhu, the<BR>descending node personified.<BR>—अभ्र-पुष्प, अस्, m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">Page0074-b+ 75</a>]<BR>N. of a cane, Calamus Rotang; (अम्), n. water; a<BR>flower in the clouds, castle in the air, anything im-<BR>possible.<BR>—अभ्र-प्रुष्, ट्, f., Ved. the sprinkling of<BR>the clouds, rain.<BR>—अभ्र-मांसी, f., N. of a plant,<BR>Valeriana Jaṭāmāṃsī.<BR>—अभ्र-मातङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>Airāvata, Indra's elephant.<BR>—अभ्र-माला, f. a line<BR>or succession of clouds.<BR>—अभ्र-रोह, अम्, n. Lapis<BR>Lazuli.<BR>—अभ्र-लिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, overspread with<BR>clouds.<BR>—अभ्र-वर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pouring<BR>water from the clouds.<BR>—अभ्र-वाटिक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a plant, Spondias Magnifera.<BR>—अभ्र-शिरस्, अस्,<BR>n. a head formed of the sky.<BR>—अभ्रावकाश (˚र-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. fall of rain, clouds as the only shelter.<BR>—अभ्रावकाशिक, अस्, आ, अम्, or अभ्रावकाशिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, exposed to the rain (and so doing penance),<BR>not seeking shelter from the rain, having the clouds<BR>for shelter, open to the sky.<BR>—अभ्रोत्थ (˚र-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. sky-born, i. e. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रक|अभ्रकं
अभ्रक, अम्, n. talc, mica; the same as अभ्र,<BR>q. v.<BR>—अभ्रक-भस्मन्, अ, n. calx of talc.<BR>—अ-<BR>भ्रक-सत्त्व, अम्, n. steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्राय
अभ्राय, nom. A. अभ्रायते, -यितुम्, to create<BR>clouds, make cloudy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रित
अभ्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, clouded, covered with clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिय|अभ्रियः
अभ्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or produced<BR>from clouds; (अस्), m. lightning; (अम्), n. a collec-<BR>tion of thunder-clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र्य
अभ्र्य, अस्, m. a naked ascetic, who is clothed<BR>only by the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम|अभ्रमः
अभ्रम अ-भ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, not blundering;<BR>steady, clear; (अस्), m. steadiness, composure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमु|अभ्रमुः
अ-भ्रमु, उस्, f. the female elephant of the east, the<BR>mate of Airāvata.<BR>—अभ्रमु-प्रिय or अभ्रमु-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, m. the male elephant of the east or<BR>Airāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रातृ
अभ्रातृ अ-भ्रातृ, ता, त्री, Ved. or अ-भ्रातृक,<BR>अस्, आ, or अ-भ्रातृ-मत्, आन्, अती, m. f. brotherless.<BR>—अ-भ्रातृ-हन्, हा, घ्नी, m. f., Ved. not killing<BR>a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रातृव्य
अभ्रातृव्य अ-भ्रातृव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>rival, without an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्त|अभ्रांत|अभ्रान्तः
अभ्रान्त अ-भ्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unperplexed,<BR>not mistaken or in error, clear, composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्ति|अभ्रांतिः|अभ्रान्तिः
अ-भ्रान्ति, इस्, f. absence of perplexity or error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रि|अभ्रिः
अभ्रि अभ्रि or अब्भ्रि, इस्, or अभ्री, f. (fr. rt.<BR>अभ्र्), a wooden scraper or shovel for cleaning a boat,<BR>a spatula, a spade, a pointed stick.<BR>—अभ्रि-खात,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. dug up with the above instrument, as<BR>a ploughed field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रेष|अभ्रेषः
अभ्रेष अ-भ्रेष, अस्, m. non-deviation,<BR>fitness, propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्व
अभ्व अ-भ्व, अस्, आ, अम् (etymology doubt-<BR>ful, भ्व = भव or भुव?), Ved. huge, immense,<BR>mighty; monstrous, terrible; (अस्), m. a powerful<BR>man, applied to an enemy; (अम्), n. immense power,<BR>monstrosity, the great pervading principle of the uni-<BR>verse; embarrassed state, great calamity; sultriness (?);<BR>a monster; offspring; water, a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् 1. अम्, ind. quickly, a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् 2. अम्, cl. 1. P. अमति, -मितुम्, Ved.<BR>अमिति or अमीति, to go; to go to or towards;<BR>to serve or honour; to sound: Caus. आमयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to afflict with sickness or pain from disease; to<BR>be afflicted or sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
1. अम, अस्, m., Ved. going, pressure, heavy weight,<BR>violence, strength, power, depriving of sensation, fright,<BR>terror; disease, sickness; a servant; companion; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), unripe; unfortunate (?).<BR>—अम-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. impetuous, violent, strong; powerful, bold,<BR>persevering, constant; attended by ministers, attended<BR>by diseases, possessed of self; (वत्), ind. impetuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमहत
—अम-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, injured by disease, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमहन्
—अम-हन्, हा, घ्नी, ह, destroying diseases, &c.<BR>1. अमत, अस्, m. sickness; disease; death; time.<BR>1. अमति, इस्, m. moon, time; (इस्), f., Ved. form,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">Page0074-c+ 70</a>]<BR>shape, a splendid shape; splendor, glitter; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>Ved. poor, indigent; (इस्), f. want, indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतीवन्
1. अमती-वन्, आ, m., Ved. poor, indigent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्र|अमत्रं
अमत्र, अमनि, अमविष्णु. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम 2. अम, अस्, m. (connected with अमु),<BR>this; self; (आ), f. soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा, ind., Ved. at home, in the house; with;<BR>together with; near: see also p. 75, col. 3.<BR>—अमा<BR>कृ, to take or carry with one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्
1. अमात्, ind., Ved. from near at hand, from the<BR>neighbourhood. (For 2. see p. 75, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम 3. अ-म, अस्, m. or अ-मा, f. (rt. मा),<BR>unmeasured state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
2. अ-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. of unmeasured lustre<BR>(the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल|अमंगल|अमङ्गलं|अमङ्गलः
