अमण्डित
अमण्डित अ-मण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत|अमतः
अमत 2. अ-मत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मन्), not<BR>felt, not perceptible by the mind; (for 1. अमत, see<BR>under 2. अम्.)<BR>—अमत-परार्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>compatible with the principal subject or subject-matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
अमति 3. अ-मति, इस्, f. unconsciousness,<BR>ignorance, feebleness of intellect, absence of fore-<BR>thought, knowledge or intention; (इस्, इस्, इ), evil-<BR>minded, unworthy of credit, depraved.<BR>—अमति-<BR>पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, unconscious, unintentional, without<BR>forethought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतीवन्
2. अमती-वन्, आ, m., Ved. evil-minded, weak-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्र|अमत्रं
