अमनुष्य|अमनुष्यः
अमनुष्य अ-मनुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not human,<BR>unfrequented by men; (अस्), m. not a man, a demon.<BR>—अमनुष्य-ता, f. unmanliness.<BR>—अ-मनुष्य-<BR>निषेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, not inhabited by men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोगत
अमनोगत अ-मनोगत, अस्, आ, अम्, unthought<BR>of, unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोज्ञ
अमनोज्ञ अ-मनोज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, unwelcome<BR>to the mind, disagreeable, disliked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोनीत
अमनोनीत अ-मनोनीत, अस्, आ, अम्, disap-<BR>proved; reprobate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोग|अमनोयोगः
अमनोयोग अ-मनोयोग, अस्, m. inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोगिन्
अ-मनोयोगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोहर
अमनोहर अ-मनोहर or अ-मनोरम्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or अ-मनोहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, disagreeable, dis-<BR>pleasing, unattractive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्तव्य
अमन्तव्य अ-मन्तव्य or अ-मननीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (rt. मन्), not to be regarded, inadmissible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्तु|अमंतु
अ-मन्तु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. unwise, foolish, indocile;<BR>(for अव-मन्तु), despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्र|अमंत्र
अमन्त्र अ-मन्त्र, अस्, m. not a Vedic verse<BR>or text; (अस्, आ, अम्), or अ-मन्त्रक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>unaccompanied by Vedic verses or texts; unentitled<BR>to or not knowing Vedic texts, as a Śūdra, a female,<BR>&c.<BR>—अ-मन्त्र-विद्, त्, त्, त्, not knowing the for-<BR>mulas or texts of the Veda; (त्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्द|अमंद|अमन्दः
अमन्द अ-मन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, not slow, active,<BR>violent; not stupid; not little, important; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्यमान
अमन्यमान अ-मन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>not understanding, offering no homage; not expect-<BR>ing, not being aware of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्युत
अमन्युत अ-मन्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>affected with secret anger, not bearing ill-will against<BR>a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम अ-मम, अस्, आ, अम्, without egotism,<BR>devoid of all selfish or wordly attachment or desire;<BR>(अस्), m. the twelfth Jaina saint of a future Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—अमम-ता, f. or अमम-त्व, अम्, n. disinterest-<BR>edness, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम्रि
अमम्रि अ-मम्रि, इस्, इस्, इ (rt. मृ), Ved. im-<BR>mortal, undying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर|अमरः
अमर अ-मर, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मृ), undying,<BR>immortal, imperishable; (अस्), m. a god, a deity;<BR>N. of a Marut; a plant, Euphorbia Tirucalli; another<BR>plant, Tiaridium Indicum; a species of pine; quick-<BR>silver, gold; N. of Amara-siṃha; of a mountain;<BR>mystical signification of the letter उ; the number 33,<BR>such being the number of gods according to the later<BR>mythology; (आ), f. the residence of Indra; the umbi-<BR>lical cord; the womb; a house-post; N. of several<BR>plants, Panicum Dactylon, Cocculus Cordifolius, &c.;<BR>(ई), f. the same as अमरा in many of its senses.<BR>—अ-<BR>मर-कण्टक, अम्, n. ‘peak of the immortals,’ N.<BR>of part of the Vindhya range near the source of the<BR>Soṇā and Narmadā.<BR>—अमर-कोट, अस्, m. the<BR>fortress of immortals; N. of the capital of a Rājput<BR>state.<BR>—अमर-कोष, अस्, m., N. of the Sanskrit<BR>dictionary of Amara or Amara-siṃha.<BR>—अमर-<BR>कोष-कौमुदी, f. title of a commentary on Ama-<BR>ra-siṃha's dictionary.<BR>—अमर-गण, अस्, m. the as-<BR>semblage of immortals.<BR>—अमर-चन्द्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the Bāla-bhārata.<BR>—अमर-ज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अमर-तटिनी, f. river of<BR>the gods; an epithet of the Ganges.<BR>—अमर-ता, f.<BR>or अमर-त्व, अम्, n. immortality; the condition of<BR>the gods.<BR>—अमर-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a lexico-<BR>grapher.<BR>—अमर-दारु, उस्, m., N. of a tree<BR>(Pinus Deodaru Roxb.).<BR>—अमर-देव, अस्, m. a<BR>N. of Amara-siṃha.<BR>—अमर-द्विज, अस्, m. a Brāh-<BR>man who lives by attending a temple or idol; super-<BR>intending a temple.<BR>—अमर-पति, इस्, m. the lord of<BR>the gods; an epithet of Indra.<BR>—अमर-पुर, अम्,<BR>n. the residence of the immortals, paradise; N. of vari-<BR>ous towns.<BR>—अमर-पुष्प or अमर-पुष्पक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of several plants; a kind of grass, Saccha-<BR>rum Spontaneum, Pandanus Odoratissimus, Magni-<BR>fera Indica.<BR>—अमर-पुष्पिका, f. a kind of anise,<BR>Anethum Sowa Roxb.<BR>—अमर-प्रख्य or अमर-<BR>प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like an immortal.<BR>—अमर-<BR>प्रभु, उस्, m. ‘lord of the immortals,’ one of the<BR>thousand names of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अमर-भर्तृ, ता,<BR>m. lord of the gods; an epithet of Indra.<BR>—अमर-<BR>माला, f. title of a dictionary, said to be by the same<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">Page0075-b+ 75</a>]<BR>author as the Amara-koṣa.<BR>—अमर-रत्न, अम्,<BR>n. crystal.<BR>—अमर-राज, अस्, m. king of the gods;<BR>an epithet of Indra.<BR>—अमरराज-शत्रु, उस्, m. an<BR>enemy of the king of the gods; an epithet of Rā-<BR>vaṇa.<BR>—अमर-लोक, अस्, m. the abode of the gods,<BR>heaven.<BR>—अमरलोक-ता, f. the bliss of heaven.<BR>—अमर-वत्, ind. like an immortal.<BR>—अमर-<BR>वल्लरी, f., N. of a plant, Cassyta Filiformis Lin.<BR>—अमर-शक्ति, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—अमर-<BR>सरित्, त्, f. the river of the gods; epithet of the<BR>Ganges.<BR>—अमर-सिंह, अस्, m. ‘god-lion,’ N. of a<BR>renowned lexicographer; he was a Buddhist, and is<BR>supposed to have adorned the court of Vikramāditya,<BR>being included among the nine gems.<BR>—अमर-स्त्री,<BR>f. an Apsaras or nymph of heaven.<BR>—अमराचार्य<BR>(˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m. Vṛhaspati, teacher of the gods.<BR>—अमराङ्गना (˚र-अङ्ग्˚), f. a nymph of Indra's<BR>heaven.<BR>—अमराद्रि (˚र-अद्˚), इस् m. the mountain<BR>of the gods; an epithet of the mount Sumeru or<BR>Meru.<BR>—अमराधिप (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m. lord of<BR>the gods; an epithet of Indra.<BR>—अमरापगा (˚र-<BR>अप्˚), f. the river of the gods; an epithet of the<BR>Ganges.<BR>—अमरेज्य (˚र-इज्˚), अस्, m., N. of Vṛhaspati.<BR>—अमरेश (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m. lord of the gods; an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva or Indra.<BR>—अमरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu, Śiva, or Indra.<BR>—अमरोत्तम<BR>(˚र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, best of the immortals.<BR>—अ-<BR>मरोपम (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, like an immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरण|अमरणं
अ-मरण, अम्, n. the not dying, immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणीय
अ-मरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, immortal.<BR>—अमरणीय-<BR>ता, f. immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरावती
अमरा-वती, f. the abode of the immortals, resi-<BR>dence of Indra; N. of a town in Berar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरिष्णु
अ-मरिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त|अमर्त्त
अ-मर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्य|अमर्त्यः
अ-मर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, immortal, imperishable, di-<BR>vine; (अस्), m. god.<BR>—अमर्त्य-ता or अमर्त्य-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. immortality.<BR>—अमर्त्य-भुवन, अम्, n.<BR>the world of the immortals, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरु|अमरुः
अमरु अमरु, उस्, m., N. of a king, the<BR>author of the अमरु-शतक, अम्, n. or the hundred<BR>verses of Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरुत
अमरुत अ-मरुत, अस्, आ, अम्, without wind,<BR>calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्दित|अमर्द्दित
अमर्दित अ-मर्दित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मृद्), un-<BR>threshed, unsubdued, not trodden down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्धत्|अमर्धन्त्
अमर्धत् अ-मर्धत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. not<BR>injuring; indefatigable (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्मन्
अमर्मन् अ-मर्मन्, आ, m., Ved. not a vital<BR>part of the body, without a joint, having no joint,<BR>having no vital part.<BR>—अ-मर्म-जात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not produced in a vital organ.<BR>—अ-मर्म-वेधिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, not injuring vital organs, mild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्याद|अमर्य्याद
अमर्याद अ-मर्याद, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>limits, transgressing every bound; (आ), f. the transgress-<BR>ing or overstepping due bounds; disrepect, impropriety<BR>of conduct; violation of decorum or due reverence;<BR>forwardness or pertness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्ष|अमर्षः
अमर्ष अ-मर्ष, अस्, m. (rt. मृष्), non-<BR>endurance; impatience; impetuosity, determination<BR>of purpose; anger, passion; (अस्, आ, अम्), unenduring,<BR>not bearing; (अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—अमर्ष-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, springing from impatience or indig-<BR>nation.<BR>—अमर्ष-हास, अस्, m. an angry laugh, a<BR>sarcastic sneer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षण|अमर्षणः
अ-मर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, or अमर्ष-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, or अ-मर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-मर्षिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, not suffering, not bearing; impatient, in-<BR>tolerant; passionate, wrathful, angry, impetuous, de-<BR>termined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमल|अमलं
अमल अ-मल, अस्, आ, अम्, spotless, stainless,<BR>clean, pure, shining, white; (आ), f., N. of the goddess<BR>Lakṣmī; the umbilical cord; N. of a tree, Emblica<BR>Officinalis Gærtn.; N. of a plant; (अम्), n. purity;<BR>the supreme spirit; talc.<BR>—अ-मल-गर्भ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—अमल-पतत्रिन्, ई, इणी, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">Page0075-c+ 69</a>]<BR>f. the wild goose.<BR>—अमल-रत्न, अम्, n. or अमल-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. f. crystal.<BR>—अमलात्मन् (˚ल-आत्˚), आ,<BR>आ, अ, of undefiled mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलय
अमलय, nom. P. अमलयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>spotless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलिन
अ-मलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, stainless, free from dirt,<BR>clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलानक|अमलानकं
अमलानक अमलानक, अम्, n. globe-ama-<BR>ranth (Gomphræna Globosa). See अमिलातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमवत्|अमवन्त्
अमवत् अम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्. See under<BR>1. अम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमविष्णु
अमविष्णु अमविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. अम्),<BR>going in different directions, up and down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस|अमसः
अमस, अस्, m. disease; stupidity, a fool, time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसृण
अमसृण अ-मसृण, अस्, आ, अम्, not soft,<BR>harsh, hard; violent, intense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस्तक
अमस्तक अ-मस्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस्तु
अमस्तु अ-मस्तु, n. curds. See मस्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा 1. अमा, f. day of conjunction of sun<BR>and moon or new moon; see अमा-वसी, p. 76, col. 1.<BR>—अमान्त (अमा-अन्त), अस्, m. the end of the day<BR>of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा 2. अमा, ind. at home, in the house;<BR>see also under 2. अम, p. 74.<BR>—अमाक्त (अमा-अक्त),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. met, come together.<BR>—अमा-जुर्,<BR>ऊर्, f., Ved. living at home during life, growing<BR>old at home; being without husband in the same<BR>dwelling with her parents (as a maiden).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांस|अमांसः
अमांस अ-मांस, अम्, n. not flesh, anything<BR>but flesh; (अस्, आ, अम्), without flesh, feeble, thin.<BR>—अ-मांसौदनिक (˚स-ओद्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, not re-<BR>lating to a preparation of rice with meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्
अमात् 2. अ-मात्, आन्, आति or आन्ति, आत्, not<BR>measuring. (For 1. see p. 74, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृक
अमातृक अ-मातृक, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>mother, motherless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातापुत्र
अ-माता-पुत्र, अस्, m. having neither mother nor<BR>son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृभोगीण
अ-मातृभोगीण, अस्, आ, अम्, not fit for the use<BR>of a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्य|अमात्यः
अमात्य अमात्य, अस्, m. (fr. 2. अमा above),<BR>inmate of the same house, belonging to the same<BR>house or family; a companion, follower, counsellor,<BR>minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्र|अमात्रः
अमात्र अ-मात्र, अम्, n. non-measure, not<BR>a measure or quantity (said of the universal spirit);<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), boundless; not whole or entire; not<BR>elementary; having the measure or quantity of the<BR>letter अ.<BR>—अमात्रवत्-त्व, अम्, n. deficiency, defect;<BR>spirit, spiritual essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानन|अमाननं
अमानन अ-मानन, अम्, n. disrespect, con-<BR>tempt, disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानव
अमानव अ-मानव, अस्, आ, अम्, not human,<BR>animal; superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानस्य|अमानस्यं
अमानस्य अ-मानस्य, अम्, n. pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिता
अमानिता अ-मानिता, f. or अ-मानित्व, अम्,<BR>n. (rt. मन्), modesty, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिन्
अ-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, humble, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमान्य|अमान्यः
अ-मान्य or अ-मानितव्य or अ-माननीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, to be disrepected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष|अमानुषः
अमानुष अ-मानुष, अस्, ई, अम्, not human,<BR>anything but man; supernatural, inhuman, a monster;<BR>not well disposed towards man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष्य
अ-मानुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not human, super-<BR>human, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामसी
अमामसी अमा-मसी or अमा-मासी for अमा-<BR>वसी, p. 76, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाय
अमाय अ-माय, अस्, आ, अम्, not cunning,<BR>not sagacious; free from error or deceit, guileless,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">Page0076-a+ 73</a>]<BR>sincere; (आ), f. absence of delusion, deceit, or guile;<BR>knowledge of the truth; sincerity, honesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिक|अमायिकः
अ-मायिक, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-मायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>without illusion or deceit, void of trick or guile; true,<BR>honest; real.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार|अमारः
अमार अ-मार, अस्, m. not dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ग|अमार्गः
अमार्ग अ-मार्ग, अस्, m. want of a road;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), pathless, without a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्गित
अमार्गित अ-मार्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, unsought,<BR>not hunted after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्जित|अमार्ज्जित
अमार्जित अ-मार्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, uncleansed,<BR>unwashed, unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसु|अमावसुः
अमावसु अमा-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Purūravas, of a son of Kuśa and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्या
अमावास्या अमा-वास्या, f. (fr. rt. वस्, ‘to<BR>dwell,’ with अमा, ‘together,’ i. e. रात्रि, night of new<BR>moon), the first day of the first quarter on which the<BR>moon is invisible; a sacrifice offered at that time; the<BR>sacrificial cake ?; (अस्, आ, अम्), or अमा-वास्यक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced in a night of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसी
अमा-वसी or अमा-वस्या or अमा-वासी, f. the night<BR>of new moon; that night during which the moon<BR>dwells together with or in the same quarter as the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाष
अमाष अ-माष, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-माषक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, having no kidney-beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित
अमित 1. अमित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अम्), gone,<BR>served, honoured, sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित
अमित 2. अ-मित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मा), un-<BR>measured, boundless, infinite; without a certain<BR>measure; neglected; unpolished, unclean.<BR>—अमित-<BR>क्रतु, उस्, m., Ved. of unbounded wisdom; of un-<BR>bounded energy.<BR>—अमित-गति, इस्, m., N. of a Jaina<BR>author.<BR>—अमित-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, of boundless<BR>glory.<BR>—अमित-द्युति, इस्, इस्, इ, of infinite splendor.<BR>—अमित-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dharma-<BR>dhvaja.<BR>—अमित-विक्रम, अस्, m. of unbounded<BR>valour, a N. of Visḥu.<BR>—अमित-वीर्य, अस्, m. of<BR>immense strength.<BR>—अमिताक्षर (˚त-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, not containing a fixed number of syllables,<BR>unbound, prosaic.<BR>—अमिताभ (˚त-आभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of unmeasured splendour; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>deity; N. of a Dhyāni-buddha.<BR>—अमितायुस् (˚त-<BR>आय्˚), उस्, m., N. of a Dhyāni-buddha.<BR>—अमितौजस्<BR>(˚त-ओज्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, of unbounded energy, all-power-<BR>ful, almighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्र|अमित्रः
अमित्र अ-मित्र, अस्, आ, m. f. not a friend,<BR>an enemy, adversary, foe. (According to some au-<BR>thorities this is not derived from अ and मित्र, a<BR>friend, but fr. rt. अम्, ‘to attack.’)<BR>—अमित्र-खाद,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. swallowing or devouring his enemies;<BR>an epithet of Indra.<BR>—अमित्र-गण-सूदन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, destroying the hosts of one's enemies.<BR>—अ-<BR>मित्र-घात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. killing enemies;<BR>(अस्), m. a N. of Vindusāra, the son of Candragupta.<BR>—अमित्र-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or अमित्र-घ्न, अस्,<BR>आ or ई, अम्, the same as the preceding.<BR>—अमित्र-<BR>जित्, त्, m. conquering one's enemies; a son of Suvarṇa.<BR>—अमित्र-ता, f. enmity.<BR>—अमित्र-दम्भन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. hurting enemies.<BR>—अमित्र-साह, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. enduring or overcoming enemies; epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—अमित्र-सेना, f. hostile arrow.<BR>—अमित्र-<BR>हन्, आ, m., Ved. killing enemies.<BR>—अमित्रा-युध्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. subduing one's enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रय
अमित्रय or अमित्राय, nom. अमित्रयति, -त्रा-<BR>यते, -यितुम्, to act like an enemy, have hostile<BR>intentions, to hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रिन्
अ-मित्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, hostile, an adversary, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रिय
अ-मित्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-मित्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>hostile; inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिथित
अमिथित अ-मिथित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not re-<BR>viled; unprovoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिथ्या
अमिथ्या अ-मिथ्या, ind. not falsely, truth-<BR>fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन्
अमिन् अमिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. अम, see अम्),<BR>sick, diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन
1. अमिन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.rt. अम्), Ved. going every-<BR>where, violent, tempestuous (?); loved by all (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन
अमिन 2. अ-मिन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unmea-<BR>sured, unparalleled, inviolable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिनत्|अमिनन्त्
अमिनत् अ-मिनत्, अन्, अती, अत् (rt. मी), Ved.<BR>not hurting; unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिलातक|अमिलातकं
अमिलातक अमिलातक, अम्, n. globe-ama-<BR>ranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्र
अमिश्र अ-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, unmixed, un-<BR>mixing; without participation of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रणीय
अ-मिश्रणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, immiscible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रित
अ-मिश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, unmixed, unblended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिष|अमिषं
अमिष 1. अमिष, अम्, n. luxury, object of<BR>enjoyment, flesh. See आमिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिष|अमिषं
अमिष 2. अ-मिष, अम्, n. honesty, simpli-<BR>city, absence of fraud; dishonesty (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीतवर्ण
अमीतवर्ण अ-मीत-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (मीत<BR>fr. rt. मी), Ved. of infinite hue; of unhurt or unex-<BR>tinguishable colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीमांसा
अमीमांसा अ-मीमांसा, f. (rt. मन्), absence<BR>of reasoning or investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीमांस्य
अ-मीमांस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be reasoned about<BR>or discussed, not to be demonstrated by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीवा
अमीवा अमीवा, f. (fr. rt. अम्), pain, distress,<BR>terror, fright; tormenting spirit, demon; affliction,<BR>disease; (अस्), m. an enemy, one who afflicts; (अम्),<BR>n. affliction, pain, grief.<BR>—अमीव-चातन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. driving away pains, diseases, enemies, or tor-<BR>menting spirits.<BR>—अमीव-हन्, आ, m., Ved. killing<BR>evil spirits, destroying pains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमु
अमु अमु, a pronominal base, used in the<BR>declension of the pronom. अदस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक|अमुकं
अमुक, अस्, आ, अम्, a certain person or thing, any-<BR>thing or person referred to without a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुतस्
अमुतस्, ind. from there, there; from that place,<BR>from above, i. e. from the other world, from heaven;<BR>hereupon, upon this; henceforth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्र
अमुत्र, ind. there; there, i. e. in what precedes<BR>or has been said; there above, i. e. in the other world,<BR>in the life to come; here.<BR>—अमुत्र-भूय, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. being there above or in the other world;<BR>dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्रत्य
अमुत्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a future state,<BR>being of the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुथा
अमुथा, ind. thus, in that manner, like that;<BR>अमुथा अस्, to be thus, a euphemistic expression used<BR>in the sense of, to fare very ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुया
अमुया, ind., Ved. in that manner, thus or thus;<BR>(with rt. अस् or भू) to be thus; to be gone, to be<BR>lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुर्हि
अमुर्हि, ind. at that time, then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुवत्
अमु-वत्, ind. like a person or thing referred to<BR>without name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्मिन्
अमुष्मिन् (loc. sing. of अदस्), in the other world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्य
अमुष्य (gen. sing. of अदस्), of such a one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यकुल
—अमुष्य-कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>family of such a one.<BR>—अमुष्य-पुत्र, अस्, ई, m.<BR>f. the son or daughter of such a one; of a good family,<BR>of known origin.<BR>—अमुष्यायण (˚य-अय्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, m. f. offspring of such a one; of respectable birth,<BR>of known origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश्
अमू-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, or अमू-दृश, or अमू-दृक्-<BR>ष, अस्, आ, अम्, like that, such like, such a one, of<BR>such form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्त|अमुक्तं
अमुक्त अ-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not loosed, not<BR>let go; not liberated from birth and death; (अम्),<BR>n. a weapon that is always grasped and not thrown,<BR>as a knife, a sword, &c.<BR>—अमुक्त-हस्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one whose hand is not open (to give); sparing;<BR>stingy; frugal, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्ति|अमुक्तिः
अ-मुक्ति, इस्, f. non-liberation; want of freedom<BR>or liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुच्
अ-मुच्, क्, f., Ved. non-liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुची
अ-मुची, f., Ved. not unbinding, not setting at<BR>liberty (epithet of an evil spirit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुख
अमुख अ-मुख, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुख्य
अ-मुख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not chief, inferior, or-<BR>dinary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुग्ध
अमुग्ध अ-मुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not con-<BR>founded, not perplexed, not foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूढ
अमूढ अ-मूढ, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मुह्), not<BR>infatuated, wise; not perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर
अमूर अ-मूर, अस्, आ, अम् (for अ-मूढ, q. v.),<BR>Ved. without error or mistake, infallible, not ignorant,<BR>not bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त|अमूर्तः|अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त्तः
अमूर्त अ-मूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, formless, shape-<BR>less, incorporeal, unembodied; (अस्), m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—अमूर्त-रजस्, आस्, or अमूर्त-रजस, अस्, m.<BR>a son of Kūśa by Vaidarbhī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्ति|अमूर्तिः|अमूर्त्ति
अ-मूर्ति, इस्, f. shapelessness, absence of shape or<BR>form; (इस्, इस्, इ), formless; (इस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>(-अयस्), m. pl. a class of Manes, who have no defi-<BR>nite form.<BR>—अमूर्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, formless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल
अमूल अ-मूल or अ-मूलक, अस्, आ, अम्, root-<BR>less, baseless; without support; without authority;<BR>without material cause or origin; not fixed in the<BR>earth; having locomotive powers; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>plant, Methonica Superba Lam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्य
अमूल्य अ-मूल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, invaluable, not<BR>to be purchased, priceless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृक्त
अमृक्त अ-मृक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unhurt,<BR>unharmed, safe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृणाल|अमृणालं
अमृणाल अ-मृणाल, अम्, n. the root of a<BR>fragrant grass, used for taties or screens, &c., com-<BR>monly called Kaskas, Andropogon Muricatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत अ-मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not dead; im-<BR>mortal, imperishable, causing immortality; beautiful,<BR>beloved, desired; (अस्), m. a god, an immortal; N.<BR>of Indra, of the sun, of Prajāpati, of the soul, of Viṣṇu,<BR>of Śiva, of Dhanvantari as physician of the gods, &c.;<BR>N. of a plant, Phaseolus Trilobus Ait.; N. of the root<BR>of a plant; (आ), f. spirituous liquor; N. of several<BR>plants, Emblica Officinalis, Terminalia Citrina Roxb.,<BR>Cocculus Cordifolius, Piper Longum, Ocymum Sanc-<BR>tum, &c.; N. of the mother of Parīkṣit; (अम्), n.<BR>immortality; the collective body of immortals; the<BR>world of immortality, heaven, paradise, eternity; the<BR>immortal light; the nectar conferring immortality,<BR>ambrosia; the Soma juice; antidote against poison; a<BR>drug; the residue of a sacrifice; unsolicited alms;<BR>water; clarified butter; milk; food; boiled rice; any-<BR>thing sweet, a sweetmeat; property; gold, quick-<BR>silver; poison; splendour; final emancipation; N. of a<BR>sacred place; N. of various conjunctions of planets sup-<BR>posed to confer long life; the number ‘four.’<BR>—अमृ-<BR>त-कुण्ड, अम्, n. the vessel containing the Amṛta<BR>or nectar.<BR>—अमृत-केशव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>temple, built by Amṛta-prabhā.<BR>—अमृत-क्षार,<BR>अम्, n. sal ammoniac.<BR>—अमृत-गति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>a metre consisting of four times ten syllables.<BR>—अ-<BR>मृत-गर्भ, अस्, m., Ved. the immortal fetus, i. e.<BR>sleep; (अस्, आ, अम्), filled with nectar.<BR>—अमृत-चिति,<BR>इस्, f. the accumulation or arrangement of sacrificial<BR>bricks conferring immortality.<BR>—अमृत-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced by the Amṛta; (आ), f., N. of a plant,<BR>Yellow Myrobalan.<BR>—अमृत-जटा, f., N. of a<BR>plant, Valeriana Jaṭāmāṃsī.<BR>—अमृत-तरङ्गिणी, f.<BR>moonlight.<BR>—अमृत-ता, f. or अमृत-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>immortality.<BR>—अमृत-दीधिति or अमृत-द्युति,<BR>इस्, m. the moon.<BR>—अमृत-द्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, shed-<BR>ding ambrosia.<BR>—अमृत-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, shed-<BR>ding or distilling ambrosia; (आ), f., N. of a metre.<BR>—अमृत-नादोपनिषद् (˚द-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an<BR>Upaniṣed, lit. ‘the sound of immortality.’<BR>—अमृत-<BR>प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking nectar; (अस्), m. a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतपक्ष|अमृतपक्षः
—अमृत-पक्ष, अस्, m. the immortal or golden<BR>wing (of sacrificial fire); having immortal or golden<BR>wings.<BR>—अमृत-प्रभा, f., N. of several women.<BR>—अमृत-फल, अस्, अम्, m. n., N. of a plant, Tri-<BR>chosanthes Diœca, Roxb.; (आ), f. a bunch of grapes;<BR>the plant Emblica Officinalis Gærtn.<BR>—अमृत-<BR>बन्धु, उस्, m., Ved. friend of immortality, keeper<BR>of immortality; a horse (so called because a horse was<BR>produced in the ocean along with the Amṛta).<BR>—अमृ-<BR>त-भवन, अम्, n., N. of a monastery.<BR>—अमृत-<BR>भुज्, क्, m. an immortal, a deity.<BR>—अमृत-भू, ऊस्,<BR>ऊस्, उ, free from birth and death.<BR>—अमृत-मति, इस्,<BR>f., N. of the metre Amṛtangati.<BR>—अमृत-मन्थन,<BR>अम्, n. the churning for the Amṛta.<BR>—अमृत-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, immortal; consisting of or full of Amṛta.<BR>—अमृतमालिनि, f., N. of Durgā.<BR>—अमृत-रस,<BR>अस्, m. nectar, ambrosia; (आ), f. dark-coloured grapes.<BR>—अमृत-लता or अमृत-लतिका, f. a nectar-giving<BR>creeping plant.<BR>—अमृत-वपुस्, उस्, m. of immortal<BR>form, Śiva.<BR>—अमृत-वर्ष, अस्, m. a shower of nec-<BR>tar.<BR>—अमृत-वल्लरी or अमृत-वल्ली, f. a creep-<BR>ing plant, Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—अमृत-वाका, f. a<BR>kind of bird.<BR>—अमृत-विन्दूपनिषद् (˚दु-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f., N. of an Upaniṣad of the Atharva-veda, lit. ‘drop<BR>of nectar.’<BR>—अमृत-सम्भवा, f. a creeping plant,<BR>Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—अमृत-सार, अस्, m. essence<BR>of ambrosia.<BR>—अमृतसार-ज, अस्, m. raw sugar,<BR>molasses.<BR>—अमृत-सू, ऊस्, m. the moon (as distilling<BR>nectar).<BR>—अमृत-सोदर, अस्, m. a horse, lit. ‘bro-<BR>ther of nectar,’ born together with the Amṛta at the<BR>churning of the ocean.<BR>—अमृत-स्रवा, f., N. of a<BR>plant and tree.<BR>—अमृत-स्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, shedding nec-<BR>tar.<BR>—अमृताकर (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘a mine of<BR>nectar;’ N. of a man.<BR>—अमृताक्षर (˚त-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, immortal and imperishable.<BR>—अमृता-<BR>नन्द (˚त-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अमृतान्-<BR>धस् (˚त-अन्˚), आस्, m. a deity, whose food is ambrosia.<BR>—अमृता-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of the Tricho-<BR>santhes.<BR>—अमृताश, (˚त-आश), अस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अमृताशन (˚त-अश्˚), अस् or अमृताशिन् (˚त-आश्˚),<BR>ई, m. eating ambrosia; a deity.<BR>—अमृतासङ्ग (˚त-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. a collyrium, extracted from the Amo-<BR>mum Anthoriza.<BR>—अमृतासु (˚त-असु), उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>whose soul is immortal.<BR>—अमृताहरण (˚त-आह्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu, who upon<BR>one occasion stole the Amṛta.<BR>—अमृताह्व (˚त-<BR>आह्˚), अम्, n. a kind of fruit.<BR>—अमृतेश or अमृ-<BR>तेश्वर (˚त-ईश्˚), अस्, m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—अमृते-<BR>शय, अस्, m. sleeping on the Amṛta, epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अमृतेष्टका (˚त-इष्˚), f. a kind of sacrificial<BR>brick, shaped like golden heads (of men, animals,<BR>&c.).<BR>—अमृतोत्पत्ति (˚त-उत्˚), इस्, f. the production<BR>of the Amṛta.<BR>—अमृतोत्पन्ना (˚त-उत्˚), f. a fly;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of collyrium.<BR>—अमृतोदन (˚त-<BR>ओद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of Siṃhahanu.<BR>—अमृतोद्-<BR>भव (˚त-उद्˚), अम्, n. a kind of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतक|अमृतकं
अमृतक, अम्, n. the nectar of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताय
अमृताय, nom. A. अमृतायते, -यितुम्, to be<BR>like nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्यु|अमृत्युः
अमृत्यु अ-मृत्यु, उस्, m. not death, im-<BR>mortality; (उस्, उस्, उ), immortal, causing immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृध्र
अमृध्र अ-मृध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. uninjured,<BR>not to be impaired, invulnerable; unremitting, un-<BR>ceasing, indefatigable (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृषा
अमृषा अ-मृषा, ind. not falsely, certainly,<BR>surely; rightly.<BR>—अमृषा-बाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speak-<BR>ing truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्ट
अमृष्ट अ-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मृज्), not<BR>rubbed.<BR>—अमृष्ट-मृज, अस्, आ, अम्, of unim-<BR>paired purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्य
अमृष्य अ-मृष्य, अस्, आ, अम् unbearable,<BR>insufferable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्यमाण
अ-मृष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, not enduring, not<BR>bearing or tolerating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेक्षण
अमेक्षण अ-मेक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>मेक्षण or mixing-instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेघ
अमेघ अ-मेघ, अस्, आ, अम्, cloudless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेदस्क
अमेदस्क अ-मेदस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, without fat,<BR>lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेधस्
अमेधस् अ-मेधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, foolish; an<BR>idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्य|अमेध्यं
अमेध्य अ-मेध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not able or not<BR>allowed to sacrifice, not fit for sacrifice, impure, un-<BR>holy, nefarious, foul; (अम्), n. fæces, excrement; an<BR>unlucky omen.<BR>—अमेध्य-कुणपाशिन् (˚प-आश्˚),<BR>ई, इनी, इ, feeding on carrion.<BR>—अमेध्य-ता, f. or<BR>अमेध्य-त्व, अम्, n. impurity, foulness, filthiness.<BR>—अ-मेध्य-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, filthy, foul.<BR>—अ-<BR>मेध्य-लिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, smeared with ordure,<BR>foul, defiled.<BR>—अमेध्य-लेप, अस्, m. smearing with<BR>ordure.<BR>—अमेध्याक्त (˚य-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, soiled<BR>by ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेन
अमेन अ-मेन, अस्, m., Ved. having no wife,<BR>a widower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेनि
अमेनि अ-मेनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. not shooting,<BR>not able to shoot, not injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेय
अमेय अ-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, immeasurable.<BR>—अमेयात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, possessing extra-<BR>ordinary powers of mind, magnanimous; (आ), m. a<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेष्ट
अमेष्ट अमेष्ट (˚मा-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>sacrificed at home. See 2. अमा, p. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्य
अमोक्य अ-मोक्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मुच्), Ved.<BR>that cannot be unloosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचन|अमोचनं
अ-मोचन, अम्, n. not loosening or letting go;<BR>non-liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचनीय
अ-मोचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be liberated, not<BR>to be let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचित
अ-मोचित, अस्, आ, अम्, not liberated, confined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्ष|अमोक्षः
अमोक्ष अ-मोक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मोक्ष्),<BR>unliberated, unloosed; (अस्), m. want of freedom,<BR>bondage, confinement; non-liberation from mundane<BR>existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघ|अमोघः
अमोघ अ-मोघ, अस्, आ, अम्, unerring, un-<BR>failing, not vain, efficacious, succeeding, reaching the<BR>mark; productive, fruitful; (अस्), m. the not erring,<BR>the not failing; unerringness; N. of Śiva and Viṣṇu;<BR>N. of a river; (आ), f. trumpet flower, Bignonia<BR>Suaveolens, Roxb: a plant of which the seed is<BR>used as a vermifuge, Erycibe Paniculata, Roxb.; Ter-<BR>minalia Citrina, Roxb.; N. of a spear; N. of Śiva's<BR>wife; mystical name of the double consonant क्ष्.<BR>—अमोघ-दण्ड, अस्, m. (unerring in punish-<BR>ment), N. of Śiva.<BR>—अमोघ-दर्शिन्, ई, m., N. of<BR>a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—अमोघ-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, of un-<BR>erring view or mind.<BR>—अमोघ-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>never-failing strength.<BR>—अमोघ-भूति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a king of the Pañjāb.<BR>—अमोघ-राज, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Bhikṣu.<BR>—अमोघ-वाच्, क्, f. words that are not<BR>vain or idle.<BR>—अमोघ-वाञ्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, never<BR>disappointed.<BR>—अमोघ-विक्रम, अस्, m. of un-<BR>erring valour; N. of Śiva.<BR>—अमोघ-सिद्ध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the fifth Dhyāni-buddha.<BR>—अमोघाचार्य<BR>(˚घ-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोत
अमोत अमोत (अमा-उत), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>woven at home, taken care of at home; see 2. अमा.<BR>—अमोत-पुत्रका, f., Ved. a maiden protected at<BR>home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोतक|अमोतकः
