अमौत्रधौत
अमौत्रधौत अ-मौत्र-धौत, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>washed by a washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमौन|अमौनं
अमौन अ-मौन, अम्, n. non-silence; know-<BR>ledge of soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्नस्
अम्नस् अम्नस् (liable to become अम्नर्),<BR>Ved. unawares, quickly; at present; a little. (The<BR>etymology is doubtful, but cf. 1. अम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब्|अंब्
अम्ब् अम्ब्, cl. 1. P. अम्बति, -बितुम्, to go;<BR>cl. 1. A. अम्बते, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब|अंब|अंबः|अम्बः
अम्ब, अस्, m. a father; sound, the Veda, one who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">Page0077-c+ 78</a>]<BR>sounds; (आ), f. a mother, see अम्बा; (अम्), n. the<BR>eye; water?; (अ), ind. a particle of affirmation, well!<BR>well now!<BR>—अम्ब-स्थल, अम्, n., N. of a moun-<BR>tain peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बक|अंबक|अंबकं|अम्बकं
अम्बक, अम्, n. a father (?), an eye [cf. त्र्य्-अम्ब-<BR>क]; copper?; (इका, f.), see under अम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बया|अंबया
अम्बया, f., Ved. mother, good woman (as a re-<BR>spectful title ?), conveying water (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बर|अंबर|अंबरं|अम्बरं|अम्बरः
अम्बर अम्बर, अम्, n. (fr. rt. अम्ब्? or rt.<BR>वृ, to surround, with अम् prefixed), circumference,<BR>compass; surrounding country, neighbourhood; clothes,<BR>apparel; cotton; sky, atmosphere, ether; saffron;<BR>talc; a perfume (Ambergris); N. of a people.<BR>—अम्बर-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, sky-going.<BR>—अम्बर-<BR>द, अम्, n. cotton.<BR>—अम्बर-युग, अम्, n. the<BR>two principal female garments, or upper and lower<BR>cloths or mantles.<BR>—अम्बर-शैल, अस्, m. a high<BR>mountain touching the sky.<BR>—अम्बर-स्थली, f. the<BR>earth.<BR>—अम्बरान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of a<BR>garment; the horizon.<BR>—अम्बरौकस् (˚र-ओक्˚),<BR>आस्, m. dwelling in heaven; a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बर्य
अम्बर्य, nom. p. अम्बर्यति, -यितुम्, to bring<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरीष|अंबरीष|अंबरीषं|अम्बरीषं|अम्बरीषः
अम्बरीष अम्बरीष, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt.<BR>अम्ब्?), a frying-pan (in this sense also written with<BR>short इ, अम्बरिष); one of the hells; remorse,<BR>war, battle; (अस्), m. a young animal, a colt; the<BR>sun; the hog-plum plant, Spondias Magnifera; N.<BR>of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of a king of the solar race,<BR>celebrated as a worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अम्बरीष-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. son of Ambarīṣa, whence the N. of<BR>a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठ|अंबष्ठ|अंबष्ठः|अम्बष्ठः
अम्बष्ठ अम्ब-ष्ठ, अस्, m. (fr. अम्ब and<BR>स्थ?), N. of a country and of its inhabitants; the<BR>offspring of a man of the Brāhman and a woman of<BR>the Vaiśya tribe, a man of the medical caste; (आ),<BR>f., N. of several plants, Jasminum Auriculatum,<BR>Clypea Hernandifolia, Oxalis Corniculata; (आ) or (ई),<BR>f. an Ambaṣṭha woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठकी|अंबष्ठकी
अम्बष्ठकी, f. the plant Clypea Hernandifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठिका|अंबष्ठिका
अम्बष्ठिका, f. the plant Clerodendrum Sipho-<BR>nanthus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बा|अंबा
अम्बा अम्बा, f. (fr. rt. अम्ब्? the voc. case in<BR>the Veda is अम्बे or अम्ब; in later Sanskrit अम्ब<BR>only), a mother, good woman (as a title of respect);<BR>N. of a plant: N. of Durgā, the wife of Śiva; N. of an<BR>Apsaras; N. of a daughter of a king of Kāśi; a sister of<BR>Pāṇḍu's mother; a term in astrology to denote the<BR>fourth condition (?). In the South-Indian languages,<BR>अम्बा is corrupted into अम्मा, and is often affixed<BR>to the names of goddesses, and females in general<BR>[with अम्बा has been compared the Germ. Amme,<BR>‘a nurse;’ Old Germ. amma, Them. ammôn, am-<BR>mûn].<BR>—अम्बा-गङ्गा, f. a river in Ceylon.<BR>—अम्बा-<BR>जन्मन्, अ, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बाडा|अंबाडा
अम्बाडा or अम्बाला or अम्बायु, उस्, f. mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बालिका|अंबालिका
अम्बालिका, f. mother, good woman (as a term of<BR>respect); N. of a plant; N. of a daughter of a king<BR>of Kāśi, wife of Vicitra-vīrya, and mother of Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बि|अंबिः|अम्बिः
अम्बि, इस्, f., Ved. water; woman, mother, nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बितमा
—अम्बि-तमा, f., Ved. the best of waters or<BR>mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिका|अंबिका
अम्बिका, f. mother, good woman (as a term of<BR>respect); N. of the plant Wrightia Antidysenterica;<BR>a sister of Rudra; N. of Pārvatī, the wife of Śiva;<BR>the wife of Rudra Ugraretas; one of the female<BR>domestic deities of the Jainas; daughter of a king<BR>of Kāśi, wife of Vicitra-vīrya, and mother of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra; N. of a place in Bengal.<BR>—अम्बिका-पति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—अम्बिका-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेय|अंबिकेय|अंबिकेयः|अम्बिकेयः
अम्बिकेय or अम्बिकेयक, अस्, m., N. of Gaṇeśa,<BR>Kārttikeya, and Dhṛta-rāṣṭra. See आम्बिकेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बु|अंबु
अम्बु अम्बु, n. (fr. rt. अम्ब्?), water; the<BR>watery element of the blood [cf. ὄμβρος imber];<BR>the plant Andropogon Schœnanthus; N. of a metre;<BR>a term in astrology = अम्बा.<BR>—अम्बु-कण, अस्, m. a<BR>drop of water.<BR>—अम्बु-कण्टक, अस्, m. the short-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-a" target="_blank">Page0078-a+ 79</a>]<BR>nosed alligator.<BR>—अम्बु-किरात, अस्, m. an alligator.<BR>—अम्बु-कीश or अम्बु-कूर्म, अस्, m. a porpoise,<BR>especially the Gangetic, Delphinus Gangeticus.<BR>—अम्-<BR>बु-केशर, अस्, m. lemon tree.<BR>—अम्बु-क्रिया, f. a<BR>funeral rite = जल-क्रिया.<BR>—अम्बु-ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>water-goer, living in water.<BR>—अम्बु-घन, अस्, m.<BR>hail, frozen rain.<BR>—अम्बु-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, moving in<BR>the water, aquatic.<BR>—अम्बु-चामर, अम्, n. water-<BR>chowrī, an aquatic plant, Valisneria.<BR>—अम्बु-चारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, moving in water, as a fish, &c.<BR>—अम्-<BR>बु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in water, water-born,<BR>aquatic; (अस्), m., N. of a plant, Barringtonia<BR>Acutangula Gærtn.; a lotus, Nymphæa Nelumbo; the<BR>thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—अम्बु-जन्मन्, अ, n. a lotus,<BR>Nymphæa Nelumbo.<BR>—अम्बुज-भू, ऊस्, m. the god<BR>Brahmā.<BR>—अम्बुज-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting on a<BR>lotus.<BR>—अम्बु-तस्कर, अस्, m. water-thief, the sun.<BR>—अम्बु-ताल, अस्, m. the plant Valisneria.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, shedding or giving water; (अस्), m. a<BR>cloud; the plant Cyperus Hexastychius Communis.<BR>—अम्बु-धर, अस्, m. a cloud.<BR>—अम्बु-धि, इस्,<BR>m. (receptacle of waters), the ocean; the number<BR>‘four.’<BR>—अम्बुधि-स्रवा, f., N. of a plant, Aloes<BR>Perfoliata.<BR>—अम्बु-निधि, इस्, m. (treasury of waters),<BR>the ocean.<BR>—अम्बु-प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking or im-<BR>bibing water; (अस्), m. a plant, Cassia Tora or Alata.<BR>—अम्बु-पत्त्रा, f., N. of a plant, Cyperus Hexasty-<BR>chius Communis Nees.<BR>—अम्बु-पद्धति, इस्, f. or<BR>अम्बु-पात, अस्, m. current, stream, flow of water.<BR>—अम्बु-प्रसाद, अस्, m. or अम्बु-प्रसादन,<BR>अम्, n. the clearing nut tree, Strychnos Potatorum:<BR>the nuts of this plant are generally used in India for<BR>purifying water; they are rubbed upon the inner<BR>surface of a vessel, and so precipitate the impurities<BR>of the fluid it contains.<BR>—अम्बु-भृत्, त्, m. a cloud;<BR>the ocean (?); a grass, Cyperus Pertenuis; talc.<BR>—अम्बु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, watery, having or con-<BR>taining water; (ती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—अम्बु-मात्र-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced only in water; (अस्), m. a<BR>bivalve shell.<BR>—अम्बु-मुच्, क्, m. a cloud.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>राज, अस्, m. the ocean; N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>राशि, इस्, m. (heap of waters), the ocean.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>रुह, अम्, n. the lotus; (आ), f. Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>—अम्बु-रोहिणी, f. the lotus.<BR>—अम्बु-वाची, f. four<BR>days in Āṣāḍha, the tenth to the thirteenth of the<BR>dark half of the month, when the earth is supposed<BR>to be unclean, and agriculture is prohibited.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>वाची-त्याग, the thirteenth of the same.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>वाची-प्रद, अम्, n. the tenth in the second half of<BR>the month Āṣāḍha.<BR>—अम्बु-वासिनी or अम्बु-वासी,<BR>f. the trumpet flower, Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>वाह, अस्, m. a cloud; the grass Cyperus Pertenuis; a<BR>water-carrier; talc; the number ‘seventeen.’<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, carrying or conveying water; (इनी),<BR>f. a wooden baling vessel; N. of a river.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>वेतस, अस्, m. a kind of cane or reed growing in<BR>water.<BR>—अम्बु-शिरीषिका, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अम्बु-<BR>सीता, f., N. of a river.<BR>—अम्बु-सर्पिणी, f. a leech.<BR>—अम्बु-सेचनी, f. a wooden baling vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बूकृत|अंबूकृत|अम्बूकृतं
अम्बू-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, pronounced indistinctly, so<BR>that the words remain too much in the mouth; sput-<BR>tered (as speech, accompanied with emission of saliva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब्य|अंब्यः|अम्ब्यः
अम्ब्य अम्ब्य, अस्, m., Ved. a chanter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भ्|अंभ्
अम्भ् अम्भ्, cl. 1. A. अम्भते, -भितुम्,<BR>to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्|अंभस्
अम्भस् 1. अम्भस्, n. also ind., power,<BR>splendor, fruitfulness; a philos. term = तुष्टि: (the<BR>etymology is doubtful; perhaps connected with obs.<BR>rt. अप्, or fr. भा, ‘to shine,’ with prefix अम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्|अंभस्
अम्भस् 2. अम्भस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. आप्;<BR>perhaps connected with 1. अम्भस् or with अप्, अब्-<BR>भ्र, अम्बु), water; the sky; the fourth sign of the<BR>zodiac; collective N. for gods, men, manes, and Asuras;<BR>mystical name of the letter व् [cf. ὄμβρος imber].<BR>—अम्भः-सार, अम्, n. a pearl.<BR>—अम्भः-सू, ऊस्,<BR>m. smoke; cloudiness.<BR>—अम्भः-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>what holds or contains water; abiding in water.<BR>—अम्भसा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done by water.<BR>—अम्भो-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in water, water-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">Page0078-b+ 76</a>]<BR>born, aquatic; (अस्), m. the moon; the sārasa or<BR>Indian crane; (अम्), n. the lotus.<BR>—अम्भोज-<BR>खण्ड, अम्, n. a group of lotus flower.<BR>—अम्भो-<BR>ज-जन्मन्, आ, m. or अम्भोज-जनि, इस्, m. or<BR>अम्भोज-योनि, इस्, m. an epithet of Brahmā, being<BR>born secondarily from a lotus.<BR>—अम्भोजिनी, f. an<BR>assemblage of lotus flowers or a place where they<BR>abound.<BR>—अम्भो-द, अस्, m. a cloud; the plant<BR>Cyperus Hexastychius Communis Nees.<BR>—अम्भो-<BR>धर, अस्, m. a cloud.<BR>—अम्भो-धि, इस्, m. (re-<BR>ceptacle of waters), the ocean.<BR>—अम्भोधि-वल्लभ,<BR>अस्, m. coral.<BR>—अम्भो-निधि or अम्भो-राशि, इस्,<BR>m. a pool, the ocean.<BR>—अम्भो-रुह्, ट्, n. or अम्भो-<BR>रुह, अम्, n. the lotus; (अस्), m. the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भिणी
अम्भिणी अम्भिणी, f., Ved., N. of an in-<BR>structress, who transmitted the white Yajur-veda to<BR>Vāc (speech).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भृण|अंभृण|अम्भृणः
अम्भृण 1. अम्भृण, अस्, आ, अम् (connected<BR>with 1. अम्भस्), Ved. powerful, great, violent [cf.<BR>ὄβριμος, ὄμβριμος].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भृण|अंभृण|अम्भृणः
अम्भृण 2. अम्भृण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>भ्रण्?), crying violently, roaring terribly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भृण|अंभृण|अम्भृणः
अम्भृण 3. अम्भृण, अस्, m. (rt. भृ with<BR>अम्?), Ved. a vessel used in preparing the Soma<BR>juice; N. of a Ṛṣi, the father of Vāc. See आम्-<BR>भृणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्मय|अम्मयं
अम्मय अम्-मय, अस्, ई, अम् (for अप्-मय),<BR>formed from or consisting of water, watery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्यक्
अम्यक् अम्यक्, ind., Ved. (rt. अच् with अम्,<BR>इ being inserted), towards, here (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्र|अम्रः
अम्र अम्र, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अम्?), the mango<BR>tree. See आम्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रात|अम्रातः
अम्रात or अम्रातक, अस्, m. a species of Spondias<BR>or hog-plum, Spondias Magnifera. See आम्रात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ल|अम्लं|अम्लः
अम्ल अम्ल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अम्, to make<BR>sick), sour, acid; (अस्), m. sourness; acidity; vinegar;<BR>wood sorrel, Oxalis Corniculata; (ई), f. Oxalis Cor-<BR>niculata; (अम्), n. sour curds.<BR>—अम्ल-काण्ड, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a plant.<BR>—अम्ल-केशर, अस्, m. citron tree.<BR>—अम्ल-चुक्रिका, f. or अम्ल-चूड, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>sorrel.<BR>—अम्ल-जम्बीर, अस्, m. lime tree.<BR>—अम्-<BR>ल-ता, f. sourness.<BR>—अम्ल-नायक, अस्, m. sorrel.<BR>—अम्ल-निम्बूक, अस्, m. the lime.<BR>—अम्ल-निशा,<BR>f., N. of a plant, Curcuma Zerumbet, Roxb.<BR>—अम्ल-<BR>पञ्चक or अम्ल-पञ्च-फल, अम्, n. a collection<BR>of five kinds of sour vegetables and fruits.<BR>—अम्ल-पत्-<BR>त्र, अस्, m., N. of the plant Oxalis, and other plants.<BR>—अम्ल-पनस, अस्, m. a tree, Artocarpus Lacucha,<BR>Roxb.<BR>—अम्ल-पित्त, अम्, n. acidity of stomach.<BR>—अम्ल-फल, अस्, m. the tamarind tree, Magnifera<BR>Indica; (अम्), n. the fruit of this tree.<BR>—अम्ल-भे-<BR>दन, अस्, m. sorrel.<BR>—अम्ल-मेह, अस्, m. a urinary<BR>disease.<BR>—अम्ल-रस, अस्, आ, अम्, sour, having a<BR>sour taste; (अस्), m. sourness, acidity.<BR>—अम्ल-रुहा,<BR>f. a kind of betel.<BR>—अम्ल-लोणिका or अम्ल-लोणी or<BR>अम्ल-लोलिका, f. wood sorrel, Oxalis Corniculata.<BR>—अम्-<BR>ल-वर्ग, अस्, m. a class of plants with acid leaves<BR>or fruits, as the lime, orange, pomegranate, tamarind,<BR>sorrel, and others.<BR>—अम्ल-वल्ली, f., N. of a plant,<BR>Pythonium Bulbiferum Schott.<BR>—अम्ल-वाटक, अस्,<BR>m. hog-plum, Spondias Magnifera.<BR>—अम्ल-वाटिका,<BR>f. a sort of betel.<BR>—अम्ल-वास्तूक, अम्, n. sor-<BR>rel.<BR>—अम्ल-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the tamarind tree.<BR>—अम्ल-वेतस, अस्, m. a kind of dock or sorrel,<BR>Rumex Vesicarius.<BR>—अम्ल-शाक, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>sorrel, commonly used as a pot-herb.<BR>—अम्ल-सार,<BR>अस्, m. the lime; a sort of sorrel; (अम्), n. rice water<BR>after fermentation.<BR>—अम्ल-हरिद्रा, f. the plant<BR>Curcuma Zerumbet, Roxb.<BR>—अम्लाक्त (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, acidulated.<BR>—अम्लाङ्कुश (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a kind of sorrel.<BR>—अम्लाध्युषित (˚ल-अध्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a disease of the eyes.<BR>—अम्लोद्गार (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m. sour eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लक|अम्लकः
अम्लक, अस्, m. the plant Artocarpus Lacucha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लिका
अम्लिका or अम्लीका, f. a sour taste in the mouth,<BR>acidity of stomach; the tamarind tree; wood sorrel,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">Page0078-c+ 76</a>]<BR>Oxalis Corniculata.<BR>—अम्लिका-वटक, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लिमन्
अम्लिमन्, आ, m. sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लीभूत
अम्ली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्व्ल|अम्व्लः
अम्व्ल, अस्, m. sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लान|अम्लानः
अम्लान अ-म्लान, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. म्लै), not<BR>withered, clean, clear; bright, unclouded; (अस्), m.<BR>globe-amaranth, Gomphræna Globosa L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानि|अम्लानिः
अ-म्लानि, इस्, f. vigour, freshness, verdure; (इस्, इस्,<BR>इ), vigorous, unfading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानिन्
अ-म्लानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, clean, clear; (इनी), f. an assem-<BR>blage of globe-amaranths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय्
अय् अय् (connected with rt. इ, q. v.), cl. 1.<BR>.A. अयते, -यितुम्, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. इ), going; a move towards the<BR>right at chess; good luck, favourable fortune; a die;<BR>N. of a Prajāpati; (अस्, आ, अम्), going, moving.<BR>—अय-<BR>ता, f. good luck.<BR>—अय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, happy.<BR>—अय-शोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bright with good fortune.<BR>—अयान्वित (अय-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fortunate, lucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथ|अयथं
अयथ, अम्, n., Ved. a leg, foot (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन|अयनं
अयन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. इ), going; especially<BR>at the end of a compound, e. g. समुद्रायण, going<BR>to the ocean; (अम्), n. going, walking, walk; a road,<BR>a path; a place, a site (?); course, circulation,<BR>period; final emancipation; a commentary, treatise;<BR>N. of certain sacrificial performances; the sun's<BR>road north and south of the equator, the half<BR>year; the equinoctial and solstitial points; way,<BR>progress, manner; a Śāstra or inspired writing.<BR>—अयन-काल, अस्, m. the interval between the equi-<BR>noxes.<BR>—अयन-देवता, f. a deity or an idol placed<BR>near a road (?).<BR>—अयन-भाग, अस्, m. or अय-<BR>नांश (˚न-अं˚), अस्, m. the arc between the vernal<BR>equinoctial point and the beginning of the fixed<BR>zodiac or first point in Aries.<BR>—अयन-वलन, अम्,<BR>n. deviation of the ecliptic.<BR>—अयन-वृत्त, अम्,<BR>n. the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयक्ष्म
अयक्ष्म अ-यक्ष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not con-<BR>sumptive; not sick, healthy; causing health; (अम्),<BR>n. health.<BR>—अयक्ष्म-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>producing health.<BR>—अयक्ष्म-ताति, इस्, f. or अय-<BR>क्ष्म-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. freedom from consump-<BR>tion; health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयक्ष्यमाण
अयक्ष्यमाण अ-यक्ष्यमाण, अस्, m. not<BR>wishing or not about to sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयजुष्क
अयजुष्क अ-यजुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. with-<BR>out a sacrificial formula or verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञ|अयज्ञः
अयज्ञ अ-यज्ञ, अस्, m. no sacrifice; a bad<BR>sacrifice; (अस्, आ, अम्), not offering sacrifice.<BR>—अ-<BR>यज्ञ-साच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. not performing a sacrifice,<BR>performing worthless sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञक
अ-यज्ञक, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञिय
अ-यज्ञिय, अस्, आ, अम्, not fit for sacrifice; not<BR>worthy of sacrifice, profane, common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्यु
अ-यज्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not sacrificing, impious,<BR>profane, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्वन्
अ-यज्वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. not offering sacrifice, profane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञदत्त
अयज्ञदत्त अ-यज्ञदत्त, अस्, m. not Yajña-<BR>datta, i. e. the vile Yajñadatta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्
अयत् अ-यत्, त्, त्, त् (rt. यम्), not making<BR>efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत
अ-यत, अस्, आ, अम्, unrestrained, uncontrolled,<BR>unchecked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयतिन्
अ-यतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, of unsubdued appetite; incon-<BR>tinent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्न|अयत्नः
अयत्न, अस्, m. absence of effort or exertion;<BR>अयत्नेन or अयत्नात् or अयत्नतस्, without effort<BR>or exertion.<BR>—अ-यत्न-कारिन्, ई, इनी, इ, making no<BR>exertion, indifferent, idle.<BR>—अ-यत्न-कृत or अ-<BR>यत्न-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, easily or readily produced,<BR>spontaneous.<BR>—अयत्न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, inactive,<BR>indifferent, idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथा
अयथा अ-यथा, ind. not as it should be,<BR>unfitly, unsuitably.<BR>—अ-यथम्, Ved. without effort.<BR>—अ-यथा-तथ, अस्, आ, अम्, not so as it should be,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">Page0079-a+ 75</a>]<BR>unfit, unsuitable; useless, unprofitable, vain; (अम्),<BR>ind. unfitly, unsuitably.<BR>—अ-यथा-तथ्य, अम्, n.<BR>unsuitableness, unprofitableness, incompatibility.<BR>—अ-<BR>यथा-द्योतन, अम्, n. intimation of something<BR>unexpected.<BR>—अ-यथा-पूर्व or अ-यथा-पुर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, unprecedented.<BR>—अ-यथा-बलम्, ind. not<BR>according to one's power.<BR>—अ-यथा-मात्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, not according to measure.<BR>—अ-यथामुखीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the face turned away.<BR>—अ-य-<BR>थार्थ (˚था-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not according to<BR>the sense or object, incongruous, unmeaning, non-<BR>sensical; improper, unfitting.<BR>—अ-यथा-वत्, ind.<BR>inaccurately, erroneously.<BR>—अ-यथाशास्त्र-कारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, not acting in accordance with the scripture.<BR>—अ-यथेष्ट (˚था-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not as<BR>wished; disliked, disapproved of; insufficient, not<BR>enough.<BR>—अ-यथोचित (˚था-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>worthily, unsuitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयदीक्षित|अयदीक्षितः
अयदीक्षित अय-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन|अयनं
अयन अयन, &c. See under अय्, p. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन्त्र|अयंत्रं
अयन्त्र अ-यन्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. non-restraint,<BR>not a means of restraining; having no restraint; a<BR>powerful weapon for restraining enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन्त्रित|अयंत्रित|अयन्त्रितः
अ-यन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, unhindered, unrestrained,<BR>self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयमित
अयमित अ-यमित, अस्, आ, अम्, unchecked,<BR>untrimmed, unpaired, unclipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयव|अयवः
अयव 1. अयव, अस्, आ, अम्, deficient; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a worm bred in the intestines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयव|अयवः
अयव 2. अ-यव, अस्, m. or अ-यवन्, आ, m.<BR>or अ-यवस्, अस्, n. the dark half of the month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयव|अयवः
अयव 3. अ-यव, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-यवक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, having worthless or no barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयवय
अ-यवय, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit for barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्
अयशस् अ-यशस्, अस्, n. infamy; (आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्), infamous, disagreeable.<BR>—अयशस्-कर, अस्, आ,<BR>or ई, अम्, disgraceful, degrading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्य
अ-यशस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, infamous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्
अयस् अयस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (fr. rt. इ), going,<BR>nimble; (अस्), n. iron, steel, gold, metal [cf. Lat.<BR>œs, œr-is for œs-is; Goth. ais, Them. aisa;<BR>Old Germ. êr, ‘iron;’ Goth. eisarn; Mod. Germ.<BR>Eisen]; (आस्), m. fire.<BR>—अयः-पान, अम्, n. a par-<BR>ticular hell.<BR>—अयः-प्रतिमा, f. iron image.<BR>—अयः-<BR>शङ्कु, उस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—अयः-शय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. lying in iron, made of iron (said of fire).<BR>—अयः-शिप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having jaws or<BR>a nose of iron.<BR>—अयः-शिरस्, आस्, m., N. of an<BR>Asura.<BR>—अयः-शीर्षन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having a<BR>head of iron.<BR>—अयः-शूल, अम्, n. an iron lance;<BR>fraudulent or cunning artifice.<BR>—अयः-स्थूण or<BR>अयस्-स्थूण or अय-स्थूण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. having<BR>iron pillars or spikes; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—अयश्-<BR>चूर्ण, अम्, n. iron filings.<BR>—अयस्-कंस, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. an iron goblet.<BR>—अयस्-काण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>an iron arrow.<BR>—अयस्-कान्त, अस्, m. a precious stone,<BR>the loadstone.<BR>—अयस्-कार, अस्, m. a blacksmith;<BR>the upper part of the thigh (?).<BR>—अयस्-कीट, अम्, n.<BR>rust of iron.<BR>—अयस्-कुम्भ, अस्, ई, m. f. an iron<BR>pot or boiler.<BR>—अयस्-कुशा, f. a rope partly consist-<BR>ing of iron.<BR>—अयस्-कृति, इस्, f. preparation of iron.<BR>—अयस्-ताप, अस्, आ, अम्, making iron red-hot.<BR>—अयस्-पात्र, अम्, n. an iron vessel.<BR>—अयस्-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. made of iron or of metal; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Manu Svārociṣa; (ई), f., N. of one<BR>of the three residences of the Asuras.<BR>For compounds beginning अयो, see s.v. अयो-गुड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस
अयस may be used for अयस् at the end of com-<BR>pounds, as कृष्णायस, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अया
अया अया, ind. (fr. pronominal base अ =<BR>अनया), Ved. in this manner, thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचक|अयाचकः
अयाचक अ-याचक, अस्, इका, अम् (rt. याच्),<BR>one who does not ask or solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयचित
अ-यचित, अस्, आ, अम्, unasked, unsolicited; अया-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">Page0079-b+ 72</a>]<BR>चितम्, ind. without being asked; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>the Ṛṣi Upavarṣa.<BR>—अयाचित-वृत्ति, इस्, f. or<BR>अयाचित-व्रत, अम्, n. subsisting on alms without<BR>begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचिन्
अ-याचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not soliciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाज्य
अयाज्य अ-याज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. यज्), a person<BR>or thing for whom or for which one must not offer<BR>sacrifices; outcast, degraded; not competent to offer<BR>sacrifice; incapable of or inadmissible to religious<BR>ceremonies.<BR>—अयाज्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state of an<BR>outcast.<BR>—अयाज्य-याजन or अयाज्य-संयाज्य, अम्,<BR>n. sacrificing for an outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातपूर्व|अयातपूर्व्व
अयातपूर्व अ-यात-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, follow-<BR>ing, subsequent to, succeeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातयाम
अयातयाम अ-यातयाम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>weak; not worn out by use; fresh; (अम्), n., N. of<BR>certain texts of the Yajur-veda, revealed to Yājiñaval-<BR>kya.<BR>—अयातयाम-ता, f., Ved. unweakened strength,<BR>freshness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातयामन्
अ-यातयामन्, आ, म्नी, अ, Ved. not weak, fresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातु|अयातुः
अयातु अ-यातु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not demoni-<BR>acal; free from evil spirits; (उस्), m. not a demon,<BR>the opposite of an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थिक
अयाथार्थिक अ-याथार्थिक, अस्, ई, अम्, impro-<BR>per, unjust; not genuine, not real, incongruous, absurd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थ्य|अयाथार्थ्यं
अ-याथार्थ्य, अम्, n. impropriety, unfitness, ab-<BR>surdity, nonsense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयान|अयानं
अयान अ-यान, अम्, n. not moving, halting,<BR>stopping; natural disposition or temperament: (in the<BR>last sense the etymology is doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानय|अयानयं|अयानयः
अयानय अयानय (˚य-अन्˚), अम्, n. good<BR>and bad luck; (अस्), m. a particular position of the<BR>pieces on a chess or backgammon board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानयीन|अयानयीनः
अयानयीन, अस्, m. a piece at chess or backgam-<BR>mon so moved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयावक
अयावक अ-यावक, अस्, आ, अम्, unstained<BR>with lac-dye, naturally red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयावन|अयावनं
अयावन अ-यावन, अम्, n. not causing to<BR>unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाशु
अयाशु अ-याशु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. unfit for<BR>copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयास्
अयास् अ-यास् (?), आस्, m. (rt. यस्), Ved. agile<BR>(without effort), dexterous, nimble; (आस्), ind. fire (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयास्य|अयास्यः
अ-यास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not to be obtained by<BR>effort, indefatigable; valiant; enterprising; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of an Aṅgiras; mystical name of the chief vital air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयासोमीय|अयासोमीयं
अयासोमीय अयासोमीय, अम्, n., N. of some<BR>verses of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयि
अयि अयि, ind. a vocative particle; a par-<BR>ticle of encouragement or introducing a kind enquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयिन्
अयिन् अयिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt. इ), at the end of<BR>compounds, going, e. g. अत्ययिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्त|अयुक्तं
अयुक्त अ-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. युज्), not<BR>yoked, not joined, not united, not married; not<BR>harnessed; not connected; not suited, unfit, unsuit-<BR>able; not attentive, not devout; negligent, not dex-<BR>terous, unpractised, untrue, wrong; indecent.<BR>—अ-<BR>युक्त-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, committing wrong acts.<BR>—अयुक्त-<BR>चार, अस्, m. (a king &c.) who does not appoint<BR>spies.<BR>—अयुक्त-ता, f. or अयुक्त-त्व, अम्, n. the not<BR>being used.<BR>—अयुक्त-पदार्थ, अस्, m. the sense<BR>of a word to be supplied.<BR>—अयुक्त-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>unfit, unsuitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्ति|अयुक्तिः
अ-युक्ति, इस्, f. disunion, separation; unreasonable-<BR>ness, want of conformity to correct principles or to<BR>analogy; impropriety, unfitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग
अ-युग or अ-युगल, अस्, आ, अम्, separate, single,<BR>odd.<BR>—अयुगार्चिस् (˚ग-अर्˚), इस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगपद्
अ-युगपद्, ind. not at once, gradually, seriatim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगपद्ग्रहण
—अयुगपद्-ग्रहण, अम्, n. apprehending gra-<BR>dually and not simultaneously.<BR>—अयुगपद्-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. successiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्म
अ-युग्म, अस्, आ, अम्, not in couples, separate,<BR>single; odd, uneven.<BR>—अयुग्म-च्छद, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the plant Alstonia Scholaris.<BR>—अयुग्म-नेत्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—अयुग्म-शर, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the god of love (‘having an odd number of arrows’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज्
अ-युज्, क्, क्, क्, not existing in couples; odd, un-<BR>even.<BR>—अयुक्-छद, अस्, m., N. of a plant, Alstonia<BR>Scholaris.<BR>—अयुक्-पलाश, अस्, m., N. of a tree.<BR>—अयुक्-पाद-यमक, अम्, n. a kind of alliteration,<BR>viz. the same syllables in the first and third Pāda<BR>of a word in a different sense.<BR>—अयुक्-शक्ति, इस्,<BR>m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—अयुग्-इषु, उस्, m., N. of Kāma,<BR>from his having five arrows; see पञ्चेषु.<BR>—अयुग्-<BR>धातु, उस्, उस्, उ, having an odd number of elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्वाण
—अयुग्-वाण, अस्, m., N. of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुङ्नेत्र
—अयुङ्-नेत्र or अयुग्-अक्ष, अस्, m., N. of Śiva, from his having<BR>three eyes; see त्रि-नेत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज
अ-युज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. without a companion,<BR>not having an equal; not existing by pairs, separate,<BR>odd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग|अयोगः
अ-योग, अस्, m. separation, disjunction; interval;<BR>unfitness, unsuitableness, unconformity; inefficacy of<BR>a remedy; medical treatment counter to the symp-<BR>toms; non-application or mis-application of re-<BR>medies; vigorous effort, exertion; a widower, an<BR>absent lover or husband; inauspicious conjunction of<BR>the planets; a conjunction of two planets; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), unconnected with; indistinctly connected with;<BR>making vigorous efforts.<BR>—अयोग-वाह, अस्, m. a<BR>term for Anusvāra, Visarjanīya, Upadhmānīya, and<BR>Jihvāmūlīya, as standing between vowels and conso-<BR>nants. (For अयो-ग, hammer, see अयो-ऽग्र below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्य
अ-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit, unsuitable, useless;<BR>immaterial; (in phil.) not ascertainable &c. by the<BR>senses.<BR>—अयोग्य-ता, f. or अयोग्य-त्व, अम्, n. un-<BR>fitness, unsuitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोजन
अ-योजन, अम्, n. disunion, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौक्तिक
अ-यौक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, not conformable to, in-<BR>consistent with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगपद्य|अयौगपद्यं
अ-यौगपद्य, अम्, n. uncontemporaneous ex-<BR>istence, unsimultaneousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगिक
अ-यौगिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having no regular derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुङ्ग|अयुंग
अयुङ्ग अ-युङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not exist-<BR>ing in couples; odd, uneven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अयुत 1. अ-युत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 2. यु), Ved.<BR>not disturbed or interrupted; (अस्), m., N. of a son<BR>of Rādhika.<BR>—अयुत-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, proved to<BR>be not separated or interrupted, proved to be inherent.<BR>—अयुत-सिद्धि, इस्, f. proof that certain things or<BR>notions are not separable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुव
अ-युव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. undisturbed, unshaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अयुत 2. अ-युत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 1. यु, to<BR>mix), disjoined, detached, not counted; (अम्), n. ten<BR>thousand, a myriad.<BR>—अयुत-जित्, त्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Bhajamāna.<BR>—अयुत-नायिन्, ई, m., N. of a king.<BR>—अयुत-शस्, ind. by myriads.<BR>—अयुत-होम, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of sacrifice.<BR>—अयुताध्यापक (˚त-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a good teacher.<BR>—अयुतायुस् (˚त-आय्˚), उस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Jayasena Ārāvin; of a son of<BR>Śrutavat.<BR>—अयुताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Sindhu-dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अयुद्ध अ-युद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. युध्), Ved.<BR>unconquered; not fighting; (अम्), n. not war, absence<BR>of war, peace.<BR>—अ-युद्ध-सेन, अस्, m., Ved. whose<BR>arrows or armies are unconquered, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध्वी
अ-युद्ध्वी, ind., Ved. without fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अ-युद्ध, अस्, m. a non-fighter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुध्य
अ-युध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुध्विन्
अ-युध्विन्, ई, m., Ved. not conquering, not a<BR>valiant warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोद्धृ
अ-योद्धृ, धा, m. no warrior, a bad fighter;<BR>unmatched by other warriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्य
अ-योध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not to be warred<BR>against, irresistible; (आ), f. the capital of Rāma, the<BR>modern Oude, on the river Sarayu.<BR>—अयोध्याधि-<BR>पति (˚या-अध्˚), इस्, m. the sovereign of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्यावासिन्
—अयोध्या-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, inhabiting Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौधिक
अ-यौधिक, अस्, m. not a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयूप
अयूप अ-यूप, अस्, m. no sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अये
अये अये, ind. a vocative particle, an inter-<BR>jection of surprise, recollection, fatigue, fear, passion;<BR>used also in the same meanings as अयि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगव|अयोगवः
अयोगव अयोगव, अस्, आ, or ई, m. f. or अयो-<BR>गू? (etymology uncertain; perhaps connected with<BR>अयस्, iron, or fr. अ-योग), the offspring of a Śūdra<BR>man and Vaiśya woman, whose business is carpentry.<BR>See आयोगव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगुड|अयोगुडः
अयोगुड अयो-गुड, अस्, m. (अयो for अयस्,<BR>iron), a chalybeate pill, one made of some prepara-<BR>tion of iron; an iron ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्र|अयोग्रं
अयो-ऽग्र or अयो-ऽग्रक (अयस्-अग्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>hammer, a forge hammer; a mace or club tipped<BR>with iron; a pestle for cleaning grain. (A form<BR>अयो-ग, अस्, m., is also given in the sense ‘iron<BR>hammer.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोघन|अयोघनः
अयो-घन, अस्, m. a hammer, a forge hammer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोच्छिष्ट|अयोच्छिष्टं
अयोच्छिष्ट (अयस्-उच्˚?), अम्, n. rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोजाल
अयो-जाल, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with iron nets;<BR>(अम्), n. iron net-work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोदंष्ट्र
अयो-दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., or अयो-दत्, अत्,<BR>अती, अत्, iron-toothed, having iron weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोदाह
अयो-दाह, अस्, m. the burning quality of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोपाष्टि
अयो-ऽपाष्टि (अयस्-अप्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. furnished<BR>with iron claws or heels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमय
अयो-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of iron. See also<BR>s.v. अयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमल|अयोमलं
अयो-मल, अम्, n. rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमुख|अयोमुखः
अयो-मुख, अस्, आ, अम्, having an iron mouth,<BR>face, or beak; tipped or pointed with iron; (अस्), m.<BR>an arrow; N. of a Dānava; N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोरज
अयो-रज, अम्, n. or अयो-रजस्, अस्, n. rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोरस
अयो-रस, अस्, m. iron rust or filings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोवत्स
अयो-वत्स, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोविकार
अयो-विकार, अस्, m. iron-work, any iron fabric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोहत
अयो-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. embossed in iron-work;<BR>made or performed by a priest &c. who wears a<BR>golden ring on his finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोहनु
अयो-हनु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. iron-jawed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोहृदय
अयो-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, iron-hearted, stern, un-<BR>relenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोद्धृ
अयोद्धृ, अपयोध्य See अ-युद्ध, p. 79, last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनि|अयोनिः
अयोनि अ-योनि, इस्, f. not the womb; any-<BR>thing but the womb; not a particular verse of the<BR>Sāma-veda; (इस्, इस्, इ), without origin; not born<BR>from the womb, born in a manner not approved by<BR>law or religion; (इस्), m., N. of Brahmā and Śiva; a<BR>pestle (for अयो-ऽग्र above ?).<BR>—अ-योनि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not born from the womb, not produced in the or-<BR>dinary course of generation, generated equivocally;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—अयोनिज-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of not being born from a womb. -अयोनिजेश<BR>(˚ज-ईश˚), अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—अयोनिजेश्वर (˚ज-<BR>ईश्˚) or अयोनिजेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—अ-योनि-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम् = अयोनिज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिक
अ-योनिक, अस्, आ, अम्, without the verse containing<BR>the word योनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर|अरं|अरः
अर अर, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. ऋ), swift, speedy;<BR>little; (at end of comp.) going; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the<BR>spoke or radius of a wheel, see also अरम्, col. 3;<BR>(अस्), m. a spoke of the time-wheel, viz. a Jaina divi-<BR>sion of time, the sixth of an Avasarpiṇī or Utsarpiṇī;<BR>the eighteenth Jaina saint of the present Avasarpiṇī;<BR>N. of an ocean in Brahmā's world.<BR>—अर-घट्ट or<BR>अर-घट्टक, अस्, m. a wheel or machine for raising<BR>water from a well (Hind. أرهٿ); a deep well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरनेमि
—अर-नेमि, इस्, m., N. of Brahma-datta, king of<BR>Kośala.<BR>—अरान्तरेषु (˚र-अन्˚), loc. pl. in the in-<BR>tervals of the spokes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक|अरकः
अरक, अस्, m. the spoke of a wheel; a Jaina<BR>division of time [cf. अर]; the plant Blyxa Octandra;<BR>another plant, Gardenia Enneandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षस्
अरक्षस् अ-रक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. harm-<BR>less, honest; not disturbed &c. by evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षित
अरक्षित अ-रक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, unprotected,<BR>undefended; not preserved, not kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरगराट
अरगराट अरगराट, अस्, m., Ved. a valley (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्कृ|अरंकृ
अरङ्कृ अरङ्-कृ, cl. 8. P., Ved. -करोति, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to prepare, make ready; serve. See अरम्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्कृत्|अरंकृत्
अरङ्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. acting satisfactorily; pre-<BR>paring, serving as a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्कृत|अरंकृत
अरङ्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. prepared, ready; gra-<BR>tified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्कृति|अरंकृति
अरङ्कृति, इस्, f., Ved. service, gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गम्|अरंगम्
अरङ्गम् अरङ्-गम्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to be present, come near (in order to help),<BR>become visible, appear. See अरम्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गम|अरंगम|अरंगमः
अरङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. coming near or into<BR>the presence, appearing (in order to help), becoming<BR>visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गर|अरंगर|अरंगरः
अरङ्गर अरङ्-गर, अस्, m., Ved. praising rea-<BR>dily (?); factitious or made up poison. See अरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गिन्|अरंगिन्
अरङ्गिन् अ-रङ्-गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, passionless.<BR>—अरङ्गि-सत्त्व, अस्, m. a passionless being, a class<BR>of gods with Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्घुष|अरंघुष
अरङ्घुष अरङ्-घुष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. prais-<BR>ing readily, sounding aloud. See अरम्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्
अरजस् अ-रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or अ-रज or<BR>अ-रजस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, dustless; free from passion<BR>or desire; clean, pure; not having the monthly<BR>courses; (आस्), f. a young girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजाय
अरजाय, nom. A. अरजायते, -यितुम्, to become<BR>dustless; to lose the monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरज्जु
अरज्जु अ-रज्जु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not consist-<BR>ing of cords; not furnished with cords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरटु|अरटुः
अरटु अरटु or अरडु, उस्, m., N. of the tree<BR>Calosanthes Indica Bl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरट्व
अरट्व, अस्, आ, अम्, made of the wood of the<BR>above tree; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण|अरणं
अरण 1. अरण, अस्, ई, अम् (rt. ऋ), Ved. de-<BR>parted, gone away; strange, foreign; distant; (अम्),<BR>n. moving, entering; being inserted; a refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणि|अरणिः
1. अरणि, इस्, ई, m. f. the wood of the Ficus Re-<BR>ligiosa used for kindling fire by attrition; the lower<BR>one (अधरारणि) of the two Araṇis; (ई), du. the<BR>two pieces of wood used in kindling the sacred fire;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of several plants, especially Premna<BR>Integrifolia; the sun; fire; a flint?; (इस्), f. a<BR>way, a path.<BR>—अरणि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, related to<BR>the two Araṇis; to be produced by the Araṇis.<BR>—अरणी-केतु, उस्, m. the Premna Integrifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण|अरणं
अरण 2. अ-रण, अस्, आ, अम्, not fighting,<BR>without fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणि|अरणिः
अरणि 2. अ-रणि, इस्, f., Ved. stinginess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्य|अरण्यं|अरण्यः
अरण्य अरण्य, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. ऋ),<BR>land neither cultivated nor grazed; a wilderness,<BR>desert, forest; N. of a plant; N. of a Sādhya.<BR>—अरण्य-कणा, f. wild cumin seed.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>कदली, f. the wood or wild plantain.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>काण्ड (?), अम्, n. title of the third book of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—अरण्य-कार्पासी, f. the wild cotton.<BR>—अरण्य-कुलत्थिका, f., N. of the plant Glycine<BR>Labialis Lin.<BR>—अरण्य-कुसुम्भ, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the plant Carthamus Tinctorius.<BR>—अरण्य-गज,<BR>अस्, m. a wild elephant.<BR>—अरण्य-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, gone into a forest.<BR>—अरण्य-गान (?), अम्,<BR>n. one of the four Gānas or hymn-books of the<BR>Sāma-veda.<BR>—अरण्य-घोली, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अ-<BR>रण्य-चटक, अस्, m. a wild pigeon.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>चर, अस्, ई, अम्, living in forests, wild.<BR>—अरण्य-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, produced or born in a forest.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>जार्द्रका (˚ज-आर्द्˚), f. wild ginger.<BR>—अरण्य-जीर,<BR>अस्, m. wild cumin.<BR>—अरण्य-जीव, अस्, आ, अम्, living<BR>in a forest.<BR>—अरण्य-दमन, अस्, m. a wild plant,<BR>called दोन.<BR>—अरण्य-द्वादशी, f. or अरण्यद्वा-<BR>दशी-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a ceremony performed on<BR>the twelfth day of the month Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">Page0080-c+ 76</a>]<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. forest usage, wild or savage state.<BR>—अरण्य-धान्य, अम्, n. wild rice.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>नृपति, इस्, m. king of the forest.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, growing in a forest, wild.<BR>—अ-<BR>रण्य-मक्षिका, f. the gad-fly.<BR>—अरण्य-मार्-<BR>जार, अस्, m. wild cat.<BR>—अरण्य-मुद्ग, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of bean.<BR>—अरण्य-यान, अम्, n. going<BR>into a forest.<BR>—अरण्य-रक्षक, अस्, m. forest-<BR>keeper, superintendent of a forest district.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>राज्, ट्, m. king of the forest; epithet of a lion or tiger.<BR>—अरण्य-राज्य, अम्, n. the sovereignty of the<BR>forest.<BR>—अरण्य-रुदित, अम्, n. weeping in a forest,<BR>i. e. weeping in vain, with no one to hear.<BR>—अरण्य-<BR>वत्, ind. like a wilderness.<BR>—अरण्य-वायस, अस्,<BR>m. a raven.<BR>—अरण्य-वास, अस्, m. a hermitage.<BR>—अरण्य-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in a forest, wild;<BR>(ई), m. forest-dweller, a hermit, anchorite; (नी),<BR>f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अरण्य-वास्तुक or अरण्य-वा-<BR>स्तूक, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अरण्य-शालि, इस्, m.<BR>wild rice.<BR>—अरण्य-शूकर, अस्, m. a wild hog.<BR>—अरण्य-शूरण, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अ-<BR>रण्य-श्वन्, आ, m. a wolf.<BR>—अरण्य-षष्ठी, f.,<BR>N. of a festival celebrated by females in the month<BR>Jyaiṣṭha.<BR>—अरण्य-सभा, f. a forest court.<BR>—अ-<BR>रण्याध्यक्ष (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, m. forest-keeper or<BR>ranger, a head-man or superintendent of a forest dis-<BR>trict.<BR>—अरण्यायन (˚य-अय्˚), अम्, n. going into<BR>the forest, becoming a hermit.<BR>—अरण्ये-तिलक, अस्,<BR>m. wild sesamum growing in a forest and containing<BR>no oil; hence, anything which disappoints expectation.<BR>—अरण्ये-ऽनूच्य (˚ये-अन्˚), अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>oblation.<BR>—अरण्यौकस् (˚य-ओक्˚), आस्, m. living in<BR>a forest, a Brāhman who has left his family and be-<BR>come an anchorite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यक|अरण्यकं
अरण्यक, अम्, n. a forest, a desert; N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानि|अरण्यानिः
अरण्यानि, इस्, or अरण्यानी, f. a wilderness, desert,<BR>large forest; the goddess of the wilderness and desert,<BR>and mother of wild animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणीय
अरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, containing a forest, near to<BR>one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत अ-रत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रम्), dull,<BR>languid, apathetic; disgusted, discontented; (अम्), n.<BR>non-copulation.<BR>—अ-रत-त्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>ashamed of copulation; (अस्), m. a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
1. अ-रति, इस्, f. dissatisfaction, discontent; absence<BR>of pleasure, pain; dulness, languor; anxiety, distress,<BR>regret; a bilious disease; (इस्, इस्, इ), discontented, un-<BR>happy; dull, languid, restless.<BR>—अरति-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dull, spiritless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति 2. अरति, इस्, m. (fr. rt. ऋ, cf. अर,<BR>अरम्), Ved. going, approaching; moving quickly;<BR>moving flame; occupying; attacking; a servant, assist-<BR>ant, manager, administrator; a master; an intelligent<BR>being of all-piercing intellect; anger, passion; anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्नि|अरत्निः
अरत्नि अरत्नि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. ऋ),<BR>the elbow, a corner; a cubit of the middle length,<BR>from the elbow to tip of the little finger, a fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निमान्त्र
—अरत्नि-मान्त्र, अस्, ई, अम्, one ell in length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निक|अरत्निकः
अरत्निक, अस्, m. the elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथ
अरथ अ-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having no carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथिन्
अ-रथिन्, ई, m. a warrior who does not fight in a<BR>car, or owns, no car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथी
अ-रथी, ईस्, m., Ved. not a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरध्र
अरध्र अ-रध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not lazy;<BR>not to be subdued; unprosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरन्तुक
अरन्तुक अरन्तुक, अस्, m., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरप
अरप अ-रप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unhurt; sin-<BR>less, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरपस्
अ-रपस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. unhurt, safe; not hurt-<BR>ing, beneficial, charitable; sinless, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरपचन|अरपचनः
अरपचन अरपचन, अस्, m. a mystical col-<BR>lective N. of the five Buddhas, each being represented<BR>by a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम्
अरम् अरम्, ind. (fr. rt. ऋ, see अर), Ved.<BR>swiftly, at hand, near, present; readily, fitly, suitably,<BR>so as to answer a purpose; enough, sufficient [cf. अलम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">Page0081-a+ 71</a>]<BR>and Gr. ἄρα].<BR>—अरङ्-कृ and अरङ्-गम्, see<BR>p. 80, col. 2.<BR>—अरमणस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (for अरम्-<BR>म्˚), Ved. ready to serve, obedient, devoted to the<BR>worship of God; (according to native interpreta-<BR>tion) having hostile intentions.<BR>—अरमति, इस्, f. (for<BR>अरम्-म्˚), Ved. readiness to serve, obedience, devo-<BR>tion; a goddess, described in the Vedas as protecting<BR>the worshippers of the gods and pious works in<BR>general; (according to others) not resting, active,<BR>going everywhere; splendor.<BR>—अरम्-इष्, ट्, ट्, ट्,<BR>Ved. hastening near (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमण
अरमण अ-रमण, अस्, ई, अम् (rt. रम्), not<BR>gratifying, not pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमणीय
अ-रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, unpleasant, disagreeable.<BR>—अरमणीय-ता, f. disagreeableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरममाण
अ-रममाण, अस्, आ, अम्, not gratifying; Ved.<BR>unremitting, unceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमयितृ
अ-रमयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, not causing gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमुडि|अरमुडिः
अरमुडि अरमुडि, इस्, m. a king of Nepāl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर|अररं|अररः
अरर अरर, अम्, n. a covering, a sheath;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), m. f. n. the leaf of a door, a door; the<BR>sheath of the shoot of a bamboo; (अस्), m. an awl;<BR>a part of a sacrifice; fighting, war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररि|अररिः
अररि, इस्, इ, m. n. a door; a door-leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररका
अररका अररका, f., N. of the ancestress<BR>of a celebrated Hindū family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररक्य
अररक्य, अस्, m. a descendant of Ararakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिन्द|अररिंदं
