अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविन्द अरविन्द, अम्, n. (fr. अ, ‘like,’ and<BR>रविन्द, q. v., for रवि-द?), a lotus, Nelumbium<BR>Speciosum or Nymphæa Nelumbo; (अस्), m. the In-<BR>dian crane; copper.<BR>—अरविन्द-दल-प्रभ, अम्,<BR>n. copper.<BR>—अरविन्द-नाभि, इस्, m. Viṣṇu, from<BR>whose navel sprung the lotus that bore Brahmā at<BR>the creation.<BR>—अरविन्द-सद्, त्, m., N. of Brahmā,<BR>‘sitting on a lotus.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दिनी|अरविंदिनी
अरविन्दिनी, f. an assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरश्मन्
अरश्मन् अ-रश्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having no<BR>ropes or reins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरस|अरसः
अरस अ-रस, अस्, आ, अम्, sapless, tasteless;<BR>weak, effectless, having no strength; dull, flat; insi-<BR>pid; (अस्), m. no juice, absence of juice.<BR>—अरसाश<BR>(˚स-आश), अस्, m. the eating of sapless food; mace-<BR>ration of the body.<BR>—अरसाशिन् (˚स-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>eating sapless food; macerating the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिक|अरसिकः
अ-रसिक, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of taste, unfeeling,<BR>dull; insipid, flavourless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहस्
अरहस् अ-रहस्, अस्, n. absence of secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहाय
अरहाय, nom. A. -यते, -यितुम्, to become public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहित
अरहित अ-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, not deprived<BR>of, possessed of, having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराग
अराग अ-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-रागिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, unimpassioned, cool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक अ-राजक, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>king or governor, anarchical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्
अ-राजन्, आ, m., Ved. not a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजभोगीन
अ-राजभोगीन, अस्, आ, अम्, not fit for the enjoy-<BR>ment or use of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजस्थापित
अ-राजस्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, not allowed or licensed<BR>by government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजिन्
अ-राजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having no splendor; un-<BR>checked, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराटकी
अराटकी अराटकी, f., Ved., N. or epithet of<BR>the plant Ajaśṛṅgī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराति|अरातिः
अराति अ-राति, इस्, f. (rt. रा), Ved. the non-<BR>offering (of sacrifice); stinginess, hardness, disfavour,<BR>severity; malignity, malevolence; failure; adversity;<BR>malignity personified; particular evil spirits, who frus-<BR>trate the good intentions and disturb the happiness of<BR>man; (इस्), m. an enemy; the number ‘six.’<BR>—अराति-<BR>दूषण, अस्, ई, अम्, or अराति-दूषि, इस्, इस्, इ, or<BR>अराति-ह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. destroying enemies or ad-<BR>versity.<BR>—अराति-भङ्ग, अस्, m. defeat of a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिय
अरातिय or अरातीय, nom. P., Ved. -यति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to desire not to offer; to act like an enemy.<BR>—अरातीयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. envious, unfriendly,<BR>not offering; behaving like an enemy, striving to<BR>cause adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयु
अरातीयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not in the habit of offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीवन्
अराती-वन्, आ, m., Ved. not offering, not giving;<BR>unfriendly, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराद्धि|अराद्धिः
अराद्धि अ-राद्धि, इस्, f., Ved. transgression,<BR>sin, envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराधस्
अराधस् अ-राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. too poor<BR>to perform sacrifices, not making oblations, unkind,<BR>hard, stringy, selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराय|अरायः
अराय अ-राय, अस्, m., Ved. too poor to make<BR>oblations, obstructing a sacrifice; niggard, stingy;<BR>(अस्, ई,) m. f. any evil spirit.<BR>—अराय-क्षयण, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, Ved. overpowering malignant spirits; (अम्), n.<BR>destruction of malignant spirits.<BR>—अराय-चातन, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, Ved. destroying evil spirits; (अम्), n. destruc-<BR>tion of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल अराल, अस्, आ, अम् (connected with अर,<BR>fr. rt. ऋ; Intens. for अरार?), crooked, curved;<BR>spreading like the spoke of a wheel; (अस्), m. a<BR>bent or crooked arm; the resin of the plant Shorea<BR>Robusta; an elephant in rut; (आ), f. a disloyal or un-<BR>chaste woman; a modest woman.<BR>—अराल-पक्ष्म-<BR>नयन, अस्, आ, अम्, whose eyelashes are curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरावन्
अरावन् अ-रावन्, आ, व्णी, अ, Ved. not offering,<BR>envious, inimical, odious; an epithet of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराष्ट्र|अराष्ट्रं
अराष्ट्र अ-राष्ट्र, अम्, n., Ved. loss of royal<BR>power or of a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि 1. अरि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. ऋ), Ved. going,<BR>moving; reaching, obtaining, making an effort to get;<BR>aspiring after; desiring, sacrificing, devoted to; (इस्),<BR>m. the wind; a lord, a master; a pious man.<BR>—अरि-<BR>गूर्त, अस्, m., Ved. praised by devoted men or<BR>by worshippers; (according to others) ready for the<BR>destruction of enemies.<BR>—अरि-धायस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. willingly yielding milk (as a cow); (according<BR>to others) to be held by lords only, very precious.<BR>—अरि-ष्टुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praised with zeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि 2. अ-रि, इस्, m. (rt. रा; but by some<BR>written अरि, and identified with 1. अरि), Ved. un-<BR>generous, malicious; not worshipping; inimical, hos-<BR>tile; an enemy; a species of Khadira or Mimosa;<BR>N. of the numeral ‘six;’ N. of a condition in as-<BR>tronomy.<BR>—अरि-कर्षण, अस्, m. tamer of enemies.<BR>—अरि-कुल, अम्, n. family of an enemy.<BR>—अरि-<BR>क्षिप, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śvaphalka.<BR>—अरि-<BR>घ्न, अस्, m. a destroyer of enemies.<BR>—अरि-चिन्तन,<BR>अम्, n. or अरि-चिन्ता, f. a plot directed against an<BR>enemy, administration of foreign affairs.<BR>—अरि-ता, f.<BR>or अरि-त्व, अम्, n. enmity.<BR>—१. अरि-त्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>protecting from enemies (for 2. see next col.).<BR>—अरि-<BR>दान्त, अस्, m. enemy-subdued; N. of a man.<BR>—अरि-<BR>नन्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, gratifying an enemy, affording<BR>triumph to an enemy; an enemy's joy.<BR>—अरि-निपात,<BR>अस्, m. an invasion made by enemies.<BR>—अरि-नुत,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">Page0081-c+ 76</a>]<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, praised even by enemies.<BR>—अरिन्-दम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, conquering, victorious; (अस्), m. a con-<BR>queror of enemies; N. of a man; N. of a Muni.<BR>—अरि-पुर, अम्, n. an enemy's town or country.<BR>—अरि-मर्द, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अरि-मर्दन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, foe-trampling, enemy-destroying; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Śvaphalka.<BR>—अरि-मित्र, अस्, m.<BR>an ally or friend of an enemy.<BR>—अरिम्-एजय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Kuru, or of Śvaphalka.<BR>—अरि-मेद,<BR>अस्, m. a fetid Mimosa, Vachellia Farnesiana; N. of<BR>a country.<BR>—अरि-मेदक, अस्, m., N. of an insect.<BR>—अरि-राष्ट्र, अम्, n. an enemy's country.<BR>—अरि-<BR>लोक, अस्, m. a hostile tribe or an enemy's country.<BR>—अरि-ष्ठानक, अम्, n. consternation, defeat.<BR>—अ-<BR>रि-सूदन or अरि-हिंसक, अस्, m. destroyer of foes.<BR>—अरि-ह, अस्, m. a son of Avācīna, a son of Devātithi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्त
अरिक्त अ-रिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थभाज्
अरिक्थभाज् अ-रिक्थ-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, not en-<BR>titled to a share of property, not an heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थीय
अ-रिक्थीय, अस्, आ, अम् = the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिणिन्
अरिणिन् अरिणिन्, ई, m. a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरितृ
अरितृ अरितृ, ता, m. (fr. rt. ऋ), Ved. a<BR>rower; a helmsman [cf. Gr. ἐρέτης, ἐρετμόν, &c.;<BR>Lat. ratis, remex, &c.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
2. अरित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. propelling, driving;<BR>(अम्), n. an oar; a rudder, helm; a ship, a boat;<BR>a part of a carriage; a Soma vessel; (अस्), m. a Soma<BR>vessel; N. of a person. [For 1. see under 2. अ-रि; also<BR>cf. Lat. aratrum.]<BR>—अरित्र-गाध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>oar-deep, shallow.<BR>—अरित्र-परण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>passing over by means of oars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिन्
अरिन् अरिन्, इ, n. a wheel, a discus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिपु
अरिपु अ-रिपु, उस्, m. the father of Nala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिप्र
अरिप्र अ-रिप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. spotless,<BR>clean, clear; faultless, blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिफित
अरिफित अ-रिफित, अस्, आ, अम्, not changed<BR>to र्, said of Visarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेफ
अ-रेफ, अस्, आ, अम्, without the letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषण्य
अरिषण्य अ-रिषण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रिष्),<BR>Ved. not hurting, defending from injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषण्यत्|अरिषण्यन्त्
अ-रिषण्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. not being hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अ-रिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, unhurt; unharmed; perfect;<BR>secure, safe; (अस्), m. a heron; a crow; N. of several<BR>plants, the soap-berry tree, Sapindus Detergens Roxb.;<BR>Azadirachta Indica; garlic; a distilled mixture; N. of<BR>an Asura, son of Bali, slain by Kṛṣṇa (Viṣṇu);<BR>N. of a son of Manu Vaivasvata; (आ), f. a bandage; a<BR>medical plant; N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and one of<BR>the wives of Kaśyapa; (अम्), n. bad or ill-luck, mis-<BR>fortune; a natural phenomenon boding misfortune;<BR>sign or symptom of approaching death; good fortune,<BR>happiness; buttermilk; vinous spirit; a woman's<BR>apartment, the lying-in chamber.<BR>—अरिष्ट-कर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a king of the Andhra dynasty.<BR>—अ-<BR>रिष्ट-गातु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having a secure residence.<BR>—अरिष्ट-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. whose cattle are un-<BR>hurt.<BR>—अरिष्ट-गृह, अम्, n. a lying-in chamber.<BR>—अरिष्ट-ग्राम, अस्, m., Ved. whose troop is com-<BR>plete in number (said of the Maruts).<BR>—अरिष्ट-<BR>ताति, इस्, f., Ved. safeness, security; (इस्, इस्, इ), auspi-<BR>cious, making fortunate or happy.<BR>—अरिष्ट-दुष्ट-<BR>धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, apprehensive of death, alarmed at its<BR>approach.<BR>—अरिष्ट-नेमि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. the felly<BR>of whose wheel is unhurt; an epithet of Tārkṣya;<BR>the twenty-second of the twenty-four Jaina Tīrtha-<BR>kāras of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR>—अरिष्ट-पुर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town.<BR>—अरिष्ट-भर्मन्, आ, m., Ved.<BR>yielding security.<BR>—अरिष्ट-मथन, अस्, m. Viṣṇu<BR>(Śiva?) as killer of the Asura.<BR>—अरिष्ट-रथ, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. whose carriage is unhurt.<BR>—अरिष्ट-वीर, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. whose heroes are unhurt.<BR>—अरिष्ट-शय्या,<BR>f. a lying-in couch.<BR>—अरिष्ट-सूदन, अस्, m. or<BR>अरिष्ट-हन्, आ, m. Viṣṇu as killer of the Asura.<BR>—अरिष्टा-श्रित-पुर (˚ट-आश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—अरिष्टासु (˚ट-असु˚), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. whose<BR>vital power is unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टक|अरिष्टकः
अ-रिष्टक, अस्, m. the same as अरिष्ट, m. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टि|अरिष्टिः
अ-रिष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. safeness, security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्यत्|अरिष्यन्त्
