अरुन्धती|अरुंधती
अरुन्धती अ-रुन्धती, f. (rt. रुध्), a medi-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-b" target="_blank">Page0082-b+ 70</a>]<BR>cinal climbing plant; the wife of Vasiṣṭha; the wife<BR>of Dharma; the morning star, personified as the wife<BR>of Vasiṣṭha or of the seven Ṛṣis; also one of the<BR>Pleiades. At marriage ceremonies Arundhatī is in-<BR>voked as a pattern of conjugal excellence by the bride-<BR>groom.<BR>—अरुन्धती-जानि, इस्, or अरुन्धती-नाथ,<BR>अस्, m. Vasiṣṭha, one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints,<BR>and stars in the great bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

