अ-रोचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, not shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचिष्णु
अ-रोचिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, dark, disagreeable, ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोदन
अरोदन अ-रोदन, अम्, n. (rt. रुद्), not<BR>weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोध्य
अरोध्य अ-रोध्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रुध्), not<BR>to be hindered or obstructed, unobstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोपण
अरोपण अ-रोपण, अम्, n. (rt. रुह्), not<BR>planting or fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोष|अरोषः
अरोष अ-रोष, अस्, m. calmness, gentleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरौद्र
अरौद्र अ-रौद्र, अस्, ई, अम्, not formidable<BR>or fierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क्
अर्क् अर्क्, cl. 10. P. अर्कयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>heat or warm; to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क अर्क, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अर्च्), a ray, flash of<BR>lightning; the sun; fire; crystal; copper; a N. of<BR>Indra; Sunday; membrum virile; N. of the plant<BR>Calotropis Gigantea; a religious ceremony; praise,<BR>hymn; praising; a singer; a learned man; an elder<BR>brother; food.<BR>—अर्क-कान्ता, f., N. of the plant<BR>Polanisia Icosandra W.<BR>—अर्क-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>field of the sun,’ N. of a sacred place in Orissa.<BR>—अर्क-चिकित्सा, f. ‘the medical art of the sun,’ title<BR>of a work on medicine.<BR>—अर्क-ज, औ, m. du. the<BR>two sons of Sūrya or the sun and Aśvinī, and physi-<BR>cians of Svarga or heaven.<BR>—अर्क-तनय, अस्, m.<BR>offspring of the sun, an epithet of Karṇa, Manu<BR>Vaivasvata, Manu Sāvarṇi, and Śani; (आ), f. an epithet<BR>of the rivers Yamunā and Tapatī.<BR>—अर्क-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. brightness, &c.<BR>—अर्क-त्विष्, ट्, f. a ray of light,<BR>the light of the sun.<BR>—अर्क-दिन, अम्, n. a solar<BR>day.<BR>—अर्क-नन्दन, अस्, m. a son of the sun; a<BR>N. of the planet Saturn; an epithet of Karṇa.<BR>—अर्क-<BR>नयन, अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—अर्क-पत्त्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the plant Calotropis Gigantea; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of birth-wort, Aristolochia Indica; (अम्), n.<BR>the leaf of the plant Calotropis Gigantea.<BR>—अर्क-<BR>पर्ण, अस्, m. the plant Calotropis Gigantea; (अम्),<BR>n. the leaf of this plant.<BR>—अर्क-पादप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the tree Melia Azadirachta Lin.<BR>—अर्क-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. the child of the sun, i. e. Karṇa.<BR>—अर्क-<BR>पुष्पिका, f., N. of the plant Gynandropsis Penta-<BR>phylla.<BR>—अर्क-पुष्पी, f., N. of the plant Kuṭumbinī.<BR>—अर्क-प्रकाश, अस्, m. ‘the revelation of the<BR>sun,’ title of a work on medicine and jurisprudence.<BR>—अर्क-प्रिया, f., N. of the plant Hibiscus Rosa<BR>Sinensis L.<BR>—अर्क-बन्धु, उस्, or अर्क-बान्धव,<BR>अस्, m. a N. of Buddha Śākya-muni.<BR>—अर्क-भक्ता,<BR>f., N. of the plant Polanisia Icosandra W. and A.<BR>—अर्क-मण्डल, अम्, n. the disc of the sun.<BR>—अर्क-मूला, f. a kind of birth-wort, Aristolochia<BR>Indica.<BR>—अर्क-रेतो-ज, अस्, m. Revanta, the son of<BR>Sūrya.<BR>—अर्क-लूष, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अर्क-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing flashes of lightning.<BR>—अर्क-वर्ष, अस्, m. a solar year.<BR>—अर्क-वल्ल-<BR>भ, अस्, m., N. of the plant Pentapetes Phœnicea<BR>Lin.<BR>—अर्क-वेध, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अर्क-<BR>व्रत, अस्, m. the rule or law of the sun; i. e. levy-<BR>ing taxes, subjecting the people to imposts, or drawing<BR>their wealth as imperceptibly as the sun evaporates<BR>water.<BR>—अर्क-शोक, अस्, m., Ved. brilliancy of rays.<BR>—अर्क-साति, इस्, f., Ved. invention of hymns, poetical<BR>inspiration.<BR>—अर्क-सूनु, उस्, m. son of the sun, an<BR>epithet of Yama.<BR>—अर्क-सोदर, अस्, m. Airāvata,<BR>the elephant of Indra.<BR>—अर्क-हिता, f., N. of the<BR>plant Polanisia Icosandra W.<BR>—अर्कांश (˚क-अं˚),<BR>अस्, m. a digit or the twelfth part of the sun's disc.<BR>—अर्काश्मन् (˚क-अश्˚), आ, m. heliotrope, girasol,<BR>crystal.<BR>—अर्काह्व (˚का-आह्˚) अस्, m. swallow wort.<BR>—अर्केन्दु-सङ्गम (˚क-इन्˚), अस्, m. the instant<BR>of conjunction of the sun and moon.<BR>—अर्कोपल<BR>(˚क-उप्˚), अस्, m. the sun-stone, a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्किन्
अर्किन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. shining; praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कीय
अर्कीय or अर्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to अर्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गड|अर्गडः
अर्गड अर्गड, अस्, आ, m. f. (for अर्गल), an<BR>impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल|अर्गलं|अर्गलः
अर्गल अर्गल, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, m. f. n. (said<BR>to be fr. rt. अर्ज्), a wooden bolt or pin for fastening<BR>a door or the cover of a vessel; a bar; a wave or billow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलिका
अर्गलिका, f. a small door pin, a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलित
अर्गलित, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened by a bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलीय
अर्गलीय or अर्गल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>a bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्
अर्घ् अर्घ्, cl. 1. P. अर्घति, -घितुम्, to<BR>be worth, to cost; to hurt ? [cf. Germ. arg,<BR>ārgern; Old Germ. arg, ark, and with a inserted,<BR>arag, arak, miserly, wicked, impious; arg, evil].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ अर्घ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अर्ह्), worth,<BR>value, price; a respectful offering of various ingre-<BR>dients to a god or Brāhman.<BR>—अर्घ-दान, अम्,<BR>n. presentation of a respectful offering.<BR>—अर्घ-<BR>बलाबल (˚ल-अब्˚), अम्, n. rate of price, proper<BR>price, the cheapness or dearness of commodities.<BR>—अर्घ-सङ्ख्यापन, अम्, n. fixing the price of<BR>commodities, appraising, assize: it is the act of the<BR>king or ruler, in concert with the traders, and should<BR>be done once a week or once a fortnight.<BR>—अर्घार्ह<BR>(˚घ-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of or requiring a<BR>respectful offering, a superior.<BR>—अर्घाष्ट-पुरक<BR>(˚घ-अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—अर्घीश<BR>(˚घ-ईश?), अस्, m. a N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, valuable; venerable; deserving<BR>a respectful oblation; (अम्), n. a respectful oblation<BR>to gods or venerable men, of rice, dūrva-grass, flowers,<BR>&c., with water; or of water only in a small boat-<BR>shaped vessel; a kind of honey.<BR>—अर्घ्य-तस्, ind.<BR>of true value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घट|अर्घटं
अर्घट अर्घट, अम्, n. ashes. See पार्घट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्
अर्च् अर्च्, cl. 1. P. अर्चति, आनर्च, अर्चिष्-<BR>यति, आर्चीत्, अर्चितुम्, to shine; to praise;<BR>to honour or treat with respect, to worship; to salute:<BR>Caus. अर्चयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to shine; to<BR>praise; to honour; worship, salute: Desid. अर्चिचिषति,<BR>to wish to honour: Ved. Pass. ऋच्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च|अर्च्च
अर्च, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining. See also अर्चा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक, अस्, आ, अम्, worshipping; (अस्), m. a wor-<BR>shipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चत्रि
अर्चत्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. sounding, neighing, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चत्र्य
अर्चत्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चद्धूम
अर्चद्-धूम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. whose smoke is<BR>shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चन|अर्च्चनं
अर्चन, अस्, ई, अम्, praising, celebrating with praise;<BR>(आ or अम्), f. n. worship, the homage paid to deities<BR>and to superiors.<BR>—अर्चनानस् (˚न-अन्˚), आस्, m.,<BR>Ved., N. of a Ṛṣi (‘he who has a sounding carriage’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनीय
अर्चनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be worshipped, respect-<BR>able, venerable, adorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा, f. worship, adoration; an image or idol<BR>destined to be worshipped.<BR>—अर्चा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>worshipped.<BR>—अर्चा-विडम्बन, अम्, n. false or<BR>feigned worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चि|अर्चिः|अर्च्चिः
अर्चि, इस्, m. ray, flame (of fire or of the dawn, &c.).<BR>—अर्चि-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अर्चि-नेत्रा-<BR>धिपति (˚र-अध्˚), इस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—अर्चि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, shining, blazing; (आन्), m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—अर्चि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. blazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चित|अर्च्चितः
अर्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured, worshipped, respected,<BR>saluted; offered with reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चितिन्
अर्चितिन्, ई, इनी, इ, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चितृ
अर्चितृ, ता, m. a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिन्
अर्चिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. praising, honouring; shining<BR>(as a ray of light), radiating; (ई), m., N. of a man;<BR>a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस्, इस्, f. n. ray of light, flame; light, lustre;<BR>(इस्), f., N. of the wife of Kṛśāśva and mother of<BR>Dhūmaketu.<BR>—अर्चिष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, brilliant,<BR>resplendent; (आन्), m. fire, the god of fire; (अती),<BR>f. one of the ten earths with Buddhists.<BR>.1. अर्च्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured or worshipped.<BR>.2. अर्च्य, ind. having honoured or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
अर्ज् 1. अर्ज्, cl. 1. P. अर्जति, आनर्ज, अर्जिष्-<BR>यति, -जितुम्, to procure; to acquire, reach,<BR>gain, earn: Caus. अर्जयति, -यितुम्, to procure, ac-<BR>quire; to work or manufacture; to make or prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक, अस्, इका, अम्, procuring, acquiring; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of several plants, Ocymum Gratissimum L.,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जन|अर्जनं|अर्ज्जनं
अर्जन, अम्, n. procuring; acquiring, gaining,<BR>earning; gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जित
अर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, acquired, gained, earned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
अर्ज् 2. अर्ज् (a doubtful root, probably<BR>distinct from the last, and connected with<BR>रज्, राज्, and अर्च्), to shine, to be white (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, white, clear, the colour<BR>of day; of silver; (अस्), m. the white colour; a<BR>peacock; cutaneous disease; the tree Terminalia<BR>Arjuna W. and A.; a N. of Indra; N. of the third<BR>of the Pāṇḍava princes, who was a son of Indra and<BR>Kuntī; N. of a son of Kṛtavīrya, who was slain by<BR>Paraśurāma; N. of a Śākya; N. of a country; the<BR>only son of his mother; (ई), f. a procuress, a bawd;<BR>cow; a kind of serpent; Uṣā wife of Aniruddha; N.<BR>of a river, more commonly called Bāhudā or Karatoyā;<BR>(न्यौ or न्यस्), du. or pl., N. of the constellation<BR>Phalgunī; (अम्), n. silver; gold; slight inflammation<BR>of the conjunctiva or white of the eye; grass; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of Arjuna.<BR>—अर्जुन-काण्ड, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having a white appendage.<BR>—अर्जुन-<BR>च्छवि, इस्, इस्, इ, of a white colour, white.<BR>—अर्जुन-<BR>तस्, ind. on the side or party of Arjuna.<BR>—अर्जुन-<BR>ध्वज, अस्, m. having a white banner, an epithet of<BR>Hanumat.<BR>—अर्जुन-पाकी, f., N. of a plant and its<BR>fruits.<BR>—अर्जुनारिष्ट-सञ्छन्न (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, covered with Arjuna and Nimb trees.<BR>—अर्जुनो-<BR>पम (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, m. the teak tree, Tectona<BR>Grandis L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनक|अर्जुनकः
अर्जुनक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Arjuna; (अस्),<BR>m. a worshipper of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनस
अर्जुनस, अस्, आ, अम्, overgrown with Arjuna<BR>plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ण|अर्णः
अर्ण अर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ऋ), being in<BR>motion, agitated; foaming, effervescing; restless;<BR>(अस्), m. a wave, flood, stream; the teak tree, Tec-<BR>tona Grandis L.; a letter; N. of a metre, comprising<BR>ten feet, and belonging to the class called Daṇḍaka;<BR>N. of a man; (अम्), n. tumult or din of battle.<BR>—अर्ण-साति, इस्, f., Ved. tumult of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णव|अर्णवः|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव, अस्, आ, अम्, being agitated; foaming;<BR>restless; (अस्), m. a wave, flood, stream; the foaming<BR>sea, high water; the ocean of air; N. of a metre;<BR>title of a work on jurisprudence.<BR>—अर्णव-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, sea-born, marine; (अस्, अम्), m. n. cuttle fish.<BR>—अर्णव-पोत, अस्, m. a boat or ship.<BR>—अर्णव-<BR>मन्दिर, अस्, m. an epithet of Varuṇa, regent of<BR>the waters.<BR>—अर्णव-यान, अम्, n. a boat or ship.<BR>—अर्णवान्त (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. the extremity of<BR>the ocean.<BR>—अर्णवोधव (˚व-उद्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्
अर्णस्, अस्, n. a wave, flood, stream; the sea, ocean;<BR>the ocean of air; river, water.<BR>—अर्णस्-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. containing many waves.<BR>—अर्णो-द, अस्, m.<BR>a cloud; N. of the plant Cyperus Rotundus.<BR>—अर्णो-<BR>भव, अस्, m. a shell.<BR>—अर्णो-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. in-<BR>cluding the waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तगल|अर्तगलः|अर्त्तगल|अर्त्तगलः
अर्तगल अर्त-गल, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>Barleria cærulea Roxb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तन|अर्त्तन|अर्त्तनं
अर्तन अर्तन, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ऋत्), blaming,<BR>reviling; (अम्), n. censure, approach, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तुक|अर्त्तुक
अर्तुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. provoking, contentious,<BR>quarrelsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ति|अर्तिः|अर्त्ति|अर्त्तिः
अर्ति अर्ति, इस्, f. (a weakened form of आर्ति,<BR>fr. rt. ऋ with आ), pain; the end of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तिका|अर्त्तिका
अर्तिका अर्तिका, f. an elder sister (in theatri-<BR>cal language), [cf. अत्तिका and अन्तिका].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्
अर्थ् अर्थ्, cl. 10. A. अर्थयते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. आर्तिथत, ep. cl. 1. A. अर्थते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-c" target="_blank">Page0083-c+ 81</a>]<BR>थितुम्, to strive to obtain, to desire, wish, request;<BR>to supplicate or entreat any one, to sue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ, अस्, अम्, m. n., in Ṛg-veda generally n.,<BR>but in later Sanskrit only m. (said to be fr. rt. ऋ,<BR>but connected with rt. अर्थ्), object; purpose; cause,<BR>motive, reason; advantage, use, utility; thing; sub-<BR>stance, wealth, property, opulence; affair, concern;<BR>request, suit, petition; asking, begging, want, need;<BR>sense, meaning, notion; manner, sort, kind; pro-<BR>hibition, prevention, abolition; price; N. of a son<BR>of Dharma. (अर्थ in some of its first senses<BR>may govern an inst. case; e. g. को मे जीवितेन<BR>अर्थः, ‘what concern have I with life?’).<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>कर, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, producing or yielding<BR>advantage or wealth; useful; enriching.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. a principal or main action.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>काम, औ, m. du. utility and desire, wealth and plea-<BR>sure; (अस्, आ, अम्), desirous of wealth.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>कृच्छ्र, अम्, n. a difficult matter.<BR>—अर्थ-कृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, causing profit, useful.<BR>—अर्थ-कृत्या, अम्, f. n.<BR>an action aiming at profit.<BR>—अर्थ-गत, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>(= गतार्थ), without an object, useless.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>गरीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, highly significant.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, wasteful, extravagant.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>जात, अस्, आ, अम्, significant, full of meaning;<BR>worth the money.<BR>—अर्थ-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, under-<BR>standing the meaning of anything.<BR>—अर्थ-तत्त्व,<BR>अम्, n. truth, the real object, nature or cause of any-<BR>thing; the true state of the case, the fact of the matter.<BR>—अर्थ-तस्, ind. towards a particular object; with<BR>reference to the meaning; in fact, really, truly;<BR>namely, that is to say; on account of, (at the end<BR>of a compound).<BR>—अर्थ-द, अस्, आ, अम्, conferring<BR>advantage; profitable, useful, complaint, favourable;<BR>liberal, munificent.<BR>—अर्थ-दूषण, अम्, n. spoil-<BR>ing of another's property; unjust seizure of property,<BR>or a withholding of what is due; waste, prodigality,<BR>extravagance; finding fault with the meaning of<BR>a passage.<BR>—अर्थ-निबन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>its cause in wealth, contingent on affluence and re-<BR>spectability.<BR>—अर्थ-निश्चय, अस्, m. determination,<BR>decision.<BR>—अर्थ-पति, इस्, m. the lord of riches;<BR>a king; an epithet of Kuvera; N. of a man.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>पर, अस्, आ, अम्, intent on gaining wealth; parsi-<BR>monious, niggardly.<BR>—अर्थ-प्रयोग, अस्, m. appli-<BR>cation of wealth, as, to trade, usury, &c.; the profession<BR>of usury.<BR>—अर्थ-प्राप्ति, इस्, f. acquisition of wealth;<BR>attainment of an object.<BR>—अर्थ-बन्ध, अस्, m. that<BR>which binds together the sense; the text.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, selfish.<BR>—अर्थ-बोध, अस्, m. in-<BR>dication of the real import.<BR>—अर्थ-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, en-<BR>titled to a share in the division of property.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, having high wages (as a servant).<BR>—अर्थ-भेद, अस्, m. distinction, difference of mean-<BR>ing.<BR>—अर्थ-मात्र, आ, अम्, f. n. property, money.<BR>—अर्थ-लाभ, अस्, m. acquisition of wealth.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>लुब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, greedy of wealth, covetous, nig-<BR>gardly.<BR>—अर्थ-लेश, अस्, m. a little wealth.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>लोभ, अस्, m. desire of wealth, avarice.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, wealthy, rich; significant, full of<BR>sense or meaning; (आन्), m. a man; (-वत्), ind.<BR>according to a purpose.<BR>—अर्थवत्-त्व, अम्, n. sig-<BR>nificance, importance.<BR>—अर्थवर्गीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>concerning the category of objects.<BR>—अर्थ-वाद,<BR>अस्, m. explanation of an affair, explanatory remark,<BR>exegesis; affirmation or narrative; declaration of<BR>purpose or object; speech or expression having a<BR>certain object; sentence; praise, eulogium.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>विज्ञान, अम्, n. comprehension of meaning, one of<BR>the six exercises of the understanding.<BR>—अर्थ-विद्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, sagacious, sensible, wise.<BR>—अर्थ-विनिश्चय, अस्,<BR>m. title of a Buddhist Sūtra work.<BR>—अर्थ-वृद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. accumulation of wealth.<BR>—अर्थ-वैकल्प, अम्<BR>n. deviation from truth, perversion or disguise of fact;<BR>prevarication.<BR>—अर्थ-व्यय, अस्, m. expenditure.<BR>—अर्थ-व्यय-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, liberal in giving<BR>and using.<BR>—अर्थ-व्यय-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, prodigal.<BR>—अर्थ-शास्त्र, अम्, n. institutes of the science of<BR>what is useful in life; science of polity or moral<BR>and political government.<BR>—अर्थ-शौच, अम्, n.<BR>purity, honesty in money matters.<BR>—अर्थ-सं-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">Page0084-a+ 80</a>]<BR>थान, अम्, n. accumulation of wealth; treasury.<BR>—अर्थ-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. accumulation of wealth;<BR>treasure.<BR>—अर्थ-सञ्चय, अस्, m. acquisition of<BR>wealth; wealth, property.<BR>—अर्थ-सम्बन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. connection of the sense with the word or sentence.<BR>—अर्थ-साधक, अस्, m. bringing any matter to<BR>a conclusion; N. of a minister of king Daśaratha.<BR>—अर्थ-सार, अस्, m. a considerable property.<BR>—अर्थ-सिद्धक, अस्, m., N. of the plant Vitex<BR>Negundo L.<BR>—अर्थ-सिद्धि, इस्, f. success.<BR>—अर्थ-<BR>हर, अस्, आ, अम्, inheriting or taking wealth.<BR>—अर्-<BR>थ-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, unmeaning, nonsensical; poor,<BR>deprived of wealth; failing.<BR>—अर्थागम (˚थ-आग्˚),<BR>अस्, m. receipt or collection of property; income, ac-<BR>quisition of wealth.<BR>—अर्थाधिकार (˚थ-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. office of treasurer, charge of money or property.<BR>—अर्थाधिकारिन् (˚थ-अध्˚), ई, m. a treasurer,<BR>a paymaster.<BR>—अर्थान्तर (˚थ-अन्˚), अम्, n. an-<BR>other matter, a different or new circumstance, a new<BR>affair; a different meaning; opposite or antithetical<BR>meaning, difference of meaning or purport.<BR>—अर्-<BR>थान्तर-न्यास, अस्, m. antithesis.<BR>—अर्थान्वित<BR>(˚थ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of wealth, rich;<BR>significant.<BR>—अर्थापत्ति (˚थ-आप्˚), इस्, f. an infer-<BR>ence from circumstances; one of the five arguments<BR>of the Mīmāṃsakas; presumption, supposition.<BR>—अर्-<BR>थार्थिन् (˚थ-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, one who solicits wealth,<BR>or endeavours to gain any object.<BR>—अर्थेत् (˚थ-इत्),<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. active, industrious; hasty.<BR>—अर्थेप्सु<BR>(˚थ-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of wealth.<BR>—अर्थेप्सु-<BR>ता, f. desire of wealth.<BR>—अर्थेहा (˚थ-ईहा˚), f. desire<BR>of wealth.<BR>—अर्थोपम (˚थ-उप्˚), अम्, n. a simile<BR>in which the object of comparision, is stated without any<BR>particle of comparison, e. g. ‘he is a dog.’<BR>—अर्थो-<BR>पार्जन (˚थ-उप्˚), अम्, n. acquisition of wealth<BR>or property.<BR>—अर्थोष्मन् (˚थ-उष्˚), अ, n. wealth,<BR>the glow or pride of wealth, the condition of being<BR>wealthy; (so, Anglice, ‘a warm man’).<BR>—अर्थौघ<BR>(˚थ-ओघ्˚), अस्, m. a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना, f. request, begging, asking, entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनीय
अर्थनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be requested, asked, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थम्
अर्थम् or अर्थे, ind. (generally at the end of com-<BR>pounds) on account of, in behalf of, for the sake of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थात्
अर्थात्, ind. according to the state of the case, ac-<BR>cording to the circumstances, as a matter of fact; in<BR>fact; that is to say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापय
अर्थापय, nom. P. अर्थापयति, -यितुम्. See<BR>rt. अर्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाय
अर्थाय, ind. on account of, for the sake of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिक|अर्थिकः
अर्थिक, अस्, m. a crier, a watchman, a minstrel,<BR>a servant, whose duty it is to announce, by song or<BR>music, fixed periods of the day, such as the hours of<BR>rising and going to rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित
अर्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, asked, desired, requested;<BR>(अम्), n. wish, desire, supplication, petition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थितव्य
अर्थितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be asked, requested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who seeks to effect or gain<BR>a purpose or object; one who asks or begs for any-<BR>thing (with inst.); desirous of (with inst.); sup-<BR>plicating or entreating any one (with gen.); a beg-<BR>gar, a petitioner, suitor; a plaintiff, a prosecutor; a<BR>servant; a follower, a companion or partizan.<BR>—अर्-<BR>थि-ता, f. the condition of a beggar, asking, wishing;<BR>begging.<BR>—अर्थि-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of a sup-<BR>pliant.<BR>—अर्थि-सात्, ind. with कृ, to dispose of any-<BR>thing in favour of one who asks or begs for it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थीय
अर्थीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (as last member of a com-<BR>pound) destined for; relating to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थे
अर्थे, ind. on account of; see अर्थम्.<BR>—अर्थे-<BR>कृ, to act on behalf of (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper, fit; rich; to be asked<BR>or sought for; intelligent, wise; (अम्), n. red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् अर्द् cl. 1. P. अर्दति, आनर्द, आर्दि-<BR>ष्यति, आर्दीत्, अर्दितुम्, Ved. 3. pl. impv.<BR>ऋअन्तु and cl. 7. P. ऋणत्ति, to move; to be moved;<BR>to be scattered as dust; to dissolve; to go; to ask,<BR>beg; to torment, hurt, kill: Caus. अर्दयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to make agitated or restless; to stir up, shake<BR>vehemently; to distort; to torment, distress; to strike,<BR>hurt, kill: Desid. अर्दिदिषति [cf. Lat. ardeo].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दन|अर्दनं|अर्दनः|अर्द्दन
अर्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, moving restlessly; disturbing,<BR>distressing; (आ), f. going; asking, begging, giving<BR>pain, killing; (अम्), n. pain, trouble, excitement, dis-<BR>turbance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनि|अर्दनिः
अर्दनि, इस्, m. sickness, disease; asking, begging;<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दित|अर्दितं|अर्द्दित|अर्द्दितः
अर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; asked, requested, beg-<BR>ged; killed, injured, pained, afflicted; (अम्), n. a<BR>disease, spasm of the jaw-bones; trismus, tetanus;<BR>or hemiplegia, i. e. paralysis of the muscles on one<BR>side of the face and neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दितिन्|अर्द्दितिन्
अर्दितिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having spasms of the jaw-bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्यमान
अर्द्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
अर्ध 1. अर्ध, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. ऋध्),<BR>Ved. side, part; place, region, country [cf. Lat. ordo,<BR>Germ. ort]. The accent is on the first syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
2. अर्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, half, halved, forming a half<BR>[cf. Osset. ardag]; अर्ध अर्ध, one part, the other<BR>part; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the half; one part of two, a<BR>part, a party; half; a short syllable. The accent is<BR>on the last syllable. (अर्ध may be compounded in<BR>a peculiar way with an ordinal, e. g. अर्ध-तृतीय,<BR>containing (two and) the third (only) half, i. e. two<BR>and a half; अर्ध-चतुर्थ, three and a half, &c.)<BR>—अर्ध-काल or अर्ध-कूट, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—अर्ध-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, half-done, half-<BR>performed.<BR>—अर्ध-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a Rudra.<BR>—अर्ध-कोटी, f. half a crore, five millions.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-कोष, अस्, m. a moiety of one's treasure.<BR>—अर्ध-क्रोश, अस्, m. half a league.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>खार, अम्, ई, n. f. a measure, half a khārī.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>गङ्गा, f., N. of the river Kāverī.<BR>—अर्ध-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. in the middle of the womb.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-गुच्छ, अस्, m. a necklace of twenty-four<BR>strings.<BR>—अर्ध-गोल, अस्, m. a hemisphere.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-चक्रवर्तिन् or अर्ध-चक्रिन्, ई, m. half a<BR>cakravartin; N. of the nine black Vāsudevas and the<BR>nine enemies of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अर्ध-चन्द्र, अस्, m.<BR>half-moon; the semicircular marks on a peacock's<BR>tail; the semicircular scratch of the finger nail; an<BR>arrow, the head of which is like a half-moon; the<BR>hand bent into a semicircle or the shape of a claw, as<BR>for the purpose of seizing or clutching anything; (आ),<BR>f., N. of the plant Convolvulus Torpethum; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), crescent-shaped, of a semilunar form.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>चन्द्राकार (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, or अर्ध-<BR>चन्द्राकृति, इस्, इस्, इ, half-moon-shaped, crescent-<BR>shaped; (अस्), m. or (इस्), f. a meniscus.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a climbing plant.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>चोलक, अस्, m. a short bodice.<BR>—अर्ध-जाह्नवी, f.,<BR>N. of the river Kāverī.<BR>—अर्ध-तनु, उस्, f. half a<BR>body.<BR>—अर्ध-तिक्त, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-तूर, अस्, m. a particular kind of musical instru-<BR>ment.<BR>—अर्ध-दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, half-burnt.<BR>—अर्ध-दिवस, अस्, m. half a day, midday; a<BR>day containing one half of a whole day, a day of<BR>twelve hours.<BR>—अर्ध-देव, अस्, m., Ved. demi-god.<BR>—अर्ध-धार, अम्, n. a knife or lancet with a<BR>single edge, the blade two inches long, the handle six.<BR>—अर्ध-नारायण, अस्, m. a form of Viṣṇu.<BR>—अर्ध-नारीश (˚री-ईश), अस्, m. one of the forms<BR>of Śiva (half male and half female).<BR>—अर्ध-नाव,<BR>अम्, n. half a boat.<BR>—अर्ध-निशा, f. midnight.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-पञ्चाशत्, f. twenty-five.<BR>—अर्ध-पण, अम्,<BR>n. a measure containing half a paṇa.<BR>—अर्ध-पथ,<BR>अम्, n. half-way; (ए), ind. midway.<BR>—अर्ध-पादिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having only half a foot.<BR>—अर्ध-पारा-<BR>वत, अस्, m. a kind of pigeon.<BR>—अर्ध-पुलायित, अम्,<BR>n. a half-gallop, canter.<BR>—अर्ध-पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>half-full.<BR>—अर्ध-प्रहर, अस्, m. half a watch, one<BR>hour and a half.<BR>—अर्ध-बृहती, f., Ved. half the<BR>usual breadth.<BR>—अर्ध-भाग, अस्, m. a half; a<BR>part.<BR>—अर्ध-भागिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or अर्ध-भा-<BR>गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, taking or sharing half.<BR>—अर्ध-भाज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, taking or sharing half; (क्), m. a sharer,<BR>companion.<BR>—अर्ध-भास्कर, अस्, m. midday.<BR>—अर्ध-भोटिक, f. a kind of cake.<BR>—अर्ध-मा-<BR>गधी, f. a variety of the Māgadhī dialect.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>माणव or अर्ध-माणवक, अस्, m. a necklace of<BR>twelve strings.<BR>—अर्ध-मात्रा, f. half a short sylla-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">Page0084-c+ 79</a>]<BR>ble.<BR>—अर्ध-मार्गे, ind. half-way, midway.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-मास, अस्, m. half a month; अर्धमास-शस्,<BR>ind. every half month, or fortnight.<BR>—अर्धमास-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, or अर्धमासिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>done or happening every half month; lasting half<BR>a month, or a fortnight.<BR>—अर्ध-मुष्टि, इस्, m. f.<BR>a half-clenched hand.<BR>—अर्ध-याम, अस्, m. half a<BR>watch, an hour and a half.<BR>—अर्ध-रथ, अस्, m.<BR>a warrior who fights on a car along with another.<BR>—अर्ध-रात्र, अस्, m. midnight; a night contain-<BR>ing half a whole day of twenty-four hours.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>रात्र-समय, अस्, m. the time of midnight.<BR>—अर्-<BR>धरात्रार्धदिवस (˚रात्र-अर्ध˚), अम्, n. the<BR>equinox.<BR>—अर्धर्च (˚ध-ऋच), अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>half a verse or hemistich.<BR>—अर्धर्च-शस्, ind. in<BR>every hemistich.<BR>—अर्ध-वस्त्र-संवीत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, clothed or enveloped in half-garments.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>विसर्ग, अस्, m. the sound Visarga before क्, ख्, प्,<BR>फ्, so called because its sign (Z) is the half of that<BR>of Visarga (ः).<BR>—अर्ध-वीक्षण, अम्, n. a side-<BR>look, a glance, a leer.<BR>—अर्ध-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>middle-aged.<BR>—अर्ध-वैनाशिक, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>followers of Kaṇāda (‘arguing half-perishableness’).<BR>—अर्ध-व्यास, अस्, m. the radius of a circle.<BR>—अर्ध-शत, अम्, n. fifty; one hundred and<BR>fifty.<BR>—अर्धशन, अम्, for अर्धाशन (˚ध-<BR>अश्˚), अम्, n. half a meal.<BR>—अर्ध-शफर, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of fish.<BR>—अर्ध-शब्द, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing a low voice.<BR>—अर्ध-शेष or अर्धावशेष<BR>(˚ध-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having only half left.<BR>—अर्-<BR>धाश्याम, अस्, आ, अम्, half-clouded.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>श्लोक, अस्, m. half a Śloka.<BR>—अर्ध-सञ्जात-शस्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having its crops half-grown.<BR>—अर्ध-<BR>सीरिन्, ई, m. a cultivator, a ploughman, who takes<BR>half the crop for his labour.<BR>—अर्ध-हार, अस्,<BR>m. a necklace of sixty-four or of forty strings.<BR>—अर्-<BR>ध-ह्रस्व, अम्, n. half a short syllable.<BR>—अर्-<BR>धांश (˚ध-अं˚), अस्, m. a half, the half.<BR>—अर्-<BR>धांशिन् (˚ध-अं˚),ई, इनी, इ, sharing a half.<BR>—अर्धा-<BR>कार (˚ध-अ˚), अस्, m. half the letter अ; another<BR>name for अवग्रह, q. v.<BR>—अर्धाङ्ग (˚ध-अङ्˚),<BR>अम्, n. half the body.<BR>—अर्धार्ध (˚ध-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. half of a half, a quarter; half and half.<BR>—अर्-<BR>धावभेदक (˚ध-अव्˚), अस्, m. pain in half the<BR>head, hemicrania; (अम्), n. dividing in equal parts.<BR>—अर्धावशेष (˚ध-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>only one half left.<BR>—अर्धाशन (˚ध-अश्˚), अम्,<BR>n. half a meal.<BR>—अर्धासन (˚ध-आस्˚), अम्, n.<BR>half a seat (it is considered a mark of high respect to<BR>make room for a guest on the same seat with one's<BR>self); greeting kindly or with respect; exemption<BR>from censure.<BR>—अर्धेन्दु (˚ध-इन्˚), उस्, m. a half-<BR>moon or crescent; the semicircular impression of a<BR>finger nail; an arrow with a crescent-shaped head;<BR>the hand expanded in a semicircular from like a claw.<BR>—अर्धेन्दु-मौलि (˚ध-इन्˚), इस्, m. Śiva, whose<BR>diadem is a half-moon.<BR>—अर्धेन्द्र (˚ध-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, that of which a half belongs to Indra.<BR>—अर्धोक्त (˚ध-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, half-uttered, said<BR>imperfectly or indistinctly.<BR>—अर्धोक्ति (˚ध-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. speaking indistinctly or incompletely, broken<BR>or interrupted speech.<BR>—अर्धोदय (˚ध-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the rising of the half-moon.<BR>—अर्धोदित<BR>(˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम् (rt. इ with उद्), half-risen;<BR>(rt. वद्), half-uttered.<BR>—अर्धोरुक (˚ध-ऊरु),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, reaching to the middle of the thighs;<BR>(अम्), n. a short petticoat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धक
अर्धक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the same as अर्ध.<BR>—अर्धक-घातिन्, ई, m., N. of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धङ्कृ
अर्धङ्-कृ, cl. 8. P., Ved. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to prefer, to favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धिक|अर्धिकः
अर्धिक, अस्, ई, अम्, measuring a half, relating to<BR>a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धिन्
अर्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, entitled to half or sharing a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धुक
अर्धुक अर्धुक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ऋध्), Ved.<BR>succeeding, prospering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध्य
अर्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be accomplished; to be<BR>obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पय
अर्पय अर्पय, Caus. of rt. ऋ; अर्पयति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">Page0085-a+ 75</a>]<BR>-यितुम्, to throw, cast; insert, fix; pierce, place in<BR>or upon; offer, deliver, consign, entrust, give back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पण|अर्पणं
अर्पण, अम्, n. throwing, casting; inserting, fix-<BR>ing; piercing; placing in or upon; offering, delivering,<BR>consigning, entrusting; giving back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पण|अर्पणं
अर्पण, अस्, आ, अम्, to be delivered, to be placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पित
अर्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, delivered, consigned; placed<BR>in or upon.<BR>—अर्पित-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, extending or<BR>giving the hand; married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पिस|अर्पिसः
अर्पिस, अस्, m. the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्प्य
अर्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be delivered, consignable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्
अर्ब् अर्ब्, cl. 1. P. अर्बति, आनर्ब, अर्बितुम्,<BR>to go, to go to or towards; to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुद|अर्बुदं|अर्बुदः|अर्ब्बुद|अर्ब्बुदः
अर्बुद अर्बुद, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>the preceding rt.), a serpent; a serpent-like demon<BR>conquered by Indra; a long round mass; a swelling,<BR>a tumour, a polypus; a hundred millions; N. of a<BR>mountain in the west of India, commonly called Abū,<BR>a place of pilgrimage, especially of the Jainas; N. of<BR>a people; N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुदि|अर्बुदिः
अर्बुदि, इस्, m., Ved. a serpent-like demon con-<BR>quered by Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुदिन्
अर्बुदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, afflicted with swelling or tumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भ|अर्भः
अर्भ अर्भ, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. ऋ),<BR>little, small, unimportant; (अस्), m. child, pupil [cf.<BR>Lat. orbus; Gr. ὀρφανός].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भक|अर्भकः
अर्भक, अस्, आ, अम्, small, minute; weak, little;<BR>emaciated; young, childish; like, similar; (अस्), m.<BR>a boy, a child, the young of any animal; a fool,<BR>an idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भग
अर्भग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. youthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म|अर्मं|अर्मः|अर्म्म|अर्म्मं
अर्म अर्म, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>ऋ), a disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मक
अर्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, narrow, thin; (अम्), n. nar-<BR>rowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मण|अर्मणं|अर्म्मण|अर्म्मणः
अर्मण, अस्, m. a measure of one droṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मन्|अर्म्मन्
अर्मन्, अ n. a disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य|अर्यः|अर्य्य|अर्य्यः
अर्य अर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ऋ), attached to,<BR>true, devoted, dear; kind; excellent; (अस्), m. a master,<BR>lord; an Āryan; a man of the third tribe, a Vaiśya;<BR>(आ), f. a woman of the third tribe, the wife of a<BR>Vaiśya.<BR>—अर्य-जारा, f., Ved. the mistress of an Ār-<BR>yan.<BR>—अर्य-पत्नी, f., Ved. wife of a true, legitimate<BR>husband.<BR>—अर्य-वर्य, अस्, m. a Vaiśya of rank.<BR>—अर्य-श्वेत, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्यमन्|अर्य्यमन्
अर्यमन्, आ, m., Ved. a bosom friend, play-fellow,<BR>companion, especially a friend who asks a woman in<BR>marriage for another; N. of an Āditya, who is com-<BR>monly invoked together with Varuṇa and Mitra; N.<BR>of the chief of the manes; the sun; the Asclepias<BR>plant.<BR>—अर्यम-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—अर्यम-देवा, f., N. of the twelfth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्यम्य|अर्यम्यः|अर्य्यम्य
अर्यम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. intimate, very friendly;<BR>(अस्), m. bosom friend, companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ययाणी
अर्ययाणी, f. a multitude of women of the Vaiśya<BR>tribe (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्याणी|अर्य्याणी
अर्याणी, f. a mistress; a woman of the third or<BR>Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्
अर्व् अर्व्, cl. 1. P. अर्वति, आनर्व, अर्वि-<BR>तुम्, to hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व|अर्व्व
अर्व अर्व, (in comp.) hither, towards, near<BR>to.<BR>—अर्व-वसु, उस्, m. one of the seven principal<BR>rays of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वट|अर्वटं|अर्व्वट
अर्वट अर्वट, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. अर्व्),<BR>ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वन्|अर्व्वन्
अर्वन् अर्वन्, आ, m. (fr. rt. ऋ), going, run-<BR>ning; epithet of a horse or its driver; a horse;<BR>one of the ten horses of the moon; epithet of Indra;<BR>a short span; (ती), f. a mare; a bawd, a procuress;<BR>(आ, अती, अत्), low, contemptible, inferior, vile.<BR>—अर्व-<BR>नस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, whose nose is like that of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वश
अर्वश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. possessed of coursers, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाच्|अर्व्वाच्
अर्वाच् अर्वाच्, वाङ्, वाची, वाक् (fr. rt. अञ्च्<BR>with अर्व; cf. अर्वन्), coming hitherward; turned<BR>towards, coming to meet any one; being on this side<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">Page0085-b+ 77</a>]<BR>(as the bank of a river); being below or behind,<BR>turned down or downwards; following, subsequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाक्|अर्व्वाक्
अर्वाक्, ind. (with abl.) hitherward; on this side;<BR>from a certain point; before, after; on the lower side<BR>of, behind, downwards; (with loc.) within; near.<BR>—अर्वाक्कालिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to proxi-<BR>mate time, modern.<BR>—अर्वाक्कालिक-ता, f. modern-<BR>ness, posteriority of time.<BR>—अर्वाक्-कूल, अम्, n. the<BR>near bank of a river.<BR>—अर्वाक्-सामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>epithet of three days, during which a Soma sacrifice<BR>is performed.<BR>—अर्वाक्-स्रोतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, N. of a<BR>creation of beings in which the current of nutriment<BR>tends downwards.<BR>—अर्वाग्-बिल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having the mouth hitherward.<BR>—अर्वाग्-वसु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. offering riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाके
अर्वाके, ind., Ved. in the proximity of, near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाचीन|अर्व्वाचीन|अर्व्वाचीनः
अर्वाचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, turned towards; favouring;<BR>being on this side or below (with abl.); born after-<BR>wards, posterior, recent, modern; reverse, contrary.<BR>—अर्वाचीन-ता, f. or अर्वाचीन-त्व, अम्, n. state of<BR>being posterior, recent or contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाचीनम्
अर्वाचीनम्, ind. (with abl.) on this side of;<BR>thenceforward, thence onward; less than.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वावत्|अर्व्वावत्
अर्वावत् अर्वा-वत्, त्, f., Ved. proximity [cf.<BR>परा-वत्]; being near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वावसु|अर्व्वावसु
अर्वावसु अर्वा-वसु, उस्, m., Ved. N. of the<BR>Hotṛ; N. of the Brahman of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वुक|अर्व्वुक
अर्वुक अर्वुक, अस्, m., N. of a tribe or peo-<BR>ple in the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्श|अर्शं|अर्शः
अर्श अर्श, अस्, m. (fr. rt. ऋश्), damage,<BR>hurt; hemorrhoids, piles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस्
अर्शस्, अस्, n. piles, hemorrhoids.<BR>—अर्शो-घ्न,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, destroying the hemorrhoids; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of the plant Amorphophallus Campanulatus Blume;<BR>one part of buttermilk with three parts of water;<BR>(ई), f., N. of the plant Curculigo Archioides Lin.<BR>—अर्शो-युज्, क्, क्, क्, afflicted with hemorrhoids.<BR>—अर्शो-रोग, अस्, m. the hemorrhoids.<BR>—अर्शोरोग-<BR>युत अस्, आ, अम्, or अर्शोरोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, afflicted<BR>with hemorrhoids, having hemorrhoids.<BR>—अर्शो-हित,<BR>अस्, m. the marking nut plant, Semecarpus Anacardium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस|अर्शसः
अर्शस, अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted with hemorrhoids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शान
अर्शान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. striving to hurt, ma-<BR>licious; (अस्), m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शिन्
अर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, afflicted with hemorrhoids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्षण
अर्षण अर्षण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ऋष्),<BR>flowing, movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्षणी
अर्षणी, f., Ved. a pricking or piercing pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्सस्
अर्सस् अर्सस्, अस्, n. hemorrhoids. See<BR>अर्शस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्
अर्ह् अर्ह्, cl. 1. P., ep. A. अर्हति, -ते,<BR>आनर्ह, अर्हिष्यति, आर्हीत्, अर्हितुम्,<BR>Ved. अर्हसे, to deserve, merit, be worthy; to have<BR>a claim to anything, to be entitled to (with acc.);<BR>to be allowed to do anything (with inf.); to be<BR>obliged or required to do anything (with acc.); to be<BR>worthy; to be worth; to counterbalance; to be able;<BR>(the 2nd pers. pres. of अर्ह् with an infinitive is often<BR>used as a softened form of imperative; e. g. दातुम्<BR>अर्हसि, ‘be pleased to give;’ श्रोतुम् अर्हसि, ‘deign<BR>to listen,’ for शृणु): Caus. अर्हयति (aor. आर्जिहत्),<BR>-यितुम्, to honour: Desid. अर्जिहिषति [cf. Gr. ἄρχω].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह, अस्, आ, अम्, meriting, deserving, worthy of,<BR>having a claim or being entitled to (with acc. or<BR>inf.); being required, obliged, or allowed (with<BR>inf.); becoming, proper, fit; worth (in money),<BR>costing; (अस्), m. a N. of Indra; (आ), f. worship;<BR>(आणि), Ved. n. pl. worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हण|अर्हणं
अर्हण, अम्, आ, n. f. worship, adoration, honour,<BR>treating with veneration or respect; (आ), ind., Ved.<BR>according to what is due; according to one's means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्|अर्हन्त्
अर्हत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, deserving, entitled to; able,<BR>allowed to; worthy; venerable, respectable; praised,<BR>celebrated; (अन्), m. a Buddha; the highest rank in<BR>the Buddhist hierarchy; an Arhat or superior divinity<BR>with the Jainas.<BR>—अर्हत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most<BR>worthy, best, most venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हन्त|अर्हंत|अर्हन्तः
अर्हन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy; (अस्), m. a Buddha;<BR>a Buddhist mendicant; N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हित|अर्हितः
अर्हित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured, worshipped, saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्य
अर्ह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy; respectable; right, fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हरिष्वणि
अर्हरिष्वणि अर्हरि-ष्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>making enemies (अर्हरि) cry aloud; (if formed by<BR>redupl. of हृष् with affix वनि) exultant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्
अल् अल्, cl. 1. P. अलति, अलितुम्, to adorn;<BR>to be competent or able; to prevent.<BR>See अलम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल|अलं
अल अल, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. अल्), the<BR>sting in the tail of a scorpion; yellow orpiment. See आल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक|अलकं|अलकः
अलक अलक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. अल्), a curl, lock; (अस्), m. a mad dog [cf. अलर्क];<BR>(आ), f. a girl from eight to ten years of age; N. of the<BR>capital of Kuvera, situated on a peak of the Himālaya<BR>inhabited also by Śiva.<BR>—अलक-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of a curl or tress.<BR>—अलक-नन्दा, f. a young girl<BR>from eight to ten years old; N. of the Gaṅgā river;<BR>N. of a river that runs from the Himālaya moun-<BR>tains and falls into the Gaṅgā.<BR>—अलक-प्रभा,<BR>f. the capital of Kuvera.<BR>—अलक-प्रिय, अस्, m., N.<BR>of the plant Terminalia Tomentosa W. and A.<BR>—अलक-संहति, इस्, f. rows of curls.<BR>—अलका-<BR>धिप (˚का-अध्˚), अस्, m. or अलकाधिपति (˚का-<BR>अध्˚), इस्, m. a N. of Kuvera.<BR>—अलकान्त (˚क-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the end of a curl, a ringlet.<BR>—अलकेश्वर<BR>(˚का-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a N. of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकम्
अलकम् अलकम्, ind., Ved. in vain, for<BR>nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्त|अलक्तः
अलक्त अलक्त or अलक्तक, अस्, m. (said to<BR>be for अ-रक्त), the red resin of certain trees; or<BR>perhaps the cochineal or its red sap.<BR>—अलक्त-रस,<BR>अस्, m. the Alakta juice [cf. the preceding].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षण|अलक्षणं
अलक्षण अ-लक्षण, अम्, n. (rt. लक्ष्), a<BR>bad, inauspicious sign; (अस्, आ, अम्), having no signs<BR>or marks; without characteristic, having no good<BR>marks, inauspicious, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षित
अ-लक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, unseen, unperceived, un-<BR>observed, unlooked for; uncharacterized, having no<BR>particular mark.<BR>—अलक्षितान्तक (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, suddenly dead.<BR>—अलक्षितोपस्थित (˚त-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has approached unobserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्य
अ-लक्ष्य or अ-लक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, invisible;<BR>unmarked, not indicated; having no particular marks,<BR>insignificant in appearance; (अस्), m., N. of a certain<BR>weapon.<BR>—अलक्ष्य-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, moving invisibly.<BR>—अलक्ष्य-लिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, disguised, incognito.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्मी
अलक्ष्मी अ-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. evil fortune, bad<BR>luck, distress, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलखान
अलखान अलखान, अस्, m., N. of a king<BR>of Gurjara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलगर्द|अलगर्दः|अलगर्द्द
अलगर्द अलगर्द or अलगर्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>water-serpent, the black variety of the Cobra de Capello<BR>(Coluber Nāga); (आ), f. a large poisonous leech;<BR>(etymology doubtful.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलग्न
अलग्न अ-लग्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. लग्), not<BR>joined or connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलग्ल
अलग्ल अ-लग्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking uncon-<BR>nectedly; stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघु
अलघु अ-लघु, उस्, वी, उ, not light, heavy;<BR>not short, long; weighty; serious, solemn; intense,<BR>violent.<BR>—अलघु-प्रतिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, solemnly<BR>pledged or promised.<BR>—अलघूपल (˚घु-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a rock.<BR>—अलघूष्मन् (˚घु-उष्˚), आ, m. in-<BR>tense heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करण|अलंकरण|अलंकरणं|अलङ्करणं
अलङ्करण अलङ्करण, अलङ्कार. See un-<BR>der अलम्, p. 86, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घन|अलंघन|अलंघनं
अलङ्घन अ-लङ्घन, अम्, n. (rt. लङ्घ्),<BR>not surmounting, not transgressing, not passing over<BR>or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घनीय|अलंघनीय
अ-लङ्घनीय or अ-लङ्घ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, insur-<BR>mountable, impassable, not to be crossed; not to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">Page0086-a+ 75</a>]<BR>transgressed, inviolable, venerable.<BR>—अलङ्घनीय-<BR>ता or अलङ्घ्य-ता, f. impassableness, insurmount-<BR>ableness, inaccessibility; inviolability; respectability;<BR>authoritative or absolute rule; superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0085-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलज|अलजः
अलज अलज, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलजी
अलजी अलजी, f. inflammation of the eye,<BR>at the edge of the cornea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलज्ज
अलज्ज अ-लज्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलञ्जर|अलंजरः|अलञ्जरः
अलञ्जर अलञ्जर, अस्, m. an earthen water-<BR>jar. See अलिञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलति|अलतिः
अलति अलति, इस्, m. a kind of song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलपत्|अलपन्त्
अलपत् अ-लपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, not speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलब्ध
अलब्ध अ-लब्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. लभ्), un-<BR>obtained.<BR>—अलब्ध-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, friendless,<BR>without a patron.<BR>—अलब्धाभीप्सित (˚ध-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, disappointed in one's desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलभमान
अ-लभमान, अस्, आ, अम्, not gaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलभ्य
अ-लभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unobtainable, unattainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्
अलम् अलम्, ind. (said to be fr. rt. अल्),<BR>enough, sufficient, adequate, equal to, competent, able.<BR>(अलम् may govern a dat., e. g. अलं जीवनाय,<BR>sufficient for living; also a loc. or inf., e. g. अलं<BR>विज्ञाने or विज्ञातुम्, able to conceive; also inst.,<BR>e. g. अलं शङ्कया, enough, i. e. away with fear!<BR>It may be used with the future tense, e. g. अलं<BR>हनिष्यति, he will be able to kill; or with an indecl.<BR>part., e. g. अलम् भुक्त्वा, enough of eating, i. e. do<BR>not eat more; अलं विचार्य, enough of consider-<BR>ation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कृ|अलंकृ
अलङ्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to prepare,<BR>make ready; to ornament, decorate; to prevent from,<BR>impede (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करण|अलंकरण|अलंकरणं|अलङ्करणं
अलङ्-करण, अम्, n. preparation, the act of de-<BR>corating, decoration; ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णुः|अलङ्करिष्णुः
अलङ्-करिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, fond of ornament;<BR>decorating, skilled in decorating; ornamented; (उस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कर्तृ|अलंकर्तृ|अलङ्कर्त्तृ
अलङ्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, decorating, skilled in<BR>decoration, a decorator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कर्मीण|अलंकर्मीण|अलङ्कर्म्मीण|अलङ्कर्म्मीणः
अलङ्कर्मीण, अस्, आ, अम्, competent to any act,<BR>skilful, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कार|अलंकार|अलंकारः|अलङ्कारः
अलङ्-कार, अस्, m. the act of decorating; ornament,<BR>decoration; a figure or rhetorical expression.<BR>—अलङ्-<BR>कार-चन्द्रिका, f. title of a commentary on Kuvala-<BR>yānanda.<BR>—अलङ्कार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, decorated,<BR>ornamented; (ती), f. title of the ninth Lambaka in<BR>the Kathāsaritsāgara; (वत्), ind. like an ornament.<BR>—अलङ्कार-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a manual or text-book<BR>of rhetoric.<BR>—अलङ्कार-सुवर्ण, अम्, n. gold used<BR>for ornaments.<BR>—अलङ्कार-सूर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>kind of meditation in Buddhism.<BR>—अलङ्कार-हीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कारक|अलंकारकः
अलङ्कारक, अस्, m. ornament, decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कृत|अलंकृत|अलङ्कृतः
अलङ्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared, made ready;<BR>ornamented, adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कृति|अलंकृति|अलंकृतिः
अलङ्-कृति, इस्, f. ornament; rhetorical ornament,<BR>figure or rhetorical expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्क्रिया|अलंक्रिया
अलङ्-क्रिया, f. adorning, ornamenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्गामिन्|अलंगामिन्
अलङ्-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going after or following<BR>in due or proper manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलञ्जीविक|अलंजीविक
अलञ्-जीविक, अस्, आ, अम्, sufficient for livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलञ्जुष|अलंजुष
अलञ्-जुष, अस्, आ, अम्, sufficient, adequate to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्तम|अलंतम
अलन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, able, sufficient, having power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्धन|अलंधन
अलन्-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing sufficient wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्धूम|अलंधूम|अलन्धूमः
अलन्-धूम, अस्, m. thick smoke, smoke enough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्पट|अलंपट|अलम्पटः
1. अलम्-पट, अस्, m. the interior of a house;<BR>woman's apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्पशु|अलंपशु|अलम्पशुः
अलम्-पशु, उस्, उस्, उ, able to keep cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्पुरुषीण|अलंपुरुषीण|अलम्पुरुषीणः
अलम्पुरुषीण, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for a man, be-<BR>coming a man; sufficient for a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्बल|अलंबल
अलम्-बल, अस्, m. strong enough, having sufficient<BR>power; an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्भूष्णु|अलंभूष्णु
अलम्-भूष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, able, competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्पट|अलंपट|अलम्पटः
अलम्पट 2. अ-लम्पट, अस्, आ, अम्, not libi-<BR>dinous, chaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्बुष|अलंबुष|अलंबुषः|अलम्बुषः
अलम्बुष अलम्बुष, अस्, m. (etymology<BR>doubtful, though connected with अलम् above), the<BR>palm of the hand with the fingers extended; vomiting;<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa or evil spirit; (आ), f. a barrier, a<BR>line or anything not to be crossed; a sort of sensitive<BR>plant; N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलय|अलयः
अलय अ-लय, अस्, m. (rt. ली, to be dissolved,<BR>or to rest, cling to), non-dissolution, permanence;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), houseless, homeless; vagrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्क|अलर्कः
अलर्क अलर्क, अस्, m. (etymology doubt-<BR>ful), a mad dog or one rendered furious; a fabulous<BR>animal, like a hog with eight legs; N. of the plant<BR>Calatropis Gigantea Alba; N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्षि
अलर्षि अलर्षि. See s. v. ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्षिराति
अलर्षि-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. eager to bestow, ready<BR>to grant gifts, one whose gifts are granted quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अललाभवत्|अललाभवन्त्
अललाभवत् अलला-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्,<BR>Ved. becoming active or lively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलले
अलले अलले, ind. a word of no import<BR>occuring in the dialect or gibberish of the Piśācas, a<BR>class of imps or goblins, introduced in plays, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलवाल|अलवालं
अलवाल अ-लवाल or अलवालक, अम्, n. a<BR>basin for water at the root of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस्
अलस् अ-लस्, अस्, अस्, अस् (rt. लस्, to shine),<BR>not shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस|अलसः
अलस अ-लस, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. लस्, to labour),<BR>inactive, without energy, lazy, idle, indolent, tired,<BR>faint; (अस्), m. sore or ulcer between the toes; N. of<BR>a small poisonous animal; N. of a plant; (आ), f., N.<BR>of the climbing plant Vitis Pedata Wall.<BR>—अलस-ता,<BR>f. or अलस-त्व, अम्, n. idleness.<BR>—अलसेक्षणा (˚स-<BR>ईक्˚), f. a woman with languishing looks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसक|अलसकः
अ-लसक, अस्, आ, अम्, indolent; (अस्), m. tympa-<BR>nitis, flatulence, intumescence of the abdomen, with<BR>constipation and wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलास्य
अ-लास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, idle, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाण्डु|अलांडुः|अलाण्डुः
अलाण्डु अलाण्डु, उस्, m., N. of a small<BR>noxious insect or other animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलात|अलातं|अलातः
अलात अलात, अम्, n. a fire-brand, coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलातृण|अलातृणः
अलातृण अ-लातृण, अस्, m. (rt. ला = रा?),<BR>Ved. not granting anything; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबु|अलाबुः
अलाबु अ-लाबु, उस् or ऊ, ऊस्, f. (fr. अ, ‘not,’<BR>and लब्, ‘to sink?’), the bottle-gourd, Lagernaria<BR>Vulgaris Ser; (उस्, उ), m. n. a vessel made of the<BR>preceding.<BR>—अलाबु-पात्र, अम्, n. a jar made of the<BR>bottle-gourd.<BR>—अलाबु-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of a<BR>bottle-gourd.<BR>—अलाबू-कट, अम्, n. the down of the<BR>bottle-gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाभ|अलाभः
अलाभ अ-लाभ, अस्, m. (rt. लभ्), non-<BR>acquirement; loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाय्य
अलाय्य अलाय्य, अस्, m. (fr. rt. ऋ?), Ved.<BR>epithet of Indra or N. of a man; an assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलार|अलारं
अलार अलार, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. ऋ),<BR>a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलास|अलासः
अलास अ-लास, अस्, m. (said to be fr. अ +<BR>लास, saliva), inflammation and abscess at the root<BR>of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलास्य
अलास्य अ-लास्य. See अ-लस above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलि|अलिः
अलि अलि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. अल्?), a crow; the<BR>Indian cuckoo; a scorpion; a large black bee; spi-<BR>rituous liquor.<BR>—अलि-कुल, अम्, n. a flight or number<BR>of bees.<BR>—अलिकुल-सङ्कुल, अस्, m. the water plant<BR>Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—अलि-जिह्वा or अलि-जिह्विका, f. the<BR>uvula or soft palate.<BR>—अलि-दूर्वा, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अलि-पत्त्रिका, f., N. of a shrub.<BR>—अलि-पर्नी, f.,<BR>N. of the plant Tragia Involucrata Lin.<BR>—अलि-प्रिय,<BR>अम्, n. the red lotus, Nymphæa Rubra; (आ), f. the<BR>trumpet flower, Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—अलि-माला, f.<BR>a flight of bees.<BR>—अलि-मोदा, f., N. of a plant, Premna<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">Page0086-c+ 69</a>]<BR>Spinosa.<BR>—अलि-विराव, अस्, m. or अलि-विरुत, अम्, n.<BR>song or hum of the bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्
अलिन्, ई, m. a scorpion; a large black bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिनी
अलिनी, f. a swarm of bees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंश|अलिंशः
अलिंश अलिंश, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिक|अलिकं
अलिक अलिक, अम्, n. (fr. rt. अल्?), the fore-<BR>head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिक्लव|अलिक्लवः
अलिक्लव अलिक्लव, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>carrion bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिगर्द|अलिगर्दः
अलिगर्द अलिगर्द, अस्, m. a snake. See<BR>अलगर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिङ्ग|अलिंग|अलिङ्गः
अलिङ्ग अ-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. absence of marks;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having no marks; (in gram.) having<BR>no gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिङ्गिन्|अलिंगिन्
अ-लिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, an impostor, a pretended ascetic<BR>or student, one wearing the usual frontal marks, skin,<BR>staff, &c., without belonging to a religious order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिञ्जर|अलिंजर|अलिंजरः|अलिञ्जरः
अलिञ्जर अलिञ्जर, अस्, m. a small earthen<BR>water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन|अलिनः
अलिन अलिन, अस्, m., Ved. N. of a tribe (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्द|अलिंदः|अलिन्दः
अलिन्द अलिन्द or अलिन्दक, अस्, m. (fr. rt.<BR>अल्?), a terrace before a house-door; (आस्), pl., N. of<BR>a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिपक|अलिपकः
अलिपक अलिपक, अस्, m. a dog; the Indian<BR>cuckoo; a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिप्सा
अलिप्सा अ-लिप्सा, f. (Desid. of rt. लभ्),<BR>freedom from desire or cupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिमक|अलिमकः
अलिमक अलिमक or अलिम्पक or अलिम्बक,<BR>अस्, m. the Indian cuckoo; a frog; a bee; N. of the<BR>plant Bassia Latifolia; the filaments of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक|अलीकं
अलीक अलीक, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>अल्, ‘to adorn,’ i. e. dress out in false colour; perhaps<BR>fr. अ, ‘not,’ and लीक, but the latter does not occur), un-<BR>pleasing, disagreeable; untrue, false; small, little;<BR>(अम्), n. anything displeasing; falsehood, untruth;<BR>the forehead; heaven.<BR>—अलीक-ता, f. falsehood, vanity.<BR>—अलीक-मत्स्य, अस्, m. a kind of dish resembling<BR>the taste of fish (‘mock-fish’), made of the flour of<BR>a sort of bean fried with Seamum oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकयु
अलीकयु, उस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकाय
अलीकाय, nom. A. अलीकायते, -यितुम्, to be de-<BR>ceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकिन्
अलीकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, disagreeable; false, deceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक्य
अलीक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to falsehood, false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीगर्द|अलीगर्दः
अलीगर्द अलीगर्द, अस्, m. a snake. See<BR>अलिगर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलु|अलुः
अलु अलु, उस्, f. a small water-pot. See आलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुप्त
अलुप्त अ-लुप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. लुप्), not cut<BR>off, undiminished.<BR>—अलुप्त-महिमन्, आ, आ, अ, of<BR>undiminished glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुब्ध|अलुब्धः
अलुब्ध अ-लुब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-लुभ्यत्,<BR>अन्, अन्ती, अत् (rt. लुभ्), Ved. moderate, content, not<BR>covetous.<BR>—अलुब्ध-त्व, अम्, n. freedom from co-<BR>vetousness, moderation, contentment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभ|अलोभः
अ-लोभ, अस्, m. non-confusion; right process (?);<BR>absence of cupidity, moderation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभिन्
अ-लोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not wanting or desiring anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलूक्ष
अलूक्ष अ-लूक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, soft. See<BR>अ-रूक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलून
अलून अ-लून, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. लू), uncut,<BR>unshorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अले
अले अले or अलेले, ind. unmeaning words<BR>in the dialect of the demons or Piśācas, intro-<BR>duced in plays, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेपक|अलेपकः
अलेपक अ-लेपक, अस्, इका, अम्, stainless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेश
अलेश अ-लेश, अस्, आ, अम्, not little, much,<BR>large; (अम्), ind. not at all.<BR>—अ-लेशैज (˚श-एज्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0086-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोक|अलोकः
अलोक अ-लोक, अस्, m. (rt. लोक्), not the<BR>world; the end of the world; the immaterial or<BR>spiritual world; not the people; (अस्, आ, अम्), not<BR>having space, finding no place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकन|अलोकनं
अ-लोकन, अम्, n. invisibility, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकनीय
अ-लोकनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, invisible, imperceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकित
अ-लोकित, अस्, आ, अम्, unseen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोक्य
अ-लोक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unusual, unallowed.<BR>—अलोक्य-<BR>ता, f. unfitness for heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलौकिक|अलौकिकः
अ-लौकिक, अस्, ई, अम्, not current in the world,<BR>not relating to this world, uncommon, supernatural;<BR>(in gram.) not current in the usual language; un-<BR>usual, rare; theoretical; Vedic (as opposed to the<BR>later usage of a word).<BR>—अलौकिक-त्व, अम्, n. rare<BR>occurence of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोपाङ्ग|अलोपांग
अलोपाङ्ग अ-लोपाङ्ग (˚प-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. not defective in a single limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोमहर्षण
अलोमहर्षण अ-लोमहर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>causing erection of the hair of the body (from joy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोल
अलोल अ-लोल, अस्, आ, अम्, unagitated, firm,<BR>steady, tranquil; (आ), f., N. of a metre containing four<BR>lines, each of fourteen syllables. See लोला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलु
अ-लोलु, उस्, उस्, उ, indifferent to sensual objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुत्व
—अलोलु-त्व, अम्, n. indifference to sensual objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुप
अलोलुप अ-लोलुप, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>desire; not greedy or covetous, apathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोह
अलोह अलोह, अस्, m., N. of a person?<BR>(Gaṇa to Pāṇini IV. 2, 97).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोहित|अलोहितं
अलोहित अ-लोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, bloodless,<BR>(अम्), n. Nymphæa Rubra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

