अल्क|अल्कः
अल्क अल्क, अस्, m. (a doubtful word), a<BR>tree; a member of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्प|अल्पं|अल्पः
अल्प अल्प, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अल्?) perhaps<BR>connected with अर्भ), small, minute, trifling; little;<BR>seldom, rare; of short existence. अल्पम्, ind. little;<BR>अल्पात्, ind. without much trouble, easily; अल्पेन,<BR>ind. easily [cf. Lith. alpstu, ap-alpstu, ‘to faint’].<BR>—अल्प-कार्य, अम्, n. small matter.<BR>—अल्प-केशी,<BR>f., N. of a plant; or perhaps the root of sweet flag.<BR>—अल्प-क्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, bought for little money,<BR>cheap.<BR>—अल्प-गन्ध, अम्, n. the red lotus.<BR>—अल्प-चेष्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, inert.<BR>—अल्प-च्छद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, scantily clad.<BR>—अल्प-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing little, ignorant, shallow, superficial.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>तनु, उस्, उस्, उ, small-bodied; short, thin.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>ता, f. or अल्प-त्व, अम्, n. smallness, minuteness;<BR>inferiority, insignificance.<BR>—अल्प-दक्षिण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, defective in presents (as a ceremony).<BR>—अल्प-<BR>दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, of confined views, narrow-minded.<BR>—अल्प-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, of little wealth, not afflu-<BR>ent.<BR>—अल्प-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, weak-minded, having lit-<BR>tle sense, foolish.<BR>—अल्प-पत्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant, a species of the Tulasi.<BR>—अल्प-पद्म, अम्,<BR>n. the red lotus.<BR>—अल्प-परीवार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a small train or retinue.<BR>—अल्प-पशु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. having a small number of cattle.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>पुण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, whose religious merits are small.<BR>—अल्प-प्रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having few descendants<BR>or few subjects.<BR>—अल्प-प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>little weight or consequence, insignificant.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>प्रभाव-त्व, अम्, n. insignificance.<BR>—अल्प-प्र-<BR>माण or अल्पप्रमाणक, अस्, आ, अम्, of little<BR>weight or measure; of little authority, resting on<BR>little evidence; (अस्), m. common cucumber, Cucu-<BR>mis Sativus.<BR>—अल्प-प्रयोग, अस्, आ, अम्, of rare ap-<BR>plication or use.<BR>—अल्प-प्राण, अस्, m. (in gram.)<BR>slight breathing or weak aspiration; the effort in<BR>uttering the vowels, the semivowels य्, र्, ल्, व्, the<BR>consonants क्, च्, ट्, त्, प्, ग्, ज्, ड्, द्, ब्, and the nasals,<BR>is said to be accompanied with slight aspiration, but<BR>practically अल्प-प्राण is here equivalent to unas-<BR>pirated, as opposed to महा-प्राण, q. v.; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), having little or short breath, asthmatic.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>बल, अस्, आ, अम्, of little strength, feeble.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-b" target="_blank">Page0087-b+ 79</a>]<BR>बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, causing little annoyance or incon-<BR>venience.<BR>—अल्प-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, weak-minded,<BR>unwise, ignorant, silly.<BR>—अल्प-भाग्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having little fortune.<BR>—अल्प-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speak-<BR>ing little, taciturn.<BR>—अल्प-मध्यम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>thin-waisted.<BR>—अल्प-मात्र, अम्, n. a little, a little<BR>merely; a short time, a few moments.<BR>—अल्प-मा-<BR>रिष, अस्, m. a kind of amaranth, Amaranthus Poly-<BR>gamus.<BR>—अल्प-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, small-bodied, dimi-<BR>nutive; (इस्), f. a small figure or object.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>मूल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of small value.<BR>—अल्प-मेधस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, of little understanding, ignorant, silly.<BR>—अल्पम्-पच, अस्, आ, अम्, cooking little, stingy.<BR>—अल्प-वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, young in age.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking little, taciturn.<BR>—अल्प-<BR>विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ignorant, ill-taught, uneducated.<BR>—अल्प-विषय, अस्, आ, अम्, of limited range or<BR>capacity, engaged in trifling matters.<BR>—अल्पशः-<BR>पङ्क्ति, इस्, f., N. of a metre.<BR>—अल्प-शक्ति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, of little strength, weak, feeble.<BR>—अल्प-शस्, ind.<BR>in a low degree, a little; separately; seldom, now<BR>and then.<BR>—अल्प-सरस्, अस्, n. a basin, a small<BR>pond, one which is shallow or dry in the hot season.<BR>—अल्प-स्नायु, उस्, उस्, उ, having few sinews.<BR>—अल्पाकाङ्क्षिन् (˚प-आक्˚), ई, इणी, इ, desiring little,<BR>contented or satisfied with little.<BR>—अल्पाञ्जि (˚प-अञ्˚),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. covered with minute spots.<BR>—अल्पा-<BR>युस् (˚प-आय्˚), उस्, उस्, उस्, short-lived; young, of<BR>few years; (उस्), m. a goat.<BR>—अल्पारम्भ (˚प-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, m. a gradual beginning.<BR>—अल्पाल्प (˚प-<BR>अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, very little, minute; little by little.<BR>—अल्पाहार (˚प-आह्˚), अस्, m. the taking little<BR>food; moderation, abstinence; (अस्, आ, अम्), absti-<BR>nent.<BR>—अल्पाहारिन् (˚प-आह्˚), ई, इणी, इ, eating little,<BR>moderate, abstemious.<BR>—अल्पेच्छु (˚प-इच्˚), उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, moderate in wishes, seeking little.<BR>—अल्पेतर<BR>(˚प-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, large, lit. other than small.<BR>—अल्पेशाख्य (अल्प-ईश-आख्य), अस्, आ, अम्, named<BR>after an insignificant chief or master, of low origin.<BR>—अल्पोन (˚प-ऊन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, slightly defective,<BR>not quite complete or not finished.<BR>—अल्पोपाय<BR>(˚प-उप्˚), अस्, m. small means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पक|अल्पकः
अल्पक, अस्, इका, अम्, small, minute, trifling;<BR>(अम्), ind. little; (अस्), m., N. of a plant, Hedysarum<BR>Alhagi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पित
अल्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, diminished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पिष्ठ|अल्पिष्ठः
अल्पिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, least, smallest, very small.<BR>—अल्पिष्ठ-कीर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, of little note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

