अवकुटार|अवकुटारं
अवकुटार, अस्, आ, अम्, opposite, contrary; back-<BR>wards, downwards; (अम्), n. reverse, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुटारिका
अवकुटारिका, f. dissimulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंश|अवंशः
अवंश अ-वंश, अस्, m. a low or despised<BR>family; (अम्), n., Ved. that which has no beams or<BR>support, the ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकट|अवकटं
अवकट, अवकुटार। See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलित|अवकलितः
अवकलित अव-कलित, अस्, आ, अम्, Seen, ob-<BR>served; wicked, perverse (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवका
अवका अवका, f. a grassy plant growing in<BR>marshy land, Blyxa Octandra Rich; otherwise called<BR>Śaivāla.<BR>—अवकाद (˚का-अद), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. eat-<BR>ing the plant Blyxa Oct. R.<BR>—अवकोल्ब (˚का-उल्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, covered or surrounded with Avakā plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश्
