अवट|अवटः
अवट अवट, अस्, m. (fr. 2. अव, q. v.), a hole,<BR>a vacuity; a hole in the ground, a chasm, a pit; any<BR>depressed part of the body, a cavity, a fosse, a sinus;<BR>a well; a juggler; N. of a man.<BR>—अवट-कच्छप,<BR>अस्, m. a tortoise in a hole (said of an inexperienced<BR>man, who has seen nothing of the world).<BR>—अवट-<BR>विरोधन, अम्, n. a particular hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवति
अवति, इस्, m. a hole in the ground; a sinus; a<BR>hollow, a cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीट|अवटीटः
अवटीट, अस्, आ, अम्, flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटु|अवटुः
अवटु, उस्, m. f. the back or nape of the neck;<BR>a hole in the ground; a well; N. of a tree; (उ), n.<BR>a hole, a rent.<BR>—अवटु-ज, अस्, m. a hind curl, the<BR>hair on the back of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट्य
अवट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

