अवतस्
अव-तस्, ind. below, in the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतर्पण|अवतर्पणं
अवतर्पण अव-तर्पण, अम्, n. (rt. तृप्),<BR>soothing remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतृद्
अवतृद् अव-तृद्, cl. 7. P., Ved. -तृणत्ति,<BR>-तर्दितुम्, to chip off, sever; to silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतॄ
अवतॄ अव-तॄ, cl. 1. P. -तरति, -तरितुम् or<BR>-रीतुम्, to descend (especially as a deity in becoming<BR>incarnate); to alight; to betake one's self to; to<BR>make one's appearance; to undertake, overcome:<BR>Caus. -तारयति, -यितुम्, to make or let one descend,<BR>to bring or fetch down; to pour down, take down,<BR>take off, remove; to bring down towards; to intro-<BR>duce, set a-going, render current; to descend (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरण|अवतरणं
