अवतरणिका
अव-तरणिका, f. the short prayer (e. g. गणेशाय<BR>नमः) at the beginning of a work, which causes the<BR>divinity so addressed to descend from heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरितव्य
अव-तरितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतार|अवतारः
अव-तार, अस्, m. descent (especially of a deity<BR>from heaven), the appearance of any deity upon earth,<BR>but more particularly the incarnations of Viṣṇu in ten<BR>principal forms, viz. the fish, tortoise, boar, man-lion,<BR>dwarf, the two Rāmas, Kṛṣṇa, Buddha, and Kalki;<BR>any new and unexpected appearance; (any distin-<BR>guished person in the language of respect is called an<BR>Avatār or incarnation of a deity); aiming at an object<BR>(with gen.); a landing-place, a Tīrtha or sacred<BR>place; a pond; translation, translating, crossing; अव-<BR>तारं लभ्, to gain one's aim or object with regard<BR>to anything (with gen.).<BR>—अवतार-कथा, f. ac-<BR>count of an Avatāra; N. of a chapter in the work<BR>entitled ‘Śaṅkara-vijaya,’ supposed to have been com-<BR>posed by Anantānanda-giri.<BR>—अवतार-द्वादश-<BR>कीर्तन, अम्, n. title of a chapter of the work<BR>‘Ūrdhvāmnāya-saṃhitā.’<BR>—अवतार-मन्त्र, अस्,<BR>m. a prayer causing the descent of a deity.<BR>—अव-<BR>तार-वादावली, f., N. of a controversial work by<BR>Puruṣottama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारक
अव-तारक, अस्, इका, अम्, making one's appear-<BR>ance; making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारण|अवतारणं
अव-तारण, अम्, n. causing to descend; transla-<BR>tion; worship, adoration; possession by an evil<BR>spirit; the ends or border of a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारित
अव-तारित, अस्, आ, अम्, taken off or out, laid down<BR>or aside; descended; translated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारिन्
अव-तारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, making one's appearance;<BR>making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतार्य
अव-तार्य, ind. having caused to alight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्ण|अवतीर्णः|अवतीर्ण्ण
