अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य अ-वद्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वद्), not<BR>to be praised; low, inferior; disagreeable, blamable,<BR>disliked; (अम्), n. anything blamable, or not to be<BR>spoken of with praise; want, imperfection, vice, sin;<BR>blame, censure; shame, reproach.<BR>—अवद्य-गोहन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. concealing or keeping off want.<BR>—अवद्य-भी, ईस्, f., Ved. fear of vices or sin.<BR>—अवद्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. disgraceful, la-<BR>mentable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्योतिन्
