अवनि|अवनिः
अवनि, इस्, f. (said to be fr. rt. अव्, but rather<BR>connected with ? अव, down), course, bed of a<BR>river; stream, river; the earth; a finger.<BR>—अवनिङ्-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, prostrate on the ground.<BR>—अवनि-<BR>चर, अस्, आ, अम्, roving over the earth, vagabond.<BR>—अवनि-पति, इस्, m. lord of the earth, a king;<BR>Viṣṇu; Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR>—अवनि-पाल, अस्, m. pro-<BR>tector of the earth, a king.<BR>—अवनि-मण्डल, अम्,<BR>n. the globe.<BR>—अवनि-रुह्, ट्, m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

