अवविद्ध अव-विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. व्यध्),<BR>cast down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवव्रश्च्
अवव्रश्च् अव-व्रश्च्, cl. 6. P. -वृश्चति, -व्र-<BR>श्चितुम्, -व्रष्टुम्, to splinter, cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवव्रश्च|अवव्रश्चः
अव-व्रश्च, अस्, m. splinter, chip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अवश अ-वश, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वश्), unsub-<BR>missive to another's will; independent, unrestrained,<BR>free; not having one's own free will; doing some-<BR>thing against one's liking or unwillingly; necessary,<BR>certain.<BR>—अवशङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, not submitting<BR>to another's will.<BR>—अवशेन्द्रिय-चित्त (˚श-इन्), अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">Page0093-c+ 73</a>]<BR>आ, अम्, whose mind and senses are not held in sub-<BR>jection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीभूत
अ-वशी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, unrestrained, independ-<BR>ent; uninfluenced by magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्य|अवश्यं
अ-वश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, untameable, ungovernable,<BR>inevitable; (अम्), ind. necessarily, inevitably, certainly,<BR>at all events, by all means; अवश्यम् एव, most<BR>surely. If compounded with a fut. pass. part. the<BR>final nasal is dropped; e. g. अवश्य-पाच्य, to be<BR>necessarily cooked; अवश्य-कार्य, to be necessarily<BR>done: but retained in अवश्यङ्-कारिन्, doing what<BR>is necessary; अवश्यम्-भाविन्, necessarily being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यक
अ-वश्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, necessary, inevitable, in-<BR>dispensable.<BR>—अवश्यक-ता, f. or अवश्यक-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. necessity, obligation, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशक्थिका
अवशक्थिका अव-शक्थिका, f. a cloth tied<BR>round the legs and knees of a person sitting on his<BR>hams. [cf. अव-सक्थिका].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशस्
अवशस् अव-शस्, अस्, f. (rt. शंस्), Ved. wrong<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशा
अवशा अ-वशा, f., Ved. not a cow, a bad cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशातन|अवशातनं
अवशातन अव-शातन, अम्, n. (Caus. of rt.<BR>शद्), withering, drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिरस्
अवशिरस् अव-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or अव-<BR>शीर्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the head turned down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्
अवशिष् अव-शिष्, Pass. -शिष्यते, to be<BR>left last or as a remnant, to remain over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्ट|अवशिष्टः
अव-शिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, left, remaining; (अम्),<BR>n. or अव-शिष्टक, अम्, n. rest, remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेष|अवशेषः
अव-शेष, अस्, (अम्?), m. (n. ?) leavings, remainder;<BR>end, close, termination. Frequently as the last mem-<BR>ber of a compound; thus, अर्धावशेष, having<BR>only one half left; कथावशेष-ता, the condition<BR>of one who survives only in narrations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेषित
अव-शेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, left remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशॄ
अवशॄ अव-शॄ, Pass. -शीर्यते, to be ṣat-<BR>tered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्या अव-श्या, f. (rt. श्यै with अव),<BR>hoar-frost; a fog or mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीन|अवशीनः
अव-शीन, अस्, m. a scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्याय|अवश्यायः
अव-श्याय, अस्, m. hoar-frost; white dew; pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्रयण|अवश्रयणं
अवश्रयण अव-श्रयण, अम्, n. (rt. श्री),<BR>taking (anything) from off the fire (opposed to अधि-<BR>श्रयण, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्वसम्
अवश्वसम् अव-श्वसम्, ind. (rt. श्वस्), Ved.<BR>as if blown away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्कयणी
अवष्कयणी अवष्कयणी, f. (= वष्कयणी),<BR>a cow that bears a calf after a long interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ्|अवष्टंभ्
अवष्टम्भ् अव-ष्टम्भ् (-स्तम्भ्), cl. 5. 9. P.<BR>-ष्टभ्नोति or -नाति, -ष्टम्भितुम्, to lean or rest<BR>upon; to be contiguous or near; to be astounded or<BR>bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्ध|अवष्टब्धं
अव-ष्टब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, supported, rested on,<BR>protected; hanging from or upon; stopped, ob-<BR>structed, stayed; paralysed; bound, tied, attached;<BR>wrapped up, enfolded; opposed; surpassed, over-<BR>come; near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टभ्य
अव-ष्टभ्य, ind. leaning upon, resting on,<BR>holding; stopping, arresting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टंभः|अवष्टम्भः
अव-ष्टम्भ, अस्, m. leaning or resting upon,<BR>having recourse to any one; stopping, standing still,<BR>staying; self-confidence, resoluteness; commencement,<BR>beginning; excellence; obstruction, impediment; sup-<BR>port, stay; paralysis; a post or pillar; gold.<BR>—अव-<BR>ष्टम्भ-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, golden, made of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भन|अवष्टंभनं
अव-ष्टम्भन, अम्, n. resting upon, having<BR>recourse to; supporting, protecting; stopping, stay-<BR>ing; paralysing; a pillar or post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वन्
अवष्वन् अव-ष्वन् (-स्वन्), cl. 1. P. -ष्व-<BR>णति, -णितुम्, to smack (one's lips) or otherwise make<BR>a noise in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वाण|अवष्वाणं|अवष्वाणः
अव-ष्वाण, अस्, m. noisy eating, smacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्
अवस् 1. अवस्, n. (fr. rt. अव्), Ved. satisfac-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">Page0094-a+ 73</a>]<BR>tion, pleasure, enjoyment; wish, desire, aspiring;<BR>favour, furtherance, protection, assistance.<BR>—अवस्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. striving, desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस|अवसं|अवसः
अवस, अम्, n., Ved. refreshment, food, provisions,<BR>viaticum; preserving, protecting; (अस्), m. a king;<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्
अवस् 2. अवस्, ind. (fr. 2. अव), Ved. adv.<BR>below, downwards, hitherward.<BR>.(As a prep. with inst. or abl. it expresses) below, at<BR>the lowest place of; without, on the outside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तात्
अवस्तात्. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका अव-सक्थिका or अव-सक्तिका,<BR>f. a cloth tied round the legs and knees of a person<BR>sitting on his hams; a wrapper; a girth or band [cf.<BR>अव-शक्थिका].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसञ्ज्|अवसंज्
अवसञ्ज् अव-सञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. -सजति, -सङ्क्तुम्,<BR>to suspend, attach, cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्त
अव-सक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, suspended from, attached<BR>to or by, in contact with, bound round, begirt; en-<BR>gaged in, intent on, eager, placed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसञ्जन|अवसंजनं
अव-सञ्जन or अव-सज्जन, अम्, n. embracing,<BR>clinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसण्डीन|अवसंडीन|अवसंडीनं
अवसण्डीन अव-सण्डीन, अम्, n. (rt. डी), the<BR>united downward flight of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ|अवसथः
अवसथ अ-वसथ, अस्, m. (for आ-वसथ,<BR>q. v.), habitation; a village; a college, a school; (अम्),<BR>n. a house. See आ-वसथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ्य|अवसथ्यः
अवसथ्य, अस्, m. a college, a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसद्
अवसद् अव-सद्, cl. 1. P. -सीदति, -सत्तुम्,<BR>to sink down, to faint; become disheartened, be ex-<BR>hausted, perish, come to an end: Caus. -सादयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to sink, dispirit, render downhearted,<BR>to ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्न|अवसन्नः
अव-सन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk down, bowed, bent;<BR>languid, enervated; melancholy, dispirited, unhappy;<BR>ended, terminated, separated; non-suited.<BR>—अव-<BR>सन्न-ता, f. or अवसन्न-त्व, अम्, n. affliction,<BR>low spirits; dejection; termination, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाद|अवसादः
अव-साद, अस्, m. sitting down; sinking, fainting;<BR>exhaustion, fatigue, lassitude, want of energy or spirit,<BR>especially as proceeding from doubtful or unsuccessful<BR>love; (in law) badness of a cause; end, termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अव-सादक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing to sink, frustrat-<BR>ing; exhausting, tiresome, wearisome; ending, finish-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादन|अवसादनं
अव-सादन, अम्, n. oppressing, disheartening;<BR>finishing; an escharotic; removing proud flesh by<BR>escharotic applications.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादित
अव-सादित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to sink, exhausted,<BR>faint, languid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसभ
अवसभ अव-सभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. excluded<BR>from society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर|अवसरः
अवसर अव-सर, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सृ with<BR>अव), descent, place of descent; descent of water;<BR>rain, raining; occasion, moment, favourable opportu-<BR>nity; leisure, advantageous situation; consultation in<BR>private; a year.<BR>—अवसर-काले, at a favourable<BR>opportunity, at a time of leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसारण
अव-सारण, अम्, n. removing, causing to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्ग|अवसर्गः
अवसर्ग अव-सर्ग. See अव-सृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्प|अवसर्पः
अवसर्प अव-सर्प, अस्, m. (rt. सृप्), a spy,<BR>a secret emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पण|अवसर्पणं
अव-सर्पण, अम्, n. stepping down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पिन्
अव-सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, stepping down; (इणी), f. a<BR>long period of time with the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसव्य|अवसव्यं
अवसव्य अव-सव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not left, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान|अवसानं
