अवसुप्त
अवसुप्त अव-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्वप्),<BR>asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृज्
अवसृज् अव-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति, -स्रष्-<BR>टुम्, to let off, to let loose, let go, fling down, pour<BR>out, dismiss, remit, liberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्ग|अवसर्गः
अव-सर्ग, अस्, m. letting off, letting go, emission,<BR>remission, laxity, relaxation, following one's own in-<BR>clinations, independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्जन|अवसर्जनं
अव-सर्जन, अम्, n., Ved. liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृष्ट
अव-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, dismissed, let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसो
अवसो अव-सो, cl. 4. P. -स्यति, -सातुम्,<BR>to finish, accomplish; to destroy: Caus. -साययति,<BR>-यितुम्, to destroy; to cause to be completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसा
अव-सा, f., Ved. liberation, setting free, deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसातृ
अव-सातृ, ता, m., Ved. a deliverer, liberator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान|अवसानं
2. अव-सान, अम्, n. place of dismounting from a<BR>horse or alighting from a carriage, stopping, resting-<BR>place, residence; conclusion, termination, cessation;<BR>death; boundary, limit; (in gram.) the last part of a<BR>word or period, disjunction of letters; a pause; the<BR>end of a verse or the verse itself: (for 1. अ-वसान,<BR>see last col.)<BR>—अवसान-दर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. look-<BR>ing at one's place of destination or residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसानक
अव-सानक, अस्, इका, अम्, coming to an end,<BR>perishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान्य
अवसान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to the end<BR>of a verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाय|अवसायः
