अवसाय|अवसायः
2. अव-साय, ind. having finished; having loosened,<BR>having set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसायिन्
अव-सायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, residing, dwelling in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाय्य
अव-साय्य, ind. having caused to be completed,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसित|अवसितं
अव-सित, अस्, आ, अम्, having settled in a place,<BR>residing; ended, terminated; finished, completed;<BR>standing in a pause; known, understood; stored (as<BR>grain, &c.); gone; (अम्), n. a dwelling-place.<BR>—अव-<BR>सित-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, frustrated, disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेय
अव-सेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed, destructible,<BR>perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्द्|अवस्कंद्
