अव-हास, अस्, m. jest, joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहास्य
अव-हास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be derided, exposed to<BR>jest, ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्त|अवहस्तः
अवहस्त अव-हस्त, अस्, m. the back of the<BR>hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहा
अवहा अव-हा, Pass. -हीयते, to be left<BR>remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहालिका
अवहालिका अवहालिका, f. (rt. हल्), a wall,<BR>a bound hedge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित|अवहितं
अवहित अव-हित. See under अव-धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्था
अवहित्था अ-वहि-त्था, f., अम्, n. (corrupted<BR>fr. अ-वहिः-स्था), dissimulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृ
अवहृ अव-हृ, cl. 1. P. -हुरति, -हर्तुम्,<BR>to lay aside, throw away, take away; Ved. to throw<BR>or knock down (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहरण|अवहरणं
अव-हरण, अम्, n. throwing away; taking away;<BR>stealing, plundering; taking back, redeeming; fining,<BR>mulcting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार|अवहारः
अव-हार, अस्, m. truce, suspension of arms, ces-<BR>sation of gambling, fighting, &c.; a thief; a shark;<BR>a water elephant; summoning, inviting; any object<BR>fit or able to be brought near; apostacy, abandoning<BR>a sect or cast; re-delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारक|अवहारकः
अव-हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who stops fighting,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. a shark, a marine monster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार्य|अवहार्य्य|अवहार्य्यः
अव-हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made to restore or<BR>compensate; finable, punishable; recoverable, re-<BR>deemable; (anything) which one is compelled to re-<BR>store.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृत
अव-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken off, back, or away;<BR>seized; stolen; fined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेल|अवहेलं|अवहेलः
अवहेल अव-हेल, अम्, आ, n. f. or अव-हेलन,<BR>अम्, n. (fr. rt. हेल् for हेड् with अव), disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलित|अवहेलितं
अव-हेलित, अस्, आ, अम्, disrespected; (अम्), n.<BR>disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवह्वर|अवह्वरः
अवह्वर अव-ह्वर, अस्, m. (rt. ह्वृ), a<BR>crooked way; trick; deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकिन्
अवाकिन् अ-वाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt. वच्), not<BR>speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्क
1. अ-वाक्क, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. speechless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
1. अ-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, speechless, dumb.<BR>—अवाक्-श्रुति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, deaf and dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
1. अ-वाच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be addressed; im-<BR>proper to be uttered; vile, bad; not distinctly<BR>expressed.<BR>—अवाच्य-ता, f. or अवाच्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>impropriety; reproach, calumny.<BR>—अवाच्य-देश, अस्,<BR>m. unmentionable region, the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकृ
अवाकृ अवा-कृ (अव-आ-कृ), cl. 8. 5. P.<BR>-करोति, -कृणोति, -कर्तुम्, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकॄ
अवाकॄ अवा-कॄ (अव-आ-कॄ), cl. 6. P. -किरति,<BR>-करितुम्, -रीतुम्, to strew, pour upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकर|अवाकरः
अवा-कर, अस्, m. a mint (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्ष|अवाक्षः
अवाक्ष अवाक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. अक्ष for<BR>अक्षि with अव), who or what looks down upon or<BR>defends, a guardian, a keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्र|अवाग्रं
अवाग्र अवाग्र (अव-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a bent top; stooping, bending, bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच् 2. अवाच्, आङ्, आची, आक् (fr. 2. अव and<BR>अञ्च्), turned downwards, being or situated below,<BR>lower than (with abl.); looking downwards, headlong;<BR>south; (ई), f. the south quarter, the lower regions<BR>[with अवाच् has been compared the Lat. au-ster for<BR>ava-ster].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्
अवाक्, ind. downwards; south, southward, southern.<BR>—अवाक्-पुष्पी, f., N. of the plant Anethum Sowa<BR>Roxb.<BR>—अवाक्-शाख, अस्, आ, अम्, having the branches<BR>turned downwards; epithet of the Ficus Religiosa.<BR>—अ-<BR>वाक्-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the head downwards,<BR>headlong.<BR>—अवाग्-भाग, अस्, m. the part below.<BR>—अवाङ्-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, looking down or away,<BR>having the face turned downwards, headlong; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a weapon.<BR>—अवाञ्-ज्ञान, अम्, n. disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्क
2. अवाक्क, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. a word formed for<BR>the etymology of अवका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाचीन|अवाचीनं
अवाचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, down-looked, headlong;<BR>south, southern; descended, gone down; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
2. अवाच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, southern, southerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाचि
अवाचि अवा-चि (अव-आ-चि), cl. 5. P. A.<BR>-चिनोति, -नुते, -चेतुम्, to heap up, accumulate,<BR>gather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्छिद्
अवाच्छिद् अवा-च्छिद् (अव-आ-छिद्), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-च्छिनत्ति, -च्छिन्ते, -च्छेत्तुम्, to tear or snatch<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्छिद्य
अवा-च्छिद्य, ind. having snatched away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाज्
अवाज् अवाज् (अव-अज्), cl. 1. P. अवाजति, -जि-<BR>तुम्, to drive down, to throw down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाजिन्
अवाजिन् अ-वाजिन्, ई, m., Ved. a bad horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात्
अवात् अवात् (अव-अत्), cl. 1. P., Ved. अवातति,<BR>तितुम्, to go down; (formed for the etym. of अवत,<BR>q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवातित
अवातित (अव-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, gone down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात
अवात 1. अ-वात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. windless,<BR>not moved by wind, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात
अवात 1. अ-वात, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वन्, whence<BR>the part. pass. वात), Ved. unattacked, untroubled,<BR>untouched; unconquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवातुल
अवातुल अ-वातुल, अस्, आ, अम्, not flatulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाद्
अवाद् अवाद् (अव-अद्), cl. 2. P., Ved. अवात्ति,<BR>त्तुम्, to cause to eat food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवादिन्
अवादिन् अ-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, no speaker, no<BR>disputer, one who does not prosecute or bring an<BR>action, peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्
अवान् अवान् (अव-अन्), cl. 2. P. अवानिति,<BR>नितुम्, to breathe or inhale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान|अवानं|अवानः
1. अवान, अस्, m. breathing, inhaling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान|अवानं|अवानः
अवान 2. अ-वान, अस्, आ, अम् (for अन्-अवान ?),<BR>dried, dry. See वान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तर|अवांतर|अवान्तरं
अवान्तर अवान्तर (अव-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>situated between; included, involved.<BR>—अवान्तर-<BR>दिश्, क्, or अवान्तर-दिशा, f. an intermediate region<BR>of the compass.<BR>—अवान्तर-देश, अस्, m. a place<BR>situated in an intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तराम्|अवांतराम्
अवान्तराम्, ind., Ved. between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्
अवाप् अवाप् (अव-आप्), cl. 5. P. A. -आप्नोति,<BR>-नुते, -आप्तुम्, to reach, enter; to receive; to attain,<BR>obtain, gain; to get, suffer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्त
अवाप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, reached, received, obtained,<BR>got.<BR>—अवाप्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, reaching, obtaining,<BR>receiving, taking; entertaining (as a belief).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तव्य
अवाप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be obtained or gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्ति|अवाप्तिः
अवाप्ति, इस्, f. obtaining, getting, receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
1. अवाप्य, ind. having obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
2. अवाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be obtained or gained;<BR>unattainable, unobtainable (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवापित
अवापित अ-वापित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वप्), not<BR>sown (as grain) but planted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवापोह्
अवापोह् अवापोह् (अव-अप-ऊह्), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>अवापोहति, -ते, -हितुम्, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाय|अवायः
अवाय अवाय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. इ with अव),<BR>giving way, yielding, complying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार|अवारं|अवारः
अवार अवार, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. 2. अव or 2.<BR>अवस्, as पार fr. पर or परस्, q. v.), this side,<BR>the near bank of a river.<BR>—अवार-तस्, ind., Ved. to<BR>this side.<BR>—अवार-पार, अस्, m. the ocean.<BR>—अवार-<BR>पारीण, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the ocean; crossing<BR>a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारीण|अवारीणः
अवारीण, अस्, आ, अम्, crossing a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य|अवार्य्य|अवार्य्यं
