अश्नया, f., Ved. hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्नीतपिबता
अश्नीत-पिबता, f. invitation to eat and to drink.<BR>—अश्नीतपिबतीयति, nom. he invites to eat and drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्
1. अश्मन्, आ, m., Ved. eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्न|अश्नः
अश्न 2. अश्न, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. अश् ?), Ved.<BR>a stone; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्म|अश्मः
अश्म, अस्, m. a mountain, a rock; Ved. a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मक|अश्मकः
अश्मक, अस्, ई, m. f., N. of several persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्
2. अश्मन्, आ, m. a stone, especially one fit for<BR>slinging; flint; hard stone, rock; a cloud; thunder-<BR>bolt; sky (?); N. of a Brāhman [cf. Zend aśman;<BR>Pers. asmān; Lith. akmu˚, Them. akmen; Slav.<BR>kamy, Them. kamen].<BR>—अश्म-कदली, f., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—अश्म-कुट्ट or अश्म-कुट्टक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>breaking or brushing anything with a stone, bruised or<BR>broken by stones.<BR>—अश्म-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अश्म-गन्धा, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अश्म-गर्भ,<BR>अम्, n. or अश्मगर्भ-ज, अम्, n. an emerald.<BR>—अश्म-घ्न, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अश्म-<BR>चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. furnished with a disk of<BR>stone.<BR>—अश्म-ज, अम्, n. red chalk; iron.<BR>—अश्म-<BR>जतुक, अम्, n. bitumen.<BR>—अश्म-दारण, अस्, m.<BR>an axe or crow for breaking stones; (अम्), n. splitting<BR>stones or rocks.<BR>—अश्म-दिद्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>throwing rocks or thunderbolts; (Sāy.) one who has<BR>obtained a weapon, having adamantine weapons.<BR>—अश्मन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. made of stone.<BR>—अश्मन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. of stone, stony.<BR>—अश्म-पुष्प, अम्, n. benzoin (styrax).<BR>—अश्म-<BR>भाल, अम्, n. a mortar of stone or iron.<BR>—अश्म-<BR>भिद्, त्, m. the plant Coleus Scutellarioides, supposed<BR>to dissolve stone in the bladder.<BR>—अश्म-भेद or<BR>अश्म-भेदक, अस्, m. the same.<BR>—अश्म-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, made or consisting of stone, stony.<BR>—अश्म-<BR>योनि, इस्, m. an emerald.<BR>—अश्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>stony, of stone.<BR>—अश्म-वर्मन्, अ, n., Ved. a wall<BR>or shield of stone.<BR>—अश्म-व्रज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>included in rocks.<BR>—अश्म-सार, अस्, अम्, m. n. iron;<BR>sapphire.<BR>—अश्मसार-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or<BR>consisting of iron.<BR>—अश्म-हन्मन्, अ, n., Ved. a<BR>stroke of the thunderbolt.<BR>—अश्मास्य (˚मन्-आस्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a stone-mouth or stone-source,<BR>i. e. flowing from a rock.<BR>—अश्मोत्थ (˚मन्-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n. asphalt, bitumen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मर|अश्मरः
अश्मर, अस्, आ, अम्, stony, rocky, appertaining to<BR>stone or rock; (ई), f. strangury, stone or gravel (the<BR>disease).<BR>—अश्मरी-घ्न, अस्, m., N. of the tree<BR>Cratæva Roxburghii R. Br., used as a lithontriptic.<BR>—अश्मरी-भेदन, अम्, n. a lithontriptic.<BR>—अश्म-<BR>री-हर, अस्, m., N. of the tree Pentaptera Arjuna,<BR>used as a lithontriptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मीर|अश्मीरं|अश्मीरः
अश्मीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. stone or gravel (the disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्त|अश्मंत|अश्मन्तं|अश्मन्तः
अश्मन्त अश्मन्त, अम्, n. (fr. 2. अश्मन् ?), a<BR>fire-place; a field, a plain; death; (अस्, आ, अम्), un-<BR>auspicious, unlucky; unbounded, unlimited; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Marut; [with this word compare Gr. κάμινος<BR>and Lat. caminus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्तक|अश्मंतकं|अश्मन्तकं|अश्मंतकः|अश्मन्तकः
अश्मन्तक, अम्, n. a fire-place; a shade for a<BR>lamp; (अस्), m., N. of a plant, from the fibres of<BR>which a Brāhman's girdle may be made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्र|अश्रं|अश्रः
अश्र 1. अश्र, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. अश्, wrongly<BR>spelt अस्र), a corner [cf. अश्रि].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्र|अश्रं|अश्रः
अश्र 2. अश्र, अम्, n. = अश्रु, a tear, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राय
अश्राय, nom. A. अश्रायते, -यितुम्, to shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रिन्
अश्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having tears, in tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्र|अश्रं|अश्रः
अश्र 3. अश्र, अम्, n. = अस्र, blood, q. v.<BR>—अश्र-प, अस्, m. fiend, a cannibal, ‘a blood-drinker.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्ध
अश्रद्ध अ-श्रद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. धा with<BR>श्रद्), not trusting in (with loc. c.); unbelieving;<BR>(आ), f. want of trust, unbelief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्दधान|अश्रद्दधानः
अ-श्रद्दधान, अस्, आ, अम्, unbelieving, incre-<BR>dulous, having no faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्धेय|अश्रद्धेयं
अ-श्रद्धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be believed, in-<BR>credible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राद्ध|अश्राद्धः
अ-श्राद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not performing funeral<BR>rites, not entitled to them, not belonging or relating<BR>to them; (अस्), m. non-performance of funeral rites.<BR>—अ-श्राद्ध-भोजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has taken<BR>the vow not to eat during the performance of the<BR>Śrāddha ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रम|अश्रमः
अश्रम अ-श्रम, अस्, m. (rt. श्रम्), freedom<BR>from fatigue, freshness; absence of toil, laziness;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. indefatigable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रमण|अश्रमणः
अ-श्रमण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. indefatigable; (अस्),<BR>m. one who is not an ascetic or Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रान्त|अश्रांत|अश्रान्तं|अश्रान्तः
अ-श्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, untired, unwearied, eternal,<BR>continual; (अम्), ind. unweariedly, continually, unin-<BR>terruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रवण|अश्रवणः
अश्रवण अ-श्रवण, अम्, n. (rt. श्रु), loss of<BR>hearing, deafness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राव्य
अ-श्राव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be heard, unfit to be<BR>heard, not to be spoken of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रातस्
अश्रातस् अ-श्रातस्, ind. (rt. श्रा), Ved. in<BR>an uncooked manner, raw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रि|अश्रिः
अश्रि अश्रि, इस्, or अश्री, f. (fr. rt. 1. अश्?),<BR>the sharp side of anything, a corner, angle of a room<BR>or house; the edge of a sword [cf. Lat. acies, acer;<BR>Lith. assmu˚].<BR>—अश्रि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, cornered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रित
अश्रित अ-श्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unap-<BR>proached, difficult of access; not stopping (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रिन्
अश्रिन् अश्रिन्. See under 2. अश्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीक
अश्रीक अ-श्रीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. श्री, q. v.),<BR>unlucky, unpropitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीमत्|अश्रीमन्त्
अ-श्रीमत्, आन्, अती, अत्, unfortunate, inglorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीर
अ-श्रीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. unpleasant, ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रील
अ-श्रील, अस्, आ, अम्, unprosperous, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लीक
अ-श्लीक, अस्, आ, अम् (श्ली substituted for श्री), un-<BR>lucky, unpropitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लील
अ-श्लील, अस्, आ, अम्, unpleasant, ugly; coarse, vul-<BR>gar; abusive, blackguard; (अम्), n. rustic language,<BR>untruth, low abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रु
अश्रु अश्रु, उ, n. a tear [supposed to stand<BR>for दश्रु fr. rt. दंश्; cf. Gr. δάκρυ Lat. lacryma<BR>for dacryma; Goth. tagrs, Them. tagra; Eng. tear;<BR>Mod. Germ. Zähre; Lith. aszara].<BR>—अश्रु-कला,<BR>f. a tear-drop.<BR>—अश्रु-नाली, f. Fistula Lachrymalis.<BR>—अश्रु-परिपूर्णाक्ष(˚ण-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, whose<BR>eyes are filled with tears.<BR>—अश्रु-परिप्लुत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, bathed in tears.<BR>—अश्रु-पात, अस्, m. flow of<BR>tears.<BR>—अश्रु-पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with tears.<BR>—अश्रु-पूर्णाकुल (˚ण-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, troubled<BR>and filled with tears.<BR>—अश्रु-पूर्णाक्ष(˚ण-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, whose eyes are filled with tears.<BR>—अश्रु-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having tears on the face.<BR>—अश्रु-<BR>लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, having tears in the eyes.<BR>—अश्रू-<BR>पहत (˚रु-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, affected by tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुत|अश्रुतं
अश्रुत अ-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. श्रु), unheard,<BR>inaudible; contrary to the Vedas; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>son of Kṛṣṇa, also of Dyutimat.<BR>—अश्रुत-वत्, ind.<BR>as if it were not heard.<BR>—अश्रुत-व्रण, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुति|अश्रुतिः
अ-श्रुति, इस्, f. not hearing, forgetfulness; not being<BR>directed by the Vedas.<BR>—अ-श्रुति-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not striking the hearing; not knowing the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेयस्
अश्रेयस् अ-श्रेयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, not the better,<BR>inferior, worse; worthless, useless, unprofitable, bad;<BR>(अस्), n. mischief, unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेष्ठ
अ-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, not the best, inferior,<BR>worse; bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेष्मन्
अश्रेष्मन् अ-श्रेष्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. without<BR>bands (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रोत्रिय
अश्रोत्रिय अ-श्रोत्रिय, अस्, m. a Brāhman<BR>who has not read the Vedas; not a theologian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघा
अश्लाघा अ-श्लाघा, f. (rt. श्लाघ्), absence of<BR>self-applause, modesty, reserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघ्य
अ-श्लाघ्य or अ-श्लाघनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, unde-<BR>serving of honour or praise, worthless; base, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषा
अश्लेषा अ-श्लेषा, f. (rt. श्लिष्), the ninth<BR>Nakṣatra or lunar mansion, containing five stars;<BR>disunion, disjunction.<BR>—अश्लेषा-भव, अस्, or अश्ले-<BR>षा-भू, ऊस्, m. a N. of Ketu, i. e. the descending<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-b" target="_blank">Page0101-b+ 80</a>]<BR>node or dragon's tail; (as formed of the lower ex-<BR>tremities of the Daitya Saiṃhika, who was cut in two<BR>by Viṣṇu at the churning of the ocean.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लोन
अश्लोन अ-श्लोन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not lame,<BR>not crippled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व|अश्वः
अश्व 1. अश्व, अस्, m. (rt. 1. अश्?), a horse,<BR>especially a stallion; the number ‘seven’ (that being<BR>the number of the horses of the sun); a race of men<BR>horse-like in strength; N. of a son of Citraka, also<BR>of a Dānava; (आ), f. a mare; (औ), du. a horse and<BR>a mare [cf. Zend aśpa; Lat. equus; Gr. ἵππος<BR>Lith. aszwa; Old Sax. ehuscalc].<BR>—अश्व-कन्दिका,<BR>f., N. of the plant Physalis Flexuosa.<BR>—अश्व-कर्ण, अस्,<BR>m. the ear of a horse; N. of the tree Vatica Robusta<BR>W. and A., so called from the shape of its leaves;<BR>a term in surgery for a particular fracture of the<BR>bones; N. of a mountain.<BR>—अश्व-कर्णक, अस्, m. =<BR>the preceding in all but its last sense.<BR>—अश्व-कुटी, f.<BR>a stable for horses.<BR>—अश्व-कुशल or अश्व-कोविद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in horses.<BR>—अश्व-क्रन्द, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a bird.<BR>—अश्व-खुर, अस्, m. a horse's<BR>hoof; a perfume, apparently a dried shell-fish; (आ or<BR>ई), f. the plant Clitoria Ternatea Lin.<BR>—अश्व-गति,<BR>इस्, f. the pace of a horse; N. of a metre containing<BR>four verses of sixteen syllables each.<BR>—अश्व-गन्धा,<BR>f. the plant Physalis Flexuosa Lin.<BR>—अश्व-गोयुग,<BR>अम्, n. a pair of horses.<BR>—अश्व-गोष्ठ, अम्, n. a<BR>stable.<BR>—अश्व-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘horse-neck,’ N. of a<BR>demon, a foe of Viṣṇu, more commonly called Haya-<BR>grīva.<BR>—अश्व-घाम, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>घास, अस्, m. pasture for horses.<BR>—अश्व-घोष,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist.<BR>—अश्व-घ्न, अस्, m.<BR>‘horse-bane,’ N. of a kind of Oleander, Nerium<BR>Odorum Ait.<BR>—अश्व-चलन-शाला, f. a riding-house.<BR>—अश्व-चिकित्सक, अस्, m. a farrier, a veterinary sur-<BR>geon.<BR>—अश्व-चिकित्सा, f. farriery.<BR>—अश्व-जघन,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of centaur, a being with lower limbs like<BR>those of a horse.<BR>—अश्व-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. gaining<BR>horses by conquest; (त्), m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>Bhikṣu.<BR>—अश्व-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage near Kānyakubja on the Gaṅgā.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving horses.<BR>—अश्व-दंष्ट्रा, f.<BR>the plant Tribulus Lanuginosus Lin.<BR>—अश्व-दा, आस्,<BR>m., Ved. or अश्व-दावन्, आ, m., Ved. giving horses.<BR>—अश्व-दूत, अस्, m. a riding messenger.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>नदी, f., N. of a river.<BR>—अश्व-नाय, अस्, m. a horse-<BR>herd, i. e. one who has the charge of a drove of<BR>grazing horses.<BR>—अश्व-निबन्धिक, अस्, m. lit. ‘a<BR>horse-fastener,’ a groom.<BR>—अश्व-निर्णिज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>decorated or embellished with horses.<BR>—अश्व-प, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. a groom.<BR>—अश्व-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord<BR>of horses; N. of several persons, of a king of Madra<BR>and father of Sāvitrī; and of an Asura.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>पर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having horses for wings.<BR>—अश्व-पस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having horses for<BR>(its) home or seat or source, consisting in horses (?),<BR>depending on horses (?).<BR>—अश्व-पाद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>horse-footed.<BR>—अश्व-पाल, अस्, m. a groom.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>पुच्छी, f. the plant Glycine Debilis Ait.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>पृष्ठ, अम्, n. horseback.<BR>—अश्व-पेशस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. decorated or embellished with horses.<BR>—अश्व-बडव or अश्व-वडव, अम्, n. horses.<BR>and mares; (औ), m. du. a horse and a mare.<BR>—अश्व-बन्ध, अस्, m. lit. ‘a horse-fastener,’ a<BR>groom, an ostler.<BR>—अश्व-बन्धन, अम्, n. fasten-<BR>ing of horses; (अस्, ई, अम्), used for fastening horses.<BR>—अश्व-बला, f., N. of a vegetable.<BR>—अश्व-बाल or<BR>अश्व-वाल, अस्, m. tail or hair of a horse; a kind<BR>of reed, Saccharum Spontaneum Lin.<BR>—अश्व-बाहु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a son of Citraka.<BR>—अश्व-बुध्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. based on horses, having its origin in<BR>horses, standing on horses, i. e. on a carriage drawn<BR>by horses.<BR>—अश्व-बुध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. based<BR>on horses, having its origin in horses (as wealth),<BR>distinguished by horses.<BR>—अश्व-भा, f. lightning.<BR>—अश्व-महिषिका, f. the natural enmity of a<BR>horse and a buffalo.<BR>—अश्व-मार or अश्व-मारक,<BR>अस्, or अश्व-हन्तृ, ता, m. ‘horse-destroying,’ a<BR>kind of Oleander, Nerium Odorum.<BR>—अश्व-माल,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of serpent.<BR>—अश्वम्-इष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-c" target="_blank">Page0101-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Ved. seeking or wishing for horses; procuring<BR>horses, an epithet of Agni; (Sāy.) whose rites are<BR>pervasive, or who desires quick worship.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having the head or countenance<BR>of a horse; (अस्), m. a Kinnara or celestial chorister<BR>(so represented); according to others, a kind of<BR>demi-god distinct from the preceding; N. of a pe-<BR>culiar race of people.<BR>—अश्व-मुच्, क्, m. a horse-<BR>stealer.<BR>—अश्व-मेध, अस्, m. the horse-sacrifice;<BR>(a celebrated ceremony, the antiquity of which<BR>reaches back to the Vedic period. For example,<BR>hymns 162 and 163 in the first Maṇḍala of the<BR>Ṛg-veda were used at this sacrifice. In later times<BR>its efficacy was so exaggerated, that a hundred such<BR>sacrifices entitled the sacrificer to displace Indra from<BR>the dominion of Svarga; kings who engaged in it<BR>spent enormous sums in gifts to the Brāhmans. It<BR>is said that the horse was sometimes not immolated,<BR>but kept bound during the ceremony); N. of a son of<BR>Bharata.<BR>—अश्वमेध-काण्ड, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>thirteenth book of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>मेध-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—अश्वमेधिक<BR>or अश्वमेधीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the horse-<BR>sacrifice; (अस्), m. a horse fit for the sacrifice, called<BR>Aśva-medha.<BR>—अश्व-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. harnessing<BR>horses; having horses put to (as a carriage); (क्), f.,<BR>N. of a constellation, the head of Aries; the first<BR>lunar mansion; m. the month Āśvina (Sept. — Oct.);<BR>(क्, क्, क्), born under the constellation Aśvayuj.<BR>—अ-<BR>श्व-युज, अस्, m. the month Āśvina.<BR>—अश्व-यूप,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. the post to which the sacrificial horse<BR>was bound.<BR>—अश्व-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing<BR>the yoking of horses, joining or reaching as quickly<BR>as horses.<BR>—अश्व-रक्ष, अस्, m. the keeper or rider<BR>of a horse, a groom.<BR>—अश्व-रथ, अस्, m. a carriage<BR>drawn by horses; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. furnishing horses.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>रोधक, अस्, m., N. of the plant Nerium Odorum<BR>Ait.<BR>—अश्व-ललित, N. of a species of the Vikṛti<BR>metre.<BR>—अश्व-लाला, f. a kind of snake.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>लोमन्, आ, m. horse-hair; a kind of snake.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>वक्त्र, अस्, m. a Kinnara or Gandharba.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>वडव, अम्, n. a stud of horses and mares;<BR>(औ), m. du. a horse and a mare; (आस्), m. horses<BR>and mares, see अश्व-बडव. — 1. अश्व-वत्, ind. like<BR>a horse.<BR>—२. अश्व-वत्, or Ved. अश्वा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessed of horses, consisting of horses.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>वदन, अस्, m., N. of a people.<BR>—अश्व-वह, अस्,<BR>m. a horseman.<BR>—अश्व-वार or अश्व-वाल, अस्, m.<BR>a horseman, a groom.<BR>—अश्व-वारक, अस्, m. a<BR>horseman, a groom.<BR>—अश्व-वारण, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the Bos Gavæus.<BR>—अश्व-वाह or अश्व-वाहक,<BR>अस्, m. a horseman.<BR>—अश्व-विक्रयिन्, ई, m. a<BR>horse-dealer.<BR>—अश्व-विद्, त्, त्, त्, skilled in taming<BR>horses, an epithet of Nala; a jockey; Ved. procuring<BR>horses.<BR>—अश्व-वृष, अस्, m., Ved. a stallion.<BR>—अश्व-वैद्य, अस्, m. a farrier, a veterinary surgeon.<BR>—अश्व-शक, अम्, n., Ved. excrements of a horse.<BR>—अश्व-शकृत्, त्, n. excrements of a horse, horse-<BR>dung; N. of a river.<BR>—अश्व-शङ्कु, उस्, m., N. of<BR>a Dānava.<BR>—अश्व-शाला, f. a stable.<BR>—अश्व-शाव, अस्,<BR>m. a foal, a colt.<BR>—अश्व-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a manual<BR>or text-book of veterinary science.<BR>—अश्व-शिरस्,<BR>अस्, n. a horse's head; (आस्, आस्, अस्), having the head<BR>of a horse, an epithet of Nārāyaṇa; (आस्), m., N. of<BR>a Dānava.<BR>—अश्व-शृगालिका, f. the natural enmity<BR>between the horse and the jackal.<BR>—अश्व-श्चन्द्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing joy (by means of) horses;<BR>brilliant with horses.<BR>—अश्व-षङ्गव, अम्, n. a set<BR>or team of six horses.<BR>—अश्व-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. or<BR>अश्व-सा or अश्व-षा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. gaining or<BR>procuring horses.<BR>—अश्व-साद, अस्, or अश्व-सादिन्,<BR>ई, m. a horseman, a rider, a horse-soldier.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>सारथ्य, अम्, n. management of horses and cars,<BR>horsemanship and driving, coachmanship, charioteer-<BR>ship.<BR>—अश्व-सूक्ति, इस्, m., N. of an author of Vedic<BR>hymns.<BR>—अश्व-सूनृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praised<BR>sincerely for (the gift of) horses; whose praise for<BR>(giving) horses is agreeable and true.<BR>—अश्व-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—अश्वसेन-नृप-नन्दन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king and saint, also Sanatkumāra.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">Page0102-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—अश्वस्तोमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to the<BR>praise of the sacrificial horse.<BR>—अश्व-स्थान, अम्,<BR>n. a stable or stall for horses; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>born in a stable.<BR>—अश्व-हय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>driving or spurring a horse.<BR>—अश्व-हारक, अस्,<BR>m. a horse-stealer.<BR>—अश्व-हृदय, अम्, n. horse-<BR>manship.<BR>—अश्वाक्ष (˚व-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a plant.<BR>—अश्वाजनी (˚व-अज्˚), f. a whip.<BR>—अश्व-<BR>धिक (˚व-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, strong in cavalry,<BR>superior in horses.<BR>—अश्वाध्यक्ष (˚व-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a guardian of horses.<BR>—अश्वा-मघ, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. rich in horses.<BR>—अश्वायुर्-वेद (˚व-आय्˚), अस्,<BR>m. veterinary science.<BR>—अश्वारि (˚व-अरि), इस्, m. a<BR>buffalo.<BR>—अश्वारूढ (˚व-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted,<BR>sitting on horseback.<BR>—अश्वारोह (˚व-आ˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>riding or mounted on a horse; (अस्), m. a horseman;<BR>(आ), f., N. of the plant Aśvagandhā.<BR>—अश्वारोहक<BR>(˚व-आर्˚), अस्, m., N. of the plant Aśvagandhā.<BR>—अश्वारोहिन् (˚व-आर्˚), ई, इणी, इ, mounted or<BR>riding on horseback.<BR>—अश्वा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, fur-<BR>nished with horses.<BR>—अश्वावरोहक (˚व-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of the plant Aśvagandhā.<BR>—अश्वेषित (˚व-<BR>इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hurried along by horse.<BR>—अश्वोरस<BR>(˚व-उर्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, broad-chested like a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व|अश्वः
2. अश्व, nom. P. अश्वति, to behave like a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वक|अश्वकः
अश्वक, अस्, आ, अम्, horse-like, acting like a horse,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. a small horse; a bad horse, a hack; a<BR>stray horse, one whose owner is not known; any horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकिनी
अश्वकिनी, f. the first Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतर|अश्वतरः
अश्वतर, अस्, आ, अम्, swift, speedy; (अस्, ई), m.<BR>f. a mule; (अस्), m. a male calf; N. of a Gandharva;<BR>one of the chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent-race, inha-<BR>biting the regions under the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थ|अश्वत्थः
अश्वत्थ, अस्, m. the holy fig tree, Ficus Religiosa<BR>L. (under which horses stand; त्थ = स्थ); Ved. a<BR>vessel made of its wood; N. of another tree (= गर्द-<BR>भाण्ड); the fruit of the Ficus Religiosa; the time at<BR>which it bears; an epithet of the sun; N. of a man;<BR>N. of a people; (आ), f. day of full moon in the month<BR>Āśvina, in which month the fruits of the Ficus Re-<BR>ligiosa generally become ripe; day of full moon; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अश्वत्थ-कुण, अस्, m. the fruit<BR>season of the holy fig tree.<BR>—अश्वत्थ-भेद, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a tree, Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थक|अश्वत्थकः
अश्वत्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, to be given or to be done<BR>&c. when the Aśvattha tree bears; (अम्), n. the pe-<BR>tals of the Arabian jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

