अश्वयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desiring horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वल|अश्वलः
अश्वल, अस्, m., N. of the Hotṛ-priest of Janaka,<BR>king of Videha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्य
अश्वस्य, nom. P. अश्वस्यति, -यितुम्, to wish for<BR>the stallion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वाय
अश्वाय, nom. P. अश्वायति, -यितुम्, Ved. to wish<BR>for horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विक
अश्विक, अस्, ई, अम्, drawn by horses, carried by<BR>horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विन्
अश्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. possessed of horses, consist-<BR>ing of horses; (ई), m. a cavalier, a horse-tamer;<BR>(नौ), m. du. the two charioteers; N. of two divini-<BR>ties, who appear in the sky before the dawn in a<BR>golden carriage drawn by horses or birds; they bring<BR>treasures to men and avert misfortune and sickness;<BR>in later times they are considered as the physicians of<BR>Svarga or heaven; (in astronomy) they are the twins<BR>of the zodiac; (इनी), f. a nymph, considered in later<BR>times as the mother of the Aśvins; she was the wife of<BR>Sūrya or the sun, who concealed herself in the form of<BR>a mare; (in astronomy) the head of Aries or the first<BR>of the twenty-eight Nakṣatras or lunar mansions;<BR>(इ), n., Ved. richness in horses.<BR>—अश्वि-देवताक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, whose divinities are the Aśvins.<BR>—अश्विनी-<BR>कुमार or अश्विनी-पुत्र or अश्विनी-सुत, औ, m. du.<BR>the twin sons of Sañjñā, the sun's wife, in the form<BR>of Aśvinī, commonly called the Aśvins.<BR>—अश्वि-मत्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">Page0102-b+ 77</a>]<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, (any Mantra &c.) containing the word<BR>Aśvin.<BR>—अश्वि-सालोक्य, अम्, n. the heaven or station<BR>of the Aśvins, to which the giver of a horse is raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विय
अश्विय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. referring to horses; (आ),<BR>Ved. neut. pl. a troop of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीन|अश्वीनः
अश्वीन, अस्, आ, अम्, distant a day's journey for a<BR>horse; more usually आश्वीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीय|अश्वीयं|अश्वीयः
अश्वीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>horse, conducive to horses; (अम्), n. a number of<BR>horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व्य|अश्व्यः
अश्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to or coming<BR>from horses; consisting of horses; (अम्), n., Ved. a<BR>number of horses, possession of horses; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of Vaśa, the son of Aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वन्त|अश्वंत|अश्वन्तं|अश्वन्तः
अश्वन्त अश्वन्त, अम्, n. (connected with<BR>अश्मन्त, q. v.), death; a field; a fire-place; ter-<BR>mination, limit; (अस्, आ, अम्), unlucky, inauspicious,<BR>unbounded, unlimited. [In the first sense अश्वन्त<BR>may be for असु-अन्त, ‘end of life.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तन
अश्वस्तन अ-श्वस्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, or अ-श्वस्त-<BR>निक, अस्, आ, अम्, of to-day, not of or not for to-mor-<BR>row; one who makes no provision for to-morrow.<BR>—अ-श्वस्तन-विद्, त्, त्, त्, ignorant of the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्
अष् अष्, cl. 1. P. A. अषति, -ते, -षितुम्,<BR>to go or move; to take or receive; to<BR>shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्षीण|अषडक्षीणः
अषडक्षीण अषडक्षीण, अम्, n. (fr. अ,<BR>षष्, अक्षि), anything not seen by six eyes, i. e.<BR>known or determined by two persons to the ex-<BR>clusion of a third; a secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषतर
अषतर अषतर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (fr. a<BR>positive, which is not preserved, but may be referred<BR>to rt. 1. अश्), more accessible or acceptable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढ|अषाढः
अषाढ अ-षाढ, or Ved. अ-षाऌह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not to be overcome, invincible; born under the<BR>constellation Aṣāḍhā; (अस्), m. the month Aṣāḍha<BR>(or Āṣāḍha), commencing with the sun's entrance<BR>into Gemini (June-July); a staff made of the wood<BR>of Palāśa, carried by a student during the performance<BR>of certain vows; N. of a teacher; N. of the Malaya<BR>mountain; (आ), f., N. of a sacred brick; N. of a<BR>constellation; pl. the eighteenth and nineteenth or<BR>twentieth and twenty-first lunar mansions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढक|अषाढकः
अषाढक, अस्, m. the month Aṣāḍha (or<BR>Āṣāḍha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टन्
अष्टन् अष्टन्, अ or औ (but अष्टौ is more<BR>common for nom., acc., and voc. cases), pl. eight<BR>[cf. Lat. octo; Gr. ὀκτώ Goth. ahtau; Mod. Germ.<BR>acht; Eng. eight; Lith. aszt˚uni; Slav. osmj]; in<BR>comp. with other numerals often अष्टा, e. g. अष्टा-<BR>दशन्, eighteen; अष्टादश, अस्, ई, अम्, the eigh-<BR>teenth, divided into eighteen parts; अष्टादश-धा,<BR>eighteen-fold; अष्टा-विंशति, twenty-eight; अष्टा-<BR>विंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the twenty-eighth, divided in-<BR>to twenty-eight parts; अष्टात्रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>the thirty-eighth, containing thirty-eight; अष्टा-<BR>चत्वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the forty-eighth.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has the number eight<BR>as a mark burnt in his ear; (अस्), m. eight-eared,<BR>an epithet of Brahmā, who is supposed to have four<BR>heads; (ई), m., N. of a man.<BR>—अष्ट-कृत्वस्, ind.<BR>eight times.<BR>—अष्ट-कोण, अस्, m. an octagon.<BR>—अष्ट-खण्ड, अस्, m. title of a collection of<BR>several sections of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—अष्ट-गव, अम्,<BR>n. a flock of eight cows.<BR>—अष्ट-गाध् (?), त्, m. a<BR>fabulous animal (called Śarabha), supposed to have<BR>eight legs; a spider (?).<BR>—अष्ट-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>eight-fold; (अम्), n. the eight qualities.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>गुणाश्रय (˚ण-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with the<BR>eight qualities, epithet of a king.<BR>—अष्ट-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. condition of eight.<BR>—अष्ट-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Virūpa, author of a hymn of the<BR>Ṛg-veda; N. of a Dānava.<BR>—अष्ट-दल, an octa-<BR>gon.<BR>—अष्ट-दिक्-पाल, आस्, m. pl. the regents of<BR>the cardinal points, as Indra of the East, Agni or<BR>Vahni of the S. E., Yama of the South, Nairṛta of<BR>the S. W., Varuṇa of the West, Marut of the N. W.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-c" target="_blank">Page0102-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Kuvera of the North, and Īśa or Śiva of the N. E.<BR>—अष्ट-दिश्, क्, f. the eight cardinal points of the<BR>compass collectively.<BR>—अष्ट-धा, ind. eight-fold,<BR>eight times, in eight parts or sections.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>धातु, उ, n. the eight metals collectively, as gold,<BR>silver, copper, tin, lead, brass, iron, and steel.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>पद, अस्, m. a Vedic metre of eight Padas.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>पाद्, त्, त्, त्, having eight legs; (त्), m. a spider;<BR>a fabulous animal with eight legs.<BR>—अष्ट-पाद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having eight legs; (अस्), m. a kind of spider<BR>with a small body and long legs.<BR>—अष्ट-पादिका,<BR>f., N. of the plant Vallaris Dichotomus Wall.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>मङ्गल, अस्, m. a horse with a white face, tail,<BR>mane, breast, and hoofs; (अम्), n. a collection of<BR>eight lucky things to be assembled on certain occa-<BR>sions (such as a coronation &c.), e. g. a lion, a bull, an<BR>elephant, a water-jar, a fan, a flag, a trumpet, and a<BR>lamp; or, according to others, a Brāhman, a cow,<BR>fire, gold, ghee, the sun, water, and a king.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>मान, अम्, n. a measure, one kuḍava.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>मासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, occurring once in eight months.<BR>—अष्ट-मूर्ति, इस्, m. eight-formed, an epithet of<BR>Śiva (as identified with the five elements, mind,<BR>egotism, and matter; or, according to the opening of<BR>the Śakuntalā, with the five elements, the sun and<BR>moon and the sacrificing priest).<BR>—अष्टमूर्ति-<BR>धर, अस्, m. possessing eight forms, an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—अष्ट-रत्न, अम्, n. the eight jewels,<BR>title of a collection of eight Ślokas on ethics.<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>रसाश्रय (˚स-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, endowed or furnished<BR>with the eight rasas or sentiments of poetry.<BR>—अष्-<BR>टर्च (˚टन्-ऋच्), अस्, m. a psalm or hymn consisting<BR>of eight verses.<BR>—अष्ट-लोहक, अम्, n. a class of<BR>eight metals, gold, silver, copper, tin, lead, the magnet,<BR>muṇḍaloha (?), and tīkṣṇaloha or steel (?).<BR>—अष्ट-<BR>वर्ग, अस्, m. a class of three principal medicaments<BR>(mostly the roots of plants from the hills), named<BR>Ṛṣabha, Jīvaka, Medā, Mahāmedā, Ṛddhi, Vṛd-<BR>dhi, Kākolī, and Kṣīrakākolī.<BR>—अष्ट-विध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, eight-fold, of eight kinds.<BR>—अष्ट-शत,<BR>अम्, n. eight hundred.<BR>—अष्ट-श्रवण, अस्, or<BR>अष्ट-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of Brahmā (eight-eared,<BR>see अष्ट-कर्ण).<BR>—अष्टसाहस्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>consisting of eight thousand.<BR>—अष्टा-कपाल, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, (an oblation) prepared or offered in eight pans;<BR>(अस्), m. a sacrifice in which ghee or clarified butter<BR>is offered in eight pans.<BR>—अष्टाक्षर (˚टन्-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, containing eight syllables; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—अष्टा-गव, अम्, n. a car or wain, one<BR>drawn by eight oxen.<BR>—अष्टाङ्ग (˚टन्-अङ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. eight parts of the body with which very profound<BR>obeisance is performed (viz. the hands, breast, fore-<BR>head, eyes, throat, and middle of the back; or the<BR>first four, with the knees and feet; or these six, with<BR>the speech and mind); the eight parts of a court, or<BR>the law, the judge, assessors, scribe, and astrologer,<BR>gold, fire, and water; any whole consisting of eight<BR>parts or members; a die, dice; (अस्, आ, अम्), con-<BR>sisting of eight parts or members.<BR>—अष्टाङ्ग-<BR>नय, अस्, m. = अष्टाङ्ग.<BR>—अष्टाङ्ग-पात or<BR>अष्टाङ्ग-प्रणाम, अस्, m. prostration of the eight<BR>parts of the body as in reverence.<BR>—अष्टाङ्ग-<BR>हृदय, अम्, n. title of a medicinal work.<BR>—अष्-<BR>टाङ्गार्घ्य (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्, m. an offering of eight<BR>articles, water, milk, kuśa grass, curds, ghee, rice,<BR>barley, and mustard; or honey, red oleander flow-<BR>ers, and sandal are substituted for the last three.<BR>—अष्टा-दंष्ट्र = अष्ट-दंष्ट्र, q. v.<BR>—अष्-<BR>टादश-भुजा, f., N. of the wife of Śiva.<BR>—अष्टा-<BR>दशाङ्ग (˚शन्-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a decoction of eighteen<BR>ingredients.<BR>—अष्टाध्यायी (˚टन्-अध्˚), f. title of<BR>the eleventh Kāṇḍa of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa, con-<BR>sisting of eight lectures.<BR>—अष्टानवत, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>the ninety-eighth.<BR>—अष्टा-पद, अस्, m. a spider;<BR>a worm; a fabulous animal with eight legs, the Śa-<BR>rabha; a wild sort of jasmin; a pin or bolt; the<BR>mountain Kailāsa or abode of Kuvera; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. a kind of chequered cloth or board for drafts, dice,<BR>&c.; gold.<BR>—अष्टा-पद-पत्त्र, अम्, n. gold-leaf;<BR>a sheet of gold.<BR>—अष्टा-पाद्, त्, -पदी, m. f., Ved.<BR>having eight legs, consisting of eight members; (in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">Page0103-a+ 77</a>]<BR>ritual language) a term for a pregnant animal; (पदी),<BR>f. a wild sort of jasmin.<BR>—अष्टा-पाद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>quartered by eight, having eight for the root.<BR>—अष्-<BR>टा-पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, eight-fold.<BR>—अष्टार-चक्र-<BR>वत् (˚टन्-अर्˚), आन्, m. having a wheel with eight<BR>spokes, an epithet of Mañju-śrī, a Jaina saint and<BR>ruler.<BR>—अष्टा-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Bhīma-<BR>ratha.<BR>—अष्टा-वक्र, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman, a<BR>son of Kahoḍa.<BR>—अष्टास्र (˚टन्-अस्˚), अम्, n. an oc-<BR>tagon.<BR>—अष्टास्रय (˚टन्-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, octan-<BR>gular.<BR>—अष्टाह (˚टन्-अह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, lasting eight<BR>days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक|अष्टकः
अष्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of eight parts,<BR>eight-fold; one who studies or is acquainted with the<BR>eight books of Pāṇini's grammar or the formulas of<BR>the Veda; (अस्), m. the eighth part, e. g. of the Ṛg-<BR>veda; N. of a son of Viśvāmitra; (आ), f. the eighth<BR>day after full moon; especially the eighth day of<BR>three months, on which the progenitors or manes are<BR>worshipped; worship of the progenitors or manes on<BR>certain days, vegetables, flesh, and cake being seve-<BR>rally offered upon these occasions, and the Brāhmans<BR>feasted; (अम्), n. a whole consisting of eight parts,<BR>e. g. the eight sections of Pāṇini's grammar.<BR>—अष्-<BR>टकाङ्ग (˚क-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a kind of board or cloth<BR>for playing with dice on, having eight divisions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकिन्
अष्टकिन्, ई, m. one who performs an Aṣṭakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतय
अष्टतय, अम्, n. a conjunction or aggregate of<BR>eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टम|अष्टमः
अष्टम, अस्, ई, अम्, the eighth; (अस्), m. the<BR>eighth part; (ई), f. (scil. रात्रि), the eighth day<BR>(night) in a half-month; N. of the medicinal plant<BR>Kṣīrakākolī, the last of a class of eight medicinal<BR>plants.<BR>—अष्टम-कालिक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>omitting seven meals partakes only of the eighth.<BR>—अष्टमांश (˚म-अं˚), an eighth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमक
अष्टमक, अस्, आ, अम्, the eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमिका
अष्टमिका, f. a śukti or weight of four tolas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टातय|अष्टातयः
अष्टातय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of eight parts;<BR>(अम्), n. collection of eight things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टि|अष्टिः
1. अष्टि, इस्, f., N. of a metre consisting of sixty-<BR>four syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टिन्
अष्टिन्, ई, इनी, इ, consisting of eight members or<BR>syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टि|अष्टिः
अष्टि 2. अष्टि, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 1. अस्), Ved. reaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ट्रा
अष्ट्रा अष्ट्रा, f. (fr. rt. 1. अश्?), Ved. a<BR>prick or goad for driving cattle; (sometimes regarded<BR>as the badge of the agriculturist, as the staff is of the<BR>Brāhman); [cf. Zend astrâ; Lith. akstinas.].<BR>—अष्-<BR>ट्रा-विन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. obeying the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठि|अष्ठिः
अष्ठि अष्ठि, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 1. अश्? connected<BR>with अशन् and अश्मन्), seed; a kernel, a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीला
अष्ठीला, f. a globular body; a round pebble or<BR>stone; kernel; seed-corn; a globular swelling below<BR>the navel, produced by wind; contusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीलिका
अष्ठीलिका, f. a kind of abscess; a pebble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीवत्|अष्ठीवन्त्
अष्ठी-वत्, वान्, वत्, m. n. the knee, knee-bone;<BR>(by native grammarians derived fr. अस्थि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
अस् 1. अस्, cl. 2. P. अस्ति, (2nd sing. असि,<BR>Impf. आसीत्, Pot. स्यात्, Impv. अस्तु, 2nd<BR>sing. एधि, Perf. आस), to be, live, exist, be present;<BR>to take place, happen; to belong to, be in the pos-<BR>session of (e. g. तस्य न किञ्चित् स्वम् अस्ति, there<BR>is no property belonging to him); to fall to the share<BR>of, to happen to any one (with gen.); to abide,<BR>dwell, stay; to turn out, tend towards any result,<BR>prove (with dat.); to be sufficient for (with dat.);<BR>to become: न अस्, to be lost, to perish; [cf. Gr.<BR>ἐσ-τί Lat. es-t; Goth. is-t; Lith. es-ti; Slav.<BR>jes-tj.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
अस् 2. अस्, cl. 4. P. अस्यति, आस, असिष्यति,<BR>आस्थत्, असितुम्, to throw, cast, shoot at<BR>(with dat., loc., or gen. of the mark); to drive or<BR>frighten away; to throw away, take away, let go, leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन|असनं|असनः
असन, अम्, n. the act of throwing, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
अस् 3. अस्, cl. 1. P. A. असति, -ते, -सितुम्,<BR>to go; to shine; to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयत्|असंयन्त्
असंयत् अ-संयत्, अन्, अती, अत् (rt. इ), Ved.<BR>not entering, not pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयत्त
असंयत्त अ-संयत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. यत्), Ved.<BR>undisturbed, (various reading for अ-संयत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयम|असंयमः
असंयम अ-संयम, अस्, m. (rt. यम्), ab-<BR>sence of check or restraint, especially of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयत|असंयतः
अ-संयत, अस्, आ, अम्, unrestrained, unassailed.<BR>—असंयतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having the<BR>soul uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुक्त
असंयुक्त अ-संयुक्त, अम्, n. (rt. युज्), non-<BR>combination, hiatus (in Vedic grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयोग|असंयोगः
अ-संयोग, अस्, m. absence of union or connec-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुत|असंयुतः
असंयुत अ-संयुत, अस्, m. unmixed, un-<BR>blended; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंरुद्ध
असंरुद्ध अ-संरुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, unob-<BR>structed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंलग्न
असंलग्न अ-संलग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, disjoined,<BR>detached, separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवत्सरभृत
असंवत्सरभृत अ-संवत्सर-भृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. not supported a whole year (as a sacred fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवत्सरभृतिन्
अ-संवत्सरभृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. one who<BR>does not support (a fire) a whole year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंविदान
असंविदान अ-संविदान, अस्, आ, अम्, ignorant,<BR>unwise; not promising or covenanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृत
असंवृत अ-संवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, uncovered,<BR>exposed; imperfectly or scarcely covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंव्यवहितम्
असंव्यवहितम् अ-संव्यवहितम्, ind. im-<BR>mediately, without interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशय
असंशय अ-संशय, अस्, m. absence of<BR>doubt; (अस्, आ, अम्), free from doubt, certain.<BR>—अ-<BR>संशयम्, ind. without doubt, certainly, verily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रव
असंश्रव अ-संश्रव, अस्, m. (rt. श्रु), the<BR>being out of hearing; (ए), ind. out of the hearing of;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), out of hearing, inaudible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रावम्
अ-संश्रावम्, ind. inaudibly, out of the hearing<BR>of (with gen. of the person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्लिष्ट|असंश्लिष्टः
असंश्लिष्ट अ-संश्लिष्ट, अस्, m. not joined,<BR>not in contact, an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसक्त
असंसक्त अ-संसक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not attached<BR>to, not joined together, disunited, indifferent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसिद्ध
असंसिद्ध अ-संसिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, unac-<BR>complished, incomplete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसूक्तगिल
असंसूक्तगिल अ-संसूक्त-गिल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. swallowing whole or without chewing (said of<BR>Rudra's dogs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृति|असंसृतिः
असंसृति अ-संसृति, इस्, f. not returning to<BR>a new course of existence, absorption into the supreme<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृष्ट
असंसृष्ट अ-संसृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, unmixed<BR>with, separate, not living in common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कृत|असंस्कृतः
असंस्कृत अ-संस्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not perfect,<BR>unpolished, rude, common; uninitiated, not having<BR>gone through the proper rites of caste, state, sex, or<BR>age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्तुत
असंस्तुत अ-संस्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, unknown,<BR>unacquainted, not known as acquaintances; not on<BR>terms of friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थान|असंस्थानं
असंस्थान अ-संस्थान, अम्, n. (rt. स्था),<BR>absence of cohesion or configuration; disorder, confu-<BR>sion; want, destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थित
अ-संस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, not arranged or arrayed,<BR>disordered, irregular; not collected; not finished, not<BR>accomplished; not ceasing, not stopping; destitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थिति|असंस्थितिः
अ-संस्थिति, इस्, f. disorder, confusion; want, desti-<BR>tution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहत|असंहतः
असंहत अ-संहत, अस्, आ, अम्, not joined;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">Page0103-c+ 70</a>]<BR>scattered, loose, straggling, uncompressed; (अम्), n.<BR>a form of array, loose or open order of troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहार्य|असंहार्य्य
असंहार्य अ-संहार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, irresistible,<BR>insuperable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहित
असंहित अ-संहित, अस्, आ, अम्, not included<BR>in the संहिता of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकल
असकल अ-सकल, अस्, आ, अम्, not all, not<BR>entire, a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्
असकृत् अ-सकृत्, ind. not once, oftener<BR>than once, again and again, repeatedly.<BR>—असकृत्-<BR>समाधि, इस्, m. repeated meditation.<BR>—असकृद्-<BR>गर्भ-वास, अस्, m. repeated birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्त
असक्त अ-सक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, detached, dis-<BR>united; detached from worldly feelings or passions;<BR>not interested in, unattached to, indifferent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्थ
असक्थ अ-सक्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, without thighs,<BR>thighless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्र
असक्र अ-सक्र, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. सश्च्), Ved. not<BR>ceasing to flow, not drying up; not going elsewhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असखि|असखिः
असखि अ-सखि, आ, m. an untrustworthy<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असखिन्
अ-सखिन्, आ, m. an enemy, an adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असगोत्र
असगोत्र अ-सगोत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, of a different<BR>family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कल्प|असंकल्प
असङ्कल्प अ-सङ्कल्प, अस्, अम्, m. n. absence<BR>of predetermination, absence of interested purpose,<BR>sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कल्पित|असंकल्पित|असङ्कल्पितः
अ-सङ्कल्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, not purposed, not re-<BR>solved or determined on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कसुक|असंकसुक
असङ्कसुक अ-सङ्कसुक, अस्, आ, अम्, not fickle,<BR>unfluctuating, firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कीर्ण|असंकीर्ण
असङ्कीर्ण अ-सङ्कीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, unmixed,<BR>uncompounded, uncollected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कुल|असंकुल|असंकुलः|असङ्कुलः
असङ्कुल अ-सङ्कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, not crowded,<BR>open, clear, broad; (अस्), m. a broad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्केत
असङ्केत अ-सङ्केत, अस्, आ, अम्, not appointed,<BR>not agreed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्केतित|असंकेतित
अ-सङ्केतित, अस्, आ, अम्, uninvited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्य|असंख्य|असंख्यः|असङ्ख्यः
असङ्ख्य अ-सङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ख्या),<BR>without number, innumerable, exceedingly numerous.<BR>—असङ्ख्य-ता, f. or असङ्ख्य-त्व, अम्, n. innu-<BR>merableness, immensity, infinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्यात|असंख्यात|असंख्यातं
अ-सङ्ख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, uncounted, innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्येय|असंख्येय|असंख्येयः
अ-सङ्ख्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, innumerable; (अस्), m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva; (अम्), n., Ved. an innumerable<BR>multitude; an exceedingly large number.<BR>—असङ्-<BR>ख्येय-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, innumerable, unnumbered.<BR>—असङ्ख्येय-ता, f. innumerableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ग|असंग|असंगः
असङ्ग 1. अ-सङ्ग, अस्, m. (rt. सञ्ज्), non-<BR>attachment; (अस्, आ, अम्), not attached, having no<BR>attachment or inclination for or interest in, inde-<BR>pendent, free from ties, not hindered, moving without<BR>hindrance.<BR>—असङ्ग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, not attached<BR>to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गिन्|असंगिन्
अ-सङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not attached to the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असज्जितात्मन्
असज्जितात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having a soul<BR>free from attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ग|असंग|असंगः
असङ्ग 2. अ-सङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. गम् with<BR>सम् and अ prefixed), not united, unassociated, soli-<BR>tary; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Yuyudhāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गत|असंगत
अ-सङ्गत, अस्, आ, अम्, ununited, unaccompanied,<BR>unassociated with; uneven, unequal; improbable, in-<BR>consistent; unpreferred, disesteemed; unbecoming,<BR>unseemly; rude, ill-mannered, unpolished, clownish.<BR>—असङ्गताचरण (˚त-आच्˚), अम्, n. inconsistent<BR>conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गति|असंगति|असंगतिः
अ-सङ्गति, इस्, f. not associating; incongruity, im-<BR>probability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गम|असंगम|असंगमः
अ-सङ्गम, अस्, m. not associating with; separa-<BR>tion, disunion; incongruity; inequality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असचद्विष्
असचद्विष् अ-सच-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. per-<BR>secuting those who are not (his) worshippers; having<BR>no enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असच्छाखा
असच्छाखा असच्-छाखा, असज्-जन, &c. See<BR>under असत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असजात
असजात अ-सजात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not re-<BR>lated by blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असजात्य
अ-सजात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. without consan-<BR>guinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंज्ञ
असंज्ञ अ-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, insensible; (आ),<BR>f., Ved. disunion, disagreement, discord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असञ्ज्ञिसत्त्व|असंज्ञिसत्त्व
अ-सञ्ज्ञि-सत्त्व, आस्, m. pl. a class of Buddhist<BR>divinities (otherwise अ-रङ्गि-सत्त्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्|असन्त्
असत् अ-सत्, अन्, अती, अत्, not being, not ex-<BR>isting, unreal; not as it should be, not answering its<BR>purpose, untrue, wrong, wicked, bad, vile; (ई), f. an<BR>unfaithful or unchaste wife; (न्), m. Indra; (त्), n.<BR>non-existence, non-entity; untruth, falsehood, a lie;<BR>evil.<BR>—असच्-छाखा (असत्-शाखा), f., Ved. an un-<BR>real branch, a seeming member (?).<BR>—असच्-छास्त्र<BR>(असत्-शास्त्र), अम्, n. heretical or heterodox doc-<BR>trine.<BR>—असज्-जन, अस्, m. a bad, wicked, or con-<BR>temptible man.<BR>—असज्-जाति-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>person.<BR>—असत्-कल्पना, f. an untrue action, or one<BR>which never took place; fabrication of falsehood.<BR>—असत्-ता, f. non-existence; untruth; wickedness.<BR>1. असत्-त्व, अम्, n. non-existence; untruth; wick-<BR>edness.<BR>—असत्-पथ, अस्, m. a bad road; evil prac-<BR>tice or doctrine.<BR>—असत्-परिग्रह, अस्, m. receiving<BR>unfit presents, or from improper persons.<BR>—असत्-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. a childless man; a wicked or disre-<BR>putable son.<BR>—असत्-संसर्ग, अस्, m. evil company.<BR>—असत्-सङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, attached to evil; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a doorkeeper or porter in the Prabodha-<BR>candrodaya.<BR>—असद्-अध्येतृ, ता, m. a Brāhman<BR>who reads heterodox works; a heterodox student.<BR>—असद्-आचार, अस्, आ, अम्, following evil practices,<BR>wicked; (अस्), m. evil practice.<BR>—असद्-आचारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, one who follows bad or heterodox practices,<BR>wicked, vile.<BR>—असद्-ग्रह or असद्-ग्राह, अस्, m.<BR>mischievous or wicked trick; caprice, idle or childish<BR>desire.<BR>—असद्ग्रहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, performing mis-<BR>chievous or malicious tricks.<BR>—असद्-दृश्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>evil-eyed.<BR>—असद्-भाव, अस्, m. non-existence, ab-<BR>sence; an evil temperament or disposition.<BR>—असद्-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. low or degrading occupation or profes-<BR>sion; wickedness.<BR>—असद्-व्यवहार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>following evil practices; (अस्), m. evil practices.<BR>—असद्व्यवहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, following evil courses.<BR>—असन्-मन्त्र, अस्, m., Ved. untrue or false<BR>counsel or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतायी
अ-सतायी, f. wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असती
अ-सती, f. an unfaithful or unchaste wife. See above.<BR>—असती-सुत, अस्, m. the son of an unchaste wife,<BR>a bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृ
असत्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to do no<BR>good, to harm, injure, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्मन्|असत्कर्म्मन्
असत्-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, wicked; (अ), n. wicked-<BR>ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कार|असत्कारः
असत्-कार, अस्, m. offence, doing injury; (अ-सत्-<BR>कार), not honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत
असत्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-done, done from im-<BR>proper motives or in an unbecoming manner; (अ-<BR>सत्कृत), not honoured; (अम्), n. wicked deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत्य
असत्-कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has done evil<BR>or wicked actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्त्व
2. अ-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, strengthless, without energy;<BR>(for 1. असत्-त्व, see under अ-सत् above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्य|असत्यः
अ-सत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, false, untrue; lying, a liar;<BR>(अम्), n. untruth, falsehood.<BR>—असत्य-वादिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, speaking falsely, giving false evidence, a liar.<BR>—असत्य-सन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, treacherous, base,<BR>wicked.<BR>—अ-सत्य-सन्निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, improba-<BR>ble, unlikely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृश|असदृशः
असदृश अ-सदृश, अस्, ई, अम्, unlike, dis-<BR>similar.<BR>—असदृश-व्यवहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, behaving<BR>improperly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्यस्
असद्यस् अ-सद्यस्, ind. not on the same<BR>day, not immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्
असन् असन्, the base of some of the cases<BR>of असृज्, blood, q. v.; thus, inst. अस्ना, gen. अस्नस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन|असनं|असनः
असन असन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 2. अस्), throwing,<BR>sending; a shot; (अस्), m., N. of the tree Termi-<BR>nalia Tomentosa, see अशन.<BR>—असन-पर्णी, f., N.<BR>of the plant Marsilea Quadrifolia, see अशन-पर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असना
असना, f., Ved. a missile, an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तति|असंतति|असन्ततिः
असन्तति अ-सन्तति, इस्, इस्, इ (rt. तन्), child-<BR>less, having no posterity; (इस्), f. want of posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तान|असंतान|असन्तानः
अ-सन्तान, अस्, आ, अम्, childless; (अस्), m. want<BR>of posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्ताप|असंताप
असन्ताप अ-सन्ताप, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. तप्), Ved.<BR>not suffering pain or sorrow; not causing pain or<BR>sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तुष्ट|असंतुष्ट|असन्तुष्टः
असन्तुष्ट अ-सन्तुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. तुष्),<BR>discontented, displeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तोष|असंतोष|असंतोषः
अ-सन्तोष, अस्, m. displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दिग्ध|असंदिग्ध
असन्दिग्ध अ-सन्दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दिह्),<BR>not indistinct; not vanished; certain, confident; un-<BR>doubted, unsuspected; (अम्), ind. without any doubt,<BR>certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दित|असंदित
असन्दित अ-सन्दित or अ-सन्दिन, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>(rt. 4. दा, to bind), Ved. unbound, unrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दिष्ट
असन्दिष्ट अ-सन्दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दिश्),<BR>unapprised, uncommunicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धान|असंधान
असन्धान अ-सन्धान, अम्, n. (rt. धा), want<BR>of aim or object, disjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धि|असंधि|असंधिः
अ-सन्धि, इस्, m. want of union or connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धित|असंधित
अ-सन्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, untied, unbound, at<BR>liberty, loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धेय|असंधेय
अ-सन्धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be made peace<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्न
असन्न अ-सन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. restless,<BR>without rest or repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्नद्ध|असंनद्ध|असन्नद्धः
असन्नद्ध अ-सन्नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. नह्),<BR>unarmed; born, produced; pretending to knowledge,<BR>conceited as a Paṇḍit or teacher; proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निकर्ष|असंनिकर्ष|असंनिकर्षः
असन्निकर्ष अ-सन्निकर्ष, अस्, m. (rt. कृष्),<BR>non-perception of objects, not bringing them to the<BR>mind, remoteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निकृष्ट|असंनिकृष्ट
अ-सन्निकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, unperceived, undis-<BR>tinguished; not near, remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निधि|असंनिधि|असंनिधिः
असन्निधि अ-सन्निधि, इस्, m. or अ-सन्नि-<BR>धान, अम्, n. (rt. धा), absence, distance; confi-<BR>dence, absence of doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निहित|असंनिहित
अ-सन्निहित, अस्, आ, अम्, not near, far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्न्यस्त|असंन्यस्त
असन्न्यस्त अ-सन्न्यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has not renounced the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्मान|असन्मानं
असन्मान अ-सन्मान, अम्, n. disrespect,<BR>impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपत्न
असपत्न अ-सपत्न, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. without<BR>another wife, without a rival; not attacked; without<BR>an adversary; not rivalling; (अम्), n. undisturbed<BR>condition, peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपिण्ड|असपिंड
असपिण्ड अ-सपिण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, unconnected<BR>by funeral offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असबन्धु
असबन्धु अ-सबन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not<BR>related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असभ्य|असभ्यः
असभ्य अ-सभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit for an<BR>assembly, vulgar, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम|असमः
असम अ-सम, अस्, आ, अम्, uneven, unequal<BR>either in surface or number; odd; unequalled, indi-<BR>vidual, without a fellow or equal; (अस्), m. a N. of<BR>Buddha or a Buddha.<BR>—असम-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. possessed of an unequalled chariot.<BR>—असम-<BR>वाण or असम-सायक, अस्, m. or असमेषु (˚म-<BR>इष्˚), उस्, m. having an odd number of arrows, i. e.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">Page0104-c+ 70</a>]<BR>the five-arrowed, an epithet of Kāma.<BR>—असमौजस्<BR>(˚म-ओज्˚), आस्, m., N. of a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमन
अ-समन, अस्, आ, अम्, going asunder or in<BR>different directions; uneven, unequal; (if, according<BR>to Sāy., derived fr. मनस्), of different minds, of<BR>different colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमान|असमानं
अ-समान, अस्, आ, अम्, not the same, not homo-<BR>geneous, not of equal birth; unlike, unequal, differ-<BR>ent.<BR>—असमान-कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, not having<BR>the same cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमक्ष
असमक्ष अ-समक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, not visible,<BR>not present, absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्र
असमग्र अ-समग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, incomplete,<BR>unentire, partial, part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्ज
असमञ्ज अ-समञ्ज, अस्, or अ-समञ्जस्, आस्,<BR>m., N. of a descendant of Ikṣvāku, a son of Sagara<BR>by Keśinī and father of Aṃśumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्जस|असमंजस|असमञ्जसं
अ-समञ्जस, अस्, आ, अम्, unequal, unlike; (अम्),<BR>n. unconformity, disparity, difference; (अम्), ind.<BR>unfitly, unbecomingly; in a fluctuating or confused<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमद्
असमद् अ-समद्, त्, f., Ved. non-conflict,<BR>harmony, concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमय|असमयः
असमय अ-समय, अस्, m. unseasonable-<BR>ness; unfit or unfavourable time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थ|असमर्थः
असमर्थ अ-समर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, unable, in-<BR>competent; feeble, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्पण
असमर्पण अ-समर्पण, अम्, n. non-de-<BR>livery, not committing or intrusting anything to<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्पित
अ-समर्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, unconsigned, unin-<BR>trusted, undelivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिन्
असमवायिन् अ-समवायिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt. इ with<BR>सम् and अव), accidental, not inherent, not intimate<BR>and inseparable.<BR>—असमवायि-कारण, अम्, n. (in<BR>logic) accidental cause, not intimate or inherent rela-<BR>tion (e. g. the separable conjunction of two different<BR>objects).<BR>—असमवायि-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of<BR>something that is not inherent and inseparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवेत
अ-समवेत, अस्, आ, अम्, not classed together, not<BR>connected, incoherent.<BR>—असमवेत-रूपम्, ind. in-<BR>coherently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमष्टकाव्य
असमष्टकाव्य अ-समष्ट-काव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. of unattainable wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमस्त
असमस्त अ-समस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, uncom-<BR>pounded, separate, several; uncollected; incomplete,<BR>imperfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाति
असमाति अ-समाति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having<BR>nothing equal, unparalleled; (इस्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—असमात्य्-ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. of unequalled<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमान|असमानं
असमान अ-समान. See अ-सम above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमापित
असमापित अ-समापित or अ-समाप्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unfinished, unaccomplished, incomplete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्ति
अ-समाप्ति, इस्, f. incompleteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावर्तक|असमावर्तकः|असमावर्त्तक
असमावर्तक अ-समावर्तक, अस्, or अ-समा-<BR>वृत्तिक, अस्, m. a religious student who has not com-<BR>pleted the period of his residence with his teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार|असमाहारः
असमाहार अ-समाहार, अस्, m. non-recovery<BR>of anything; disjunction, disconnection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार्य|असमाहार्य्य
अ-समाहार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, irrecoverable, not to<BR>be combined or united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्य
असमीक्ष्य अ-समीक्ष्य, ind. not having<BR>considered.<BR>—असमीक्ष्य-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting<BR>inconsiderately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीचीन
असमीचीन अ-समीचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, improper,<BR>incorrect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमृद्ध
असमृद्ध अ-समृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>increased, not prosperous; one whose wishes are<BR>frustrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमृद्धि|असमृद्धिः
अ-समृद्धि, इस्, f. non-increase; failing, perish-<BR>ing; (इस्, इस्, इ), unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पत्ति|असंपत्ति|असंपत्तिः
असम्पत्ति अ-सम्पत्ति, इस्, f. (rt. पद्), ill-<BR>luck, want of success; non-accomplishment, failure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पन्न|असंपन्न
अ-सम्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, uneffected, unaccom-<BR>plished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पर्क|असंपर्क
असम्पर्क अ-सम्पर्क, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. पृच्),<BR>destitute of contact, without connection or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पर्कीय
अ-सम्पर्कीय, अस्, आ, अम्, unconnected with,<BR>not belonging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पूर्ण|असंपूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण्ण
असम्पूर्ण अ-सम्पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, incom-<BR>plete, not entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्प्रति|असंप्रति
असम्प्रति अ-सम्प्रति, ind., Ved. not accord-<BR>ing to the moment or to present circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्प्राप्य|असंप्राप्य
असम्प्राप्य अ-सम्प्राप्य, ind. without reach-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बद्ध|असंबद्ध|असम्बद्धं
असम्बद्ध अ-सम्बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. बन्ध्),<BR>not closely associated, distant, not related; uncon-<BR>nected, incoherent, unmeaning; improper, wrong;<BR>speaking unconnectedly or unmeaningly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बन्ध|असंबंध|असंबन्ध|असंबन्धः
अ-सम्बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, unconnected, not re-<BR>lating or belonging to; (अस्), m. non-connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बाध|असंबाध
असम्बाध अ-सम्बाध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. बाध्),<BR>unconfined, spacious, wide, large; open, accessible;<BR>(आ), f. a species of the Śarkarī metre, consisting of<BR>fifty-six syllables; (अम्), n., Ved. non-confinement,<BR>open space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भव|असंभव|असंभवः
असम्भव अ-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. भू),<BR>inconsistent, improbable, unlikely; non-existent; (अम्,<BR>आ), n. f. any extraordinary event; non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भव्यम्|असंभव्यम्
अ-सम्भव्यम्, ind., Ved. in an incomprehensible<BR>or extraordinary manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भावना|असंभावना
अ-सम्भावना, f. difficulty or impossibility of<BR>conceiving or comprehending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भावनीय|असंभावनीय
अ-सम्भावनीय or अ-सम्भाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>inconceivable, incomprehensible, impossible.<BR>—असम्-<BR>भाव्यम्, ind. in an incomprehensible or impossible<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भूत|असंभूत
अ-सम्भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, unproduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भूति|असंभूति|असंभूतिः
अ-सम्भूति, इस्, f., Ved. non-existence, the not<BR>being born again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भोग|असंभोग
असम्भोग अ-सम्भोग, अस्, m. non-enjoy-<BR>ment, not using or enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

