असाहाय्य
असाहाय्य अ-साहाय्य, अम्, n. want of assist-<BR>tance or co-operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असि|असिः
असि असि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. अस्), a sword, a<BR>cimeter, a knife used for killing animals.<BR>—असि-गण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. a small pillow for the cheek.<BR>—असि-दंष्-<BR>ट्र or असि-दंष्ट्रक, अस्, m. the marine monster<BR>Makara, painted on the banner of Kāmadeva.<BR>—असि-दन्त, अस्, m. a crocodile.<BR>—असि-धारा, f.<BR>the edge of a sword.<BR>—असिधारा-व्रत, अम्, n. a<BR>vow of standing on the edge of a sword, used figura-<BR>tively for any hopelessly difficult task.<BR>—असि-धाव<BR>or असि-धावक, अस्, m. an armourer, a furbisher, a<BR>sword or tool cleaner.<BR>—असि-धेनु, उस्, or असि-धे-<BR>नुका, f. a knife.<BR>—असि-पत्त्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>blade of a sword; a sheath, a scabbard; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>whose leaves are swords, having sword-shaped leaves;<BR>(अस्), m. the sugar-cane, Scirpus Kysoor Roxb.; a<BR>kind of tree which grows in the lower world; a hell<BR>paved with swords.<BR>—असि-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. sugar-<BR>cane.<BR>—असिपत्त्र-वन, अम्, n. a hell where the<BR>trees have leaves as sharp as swords.<BR>—असि-पथ,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. the course of a sacrificial knife (?).<BR>—असि-पुच्छक, अस्, m. the Gaṅgetic porpoise, Del-<BR>phinus Gangeticus.<BR>—असि-पुत्रिका or असि-पुत्री, f. a<BR>knife, lit. daughter of a sword.<BR>—असि-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. furnished with knives or daggers.<BR>—असि-<BR>मेद, अस्, m. the fetid Mimosa Vachellia Farnesiana<BR>W. and A.<BR>—असि-लोमन्, आ, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—असि-हत्य, अम्, n. fighting with knives or swords.<BR>—असि-हेति, इस्, m. a swordsman or soldier armed<BR>with a sword.<BR>—अस्य्-असि, ind. sword to sword, sword<BR>against sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक|असिकं
असिक, अम्, n. (fr. असि ?), the part of the face be-<BR>tween the underlip and the chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्नी
असिक्नी असिक्नी. See 2. असित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
असित 1. अ-सित, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. सि), Ved.<BR>unbound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
असित 2. असित, अस्, f. असिता or Ved. f. असि-<BR>क्नी, अम्, (सित, ‘white,’ appears to have been formed<BR>from this word, which is probably original, and not a<BR>compound of अ and सित; cf. the formation of सुर<BR>fr. असुर), dark-coloured, black, dark-blue; (अस्), m.<BR>the black colour; N. of the planet Saturn; the dark<BR>fortnight of a lunar month; N. of a being presiding<BR>over darkness and magic; N. of a descendant of Kāś-<BR>yapa and several other persons; N. of a mountain;<BR>a black snake; (ता), f. the indigo plant; N. of an<BR>Apsaras; (असिक्नी), f., Ved. ‘the dark one,’ the night;<BR>a girl attending upon the inner or women's apart-<BR>ments (whose hair is not whitened by age); N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">Page0106-a+ 77</a>]<BR>daughter of Vīraṇa and wife of Dakṣa; N. of the<BR>river Akesines (afterwards Candra-bhāga) in the Pañ-<BR>jāb.<BR>—असित-केशान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having black locks.<BR>—असित-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a black<BR>neck.<BR>—असित-ज्ञु, उस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. having black<BR>knees.<BR>—असित-नयन, अस्, आ, अम्, black-eyed.<BR>—असित-भ्रू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, having black eyelids.<BR>—असित-मृग, अस्, m., N. of a family.<BR>—असिताभ्र-<BR>शेखर (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of Buddha.<BR>—असि-<BR>ताम्बुरुह (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, m. the blue lotus.<BR>—असितार्चिस् (˚त-अर्˚), इस्, m. fire.<BR>—असितालु (˚त-<BR>आल्˚), उस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—असिताश्मन् (˚त-अश्˚),<BR>आ, m. the lapis lazuli; any black or dark-blue stone.<BR>—असितोत्पल (˚त-उत्˚), अम्, n. the blue lotus, Nym-<BR>phæa Cærulea.<BR>—असितोपल (˚त-उप्˚), अम्, n. lapis<BR>lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्निका
असिक्निका, f. a woman-servant [cf. असिक्नी].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितकी
असितकी, f., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्ध|असिद्धं|असिद्धः
असिद्ध अ-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, imperfect, in-<BR>complete; unaccomplished, uneffected; unproved;<BR>unripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धि|असिद्धिः
अ-सिद्धि, इस्, f. imperfect or incomplete accom-<BR>plishment, failure; (in logic) want of proof, con-<BR>clusion not warranted by the premises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिन्व
असिन्व अ-सिन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-सिन्वत्, अन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. insatiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिर|असिरः
असिर असिर, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. अस्, to throw),<BR>Ved. a beam, a ray; an arrow, a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिष्ठ
असिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, (superl.) Ved. most skilful<BR>in shooting (arrows &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असी
असी असी, f., N. of a river, = असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असीमकृष्ण
असीमकृष्ण असीम-कृष्ण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असु|असुः
असु असु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. अस्, to be), breath,<BR>life, spiritual life; life of the spiritual world or departed<BR>spirits; water ?; [cf. ἀάζω, ἄσθμα]; (असवस्),<BR>nom. pl. the five vital breaths or airs of the body;<BR>animal life; (उ), n. reflection, thought or the heart as<BR>the seat of it; grief.<BR>—असु-धारण, अम्, n. life,<BR>existence.<BR>—असु-नीत, अम्, n., Ved. the world of<BR>spirits, or (अस्), m. the lord of the spirits.<BR>—असु-नीति,<BR>इस्, f., Ved. the life or the world of spirits; that life<BR>personified as a female deity invoked for the preserva-<BR>tion of life, or as Yama, lord of the dead.<BR>—असु-<BR>भङ्ग, अस्, m. breaking of life; fear about life;<BR>danger of life.<BR>—असु-भृत्, त्, m. breathing, living, a<BR>creature.<BR>—असु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, living, breathing;<BR>(मान्), m. life, the principle of vitality, the portion of<BR>spirit connected with the attributes of existence.<BR>—असु-<BR>सम, अस्, आ, अम्, dearly loved, as dear as life; (अस्),<BR>m. a husband, a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. living, alive, spiritual; an<BR>epithet of the supreme spirit; Varuṇa; incorporeal, super-<BR>human, divine; (अस्), m. spirit; an incorporeal being<BR>of an evil kind; an evil spirit, a demon; a ghost or<BR>spectre; a general name for the chief of the Asuras<BR>[these Asuras are often regarded as the children of<BR>Diti by Kaśyapa, see दैत्य; as such they are<BR>demons of the first order in perpetual hostility with<BR>the gods, and must not be confounded with the<BR>Rākṣasas or imps who animate dead bodies and<BR>disturb sacrifices]; the sun; Rāhu; an elephant; N.<BR>of a warrior-tribe; (according to Sāy.) a cloud ?;<BR>(आ), f. night; a zodiacal sign; a prostitute; (ई), f. a<BR>female demon, the wife of an Asura; N. of the plant<BR>Sinapis Racemosa Roxb. [Observe, in later San-<BR>skṛt, सुर has been formed from असुर, as सित<BR>from असित, q. v.]<BR>—असुर-कुमार, आस्, m. pl. a<BR>class of deities belonging to the Bhavanādhīśas.<BR>—असुर-क्षयण, अस्, आ, अम्, or असुर-क्षिति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. destroying the Asuras.<BR>—असुर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. spirituality, supernatural or divine dig-<BR>nity.<BR>—असुर-माया, f., Ved. demoniacal magic.<BR>—असुर-रक्षस, आनि, n. pl., Ved. the Asuras<BR>and Rākṣasas; (अम्), n. sing. a demoniacal being,<BR>partaking of the qualities of both the classes of<BR>evil spirits.<BR>—असुर-राज्, ट्, m. king of the Asuras,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">Page0106-b+ 69</a>]<BR>epithet of the Asura Baka.<BR>—असुर-रिपु, उस्, m.<BR>enemy of the Asuras, epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—असुर-<BR>सूदन, अस्, m. destroyer of the Asuras, epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—असुर-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, Ved. destroying<BR>the Asuras, epithet of Agni, Indra, &c.<BR>—असुरा-<BR>चार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m. teacher of the Asuras;<BR>epithet of the regent of the planet Venus.<BR>—असुरा-<BR>धिप (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m. lord of the Asuras; N. of<BR>Bali Vairocani and of Māyādhara.<BR>—असुराह्व (˚र-<BR>आह्˚), अम्, n. bell-metal, named after an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्य|असुर्यः|असुर्य्य
असुर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. incorporeal, spiritual,<BR>divine; demoniacal, belonging to the Asuras; (अम्),<BR>n. spirituality, divine nature; the incorporeal, the<BR>collective body of spiritual beings; (according to<BR>Sāy.) the water of the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुकर
असुकर अ-सुकर, अस्, आ, अम्, not easy to<BR>be done, difficult, arduous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुक्षण|असुक्षणं
असुक्षण असुक्षण, a various reading for<BR>असूक्षण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुख|असुखं
असुख अ-सुख, अस्, आ, अम्, unhappy, sorrow-<BR>ful, melancholic; (अम्), n. sorrow, pain, affliction.<BR>—असुख-जीविका, f. a joyless life.<BR>—असुख-पीडित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, pained with grief.<BR>—असुखावह (˚ख-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, producing unhappiness.<BR>—असुखा-<BR>विष्ट (˚ख-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted with grief,<BR>pain, or unhappiness.<BR>—असुखोदय (˚ख-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, causing or ending in unhappiness.<BR>—असुखो-<BR>दर्क (˚ख-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, productive of or<BR>ending in unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखिन्
अ-सुखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, unhappy, sorrowful, afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुगम
असुगम अ-सुगम, अस्, आ, अम्, difficult of<BR>attainment or accomplishment, hard, unattainable;<BR>difficult to be understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
असुत 1. अ-सुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 2. सु), Ved. not<BR>pressed out, not cleared or purified, not ready (as<BR>the Soma juice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्व
अ-सुन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-सुन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्,<BR>or अ-सुष्वि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. not pressing out the<BR>Soma juice, not worshipping the gods, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
असुत 2. अ-सुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 1. सु), child-<BR>less. See अ-सू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतर
असुतर अ-सुतर, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. तृ), not to<BR>be easily passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतृप्
असुतृप् अ-सुतृप्, प्, प्, प्, Ved. insatiable,<BR>not easily satiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुनिरस
असुनिरस अ-सुनिरस, अस्, आ, अम्, disagree-<BR>able, unpleasant, offensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्दर
असुन्दर अ-सुन्दर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, plain,<BR>ugly; improper, unbecoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुप्त
असुप्त अ-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not asleep.<BR>—अ-<BR>सुप्त-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, never closing the eyes in sleep,<BR>ever-seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुम्न
असुम्न अ-सुम्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. contrary,<BR>adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर असुर. See under असु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष
असुरक्ष अ-सुरक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, perishable,<BR>volatile, transitory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष्य
अ-सुरक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, difficult of retention or<BR>preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरसा
असुरसा अ-सुरसा, f. the plant Basilicum<BR>Pilosum Benth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुलभ
असुलभ अ-सुलभ, अस्, आ, अम्, difficult of<BR>attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुष्वि
असुष्वि अ-सुष्वि. See under. 1. अ-सुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुस्थ|असुस्थः
असुस्थ अ-सुस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, unwell, indis-<BR>posed, not well placed, uncomfortable.<BR>—असुस्थ-ता,<BR>f. indisposition, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुहृद्
असुहृद् अ-सुहृद्, त्, m. not a friend, an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असू
असू अ-सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, m. f. (rt. 1. सु, to bring<BR>forth), Ved. not bringing forth, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूत
अ-सूत or अ-सूतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who<BR>has not brought forth, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूति|असूतिः
अ-सूति, इस्, f. non-production; obstruction, removal;<BR>barrenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूसु
अ-सूसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not bringing forth, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्षण|असूक्षणं
असूक्षण असूक्षण or असुक्षण or असुर्-<BR>क्षण or असूर्क्षण or अस्तर्क्षण, अम्, n.<BR>(etymology doubtful), disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्ष्म
असूक्ष्म अ-सूक्ष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, not fine, not<BR>minute, large, thick, gross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूय
असूय असूय (fr. असु), nom. P. A. असूयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to murmur at, to detract from, depre-<BR>ciate; to envy, scorn, be displeased or discontented<BR>with, or grumble at (with dat. or acc.): Caus. असू-<BR>ययति, -यितुम्, to cause to murmur or be displeased<BR>or discontented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयक|असूयकः
असूयक, अस्, इका, अम्, detracting, envious, calum-<BR>nious, discontented, displeased; (by some written<BR>असूक ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयन|असूयनं
असूयन, अम्, n. calumny, detraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूययित्वा
असूययित्वा, ind. having scorned, having cursed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूया
असूया, f. displeasure, indignation, especially at the<BR>merits or the happiness of another, envy, jealousy;<BR>calumny, detraction; aversion; N. of the wife of Atri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयितृ
असूयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, murmuring, detracting, dis-<BR>pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयु|असूयुः
असूयु, उस्, उस्, उ, envious, displeased; (उस्), m.<BR>calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर
असूर अ-सूर, अम्, n., Ved. absence of a<BR>person to press out the Soma juice; (Sāy.) a place<BR>or country devoid of praise or worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्क्षण
असूर्क्षण असूर्क्षण, अम्, n. disrespect.<BR>See असूक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्त|असूर्त्त
असूर्त अ-सूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not moving,<BR>remote (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्य
असूर्य अ-सूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sunless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्यम्पश्या|असूर्यंपश्या|असूर्य्यम्पश्या
अ-सूर्यम्-पश्या, f. the wife of a king who being<BR>shut up in the inner apartments never sees the sun,<BR>a chaste and loyal wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
असृज् असृज्, क्, n. (said to be fr. rt. सृज् with<BR>अ, which may stand for अव or आ), blood; saffron;<BR>(क्), m. a kind of religious abstraction; [cf. Lat.<BR>sanguis.]<BR>—असृक्-कर, अस्, m. the essence of the<BR>body, lymph, serum, &c.<BR>—असृक्-प, अस्, m. a Rāk-<BR>ṣasa or imp of malicious propensities, who drinks blood.<BR>—असृक्-पात, अस्, m. the falling of blood; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. drops of blood, as from a wound.<BR>—असृक्-पावन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. drinking blood.<BR>—असृक्-श्राव, अस्, m.<BR>bleeding, letting blood.<BR>—असृक्-श्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>bleeding, who or what takes away blood.<BR>—असृग्-<BR>दर, अस्, m. irregular or excessive menstruation,<BR>mœnorrhagia.<BR>—असृग्-दोह, अस्, आ, अम्, shedding<BR>blood, bleeding.<BR>—असृग्-धरा, f. the skin.<BR>—अस्-<BR>ऋग्-धारा, f. a stream of blood; the skin.<BR>—असृग्-<BR>वहा, f. a blood-vessel.<BR>—असृग्-विमोक्षण, अम्, n.<BR>blood-letting, bleeding.<BR>—असृङ्-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>mixed or covered with blood.<BR>—असृङ्-मुख, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, Ved. whose face is bloody.<BR>—असृ-पाट, अस्, ई,<BR>m. f. (for असृक्-पात), a stream of blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृणि
असृणि अ-सृणि, इस्, इस्, इ, unrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृष्ट
असृष्ट अ-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. सृज्), un-<BR>created; undistributed, not presented; continued.<BR>—असृष्टान्न (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who does<BR>not distribute food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचन
असेचन अ-सेचन or अ-सेचनक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>that on which one cannot look enough; charming,<BR>lovely [cf. आ-सेचनक].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेन्य
असेन्य अ-सेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not worthy<BR>of an army; not striking, not wounding (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवन
असेवन अ-सेवन, अम्, n. or अ-सेवा, f. (rt.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">Page0107-a+ 75</a>]<BR>सेव्), disregarding, neglecting; not following or prac-<BR>tising, shunning; disregard, inattention, disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवित
अ-सेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, neglected, unattended to, dis-<BR>obeyed; abstained from, disused.<BR>—अ-सेवितेश्वर-<BR>द्वार (˚त-ईश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not waiting at the<BR>doors of the great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेव्य
अ-सेव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be served or attended<BR>to; not to be used or practised, not to be eaten,<BR>drank, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौकृ
असौकृ असौ-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to do such and such a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौनामन्
असौ-नामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having such and such a<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौन्दर्य|असौन्दर्य्य
असौन्दर्य अ-सौन्दर्य, अम्, n. ugliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्य
असौम्य अ-सौम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ugly, un-<BR>lovely; disagreeable, displeasing.<BR>—असौम्य-स्वर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a bad or croaking voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्ठव|असौष्ठवं
असौष्ठव अ-सौष्ठव, अम्, n. ugliness, de-<BR>formity; demerit, worthlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्न
अस्कन्न अ-स्कन्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्कन्द्), Ved.<BR>not spilt, not effused, not fallen; not sprinkled, not<BR>covered; permanent, durable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्दित|अस्कंदित
अ-स्कन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, not spilt, not fallen, not<BR>gone, not attacked.<BR>—अस्कन्दित-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>true to vows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कम्भन
अस्कम्भन अ-स्कम्भन, अम्, n., Ved. want<BR>of a pillar or support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कृधोयु
अस्कृधोयु अ-स्कृधोयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not<BR>narrow or deficient, abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्खलित
अस्खलित अ-स्खलित, अस्, आ, अम्, unshaken,<BR>unyielding, firm, permanent; not stumbling or slip-<BR>ping, undeviating.<BR>—अ-स्खलित-प्रयाण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not stumbling in progress, with unfaltering step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त 1. अस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. अस्), thrown,<BR>cast; expelled, sent away; sent, despatched; removed,<BR>laid or set aside; finished; (आ), f., Ved. a missile,<BR>an arrow.<BR>—अस्त-कोप, अस्, आ, अम्, whose anger is<BR>laid aside.<BR>—अस्त-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, foolish.<BR>—अस्त-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, obstructed (?).<BR>—अस्त-व्यस्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, scattered hither and thither, confused, disordered,<BR>irrelevant.<BR>—अस्त-सङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृ
अस्तृ, ता, m., Ved. throwing, a shooter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त 2. अस्त, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. अस् ?), Ved.<BR>home; death, end; (अस्), m. the western mountain,<BR>behind which the sun is supposed to set; sunset;<BR>(in astronomy) the seventh lunar mansion.<BR>—अस्तम्,<BR>ind. at home, home.<BR>—अस्तम् इ or गम् or या, to<BR>go home; to go down, to set; अस्तं नी or वह्,<BR>to conduct or lead home; to lead to setting, to cause<BR>to set; अस्तं गम् or इ or प्राप्, to go to one's eter-<BR>nal home, to cease, to vanish, to die.<BR>—अस्त-गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, set (as the sun).<BR>—अस्त-गमन, अम्,<BR>n. setting.<BR>—अस्त-गिरि, इस्, m. the western mountain.<BR>—अस्तम्-अय, अस्, m. or अस्तम्-अयन, अम्, n.<BR>disappearance, setting.<BR>—अस्तम्-इत, अस्, आ, अम्, set<BR>(as the sun).<BR>—अस्ताचल (˚त-अच्˚), अस्, m. the west-<BR>ern mountain.<BR>—अस्ताचलावलम्बिन् (˚ल-अव्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, reclining on the western mountain, about to<BR>set.<BR>—अस्ताद्रि (˚त-अद्˚), इस्, m. the western moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—अस्तावलम्बन (˚त-अव्˚), अम्, n. the resting<BR>of a heavenly body on the western part of the<BR>horizon.<BR>—अस्तावलम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, setting as the<BR>sun, on the point of setting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तक|अस्तकः
अस्तक, अम्, n., Ved. home; (अस्), m. going to<BR>one's eternal home, beatitude, eternal felicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तताति|अस्ततातिः
अस्तताति, इस्, f., Ved. home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमती
अस्तमती, f. (perhaps a corruption of अंशु-मती),<BR>the plant Desmodium Gangeticum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमन|अस्तमनं
अस्तमन, अम्, n. corruption of (अस्तम्-अयन),<BR>setting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमीके
अस्तमीके, ind., Ved. at home, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ता
अस्ता, ind., Ved. at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अस्तब्ध अ-स्तब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, not firm or<BR>self-possessed, confounded.<BR>—अस्तब्ध-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>being confused or confounded, want of self-possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तर्क्षण|अस्तर्क्षणं
अस्तर्क्षण अस्तर्क्षण, अम्, n. disrespect.<BR>See असूक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताग
अस्ताग अस्ताग, अस्, m., N. of the fifteenth<BR>Arhat of the past Utsarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताघ|अस्ताघः
अस्ताघ अस्ताघ, अस्, आ, अम्, very deep. See<BR>अस्थाघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ति|अस्तिः
अस्ति अस्ति, ind. (3rd sing. pres. of rt. I. अस्),<BR>being, existent, present; (इस्), f., N. of a sister of<BR>Prāpti, daughter of Jarāsandhas and wife of Kaṃsa.<BR>—अस्ति-काय, अस्, m. a category or predicament.<BR>—अस्ति-क्षीर, अस्, आ, अम्, having milk.<BR>—अस्ति-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. existence.<BR>—अस्ति-नास्ति (˚न-अस्˚), ind. doubt-<BR>ful, partly true and partly not.<BR>—अस्तिनास्ति-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. or अस्तिनास्ति-ता, f. uncertain or doubtful existence;<BR>partial existence.<BR>—अस्ति-प्रवाद, अम्, n. title of the<BR>fourth of the fourteen Pūrvas or older writings of the<BR>Jainas.<BR>—अस्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of property,<BR>wealthy, opulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्तु (3rd sing. impv. of rt. 1. अस्), let it be, be<BR>it so, implying assent, also reluctance and pain.<BR>—अस्तुङ्-कार, अस्, आ, अम्, efficacious, as a medica-<BR>ment; (अस्तुम् is here the acc. of अस्तु, ‘producing<BR>that which the physician promises shall be.’)<BR>—अस्त्व्-<BR>एवम्, ind. be it so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तुत
अस्तुत अ-स्तुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्तु), Ved. not<BR>praised, not deserving praise; not recited in prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तुति
अ-स्तुति, इस्, m. the absence of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृत
अस्तृत अ-स्तृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not over-<BR>come, invincible, indestructible.<BR>—अस्तृत-यज्वन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, Ved. sacrificing indefatigably or invincibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेन
अस्तेन अ-स्तेन, अम्, or अ-स्तेय, अम्, n. ab-<BR>sence of theft, honesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्य
अस्त्य अस्त्य, अम्, n., Ved. a house. See 2. अस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्यान|अस्त्यानं
अस्त्यान अ-स्त्यान, अम्, n. reproach, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्र|अस्त्रं
अस्त्र अस्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 2. अस्), a missile<BR>weapon, bolt, arrow; bow; a weapon in general, a<BR>sword; [with अस्त्र cf. Gr. ἄστρον and ἀστήρ per-<BR>haps that which throws out or emits rays of light.]<BR>—अस्त्र-कण्टक, अस्, m. an arrow.<BR>—अस्त्र-कारक<BR>or अस्त्र-कार, अस्, or अस्त्र-कारिन्, ई, m. an armourer,<BR>maker of weapons.<BR>—अस्त्र-क्षेपक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>shooting arrows.<BR>—अस्त्र-चिकित्सक, अस्, m. a surgeon.<BR>—अस्त्र-चिकित्सा, f. surgery.<BR>—अस्त्र-जित्, त्, n., N.<BR>of a plant.<BR>—अस्त्र-जीव, अस्, m. a soldier, a warrior.<BR>—अस्त्र-धारण, अम्, n. the bearing of arms.<BR>—अस्त्र-धारिन्, ई, m. one who bears arms, a<BR>soldier.<BR>—अस्त्र-निवारण, अम्, n. warding off a<BR>blow.<BR>—अस्त्र-मार्ज or अस्त्रमार्जक, अस्, m. an<BR>armourer, a sword-polisher or tool-cleaner, furbisher.<BR>—अस्त्र-युद्ध, अस्, m. fighting with weapons.<BR>—अस्त्र-लाघव, अम्, n. dexterity in arms.<BR>—अस्त्र-<BR>विद्, त्, त्, त्, skilled in the science of arms or war.<BR>—अस्त्र-विद्या, f. the military science.<BR>—अस्त्र-<BR>विद्वस्, आन्, उषी, अस्, skilled in the use of arms.<BR>—अस्त्र-वृष्टि, इस्, f. shower of arrows.<BR>—अस्त्र-<BR>वेद, अस्, m. the science of arms and war.<BR>—अस्त्र-<BR>शस्त्र, अम्, n. all sorts of arms (as arrows and<BR>swords).<BR>—अस्त्र-शिक्षा, f. military exercise, passage<BR>of arms.<BR>—अस्त्र-सायक, अस्, m. an iron arrow.<BR>—अस्त्र-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, unarmed, defenceless.<BR>—अस्त्रागार (˚त्र-आग्˚), अस्, m. an arsenal, an<BR>armoury.<BR>—अस्त्राघात (˚त्र-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a wound,<BR>a cut.<BR>—अस्त्राहत (˚त्र-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, struck,<BR>wounded, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रिन्
अस्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, fighting with a missile weapon,<BR>an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्री
अस्त्री अ-स्त्री, f. not a woman; (in gram.)<BR>the masculine and neuter genders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रीक
अ-स्त्रीक, अस्, आ, अम्, having no wife, without a<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रैण
अ-स्त्रैण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. without a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थन्
अस्थन् अस्थन्, the base of some of the<BR>cases of अस्थि, ‘a bone,’ q. v.; thus, inst. अस्थ्ना, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थ
अस्थ = अस्थि at the end of some compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थला
अस्थला अ-स्थला, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्था
अस्था अस्था, f. (?), Ved. a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाग|अस्थागं
अस्थाग अस्थाग, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्था with अ?),<BR>very deep; also written अस्ताग, अस्थाघ, अस्थान,<BR>अस्थार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थान|अस्थानं
अस्थान अ-स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. स्था), very<BR>deep; (अम्), n. no place, a place where there is no<BR>firm footing, a bad or wrong place; (अम्), ind. un-<BR>suitably, unseasonably; अ-स्थाने, ind. unseasonably,<BR>inopportunely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायिन्
अ-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not permanent^1, perishable,<BR>transient.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थावर|अस्थावरं
अ-स्थावर, अस्, आ, अम्, moveable, moving, not<BR>fixed; (in law) personal, as property, money, cattle,<BR>&c., opposed to land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थित
अ-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, not standing still, not fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिति|अस्थितिः
अ-स्थिति, इस्, f. want of place or condition, want of<BR>firm continuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थि
अस्थि अस्थि, इ, Ved. अस्थन्, अ, n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. 2. अस्; perhaps fr. अ-स्था for आ-स्था), a bone;<BR>the kernel or stone of a fruit. At end of compounds<BR>अस्थ is found, e. g. अन्-अस्थ, q. v. The weakest<BR>cases of अस्थि are derived from अस्थन्, q. v.; the<BR>Veda has also अस्थानि, अस्थभिस्, &c. [cf. Lat. os,<BR>ossis, assimilated fr. ostis; Gr. ὀστέον Slav. kosti,<BR>with k prefixed].<BR>—अस्थन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>having bones, bony.<BR>—अस्थि-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, m. f. n. mar-<BR>row.<BR>—अस्थि-च्छल्लित, अम्, n. a particular fracture<BR>of the bones.<BR>—अस्थि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. produced in<BR>the bones; (अस्), m. marrow; the thunderbolt; in<BR>the last sense a various reading for अक्ष-ज.<BR>—अस्थि-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, m. marrow.<BR>—अस्थि-तुण्ड, अस्, आ, m. f. a<BR>bird (whose mouth or beak consists of bone).<BR>—अस्-<BR>थि-तेजस्, अस्, n. marrow.<BR>—अस्थि-तोद, अस्, m. pain<BR>in the bones.<BR>—अस्थि-त्वच्, क्, f. the periosteum.<BR>—अस्थि-धन्वन्, आ, m. a N. of Śiva.<BR>—अस्थि-<BR>पञ्जर, अस्, m. a skeleton; lit. a cage of bones.<BR>—अस्थि-भक्ष, अस्, m. a dog (eating bones).<BR>—अस्थि-भङ्ग, अस्, m. fracture of the bones; N.<BR>of the plant Vitis Quadrangularis.<BR>—अस्थि-भुज्, क्,<BR>m. a bone-eater, a dog.<BR>—अस्थि-भूयस्, आन्, असी,<BR>अस्, Ved. consisting chiefly of bones, dried up.<BR>—अस्-<BR>थि-भेद, अस्, m. fracturing, breaking or wounding<BR>a bone; a sort of bone, a bone.<BR>—अस्थि-भेदक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, a bone-breaker, who or what breaks<BR>bones.<BR>—अस्थि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having bones, verte-<BR>brated.<BR>—अस्थि-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, bony, consisting of<BR>bones.<BR>—अस्थि-माला, f. a necklace of bones.<BR>—अस्थि-<BR>मालिन्, ई, m. an epithet of Śiva (this deity being<BR>commonly represented with a necklace of skulls).<BR>—अस्थि-योग, अस्, m. the joining of a broken bone.<BR>—अस्थि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, bony, osseous.<BR>—अस्थि-<BR>विग्रह, अस्, m. a N. of Bhṛṅgin, one of Śiva's at-<BR>tendants.<BR>—अस्थि-शृङ्खला, f. or अस्थि-संहार,<BR>अस्, ई, m. f., N. of the plant Heliotropium Indicum.<BR>—अस्थि-शोष, अस्, m. dryness and decay of the<BR>bones.<BR>—अस्थि-संहारक, अस्, m. ‘bone-seizer,’<BR>the adjutant bird.<BR>—अस्थि-सञ्चय, अस्, m. collecting<BR>the bones or their ashes after burning a corpse.<BR>—अस्थि-सन्धि, इस्, m. a joint, an articulation;<BR>uniting of a broken bone.<BR>—अस्थि-समर्पण, अम्,<BR>n. throwing the bones of a dead body into the Gan-<BR>ges.<BR>—अस्थि-सार, अस्, m. marrow.<BR>—अस्थि-स्थूण,<BR>अस्, m. the body, ‘having the bones for its pillars.’<BR>—अस्थि-स्नेह, अस्, m. marrow.<BR>—अस्थि-स्रंस, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, Ved. causing the bones to fall asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिक
अस्थिक, अम्, n. a bone; used at the end of com-<BR>pounds, e. g. अन्-अस्थिक, अस्, आ, अम्, boneless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिर|अस्थिरः
अस्थिर अ-स्थिर, अस्, आ, अम्, unsteady;<BR>trembling, shaking; uncertain, unascertained; un-<BR>worthy of confidence.<BR>—अस्थिर-ता, f. or अस्थिर-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. unsteadiness, fickleness, mutability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थेयस्
अ-स्थेयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, unsteady, not firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्य|अस्थैर्य्य|अस्थैर्य्यं
अ-स्थैर्य, अम्, n. instability, unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थूरि|अस्थूरिः
अस्थूरि अ-स्थूरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. furnished<BR>with more than one horse; not one-sided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थूल
अस्थूल अ-स्थूल, अस्, आ, अम्, not bulky, de-<BR>licate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नातृ
अस्नातृ अ-स्नातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. not fond<BR>of bathing, not a bather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नाविर
अस्नाविर अ-स्नाविर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. with-<BR>out sinews, without bands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्निग्ध
अस्निग्ध अ-स्निग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्निह्), not<BR>smooth, harsh, hard, dry; unkind.<BR>—अस्निग्ध-दारु,<BR>उ, n. a kind of pine tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेह|अस्नेहः
अ-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, unkind; harsh, hard, dry;<BR>(अस्), m. unkindness, want of affection; absence of<BR>oiliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पन्द|अस्पंद
अस्पन्द अ-स्पन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, not trembling,<BR>not moving, fixed, unchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्श|अस्पर्शः
अस्पर्श अ-स्पर्श, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्पृश्), not<BR>touching, not in contact; (अस्), m. not touching, non-<BR>contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शन|अस्पर्शनं
अ-स्पर्शन, अम्, n. non-contact, avoiding the con-<BR>tact of anything, especially of one who is impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शनीय
अ-स्पर्शनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be touched,<BR>impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शित
अ-स्पर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, untouched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृश्य
अ-स्पृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be touched, intan-<BR>gible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्ट
अ-स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, untouched.<BR>—अस्पृष्ट-<BR>रजस्-तमस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, perfectly pure.<BR>—अस्पृ-<BR>ष्ट-वह्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, unscathed by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टि|अस्पृष्टिः
अ-स्पृष्टि, इस्, f. not touching, avoiding contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पष्ट|अस्पष्टं
अस्पष्ट अ-स्पष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, indistinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृत
अस्पृत अ-स्पृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. uncon-<BR>quered, irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृह
अस्पृह अ-स्पृह, अस्, आ, अम्, undesirous,<BR>content; indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृहणीय
अ-स्पृहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, undesirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुट|अस्फुटं
अस्फुट अ-स्फुट, अम्, n. indistinct speech;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), indistinct, obscure, invisible, unblown.<BR>—अस्फुट-फल, अम्, n. indistinct result; (in<BR>geom.) gross area of a triangle, &c.<BR>—अ-स्फुट-<BR>वाच्, क्, क्, क्, lisping, speaking indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्म
अस्म अ-स्म, a pronominal base (supposed<BR>to be compounded fr. अ and स्म) from which several<BR>cases of the pronoun of the 1st person plur. and of<BR>the 3rd sing. are derived. See also the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्
अस्मद् अस्मद्, the plural base of the 1st<BR>personal pronoun (said to be fr. 2. अस्, ‘to throw’,<BR>Uṇ-sūt. I. 138; or fr. 1. अस्, ‘to be’), nom. sing.<BR>अहम्, ‘I,’ du. आवाम्, ‘we two,’ pl. वयम्, ‘we;’<BR>acc. pl. अस्मान्, inst. अस्माभिस्, dat. अस्मभ्यम्,<BR>abl. अस्मत् or अस्मत्तस्, gen. अस्माकम्, loc. अस्-<BR>मासु. Native grammarians derive the sing. as well<BR>as plur. from the base, अस्मद्. The form अस्मे,<BR>common to all oblique cases of the plur., is confined<BR>to the Vedas; and sometimes a form अस्माक is<BR>used for the gen. अस्माकम्. The form नस् for<BR>acc., dat., and gen. is enclitic. The form अस्म<BR>is met with in the Vedas as well as the अस्मद् of<BR>the classical language, especially at the beginning of<BR>compounds [cf. Gr. ἄμμες fr. ἄσμες Goth. unsa<BR>for usna; Mod. Germ. unser].<BR>—अस्म-त्रा, ind.,<BR>Ved. to us, with us, among us.<BR>—अस्मत्राञ्च्, आङ्,<BR>आची, आक्, Ved. turned towards us.<BR>—अस्मद्-रात, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. given by us.<BR>—अस्म-द्रुह्, -ध्रुक्,<BR>क्, क्, Ved. forming a plot against us or me, inimical.<BR>—अस्मद्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, or अस्मादृश, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, or अस्मादृश्, क्, क्, क्, similar, or like us or<BR>me; one of us.<BR>—अस्मे-हिति, इस्, f., Ved. errand or<BR>message for us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मदीय
अस्मदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, our, ours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्र्यञ्च्|अस्मद्र्यंच्
अस्मद्र्यञ्च्, आङ्, द्रीची, अक्, Ved. turned towards<BR>us; (क्), ind. towards us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मयु
अस्मयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. endeavouring to attain<BR>us, desiring us, favourable to us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्माक
अस्माक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. our, ours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मन्त|अस्मंतं|अस्मन्तं
अस्मन्त अस्मन्त, अम्, n. a furnace or fire-<BR>place. See अश्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरण|अस्मरणं
अस्मरण अ-स्मरण, अम्, n. (rt. स्मृ), for-<BR>getfulness, forgetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरणीय
अ-स्मरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be recollected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मार्त|अस्मार्त्त
अ-स्मार्त, अस्, ई, अम्, immemorial, not within<BR>memory; illegal, not according to law; not belonging<BR>to the Hindū institutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृत
अ-स्मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, not remembered, forgotten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृति|अस्मृतिः
अ-स्मृति, इस्, f. want of memory, forgetfulness;<BR>the not being part of the institutes of law; (इ), ind.,<BR>Ved. inattentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मिता
अस्मिता अस्मि-ता, f. (abstract noun formed<BR>fr. अस्मि, 1st pers. sing. pres. of 1. अस्, ‘I am’),<BR>egotism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मेर
अस्मेर अ-स्मेर, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्मि), Ved. not<BR>sullen, confiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यन्दमान
अस्यन्दमान अ-स्यन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>not gliding away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यवामीय|अस्यवामीयं
अस्यवामीय अस्यवामीय, अम्, n. the hymn<BR>beginning with the words अस्य वाम् (Ṛg-veda 1. 164).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यहत्य
अस्यहत्य अस्य-हत्य, अस्यहेति अस्य-हेति.<BR>See Gaṇa Anuśatikādi to Pāṇini VII. 3, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्युद्यत
अस्युद्यत अस्य्-उद्यत, अस्, आ, अम् (for उद्य-<BR>तासि), having the sword raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्र|अस्रं|अस्रः
अस्र अस्र, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 2. अस्), hair<BR>of the head; a corner, an angle, see अश्र; (अम्),<BR>n. blood; a tear, see असृज् and असन्.<BR>—अस्र-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, m. an arrow; (perhaps a variation from<BR>अस्त्र-कण्ठ ?).<BR>—अस्र-खदिर, अस्, m. a red Mi-<BR>mosa.<BR>—अस्र-ज, अम्, n. flesh.<BR>—अस्र-जित्, त्, m. a<BR>plant; see अस्त्र-जित्.<BR>—अस्र-प, अस्, m. a Rākṣasa<BR>or goblin; (आ), f. a leech; a Dākinī or female imp.<BR>—अस्र-पत्त्रक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, Rubia<BR>Cordifolia L. (?).<BR>—अस्र-पित्त, अम्, n. plethora,<BR>hemorrhage, epistaxis, involuntary discharge of blood<BR>from the mouth, nostrils, anus, &c.<BR>—अस्र-फला, f.<BR>the plant Boswellia Thurifera Roxb.<BR>—अस्र-मातृका,<BR>f. chyle, chyme.<BR>—अस्र-रोधिनी, f. the plant Mi-<BR>mosa Pudica.<BR>—अस्र-विन्दु-च्छदा, f., N. of a tu-<BR>berous plant.<BR>—अस्रार्जक (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>white Tulasī plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्राय
अस्राय, nom. A. अस्रायते, -यितुम्, to shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रवत्|अस्रवन्त्
अस्रवत् अ-स्रवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (rt. स्रु), not<BR>flowing; Ved. not leaky (as a ship).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रुव
अ-स्रुव, अम्, n. granulation (of a running sore).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्राम
अस्राम अ-स्राम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not stiff,<BR>not lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रि|अस्रिः
अस्रि अस्रि, इस्, f. an angle; ten millions.<BR>See अश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रिध्
अस्रिध् अ-स्रिध्, त्, त्, त्, or अ-स्रिधान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or अ-स्रेधत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. not doing<BR>harm; uninjured, unfatigued; pious, peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रीवयस्
अस्रीवयस् अस्री-वयस्, Ved. having food<BR>which falls or drops down (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रु
अस्रु अस्रु, n. a tear, &c. See अश्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रेमन्
अस्रेमन् अस्रेमन्, आ, m., Ved. praiseworthy,<BR>to be praised; (if fr. rt. स्रिव्) undecaying, immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्व|अस्वः
अस्व अ-स्व, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-स्वक, अस्, अका<BR>or इका, अम्, or अ-स्वकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not one's<BR>own, belonging to another.<BR>—अ-स्व-ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. not going to one's own home, homeless.<BR>—अ-<BR>स्वग-ता, f., Ved. homelessness.<BR>—अ-स्व-जाति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, of a different caste, of a different species.<BR>—अस्व-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. or अस्व-ता, f. want of claim or right to<BR>anything, having no indefeasible property in it, ab-<BR>sence of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छन्द|अस्वच्छंद|अस्वच्छन्दः
अ-स्वच्छन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, docile; not self-willed,<BR>dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वतन्त्र|अस्वतंत्र|अस्वतन्त्रः
अ-स्वतन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, not self-willed, dependant,<BR>subject; docile, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वभाव|अस्वभावः
अ-स्वभाव, अस्, m. unnatural or unusual character<BR>or temperament; (अस्, आ, अम्), of a different nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरूप
अ-स्वरूप, अस्, आ, अम्, essentially different or<BR>unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ववेश
अ-स्ववेश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having no home of<BR>one's own, expelled from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाध्याय|अस्वाध्यायः
अ-स्वाध्याय (˚स्व-अध्˚), अस्, m. a Brāhman<BR>who has not performed his studies, who has not read<BR>the Vedas previously to his investiture; interruption<BR>or interval of study, prohibited on certain days of the<BR>moon, at eclipses, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वार्थ
अ-स्वार्थ (˚स्व-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not for one's<BR>self; not for a proper object; having a different<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वीकार
अ-स्वीकार, अस्, m. non-acquiescence, dissent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वीकृत
अ-स्वीकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, dissented from, refused,<BR>not promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छ
अस्वच्छ अ-स्वच्छ, अस्, आ, अम्, not clear,<BR>opaque.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वन्त|अस्वंत|अस्वन्तः
अस्वन्त अ-स्वन्त (अ-सु-अन्त), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ending ill, leading to or having an unfavourable issue;<BR>(fr. असु-अन्त ?) approaching the end of life; a fire-<BR>place, see अश्वन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्न|अस्वप्नः
अस्वप्न अ-स्वप्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sleepless,<BR>awake; (अस्), m. sleeplessness, the being awake; a<BR>god, a deity [cf. ἄϋπνος].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्नज्
अ-स्वप्नज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. not sleepy, sleepless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर|अस्वरः
अस्वर अ-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, not aloud,<BR>speaking in an under tone, indistinct; having a bad<BR>or croaking voice; (अम्), ind. not aloud, in a low<BR>tone, indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर्ग्य
अस्वर्ग्य अ-स्वर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not leading<BR>to heaven, unheavenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वस्थ
अस्वस्थ अ-स्व-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, not in good<BR>health, not one's self, sick.<BR>—अस्वस्थ-ता, f. want of<BR>firmness; weakness, illness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वास्थ्य|अस्वास्थ्यं
अ-स्वास्थ्य, अम्, n. indisposition, sickness, dis-<BR>comfort, indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वादु
अस्वादु अ-स्वादु, उस्, उस्, उ, tasteless, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिक|अस्वामिकं
अस्वामिक अ-स्वामिक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, un-<BR>owned, unclaimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिन्
अ-स्वामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having no right or title to<BR>anything, not being master of it; that which has no<BR>master or owner.<BR>—अ-स्वामि-विक्रय, अस्, m. sale<BR>without ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाम्य|अस्वाम्यं
अ-स्वाम्य, अम्, n. absence of right or title to pro-<BR>perty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वार्थ
अस्वार्थ अ-स्वार्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, unselfish,<BR>disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वेद
अस्वेद अ-स्वेद, अस्, m. suppressed perspira-<BR>tion; (अस्, आ, अम्), not perspiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
अह् 1. अह् (connected with rt. नह्), cl. 1.<BR>P., Ved. अहति, 2nd pl. perf. अनाह, to string toge-<BR>ther (?), to compose, to celebrate, to prepare, to in-<BR>crease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
अह् 2. अह्, cl. 5. P., Ved. अह्नोति or अड्नोति,<BR>to pervade or occupy; to go or move; cl. 10 (?) to<BR>cause to shine (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन
अहन, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminating, spreading light<BR>(epithet of the dawn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
अह् 3. अह् (defect. verb, preserved only in<BR>five persons of the perfect, viz. आत्थ, आह, आहथुस्,<BR>आहतुस्, आहुस्, which may have a present significa-<BR>tion), to say, speak; to acknowledge, accept, state;<BR>to declare, express, signify; to call; to attribute; to<BR>call (with two acc.); to hold, consider, regard; to<BR>adjudge anything (acc.) to any one (gen.). [To<BR>this rt. are referred, Hib. ag-all, ‘speech;’ ag-aill,<BR>‘to speak;’ eigh-im, ‘I call:’ Goth. af-aika, ‘I<BR>deny:' Lat. nego for न्ऽ — एगो, 'to say no:' also ajo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह अह, ind. (as a particle implying<BR>ascertainment, affirmation, certainty, &c.) surely, cer-<BR>tainly, yes, well; (as explaining, defining, admitting,<BR>limiting, &c.) namely; I grant you, granted, indeed,<BR>of course; at least. This particle is also said to im-<BR>ply rejecting, sending; deviation from custom, im-<BR>propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयाति
अहंयाति, अहंयु, &c. See under अहम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत|अहतं
अहत अ-हत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. हन्), unhurt,<BR>uninjured, not struck, not killed; unbeaten (as clothes<BR>in washing); unwashed, new; unblemished, un-<BR>soiled; not disappointed; (अम्), n. unwashed or new<BR>clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहति|अहतिः
अ-हति or अ-हन्ति, इस्, f., Ved. safeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत्वा
अ-हत्वा, ind. not having killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहननीय
अ-हननीय or अ-हन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be<BR>killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्त्य|अहंत्य
अ-हन्त्य or अ-हन्त्र or अ-हन्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. indestructible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन् अहन् and अहस्, n. (said to be fr. 2.<BR>हा with अ, ‘not;’ according to others, who compare<BR>the Goth. daya, Germ. tag, Eng. day, a corruption<BR>of दहन् fr. rt. दह्; the nom. acc. voc. sing. and<BR>the middle cases come fr. अहस्, the others fr. अहन्;<BR>in the Vedas the middle cases also are sometimes<BR>formed fr. अहन्, e. g. अहभ्यस्, अहभिस्); a day;<BR>a sacrificial or festival day; a day's work; a portion<BR>of a book appointed for one day's reading; day per-<BR>sonified as one of the eight Vasus; N. of a Tīrtha;<BR>अहन्य्-अहनि or अहर्-अहः, day by day, daily;<BR>अहनी, du. day and night; तद् अहस्, on that very<BR>day; यद् अहस्, on which day. (As the last mem-<BR>ber of a compound अहन् generally appears in the<BR>form अह, m., rarely n., but sometimes also in the<BR>form अहन्, e. g. पुण्याह, एकाहन्, q. v. As the<BR>first member of a compound अहस् and अहर् are the<BR>usual forms; as in the following examples.)<BR>—अहः-<BR>पति, इस्, m. lord of the day, the sun; see अहर्-<BR>पति.<BR>—अहः-शेष, अम्, n. evening.<BR>—अहर्-आगम,<BR>अस्, m. the approach of day.<BR>—अहर्-गण, अस्, m. a<BR>series of sacrificial days; a month; any calculated<BR>term.<BR>—अहर्-जर, अस्, m., Ved. the year (as making<BR>days become old).<BR>—अहर्-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>born in the day or from day, not belonging to night<BR>or to the spirits of darkness.<BR>—अहर्-दिव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. existing every day; (अम्), ind. daily, day by day.<BR>—अहर्-दिवि, ind., Ved. day by day, every day, con-<BR>stantly.<BR>—अहर्-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. beholding the day,<BR>living.<BR>—अहर्-निश, अम्, n. day and night, a whole<BR>day; (अम्), ind. day and night, during the whole<BR>day, continually.<BR>—अहर्-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the<BR>day; the sun; epithet of Śiva; also written अहः-<BR>पति.<BR>—अहर्-बान्धव, अस्, m. the sun.<BR>—अहर्-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. partaking of the day.<BR>—अहर्-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. the sun.<BR>—अहर्-मुख, अम्, n. com-<BR>mencement of the day, morning, dawn.<BR>—अहर्-<BR>लोक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. taking the place of day.<BR>—अहर्-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. existing (many) days;<BR>known long ago; knowing the (fit) time or season.<BR>—अहश्-शस्, ind., Ved. every day.<BR>—अहस्-कर,<BR>अस्, m. the sun.<BR>—अहस्-पति, इस्, m. the sun; swallow<BR>wort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहो-रात्र, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन
अहन अहन. See 2. अह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्
अहम् अहम्, nom. sing. ‘I.’ The supposed<BR>base of this 1st personal pronoun is अस्मद्, q. v. [cf.<BR>Zend azem; Gr. ἐγών, ἐγώ, ἱών; Lat. ego; Goth.<BR>ik; Mod. Germ. ich; Lith. asz; Slav. az; Cambro-<BR>brit. ym; Bret. am, em].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयाति
अहं-याति, इस्, m., N. of a son of Saṃyāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयु|अहंयुः
अहंयु, उस्, उस्, उ, selfish, proud, haughty; (उस्),<BR>m. a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंवादिन्
अहं-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking only of one's self,<BR>presumptuous, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंश्रेयस्
अहं-श्रेयस्, अस्, or अहं-श्रेयस, अम्, n. claim-<BR>ing superiority for one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंसन
अहं-सन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. gaining for one's<BR>self, obtaining for one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कर्तव्य|अहंकर्तव्य
अहङ्-कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be referred to self;<BR>(अम्), n. the object of Ahaṅkāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कार|अहंकार|अहङ्कारः
अहङ्-कार, अस्, m. the making of self, sense of<BR>self, thinking of self, egotism, individuality; self-con-<BR>sciousness, pride, haughtiness; (in the Sāṅkhya phil.)<BR>the third of the eight producers or elements of crea-<BR>tion, viz. the conceit or conception of individuality,<BR>individualization.<BR>—अहङ्कार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, con-<BR>scious, selfish, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारिन्|अहंकारिन्
अहङ्-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, self-important, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कार्य|अहंकार्य
अहङ्-कार्य, अम्, n. that which is to be done by<BR>one's self, any personal object, business or matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृत|अहंकृत
अहङ्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, egotistic; proud, haughty;<BR>conscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृति|अहंकृति|अहङ्कृतिः
अहङ्-कृति, इस्, f. egotism, high opinion of one's<BR>self, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमग्रिका
अहम्-अग्रिका, f. or अहम्-उत्तर, अम्, n. a contest<BR>for superiority, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमहमिका
अहम्-अहमिका, f. assertion or conceit of superi-<BR>ority, boasting, egotism; military vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्व|अहंपूर्व
अहम्-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desirous of being<BR>first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्विका|अहंपूर्विका|अहम्पूर्व्विका
अहम्-पूर्विका, f. or अहम्-प्रथमिका, f. emu-<BR>lative onset, the running forward of soldiers with<BR>emulation; conceit, vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्भद्र|अहंभद्र
अहम्-भद्र, अम्, n. self-conceit, a high notion<BR>of one's own superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्मति|अहंमति|अहम्मतिः
अहम्-मति, इस्, f. or अहम्-मान, अम्, n. self-<BR>illusion, spiritual ignorance, conceit, self-love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर|अहरः
अहर अ-हर, अस्, m. (rt. हृ), N. of the<BR>twelfth Manu; a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरणीय
अ-हरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be taken away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहारिन्
अ-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, not taking (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्य|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अ-हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be stolen, not to be<BR>removed; (अस्), m. a mountain.<BR>—अहार्य-ता, f. or<BR>अहार्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state of not being liable to<BR>be taken away, security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरित
अहरित अ-हरित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्ष
अहर्ष अ-हर्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. हृष्), un-<BR>happy, gloomy, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्षित
अ-हर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, unhappy, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल
अहल अ-हल, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-हलि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>unploughed, unfurrowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्य|अहल्यः
अ-हल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not arable, unploughed;<BR>(आ), f., N. of an Apsaras; N. of the wife of Gautama<BR>or Śaradvat; N. of a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्लिक|अहल्लिकः
अहल्लिक अहल्लिक, अस्, m., Ved. a talker,<BR>tattler (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहवनीय
अहवनीय अ-हवनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. हु),<BR>not to be offered as an oblation, not fit or proper to<BR>be sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहविस्
अ-हविस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. without oblations, sacri-<BR>ficeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्त
अहस्त अ-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, handless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहह
अहह अहह or अहहा, ind. a particle or<BR>interjection, as Ah! Aha! &c., implying surprise,<BR>fatigue, pain, sorrow, pleasure, calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्य|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अहार्य अ-हार्य, &c. See under अ-हर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहावस्
अहावस् अहावस्, Ved., said to be a sound<BR>like a flourish at the end of a hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहि|अहिः
अहि अहि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. अंह्; according to<BR>Sāy. fr. rt. हन् with आ prefixed and shortened, ‘one<BR>that destroys on all sides’), a snake; the serpent of<BR>the sky, the demon Vṛtra; a cloud; water; lead;<BR>a traveller; the sun; a N. of Rāhu, the ascending<BR>node; the navel; [cf. अघ and अंहु, pp. 1, 6; Lat.<BR>anguis; Gr. ἔχι-ς, ἔχιδνα, ἔγχε-λυς and ὄφις<BR>Lith. ungury-s; Russ. ûgorj; Armen. ôz; Germ.<BR>unc; Mod. Gr. ἀχέλι]<BR>—अहि-कान्त, अस्, m. air,<BR>wind; (snakes being supposed to feed upon air.)<BR>—अहि-कोष, अस्, m. the slough or cast skin of a<BR>snake.<BR>—अहि-क्षत्र and अहि-क्षेत्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a country.<BR>—अहि-गोप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. guarded<BR>by a serpent.<BR>—अहि-घ्न, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>slaying of the serpent or demon (Vṛtra) who ob-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">Page0109-c+ 79</a>]<BR>structs the heavenly waters.<BR>—अहि-घ्नी, ईस्, m., Ved.<BR>killing snakes.<BR>—अहि-च्छत्र, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>vegetable poison; the plant Gymnema Sylvestre (?);<BR>N. of a country; (आ), f. sugar; the city of Ahi-<BR>cchatra.<BR>—अहि-च्छत्रक, अम्, n. a mushroom.<BR>—अहि-जित्, त्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa, also of Indra.<BR>—अहि-तुण्डिक, अस्, m. a snake-catcher or ex-<BR>hibiter; see आहितुण्डिक.<BR>—अहि-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्,<BR>or अहि-दन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, having the teeth of a ser-<BR>pent.<BR>—अहि-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, enemy of the serpents or<BR>of Vṛtra; (ट्), m. an ichneumon; a peacock; Garuḍa,<BR>the bird of Viṣṇu; Indra.<BR>—अहि-नकुलिका, f. the<BR>natural enmity between a snake and an ichneumon.<BR>—अहि-नाम-भृत्, त्, m., N. of Baladeva (as identi-<BR>fied with Śeṣa).<BR>—अहि-निर्मोक, अस्, m. or अहि-<BR>निर्व्लयनी, f. the cast off skin of a snake.<BR>—अहि-<BR>पताक, अस्, m. a kind of snake, not venomous.<BR>—अहि-पति, इस्, m., N. of Śeṣa, sovereign of<BR>the snakes, also of Vāsuki and others; any large<BR>serpent.<BR>—अहि-पुत्रक, अस्, m. a kind of boat.<BR>—अहि-पूतन, अस्, आ, m. f. sores on the hinder<BR>part of the body (of children).<BR>—अहि-फेन, अम्,<BR>n. opium, the saliva or venom of a snake [cf. 2.<BR>अ-फेन].<BR>—अहि-ब्रध्न, अस्, m., N. of Śiva; one<BR>of the Rudras; corrupted fr. अहिर्-बुध्न्यस्.<BR>—अहि-<BR>ब्रध्न-देवता, f. the twenty-sixth lunar mansion.<BR>—अहि-भय, अस्, m. fear of a lurking snake;<BR>apprehension of treachery.<BR>—अहिभय-दा, f., N.<BR>of the plant Flacourtia Cataphracta Roxb.<BR>—अहि-<BR>भानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. shining like serpents; epithet<BR>of the Maruts.<BR>—अहि-भुज्, क्, m. Garuḍa, the bird<BR>of Viṣṇu; a peacock; N. of a plant.<BR>—अहि-भृत्,<BR>त्, m. ‘carrying serpents,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—अहि-मन्यु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. enraged like serpents, epithet of the<BR>Maruts; (Sāy.) ‘endowed with destructive anger,’<BR>or ‘with unimpaired knowledge.’<BR>—अहि-मर्दनी,<BR>f., N. of a plant.<BR>—अहि-माय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>multiform or versatile like a snake, showing the same<BR>variety of colour and shape.<BR>—अहि-मार or अहि-<BR>मेदक, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—अहि-रिपु, उस्, m.<BR>a peacock.<BR>—अहिर्-बुध्न, अस्, m., N. of Śiva; cor-<BR>rupted fr. अहिर्-बुध्न्यस्.<BR>—अहिर्बुध्न-देवता,<BR>आस्, f. pl. the twenty-sixth lunar mansion.<BR>—अहिर्-<BR>ब्रध्न, अस्, m., N. of a Rudra.<BR>—अहि-लता, f., the<BR>plant Betel; another plant.<BR>—अहि-लोचन, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a servant of Śiva.<BR>—अहि-विदष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>snake-bitten.<BR>—अहि-विद्विष्, ट्, m. Garuḍa; Indra.<BR>—अहि-शुष्मसत्त्वन्, आ, m., Ved. one whose men<BR>(the Maruts) hiss like serpents; epithet of Indra; (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. अहि-शुष्म means ‘of all-pervading<BR>strength,’ and is to be separated from सत्त्वन्.)<BR>—अहि-<BR>हत्य, अम्, n. the slaying of the serpent or demon<BR>(Vṛtra) who obstructs the heavenly waters.<BR>—अहि-हन्,<BR>आ, m., Ved. killing serpents or Vṛtra.<BR>—अह्य्-अर्षु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. gliding like a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिक|अहिकः
1. अहिक, अस्, m. a blind snake, not venomous,<BR>see अन्धाहिक; (आ), f., N. of the silk-cotton tree,<BR>Bombax Heptaphyllum Salmalia Malabarica. (For 2.<BR>अहिक, see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसक
अहिंसक अ-हिंसक, अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-हिंसत्,<BR>अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or अ-हिंसान, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. हिंस्),<BR>Ved. not hurting, harmless, innocuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसा
अ-हिंसा, f. harmlessness, not injuring anything,<BR>one of the cardinal virtues of most Hindū sects, but<BR>particularly of the Buddhists and Jainas; security,<BR>safeness.<BR>—अहिंसा-निरत, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to<BR>harmlessness or gentleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसित
अ-हिंसित or अ-हिंस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. un-<BR>injured, being unharmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्र|अहिंस्रः
अ-हिंस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, innocuous, innocent, harm-<BR>less; (अम्), n. harmless behaviour; (आ), f., N. of the<BR>plant Momordica Cochinchinensis, Spreng, (commonly<BR>called Kūrkavāli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिक|अहिकः
अहिक 2. अहिक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अहन्, q. v.),<BR>is found at the end of a few compounds in the sense<BR>of lasting a certain number of days, e. g. दशाहिक,<BR>lasting for ten days. See 1. अहिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिण्डुका|अहिंडुका
अहिण्डुका अहिण्डुका, f. a kind of small poi-<BR>sonous animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहित|अहितः
अहित अ-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. धा), not placed,<BR>not put, not fixed; unfit, improper; unadvantageous,<BR>noxious; hurtful, prejudicial; hostile, inimical; (अस्),<BR>m. an enemy; (अम्), n. damage; food &c. contra-<BR>indicated in a disease.<BR>—अहित-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, ad-<BR>verse, inimical, acting unkindly.<BR>—अ-हित-नामन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. having as yet no name.<BR>—अ-हित-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, not friendly-minded, hating, ad-<BR>verse, inimical.<BR>—अहित-हित-विचार-शून्य-बुद्धि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, whose intellect is incapable of discriminating<BR>between good and evil.<BR>—अहितेच्छु (˚त-इच्˚), उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, not wishing well, malevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिमकर|अहिमकरः
अहिमकर अ-हिम-कर, अस्, or अ-हिम-तेजस्,<BR>आस्, or अ-हिम-रुचि, इस्, or अ-हिमांशु (˚म-अं˚),<BR>उस्, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अही
अही अही, ईस्, m., Ved., N. of a demon con-<BR>quered by Indra and his companions; a serpent (see<BR>अहि); a cow; (ई), du. heaven and earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन 1. अहीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अहन्), lasting<BR>several days; (अस्), m. a sacrifice lasting several days;<BR>one lasting twelve days (i. e. स्तोम or यज्ञ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन 2. अहीन, अस्, m. (fr. अहि, q. v.), a<BR>large snake (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन 3. अ-हीन, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 2. हा), un-<BR>impaired, whole, entire; full, luxurious; not deprived<BR>of, not withdrawing; possessed of; not outcast or<BR>vile.<BR>—अ-हीन-गु, उस्, m., N. of a prince, son of<BR>Devānīka.<BR>—अ-हीन-वादिन्, ई, m. a witness capable<BR>of giving evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीर|अहीरः
अहीर अहीर, अस्, m. a cowherd. See अभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीरणि|अहीरणिः
अहीरणि अहीरणि, इस्, or अहीरणिन्, ई, m. a<BR>kind of snake, said to be two-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीशुव
अहीशुव अहीशुव, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>demon conquered by Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहु
अहु अहु, उस्, वी, उ, (in compounds) narrow.<BR>See अंहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहुत|अहुतः
अहुत अ-हुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. हु), unsacri-<BR>ficed, unoffered, not yet sacrificed; one who has<BR>not received any sacrifice; not gained or obtained by<BR>sacrifice; (अस्), m. religious meditation, prayer, and<BR>study of the Veda, considered as one of the five great<BR>sacraments, otherwise called Brahma-yajña.<BR>—अ-हुताद्<BR>(˚त-अद्), त्, त्, त्, Ved. not eating of a sacrifice; not<BR>allowed to partake of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहूत
अहूत अ-हूत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ह्वे), uncalled, un-<BR>summoned, unchallenged. (The form अ-हुत with the<BR>sense ‘uncalled,’ given by Wilson, is very questionable.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहृणान
अहृणान अ-हृणान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>being angry, friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहृणीयमान
अ-हृणीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not being angry,<BR>jealous, or envious; not discontented, willing; that<BR>which is bestowed willingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहृद्य
अहृद्य अ-हृद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not desired, not<BR>agreeable.<BR>—अहृद्य-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, disagreeable, caus-<BR>ing disgust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहे
अहे अहे, ind. a particle implying reproach,<BR>rejection, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतु|अहेतुः
अहेतु अ-हेतु, उस्, m. absence of cause or<BR>reason.<BR>—अहेतु-ता, f. or अहेतु-त्व, अम्, n. absence<BR>of cause, reason, or necessity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुक
अ-हेतुक, अस्, आ, अम्, causeless, groundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहैतुक
अ-हैतुक, अस्, ई, अम्, having no reason or founda-<BR>tion; causeless, having no motive, disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेरु|अहेरुः
अहेरु अहेरु, उस्, f. the plant Asparagus<BR>Racemosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेळत्|अहेळन्त्
अहेळत् अ-हेऌअत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or अ-हेऌअमान,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or अ-हेऌअयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (rt. हेड्, Ved.<BR>हेल् with अ), Ved. not angry, not displeased, favour-<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहो
अहो अहो, ind. (as a particle and inter-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">Page0110-b+ 71</a>]<BR>jection of joyful or painful surprise) Ah! (of enjoy-<BR>ment or satisfaction) Oh! (of fatigue, discontent,<BR>compassion, sorrow, regret) Alas! Ah! (of praise)<BR>Bravo! (of reproach) Fie! (of calling) Ho! Halo!<BR>(of doubt, deliberation) either, or; (of contempt)<BR>Pshaw! It is also sometimes an expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोपुरुषिका
अहो-पुरुषिका, f. self-confidence; boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोतृ
अहोतृ अ-होतृ, ता, m., Ved. not sacrificing;<BR>not competent to sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहोरात्र अहो-रात्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. अहन्,<BR>q. v. + रात्रि, q. v.), a day and night, νυχθήμερον a<BR>day of twenty-four hours or thirty Muhūrtas, from<BR>sunrise to sunrise; a day and night of the Pitṛs = a<BR>month of the gods = a year of Brahmā = 2000 Yugas<BR>of the gods; (अम्), ind. day and night, continually,<BR>always.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरूप
अहो-रूप, अम्, n. the appearance of day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोवत
अहोवत अहोवत, ind. a particle of calling,<BR>of compassion, of fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोही
अहोही अहोही, ind. in a variegated or<BR>wonderful manner (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्न|अह्नः
अह्न अह्न, अस्, m. as last member of a<BR>compound = अहन्, a day, q. v.; e. g. मध्याह्न,<BR>midday; अपराह्ण, afternoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नाय
अह्नाय, ind. formerly; instantly; soon, speedily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्निक
अह्निक, अस्, आ, अम्, as last member of a compound<BR>= अहन्; e. g. द्व्य्-अह्निक, अस्, आ, अम्, lasting two<BR>days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नी
अह्नी, f. and अह्नीय, अस्, आ, अम्, or अह्न्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (all fr. अहन्), used at the end of compounds;<BR>e. g. रथाह्न्य, अम्, n. the daily journey of a<BR>chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नवाय्य
अह्नवाय्य अ-ह्नवाय्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ह्नु),<BR>Ved. not to be denied or set aside; (अस्), m. accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. the N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्यर्षु
अह्यर्षु अह्य्-अर्षु. See under अहि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रय
अह्रय अ-ह्रय or अ-ह्रयाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>ह्री, shame, q. v.), Ved. luxurious, proud, bold, con-<BR>scious of one's own power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रि
अ-ह्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. luxurious, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्री
अ-ह्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. shameless, importunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रीक|अह्रीकः
अ-ह्रीक, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless; (अस्), m. a Bud-<BR>dhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रुत
अह्रुत अ-ह्रुत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ह्वृ), Ved.<BR>not fluctuating, not stumbling; going in a straight<BR>line; not crooked, straight.<BR>—अह्रुत-प्सु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. of straight or upright appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्वला
अह्वला अ-ह्वला, f., Ved. not fluctuating,<BR>not stumbling, firmness; the plant Semecarpus Ana-<BR>cardium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ 1. आ, the second letter of the alphabet,<BR>corresponding to अ long, as in far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ 2. आ, (as a particle or interjection of as-<BR>sent) yes, verily; (of compassion or pain) Ah!<BR>Alas! in the latter sense it is more correctly written<BR>आस्; (of reminiscence) Ah! Oh! (a conjunction dis-<BR>junctive) but; (a conjunction copulative) and. This<BR>particle remains unaltered in orthography even before<BR>vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ 3. आ a prefix to verbs and nouns, (ex-<BR>pressing) near, near to, towards, from all sides, all<BR>around; and sometimes redundant. As a prefix to verbs<BR>of motion it expresses the notion of moving or going<BR>towards; e. g. आ-क्रामति, he goes towards. When<BR>prefixed to roots like गम्, या, and इ, to go, and दा,<BR>to give, it reverses the action; e. g. आ-गच्छति, he<BR>comes; आ-दत्ते, he takes.<BR>As unconnected with verbs and prefixed to nouns it<BR>forms with them either compound adverbs or adjectives,<BR>implying the limit conclusive (until, unto, as far as),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">Page0110-c+ 65</a>]<BR>or the limit inceptive (from, from thence or that<BR>time); e. g. आ-मरणम्, till death; आ-कुमारम्,<BR>from childhood [cf. a puero]; आ-गोपाला द्विजातयः,<BR>the twice-born including the cowherds.<BR>(Prefixed to adjectives &c. it implies) diminution;<BR>e. g. आ-पाण्डु, a little pale; आ-पक्व, half-cooked.<BR>(As a separable adverb आ implies) near, near to,<BR>towards; thereto, further, also, and; especially, even.<BR>In many places in the Vedas आ gives force to the<BR>word which precedes it (e. g. महिमा वाम् इन्-<BR>द्राग्नी पनिष्ठ आ, ‘your greatness, O Indra and<BR>Agni, is praiseworthy indeed’); and in a similar man-<BR>ner we find it in the Veda placed after prepositions,<BR>the sense of which is strengthened by it.<BR>(As a separable preposition with acc. or abl.) near<BR>to, up to, to, as far as; e. g. शतम् आ जातीस्, as<BR>far as a hundred births; आ समुद्रात्, as far as the<BR>ocean: (with abl.) away from, from; out of, of, from<BR>among; e. g. आ मूलात्, from the beginning; बहुभ्य<BR>आ, from among many: (with loc.) in, at; e. g.<BR>दम आ, in a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ 4. आ, आस्, m., N. of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आइ
आ-इ आ-इ. See ए.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आइन्ध्
आ-इन्ध् आ-इन्ध्. See एन्ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आइन्व्
आ-इन्व् आ-इन्व्. See एन्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आइष्
आ-इष् आ-इष्. See एष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आईक्ष्
आ-ईक्ष् आ-ईक्ष्. See एक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आईर्
आ-ईर् आ-ईर्. See एर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आईष्
आ-ईष् आ-ईष्. See एष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आउ
आ-उ आ-उ. See ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आउक्ष्
आ-उक्ष् आ-उक्ष्. See ओक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आऊर्णु
आ-ऊर्णु आ-ऊर्णु. See ओर्णु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आऊह्
आ-ऊह् आ-ऊह्. See ओह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आऋ
आ-ऋ आ-ऋ. See आर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आऋछ्
आ-ऋछ् आ-ऋछ्. See आर्छ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आऋञ्ज्
आ-ऋञ्ज् आ-ऋञ्ज्. See आर्ञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आऋध्
आ-ऋध् आ-ऋध्. See आर्ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकच्
आकच् आ-कच्, cl. 1. A. -कचते, -चितुम्, to<BR>tie on, to fasten on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकत्थन|आकत्थनं
आकत्थन आ-कत्थन, अस्, आ, अम्, boasting,<BR>swaggering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकन्
आकन् आ-कन्, cl. 1. P. -कनति, -नितुम्, or<BR>Intens. -चाकन्ति, to be pleased with (with loc.); to<BR>endeavour to obtain; to love, to desire, solicit, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प्|आकंप्
आकम्प् आ-कम्प्, cl. 1. A. -कम्पते, -पितुम्,<BR>to tremble: Caus. -कम्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प|आकंपः|आकम्पः
आ-कम्प, अस्, m. or आ-कम्पन, अम्, n. trem-<BR>bling motion, shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पित|आकंपित|आकम्पितं
आ-कम्पित or आ-कम्प्र, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken,<BR>trembling; moved, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर|आकरः
आकर आ-कर, आकरिन्, &c. See under आ-कॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरण|आकरणं
आकरण आ-करण. See under आ-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ण्
आकर्ण् आ-कर्ण्, cl. 10. P. -कर्णयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to give ear to, listen to, hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ण
आ-कर्ण, up to the ear, (occurs at the commence-<BR>ment of several compounds to denote the end of an<BR>arrow reaching to the ear in drawing a bow.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णन|आकर्णनं
आ-कर्णन, अम्, n. hearing, listening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णित
आ-कर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, heard, listened to; over-<BR>heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ण्य
आ-कर्ण्य, ind. having heard or listened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ष|आकर्षः
आकर्ष आ-कर्ष, आ-कर्षिन्, &c. See under<BR>आ-कृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्
आकल् आ-कल्, cl. 10. P. -कलयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to shake, agitate, throw, cast; to lay hold of, seize;<BR>to tie, fasten; to surrender, transfer; to observe, take<BR>into consideration; to consider [cf. Gr. ὀκέλλω].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलन|आकलनं
आ-कलन, अम्, n. binding, confinement; counting,<BR>reckoning; laying hold of; wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलित
आ-कलित, अस्, आ, अम्, bound; counted, reckoned;<BR>seized, held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्प|आकल्पः
आकल्प आ-कल्प, अस्, m. (rt. कॢप् with आ),<BR>adding to, improving, increasing; ornament, decora-<BR>tion; sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पक|आकल्पकः
