आकषक
आ-कषक, अस्, इका, अम्, cutting, rubbing, or test-<BR>ing with a touchstone, touching, assaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषिक
आ-कषिक, अस्, ई, अम्, touching, testing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकस्मिक|आकस्मिकं
आकस्मिक आकस्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-कस्मात्),<BR>causeless, unforeseen, unexpected, sudden.<BR>—आकस्मि-<BR>क-त्व, अम्, n. suddenness, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष्|आकांक्ष्
आकाङ्क्ष् आ-काङ्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. A. -काङ्क्षति,<BR>-ते, -षितुम्, to desire, long for, hope for, endeavour<BR>to gain, expect (with acc.); to endeavour to reach a<BR>place, turn to; (in gram.) to require some word or<BR>words to be supplied for the completion of the sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष|आकांक्ष
आ-काङ्क्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring, wishing; (in<BR>gram.) requiring a word or words to complete the<BR>sense; (आ), f. desire, wish; (in gram.) the requiring<BR>of a word or period for the completion of the sense;<BR>looking at or towards; purpose, intention; enquiry,<BR>asking; the significancy of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षणीय
आ-काङ्क्षणीय or आ-काङ्क्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be desired or expected, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षत्
आ-काङ्क्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing, expecting;<BR>looking at, looking to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षित|आकांक्षित
आ-काङ्क्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired; asked,<BR>enquired; regarded, looked at; wanted, necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षिन्|आकांक्षिन्
आ-काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wishing, desirous, wishful,<BR>hopeful; asking, enquiring, expectant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्ष्य|आकांक्ष्य
आ-काङ्क्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, desirable; (अम्), n. need<BR>of supplying a word or words for the completion of<BR>the sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाय|आकायः
आकाय आ-काय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. चि with आ), a<BR>funeral pile; abode, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाय्य
आकाय्य आ-काय्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. कि with<BR>आ), Ved. desirable; in every way praiseworthy or<BR>commendable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकार|आकारः
आकार आ-कार. See under आ-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाल|आकालः
आकाल आ-काल, अस्, m. the right time; (for<BR>अ-काल) wrong or inauspicious time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिक|आकालिकं
आकालिक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, not filling a space of<BR>time, momentary, instantaneous; unseasonable; (ई),<BR>f. lightning.<BR>—आकालिक-त्व, अम्, n. unseasonableness,<BR>suddenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश्
आकाश् आ-काश्, cl. 1. A. -काशते, -शितुम्, to<BR>shine, be bright; to view, recognize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश|आकाशं|आकाशः
आ-काश, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in Ved. m.) light, clear-<BR>ness; a free space, vacuity; the ether, the sky or<BR>atmosphere considered as the fifth element; Brahma<BR>as identical with ether. आकाश is the subtle and<BR>ethereal fluid, supposed to fill and pervade the uni-<BR>verse and to be the peculiar vehicle of life and of<BR>sound. आकाशे, ind. in the air; a stage direction<BR>implying something said by or to a person out of<BR>sight.<BR>—आकाश-कक्षा, f. the horizon, ‘girdle of the<BR>sky.’<BR>—आकाश-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going through the<BR>atmosphere.<BR>—आकाश-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—आकाश-चमस, अस्, m. the moon, (‘a cup<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">Page0111-b+ 75</a>]<BR>or vessel with ether.’)<BR>—आकाश-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, pro-<BR>duced in the sky.<BR>—आकाश-जननिन्, ई, m. a loop-<BR>hole, a casement, an embrasure.<BR>—आकाश-दीप or<BR>आकाश-प्रदीप, अस्, m. a lamp or torch lighted in<BR>honour of Lakṣmī or Viṣṇu and elevated on a pole<BR>in the air at the Dīvāli (Dīpāli) festival, in the month<BR>Kārttika; a beacon, a lantern on a pole.<BR>—आकाश-<BR>प्रतिष्ठित, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—आकाश-<BR>बुद्ध-लक्ष, अस्, m. (in theatrical language) fixing<BR>the gaze on some object out of sight of the audience.<BR>—आकाश-भाषित, अम्, n. (in dramatic language)<BR>speaking outside or off the stage; a supposed speech,<BR>which is replied to as if it had been spoken; a voice<BR>or sound in the air.<BR>—आकाश-मण्डल, अम्, n. the<BR>celestial sphere; the atmosphere.<BR>—आकाश-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, consisting of ether.<BR>—आकाश-मांसी, f. the<BR>plant Nardostachys Jaṭāmāṃsī.<BR>—आकाश-मूली, f. the<BR>aquatic plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—आकाश-यान, अम्, n.<BR>a heavenly car, one moving through the air.<BR>—आकाश-<BR>रक्षिन्, ई, m. a warder, a watchman on the outer<BR>battlements.<BR>—आकाश-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, filling a cer-<BR>tain place, spacious, extensive.<BR>—आकाश-वर्त्मन्, अ,<BR>n. the atmosphere, the firmament, the air.<BR>—आकाश-<BR>वल्ली, f. a sort of creeper, a parasite, Cassyta Filiformis.<BR>—आकाश-वाणी, f. a voice from heaven; m., N.<BR>of the author of a Hanumat-stotra.<BR>—आकाश-सलिल,<BR>अम्, n. rain.<BR>—आकाश-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, abiding in<BR>the sky, aerial.<BR>—आकाश-स्फटिक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>crystal supposed to be formed in the atmosphere. It is<BR>of two kinds, Sūrya-kānta and Candra-kānta, q. v.<BR>—आकाशानन्त्यायतन (˚श-अनन्त्य-आय्˚), अम्, n.<BR>abode of infinity or of infinite space; N. of a world<BR>with Buddhists.<BR>—आकाशेश (˚श-ईश्˚), अस्, m. epithet<BR>of Indra, as ruler of the firmament; (in law) any<BR>helpless person, as a child, a woman, a pauper or in-<BR>valid (who has no other possession than the air).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशीय
आकाशीय, अस्, आ, अम्, or आकाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, atmo-<BR>spherical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश्य
आकाश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिञ्चन|आकिंचन|आकिंचनं|आकिञ्चनं
आकिञ्चन आकिञ्चन or आकिञ्चन्य, अम्, n.<BR>(fr. अ-किञ्चन), want of any possession, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिदन्ति
आकिदन्ति आकिदन्ति, इस्, and आकिदन्तीय, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a warrior-tribe and its chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीम्
आकीम् आ-कीम्, ind., Ved. (with abl.) from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्च्|आकुंच्
आकुञ्च् आ-कुञ्च्, cl. 6. P., 1. A. -कुचति,<BR>-कुञ्चते, -चितुम्, to bend: Caus. -कुञ्चयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to draw together, contort, contract; to bend inwards,<BR>shorten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चन|आकुंचनं|आकुञ्चनं
आ-कुञ्चन, अम्, n. compression, contraction,<BR>shrinking; collecting, heaping; curving, flexure;<BR>contortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चित
आ-कुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, contorted, contracted;<BR>twisted, crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुण्ठित
आकुण्ठित आ-कुण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>founded, abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुर्वती
आकुर्वती आ-कुर्वती. See under आ-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुल|आकुलं
आकुल आ-कुल, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. कुल्, to com-<BR>pact or compress together), filled, full, overburdened<BR>with (with inst.); confounded, confused, agitated,<BR>flurried; confused (in order), disordered; taken out<BR>of one's natural condition; incoherent, contradic-<BR>tory; (अम्), n. an inhabited place.<BR>—आकुल-ता, f. or<BR>आकुल-त्व, अम्, n. accumulation, multitude; perplexity,<BR>confusion, bewilderment.<BR>—आकुलेन्द्रिय (˚ल-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, confused in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलय
आकुलय, nom. P. आकुलयति, -यितुम्, to con-<BR>found, make disordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलि|आकुलिः
आकुलि, इस्, m., N. of an Asura priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलित
आकुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, confounded; bewildered, flur-<BR>ried, agitated; distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीकृ
आकुली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to fill with;<BR>to confound.<BR>—आकुली-करण, अम्, n. confounding.<BR>—आकुली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, confounded; perplexed,<BR>bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीभू
आकुली-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्, to become<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">Page0111-c+ 77</a>]<BR>perplexed.<BR>—आकुली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, perplexed, con-<BR>founded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुष्ट
आकुष्ट आ-कुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, expelled, ex-<BR>tracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूज्
आकूज् आ-कूज्, cl. 1. P. -कूजति, -जितुम्, to<BR>twitter, warble, coo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूत|आकूतं
आकूत आ-कूत, अम्, n. (rt. कू or कु, to<BR>sound), meaning, intention, purpose; wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूति|आकूतिः
आ-कूति, इस्, f. intention, wish, desire; N. of a<BR>daughter of Manu Svāyambhuva and of Śatarūpā.<BR>—आकूति-प्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. accomplishing one's<BR>intentions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूवार
आकूवार आकूवार, अस्, m. = अ-कू-पार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृ
आकृ आ-कृ, cl. 8. 5. P. -करोति, -कृणोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to bring near or towards, to bring down,<BR>to make or form wholly; to drive near to or together:<BR>Caus. P. -कारयति, -यितुम्, to ask any one (acc.)<BR>for anything (acc.); to invite to a place, to call into<BR>existence, to cause to appear: Desid. -चिकीर्षति,<BR>to intend to accomplish: Intens. -करिक्रति, 3rd pl.,<BR>Ved. to attract repeatedly towards one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकार|आकारः
आ-कार, अस्, m. form, figure, shape, stature, appear-<BR>ance, aspect, behaviour, external gesture or aspect of<BR>the body, the expression of the face, as furnishing<BR>a clue to the disposition of mind; hint, sign, token;<BR>the letter आ.<BR>—आकार-गुप्ति, इस्, f. or आकार-गोपन,<BR>अम्, n. dissimulation, suppressing all sign or inclina-<BR>tion of the feelings.<BR>—आकार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a shape, embodied, symmetrical, handsome, well-<BR>formed.<BR>—आकार-वर्ण-सुश्लक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>licate in shape and colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारण|आकारणं
आ-कारण or आ-करण, अम्, आ, n. f. calling, in-<BR>viting, a call or summons; challenging, a challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारणीय
आ-कारणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारित
आ-कारित, अस्, आ, अम्, called, summoned; stipulated,<BR>agreed; demanded, exacted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुर्वती
आ-कुर्वती, f., N. of a certain rocky hill. (Rām. II.<BR>71. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृत
आ-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. brought near to; being<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृति|आकृतिः
आ-कृति, इस्, f., Ved. a constituent part; form, figure,<BR>shape, appearance, aspect; character, specimen; the<BR>body; tribe, species; a metre consisting of four lines<BR>with twenty-two syllables to each line.<BR>—आकृति-गण,<BR>अस्, m. a list of specimens, a collection of words belong-<BR>ing to a certain grammatical rule, which does not ex-<BR>hibit every word belonging to that rule, but only speci-<BR>mens; whereas a simple Gaṇa exhibits every word;<BR>(explained by native authorities to mean a list of words,<BR>the fact of a word belonging to which can only be<BR>determined by observing the forms used by classical<BR>authors.)<BR>—आकृति-च्छत्रा, f. the plant Achyranthes<BR>Aspera.<BR>—आकृति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having shape, em-<BR>bodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्
आकृष् आ-कृष्, cl. 1. P., 6. P. A. -कर्षति,<BR>कृषति, -ते, -कर्ष्टुम् or -क्रष्टुम्, to draw<BR>towards, attract, put on, draw away; to bend (e. g.<BR>चापम्, a bow); to draw or tear off, draw out of;<BR>to withdraw, deprive of, take away; to borrow: Caus.<BR>-कर्षयति, -यितुम्, to draw near to one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ष|आकर्षः
आ-कर्ष, अस्, m. drawing or attracting towards<BR>one's self, pulling to or towards, dragging, attracting,<BR>hawling; drawing the bow; attraction, fascination;<BR>spasm; playing with dice; a die or dice; a board for<BR>such a game; an organ of sense; magnetic attrac-<BR>tion; a magnet, a loadstone; N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षक|आकर्षकः
आ-कर्षक, अस्, इका, अम्, attractive, what draws<BR>or attracts; (अस्), m. a magnet or loadstone; (इका),<BR>f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षण|आकर्षणं
आ-कर्षण, अम्, n. pulling, drawing, attracting;<BR>(ई), f. a crooked stick for pulling down fruit, &c.; any<BR>instrument for pulling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिक
आ-कर्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, magnetic, attractive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षित
आ-कर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn, attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिन्
आ-कर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, attractive; (णी), f. a rod with<BR>a hook at the end for pulling down boughs in order<BR>to gather fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्ट|आकृष्टं
आ-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn, pulled, attracted.<BR>—आकृष्ट-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, distracted in mind.<BR>—आकृष्ट-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pulling, dragging, pull-<BR>ing up or out; pulling to, attracting; charming,<BR>fascinating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टि|आकृष्टिः
