आ-क्रोश, अस्, m. calling or crying out, vociferation;<BR>scolding, reviling, blaming, censuring, abuse; a curse<BR>or oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशक|आक्रोशकः
आ-क्रोशक, अस्, ई, अम्, vociferous, abusing, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशन|आक्रोशनं
आ-क्रोशन, अम्, n. assailing with harsh language,<BR>scolding, censuring; imprecation, curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशनीय
आ-क्रोशनीय or आ-क्रोशितव्य or आ-क्रोश्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, censurable, to be reviled or cursed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशित
आ-क्रोशित, अस्, आ, अम्, cursed, abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोष्टृ
आ-क्रोष्टृ, टा, m. a reviler; one who vociferates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ली
आक्ली आ-क्ली, an undeclinable word joined<BR>to the roots अस्, कृ, and भू. See Gaṇa to Pāṇini<BR>I. 4, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्लेद|आक्लेदः
आक्लेद आ-क्लेद, अस्, m. moistening, sprink-<BR>ling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षद्यूतिक
आक्षद्यूतिक आक्षद्यूतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, effected<BR>or completed by gambling. See अक्ष-द्यूत under<BR>3. अक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपण|आक्षपणं
आक्षपण आ-क्षपण, अम्, n. (rt. 1. क्षप्),<BR>fasting, purification by fasting, abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाटिक|आक्षपाटिकः
आक्षपाटिक आक्षपाटिक, अस्, m. a judge.<BR>See अक्ष-पाटक under 2. अक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाद|आक्षपादः
आक्षपाद आक्षपाद, अस्, m. a follower of<BR>the Nyāya doctrine; a logician. See under 2. अक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षभारिक
आक्षभारिक आक्षभारिक. See Gaṇa to<BR>Pāṇini V. 1. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षर्
आक्षर् आ-क्षर्, cl. 10. P. -क्षारयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to abuse, revile, accuse, punish. (Sometimes<BR>regarded as a nom. fr. the next.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षार|आक्षारः
आ-क्षार, अस्, m. calumny, accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारण|आक्षारणं
आ-क्षारण, अम्, आ, n. f. abuse; calumnious ac-<BR>cusation (especially of adultery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारित|आक्षारितं
आ-क्षारित, अस्, आ, अम्, calumniated, falsely ac-<BR>cused; accused of adultery or fornication; guilty,<BR>criminal; reviled, abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षि
आक्षि आ-क्षि, cl. 2. 6. P. -क्षेति, -क्षियति,<BR>-क्षेतुम्, to abide, dwell in, stay at (with acc.);<BR>to inhabit; to exist; to possess, take possession of<BR>(with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षित्
आ-क्षित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. abiding, dwelling in, stay-<BR>ing at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिक|आक्षिकः
आक्षिक आक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. अक्ष),<BR>relating or belonging to a die or to gambling, &c.;<BR>won at dice; (अम्), n. a gambling debt, money lost<BR>at play; (अस्), m., N. of the tree Morinda Tinc-<BR>toria.<BR>—आक्षिक-पण, अस्, m. a stake, a wager, a<BR>bet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्
आक्षिप् आ-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -क्षिपति, -ते,<BR>-क्षेप्तुम्, to cast or throw at or down; to strike<BR>with a bolt; to draw near or together, to contract,<BR>convulse, cause to tremble; to draw or take off or<BR>away, withdraw; to chase or drive out of a place;<BR>to hang out or expose to view; put into; point to,<BR>apply to, refer to, hint, indicate; to refuse, not to<BR>have regard to, refuse as wrong; to insult, deride;<BR>to say or state ironically: Caus. P. -क्षेपयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to throw down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिपत्
आ-क्षिपत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, casting, striking,<BR>tossing, sending; reviling, abusing; excelling so as<BR>to reproach or put to shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्त
आ-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cast, thrown, tossed;<BR>thrown down or away; taken away; borne, carried;<BR>insulted, reviled, abused, blamed, ridiculed; equal or<BR>equivalent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्तिका
आ-क्षिप्तिका, f. a particular air or song which is<BR>sung by a person approaching the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्य
आ-क्षिप्य, ind. having spurned, having insulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेप|आक्षेपः
आ-क्षेप, अस्, m. throw, toss, drawing together or<BR>near to one's self, attraction, convulsion, palpitation;<BR>hinting; applying, laying on (as a colour); throwing<BR>away, giving up; sustaining (as a sound); reviling,<BR>abuse, censure, blame, reproach; objection; doubt,<BR>irony (as a figure in rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपक|आक्षेपकः
आ-क्षेपक, अस्, इका, अम्, blaming, censuring, re-<BR>viling; (अस्), m. a thrower, a detractor, a calumniator<BR>or accuser; sickness, disease; convulsion, spasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपण|आक्षेपणं
आ-क्षेपण, अम्, n. throwing, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपिन्
आ-क्षेपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, applying to, concerning; (also<BR>= आ-क्षेपक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीव
आक्षीव आक्षीव, अस्, m., N. of the plant<BR>Morunga Guilandina and Hyperanthera. See<BR>अक्षिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षैत्रज्ञ्य|आक्षैत्रज्ञ्यं
आक्षैत्रज्ञ्य आक्षैत्रज्ञ्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-क्षे-<BR>त्रज्ञ, q. v.), spiritual ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोट|आक्षोटः
आक्षोट आक्षोट or आक्षोड, अस् or अम् (?),<BR>m. or n. (?) a walnut (Pistacio nut ?); N. of a tree,<BR>Pīlu; also of another tree, Aleurites Triloba. See<BR>अक्षोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोदन|आक्षोदनं
आक्षोदन आक्षोदन, अम्, n. hunting (also<BR>आच्छोदन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ष्णु
आक्ष्णु आ-क्ष्णु, cl. 2. P. -क्ष्णौति, -क्ष्ण-<BR>वितुम्, to rub, polish up; sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ष्यत्|आक्ष्यन्त्
आक्ष्यत् आ-क्ष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fut. part. fr.<BR>अक्ष् or अश् with आ ?); आक्ष्यन्ति अहानि, days leading<BR>to completion, complemental days; the N. of certain<BR>days on which the ceremony Ayana, performed for<BR>the Ādityās and Aṅgirasas, is finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण
आखण आखण, अस्, आ, अम्, hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डयितृ
आखण्डयितृ आ-खण्डयितृ, ता, m. (rt.<BR>खण्ड्), a breaker, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डल|आखंडलः|आखण्डलः
आ-खण्डल, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking, destroying;<BR>destroying enemies; (अस्), m. a N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखन्
आखन् आ-खन्, cl. 1. P. -खनति, -नितुम्,<BR>to dig. (It is doubtful whether आ-खन् is used as a<BR>verb, but the nouns which follow are all derived<BR>from it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख|आखः
आ-ख, अस्, m. a spade, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखन|आखनः
आ-खन, अस्, m. a digger, a spade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिक|आखनिकः
आ-खनिक, अस्, m. a digger, a ditcher, a miner; a<BR>thief; a hog; a rat; a mouse; a spade.<BR>—आखनिक-<BR>बक or आखनिक-वक, अस्, m. a stork in relation<BR>to a mouse; (metaphorically) a man who behaves as<BR>an hero towards a weak person; a digger, a spade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखर|आखरः
आ-खर, अस्, m., Ved. the hole or cover of any<BR>animal; a stable; a spade, a digger.<BR>—आखरे-ष्ठ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abiding or dwelling in a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखात|आखातं|आखातः
आ-खात, अस्, अम्, m. n. a natural pond. See<BR>अ-खात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखान|आखानः
आ-खान, अस्, m. a spade, a digger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखु|आखुः
आ-खु, उस्, m. a mouse, a rat, a mole; the grass<BR>Lipeocercis Serrata; a thief; a hog; a digger, a<BR>spade.<BR>—आखु-करीष, अम्, n., Ved. a mole-hill.<BR>—आखु-कर्णी, f., N. of the plant Salvinia Cucul-<BR>lata.<BR>—आखु-ग, अस्, m. (riding on a rat), an epithet<BR>of Gaṇeśa and of Kārttikeya.<BR>—आखु-घात, अस्, m.<BR>a Śūdra or man of low caste and profession, lit. ‘a rat-<BR>catcher.’<BR>—आखु-पर्णिका or आखु-पर्णी, f., N. of<BR>the plant Salvinia Cucullata Roxb. (?).<BR>—आखु-पा-<BR>षाण, अस्, m. a kind of mineral, a loadstone.<BR>—आखु-भुज्, क्, m. ‘a mouse-eater,’ a cat.<BR>—आखु-<BR>रथ, अस्, m. a N. of Gaṇeśa, ‘having a rat for his<BR>vehicle.’<BR>—आखु-विष-हा, f. a kind of grass, Andro-<BR>pogon Serratum, considered as a remedy for a rat's<BR>bite.<BR>—आखूत्कर (˚खु-उत्˚), अस्, m. a mole-hill.<BR>—आखूत्थ (˚खु-उत्˚), अस्, m. the rising up or appear-<BR>ance of rats or moles, a swarm of rats or moles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखाद्
आखाद् आ-खाद्, cl. 1. P. -खादति, -दितुम्,<BR>to chew, to bite into pieces; to eat, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखिद्
आखिद् आ-खिद्, cl. 6. P., Ved. -खिदति,<BR>Class. -खिन्दति, -खेत्तुम्, to take away and appro-<BR>priate to one's self, to draw to one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखिल्य
आखिल्य आखिल्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-खिल), the<BR>whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेट|आखेटः
आखेट आ-खेट, अस्, m. (rt. खिट् ?), chase,<BR>hunting; terror, fright.<BR>—आखेट-शीर्षक, अम्, n.<BR>a cavern, a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटक|आखेटकः
आ-खेटक, अस्, आ, अम्, hunting, a hunter; fright-<BR>ening, frightful; (अम्), n. hunting, chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटिक|आखेटिकः
आखेटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, who or what hunts; terrible,<BR>frightful; (अस्), m. a hound; a hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखोट|आखोटः
आखोट आखोट, अस्, m. the walnut tree.<BR>See अक्षोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या आ-ख्या, cl. 2. P. -ख्याति, -तुम्,<BR>Ved. to look at; to count, number; to recite; to<BR>tell, notify; inform, communicate, declare, make<BR>known; to announce; to call, signify (with two acc.);<BR>Caus. P. -ख्यापयति, -यितुम्, to make known, de-<BR>clare; A. to cause to tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यस्
आ-ख्यस्, आस्, m., N. of Prajāpati, the lord of creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
2. आ-ख्या, f. appellation, name; (अस्, आ, अम्), often<BR>at the end of a compound in the sense of ‘named,’<BR>‘called.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यात|आख्यातं
आ-ख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, counted, recited; said, spoken;<BR>called; declared, made known; inflected, declined,<BR>conjugated; (अम्), n. a verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातव्य
आ-ख्यातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be told; to be de-<BR>clared, to be made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्याति|आख्यातिः
आ-ख्याति, इस्, f. telling, communication, publication<BR>of a report; fame; name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातिक
आख्यातिक, adj. fr. आ-ख्यात. Pāṇini IV. 3, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातृ
आ-ख्यातृ, ता, m. one who tells or speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यान|आख्यानं
आ-ख्यान, अम्, n. saying, declaring; speech; a<BR>tale, story, legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानक|आख्यानकं
आख्यानक, अम्, n. a tale, a short narrative; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a metre, being a combination of the Indravajrā<BR>and Upendravajrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यापन
आ-ख्यापन, अम्, n. causing one to tell, making<BR>known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायक|आख्यायकः
आ-ख्यायक, अस्, m. a messenger, a teller, an<BR>announcer or relater; (इका), f. a tale or short narra-<BR>tive; a true or probable story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिन्
आ-ख्यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, telling, declaring, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्येय
आ-ख्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be told or related; fit or<BR>proper to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग|आगः
आग 1. आग = आगस् in अन्-आग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्
आगम् आ-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्तुम्,<BR>to come; to make one's appearance; to come near,<BR>go towards or to or into; to arrive at, attain, reach,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">Page0113-b+ 80</a>]<BR>strike; to return; to fall into (any state of mind);<BR>have recourse to: Caus. P. -गमयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to come near; to lead towards; to convey; to<BR>announce the arrival (of any one); to obtain inform-<BR>ation about anything, ascertain (with acc.); A. to<BR>wait for, to have patience: Intens. Ved. -गनीगन्ति,<BR>to approach repeatedly: Desid. -जिगमिषति, to be<BR>about to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग|आगः
2. आ-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, accidental; happening acci-<BR>dentally.<BR>—आग-त्व, अम्, n. accident, chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत|आगतं
आ-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, come, arrived; occurred, hap-<BR>pened; living or residing in; returned; fallen to one's<BR>share; fallen into; received, obtained; passed; (अम्),<BR>n. occurrence, event [cf. अन्-आगत, स्व्-आगत].<BR>—आगत-क्षोभ, अस्, आ, अम्, confounded, perplexed.<BR>—आगत-साध्वस, अस्, आ, अम्, terrified, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगति|आगतिः
आ-गति, इस्, f. arrival, coming; return; origin; ac-<BR>cident, chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत्य
आ-गत्य, ind. having come, having arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तव्य|आगंतव्य
आ-गन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be arrived, what is<BR>likely to arrive; to be come to (with acc. or loc.<BR>of the place); obliged to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तु|आगंतु|आगन्तुः
आ-गन्तु, उस्, उस्, उ, coming, arriving; what is<BR>added, adhering; coming from the outside, external;<BR>adventitious, incidental; (उस्), m. a new comer, a<BR>stranger, a guest; an accident, any accidental hurt or<BR>wound<BR>—आगन्तु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, arising accidentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुक|आगंतुक|आगन्तुकं
आगन्तुक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, coming, arriving; ar-<BR>riving of one's own accord; stray; incidental, acci-<BR>dental, adventitious (as pleasure, pain, ornament, &c.);<BR>(अस्), m. a new comer, a stranger, a guest; an inter-<BR>polated पाठ or various reading (which has crept<BR>in without authority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम|आगमं|आगमः
आ-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, coming near, approaching,<BR>supplying; (अस्), m. arrival, appearance; coming,<BR>approach; addition; course; the mouth of a river;<BR>supply of money, income, revenue; increase of pro-<BR>perty (especially in the compound अर्थागम), lawful<BR>acquisition of anything; increase of knowledge (espe-<BR>cially in the compound विद्यागम); knowledge,<BR>science, intelligence; a traditional doctrine or precept,<BR>a collection of such doctrines or precepts, a sacred<BR>work, scripture; a manual; an affix; the interpola-<BR>tion of a letter in grammar, a grammatical augment,<BR>a meaningless syllable or letter inserted in any part of<BR>the radical word; record, title-deed, legal title, a<BR>voucher or written testimony; (अम्), n. a Tantra or<BR>any work inculcating the mystical worship of Śiva<BR>and Śakti.<BR>—आगम-निरपेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, inde-<BR>pendent of a written voucher or title.<BR>—आगम-नीत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, studied, read, examined.<BR>—आगम-रहित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of a written title or a voucher;<BR>without a Śāstra.<BR>—आगम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having an<BR>augment or addition of any kind; having approached<BR>for sexual intercourse.<BR>—आगम-सापेक्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, with or supported by legal vouchers.<BR>—आगमा-<BR>पायिन् (˚म-अप्˚), ई, इनी, इ, transient, of short dura-<BR>tion.<BR>—आगमावर्ता (˚म-आव्˚), f., N. of the plant<BR>Tragia Involucrata Lin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमन|आगमनं
आ-गमन, अम्, n. coming, approaching, arriving;<BR>returning; arising; approaching a woman for sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>—आगमन-कारण, अम्, n. reason of<BR>one's coming.<BR>—आगमन-तस्, ind. on account of<BR>an arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमय्य
आ-गमय्य, ind. having explored or discovered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमित|आगमितं
आ-गमित, अस्, आ, अम्, read over, perused, studied;<BR>understood, ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमिन्
आगमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (in gram.) receiving an augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमिष्ठ
आ-गमिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl.), Ved. coming<BR>with pleasure or very quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्य
1. आ-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be approached, accessi-<BR>ble; to be acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्य
2. आ-गम्य, ind. having arrived or come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगान्तु|आगान्तुः
आ-गान्तु, उस्, m. a guest. See आ-गन्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिक
आगामिक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to the<BR>future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिन्
आ-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, coming, about to come, ar-<BR>riving, impending; future.<BR>—आगामि-काल, अस्, m.<BR>future time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामुक
आ-गामुक, अस्, आ, अम्, coming, arriving; future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगर|आगरः
आगर आगर, Ved. = आ-गार (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगलित
आगलित आ-गलित, अस्, आ, अम्, drooping,<BR>languishing, dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगविष्ठ
आगविष्ठ आ-गविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (either a<BR>false reading for आ-गमिष्ठ or fr. an adj. आ-गु),<BR>Ved. coming near (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगवीन
आगवीन आ-गवीन, अस्, आ, अम्, occupied with<BR>any business till the return of the cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस् आगस्, अस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. इ with<BR>आग substituted), transgression, offence, sin, fault [cf.<BR>Gr. ἄγος].<BR>—आगस्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, offending;<BR>offended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्य|आगस्त्यः
आगस्त्य आगस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, referring to the<BR>sage Agasti, q. v.; originating from the plant Agasti<BR>Grandiflorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्तीय
आगस्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or tending to the<BR>advantage of Agasti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगा
आगा 1. आ-गा, cl. 2. P. -गाति, -तुम्, to come<BR>towards or into; to approach, make one's appearance;<BR>to meet with; to visit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगा
2. आ-गा, आस्, आस्, अम्, coming towards, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगाध|आगाधं
आगाध आगाध = अ-गाध, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगार|आगारं
आगार आ-गार, अम्, n. (probably fr. आ-गॄ,<BR>‘to swallow down,’ and denoting first any inner re-<BR>ceptacle), room, covered place, dwelling, house, recep-<BR>tacle [cf. अ-गार].<BR>—आगार-गोधिका, f. a lizard (?).<BR>—आगार-दाह, अस्, m. arson, setting a house on<BR>fire.<BR>—आगार-दाहिन्, ई, m. an incendiary.<BR>—आगार-<BR>धूम, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगुर् 1. आ-गुर्, cl. 6. A. -गुरते, -रितुम्<BR>(गुर् = rt. गॄ, see आ-गॄ), to approve, to agree or<BR>assent to, to promise, to pronounce the Āgur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
2. आ-गुर्, ऊर्, f., Ved., N. of a class of plauditory or<BR>approving exclamations or formularies used by the<BR>priests in sacrificial rites; assent, an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरण|आगुरणं
आ-गुरण or आ-गूरण or आ-गूर्ण, अम्, n. recita-<BR>tion of the Āgur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगू
आ-गू, ऊस्, f. an agreement (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्तिन्|आगूर्त्तिन्
आ-गूर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. performing or pronounc-<BR>ing the Āgur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरव
आगुरव आगुरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-गुरु),<BR>originating from or formed of Agallochum. See<BR>अ-गुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगॄ
आगॄ आ-गॄ, cl. 9. P. A., Ved. -गृणाति, -णीते,<BR>-गरितुम् or -रीतुम्, to approve, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगै
आगै आ-गै, cl. 1. P., Ved. -गायति, -गातुम्,<BR>to sing to, to obtain by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगातृ
आ-गातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, obtaining by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगान|आगानं
आ-गान, अम्, n. the act of obtaining by song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नापौष्ण
आग्नापौष्ण आग्नापौष्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>belonging or referring to Agni and Pūṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नावैष्णव
आग्नावैष्णव, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. belonging or<BR>referring to Agni and Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निक
आग्निक आग्निक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अग्नि), fiery,<BR>belonging to fire or to a sacrifice performed with fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निमारुत
आग्निमारुत, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or referring to<BR>Agni and the Maruts; (अस्), m. an epithet of Agastya;<BR>(अम्), n. a hymn praising Agni and the Maruts [cf.<BR>Pāṇini VII. 3, 21; VI. 3, 28].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निवारुण
आग्निवारुण, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or referring to<BR>Agni and Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निवेश्य
आग्निवेश्य and आग्निवेश्यायन, अस्, m., N. of<BR>two teachers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निष्टोमिक
आग्निष्टोमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the Ag-<BR>niṣṭoma; one who recites or is conversant with the<BR>Agniṣṭoma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निहोत्र
आग्निहोत्र, अस्, ई, अम्, fit for the Agnihotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं|आग्नीध्रः
आग्नीध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. originating from or<BR>belonging to the Agnīdh, i. e. to the priest who kindles<BR>the fire; (अस्), m. the priest who kindles the fire;<BR>(आ), f. care of the sacred fire; (अम्), n. the place<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">Page0114-a+ 76</a>]<BR>where a sacrificial fire is kindled; the function of the<BR>priest who kindles the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रीय|आग्नीध्रीयः
आग्नीध्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, being within the Āgnī-<BR>dhra or the place where a sacrificial fire is kindled;<BR>(अस्), m. the fire (अग्नि) within the Āgnīdhra; the<BR>fire-place (धिष्ण्य) within the Āgnīdhra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र्य
आग्नीध्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Āgnīdhra<BR>or the priest who kindles the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेन्द्र|आग्नेंद्र
आग्नेन्द्र, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. consecrated to Agni<BR>and Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेय|आग्नेयं|आग्नेयः
आग्नेय, अस्, ई, अम्, fiery, belonging or relating or<BR>consecrated to fire or its deity Agni; similar to fire or<BR>Agni; belonging to Agnāyī, wife of Agni; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Skanda; of Agastya; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (ई), f., N. of Agnāyī, wife of Agni; the wife of<BR>Ūru and daughter of Agni (?); the south-east quarter,<BR>of which Agni is the regent; (अम्), n. blood; ghee<BR>or boiled butter; gold; N. of a region.<BR>—आग्नेय-<BR>कीट, अस्, m. an insect (कीट) which flies into the fire<BR>(applied to a thief who breaks into a room and<BR>extinguishes the lamp).<BR>—आग्नेय-पुराण, अम्, n.<BR>the same as the अग्नि-पुराण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्न्याधेयिक
आग्न्याधेयिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Agny-<BR>ādheya. See under अग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रन्थ्
आग्रन्थ् आ-ग्रन्थ्, cl. 9. 1. P. -ग्रथ्नाति,<BR>-ग्रन्थति, -थितुम्, to wind round, to intwine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रभोजनिक|आग्रभोजनिकः
आग्रभोजनिक आग्रभोजनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अग्र-भोजन), one to whom food is first offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयण|आग्रयणं|आग्रयणः
आग्रयण आग्रयण, अस्, m. (fr. अग्र), the<BR>first Soma libation at the Agniṣṭoma sacrifice (see<BR>ग्रह); a form of Agni; (ई), f. an oblation consisting<BR>of first-fruits or firstling; (अम्), n. oblation consisting<BR>of first-fruits at the end of the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रस्त
आग्रस्त आ-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bored, per-<BR>forated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह्
आग्रह् आ-ग्रह्, Ved. -ग्रभ्, cl. 9. P. A.<BR>-गृह्णाति, -णीते, Ved. -गृभ्णाति, -णीते, -ग्रही-<BR>तुम्, to seize, take hold of; to draw tight (as reins).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह|आग्रहः
आ-ग्रह, अस्, m. seizing, taking; attack; surpass-<BR>ing, surmounting; favour; patronage; power, ability;<BR>moral power, courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहिका
आग्रहिका, f. favour, patronage, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहयण
आग्रहयण आग्रहयण, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging<BR>to the month Agra-hayaṇa (= अग्र-हायण, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायण|आग्रहायणः
आग्रहायण, अस्, m. ‘commencement of the year,’<BR>N. of a Hindū month commencing about the 12th<BR>of November, see अग्र-हायण; (ई), f. the day of<BR>full moon (पौर्णमासी) in the month Agra-hāyaṇa;<BR>a particular kind of Pāka-yajña, q. v.; N. of a con-<BR>stellation consisting of three stars, one of which is λ<BR>Orionis, figured by an antelope's head, hence also<BR>called Mṛga-śiras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणक|आग्रहायणकः
आग्रहायणक, अस्, ई, अम्, to be paid (as a debt<BR>&c.) on the day of full moon in the month Agra-<BR>hāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणिक|आग्रहायणिकः
आग्रहायणिक, अस्, m. the month Agra-hāyaṇa;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), to be paid on the day of full moon in<BR>the month Agra-hāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहारिक
आग्रहारिक आग्रहारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who<BR>appropriates to himself an Agra-hāra, viz. an endow-<BR>ment of lands or villages conferred upon Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रायण
आग्रायण आग्रायण, अस्, m., N. of a gram-<BR>marian; a sacrifice offered when the new rice or wheat<BR>ripens; (see आग्रयण, which is the correct reading.)<BR>—आग्रायणेष्टि (˚ण-इष्˚), इस्, f. the ceremony<BR>Āgrāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टक|आघट्टकः
आघट्टक आ-घट्टक, अस्, m. (rt. घट्ट् or<BR>घट्), a rubber; anything which causes friction;<BR>the plant Desmochæta Atropurpurea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टन
आ-घट्टन, अम्, n. friction, rubbing, contact,<BR>shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघट्टित
अ-घट्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed, touched, shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाट|आघाटः
आ-घाट, अस्, m., Ved. a musical instrument used<BR>for accompanying a dance; a cymbal or rattle; boun-<BR>dary, limit; the plant Achyranthes Aspera; (at the<BR>end of some compounds) = आ-घात, see next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाटि|आघाटिः
आ-घाटि, इस्, इस्, m. f, Ved. a musical instrument<BR>which sounds on being shaken, a cymbal or rattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्ष|आघर्षः
आघर्ष आ-घर्ष, अस्, m. (rt. घृष्),<BR>rubbing, friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षण|आघर्षणं
आ-घर्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, scratching, rubbing;<BR>(अम्), n. rubbing, friction; (ई), f. a brush, a rubber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षित
आ-घर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed, brushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघात|आघातः
आघात आ-घात, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हन् with आ),<BR>striking, a blow, a wound; killing; a beater, striker;<BR>retention of urine; misfortune, pain; a slaughter-house,<BR>a place for killing animals or victims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातन|आघातनं
आ-घातन, अम्, n. striking, killing; a slaughter-<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्नत्
आ-घ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, striking, beating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघार|आघारः
आघार आ-घार. See under आ-घृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघुष्
आघुष् आ-घुष्, cl. 1. P. -घोषति, -घो-<BR>षितुम्, to make one's self audible; to cry aloud, to<BR>proclaim; to praise; to listen to: Caus. -घोषयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to make a noise, to cause to sound; to pro-<BR>claim or cause to proclaim aloud; to complain con-<BR>tinually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोष|आघोषः
आ-घोष, अस्, m. calling out to, invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषण|आघोषणं
आ-घोषण, अम्, आ, n. f. a crying or proclaiming,<BR>public announcement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्ण्
आघूर्ण् आ-घूर्ण्, cl. 6. P., 1. A. -घूर्णति,<BR>-घूर्णते, -णितुम्, to fluctuate, stagger; to roll,<BR>whirl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णन|आघूर्णनं
आ-घूर्णन, अम्, n. rolling, tossing; fluctuating,<BR>whirling round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णित|आघूर्णितं
आ-घूर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, rolled, rolling; whirled<BR>round, fluctuating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृ
आघृ आ-घृ, cl. 1., and Ved. cl. 3. P.<BR>-घरति, -जिघर्ति, -घर्तुम्, to sprinkle towards<BR>or upon: Caus. -घारयति, -यितुम्, to sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघार|आघारः
आ-घार, अस्, m. sprinkling, sprinkling clarified<BR>butter upon the fire at certain sacrifices; ghee or<BR>clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृणि|आघृणिः
आघृणि आ-घृणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. glowing<BR>with heat; endowed with splendor^1; epithet of the<BR>god Pūṣan.<BR>—आघृणी-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. rich<BR>with heat, epithet of Agni; (Sāy.) having splendid<BR>wealth.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रा
आघ्रा आ-घ्रा, cl. 1. P. -जिघ्रति, -घ्रातुम्,<BR>to smell, smell at; to kiss: Caus. -घ्रापयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause to smell at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राण|आघ्राणं
आ-घ्राण, अम्, n. smelling; satisfaction, satiety;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), satisfied, satiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रात|आघ्रातः
आ-घ्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, smelled, scented; satisfied,<BR>satiated; surmounted, surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रेय
आ-घ्रेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smelled at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्कुशायन
आङ्कुशायन आङ्कुशायन, adj. formed fr.<BR>अङ्कुश. See Gaṇa to Pāṇini IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्कृति|आंकृति
आङ्कृति आङ्कृति, इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्क्षी|आंक्षी
आङ्क्षी आङ्क्षी, f. a musical instrument, a<BR>tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग|आंग|आङ्गं|आङ्गः
आङ्ग आङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. अङ्ग), re-<BR>lating to the base (अङ्ग), of a word in grammar;<BR>bodily, corporeal; having limbs or parts or relating<BR>to them; relating to the inferior persons of a drama,<BR>to a portion of the Vedas, &c.; (अम्), n. a soft deli-<BR>cate form or body; (अस्, ई, अम्, pl. ăङ्गास्), produced or<BR>born in the country Aṅga; a prince of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गक|आंगक|आङ्गकः
आङ्गक, अस्, m. the ruler of the country Aṅga;<BR>an inhabitant of the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गविद्य|आंगविद्य
आङ्गविद्य, अस्, ई, अम्, occurring in or being fami-<BR>liar with chiromancy or the knowledge of lucky and<BR>unlucky marks on the body. See अङ्ग-विद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिक|आंगिक|आङ्गिकः
आङ्गिक, अस्, ई, अम्, bodily, corporeal; gesticulated,<BR>expressed by bodily action (dramatic sentiment, pas-<BR>sion &c., exhibited by attitude, gesture &c.); (अस्),<BR>m. a player on a tabor or drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गदी
आङ्गदी आङ्गदी, f., N. of the capital of<BR>Aṅgada's kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गार|आंगार|आंगारं|आङ्गारं
आङ्गार आङ्गार, अम्, n. (fr. अङ्गार), a mul-<BR>titude of firebrands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरस|आंगिरस|आङ्गिरसः
आङ्गिरस आङ्गिरस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अङ्गिरस्),<BR>descended from or belonging to or referring to the<BR>Aṅgirasas or to Aṅgiras; (अस्), m. a descendant of<BR>Aṅgiras; especially a N. of Vṛhaspati, the preceptor<BR>of the gods; a Kṣatriya by will of Brahmā and by<BR>profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गुलिक
आङ्गुलिक आङ्गुलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अङ्गुलि,<BR>q. v.), like a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गूष|आंगूषः|आङ्गूषः
आङ्गूष आङ्गूष, अस्, m., Ved. praising aloud,<BR>a hymn [cf. अङ्गूष, अङ्गोषिन्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गूष्य
आङ्गूष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praising aloud, sound-<BR>ing; fit for praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गेयी
आङ्गेयी आङ्गेयी probably = आङ्गी. See<BR>आङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग्य
आङ्ग्य, adj. fr. अङ्ग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच
आच 1. आच, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच
आच 2. आच, in the words आच-पराच and<BR>आचोपच, ‘turned towards and away from’ (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्ष्
आचक्ष् आ-चक्ष्, cl. 2. A. -चष्टे, -ष्टुम्, to<BR>look at, inspect; to tell, relate, make a communication<BR>about anything (with acc.); to announce, declare; to<BR>make known, confess; to acquaint, introduce to; to<BR>address any one (with acc.); to call, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षमाण
आ-चक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, saying, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षुस्
आ-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. a learned man, a Paṇḍit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचतुरम्
आचतुरम् आ-चतुरम्, ind. till the fourth<BR>generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचतुर्य|आचतुर्य्य
आचतुर्य आचतुर्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-चतुर),<BR>clumsiness, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम्
आचम् आ-चम्, cl. 1. P. -चामति, -चमितुम्,<BR>to sip; to rinse the mouth (with inst. of the thing);<BR>to lap up, lick up, to cause to disappear (as the wind<BR>licks up moisture): Caus. -चामयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to sip water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम|आचमः
आ-चम, अस्, m. rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमन|आचमनं
आ-चमन, अम्, n. rinsing the mouth, sipping<BR>water (before religious ceremonies, before meals &c.,<BR>from the palm of the hand. It is usual to spit the<BR>water out again; the ceremony also includes touching<BR>the body in various parts); gargling the throat; the<BR>water used for rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनक|आचमनकं|आचमनकः
आ-चमनक, अस्, m. a spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीय|आचमनीयं
आचमनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, used for rinsing the<BR>mouth; (अम्), n. water for rinsing the mouth, a<BR>gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम्य
आ-चम्य, ind. having rinsed the mouth, having<BR>sipped and ejected a little water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचान्त|आचांत|आचान्तः
आ-चान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sipped and ejected (as water);<BR>one who has rinsed his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम|आचामः
आ-चाम, अस्, m. sipping water, rinsing the mouth;<BR>the water or foam of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामक
आ-चामक, अस्, आ, अम्, rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामनक|आचामनकं
आ-चामनक, अस्, m. a spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम्य
आ-चाम्य, अम्, n. rinsing the mouth, water so<BR>used, a gargle; (अस्, आ, अम्), to be rinsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचय|आचयः
आचय आ-चय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. चि with आ),<BR>collection, plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचयक
आचयक, अस्, आ, अम्, collecting, skilful in col-<BR>lecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्
आचर् आ-चर्, cl. 1. P. ep. A. -चरति, -ते,<BR>-रितुम्, Ved. -रध्यै, -रितवे, -रसे, to come near<BR>to, approach; to step upon, pass through; to pro-<BR>ceed, manage, behave one's self towards (with loc.);<BR>to treat; to have intercourse with, frequent; to act,<BR>undertake, do, exercise, practice, perform; to devour,<BR>eat into; to help forward, put into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण|आचरणं
आ-चरण, अम्, n. approaching, arrival; following,<BR>observing, conduct, usage, practice; an institute, rite<BR>or rule of conduct; a cart, carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणीय
आ-चरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done or performed;<BR>to be followed or observed, right, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरत्
आ-चरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, following, practising, ob-<BR>serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरित|आचरितं
आ-चरित, अस्, आ, अम्, observed, practised, as a rite<BR>or usage; usual, customary; enjoined, fixed by rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरितव्य
आ-चरितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be performed in a<BR>customary manner; to be done or performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्य|आचर्य्य
आ-चर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone to or approached;<BR>to be done or performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार|आचारः
आ-चार, अस्, m. conduct, manner of action; beha-<BR>viour; good conduct, good behaviour; custom, prac-<BR>tice, usage; an established rule of conduct, an ordi-<BR>nance, an institute, a precept; manner of conducting<BR>one's self, diet; rule; [cf. Hib. acara, ‘convenience,<BR>conveniency, use.’]<BR>—आचार-चन्द्रिका, f. title of a<BR>work on the religious customs of the Śūdras.<BR>—आचार-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n. one of the four classes of Tantras<BR>with Buddhists.<BR>—आचार-दीप, अस्, m. ‘lamp of re-<BR>ligious customs,’ title of a work.<BR>—आचार-भ्रष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from established usage, apostate.<BR>—आचार-मयूख, अस्, m. ‘ray of religious cus-<BR>toms,’ title of a work.<BR>—आचार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, well-<BR>conducted, virtuous.<BR>—आचार-वरिजित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>irregular, out of rule; outcast.<BR>—आचार-विरुद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, contrary to custom.<BR>—आचार-वेदी, f.<BR>‘altar of religious customs,’ a N. of Āryāvarta.<BR>—आ-<BR>चार-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of established ordi-<BR>nances, outcast.<BR>—आचाराङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अम्, n. title<BR>of the first of the twelve sacred books of the Jainas.<BR>—आचारादर्श (˚र-आद्˚), अस्, m. ‘looking-glass<BR>of religious customs,’ title of a work.<BR>—आचारार्क<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘sun of religious customs,’ title of<BR>a work.<BR>—आचारोल्लास (˚र-उल्ल्˚), अस्, m. ‘light of<BR>religious customs,’ title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिक
आचारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, conformable to rule or prac-<BR>tice, prescriptive, authorized; (अम्), n. rules for the<BR>preservation of health, habit of life, regimen, diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिन्
आचारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, following established rites or<BR>practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारी
आ-चारी, f. the plant Hingtsha Repens, also called<BR>Hilamocikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य|आचार्यः|आचार्य्य|आचार्य्यः
आ-चार्य, अस्, m. lit. ‘one to whom one must have<BR>recourse’ or ‘one who is to be attended to or waited<BR>on’ or ‘one whose precepts are to be followed’ or<BR>‘one who knows the आचार or rules;’ a spiritual guide<BR>or teacher, especially one who invests the student<BR>with the sacrificial thread, and instructs him in the<BR>Vedas, in the law of sacrifice and religious mysteries<BR>(Manu 2. 140, 171); an epithet of Droṇa the teacher<BR>of the Pāṇḍus; (आ), f. a spiritual preceptress. The<BR>title आचार्य affixed to names of learned men is<BR>rather like our Dr.; e. g. राघवाचार्य, &c.<BR>—आचार्य-करण, अम्, n. acting as teacher.<BR>—आ-<BR>चार्य-ता, f. or आचार्य-त्व, अम्, n. the office or pro-<BR>ficiency of a holy teacher.<BR>—आचार्य-देव, अस्, m.<BR>one whose preceptor is his god.<BR>—आचार्य-भो-<BR>गीन, अस्, आ, अम्, delighting the holy teacher.<BR>—आचार्य-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, venerable, honourable.<BR>—आचार्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has a teacher.<BR>—आचार्योपासन (˚य-उप्˚), अम्, n. waiting upon<BR>or serving the spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यक|आचार्य्यक
आचार्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, originating from a spiritual<BR>teacher; (अम्), n. the proficiency of a holy teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यानी
आचार्यानी, f. (with dental न्, Pāṇini IV. 1, 49.<BR>Vārt. 6), the wife of an Ācārya or holy teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचीर्ण
आ-चीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (anom. past pass. part.), de-<BR>voured, eaten into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण्य
आचरण्य आ-चरण्य (nom. fr. चरण), P.<BR>-चरण्यति, -यितुम्, to move one's self, to move or<BR>extend towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचल्
आचल् आ-चल्, Caus. P. -चालयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>move, draw away from one's place, stir up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचान्त|आचांत|आचान्तः
आचान्त, आचाम। See under आ-चम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचि
आचि आ-चि, cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति, -नुते, -चेतुम्,<BR>to accumulate; to collect; to heap up, load with;<BR>to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित|आचितं|आचितः
आ-चित, अस्, आ, अम्, collected, accumulated, heaped;<BR>filled, loaded with, covered; spread, diffused; inlaid,<BR>set (e. g. अर्धाचिता रसना, a girdle half set with<BR>gems); larded; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a cart-load; a mea-<BR>sure of ten bhāras or cart-loads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितिक
आचितिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or आचितीन, अस्, आ, अम्, holding<BR>or being equal to or cooking a quantity equal to the<BR>preceding measure; (a numeral may be placed be-<BR>fore these forms, e. g. द्व्याचितिक, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचिख्यासा
आचिख्यासा आ-चिख्यासा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>ख्या with आ), desire or intention of expressing or<BR>denoting something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित्
आचित् 1. आ-चित्, cl. 1. 3. P. -चेतति, -चिकेत्ति,<BR>A. -चिकिते, -चेत्तुम्, to attend to, to keep in mind;<BR>to comprehend, understand, know; to invent; to ap-<BR>pear, become visible, distinguish one's self: Desid.<BR>-चिकित्सति, -ते, to wait for, watch clandestinely, lurk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित्
2. आ-चित्, त्, f., Ved. taking notice or cognizance,<BR>attention to; (according to Sāy. the form आ-चिता may<BR>stand for आ-चिते fr. आ-चित above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचीर्ण
आचीर्ण आ-चीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्. See under<BR>आ-चर् last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचूषण|आचूषणं
आचूषण आ-चूषण, अम्, n. suction; suck-<BR>ing out; application of cupping-glasses to the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचृत्
आचृत् आ-चृत्, cl. 6. P. -चृतति, -चर्तितुम्,<BR>to fasten, tie, affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचेश्वर
आचेश्वर आचेश्वर (˚च-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>sanctuary built by Āca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचेष्ट्
आचेष्ट् आ-चेष्ट्, cl. 1. P. A. -चेष्टति, -ते,<BR>-टितुम्, to undertake; to do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचोपच
आचोपच आचोपच. See 2. आच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छद्|आछद्
आच्छद् 1. आ-च्छद् (-छद्), cl. 10. P. -च्छ-<BR>दयति or -च्छादयति, -यितुम्, to cover, hide; to<BR>clothe, to dress, put on clothes; to conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छद्|आछद्
2. आ-च्छद्, त्, f., Ved. a cover, covering; a sheath.<BR>—आच्छद्-विधान, अम्, n., Ved. an arrangement<BR>made for defence, a means of covering; or (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>one who has such means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छन्न|आच्छन्नं
आ-च्छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, concealed, clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद|आच्छादः|आछाद
आ-च्छाद, अस्, m. cloth, clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादक
आ-च्छादक, अस्, आ, अम्, concealing, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादन|आच्छादनं|आछादन
आ-च्छादन, अम्, n. covering, concealing, hiding;<BR>disappearance; a covering, a sheath; cloth, clothes;<BR>mantle, cloak, &c.; the wooden frame of a roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादित|आच्छादितं
आ-च्छादित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादिन्
आ-च्छादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, covering, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद्य
1. आ-च्छाद्य, ind. having clothed or put on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद्य
2. आ-च्छाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be covered or clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाक|आच्छाकः
