आजयन|आजयनं
आ-जयन, अम्, n. conquering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिगीषु
आ-जिगीषु, उस्, उस्, उ, ambitious, wishing to excel<BR>or overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिग्रह
आजिग्रह आ-जिग्रह, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ग्रह्),<BR>who or what takes or seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिज्ञासेन्य
आजिज्ञासेन्य आ-जिज्ञासेन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>Desid. of rt. ज्ञा with आ), Ved. liable to investigation;<BR>(आस्), f. pl., N. of a short section of the Kuntāpa<BR>hymns in the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa; (the word ऋचस्<BR>must be supplied.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिहीर्षु
आजिहीर्षु आ-जिहीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid.<BR>of rt. हृ with आ), about to bring towards (with acc.);<BR>wishing to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीकूल
आजीकूल आजीकूल, N. of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीगर्ति|आजीगर्त्ति
आजीगर्ति आजीगर्ति, a patronymic fr. अजी-<BR>गर्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्
आजीव् आ-जीव्, cl. 1. P. -जीवति, -वितुम्, to<BR>live by; to have the use or enjoyment of; to subsist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव|आजीवः
आ-जीव, अस्, m. livelihood, subsistence; a Jaina<BR>beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवक|आजीवकः
आ-जीवक, अस्, m. a beggar, one who obtains his<BR>livelihood everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवन|आजीवनं
आ-जीवन, अम्, n. livelihood, subsistence.<BR>—आजीव-<BR>नार्थ (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m. (अम्, n. ?) means of live-<BR>lihood or subsistence, business, profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीविन्
आ-जीविन्, ई, m. having a livelihood; a peculiar kind<BR>of beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्य
आ-जीव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be practised as a means of<BR>living; fit for or affording a livelihood; habitable,<BR>fertile; fruitful; (अम्), n. means of living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजुर्
आजुर् आ-जुर्, ऊर्, f. or आ-जू, ऊस्, f. (fr. rt. जॄ<BR>with आ ?), unpaid labour, working without wages;<BR>consigning to hell; infirm age (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
आज्ञा 1. आ-ज्ञा, cl. 9. P. -जानाति, -ज्ञातुम्,<BR>to know, understand, learn, obtain information, ascer-<BR>tain, notice, perceive: Caus. -ज्ञापयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>publish, order, command, direct; to assure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्त|आज्ञप्तः
आ-ज्ञप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ordered, commanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्ति|आज्ञप्तिः
आ-ज्ञप्ति, इस्, f. order, injunction, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
2. आ-ज्ञा, f. an order, a command; allowance, per-<BR>mission; [cf. Hib. agna, ‘wisdom.’]<BR>—आज्ञा-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, executing an order, obeying, obedient;<BR>(अस्), m. a servant.<BR>—आज्ञा-करण, अम्, n. execu-<BR>tion of orders, obedience.<BR>—आज्ञाकर-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the office of a servant.<BR>—आज्ञा-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>one who obeys or executes orders, obedient, minis-<BR>trant.<BR>—आज्ञा-चक्र, अम्, n. a mystical circle or dia-<BR>gram, one of six described by the Tantras.<BR>—आज्ञा-<BR>नुयायिन् or आज्ञानुवर्तिन् (˚ज्ञा-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>obeying or executing orders, obedient.<BR>—आज्ञानु-<BR>सारिन् (˚ज्ञा-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, executing orders, obe-<BR>dient.<BR>—आज्ञा-पत्त्र, अम्, n. an edict, written<BR>order.<BR>—आज्ञा-प्रतिघात अस्, m. disobedience, re-<BR>bellion.<BR>—आज्ञा-भङ्ग, अस्, m. disobedience, insub-<BR>ordination, disloyalty.<BR>—आज्ञा-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, obe-<BR>dient, subject, ministrant.<BR>—आज्ञा-सम्पादिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, executing an order, obedient, submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञात
आ-ज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, ordered, commanded; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of one of the first five pupils of Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञातृ
आ-ज्ञातृ, ता, m., Ved. one who orders or directs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञान|आज्ञानं
आ-ज्ञान, अम्, n. the act of noticing, perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापक|आज्ञापकः
आ-ज्ञापक, अस्, आ, अम्, giving orders, commanding,<BR>a commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापन|आज्ञापनं
आ-ज्ञापन, अम्, n. ordering, commanding, making<BR>known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापित
आ-ज्ञापित, अस्, आ, अम्, ordered, commanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाप्य
आ-ज्ञाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be directed or commanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञायिन्
आ-ज्ञायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, perceiving, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्य|आज्यं
आज्य आज्य, अम्, n. (fr. rt. अञ्ज् with आ),<BR>melted or clarified butter used for oblations, or for<BR>pouring into the holy fire at the sacrifice, or for<BR>anointing anything sacrificed or offered; (in a wider<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">Page0116-b+ 71</a>]<BR>sense) oil and milk used instead of clarified butter<BR>at a sacrifice; N. of a sort of chant or religious<BR>service; turpentine.<BR>—आज्य-प, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>drinking the clarified butter; (आस्), m. pl. a class of<BR>Manes who are the sons of Pulastya and the ancestors<BR>of the Vaiśya order.<BR>—आज्य-पात्र, अम्, n. a vessel<BR>or dish to hold clarified butter.<BR>—आज्य-भाग, अस्,<BR>m. a portion of clarified butter; (औ), m. du. the<BR>two portions of clarified butter belonging to Agni<BR>and Soma; (अस्, आ, अम्), partaking of the clarified<BR>butter; offering clarified butter at certain ceremonies.<BR>—आज्य-भुज्, क्, m. ‘consumer of clarified butter,’<BR>epithet of Agni.<BR>—आज्य-वारि, इस्, m. ‘sea of clarified<BR>butter,’ one of the seven seas.<BR>—आज्य-स्थाली, f.,<BR>see आज्य-पात्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्च्
आञ्च् आञ्च् (आ-अञ्च्), cl. 1. P. A. आञ्चति, -ते,<BR>-चितुम्, to bend, crook, curve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्चन|आंचनं
आञ्चन, अम्, n. partial extraction of thorns or<BR>arrows and the like from the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्छ्|आंछ्
आञ्छ् आञ्छ्, cl. 1. P. आञ्छति, आञ्छ or<BR>आनाञ्छ, आञ्छितुम्, to make straight;<BR>to lengthen or stretch; to regulate, draw into the<BR>right position; to set (a bone or leg).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्छन|आंछनं
आञ्छन, अम्, n. setting (a bone or leg), bringing<BR>back into the right place by stretching, bending, or<BR>drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्ज्
आञ्ज् आञ्ज् (आ-अञ्ज्), cl. 7. P. आनक्ति, आञ्जि-<BR>तुम् or आङ्क्तुम्, to anoint; to smooth, polish, pre-<BR>pare; to honour, receive respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जन|आंजन|आञ्जनः
आञ्जन, अम्, ई, n. f. ointment, especially for the<BR>eyes; fat.<BR>—आञ्जनाभ्यञ्जनीय (˚न-अभ्य्˚), अम्,<BR>आ, n. f., N. of a certain ceremony.<BR>—आञ्जनी-कारी, f.<BR>a woman who anoints or makes ointments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनेय|आंजनेयः|आञ्जनेयः
आञ्जनेय आञ्जनेय, अस्, m. (fr. अञ्जना, his<BR>mother), N. of the monkey Hanumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जलिक्य|आंजलिक्यं
आञ्जलिक्य आञ्जलिक्य (fr. अञ्जलिक). See<BR>Gaṇa to Pāṇini V. 1. 128.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जिक
आञ्जिक आञ्जिक, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जिनेय|आंजिनेयः|आञ्जिनेयः
आञ्जिनेय आञ्जिनेय, अस्, m. an insect, a kind<BR>of lizard, Lacerta Unjinensis. See अञ्जन and अञ्-<BR>जनिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आट
आट आट, अस्, m., N. of a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटरूष|आटरूषः
आटरूष आटरूष, अस्, m., N. of the tree<BR>Justicia Adhenatoda. See अटरूष or अटरूषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटविक|आटविकः
आटविक आटविक, अस्, m. (fr. अटवी), the<BR>inhabitant of a forest; a woodman, a pioneer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटवी
आटवी, f., N. of a town in the Mahā-bhārata (2.<BR>1175).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटव्य
आटव्य आटव्य, अस्, m., N. of a teacher in<BR>the Vāyu-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटि|आटिः
आटि आटि, इस्, f. (rt. अट्, to wander), N. of<BR>the bird Turdus Ginginianus [cf. आडि and आति].<BR>—आटी-मुख, अस् or अम् ?, m. or n. ? a surgical in-<BR>strument employed in blood-letting, the top of which<BR>is like the beak of the bird आटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिक
आटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, able to wander; (ई), f., N. of<BR>the wife of Uṣasti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिक्य
आटिक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being on a voyage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकन|आटीकनं
आटीकन आ-टीकन or आ-टीलक, अम्, n. (fr. rt.<BR>टीक् with आ), the leaping motion of a calf [cf. आढी-<BR>लक and आलीढक].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिकर
आ-टिकर, अस्, m. a bull (etym. probably the same<BR>as the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटोप|आटोपः
आटोप आटोप, अस्, m. (said to be fr. a<BR>Sautra rt. टुप् with आ), puffing, swelling; flatulence,<BR>borborygmi; pride, self-conceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आट्टस्थलक
आट्टस्थलक आट्टस्थलक (fr. अट्ट-स्थली)<BR>Gaṇa to Pāṇini IV. 2, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आट्णार
आट्णार आट्णार, अस्, m. (fr. अट्णार), Ved.,<BR>N. of Para in the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>fond of wandering (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बर|आडंबरः|आडम्बरः
आडम्बर आडम्बर, अस्, m. (etym. doubtful,<BR>probably rt. डम्ब् with आ), a drum used in battle;<BR>charge sounded by musical instruments; the sounding<BR>of a trumpet as a sign of attack; the roaring of<BR>elephants; pride, arrogance (in this sense perhaps<BR>connected with संरम्भ?); commencement (in<BR>this sense perhaps connected with आरम्भ?); anger,<BR>passion; happiness, pleasure; the eyelid; (अम्), n.<BR>rubbing and kneading the body; (sometimes this<BR>word is written आडम्पर.)<BR>—आडम्बराघात<BR>(˚र-आघ्˚), अस्, m., Ved. one who beats a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बरिन्|आडंबरिन्
आडम्बरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, arrogant, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडि|आडिः
आडि आडि, इस्, f. a bird, the Śarāli (Turdus<BR>Ginginianus); a kind of fish. See आटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडु
आडु आडु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. अड्), striving to<BR>obtain anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडू
आडू आडू, ऊस्, m. (or f. ?) a raft, a float.<BR>See आतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढक|आढकं|आढकः
आढक आढक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (etym. doubt-<BR>ful), a measure of grain, the 4th of a droṇa and equal<BR>to 4 prasthas = 16 kuḍavas = 64 palas = 256 karṣas =<BR>4096 māṣas; or containing nearly 7 lbs. 11 ozs. avoir-<BR>dupois. In Bengal an आढक is equal to two mans or<BR>164 lbs. avds.; (ई), f. a kind of pulse, Cajanus Indicus<BR>Spreng.; a kind of fragrant earth.<BR>—आढक-जम्बु,<BR>N. of a country.<BR>—आढकजम्बुक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>relating to that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकिक|आढकिकः
आढकिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or आढकीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>holding or containing an āḍhaka; sown with an<BR>āḍhaka of seed, as a field &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढीलक
आढीलक आढीलक, a various reading for<BR>आ-टीलक. See आ-टीकन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्य|आढ्यः
आढ्य आढ्य, अस्, आ, अम् (etym. doubtful,<BR>perhaps for आर्ध्य fr. ऋध्), opulent, wealthy, rich;<BR>(with an inst. or as last member of a comp.) rich in,<BR>abounding in, productive; possessing abundantly; mixed<BR>with, watered with; abundant, existing in abundance.<BR>—आढ्यकुलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, descended from a rich<BR>family.<BR>—आढ्यङ्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, enriching;<BR>(अम्), n. the means of enriching, wealth, prosperity.<BR>—आढ्य-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, once opulent (?).<BR>—आढ्य-<BR>ता, f. opulence, wealth.<BR>—आढ्यम्-भविष्णु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, or आढ्यम्-भावुक, अस्, ई, अम्, becoming<BR>rich or eminent.<BR>—आढ्य-वात, अस्, m. (abundant<BR>wind), a convulsive or rheumatic palsy of the loins.<BR>—आढ्याडु (˚ढ्य-आडु), उस्, उस्, उ, striving to get<BR>wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यक
आढ्यक, अम्, n. wealth, opulence, abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणक|आणकः
आणक आणक, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. अणु, q. v.), low,<BR>inferior. See अणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणव
आणव, अम्, n. exceeding smallness; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>very small, fine (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणवीन|आणवीनं
आणवीन, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing or fit to bear Pani-<BR>cum Miliaceum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणि|आणिः
आणि आणि, इस्, m. f. [cf. अणि], the pin of the<BR>axle of a cart, the linch-pin; the part of the leg just<BR>above the knee; the corner of a house; a limit, a<BR>boundary; the edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्ड|आंड|आण्डः
आण्ड आण्ड, अम्, n. (fr. अण्ड, q. v.), an egg;<BR>a multitude of eggs, a brood; (औ), m. du., Ved. the<BR>testicles [cf. अण्ड].<BR>—आण्ड-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born from<BR>an egg.<BR>—आण्ड-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of eggs or<BR>testicles.<BR>—आण्डाद् (˚ड-अद्), त्, m., Ved. one who eats<BR>eggs, N. of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डी|आंडी
आण्डी, f., Ved. a testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डीक|आंडीक
आण्डीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bearing eggs, as a plant<BR>with egg-shaped fruits or bulbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डीर|आंडीर
आण्डीर, अस्, आ, अम्, having many eggs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्
आत् आत्, ind. (fr. 4. अ), Ved. afterwards,<BR>then; (in which senses it is often used in a concluding<BR>paragraph antithetically to यद्, यदा, यदि, being<BR>then sometimes strengthened by the particles अह, इद्,<BR>ईम्, उ; e. g. यदेद् अयुक्त हरितः सधस्थाद्<BR>आद् रात्री वासस् तनुते सिमस्मै, ‘at the very time<BR>when he has unyoked his coursers from his car, then<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">Page0117-a+ 76</a>]<BR>night extends the veiling darkness over all;’ वृत्रं<BR>यद् इन्द्र शवसावधीर् अहिम् आद् इत् सूर्यं<BR>दिव्य् आरोहयो दृशे, ‘when, O Indra, thou didst slay<BR>with thy power the dragon Vṛtra, then indeed thou<BR>didst raise the sun in the sky, that it might be seen.’<BR>In other passages आत् is simply used like a conjunc-<BR>tion, equivalent to ‘then, further, also, and.’ Sometimes<BR>it only serves to strengthen the meaning of another<BR>word, or to give emphasis to an interrogative pronoun,<BR>in the same way as उ, नु, अङ्ग, &c.; e. g. य एक<BR>इद् अप्रतिर् मन्यमान आद् अस्माद् अन्यो अज-<BR>निष्ट तव्यान्, ‘he who considered himself alone<BR>irresistible, another was born mightier even than he;’<BR>किम् आत् प्र ब्रवाम, ‘How can we at all pro-<BR>claim ?’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत|आतः
आत आत, अस्, आ, m. f. (fr. आ-तन् below ?),<BR>Ved. a scaffold; the frame of a door; (Sāy.) a quarter<BR>of the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतंस्
आतंस् आ-तंस्, Caus. A., Ved. -तंसयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to shake out; (Sāy) to decorate from all<BR>sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतक
आतक आतक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतक्ष्
आतक्ष् आ-तक्ष्, cl. 1. P. A., Ved. -तक्षति,<BR>-ते, -क्षितुम्, -तष्टुम्, to bring from all sides, to<BR>procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतञ्च्|आतंच्
आतञ्च् आ-तञ्च्, cl. 7. P. -तनक्ति, -तङ्क्तुम्<BR>or -तञ्चितुम्, to cause to shrink or contract, to<BR>coagulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतङ्क|आतंक|आतंकः|आतङ्कः
आ-तङ्क, अस्, m. (this word may also be connected<BR>with rt. तङ्क्, q. v.), disease or sickness of the body;<BR>pain or affliction of mind, disquietude, apprehension,<BR>fear; fever; the sound of a drum or tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतञ्चन|आतंचनं|आतञ्चनं
आ-तञ्चन, अम्, n. casting one thing into another<BR>to effect some change, as butter-milk into fresh milk<BR>to turn it; the act of causing to contract; that which<BR>causes coagulation; runnet; curdled milk; a sort of<BR>whey; calcining, adding a powder or flux to metals<BR>in fusion; the flux so used; casting away, destroying;<BR>danger, calamity (as a pestilence or epidemic); speed,<BR>velocity; gratifying, satisfying; making fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतड्
आतड् आ-तड्, cl. 10. P. -ताडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to thump, strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतन्
आतन् आ-तन्, cl. 8. P. -तनोति, -नितुम्, to<BR>extend over, stretch over, penetrate, to spread, over-<BR>spread; to illuminate; to take hold of, seek to attain,<BR>assume a (hostile) attitude; to stretch (as a bow for<BR>shooting); to diffuse; to bring to pass, effect: Caus.<BR>-तानयति, -यितुम्, to stretch (a bow); [cf. rt. ताय्,<BR>with which some of the following forms are connected.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतत
आ-तत, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, extended, stretched (as<BR>2 bow), &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिन्
आततायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one whose bow is stretched to<BR>take another's life; endeavouring to kill some one;<BR>2 felon, a thief, a murderer, incendiary, ravisher.<BR>—आततायि-ता, f. or आततायि-त्व, अम्, n. persecuting,<BR>murdering, destroying, stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतताविन्
आतता-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. one whose bow is<BR>stretched. See आततायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतन|आतनं
आ-तन, अम्, n. spreading, expanding; sight, view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतनि
आ-तनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. spreading, penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतान|आतानः
आ-तान, अस्, m., Ved. an extended cord, string, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतायिन्
आ-तायिन्, ई, m. a falcon, a kite. See आतापिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्
आतप् 1. आ-तप्, cl. 1. P. -तपति, -तप्तुम्,<BR>to radiate heat; to blaze, to heat; to cause to glow:<BR>Pass. -तप्यते, to suffer pain, be afflicted; to inflict<BR>(austerities) upon one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्
2. आ-तप्, प्, f., Ved. heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप|आतपः
आ-तप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing pain or affliction;<BR>(अस्), m. heat of the sun, sunshine.<BR>—आतप-त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a large umbrella of silk or leaves used in the East<BR>as a parasol.<BR>—आतपत्रक, अम्, n. a small um-<BR>brella, a mat or basket carried on the head as one.<BR>—आतप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, irradiated by the sun.<BR>—आतप-वर्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (water &c.)<BR>produced by rain during sunshine.<BR>—आतप-वारण,<BR>अम्, n. a parasol.<BR>—आतप-शुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, dried in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">Page0117-b+ 66</a>]<BR>the sun, evaporated by the solar heat.<BR>—आतपाभाव<BR>(˚प-अभ्˚), अस्, m. non-existence of sunshine, shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपन|आतपनः
आ-तपन, अस्, m. causing heat, an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपीय
आतपीय, अस्, आ, अम् (adj. fr. आ-तप), sunshiny (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्य
आतप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतम्
आतम् आ-तम्, cl. 4. P. -ताम्यति, -तमितुम्,<BR>to faint, to swoon, to become senseless; to despond,<BR>to languish, fade away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतमाम्
आतमाम् आ-तमाम् ? (a superlative form fr.<BR>3. आ ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर|आतरः
आतर आ-तर. See under आ-तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्ज्
आतर्ज् आ-तर्ज्, cl. 10. P. -तर्जयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to scold, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्दन|आतर्दनं
आतर्दन आ-तर्दन. See under आ-तृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्पण|आतर्पणं
आतर्पण आ-तर्पण. See under आ-तृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतव
आतव आतव, a proper N. (whence the<BR>patron. आतवायन Pāṇini IV. 1, 110. Gaṇa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतान|आतानः
आतान आ-तान. See under आ-तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिन्
आतापिन् आतापिन् or आतायिन्, ई, m., N. of the<BR>bird Falco Cheela. See under आ-तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतार|आतारः
आतार आ-तार, आ-तार्य. See under आ-तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आताली
आताली आताली, an indeclinable word com-<BR>pounded with अस्, भू, and कृ (see Pāṇini I. 4, 61).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आति|आतिः
आति आति, इस्, m. f. (fr. rt. अत्), Ved. a kind<BR>of water-bird; the bird Turdus Ginginianus (see<BR>आटि); going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेय|आतिथेयः
आतिथेय आतिथेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अतिथि, q. v.),<BR>proper for a guest, hospitable, attentive to a guest;<BR>(ई or अम्), f. n. hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं|आतिथ्यः
आतिथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper for a guest, hospitable,<BR>attentive to a guest; (अस्), m. a guest; (अम्), n. hos-<BR>pitable reception; hospitality; a particular rite, the<BR>reception of the Soma when it is brought to the<BR>place of sacrifice, also called आतिथ्येष्टि.<BR>—आतिथ्य-<BR>रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the place of the<BR>Ātithya rite.<BR>—आतिथ्य-सत्कार, अस्, m. the rites of<BR>hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिदेशिक
आतिदेशिक आतिदेशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (in gram.)<BR>connected with an अति-देश, q. v.; having reference to<BR>substitution or putting one thing for another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरश्चीन
आतिरश्चीन आ-तिरश्चीन, अस्, आ, अम्, a little<BR>transverse or across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरैक्य|आतिरैक्यं
आतिरैक्य आतिरैक्य, अम्, n. (fr. अति-रेक),<BR>superfluity, excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिविज्ञान्य
आतिविज्ञान्य आतिविज्ञान्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अति-<BR>विज्ञान), surpassing the perception or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिशय्य|आतिशय्यं
आतिशय्य आतिशय्य, अम्, n. (fr. अति-शय),<BR>excess, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिष्ठ|आतिष्ठं
आतिष्ठ आतिष्ठ, अम्, n. (fr. अति-ष्ठ), Ved.<BR>the being placed at the head of something, being a<BR>universal ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतु|आतुः
आतु आतु, उस्, m. (said to come fr. आ-तॄ<BR>next col.; but probably fr. rt. अत्), a raft, a float.<BR>See आडू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुच्
आतुच् आ-तुच्, क्, f., Ved. growing dusk,<BR>evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुज्
आतुज् 1. आ-तुज्, cl. 1. 6. P., Ved. -तोजति,<BR>-तुजति, -तोजितुम्, to bring near, to procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुज्
2. आ-तुज्, m. (Sāy.) destroyer of enemies, or giver<BR>of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुजि
आ-तुजि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. rushing on, hastening towards;<BR>carrying off (as booty), injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुद्
आतुद् आ-तुद्, cl. 6. P. A. -तुदति, -ते, -तोत्-<BR>तुम्, to strike, to push, spur on, stir up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोदिन्
आ-तोदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. striking, pushing, pricking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोद्य|आतोद्यं
आ-तोद्य, अम्, n. ‘to be struck,’ a musical instru-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर|आतुरः
आतुर आ-तुर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तुर्व् with आ),<BR>hurt, injured; suffering; sick in body or mind, dis-<BR>abled, diseased; feeble, weak, incapable of doing<BR>anything (with inf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुल्
आतुल् आ-तुल्, cl. 10. P. -तोलयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to lift up, raise, elevate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृद्
आतृद् आ-तृद्, cl. 7. P. -तृणत्ति, -तर्दितुम्,<BR>to split, sever, pierce; to push open, open; A.<BR>-तृन्ते, to become split or severed, to sever one's<BR>self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्दन|आतर्दनं
आ-तर्दन, अम्, n. pushing open, opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृण्ण
आ-तृण्ण, अम्, n. an opening, hole; an open<BR>wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्
आतृप् आ-तृप्, cl. 4. 5. 6. P. -तृप्यति,<BR>तृप्नोति, -तृम्पति, -तर्प्तुम् or -त्रप्तुम्, to be<BR>satisfied: Caus. -तर्पयति, -यितुम्, to satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्पण|आतर्पणं
आ-तर्पण, अम्, n. satisfying, gratification, satis-<BR>faction; whitening the wall, floor or seat on festive<BR>occasions; the pigment used for that purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्य|आतृप्यं|आतृप्यः
आ-तृप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfiable, to be satisfied;<BR>(अस्), m. the custard apple tree Annona Reticulata;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतॄ
आतॄ आ-तॄ, cl. 1. P., Ved. -तरति, -तरितुम्<BR>or -रीतुम्, to pass through or over; to cross over;<BR>to overcome; to enlarge, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर|आतरः
आ-तर, अस्, m. fare for being ferried over a river,<BR>passage money, freight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतार|आतारः
आ-तार, अस्, m. landing, coming to shore, fare,<BR>freight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतार्य
आ-तार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be crossed; (Ved.) land-<BR>ing, coming to shore, relating to landing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्त
आत्त आ-त्त, अस्, आ, अम् (contracted fr. आ-दत्त,<BR>part. pass. of आ-दा, q. v.), taken, accepted; assumed;<BR>attracted.<BR>—आत्त-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>smell is taken away, one who is throttled; hence one<BR>whose pride is humbled, insulted.<BR>—आत्त-गर्व, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, whose pride has been taken down, humiliated,<BR>degraded.<BR>—आत्त-मनस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, whose mind<BR>is transported or carried away (with joy).<BR>—आत्त-<BR>लक्ष्मी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, stripped of wealth.<BR>—आत्त-वचस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. destitute of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्थ
आत्थ आत्थ, thou saidst. See under rt. 3. अह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्
आत्मन् आत्मन्, आ, m. (fr. rt. अन्, to breathe,<BR>or अत्, to go; or, according to some, fr. rt. अह् and<BR>connected with अहम्, I; or, according to others, a<BR>contraction of अवत्मन् fr. rt. अव् = वा; but the ex-<BR>istence of the old Vedic form त्मन् makes all these<BR>etymologies doubtful); the breath, soul, the principle<BR>of life and sensation, the individual soul, the self, the<BR>abstract individual (e. g. आत्मन् Ved. loc. धत्ते,<BR>‘he places in himself, he makes his own;’ आत्मना<BR>वि-युज्, ‘to lose one's life;’ आत्मना सप्तमस्, ‘made<BR>the seventh by one's self,’ i. e. ‘being one's self the<BR>seventh with six others’); self, one's self, used as a<BR>reflexive pronoun for all three persons (e. g. आत्मा-<BR>नं सा हन्ति, ‘she strikes herself’); and used in the<BR>singular even when it refers to a dual or plural (e. g.<BR>पुत्रम् आत्मनः स्पृष्ट्वा निपेततुः, ‘they two<BR>having touched their son fell down’); the natural tem-<BR>perament or disposition; essence, nature, character,<BR>peculiarity; the person or whole body considered<BR>as one and opposed to the separate members of the<BR>body; the body; the understanding, intellect, the<BR>mind, the faculty of thought or reason, the thinking<BR>faculty; the highest personal principle of life, Brahma,<BR>the supreme deity and soul of the universe (but पर-<BR>मात्मन् is more usual in this latter sense); care,<BR>effort, pains; firmness; the sun; fire; wind; air; a son;<BR>[cf. Goth. ahma; Old Germ. ātum, Them. ātuma;<BR>Angl. Sax. œdhm; Mod. Germ. Athem, Odem;<BR>Hib. adhm, ‘knowledge,’ and adhma, ‘knowing;’<BR>Gr. ἀϋτμήν, ἀϋτμή (?); ἀτμός, ἀτμή (?): cf. also<BR>rt. ἄω &c. = rt. वा.]<BR>—आत्म is used at the end of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-a" target="_blank">Page0118-a+ 81</a>]<BR>some compounds for आत्मन्; e. g. प्रत्ययात्म,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, whose natural disposition is confidence.<BR>—आत्म-कर्मन्, अ, n. one's own act.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, loving one's self, possessed of<BR>self-conceit; loving Brahma, the supreme spirit.<BR>—आत्म-कामेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>कामेयक, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabited by the Ātmakāme-<BR>yas.<BR>—आत्म-कार्य, अम्, n. one's own business, pri-<BR>vate affairs.<BR>—आत्म-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, self-executed,<BR>done of one's self; done against one's self.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>गतम्, ind. lit. ‘gone to one's self,’ aside (used in<BR>theatrical language, like the English ‘aside,’ to denote<BR>that the words which follow are supposed to be<BR>spoken privately, as if to the speaker's self and not in<BR>the hearing of any one but the audience).<BR>—आत्म-<BR>गति, इस्, f. course of the soul's existence, life of the<BR>spirit; one's own course.<BR>—आत्म-गत्या, ind. by<BR>one's own act (without the intervention of another).<BR>—आत्म-गुप्ता, f., N. of the plant Mucuna Pruritus<BR>Hook.; (according to others) Cowach or Cowhage.<BR>—आत्म-गुप्ति, इस्, f. a cave, the hiding-place of an<BR>animal.<BR>—आत्म-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, selfish, greedy,<BR>taking care of one's self, appropriating, taking for<BR>one's self.<BR>—आत्म-घात, अस्, m. suicide; heresy,<BR>schism.<BR>—आत्म-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a suicide, a here-<BR>tic, a schismatic, one who disregards moral or religious<BR>institutions.<BR>—आत्म-घोष, अस्, m. a crow; a cock<BR>(‘one who calls out to himself’).<BR>—आत्म-ज, अस्, m.<BR>a son; (आ), f. a daughter; a descendant; the reason-<BR>ing faculty, understanding.<BR>—आत्म-जन्मन्, अ, n.<BR>the birth of one's self, i. e. the birth of a son; (आ),<BR>m. a son.<BR>—आत्म-जय, अस्, m. one's own victory;<BR>victory over one's self.<BR>—आत्म-ज्ञ, अस्, m. a sage,<BR>one who knows his own nature and that of spirit, self-<BR>knowing.<BR>—आत्म-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of the<BR>soul or supreme spirit, spiritual knowledge, philoso-<BR>phical knowledge of the spiritual principle in creation;<BR>self-knowledge, true wisdom.<BR>—आत्म-तत्त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the true nature of the soul or of the supreme spirit.<BR>—आत्मतत्त्व-ज्ञ, अस्, m. a sage versed in the Ve-<BR>dānta doctrines.<BR>—आत्म-ता, f. or आत्म-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>identity with self, spirituality.<BR>—आत्म-त्याग, अस्, m.<BR>self-sacrifice, giving up one's own life, suicide.<BR>—आत्-<BR>म-त्यागिन्, ई, m. one who gives up his own life, a<BR>suicide; a heretic, an unbeliever.<BR>—आत्म-त्राण, अम्,<BR>n. self-preservation, a body-guard.<BR>—आत्म-दर्श, अस्,<BR>m. ‘self-shower,’ a mirror.<BR>—आत्म-दर्शन, अम्,<BR>n. seeing one's self; knowledge of man's real nature,<BR>spiritual knowledge.<BR>—आत्म-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>granting personal existence or life.<BR>—आत्म-दान,<BR>अम्, n. gift of self, self-sacrifice, resignation.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>दूषि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. corrupting the soul, soul-destroy-<BR>ing.<BR>—आत्म-देवता, f. a tutelary deity.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>द्रोहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, self-tormenting, fretful, miserable.<BR>—आत्म-नित्य, अस्, आ, अम्, constantly in the heart,<BR>greatly endeared to one's self.<BR>—आत्म-निन्दा, f.<BR>self-reproach.<BR>—आत्म-निवेदन, अम्, n. offering<BR>one's self as a living sacrifice to the deity.<BR>—आत्मन्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a soul, animated, alive,<BR>personal.<BR>—आत्मन्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. animated,<BR>having a soul.<BR>—आत्म-पराजित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>one who has lost himself.<BR>—आत्म-परित्याग, अस्,<BR>m. self-sacrifice.<BR>—आत्म-प्रबोध, अस्, m. cognition<BR>of soul or supreme spirit; title of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—आत्म-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, shining by one's own<BR>light. self-illuminated.<BR>—आत्म-प्रवाद, अस्, m. con-<BR>versation about the soul or supreme spirit; N. of the<BR>seventh of the fourteen Pūrvas or most ancient sacred<BR>writings of the Jainas.<BR>—आत्म-प्रशंसा, f. self-<BR>applause.<BR>—आत्म-प्रीति, इस्, f. self-enjoyment, self-<BR>indulgence.<BR>—आत्म-बध, see आत्म-वध.<BR>—आत्म-बन्धु, उस्, m. one's own kinsman, a<BR>first cousin or father's sister's son, mother's brother's<BR>son, mother's sister's son.<BR>—आत्म-बुद्धि, इस्, f. self-<BR>knowledge.<BR>—आत्म-बोध, अस्, m. knowledge of soul<BR>or supreme spirit; self-knowledge; N. of a work of<BR>Śaṅkarācārya; N. of one of the Upaniṣads of the<BR>Atharva-veda; (अस्, आ, अम्), possessed of a knowledge<BR>of soul or the supreme spirit.<BR>—आत्म-भव, अस्,<BR>m. becoming or existing of one's self; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>produced in one's self, caused by one's self.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-b" target="_blank">Page0118-b+ 81</a>]<BR>भाव, अस्, m. existence of the soul; the self, proper<BR>or peculiar nature; the body.<BR>—आत्म-भू, ऊस्, m.<BR>self-born, self-existent; an epithet of Brahmā, Viṣṇu,<BR>Śiva, and Kāmadeva, the god of love.<BR>—आत्म-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, self-produced, become one's self, own,<BR>peculiar, belonging to; attached to, faithful.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>भूय, अम्, n. peculiarity, own nature.<BR>—आत्म-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, spiritual.<BR>—आत्म-मात्रा, f. a particle of<BR>the supreme spirit.<BR>—आत्म-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, self-<BR>honouring, self-respecting, decorous, respectable.<BR>—आत्-<BR>म-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, self-existent; (ई), f., the plant<BR>Alhagi Maurorum (‘striking root in self’).<BR>—आत्मम्-<BR>भरि, इस्, इस्, इ, self-nourishing, one who takes care only<BR>of his own person, selfish, greedy.<BR>—आत्म-याजिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, sacrificing for one's self; one who sacrifices himself;<BR>(ई), m. a wise or learned man, one who studies his own<BR>nature and that of the soul.<BR>—आत्म-योनि, इस्, m. one<BR>whose birth-place is self; an epithet of Brahmā,<BR>Viṣṇu, Śiva, and Kāmadeva, the god of love.<BR>—आत्म-रक्षा, f. the plant Cucumis Colocynthis<BR>or Trichosanthes Bracteata (a creeper with a poisonous<BR>fruit).<BR>—आत्म-राम-योगेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—आत्म-लोमन्, अ, n. the hair of the<BR>body; the beard.<BR>—आत्म-वञ्चक, अस्, आ, अम्, self-<BR>deceiver.<BR>—आत्म-वञ्चना, f. self-delusion.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, self-possessed, composed, prudent;<BR>knowing spirit; (त्), ind. like one's self.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>वत्-ता, f. self-possession, self-regard, prudence; self-<BR>resemblance, proportion, analogy.<BR>—आत्म-वध, अस्,<BR>m. or आत्म-वध्या, f. suicide.<BR>—आत्म-वश, अस्,<BR>m. subjection of the mind, self-control, self-govern-<BR>ment; (अस्, आ, अम्), depending on one's own will.<BR>—आत्म-विक्रय, अस्, m. sale of one's self, sale of<BR>one's liberty.<BR>—आत्म-विद्, त्, m. a wise man, a sage,<BR>one who knows the nature of the soul or spirit;<BR>a sensible man, one who knows himself; a N. of Śiva.<BR>—आत्म-विद्या, f. knowledge of soul or the supreme<BR>spirit; spiritual knowledge.<BR>—आत्म-विवृद्धि or<BR>आत्म-वृद्धि, इस्, f. self-advantage.<BR>—आत्म-वीर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, existent, sentient; appropriate, good for<BR>one's self, suitable as diet &c.; (अस्), m. a mighty<BR>man; a son; a wife's brother; the jester or Vidū-<BR>shaka in a play.<BR>—आत्म-वृत्तान्त, अस्, m. one's own<BR>story, account of one's self, autobiography.<BR>—आत्म-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. one's own circumstances; practising one's<BR>own duties or occupation.<BR>—आत्म-शक्ति, इस्, f. inhe-<BR>rent or own power or effort.<BR>—आत्म-शल्या, f. the<BR>plant Asparagus Racemosus Willd.<BR>—आत्म-शुद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. self-purification.<BR>—आत्म-श्लाघा, f. self-praise,<BR>boasting.<BR>—आत्म-संयम, अस्, m. self-restraint,<BR>stoicism.<BR>—आत्म-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. dwelling in self.<BR>—आत्म-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting the breath of<BR>life.<BR>—आत्म-सन्देह, अस्, m. internal doubt, personal<BR>risk.<BR>—आत्म-सम्भव, अस्, m. a son; (आ), f. a<BR>daughter.<BR>—आत्म-सात्, ind. one's own; (used in con-<BR>nection with rt. कृ, see आत्मसात्-कृ next col.)<BR>—आत्-<BR>म-सिद्धि, इस्, f. personal aggrandizement, self-ad-<BR>vantage.<BR>—आत्म-सुख, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—आत्-<BR>म-स्तुति, इस्, f. self-praise.<BR>—आत्म-हत्या, f. self-<BR>destruction, suicide.<BR>—आत्म-हन्, आ, m. one who<BR>kills his soul, or does not concern himself about the<BR>welfare of his soul; a heretic, an unbeliever; a self-<BR>murderer, a suicide; a priest in a temple, a servant<BR>or attendant upon an idol; (the priest subsisting by<BR>appropriating to himself offerings to deities, for which<BR>future punishment is assigned.)<BR>—आत्म-हनन, अम्,<BR>n. suicide.<BR>—आत्म-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, beneficial to one's<BR>self; (अम्), n. one's own profit or advantage.<BR>—आत्मा-<BR>दिष्ट (˚म-आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, self-counselled; (अस्),<BR>m. a treaty dictated by the party wishing it himself.<BR>—आत्माधीन (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, depending<BR>on self, independent; sentient, existent; (अस्), m. a<BR>son; a wife's brother; the jester or Vidūṣaka in a<BR>play, see आत्मनीन and आत्म-वीर.<BR>—आत्मापराध<BR>(˚म-अप्˚), अस्, m. own offence, personal transgression.<BR>—आत्मापहारक (˚म-अप्˚), अस्, m. an impostor,<BR>one who pretends to belong to a higher class than his<BR>own.<BR>—आत्माभिलाष (˚म-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the soul's<BR>desire.<BR>—आत्मार्थ (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, for one's<BR>own sake, for the sake of one's self.<BR>—आत्माशिन्<BR>(˚म-आश्˚), ई, m. a fish, supposed to eat its young.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">Page0118-c+ 78</a>]<BR>—आत्माश्रय (˚म-आश्˚), अस्, m. self-dependance;<BR>innate idea, abstract knowledge which is independant<BR>of the thing to be known.<BR>—आत्मेश्वर (˚म-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. master of one's self, self-possessed; God.<BR>—आत्-<BR>मोदय (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. self-advantage or elevation.<BR>—आत्मोद्भव (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, born or pro-<BR>duced from one's self; (अस्), m. a son; (आ), f. a<BR>daughter; N. of the plant Glycine Debilis Roxb.<BR>—आत्मोपजीविन् (˚म-उप्˚), ई, इनी, इ, one who lives<BR>by his own labour; one who lives by his wife;<BR>a public performer, actor, singer, dancer, &c.; a day-<BR>labourer.<BR>—आत्मोपनिषद् (˚म-उप्˚), त्, f. title of<BR>an Upaniṣad which treats of the supreme spirit.<BR>—आत्मोपम (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, like one's self.<BR>—आत्मौपम्य (˚म-औप्˚), अम्, n. likeness to<BR>self, analogy to one's own self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मक
आत्मक, अस्, इका, m. f. = आत्मन्, essence, nature,<BR>character, property, peculiarity; (अस्, आ, अम्), belong-<BR>ing to the nature or essence of a thing, of the same<BR>nature as. आत्मक often occurs as the last member<BR>of a compound; e. g. सङ्कल्पात्मक, whose charac-<BR>teristic is सङ्कल्प; पञ्चात्मक, five-fold, com-<BR>posed of five; विषात्मक, poisonous; ऋग्-आत्मक,<BR>belonging to the Rig-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकीय
आत्मकीय or आत्मीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>one's self, one's own, own; cognate, related of kin.<BR>Used reflexively for all three persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनीन|आत्मनीनं|आत्मनीनः
आत्मनीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to self, own;<BR>appropriate, good for, fit for, suitable (as diet &c.),<BR>existent, sentient; (अस्), m. a son; any living being;<BR>a wife's brother; the jester or Vidūṣaka (q. v.) in a<BR>drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनेपद|आत्मनेपदं
आत्मने-पद, अम्, n. ‘word to one's self,’ form<BR>for one's self; that form of the verb which implies<BR>an action belonging or reverting to self; that voice<BR>which corresponds to the Greek middle; the ter-<BR>minations of that voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनेपदिन्
आत्मनेपदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, taking the terminations<BR>of the middle voice, inflected in this voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनेभाषा
आत्मने-भाषा, f. the Sanskrit middle voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्कृ
आत्मसात्-कृ, to make one's own, to acquire or<BR>gain for one's self, to place upon one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्कृत
आत्मसात्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made one's own, ap-<BR>propriated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीभाव|आत्मीभावः
आत्मी-भाव, अस्, m. becoming part of the supreme<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्म्य
आत्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to self, personal;<BR>(at the end of a comp.) having the nature of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिक|आत्यंतिक
आत्यन्तिक आत्यन्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अत्य्-अन्त),<BR>continual, uninterrupted, infinite, endless; excessive, su-<BR>perlative, abundant; supreme.<BR>—आत्यन्तिक-प्रलय,<BR>अस्, m. the grand or universal destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ययिक
आत्ययिक आत्ययिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अत्य्-अय),<BR>having a rapid course, rushing quickly to a termination,<BR>not suffering delay, pressing, urgent; destructive, dis-<BR>astrous, distressing, painful, ill-omened, unpropitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यूह|आत्यूहः
आत्यूह आत्यूह, अस्, m. a gallinule. See<BR>दात्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेय|आत्रेयः
आत्रेय आत्रेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अत्रि), origin-<BR>ating from Atri; (अस्), m. a descendant of Atri;<BR>a priest who is closely related to the Sadasya<BR>(perhaps because this office was generally held by a<BR>descendant of Atri); an epithet of Śiva; an essential<BR>humor or juice of the body; (ई), f. a female descend-<BR>ant of Atri; a woman in her courses; any woman of<BR>the Brāhmanical order; N. of a river in the north of<BR>Bengal, otherwise called Tistā.<BR>—आत्रेयी-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेयिका
आत्रेयिका, f. a woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वण|आथर्वणः|आथर्व्वण|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्वण आथर्वण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अथर्वन्),<BR>originating from, or belonging or relating to Atharvan<BR>or the Atharvans; (अस्), m. a descendant of Atharvan;<BR>a priest whose ritual is comprised in the Atharva-veda;<BR>a Brāhman versed in the Atharva-veda; a house-<BR>priest; the Atharva-veda; (अम्), n. a private apartment<BR>in which, after a sacrifice, the sacrificer is informed of<BR>the happy event of the sacrifice by the officiating<BR>Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणिक|आथर्वणिकः|आथर्व्वणिक
आथर्वणिक, अस्, m. a Brāhman who has studied<BR>the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणीयरुद्रोपनिषद्
आथर्वणीय-रुद्रोपनिषद् (˚र-उप्˚), त्, f., N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्
आद् आद् (आ-अद्), cl. 2. P., Ved. आत्ति, आत्तुम्,<BR>to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदंश्
आदंश् आ-दंश्, cl. 1. P. -दंशति, -दंष्टुम्,<BR>to nibble, bite or peck at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदंश|आदंशः
आ-दंश, अस्, m. a bite, a wound caused by biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदष्ट
आ-दष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, nibbled, pecked at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदघ्न
आदघ्न आ-दघ्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. आस्-द्˚), Ved.<BR>reaching up to the mouth (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदम्भ्
आदम्भ् आ-दम्भ्, cl. 5. P., Ved. -दभ्नोति,<BR>-दम्भितुम्, to harm, hurt, injure, treat injuriously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आदर आ-दर. See under आ-दृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आदर्श आ-दर्श. See under आ-दृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदह्
आदह् आ-दह्, cl. 1. P. -दहति, -दग्धुम्,<BR>to burn, burn up: Caus. -दाहयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to burn: Caus. Pass. -दाह्यते, to be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदहन|आदहनं
आ-दहन, अम्, n., Ved. a place where anything<BR>is burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदा
आदा 1. आ-दा, cl. 3. A. (Ved. sometimes P.)<BR>-दत्ते, -ददाति, -दातुम्, to give to one's self, ap-<BR>propriate to one's self, take, receive, accept, seize,<BR>take away, separate; to carry off, to put on (as<BR>clothes), to perceive, comprehend; to agree to; to<BR>undertake, begin; to begin to speak; to repeat (with<BR>पुनर्): Caus. -दापयति, -यितुम्, to cause one<BR>to take: Desid. A. -दित्सते, to desire to take, to be<BR>on the point of taking or seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद
आ-द, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of some compounds)<BR>taking, receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्त
आ-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (sometimes contracted to<BR>आत्त, q. v.), taken, seized, put on; agreed to, under-<BR>taken, begun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आददान
आ-ददान, अस्, आ, अम्, taking, accepting, under-<BR>taking, beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आददि
आ-ददि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. procuring, gaining; taking<BR>or carrying away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदातव्य
आ-दातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदातृ
आ-दातृ, ता, m. a receiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदान|आदानं
1. आ-दान, अम्, n. taking, seizing; receipt, accept-<BR>ance; taking for one's self, drawing near to one's<BR>self; receiving; taking away or off; a symptom:<BR>(for 2. आ-दान see below under 2. आ-दा.)<BR>—आदान-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who receives something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदानी
आ-दानी, f., N. of a plant, commonly called हस्ति-<BR>घोषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदापन|आदापनं
आ-दापन, अम्, n. inviting or causing another to<BR>accept something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदाय|आदायः
1. आ-दाय, अस्, आ, अम्, receiving, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदाय|आदायः
2. आ-दाय, ind. having taken.<BR>—आदाय-चर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who goes away after having taken any-<BR>thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायमान
आ-दायमान, अस्, आ, अम् (epic form for आ-ददान),<BR>taking, seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायिन्
आ-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, receiving, inclined to receive<BR>(gifts), taking gifts for one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेय
आ-देय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or received, re-<BR>ceivable, leviable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदा
आदा 2. आ-दा, cl. 2. 4. P. -दाति, -द्यति,<BR>दातुम्, to bind, fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदान|आदानं
2. आ-दान, अम्, n., Ved. binding, fettering; a horse's<BR>trappings. (For 1. आ-दान see under 1. आ-दा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदादिक
आदादिक आदादिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अद्-आदि),<BR>belonging to that class of roots of which the first is<BR>अद्, i. e. to the second class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि आदि, इस्, m. (fr. 1. आ-दा ?), beginning,<BR>commencement; a firstling, first-fruits; first, prior,<BR>prime, pre-eminent; (very often at the end or in the<BR>middle of a compound in the sense) beginning with,<BR>et cætera, and so on (e. g. इन्द्रादयः सुराः, the<BR>gods beginning with Indra, i. e. Indra &c.; गृहादि-<BR>युक्त, possessed of houses, &c.; एवम्-आदीनि वस्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-b" target="_blank">Page0119-b+ 81</a>]<BR>तूनि, such and similar things; शय्या खट्वादिः,<BR>the word शय्या means a bed &c.); आदौ, ind. in the<BR>commencement or beginning, at first; [with this<BR>word has been compared the Slav. jedin, ‘one.’]<BR>—आदि-कर, अस्, m. the creator; an epithet of<BR>Brahmā.<BR>—आदि-कर्तृ, ता, m. the creator; an epi-<BR>thet of Brahmā, Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—आदि-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. (in gram.) the beginning or commencement of<BR>an action (as in the example सूर्यः प्रद्योतितः,<BR>‘the sun has begun to shine;’ see Gram. 895. a).<BR>—आदि-कवि, इस्, m. the first poet; an epithet of<BR>Brahmā, or of Vālmīki.<BR>—आदि-काण्ड, अम्, n. first<BR>part or chapter; title of the first book of the Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa.<BR>—आदि-कारण, अम्, n. a primary cause; ana-<BR>lysis, algebra.<BR>—आदि-काल, अस्, m. primitive time,<BR>remote antiquity.<BR>—आदि-काव्य, अम्, n. the first poem,<BR>an epithet of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—आदि-क्रित्, त्, m. the<BR>creator; see आदि-कर्तृ above.<BR>—आदि-केशव, अस्,<BR>m. the first keśava, an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—आदि-तस्,<BR>ind. from the beginning, from the first, in the be-<BR>ginning, at first, at the head of (with gen.).<BR>—आदि-<BR>ता, f. or आदि-त्व, अम्, n. priority, precedence.<BR>—आदि-देव, अस्, m. the first god, the creator; N. of<BR>Brahmā, Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa, or Nārāyaṇa; the sun.<BR>—आदि-दैत्य, अस्, m. epithet of Hiraṇyakaśipu.<BR>—आदि-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of Ādi-buddha; N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—आदि-पर्वन्, अ, n. first section or chapter,<BR>title of the first book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—आदि-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n. the primitive Purāṇa, N. of the<BR>Brahma-Purāṇa.<BR>—आदि-पुरुष or आदि-पूरुष,<BR>अस्, m. the first male or progenitor, usually applied to<BR>Viṣṇu; the primeval spirit.<BR>—आदि-बल, अम्, n.<BR>generative power (first vigour).<BR>—आदि-बुद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, perceived in the beginning; (अस्), m. the<BR>primitive Buddha, the chief deity of the northern<BR>Buddhists.<BR>—आदि-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, produced at first;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—आदि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>first-born or existent; (अस्), m., a N. of Brahmā.<BR>—आदि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a beginning<BR>—आदि-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. primitive foundation, primeval cause.<BR>—आदि-योगाचार्य (˚ग-आच्˚), अस्, m. primitive<BR>teacher of devotion; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—आदि-<BR>रस, अस्, m. the first or chief of the eight rasas, the<BR>principal sentiment or emotion, i. e. sṛṅgāra or love.<BR>—आदिरस-श्लोक, अस्, m., N. of a poem supposed to<BR>be written by Kālidāsa.<BR>—आदि-राज, अस्, m. the first<BR>king; an epithet of Manu; of a son of Kuru; of<BR>Pṛthu.<BR>—आदि-वंश, अस्, m. primeval race, primitive<BR>family.<BR>—आदि-वराह, अस्, m. the first boar; N. of<BR>Viṣṇu, alluding to his incarnation in that form.<BR>—आदिवाराह, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the first boar.<BR>—आदि-विपुला, f., N. of a metre.<BR>—आदि-शरीर, अम्,<BR>n. the primitive body.<BR>—आदि-सर्ग, अस्, m. primitive<BR>creation.<BR>—आदि-सूर, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—आदी-<BR>श्वर (˚दि-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—आद्य्-अन्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having beginning and end; from the be-<BR>ginning to the end; (अम्), n. beginning and end,<BR>first and last.<BR>—आद्यन्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>beginning and end, finite.<BR>—आद्य्-अन्तान्तर-वर्तिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, containing beginning, end, and middle;<BR>being all in all.<BR>—आद्य्-उदात्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the acute accent on the first syllable.<BR>—आद्युदात्-<BR>त-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of having the acute<BR>accent on the first syllable.<BR>—आद्योपान्तम् (˚द्य-<BR>उप्˚), ind. from first to last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिक
आदिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (used like आदि, q. v., at the end<BR>of compounds) beginning with, et cætera, and so on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम, अस्, आ, अम्, first, prior, primitive, original.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
1. आद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being at the beginning, first,<BR>primitive; beginning with (used in this sense like<BR>आदि; e. g. इन्द्राद्याः सुराः, the gods beginning<BR>with Indra, i. e. Indra &c.); immediately preceding<BR>(e. g. एकादशाद्य, immediately before the eleventh,<BR>i. e. the tenth; संयुक्ताद्य, immediately pre-<BR>ceding a double consonant); being at the head, un-<BR>paralleled, unprecedented, excellent; (अम्), n. the<BR>beginning; आद्ये, in the beginning; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a class of deities; (आ), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—आद्य-कवि, इस्, m. the first poet, a N. of Vālmīki,<BR>the author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—आद्य-माषक, अस्,<BR>m. a māṣa, a weight equal to five guñja or retti<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">Page0119-c+ 77</a>]<BR>seeds, about 17(1/2) grains troy.<BR>—आद्य-वीज, अम्, n.<BR>a primary cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिग्ध
आदिग्ध आ-दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. दिह्), be-<BR>smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितेय|आदितेयः
आदितेय आदितेय, अस्, m. (fr. अदिति), a son<BR>of Aditi; a god, a deity, a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or devoted to, or<BR>originating from Aditi; belonging or relating to, or<BR>originating from the Ādityas; (अस्), m. a son of<BR>Aditi. In the earliest times this is the N. of seven<BR>deities of the heavenly sphere, of whom Varuṇa is<BR>the chief and to whom therefore especially belongs<BR>the title Āditya. The names of six of the seven are<BR>Varuṇa, Mitra, Aryaman, Bhaga, Dakṣa, and Aṃśa; that<BR>of the seventh is not clearly ascertained. Sometimes their<BR>number is supposed to be eight; and in the period of<BR>the Brāhmaṇas twelve, as representing the sun in<BR>the twelve months of the year. The name Āditya<BR>was afterwards applied to any god, though especially<BR>applicable to Sūrya, the sun; N. of Viṣṇu in his<BR>Vāmana or dwarf avatār, as son of Kaśyapa and Aditi<BR>and younger brother of Indra; the plant Calotropis<BR>Gigantea; N. of a man; (औ), m. du., N. of a constel-<BR>lation, the seventh lunar mansion.<BR>—आदित्य-केतु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—आदित्य-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—आदित्य-चन्द्रौ,<BR>m. du. sun and moon.<BR>—आदित्य-दास, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—आदित्य-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a plant = अर्क-<BR>पत्त्र.<BR>—आदित्य-पर्णिनी, f. a creeping plant with<BR>gold-coloured flowers, growing near the banks of<BR>water.<BR>—आदित्य-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of an Upa-<BR>purāṇa.<BR>—आदित्य-पुष्पिका, f. red swallow wort.<BR>—आदित्य-प्रभ, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—आदित्य-<BR>भक्ता, f. = अर्क-भक्ता, q. v.<BR>—आदित्य-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. the disc or orb of the sun.<BR>—आदित्य-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, surrounded by the Ādityas.<BR>—आदित्य-वनि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. winning the (favour of the) Ādityas.<BR>—आदित्य-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, having the colour of<BR>the sun; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—आदित्य-वर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a king.<BR>—आदित्य-व्रत, अम्, n. = अर्क-<BR>व्रत, q. v.<BR>—आदित्य-सदृश, अस्, ई, अम्, like the<BR>sun.<BR>—आदित्य-सूनु, उस्, m., son of the sun; N. of<BR>Sugrīva, the monkey-king; of Yama, Saturn, Sāvarṇi<BR>Manu, and Vaivasvata Manu.<BR>—आदित्य-सेन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king of Ujjayinī.<BR>—आदित्याचार्य (˚त्य-आच्),<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सा
आदित्सा आ-दित्सा, f. (fr. Desid. of 1. आ-दा),<BR>desire to seize or take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सु
आ-दित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to take or have (with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिन्
आदिन् आदिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt. अद्), eating (used<BR>at the end of compounds; cf. अन्नादिन् &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिनव|आदिनवं|आदिनवः
आदिनव आदिनव, अम्, n. (?), Ved. misfor-<BR>tune, hinderance, want of luck (in dice); see आदीनव.<BR>—आदिनव-दर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having evil<BR>designs towards a fellow-player at dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिश्
आदिश् 1. आ-दिश्, cl. 6. P. A. -दीशति, -ते,<BR>-देष्टुम्, to aim at, to assign; to point out, indicate,<BR>report, announce, teach, determine, specify, foretel;<BR>to order, direct, command; to provoke, challenge; to<BR>undertake, try; to profess as one's purpose or duty:<BR>Caus. -देशयति, -यितुम्, to indicate, announce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिश्
2. आ-दिश्, क्, f., Ved. aiming at, design, intention;<BR>project, proposition; proposal, declaration; region,<BR>quarter; (Sāy.) a sacrifice offered or assigned (to a<BR>particular deity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिश्य
आ-दिश्य, ind. announcing, apprising, aiming at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्ट|आदिष्टं|आदिष्टः
आ-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, advised, enjoined; directed,<BR>commanded; said; (अम्), n. command, order; frag-<BR>ments or leavings of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टिन्
आदिष्टिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or (ई), m. one who receives<BR>instruction, a pupil, a student, a Brāhman in the first<BR>order or quarter of his life; a penitent, one engaged<BR>in any expiatory rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश|आदेशः
आ-देश, अस्, m. account, information; advice, in-<BR>struction, precept, rule; an order, command; fore-<BR>telling; (in gram.) a substitute, substituted form or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">Page0120-a+ 76</a>]<BR>letter, &c.; (in astrology) event, result, consequence<BR>of stellar conjunctions.<BR>—आदेश-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, obe-<BR>dient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशन|आदेशनं
आ-देशन, अम्, n. the act of instructing, command-<BR>ing or prescribing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिन्
आ-देशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ordering, commanding, insti-<BR>gating, exciting (e. g. कपोल-पाटलादेशिन्, exciting<BR>a glow on the cheek); (ई), m. a commander, a<BR>director; an astrologer, a fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश्य
आ-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ordered or commanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेष्टृ
आ-देष्टृ, टा, m. an adviser, a director, a com-<BR>mander; an employer of priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनव|आदीनवं|आदीनवः
आदीनव आदीनव, अस्, m. distress, pain, un-<BR>easiness; fault, transgression; an afflicter of distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीप्
आदीप् आ-दीप्, Caus. P. -दीपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to blaze, kindle, set on fire, illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपन|आदीपनं
आ-दीपन, अम्, n. setting on fire, inflaming, ex-<BR>citing, embellishing; whitening the wall, floor or<BR>seat &c. upon festival occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपित
आ-दीपित, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminated, inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीप्त
आ-दीप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, set on fire, blazing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदु
आदु आ-दु, cl. 5. P. A. -दुनोति, -ते, -दोतुम्,<BR>to feel pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृ
आदृ आ-दृ, cl. 6. A. or poet. P. -द्रियते,<BR>-ति, -दर्तुम्, to feel timid from veneration; to re-<BR>spect, mind; to honour, reverence; to enjoy honour,<BR>be honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आ-दर, अस्, m. respect shown to a person or thing,<BR>notice, care; reverence; commencement, beginning;<BR>[cf. Hib. adharadh, ‘adoration;’ adharach, ‘one<BR>who adores.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरण|आदरणं
आ-दरण, अम्, n. notice, respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरणीय
आ-दरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, venerable, respectable;<BR>to be attended to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्तव्य|आदर्त्तव्य
आ-दर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be respected or regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्य|आदर्य्य|आदर्य्यः
आ-दर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, venerable, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदार|आदारः
आ-दार, अस्, m., Ved. allurement, attraction; (Sāy.)<BR>an instigator; N. of a plant used instead of the Soma<BR>plant, if this cannot be had.<BR>—आदार-बिम्बी, f., N. of<BR>a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदारिन्
1. आ-दारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. attracting, alluring; (Sāy.)<BR>destroying (as if fr. आ-दॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदुरि
1. आ-दुरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. careful, attentive. (For<BR>2. आ-दुरि see under आ-दॄ below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत|आदृतः
आ-दृत, अस्, आ, अम्, respected, honoured, worship-<BR>ped; zealous, diligent; respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत्य|आदृत्यः
1. आ-दृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, venerable, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत्य|आदृत्यः
2. आ-दृत्य, ind. having respected, having honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृश्
आदृश् आ-दृश्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -पश्यति,<BR>-द्रष्टुम्, to look at: Caus. P. -दर्शयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to show, exhibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आ-दर्श, अस्, m. a looking-glass, a mirror; copy<BR>of a work; the original manuscript from which a<BR>copy is taken; a commentary; N. of a son of the<BR>eleventh Manu; N. of a country.<BR>—आदर्श-मण्डल,<BR>having mirror-like spots; N. of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शक|आदर्शकः
आ-दर्शक, अस्, m. a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शन|आदर्शनं
आ-दर्शन, अम्, n. showing, making apparent or<BR>seen; a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शित
आ-दर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, shown, made apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृष्टि|आदृष्टिः
आ-दृष्टि, इस्, f. looking at, power of looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदॄ
आदॄ आ-दॄ, cl. 9. P. A. -दृणाति, -णीते, -दरि-<BR>तुम् or -रीतुम्, to crush, to force or split open, make<BR>accessible, bring to light: Intens. -दर्दरीति, to crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्दरि
आ-दर्दरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. crushing, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदारिन्
2. आ-दारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, crushing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीर्य
आ-दीर्य, ind. having split, showing fissures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदुरि
2. आ-दुरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. crushing, bruising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेय
आदेय आ-देय. See under 1. आ-दा last page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवक
आदेवक आ-देवक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. दिव् with<BR>आ), one who sports or plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवन|आदेवनं
आ-देवन, अम्, n. a place for playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यून|आद्यूनः
1. आ-द्यून, अस्, आ, अम्, shamelessly voracious (said<BR>to come fr. आ-दिव्, but the connection of this meaning<BR>with rt. दिव् is not very apparent). For 2. आद्य्-ऊन<BR>see next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदो
आदो आ-दो, cl. 4. P. -द्यति, -दातुम्, to re-<BR>duce to pieces or fragments; to tie, fetter. (In this<BR>last sense, the rt. is better written दा; see 2. आ-दा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य 2. आद्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अद्), to be<BR>eaten edible; (अम्), n. grain, food. (For 1. आद्य see<BR>s. v. आदि last page, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यून|आद्यूनः
आद्यून 2. आद्य्-ऊन, अस्, आ, अम्, without be-<BR>ginning. (For 1. आ-द्यून see last col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्योत|आद्योतः
आद्योत आ-द्योत, अस्, m. (rt. द्युत्), light,<BR>brilliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्रिसार
आद्रिसार आद्रिसार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अद्रि-सार),<BR>made of iron, iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्रु
आद्रु आ-द्रु, cl. 1. P., Ved. A. -द्रवति, -ते,<BR>-द्रोतुम्, to run towards, to hasten towards, to ap-<BR>proach running; to bring running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्वादशम्
आद्वादशम् आ-द्वादशम्, ind., Ved. up to<BR>twelve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमन|आधमनं
आधमन आ-धमन, अम्, n. (fr. आ-धा be-<BR>low or fr. आ-धम् for आ-ध्मा?), a deposit, pledge;<BR>fraudulent puffing of goods at a sale (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमर्ण्य|आधमर्ण्यं
आधमर्ण्य आधमर्ण्य, अम्, n. (fr. अध-<BR>मर्ण), the state of being indebted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्मिक|आधर्म्मिक
आधर्मिक आधर्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-धर्म),<BR>unjust, unrighteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षण|आधर्षणं
आधर्षण आ-धर्षण. See आ-धृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधा
आधा आ-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति, -धत्ते,<BR>-धातुम्, to place, deposit, apply, appoint, direct,<BR>propose, supply, give, make, constitute; (only A.) to<BR>appropriate to one's self, hold, possess, take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदधान
आ-दधान, अस्, आ, अम्, having, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधान|आधानं
आ-धान, अम्, n. putting near or upon, placing;<BR>taking, having; receiving, recovering; the containing<BR>anything, the being in possession of a thing; a cere-<BR>mony performed with consecrated fire (see अग्न्या-<BR>धान); a ceremony performed previous to concep-<BR>tion (see गर्भाधान); a pledge, a deposit; a<BR>surety; assigning, attributing, employing; the place<BR>in which anything is deposited or rests; a receptacle;<BR>enclosure, circuit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधानिक|आधानिकं|आधानिकः
आधानिक, अम्, n. a ceremony performed after<BR>cohabitation to procure or favour conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाय|आधायः
आ-धाय, ind. having deposited or placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधायक
आ-धायक, अस्, इका, अम्, placing, assigning, attri-<BR>buting, applying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
1. आ-धि, इस्, m. (for 2. आ-धि see under आ-ध्यै),<BR>place, situation; a pledge, deposit; a pawn, a mort-<BR>gage; location fixing, site; definition, epithet.<BR>—आ-<BR>धि-त्व, अम्, n. the nature or circumstance of a<BR>pledge.<BR>—आधित्वोपाधि (˚त्व-उप्˚), इस्, m. the ob-<BR>ject or purpose with which a pledge is given, the<BR>conditions or terms of a mortgage.<BR>—आधि-भोग,<BR>अस्, m. enjoyment or use of a deposit, use of a horse,<BR>cow, &c., when pledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृ
आधी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to pledge,<BR>mortgage. pawn, make a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकरण|आधीकरणं
आधी-करण, अम्, n. pledging, mortgaging, a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृत
आधी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, pledged. pawned, mortgaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृत्य
आधी-कृत्य, ind. having pledged, mortgaged, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीयमान
आ-धीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being placed, being de-<BR>posited.<BR>—आधीयमान-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>heart applied or intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेय|आधेयं
आ-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be deposited or placed;<BR>to be pledged or mortgaged; what is put down or has<BR>a place assigned to it; to be assigned, attributed or<BR>given; to be received, held or supported; (अम्), n.<BR>= आ-धान, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार|आधारः
आधार आ-धार. See under आ-धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाव्
आधाव् आ-धाव्, cl. 1. P. -धावति, -वितुम्,<BR>to come running, to run towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधावमान
आ-धावमान, अस्, आ, अम्, running, rushing on-<BR>wards or at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
आधि आ-धि. See under आ-धा above for<BR>1. आ-धि, and under आ-ध्यै for 2. आ-धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारण्य|आधिकारण्यं
आधिकारण्य आधिकारण्य, अम्, n. (fr. अधि-<BR>करण्य), possession, location.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारिक
आधिकारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अधि-कार), supreme,<BR>superior, relating or belonging to anything or person<BR>in authority; official, relating to any office or duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिक्य|आधिक्यं
आधिक्य आधिक्य, अम्, n. (fr. अधिक), ex-<BR>cess, abundance, superabundance, high degree, over-<BR>weight, preponderance; superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविक|आधिदैविकं
आधिदैविक आधिदैविक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अधि-<BR>देव), relating to a tutelary or presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिपत्य|आधिपत्यं
आधिपत्य आधिपत्य, अम्, n. (fr. अधि-पति),<BR>supremacy, sovereignty, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभौतिक|आधिभौतिकं
आधिभौतिक आधिभौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अधि-भूत), relating to beings; elementary, derived<BR>or produced from the primitive elements, material.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिराज्य|आधिराज्यं
आधिराज्य आधिराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. अधि-राजन्),<BR>royalty, royal government, supreme sway.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिवेदनिक|आधिवेदनिकं
आधिवेदनिक आधिवेदनिक, अम्, n. (fr. अधि-<BR>वेदन), property, gifts &c. given to a first wife<BR>upon marrying a second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधु
आधु आ-धु or -धू, cl. 5. 9. P. -धुनोति,<BR>-धुनाति or -धूनोति, -नाति, -धवितुम् or -धो-<BR>तुम्, to stir, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधव|आधवः
आ-धव, अस्, m., Ved. one who stirs up or agitates;<BR>that which is agitated, mixture; throwing; also =<BR>आ-धवनीय (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधवन|आधवनं
आ-धवन, अम्, n. agitating, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधवनीय|आधवनीयः
आ-धवनीय, अस्, m. a vessel in which the Soma<BR>plant is shaken and cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाव|आधावः
आ-धाव, अस्, m., Ved. that which is shaken or<BR>cleansed by shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुत|आधुतः
आ-धुत or आ-धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, agitated,<BR>trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुनिक|आधुनिकः
आधुनिक आधुनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अधुना),<BR>new, recent, of the present moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधूर्य|आधूर्य्य
आधूर्य आधूर्य, अम्, n. weakness (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृ
आधृ आ-धृ, cl. 1. P. -धरति, -धर्तुम्,<BR>to hold, keep, support: Caus. P. -धारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to bring, supply: Pass. -ध्रियते, to be brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार|आधारः
आ-धार, अस्, m. support, prop, stay; the power of<BR>sustaining, or the support given, aid, patronage, as-<BR>sistance; that which contains; a vessel or receptacle;<BR>a dike, dam; a canal; a basin round the foot of a<BR>tree; comprehension, location, the sense of the loca-<BR>tive case; relation.<BR>—आधाराधेय-भाव (˚र-<BR>आध्˚), अस्, m. the influence or action of the support<BR>or recipient upon the thing received or supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारक|आधारकः
आ-धारक, अस्, m. foundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधारण|आधारणं
आ-धारण, अम्, n. bearing, holding, supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार्य
आ-धार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be located, that to which<BR>a location is to be assigned.<BR>—आधार्याधार-सम्-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. the relation of the recipient or recep-<BR>tacle and the thing to be received or located.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृत
आ-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. contained, supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृष्
आधृष् आ-धृष्, cl. 5. P., Ved. -धृष्णोति,<BR>-धर्षितुम्, to assail, defy, injure, overcome; cl.<BR>10. P. -धर्षयति, -यितुम्, to injure, hurt, over-<BR>come, defy; refute, convict: Intens. Ved. -दधर्-<BR>षति or Leṭ of Caus. to overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षण|आधर्षणं
आ-धर्षण, अम्, n. conviction of crime or error;<BR>sentence, refutation; injuring, annoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षित
आ-धर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, convicted, sentenced;<BR>refuted in argument, disproved, injured, aggrieved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृष्ट
आ-धृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, checked, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृष्टि|आधृष्टिः
आ-धृष्टि, इस्, f. assailing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेनव|आधेनवं
आधेनव आधेनव, अम्, n. (fr. अ-धेनु),<BR>want of cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधोरण|आधोरणः
आधोरण आधोरण, अस्, m. the rider or<BR>driver of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मा
आध्मा आ-ध्मा, cl. 1. P. -धमति, -ध्मातुम्,<BR>to inflate, puff up; to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मात|आध्मातः
आ-ध्मात, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, sounding; inflated,<BR>burnt; (अस्), m. flatulence, borborygmi, swelling of<BR>the abdomen with noise, war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मान|आध्मानं
आ-ध्मान, अम्, n. blowing, inflation; boasting;<BR>a bellows; intumescence, swelling of the body, dropsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मापन|आध्मापनं
आ-ध्मापन, अम्, n. a means of inflating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यक्ष्य|आध्यक्ष्यं
आध्यक्ष्य आध्यक्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. अध्य्-अक्ष),<BR>Ved. superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यश्वि
आध्यश्वि आध्यश्वि, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यात्मिक|आध्यात्मिकं
आध्यात्मिक आध्यात्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अध्य्-<BR>आत्मन्), relating to self (as आध्यात्मिकी ऋच्, a hymn<BR>sung by any deity or other personage in praise of him-<BR>self); relating to the supreme spirit; spiritual, holy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यान|आध्यानं
आध्यान आ-ध्यान. See under आ-ध्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यापक|आध्यापकः
आध्यापक आध्यापक, अस्, m. a teacher, a<BR>scriptural preceptor; = अध्य्-आपक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यायिक
आध्यायिक आध्यायिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अध्य्-<BR>आय, q. v.), occupied or employed with reading or<BR>studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यै
आध्यै आ-ध्यै, cl. 1. P. -ध्यायति, -ध्यातुम्,<BR>to think on, meditate on, remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
2. आ-धि, इस्, m. (for 1. see under आ-धा), thought,<BR>care, anxious reflection, mental agony, anxiety, pain;<BR>misfortune; reflection on religion or duty; hope, ex-<BR>pectation; a man solicitous for his family's livelihood.<BR>—आधि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by pain, &c.<BR>—आधि-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, suffering pain, distressed; crooked.<BR>—आधि-मन्यु, अवस्, m. pl. feverish heat or burning.<BR>—आधि-म्लान, अस्, आ, अम्, withered with anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधी
आ-धी, f., Ved. thinking, longing, care.<BR>—आधी-<BR>पर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. winged with longing or<BR>hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीत
आ-धीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. reflected or meditated<BR>upon; (अम्), n. the object or subject of one's thoughts,<BR>anything intended or hoped for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्या
आ-ध्या, f. recollection, remembering especially<BR>with regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यान|आध्यानं
आ-ध्यान, अम्, n. remembering with regret, pen-<BR>sive or sorrowful recollection, dwelling or meditating<BR>upon, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्र|आध्रः
आध्र आध्र, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. ध्रै?), Ved.<BR>poor, destitute, indigent, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वनिक
आध्वनिक आध्वनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अध्वन्),<BR>being on a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वरिक|आध्वरिकः
आध्वरिक आध्वरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-ध्वर),<BR>belonging to a Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वर्यव|आध्वर्य्यव
आध्वर्यव आध्वर्यव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अध्-<BR>वर्यु), belonging to the Adhvaryu or to the Yajur-<BR>veda; (अम्), n. service at a sacrifice, especially the<BR>office of an Adhvaryu priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन|आनः
आन आन, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अन्), inhalation,<BR>breath inspired; Ved. mouth, nose; breathing, blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन|आननं
आनन, अम्, n. the mouth, the face.<BR>—आननाब्ज<BR>(˚न-अब्˚), अम्, n. face-lotus (i. e. lotus-like face).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक|आनकः
आनक आनक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अन्?), a large<BR>military drum beaten at one end, a double drum, a<BR>small drum or tabor; the thunder-cloud or a cloud to<BR>which the noise of the thunder is ascribed.<BR>—आनक-<BR>दुन्दुभि, इस्, m. (a patronymic fr. अनक-दुन्दुभ,<BR>q. v.), an epithet of Vasudeva the father of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>(इस्, ई), m. f. a large drum beaten at one end, a large<BR>द्ऽहोल्, a kettle-drum.<BR>—आनक-स्थली, f., N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक्य
आनक्य आनक्य, अस्, m. (?), N. of a sage<BR>(for Cāṇakya ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक्ष्
आनक्ष् आ-नक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -नक्षति, -षितुम्,<BR>to approach, obtain, reach, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनडुह
आनडुह आनडुह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनड्-उह्),<BR>originating from a bull; (अम्), n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्
आनद् आ-नद्, Caus. P. -नादयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to make resonant, cause to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनादयत्
आ-नादयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to sound, mak-<BR>ing to ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्ध|आनद्धं|आनद्धः
आनद्ध आ-नद्ध. See under आ-नह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन|आननं
आनन आनन. See s. v. आन above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्तर्य|आनंतर्यं|आनन्तर्य्य
आनन्तर्य आनन्तर्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्-अन्तर),<BR>immediate consequence or succession; proximity,<BR>absence of interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्त्य|आनंत्यं
आनन्त्य आनन्त्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्-अन्त), in-<BR>finity; immortality, future happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्द्|आनंद्
आनन्द् आ-नन्द्, cl. 1. P. -नन्दति, -दितुम्,<BR>to rejoice: Caus. P. -नन्दयति, -यितुम्, to gladden;<BR>A. to amuse one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्द|आनंदः|आनन्दः
आ-नन्द, अस्, m. happiness, joy, enjoyment, sen-<BR>sual pleasure; N. of the forty-eighth year of the<BR>cycle of Jupiter; an epithet of Śiva; N. of a Bala-rāma<BR>according to the Jaina doctrine of many Kṛṣṇas and<BR>many Bala-rāmas; N. of a cousin and a zealous follower<BR>and favourite disciple of Buddha Śākya-muni, compiler<BR>of the Sūtras; (आ and ई), f., N. of two plants; (अम्),<BR>n. God, the supreme spirit according to the Vedānta.<BR>—आनन्द-गिरि, इस्, or आनन्द-ज्ञान, अस्, or आनन्द-<BR>ज्ञान-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of an annotator on Śaṅka-<BR>rācārya.<BR>—आनन्द-ता, f. joyfulness, joy.<BR>—आनन्द-<BR>तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR>—आनन्द-द or<BR>आनन्द-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, exhilarating, delighting.<BR>—आनन्द-दत्त, अस्, m. membrum virile.<BR>—आ-<BR>नन्द-पट, अम्, n. a bridal garment.<BR>—आनन्द-<BR>पूर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—आनन्द-प्रभव,<BR>अम्, n. the seminal fluid.<BR>—आनन्द-बोधेन्द्र<BR>(˚ध-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR>—आनन्द-<BR>भैरव, अस्, आ, अम्, causing both enjoyment and<BR>fear.<BR>—आनन्द-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, blissful, made up<BR>or consisting or happiness; (अम्), n. the supreme<BR>spirit.<BR>—आनन्दमय-कोष, अस्, m. the innermost<BR>case of the body, or causal frame enshrining the soul.<BR>—आनन्द-राम, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—आनन्द-<BR>लहरि, इस् or ई, f. ‘wave of enjoyment,’ title of a<BR>hymn by Śaṅkarācārya, addressed to Pārvatī.<BR>—आ-<BR>नन्द-वन, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR>—आनन्द-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, enhancing enjoyment; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a poet.<BR>—आनन्द-वल्ली, f. title of the<BR>second part of the Taittirīya-Upaniṣad.<BR>—आनन्द-<BR>वेद, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—आनन्दानन्दन<BR>(˚द-आन्˚), अस्, m. a king.<BR>—आनन्दाश्रम (˚द-आश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दक|आनंदक
आ-नन्दक, अस्, आ, अम्, gladdening, rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दथु|आनंदथु|आनन्दथुः
आ-नन्दथु, उस्, उस्, उ, happy, joyful; (उस्), m.<BR>happiness, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दन|आनंदन|आनन्दनं
आ-नन्दन, अम्, n. delighting, making happy;<BR>civility, courtesy, courteous treatment of a friend or<BR>guest at meeting and parting; what gives or occasions<BR>delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दयितव्य|आनंदयितव्यं
आ-नन्दयितव्य, अम्, n. the object of enjoyment<BR>or sensual pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दयितृ|आनंदयितृ
आ-नन्दयितृ, ता, m. one who gladdens or makes<BR>joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दि|आनंदिः|आनन्दिः
आ-नन्दि, इस्, ई, m. f. happiness, enjoyment, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दित|आनन्दितः
आ-नन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoiced, delighted, happy;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दिन्|आनंदिन्
आ-नन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, happy, joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनपत्य|आनपत्यं
आनपत्य आनपत्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्-अपत्य),<BR>childlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनभिम्लात
आनभिम्लात आनभिम्लात, अस्, m. a descend-<BR>ant of An-abhimlāta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्
आनम् आ-नम्, cl. 1. P. -नमति, -नन्तुम्,<BR>to bend, bend down, bow, incline; to humble; to<BR>salute reverently: Caus. P. -नामयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनत|आनतः
आ-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, bending, stooping, bowed;<BR>pacified, conciliated; humbled; submissive, obedient;<BR>saluted reverently.<BR>—आनत-ज, आस्, m. pl. a class of<BR>divine beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनति|आनतिः
आ-नति, इस्, f. bending, bowing, stooping; saluting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम|आनमः
आ-नम, अस्, m. bending, stretching (a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनमित
आ-नमित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, bowed down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्य
1. आ-नम्य or आ-नाम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्य
2. आ-नम्य or आ-नत्य, ind. having bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्र
आ-नम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (3. आ prefixed in the sense of di-<BR>minution), a little bent, bowing, stooping, bowed down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनय|आनयः
आनय आ-नय, &c. See under आ-नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्त|आनर्तः|आनर्त्त|आनर्त्तः
आनर्त आ-नर्त, अस्, m. (fr. आ-नृत्, q. v.), a<BR>stage, a theatre; war; N. of a country and its in-<BR>habitants in the peninsula Gujarat with its capital<BR>Dvārakā or Kuśasthalī.<BR>—आनर्त-नगरी, f. the<BR>capital of Ānarta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्तीय|आनर्त्तीय
आनर्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or coming<BR>from Ānarta; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्थक्य|आनर्थक्यं
आनर्थक्य आनर्थक्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्-<BR>अर्थक), unfitness, impropriety; uselessness, un-<BR>profitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनलवि
आनलवि आनलवि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनव|आनवः
आनव आनव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु), Ved. kind<BR>to men, benevolent (?); human; (अस्), m. men,<BR>people; foreign men or people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनस
आनस आनस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनस्), Ved. be-<BR>longing to a waggon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनह्
आनह् आ-नह्, cl. 4. P. A. -नह्यति, -ते,<BR>-नद्धुम्, to bind to; A. to be stopped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्ध|आनद्धं|आनद्धः
आ-नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound, tied, costive; (अम्),<BR>n. a drum in general, dressing, putting on clothes or<BR>ornaments.<BR>—आनद्ध-वस्ति-ता, f. retention of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाह|आनाहः
आ-नाह, अस्, m. epistasis, suppression of urine, or<BR>constipation; length, especially of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाहिक
आनाहिक, अस्, ई, अम्, to be used in cases of epistasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाथ्य|आनाथ्यं
आनाथ्य आनाथ्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-नाथ), state<BR>of being unprotected or without a guardian, orphanism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिर्हत|आनिर्हतः
आनिर्हत आनिर्हत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-निर्हत),<BR>Ved. indestructible nature; (according to Mahī-dhara)<BR>wholly gone out of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिल|आनिलः
आनिल आनिल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनिल), pro-<BR>ceeding from or produced by wind, windy; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of Hanumat and Bhīma; (ई), f., N. of the fifteenth<BR>lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिलि|आनिलिः
आनिलि, इस्, m., N. of Hanumat and Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनी
आनी आ-नी, cl. 1. P. -नयति, -नेतुम्, to<BR>lead towards or near; to bring, fetch, bring back or<BR>take back: Caus. P. -नाययति, -यितुम्, to have<BR>anything brought, to cause to be fetched: Pass.<BR>-नीयते, to be brought or fetched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनय|आनयः
आ-नय, अस्, m. bringing, investiture with the<BR>sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयन|आनयनं
आ-नयन, अम्, n. bringing or leading near to;<BR>investiture with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयितव्य
आ-नयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought or led near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय|आनायः
1. आ-नाय, अस्, m. a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय|आनायः
2. आ-नाय, nom. A. आनायते, -यितुम्, to form or<BR>represent a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनायिन्
आनायिन्, ई, m. a fisherman, a fisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय्य|आनाय्यः
1. आ-नाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought near; (अस्),<BR>m. consecrated fire, taken from the Gārhapatya or<BR>household fire, and placed on the south side, whence<BR>it is called Dakṣiṇāgni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय्य|आनाय्यः
2. आ-नाय्य, ind. having caused to be brought,<BR>having caused to be introduced, having brought to-<BR>gether, having convened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीत
आ-नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken, brought, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीति|आनीतिः
आ-नीति, इस्, f. leading near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीय
आ-नीय, ind. having taken, having brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतव्य
आ-नेतव्य or आ-नेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought,<BR>to be fetched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतृ
आ-नेतृ, ता, m. a bringer, bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनील|आनीलः
आनील आ-नील, अस्, आ, अम्, darkish; slightly<BR>black or blue; (अस्), m. a black horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनु
आनु आ-नु, cl. 2. P. -नौति, -नवितुम् or<BR>-नुवितुम्, Ved. 1. A. -नवते, to sound, scream,<BR>warble: Intens. Ved. -नवीनोति, to sound through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकल्पिक
आनुकल्पिक आनुकल्पिक, अस्, m. one who<BR>knows the अनु-कल्प, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूलिक
आनुकूलिक आनुकूलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>कूल), favourable, conformable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूल्य|आनुकूल्यं
आनुकूल्य, अम्, n. conformity, suitableness; favour,<BR>kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकृष्ट
आनुकृष्ट आनुकृष्ट = अनु-कृष्ट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगत्य|आनुगत्यं
आनुगत्य आनुगत्य, अम्, n. (fr. अनु-गत),<BR>acquaintance, familiarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगतिक
आनुगतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगादिक
आनुगादिक आनुगादिक = अनु-गादिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुग्रामिक
आनुग्रामिक आनुग्रामिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>ग्राम), about or belonging to a village, rustic,<BR>rural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुजावर
आनुजावर आनुजावर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>जावर, rt. जन्), Ved. posthumous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुदृष्टिनेय
आनुदृष्टिनेय आनुदृष्टिनेय, अस्, m. a pa-<BR>tronymic from अनु-दृष्टि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुनासिक्य|आनुनासिक्यं
आनुनासिक्य आनुनासिक्य, अम्, n. (fr. अनु-<BR>नासिक), nasality (of a sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपदिक
आनुपदिक आनुपदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>पद), following, pursuing, tracking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व|आनुपूर्वं|आनुपूर्व्व
आनुपूर्व आनुपूर्व, अम्, ई, n. f. (fr. अनु-<BR>पूर्व), order, series, succession; (in law) direct<BR>order of the castes; (in logic) a conclusion, regularly<BR>or syllogistically deduced.<BR>—आनुपूर्वेण or आनुपूर्-<BR>व्या, ind. one after the other, in due order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्य|आनुपूर्व्यं
आनुपूर्व्य, अम्, n. order, series, succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुमत
आनुमत आनुमत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-मत,<BR>rt. मन्), relating to the consent or favour (of<BR>another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुमानिक|आनुमानिकः
आनुमानिक आनुमानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>मान, rt. मा), relating to a conclusion; derived<BR>from inference, subject to inference, inferable, inferred.<BR>—आनुमानिक-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being infer-<BR>able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुरक्ति|आनुरक्तिः
आनुरक्ति आनुरक्ति, इस्, f. passion, affection;<BR>the same as अनु-रक्ति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोम्य
आनुलोम्य आनुलोम्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>लोम), in the direction of the hair, produced in<BR>natural or direct order; (अम्), n. a direction similar<BR>to that of the hairs, natural or direct order; favour-<BR>able direction, fit disposition, favourableness; regular<BR>series or succession; bringing to one's right place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोमिक
आनुलोमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, regular, orderly, in due<BR>course or series; favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुविधित्सा
आनुविधित्सा आनुविधित्सा, f. (corrupted fr.<BR>अन्-अनुविधित्सा fr. rt. धा?), ingratitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुवेश्य|आनुवेश्यः
आनुवेश्य आनुवेश्य, अस्, m. (fr. अनु-वेश), a<BR>neighbour who lives in the same house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुशासनिक
आनुशासनिक आनुशासनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अनु-शासन), relating to or treating of instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुशूक
आनुशूक आनुशूक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-शूक),<BR>being with or within the awns (as rice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुश्रविक|आनुश्रविकः
आनुश्रविक आनुश्रविक or आनुश्राविक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. अनु-श्रव), according to hearing, resting on<BR>tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषक्
आनुषक् आनुषक्, ind. (fr. अनु-सञ्ज्, q. v.),<BR>Ved. in continuous order, uninterruptedly, one after<BR>the other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषङ्गिक|आनुषंगिक
आनुषङ्गिक, अस्, ई, अम्, connected with, con-<BR>comitant, necessarily following, adherent, inherent,<BR>implied; proportionate, like, analogous, relative;<BR>necessary as a result or consequence, inevitable; (in<BR>gram.) elliptical, including or agreeing with words not<BR>comprised in the sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषण्ड
आनुषण्ड आनुषण्ड or आनुषण्डक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्. See Gaṇa to Pāṇini IV. 2, 133. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषूक
आनुषूक आनुषूक, अस्, ई, अम् (either = आनु-<BR>शूक or fr. rt. सू ?), promoting, driving forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुष्टुभ
आनुष्टुभ आनुष्टुभ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनु-<BR>ष्टुभ्), consisting of Anuṣṭubhs, formed like the<BR>Anuṣṭubh metre (e. g. composed of four divisions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुसूय
आनुसूय आनुसूय, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from<BR>Anusūyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूकम्
आनूकम् आनूकम्, ind. (fr. आ-अनूकम् ?), Ved.<BR>in abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूप|आनूपः
आनूप आनूप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अनूप), wet,<BR>watery, marshy; (अस्), m. any animal frequenting<BR>watery or marshy places, as a buffalo, &c.<BR>—आनूप-<BR>मांस, अस्, m. the flesh or meat of animals fre-<BR>quenting marshes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूपक
आनूपक, अस्, ई, अम्, living or happening in<BR>marshy places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्य|आनृण्यं
आनृण्य आनृण्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्-ऋण), ac-<BR>quittance of debt or obligation, the not being indebted<BR>to (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृत्
आनृत् आ-नृत्, cl. 4. P. -नृत्यति, -नर्तितुम्,<BR>to dance towards, hasten near, dance: Caus. P. -नर्-<BR>तयति, -यितुम्, to agitate gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्त|आनर्तः|आनर्त्त|आनर्त्तः
आ-नर्त, अस्, m. a stage, theatre; war. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृत
आनृत आनृत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्-ऋत), un-<BR>truthful; (अस्), m., N. of a people (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृतक
आनृतक, अस्, ई, अम्, inhabited by the Ānṛtas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस
आनृशंस आनृशंस or आनृशंस्य, अम्, n.<BR>(fr. अ-नृशंस), mildness, kindness, mercy, com-<BR>passion; cruelty (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतव्य
आनेतव्य आ-नेतव्य, आ-नेय. See under आ-नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैपुण|आनैपुणं
आनैपुण आनैपुण, अम्, n. (fr. अ-निपुण),<BR>clumsiness, stupidity; = अ-नैपुण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैश्वर्य|आनैश्वर्यं|आनैश्वर्य्य
आनैश्वर्य आनैश्वर्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्-ईश्वर),<BR>absence of power or supremacy. See अन्-ऐश्वर्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त 1. आन्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अम्), gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त 2. आन्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्त), final,<BR>terminal, relating to the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्य|आंत्यः|आन्त्यः
आन्त्य, अस्, m., Ved. one who finishes; personified<BR>as Bhauvana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तम्
आन्तम् आन्तम्, ind. (fr. आ + अन्तम्), to the<BR>end, completely, from head to foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरतम्य|आंतरतम्यं
आन्तरतम्य आन्तरतम्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्त-<BR>रतम), nearest or closest relationship (as of two<BR>letters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्य|आंतर्यं|आन्तर्य्य
आन्तर्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्तर), near relationship<BR>(of two letters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरिक्ष|आंतरिक्ष
आन्तरिक्ष आन्तरिक्ष or आन्तरीक्ष, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. अन्तरिक्ष), belonging to the intermediate<BR>space between earth and heaven, atmospherical, hea-<BR>venly, celestial, produced in the atmosphere; (अम्),<BR>n. the firmament, the intermediate region between<BR>earth and sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्गणिक|आंतर्गणिक
आन्तर्गणिक आन्तर्गणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्तर्-<BR>गण), included, comprehended (as in a class or troop).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्गेहिक|आंतर्गेहिक
आन्तर्गेहिक आन्तर्गेहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्तर्-<BR>गेह), being inside a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्वेश्मिक
आन्तर्वेश्मिक आन्तर्वेश्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अन्तर्-वेश्मन्), produced or occurring within a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तिका|आंतिका
आन्तिका आन्तिका, f. an elder sister. See<BR>अन्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्र|आंत्र
आन्त्र आन्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. the bowels, entrails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्रिक|आंत्रिक|आन्त्रिकः
आन्त्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, visceral, within, or relating<BR>to the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्द
आन्द आन्द, अस्, m., N. of a despised class<BR>of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलय्
आन्दोलय् आन्दोलय्, cl. 10. P. आन्दोलयति,<BR>यितुम्, to swing. See अन्दोलय्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोल|आंदोलः|आन्दोलः
आन्दोल, अस्, m. swinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलन|आंदोलनं|आन्दोलनं
आन्दोलन, अम्, n. swinging, a swing; trembling,<BR>oscillation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलित|आन्दोलितं
आन्दोलित, अस्, आ, अम्, swung, shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धस|आंधसः|आन्धसः
आन्धस आन्धस, अस्, m. (fr. अन्धस्, q. v.),<BR>the scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धसिक|आंधसिकः|आन्धसिकः
आन्धसिक, अस्, m. a cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्य|आंध्यं
आन्ध्य आन्ध्य, अम्, n. (fr. अन्ध), blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्र|आंध्र|आन्ध्रः
आन्ध्र आन्ध्र, आस्, m. pl. the Telugu country,<BR>Telingana, see अन्ध्र; (अस्, आ, अम्), anything re-<BR>lating to this country (as the Telugu language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्न
आन्न आन्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्न), fed, having<BR>food; relating to food, derived from it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्यतरेय|आन्यतरेयः
आन्यतरेय आन्यतरेय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वयिक|आन्वयिकः
आन्वयिक आन्वयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्व्-अय),<BR>of a good family, well born; orderly, according to<BR>order or arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वाहिक
आन्वाहिक आन्वाहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अन्व्-<BR>अहम्), daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वीक्षिकी
आन्वीक्षिकी आन्वीक्षिकी, f. (fr. अन्व्-ईक्षा),<BR>logic, logical philosophy, metaphysics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्
आप् आप्, cl. 5. 1. P. आप्नोति or आपति, आप,<BR>आप्स्यति, आपत्, आप्तुम्, to reach, over-<BR>take, meet with, fall upon; to obtain, gain, take<BR>possession of, undergo, suffer; to enter, pervade,<BR>occupy, to equal: Pass. आप्यते, to be reached, found,<BR>met with, obtained; to arrive at one's aim or end,<BR>become filled: Caus. P. आपयति, -यितुम्, aor. आपिपत्,<BR>to cause to reach or obtain or gain; to cause any<BR>one to feel; to hit: Desid. P. ईप्सति, to strive to<BR>reach or obtain: Desid. of the Caus. आपिपयिषति,<BR>to strive to reach; [cf. Lat. apio, aptus; adipiscor:<BR>Old Germ. uoban: Mod. Germ. üben.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
1. आप, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of compounds; e. g.<BR>दुर्-आप, difficult to be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन|आपनं
आपन, अम्, n. reaching, obtaining; pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनेय
आपनेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be reached or obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपयितृ
आपयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who procures, procuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपि|आपिः
आपि, इस्, m., Ved. an ally, a friend, an acquaintance.<BR>—आपि-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. confederation, friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, reached, overtaken, equalled;<BR>got, gained, obtained; reaching to, extending; abun-<BR>dant, full; apt, fit, true, exact, clever, trusted, trust-<BR>worthy, confidential; intimate, related, acquainted;<BR>appointed; generally received; commonly used; au-<BR>thentic; accused, prosecuted; (अस्), m. a fit person,<BR>a credible person, a warranter, guarantee; a friend;<BR>an Arhat; N. of a Nāga; (आ), f. a twisted band or<BR>lock of hair; (अम्), n. a quotient; equation of a<BR>degree.<BR>—आप्त-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>gained his wish, satisfied.<BR>—आप्त-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>managing things in a fit or confidential manner; (ई),<BR>m. a trusty agent, a confidential servant.<BR>—आप्त-<BR>गर्भा, f. a pregnant woman.<BR>—आप्त-गर्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, proud, arrogant.<BR>—आप्त-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having proper gifts, or furnished with gifts.<BR>—आप्त-<BR>वचन, अम्, n. received text, revelation, authority.<BR>—आप्त-वज्र-सूचि, इस्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—आप्त-वाक्य, अम्, n. a correct sentence.<BR>—आप्त-<BR>वाच्, क्, f. the evidence of a credible person; (क्), m.<BR>one whose evidence is credible.<BR>—आप्तोक्ति (˚त-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. augment or affix; a word of received acceptation<BR>and established by usage only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तव्य
आप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be reached, obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्ति|आप्तिः
आप्ति, इस्, f. reaching, meeting with; obtaining,<BR>gain, acquisition; binding, connection, relation, fit-<BR>ness, aptitude; (अयस्), f. pl., N. of twelve sacrificial<BR>verses beginning with आपये (dat. case of आपि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
1. आप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, obtainable. See आप्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
2. आप्य, अम्, n., Ved. confederation, alliance, re-<BR>lationship, friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
आप 2. आप, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with अप्, आपस्, q. v.), N. of one of the eight demi-<BR>gods called Vasus. (For 1. आप see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपकर
आपकर आपकर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अप-कर),<BR>offensive, mischievous, unfriendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक्व|आपक्वं
आपक्व आ-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. पच् with 3. आ,<BR>implying diminution), half-baked, crude, raw; nearly<BR>ripe, not quite ripe; undressed, what is eaten without<BR>further preparation (as bread &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगा
आपगा आपगा, f. (fr. rt. गा with अप ?), a<BR>river, a stream; N. of a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगेय|आपगेयः
आपगेय, अस्, m. the son of a river; an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपट्
आपट् आ-पट्, cl. 10. P. -पाटयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to split; to sever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपण|आपणः
आपण आ-पण, अस्, m. (rt. पण् with आ), a<BR>market, a shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणिक|आपणिकः
आपणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, mercantile, relating to traffic,<BR>to a market &c.; (अस्), m. a merchant, a dealer, a<BR>shop-keeper; tax on markets or shops; assize, market-<BR>rate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्
आपत् आ-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -तितुम्, to fly<BR>towards, to come flying, to come in haste, to rush<BR>in or on; to assail; to approach; to fall to one's<BR>share, to befal, happen: Caus. P. -पातयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to throw down, let fall, shed; -पतयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to go towards, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतत्
आ-पतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, approaching, preparing to<BR>assail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतन|आपतनं
आ-पतन, अम्, n. coming, approaching; descend-<BR>ing, alighting, happening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपति|आपतिः
आ-पति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. coming in haste, rushing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिक|आपतिकः
आ-पतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, accidental, unforeseen, sent<BR>from heaven; (अस्), m. a hawk. a falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतित
आ-पतित, अस्, आ, अम्, happened, befallen; alighted,<BR>descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आ-पात, अस्, आ, अम्, rushing upon, attacking, ap-<BR>proaching; (अस्), m. rushing upon, pressing against,<BR>falling, descending; throwing down; causing to de-<BR>scend; happening, becoming apparent, appearance;<BR>the instant, the current moment; (अतस्), ind. at the<BR>first attack, instantly, immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातिन्
आ-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling on, descending, happening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतालिका
आपतालिका आपतालिका, f. (fr. अप-ताल?),<BR>N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्य
आपत्य आपत्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अपत्य), relat-<BR>ing to offspring; (in gram.) relating to the formation<BR>of patronymic nouns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथि|आपथिः
आपथि आ-पथि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. पथिन् with आ),<BR>Ved. being on the way or on a voyage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथी
आ-पथी, ईस्, or आ-पथ्य, अस्, m., Ved. a traveller,<BR>wanderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् 1. आ-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते, -पत्तुम्,<BR>to come, walk towards; to enter into, attain; to get<BR>into trouble, fall into misfortune; to happen: Caus.<BR>P. -पादयति, -यितुम्, to bring on, bring to pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्ति|आपत्तिः
आ-पत्ति, इस्, f. entering into a state or condition,<BR>entering into relationship with anything, changing<BR>into; obtaining, procuring; misfortune, calamity,<BR>fault, transgression; remonstrance, expostulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
2. आ-पद्, त्, f. misfortune, calamity; [cf. Hib.<BR>âpadh, ‘death;’ âpthach, ‘mortal.’]<BR>—आपत्-काल,<BR>अस्, m. season of distress.<BR>—आपत्कालिक, अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, occurring in a time of calamity, belonging to<BR>such a time.<BR>—आपत्-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unfortunate,<BR>unhappy, afflicted.<BR>—आपद्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen<BR>into misfortune.<BR>—आपद्-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, seized<BR>by misfortune, unfortunate, unhappy, in misfortune.<BR>—आपद्-धर्म, अस्, m. practice or profession<BR>other than that proper to caste, but allowable in time<BR>of distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपदा
आ-पदा, f. misfortune, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्न|आपन्नः
आ-पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, gained, obtained, acquired;<BR>afflicted, unfortunate.<BR>—आपन्न-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>impregnated, pregnant; (आ), f. a pregnant woman.<BR>—आपन्नार्ति-प्रशमन-फल (˚न-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fruitful in the relieving of the pains of the<BR>afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाद|आपादः
आ-पाद, अस्, m. reward, remuneration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपादन|आपादनं
आ-पादन, अम्, n. causing to arrive at, leading to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन|आपनं
आपन आपन, आपनेय. See under rt. आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनिक|आपनिकः
आपनिक आपनिक, अस्, m. an emerald; a<BR>kirāta or barbarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपमित्यक|आपमित्यकं
आपमित्यक आपमित्यक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अप-<BR>मित्य, rt. मा with अप; cf. अप-मित्यक), received<BR>by barter; (अम्), n. property &c. obtained by barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपया
आपया आपया, f., Ved., N. of a river near<BR>the Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपयितृ
आपयितृ आपयितृ. See under rt. आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपराह्णिक
आपराह्णिक आपराह्णिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अपराह्ण), occurring in the afternoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपर्तुक|आपर्त्तुक
आपर्तुक आपर्तुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अप-ऋतु),<BR>not bound to fixed times, not restricted to particular<BR>seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपव|आपवः
आपव आपव, अस्, m. an epithet of Vaśiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपवर्ग्य
आपवर्ग्य आपवर्ग्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अप-<BR>वर्ग), conferring final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्
आपस् आपस्, n. a religious ceremony;<BR>water (see अप्); sin [cf. अपस्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्कार|आपस्कारं
आपस्कार आपस्कार, अम्, n. (fr. अप-स्कर),<BR>the root or extremity of the trunk or body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्तम्ब
आपस्तम्ब आपस्तम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a re-<BR>nowned sage and writer on ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्तम्बि
आपस्तम्बि, इस्, m. a patronymic from the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्तम्भिनी
आपस्तम्भिनी आपस्तम्भिनी, f., N. of a plant,<BR>perhaps Eriocaulon Quinquangulare Lin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपा
आपा आ-पा, cl. 1. P. -पिबति or -पिवति,<BR>पातुम्, to drink up, to drink out of or at; to drink<BR>with the ears or eyes, hear, see: Caus. -पाययति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपान|आपानं
आ-पान, अम्, n. a drinking-party, a banquet; a<BR>tavern, a liquor shop, a place for drinking in company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपान्तमन्यु
आपान्त-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. giving zeal or<BR>courage when drunk (said of the Soma juice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपायिन्
आ-पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fond of drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
1. आ-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, drunk up, exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाक|आपाकः
आपाक आ-पाक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पच् with आ),<BR>a baking oven, a potter's kiln.<BR>—आपाके-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. standing in an oven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाङ्ग्य|आपांग्यं
आपाङ्ग्य आपाङ्ग्य, अम्, n. (fr. अपाङ्ग),<BR>anointing the corners of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाण्डुर
आपाण्डुर आ-पाण्डुर, अस्, आ, अम्, slightly<BR>pale, palish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आपात आ-पात. See under आ-पत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाद|आपादः
आपाद आ-पाद, आ-पादन. See under आ-पद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपालि|आपालिः
आपालि आ-पालि, इस्, m. a louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपि|आपिः
आपि आपि. See under rt. आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिञ्जर|आपिंजर|आपिञ्जरं
आपिञ्जर आ-पिञ्जर, अस्, आ, अम्, somewhat<BR>red, reddish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिश्
आपिश् आ-पिश्, cl. 6. P., Ved. -पिंशति, -पेशि-<BR>तुम्, to shape, configurate; to decorate, ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशलि|आपिशलिः
आपिशलि आपिशलि, इस्, m., N. of an old<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशल|आपिशलः
आपिशल, अस्, ई, अम्, originating from Āpiśali; (अस्),<BR>m. a pupil of Āpiśali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिष्
आपिष् आ-पिष्, cl. 7. P., Ved. -पिनष्टि,<BR>-पेष्टुम्, to press, touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी आपी, आपीन आ-पीन. See आ-प्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड्
आपीड् आ-पीड्, cl. 10. P. -पीडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to press, weigh down; to press hard, give pain, per-<BR>plex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड|आपीडः
आ-पीड, अस्, m. compressing, squeezing; giving<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">Page0123-c+ 69</a>]<BR>pain, hurting; a chaplet tied on the crown of the<BR>head; (आ), f., N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडन|आपीडनं
आ-पीडन, अम्, n. compressing, squeezing, tying<BR>or drawing tightly; embracing, clasping; giving pain,<BR>hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडित
आ-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, compressed, squeezed;<BR>bound tightly, embraced; hurt; decorated with<BR>chaplets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
आपीत 2. आ-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, yellowish;<BR>(अम्), n. a pyritic mineral. (For 1. आ-पीत see under<BR>आ-पा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपू
आपू आ-पू, cl. 1. A. -पवते, -वितुम्, to be<BR>pure; to flow towards after purification; to carry<BR>towards in its course (said of a stream).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिक|आपूपिकं|आपूपिकः
आपूपिक आपूपिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अपूप),<BR>selling cakes; accustomed to eat cakes; fond of cakes,<BR>eating cakes (with benefit); a good maker of cake;<BR>(अस्), m. a baker; a confectioner; (अम्), n. a mul-<BR>titude of cakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूप्य|आपूप्यः
आपूप्य, अम्, n. flour, meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूय्
आपूय् आ-पूय्, cl. 1. P. -पूयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>be putrescent, putrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूष|आपूषं
आपूष आपूष, अम्, n. tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्
आपृच् आ-पृच्, cl. 7. P. A. -पृणक्ति, -पृङ्क्ते,<BR>-पर्चितुम्, to fill, pervade; A. to satiate one's self; to<BR>mix with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृक्
आ-पृक्, ind., Ved. in a mixed manner, confusedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छा
आपृच्छा आ-पृच्छा, &c. See under आ-प्रछ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपॄ
आपॄ आ-पॄ, Caus. P. -पूरयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>fill, fulfil: Pass. -पूर्यते, to be filled, become full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर|आपूरः
आ-पूर, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूरण
आ-पूरण, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming full; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Nāga; (अम्), n. filling, making full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्ति|आपूर्तिः|आपूर्त्ति|आपूर्त्तिः
आ-पूर्ति, इस्, f. filling; fulness, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्य
आ-पूर्य, ind. filling, having filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्यमाण|आपूर्य्यमाण
आ-पूर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming full, being<BR>filled.<BR>—आपूर्यमाण-पक्ष, अस्, m. the crescent<BR>or waxing moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपेक्षिक
आपेक्षिक आपेक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अपेक्षा),<BR>raising expectations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोक्लिम|आपोक्लिमं
आपोक्लिम आपोक्लिम, अस्, m., in astronomy<BR>= Gr. ἀπόκλιμα<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोमय
आपोमय आपो-मय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. आपस्, nom.<BR>pl. of अप्, q. v.), consisting of water.<BR>—आपो-मात्रा,<BR>f. the subtle elementary principle of water.<BR>—आपो-<BR>मूर्ति, इस्, m., N. of a deity under Manu Svārociṣa,<BR>one of the seven Ṛṣis of the tenth Manvantara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोशान|आपोशानः
आपोशान आपोशान, अस्, m., N. of a kind of<BR>prayer spoken before and after eating; perhaps con-<BR>tracted from आपो ऽशान, ‘drink the water,’ with<BR>which words the prayer began.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त, आप्ति, आप्तोक्ति, &c. See under rt. आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तोर्यामन्
आप्तोर्यामन् आप्तोर्-यामन्. See अप्तोर्-याम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त्य|आप्त्यः
आप्त्य आप्त्य, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a class of<BR>deities, and especially of the deity Trita, as one of<BR>that class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य 3. आप्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अप्), belonging<BR>or relating to water; watery; consisting of water;<BR>living in water. (For 1. 2. आप्य see under rt. आप्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य 4. आप्य, अस्, m. (for आप्त्य), N. of a<BR>class of deities in the sixth Manvantara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य 5. आप्य, अम्, n., N. of a plant, a kind<BR>of Costus. See वाप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यै
आप्यै आ-प्यै, cl. 1. A. -प्यायते, -प्यातुम्,<BR>to grow fat or comfortable, to increase, become full,<BR>enlarge: Caus. P. -प्याययति, -यितुम्, to make fat<BR>or comfortable; to enlarge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी, ईस्, f. the twentieth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आ-पीन, अस्, आ, अम्, stout, fat; (अस्), m. a well;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">Page0124-a+ 76</a>]<BR>(अम्), n. an udder.<BR>—आपीन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>containing the rt. प्यै with आ (said of a ऋच् or<BR>verse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यान
आ-प्यान, अस्, आ, अम्, stout, robust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्याय|आप्यायः
आ-प्याय, अस्, m. becoming full or fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायन|आप्यायनं
आप्यायन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing fulness or stout-<BR>ness, increasing welfare; (अम्), n. the act of making<BR>full or fat; satisfying, refreshing, pleasing; satiety,<BR>satisfaction; advancing; anything which causes cor-<BR>pulency or good condition; strengthening medicine;<BR>corpulency, growing or being fat or stout; (in certain<BR>ceremonies) the act of pouring water &c. on the<BR>Soma and so causing it to swell.<BR>—आप्यायन-शील,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायित|आप्यायितः
आ-प्यायित, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied, increased, im-<BR>proved, pleased, gratified; stout, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्र
आप्र आप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. पॄ with आ ?),<BR>Ved. busy, zealous; (Sāy.) able to reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रछ्|आप्रच्छ्
आप्रछ् आ-प्रछ्, cl. 6. A. or poet. P. -पृच्-<BR>छते, -ति, -प्रष्टुम्, to bid farewell; to salute on<BR>receiving or parting with a visitor; to extol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छा
आ-पृच्छा, f. conversation, speaking to or with;<BR>bidding farewell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छ्य|आपृछ्य
1. आ-पृच्छ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be saluted, to<BR>be welcomed, to be honoured; laudable, commendable,<BR>beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छ्य|आपृछ्य
2. आ-पृच्छ्य, ind. having saluted, having bid adieu.<BR>(In Rāmāyaṇa I. 72, 20, a form आ-पृष्ट्वा occurs.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छन|आप्रच्छनं
आ-प्रच्छन, अम्, n. expressions of civility on re-<BR>ceiving or parting with a visitor, welcome, bidding<BR>adieu, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रतिनिवृत्त
आप्रतिनिवृत्त आ-प्रतिनिवृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, pre-<BR>vented, turned back (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रदिवम्
आप्रदिवम् आ-प्रदिवम्, ind., Ved. for ever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपद|आप्रपदं
आप्रपद आ-प्रपद, अम्, n. a dress reaching<BR>to the feet; (अम्), ind. to the end of the foot,<BR>reaching to the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीन|आप्रपदीनं
आप्रपदीन, अस्, आ, अम्, reaching from the shoulders<BR>to the feet (as a dress).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीनक
आप्रपदीनक, अम्, n. a dress reaching to the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रावृषम्
आप्रावृषम् आ-प्रावृषम्, ind. until the<BR>rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्री
आप्री आ-प्री, f. (fr. rt. प्री with आ), Ved.<BR>gaining one's favour, conciliation, propitiation; (आ-प्रि-<BR>यस्), propitiatory verses; N. of certain invocations<BR>addressed to a series of deified objects in order, and<BR>said to be introductory to the animal sacrifice. Accord-<BR>ing to others, the objects propitiated by these hymns<BR>are the real āprīs or आप्रियस्; whence the hymns<BR>themselves are called आप्री hymns. The objects in-<BR>voked are in a series of twelve verses, as follows:<BR>1. Su-samiddha (or the fuel); 2. and 3. Tanūnapāt<BR>and Narāśaṃsa (these are sometimes invoked in one<BR>verse as mystic names of fire); 4. The divine being<BR>who bears the invocations to the gods (see under इड्);<BR>5. Barhis (or the sacred grass); 6. The doors of the<BR>chambers in which the sacrifice is offered; 7. Night<BR>and dawn; 8. The two divine beings, sometimes<BR>called Pracetasas, who preside over and protect the<BR>sacrificial rite; 9. The three goddesses, Ilā (see under<BR>इडा), Sarasvatī (goddess of eloquence), and Mahī (a<BR>form of Bhāratī or speech); 10. Tvaṣṭṛ (the maker<BR>or creator); 11. Vanas-pati (the tree or wooden column<BR>to which the victim is tied); 12. Svāhā (the exclama-<BR>tion used in inviting the gods to the sacrifice when<BR>finally offered in the fire). All these are by Sāy. re-<BR>garded as forms of Agni. See Ṛg-veda I. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रीतपा
आ-प्रीत-पा, आस्, m., Ved. epithet of Viṣṇu, ‘guard-<BR>ing those who have appeased his anger.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लु
आप्लु आ-प्लु, cl. 1. A. -प्लवते, -प्लोतुम्, to<BR>bathe, wash, immerse one's self; to jump up, dance:<BR>Caus. P. -प्लावयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be bathed<BR>or washed; to wash or wet; to overflow, overwhelm;<BR>to set in commotion; A. -प्लावयते, to bathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लव|आप्लवः
आ-प्लव, अस्, m. bathing, sprinkling with water.<BR>—आप्लव-व्रतिन्, ई, m. an initiated householder,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">Page0124-b+ 71</a>]<BR>who has passed through the first order (Brahma-cārin),<BR>and is admitted into the second. See स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवन|आप्लवनं
आ-प्लवन, अम्, n. immersing, bathing, sprinkling<BR>with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लाव|आप्लावः
आ-प्लाव, अस्, m. bathing, sprinkling, wetting; a<BR>submerging; a flood, an inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लावित
आ-प्लावित, अस्, आ, अम्, inundated, overflowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लाव्य
आ-प्लाव्य, ind. having wetted or sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत|आप्लुतः
आ-प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, bathed; wetted, sprinkled.<BR>In comp. sometimes used figuratively (e. g. स्नेहा-<BR>प्लुत, overflowing with affection); (अस्), m. an ini-<BR>tiated householder, see आप्लव-व्रतिन्; (अम्), n.<BR>bathing.<BR>—आप्लुत-व्रतिन्, ई, m. an initiated house-<BR>holder; see आप्लव-व्रतिन्.<BR>—आप्लुताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, bathed all over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत्य
आ-प्लुत्य, ind. having bathed, having washed;<BR>having jumped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वन्
आप्वन् आप्वन्, आ, m. (fr. rt. आप्), air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वा
आप्वा, f. the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्सव
आप्सव आप्सव, अस्, m. (fr. अप्सु, loc. pl. of<BR>अप्), epithet of a Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आफूक|आफूकं
आफूक आफूक, अम्, n. opium. See 2.<BR>अ-फेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्ध्|आबंध्
आबन्ध् आ-बन्ध्, cl. 9. P. -बध्नाति, -बन्द्-<BR>धुम्, to bind or tie on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्ध|आबद्धः
आ-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, tied, bound, joined; (अस्),<BR>m. a binding, a yoke; ornament; affection.<BR>—आबद्-<BR>ध-माल, अस्, आ, अम्, forming a wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबध|आबधः
आ-बध, अस्, m., Ved. binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्ध|आबंधः|आबन्धः
आ-बन्ध, अस्, m. a tie or bond; the tie of a<BR>yoke, that which fastens the ox to the yoke, or the<BR>latter to the plough; ornament, decoration; affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्धन|आबंधनं
आ-बन्धन, अम्, n. tying, binding on or round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबयु
आबयु आबयु, उस्, Ved., perhaps the N. of<BR>a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्ह|आबर्हः
आबर्ह आ-बर्ह, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. वृह् or बृह्<BR>with आ), having the property or power of tearing or<BR>pulling out; (अस्), m. tearing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हण
आ-बर्हण, अम्, n. the act of tearing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हिन्
आ-बर्हिन्, ई, इणी, इ, fit for tearing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबल्य|आबल्यं
आबल्य आबल्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-बल), weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाध्
आबाध् आ-बाध्, cl. 1. A. -बाधते, -धितुम्,<BR>to check, rein in, restrain; to interrupt, molest, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाध|आबाधः
आ-बाध, अस्, m., Ved. attack; molestation, trouble,<BR>interruption, damage; (आ), f. pain, distress, segment<BR>of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाल्य|आबाल्यं
आबाल्य आ-बाल्य, अम्, n. age ending with<BR>infancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबिलम्
आबिलम् आ-बिलम्, ind., Ved. to the hole or<BR>aperture [cf. विल].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुत्त|आबुत्तः
आबुत्त आबुत्त, अस्, m. (perhaps corrupted<BR>fr. आर्य-पुत्र), a sister's husband (in theatrical lan-<BR>guage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुध्
आबुध् आ-बुध्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -बोधति,<BR>-बोद्धुम्, to perceive, notice, understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबोधन|आबोधनं
आ-बोधन, अम्, n. knowledge, understanding;<BR>instructing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्दिक
आब्दिक आब्दिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अब्द), annual,<BR>yearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभज्
आभज् आ-भज्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -भजति, -भक्-<BR>तुम्, to make one share, cause one to partake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभग|आभगः
आ-भग, अस्, m., Ved. a partaker of (with loc.);<BR>(Sāy.) to be shared in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरण|आभरणं
आभरण आ-भरण, अम्, n. See under<BR>आ-भृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा 1. आ-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति, -तुम्, to<BR>shine, blaze; to irradiate; to outshine; to appear, to<BR>look like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
2. आ-भा, f. splendor, light; a flash; colour, appear-<BR>ance, beauty; a reflected image, shade; likeness,<BR>resemblance: (अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of compounds)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">Page0124-c+ 72</a>]<BR>like, resembling, appearing; e. g. हेमाभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, shining like gold; [cf. Hib. aoibh, ‘likeness,<BR>similitude;’ aoibe, ‘neatness, elegance;’ aoibheal,<BR>‘a spark of fire.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाति|आभातिः
आ-भाति, इस्, f. splendor, light; shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्
आभाष् आ-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भाषते, -षितुम्,<BR>to address, speak to; to talk, shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष|आभाषः
आ-भाष, अस्, m. addressing; introduction, preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषण|आभाषणं
आ-भाषण, अम्, n. addressing, speaking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्य
1. आ-भाष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be addressed, worthy<BR>of being spoken to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्य
2. आ-भाष्य, ind. having addressed, having<BR>spoken to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् 1. आ-भास्, cl. 1. A. -भासते, -सितुम्,<BR>to shine, blaze; to be bright: Caus. -भासयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
2. आ-भास्, f. splendor, lustre, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास|आभासः
आ-भास, अस्, m. splendor, light, colour, appear-<BR>ance; semblance, phantom; mere appearance; falla-<BR>cious appearance; reflection; intention, purpose; (in<BR>logic) fallacy, semblance of a reason, sophism, an erro-<BR>neous though plausible argument (regarded by logi-<BR>cians as of various kinds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासन|आभासनं
आ-भासन, अम्, n. illuminating, making apparent<BR>or clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासुर|आभासुरः
आ-भासुर, अस्, m., N. of a class of deities or demi-<BR>gods, sixty in number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्वर|आभास्वरः
आ-भास्वर, अस्, m. a demi-god, of a class consist-<BR>ing of sixty-four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचरणिक
आभिचरणिक आभिचरणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अभि-चरण), maledictory, imprecatory, serving for<BR>malediction or cursing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचारिक
आभिचारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभि-चार), magical,<BR>relating to magic; (अम्), n. incantation, magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजन|आभिजनः
आभिजन आभिजन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभि-जन,<BR>rt. जन्), relating to descent; (अम्), n. loftiness of<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजात्य|आभिजात्यं
आभिजात्य, अम्, n. (fr. अभि-जात, rt. जन्), the<BR>nature or state of a man of noble birth, nobility;<BR>birth, family, rank, learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजित
आभिजित आभिजित, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभि-जित्),<BR>born under the constellation Abhijit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधा
आभिधा आभिधा, f. or आभिधातक, अम्, n.<BR>a sound, a word, a name. See अभि-धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानिक|आभिधानिकः
आभिधानिक, अस्, ई, अम्, contained in a dictionary,<BR>lexicographical; (अस्), m. a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानीयक
आभिधानीयक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभि-धान), re-<BR>lating or belonging to a name or word; (अम्), n. the<BR>property of a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिप्लविक
आभिप्लविक आभिप्लविक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभि-<BR>प्लव), relating to the religious ceremony called<BR>Abhi-plava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमुख्य|आभिमुख्यं
आभिमुख्य आभिमुख्य, अम्, n. (fr. अभि-<BR>मुख), direction towards anything; wish or desire<BR>directed towards anything; presence, being in front<BR>of or face to face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिषेचनिक
आभिषेचनिक आभिषेचनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अभि-षेचन), relating to the inauguration of a king;<BR>serving for it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिहारिक
आभिहारिक आभिहारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभि-<BR>हार), taken by force or fraud; (अम्), n. a room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक|आभीकं
आभीक आभीक, अम्, n., N. of a Sāma<BR>melody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक्ष्ण|आभीक्ष्णं
आभीक्ष्ण आभीक्ष्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभीक्ष्ण),<BR>much, exceeding, eternal; (अम्), ind. exceedingly,<BR>eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक्ष्ण्य|आभीक्ष्ण्यं
आभीक्ष्ण्य, अम्, n. continued repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीय
आभीय आभीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. आ-भात्, ‘up<BR>to भ’), contained in a chapter of Pāṇini which<BR>ends with भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीर|आभीरः
आभीर आभीर, अस्, m., N. of a people; a<BR>cowherd sprung from a Brāhman and female of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">Page0125-a+ 71</a>]<BR>Ambaṣṭha or medical tribe; N. of a metre; (ई),<BR>f. a cowherd's wife or woman of the Ābhīra tribe;<BR>the language of the Ābhīra.<BR>—आभीर-पल्लि, इस् or ई<BR>or इका, f. a station of herdsmen, a village inhabited<BR>by cowherds only, an abode of cowherds &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभील|आभीलं|आभीलः
आभील आ-भील, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. भी with<BR>आ), formidable, fearful; suffering pain; (अम्), n.<BR>bodily pain; [cf. Hib. abhéil, ‘terrible, dreadful.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभु
आभु आभु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. empty; one<BR>whose hands are empty; stingy; (Sāy.) pervading,<BR>reaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूक
आभूक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. empty, having no con-<BR>tents, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभुग्न
आभुग्न आ-भुग्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 1. भुज् with<BR>3. आ implying diminution), a little curved or bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
आभू 1. आ-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्,<BR>to be present, continue one's existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
2. आ-भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. strong, sufficient, effica-<BR>cious; (Sāy.) approaching (as a praiser); a prison, a<BR>place of confinement; applied according to rule (as a<BR>hymn); very prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूति|आभूतिः
आ-भूति, इस्, f., Ved. capability, efficiency; (Sāy.)<BR>overpowering strength; (इस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूषेण्य
आ-भूषेण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be obeyed;<BR>(Sāy.) praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूष्
आभूष् आ-भूष्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -भूषति,<BR>-षितुम्, to adorn, to adorn with one's presence, i. e.<BR>to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभृ
आभृ आ-भृ, cl. 1. P., Ved. -भरति, -भर्-<BR>तुम्, to bring; to carry; to bear; to support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरण|आभरणं
आ-भरण, अम्, n. ornament, decoration (as jewels<BR>&c.); act of nourishing; title of several works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरत्
आ-भरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bringing.<BR>—आभरद्-<BR>वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. bringing property, goods, &c.;<BR>(उस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभेरी
आभेरी आभेरी, f. one of the Rāgiṇīs or<BR>modes of music, personified as a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोग|आभोगः
आभोग 1. आ-भोग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. भुज्,<BR>to curve, bend, with prep. आ), winding, curving,<BR>curve, crease; crumpling; circuit, circumference, en-<BR>virons, extension, fulness, expanse; a serpent; the<BR>expanded hood of the Cobra Capella (used by Varuṇa<BR>as his umbrella); effort, pains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोग|आभोगः
आभोग 2. आ-भोग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. भुज्,<BR>to eat, enjoy), enjoyment, satiety, fulness, comple-<BR>tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगय
आ-भोगय, अम्, n., Ved. means of supporting life,<BR>livelihood; (Sāy.) to be enjoyed (as Soma juice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगि|आभोगिः
आ-भोगि, इस्, f., Ved. living, supporting life; (Sāy.)<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यन्तर|आभ्यंतर|आभ्यन्तरः
आभ्यन्तर आभ्यन्तर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभ्य्-<BR>अन्तर), being inside, interior, inner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यवकाशिक
आभ्यवकाशिक आभ्यवकाशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अभ्य्-अवकाश), living in the open air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्याशिक
आभ्याशिक आभ्याशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभ्य्-<BR>आश), being near to each other, neighbouring; (less<BR>correctly in this sense written आभ्यासिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यासिक
आभ्यासिक आभ्यासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभ्य्-<BR>आस), resulting from practice, practising, repeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिक|आभ्युदयिकं
आभ्युदयिक आभ्युदयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>अभ्य्-उदय), connected with the rising or begin-<BR>ning of anything; relating to or granting prosperity;<BR>high, exalted, important; (अम्), n. a Śrāddha or offer-<BR>ing to ancestors on occasions of rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्रिक
आभ्रिक आभ्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अभ्रि), one<BR>who digs with a spade or a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्
आम् आम्, ind. an interjection of assent or<BR>recollection, (a vocative following this particle is अनु-<BR>दात्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम 1. आम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. अम्?), raw,<BR>uncooked (the opposite to पक्व, q. v.; in the Veda<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">Page0125-b+ 75</a>]<BR>often an epithet of the cow considered as the raw<BR>material which produces the milk); unbaked, unan-<BR>nealed; undressed; unripe, immature; undigested;<BR>(अम्), n. condition of being raw; constipation, pass-<BR>ing hard and unhealthy excretions; grain freed from<BR>chaff; [cf. Gr. ὠμό-ς Hib. amh, ‘raw, unsodden,<BR>crude, unripe.’]<BR>—आम-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a water-jar<BR>of unbaked clay.<BR>—आम-गन्धि, n. smell of raw<BR>meat or of a burning corpse.<BR>—आम-गन्धिक, अम्,<BR>n. the smell of raw meat.<BR>—आम-ता, f. rawness, un-<BR>readiness.<BR>—आम-त्वच्, क्, क्, क्, tender-skinned.<BR>—आम-पात्र, अम्, n. an unannealed vessel.<BR>—आम-<BR>पीनस, अम्, n. running at the nose, defluxion.<BR>—आम-मांस, अस्, m. raw flesh.<BR>—आममांसाशिन्<BR>(˚स-आश्˚), ई, m. a cannibal, eater of raw flesh.<BR>—आम-रक्त, अस्, m. dysentery.<BR>—आम-रस, अस्,<BR>m. imperfect chyme.<BR>—आम-वात, अस्, m. constipa-<BR>tion or torpor of the bowels with flatulence and intu-<BR>mescence.<BR>—आम-शूल, अस्, m. the cholic, pain<BR>arising from indigestion.<BR>—आमातिसार (˚म-अत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. dysentery or diarrhœa produced by vitiated<BR>mucus in the abdomen; the excretion being mixed<BR>with hard and fetid matter.<BR>—आमाद् (˚म-अद्), त्, त्,<BR>त्, eating raw flesh or food.<BR>—आमान्न (˚म-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. undressed rice.<BR>—आमाशय (˚म-आश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the receptacle of the undigested food, the upper<BR>part of the belly to the navel, the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमक
आमक, अस्, आ, अम्, raw, uncooked, &c. See<BR>1. आम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिष|आमिषं
आमिष, अम्, n. flesh. See s. v. next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम 2. आम, अस्, m. or आमन, अम्, n. (fr.<BR>rt. 2. अम्), sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमय|आमयं|आमयः
आमय, अस्, m. damage, hurt; disease, sickness;<BR>indigestion; (अम्), n., N. of the medical plant Cos-<BR>tus Speciosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयाविन्
आमयाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, sick, diseased, affected with<BR>indigestion, dyspeptic.<BR>—आमयावि-त्व, अम्, n. indi-<BR>gestion, dyspepsia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमण्ड|आमंडः|आमण्डः
आमण्ड आमण्ड, अस्, m. the castor-oil plant<BR>[cf. अमण्ड and मण्ड].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन|आमनं
आमन आ-मन, अम्, n. (rt. मन्), Ved.<BR>friendly disposition, inclination, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनस्
आ-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, friendly disposed, kind,<BR>favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनस्य|आमनस्यं
आमनस्य आमनस्य or आमानस्य, अम्, n. (fr.<BR>अ-मनस्), pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्र्|आमंत्र्
आमन्त्र् आ-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्रयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to address, especially in saluting and in bid-<BR>ding farewell; to ask, invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रण|आमंत्रणं|आमन्त्रणं
आ-मन्त्रण, अम्, आ, n. f. addressing, speaking to,<BR>calling or calling to; greeting, courtesy, welcome,<BR>bidding adieu, taking leave; inviting, invitation; de-<BR>liberation, interrogation; the vocative case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रणीय
आ-मन्त्रणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be addressed<BR>or asked, to be asked for advice or consulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रयितृ|आमंत्रयितृ
आ-मन्त्रयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, asking, inviting, call-<BR>ing; (ता), m. an inviter, entertainer, especially of<BR>Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रित|आमंत्रित
आ-मन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, invited, summoned,<BR>called; (अम्), n. addressing; the vocative case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्र्य|आमंत्र्य
1. आ-मन्त्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be addressed or called<BR>to; to be invited; (अम्), n. a word standing in the<BR>vocative case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्र्य|आमंत्र्य
2. आ-मन्त्र्य, ind. having taken leave, bidding<BR>farewell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्थ्
आमन्थ् आ-मन्थ् or आ-मथ्, cl. 1. P. -मन्-<BR>थति, -थितुम्, to agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्द्र|आमंद्र|आमन्द्रः
आमन्द्र आ-मन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having a slightly<BR>deep tone, making a low muttering sound (like thunder).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्त|आमरणांत
आमरणान्त आ-मरणान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, or आ-म-<BR>रणान्तिक (˚ण-अन्त्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having death as<BR>the limit, continuing till death, lasting for life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरितृ
आमरितृ आ-मरितृ, ता, m. (rt. मृ or मृण्<BR>with आ), Ved. one who hurts or destroys; a de-<BR>stroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्द|आमर्दः
आमर्द, आमर्दिन्। See under आ-मृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्ष|आमर्षः
आमर्ष आ-मर्ष, अस्, m. (for अ-मर्ष,<BR>q. v.), impatience, anger, wrath. (For आ-मर्श see<BR>under आ-मृश्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षण|आमर्षणं
आ-मर्षण, अम्, n. anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलक|आमलकं|आमलकः
आमलक आमलक, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. the plant<BR>Emblic Myrobalan, Emblica Officinalis Gærtn.; (अस्),<BR>m. another plant, Gendarussa Adhatoda; (अम्), n.<BR>the fruit of the Emblic Myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमहीया
आमहीया आमहीया, f. designation of a<BR>particular (ऋच्) verse of the Ṛg-veda (viz. Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 48, 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमहीयव
आमहीयव, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमा
आमा आ-मा, cl. 3. A. -मिमीते, -मातुम्, to<BR>effect, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमात्य|आमात्यः
आमात्य आमात्य, अस्, m. a minister, a coun-<BR>sellor, an adviser; a general. See अमात्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमालक|आमालकः
आमालक आमालक, अस्, अम्, m. n. land near<BR>a mountain (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमावास्य
आमावास्य आमावास्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अमा-<BR>वास्या), belonging to the new moon or its festival;<BR>born at the time of new moon; occurring on the<BR>day of conjunction; (अम्), n. the new moon oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षा
आमिक्षा आमिक्षा, f. curd of two-milk whey,<BR>a mixture of boiled and coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्ष्य|आमिक्ष्यं
आमिक्ष्य or आमिक्षीय, अस्, आ, अम्, suitable for<BR>the preparation of Āmikṣā; made of curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमित्र
आमित्र आमित्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-मित्र), pro-<BR>duced by an enemy, inimical, odious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिश्ल
आमिश्ल आ-मिश्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a<BR>tendency to mix, readily mixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिष|आमिषं
आमिष आमिष, अम्, n. (connected with 1.<BR>आम), flesh, enjoyment; an object of enjoyment, a<BR>pleasing or beautiful object &c.; a bribe; coveting,<BR>longing for; lust, desire; food; form.<BR>—आमिष-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of flesh-meat, carnivorous;<BR>(अस्), m. a heron.<BR>—आमिष-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, carni-<BR>vorous.<BR>—आमिषाशिन् (˚ष-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, carni-<BR>vorous, eating flesh and fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिस्
आमिस्, m. (occurring in loc. c. आमिषि), Ved. raw<BR>flesh, meat; a dead body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमी
आमी आ-मी, cl. 9. P., Ved. -मिनाति, -मातुम्,<BR>to destroy, neutralize, curtail; A. -मिनीते, to destroy<BR>or neutralize mutually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीक्षा
आमीक्षा आमीक्षा, f. = आमिक्षा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमील्
आमील् आ-मील्, cl. 1. P. -मीलति, -लितुम्, to<BR>close the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीलन|आमीलनं
आ-मीलन, अम्, n. closing of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीवत्|आमीवन्त्
आमीवत् आ-मीवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or आमीवत्क,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. attacking, pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुख|आमुखं
आमुख आ-मुख, अम्, n. commencement;<BR>prelude, prologue; (अम्), ind. to the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुच्
आमुच् आ-मुच्, cl. 6. P. -मुञ्चति, -मोक्तुम्,<BR>to loosen, let go; to put on a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्त|आमुक्तः
आ-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed, let go; liberated;<BR>discharged, cast, shot off; put on as clothes or armour;<BR>dressed, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्ति|आमुक्तिः
आ-मुक्ति, इस्, f. liberation, the being let loose;<BR>final liberation; (इ), ind. to the end of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचन|आमोचनं
आ-मोचन, अम्, n. the act of loosing, liberating;<BR>emitting, shedding, letting forth, putting or tying on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुप|आमुपः
आमुप आमुप, अस्, m. the cane Bambusa<BR>Spinosa Hamilt. Roxb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुर्
आमुर् आ-मुर्, ऊर्, or आ-मुरि, इस्, m. (fr. rt.<BR>मृ with आ), Ved. destroying, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्मिक
आमुष्मिक आमुष्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अमुष्-<BR>मिन्, loc. of 1. अदस्), of that state, being there,<BR>belonging to the other world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यकुलक
आमुष्यकुलक, अम्, n., आमुष्यपुत्रक, अम्,<BR>n., Gaṇa to Pāṇini V. 1. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायण|आमुष्यायणः
आमुष्यायण, अस्, m. (fr. अमुष्य, gen. of<BR>1. अदस्), son or descendant of such a one, son or<BR>descendant of an illustrious person; (अस्, ई, अम्), well-<BR>born, well descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमूलम्
आमूलम् आ-मूलम्, ind. to the root, by the<BR>root, entirely, radically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृज्
आमृज् आ-मृज्, cl. 1. 2. P. -मार्जति, -मार्ष्टि,<BR>मार्जितुम्, -मार्ष्टुम्, to wipe, rub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृज्य
आ-मृज्य, ind. having wiped or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृष्ट
आ-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, wiped, rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृण
आमृण आ-मृण, अस्, आ, अम्, vulnerable. See<BR>अन्-आमृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृत
आमृत आ-मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. मृ with<BR>आ), mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृत्योस्
आमृत्योस् आ-मृत्योस्, ind. until death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृद्
आमृद् आ-मृद्, cl. 9. P. -मृद्नाति, -मर्दि-<BR>तुम्, to crush by rubbing; to crumple; to press, to<BR>squeeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्द|आमर्दः
आ-मर्द, अस्, m. crushing, handling roughly; press-<BR>ing, squeezing; N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्दिन्|आमर्द्दिन्
आ-मर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crushing; pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृश्
आमृश् आ-मृश्, cl. 6. P. -मृशति, -मर्ष्टुम्<BR>or -म्रष्टुम्, to touch, handle roughly, rub, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्श|आमर्शः
आ-मर्श, अस्, m. advice, counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्शन|आमर्शनं
आ-मर्शन, or less correctly आ-मर्षण, अम्,<BR>n. rubbing, wiping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमेन्य
आमेन्य आ-मेन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मेनि with<BR>आ), Ved. to be reached with an arrow or bolt; (Sāy.)<BR>to be measured from all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोक्षण
आमोक्षण आ-मोक्षण, अम्, n. the act of<BR>fixing or tying on or to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचन|आमोचनं
आमोचन आ-मोचन. See under आ-मुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोद|आमोदः
आमोद आ-मोद, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. मुद् with<BR>आ), gladdening, cheering up; (अस्), m. joy, serenity,<BR>pleasure; fragrancy, a diffusive perfume; strong smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदन|आमोदनं
आ-मोदन, अम्, n. rejoicing, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदित|आमोदितः
आ-मोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, delighted, fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदिन्
आ-मोदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fragrant; happy, delighted;<BR>(at the end of compounds) fragrant or perfumed with,<BR>e. g. कदम्बामोदिन्, perfumed with kadambas;<BR>(ई), m. a perfume for the mouth made up in the<BR>form of a pill or bolus of camphor &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोष|आमोषः
आमोष आ-मोष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. मुष् with<BR>आ), robbing, stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोषिन्
आ-मोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, who or what steals, a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोहनिका
आमोहनिका आ-मोहनिका, f. (fr. rt. मुह् with<BR>आ), a particular fragrant odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ना
आम्ना आ-म्ना, cl. 1. P., Ved. -मनति, -म्ना-<BR>तुम्, to keep in mind, to repeat, commit to memory,<BR>hand down in sacred texts; to celebrate, to hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नात
आ-म्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, kept in mind, remembered,<BR>committed to memory, learnt by heart, repeated,<BR>handed down in sacred texts, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नान|आम्नानं
आ-म्नान, अम्, n. mention, repetition, handing<BR>down by sacred texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नाय|आम्नायः
आ-म्नाय, अस्, m. sacred tradition, sacred texts<BR>handed down by repetition; that which is to be re-<BR>membered, studied or learnt by heart; a Veda or the<BR>Vedas in the aggregate; received doctrine; traditional<BR>usage, family or national customs; advice, instruction<BR>in past and present usage; a Tantra; an element of<BR>being, a property of substance (?); a family, series of<BR>families.<BR>—आम्नाय-सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, observing the<BR>Vedas and traditional customs, pious; containing the<BR>essence of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्प्रत्यय
आम्प्रत्यय आम्-प्रत्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>आम् for its affix (e. g. a root like ईश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बरीषपुत्रक|आंबरीषपुत्रकः|आम्बरीषपुत्रकः
आम्बरीषपुत्रक आम्बरीषपुत्रक, अस्, m. a<BR>country inhabited by the Ambarīṣa-putras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बष्ठ|आंबष्ठः|आम्बष्ठः
आम्बष्ठ आम्बष्ठ, अस्, m. an inhabitant of<BR>Ambaṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बिकेय|आंबिकेयः|आम्बिकेयः
आम्बिकेय आम्बिकेय, अस्, m. (fr. अम्बिका), an<BR>epithet of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; also of Kārttikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भस|आंभस
आम्भस आम्भस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. अम्भस्),<BR>watery, fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भसिक|आंभसिक|आम्भसिकः
आम्भसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, living in water, aquatic;<BR>(अस्), m. a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भृणी
आम्भृणी आम्भृणी, f. a N. of Vāc, the<BR>daughter of the Ṛṣi Ambhṛṇa. See 3. अम्भृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्र|आम्रः
आम्र आम्र, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 2. अम्),<BR>the mango tree, Mangifera Indica; (अम्), n. the fruit<BR>of the mango tree.<BR>—आम्र-कूट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a mountain.<BR>—आम्र-गन्धक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—आम्र-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—आम्र-<BR>पाली, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—आम्र-पेशी, f. a portion<BR>of dried mango fruit.<BR>—आम्र-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of mangoes (as sauce).<BR>—आम्र-वण, अम्, n.<BR>a mango forest.<BR>—आम्रावर्त (˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. in-<BR>spissated mango juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रात|आम्रातः
आम्रात, अस्, m. the hog-plum, Spondias Mangi-<BR>fera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातक|आम्रातकः
आम्रातक, अस्, m. the hog-plum, Spondias Mangi-<BR>fera; inspissated mango juice; N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रावती
आम्रावती, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रिमन्
आम्रिमन्, आ, m., Gaṇa to Pāṇini V. 1, 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडन|आम्रेडनं
आम्रेडन आ-म्रेडन, अम्, n. tautology, re-<BR>iteration of words or sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडित|आम्रेडितं
आ-म्रेडित, अस्, आ, अम्, reiterated, repeated; (अम्),<BR>n. repetition of a sound or word; (in gram.) redu-<BR>plication, the second word in reduplications.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ल|आम्लः
आम्ल आम्ल, अस्, आ, m. f. (fr. अम्ल), the<BR>tamarind tree, Tamarindus Indica; (अम्), n. sour-<BR>ness, acidity.<BR>—आम्ल-वेतस, अस्, m. the plant Rumex<BR>Vesicatorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लिका
आम्लिका, f. the tamarind tree; sourness in the<BR>mouth, acidity of stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लीका
आम्लीका, f. the tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आय|आयः
आय आय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. इ with आ), arrival,<BR>approach; income, revenue; gain, profit; the guard<BR>of the women's apartments; the eleventh lunar man-<BR>sion.<BR>—आय-व्यय, अम् or औ, n. or m. du. receipt<BR>and disbursement, income and expenditure.<BR>—आय-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. a place where revenues are collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
1. आ-यत्, अन्, अती, अत्, coming, approaching.<BR>—आयती-<BR>गवम्, ind. at the time when the cows come home.<BR>—आयद्-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one to whom goods<BR>come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयन|आयनं
आयन, अम्, n., Ved. coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयिन्
आयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. driving near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयःशूलिक|आयःशूलिकः
आयःशूलिक आयःशूलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अयः-<BR>शूल), active, diligent, indefatigable; (अस्), m. a<BR>man who, in order to obtain an object, uses forcible<BR>instead of gentle means; as, for instance, a beggar who<BR>holds a lance to your breast in asking for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयज्
आयज् आ-यज्, cl. 1. A. -यजते, -यष्टुम्,<BR>to honour (the gods); to give, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजि
आ-यजि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. procuring, granting; (Sāy.)<BR>accomplishing sacrifices from all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजिष्ठ
आ-यजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. procuring most or<BR>best; (Sāy.) sacrificing best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयज्यु
आ-यज्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. endeavouring to gain;<BR>inclined to sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाग|आयागः
आ-याग, अस्, m. a gift given at a sacrifice.<BR>—आया-<BR>ग-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained by sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत् 2. आ-यत्, cl. 1. A. -यतते, -तितुम्, to<BR>make effort; to rest on, to depend on, to have the<BR>upper hand (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतन|आयतनं
आ-यतन, अम्, n. resting-place, support, seat,<BR>place, home, house, abode; the place of the sacred<BR>fire, an altar, a shed for sacrifices; a sanctuary; a<BR>ground-plot, the site of a house; a barn; (with Bud-<BR>dhists) an inner seat (the five senses and Manas are<BR>considered as the six inner seats or āyatanas); the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">Page0126-c+ 75</a>]<BR>cause of disease.<BR>—आयतन-त्व, अम्, n. state of<BR>being an altar or seat.<BR>—आयतन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. having a certain seat or home; (आन्), m., N.<BR>of the fourth foot of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्त|आयत्तः
आ-यत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, dependant, tractable, docile.<BR>—अयत्त-ता, f. or आयत्त-त्व, अम्, n. dependence,<BR>humility, tractableness, docility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्ति|आयत्तिः
आ-यत्ति, इस्, f. dependence, subjection, subjecting;<BR>affection; power, strength; day; boundary, limit;<BR>sleeping; length (? for आ-यति below); majesty,<BR>dignity; future time (? for आ-यति); continuance in<BR>the right way, steadiness of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथातथ्य|आयथातथ्यं
आयथातथ्य आयथातथ्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-य-<BR>थातथ), unsuitableness, unfitness, incompatibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्
आयम् आ-यम्, cl. 1. P. -यच्छति, -यन्तुम्,<BR>to stretch, lengthen out, extend, restrain; A. -यच्-<BR>छते, to stretch one's self or be stretched, to grow<BR>long; to grasp, possess: Caus. -यामयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>to lengthen, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत|आयतः
आ-यत, अस्, आ, अम्, long; diffuse, prolix; (अस्), m.<BR>an oblong figure (in geometry).<BR>—आयत-च्छदा, f.<BR>the plantain tree Musa Paradisiaca Lin.<BR>—आयत-<BR>स्तू, ऊस्, m. a panegyrist.<BR>—आयताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having large eyes or long eyelids.<BR>—आयता-<BR>पाङ्ग (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having a long-cornered<BR>eye.<BR>—आयतायति (˚त-आय्˚), इस्, f. long continu-<BR>ance, remote futurity.<BR>—आयतार्ध (˚त-अर्ध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. (in geometry) half an oblong.<BR>—आयतेक्षण<BR>(˚त-ईक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, long-eyed, having long or<BR>large eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयति|आयतिः
आ-यति, इस्, f. extension, length; stretching the<BR>hand, accepting, obtaining; connection, junction;<BR>meeting; following or future time; the future, ‘the<BR>long run;’ majesty, dignity; restraint of mind; N.<BR>of a daughter of Meru.<BR>—आयति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>long, extended; stately, dignified; self-restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयन्तृ|आयंतृ
आ-यन्तृ, ता, m., Ved. one who fastens or raises;<BR>(Sāy.) one who approaches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयमन|आयमनं
आ-यमन, अम्, n. stretching (as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्य
1. आ-यम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stretched; to be<BR>restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्य
2. आ-यम्य or आ-यत्य, ind. having restrained,<BR>suppressed or stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाम|आयामः
आ-याम, अस्, m. stretching, extending; restraining,<BR>restraint, stopping; expansion, length (either in space<BR>or time), breadth (in mensuration).<BR>—आयाम-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, extended, long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामित
आ-यामित, अस्, आ, अम्, lengthened out, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामिन्
आ-यामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who restrains, long in<BR>space or time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयल्लक|आयल्लकं|आयल्लकः
आयल्लक आयल्लक, अम्, n. impatience, long-<BR>ing for, missing, regretting (etym. doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवन|आयवनं
आयवन आ-यवन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. यु with<BR>आ), Ved. a spoon for stirring, any similar implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवस|आयवसं|आयवसः
आयवस आ-यवस, अस् or अम् (?), m. n., Ved.<BR>pasture-ground, place for feeding; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्
आयस् आ-यस्, cl. 4. P. -यस्यति, -सितुम्, to<BR>exert one's self, to weary one's self, become exhausted:<BR>Caus. -यासयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to weary, worry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्त|आयस्तः
आ-यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, pained, distressed; vexed,<BR>angry; hurt, killed; managed or effected with diffi-<BR>culty; labouring, toiling, making effort or exertion;<BR>sharpened, whetted; thrown, cast, sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयास|आयासः
आ-यास, अस्, m. effort, exertion (of bodily or mental<BR>power), trouble, labour; fatigue, weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासक
आ-यासक, अस्, ई, अम्, causing effort, fatigue or<BR>weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासिन्
आ-यासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, making exertion, active, labo-<BR>rious; exhausted by labour, wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस|आयसं
आयस आयस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अयस्), of iron,<BR>made of iron or metal, metallic; armed with an iron<BR>weapon; zealous ?; (ई), f. armour for the body, a<BR>breastplate, a coat of mail; (अम्), n. iron; anything<BR>made of iron; a weapon; a wind-instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्कार|आयस्कारः
आयस्कार आयस्कार, अस्, m. the upper part<BR>of the thigh of an elephant. See अयस्-कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आया
आया आ-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -तुम्, to come,<BR>arrive, approach, reach, attain; Ved. to bring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयात|आयातं
आ-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, come; (अम्), n. excess, super-<BR>abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाति|आयातिः
आ-याति, इस्, f. coming near, arrival; (इस्), m., N. of<BR>a son of Nahuṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयान|आयानं
आ-यान, अम्, n. coming, arrival; the natural tem-<BR>perament or disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयापन|आयापनं
आ-यापन, अम्, n. causing to come, inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाचित
आयाचित आ-याचित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. याच्),<BR>urgently requested or desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयु|आयुः
आयु आयु, उस्, उस्, उ (perhaps fr. rt. अन्, but<BR>said to be fr. rt. अय्, to go), Ved. living, movable;<BR>(उस्), m. a living being, man; living beings collectively;<BR>mankind; the human race; the first man; life, du-<BR>ration of life; wind; a son, descendant, offspring;<BR>the son of Purūravas and Urvaśī; N. of a man per-<BR>secuted by Indra, also of one protected by him;<BR>N. of a Riṣi; of a son of Hrada; of a king of<BR>frogs.<BR>—आयु-षक्, ind. (षक् fr. rt. सच्), Ved.<BR>joined with men, with the co-operation of men;<BR>(Sāy.) attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्
आयुस्, n. life, vital power, health, duration of life,<BR>long life, vital power; N. of a ceremony, commonly<BR>called Āyuṣṭoma, performed to obtain longevity and<BR>forming part together with the Go and Jyotis of the<BR>Abhi-plava ceremony; food; [cf. Dor. αἰές perhaps<BR>also αἰών]; (उस्), m. the son of Purūravas and Urvaśī.<BR>—आयुः-शेष, अस्, m. end of life, death.<BR>—आयुः-<BR>शेष-ता, f. the state of having nothing left but life.<BR>—आयुर्-दद्, त्, त्, त्, or आयुर्-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, or<BR>आयुर्-दावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. giving life.<BR>—आयुर्-<BR>द्रव्य, अम्, n. a medicament.<BR>—आयुर्-वेद, अस्,<BR>m. the science of health or medicine; it is classed<BR>among sacred sciences, and considered as a supplement<BR>of the Atharva-veda; it contains eight departments:<BR>1. Śalya, surgery; 2. Śālākya, inquiry into diseases<BR>of the head and its organs; 3. Kāya-cikitsā, treatment<BR>of diseases affecting the whole body; 4. Bhūta-vidyā,<BR>treatment of diseases of the mind supposed to be pro-<BR>duced by demoniacal influence; 5. Kaumāra-bhṛtya,<BR>treatment of children; 6. Agada-tantra, doctrine of<BR>antidotes; 7. Rāsāyana-tantra, doctrine of elixirs; 8.<BR>Vājīkaraṇa-tantra, rules for increasing generative power.<BR>—आयुर्वेद-दृश्, क्, m. a physician.<BR>—आयुर्वेद-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, acquainted with medical science.<BR>—आयुर्वेदिक, अस्, m. acquainted or familiar with<BR>medical science, a physician.<BR>—आयुर्वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>belonging to medicine, of the medical profession,<BR>medical, medicinal, &c.; (ई), m. a practiser of physic,<BR>a physician or surgeon.<BR>—आयुष्-काम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>wishing for life or health.<BR>—आयुष्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>producing or creating life.<BR>—अयुष्टोम, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>आयुस्-स्तोम), a sacrifice to obtain longevity.<BR>—आयुष्-<BR>पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. preserving life.<BR>—आयुष्-<BR>प्रतरण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. prolonging life.<BR>—आयुष्-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of vital power, healthy,<BR>long-lived; alive, living; lasting; old; (आन्), m. the<BR>third of the twenty-seven Yogas or divisions of the<BR>ecliptic; the Yoga star in the third lunar mansion;<BR>N. of a son of Uttānapāda, also of Saṃhrāda.<BR>—आयुस्-<BR>कर, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, promoting longevity, supporting<BR>life.<BR>—आयुस्-तेजस्, आस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष|आयुषं
आयुष, अम्, n. (at the end of some compounds)<BR>= आयुस्, life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्क|आयुष्कः
आयुष्क, (with Jainas) union or connection with<BR>the body or person; that which proclaims (कायते)<BR>age (आयुस्) or duration of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्य|आयुष्यं
आयुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, giving long life, vital, preserv-<BR>ative of life, for the sake of life, relating or belong-<BR>ing to it; (अम्), n. vital power, abundance of life;<BR>‘vivifying,’ N. of a ceremony performed after a child's<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुज्
आयुज् 1. आ-युज्, cl. 7. P. A. -युनक्ति,<BR>-युङ्क्ते, -योक्तुम्, to yoke to (anything); to join;<BR>to appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुक्त|आयुक्तः
आ-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, appointed, charged with;<BR>united, joined, obtained; (अस्), m. a minister, an<BR>agent or deputy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुज्
2. आ-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. uniting, joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोग|आयोगः
आ-योग, अस्, m. appointment; action, the perform-<BR>ance of an act; presenting or offering flowers, per-<BR>fumes, &c.; a shore or bank, a quay to which boats<BR>are attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजन|आयोजनं
आ-योजन, अम्, n. effort, exertion; taking, seizing;<BR>collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजित
आ-योजित, अस्, आ, अम्, collected together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुत
आयुत आ-युत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. यु), melted,<BR>mixed, mingled; (अम्), n. (with आ implying diminu-<BR>tion), half-melted butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुवमान
आ-युवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. mixing, mingling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध्
आयुध् आ-युध्, cl. 4. P. A. -युध्यति, -ते,<BR>-योद्धुम्, to war against, attack, oppose: Caus.<BR>-योधयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to attack, oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध|आयुधं|आयुधः
आ-युध, अस्, अम्, m. n. a weapon; Ved. a vessel;<BR>(आनि), n. pl., Ved. water; (अम्), n. gold used for<BR>ornaments.<BR>—आयुध-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living by one's<BR>weapon; (ई), m. a warrior.<BR>—आयुध-धर्मिणी, f.<BR>the plant Sesbania Ægyptiaca, commonly called<BR>Jayantī.<BR>—आयुधागार (˚ध-आग्˚), अम्, n. an ar-<BR>moury, arsenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिक|आयुधिकः
आयुधिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to arms; (अस्), m.<BR>a soldier, warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिन्
आयुधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing weapons; (ई), m. a<BR>warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीय|आयुधीयः
आयुधीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or connected<BR>with arms; (अस्), m. a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोधन|आयोधनं
आ-योधन, अम्, n. war, battle; slaughter, killing;<BR>battle-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आये
आये आये, ind. an interjection of calling,<BR>expressive of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगव|आयोगवः
आयोगव आयोगव, अस्, m. a man belonging<BR>to the tribe of Ayogu; a man of a mixed tribe sprung<BR>from a Śūdra man and Vaiśya woman; his business<BR>is carpentry &c.; (ई), f. a woman of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोद|आयोदः
आयोद आयोद, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्
आर् 1. आर्, आर्यति Ved. to praise; (Sāy.)<BR>to approach or to make master of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्
आर् 2. आर् (आ-ऋ), cl. 3. P. एयर्ति, or cl. 5. P.<BR>आर्णोति, आर्तुम्, आरितुम् or आरीतुम्, to come; to<BR>reach, obtain, fall into; to inflict; to insert, place<BR>in: Caus. आर्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause to partake of;<BR>to fix, settle, annex; to ordain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर|आरं|आरः
1. आर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (? fr. rt. ऋ), an angle, a<BR>corner; N. of a tree; N. of a lake; brass; oxide of<BR>iron; (अस्), m. the planet Mars, Ἄρης the planet<BR>Saturn; (आ), f. a shoemaker's awl or knife, a bore,<BR>a probe, a spoke.<BR>—आर-कूट, अस्, अम्, m. n. brass.<BR>—आराग्र (˚रा-अग्˚), अम्, n. the point of an awl;<BR>the iron thong at the end (of a whip); the edge of<BR>a semicircular arrow-head; (अस्, आ, अम्), sharpened,<BR>sharp at the top and broad at the bottom like an awl.<BR>—आरावली (˚रा-आव्˚), f., N. of a chain of mountains,<BR>a spur of the Vindhya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त|आर्त्त|आर्त्तः
आर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted, pained. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्पित
आर्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened to, annexed; depend-<BR>ing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर|आरं|आरः
आर 2. आर (contained in आरात्, आरे, q. v.),<BR>distance; proximity (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकात्
आरकात्, ind., Ved. (with abl.) far from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर|आरं|आरः
आर 3. आर, probably a wrong reading for<BR>अर, a spoke, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्त
आरक्त आ-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (see 3. आ), reddish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष|आरक्षं|आरक्षः
आरक्ष आ-रक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रक्ष्), pre-<BR>served, defended, proper or worthy to be preserved;<BR>(अस्), m. protection, guard, preservation; the junction<BR>of the frontal sinuses of an elephant; the part of the<BR>forehead below this junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षक|आरक्षकः
आ-रक्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what guards or<BR>protects; (अस्), m. a watchman; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षिक|आरक्षिकः
आ-रक्षिक, अस्, m. a watchman, a patrol; a vil-<BR>lage or police magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष्य
आ-रक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be preserved or guarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरग्बध
आरग्बध आरग्-बध, अस्, m. the tree Ca-<BR>thartocarpus (Cassia) Fistula; (अम्), n. its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरङ्गर|आरङ्गरः
आरङ्गर आरङ्गर, अस्, m., Ved. epithet of<BR>a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरचित
आरचित आ-रचित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. रच्), ar-<BR>ranged, prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट|आरटः
आरट आरट, अम्, n. flesh. (This word is<BR>also one of the Gaṇa गौरादि Pāṇini IV. 1. 41.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्ट|आरट्टः
आरट्ट आरट्ट, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>and country in Pañca-nada or the Pañjāb.<BR>—आरट्ट-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, born in Āraṭṭa; (अस्), m. an inhabitant<BR>of this country; a horse from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरडव
आरडव आरडव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अरडु),<BR>Pāṇini IV. 2, 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण|आरणं
आरण आरण, अम्, n. (probably related to<BR>1. अरण), Ved. depth, abyss, precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणज
आरणज आरणज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a class<BR>of deities forming part of the Kalpa-bhavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणि|आरणिः
आरणि आरणि, इस्, m. an eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणेय|आरणेयः
आरणेय आरणेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अरणि, q. v.),<BR>relating to the Araṇis or two pieces of wood by the<BR>attrition of which sacred fire is kindled; (अम्), n.<BR>or आरणेय-पर्वन्, अ, n. title of the last section of<BR>the third book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्य|आरण्यः
आरण्य आरण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अरण्य),<BR>forest, relating to a forest, forest-born, wild; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. wild animals.<BR>—आरण्य-गान, अम्, n. one of the<BR>four Gānas or psalm-books of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—आ-<BR>रण्य-पर्वन्, अ, n., N. of the third book of the<BR>Mahā-bhārata, more usually called वन-पर्वन्.<BR>—आरण्य-पशु, उस्, m. a wild or forest animal (as a<BR>buffalo, monkey, &c.).<BR>—आरण्य-मुद्गा, f. a kind<BR>of bean, Phaseolus Trilobus Ait.<BR>—आरण्य-राशि, इस्,<BR>m. (in the zodiac) the sign Leo; Aries and Taurus;<BR>the former half of Capricorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यक|आरण्यकः
आरण्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, forest, wild, forest-born,<BR>produced in a forest, relating to a forest; the आर-<BR>ण्यकम् पर्व of the Mahā-bhārata is either the<BR>whole third book or only the first section of it; (अस्),<BR>m. a forester, an inhabitant of the woods; (अम्), n.<BR>an आरण्यक, i. e. one of a class of religious and phi-<BR>losophical writings (closely connected with the Brāh-<BR>maṇas) which are either composed in forests or must<BR>be studied there; the Upaniṣads are considered to<BR>be attached to them.<BR>—आरण्यक-काण्ड, अम्, n.<BR>title of the third book of the Rāmāyaṇa and of the<BR>fourteenth book of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरद्ध
आरद्ध आरद्ध, अस्, or आरद्वत्, आन्, m., N.<BR>of a son of Setu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनाल|आरनालं
आरनाल आरनाल or आरनालक, अम्, n. sour<BR>gruel made from the fermentation of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्
आरभ् आ-रभ्, cl. 1. A. -रभते, -रब्धुम्,<BR>to commence, begin, undertake; to be active or ener-<BR>getic; to rely, obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्ध|आरब्धं
आ-रब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, begun, commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्धि|आरब्धिः
आ-रब्धि, इस्, f. beginning, commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभट|आरभटः
आ-रभट, अस्, m. an enterprising, courageous<BR>man; (अस्, ई), m. f. boldness, confidence; (ई), f. a<BR>branch of the dramatic art, the machinery of the<BR>drama, the representation of supernatural and horrible<BR>events on the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभमाण
आ-रभमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, beginning, commencing<BR>resolutely with a determination to finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्य
आ-रभ्य, ind. having begun, beginning from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्यमाण
आ-रभ्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भ|आरंभः|आरम्भः
आ-रम्भ, अस्, m. undertaking, beginning; a<BR>thing begun; commencement; haste, speed; effort,<BR>exertion; pride; killing, slaughter; an introduction,<BR>a prologue, &c.<BR>—आरम्भ-ता, f. beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भक|आरंभक
आ-रम्भक, अस्, ई, अम्, undertaking, beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भण|आरंभणं
आ-रम्भण, अम्, n. taking hold of, seizing,<BR>using; the place of seizing, a handle.<BR>—आरम्भण-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, seizable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भणीय
आ-रम्भणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, that with which one<BR>must begin, forming the commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भिन्|आरंभिन्
आ-रम्भिन्, ई, इणी, इ, enterprising, one who makes<BR>many new projects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्
आरम् आ-रम्, cl. 1. P. -रमति, -रन्तुम्, to<BR>delight in; to rest; to leave off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरत
आ-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, quiet, gentle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरति|आरतिः
आ-रति, इस्, f. stopping, ceasing; waving lights be-<BR>fore an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरमण|आरमणं
आ-रमण, अम्, n. taking delight; cessation, pause;<BR>resting-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराम|आरामः
आ-राम, अस्, m. delight, pleasure; place of pleasure,<BR>a garden, a grove; [with this word cf. ἠμέρα and<BR>ἔρημος]<BR>—आराम-शीतला, f., N. of a fragrant plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरामिक|आरामिकः
आरामिक, अस्, m. a gardener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्बण|आरंबणं
आरम्बण आ-रम्बण, अम्, n. (= आ-लम्बन),<BR>support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरव|आरवः
आरव, आराव See under 1. आ-रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरस्
आरस् आ-रस्, cl. 1. P. -रसति, -सितुम्, to<BR>bewail, to lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरस्य|आरस्यं
आरस्य आरस्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-रस), insi-<BR>pidity, want of flavour or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरा
आरा आरा, f. a probe, an awl. See under<BR>2. आर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराग
आराग आ-राग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. रञ्ज् with आ),<BR>one of the seven suns at the end of a period of the<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराज्ञी
आराज्ञी आ-राज्ञी, f. (fr. राजन् with 3. अ), N.<BR>of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराड
आराड आराड, अस्, m. with the epithet<BR>कालाप, N. of a teacher of Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराढि
आराढि आराढि, इस्, m. a patronymic of a<BR>teacher named Saugata in the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्
आरात् आरात्, ind. (see 2. आर), from a dis-<BR>tant place; distant; to a distant place; far from (with<BR>abl.); near; directly, immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातीय
आरातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, remote; near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्तात्
आरात्तात्, ind., Ved. from a distant place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराति|आरातिः
आराति आराति, इस्, m. an enemy. See अ-राति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्रिक|आरात्रिकं
आरात्रिक आ-रात्रिक, अम्, n. the light or the<BR>vessel containing it which is waved at night before<BR>an idol; N. of this ceremony; N. of another cere-<BR>mony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्
आराध् आ-राध्, cl. 5. P. -राध्नोति, -राद्धुम्,<BR>or Caus. P. -राधयति, -यितुम्, to conciliate, pro-<BR>pitiate; strive to obtain the favour of; to honour,<BR>worship; to deserve, merit: Pass. -राध्यते, to be<BR>effected or accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधक
आ-राधक, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what worships,<BR>a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधन|आराधनं
आ-राधन, अम्, n. propitiating, rendering favour-<BR>able to one's self; (अम्), n. accomplishment, under-<BR>taking; cooking; acquirement, attainment; grati-<BR>fying, propitiating, worshipping; (आ), f. service; (ई),<BR>f. worship, adoration, propitiation of the deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनीय
आ-राधनीय or आ-राधितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>worshipped or adored, to be conciliated or propitiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधयितृ
आ-राधयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, endeavouring to conci-<BR>liate or propitiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधयिष्णु
आ-राधयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, propitiatory; = the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधित
आ-राधित, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished, effected;<BR>propitiated, pleased; worshipped, honoured, rever-<BR>enced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्य
आ-राध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made favourable, to<BR>be worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्यमान
आ-राध्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being in course of<BR>fulfilment, being accomplished; being worshipped,<BR>receiving worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरिराधयिषु
आ-रिराधयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, endeavouring to gain<BR>one's favour, desirous of worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरालिक|आरालिकः
आरालिक आरालिक, अस्, ई, m. f. a cook,<BR>(etymology doubtful, said to be fr. अराल, i. e. bend-<BR>ing over dishes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरावली
आरावली आरावली, f. See under 2. आर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरिच्
आरिच् आ-रिच्, cl. 7. P. A. -रिणक्ति, -रिङ्क्ते,<BR>-रेक्तुम्, to empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेक|आरेकः
आ-रेक, अस्, m. emptying, doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेचित
आ-रेचित, अस्, आ, अम्, emptied, contracted, mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरित्रिक
आरित्रिक आरित्रिक, adj. fr. अरित्र. Pāṇini<BR>IV. 2, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरिन्दम|आरिंदम
आरिन्दम आरिन्दम, अस्, m. patronymic of<BR>the prince Sana-śruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरी
आरी आ-री, cl. 4. A. -रीयते, -रेतुम्, to<BR>trickle or flow upon, to flow over, water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरु|आरुः
आरु 1. आ-रु, cl. 2. P. -रौति or -रवीति, -रवि-<BR>तुम्, to shout, to cry out; to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरव|आरवः
आ-रव, अस्, m. cry, crying, howling, crash, sound;<BR>N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराव|आरावः
आ-राव, अस्, m. cry, crying; humming (of bees<BR>&c.); sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराविन्
आ-राविन्, ई, m. epithet of Jayasena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरु|आरुः
आरु 2. आरु, उस्, m. a hog; a crab; the tree<BR>Lagerstrœmia Regina; (उस्), f. a pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुक|आरुकः
आरुक आरुक, अम्, n. a medicinal plant of<BR>cooling properties growing on the Himālaya moun-<BR>tains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुच्
आरुच् आ-रुच्, Caus. -रोचयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>regard as pleasant, to choose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोक|आरोकः
आ-रोक, अस्, m. shining through; small points of<BR>light between the threads of a web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोचन
आ-रोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुज्
आरुज् आ-रुज्, क्, क्, क् (rt. रुज्), breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुज
आ-रुज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. breaking, destroying; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a Rakṣas attendant on Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुजत्नु
आ-रुजत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग
आ-रोग, अस्, m., N. of a sun [cf. आ-राग].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणपराजिन्
आरुणपराजिन् आरुणपराजिन्, ई, m., N. of<BR>an ancient Kalpa work on the ritual of the Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणि|आरुणिः
आरुणि आरुणि, इस्, m. (fr. अरुण), N. of<BR>Uddālaka, a renowned Brāhmaṇa teacher, son of Aruṇa<BR>Aupaveśi and father of Śvetaketu; N. of Auddālaki,<BR>i. e. of Śvetaketu; of Suparṇeya, son of Prajāpati;<BR>of Vainateya, son of Vinatā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणेय|आरुणेयः
आरुणेय, अस्, m. epithet of Śvetaketu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणिन्
आरुणिन् आरुणिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a school<BR>derived from Vaiśāmpāyana Āruṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणी
आरुणी आरुणी, f., Ved. ‘the red one,’ a N.<BR>given to the horses of the Maruts, which are females.<BR>See अरुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुध्
आरुध् आ-रुध्, cl. 7. P. -रुणद्धि, -रोद्धुम्,<BR>to keep off: Caus. -रोधयति, -यितुम्, to obstruct,<BR>impede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोधन|आरोधनं
आ-रोधन, अम्, n., Ved. secret place, innermost part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुषी
आरुषी आरुषी, f. (fr. अरुष), N. of a<BR>daughter of Manu and mother of Aurva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुष्कर|आरुष्करं
आरुष्कर आरुष्-कर, अम्, n. the fruit of<BR>the Semecarpus Anacardium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्
आरुह् 1. आ-रुह्, cl. 1. P. -रोहति, -रोढुम्,<BR>to ascend, mount, bestride; to venture upon, under-<BR>take; to attain, gain: Caus. -रोहयति or -रोपयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to mount or ascend, raise; to cause<BR>to grow; to plant; to place, fasten; to attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुरुक्षमाण
आ-रुरुक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (Desid.), wishing to<BR>ascend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुरुक्षु
आ-रुरुक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous to rise or ascend<BR>or advance, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्
2. आ-रुह्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. ascending; (क्), f. excrescence,<BR>shoot (of a plant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह|आरुहः
आ-रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, leaping up, mounting, ascend-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. ascent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्य
आ-रुह्य, ind. having mounted, having ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढ|आरूढः
आ-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, mounted, ascended, risen;<BR>raised up, elevated on high; often used in compounds,<BR>e. g. इन्द्रियारूढ, brought under the cognizance<BR>of the senses, perceived.<BR>—आरूढ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>mounting, rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढि|आरूढिः
आ-रूढि, इस्, f. ascent, mounting, ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोढव्य
आ-रोढव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ascended or mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोढृ
आ-रोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ, who or what mounts<BR>or rides, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोप|आरोपः
आ-रोप, अस्, m. imposing (as a burden), burdening<BR>with, charging with; placing in or on; assigning or<BR>attributing to; relating to; superior position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपक
आ-रोपक, अस्, आ, अम्, planting, fixing, causing to<BR>ascend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपण|आरोपणं
