आर्जव|आर्जवं
आर्जव आर्जव, अम्, n. (fr. ऋजु), straight-<BR>ness, straight direction; rectitude, propriety of act or<BR>observance; honesty, open behaviour; sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीक|आर्जीकः
आर्जीक आर्जीक, अस्, m. (cf. ऋजीक), Ved.<BR>originally perhaps a milk-vessel. This word probably<BR>denotes a celestial vessel, in which the heavenly Soma<BR>is purified, or one of the rivers which it forms in<BR>the sky; (Sāy.) a lake in the country Ṛjīkā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीकीय
आर्जीकीय, अस्, m. = the preceding; (आ), f. a terres-<BR>trial river; N. of the river Vipāśā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनायन
आर्जुनायन आर्जुनायन, आस्, m. pl. (fr. अर्-<BR>जुन), N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनायनक
आर्जुनायनक, अस्, ई, अम्, inhabited by the Ārju-<BR>nāyanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनि|आर्जुनिः|आर्ज्जुनि
आर्जुनि आर्जुनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनेय|आर्ज्जुनेय
आर्जुनेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of Kutsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ञ्ज्
आर्ञ्ज् आर्ञ्ज् (आ-ऋञ्ज्), cl. 1. A. आर्ञ्जते, -जितुम्,<BR>to strive after, to endeavour to obtain, to wish to<BR>possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त|आर्त्त|आर्त्तः
आर्त आर्त, अस्, आ, अम् (probably past pass.<BR>part. of rt. ऋ with prep. आ, but according to some fr.<BR>rt. ऋत्, and according to others an irreg. formation<BR>fr. rt. अर्द्, which ought to form अर्ण with prep.<BR>सम्, नि and वि, and अर्दित in other cases), struck<BR>by calamity, afflicted, pained, disturbed; injured; op-<BR>pressed, suffering, sick, unhappy.<BR>—आर्त-गल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the plant Barleria Cærulea.<BR>—आर्त-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, extremely pained, disturbed, confounded.<BR>—आर्त-ता, f. state of affliction, pain.<BR>—आर्त-नाद<BR>or आर्त-स्वर, अस्, m. a cry of pain.<BR>—आर्त-बन्धु,<BR>उस्, m. friend of the distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ति|आर्तिः|आर्त्ति|आर्त्तिः
आर्ति, इस्, f. painful occurrence, pain, injury, mischief,<BR>evil; sickness; the end of a bow [cf. अर्ति and<BR>आर्त्नी].<BR>—आर्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having or suffering<BR>pain; (आन्), m., N. of a serpent.<BR>—आर्ति-हन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>or आर्ति-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying pain.<BR>—आर्त्य्-<BR>अपहरण, अम्, n. the relieving of distress, pain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तना
आर्तना आर्तना, f. (according to Sāy. de-<BR>rived fr. आर्त above), Ved. a destructive combat;<BR>(as an adj. ?) uncultivated, wild ground (? connected<BR>with आर, अरण, अरण्य, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तपर्णि|आर्त्तपर्ण्णि
आर्तपर्णि आर्तपर्णि, इस्, m. the son of Ṛta-<BR>parṇa, a patronymic of Sudāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तभाग|आर्त्तभाग
आर्तभाग आर्तभाग, अस्, m. son of Ṛta-<BR>bhāga, a patronymic of Jarat-kārava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तव|आर्तवः|आर्त्तव|आर्त्तवं|आर्त्तवः
आर्तव आर्तव, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. ऋतु), be-<BR>longing or conforming to the seasons or periods of<BR>time, seasonable; menstrual, relating to or produced<BR>by this discharge; (अस्), m. a section of the year, a<BR>combination of several seasons; (ई), f. a mare; (अम्),<BR>n. the menstrual discharge, certain days after the men-<BR>strual discharge fit for generation; fluid discharged<BR>by the female of an animal at the time of rut; a<BR>flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्वेयी
आर्त्वेयी, f. a woman during her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्नी
आर्त्नी आर्त्नी, f., Ved. the end of a bow, the<BR>place where the string or sinew is fastened; (κορώνη)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्विजीन
आर्त्विजीन आर्त्विजीन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ऋत्विज्),<BR>fit for the office of a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्विज्य|आर्त्विज्यं
आर्त्विज्य, अम्, n. the office or business of a sacri-<BR>ficing priest, his rank or order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्व्य
आर्त्व्य आर्त्व्य, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Dvi-mūrdhan, a kind of Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थ
आर्थ आर्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अर्थ), relating<BR>to a thing or object; material, significant (opposed to<BR>शाब्द, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थपत्य|आर्थपत्यं
आर्थपत्य, अम्, n. (fr. अर्थ-पति), power over<BR>or possession of a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थिक
आर्थिक, अस्, ई, अम्, significant, wise, rich; substan-<BR>tial, real, pertaining to the true substance of a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्र|आर्द्रं
आर्द्र आर्द्र, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>अर्द्), wet, moist, damp; fresh, not dry, succulent,<BR>green (as a plant), living; fresh, new; soft, tender,<BR>full of feeling, warm; loose, flaccid; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a grandson of Pṛthu; (आ), f. the fourth or sixth<BR>Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR>—आर्द्र-काष्ठ, अम्,<BR>n. green wood, timber not dry.<BR>—आर्द्र-ता, f. or<BR>आर्द्र-त्व, अम्, n. wetness, moisture; freshness,<BR>greenness; softness, tenderness.<BR>—आर्द्र-दानु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. granting moisture.<BR>—आर्द्र-नयन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, moist-eyed, weeping, suffused with tears.<BR>—आर्द्र-पवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having moist or drip-<BR>ping fellies (said of a carriage).<BR>—आर्द्र-पवित्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a wet strainer; epithet of<BR>the Soma.<BR>—आर्द्र-माषा, f. a leguminous shrub,<BR>Glycine Debilis.<BR>—आर्द्र-शाक, अम्, n. fresh ginger.<BR>—आर्द्र-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. moist-handed.<BR>—आर्द्रा-लुब्धक, अस्, m. the dragon's tail or de-<BR>scending node.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रक|आर्द्रकं
आर्द्रक, अम्, n. ginger in its undried state; (अस्,<BR>ई, अम्), born under the constellation Ārdrā; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Vasumitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रय
आर्द्रय, nom. P. आर्द्रयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>wet, moisten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ध्
आर्ध् आर्ध् (आ-ऋध्), Desid. A. एर्त्सते, to<BR>wish to obtain or to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ध
आर्ध आर्ध (fr. अर्ध), used at the begin-<BR>ning of compounds to express ‘half.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धद्रौणिक
आर्धद्रौणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, bought with half a<BR>drona, containing it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धधातुक
आर्धधातुक, अस्, ई, अम्, applicable to half the<BR>root or to the shorter form of the verbal base; this<BR>is the name of those terminations and affixes which<BR>belong to the six non-conjugational or general tenses.<BR>These terminations are supposed to be affixed im-<BR>mediately to the root or with the interposition only<BR>of an augment, such as the inserted इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धप्रस्थिक
आर्धप्रस्थिक, अस्, ई, अम्, bought &c. with<BR>half a prastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धमासिक
आर्धमासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, lasting &c. for half a<BR>month; observing or practising (continence &c.) for<BR>a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धरात्रिक
आर्धरात्रिक, आस्, m. pl. (fr. अर्ध-रात्र), N.<BR>of an astronomical school who reckoned the begin-<BR>ning of the motions of the planets from midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धिक|आर्धिकः
आर्धिक, अस्, ई, अम्, sharing half, an equal partner;<BR>relating to half; (अस्), m. one who ploughs the<BR>ground for half the crop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धुक
आर्धुक आर्धुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. ऋध्), Ved.<BR>conducive to success, useful, beneficial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्पय्
आर्पय् आर्पय्, Caus. fr. rt. ऋ with आ. See 2. आर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्पयितृ
आर्पयितृ, ता, m., Ved. one who injures or hurts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्भव
आर्भव आर्भव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ऋभु), be-<BR>longing or sacred to the Ṛbhus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य|आर्यः|आर्य्य|आर्य्यः
आर्य आर्य, अस्, आ, m. f. (fr. अर्य, rt. ऋ), a<BR>loyal or faithful man, a man of one's own race; one<BR>who is faithful to the deities of his country; N. of<BR>the Hindū and Iranian people (opposed to अन्-आर्य,<BR>दस्यु, दास); in later times N. of the first three<BR>castes (opposed to शूद्र); a man highly esteemed,<BR>a respectable, honourable man; a master, an owner; a<BR>friend; a Vaiśya; Buddha; (with Buddhists) a man who<BR>has thought on the four chief principles of Buddhism<BR>and lives according to them; a son of Manu Sāvarṇa;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-c" target="_blank">Page0129-c+ 79</a>]<BR>(अस्, आ, or ई, अम्), Āryan, favourable to the Āryan<BR>people; behaving like an Āryan, worthy of one,<BR>honourable, respectable, noble; of a good family;<BR>excellent; wise; suitable; (आ), f. a name of Pārvatī;<BR>a kind of metre of two lines, each, line consisting of<BR>seven and a half feet; each foot containing four in-<BR>stants, except the sixth of the second line, which con-<BR>tains only one, and is therefore a single short syllable;<BR>hence there are thirty instants in the first line and<BR>twenty-seven in the second; [with आर्य cf. the Old<BR>Germ. êra and Mod. Germ. Ehre.]<BR>—आर्य-गृह्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, easily to be got by honourable men, to<BR>be received with honour by noble men; decorous,<BR>respectable, right.<BR>—आर्य-ता, f. or आर्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>honourable behaviour.<BR>—आर्य-देव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>pupil of Nāgārjuna.<BR>—आर्य-देश, अस्, m. a region<BR>inhabited by Āryans or followers of the Āryan laws.<BR>—आर्यदेश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, originating from such a<BR>region.<BR>—आर्य-पुत्र, अस्, m. son of an Āryan or<BR>honourable man; the son of a spiritual preceptor;<BR>honorific designation of the son of an elder brother;<BR>of a husband by his wife; of a prince by a general;<BR>a husband (in theatrical language).<BR>—आर्य-प्राय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, inhabited by Āryan people; abound-<BR>ing with respectable persons.<BR>—आर्य-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a renowned astronomer, the inventor of<BR>algebra, among the Hindūs.<BR>—आर्य-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. honourable character or behaviour.<BR>—आर्य-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, m. the way of the honourable, the<BR>respectable way.<BR>—आर्य-मिश्र, आस्, m. pl. an as-<BR>sembly of respectable or honourable men; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), distinguished, respectable; (अस्), m. a gentleman,<BR>a man of consequence.<BR>—आर्य-युवन्, आ, m. an Āryan<BR>youth.<BR>—आर्य-राज, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—आर्य-<BR>रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has only the form of an<BR>Āryan; a hypocrite, an impostor.<BR>—आर्यलिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, one who bears the external semblance of an Āryan<BR>or honourable man, an impostor.<BR>—आर्य-वर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—आर्य-वृत्त, अम्, n. the behaviour<BR>of an Āryan or noble man; (अस्, आ, अम्), behaving<BR>like an Āryan; virtuous, good, pious.<BR>—आर्य-वेश,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dressed like an Āryan, well clothed, fine.<BR>—आर्य-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who observes the<BR>laws and ordinances of the Āryans or honourable men.<BR>—आर्य-सङ्घ, अस्, m. the whole body of the<BR>Āryans, the collective body of noblemen; N. of a<BR>renowned philosopher, founder of the school of the<BR>Yogākāras.<BR>—आर्य-सत्य, अम्, n. a noble or sublime<BR>truth; four such truths form the four chief principles<BR>of Buddhism.<BR>—आर्य-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>patriarch.<BR>—आर्य-हृद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, beloved by the<BR>noble.<BR>—आर्या-गीति, इस्, f. a variety of the Āryā metre,<BR>containing eight equal feet or thirty-two syllabic in-<BR>stants in each verse of the couplet.<BR>—आर्यावर्त (˚य-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. abode of the noble or excellent; the<BR>sacred land or place of residence of the Āryans; N.<BR>of the land extending from the eastern to the western<BR>sea, and bounded on the north and south by the<BR>Himālaya and Vindhya mountains.<BR>—आर्या-विलास,<BR>अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—आर्याष्टशत (˚य-अष्ट-<BR>श˚), अम्, n. title of a work of Ārya-bhaṭṭa's, consisting<BR>of eight hundred distichs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यक|आर्यकः|आर्य्यक|आर्य्यकं|आर्य्यकः
आर्यक, अस्, m. an honourable, respectable man; a<BR>grandfather; N. of a cowherd who became king; of<BR>a Nāga.<BR>—आर्यका or आर्यिका, f. a respectable woman;<BR>(इका), f., N. of a Nakṣatra; (अकम्), n. a ceremony<BR>performed to the manes, the vessel &c. used in sacri-<BR>fices made to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्याणक
आर्याणक, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्वाक्|आर्व्वाक्
आर्वाक् आर्वाक्, ind. after, afterwards, be-<BR>hind. See अर्वाक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्श
आर्श आर्श, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ऋश्य), Ved. belong-<BR>ing to the antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ष|आर्षः
आर्ष आर्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ऋषि), relating or<BR>belonging to or derived from Ṛṣis, i. e. the poets<BR>of the Vedic and other old hymns, archaistic; (अस्), m.<BR>a form of marriage derived from the Ṛṣis, the<BR>father of the bride receiving one or two pairs of kine<BR>from the bridegroom; (अम्), n. the speech of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">Page0130-a+ 75</a>]<BR>Ṛṣi, the holy text, the Vedas; sacred descent; the<BR>derivation (of a poem) from a Ṛṣi author; (आ),<BR>f. a class of Vedic metres.<BR>—आर्षोढा (˚ष-ऊढ्˚),<BR>f. a wife married according to the Ārṣa form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षेय
आर्षेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to or<BR>derived from a Ṛṣi, of sacred descent; venerable,<BR>respectable; (अम्), n. sacred descent.<BR>—आर्षेय-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. connected with sacred descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ
आर्षभ आर्षभ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ऋषभ),<BR>derived from a bull, produced by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभि|आर्षभिः
आर्षभि, इस्, m., N. of the first Cakravartin in<BR>Bhārata; a son of the first Tīrthakṛt Ṛṣabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ्य|आर्षभ्यः
आर्षभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, a steer sufficiently full-grown<BR>to be used or one fit to be castrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ष्टिषेण
आर्ष्टिषेण आर्ष्टिषेण, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>of Devāpi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत|आर्हतः
आर्हत आर्हत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अर्हत्), belong-<BR>ing to the doctrine of Jina or the Jains; (अस्), m. a<BR>Jaina, a follower of the doctrines of Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत्य|आर्हत्यं
आर्हत्य, अम्, n. the quality or practice of an<BR>Arhat or Jain saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आल|आलं|आलः
आल आल, अम्, n. spawn, any discharge of<BR>venomous matter from poisonous animals; yellow<BR>arsenic, orpiment; (अस्, आ, अम्), not small, large, ex-<BR>tensive.<BR>—आलाक्त (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. anointed<BR>with poison (as an arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्ष्
आलक्ष् आ-लक्ष्, cl. 10. P. A. -लक्षयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to descry, behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्ष्य
1. आ-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be observed, visible,<BR>apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्षण्य|आलक्षण्यं
आलक्षण्य आलक्षण्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-ल-<BR>क्षण), misfortune, crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्ष्य
आलक्ष्य 2. आ-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम् (3. आ pre-<BR>prefixed in the sense of diminution), scarcely visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलगर्द|आलगर्दः|आलगर्द्द|आलगर्द्दः
आलगर्द आलगर्द, अस्, m. a species of<BR>Cobra. See अलगर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलप्
आलप् आ-लप्, cl. 1. P. -लपति, -पितुम्, to<BR>address, speak to, converse: Caus. -लापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to engage (another) in conversation, to question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाप|आलापः
आ-लाप, अस्, m. speaking to, addressing, speech,<BR>conversation, communication; statement of the ques-<BR>tion in an arithmetical or algebraic sum; a question.<BR>—आलाप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, speaking, addressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापन
आ-लापन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to speak or converse<BR>about; (अम्), n. speaking to, conversing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापनीय
आ-लापनीय or आ-लाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be said or<BR>spoken, to be spoken to or addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापिन्
आ-लापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking or conversing with;<BR>(इनी), f. a lute made of a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्
आलभ् आ-लभ्, cl. 1. A. -लभते, -लब्धुम्,<BR>to take hold of, touch, handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभन|आलभनं
आ-लभन, अम्, n. taking hold of, bringing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्य
1. आ-लभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fit to be killed or<BR>sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्य
2. आ-लभ्य, ind. having received or obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भ|आलंभः|आलम्भः
आ-लम्भ, अस्, m. taking hold of, seizing, touching;<BR>tearing off, rooting out (of plants); the killing of the<BR>animal at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भन|आलंभनं
आ-लम्भन, अम्, n. taking hold of, touching;<BR>killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भनीय|आलंभनीय
आ-लम्भनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken hold of or<BR>handled, to be touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भिन्|आलंभिन्
आ-लम्भिन्, ई, इनी, इ, touching, taking hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भ्य
आ-लम्भ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, obtainable, to be obtained;<BR>fit or proper to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब्|आलंब्
आलम्ब् आ-लम्ब्, cl. 1. A. -लम्बते, -बितुम्,<BR>to rest or lean upon; to hang from; to depend; to<BR>lay hold of, support, seize; to strike up (a tune or<BR>note).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब|आलंब|आलम्बः
आ-लम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, hanging down; (अस्), m.<BR>that on which one rests or leans; support; receptacle;<BR>a prop; an asylum; depending on or from; a per-<BR>pendicular; (आ), f., N. of a plant with poisonous<BR>leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बन|आलंबनं|आलम्बनं
आ-लम्बन, अम्, n. depending on or resting upon,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">Page0130-b+ 71</a>]<BR>hanging from; supporting, sustaining; fundament,<BR>base; reason, cause; (in rhetoric) the natural and<BR>necessary connection of feeling with the cause which<BR>excites it; the mental exercise practised by the Yogin<BR>in endeavouring to realize the gross form of the<BR>eternal; silent repetition of a prayer; (with Bud-<BR>dhists) the five attributes of things corresponding to the<BR>five senses, viz. form, sound, smell, taste, and touch;<BR>also धर्म or law corresponding to मनस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बायन
आलम्बायन or आलम्बायनी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बि
आ-लम्बि, इस्, m., N. of a pupil of Vaiśampāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बित|आलंबित
आ-लम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, pendent, suspended, hang-<BR>ing from or on; supported, upheld; protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बिन्|आलंबिन्
आ-लम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hanging from, resting or<BR>leaning upon; depending on or from; laying hold<BR>of, supporting, maintaining; wearing; (इनस्), m. pl.<BR>N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब्य
आ-लम्ब्य, ind. having supported; supporting,<BR>sustaining; taking by the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलय|आलयं|आलयः
आलय आ-लय. See under 2. आ-ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलर्क
आलर्क आलर्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अलर्क), caused<BR>by or relating to a mad dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवण्य|आलवण्यं
आलवण्य आलवण्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-लवण),<BR>ugliness, insipidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवाल|आलवालं
आलवाल आलवाल, अम्, n. a basin for water<BR>round the root of a tree. See अलवाल, आवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस|आलसः
आलस आलस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अ-लस), idle,<BR>slothful, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस्य|आलस्यं|आलस्यः
आलस्य, अस्, ई, अम्, idle, slothful, apathetic; (अम्),<BR>n. idleness, sloth, want of energy.<BR>—आलस्य-निबन्-<BR>धन, अस्, आ, अम्, originating in indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाक्त
आलाक्त आलाक्त. See under आल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाट्य
आलाट्य आलाट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. लट् for रट्),<BR>Ved. being amongst the breakers of the sea (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलात|आलातं
आलात आलात, अम्, n. a firebrand; a coal<BR>burning or extinguished. See अलात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलान|आलानं
आलान आलान, अम्, n. (etym. doubtful), the<BR>post to which an elephant is tied; the rope that ties<BR>him; a fetter, a tie; a rope or string; tying, binding;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a minister of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलानिक
आलानिक, अस्, आ, अम्, serving as a post to which an<BR>elephant is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाप|आलापः
आलाप आ-लाप, &c. See under आ-लप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबु|आलाबुः
आलाबु आलाबु, उस्, or आलाबू, ऊस्, f. a pump-<BR>kin gourd. See अ-लाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलावर्त|आलावर्तं|आलावर्त्त|आलावर्त्तं
आलावर्त आलावर्त (˚ल-आव्˚?), अम्, n. a fan<BR>made of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलास्य|आलास्यः
आलास्य आलास्य (˚ल-आस्˚), अस्, m. a croco-<BR>dile (‘poison-mouthed;’ see आल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलि|आलिः
आलि आलि, इस्, m. (see अलि), a scorpion; a<BR>bee; (इस्), f. a woman's female friend; a row, range,<BR>continuous line [cf. आवलि]; a ridge or mound of<BR>earth crossing ditches, dividing fields, &c.; a dike;<BR>a line, a race, family; (इस्, इस्, इ), useless, idle, un-<BR>meaning; pure, honest, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्
आलिन्, ई, m. a scorpion [cf. अलिन्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली, f. a female friend, row, range, line, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिख्
आलिख् आ-लिख्, cl. 6. P. -लिखति, -लेखितुम्,<BR>to write, delineate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिखत्|आलिखन्त्
आ-लिखत्, अन्, m. scratching; N. of an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिख्य
आ-लिख्य, ind. pourtraying, delineating, sketching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखन|आलेखनं|आलेखनः
आ-लेखन, अस्, आ, अम्, scratching, painting; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a teacher; (ई), f. a brush, a pencil; (अम्),<BR>n. scratching, writing, painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्य|आलेख्यं
आ-लेख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be written, to be deline-<BR>ated or painted; (अम्), n. a painting, writing.<BR>—आले-<BR>ख्य-लेखा, f. painting.<BR>—आलेख्य-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having nothing left but a painting, deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिगी
आलिगी आलिगी, f., Ved., N. of a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग्|आलिंग्
आलिङ्ग् आ-लिङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. A. -लिङ्गति, -ते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">Page0130-c+ 73</a>]<BR>गितुम्, or cl. 10. P. -लिङ्गयति, -यितुम्, to clasp,<BR>join the limbs closely; to encircle, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग|आलिंगः|आलिङ्गः
आ-लिङ्ग, अस्, m. embracing; a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गन|आलिंगन|आलिंगनं|आलिङ्गनं
आ-लिङ्गन, अम्, n. clasping, embracing, an em-<BR>brace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गित|आलिंगित|आलिङ्गितः
आ-लिङ्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, embraced; (अम्), n. an<BR>embrace.<BR>—आलिङ्गित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has<BR>embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गिन्|आलिंगिन्
आ-लिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, embracing; (ई), m. a small<BR>drum, shaped like a barley corn and carried upon the<BR>breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग्य|आलिंग्य|आलिङ्ग्यः
1. आ-लिङ्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be embraced; (अस्), m.<BR>a small drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग्य|आलिंग्य|आलिङ्ग्यः
2. आ-लिङ्ग्य, ind. having embraced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिञ्जर|आलिंजर|आलिंजरः|आलिञ्जरः
