आशर|आशरः
आशर आ-शर, अस्, m. (rt. शॄ), fire; a<BR>Rakṣas, a goblin; the wind ? [cf. 1. आशिर].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशरीक|आशरीकः
आ-शरीक, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a disease, violent and<BR>acute pain in the limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशल|आशलः
आशल आशल, अस्, m. a tree. See जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशव|आशवं
आशव आशव, अम्, n. (fr. आशु), speed, quick-<BR>ness; (for आ-सव, q. v.) a spirit distilled from molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशसन|आशसनं
आशसन आ-शसन, अम्, n. (rt. शस्), Ved.<BR>cutting up an animal when killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशा
आशा 2. आशा, f. (fr. rt. 1. अश्; for 1. आ-शा see<BR>last page under आ-शंस्), space, region, quarter of the<BR>compass, an intermediate region.<BR>—आशा-गज, अस्, m.<BR>an elephant of a quarter or point of the compass, sup-<BR>porting one division of the globe.<BR>—आशा-दामन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—आशादित्य (˚शा-आद्˚) or आशार्क<BR>(˚शा-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—आशा-पाल,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. a defender or guardian of the regions or<BR>quarters.<BR>—आशा-पुर, आम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—आशा-<BR>पुर-गुग्गुलु, उस्, or आशापुर-सम्भव, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाढ|आशाढः
आशाढ आशाढ for आषाढ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशार|आशारः
आशार आ-शार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. श्रि with आ),<BR>shelter.<BR>—आशारैषिन् (˚र-एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ, Ved. seek-<BR>ing shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्
आशास् आ-शास्, cl. 2. P. -शास्ति, -शासितुम्, to<BR>order, command, relate; A. -शास्ते, to wish well<BR>towards, pray for; to praise; to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्य
आ-शास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished, desirable; (अम्),<BR>n. wish, benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिस्
1. आ-शिस्, ईस्, f. asking for, prayer, wish; blessing,<BR>benediction; bestowing or praying for a blessing upon<BR>others; one of the eight chief medicaments.<BR>—आशिर्-<BR>वाद or आशीर्-वाद, अस्, m. expression of a prayer or<BR>wish, benediction.<BR>—आशीर्-गेय, अम्, n. a song ac-<BR>companied with benedictions.<BR>—आशीर्-दा, f., Ved. the<BR>offering of a prayer.<BR>—आशीर्-वचन, अम्, n. a bless-<BR>ing, a benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
1. आ-शी, f. wishing or bestowing a blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशि|आशिः
आशि 2. आ-शि, cl. 3. P., Ved. -शिशेति, -शेतुम्,<BR>to incite. (For 1. आशि see under आश last page.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिक्षा
आशिक्षा आ-शिक्षा. See under आ-शक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिञ्जित|आशिंजित
आशिञ्जित आ-शिञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, tinkling (as<BR>of the ornaments worn on the hands and feet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित, आशिन्, आशिर। See under आश<BR>last page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन
आशिन आशिन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. अश्), Ved.<BR>aged; (reaching to many years.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिमन्
आशिमन् आशिमन्. See under आशु next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर्
आशिर् आशिर्, ईस्, f. (fr. rt. शॄ for श्री with आ),<BR>Ved. the milk which is mixed with the Soma juice to<BR>purify it (e. g. दध्याशिरः सोमासः = Soma offer-<BR>ings purified by mixture with thickened milk).<BR>—आशीर्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. mixed with milk (as Soma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर|आशिरः
2. आशिर, a form sometimes used for आशिर्. See also<BR>under आश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिरःपादम्
आशिरःपादम् आ-शिरः-पादम्, ind. from<BR>head to foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिस्
आशिस् 2. आशिस्, ईस्, f. (fr. rt. 1. अश्), a ser-<BR>pent's fang: (for 1. आ-शिस् see above.)<BR>—आशिर्-विष,<BR>अस्, m. a snake (having venom in its fang).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
2. आशी, f. a serpent's fang; a kind of venom, the<BR>venom of a snake.<BR>—आशी-विष, see आशिर्-विष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी 3. आ-शी, cl. 2. A. -शेते, -शयितुम्, to<BR>lie or sleep on, pass (the night) in sleep; to inhabit,<BR>have for one's home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशय|आशयः
आ-शय, अस्, m. bed-chamber, resting-place, seat,<BR>place, an asylum, an abode or retreat; a receptacle;<BR>any recipient, any vessel or viscus of the body (e. g.<BR>रक्ताशय, the heart; आमाशय, the stomach, &c.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">Page0133-b+ 76</a>]<BR>the stomach in particular; the seat of feelings and<BR>thoughts, the mind, heart; the thought lying in the<BR>mind, meaning, intention; disposition of mind, mode<BR>of thinking; will or pleasure; virtue, vice; fate, for-<BR>tune; property, possessions; a miser, a niggard; N.<BR>of the plant Artocarpus Integrifolia.<BR>—आशयाश (˚य-<BR>आश), अस्, m. fire; [cf. आश्रयाश under 1. आ-श्रि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशु|आशुः
आशु आशु, उस्, उस्, उ (said to be fr. 1. अश्),<BR>fast, quick, going quickly; (उ), ind. quickly, quick,<BR>immediately, directly; (उस्), m., Ved. the quick one,<BR>a horse; (उस् or उ), m. n. rice ripening quickly in the<BR>rainy season; [cf. Gr. ὠκύς, ὤκιστος Lat. acu in<BR>acupedeus, ôcissimus: of the same origin may be<BR>the Lat. aquila and accipiter.]<BR>—आशु-कारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, doing anything quickly, smart, active; (in medic.)<BR>operating speedily.<BR>—आशु-कोपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, easily pro-<BR>voked, irritable.<BR>—आशु-क्रिया, f. quick procedure.<BR>—आशु-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going or moving quickly,<BR>swift, fleet; (अस्), m. the wind; the sun; an arrow;<BR>N. of one of the first five followers of Śākya-muni.<BR>—आशु-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going or moving quickly;<BR>(ई), m. an epithet of the sun.<BR>—आशुङ्-ग, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>N. of an animal, perhaps a bird; going to the horse (?).<BR>—आशु-तोष, अस्, आ, अम्, easily pleased or appeased;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—आशु-त्व, अम्, n. quickness.<BR>—आशु-पत्त्री, f. a tree which yields frankincense,<BR>Boswellia Serrata.<BR>—आशु-पत्वन्, आ, m., Ved. flying<BR>quickly.<BR>—आशु-फल, अस्, m. a kind of weapon.<BR>—आशु-बोध, ‘easily understood,’ ‘teaching quickly,’<BR>title of a grammar.<BR>—आशु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. quick;<BR>(अत्), ind. quickly.<BR>—१. आशु-या, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. (Sāy.)<BR>going quickly.<BR>—आशु-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pos-<BR>sessing a fast chariot.<BR>—आशु-व्रीहि, इस्, m. rice ripen-<BR>ing quickly in the rainy season.<BR>—आशु-षेण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having swift arrows.<BR>—आशु-हेमन्, आ, m.,<BR>Ved. urged to fast course, running on quickly; inciting<BR>his horses (as an epithet of Agni, especially when<BR>regarded as Apāṃ-napāt).<BR>—आशु-हेषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. having neighing horses; (Sāy.) having quick<BR>horses or quickly praised; epithet of the Aśvins.<BR>—आश्व्-<BR>अपस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. acting quickly.<BR>—आश्व्-अश्व, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. possessed of quick horses; an epithet of<BR>the Maruts.<BR>—आश्वश्व्य, अम्, n., Ved. possession of<BR>quick horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिमन्
आशिमन्, आ, m. quickness, rapidity; = आशव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुया
2. आशुया, ind., Ved. quickly, rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुशुक्षणि|आशुशुक्षणिः
आशुशुक्षणि आ-शुशुक्षणि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt.<BR>शुच् with आ), Ved. shining forth; (Sāy.) ‘being<BR>worshipped on account of shining very quickly’ or<BR>‘causing sorrow (to one's enemies’); (इस्), m. fire,<BR>wind; air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशेकुटिन्
आशेकुटिन् आशेकुटिन्, ई, m. a mountain<BR>(etymology doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशोषण|आशोषणं
आशोषण आ-शोषण, अम्, n. the act of drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौच|आशौचं
आशौच आशौच, अम्, n. (fr. अ-शुचि), impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य|आश्चर्य्य|आश्चर्य्यं
आश्चर्य 1. आश्चर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. चर् with<BR>आ, with a sibilant inserted), appearing rarely, curious,<BR>marvellous, astonishing, wonderful, extraordinary;<BR>(अम्), ind. rarely, wonderfully; (अम्), n. strange ap-<BR>pearance; a wonder, miracle, marvel, prodigy; won-<BR>der, surprise; astonishment.<BR>—आश्चर्य-ता, f. or आश्-<BR>चर्य-त्व, अम्, n. wonderfulness, wonder, astonish-<BR>ment.<BR>—आश्चर्य-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, having a mar-<BR>vellous appearance, wonderful.<BR>—आश्चर्य-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, wonderful, marvellous, miraculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य|आश्चर्य्य|आश्चर्य्यं
2. आश्चर्य, nom. P. (?) -यति, -यितुम्, to be won-<BR>derful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चोतन
आश्चोतन आ-श्चोतन or आ-श्च्योतन, अम्, n.<BR>(fr. rt. श्चुत् or श्च्युत् with आ), aspersion, sprinkling;<BR>applying ghee &c. to the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्म|आश्मः
आश्म आश्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्मन्), stony,<BR>made of stone.<BR>—आश्मभारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्म-<BR>भार), having a mass of stones.<BR>—आश्मरथ्य, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a teacher of ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मन|आश्मनः
आश्मन, अस्, ई, अम्, stony, made of stone; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Aruṇa, the charioteer of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मरिक|आश्मरिकः
आश्मरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, suffering from stone in the<BR>bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मिक
आश्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, made of stone, consisting of<BR>stone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यै
आश्यै आ-श्यै, cl. 1. A. -श्यायते, -श्यातुम्,<BR>to become coagulated or congealed, to congeal, to<BR>become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यान
1. आ-श्यान, अस्, आ, अम्, consolidated, coagulated,<BR>congealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यान
2. आ-श्यान, अस्, आ, अम् (आ implying diminution),<BR>partially dried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रपण|आश्रपणं
आश्रपण आ-श्रपण, अम्, n. (rt. श्री with आ),<BR>the act of cooking slightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रम|आश्रमं|आश्रमः
आश्रम आ-श्रम, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. श्रम्<BR>with आ), a hermitage, the abode of ascetics, the<BR>cell of a hermit or of retired saints or sages; a period<BR>in the religious life of a Brāhman, of which there are<BR>four referable to the different periods of life (viz. 1st,<BR>that of the Brahma-cārin or student; 2nd, that of the<BR>Gṛha-stha or householder; 3rd, that of the Vāna-<BR>prastha or anchorite; and 4th, that of the Bhikṣu or<BR>beggar: in some places the law-givers mention only<BR>three such periods of religious life, the first period<BR>being then omitted); a college, a school; a wood or<BR>thicket.<BR>—आश्रम-गुरु, उस्, m. the head of a re-<BR>ligious order, a preceptor, a principal.<BR>—आश्रम-<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. the special duty or duties of each<BR>order or period of life.<BR>—आश्रम-पद, अम्, n. a<BR>hermitage; a period in the religious life of a Brāhman.<BR>—आश्रम-पर्वन्, अ, n. the first section of the fif-<BR>teenth book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—आश्रम-भ्र-<BR>ष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen or apostatising from an आश्रम<BR>or religious order.<BR>—आश्रम-मण्डल, अम्, n. the<BR>circle of a hermitage, a hermitage.<BR>—आश्रमवासिक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, relating to residence in a hermitage;<BR>आश्रमवासिकम् पर्व, title of the fifteenth book of<BR>the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—आश्रम-वासिन्, ई, or आश्रम-<BR>सद्, त्, m. an inhabitant of a hermitage, an ascetic.<BR>—आश्रम-स्थान, अम्, n. the abode of hermits, a<BR>hermitage.<BR>—आश्रमालय (˚म-आल्˚), अस्, m. an in-<BR>habitant of a hermitage, an ascetic.<BR>—आश्रमोपनि-<BR>षद् (˚म-उप्˚), त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिक|आश्रमिकः
आश्रमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or आश्रमिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>belonging to one of the four orders or periods of<BR>religious life; belonging to a hermitage, a hermit,<BR>an anchorite, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
आश्रव 1. आ-श्रव, अस्, m. (more correctly<BR>written आ-स्रव, q. v.), stream, flow, river; distress,<BR>fatigue; fault, transgression. (For 2. आ-श्रव see<BR>under आ-श्रु next page.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि 1. आ-श्रि, cl. 1. P. A. -श्रयति, -ते,<BR>-यितुम्, to resort to, betake one's self to; seek refuge<BR>in, enter, inhabit; depend on, choose, prefer; to<BR>assist, adhere to, be subject to, keep in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रय|आश्रयः
आ-श्रय, अस्, m. that to which anything is annexed,<BR>or with which anything is closely connected, or on<BR>which anything depends or rests; a recipient, the per-<BR>son or thing in which any quality or article is inherent<BR>or retained or received; seat, resting-place; dwelling,<BR>asylum, place of refuge, shelter; depending on, having<BR>recourse to; help, assistance, protection; authority,<BR>sanction, warrant; a plea, an excuse; being inclined<BR>or addicted to, following, practising; attaching to,<BR>choosing, taking; joining, union, attachment; de-<BR>pendance, contiguity, vicinity; relation; connection;<BR>appropriate act or one consistent with the character<BR>of the agent; (in gram.) the subject, that to which<BR>the predicate is annexed; (with Buddhists) the five<BR>organs of sense with मनस् or mind (the six together<BR>being the recipients of the आश्रित or objects which enter<BR>them by way of their आलम्बन or qualities); source,<BR>origin. आश्रय may occur at the end of compounds<BR>in the sense of ‘depending on, resting on, endowed<BR>or furnished with’ (e. g. अष्ट-गुणाश्रय, see under<BR>अष्ट).<BR>—आश्रय-तस्, ind. in consequence of the<BR>proximity.<BR>—आश्रय-त्व, अम्, n. the state of आ-श्रय<BR>above.<BR>—आश्रय-भुज्, क्, m. fire; see आश्रयाश.<BR>—आश्रय-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who is the refuge<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">Page0134-a+ 78</a>]<BR>or support of another person, protecting, supporting.<BR>—आश्रय-लिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, a word the gender of<BR>which must agree with the gender of the word to<BR>which it is referred, an adjective.<BR>—आश्रय-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having help or support.<BR>—आश्रयाश (˚य-<BR>आश), अस्, आ, अम्, consuming everything with which<BR>(it) comes in contact; (अस्), m. fire; a forfeiter of<BR>an asylum, one who by misconduct &c. loses patronage<BR>or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयण
आ-श्रयण, अस्, ई, अम्, resorting to, seeking refuge<BR>in; relating to; (अम्), n. betaking one's self to;<BR>joining, accepting, choosing; refuge, asylum, means<BR>of protection or security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयणीय
आ-श्रयणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be had recourse to,<BR>to be practised or followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित|आश्रितः
आ-श्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabiting, dwelling in, resort-<BR>ing to as a retreat or asylum; having recourse to;<BR>following, practising, observing; using, employing;<BR>receiving anything as an inherent or integral part;<BR>taking one's station at a window or seat &c.; depend-<BR>ant on, a dependant; (आनि), n. pl. the objects perceived<BR>by the senses and मनस् or mind.<BR>—आश्रित-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. dependance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित्य
आ-श्रित्य, ind. having sought or obtained an asylum;<BR>having recourse to, employing, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि 2. आश्रि, इस्, f. the edge of a sword.<BR>See अश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रु
आश्रु आ-श्रु, cl. 5. P. -शृणोति, -श्रोतुम्, to<BR>listen to, to hear; to accept, promise: Caus. -श्राव-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to hear, to call, to tell: Desid.<BR>-शुश्रूषति, to wish to hear; to listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
2. आ-श्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, obedient, compliant; (अस्),<BR>m. a promise, an engagement. (For 1. आ-श्रव see<BR>last page.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रावण|आश्रावणं
आ-श्रावण, अम्, n. calling out so as to make one<BR>listen; designation of certain short words uttered at<BR>ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्राव्य
आ-श्राव्य, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत|आश्रुतः
आ-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, heard, promised, agreed; (अम्),<BR>n. calling so as to make one listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुति|आश्रुतिः
आ-श्रुति, इस्, f., Ved. hearing; range of hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत्कर्ण
आश्रुत्-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. one whose ears<BR>listen all around.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्
आश्लिष् आ-श्लिष्, cl. 4. P. A. -श्लिष्यति, -ते,<BR>-श्लेष्टुम्, to embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रेष
आ-श्रेष, अस्, m. (for आ-श्लेष), Ved. one who<BR>embraces; N. of an evil spirit or goblin; (आस्), f. pl.,<BR>N. of the seventh Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्ट
आ-श्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, embraced; embracing, who<BR>or what embraces; connected, interwoven, blended;<BR>attaching to, joining, who or what adheres to; in-<BR>vested, spread; connected as a consequence, deduced,<BR>concluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेष|आश्लेषः
आ-श्लेष, अस्, m. embracing, embrace, intwining;<BR>intimate connection, contact; site of any act; (आस्),<BR>f. pl., N. of the seventh Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्व|आश्वं
आश्व आश्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व), relating or<BR>belonging to a horse, equestrian, coming from a horse<BR>(e. g. आश्वम् मूत्रम्, ‘the urine of a horse’); drawn<BR>by horses (e. g. आश्वो रथः, ‘a chariot drawn by<BR>horses’); (अम्), n. a number of horses, a chariot<BR>drawn by horses; the state or action of a horse.<BR>—आश्व-घ्न, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वतर
आश्वतर, अस्, m. (fr. अश्व-तर), patronymic of<BR>Buḍila (Bulila); a descendant of Aśvatara, son of<BR>Aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थ|आश्वत्थं
आश्वत्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्वत्थ), taken from<BR>or made of the tree Ficus Religiosa; relating to the<BR>fruit-bearing season of this tree; (अम्), n. the fruit<BR>of the holy fig tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थिक
आश्वत्थिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or produced by<BR>the Aśvattha tree; relating to its fruit-bearing season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वपेजिन्
आश्वपेजिन्, इनस्, m. pl. (fr. अश्व-पेज), the pupils<BR>or followers of Aśva-peja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वबल
आश्वबल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व-बला), produced<BR>by the plant Aśva-balā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वबाल
आश्वबाल or आश्ववाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व-बाल),<BR>made of the cane Aśva-bāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वमेधिक
आश्वमेधिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व-मेध), be-<BR>longing to the horse-sacrifice; (आश्वमेधिकम्<BR>पर्व is the N. of the fourteenth book of the Mahā-<BR>bhārata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुज|आश्वयुजः
आश्वयुज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व-युज्), born under<BR>the constellation Aśvayuj, belonging to or occurring<BR>in the month Āśvina; (अस्), m. the month Āśvina;<BR>(ई), f. the day of full moon in Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुजक
आश्वयुजक, अस्, ई, अम्, sown at the day of full<BR>moon in the month Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वरथ
आश्वरथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व-रथ), belonging<BR>to a chariot drawn by horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलक्षणिक|आश्वलक्षणिकः
आश्वलक्षणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अश्व-लक्षण),<BR>knowing the marks of horses; (अस्), m. a farrier,<BR>a groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वायन
आश्वायन, अस्, m. (fr. अश्व + अयन), a descendant<BR>of Aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विक|आश्विकः
आश्विक, अस्, ई, अम्, equestrian, cavalier, relating to<BR>a horse, drawn by horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विन|आश्विनः
आश्विन, अस्, ई, अम्, (if fr. 1. अश्विन्) Ved. like<BR>riders; belonging to or devoted to the Aśvins; (if fr.<BR>rt. 1. अश्, to pervade), pervading, penetrating; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a month of the rainy season, during which<BR>the moon is near to the constellation Aśvinī; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of certain (इष्टका), bricks; (अम्), n. a day's<BR>journey for a horse or rider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनेय|आश्विनेयः
आश्विनेय, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. अश्विनौ, the<BR>fathers of the twins Nakula and Sahadeva), N. of<BR>Sahadeva, the youngest of the Pāṇḍava princes; (fr.<BR>their mother अश्विनी), an epithet of either of the two<BR>Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीन|आश्वीनं|आश्वीनः
आश्वीन, अस्, ई, अम्, passed over by a horse in one<BR>day; (अम्), n. a day's journey for a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीय|आश्वीयं
आश्वीय, अम्, n. a number of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वेय
आश्वेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Aśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वपस्
आश्वपस् आश्व्-अपस्, &c. See under आशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलायन|आश्वलायनः
आश्वलायन आश्वलायन, अस्, m. (patronymic<BR>fr. अश्वल), N. of the author of a ritual work, called<BR>the Āśvalāyana Sūtras; he was a disciple of Śaunaka;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), belonging to Āśvalāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वस्
आश्वस् आ-श्वस्, cl. 2. P. -श्वसिति, -सितुम्, to<BR>breathe, breathe again, breathe freely, take breath,<BR>recover breath, take heart or courage; to revive:<BR>Caus. P. -श्वासयति, -यितुम्, to cause one to take<BR>breath; to encourage, comfort, cheer up; to con-<BR>ciliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वसत्
आ-श्वसत्, अन्, अती, अत्, taking breath, breathing<BR>anew; reviving; recovering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वसित
आ-श्वसित, अस्, आ, अम्, encouraged, cheered, con-<BR>soled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास|आश्वासः
आ-श्वास, अस्, m. breathing again, taking breath,<BR>breathing freely, recovery; cheering up, consolation;<BR>a chapter or section, the division of a book; a pro-<BR>bable story; cessation, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासक|आश्वासकः
आ-श्वासक, अस्, इका, अम्, consolatory, consoling,<BR>comforting; (अस्), m. clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासन|आश्वासनं
आ-श्वासन, अम्, n. making or letting one take<BR>breath, consoling, encouraging, reviving; cheering up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासयत्
आ-श्वासयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, encouraging, animating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासित
आ-श्वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, encouraged, animated, com-<BR>forted, consoled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासिन्
आ-श्वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, breathing freely, reviving, be-<BR>coming cheerful; consoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास्य
आ-श्वास्य, ind. having consoled, having cherished;<BR>having recovered or revived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढ|आषाढः
आषाढ आषाढ, अस्, m. (fr. अ-षाढा), N.<BR>of a month, corresponding to part of June and July,<BR>in which the full moon is near the constellation<BR>Aṣāḍhā; a staff of the wood of the Palāśa, carried<BR>by an ascetic during certain vows in the month<BR>Āṣāḍha; N. of a prince; the Malaya mountain;<BR>(आ), f. the twenty-first and twenty-second lunar<BR>mansions, commonly compounded with पूर्व and<BR>उत्तर; (ई), f. the day of full moon in the month<BR>Āṣāḍha.<BR>—आषाढ-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>in the month Āṣāḍha; (अस्), m. the planet Mars.<BR>—आषाढ-भूति, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—आषाढा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">Page0134-c+ 74</a>]<BR>भू, ऊस्, m. produced in the month Āṣāḍha; the<BR>planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढक|आषाढकः
आषाढक, अस्, m. the month Āṣāḍha; N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढिका
आषाढिका, f., N. of a Rākṣasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढीय
आषाढीय, अस्, आ, अम्, born under the constella-<BR>tion Aṣāḍhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्टक
आष्टक आष्टक, N. of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्टम|आष्टमः
आष्टम आष्टम, अस्, m. (fr. अष्टम), the<BR>eighth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्र|आष्ट्रं
आष्ट्र आष्ट्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. अश्), ether,<BR>sky, atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्री
आष्ट्री आष्ट्री, f., Ved. kitchen, fire-place;<BR>(if fr. rt. 1. अश्, according to Sāy.) an extensive forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ठा
आष्ठा आष्ठा, f. [cf. 2. आशा], region, quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् 1. आस्, ind. (an interjection implying<BR>joy, anger, menace, pain, affliction, recollection) Ah!<BR>Oh! &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् 2. आस् (आ-अस्), cl. 4. P., Ved. आस्यति,<BR>सितुम्, to enclose, border; to admit (as water) into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
3. आस् (fr. 2. आस् above ? or fr. rt. 2. अस्; cf. Lat. os),<BR>mouth, face; only used in two forms, as follows: आसस्,<BR>abl., Ved. from mouth to mouth, in close proximity;<BR>आसा, inst., Ved. before one's eyes; by word of mouth,<BR>personally; present; in one's own person; immedi-<BR>ately.<BR>—आस्-पात्र, अम्, n., Ved. a vessel which is as<BR>it were the mouth of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् 4. आस्, cl. 2. A. आस्ते (Ved. and poet.<BR>also cl. 1. A. आसते), आसाञ्-चक्रे, आसिष्यते,<BR>-आसिष्ट, -सितुम्, to sit, sit down, rest, lie; to be<BR>present, to exist, to inhabit, dwell in; to make one's<BR>abode in; to sit quietly, abide, remain, continue; to<BR>cease, have an end; to solemnize, celebrate; to do<BR>anything without interruption, to continue doing any-<BR>thing, to continue in any situation, to last. It is used<BR>in the sense of ‘continuing,’ with a participle, adj., or<BR>subst. (e. g. एतत् साम गायन्न् आस्ते, ‘he continues<BR>singing this verse’); with an indeclinable participle in<BR>त्वा, य, or अम् (e. g. उपरुध्य अरिम् आसीत, ‘he<BR>should continue blockading the foe’); with an adverb<BR>(e. g. तूष्णीम् आस्ते, ‘he continues quiet;’ सुखम्<BR>आस्व, ‘continue well’); with an inst. case (e. g.<BR>सुखेन आस्ते, ‘he continues well’); with a dat. case<BR>(e. g. आस्तां तुष्टये, ‘may it be to your satisfac-<BR>tion’): Caus. आसयति, -यितुम्, to cause any one to<BR>sit down: Desid. आसिसिषते; [cf. Gr. ἧ(σ)-μαι, ἧσ-<BR>ται Lat. âsa changed to âra; â-nus for âs-nus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
1. आस, seat (e. g. in the compound स्वास-स्थ,<BR>‘staying in one's own seat’); (अम्), n. the seat or<BR>lower part of the body; proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन|आसनं|आसनः
1. आसन, अम्, n. sitting, sitting down; sitting in<BR>peculiar postures, according to the custom of devotees,<BR>(five or, in other places, even eighty-four postures are<BR>enumerated; see पद्मासन, भद्रासन, वज्रा-<BR>सन, वीरासन, स्वस्तिकासन: the manner of<BR>sitting forming part of the eight-fold observances of<BR>ascetics); halting, stopping, encamping; abiding,<BR>dwelling; seat, place, stool; the withers of an ele-<BR>phant, the part where the driver sits; maintaining a<BR>post against an enemy; (आ), f. stay, abiding; (ई), f.<BR>stay, abiding, sitting; a shop, a stall; a small seat, a<BR>stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसित
आसित, अस्, आ, अम्, seated, at rest, one who has sat<BR>down, one who is seated or dwells; (अम्), n. sitting,<BR>sitting down; a seat; place where one has lived,<BR>place of abode, a city; दुर्-आसितम्, an improper<BR>way of sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीन|आसीनः
आसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting, seated.<BR>—आसीन-प्रच-<BR>लायित, अम्, n. nodding, nodding when seated, falling<BR>asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्या
आस्या, f. sitting, abiding, abode, state of rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् 5. आस् (आ-आस्), cl. 2. P., Ved. आस्ते, -सि-<BR>तुम्, to sit down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
आस 2. आस, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. अस्, to throw),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">Page0135-a+ 77</a>]<BR>Ved. ashes, dust which easily flies away; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a bow. (For 1. आस see under 4. आस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन|आसनं|आसनः
2. आसन, अम्, n. throwing; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>tree. See असन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसार
आसंसार आ-संसार, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. सृ), liable<BR>to continuous flow, progress or alteration; (अम्), ind.<BR>as long as the world goes on, till the end of the<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गत्य|आसंगत्य|आसंगत्यं
आसङ्गत्य आसङ्गत्य, अम्, n. (fr. अ-सङ्गत),<BR>detachment, disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसञ्ज्|आसंज्
आसञ्ज् आ-सञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. -सजति, -सङ्क्तुम्,<BR>to fasten on, attach, fix; to fasten on one's self, put<BR>on (as dress, armour, &c.); to take up: Caus. -सञ्ज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to attach, have (anything)<BR>fastened or put on: Pass. -सज्यते, to adhere, cohere,<BR>to be attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्त|आसक्तं|आसक्तः
आ-सक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, attached strongly to or intent<BR>on; zealously following or pursuing; trusting to,<BR>confiding in, eternal; (अम्), ind. eternally.<BR>—आसक्त-<BR>चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having the mind deeply engaged<BR>in, intent on, devoted to, absorbed in.<BR>—आसक्त-<BR>चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the mind fixed or intent on<BR>any object.<BR>—आसक्त-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having the<BR>mind fixed upon any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्ति|आसक्तिः
आ-सक्ति, इस्, f. devotedness or attachment (as to<BR>one object or pursuit), diligence, application; Ved.<BR>lying wait for, way-laying; (इ), ind., Ved. purposely,<BR>intentionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्ग|आसंग|आसङ्गं|आसङ्गः
आ-सङ्ग, अस्, m. fastening to, fixing; association,<BR>connection; attachment to any object; proximity,<BR>contact; Ved. way-laying; N. of a man; (अम्), n.<BR>a kind of fragrant earth; (अस्, आ, अम्), uninterrupted,<BR>eternal; (अम्), ind. without interruption; eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गिनी|आसंगिनी
आ-सङ्गिनी, f. a whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गिम|आसंगिमः|आसङ्गिमः
आसङ्गिम, अस्, m. (in surgery) a kind of bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसञ्जन|आसंजनं
आ-सञ्जन, अम्, n., Ved. putting on (dress, armour,<BR>ornaments, &c.); fastening to, fixing; a handle, a<BR>hook.<BR>—आसञ्जन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a handle,<BR>hook, loop, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसद्
आसद् आ-सद्, cl. 1. P. -सीदति, -सत्तुम्, to<BR>sit down, sit near; to place; to approach, meet with,<BR>find; encounter, attack, commence, undertake; cl.<BR>10. P. -सादयति, -यितुम्, to approach, meet with,<BR>find; encounter, attack; commence, undertake; Ved.<BR>to make one sit down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसत्ति|आसत्तिः
आ-सत्ति, इस्, f. intimate union, meeting, junction;<BR>gain, profit, acquirement; (in logic) connection or<BR>relation between two or more proximate terms and<BR>the sense they convey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसदन|आसदनं
आ-सदन, अम्, n. the act of sitting down; a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्न|आसन्नः
आ-सन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, near, proximate; (अस्), m.<BR>the setting sun.<BR>—आसन्न-काल, अस्, m. the hour of<BR>death; one whose last hour is at hand.<BR>—आसन्न-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम्, nearer.<BR>—आसन्नतर-ता, f. greater<BR>nearness.<BR>—आसन्न-प्रसव, अस्, आ, अम्, near par-<BR>turition, about to bring forth or to lay eggs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद|आसादः
आ-साद, अस्, m., Ved. a cushion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादन|आसादनं
आ-सादन, अम्, n. putting or laying down; attack-<BR>ing, making war upon; going to or towards; meeting<BR>with; obtaining, attaining; accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादयितव्य
आ-सादयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attacked, to be<BR>encountered; attainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादित|आसादितः
आ-सादित, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained, acquired, gained,<BR>reached, gone to; spread, extended, overspread;<BR>effected, completed; met with, attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद्य
1. आ-साद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, attainable, obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद्य
2. आ-साद्य, ind. having attained or reached; hav-<BR>ing obtained, according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिसादयिषु
आ-सिसादयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, about to attack; wishing<BR>to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्
आसन् आसन्, n. [cf. 2. आस् and आस्य], Ved.<BR>the mouth, the jaws; (this word occurs in inst.,<BR>dat., abl., loc. sing., and inst. plur.)<BR>—आसन्न्-इषु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one who has arrows in his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्य
आसन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन|आसनं|आसनः
आसन आसन, See under 4. आस् and 2. आस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्द|आसंदः|आसन्दः
आसन्द आसन्द, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सद् with आ ?),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">Page0135-b+ 71</a>]<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; (ई), f. a small couch or oblong<BR>chair, the seat of which is made of basket work;<BR>a chair, arm-chair.<BR>—आसन्दी-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्वत्|आसन्वन्त्
आसन्वत् आसन्वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. rt. 1. अस्?),<BR>Ved. what exists or is present (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसमुद्रात्
आसमुद्रात् आ-समुद्रात्, ind. as far as the<BR>ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसम्बाध|आसंबाध
आसम्बाध आ-सम्बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, blocked<BR>up, obstructed, confined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसया
आसया आसया, ind. (irreg. inst. case fr.<BR>3. आस्, q. v.), Ved. together with, from mouth to<BR>mouth, near to, in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
आसव आ-सव. See under आ-सु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसात्
आसात् आसात्, ind. (fr. 1. आस), Ved. from or<BR>in the proximity, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाधन|आसाधनं
आसाधन आ-साधन, अम्, n. (rt. 1. सिध्),<BR>accomplishment, attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिद्ध
1. आ-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished, effected.<BR>(For 2. आ-सिद्ध see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसार|आसारः
आसार आ-सार, अस्, m. (rt. सृ), surrounding<BR>an enemy; incursion; attack; a hard shower; the<BR>army of an ally or of a king, whose dominions are<BR>separated by other intervening states; provision, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाव्य
आसाव्य आ-साव्य. See under 2. आ-सु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक|आसिकः
आसिक आसिक, अस्, m. (fr. असि), a swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिका
आसिका आसिका, f. (fr. rt. 4. आस्), turn or<BR>order of sitting; sitting; (अस्, आ, अम्), one who sits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिच्
आसिच् 1. आ-सिच्, cl. 6. P. -सिञ्चति, -सेक्तुम्,<BR>to pour in or on, besprinkle, wet, water: Caus.<BR>-सेचयति, -यितुम्, to have (anything) poured in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक्त
आ-सिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, poured in or on; sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिच्
2. आ-सिच्, क्, f., Ved. a dish, vessel; (Say.) an oblation<BR>which is poured out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेक|आसेकः
आ-सेक, अस्, m. wetting, sprinkling, pouring in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचन|आसेचनः
आ-सेचन, अम्, n. the act of pouring into, wetting,<BR>sprinkling; Ved. a reservoir or vessel for fluids;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), charming, lovely, beloved [cf. अ-सेचन,<BR>for which it may be a substitute].<BR>—आसेचन-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, containing a reservoir or cavity, hollow,<BR>concave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचनक|आसेचनकः
आसेचनक, अस्, आ, अम् (?), beloved, desired, charm-<BR>ing [cf. अ-सेचन].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिद्ध
आसिद्ध 2. आ-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 2. सिध्),<BR>put under restraint, imprisoned. (For 1. see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेद्धृ
आ-सेद्धृ, धा, m. one who confines or arrests<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध|आसेधः
आ-सेध, अस्, m. arrest, custody, legal restraint of<BR>four kinds, viz. कालासेध, limitation of time; स्था-<BR>नासेध, confinement to a place; प्रवासासेध,<BR>prohibition against removal or departure; कर्मा-<BR>सेध, restriction from employment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेधक
आ-सेधक, अस्, आ, अम्, restraining, confining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेधनीय
आ-सेधनीय or आ-सेध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed<BR>in custody, restrained, confined, prohibited, interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसु
आसु 1. आ-सु, cl. 5. P., Ved. -सुनोति, -सोतुम्,<BR>to press out Soma juice, to distil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
1. आ-सव, अस्, m. distilling, distillation; decoction;<BR>rum, spirit distilled from sugar or molasses, spirituous<BR>liquor in general: (for 2. आ-सव see next col.)<BR>—आसव-द्रु, उस्, m., N. of the Palmyra tree, Bo-<BR>rassus Flabellifornis; (its juice on fermenting afford-<BR>ing a spirituous liquor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाव|आसावः
आ-साव, अस्, m., Ved. one who presses out the<BR>Soma juice; (Sāy.) a praiser (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुति|आसुतिः
1. आ-सुति, इस्, f. distilling; decoction; a draught so<BR>prepared; distillation: (for 2. आ-सुति see next col.)<BR>—आसुती-वल, अस्, m. a sacrificing priest; a sacrificer<BR>at the full and change of the moon; one who pre-<BR>pares or sells spirituous liquors, a distiller; one who<BR>sells female slaves (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसु
आसु 2. आ-सु, cl. 2. P., Ved. -सौति, -सोतुम्,<BR>to bring forth, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
2. आ-सव, अस्, m., Ved. exciting, enlivening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसवितृ
आ-सवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. exciting, an exciter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाव्य
आ-साव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुति|आसुतिः
2. आ-सुति, इस्, f., Ved. exciting, enlivening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर आसुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. असुर), spiritual,<BR>divine; belonging to or devoted to evil spirits; be-<BR>longing or relating to the Asuras; infernal, demoni-<BR>acal; (अस्), m. an Asura or demon; a form of mar-<BR>riage in which the bridegroom purchases the bride<BR>from her father and paternal kinsmen; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the stars of the southern hemisphere; a prince of the<BR>warrior-tribe Asura; (ई), f. a division of medicine,<BR>surgery, curing by cutting with instruments, applying<BR>the actual cautery; N. of the plant Sinapis Ramosa;<BR>(अम्), n. blood; black salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरायण|आसुरायणः
आसुरायण, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरि|आसुरिः
आसुरि, इस्, m. (patron. fr. असुर), N. of a teacher.<BR>—आसुरि-वासिन्, ई, m. an epithet of Prāśnīputra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरीय
आसुरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or coming from<BR>Āsuri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसू
आसू आ-सू, cl. 6. P., Ved. -सुवति, -सवितुम्,<BR>to bring or send quickly, yield, grant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसूत्रित
आसूत्रित आ-सूत्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, tied on or<BR>round, forming or wearing a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसृज्
आसृज् आ-सृज्, cl. 6. P., Ved. -सृजति, -स्रष्-<BR>टुम्, to pour out upon, pour in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध|आसेधः
आसेध आ-सेध. See 2. आ-सिद्ध last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेव्
आसेव् आ-सेव्, cl. 1. A. or poet. P. -सेवते,<BR>-ति, -वितुम्, to attend to, accomplish; carry out,<BR>practice, perform assiduously; to indulge in, enjoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवन|आसेवनं
आ-सेवन, अम्, n. assiduous practice or performance<BR>of any action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवा
आ-सेवा, f. zealous cultivation of any pursuit; com-<BR>merce, intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेविन्
आ-सेविन्, ई, इनी, इ, performing assiduously, acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्द्|आस्कंद्
आस्कन्द् आ-स्कन्द्, cl. 1. P. -स्कन्दति, -स्कन्-<BR>तुम्, to invade, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्द|आस्कंदः|आस्कन्दः
आ-स्कन्द, अस्, m. ascending, mounting; assault,<BR>attack; an assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दन|आस्कंदनं|आस्कन्दनं
आ-स्कन्दन, अम्, n. going towards, assailing, at-<BR>tack; battle, war; reproach, abuse; effacing, destroy-<BR>ing; drying (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दित|आस्कंदितं|आस्कन्दितं
आ-स्कन्दित or आ-स्कन्दितक, अम्, n. the walk of<BR>an horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दिन्|आस्कंदिन्
आ-स्कन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, jumping upon, assailing;<BR>causing to flow; granting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कु
आस्कु आ-स्कु, cl. 5. P., Ved. -स्कुनोति, -स्को-<BR>तुम्, to snatch up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्क्र
आस्क्र आ-स्क्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. स्कृ = rt. कृ?),<BR>Ved. joined, united; (Sāy.) attacking, assailing ene-<BR>mies, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तर|आस्तरः
आस्तर, आस्तरण, &c. See under आ-स्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्ताव|आस्तावः
आस्ताव आ-स्ताव, अस्, m. (rt. स्तु), Ved. the<BR>place of reciting a particular hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक|आस्तिकः
आस्तिक आस्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अस्ति, 3rd pers.<BR>sing. of rt. 1. अस्), a believer in sacred tradition; one<BR>who believes in God and another world; believing,<BR>pious, faithful; (अस्), m., N. of a Muni or saint,<BR>more correctly written आस्तीक, q. v.<BR>—आस्तिक-ता, f.<BR>or आस्तिक-त्व, अम्, n. belief in God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकार्थद|आस्तिकार्थदः
आस्तिकार्थद or आस्तीकार्थद (˚क-अर्थ-द),<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of king Janam-ejaya (who granted<BR>the request of the sage Āstika, and spared the Nāga<BR>Takṣaka from the destruction to which he had<BR>doomed the serpent-race).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक्य|आस्तिक्यं
आस्तिक्य, अम्, n. belief in God, piety, faithfulness,<BR>a believing nature or disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक|आस्तीकः
आस्तीक, अस्, m., N. of an old saint, the son of<BR>Jarat-kāru; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to or treating of<BR>that saint; आस्तीकम् पर्व, a section of the first<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">Page0136-a+ 74</a>]<BR>book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—आस्तीक-जननी, f. the<BR>wife of Jarat-kāru and mother of Āstīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक्य
आस्तीक्य, अम्, n. (? error for आस्तिक्य), belief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तृ
आस्तृ आ-स्तृ or आ-स्तॄ, cl. 5. 9. P. A. -स्तृ-<BR>णोति, -णुते, -णाति, -णीते, -स्तर्तुम्, -रितुम्, -रीतुम्,<BR>to spread (as a carpet &c.), deck, bestrew, scatter<BR>over, cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तर|आस्तरः
आ-स्तर, अस्, m. a covering, coverlet, blanket<BR>thrown over the back of a horse or elephant; a carpet,<BR>bed; spreading (clothes &c.); N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरण|आस्तरणं
आ-स्तरण, अम्, ई, n. f. the act of spreading; a<BR>carpet, a rug, a cushion, a quilt, bed-clothes; a bed;<BR>a layer of sacred grass spread out at a sacrifice;<BR>an elephant's housings, a painted cloth or blanket<BR>worn on his back.<BR>—आस्तरण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>covered with a cloth or carpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरणिक
आस्तरणिक, अस्, आ, अम्, resting on a cloth or<BR>carpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तार|आस्तारः
आ-स्तार, अस्, m. spreading, strewing, scattering.<BR>—आस्तार-पङ्क्ति, इस्, f., N. of a metre, the first<BR>verse of which consists of two Pādas of eight syllables<BR>each, the second of two Pādas of twelve syllables<BR>each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीर्ण|आस्तीर्ण्ण
आ-स्तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, strewed, scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तृत
आ-स्तृत, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, covered, strewed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्त्रबुध्न
आस्त्रबुध्न आस्त्रबुध्न, अस्, m., Ved., N. of<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था 1. आ-स्था, cl. 1. P. or poet. A.<BR>-तिष्ठति, -ते, -स्थातुम्, to stand or remain on or<BR>by; to stay near, go towards, resort to; to ascend,<BR>mount; to undertake, perform, do, carry out, practise,<BR>use; to behave; to exhibit, aim at; to undertake,<BR>i. e. promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
2. आ-स्था, f. consideration, regard, care, care for<BR>(with loc., e. g. मयि आस्था, care for me); assent,<BR>promise; confidence, hope; prop, stay, support;<BR>place or means of abiding; an assembly; state, con-<BR>dition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थातृ
आ-स्थातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. standing on, mount-<BR>ing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थान|आस्थानं
आ-स्थान, अम्, n. place, site, ground, base; an<BR>assembly; a hall of audience; (ई), f. an assembly.<BR>—आस्थान-गृह, अम्, n. an assembly-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थापन|आस्थापनं
आ-स्थापन, अम्, n. placing, fixing, causing to stay<BR>or remain; a strengthening remedy; an enema of oil,<BR>ghee, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थापित
आ-स्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed, fixed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थाय
आ-स्थाय, ind. having recourse to, using, employ-<BR>ing; having ascended; standing, standing by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थायिका
आ-स्थायिका, f. audience; (e. g. आस्थायिकां दा,<BR>to give an audience.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थित
आ-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, stayed, dwelt, abiding, abode;<BR>having recourse to; applied to; occupied, engrossed<BR>by, engaged in; spread, overspread; obtained; ob-<BR>serving, adhering to, following, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थेय
आ-स्थेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be approached, to be<BR>seized, to be applied or practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्नान|आस्नानं
आस्नान आ-स्नान, अम्, n. (rt. स्ना), Ved.<BR>water for washing, a bath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्नेय
आस्नेय आस्नेय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. असन्), Ved.<BR>bloody, being in blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पद|आस्पदं
आस्पद आस्पद, अम्, n. (fr. पद with आ<BR>prefixed, स् being inserted), place, site, seat, office;<BR>rank, station; dignity, authority; business, affair.<BR>Often used in comp.; e. g. अहङ्कारास्पदम्, the<BR>seat of consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पन्दन|आस्पन्दनं
आस्पन्दन आ-स्पन्दन, अम्, n. trembling,<BR>throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धा
आस्पर्धा आ-स्पर्धा, f. emulation, rivalry,<BR>endeavour after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धिन्
आ-स्पर्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, emulous, striving after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्श
आस्पर्श आ-स्पर्श, अस्, m. (rt. स्पृश्), contact;<BR>आस्पर्श-तस्, by the contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पात्र
आस्पात्र आस्-पात्र. See 3. आस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फल्
आस्फल् आ-स्फल् or आ-स्फुल्, Caus. -स्फाल-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to flap, rock or shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फाल|आस्फालः
आ-स्फाल, अस्, m. striking, rubbing, causing to<BR>move gently; flapping, clapping; the flapping mo-<BR>tion of an elephant's ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालन|आस्फालनं
आ-स्फालन, अम्, n. rubbing, stirring, flapping,<BR>moving gently; striking; pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालित
आ-स्फालित, अस्, आ, अम्, struck gently, rubbed,<BR>touched, stirred; flapped, clapped, struck together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फाय्
आस्फाय् आ-स्फाय्, cl. 1. A. -स्फायते, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to grow, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुजित्
आस्फुजित् आस्फुजित् = Ἀφροδίτη N. of the<BR>planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुल्
आस्फुल् आ-स्फुल्. See आ-स्फल् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोट|आस्फोटः
आस्फोट आ-स्फोट, अस्, m. (rt. स्फुट्), moving<BR>or flapping to and fro, quivering, trembling, shaking,<BR>the sound of clapping or striking on the arms as<BR>made by combatants, wrestlers, &c.; a plant, see<BR>आ-स्फोत; (आ), f. a wild variety of Jasmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटक|आस्फोटकः
आ-स्फोटक, अस्, m., the plant Careya Arborea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटन|आस्फोटनं
आ-स्फोटन, अम्, n. moving to and fro, flapping,<BR>trembling; shaking; blowing, expanding; contracting,<BR>closing, sealing; slapping or clapping the arms, or<BR>the noise made by it; (ई), f. a gimlet or auger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोत|आस्फोतः
आ-स्फोत or आ-स्फोतक, अस्, m. (probably an in-<BR>correct form of आ-स्फोट), N. of several plants, Ca-<BR>lotropis Gigantea, Bahinia Variegata L., Echites Di-<BR>chotoma Roxb.; (आ), f., N. of several plants, Jasmi-<BR>num Sambac, Clitoria Terneata, Echites Frutescens<BR>or Echites Dichotoma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माक
आस्माक आस्माक, अस्, ई, अम्, or आस्माकीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अस्माकम्), our, ours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्य|आस्यं
आस्य आस्य, अम्, n. (see 3. आस्), mouth,<BR>jaws; face; a part of the mouth as the organ of<BR>pronouncing letters; mouth, opening; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>belonging or relating to the mouth or face.<BR>—आस्यन्-<BR>धय, अस्, ई, अम्, drinking the mouth, kissing.<BR>—आस्य-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a lotus.<BR>—आस्य-लाङ्गल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘whose face is a plough;’ a hog, a boar.<BR>—आस्य-लोमन्, अ, n. the hair of the face, the beard.<BR>—आस्यासव (˚य-आस्˚), अस्, m. spittle, saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यन्दन|आस्यंदनं
आस्यन्दन आ-स्यन्दन, अम्, n. flowing near.<BR>—आस्यन्दन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, flowing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यहात्य
आस्यहात्य आस्यहात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, containing<BR>the word अस्यहत्य (a chapter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्या
आस्या आस्या, f. See under 4. आस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रप|आस्रपः
आस्रप आस्रप, अस्, m. (fr. अस्र-प), the<BR>nineteenth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रव|आस्रवः
आस्रव आ-स्रव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्रु with<BR>prep. आ), the foam on boiling rice; flowing, running,<BR>discharge; distress, pain, affliction; (with Jainas) that<BR>which directs the embodied spirit towards eternal<BR>objects, (viz. the occupation or employment of the<BR>senses or organs on sensible objects; or the association<BR>or connection of body with right and wrong deeds.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राव|आस्रावः
आ-स्राव, अस्, m. flow, issue, running, discharge;<BR>pain, affliction; a disease of the body.<BR>—आस्राव-<BR>भेषज, अम्, n., Ved. a medicament, medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राविन्
आस्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, flowing, emitting fluid, dis-<BR>charging humor; an epithet of the elephant (a fluid<BR>issuing from its temples during the rutting-time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रस्त
आस्रस्त आ-स्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen off,<BR>loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वद्
आस्वद् आ-स्वद् or -स्वाद्, cl. 1. A. -स्वदते<BR>or -स्वादते, -दितुम्, to taste, eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद|आस्वादः
आ-स्वाद, अस्, आ, अम्, tasting, eating; (अस्), m.<BR>tasting, enjoying, eating; flavour.<BR>—आस्वाद-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having a good taste, palatable; delicious in<BR>flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादक
आ-स्वादक, अस्, इका, अम्, tasting, enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादन|आस्वादनं
आ-स्वादन, अम्, n. tasting, enjoying, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादित
आ-स्वादित, अस्, आ, अम्, tasted, enjoyed, possessed;<BR>eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद्य
आ-स्वाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be tasted or enjoyed,<BR>to be eaten; having a good taste, palatable, delicious.<BR>—आस्वाद्य-तोय, अस्, आ, अम्, having sweet or palata-<BR>ble water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वन्
आस्वन् आ-स्वन्, cl. 1. P. -स्वनति, -नितुम्,<BR>to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वनित
आ-स्वनित or आ-स्वान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह
आह 1. आह, ind. (an interjection implying<BR>reproof, severity, command, casting, sending) Ah!<BR>Aha! &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह
आह 2. आह. See rt. 3. अह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहक|आहकः
आहक आहक, अस्, m. a peculiar disease of<BR>the nose, inflammation of the Schneiderian membrane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहङ्कार्य|आहंकार्यं
आहङ्कार्य आहङ्कार्य, अम्, n. (fr. अहङ्-कार),<BR>conceitedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहन्
आहन् आ-हन्, cl. 2. P. A. -हन्ति, -हते,<BR>-हन्तुम्, to strike at, hit, beat, kill; commit<BR>slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत|आहतं|आहतः
आ-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck, beaten; injured, killed;<BR>multiplied; known, understood; uttered falsely; (अस्),<BR>m. a drum; (अम्), n. old cloth or raiment; new cloth<BR>or clothes; assertion of an impossibility.<BR>—आहत-<BR>लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, noted for good qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहति|आहतिः
आ-हति, इस्, f. hitting, striking, a blow, a hit;<BR>killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहनन|आहननं
आ-हनन, अम्, n. the act of striking at, beating;<BR>killing of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहनन्य
आहनन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. making one's self<BR>known by beating (a drum &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहनस्
आहनस् आहनस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (fr. rt. हन् ?),<BR>Ved. swelling, tumid, crammed full; fat, luxuriant,<BR>lascivious; (Sāy.) to be beaten or pressed out (as<BR>Soma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहनस्य
आहनस्य, अम्, n., Ved. luxuriancy, lasciviousness;<BR>(आस्), f. pl. verses (ऋचस्) of a lascivious character.<BR>—आहनस्य-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. uttering las-<BR>civious words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहलक्
आहलक् आहलक्, ind., Ved. a smacking<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
आहव, आहवन, आह्व, &c. See under<BR>आ-हु and आ-ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिक|आहिकः
आहिक आहिक, अस्, m. (fr. अहि), the descend-<BR>ing node; an epithet of the grammarian Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिकम्
आहिकम् आहिकम्, a particle = आहि कम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिण्ड्|आहिंड्
आहिण्ड् आ-हिण्ड्, cl. 1. A. -हिण्डते, -डितुम्,<BR>to roam about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिण्डिक|आहिंडिकः|आहिण्डिकः
आहिण्डिक आहिण्डिक, अस्, m. a man of mixed<BR>origin, the son of a Niṣāda father and a Vaidehī mother,<BR>employed as a watchman on the outside of gaols &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहित|आहितः
आहित आ-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. धा with<BR>prep. आ), placed, deposited; entertained, felt; com-<BR>prising, containing; performed, done.<BR>—आहित-क्लम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, exhausted.<BR>—आहित-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>noted or known for good qualities; [cf. आहत-<BR>लक्षण.]<BR>—आहित-व्यथ, अस्, आ, अम्, pained,<BR>grieved.<BR>—आहित-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, uttering or<BR>making a sound noisy.<BR>—आहिताग्नि (˚त-अग्˚), इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, one who has placed the sacred fire upon the altar,<BR>a sacrificer; a Brāhman who has kept alive a sacred<BR>fire perpetually in a family &c.<BR>—आहिताङ्क (˚त-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, marked, spotted, stained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिति|आहितिः
आ-हिति, इस्, f., Ved. placing on; anything placed on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितुण्डिक|आहितुंडिकः|आहितुण्डिकः
आहितुण्डिक आहितुण्डिक or अहितुण्डिक, अस्,<BR>m. (fr. अहि-तुण्ड), a snake-catcher, a juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहीरणिन्
आहीरणिन् आहीरणिन्, ई, m. a two-headed<BR>snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहु|आहुः
आहु आ-हु, cl. 3. P. A. -जुहोते, -जुहुते, -हो-<BR>तुम्, to sacrifice, to offer an oblation, to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
1. आ-हव, अस्, m. sacrificing, sacrifice. (For 2.<BR>आ-हव see under आ-ह्वे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0136-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवन|आहवनं
आ-हवन, अम्, n., Ved. offering an oblation,<BR>offering sacrifice, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीय|आहवनीयः
आ-हवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be offered as an obla-<BR>tion; (अस्), m. a consecrated fire taken from the<BR>householder's perpetual fire and prepared for receiving<BR>oblations; the eastern of the three fires burning at<BR>a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयक|आहवनीयकः
आहवनीयक, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for a burnt offering;<BR>(अस्), m. a consecrated fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहाव|आहावः
1. आ-हाव, अस्, m., Ved. a trough, a pail, a vessel;<BR>a trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुत|आहुतं
आ-हुत, अम्, n. an offering made to men, hospi-<BR>tality; the nourishment of all created beings con-<BR>sidered as one of the five sacraments or principal<BR>sacrifices of the Hindūs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुति|आहुतिः
1. आ-हुति, इस्, f. offering oblations with fire to the<BR>deities; any solemn rite accompanied with oblations:<BR>(for 2. आ-हुति see under आ-ह्वे.)<BR>—आहुती-वृध्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. delighting in sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुक|आहुकः
आहुक आहुक, अस्, m., N. of a prince, great-<BR>grandfather of Kṛṣṇa, a son or grandson of Abhi-<BR>jit; (ई), f. a sister of this prince; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुल्य|आहुल्यं
आहुल्य आहुल्य, अम्, n., N. of the legumi-<BR>nous shrub Tabernæmontana Coronaria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृ
आहृ आ-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते, -हर्तुम्,<BR>to fetch, bring, bring near, give; to recover, bring<BR>back; to get, take; to offer in sacrifice: Caus. P.<BR>-हारयति, -यितुम्, to make one pay or give or<BR>fetch or bring; to exact; to exert, exhibit: Desid.<BR>A. -जिहीर्षते, to seek to recover or get back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर|आहरः
आ-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of compounds)<BR>bringing, fetching; (अस्), m. taking, seizing; accom-<BR>plishing, offering of a sacrifice; drawing in breath,<BR>inhaling, inhaled air; breath inspired, inspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरण|आहरणं
आ-हरण, अस्, आ, अम्, taking away, robbing; (अम्),<BR>n. taking, seizing, bringing near; extracting, remov-<BR>ing; accomplishing, offering at a sacrifice; causing,<BR>inducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरणीकृ
आहरणी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to give<BR>as a present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर्तृ|आहर्त्तृ
आ-हर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who takes, seizes, brings<BR>or procures; inducing, causing; offering; (ता), m.<BR>a copy holder (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार|आहारः
आ-हार, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, bringing near, procuring;<BR>going to fetch; (अस्), m. taking, fetching, bringing<BR>near; employing; taking food, food (e. g. आहारं<BR>कृ, to take food, eat).<BR>—आहार-विरह, अस्, m.<BR>want of food.<BR>—आहार-सम्भव, अस्, m. the juice<BR>of the body, chyle, lymph, serum.<BR>—आहारार्थिन्<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, begging or seeking for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारक
आ-हारक, अस्, आ, अम्, going to fetch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारिक|आहारिकं
आ-हारिक, (with Jainas) one of the five bodies<BR>belonging to the soul; described by Colebrooke as a<BR>minute form, issuing from the head of a meditative<BR>sage to consult an omniscient saint and returning with<BR>the desired information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य|आहार्यः|आहार्य्य|आहार्य्यं|आहार्य्यः
आ-हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or seized; to be<BR>fetched or brought near; to be extracted or removed;<BR>what may be removed, adventitious, accessary, inci-<BR>dental; to be eaten; (अस्), m. a kind of bandage;<BR>(अम्), n. any disease to be treated by the operation of<BR>extracting; extraction; a vessel; the ornamentative<BR>part of the drama, the dress, decorations, &c.<BR>—आहार्य-<BR>शोभा, f. adventitious beauty, beauty not natural but<BR>the effect of paints, ornaments, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृत
आ-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought, taken, collected.<BR>—आहृत-यज्ञ-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. intending<BR>(to offer) a prepared sacrifice; preparing a sacrificial<BR>act (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृत्य
आ-हृत्य, ind. having taken or received, having<BR>brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहेय|आहेयं
आहेय आहेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. अहि), belonging<BR>or relating to a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहो
आहो आहो, ind. (an interjection of doubt<BR>and of asking) or, or perhaps.<BR>—आहो-पुरुषिका, f.<BR>great self-conceit, boasting, military vaunting; a vain<BR>determination to accomplish an object, vaunting of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">Page0137-b+ 78</a>]<BR>one's power.<BR>—आहो-स्वित्, ind. a particle implying<BR>doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्न|आह्नः
आह्न आह्न, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. अहन्), a series<BR>of days, many days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निक|आह्निकं
आह्निक, अस्, ई, अम्, daily, diurnal, performed on a<BR>day, performed every day; (अम्), n. a religious cere-<BR>mony to be performed every day at a fixed hour; a<BR>day's work, what may be read on one day, the division<BR>or section of a book; constant occupation, daily work;<BR>daily food, &c.<BR>—आह्निकाचार (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, m. daily<BR>observance, the prayers and practices necessary for<BR>bodily and mental purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्नेय
आह्नेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of Śauca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लाद्
आह्लाद् आ-ह्लाद्, Caus. P. -ह्लादयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to gladden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लाद|आह्लादः
आ-ह्लाद, अस्, m. joy, delight.<BR>—आह्लाद-दुघ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, conferring delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादन
आ-ह्लादन, अम्, n. gladdening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादि
आ-ह्लादि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Babhru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादित|आह्लादितः
आ-ह्लादित, अस्, आ, अम्, delighted, rejoiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृ
आह्वृ आ-ह्वृ, cl. 1. P., Ved. -ह्वरति, -ह्वर्-<BR>तुम्, to make crooked, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूर्य
आ-हूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be bent down or<BR>brought near; to be made favourable, one towards<BR>whom one must bow; (Sāy.) to be invoked (fr. rt.<BR>ह्वे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्रुत
आ-ह्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, injured.<BR>—आह्रुत-भेषज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. curing what is bent or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वर
आ-ह्वर, अस्, m., N. of a fortress of the Uśīnaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वरक|आह्वरकः
आ-ह्वरक, अस्, m. a low or expelled man who,<BR>after having offered a sacrifice to the manes, takes<BR>the sacrificial food for himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वारक|आह्वारकः
आह्वारक, आस्, m. pl. the Āhvārakas, a recension<BR>of the black Yajur-veda (distinct from the Taittirīya)<BR>named from Ahvāra or Āhvāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृति
आ-ह्वृति, इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वे
आह्वे आ-ह्वे, cl. 1. P. or poet. A. -ह्वयति,<BR>-ते, -ह्वातुम्, to call near; to summon; to invite,<BR>ask; A. to provoke, challenge, emulate: Caus.<BR>-ह्वाययति, -यितुम्, to send for; to cause to invite<BR>or summon or challenge; provoked: Desid. -जुहू-<BR>षति, to wish to call near or invite: Intens. -जोहवीति,<BR>to call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
2. आ-हव, अस्, m. challenge, provoking, calling;<BR>war, battle.<BR>—आहव-काम्या, f. desire of war: (for<BR>1. आ-हव see under आ-हु, page 136, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहाव|आहावः
2. आ-हाव, अस्, m. calling, invoking; battle, war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुति|आहुतिः
2. आ-हुति, calling, invoking. (This word may<BR>sometimes have this sense in the oldest Vedic texts,<BR>but see the more correct form आ-हूति. For 1. आ-<BR>हुति see under आ-हु last col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुव
आ-हुव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (Sāy.) to be invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहू
आ-हू, f., Ved. calling, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूत|आहूतं|आहूतः
2. आ-हूत, अस्, आ, अम्, called, summoned, invoked,<BR>invited.<BR>—आहूत-प्रपलायिन्, ई, m. a defendant or<BR>witness absconding or not appearing when summoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूति|आहूतिः
आ-हूति, इस्, f. calling, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूय
आ-हूय, ind. having invited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्व
आ-ह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what calls, a crier;<BR>named, called; (आ), f. a name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वय|आह्वयः
आ-ह्वय, अस्, m. a lawsuit arising from a dispute<BR>about games with animals, as cock-fighting &c.; ap-<BR>pellation, name (generally as last member of a com-<BR>pound, the first member of which, though commonly<BR>an appellative noun, is used as a proper name).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयत्
आ-ह्वयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, calling, challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयन
आ-ह्वयन, अम्, n. appellation, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयितव्य
आ-ह्वयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be summoned or<BR>invited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वान|आह्वानं
आ-ह्वान, अम्, n. calling, invitation, a call or sum-<BR>mons; invocation of a deity; challenge; legal sum-<BR>mons; an appellation, a name; designation of a<BR>liturgical formula.<BR>—आह्वान-दर्शन, अम्, n. day<BR>of trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानय
आह्वानय, nom. P. आह्वानयति, -यितुम्, (in law)<BR>to summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वाय|आह्वायः
आ-ह्वाय, अस्, m. a summons, a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायक|आह्वायकः
आ-ह्वायक, अस्, m. a messenger, a courier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वाययितव्य
आ-ह्वाययितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be called before<BR>a tribunal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ 1. इ, the third vowel of the alphabet,<BR>corresponding to इ short, and pronounced as that letter<BR>in kill &c.<BR>—इ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ 2. इ, ind. an interjection of anger, calling,<BR>sorrow, distress, compassion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ 3. इ, pronominal base of the 3rd person;<BR>[cf. इतर, इतस्, इति, इद्, इदम्, इदा, इयत्, इव, इह:<BR>cf. also Lat. id; Goth. ita; Eng. it; Old Germ.<BR>iz; Mod. Germ. es.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ 4. इ, इस्, m. a N. of Kāmadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ 5. इ, cl. 2. P., 1. P. A. एति, अयति, -ते,<BR>इयाय, एष्यति, एतुम्, Ved. एतवे, एतवै, एतोस्,<BR>to go; to go to or towards (with acc.); to come; to<BR>go away, escape, pass, retire; to return; to arrive at,<BR>reach, obtain; to fall into; to arise from, come<BR>from; to approach with prayers, ask; to undertake<BR>anything (with acc.); to appear, to be; to go on<BR>well, to prosper (e. g. तस्मिन् युक्तस्य एति प्रेत-<BR>कृत्या, ‘the funeral ceremony of one engaged in that<BR>goes on well or prospers’); to be employed in, go on<BR>with, be in any condition or relation (with a part. or<BR>inst., e. g. असुर-रक्षसानि मृद्यमानानि यन्ति,<BR>‘the Asuras and Rakṣas are being trampled upon;’<BR>गवामयनेन ईयुः, ‘they were engaged in the<BR>Gavāmayana’): Intens. or cl. 4. A. ईयते, inf., Ved.<BR>ईयध्यै, to go quickly or repeatedly; to come,<BR>wander, run; to appear, make one's appearance; to<BR>approach any one with requests (with two acc.), ask,<BR>request; to be asked or requested: Caus. आययति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to come; [cf. Gr. εἶ-μι, ἴ-μεν;<BR>Lat. eo, îmus; Lith. ei-mi, ‘I go;’ Slav. i-dû,<BR>‘I go,’ i-ti, ‘to go;’ Goth. i-ddja.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्
इत्, (at the end of a few compounds) going; cf.<BR>अर्थेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत|इतः
इत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; returned; obtained; re-<BR>membered; (अम्), n. way.<BR>—इतासु (˚त-अस्˚), उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, Ved. whose vital spirits have departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
1. इति, इस्, f., Ved. going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्य|इत्यः
इत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्या
इत्या, f., Ved. going, a way; a litter, a palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वन्
इत्वन्, आ, आ, अ, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वर|इत्वरः
इत्वर, अस्, ई, अम्, going, travelling, a traveller;<BR>cruel, harsh; poor, indigent; low, vile; contemned;<BR>(ई), f. a disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्कट|इक्कटः
इक्कट इक्कट, अस्, m. a kind of reed. See<BR>इत्कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्कवाल|इक्कवालः
इक्कवाल इक्कवाल in astrology = إِقْبال<BR>iqbâl, good fortune, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षु|इक्षुः
इक्षु इक्षु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. इष्?), the sugar-<BR>cane (twelve species of it are enumerated); N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—इक्षु-काण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. the stem or<BR>cane of the Saccharum Officinale, the sugar-cane;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of two different species of sugar-cane,<BR>viz. Saccharum Munja Roxb. and Saccharum Spon-<BR>taneum L.<BR>—इक्षु-कुट्टक, अस्, m. a gatherer or<BR>reaper of sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-गन्ध, अस्, m. Sac-<BR>charum Spontaneum; a kind of Asteracantha Longi-<BR>folia; (आ), f. Saccharum Spontaneum, Asteracantha<BR>Longifolia, Capparis Spinosa, Batatas Paniculata.<BR>—इक्षु-गन्धिका, f. Batatas Paniculata.<BR>—इक्षु-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-<BR>तुल्या, f. Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—इक्षु-दण्ड,<BR>अम्, n. the stem or cane of the Saccharum Officinale.<BR>—इक्षु-दर्भा, f. a kind of grass or sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-दा, f., N. of a river; see इक्षुला, इक्षु-<BR>मालिनी, इक्षु-मालवी.<BR>—इक्षु-नेत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the grain<BR>Penicillaria Spicata.<BR>—इक्षु-पाक, अस्, m. molasses.<BR>—इक्षु-प्र, अस्, m. the plant Saccharum Sara.<BR>—इक्षु-बालिका, f. Saccharum Spontaneum, = इक्षु-<BR>तुल्या.<BR>—इक्षु-भक्षिका, f. a meal of sugar or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">Page0138-a+ 78</a>]<BR>molasses.<BR>—इक्षु-मती, f., N. of a river in Kuru-<BR>kṣetra.<BR>—इक्षु-मालवी or इक्षु-मालिनी, f., N. of<BR>a river; see इक्षु-दा.<BR>—इक्षु-मूल, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of sugar-cane; the root of sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-मेह,<BR>अस्, m. diabetes or diabetes mellitus; see मधु-<BR>मेह.<BR>—इक्षुमेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, diabetic.<BR>—इक्षु-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a sugar-mill.<BR>—इक्षु-योनि, इस्, m.<BR>Saccharum Officinarum.<BR>—इक्षु-रस, अस्, m. the<BR>juice of the sugar-cane; molasses, unrefined sugar;<BR>the cane Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—इक्षुरस-<BR>क्वाथ, अस्, m. raw or unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR>—इक्षुरसोद (˚स-उद्˚), अस्, m. the sea of syrup.<BR>—इक्षु-वण, अम्, n. a sugar-cane wood.<BR>—इक्षु-<BR>वल्लरी and इक्षु-वल्ली, f. Batatas Paniculata.<BR>—इक्षु-वाटिका or इक्षु-वाटी, f. Saccharum Offici-<BR>narum, the common yellow cane.<BR>—इक्षु-वारि, n.<BR>the sea of syrup, one of the seven seas.<BR>—इक्षु-<BR>विकार, अस्, m. sugar, molasses; any sweetmeat.<BR>—इक्षु-वेष्टन, अस्, m. a kind of sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-शाकट or इक्षु-शाकिन, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of sugar-cane.<BR>—इक्षु-समुद्र, अस्, m. the sea of<BR>syrup, one of the seven seas.<BR>—इक्षु-सार, अस्, m.<BR>molasses, raw or unrefined sugar.<BR>—इक्ष्वारि, इस्, m.<BR>(for इक्षु-वारि ?), Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—इक्ष्-<BR>वालिक, अस्, m. (for इक्षु-बालिक), Saccharum Spon-<BR>taneum; (आ), f. another sort, Saccharum Fuscum,<BR>(native reed-pens are made from its stem.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0137-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुक|इक्षुकः
इक्षुक, अस्, m. sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुकीया
इक्षुकीया, f. a region abounding in sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुर|इक्षुरः
इक्षुर, अस्, m. Capparis Spinosa; Asteracantha<BR>Longifolia; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरक|इक्षुरकः
इक्षुरक, अस्, m. Capparis Spinosa; Saccharum<BR>Spontaneum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुला
इक्षुला, f., N. of a river. See इक्षु-दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्ष्वाकु|इक्ष्वाकुः
इक्ष्वाकु इक्ष्वाकु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Manu Vaivasvata, father of Kukṣi and first king of<BR>the solar dynasty in Ayodhyā; a descendant of<BR>Ikṣvāku; the Jainas derive their Cakravartins and<BR>many of their Arhats from Ikṣvāku; (आस्), m., N.<BR>of a warrior-tribe derived from Ikṣvāku; (उस्), f. a<BR>bitter gourd; according to some, the Coloquintida<BR>(Citrillus Colocynthis), the fruit of a wild species of<BR>Lagenaria Vulgaris.<BR>—इक्ष्वाकु-कुल-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>born in the family of Ikṣvāku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इख्
इख् इख्, cl. 1. P. एखति, इयेख, एखिष्-<BR>यति, एखितुम्, to go, move; [cf. Gr. εἴκω<BR>οἴχομαι ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्कार|इंकार
इङ्कार इङ्-कार and इङ्-कृत = हिङ्-कार,<BR>हिङ्-कृत, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्ख्|इंख्
इङ्ख् इङ्ख्, cl. 1. P. इङ्खति, इङ्खाञ्-चकार,<BR>इङ्खिष्यति, इङ्खितुम्, to go, move; [cf.<BR>Hib. imchim, ‘I go on, proceed, march.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्ग्|इंग्
इङ्ग् इङ्ग्, cl. 1. P., ep. A. इङ्गति, -ते,<BR>इङ्गाञ्-चकार, इङ्गिष्यति, इङ्गितुम्, to<BR>go, go to or towards; to move or agitate: Caus.<BR>P. इङ्गयति, -यितुम्, to move, agitate, shake; (in<BR>gram.) to divide or separate the members of a com-<BR>pound word, to use a word or bring it into such a<BR>grammatical relation that it is considered इङ्ग्य; see<BR>below; [cf. Hib. ing, ‘a stir, a move.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्ग|इंग|इङ्गं|इङ्गः
इङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, movable, locomotive; surprising,<BR>wonderful; (अस्), m. a hint or sign, an indication of<BR>sentiment by gesture, knowledge; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>counting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गन|इंगन|इंगनं
इङ्गन, अम्, n. shaking; (in gram.) the operation<BR>by which one member of a compound is separated<BR>from another, as by the अव-ग्रह or mark of tmesis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गित|इंगित|इङ्गितं
इङ्गित, अम्, n. palpitation, change of the voice,<BR>internal motion, motion of various parts of the body<BR>as indicating the intentions; hint, sign, gesture;<BR>aim, intention, real but covert purpose.<BR>—इङ्गित-<BR>कोविद or इङ्गित-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, understanding<BR>signs, acquainted with the gesture of another, skilled<BR>in the expression or interpretation of the internal<BR>sentiments by the external gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्ग्य|इंग्य
इङ्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, movable from its place; in the<BR>Prātiśākhyas a term for those words or rather parts<BR>of a compound word which in certain grammatical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">Page0138-b+ 73</a>]<BR>operations may be separated from the preceding parts,<BR>a word which in the Pada-pātḥa is divided by the<BR>अव-ग्रह or mark of tmesis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गिड
इङ्गिड इङ्गिड, N. of a plant, = इङ्गुद (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गुद|इंगुद|इंगुदः|इङ्गुदः
इङ्गुद इङ्गुद, अस्, ई, m. f., N. of a medicinal<BR>tree, Terminalia Catappa; in Bengal confounded with<BR>Putrañjīva Roxburghii Wall.; (अम्), n. the nut of<BR>the tree Terminalia Catappa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गुल|इंगुलः|इङ्गुलः
इङ्गुल, अस्, ई, m. f., N. of the tree Terminalia<BR>Catappa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इचिकिल|इचिकिलः
इचिकिल इचिकिल, अस्, m. a pond, mud, mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक 1. इच्छक, अस्, m. the citron, Citrus<BR>Medica L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक 2. इच्छक, इच्छा इच्छा, &c. See<BR>under 3. इष् at page 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्जल|इज्जलः
इज्जल इज्जल, अस्, m. a small tree growing<BR>in wet and saline soil, or on low grounds near the<BR>sea, Barringtonia Acutangula Gærtn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्य|इज्यः
इज्य इज्य, अस्, m. (fr. rt. यज्), a teacher; an<BR>epithet of Bṛhaspati the teacher or Guru of the gods;<BR>(आ), f. a sacrifice, making offerings to the gods or<BR>manes; a gift, a donation; worship, reverence; meet-<BR>ing, union; a cow; a bawd or procuress.<BR>—इज्या-<BR>शील, अस्, m. a frequent sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इञ्चाक|इंचाकः|इञ्चाकः
इञ्चाक इञ्चाक, अस्, m. a shrimp or prawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्
इट् इट्, cl. 1. P. एटति, एटितुम्, to go, to go<BR>to or towards; Ved. to make haste, to err.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट|इटः
इट इट, अस्, m., Ved. cane or grass; a web<BR>made of it, a mat.<BR>—इट-सून, अम्, n., Ved. a tex-<BR>ture of reed, a mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इटत
इटत इटत, अस्, m., N. of a Bhārgava, author<BR>of a hymn of the Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्चर|इट्चरः
इट्चर इट्-चर, अस्, m. (fr. 4. इष् and चर),<BR>a bull or steer allowed to go at liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इठिमिका
इठिमिका इठिमिका, f. title of a section of<BR>the Kāṭhaka recension of the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्
इड् इड्, Ved. (only in inst., gen., abl. sing.,<BR>and acc. pl. इडा and इडस्; or, according to the spell-<BR>ing of the Ṛg-veda, इऌआ and इऌअस्), a refreshing draught,<BR>refreshment, libation offered to the gods; the flow of<BR>speech, the stream of sacred words and worship,<BR>prayer; (Sāy.) the earth, food; (इडस् or इऌअस्), pl.<BR>the object of devotion, addressed in the third or<BR>fourth verses of the Āprī hymns, (so used only in<BR>Ṛg-veda 3, 4. 3; but also erroneously referred to in<BR>the Brāhmaṇas &c. as if etymologically connected<BR>with the words ईड्य, ईडित, ईऌइत, ‘the praiseworthy,’<BR>‘the praised,’ which are used in the third or fourth<BR>verses of the other Āprīs as the designation of the same<BR>object of worship.)<BR>—इडस्-पति, इस्, m., N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—इड्-देवता, f. deity of the libation.<BR>—इऌअस्-पति, इस्,<BR>m., Ved. a N. of Pūṣan.<BR>—इऌअस्-पदे, in the place of<BR>sacred libation, i. e. at the altar or place of offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड|इडः
इड, अस्, m., Ved. This word occurs only in one<BR>sacred formula as an epithet of Agni, who is to be<BR>addressed with prayers, or invoked with the stream<BR>or flow of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडा
इडा, f. or (in Ṛg-veda) इऌआ, (not to be confounded<BR>with the inst. case of इड् above), refreshing draught,<BR>refreshment, animation, recreation, comfort, vital<BR>spirit; food; offering, libation, especially a holy liba-<BR>tion, coming between the Prayāga and Anuyāga, and<BR>consisting of four preparations of milk, poured into<BR>a vessel containing water, and then partially drank<BR>by the priest and sacrificers; (metaphorically cf. इड्)<BR>stream or flow of praise and worship, personified as<BR>the goddess of sacred speech and action, invoked toge-<BR>ther with Aditi and other deities, but especially in<BR>the Āprī hymns together with Sarasvatī and Mahī or<BR>Bhāratī; (Sāy.) the earth, food; (इडा, as the libation<BR>and offering of milk is personified in the cow, the<BR>symbol of feeding and giving, whence the word इडा<BR>is given as a synonym of ‘cow.’ The goddess इडा or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">Page0138-c+ 76</a>]<BR>इला is the daughter of Manu or of man thinking on<BR>and worshipping the gods; she is the wife of Budha<BR>and mother of Purū-ravas; in another aspect she is<BR>called Maitrāvaruṇi as daughter of Mitra-Varuṇa, two<BR>gods who were objects of the highest and most<BR>spiritual devotion. इला is also a N. of Durgā, of a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa, of a wife of<BR>Vasudeva and of the Rudra, Rita-dhvaja); heaven;<BR>a tubular vessel, one of the principal channels of the<BR>vital spirit, that which is on the right side of the<BR>body. इऌआयास्-पदे, at the place of Iḍā, i. e. of<BR>worship and libation, earth.<BR>—इडा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. refreshing, granting fresh vital spirits; possessed<BR>of refreshment, refreshed; (Sāy.) possessed of sacri-<BR>ficial food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडाचिका
इडाचिका, f. (fr. इडा ?), a wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिका
इडिका, f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिक्क|इडिक्कः
इडिक्क इडिक्क, अस्, m. a wild goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्वर|इड्वरः
इड्वर इड्वर, अस्, m. a bull fit to be set at<BR>liberty. See इट्-चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्डीन्थ
इण्डीन्थ इण्डीन्थ, अस्, m. a knife (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्ड्व|इंड्वं
इण्ड्व इण्ड्व, अम्, n., Ved. (used in du.) two<BR>round small plates made of Muñja reed, used as cover-<BR>ings for the hands in taking the fire-pans from the fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्वीन्दु
इण्वीन्दु इण्वीन्दु, उस्, m. the tree Trochis<BR>Aspera (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्वेरिका
इण्वेरिका इण्वेरिका, f. a kind of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतर|इतरः
इतर इ-तर, अस्, आ, अत्, Ved. अम् (comparative<BR>form of pronom. base 3. इ; cf. Lat. iterum; Hib. iter),<BR>the other (of two), another; (pl.) the rest; (with<BR>abl.) different from; low, vile; expelled, rejected;<BR>इतर इतर, the one — the other, this — that. (इतर<BR>connected antithetically with a preceding word often<BR>signifies the contrary idea, e. g. विजयाय इतराय<BR>वा, to victory or defeat; so in Dvandva compounds,<BR>सुखेतरेषु, in happiness and distress. It some-<BR>times, however, forms a Tat-puruṣa compound with<BR>another word to express the one idea implied in the<BR>contrary of that word, e. g. दक्षिणेतर, the left<BR>hand.)<BR>—इतर-जन, आस्, m. pl. other men; a euphe-<BR>mistic title of certain beings who appear to be consi-<BR>dered as spirits of darkness; Kuvera belongs to them.<BR>—इतर-तस्, ind. otherwise than, different from;<BR>इतश्चेतरतश्च, hither and thither.<BR>—इतर-था,<BR>ind. in another manner, in a contrary manner; per-<BR>versely; on the other hand, else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरा
इतरा, f., N. of the mother of Aitareya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतर|इतरेतरं
इतरेतर, अस्, आ, अम् (occurring chiefly in oblique<BR>cases of sing. and in comp.; fr. इतर-इतर, which<BR>may be for इतरस्-इतर, cf. अन्योऽन्य, परस्-<BR>पर), one another, one with another, mutual, re-<BR>spective, several; (अम्), n. or adv. mutually, &c.<BR>—इतरेतर-काम्या, f. respective or several fancies<BR>or inclinations.<BR>—इतरेतराश्रय (˚र-आश्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, affecting or concerning mutually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेद्युस्
इतरे-द्युस्, ind. at another or different day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतम
इ-तम, अस्, आ, अत् (superlative form of 3. इ), another<BR>(of many ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्
इतस् इ-तस्, ind. (fr. 3. इ with affix तस्, used<BR>like the abl. case of the pronoun इदम्), from hence,<BR>hence, here (opposed to अमु-तस् and अमु-त्र);<BR>from this point; from this world, in this world; इतस्<BR>इतस्, here — there; इतश्चेतश्च, hence and thence,<BR>hither and thither, here and there, to and fro; from<BR>this time, now; therefore.<BR>—इत-ऊति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>extending or reaching from hence; existing or lasting<BR>longer than the present time, future; (Sāy.) one who<BR>has obtained help.<BR>—इतस्-ततस्, ind. here and there,<BR>hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति 2. इति, ind. (fr. pronominal base 3. इ),<BR>in this manner, thus. In its original signification इति<BR>refers to something that has been said or thought, or<BR>lays stress on what precedes. In the Brāhmaṇas it is<BR>often equivalent to ‘as you know,’ reminding the<BR>hearer or reader of certain customs, conditions, &c.,<BR>supposed to be known to him.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">Page0139-a+ 75</a>]<BR>In quotations of every kind इति means that the pre-<BR>ceding words are the very words which some person<BR>has or might have spoken, and placed thus at the end<BR>of a speech it serves the purpose of inverted commas<BR>(e. g. इत्य् उक्त्वा, having so said; इति कृत्वा, having so<BR>considered, having so decided). It may often have<BR>reference merely to what is passing in the mind, e. g.<BR>बालोऽपि नावमन्तव्यो मनुष्य इति भूमिपः,<BR>a king, though a child, is not to be despised, saying<BR>to one's self, ‘he is a mortal,’ (Gram. 928.) In<BR>theatrical language इति तथा करोति = after these<BR>words he acts so.<BR>Sometimes इति is used to include under one head<BR>a number of separate objects aggregated together<BR>(e. g. इज्याध्ययनदानानि तपः सत्यं क्षमा<BR>दमः अलोभ इति मार्गोऽयम्, ‘sacrificing, study-<BR>ing, liberality, penance, truth, patience, self-restraint,<BR>absence of desire,’ this course of conduct, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति is sometimes followed by एवम्, इव, or a<BR>demonstrative pronoun pleonastically (e. g. ताम्<BR>ब्रूयाद् भवतीत्य् एवम्, her he may call ‘lady,’<BR>thus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति may form an adverbial compound with the name<BR>of an author (e. g. इतिपाणिनि, thus according to Pāṇini).<BR>It may also express manifestation (lo! behold!), some-<BR>thing additional (as in इत्य्-आदि, et cetera), order, ar-<BR>rangement specific or distinctive, and identity. It is<BR>used by native commentators after quoting a rule to<BR>express ‘according to such a rule’ (e. g. अनुदात्त-<BR>ङित इत्य् आत्मनेपदम् भवति, according to the<BR>rule of Pāṇini 1. 3, 12, the Ātmane-pada takes place).<BR>किम् इति = किम्, wherefore, why ? (In the Śata-<BR>patha-Brāhmaṇa ति occurs for इति; cf. Prākṛt ति and<BR>त्ति.)<BR>—इति-कथ, अस्, आ, अम्, unworthy of trust, not<BR>fit to be credited; wicked, lost; (आ), f. unmeaning or<BR>nonsensical discourse; (? for अति-कथ, q. v.)<BR>—इति-<BR>करण, अम्, n. or इति-कार, अस्, m. the word इति.<BR>—इति-कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper or necessary to be<BR>done according to certain conditions; (अम्), n. duty,<BR>obligation.<BR>—इतिकर्तव्य-ता, f. or इतिकार्य-ता or इति-<BR>कृत्य-ता, f. any proper or necessary measure, obliga-<BR>tion.<BR>—इतिकर्तव्यता-मूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, embar-<BR>rassed, dumbfounded, wholly at a loss what to do.<BR>—इति-<BR>थ, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. such a one, such, e. g. पुरेति-<BR>थ्यै (? रात्र्यै dat. sing.) मरिष्यसि, before<BR>such and such a day thou wilt die.<BR>—इति-मात्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of such extent or quality.<BR>—इति-वत्, ind. in<BR>the same manner.<BR>—इति-वृत्त, अम्, n. occurrence,<BR>event.<BR>—इत्य्-अर्थम्, ind. for this purpose.<BR>—इत्य्-आदि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, having such (thing or things) at the begin-<BR>ning, thus beginning, and so forth, et cetera.<BR>—इत्य्-<BR>उक्त, अम्, n. information, report, narrative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिह
इति-ह, ind. thus indeed, (according to tradition.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहास|इतिहासः
इति-हास, अस्, m. (इति-ह-आस, ‘so indeed it was’),<BR>talk, legend, tradition, history, traditional accounts of<BR>former events, heroic history, as the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहास|इतिहासः
इतिहास इति-हास. See under 2. इति above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतीक
इतीक इतीक, अस्, m., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्कट|इत्कटः
इत्कट इत्कट, अस्, m. a kind of reed or grass.<BR>See इक्कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्किला
इत्किला इत्किला, f., N. of a perfume. See<BR>रोचना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थ|इत्थं
इत्थ इत्थ, अम्, n. in astronomy = ἰχθύς<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्
इत्थम् इत्थम्, ind. (fr. इद्, q. v.), thus, in<BR>this manner; [cf. Lat. item.]<BR>—इत्थं-विध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of such a kind, endowed with such qualities.<BR>—इत्थङ्-कारम्, ind. in this manner.<BR>—इत्थम्-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the being thus endowed.<BR>—इत्थम्-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become thus, being thus or in<BR>such manner; so circumstanced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थशाल|इत्थशालः
इत्थशाल इत्थशाल, (in astrology) N. of the<BR>third Yoga, = Arabic إِتِّصال<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्था
इत्था इत्था, ind., Ved. thus; (often used<BR>in the Ṛg-veda, and sometimes only to lay stress on<BR>a following word; therefore by native etymologists<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">Page0139-b+ 77</a>]<BR>considered as a particle of affirmation.) इत्था is<BR>often connected with words expressing devotion to<BR>the gods &c. in the sense of thus, truly, really;<BR>especially with धी as an adjective. Hence इत्था-<BR>धी = such, i. e. true (सत्या) or real worship. Simi-<BR>larly, इत्था-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, so devout, so pious, i. e.<BR>very devout; (Sāy.) performing such or true works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थात्
इत्थात् इत्थात्, ind. (= इत्थम्), Ved. thus,<BR>in this way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्
इद् इद्, ind., Ved. (probably the neut. form<BR>of the pronom. base इ, see 3. इ; a particle of affirma-<BR>tion), even, just, only; (especially in strengthening<BR>an antithesis, e. g. यथा वशन्ति देवास् तथा इद्<BR>असत्, as the gods wish it, thus indeed it will be; दिप्-<BR>सन्त इद् रिपवो नाह देभुः, the enemies wishing<BR>indeed to hurt were in nowise able to hurt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्
इद् is often added to words expressing excess or<BR>exclusion (e. g. विश्व इत्, everyone indeed; शश्वद्<BR>इत्, constantly indeed; एक इत्, one only). At the be-<BR>ginning of sentences it often adds emphasis to pro-<BR>nouns, prepositions, particles (e. g. त्वम् इत्, thou<BR>indeed; यदि इत्, if indeed, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्
इद् occurs often in the Ṛg-veda, seldom in the<BR>Brāhmaṇas, and its place is taken in classical Sanskrit<BR>by एव and other particles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम् इदम्, अयम्, इयम्, इदम् (fr. इद्, a kind<BR>of neut. of the pronom. base 3. इ with अम्; cf. Lat. is,<BR>ea, id, and idem; the regular forms are partly de-<BR>rived from the pronom. base अ; see Gram. 224.<BR>The Veda exhibits various irregular formations, e. g.<BR>fr. pronom. base अ, an inst. एना, अया, and gen. loc.<BR>du. अयोस्; fr. the base इम, a gen. sing. इमस्य,<BR>&c.; the forms derived fr. अ are used enclitically if<BR>they take the place of the third personal pronoun, do<BR>not stand at the beginning of a verse or period, and<BR>have no peculiar stress laid upon them), this, this here,<BR>referring to something near the speaker; known, pre-<BR>sent; (opposed to अदस्, e. g. अयं लोकः or इदं<BR>विश्वम् or इदं सर्वम्, this earthly world, this<BR>universe; अयम् अग्निः, this fire which burns on the<BR>earth; but असाव् अग्निः, that fire in the sky, i. e. the<BR>lightning: so also इदम् or इयम् alone signifies ‘this<BR>earth;’ इमे स्मः, here we are.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम् often refers to something immediately fol-<BR>lowing, whereas एतद् points to what precedes (e. g.<BR>श्रुत्वा एतद् इदम् ऊचुः, having heard that they<BR>said this).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम् occurs connected with यद्, तद्, एतद्, किम्,<BR>and a personal pronoun, partly to point out anything<BR>more distinctly and emphatically, partly pleonastically<BR>(e. g. तद् इदम् वाक्यम्, this speech here following;<BR>सोऽयं विदूषकः, this Vidūṣaka here).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम्, ind., Ved. here, to this place; now, even,<BR>just; there; with these words.<BR>—इदं-रूप, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having this shape.<BR>—इदं-विद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>knowing this or conversant with this.<BR>—इदङ्-कार्या,<BR>f. the plant Hedysarum Alhagi.<BR>—इदद्-वसु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. rich in this and that.<BR>—इदन्-ता, f. iden-<BR>tity.<BR>—इदम्-प्रकारम्, ind. in this manner.<BR>—इदम्-प्रथम, अस्, आ, अम्, doing anything for<BR>the first time.<BR>—इदम्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. made<BR>or consisting of this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंयु
इदंयु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदा
इदा इ-दा, ind. (fr. pronom. base 3. इ), Ved.<BR>now, at this moment; (often connected with a gen.<BR>of अहन्, e. g. इदा अह्नः or अह्न इदा, this present<BR>day, ‘now-a-days;’ and with ह्यस्, e. g. इदा ह्यः,<BR>only yesterday.)<BR>—इदा-वत्सर, अस्, m. originally<BR>perhaps ‘the present or current year;’ then one of the<BR>names given to the single years of a period of five<BR>years; one of the five years in which gifts of clothes<BR>and food are productive of great rewards.<BR>—इदा-<BR>वत्सरीय, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to such a year.<BR>—इदु-<BR>वत्सर and इद्-वत्सर = इदा-वत्सर above.<BR>—इद्-<BR>वत्सरीय = इदावत्सरीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीम्
इ-दानीम्, ind. now, at this moment, in this case,<BR>just, even; (with gen. of अहन्, e. g. इदानीम् अह्नः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">Page0139-c+ 74</a>]<BR>this present day, ‘now-a-days;’ इदानीम् एव, just<BR>now; immediately; इदानीम् अपि, in this case too;<BR>तत इदानीम्, thereupon, then.) In rare cases it is<BR>an expletive, affecting but slightly the sense. इदानीम्<BR>as a measure of time is the fifteenth part of an एतर्हि,<BR>and is then declinable (e. g. यावन्त्य् एतर्हीणि ताव-<BR>न्ति पञ्चदशकृत्व इदानीनि, as many Etarhis, so<BR>many Idānīms fifteen times repeated).<BR>—इदानीन्-<BR>तन, अस्, ई, अम्, present, momentary, of the present<BR>moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इद्ध, इध्म, &c. See under इन्ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्
इन् इन्, cl. 8. P., Ved. इनोति, ऐनोत्, 2nd<BR>sing. impv. इनुहि or इनु, cl. 9. P., 1st pl.<BR>इनीमसि, cl. 6. P. (fr. इन्व्) इन्वति, perf. 3rd pl.<BR>इन्विरे, to advance upon, press upon, drive; to infuse<BR>strength, invigorate; to use force, to force; drive away,<BR>keep back, remove; to have in one's power, to take<BR>possession of, pervade; dispose; to be lord or master<BR>of a thing or an art. See इन्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन|इनः
इन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. able, strong, energetic, de-<BR>termined, bold; powerful, mighty, wild; glorious;<BR>(अस्), m. a lord, a master; a king; the sun; the<BR>lunar mansion Hasta.<BR>—इन-सभ, अम्, n. a royal<BR>court or assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनक्ष्
इनक्ष् इनक्ष्, इनक्षति (a Ved. Desid. of<BR>नक्ष्), to endeavour to reach, strive to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनानी
इनानी इनानी, f., N. of a plant (= Vaṭapattrī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनु
इनु इनु, उस्, m., N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्थिहा|इंथिहा
इन्थिहा इन्थिहा, f., an astrological term<BR>taken from the Arabic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्|इंद्
इन्द् इन्द्, cl. 1. P. इन्दति, ऐन्दत्, इन्दाम्-<BR>बभूव, इन्दितुम्, to be powerful; (this<BR>root seems to be formed merely for the etymology of<BR>the word इन्द्र, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दम्बर|इंदंबरं|इन्दम्बरं
इन्दम्बर इन्दम्बर, अम्, n. the blue lotus,<BR>Nymphæa Cærulea. See इन्दी-वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिन्दिर|इंदिंदिरः|इन्दिन्दिरः
इन्दिन्दिर इन्दिन्दिर, अस्, m. a large bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरा|इंदिरा
इन्दिरा इन्दिरा, f. epithet of Lakṣmī, wife<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—इन्दिरा-मन्दिर, अस्, m. epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—इन्दिरालय (˚रा-आल्˚), अम्, n. (lit. ‘the<BR>abode of इन्दिरा or Lakṣmī’), the blue lotus, Nym-<BR>phæa Stellata and Cyanea. (The goddess इन्दिरा<BR>issued at the creation from the petals of the flower.)<BR>—इन्दिरा-वर, अम्, n. = preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवर|इंदीवर|इंदीवरं|इन्दीवरं
इन्दीवर इन्दी-वर or इन्दी-वार or इन्दि-वर,<BR>अम्, m. (contracted fr. इन्दिरा-वर), the blue lotus,<BR>Nymphæa Stellata and Cyanea, see इन्दिरा; (ई), f. the<BR>plant Asparagus Racemosus; (आ), f., N. of another<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवरिणी|इंदीवरिणी
इन्दीवरिणी, f. a group of blue lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दु|इंदुः|इन्दुः
इन्दु इन्दु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. उन्द्; per-<BR>haps connected with विन्दु, which last is unknown in<BR>the Ṛg-veda), Ved. a drop, especially of Soma, Soma;<BR>a bright drop, a spark; the moon; (अवस्), m. pl.<BR>the moons, i. e. the periodic changes of the moon;<BR>time of moonlight, night; (उस्), m. camphor. (In<BR>the Brāhmaṇas इन्दु is used only for the moon; but<BR>the connection between the senses ‘Soma juice’ and<BR>‘moon’ in the word इन्दु has led to the same two<BR>ideas being transferred in classical Sanskrit to the<BR>word सोम, although the latter has properly only<BR>the sense ‘Soma juice.’)<BR>—इन्दु-कमल, अम्, n. the<BR>white lotus.<BR>—इन्दु-कला, f. a digit of the moon;<BR>N. of several plants, Cocculus Cordifolius, Sarcostema<BR>Viminale, Ligusticum Ajowan.<BR>—इन्दु-कलिका, f. the<BR>plant Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR>—इन्दु-कान्त, अस्,<BR>m. the lunar gem, the moon-stone; (आ), f. night.<BR>—इन्दु-ज, अस्, m. epithet of the planet mercury,<BR>‘son of the moon;’ (आ), f., N. of the river Revā or<BR>Narmadā in the Dekhan.<BR>—इन्दु-जनक, अस्, m. the<BR>ocean, lit. ‘father of the moon,’ (the moon being<BR>produced amongst other things at the churning of<BR>the ocean.)<BR>—इन्दु-दल, अस्, m. a portion of the<BR>moon, a digit, crescent.<BR>—इन्दु-पुत्र, अस्, m. epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-a" target="_blank">Page0140-a+ 79</a>]<BR>of the planet Mercury.<BR>—इन्दु-पुष्पिका, f. the plant<BR>Methonica Superba.<BR>—इन्दु-भृत्, त्, m. epithet of<BR>Śiva. ‘bearing the crescent on his forehead.’<BR>—इन्दु-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. the moon-stone.<BR>—इन्दु-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. the orb or disc of the moon.<BR>—इन्दु-मत्,<BR>आन्, m., Ved. (in liturgical language) an epithet of<BR>Agni, because in the verses in which he is addressed<BR>the word इन्दु occurs; (ती), f. day of full moon; N.<BR>of the sister of Bhoja and wife of Aja; N. of a river.<BR>—इन्दु-मौलि, इस्, m. epithet of Śiva; see इन्दु-<BR>भृत्.<BR>—इन्दु-रत्न, अम्, n. a pearl.<BR>—इन्दु-राज्, ट्,<BR>m. the moon, king of the stars.<BR>—इन्दु-रेखा, f. a<BR>digit of the moon.<BR>—इन्दु-लेखा, f. a digit of<BR>the moon; the plant Menispermum Glabrum;<BR>the moon-plant Asclepias Acida; a kind of lovage,<BR>Ligusticum Ajwæn.<BR>—इन्दु-लोहक, अम्, n. silver.<BR>—इन्दु-वदना, f. a metre of four verses of which<BR>each contains fourteen syllables.<BR>—इन्दु-वल्ली, f. the<BR>plant Sarcostemma Viminale.<BR>—इन्दुवार in astrology<BR>= the Arabic إِدْبار<BR>—इन्दु-व्रत, अम्, n. a reli-<BR>gious observance depending on the age of the moon;<BR>diminishing the quantity of food by a certain portion<BR>daily, for a fortnight or a month, &c.<BR>—इन्दु-शेखर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘moon-crested,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुक|इन्दुकः
इन्दुक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = अश्मन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दूर|इंदूरः|इन्दूरः
इन्दूर इन्दूर, अस्, m. a rat, a mouse [cf.<BR>उन्दुर, उन्दुरु].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्र|इंद्रः|इन्द्रः
इन्द्र इन्द्र, अस्, m. (fr. rt. इन् or इन्द् or ob-<BR>solete rt. इद् ?), the god who in Vedic mythology<BR>reigns over the deities of the intermediate region or<BR>atmosphere; he fights against and conquers with his<BR>thunderbolt (वज्र) the demons of darkness, and is<BR>in general a symbol of generous heroism; (इन्द्र was<BR>not originally lord of the gods of the sky, but his<BR>deeds were most useful to mankind, and he was there-<BR>fore addressed in prayers and hymns more than any<BR>other deity, and ultimately superseded the more lofty<BR>and spiritual Varuṇa. In the later mythology इन्द्र is<BR>subordinated to the triad Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and Śiva,<BR>but remained the chief of all other deities in the<BR>popular mind; he is also regent of the east quarter,<BR>and considered one of the twelve Ādityas: in the<BR>Vedānta he is identified with the supreme being);<BR>the first, the chief (of any class of objects); a prince;<BR>the pupil of the right eye (that of the left being called<BR>Indrāṇī or Indra's wife); N. of the plant Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica, &c. (see कुटज); a vegetable poi-<BR>son; N. of the twenty-sixth Yoga or division of a<BR>circle on the plane of the ecliptic; the Yoga star in<BR>the twenty-sixth Nakṣatra, γ Pegasi; the human or<BR>animal soul, the portion of spirit residing in the body;<BR>night; one of the nine divisions of Jambu-dvīpa or<BR>the known continent; best, excellent (in compounds);<BR>(आ), f. the wife of Indra, see इन्द्राणी; N. of a<BR>plant, Marjoram (?), see फणिज्झव.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>ऋषभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having Indra as a bull,<BR>or impregnated by Indra, epithet of the earth.<BR>—इन्द्र-कर्मन्, आ, m. epithet of Viṣṇu, ‘per-<BR>forming Indra's deeds.’<BR>—इन्द्र-कील, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a mountain; a rock.<BR>—इन्द्र-कुञ्जर, अस्, m.<BR>Indra's elephant; see ऐरावत.<BR>—इन्द्र-कूट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—इन्द्र-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ploughed by Indra, growing in a wild state.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>केतु, उस्, m. Indra's banner; N. of a man.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>कोश or इन्द्र-कोष or इन्द्रकोषक, अस्, m. a<BR>platform, a scaffold; a projection of the roof of a<BR>house, forming a kind of balcony or terrace; a pin or<BR>bracket projecting from the wall.<BR>—इन्द्र-गिरि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—इन्द्र-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. guarded or protected by Indra; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a Brāhman.<BR>—इन्द्र-गुरु, उस्, m. teacher of Indra;<BR>an epithet of Kaśyapa.<BR>—इन्द्र-गोप, अस्, or आ, आस्,<BR>m., Ved. having Indra as one's protector; (अस्), m.<BR>the insect cochineal of various kinds; in this sense<BR>also इन्द्रगोपक.<BR>—इन्द्र-घोष, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>noise of Indra personified; having the name Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-चन्दन, अम्, n. = हरि-चन्दन.<BR>—इन्-<BR>द्र-चाप, अस्, m. Indra's bow, a rainbow.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>चिर्भिटी, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—इन्द्र-च्छन्दस्, n. a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-b" target="_blank">Page0140-b+ 81</a>]<BR>necklace consisting of 1008 strings.<BR>—इन्द्र-जनन,<BR>अम्, n. Indra's birth.<BR>—इन्द्रजननीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>treating of Indra's birth.<BR>—इन्द्र-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. originating from Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-जानु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of a monkey.<BR>—इन्द्र-जाल, अम्, n., Ved. the net<BR>of Indra; a weapon employed by Arjuna, stratagem<BR>or trick in war; deception, cheating; conjuring,<BR>juggling.<BR>—इन्द्रजालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, a juggler, a<BR>conjurer; deceptive, unreal.<BR>—इन्द्रजालिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—इन्द्र-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror<BR>of Indra,’ N. of the son of Rāvaṇa; of a Dānava; of<BR>the father of Rāvaṇa and king of Kāśmīra; an author<BR>of the seventeenth century.<BR>—इन्द्रजिद्-विजयिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘conqueror of Indrajit,’ an epithet of Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—इन्द्र-जूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. promoted, excited, or<BR>procured by Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>whose chief is Indra, led by Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most Indra-like, mighty, powerful.<BR>—इन्द्र-ता, f. power and dignity of Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>तापन, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—इन्द्र-तूल or<BR>इन्द्रतूलक, अम्, n. a flock of cotton, a flocculent<BR>seed &c. blown about in the air.<BR>—इन्द्र-तोया, f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—इन्द्र-त्व, अम्, n. Indra's power and<BR>dignity; kingship.<BR>—इन्द्र-त्वोत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>इन्द्र-त्वा-ऊत), Ved. favoured or protected by thee,<BR>O Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—इन्द्र-दारु, उस्, m., the tree Pinus Devadāru.<BR>—इन्द्र-देवी, f., N. of the wife of king Meghavā-<BR>hana, who built a monastery called इन्द्रदेवी-भ-<BR>वन.<BR>—इन्द्र-द्युम्न, अस्, m., N. of a man with<BR>the patronymic Bhāllaveya; (अम्), n., N. of a lake.<BR>—इन्द्र-द्रु, उस्, m. the plants Terminalia Arjuna<BR>and Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR>—इन्द्र-द्रुम, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Terminalia Arjuna.<BR>—इन्द्र-द्वीप, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. one of the nine dvīpas or divisions of the<BR>known continent.<BR>—इन्द्र-धनुस्, उस्, n. Indra's<BR>bow, the rainbow.<BR>—इन्द्र-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Tathāgata or of a Nāga.<BR>—इन्द्र-नक्षत्र, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved., Indra's lunar mansion; an epithet of Phalgunī.<BR>—इन्द्र-नील, अस्, m. a sapphire.<BR>—इन्द्रनीलक,<BR>अस्, m. an emerald.<BR>—इन्द्र-पत्नी, f., Ved. the wife<BR>of Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-पर्णी, f., N. of a plant, perhaps<BR>Methonica Superba.<BR>—इन्द्र-पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a mountain.<BR>—इन्द्र-पातम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>drunk by Indra with more pleasure than by any one<BR>else.<BR>—इन्द्र-पान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. drunk by Indra<BR>(anything which serves as his drink).<BR>—इन्द्र-पालित,<BR>अस्, m. ‘protected by Indra,’ N. of a king; also of a<BR>Vaiśya.<BR>—इन्द्र-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. drunk by<BR>Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-पुत्रा, f., Ved. daughter of Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-पुरोगम, अस्, आ, अम्, preceded or led on<BR>by Indra, having Indra as leader.<BR>—इन्द्र-पुरोहिता,<BR>f. the asterism Puṣya.<BR>—इन्द्र-पुष्पा or इन्द्र-<BR>पुष्पिका or इन्द्र-पुष्पी, f. the medicinal plant<BR>Methonica Superba.<BR>—इन्द्र-प्रमति, इस्, m. a de-<BR>scendant of Vasiṣṭha, author of some verses of the<BR>Ṛg-veda.<BR>—इन्द्र-प्रमद, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—इन्द्र-प्रसूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. caused or im-<BR>pelled by Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-प्रस्थ, अस्, अम्, m. n.,<BR>N. of a city on the Yamunā (now Delhi), the resi-<BR>dence of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—इन्द्र-प्रहरण, अम्,<BR>n. Indra's weapon, the thunderbolt.<BR>—इन्द्र-ब्राह्-<BR>मण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—इन्द्र-भगिनी, f.<BR>‘Indra's sister,’ epithet of the wife of Śiva.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>भूति, इस्, m., N. of one of the eleven Gaṇādhipas<BR>of the Jainas.<BR>—इन्द्र-भेषज, अम्, n. dried ginger.<BR>—इन्द्रमह, अम्, n., N. of a ceremony beginning<BR>with the words इन्द्रम् अहम्.<BR>—इन्द्रमह-का-<BR>मुक, अस्, m. a dog.<BR>—इन्द्र-मादन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. animating or delighting Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-मार्ग,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—इन्द्र-मेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>Ved. whose friend or ally is Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-यव,<BR>अम्, n. Indra-grain; the seed of the Wrightia Anti-<BR>dysenterica.<BR>—इन्द्र-योग, अस्, m., Ved., Indra's union<BR>or uniting power.<BR>—इन्द्र-लुप्त, अस्, अम्, m. n. or<BR>इन्द्र-लुप्तक, अम्, n. morbid baldness of the head;<BR>loss of beard.<BR>—इन्द्र-लोक, अस्, m. Indra's world;<BR>Svarga or paradise.<BR>—इन्द्रलोकागमन (˚क-आग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. (Arjuna's) approach to Indra's world.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>लोकेश (˚क-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord of Indra's world,<BR>i. e. Indra; a guest (as conferring paradise on his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-c" target="_blank">Page0140-c+ 81</a>]<BR>host).<BR>—इन्द्र-वंशा, f. a metre of four lines, each<BR>of which contains twelve syllables.<BR>—इन्द्र-वज्रा, f.<BR>a metre of four lines occurring frequently in epic<BR>poetry; each line contains eleven syllables.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>वत्, or in some cases इन्द्रा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>associated with or accompanied by Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a warrior.<BR>—इन्द्र-वल्लरी or<BR>इन्द्र-वल्ली, f. the plant Cucumis Colocynthis (?).<BR>—इन्द्र-वस्ति, इस्, m. f. (?) the calf (of the leg).<BR>—इन्द्र-वाततम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. much desired<BR>by Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-वायु, ऊ, m. du. Indra and Vāyu.<BR>—इन्द्र-वारुणिका or इन्द्र-वारुणी, f. Colocynth,<BR>a wild bitter gourd, Cucumis Colocynthis; the favourite<BR>plant of Indra and Varuṇa.<BR>—इन्द्र-वाह्, ट्, m., Ved.<BR>carrying Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-वीज, अम्, n. the seed of the<BR>Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR>—इन्द्र-वृक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>= इन्द्र-दारु.<BR>—इन्द्र-वृद्धा, f. a kind of ab-<BR>scess.<BR>—इन्द्र-वृद्धिक, अस्, m. a kind of horse.<BR>—इन्द्र-वैदूर्य, अम्, n. a kind of precious stone.<BR>—इन्द्र-व्रत, अम्, n. ‘Indra's rule of conduct,’<BR>one of the duties of a king, viz. to distribute benefits,<BR>as Indra pours down rain.<BR>—इन्द्र-शक्ति, इस्, f. In-<BR>drāṇī the wife or personified energy of Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>शत्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. whose enemy or conquerer is<BR>Indra, conquered by Indra (with the Udātta on the first<BR>syllable; differently accented the word might mean<BR>‘an enemy of Indra’); (उस्), m. ‘Indra's enemy,’<BR>epithet of Prahlāda.<BR>—इन्द्र-शलभ, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—इन्द्र-शैल, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—इन्द्र-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having Indra<BR>as chief, led by Indra; see इन्द्र-ज्येष्ठ.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>सखि, आ, m., Ved. one whose ally or companion is<BR>Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-सन्धा, f. connection or alliance with<BR>Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-सारथि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. driving in<BR>the same carriage with Indra, an epithet of Vāyu.<BR>—इन्द्र-सावर्णि, इस्, m., N. of the fourteenth<BR>Manu.<BR>—इन्द्र-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Indra,’ N. of<BR>the monkey-king Bali; also an epithet of Arjuna and<BR>Jayanta.<BR>—इन्द्र-सुरस, अस्, m. a shrub, the leaves<BR>of which are used in discutient applications, Vitex<BR>Negundo.<BR>—इन्द्र-सुरा, f. or इन्द्र-सुरिस, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the same plant (?).<BR>—इन्द्र-सूनु, उस्, m. ‘the<BR>son of Indra,’ epithet of the monkey-king Bali.<BR>—इन्द्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of several men; N. of a<BR>Nāga; (आ), f., N. of several women.<BR>—इन्द्रसेन-<BR>द्वितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, attended by Indrasena.<BR>—इन्द्र-<BR>सेना, f., Ved., Indra's missile.<BR>—इन्द्र-स्तुत्, त्, m. or<BR>इन्द्र-स्तोम, अस्, m. ‘praise of Indra;’ N. of particular<BR>hymns to Indra in certain ceremonies.<BR>—इन्द्रस्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. similar to Indra; (Sāy.) accompanied<BR>by Indra, possessed of power (?).<BR>—इन्द्र-हव, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. invocation of Indra.<BR>—इन्द्र-हस्त, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of medicament.<BR>—इन्द्राग्नि-देवता (˚र-अग्˚),<BR>f. the sixteenth lunar mansion.<BR>—इन्द्राग्नि-धूम,<BR>अस्, m. frost, snow.<BR>—इन्द्रानुज (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘the younger brother of Indra,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—इन्द्राभ (˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>grandson (?) of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—इन्द्रायुध (˚र-<BR>आय्˚), अम्, n. Indra's weapon, the rainbow; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a horse; a horse marked with black about the<BR>eyes; (आ), f. a kind of leech having rainbow tints on<BR>the back.<BR>—इन्द्रायुध-शिखिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>Nāga.<BR>—इन्द्रारि (˚र-अर्˚), इस्, m. Indra's enemy,<BR>an Asura or demon.<BR>—इन्द्रावरज (˚र-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘the younger brother of Indra,’ an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—इन्द्राशन (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>hemp, dried and chewed; the shrub which bears the<BR>seed used as a jeweller's weight, Albus Precatorius.<BR>—इन्द्रासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. the throne of Indra,<BR>any throne; a foot of five short syllables.<BR>—इन्द्रेज्य<BR>(˚र-इज्˚), अस्, m., N. of Vṛhaspati, the preceptor of the<BR>gods.<BR>—इन्द्रेषित (˚र-इष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sent or<BR>driven or instigated by Indra.<BR>—इन्द्रोत (˚र-ऊत), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Ṛkṣa and of Devāpi.<BR>—इन्द्रो-<BR>त्सव (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m. a festival honouring Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रक|इंद्रकं|इन्द्रकं
इन्द्रक, अम्, n. an assembly-room, a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रय
इन्द्रय, nom. A., Ved. इन्द्रयते, -यितुम्, to<BR>behave like Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयु|इंद्रयु
इन्द्रयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. longing for or wishing<BR>to approach Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणिका|इंद्राणिका
इन्द्राणिका, f. the plant Vitex Negundo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणी|इंद्राणी
इन्द्राणी, f. the wife of Indra; N. of Durgā,<BR>reckoned as one of the eight mothers (मातृका) or<BR>divine energies; a kind of coitus; the plant Vitex<BR>Negundo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for or belonging to or<BR>agreeable to Indra; (अस्), m. a companion of Indra;<BR>(अम्), n. power, force, the quality which belongs<BR>especially to the mighty Indra; exhibition of power,<BR>powerful act; bodily power, power of the senses;<BR>virile power; semen virile; faculty of sense, sense,<BR>organ of sense; the number five as symbolical of the<BR>five senses. (In addition to the five organs of per-<BR>ception, बुद्धीन्द्रियाणि or ज्ञानेन्द्रियाणि, i. e.<BR>eye, ear, nose, tongue, and skin, the Hindūs enu-<BR>merate five organs of action, कर्मेन्द्रियाणि, i. e.<BR>larynx, hand, foot, anus, and parts of generation; be-<BR>tween these ten organs and the soul or आत्मन् stands<BR>मनस् or mind, considered as an eleventh organ.<BR>In the Vedānta, मनस्, बुद्धि, अहङ्कार, and<BR>चित्त form the four inner or internal organs, अन्तर्-<BR>इन्द्रियाणि, so that according to this reckoning the<BR>organs are fourteen in number, each being presided<BR>over by its own ruler or नियन्तृ; thus, the eye by<BR>the Sun, the ear by the Quarters of the world, the<BR>nose by the two Aśvins, the tongue by Pracetas, the<BR>skin by the Wind, the voice by Fire, the hand by<BR>Indra, the foot by Viṣṇu, the anus by Mitra, the<BR>parts of generation by Prajāpati, manas by the Moon,<BR>buddhi by Brahman, ahaṅkāra by Śiva, citta by<BR>Viṣṇu as Acyuta. In the Nyāya philosophy each<BR>organ is connected with its own peculiar element,<BR>the nose with the Earth, the tongue with Water, the<BR>eye with Light or Fire, the skin with Air, the ear with<BR>Ether. The Jainas divide the whole creation into<BR>five sections, according to the number of organs<BR>attributed to each being.)<BR>—इन्द्रिय-काम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. desiring or endeavouring to obtain power.<BR>—इन्द्रि-यगोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, perceptible, capable<BR>of being ascertained by the senses.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-ग्राम,<BR>अस्, m. the assemblage of the organs, the senses or<BR>organs of sense collectively.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-ज्ञान, अम्,<BR>n. the faculty of perception, sense, consciousness.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-निग्रह, अस्, m. restraint of the organs<BR>of sense.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-बुद्धि, इस्, f. perception by the<BR>senses, the exercise of any sense, the faculty of any<BR>organ.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-बोधन, अस्, आ, अम्, exciting<BR>power, arousing or sharpening the senses; (अम्), n.<BR>any excitement of sense, an object of perception, a<BR>stimulus, &c.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-वर्ग, अस्, m. the assem-<BR>blage of organs, the organs of sense collectively.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-विप्रतिपत्ति, इस्, f. perversion of the<BR>organs, erroneous or perverted perception.<BR>—इन्द्रिय-<BR>स्वाप, अस्, m. sleep of the senses, unconsciousness,<BR>insensibility; the end of the world.<BR>—इन्द्रियागोचर<BR>(˚य-अ-गोच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, imperceptible.<BR>—इन्द्रि-<BR>यात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—इन्द्रियायतन (˚य-आय्˚), अम्, n. the residence<BR>of the senses; the body.<BR>—इन्द्रियार्थ (˚य-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an object of sense (as sound, smell, &c.),<BR>anything exciting the senses.<BR>—इन्द्रिया-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, or इन्द्रिया-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. powerful,<BR>mighty; sometimes also इन्द्रिय-वत्.<BR>—इन्द्रिया-<BR>सङ्ग (˚य-अ-स्˚), अस्, m. non-attachment to sensual<BR>objects, stoicism, philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय इन्द्रिय. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध्|इंध्
इन्ध् इन्ध्, cl. 7. A. इन्द्धे, इन्धाञ्-चक्रे<BR>or ईधे, इन्धिष्यते, ऐन्धिष्ट, इन्धि-<BR>तुम्, to kindle, light, set on fire: Pass. इन्ध्यते,<BR>to be lighted; to blaze, flame; [with इन्ध् cf. Gr.<BR>αἴθω, ἰθαρός; αἰθήρ, Αἴτνη; Ἥφ-αισ-τας Lat.<BR>œs-tus, œs-tas: Old Germ. eit, ‘fire.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, kindled, lighted, alight; shin-<BR>ing, glowing, blazing; clean, clear, bright; wonder-<BR>ful; obeyed, unresisted ?; (अम्), n. sunshine, light,<BR>heat; a wonder.<BR>—इद्ध-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>the anger excited or kindled.<BR>—इद्धाग्नि (˚ध-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. one whose fire burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्
इध्, (at the end of compounds) lighting; [cf.<BR>अग्नीध्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्म|इध्मं|इध्मः
इध्म, अस्, अम्, m. n. fuel, especially that which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">Page0141-b+ 74</a>]<BR>is used for the sacred fire; [cf. Hib. adhmad;<BR>Zend aiśma.]<BR>—इध्म-जिह्व, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Priya-vrata.<BR>—इध्म-प्रव्रश्चन, अस्, m. a<BR>hatchet, an axe.<BR>—इध्म-भृति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>bringing fuel.<BR>—इध्म-वाह, अस्, m. epithet of<BR>Dṛḍhasyu or Dṛḍhadasyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्या
इध्या, f. kindling, lighting. See वाजेध्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध|इंध|इन्धः
इन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, lighting, kindling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धन|इंधन|इन्धनं
इन्धन, अम्, n. kindling, lighting; [cf. अग्नीन्-<BR>धन]; fuel; wood, grass &c. used for this purpose.<BR>—इन्धन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of fuel.<BR>—इन्धन्-वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. possessed of fuel;<BR>flaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्व्
इन्व् इन्व्, cl. 6. P. इन्वति, इन्वाञ्-चकार,<BR>इन्विष्यति, ऐन्वीत्, इन्वितुम्, to pervade,<BR>surround, embrace, seize, take possession of; to invi-<BR>gorate, gladden. See इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्व
इन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, pervading (in विश्वम्-इन्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्वका
इन्वका इन्वका, आस्, f. pl. stars in the head<BR>of Orion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ|इभः
इभ इभ, अस् or अम्?, m. or n. ? (said to be<BR>fr. rt. इ, to go), Ved. servants, dependants, domestics,<BR>household, family; (Sāy.) fearless power; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>followed by attendants; (अस्), m. an elephant; (ई),<BR>f. a female elephant; [with this word cf. the Gr.<BR>ἐλ-έφας and the Lat. ebur.]<BR>—इभ-कणा, f. a plant<BR>with an aromatic seed, Scindapsus Officinalis.<BR>—इभ-<BR>केशर, अस्, m. the tree Mesua Roxburghii.<BR>—इभ-<BR>गन्धा, f., N. of a poisonous fruit.<BR>—इभ-दन्ता,<BR>f. the plant Tiaridium Indicum.<BR>—इभ-निमीलिका, f.<BR>smartness, shrewdness, sagacity (like that of an ele-<BR>phant).<BR>—इभ-पालक, अस्, m. the driver or keeper<BR>of an elephant.<BR>—इभ-पोटा, f. a young elephant, a<BR>cub.<BR>—इभम्-आचल, अस्, m. a lion.<BR>—इभ-युवति,<BR>इस्, f. an elephant's cub.<BR>—इभाख्य (˚भ-आख्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the plant Mesua Roxburghii.<BR>—इभारि (˚भ-<BR>अर्˚), इस्, m. a lion (‘enemy of the elephant’).<BR>—इभो-<BR>षणा (˚भ-उष्˚), f. a kind of aromatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्य|इभ्यः
इभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to one's servants<BR>or attendants; wealthy, opulent, having many attend-<BR>ants; (Sāy.) (अस्), m. an enemy; (आ), f. a female<BR>elephant; N. of the Olibanum tree, Boswellia Serrata.<BR>—इभ्य-तिल्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abundantly pos-<BR>sessed of household requisites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इम
इम इम, a pronominal base. See इदम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इमक
इमक, अस्, आ, अम्, diminutive of इम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इमथा
इमथा, ind., Ved. as in this place, as here, as now.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयक्ष्
इयक्ष् इयक्ष् (Anomalous Desid. of rt. यज्),<BR>Ved. occurring only in the part. pres. इयक्षत् and<BR>इयक्षमाण, and in impf. subj. इयक्षान्, to go<BR>towards, approach; to request, endeavour to gain; to<BR>long for, seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयक्षु
इयक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. longing for, seeking to gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्|इयन्त्
इयत् इयत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. pronominal base<BR>3. इ), so large, only so large; so much, only so<BR>much; [with इयत् cf. the syllable iens or ies in such<BR>Lat. words as totiens, toties, quotiens, quoties, and<BR>in numeral adverbs as quinquies.]<BR>—इयत्-ता, f. or<BR>इयत्-त्व, अम्, n. quantity, fixed measure or quantity,<BR>so much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्तक
इयत्तक, अस्, इका, अम्, Ved. so small, very small,<BR>wee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयस्य
इयस्य इयस्य (Anomalous Intens. of rt.<BR>यस्), A., Ved. इयस्यते, to relax, weaken; to vanish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयसा
इयसा, f., Ved. lassitude, dejection, low spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्
इर् इर्, cl. 6. P. इरति, to go; [cf. इल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरज्य
इरज्य इरज्य (Anomalous Intens. of रज्,<BR>राज्), P. rarely A., Ved. इरज्यति, -ते, to order, pre-<BR>pare, arrange; to lead; to dispose, be master of;<BR>(Sāy.) to grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरज्यु
इरज्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. busy with preparations for<BR>the sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरण|इरणं
इरण इरण, desert; salt or barren (soil);<BR>= इरिण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरध्
इरध् इरध् (Anomalous Intens. of राध्),<BR>इरधते and इरध्यति, Ved. to endeavour to gain;<BR>(Sāy.) to worship. The inf. इरध्यै is by some<BR>referred to this form, and regarded as a shortened<BR>form of इरधध्यै; but Sāy. refers it to rt. ईर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरंमद|इरम्मद|इरम्मदः
इरंमद इरं-मद, अस्, m., Ved. delighting<BR>in drink; an epithet of Agni, in the form of light-<BR>ning and Apāṃ-napāt; a flash of lightning or the<BR>fire attending the fall of a thunderbolt; submarine<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरस्य
इरस्य इरस्य, P., Ved. इरस्यति, to behave<BR>insolently, be angry; (with dat.) to be ill-affected<BR>towards; [cf. Lat. ira, irasci.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरस्या
इरस्या, f., Ved. ill-will, malevolence; (Sāy.) wish<BR>for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरा
इरा इरा, f. (closely allied to इडा and इऌआ),<BR>Ved. any drinkable fluid; a draught (especially of<BR>milk); refreshment, comfort, enjoyment; N. of an<BR>Apsaras, a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa;<BR>water; ardent spirits; the earth; speech; the god-<BR>dess of speech, Sarasvatī; [cf. इडा.]<BR>—इरा-क्षीर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. whose milk is a refreshment or enjoy-<BR>ment.<BR>—इरा-चर, अम्, n. hail; (अस्, आ or ई, अम्),<BR>earth-born, terrestrial, aquatic.<BR>—इरा-ज, अस्, m. a<BR>N. of Kāma, god of love, ‘born from water.’<BR>—इरा-<BR>मुख, अम्, n., N. of an Asura-town near Meru.<BR>—इरा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. granting drink or re-<BR>freshment, satiating, giving enjoyment; endowed with<BR>provisions; comfortable; (आन्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Arjuna; the ocean, a cloud; a king; (ई), f., N. of<BR>a plant; N. of Durgā, the wife of Rudra, daughter of<BR>the Nāga Suśravas; N. of a river in the Pañjāb, now<BR>called Rāvī.<BR>—इरा-वेल्लिका, f. pimples or pustules on<BR>the head.<BR>—इरेश (˚रा-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>a king, a sovereign; Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिका
इरिका इरिका, f., N. of a plant or tree.<BR>—इरिका-वन, अम्, n. a grove of such trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण|इरिणं|इरिणः
इरिण इरिण, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. ऋ,<BR>to go; connected with इरा), Ved. a water-course, a<BR>rivulet, a well; any incision in the ground, a hollow,<BR>hole; a desert, an inhospitable region; a bare plain,<BR>barren soil; salt soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण्य
इरिण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging or relating to<BR>a desert &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिन्
इरिन् इरिन्, ई, इणी, इ (connected with इन ?),<BR>Ved. powerful, violent; an overbearing fellow; (Sāy.)<BR>an instigator; [cf. इरस्य &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिमेद|इरिमेदः
इरिमेद इरिमेद, अस्, m., N. of a plant, =<BR>अरि-मेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिम्बिठि|इरिम्बिठिः
इरिम्बिठि इरिम्बिठि, इस्, m., N. of a man of<BR>the family of Kāṇva, author of several hymns of the<BR>Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिविल्ला
इरिविल्ला इरिविल्ला or इरिवेल्लिका, f. pimples<BR>or pustules on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्य|इर्य्य
इर्य इर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. active, powerful,<BR>energetical; epithet of Pūṣan and of the Aśvins;<BR>(Sāy.) instigating; destroying enemies; a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारु|इर्वारुः|इर्व्वारु|इर्व्वारुः
इर्वारु इर्वारु, उस्, m. f., N. of an eatable<BR>cucumber, Cucumis Utilissimus; of another kind,<BR>Cucumis Colocynthis; see इर्वालु, ईर्वारु, उर्वारु,<BR>एर्वारु.<BR>—इर्वारु-शुक्तिका, f. a kind of melon, com-<BR>monly Sphuti or Sphut, Cucumis Momordica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारुक|इर्वारुकः
इर्वारुक, अस्, m. an animal living in caves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वालु|इर्व्वालु|इर्व्वालुः
इर्वालु, उस्, m. f. Cucumis Utilissimus Roxb. or<BR>Cucumis Colocynthis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्
इल् इल्, cl. 6. P. इलति, इयेल, एलिष्यति,<BR>ऐलीत्, एलितुम्, or cl. 10. P. इलयति or<BR>एलयति, -यितुम्, aor. ऐलिलत् or ऐलयीत्, to keep<BR>still, not to move; to become quiet; to send, to<BR>cast; to sleep; to move, to go; [a various reading<BR>has the form इऌ: cf. Old Germ. îllu, îllo, for îlju;<BR>Mod. Germ. Eile; Cambro-Brit. il, ‘progress, mo-<BR>tion;’ Gr. ἐλάω]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलय
इलय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. resting, motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलव|इलवः
इलव इलव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sounding, noisy,<BR>loud; [cf. ऐलब.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलविल
इलविल इलविल, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Daśaratha; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of Tṛṇavindu,<BR>wife of Viśravas and mother of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इला
इला इला, f. flow, speech, the earth, &c.; see<BR>इडा.<BR>—इला-गोल, अम्, n. the earth, the globe.<BR>—इला-<BR>तल, अम्, n. the fourth place in the circle of the<BR>zodiac; the surface of the earth.<BR>—इला-दध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a certain sacrifice.<BR>—इलान्-द, अम्, n.<BR>‘granting refreshment or food,’ N. of a ceremony or<BR>of a verse; N. of a Sāman.<BR>—इला-वृत, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a son of Agnīdhra, who received the Varṣa इला-वृत<BR>as his kingdom; (अम्), n. one of the nine Varṣas or<BR>divisions of the known world, comprehending the<BR>highest and most central part of the old continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिका
इलिका, f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिनी
इलिनी इलिनी, f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Medhātithi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इली
इली इली, f. a cudgel, a stick shaped like a<BR>sword or a short sword. See ईली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीबिश|इलीबिशः
इलीबिश इलीबिश, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>demon conquered by Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीश|इलीशः
इलीश इलीश, अस्, m. (said to be fr. इल्, to<BR>go), a fish, commonly the hilsa or sable, Clupea Alosa;<BR>the fish being one of high flavour, and very abundant<BR>at certain seasons, is generally eaten both by the<BR>natives of Bengal and by Europeans residing there;<BR>[cf. इल्लिश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलूष
इलूष इलूष, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Kavasha. See ऐलूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्प
इल्प इल्प, अस्, m., N. of a wonderful tree<BR>in the other world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लक
इल्लक इल्लक, अस्, m., N. of a merchant's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लल|इल्ललः
इल्लल इल्लल, अस्, m., N. of a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लिश|इल्लिशः
इल्लिश इल्लिश, अस्, m. the fish Clupea Alosa;<BR>[cf. इलीश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वका
इल्वका इल्वका, आस्, f. pl. the five stars in<BR>Orion's head. See इल्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वल|इल्वलः
इल्वल इल्वल, अस्, m. a kind of fish; N. of<BR>a Daitya, the brother of Vātāpi; (आस्), f. pl., N. of<BR>the five stars in Orion's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव इव, ind. (fr. pronominal base 3. इ),<BR>like, in the same manner as (in this sense = यथा,<BR>and used correlatively to तथा); as it were (after a<BR>metaphorical expression, e. g. पथा इव यन्तौ,<BR>on a path going as it were); in a certain manner, in<BR>some measure, a little, perhaps (in qualification or<BR>mitigation of a strong assertion); nearly, almost, about<BR>(e. g. मुहूर्तम् इव, almost an hour); so, just so,<BR>just, exactly, indeed, very (especially after words<BR>which involve some restriction, e. g. ईषद् इव, just<BR>a little; किञ्चिद् इव, just a little bit: and after a nega-<BR>tion, e. g. नचिराद् इव, very soon). इव is connected<BR>vaguely, and somewhat pleonastically, with an inter-<BR>rogative pronoun or adverb (e. g. किम् इव, what ?<BR>कथम् इव, how could that possibly be ? क्वेव,<BR>where, I should like to know ?). In the Pada texts<BR>of the Ṛg, Yajur, and Atharva-veda, and by native<BR>grammarians, इव is considered to be compounded<BR>with the word after which it stands, and is therefore<BR>enclitic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इवीलक
इवीलक इवीलक, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Lambodara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इशीका
इशीका इशीका, f. an elephant's eyeball.<BR>See इषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् 1. इष्, cl. 4. P. इष्यति, इयेष, एषिष्-<BR>यति, ऐषीत्, एषितुम्, to move, to cause to<BR>move; to let fly, to throw, cast; to raise (as one's<BR>voice); to sprinkle; cl. 9. P. इष्णाति, to cause to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">Page0142-b+ 80</a>]<BR>move quickly, to cast, let fly, swing; to strike; to<BR>fly off, escape; to impel, incite, animate, promote:<BR>Caus. P. एषयति, -यितुम्, to bring, offer: Desid.<BR>एषिषिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
2. इष्, (at the end of some compounds) moving<BR>quickly, speedy. See अरम्-इष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणय
इषणय, nom. (from the next) A., Ved. इष-<BR>णयते, -यितुम्, to move, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणि|इषणिः
1. इषणि, इस्, f., Ved. impulse, desire. (For 2. see<BR>under 3. इष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषण्य
इषण्य, nom. P., Ved. इषण्यति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to make haste, to excite, drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषण्या
इषण्या, f., Ved. impulse, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषव्य
इषव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. इषु below), Ved. skilled<BR>in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिका
इषिका = इषीका and ईषिका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषित
इषित, अस्, आ, अम्, moved, driven, tossed, sent;<BR>caused, excited, animated; quick.<BR>—इषित-त्वता, ind.,<BR>Ved. by impulse or excitement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषीक
इषीक, अस्, m., N. of a people, = ऐषीक; (आ),<BR>f. reed, rush, stem or stalk of grasses; an arrow; a<BR>sort of sugar-cane, Saccharum Spontaneum; a brush;<BR>a small stick of wood or iron used for trying whether<BR>or not the gold in a crucible is melted; the eyeball<BR>of an elephant; see इषिका, ईषिका, ईषीका, इशीका.<BR>—इषीक-तूल, अम्, n. the point or upper part of<BR>a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषु|इषुः
इषु, उस्, m. f. an arrow; (in mathematics) a<BR>versed sine; N. of a Soma ceremony.<BR>—इषु-कार,<BR>अस्, or इषु-कृत्, त्, m., Ved. an arrow-maker.<BR>—इषु-<BR>धर, अस्, m. an archer.<BR>—इषु-धि, see s. v. below.<BR>—इषु-प, अस्, m., N. of an Asura, who appeared<BR>on earth as king Magna-jit.<BR>—इषु-पथ, अस्, m.<BR>the range of an arrow.<BR>—इषु-पुष्पा, f., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—इषु-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. powerful by<BR>arrows.<BR>—इषु-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, carrying arrows, an<BR>archer.<BR>—इषु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of<BR>arrows.<BR>—इषु-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, having the length<BR>of an arrow, i. e. about five short spans or three<BR>feet; (अम्), ind. as far as the range of an arrow.<BR>—इषुस्-त्रिकाण्डा, f. the threefold arrow, N. of a<BR>constellation, perhaps the girdle of Orion.<BR>—इषु-<BR>हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘arrow-handed,’ carrying arrows<BR>in the hand.<BR>—इष्व्-अग्र, अम्, n. the point of an<BR>arrow.<BR>—इष्व्-अनीक, अम्, n. the point of an arrow.<BR>—इष्वर्ग, अस्, m. (for इषु-वर्ग), Ved. one who<BR>averts arrows, a shield-bearer.<BR>—इष्व्-असन or<BR>इष्व्-अस्त्र, अम्, n. a bow (‘arrow-thrower’).<BR>—इष्व्-<BR>आयुध, अम्, n., Ved. arrow and weapons.<BR>—इष्व्-<BR>आस, अस्, आ, अम्, throwing arrows; (अस्), m. a bow;<BR>an archer, a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुक
इषुक, अस्, ई, अम्, arrow-like; (आ), f., Ved. an<BR>arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधि|इषुधिः
इषु-धि, इस्, m. f. (rt. धा), a quiver.<BR>—इषुधि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्य
इषुध्य, nom. P., Ved. -ध्यति, -यितुम्, to be<BR>a quiver, to contain arrows; to implore, request;<BR>(Sāy.) to desire oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्या
इषुध्या, f., Ved. imploring, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्यु
इषुध्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. imploring, requesting;<BR>(Sāy.) going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
1. इष्टि, इस्, f. impulse, acceleration, hurry; invita-<BR>tion, order, despatch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्मिन्
इष्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. going quickly, speedy, im-<BR>petuous; an epithet of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् 3. इष्, cl. 6. P., ep. also A. इच्छति,<BR>-ते, इयेष, एषिष्यति, ऐषीत्, एषितुम् or<BR>एष्टुम्, to endeavour to obtain, strive, seek for; to<BR>endeavour to make favourable; desire, wish, long for;<BR>to request; to be willing, to be about to do anything,<BR>to intend; to strive to obtain anything (acc.) from<BR>any one (abl. or loc.); to expect anything from any<BR>one; to assent; to be favourable; to ask anything<BR>(acc.) from any one (loc.); to acknowledge, to regard:<BR>Pass. इष्यते, to be wished or liked; to be asked,<BR>requested, prescribed; to be approved, acknowledged,<BR>accepted, regarded as; to be worth; to be wanted as a<BR>desideratum, see 2. इष्टि: Caus. P. एषयति, -यितुम्,<BR>ऐषिषत्: Desid. एषिषिषति; [with इष् cf. Old<BR>Germ. eiscôm, ‘I ask;’ Mod. Germ. heische: cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">Page0142-c+ 80</a>]<BR>also Gr. προΐσσομαι, πρα-ΐκτης, προ-ΐξ; and per-<BR>haps Gr. ἰό-της and ἵ-μερος]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक, अस्, इका, अम्, wishing, desirous of; (अस्),<BR>m. demand, the sum sought (in arithmetic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छत्
इच्छत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, wishing, wishful, de-<BR>sirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छता
इच्छ-ता, f. or इच्छ-त्व, अम्, n. desire, wishfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छा
इच्छा, f. wish, desire, inclination; (in mathematics)<BR>a question or problem; (in gram.) the desiderative<BR>form; इच्छया, according to one's wish or desire;<BR>इच्छां नि-ग्रह्, to suppress one's desire.<BR>—इच्छा-<BR>दान, अम्, n. the granting or gratification of a wish.<BR>—इच्छा-निवृत्ति, इस्, f. suppression of desire.<BR>—इच्-<BR>छान्वित (˚छा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a desire,<BR>wishing, wishful.<BR>—इच्छा-फल, अस्, m. (in mathe-<BR>matics) the solution of a question or problem.<BR>—इच्छा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, wishing, wishful, desirous; (ती), f. a<BR>woman desirous of anything.<BR>—इच्छा-वसु, उस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Kuvera (‘possessing wealth according to<BR>wish’).<BR>—इच्छा-सम्पद्, त्, f. fulfilment or attain-<BR>ment of wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छु|इच्छुः
इच्छु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing, desiring (with acc. or<BR>inf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छुक|इच्छुकः
इच्छुक, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, wishing, desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
4. इष्, ट्, f. wish; [cf. इट्-चर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणि|इषणिः
2. इषणि, इस्, f., Ved. wish, desire. (For 1. see<BR>under 1. इष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषूय
इषूय, P., Ved. इषूयति, -यितुम्, to request,<BR>ask; (Sāy.) to wish for food, wish to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट|इष्टं|इष्टः
1. इष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see next page), sought;<BR>wished, desired; liked, beloved; agreeable; cherished;<BR>worshipped, reverenced, respected; regarded as good,<BR>approved; valid; (अस्), m. a lover, a husband; the<BR>plant Ricinus Communis; (आ), f., N. of a plant;<BR>(अम्), n. wish, desire; (अम्), ind. voluntarily.<BR>—इष्-<BR>ट-कर्मन्, अ, n. (in arithmetic) rule of supposition,<BR>operation with an assumed number.<BR>—इष्ट-काप-<BR>थ, अस्, m. the root of the fragrant grass Andropo-<BR>gon Muricatus.<BR>—इष्ट-काम-दुह्, धुक्, f. ‘grant-<BR>ing the wished-for desires,’ epithet of the cow of<BR>plenty.<BR>—इष्ट-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fragrant; (अस्),<BR>m. any fragrant substance; (अम्), n. sand.<BR>—इष्ट-<BR>जन, अस्, m. a beloved person, man or woman; a<BR>loved one.<BR>—इष्ट-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most desired,<BR>best beloved, beloved, dearest.<BR>—इष्ट-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, more desired, more dear, dearer.<BR>—इष्ट-तस्,<BR>ind. according to one's wish or desire.<BR>—इष्ट-ता, f.<BR>or इष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. desirableness, the state of being<BR>beloved or reverenced.<BR>—इष्ट-देव, अस्, m. or<BR>इष्ट-देवता, f. a chosen or tutelary deity, a<BR>favourite god, one particularly worshipped.<BR>—इष्ट-<BR>यामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. going according to one's de-<BR>sire.<BR>—इष्ट-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having desired<BR>or best reins or bridles.<BR>—इष्ट-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. obeying one's wish; (Say.) that by which good<BR>works succeed.<BR>—इष्टा-कृत, अम्, n., Ved. wish and<BR>deed, i. e. accomplishment of a wish (?); N. of a<BR>certain sacrificial ceremony.<BR>—इष्टा-पूर्त, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. wish and fulfilment, i. e. fulfilment of one's<BR>wishes; any religious duty or pious act, as oblation,<BR>sacrifice, penance, holy study, digging a well, plant-<BR>ing a tree, &c.<BR>—इष्टार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, m. any-<BR>thing desired or agreeable.<BR>—इष्टार्थोद्युक्त (˚थ-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, zealously active, diligent for a<BR>desired object.<BR>—इष्टाश्व (˚ट-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having desired or best horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
2. इष्टि, इस्, f. seeking, endeavouring to obtain;<BR>wish, request, desire; any desired object, a desired<BR>rule, a desideratum (a term applied to Patañjali's ad-<BR>ditions to Pāṇini's rules); (इस्), m., Ved. seeking,<BR>going after, guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टु|इष्टुः
इष्टु, उस्, f. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्म|इष्मः
इष्म, अस्, m. the spring; love or the deity Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्य|इष्यं|इष्यः
इष्य, अस्, अम्, m. n. the spring season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्व|इष्वः
इष्व, अस्, m. a spiritual teacher. See ईष्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् 5. इष्, ट्, f., Ved. that which is drunk,<BR>a draught, refreshment, enjoyment; libation; the<BR>refreshing waters of the sky; sap, strength, freshness,<BR>comfort, increase; good condition, affluence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष|इषः
इष, अस्, m. one who possesses sap and strength;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">Page0143-a+ 74</a>]<BR>the month Āśvina (September-October); strength,<BR>vigour (?).<BR>—इष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. vigorous.<BR>—इष-स्तुत्, त्, m., Ved. a praiser of the desired<BR>(Sun); (त्), f. praise of comfort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषय
इषय, nom. P. A., Ved. इषयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>to be succulent, swell; to be fresh, active, powerful;<BR>to refresh, strengthen, animate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिर|इषिरः
इषिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. succulent, refreshing, fresh,<BR>flourishing; vigorous, active, quick; [cf. Gr. ἱερός];<BR>(अस्), m. fire ?; (अम्), ind. quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषेत्वाक
इषेत्वाक, अस्, आ, अम् (an Adhyāya or Anuvāka),<BR>containing the words इषे त्वा, ‘for rain thee.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषु|इषुः
इषु इषु, इषु-धि, &c. See 1. इष् last page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृ
इष्कृ इष्-कृ, cl. 8. P., Ved. -करोति, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to arrange, set in order, prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कर्तृ|इष्कर्त्तृ
इष्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. arranging, preparing,<BR>setting in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृत
इष्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. arranged.<BR>—इष्कृता-<BR>हाव (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. whose Soma vessel<BR>is prepared or ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट|इष्टं|इष्टः
इष्ट 2. इष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. यज्; for 1. इष्ट<BR>see last page), sacrificed, worshipped with sacrifices;<BR>(अस्), m. sacrifice; (अम्), n. sacrificing; sacred rite,<BR>sacrament.<BR>—इष्ट-यजुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. one to<BR>whom sacrificial verses have been offered or addressed.<BR>—इष्टा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका, f. a brick, especially one used in building<BR>the altar of a sacrifice.<BR>—इष्टका-गृह, अम्, n. a<BR>brick house.<BR>—इष्टका-चित, अस्, आ, अम्, built of bricks.<BR>—इष्टका-न्यास, अस्, m. laying the foundation of a<BR>house.<BR>—इष्टका-राशि, इस्, m. a pile of bricks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
3. इष्टि, इस्, f. sacrificing, sacrifice; oblation con-<BR>sisting of butter, fruits, &c., opposed to the sacrifice<BR>of an animal or of Soma.<BR>—इष्टि-पच, अस्, or इष्टि-<BR>मुष्, ट्, m. an Asura, a demon.<BR>—इष्ट्य्-अयन, अम्,<BR>n. a series of oblations, a sacrifice lasting a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिका
इष्टिका, f. a brick, especially one used in building<BR>the sacrificial altar. See इष्टका above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिन्
इष्टिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट्वा
इष्ट्वा, ind. having sacrificed or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टनि
इष्टनि इष्टनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (if fr. rt. यज्),<BR>to be worshipped; (if instead of नि-ष्टनि, fr. rt.<BR>स्तन्), rustling, rushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इस्
इस् इस्, ind. an interjection of anger, pain,<BR>or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह इह, ind. (fr. pronom. base 3. इ), in this<BR>place, here; to this place; in this world; in this<BR>book or system; in this case (e. g. तेन इह न,<BR>‘therefore not in this case,’ i. e. the rule does not<BR>apply here); now, at this time; [cf. Zend idha,<BR>‘here;’ Gr. ἰθᾱ or ἰθαι in ἰθα-γενής and ἰθαι-γενής;<BR>Goth. ith; perhaps Lat. igi-tur.]<BR>—इह-काल, अस्,<BR>m. this life.<BR>—इह-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, or इह-चित्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. whose intentions or thoughts are<BR>in this world or place.<BR>—इह-त्र, ind. here, in this<BR>world.<BR>—इह-भोजन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. whose goods<BR>and gifts come hither.<BR>—इह-लोक, अस्, m. this world,<BR>this life; (ए), ind. in this world.<BR>—इह-समये, ind.<BR>here, now, on the present occasion, at such a time as<BR>this.<BR>—इह-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing here.<BR>—इह-<BR>स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, whose place or residence is on<BR>the earth; (ए), ind. in this place.<BR>—इहागत (˚ह-<BR>आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, come or arrived hither.<BR>—इहामुत्र<BR>(˚ह-अम्˚), ind. here and there, in this world and in<BR>the next.<BR>—इहेह (इह-इह), ind. here and there, now<BR>and then, repeatedly.<BR>—इहेह-मातृ, ता, m., Ved.<BR>of whose mothers one is here and one there; (Say.)<BR>whose mother is here and there, i. e. everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहत्य
इहत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, or इहत्यक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>being here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई 1. ई, the fourth letter of the alphabet,<BR>corresponding to इ long, and having the sound of एए<BR>in feel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई 2. ई, ईस्, m., N. of Kandarpa, the god of<BR>love; ई or ईस्, f., N. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई 3. ई, ind. an interjection of pain, anger,<BR>consciousness or perception, consideration, compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई 4. ई for rt. इ. See under 5. इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष्
ईक्ष् ईक्ष्, cl. 1. A. ईक्षते, ईक्षाञ्-चक्रे,<BR>ईक्षिष्यते, ऐक्षिष्ट, ईक्षितुम्, to see,<BR>look, view, behold, look at, gaze at (with acc. or<BR>rarely loc.); to see in one's mind, think, have a<BR>thought, regard, consider; to look to the welfare of<BR>any one (with dat.): Caus. ईक्षयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make one look at (with acc.). (This root is per-<BR>haps connected with अक्षि, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षक|ईक्षकः
ईक्षक, अस्, m. a spectator, a beholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षण|ईक्षणं
ईक्षण, अम्, n. a look, view, aspect, sight; re-<BR>garding, looking after, caring for; an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिक|ईक्षणिकः
ईक्षणिक, अस्, आ, m. f. a looker into the future,<BR>a fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षमाण
ईक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking at, surveying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षा
ईक्षा, f. sight, viewing, considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षित
ईक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, seen, beheld, regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षितृ
ईक्षितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, seeing, beholding, a beholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षेण्य
ईक्षेण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. deserving to be seen,<BR>curious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष्यमाण
ईक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being beheld, being<BR>viewed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख्
ईख् ईख् or इख्, cl. 1. P. एखति, इयेख, or<BR>ईखति, ईखाञ्-चकार, एखितुम् or ईखि-<BR>तुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईङ्ख्|ईंख्
ईङ्ख् ईङ्ख् or इङ्ख्, cl. 1. P. इङ्खति, इङ्खाञ्-<BR>चकार, or ईङ्खति, ईङ्खाञ्-चकार, इङ्खि-<BR>तुम् or ईङ्खितुम्, to go, move; Caus. ईङ्खयति,<BR>यितुम्, to move backwards and forwards, to move<BR>up and down, to swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज्
ईज् ईज् or ईञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. ईजति, ईजाञ्-चकार,<BR>ईजितुम् or ईञ्जति, &c., to go; to blame or<BR>censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईजिक
ईजिक ईजिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् 1. ईड्, cl. 2. A. ईट्टे (2nd sing. pres.<BR>ईडिषे, Ved. ईऌइषे), ईडाञ्^1-चक्रे, ईडिष्यते,<BR>ऐडिष्ट, ईडितुम्, Ved. ईऌए, &c., to implore, request,<BR>ask for (with two acc.); to praise: Caus. P. ईडयति,<BR>यितुम्, to ask; to praise.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk. on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 303. note: confirm VCP.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडन|ईडनं
ईडन, अम्, n. the act of praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडा
ईडा, f. praise, commendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडित|ईडितः
ईडित or ईऌइत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised, commended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडेन्य
ईडेन्य or ईऌएन्य or ईड्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be<BR>invoked or implored, to be praised or glorified, praise-<BR>worthy, laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्यमान
ईड्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् 2. ईड्, ईट्, f., Ved. = इड्, refreshment,<BR>libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईढ
ईढ ईढ, अस्, आ, अम् (? fr. ईह्), sought (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति ईति, इस्, f. (fr. 4. ई?), plague, distress,<BR>any calamity of the season (as drought, excessive<BR>rain, swarm of rats, foreign invasion, &c.); infectious<BR>disease; an affray; travelling in foreign countries,<BR>sojourning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष ईदृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इद्, neut. of pro-<BR>nom. base 3. इ, and दृक्ष, rt. दृश्, dropping one<BR>द् and lengthening the preceding इ, as in तादृक्ष<BR>from तद्, &c.), of this aspect, of such a kind,<BR>endowed with such qualities, such like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश्
ई-दृश्, क्, Ved. ङ्, endowed with such qualities,<BR>such; (क्), n., Ved. such a condition, such occasion.<BR>—ईदृक्-ता, f. quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश|ईदृशः
ईदृश, अस्, ई, अम्, or ईदृशक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>endowed with such qualities, such; [with the final<BR>syllables दृश् and दृश of these words cf. the Gr.<BR>λικ in δμῆλιξ, λικο in τηλίκο-ς, &c.; Goth. leika<BR>in hvêleiks, ‘welcher,’ svaleik-s, ‘such;’ Mod.<BR>Germ. solcher; Slav. liko, nom. lik, e. g. tolik,<BR>‘such;’ Lat. li in tâlis, quâlis.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईन्त्|ईंत्
ईन्त् ईन्त्, cl. 1. P. ईन्तति, -तितुम्, to bind;<BR>[cf. अन्त् and अन्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्स्
ईप्स् ईप्स् (Desid. of rt. आप्, q. v.), to wish<BR>to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सन
ईप्सन, अम्, n. desiring, wishing to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सा
ईप्सा, f. asking, desire, wish to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, striving to obtain; wishing to get<BR>or obtain, desirous of (with acc.).<BR>—ईप्सु-यज्ञ, अस्,<BR>m. a particular Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईम्
ईम् ईम्, ind. (fr. pronominal base 3. इ), Ved.<BR>a particle of affirmation and restriction, generally after<BR>short words at the beginning of a period, or after the re-<BR>lative pronouns, the conjunction यद्, prepositions and<BR>particles such as आत्, उत, अथ, &c. ईम् has also the<BR>sense ‘now’ (= इदानीम्), and is by Sāy. sometimes<BR>considered as an acc. case for एनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईयचक्षस्
ईयचक्षस् ईय-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (ईय fr. rt.<BR>इ), Ved. one whose eyes go or look about everywhere;<BR>(Sāy.) of pervading sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईयिवस्
ईयिवस्, आन्, -युषी, अस्, gone, having gone, having<BR>obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् ईर्, cl. 2. A. ईर्ते, ईराञ्-चक्रे, ईरिष्यति,<BR>ऐरिष्ट, ईरितुम्, Ved. inf. इरध्यै, to go,<BR>move, rise, arise from; to go away, retire; to agitate,<BR>elevate, raise (one's voice): Caus. P. ईरयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to agitate, throw, cast; to excite; to cause to rise;<BR>to bring to life; to raise one's voice, utter, pronounce,<BR>proclaim, cite; to elevate; A. to raise one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरण|ईरणः
ईरण, अस्, आ, अम्, agitating, driving; (अस्), m.<BR>the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरित|ईरितं
ईरित, अस्, आ, अम्, sent, despatched; said, uttered.<BR>—ईरिताकूत (˚त-आक्˚), अम्, n. declared purpose or<BR>intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्य
ईर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excited.<BR>—ईर्य-ता, f., Ved.<BR>the condition of one who is to be excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्या|ईर्य्या
ईर्या, f. wandering about as a religious mendicant.<BR>—ईर्या-पथ, अस्, m. the observances of a religious<BR>mendicant; the four positions of the body, viz.<BR>going, standing upright, sitting and lying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरामा
ईरामा ईरामा, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण ईरिण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ईर् ?), desert;<BR>(अम्), n. salt and barren soil. See इरिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिन्
ईरिन् ईरिन्, ई, m., N. of a man; (इणस्), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of this man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य्
ईर्क्ष्य् ईर्क्ष्य्. See ईर्ष्य्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म|ईर्मः|ईर्म्म
ईर्म 1. ईर्म, ind., Ved. in this place, here,<BR>to this place; (Sāy.) going constantly, or instigating<BR>everything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म|ईर्मः|ईर्म्म
ईर्म 2. ईर्म, अस्, m., Ved. the arm, the fore-<BR>quarter of an animal; (अम्), n. a sore or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्मान्त|ईर्मांत
ईर्मान्त ईर्मान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. epithet of a<BR>team of horses or of the horses of the sun's car; full-<BR>haunched (lit. full-ended); thin-haunched; (perhaps)<BR>having the biggest horses on both sides of the team.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्वारु|ईर्वारुः|ईर्व्वारु|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्वारु ईर्वारु, उस्, m. a cucumber, Cucumis<BR>Utilissimus. See इर्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य् ईर्ष्य् or ईर्क्ष्य्, cl. 1. P. ईर्ष्यति,<BR>ईर्ष्याञ्-चकार, ईर्ष्यितुम्, or ईर्क्ष्यति,<BR>&c., to envy, to feel impatient at another's prosperity<BR>(with dat.): Desid. ईर्ष्यिषिषति or ईर्ष्यियिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा, f. impatience, envy of another's success;<BR>more properly read ईर्ष्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्षालु, उस्, उस्, उ, impatient of another's success,<BR>envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षित
ईर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, envied; (अम्), n. envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षितव्य
ईर्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be envied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षु
ईर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, envious, envying; (आ), f. envy<BR>or impatience of another's success; spite, malice.<BR>—ईर्ष्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or ईर्ष्या-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, envious, spiteful,<BR>—ईर्ष्या-वश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>overcome with envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, envious, envying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यमाण
ईर्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, envying, envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यालु|ईर्ष्यालुः
ईर्ष्यालु, उस्, उस्, उ, envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यिन्
ईर्ष्यिन्, ई, इणी, इ, envious, spiteful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यु
ईर्ष्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलिन|ईलिनः
ईलिन ईलिन, अस्, m., N. of a son of Taṃsu<BR>and father of Dushyanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईली
ईली ईली or ईलि, इस्, f. a weapon, sometimes<BR>considered as a cudgel and sometimes as a short sword<BR>or stick shaped like a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईळ्
ईळ् ईऌ, ईऌआ, &c. See under ईड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईवत्|ईवन्त्
ईवत् ई-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. pronominal base<BR>3. इ), Ved. so large, so stately, so magnificent, so much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
ईश् 1. ईश्, cl. 2. A. ईष्टे, or Ved. ईशे, ईशञ्-<BR>चक्रे, ईशिष्यति, ईशितुम्, to own, possess;<BR>to belong to; to dispose of, be valid or powerful, to<BR>be master of (with gen., or Ved. with gen. of an inf.,<BR>or with a common inf., or the loc. of an abstract<BR>noun); to command; to rule, reign; to behave like<BR>a master, allow; [with this word are perhaps con-<BR>nected Goth. aigan, ‘to have;’ Old Germ. eigan,<BR>adj. eigan, ‘own;’ Mod. Germ. eigen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
2. ईश्, ट्, m., Ved. master, lord, the supreme spirit.<BR>—ईशा-वास्य, अम्, n. ‘to be clothed or pervaded by<BR>the supreme,’ a title of the Īśa-upaniṣad, which com-<BR>mences with that expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश, अस्, आ, अम्, owning, possessing, sharing; one<BR>who is completely master of anything; capable of<BR>(with gen.); powerful, supreme; a ruler, a master,<BR>a lord; (अस्), m. a husband; a Rudra; the number<BR>‘eleven’ (as there are eleven Rudras); N. of Śiva<BR>as regent of the north-east quarter; (आ), f. faculty,<BR>power, dominion.<BR>—ईश-त्व, अम्, n. supremacy, supe-<BR>riority.<BR>—ईश-सखि, आ, m. Śiva's friend, an epithet of<BR>Kuvera.<BR>—ईशाध्याय (˚श-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of the<BR>Īśa-upaniṣad.<BR>—ईशोपनिषद् (˚श-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of<BR>an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशन|ईशनं
ईशन, अम्, n. commanding, reigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशान|ईशानं|ईशानः
ईशान, अस्, आ, अम्, owning, possessing, wealthy;<BR>reigning; (अस्), m. a ruler, master, one of the older<BR>names of Śiva-Rudra; one of the Rudras; the sun<BR>as a form of Śiva; a Sādhya; epithet of Viṣṇu; N.<BR>of a man; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā; (अस् or ई), m.<BR>or f. the silk-cotton tree, Bombax Heptaphyllum;<BR>(अम्), n. light, splendor.<BR>—ईशान-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>acting like a competent person, making use of one's<BR>possessions or faculties; (Sāy.) rendering one a master<BR>or able.<BR>—ईशान-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a physician.<BR>—ईशान-ज, आस्, m. pl. a class of deities forming a<BR>section of the Kalpa-bhavas.<BR>—ईशान-देवी, f., N. of a<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितृ
ईशितृ, ता, m. a master, an owner or proprietor; a<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिन्
ईशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, commanding, reigning; (इनी), f.<BR>supremacy.<BR>—ईशि-ता, f. or ईशि-त्व, अम्, n. superiority,<BR>supremacy, one of the eight attributes of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, able to do, capable of (with<BR>gen. of Vedic inf., or with common inf.), liable, ex-<BR>posed to; (अस्, ई), m. f. master, lord, prince, king, mis-<BR>tress, queen; (अस्), m. a husband; god, the supreme,<BR>especially Śiva, one of the Rudras, the god of love,<BR>the soul or supreme soul (आत्मन्), N. of a prince;<BR>(आ or ई), f., N. of Durgā; of Lakṣmī or of any<BR>other of the Śaktis or female energies of the deities.<BR>—ईश्वर-कृष्ण, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Sāṅkhya-kārikā.<BR>—ईश्वर-गीता, f. pl. a section of the<BR>Kūrma-Purāṇa.<BR>—ईश्वर-ता, f. or ईश्वर-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. superiority, supremacy.<BR>—ईश्वर-दत्त, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—ईश्वर-निषेध, अस्, m. atheism.<BR>—ईश्वर-निष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, trusting in God.<BR>—ईश्वर-पूजक, अस्, आ, अम्, pious.<BR>—ईश्वर-पूजा,<BR>f. worship of God.<BR>—ईश्वर-प्रसाद, अस्, m. divine<BR>grace.<BR>—ईश्वर-भाव, अस्, m. royal or imperial state.<BR>—ईश्वर-सद्मन्, अ, n. a temple.<BR>—ईश्वर-सभ,<BR>अम्, n. a royal court or assembly.<BR>—ईश्वर-सेवा, f.<BR>the worship of God.<BR>—ईश्वराधीन (˚र-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, subject to a king, dependant on a master or<BR>on God.<BR>—ईश्वराधीन-ता, f. or ईश्वराधीन-त्व,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">Page0144-b+ 72</a>]<BR>अम्, n. dependance upon God, subjection to a ruler.<BR>—ईश्वरानन्द. (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्
ईष् ईष्, cl. 1. A. (with prep. also P.)<BR>ईषते, -ति, ईषाञ्-चक्रे or -चकार, and<BR>Ved. ईषे, ईषितुम्, to go, to fly away, escape; to<BR>attack, to hurt; to glean, to collect a few grains;<BR>to look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषण
ईषण, अस्, आ, अम्, hastening; (आ), f. haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषणिनि
ईषणिनि, ई, इनी, इ, hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष|ईषः
ईष ईष, अस्, m. the month Āśvina; see<BR>इष; a son of the third Manu; a servant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्
ईषत् ईषत्, ind. (said to be a pres. part. fr.<BR>rt. ईष्), little, a little, slightly.<BR>—ईषच्-छ्वास, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, slightly resounding.<BR>—ईषज्-जल, अम्, n. shallow<BR>water, a little water.<BR>—ईषत्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, doing<BR>little; easy to be accomplished.<BR>—ईषत्-कार्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, connected with slight effort.<BR>—ईषत्-पाण्डु,<BR>उस्, m. a pale or light brown colour.<BR>—ईषत्-पान,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, that of which a little is drunk; (अम्),<BR>n. a little draught.<BR>—ईषत्-पुरुष, अस्, m. a mean<BR>man.<BR>—ईषत्-प्रलम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gained<BR>for little.<BR>—ईषत्-स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, slightly touched<BR>(applied to the semivowels).<BR>—ईषद्-उष्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, tepid, slightly warm.<BR>—ईषद्-ऊन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not quite complete or entire.<BR>—ईषद्-गुण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of little merit.<BR>—ईषद्-दर्शन, अम्, n. a glance,<BR>a slight inspection.<BR>—ईषद्-धास (ईषत्-हास), अस्,<BR>m. slight laughter, a smile.<BR>—ईषद्-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pale red.<BR>—ईषद्-विवृत, अस्, आ, अम्, slightly open.<BR>—ईषन्-नाद, अस्, आ, अम्, slightly sounding (applied<BR>to unaspirated soft consonants).<BR>—ईषन्-निमय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, exchanged for a little.<BR>—ईषल्-लभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be obtained for a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषा
ईषा ईषा, f. (said to be fr. ईष्), the pole or<BR>the shafts of a carriage or plough; (ए), du. the double<BR>or fork-shaped pole.<BR>—ईषा-दण्ड, अस्, m. the handle<BR>of a plough.<BR>—ईषा-दन्त, अस्, m. an elephant with<BR>a large tusk or tooth, the tusk of an elephant.<BR>—ईषाधार (˚षा-आध्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिका
ईषिका ईषिका, f. an elephant's eyeball; a<BR>painter's brush, &c.; a weapon, a dart or arrow. See<BR>इषीका and ईषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिर|ईषिरः
ईषिर ईषिर, अस्, m. fire. See इषिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषीका
ईषीका ईषीका, f. a painter's brush, a fibrous<BR>stick used as one; an ingot-mould; a dipping rod or<BR>something cast into a crucible to examine if the<BR>metal it contains is in fusion. See ईक्षिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्म|ईष्मः
ईष्म ईष्म and ईष्व, अस्, m. Kāmadeva;<BR>spring. See इष्म and इष्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्व|ईष्वः
ईष्व ईष्व, अस्, m. a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह्
ईह् ईह्, cl. 1. A. ईहते, ईहाञ्-चक्रे, ईहिष्-<BR>यते, ईहितुम्, rarely P. ईहति, &c., to en-<BR>deavour to obtain; to aim at or attempt; to long for,<BR>desire; to take care of; to have in mind, think of<BR>(with acc.): Caus. ईहयति, -यितुम्, to impel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह|ईहः
ईह, अस्, m. attempt (e. g. ऊर्ध्वेह, attempt to rise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहमान
ईहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, attempting, undertaking,<BR>performing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहा
ईहा, f. effort, exertion, activity; request, desire,<BR>wish.<BR>—ईहा-तस्, ind. diligently, energetically, by or<BR>with labour or exertion.<BR>—ईहा-मृग, अस्, m. a wolf;<BR>a division of the drama.<BR>—ईहार्थिन् (ईहा-अर्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, aiming at any object, seeking wealth.<BR>—ईहा-<BR>वृक, अस्, m. a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहित
ईहित, अस्, आ, अम्, sought, attempted, striven for;<BR>wished, desired; (अम्), n. desire, request, wish, effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ 1. उ, the fifth letter and third short<BR>vowel of the alphabet, pronounced as the उ in full.<BR>—उ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ 2. उ, ind. an interjection of assent, call-<BR>ing, compassion, anger, and command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ 3. उ, ind. an enclitic copula, used fre-<BR>quently in the Vedas; (as a particle implying re-<BR>striction and antithesis, generally after pronominals,<BR>prepositions, particles, and before नु and सु, equiva-<BR>lent to) and, also, further; on the other hand (espe-<BR>cially in connection with a relative, e. g. य उ, he on<BR>the contrary who &c.).<BR>This particle may serve to give emphasis, like इद्<BR>and एव, especially after prepositions or demonstrative<BR>pronouns, in conjunction with नु, वै, हि, चिद्, &c.<BR>(e. g. अयम् उ वाम् पुरुतमो जोहवीमि, I this very<BR>person invoke you constantly). It is especially used in<BR>the figure of speech called Anaphora, and particularly<BR>when the pronouns are repeated (e. g. तम् उ स्तुष<BR>इन्द्रम् तम् गृणीषे, him I praise, Indra, him<BR>I sing). It may be used in drawing a conclusion, like<BR>the English ‘now’ (e. g. तद् उ तथा न कुर्यात्,<BR>that now he should not do in such a manner), and<BR>is frequently found in interrogative sentences (e. g. क<BR>उ तच् चिकेत, who, I ask, should know that ?).<BR>Pāṇini calls this particle उञ् to distinguish it from<BR>the interrogative उ. In the Pada-pāṭha it is written<BR>ऊं.<BR>In the classical language उ occurs only after अथ,<BR>न, and किम्, with a slight modification of the sense,<BR>and often only as an expletive (see किम्); उ-उ or<BR>उ-उत, on the one hand — on the other hand; partly —<BR>partly; as well — as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ 4. उ, cl. 1. A. अवते, ऊवे, ओष्यते, औष्ट,<BR>ओतुम्, to sound, to make a noise; to roar, bel-<BR>low: Caus. P. आवयति, -यितुम्, to cause to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ 5. उ, cl. 5. P., Ved. उनोति, ओतुम्, to<BR>animate, ask, demand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ 6. उ, उस्, m., N. of Śiva; also of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकनाह|उकनाहः
उकनाह उकनाह, अस्, m. a horse of a red<BR>and yellow or red and black colour, a bay or chesnut<BR>horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकुण|उकुणः
उकुण उकुण, अस्, m. a bug; also उत्कुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त उक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part.<BR>of rt. वच्), uttered, said, spoken; (अम्), n. word,<BR>sentence; (अम्, आ), n. f. a stanza of four lines with<BR>one syllabic instant, one long or two short syllables<BR>in each; [cf. Zend ukhta.]<BR>—उक्त-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>being spoken or uttered.<BR>—उक्त-निर्वाह, अस्, m.<BR>maintaining an assertion.<BR>—उक्त-पुंस्क, a (femi-<BR>nine or neuter) word, of which also a masculine is<BR>mentioned or exists, and whose meaning only differs<BR>from that of the masculine by the notion of gender<BR>(e. g. the word गङ्गा is not उक्त-पुंस्क, whereas<BR>the word शोभना is so; cf. भाषित-पुंस्क).<BR>—उक्त-प्रत्युक्त, अम्, n. speech and reply, dis-<BR>course, conversation.<BR>—उक्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one<BR>who has spoken.<BR>—उक्त-वर्जम्, ind. except the<BR>cases mentioned.<BR>—उक्त-वाक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has given an opinion; (अम्), n. a dictum, a decree.<BR>—उक्तानुक्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, spoken and not<BR>spoken.<BR>—उक्तोपसंहार (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m. any<BR>brief or compendious phrase or description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ति|उक्तिः
उक्ति, इस्, f. sentence, proclamation, speech, expres-<BR>sion, word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त्वा
उक्त्वा, ind. having spoken or said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ|उक्थं|उक्थः
उक्थ, अम्, n. a saying, sentence, verse, eulogy, praise;<BR>(in the ritual) a kind of recitation or certain recited<BR>verses forming a subdivision of the Śăstras. They<BR>generally form a series, and are spoken or recited in<BR>opposition to those verses which are sung (सामन्)<BR>and to the muttered sacrificial formulas (यजुस्).<BR>The great उक्थ (महद्-उक्थम् or बृहद्-उक्-<BR>थम्) forms a series of verses, in three sections, each<BR>containing eighty threefold verses (तृच), recited at<BR>the end of the Agnicayana; a N. of the Sāma-veda;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of metre, a stanza of four lines having<BR>one long or two short syllables in each; (अस्), m. a<BR>form of Agni; N. of a prince.<BR>—उक्थ-पत्त्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having verses as wings.<BR>—उक्थ-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. vessels or libations offered during the recita-<BR>tion of an uktha.<BR>—उक्थ-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. offering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">Page0145-a+ 77</a>]<BR>ukthas.<BR>—उक्थ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. connected<BR>with an uktha.<BR>—उक्थ-वर्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>strengthening one's self by or delighting in praise;<BR>(Sāy.) to be celebrated in praise.<BR>—उक्थ-वाहस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, Ved. offering verses; one to whom verses<BR>are offered.<BR>—उक्थ-शंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. praising;<BR>uttering the ukthas.<BR>—उक्थ-शस्, अस्, अस्, or उक्थ-<BR>शास्, आस्, आस्, m. f. or उक्थ-शस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. utter-<BR>ing a verse, praising.<BR>—उक्थ-शुष्म, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. loudly resonant with verses, moving on with the<BR>sound of verses (as with the roaring of waters), ac-<BR>companied by sounding verses; (Sāy.) whose strength<BR>is praise.<BR>—उक्था-मद, अम्, n., Ved. praise and re-<BR>joicing.<BR>—उक्थार्क (˚थ-अर्˚), अम्, n., Ved. recitation<BR>and hymn.<BR>—उक्था-वी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. fond of verses.<BR>—उक्था-शस्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. recitation and praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थिन्
उक्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. uttering verses, praising,<BR>lauding; accompanied by praise, or (in ritual) by<BR>ukthas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ्य|उक्थ्यः
उक्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. accompanied by verse or<BR>praise, consisting of praise, deserving praise, skilled in<BR>praising; accompanied by ukthas; (अस्), m. a liba-<BR>tion (ग्रह) at the morning and midday sacrifice;<BR>(scil. क्रतु) N. of a liturgical ceremony, forming<BR>part e. g. of the Jyotiṣṭoma; a Soma-yajña.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष्
उक्ष् 1. उक्ष्, cl. 1. 6. P. A. उक्षति, -ते,<BR>उक्षाञ्-चकार (Ved. ववक्ष, -षे),<BR>उक्षितुम्, to sprinkle, moisten, wet; to sprinkle or<BR>scatter in small drops, to emit; to throw out, scatter<BR>(as sparks); to clean; [cf. Lith. ûkana: Hib. uisg,<BR>uisge, ‘water, a river;’ uisgeach, ‘aquatic, watery,<BR>fluid, moist, pluvial.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
1. उक्ष, अस्, m. (at the end of some compounds)<BR>= उक्षन् below; (अस्, आ, अम्), clean (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण|उक्षणं
उक्षण, अम्, n. sprinkling, consecrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्य
उक्षण्य, nom. P., Ved. उक्षण्यति, to do or<BR>behave like Ukṣan; (Sāy.) to desire one who pours<BR>down riches &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्यायन
उक्षण्यायन, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from<BR>Ukṣaṇya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्यु
उक्षण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. behaving or doing like<BR>Ukṣan; (Sāy.) desirous of one who pours down<BR>riches &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षन्
उक्षन्, आ, m. an ox or bull (especially as drawing<BR>the chariot of Uṣas or dawn); epithet of the Soma<BR>(as sprinkling or scattering small drops); of the<BR>Maruts; of the sun and Agni; one of the eight chief<BR>medicaments (ऋषभ); N. of a man; (आ, आ, अ),<BR>large (?); [cf. Zend ukhṣan; Goth. auhsa and<BR>auhsu; Armen. eṣn.]<BR>—उक्ष-तर, अस्, m. a small<BR>bull or ox; a large bull.<BR>—उक्ष-वश, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>a bull-calf, male calf.<BR>—उक्ष-वेहत्, अत्, m., Ved. an<BR>impotent bull (?).<BR>—उक्षान्न (˚क्ष-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. one whose food is oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षित
1. उक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled, moistened,<BR>cleansed, perfumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष्
उक्ष् 2. उक्ष्, cl. 1. P., Ved. उक्षति,<BR>ववक्ष, and A. ववक्षे, उक्षितुम्,<BR>to grow up, to grow strong; A. to strengthen one's<BR>self; become strong: Caus. उक्षयते, -यितुम्, to<BR>strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
2. उक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षाल|उक्षालः
उक्षाल, अस्, आ, अम् (?), swift, excellent, terrible,<BR>high, much; (अस्), m. a monkey (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षित
2. उक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, adult, of full growth, strong;<BR>old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्
उख् उख्, cl. 1. P. ओखति, उवोख, ओखि-<BR>तुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख|उखः
उख उख, अस्, m. (fr. rt. खन् with उद् ?),<BR>Ved. a boiler, a pot, a vessel; N. of a pupil of Tittiri;<BR>(आ), f. a boiler, any saucepan, a pot or vessel which<BR>can be put on the fire; a part of the body.<BR>—उख-<BR>च्छिद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. breaking the pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्य|उख्यं|उख्यः
उख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in a dish; boiled,<BR>dressed in a pot (flesh, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखर्वल|उखर्वलः|उखर्व्वल|उखर्व्वलः
उखर्वल उखर्वल or उखल, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of grass, a sort of Andropogon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखुली
उखुली उखुली, f., N. of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उगण
उगण उगण, अस्, आ, अम् (corrupted fr. उद्-<BR>गण or उरु-गण ?), Ved. consisting of extended<BR>troops (used as an epithet of सेना, an army).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्र|उग्रं|उग्रः
उग्र उग्र, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. उच्,<BR>but probably fr. a rt. उज् or वज्, fr. which also ओजस्,<BR>वाज, वज्र, may be derived; comparative उग्र-<BR>तर and ओजियस्; superl. उग्रतम and ओजिष्ठ),<BR>powerful, violent, mighty, strong beyond measure,<BR>huge, formidable, terrible; high, noble; cruel, fierce,<BR>ferocious, savage; angry, passionate, wrathful; hot,<BR>sharp, pungent, acrid; (अस्), m., N. of Rudra or Śiva;<BR>N. of a mixed tribe, from a Kṣatriya father and<BR>Śūdra mother, (the employment of this caste, accord-<BR>ing to Manu, is the killing or catching of animals<BR>that live in holes, as of snakes &c.; but according to<BR>the Tantras the Ugra is an encomiast or bard); the<BR>tree Hyperanthera Moringa; N. of a Dānava; a son<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; the Guru of Narendrāditya, who<BR>built a temple called Ugreśa; a group of asterisms<BR>(viz. पूर्वफाल्गुनी, पूर्वाषाढा, पूर्वभाद्र-<BR>पद, मघा, भरणी); N. of the Malabar country;<BR>(आ), N. of different plants, Artemisia Sternutatoria,<BR>Coriandrum Sativum, &c.; (ई), f. a being belonging<BR>to the class of demons; (अम्), n. a certain poison,<BR>the root of Aconitum Ferox; wrath, anger; [cf.<BR>Zend ughra.]<BR>—उग्र-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, fierce in<BR>action, violent, cruel.<BR>—उग्र-काण्ड, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of gourd, Momordica Charantia.<BR>—उग्र-गन्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, strong-smelling; (अस्), m. the plant<BR>Michelia Champaca; garlic; (आ), f. orris root; a<BR>medicinal plant; Artemisia Sternutatoria; Pimpinella<BR>Involucrata; the common carraway (Carum Carui,<BR>&c.); Ligusticum Ajowan; (अम्), n. Asa Fœtida.<BR>—उग्रगन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, strong-smelling.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>चय, अस्, m. strong desire.<BR>—उग्र-चारिणी, f., N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—उग्र-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, base-born.<BR>—उग्र-जित्,<BR>त्, f., Ved., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—उग्र-ता, f. or उग्र-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. violence, passion, anger; pungency,<BR>acrimony.<BR>—उग्र-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, endowed with<BR>great or terrible energy; (आस्), m., N. of a Nāga; of a<BR>Buddha; of another divine being.<BR>—उग्र-दंष्ट्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having terrific teeth.<BR>—उग्र-दण्ड, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, lit. ‘stern-sceptred’ or holding a terrible rod;<BR>relentless, remorseless.<BR>—उग्र-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of a frightful appearance, frightful, terrible.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>दुहितृ, ता, f. daughter of a powerful man.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>धन्वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having a powerful bow,<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>—उग्र-नासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, large-<BR>nosed.<BR>—उग्र-पुत्र, अस्, m. son of a powerful<BR>man; (अस्, आ, अम्), having mighty sons.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. whose arms are large or power-<BR>ful.<BR>—उग्रम्-पश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, frightful, hideous,<BR>fierce looking; malignant, wicked; (आ), f., N. of an<BR>Apsaras.<BR>—उग्र-रेतस्, आस्, m. a form of Rudra.<BR>—उग्र-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having powerful men.<BR>—उग्र-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, terrible in might.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>वेग, अस्, आ, अम्, of terrible velocity.<BR>—उग्र-व्यग्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—उग्र-शक्ति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a son of king Amara-śakti.<BR>—उग्र-शासन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, severe in command, strict in orders.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>शेखरा, f. ‘crest of Śiva,’ N. of the Gaṅgā.<BR>—उग्र-शोक, अस्, आ, अम्, sorely grieving.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>श्रवण-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, terrible to hear and<BR>see.<BR>—उग्र-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उग्र-<BR>सेन, अस्, m., N. of several princes, e. g. of a brother<BR>of Janam-ejaya; (आ), f., N. of the wife of Akrūra.<BR>—उग्रसेन-ज, अस्, m. a N. of Kaṃsa, the uncle and<BR>enemy of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—उग्राचार्य (˚ग्र-आच्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author.<BR>—उग्रा-देव, अस्, m., Ved. having<BR>mighty deities, N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—उग्रायुध (˚ग्र-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having powerful weapons;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—उग्रेश (˚ग्र-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the mighty or terrible lord, an epithet of Śiva;<BR>N. of a sanctuary built by Ugra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रक
उग्रक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उङ्कार|उंकार
उङ्कार उङ्-कार, अस्, m., N. of a companion<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उङ्कुण|उंकुणः|उङ्कुणः
उङ्कुण उङ्कुण, अस्, m. a bug. See उत्-कुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्
उच् उच्, cl. 4. P. उच्यति, उवोच, उचिष्यति,<BR>उचितुम्, to take pleasure in; to delight in,<BR>to be fond of; to be accustomed, to be suitable, to<BR>suit, to fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचित|उचितं
उचित, अस्, आ, अम्, delightful, pleasurable, agreeable;<BR>customary, usual; proper, suitable, convenient; ac-<BR>ceptable, fit or right to be taken; known, under-<BR>stood; intrusted, deposited; measured, adjusted,<BR>accurate; delighting in, used to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचथ|उचथं
उचथ उचथ, अम्, n. (fr. rt. वच्), Ved.<BR>verse, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचथ्य
उचथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. deserving praise; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of an Āṅgirasa, author of some hymns of the<BR>Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्च|उच्चं|उच्चः
उच्च उच्च, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. 1. उद् with<BR>च fr. rt. अञ्च्), high, lofty, elevated; tall; deep; high-<BR>sounding, loud, pronounced with the Udātta accent;<BR>intense, violent; (अस्), m. the apex of the orbit of a<BR>planet; [cf. Hib. uchdan, ‘a hillock;’ Cambro-Brit.<BR>uched, ‘cleve.’]<BR>—उच्च-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, highest.<BR>—उच्च-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, higher, more lofty.<BR>—उच्च-<BR>तरु, उस्, m. the cocoa-nut tree; any lofty tree.<BR>—उच्च-ता, f. or उच्च-त्व, अम्, n. height, superi-<BR>ority.<BR>—उच्च-ताल, अम्, n. music and dancing at<BR>feasts, drinking parties, &c.<BR>—उच्च-देव, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—उच्च-देवता, f. time<BR>personified, chronos.<BR>—उच्च-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Śākya-muni as teacher of the gods among the Tuṣitas,<BR>q. v.<BR>—उच्च-नीच, अस्, आ, अम्, high and low, varie-<BR>gated, heterogeneous; (अम्), n. the upper and lower<BR>station of the planets; change of accent.<BR>—उच्च-<BR>पद, अम्, n. a high situation, a high office.<BR>—उच्-<BR>च-भाषण, अम्, n. speaking aloud.<BR>—उच्च-भा-<BR>षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking with a loud voice, shouting,<BR>brawling.<BR>—उच्च-ललाटा or -इका, f. a woman with a<BR>high or projecting forehead.<BR>—उच्चावच, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>(fr. उच्च = उद् + च and अव + च?), high and low,<BR>great and small, variegated, heterogeneous; various,<BR>multiform; uneven, irregular, undulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चकैस्
उच्चकैस्, ind. excessively lofty; tall; loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चा
उच्चा, ind., Ved. above (in heaven), from above,<BR>upwards; उच्चा कृ, to carry upwards.<BR>—उच्चा-चक्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a wheel above (epithet of a<BR>well).<BR>—उच्चा-बुध्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the<BR>bottom upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्
उच्चैस्, ind. (used adjectively in comp.) aloft, high,<BR>above, upwards, from above; loud, accentuated; in-<BR>tensely, much, powerfully.<BR>—उच्चैः-कर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>making acutely accented.<BR>—उच्चैः-कुल, अम्, n. a<BR>high family; (अस्, आ, अम्), of high family.<BR>—उच्चैर्-<BR>घुष्ट, अम्, n. making a loud noise, clamour.<BR>—उच्चैर्-घोष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sounding aloud,<BR>crying, neighing, roaring, rattling.<BR>—उच्चैर्-भुज-<BR>तरु, उस्, उस्, उ, having trees like outstretched arms.<BR>—उच्चैः-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, carrying one's head high,<BR>a man of high rank.<BR>—उच्चैः-श्रवस्, आस्, m. long-<BR>eared or neighing aloud; epithet of the horse of<BR>Indra, produced at the churning of the ocean, (re-<BR>garded as the prototype and king of horses.)<BR>—उच्चैः-<BR>श्रवस, अस्, m. = the same.<BR>—उच्चैः-स्वर, अस्, m.<BR>a loud sound or voice; (अस्, आ, अम्), making a loud<BR>sound.<BR>—उच्चैस्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, very high, tall or<BR>lofty; very loud.<BR>—उच्चैस्-तमाम्, ind. exceedingly<BR>high; on high; loudly, aloud.<BR>—उच्चैस्-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, higher, very high, loftier, louder; pronounced<BR>with a higher accent.<BR>—उच्चैस्तर-त्व, अम्, n. state<BR>of being too high.<BR>—उच्चैस्-त्व, अम्, n. height.<BR>—उच्चैः-स्थान, अम्, n. a high place; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>of high rank or family.<BR>—उच्चैः-स्थेय, अम्, n.<BR>lofty, firmness (of character).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चक्
उच्चक् उच्-चक् (उद्-चक्), cl. 1. P. A. चकति,<BR>-ते, -कितुम्, to look up at, behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चक्षुस्
उच्चक्षुस् उच्-चक्षुस् (उद्-च˚), उस्, उस्, उस्,<BR>whose eyes are directed upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चघन|उच्चघनं
उच्चघन उच्चघन, अम्, n. laughter in the<BR>mind not expressed in the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चट्
उच्चट् उच्-चट् (उद्-चट्), cl. 1. P. -चटति, -टि-<BR>तुम्, to go away, disappear; Caus. P. -चाटयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to drive away, expel, scare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटन|उच्चाटनं|उच्चाटनः
उच्-चाटन, अम्, n. eradicating (as a plant), ex-<BR>pulsion; ruining (an adversary), causing a person to<BR>quit his occupation by means of magical incantations,<BR>exciting disgust for one's profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटनीय
उच्-चाटनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be driven away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटित
उच्-चाटित, अस्, आ, अम्, driven away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चटा
उच्चटा उच्चटा, f. (perhaps connected with<BR>उच्च or in some sense fr. उच्-चट् above), pride,<BR>arrogance; habit, usage; N. of different plants, a<BR>species of cyperus, a kind of garlic, Abrus Precatorius,<BR>Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चण्ड|उच्चंड|उच्चण्डः
उच्चण्ड उच्-चण्ड (उद्-च˚), अस्, आ, अम्, quick,<BR>expeditious; passionate, violent; hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चन्द्र|उच्चंद्र|उच्चंद्रः|उच्चन्द्रः
उच्चन्द्र उच्-चन्द्र (उद्-च˚), अस्, m. the moon-<BR>less period of the night, the last watch of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चर्
उच्चर् उच्-चर् (उद्-चर्), cl. 1. P. -चरति, -रि-<BR>तुम् (ep. sometimes -चर्तुम्), Ved. -रितवे or -वै,<BR>-रसे, -रध्यै, to go upwards, ascend, rise (as the<BR>sun), issue forth, go forth; to rise (as the voice); to<BR>let the contents (of anything) issue out, to empty the<BR>body by evacuations; to emit (sounds), utter, pro-<BR>nounce; to quit, leave; to sin against, to be unfaith-<BR>ful to a husband; to transgress against: Caus. -चार-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to go forth, to evacuate the<BR>body by excretion, to discharge feces, to emit, to<BR>cause to sound, utter, pronounce, declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरण|उच्चरणं
उच्-चरण, अम्, n. going up or out, uttering,<BR>articulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरण्य
उच्-चरण्य, nom. P. -चरण्यति, -यितुम्, to move<BR>out, stretch out to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरित
उच्-चरित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone up or out, risen;<BR>uttered, articulated; (अम्), n. excrement, dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार|उच्चारः
उच्-चार, अस्, m. feces, excrement; discharge; pro-<BR>nunciation, utterance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारक
उच्-चारक, अस्, आ, अम्, pronouncing, making audible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारण|उच्चारणं
उच्-चारण, अम्, n. pronunciation, articulation, enun-<BR>ciation; making audible.<BR>—उच्चारण-ज्ञ, अस्, m. a<BR>linguist, one skilled in utterances or sounds.<BR>—उच्-<BR>चारण-स्थान, अम्, n. the part of the throat whence<BR>certain sounds such as nasals, gutturals &c. proceed.<BR>—उच्चारणार्थ (˚ण-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, useful for pro-<BR>nunciation; necessary for pronunciation, a redundant<BR>letter &c. only used to make pronunciation easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणीय
उच्-चारणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pronounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारित
उच्-चारित, अस्, आ, अम्, pronounced, uttered, arti-<BR>culated; having excrements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्य|उच्चार्य्य
1. उच्-चार्य, ind. having spoken, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्य|उच्चार्य्य
2. उच्-चार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken, to be pro-<BR>nounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्यमाण|उच्चार्य्यमाण
उच्-चार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being uttered or pro-<BR>nounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल्
उच्चल् उच्-चल् (उद्-चल्), cl. 1. P. -चलति, -लि-<BR>तुम्, to go or move away from; to free one's self<BR>from, loosen one's self from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल|उच्चलं
उच्-चल, अम्, n. the mind, the understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलन|उच्चलनं
उच्-चलन, अम्, n. going off or out, moving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलित
उच्-चलित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone up or out, winnowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चि
उच्चि उच्-चि (उद्-चि), cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति, -नुते,<BR>-चेतुम्, to gather, collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चय|उच्चयः
उच्-चय, अस्, m. gathering, picking up from the<BR>ground; adding to, annumeration; collection, heap,<BR>plenty, multitude; the knot of the string or cloth<BR>which fastens the lower garments round the loins tied<BR>in front; the opposite side of a triangle.<BR>—उच्चया-<BR>पचय (˚य-अप्˚), औ, m. du. prosperity and decline,<BR>rise and fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिङ्गट|उच्चिंगटः|उच्चिङ्गटः
