उत्
उत् उत्, ind. a particle of doubt or delibera-<BR>tion = how, what (?), either, or; see 2. उत. (For<BR>the prep. उद् see 1. उद्, page 153.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत|उतं
उत 1. उत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वे), sewn,<BR>woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत|उतं
उत 2. उत, ind. (as a particle of doubt or<BR>deliberation) and, also, even, or. Often used for the<BR>sake of emphasis, especially at the end of a line after<BR>इति or a verb (e. g. सर्व-भूतानि तम् पार्थ सदा<BR>परिभवन्त्य् उत, all creatures, O king, certainly<BR>always despise him).<BR>(As an interrogative particle, generally at the begin-<BR>ning of the second or following part of a double in-<BR>terrogation) or, utrum-an (e. g. कथम् निर्णीयते<BR>किं स्यान् निष्कारणो बन्धुर् उत विश्वास-घा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">Page0147-c+ 73</a>]<BR>तकः, how can it be decided whether he be a friend<BR>without a motive or a violator of confidence ?). In<BR>this sense it may be strengthened by आहो (e. g. कच्चित्<BR>त्वम् असि मानुषी उताहो सुराङ्गना, art thou a<BR>mortal woman or divine ?), or by आहो-स्वित् (e. g.<BR>शालिहोत्रः किं नु स्याद् उताहोस्विद् राजा नलः,<BR>can it be Śālihotra or king Nala ?). Rarely किम् is<BR>repeated before उत used in this sense (e. g. किं नु<BR>स्वर्गात् प्राप्ता तस्या रूपेण किमुत अन्या आगता,<BR>has she arrived from heaven or has another come in<BR>her form ?).<BR>(As a particle of wishing, especially at the beginning<BR>of a sentence followed by a potential) would that!<BR>utinam! (e. g. उत अधीयीत, would that he would<BR>read!).<BR>(उत preceded by किम्) on the contrary, how<BR>much more, how much less (e. g. समर्थो ऽसि स-<BR>हस्रम् अपि जेतुं किमुत एकम्, thou art able to<BR>conquer even a thousand, how much more one ?).<BR>(उत preceded by प्रति) on the contrary, rather<BR>(e. g. एष पृष्टो ऽस्माभिर् न जल्पति हन्ति<BR>प्रत्युत पाषाणैः, this one questioned by us does<BR>not speak, but rather throws stones at us). उत वा,<BR>or else, and (e. g. समुद्राद् उत वा पुरीषात्, from<BR>the sea or from the moisture in the air); वा-उत<BR>वा or उताहो वापि-वा, either — or; उत-उत, both —<BR>and (e. g. उत बलवान् उत अबलः, both the strong<BR>and the weak); किम्-उत वा, whether — or else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतङ्क
उतङ्क उतङ्क, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—उतङ्क-मेघ, अस्, m. a kind of cloud named<BR>after that Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्य|उतथ्यः
उतथ्य उतथ्य, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Aṅgiras and elder brother of Bṛhaspati.<BR>—उतथ्य-<BR>तनय, अस्, m. an epithet of Gautama.<BR>—उतथ्या-<BR>नुज, अस्, m. or उतथ्यानुजन्मन् (˚य-अनु-ज˚),<BR>आ, m. a N. of Bṛhaspati, regent of the planet Jupiter<BR>(younger brother of Utathya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उताहो
उताहो उताहो, ind. (fr. 2. उत + आहो), a par-<BR>ticle of doubt or deliberation = either, or; see under<BR>2. उत above.<BR>—उताहो-स्वित्, see under 2. उत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतूल
उतूल उतूल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>also कुलूट or उलूट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क|उत्कः
उत्क उत्क, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. उद्), excited by<BR>the desire of obtaining anything; wishing for (with<BR>inf.), desirous of, longing for; regretting, sad, sor-<BR>rowful; absent, thinking of something else; (अस्), m.<BR>desire; opportunity, occasion.<BR>—उत्क-ता, f. a state of<BR>longing or regret; the plant Pothos Officinalis having<BR>aromatic seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्काय
उत्काय, nom. A. -यते, -यितुम्, to long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कच
उत्कच उत्-कच, अस्, आ, अम्, having the hairs<BR>erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कच्छा
उत्कच्छा उत्-कच्छा, f. a metre of six verses,<BR>each verse containing eleven syllabic instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कञ्चुक|उत्कंचुक
उत्कञ्चुक उत्-कञ्चुक, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>coat of mail, without bodice or jacket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कट|उत्कटं|उत्कटः
उत्कट उत्-कट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. उद्), ex-<BR>ceeding the usual measure, important; richly endowed<BR>with, abounding in; drunk, mad, furious; excessive,<BR>much; superior, high, proud, haughty; uneven;<BR>difficult; (अस्), m. fluid dropping from the temples<BR>of an elephant in rut; the plant Saccharum Sara, or<BR>a similar kind of grass; intoxication, pride; (आ), f.<BR>the plant Laurus Cassia; N. of a town; (अम्), n. the<BR>fragrant bark of Laurus Cassia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कटुकासन|उत्कटुकासनं
उत्कटुकासन उत्कटुकासन, अम्, n. sitting<BR>on the hams, squatting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कणिका
उत्कणिका उत्-कणिका, f. a raised particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठ|उत्कंठ|उत्कण्ठः
उत्कण्ठ 1. उत्-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>neck uplifted, on the point of doing anything; (अस्<BR>or आ), m. f. longing for a beloved person or thing;<BR>regretting, missing anything or person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठ|उत्कंठ|उत्कण्ठः
2. उत्कण्ठ, nom. A. उत्कण्ठते, -ठितुम्, to long<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-a" target="_blank">Page0148-a+ 67</a>]<BR>for, regret, sorrow, for: Caus. उत्कण्ठयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to excite longing, inspire with tender emotions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठित|उत्कंठित|उत्कण्ठितं
उत्कण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, regretting, wishing or sor-<BR>rowing for, distressed, sorrowful; (आ), f. a woman<BR>longing after her absent lover or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कन्द्
उत्कन्द् उत्-कन्द् (उद्-स्कन्द्), cl. 1. P. -कन्-<BR>दति, -कन्तुम्, to leap, jump over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कन्दक
उत्-कन्दक, अस्, m. a kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कन्धर|उत्कंधर|उत्कन्धरं
उत्कन्धर उत्-कन्धर, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the neck erect or uplifted; (अम्), n. bending back<BR>the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कम्प्|उत्कंप्
