उत्क्रम्
उत्क्रम् उत्-क्रम् (उद्-क्˚), cl. 1. P. A., 4. P.<BR>-क्रामति, -क्रमते, -क्राम्यति, -क्रमितुम्, to<BR>step up, go up, ascend; to step out, go out or away;<BR>to pass away, die; to go over; pass over; omit; not to<BR>notice; to neglect, transgress: Caus. P. -क्रमयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to go up or ascend: Desid. Ved.<BR>-चिक्रमिषति or -चिक्रमिष्यति, to wish to go up<BR>or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रम|उत्क्रमः
उत्-क्रम, अस्, m. going up or out; progressive<BR>increase; going astray, acting improperly, deviation,<BR>transgression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमण|उत्क्रमणं
