उत्क्रान्तिन्|उत्क्रांतिन्
उत्क्रान्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, passing, passing away, gone,<BR>departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्राम|उत्क्रामः
उत्-क्राम, अस्, m. going from or out, going above,<BR>surpassing, deviating from propriety, transgression;<BR>opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रामत्
उत्-क्रामत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going out, going over<BR>or above, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुश्
उत्क्रुश् उत्-क्रुश् (उद्-क्˚), cl. 1. P. -क्रोशति,<BR>-क्रोष्टुम्, to cry out, to call to (with acc.), ex-<BR>claim; proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुष्ट
उत्-क्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, crying, speaking out or<BR>aloud; (अम्), n. crying out, calling, exclaiming, con-<BR>versation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोश|उत्क्रोशः
उत्-क्रोश, अस्, m. clamour, outcry, proclamation;<BR>an osprey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोद|उत्क्रोदः
उत्क्रोद उत्-क्रोद, अस्, m. (fr. क्रुद् = कुर्द्<BR>with उद् ?), Ved. exultation (?); cf. उत्-कूर्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लिश्
उत्क्लिश् उत्-क्लिश् (उद्-क्˚), cl. 9. P. -क्लिश्नाति,<BR>-क्लेशितुम् or -क्लेष्टुम्, to feel uneasy, to be uncom-<BR>fortable or distressed: Caus. P. -क्लेशयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to excite, stir up, expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेश|उत्क्लेशः
उत्-क्लेश, अस्, m. excitement, disquietude; disorder<BR>or corruption of the humors (of the body); sickness,<BR>nausea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशक|उत्क्लेशकः
उत्-क्लेशक, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशन
उत्-क्लेशन, अस्, आ, अम्, or उत्-क्लेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>exciting, stirring up, causing disorder (e. g. कफोत्-<BR>क्लेशिन्, exciting phlegm).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेद|उत्क्लेदः
उत्क्लेद उत्-क्लेद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. क्लिद् with<BR>उद्), the becoming wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेदिन्
उत्-क्लेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wet, becoming moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्वथ्
उत्क्वथ् उत्-क्वथ् (उद्-क्˚), cl. 1. P. -क्वथति,<BR>-थितुम्, to boil out, extract by boiling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्
उत्क्षिप् उत्-क्षिप् (उद्-क्˚), cl. 6. P. A. -क्षि-<BR>पति, -ते, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw up, raise, set up, erect;<BR>to throw away, reject, get rid of, vomit up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्त|उत्क्षिप्तः
उत्-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown upwards, tossed,<BR>raised; thrown out, ejected; vomited; rejected, dis-<BR>missed; (अस्), m. the thorn apple (Datura Metel and<BR>Fastuosa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्तिका
उत्क्षिप्तिका, f. an ornament in the shape of a<BR>crescent worn in the upper part of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेप|उत्क्षेपः
उत्-क्षेप, अस्, m. throwing or tossing up; throw-<BR>ing away; sending, despatching; bringing up, vomit-<BR>ing; the region above the temples; N. of a country;<BR>also of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपक|उत्क्षेपकः
उत्-क्षेपक, अस्, आ, अम्, throwing, a thrower, who<BR>or what elevates or raises; one who sends or orders;<BR>(अस्), m. a stealer of clothes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपण|उत्क्षेपणं
उत्-क्षेपण, अम्, n. throwing upwards, tossing;<BR>sending, sending away; vomiting, taking up; a kind<BR>of basket or bowl used for cleaning corn; a fan; a<BR>measure of sixteen panas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खचित
उत्खचित उत्-खचित, अस्, आ, अम्, intermixed<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खन्
उत्खन् उत्-खन् (उद्-ख्˚), cl. 1. P. A. -ख-<BR>नति, -ते, -नितुम्, to dig up or out, to excavate; to<BR>tear out by the roots, root up; to draw or tear out;<BR>to destroy entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खात|उत्खातं
उत्-खात, अस्, आ, अम्, dug up; excavated, eradicated,<BR>pulled up by the roots; destroyed, annihilated; (अम्),<BR>n. a hole, a cavity, a deepening, uneven ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खातिन्
उत्खातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having cavities or holes, un-<BR>even; destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खरिन्
उत्खरिन् उत्-खरिन्, ई, m., N. of a deity;<BR>(a various reading has उत्कलि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खला
उत्खला उत्खला, f. (fr. उद् and खल?), a<BR>kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खिद्
उत्खिद् उत्-खिद् (उद्-ख्˚), cl. 6. P. -खिन्दति<BR>(Ved. -खिदति), -खेत्तुम्, to draw out, extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त|उत्तं
उत्त उत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, wet, moistened. See<BR>2. उद्, page 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंस|उत्तंसः
उत्तंस उत्-तंस, अस्, अम्, m. n. (rt. तंस्), an<BR>earring; a crest, a chaplet, a wreath worn on the<BR>crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसिक
उत्तंसिक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसित
उत्तंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, having earrings, crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तक्ष्
उत्तक्ष् उत्-तक्ष् (उद्-त्˚), cl. 1. 5. P., Ved.<BR>-तक्षति, -क्ष्णोति, -क्षितुम् or -तष्टुम्, to form<BR>(anything) out of any other thing; (Sāy.) to take<BR>(anything) out of any other thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तङ्ग
उत्तङ्ग उत्तङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a servant of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तट
उत्तट उत्-तट, अस्, आ, अम्, overflowing its<BR>banks (as a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तन्
उत्तन् उत्-तन् (उद्-त्˚), cl. 8. P. A. -तनोति,<BR>-नुते, -नितुम्, to stretch upwards, stretch out; en-<BR>deavour to rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्-तान, अस्, आ, अम्, stretched out, spread out,<BR>lying on the back, sleeping supinely or with the face<BR>upwards; upright; turned so that the mouth or<BR>opening is uppermost (as a vessel), concave; spread-<BR>ing out over the surface; shallow; open.<BR>—उत्तान-<BR>कूर्मक, अम्, n. a particular posture in sitting.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तान-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. a species of Ricinus.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तान-पद्, f., Ved. one whose legs are extended (in<BR>parturition or creation); epithet of a peculiar creative<BR>agency described in Ṛg-veda X. 72; (Sāy.) vegetation,<BR>the whole creation of upward-germinating plants.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तान-पर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having extended leaves.<BR>—उत्तान-पाद, अस्, m. the star ß in the little bear,<BR>personified as son of Vīra or Manu Svāyambhuva and<BR>father of Dhruva, the polar-star.<BR>—उत्तानपाद-ज,<BR>अस्, m. a N. of Dhruva or the polar-star.<BR>—उत्तान-<BR>बर्हिस्, इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—उत्तान-शय, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">Page0149-b+ 78</a>]<BR>आ, अम्, lying on the back, sleeping with the face up-<BR>wards; (अस्, आ), m. f. a little child.<BR>—उत्तान-शीवन्,<BR>आ, अरी, अ, Ved. lying extended, stagnant.<BR>—उत्तान-<BR>हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the hands extended,<BR>extending them in prayer; (औ), m. du. the two<BR>hands with the fingers stretched out, but with the<BR>backs towards the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानक|उत्तानकः
उत्तानक, अस्, m. a species of Cyperus grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानिका
उत्तानिका, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्
उत्तप् उत्-तप् (उद्-त्˚), cl. 1. P. rarely A.<BR>-तपति, -ते, -प्तुम्, to make warm or hot, to heat<BR>thoroughly; to pain, torment; to excite, urge on,<BR>press hard: Caus. P. -तापयति, -यितुम्, to warm<BR>up, heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्त|उत्तप्तं|उत्तप्तः
उत्-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt, seared; bathed, washed;<BR>anxious, excited; (अम्), n. dried flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताप|उत्तापः
उत्-ताप, अस्, m. great heat, affliction, distress,<BR>anxiety, excitement, ardour, effort, energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापित
उत्-तापित, अस्, आ, अम्, heated, made hot, pained,<BR>distressed, roused, excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्
उत्तम् उत्-तम् (उद्-त्˚), cl. 4. P. -ताम्यति,<BR>-तमितुम्, to be distressed, to lose heart, to faint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम|उत्तमः
उत्तम उत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम् (superlative fr. 1. उद्;<BR>opposed to अवम, अधम, &c.; cf. अन्-उत्तम),<BR>uppermost, highest, chief; most elevated, principal;<BR>best, excellent (often at the end of compounds, e. g.<BR>द्विजोत्तमस्, best of the twice-born); first, greatest;<BR>the highest (tone); the most removed or last in place,<BR>order, or time; (अम्), ind. most, in the highest de-<BR>gree; (अस्), m. the last person (= in European gram-<BR>mars the first person); N. of a brother of Dhruva,<BR>son of Uttāna-pāda and nephew of Priya-vrata; a<BR>son of Priya-vrata and third Manu; the twenty-first<BR>Vyāsa; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. a kind<BR>of piḍakā or pustule; the plant Oxystelma Esculentum<BR>(Asclepias Rosea Roxb.); an excellent woman, one<BR>who is handsome, healthy, and affectionate.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तम-गन्धाढ्य (˚ध-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing abundantly the most delicate scent or delicious<BR>fragrance.<BR>—उत्तम-ता, f. or उत्तम-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>excellence, superiority; goodness, good quality.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तम-पद, अम्, n. a high office.<BR>—उत्तम-पुरु-<BR>ष or उत्तम-पूरुष, अस्, m. the last person in<BR>verbal conjugation, i. e. I, we two, we (= in European<BR>grammars the first person, our third person being re-<BR>garded in Hindū grammars as the प्रथम-पुरुष,<BR>q. v.; cf. also मध्यम-पुरुष); the supreme<BR>spirit; an excellent man.<BR>—उत्तम-फलिनी, f. the<BR>plant Oxystelma Esculentum (Asclepias Rosea Roxb.).<BR>—उत्तमर्ण (˚म-ऋण), अस्, m. a creditor; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—उत्तमर्णिक, अस्, m. a<BR>creditor.<BR>—उत्तमर्णिन्, ई, m. a creditor.<BR>—उत्तम-<BR>लाभ, अस्, m. great profit, a double return.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तम-वेश, अस्, m. ‘having the most excellent dress,’<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>—उत्तम-शाख, अस्, m., N. of a region.<BR>—उत्तम-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. intriguing with another<BR>man's wife, addressing her privately, casting amorous<BR>looks &c.<BR>—उत्तम-साहस, अम्, n. the highest of<BR>the three fixed mulcts or fines; a fine of 1000 or of<BR>80,000 paṇas; capital punishment, branding, banish-<BR>ment, confiscation, mutilation, and death.<BR>—उत्तम-<BR>सुख, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उत्तमाङ्ग (˚म-<BR>अङ्˚), अम्, n. the highest or chief part of the body,<BR>the head.<BR>—उत्तमाधम (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>high and low.<BR>—उत्तमाधम-मध्यम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, good, bad, and indifferent; high, low, and<BR>middling.<BR>—उत्तमारणी (˚म-अर्˚), f. the plant As-<BR>paragus Racemosus.<BR>—उत्तमार्ध (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the last half or part; the best half.<BR>—उत्तमार्ध्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or connected with the last part<BR>or the best half.<BR>—उत्तमाह (˚म-अह्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>last or latest day, a fine day (?), a lucky day (?).<BR>—उत्-<BR>तमोपपद (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one to whom<BR>the best term is applicable, best, good.<BR>—उत्तमौजस्<BR>(˚म-ओज्˚), आस्, m. ‘of excellent valour,’ N. of one of<BR>the warriors of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाय्य
उत्तमाय्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fut. pass. part. fr. a nom.<BR>उत्तमाय ?), Ved. to be raised or celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमीय
उत्तमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, uppermost, highest, chief,<BR>best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर|उत्तरं|उत्तरः
1. उत्-तर, अस्, आ, अम् (comparative fr. 1. उद्; opposed<BR>to अधर; declined Gram. 238. a), upper, higher,<BR>superior (e. g. उत्तरे दन्तास्, the upper teeth);<BR>northern (because the northern part of India is high);<BR>left (opposed to दक्षिण or right, because in pray-<BR>ing the face being turned to the east the north would<BR>be on the left-hand); later, following, subsequent,<BR>latter, concluding, posterior, future (opposed to पूर्व,<BR>&c., e. g. उत्तरः कालः, future time; उत्तरं<BR>वाक्यम्, a following speech, answer, reply; फलम्<BR>उत्तरम्, subsequent result, future consequence;<BR>वर्षोत्तरेषु, in future years); superior, chief,<BR>excellent, dominant, predominant, more powerful;<BR>better, more excellent; (अस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Virāṭa; a king of the Nāgas; N. of a mountain;<BR>(आ), f. the north (i. e. the northern दिश् or quarter);<BR>N. of a daughter of Virāṭa and daughter-in-law of<BR>Arjuna; (अम्), n. upper surface or cover; the north;<BR>the following member, the last part of a compound;<BR>answer, reply; (in law) a defence, a rejoinder; (in<BR>the Mimāṃsā philosophy) the answer, the fourth<BR>member of an adhikaraṇa or case; superiority, ex-<BR>cellence, competency; result, the chief or prevalent<BR>result or characteristic, what remains or is left, con-<BR>clusion, remainder, excess, over and above, (often<BR>at the end of a compound, e. g. षष्ट्युत्तरं<BR>सहस्रम्, one thousand with an excess of sixty, i. e.<BR>1060; सप्तोत्तरं शतम्, 107; भयोत्तर, at-<BR>tended with danger, having danger as the result;<BR>धर्मोत्तर, chiefly characterized by virtue); re-<BR>mainder, difference (in arithmetic); N. of a song;<BR>(अम्), ind. at the conclusion, at the end, e. g. भवद्-<BR>उत्तरम्, with the word ‘bhavad’ at the end; अस्रोत्-<BR>तरम् ईक्षिता, looked at with tears at the end, i. e.<BR>with a glance ending in tears; [cf. Gr. ὕστερος.]<BR>—उत्तर-काण्ड, अम्, n. following or concluding<BR>book; the seventh book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>काय, अस्, m. the upper part of the body.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>काल, अस्, m. future time; time reckoned from full<BR>moon to full moon.<BR>—उत्तर-कुरु, उस् or उ, m. n. one<BR>of the nine divisions of the world, the country of the<BR>northern Kurus, situated in the north of India, and<BR>described as the country of eternal beatitude.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तर-कोशला, f. the city Ayodhyā, the modern Oude.<BR>—उत्तर-क्रिया, f. the last sacred action, funeral<BR>rites, obsequies.<BR>—उत्तर-खण्ड, अम्, n. last section;<BR>the concluding book of the Padma-purāṇa, also of the<BR>Śiva-purāṇa.<BR>—उत्तर-खण्डन, अम्, n. cutting off<BR>a reply, refutation.<BR>—उत्तर-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. title of<BR>a supplement of the Yoni-grantha.<BR>—१. उत्तरङ्-ग,<BR>अम्, n. a wooden arch surmounting the door frame.<BR>—उत्तर-च्छद, अस्, m. a cover, what is thrown<BR>over anything.<BR>—उत्तर-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born in the<BR>latter (or last-mentioned kind of wedlock); born<BR>subsequently or afterwards, posterity.<BR>—उत्तर-ज्या,<BR>f. the versed sine of an arc, or rather the second half<BR>of the chord halved by the versed sine.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>ज्योतिष, अम्, n., N. of a country.<BR>—उत्तर-तन्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. ‘concluding doctrine,’ N. of a supplementary<BR>section in the medical manual of Suśruta.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम् (compar. fr. उत्तर), still further<BR>removed, still more distant, still higher.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>तस्, ind. at the top, above, from the north, north-<BR>ward, to the left (opposed to दक्षिण-तस्); after-<BR>wards; behind.<BR>—उत्तरतः-पश्चात्, ind. north-<BR>westward (with gen.).<BR>—उत्तर-तापनीय, title of<BR>the second part of the Nṛsiṃha-tāpanīyopaniṣad.<BR>—उत्तर-त्र, ind. in what follows, after, subse-<BR>quently, later, further on, beyond, below (in a work),<BR>northward; (पूर्वत्र उत्तरत्र, in the first case or<BR>place — in the second.)<BR>—उत्तर-दायक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>replying, giving an answer, impertinent.<BR>—उत्तरदिक्-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated in the north, northern.<BR>—उत्तर-दिश्, क्, f. the north quarter.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>देश, अस्, m. the country towards the north, the up-<BR>country.<BR>—उत्तर-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done<BR>subsequently.<BR>—उत्तर-पक्ष, अस्, m. the northern<BR>or left wing (side); second or following part of an<BR>argument, the reason प्रो, the reply, refutation;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-a" target="_blank">Page0150-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the answer to the first or objectionable argument, the<BR>right argument, demonstrated truth, or conclusion; the<BR>minor proposition in a syllogism.<BR>—उत्तरपक्ष-<BR>ता, f. or उत्तरपक्ष-त्व, अम्, n. conclusion, de-<BR>monstration, reply.<BR>—उत्तर-पट, अस्, m. an upper<BR>garment.<BR>—उत्तर-पथ, अस्, m. the northern way,<BR>the way leading to the north.<BR>—उत्तरपथिक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, inhabiting the northern country.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तर-पद, अम्, n. the last member of a com-<BR>pound word.<BR>—उत्तरपदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or उत्तर-<BR>पदकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or studying the<BR>last word or term.<BR>—उत्तर-पर्वत, अस्, m. the<BR>northern mountain.<BR>—उत्तर-पश्चार्ध (˚च-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the north-western half.<BR>—उत्तर-पश्चिम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, north-western; (आ), f. the north-west<BR>(scil. दिश्).<BR>—उत्तर-पाद, अस्, m. a division of legal<BR>practice, that part which relates to the reply or de-<BR>fence, four divisions being admitted in every suit.<BR>—उत्तर-पुरस्तात्, ind. north-eastward (with gen.).<BR>—उत्तर-पुरुष, अस्, m. = उत्तम-पुरुष (?).<BR>—उत्तर-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, north-eastward; one who<BR>takes the north for the east.<BR>—उत्तर-प्रच्छद,<BR>अस्, m. a coverlid, a quilt.<BR>—उत्तर-प्रत्युत्तर,<BR>अम्, n. a dispute, an altercation, a discussion; the<BR>pleadings in a law-suit.<BR>—उत्तर-फल्गुनी or उत्त-<BR>र-फाल्गुनी, f. the twelfth lunar mansion, containing<BR>two stars, figured by a bed.<BR>—उत्तर-भाद्रपद्, त्,<BR>f. or उत्तर-भाद्रपदा, f. the twenty-sixth lunar<BR>mansion, figured by a couch, and comprehending two<BR>stars, of which one is अ Andromedæ.<BR>—उत्तर-मति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उत्तर-मन्द्रा, f. a loud but<BR>slow manner of singing.<BR>—उत्तर-मात्र, अम्, n. a<BR>mere reply, even a reply.<BR>—उत्तर-मानस, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—उत्तर-मीमांसा, f. the Vedānta<BR>philosophy, an inquiry into the Jñāna-kāṇḍa or second<BR>portion of the Veda (opposed to पूर्व-मीमांसा;<BR>see मीमांसा).<BR>—उत्तर-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid<BR>of reply, having no answer.<BR>—उत्तर-राम-चरित or<BR>-चरित्र, अम्, n. ‘the further or later deeds of Rāma,’<BR>title of a drama of Bhavabhūti.<BR>—उत्तर-लक्षण,<BR>अम्, n. the indication of an actual reply; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>marked on the left side.<BR>—उत्तर-लोमन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>having the hairs turned upwards or outwards.<BR>—उत्तर-<BR>वयस, अम्, n. the latter or declining years of life.<BR>—उत्तर-वल्ली, f. title of the second section of the<BR>Kāṭhakopaniṣad when divided into two Adhyāyas.<BR>—उत्तर-वस्ति, इस्, f. a small syringe, a urethra<BR>injection pipe.<BR>—उत्तर-वस्त्र, अम्, n. an upper<BR>garment.<BR>—उत्तर-वादिन्, ई, m. a replicant; a de-<BR>fendant; one whose claims are of later date than<BR>another's.<BR>—उत्तर-वासस्, अस्, n. an upper garment.<BR>—उत्तर-वेदि, इस् or ई, f., Ved. the northern altar<BR>made for the sacred fire.<BR>—उत्तर-सक्थ, अम्, n.<BR>the left thigh.<BR>—उत्तर-सञ्ज्ञित, अस्, आ, अम्, desig-<BR>nated in the reply (a witness &c.); hear-say evidence,<BR>see the next.<BR>—उत्तर-साक्षिन्, ई, m. witness for the<BR>defence; a witness testifying from the report of others.<BR>—उत्तर-साधक, अस्, आ, अम्, finishing what re-<BR>mains or follows, assisting at a ceremony, befriending;<BR>an assistant, a helper, a friend; who or what establishes<BR>a reply.<BR>—उत्तर-हनु, उस्, m., Ved. the upper jaw-<BR>bone.<BR>—उत्तराधर (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, superior<BR>and inferior, higher and lower; (अम्), n. the upper<BR>and under lip; the lips; see अधरोत्तर.<BR>—उत्तरा-<BR>धिकार (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m. right to property &c.<BR>in succession to another person, heirship, inheritance.<BR>—उत्तराधिकारि-ता, f. or उत्तराधिकारि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. right of succession.<BR>—उत्तराधिकारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>an heir or claimant subsequent to the death of the<BR>original owner, an heir who claims as the second<BR>in succession.<BR>—उत्तरान्वित (˚रा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>accompanied by Uttarā.<BR>—उत्तरा-पथ, अम्, n. the<BR>northern road or direction, the northern country,<BR>north.<BR>—उत्तराभास (˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, m. a false,<BR>indirect or prevaricating reply.<BR>—उत्तराभास-ता, f.<BR>or उत्तराभास-त्व, अम्, n. inadequacy of a reply,<BR>the semblance without the reality.<BR>—उत्तरायण<BR>(˚र-अय्˚), अम्, n. the progress (of the sun) to the<BR>north; the period of the sun's progress to the north<BR>of the equator, the summer solstice.<BR>—उत्तरारणि<BR>(˚र-अर्˚), इस् or ई, m. f. the upper अरणि (q. v.) which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">Page0150-b+ 75</a>]<BR>by cutting becomes the प्रमन्थ or churner.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तरार्थ (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, for the sake of what<BR>follows.<BR>—उत्तरार्ध (˚र-अर्˚), अम्, n. the upper<BR>part (of the body); the northern part; the latter<BR>half; the further end.<BR>—उत्तरार्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. being on the northern side.<BR>—उत्तरा-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. victorious, overpowering.<BR>—उत्तराशा<BR>(˚र-आशा), f. the northern quarter, the north.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तराशाधिपति (˚शा-अध्˚) or उत्तराशा-पति, इस्,<BR>m. the regent of the northern quarter, an epithet of<BR>Kuvera.<BR>—उत्तराश्मन् (˚र-अश्˚), आ, m., N. of a<BR>rocky river in the north.<BR>—उत्तराषाढा (˚र-अष्˚),<BR>f. the twenty-first of the lunar mansions, figured by<BR>an elephant's tooth or a bed, and containing two stars,<BR>one of which is ß in Sagittarius.<BR>—उत्तरासङ्ग<BR>(˚र-आस्˚), अस्, m. an upper or outer garment.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तराह (˚र-अह्˚), अस्, m. the following day.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तरेतरा (˚र-इत्˚), f. the southern quarter.<BR>—उत्-<BR>तरोत्तर (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, more and more,<BR>higher and higher, further and further; always in-<BR>creasing, always following; (अम्), ind. higher and<BR>higher, more and more, in constant continuation,<BR>one on the other; (अम्), n. reply to an answer, reply<BR>on reply; conversation; a rejoinder; excess, exceed-<BR>ing quantity or degree; succession, gradation; de-<BR>scending.<BR>—उत्तरोत्तरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, constantly in-<BR>creasing; one following the other.<BR>—उत्तरोष्ठ or<BR>उत्तरौष्ठ (˚र-ओष्˚), अस्, m. the upper lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरम्
उत्तरम्, ind. further on, forward; hereafter, in<BR>the following part (of a book).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरा
उत्तरा, ind. north, northerly, northward (with<BR>gen. or abl.).<BR>—उत्तरा-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. seated north-<BR>ward or on the left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरात्
उत्तरात्, ind. from the left, from the north, north-<BR>ward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरात्तात्
उत्तरात्तात्, ind., Ved. from the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराहि
उत्तराहि, ind. northerly, from the north (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरिन्
उत्तरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीय|उत्तरीयं
उत्तरीय or उत्तरीयक, अम्, n. an upper or outer<BR>garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेण
