उत्पीड|उत्पीडः
उत्-पीड, अस्, m. pressing out, pressure; foam,<BR>froth, a gush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीडन|उत्पीडनं
उत्-पीडन, अम्, n. the act of pressing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुच्छय
उत्पुच्छय उत्-पुच्छय, nom. (fr. उद्-पुच्छ)<BR>A. उत्पुच्छयते, to raise or cock the tail; P. -यति,<BR>to make one raise the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुटक|उत्पुटकः
उत्पुटक उत्-पुटक, अस्, m. a disease of the<BR>external ear; [cf. उत्-पाट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुलक
उत्पुलक उत्-पुलक, अस्, आ, अम्, joyful, de-<BR>lighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पू
उत्पू उत्-पू (उद्-पू), cl. 9. P. A. -पुनाति,<BR>-पुनीते, -पवितुम्, to cleanse, purify; to extract<BR>anything that has been purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवन|उत्पवनं
उत्-पवन, अम्, n. cleaning, cleansing; straining<BR>liquids for domestic or religious uses; any implement<BR>for cleaning; the act of sprinkling clarified butter or<BR>other fluids on the sacrificial fire with two blades of<BR>Kuśa grass, the ends of which are held in either hand<BR>and the centre dipped into the liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवितृ
उत्-पवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, purifying; a purifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाव|उत्पावः
उत्-पाव, अस्, m. purifying ghee &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पोषध
उत्पोषध उत्-पोषध, अस्, m., N. of an old<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रभ|उत्प्रभः
उत्प्रभ उत्-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, flashing forth<BR>or diffusing light, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रसव|उत्प्रसवः
उत्प्रसव उत्-प्रसव, अस्, m. abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रास|उत्प्रासः
उत्प्रास उत्-प्रास, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. अस् with<BR>प्र and उद्), hurling, throwing afar; violent burst<BR>of laughter; ridicule, derision; excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासन|उत्प्रासनं
उत्-प्रासन, अम्, n. = the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रुष्
उत्प्रुष् उत्-प्रुष्, ट्, f., Ved. that which bub-<BR>bles up, a bubble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्ष्
उत्प्रेक्ष् उत्-प्रेक्ष् (उद्-प्र-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-प्रेक्षते, -षितुम्, to look up to with attention<BR>(as a pupil to his teacher); to perceive; to transfer<BR>(with loc.); to compare one thing with another,<BR>illustrate by a simile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षण|उत्प्रेक्षणं
उत्-प्रेक्षण, अम्, n. looking into, perceiving,<BR>foreseeing, comparing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षा
उत्-प्रेक्षा, f. overlooking, disregarding, careless-<BR>ness, indifference; (in rhetoric) comparison in general,<BR>simile, illustration, metaphor; a parable; an ironical<BR>comparison.<BR>—उत्प्रेक्षा-वल्लभ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षित
उत्-प्रेक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, compared (as in a simile).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्ष्य
उत्-प्रेक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, that with which anything<BR>is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लु
उत्प्लु उत्-प्लु (उद्-प्˚), cl. 1. A. -प्लवते,<BR>-प्लोतुम्, to jump up, leap up; to bound; to spring<BR>or jump upon; to float upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लव|उत्प्लवः
उत्-प्लव, अस्, m. a jump, leap, bound; (आ), f. a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवन|उत्प्लवनं
उत्-प्लवन, अम्, n. jumping or leaping up, spring-<BR>ing upon; skimming off impure oil or ghee, or any<BR>dirt floating on a fluid, by passing a blade of Kuśa<BR>grass over it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुत
उत्-प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, jumped up or upon, sprung<BR>upon suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुत्य
उत्-प्लुत्य, ind. having sprung up or jumped upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फल्
उत्फल् उत्-फल् (उद्-फ्˚), cl. 1. P. -फलति,<BR>-लितुम्, to spring; to part asunder, to expand (as a<BR>flower): Caus. P. -फालयति, -यितुम्, to open,<BR>open wide, cause to expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फाल|उत्फालः
उत्-फाल, अस्, m. a jump, a spring, leaping up or<BR>out of, moving or shuffling of feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुल्ल|उत्फुल्लः
उत्-फुल्ल, अस्, आ, अम् (फुल्ल pass. part. of rt.<BR>फल्), widely opened (as the eyes); blown as a<BR>flower; swollen, increased in bulk; sleeping supinely;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फल|उत्फलं
उत्फल उत्-फल, अम्, n. excellent fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स|उत्सः
उत्स उत्स, अस्, m. (fr. 2 उद्), Ved. a spring,<BR>a fountain (metaphorically applied to the clouds).<BR>—उत्स-धि, इस्, m., Ved. the receptacle of a spring, a<BR>well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सक्थ
उत्सक्थ उत्-सक्थ, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. opening<BR>the thighs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्ग|उत्संग|उत्संगः|उत्सङ्गः
उत्सङ्ग उत्-सङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सञ्ज् with<BR>उद्), embrace, association, union; slope, side; the<BR>haunch or part above the hip; the lap; the acclivity<BR>or edge of a hill; the roof of a house; the bottom<BR>or deep part of an ulcer; a high number = 100<BR>Vivāhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गित|उत्संगित
उत्-सङ्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, associated, combined, joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गिन्|उत्संगिन्
उत्-सङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, associating or combining with,<BR>an associate, a partner; deep-seated, as an ulcer; (ई),<BR>m. an ulcer, a deep sore; (इनी), f. pimples on the<BR>inner edge of the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सञ्जन|उत्संजन|उत्संजनं
उत्-सञ्जन, अम्, n. leading upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सद्
उत्सद् उत्-सद् (उद्-स्˚), cl. 1. P. -सीदति, -सत्-<BR>तुम्, to sink, settle down, fall into ruin or decay; to<BR>leave off; to rise up: Caus. P. -सादयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to destroy, overturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सन्न
उत्-सन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, decayed, in ruins; destroyed,<BR>overturned; disused, fallen into disuse; risen, in-<BR>creased.<BR>—उत्सन्न-धर्म, अस्, or उत्सन्न-यज्ञ,<BR>अस्, m. an interrupted or suspended sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साद|उत्सादः
उत्-साद, अस्, m., Ved. a particular part of the<BR>sacrificial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादक
उत्-सादक, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, overturning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादन|उत्सादनं
उत्-सादन, अम्, n. destroying, overturning; sus-<BR>pending, interrupting, omitting; cleaning the person<BR>with perfumes, rubbing or chafing the limbs; healing<BR>a sore, causing it to fill up; going up, ascending,<BR>rising; raising, elevating; ploughing a field twice or<BR>thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनीय
उत्-सादनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed; to be<BR>effected; to be gone up or ascended; (अम्), n. any<BR>application to a sore producing granulations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादित|उत्सादितं
उत्-सादित, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed, overturned;<BR>cleansed, purified with oil, perfumes, &c.; risen, as-<BR>cended; raised, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादितव्य
उत्-सादितव्य or उत्-साद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be de-<BR>stroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर|उत्सरः
उत्सर, उत्सारक, &c. See under उत्-सृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्ग|उत्सर्गः
उत्सर्ग उत्-सर्ग. See under उत्-सृज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सव|उत्सवः
उत्सव उत्सव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. सु with उद्?),<BR>enterprise, beginning; a festival, a jubilee; joy, glad-<BR>ness; merry-making; height, elevation, insolence;<BR>passion, wrath; wish; rising of a wish; a section of a<BR>book.<BR>—उत्सव-सङ्केत, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सह्
उत्सह् उत्-सह् (उद्-स्˚), cl. 1. A. -सहते,<BR>-सहितुम् or -सोढुम्, to be able, to be adequate,<BR>to have power (with inf., or with dat. of an abstract<BR>noun); to act with courage or energy: Caus. -साह-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to animate, encourage, excite; Desid.<BR>of the Caus. -सिसाहयिषति, to wish to excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साह|उत्साहः
उत्-साह, अस्, m. power, strength, strength of will,<BR>resolution; effort, perseverance, strenuous and con-<BR>tinued exertion, energy; firmness, fortitude; hap-<BR>piness; a thread.<BR>—उत्साह-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, active,<BR>energetic, persevering.<BR>—उत्साह-वर्धन, अस्, m. the<BR>heroic रस or feeling; (अम्), n. increase of energy,<BR>heroism.<BR>—उत्साह-सम्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, active,<BR>persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहन|उत्साहनं
उत्-साहन, अम्, n. effort, perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहिन्
उत्साहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, active, persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिच्
उत्सिच् उत्-सिच् (उद्-स्˚), cl. 6. P. A. -सिञ्चति,<BR>-ते, -सेक्तुम्, to sprinkle, pour, to spread; to make<BR>proud: Pass. -सिच्यते, to spout or foam up or over;<BR>to be puffed up; to overflow, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिक्त|उत्सिक्तः
उत्-सिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled; flooded, abun-<BR>dantly furnished; elevated, raised, haughty, proud,<BR>rude; enlarged, increased; disordered, disturbed in<BR>mind &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिच्यमान|उत्सिच्यमानः
उत्-सिच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, foaming or spouting<BR>up, showering; increasing, overflowing, growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेक|उत्सेकः
उत्-सेक, अस्, m. sprinkling, pouring; foaming up-<BR>wards, spouting out or over, showering; overflow,<BR>increase, enlargement; haughtiness, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेकिन्
उत्सेकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, overflowing; proud, haughty,<BR>puffed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेचन|उत्सेचनं
उत्-सेचन, अम्, n. the act of showering or spout-<BR>ing upwards, boiling or foaming over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुक|उत्सुकः
उत्सुक उत्सुक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. उद् and सुक;<BR>the latter does not exist separately, but may be derived<BR>from the particle सु, as अनुक fr. अनु, अभिक<BR>fr. अभि; cf. also उत्क), restless, uneasy, unquiet,<BR>anxious; anxiously desirous, zealously active, striving<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">Page0152-c+ 76</a>]<BR>or making exertions for any object (e. g. जयोत्सुक,<BR>anxiously striving for victory); eager for, fond of, at-<BR>tached to; regretting, repining, missing, sorrowing<BR>for; (अस्), m. (?) longing for.<BR>—उत्सुक-ता, f. or<BR>उत्सुक-त्व, अम्, n. restlessness, uneasiness, unquiet-<BR>ness, zeal; attachment, affection; sorrow, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकाय
उत्सुकाय, nom. A. उत्सुकायते, to become un-<BR>quiet &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूत्र
उत्सूत्र उत्-सूत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, unstrung; irre-<BR>gular, out of rule, loose, detached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूर|उत्सूरः
उत्सूर उत्-सूर, अस्, m. evening, twilight<BR>(when the sun sets).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूर्य
उत्सूर्य. See under ओत्सूर्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृ
उत्सृ उत्-सृ (उद्-सृ), Caus. P. -सारयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to expel, turn out, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर|उत्सरः
उत्-सर, अस्, m. a species of the Ati-śakvarī metre,<BR>consisting of four verses of fifteen syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्या|उत्सर्य्या
उत्-सर्या, f. a cow when grown up and fit to take<BR>the bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारक|उत्सारकः
उत्-सारक, अस्, m. one who drives away the mob<BR>from a person of rank, a policeman; a guard, a<BR>guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारण|उत्सारणं
उत्-सारण, अम्, n. moving, causing to move, re-<BR>moving, keeping at a distance, driving out of the<BR>way; assisting any one to step out (of a palanquin<BR>&c.); reception of a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृज्
उत्सृज् उत्-सृज् (उद्-स्˚), cl. 6. P. -सृजति,<BR>-स्रष्टुम्, to pour out, emit, send forth; to let<BR>loose; to cast forth or away; to lay aside, quit, leave,<BR>abandon, avoid, eschew; to abolish (a rule &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्ग|उत्सर्गः
उत्-सर्ग, अस्, m. pouring out, pouring forth, emis-<BR>sion, dejection, excretion, voiding by stool &c.;<BR>laying aside, abandoning, resigning, quitting, retiring<BR>from, suspending; loosening, delivering; oblation,<BR>libation; presentation of anything promised to a<BR>god or Brāhman with suitable ceremonies; giving,<BR>donation; a particular ceremony on suspending a<BR>Vedic lecture; (in gram.) any general precept or<BR>rule (opposed to अपवाद, special rule or exception,<BR>and so called because only abolished in express cases<BR>by a substitute).<BR>—उत्सर्ग-तस्, ind. generally, i. e.<BR>without any special limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गिन्
उत्सर्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, leaving out or off; omitting,<BR>abandoning, quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्जन|उत्सर्जनं
उत्-सर्जन, अम्, n. letting loose, abandoning,<BR>leaving, &c.; gift, donation, oblation; suspending (a<BR>lecture in the Veda), a ceremony connected with it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिसृक्षु
उत्-सिसृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृज्य
उत्-सृज्य, ind. having abandoned, having quitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्ट|उत्सृष्टः
उत्-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, left, abandoned; given<BR>up, given, presented; poured forth, cast into or upon.<BR>—उत्सृष्ट-पशु, उस्, m. a bull set at liberty upon<BR>particular occasions, as on a marriage &c., and allowed<BR>to go about at will.<BR>—उत्सृष्ट-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one<BR>who has let fall, who has shed (a tear &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टि|उत्सृष्टिः
उत्-सृष्टि, इस्, f. abandonment, letting go, emission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्रष्टुकाम
उत्स्रष्टु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to let go or<BR>put down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृप्
उत्सृप् उत्-सृप् (उद्-स्˚), cl. 1. P. -सर्पति,<BR>-सर्प्तुम् or -स्रप्तुम्, to go, glide or soar upwards,<BR>to spread out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प|उत्सर्पः|उत्सर्प्प
उत्-सर्प, अस्, m. going or gliding upwards; swell-<BR>ing, heaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पण|उत्सर्पणं|उत्सर्प्पण
उत्-सर्पण, अम्, n. gliding upwards; swelling,<BR>heaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पित|उत्सर्प्पित
उत्-सर्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, gliding or going upwards;<BR>heaving, heaved, undulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पिन्|उत्सर्प्पिन्
उत्-सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, moving or gliding upwards;<BR>rising; soaring; (इणी), f. a Jaina division of time, a<BR>long period described as ten crores of crores of oceans<BR>of years; this period alternates with one of similar<BR>duration. See अव-सर्पिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेध|उत्सेधः
उत्सेध उत्-सेध, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. सिध् with<BR>उद्), height, elevation; thickness, fatness, obesity;<BR>intumescence; excelling, sublimity; the body; (अम्),<BR>n. killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्थल
उत्स्थल उत्-स्थल, अम्, n., N. of an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मि
उत्स्मि उत्-स्मि (उद्-स्˚), cl. 1. A. -स्मयते,<BR>-स्मेतुम्, to smile at, deride: Caus. P. -स्माययति,<BR>-यितुम्, to make a fool of one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मय|उत्स्मयः
उत्-स्मय, अस्, m. a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मयत्
उत्-स्मयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्य
उत्स्य उत्स्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. उत्स), Ved. coming<BR>from a well or fountain (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्वप्नाय
उत्स्वप्नाय उत्स्वप्नाय, nom. (fr. उद्-स्वप्न)<BR>A. उत्स्वप्नायते, to talk in one's sleep; to dream<BR>uneasily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् 1. उद्, a particle and prefix to verbs<BR>and nouns. (As implying superiority in place, rank,<BR>station, or power) up, upwards; upon, on; over,<BR>above. (As implying separation and disjunction)<BR>out, out of, from, off, away from, apart. (According<BR>to native authorities उद् may also imply publicity,<BR>pride, indisposition, weakness, helplessness, binding,<BR>loosing, existence, acquisition.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् is not used as a separable adverb or preposition;<BR>in those rare cases, in which it appears in the Veda<BR>uncompounded with a verb, the latter has to be sup-<BR>plied from the context (e. g. उद् उत्सम् शतधारम्,<BR>out (pour) a fountain of a hundred streams).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् is sometimes repeated in the Veda to fill out<BR>the verse (e. g. किं न उद् उद् उ हर्षसे).<BR>[Cf. Zend उश्; Hib. uas and in composition os,<BR>ois, e. g. os-car, ‘a leap, bound,’ &c. See also उत्-<BR>तम, 1. उत्-तर, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् 2. उद् or उन्द्, cl. 7. P. उनत्ति, उन्दाञ्-<BR>चकार, उन्दिष्यति, औन्दीत्, उन्दितुम्, to<BR>flow or issue out, to spring (said of water); to wet,<BR>bathe: Caus. उन्दयति, aor. औन्दिदत्: Desid. उन्दि-<BR>दिषति; [cf. Gr. ὕδωρ Lat. unda; Goth. vato;<BR>Lit. wandū́.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद|उदं
उद, अम्, n. (only at the beginning or end of a<BR>compound) water.<BR>—उद-कीर्ण or उद-कीर्य, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Galedupa Piscidia, the bark of which is<BR>rubbed and scattered into water to stun the fishes.<BR>—उद-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a water-jar, a jar with water.<BR>—उद-ग्राभ, अस्, m., Ved. holding water.<BR>—उद-<BR>चमस, अस्, m. a cup containing water.<BR>—१. उद-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see उद्-अज् 3rd col.), aquatic, watery,<BR>produced in or by water.<BR>—उद-ज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—उद-धान, अस्, आ, अम्, containing water.<BR>—उध-धि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. containing water; (इस्),<BR>m. a water-jar, a reservoir for water; a cloud; a<BR>lake; the ocean.<BR>—उदधि-कुमार, आस्, m. pl. a<BR>class of divinities, belonging to the Bhavanādhīśās.<BR>—उदधि-क्रम, अस्, m. or उदधि-क्रा, आस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a voyager, a mariner.<BR>—उदधि-मल, अस्, m.<BR>cuttle-fish bone.<BR>—उदधि-मेखला, f. the earth<BR>(girdled by the ocean).<BR>—उदधि-राज, अस्, m. the<BR>king of the waters, the ocean.<BR>—उदधि-सुता, f. the<BR>daughter of the ocean; an epithet of Lakṣmī; and<BR>of Dvārakā, the capital of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—उद-प, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, crossing the water, as a boat.<BR>—उद-पात्र,<BR>अम्, ई, n. f. a water-jug, a ewer.<BR>—उद-पान, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a well.<BR>—उदपान-मण्डूक, अस्, m. a<BR>frog in a well; (metaphorically) an inexperienced man<BR>of limited ideas who knows only his own neighbour-<BR>hood.<BR>—उद-पू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. cleansing one's self<BR>with water, purified with water.<BR>—उद-पेष, अम्,<BR>n. a paste, anything ground with water; (अम्), ind.<BR>by grinding in water.<BR>—उद-प्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. swim-<BR>ming or splashing in water; (Say.) causing water to<BR>flow.<BR>—उद-प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. swimming in<BR>water.<BR>—उद-भार, अस्, m. a water-carrier, a cloud.<BR>—उद-भृज्ज and उद-मज्ज, अस्, m., N. of two<BR>men.<BR>—उद-मन्थ, अस्, m. barley-water.<BR>—उद-<BR>मेघ, अस्, m. a watery cloud; a shower of rain.<BR>—उद-लावणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, salted, prepared with<BR>brine.<BR>—उद-वज्र, अस्, m. a thunder-shower, a water-<BR>spout.<BR>—उद-वाप, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उद-<BR>वास, अस्, m. residence in water; (अम्), n. a house<BR>on the margin of a stream or pond, a marine grotto<BR>&c.<BR>—उद-वाह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bringing water;<BR>epithet of the Maruts.<BR>—उद-वाहन, अम्, n. any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-b" target="_blank">Page0153-b+ 81</a>]<BR>water-vessel; a cloud.<BR>—उद-विन्दु, उस्, m. a drop<BR>of water.<BR>—उद-वीवध, अस्, m. a yoke for carrying<BR>water.<BR>—उद-व्रज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उद-<BR>शराव, अस्, m. a jar filled with water.<BR>—उद-शुद्ध,<BR>अस्, m. a water-jar.<BR>—उद-श्वित्, त्, n. two portions of<BR>buttermilk and one portion of water.<BR>—उद-स्थाली,<BR>f. a caldron, a kettle.<BR>—उद-हरण, अस्, m. a vessel<BR>for drawing water.<BR>—उद-हार, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>fetching or carrying water; (अस्), m. a water-carrier,<BR>a cloud.<BR>—उदौदन, see उदकौदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक|उदकं
उदक, अम्, n. water; उदकं दा or प्रदा or<BR>कृ, to offer a libation of water to a dead person<BR>(with gen. or dat. of the person); उदकम् उप-<BR>स्पृश्, to touch certain parts of the body with water,<BR>as prescribed by law; (the word उदक may be used<BR>alone to express this ceremony, e. g. उदकार्थम्,<BR>for the sake of the उदक ceremony.)<BR>—उदक-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. or उदक-क्रिया, f. presentation of<BR>water to dead ancestors as far as the fourteenth de-<BR>gree.<BR>—उदक-कार्य, अम्, n. a religious ceremony<BR>performed with water; ablution of the body; obla-<BR>tions to the dead.<BR>—उदक-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a<BR>water-jar.<BR>—उदक-क्रीडन, अम्, n. sporting about<BR>in water.<BR>—उदक-गाह or उद-गाह, अस्, m. enter-<BR>ing the water.<BR>—उदक-गिरि, इस्, m. a mountain<BR>abounding in streams of water.<BR>—उदक-चन्द्र, a<BR>kind of magic.<BR>—उदक-द, अस्, आ, अम्, a giver of<BR>water, yielding water, offering water to the manes;<BR>(अस्), m. an heir, a near kinsman.<BR>—उदक-दातृ,<BR>ता, or उदक-दायिन्, ई, m. one who presents liba-<BR>tions of water to the manes, an heir or kinsman.<BR>—उदक-दान, अम्, n. gift of water, especially to<BR>the manes, as a religious or obsequial rite.<BR>—उदक-<BR>दानिक, अस्, आ, अम्, referring to the above obsequial<BR>rite.<BR>—उदक-धर, अस्, m. ‘water-holder,’ a cloud.<BR>—उदक-पर्वत, अस्, m.; see उदक-गिरि.<BR>—उद-<BR>क-पूर्वकम्, ind. preceded by the water-rite, i. e. by<BR>pouring water on the hand as preparatory to or con-<BR>firmatory of a gift or promise.<BR>—उदक-प्रतीकाश,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, like water, watery, fluid.<BR>—उदक-भार,<BR>अस्, m. a yoke for carrying water.<BR>—उदक-भूम,<BR>अस्, m. humid soil.<BR>—उदक-मञ्जरी, f. title of a<BR>work on medicine.<BR>—उदक-मण्डलु, उस्, m., Ved.<BR>a water-pitcher.<BR>—उदक-मन्थ or उद-मन्थ,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of peeled grain.<BR>—उदक-मेह, अस्, m.<BR>a sort of diabetes, passing watery urine.<BR>—उदकमे-<BR>हिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from this disease.<BR>—उदक-<BR>वज्र, अस्, m. a thunder-shower, a thunderstorm with<BR>rain; [cf. उद-वज्र.]<BR>—उदक-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>furnished with water.<BR>—उदक-विन्दु, उस्, m. a drop<BR>of water.<BR>—उदक-वीवध, अस्, m. a yoke for carry-<BR>ing water; [cf. उद-वीवध.]<BR>—उदक-शाक, अम्,<BR>n. any aquatic herb.<BR>—उदक-शान्ति, इस्, f. sprinkling<BR>consecrated water over a sick person to allay fever.<BR>—उदक-सक्तु, उस्, m. ground rice moistened with<BR>water.<BR>—उदक-स्पर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, touching different<BR>parts of the body with water; touching water in con-<BR>firmation of a promise.<BR>—उदक-हार, अस्, m. a<BR>water-carrier.<BR>—उदकात्मन् (˚क-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, chiefly<BR>consisting of water, whose chief substance is water.<BR>—उदकाधार (˚क-आध्˚), अस्, m. a reservoir, a<BR>cistern, a well.<BR>—उदकान्त (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m. margin<BR>of water, bank, shore.<BR>—उदकार्थिन् (˚क-अर्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, desirous of water, thirsty.<BR>—उदकाहार (˚क-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, m. the drawing up of water.<BR>—उदके-चर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, moving or living in or inhabiting water.<BR>—उदके-विशीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, dried in water, (a<BR>metaphorical expression for anything unheard of or<BR>impossible.)<BR>—उदकोदञ्जन (˚क-उद्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>water-jar.<BR>—उदकोदर (˚क-उद्˚), अम्, n. dropsy.<BR>—उदकोदरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, dropsical.<BR>—उदकौदन<BR>(˚क-ओद्˚), अस्, m. rice boiled with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकल
उदकल, अस्, आ, अम्, watery, containing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकिल
उदकिल, अस्, आ, अम्, watery, containing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्य
उदक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in water; (आ), f. a woman<BR>in her courses (requiring water for purification).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्
1. उदन्, n. (not used in the nom. sing. du. plur.<BR>and the acc. sing. and du.), Ved. a wave, water.<BR>—उदन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. wavy, watery,<BR>abounding in water; (आन्), m. the ocean; N. of a<BR>Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदनिमत्|उदनिमन्त्
उदनि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. abounding in waves<BR>or water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्य
1. उदन्य, nom. P., Ved. उदन्यति, to irrigate;<BR>to thirst, be thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्य
2. उदन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. watery; (आ), f. thirst.<BR>—उदन्य-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. born in or living in<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्यु
उदन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. liking or seeking water,<BR>walking in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दन|उंदनं
उन्दन, उन्न, &c. See under उन्द्, p. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्
उदक् उदक्. See under 2. उद्-अञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्र|उदग्रं
उदग्र उद्-अग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, with elevated top,<BR>having the top upwards, over-topping, towering or<BR>pointing upwards; projecting; high, tall, long; ad-<BR>vanced (in age); increased, large, vast, fierce, intense;<BR>excited, enraptured.<BR>—उदग्र-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, hav-<BR>ing projecting teeth, large-toothed; (अन्), m. an ele-<BR>phant with a large tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदज्
उदज् उद्-अज्, cl. 1. P. A. -अजति, -ते, -अजितुम्,<BR>to drive out, expel, pull off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदज|उदजः
2. उद्-अज, अस्, m. (for 1. see under उद 1st col.),<BR>the driving out or forth (of cattle &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाज|उदाजः
उद्-आज, अस्, m. leading up or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदजलक
उदजलक उदजलक, अस्, m., N. of a wheel-<BR>wright in the Pañca-tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्च्|उदंच्
उदञ्च् 1. उद्-अञ्च् or उद्-अच्, cl. 1. P. A. -अञ्-<BR>चति, -ते, -चितुम्, to elevate, raise up, lift up, throw<BR>up; to send forth, utter, cause to resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्त
उद्-अक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, gone up, raised up, risen,<BR>ascended; sent forth; uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदङ्क|उदंक|उदंकः|उदङ्कः
उद्-अङ्क, अस्, m. a vessel or bucket (for oil &c.,<BR>but not for water); Pāṇini III. 3, 123, N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्च्|उदंच्
2. उद्-अञ्च् or उद्-अच्, अङ्, ईची, अक्, turned or going<BR>upwards; upper, upwards; turned to the north, north-<BR>ern (opposed to अधराञ्च् and दक्षिण); subse-<BR>quent, posterior; (क्), ind. above; northward; subse-<BR>quently; उदीची, the northern दिश् or quarter, the<BR>north.<BR>—उदक्तात्, ind., Ved. towards the north,<BR>northward.<BR>—उदक्-पथ, अस्, m. the northern coun-<BR>try.<BR>—उदक्-प्रवण, अस्, आ, अम्, sloping towards<BR>the north; proceeding well (as a sacrifice?).<BR>—उदक्-<BR>सेन, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—उदग्-अद्रि, इस्, m.<BR>the northern mountain; the Himālaya mountain to<BR>the north of Hindūstan.<BR>—उदग्-अयन, अम्, n. the<BR>sun's progress north of the equator, the half-year from<BR>the winter to the summer solstice.<BR>—उदग्-दश, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the border turned upwards or to the<BR>north.<BR>—उदग्-भूम, अस्, m. fertile soil (turned up-<BR>wards or towards the north).<BR>—उदग्-भूमि, इस्, m.<BR>good or fertile soil.<BR>—उदङ्-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, facing<BR>the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चन|उदंचन|उदंचनं|उदञ्चनं
उद्-अञ्चन, अम्, n. a bucket, a pail for drawing<BR>water out of a well; (अम्), n. directing or throwing<BR>upwards; rising, ascending; a cover or lid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चित|उदञ्चितं
उद्-अञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, raised up, thrown up,<BR>tossed; worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चु|उदंचु
उद्-अञ्चु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्जलि|उदंजलि
उदञ्जलि उद्-अञ्जलि, इस्, इस्, इ, hollowing the<BR>palms and then raising them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदण्डपाल|उदंडपाल|उदंडपालः|उदण्डपालः
उदण्डपाल उद्-अण्ड-पाल, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>fish; a sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधि|उदधिः
उदधि उद-धि. See under उद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्
उदन् 2. उद्-अन्, cl. 2. P. -अनिति, -नितुम्, to<BR>breathe upwards, emit the breath in an upward direc-<BR>tion; to breathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदान|उदानः
उद्-आन, अस्, m. breathing upwards, breathing,<BR>breath; one of the three or five vital airs, that which<BR>rises up the throat and passes into the head; (with<BR>Buddhists) an expression of joy or praise; the navel;<BR>an eyelash; a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्त|उदंत|उदन्तः
उदन्त उद्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, reaching to the<BR>end or border of anything; (अस्), m. ‘telling to the<BR>end,’ full tidings, intelligence; news; a pure and<BR>virtuous man; supporting one's self by sacrificing for<BR>others; one who gets a livelihood by a trade &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्तक|उदंतक|उदंतकः|उदन्तकः
उदन्तक, अस्, m. news, tidings, intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्तिका|उदंतिका
उद्-अन्तिका, f. satisfaction, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्त्य|उदंत्य
उदन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, living beyond a limit or<BR>boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्य
उदन्य उदन्य. See under 2. उद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदय|उदयः
उदय उद्-अय, &c. See under उद्-इ 3rd col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर|उदरं|उदरः
उदर उदर, अम्, n. (fr. rt. ऋ with उद्?),<BR>the belly; a cavity, the interior or inside of anything<BR>(e. g. उदरे, inside, in the interior); enlargement of<BR>the abdomen from dropsy or flatulence, any mor-<BR>bid abdominal affection, as liver, spleen, &c., a class<BR>of eight different diseases; the thick, inner side of<BR>the अन्गुष्ठ or thumb; slaughter; [cf. Lat. uterus.]<BR>—उदर-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. disease of the spleen, lit.<BR>‘knot of the belly’ (a chronic affection of this organ<BR>not uncommon in India).<BR>—उदर-त्राण, अम्, n. a<BR>cuirass, armour covering the front of the body; a<BR>girth, a belly-band.<BR>—उदर-दार, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>particular disease of the belly.<BR>—उदर-पिशाच, अस्,<BR>m. a glutton, voracious, one who devours everything,<BR>flesh, fish, &c.<BR>—उदर-पूरम्, ind. till the belly is<BR>full.<BR>—उदर-पोषण, अम्, n. feeding the belly, sup-<BR>porting life.<BR>—उदर-भरण-मात्र-केवलेच्छु<BR>(˚ल-इच्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, desirous only of the mere filing<BR>of the belly.<BR>—उदरम्-भरि, इस्, इस्, इ, nourishing<BR>only one's own belly, selfishly voracious, gluttonous.<BR>—उदर-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a large belly,<BR>corpulent.<BR>—उदर-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping on the<BR>face or belly.<BR>—उदर-शाण्डिल्य, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>sage.<BR>—उदर-सर्वस्व, अस्, m. an epicure, a glutton.<BR>—उदराध्मान (˚र-आध्˚), अम्, n. flatulence of<BR>the body.<BR>—उदरामय (˚र-आम्˚), अस्, m. disease<BR>of the belly, dysentery, diarrhœa.<BR>—उदरामयिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, suffering from dysentery or diarrhœa.<BR>—उद-<BR>रावर्त (˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. the navel.<BR>—उदरावेष्ट<BR>(˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. tape worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरक
उदरक, अस्, ई, अम्, abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिक
उदरिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a large belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिन्
उदरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a large belly, fat, corpu-<BR>lent; abdominal; (इणी), f. a pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

