उदायुध
उदायुध उद्-आयुध, अस्, आ, अम्, with uplifted<BR>weapon, upraising weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदार|उदारः
उदार उद्-आर, अस्, आ, or ई, अम् (fr. rt. ऋ with<BR>उद्), high, lofty, exalted, noble, illustrious, generous,<BR>liberal, gentle, munificent, great, best; upright, honest,<BR>sincere; proper, right; eloquent; unperplexed; Ved.<BR>causing to rise, exciting, driving forth; (अम्), ind.<BR>aloud; (अस्), m., Ved. a rising fog or vapour; a sort<BR>of grain with long stalks; a figure in rhetoric, attri-<BR>buting nobleness to an inanimate object; (आस्), pl.<BR>nebulous forms, spirits (?).<BR>—उदार-चरित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of a generous disposition, noble-minded.<BR>—उदार-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">Page0154-c+ 75</a>]<BR>चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, high-minded, magnanimous.<BR>—उदा-<BR>र-ता, f. liberality, generosity.<BR>—उदार-धी, ईस्, ईस्,<BR>इ, highly intelligent, wise, sagacious, noble-minded.<BR>—उदार-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of great power.<BR>—उदार-<BR>सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, generous-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारक
