उदावर्तिन्
उदावर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from such diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावसु|उदावसुः
उदावसु उदावसु, उस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Videha, a son of Janaka; [cf. उपावसु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावह्
उदावह् उद्-आ-वह्, cl. 1. P. A. -वहति, -ते,<BR>-वोढुम्, to extol, to praise; to draw, lead along;<BR>to marry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्
उदास् उद्-आस्, cl. 2. A. -आस्ते, -आसितुम्, to sit<BR>separate or away from, to sit on one side or apart,<BR>not to share in, not to show interest in; to be un-<BR>concerned about, to be indifferent or passive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
2. उद्-आस, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see under उद्-अस्),<BR>indifferent, unconcerned, apathetic; (अस्), m. a stoic,<BR>a philosopher; indifference, apathy, stoicism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासितृ
उद्-आसितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, indifferent, disregarding,<BR>stoical, one void of concern or affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासिन्
उद्-आसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, indifferent, disregarding; (ई),<BR>m. a stoic, a philosopher; one who has no passion<BR>nor affection for anything; in popular acceptation, a<BR>religious mendicant in general, or one of a particular<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उद्-आसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting apart, indifferent,<BR>free from affection; (in law) not involved in the<BR>dispute; (अस्), m. a stranger, a neutral, a common<BR>acquaintance, a person neither a friend nor a foe.<BR>—उदासीन-ता, f. indifference, apathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थित|उदास्थितः
उदास्थित उद्-आस्थित, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्था<BR>with आ and उद्), a superintendent, a doorkeeper; a<BR>spy, an emissary; an ascetic who has given up his<BR>vow; (अस्, आ, अम्), set over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहित
उदाहित उद्-आहित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. धा with<BR>आ and उद्), elevated, raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृ
उदाहृ उद्-आ-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते,<BR>-हर्तुम्, to relate, declare, announce; illustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहरण|उदाहरणं
उद्-आहरण, अम्, n. relating, saying, declaring,<BR>declaration; referring a general rule to a special case,<BR>an example or illustration; an apposite argument, the<BR>third of the five premises of rhetorical reasoning; the<BR>example or third member in a fivefold syllogism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहार|उदाहारः
उद्-आहार, अस्, m. an example or illustration; the<BR>beginning of a speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहार्य
उद्-आहार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be referred as a general<BR>rule to a special case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृत
उद्-आहृत, अस्, आ, अम्, said, illustrated, called,<BR>named, entitled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृति|उदाहृतिः
उद्-आ-हृति, इस्, f. an example, an illustration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदि
उदि उद्-इ, cl. 2. P. -एति, -एतुम्, to go up or<BR>proceed; to rise (e. g. as a star), to come up (as a<BR>cloud); to go out of; to come out or arise from; to<BR>escape; to start up; to rise up against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदय|उदयः
उद्-अय, अस्, आ, अम्, (in gram.) following, coming<BR>after or upon (as one letter, accent &c. upon another);<BR>(अस्), m. going upwards; rising (of the sun or planets<BR>or of a cloud); the eastern mountain behind which<BR>the sun is supposed to rise; coming forth, creation,<BR>production, becoming visible, appearance, develop-<BR>ment; light, splendor; conclusion, result, conse-<BR>quence; rising, reaching one's aim, elevation; profit,<BR>advantage, income, revenue, interest; outlet, exit; N.<BR>of the seventh Arhat of the future Utsarpiṇi, = Udayā-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">Page0155-a+ 76</a>]<BR>śva; a son of Yājñika; a follower of Śākya-muni.<BR>—उदय-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उदय-जित्,<BR>त्, m., N. of a son of Guṇala.<BR>—उदय-धवल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince.<BR>—उदय-पर्वत, अस्, m. or<BR>उदय-गिरि, इस्, m. or उदय-शैल, अस्, m. or<BR>उदयाचल (˚य-अच्˚), अस्, m. or उदयाद्रि (˚य-<BR>अद्˚), इस्, m. the eastern mountain behind which the<BR>sun rises.<BR>—उदय-पुर, अम्, n., N. of the capital<BR>of Marvar.<BR>—उदय-प्रस्थ, अस्, m. the plateau of<BR>the mountain behind which the sun rises.<BR>—उदय-<BR>राज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उदय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>risen.<BR>—उदय-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—उदया-<BR>दित्य (˚य-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—उदयाश्व<BR>(˚य-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a grandson of Ajāta-śatru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयत्
उद्-अयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going upwards, rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयन|उदयनं|उदयनः
उद्-अयन, अम्, n. rising, ascending (of the sun);<BR>exit, result; conclusion, end; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Agastya; N. of a king of Vatsa; N. of a Purohita of<BR>king Śuddhodana.<BR>—उदयन or उदयनाचार्य, अस्,<BR>m. a philosopher and violent persecutor of the Bud-<BR>dhists.<BR>—उदयन-चरित, अम्, n. title of a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनीय
उदयनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to an end or<BR>conclusion, finishing (as a ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयिन्
उद्-अयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rising, ascending, prosperous,<BR>flourishing; (ई), m., N. of a man.<BR>—उदयि-भद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Ajāta-śatru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाय
उद्-आय. See s. v. त्र्य्-उदाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
1. उद्-इत, अस्, आ, अम्, risen, ascended, being above;<BR>high, tall, lofty; grown, augmented, born, produced;<BR>incurred, experienced.<BR>—उदित-होमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved.<BR>sacrificing after sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदिति|उदितिः
1. उद्-इति, इस्, f., Ved. ascending, rising (of the<BR>sun); going away or down, setting (of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीयमान
उद्-ईयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदिङ्ग्
उदिङ्ग् उद्-इङ्ग्, Caus. P. -इङ्गयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to impart a tremulous motion, to vibrate; to utter<BR>with a whirring or vibratory sound; to cause to whir<BR>(said of the pronunciation of certain letters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित 2. उदित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वद्), said,<BR>spoken.<BR>—उदितोदित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. उदित with<BR>1. उद्-इत), well-grounded in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदिति|उदितिः
2. उदिति, इस्, f., Ved. speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित 3. उदित, अस्, आ, अम् (incorrectly spelt<BR>for उद्-दित, see 4. दा), bound, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदिनक्ष्
उदिनक्ष् उद्-इनक्ष् (irreg. Desid. of rt.<BR>नक्ष्), Ved. -इनक्षति, to attain, obtain, reach; to<BR>wish to gain, to pretend to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्ष्
उदीक्ष् उद्-ईक्ष्, cl. 1. A. -ईक्षते, -षितुम्,<BR>to look up to; to look at, regard, view, behold; to<BR>wait, to delay, to expect: Caus. -ईक्षयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to look up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्षण|उदीक्षणं
उद्-ईक्षण, अम्, n. looking up, seeing, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्ष्य
उद्-ईक्ष्य, ind. having looked up at, having seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन उदीचीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. उद्-अञ्च्),<BR>turned towards the north, northern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being or living in the north;<BR>(अस्), m. the country to the north and west of the<BR>river Sarasvatī, the northern region; (आस्), m. the<BR>inhabitants of this country; (अम्), n. a kind of per-<BR>fume.<BR>—उदीच्य-वृत्त, अम्, n. the metre of the<BR>inhabitants of the northern country, a species of the<BR>Vaitālīya metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीप|उदीपः
उदीप उद्-ईप, अस्, m. (fr. 1. उद् and अप्, water),<BR>high water, an inundation; (अस्, आ, अम्), flooded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्
उदीर् उद्-ईर्, cl. 2. A. -ईर्ते, -ईरितुम्, to rise;<BR>to start (in order to go or to come); to move up-<BR>wards, ascend; to arise, originate: Caus. -ईरयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to rise or move; to throw or cast<BR>upwards, to cast, throw, discharge, to drive forward;<BR>to rouse up, excite; to raise one's voice; to utter,<BR>speak; to effect; to make visible: Pass. -ईर्यते, to be<BR>cast or thrown upwards; to be excited; to be uttered,<BR>announced, enunciated; to sound; to issue forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरण|उदीरणं
उद्-ईरण, अं, n. throwing, casting, discharging<BR>(a missile); speaking, saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरित
उद्-ईरित, अस्, आ, अम्, said, uttered; excited, ani-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">Page0155-b+ 70</a>]<BR>mated.<BR>—उदीरित-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, whose mind is active,<BR>acute-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्ण|उदीर्णः
उद्-ईर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, issued out, excited, increased,<BR>intense; generous, great, excellent.<BR>—उदीर्ण-ता, f.<BR>excitement, activity, agility.<BR>—उदीर्ण-दीधिति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, intensely bright.<BR>—उदीर्ण-वेग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>impetuous in its course (as a torrent), violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्य|उदीर्य्य
1. उद्-ईर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be raised, uttered, spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्य|उदीर्य्य
2. उद्-ईर्य, ind. having uttered, having spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्यमाण|उदीर्य्यमाण
उद्-ईर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being cast or discharged;<BR>being spoken or uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीष्
उदीष् उद्-ईष्, cl. 1. A. -ईषते, -ईषितुम्, to<BR>rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीषित
उद्-ईषित, अस्, आ, अम्, risen, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुक्ष्
उदुक्ष् उद्-उक्ष्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -उक्षति,<BR>-षितुम्, to sprinkle upwards or outwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुब्ज्
उदुब्ज् उद्-उब्ज्, cl. 6. P. -उब्जति, -जितुम्, to<BR>cleave asunder (?); to set up, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बर|उदुंबर|उदुम्बरं|उदुंबरः|उदुम्बरः
उदुम्बर उदुम्बर, अस्, m. (Ved. written with<BR>द्, in later books generally with ड्), the glomerous<BR>fig tree, Ficus Glomerata; a kind of leprosy; a thres-<BR>hold; a eunuch; (अम्), n. the fruit of the glomerous<BR>fig tree; copper; the weight karṣa.<BR>—उदुम्बर-<BR>पर्णी or उदुम्बर-दला, f., N. of the plant Croton<BR>Polyandra.<BR>—उदुम्बरा-वती, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बल|उदुंबल|उदुम्बलः
उदुम्बल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. copper-coloured?;<BR>(Say.) of extended power (for उरु-बल; said of the<BR>two dogs, the messengers of Yama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

