उन्नद्
उन्नद् उन्-नद् (उद्-नद्), cl. 1. P. -नदति,<BR>-दितुम्, to cry out, sound, roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाद|उन्नादः
उन्-नाद, अस्, m. crying out, humming, chirping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्
उन्नम् उन्-नम् (उद्-नम्), cl. 1. P. -नमति,<BR>-नन्तुम्, to rise, ascend; to bend up, raise, elevate,<BR>erect: Caus. P. -नमयति, -यितुम्, to bend up-<BR>wards, raise, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नत|उन्नतः
उन्-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, raised, held or lifted up;<BR>high, tall; projecting, plump, full; great, eminent;<BR>(अस्), m. a boa (अज-गर); N. of a Buddha; (अम्),<BR>n. elevation, ascension.<BR>—उन्नत-चरण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">Page0159-b+ 74</a>]<BR>with uplifted paws, rampant.<BR>—उन्नत-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>height, sublimity, majesty.<BR>—उन्नत-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having a projecting navel, i. e. corpulent.<BR>—उन्नत-<BR>शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, holding up the head, carrying the<BR>head high; with head upraised.<BR>—उन्नतानत (˚त-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, elevated and depressed, uneven, un-<BR>dulating, wavy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नति|उन्नतिः
उन्-नति, इस्, f. elevation, height; rising, ascending;<BR>increase, advancement, prosperity; N. of a daughter<BR>of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma; the wife of Garuḍa.<BR>—उन्नति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, elevated, projecting,<BR>plump; high, sublime.<BR>—उन्नतीश (˚ति-ईश), अस्, m.<BR>a N. of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमन|उन्नमनं
उन्-नमन, अम्, n. bending upwards, raising,<BR>lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमय्य
उन्-नमय्य, ind. having raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमित|उन्नमितः
उन्-नमित, अस्, आ, अम्, raised, elevated, lifted or<BR>pulled up; heightened, increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्र
उन्-नम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, erect, upright, elevated,<BR>lofty, high.<BR>—उन्नम्र-ता, f. erectness, uprightness<BR>(of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाम|उन्नामः
उन्-नाम, अस्, m. bending upwards, raising, lift-<BR>ing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नय|उन्नयः
उन्नय उन्-नय. See under 1. उन्-नी below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयनपङ्क्ति
उन्नयनपङ्क्ति उन्-नयन-पङ्क्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, hav-<BR>ing the line of the eyelids uplifted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नस
उन्नस उन्-नस (उद्-नस्), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a prominent nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नह्
उन्नह् उन्-नह् (उद्-नह्), cl. 4. P. -नह्यति,<BR>-नद्धुम्, to tie up, bind up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्ध
उन्-नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, tied up; swelled, in-<BR>creased; unbound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाह|उन्नाहं|उन्नाहः
उन्-नाह, अस्, m. sour gruel made from the fer-<BR>mentation of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाभ|उन्नाभः
उन्नाभ उन्-नाभ, अस्, m. (fr. उद् + नाभि),<BR>N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्र|उन्निद्रः
उन्निद्र उन्-निद्र (उद्-न्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sleep-<BR>less, awake; expanded as a flower; budded, blown;<BR>shining (as the moon, supposed to be awake when<BR>others are asleep).<BR>—उन्निद्र-ता, f. sleeplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नी
उन्नी 1. उन्-नी (उद्-नी), cl. 1. P. -नयति, -ने-<BR>तुम्, to lead upwards or up to, bring up; to set up,<BR>erect; to bring out of, free from, help, rescue, re-<BR>deem; to draw up (as water); to lead away; to stroke,<BR>smooth; to lead out; press out, extract; to find out,<BR>ascertain by inference, infer; lead off (in singing):<BR>Desid. A. -निनीषते, to intend or wish to lead out &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नय|उन्नयः
उन्-नय, अस्, m. raising, elevating, hoisting, lead-<BR>ing upwards; analogy, resemblance, consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयन|उन्नयनं
उन्-नयन, अम्, n. raising, elevating, lifting up;<BR>taking out of, drawing water; the vessel out of which<BR>a fluid is taken; leading away; making straight,<BR>smoothing; deliberation, discussion, logic, reasoning,<BR>inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाय|उन्नायः
उन्-नाय, अस्, m. raising, elevating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायक
उन्-नायक, अस्, आ, अम्, what raises; what leads to<BR>an inference or conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नी
2. उन्-नी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, bringing or leading upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नीत
उन्-नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, led up, led away, inferred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेतृ
उन्-नेतृ, ता, m. one who pours a fluid out of one<BR>vessel into another, especially the priest who pours<BR>the Soma juice into the cups.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेत्र|उन्नेत्रं
उन्नेत्र, अम्, n. the office of the Unnetṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेय
उन्-नेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be inferred, to be ascer-<BR>tained by analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्ज्
उन्मज्ज् उन्-मज्ज् (उद्-म्˚), cl. 6. P. -मज्जति,<BR>-मङ्क्तुम्, to emerge: Caus. -मज्जयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to emerge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जन|उन्मज्जनं|उन्मज्जनः
उन्-मज्जन, अस्, m., N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्त|उन्मत्तः
उन्मत्त उन्-मत्त. See उन्-मद् next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथ्
उन्मथ् उन्-मथ् or उन्-मन्थ् (उद्-म्˚), cl. 1.<BR>9. P. -मथति or -मन्थति, -मथ्नाति, -मन्थि-<BR>तुम्, to shake up, disturb, excite; to shake, tear, or<BR>cut off; to strike, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथन
उन्-मथन, अम्, n. shaking off, throwing off or<BR>down, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथित
उन्-मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थ|उन्मंथ|उन्मंथः|उन्मन्थः
उन्-मन्थ, अस्, m. agitation; killing, slaughter;<BR>a disease of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थक|उन्मंथक|उन्मन्थकः
उन्-मन्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking up or off,<BR>agitating, stirring; throbbing, beating; (अस्), m. in-<BR>flammation of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थन|उन्मंथन|उन्मंथनं
उन्-मन्थन, अम्, n. the act of shaking or agi-<BR>tating; hurting, killing; probing, stirring a weapon<BR>&c. lodged in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थित
उन्-मन्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken up, moved,<BR>agitated, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथ|उन्माथः
उन्-माथ, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, killing; (अस्),<BR>m. shaking; killing, slaughter; a snare or trap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथिन्
उन्-माथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद्
उन्मद् उन्-मद् (उद्-म्˚), cl. 4. P. -माद्यति,<BR>-मदितुम्, to be or become mad: Caus. P. -मद-<BR>यति or -मादयति, -यितुम्, to madden, inebriate,<BR>render drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्त|उन्मत्तः
उन्-मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, insane, frantic, mad; drunk,<BR>intoxicated; (अस्), m. the thorn-apple, Datura Metel<BR>and Fastuosa; another tree, Pterospermum Aceri-<BR>folium; N. of a Rakṣas.<BR>—उन्मत्त-कीर्ति, इस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—उन्मत्त-गङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a region (‘where the Gaṅgā roars’).<BR>—उन्मत्त-ता,<BR>f. or उन्मत्त-त्व, अम्, n. insanity, intoxication.<BR>—उन्मत्त-दर्शन or उन्मत्त-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>maniac-like, mad.<BR>—उन्मत्त-प्रलपित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>spoken in drunkenness or madness.<BR>—उन्मत्त-भै-<BR>रव-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—उन्मत्त-<BR>लिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, feigning madness.<BR>—उन्मत्त-वत्,<BR>ind. like one mad, as if mad, like a maniac.<BR>—उन्-<BR>मत्त-वेश, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—उन्मत्ता-<BR>वन्ति (˚त-अव्˚), इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तक
उन्मत्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, insane, mad; drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद|उन्मदः
उन्-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, mad, furious, extravagant;<BR>drunk, intoxicated; (अस्), m. insanity, either morbid<BR>or as the effect of temporary excitement, intoxication,<BR>ecstacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदन
उन्-मदन, अस्, आ, अम्, inflamed with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदिष्णु|उन्मदिष्णुः
उन्-मदिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, mad, insane, crazed, in-<BR>toxicated; in rut (as an elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माद|उन्मादः
उन्-माद, अस्, आ, अम्, mad, insane, extravagant;<BR>(अस्), m. madness, extravagance; (in medicine) mania.<BR>—उन्माद-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, mad, insane, wild, ex-<BR>travagant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादन|उन्मादनः
उन्-मादन, अस्, आ, अम्, maddening, exciting, in-<BR>toxicating; (अस्), m. one of the five arrows of the<BR>god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादिन्
उन्मादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, mad, intoxicated; (नी), f., N.<BR>of a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादुक
उन्-मादुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fond of drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्
उन्मनस् उन्-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or उन्-मनस्क<BR>(उद्-म˚), अस्, आ, अम्, excited or disturbed in mind,<BR>perplexed, disturbed; regretting, missing, repining for<BR>a lost or departed friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनाय
उन्मनाय, nom. A. उन्मनायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>become excited or disturbed in mind, to repine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीकृ
उन्मनी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>excited, to excite, disturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीभू
उन्मनी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्, to be-<BR>come disturbed in mind, to repine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मयूख
उन्मयूख उन्-मयूख (उद्-म्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>shining, radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

