उन्-मुच, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मोचन|उन्मोचनं
उन्-मोचन, अम्, n. unfastening, loosening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुद्र|उन्मुद्रः
उन्मुद्र उन्-मुद्र (उद्-म्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>sealed, opened; blown as a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूल
उन्मूल उन्-मूल (उद्-म्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, eradi-<BR>cated, pulled up by the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलन|उन्मूलनं
उन्-मूलन, अम्, n. eradicating, pulling up by the<BR>roots; destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलय
उन्मूलय, nom. P. उन्मूलयति, -यितुम्, to era-<BR>dicate, pull up by the roots; to extirpate, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलित|उन्मूलितं
उन्-मूलित, अस्, आ, अम्, eradicated, pulled up by<BR>the roots; destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृज्
उन्मृज् उन्-मृज् (उद्-म्˚), cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि,<BR>मार्जितुम् or -मार्ष्टुम्, to rub off, wipe off;<BR>efface; blot out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्जन|उन्मार्जनं
उन्-मार्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbing or wiping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृजावमृजा
उन्मृजावमृजा (˚ज-अव्˚), f. repeatedly rubbing<BR>up and down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृष्ट
उन्-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, worn off, blotted out,<BR>effaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृश्य
उन्मृश्य उन्-मृश्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. मृश् with<BR>उद्), Ved. to be reached, to be touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेदा
उन्मेदा उन्-मेदा, f. (fr. rt. मिद् with उद्),<BR>corpulence, fatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप
उप उप, a prefix to verbs and nouns (ex-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">Page0160-b+ 73</a>]<BR>pressing) towards, near to (opposed to अप, away), by<BR>the side of, with, together with, under, down (e. g. उप-<BR>गम्, to go near, undergo; उप-गमन, approach-<BR>ing. In the Veda the verb has sometimes to be supplied<BR>from the context, and sometimes उप is placed after the<BR>verb with which it ought to have been compounded,<BR>e. g. आययुर् उप = उपाययुः, they approached).<BR>(As unconnected with verbs and prefixed to nouns<BR>उप expresses) direction towards, nearness, contiguity<BR>in space, time, number, degree, resemblance, and re-<BR>lationship, but with the idea of subordination and inferi-<BR>ority (e. g. उप-कनिष्ठिका, the finger next to the<BR>little finger; उप-पुराणम्, a secondary or subordinate<BR>Purāṇa; उप-दश, nearly ten); sometimes forming<BR>with the nouns to which it is prefixed compound ad-<BR>verbs (e. g. उप-मूलम्, at the root; उप-पूर्व-<BR>रात्रम्, towards the beginning of night; उप-कूपे,<BR>near a well), which adverbs lose their adverbial ter-<BR>minations if they are again compounded with nouns<BR>(e. g. उपकूप-जलाशय, a reservoir in the neigh-<BR>bourhood of a well). Prefixed to proper names उप<BR>may express in classical literature ‘a younger brother’<BR>(e. g. उपेन्द्र, ‘the younger brother of Indra’), and<BR>in Buddhist literature ‘a son.’<BR>(As a separable adverb उप rarely expresses) thereto,<BR>further, moreover (e. g. तत्र उप ब्रह्म यो वेद,<BR>who further knows the Veda).<BR>(As a separable preposition with locative) near to,<BR>towards, in the direction of, under, below (e. g. उप<BR>आशाः, towards the regions); near to, at, on, upon; at<BR>the time of, upon, up to, in, above (with loc., e. g.<BR>उप सानुषु, on the tops of the mountains); with,<BR>together with, at the same time with, according to<BR>(with inst., e. g. उप धर्मभिः, according to the<BR>rules of duty).<BR>Besides the meanings given above उप is said to<BR>imply disease, extinction; ornament; command; re-<BR>proof; undertaking; giving; killing; diffusing; wish;<BR>power; effort; resemblance, &c.; [cf. Gr. ὑπό Lat.<BR>sub; Goth. up; Old Germ. oba; Mod. Germ. ob<BR>in obdach, obliegen, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक
उपक, अस्, m. a diminutive of all proper names<BR>beginning with उप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपऋ
उप-ऋ उप-ऋ. See उपार्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकक्ष
उपकक्ष उप-कक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. reach-<BR>ing to the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकण्ठम्|उपकंठम्
उपकण्ठम् उप-कण्ठम्, ind. upon the<BR>neck, near the throat; in the proximity of; (अम्),<BR>n. proximity, neighbourhood, contiguous space; space<BR>near a village or its boundary; one of a horse's paces;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकथा
उपकथा उप-कथा, f. a short story, tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकनिष्ठिका
उपकनिष्ठिका उप-कनिष्ठिका, f. the last<BR>finger but one; the finger next to the little finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकन्यापुरम्
उपकन्यापुरम् उप-कन्यापुरम्, ind. near<BR>the women's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकरण|उपकरणं
उपकरण, उपकार, &c. See उप-कृ next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णम्
उपकर्णम् उप-कर्णम्, ind. close to the ear,<BR>into the ear, (whispered &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णिका
उपकर्णिका, f. what goes from ear to ear, ru-<BR>mour, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पन|उपकल्पनं
उपकल्पन उप-कल्पन. See उप-कॢप्, p. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकान्तम्
उपकान्तम् उप-कान्तम्, ind. near a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकाल
उपकाल उप-काल, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>the Nāgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

