उपढौकन|उपढौकनं
उप-ढौकन, अम्, n. a respectful offering or<BR>present, a Nazr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतक्ष
उपतक्ष उप-तक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a certain<BR>semi-divine being, belonging to the class of Gandhar-<BR>vas or of Nāgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतटम्
उपतटम् उप-तटम्, ind. near the skirt;<BR>(अस्), m. (?) the skirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्
उपतप् उप-तप्, cl. 1. P. -तपति, -तप्तुम्,<BR>to make warm, to heat; to feel pain, become sick;<BR>to afflict, befal (as an illness; sometimes used im-<BR>personally with gen. or acc.): Pass. -तप्यते, to feel<BR>pain, become ill, be afflicted with; to be emaciated<BR>with penance (तपस्): Caus. -तापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to kindle, ignite, burn, consume; to cause pain, ma-<BR>cerate the body by penance; torment, hurt, offend,<BR>oppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतपत्|उपतपन्त्
उप-तपत्, अम्, m., Ved. (scil. अग्नि) interior heat,<BR>a disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्त
उप-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, heated, parched; distressed,<BR>pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्तृ
उप-तप्तृ, ता, m. morbid heat; any cause of<BR>heat, burning or inflammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्यमान
उप-तप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपताप|उपतापः
