उपदिश्
उपदिश् 1. उप-दिश्, cl. 6. P. A. -दिशति, -ते,<BR>-देष्टुम्, to point out to; to indicate, specify, ex-<BR>plain, instruct, teach; advise, admonish; to assign the<BR>right place to anything, arrange; to mention, exhibit;<BR>to inform; to settle, prescribe; to dictate, command,<BR>govern; to name: Pass. -दिश्यते, to be taught &c.,<BR>to be called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्
2. उप-दिश्, क्, or उप-दिशा, f. an intermediate<BR>region, as north-east &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश
उप-दिश, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vasu-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्य
उप-दिश्य, ind. having advised or instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिष्ट|उपदिष्टः
उप-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, specified, particularized;<BR>taught, instructed, advised; assigned as a plea or<BR>reason; initiated; (अम्), n. council, advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेश|उपदेशः
उप-देश, अस्, m. pointing out to, instruction, teach-<BR>ing, informing, advice, prescription; specification; plea,<BR>pretext; initiation, communication of the initiatory<BR>Mantra or formula; (in gram.) a form in a rule, an<BR>indicatory form, i. e. a root, base, affix, augment, or<BR>any other word or part of a word furnished with in-<BR>dicatory letters (anubandhas) which serve as a guide<BR>to the application of particular grammatical rules and<BR>are rejected when the word or part of a word is ready<BR>for use.<BR>—उपदेश-ता, f. the state of being a precept<BR>or rule; injunction; manner of instructing; doc-<BR>trine.<BR>—उपदेश-सहस्री, f. title of a work of<BR>Śaṅkara on philosophy.<BR>—उपदेशार्थवक्य (˚श-<BR>अर्˚), अम्, n. a parable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशक|उपदेशकः
उप-देशक, अस्, आ, अम्, giving instruction, in-<BR>structing, instructive, didactic; (अस्), m. an instructor,<BR>a guide, especially a spiritual guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशन|उपदेशनं
उप-देशन, अम्, n. advising, instructing; (आ), f.<BR>information, doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशिन्
उप-देशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, advising, instructing, inform-<BR>ing; (ई), m. a teacher, adviser; a word or affix &c. in<BR>the shape in which it appears in grammatical works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेश्य
उप-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be taught; that<BR>which is to be taught or learnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टव्य
उप-देष्टव्य or उप-देशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to<BR>be taught or advised, fit or proper to be taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टृ
उप-देष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, one who points out, an<BR>adviser, teacher; a Guru or spiritual guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदी
उपदी उपदी, f. the plant Vanda Roxburghii<BR>or Aërides Tesselata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीका
उपदीका उपदीका, f. a kind of ant; also<BR>उप-देहिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीक्षिन्
उपदीक्षिन् उप-दीक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, sharing in<BR>an initiatory or other religious rite; a near relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीप्
उपदीप् उप-दीप्, Caus. P. -दीपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to kindle, set fire to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृश्
उपदृश् 1. उप-दृश्, cl. 1. P. -पश्यति,<BR>-द्रष्टुम्, to look at; to perceive, observe: Pass.<BR>-दृश्यते, to be or become visible, appear: Caus.<BR>-दर्शयति, -यितुम्, to cause to see, show, exhibit;<BR>to present a false show, impose upon another person<BR>by sham appearances; to illude; to explain, illustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शक|उपदर्शकः
उप-दर्शक, अस्, m. a guide, one who shows the<BR>way, a door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शन|उपदर्शनं
उप-दर्शन, अम्, n. a commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शित
उप-दर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, perceived, distinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृश्
2. उप-दृश्, क्, f., Ved. a view, aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृष्टि|उपदृष्टिः
उप-दृष्टि, इस्, f. aspect, view, show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रष्टृ
उप-द्रष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, Ved. a supervisor, in-<BR>spector; overseeing, overlooking; (टा), m. a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृषद्
उपदृषद् उप-दृषद् or उप-दृषदम्,<BR>ind. near a boundary stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेव|उपदेवः
उपदेव उप-देव, अस्, m. an inferior deity;<BR>N. of a son of Akrūra; also of Devaka; (ई), f., N.<BR>of the wife of Vasu-deva; of a daughter of Devaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवता
उप-देवता, f. a minor deity, as a Yakṣa, Gan-<BR>darbha, Apsaras, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेश|उपदेशः
उपदेश उप-देश, &c. See under 1. उप-दिश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदोह|उपदोहः
उपदोह उप-दोह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. दुह् with<BR>उप), a nipple of the udder of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रु
उपद्रु उप-द्रु, cl. 1. P. -द्रवति, -द्रोतुम्, to<BR>run near to, run towards, run at, rush at, assault, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रव|उपद्रवः
उप-द्रव, अस्, m. that which befalls suddenly,<BR>an unhappy accident, misfortune, calamity, mischief;<BR>national distress (whether the act of the seasons or the<BR>king, famine, exaction, &c.); national commotion,<BR>rebellion; violence, outrage; a symptom, a super-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">Page0163-c+ 75</a>]<BR>venient disease, one brought on whilst a person labours<BR>under another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रविन्
उप-द्रविन्, ई, इणी, इ, attacking, falling on; tyran-<BR>nical, violent, factious; (ई), m. a tyrant, an oppressor,<BR>a rebel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रुत
उप-द्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, visited by calamities, op-<BR>pressed, attacked, persecuted, tyrannized over; (in<BR>astron.) eclipsed; boding evil, inauspicious; (अम्), n.<BR>a term of the Bāṣkalas for that kind of Sandhi, which<BR>is also called उद्ग्राहवत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्वीप|उपद्वीपः
उपद्वीप उप-द्वीप, अस्, m. an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधर्म|उपधर्मः|उपधर्म्म|उपधर्म्मः
उपधर्म उप-धर्म, अस्, m. a minor or sub-<BR>ordinate duty; a by-law; a heretic, a schismatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा 1. उप-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to place or lay upon, place near<BR>to, put into; to place, lay; to put to (as horses to a<BR>carriage); to impose, lay upon, bestow upon, charge<BR>with (as a duty); to lay a command upon, enjoin,<BR>instruct in (with acc.); to place under one's self, to<BR>lie down upon; to place over, cover, conceal; to<BR>locate; to place in addition, to add; to communicate,<BR>cause to share in; (in gram.) to lie or be placed close<BR>to, to precede without the intervention of another<BR>syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदधि
उप-दधि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. placing upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
2. उप-धा, f. imposition, forgery, fraud, deceit,<BR>trick, a false pretence; trial or test of honesty &c., of<BR>four kinds, viz. of loyalty, disinterestedness, conti-<BR>nence, and courage; (in gram.) a penultimate letter.<BR>—उपधा-भृत, अस्, m. a servant who has been<BR>guilty of dishonesty.<BR>—उपधा-रञ्जन, अम्, n.<BR>nasalization of the penultimate (?).<BR>—उपधा-शुचि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, approved, tried, of approved loyalty &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधान|उपधानं
उप-धान, अम्, n. placing or resting upon; that<BR>on which one rests, a pillow, cushion; individuality,<BR>peculiarity; affection, kindness; religious observance<BR>or obligation; poison; excellence, excellent quality;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), employed in placing upon, i. e. used (as a<BR>Mantra) in the putting up (of the sacrificial bricks).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीय|उपधानीयं
उपधानीय, अम्, n. a pillow, cushion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाय
उप-धाय, ind. having placed or rested upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधायिन्
उप-धायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, placing under.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधि|उपधिः
उप-धि, इस्, m. the part of a wheel between the<BR>nave and the circumference; fraud, circumvention; fear,<BR>terror; foundation, (with Buddhists) substratum (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिक|उपधिकः
उपधिक, अस्, m. a cheat, a knave, especially one<BR>who imposes by threats, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधीयमान
उप-धीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being preceded by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधेय
उप-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहित
उप-हित. See p. 170, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधातु|उपधातुः
उपधातु उप-धातु, उस्, m. an inferior mine-<BR>ral, a semi-metal, (seven are specified; pyrites, sulphate<BR>of copper, talc, antimony, red orpiment, yellow orpi-<BR>ment, and calx of brass); secondary secretion of the<BR>body, as the milk, menses, adeps, sweat, teeth, hair,<BR>and lymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधारण|उपधारणं
उपधारण उप-धारण. See under उप-<BR>धृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाव्
उपधाव् उप-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति, -ते,<BR>-वितुम्, to run near to, approach hastily; have re-<BR>course to for assistance; A. to run, glide, soar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधावन|उपधावनः
उप-धावन, अस्, m. a follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधि|उपधिः
उपधि उप-धि. See उप-धा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित उप-धूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, fumigated;<BR>one to whom decline or death is near; being at the<BR>point of death; suffering extreme pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृ
उपधृ उप-धृ, Caus. P. -धारयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to hold up, support, bear, carry; to hold as, consider<BR>as, regard as; to hold in the mind, to comprehend,<BR>perceive, hear, experience, observe; to reflect or me-<BR>ditate on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधारण|उपधारणं
उप-धारण, अम्, n. considering, consideration,<BR>reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधार्य|उपधार्य्य
उप-धार्य, ind. having taken or held up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृति|उपधृतिः
उप-धृति, इस्, f. a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधे
उपधे उप-धे, Caus. A., Ved. -धापयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to rear by suckling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मा
उपध्मा 1. उप-ध्मा, cl. 1. P. -धमति,<BR>-ध्मातुम्, to blow or breathe at or upon, fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मा
2. उप-ध्मा, f. blowing upon, breathing; the<BR>effort of the voice which produces the sound Upa-<BR>dhmānīya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मान|उपध्मानः
उप-ध्मान, अम्, n. blowing upon, breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानिन्
उपध्मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, blowing upon, fanning,<BR>breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानीय|उपध्मानीयः
उप-ध्मानीय, अस्, m. the aspirate Visarga before<BR>the letters प् and फ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्यै
उपध्यै उप-ध्यै, cl. 1. P., ep. also A.<BR>-ध्यायति, -ते, -ध्यातुम्, to think of, remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्वस्त
उपध्वस्त उप-ध्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>ध्वंस् with उप), Ved. spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनक्षत्र|उपनक्षत्रं
उपनक्षत्र उप-नक्षत्र, अम्, n., Ved. a<BR>secondary star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनख|उपनखं
उपनख उप-नख, अम्, n. a disease of the<BR>finger-nails, whitlow, agnail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनगर|उपनगरं
उपनगर उप-नगर, अम्, n. a suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनति|उपनतिः
उपनति उप-नति. See under उप-नम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनदम्
उपनदम् उप-नदम् and उप-नदि, ind.<BR>near a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनन्द
उपनन्द उप-नन्द, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Vasu-deva; a pupil of Śākya-muni; a king of the<BR>Nāgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनन्दक
उप-नन्दक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनम्
उपनम् उप-नम्, cl. 1. P. A. -नमति, -ते,<BR>-नन्तुम्, to bend towards, tend towards, approach;<BR>to come to, arrive at; to fall to the share of; share in<BR>(with acc., dat., or gen.): Caus. -नामयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to lead towards or into the presence of (with gen.),<BR>introduce to; to offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनत|उपनतः
उप-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, bent towards, bent inwards;<BR>brought under, subjected, surrendered; dependent on<BR>(for protection &c.); brought near to; fallen to one's<BR>share; approached, approximate, near (either in time<BR>or space); brought about, produced, existing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनति|उपनतिः
उप-नति, इस्, f., Ved. inclination, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनामुक
उप-नामुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bending towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनय|उपनयः
उपनय उप-नय. See under 1. उप-नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनर
उपनर उप-नर, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>the Nāgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनह्
उपनह् उप-नह्, cl. 4. P. A. -नह्यति, -ते,<BR>-नद्धुम्, to tie up, tie together; to make up into<BR>a bundle, bind together; to inlay; to set with: Caus.<BR>-नाहयति, -यितुम्, to cause to bind together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनहन|उपनहनं
उप-नहन, अम्, n., Ved. a cloth in which any-<BR>thing is bound up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाह|उपनाहः
उप-नाह, अस्, m. a bundle; a plaster, an unguent<BR>applied to a wound or sore; the tie of a lute, the<BR>lower part of the tail-piece where the wires are fixed;<BR>inflammation of the ciliary glands, stye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहन|उपनाहनं
उप-नाहन, अम्, n. putting a plaster upon, apply-<BR>ing an unguent, unction, anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनामन्
उपनामन् उप-नामन्, अ, n. a nickname,<BR>surname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनासिक|उपनासिकं
उपनासिक उप-नासिक, अम्, n. the part sur-<BR>rounding, the nose, that which is near the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षिप्
उपनिक्षिप् उप-नि-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A., 4. P.<BR>-क्षिपति, -ते, -क्षिप्यति, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw<BR>down, place down, deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षेप|उपनिक्षेपः
उप-निक्षेप, अस्, m. a deposit sealed or covered<BR>up so that the contents are unknown; any article<BR>intrusted to one's keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिगम्
उपनिगम् उप-नि-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to meet with, fall into, fall upon, fall into<BR>any state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिग्रह्
उपनिग्रह् उप-नि-ग्रह्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृह्-<BR>णाति, -णीते (Ved. -गृभ्णाति, -णीते), -ग्रहीतुम्, to<BR>press down upon, bring near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधा
उपनिधा उप-नि-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to put or place near, to put down,<BR>place before any one (as a meal &c.), bring near, lead<BR>near to; to produce, cause; to deposit, to intrust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधातृ
उप-निधातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, putting down, laying<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधान|उपनिधानं
उप-निधान, अम्, n. a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधि|उपनिधिः
उप-निधि, इस्, m. a deposit, pledge, property put<BR>under the care of a creditor, friend, &c.; in law this<BR>word ordinarily implies especially a sealed deposit,<BR>but according to some, any article intrusted to a<BR>friend which he may use whilst in his keeping; N.<BR>of a son of Vasu-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिहित
उप-निहित, अस्, आ, अम्, deposited with, intrusted<BR>to; placed near to; offered, presented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपत्
उपनिपत् उप-नि-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -ति-<BR>तुम्, to fly down to; to take place in addition; to<BR>be mentioned incidentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपात|उपनिपातः
उप-निपात, अस्, m. sudden and unexpected attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपातिन्
उप-निपातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling into; attacking<BR>suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपीड्
उपनिपीड् उप-नि-पीड्, cl. 10. P. -पीडयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to oppress, disturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिमन्त्र्
उपनिमन्त्र् उप-नि-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्र-<BR>यते, -यितुम्, to invite, consecrate, inaugurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिमन्त्रण|उपनिमंत्रण|उपनिमंत्रणं
उप-निमन्त्रण, अम्, n. invitation, inauguration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवपन|उपनिवपनं
उपनिवपन उप-निवपन, अम्, n. (rt. वप्),<BR>scattering or pouring down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशिन्
उपनिवेशिन् उप-निवेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ (rt. विश्),<BR>attached to, inherent, annexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषद्
उपनिषद् उप-निषद्, त्, f. (rt. सद् with उप<BR>and नि, implying originally sitting down at the feet<BR>of another in order to listen to his words, and hence<BR>confidential information given in this manner; but<BR>according to native authorities उप-नि-षद् means<BR>‘to destroy ignorance by revealing the knowledge of<BR>the supreme spirit’); esoteric doctrine, secret doctrine,<BR>mysterious or mystical meaning, words of mystery &c.;<BR>certain mystical writings attached to the Brāhmaṇas,<BR>the aim of which is the ascertainment of the secret<BR>sense of the Veda, (they are more than a hundred in<BR>number, and are said to have been the source of<BR>the six darśanas or systems of philosophy; perhaps<BR>the most celebrated is the Bṛhad-āraṇyaka-upaniṣad<BR>attached to the Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa); true know-<BR>ledge; a neighbouring mansion; a lonely place; (at<BR>the end of compounds उपनिषद् sometimes be-<BR>comes उपनिषद.)<BR>—उपनिषत्-कृ, to regard as<BR>a mystical or secret doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषादिन्
उप-निषादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sitting at the feet of a<BR>person; subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्कर|उपनिष्करं|उपनिष्करः
उपनिष्कर उप-निष्कर, अम्, n. (rt. कृ), a<BR>street, a principal or royal road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रम्
उपनिष्क्रम् उप-निष्-क्रम् (-निस्-क्रम्), cl.<BR>1. P. A., 4. P. -क्रामति, -क्रमते (ep. also -क्रा-<BR>मते), -क्राम्यति, -क्रमितुम्, to go out towards,<BR>step out, go out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रमण|उपनिष्क्रमणं
उप-निष्क्रमण, अम्, n. going out towards; a<BR>particular religious rite, one of the Saṃskāras, taking<BR>a child in the fourth month of its age for the first<BR>time into the open air (see Manu 11. 34); a main<BR>or royal road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनी
उपनी 1. उप-नी, cl. 1. P. A. -नयति, -ते,<BR>-नेतुम्, to lead near to, bring near, bring, adduce,<BR>offer; bring information, communicate; to bring<BR>about, produce; to employ, to bring into any state,<BR>bring into one's possession, lead away, lead; to bring<BR>near to one's self (as a teacher receives a pupil for in-<BR>struction), to invest with the sacred thread, initiate;<BR>A. to take into one's service: Caus. -नाययति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause (a master) to receive (a pupil), to<BR>cause to invest with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनय|उपनयः
उप-नय, अस्, m. bringing near, procuring; at-<BR>taining, gaining; employing; the fourth member in<BR>a fivefold syllogism, the application to the special<BR>case in question; leading a youth of the three first<BR>castes to a teacher; initiation; investiture with a pe-<BR>culiar thread or cord worn over the left shoulder and<BR>under the right, by which act spiritual birth is con-<BR>ferred and the youth is reckoned a member of the<BR>twice-born classes; (the cord of the Brāhman is of<BR>cotton, Munja or Kuśa grass; of the Kṣatriya, of Śaṇa<BR>or hemp; and of the Vaiśya, of wool: the youths should<BR>be invested, respectively, from eight to sixteen, from<BR>eleven to twenty-two, and from twelve to twenty-four<BR>years of age.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयन|उपनयनं
उप-नयन, अम्, n. leading to, bringing; leading<BR>to a teacher, initiation. See उप-नय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाय|उपनायः
उप-नाय, अस्, m. or उप-नायन, अम्, n. leading<BR>to a teacher, initiation. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायिक
उप-नायिक, अस्, आ, अम्, leading to; N. of a<BR>Sūtra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीत|उपनीतः
उप-नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought near, approximated;<BR>presented; known; obtained, attained; cited, ad-<BR>duced; (अस्), m. the youth led to a teacher and in-<BR>vested with the characteristic cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीय
उप-नीय, ind. having led towards or brought,<BR>having invested (with the sacred thread).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीयमान
उप-नीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being initiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतव्य
उप-नेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought near; to<BR>be employed or observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतृ
उप-नेतृ, ता, m. one who leads or brings near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनी
उपनी 2. उप-नी (उप-नि-इ), cl. 2. P. -न्येति,<BR>-तुम्, to enter into, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनुद्
