उपसद्
2. उप-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. one who goes near to,<BR>serving, attending, waiting upon; (त्), f. siege, assault;<BR>laying up, accumulating; service; N. of a ceremony<BR>lasting several days and forming part of the Jyotiṣ-<BR>ṭoma ceremony.<BR>—उपसद्-वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. one<BR>who has attendants or worshippers, one who is wor-<BR>shipped.<BR>—उपसद्-व्रतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, observing the<BR>rules of the Upasad, viz. drinking milk in certain<BR>quantities, sleeping on the bare earth, chastity, si-<BR>lence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

