उपसृज्
उपसृज् उप-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति, -स्रष्टुम्,<BR>to pour out or on, to offer, make an oblation; to<BR>join, attach, connect with; to beset with, oppress;<BR>to eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्ग|उपसर्गः
उप-सर्ग, अस्, m. addition; trouble, misfortune;<BR>a portent, a natural phenomenon supposed to forbode<BR>future evil, an eclipse; a disease, possession by an<BR>evil spirit; change occasioned by any disease; indi-<BR>cation or symptom of death; a disease superinduced<BR>on another; an inseparable particle or preposition<BR>prefixed to roots; see कर्म-प्रवचनीय.<BR>—उप-<BR>सर्ग-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, having the character of a<BR>preposition, to be treated like one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्जन|उपसर्जनं|उपसर्ज्जन|उपसर्ज्जनं
उप-सर्जन, अम्, n. pouring on; misfortune,<BR>inauspicious phenomenon, portent, eclipse; passing<BR>by, leaving, eclipsing; any person or thing subordi-<BR>nate or subsidiary to another, a substitute, a repre-<BR>sentative; (in gram.) a word which by composition<BR>or derivation loses its original independance, while<BR>it also determines the sense of another word; for<BR>instance, in the derivative औपिशल, a pupil of Api-<BR>śali, अपिशलि has become the उपसर्जन; so also in<BR>the compound राज-पुरुष (fr. राजन् and पुरुष)<BR>the first loses its independant character when com-<BR>pounded and is therefore the उपसर्जन; (ई), f.<BR>an infusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उप-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, joined, attached, connected<BR>to or with, attended by or accompanied with; seized<BR>or possessed by (evil demons &c.); eclipsed, as the<BR>sun or moon; furnished with an उपसर्ग or prepo-<BR>sition (e. g. the root दा with आ prefixed is said to be<BR>उपसृष्ट); (अम्), n. coition, copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

