उपस्तरण उप-स्तरण. See उप-स्तृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्ति|उपस्तिः
उपस्ति उप-स्ति, इस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. अस् with उप),<BR>Ved. an attendant, a follower, a servant, a subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तु
उपस्तु उप-स्तु, cl. 2. P. A. -स्तौति or -स्त-<BR>वीति, -स्तुते or -स्तुवीते, -स्तोतुम्, to praise, invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुत्
उप-स्तुत्, त्, f., Ved. invocation, praise, invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुत
उप-स्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, invoked, praised; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुति|उपस्तुतिः
उप-स्तुति, इस्, f., Ved. invocation, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुत्य
उप-स्तुत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised or invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तृ
उपस्तृ उप-स्तृ or -स्तॄ, cl. 5. 9. P. A. -स्तृ-<BR>णोति, -णुते, -णाति, -णीते, -स्तर्तुम्, -रितुम् or -री-<BR>तुम्, to spread, arrange, set in order; [cf. Lat.<BR>substerno.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तरण|उपस्तरणं
उप-स्तरण, अम्, n., Ved. spreading out, scatter-<BR>ing; what is spread out; a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तिर्
उप-स्तिर्, f., Ved. scattering about, spreading; what<BR>is spread; a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तीर्ण
उप-स्तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, spread out, arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्त्री
उपस्त्री उप-स्त्री, f. a concubine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्था
उपस्था 1. उप-स्था, cl. 1. P. A. -तिष्ठति, -ते,<BR>-स्थातुम्, to stand near, stand by the side of in order<BR>to serve, wait on, attend on, serve (with acc.); to be<BR>or remain near; stay with; to come near, approach;<BR>to approach a god with prayer, worship; to stand<BR>under in order to support; to approach for inter-<BR>course, have intercourse with; to approach for assist-<BR>ance; to approach with hostile intentions, attack;<BR>to occur, come to pass, arise, be present; to meet<BR>with, obtain; to fall to one's share, come to the<BR>possession of; to conciliate: Caus. P. -स्थापयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to stand near, to provide, present,<BR>furnish with, place upon or near; to produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थ|उपस्थः
उप-स्थ, अस्, m. the lap, middle part in general,<BR>a secure place; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the organs of genera-<BR>tion, especially of a woman; the anus; the haunch<BR>or hip; (अस्, आ, अम्), near, proximate; उपस्थं<BR>कृ, to sit down with the legs bent, make a lap;<BR>उपस्थे कृ, to take on one's lap.<BR>—उपस्थ-<BR>दघ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, reaching to the lap.<BR>—उपस्थ-<BR>निग्रह, अस्, m. restraint of sensual appetite; con-<BR>tinence.<BR>—उपस्थ-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the Indian fig<BR>tree.<BR>—उपस्थ-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sitting in the lap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्था
2. उप-स्था, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. standing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थातृ
उप-स्थातृ, ता, m. an attendant, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थान|उपस्थानं
उप-स्थान, अम्, n. standing near, presence,<BR>proximity, nearness; approaching, appearing, coming<BR>into the presence of, introducing one's self; worship-<BR>ping, waiting on; attendance; obeisance; abode; an<BR>assembly; any object approached with respect, a<BR>sanctuary; obtaining, getting; उपस्थानं कृ, to<BR>give access or scope for action.<BR>—उपस्थान-शाला, f.<BR>the assembly-room of a Buddhist monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानीय
उप-स्थानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stayed with or<BR>near, to be kept near; to be attended on or served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापक
उप-स्थापक, अस्, आ, अम्, placing or bringing near,<BR>causing to obtain; explaining, teaching, a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापन|उपस्थापनं
उप-स्थापन, अम्, n. placing near; attendance,<BR>service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापनीय
उप-स्थापनीय or उप-स्थापयितव्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be placed near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापित
उप-स्थापित, अस्, आ, अम्, placed near, attended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थाप्य
उप-स्थाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed near, to be<BR>produced or made visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थाय
उप-स्थाय, ind. having approached, having<BR>brought near to or assembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायक|उपस्थायकः
उप-स्थायक, अस्, m. a servant; (with Buddhists)<BR>a follower of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायिन्
उप-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, standing near, being pre-<BR>sent, appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थावर
उप-स्थावर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. stopping, not<BR>moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थित|उपस्थितः
उप-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, approached, arrived, arisen,<BR>appeared, present; staying by or near at hand, im-<BR>pending, ready; received, obtained, gained; accom-<BR>plished, taken place, happened; caused, occasioned;<BR>felt; known; clean, cleansed; (in Ved. gram.) in the<BR>Pada text followed by the particle इति; (अम्), n. the<BR>particle इति used in this manner; the position of<BR>words before and after इति; (आ), f., N. of a metre of<BR>four lines of ten syllables each; N. of another metre<BR>of four lines of eleven syllables each.<BR>—उपस्थित-<BR>प्रचुपित, N. of a metre consisting of four lines and<BR>fifty-one syllables.<BR>—उपस्थित-वक्तृ, ता, m. a ready<BR>speaker, an eloquent man.<BR>—उपस्थित-सम्प्रहार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, about to engage in a battle, having battle<BR>at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थिति|उपस्थितिः
उप-स्थिति, इस्, f. standing near, approach, presence,<BR>proximity, arrival; obtaining, getting; effecting, ac-<BR>complishing; remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थेय
उप-स्थेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attended to, to be<BR>worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेह|उपस्नेहः
उपस्नेह उप-स्नेह, अस्, m. (rt. स्निह्), moisten-<BR>ing, attracting moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पिज्
उपस्पिज् उप-स्पिज् (only used in acc. -जम्),<BR>Ved. inconsiderate curiosity or jest (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृश्
उपस्पृश् 1. उप-स्पृश्, cl. 6. P. -स्पृशति,<BR>-स्प्रष्टुम् or -स्पर्ष्टुम्, to touch (water); to<BR>wash or rinse the mouth; to sip water, to sprinkle;<BR>to wash off; to gnash (the teeth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्श|उपस्पर्शः
उप-स्पर्श, अस्, m. touching, contact; washing,<BR>bathing, ablution; rinsing the mouth, sipping water<BR>and ejecting it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शन|उपस्पर्शनं
उप-स्पर्शन, अम्, n. touching; bathing; rinsing<BR>the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शिन्
उप-स्पर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, touching, sipping water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृश्
2. उप-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृश्य
उप-स्पृश्य, ind. having sipped water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृष्ट
उप-स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, touched, sipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्मृति|उपस्मृतिः
उपस्मृति उप-स्मृति, इस्, f. a minor law-<BR>book; eighteen such books are mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्रवण|उपस्रवणं
उपस्रवण उप-स्रवण, अम्, n. (rt. स्रु),<BR>flowing, the periodical flow of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वत्व|उपस्वत्वं
उपस्वत्व उपस्व-त्व, अम्, n. revenue, profit,<BR>what is derived from land or other capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वावत्|उपस्वावन्त्
उपस्वा-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a son of Satrājit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वेद|उपस्वेदः
उपस्वेद उप-स्वेद, अस्, m. (rt. स्विद्), moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहन्
उपहन् उप-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -तुम्, to<BR>kill, injure, destroy, disturb, vex; to waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत|उपहतः
उप-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, injured, impaired, evilly<BR>affected by; struck by lightning &c.; pained, hurt;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">Page0170-c+ 75</a>]<BR>destroyed; infected, polluted, vitiated; impure.<BR>—उप-<BR>हत-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, dazzled, blinded.<BR>—उपहत-धी,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, infatuated.<BR>—उपहतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, agitated in mind, mentally affected as by passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतक
उपहतक, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-fated, unfortunate, un-<BR>lucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्नु
उप-हत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्या
उप-हत्या, f. dazzling of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहन्तव्य
उप-हन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहन्तृ|उपहंतृ
उप-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, having a contrary effect,<BR>disturbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरण|उपहरणं
उपहरण उप-हरण. See under उप-हृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्
उपहस् उप-हस्, cl. 1. P. -हसति, -सितुम्,<BR>to laugh at, deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसित|उपहसितं
उप-हसित, अम्, n. satirical laughter, laughing;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), laughed at, derided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्वन्
उप-हस्वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. laughing at, a derider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास|उपहासः
उप-हास, अस्, m. fun, play, ridicule, derision,<BR>laughing at any one, satirical laughter.<BR>—उपहासा-<BR>स्पद (˚स-आस्˚), अम्, n. a laughing-stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासक|उपहासकः
उप-हासक, अस्, आ, अम्, ridiculing others, jocose;<BR>(अस्), m. a jester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास्य
उप-हास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be laughed at, ridi-<BR>culous, laughable.<BR>—उपहास्य-ता, f. ridiculousness.<BR>—उपहास्य-तां गम्, to expose one's self to<BR>laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्तिका
उपहस्तिका उपहस्तिका, f. (fr. उप-हस्त), a<BR>small bag or box containing condiments or betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहा
उपहा उप-हा, cl. 3. A. -जिहीते, -हातुम्, to<BR>go down, descend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहालक|उपहालकः
उपहालक उपहालक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>country, part of the peninsula of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहिंस्
उपहिंस् उप-हिंस्, cl. 7. 1. P. -हिनस्ति, -हिं-<BR>सति, -सितुम्, to injure, hurt, wound; to overpower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहित
उपहित उप-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part.<BR>of 1. उप-धा, p. 163), placed, deposited, placed in<BR>or upon; preceded by; laid aside, joined; mixed;<BR>ready, deputed to act as a spy, connected with.<BR>—उपहित-भर, अस्, आ, अम्, having the weight<BR>carried; (a better reading has अप-हृत-.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृ
उपहृ उप-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते,<BR>-हर्तुम्, to bring near, offer; to take away, destroy:<BR>Caus. -हारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to offer: Desid.<BR>-जिहीर्षति, to wish to offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरण|उपहरणं
उप-हरण, अम्, n. bringing near; offering gifts<BR>to superiors; presenting victims; distributing or<BR>serving out food; taking, seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरणीय
उप-हरणीय or उप-हर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to<BR>be presented, to be offered as a victim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्तृ|उपहर्त्तृ
उप-हर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, offering victims, serving<BR>out food &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहार|उपहारः
उप-हार, अस्, m. oblation; a complimentary gift,<BR>a present to a superior &c.; an offering to a deity, a<BR>victim &c.; honour; tribute, indemnification, pre-<BR>sents as the price of peace; food distributed to guests<BR>&c.; exultation, mirth (consisting in laughter, dance,<BR>song, bellowing as a bull, bowing, recital of prayer &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारक|उपहारकः
उप-हारक, अस्, m. an oblation &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारिन्
उप-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, giving, presenting; sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारीकृ
उपहारी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make an oblation, to offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृत
उप-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, offered, presented; im-<BR>molated, offered as a victim; served out as food;<BR>taken, collected, gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहोम|उपहोमः
उपहोम उप-होम, अस्, m. a supplementary<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वर|उपह्वरं|उपह्वरः
उपह्वर उप-ह्वर, अस्, m. (rt. ह्वृ), Ved.<BR>bend, curve, arch, slope; declivity; the curved form<BR>of the Soma vessel; (अम्), n. proximity; a solitary<BR>or private place; (अस्), m. a car, a carriage; (ए), ind.<BR>in the proximity of, near to, in a private place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वे
उपह्वे उप-ह्वे, cl. 1. P. A. -ह्वयति, -ते,<BR>-ह्वातुम्, to invoke, call near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहव|उपहवः
उप-हव, अस्, m. calling to, inviting, invitation;<BR>summoning, invoking; उपहवम् इष्, to wish to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">Page0171-a+ 75</a>]<BR>receive an invitation from (with loc., e. g. तस्मिन्न्<BR>इन्द्र उपहवम् ऐच्छत, Indra wished to re-<BR>ceive an invitation from him).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहव्य|उपहव्यः
उप-हव्य, अस्, m., N. of a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूत
उप-हूत, अस्, आ, अम्, invoked, invited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूय
उप-हूय, ind. having invoked or called or ad-<BR>dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वान|उपह्वानं
उप-ह्वान, अम्, n. act of inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु उपांशु, ind. in a low voice, in a<BR>whisper; secretly, in secret (e. g. उपांशु-व्रत, a<BR>vow observed in secret); (उस्), m. a prayer uttered<BR>in a low voice; muttering prayers, reciting them in<BR>a low voice so as not to be overheard; N. of a Soma<BR>offering.<BR>—उपांशु-क्रीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, played with<BR>in secret, made the companion of (a king's) private<BR>amusements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक
उपाक उपाक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अञ्च् with<BR>उप), Ved. brought near to one another, joined,<BR>approximate; (ए), Ved. du. an epithet of night and<BR>morning; (ए), ind. in the next neighbourhood, in<BR>the presence of, before.<BR>—उपाक-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. standing present before the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृ
उपाकृ उपा-कृ (उप-आ-कृ), cl. 5. 8. P. A.<BR>-कृणोति, -नुते, -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to bring<BR>near or towards, to fetch; to summon, invite; to<BR>deliver, commit to, offer, grant, bestow; to acquire,<BR>obtain; to bring about, make preparations for a<BR>sacred action; to undertake, begin; to enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकरण|उपाकरणं
उपा-करण, अम्, n. bringing near, inviting, in-<BR>vitation to begin; a term applied to certain sentences,<BR>called Praiṣas &c., with which one priest invites an-<BR>other to perform a sacrifice; immolation, sacrifice<BR>of an animal duly consecrated; preparation, begin-<BR>ning; commencement of reading the Veda after the<BR>performance of a preparatory rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्मन्|उपाकर्म्मन्
उपा-कर्मन्, अ, n. preparation, beginning; a<BR>ceremony performed before reading the Vedas; be-<BR>ginning to read the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृत|उपाकृतं|उपाकृतः
उपा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought near, invited, ad-<BR>dressed with invitatory sentences; (अस्), m. a sacri-<BR>ficial animal killed during the recitation of prescribed<BR>prayers; attended with evil omens, disastrous, cala-<BR>mitous; (अस्), m. misfortune; a portent, a pheno-<BR>menon announcing calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक्रम्
उपाक्रम् उपा-क्रम् (उप-आ-क्रम्), cl. 1. P. A.,<BR>4. P. -क्रामति, -क्रमते (ep. also -क्रामते),<BR>-क्राम्यति, -क्रमितुम्, to advance against in order<BR>to seize, to fall upon, take possession of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक्षम्
उपाक्षम् उपाक्षम् (उप-अक्˚), ind. before<BR>the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्या
उपाख्या उपा-ख्या (उप-आ-), cl. 2. P. -ख्याति,<BR>-तुम्, to tell a story, narrate; to relate or give an<BR>account about anything (with acc.); to observe (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्य
उपा-ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, observable by the eyes; [cf.<BR>निर्-उपाख्य]; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यान|उपाख्यानं
उपाख्यान (उप-आख्˚), अम्, n. a tale, a short<BR>narrative, an episode; telling or repetition of a story<BR>already heard from another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यानक|उपाख्यानकं
उपाख्यानक, अम्, n. a short tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम्
उपागम् उपा-गम् (उप-आ-), cl. 1. P. -गच्छति,<BR>-गन्तुम्, to go near or towards, to approach, visit;<BR>to return; to pass into any condition or relation; to<BR>undergo, suffer, endure; to occur, to come or fall to<BR>one's share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागत
उपा-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, approached, arrived; occurred,<BR>happened; promised; suffering, feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम|उपागमः
उपा-गम, अस्, m. approach, arrival; occurrence;<BR>promise, agreement; the state of suffering, feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम्य
उपा-गम्य or उपा-गत्य, ind. having approached,<BR>having gone near or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागा
उपागा उपा-गा (उप-आ-गा), cl. 3. P. -जिगाति,<BR>गातुम्, to come near, approach, come to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्नि
उपाग्नि उपाग्नि (उप-अग्नि), ind. near a fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्र|उपाग्रं
उपाग्र उपाग्र (उप-अग्˚), अम्, n. the part<BR>which is next to the end or top; a secondary member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रह्
उपाग्रह् उपा-ग्रह् (उप-आ-ग्रह्), cl. 9. P. A.<BR>-गृह्णाति, -णीते (Ved. -गृभ्णाति, -णीते), -ग्रहीतुम्,<BR>to comprehend, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहण|उपाग्रहणं
उपा-ग्रहण, अम्, n. reading the Vedas after<BR>initiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहायणम्
उपाग्रहायणम् उपाग्रहायणम् or उपाग्रहा-<BR>यणि (उप-अग्˚), ind. towards the day of full moon<BR>in the month Agrahāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाघ्रा
उपाघ्रा उपा-घ्रा (उप-आ-घ्रा), cl. 1. P.<BR>-जिघ्रति, -घ्रातुम्, to smell at; to kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्क्य
उपाङ्क्य उपाङ्क्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. उप-अङ्क),<BR>to be marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्ग|उपांग|उपांगः|उपाङ्गः
उपाङ्ग उपाङ्ग (उप-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a sub-<BR>division; any minor limb or member; a subsidiary<BR>or supplementary work of low value; a supplement<BR>of a supplement; secondary portion of science;<BR>(twelve Aṅgas and Upāṅgas constitute the sacred<BR>writings of the Buddhists); the sectarial mark made<BR>with Sandal &c. on the forehead.<BR>—उपाङ्ग-गीत,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचर्
उपाचर् उपा-चर् (उप-आ-), cl. 1. P. A. -च-<BR>रति, -ते, -रितुम्, Ved. -तवे, &c., to come near to;<BR>to attend upon, be attached to, to wait on, serve; to<BR>be obedient; to treat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचरित|उपाचरितः
उपा-चरित, अस्, आ, अम्, attached to any one's<BR>service, obedient; (in gram.) that rule of Sandhi by<BR>which the sound Visarga becomes स् before क् and प्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचार|उपाचारः
उपा-चार, अस्, m. position (as of a word in a<BR>sentence); procedure; Sandhi by which the sound<BR>Visarga becomes स् before क् and प्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाच्छिद्
उपाच्छिद् उपा-च्छिद् (उप-आ-छिद्), cl. 7. P. A.<BR>-च्छिनत्ति, -च्छिन्ते, -च्छेत्तुम्, to tear away from,<BR>cut off from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाज्
उपाज् उपाज् (उप-अज्), cl. 1. P. A., Ved. उपा-<BR>जति, -ते, -जितुम्, to bring near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाजेकृ
उपाजे-कृ, to support.<BR>—उपाजे-कृत्य or उपाजे-<BR>कृत्वा, having supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाञ्च्
उपाञ्च् उपाञ्च् (उप-अञ्च्) or उपाच् (उप-अच्),<BR>cl. 1. P. A. उपाञ्चति, -ते, or उपाचति, -ते, -चितुम्,<BR>to draw (water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाञ्जन|उपांजन|उपांजनं
उपाञ्जन उपाञ्जन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. अञ्ज् with<BR>उप), anointing, plastering the ground with cow<BR>dung &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपातिगम्
उपातिगम् उपाति-गम् (उप-अति-गम्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-गच्छति, -गन्तुम्, to pass over, cross (a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाती
उपाती उपाती (उप-अति-इ), cl. 2. P. उपात्य्-<BR>एति, -तुम्, to pass over; to be added as a surplus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्यय|उपात्ययः
उपात्य्-अय, अस्, m. neglect or disobedience of<BR>customs; disorderly behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादा
उपादा उपा-दा (उप-आ-दा), cl. 3. A. -दत्ते,<BR>दातुम्, to receive, accept; to gain, acquire; to<BR>take, appropriate to one's self; to take away or off,<BR>carry off, steal; to seize, lay hold of, gather; to draw<BR>(water); to assume a form; to feel, perceive, consider,<BR>regard; to take in addition, include, comprise; to<BR>employ, apply, use; to undertake, begin; to men-<BR>tion, enumerate: Caus. -दापयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to employ or apply; to make use of: Desid. P.<BR>-दित्सति, to strive to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्त|उपात्तं|उपात्तः
उपा-त्त, अस्, आ, अम्, received, accepted, acquired,<BR>gained, obtained; appropriated; taken away; seized,<BR>gathered; shaped; felt, perceived, regarded; com-<BR>prised; employed, used; begun; enumerated; allowed<BR>in argument, granted, conceded; (अस्), m. an elephant<BR>out of rut.<BR>—उपात्त-रंहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, acquiring<BR>speed, quick, fleet.<BR>—उपात्त-शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>taking up arms, armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादान|उपादानं
उपा-दान, अम्, n. taking, acquiring, taking away,<BR>abduction, appropriating to one's self, accepting, em-<BR>ployment, using, becoming familiar with; mentioning,<BR>enumeration; saying, speaking; including, containing;<BR>abstraction, withdrawing the organs of sense and per-<BR>ception from the outer world; cause, motive; imme-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">Page0171-c+ 74</a>]<BR>diate or proximate cause; the formal or distinct form,<BR>the material cause; a double meaning, an expression<BR>conveying a sense besides that which appears in-<BR>tended; (with Buddhists) conception; effort or ex-<BR>ertion of body or speech.<BR>—उपादान-कारण, अम्,<BR>n. a proximate cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादाय
उपा-दाय, ind. having seized, containing; includ-<BR>ing, inclusive of; together with; by means of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादेय|उपादेयः
उपा-देय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or received,<BR>acceptable, admissible; to be chosen; to be selected,<BR>excellent, admirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिक|उपादिकः
उपादिक उपादिक, अस्, m. a sort of insect;<BR>[cf. उत्पादक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिश्
उपादिश् उपा-दिश् (उप-आ-), cl. 6. P. A. -दि-<BR>शति, -ते, -देष्टुम्, to advise, show, point out, to indi-<BR>cate, inform, declare; to prescribe, give an order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाद्रु
उपाद्रु उपा-द्रु (उप-आ-), cl. 1. P. -द्रवति,<BR>-द्रोतुम्, to run near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधा
उपाधा उपा-धा (उप-आ-), cl. 3. P. A. -द-<BR>धाति, -धत्ते, -धातुम्, to place near, place upon;<BR>to offer; render, make, effect, fix; to keep, hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधि|उपाधिः
1. उपा-धि, इस्, m. (for 2. see below), deceit, de-<BR>ception, disguise (in the Vedānta this is especially<BR>applied to certain natural forms or properties, con-<BR>sidered as disguises of the spirit); that which more<BR>closely defines, a discriminative or distinguishing pro-<BR>perty, an attribute, a peculiarity, an indispensable<BR>condition; limitation (e. g. अन्-उपाधि-रमणीयो<BR>देशः, a country beautiful without limitation, i. e.<BR>altogether beautiful); a title, a discriminative appella-<BR>tion, a nickname; a purpose, an occasion, an object;<BR>(in logic) a special cause for a general effect; (in<BR>rhetoric) the natural character of species, quality or<BR>action. उपाधि-तस्, ind. in consequence of a pe-<BR>culiarity. (At the end of a compound the affix क<BR>may be added to उपाधि, e. g. अस्त्य्-उपाधिक,<BR>having ‘is’ as an attribute.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहित|उपाहितः
उपा-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, deposited, placed; put on,<BR>worn; joined, annexed; agreed upon, made or done<BR>mutually; (अस्), m. a fiery portent, a meteor, a comet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधि|उपाधिः
उपाधि 2. उपा-धि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. ध्यै with<BR>उप-आ), reflection on duty; virtuous reflection; a<BR>man who is careful to support his family. (For 1.<BR>see under उपा-धा above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिक
उपाधिक उपाधिक (उप-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>exceeding, supernumerary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्याय|उपाध्यायः
उपाध्याय उपाध्य्-आय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 5. इ<BR>with उप-अधि), a sub-teacher who instructs in a<BR>part only of the Veda or in grammar and the other<BR>Vedāṅgas, and is therefore inferior to the Ācārya<BR>who instructs in the whole Veda with the Kalpa and<BR>Upaniṣads (see Manu II. 141); a spiritual teacher,<BR>a teacher in general; (आ), f. a female preceptor; (ई),<BR>f. a female teacher or the wife of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायानी
उपाध्यायानी, f. the wife of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानस
उपानस उपानस, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. उप and<BR>अनस्), Ved. being on a carriage; (अम्), n. the space<BR>in a carriage; carriage-load; anything placed on a<BR>carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानह्
उपानह् उपा-नह्, त्, f. (rt. नह्), a sandal, a<BR>shoe.<BR>—उपानद्-गूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with<BR>a shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानी
उपानी उपा-नी (उप-आ-), cl. 1. P. A. -नयति,<BR>-ते, -नेतुम्, to lead or carry or bring near or<BR>towards; lead away, carry off; to initiate, conse-<BR>crate; [cf. उप-नी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानुवाक्य
उपानुवाक्य उपानुवाक्य (उप-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. an epithet of Agni; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>section of the Taittirīya-Saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त|उपांत|उपान्तः
उपान्त उपान्त (उप-अन्˚), अम्, n. proximity<BR>to the edge or margin, border, edge; the angle of<BR>the eye; immediate proximity; the last letter but<BR>one; (अस्, आ, अम्), near to the end, last but one;<BR>near.<BR>—उपान्त-सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, coming near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तिक|उपांतिक
उपान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, near, proximate, neighbour-<BR>ing; (अम्), n. proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानिय
उपानिय, अस्, आ, अम्, last but one; (अस्), m. the<BR>corner of the eye; (अम्), n. vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाप्
उपाप् उपाप् (उप-आप्), cl. 5. P. -आप्नोति,<BR>-प्तुम्, to reach, to arrive at: Desid. उपेप्सति, to<BR>wish to reach, to desire to win over or conciliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाप
उपाप in दुर्-उपाप, अस्, आ, अम्, difficult to be<BR>obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाप्ति|उपाप्तिः
उपाप्ति, इस्, f. reaching, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेप्सा
उपेप्सा, f. desire to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाप्रछ्
उपाप्रछ् उपा-प्रछ् (उप-आ-), cl. 6. P. -पृच्-<BR>छति, -प्रष्टुम्, to take leave of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाभृति
उपाभृति उपा-भृति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. भृ with<BR>उप-आ), Ved. act of bringing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपामन्त्र्य
उपामन्त्र्य उपा-मन्त्र्य (उप-आ-), ind. having<BR>taken leave, having received permission to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाय|उपायः
उपाय उपाय. See under 1. उपे 3rd col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाया
उपाया उपा-या (उप-आ-), cl. 2. P. -याति, -तुम्,<BR>to approach, arrive at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायात
उपा-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, approached; (अम्), n. arrival;<BR>an event, an accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्
उपार् उपार् (उप-ऋ), cl. 3. P., Ved. उपे-<BR>यर्ति, उपार्तुम्, -रितुम् or -रीतुम्, to offend against,<BR>make a mistake; to injure: Caus. P. उपार्पयति,<BR>यितुम्, to bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार|उपारः
उपार, अस्, m. or उपारण, अम्, n., Ved. a mis-<BR>take, offence, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम्
उपारम् उपा-रम् (उप-आ-), cl. 1. A. -रमते,<BR>-रन्तुम्, to sport, take one's pleasure, delight in;<BR>to cease; to rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारत
उपा-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, delighted; engaged in, occu-<BR>pied with; frequenting, resorting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम|उपारमः
उपा-रम, अस्, m. engaging in, going to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाराध्
उपाराध् उपा-राध् (उप-आ-), cl. 5. P. -राध्-<BR>नोति, -राद्धुम्, to serve, wait upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाराध्य
उपा-राध्य, ind. having served, having waited on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारुद्
उपारुद् उपा-रुद् (उप-आ-), cl. 2. P. -रोदिति,<BR>-रोदितुम्, to weep, deplore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारुह्
उपारुह् उपा-रुह्, क्, f. (rt. रुह् with उप<BR>and आ), Ved. the shoot of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारूढ
उपा-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, grown, increased.<BR>—उपा-<BR>रूढ-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, whose affection has in-<BR>creased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्
उपार्ज् उपार्ज् (उप-अर्ज्), cl. 1. P. उपार्जति,<BR>जितुम्, to bring near to: Caus. उपार्जयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to bring near, convey near, acquire, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जक
