उपाहार (उप-आह्˚), अस्, m. slight refreshment<BR>(consisting of fruits, sweetmeats, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहृत
उपा-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, offered, prepared; seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाह्वे
उपाह्वे उपा-ह्वे (उप-आ-), cl. 1. P. A. -ह्व-<BR>यति, -ते, -ह्वातुम्, to challenge, invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपे
उपे 1. उपे (उप-इ), cl. 2. P. उपैति, -तुम्,<BR>to go near, approach (as a friend or enemy); come<BR>near to, arrive at, reach; to go to (a master), become<BR>a pupil; to undergo, perform, undertake, devote one's<BR>self to; to pass into any state, to fall into (misfortune<BR>&c.), incur, be present at; to obtain; to fall to one's<BR>share; to befal; to regard as, admit, acknowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाय|उपायः
उपाय, अस्, m. approaching, approach; that by<BR>which one reaches an aim, a means, an expedient, a<BR>way, stratagem; a means of success against an enemy<BR>(four of which are usually enumerated, sowing dissen-<BR>sion, negotiation, bribery, and open attack); joining<BR>(in singing &c.).<BR>—उपाय-चतुष्टय, अम्, n. the<BR>four expedients against an enemy; see above.<BR>—उपा-<BR>य-चिन्ता, f. devising an expedient, thinking of a re-<BR>source.<BR>—उपाय-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, fertile in expedients,<BR>contriving, provident.<BR>—उपाय-तस्, ind. by some<BR>means or expedient.<BR>—उपाय-तुरीय, अस्, m. a fourth<BR>means, punishment.<BR>—उपाय-त्व, अम्, n. state of<BR>being provided with means.<BR>—उपाय-योग, अस्, m.<BR>application of means or combination of expedients.<BR>—उपायान्तर (˚य-अन्˚), अम्, n. a remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायन|उपायनं
उपायन, अम्, n. approaching, going near to, going<BR>to a teacher, becoming a pupil, engaging in any re-<BR>ligious observance; undertaking, accepting; a present,<BR>a gift, a complementary or respectful gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिक
उपायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, conducive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिन्
उपायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, approaching; having sexual in-<BR>tercourse with; expert in the use of means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायु
उपायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going near to, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत
उपेत, अस्, आ, अम्, come near, approached, arrived<BR>at, come near to, present, existent; accompanied by,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">Page0173-a+ 71</a>]<BR>endowed with, possessed of, having, possessing; sur-<BR>rounded, invested; fallen into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेति|उपेतिः
उपेति, इस्, f., Ved. approach, arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतृ
उपेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, approaching, going near to;<BR>contriving, a contriver, one who employs expedients,<BR>one who comes as an assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत्य
उपेत्य, ind. having approached, having gone near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेय|उपेयः
उपेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone to or approached,<BR>to be effected by any means; assailable; to be sought,<BR>to be had recourse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयिवस्
उपेयिवस्, आन्, युषी, अत्, accompanied or followed<BR>by, associated with, united; obtained, got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपे
उपे 2. उपे (उप-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. उपैति, -तुम्,<BR>to come near to, go to, approach, visit; to have<BR>sexual intercourse with; to undergo, incur, fall into<BR>(misfortune &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्ष्
उपेक्ष् उपेक्ष् (उप-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A. उपेक्षते,<BR>षितुम्, to look at, regard; to perceive; to notice,<BR>have regard to; to consider, expect; to overlook,<BR>disregard; to neglect, to quit, abandon; to despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्ष
उपेक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śvaphalka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षक
उपेक्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, disregarding, neglecting,<BR>looking at inattentively, disdaining; patient, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षण|उपेक्षणं
उपेक्षण, अम्, n. overlooking, looking at without<BR>interest or attention, disregarding, neglecting, disdain-<BR>ing; leaving, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षणीय
उपेक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be neglected or dis-<BR>regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षा
उपेक्षा, f. overlooking, negligence, neglect; in-<BR>diference, contempt, disdain; abandoning, leaving;<BR>endurance, patience; dissent; trick, deceit (as one of<BR>the minor expedients in war); regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षित
