उपोह्
उपोह् उपोह् (उप-ऊह्; in some of its senses<BR>connected with उप-वह्), cl. 1. P. उपोहति, -हितुम्,<BR>to push or impel towards; to push under, insert; to<BR>bring near, produce; to accumulate: Pass. उपोह्यते,<BR>to be brought about, to advance, begin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
2. उपोढ, अस्, आ, अम्, brought near, brought about,<BR>advanced, commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोह|उपोहः
उपोह, अस्, m., Ved. adding, accumulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोह्यमान
उपोह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being brought about or<BR>commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त|उप्तः
उप्त उप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part. of rt.<BR>वप्), sown (as seed).<BR>—उप्त-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ploughed after sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्ति|उप्तिः
उप्ति, इस्, f. sowing seeds.<BR>—उप्ति-विद्, त्, m. an<BR>agriculturist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त्रिम
उप्त्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, sown, cultivated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्य
उप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be scattered or sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्यमान
उप्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज्
उब्ज् उब्ज्, cl. 6. P. उब्जति, उब्जाञ्-चकार,<BR>उब्जिष्यति, औब्जीत्, उब्जितुम्, to press<BR>down, subdue, keep under; to make straight: Desid.<BR>उब्जिजिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज
उब्ज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्जित
उब्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, pressed down, subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ्
उभ् उभ् or उम्भ्, cl. 6. 9. 7. P., Ved.<BR>उभति or उम्भति, उभ्नाति, उनप्ति,<BR>impf. औनप्, उवोभ or उम्भाञ्-चकार, उभितुम्<BR>or उम्भितुम्, to compact together; to confine; to<BR>cover over, fill with; (Sāy.) to break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ उभ, pron. (nom. du. उभौ, pl. उभे;<BR>said to be fr. rt. उभ् above, and connected with<BR>Gr. ἄμφω Lat. ambo; Slav. oba; Lith. abbù;<BR>Goth. bai, ba), both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभय|उभयं|उभयः
उभय, अस्, ई, अम्, (pl. m. f. n. ए, आस्, आनि, only<BR>used in sing. and pl., but by some authorities also in<BR>dual), both.<BR>—उभय-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed<BR>of both qualities.<BR>—उभयङ्-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>effecting or accomplishing both.<BR>—उभय-चर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘moving in or on both,’ living in water<BR>and on land or in the air, amphibious.<BR>—उभय-<BR>द्युस्, ind., Ved. on both days, on two subsequent days;<BR>the day past and to come.<BR>—उभय-भाग-हर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, applicable to two purposes, taking two<BR>shares or parts; (अम्), n. a medicine that acts in two<BR>ways, as an emetic and a purge.<BR>—उभय-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. furnished with or containing both.<BR>—उभय-विद्या, f. the twofold science, i. e. religious<BR>knowledge and acquaintance with worldly affairs.<BR>—उभय-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, appearing under two<BR>forms.<BR>—उभय-विपुला, f., N. of a metre.<BR>—उभ-<BR>य-वेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, serving two masters, receiving<BR>wages from both.<BR>—उभय-व्यञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the marks of both sexes.<BR>—उभय-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m. a dilemma.<BR>—उभयात्मक (˚य-आत्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, belonging to both.<BR>—उभयानुमत (˚य-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, agreed to or accepted mutually or on both<BR>sides.<BR>—उभयार्थम् (˚य-अर्˚), ind. for a double<BR>object, as for prosperity on earth and happiness in<BR>heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतस्
उभयतस्, ind. from both sides, on both sides, to<BR>both sides; in both cases.<BR>—उभयतः-क्ष्णुत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. two-edged.<BR>—उभयतो-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a double row of teeth (man, animal, &c.).<BR>—उभयतो-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, looking either way, two-faced.<BR>—उभयतो-ह्रस्व, अस्, आ, अम्, having a short<BR>vowel on both sides, (an accented vowel) produced<BR>by two short vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयत्र
उभयत्र, ind. in both places, on both sides; in<BR>both cases, both times.<BR>—उभयत्रोदात्त (˚र-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having an Udātta accent on both sides;<BR>resulting from the blending of two Udātta accents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयथा
उभयथा, ind. in both ways; in both cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभया
उभया, ind., Ved. in both ways.<BR>—उभया-दत्,<BR>अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having teeth on both sides.<BR>—उभया-<BR>विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. being on both sides, partaking of<BR>both.<BR>—उभया-हस्ति, ind., Ved. as much as may be<BR>grasped with both hands.<BR>—उभया-हस्त्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. filling both hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयीय
उभयीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयेद्युस्
उभये-द्युस्, ind. on both days, on two subse-<BR>quent days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्
उम् उम्, ind. an interjection of anger, in-<BR>terrogation, promise or assent, of cordiality or pacifi-<BR>cation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम|उमः
उम उम, अस्, m. a city, a town; a wharf,<BR>a landing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमा
उमा उमा, f. (in the first sense perhaps fr.<BR>rt. वे), flax (Linum Usitatissimum); the plant Cur-<BR>cuma; N. of the daughter of Himavat and Menā,<BR>and wife of Rudra or Śiva (she is also called Pārvatī<BR>and Durgā); light, splendor; fame, reputation;<BR>quiet, tranquillity; night. According to the Kumāra-<BR>sambhava. 1. 26, the name उमा is derived from उ मा,<BR>O do not (practice austerities)! the exclamation ad-<BR>dressed to Pārvatī by her mother.<BR>—उमा-कट, अस्<BR>or अम्, m. or n. the pollen of flax.<BR>—उमा-गुरु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of the mountain Himālaya as father of Umā.<BR>—उमागुरु-नदी, f., N. of a river.<BR>—उमा-पति,<BR>इस्, m. epithet of Śiva as husband of Umā.<BR>—उमा-<BR>पति-धर, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—उमापति-सेविन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, worshipping Śiva.<BR>—उमा-वन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of the town Vana-pura or Devī-koṭa (Devi Cote).<BR>—उमा-सहाय, अस्, m., N. of Śiva as companion of<BR>Umā.<BR>—उमा-सुत, अस्, m., N. of Kārttikeya as son<BR>of Umā.<BR>—उमेश (उमा-ईश), अस्, m., N. of Śiva as<BR>lord of Umā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्य|उम्यं
उम्य, अम्, n. a field of linseed or of Curcuma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्बर|उंबर|उंबरः|उम्बरः
उम्बर उम्बर, अस्, m. the upper timber of<BR>a door frame; N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्बी|उंबी
उम्बी उम्बी, f. the stalks of wheat or barley<BR>fried over a fire of wet grass, considered as a tonic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्बुर|उंबुर|उंबुरः|उम्बुरः
उम्बुर उम्बुर, अस्, m. the upper timber of<BR>a door frame; [cf. उम्बर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्लोचा
उम्लोचा उम्लोचा, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्
उर् उर्, to go; (a Sautra root, i. e. one<BR>occurring only in grammatical Sūtras and not in the<BR>Dhātu-pāṭha.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर|उरः
उर उर, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi said to be of<BR>the family of Vāta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरक
उरक उरक, अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's<BR>attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरग|उरगः
उरग उर-ग, अस्, m. (fr. उर = उरस् and<BR>rt. गम्), a snake (‘going on the breast’); in<BR>mythology a Nāga or semi-divine serpent usually re-<BR>presented with a human face of great beauty; lead;<BR>(ई), f. a female snake; (आ), f., N. of a town.<BR>—उरग-<BR>प्रतिसर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a serpent for a wedding<BR>ring.<BR>—उरग-भूषण, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva,<BR>whose ornaments consist of snakes.<BR>—उरग-राज,<BR>अस्, m. the king of snakes, Śeṣa or Vāsuki.<BR>—उरग-<BR>सार-चन्दन, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of sandal-wood.<BR>—उरग-स्थान, अम्, n. the abode of the Nāgas,<BR>i. e. Pātāla, a region below the earth (not to be con-<BR>founded with hell).<BR>—उरगारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m. Garuḍa,<BR>the bird of Viṣṇu; a large crane; (lit. ‘the enemy of<BR>the snakes.’)<BR>—उरगाशन (˚ग-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>Garuḍa; a gigantic crane; (‘whose food consists of<BR>serpents.’)<BR>—उरगास्य (˚ग-आस्˚), अम्, n. a kind of<BR>spade.<BR>—उरगेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚), अस्, m. the king of<BR>the snakes, Śeṣa or Vāsuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरङ्ग|उरंग|उरंगः|उरङ्गः
उरङ्-ग and उरङ्-गम, अस्, m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरण|उरणः
उरण उरण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 4. ऋ),<BR>a ram, a sheep, a young ram; a certain demon slain<BR>by Indra; a cloud?; (ई), f. a ewe.<BR>—उरणाक्ष<BR>(˚ण-अक्˚) or उरणाक्षक, अस्, m. the plant Cassia<BR>Alata or Tora.<BR>—उरणाख्य (˚ण-आख्˚) or उरणा-<BR>ख्यक, अस्, m. the plant Tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणक|उरणकः
उरणक, अस्, m. a ram; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरभ्र|उरभ्रः
उरभ्र उरभ्र, अस्, m. (fr. उर = ऊर्णा and<BR>rt. भृ?), a ram; a kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररी
उररी उररी, ind. (perhaps connected with<BR>उरु; cf. उरी, ऊरी, ऊररी), a particle implying assent,<BR>admission, extension, expansion, diffusion; often com-<BR>pounded with the roots, अस्, भू, and कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकृ
उररी-कृ, to allow, admit, assent.<BR>—उररी-कार,<BR>अस्, m. a promise, agreement; admission.<BR>—उररी-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, promised, agreed; spread, ex-<BR>tended, diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरश|उरशः
उरश उरश, अस्, m., N. of a country in-<BR>habited by a warrior-tribe; (आ), f., N. of a town;<BR>also उरसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्
उरस् उरस्, n. (fr. rt. वृ, to cover; cf. उरु),<BR>the breast, the bosom; (आस्, आस्, अस्), best, excellent;<BR>उरसि कृ, to press any one to one's breast; to assent.<BR>—उरः-क्षत, अम्, n. injury to the chest, breaking<BR>a blood-vessel in the chest, consumption.<BR>—उरः-<BR>सूत्रिका, f. a pearl necklace hanging over the breast.<BR>—उरः-स्थल, अम्, n. the breast, the bosom.<BR>—उरश्-छद, अस्, m. a cuirass, breastplate, armour,<BR>mail.<BR>—उरसि-ज or उरसि-रुह, अस्, m. the female<BR>breast (lit. ‘produced on the chest’).<BR>—उरसि-लोमन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, having hairs on the breast.<BR>—उरस्-कट, अस्,<BR>m. the sacrificial thread hung round the neck and<BR>upon the breast, as sometimes worn.<BR>—उरस्-तस्, ind.<BR>from the breast, in the direction of the breast.<BR>—उरस्-<BR>त्राण, अम्, n. a breastplate, cuirass, coat of mail.<BR>—उरस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, broad-chested, full-breasted,<BR>strong.<BR>—उरो-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going on the breast<BR>(as a reptile), creeping, crawling.<BR>—उरो-ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m. disease of the chest, pleurisy.<BR>—उरो-घात, अस्,<BR>m. striking or beating the breast; pain in the chest.<BR>—उरो-ज, अस्, m. the female breast (lit. ‘born on the<BR>chest’).<BR>—उरो-बृहती, f., N. of a metre.<BR>—उरो-<BR>भूषण, अम्, n. an ornament of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस
उरस, अस्, आ, अम्, having a strong broad breast;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">Page0174-b+ 78</a>]<BR>(अम्), n. (at the end of compounds) best, most ex-<BR>cellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिल|उरसिलः
उरसिल, अस्, आ, अम्, broad-chested, having a full<BR>or broad breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्य|उरस्यः
1. उरस्य, nom. P. उरस्यति, -यितुम्, to be strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्य|उरस्यः
2. उरस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, situated in the breast; pec-<BR>toral; (labour or exertion) requiring an effort of the<BR>chest; legitimate (as a son or daughter); one born<BR>from a married couple of the same tribe or caste;<BR>excellent (i. e. the very heart, the breast or best part).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरा
उरा उरा, f. (fr. rt. वृ?), Ved. a ewe.<BR>—उरा-मथि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. killing sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उराह|उराहः
उराह उराह, अस्, m. a horse of a pale colour<BR>with dark legs; (probably a foreign word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरी
उरी उरी, ind. (cf. उररी, ऊररी, ऊरी), a particle<BR>implying (especially in composition with the roots<BR>अस्, भू, and कृ) promise, assent, admission, ex-<BR>tension, diffusion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकृ
उरी-कृ, to promise, allow, admit, assent.<BR>—उरी-<BR>कार, अस्, m. promise, admission, extension.<BR>—उरी-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, promised, extended, spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरु|उरुः
उरु उरु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ (fr. rt. वृ, to cover),<BR>wide, spacious; extended, great, large; much, excessive;<BR>excellent, precious, valuable; (उ), n., Ved. wide space,<BR>space, room; उरु कृ, to grant space or scope, give<BR>opportunity; (उ), ind. far, far off; (वी), f. the wide<BR>earth, see उर्वी next col.; comparative वरीयस्, super-<BR>lative वरिष्ठ; [cf. Gr. εὐρύς Hib. ur, ‘very;’<BR>ur-ard, ‘very high;’ uras, ‘power, ability.’]<BR>—उरु-<BR>काल or उरुकालक, अस्, m. the creeper Cucumis<BR>Colocynthis.<BR>—उरु-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. making room,<BR>granting space.<BR>—उरु-क्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. far-<BR>stepping, making wide strides; of high rank; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—उरु-क्षय, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>a spacious dwelling, a wide habitation; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>occupying spacious dwellings, an epithet of Mitra and<BR>Varuṇa and the Maruts; (अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—उरु-क्षिति, इस्, f., Ved. a spacious or comfortable<BR>dwelling.<BR>—उरु-क्षेप, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—उरु-गव्यूति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a wide domain<BR>or territory.<BR>—उरु-गाय, अस्, आ, अम् (गाय fr. rt. गा),<BR>Ved. far-going, far-striding; an epithet of Viṣṇu,<BR>the Aśvins, Soma, and Indra; offering wide space or<BR>scope for movement; (Sāy.) praised by the great;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. wide space,<BR>scope for movement or free and unconfined motion.<BR>—उरुगाय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, offering ample space<BR>for motion, unconfined,<BR>—उरु-गूला (?), f., Ved., N.<BR>of a snake.<BR>—उरु-चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>wide wheels.<BR>—उरु-चक्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. allowing<BR>unrestrained motion; (Sāy.) granting ample assist-<BR>ance.<BR>—उरु-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. far-seeing;<BR>epithet of Mitra-Varuṇa and of the Ādityas.<BR>—उरु-<BR>ज्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having a wide path or range.<BR>—उरु-ज्रयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or उरु-ज्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>moving in a wide course, extending over a wide space;<BR>(Sāy.) of great impetuosity, of mighty impetus; epi-<BR>thet of Agni and of Indra.<BR>—उरु-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>widest, greatest.<BR>—उरु-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, wider,<BR>greater, larger.<BR>—उरु-ता, f., Ved. wideness; opening.<BR>—उरु-ताप, अस्, m. great heat.<BR>—उरु-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>magnitude, vastness.<BR>—उरु-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>giving a broad stream (of milk, as a cow).<BR>—उरु-<BR>प्रथस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. wide-spreading, widely ex-<BR>tended, far-spread.<BR>—उरु-बिल, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. having<BR>a wide opening.<BR>—उरुब्ज (उरु-उब्ज ?), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. widely opened; (Sāy.) excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>—उरु-मार्ग, अस्, m. a long road.<BR>—उरु-मुण्ड,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—उरु-युग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>furnished with a broad yoke.<BR>—उरु-लोक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. containing wide space, widely extended; (Sāy.)<BR>widely illuminating.<BR>—उरु-विक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>valiant, mighty.<BR>—उरु-विन्दु, उस्, m., N. of a Fla-<BR>mingo (in the Hari-vaṃśa, whose condition was that<BR>of a hunter in a former birth).<BR>—उरु-विल्वा, f., N. of<BR>a village.<BR>—उरुविल्वा-कल्प, N. of a place.<BR>—उरु-<BR>व्यचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. occupying wide space,<BR>widely extending, widely capacious; (आस्), m. a ma-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">Page0174-c+ 73</a>]<BR>lignant spirit, an imp or goblin.<BR>—उरु-व्यञ्च्, अन्,<BR>उरूची, अक्, Ved. extending far; far-reaching, capacious;<BR>perceived in a distant place (as a sound); containing<BR>wide spaces.<BR>—उरु-व्रज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a<BR>wide domain or territory.<BR>—उरु-शंस, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. praising aloud; (Sāy.) to be praised by many;<BR>reigning over a wide territory; (Sāy.) praised by<BR>many; epithet of Varuṇa, Pūṣan, the Ādityas, In-<BR>dra, and Soma.<BR>—उरु-शर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. finding<BR>refuge everywhere throughout the universe, widely<BR>pervading.<BR>—उरु-षा, आस्, आस्, अम् (rt. सन्), Ved.<BR>granting wide space or free scope; (Sāy.) granting<BR>much.<BR>—उरु-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, magnanimous, of a<BR>generous or noble nature.<BR>—उरु-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>stentorian.<BR>—उरु-हार, अस्, m. a valuable necklace.<BR>—उरू-णस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. broad-nosed, having a<BR>good scent (as a hound).<BR>—उरु-अङ्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>mountain; the ocean.<BR>—उरु-अज्र, अस्, m., Ved. an<BR>extensive field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवु|उरुवुः
उरुवु, उस्, m. or उरुवुक, अस्, m. or उरुवूक,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. the plant Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुष्य
उरुष्य, nom. P., Ved. उरुष्यति, to desire wide<BR>scope or freedom, to escape from (with acc.); to protect,<BR>preserve, secure, defend from (with abl.), to avert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुष्या
उरुष्या, f., Ved. (only in inst.) with protecting<BR>hands; (Sāy.) with desire to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुष्यु
उरुष्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going to a distant place;<BR>(Sāy.) desiring to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरूल
उरूल, अस्, आ, अम्, liking space; fond of expatiating;<BR>free, unrestrained, disobedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्विया
उर्विया, ind., Ved. far, far off, far and near, widely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वी|उर्व्वी
उर्वी, f. the wide earth, the earth, the soil; space,<BR>the open space or great expanse comprising the six<BR>spaces, viz. the four quarters of the sky with the upper<BR>and lower spaces; a river; (वी), du., Ved. the two<BR>worlds, or heaven and earth.<BR>—उर्वी-धर, अस्, m.<BR>a mountain; the serpent Śeṣa.<BR>—उर्वी-पति, इस्, m.<BR>a king.<BR>—उर्वी-भृत्, त्, m. a mountain.<BR>—उर्वी-<BR>रुह, अस्, m. a tree, ‘growing on the earth.’<BR>—उर्वीश<BR>(˚वी-ईश), अस्, m. a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्या
उर्व्या, f. protection, security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्यूति
उर्व्य्-ऊति, इस्, इस्, इ, (fr. उर्विया-ऊति ?), Ved. able to<BR>help or defend far and near; (Sāy.) granting extensive<BR>protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुण्ड
उरुण्ड उरुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a demon;<BR>also of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुरी
उरुरी उरुरी, ind. a particle of assent and<BR>admission. See उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरूक|उरूकः
उरूक उरूक, अस्, m. an owl; [cf. उलूक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरूची
उरूची उरूची. See उरु-व्यञ्च् under उरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्जित|उर्ज्जित|उर्ज्जितं
उर्जित उर्जित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वृज्), aban-<BR>doned, left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्जिहाना
उर्जिहाना उर्जिहाना, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णनाभ|उर्णनाभः|उर्ण्णनाभ
उर्णनाभ उर्ण-नाभ, अस्, m. a spider; [cf.<BR>ऊर्ण-नाभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णा
उर्णा उर्णा, f. wool, felt, the hair of camels<BR>&c.; a circle of hair between the eyebrows. See ऊर्णा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द्
उर्द् उर्द्, cl. 1. A. ऊर्दते, ऊर्दाञ्-चक्रे,<BR>ऊर्दिष्यते, और्दिष्ट, ऊर्दितुम्, to mea-<BR>sure; to play; to be easy or cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द्र|उर्द्रः
उर्द्र उर्द्र, अस्, m. an otter. See उद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्
उर्व् उर्व्, cl. 1. P. ऊर्वति, ऊर्वाञ्-चकार,<BR>ऊर्वितुम्, to kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व|उर्व्व
उर्व उर्व, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वट|उर्वटः|उर्व्वट|उर्व्वटः
उर्वट उर्वट, अस्, m. a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वरा|उर्व्वरा
उर्वरा उर्वरा, f., Ved. fertile soil, yielding<BR>every kind of crop, field sown with corn; land in<BR>general; a mixed mass of fibres, wool, &c.; jocular<BR>term for curled hairs; N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—उर्वरा-<BR>जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. acquiring fields.<BR>—उर्वरा-पति,<BR>इस्, m., Ved. master of the fields sown with corn.<BR>—उर्वरा-सा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. granting fields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वरी
उर्वरी, f., Ved. tow, fibres drawn out of the distaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वर्य
उर्वर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to a field<BR>which is sown with corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वशी|उर्व्वशी
उर्वशी उर्वशी, f. (fr. उरु-वशी), Ved. wish,<BR>ardour, hot desire; N. of an Apsaras or nymph of<BR>Indra's heaven, who became the wife of Purūravas;<BR>she is also identified with the Gaṅgā.<BR>—उर्वशी-<BR>नाम-माला, f., N. of a glossary of synonymous<BR>words by an anonymous author.<BR>—उर्वशी-रमण,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of Aila or Purūravas, the second king<BR>of the lunar race and the husband of the Apsaras<BR>Urvaśī.<BR>—उर्वशी-वल्लभ or उर्वशी-सहाय, अस्,<BR>m. epithet of Purūravas; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वारु|उर्वारुः|उर्व्वारु|उर्व्वारुः
उर्वारु उर्वारु, उस्, m. a kind of cucumber,<BR>Cucumis Usitatissimus. See इर्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वारुक|उर्वारुकं
उर्वारुक, अम्, n. the fruit of the above plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वारू
उर्वारू, ऊस्, f., Ved. = the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्
उल् उल्, उलति, to burn; (a Sautra root,<BR>i. e. one mentioned only in grammatical<BR>Sūtras but not occurring in the Dhātu-pāṭha.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल|उलः
उल उल, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of wild animal;<BR>N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलप|उलपः
उलप उलप, अस्, m., Ved. a shrub, bush;<BR>a wick; the stalk of a shrub used as a wick (?); a<BR>creeping plant, a spreading creeper; the grass or reed<BR>Saccharum Cylindricum; N. of a pupil of Kalāpin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलप्य|उलप्यः
उलप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. connected with or refer-<BR>ring to a shrub &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलिन्द|उलिंदः|उलिन्दः
उलिन्द उलिन्द, अस्, m., N. of a country;<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुप|उलुपः
उलुप उलुप, अस्, अम्, m. n. a spreading<BR>creeper; (अस्), m. the reed Saccharum Cylindricum.<BR>See उलप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुपिन्
उलुपिन् उलुपिन् or उलपिन् or उलूपिन्, ई, m.<BR>a guinea-pig, a porpoise or fish resembling it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुलि|उलुलिः
उलुलि उलुलि, इस्, इस्, इ or इस्, m., Ved. ulula-<BR>tion, howling, a howl; [cf. Lat. ululabilis, ululatus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूक|उलूकं|उलूकः
उलूक उलूक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. वल्),<BR>an owl; N. of a country and people (pl.), and of their<BR>king, who appears in the Mahā-bhārata as a hero on<BR>the side of the Kurus; a son of Viśvā-mitra; of Śakuni;<BR>an epithet of Indra; N. of a king of the Nāgas; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of the reed Saccharum Cylindricum; [cf. Lat.<BR>ulula; Germ. Eule; Old Germ. uwila, ûla; Eng.<BR>owl; Fr. hulotte.]<BR>—उलूक-यातु, उस्, m., Ved. a<BR>demon in the shape of an owl.<BR>—उलूकाश्रम (˚क-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m. Indra's hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखल|उलूखलं|उलूखलः
उलूखल उलूखल, अम्, n. a wooden mortar<BR>used for cleansing rice from the husk &c.; bdellium,<BR>a gummy substance; (अस्), m. a staff of Udumbara<BR>wood, carried on certain occasions; N. of an evil<BR>spirit.<BR>—उलूखल-सुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pressed out<BR>or pounded in a mortar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलक|उलूखलकं
उलूखलक, अम्, n., Ved. a mortar; bdellium, a<BR>gummy substance, or the plant which produces it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलिक
उलूखलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, pounded in a mortar,<BR>cleansed from the husk; (at the end of a compound)<BR>using as a mortar (e. g. दन्तोलूखलिक, using the<BR>teeth as a mortar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूट
उलूट उलूट or उतूल or कुलूट, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूत|उलूतः
उलूत उलूत, अस्, m. a large snake, the Boa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूप
उलूप उलूप, अस्, m. a spreading creeper;<BR>(अम्), n. a sort of grass; (ई), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Nāga Kauravya, married to Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूलु
उलूलु उलूलु, उस्, उस्, उ or उस्, m. ululation,<BR>howling. See उलुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्का
उल्का उल्का, f. (said to be fr. rt. 1. उष्), a fiery<BR>phenomenon in the sky, a meteor, fire falling from<BR>heaven; a firebrand; torch; fire, a flame, title of a<BR>grammar; [cf. Cambro-Brit. ulw, ‘ashes.’]<BR>—उल्का-<BR>जिह्व, अस्, m., N. of a Rakṣas.<BR>—उल्का-धारिन्, ई,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">Page0175-b+ 75</a>]<BR>इणी, इ, a torch-bearer.<BR>—उल्का-पात, अस्, m. the fall<BR>of a meteor.<BR>—उल्का-मालिन्, ई, m., N. of one of Śiva's<BR>attendants.<BR>—उल्का-मुख, अस्, m. a demon or<BR>goblin (with a face or mouth of fire who eats what is<BR>vomited, having been a negligent Brāhman in his<BR>lifetime); N. of a descendant of Ikṣvāku; (ई), f.<BR>a fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्कुषी
उल्कुषी, f. a fiery phenomenon in the sky, a<BR>meteor; firebrand.<BR>—उल्कुषी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>accompanied by fiery phenomena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्मुक|उल्मुकं|उल्मुकः
उल्मुक, अम्, n. a firebrand, wood burning or<BR>burnt as charcoal; N. of a son of Bala-rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्मुक्य
उल्मुक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or connected<BR>with a firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ब|उल्बं
उल्ब उल्ब or उल्व, अम्, n. (fr. rt. वृ), Ved.<BR>the bag which surrounds the embryo; the vulva; the<BR>womb; a cave; [cf. Lat. alvus, vulva; Lith. urwa,<BR>üla; Hib. uile, ‘a corner.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्बण|उल्बणः
उल्बण or उल्वण, अस्, आ, अम्, thick, clotted,<BR>abundant; much, exceeding, superfluous, immense,<BR>strong, powerful; abundantly furnished with; manifest;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Vasiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ब्य|उल्ब्यं
उल्ब्य, अस्, आ, अम्, with आपः, the fluid connected<BR>with the embryo; (अम्), n. excess and vitiation of<BR>any of the three humors of the body, bile, phlegm<BR>or wind; any calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लकसन|उल्लकसनं
उल्लकसन उल्लकसन, अम्, n. horripilation,<BR>erection of the hairs of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लग्न
उल्लग्न उल्लग्न, अस्, m. the lagna (q. v.) of<BR>any particular place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घ्|उल्लंघ्
उल्लङ्घ् उल्-लङ्घ् (उद्-ल्˚), cl. 1. P. A. -लङ्-<BR>घति, -ते, -घितुम्, to leap over, pass over or beyond,<BR>to cross over; transgress, exceed, violate, spurn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घन|उल्लंघन|उल्लंघनं|उल्लङ्घनं
उल्-लङ्घन, अम्, n. leaping or passing over or<BR>beyond; transgression, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घनीय
उल्-लङ्घनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be transgressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घित|उल्लंघित
उल्-लङ्घित, अस्, आ, अम्, jumped over or across,<BR>passed over or beyond; exceeded, transgressed, vio-<BR>lated, apostatized.<BR>—उल्लङ्घित-शासन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>transgressing orders, rebellious, disobedient.<BR>—उल्लङ्-<BR>घिताध्वन् (˚त-अध्˚), आ, आ, अ, having passed over<BR>the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घ्य|उल्लंघ्य
उल्-लङ्घ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be passed over or be-<BR>yond, to be crossed; to be disregarded or neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लभ्
उल्लभ् उल्-लभ् (उद्-लभ्), cl. 1. A. -लभते,<BR>-लब्धुम्, to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लम्बित|उल्लंबित
उल्लम्बित उल्-लम्बित (उद्-ल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>erected, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लल|उल्ललः
उल्लल उल्-लल, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. लल्), covered<BR>with thick hair; shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललत्
उल्-ललत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shaking, trembling; moving<BR>irregularly or convulsively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललित|उल्ललितः
उल्-ललित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, trembling, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाल
उल्-लाल, N. of a metre of two verses, each con-<BR>taining 15 + 13 syllabic instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लस्
उल्लस् उल्-लस् (उद्-लस्), cl. 1. P. -लसति, -सि-<BR>तुम्, to jump up, sport, play, dance, flash, shine:<BR>Caus. P. -लासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to jump up or<BR>play; to cause to shine; to divert, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लस
उल्-लस, अस्, आ, अम्, sporting, bright, shining;<BR>merry, happy; going out, issuing.<BR>—उल्लस-ता, f.<BR>splendor, brilliancy; mirth, happiness, going forth,<BR>issuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसत्
उल्-लसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sporting, dancing, brilliant,<BR>shining; wantoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसित
उल्-लसित, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, bright, splendid;<BR>happy; ejected, brought to the top or surface, drawn<BR>up, uplifted, brandishing.<BR>—उल्लसित-हरिण-केतन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having its deer-marked banner gleaming<BR>or fluttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लास|उल्लासः
उल्-लास, अस्, m. jumping or leaping up, happiness,<BR>joy; light, splendor; (in rhetoric) giving prominence<BR>to any subject by comparison or opposition; division<BR>of a book, chapter, section (e. g. आचारोल्लास, a chapter<BR>treating of customs and observances).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासन
उल्-लासन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to leap or dance;<BR>(अम्), n. splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासित
उल्-लासित, अस्, आ, अम्, delighted, overjoyed, re-<BR>joicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाघ|उल्लाघः
उल्लाघ उल्लाघ, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>लाघ्; in some of its senses perhaps related to<BR>लघु), recovered from sickness, convalescent; dex-<BR>trous, clever, intelligent; pure; happy, delighted;<BR>wicked; black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाप|उल्लापः
उल्लाप उल्-लाप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. लप् with उद्),<BR>calling out in a loud voice; change of voice in grief,<BR>sickness, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लापिक|उल्लापिकः
उल्लापिक, अस्, आ, अम्, betraying, indicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लापिन्
उल्-लापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाप्य|उल्लाप्यं
उल्-लाप्य, अम्, n. a kind of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिख्
उल्लिख् उल्-लिख् (उद्-लिख्), cl. 6. P. -लिखति,<BR>-लेखितुम्, to scratch, scrape, cut up, scarify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखत्
उल्-लिखत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, scratching, scrap-<BR>ing; scarifying, making lines or streaks above or on<BR>high; painting, writing; bearing, raising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखित|उल्लिखितः
उल्-लिखित, अस्, आ, अम्, scraped, scratched; scarified;<BR>thrown up, tossed; painted, delineated; written over<BR>or above; pared, made thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेख|उल्लेखः
उल्-लेख, अस्, m. description; (in rhetoric) de-<BR>scription of an object according to the different<BR>impressions caused by its appearance^1; speaking, utter-<BR>ance, pronunciation.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेखन|उल्लेखनं
उल्-लेखन, अम्, n. scraping, scratching, scarifying,<BR>paring; digging; vomiting; raising up, elevating;<BR>uttering, utterance; writing, painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेख्य
उल्-लेख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be scraped or pared;<BR>to be written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिङ्गित|उल्लिंगित
उल्लिङ्गित उल्-लिङ्गित (उद्-ल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dis-<BR>criminated, distinguished, known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुञ्चन|उल्लुंचन|उल्लुंचनं
उल्लुञ्चन उल्-लुञ्चन, अम्, n. plucking out<BR>the hair; cutting the hair; pulling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुण्ठा|उल्लुंठा
उल्लुण्ठा उल्-लुण्ठा, f. (fr. rt. लुण्ठ् with उद्),<BR>irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लू
उल्लू उल्-लू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (fr. rt. लू with उद्),<BR>cutting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेख|उल्लेखः
उल्लेख उल्-लेख. See उल्-लिख् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोच|उल्लोचः
उल्लोच उल्-लोच, अस्, m. (rt. लोच्), an awning,<BR>a canopy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोप्य
उल्लोप्य उल्-लोप्य, अम्, n. (rt. लुप्), N. of a<BR>song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोल|उल्लोलः
उल्लोल उल्-लोल (उद्-ल्˚), अस्, m. a large wave<BR>or billow; a surge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्व|उल्वं
उल्व उल्व and उल्वण. See उल्ब and उल्-<BR>बण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उवट|उवटः
उवट उवट, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast on<BR>Vedic works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशङ्गव|उशंगव
उशङ्गव उशङ्गव, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशत्|उशन्त्
उशत् उशत्, अन्, अती, अत् (fr. rt. वश्, to desire),<BR>loving, desirous, auspicious, pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशधक्
उश-धक्, Ved. only in connection with वन,<BR>wood (fr. उश, i. e. rt. वश् and धज्, i. e. rt. धे?;<BR>according to native etym. connected with rt. दह्),<BR>(fire) consuming (wood &c.) with desire (?); (Sāy.)<BR>desiring and burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशनस्
उशनस्, आ, m., N. of a sage mentioned in the<BR>Veda and having the epithet kāvya (उशना काव्यः);<BR>in the epic poems he is identified with Śukra, the<BR>regent of the planet Venus, and described as the pre-<BR>ceptor of the Asuras or Daityas, and possessor of vast<BR>knowledge; N. of the author of a Dharma-śāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशना
उशना, ind., Ved. with desire, joyfully, with haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशाना
उशाना, f., Ved. the desired one; N. of a plant,<BR>from which the Soma juice is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशिज्
उशिज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. desiring, striving earnestly;<BR>devoted to, willing; (क्), m. ghee or boiled butter;<BR>fire; (क्), f., N. of a female slave, the mother of<BR>Kakṣīvat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशित
उशित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशी
उशी, ईस्, f. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशेन्य
उशेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be wished, to be<BR>longed for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशती
उशती उशती, f. (for रुशती, scil. वाच्), inju-<BR>rious discourse; cutting speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशनस्
उशनस् उशनस्. See under उशत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीनर|उशीनरः
उशीनर उशीनर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>or country, Kandahar; (अस्), m. the king of this<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीर|उशीरं|उशीरः
उशीर उशीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. वश्), the fragrant root of the plant Andropogon<BR>Muricatus; (ई), f. a sort of grass, a small sort of<BR>Saccharum.<BR>—उशीर-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—उशीर-वीज, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीरक|उशीरकं
उशीरक, अम्, n. the fragrant root of the plant<BR>Andropogon Muricatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीरिक
उशीरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, trading in or selling Uśīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्
उष् 1. उष्, cl. 1. P. ओषति, औषत्, उवोष<BR>or ओषाञ्-चकार, ओषिष्यति, औषीत्, ओषि-<BR>तुम्, to burn; to punish; to consume; to kill, injure:<BR>Caus. ओषयति, -यितुम्: Desid. ओषिषिषति; [cf.<BR>Lat. uro, ustus; Gr. αὔω, αὖος Hib. usga, ‘incense.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
1. उष, अस्, m. bdellium; saline earth; (अम्), n.<BR>fossile salt. See ऊष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषण|उषणं
उषण, अम्, n. black pepper; the root of Piper<BR>Longum; (आ), f. Piper Longum; Piper Chaba;<BR>dried ginger. See ऊषण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषप|उषपः
उषप, अस्, m. fire; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषा
1. उषा, f. burning, scorching. (For 2. see next col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित|उषितः
1. उषित or उष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt; quick,<BR>expeditious. (For 2. see next col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ण|उष्णः
उष्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (opposed to शीत), hot, warm;<BR>pungent, acrid; sharp, active; impetuous, warm,<BR>passionate; (अस्, अम्), m. n. heat, warmth, the<BR>hot season (June and July); sunshine; a deep or<BR>feverish sigh; (अस्), m. an onion; N. of a prince;<BR>(आ), f. heat; consumption; bile.<BR>—उष्ण-कर, अस्,<BR>m. the sun (‘having hot rays’).<BR>—उष्ण-काल, अस्,<BR>m. the hot season.<BR>—उष्ण-ग, अस्, m. the hot sea-<BR>son.<BR>—उष्ण-गु, उस्, m. the sun (‘having hot rays’).<BR>—उष्णङ्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, making hot or warm,<BR>heating.<BR>—उष्ण-ता, f. or उष्ण-त्व, अम्, n. heat,<BR>warmth.<BR>—उष्ण-दीधिति, इस्, m. the sun (‘having<BR>hot rays’).<BR>—उष्ण-नदी, f. the hot river; N. of the<BR>Vaitaraṇī or river of hell.<BR>—उष्ण-रश्मि or उष्ण-<BR>रुचि, इस्, m. the sun (‘having hot rays’).<BR>—उष्ण-<BR>वारण, अस्, अम्, m. n. an umbrella or parasol, a<BR>chattar.<BR>—उष्ण-वाष्प, अस्, m. hot vapour, steam;<BR>tears.<BR>—उष्ण-वीर्य, अस्, m. Delphinus Gangeticus.<BR>—उष्ण-वेताली, f., N. of a female deity.<BR>—उष्णांशु<BR>(˚ण-अं˚), उस्, m. the sun (‘having hot rays’).<BR>—उष्-<BR>णागम (˚ण-आग्˚), अस्, m. approach of the heat,<BR>the hot season, consisting of two months, about June<BR>and July.<BR>—उष्णाभिगम (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>hot season.<BR>—उष्णासह (˚ण-अस्˚), अस्, m. the cold<BR>season.<BR>—उष्णोदक (˚ण-उद्˚), अम्, n. warm or<BR>hot water, to be drunk on certain occasions; it be-<BR>longs to the six prāṇa-karāṇi.<BR>—उष्णोपगम<BR>(˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, m. the hot season, summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णक|उष्णकः
उष्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, sharp, smart, active; suffering<BR>pain; sick of fever; warming, heating; bent, inclin-<BR>ing, stooping; (अस्), m. the heat, the hot season<BR>(lasting for two months, about June and July); re-<BR>volving, turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णालु
उष्णालु, उस्, उस्, उ, suffering from heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिका
उष्णिका, f. rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिमन्
उष्णिमन्, आ, m. heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीकृ
उष्णी-कृ, cl. 8. 5. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कृ-<BR>णोति, -णुते, -कर्तुम्, to make warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीगङ्ग
उष्णी-गङ्ग, the hot Gaṅgā, i. e. the Badarī,<BR>having hot sources; (perhaps merely a wrong reading<BR>for तूष्णीङ्गङ्ग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्म|उष्मं|उष्मः
उष्म, अस्, m. heat; the hot season (June and<BR>July); spring (April and May); anger, warmth of<BR>temper; ardour, eagerness; [cf. उष्मन् and ऊष्-<BR>मन्.]<BR>—उष्म-ता, f. = उष्ण-ता, q. v.<BR>—उष्म-<BR>पा, आस्, m. a spirit of an inferior order, a deceased<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">Page0176-b+ 75</a>]<BR>ancestor; [cf. ऊष्म-प.]<BR>—उष्म-भास्, स्, m. the sun<BR>(‘having hot beams’).<BR>—उष्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, heated,<BR>burning, smoking.<BR>—उष्म-स्वेद, अस्, m. a vapour<BR>bath.<BR>—उष्मागम (˚म-आग्˚), अस्, m. the hot sea-<BR>son.<BR>—उष्मान्वित (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, enraged.<BR>—उष्मोपगम (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m. the hot season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मक|उष्मकः
उष्मक, अस्, m. the hot season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मन्
उष्मन्, आ, m. heat, ardour, steam; the hot season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्माय
उष्माय, nom. A. उष्मायते, to emit heat or<BR>steam. See ऊष्माय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मायण|उष्मायणः
उष्मायण, अस्, m. the hot season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्
उष् 2. उष् (connected with rt. 3. वस्, to<BR>shine; used as a noun but only in the form उषस्),<BR>Ved. light, morning, dawn; उषस् तिस्रः, morning,<BR>midday, and evening. (The words उषस् and उषा<BR>below are connected by native authorities with 1. उष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
2. उष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining, brilliant; (अस्),<BR>m. early morning, dawn, day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्
उषस्, आस्, f. morning light, dawn, morning; per-<BR>sonified as the daughter of Heaven and sister of the<BR>Ādityas; evening light; उषसौ or उषासौ, du. the<BR>two dawns, i. e. night and day; the outer passage<BR>of the ear; the Malaya range; (सी), f. the end of<BR>the day, twilight; [cf. Gr. ἠώς Lat. aurora; Lith.<BR>auszra; Goth. uh-tvô; Old Germ. uohta.]<BR>—उषर्-<BR>बुध्, भुत्, त्, त्, Ved. awaking with the morning light,<BR>early awaked.<BR>—उषर्-बुध, अस्, m. fire; a child.<BR>—उषासा-नक्ता, f. du., Ved. dawn and night.<BR>—उषो-<BR>देवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, whose deity is the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्य
1. उषस्य, nom. P. उषस्यति, -यितुम्, to be-<BR>come day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्य
2. उषस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, sacred to the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषा
2. उषा, f. morning light, dawn, morning; twilight,<BR>night; a cow; N. of a wife of Bhava (who was a<BR>manifestation of Rudra); of a daughter of Bāṇa and<BR>wife of Aniruddha; (आ), ind. at day-break; at night;<BR>at twilight (?).<BR>—उषा-काल, अस्, m. a cock.<BR>—उषा-<BR>पति, इस्, m. an epithet of Aniruddha, the son of<BR>Kāmadeva and husband of Uṣā.<BR>—उषा-रमण,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Aniruddha.<BR>—उषेश (उषा-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्र|उस्रः
1. उस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to or seen in the<BR>morning; bright; shining; clear; (Sāy. उत्सरण-<BR>शील) rising on high; (अस्), m. a ray of light; (आ),<BR>f. morning light, dawn, morning; light, bright sky.<BR>—उस्र-धन्वन्, आ, m. having a bright bow; an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>—उस्र-यामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. going<BR>out in the early morning light (as the carriage of the<BR>Aśvins); going out at daylight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रिया
उस्रिया, f., Ved. brightness, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
उष 3. उष, अस्, आ, अम् (connected with rt.<BR>वश्), wishing, desiring; (अस्), m. a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषत्|उषन्त्
उषत्, अन्, m., N. of a son of Suyajña.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषङ्गु|उषंगु|उषंगुः|उषङ्गुः
उषङ्गु उषङ्गु, उस्, m. an epithet of Śiva;<BR>[cf. उशङ्गव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषती
उषती उषती, f. injurious discourse; cutting<BR>speech. See उशती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषद्गु
उषद्गु उषद्गु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Svāhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषद्रथ
उषद्रथ उषद्रथ, अस्, m. a son of Titikṣu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्त
उषस्त उषस्त, अस्, m., N. of a man, with<BR>the patronymic cākrāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित|उषितः
उषित 2. उषित, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 1. वस्), in-<BR>habited, dwelt; fixed, remaining in or on; stale.<BR>—उषितङ्-गवीन, अस्, आ, अम्, formerly inhabited<BR>by cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित्वा
उषित्वा, ind. having resided in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्य
उष्य, ind. (irreg. form for उषित्वा), having<BR>resided or dwelt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषीर|उषीरं|उषीरः
उषीर उषीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the root of<BR>Andropogon Muricatum. See उशीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्र|उष्ट्रः
उष्ट्र उष्ट्र, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 1. उष्),<BR>a buffalo; a bull with a hump; a camel; a cart, a<BR>waggon; N. of an Asura; (ई), f. a she-camel; an<BR>earthen vessel in the shape of a camel.<BR>—उष्ट्र-<BR>कर्णिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—उष्ट्र-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">Page0176-c+ 71</a>]<BR>काण्डी, f. a flower of a red colour.<BR>—उष्ट्र-क्रोशिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, making a noise like a camel.<BR>—उष्ट्र-<BR>गोयुग, अम्, n. a couple of camels.<BR>—उष्ट्र-ग्रीव,<BR>अस्, m. hemorrhoids.<BR>—उष्ट्र-धूसर-पुच्छिका,<BR>f. the plant Tragia Involucrata.<BR>—उष्ट्र-पादिका, f.<BR>the plant Jasminum Sambac.<BR>—उष्ट्र-यान, अम्, n.<BR>a camel-litter, a vehicle drawn by camels.<BR>—उष्ट्र-<BR>शिरो-धर, अम्, n. hemorrhoids, piles, bleeding piles.<BR>—उष्ट्र-स्थान, अम्, n. a stable for camels; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), born in a camel-stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्टृ
उष्टृ, टा, m., Ved. a bull drawing a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रिका
उष्ट्रिका, f. a she-camel; an earthen vessel of the<BR>shape of a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ण|उष्णः
उष्ण उष्ण. See under 1. उष् 1st col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिह्
उष्णिह् उष्णिह्, क्, f. (fr. उद्-स्निह् ?), N. of<BR>a Vedic metre of three Pādas, the first two containing<BR>eight each, and the third twelve syllables; a classical<BR>metre of four Pādas of seven syllables; a brick sacred<BR>to the metre Uṣṇih.<BR>—उष्णिक्छन्दस्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the metre Uṣṇih.<BR>—उष्णिग्-गर्भा, f.,<BR>N. of a Gāyatrī of three Pādas of six, seven, eleven<BR>syllables respectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिहा
उष्णिहा, f. the metre Uṣṇih; (आस्), pl., Ved. the<BR>nape of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीष|उष्णीषं|उष्णीषः
उष्णीष उष्णीष, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>connected with उष्ण), anything wound round the<BR>head; a turban, a diadem; a bandage of any kind;<BR>a distinguishing mark; the hair with which a Buddha<BR>is born and which indicates his future sanctity.<BR>—उष्-<BR>णीष-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wearing a turban, turbaned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीषिन्
उष्णीषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, furnished with a turban; an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्म|उष्मं|उष्मः
उष्म उष्म. See under 1. उष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्य
उष्य उष्य. See under 2. उषित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्यल
उष्यल उष्यल, अम्, n., Ved. the frame (of<BR>a bed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्र|उस्रः
उस्र 2. उस्र, अस्, m. a bull; (आ), f. a cow; the<BR>plant Anthericum Tuberosum. (For 1. see last col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रि
उस्रि, इस्, f., Ved. a cow (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रिक|उस्रिकः
उस्रिक, अस्, m., Ved. a small ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रिय|उस्रियः
उस्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to or coming<BR>from a cow or ox; (अस्), m. an ox; (आ), f. a cow;<BR>a calf; milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रीय
उस्रीय, nom. P. उस्रीयति, -यितुम्, to desire or<BR>wish for a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उह्
उह् उह्, cl. 1. P. ओहति, उवोह, ओहितुम्, to hurt<BR>or give pain; to kill, to destroy. See ऊह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उहन्
उहन्, Ved. a wrong reading for उदन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उहान|उहानः
उहान, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उहू
उहू उहू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (fr. rt. वह्), Ved. bear-<BR>ing, carrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उह्यमान
उह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being conveyed, borne along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उह्यगान
उह्यगान उह्यगान, a various reading for<BR>ऊह्यगान, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ 1. ऊ, the sixth letter of the alphabet,<BR>corresponding to उ long, and having the sound of<BR>that letter in the word रुले.<BR>—ऊ-कार, अस्, m. the<BR>letter or sound ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ 2. ऊ, ind. an interjection of compassion,<BR>of regard; an incipient particle used at the beginning<BR>of a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ 3. ऊ, ऊस्, m. the moon; epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ 4. ऊ (fr. rt. अव्), ‘a preserver’ (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊत|ऊतं
1. ऊत, अस्, आ, अम्, favoured, preserved, promoted,<BR>loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊति|ऊतिः
1. ऊति, इस्, f. favouring, protecting, promoting, aid,<BR>assistance, help, favour, kindness, friendly feeling, affec-<BR>tion, wish, desire, striving after, hastening towards,<BR>delight, enjoyment, sport, play, distillation; (अयस्),<BR>pl. objects of enjoyment, as food &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊम|ऊमं|ऊमः
ऊम, अस्, m., Ved. a good friend, an affectionate<BR>companion, an intimate associate; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>town or country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊअट
ऊअट ऊअट, a various reading for उवट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊठ्
ऊठ् ऊठ्, a various reading for उठ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढ|ऊढः
ऊढ 1. ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वह् or 1. ऊह्,<BR>for 2. ऊढ see 2. ऊह्), carried as a load or burden;<BR>married; (आ), f. a bride, a wife espoused according<BR>to the ritual.<BR>—ऊढ-कङ्कट, अस्, आ, अम्, armed,<BR>mailed.<BR>—ऊढ-भार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>married a wife.<BR>—ऊढ-वयस्, आस्, m. a young man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढय
ऊढय, nom. (fr. ऊढ or ऊढि) P. ऊढयति,<BR>aor. औजढत् or औजिढत्, or औडिढत्, to carry (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढि|ऊढिः
ऊढि, इस्, f. carrying, bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊणीतेजस्
ऊणीतेजस् ऊणी-तेजस्, आस्, m., N. of a Buddha;<BR>(a various reading has ऊर्णीतेजस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊत|ऊतं
ऊत 2. ऊत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वे), woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊति|ऊतिः
2. ऊति, इस्, f. weaving, sewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधन्
ऊधन् ऊधन् and उधर्, forms used in the<BR>Veda for some of the cases of ऊधस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधस्
ऊधस् ऊधस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. वह्. In<BR>the Veda the forms ऊधर् and ऊधन् are used for<BR>some of the cases, e. g. sing. nom. ऊधर्, gen. abl.<BR>ऊध्नस्, loc. ऊधन् or ऊधनि; pl. inst. ऊधभिस्,<BR>loc. ऊधस्सु), an udder; a covered secret place where<BR>only friends are admitted; the bosom; the breast of<BR>a mother; the udder of the sky, i. e. the clouds. In<BR>classical Sanskrit the form ऊधन् appears only in<BR>the fem. of adjective compounds, cf. अध्य्-ऊध्नी,<BR>कुण्डोध्नी, घटोध्नी, पीनोध्नी; [cf. Gr. οὖθαρ<BR>Lat. uber; Germ. ûtar, euter; Angl. Sax. uder;<BR>Eng. udder; Hib. uit, uitche.]<BR>—ऊधस्-वती, f.<BR>having a full udder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधन्य|ऊधन्यं
ऊधन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from the udder;<BR>(अम्), n. milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधस्य|ऊधस्यं
ऊधस्य, अम्, n. milk, ‘produced from the udder.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊन|ऊनं
ऊन ऊन, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. अव् and<BR>opposed to पूर्ण, अति-रिक्त, अधिक), wanting, de-<BR>ficient, defective, short of any quantity, less than the<BR>right number, not sufficient; less (in number, size,<BR>or degree), minus, fewer, smaller, inferior, &c. (e. g.<BR>ऊन-द्विवर्ष, not quite two years old; द्वाभ्याम्<BR>ऊन, less by two; अल्पोन, ‘less by a little,’ ‘a little<BR>less.’ Prefixed to any even decimal numeral from<BR>twenty up to a hundred, ऊन serves to denote one<BR>less than the even ten, e. g. ऊन-विंशति, twenty<BR>minus one or nineteen; ऊन-त्रिंशत्, thirty minus<BR>one; ऊनत्रिंश, the thirtieth minus one or twenty-<BR>ninth: so also with other numerals prefixed, e. g.<BR>पञ्चोन-त्रिंशत्, thirty minus five or twenty-five;<BR>एकोनचत्वारिंश, the fortieth minus one or thirty-<BR>ninth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊनक
ऊनक, अस्, आ, अम्, not sufficient, less, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊनय
ऊनय, nom. P. ऊनयति, -यितुम्, to leave defi-<BR>cient or unfinished; to deduct or lessen; to mete<BR>out in small quantities; to measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊनित
ऊनित, अस्, आ, अम्, lessened by subtraction or deduc-<BR>tion, less, fewer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊम्
ऊम् ऊम्, ind. an interjection of interroga-<BR>tion; of anger; of reproach, abuse, envy, and arro-<BR>gance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊम|ऊमं|ऊमः
ऊम ऊम. See under 4. ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊय्
ऊय् ऊय्, cl. 1. A. ऊयते = वे, वयति, to<BR>weave, sew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊररी
ऊररी ऊररी, ind. a particle of assent and<BR>diffusion; ऊररी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, allowed, promised.<BR>See उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरी
ऊरी, ind. = ऊररी; see उरी.<BR>—ऊरी-कृत्य, ind.<BR>having promised, agreed, assented to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरु|ऊरुः
ऊरु ऊरु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. ऊर्णु), the<BR>thigh; N. of a son of Manu Cākṣuṣa; (वी), f. the<BR>middle of the thigh or a principal vein situated there.<BR>When ऊरु is used at the end of a compound the<BR>fem. form may end in either short or long उ, but<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">Page0177-b+ 79</a>]<BR>more properly in the latter (e. g. वामोरुस् or वामो-<BR>रूस्, a beautiful-thighed woman; रम्भोरु and<BR>वरोरु, O beautiful-thighed one; voc. cases of<BR>वरोरू and रम्भोरू).<BR>—ऊरु-ग्लानि, इस्, f. weakness<BR>of the thigh.<BR>—ऊरु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born from the<BR>thigh; (अस्), m. a Vaiśya.<BR>—ऊरु-दघ्न or ऊरु-<BR>द्वयस or ऊरु-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, reaching to the<BR>thighs, as high as the thighs.<BR>—ऊरु-पर्वन्, आ or<BR>अ, m. n. the knee.<BR>—ऊरु-फलक, अम्, n. the thigh-<BR>bone, the hip-bone.<BR>—ऊरु-भिन्न, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>a rent in the thigh (according to Pāṇini IV. 1, 52,<BR>used as a Bahu-vrīhi).<BR>—ऊरु-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sprung from the thigh.<BR>—ऊरु-स्तम्भ, अस्, m.<BR>paralysis of the lower extremities, rheumatism of the<BR>thigh; (आ), f. the plantain tree.<BR>—ऊरूद्भव (ऊरु-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from the thigh.<BR>—ऊरु-<BR>अष्ठीव, अम्, n. thigh and knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरव्य|ऊरव्यः
ऊरव्य, अस्, m. a man of the third or Vaiśya tribe<BR>as born from the thighs of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुरी
ऊरुरी ऊरुरी, ind. a particle implying as-<BR>sent, admission, promise, diffusion, &c.; [cf. ऊररी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज्
ऊर्ज् ऊर्ज्, क्, f. (fr. rt. वृज्; cf. Eng. work),<BR>food, strength, vigour, sap, juice; often occurring in<BR>conjunction with इष् (e. g. इषम् ऊर्जम् अश्युः,<BR>‘may they obtain food and strength’); [cf. Gr. ὀργάω<BR>and ὀργάς Lat. urgeo; Hib. orc, ‘a prince, a hero;’<BR>orcaim, ‘I kill, I destroy.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज|ऊर्जः|ऊर्ज्ज|ऊर्ज्जं|ऊर्ज्जः
ऊर्ज, अस्, m., N. of the month Kārttika, i. e.<BR>November-December (as imparting food or strength);<BR>power, strength; effort, exertion; procreative power;<BR>life, breath; N. of a son of the second Manu; of<BR>Satyahita; of Vatsara; of the sons of Hiraṇya-garbha<BR>who are reckoned among the seven Ṛṣis of the<BR>third Manvantara; (आ), f. food, strength, sap; N. of<BR>a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Vasiṣṭha; (अम्),<BR>n. water.<BR>—ऊर्ज-योनि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Viśvā-<BR>mitra.<BR>—ऊर्ज-वाह, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śuci.<BR>—ऊर्ज-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting strength.<BR>—ऊर्ज-स्तम्भ, अस्, m., N. of one of the seven<BR>Ṛṣis of the second Manvantara.<BR>—ऊर्जाद् (˚जा-अद्),<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. an eater of strengthening food.<BR>—ऊर्जा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in food.<BR>—ऊर्जाहुति (˚जा-<BR>आह्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. offering nourishing or strength-<BR>giving sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जय
ऊर्जय, nom. P. ऊर्जयति, -यितुम्, to feed,<BR>strengthen; A. to become strong, to be powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जयत्|ऊर्जयन्त्
ऊर्जयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. strong, full of sap or<BR>juice, succulent; feeding, strengthening, nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जव्य|ऊर्ज्जव्य
ऊर्जव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abounding in food or<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जस्|ऊर्ज्जस्
ऊर्जस्, a form for ऊर्ज्, used in compounds and with<BR>affixes, thus ऊर्जस्-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, causing strength.<BR>—ऊर्जस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, rich in food, abounding in<BR>sap or juice, juicy, succulent, powerful, vigorous,<BR>robust, strong; (ती), f., N. of a daughter of Dakṣa<BR>and wife of Dharma; of a daughter of Priya-vrata<BR>and wife of Uśanas; wife of Prāṇa.<BR>—ऊर्जस्-वल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, strong, powerful.<BR>—ऊर्जस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>strong, powerful; (इ), n. a figure of rhetoric, speak-<BR>ing of anything with disdain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जानी
ऊर्जानी, f., Ved. ऊर्जा personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जित|ऊर्ज्जित
ऊर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, powerful, strong, mighty, great,<BR>excellent, exceeding, much; (अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—ऊर्जिताश्रय (˚त-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, spirited, mag-<BR>nanimous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जिन्
ऊर्जिन्, ई, इनी, इ, abounding in food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ण|ऊर्णं|ऊर्ण्ण
ऊर्ण ऊर्ण, अम्, आ, n. f. (fr. rt. वृ, to cover,<BR>and connected with rt. ऊर्णु next col.), wool; (आ), f.<BR>a circle of hair between the eyebrows; N. of the wife<BR>of Citra-ratha and mother of Samrāj; [cf. Lat. villus,<BR>vellus; Goth. vulla; Old Germ. wolla; Mod. Germ.<BR>Wolle; Eng. wool; Lith. wilna; Russ. vòlna; Gr.<BR>ἔρος, ἐρέα, εἶρος, εἴριον; Hib. olaun.]<BR>—ऊर्ण-<BR>नाभ, अस्, m. a spider (as having wool on the navel<BR>or belly); N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a Dānava.<BR>—ऊर्ण-पट, अस्, m. a spider.<BR>—ऊर्ण-म्रदस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, or ऊर्ण-म्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, soft as wool.<BR>—ऊर्ण-वाभि, इस्, m. a spider (‘wool-weaver?;’ per-<BR>haps the original form of ऊर्ण-नाभि, derived from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">Page0177-c+ 78</a>]<BR>an obsolete rt. वभ्, to weave).<BR>—ऊर्णा-देश, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a country.<BR>—ऊर्णा-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a ball<BR>of wool.<BR>—ऊर्णा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, woollen, made of<BR>wool.<BR>—ऊर्णा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, woollen; (आन्), m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—ऊर्णा-वल, अस्, आ, अम्, woollen.<BR>—ऊर्णा-सूत्र, अम्, n., Ved. a thread of wool.<BR>—ऊर्णा-स्तुका, f., Ved. a tuft of wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णायु|ऊर्णायुः|ऊर्ण्णायु
ऊर्णायु, उस्, उस्, उ, woollen; (उस्), m. a ram; a<BR>woollen blanket; a spider; N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णु|ऊर्ण्णु
ऊर्णु ऊर्णु (connected with rt. वृ), cl. 2.<BR>P. A. ऊर्णोति and ऊर्णौति, ऊर्णुते, ऊर्णु-<BR>नाव, ऊर्णुनुवे, ऊर्णविष्यति, -ते, ऊर्णुविष्यति,<BR>-ते, और्णावीत्, और्णवीत्, और्णुवीत्, और्णविष्ट,<BR>और्णुविष्ट, ऊर्णवितुम्, ऊर्णुवितुम्, to cover,<BR>surround, hide; A. to cover one's self: Caus. ऊर्णा-<BR>वयति, aor. और्णुनुवत्: Desid. ऊर्णुनूषति, -ते,<BR>ऊर्णुनविषति, -ते, ऊर्णुनुविषति, -ते: Intens.<BR>ऊर्णोनूयते, ऊर्णोनवीति, ऊर्णोनौति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णुत
ऊर्णुत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्
ऊर्द् ऊर्द्, a various reading for rt. उर्द्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्दर|ऊर्दरं|ऊर्दरः|ऊर्द्दर|ऊर्द्दरः
ऊर्दर ऊर्दर, अस्, m. (said to be in some of<BR>its meanings fr. ऊर्ज् and rt. दॄ), Ved. a vessel for<BR>measuring corn, a bushel; a hero, a champion; a<BR>Rakṣas, a goblin or fiend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध|ऊर्द्धः
ऊर्ध ऊर्ध and ऊर्धक, a wrong reading<BR>for ऊर्ध्व and ऊर्ध्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्व|ऊर्द्ध्वः
ऊर्ध्व ऊर्ध्व, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वृध्), rising<BR>upwards, tending upwards, raised, elevated, erected,<BR>erect, upright; being above; above, high, superior,<BR>upper. In classical Sanskrit an example of the un-<BR>compounded adjective as in ऊर्ध्वैः पादैः, ‘with<BR>raised feet,’ is rare. (अम्), n. elevation, height, any-<BR>thing situated above; (अम्), ind. upwards, towards<BR>the upper part, aloft, above, in the upper regions, on<BR>the upper side of (with abl.); in the sequel (as of a<BR>book, the upper leaves of a MS. being read last);<BR>subsequent, after (with abl.); in a high tone, aloud;<BR>ऊर्ध्वं द्वितीयाद् अचः, after the second vowel;<BR>ऊर्ध्वम् पितुः, after the father's death; संवत्-<BR>सराद् ऊर्ध्वम्, after a year; अत ऊर्ध्वम्, hence-<BR>forward, from that time forward, hereafter; ऊर्ध्वं<BR>गम्, to go upwards, to die; [cf. Gr. ὀρθός; Lat.<BR>arduus; Gaël. ard.]<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-कच, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Ketu (whose hair streams upwards in the<BR>sky).<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-कण्ठ, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a plant.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the ears pricked up or erect.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. motion or action tending upwards;<BR>(आ), m., N. of a Viṣṇu (going upwards).<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>काय, अस्, m. the upper part of the body.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>कृशन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. effervescing, fermenting;<BR>epithet of the Soma; (Sāy.) having its sharp qualities<BR>stirred up.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Sanad-rāja.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>hair erect.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-क्रिया, f. motion or action tend-<BR>ing upwards.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going upwards,<BR>ascending, hovering; being on high.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, gone up, risen, ascended.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-गति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, going upwards; (इस्), f. ascent, elevation.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वग-पुर, अम्, n. the city of Hariścandra,<BR>who with his subjects is supposed to be suspended<BR>in the atmosphere.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-गम, अस्, m. upward<BR>motion of any kind.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-गमन, अम्, n. going<BR>upwards, ascending; elevation in the scale of being.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going up or above,<BR>ascending.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-ग्रावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. raising<BR>the stones to press out the Soma plant.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>चरण, अस्, आ, अम्, supine, having the feet upwards.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. piling up, heaping up.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-जानु, उस्, उस्, उ, or ऊर्ध्व-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or ऊर्ध्व-ज्ञु, उस्, उस्, उ, raising the knees, sitting on<BR>the hams; long-shanked.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-तिलकिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>having a sectarian mark on the forehead.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. or ऊर्ध्व-ता, f. height, elevation.<BR>—ऊर्ध्-<BR>व-था or ऊर्ध्व-धा, ind., Ved. upwards, erect.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-दंष्ट्रा-केश, अस्, m. whose teeth and<BR>hair are erect; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-दृष्टि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-a" target="_blank">Page0178-a+ 80</a>]<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, looking upwards, of high views, aspiring.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-देव, अस्, m. a superior deity; an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-देह, अम्, n. (‘the body gone<BR>above’), a funeral ceremony.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-नभस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, Ved. being above in the clouds.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वन्-<BR>दम, अस्, आ, अम्, going upwards, erected, exalted,<BR>elevated; (perhaps a wrong reading for ऊर्ध्वन्-<BR>गम.)<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पथ, अस्, m. the upper region,<BR>the ether.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पातन, अम्, n. causing to<BR>ascend, sublimation.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पात्र, अम्, n. a sacri-<BR>ficial vessel.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पाद, अस्, आ, अम्, heels up-<BR>wards; (अस्), m. a fabulous animal with eight legs;<BR>see शरभ.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पुण्ड्र or ऊर्ध्व-पुण्ड्र-<BR>क, अम्, n. a perpendicular line on the forehead of a<BR>Brāhman made with sandal &c., a Vaiṣṇaya mark.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पूरम्, ind. full to the brim, full to over-<BR>flowing.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-पृश्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. spotted<BR>above.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-बर्हिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. being over<BR>the sacrificial grass.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-बाल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the hair erect.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>having the arms raised; (उस्), m. a devotee who<BR>holds his arms above his head constantly till they are<BR>fixed in that position; N. of one of the seven Ṛṣis<BR>of the fifth Manvantara; one of the seven Ṛṣis of<BR>the south; one of the seven sons of Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-बुध्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bottom upwards,<BR>upside down.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-बृहती, f., N. of a metre.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-भाग, अस्, m. the upper part; any part<BR>of a word coming after another part.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-भाज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, partaking of the upper part; a N. of Baḍa-<BR>vāgni or submarine fire.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-मन्थिन्, living<BR>in perpetual chastity; see ऊर्ध्व-रेतस्.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>मान, अम्, n. an instrument for measuring altitudes.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-मायु, उस्, उस्, उ, giving forth a loud<BR>noise.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-मारुत, अम्, n. pressure of the<BR>wind (of the body) upwards.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-मुख, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having the mouth or opening turned upwards.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-मौहूर्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, happening after<BR>a short time.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-रेखा-शवल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>variegated with lines above.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-रेतस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, ‘having the semen above,’ abstaining from sexual<BR>intercourse, one who lives in perpetual chastity; a N.<BR>of Śiva, also of Bhīṣma.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-रोमन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>having the hairs of the body erect; N. of a mountain.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-लिङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>लोक, अस्, m. the upper world, the world above,<BR>heaven.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-वर्त्मन्, आ, m. the atmosphere,<BR>heaven.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-वात, अस्, m. or ऊर्ध्व-वायु,<BR>उस्, m. the wind in the upper part of the body.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, put on above, put on<BR>over the head or shoulder (as the sacred thread of<BR>the Brāhman).<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sleeping<BR>upright; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-शोधन, अम्,<BR>n. ‘purifying upwards,’ i. e. vomiting.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-शो-<BR>षम्, ind. so as to dry (anything) above.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>श्वास, अस्, m. expiration.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-सानु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. carrying the neck high, with lofty or uplifted<BR>neck; (Sāy.) rising higher and higher.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being above, superior, situated on<BR>high.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, being or standing<BR>above.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-स्थिति, इस्, f. the rearing of a horse;<BR>a horse's back, the part where the rider sits; eleva-<BR>tion, superiority.<BR>—ऊर्ध्व-स्रोतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, N. of<BR>a creation of beings whose stream of life or current<BR>of nutriment tends upwards.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वाङ्गुलि (˚व-<BR>अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, with raised finger.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वाम्नाय-<BR>संहिता (˚व-आम्˚), f. the doctrines of a particular<BR>Vaiṣṇava sect.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वायन (˚व-अय्˚), आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a caste in Plaksha-dvīpa.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वावर्त (˚व-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. rearing of a horse.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वासित<BR>(˚व-आस्˚), अस्, m. the plant Momordica Charantia.<BR>—ऊर्ध्वेह (˚व-ईह), अस्, m. motion or tendency<BR>upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वक|ऊर्द्ध्वकः|ऊर्ध्वकः
ऊर्ध्वक अस्, m. a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वसान
ऊर्ध्वसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rising, erecting<BR>one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ध्वीकृ
ऊर्ध्वी-कृ, cl. 5. 8. P. A. -कृणोति, -णुते, -करोति,<BR>-कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to raise aloft, to elevate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मि|ऊर्मिः|ऊर्म्मि|ऊर्म्मिः
ऊर्मि ऊर्मि, इस्, m. f. (fr. rt. वृ), a wave; a<BR>current, the flowing of water; human infirmity (as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">Page0178-b+ 72</a>]<BR>grief, illusion, hunger, thirst, decay, death); speed,<BR>velocity; a fold or plait in a garment; a line, a row;<BR>manifestation, light; mental suffering, distress, un-<BR>easiness, pain; missing, regretting; association, num-<BR>ber, quantity; [cf. Lith. wilni-s; Old Germ. wella;<BR>Mod. Germ. Welle; Eng. well.]<BR>—ऊर्मि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, wavy, undulating, billowy; crooked; plaited,<BR>curled (as hair).<BR>—ऊर्मिमत्-ता, f. undulation; crook-<BR>edness.<BR>—ऊर्मिमालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wreathed with waves,<BR>adorned with waves; (ई), m. the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मिका|ऊर्म्मिका
ऊर्मिका, f. a wave; a plait or fold in a garment;<BR>a finger ring; regret, sorrowing for anything lost;<BR>the buzzing of a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मिन्|ऊर्म्मिन्
ऊर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. having waves, undulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्मिला|ऊर्म्मिला
ऊर्मिला, f., N. of a daughter of Janaka and wife<BR>of Lakṣmaṇa, mother of Gandharvī Somadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्य
ऊर्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. undulating, having waves,<BR>agitated; (आ), f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व|ऊर्वः
ऊर्व 1. ऊर्व, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वृ), Ved. a re-<BR>ceptacle (for water), a reservoir; a cloud; an enclosed<BR>place, a stable for cattle; a prison, captivity (?); an<BR>epithet of the Pitṛs or manes of deceased ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्य|ऊर्व्यः
ऊर्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in reservoirs, lakes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व|ऊर्वः
ऊर्व 2. ऊर्व, अस्, m. (fr. ऊरु ?), N. of a saint<BR>from whose thighs sprang Aurva, a fiery being received<BR>by the ocean; the submarine fire; N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्वरा|ऊर्व्वरा
ऊर्वरा ऊर्वरा, f. fertile soil, land bearing<BR>any and every crop. See उर्वरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्वशी|ऊर्व्वशी
ऊर्वशी ऊर्वशी, f., N. of an Apsaras. See<BR>उर्वशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्वष्ठीव
ऊर्वष्ठीव ऊर्व्-अष्ठीव. See under ऊरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्वी
ऊर्वी ऊर्वी. See under ऊरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्यङ्ग|ऊर्व्यंगं|ऊर्व्यङ्गं|ऊर्व्व्यङ्ग
ऊर्व्यङ्ग ऊर्व्यङ्ग, अम्, n. (said to be fr.<BR>ऊर्वी = उर्वी, ‘earth,’ and अङ्ग), a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्षा
ऊर्षा ऊर्षा, f. a kind of grass, Andropogon<BR>Serratum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊलुपिन्
ऊलुपिन् ऊलुपिन्, ई, m. a porpoise. See<BR>उलुपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊलूक|ऊलूकः
ऊलूक ऊलूक, अस्, m. an owl. See उलूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊवट
ऊवट ऊवट, a various reading for उवट<BR>and ऊअट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊवध्य
ऊवध्य ऊवध्य or ऊबध्य, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>undigested grass &c. in the stomach (of an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष्
ऊष् ऊष्, cl. 1. P. ऊषति, -षितुम्, to be<BR>diseased or disordered, to be sick or ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष|ऊषं|ऊषः
ऊष ऊष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. उष् or fr. ऊष्<BR>above ?), salt ground, soil impregnated with saline par-<BR>ticles; a cleft, a hole; the cavity of the ear; dawn, day-<BR>break (in the latter sense neut. according to some); the<BR>mountain Malaya; (ई), f. soil impregnated with saline<BR>particles or not fertile.<BR>—ऊष-पुट, अम्, n. particles<BR>of salt wrapped up in paper.<BR>—ऊष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>consisting of saline soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषक|ऊषकं
ऊषक, अम्, n. salt, pepper; dawn, day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषण|ऊषणं|ऊषणः
ऊषण, अम्, n. black pepper; (आ), f. long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषर|ऊषरः
ऊषर, अस्, आ, अम्, impregnated with salt; (अम्),<BR>n. a barren spot with saline soil.<BR>—ऊषर-ज, अम्,<BR>n. salt produced from salt soil; a kind of magnet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषा
ऊषा ऊषा, f., N. of the wife of Aniruddha.<BR>See उषस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष्मन्
ऊष्मन् ऊष्मन्, आ, m. (fr. rt. 1. उष्), heat,<BR>steam, vapour, exhalation; ardour, passion, violence; the<BR>hot season; (in gram.) the sounds श्, ष्, स्, ह्; ष्क्,<BR>ष्प्, अं, अः, and more especially the first four of<BR>these sounds.<BR>—ऊष्म-प, अस्, आ, अम्, imbibing the<BR>steam of hot food; (आस्), m. pl. a class of manes or<BR>deceased ancestors; (अस्), m. fire.<BR>—ऊष्म-पर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, followed by an Ūṣman.<BR>—ऊष्म-प्रकृति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, produced from an Ūṣman.<BR>—ऊष्म-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, hot, steaming.<BR>—ऊष्मान्त (˚म-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ending in an Ūṣman.<BR>—ऊष्मान्तःस्थ<BR>(˚म-अन्˚), आस्, m. pl. the sounds called Ūṣman and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">Page0178-c+ 75</a>]<BR>the semivowels.<BR>—ऊष्मोपगम (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the approach of the heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष्मण
ऊष्मण or ऊष्मण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. steaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष्माय
ऊष्माय, nom. A. ऊष्मायते, -यितुम्, to emit<BR>heat or steam, to steam, perspire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह्
ऊह् 1. ऊह्, cl. 1. P. (with prep. also A.)<BR>ऊहति, -ते, औहीत्, ऊहितुम्, to change,<BR>modify; (with prep.) to push, thrust, move, remove,<BR>touch lightly. (This root is connected with rt. वह्;<BR>and it is often difficult to decide to which of these two<BR>roots forms like 1. ऊढ, p. 177, are to be assigned.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह|ऊहः
1. ऊह, अस्, m. change, modification.<BR>—ऊह-गान,<BR>अम्, n. or ऊह-गीति, इस्, f., N. of the third Gāna or<BR>song book of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहनी
ऊहनी, f. a broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह्यगान
ऊह्य-गान, अम्, n., N. of the fourth Gāna or<BR>song book of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह्
ऊह् 2. ऊह्, cl. 1. P. A. ऊहति, -ते (Ved.<BR>ओहते), ऊहे and ऊहाञ्-चक्रे, ऊहिष्यते,<BR>औहिष्ट, ऊहितुम्, to observe, mark, note, attend<BR>to (with acc.): to reckon on (with loc.); to wait for;<BR>to comprehend, conceive, conjecture, suppose, infer,<BR>reason, deliberate about; to be regarded as: Caus.<BR>ऊहयति, -यितुम्, aor. औजिहत्, to cause to think,<BR>reason, infer, or conjecture; to attend to (?); to do,<BR>accomplish (?): Desid. ऊजिहिषते; [cf. Hib. uige;<BR>Lat. äugeo; Goth. auka; Hib. ugtar, ‘augmentation.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढ|ऊढः
2. ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम्, observed, inferred, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह|ऊहः
2. ऊह, अस्, m. deliberation, examination; reason-<BR>ing; understanding; completing a defective sentence<BR>or verse, supplying an ellipsis; [cf. Hib. uga, ‘choice,<BR>election.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहन|ऊहनं
ऊहन, अम्, n. reasoning, inferring, concluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहिन्
ऊहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who or what reasons; who or<BR>what assembles, infers, or conjectures; (इनी), f. an<BR>assemblage, a collection; arrangement, a multitude<BR>reduced to order; [cf. अक्षौहिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह्य
ऊह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, inferrible, to be investigated,<BR>requiring to be supplied, elliptical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ 1. ऋ, the seventh vowel of the Sanskrit<BR>alphabet and peculiar to it, resembling the sound of रि<BR>in (मेरृल्य्).<BR>—ऋ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ 2. ऋ, ind. an interjection of abuse,<BR>laughter; a sound inarticulate or reiterated as in<BR>stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ 3. ऋ, आ, f. a N. of Aditi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ 4. ऋ, cl. 1. 9. (Ved. also 3. 4. 5. P.)<BR>ऋच्छति, ऋणाति (Ved. इयर्ति, आर्यते, ऋ-<BR>णोति or ऋण्वति), आर or अराञ्-चकार, अरिष्यति or<BR>अरीष्यति (?), आरत्, अर्तुम्, अरितुम् or अरीतुम् (?),<BR>(Ved. 3rd pl. impf. रन्त), to rise, tend upwards; to go,<BR>move; to meet with, fall upon or into, reach, obtain;<BR>to fall to one's share (with acc.); to move, excite,<BR>raise, raise (in singing, e. g. वाचम् इयर्ति, he raises<BR>his voice; स्तोमान् इयर्ति, he sings hymns); to dis-<BR>play; to injure, hurt: Caus. अर्पयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>throw, cast; to put, place, insert, fix, fasten; to direct<BR>towards, cast upon; to pierce; to place on, apply;<BR>to offer, give, give up, surrender; to give back,<BR>restore: Intens. Ved. 2nd pers. अलर्षि, 3rd pers.<BR>अलर्ति, to move, come; strive, make effort, exert<BR>one's strength: Intens. Class. अरार्यते, to wander<BR>about; to run or fly towards: Desid. अरिरिषति;<BR>[cf. Goth. airus, ‘a messenger;’ Hib. ria or rather<BR>do ria, ‘he will come or arrive;’ ria, ‘running,<BR>speed;’ riach, ‘he came;’ riachtaim, ‘I arrive;’<BR>ar, ‘guiding, conducting.’ With the Caus. have<BR>been compared Old Germ. arbjan, ‘to inherit;’ ki-<BR>erpit, ‘possession;’ Goth. arbi, Them. arbja, ‘in-<BR>heritance:’ cf. also Lat. aro; Goth. arja; Old Germ.<BR>erru; Lith. arù; Lith. orjû; Gr. αἴρω Hib. ar,<BR>‘slaughter, destruction, plague, the slain in fight;’<BR>aor, ‘a satire, a course.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्छस्
ऋक्छस् ऋक्-छस्. See under 2. ऋच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ण
ऋक्ण 1. ऋक्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (for वृक्ण fr. rt.<BR>व्रश्च्), wounded.<BR>—ऋक्ण-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, whose<BR>shoulders are wounded or made sore by drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ण
ऋक्ण 2. ऋक्ण = ऋक्थ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थ|ऋक्थं
ऋक्थ ऋक्थ, अम्, n. (fr. rt. रिच्), property,<BR>wealth, possessions, effects (especially left at death);<BR>gold; see रिक्थ.<BR>—ऋक्थ-ग्रहण, अम्, n. re-<BR>ceiving or inheriting property.<BR>—ऋक्थ-ग्राह, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, an inheritor or receiver of property; (अस्),<BR>m. inheriting or receiving property.<BR>—ऋक्थ-जात,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, formed into property, accumulated (as<BR>property).<BR>—ऋक्थ-भाग, अस्, m. division of pro-<BR>perty, inheritance, partition, a share.<BR>—ऋक्थ-भा-<BR>गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, an heir, a coheir; inheriting or sharing<BR>property.<BR>—ऋक्थ-हर, अस्, ई, अम्, an heir, a co-<BR>heir.<BR>—ऋक्थ-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, inheriting or sharing<BR>property; an heir.<BR>—ऋक्थादान (˚थ-आद्˚), अस्,<BR>m. an inheritor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्व
ऋक्व ऋक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, or ऋक्वन्, आ, आ, अ (fr.<BR>rt. अर्च्), Ved. praising, rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष्
ऋक्ष् ऋक्ष्, cl. 5. P. ऋक्ष्णोति, to kill;<BR>to hurt or seek to hurt; (a doubtful root.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष 1. ऋक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bald, bare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष 2. ऋक्ष, अस्, m. (fr. preceding rt.<BR>ऋक्ष्? or fr. rt. रिश्? or fr. rt. व्रश्च्?, cf. 1. ऋक्ण;<BR>or fr. rt. ऋच् connected with rt. अर्क्, to shine?; con-<BR>nected with रक्षस् ?), Ved. one who hurts or<BR>destroys (?); a bear (as having a shining coat?); (ई),<BR>f. a female bear; (आस्), m. pl. the seven stars, the<BR>Pleiades, Ἄρκτος Ursa; in later times the seven<BR>Ṛṣis; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a star, a constellation in<BR>general, a lunar mansion; the particular star in the<BR>twenty-seven mansions of the moon under which a<BR>person happens to be born; (अस्), m., N. of the plant<BR>Bignonia Indica, and of a similar species; N. of a<BR>man, a son of Ajamīḍha, or Ariha, or Vidūratha, or<BR>Revata; of Akrodhana; a descendant of Bhṛgu,<BR>identified with Valmīki; N. of a mountain; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of the wife of Ajamīḍha; [cf. Gr. ἄρκτος Lat.<BR>ursus; Hib. art; Lith. lokys for olkys; Armen.<BR>arǵ.]<BR>—ऋक्ष-गन्धा, f. the plant Argyreia Ar-<BR>gentea.<BR>—ऋक्ष-गन्धिका, f. the plant Batatas<BR>Paniculata.<BR>—ऋक्ष-ग्रीव, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>imp or demon.<BR>—ऋक्ष-नाथ, अस्, m. lord of the<BR>stars, an epithet of the moon.<BR>—ऋक्ष-नेमि, इस्, m.<BR>a N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—ऋक्ष-राज, अस्, m. the king of<BR>the bears; king of the stars, an epithet of the moon.<BR>—ऋक्ष-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—ऋक्ष-<BR>वन्त, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—ऋक्ष-विभावन,<BR>अम्, n. observing the stars.<BR>—ऋक्ष-हरीश्वर (˚रि-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord of bears and apes.<BR>—ऋक्षेश<BR>(˚ष-ईश), अस्, m. lord of the stars, an epithet of<BR>the moon.<BR>—ऋक्षेष्टि (˚ष-इष्˚), इस्, f. offering<BR>worship to the planets and stars.<BR>—ऋक्षोद (˚ष-<BR>उद), अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षीका
ऋक्षीका, f., Ved., N. of certain demons or evil<BR>spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष 3. ऋक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps a wrong<BR>reading for ऋक्ण), pierced, cut, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षर|ऋक्षरं|ऋक्षरः
ऋक्षर ऋक्षर, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. or 2. ऋष्?), a<BR>thorn; a family priest; (अम्), n. a shower, a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षला
ऋक्षला ऋक्षला, f., Ved. a fetter; [cf.<BR>ऋच्छरा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋघाय
ऋघाय ऋघाय, nom. P. A. (fr. an obso-<BR>lete noun ऋघ), Ved. ऋघायति, -ते, -यितुम्, to<BR>tremble; to tremble with passion, rage, rave; [cf.<BR>Zend ereghata; Germ. arg.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋघावत्|ऋघावन्त्
ऋघा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. raving, impetuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्
ऋच् 1. ऋच् (connected with rt. अर्च् and<BR>with rt. अर्क्, q. q. v. v.), cl. 6. P. ऋचति,<BR>आनर्च, अर्चिष्यति, अर्चितुम्, Ved. inf. ऋचसे, to<BR>praise, extol, laud, celebrate; to cover, screen; to<BR>shine (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्
2. ऋच्, क्, f. (fr. preceding rt. or fr. rt. अर्च्), lustre,<BR>splendor; a hymn; a single verse, stanza or text,<BR>especially verses recited or spoken at a sacrifice or<BR>religious^1 ceremony (whereas the verses called सामन्<BR>[pl. सामानि] are sung, and the verses called यजुस्<BR>[pl. यजूंषि] are some of them not metrical and are<BR>muttered in a peculiar manner; these three kinds of<BR>verse constitute the Mantra and are considered as<BR>sacred speech); a verse of the Ṛg-veda, the particular<BR>verse or text on the authority of which a ceremony is pre-<BR>scribed and to which the explanation in the Brāhmaṇa<BR>refers; the collective body of the Ṛc, i. e. the Ṛg-veda<BR>(but in this sense generally pl. ऋचस्).<BR>—ऋक्-छस् or<BR>ऋक्-शस्, ind. verse by verse, one verse after the other.<BR>—ऋक्-तन्त्र-व्याकरण, अम्, n. one of the Pari-<BR>śiṣṭas of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—ऋक्-तस्, ind. from a Ṛc,<BR>with reference to a Ṛc.<BR>—ऋक्-प्रातिशाख्य, अम्, n.<BR>the Prātiśākhya of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—ऋक्-शत, अम्, n.<BR>a hundred texts.<BR>—ऋक्-षम (fr. ऋच् and सम),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. similar to a Ṛc; N. of a Sāman.<BR>—ऋक्-संशित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. instigated by the<BR>Ṛc.<BR>—ऋक्-संहिता, f. the arranged collection of the<BR>hymns of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—ऋक्-सम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. similar to a Ṛc (as a Sāman).<BR>—ऋक्-साम, ए,<BR>n. du., Ved. the verses called Ṛc and Sāman.<BR>—ऋक्-<BR>सामन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—ऋक्साम-शृङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—ऋग्-आवानम्, ind.<BR>(आवानम् fr. rt. वे with आ), Ved. connecting one Ṛc<BR>with another, not interrupting their continuance.<BR>—ऋग्-गाथा, f., N. of a certain song.<BR>—ऋग्-भाज्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, partaking of a Ṛc, as a deity who is ad-<BR>dressed with it.<BR>—ऋग्-यजुः-साम-वेदिन्, ई, m. one<BR>who is familiar with the Ṛg, Yajur, and Sāma-veda.<BR>—ऋग्-विधान, अम्, n. title of a work of Śaunaka.<BR>—ऋग्-वेद, अस्, m. the Ṛg-veda; the collective<BR>body of sacred verses which as being recited are<BR>called Ṛcas and differ from Sāmāni and Yajūṃṣi<BR>in the manner described above; the arranged collection<BR>of these hymns as the most ancient sacred book of the<BR>Hindūs. (The Ṛg-veda consists of ten books or Maṇ-<BR>ḍalas; the first eight books contain groups of hymns,<BR>each group ascribed to one author or to the members<BR>of one family; the ninth book contains the songs<BR>recited at the Soma ceremonies; the tenth contains<BR>hymns of a very different character, composed by a<BR>greater variety of individual authors. In its wider<BR>sense the term Ṛg-veda comprehends the Brāhmaṇas<BR>and the Sūtra works on the ritual connected with the<BR>hymns.)<BR>—ऋग्वेद-प्रातिशाख्य, अम्, n. the Prā-<BR>tiśākhya of the Ṛg-veda, attributed to Śaunaka.<BR>—ऋग्वेद-विद्, त्, m. a Brāhman familiar with the<BR>Ṛg-veda.<BR>—ऋग्वेदानुक्रमणिका (˚द-अन्˚), f. the<BR>index of the Ṛg-veda, attributed to Kātyāyana.<BR>—ऋग्-<BR>वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, conversant with the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—ऋङ्-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of Ṛcas.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्म
ऋग्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the character of a Ṛc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्मिन्
ऋग्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. praising exulting with joy,<BR>jubilant with praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्मिय
ऋग्मिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. deserving praise, laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच
ऋच (at the end of some compounds) = ऋच्; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a prince, a son of Sunīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋचीक|ऋचीकः
ऋचीक ऋचीक, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Jamadagni, a son of Heaven; N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋचीष|ऋचीषं|ऋचीषः
ऋचीष ऋचीष, अम्, n. a frying-pan; (अस्),<BR>m. a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋचीषम
ऋचीषम ऋचीषम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (Sāy.<BR>fr. ऋच् and सम) equal to the Ṛc; epithet of Indra;<BR>(perhaps this word is related to ऋजीष, ऋजीषिन्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋचेयु
ऋचेयु ऋचेयु, उस्, m., N. of a man; a son<BR>of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋछ्|ऋच्छ्
ऋछ् ऋछ्, cl. 6. P. ऋच्छति, आनर्च्छ,<BR>अर्च्छितुम्, to go, move; to fail in facul-<BR>ties; to become hard or stiff; [cf. Lat. rigere.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्छका
ऋच्छका ऋच्छका, f. (fr. rt. 4. ऋ), wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्छरा
ऋच्छरा ऋच्छरा, f., Ved. a fetter; a har-<BR>lot, a courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्
ऋज् 1. ऋज्, cl. 1. P. अर्जति, आनर्ज, अर्-<BR>जितुम्, to bring near, obtain, get, acquire:<BR>Caus. अर्जयति, -यितुम्, to obtain, get, acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्
ऋज् 2. ऋज्, cl. 1. A. अर्जते, -जितुम्, to<BR>go; to stand or be firm; to acquire; to<BR>be healthy or strong; [cf. Lat. rego, rectus; Goth.<BR>raihts; Mod. Germ. recht; Gr. ὀρέγω Hib. righim,<BR>‘I reach, arrive, stretch.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजिप्य
ऋजिप्य ऋजिप्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. ऋञ्ज्?), Ved.<BR>going quick, striving upwards; [cf. Zend. ĕrĕzifja.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजिश्वन्
ऋजिश्वन् ऋजिश्वन्, आ, m., Ved., N. of a man<BR>(protected by Indra) who has the epithet Vaidathina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीक|ऋजीकः
ऋजीक ऋजीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. अर्ज्), Ved.<BR>coloured, variegated; mixed with; polluted; (अस्), m.<BR>smoke; an epithet of Indra; N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीति|ऋजीतिः
ऋजीति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. burning, sparkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीष|ऋजीषं
ऋजीष ऋजीष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. ऋञ्ज्?), Ved.<BR>epithet of Indra, carrying or driving away, (or perhaps<BR>= ऋजीषिन् below); (अम्), n. the sediment or residue<BR>of Soma; a frying-pan; N. of a hell; (Sāy.) water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीषिन्
ऋजीषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. hastening towards, seizing;<BR>consisting of or receiving the sediment or residue of<BR>Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजु
ऋजु ऋजु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. 2. ऋञ्ज्), tending in<BR>a straight direction, straight; straight metaphorically<BR>as in morals, right, honest, upright; (in Ved. = साधु<BR>and opposed to वृजिन; in classical Sanskrit opposed<BR>to जिह्म and तिर्यच्); comparative ऋजीयस्, Ved.<BR>रजीयस्; superlative ऋजिष्ठ, Ved. रजिष्ठ;<BR>(उस्), m., N. of a son of Vasu-deva; [cf. Hib. aroch;<BR>Zend ĕrĕśu.]<BR>—ऋजु-काय, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>straight body; (अस्), m., N. of the saint Kaśyapa.<BR>—ऋजु-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. intending what is<BR>honest; (Sāy.) acting honestly.<BR>—ऋजु-ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. going straight.<BR>—ऋजु-गाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>singing correctly.<BR>—ऋजु-ता, f. or ऋजु-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>straight direction, straightness; uprightness, sincerity,<BR>honesty.<BR>—ऋजु-दास, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vasu-<BR>deva.<BR>—ऋजु-धा, ind. straight, right.<BR>—ऋजु-नीति,<BR>इस्, f., Ved. right conduct.<BR>—ऋजु-मिताक्षरा, f. title<BR>of a commentary on Yājñavalkya's law-book, generally<BR>called Mitākṣarā.<BR>—ऋजु-मुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having straight generative organs; (Sāy.) strong and<BR>muscular.<BR>—ऋजु-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having straight<BR>rope-traces (said of a chariot).<BR>—ऋजु-रोहित, अम्, n.<BR>the straight red bow of Indra.<BR>—ऋजु-वनि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. striving straightforward; (Sāy.) granting auspi-<BR>cious gifts.<BR>—ऋजु-शंस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desiring<BR>what is right.<BR>—ऋजु-सर्प, अस्, m. a kind of snake.<BR>—ऋजु-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. extending the hand.<BR>—ऋजू-नस्, आस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूक
ऋजूक, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूकृ
ऋजू-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to straighten,<BR>rectify.<BR>—ऋजू-करण, अम्, n. straightening.<BR>—ऋजू-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूय
ऋजूय, nom. Ved. ऋजूयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to walk<BR>straightforward, on the right or honest way; to direct<BR>one's way towards anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूया
ऋजूया, ind., Ved. in a straight line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूयु
ऋजूयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. honest; upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्वच्
ऋज्वच्, आङ्, ऊची (?), अक्, Ved. going straightforward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्र|ऋज्रः
ऋज्र 1. ऋज्र, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 2. अर्ज्), Ved.<BR>reddish, dark red, reddish brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्रिय
ऋज्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. reddish, red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्र|ऋज्रः
ऋज्र 2. ऋज्र, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. ऋञ्ज्?), a leader.<BR>—ऋज्राश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋञ्ज्|ऋंज्
ऋञ्ज् 1. ऋञ्ज्, cl. 1. A. ऋञ्जते, ऋञ्जाञ्-<BR>चक्रे, -जितुम्, to fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋञ्ज्|ऋंज्
ऋञ्ज् 2. ऋञ्ज्, cl. 6. P. A. ऋञ्जति, -ते,<BR>-जितुम्, to spring forward, run; to strive<BR>after, long for; (Sāy.) to decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋञ्जसान|ऋंजसान|ऋञ्जसानः
ऋञ्जसान, अस्, आ, अम्, running towards, striving<BR>after; (अस्), m. a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋण|ऋणं
ऋण ऋण, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. 4. ऋ;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-a" target="_blank">Page0180-a+ 80</a>]<BR>cf. Lat. reus), Ved. guilty; (अम्), n. guilt; obliga-<BR>tion, debt (opposed to धन and ऋक्थ, ‘pro-<BR>perty’); a fort, a stronghold; water; a negative<BR>quantity, minus; (अस्), m. a N. of a Vyāsa; अन्त्यम्<BR>ऋणम्, the last debt, a debt to the manes, i. e. the<BR>generation of a son; ऋणं कृ, to get into debt;<BR>ऋणं धृ, to be indebted; ऋणं दा or प्र-<BR>यम् or सं-नी, to pay a debt; ऋणम् प्राप्, to<BR>become indebted; ऋणम् परीप्स् (Desid. fr. rt. आप्<BR>with परि), to require payment of a debt, call in a<BR>debt.<BR>—ऋण-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, getting into debt,<BR>indebted.<BR>—ऋण-काति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. requiring pay-<BR>ment of debts, ‘taking revenge;’ (Sāy.) one to<BR>whom praise is due as a debt, or one who receives<BR>praise as a debt to be repaid in benefits.<BR>—ऋण-<BR>ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, indebted, involved in debt.<BR>—ऋण-ग्रह, अस्, m. borrowing; a borrower.<BR>—ऋण-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, borrowing; a borrower.<BR>—ऋण-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. punishing offences or guilt;<BR>(Sāy.) acknowledging (praise) as an obligation to be<BR>paid for.<BR>—ऋण-च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. granting quittance<BR>of a debt or an offence.<BR>—ऋणञ्-चय, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a prince of the Ruśamas; N. of an author of a hymn<BR>in the Ṛg-veda (IX. 108).<BR>—ऋण-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or ऋण-दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or ऋण-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>one who pays a debt.<BR>—ऋण-दान, अम्, n. payment<BR>of a debt.<BR>—ऋण-दास, अस्, m. lit. ‘a debt-slave,’<BR>i. e. one who becomes a slave to his creditor till his<BR>debt is paid.<BR>—ऋण-मत्कुण, अस्, m. a security, a<BR>bail (which sticks to the debtor like an insect).<BR>—ऋण-मार्गण, अस्, m. a security.<BR>—ऋण-मुक्त,<BR>अस् आ, अम्, released from debt.<BR>—ऋण-मुक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>discharge of a debt.<BR>—ऋण-मोक्ष, अस्, m. paying<BR>a debt.<BR>—ऋण-या, आस्, आस्, अम्, or ऋण-यावन्, आ, आ,<BR>अ, Ved. punishing or prosecuting guilt; keeping off<BR>debt or guilt.<BR>—ऋण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who is<BR>in debt, one who is under obligation (to another),<BR>indebted.<BR>—ऋण-वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. guilty, indebted;<BR>obliged, under obligation (to another).<BR>—ऋण-शो-<BR>धन, अम्, n. payment or discharge of a debt.<BR>—ऋणादान (˚ण-आद्˚), अम्, n. recovery of a debt,<BR>receipt of money &c. lent (as one of the eighteen<BR>titles or subjects of judicial procedure).<BR>—ऋणान्तक<BR>(˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, m. the planet Mars (as the patron of<BR>debtors).<BR>—ऋणापनयन (˚ण-अप्˚), अम्, n. dis-<BR>charge of a debt.<BR>—ऋणापनोदन (˚ण-अप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. payment of a debt.<BR>—ऋणापाकारण (˚ण-अप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. paying off a debt.<BR>—ऋणार्ण (˚ण-ऋ˚), अम्,<BR>n. debt of a debt, compound interest; [cf. Gram. 38. d.]<BR>—ऋणोद्ग्रहण (˚ण-उद्˚), अम्, n. recovering a<BR>debt in any way from the creditor by friendly or legal<BR>proceedings, by stratagem or by arrest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिक|ऋणिकः
ऋणिक, अस्, m. a debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिन्
ऋणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a debtor, one under any obliga-<BR>tion (to another), indebted, of or belonging to a debt;<BR>[cf. अन्-ऋणिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्
ऋत् ऋत्, A. ऋतीयते, to reproach, contemn,<BR>pity; to rival, have power, domineer; hate; go; (a<BR>Sautra root, i. e. a root occurring only in grammatical<BR>Sūtras and not in the Dhātu-pāṭha.) [To this root<BR>have been referred Goth. rt. lith in leitha, laith,<BR>लिथुम्; Hib. rith, ‘course, flight, gallop, race;’<BR>rithim, ‘I run, range, rush.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत|ऋतं|ऋतः
ऋत ऋत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 4. ऋ), proper,<BR>right; honest, brave, competent; true; worshipped,<BR>respected; enlightened, luminous; gone, risen, moved,<BR>affected by; (अम्), ind. right, duly, properly, ener-<BR>getically; ऋतम् इ, to go the right way, to live<BR>virtuously; (अस्), m., N. of a Rudra; of a prince;<BR>(अम्), n. fixed or settled order, law, rule (especially<BR>in religion); sacred or pious custom, pious action;<BR>divine law, faith, divine truth; (Sāy.) water, sacrifice,<BR>sacrificial rite; the sun (e. g. ऋतम् बृहत्, the great<BR>divine law, supreme truth, or according to Sāy. a<BR>great sacrifice; ऋतस्य गर्भः or प्रजाः, the off-<BR>spring of divine truth, or according to Sāy. the off-<BR>spring of the water or of sacrifice, as an epithet of<BR>Agni, of Soma, or of Viṣṇu; प्रथमजा ऋतस्य,<BR>the first-born of divine truth or Prajāpati; ऋतस्य<BR>सदनम् or सदः or सद्म or पदम् or नाभिः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-b" target="_blank">Page0180-b+ 81</a>]<BR>the seat or centre of religious faith, as the altar &c.,<BR>or according to Sāy. the seat of water or of the sun;<BR>ऋतस्य योनिः, water; ऋतस्य गोपाः or नेता or<BR>रथीः or पतिः, the protector or leader or lord of<BR>divine truth, or according to Sāy. of the sacrifice, as<BR>an epithet of Agni, of Soma, of the Ādityas, and<BR>other gods, or sometimes applied to men who are<BR>guardians of the truth); truth in general, right (e. g.<BR>पथ्या or पन्था ऋतस्य, the path of truth, the<BR>right way, a virtuous life, or according to Sāy. the<BR>way of the water); truth personified (as an object of<BR>worship, and hence enumerated among the sacred<BR>objects in the last chapter of the Nighaṇṭavas. In<BR>later Sanskrit he is regarded as a child of Dharma);<BR>gleaning, i. e. the lawful and right means of getting a<BR>livelihood for Brāhmans as opposed to the cultivation<BR>of the ground (this latter being metaphorically called<BR>अन्-ऋत, improper).<BR>—ऋत-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. observing<BR>the sacred law, conversant or familiar with it; (Sāy.)<BR>knowing the sacrifice or water.<BR>—ऋत-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>or ऋत-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. happening at the right<BR>time, of a true nature, sprung from sacred truth,<BR>according to sacred truth.<BR>—ऋत-जात-सत्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. realizing what is according to the sacred<BR>law; (Sāy.) born for the sake of the sacrifice and<BR>having true result.<BR>—ऋत-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. gaining the<BR>right.<BR>—ऋत-जुर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, उर्, Ved. grown quite old;<BR>(Sāy.) growing old in religious worship.<BR>—ऋत-ज्ञा,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. well informed; familiar with the<BR>sacred law; (Sāy.) knowing the sacrifice.<BR>—ऋत-ज्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. furnished with a good bow-string;<BR>(Sāy.) whose string is truth, truth-strung (said of a<BR>bow).<BR>—ऋत-द्युम्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. filled with<BR>sacred strength.<BR>—ऋत-धामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. of true<BR>or pure nature; (आ), m., N. of Viṣṇu; of the thir-<BR>teenth Manu; of the Indra in the twelfth Manvantara.<BR>—ऋत-धीति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. of true or sacred disposi-<BR>tion; epithet of the gods; (Sāy.) receiving true praise;<BR>whose actions are unobstructed.<BR>—ऋत-ध्वज, अस्,<BR>m. epithet of Rudra; N. of a sage; a son of Kaṅka;<BR>epithet of Pratardana.<BR>—ऋत-नी, ईस्, इ, Ved. lead-<BR>ing in the right way; (Sāy.) leader of truth (as the<BR>Ādityas).<BR>—ऋत-पर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a prince (son<BR>of Ayutājit and friend of Nala).<BR>—ऋत-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. observing the truth; observing the law; (Sāy.)<BR>protecting truth or the sacrifice.<BR>—ऋत-पेय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a certain ceremony.<BR>—ऋत-पेशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. having a perfect shape; epithet of Varuṇa;<BR>(Sāy.) one whose form consists of water.<BR>—ऋत-<BR>प्रजात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. happening at the right<BR>time, of true nature, born from sacred truth, accord-<BR>ing to sacred truth; (Sāy.) produced from water.<BR>—ऋत-प्रवीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. conceived in the<BR>right manner; (Sāy.) invested with truth, or with<BR>water, or with the sacrifice.<BR>—ऋत-प्सु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. having a perfect shape or aspect; (Sāy.) whose<BR>form is truth, or who consumes the sacrificial food.<BR>—ऋत-भाग, अस्, m., N. of a man, Ἀρταβάζης<BR>—ऋतम्-भर, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing the truth in<BR>one's self, an epithet of Brahmā, also of Viṣṇu;<BR>(आ), f. intellect; N. of a river.<BR>—ऋत-युक्ति, इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. right union; (Sāy.) true application of a hymn.<BR>—ऋत-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. well harnessed; well<BR>allied; (Sāy.) going to the sacrifice.<BR>—ऋत-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, being right, saying the truth.<BR>—ऋत-वाक,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. true or pious speech, speaking of truth.<BR>—ऋत-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. saying right, speaking<BR>truth.<BR>—ऋत-व्रत, आस्, m. pl., N. of the inhabitants<BR>of Śākadvīpa.<BR>—ऋत-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. dwelling or<BR>seated in truth; (Sāy.) dwelling in the sacrifice.<BR>—ऋत-सदन, अम्, ई, n. f., Ved. the right or<BR>usual seat.<BR>—ऋत-साप्, प्, प्, प्, Ved. practising pious<BR>acts, of a pious disposition; steady in religious belief;<BR>(Sāy.) pervading truth.<BR>—ऋत-स्तुभ्, प्, m. ‘praising<BR>in the right manner,’ N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋत-स्था,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. standing right.<BR>—ऋतस्-पति, इस्,<BR>m., Ved. lord of divine truth; an epithet of Vāyu;<BR>(Sāy.) lord of sacrifices.<BR>—ऋत-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>loving sacred truth; an epithet of the Ādityas and of<BR>Mitra-Varuṇa; (Sāy.) touching water.<BR>—ऋतानृत<BR>(˚त-अन्˚), अम्, n. truth and falsehood.<BR>—ऋता-वन्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">Page0180-c+ 80</a>]<BR>अरी, अ, Ved. of true nature or character, according to<BR>fixed order, epithet of any object in nature subject to<BR>fixed laws (e. g. of the moon, of plants, of waters, the<BR>dawn, &c.); true to sacred law; just, pious, faithful,<BR>believing; epithet of Agni, as always present at and<BR>presiding over sacrificial rites and the worship of the<BR>deities; epithet of Bṛhaspati, of Sarasvatī, of Soma,<BR>and especially of the Ādityas; (Sāy.) bestowing food;<BR>possessed of sacrifice.<BR>—ऋता-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. re-<BR>joicing in justice and piety, holy-minded, especially as<BR>an epithet of the Ādityas; (Sāy.) increasers of water,<BR>or of sacrifice, or of truth.<BR>—ऋता-षह्, -षाट्, ट्, ट्,<BR>Ved. maintaining the sacred law.<BR>—ऋतोक्ति (˚त-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. speaking truth.<BR>—ऋतोद्य (˚त-उद्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. true speech, truth; (Sāy.) born for sacrifice or<BR>religious rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतय
ऋतय, nom. P. A. ऋतयति, -ते, -यितुम् (generally<BR>used in pres. part. ऋतयत् or ऋतायत्), to submit to<BR>divine ordinances, to act piously; to observe the<BR>sacred law, be obedient or pious; (Sāy.) to desire<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतया
ऋतया, inst., Ved. in right manner; (Sāy.) through<BR>desire of reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतयु
ऋतयु or ऋतायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. observing the<BR>sacred law, obedient, pious; (Sāy.) desirous of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतायिन्
ऋतायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. observing the sacred law.<BR>See ऋतयु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋते
ऋते, ind. except, excepting, with the exception of,<BR>to the exclusion of, besides, without (with abl. or<BR>acc.); sometimes used at the beginning of a com-<BR>pound, e. g. ऋते-रक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, (any rite &c.)<BR>from which the Rakṣasas are excluded.<BR>—ऋते-<BR>कर्मम्, ind., Ved. acting according to fixed rule<BR>or settled law; (Sāy.) granting rain.<BR>—ऋते-जा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. living in truth, true to the law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतेन
ऋतेन, ind. according to settled law, duly, properly,<BR>rightly, regularly, in the prescribed manner, justly,<BR>strictly, fairly, truly, honestly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋति|ऋतिः
ऋति ऋति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 4. ऋ, and therefore<BR>connected with ऋत above), going, motion; assault,<BR>combat; abuse, censure, reproach; emulation, envy;<BR>manner of proceeding, manner; road, way; prosperity,<BR>felicity; fitness, trueness (?); remembrance; protec-<BR>tion; misfortune; (some of the latter meanings are<BR>only found in lexicons); [cf. Hib. raith, ‘prosperity,<BR>increase, profit, benefit, good;’ raite, ‘ways, passages,<BR>road.’]<BR>—ऋतिङ्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, unfortunate, pro-<BR>pitious.<BR>—ऋती-षह्, -षाट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. enduring an<BR>assault, able to resist, enduring; (Sāy.) subduing an<BR>assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीय
ऋतीय, nom. A. P. ऋतीयते, -ति, -यितुम्, to<BR>quarrel, litigate; to be in discord with one's self, be<BR>ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीया
ऋतीया, f. censure, reproach; (according to others)<BR>shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतु|ऋतुः
ऋतु ऋतु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 4. ऋ?), any settled<BR>point of time, a fixed time, time appointed for<BR>sacrifices and other regular worship, right time, fit<BR>season (especially in the inst. pl. ऋतुभिस्, at the<BR>right time or at the appointed time for sacrifice or<BR>for a festival); an epoch, a period, a period of the<BR>year, a season; (the number of seasons is sometimes<BR>limited to three, or sometimes to five, viz. Vasanta,<BR>‘spring;’ Grīṣma, ‘the hot season;’ Varṣa, pl.<BR>‘the rains;’ Sarad, ‘the autumn;’ Hemanta-śiśira,<BR>du. ‘the cold and dewy season:’ but is more com-<BR>monly reckoned as six, Hemanta and Śiśira being<BR>regarded as distinct: occasionally as seven, or even as<BR>twelve, in the latter case each season lasting one<BR>month. The Ṛtus or seasons are occasionally ad-<BR>dressed in the Veda and libations offered to them);<BR>the menstrual evacuation, the time favourable for pro-<BR>creation, or sixteen days in each month; fixed order,<BR>order, rule; light, splendor; the number six (from<BR>the six seasons); a kind of collyrium; N. of the<BR>twelfth Manu; [cf. Hib. raithe, ‘a quarter of a<BR>year;’ alt, ‘time, a joint, an article.’]<BR>—ऋतु-<BR>काल, अस्, m. the duration of a season; the period of<BR>menstruation, the period favourable for procreation,<BR>sixteen days of each month.<BR>—ऋतु-गण, अस्, m. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">Page0181-a+ 78</a>]<BR>seasons collectively.<BR>—ऋतु-गामिन्, ई, m. having in-<BR>tercourse with a wife after the period of menstrua-<BR>tion.<BR>—ऋतु-ग्रह, अस्, m., Ved. a libation offered<BR>to the seasons.<BR>—ऋतु-जित्, त्, m., N. of a prince of<BR>Mithilā.<BR>—ऋतु-धामन्, आ, m. epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>N. of the Indra of the twelfth Manvantara.<BR>—ऋतु-<BR>पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the seasons; an epithet of<BR>Agni.<BR>—ऋतु-पर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a king of Ayo-<BR>dhyā.<BR>—ऋतु-पर्याय, अस्, m. the revolution of the<BR>seasons.<BR>—ऋतु-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. drinking or com-<BR>ing to the libation regularly or at the appointed seasons.<BR>—ऋतु-पात्र, अम्, n., Ved. the cup in which the liba-<BR>tion to the seasons is offered.<BR>—ऋतु-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>productive in due season, fruitful, fertile.<BR>—ऋतु-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. observing regular times, coming at<BR>regular times; enjoying the seasons; (ती), f. a woman<BR>during her courses, a woman during menstruation or<BR>in the period favourable for procreation; (त्) n., N.<BR>of Varuṇa's grove or garden.<BR>—ऋतु-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of the seasons.<BR>—ऋतु-मुख, अम्, n. the<BR>beginning or first day of a season.<BR>—ऋतु-याज, अस्,<BR>m. sacrifice offered to the seasons; N. of a ceremony<BR>of the Prātaḥ-savana, just before the Ājya-śastra.<BR>—ऋतु-राज, अस्, m. the spring (king of the sea-<BR>sons).<BR>—ऋतु-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. characteristic or sign of<BR>the season; symptom of menstruation.<BR>—ऋतु-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, m. revolution of the seasons, a year.<BR>—ऋतु-वेला,<BR>f. the period of menstruation; the period favourable<BR>for procreation, sixteen days of each month.<BR>—ऋतु-<BR>शस्, ind., Ved. in order, duly; at the right or fixed<BR>time.<BR>—ऋतु-ष्ठा and ऋतु-स्था, आस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>fixed at the proper seasons.<BR>—ऋतु-संहार, अस्, m.<BR>‘collection of the seasons,’ title of a poem ascribed<BR>to Kālidāsa in praise of the six seasons.<BR>—ऋतु-<BR>सन्धि, इस्, m. the interval or junction between two<BR>seasons, the last seven days of one season and the<BR>first seven of the next.<BR>—ऋतु-समय, अस्, m. the<BR>period favourable for procreation.<BR>—ऋतु-सात्म्य,<BR>अम्, n. diet &c. suited to the season.<BR>—ऋतु-स्थला,<BR>f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—ऋतु-स्नाता, f. a woman who<BR>has bathed after menstruation and so prepared herself<BR>for sexual intercourse.<BR>—ऋतु-स्नान, अम्, n. bathing<BR>after menstruation.<BR>—ऋत्व्-अन्त, अस्, m. the close of<BR>a season, the termination of menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतव्य
ऋतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to the seasons, one<BR>who worships them as divinities, relating to the season,<BR>seasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुथा
ऋतुथा, ind. in order, duly; distinctly, precisely,<BR>exactly; (Sāy.) at a right or fixed time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विज्
ऋत्व्-इज्, क्, क्, क्, (इज् fr. rt. यज्), Ved. sacrificing at the<BR>proper seasons, sacrificing regularly; (क्), m. a priest;<BR>(the four chief Ṛtvijas or priests are the Hotṛ, Udgātṛ,<BR>Adhvaryu, and Brahman; sometimes eight are enume-<BR>rated, and at very grand ceremonies sixteen, viz. Hotṛ,<BR>Ud-gātṛ, Adhvaryu, Brahman, Brāhmaṇācchaṃsin,<BR>Pra-stotṛ, Maitrā-varuṇa, Prati-prasthātṛ, Potṛ,<BR>Prati-hartṛ, Acchāvāka, Neṣṭṛ, Agnīdh, Subrah-<BR>maṇya, Grāva-stut, and Un-netṛ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विय
1. ऋत्विय, अस्, आ, अम्, due, regular; happening at<BR>fixed or regular times; conforming to ceremonial<BR>rules, familiar with those rules.<BR>—ऋत्विया-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. conformable to law or rule, formal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विय
2. ऋत्विय or ऋत्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, menstruating;<BR>being in the period most favourable for procreation;<BR>(अम्), n. menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋते
ऋते ऋते. See under ऋत, p. 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विज्
ऋत्विज् ऋत्व्-इज्. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋदूदर
ऋदूदर ऋदूदर, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps related<BR>to मृदु), Ved. mild, soft, kind, gracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋदूपा
ऋदूपा, f. (for मृदु-पा?), Ved. a bee or any<BR>other insect fond of sweets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋदूवृध्
ऋदू-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. rejoicing in sweets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋध्
ऋध् ऋध्, cl. 4. 5. 7. P. ऋध्यति, ऋध्-<BR>नोति, ऋणद्धि (and in some forms cl. 2,<BR>as pres. 2nd du. ऋधाथे, pot. 1st pl. ऋध्याम,<BR>impf. 1st pl. आर्ध्म), आनर्ध, अर्धिष्यति,<BR>आर्धीत्, अर्धितुम्, to succeed, prosper; to grow,<BR>increase, flourish; to be prosperous and happy, to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">Page0181-b+ 77</a>]<BR>make prosperous, cause to succeed; to accomplish;<BR>to gratify, satisfy: Caus. अर्धयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to prosper, accomplish; to satisfy: Desid.<BR>ईर्त्सति; [cf. Lat. ol-esco, ad-ul-tus, radix; Goth.<BR>aurti, ‘plant,’ in aurti-gards; Lat. alo; Gr.<BR>ἀλδαίνω Goth. alja; Hib. alt, ‘nursing.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्ध|ऋद्धं|ऋद्धः
ऋद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, prosperous; increased; thriv-<BR>ing, rising; stored, as grain; (अम्), n. stored grain;<BR>a demonstrated conclusion, a distinct result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धि|ऋद्धिः
ऋद्धि, इस्, f. success, prosperity, good fortune,<BR>affluence, increase, growth, accomplishment; perfec-<BR>tion, supernatural power or supremacy; N. of a<BR>medicinal plant; prosperity personified as the wife of<BR>Kuvera; N. of the goddess Pārvatī.<BR>—ऋद्धि-काम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, desiring increase or prosperity.<BR>—ऋद्धि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, being in a prosperous state, pros-<BR>perous, wealthy, respectable, rich; making a fine<BR>appearance, bringing happiness.<BR>—ऋद्धि-साक्षात्-<BR>क्रिया, f. manifestation of supernatural power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधत्
ऋधत्, अन्, अती, अत् (pres. part. from a form in cl. 2),<BR>prospering, thriving, &c.<BR>—ऋधद्-री, ईस्, m. (री =<BR>रै), N. of a man.<BR>—ऋधद्-वार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>increasing one's goods; (Sāy.) having desirable or<BR>prosperous wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधिल
ऋधिल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधक्
ऋधक् ऋधक्, ind. (related to अर्ध), Ved.<BR>separately; aside, apart; singly, one by one; in a dis-<BR>tinguished manner, particularly.<BR>—ऋधङ्-मन्त्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who is destitute of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋधुक
ऋधुक ऋधुक, अस्, आ, अम्, short (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋफ्
ऋफ् ऋफ् or ऋन्फ् or ऋम्फ्, cl. 6. P.<BR>ऋफति, आनर्फ or ऋम्फाञ्-चकार,<BR>to injure, kill; [cf. rt. रिफ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋबीस|ऋबीसं
ऋबीस ऋबीस, अम्, n., Ved. a fissure, rent,<BR>gulf, abyss; warmth of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभु|ऋभुः
ऋभु ऋभु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. रभ्), Ved.<BR>clever, skilful, inventive, prudent (often as an epithet<BR>of the gods Indra, Agni, and the Ādityas); handy<BR>(as a weapon), easy to be used; (Sāy.) shining far,<BR>diffusing light; (उस्), m. an artist, one who works in<BR>iron, a smith, a builder (especially of carriages); N.<BR>of three semi-divine beings (called Ṛbhu, Vibhvan,<BR>and Vāja, sons of Su-dhanvan, a descendant of<BR>Aṅgiras, and called Ṛbhus from the name of the<BR>elder. Through their performance of good works<BR>[स्व्-अपस्] they obtained divinity, exercised super-<BR>human powers, and became entitled to worship.]<BR>They are supposed to dwell in the solar sphere, and<BR>are the artists who formed the horses of Indra, the<BR>carriage of the Aśvins, and the miraculous cow of<BR>Bṛhaspati; they made their aged parents young, and<BR>constructed four cups at a sacrifice from the one cup<BR>of Tvaṣṭṛ who, as the proper artificer of the gods,<BR>was in this respect their rival; they appear generally<BR>as accompanying Indra, especially at the evening sacri-<BR>fice. In later mythology ऋभु is a son of Brahmā);<BR>a deity, a divinity in general; [cf. Ὀρφεύς.]<BR>—ऋभु-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. clever, skilful, prudent; con-<BR>nected with or accompanied by the Ṛbhus; (Sāy.)<BR>wide-shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्ष|ऋभुक्षः
ऋभुक्ष, अस्, m. Indra; Indra's heaven or para-<BR>dise; the thunderbolt of Indra. (This word does<BR>not seem to be used, but appears to owe its origin to<BR>the next.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्षिन्
ऋभुक्षिन्, आस्, m. (in the Ved. only the following<BR>forms occur, nom. sing. -क्षास्, acc. sing. -क्षणम्,<BR>nom. pl. -क्षास् and -क्षणस्), the first of the three<BR>Ṛbhus, who is the Ṛbhu par excellence; a Ṛbhu<BR>in general; a N. of Indra; N. of the Maruts; (the<BR>word means, according to the scholiasts, ‘governing<BR>far or reigning over the Ṛbhus.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभ्व
ऋभ्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. attacking, assailing, cou-<BR>rageous, determined; extending far; clever; skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभ्वन्
ऋभ्वन्, आ, आ, अ, or ऋभ्वस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>attacking, assailing, courageous, determined; (Sāy.)<BR>shining widely or far extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋल्लक|ऋल्लकः
ऋल्लक ऋल्लक, अस्, m. a player on a kind<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">Page0181-c+ 78</a>]<BR>of musical instrument; (perhaps a wrong reading for<BR>झल्लक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋल्लरी
ऋल्लरी, f. a kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्य|ऋश्यः
ऋश्य ऋश्य or ऋश, अस्, m. the male of a<BR>species of antelope, the painted or white-footed ante-<BR>lope; [cf. ऋष्य and रिश्य.]<BR>—ऋश्य-केतु, उस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Aniruddha; (a various reading for विश्व-<BR>केतु.)<BR>—ऋश्य-द, अस्, m. (द fr. rt. 4. दा, ‘to bind’),<BR>a pit for catching antelopes.<BR>—ऋश्य-पद्, आत्, अदी,<BR>अत्, Ved. having the feet of an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्
ऋष् 1. ऋष् (connected with rt. वृष्),<BR>cl. 1. P. अर्षति, आनर्ष, अर्षितुम्, to<BR>flow, flow quickly; to bring anything near by flowing;<BR>to glide, to move with a gliding or quick motion;<BR>[cf. Goth. airz-ja; Old Germ. irru; Lat. erro.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषद्गु
ऋषद्-गु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Vṛjinīvat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभ|ऋषभः
ऋषभ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. ऋष् as वृषभ fr.<BR>वृष्, ‘to sprinkle,’ the idea of impregnating being<BR>involved), a bull, a young bull; (in comp. with other<BR>names of animals) the male animal; (in comp. with<BR>other nouns) the best or most excellent of any species<BR>or race (e. g. पुरुषर्षभ, an excellent man;<BR>भरतर्षभ, the most eminent of the Bharata<BR>race); the second of the seven notes of the Hindū<BR>gamut, in abbreviation Ṛ; the hollow of the ear;<BR>a boar's tail; a crocodile's tail; a dried plant, one of<BR>the eight principal medicaments; N. of an antidote;<BR>N. of a ceremony; N. of a king of the Śviknas; of<BR>a descendant of Viśvā-mitra and author of several<BR>hymns of the Ṛg-veda; of a Nāga; of a prince,<BR>a son of Nābhi and Meru; of a son of Kuśāgra; of<BR>one of the seven Ṛṣis of the second Manvantara;<BR>of the first Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī, a son of<BR>Nābhi and Marudevā; of a mountain; (ई), f. a woman<BR>with masculine peculiarities, as with a beard &c.; a<BR>widow; the plant Carpopogon Pruriens; N. of another<BR>plant; [cf. Zend arshan; Gr. ἄρσην]<BR>—ऋषभ-<BR>कूट, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—ऋषभ-गज-<BR>विलसित, अम्, n., N. of a metre consisting of four lines<BR>of sixteen syllables each.<BR>—ऋषभ-तर, अस्, m. a<BR>small bull.<BR>—ऋषभ-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, giving a<BR>bull.<BR>—ऋषभ-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—ऋषभ-ध्वज, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva; N.<BR>of an Arhat or Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभक|ऋषभकः
ऋषभक, अस्, m., N. of a medicinal plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्
ऋष् 2. ऋष्, cl. 6. P. ऋषति, आनर्ष,<BR>अर्षिष्यति, आर्षीत्, अर्षितुम्, to push;<BR>to pierce; to go, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषि|ऋषिः
ऋषि ऋषि, इस्, m. (said to be either fr. rt.<BR>दृश्, ‘to see,’ or fr. 1. ऋष्; perhaps related to अर्च्<BR>or ऋच्, ‘to praise’), a singer of sacred hymns, an in-<BR>spired poet or sage, any person who alone or with<BR>others invokes the deities in rhythmical speech or<BR>song, especially in song of a sacred character (e. g. the<BR>ancient hymn-singers Kutsa, Atri, Rebha, Agastya,<BR>Kuśika, Vasiṣṭha, Vy-aśva, who were regarded by<BR>later generations as patriarchal sages or saints, occupy-<BR>ing the same position in Indian history as the heroes<BR>and patriarchs of other countries. They Ṛṣis con-<BR>stitute a peculiar class of beings in the early mythical<BR>system, as distinct from gods, men, Asuras, &c.;<BR>they are the authors or rather seers of the Vedic<BR>hymns, i. e. according to orthodox Hindū ideas they<BR>are the inspired personages to whom these hymns<BR>were revealed, and such an expression as ‘the Ṛṣi<BR>says’ is equivalent to ‘so it stands in the sacred texts.’<BR>Seven Ṛṣi, सप्त ऋषयः or सप्तऋषयः or<BR>सप्तर्षयः, are often mentioned in the Brāhmaṇas<BR>and later works as typical representatives of the charac-<BR>ter and spirit of the pre-historic or mythical period; in<BR>the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa their names are given as<BR>follows, Gotama, Bharadvāja, Viśvā-mitra, Jamadagni,<BR>Vasiṣṭha, Kaśyapa, and Atri; in the Mahā-bhārata<BR>thus, Marīci, Atri, Aṅgiras, Pulaha, Kratu, Pulastya,<BR>Vasiṣṭha; in Manu they are called Prajāpatis or<BR>patriarchs, and are reckoned as ten, three other names<BR>being added, viz. Pracetas or Dakṣa, Bhṛgu, and Nā-<BR>rada, these ten being created by Manu Svāyambhuva<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-a" target="_blank">Page0182-a+ 79</a>]<BR>for the production of all other beings including gods<BR>and men. The seven Ṛṣis form in astronomy the<BR>constellation of ‘the Great Bear.’ Metaphorically,<BR>the seven Ṛṣis may stand for the seven senses or<BR>the seven vital airs of the body); in later times a<BR>saint or sanctified sage in general, an ascetic, an an-<BR>chorite, (sometimes three orders of these Ṛṣis are enu-<BR>merated, viz. Devarṣis, Brahmarṣis, and Rājarṣis;<BR>sometimes seven, four others being added, viz. Ma-<BR>harṣis, Paramarṣis, Śrutarṣis, and Kāṇḍarṣis); a<BR>ray of light; an imaginary circle; the fish Cyprinus<BR>Ṛṣi; [cf. Hib. arsan, ‘a sage, a man old in<BR>wisdom;’ arrach, ‘old, ancient, aged.’]<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>कुल्या, f. ‘the river of the Ṛṣis,’ a sacred river, as<BR>the Sarasvatī or Gaṅgā; a river in general; N. of the<BR>wife of Bhūman and mother of Udgītha.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. rendering a poet inspired, inspiring;<BR>(Sāy.) making one's appearance, appearing.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>गण, अस्, m. a company or number of sages, the<BR>host of patriarchal sages.<BR>—ऋषि-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a mountain in Magadha.<BR>—ऋषि-गुप्त, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Buddha.<BR>—ऋषि-चोदन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. in-<BR>spiring the singer.<BR>—ऋषि-च्छन्दस्, अस्, n. the<BR>metre of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-जाङ्गल, अस्, m. or ऋषि-<BR>जाङ्गलिकी, f. the plant Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR>—ऋषि-तर्पण, अम्, n. libation offered to the<BR>Ṛṣis.<BR>—ऋषि-त्व, अम्, n. the order or state of a<BR>Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-देव, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. hating an inspired poet.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>पञ्चमी, f., N. of a festival on the fifth day in the<BR>second half of the month Bhādra.<BR>—ऋषि-पतन,<BR>N. of a country near Vārāṇasī.<BR>—ऋषि-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an author.<BR>—ऋषि-प्रशिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. instructed by the Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-प्रोक्ता, f. the<BR>plant Glycine Debilis.<BR>—ऋषि-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. related to a Ṛṣi, connected with a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n. title of a work.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having the mind of a sacred<BR>poet, inspired.<BR>—ऋषि-मुख, अम्, n. the beginning<BR>of a Maṇḍala composed by a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-यज्ञ,<BR>अस्, m. sacrifice offered to a Ṛṣi, consisting of a<BR>prayer uttered in a low voice.<BR>—ऋषि-लोक, अस्, m.<BR>the world of the Ṛṣis.<BR>—ऋषि-वत्, ind., Ved. like<BR>a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-वदन, N. of a country; see ऋषि-<BR>पतन.<BR>—ऋषि-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing or con-<BR>veying a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषि-षह्, षाट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. intoxi-<BR>cating and inspiring the singer, as the Soma.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>षेण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—ऋषि-ष्टुत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, praised by the sacred poets.<BR>—ऋषि-सत्तम,<BR>अस्, m. best or most excellent of the sages.<BR>—ऋषि-<BR>स्तोम, अस्, m. praise of the Ṛṣis.<BR>—ऋषि-स्वर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praised by a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ऋषी-तत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, celebrated by the sacred singers.<BR>—ऋषी-<BR>वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. equal to the Ṛṣis; (Sāy.) accom-<BR>panied by Ṛṣis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिक|ऋषिकः
ऋषिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (अस्), m. sing.<BR>a prince of this people; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिषाण
ऋषिषाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. attracted by the<BR>pious singer; (Sāy.) worshipped by the praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषु|ऋषुः
ऋषु ऋषु (occurring only in gen. plur.<BR>ऋषूणाम्), Ved. a firebrand; glowing fire; (Sāy.)<BR>one who approaches; a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्टि|ऋष्टिः
ऋष्टि ऋष्टि, इस्, m. f. (fr. rt. 2. ऋष्?), a<BR>spear, a lance, a sword, the weapon of the Maruts;<BR>[cf. रिष्टि.]<BR>—ऋष्टि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. fur-<BR>nished with spears as the Maruts.<BR>—ऋष्टि-विद्युत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. casting spears like lightning; (Sāy.) shining<BR>with weapons.<BR>—ऋष्टि-षेण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्य|ऋष्यः
ऋष्य ऋष्य, अस्, m. [cf. ऋश्य], the painted<BR>or white-footed antelope; N. of a son of Devātithi;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of leprosy.<BR>—ऋष्य-केतन, अस्, and<BR>ऋष्य-केतु, उस्, m., N. of Aniruddha.<BR>—ऋष्य-<BR>गता, f. the plant Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—ऋष्य-<BR>गन्धा, f. the plant Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR>—ऋष्य-<BR>जिह्व, अम्, n. a kind of leprosy.<BR>—ऋष्य-प्रोक्ता,<BR>f., N. of several plants, Carpopogon Pruriens, Aspa-<BR>ragus Racemosus, Sida Cordifolia or Rhombifolia.<BR>—ऋष्य-मूक, अस्, m. a mountain in the Dekhan,<BR>the temporary abode of Rāma with the monkey-chief<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">Page0182-b+ 71</a>]<BR>Sugrīva.<BR>—ऋष्य-शृङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a personage<BR>(son of the Ṛṣi Vibhāṇḍaka) whose story is told in<BR>Rāmāyaṇa. 1. 9; N. of a legislator.<BR>—ऋष्याङ्क<BR>(˚य-अङ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Aniruddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यक|ऋष्यकः
ऋष्यक, अस्, m. the painted or white-footed<BR>antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्व|ऋष्वः
ऋष्व ऋष्व, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. ऋष्), Ved.<BR>elevated, high, sublime, great; epithet of several<BR>deities, especially of Agni and Indra.<BR>—ऋष्व-वीर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. inhabited by sublime beings (as the<BR>sky).<BR>—ऋष्वौजस् (˚व-ओज्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. pos-<BR>sessing high power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋहत्|ऋहन्त्
ऋहत् ऋहत्, अन्, अती, अत्, Ved. small, weak,<BR>powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ ऌ ॡ No Sanskrit word begins with any of these vowels;<BR>ॠ appears only in the gen. plur. of nouns terminating<BR>in ऋ, in the acc. plur. of fem. nouns. of relationship<BR>in ऋ, and in the nom. and acc. plur. of neuter nouns<BR>in ऋ. As to the vowel ऌ it occurs only in some<BR>forms of the root कॢप्. The long ॡ is a mere<BR>invention of grammarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ॠ ऌ ॡ No Sanskrit word begins with any of these vowels;<BR>ॠ appears only in the gen. plur. of nouns terminating<BR>in ऋ, in the acc. plur. of fem. nouns. of relationship<BR>in ऋ, and in the nom. and acc. plur. of neuter nouns<BR>in ऋ. As to the vowel ऌ it occurs only in some<BR>forms of the root कॢप्. The long ॡ is a mere<BR>invention of grammarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॠ ऌ ॡ No Sanskrit word begins with any of these vowels;<BR>ॠ appears only in the gen. plur. of nouns terminating<BR>in ऋ, in the acc. plur. of fem. nouns. of relationship<BR>in ऋ, and in the nom. and acc. plur. of neuter nouns<BR>in ऋ. As to the vowel ऌ it occurs only in some<BR>forms of the root कॢप्. The long ॡ is a mere<BR>invention of grammarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ 1. ॠ, ind. a particle uttered at the be-<BR>ginning of a speech; an interjection of warding off<BR>reproach and terror; (ॠस् or री), f. the mother of the<BR>gods; also of the demons; recollection; (आ), m. a N.<BR>of Bhairava; a Dānava or demon; the breast; motion,<BR>going.<BR>—ॠ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ॠ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ 2. ॠ for rt. 4. ऋ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ऌ ऌ, ind. the earth; a mountain; the<BR>mother of the gods; the divine nature; a mystical<BR>letter.<BR>—लृ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ऌ.<BR>—लृ-वर्ण, अम्, n. the vowel ऌ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॡ ॡ, ind. a mother; a divine female;<BR>female nature; (ॡस्) m. a N. of Śiva; (ॡस्), f. the<BR>mother of the Dānavas; wife of a Daitya; the mother<BR>of the all-bestowing cow of plenty; ind. a mystical<BR>letter used once or repeatedly in Mantras or mystical<BR>formularies; (the letters ॠ and ॡ are employed in<BR>the same manner; they have apparently no significa-<BR>tion, but are personified and invested with mystical<BR>properties in the Tantras.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए 1. ए, the eleventh vowel of the alphabet,<BR>corresponding to the letter ए as pronounced in most<BR>languages, and having the sound of ए in प्रेय्, ग्रेय्.<BR>In English, however, this sound is rarely given to ए.<BR>—ए-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ए.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए 2. ए, ind. an interjection of remembering,<BR>addressing, censure or contempt, and compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए 3. ए, एस्, m. a N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए 4. ए (आ-इ), cl. 2. P. ऐति, -तुम्, to come,<BR>come near, come to, to fall to one's share (with acc.);<BR>to arrive at, enter; to addict one's self to; to fall<BR>into; to gain: Intens. Ved. एयते, to hasten towards;<BR>to request, to obtain by entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एक|एकं|एकः
एक एक, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. 5. इ;<BR>perhaps fr. the pronom. base ए contained in एतद्),<BR>one, alone, solitary, single, happening only once; the<BR>same, one and the same, identical; single of its kind,<BR>unique, singular, chief, pre-eminent, excellent; one<BR>of two or many [cf. एक-तर, एक-तम]; in later<BR>Sanskrit used as an indefinite article; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a man, the son of Raja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एक|एकं|एकः
एक follows the declension of pronominals (see<BR>Gram. 200, 237), and may be declined in the plural (e. g.<BR>एके, some, several; एके — एके or एके — अपरे or एके —<BR>अन्ये or एके — एके — अपरे or एके — अन्ये — एके — अपरे<BR>—अपरे, some — others). Sometimes एक may be<BR>repeated in the sense of ‘the one — the other, one — an-<BR>other’ (e. g. एक — एक = एक — अन्य or एक — द्वितीय,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-c" target="_blank">Page0182-c+ 81</a>]<BR>one — the other), or in the sense of ‘one after another’<BR>(e. g. एक एकः पुरुषः, one man after another). It<BR>is often used in the middle of compounds either sub-<BR>stantively or adverbially (e. g. पुण्यैक-कर्मा, prac-<BR>tising only virtue; स्वर्गैक-सम्मुखी, f. look-<BR>ing only up to the sky; कर-पादैक-हीनस्, de-<BR>prived of one foot and one hand). In Vedic Sanskrit<BR>it may sometimes be placed, together with न, before<BR>a decad to lessen it by one, being then used in the<BR>inst. or acc. fem., inst. or abl. neut. (e. g. एकया न<BR>त्रिंशत् or एकां न त्रिंशत् = twenty-nine; एकेन<BR>न विंशतिः or एकाद् न विंशतिः = nineteen). In<BR>compounds and derivatives एक never appears in its<BR>fem. form एका (e. g. एकस्याः क्षीरम्, the milk of<BR>one female, is compounded into एक-क्षीरम् not<BR>एका-क्षीरम्); [cf. Lith. ni-ékas, ‘no:’ Hib. each,<BR>‘any;’ neach, ‘any one, one, some one, he;’ neach-<BR>tar, ‘neither;’ neachdarach, ‘neutral:’ Gr. ἑκάτερος<BR>ἕκα-τος Lat. œquus, c-ocles fr. êc-ocles:<BR>Goth. ha in compounds, as haihs, Them. haiha,<BR>ha-iha, ‘one-eyed;’ ha-nfs, Them. ha-nfa, ‘one-<BR>handed;’ halts, Them. ha-lta, ‘lame;’ ha-lbs,<BR>Them. ha-lba, ‘half.’]<BR>—एक-ऋक्थिन्, &c.; see<BR>एक-रिक्थिन्, &c.<BR>—एक-कपाल, अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of one cup, contained in one cup.<BR>—एक-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, doing only one thing; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), one-handed, one-rayed.<BR>—एक-कर्म-<BR>कारक, अस्, आ, अम्, doing the same thing, of<BR>the same profession.<BR>—एक-कार्य, अम्, n. sole<BR>business, the same business or work; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>performing the same work, answering the same end.<BR>—एक-काल, अस्, m. one time, the same time; (अम्),<BR>ind. at one time, only once; (ए), ind. at the same<BR>time, at once.<BR>—एककाल-भोजन, अम्, n. eating<BR>but one meal in any given time.<BR>—एककालिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, happening only once; happening once a day.<BR>—एककालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, contemporary, coeval,<BR>simultaneous.<BR>—एक-कुण्डल, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Kuvera; of Balabhadra; and of Śeṣa, the king of<BR>the Nāgas.<BR>—एक-कुष्ठ, अम्, n. a kind of leprosy,<BR>ichthyosis.<BR>—एक-क्षीर, अम्, n. the milk of one<BR>(nurse &c.).<BR>—एक-गुरु, उस्, or एक-गुरुक, अस्,<BR>m. a spiritual brother, pupil of the same pre-<BR>ceptor; having the same preceptor.<BR>—एक-ग्राम,<BR>अस्, m. the same village.<BR>—एकग्रामीण or एक-<BR>ग्रामीय, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabiting the same village.<BR>—एक-चक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having only one wheel;<BR>passed over by the wheel (of the carriage) of<BR>only one (king), i. e. governed by only one king;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Dānava; (आ), f., N. of a town of<BR>the Kīcakas.<BR>—एकचक्रवर्ति-ता, f. state of being<BR>sole master of the whole earth.<BR>—एकचक्र-वर्तिन्,<BR>ई, m. sole master of the whole earth.<BR>—एकचत्वा-<BR>रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the forty-first.<BR>—एक-चत्वारिंशत्,<BR>त्, f. forty-one.<BR>—एक-चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, wander-<BR>ing or living alone, not living in company, segregari-<BR>ous, solitary, alone; having one follower; going<BR>together or at the same time; gregarious; (अस्), m.<BR>a rhinoceros.<BR>—एक-चरण, अस्, आ, अम्, having only<BR>one foot; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a fabulous race.<BR>—एक-<BR>चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, living alone, not in society; going<BR>alone or with one follower only; (ई), m. a Pratyeka-<BR>buddha; a follower of Buddha; (इणी), f. a loyal wife.<BR>—एक-चित्त, अम्, n. fixedness of thought on one<BR>object; one and the same thought, unanimity; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), thinking of one thing only, intent upon,<BR>absorbed in (e. g. तद्-एकचित्ता, f. thinking only of<BR>him); having the same thought, of one mind,<BR>agreeing, concurring.<BR>—एकचित्त-ता, f. fixedness of<BR>mind, agreement, unanimity.<BR>—एकचित्ती-भूय, ind.<BR>having become unanimous.<BR>—एक-चिन्तन, अम्, n.<BR>thinking of only one thing.<BR>—एक-चूर्णि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—एक-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, of one mind,<BR>unanimous.<BR>—एक-चोदन, अम्, n. mentioning in the<BR>singular number; (अस्, आ, अम्), resting upon one rule.<BR>—एक-च्छाय, अस्, आ, अम्, having only shadow,<BR>quite dark.<BR>—एक-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. born alone or<BR>single, produced alone; growing alone (said of a<BR>tree); alone of its kind; of one kind, unchanging.<BR>—एक-जन्मन्, आ, m. a king, a sovereign (whose<BR>birth is pre-eminent); once-born, a Śūdra (opposed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0183-a" target="_blank">Page0183-a+ 81</a>]<BR>to द्वि-जन्मन्, ‘twice-born’).<BR>—एक-जात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of one parentage, born of the same parents.<BR>—एक-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, once-born; belonging to the<BR>same family or kind, of the same caste; (इस्), m. a<BR>Śūdra.<BR>—एकजाति-प्रतिबद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound<BR>only to one birth, not born again.<BR>—एक-जातीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, belonging to the same family or kind; of the<BR>same kind.<BR>—एक-ज्या, f. the cord of an arc; sine of<BR>30° or of the radius.<BR>—एक-ज्योतिस्, इस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—एक-तम, अस्, आ, अत्, one of many; one<BR>of two; one (used sometimes as an indefinite article).<BR>—एक-तर, अस्, आ, अम् (neut. अम् not अत् by Pā-<BR>ṇini VII. 1, 26), one of two, either, other, different;<BR>one of many; [Gr. ἑκάτερος Hib. n'-eachtar,<BR>‘neither of two.’]<BR>—एक-ता, f. oneness, unity, union,<BR>coincidence, identity.<BR>—एक-तान, अस्, आ, अम्, directed<BR>to one object only, having the mind fixed on one<BR>object only, closely attentive; (अस्), m. attention fixed<BR>on only one object; musical harmony, (? a various<BR>reading for the next.)<BR>—एक-ताल, अस्, m. harmony,<BR>unison, the accurate adjustment of song, dance, and<BR>instrumental music; (ई), f. an instrument for beating<BR>time, any instrument having but one note.<BR>—एक-<BR>तीर्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bathing in the same holy water, in-<BR>habiting the same hermitage; (ई), m. an associate in<BR>religious offices or objects, a spiritual brother.<BR>—एक-<BR>तेजन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having one shaft (as an ar-<BR>row).<BR>—एकत्रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the thirty-first.<BR>—एक-<BR>त्रिंशत्, त्, f. thirty-one.<BR>—एक-त्रिक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a ceremony.<BR>—एक-त्व, अम्, n. oneness, unity,<BR>union, coincidence, identity; (in gram.) the singular<BR>number.<BR>—एक-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m. single-toothed or<BR>tusked; a N. of Gaṇeśa, as having one tusk, the<BR>fellow-tusk being broken off in a scuffle by Kārtti-<BR>keya, or according to another legend by Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—एक-दण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having only one stick;<BR>designation of a class of beggars; [cf. त्रि-दण्डिन्.]<BR>—एक-दन्त, अस्, m. a N. of Gaṇeśa; [cf. एक-<BR>दंष्ट्र.]<BR>—एक-दिश्, क्, f. the same region.<BR>—एक-<BR>दुःख-सुख, अस्, आ, अम्, sympathizing, having the<BR>same joys and sorrows.<BR>—एक-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, one-<BR>eyed; (क्), m. a crow (as having excellent sight); an<BR>epithet of Śiva (as having one eye in his forehead).<BR>—एक-दृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, alone worthy of being<BR>beheld, the sole object of vision.<BR>—एक-दृष्टि,<BR>इस्, f. gaze fixed upon one object.<BR>—एक-देवत or<BR>एक-देवत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted or offered to one<BR>deity; directed to one deity.<BR>—एक-देश, अस्, m.<BR>one spot; a part, a portion or division of a whole;<BR>(एन), inst. partly; (अस्, आ, अम्), occupying the<BR>same place.<BR>—एकदेश-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated in<BR>the same region.<BR>—एकदेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, consisting<BR>of parts or portions, divided into parts (as a whole).<BR>—एक-देह, अस्, आ, अम्, having only one body,<BR>single-bodied, consisting of only one individual;<BR>elegantly formed; (अस्), m. the planet Mercury.<BR>—एक-द्यू, ऊस्, m., N. of a son of Nodhas (men-<BR>tioned Ṛg-veda VIII. 69, 6. Anukram.).<BR>—एक-<BR>धन, अम्, n. an excellent gift, an honorific offer-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. a kind of jug with which water is<BR>taken up at certain religious ceremonies; (आस्), f. pl.<BR>(scil. आपः) the water taken up by means of these<BR>vessels.<BR>—एकधन-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. taking or ob-<BR>taining the vessels of water called Ekadhana; obtain-<BR>ing an honorific offering.<BR>—एकधनिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>Ved. carrying the vessels called Ekadhana.<BR>—एक-<BR>धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having the same properties, of<BR>the same kind, professing the same religion.<BR>—एक-<BR>धुर्, ऊर्, f. a particular load or conveyance (?).<BR>—एक-धुर or एकधुरा-वह or एकधुरीण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fit for but one kind of labour, or for only<BR>one yoke; cattle for special burden.<BR>—एक-नक्ष-<BR>त्र, अम्, n. a lunar mansion consisting of only one<BR>star.<BR>—एक-नट, अस्, m. the principal actor in a<BR>drama, the manager, who recites the prologue.<BR>—एकनवत, अस्, ई, अम्, the ninety-first.<BR>—एक-<BR>नवति, इस्, f. ninety-one.<BR>—एकनवति-तम, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, the ninety-first.<BR>—एक-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having one master; (अस्), m. sole master or lord;<BR>N. of a copyist.<BR>—एक-नायक, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—एक-निश्चय, अस्, m. general agreement<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0183-b" target="_blank">Page0183-b+ 81</a>]<BR>or conclusion; (अस्, आ, अम्), having come to the<BR>same conclusion or resolution, having the same aim.<BR>—एक-निष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, intently fixed on one<BR>object.<BR>—एक-नीड, अस्, आ, अम्, having only one<BR>seat; having a common home.<BR>—एक-नेत्र, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva (‘one-eyed’).<BR>—एक-नेमि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, Ved. having one circumference.<BR>—एक-पक्ष,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of the same side or party, an associate, a<BR>firm partisan; partial, taking one view only; (अस्),<BR>m. one side; (ए), ind. in one point of view.<BR>—एक-<BR>पञ्चाश, अस्, ई, अम्, the fifty-first.<BR>—एक-पञ्चाशत्,<BR>त्, f. fifty-one.<BR>—एकपञ्चाशत्-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>fifty-first.<BR>—एक-पतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the same<BR>husband.<BR>—एक-पत्त्रिका, f. the plant Ocimum Gra-<BR>tissimum.<BR>—एक-पत्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, having only one<BR>wife.<BR>—एक-पत्नी, f. only one wife; the wife of one<BR>man, a faithful wife, one devoted to her husband;<BR>the wife of a man who has no other wives; the wife<BR>of the same man.<BR>—एक-पद् or एक-पाद्, पात्,<BR>पदी, पत्, having only one foot, limping, lame, in-<BR>complete; (पात्), m. an epithet of Śiva or of Viṣṇu;<BR>N. of a Dānava; (पदी), f. a foot-path; a path, a<BR>way, a road, (अज एकपाद्, त्, m., Ved. ‘the one-<BR>footed driver,’ probably a deity presiding over storms;<BR>according to the commentator a N. of the sun.)<BR>—एक-पद, अम्, n. only one step; a simple word,<BR>a simple nominal formation; present time, same<BR>time; (ए), ind. at the same moment, at once, sud-<BR>denly; (अस्, आ, अम्), having only one foot; consisting<BR>of a single word, named with a single word; (अस्),<BR>m. a kind of coitus; (आ), f. (scil. ऋच्) a verse con-<BR>sisting of only one Pāda or quarter-stanza; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a fabulous race.<BR>—एकपद-वत्, ind. like<BR>one word.<BR>—एकपद-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing in<BR>the same word.<BR>—एक-पदि, ind. upon one foot,<BR>with one foot.<BR>—एक-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. deciding<BR>by one (mark of the dice), an epithet of the dice in<BR>which one is decisive or of pre-eminent importance.<BR>—एक-परि, ind. one over or under, a term at dice.<BR>—एक-पर्णा, f., N. of a younger sister of Durgā<BR>and wife of Asita-Devala; an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—एक-पर्वतक, अस्, m. the same mountain, or<BR>N. of a certain mountain.<BR>—एक-पलाश, अस्, m. a<BR>single Butea Frondosa.<BR>—एक-पाटला, f., N. of a<BR>younger sister of Durgā and wife of Jaigīṣavya; an<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—एक-पाण, अस्, m. a single wager<BR>or stake.<BR>—एक-पात, अस्, आ, अम्, happening at once,<BR>sudden, rapid, coming suddenly.<BR>—एक-पातिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, standing alone or solitary, independant; (इनी), f.<BR>(scil. ऋच्) a verse to be taken by itself or regarded<BR>independently of the hymn to which it belongs.<BR>—एक-पाद, अस्, m. one foot; one and the same<BR>Pāda; (अस्, आ, अम्), having only one foot; standing<BR>on one foot, using only one foot; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a fabulous race.<BR>—एक-पादिका, f. title of the<BR>second book of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—एक-<BR>पादुक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a fabulous race (‘wearing<BR>only one shoe’).<BR>—एक-पिङ्ग or एक-पिङ्गल, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Kuvera (‘having a yellow mark in<BR>the place of one of his eyes’).<BR>—एक-पिण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, related, near of kin, united by the offering of<BR>the funeral cake.<BR>—एकपिण्ड-ता, f. or एकपिण्ड-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. connection by the funeral cake, con-<BR>sanguinity.<BR>—एक-पुत्र, अस्, m. having only one<BR>son.<BR>—एक-पुरुष, अस्, m. the one supreme spirit;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), consisting of only one man.<BR>—एक-<BR>पुष्पा, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—एक-पृथक्त्व, अम्,<BR>n. unity and distinctness.<BR>—एक-प्रकार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of the same kind.<BR>—एक-प्रख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, singu-<BR>larly like, pre-eminently similar.<BR>—एक-प्रभुत्व,<BR>अम्, n. the sovereignty of one, monarchy.<BR>—एक-<BR>प्रयत्न, अस्, m. one effort (of the voice).<BR>—एक-<BR>प्रहारिक, अस्, आ, अम्, killed by one blow.<BR>—एक-<BR>प्राण-योग, अस्, m. union in one breath.<BR>—एक-फल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having one or a principal result or object;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a plant.<BR>—एक-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, having<BR>only one thought; (इस्), m., N. of a frog in the<BR>Pañca-tantra.<BR>—१. एक-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, serving<BR>one and the same master; worshipping one deity.<BR> — 2. एक-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, eating together; (अम्),<BR>n. eating but one meal (a day).<BR>—एकभक्त-व्रत,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0183-c" target="_blank">Page0183-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n. eating but once a day as a religious obligation.<BR> — 1. एक-भक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, of one faith, believing in<BR>one deity.<BR>—२. एक-भक्ति, इस्, f. eating but one meal<BR>(a day).<BR>—एक-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, of the same<BR>nature; of a simple or single nature or temperament;<BR>(अस्), m. becoming one, oneness, agreement.<BR>—एक-<BR>भुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, eating but one meal (a day &c.);<BR>eating together.<BR>—एक-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being one,<BR>undivided; not distracted, closely attentive.<BR>—एक-<BR>भोजन, अम्, n. eating one meal a day; eating in<BR>common, feeding together.<BR>—एक-मति, इस्, f. the<BR>mind fixed upon one object; (इस्, इस्, इ), unanimous.<BR>—एक-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, fixing the mind upon<BR>one object, having only one thought, attentive;<BR>unanimous.<BR>—एक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>one.<BR>—एक-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, of one syllabic instant.<BR>—एक-मुख, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, having the face<BR>directed towards one spot, having the same aim; hav-<BR>ing one chief or head, having one overseer.<BR>—एक-<BR>मूर्धन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having the face directed to<BR>one spot, directed towards the same aim.<BR>—एक-<BR>मूला, f. the plants Linum Usitatissimum and Desmo-<BR>dium (Hedysarum) Gangeticum.<BR>—एक-यकार, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, containing only one य्.<BR>—एक-यष्टि, इस्, f.<BR>a single string of pearls.<BR>—एक-यष्टिका, f. a single<BR>string of flowers, pearls, &c.<BR>—एक-यावन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—एक-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, of the same<BR>womb, uterine; of the same mother, family or caste.<BR>—एक-रज, अस्, m. the plant Verbesina Scandens;<BR>see भृङ्ग-राज.<BR>—एक-रस, अस्, m. the only fla-<BR>vour, the only pleasure; (अस्, आ, अम्), of one flavour,<BR>relishing or finding pleasure in only one thing.<BR>—एक-<BR>रसिक, अस्, आ, अम्, influenced by one feeling, relishing<BR>one thing only.<BR>—एक-राज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, shining alone; (ट्),<BR>m. single or absolute king, the king by himself as dis-<BR>tinct from the people.<BR>—एक-राज, अस्, m. an absolute<BR>king.<BR>—एक-रात्र, अस्, m. a ceremony lasting one<BR>night; (अम्), n. duration of one night, one night, a<BR>night.<BR>—एकरात्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, sufficient for one<BR>night (or day).<BR>—एक-राशि, इस्, f. a heap, a crowd.<BR>—एकराशि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, heaped or collected<BR>together.<BR>—एक-रिक्थिन्, ई, m. a coheir.<BR>—एक-<BR>रूप, अम्, n. one form, one kind; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>uniform, of one kind, one-coloured.<BR>—एकरूप-तस्,<BR>ind. in one form, unalterably.<BR>—एकरूप-ता, f. uni-<BR>formity, unvariableness.<BR>—एकरूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>formed or arising from one.<BR>—एकर्च (एक-ऋच),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of one verse; (अम्), n., Ved.<BR>a hymn consisting of only one verse.<BR>—एकर्तु (एक-<BR>ऋतु), उस्, m., Ved. one time or season.<BR>—एकर्षि<BR>(एक-ऋषि), इस्, m. the only or chief Ṛṣi.<BR>—एक-<BR>लव्य, अस्, m., N. of a son of Hiraṇya-dhanus and<BR>king of the Niṣādas.<BR>—एक-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. a place<BR>or district in which for five Krośas there is but one<BR>Phallus, an isolated Liṅga; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Kuvera; [cf. एक-पिङ्ग.]<BR>—एक-लू, ऊस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—एक-वक्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava; perhaps<BR>a wrong form for एक-चक्र.<BR>—एक-वचन, अम्, n.<BR>the singular number.<BR>—एक-वत्, ind. like one, simple.<BR>—एकवद्-भाव, अस्, m. an aggregate of many, as<BR>in grammar, the formation of a compound noun of<BR>several nouns.<BR>—एक-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, of one colour,<BR>one-coloured; identical; of one tribe, of one caste;<BR>consisting of only one letter; of one quality; (ई), f.<BR>beating time, marking musical measure by clapping<BR>the hands, or the instrument which does so, a casta-<BR>net; see एक-ताली.<BR>—एकवर्ण-वत्, ind. like one<BR>letter.<BR>—एकवर्ण-समीकरण, अम्, n. an equation<BR>involving only one unknown quantity; uniliteral equa-<BR>tion.<BR>—एकवर्णिक, अस्, आ, अम्, of one colour, of<BR>one caste.<BR>—एक-वर्षिका, f. a heifer one year old.<BR>—एक-वसन, अस्, आ, अम्, having only one gar-<BR>ment or robe.<BR>—एक-वस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having only<BR>one garment, in one dress.<BR>—एकवस्त्र-ता, f. the<BR>state of having only one garment.<BR>—एकवस्त्र-<BR>संवीत, अस्, आ, अम्, clothed in one garment.<BR>—एक-<BR>वस्त्रार्ध-संवीत, अस्, आ, अम्, clothed in half a single<BR>garment.<BR>—एक-वाक्य, अम्, n. one opinion.<BR>—एक-<BR>वाक्य-ता, f. unanimity.<BR>—एकवाण-वत्, ind. as one<BR>arrow.<BR>—एक-वाद, अस्, m. a musical instrument, a<BR>kind of drum or tabor.<BR>—एक-वाद्या, f., Ved. a kind<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0184-a" target="_blank">Page0184-a+ 81</a>]<BR>of imp or demon.<BR>—एक-वारम् or एक-वारे, ind.<BR>only once, at once, at one time, suddenly.<BR>—एक-<BR>वास, अस्, आ, अम्, having one house or one residence.<BR>—एक-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having only one garment,<BR>in one dress.<BR>—एकविंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the twenty-<BR>first; consisting of twenty-one; connected with the<BR>Ekaviṃśa-stoma; (अस्), m. the Ekaviṃśa-stoma; N. of<BR>one of the six Pṛṣṭhya-stomas.<BR>—एकविंशक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the twenty-first; containing twenty-one.<BR>—एक-<BR>विंशत्, त्, or एक-विंशति, इस्, f. twenty-one, a com-<BR>bination or collection of twenty-one.<BR>—एकविंशति-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the twenty-first.<BR>—एकविंशति-धा,<BR>ind. twenty-one-fold, in twenty-one parts.<BR>—एक-<BR>विंश-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. connected with the Eka-<BR>viṃśa-stoma.<BR>—एकविंश-स्तोम, अस्, m., Ved. a Stoma<BR>consisting of twenty-one parts.<BR>—एक-विध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of one kind, simple.<BR>—एक-विलोचन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one-eyed; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a fabulous race of people.<BR>—एकविषयिन्, ई, m. having one common object or<BR>end, a rival.<BR>—एक-वीर, अस्, m. a pre-eminent hero<BR>or warrior; N. of a plant.<BR>—एक-वृक्ष, अस्, m. an<BR>isolated tree; a desert place in which but one tree is<BR>seen for four Krośas.<BR>—एक-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. simple.<BR>—एक-वृन्द, अस्, m. a peculiar disease of the<BR>throat.<BR>—एक-वृष, अस्, m., Ved. the chief bull,<BR>the master of the herd.<BR>—एक-वेणि, इस् or ई, f. a single<BR>braid of hair (worn by a woman as a mark of mourn-<BR>ing for an absent husband &c.); a woman whose<BR>hair is tied in a single braid.<BR>—एक-वेश्मन्, अ, n. a<BR>solitary house or room.<BR>—एक-व्यवसायिन्, ई, m.<BR>following the same employment.<BR>—एक-व्रात्य, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. the chief or principal Vrātya.<BR>—एक-शत,<BR>अम्, n. 101; (अस्, ई, अम्), the 101st.<BR>—एकशत-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 101st.<BR>—एकशत-धा, ind.<BR>101-fold; in 101 parts.<BR>—एकशत-विध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, 101-fold.<BR>—एक-शफ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. whole-<BR>hoofed, not cloven-hoofed; (अस् or अम्), m. n.<BR>any animal whose hoof is not cloven; (अस्), m.<BR>a horse.<BR>—एक-शरण, अम्, n. one only hope or<BR>refuge, especially applied to a deity.<BR>—एक-शरीर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of one body or blood; consanguineous.<BR>—एकशरीरान्वय (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m. consangui-<BR>neous descent.<BR>—एकशरीरारम्भ (˚र-आर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. commencement of consanguinity by the union of<BR>father and mother.<BR>—एक-शरीरावयव (˚र-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a descendant in a right line, a blood-kinsman.<BR>—एकशरीरावयव-त्व (˚र-अव्˚), अम्, n. con-<BR>sanguineous descent or connection.<BR>—एक-शाख, अस्,<BR>m. a Brāhman of the same branch or school.<BR>—एक-<BR>शाल, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—एक-शिति-पद्, पात्,<BR>पदी, पत्, Ved. having one white foot.<BR>—एक-<BR>शीर्षन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having the face turned towards<BR>the same place.<BR>—एकशील-समाचर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who leads one manner of life, whose manners<BR>are always the same.<BR>—एक-शुङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having one sheath.<BR>—एक-शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>only one horn; (अस्), m. a unicorn, a rhinoceros, an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; (आस्), m. a class of Pitṛs; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of the mind-born daughter of the Pitṛs called<BR>Sukālas.<BR>—एक-शेप, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—एक-<BR>शेष, अस्, m. ‘the remainder of one only,’ a term in<BR>grammar denoting that of two or more words only<BR>one remains or is retained (e. g. the dual रामौ is<BR>the one remainder of रामः + रामः).<BR>—एक-<BR>श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, once heard.<BR>—एकश्रुत-धर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, keeping in mind what one has heard<BR>once.<BR>—एकश्रुतधर-त्व, अम्, n. state of such a<BR>person.<BR>—एक-श्रुति, इस्, f. the hearing of only one<BR>sound, monotony; the neutral accentless tone; (इ),<BR>ind. in a monotonous manner.<BR>—एक-श्रुष्टि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, Ved. obedient to one command.<BR>—एकषष्ट,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the sixty-first; connected with sixty-one.<BR>—एक-षष्टि, इस्, f. sixty-one.<BR>—एकषष्टि-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the sixty-first.<BR>—एकसप्तत, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the seventy-first.<BR>—एक-सप्तति, इस्, f. seventy-<BR>one.<BR>—एकसप्तति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the seventy-<BR>first.<BR>—एक-सभ, अम्, n. a common or general<BR>place of meeting.<BR>—एक-सर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, closely<BR>attentive, having the mind intent upon one object.<BR>—एक-सहस्र, अम्, n. 1001.<BR>—एक-साक्षिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, witnessed by one.<BR>—एक-सार्थम्, ind. to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0184-b" target="_blank">Page0184-b+ 81</a>]<BR>gether, in one company.<BR>—एक-सूत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>small double drum played by a string and ball at-<BR>tached to the body of it.<BR>—एक-सूनु, उस्, m. an<BR>only son.<BR>—एक-स्तोम, अस्, m. ‘consisting of one<BR>Stoma,’ N. of a Soma ceremony.<BR>—एक-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, standing together, remaining in one place, re-<BR>maining in the same place, conjoined, collected,<BR>combined, assembled.<BR>—एक-स्थान, अम्, n. one<BR>place, the same place.<BR>—एक-हंस, अस्, m. the<BR>chief or highest Haṃsa (an allegorical designation of<BR>the soul); N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—एक-हायन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>one year old; (ई), f. a heifer one year old; (अम्), n.<BR>the period of one year.<BR>—एकांश (एक-अं˚), अस्, m.<BR>a distinct or separate part, a part in general.<BR>—एका-<BR>क्ष (एक-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having only one axle;<BR>one-eyed; having an excellent eye; (अस्), m. a crow;<BR>an epithet of Śiva; N. of a Dānava.<BR>—एकाक्षर<BR>(एक-अक्˚), अम्, n. a monosyllable; the sacred mono-<BR>syllable ॐ.<BR>—एकाषर-कोष, अस्, m. a vocabulary<BR>of monosyllabic words by Puruṣottamadeva.<BR>—एका-<BR>क्षर-गणपति-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. a hymn in honour of<BR>Gaṇeśa, a portion of the Rudrayāmala.<BR>—एकाक्षरी-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the production of only one syllable, con-<BR>traction.<BR>—एकाग्र (एक-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having one<BR>point, fixing one's attention on only one point or<BR>object, closely attentive, intent; undisturbed, unper-<BR>plexed; known, celebrated; single-pointed; (अस्), m.<BR>(in mathematics) the whole of the long side of a figure<BR>which is subdivided.<BR>—एकाग्र-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the mind intent on one object.<BR>—एकाग्र-<BR>तस्, ind. with undivided attention.<BR>—एकाग्र-ता, f.<BR>or एकाग्र-त्व, अम्, n. intentness in the pursuit of<BR>one object, close and undisturbed attention.<BR>—एका-<BR>ग्र-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, fixing one's eyes on one spot.<BR>—एकाग्र-मनस्, अस्, n. intentness.<BR>—एकाग्र्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, closely attentive; (अम्), n. close attention.<BR>—एकाङ्ग (एक-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a single member, a<BR>single part; (अस्), m. a body-guard; the planet<BR>Mercury; the planet Mars; an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>(अम्), n. sandal-wood.<BR>—एकाङ्गिका, f. a preparation<BR>made with sandal-wood.<BR>—एकातपत्र (एक-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, characterized by one umbrella (said of<BR>universal sovereignty having an umbrella as one of<BR>its insignia).<BR>—एकात्म-ता, f. the unity of spiritual<BR>essence, the doctrine of one universal spirit.<BR>—एकात्-<BR>मन् (एक-आत्˚), आ, m. the one spirit; (आ, आ, अ),<BR>depending solely on self, solitary.<BR>—एकात्म्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, only, alone, homogeneous.<BR>—एकादश, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the eleventh; consisting of eleven, lasting eleven<BR>months; (ई), f. the eleventh day of the half month,<BR>especially sacred to Viṣṇu, when fasting is very effi-<BR>cacious; presentation of offerings to deceased ancestors<BR>or Pitṛs on the eleventh day after his decease, on<BR>which occasion Brāhmans are fed and the period of<BR>impurity for a Brāhman terminates; (अम्), n. the<BR>number eleven.<BR>—एकादशक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting<BR>of eleven, consisting of eleven parts; (अम्), n. the<BR>number eleven.<BR>—एकादश-कृत्वस्, ind. eleven<BR>times.<BR>—एका-दशन्, अ, pl. eleven.<BR>—एकादशम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the eleventh.<BR>—एकादश-विध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, eleven-fold.<BR>—एकादशाह (˚श-अह), अस्, m. a<BR>sacrifice lasting eleven days.<BR>—एकादशिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>consisting of eleven; (इनी), f., Ved. the number eleven.<BR>—एकादशिन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to eleven (?).<BR>—एकादशी-तत्त्व, अम्, n. part of the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—एकादशी-व्रत, अम्, n. fasting on the eleventh day.<BR>—एकादशोत्तम (˚श-उत्˚), अस्, m. chief of eleven;<BR>epithet of Śiva (chief among the eleven Rudras).<BR>—एकादेश (एक-आद्˚), अस्, m. one substitute for two<BR>or more letters (e. g. one vowel substituted for two<BR>other vowels either by the blending of the two vowels<BR>together or by the dropping of one).<BR>—एकाधिपति<BR>(एक-अध्˚), इस्, m. a sole monarch.<BR>—एकानंशा<BR>(एक-अन्-अंश), f. ‘the only (day) receiving no part<BR>(of the moon),’ an epithet of Kuhū or the day of the<BR>new moon personified as a daughter of Aṅgiras and<BR>identified with Durgā, born together with Kṛṣṇa,<BR>worshipped with Kṛṣṇa and Baladeva.<BR>—एकानु-<BR>दिष्ट (एक-अन्˚), अम्, n. (scil. श्राद्ध) a funeral<BR>ceremony performed for only one ancestor recently<BR>dead; (अस्, आ, अम्), left as a funeral feast; one who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0184-c" target="_blank">Page0184-c+ 81</a>]<BR>has recently partaken of it.<BR>—एकान्त (एक-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the only end or aim, exclusiveness; a lonely, re-<BR>tired or secret place; devotion to one, worship of<BR>one being, unitarian doctrine, monotheism; (अम् or<BR>एन or ए), ind. solely, only exclusively, absolutely; ne-<BR>cessarily; alone, apart, privately; much, exceedingly;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), directed towards one point or object;<BR>worshipping only one; excessive; solitary, lonely,<BR>retired; aside, apart.<BR>—एकान्त-करुण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very compassionate, weakly charitable.<BR>—एकान्त-तस्,<BR>ind. solely, only exclusively, apart; see एकान्तम्.<BR>—एकान्त-त्व, अम्, n. exclusive worship.<BR>—एकान्त-<BR>दुःषमा (˚दुस्-समा), f. ‘containing only bad<BR>years,’ with Jainas an epithet of two spokes in the<BR>wheel of time, the sixth of the Avasarpiṇī and the<BR>first of the Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—एकान्त-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being alone or solitary.<BR>—एकान्त-मति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>devoted to one object.<BR>—एकान्तर (एक-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, separated by one intermediate member, next<BR>but one.<BR>—एकान्त-राज्, ट्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—एकान्त-विहारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, a solitary wanderer.<BR>—एकान्त-सुषमा (˚सु-समा), f. ‘containing ex-<BR>clusively good years,’ with Jainas an epithet of two<BR>spokes in the wheel of time, the first of the Avasar-<BR>piṇī and the sixth of the Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—एकान्त-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, staying or remaining alone or apart.<BR>—एकान्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, final, conclusive.<BR>—एकान्ति-<BR>क-त्व, अम्, n. the being devoted to one object.<BR>—एकान्ति-त्व, अम्, n. devotion to one (with loc.).<BR>—एकान्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, devoted to only one, having<BR>the mind fixed on only one object, worshipping only<BR>one (with gen.).<BR>—एकान्न (एक-अन्˚), अम्, n. one<BR>and the same food; (अस्), m. a mess-mate.<BR>—एकान्न-<BR>भुज्, क्, m. a mess-mate.<BR>—एकान्नादिन् (एक-अन्न-<BR>आद्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating a supply of food from one<BR>person only.<BR>—एकाब्दा (एक-अब्˚), f. a heifer one<BR>year old.<BR>—एकायन (एक-अय्˚), अम्, n. a lonely,<BR>retired place; a meeting-place; rendezvous of all<BR>thoughts, union of thoughts; devotion to one, doc-<BR>trine of unity, monotheism; N. of a Śākhā or<BR>branch of the Veda; (अस्, आ, अम्), passable for only<BR>one, as a foot-path; fixing one's thoughts on one<BR>object, closely attentive, intent.<BR>—एकायन-गत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has fixed all his thoughts on one<BR>object.<BR>—एकायु (एक-आयु), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. assem-<BR>bling or collecting all living beings; the first living<BR>being; (Sāy.) providing the most excellent food.<BR>—एकार्णव (एक-अर्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. a general<BR>inundation.<BR>—एकार्थ (एक-अर्˚), अस्, m. the same<BR>object; (अस्, आ, अम्), having one or the same aim or<BR>object; having one meaning; N. of a glossary; ex-<BR>pressing one thing, forming only one notion.<BR>—एकार्-<BR>थ-ता, f. or एकार्थ-त्व, अम्, n. state of having<BR>only one aim or object.<BR>—एकार्थ-समुपेत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, arrived at one object.<BR>—एकार्थी-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the having one meaning.<BR>—एकावम (एक-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, inferior or less by one.<BR>—एकावयव<BR>(एक-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, made up of the same mem-<BR>bers or constituent parts.<BR>—एकावली (एक-आव्˚), f. a<BR>single line, a single string of pearls, beads, flowers,<BR>&c.; (in rhetoric) a series of periods in which there<BR>is a regular transition from a predicate to a subject or<BR>from a subject to a predicate.<BR>—एकाशीत, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>the eighty-first.<BR>—एकाशीति (एक-अस्˚), इस्, f. eighty-one.<BR>—एकाशीति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the eighty-first.<BR>—एका-<BR>श्रम (एक-आश्˚), अस्, m. a solitary hermitage.<BR>—एका-<BR>श्रित (एक-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, resting upon or clinging<BR>to one object.<BR>—एकाश्रित-गुण, अस्, m. a simple<BR>attribute or predicate, as form, taste, smell, &c.<BR>—एकाष्टका (एक-अष्˚), f. the first or chief Ash-<BR>ṭakā, either the first Aṣṭakā after full moon (=<BR>अष्टका) or the first Aṣṭakā of a year or a longer<BR>period of time.<BR>—एकाष्टी, f. a pod or one seed of<BR>cotton.<BR>—एकाष्ठील (एक-अष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>one kernel; (अस्), m., N. of the plant Agati Grandi-<BR>flora Desv.; (आ), f. the plant Clypea Hernandifolia.<BR>—एकासनिक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. एक and आसन), hav-<BR>ing only one seat.<BR>—एकाह (एक-अह), अस्, m. the<BR>period of one day; a ceremony or sacrifice lasting<BR>only one day, a Soma sacrifice in which Soma is<BR>only once prepared; (अम्), ind. during one day.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">Page0185-a+ 79</a>]<BR>—एकाह-गम, अस्, m. a day's journey.<BR>—एका-<BR>हार (एक-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taking food only once a<BR>day.<BR>—एकेष (एक-ईषा), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. furnished<BR>with one pole.<BR>—एकैक (एक-एक), अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>by one, single, every single one; (अम्), ind. singly,<BR>one by one.<BR>—एकैक-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, one by one<BR>(of many).<BR>—एकैक-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, existing in<BR>every single one.<BR>—एकैक-शस्, ind. one by one,<BR>severally, seriatim.<BR>—एकैकश्य, अम्, n. single state,<BR>severalty; (एन), ind. severally.<BR>—एकैषिका (एक-<BR>एष्˚), f., N. of a medicinal plant.<BR>—एकोक्ति (एक-उक्˚),<BR>इस्, f. a single expression, a single word.<BR>—एकोत्तर<BR>(एक-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, greater or more by one, in-<BR>creasing by one.<BR>—एकोत्तरिका, f. title of the fourth<BR>Āgama of the Buddhists.<BR>—एकोदक (एक-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, connected (as relatives) by the offering of<BR>funereal oblations of water to the same deceased an-<BR>cestor.<BR>—एकोदात्त (एक-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>one Udātta accent.<BR>—एकोद्दिष्ट (एक-उद्˚), अम्, n.<BR>(scil. श्राद्ध) the Śrāddha or funeral rite performed<BR>for one definite individual deceased, not including<BR>other ancestors.<BR>—एकोन (एक-ऊन), अस्, आ, अम्, less<BR>by one, minus one; (used in composition with विं-<BR>शति and the following decads, e. g. एकोनविंशति =<BR>nineteen.)<BR>—एकोशिका, f. the plant Cissampelos Hexan-<BR>dra (?).<BR>—एकौघ-भूत (एक-ओघ-भ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>collected into one mass, heaped or crowded together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकक|एककः
एकक, अस्, आ, अम्, single, alone, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकत|एकतः
एकत, अस्, m., N. of a deity [cf. द्वित and त्रित],<BR>one of the seven Dharmarājartvijas; N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतस्
एकतस्, ind. from one side, on one side, on one<BR>part; singly, one by one; used sometimes as an abl.<BR>c. of एक (e. g. एकतो ऽपि पदात्, ‘after the same<BR>word’); एकतस् — एकतस्, on the one hand — on the<BR>other hand, on the one side — on the other side, here<BR> — there.<BR>—एकतो-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, having teeth on<BR>only one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकत्र
एकत्र, ind. in one place, on one spot, in close<BR>connection; in a combined manner, together; used<BR>sometimes as a loc. c. of एक (e. g. एकत्र करे, ‘on<BR>one hand’); एकत्र — अपरत्र or एकत्र — अन्यस्-<BR>मिन्, on the one side — on the other side, here — there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदा
एकदा, ind. at the same time, at once; once,<BR>sometimes; once on a time, one day; at one time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधा
एकधा, ind. simply, singly; in one way, to-<BR>gether; at once, once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकल|एकलः
एकल, अस्, आ, अम्, alone, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशस्
एकशस्, ind. one by one, singly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाकिन्
एकाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. एक and rt. अञ्च्?), alone,<BR>solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीकृ
एकी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to unite, associate, join together; combine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीभू
एकी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्, to become<BR>one, to join together, blend, combine, mingle.<BR>—एकी-<BR>भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, blending together, contracted.<BR>—एकी-भाव, अस्, m. becoming one, combination,<BR>association; common nature or property.<BR>—एकी-<BR>भाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, relating to the blending of vowels<BR>or accents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीय|एकीयः
एकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to one, proceeding<BR>from one; belonging to the same party; a partisan<BR>or associate, a companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्त|एकान्तं|एकान्तः
एकान्त, एकैक, &c. See under एक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एक्ष्
एक्ष् एक्ष् (आ-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A. एक्षते, -षितुम्,<BR>to look at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एज्
एज् एज्, cl. 1. P. A. एजति, -ते, एजाञ्-चक्रे,<BR>एजिष्यति, एजितुम्, to stir, move, tremble,<BR>shake; A. to shine: Caus. एजयति, -यितुम्, to move:<BR>Desid. एजिजिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजक
एजक, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजत्|एजन्त्
एजत्, त्, n., Ved. anything moving or living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजत्क
एजत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling; (अस्), m., Ved. a<BR>kind of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजथु|एजथुः
एजथु, उस्, m., Ved. trembling, shaking (of the<BR>earth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजन|एजनं
एजन, अम्, n. trembling, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजय
एजय, अस्, आ, अम्, or एजयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, caus-<BR>ing to shake or tremble, driving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजित
एजित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, agitated, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजितव्य
एजितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजितृ
एजितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a shaker, shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजि
एजि एजि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एज्य
एज्य एज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. यज् with आ),<BR>Ved. to be offered (as an oblation or sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एठ्
एठ् एठ्, cl. 1. A. एठते, to annoy, resist<BR>or oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एड|एडः
एड एड, अस्, आ, अम्, deaf; (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of sheep.<BR>—एड-गज, अस्, m. the medicinal plant<BR>Cassia Tora or Alata, used for the cure of ring-worm.<BR>—एड-मूक, अस्, आ, अम्, deaf and dumb; wicked,<BR>perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडक|एडकः
एडक, अस्, m. a kind of sheep, a ram, a wild<BR>goat; a certain medicinal plant; (आ), f. a ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडुक|एडुकं|एडुकः
एडुक एडुक, अम्, n. or एडूक or एडोक, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a building constructed of rubbish, bones,<BR>&c., or of hard substances resembling bones; a wall<BR>enclosing bones, a tomb, &c.; (with Buddhists) a<BR>sanctuary filled with relics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एण|एणः
एण एण, अस्, ई, m. f. or एणक, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of deer or antelope, described as being of a black<BR>colour with beautiful eyes and short legs; (in astron.)<BR>Capricorn.<BR>—एण-तिलक, अस्, m. the moon; (the<BR>marks of an antelope being fancifully visible on its<BR>disk.)<BR>—एण-दृश्, क्, m. Capricorn.<BR>—एण-भृत्, त्,<BR>m. the moon.<BR>—एणाजिन (एण-अज्˚), अम्, n. deer-<BR>skin.<BR>—एणी-पचन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race (cooking<BR>antelopes for food).<BR>—एणी-पद, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>snake; (ई), f. a kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत|एतं|एतः
एत 1. एत, एतस्, एता or एनी, एतम् (said to be<BR>fr. rt. 5. इ), of a variegated colour, shining, varying the<BR>colours; (Sāy.) going, flowing; (अस्), m. a deer or<BR>antelope; the hide of one; a variegated colour;<BR>(नी) f., Ved. a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतग्व|एतग्वः
एतग्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of a variegated or dark<BR>colour; (Sāy. also) going on their way; epithet of<BR>the horses of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतश|एतशः
एतश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of variegated colour, shin-<BR>ing; epithet of Brahmaṇaspati; (अस्), m. a horse of<BR>variegated colour, a dappled horse, especially the<BR>horse or horses of the sun; N. of a favourite of Indra,<BR>who defends him from Sūrya; N. of one of the seven<BR>sons of Vātaraśana, author of two Ṛg-veda hymns;<BR>a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतशस्
एतशस्, आस्, m. a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत|एतं|एतः
एत 2. एत, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 5. इ with आ), arrived,<BR>come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एति|एतिः
एति, इस्, f., Ved. arrival, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत्य
एत्य, ind. having gone near to or approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद् एतद्, एषस्, एषा, एतद् (fr. ए with pro-<BR>nom. base त. The vowel ए appears also in एक, एव,<BR>&c.; and just as the simple base त substitutes स for<BR>the nom. sing. m. and f., so एत makes एषस्,<BR>एषा; but एत appears in all the other cases, and the<BR>neut. एतद् is used as the base to form derivatives<BR>such as एतदीय &c., and at the beginning of com-<BR>pounds), this, this here, here, especially as pointing<BR>to what is nearest to the speaker (e. g. एष वाणः,<BR>this arrow here in my hand; एष याति पन्थाः,<BR>here goes the way; एष कालः, here, i. e. now, is<BR>the time; एतद्, this here, i. e. this world here below).<BR>एतद् is sometimes used in this sense to give emphasis<BR>to the personal pronouns (e. g. एषो ऽहम्, I this very<BR>person here) or with omission of those pronouns<BR>(e. g. एष त्वां स्वर्गं नयानि, I standing here<BR>will convey you to heaven; एतौ प्रविष्टौ स्वः,<BR>we two here have entered). एतद् as the subject of<BR>a sentence agrees in gender and number with the<BR>predicate without reference to the noun to be supplied<BR>(e. g. एतद् मे धनम्, this [scil. cow] is my<BR>wealth); but may sometimes remain in the neut.<BR>sing. (e. g. एतद् गुरुषु वृत्तिः, this is the custom<BR>among Gurus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद् often refers to what precedes, especially when<BR>it is associated with इदम्, the latter then referring<BR>to what follows (e. g. एष प्रथमः कल्पः —<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">Page0185-c+ 78</a>]<BR>अनुकल्पस् to अयं ज्ञेयः, this before-mentioned<BR>is the first rule, but this following may be considered<BR>a secondary rule).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद् may be used in connection with a relative<BR>clause, in which case the relative generally follows<BR>(e. g. एष चैव गुरुर् धर्मो यम् प्रवक्ष्-<BR>याम्य् अहं तव, this is the important law, which<BR>I will proclaim to you).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद्, ind. in this manner, thus, so, here, at this<BR>time, now (e. g. एतत् सुप्तः, asleep in this manner;<BR>न वा उ एतद् म्रियसे, not at this time dost thou<BR>die).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद् appears at the beginning of compounds, as<BR>in the following examples.<BR>—एतज्-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>arising from this.<BR>—एतत्-काल, अस्, m. the present<BR>time; (ए), ind. now.<BR>—एतत्कालीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>belonging to the present time.<BR>—एतत्-क्षणात्, ind.<BR>from this moment, henceforth; (ए), ind. now.<BR>—एतत्-<BR>तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, similar to this.<BR>—एतत्-प्रथम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who does anything for the first time.<BR>—एतत्-सम, अस्, आ, अम्, equal to this.<BR>—एतद्-<BR>अतिरिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, besides this.<BR>—एतद्-अनन्तरम्,<BR>ind. immediately after this.<BR>—एतद्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>terminating with this, ending thus.<BR>—एतद्-अर्थ,<BR>अस्, m. this matter; (अम् or ए), ind. on this account,<BR>for this end, therefore; एतद्-अर्थम् — यत्, for this<BR>end — that.<BR>—एतद्-अवधि, ind. to this limit, so far.<BR>—एतद्-अवस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, of such a state or con-<BR>dition.<BR>—एतद्-आत्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in this<BR>Ātman or supreme soul.<BR>—एतद्-आदि, इस्, इस्, इ, be-<BR>ginning thus, and so forth.<BR>—एतद्-एव, ind. this<BR>very same.<BR>—एतद्-द्वितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>does anything for the second time.<BR>—एतद्-योनिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, residing or having one's origin in that.<BR>—एतद्-<BR>वत्, ind. like this, thus.<BR>—एतन्-न, ind. not so.<BR>—एतन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of this, of such<BR>a kind; [cf. Zend aiśa, aita; Old Pers. aita;<BR>Armen. ais, aid; Osk. eiso; Hib. ise, ‘he, himself;’<BR>isa and isi, ‘she, herself.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतदीय
एतदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतर्हि
एतर्हि, ind., Ved. (very often in the Brāhmaṇas),<BR>now, at this time, at present, now-a-days; then (cor-<BR>relative to यर्हि); a certain measure of time = fifteen<BR>इदानीम्s or one fifteenth of a क्षिप्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतादृक्ष
एतादृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved., or एतादृश्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, or एतादृश, अस्, ई, अम्, such, such like; so<BR>formed, of this kind, similar to this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतावत्|एतावन्त्
एतावत्, आन्, अती, अत्, so great, so much, so many,<BR>of such a measure or compass, of such extent, so<BR>far, of such quality or kind; often found in connection<BR>with a relative clause, in which case the latter gene-<BR>rally follows (e. g. एतावान् एव पुरुषो यज् जायात्मा<BR>प्रजेति ह, a man is of such a measure as [i. e. is<BR>made complete by] himself, his wife, and his progeny);<BR>(वत्), ind. so far, thus far, so much, in such a degree,<BR>thus, &c.<BR>—एतावत्-त्व, अम्, n. quantity, number;<BR>greatness; (with following यद्) such a state or con-<BR>dition that; such extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतन|एतनः
एतन एतन, अस्, m. expiration, breathing<BR>out, discharging air from the lungs; the fish Silurus<BR>Pelorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतृ
एतृ एतृ, ता, m. (rt. 5. इ), Ved. going, ap-<BR>proaching, asking, requesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एम|एमः
एम, अस्, m. or एमन्, अ, n., Ved. a course, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एदिधिषुःपति|एदिधिषुःपतिः
एदिधिषुःपति एदिधिषुःपति, इस्, m., Ved.<BR>the husband of a younger sister, whose elder sister<BR>has not yet been married. See दिधिषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एध्
एध् एध् (connected with rt. ऋध्), cl. 1. A.<BR>(rarely P.) एधते, एधाञ्-चक्रे, एधिष्यते,<BR>ऐधिष्ट, एधितुम्, to prosper, increase, grow, be-<BR>come happy, grow strong, become great; to extend;<BR>to swell, rise (as waters): Caus. एधयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to prosper, increase, celebrate, honour: Desid.<BR>एदिधिषते; [said to be related to Gr. οἶδος, οἰδἀω;<BR>perhaps also to Lat. œsculus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधतु|एधतुः
1. एधतु, उस्, m. (for 2. see एन्ध् next page), Ved.<BR>prosperity, happiness; a man; (उस्, उस्, उ), increased,<BR>grown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधनीय
एधनीय or एधितव्य or एध्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be increased or enlarged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधमान
एधमान, अस्, आ, अम्, prospering, increasing.<BR>—एधमान-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. hating the pros-<BR>perous, especially those rendered insolent by pros-<BR>perity; (Sāy.) hating the impious who prosper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधस्
1. एधस्, अस्, n. (in comp.) prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधा
एधा, f. happiness, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधित|एधितः
एधित, अस्, आ, अम्, grown, increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधितृ
एधितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, increasing, growing, enlarging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एन|एनः
एन एन, a pronom. base (used for certain<BR>cases of the 3rd personal pronoun, and occurring only<BR>in the acc. sing. du. pl. (एनम्, एनाम्, एनद्, &c.),<BR>inst. sing. (एनेन, एनया), gen. loc. du. (एनयोस्, Ved.<BR>एनोस्); the other cases are formed fr. the pronom.<BR>base अ, see under इदम्), he, she, it; this, that.<BR>This pronoun is enclitic and cannot begin a sentence.<BR>It is generally used alone, so that एनम् पुरुषम्,<BR>‘that man,’ would be very unusual if not incorrect.<BR>Grammarians assert that the substitution of एनम्<BR>for इमम् or एतम् takes place in case of the re-em-<BR>ployment of these pronouns in the subsequent part<BR>of a sentence; see Gram. 836; [cf. Gr. ἕν, οἶος<BR>Goth. ains; Old Pruss. ains; Lat oinos, unus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एना
एना, ind., Ved. in this manner, thus; here, there;<BR>then, at that time; पर एना, further on; पर एना<BR>पृथिव्या, beyond the earth here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनस्
एनस् एनस्, अस्, n. (fr. इन्, but said to be<BR>fr. rt. 5. इ), mischief, crime; curse, unhappiness; sin,<BR>offence, fault; censure, blame.<BR>—एनस्-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, or एनस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, wicked, sinful, a sinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनस्य
एनस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. caused by crime; sinful,<BR>wicked, wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनी
एनी एनी. See under 1. एत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एन्ध्
एन्ध् एन्ध् (आ-इन्ध्), cl. 7. A. एन्धे, एन्धितुम्,<BR>to kindle, inflame; to be inflamed, to flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एध|एधः
एध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. simple rt. इन्ध्), kindling,<BR>one who kindles, cf. अग्न्य्-एध; (अस्), m. fuel, as<BR>wood, grass, &c.; [cf. Gr. αἰθός]<BR>—एधाहार<BR>(एध-आह्˚), अस्, m. one who collects fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधतु|एधतुः
2. एधतु, उस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधस्
2. एधस्, अस्, n. fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एन्व्
एन्व् एन्व् (आ-इन्व्), cl. 1. P. एन्वति, -वितुम्, to<BR>bring near, to bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एम|एमः
एम एम. See under एतृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एमूष
एमूष एमूष, अस्, m., Ved. corrupted from<BR>एमुषम्, the part. perf. of rt. अम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्
एर् एर् (आ-ईर्), cl. 2. A. एर्ते, एरितुम्, to go to or<BR>into: Caus. एरयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to bring near, pro-<BR>cure; to obtain; to raise (the voice in singing &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरक
एरक एरक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga; (आ), f.<BR>a sort of grass of emollient and diluent properties;<BR>(in the Mausala-parva of the Mahā-bh. this grass when<BR>plucked by Kṛṣṇa and his family turned to clubs);<BR>(अम्), n. a woollen carpet; [cf. ऐरक्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरङ्ग|एरंगः|एरङ्गः
एरङ्ग एरङ्ग, अस्, m. a kind of fish; [cf.<BR>एलङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्ड|एरंडः|एरण्डः
एरण्ड एरण्ड, अस्, m. the castor-oil plant,<BR>Palma Christi or Ricinus Communis; (आ), f. long<BR>pepper.<BR>—एरण्ड-पत्त्रिका, f. or एरण्ड-फला, f.<BR>the plant Croton Polyandrum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डक|एरंडकः|एरण्डकः
एरण्डक, अस्, m. the plant Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरमत्तक
एरमत्तक एरमत्तक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरु
एरु एरु, a word of doubtful meaning in<BR>Atharva-veda VI. 22, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्त्स्
एर्त्स् एर्त्स्, Desid. of आर्ध्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्वारु|एर्वारुः|एर्व्वारुः
एर्वारु एर्वारु, उस्, m. f. or एर्वारुक, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of cucumber, Cucumis Utilissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एल
एल एल, अम्, n. a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलद
एलद, अम्, n. a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलक|एलकः
एलक एलक, अस्, m. a ram. See एडक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलङ्ग|एलंगः|एलङ्गः
एलङ्ग एलङ्ग, अस्, m. a kind of fish; [cf.<BR>एरङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलपुर
एलपुर एलपुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालु
एलवालु एलवालु, n. or एलवालुक or एल्ववा-<BR>लुक, अम्, n. the fragrant bark of Feronia Elephantum;<BR>a granular substance, apparently a vegetable of a red-<BR>dish-brown colour (it is used as a drug and perfume).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलविल|एलविलः
एलविल एलविल, अस्, m. an epithet of Ku-<BR>vera. See ऐलविल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एला
एला एला, f. cardamoms, the seed of the<BR>Elettaria Cardamomum or Alpinia Cardamomum, it<BR>applies to both the large and small cardamom, but<BR>more commonly to the former; N. of a river; N. of a<BR>metre consisting of four lines of fifteen syllables each.<BR>—एला-पत्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—एला-पर्णी,<BR>f. the plant Mimosa Octandra.<BR>—एला-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलाक
एलाक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलीका
एलीका, f. small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलाय
एलाय एलाय (less correctly इलाय), nom.<BR>P. एलायति, -यितुम्, to be wantonly mischievous or<BR>wild in behaviour, to be merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलु
एलु एलु, n. a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलुक|एलुकं
एलुक एलुक, N. of a medicinal substance<BR>or plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलूक
एलूक एलूक, अम्, n. probably identical with<BR>एडूक, a wall enclosing bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
एव 1. एव (fr. pronom. base ए, see एतद्,<BR>Zend ऐव), so, just so, exactly so (e. g. य एवेदम्<BR>इति ब्रवत्, who may say ‘it is so;’ in this sense<BR>एव = the more modern word एवम्); like (e. g. त्वम्<BR>एव यन्ता, a driver like you; but examples of एव<BR>in the sense of इव are rare); indeed, truly, really<BR>(often in this sense found in the Veda at the begin-<BR>ning of a verse in conjunction with other particles of<BR>affirmation, especially with इद्, इद् नु कम्, हि, &c., e. g.<BR>एवेन्नु कं ततार, he most certainly crossed; एवा<BR>ह्य् असि वीरयुः, thou art indeed hero-like.<BR>(In its most frequent use of strengthening the idea<BR>expressed by any word, एव, if translateable, must be<BR>variously rendered by such adverbs as) just, exactly, very,<BR>merely, only, even, at the very moment, immediately on,<BR>scarcely, still, already, &c. (e. g. तावतीम् एव रात्रिम्,<BR>just so long a night; एवम् एव, exactly so; तान्<BR>एव, these very persons; नचिराद् एव, in no very<BR>long time; अपः स्पृष्ट्वैव, by merely touching<BR>water; जप्येनैव, by sole repetition; अभुक्त्वैव,<BR>even without having eaten; इति वदन्न् एव, at the<BR>very moment of saying so; नाम्नि कीर्तित एव,<BR>scarcely had the name been mentioned; स जीवन्न्<BR>एव, he while still living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
एव may often be connected with other adverbs<BR>in the sense of ‘also,’ ‘likewise,’ &c., as in the fol-<BR>lowing examples: तथैव, so also; तथैव<BR>च, and so likewise; एव च, and also; चैव, and<BR>also; एव वा, or also; न त्व् एव, but not also.<BR>Grammarians assert that एव cuts off the final of क्व<BR>when it follows that adverb, as क्व्-एव, where pos-<BR>sibly ? i. e. nowhere. Lexicographers affirm that<BR>एव may imply emphasis, affirmation, detraction,<BR>diminution, command, restraint; or be used as an<BR>expletive; [cf. Goth. aiv, Them. aiva; Old Germ.<BR>eo, io; Mod. Germ. je: perhaps also Lat. œvum;<BR>Goth. ibus; Old Germ. ebanêr; Mod. Germ.<BR>ebener, eben.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवथा
एवथा, ind., Ved. indeed, certainly, even; (Sāy.<BR>either fr. rt. 5. इ) assailing the strongholds of enemies,<BR>going to war; (or fr. rt. अव्) protecting, protection,<BR>assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
एव 2. एव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 5. इ), Ved. going,<BR>moving, speedy, quick; (अस्), m. a course, way, (often<BR>in inst. pl., e. g. सनाद् दिवम् परि भुमा स्वेभिर्<BR>एवैर् अक्तोषा चरतः, from all eternity day and<BR>night move round heaven and earth in their accus-<BR>tomed course); earth, world?; (Sāy.) a courser, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-c" target="_blank">Page0186-c+ 78</a>]<BR>fleet horse; (आस्), m. pl. way or manner of acting,<BR>mode of proceeding, custom, usage, habit; (Sāy.)<BR>desire, a hymn which goes or is directed to the<BR>object of praise (e. g. अभि चष्टे सूरो अर्य एवान्,<BR>the sun sees into the conduct of the worshipper; or<BR>according to Sāy. the sun being a lord makes mani-<BR>fest or grants desires). When the inst. c. is used, the<BR>meaning is hardly to be distinguished from that in<BR>the first example (e. g. स्वैर् एवैः, in his usual way<BR>of proceeding; पूर्व्येभिर् एवैः, in the ancient<BR>mode; or according to Sāy. with ancient hymns).<BR>—एव-या, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. going in ways or<BR>courses, i. e. either going quickly or going the usual<BR>way; epithet of Viṣṇu; (Sāy.) granting protection.<BR>—एवया-मरुत्, Ved., (Sāy.) N. of the author of<BR>a Ṛg-veda hymn, but perhaps rather an exclamation<BR>meaning either एव-या, i. e. ‘Viṣṇu (cf. the pre-<BR>ceding word) and the Maruts!’ or ‘moving Maruts.’<BR>—एव-यावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. going quickly, or going<BR>the usual way; epithet of Viṣṇu and of the Maruts;<BR>(Sāy.) going with horses; granting desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्
एवम् एवम्, ind. (cf. 1. एव and एतद्), so,<BR>thus, in this way, in such a manner, such. एवम् is<BR>not found in the oldest hymns of the Veda, where its<BR>place is taken by एव, but occurs in later hymns and<BR>in the Brāhmaṇas, especially in connection with the<BR>rt. विद्, ‘to know,’ and its derivatives (e. g. य एवं<BR>वेद, he who knows so; cf. एवं-विद् below). In<BR>classical Sanskrit एवम् occurs very frequently, espe-<BR>cially in connection with the roots वच्, ‘to speak,’<BR>and श्रु, ‘to hear,’ and refers to what precedes as<BR>well as to what follows (e. g. एवम् उक्त्वा, having so<BR>said; एवमेवैतत्, this is so; एवम् अस्तु or एवम्<BR>भवतु, be it so, I assent; अस्त्य् एवम्, it is so;<BR>यद्य् एवम्, if this be so; किम् एवम्, how so?<BR>what is the meaning of it? what does this refer to?<BR>मैवम्, not so! एवम् — यथा or यथा — एवम्,<BR>so — as). एवम् is often used like an adjective (e. g.<BR>एवं ते वचने रतः, rejoicing in such words of<BR>thine; where एवम् = एवं-विधे). Sometimes<BR>एवम् is merely an expletive. According to lexico-<BR>graphers एवम् may imply likeness (so); sameness<BR>of manner (thus); assent (yes, verily); affirmation<BR>(certainly, indeed, assuredly); command (thus, &c.);<BR>and be used as an expletive.<BR>—एवं-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of such a form or kind.<BR>—एवं-वाद, अस्, m. such<BR>an expression.<BR>—एवं-विद्, त्, त्, त्, or एवं-विद्वस्,<BR>आन्, उषी, अस्, Ved. knowing so or such, well instructed,<BR>familiar with what is right.<BR>—एवं-विध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of such a kind, in such form or manner, such.<BR>—एवं-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, strong in such a manner,<BR>possessing such a power.<BR>—एवं-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>behaving or acting thus, of such a kind.<BR>—एवं-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, behaving thus.<BR>—एवङ्-कारम्, ind.<BR>in this manner.<BR>—एवङ्-काल, अस्, आ, अम्, containing<BR>so many syllabic instants.<BR>—एवङ्-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. thus minded.<BR>—एवङ्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>in such a condition or state, so circumstanced, of such<BR>kind; (ए), ind. under such circumstances.<BR>—एवङ्-<BR>गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing such qualities or such<BR>good qualities.<BR>—एवन्-दुःसह, अस्, आ, अम्, so hard<BR>to bear.<BR>—एवन्-नामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. so called.<BR>—एवम्-अवस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, so situated.<BR>—एवम्-<BR>आदि, इस्, इस्, इ, or एवम्-आद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>such a beginning, of such qualities or kind.<BR>—एवम्-<BR>प्रकार or एवम्-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, of such a kind.<BR>—एवम्-प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of such<BR>power.<BR>—एवम्-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, of such quality,<BR>of such a description, in such a manner, so, such.<BR>—एवम्भूत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with any-<BR>thing similar.<BR>—एवम्-भूमि, इस्, f. such a place,<BR>a place like the one just described.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवार
एवार एवार, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. एव and अरम्?),<BR>Ved. so prepared, ready; (Sāy.) N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवावद|एवावदः
एवावद एवा-वद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. so speak-<BR>ing, true; (अस्), m., (Sāy.) N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्
एष् 1. एष् (आ-इष्), cl. 6. P. एच्छति, ऐषि-<BR>तुम् or -ष्टुम्, to wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्ट
एष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, desired, wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्
एष् 2. एष् (आ-ईष्), cl. 1. P. A., Ved. एषति,<BR>-ते, एषितुम्, to hasten near to or towards; to fly at;<BR>to attack any one; to endeavour to reach or gain; to<BR>desire; to request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टि|एष्टिः
एष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. seeking to go towards, desire,<BR>wish; (Sāy.) wishing; (or fr. rt. यज्) worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्
एष् 3. एष्, cl. 1. P. A. एषति, -ते, एषाञ्-<BR>चकार, एषाञ्-चक्रे, एषितुम्, to creep,<BR>glide; to go or approach: Caus. एषयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to probe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष|एषः
1. एष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. gliding, running; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; (Sāy.) to be desired, desirable;<BR>to be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष|एषः
एष 2. एष. See एतद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष|एषः
एष 3. एष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. इष्), seeking;<BR>(अस्), m. running or hastening towards; (according to<BR>Sāy. एषे is an inf. fr. rt. इ, ‘to go’) seeking; wish,<BR>election; (आ), f. wish.<BR>—एषैष्य (एष-एष्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. to be sought, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषण|एषणः
एषण, अस्, आ, अम्, seeking; (अस्), m. an iron<BR>arrow; (अम्), n. driving, pressing; seeking; probing;<BR>wish, desire; (आ), f. seeking, wish, desire, begging,<BR>solicitation, request; (ई), f. an iron or steel probe; a<BR>goldsmith's balance, assay scales.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणिका
एषणिका, f. a goldsmith's balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणिन्
एषणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, seeking, striving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणीय
एषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired, desirable; to<BR>be aimed at; (at the end of a compound) relating to<BR>medical examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषितृ
एषितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, wishing, desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषिन्
एषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, driving, impelling; (at the end<BR>of compounds) seeking, desiring, desirous of, wishing<BR>(e. g. हितैषिन्, well-wishing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टव्य
एष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sought, desirable,<BR>wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टृ
एष्टृ, टा, ट्री, तृ, seeking, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्य
एष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sought for; to be in-<BR>vestigated or probed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषवीर|एषवीरः
एषवीर एष-वीर, अस्, m. designation of a<BR>despised Brāhmaṇic family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्यत्|एष्यन्त्
एष्यत् एष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत् (fut. part.<BR>fr. rt. 5. इ), what is to come, future.<BR>—एष्यत्कालीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एह
एह एह, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ईह्), Ved. desirous,<BR>wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एहस्
एहस्, अस्, n., Ved. anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एहि
एहि एहि (imperative of rt. 5. इ with आ),<BR>come!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एहिमाय
एहिमाय एहिमाय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., = अहि-<BR>माय, q. v., an epithet of the Viśvedevās; (Sāy.) of<BR>all-pervading intelligence; or these deities may be so<BR>named because they uttered on one occasion the words<BR>‘Come near, do not go away’ (एहि मा यासीः. See<BR>Ṛg-veda 1. 3, 9).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ 1. ऐ, the twelfth vowel of the alphabet,<BR>having the sound of ei in heighth.<BR>—ऐ-कार, अस्, m.<BR>the letter or sound ऐ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ 2. ऐ, ind. (an interjection of calling or<BR>summoning) Hola, Ho, Heigh; (and of remembering)<BR>Aye, Ha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ 3. ऐ, ऐस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकध्य|ऐकध्यं
ऐकध्य ऐकध्य, अम्, n. (fr. एकधा), single-<BR>ness of time or occurrence; (अम् or अतस्), ind. at<BR>once, together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपत्य|ऐकपत्यं
ऐकपत्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-पति), the sovereignty<BR>of one, absolute monarchy; supreme authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपदिक
ऐकपदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एक-पद), belonging<BR>to a simple word; consisting of single words; the N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">Page0187-b+ 78</a>]<BR>given to the Naigama section of Yāska's commentary<BR>on the Nighaṇṭavas, or collection of Vedic words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकपद्य|ऐकपद्यं
ऐकपद्य, अम्, n. unity of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकभाव्य|ऐकभाव्यं
ऐकभाव्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-भाव), singleness<BR>of nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकमत्य|ऐकमत्यं
ऐकमत्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-मति), unanimity,<BR>sameness of doctrine or of opinion, agreement, con-<BR>sent, concurrence, confederation; (अस्, ई, अम्), con-<BR>nected with sameness of opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकराज्य|ऐकराज्यं
ऐकराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-राज्), monarchy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकलव्य
ऐकलव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic fr. एक-लू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशतिक
ऐकशतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एक-शत), provided<BR>with 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशफ
ऐकशफ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एक-शफ), produced<BR>by or belonging to animals with uncloven hoofs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकश्रुत्य|ऐकश्रुत्यं
ऐकश्रुत्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-श्रुति, q. v.), the one<BR>accentless monotonous tone, monotony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकसहस्रिक
ऐकसहस्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एक-सहस्र), pro-<BR>vided with 1001.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकस्वर्य|ऐकस्वर्यं
ऐकस्वर्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-स्वर), oneness of<BR>accent (as in the case of a compound which has only<BR>one accent, though the separate members when un-<BR>compounded are each accented).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकागारिक|ऐकागारिकः
ऐकागारिक, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. एक-आगार), a thief, a<BR>robber breaking into lonely houses; the possessor of<BR>one residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाग्र्य|ऐकाग्र्यं
ऐकाग्र्य, अम्, n. (fr. एकाग्र), intentness on one<BR>object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाङ्ग|ऐकांग|ऐकांगः|ऐकाङ्गः
ऐकाङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. एकाङ्ग), a soldier of the<BR>body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकात्म्य|ऐकात्म्यं
ऐकात्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक-आत्मन्), unity of the<BR>soul, unity of being; oneness with the supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकादशाक्ष
ऐकादशाक्ष, अस्, m. (fr. एकादश + अक्ष), N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकादशिन
ऐकादशिन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एकादशिनी), Ved. be-<BR>longing to a collection or association of eleven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाधिकरण्य|ऐकाधिकरण्यं
ऐकाधिकरण्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक + अधिकरण),<BR>oneness of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्तिक|ऐकांतिक
ऐकान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एकान्त), absolute, com-<BR>plete, perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्यिक|ऐकान्यिकः
ऐकान्यिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एक + अन्य), one who<BR>commits a single error in reading (who makes one<BR>thing another or otherwise than right).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकार्थ्य|ऐकार्थ्यं
ऐकार्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. एकार्थ), oneness of aim<BR>or intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाहिक|ऐकाहिकं
ऐकाहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एकाह), ephemeral,<BR>quotidian, of one day, of the same day; belonging<BR>to a ceremony which lasts one day, belonging to a<BR>simple oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्य|ऐक्यं
ऐक्य, अम्, n. (fr. एक), oneness, unity, single-<BR>ness, identity, harmony, sameness; the identity of<BR>the human soul or of the universe with the Deity;<BR>an aggregate, whole, total; (in alg.) the product of<BR>the length and depth of the portions, or of the little<BR>excavations differing in depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षव|ऐक्षवं
ऐक्षव ऐक्षव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इक्षु), pro-<BR>duced from or relating to the sugar-cane, sugary;<BR>(अम्), n. sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षव्य
ऐक्षव्य, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. produced from or re-<BR>lating to the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुक|ऐक्षुकः
ऐक्षुक, अस्, ई, अम्, suitable for sugar-cane;<BR>bearing sugar-cane; (अस्), m. a carrier of sugar-canes;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of Ikṣukīyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुभारिक
ऐक्षुभारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इक्षु-भार),<BR>carrying a load of sugar-canes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाक|ऐक्ष्वाकः
ऐक्ष्वाक ऐक्ष्वाक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इक्ष्वाकु),<BR>belonging to Ikṣvāku, of the family of Ikṣvāku;<BR>(अस्), m. a descendant of Ikṣvāku; epithet of Puru-<BR>kutsa, and of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाकु|ऐक्ष्वाकुः
ऐक्ष्वाकु, उस्, m. a descendant of Ikṣvāku;<BR>epithet of Triśaṅku, and of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐङ्गुद|ऐंगुद|ऐङ्गुदं
ऐङ्गुद ऐङ्गुद, अस्, ई, अम्, produced from<BR>the Iṅguda plant; (अम्), n. scil. फलम्, the fruit<BR>of the Iṅguda plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐच्छिक
ऐच्छिक ऐच्छिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इच्छा), optional,<BR>voluntary, arbitrary, at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐड|ऐडः
ऐड ऐड, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इडा), Ved. contain-<BR>ing anything refreshing or strengthening; containing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">Page0187-c+ 71</a>]<BR>the word इडा; (अस्), m. the son of Iḍā, epithet of<BR>Purūravas; [cf. ऐल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडक|ऐडकः
ऐडक ऐडक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एडक), produced<BR>from the animal Eḍaka; (अस्), m. a species of sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडविड|ऐडविडः
ऐडविड ऐडविड, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Kuvera; N. of a son of Daśaratha; also ऐडविल;<BR>[cf. ऐलविल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडुक|ऐडुकं
ऐडुक ऐडुक or ऐडूक, अम्, n. a wall &c.<BR>of bones and rubbish. See एडुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐण|ऐणं
ऐण ऐण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एण), produced from<BR>or belonging to the male black antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणिक|ऐणिकः
ऐणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, hunting black antelopes, a<BR>deer-killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणेय|ऐणेयं|ऐणेयः
ऐणेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एणी), produced from the<BR>black doe or female antelope; produced from any-<BR>thing belonging to a black doe or female antelope;<BR>(अस्), m. the black antelope; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐण्डिनेय
ऐण्डिनेय ऐण्डिनेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>Śākhā or branch of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतदात्म्य|ऐतदात्म्यं
ऐतदात्म्य ऐतदात्म्य, अम्, n. (abstr. noun<BR>of एतदात्मन्), the state of having this property<BR>or peculiarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेय|ऐतरेयः
ऐतरेय ऐतरेय, अस्, m. a descendant of Itarā,<BR>to whom the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa and Āraṇyaka were<BR>revealed; (अस्, ई, अम्), originating from Aitareya.<BR>—ऐतरेय-ब्राह्मण or ऐतरेयक, अम्, n. (scil.<BR>ब्राह्मण) title of a Brāhmaṇa attached to the<BR>Ṛg-veda and prescribing the duties of the Hotṛ<BR>priest. It consists of forty Adhyāyas, divided into<BR>eight Pañcikās.<BR>—ऐतरेयोपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f., N. of an Upaniṣad forming part of the Aitareya-<BR>Āraṇyaka.<BR>—ऐतरेयोपनिषद्-भाष्य, अम्, n. a<BR>commentary on the last by Saṅkarācārya.<BR>—ऐतरे-<BR>योपनिषद्भाष्य-टिप्पणी, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary on the last work by Anantānandagiri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयिन्
ऐतरेयिन्, ई, m. a follower of Aitareya, a reader of<BR>the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतश|ऐतशः
ऐतश ऐतश, अस्, m., N. of a Muni of the<BR>family of Aurva (Bhṛgu), author of the Aitaśa-<BR>pralāpa forming part of the Kuntāpa hymns of the<BR>Atharva-veda and used with these hymns in the<BR>ritual belonging to the Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतशायन
ऐतशायन, आस्, m. pl. the descendants of Aitaśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिशायन
ऐतिशायन, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिहासिक|ऐतिहासिकः
ऐतिहासिक ऐतिहासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इति-<BR>हास), derived from ancient legends, legendary,<BR>historical, traditional; (अस्), m. one who relates or<BR>knows ancient legends, an historian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिह्य|ऐतिह्यं
ऐतिह्य ऐतिह्य, अम्, n. (fr. इति-ह; see under<BR>इति, p. 139), traditional instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐदंयुगीन
ऐदंयुगीन ऐदंयुगीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. इदं-<BR>युग), fit for this yoke or team.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐध्
ऐध् ऐध्, f. or ऐध, अस्, m. or ऐधा, f.<BR>(fr. rt. इन्ध् with आ), Ved. flaming, a flame, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन
ऐन ऐन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐनस|ऐनसं
ऐनस ऐनस, अम्, n. (fr. एनस्), sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दव|ऐंदव|ऐन्दवं|ऐन्दवः
ऐन्दव ऐन्दव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इन्दु), lunar,<BR>belonging or relating or similar to the moon; (ई), f.<BR>the plant Serratula Anthelminthica; (अम्), n. the<BR>asterism Mṛgaśiras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्र|ऐंद्र|ऐन्द्रं|ऐन्द्रः
ऐन्द्र ऐन्द्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इन्द्र), belonging<BR>to or sacred to Indra, proceeding from Indra, similar<BR>to Indra; (अस्), m. the part of a sacrifice offered to<BR>Indra; (ई), f. (scil. ऋच्) a verse addressed to Indra;<BR>(scil. दिश्) the east quarter, of which Indra is regent<BR>(e. g. ऐन्द्र्यां दिशि, in the east); the eighteenth<BR>lunar mansion; the eighth day in the second half of<BR>the month Mārgaśīrṣa, and of the month Pauṣa;<BR>Indra's energy, personified as his wife and by some<BR>identified with Durgā; epithet of Durgā; misfortune,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">Page0188-a+ 77</a>]<BR>misery (personified); N. of a plant, a kind of cucum-<BR>ber, Cucumis Madraspatanus; (अम्), n. the eighteenth<BR>lunar mansion (ज्येष्ठा); wild ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रजालिक|ऐंद्रजालिक|ऐन्द्रजालिकः
ऐन्द्रजालिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इन्द्र-जाल), familiar<BR>with or relating to magic, magical, deceptive, illusory;<BR>(अस्), m. a juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रतुरीय|ऐंद्रतुरीयः|ऐन्द्रतुरीयः
ऐन्द्रतुरीय, अस्, ई, अम्, a libation (ग्रह) &c.,<BR>the fourth part of which is offered to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रद्युम्न
ऐन्द्रद्युम्न, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Indra-<BR>dyumna; N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक|ऐंद्रलुप्तिक|ऐन्द्रलुप्तिकः
ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इन्द्र-लुप्त),<BR>afflicted with morbid baldness of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रवायव
ऐन्द्रवायव, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. belonging to Indra<BR>and Vāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रशिर|ऐंद्रशिरः|ऐन्द्रशिरः
ऐन्द्रशिर, अस्, m. a species of elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्राग्न|ऐंद्राग्न
ऐन्द्राग्न, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. sacred to or belonging<BR>to Indra and Agni, proceeding from Indra and Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रानैरृत
ऐन्द्रानैरृत, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Indra<BR>and Nirṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रापौष्ण
ऐन्द्रापौष्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Indra<BR>and Pūṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्राबार्हस्पत्य
ऐन्द्राबार्हस्पत्य, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Indra<BR>and Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रामारुत
ऐन्द्रामारुत, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Indra and<BR>the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रायुध
ऐन्द्रायुध, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Indra's bow<BR>or the rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रावरुण
ऐन्द्रावरुण, अस्, ई, अम्, sacred to Indra and<BR>Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रावैष्णव
ऐन्द्रावैष्णव, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Indra<BR>and Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रासौम्य
ऐन्द्रासौम्य, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Indra<BR>and Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रि|ऐंद्रिः|ऐन्द्रिः
ऐन्द्रि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Jayanta, the son<BR>of Indra; N. of Arjuna; N. of the monkey-king<BR>Bāli; a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रिय|ऐंद्रिय
ऐन्द्रिय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इन्द्रिय and connected<BR>with इन्द्र, q. v.), relating to or belonging to the<BR>senses, sensual; perceptible, perceived, present; (अम्),<BR>n. the world of the senses; a section of the Āyur-<BR>veda treating on the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियक|ऐंद्रियक|ऐन्द्रियकं
ऐन्द्रियक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the senses;<BR>perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियेधी|ऐंद्रियेधी
ऐन्द्रिये-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, thinking only of sensual<BR>pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्धन|ऐंधन|ऐन्धनः
ऐन्धन ऐन्धन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इन्धन),<BR>consisting of fuel; an epithet of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐभावत
ऐभावत ऐभावत, अस्, m. (fr. इभा-वत्), a<BR>patronymic of Pratīdarśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐभी
ऐभी ऐभी, f., N. of a plant; = इभ्या ?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐयत्य|ऐयत्यं
ऐयत्य ऐयत्य, अम्, n. (fr. इयत्), quantity,<BR>number, value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरंमद
ऐरंमद ऐरंमद, अस्, m. (fr. इरंमद),<BR>a patronymic of Deva-muni, author of a Ṛg-veda<BR>hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरंमदीय
ऐरंमदीय, अम्, n., N. of a sea in Brahmā's<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावण|ऐरावणः
ऐरावण ऐरावण, अस्, m. (fr. इरा-वन् =<BR>इरा-वत्, ‘possessed of or proceeding from water’),<BR>N. of a king of the Nāgas; Indra's elephant, pro-<BR>duced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावत|ऐरावतं|ऐरावतः
ऐरावत, अस्, m. a patronymic of a fabulous serpent-<BR>like being called Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; a serpent, one of the<BR>chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent-race, inhabiting the<BR>lower world or Pātāla; N. of the elephant of Indra,<BR>produced at the churning of the ocean, and the pro-<BR>totype of the elephant race, considered also as the<BR>elephant of the east quarter; [cf. नाग, which means<BR>both serpent and elephant]; an excellent elephant;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a kind of rainbow, considered as the<BR>long and unbent bow of Indra; a kind of lightning;<BR>(अस्), m. the orange tree; another tree, Artocarpus<BR>Lacucha; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a vast and waterless<BR>region; (आनि), n. pl., N. of a Varṣa; N. of the<BR>northern path of the moon; the fruit of the tree<BR>Artocarpus Lacucha; (ई), f. the female of Indra's<BR>elephant; lightning; N. of a plant; N. of the Ravi<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">Page0188-b+ 68</a>]<BR>river in the Pañjāb; N. of a particular portion of the<BR>moon's path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरिण|ऐरिणं
ऐरिण ऐरिण, अम्, n. (fr. इरिण), fossil or<BR>rock salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरेय|ऐरेयं
ऐरेय ऐरेय, अम्, n. (fr. इरा), a spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐर्म्य|ऐर्म्यं
ऐर्म्य ऐर्म्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ईर्मा), good for<BR>healing wounds, (a plaster &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐल|ऐलः
ऐल ऐल, अस्, m. (= ऐड), N. of Purūravas<BR>as son of Ilā; (अम्), n. a particular number.<BR>—ऐल-<BR>धान, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलब
ऐलब ऐलब, अस्, m., Ved. noise, roaring,<BR>cry.<BR>—ऐलब-कार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. making a noise,<BR>roaring (epithet of Rudra's dogs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलबृद
ऐलबृद ऐलबृद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bringing<BR>food; (perhaps related to ऐलब.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवालुक|ऐलवालुकः
ऐलवालुक ऐलवालुक, अम्, n. a perfume.<BR>See एलवालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलविल|ऐलविलः
ऐलविल ऐलविल, अस्, m., N. of Kuvera as<BR>son of Ilavilā; (also ऐडविद, ऐडविल, and एल-<BR>विल); N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलूष|ऐलूषः
ऐलूष ऐलूष, अस्, m. (fr. इलूष), a patrony-<BR>mic of Kavasha, the author of two Ṛg-veda hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलेय|ऐलेयं|ऐलेयः
ऐलेय ऐलेय, अम्, n. a perfume; = एलवालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश
ऐश ऐश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ईश), proceeding from<BR>or relating to Śiva; divine, supreme, regal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशान
ऐशान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ईशान), belonging to Śiva;<BR>(ई), f. (scil. दिश्) the quarter of Śiva, the north-east<BR>quarter.<BR>—ऐशान-ज, आस्, m. pl. = ईशान-ज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशिक|ऐशिकः
ऐशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Śiva; divine,<BR>heavenly; royal, regal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर
ऐश्वर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ईश्वर), fit for or belong-<BR>ing to or produced by a master, or by the supreme<BR>lord; mighty, majestic; divine, relating to God;<BR>supreme, royal; belonging to Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वरिक|ऐश्वरिकः
ऐश्वरिक, अस्, m. (with Buddhists) a theist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर्य|ऐश्वर्यं|ऐश्वर्य्य|ऐश्वर्य्यं
ऐश्वर्य, अम्, n. power, might, sway; dominion;<BR>supremacy; superhuman power; the divine faculties<BR>of omnipresence, omnipotence, invisibility, &c. (some-<BR>times their number is given as five, with reference to<BR>the five elements).<BR>—ऐश्वर्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, en-<BR>dowed with superhuman faculties, possessed of super-<BR>natural powers, connected with them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्
ऐषमस् ऐषमस्, ind. (ऐ related to ए or इ<BR>in एतद् or इदम्, and समस् from समा, ‘year’),<BR>during this year, in the present year; [cf. Gr. σῆτες<BR>σήμερον]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्तन|ऐषमस्तनः
ऐषमस्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, or ऐषमस्त्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of or belonging to the present year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषावीर
ऐषावीर ऐषावीर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. एष-वीर ?),<BR>Ved. weak, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषीक
ऐषीक ऐषीक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इषीका), con-<BR>sisting of stalks made of reeds or cane; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people; ऐषीकम् पर्व, a section of the<BR>tenth book or Sauptika-parva of the Mahā-bhārata<BR>(Adhyāya 10-18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषुकारि
ऐषुकारि ऐषुकारि, अयस्, m. pl. (fr. इषु-<BR>कार), N. of a tribe or caste.<BR>—ऐषुकारि-भक्त,<BR>अम्, n. the country inhabited by this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टक|ऐष्टकं
ऐष्टक ऐष्टक, अम्, n. (fr. इष्टका), Ved. the<BR>sacrificial bricks collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिक
ऐष्टिक ऐष्टिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. इष्टि),<BR>sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिकपौर्तिक|ऐष्टिकपौर्त्तिक
ऐष्टिकपौर्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the<BR>Iṣṭāpūrta, ceremonial and meritorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहलौकिक
ऐहलौकिक ऐहलौकिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इह-<BR>लोक), of this world, happening in this world, terres-<BR>trial, sublunary; (opposed to पारलौकिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिक|ऐहिकं
ऐहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. इह), of this place, of this<BR>world, temporal, worldly, secular, local; (opposed to<BR>आमुष्मिक.)<BR>—ऐहिक-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, worldly-<BR>minded, concerned about worldly affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ 1. ओ, the vowel ओ, the thirteenth letter<BR>of the alphabet.<BR>—ओ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or<BR>sound ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ 2. ओ, ind. a vocative particle, Oh; an<BR>interjection of calling, Ho, Holla; of reminiscence,<BR>Ho, Ah; of compassion, Ah, Oh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ 3. ओ, औस्, m. a N. of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ 4. ओ (आ-उ), only occurring in the past pass.<BR>part.<BR>—१. ओत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. invoked, summoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक|ओकं|ओकः
ओक ओक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. उच्), a house; an<BR>asylum, a refuge (see ओकस् below); a bird?; [cf. Lith.<BR>ûkis, ‘a dwelling;’ ûkininkas: Gr. οἶκος belongs<BR>to rt. विश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकस्
ओकस्, अस्, n. gratification, pleasure; place of hap-<BR>piness or pleasure, a resting-place, a home, house;<BR>an asylum, a refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकिवस्
ओकिवस्, आन् (irreg. perf. part. Par. ?), Ved. delighting<BR>in anything; (Sāy.) meeting together, united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्य
ओक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. favourable to the (inmates<BR>of a) house; good for a house, kind to a household;<BR>(अम्), n. gratification, pleasure; a comfortable place;<BR>a resting-place, a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकण|ओकणः
ओकण ओकण, अस्, or ओकणि, इस्, m. a bug.<BR>See ओकोदनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकुल|ओकुलः
ओकुल ओकुल, अस्, m. a cake of flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकोदनी
ओकोदनी ओकोदनी or ओक्कणी, f. a bug.<BR>See ओकण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्ष्
ओक्ष् ओक्ष् (आ-उक्ष्), cl. 1. P. ओक्षति, -षि-<BR>तुम्, to sprinkle over or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओख्
ओख् ओख्, cl. 1. P. ओखति, ओखाञ्-चकार,<BR>ओखितुम्, to be dry or arid; to be able or<BR>competent; to adorn, suffice; to refuse, prevent, ward<BR>off: Caus. ओखयति, -यितुम्: Desid. ओचिखिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओगण
ओगण ओगण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. अव-गण?),<BR>Ved. repudiated by one's companions, solitary, de-<BR>spised; (Sāy.) collected, united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओगीयस्
ओगीयस् ओगीयस् = ओजीयस्, comparative of<BR>उग्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघ|ओघः
ओघ ओघ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वह्), flood,<BR>stream; a torrent, a rapid flow of water, an inunda-<BR>tion; a heap or quantity, flock, multitude, abundance;<BR>the whole; quick time in music; tradition, traditional<BR>advice or instruction; [cf. Gr. ὄχλος?].<BR>—ओघ-रथ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Oghavat and brother of Ogha-<BR>vatī.<BR>—ओघ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a strong stream;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a prince, father-in-law or brother-in-<BR>law of Sudarśana; (ती), f., N. of a daughter of Ogha-<BR>vat; N. of the river Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओङ्कार|ओंकार|ओंकारः|ओङ्कारः
ओङ्कार ओङ्कार. See under ॐ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्
ओज् ओज् (connected with ओजस् below),<BR>cl. 1. 10. P. ओजति, ओजितुम्, or ओजयति,<BR>यितुम्, to be strong or able; to increase, to have<BR>vital power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज ओज, अस्, आ, अम्, odd (as the first, third,<BR>fifth, &c., in a series).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्
ओजस् ओजस्, अस्, n. (fr. उज् = वज्; see उग्र),<BR>bodily strength, vigour, energy, ability; vitality, the<BR>principle of vital warmth and action diffused through-<BR>out the body; virility, the generative faculty; support,<BR>stay; (in rhetoric) a form of style, elaborate style,<BR>abounding with compounds; (in astrology) each<BR>alternate sign of the zodiac (as the first, third,<BR>fifth, &c.); water; light, splendor; metallic lustre;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">Page0189-a+ 74</a>]<BR>manifestation, appearance; ओजसा, with strength,<BR>resolutely, energetically (sometimes used at the be-<BR>ginning of a compound, e. g. ओजसा-कृत, done ener-<BR>getically); [cf. अमितौजस्, उत्तमौजस्, &c.: cf. also<BR>Gr. ὑγιής Zend auṣo; Hib. og, ‘young, juvenile,<BR>fresh;’ oig, ‘a champion;’ oighe, ‘entireness, virginity.’]<BR>—ओजस्-तर, अस्, आ, अम् (comparative), more strong.<BR>—ओजस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or ओजस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, vigorous,<BR>powerful, strong, energetic; splendid, bright.<BR>—ओजस्वि-<BR>ता, f. strength, power.<BR>—ओजो-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>granting power, strengthening, possessed of strength.<BR>—ओज-बला, f. (with Buddhists) N. of a goddess of<BR>Bodhidruma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजसीन
ओजसीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. showing strength, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्य
ओजस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, showing strength, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजाय
ओजाय, nom. A. ओजायते, -यितुम्, to exhibit<BR>strength or energy, to make effort; to be strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजिष्ठ
ओजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (regarded as superlative उग्र,<BR>q. v.), strongest, most vigorous or vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजीयस्
ओजीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (regarded as comparative of<BR>उग्र, q. v.), stronger, more vigorous or vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्मन्
ओज्मन्, आ, m., Ved. strength; (Sāy.) speed; an<BR>instigator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड
ओड ओड, अस्, m., N. of a minister of Pra-<BR>tāpāditya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडक
ओडक ओडक or ओडव, अस्, m. a musical<BR>mode which omits two of the notes of the scale, Ṛ<BR>and Pa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडिका
ओडिका ओडिका or ओडी, f. wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्र|ओड्रः
ओड्र ओड्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people and<BR>country, the northern part of Orissa; (अस्), m. the<BR>China rose.<BR>—ओड्र-पुष्प, अम्, n. Hibiscus Rosa<BR>Sinensis, and its flowers.<BR>—ओड्राख्या (˚र-आख्˚),<BR>f. the China rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओढ
ओढ ओढ, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part. of<BR>आ-वह्, q. v.), brought or carried near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण्
ओण् ओण्, cl. 1. P. ओणति, ओणाञ्-चकार,<BR>ओणितुम्, to remove, take away, drag<BR>along: Caus. ओणयति, -यितुम्, औणिणत्: Desid.<BR>औणिणिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओणि
ओणि ओणि, इस्, m. or f. (generally in du. ई;<BR>said to be fr. preceding rt.), Ved. a vessel used in the<BR>preparation of the Soma juice, and said to consist of<BR>two pieces (?), heaven and earth; preserving power;<BR>protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओत
ओत 1. ओत. See 4. ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओत
ओत 2. ओत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वे with आ),<BR>woven, sewn with the threads across; [cf. प्रोत.]<BR>—ओत-प्रोत, अस्, आ, अम्, sewn crosswise and length-<BR>wise, extending to every quarter?; (अम्), ind. cross-<BR>wise and lengthwise, vertically and horizontally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतु|ओतुः
ओतु, उस्, m. the woof or cross-threads of a web;<BR>(उस्), m. f. a cat, (in this sense said to be fr. rt. अव्.)<BR>In a compound a final अ preceding may optionally be<BR>dropped (e. g. स्थूलोतु or स्थूलौतु, a fat cat.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओत्स
ओत्स ओत्स, अस्, m., N. of an Agrahāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदती
ओदती ओदती, f. (part. of rt. 2. उद्), Ved.<BR>flowing forth, issuing out, rising upwards; epithet of<BR>the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदन|ओदनं|ओदनः
ओदन, अस्, अम्, m. n. grain mashed and cooked<BR>with milk, boiled rice; a cloud; (नी), f. the plant<BR>Sida Cordifolia. When a name is given to a pupil<BR>to indicate his attachment to any particular master,<BR>ओदन may be prefixed to denote that the pupil's<BR>object is rather food than instruction (e. g. ओदन-<BR>पाणिनीयः, a pupil of Pāṇini whose object is only<BR>to be fed by Pāṇini).<BR>—ओदनाह्वया (˚न-आह्˚) or<BR>ओदनाह्वा or ओदनिका, f., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनीय
ओदनीय, nom. P. ओदनीयति, -यितुम्, to wish to<BR>make mashed food of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्म|ओद्मः
ओद्म, अस्, m. or ओद्मन्, अ, n. flowing, flooding;<BR>wetting, moistening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओधस्
ओधस् ओधस्, अस्, n. an udder; = ऊधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओपश|ओपशः
ओपश ओपश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पश् ?), Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">Page0189-b+ 75</a>]<BR>an ornament of the head, lock of hair, curl; tuft of<BR>hair ?; (Sāy.) a horn (fr. उप-शी with आ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओपशिन्
ओपशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. adorned with curls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्
ओम् ॐ, ind. (said to be fr. rt. अव्; perhaps<BR>originally ॐ, which may be derived fr. आं, and this<BR>fr. आ), a word of solemn affirmation and respectful<BR>assent (sometimes translated by yes, verily, so be it,<BR>and in this sense compared with Amen). It is placed<BR>at the commencement of most Hindū works, and as<BR>a sacred exclamation may be uttered (but not so as<BR>to be heard by ears profane) at the beginning and<BR>end of a reading of the Vedas or previously to any<BR>prayer. It is also regarded as a particle of auspicious<BR>salutation (Hail!). ॐ appears first in the Upani-<BR>shads as a mystic monosyllable, and is there set forth<BR>as the object of profound religious meditation, the<BR>highest spiritual efficacy being attributed not only to<BR>the whole word but also to the three sounds अ, उ, म्,<BR>of which it consists. In later times ॐ is the mystic<BR>name for the Hindū triad, and represents the union of<BR>the three gods, viz. अ (Viṣṇu), उ (Śiva), म् (Brahmā).<BR>It may also be typical of the three Vedas. ॐ is<BR>usually called प्रणव, more rarely अक्षरम् or<BR>एकाक्षरम्, and only in later times ॐ-कार.<BR>The Buddhists use ॐ at the commencement of<BR>their विद्या षड्-अक्षरी or mystical formulary in<BR>six syllables (viz. ॐ मानि पद्मे हूं). Lexico-<BR>graphers affirm that besides the above uses, ॐ may<BR>imply command or injunction, removal or warding<BR>off (Away! Hence!), and be used as an inceptive par-<BR>ticle. Grammarians assert that before ॐ a preced-<BR>ing अ or आ at the end of a word should be cut off<BR>(e. g. विजयोङ्कारः for विजयौङ्कारः^1 (˚य-ओङ्˚),<BR>thanksgiving for victory; see Gram. 38. b).<BR>—ॐ-कार,<BR>अस्, m. the sacred and mystical syllable ॐ; the ex-<BR>clamation ॐ; pronouncing the syllable ॐ; (आ), f.<BR>a Buddhist Śakti or female personification of divine<BR>energy.<BR>—ओंकार-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. title of a work<BR>of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—ओंकार-तीर्थ, N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—ओंकार-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 311-315. note: missing underdot final letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम|ओमः
ओम ओम, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अव्, cf. 4. ऊ), Ved.<BR>a protector; any one favourably disposed (towards<BR>another); any one worthy of favour or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमन्
ओमन्, आ, m., Ved. protection, assistance; favour,<BR>kindness; a kind person.<BR>—ओमन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. friendly, agreeable; favourable, kind; satiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमात्रा
ओमात्रा, f., Ved. protection, assistance, kindness,<BR>readiness to help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्या
ओम्या, f., Ved. favour, protection.<BR>—ओम्या-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. friendly, favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमिल
ओमिल ओमिल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओरिमिका
ओरिमिका ओरिमिका, f. title of a section of<BR>the Kāṭhaka Recension of the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओर्णु
ओर्णु ओर्णु (आ-ऊर्णु), cl. 2. P. A. ओर्णोति or<BR>-णौति, -णुते, -णवितुम् or -णुवितुम्, to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल|ओलं|ओलः
ओल ओल or ओल्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, wet, damp;<BR>(अस्), m. an esculent root, Arum Campanulatum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलण्ड्|ओलंड्
ओलण्ड् ओलण्ड्, cl. 10. P. ओलण्डयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cast upwards, throw<BR>up; (various readings have ओलज् and ओल्ज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओशिष्ठहन्
ओशिष्ठहन् ओशिष्ठ-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ (fr. ओशि-<BR>ष्ठ = ओषिष्ठ and हन्), Ved. striking very<BR>quickly; [cf. ओषिष्ठ-दावन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष|ओषं|ओषः
ओष ओष, अस्, m. (fr. 1. उष्), burning,<BR>combustion; [cf. Goth. azgô; Angl. Sax. asca;<BR>Old Germ. asga; Mod. Germ. asche; Eng. ashes.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषण|ओषणः
ओषण, अस्, m. pungency, biting or pungent taste,<BR>sharp flavour; (ई), f. a pot-herb, commonly called Pūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधि|ओषधिः
ओषधि ओषधि, इस्, or ई, f. (a contraction<BR>fr. अवस and धि, ‘containing refreshment or food?;’<BR>according to Pāṇini VI. 3. 132, the form in ई is only<BR>used for the oblique cases in the Veda; but this re-<BR>striction does not seem to be universal), a herb, a plant,<BR>medicinal plant; an annual plant or herb, one that<BR>dies after becoming ripe.<BR>—ओषधि-गर्भ, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">Page0189-c+ 73</a>]<BR>the moon (as containing the herbs in its interior).<BR>—ओषधि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. born or living<BR>among herbs; produced from plants.<BR>—ओषधि-<BR>पति, इस्, m. a physician (master of the medicinal<BR>plants); the moon.<BR>—ओषधि-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a mythic town, the town of Himavat.<BR>—ओषधी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. the moon.<BR>—ओषधी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. connected with herbs.<BR>—ओषधीश (˚धि-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. the moon (presiding over the plants).<BR>—ओष-<BR>धी-संशित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. impelled or influ-<BR>enced by herbs.<BR>—ओषधी-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषम्
ओषम् ओषम्, ind. (fr. rt. 1. उष् ?), Ved.<BR>quickly, immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषिष्ठदावन्
ओषिष्ठ-दावन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. giving very quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठ|ओष्ठः
ओष्ठ ओष्ठ, अस्, m. (contracted fr. अव-<BR>स्थ), the down-hanging lip, i. e. the upper lip (op-<BR>posed to अधर), a lip in general; ओष्ठौ or<BR>द्वाव् ओष्ठौ, du. the lips, the two lips; (ई), f. a<BR>creeper bearing a red flower, to which the lip is com-<BR>monly compared (Coccinia Grandis); [cf. बिम्ब:<BR>cf. also Slav. ûsta, neut. pl.; ûstna, f.: Lat. ostium.]<BR>In compounds a final अ or आ before ओष्ठ may be<BR>optionally dropped (e. g. बिम्ब + ओष्ठ becomes<BR>either बिम्बोष्ठ or बिम्बौष्ठ, ‘red-lipped,’<BR>and the fem. of the comp. adj. may be formed in आ<BR>or ई).<BR>—ओष्ठ-कर्णक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a fabu-<BR>lous race who have their ears and lips very near<BR>each other.<BR>—ओष्ठ-कोप or ओष्ठ-प्रकोप, अस्,<BR>m. a disease of the lips.<BR>—ओष्ठ-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>produced by the lips, labial.<BR>—ओष्ठ-जाह, अम्, n.<BR>the root of the ear.<BR>—ओष्ठ-पल्लव, अम्, n. a lip<BR>or the lips.<BR>—ओष्ठ-पुट, अम्, n. the cavity made<BR>by opening the lips.<BR>—ओष्ठ-पुष्प, अम्, n. the<BR>plant Pentaptera Tomentosa.<BR>—ओष्ठ-रोग, अस्,<BR>m. any morbid affection of the lips.<BR>—ओष्ठाधर<BR>(˚ठ-अध्˚), औ, du. or अम्, n. the upper and lower<BR>lip.<BR>—ओष्ठोपम-फला (˚ठ-उपमा-फ्˚), f. the<BR>creeper Bryonia Grandis, whose flower resembles<BR>a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठक|ओष्ठकः
ओष्ठक (at the end of compounds) = ओष्ठ;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), taking care of the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठ्य
ओष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being at the lips; belonging<BR>to or fit for the lips, labial (as the sounds उ, ऊ, ओ, औ,<BR>प्, फ्, ब्, भ्, म्, व्, and the Upadhmānīya).<BR>—ओष्-<BR>ठ्य-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, produced from labial sounds.<BR>—ओष्ठ्य-स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, pronounced with the<BR>lips, as ओ and औ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ण
ओष्ण ओष्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. आ, implying di-<BR>minution, and उष्ण), a little warm, tepid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओह्
ओह् ओह् (rt. 2. ऊह् with आ), cl. 1. A. ओहते,<BR>हितुम्, to understand, admit, receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओह|ओहः
ओह, अस्, m. (fr. 2. ऊह्), Ved. meditation; (Sāy.)<BR>bringing, performing; reaching.<BR>—ओह-ब्रह्मन्, आ,<BR>m., Ved. really a Brāhman, a Brāhman valued as one;<BR>(Sāy.) one who has sacred knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओहल
ओहल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओहस्
ओहस्, अस्, n., Ved. idea, true notion; (Sāy.) praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओहान
ओहान, अस्, आ, अम्, considering, reflecting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ 1. औ, the fourteenth letter of the<BR>alphabet, having the same sound as ओउ in our.<BR>—औ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound औ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ 2. औ, ind. an interjection of calling,<BR>Ho, Hola; of addressing, Oh; of prohibition and<BR>of asseveration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ 3. औ, औस्, m. sound; an epithet of<BR>Śeṣa or Ananta; (औस्), f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थिक|औक्थिकः
औक्थिक औक्थिक, अस्, m. (fr. उक्थ), a<BR>Brāhman acquainted with the Ukthas, reciting them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थिक्य|औक्थिक्यं
औक्थिक्य, अम्, n. the text of the Ukthas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थ्य
औक्थ्य, अम्, n. a peculiar mode of recitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्ष|औक्षं
औक्ष औक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उक्षन्), Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">Page0190-a+ 68</a>]<BR>relating to an ox, derived from one, &c.<BR>—औक्ष-<BR>गन्धि, इस्, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्षक|औक्षकं
औक्षक, अम्, n. a multitude of oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्ष्ण
औक्ष्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to an ox, derived<BR>from one; (अस्), m. a patronymic from Ukṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औखीय
औखीय औखीय, आस्, m. pl. the followers<BR>of Ukha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औख्य|औख्यं
औख्य औख्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. उखा), boiled<BR>or dressed in a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औग्रसेनि
औग्रसेनि औग्रसेनि, इस्, m. or औग्रसेन्य,<BR>अस्, m. a patronymic fr. उग्र-सेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औग्रसैन्य
औग्रसैन्य, अस्, m. an epithet of Yudhāṃśrau-<BR>ṣṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औग्र्य|औग्र्यं
औग्र्य, अम्, n. (fr. उग्र), horribleness, dread-<BR>fulness, fierceness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औघ|औघः
औघ औघ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वह्), a flood;<BR>[cf. ओघ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औचथ्य
औचथ्य औचथ्य, अस्, m. (fr. उचथ्य), a<BR>patronymic of Dīrgha-tamas of the family of Aṅgiras;<BR>[cf. औतथ्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औचित्य|औचित्यं
औचित्य औचित्य, अम्, n. or औचिती, f. (fr.<BR>उचित), aptness, fitness, propriety, suitableness; taking<BR>pleasure in anything, habituation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औच्चैःश्रवस|औच्चैःश्रवसः
औच्चैःश्रवस औच्चैःश्रवस, अस्, m. (fr. उच्-<BR>चैः-श्रवस्), N. of Indra's horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औजस|औजसं
औजस औजस, अम्, n. (fr. ओजस्), gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औजसिक|औजसिकः
औजसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, energetic, vigorous, acting<BR>with strength or energy; (अस्), m. a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औजस्य
औजस्य, conducive to vitality or energy; (अम्), n.<BR>freshness or vigour of life, energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औज्जिहायनक
औज्जिहायनक औज्जिहायनक, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a grammatical school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औज्ज्वल्य|औज्ज्वल्यं
औज्ज्वल्य औज्ज्वल्य, अम्, n. (fr. उज्-ज्वल),<BR>brightness, brilliancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडवि
औडवि औडवि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-<BR>tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडवीय
औडवीय, अस्, m. a prince of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुपिक|औडुपिकः
औडुपिक औडुपिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उडुप),<BR>crossing in a boat; (अस्), m. a passenger, one going<BR>in a raft or boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुम्बर|औडुंबर|औडुम्बरं|औडुम्बरः
औडुम्बर औडुम्बर. See औदुम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुलोमि|औडुलोमिः
औडुलोमि औडुलोमि, इस्, m. (fr. उडुलोमन्),<BR>N. of a philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औड्र|औड्रः
औड्र औड्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people and<BR>the country inhabited by them. See ओड्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औतङ्क
औतङ्क औतङ्क, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to<BR>Utan.ka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औतथ्य
औतथ्य औतथ्य, अस्, m. (fr. उतथ), an<BR>epithet of Dīrgha-tamas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्कण्ठ्य|औत्कंठ्यं
औत्कण्ठ्य औत्कण्ठ्य, अम्, n. (fr. उत्कण्ठ),<BR>desire, longing for.<BR>—औत्कण्ठ्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>desirous, longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्कर्ष्य|औत्कर्ष्यं
औत्कर्ष्य औत्कर्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. उत्-कर्ष),<BR>excellence, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तमि|औत्तमिः
औत्तमि औत्तमि, इस्, m. (fr. उत्तम), epithet<BR>of the third Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तमिक
औत्तमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the gods who<BR>are in the highest place (in the sky).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तर
औत्तर औत्तर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. उत्तर),<BR>living in the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तरपथिक
औत्तरपथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्तर-पथ),<BR>going or coming in a northerly direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तरपदिक
औत्तरपदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्तर-पद),<BR>comprehending the last word or term (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तरवेदिक
औत्तरवेदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the Ut-<BR>tara-vedi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तराधर्य|औत्तराधर्य्य
औत्तराधर्य, अम्, n. (fr. उत्तराधर), state<BR>of being below and above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तराह
औत्तराह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्तराक), of or belong-<BR>ing to the following day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तरेय|औत्तरेयः
औत्तरेय, अस्, m., N. of a son of Uttarā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तानपाद|औत्तानपादः
औत्तानपाद औत्तानपाद, अस्, and औत्तान-<BR>पादि, इस्, m. (fr. उत्तान-पाद), a N. of Dhruva; (in<BR>mythology) the son of Uttāna-pāda, and grandson of<BR>the first Manu; (in astronomy) the polar star or the<BR>north pole itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पत्तिक
औत्पत्तिक औत्पत्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्-पत्ति),<BR>inborn, innate; natural; produced at the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पात
औत्पात औत्पात, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्-पात),<BR>treating of portents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पातिक
औत्पातिक, अस्, ई, अम्, portentous, prodigious, as-<BR>tounding, calamitous; (अम्), n. a portent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पाद
औत्पाद औत्पाद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्-पाद),<BR>relating to or treating of birth or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पुटिक
औत्पुटिक औत्पुटिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्पुट),<BR>receiving anything with the mouth or beak turned<BR>upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्र
औत्र औत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (for औत्तर?), gross,<BR>rough, inexact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्स
औत्स औत्स, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्स), born or<BR>produced in a well or fountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सङ्गिक|औत्संगिक
औत्सङ्गिक औत्सङ्गिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्-<BR>सङ्ग), carried or placed upon the hip or flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सर्गिक|औत्सर्गिकः
औत्सर्गिक औत्सर्गिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उत्-<BR>सर्ग), that which is abandoned (उत्सृज्यते) or<BR>liable to be abolished in exceptional cases, but valid<BR>generally (as a rule of grammar); general as opposed<BR>to special, not particular, not restricted, abandoning,<BR>omitting, leaving; terminating, completing, relating<BR>or belonging to a final ceremony by which a rite is<BR>dismissed; natural, inherent; produced directly and<BR>naturally; derivative.<BR>—औत्सर्गिक-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>generality of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सुक्य|औत्सुक्यं
औत्सुक्य औत्सुक्य, अम्, n. (fr. उत्सुक),<BR>anxiety, disquietude, uneasiness, regret; ardent desire,<BR>longing, eagerness, zeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदक
औदक औदक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उदक), aquatic,<BR>watery, of or belonging to water.<BR>—औदक-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced by aquatic plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदकि
औदकि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदकीय
औदकीय, अस्, m. a prince of this warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदङ्कि
औदङ्कि औदङ्कि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदङ्कीय
औदङ्कीय, अस्, m. a prince of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदञ्चन|औदंचन
औदञ्चन औदञ्चन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उद्-<BR>अञ्चन), contained in a pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदनिक|औदनिकः
औदनिक औदनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ओदन),<BR>one who knows how to cook mashed grain &c., a<BR>cook; one to whom mashed grain is given at regular<BR>times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदन्य
औदन्य, अस्, m. a patronymic of Muṇḍibha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदपान
औदपान औदपान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उद-पान),<BR>raised from wells or drinking fountains (as a tax);<BR>coming from the village Udapāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदमेघीय
औदमेघीय औदमेघीय, अस्, ई, अम्, belong-<BR>ing to Audameghi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदयक
औदयक औदयक, आस्, m. pl. (fr. उद्-अय),<BR>a school of astronomers who reckoned the first motion<BR>of the planets from sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदरिक|औदरिकः
औदरिक औदरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उदर),<BR>greedily voracious, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदर्य|औदर्यः|औदर्य्य
औदर्य, being in the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदल
औदल औदल, a patronymic from Udala;<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदवापि
औदवापि औदवापि, a patronymic from<BR>Uda-vāpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदवापीय
औदवापीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Audavāpi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदवाहि
औदवाहि औदवाहि, a patronymic from<BR>Uda-vāha; N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदश्वित|औदश्वितं
औदश्वित औदश्वित or औदश्वित्क, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. उद-श्वित्), made of buttermilk; (अम्), n. butter-<BR>milk with an equal proportion of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदस्थान
औदस्थान औदस्थान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उद-<BR>स्थान), accustomed to stand in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदात्त्य
औदात्त्य औदात्त्य, अम्, n. (fr. उदात्त), the<BR>state of having the high tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदारिक|औदारिकं
औदारिक औदारिक, (with Jainas) the gross<BR>body which invests the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदार्य|औदार्यं|औदार्य्य|औदार्य्यं
