औरस्क, अस्, ई, अम्, excellent, distinguished; [cf.<BR>उरस्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरस्य|औरस्यः
औरस्य (?), belonging to or being in the breast;<BR>legitimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरस|औरसः
औरस 2. औरस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उरशा or<BR>उरसा), coming from Urasā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरुक्षयस
औरुक्षयस औरुक्षयस, a patronymic<BR>from Uru-kṣayas = Uru-kṣaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ण|और्ण्ण
और्ण और्ण or और्णक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ऊर्णा),<BR>made of wool, woollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्णनाभ
और्णनाभ, a patronymic from Ūrṇa-nābha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्णनाभक
और्णनाभक, अस्, ई, अम्, inhabited by the tribe<BR>of the Ūrṇa-nābhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्णवाभ
और्णवाभ, a patronymic of Ūrṇa-vābhi; N. of<BR>a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्णिक|और्ण्णिक
और्णिक, अस्, ई, अम्, woollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ध्वकालिक
और्ध्वकालिक और्ध्वकालिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्<BR>(fr. ऊर्ध्व-काल), relating to subsequent or later<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ध्वदेह|और्ध्वदेहं
और्ध्वदेह, अम्, n. (fr. ऊर्ध्व + देह), a<BR>funeral ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ध्वदेहिक|और्द्ध्वदेहिकं
और्ध्वदेहिक, अस्, आ, अम्, referring to the state<BR>after death, relating to a deceased person, any rite<BR>performed in honour of the dead; funereal, funeral;<BR>(अम्), n. the obsequies of a deceased person; funeral<BR>solemnities; whatever is given or performed on a<BR>person's decease, as burning of the body, offering<BR>cakes, distributing alms, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ध्वदैहिक
और्ध्वदैहिक, अस्, ई, अम्, funereal, funeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ध्वसद्मन
और्ध्वसद्मन, अम्, n. (fr. ऊर्ध्व + सद्मन्),<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ध्वस्रोतसिक|और्ध्वस्रोतसिकः
और्ध्वस्रोतसिक or और्ध्वश्रोतसिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. ऊर्ध्व-स्रोतस्, a N. of Śiva, ‘above whom<BR>or in whose head is the river or the Ganges’), a Śaiva<BR>or adherent of the sect which gives Śiva the pre-<BR>eminence in the Hindū triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व|और्वः|और्व्व|और्व्वं|और्व्वः
और्व और्व, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. उर्व),<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi, a son of Ūrva and descendant of<BR>Bhṛgu, mentioned in Ṛg-veda VIII. 102, 4. (This<BR>Aurva, who is called Bhārgava and described in Ma-<BR>hā-bh. 1. 2610. as a son of Cyavana by his wife<BR>Āruṣī and therefore grandson of Bhṛgu, is the sub-<BR>ject of a legend told in Mahā-bh. 1. 6802. There<BR>it is said that the sons of Kṛtavīrya, wishing to destroy<BR>the descendants of Bhṛgu in order to recover the<BR>wealth left them by their father, slew even the children<BR>in the womb. One of the women of the family of<BR>Bhṛgu, in order to preserve her embryo, secreted it<BR>in her thigh (ऊरु), whence the child at its birth was<BR>named Aurva; on beholding whom, the sons of<BR>Kṛtavīrya were struck with blindness, and from whose<BR>wrath proceeded a flame that threatened to destroy<BR>the world, had not Aurva at the persuasion of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">Page0192-b+ 73</a>]<BR>Bhārgavas cast it into the ocean, where it remained<BR>concealed, and having the face of a horse. Aurva<BR>was afterwards preceptor to Sagara and gave him the<BR>Āgneyāstram, with which he conquered the barba-<BR>rians who invaded his possessions; cf. बडवा-मुख,<BR>बडवाग्नि); a N. of a son of Vasiṣṭha; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), produced by Aurva, relating to Aurva; (अस्),<BR>m. submarine fire; (अम्), n. fossil salt.<BR>—और्वानल<BR>(˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्वश
और्वश और्वश, अस्, ई, अम्, an Adhyāya or<BR>Anuvāka containing the word Urvaśī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्वशेय|और्वशेयः|और्व्वशेय|और्व्वशेयः
और्वशेय, अस्, m. an epithet of Agastya, the son<BR>of Urvaśī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलपि
औलपि औलपि, अयस्, m. pl. (a patronymic<BR>fr. उलप), N. of a warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलपिन्
औलपिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलपीय
औलपीय, अस्, m. a prince of the Aulapis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलान|औलानं
औलान औलान, Ved. a reservoir for water (?),<BR>a sacrificial oblation (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक|औलूकं
औलूक औलूक, अम्, n. (fr. उलूक), a number<BR>of owls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक्य|औलूक्यः
औलूक्य, a patronymic from Ulūka; (अस्), m. a<BR>follower of the Vaiśeṣika doctrine; (‘like an owl;’<BR>this etymology, and perhaps the epithet itself, owes<BR>its origin to controversial animosity.)<BR>—औलूक्य-<BR>दर्शन, अम्, n., N. of the system of these philo-<BR>sophers treated of in the Sarvadarśana-saṅgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूखल
औलूखल औलूखल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उलूखल),<BR>coming from a mortar; ground or pounded in a<BR>mortar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औल्वण्य
औल्वण्य औल्वण्य, अम्, n. excess, super-<BR>abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औवेणक
औवेणक औवेणक, अम्, n., N. of a song<BR>(Gītaka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशन
औशन औशन or औशनस, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>originating from Uśanas, peculiar to him; (अस्, ई), m.<BR>f. a patronymic from Uśanas; (अम्), n. (scil. शास्त्र)<BR>the law-book of Uśanas; N. of an Upa-purāṇa; N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशिज
औशिज औशिज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उशिज्), Ved.<BR>desirous zealous, wishing; a patronymic of Kakṣīvat<BR>and others; (अस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीनर|औशीनरः
औशीनर औशीनर, अस्, ई, m. f. a prince of<BR>the Uśīnaras; (ई), f. the wife of Purūravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औसीनरि
औसीनरि, इस्, m. a prince of the Uśīnaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीर|औशीरं|औशीरः
औशीर औशीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (‘made of<BR>Uśīra’), the stick which serves as a handle to the<BR>cow's tail used as a fan or chowri; the cow's tail<BR>used as a fan, the chowri; (अम्), n. a bed, used also<BR>as a seat; a seat, a chair or stool; the root of a fra-<BR>grant grass, Andropogon Muricatum; an unguent,<BR>made of Uśīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीरिका
औशीरिका, f. the shoot (of a plant); a basin, a<BR>bowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषण|औषणं
औषण औषण, अम्, n. (fr. उषण), pun-<BR>gency; black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषदश्वि
औषदश्वि औषदश्वि, इस्, m. (fr. ओषदश्व),<BR>a patronymic of Vasumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषध|औषधं
औषध औषध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ओषधि),<BR>consisting of herbs; (अम्), n. a herb, herbs collec-<BR>tively; herbs used in medicine, a medicament, a drug,<BR>a medicine in general; a vessel for herbs; a mineral.<BR>—औषधावली (˚ध-आव्˚), f. a medical work com-<BR>posed by Prāṇakṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधि|औषधिः
औषधि, इस् or ई, f. a herb, a plant, a medicinal<BR>herb, an annual or deciduous plant, as grass &c.; a<BR>plant in general, = ओषधि, q. v.; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>goddess.<BR>—औषधी-पति, इस्, m. an epithet of the<BR>Soma, lord of the plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीकृ
औषधी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to reduce to a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीय
औषधीय, अस्, ई, अम्, medicinal, consisting of<BR>herbs, herby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषर|औषरं
औषर औषर or औषरक, अम्, n. (fr.<BR>ऊषर), fossil salt; iron stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस
औषस औषस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उषस्), relat-<BR>ing to dawn, early, matutinal; (ई), f. day-break;<BR>morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस्य
औषस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, sacred to Uṣas or the<BR>dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषिक
औषिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. उषा), walking out at<BR>day-break; early, matutinal, &c., with the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषिज
औषिज औषिज or औषीज, desirous &c.;<BR>= औशिज above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्र
औष्ट्र औष्ट्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उष्ट्र), derived<BR>from or relating to a camel; abounding in camels;<BR>(अम्), n. the camel genus or species, camel-nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रक|औष्ट्रकं
औष्ट्रक, अस्, ई, अम्, coming or derived from a<BR>camel; (अम्), n. a herd or multitude of camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्ररथ
औष्ट्ररथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. उष्ट्र-रथ), be-<BR>longing to a carriage drawn by camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्राक्षि
औष्ट्राक्षि, इस्, m. (fr. उष्ट्र + अक्ष), epithet<BR>of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रिक|औष्ट्रिकः
औष्ट्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from or relating to<BR>a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ
औष्ठ औष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ओष्ठ), lip-<BR>shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्णिह
औष्णिह औष्णिह, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. in the<BR>Uṣṇih metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्णीक
औष्णीक औष्णीक, perhaps a wrong reading<BR>for औष्णीष, = उष्णीषिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ण्य|औष्ण्यं
औष्ण्य औष्ण्य, अम्, n. (fr. उष्ण) or औष्-<BR>म्य, अम्, n. (fr. उष्मन्), heat, warmth; burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क 1. क, the first consonant of the alphabet,<BR>and the first of the guttural letters, corresponding in<BR>sound to क् in keep or किन्ग्.<BR>—क-कार, अस्, m. the<BR>letter or sound क.<BR>—ककार-वर्ग, अस्, m. the<BR>guttural consonants collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क 2. क, कस्, का, किम्, interrog. pron. (see<BR>किम् and 2. कद्, and cf. the following words in which<BR>the interrogative base क appears, कतम, कतर,<BR>कति, कथम्, कदा, कर्हि, का, &c.), who? which?<BR>what? In its declension क follows the pronoun तद्<BR>(Gram. 223) except in nom. acc. sing. neut., where<BR>किम् has taken the place of कद् or कत् in classical<BR>Sanskrit; but the old form कद् is found in the Veda.<BR>The interrogative sentence introduced by क is often<BR>terminated by इति (e. g. कस्य स पुत्र इति कथ्-<BR>यताम्, let it be said, ‘whose son is he?’), but इति<BR>may be omitted and the sentence lose its direct<BR>interrogative character (e. g. कस्य स पुत्रो न<BR>ज्ञायते, it is not known whose son he is). क with<BR>or without अस्, ‘to be,’ may express ‘how is it possible<BR>that?’ ‘what power have I, you, they, &c.?’ (e. g.<BR>के मम धन्विनो ऽन्ये, what can the other archers<BR>do against me? के आवाम् परित्रातुम्, what power<BR>have we to rescue you?). क is often connected<BR>with a demonstrative pron. (e. g. को ऽयम् आयाति, who<BR>comes here?) or with the potential (e. g. को हरिं<BR>निन्देत्, who will blame Hari?). क is sometimes<BR>repeated (e. g. कः को ऽत्र, who is there? कान् कान्,<BR>whom? whom? i. e. which of them? cf. Gram. 53. a),<BR>and the repetition is often due to a kind of attrac-<BR>tion (e. g. केषां किं शास्त्रम् अध्ययनीयम्,<BR>which book is to be read by whom? Gram. 836. a).<BR>When किम् is connected with the inst. c. of a noun<BR>or with the indecl. participle it may express ‘what is<BR>gained by doing so, &c.?’ (e. g. नीरुजः किम् औ-<BR>षधैः, what is the use of medicine to the healthy?<BR>किं विलम्बेन, what is gained by delay? किम् ब-<BR>हुना, what is the use of more words? किम् पौरु-<BR>षं हत्वा सुप्तम्, what manliness is there in<BR>killing one asleep ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क is often followed by the particles इव, उ, नाम,<BR>नु, वा, स्विद्, some of which serve merely to gene-<BR>ralize the interrogation (e. g. किम् इव एतद्, what<BR>can this be? क उ श्रवत्, who can possibly hear?<BR>को नाम जानाति, who indeed knows? को न्व् अयम्,<BR>who is this? किं नु कार्यम्, what is to be done?<BR>को वा देवाद् अन्यः, who possibly other than a god?<BR>कस्य स्विद् हृदयं नास्ति, of what person is there<BR>no heart ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क is occasionally used alone as an indefinite pro-<BR>noun, especially in negative sentences (e. g. न कस्य<BR>को वल्लभः, no one is a favourite of any one;<BR>नान्यो जानाति कः, no one else knows; कथं स<BR>घातयति कम्, how does he kill any one? More<BR>usually, however, क is only made indefinite when con-<BR>nected with the particles च, चन, चिद्, वा, and अपि,<BR>in which case क may sometimes be preceded by the<BR>relative य (e. g. ये के च, any persons whatsoever;<BR>यस्यै कस्यै च देवतायै, to any deity whatso-<BR>ever; यानि कानि च मित्राणि, any friends whatsoever;<BR>यत् किञ्च, whatever). The particle चन, being<BR>composed of च and न, properly gives a negative<BR>force to the pronoun (e. g. यस्माद् इन्द्राद् ऋते<BR>किञ्चन, without which Indra there is nothing), but<BR>the negative sense is generally dropped (e. g. कश्चन,<BR>any one; न कश्चन, no one), and a relative is<BR>sometimes connected with it (e. g. यत् किञ्चन,<BR>anything whatsoever). Examles of चिद् with the<BR>interrogative are common; वा and अपि are not so<BR>common, but the latter is often found in classical<BR>Sanskrit (e. g. कश्चिद्, any one; केचिद्, some; न<BR>कश्चिद्, no one; न किञ्चिद् अपि, nothing whatso-<BR>ever; यः कश्चिद्, any one whatsoever; केचित् —<BR>केचित्, some — others; यस्मिन् कस्मिन् वा देशे, in<BR>any country whatsoever; न को ऽपि, no one; न<BR>किमपि, nothing whatever).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क may sometimes be used, like 2. कद्, at the<BR>beginning of a compound. See क-पूय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क 3. क, अस्, m. the Who? the Inexplicable,<BR>the Unknown. By a forced and erroneous interpreta-<BR>tion of the interrogative pronoun occurring in a hymn<BR>of the Ṛg-veda (X. 121. कस्मै देवाय हविषा<BR>विधेम, what god shall we worship with oblations?)<BR>the word क is applied as a name to any chief god<BR>or object of worship, as Prajāpati, Brahmā, Viṣṇu;<BR>air or wind; the sun; the mind; the soul; Yama;<BR>Kāma-deva, the god of love; fire; a peacock; a N. of<BR>Dakṣa (a clever or dexterous man?); a knot, joint;<BR>the king of the birds; a prince in general; the body;<BR>time; wealth, property; sound; light, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क 4. क, अम्, n. (also regarded as ind.),<BR>happiness, joy, pleasure; water; the head, hair; a<BR>head of hair. (Perhaps this word has arisen from a<BR>far-fetched etymology of the word नाक, ‘pleasure,’<BR>i. e. न-अ-क, ‘not-not-pleasure.’)<BR>—क-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced in or by water, watery, aquatic; (अम्),<BR>n. a lotus.<BR>—क-द, अस्, m. ‘giving water,’ a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम्, ind. See 1. कम्, s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क 5. क, a Taddhita affix much used in<BR>forming adjectives. It may also be added to nouns<BR>to express diminution, deterioration, or similarity<BR>(e. g. पुत्रक, a little son; अश्वक, a bad horse or<BR>like a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्य
कंय्य कंय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, or कंय्यु, उस्, उस्, उ<BR>(fr. 1. कम्), happy, prosperous; according to other<BR>authorities also written कंय or कंयु or कंव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंवूल
कंवूल कंवूल or कवूल, अम्, n., N. of<BR>the eighth Yoga, = Arabic قبول<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंश|कंशः
कंश कंश, अस्, अम्, m. n. = कंस, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस्
कंस् कंस्, cl. 2. A. कंस्ते, -सितुम्, to go;<BR>to command; to destroy. See कस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस|कंसं|कंसः
कंस कंस, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>2. कम्; according to others fr. the last), a vessel<BR>made of metal, a drinking vessel, a cup, a goblet (a<BR>noun ending in अस् followed by कंस in a compound<BR>does not change its final, e. g. अयस्-कंस, पयस्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">Page0193-b+ 75</a>]<BR>कंस, &c.); a particular measure; a metal, tutanag<BR>or white copper, brass, bell-metal; cf. कंसास्थि and<BR>कांस्य; (अस्), m., N. of a king of Mathurā, son of<BR>Ugra-sena and cousin of the Devakī who was mother<BR>of Kṛṣṇa, (Ugra-sena being brother of Devaka, who<BR>was father of Devakī.) He is usually called the uncle,<BR>but was really a cousin of Kṛṣṇa, and became his<BR>implacable enemy because it had been prophesied to<BR>him that he would be killed by a child of Devakī<BR>(Vish. Pur. p. 493); as the foe of the deity he is<BR>identified with the Asura Kālanemi; and, as he was<BR>ultimately slain by Kṛṣṇa, the latter receives epithets<BR>like कंस-जित्, the conqueror of Kaṃsa, &c.; (आ), f.<BR>N. of a daughter of Ugra-sena and sister of Kaṃsa.<BR>—कंस-कार, अस्, ई, m. f. a worker in pewter or<BR>white brass, a bell-founder, considered as an inter-<BR>mediate caste.<BR>—कंस-जित्, त्, m. an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa, the conqueror of Kaṃsa.<BR>—कंस-बणिज्, क्,<BR>m. a brazier or seller of brass vessels.<BR>—कंस-<BR>बध, अस्, m. the slaying of Kṛṣṇa; title of a<BR>comedy of Śeṣa-Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कंस-माक्षिक, अम्,<BR>n. a metallic substance in large grains, a sort of<BR>pyrites.<BR>—कंस-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a particular sacrifice.<BR>—कंस-वती, f., N. of a daughter of Ugra-sena and<BR>sister of Kaṃsa and Kaṃsā.<BR>—कंस-हन्, आ, m. an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa, the destroyer of Kaṃsa.<BR>—कंस-<BR>हनन, अम्, n. the slaying of Kaṃsa.<BR>—कंसाराति<BR>(˚स-अर्˚), इस्, or कंसारि (˚स-अरि), इस्, m. epithet<BR>of Kṛṣṇa, the enemy of Kaṃsa.<BR>—कंसास्थि (˚स-<BR>अस्˚), इ, n. tutanag, white copper, any alloy of tin and<BR>copper.<BR>—कंसोद्भवा (˚स-उद्˚), f. a fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसक|कंसकं
कंसक, अम्, n. a mineral substance, a salt of<BR>iron used as an application to the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसिक
कंसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, made of bell-metal &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीय
कंसीय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for or relating to a cup;<BR>(अम्), n. bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसार|कंसारं
कंसार कं-सार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (rice) the<BR>grain of which hardens in the centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्
कक् कक्, cl. 1. A. ककते, चकके, ककि-<BR>तुम्, to be unsteady; to be proud; to be<BR>thirsty; [cf. Lat. vacillo for qvacillo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककजाकृत
ककजाकृत ककजा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>mutilated, torn to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककन्द|ककंदः|ककन्दः
ककन्द ककन्द, अस्, m. gold; N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककर|ककरः
ककर ककर, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककर्दु|ककर्दुः|ककर्द्दु
ककर्दु ककर्दु, उस्, m. (?), Ved. destruction<BR>of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककाटिका
ककाटिका ककाटिका, f., Ved. a part of the<BR>back of the human head, (enumerated together with<BR>मस्तिष्क, ललाट, and कपाल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुञ्जल|ककुंजल|ककुंजलः|ककुञ्जलः
ककुञ्जल ककुञ्जल, अस्, m. the bird Cātaka;<BR>[cf. कपिञ्जल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुत्सल
ककुत्सल ककुत्सल, अस्, m., Ved. an ex-<BR>pression of endearment applied to a child (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद् ककुद्, त्, f. a peak or summit (cul-<BR>men); chief, head; any projecting corner; the hump<BR>on the shoulders of the Indian bull; a horn; an en-<BR>sign or symbol of royalty, as, the white parasol &c.;<BR>N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma.<BR>(According to native grammarians ककुद् is the form<BR>which must be substituted for ककुद at the end of<BR>compounds, e. g. त्रि-ककुद्, three-peaked.)<BR>—ककुत्-<BR>स्थ, अस्, m., N. of a grandson of Ikṣvāku and son<BR>of Śaśāda, said to be so called because in a battle he<BR>stood on the hump of Indra, who had been changed<BR>into a bull; according to the Rāmāyaṇa he is a son<BR>of Bhagīratha.<BR>—ककुद्-मत् or ककुन्-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, running high (as a wave); furnished with a<BR>hump; (आन्), m. a mountain; a buffalo with a hump<BR>on his shoulders; N. of a medicinal plant; (ती), f. the<BR>hip and loins; N. of a metre; [cf. Lat. cacûmen<BR>and culmen for caculmen.]<BR>—ककुद्मि-कन्या, f.<BR>a river (‘mountain-daughter’).<BR>—ककुद्-मिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, peaked, humped; (मी), m. a mountain; a buffalo<BR>with a hump on his shoulders; an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">Page0193-c+ 74</a>]<BR>N. of a prince of the Ānartas; (इनी), f., N. of a river.<BR>—ककुद्रुम, अस्, m. (for ककुद्-द्रुम ?), N.<BR>of a jackal in the Pañcatantra.<BR>—ककुद्-वत्, आन्, m.<BR>a buffalo with a hump on his shoulders; (ती), f., N.<BR>of the wife of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद|ककुदं|ककुदः
ककुद, अस्, अम्, m. n. the summit of a moun-<BR>tain; chief, pre-eminent; the hump on the shoulders<BR>of the Indian bull; a species of serpent; an ensign<BR>or symbol of royalty, as the white parasol, &c.<BR>—ककुद-कात्यायन, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman<BR>who was a violent adversary of Śākya-muni.<BR>—क-<BR>कुदाक्ष (˚द-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुन्दर|ककुंदर|ककुंदरं|ककुन्दरं
ककुन्दर ककुन्दर, अम्, n. the cavities of<BR>the loins; (ककुद्मती-दर?; cf. ककुद्मती and<BR>कुकुन्दर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ् ककुभ्, प्, f. (connected with ककुद्),<BR>a peak or summit (cacumen); space, region or quarter,<BR>as east, west, &c.; N. of a metre of three Pādas con-<BR>sisting of eight, twelve, and eight syllables respectively,<BR>so called because the second Pāda exceeds the others<BR>by four syllables; unornamented hair or the hair<BR>hanging down as a tail; a wreath of Campaka<BR>flowers; splendor, beauty; a Śāstra or sacred treatise;<BR>a Rāgiṇī or personified mode of music; the personi-<BR>fied quarter of the sky; a daughter of Dakṣa and<BR>wife of Dharma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. excelling, distinguished;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of goblin or evil spirit; the tree<BR>Terminalia Arjuna; a part of a lute called the belly,<BR>a wooden vessel covered with leather placed under its<BR>neck to render the sound deeper, or a crooked piece<BR>of wood at the end of the lute; one of the Rāgas or<BR>personified musical modes; N. of a man; N. of a<BR>mountain; (आ), f. space, region, quarter; one of the<BR>Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR>—ककु-<BR>भादनी (˚भा-अद्˚), f. ‘food of the sky,’ a kind of<BR>fragrance or perfume; [cf. नली. ]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुह|ककुहः
ककुह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. eminent, excelling others,<BR>excellent; (अस्), m., Ved. a part of a carriage, perhaps<BR>the seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककेरुक|ककेरुकः
ककेरुक ककेरुक, अस्, m. a worm in the<BR>stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क्
कक्क् कक्क्, a various reading for कख्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कट|कक्कटः
कक्कट कक्कट, अस्, m., Ved. a species of<BR>animal, perhaps a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कुल|कक्कुलः
कक्कुल कक्कुल, अस्, m., N. of a Bhikṣu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोल|कक्कोलः
कक्कोल कक्कोल, अस्, m., N. of a plant bear-<BR>ing a berry, the inner part of which is a waxy and<BR>aromatic substance; (अम्), n. or कक्कोलक, अम्, n.<BR>a perfume prepared from the berries of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क्वल्ल
कक्क्वल्ल कक्क्वल्ल, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Guṇacandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख्
कक्ख् कक्ख्, a various reading for कख्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट कक्खट, अस्, आ, अम्, hard, solid;<BR>(ई), f. chalk.<BR>—कक्खट-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Corchorus Olitorius; (rope is made from its<BR>fibre.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष|कक्षः
कक्ष कक्ष, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कष्),<BR>a lurking or hiding-place; an inner recess, the interior<BR>of a forest; a forest of dead trees, a dry wood (the<BR>lair of wild beasts), grass, dry grass; a spreading<BR>creeper, a climbing plant; the armpit (as the most<BR>concealed part of the human body); the side or flank;<BR>the orbit of a planet or the circle anciently termed a<BR>deferent; sin; a buffalo; a gate; the Beleric Myroba-<BR>lan or Terminalia Belerica; (आ), f. painful boils in the<BR>armpit, side, shoulder, &c.; an elephant's rope, the<BR>string round his neck, also his girth; a woman's<BR>girdle or zone; a surrounding wall, a wall; a place<BR>surrounded by walls; a court or court-yard; an en-<BR>closure; a secluded portion of an edifice; a private<BR>or inner chamber, the private apartment for women<BR>&c., a room in general; a particular part of a carriage;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">Page0194-a+ 77</a>]<BR>resemblance, similarity; objection or reply in argu-<BR>ment; emulation, rivalry, object of emulation; the<BR>jeweller's weight, the Retti; (अस्, आ), m. f. the end of<BR>the lower garment which, after the cloth is carried<BR>round the body, is brought up behind and tucked<BR>into the waistband; a border, lace; the scale or basin<BR>of a balance; (अम्), n. a star, a constellation (perhaps<BR>a wrong reading for ऋक्ष); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—कक्ष-धर, अम्, n. the part of the<BR>body where the upper arm is connected with the<BR>shoulder, the shoulder-joint.<BR>—कक्ष-प, अस्, m.<BR>one of the nine treasures of Kuvera; [cf. कच्छप.]<BR>—कक्ष-पुट, अस्, m. the armpit; title of a<BR>work on magic.<BR>—कक्ष-रुहा, f. a fragrant grass,<BR>Cyperus.<BR>—कक्ष-शाय, अस्, m. a dog; [cf.<BR>कङ्कशाय.]<BR>—कक्ष-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a Rā-<BR>jarshi.<BR>—कक्ष-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated on the<BR>side, seated on the hip or flank.<BR>—कक्षाध्याय<BR>(˚ष-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of a part of a commentary<BR>by Bhūdhara on the Sūrya-siddhānta.<BR>—कक्षान्-<BR>तर (˚ष-अन्˚), अम्, n. the inner or private<BR>apartment.<BR>—कक्षा-पट, अस्, m. a cloth passed<BR>between the legs to cover the privities.<BR>—कक्षा-<BR>पुटि, इस्, m., N. of a physician; (wrong reading for<BR>काक्षपुटि ?).<BR>—कक्षावेक्षक, अस्, m. (कक्षा<BR>+ अवेक्षक fr. rt. ईक्ष् with अव), a guard of the<BR>inner or queen's apartments; keeper of a royal<BR>garden; a door-keeper; a poet; a debauchee; a<BR>player, a painter; warmth of feeling, strength of<BR>sentiment.<BR>—कक्षी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, assented, pro-<BR>mised, (touching the armpit with the hand was per-<BR>haps a manner of affirming anything; cf. उरसि कृ<BR>under उरस्.)<BR>—कक्षोत्था (˚ष-उत्˚), f. a fragrant<BR>grass, Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षक
कक्षक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षतु
कक्षतु, उस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षाय
कक्षाय, nom. A. कक्षायते, -यितुम्, to wait<BR>for any one in a hidden place, lie in ambush; to<BR>intend anything wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीवत्|कक्षीवन्त्
कक्षीवत्, आन्, m. (fr. कक्ष्या), N. of a renowned<BR>Ṛṣi, sometimes called Pajriya; he is the author of<BR>several hymns of the Ṛg-veda, and is described in<BR>legends as a son of Uśij and Dīrgha-tamas; (अन्तस्),<BR>m. pl. the family or the descendants of Kakṣīvat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षेयु
कक्षेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva and<BR>Ghṛtācī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्य|कक्ष्यं
कक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. consisting of shrubs or<BR>dry grass; secret; (Sāy.) filling the girth, as a well-fed<BR>horse; (आ), f. the girth of an elephant or horse, con-<BR>sisting of rope or leather; a woman's girdle or zone;<BR>metaphorically the fingers (encircling the Soma cup);<BR>an upper garment, the border or lace of one; the<BR>enclosure of an edifice, i. e. either the wall &c. so en-<BR>closing it, or the court or chamber constituting the<BR>enclosure, the inner apartment of a palace; similarity;<BR>effort, exertion; a shrub yielding the black and red<BR>berry that serves as a jeweller's weight, the Retti or<BR>Gunja, Abrus Precatorius; (अम्), n. the cup or re-<BR>ceptacle of a balance; a part of a carriage.<BR>—कक्ष्य-<BR>प्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. filling the girth (as a well-fed<BR>horse).<BR>—कक्ष्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with<BR>a girth.<BR>—कक्ष्यावेक्षक, अस्, m. = कक्षा-<BR>वेक्षक, q. v.<BR>—कक्ष्या-स्तोत्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>hymn by Divākara-vatsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्
कख् कख्, cl. 1. P. कखति, -खितुम्,<BR>to laugh, laugh at or deride: Caus. P.<BR>कखयति, -यितुम्, to cause to laugh; [cf. Lat.<BR>cachinnare; Gr. καχάζω, καγχάζω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या कख्या, f. an enclosure, a division<BR>of a large building; (a wrong reading for कक्ष्या.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कग्
कग् कग्, cl. 1. P. कगति, -गितुम्, to act,<BR>perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्क्|कंक्
कङ्क् कङ्क्, cl. 1. A. कङ्कते, -कितुम्, to<BR>go; [cf. Hib. cichet, ‘walking;’ ciocair, ‘a<BR>way, a road:’ Lith. kankù; ifs-kankù, ‘to come to.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्क|कंक|कंकः|कङ्कः
कङ्क कङ्क, अस्, m. a heron (a bird of prey?);<BR>a kind of mango; an epithet of Yama; N. of a<BR>king; a Vṛṣṇi; a son of Ugra-sena, a son of Śūra;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">Page0194-b+ 73</a>]<BR>pl., N. of a people; a title of Yudhiṣṭhira (from his<BR>assuming the disguise of a Brāhman before king<BR>Virāṭa); a false or pretended Brāhman; a man of<BR>the second or military tribe (perhaps a man of that<BR>caste pretending to be a Brāhman); one of the<BR>eighteen divisions of the continent; the brother of<BR>Kaṃsa; (आ), f. a sort of sandal; scent of the lotus;<BR>N. of a daughter of Ugra-sena and sister of Kaṅka.<BR>—कङ्क-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. collected into a heap<BR>resembling a heron.<BR>—कङ्क-तुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Rakṣas.<BR>—कङ्क-त्रोट, अस्, or कङ्क-त्रोटि, इस्, m.<BR>a kind of fish, commonly काङ्किला; Esox Kankila.<BR>—कङ्क-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a heron's feather fixed on<BR>an arrow; (अस्, आ, अम्), furnished with the feathers of<BR>a heron; (अस्), m. an arrow furnished with heron's<BR>feathers.<BR>—कङ्कपत्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, furnished with<BR>heron's feathers.<BR>—कङ्क-पर्वन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>serpent.<BR>—कङ्क-माला, f. a kind of musical instru-<BR>ment; beating time by clapping the hands.<BR>—कङ्क-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, shaped like a heron's mouth;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a pair of tongs, a sort of forceps.<BR>—कङ्क-शत्रु, उस्, m. the plant Desmodium<BR>Gangeticum.<BR>—कङ्क-शाय, अस्, m. a dog (sleeping<BR>like a heron).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कट|कंकट|कंकटः|कङ्कटः
कङ्कट कङ्कट or कङ्कटक, अस्, m. (said<BR>to be fr. rt. कङ्क्), mail, defensive armour; an iron<BR>hook to goad an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कटेरी
कङ्कटेरी कङ्कटेरी, f. turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कण|कंकण|कंकणं|कङ्कणं|कंकणः|कङ्कणः
कङ्कण कङ्कण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. कै), a bracelet, an ornament of the wrist<BR>(used also as a weapon); a string or ribbon tied<BR>round the wrist; an ornament round the foot of an<BR>elephant; any ornament or trinket; a crest; (ई), f.<BR>a small bell or tinkling ornament; an ornament<BR>furnished with bells: see किङ्किणी; [cf. Lith. kan-<BR>kala-s.]<BR>—कङ्कण-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town,<BR>called from कङ्कण-वर्ष.<BR>—कङ्कण-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a servant of Śiva.<BR>—कङ्कण-भू-<BR>षण, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned with tinkling orna-<BR>ments.<BR>—कङ्कण-मणी, f. the jewel in a bracelet.<BR>—कङ्कण-वर्ष, अस्, m., N. of an alchemist^1;<BR>epithet of the king Kṣemagupta.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कणिन्|कंकणिन्
कङ्कणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ornamented with a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कणीका|कंकणीका
कङ्कणीका, f. an ornament furnished with bells;<BR>a string tied round the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत|कंकत|कंकतं|कङ्कतं|कंकतः|कङ्कतः
कङ्कत कङ्कत, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. or कङ्क-<BR>तिका, f. a comb, a hair-comb; (अस्), m. a tree; (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy.) a poisonous animal, a slightly venomous<BR>reptile (mentioned in a verse of Ṛg-veda 1. 191,<BR>used as a mystical spell against poison).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कतीय
कङ्कतीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कर|कंकर|कङ्करं|कङ्करः
कङ्कर कङ्कर, अस्, ई, अम्, vile, bad; (अम्),<BR>n. buttermilk mixed with water; a high number, =<BR>100 niyutas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्करोल|कंकरोलः|कङ्करोलः
कङ्करोल कङ्करोल, अस्, m. the plant Alan-<BR>gium Hexapetalum. See निकोचक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कलोड्य|कंकलोड्यं|कङ्कलोड्यं
कङ्कलोड्य कङ्कलोड्य, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>drug, = अल्कलोड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्काल|कंकाल|कंकालं|कंकालः|कङ्कालः
कङ्काल कङ्काल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a skeleton;<BR>[cf. Mod. Gr. κώκαλον.]<BR>—कङ्काल-केतु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Dānava.<BR>—कङ्काल-भैरव-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—कङ्कालमालिन्, ई, m. an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva, whose necklace is formed of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कालय|कंकालय|कंकालयः|कङ्कालयः
कङ्कालय कङ्कालय or कल्कालय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कु|कंकुः|कङ्कुः
कङ्कु कङ्कु, उस्, m. = कङ्गु, N. of a son<BR>of Ugra-sena and brother of Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कुष्ठ|कंकुष्ठं|कङ्कुष्ठं|कंकुष्ठः|कङ्कुष्ठः
कङ्कुष्ठ कङ्कुष्ठ, अस्, m. a medicinal earth,<BR>described as of two colours, one of a silvery and one<BR>of a gold colour, or one of a light and one of a dark<BR>yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कूष|कंकूषः|कङ्कूषः
कङ्कूष कङ्कूष, (?) Atharva-veda IX. 8, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केरु|कंकेरुः|कङ्केरुः
कङ्केरु कङ्केरु, उस्, m. a kind of crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केल्ल|कंकेल्लः|कङ्केल्लः
कङ्केल्ल कङ्केल्ल, अस्, m. the tree Jonesia<BR>Aśoka; a kind of pot-herb, Chenopodium Esculentum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केल्लि|कंकेल्लिः|कङ्केल्लिः
कङ्केल्लि, इस्, m. Jonesia Aśoka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कोल
कङ्कोल कङ्कोल, अस्, m. a king of the Nāgas;<BR>N. of the author of a hymn called Gaṇapatyārādhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्ख|कंखं|कङ्खं
कङ्ख कङ्ख, अम्, n. enjoyment, fruition;<BR>(perhaps a combination of क and ख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गु|कंगु|कङ्गुः
कङ्गु कङ्गु, उस्, f. or कङ्गुनी, f. a kind of<BR>Panic seed, Panicum Italicum; several varieties of it<BR>are cultivated and form articles of food for the poor.<BR>—कङ्गुनी-पत्त्रा, f. a kind of grass, = पण्यान्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुल|कंगुल|कंगुलः|कङ्गुलः
कङ्गुल कङ्गुल, अस्, m. the hand; [cf.<BR>अङ्गुलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्
कच् कच्, cl. 1. A. कचते, चकचे, कचि-<BR>तुम्, to bind; to shine; P. कचति, to<BR>sound, cry; [cf. कञ्च्; cf. also Hib. cacht, ‘a strait,<BR>a narrow place; bonds, fetters.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच|कचः
कच, अस्, m. the hair (especially of the head); a<BR>cicatrix, a dry or healed sore, a scar; a binding, band;<BR>the hem of a garment; a cloud; N. of a son of<BR>Bṛhaspati; N. of a place; (आ), f. a female elephant;<BR>beauty, brilliancy; [cf. अ-कच, उत्-कच, &c.]<BR>—कच-<BR>प, अस्, m. ‘cloud-drinker,’ grass; a leaf; (अम्), n.<BR>a vessel for vegetables; a leaf of a vegetable (?).<BR>—कच-पक्ष or कच-पाश, अस्, m. thick or<BR>ornamented hair.<BR>—कच-माल, अस्, m. smoke; (per-<BR>haps a wrong reading for खतमाल?).<BR>—कच-<BR>रिपु-फला, f., N. of a tree; see शमी.<BR>—कच-<BR>हस्त, अस्, m. thick or ornamented hair, a beautiful<BR>head of hair.<BR>—कचा-कचि, ind. hair against hair,<BR>pulling each other's hair.<BR>—कचाचित (˚च-अच्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having long or dishevelled hair.<BR>—कचामोद<BR>(˚च-आम्˚), अम्, n. a fragrant ointment for the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचङ्गन|कचंगन|कचंगनं|कचङ्गनं
कचङ्गन कचङ्गन, अम्, n. a free market,<BR>a place of sale paying no duty or custom; [cf. कराङ्-<BR>गण, अङ्गण, and अङ्गन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचङ्गल|कचंगल|कचंगलः|कचङ्गलः
कचङ्गल कचङ्गल, अम्, n. the ocean; N.<BR>of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाकु|कचाकुः
कचाकु कचाकु, उस्, उस्, उ, ill-disposed,<BR>wicked; intolerable, difficult to be borne; difficult<BR>to be attained; (उस्), m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाटुर|कचाटुरः
कचाटुर कचाटुर, अस्, m. a gallinule. See<BR>दात्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचु|कचुः
कचु कचु, उस्, f. an esculent root, Arum<BR>Colocasia and other kinds, many of which are culti-<BR>vated for food. See कच्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचेल|कचेलं
कचेल कचेल, अम्, n. a string or cover con-<BR>taining and keeping together the leaves of a manu-<BR>script; (perhaps a various reading for काचन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चट|कच्चटं
कच्चट कच्चट, अम्, n. an aquatic plant, =<BR>जलपिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चर|कच्चरं
कच्चर कच्चर (कद्-चर,) अस्, आ, अम्, dirty,<BR>foul; spoiled, spoiled by dirt; vile, wicked, bad;<BR>(अम्), n. buttermilk diluted with water; [cf. कङ्-<BR>कर, कटुर, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चिद्
कच्चिद् कच्-चिद् (= कद्-चिद्). See under 2. कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छ|कच्छं|कच्छः
कच्छ कच्छ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in the first<BR>sense a Prākṛt form for कक्ष; cf. कच्छटिका),<BR>the hem or end of a lower garment tucked into the<BR>girdle or waistband; (according to some m. f. n. in<BR>the next senses, according to others only m.) a bank<BR>or any ground bordering on water, as the margin of<BR>a river, lake, tank, &c.; a mound or causeway,<BR>watery soil, marshy ground, a marsh, a morass, low or<BR>flat land skirting mountains; N. of several places; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the people inhabiting them; (अस्), m. a part<BR>of a boat; a particular part of a tortoise; a tree, the<BR>timber of which is used for making furniture &c.,<BR>Cedrela Toona or common Tūn; another tree,<BR>Hibiscus Populneoides; (आ), f. a cricket; the plant<BR>Lycopodium Imbricatum; see वाराही.<BR>—कच्छ-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">Page0195-a+ 74</a>]<BR>देश, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—कच्छ-प, अस्,<BR>m. a turtle, a tortoise (as inhabiting marshy<BR>places); a tumour on the palate; an apparatus used<BR>in the distillation of spirituous liquor, a flat kind of<BR>still; an attitude in wrestling; the tree Cedrela<BR>Toona; one of the nine nidhis or treasures of<BR>Kuvera; N. of a Nāga; a son of Viśvā-mitra; N. of<BR>a country; (ई), f. a female tortoise or a small species<BR>of tortoise; a cutaneous disease, wart or blotch; a<BR>kind of lute, also the lute of Sarasvatī (so named from<BR>being similar in shape to the tortoise).<BR>—कच्छ-<BR>प-देश, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—कच्छ-भू,<BR>ऊस्, f. marshy ground, a swamp, a morass.<BR>—कच्छ-<BR>रुहा, f. a kind of grass, Dūrva, Agrostis Linearis,<BR>Panicus Dactilon.<BR>—कच्छ-विहार, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a marshy region.<BR>—कच्छान्त (˚छ-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the border of a lake or stream.<BR>—कच्छेश्वर<BR>(˚छ-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छटिका
कच्छटिका or कच्छाटिका or कच्छाटी, f. the<BR>end or hem of a lower garment or cloth gathered up<BR>behind and tucked into the waistband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपिका
कच्छपिका, f. a pimple, a blotch or wart; a<BR>wart accompanying gonorrhœa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छर
कच्छर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छोटिका
कच्छोटिका, f. = कच्छटिका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छिय
कच्छिय कच्छिय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(various readings have कक्ष and कच्छ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छु|कच्छुः
कच्छु कच्छु, उस्, or कच्छू, ऊस्, f. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. कष्), itch, formation of watery pustules on<BR>the hands &c., scab. (The form कच्छू is the older<BR>and more correct form.)<BR>—कच्छु-घ्नी, f. the plant<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca; another plant, = हपुयाभेद.<BR>—कच्छू-मती, f. the plant Carpopogon Pruriens,<BR>said to cause itching on being applied to the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुर|कच्छुरः
कच्छुर, अस्, आ, अम्, scabby, itchy; unchaste,<BR>libidinous; (आ), f. the plant Alhagi Maurorum; a<BR>species of Curcuma; the plant Carpopogon Pruriens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छोर|कच्छोरं
कच्छोर, अम्, n. a kind of Curcuma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्वी
कच्वी कच्वी, f. a plant with an esculent<BR>root (Arum Colocasia) cultivated for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्
कज् कज्, cl. 1. P. कजति, -जितुम्, to be<BR>happy; to be confused with joy, pride or<BR>sorrow; to grow, (in the last sense a Sautra root.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कज क-ज. See under 4. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कजिङ्ग
कजिङ्ग कजिङ्ग, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जल|कज्जलं|कज्जलः
कज्जल कज्जल, अस्, m. (in the first sense<BR>from कद्-जल), a cloud; (अम्), n. lampblack, con-<BR>sidered as a collyrium and applied to the eyelashes<BR>or eyelids medicinally or as an ornament, also sulphu-<BR>ret of lead or antimony so used; (आ, ई), f. the fish<BR>Cyprinus Atratus, or any kind peculiar to stagnant<BR>waters, whence the name; (ई), f. sulphuret of mer-<BR>cury, Æthiop's mineral; ink.<BR>—कज्जल-ध्वज, अस्,<BR>m. a lamp.<BR>—कज्जल-रोचक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>wooden stand or tripod on which a lamp is placed,<BR>a candlestick.<BR>—कज्जली-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जलित
कज्जलित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with lampblack or<BR>with a collyrium prepared from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वल|कज्ज्वलं
कज्ज्वल कज्ज्वल, अम्, n. lampblack, especially<BR>considered as an application to the eyes; [cf. कज्जल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्च्|कंच्
कञ्च् कञ्च्, cl. 1. A. कञ्चते, चकञ्चे,<BR>कञ्चितुम्, to bind; to shine; [cf. कच्<BR>and काञ्च्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चट|कञ्चटं|कञ्चटः
कञ्चट कञ्चट, अस्, m. the aquatic plant<BR>Commelina Salicifolia and C. Bengalensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चड|कञ्चडः
कञ्चड, अस्, m. the plant Commelina Bengalensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चार|कंचार|कंचारः|कञ्चारः
कञ्चार कञ्चार, अस्, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चिका|कंचिका
कञ्चिका कञ्चिका, f. a small boil; the branch<BR>of a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुक|कंचुक|कंचुकः|कञ्चुकः
कञ्चुक कञ्चुक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कञ्च् ?), a dress<BR>fitting close to the upper part of the body; armour,<BR>mail; a bodice, jacket; the skin of a snake; cloth,<BR>clothes; a kind of drawers or short breeches; a strap<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">Page0195-b+ 77</a>]<BR>of leather; the cast-off skin of a snake; (ई), f., N.<BR>of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकालु|कंचुकालु|कंचुकालुः|कञ्चुकालुः
कञ्चुकालु, उस्, m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकित|कंचुकित
कञ्चुकित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with armour or<BR>mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकिन्|कंचुकिन्
कञ्चुकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with armour or<BR>mail; (ई), m. an attendant on or overseer of the women's<BR>apartments, a chamberlain; a libidinous man, a de-<BR>bauchee, one addicted to women; a serpent; N. of<BR>several plants, Agallochum, barley, Cicer Arietinum.<BR>—कञ्चुकि-रेचक, औ, m. du. the chamberlain and<BR>the forester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुलिका|कंचुलिका
कञ्चुलिका, f. a bodice or jacket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चूल|कंचूलं
कञ्चूल, अस्, अम्, m. n. an article of female dress,<BR>perhaps a bodice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्ज|कंज|कञ्जं|कंजः|कञ्जः
कञ्ज कञ्-ज, अस्, m. (fr. कम् = head), the<BR>hair; (fr. कम् = water), an epithet of Brahmā; (अम्),<BR>n. a lotus; the Amṛta or food of the immortals;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), produced in or from water; (in com-<BR>position कञ्ज may follow or precede the term<BR>compounded with it, e. g. कञ्ज-वदन or वदन-<BR>कञ्ज, a lotus-face.)<BR>—कञ्ज-ज, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Brahmā (born from a lotus).<BR>—कञ्ज-नाभ,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जक|कंजक|कंजकः|कञ्जकः
कञ्जक कञ्जक, अस्, m. a kind of bird,<BR>Gracula Religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जन|कंजन|कंजनः|कञ्जनः
कञ्जन, अस्, m. the bird Gracula Religiosa, the<BR>bird of Kandarpa; N. of Kandarpa, the deity of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जल|कंजल|कंजलः|कञ्जलः
कञ्जल, अस्, m., N. of the bird Gracula Religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जर|कंजर|कंजरः|कञ्जरः
कञ्जर कञ्जर, अस्, m. the belly; an ele-<BR>phant; the sun; an epithet of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जार|कंजार|कंजारः|कञ्जारः
कञ्जार, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कज्), a peacock;<BR>the belly; an elephant; a Muni or holy sage, an<BR>hermit; the sun; an epithet of Brahmā; also =<BR>व्यञ्जन (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जाण
कञ्जाण कञ्जाण, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N.<BR>of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जिका|कंजिका
कञ्जिका कञ्जिका, f. the plant Siphonanthus<BR>Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्
कट् 1. कट् or कण्ट्, cl. 1. P. कटति or<BR>कण्टति, -टितुम्, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्
कट् 2. कट्, cl. 1. P. कटति, चकाट, कटि-<BR>तुम्, to rain; surround; to encompass, to<BR>cover or screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट|कटः
कट, अस्, m. a twist of straw or grass, a straw mat;<BR>a screen of straw; the hip; the hollow above the hip or<BR>the loins; the hip and loins; the temples of an elephant;<BR>a particular throw of the dice in hazard; (at the end of<BR>some compounds) much, excessive (but in the words<BR>अवकट, उत्कट, प्रकट, and सङ्कट considered<BR>as an affix); N. of a Rakṣas; a corpse; a hearse, a<BR>bier, a bed &c. used for conveying a dead body; a<BR>place where dead bodies are burnt or buried, a place<BR>of sepulture; a time or season; excess, superabundance;<BR>the plant Saccharum Sara; an annual plant; grass;<BR>a thin piece of wood, a plank; (अम्), n. (considered<BR>as an affix at the end of compounds), dust of flowers;<BR>(ई), f. long pepper; (अस्, ई, अम्), an agent in any<BR>action.<BR>—कट-खादक, अस्, आ, अम्, eating much,<BR>one who eats voraciously; (अस्), m. a jackal; a crow;<BR>a glass vessel, a tumbler or bowl.<BR>—कट-घोष,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a region in the east of India.<BR>—कट-<BR>नगर, N. of a place in the East.<BR>—कट-पल्लि-<BR>कुञ्चिका, f. a straw hut (?).<BR>—कट-पल्वल, N. of a<BR>place in the East.<BR>—कट-पूतन, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>demon (a Kṣatriya not performing his duties is born<BR>after his death as such a goblin); a kind of Preta or<BR>inhabitant of the lower regions; see पूतना and<BR>अन्धपूतना.<BR>—कट-प्रू, ऊस्, m. a worm; one<BR>who gambles or plays with dice; an epithet of Śiva<BR>or Mahādeva; a Rakṣas, an imp or goblin; a kind<BR>of demi-god, one of the class of Vidyādharas.<BR>—कट-<BR>प्रोथ, अस्, m. the buttocks.<BR>—कट-भङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m. gleaning, plucking or gathering corn with the<BR>hands; the destruction of a prince; royal misfortune,<BR>as deposure, defeat, &c.<BR>—कट-भी, f., N. of several<BR>plants, Cardiospermum Halicacabum (an annual plant);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-c" target="_blank">Page0195-c+ 73</a>]<BR>Clitoria Ternatea = अपराजिता; N. of a tree.<BR>—कट-<BR>मालिनी, f. wine or any vinous liquor.<BR>—कटम्-<BR>भर, अस्, m. the plant Bignonia Indica; another<BR>plant, = कटभी; (आ), f. several plants, Pœderia<BR>Fetida; a medicinal plant, Kaṭukī; a sort of cucum-<BR>ber, Cucumis Madraspatanus; Bœrhavia Diffusa, Ale-<BR>tris Hyacinthoides; hog-weed; a female elephant;<BR>red arsenic.<BR>—कट-व्रण, अस्, m. ‘wounding in the<BR>hips,’ a N. of Bhīma-sena.<BR>—कट-शर्करा, f. a frag-<BR>ment of a mat broken off, or of straw; the plant<BR>Guilandina Bonducella; [cf. कटु-करञ्ज.]<BR>—कट-<BR>स्थल, अम्, n. the hip and loins, an elephant's tem-<BR>ples.<BR>—कटाक्ष (˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, m. a glance or side<BR>look, a leer.<BR>—कटाक्ष-क्षेत्र, N. of a place.<BR>—कटाक्ष-मुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, caught by a glance.<BR>—कटाक्ष-विशिख, अस्, m. an arrow-like look of<BR>love.<BR>—कटाक्षावेक्षण (˚ष-अव्˚), अम्, n. cast-<BR>ing lewd or amorous glances, ogling.<BR>—कटाग्नि (˚ट-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m. a fire kept up with dry grass or straw; the<BR>straw placed round a criminal who is to be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटक|कटकं|कटकः
कटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a string; a ring placed as<BR>an ornament upon an elephant's tusk; a bracelet of<BR>gold or of shell &c.; a zone; the link of a chain;<BR>a mat; the side or ridge of a hill or mountain; table<BR>land; a circle, a wheel, an army, a camp; a royal<BR>metropolis, a city or town, a village, a house or<BR>dwelling; N. of the capital of Orissa (Cuttack); sea- salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

