कटाह|कटाहः
कटाह कटाह, अस्, m. (according to the<BR>Schol. m. f. n.), a frying-pan, a boiler or a frying-<BR>vessel of a semispheroidal shape and with handles;<BR>a shallow boiler for oil or butter; a turtle's shell; a<BR>well; a winnowing basket; a hill of earth; hell, the<BR>infernal regions; a young female buffalo whose horns<BR>are just appearing; a dvīpa or division of the known<BR>continent, so called, (perhaps the Katai of the Muham-<BR>medans or China.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाहक|कटाहकं
कटाहक, अम्, n. a pan, a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटि|कटिः
कटि कटि, इस्, or कटी, f. (fr. rt. 2. कट् ?), the<BR>hip; the buttocks; an elephant's cheek; (ई), f. long<BR>pepper.<BR>—कटि-कुष्ठ, अम्, n. leprosy of the hip.<BR>—कटि-कूप, अस्, m. the hollow above the hip, the<BR>loins.<BR>—कटि-तट, अम्, n. the loins, the hip.<BR>—कटि-<BR>त्र, अम्, n. anything to protect the hips; a cloth tied<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">Page0196-a+ 79</a>]<BR>round the loins; a zone; an ornament of small bells<BR>worn round the loins; armour for the hip or loins.<BR>—कटि-देश, अस्, m. the loins.<BR>—कटि-प्रोथ or<BR>कटी-प्रोथ, अस्, m. the buttocks; [cf. कट-प्रोथ.]<BR>—कटि-मालिका, f. a woman's zone.<BR>—कटि-रोहक,<BR>अस्, m. the rider of an elephant who sits upon the<BR>hinder parts of the elephant, as distinct from the<BR>driver or the person sitting upon the loins.<BR>—कटि-<BR>शीर्षक, अस्, m. the hip (as projecting like a head);<BR>the hip and loins or the hollow above the hip.<BR>—कटि-शृङ्खला, f. a girdle of small bells.<BR>—कटि-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n. a female zone or waistband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिका
कटिका, f. the hip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीर|कटीरं|कटीरः
कटीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the cavity of the loins or the<BR>iliac region; (अस्), m. Mons Veneris; a cave; (अम्),<BR>n. a hip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीरक|कटीरकं|कटीरकः
कटीरक, अम्, n. the posteriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिल्लक|कटिल्लकः
कटिल्लक कटिल्लक, अस्, m. a species of the<BR>balsam apple, Momordica Charantia; [cf. कठिल्लक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीतल|कटीतलः
कटीतल कटीतल, अस्, m. a crooked sword;<BR>a sabre or scymitar; [cf. कडितुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटु|कटुः
कटु कटु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कट्), pungent, acrid, sharp (one of the six kinds of<BR>flavour); pungent, stimulating (smell); strong-scented,<BR>ill-smelling; bitter, caustic (words); displeasing, dis-<BR>agreeable; fierce, impetuous, hot; envious; (उस्),<BR>m. pungency, acerbity (as a flavour); the plants<BR>Michelia Champaca, Trichosanthes Diœca, camphor,<BR>&c.; (उस्), f. various plants, = कटु-रोहिणी, a medi-<BR>cinal plant; Sinapis Ramosa; (वी), f., N. of a plant;<BR>(उ), n. an improper action, an act which ought not<BR>to have been done; blaming, reviling, scandal.<BR>—क-<BR>टु-कन्द, अस्, अम्, m. n. ginger, the fresh root or<BR>the plant; garlic; the plant Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR>—कटु-करञ्ज, अस्, m. the plant Guilandina<BR>Bonducella.<BR>—कटु-कीट or कटुकीटक, अस्, m.<BR>a gnat or musquito.<BR>—कटु-क्वाण, अस्, m. a spe-<BR>cies of chicken, Parra Jacana or Gœnsis (making a<BR>sharp or piercing noise).<BR>—कटु-ग्रन्थि, इ, n. dried<BR>ginger; the root of long pepper.<BR>—कटु-चातुर्जातक,<BR>अम्, n. an aggregate of four acid substances, as of<BR>cardamoms, the bark and leaves of Laurus Cassia<BR>and of black pepper.<BR>—कटु-च्छद, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a tree with pungent leaves; [cf. तगर.]<BR>—कटु-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared from acid substances, as a<BR>kind of drink.<BR>—कटु-तिक्तिक, अस्, m. the plants<BR>Gentiana Cherayta and Cannabis Sativa; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a plant.<BR>—कटु-तुण्डिका and कटु-तुण्डी, f., N.<BR>of a plant, = तिक्त-तुण्डी, commonly कटुतराई.<BR>—कटु-तुम्बी, f. a kind of bitter gourd.<BR>—कटु-<BR>त्रय, अम्, n. the aggregate of three black sub-<BR>stances or spices, ginger, black and long pepper.<BR>—कटु-दला, f., N. of a plant, = कर्कटी.<BR>—कटु-<BR>निष्प्लाव, अस्, m. grain not inundated.<BR>—कटु-<BR>पत्त्र, अस्, m. the medicinal plant Oldenlandia<BR>Biflora, and of another plant Sitārjaka.<BR>—कटु-<BR>पत्त्रिका, f., N. of a tree, = कारी.<BR>—कटु-पद्र,<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—कटु-पाक, अस्, आ, अम्, or कटु-<BR>पाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, producing acrid humors in digestion.<BR>—कटु-फल, अस्, m. a sort of cucumber, Tricho-<BR>santhes Diœca.<BR>—कटु-बदरी, f., N. of a plant and<BR>of a village called from this plant.<BR>—कटु-भङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. dried ginger.<BR>—कटु-भद्र, अम्, n. dried<BR>ginger, or ginger in general.<BR>—कटु-मञ्जरिका, f.<BR>the plant Achyranthes Aspera.<BR>—कटु-मोद, अम्,<BR>n. a certain perfume.<BR>—कटु-रव, अस्, m. a frog.<BR>—कटु-रोहिणी, f. the medicinal plant Helleborus<BR>Niger.<BR>—कटु-वार्ताकी, f. a variety of Solanum.<BR>—कटु-विपाक, अस्, आ, अम्, producing acrid humors<BR>in digestion.<BR>—कटु-वीजा, f. long pepper.<BR>—कटु-<BR>शृङ्गाल, अम्, n., N. of a vegetable.<BR>—कटु-स्नेह,<BR>अस्, m. the mustard-seed plant, Sinapis Dichotoma.<BR>—कटूत्कट (˚टु-उत्˚), अस्, m. ginger.<BR>—कटूत्-<BR>कटक, अम्, n. dry ginger.<BR>—कट्फल, अस्, m.<BR>(for कटु-फ्˚), a small tree found in the north-west<BR>of Hindūstan, the bark and seeds of which are used<BR>in medicine, and as aromatics; the fruit also is eaten;<BR>the common name is Kāyaphal; (आ), f., N. of several<BR>plants, as of Gmelina Arborea and different kinds of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">Page0196-b+ 74</a>]<BR>Solanum, = देवदाली and मृगेर्वारु.<BR>—कट्व्-अङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Calosanthes Indica; an epithet of<BR>Dilīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुक|कटुकं|कटुकः
कटुक, अस्, आ, अम्, sharp, pungent, bitter, fierce,<BR>impetuous, hot; (अस्), m. pungency, acerbity; N. of<BR>several plants, Trichosanthes Diœca, a fragrant kind<BR>of grass; gigantic swallow wort, Calotropis Gigantea;<BR>a plant the bark and seed of which have an acrid and<BR>bitter taste, and are used in medicine for worms,<BR>dysentery, &c., Wrigthia Antidysenterica; Sinapis Di-<BR>chotoma or Ramosa; N. of a man; (आ), f., N. of<BR>several plants, = कट्वी and कटु-रोहिणी; Areca Fau-<BR>fel or Catechu; Ruellia Longifolia; (ई), f. = कटु-<BR>रोहिणी; (अम्), n. pungency, acerbity (at the end of<BR>compounds in a bad sense, e. g. दधि-कटुकम्,<BR>bad coagulated milk); a compound of pungent sub-<BR>stances, as black pepper, long pepper, dry ginger.<BR>—क-<BR>टुक-त्रय, अम्, n. an aggregate of three pungent<BR>substances, as black pepper, long pepper, and ginger.<BR>—कटुक-त्व, अम्, n. pungency.<BR>—कटुक-फल,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a perfume prepared from the berries<BR>of the plant Kakkola.<BR>—कटुक-भक्षिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—कटुक-रोहिणी, f. = कटु-रोहिणी.<BR>—क-<BR>टुक-वल्ली, f. = कट्वी.<BR>—कटुकालाबु (˚क-अल्˚), उस्,<BR>m. a kind of bitter gourd, Trichosanthes Diœca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुङ्कता|कटुंकता
कटुङ्कता कटुङ्कता, f. rough manners.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुर|कटुरं|कटुरः
कटुर कटुर, अम्, n. buttermilk mixed<BR>with water, = तक्र; [cf. कङ्कर, कच्चर, कट्-<BR>वर, कदर, कद्वर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटेरकग्राम
कटेरकग्राम कटेरक-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोदक
कटोदक कटोदक, अम्, n. (fr. कट = कर्त<BR>= गर्त ? and उदक), water for a funeral libation,<BR>a funeral rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोरा
कटोरा कटोरा, f. a shallow cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोल|कटोलः
कटोल कटोल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कट्), a pungent flavour; a man of an inferior and<BR>degraded tribe, a Caṇḍāla, a Pariah, &c.; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>pungent.<BR>—कटोल-वीणा, f. a kind of lute played by<BR>the common people or Caṇḍālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्टार|कट्टारः
कट्टार कट्टार, अस्, m. a weapon, a dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वर|कट्वरं
कट्वर कट्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, despised; (अम्),<BR>n. the skim or whey of curds; buttermilk with<BR>water; a sauce, condiment; [cf. कङ्कर, कच्चर,<BR>कटुर, कदर, कद्वर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वाङ्ग
कट्वाङ्ग कट्वाङ्ग, a wrong reading for<BR>खट्वाङ्ग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ्
कठ् कठ्, cl. 1. P. कठति, -ठितुम्, to<BR>live in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ|कठः
कठ कठ, अस्, m., N. of a sage, a pupil of<BR>Vaiśampāyana and founder of a branch of the Yajur-<BR>veda, called after him; a Brāhman; a note or simple<BR>sound; (आस्), m. pl. the followers or pupils of Kaṭha;<BR>(ई), f. a female follower of Kaṭha; the wife of a<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—कठ-कालापाः, the schools of Kaṭha<BR>and Kalāpin.<BR>—कठ-कौथुमाः, the schools of<BR>Kaṭha and Kuthumin.<BR>—कठ-धूर्त, अस्, m. a<BR>Brāhman skilled in the Kaṭha branch of the Yajur-<BR>veda.<BR>—कठ-वल्ली or कठवल्ल्य्-उपनिषद्, त्,<BR>or कठ-श्रुति, इस्, or कठोपनिषद् (˚ठ-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad consisting of two Adhyāyas<BR>of three Vallī each.<BR>—कठ-शाखा, f. a branch of<BR>the Yajur-veda; also of the Ṛg-veda (?).<BR>—कठ-<BR>शाठ, अस्, m., N. of a man; काठशाठिन्, इनस्,<BR>m. pl., N. of a school.<BR>—कठ-श्रोत्रिय, अस्, m. a<BR>Brāhman who has studied the Kaṭha branch of the<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR>—कठाध्यापक (˚ठ-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a teacher of the Kaṭha branch of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—कठोपनिषद्-भाष्य-टीका, f. a commentary<BR>by Anantānanda on a Kaṭhopaniṣadbhāṣya.<BR>—क-<BR>ठोपनिषद्भाष्यटीका-विवरण, अम्, n. a com-<BR>mentary by Vyāsatīrtha on the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठमर्द|कठमर्दः|कठमर्द्द|कठमर्द्दः
कठमर्द कठमर्द, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; (fr. कठ, distress ? मर्द, dissipating.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठर|कठरः
कठर कठर, अस्, आ, अम्, hard; [cf. कठिन<BR>and कठोर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठल्य|कठल्यः
कठल्य कठल्य or कठल्ल, अस् or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?), gravel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाकु|कठाकुः
कठाकु कठाकु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कठ्), a bird (or more probably a particular bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाहक|कठाहकः
कठाहक कठाहक, अस्, m. a gallinule. See<BR>दात्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिका
कठिका कठिका, f. chalk; the plant com-<BR>monly called Tulasī; [cf. कठिनी and कठिञ्जर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिञ्जर|कठिंजरः|कठिञ्जरः
कठिञ्जर कठिञ्जर, अस्, m. the tree Ocy-<BR>mum Sanctum, commonly Tulasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिन|कठिनं|कठिनः
कठिन कठिन, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कठ्), hard, stiff (opposed to मृदु); inflexible;<BR>violent, as pain; (अस्), m. a thicket; (आ), f. crystal-<BR>ized sugar, a sweetmeat made with refined sugar;<BR>(ई), f. chalk; (अम्), n. an earthen vessel for cooking<BR>(according to some also f.); [cf. Lat. catinum; Gr.<BR>κόφινος]<BR>—कठिन-ता, f. or कठिन-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>hardness, firmness; severity; difficulty, obscurity.<BR>—कठिन-पृष्ठ or कठिन-पृष्ठक, अस्,<BR>m. a tortoise.<BR>—कठिन-हृदय or कठिन-चित्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, hard-hearted, cruel, unkind.<BR>—कठिनान्तः-<BR>करण (˚न-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, harsh, cruel, severe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनिका
कठिनिका, f. chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

