कठेरु
कठेरु कठेरु, उस्, m., N. of Kuvera (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोर|कठोरः
कठोर कठोर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कठ्), hard, solid, stiff; offering resistance; sharp,<BR>piercing; severe, cruel, hard-hearted; full, complete,<BR>full-grown; full (as the moon); [cf. कठिन.]<BR>—क-<BR>ठोर-गिरि-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. a portion of the<BR>Brahmāṇḍa-Purāṇa.<BR>—कठोर-ता, f. or कठोर-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. hardness, firmness; severity, rigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोल|कठोलः
कठोल, अस्, आ, अम्, resisting, hard, &c., = कठोर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड्
कड् कड्, cl. 1. P. कडति, -डितुम्, to be<BR>confused or disturbed by pleasure or pain, to<BR>be elated or intoxicated; cl. 6. P. कडति, to con-<BR>sume; cl. 10. P. काडयति, -यितुम्, to break off a<BR>part, to tear, to separate or detach; to remove the<BR>chaff or husk of grain &c.; to preserve; [cf. कण्ड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड|कडः
कड, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. preceding), dumb,<BR>hoarse; ignorant, stupid; [cf. जड.]<BR>—कडङ्-कर<BR>or कडङ्-गर, अस्, m. straw, the stalks of various<BR>sorts of pulse &c. (rendering hoarse).<BR>—कडङ्करीय<BR>or कडङ्कर्य or कडङ्गरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>fed with straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडक|कडकं
कडक कडक, अम्, n. sea-salt obtained by<BR>evaporation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्ग|कडंगः|कडङ्गः
कडङ्ग कडङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कड् ?), a<BR>spirituous liquor, a kind of rum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडत्र|कडत्रं
कडत्र कडत्र, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>गड्), a kind of vessel or receptacle. See कलत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडन्दिका|कडंदिका
कडन्दिका कडन्दिका, f. science, = कलन्-<BR>दिका, कलिन्दिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडम्ब|कडंब|कडंबः|कडम्बः
कडम्ब कडम्ब, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कड्), the end or point; the stalk of a pot-herb; (ई),<BR>f. the pot-herb Convolvulus Repens. See कलम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडार|कडारः
कडार कडार, अस्, ई, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>गड्), tawny; (अस्), m. tawny (the colour); a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडितुल|कडितुलः
कडितुल कडितुल, अस्, m. a sword, a scymi-<BR>tar, a sacrificial knife; [cf. कटी-तल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड्ड्
कड्ड् कड्ड्, cl. 1. P. कड्डति, -डितुम्, to be<BR>hard, rough; to be harsh or severe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्
कण् कण्, cl. 1. P. कणति, चकाण, कणि-<BR>ष्यति, अकणीत् or अकाणीत्, कणितुम्, to<BR>become small; to sound, cry as in distress; to go or<BR>approach: Caus. काणयति, -यितुम्, aor. अचीकणत्<BR>and अचकाणत्, to sigh, sound; cl. 10. P. काणयति,<BR>यितुम्, to wink; to close the eye with the lids or<BR>lashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणित|कणितं
कणित, अम्, n. crying out with pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण|कणः
कण कण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कण्;<BR>according to others related to कना, कनिष्ठ,<BR>कनीयस्, कन्या, in all of which the notion of small-<BR>ness prevails), a grain, a single seed; a grain or<BR>particle of dust; flake (of snow); a drop of water;<BR>a spark of fire, the spark or facet of a gem; an ear<BR>of corn; an atom, a minute particle; small, minute;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of fly, commonly कुमीरापोका; long<BR>pepper; cummin seed; (ई), f. a drop, an atom; the<BR>plant Premna Spinosa or Longifolia; a kind of<BR>corn; see कणिका.<BR>—कण-गुग्गुलु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant; [cf. गन्धराज, स्वर्णकर्ण, and others.]<BR>—कण-जीर, अस्, m. a white kind of cummin seed.<BR>—कण-जीरक, अम्, n. small cummin seed.<BR>—कण-<BR>भक्ष, अस्, m. ‘eating atoms or grains’ (?), i. e. liv-<BR>ing on minute particles of food; a nickname of the<BR>philosopher Kaṇāda.<BR>—कण-भक्षक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of bird; [cf. भारिट, श्यामचतक, शैशिर.]<BR>—कण-भक्षण, अम्, n. the eating of grains.<BR>—कण-भुज्, क्, m. nickname of Kaṇāda; see<BR>कण-भक्ष.<BR>—कण-लाभ, अस्, m. a whirlpool.<BR>—कण-शस्, ind. in small parts, in minute particles.<BR>—कणान्न (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose food<BR>consists of grains.<BR>—कणान्न-ता, f. the state of one<BR>who is made to feed on grains (of rice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिक|कणिकः
कणिक, अस्, m. a grain, an ear of corn; the meal<BR>of parched wheat, the heart of wheat (commonly suji or<BR>semoule); a small particle, as a crystal &c.; an enemy;<BR>N. of a purificatory ceremony, viz, whirling round lamps<BR>at sacrificial rites [cf. नीराजन]; N. of a minister of<BR>king Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; (आ), f. a drop, an atom, a small<BR>particle; small, minute; the plant Premna Spinosa<BR>or Longifolia; a kind of corn or rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिश|कणिशं|कणिशः
कणिश, अस्, अम्, m. n. an ear or spike of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिष्ठ
कणिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. कनिष्ठ], the small-<BR>est, the most minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीक|कणीकं|कणीकः
कणीक, अस्, आ, अम्, small, diminutive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीयस्
कणीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, very small; young, younger;<BR>[cf. कनीयस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणप|कणपः
कणप कणप, अस्, m. a kind of spear or<BR>lance; (various readings have कणय and कनय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणभ|कणभः
कणभ कणभ, अस्, m. a kind of fly with a<BR>sting; [cf. कणा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाटीन|कणाटीनः
कणाटीन कणाटीन or कणाटीर or कणाटीरक,<BR>अस्, m. a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाद|कणादः
कणाद कणाद, अस्, m., N. of a celebrated<BR>sage, considered as the author of the Vaiśeṣika<BR>philosophy, a branch of the Nyāya. He is also<BR>called Kāśyapa, and considered as a Devarṣi; the<BR>nicknames कण-भक्ष and कण-भुज् refer to<BR>the etymology of this name कण-अद, ‘eating<BR>atoms or grains;’ a goldsmith; [cf. कलाद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणित|कणितं
कणित कणित. See under कण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीचि|कणीचिः
कणीचि कणीचि, इस्, and कनीची, f. a sound;<BR>a tree (पल्लविन्); a creeper in flower; the plant<BR>Abrus Precatorius; a cart; [cf. कनीचि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणूकय
कणूकय कणूकय, nom. P. (connected with<BR>rt. कण्), Ved. to desire to utter words of blame or<BR>censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणे
कणे कणे, ind. a particle expressing the<BR>satisfying of a desire.<BR>—कणे-हत्य, ind. (rt. हन्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-b" target="_blank">Page0197-b+ 78</a>]<BR>satiating one's self (e. g. कणे-हत्य पयः पिबति,<BR>he drinks milk till he is satiated.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणेर|कणेरः
कणेर कणेर, अस्, m., N. of a tree, Cascaria<BR>Ovata [cf. कर्णिकार]; (आ), f. a she-elephant; a<BR>courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणेरु|कणेरुः
कणेरु, उस्, m., N. of a tree; f. a she-elephant;<BR>a courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ट्|कंट्
कण्ट् कण्ट्, cl. 1. P. कण्टति, -टितुम्, to<BR>go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टक|कंटक|कंटकं|कंटकः|कण्टकः
कण्टक कण्टक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. कण्ट्?),<BR>a thorn; anything pointed, the point of a pin or<BR>needle, a prickle, sting; a fish-bone; a finger-nail [cf.<BR>कर-कण्टक]; the erection of the hair of the body<BR>in thrilling emotions, horripilation; any troublesome<BR>seditious person who is, as it were, a thorn to the<BR>state and an enemy of order and good government,<BR>a paltry foe (क्षुद्र-शत्रु); a sharp stinging<BR>pain, symptom of a disease; a vexing or injurious<BR>speech; any annoyance or source of vexation; a term<BR>in the Nyāya philosophy implying refutation of argu-<BR>ment, detection of error, &c.; impediment, obstacle;<BR>the first, fourth, seventh, and tenth lunar mansion;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a barber; N. of the horse of Śākya-<BR>muni (a wrong form for कण्ठक); N. of an Agra-<BR>hāra; (according to lexicographers also) a bamboo;<BR>a workshop, a manufactory; fault, defect; N. of<BR>Makara or the marine monster, the symbol of Kāma-<BR>deva; (ई), f. a species of Solanum. (कण्टक takes<BR>the form कण्ट at the beginning of some compounds<BR>and in कण्टल, कण्टालु, कण्टिन्; cf. Gr. κεντέω<BR>κεσ-τός, κέσ-τρον.)<BR>—कण्टक-द्रुम, अस्, m. a<BR>tree with thorns, a thorn bush; the Sālmali or silk-<BR>cotton tree, Bombax Heptaphyllum.<BR>—कण्टक-<BR>प्रावृता, f. the plant Aloe Perfoliata.<BR>—कण्टक-<BR>फल, अस्, m. the Jaka or bread-fruit tree, Arto-<BR>carpus Integrifolia; another plant, Ruellia Longifolia<BR>(commonly called Go-kṣura); the castor-oil tree;<BR>the Datura; the term is applicable to any plant the<BR>fruit of which is invested with a hairy or thorny coat;<BR>[cf. कण्टकि-फल.]<BR>—कण्टक-भुज्, क्, m. a camel<BR>(‘eating thorns’).<BR>—कण्टक-मर्दन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>treading down thorns; suppressing disturbances, an-<BR>noyances, &c.; (अम्), n. the act of beating or<BR>treading down thorns; suppressing disturbances &c.<BR>—कण्टक-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having thorns, thorny.<BR>—कण्टक-वृन्ताकी, f. the plant Solanum Jacquini,<BR>a species of nightshade with thorny leaves.<BR>—कण्-<BR>टक-श्रेणी, f. the Solanum Jacquini; a porcupine.<BR>—कण्टक-स्थली, f., N. of a region.<BR>—कण्टका-<BR>ख्य (˚क-आख्या), अस्, m. the plant Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—कण्टकागार (˚क-अग्˚), अस्, m. a kind of lizard;<BR>a porcupine.<BR>—कण्टकाशन (˚क-अश्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>camel (eating thorns, thistles, &c.; cf. कण्टक-<BR>भुज्).<BR>—कण्टकाष्ठील (˚क-अष्˚), अस्, m. a kind<BR>of fish, having many bones.<BR>—कण्टकी-कारी, f.,<BR>Ved. working in thorns.<BR>—कण्टकी-द्रुम, अस्,<BR>m. Acacia Catechu.<BR>—कण्टकी-फल = कण्टकि-<BR>फल.<BR>—कण्ट-कुरण्ट, अस्, m. = झिण्टी, Barleria<BR>Cristata.<BR>—कण्टकोद्धरण (˚क-उद्˚), अम्, n.<BR>weeding, extracting thorns &c.; removing annoy-<BR>ances; extirpating thieves, rogues, &c., or all national<BR>and public nuisances.<BR>—कण्ट-तनु, उस्, f. a species<BR>of Solanum.<BR>—कण्ट-दला, f. the plant Pandanus<BR>Odoratissimus.<BR>—कण्ट-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Flacourtia Sapida.<BR>—कण्टपत्त्र-फला, f., N. of<BR>a plant, = ब्रह्मदण्डी.<BR>—कण्ट-पाद = कण्ट-<BR>पत्त्र.<BR>—कण्ट-फल, अस्, m., N. of several plants,<BR>= गोक्षुर; bread-fruit tree, Datura Fastuosa, =<BR>लताकरञ्ज = तेजःखल (?); Ricinus Communis;<BR>(आ), f. = देवदालीलता.<BR>—कण्ट-वल्ली, f. = श्रीवल्ली-<BR>वृक्ष.<BR>—कण्ट-वृक्ष, अस्, m. = तेजःफल-<BR>वृक्ष.<BR>—कण्टा-फल, अस्, m. = कण्ट-फल.<BR>—कण्टार्तगला (˚ट-आर्˚), f. the plant Barleria<BR>Cærulea.<BR>—कण्टाह्वय (˚ट-आह्˚), अम्, n. the tube-<BR>rous root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकार|कंटकारः|कण्टकारः
कण्टकार, अस्, m., N. of a plant; (ई), f., N. of<BR>several plants, Solanum Jacquini; Bombax Hepta-<BR>phyllum, the silk-cotton tree; Flacourtia Sapida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकारिका|कंटकारिका
कण्टकारिका, f. Solanum Jacquini; also the fruit<BR>of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाल|कंटकालः|कण्टकालः
कण्टकाल, अस्, m. = कण्टक-फल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकालुक|कण्टकालुकः
कण्टकालुक, अस्, m. Hedysarum Alhagi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकित|कंटकित
कण्टकित, अस्, आ, अम्, thorny; covered with erect<BR>hairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिन्|कंटकिन्
कण्टकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, thorny, prickly; vexatious,<BR>annoying; (ई), m., N. of several thorny plants,<BR>Acacia Catechu; Vanguiera Spinosa; Ruellia Longi-<BR>folia; Zizyphus Jujuba, bamboo; a fish; (नी), f., N.<BR>of several plants, Solanum Jacquini, red amaranth.<BR>—कण्टकि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from a fish;<BR>produced by the Mimosa tree.<BR>—कण्टकि-फल, अस्,<BR>m. the Indian bread-fruit tree or Jaka; see कण्टक-<BR>फल.<BR>—कण्टकि-लता, f. a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिल|कंटकिल|कंटकिलः|कण्टकिलः
कण्टकिल, अस्, m. a thorny kind of bamboo,<BR>Bambusa Spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टल|कंटलः|कण्टलः
कण्टल, अस्, m. the plant Mimosa Arabica; gene-<BR>rally वावल, a tree yielding a species of Gum Arabic;<BR>the branches are prickly, whence the name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टालु|कंटालुः|कण्टालुः
कण्टालु, उस्, m., N. of different plants; Solanum<BR>Jacquini; another species of Solanum; a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टिन्|कंटिन्
कण्टिन्, ई, m., N. of several plants, Achyranthes<BR>Aspera; Acacia Catechu; Ruellia Longifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्|कंठ्
कण्ठ् कण्ठ्, cl. 1. P. A., 10. P. कण्ठति,<BR>-ते, -ठितुम्, कण्ठयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>mourn; to long for; [cf. उत्कण्ठ्; cf. also Gr.<BR>πένθος, πόθος; Lat. patior.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ|कंठ|कंठं|कंठः|कण्ठः
कण्ठ कण्ठ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. कण्), the throat, the neck (e. g. आकण्ठ-तृप्त,<BR>filled up to the throat, quite satiated); the voice (e. g.<BR>सन्न-कण्ठेन, with broken voice); sound, espe-<BR>cially guttural sound; the neck (of a pitcher or other<BR>vessel); the opening of the womb; metaphorically a<BR>bud on a stalk; immediate proximity; the space of<BR>an inch from the edge of the hole in which sacrificial<BR>fire is deposited; the tree Vanguiera Spinosa; N. of<BR>a Maharṣi; (ई), f. neck, throat; a rope or leather<BR>round the neck of a horse; a necklace, a collar; [cf.<BR>अधर-कण्ठ, उत्-कण्ठा; cf. also Lat. collum?].<BR>—कण्ठ-कुब्ज, अस्, m. a kind of fever.<BR>—कण्ठ-<BR>कुब्ज-प्रतीकार, अस्, m. the cure of the preceding<BR>disease.<BR>—कण्ठ-कूणिका, f. the Vīṇā or Indian lute.<BR>—कण्ठ-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, reaching or extending to<BR>the throat.<BR>—कण्ठ-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being at or<BR>in the throat; approaching or reaching the throat.<BR>—कण्ठ-तट, अस्, अम्, m. n. the side of the neck.<BR>—कण्ठ-तलासिका (˚ल-अस्˚?), f. the leather or<BR>rope passing round the neck of a horse.<BR>—कण्ठ-<BR>दघ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, reaching to the neck.<BR>—कण्ठ-<BR>धान, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—कण्ठ-नीडक,<BR>अस्, m. Falco Cheela; a kite.<BR>—कण्ठ-नीलक, अस्,<BR>m. a torch, a whisp of lighted straw &c. (= उल्का,<BR>commonly मसाल).<BR>—कण्ठ-पण्डित, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a poet.<BR>—कण्ठ-पाशक, अस्, m. a halter; a<BR>rope passing round an elephant's neck.<BR>—कण्ठ-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. a rope tied round an elephant's neck.<BR>—कण्ठ-भूषा, f. a collar or short necklace.<BR>—कण्ठ-मणि, इस्, m. a jewel worn on the throat,<BR>a dear or beloved object.<BR>—कण्ठ-रव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author; N. of a certain medical writer.<BR>—कण्ठ-लग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened or suspended<BR>round the throat; clinging to, embracing.<BR>—कण्ठ-<BR>लता, f. a collar; a horse's halter.<BR>—कण्ठ-वर्तिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, being in the throat; [cf. कण्ठ-गत.]<BR>—कण्ठ-शालूक, अम्, n. a hard tumour in the<BR>throat.<BR>—कण्ठ-शुण्डी, f. swelling of the tonsils.<BR>—कण्ठ-शोष, अस्, m. drying the throat; fruitless<BR>expostulation.<BR>—कण्ठ-श्रुत्य्-उपनिषद्, त्, f., N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad belonging to the Atharva-veda.<BR>—कण्ठ-सज्जन, अम्, n. hanging on or round<BR>the throat.<BR>—कण्ठ-सूत्र, अम्, n. a kind of em-<BR>brace.<BR>—कण्ठ-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, sticking in the<BR>throat; being in or upon the throat; guttural; being<BR>in the mouth ready to be repeated by rote, learnt<BR>and ready to be recited.<BR>—कण्ठागत (˚ठ-आग्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, come to the throat (as the breath or soul<BR>of a dying person).<BR>—कण्ठाग्नि (˚ठ-अग्˚), इस्, m.<BR>a bird (digesting in the throat or gizzard).<BR>—कण्ठा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">Page0198-a+ 75</a>]<BR>भरण (˚ठ-आभ्˚), अम्, n. a neck-ornament, a<BR>necklace; a shorter N. of the work called Sarasvatī-<BR>kaṇṭhābharaṇa.<BR>—कण्ठाभरण-दर्पण, अस्,<BR>m. a commentary of Rāmasiṃha-deva on the last.<BR>—कण्ठाभरण-मार्जन, a commentary by<BR>Hari-nātha on the same work.<BR>—कण्ठावसक्त<BR>(˚ठ-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, clinging to the neck, em-<BR>bracing.<BR>—कण्ठी-रव, अस्, m. a lion (roaring from<BR>the throat); an elephant in rut; a pigeon; (ई), f. the<BR>plant Gendarussa Vulgaris.<BR>—कण्ठे-काल, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva (‘blue on the neck’).<BR>—कण्ठे-<BR>विद्ध, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कण्ठेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ (˚ठ-ईश्˚), N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कण्ठोक्त (˚ठ-<BR>उक्˚), अम्, n. personal testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठक
कण्ठक, अस्, m., N. of a horse of Śākya-muni;<BR>[cf. कण्टक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतस्|कंठतस्
कण्ठतस्, ind. from the throat, with distinct<BR>words, explicitly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठिका|कंठिका
कण्ठिका, f. a necklace of one string or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठिन्|कंठिन्
कण्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belonging to the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्य|कंठ्य|कण्ठ्यः
कण्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being at or in the throat;<BR>suitable to the throat; belonging to the throat, pro-<BR>nounced from the throat, guttural; (according to a<BR>Prātiśākhya the guttural letters are अ, ह्, and the<BR>जिह्वामूलीय; according to Pāṇini अ, क्, ख्, ग्, घ्,<BR>न्, and ह्; according to Vopadeva also ए.)<BR>—कण्ठ्य-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, m. a guttural letter.<BR>—कण्ठ्य-स्वर,<BR>अस्, m. a guttural vowel, i. e. अ and आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाल|कंठाल|कंठालः|कण्ठालः
कण्ठाल कण्ठाल, अस्, m. a boat, a ship; a<BR>hoe, a spade; war; an esculent root, Arum Campa-<BR>nulatum; a camel [cf. कण्टकाशन and कण्डोल];<BR>a churning-vessel; (आ), f. a churning-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठील|कंठील|कंठीलः|कण्ठीलः
कण्ठील, अस्, m. a camel; (अस्, आ), m. f. a churn-<BR>ing-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्|कंड्
कण्ड् कण्ड्, cl. 1. P. A. कण्डति, -ते, -डि-<BR>तुम्, to be glad; cl. 10. P. कण्डयति,<BR>यितुम्, to separate the chaff from the grain; to<BR>protect; [cf. कड्: cf. also Lith. kándu, ‘to bite;’<BR>Cambro-Brit. cat, ‘a fragment.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डन|कंडन|कंडनं|कण्डनं
कण्डन, अम्, n. threshing, separating the chaff<BR>from the grain in mortar; that which is separated<BR>from the grain, chaff; (ई), f. a wooden bowl or<BR>mortar in which the cleaning or threshing of grain<BR>is performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डरा|कंडरा
कण्डरा कण्डरा, f. a sinew (of which six-<BR>teen are considered to be in the human body); a<BR>principal vessel of the body, a large artery, vein, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डरीक
कण्डरीक कण्डरीक, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kauśika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डानक|कंडानकः|कण्डानकः
कण्डानक कण्डानक, अस्, m., N. of a servant<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डिका|कंडिका
कण्डिका कण्डिका, f. a short section, the<BR>shortest subdivision in the arrangement of certain<BR>Vedic compositions, as in the White Yajur-veda;<BR>[cf. काण्ड and काण्डिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डु|कंडु|कंडुः|कण्डुः
कण्डु कण्डु, उस्, m. f. or usually कण्डू, ऊस्,<BR>f. (fr. rt. कण्ड्), scratching; itching, the itch; (उस्),<BR>m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—कण्डू-करी, f. the plant Mu-<BR>cuna Pruritus.<BR>—कण्डू-घ्न, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Cathartocarpus (Cassia) Fistula; white mustard.<BR>—कण्डूमका, f. (मका = मक्षिका or मशक?),<BR>a kind of insect with a poisonous bite.<BR>—कण्डू-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, scratching, itching.<BR>—कण्ड्व्-आदि,<BR>अयस्, m. pl. the nominal verbs, in the list of which<BR>कण्डूयति is the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुक
कण्डुक, अस्, m., N. of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुर|कंडुर|कण्डुरः
कण्डुर, अस्, आ, अम्, scratching; (अस्), m. the<BR>plant Momordica Charantia, a species of reed; (आ), f.<BR>the plants Mucuna Pruritus and Aty-amlaparnī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूति|कंडूति|कंडूतिः|कण्डूतिः
कण्डूति, इस्, f. scratching; itching, the itch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूय
कण्डूय, nom. P. A. कण्डूयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>to scratch, scrape, rub: Desid. कण्डूयियिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयत्
कण्डूयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, scratching, rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयन|कंडूयन|कण्डूयनं
कण्डूयन, अम्, n. scratching, scraping, rubbing,<BR>itching; (ई), f. a brush for rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनक|कंडूयनक|कण्डूयनकः
कण्डूयनक, अस्, ई, अम्, scratching, scraping;<BR>(अस्), m. a tickler, one who tickles or scratches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयमान
कण्डूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूया|कंडूया
कण्डूया, f. scratching, itching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयित|कंडूयितं
कण्डूयित, अम्, n. scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयितृ|कंडूयितृ
कण्डूयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, scratching, a scratcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूरा|कंडूरा
कण्डूरा, f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus; ‘what<BR>causes itching,’ alluding to the irritating property of<BR>this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूल|कंडूल|कण्डूलः
कण्डूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having or feeling the itch,<BR>itchy; (अस्), m. an esculent root (Arum Campanu-<BR>latum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोल|कंडोल|कंडोलः|कण्डोलः
कण्डोल कण्डोल, अस्, m. a basket for holding<BR>grain, made of bamboo or canes; a safe, any place<BR>in which provisions are kept; a camel; [cf. कण्-<BR>ठाल;] (ई), f. the lute of the Cāṇḍāla; [cf. कटोल,<BR>गण्डोल.]<BR>—कण्डोल-वीणा, f. the lute of the Cāṇ-<BR>ḍāla, a vulgar lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलक|कंडोलकः|कण्डोलकः
कण्डोलक, अस्, m. a basket, a safe, a store-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोष|कंडोष|कंडोषः|कण्डोषः
कण्डोष कण्डोष, अस्, m. a caterpillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्व|कण्वं|कण्वः
कण्व कण्व, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कण्), deaf; (अस्), m., Ved. a peculiar class of evil<BR>spirits, against whom charms are used; a praiser;<BR>N. of a renowned Ṛṣi, author of several hymns of<BR>the Ṛg-veda; he is called a son of Ghora and is said<BR>to belong to the family of Aṅgiras; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>family or descendants of Kaṇva; (besides the cele-<BR>brated Ṛṣi there occur a Kaṇva Nārṣada, Kaṇva Śrā-<BR>yasa, Kaṇva Kāśyapa; the founder of a Vedic school;<BR>a prince, son of Pratiratha and father of Medhātithi;<BR>a son of Apratiratha; a son of Ajamīḍha and father<BR>of Medhātithi; the author of a law-book; a gram-<BR>marian.) The name कण्व was perhaps originally<BR>mythic, and afterwards transferred to a human<BR>family, as was the case with the name Aṅgiras;<BR>(अम्), n. sin, evil.<BR>—कण्व-जम्भन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. consuming or destroying the evil spirits called<BR>Kaṇvas.<BR>—कण्व-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very much<BR>like Kaṇva, very wise.<BR>—कण्व-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. prepared after the manner of the Kaṇvas (as<BR>Soma); (Sāy.) united with praisers or with the<BR>Kaṇvas (as Indra).<BR>—कण्व-वत्, ind. like Kaṇva.<BR>—कण्व-सखि, आ, m., Ved. a friend of the Kaṇvas,<BR>friendly disposed towards them.<BR>—कण्व-होतृ, ता,<BR>m., Ved. one whose Hotṛ priest is a Kaṇva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वाय
कण्वाय, nom. A. कण्वा-यते, -यितुम्, to do<BR>mischief; perhaps originally ‘to act like a Kaṇva or<BR>evil spirit.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत|कतः
कत कत, अस्, m. the clearing nut plant;<BR>see the following; N. of a Muni or saint.<BR>—कत-<BR>फल, अस्, m. the clearing nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतक|कतकः
कतक, अस्, m. the clearing nut plant, Strychnos<BR>Potatorum, (one of the seeds of this plant being rubbed<BR>upon the inside of the water-jars used in Bengal occa-<BR>sions a precipitation of the earthly particles diffused<BR>through the water and removes them.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम
कतम कतम, अस्, आ, अत् (superlative of 2. क;<BR>declined as a pronom., Gram. 236), who or which of<BR>many ? (e. g. कतमेन पथा यातास् ते, by which<BR>road have they gone?). कतम is often a mere<BR>strengthened substitute for क, the superlative affix<BR>imparting emphasis. Hence it may occasionally be<BR>used for ‘who or which of two?’ (e. g. तयोः कत-<BR>मस्मै, to which of these two ?). It may option-<BR>ally be compounded with the word to which it refers<BR>(e. g. कतमः कठः or कतम-कठः, which<BR>Kaṭha out of many?). When followed by च and<BR>preceded by यतम an indefinite expression is<BR>formed equivalent to ‘any whosoever,’ ‘any whatso-<BR>ever,’ &c. (e. g. यतमद् एव कतमच् च विद्यात्,<BR>he may know anything whatsoever). In negative<BR>sentences कतम with चन or कतम with अपि<BR>= not even one, none at all (e. g. न कतमच्-<BR>चनाहः, not even on a single day, on no day at<BR>all). In addition to the above uses कतम is said to<BR>mean ‘best,’ ‘excessively good-looking;’ [cf. 3. क.]<BR>—कतमोरग (˚म-उर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतर
कतर, अस्, आ, अत् (comparative of 2. क; declined<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">Page0198-c+ 75</a>]<BR>as a pronom., Gram. 236), who or which of two?<BR>whether of two? Analogously to कतम above<BR>कतर may occasionally be used to express ‘who or<BR>which of many’ (e. g. कतरस्यां दिशि, in which<BR>quarter ?), and may optionally be compounded with<BR>the word to which it refers (e. g. कतरः कठः<BR>or कतर-कठः). In negative sentences कतर<BR>with चन = neither of the two (e. g. न कतरश्-<BR>चन जिग्ये, neither of the two was conquered;<BR>[cf. Gr. πότερος, κότερος; Goth. hvathar; Eng.<BR>whether; Lat. uter; Old Germ. huedar; Slav.<BR>kotoryi.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतरतस्
कतरतस्, ind. on which of the two sides ?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
1. कति (fr. 2. क, declined in pl. only, Gram. 227.<BR>अ, all the cases except the nom. voc. and acc. taking<BR>terminations, whereas the correlative इति has become<BR>fixed as an indeclinable adverb), how many? quot?<BR>several (e. g. कति देवाः, how many gods? कति<BR>व्यापादयति कति वा ताडयति, some he kills and<BR>some he strikes). In the sense of ‘several,’ ‘some,’<BR>कति is generally followed by चिद् or अपि (e. g. कतिचिद्<BR>अहानि, for several or some days). कति may be used<BR>as an adverb with चिद् in the sense of ‘oftentimes,’<BR>‘much,’ ‘in many ways’ (e. g. कतिचित् स्तुतः, much<BR>or often praised). कति-कृत्वस्, ind. how many<BR>times? कति-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of how many kinds?<BR>कति-शस्, how many at a time?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिथ
कतिथ, अस्, ई, अम्, to what place or stage or<BR>degree advanced? (the how-maniest?) with चिद् =<BR>advanced to such and such a point (e. g. अहं<BR>कतिथश्चिद् आस, I was so far advanced on to such<BR>and such a point).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिधा
कतिधा, ind. in how many places? in how many<BR>parts? how often? कतिधा चित्, everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपय|कतिपयः
कतिपय, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (pl. m. ए and आस्),<BR>several, some; a certain number, so many; कति-<BR>पयेन अहर्गणेन, after some days; also कति-<BR>पयैर् अहोभिः, कतिपयाहस्य, &c.<BR>—कतिप-<BR>येन or कतिपयात्, ind. with some exertion; [the<BR>affix पय has been compared with Gr. ποῖος]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपयथ
कतिपयथ, अस्, ई, अम्, advanced to a certain<BR>place or degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमाल|कतमालः
कतमाल कतमाल, अस्, m. fire; the right<BR>form is खतमाल; [cf. also कचमाल and कर-<BR>माल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
कति 2. कति, इस्, m., N. of a sage, son of<BR>Viśvā-mitra and ancestor of Kātyāyana. (For 1. see<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिक
कतिक or कतिका, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतीमुष
कतीमुष कतीमुष, अम्, n., N. of an Agra-<BR>hāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्ताशब्द|कत्ताशब्दः
कत्ताशब्द कत्ता-शब्द, अस्, m. the rattling<BR>sound of dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तृण|कत्तृणं
कत्तृण कत्-तृण, कत्-तोय, कत्-त्रि. See<BR>under 2. कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थ्
कत्थ् कत्थ्, cl. 1. A. कत्थते, -थितुम्,<BR>to boast; to mention with praise, to praise<BR>or celebrate; to flatter or coax; to abuse, revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थन
कत्थन, अस्, आ, अम्, boasting, praising; a boaster,<BR>praiser; (अम्), n. boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्पय
कत्पय कत्-पय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. कद् and<BR>पय fr. पी = प्यै), Ved. swelling, rising; (Sāy.)<BR>one whose waters cause happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्र्
कत्र् कत्र्, cl. 10. P. कत्रयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>loosen, slacken, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्सवर|कत्सवरं
कत्सवर कत्सवर, अम्, n. the shoulder,<BR>the shoulder-blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्
कथ् कथ् (this rt. is perhaps connected<BR>with कथम्), cl. 10. P., ep. also A.<BR>कथयति, -ते, aor. अचकथत् or अचीकथत्, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to converse with any one (with inst. c. alone or<BR>after सह); to tell, relate, narrate, report, inform,<BR>speak about, declare, explain (with acc. of the thing<BR>or person spoken about); to describe; to denounce,<BR>betray; to suppose, state; Pass. कथ्यते, to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">Page0199-a+ 81</a>]<BR>called; be regarded or considered as: Desid. चिक-<BR>थयिषति, to desire to tell; [cf. Goth. qvath;<BR>Eng. quoth and quote; Gr. κωτίλος, κωτίλλω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक, अस्, आ, अम्, a narrator, a relater, one<BR>who recites a story or who publicly reads and ex-<BR>pounds the Purāṇas &c., one who speaks or tells;<BR>(अस्, आ), m. f. the speaker of a prologue or mono-<BR>logue; a professional story-teller; chief actor; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन|कथनं
कथन, अस्, आ, अम्, telling, talkative; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of telling, narration, relating, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथनीय
कथनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be said, to be told or<BR>declared; worthy of relation, to be named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथयान
कथयान, अस्, आ, अम्, telling, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथयितव्य
कथयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be told, to be men-<BR>tioned, to be communicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
1. कथा, f. conversation, speech, tale; a fable, a<BR>feigned story; talk, mention; (in phil.) disputation;<BR>का कथा (with gen. or more commonly with loc.<BR>and sometimes with प्रति), what should one<BR>say of? how should one speak of? (e. g. एको ऽपि<BR>कृच्छ्राद् वर्तेत, भूयसां कथैव का, even<BR>one person would live with difficulty, what should<BR>one say of many? i. e. how much more many?).<BR>—कथाक्रम (˚था-आक्˚), अस्, m. the commence-<BR>ment of a conversation.<BR>—कथा-छल, अम्, n. the<BR>device of a fable.<BR>—कथा-जव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—कथानुराग (˚था-अन्˚), अस्, m. attention,<BR>taking pleasure in a discourse.<BR>—कथान्त (˚था-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. end of a conversation.<BR>—कथान्तर<BR>(˚था-अन्˚), अम्, n. the course of a conversation.<BR>—कथा-पीठ, N. of the first Lambaka or book of<BR>the Kathā-sarit-sāgara.<BR>—कथा-प्रबन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>a narrative, a tale, a composed story, a fiction.<BR>—क-<BR>था-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m. connection of speeches or<BR>discourse, talking, conversation, speaking to or with,<BR>rumour, report; (अस्, आ, अम्), talkative, talking much<BR>and foolishly, half-witted, foolish; a conjuror, a dealer<BR>in antidotes &c.<BR>—कथा-प्राण, अस्, m. an actor,<BR>the speaker of a prologue or monologue, the intro-<BR>ducer of a drama; a professed story-teller.<BR>—कथा-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of tales.<BR>—कथा-मुख,<BR>अम्, n. the introduction to a tale; N. of the second<BR>Lambaka or book of the Kathā-sarit-sāgara.<BR>—कथा-<BR>योग, अस्, m. conversation, talk, discourse.<BR>—कथा-<BR>रम्भ (˚था-आर्˚), अस्, m. beginning of a story or<BR>narrative, story-telling.<BR>—कथारम्भ-काल (˚था-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, m. story-beginning-time.<BR>—कथाराम<BR>(˚था-आर्˚), अस्, m. garden of fable.<BR>—कथार्णव<BR>(˚था-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a collection of stories at-<BR>tributed to Śivadāsa.<BR>—कथालाप (˚था-आल्˚), अस्,<BR>m. speech, conversation.<BR>—कथावशेष (˚था-अव्˚),<BR>or कथा-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, one of whom only the<BR>narrative remains, i. e. deceased, dead; कथाव-<BR>शेषतां गतः, deceased, dead.<BR>—कथा-विरक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, reserved, taciturn, disliking conversation.<BR>—कथा-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. a collection of tales or<BR>fables.<BR>—कथा-सरित्-सागर, अस्, m. the ocean of<BR>the rivers of stories; title of a work of Somadeva.<BR>—कथोदय (˚था-उद्˚), अस्, m. the beginning of<BR>a tale, introduction to a tale.<BR>—कथोद्घात (˚था-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. the opening of a drama by the character<BR>that first enters overhearing and repeating the last<BR>words of the prelude.<BR>—कथोपकथन (˚था-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. conversation, conference, narration.<BR>—कथो-<BR>पाख्यान (˚था-उप्˚), अम्, n. narration, narrative,<BR>relation, telling a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानक|कथानकं
कथानक, अम्, n. a small tale; [cf. क्रयाणक,<BR>भयानक, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथापय
कथापय, nom. P. कथापयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>tell, relate, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथिक|कथिकः
कथिक, अस्, ई, अम्, a narrator, a relater, a story-<BR>teller by profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथित|कथितः
कथित, अस्, आ, अम्, told, said, related; (अम्), n.<BR>a conversation, discourse.<BR>—कथित-पद, अम्, n.<BR>repetition, tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथीकृ
कथी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to transform into a tale.<BR>—कथी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>transformed into a tale, deceased, dead (e. g. कथी-<BR>कृतं वपुः, a body of which one can only give<BR>a history, a deceased body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्य
कथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken about, to be<BR>told, fit to be mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्यमान
कथ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being told or mentioned,<BR>under narration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् कथम् (fr. 2. क), ind. how? in what<BR>manner? whence? (e. g. कथम् एतत्, how is that?<BR>कथम् इदानीम्, how now? what is now to be<BR>done? कथम् मारात्मके त्वयि विश्वासः, how<BR>can there be reliance on thee of murderous mind?<BR>कथम् उत्सृज्य त्वां गच्छेयम्, how can I go<BR>away deserting you? कथम् बुद्ध्वा भविष्यति<BR>सा, how will she be when she awakes? कथम् मृ-<BR>त्युः प्रभवति वेदविदाम्, whence is it that death<BR>has power over those that know the Veda? कथम्<BR>अवगम्यते, whence is it inferred?). Sometimes<BR>कथम् merely introduces an interrogation (e. g. क-<BR>थम् आत्मानं निवेदयामि कथं वा आत्मा-<BR>पहारं करोमि, shall I declare myself or shall I<BR>withdraw ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् is often found in connection with the<BR>particles इव, नाम, नु, स्विद्, which appear to gene-<BR>ralize the interrogation (how possibly? &c.); with नु<BR>it sometimes = किमु or कुतस् (e. g. कथं नु, how<BR>much more! न कथं नु, how much less!).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् is often connected, like किम्, with the<BR>particles चन, चिद्, and अपि, which give an inde-<BR>finite sense to the interrogative (e. g. कथं चन,<BR>in no way, not at all). When not itself negative<BR>कथं चन = in some way, some how; scarcely,<BR>with difficulty; न कथं चन, in no way; क-<BR>थञ्चित्, some how or other, by some means or<BR>other, in any way, with some difficulty, scarcely, in<BR>a moderate degree, a little; न कथञ्चित्, not at all,<BR>in no way whatever; न कथञ्चिद् न, in no way<BR>not, i. e. most decidedly; यथा कथञ्चित्, in any<BR>way whatsoever; कथञ्चिद् यदि जीवति, it is with<BR>difficulty that he lives; कथम् अपि, some how or<BR>other, with some difficulty, scarcely, a little; कथम्<BR>अपि न, by no means, not at all. In addition to<BR>the above senses lexicographers assert that कथम्<BR>may imply ‘amazement, surprise, pleasure, abuse;’<BR>[with कथम् cf. Gr. κατά.]<BR>At the beginning of an adjective compound कथम्<BR>may have the same sense as किम्.<BR>—कथं-रूप,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of what shape ?<BR>—कथं-वीर्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of what power?<BR>—कथङ्-कथिक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (fr. कथम् कथम्), one who is always<BR>asking questions, an inquisitive person.<BR>—कथङ्-<BR>कथिक-ता, f. questioning, inquiring, inquisitiveness.<BR>—कथङ्कथित (?), अस्, m. an interrogant, one<BR>who puts questions.<BR>—कथन्-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, how<BR>acting.<BR>—कथङ्-कारम्, ind. in which manner?<BR>—कथन्-ता, f. enquiry, question, demand.<BR>—क-<BR>थम्-प्रमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, of what measure?<BR>—क-<BR>थम्-भाव, अस्, m. what state?<BR>—कथम्-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, how being? of what kind?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
2. कथा, ind. (for कथम्), Ved. how? whence?<BR>why? Sometimes merely a particle of interrogation<BR>(e. g. कथा शृणोति इन्द्रः, does Indra hear?<BR>यथा कथा च, in any way whatsoever).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् 1. कद्, cl. 1. A. कदते, -दितुम्, perf.<BR>चकाद, to be confused, suffer mentally; to<BR>grieve; to confound; to kill or hurt; to call; to cry<BR>or shed tears; चकाद कदनम्, he accomplished a<BR>destruction; [cf. Gr. κῆδας; Goth. hatan: cf. also<BR>कन्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन|कदनं
कदन, अम्, n. destruction, killing, slaughter; war,<BR>sin.<BR>—कदन-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—क-<BR>दन-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, loving slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् 2. कद्, ind. (originally the neuter form<BR>of the interrogative pronoun क), Ved. a particle of<BR>interrogation, where? कद् is used, like किम्, with the<BR>particles चन and चिद् (e. g. न कच्चन उपब्दिः<BR>शृण्वे रथस्य, not at any time or in any manner<BR>is heard the noise of thy chariot; वेति दिवः-कच्चिद्<BR>आ, he comes from heaven now and then).<BR>—कच्चिद् is<BR>sometimes used, like the simple कद्, as a particle of in-<BR>terrogation (e. g. कच्चिद् दृष्टा त्वया दमयन्ती,<BR>was Damayantī seen by thee?). कच्चिद् may some-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">Page0199-c+ 77</a>]<BR>times be equivalent to ‘I hope that’ (e. g. व्याधिर् न<BR>कच्चित् ते शरीरम् प्रतिबाधते, I hope no illness<BR>afflicts thy body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् at the beginning of a compound marks the<BR>uselessness, badness or defectiveness of anything; as in<BR>the following examples.<BR>—कत्-तृण, अम्, n. a fragrant<BR>grass; the plant Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—कत्-तोय, अम्, n.<BR>an intoxicating drink, wine or vinous spirit.<BR>—कत्-त्रि,<BR>अयस्, m. pl. three inferior articles.<BR>—कद्-अक्षर,<BR>अम्, n. a bad letter, bad writing.<BR>—कद्-अग्नि, इस्, m.<BR>some or a little fire.<BR>—कद्-अध्वन्, आ, m. a bad road.<BR>—कद् अन्न, अम्, n. bad food.<BR>—कद्-अपत्य, अम्,<BR>n. bad posterity; bad children.<BR>—कद्-अभ्यास, अस्,<BR>m. a bad habit.<BR>—कद्-अर्थ, अस्, m. a useless thing;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), useless, unmeaning; having what purpose<BR>or aim?<BR>—कदर्थन, अम्, आ, n. f. tormenting,<BR>torture.<BR>—कदर्थय, nom. P. कदर्थयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to despise, to estimate lightly; to torment, tor-<BR>ture, trouble.<BR>—कदर्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, despised,<BR>disdained, rejected; rendered useless.<BR>—कदर्थी-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>disdain, despise, to estimate at small value.<BR>—क-<BR>दर्थी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, despised, disdained, ren-<BR>dered useless and unavailing.<BR>—कद्-अर्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, avaricious, miserly; little, insignificant, mean;<BR>bad, disagreeable; (अस्), m. a miser.<BR>—कदर्य-ता,<BR>f. or कदर्य-त्व, अम्, n. avarice; insignificance;<BR>badness.<BR>—कदर्य-भाव, अस्, m. avarice, stingi-<BR>ness.<BR>—कद्-अश्व, अस्, m. a bad horse.<BR>—कद्-आकार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ill-formed, ugly.<BR>—कद्-आख्य, अम्, n.<BR>the plant Costus Speciosus (‘having a bad name,’<BR>i. e. कुष्ठ or दुष्ट).<BR>—कद्-आचार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wicked, abandoned, following evil practices;<BR>(अस्), m. bad conduct.<BR>—कद्-इन्द्रिय, आणि, n. pl.<BR>bad organs of sense.<BR>—कद्-उष्ट्र, अस्, m. a bad<BR>camel.<BR>—कद्-उष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, tepid, lukewarm;<BR>(अम्), n. warmth, lukewarmness, gentle warmth; [cf.<BR>कवोष्ण, कोष्ण.]<BR>—कद्-रथ, अस्, m. a bad<BR>carriage.<BR>—कद्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing the word<BR>क.<BR>—कद्-वद, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking ill or inaccu-<BR>rately or indistinctly; contemptible, vile, base.<BR>—कल्-<BR>लोल, see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद|कदः
कद क-द, अस्, m. a cloud. See 4. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक|कदकं|कदकः
कदक कदक, अस्, m. an awning; [cf.<BR>कन्दक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन|कदनं
कदन कदन. See under 1. कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्ब|कदंब|कदम्बं|कदंबः|कदम्बः
कदम्ब कदम्ब, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 1.<BR>कद्), the tree Nauclea Cadamba, a tree with orange-<BR>coloured fragrant blossoms; the mustard-seed plant,<BR>Sinapis Dichotoma; a kind of grass, Andropogon<BR>Serratus; a particular mineral substance; turmeric;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a plant; (अम्), n. a multitude, an as-<BR>semblage or collection.<BR>—कदम्ब-पुष्पा or ई, f.<BR>a plant, the flowers of which resemble those of the<BR>Kadamba, commonly called Mandīri.<BR>—कदम्ब-<BR>वायु, उस्, m. a fragrant breeze.<BR>—कदम्बानिल<BR>(˚ब-अन्˚), अस्, m. a fragrant breeze, spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बक|कदंबक|कदम्बकं|कदंबकः|कदम्बकः
कदम्बक, अस्, m. the plant Nauclea Cadamba,<BR>Sinapis Dichotoma, = हरिद्रु; (अम्), n. a multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बद|कदंबदः|कदम्बदः
कदम्बद, अस्, m. the mustard-seed plant, Si-<BR>napis Dichotoma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर|कदरं|कदरः
कदर कदर, अस्, m. a saw; an iron goad<BR>for guiding an elephant; N. of a tree, which may be<BR>substituted for Khadira as a sacrificial post; a white<BR>sort of Mimosa; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a corn, a callosity<BR>of the feet caused by external friction; (अम्), n. coagu-<BR>lated milk; [cf. कङ्कर, कच्चर, कटुर, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदल|कदलः
कदल कदल, अस्, ई, m. f. the plantain tree<BR>(Musa Sapientum), called also banana. It has a soft<BR>perishable stem, poetically a symbol of the frailty of<BR>human life; (आ), f., N. of several plants, Pistia Stra-<BR>tiotes; Bombax Heptaphyllum; (ई), f. a kind of deer,<BR>the hide of which is used as a seat &c.; a flag, a<BR>banner, a flag carried by an elephant.<BR>—कदली-<BR>स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a kind of illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलक|कदलकः
कदलक, अस्, m. the plantain or banana tree,<BR>Musa Sapientum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलिन्
कदलिन्, ई, m. a kind of antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीक्षता
कदलीक्षता कदलीक्षता, f. a sort of cu-<BR>cumber; a fine woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदा
कदा कदा, ind. (fr. 2. क), when? at what<BR>time? (with following fut. or pres. tense); how?<BR>कदा is sometimes found with a following च and<BR>preceding यदा (e. g. यदा कदा च सुनवाम<BR>सोमम्, let us press out the Soma as often as may<BR>be or at all times); कदा चन, (though originally<BR>negative, generally = ) at some time, one day, once;<BR>न कदा चन, never at any time; कदा चित्, at<BR>some time or other, sometimes, once; न कदा चित्,<BR>never; कदापि (कदा-अपि), sometimes, now and<BR>then; न कदापि, never; [cf. Gr. κοτέ and ποτέ<BR>Lat. quando; Lith. kadà; Slav. kogda.]<BR>—कदा-<BR>मत्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदूहि
कदूहि कदूहि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रु|कद्रुः
कद्रु कद्रु, उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कव्), tawny, reddish-brown; (उस्), m. tawny (the<BR>colour); N. of a Ṛṣi; (ऊस्), f. a Soma vessel (?); a<BR>personification described in certain legends which re-<BR>late to the bringing down of the Soma from heaven,<BR>according to the Brāhmaṇas ‘the earth personified;’ N.<BR>of a daughter of Dakṣa, wife of Kaśyapa and mother<BR>of the Nāgas or the serpent-race; N. of a plant.<BR>—क-<BR>द्रु-पुत्र, अस्, m. or कद्रु-सुत, अस्, m. a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्र्यच्
कद्र्यच् कद्र्यच्, आङ्, कद्रीची, अक् (fr. 2. क<BR>and rt. अञ्च्), Ved. turned towards what?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्वत्|कद्वन्त्
कद्वत् कद्-वत्. See under 2. कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्वर|कद्वरं
कद्वर कद्वर, अम्, n. whey; buttermilk<BR>mixed with water; [cf. कङ्कर, कच्चर, कटुर,<BR>कट्वर, and कदर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कधप्रिय
कधप्रिय कध-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, or कध-<BR>प्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. friendly towards whom?; (Sāy.)<BR>fond of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्
कन् कन्, cl. 1. P., Ved. कनति, चकान,<BR>अकानीत्, कन्तुम् (of the simple root only<BR>the aor. is used), to be satisfied; to be contented<BR>with, to accept anything (acc.) with satisfaction;<BR>(Sāy.) to love, wish, desire; to shine; to go: Intens.<BR>चाकन्ति, impf. चाकन्, perf. चाकन and चके, to be<BR>satisfied, to like, enjoy anything (with loc., gen.); to<BR>inst.); to be liked, wished, desired (with gen.); to<BR>strive after, seek, desire (with acc. or dat.); [cf. कम्<BR>and चन्: cf. also Lat. canus, caneo, candeo, can-<BR>dela; Hib. canu, ‘full moon.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन
कन कन, a substitute for अल्प, little,<BR>small, not occurring alone, but regarded as the source<BR>of the following derivatives; [cf. कण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनय
कनय, nom. P. कनयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>less or smaller, diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कना
कना, f., Ved. a girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
कनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, the smallest, least (opposed<BR>to भूयिष्ठ); the youngest, younger born (opposed<BR>to ज्येष्ठ and वृद्ध); (आ), f. (with or without<BR>अङ्गुलिः) the little finger; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class<BR>of deities of the fourteenth Manvantara; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of heroine.<BR>—कनिष्ठ-ता, f. or कनिष्ठ-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of being younger or smaller.<BR>—कनिष्ठ-पद or कनिष्ठ-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>the least or first root; that quantity of which the<BR>square multiplied by the given multiplicator and<BR>having the given addend added or subtrahend sub-<BR>tracted is capable of affording an exact square root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठक|कनिष्ठकं
कनिष्ठक, अस्, इका, अम्, Ved. the smallest;<BR>(आ), f. the little finger; (अम्), n. a kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनी
कनी, f. a girl, a maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीन
कनीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. young; (ई), f. the pupil<BR>of the eye; the little finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीनक|कनीनकः
कनीनक, अस्, m. a boy, a youth; the pupil of<BR>the eye; the caruncula lacrymalis; (आ), f. a maiden,<BR>a young girl, a virgin; the pupil of the eye; (इका),<BR>f. the pupil of the eye; the little finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस्
कनीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (opposed to भूयस्, ज्यायस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">Page0200-b+ 76</a>]<BR>उत्तम), smaller, less; younger, a younger brother<BR>or sister, a younger son or daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस|कनीयसं
कनीयस, अस्, आ, अम्, smaller, less; younger;<BR>(अम्), n. copper (‘of less value’); [cf. कन्यस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यका
कन्यका, कन्या. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनक|कनकं|कनकः
कनक कनक, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. कन्),<BR>gold; N. of several plants, Datura Metel and Fastuosa,<BR>thorn apple; Mesua Ferrea; Michelia Champaka;<BR>Butea Frondosa; Bauhinia Variegata; a black sort<BR>of Agallochum or sandal-wood; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>prince, a son of Durdama; N. of a son of a goddess;<BR>N. of a minister of Narendrāditya; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people; (आ), f. one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>—कनक-कुण्डला, f. the mother of Harikeśa.<BR>—कनक-क्षर, अस्, m. borax.<BR>—कनक-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of the founder of a sect.<BR>—कनक-टङ्क,<BR>अस्, m. a golden hatchet.<BR>—कनक-तालाभ (˚ल-<BR>आभा), अस्, आ, अम्, bright as a golden palm tree.<BR>—कनक-दण्डक, अस्, m. the royal parasol<BR>(golden-sticked).<BR>—कनक-दत्त, अस्, m. the son<BR>of Nidhipati.<BR>—कनक-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कनक-पराग, अस्, m. gold-<BR>dust.<BR>—कनक-पल, अस्, m. a Pala, a weight of<BR>gold and silver equal to sixteen Māṣakas, or about<BR>280 grains troy.<BR>—कनक-पिङ्गल, N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कनक-पुर, अम्, ई, n. f., N. of a town.<BR>—क-<BR>नक-प्रभा, f., N. of a plant; N. of a metre con-<BR>sisting of four lines of thirteen syllables each; N. of<BR>a princess; (अस्, आ, अम्), bright as gold.<BR>—कनक-<BR>प्रसवा, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कनक-भङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m. a piece of gold.<BR>—कनक-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>golden, consisting or made of gold.<BR>—कनक-<BR>मुनि, इस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—कनक-रम्भा,<BR>f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कनक-रस, अस्, m. fluid<BR>gold; a yellow orpiment.<BR>—कनक-रेखा, f., N. of<BR>a daughter of Kanaka-prabhā.<BR>—कनकलोद्भव,<BR>अस्, m. (fr. कनक-कल-उद्भव ?), resin of the<BR>plant Shorea Robusta.<BR>—कनक-वती, f., N. of the<BR>residence of king Kanaka-varṇa; [cf. कनका-वती.]<BR>—कनक-वर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a king supposed to<BR>be a former manifestation of Śākya-muni.<BR>—कनक-<BR>वाहिनी, f., N. of a river (‘gold stream’).<BR>—कनक-<BR>विग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a king of Viśālapurī.<BR>—क-<BR>नक-शक्ति, इस्, m. an epithet of Kārttikeya; [cf.<BR>शक्ति-धर.]<BR>—कनक-सूत्र, अम्, n. a gold<BR>cord.<BR>—कनक-स्तम्भ-रुचिर, अस्, आ, अम्, shin-<BR>ing with columns of gold.<BR>—कनक-स्थली, f. a gold<BR>mine, golden soil.<BR>—कनकाङ्गद (˚क-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कनकाचल<BR>(˚क-अच्˚), अस्, m. the golden mountain; an epithet<BR>of the mountain Sumeru.<BR>—कनकाद्रि-खण्ड<BR>(˚क-अद्˚), अम्, n. a section of the Skanda-purāṇa.<BR>—कनकाध्यक्ष (˚क-अध्˚), अस्, m. the trea-<BR>surer or superintendent of the gold.<BR>—कनकायु<BR>(˚क-आयु), उस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; (a<BR>various reading has करकायु.)<BR>—कनकालुका (˚क-<BR>आल्˚), f. a golden jar or vase.<BR>—कनका-वती, f. a<BR>proper name.<BR>—कनकावती-माधव, अस्, m. title<BR>of a work.<BR>—कनकाह्व (˚क-आह्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>blossom of the tree Mesua Ferrea.<BR>—कनकाह्वय,<BR>अस्, m. the thorn apple; Mesua Ferrea; N. of a<BR>Buddha.<BR>—कनकेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकारक|कनकारकः
कनकारक, अस्, m. the tree Bauhinia Variegata<BR>Lin.; [cf. काञ्चनार and कान्तार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनक्नक
कनक्नक कनक्नक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. epithet<BR>of a kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनखल|कनखलं
कनखल कनखल, अम्, n. and (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha and the mountains surrounding it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनटी
कनटी कनटी, f. red arsenic, = कुनटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनदेव
कनदेव कनदेव, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>patriarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनन|कननः
कनन कनन, अस्, आ, अम्, one-eyed; [cf. काण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनप|कनपः
कनप कनप, a various reading for क-<BR>णप, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनवक
कनवक कनवक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śūra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनाठ
कनाठ कनाठ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिक्रद
कनिक्रद कनिक्रद, अस्, आ, अम् (an Intens.<BR>form of rt. क्रन्द्), Ved. neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्क|कनिष्कः
कनिष्क कनिष्क, अस्, m., N. of an Indo-<BR>scythic king, celebrated in the history of Buddhism.<BR>—कनिष्क-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town founded<BR>by Kaniṣka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
कनिष्ठ, कनी, कनीन, कनीयस्। See under<BR>कन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीचि|कनीचिः
कनीचि कनीचि, इस्, f. a cart; a creeping plant<BR>with blossoms; the plant Abrus Precatorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनूज
कनूज कनूज, a corruption of कन्या-कुब्ज,<BR>q. v.<BR>—कनूज-देश, अस्, m. the country round<BR>Kanyā-kubja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनेरा
