कन्त|कंत
कन्त कन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, or कन्ति, इस्, इस्, इ (fr.<BR>1. कम्), happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्तु|कंतु|कन्तुः
कन्तु, उस्, उस्, उ, happy; (उस्), m. the heart as<BR>the seat or faculty of perception and feeling; Kāma-<BR>deva, the deity of love; a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थक
कन्थक कन्थक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थरी
कन्थरी कन्थरी, f., N. of a tree. See कन्-<BR>था, कन्थारी, क्रूरगन्धा, तीक्ष्णकण्टका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्था|कंथा
कन्था कन्था, f. a rag, a patched garment,<BR>especially one worn by certain ascetics; a wall; a<BR>town (in composition the word is neuter if the com-<BR>pound imply a town of the Uśīnāras); a kind of<BR>tree; N. of a country.<BR>—कन्था-धारण, अम्, n.<BR>wearing a patched garment as practised by certain<BR>Yogis.<BR>—कन्था-धारिन्, ई, इणी, m. f. a Yogi, a<BR>religious mendicant.<BR>—कन्थेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚था-<BR>ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थारी
कन्थारी कन्थारी, f., N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्द्|कंद्
कन्द् कन्द्, cl. 1. P. कन्दति, -दितुम्, to<BR>cry, utter lamentations; A. कन्दते, to be<BR>confounded, confound; [cf. 1. कद्, क्रन्द्, क्लन्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्द|कंद|कंदं|कन्दं|कंदः|कन्दः
कन्द कन्द, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कन्), a bulbous or tuberous root; a bulb; the bulb-<BR>ous root of Amorphophallus Campanulatus; garlic;<BR>a lump, swelling, knot; an affection of the feminine<BR>organ, considered as a fleshy excrescence, but ap-<BR>parently prolapsus uteri; N. of a metre of four lines<BR>of thirteen syllables each; a cloud (in this sense fr.<BR>कम्, water, and द).<BR>—कन्द-गुडूची, f., N. of a<BR>plant, = कन्द-रोहिणी, &c.<BR>—कन्द-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>growing from bulbs.<BR>—कन्द-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving<BR>or forming bulbs.<BR>—कन्द-फला, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कन्द-बहुला, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कन्द-मूल,<BR>अम्, n. a radish.<BR>—कन्द-लता, f., N. of a plant<BR>with a bulbous root.<BR>—कन्द-वत्, आन्, m. a species<BR>of the Soma plant.<BR>—कन्द-वर्धन, अस्, m.<BR>the esculent root of Amorphophallus Campanulatus.<BR>—कन्द-वल्ली, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कन्द-शूरण,<BR>अस्, m. the plant Amorphophallus Campanulatus.<BR>—कन्द-सञ्ज्ञ, अम्, n. prolapsus uteri; [cf.<BR>कन्द.]<BR>—कन्द-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, growing<BR>from bulbs.<BR>—कन्द-सार, अम्, n. the garden or<BR>grove of Indra.<BR>—कन्दाढ्य, (˚द-आढ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a kind of tuberous plant.<BR>—कन्दामृता (˚द-अम्˚),<BR>f., N. of a plant, = कन्द-गुडूची.<BR>—कन्दार्ह<BR>(˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m. the plant Amorphophallus Cam-<BR>panulatus.<BR>—कन्दोद्भवा (˚द-उद्˚), f., N. of a<BR>plant, = कन्द-गुडूची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दालु|कन्दालुः
कन्दालु, उस्, m., N. of several plants; an escu-<BR>lent root; a sort of Arum &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दिन्|कंदिन्
कन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a bulbous root; (ई), m.<BR>the plant Amorphophallus Campanulatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दक|कंदकः|कन्दकः
कन्दक कन्दक, अस्, m. a palanquin, =<BR>कदक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दट|कंदट|कन्दटं
कन्दट कन्दट, अम्, n. the white esculent<BR>water-lily; [cf. कन्दोट and कन्दोत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर|कंदर|कंदरं|कन्दरं|कंदरः|कन्दरः
कन्दर कन्दर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, m. f. n.<BR>(perhaps fr. कम्-दर), an artificial or natural cave;<BR>a glen, a defile, a valley; (अस्), m. a hook for driving<BR>an elephant; (अम्), n. dry ginger (in this sense fr.<BR>कन्द, ‘consisting of bulbs’?).<BR>—कन्दर-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, containing caves or valleys (as a moun-<BR>tain).<BR>—कन्दराकार (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, m. a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—कन्दरान्तर (˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. the interior<BR>of a cave.<BR>—कन्दराल (˚र-आल = आलय), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of several plants, Hibiscus Populneoides; Ficus<BR>Infectoria.<BR>—कन्दरालक, अस्, m. the tree Ficus<BR>Infectoria.<BR>—कन्दरोद्भवा (˚र-उद्˚), f., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्प|कंदर्प|कंदर्पः|कन्दर्पः
कन्दर्प कन्दर्प, अस्, m. (fr. कम्-दर्प,<BR>‘how haughty;’ or, according to others, ‘the in-<BR>flamer even of the chief of gods;’ see 3. क), N.<BR>of the deity Kāma, or the god of love, the Cupid of<BR>the Hindū mythology; love; (आ), f. one of the pre-<BR>siding female deities of the Jainas executing the<BR>orders of the fifteenth Arhat.<BR>—कन्दर्प-कूप,<BR>अस्, m. pudendum muliebre, (‘a well of love.’)<BR>—कन्दर्प-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कन्-<BR>दर्प-केलि, इस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—कन्दर्प-<BR>जीव, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = काम-वृद्धि.<BR>—कन्-<BR>दर्प-ज्वर, अस्, m. passion, desire.<BR>—कन्दर्प-<BR>दहन, अम्, n. a section of the Śiva-purāṇa.<BR>—कन्दर्प-मुसल, अस्, m. membrum virile.<BR>—कन्दर्प-शृङ्खल, अस्, m. a kind of coitus.<BR>—कन्दर्प-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast<BR>on Supadma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दल|कंदल|कंदलं|कन्दलं|कंदलः|कन्दलः
कन्दल कन्दल, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. the skull<BR>(= कपाल); the cheek, or the cheek and temple;<BR>a new shoot or sprig; a low soft tone; a portent, a<BR>natural phenomenon supposed to forbode evil; re-<BR>proach, censure; (अस्), m. gold; war, battle; (ई), f.<BR>a species of deer of which the hide is used; a plant,<BR>the plantain tree or banana tree (Musa Sapientum;<BR>see कदली); lotus seed; a flag, a banner; (अम्), n.<BR>the flower of Musa Sapientum; perhaps a mushroom.<BR>—कन्दली-कार, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—कन्-<BR>दली-कुसुम, अम्, n. a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलित|कंदलित
कन्दलित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with mushrooms (?) ;<BR>budded, blown; put forth, emitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलिन्
कन्दलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, covered with mushrooms;<BR>(ई), m. a kind of antelope (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दिरी|कंदिरी
कन्दिरी कन्दिरी, f. the plant Mimosa<BR>Pudica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दु|कंदुः|कन्दुः
कन्दु कन्दु, उस्, m. f. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>स्कन्द्), a boiler, a saucepan, or other cooking<BR>utensil of iron; an oven, or vessel serving for one;<BR>(उस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—कन्दु-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>parched, roasted (as grain), fried &c. in a pan, dressed<BR>without water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दुक|कंदुक|कंदुकं|कंदुकः|कन्दुकः
कन्दुक कन्दुक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. the preceding), a ball of wood or pith for playing<BR>with; (अम्), n. a pillow; a germ (?) .<BR>—कन्दुक-<BR>प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR>—कन्दुक-लीला, f.<BR>any game with a ball, fives.<BR>—कन्दुकेश (˚क-ईश),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कन्दुकेश्वर-लिङ्ग (˚क-<BR>ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दोट|कंदोट|कन्दोटं|कंदोटः|कन्दोटः
कन्दोट कन्दोट, अस्, m. the white lotus,<BR>Nymphæa Esculenta; (अम्), n. the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दोत|कंदोतः|कन्दोतः
कन्दोत, अस्, m. the white lotus, Nymphæa Escu-<BR>lenta. See कन्दट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्ध|कंध|कंधः|कन्धः
कन्ध कन्-ध, अस्, m. (fr. कम्, water, and<BR>ध fr. rt. धा), a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धर|कंधर|कंधरः|कन्धरः
कन्-धर, अस्, आ, m. f. (fr. कम्, head, and<BR>धर fr. rt. धृ), the neck; (अस्), m. the plant<BR>Amaranthus Oleraceus; (कम् = water), a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धि|कंधि|कंधिः|कन्धिः
कन्-धि, इस्, m. (fr. कम्, water, and धि fr. rt.<BR>धा), the ocean; (इस्), f. (कम् = head), the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्न|कन्नं
कन्न कन्न, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi; (अम्), n.<BR>fainting, falling in a fit or state of insensibility; sin;<BR>(a various reading has कल्ल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यका
कन्यका कन्यका, f. (see कन), a girl, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-b" target="_blank">Page0201-b+ 81</a>]<BR>maiden; a young virgin; a daughter; the constellation<BR>Virgo in the zodiac; the plant Aloe Perfoliata.<BR>—कन्-<BR>यका-गुण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—कन्यका-<BR>छल, अम्, n. beguiling a maiden, seduction, betrayal.<BR>—कन्यका-जन, अस्, m. a maiden.<BR>—कन्यका-<BR>जात, अस्, m. the son of an unmarried woman.<BR>—कन्यका-पति, इस्, m. a daughter's husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यना
कन्यना or कन्यला, f., Ved. a girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्या
कन्या, f. (the gen. pl. in Ṛg-veda is कनीनाम्),<BR>a girl, a virgin, a daughter; (कन्यां दा or प्र-दा or<BR>प्र-यम् or उप-पद् in Caus., to give one's daughter<BR>in marriage; कन्याम् प्रति-ग्रह् or हृ or वह्, to<BR>receive a girl in marriage, to marry); the sign of the<BR>zodiac Virgo; an epithet of Durgā; N. of a metre<BR>of four lines, each of them containing four long<BR>syllables; an annual plant; N. of several plants, the<BR>plant Aloe Perfoliata, a tuberous plant growing in<BR>Kāśmīra; large cardamoms; [cf. Zend kainê; Hib.<BR>cain, ‘chaste, undefiled;’ caile, ‘a country-woman,<BR>a harlot;’ caileamhuil, ‘girlish, effeminate.’]<BR>—कन्-<BR>या-काल, अस्, m. the time of virginity.<BR>—कन्या-<BR>कुब्ज or कन्य-कुब्ज, अम्, n., N. of an ancient city<BR>of great note, in the north of Hindūstan, situated on the<BR>काली नदी, a branch of the Ganges, in the modern<BR>district of Furruckabad. The popular spelling of the<BR>name presents, perhaps, greater variations than that of<BR>any place in India (e. g. Kunnoj, Kunnouj, Kinoge,<BR>Kinnoge, Kinnauj, Kanoj, Kannauj, Kunowj,<BR>Canowj, Canoje, Canauj, &c.). In antiquity this<BR>city ranks next to Ayodhyā in Oude. It is known<BR>to classical geography as Canogyza; but the name<BR>applies also to its dependencies and the surrounding<BR>district; the etymology (कन्या, a girl, and कुब्ज,<BR>round-shouldered or crooked) refers to a legend relat-<BR>ing to the hundred daughters of Kuśanābha, the king<BR>of this city, who were all rendered crooked by Vāyu<BR>for non-compliance with his licentious desires. The<BR>ruins of the ancient city are said to occupy a site<BR>larger than that of London.<BR>—कन्याकुब्ज-देश,<BR>अस्, m. the country round Kanyākubja.<BR>—कन्या-<BR>कुमारी or कन्य-कुमारि, इस्, f. the youthful god-<BR>dess, an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—कन्या-कूप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कन्या-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, inhe-<BR>rent in or pertaining to a virgin; the position of<BR>a planet in the sign Virgo.<BR>—कन्या-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, m. the offspring of an unmarried woman.<BR>—कन्या-ग्रहण, अम्, n. taking a girl in mar-<BR>riage.<BR>—कन्याट (˚या-आट), अस्, आ, अम्, follow-<BR>ing after young girls; (अस्), m. the middle of a<BR>house, the inner or private apartments for women.<BR>—कन्या-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कन्या-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. virginity.<BR>—कन्या-दातृ, ता, m. a father<BR>who gives a girl in marriage.<BR>—कन्यादान (either<BR>˚या-द्˚ or ˚या-आद्˚), अम्, n. giving a girl in mar-<BR>riage; receiving a girl in marriage<BR>—कन्या-दू-<BR>षक, अस्, m. the violator or defiler of a virgin;<BR>the calumniator of a girl.<BR>—कन्या-दूषण, अम्,<BR>n. defiling a virgin, calumniating a girl.<BR>—कन्या-<BR>दोष, अस्, m. a blemish in a virgin, disease, bad<BR>repute, &c.<BR>—कन्या-धन, अम्, n. a portion,<BR>dowry.<BR>—कन्या-पति, इस्, m. a daughter's husband.<BR>—कन्या-पाल, अस्, m. a dealer in slave girls; the<BR>father of a maiden; [cf. कल्या-पाल.]<BR>—कन्या-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. the offspring of an unmarried daughter.<BR>—कन्या-पुर, अम्, n. the women's apartments.<BR>—कन्या-प्रदान, अम्, n. giving a daughter in<BR>marriage.<BR>—कन्या-भर्तृ or कन्या-हर्तृ (?) , ता,<BR>m. an epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—कन्या-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>virginity.<BR>—कन्या-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting in a<BR>girl (as property &c.), being a girl.<BR>—कन्या-रत्न,<BR>अम्, n. a jewel of a damsel, a lovely girl.<BR>—कन्या-<BR>राम, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—कन्या-राशि, इस्,<BR>m. the sign Virgo.<BR>—कन्या-वेदिन्, ई, m. a son-in-law.<BR>—कन्या-शुल्क, अम्, n. the purchase-money of a<BR>maiden, money given to the bride's father.<BR>—कन्या-<BR>श्रम (˚या-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a hermitage.<BR>—कन्या-संवेद्य, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कन्या-समुद्भव, अस्, m. the son of an un-<BR>married girl.<BR>—कन्या-सम्प्रदान, अम्, n. the<BR>giving away a maiden in marriage.<BR>—कन्या-स्व-<BR>यंवर, अस्, m. the choice of a husband by a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">Page0201-c+ 75</a>]<BR>maiden.<BR>—कन्या-हरण, अम्, n. carrying off a<BR>girl, rape, ravishment.<BR>—कन्या-ह्रद, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याका
कन्याका or कन्यिका, f. a young girl, a virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यस|कन्यसः
कन्यस कन्यस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कनीयस्),<BR>younger; (आ), f. the little finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्युष|कन्युषं
कन्युष कन्युष, अम्, n. the hand below<BR>the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप्
कप् कप्, a various reading for क्रप्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप
कप कप, आस्, m. pl. a class of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपट|कपटं|कपटः
कपट कपट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. कम्प्), fraud, deceit, cheating, circumvention;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Dānava; (ई), f. a measure equal to<BR>the capacity of the hollows of the two hands joined.<BR>—कपट-ता, f. or कपट-त्व, अम्, n. deceitful-<BR>ness.<BR>—कपट-तापस, अस्, m. one who deceitfully<BR>pretends to be an ascetic.<BR>—कपट-दैत्य-बध,<BR>अस्, m. title of a chapter of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa<BR>(‘destruction of the Daitya Kapaṭa’).<BR>—कपट-<BR>प्रबन्ध, अस्, m. fraud, trick, fraudulent plot or<BR>contrivance.<BR>—कपट-लेख्य, अम्, n. a forged docu-<BR>ment, a false or fraudulent statement.<BR>—कपट-<BR>वचन, अम्, n. deceitful talk.<BR>—कपट-वेश, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, assuming a false dress or appearance, masked,<BR>disguised; (अस्), m. disguise.<BR>—कपटवेशिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, disguised, in masquerade.<BR>—कपटेश्वरी (˚ट-ईश्˚),<BR>f., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिक|कपटिकः
कपटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, acting deceitfully, fraudu-<BR>lent, dishonest, a rogue, a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिन्
कपटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fraudulent, dishonest, a cheat;<BR>(इनी), f. a kind of perfume, = चीदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपना
कपना कपना, f. (said to be fr. rt. कम्प्),<BR>Ved. a worm, a caterpillar; [cf. κάμπη]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द|कपर्दः|कपर्द्द|कपर्द्दः
कपर्द कपर्द, अस्, m. a small shell or<BR>cowrie used as a coin and as a die in gambling,<BR>Cypræa Moneta; braided and knotted hair, especially<BR>that of Śiva (knotted so as to resemble the cowrie<BR>shell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्दक|कपर्दकः|कपर्द्दक|कपर्द्दकः
कपर्दक, अस्, m. = कपर्द above; (इका), f.<BR>Cypræa Moneta. See कपर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्दिन्|कपर्द्दिन्
कपर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, shaggy; wearing braided and<BR>knotted hair like the cowrie shell; epithet of Rudra, of<BR>Pūṣan, of the descendants of Vasiṣṭha and of Durgā;<BR>(ई), m., N. of Śiva; N. of one of the eleven Rudras.<BR>—कपर्दि-कारिका, आस्, f. pl., N. of a work.<BR>—कपर्दि-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपल|कपलं
कपल कपल, अम्, n., Ved. a half, a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाट|कपाटं|कपाटः
कपाट कपाट, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. a door,<BR>the leaf or panel of a door.<BR>—कपाट-घ्न, अस्, m.<BR>one who breaks the door, a house-breaker, a thief.<BR>—कपाट-सन्धि, इस्, m. the junction of the leaves<BR>of a door; a mode of multiplying in which the<BR>multiplicand is placed in a certain manner under the<BR>multiplying quantity.<BR>—कपाटसन्धिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>term used for a kind of bandage; similarly अर्ध-<BR>कपाटसन्धिक.<BR>—कपाटोद्घाटन (˚ट-उद्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a door-key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाल|कपालं|कपालः
कपाल कपाल, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कम्प्), a cup, a jar, a dish, used especially for the<BR>Puroḍāśa offering (often at the end of a compound,<BR>the first member of which is a numeral, e. g. त्रि-<BR>कपाल, ‘consisting of three cups’); the shell of an<BR>egg, shell of a tortoise; the cotyla of the leg of a<BR>man or animal, any flat bone; a kind of leprosy;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. the fragment of a vessel, a pot-<BR>sherd; a cover or lid; the skull, the cranium, the<BR>skull-bone; either half of a water-jar; multitude,<BR>assemblage, collection; a treaty of peace on equal<BR>terms, = कपाट?; (अस्), m., N. of an intermediate<BR>caste; N. of a man; (अम्, ई), n. f. a beggar's bowl;<BR>[cf. Gr. κεφαλή; Lat. caput; Germ. haupt; Goth.<BR>haubith, Them. haubida.]<BR>—कपाल-नालिका, f. a<BR>sort of pin or spindle for winding cotton, thread, &c.<BR>—कपाल-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a pot in hand to<BR>receive food (as a beggar).<BR>—कपाल-भाती, f. a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-a" target="_blank">Page0202-a+ 80</a>]<BR>particular sort of penance, consisting in alternate<BR>suppression and emission of the breath.<BR>—कपाल-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. an epithet of Śiva or Mahā-deva (who<BR>wears skulls).<BR>—कपालमालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing a<BR>garland of skulls; epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कपाल-मोचन,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कपाल-शिरस् (?), आस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Muni; (a various reading has कलाप-शिरस्.)<BR>—कपाल-सन्धि, इस्, m. a treaty of peace on equal<BR>terms (= कपाट-सन्धि?).<BR>—कपाल-स्फोट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Rakṣas (‘splitting the skull’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिका
कपालिका, f. a potsherd; the tartar of the teeth;<BR>[cf. कापालिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिन्
कपालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with or bearing<BR>skulls; (ई, इनी), m. f. a man or woman of low caste,<BR>son or daughter of a Brāhman mother and a fisherman<BR>father; the follower of a certain Śaiva sect, [cf.<BR>कापालिक]; (ई), m. an epithet of Śiva (as wearing<BR>skulls); N. of one of the eleven Rudras; N. of a<BR>servant of Śiva; (इनी), f. the goddess Durgā as the<BR>wife of Śiva-kapālin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपि|कपिः
कपि कपि, इस्, इस्, इ (said to be fr. rt. कम्प्),<BR>brown; (इस्), m. an ape or monkey; an elephant;<BR>the plant Emblica Officinalis or a species of Karañja;<BR>incense, storax or impure benzoin, [cf. कपि-ज,<BR>कपि-तैल, &c.]; the sun; an epithet of Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa; N. of a Muni, the author of a Vedic verse,<BR>son of Uru-kṣaya; (इस् or ई), f. a female ape or<BR>monkey; [cf. Gr. κῆπος, κεῖπος; Old Germ. affo;<BR>Angl. Sax. apa; Eng. ape.]<BR>—कपि-कच्छु, उस् or<BR>ऊ, ऊस्, f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus.<BR>—कपिकच्छु-<BR>फलोपमा (˚ल-उप्˚), f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कपि-<BR>कच्छुरा, f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus.<BR>—कपि-<BR>कन्दुक, अम्, n. the skull, the cranium (‘playing-<BR>ball of monkeys’).<BR>—कपि-केतन, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Arjuna, the third son of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—कपि-केश, अस्,<BR>m. monkey's hair (?) .<BR>—कपि-कोलि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—कपि-चूडा, f. or कपि-चूत, अस्, m. the tree<BR>Spondias Magnifera.<BR>—कपि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born of<BR>a monkey; (अस्), m. incense, benzoin.<BR>—कपि-तैल,<BR>अम्, n. benzoin or storax.<BR>—कपि-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of an ape, apishness.<BR>—कपि-ध्वज, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Arjuna (having a monkey as his symbol,<BR>his ensign or arms).<BR>—कपि-नामन्, आ, m. incense.<BR>—कपि-पिप्पली, f., N. of two different kinds of<BR>plants.<BR>—कपि-प्रभा, f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus.<BR>—कपि-प्रभु, उस्, m. an epithet of Rāma, general<BR>of the monkey-force, with which he invaded Laṅkā.<BR>—कपि-प्रिय, अस्, m. the tree Spondias Magnifera<BR>and the tree Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—कपि-भक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. the food of apes; N. of a certain eatable<BR>substance.<BR>—कपि-रथ, अस्, m. an epithet of Rāma;<BR>[cf. कपि-प्रभु.]<BR>—कपि-रोम-फला, f. the plant<BR>Mucuna Pruritus.<BR>—कपि-लोम-फला, f. the plant<BR>Mucuna Pruritus.<BR>—कपि-लोमा, f. a kind of perfume.<BR>—कपि-लोह, अम्, n. brass (monkey-coloured metal).<BR>—कपिल्लिका, f. (contracted from कपि-वल्लिका?),<BR>a plant which bears a seed resembling pepper, Scin-<BR>dapsus Officinalis, = गज-पिप्पली.<BR>—कपि-वक्त्र,<BR>अस्, m. a N. of Nārada, a saint and philosopher and<BR>friend of Kṛṣṇa, having a face like a monkey.<BR>—कपि-वन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कपि-वल्ली,<BR>f. the plant Scindapsus Officinalis.<BR>—कपि-शाक, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a cabbage.<BR>—कपि-शीर्ष, अम्, n. the<BR>upper part or coping of a wall.<BR>—कपि-शीर्षक,<BR>अम्, n. vermilion, the red sulphuret of mercury.<BR>—कपि-शीर्ष्णी, f. a kind of musical instrument.<BR>—कपि-ष्ठल (˚पि-स्थ˚), अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this Ṛṣi.<BR>—कपि-स्कन्-<BR>ध, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—कपि-स्थल, अम्, n.<BR>a place frequented by monkeys.<BR>—कपि-स्वर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—कपी-कच्छु, उस्, f. the plant<BR>Mucuna Pruritus; see कपि-कच्छु.<BR>—कपीज्य, अस्,<BR>m. (कपि-इज्या?), the tree Mimusops Kauki.<BR>—क-<BR>पीन्द्र (˚पि-इन्˚), अस्, m. the chief of the monkeys;<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; of Jāmbavat, the father-in-law<BR>of Kṛṣṇa; of Hanumat; of Sugrīva, &c.<BR>—कपी-<BR>वत्, आन्, m., N. of a sage; one of the seven sages<BR>of the fourth Manvantara; (ती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—कपीष्ट (˚पि-इष्˚), अस्, m. the tree Feronia<BR>Elephantum.<BR>—कप्य्-आख्य, अस्, m. incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिका
कपिका, f., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थ|कपित्थः
कपित्थ, अस्, m. (त्थ = स्थ fr. rt. स्था, ‘on<BR>which monkeys dwell;’ cf. अश्वत्थ), the elephant<BR>or wood apple tree, Feronia Elephantum; a particular<BR>position of the hands and fingers; (अम्), n. the fruit<BR>of Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—कपित्थ-त्वच्, क्, n. the<BR>bark of the tree Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—कपित्थ-<BR>पर्णी and कपित्थानी, f., N. of a plant, = चित्र-<BR>पत्त्रिका, &c.<BR>—कपित्थास्य (˚थ-आस्य), अस्, m. a<BR>kind of monkey (having a roundish face, in shape<BR>like the wood apple).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थक
कपित्थक, N. of a place in Avanti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थिनी
कपित्थिनी, f. a region abounding in Kapitthas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिरक
कपिरक = कपिलक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिल|कपिलः
कपिल, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘monkey-coloured,’ brown,<BR>tawny, reddish; (अस्), m. the brown or tawny colour;<BR>a (brown) dog; incense; N. of an ancient sage,<BR>identified by some with Viṣṇu and considered as the<BR>founder of the Sāṅkhya system of philosophy; a son<BR>of Vitatha; or a son of Vasu-deva by Narācī; or a<BR>son of Kardama by Devahūti; a form of fire; an epi-<BR>thet of the sun, considered as king of the Nāgas;<BR>N. of a Dānava; N. of a mountain; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people; (आ), f. a brown cow, a fabulous cow cele-<BR>brated in the Purāṇas; N. of two plants, a kind of<BR>Śiṃśapā or Śiṃśapā itself; the plant Aloe Perfoliata;<BR>a sort of perfume; a kind of brass; the common<BR>leech; N. of a daughter of Dakṣa; N. of the female<BR>elephant of the south-east, the male being called<BR>Puṇḍarīka; N. of a river.<BR>—कपिल-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of a Smṛti.<BR>—कपिल-द्युति, इस्,<BR>m. a N. of Sūrya or the sun.<BR>—कपिल-द्राक्षा, f.<BR>a vine with brown or tawny coloured grapes.<BR>—क-<BR>पिल-द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of a perfume or sweet scented<BR>wood (काक्षी).<BR>—कपिल-धारा, f. an epithet of<BR>the Gaṅgā; N. of a Tīrtha; a holy place, a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—कपिल-फला, f. a vine with brown<BR>grapes.<BR>—कपिल-भद्रा, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—क-<BR>पिल-मत, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—कपिल-रुद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कपिल-वस्तु, उ, n., N. of<BR>the town in which Śākya-muni or Buddha was born.<BR>—कपिल-शिंशपा, f. a variety of Śiṃśapā with<BR>reddish flowers.<BR>—कपिल-संहिता, f. title of an<BR>Upa-purāṇa, a dialogue between Kapila and Satyajit.<BR>—कपिलाक्षी (˚ल-अक्˚), f. a kind of deer (‘with<BR>brown eyes’); a variety of Śiṃśapā with reddish<BR>flowers.<BR>—कपिलाञ्जन (˚ल-अञ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva; [cf. कपिशाञ्जन.]<BR>—कपिला-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha, (any one bathing there obtains<BR>1000 brown cows.)<BR>—कपिलावट (˚ल-अव्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कपिलाश्व (˚ल-अश्˚), अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of the god of Indra; N. of a man, a son of<BR>Dhundhumāra.<BR>—कपिला-ह्रद, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलक
कपिलक, अस्, इका, अम्, reddish; (इका), f., N. of<BR>a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलीकृ
कपिली-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to colour brown or reddish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिश|कपिशः
कपिश, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘ape-coloured,’ brown, reddish-<BR>brown; (अस्), m. brown or reddish colour, a com-<BR>pound of black and yellow; incense, storax or coarse<BR>benzoin; (आ or ई), f. a spirit, a sort of rum; (आ), f.<BR>the mother of the demons called Piśācas; N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—कपिशाञ्जन (˚श-अञ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—कपिशा-पुत्र, अस्, m. a Piśāca, an imp<BR>or goblin.<BR>—कपिशायन (˚श-अय्˚), अस्, m. a deity;<BR>a sort of spirit or rum.<BR>—कपिशावदान (˚श-अव्˚),<BR>N. of a Buddhist work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशित
कपिशित, अस्, आ, अम्, embrowned, made brown<BR>or dusky red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीका
कपिशीका, f. a kind of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीत|कपीतः
कपीत, अस्, m., N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीतन|कपीतनः
कपीतन, अस्, m., N. of several plants; a tree<BR>bearing an acid fruit, Spondias Magnifera; the plant<BR>Thespesia Populnea; Acacia Sirisa; the holy fig tree,<BR>Ficus Religiosa; the betel nut tree, Areca Faufel;<BR>Ægle Marmelos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिजङ्घिका
कपिजङ्घिका कपिजङ्घिका, f. a kind of ant;<BR>also spelt कपिजाङ्घिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिञ्जल|कपिंजल|कपिंजलः|कपिञ्जलः
कपिञ्जल कपिञ्जल, अस्, m. (fr. क + पिञ्जल?,<BR>sometimes कपिङ्गल), a bird, the francoline par-<BR>tridge; the Caṭaka; N. of a man; also of a sparrow;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—कपिञ्जलार्म (˚ल-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a region (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुच्छल|कपुच्छलं
कपुच्छल क-पुच्छल, अम्, n., Ved. the fore<BR>part of a sacrificial ladle, i. e. the part with which the<BR>fluid is skimmed off; hair hanging down to the<BR>ground, or a lock of hair tied on the right side of<BR>the crown of a young Brāhman, when he is invested<BR>with the sacerdotal thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुष्टिका
कपुष्टिका कपुष्टिका, f. a patch of hair on<BR>each side of the head; also written कपुष्णिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपूय
कपूय क-पूय, अस्, आ, अम् (see 2. क), smell-<BR>ing badly, disgusting, disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपृथ्
कपृथ् क-पृथ्, त्, or क-पृथ, अस्, m. (see<BR>4. क), Ved. ‘causing pleasure,’ membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोत|कपोतः
कपोत क-पोत, अस्, m. (2. क + पोत, q. v.),<BR>a dove, pigeon, especially the spotty-necked pigeon;<BR>(in the Vedas often a bird of evil omen); a bird in<BR>general; a particular position of the hands; the gray<BR>colour of a pigeon; the brightness of antimony (of a<BR>gray colour).<BR>—कपोत-चरणा, f. a kind of perfume.<BR>—कपोत-पाक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a mountain-tribe;<BR>(आ), f. a princess of this tribe.<BR>—कपोत-पाद, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having feet like those of a pigeon.<BR>—कपोत-<BR>पालिका or कपोत-पाली, f. a dove-cot, an aviary or<BR>pigeon-house.<BR>—कपोत-राज, अस्, m. the king of<BR>the pigeons.<BR>—कपोत-रेतस, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कपोत-रोमन्, आ, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कपोत-<BR>वङ्का, f., N. of a medicinal plant (used as a remedy<BR>for the stone).<BR>—कपोत-वर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, of the<BR>colour of a pigeon, of a bright gray, lead-gray; (ई),<BR>f. small cardamoms.<BR>—कपोत-वल्ली, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कपोत-वाणा, f. a kind of perfume.<BR>—कपोत-<BR>वेगा, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कपोत-सार, अम्, n. the<BR>brightness of antimony, antimony.<BR>—कपोत-हस्त<BR>or कपोत-हस्तक, अस्, m. a mode of joining the<BR>hands in prayer, entreaty, or fear, &c.<BR>—कपोताङ्घ्रि<BR>(˚त-अङ्˚), इस्, f. a kind of perfume.<BR>—कपोताञ्जन<BR>(˚त-अञ्ज्˚), अम्, n. = कापोताञ्जन, the brightness of<BR>antimony, antimony.<BR>—कपोताभ (˚त-आभा), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of the colour of a pigeon, of a bright gray;<BR>(अस्), m. a pale or dirty white colour.<BR>—कपोतारि<BR>(˚त-अरि), इस्, m. a hawk, a falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतक|कपोतकं|कपोतकः
कपोतक, अस्, m. a small pigeon or dove; a mode<BR>of joining the hands; (अम्), n. antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतकीया
कपोतकीया, f. a region abounding in pigeons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतिन्
कपोतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having pigeons, pigeon-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोल|कपोलः
कपोल कपोल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कम्प्), a cheek; (ई), f. the fore part of the knee,<BR>the knee-cap or pan; [cf. कपाल.]<BR>—कपोल-कवि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कपोल-काष, अस्, m. any ob-<BR>ject against which the cheeks or temples are rubbed;<BR>the elephant's temples and cheeks.<BR>—कपोल-फ-<BR>लक, अस्, m. the cheek; (perhaps) the cheek-bone.<BR>—कपोल-भित्ति, इस्, m. the temples and cheek,<BR>the upper part of the face; (perhaps) the opening in<BR>the temples of an elephant during rut.<BR>—कपोल-<BR>राग, अस्, m. colour or flush in the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप्फिण
कप्फिण कप्फिण, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(various readings have कप्फिल्ल, कफिन, कफिन्,<BR>कफिल, कम्फिल्ल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफ|कफः
कफ कफ, अस्, m. phlegm, one of the<BR>three humors of the body (the other two are वायु<BR>and पित्त), watery froth or foam in general.<BR>—कफ-<BR>कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, or कफ-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>producing phlegm; occasioning colds.<BR>—कफ-<BR>कूर्चिका, f. saliva, spittle.<BR>—कफ-क्षय, अस्, m.<BR>pulmonary consumption.<BR>—कफ-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>removing phlegm, antiphlegmatic, curing colds (epi-<BR>thet of many plants); (ई), f., N. of a plant.<BR>—क-<BR>फ-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, arising from or produced by<BR>phlegm.<BR>—कफ-ज्वर, अस्, m. fever arising from<BR>excess of phlegm.<BR>—कफ-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">Page0203-a+ 75</a>]<BR>antiphlegmatic.<BR>—कफ-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, phlegm-<BR>atic.<BR>—कफ-वर्धक, अस्, ई, अम्, exciting or<BR>increasing phlegm.<BR>—कफ-वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>exciting or increasing phlegm; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>plant, a species of Tabernæmontana.<BR>—कफ-वि-<BR>रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, obstructing the phlegm; (इ), n.<BR>pepper.<BR>—कफ-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, arising<BR>from phlegm.<BR>—कफ-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, or क-<BR>फ-हृत्, त्, त्, त्, removing phlegm, antiphlegmatic.<BR>—कफात्मक (˚फ-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, phlegmatic.<BR>—कफान्तक (˚फ-अन्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant, = वर्वूर.<BR>—कफारि (˚फ-अरि), इस्, m. dry<BR>ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफल
कफल, अस्, आ, अम्, phlegmatic, having phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफिन्
कफिन्, ई, इनी, इ, phlegmatic; filled with mucus;<BR>(ई), m. an elephant; a various reading for कप्फिण;<BR>(इनी), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफेलू
कफेलू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, phlegmatic, causing or exciting<BR>phlegm; (ऊस्), m. a plant, Cordia Latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफणि|कफणिः
कफणि कफणि, इस्, m. f. the elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफोणि|कफोणिः
कफोणि, इस्, ई, m. f. the elbow.<BR>—कफोणि-<BR>घात, अस्, m. a stroke with the elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफौड|कफौडः
कफौड कफौड, अस्, m., Ved. the elbow (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कब्
कब् कब्, cl. 1. A. कबते, -बितुम्, to<BR>colour, to tinge with various hues; to<BR>praise; [cf. कव्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबन्ध|कबंध|कबंधं|कबन्धं|कबंधः|कबन्धः
कबन्ध क-बन्ध or क-वन्ध, अस् or अम्,<BR>m. or n. a big barrel or cask, a large-bellied vessel;<BR>(metaphorically) a cloud; the belly; the clouds<BR>which obscure the sun at sunset and sunrise (some-<BR>times they are personified); water; a N. of Rāhu;<BR>a headless trunk (shaped like a barrel), especially one<BR>retaining vitality; (अस्), m., N. of an Ātharvaṇa and<BR>Gandharva; N. of a Muni; N. of the Dānava or<BR>Rākṣasa called Danu, who was son of Śrī. (His story<BR>is told in Rāmāy. III. 75. It is there related that<BR>Indra punished him for his insolence in challenging the<BR>god to combat, by striking his head and thighs with<BR>his thunderbolt and so pressing them into his body.<BR>He had enormously long arms and a huge mouth in<BR>his belly. It was predicted that he would not recover<BR>his original shape until killed in a battle with Rāma<BR>and Lakṣmaṇa. The whole story probably repre-<BR>sents one of Indra's battles with the clouds.)<BR>—क-<BR>बन्ध-ता, f. or कबन्ध-त्व, अम्, n. headlessness,<BR>decapitation.<BR>—कबन्ध-वध, अस्, m. ‘the slay-<BR>ing of Kabandha,’ title of a chapter of the Padma-<BR>purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबन्धिन्|कबंधिन्
कबन्धिन् or कवन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. ‘bearing<BR>huge vessels of water or the clouds;’ (Sāy.) ‘endowed<BR>with water,’ an epithet of the Maruts who open the<BR>clouds and send down rain; (ई), m., N. of a Kātyā-<BR>yana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबित्थ|कबित्थः
कबित्थ कबित्थ, अस्, m. the elephant or<BR>wood apple tree, Feronia Elephantum. See कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबिल|कबिलः
कबिल कबिल, अस्, आ, अम्, tawny-coloured;<BR>(अस्), m. tawny (the colour). See कपिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबुलि|कबुलिः
कबुलि कबुलि, इस्, f. the hinder part of an<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कब्रु
कब्रु कब्रु, Atharva-veda II. 3, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम् 1. कम्, ind. (Gr. κεν), well, bene (op-<BR>posed to अकम्, ‘badly’), a particle placed after the<BR>word to which it belongs with an affirmative sense<BR>(Well, Yes), which sense, however, is generally so weak<BR>that the Indian grammarians are perhaps right in<BR>enumerating कम् among the expletives; it is often<BR>found attached to a dat. case, giving to the latter a<BR>stronger meaning, and is generally placed at the end<BR>of the Pāda (e. g. अजीजन ओस्कधीर् भोजनाय<BR>कम्, thou didst create the plants for actual food);<BR>it is also used as an enclitic with the particles नु, सु,<BR>and हि, but is nevertheless treated in the Padapāṭha<BR>as a separate word. Rarely कम् seems to be used,<BR>like कद् and किम्, as an interrogative particle; some-<BR>times it occurs, like किम् and कद्, at the beginning<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">Page0203-b+ 80</a>]<BR>of compounds, marking the strange or unusual cha-<BR>racter of anything, [cf. कन्दर्प]: according to<BR>native lexicographers कम् means also head; water;<BR>food.<BR>—कम्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्ब
कम्ब or कम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, well (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम् 2. कम्, A. (not used in the con-<BR>jugational tenses) चकमे, कमिष्यते,<BR>अचकमत, कमितुम्, to wish, desire, long for;<BR>to love, be in love with; to have sexual intercourse<BR>with: Caus. A. (ep. also P.) कामयते, -ति, काम-<BR>याञ्-चक्रे, कामयिष्यते, अचीकमत, कामयि-<BR>तुम्, to wish, desire, long for (with pot. or inf.,<BR>e. g. कामये भुञ्जीत, I wish he may eat; कामये<BR>दातुम्, I wish to give); to love, have sexual inter-<BR>course with; to be inflamed with love; (with बहु<BR>or अत्यर्थम्) to rate or value highly; to cause any<BR>one to love, [cf. also कन्]: Desid. चिकमिषते and<BR>चिकामयिषते: Intens. चङ्कम्यते; [cf. Lat.<BR>comis; also amo with loss of the initial; câ-rus for<BR>cam-rus; Hib. caemh, ‘love, desire; fine, hand-<BR>some, pleasant;’ caomhach, ‘a friend, a companion;’<BR>caomhaim, ‘I save, spare, protect:’ perhaps Old<BR>Germ. scim, scimo, ‘splendor;’ Armen. kamim.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन|कमनं|कमनः
कमन, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing for, desirous; libi-<BR>dinous, beautiful, desirable, lovely; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>Kāma, the god of love; N. of Brahmā; the tree<BR>Jonesia Aśoka.<BR>—कमन-च्छद (˚न-छ˚), अस्,<BR>m. a heron (having beautiful plumage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनीय|कमनीयं
कमनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or wished for,<BR>desirable; lovely, pleasing, beautiful.<BR>—कमनीय-<BR>ता, f. or कमनीय-त्व, अम्, n. loveliness, beauty;<BR>desirableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमर|कमरः
कमर, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous, lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमल|कमलं|कमलः
कमल, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous, lustful; (अस्), m. a<BR>species of deer; the Indian crane, Ardea Sibirica; an<BR>epithet of Brahmā; N. of a man; (अम्), n. (ac-<BR>cording to some m. or n.) the lotus, Nelumbium;<BR>water; copper; the bladder; a medicament, a drug;<BR>N. of a town built by Kamalā; a particular high<BR>number; Ved., N. of a certain colour; (अम् or ई),<BR>n. f., N. of a metre of four lines of three short sylla-<BR>bles each; (आ), f. an epithet of Lakṣmī; an excel-<BR>lent woman; N. of a female dancer who afterwards<BR>became the wife of king Jayāpīḍa.<BR>—कमल-कीकर<BR>and कमल-कीट, N. of two Grāmas or villages.<BR>—कमल-खण्ड, अम्, n. an assemblage of lotuses.<BR>—कमल-गर्भाभ (˚भ-आभा), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bright as the lotus-cup.<BR>—कमल-देवी, f., N. of the<BR>wife of king Lalitāditya and mother of king Kuva-<BR>layāpīḍa.<BR>—कमल-पत्त्राक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one whose eyes are like lotuses.<BR>—कमल-<BR>भव, अस्, m. or कमल-योनि, इस्, m. ‘sprung<BR>from the lotus,’ an epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—कमल-<BR>भिदा, f., N. of a Grāma or village.<BR>—कमल-वती,<BR>f., N. of the wife of king Lalitāditya.<BR>—कमल-<BR>वदन, अम्, n. a lotus face, i. e. a lovely face.<BR>—कमल-वर्धन, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Kampana.<BR>—कमल-सम्भव, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Brahmā.<BR>—कमलाकर (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, m. an<BR>assemblage of lotuses; a lake &c. where lotuses<BR>abound; N. of several authors.<BR>—कमला-केशव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a sanctuary built by Kamalavatī.<BR>—कमलाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), N. of a place.<BR>—कमला-<BR>नन्दन, अस्, m. son of Kamalā, an epithet of<BR>Miśra-dinakara.<BR>—कमला-पति, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>copyist.<BR>—कमलायताक्ष (˚ल-आयत-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having large lotus eyes.<BR>—कमलायुध<BR>(˚ल-आय्˚), अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कमलालया<BR>(˚ल-आल्˚), f. an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—कमलासन<BR>or कमलासन-स्थ (˚ल-आस्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Brahmā.<BR>—कमला-हट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a market-<BR>place founded by Kamalavatī.<BR>—१. कमलाहास (˚ल-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, m. the shutting or opening of a lotus.<BR>—२.<BR>कमलाहास, nom. (fr. the last) P. -हासति, -सितुम्,<BR>to smile like a lotus.<BR>—कमलेक्षण (˚ल-ईक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, lotus-eyed.<BR>—कमलोत्तर (˚ल-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n. safflower, Carthamus Tinctorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलक|कमलकं
कमलक, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलिनी
कमलिनी, f. a number of lotus flowers or a lake<BR>or place abounding with them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमा
कमा, f. loveliness, beauty, radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमितृ
कमितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, lustful, desirous, cupidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्र|कम्रः
कम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous, cupidinous; beautiful,<BR>desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमक
कमक कमक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of this man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमठ|कमठं|कमठः
कमठ कमठ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 2. कम्),<BR>a tortoise; a porcupine; a water-jar, especially one<BR>made of a hollow gourd or cocoa-nut, and used by<BR>ascetics; a bamboo; N. of a prince; of a Muni; and<BR>of a Daitya; (ई), f. a female tortoise, a small one.<BR>—कमठ-पति, इस्, m. the king of tortoises.<BR>—कमठासुर-वध (˚ठ-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘the<BR>slaying of the Daitya Kamaṭha,’ a section of the<BR>Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमण्डलु|कमंडलु|कमंडलुः|कमण्डलुः
कमण्डलु कमण्डलु, उस्, उ, m. n. an earthen<BR>or wooden water-pot used by the ascetic and religious<BR>student; a vessel with a spout; the waved-leaf fig<BR>tree, Ficus Infectoria.<BR>—कमण्डलु-तरु, उस्, m.<BR>the tree Ficus Infectoria.<BR>—कमण्डलु-धर, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमद्यू
कमद्यू कमद्यू, ऊस्, f. (fr. कम derived fr.<BR>2. कम् and द्यू?), Ved., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन्तक
कमन्तक कमन्तक and कमन्दक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of two men; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of<BR>these men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन्ध|कमन्धं
कमन्ध कमन्ध, अम्, n. water; (a various<BR>reading for कबन्ध; considered also as a com-<BR>pound of कम् and अन्ध, both being, according to<BR>native lexicographers, synonyms of water.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमल|कमलं|कमलः
कमल कमल. See under rt. 2. कम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प्|कंप्
कम्प् कम्प्, cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.) कम्-<BR>पते, कम्पति, चकम्पे, कम्पिष्यते,<BR>अकम्पिष्ट, कम्पितुम्, to tremble, shake: Caus.<BR>P. कम्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause to tremble, make<BR>tremble, shake; to pronounce in a tremulous manner,<BR>i. e. with a trill or shake: Desid. चिकम्पिषते:<BR>Intens. चङ्कम्प्यते, चङ्कम्प्ति; [cf. Gr. κάμπτω<BR>πέμπω; Hib. cabhóg, ‘hastening.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प|कंप|कंपः|कम्पः
कम्प, अस्, m. trembling, tremor, trembling<BR>motion, shaking; a tremulous or trilling pronuncia-<BR>tion, a modification of the Svarita accent, which may<BR>take place if the Svarita syllable is followed by an<BR>Udātta syllable; N. of a man.<BR>—कम्प-राज, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—कम्प-लक्ष्मन्, आ, m. air,<BR>wind.<BR>—कम्पान्वित (˚प-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, affected<BR>with trembling, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पन|कंपन|कम्पनं|कम्पनः
कम्पन, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaken, un-<BR>steady; causing to tremble, shaking; (अस्), m. a<BR>kind of weapon; the dewy season (November-De-<BR>cember); N. of a prince; N. of a country near<BR>Kāśmīra; (आ), f., N. of a river; (अम्), n. trembling,<BR>quivering; quivering pronunciation, a modification of<BR>the Svarita accent (see कम्प); shaking, swinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पनीय
कम्पनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shaken, movable,<BR>vibratory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पमान
कम्पमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पयत्
कम्पयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shaking, causing to<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पाक|कंपाक|कंपाकः|कम्पाकः
कम्पाक, अस्, m. (a wrong reading for कम्-<BR>पाङ्क), wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पित|कंपित|कम्पितं
कम्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaking; caused<BR>to tremble, shaken, swung; (अम्), n. trembling, a<BR>trembling, a tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पिन्
कम्पिन्, ई, इनी, इ, trembling, quivering, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पिल|कम्पिलः
कम्पिल or कम्पिल्य or कम्पिल्ल or कम्-<BR>पिल्लक or कम्पील, अस्, m., N. of a plant, Cri-<BR>num Amaryllacee (?); commonly कमलागुण्डि; [cf.<BR>काम्पिल्ल and शुण्डा-रोचनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प्य
कम्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shaken, to be made to<BR>tremble, to be moved away from one's place; to be<BR>pronounced in a quivering manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प्र|कंप्र
कम्प्र, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaken, mova-<BR>ble; agile, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0203-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्ब्|कंब्
कम्ब् कम्ब्, cl. 1. P. कम्बति, -बितुम्, to<BR>go, move; (a various reading for कर्ब्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बर|कंबर|कम्बरः
कम्बर कम्बर, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, spot-<BR>ted; (अस्), m. variegated colour; [cf. कर्बुर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बल|कंबल|कम्बलं|कंबलः|कम्बलः
कम्बल कम्बल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. 2. कम्), a woollen blanket or cloth; an upper<BR>cloth or garment of wool; (अस्), m. a dew-lap; a<BR>small worm or insect; a sort of deer; N. of a Nāga;<BR>N. of a man; (अम्), n. water; [cf. कमल.]<BR>—कम्बल-कारक, अस्, m. a woollen cloth manu-<BR>facturer.<BR>—कम्बल-चारायणीय, आस्, m. pl. a nick-<BR>name of a school of Cārāyaṇa.<BR>—कम्बल-धा-<BR>वक, अस्, m. one who cleans woollen clothes.<BR>—कम्बल-बर्हिष, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कम्बल-वाह्य, अस्, m. or कम्बल-वाह्यक,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of carriage covered with a coarse<BR>blanket or woollen cloth and drawn by oxen. (The<BR>more correct spelling seems to be कम्बलि-वाह्य<BR>and कम्बलि-वाह्यक.)<BR>—कम्बल-हार, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलक|कंबलकं|कंबलकः|कम्बलकः
कम्बलक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a woollen cloth, a<BR>garment of wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलिन्|कंबलिन्
कम्बलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, covered with a woollen cloth<BR>or blanket.<BR>—कम्बलि-वाह्यक, अम्, n. a carriage<BR>so covered and drawn by oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलीय
कम्बलीय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for woollen blankets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बल्य
कम्बल्य, अम्, n. 100 Palas of wool (so much<BR>being necessary for making a woollen blanket).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बालायिन्
कम्बालायिन् कम्बालायिन्, ई, m. a sort of kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बि|कंबिः|कम्बिः
कम्बि कम्बि, इस्, f. a ladle or spoon; a<BR>shoot, a branch or joint of a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बु|कंबु|कम्बुः
कम्बु कम्बु, उस्, उ, m. n. a conch, a shell;<BR>a bivalve shell; a bracelet, a ring made of shells;<BR>(उस्), m. an elephant; the neck; a tube-shaped<BR>bone; a vein or tubular vessel of the body; a sort<BR>of Curcuma.<BR>—कम्बु-काष्ठा, f. the tree Physalis<BR>Flexuosa.<BR>—कम्बु-ग्रीव, अस्, m., N. of a tortoise;<BR>(आ), f. a neck marked with three lines like a shell,<BR>and considered to be indicative of exalted fortune;<BR>a shell-shaped neck.<BR>—कम्बु-पुष्पी and कम्बु-<BR>मालिनी, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—कम्बु-आतायिन्, ई, m.<BR>the bird Falco Cheela.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बुक|कंबुकः|कम्बुकः
कम्बुक, अस्, m. a conch, a shell; a mean per-<BR>son; (आ), f. the tree Physalis Flexuosa; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बू|कंबू
कम्बू कम्बू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (said to be fr. 2. कम्),<BR>stealing; (ऊस्), m. a thief, a plunderer; a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बूक
कम्बूक कम्बूक, अस्, m., Ved. the husk of<BR>rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बोज|कंबोज|कंबोजः|कम्बोजः
कम्बोज कम्बोज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a country<BR>and its inhabitants; (अस्), m. the prince of this<BR>country; a shell; a kind of shell; a species of<BR>elephant; [cf. कम्बु and काम्बोज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्भारी
कम्भारी कम्भारी, f. = गम्भारी, the plant<BR>Gmelina Arborea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्भु|कंभु
कम्भु कम्भु, उ, n. the fragrant root of<BR>Andropogon Muricatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कय
कय कय, a Vedic form for 2. क, occurring<BR>only in the genitive case with चिद्; e. g. कयस्य चिद्,<BR>of every one; (नि षू नम अतिमतिम् कयस्य<BR>चित्, bow well down the haughtiness of every one);<BR>[cf. Zend kaya; Armen. ui.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कयस्था
कयस्था कयस्था, f. a medicinal plant, =<BR>काकोली; (probably a various reading for वयस्था:<BR>cf. कायस्था.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कया
कया कया, ind., Ved. (fr. 2. क inst. fem.),<BR>in what manner?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कयाद्
कयाद् कयाद्, त्, त्, त् (fr. कय for काय? and<BR>rt. अद्), Ved. consuming the body; (a various reading<BR>for क्रव्याद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कयाधू
कयाधू कयाधू, ऊस्, f., N. of the wife of<BR>Hiraṇyakaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कय्य
कय्य कय्य, अस्, m., N. of a prince, founder<BR>of a sanctuary (श्रीकय्य-स्वामिन्) and of a Vihāra<BR>(कय्य-विहार) called after him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कय्यक
कय्यक कय्यक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर|करः
कर 1. कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. कृ, to do;<BR>for 2. कर see p. 205), who or what does or makes<BR>or causes; causing, doing, making (especially at the<BR>end of compounds, e. g. भयङ्-कर, causing fear,<BR>frightful; दुःख-कर, causing pain; वृद्धि-कर,<BR>causing increase; सम्पत्-कर, causing prosperity;<BR>अर्थ-करी विद्या, a science productive of wealth<BR>&c.); (अस्), m. the hand (‘the active one’); a<BR>measure, the breadth of twenty-four thumbs; an<BR>elephant's trunk; the act of doing, making, &c.;<BR>(at the end of several compounds with a passive<BR>sense, e. g. ईषत्-कर and सु-कर, easy to be<BR>done; दुष्-कर, difficult to be done; ईषद्-<BR>आढ्यङ्-कर, easy to be made rich); [cf. Lith. kaire,<BR>‘the left hand.’]<BR>—कर-कण्टक, अस्, m. a finger-<BR>nail (‘thorn of the hand’).<BR>—कर-कमल, अम्,<BR>n. the hand, especially of a lover or a mistress &c.<BR>(lit. ‘hand-lotus;’ similar compounds are कर-पद्-<BR>म, कर-पङ्कज, कर-पल्लव, &c.).<BR>—कर-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कर-कलश, अस्,<BR>m. the hand hollowed to receive water.<BR>—कर-<BR>किसलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. a hand which is like a<BR>branch; the finger (‘shoot of the hand’).<BR>—कर-<BR>कुद्मल, अम्, n. the finger (‘bud of the hand’).<BR>—कर-कोष, अस्, m. the hand hollowed to receive<BR>water; [cf. कर-कलश.] — 1. कर-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>(for 2. see under 2. कर, p. 205), taking the hand<BR>(of the bride in the marriage ceremony; one part of<BR>the ceremony of marriage is the placing of the right<BR>hand of the bride, with the palm uppermost, in the<BR>right hand of the bridegroom), marriage.<BR>—१. कर-<BR>ग्रहण, अम्, n. (for 2. see under 2. कर), taking<BR>the hand, marriage.<BR>—१. कर-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>taking the hand.<BR>—कर-घर्षण, अस्, m. a<BR>churning-stick; (अम्), n. rubbing the hands together.<BR>—कर-घर्षिन्, ई, m. the churning-stick.<BR>—कर-<BR>घाट, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous tree.<BR>—कर-<BR>च्छद, अस्, m. the teak tree, Trophis Aspera; (आ),<BR>f. a tree, commonly called सिन्दूर-पुष्पी-वृक्ष.<BR>—कर-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in or from the<BR>hand; (अस्), m. a finger-nail; N. of a timber tree,<BR>= करञ्ज or Pongamia Glabra; (अम्), n. a per-<BR>fume, = व्याघ्रनख, resembling a nail in appear-<BR>ance.<BR>—करज-वर्धन, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—करजाख्य (˚ज-आख्˚), अस्, m. a perfume, =<BR>कर-ज.<BR>—कर-ज्योडि, इस्, m., N. of a tree, =<BR>हस्त-ज्योडि.<BR>—कर-तल, अस्, m. the palm of the<BR>hand; करतली-कृ, to take in the palm of the hands.<BR>—करतल-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the hand or<BR>in one's possession.<BR>—करतल-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>held in the hand.<BR>—करतल-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>held in the hand, resting in the palm of the<BR>hand.<BR>—कर-तस्, ind. from the hand, out of the<BR>hand.<BR>—कर-ताल, अम्, n. a musical instrument,<BR>a cymbal; (ई), f. beating time by clapping the<BR>hands.<BR>—करतालक, अम्, n. a musical instru-<BR>ment, a cymbal.<BR>—करताल-ध्वनि, इस्, m. the<BR>sound of cymbals.<BR>—कर-तोया, f. the Karatoyā<BR>river in the north-east of Bengal, (at the wedding of<BR>Śiva and Pārvatī the water which had been poured<BR>into the hand of the former constituted, upon its<BR>being thrown on the ground, the source of this river.)<BR>—करतोयिनी, f., N. of a river, perhaps the same as<BR>the preceding (?) .<BR>—१. कर-द, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see<BR>under 2. कर), one who gives his hand &c.<BR>—कर-<BR>दक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, handy, dexterous, ready.<BR>—कर-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of a tree, = कारस्कर.<BR>—कर-<BR>धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, held or supported by the hand.<BR>—कर-निहित, अस्, आ, अम्, held in the hand.<BR>—क-<BR>रन्-धम, अस्, m., N. of two princes.<BR>—कर-<BR>न्यस्त-कपोलान्तम्, ind. the end of the cheek held<BR>in the hand.<BR>—कर-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a saw; splashing<BR>water about while bathing, playing or gamboling in<BR>water; see कर-पात्र.<BR>—करपत्त्रक, अम्, n. a<BR>saw.<BR>—करपत्त्र-वत्, आन्, m. the palmyra tree,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-c" target="_blank">Page0204-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Borassus Flabelliformis, (the leaves being compared<BR>to a saw.)<BR>—करपत्त्रिका, f. playing with water<BR>or in it, splashing it about &c.; [cf. कर-पत्त्र<BR>and कर-पात्र.]<BR>—कर-पर्ण, अस्, m., N. of<BR>two plants, commonly called भिण्डा-वृक्ष and<BR>रक्तैरण्ड.<BR>—कर-पल्लव, अस्, m. a finger, the<BR>hand; conversation with the fingers.<BR>—कर-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. splashing water about while bathing, throwing<BR>water about in sport; the hand hollowed so as to<BR>hold anything; [cf. कर-पत्त्र and करपत्त्रिका.]<BR>—कर-पाल, अस्, m. a sword, a scymitar (‘pro-<BR>tecting the hand’).<BR>—करपालिका, f. a cudgel, a<BR>short club or wooden sword, a sword or one-edged<BR>knife.<BR>—कर-पुट, अस्, m. joining the palms of<BR>the hands in token of respect; the hands joined and<BR>hollowed to receive anything.<BR>—कर-पृष्ठ, अम्,<BR>n. the back of the hand.<BR>—१. कर-प्रचेय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (for 2. see under 2. कर), to be held, to be<BR>taken hold of by the hand.<BR>—१. कर-प्रद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, giving the hand &c.<BR>—कर-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>held in the hand; obtained, secured.<BR>—करबाल<BR>and करवाल, अस्, m. (corruptions of कर-पाल),<BR>a sword, a scymitar; a finger-nail.<BR>—करबालिका, f.<BR>a small sword; [cf. करपालिका.]<BR>—कर-भञ्जक,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (a various reading has<BR>कर-भञ्जिक.)<BR>—कर-भाजन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—कर-भू, ऊस्, m. a finger-nail.<BR>—कर-<BR>भूषण, अम्, n. a bracelet, an ornament worn<BR>round the wrist.<BR>—कर-मर्द, अस्, ई, m. f. a<BR>small tree bearing an acid fruit, Carissa Carandas;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of this tree.<BR>—करमर्दक, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Carissa Carandas; see the preceding.<BR>—कर-माला, f. the hand used as a rosary, the<BR>joints of the fingers corresponding to the beads.<BR>—कर-मुक्त, अम्, n. (scil. अस्त्रम्) a missile<BR>weapon thrown with the hand, a dart, a javelin, &c.<BR>—कर-रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, stopped by the hand,<BR>held tight or fast.<BR>—कर-रुह, अस्, m. a finger-<BR>nail (growing from the hand).<BR>—करर्द्धि (˚र-<BR>ऋद्धि), इस्, f. a cymbal; a small musical instrument<BR>used for marking time, (a castanet?); clapping the<BR>hands together for that purpose; [cf. कर-ताल. ]<BR>—कर-वारक, अस्, m. an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—करवालिका, f. a small club; see करबालिका.<BR>—कर-वीर, अस्, m. a fragrant Oleander, Nerium<BR>Odorum; a species of Soma; a sword or scymitar;<BR>a particular magical formulary or spell for recovering<BR>or attracting back a missile weapon of mystic pro-<BR>perties after its discharge; a cemetery, a place for<BR>burning or interring the dead; N. of a Nāga; of a<BR>Daitya; of a mountain; of a town on the river<BR>Veṇvā, founded by Padma-varṇa; of a town on the<BR>river Dṛṣadvatī, the residence of Candra-śekhara;<BR>(आ), f. red arsenic; (ई), f. a woman who has borne<BR>a son, a mother; a good cow; N. of Aditi, the<BR>mother of the gods; (अम्), n. the flower of Nerium<BR>Odorum.<BR>—करवीरक, अस्, m. the poisonous root<BR>of the fragrant Oleander, a poison; the tree Ter-<BR>minalia Arjuna; a sword; N. of a Nāga.<BR>—कर-<BR>वीर-कन्द-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, m. a species of onion or<BR>bulb, = तैल-कन्द.<BR>—करवीर-पुर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a town founded by Padma-varṇa.<BR>—करवीर-<BR>भुजा, f. Cajanus Indicus.<BR>—कर-वीर्य, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a physician.<BR>—कर-शाखा, f. a finger.<BR>—कर-<BR>शीकर, अस्, m. water expelled by an elephant's<BR>trunk.<BR>—कर-शूक, अस्, m. a finger-nail.<BR>—कर-<BR>शोथ, अस्, m. œdematous swelling of the hands.<BR> — 1. कर-साद, अस्, m. languor or weakness of the<BR>hands.<BR>—कर-स्थालिन्, ई, m. an epithet of Śiva,<BR>who uses his hands as a vessel for holding food.<BR>—कर-स्वन, अस्, m. sound produced by beating<BR>the hands together.<BR>—कराग्र (˚र-अग्˚), अम्, n.<BR>the tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>—कराग्र-पल्लव,<BR>अस्, m. finger.<BR>—कराघात (˚र-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>thumb, a blow with the hand.<BR>—करा-मर्द, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Carissa Carandas; [cf. कर-मर्द.]<BR>—कराम्बुक or कराम्लक, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>same tree.<BR>—करारोट, अस्, m. a finger-ring; (fr. कर<BR>and?).<BR>—करार्पित (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taken in<BR>the hand.<BR>—करालम्ब (˚र-आल्˚), अस्, m. the act of<BR>supporting with the hand, giving a helping hand;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-a" target="_blank">Page0205-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), stretching out one's hand to support or<BR>raise another.<BR>—करालम्बन, अम्, n. extending<BR>the hand, taking by the hand, helping, sustaining.<BR>—करोत्पल (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n. a lotus-hand.<BR>—करोदक (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n. water held in or<BR>poured into the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0204-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करक|करकं|करकः
1. करक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the water-pot of the<BR>student or ascetic; the shell of the cocoa-nut hollowed<BR>to form a vessel; shell of the cocoa-nut in general;<BR>(अस्), m. hand; a species of bird; N. of several<BR>plants, the pomegranate tree, = दाडिम; Pongamia<BR>Glabra; Butea Frondosa; Bauhinia Variegata; Mi-<BR>musops Elengi; Capparis Aphylla; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people.<BR>—करक-पात्रिका, f. a leather vessel<BR>for holding water.<BR>—करकाम्भस् (˚क-अम्˚), आस्,<BR>m. the cocoa-nut tree, Cocos Nucifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण|करणं|करणः
करण, अस्, ई, अम्, doing, making, effecting,<BR>causing (especially at the end of compounds; cf.<BR>अन्त-करण, अन्धङ्-करण, उष्णङ्-करण,<BR>&c.); Ved. clever, skilled; (अस्), m., Ved. an assistant;<BR>a man of a mixed class, the son of a Śūdra woman by<BR>a Vaiśya, or (according to some) of an outcast Kṣa-<BR>triya (the occupation of this class is writing, accounts,<BR>&c.); a writer, a scribe; (अम्), n. making, doing,<BR>producing, effecting, accomplishing (very often as last<BR>member of a compound, e. g. मुष्टि-करण,<BR>committing theft; विरूप-करण, producing de-<BR>formity); an action, especially a religious action;<BR>business, occupation (as trade &c.); the special<BR>business of any tribe or caste; plastering, spreading<BR>anything with the hand; the usage or practice of<BR>the writer-caste; an act, a deed; an instrument or<BR>means of action, an expedient; an organ, an organ<BR>of sense or of speech; (in gram.) the immediate<BR>cause of an action, the idea expressed by the instru-<BR>mental case, instrumentality; the body; (in law)<BR>an instrument, document, a bond; a cause, motive;<BR>the posture of an ascetic; posture in sexual intercourse,<BR>copulation; pronunciation, articulation; (in gram.)<BR>the term used in designating a sound or word when<BR>referring to it as an independent part of speech or as<BR>separated from its context, (करण may be used in<BR>this way, like कार, e. g. इति-करण, the word इति);<BR>rhythm, time; dramatic action (?), singing (?); an<BR>astrological division of the day, (these Karaṇas are<BR>eleven, viz. वव, वालव, कौलव, तैतिल, गर,<BR>बणिज, विष्टि, शकुनि, चतुष्पद, किन्तुघ्न,<BR>and नाग, two being equal to a lunar day, or the<BR>time during which the moon's motion amounts to 6°;<BR>the first seven are called अ-ध्रुवाणि or movable, and<BR>fill, when eight times repeated, the space from the<BR>second half of the first day in the moon's increase to<BR>the first half of the fourteenth day in its wane; the<BR>four others are ध्रुवाणि or fixed, and occupy the<BR>four half-days from the second half of the fourteenth<BR>day in the wane of the moon to the first half of the<BR>first day in its increase); title of a treatise of Varā-<BR>ha-mihira on the motions of the planets; a field;<BR>grain (?); the mind or heart (?); (ई), f. a woman of a<BR>mixed caste; a surd or irrational number, a surd root<BR>in arithmetic.<BR>—करण-कुतूहल, अम्, n. title of a<BR>work on practical astronomy by Bhāskara.<BR>—करण-<BR>ग्राम, अस्, m. the senses collectively.<BR>—करण-<BR>त्राण, अम्, n. the head (‘protecting the organs of<BR>sense’).<BR>—करण-त्व, अम्, n. instrumentality, medi-<BR>ate agency.<BR>—करण-नियम, अस्, m. suppression or<BR>restraint of the organs of sense.<BR>—करण-विन्यय,<BR>अस्, m. manner of pronunciation.<BR>—करण-सार,<BR>अस्, m. title of a work on practical astronomy by<BR>Bhāskara.<BR>—करण-स्थान-भेद, अस्, m. differ-<BR>ence of articulation or organ.<BR>—करणाधिकार<BR>(˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, m. a section on articulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणि
करणि, इस्, f. doing, making, effecting (only oc-<BR>curring with अ privative, e. g. अ-करणि, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणीय|करणीयं
करणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done or made; feasi-<BR>ble, to be accomplished; to be caused or effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभ|करभः
करभ, अस्, m. the metacarpus, the hand from<BR>the wrist to the root of the fingers; the trunk of<BR>an elephant; a young elephant; a camel; a young<BR>camel or any young animal; a camel three years old;<BR>a perfume (= नख, commonly called नखि); an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">Page0205-b+ 79</a>]<BR>epithet of Danta-vakra, prince of the Karūṣas; (ई),<BR>f. a she-camel; the plant Tragia Involucrata; [cf. Gr.<BR>κάρπος]<BR>—करभ-काण्डिका, f., N. of a plant; [cf.<BR>उष्ट्र-काण्डी.]<BR>—करभ-प्रिया, f. a plant, a sort<BR>of Hedysarum.<BR>—करभ-वल्लभ, अस्, m. the<BR>tree Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—करभादनी (˚भ-<BR>अदन), f., N. of a plant; [cf. करभ-प्रिया.]<BR>—करभोरू (˚भ-ऊरु), ऊस्, f. a woman whose<BR>thighs resemble the trunk of an elephant; see ऊरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभक|करभकः
करभक, अस्, m., N. of a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभिन्
करभिन्, ई, m. an elephant (‘having a trunk’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करस्
करस्, अस्, n., Ved. an action, a deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करस्न
करस्न, अस्, m., Ved. the arm, the fore part of<BR>the arm; a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करि
करि, इस्, इस्, इ, causing, accomplishing (at the end<BR>of a compound, e. g. शकृत्-करि, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिका
करिका, f. a wound caused by a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिन्
करिन्, ई, m. ‘having a trunk,’ an elephant; (णी),<BR>f. a female elephant.<BR>—करि-कणा-वल्ली, f. a species<BR>of pepper, Piper Chaba.<BR>—करि-कुम्भ, अस्, m. the<BR>frontal globe of an elephant.<BR>—करि-कुसुम्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a fragrant powder prepared from the flowers of<BR>Nāga-keśara.<BR>—करि-कुसुम्भक, अस्, m. the same.<BR>—करि-गर्जित, अम्, n. the roaring of elephants.<BR>—करि-चर्मन्, अ, n. an elephant's hide.<BR>—करि-ज,<BR>अस्, m. a young elephant.<BR>—करिणी-सहाय, अस्, m.<BR>the mate of the female elephant.<BR>—करि-दन्त, अस्,<BR>m. an elephant's tusk; ivory.<BR>—करि-दारक, अस्, m. a<BR>lion.<BR>—करि-नासिका, f. a musical instrument.<BR>—करि-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a plant; see तालीश-पत्त्र.<BR>—करि-पथ, अस्, m. the way or habits of an<BR>elephant.<BR>—करि-पिप्पली, f. a plant bearing a pun-<BR>gent fruit, Pothos Officinalis.<BR>—करि-पोत, अस्, m. a<BR>young elephant, one under ten years old.<BR>—करि-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. the post to which an elephant is<BR>tied.<BR>—करि-मकर, अस्, m. a fabulous monster.<BR>—करि-माचल, अस्, m. a lion, this animal being<BR>considered as the natural enemy and destroyer of the<BR>elephant; [cf. गज-माचल.]<BR>—करि-मुख, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Gaṇeśa, this deity having an ele-<BR>phant's trunk on his face.<BR>—करि-यादस्, n. a water-<BR>elephant, a hippopotamos.<BR>—करि-वर, अस्, m. an<BR>excellent elephant.<BR>—करि-वैजयन्ती, f. a flag car-<BR>ried by an elephant.<BR>—करि-शावक, अस्, m. a young<BR>elephant under five years old, (according to some)<BR>also until ten years.<BR>—करि-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a troop<BR>of elephants.<BR>—करीन्द्र (˚रि-इन्˚), अस्, m. a large ele-<BR>phant, a war or state elephant; Indra's elephant (?) .<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर|करः
कर 2. कर, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. कॄ, to scatter;<BR>for 1. कर see p. 204), a ray of light, a sun-beam,<BR>a moon-beam; hail; royal revenue, toll, tax, import,<BR>tribute.<BR>—२. कर-ग्रह, अस्, m. levying or gathering<BR>taxes, a tax-gatherer.<BR>—२. कर-ग्रहण, अम्, n.<BR>levying or gathering taxes.<BR>—२. कर-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, levying a tax, a tax-collector.<BR>—कर-जाल, अम्, n. a<BR>pencil of rays, a stream of light.<BR>—२. कर-द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, paying taxes, subject to tax or duty, tributary.<BR>—करदी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to render tributary.<BR>—करदी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>tributary, subjugated.<BR>—कर-पण्य, अम्, n. a com-<BR>modity given as tribute.<BR>—२. कर-प्रचेय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be collected by taxes.<BR>—२. कर-प्रद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, paying taxes, subject to tax or duty, tributary.<BR>—कर-रुध्, त्, त्, त्, ray-obstructing.<BR>—२. कर-<BR>साद, अस्, m. the fading away of rays.<BR>—करोत्कर<BR>(˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m. a bundle of rays; a heavy tax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करक|करकं|करकः
2. करक, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. (according to some<BR>only m. and f.), hail; a thunderstone (?); (अस्), m.<BR>toll, tax, tribute (?).<BR>—१. करकासार (˚क-आस्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a shower of hail.<BR>—२. करकासार, nom. P. क-<BR>रकासारति, to pour or shower down like hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीकृ
करी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to offer as a tribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर|करः
कर 3. कर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. कृ, to<BR>praise), Ved. devoted, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

