करञ्ज|करंज|करंजः|करञ्जः
करञ्ज करञ्ज, अस्, m. the tree Pongamia<BR>Glabra, used medicinally; N. of an enemy of Indra,<BR>slain by this god.<BR>—करञ्ज-फलक, अस्, m. Fero-<BR>nia Elephantum; see कपित्थ.<BR>—करञ्ज-ह, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. pernicious to Karañja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करञ्जक|करञ्जकः
करञ्जक, अस्, m., N. of the tree Pongamia<BR>Glabra; also of Verbesina Scandens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करट|करटः
करट करट, अस्, m. an elephant's cheek;<BR>a crow; a man of a low or degraded profession; a<BR>bad Brāhman; an atheist, an unbeliever, an impugner<BR>of the doctrines of the Vedas; a musical instrument<BR>(castanets?); the plant Carthamus Tinctorius; the<BR>first Śrāddha or ceremony performed in honour of a<BR>deceased relative; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; also<BR>of a family; (आ), f. an elephant's cheek; a cow<BR>difficult to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

