कराल|करालं|करालः
कराल कराल, अस्, आ, अम्, opening wide,<BR>cleaving asunder, gaping (as a wound); having for-<BR>midable projecting teeth, formidable, dreadful, terrible<BR>(especially as an epithet of the Rākṣasas, of Śiva, of<BR>Kāla, of Viṣṇu, and of a certain Devagandharva);<BR>great, large, high, lofty; spacious, wide; deformed;<BR>(अस्), m. a certain species of animal; resin, pitch, or<BR>a mixture of oil and the resin of the tree Shorea<BR>Robusta; N. of a region; (आ), f. the plant Hemi-<BR>desmus Indicus; an epithet of Durgā; N. of a certain<BR>woman; (ई), f. one of the seven tongues and nine<BR>Samidhs of Agni; (अम्), n. a kind of Ocimum.<BR>—कराल-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a powerful arm<BR>or hand; having a large trunk, as an elephant.<BR>—कराल-केशर, अस्, m., N. of a lion in the<BR>Pañcatantra.<BR>—कराल-त्रिपुटा, f. a species of corn.<BR>—कराल-दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having terrific<BR>teeth.<BR>—कराल-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, terrific.<BR>—क-<BR>राल-वदना, f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—करालानन<BR>(˚ल-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, terrific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालक|करालकः
करालक, अम्, n. a kind of Ocimum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालिक|करालिकः
करालिक, अस्, m. a tree; a sword; (आ), f. an<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालित
करालित, अस्, आ, अम्, rendered formidable; afraid<BR>of, alarmed by or at; magnified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करि
करि करि, &c. See under 1. कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिभ
करिभ करिभ, अस्, m. the tree Ficus Re-<BR>ligiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिर|करिरः
करिर करिर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the shoot of a<BR>bamboo. See करीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्ठ
करिष्ठ करिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superlative fr. 1.<BR>कर), doing most, doing very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्णु
करिष्णु, used in comp. See अलङ्-करिष्णु<BR>and निर्-आकरिष्णु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्य
करिष्य, अस्, आ, अम् (?) , Ved. to be done (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्यत्|करिष्यन्त्
करिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, willing to do,<BR>about to do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्यमाण
करिष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, about to do, going<BR>to do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीयस्
करीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (comparative fr. 1. कर),<BR>doing more; one who does much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीकृ
करीकृ करी-कृ. See under 2. कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीति
करीति करीति, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीर|करीरः
करीर करीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. 1. कॄ), the shoot of a bamboo; (अस्), m. a water-<BR>jar; a thorny plant, described as growing in deserts<BR>and fed upon by camels, Capparisaphylla; (अम्), n.<BR>the fruit of this plant; (आ or ई), f. the root of an<BR>elephant's tusk; a cricket, a small grasshopper.<BR>—करीर-कुण, अस्, m. the fruit season of Cap-<BR>parisaphylla.<BR>—करीर-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>town; (a various reading has करीरि-प्रस्थ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरिका
करीरिका, f. the root of an elephant's tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरक|करीरकं
करीरक करीरक, अम्, n. fight, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीलदेश
करीलदेश करील-देश, अस्, m., N. of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीष|करीषं|करीषः
करीष करीष, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. 1. कॄ), rub-<BR>bish, refuse, dung; dry cow-dung; N. of a mountain;<BR>[cf. आखु-करीष.]<BR>—करीष-गन्धि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—करीषङ्-कष, अस्, आ, अम्, sweeping<BR>away dung; (आ), f. a strong wind, a gale.<BR>—करी-<BR>षाग्नि (˚ष-अग्˚), इस्, m. a fire of dry cow-dung;<BR>(this substance is very generally used as fuel in<BR>Hindūstan.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषक
करीषक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषिन्
करीषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, abounding in dung; (इणी), f.<BR>a region abounding in cow-dung; N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुण|करुणः
करुण करुण, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. कॄ, but in some of its meanings fr. 1. कृ), mourn-<BR>ful, miserable, lamenting; (अम्), ind. mournfully,<BR>wofully, pitifully, in distress; (अस्), m. that which<BR>causes pity, sorrow, affliction, tenderness, pity, com-<BR>passion; one of the nine Rasas or sentiments of a<BR>poem, the pathetic sentiment; a fruit tree, the<BR>pamplemousse^1, Citrus Decumana; N. of a Buddha;<BR>a Jaina saint; N. of an Asura; (आ), f. pity, com-<BR>passion; (ई), f., N. of a plant, also called ग्रीष्म-<BR>पुष्पी, चारिणी, &c.; (अम्), n., Ved. an action, a<BR>holy work.<BR>—करुण-ध्वनि, इस्, m. a cry of<BR>distress.<BR>—करुण-पुण्डरीक, अम्, n. title of a<BR>Buddhist work.<BR>—करुण-मल्ली, f. the plant Jasmi-<BR>num Sambac; also read करुणा-मल्ली.<BR>—करुण-<BR>वेदि-त्व, अम्, n. compassion, sympathy.<BR>—करुण-<BR>वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, knowing affliction or distress,<BR>sympathising, pitiful.<BR>—करुणाकर (˚ण-आक्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the father of Padmanābha.<BR>—करुणात्मक<BR>(˚ण-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, compassionate, tender-hearted.<BR>—करुणात्मन् (˚ण-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, kind.<BR>—क-<BR>रुणा-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, compassionate, tender.<BR>—करुणा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, gentle, compassionate.<BR>—करुणारम्भ (˚ण-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, engaging<BR>in deplorable actions.<BR>—करुणार्द्र (˚ण-आर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, tender-hearted, soft, sensitive.<BR>—करुणार्-<BR>धित (˚ण-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, kind.<BR>—करुणा-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, being in a pitiful state, pitiable.<BR>—करुणा-<BR>विप्रलम्भ, अस्, m. grief of separation with the un-<BR>certainty of meeting again, fears occurring in absence.<BR>—करुणा-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, disposed to pity.<BR>—क-<BR>रुणा-वेदिता, f. charitableness, kindliness, sympathy.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणाय
करुणाय, nom. P. A. -णायति, -ते, -यितुम्, to<BR>be in a pitiful condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणिन्
करुणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being in a pitiful condition,<BR>pitiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुत्थाम
करुत्थाम करुत्थाम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince, a son of Dushyanta and father of Ākrīḍa;<BR>[cf. अश्वत्थामन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुन्धक
करुन्धक करुन्धक, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Śūra and brother of Vasu-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुम
करुम करुम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. an epithet<BR>of certain spectral or ghost-like appearances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करूकर
करूकर करूकर, अम्, n., Ved. the joint of<BR>the neck and the chine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करूळतिन्
करूळतिन् करूऌअतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. one whose<BR>teeth are decayed and broken; [cf. the next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करूष|करूषः
करूष करूष, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>descended from a son of Manu Vaivasvata, (a prince<BR>of this people is named Danta-vakra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करूषक
करूषक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Manu Vaiva-<BR>svata; (अम्), n., N. of a species of fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेट|करेटः
करेट करेट, अस्, m. a finger-nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटव्या
करेटव्या करेटव्या, f. or करेटु, उस्, m. the<BR>numidian crane; [cf. करटु, कर्कट, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणु|करेणुः
करेणु करेणु, उस्, m. f. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>कृ; cf. 1. कर), a male or female elephant, gene-<BR>rally used for the latter; according to some also<BR>करेणू; (उस्), m. the tree Pterospermum Aceri-<BR>folium; (उस्), f., N. of a plant used as a drug and<BR>supposed to grow in Kāśmīra.<BR>—करेणु-पाल, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">Page0206-c+ 76</a>]<BR>m. the groom or keeper of a female elephant; N. of<BR>a man; [cf. कारेणुपालि.]<BR>—करेणु-भू, ऊस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Pālakāpya.<BR>—करेणु-मती, f., N. of the<BR>wife of Nakula, daughter of a king of Cedi.<BR>—क-<BR>रेणु-वर्य, अस्, m. a large or powerful elephant.<BR>—करेणु-सुत, अस्, m. an epithet of Pālakāpya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुक|करेणुकं
करेणुक, अम्, n. the poisonous fruit of the<BR>plant Kareṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणू
करेणू, ऊस्, m. f. a male or female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेनर|करेनरः
करेनर करेनर, अस्, m. benzoin or storax.<BR>See करेवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेन्दुक|करेन्दुकः
करेन्दुक करेन्दुक, अस्, m. a species of<BR>grass, = भू-तृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेवर|करेवरः
करेवर करेवर, अस्, m. benzoin or storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोट|करोटं
करोट करोट, अस्, m. f. a basin, a cup; the<BR>bones of the head, the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोटक
करोटक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोटि|करोटिः
करोटि, इस्, or करोटी, f. a basin, a cup; the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोत्कर
करोत्कर करोत्कर, करोत्पल, &c. See<BR>under 1. and 2. कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क्
कर्क् कर्क्, to laugh; a Sautra root, or<BR>one occurring in grammatical Sūtras but<BR>not in the Dhātu-pāṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क|कर्कः
कर्क कर्क, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. 1. कृ),<BR>white; good; excellent; (अस्), m. a white horse; a<BR>crab; the sign Cancer; a water-jar; fire; a mirror;<BR>N. of various plants, = कर्कट, कर्केतन, and<BR>कर्केतिल; beauty; N. of a commentator on Kātyā-<BR>yana's Śrauta-sūtras; (ई), f., Ved. a white cow (?).<BR>—कर्क-खण्ड, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—कर्क-चिर्भिटी (?), f. a small cucumber.<BR>—कर्क-<BR>फल, अम्, n., N. of a plant.<BR>—कर्क-सार, अम्,<BR>n. flour or meal mixed with curds.<BR>—कर्की-प्रस्थ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कट|कर्कटः
कर्कट, अस्, m. a crab; the sign Cancer; a kind<BR>of bird, the numidian crane, Lanius Excubitor; N.<BR>of a plant with poisonous tubers, the fibrous root of<BR>a lotus; the curved end of the beam of a balance (to<BR>which the strings supporting the scale are attached);<BR>a kind of coitus; the radius of a circle; compass,<BR>circuit; (आ), f. the plant Momordica Mixta; (ई), f.<BR>a female crab; a snake (?); a kind of cucumber,<BR>Cucumis Utilissimus; the fruit of the plant Bombax<BR>Heptaphyllum; the curved end of the beam of a<BR>balance &c.; a small water-jar; [cf. कर्कर, कर्-<BR>कश; cf. also Gr. καρκῖνος; Lat. cancer.]<BR>—कर्कट-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—कर्कट-शृङ्ग,<BR>अम्, n. the claw of a crab.<BR>—कर्कट-शृङ्गिका or<BR>कर्कट-शृङ्गी, f. a plant, the fruit of which is<BR>compared to the claw or feelers of a crab, the horn<BR>of a goat &c., see अज-शृङ्गी; other names of this<BR>plant are काम-नाशिनी, कौलीरा, कुलिङ्गी, &c.<BR>—कर्कटाक्ष (˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, m. the plant Cucu-<BR>mis Utilissimus.<BR>—कर्कटाख्या (˚ट-आख्˚), f. the<BR>plant Karkaṭa-śriṅgī.<BR>—कर्कटाङ्गा (˚ट-अङ्˚), f.<BR>the same plant.<BR>—कर्कटास्थि (˚ट-अस्˚), n. the shell<BR>or crust of a crab.<BR>—कर्कटाह्व (˚ट-आह्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the plant Ægle Marmelos; (आ), f. the plant Karkaṭa-<BR>śṛṅgī.<BR>—कर्कटेश (˚ट-ईश), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>sanctuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटक|कर्कटकः
कर्कटक, अस्, m. a crab; the sign Cancer; the<BR>plant Momordica Mixta (?); a kind of sugar-cane; a<BR>hook shaped like the claw of a crab; N. of a Nāga;<BR>(ई), f. a female crab; (अम्), n. a poisonous root; a<BR>particular fracture of the bones.<BR>—कर्कटक-रज्जु,<BR>उस्, m. a rope with a hook attached to it, shaped like<BR>the claw of a crab.<BR>—कर्कटकास्थि (˚क-अस्˚), n.<BR>the shell or crust of a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटि|कर्कटिः
कर्कटि, इस्, f. a sort of cucumber, Cucumis Uti-<BR>lissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटिका
कर्कटिका, f., N. of a plant, a kind of gourd; a<BR>kernel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटिनी
कर्कटिनी, f. the plant Curcuma Xanthorrhiza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटु|कर्कटुः
कर्कटु, उस्, m. the numidian crane; [cf. करटु,<BR>&c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कन्धु|कर्कंधु|कर्कंधुः|कर्कन्धुः
कर्कन्धु कर्कन्धु, उस्, ऊस्, m. f. (considered<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">Page0207-a+ 71</a>]<BR>by some as an irregular compound of कर्क and<BR>अन्धु), the jujube tree, Zizyphus Jujuba; a species<BR>of this tree with a larger fruit; (उ), n. the fruit of<BR>this tree, or the uneatable fruits of a wild species;<BR>(ऊस्), f. the berry of this tree; (उस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—कर्कन्धु-कुण, अम्, n. the fruit season<BR>of the Karkandhu tree.<BR>—कर्कन्धु-प्रस्थ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a town.<BR>—कर्कन्धु-मती, f., N. of a<BR>woman (?).<BR>—कर्कन्धु-रोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, red<BR>like the berries of the jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कफल
कर्कफल कर्क-फल. See under कर्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कर|कर्करं|कर्करः
कर्कर कर्कर, अस्, आ, अम्, hard, firm; (अस्),<BR>m. a bone; a hammer; a mirror [cf. कर्फर];<BR>a strap of leather (?); N. of a Nāga; (अम्), n. stone,<BR>limestone, especially the nodule found in Bengal un-<BR>der the name of Kaṅkar; [cf. कर्कट, कर्कश.]<BR>—कर्कराक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, m. a wagtail.<BR>—कर्कराङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a kind of bird, a<BR>gallinule (?).<BR>—कर्करान्धुक (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a blind well, one of which the mouth is overgrown<BR>with grass &c. so as to be hidden; also read कर्क-<BR>रान्धक; see अन्ध-कूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटु|कर्कराटुः
कर्कराटु कर्कराटु, उस्, m. a glance, a side-<BR>look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटुक|कर्कराटुकः
कर्कराटुक कर्कराटुक, अस्, m. the numi-<BR>dian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेटु|कर्करेटुः
कर्करेटु, उस्, m. = the preceding; [cf. करटु,<BR>&c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराल|कर्करालः
कर्कराल कर्कराल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a curl, a<BR>ringlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करि|कर्करिः
कर्करि कर्करि, इस् or ई, f., Ved. a kind of<BR>musical instrument, a lute; (ई), f. a water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करीका
कर्करीका, f. a small water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेट|कर्करेटं
कर्करेट कर्करेट, अम्, n. the hand curved<BR>as a claw for the purpose of grasping anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेटु|कर्करेटुः
कर्करेटु कर्करेटु. See कर्कराटुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कश|कर्कशः
कर्कश कर्कश, अस्, आ, अम्, hard, harsh,<BR>rough (opposed to कोमल, श्लक्ष्ण); intangible;<BR>violent, cruel; unfeeling, unmerciful; harsh, unkind,<BR>miserly; (अस्), m. a sword, a scymitar; N. of several<BR>plants, = काम्पिल्ल = गुण्डारोचनी (commonly called<BR>Sunda Rochani); a kind of cassia, Cassia or Senna<BR>Esculenta; a species of sugar-cane; (आ), f. a thorny<BR>plant, Tragia Involucrata; (ई), f. the wild jujube; [cf.<BR>कर्कट, कर्कर.]<BR>—कर्कश-च्छद, अस्, m. the<BR>plants Trophis Aspera and Trichosanthes Diœca;<BR>(आ), f. the plant Luffa Acutangula.<BR>—कर्कश-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. hardness, harshness, rough manners.<BR>—कर्-<BR>कश-दल, अस्, m. the plant Trichosanthes Diœca;<BR>(आ), f. another plant.<BR>—कर्कश-वाक्य, अम्, n.<BR>harsh or contumelious speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशिका
कर्कशिका, f. wild jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कसार|कर्कसारं
कर्कसार कर्क-सार. See under कर्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कारु|कर्कारुः
कर्कारु कर्कारु, उस्, उ, m. n. a kind of<BR>gourd, Beninkasa Cerifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कारुक|कर्कारुकः
कर्कारुक, अस्, m. the plant Convolvulus Pani-<BR>culatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कि|कर्किः|कर्क्कि
कर्कि कर्कि, इस्, m. the sign of the zodiac,<BR>Cancer; also read कर्किन्, ई, m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कीप्रस्थ
कर्कीप्रस्थ कर्की-प्रस्थ. See under कर्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्केतन|कर्केतनं|कर्केतनः
कर्केतन कर्केतन or कर्केतर, अस्, m. (?)<BR>a kind of gem or precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोट|कर्कोटः
कर्कोट कर्कोट, अस्, m. one of the principal<BR>serpents or Nāgas of Pātāla; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (अम्), n. a poisonous fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोटक|कर्कोटकः
कर्कोटक, अस्, m. several plants, Momordica<BR>Mixta; Ægle Marmelos; the sugar-cane; N. of a<BR>Nāga or serpent; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a barbarous<BR>tribe of low origin; (ई), f., N. of a plant; (का), f.<BR>the plant Momordica Mixta.<BR>—कर्कोटक-विष,<BR>अम्, n. the poison of Karkoṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूर|कर्चूरः|कर्च्चूरं|कर्च्चूरः
कर्चूर कर्चूर, अस्, m., N. of a plant, a kind<BR>of Curcuma; (अम्), n. gold; an orpiment; [cf. कर्-<BR>बुर and कर्बूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूरक|कर्चूरकः|कर्च्चूरकः
कर्चूरक, अस्, m. the plant Curcuma Zerumbet;<BR>also read कर्बूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ज्
कर्ज् कर्ज्, cl. 1. P. कर्जति, -जितुम्, to<BR>pain or make uneasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण्
कर्ण् कर्ण्, cl. 10. P. कर्णयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to pierce, bore. See आ-कर्ण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण कर्ण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. कॄ),<BR>the ear, the handle or ear of a vessel; the helm or<BR>rudder of a ship; the plants Cassia Fistula and Calo-<BR>tropis Gigantea; (in prosody) a spondee, a foot of<BR>two long syllables; (in geometry) the hypothenuse<BR>of a triangle or the diagonal of a tetragon; N. of a<BR>renowned hero in the Mahā-bhārata, king of Aṅga<BR>and elder brother by the mother's side of the Pāṇḍu<BR>princes, being the son of the god Sūrya by Pṛthā or<BR>Kuntī, before her marriage with Pāṇḍu. (Afraid of<BR>the censure of her relatives, Kuntī deserted the child<BR>and exposed it in the river, where it was found by a<BR>charioteer named Adhi-ratha and nurtured by his<BR>wife Rādhā; hence कर्ण is sometimes called Sūta-<BR>putra or Sūta-ja, sometimes Rādheya, though named<BR>by his foster-parents Vasu-ṣeṇa); N. of a son of<BR>Viśvajit; (with Buddhists) a son of Mahā-sammata<BR>and king in Potāla; N. of a king, father of Viśoka-<BR>deva; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. eared, furnished with long<BR>ears; furnished with chaff (as grain). कर्णे, (in<BR>theatrical language) into the ear, in a low voice,<BR>aside; अपि कर्णे, Ved. behind the ear or back,<BR>from behind, after [cf. अपि-कर्ण]; कर्णं दा,<BR>to give ear to, listen to; कर्णम् आ-गम्, to come<BR>to one's ears, become known to.<BR>—कर्ण-कण्डु,<BR>उस् or ऊ, ऊस्, m. f. painful itching of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>कीटा, f. an insect or worm with many feet and of a<BR>reddish colour, Julus Cornifex; a small centipede;<BR>according to some कर्ण-कीटी.<BR>—कर्ण-कुब्ज, अम्,<BR>n., N. of an imaginary town.<BR>—कर्ण-क्ष्वेड, अस्,<BR>m. an affection of the ear, a roaring or constant<BR>noise in it.<BR>—कर्ण-खरिक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Vaiśya.<BR>—कर्ण-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, touching the ear,<BR>hanging on it, next to the ear, extending to the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-गूथ, अम्, n. ear-wax; (अस्), m. or<BR>कर्ण-गूथक, अस्, m. hardening of the wax of the<BR>ear.<BR>—कर्ण-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, seized by the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-गृह्य, ind. seizing by the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, perceptible to the ear, audible.<BR>—कर्ण-ग्राह, अस्, m. a helmsman.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>ग्राह-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with a helmsman<BR>(as a ship).<BR>—कर्ण-च्छिद्र, अम्, n. the outer<BR>auditory passage; [cf. कर्ण-पुट, कर्ण-रन्ध्र,<BR>&c.]<BR>—कर्ण-जप, अस्, m. ‘ear-whisperer,’ an in-<BR>former.<BR>—कर्ण-जलूका, f. an insect, Julus; a small<BR>centipede; [cf. कर्ण-कीटा.]<BR>—कर्ण-जलौका, f. or<BR>कर्ण-जलौकस्, आस्, f. the same.<BR>—कर्ण-जाप or<BR>कर्ण-जप, अस्, m. whispering in the ear, tale-<BR>bearing, calumniating.<BR>—कर्ण-जाह, अम्, n. the<BR>root of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-जित्, त्, m. ‘the conqueror<BR>of Karṇa,’ an epithet of Arjuna; (Karṇa having<BR>taken the part of the Kurus, was killed by Arjuna in<BR>one of the great battles between them and the<BR>Pāṇḍus.)<BR>—कर्ण-तस्, ind. away from the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-ताल, अस्, m. the flapping of an elephant's<BR>ears.<BR>—कर्ण-दर्पण, अस्, m. an ear-ring, an<BR>ornament for the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-दुन्दुभि, इस्, f. a<BR>kind of worm (making a noise in the ear like a<BR>drum); see कर्ण-कीटा.<BR>—कर्ण-देव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—कर्ण-धार, अस्, m. a helmsman, a<BR>pilot.<BR>—कर्णधार-ता, f. the office of an helms-<BR>man.<BR>—कर्ण-धारिणी, f. a female elephant.<BR>—कर्ण-नाद, अस्, m. ringing in the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>नासा, f. the ears and the nose.<BR>—कर्णन्दु, उस्, f.<BR>a woman's ear-ring; see कर्णान्दु.<BR>—कर्ण-प,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कर्ण-पत्त्रक, अस्, m.<BR>the tragus, a part of the external ear.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>पथ, अस्, m. the compass or range of hearing;<BR>कर्णपथम् आ-या or उपे (उप-इ), to come within<BR>the range of the ear, to be heard.<BR>—कर्ण-पर,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-c" target="_blank">Page0207-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. an ornament for the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-परम्-<BR>परा, f. going from one ear to another.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>पराक्रम, अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>पर्वन्, अ, n. ‘the Karṇa section,’ title of the<BR>eighth book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—कर्ण-पाक,<BR>अस्, m. inflammation of the outer ear.<BR>—कर्ण-पालि,<BR>इस्, f. the lobe of the ear; the outer and curving<BR>edge of the ear; (ई), f. an ornament of the ear, a<BR>garland or string of jewels pendent from it; N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—कर्ण-पाश, अस्, m. a beautiful ear.<BR>—कर्-<BR>ण-पुट, अम्, n. the auditory passage of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-पुर्, ऊर्, f. or कर्ण-पुरी, f. the capital<BR>of Karṇa, i. e. Campā, the ancient N. of Bhagalpur.<BR>—कर्ण-पुष्प, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = मोरट.<BR>—कर्ण-पूर, अस्, m. an ornament of flowers worn<BR>round the ears; an ear-ring; N. of several plants,<BR>blue lotus; Acacia Sirissa; Jonesia Aśoka; N. of the<BR>father of Kavicandra, author of the Alaṅkāra Kau-<BR>stubha.<BR>—कर्ण-पूरक, अस्, m. the Kadamba<BR>tree, Nauclea Cadamba; N. of a servant.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>पूरण, अम्, n. the act of filling the ears (with<BR>cotton &c.); any substance used for that purpose;<BR>(अस्), m. = कर्ण-पूर.<BR>—कर्ण-प्रतिनाह or<BR>कर्ण-प्रतीनाह, अस्, m. a disease of the ear, sup-<BR>pression of its excretion or wax, which is supposed<BR>to have dissolved and pass by the nose and mouth.<BR>—कर्ण-प्रयाग, अस्, m., N. of the confluence of<BR>the river Gaṅgā and Pindar.<BR>—कर्ण-प्रान्त, अस्,<BR>m. the lobe of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-प्रावरण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, using the ears for a covering; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a fabulous people.<BR>—कर्ण-फल, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>fish, Ophiocephalus Kurrawey.<BR>—कर्ण-भूषण,<BR>अम्, n. or कर्ण-भूषा, f. an ear ornament.<BR>—कर्ण-मद्गुर, अस्, m. a sort of sheat fish,<BR>Silurus Unitus.<BR>—कर्ण-मल, अम्, n. the excretion<BR>or wax of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-मुकुर, अस्, m. an ear<BR>ornament; an ear-ring.<BR>—कर्ण-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>headed by Karṇa, having Karṇa as leader.<BR>—कर्ण-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. the root of the ear.<BR>—कर्णमूलीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, near the root of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-मोटि,<BR>इस्, f. an epithet of Devī or Durgā in one of her<BR>forms or incarnations (Cāmuṇḍā).<BR>—कर्ण-योनि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having the ear as a source or starting-<BR>point, going forth from the ear, an epithet of an<BR>arrow, because in shooting the bow-string is drawn<BR>back to the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-रन्ध्र, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>the orifice or auditory passage of the ear; [cf. कर्ण-<BR>च्छिद्र, कर्ण-पुट, &c.]<BR>—कर्ण-रोग, अस्, m.<BR>disease of the ear.<BR>—कर्णरोग-प्रतिषेध, अस्,<BR>m. cure of a disease of the ear.<BR>—कर्णरोग-<BR>विज्ञान, अम्, n. diagnosis of any disease of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-लता, f. or कर्ण-लतिका, f. the lobe of<BR>the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-वंश, अस्, m. an elevated plat-<BR>form of bamboo.<BR>—कर्ण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>ears, long-eared; furnished with tendrils or hooks;<BR>having a helm.<BR>—कर्ण-वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, earless;<BR>(अस्), m. a snake.<BR>—कर्णविट्क, अस्, आ, अम्, fur-<BR>nished with ear-wax.<BR>—कर्ण-विद्रधि, इस्, f. ulcer-<BR>ation of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-विवर, अम्, n. the audi-<BR>tory passage of the ear.<BR>—कर्ण-विष्, ट्, f. ear-wax.<BR>—कर्ण-वेध, अस्, m. ‘ear-piercing,’ a religious<BR>ceremony performed to prevent a person from dying,<BR>if the birth of a third son be expected; piercing the<BR>ear to receive ear-rings.<BR>—कर्ण-वेधनी or कर्ण-<BR>वेधनिका, f. an instrument for piercing the ear of<BR>an elephant.<BR>—कर्ण-वेष्ट, अस्, m. an ear-ring;<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—कर्ण-वेष्टक, अस्, m. the flaps<BR>of a cap protecting the ear; (अस् or अम्), m. n. (?)<BR>an ear-ring.<BR>—कर्ण-वेष्टन, अम्, n. an ear-ring.<BR>—कर्ण-शष्कुली, f. the outer part of the ear, the<BR>exterior cartilaginous portion leading to the auditory<BR>passage.<BR>—कर्ण-शिरीष, अस्, m. a Śirīṣa flower<BR>fastened to the ear as an ornament.<BR>—कर्ण-शूल,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. ear-ache.<BR>—कर्णशूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>having ear-ache.<BR>—कर्ण-शोभन, अम्, n., Ved. an<BR>ear ornament.<BR>—कर्ण-श्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, audible,<BR>loud.<BR>—कर्ण-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—कर्ण-श्रुत्, त्, m., N. of the author of several<BR>hymns of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—कर्ण-संस्राव or कर्-<BR>ण-स्रव or कर्ण-स्राव, अस्, m. running of the<BR>ear, discharge of pus or ichorous matter from the ear.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">Page0208-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—कर्ण-सू, ऊस्, m. the father of Karṇa, an epithet<BR>of Sūrya or the sun.<BR>—कर्ण-सूचि, इस्, m. a kind of<BR>insect.<BR>—कर्ण-स्फोटा, f. a sort of creeper (com-<BR>monly काणफाटा).<BR>—कर्ण-कर्णि, ind. from ear<BR>to ear, whispering into each other's ears.<BR>—कर्-<BR>णाञ्जलि (˚ण-अञ्˚), इस्, m. the auditory passage of<BR>the outer ear.<BR>—कर्णाढक (˚ण-आढ्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this man.<BR>—कर्णादेश (˚ण-आद्˚), अस्, m. an ear-ring (?).<BR>—कर्णानुज (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira, the younger brother of Karṇa, one of<BR>the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>—कर्णान्तिक (˚ण-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, near or close to the ear.<BR>—कर्णान्दु<BR>(˚ण-अन्˚), उस् or ऊ, ऊस्, f. an ornament for the ear;<BR>an ear-ring.<BR>—कर्णाभरणक (˚ण-आभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the tree Cathartocarpus (Cassia) Fistula.<BR>—कर्-<BR>णारा (˚ण and rt. ऋ?), f. an instrument for perfo-<BR>rating the ear of an elephant.<BR>—कर्णारि (˚ण-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. an epithet of Arjuṇa (as the enemy of Karṇa);<BR>the tree Terminalia Arjuna.<BR>—कर्णार्पण (˚ण-<BR>अर्˚), अम्, n. applying the ear, giving ear, paying<BR>attention, listening to.<BR>—कर्णालङ्कार (˚ण-अल्˚),<BR>अस्, m. or कर्णालङ्क्रिया, f. or कर्णालङ्कृति, इस्,<BR>f. an ear ornament, an ear-ring.<BR>—कर्णाश्व (˚ण-<BR>अश्˚?), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कर्णास्फाल (˚ण-<BR>आस्˚), अस्, m. the flapping to and fro of an elephant's<BR>ears.<BR>—कर्णे-चुरुचुरा, f. tale-bearing.<BR>—कर्णे-<BR>जप, अस्, आ, अम्, a slanderous whisperer, a secret<BR>traducer, a tale-bearer, an informer.<BR>—कर्णे-टिरि-<BR>टिरा, f. tale-bearing.<BR>—कर्णेन्दु (˚ण-इन्˚), उस्,<BR>f. a semicircular ornament of the ear, an ear-ring;<BR>[cf. कर्णान्दु.]<BR>—कर्णोत्पल (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—कर्णोदय (˚ण-उद्˚), N. of a book.<BR>—कर्णोपकर्णिका (˚ण-उप्˚), f. a female tale-<BR>bearer or informer.<BR>—कर्णोर्ण (˚ण-ऊर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having wool on the ears (as any animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णक|कर्णकः
कर्णक, अस्, m., Ved. a prominence, handle, or<BR>projection on the side or sides (of a vessel &c.);<BR>a tendril; applied also to the legs when spread out;<BR>N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this<BR>man.<BR>—कर्णक-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. furnished<BR>with tendrils or side branches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकित
कर्णकित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with tendrils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णल|कर्णलः|कर्ण्णल
कर्णल, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिक|कर्णिकः
कर्णिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having ears, having large or<BR>long ears; having a helm; (अस्), m. a steersman;<BR>pl., N. of a people; N. of a king in Potāla; (आ), f.<BR>an ear-ring or ornament for the ear; a knot, tubercle;<BR>round protuberance (e. g. the round protuberance at<BR>the end of a reed or cane); the pericarp of a lotus;<BR>a fruit-stalk; the tip of an elephant's trunk; the<BR>middle finger; chalk; a pen or small brush; a trowel;<BR>the plants Premna Spinosa or Longifolia, and Odina<BR>Pinnata; a bawd; N. of an Apsaras; N. of the wife<BR>of Kaṅka.<BR>—कर्णिकाचल, अस्, m. an epithet of the<BR>fabulous mountain Meru; (fr. कर्णिका, the seed<BR>vessel of a lotus, and अचल, a mountain, Meru being<BR>in the centre of the world, the divisions of which<BR>are compared to the leaves of a lotus); also कर्णि-<BR>काद्रि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकार|कर्णिकारः|कर्ण्णिकार
कर्णिकार, अस्, m. the tree Pterospermum Aceri-<BR>folium; also Cassia Fistula; the pericarp of a lotus;<BR>(अम्), n. the flower of the tree Pterospermum Ace-<BR>rifolium and of Cassia Fistula.<BR>—कर्णिकार-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकिन्
कर्णिकिन्, ई, m. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिन्
कर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having ears, relating to the ear;<BR>long-eared; (at the end of compounds) having (any-<BR>thing) attached to the ear; furnished with flaps or<BR>anything similar (said of shoes); barbed, furnished<BR>with knots &c. (as an arrow); having a helm; (ई),<BR>m. the side of the neck, the part near the ear; a<BR>steersman; N. of a mountain, one of the seven prin-<BR>cipal ranges of the mountains, dividing the universe;<BR>(इनी), f. (scil. योनि) a disease of the uterus, prolapsus<BR>or polypus uteri.<BR>—कर्णी-रथ, अस्, m. (for कर्णि-<BR>रथ), a covered car, or (according to some) a litter<BR>for the conveyance of women &c., borne on men's<BR>shoulders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिल
कर्णिल, अस्, आ, अम्, long-eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णी
कर्णी, a fem. form related to कर्ण and appear-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">Page0208-b+ 75</a>]<BR>ing in compounds (e. g. अयस्-कर्णी).<BR>—कर्णी-सुत,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Kaṃsa, the enemy of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>according to the scholiast the author of a thieves'<BR>manual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण्य
कर्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in or at the ear; suita-<BR>ble to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाट|कर्णाटः
कर्णाट कर्णाट, आस्, m. pl., N. of a country<BR>and the people inhabiting it, whence the modern<BR>Karnatic; the name, however, was anciently applied<BR>to the central districts of the peninsula, including<BR>Mysore; (ई), f. a princess of Karṇāṭa; a plant, com-<BR>monly Haṃsapadī; one of the Rāgiṇīs or female<BR>personifications of the musical modes, the bride of<BR>the Rāga Mālava.<BR>—कर्णाट-देश, अस्, m. the<BR>Karṇāṭa country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाटक|कर्णाटकः
कर्णाटक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a country and the<BR>people inhabiting it.<BR>—कर्णाटक-देश, अस्, m. the<BR>Karṇāṭa country.<BR>—कर्णाटक-भाषा, f. the dia-<BR>lect of Karṇāṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णार्पण
कर्णार्पण कर्णार्पण. See under कर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्|कर्त्त्
कर्त् कर्त् (a various reading for कत्र्,<BR>कर्त्र्), cl. 10. P. कर्तयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>slacken or unloose, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त|कर्तः|कर्त्त|कर्त्तः
कर्त कर्त, अस्, m. (fr. 1. कृत्?), Ved. a hole,<BR>a cavity; (a more recent form is गर्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तन|कर्त्तन|कर्त्तनं
कर्तन 1. कर्तन, अम्, n. (fr. 1. कृत्), cutting,<BR>cutting off or in pieces, excision; (ई), f. scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तरि|कर्त्तरि
कर्तरि, इस्, f. scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तरिका|कर्त्तरिका
कर्तरिका, f. a knife, a small sword or cutlass; a<BR>hunter's knife or sword, a couteau de chasse; scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तरी|कर्त्तरी
कर्तरी, f. a scissors or shears; a knife; a small<BR>sword or cutlass; the part of an arrow to which the<BR>feathers are attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तन|कर्त्तन|कर्त्तनं
कर्तन 2. कर्तन, अम्, n. (fr. 2. कृत्), spin-<BR>ning cotton or thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तरीय
कर्तरीय कर्तरीय, a kind of poisonous<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तव्य|कर्त्तव्य|कर्त्तव्यं|कर्त्तव्यः
कर्तव्य कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fut. pass. part.<BR>fr. 1. कृ), to be done, made or accomplished, what<BR>ought to be done; to be imposed (as a punishment);<BR>to be turned towards (as the mind); to be offered;<BR>to be acted; (अम्), n. what ought to be done, obliga-<BR>tion, duty, task.<BR>—कर्तव्य-ता, f. or कर्तव्य-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. necessity, obligation; propriety, fitness; suit-<BR>able measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तु
कर्तु, the base of several cases, used as infinitives<BR>of the verb कृ in the Veda (e. g. कर्तुम्, कर्तवे,<BR>कर्तवै, कर्तोस्).<BR>—कर्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>sirous or intending to do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तृ|कर्त्तृ
कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a doer, a maker, one who<BR>makes or does, an agent, one who practises what he<BR>knows; one who acts in a religious ceremony, a<BR>priest; (very often at the end of compounds, e. g.<BR>भय-कर्तृ, राज्य-कर्तृ, &c.); (ता), m. the<BR>creator of the world, an epithet of Brahmā, of<BR>Viṣṇu, and of Śiva; (in gram.) an agent, one who<BR>acts of his own accord (स्व-तन्त्रः), the active noun,<BR>the nominative case.<BR>—कर्तृ-ता, f. the state of being<BR>the agent of an action.<BR>—कर्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. agency,<BR>the act or property of an agent.<BR>—कर्तृ-पुर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town.<BR>—कर्तृ-वाच्य, अस्, m. the active<BR>voice.<BR>—कर्तृ-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or being<BR>within the agent.<BR>—कर्तृस्थ-क्रियक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, any (root &c.) whose action stands within the<BR>agent.<BR>—कर्तृस्थ-भावक, अस्, आ, अम्, any (root<BR>&c.) whose state or भाव stands within the agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तृक|कर्त्तृक
कर्तृक, अस्, आ, अम्, an agent, one who does<BR>anything.<BR>—कर्तृक-त्व, अम्, n. agency, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्र|कर्त्रं
कर्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. an incantation, charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्व
कर्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be done or accom-<BR>plished; (अम्), n. obligation, duty; task.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तित|कर्त्तित
कर्तित कर्तित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कृत्),<BR>cut, cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्तिष्यत्|कर्त्तिष्यत्
कर्तिष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, or कर्तिष्य-<BR>माण, अस्, आ, अम्, intending or wishing to cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तव्य|कर्तव्य|कर्त्तव्यं|कर्त्तव्यः
कर्त्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut down, to be<BR>killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृका|कर्तृका
कर्त्तृका, f. a small sword, a knife; [cf. the next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्त्रिका
कर्त्त्रिका, f. a hunter's knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्त्री
कर्त्त्री, f. a pair of scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्य
कर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्र्
कर्त्र् कर्त्र्, cl. 10. P. कर्त्रयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to unloose, remove; [cf. कर्त् and कत्र्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द्
कर्द् कर्द्, cl. 1. P. कर्दति, -दितुम्, to rum-<BR>ble, as the bowels; to caw, as a crow; or to<BR>make any similar noise; [cf. पर्द्; Gr. χορδή.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दन|कर्दनं|कर्द्दन|कर्द्दनं
कर्दन, अम्, n. rumbling of the bowels, bor-<BR>borygmi; (ई), f. the day of full moon in the month<BR>Caitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द कर्द, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कर्द्),<BR>mud; clay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दट|कर्दटः|कर्द्दट|कर्द्दटः
कर्दट, अस्, m. mud, dirt; the fibrous root of<BR>the lotus (= करहाट); any aquatic weed, as<BR>Vallisneria &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दम|कर्दमः|कर्द्दम|कर्द्दमं|कर्द्दमः
कर्दम, अस्, m. mud, slime; mire, clay; dirt,<BR>filth, sin; a kind of plant; a poisonous kind of bulb;<BR>N. of a Nāga; N. of a Prajāpati, born from the<BR>shadow of Brahmā, or son of that god by Chāyā, and<BR>the husband of Devahūti and father of Kapila; a son<BR>of Prajāpati Pulaha; (ई), f., N. of a plant; (अम्),<BR>n. flesh; (अस्, आ, अम्), furnished with mud, mire,<BR>dirt, filth.<BR>—कर्दम-राज, अस्, m. or कर्दम-<BR>राजन्, आ, m., N. of a man, a son of Kṣema-gupta.<BR>—कर्दमाटक (˚म-आट्˚), अस्, m. a receptacle for<BR>filth, a sewer, &c.; [cf. कन्याट, पत्न्याट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमक|कर्दमकः|कर्द्दमक
कर्दमक, अस्, m. a kind of granulous fruit;<BR>a poisonous kind of bulb; a kind of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमित
कर्दमित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with mud, dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमिनी|कर्द्दमिनी
कर्दमिनी, f. a marshy region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमिल
कर्दमिल, अम्, n., N. of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पट|कर्पटं|कर्पटः
कर्पट कर्पट, अस्, अम्, m. n. old or patched<BR>or ragged garments; [cf. कार्पटिक and पञ्च-<BR>कर्पट.]<BR>—कर्पट-धारिन्, ई, m. a religious men-<BR>dicant, a beggar in patched or ragged clothes, or some-<BR>times with merely a cloth to cover the privities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटिक|कर्पटिकः|कर्प्पटिक
कर्पटिक, अस्, आ, अम्, or कर्पटिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>covered with patched or ragged garments, clothed in<BR>beggar's raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पण|कर्पणः
कर्पण कर्पण, a kind of lance or spear;<BR>[cf. कणप and कर्पर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पर|कर्परः
कर्पर कर्पर, अस्, m. a cup, a pot, an iron<BR>saucepan or frying-pan (according to some also n.<BR>in this sense); the skull, the cranium; a kind of<BR>weapon; the plant Ficus Glomerata, [cf. उदुम्-<BR>बर]; (ई), f. a collyrium extracted from the Amo-<BR>mum Anthorhiza, [cf. घट-कर्पर, खर्पर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पराल|कर्परालः
कर्पराल, अस्, m. a tree described as a Pīlu grow-<BR>ing in the hills; (a various reading for कन्दराल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पराश
कर्पराश, अस्, m. sand, gravel, a sandy soil; (a<BR>wrong reading for कर्परांश, a potsherd.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्परिका
कर्परिका, f. (diminutive fr. कर्परी) in कर्प-<BR>रिकातुत्थ, अम्, n. a collyrium extracted from the<BR>Amomum Anthorhiza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्परीक
कर्परीक (?), अस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पास|कर्पासं|कर्पासः
कर्पास कर्पास, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. 1. कृ), cotton, Gossypium Herbaceum; (ई), f.<BR>the cotton tree; [cf. कार्पास; cf. also Gr. κάρπασος;<BR>Lat. carbasus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूर|कर्पूरं|कर्पूरः
कर्पूर 1. कर्पूर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. कृप्), camphor (the plant and resinous exuda-<BR>tion and fruit); (अस्), m., N. of a poet; N. of the<BR>father of Gajamalla and uncle of Kalyāṇamalla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरकवि
कर्पूर-कवि, इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कर्पूर-<BR>खण्ड, अस्, m. a field of camphor.<BR>—कर्पूर-<BR>गौर, अम्, n., N. of a lake or pond (yellowish-<BR>white like camphor).<BR>—कर्पूरगौराख्य (˚र-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, called Karpūragaura.<BR>—कर्पूर-<BR>तिलक, अस्, m., N. of an elephant; (आ), f. an epithet<BR>of Jayā, one of Durgā's female attendants or confi-<BR>dantes.<BR>—कर्पूर-तैल, अम्, n. camphor liniment.<BR>—कर्पूर-नालिका, f. a kind of food prepared with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">Page0209-a+ 77</a>]<BR>camphor, rice dressed with spices and camphor and<BR>ghee.<BR>—कर्पूर-प्रकरण, अम्, n. a Jaina work<BR>by Hari.<BR>—कर्पूर-मञ्जरी, f. title of a dramatic<BR>work by Rāja-śekhara.<BR>—कर्पूर-मणि, इस्, m. a<BR>white mineral used medicinally.<BR>—कर्पूर-सरस्,<BR>अस्, n., N. of a lake or pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूर|कर्पूरं|कर्पूरः
2. कर्पूर, nom. P. कर्पूरति, -रितुम्, to spread<BR>like the smell of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरक|कर्पूरकः
कर्पूरक, अस्, m. zedoary, Curcuma Zerumbet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्फर|कर्फरः
कर्फर कर्फर, अस्, m. a mirror; [cf. कर्-<BR>कर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ब्
कर्ब् कर्ब्, cl. 1. P. कर्बति, -बितुम्, to<BR>go, move, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बर
कर्बर कर्बर. See कर्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बु
कर्बु कर्बु, उस्, उस्, उ (said to be fr. rt. कव्,<BR>to paint, colour), variegated, spotted.<BR>—कर्बु-दार,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Bauhinia Candida or Barleria Cærulea.<BR>—कर्बु-दारक, अस्, m. the tree Cordia Latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुक
कर्बुक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुर|कर्बुरः|कर्ब्बुरं|कर्ब्बुरः
कर्बुर and कर्वुर, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, of<BR>a spotted or variegated colour; white; (अस्), m. a<BR>variegated colour; sin; a Rakṣas; the plant Cur-<BR>cuma Amhaldi or Zerumbet; rice growing amidst<BR>inundation; (आ), f. the plant Bignonia Suaveolens;<BR>another plant, commonly called Varvarā; (ई), f. an<BR>epithet of the goddess Durgā; (अम्), n. gold; the<BR>plant Datura, and the fruit of it; water.<BR>—कर्बुर-<BR>फल, अस्, m. a plant, commonly called Sākuruṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूर|कर्बूरः|कर्ब्बूरं|कर्ब्बूरः
कर्बूर or कर्वूर, अस्, m. a Rakṣas; the plant<BR>Curcuma Amhaldi or Zerumbet; (आ), f. a leech;<BR>(अम्), n. gold; a yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरक|कर्ब्बूरकः
कर्बूरक, अस्, m. the plant Curcuma Amhaldi<BR>or Zerumbet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरित|कर्ब्बूरित
कर्बूरित, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, many-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बेल
कर्बेल कर्बेल, अस्, m. an epithet of the<BR>copyist Viṣṇu-bhaṭṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्|कर्म्मन्
कर्मन् कर्मन्, अ, n. (fr. rt. 1. कृ; according<BR>to some also m.), action, work, deed; performance,<BR>business; office; specific action, moral duty, the<BR>obligation imposed by peculiarities of tribe, occupa-<BR>tion, &c.; labour (as opposed to rest, प्रशान्ति);<BR>any religious action or rite (as sacrifice, ablution, &c.,<BR>especially as originating in the hope of future re-<BR>compense and as opposed to speculative religion or<BR>knowledge of spirit); action consisting in motion as<BR>the third among the seven categories of the Nyāya<BR>philosophy, (of these motions there are five, viz.<BR>उत्-क्षेपण, throwing upwards; अव-क्षेपण,<BR>throwing downwards; आ-कुञ्चन, contraction; प्र-<BR>सारण, extension or dilatation; and गमन, going<BR>or motion in general); product, result, effect; organ<BR>of sense [cf. कर्मेन्द्रिय]; natural or active pro-<BR>perty (as maturity, of heat; support, of earth; disper-<BR>sion, of wind, &c.); the immediate object of an agent<BR>or act; (in grammar) the idea or notion expressed<BR>by the acc. case, (this object is of four kinds, viz.<BR>a. निर्वर्त्य, when anything new is produced, e. g.<BR>कटं करोति, ‘he makes a mat;’ पुत्रम् प्रसूते,<BR>‘she bears a son:’ b. विकार्य, when change is implied<BR>either of the substance and form, e. g. काष्ठम्<BR>भस्म करोति, ‘he makes ashes out of fuel;’ or<BR>of the form only, e. g. सुवर्णं कुण्डलं क-<BR>रोति, ‘he fashions gold into an ear-ring:’ c. प्राप्य,<BR>when any desired object is attained, e. g. ग्रामं<BR>गच्छति, ‘he goes to the village;’ चन्द्रम् पश्यति,<BR>‘he sees the moon:’ d. अनीप्सित, when an undesired<BR>object is abandoned, e. g. पापं त्यजति, ‘he leaves<BR>the wicked’); fate, the certain consequence of previous<BR>acts [cf. कर्म-पाक and कर्म-विपाक]; (in as-<BR>tronomy) the tenth lunar mansion.<BR>—कर्म-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, working for other people, a hired labourer,<BR>a servant of any kind (as a pupil &c.) who is not a slave,<BR>an agent, any one who does work or business; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Yama, the regent of the dead; (ई),<BR>f. the plant Sanseviera Zeylonica; the plant Momor-<BR>dica Monadelpha.<BR>—कर्म-कर्तृ, ता, m. ‘an object-<BR>agent’ or ‘object-containing agent,’ i. e. an agent which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-b" target="_blank">Page0209-b+ 81</a>]<BR>is at the same time the object of an act on (this is the<BR>idea expressed by the reflexive passive, as in ओदनः<BR>पच्यते, ‘the mashed grain cooks of itself,’ see<BR>Gram. 461. c); कर्म-कर्तारौ, m. du. the work<BR>and the person accomplishing it.<BR>—कर्म-काण्ड,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. that department of the Veda which<BR>relates to ceremonial acts and sacrificial rites; N. of<BR>a Jaina work.<BR>—कर्म-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, a worker,<BR>one who does any business, an artisan, a mechanic;<BR>one who performs any act (without receiving wages<BR>for it, according to native lexicographers); (अस्), m.<BR>a bull; a blacksmith (forming a mixed caste re-<BR>garded as the progeny of the divine artist Viśva-<BR>karman and a Śūdrā woman); (ई), f. the plants<BR>Sanseviera Zeylonica and Momordica Monadelpha.<BR>—कर्म-कारक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who does any<BR>act or work.<BR>—कर्मकारापय, nom. (fr. कर्म-<BR>कार) A. कर्मकारापयते, -यितुम्, to cause any<BR>one to work as a servant.<BR>—कर्म-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>working, doing any work or act, (in compounds<BR>preceded by an adjective or pronoun, e. g. शुभ-<BR>कर्म-कारिन्, doing good works; तत्-कर्म-का-<BR>रिन्, performing the same business.)<BR>—कर्म-कार्-<BR>मुक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. ‘the bow of action,’ i. e.<BR>an efficacious or strong bow.<BR>—कर्म-कीलक, अस्,<BR>m. a washerman.<BR>—कर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, performing<BR>any work, skilful in work (e. g. तीक्ष्ण-कर्म-<BR>कृत्, working with zeal); a workman, an artisan;<BR>a servant; one who has done any work.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>कृतवत्, आन्, m. the director of a religious rite, the<BR>reciter of Mantras or formularies.<BR>—कर्म-कृत्य,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. activity, the state of active exertion.<BR>—कर्म-क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, competent to per-<BR>form an act, able to do it.<BR>—कर्म-क्षेत्र, अम्,<BR>n. the district or region of religious acts; [cf. कर्म-<BR>भूमि.]<BR>—कर्म-ग्रन्थि-प्रथम-विचार, title<BR>of a Jaina work.<BR>—कर्म-घात, अस्, m. lit. ‘the<BR>killing of work,’ i. e. the act of leaving off work.<BR>—कर्म-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a prince of Mā-<BR>lava.<BR>—कर्म-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. collected or accom-<BR>plished by work.<BR>—कर्म-चेष्टा, f. active exertion,<BR>action.<BR>—कर्म-चोदना, f. the motive impelling to<BR>ritual acts.<BR>—कर्म-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, resulting from<BR>or produced by any act whether religious or immoral;<BR>(अस्), m. the holy fig tree, Ficus Religiosa; the<BR>Kali-yuga or fourth and present age of the world,<BR>the age of iniquity.<BR>—कर्मज-गुण, अस्, m. a<BR>property resulting from human acts (as separation,<BR>reunion, &c.).<BR>—कर्म-जित्, त्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कर्म-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in any work;<BR>acquainted with religious rites.<BR>—कर्मणि-वाच्य,<BR>अस्, m. the passive voice in grammar, (but according<BR>to Pāṇini the passive is an Ātmane-pada verb with<BR>the affix यक् in four tenses, and कर्मन् expresses<BR>only one idea of the passive.)<BR>—कर्म-त्याग, अस्,<BR>m. abandonment of worldly duties or ceremonial<BR>rites.<BR>—कर्म-त्व, अम्, n. or कर्म-ता, f. state<BR>of action, any act, the active discharge of the duties<BR>and functions of life.<BR>—कर्म-दुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>corrupt in action, wicked in practice, immoral, dis-<BR>reputable.<BR>—कर्म-देव, अस्, m., Ved. a god by<BR>actions (opposed to आजान-देव, a god by birth).<BR>—कर्म-दोष, अस्, m. a sinful work, sin, vice;<BR>error, blunder; the evil consequence of human acts,<BR>discreditable conduct or business.<BR>—कर्म-धारय,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a class of compounds (see Gram. 755);<BR>according to native grammarians a subdivision of the<BR>Tat-puruṣa class, the members of which are in the<BR>same relationship either as adjective and substan-<BR>tive or as two substantives in apposition (e. g. श्वे-<BR>ताश्व, ‘a white horse;’ Pāṇini I. 2, 42, calls a<BR>Karma-dhāraya comp. a Samānādhikaraṇa-tatpu-<BR>rusha; cf. अधि-करण).<BR>—कर्म-ध्वंस, अस्,<BR>m. loss of benefit arising from religious acts, destruc-<BR>tion of any work, disappointment.<BR>—कर्म-नामन्,<BR>अ, n. a participle.<BR>—कर्म-नाशा, f., N. of a river<BR>between Kāśī and Vihāra, contact with which destroys<BR>the merit of works.<BR>—कर्म-निबन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>necessary consequence of works.<BR>—कर्म-निर्हार,<BR>अस्, m. removal of (bad) deeds or their effects.<BR>—कर्म-निष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. diligent in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-c" target="_blank">Page0209-c+ 81</a>]<BR>religious actions, engaged in active duties; (अस्), m.<BR>a Brāhman who performs sacrifices &c.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>पथ, अस्, m. the way or direction of an action.<BR>—कर्म-पद्धति, इस्, f. title of a work.<BR>—कर्-<BR>म-पाक, अस्, m. the ripening of actions, i. e. re-<BR>compense for actions done in a former life; [cf.<BR>कर्म-विपाक.]<BR>—कर्म-प्रदीप, अस्, m. title of<BR>a work of Kātyāyana; N. of a work of Miśra.<BR>—कर्मप्रदीप-विवृति, N. of Śivarāma's com-<BR>mentary on the Karmapradīpa.<BR>—कर्म-प्रदीपिका,<BR>f. title of a work of Kāma-deva.<BR>—कर्म-प्रव-<BR>चनीय, employed for the definition of an action;<BR>(अस्), m. (scil. शब्दस्) a term for certain preposi-<BR>tions, particles, or adverbs, not connected with a verb,<BR>but with a case of a noun; (according to Pāṇini the<BR>first and general category to which prepositions belong<BR>is that of Nipātas or particles; they are Upasargas<BR>and Gatis when they are in connection with verbal<BR>action, i. e. with the tenses of a verb; but the term<BR>गति is more comprehensive than उपसर्ग, and is<BR>applicable also when the verbal root becomes de-<BR>veloped into a noun substantive, adjective, or parti-<BR>ciple. Moreover, the term उपसर्ग is confined to<BR>the prepositions with सु and दुस्, whereas the Gatis<BR>include many other adverbial prefixes such as अलम्<BR>and the nouns and adjectives which take the affix च्वि<BR>&c. Lastly, prepositions are Karmapravacanīyas if they<BR>are unconnected with verbs and govern a noun either<BR>separated from it or forming a compound with it. A<BR>Karmapravacanīya never loses its accent, and exercises<BR>no euphonic influence on the initial letters of a fol-<BR>lowing verb.)<BR>—कर्म-प्रवाद, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>eighth of the fourteen Pūrvas or oldest religious<BR>writings of the Jainas.<BR>—कर्म-फल, अम्, n. the<BR>fruit or recompense of actions; pain, pleasure, &c.,<BR>considered as the consequence of acts; the fruit of<BR>the tree Averrhoa Carambola; [cf. कर्मरङ्ग.]<BR>—कर्मफलोदय (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. the occur-<BR>rence of consequences.<BR>—कर्म-बन्ध, अस्, m. the<BR>tie of works (by which the soul is attached to pleasure<BR>&c.).<BR>—कर्म-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, bound by<BR>acts; (अम्), n. confinement to repeated existence, as<BR>the consequence of acts.<BR>—कर्म-भू, ऊस्, f. tilled<BR>or cultivated ground.<BR>—कर्म-भूमि, इस्, f. the<BR>land or region of religious actions, i. e. where such<BR>actions are performed; (according to Hemacandra<BR>the Karmabhūmis are Bharata, Airāvata, and Videha,<BR>but not the district of the Kurus; the other Varṣas<BR>are फल-भूमयस्, i. e. lands of recompense; cf.<BR>कर्म-क्षेत्र.)<BR>—कर्म-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of works, resulting from works.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, m. the way of work; a technical term<BR>used by thieves for the breaking of walls &c.<BR>—कर्-<BR>म-मीमांसा, see s. v. मीमांसा.<BR>—कर्म-मूल,<BR>अम्, n. Kuśa or sacrificial grass, used as an essential<BR>part in many religious and sacred rites.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>युग, अम्, n. the fourth and present age of the<BR>world, the iron age, the Kali-yuga.<BR>—कर्म-योग,<BR>अस्, m. performance of a work or business or of<BR>worldly functions and religious duties; active exer-<BR>tion, industry; connection with a sacrifice.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>योनि, इस्, m. f. source of action.<BR>—कर्मर्घ, अस्,<BR>m. (fr. कर्मन् and ऋघ in ऋघाय), N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR>—कर्म-वचन, अम्, n. (with Buddhists)<BR>the ritual.<BR>—कर्म-वज्र, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘whose<BR>thunderbolt is work;’ an epithet of the Śūdra.<BR>—कर्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, busy with a work, em-<BR>ployed in it.<BR>—कर्म-वश, अस्, आ, अम्, being in<BR>the power of or subject to former actions; (अस्), m.<BR>the necessary influence of acts; fate, considered as the<BR>inevitable consequence of actions done in a former<BR>life.<BR>—कर्मवशि-ता, f. the condition of having<BR>power over works, a quality of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—कर्म-वशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having power over<BR>works.<BR>—कर्म-वाटी, f. a lunar day or the thirtieth<BR>division of a lunar month (regulating all ceremonies,<BR>observances, religious actions, &c.).<BR>—कर्म-विघ्न,<BR>अस्, m. an impediment to work, obstruction.<BR>—कर्-<BR>म-विधि, इस्, m. rule of action, observance, practice,<BR>mode of conducting any ceremony.<BR>—कर्म-वि-<BR>पर्यय, अस्, m. succession of office or employment,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-a" target="_blank">Page0210-a+ 81</a>]<BR>revolving or alternating duty; contrariety or reverse<BR>of any act or business.<BR>—कर्म-विपाक, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>ripening of actions,’ i. e. the good or evil consequences<BR>in this life of human acts performed in previous<BR>births; title of a work on this subject, explaining ex-<BR>piatory rites to be performed in cases of disease &c.,<BR>supposed to be the punishment of offences committed<BR>in a previous existence (written in Ślokas in the form<BR>of a dialogue between Śakuntalā-Bharata and Śātā-<BR>tapa-Bhṛgu), a work of Viśveśvara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>विपाक-सङ्ग्रह, title of a book.<BR>—कर्मविपाक-<BR>सार, title of a book composed by Dinakara, the<BR>brother of Kamalākara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—कर्म-विशेष, अस्,<BR>m. variety of act or actions.<BR>—कर्म-वीज, अम्, n.<BR>the seed of works.<BR>—कर्म-शाला, f. a workshop, a<BR>house of business.<BR>—कर्म-शाली, f., N. of a river in<BR>Caturgrāma.<BR>—कर्म-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, assiduous,<BR>laborious, one who perseveres in his duties without<BR>looking to their reward.<BR>—कर्म-शुद्ध (?), अम्,<BR>n. approved occupation.<BR>—कर्म-शूर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>assiduous, laborious; (अस्), m. a skilful or clever work-<BR>man.<BR>—कर्म-शौच, अम्, n. humility.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Pulaha by Gati.<BR>—कर्म-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. assemblage of acts, com-<BR>prising the act, its performance and the performer.<BR>—कर्म-सचिव, अस्, m. a minister, any officer<BR>employed upon active duties, as a judge, a deputy, &c.<BR>—कर्म-सन्न्यासिक, अस्, m. an ascetic, a religious<BR>person who has withdrawn from works.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>समाधि, इस्, m. devotion, abstraction (?) .<BR>—कर्म-<BR>सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by or resulting from<BR>acts.<BR>—कर्म-साक्षिन्, ई, m. ‘the witness of all acts,’<BR>epithet of the sun.<BR>—कर्म-साधक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>accomplishing a work.<BR>—कर्म-साधन, अम्, n.<BR>implement, means; articles essential to the perform-<BR>ance of any religious act.<BR>—कर्म-सिद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>accomplishment of an act, success.<BR>—कर्म-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the father of Rāma-candra.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or being within the object.<BR>—कर्मस्थ-क्रियक, अस्, आ, अम्, any (root)<BR>whose action stands within the object.<BR>—कर्मस्थ-<BR>भावक, अस्, आ, अम्, any (root &c.) whose state<BR>(भाव) stands within the object.<BR>—कर्म-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. a public office or place of business.<BR>—कर्म-<BR>हेतु, उस्, उस्, उ, caused by acts, arising from acts.<BR>—कर्माक्षम (˚म-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, incapable<BR>of business.<BR>—कर्माङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, m. part<BR>of any act, part of a sacrificial rite.<BR>—कर्मात्मन्<BR>(˚म-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one whose character is action,<BR>endowed with principles of action, active, acting.<BR>—कर्मादित्य (˚म-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—कर्माधिकार (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, m. the right of<BR>action (in the Mīmāṃsa philosophy).<BR>—कर्मानु-<BR>बन्ध (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. connection with or de-<BR>pendance upon acts.<BR>—कर्मानुबन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>connected with or involved in works.<BR>—कर्मानु-<BR>रूप (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, according to action,<BR>according to function or duty.<BR>—कर्मानुरूपतस्,<BR>ind. conformably to act, function &c.<BR>—कर्मानु-<BR>ष्ठान (˚म-अन्˚), अम्, n. practising one's duties,<BR>discharging peculiar functions.<BR>—कर्मानुष्ठायिन्<BR>(˚म-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, practising duties, performing<BR>rites &c.<BR>—कर्मानुसार (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. conse-<BR>quence of or conformity to acts.<BR>—कर्मानुसारतस्,<BR>ind. according to one's deeds.<BR>—कर्मान्त (˚म-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. work, business, administration of an office;<BR>management of any business; the end of any task<BR>or act; the end or abandonment of ritual acts; tilled<BR>or cultivated ground.<BR>—कर्मान्तर (˚म-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. interval between religious actions, suspense of<BR>such an action; difference or contrariety of action;<BR>penance, expiation.<BR>—कर्मान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, final,<BR>completing; (अस्), m. a workman, a servant, one<BR>who finishes a work.<BR>—कर्माभिधायक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or कर्माभिधायिन् (˚म-अभ्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>enjoining or prescribing duties or acts.<BR>—कर्मा-<BR>रम्भ (˚म-आर्˚), अस्, m. commencement of any<BR>act.<BR>—कर्मार्ह (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fit for<BR>work, able to do any work, suitable to any rite; (अस्),<BR>m. a man.<BR>—कर्मेन्द्रिय (˚म-इन्˚), अम्, n. an<BR>organ of action (opposed to the बुद्धीन्द्रियाणि or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">Page0210-b+ 75</a>]<BR>perceptive organs of sense; five are reckoned, viz.<BR>the hand, the foot, the larynx or organ of the voice,<BR>the organ of generation and of excretion).<BR>—कर्मो-<BR>दार (˚म-उद्˚), अम्, n. any honourable or valiant<BR>act, magnanimity, prowess.<BR>—कर्मोद्युक्त (˚म-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, actively labouring, busily engaged.<BR>—कर्मोद्योग (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. engaging actively<BR>in any work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म|कर्म्म
कर्म, अस्, अम्, m. n. according to some lexico-<BR>graphers = कर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मक
कर्मक (at the end of some compounds) = कर्-<BR>मन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मठ|कर्मठः|कर्म्मठ|कर्म्मठः
कर्मठ, अस्, आ, अम्, skilful or clever in work,<BR>clever; working diligently, accomplishing any rite,<BR>anxious to perform anything; (अस्), m. the director<BR>and performer of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मण्य|कर्म्मण्य|कर्म्मण्यः
कर्मण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. skilful in work, clever,<BR>diligent; proper or fit for any act, suitable to it; (at<BR>the end of compounds) relating to any business or to<BR>the accomplishment of anything; (आ), f. wages, hire;<BR>(अम्), n. energy, activity.<BR>—कर्मण्य-ता, f. skil-<BR>fulness, cleverness.<BR>—कर्मण्य-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, re-<BR>ceiving wages, working for hire; (a various reading<BR>for भरण्य-भुज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मतस्
कर्मतस्, ind. according to actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मार|कर्मारः|कर्म्मार|कर्म्मारः
कर्मार, अस्, m., Ved. an artificer, a mechanic,<BR>a blacksmith, a brazier, a carpenter, &c.; a bamboo;<BR>the plant Averrhoa Carambola, = कर्मरङ्ग below.<BR>—कर्मार-वन, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मारक
कर्मारक, अस्, m. the plant Averrhoa Carambola.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिक
कर्मिक, अस्, आ, अम्, acting, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिन्|कर्म्मिन्
कर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting, active, busy; performing<BR>a religious action; engaged in any work or business;<BR>belonging or relating to any act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठः
कर्मिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be a superlative<BR>of the last), very active, assiduous, diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मीण
कर्मीण = कर्मन् at the end of a compound;<BR>[cf. अलङ्कर्मीण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्द|कर्म्मन्द
कर्मन्द कर्मन्द, अस्, m., N. of a man,<BR>author of a Bhikṣu-sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्दिन्|कर्मंदिन्|कर्म्मन्दिन्
कर्मन्दिन्, ई, m. a beggar, a religious mendi-<BR>cant, a member of the fourth order (lit. ‘a follower<BR>of Karmanda’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मर
कर्मर कर्मर and कर्मरक, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Averrhoa Carambola.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मरङ्ग|कर्म्मरङ्ग|कर्म्मरङ्गः
कर्मरङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of the same plant;<BR>(अम्), n. the acid fruit of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मरी|कर्म्मरी
कर्मरी कर्मरी, f. the manna of the bam-<BR>boo; [cf. वंश-रोचना.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मष
कर्मष कर्मष = कल्मष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मस
कर्मस कर्मस, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Pulaha and Kṣamā; [cf. कर्म-श्रेष्ठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मीर|कर्म्मीर|कर्म्मीरः
कर्मीर कर्मीर, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated; (a<BR>various reading for किर्मीर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मीरक|कर्म्मीरक
कर्मीरक, अस्, m. a small tree, Trophis Aspera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्
कर्व् कर्व्, cl. 1. P. कर्वति, -वितुम्, to be<BR>proud, to boast; [cf. खर्व् and गर्व्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व|कर्वः|कर्व्व|कर्व्वः
कर्व कर्व, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. कॄ),<BR>love, desire; a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वट|कर्वटः|कर्व्वट|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्वट कर्वट, अस्, अम्, m. n. declivity of a<BR>mountain; a village, market-town, the capital of a<BR>district (of two or four hundred villages) in a pleasant<BR>site and of handsome construction; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a country or a people; (ई), f., N. of a river; (अम्),<BR>n. a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वटक
कर्वटक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?) declivity of a<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वर|कर्वरः|कर्व्वर
कर्वर 1. कर्वर, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. कृ), Ved.<BR>a deed, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वर|कर्वरः|कर्व्वर
कर्वर 2. कर्वर or कर्बर, अस्, आ, अम् (said<BR>to be fr. rt. 1. कॄ), variegated, spotted; (अस्), m. sin;<BR>a tiger; a Rakṣas; a sort of medicament; (ई), f.<BR>an epithet of Durgā; night; a Rākṣasī; a tigress;<BR>the leaf of the plant Asa Fœtida; [cf. करवी, कवरी,<BR>कारवी.] See कर्बुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्शन|कर्शनः
कर्शन कर्शन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. कृश्), ren-<BR>dering lean, attenuating, causing emaciation; (अस्),<BR>m. fire; [cf. कृशानु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्शफ
कर्शफ कर्शफ, अस्, m., Ved. an epithet of<BR>imps or goblins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्श्य|कर्श्यः
कर्श्य कर्श्य, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = कर्-<BR>चूर; [cf. कार्श्य and कार्ष्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ष|कर्षः
कर्ष कर्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कृष्), drawing,<BR>dragging, pulling; attracting; ploughing; a furrow,<BR>a trench; a scratch; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a weight of<BR>gold or silver, equal to 16 Māṣas = (1/4) Pala = (1/400) of a<BR>Tulā = 11, 375 French grains; according to the ancient<BR>division of 5 Rettis to the Māṣa the Karṣa would<BR>be equal to about 176 grains troy; in common use<BR>8 Rettis are given to the Māṣa, and the Karṣa is<BR>then about 280 grains troy.<BR>—कर्ष-फल, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Terminalia Bellerica; this tree is also<BR>called Akṣa, because its fruits are used as dice; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Emblica Officinalis.<BR>—कर्षार्ध (˚ष-<BR>अर्˚), अम्, n. a Tolaka, a weight of 16 Māṣas<BR>(according to some calculations).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, a cultivator of the soil, one<BR>who ploughs or lives by tillage; a husbandman; who<BR>or what draws or drags, attractive, what attracts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, pulling to and fro, drag-<BR>ging, attracting, overpowering, injuring; tormenting;<BR>harassed; extending (in time); (अम्), n. the act of<BR>dragging or pulling; drawing to and fro; removing,<BR>hurting, injuring; bending (a bow); ploughing, cul-<BR>tivating the ground; cultivated land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणि|कर्षणिः
कर्षणि, इस्, f. an unchaste woman (attracting<BR>the men).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणी
कर्षणी, f., N. of a plant; [cf. कर्षिणी and<BR>क्षीरिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणीय
कर्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be drawn or pulled;<BR>to be attracted; to be conciliated or won.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षयत्
कर्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, dragging, pulling; at-<BR>tracting; harassing, annoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षित
कर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn, attracted; distracted,<BR>tormented, harassed; worn out; ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिन्
कर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, who or what pulls or draws or<BR>attracts; attractive; inviting; who or what ploughs<BR>or furrows, a ploughman, peasant; (इणी), f. the bit<BR>of a bridle; a medicinal moon-plant; [cf. कर्षणी,<BR>क्षीरिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षू
कर्षू, ऊस्, f. a furrow, trench, incision; a river;<BR>a canal; a shallow trench for receiving the sacrificial<BR>fire; (ऊस्), m. a fire of dried cow-dung; agriculture,<BR>cultivation; livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षापण
कर्षापण कर्षापण = कार्षापण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हि
कर्हि कर्हि, ind. (fr. 2. क), Ved. when?<BR>at what time? (followed by the future or present tense)<BR>कर्हि-चिद् or कर्ह्य्-अपि, at any time; [cf. Goth.<BR>hvar, ‘where?’ Eng. where? Germ. war and wor<BR>in warum, woraus, &c.; Lith. kur.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
कल् 1. कल्, cl. 1. A. कलते, -लितुम्, to<BR>sound; to count; [Gr. καλέω ? Lat.<BR>calculo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
कल् 2. कल्, cl. 10. P. कालयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to push on, drive forward, drive away;<BR>carry off; to drive together, collect; to throw; to<BR>announce the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
कल् 3. कल्, cl. 10. P. कलयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to impel, incite, urge on; to bear, carry;<BR>to do, make, accomplish; to tie on, attach, affix; to<BR>utter a sound, murmur; to furnish with; to observe,<BR>perceive, take notice of; to regard, consider, count,<BR>reckon, calculate; to go; to take hold of the die<BR>called Kali (in this last sense कल् may be considered<BR>as a nom. fr. कलि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल, अस्, आ, अम्, dumb, hoarse, indistinct, inarticu-<BR>late (especially in composition with वाष्प and अश्रु,<BR>e. g. वाष्प-कल, अश्रु-कल, having the speech<BR>impeded by tears, sobbing); emitting a low or soft<BR>tone, as humming, buzzing, &c.; weak; crude,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">Page0211-a+ 79</a>]<BR>undigested; (अस्), m. (scil. स्वर) a low or soft and<BR>inarticulate tone, as humming, buzzing, &c.; the<BR>tree Shorea Robusta; (in poetry) time equal to four<BR>Mātras or instants; (आस्), m. pl. a class of manes or<BR>deceased ancestors; (अम्), n. semen virile; the ju-<BR>jube, Zizyphus Jujuba; (for कला see below, s. v.)<BR>—कल-कण्ठ, अस्, m. a pleasing tone or note; a<BR>low murmuring tone; having a sweet voice, N. of<BR>several birds, as of the Indian cuckoo; a dove, a<BR>pigeon; a goose.<BR>—कल-कल, अस्, m. a confused<BR>noise, the murmuring or buz of a crowd; resin,<BR>pitch, the resinous exudation of the tree Shorea<BR>Robusta; an epithet of Śiva; [cf. कटकट, कटङ्-<BR>कट.]<BR>—कलकल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, causing hum-<BR>ming or murmuring.<BR>—कल-कीट, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Grāma.<BR>—कल-कूजिका, f. a wanton, a lascivious<BR>woman.<BR>—कल-कूट, अस्, m., N. of a warrior-tribe<BR>and the country inhabited by it.<BR>—कल-कूणिका, f.<BR>a wanton, a lascivious woman.<BR>—कल-घोष, अस्,<BR>m. the Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>—कलङ्-कष,<BR>अस्, m. a lion; a musical instrument; see कर-ताली.<BR>—कलङ्-कुर, अस्, m. an eddy, a whirlpool.<BR>—कल-<BR>ता, f. or कल-त्व, अम्, n. melody, music.<BR>—कल-<BR>तूलिका, f. a wanton or lascivious woman; [cf. कल-<BR>कूणिका.]<BR>—कल-धूत, अम्, n. silver; (wrong read-<BR>ing for कल-धौत?).<BR>—कल-धौत, अम्, n. gold<BR>and silver (sounding and shining); (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>a low or pleasing tone.<BR>—कलधौत-लिपि, इस्, f. a<BR>streak of gold, illumination of a manuscript with gold.<BR>—कल-ध्वनि, इस्, m. a low sweet tone; the Ko-<BR>kila or Indian cuckoo; the turtle-dove; a peacock.<BR>—कल-नाद, अस्, m. a sort of goose; see कल-<BR>हंस.<BR>—कल-भाषण, अम्, n. the prattle of<BR>childhood.<BR>—कल-भैरव, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a deep ravine in the mountains between the<BR>rivers Tāpī and Narmadā.<BR>—कल-रव, अस्, m. a<BR>low sweet tone; a dove; the Indian cuckoo; [cf.<BR>Lat. columba.]<BR>—कल-वचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, speaking<BR>sweetly, singing.<BR>—कल-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a charming voice (a bird).<BR>—कल-स्वर, अम्, n. a<BR>low musical sound.<BR>—कल-हंस, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>duck or goose; a gander; another bird, Gallinula<BR>Porphyria; a drake or (according to some) a teal;<BR>an excellent king; Brahma or the supreme spirit;<BR>N. of a metre consisting of four lines of thirteen sylla-<BR>bles each.<BR>—कलानुनादिन् (˚ल-अन्˚), ई, m. a sparrow;<BR>a bee, but particularly one of a very large kind; the<BR>Cātaka bird.<BR>—कलालाप (˚ल-आल्˚), अस्, m. a sweet<BR>humming sound, discourse; a bee.<BR>—कलोत्ताल (˚ल-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, high, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन|कलनं|कलनः
कलन, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of compounds),<BR>causing, effecting; (अस्), m. a sort of cane; (आ), f.<BR>doing, making, effecting; subjection, submission;<BR>emitting (?); काल-कलना, fulfilling one's time,<BR>dying; (अम्), n. an embryo at the first stage after<BR>conception; a spot, a stain; an offence, fault, defect;<BR>murmuring, sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित, अस्, आ, अम्, impelled, driven, borne on-<BR>wards; held, laid hold of; attached, affixed, furnished,<BR>endowed with; gained, acquired; considered, known,<BR>understood; numbered, counted, reckoned; separated,<BR>divided; sounded indistinctly, buzzed, murmured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलक|कलकः
कलक कलक, अस्, m. a kind of fish; a<BR>kind of prose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्क|कलंक|कलंकः|कलङ्कः
कलङ्क कलङ्क, अस्, m. a spot, a mark; the<BR>rust of iron; a fault, defamation, abuse.<BR>—कलङ्क-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, censorious, calumniating, defaming;<BR>spotting, staining.<BR>—कलङ्क-कला, f. a digit of the<BR>moon in shadow.<BR>—कलङ्क-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, spot-<BR>ted, stained; calumniated, defamed.<BR>—कलङ्क-<BR>हृत्, त्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कय
कलङ्कय, nom. P. कलङ्कयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>spot, defame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कित|कलंकित
कलङ्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, spotted, soiled, stained;<BR>calumniated, defamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्किन्
कलङ्किन्, ई, इनी, इ, soiled, stained; disgraced,<BR>reviled, rusty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलञ्ज|कलंज|कलंजः|कलञ्जः
कलञ्ज कलञ्ज, अस्, m. an animal struck<BR>with a poisoned weapon; tobacco.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलट|कलटं
कलट कलट, अम्, n. the thatch of a house;<BR>(other works read this कुटल, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत
कलत कलत, अस्, आ, अम्, = खलति, bald-<BR>headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्र|कलत्रं
कलत्र कलत्र, अम्, n. (see कडत्र), a<BR>wife; any female; the hip and loins; pudendum<BR>muliebre; a royal citadel, a strong hold or fastness;<BR>the seventh lunar mansion in astronomy.<BR>—क-<BR>लत्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or कलत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having<BR>a wife, united to a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्तक
कलन्तक कलन्तक or कलन्दक, अस्, m. a<BR>species of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दन
कलन्दन कलन्दन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दर|कलंदरः|कलन्दरः
कलन्दर कलन्दर, अस्, m. a man of a mixed<BR>caste, the son of a Leṭa (?) man and a Tīvara woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दिका|कलंदिका
कलन्दिका कलन्दिका, f. knowledge, intel-<BR>ligence, wisdom in general; (a various reading for<BR>कलिन्दिका, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्धु|कलन्धुः
कलन्धु कलन्धु, उस्, m. a kind of vegetable;<BR>[cf. घोली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभ|कलभः
कलभ कलभ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 3.<BR>कल्), a young elephant; an elephant thirty years old;<BR>a young camel (perhaps also the young of other<BR>animals); the tree Datura Fastuosa [cf. धुस्तूर];<BR>(ई), f. a sort of Ricinus (चञ्चु).<BR>—कलभ-वल्लभ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a tree; [cf. पीलु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम|कलमः
कलम कलम, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 3. कल्),<BR>rice, which is sown in May and June, and ripens in<BR>December or January; a white rice growing in deep<BR>water; a pen, a reed for writing with; a thief, a<BR>rogue; [cf. Gr. κάλαμος Lat. calamus, culmus;<BR>and Arab. قلم]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्ब|कलंब|कलंबः|कलम्बः
कलम्ब कलम्ब, अस्, m. the stalk of a pot-<BR>herb; an arrow; the tree Nauclea Cadamba; (ई), f.<BR>(according to a scholiast also m.), the pot-herb Convol-<BR>vulus Repens; (अम्), n. Calumba root, Menispermum<BR>Calumba; [cf. कडम्ब, कदम्ब.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बक|कलम्बकः
कलम्बक, अस्, m., N. of a plant; [cf. धारा-<BR>कदम्ब.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बिका|कलंबिका
कलम्बिका, f. the nape of the neck (in this sense<BR>usually used in du.); the pot-herb Convolvulus Repens;<BR>[cf. कलम्बी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बू
कलम्बू, ऊस्, f. the same pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बुट|कलंबुट|कलम्बुटं
कलम्बुट कलम्बुट, अम्, n. fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलल|कललं|कललः
कलल कलल, अस्, अम्, m. n. the womb, the<BR>uterus; a small round lump, a term for the embryo<BR>a short time after conception; [cf. कलन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललज|कललजः
कललज कललज, अस्, m. the resinous ex-<BR>udation of the Shorea Robusta; [cf. कल-कल.]<BR>—कललजोद्भव (˚ज-उद्˚), अस्, m. the tree<BR>Shorea Robusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविङ्क|कलविंक|कलविंकः|कलविङ्कः
कलविङ्क कलविङ्क, अस्, m. a sparrow; a<BR>spot, a stain [cf. कलङ्क]; a white Cāmara; the<BR>plant Echites Antidysenterica [cf. कलिङ्गक]; N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलश|कलशः
कलश कलश, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. a water-<BR>pot, a pitcher, a jar, a dish; (अस्), m., N. of a poet;<BR>(ई), f. the plant Hemionitis Cordifolia; N. of a<BR>Tīrtha; a churn; [cf. कलस and द्रोण-कलश;<BR>Gr. κάλιξ Lat. calix.]<BR>—कलश-दिर्, ईर्, m., Ved.<BR>one whose pot or pitcher is broken.<BR>—कलश-<BR>पोतक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—कलशी-कण्ठ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of<BR>this man.<BR>—कलशी-पदी, f. having feet like a water-<BR>jar.<BR>—कलशी-मुख, अस्, m. a sort of musical instru-<BR>ment.<BR>—कलशी-सुत, अस्, m. an epithet of Agastya.<BR>—कलशोदर (˚श-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशि|कलशिः
कलशि, इस्, f. a water-pot, pitcher, dish, water-jar;<BR>the plant Hemionitis Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलस|कलसः
कलस, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. a pot, a water-jar;<BR>(अस्), m. a Droṇa measure; a rounded pinnacle or ball<BR>on the top of a temple; (ई), f. the plant Hemionitis<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-c" target="_blank">Page0211-c+ 79</a>]<BR>Cordifolia.<BR>—कलसोदधि (˚स-उद्˚), इस्, m. the<BR>ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलह|कलहं|कलहः
कलह कलह, अस्, अम्, m. n. strife, conten-<BR>tion, quarrel, war, battle; the sheath of a sword, a<BR>scabbard; a road, a way; deceit, falsehood; violence<BR>without murderous weapons, abuse, beating, kicking,<BR>&c.<BR>—कलह-कन्दल, अस्, m., N. of an actor.<BR>—कलह-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, quarrelsome, turbulent;<BR>contentious, pugnacious; (ई), f., N. of the wife of<BR>Vikramacaṇḍa.<BR>—कलह-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, quarrel-<BR>some, contentious.<BR>—कलह-नाशन, अस्, m. the<BR>tree Cæsalpina Bonducella.<BR>—कलह-प्रिय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fond of contention, quarrelsome, turbulent; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Nārada; (आ), f. the bird Gracula<BR>Religiosa.<BR>—कलहान्तरिता (˚ह-अन्˚), f. a heroine<BR>separated from her lover in consequence of a quarrel;<BR>an appeased wife, one who has been angry and is<BR>sorry for it.<BR>—कलहापहृत (˚ह-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>taken away by force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहाय
कलहाय, nom. A. कलहायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>quarrel, contend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहिन्
कलहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, contentious, quarrelsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहु
कलहु कलहु, a particular high number;<BR>[cf. करफु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कला
कला कला, f. (said to be fr. 3. कल्), a small<BR>part of anything, any single part or portion of a<BR>whole, but especially a sixteenth part; a digit or one<BR>sixteenth of the moon's diameter (personified as a<BR>daughter of Kardama and wife of Marīci); interest<BR>on capital, considered as a certain part of it; a division<BR>of time (according to some (1/900) of a day, i. e. 1<BR>minute and 36 seconds; according to others (1/1800) of a<BR>day, i. e. 48 seconds; according to others 20(1/10) Kalās<BR>= 1 Muhūrta or (1/30) of a day, therefore 1 Kalā =<BR>2 minutes and 26(54/201) seconds; according to others<BR>30(1/10) Kalās = 1 Muhūrta, therefore 1 Kalā = 1<BR>minute and 35(205/301) seconds; according to others<BR>1 Kalā = 8 seconds); the sixtieth part of one thirtieth<BR>of a zodiacal sign, a minute of a degree; (in prosody)<BR>a syllabic instant; a term for the seven substrata of<BR>the elements or Dhātus of the human body (which<BR>according to one reckoning are seven, as follows,<BR>flesh, blood, fat, phlegm, urine, bile, and semen; but<BR>according to Hemacandra रस ‘chyle,’ अस्थि ‘bone,’<BR>and मज्ज ‘marrow,’ take the place of phlegm, urine,<BR>and bile); an atom (there are 3015 Kalās or atoms<BR>in every one of the six Dhātus, not counting the<BR>रस, therefore in all 18090); a small round lump,<BR>a term for the embryo shortly after conception [cf.<BR>कलन]; the menstrual discharge; any practical art,<BR>any mechanical or fine art (sixty-four such are enu-<BR>merated, as carpentering, architecture, jewellery, far-<BR>riery, acting, dancing, music, medicine, poetry,<BR>&c.); skill, ingenuity, contrivance, fraud, deceit; a<BR>boat; title of a grammatical commentary; N. of a<BR>deity; [cf. अ-कल, निष्कल, सकल.]<BR>—कला-<BR>कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in the elegant arts, singing,<BR>dancing, &c.<BR>—कला-केलि, इस्, इस्, इ, gay, frolicsome,<BR>wanton; (इस्), m. an epithet of Kāma, the god of<BR>love.<BR>—कला-धर, अस्, m. ‘bearing a digit of the<BR>moon;’ an epithet of Śiva; N. of a copyist.<BR>—कला-<BR>निधि, इस्, m. ‘a treasure or storehouse of digits,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—कलान्तर (˚ला-अन्˚), अम्, n. interest,<BR>profit.<BR>—कलाप (˚ला + आप fr. rt. आप्), अस्, m. ‘that<BR>which holds together the single parts,’ a band, a<BR>bundle (e. g. मुक्ता-कलाप, an ornament consisting<BR>of several strings of pearls; रशना-कलाप, a zone<BR>consisting of several strings, worn by women round<BR>the waist; जटा-कलाप, a tuft or knot of braided<BR>hair); totality, whole body or collection of a number<BR>of separate things, a zone, a string of bells worn by<BR>women round the waist; the rope round an elephant's<BR>neck; a bundle of arrows, a quiver with arrows, a<BR>quiver; a peacock's tail (as consisting of a multitude of<BR>single feathers); an ornament in general; N. of a<BR>grammar, supposed to be revealed by the god Kumāra<BR>or Kārttikeya to Sarva-varman; a village where the<BR>destroyer Kalki is to be born; the moon; a clever<BR>and intelligent man; a poem written in one metre;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">Page0212-a+ 72</a>]<BR>(ई), f. a bundle of grass.<BR>—कलापक, अस्, m. a band,<BR>a bundle; a string of pearls; the rope round an ele-<BR>phant's neck; a sectarian mark on the forehead; (अम्),<BR>n. a number of verses in one metre; a series of four<BR>stanzas on one subject; the eye in a peacock's<BR>feather?; (अस्, इका, अम्), to be repaid when the<BR>peacocks spread their tails.<BR>—कलाप-ग्राम, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Grāma or village.<BR>—कलाप-च्छन्द, अस्,<BR>m. an ornament of pearls consisting of twenty-four<BR>strings.<BR>—कलाप-तत्त्वार्णव (˚व-अर्˚), title of<BR>a commentary on the Kalāpa grammar.<BR>—कलाप-<BR>द्वीप, N. of a place, perhaps the same as कलाप-<BR>ग्राम.<BR>—कलाप-शिरस्, आस्, m., N. of a Muni; (a<BR>various reading for कपाल-शिरस्.)<BR>—कलापानुसारिन्<BR>(˚प-अन्˚), ई, m. a follower of the Kalāpa grammar.<BR>—कलापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with a bundle of<BR>arrows, bearing a quiver with arrows; spreading its<BR>tail (said of a peacock &c.); (ई), m. a peacock; the<BR>Indian cuckoo; the waved-leaf fig tree, Ficus Infec-<BR>toria; N. of an old teacher, a pupil of Vaiśampāyana;<BR>(according to some) the author of the Kalāpa<BR>grammar; the time (scil. कालः) when peacocks<BR>spread their tails; (इनी), f. night; the moon; a<BR>species of Cyperus.<BR>—कला-पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, filled<BR>up by single or separate parts; (अस्), m. the moon.<BR>—कला-भृत्, त्, m. ‘digit-bearer,’ the moon; an<BR>artist, a mechanic, &c.<BR>—कलायन (˚ला-अय्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a tumbler, a dancer, but especially one who dances<BR>or walks on a sharp edge, as the edge of a sword &c.<BR>—कला-वत्, आन्, m. ‘having digits,’ the moon;<BR>(ती), f. a mystical ceremony, the initiation of the<BR>Tantrika student, in which the goddess Durgā is<BR>supposed to be transferred from the water-jar to the<BR>body of the novice; N. of an Apsaras; N. of the<BR>mother of Rādhā; N. of the wife of Kṛta-varman,<BR>king of Ayodhyā; N. of the wife of Dāśārha; N. of<BR>the lute of the Gandharva Tumburu.<BR>—कला-वाद-<BR>तन्त्र, कला-विधि-तन्त्र, कला-सार-तन्त्र,<BR>names of Tantras.<BR>—कला-विलास, अस्, m. a work<BR>on rhetoric.<BR>—कला-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a work by<BR>Viśākhila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका, f. a digit of the moon. See below, s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकन्द
कलाकन्द कलाकन्द = कन्द, a species of<BR>the Atijagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकुल
कलाकुल कलाकुल, अम्, n. poison; [cf.<BR>हलाहल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाङ्कुर|कलांकुर|कलांकुरः|कलाङ्कुरः
कलाङ्कुर कलाङ्कुर, अस्, m. the bird Ardea<BR>Sibirica, a crane; an epithet of the Asura Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाङ्गल
कलाङ्गल कलाङ्गल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?)<BR>a kind of weapon (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाचिक
कलाचिक कलाचिक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?)<BR>a ladle; (आ), f. or कलाची, f. the fore-arm, the arm<BR>below the elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाटीन|कलाटीनः
कलाटीन कलाटीन, अस्, m. the white water<BR>wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाद|कलादः
कलाद कलाद, अस्, m. a goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाधिक|कलाधिकः
कलाधिक कलाधिक, अस्, m. (fr. कल and<BR>अधिक ?), a cock; [cf. कलाविक and उषाकल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलानक
कलानक कलानक, अस्, m., N. of one of<BR>the attendants of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाप|कलापः
कलाप कलाप, &c. See under कला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापूर
कलापूर कलापूर, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?),<BR>and आ, f. a kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलामक|कलामकः
कलामक कलामक, अस्, m. a kind of rice<BR>ripening in the cold season; [cf. कलम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाम्बि|कलांबिः|कलाम्बिः
कलाम्बि कलाम्बि, इस्, f. or कलाम्बिका, f.<BR>lending, a loan; usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाय|कलायः
कलाय कलाय, अस्, m., N. of various legu-<BR>minous seeds, chiefly of the order Phaseolus, particular<BR>kinds of pulse or vetches; (आ), f. a kind of Panicum,<BR>= गण्डदूर्वा.<BR>—कलाय-खञ्ज, अस्, m. one who<BR>trembles and totters as he walks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविक|कलाविकः
कलाविक कलाविक, अस्, m. a cock; [cf.<BR>कलाधिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविकल|कलाविकलः
कलाविकल कलाविकल, अस्, m. a sparrow;<BR>[cf. कलविङ्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाहक|कलाहकः
कलाहक कलाहक, अस्, m. a kind of musical<BR>instrument; [cf. काहल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलि|कलिः
कलि कलि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 3. कल्),<BR>N. of the die or side of a die, which is marked with<BR>one point (personified as a deity or evil genius in<BR>the poem of Nala); the plant Terminalia Bellerica,<BR>the nuts of which in olden times were used as dice;<BR>N. of the last and worst of the four Yugas, the present<BR>or iron age, the age of vice; (the four Yugas or ages<BR>have received their names from the marks on dice, the<BR>best mark being four points and the worst one; the<BR>Kali or fourth age contains, inclusive of the two dawns,<BR>1200 years of the gods or 432,000 years of men,<BR>and begins the eighteenth of February 3102 B. C.;<BR>at the end of this Yuga the world is to be destroyed);<BR>strife (considered as the son of क्रोध ‘Anger’ and<BR>हिंसा ‘Injury,’ and as generating with his sister<BR>दुरुक्ति ‘Calumny,’ two children, viz. भय ‘Fear’<BR>and मृत्यु ‘Death’); dissension, war, battle; the worst<BR>in any class; a hero; an arrow; Ved., N. of a class of<BR>mythic beings related to the Gandharvas, and sup-<BR>posed by some to be fond of gambling; in epic<BR>poetry कलि is held to be the fifteenth of the Deva-<BR>gandharvas or children of the Munis; N. of a man;<BR>(इस् or ई), f. an unblown flower, a bud.<BR>—कलि-कार,<BR>अस्, m., N. of several birds, the fork-tailed shrike;<BR>Loxia Philippensis, a small bird with a yellow head;<BR>a kind of chicken; a plant bearing a nut which is<BR>used as a febrifuge, Grey Bonduc, = करञ्ज and<BR>पूतिकरञ्ज; an epithet of Nārada; (ई), f. the<BR>poisonous plant Methonica Superba.<BR>—कलि-कारक,<BR>अस्, m. the plant Cæsalpinia Bonducella; (a various<BR>reading has कलि-मारक); an epithet of Nārada<BR>(‘the quarrelsome’).<BR>—कलि-द्रुम, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Terminalia Bellerica or the tree of strife, being sup-<BR>posed to be the favourite haunt of imps or goblins.<BR>—कलि-धर्म-निर्णय, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—कलि-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a writer on music.<BR>—कलि-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, quarrelsome, mischievous,<BR>mischief-making; (अस्), m. a monkey, an ape; an<BR>epithet of Nārada.<BR>—कलि-मारक, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Cæsalpinia Bonducella; (a various reading for कलि-<BR>कारक, q. v.)<BR>—कलि-मालक, अस्, m. and कलि-<BR>माल्य, अस्, m. the plant Cæsalpinia Bonducella.<BR>—कलि-युग, अम्, n., N. of the fourth age, the<BR>present or iron age.<BR>—कलि-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the tree<BR>Terminalia Bellerica.<BR>—कलि-संश्रय, अस्, m. the<BR>act of betaking one's self to Kali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिक|कलिकः
कलिक कलिक, अस्, m. a curlew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका कलिका, f. (fr. कला), a digit or the<BR>sixteenth part of the moon; an unblown flower<BR>[cf. कलि]; the bottom or peg of the Indian lute,<BR>made of cane; N. of several metres, a metre con-<BR>taining 4 × 8 + 16 syllabic instants; a metre of four<BR>lines, each containing fifteen syllables; a metre con-<BR>sisting of 12 + 8 + 16 + 20 syllables; title of a work<BR>on medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकाता
कलिकाता कलिकाता, f. the modern name<BR>Calcutta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकापूर्व|कलिकापूर्व्व|कलिकापूर्व्वं
कलिकापूर्व कलिकापूर्व, अम्, n. (fr. कलिका<BR>and अपूर्व?), acts leading to future consequences<BR>not connected with those of a previous birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्ग|कलिंग|कलिङ्गं|कलिङ्गः
कलिङ्ग कलिङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a country;<BR>the name is applied in the Purāṇas to several places,<BR>but especially signifies a district on the Coromandel<BR>coast, extending from below Cuttack (Kaṭaka) to<BR>the vicinity of Madras; in this sense, like some other<BR>names of countries, it is usually confined to the plural<BR>number, confounding the place with the people in-<BR>habiting it, (these people are said to owe their origin<BR>to Kaliṅga, the son of Dīrgha-tamas and Sudeṣṇā;<BR>Kaliṅga being sometimes identified with the epic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">Page0212-c+ 74</a>]<BR>Bali); N. of a scholiast on the Amara-koṣa; N. of<BR>a poet; the fork-tailed shrike, Lanius Forficatus, (in<BR>this sense derived from कलिम् and ग?; cf. कलि-<BR>कार); the plants Cæsalpinia Bonducella, Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica, Acacia Sirisa, Ficus Infectoria; (आ),<BR>f. a beautiful woman; the plant Ipomœa Turpethum;<BR>(अम्), n. Indra-grain [cf. इन्द्र-यव]; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), clever; cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्गक|कलिङ्गकः
कलिङ्गक, अस्, m. the seed of the Coraiya, Indra-<BR>grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्गडी
कलिङ्गडी, f. (?) an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिञ्ज|कलिंज|कलिंजः|कलिञ्जः
कलिञ्ज कलिञ्ज, अस्, m. a mat, a screen;<BR>(a various reading for किलिञ्ज.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित कलित. See 3. कल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्द|कलिंद|कलिंदः|कलिन्दः
कलिन्द कलिन्द, अस्, m. the tree Terminalia<BR>Bellerica; the sun; (in these meanings perhaps a<BR>compound of कलिम् and द); N. of a mountain on<BR>which the river Yamunā rises; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (ई), f. a N. of the river Yamunā or Jumnā.<BR>—कलिन्द-कन्या or कलिन्द-नन्दिनी or क-<BR>लिन्द-शैल-जाता, f. epithets of the river Yamunā or<BR>Jumnā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दिका
कलिन्दिका कलिन्दिका, f. science; (a various<BR>reading has कलन्दिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिल|कलिलः
कलिल कलिल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कॄ?),<BR>covered with, full of; mixed, blended; impenetrable,<BR>impervious; (अम्), n. a large heap, thicket, confusion;<BR>[cf. कलुष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुक्क|कलुक्कः
कलुक्क कलुक्क, अस्, m. a musical instru-<BR>ment, a cymbal; (आ), f. a tavern; a meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुष|कलुषं|कलुषः
कलुष कलुष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कॄ?, said<BR>to be fr. rt. 3. कल्), turbid, foul, muddy, unclean;<BR>dark, opaque, without brilliancy; hoarse (as the<BR>voice); wicked, bad; lazy, idle; (अस्), m. a buffalo;<BR>(अम्), n. dirt, uncleanness; sin, wrath.<BR>—कलुष-<BR>ता, f. or कलुष-त्व, अम्, n. foulness, turbidness;<BR>darkness, opacity; agitation, trouble, anger.<BR>—कलु-<BR>ष-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, of impure origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषाय
कलुषाय, nom. A. कलुषायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>become turbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषित
कलुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, foul, impure; defiled, con-<BR>taminated; wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषिन्
कलुषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, foul, impure; defiled, depraved;<BR>wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषीकृ
कलुषी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make turbid or unclean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलूतर
कलूतर कलूतर, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलेवर|कलेवरं|कलेवरः
कलेवर कलेवर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the body;<BR>[cf. Lat. cadâver.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्क|कल्कः
कल्क कल्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>3. कल्), a viscous sediment deposited by oily sub-<BR>stances when ground; a kind of tenacious paste;<BR>dirt, filth; the wax of the ear; ordure, fæces; mean-<BR>ness, falsehood, deceit, sin, hypocrisy, pride; the<BR>tree Terminalia Bellerica; incense; levigated powder;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), sinful, wicked; [cf. कलुष, कल्म-<BR>ष, किल्विष.]<BR>—कल्क-फल, अस्, m. the pome-<BR>granate plant (दाडिम).<BR>—कल्कालय (˚क-आल्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कन|कल्कनं
कल्कन, अम्, n. falsehood, deceit, cheating,<BR>quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कि|कल्किः
कल्कि, इस्, m. a N. of Viṣṇu in his future capacity<BR>of destroyer of the wicked and liberator of the world<BR>from its enemies. This will constitute the tenth and<BR>last Avatāra or descent of the deity, and is to take<BR>place at the end of the four Yugas or ages.<BR>—कल्कि-<BR>प्रादुर्भाव, अस्, m. the apparition of Kalki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्किन्
कल्किन्, ई, इनी, इ, foul, turbid, having sediment,<BR>dirty, wicked; (ई), m. = कल्कि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कल
कल्कल कल्कल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प|कल्पः
कल्प कल्प, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. कॢप्), prac-<BR>ticable, feasible, possible; proper, fit, able, competent<BR>(with gen., loc., inf., and at the end of a compound,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-a" target="_blank">Page0213-a+ 81</a>]<BR>e. g. धर्मस्य कल्पः, competent for duty; स्व-<BR>कर्मणि न कल्पः, not competent for his own work;<BR>यदा न शासितुं कल्पः, if he is not able to rule);<BR>strong, vigorous; कल्पे वयसि, in the vigorous<BR>period of life; (अस्), m. a sacred precept, law, ordi-<BR>nance [cf. विधि, न्याय]; manner of acting, pro-<BR>ceeding, practice prescribed by the Vedas (e. g. प्र-<BR>थमः कल्पः, a rule to be observed before any<BR>other rule, first duty; एतेन कल्पेन, in this way;<BR>पशु-कल्प, the rites at the animal sacrifice; न<BR>कल्प-मात्रे, not according to the mere letter<BR>of the rule without regard to its spirit); the most<BR>complete of the six Vedāṅgas, that which prescribes<BR>the ritual and gives rules for ceremonial or sacrificial<BR>acts; (in medic.) treatment of the sick, manner of<BR>curing (e. g. कल्पेतर, one cured or treated differ-<BR>ently); the doctrine of poisons and antidotes; (at<BR>the end of an adjective compound) having the manner<BR>or form of anything, similar to, resembling, like but<BR>with a degree of inferiority (e. g. प्रभात-कल्पा<BR>शर्वरी, the night which is something similar to<BR>dawn, i. e. the night at the approach of dawn; मृ-<BR>त-कल्प, similar to a dead person, almost dead;<BR>अभेद्य-कल्प, almost impenetrable; according to<BR>native grammarians कल्प so used is an accentless<BR>affix, before which a final स् is left unchanged, and<BR>final ई and ऊ shortened; native authorities also con-<BR>nect कल्प with a simple verb, thus पचति-कल्पम्,<BR>he cooks pretty well); a resolve, a determination; pro-<BR>priety, fitness (?); optionality, alternative [cf. वि-कल्प],<BR>doubt; a fabulous period of time, a day of Brahmā<BR>or 1000 Yugas, a period of four hundred and thirty-<BR>two million years of mortals, measuring the duration<BR>of the world; (a month of Brahmā is supposed to<BR>contain thirty such Kalpas; according to the Mahā-<BR>bhārata twelve months of Brahmā constitute his year,<BR>and one hundred such years his lifetime; fifty years<BR>of Brahmā are supposed to have elapsed, and we are<BR>now in the श्वेतवाराह-कल्प of the fifty-first.<BR>The Kalpa, in the same way as the Saṃvatsara or<BR>year, is personified as son of Dhruva and Bhrami; at<BR>the end of a Kalpa the world is annihilated; hence<BR>कल्प is sometimes used for कल्पान्त or the de-<BR>struction of the world); N. of certain sentences or<BR>verses containing the verb कॢप्; one of the trees<BR>of paradise, see कल्प-तरु below; (with Jainas)<BR>a term for a particular abode of the deities [cf.<BR>कल्प-भव and कल्पातीत]; (अम् or आ), m. f. a<BR>kind of intoxicating liquor; [cf. अ-कल्प, अनु-कल्प,<BR>उप-कल्प, &c.]<BR>—कल्प-कार, अस्, m. an author of<BR>ritual or ceremonial rules.<BR>—कल्प-केदार, a medical<BR>work by Kālīśiva.<BR>—कल्प-क्षय, अस्, m. the end<BR>of a Kalpa, end of the world, destruction of all things.<BR>—कल्प-गा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—कल्प-तरु, उस्,<BR>m. one of the trees of Svarga or Indra's paradise,<BR>a fabulous tree, granting all desires, hence figuratively<BR>a generous person; title of a work on jurisprudence;<BR>also a work of Lakṣmīdhara; also one of Vācaspati.<BR>—कल्प-द्रु, उस्, m. = कल्प-तरु, also N. of a<BR>lexicon by Keśava.<BR>—कल्प-द्रुम, अस्, m. = कल्प-<BR>तरु; a work on jurisprudence; also a Tantra work;<BR>the collection of roots by Vopadeva is called कवि-<BR>कल्पद्रुम, the tree from which poets obtain all<BR>desired roots; and the modern encyclopedia of Rā-<BR>dhākānta is entitled शब्द-कल्पद्रुम, the tree<BR>which satisfies every desire for words.<BR>—कल्प-पा-<BR>दप, अस्, m. = कल्प-तरु above.<BR>—कल्प-पाल,<BR>अस्, m. a protector of order, a legitimate prince; a<BR>person who distils or sells spirituous liquors.<BR>—कल्प-<BR>भव, आस्, m. pl., N. of a certain class of deities.<BR>—कल्प-महीरुह्, ट्, m. = कल्प-वृक्ष.<BR>—कल्-<BR>प-युक्ति, title of a work by Budha.<BR>—कल्प-लता,<BR>f. a creeper yielding everything desired; कल्पलता-<BR>वतार, title of a commentary of Kṛṣṇa on the<BR>Vīja-gaṇita; कल्पलता-प्रकाश, title of a com-<BR>mentary on the Viṣṇu-bhaktilatā.<BR>—कल्प-लतिका,<BR>f. = कल्प-लता above; (शब्द-क्˚, title of a dic-<BR>tionary.)<BR>—कल्प-वर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Vasu-deva and Upa-devā.<BR>—कल्प-वल्ली, f. = कल्प-<BR>लता above.<BR>—कल्प-वायु, उस्, m. the wind that is<BR>to blow at the end of the world.<BR>—कल्प-विटपिन्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">Page0213-b+ 77</a>]<BR>ई, m. or कल्प-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the fabulous tree of<BR>Indra's heaven; see above.<BR>—कल्प-विधि, इस्, m. a<BR>rule resembling a ceremonial injunction.<BR>—कल्प-<BR>वृक्ष-लता, f. a work by Lollaṭa.<BR>—कल्प-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n. a Sūtra manual of ritual; also a medicinal<BR>work and a work of the Jaina sect so called.<BR>—कल्प-<BR>सूत्र-व्याख्या, f. a Jaina work on the Kalpasūtras.<BR>—कल्पातीत (˚प-अत्˚), आस्, m. pl., N. of a certain<BR>class of deities.<BR>—कल्पादि (˚प-आदि), इस्, m. the<BR>beginning of a Kalpa, the renovation of all things.<BR>—कल्पानुपद (˚प-अन्˚), अम्, n. title of a work<BR>belonging to the Sāma-veda.<BR>—कल्पान्त (˚प-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the end of a Kalpa, the destruction of the<BR>world.<BR>—कल्पान्तर (˚प-अन्˚), अम्, n. another<BR>Kalpa.<BR>—कल्पान्त-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, lasting to the<BR>end of a Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पक|कल्पकः
कल्पक, अस्, m. a rite, a ceremony; a barber [cf.<BR>कल्पनी]; a kind of Curcuma, commonly कर्चूर.<BR>—कल्पक-तरु, उस्, m., N. of a tree of Indra's<BR>paradise; [cf. कल्प-तरु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पन|कल्पनं
कल्पन, अम्, n. forming, fashioning; doing,<BR>performing; fixing, constituting; anything fixed or<BR>placed upon another thing for ornament; act of<BR>clipping, cutting; (आ), f. fixing, constituting, settling;<BR>making, performing; fabrication; composing, com-<BR>position (of a poem &c.); inventing, invention; for-<BR>gery; a fancy, an idea or image formed in the mind;<BR>an imagination, intention; contrivance, plan, infer-<BR>ence; caparisoning or decorating an elephant; (ई),<BR>f. a scissors or shears.<BR>—कल्पना-शक्ति, इस्, f. the<BR>power of forming ideas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पनीय
कल्पनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made, fashioned or<BR>contrived, to be accomplished, possible, to be substi-<BR>tuted or supplied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पिक
कल्पिक, अस्, आ, अम्, fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पित|कल्पितः
कल्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, made, fabricated, artificial;<BR>composed, invented; arranged, put in order; pre-<BR>pared; brought; inferred; (अस्), m. an elephant<BR>armed or caparisoned for war.<BR>—कल्पितार्घ (˚त-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one for whom a respectful offering<BR>is prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पिन्
कल्पिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. a term used in gambling<BR>with dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प्य
कल्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made or contrived or<BR>performed, to be prescribed; relating to ritual; to<BR>be substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मन्
कल्मन् कल्मन्, अ, n. according to native<BR>grammarians = कर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मलि|कल्मलिः
कल्मलि कल्मलि, Ved. splendor (of the<BR>stars?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मलीक|कल्मलीकं
कल्मलीक, अम्, n. brightness, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मलीकिन्
कल्मलीकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. burning, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मष|कल्मषं|कल्मषः
कल्मष कल्मष, अस्, अम्, m. n. stain, dirt,<BR>sin, dregs; जल-कल्मष, the dirt or sediment of<BR>water; (अम्), n. darkness, a division of the infernal<BR>regions; the hand below the wrist; (अस्, आ, अम्), dirty,<BR>foul.<BR>—कल्मष-ध्वंस-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, destroy-<BR>ing darkness or sin; preventing the commission of<BR>crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माष|कल्माषः
कल्माष कल्माष, अस्, ई, अम्, variegated,<BR>spotted; black, black and white; (अस्), m. a variegated<BR>colour; a mixture of black and white, the black<BR>colour; a Rakṣas, demon or goblin; a species of<BR>fragrant rice; N. of a Nāga; a form of fire; N. of<BR>a servant of the sun, identified with Yama; Śākya-<BR>muni in a former birth; (ई), f. the spotted cow of<BR>Jamadagni, the giver of all desires; N. of a river;<BR>(अम्), n. a stain.<BR>—कल्माष-कण्ठ, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कल्माष-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having a variegated neck.<BR>—कल्माष-तन्तुर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—कल्माष-ता, f. spottedness, the<BR>state of being variegated.<BR>—कल्माष-पाद, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king; also Saudāsa, a descendant of Ikṣvāku,<BR>transformed to a Rākṣasa by Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—कल्मा-<BR>षाङ्घ्रि (˚ष-अङ्˚), इस्, m. another N. of the same<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्य|कल्यं|कल्यः
कल्य कल्य, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. 3. कल्?), well,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">Page0213-c+ 77</a>]<BR>sound, healthy, free from sickness; ready, prepared,<BR>armed; clever, dexterous; agreeable, auspicious (as a<BR>speech or discourse); instructive, admonitory; deaf and<BR>dumb [cf. कल and कल्ल]; (अम्), n. dawn, day-<BR>break; to-morrow; yesterday (?); कल्यम् or कल्ये,<BR>ind. at day-break; (अम् or आ), n. f. spirituous liquor;<BR>congratulation; good wishes; good tidings; (आ), f.<BR>Emblic Myrobalan, see हरीतकी; [cf. Gr. καλός<BR>καλλίων, κάλλιστος &c., for καλyος &c.]<BR>—कल्य-<BR>जग्धि, इस्, f. the morning-meal, breakfast.<BR>—कल्य-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. or कल्य-ता, f. health; recovery, con-<BR>valescence.<BR>—कल्य-पाल or कल्या-पाल or कल्य-<BR>पालक or कल्या-पालक, अस्, m. a distiller.<BR>—कल्-<BR>य-वर्त, अस्, m. the morning-meal, breakfast; a<BR>light meal; (अम्), n. anything light, a trifle, a trivial<BR>or unimportant matter; [cf. प्रातराश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याण|कल्याणं|कल्याणः
कल्याण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, beautiful, agreeable, friendly,<BR>illustrious, noble, excellent, happy, beneficial, salutary,<BR>prosperous, propitious, lucky, well, right, good; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a prince, also called Bhaṭṭaśrīkalyāṇa; N. of<BR>the author of the poem Gītāgaṅgādhara; (ई), f. a cow;<BR>a leguminous shrub, Glycine Debilis; N. of two cities;<BR>N. of a river in Ceylon; N. of a deity; (अम्), n. good<BR>fortune, happiness, prosperity; virtue; a festival;<BR>gold; heaven; N. of the eleventh of the fourteen<BR>Pūrvas or most ancient writings of the Jainas.<BR>—कल्-<BR>याण-कटक, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—कल्याण-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, propitious, auspicious, conferring<BR>good fortune &c.<BR>—कल्याण-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, or<BR>कल्याण-कारक, अस्, आ, अम्, creating prosperity or<BR>profit.<BR>—कल्याण-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, virtuous, good; pro-<BR>pitious, lucky.<BR>—कल्याण-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>astronomer in the twelfth century A. D.<BR>—कल्याण-<BR>चार, अस्, ई, अम्, following virtuous courses; lucky,<BR>fortunate.<BR>—कल्याण-देवी, f., N. of the wife of Ja-<BR>yāpīḍa.<BR>—कल्याण-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, virtuous,<BR>good.<BR>—कल्याण-पञ्चमीक, अस्, m. a fortnight,<BR>the fifth lunar day of which is lucky.<BR>—कल्याण-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—कल्याण-मल्ल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince; N. of the author of a work<BR>called Anaṅgaraṅga; N. of a son of Gajamalla,<BR>author of the commentary called Mālatī.<BR>—कल्याण-<BR>मित्र, अम्, n. a friend of virtue, a religious counsellor.<BR>—कल्याण-राज-चरित्र, अम्, n. ‘the life of king<BR>Kalyāṇa’ by Madana.<BR>—कल्याण-वचन, अम्, n.<BR>friendly speech, good wishes.<BR>—कल्याण-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, happy.<BR>—कल्याण-वर्त्मन्, आ, f., N. of<BR>a princess, who erected a statue of Viṣṇu, called<BR>Kalyāṇa-svāmi-keśava.<BR>—कल्याण-वर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of an astronomer.<BR>—कल्याण-वीज, अस्, m. a<BR>sort of pulse, Ervum Hirsutum.<BR>—कल्याण-शर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a scholiast on Varāha-mihira.<BR>—कल्याण-<BR>सूत्र, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—कल्याणाचार<BR>(˚ण-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, following good practices,<BR>virtuous.<BR>—कल्याणाभिजन (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>of illustrious birth.<BR>—कल्याणी-पञ्चमा, आस्, f. pl.<BR>(scil. रात्रयस्) nights of which the fifth is lucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणक
कल्याणक, अस्, इका, अम्, auspicious, efficacious (as<BR>a drug), prosperous, happy; (इका), f. red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिन्
कल्याणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, happy, lucky, prosperous;<BR>illustrious; virtuous, good; (इनी), f. the water-plant<BR>Sida Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्युष
कल्युष कल्युष, अम्, n. the wrist (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल्
कल्ल् कल्ल्, cl. 1. A. कल्लते, -लितुम्, to<BR>sound indistinctly; to sound; to be mute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, deaf; (also a various reading<BR>for कन्न, q. v.)<BR>—कल्ल-त्व, अम्, n. or कल्ल-ता,<BR>f. deafness; indistinct articulation, hoarseness.<BR>—कल्-<BR>ल-मूक, अस्, आ, अम्, deaf and dumb.<BR>—कल्ल-वीर-<BR>तन्त्र, a Buddhist work, also called Caṇḍamahā-<BR>roṣaṇa-tantra.<BR>—कल्लार्य, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लट
कल्लट कल्लट, अस्, m., N. of a prince; श्री-<BR>कल्लट, N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लि
कल्लि कल्लि, ind. to-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लिनाथ
कल्लिनाथ कल्लिनाथ, अस्, m., N. of a writer<BR>on music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोल|कल्लोलः
कल्लोल कल्लोल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. कद् + लोल),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">Page0214-a+ 70</a>]<BR>inimical, hostile; (अस्), m. a wave; a surge, a billow;<BR>an enemy; joy, happiness, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोलित
कल्लोलित, अस्, आ, अम्, surging, billowy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोलिनी
कल्लोलिनी, f. a surging stream, a river in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्हण
कल्हण कल्हण, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Rāja-taraṅgiṇī (often spelt कह्लण); N. of<BR>the father of the copyist Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्हार|कल्हारं
कल्हार कल्हार, अम्, n. a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्
कव् कव्, cl. 1. A. कवते, -वितुम्, to de-<BR>scribe (as a poet); to paint; to picture,<BR>colour; [cf. कब्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव
कव 1. कव, a form substituted for क, का,<BR>and 1. कु, to express deterioration or deficiency.<BR>—क-<BR>व-पथ, अस्, m., Ved. a bad way.<BR>—कवाग्नि (˚व-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m. a little fire.<BR>—कवोष्ण (˚व-उष्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, slightly warm, tepid; (अम्), n. slight warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव
2. कव in अ-कव and कवासख; [cf. कवत्नु<BR>and कवारि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवक|कवकं|कवकः
कवक कवक, अम्, n. a fungus, a mush-<BR>room; a mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवच|कवचं|कवचः
कवच कवच, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>3. कु), armour, mail, a coat of mail, a cuirass; the<BR>jacket of a boy; an amulet, a charm, the mystical<BR>syllable हुम् or हूम्, forming part of a Mantra and<BR>considered as a preservative like armour; it is also<BR>inscribed on a birch leaf &c. and worn as an amulet,<BR>being carried about the person as a charm (this is<BR>the probable meaning in the titles दुर्गा-कवच,<BR>सूर्यक्˚, शिवक्˚, भवानीक्˚, &c.); a drum used in<BR>battle, a kettle-drum; the tree Hibiscus Populneoides.<BR>—कवच-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the leaf of a birch tree;<BR>[cf. भूर्ज-पत्त्र.]<BR>—कवच-पाश, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>the fastening of a cuirass or coat of mail.<BR>—कवच-<BR>हर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, wearing armour or mail, or a<BR>jacket; wearing amulets; (अस्), m. a boy, a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचित
कवचित, अस्, आ, अम्, dressed in armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचिन्
कवचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dressed in armour; (ई), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवटी
कवटी कवटी, f. the leaf or panel of a door;<BR>[cf. कवाट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवड|कवडः
कवड कवड, अस्, m. water &c. for washing<BR>the mouth; [cf. कवल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवत्नु
कवत्नु कवत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. 1. कु), Ved. self-<BR>ish, stingy; (Sāy.) a bad deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवन|कवनं
कवन कवन, अम्, n. water; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a son of Śṛṅgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवन्तक
कवन्तक कवन्तक, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवन्ध
कवन्ध कवन्ध and कवन्धिन्. See क-<BR>बन्ध and कबन्धिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवपथ
कवपथ कव-पथ. See under 1. कव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवयी
कवयी कवयी, f. the fish Cojus Cobojus<BR>(commonly called Kavay or Kay), remarkable for<BR>going by land from one spot to another; [cf. क-<BR>विका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवर|कवरं|कवरः
कवर कवर, अस्, आ or ई (?), अम् (fr. rt. 3. कु),<BR>mixed, intermingled, blended; set, inlaid; (अस्), m.<BR>a lecturer; (अस्, ई), m. f. (according to some also n.)<BR>a braid or fillet of hair; (अस्, अम्), m. n. salt; sour-<BR>ness or acidity; (आ), f. the plant Ocimum Gratissi-<BR>mum; (ई), f. the leaf of the Asa Fœtida plant,<BR>Hiṅgupattrī.<BR>—कवर-पुच्छी, f. having a twisted<BR>tail or one which resembles a braid.<BR>—कवरी-भर<BR>or कवरी-भार, अस्, m. a fine head of hair.<BR>—क-<BR>वरी-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, wearing a fillet of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरकी
कवरकी कवरकी, f. a captive, a prisoner;<BR>[cf. वन्दि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवल|कवलं|कवलः
कवल कवल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. 3. कु?), a<BR>mouthful; an astringent wash for cleansing the mouth,<BR>a gargle; a kind of fish, commonly called Baliya; [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">Page0214-b+ 77</a>]<BR>Hib. caomhna, caomhnadh, ‘food, nourishment.’]<BR>—कवल-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिका
कवलिका, f. a piece of cloth over a sore or wound,<BR>a bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowed as a mouthful,<BR>eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवष|कवषः
कवष कवष, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. according to<BR>Mahīdhara either ‘sounding, creaking,’ or ‘pierced’<BR>(said of the leaves of a door); (अस्), m. a shield; N.<BR>of a man, son of Ilūṣa or Ailūṣī, author of several<BR>hymns of the Ṛg-veda; N. of a Muni; N. of the<BR>author of a Dharma-śāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवस|कवसः
कवस कवस, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 3. कु),<BR>armour, a coat of mail; a prickly shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट कवाट, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. (for क-<BR>पाट), the leaf or panel of a door; a door; (at the<BR>end of a compound कवाटक; cf. कवटी.)<BR>—क-<BR>वाट-घ्न, अस्, m. breaking the door, a thief; [cf.<BR>कपाट-घ्न.]<BR>—कवाट-वक्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>plant; commonly called कवाटवेटु; or according<BR>to others कवाडवेण्टुया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवार|कवारं
कवार कवार, अस्, m. the bird Tantalus<BR>Falcinellus; (अम्), n. a lotus; [cf. कवेल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवारि
कवारि कवारि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. selfish, stingy;<BR>[cf. अ-कवारि, अ-कव, कवत्नु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवासख
कवा-सख, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. a companion of the<BR>selfish man, selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि कवि, इस्, इस् or ई, इ (said to be fr. rt. 3.<BR>कु; but perhaps related to आकूत, आकूति), sensible,<BR>intelligent, prudent, clever, wise, learned; a thinker,<BR>a wise man, a sage, an intelligent man; (metaphoric-<BR>ally) epithet of the gates of the sacrificial enclosure;<BR>epithet of the Ṛbhus (as skilful in contrivance);<BR>epithet of the old sages or patriarchs, now as spirits<BR>surrounding the sun; epithet of the gods, especially<BR>of Agni, Indra, Varuṇa, the Maruts, and Ādityas;<BR>epithet of the Soma priest &c.; (इस्), m. a poet,<BR>especially one who composes artificial poems; N.<BR>of a man, according to some genealogies a son of<BR>Brahmā, according to others a son of Bhṛgu and<BR>father of Śukra; epithet of Śukra, the regent of the<BR>planet Venus and preceptor of the demons; the sons<BR>of several Manus are also called Kavis; N. of a son of<BR>Kauśika and pupil of Garga; also a son of Ṛṣabha;<BR>N. of Vālmīki, the inventor of poesy and author of<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa; the sun ?; (इस् or ई), f. the bit of<BR>a bridle or the reins altogether; a ladle.<BR>—कवि-<BR>कण्ठ-हार, अस्, m. ‘the ornament of the neck of<BR>a poet,’ title of a work on rhetoric.<BR>—कवि-कल्प-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. title of a collection of roots written<BR>in verse by Vopadeva.<BR>—कवि-कल्प-लता, f. title of<BR>a work on rhetoric by Devendra.<BR>—कवि-क्रतु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. having wise designs, wise; (Sāy.) one<BR>who possesses wisdom or sacrifices.<BR>—कवि-चन्द्र,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Karṇa-pūra and father of Kavi-<BR>vallabha, author of the Kāvya-candrikā; the author<BR>of the Dhātu-candrikā; the author of the Ratnāvalī;<BR>the author of the Rāmacandra-campū; the author<BR>of the Śānti-candrikā; the author of a grammar<BR>called Sārala-harī; the author of a book named<BR>Stavāvalī.<BR>—कवि-च्छद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. delighting<BR>in wise men; (Sāy.) causing pleasure to the wise.<BR>—कवि-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, m. an epithet of Vālmīki,<BR>the author of the Rāmāyaṇa, ‘the oldest of poets.’<BR>—कवि-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, wisest.<BR>—कवि-तर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, wiser.<BR>—कवि-ता, f. poesy, poetic style<BR>or composition.<BR>—कवितामृत-कूप (˚ता-अम्˚),<BR>अस्, m. title of a modern collection of verses, ‘a well<BR>of nectar of poetry.’<BR>—कविता-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, un-<BR>derstanding poesy, wise, learned, a poet, a genius.<BR>—कवि-त्व, अम्, n. wisdom; poesy.<BR>—कवि-त्वन,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. wisdom.<BR>—कवित्व-रत्नाकर, अस्,<BR>m. title of a modern work on rhetoric.<BR>—कवि-<BR>दर्पण, N. of a work by Raghu.<BR>—कवि-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a dramatic author.<BR>—कवि-प्रशस्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. highly esteemed or praised by sages.<BR>—कवि-प्रिया, f. a work on rhetoric by Keśava-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">Page0214-c+ 73</a>]<BR>dāsa.<BR>—कवि-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कवि-<BR>भूम, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कवि-भूषण,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Kavi-candra.<BR>—कवि-रथ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince, a son of Citra-ratha.<BR>—कवि-<BR>रहस्य, अम्, n. ‘the secret of the learned,’ title<BR>of a collection of roots by Halāyudha.<BR>—कवि-राज,<BR>अस्, m. king of the poets, N. of the author of the<BR>Rāghavapāṇḍavīya.<BR>—कवि-रामायण, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Vālmīki, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>(an incorrect form for रामायण-कवि.)<BR>—कवि-<BR>लासिका or कवि-लाशिका, f. (?) a kind of lute.<BR>—कवि-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, m., N. of the son of Kavi-candra.<BR>—कवि-वृध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. prospering the<BR>wise.<BR>—कवि-शस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praised by wise<BR>men.<BR>—कवीश्वर (˚वि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a king of poets;<BR>N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविक|कविकं|कविकः
कविक, अम्, n. the bit of a bridle or the reins<BR>altogether; (आ), f. the bit of a bridle; N. of a flower, =<BR>केविकापुष्य; a sort of fish, commonly called Kay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवितृ
कवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ (?), wise, learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविय|कवियं
कविय, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bit of a bridle or the reins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीय|कवीयं
1. कवीय, nom. P., Ved. कवीयति, -यितुम्, to act<BR>like a wise man; A. to claim wisdom for one's self,<BR>pretend to it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीय|कवीयं
2. कवीय, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bit of a bridle or the<BR>reins; [cf. कविय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीयस्
कवीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. (comparative for कवि-<BR>तर), wiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्य|कव्यं|कव्यः
कव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. a wise, intelligent man;<BR>(अस्), m. a class of manes; N. of one of the seven<BR>sages of the fourth Manvantara; (अम्), n. the quali-<BR>ties or the actions of a sage; ‘what must be offered<BR>to sages,’ an oblation or offering of food to deceased<BR>ancestors; (generally connected with हव्य.)<BR>—क-<BR>व्य-ता, f., Ved. the qualities or the actions or the<BR>state of a sage, wisdom.<BR>—कव्य-वाड or कव्य-<BR>वाल, अस्, m. (formed fr. कव्य-वाह्), a class of<BR>manes or deified ancestors.<BR>—कव्य-वाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, or<BR>कव्य-वाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. an offering to sages,<BR>what must be offered or what belongs to them; (अस्),<BR>m. fire; an epithet of Śiva; (the word is formed<BR>like हव्य-वाहन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविञ्जुक
कविञ्जुक कविञ्जुक, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवूल
कवूल कवूल (in astrol.) = Arabic قبول<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवेल|कवेलं
कवेल कवेल, अम्, n. a lotus; [cf. कवार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवोष्ण|कवोष्णं
