कश्
कश् कश्, cl. 1. P. कशति, -शितुम्, to sound;<BR>(कश् occurs also as a various reading for<BR>कंस्, कस्, झष्, and शश्); [cf. rt. काश्; cf. also<BR>Hib. casgairim.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश|कशः
कश कश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कश् above?; in<BR>the sense ‘whip’ connected with rt. कष्), Ved. a<BR>species of small animal; a whip; (आ), f. a whip;<BR>whipping, flogging; a string, a rope; the mouth; a<BR>quality; (sometimes spelt कषा.)<BR>—कश-कृत्स्न,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कशा-त्रय, अम्, n. three<BR>modes of whipping (a horse), good, bad, and middling.<BR>—कशार्ह (˚शा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deserving a whip-<BR>ping.<BR>—कशा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with a whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्य|कश्यं
कश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, deserving the whip; (अम्), n.<BR>a horse's flank; spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशस्
कशस् कशस्, अस्, n. water.<BR>—कशो-जू, ऊस्, ऊस्,<BR>उ, Ved. running near the water; (perhaps a Pr. N.?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपु|कशिपुः
कशिपु कशिपु, उस्, उ, m. n. a mat; a pillow;<BR>(उस्), m. food; clothing; (ऊ), du. food and clothing;<BR>(sometimes spelt कसिपु; cf. हिरण्य-कशिपु.)<BR>—कशिपूपबर्हण (˚पु-उप्˚), अम्, n., Ved. a<BR>cover of a pillow, cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशीका
कशीका कशीका, f., Ved. a weasel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशु
कशु कशु, उस्, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरक
कशेरक कशेरक, अस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरु|कशेरुः
कशेरु कशेरु or कसेरु, उस्, उ, m. n. (fr.<BR>rt. शॄ with क prefixed?), the back-bone; a kind of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">Page0215-a+ 74</a>]<BR>grass, Scirpus Kysoor; (उस्), m. one of the nine<BR>divisions of Jambu-dvīpa; (उस्), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Tvaṣṭṛ; (sometimes spelt कसेरु.)<BR>—कशेरु-मत्<BR>or कसेरु-मत्, आन्, m., N. of a Yavana; N. of a<BR>part of Bharata-varṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुक|कशेरुकं|कशेरुकः
कशेरुक or कसेरुक, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. a sort<BR>of grass, Scirpus Kysoor; (आ), f. the back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुस्
कशेरुस्, उस्, n. or कशेरू, ऊस्, f. a sort of grass,<BR>Scirpus Kysoor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशोक
कशोक कशोक, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a class<BR>of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्चन
कश्चन कश्चन, &c. See under 2. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मल|कश्मलं
कश्मल कश्मल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. कस्?),<BR>consternation, alarm; fainting, syncope; dejection of<BR>mind, depression of spirit, lowness, weakness; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), foul, dirty.<BR>—कश्मल-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>mentally debased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मश
कश्मश कश्मश, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), Ved.<BR>consternation (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीर|कश्मीरः
कश्मीर कश्मीर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कश्), N. of a country; according to Burnouf a<BR>contraction of Kaśyapamīra; [cf. काश्मीर.]<BR>—कश्-<BR>मीर-जन्मन्, आ or अ, m. n. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्य|कश्यं
कश्य कश्य. See under कश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यत
कश्यत कश्यत, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यप|कश्यपः
कश्यप कश्यप, अस्, आ, अम्, having black<BR>teeth; (अस्), m. a tortoise; a sort of fish; a kind of<BR>deer; a class of divine beings similar to or equal to<BR>Prajāpati, (also in pl. a peculiar class of semi-divine<BR>spirits or genii connected with or regulating the course<BR>of the sun); a mythical Ṛṣi; N. of an old sage, con-<BR>versant with the Mantras, author of several hymns of<BR>the Ṛg-veda, and according to the Anukramaṇī a de-<BR>scendant of Marīci. (In the later mythology he is the<BR>husband of Aditi and twelve other daughters of Dakṣa,<BR>and father by them of gods, demons, men, fish, rep-<BR>tiles, and all animals; he is also regarded as one of the<BR>seven sages, and in some legends as father of Vivasvat<BR>and of Viṣṇu. He is supposed by some to be a<BR>personification of the race who resided in Caucasus,<BR>the Caspian, Kaṣmīr, &c.); the author of a Dharma-<BR>śāstra; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Kaśyapa;<BR>कश्यप is also a constellation; (आ), f., N. of the<BR>authoress of a verse in the White Yajur-veda.<BR>—कश्य-<BR>प-नन्दन, अस्, m. an epithet of Garuḍa, the bird<BR>of Viṣṇu; (‘son of Kaśyapa.’)<BR>—कश्यप-संहिता,<BR>f. and कश्यप-स्मृति, इस्, f., N. of two works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्
कष् कष्, cl. 1. P. A. कषति, -ते, चका-<BR>ष, कषिष्यति, अकषीत् and अकाषीत्,<BR>कषितुम्, to rub, scratch, scrape; to itch; to rub<BR>with a touchstone, test, try; to injure, hurt, destroy,<BR>kill; to leap: cl. 10. P. काषयति, -यितुम्, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbing, scraping, rubbing<BR>down; (अस्), m. rubbing; the touchstone; (आ), f. a<BR>whip; see कश.<BR>—कष-पाषाण, अस्, m. a touch-<BR>stone.<BR>—कषाघात (˚षा-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a cut, a<BR>stroke with a whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषण|कषणः
कषण, अस्, आ, अम्, unripe, immature; (अम्), n.<BR>rubbing, marking; touch or test of gold by the<BR>touchstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषन्मुख
कषन्-मुख, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाकु|कषाकुः
कषाकु, उस्, m. fire, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषि|कषिः
कषि, इस्, इस्, इ, injurious, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषित
कषित, अस्, आ, अम्, hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टि|कष्टिः
कष्टि, इस्, f. test, trial; pain, trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषापुत्र
कषापुत्र कषापुत्र, अस्, m. a Rakṣas;<BR>[cf. निकषात्मज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाय|कषायः
कषाय कषाय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. कष्?),<BR>astringent; fragrant; red, dark-red; brown, of a<BR>colour composed of red and yellow; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>an astringent flavour or taste; the red colour; a de-<BR>coction or infusion, that form of a decoction which<BR>has one part of a drug combined with four or<BR>(according to other authorities) with eight or sixteen<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">Page0215-b+ 75</a>]<BR>parts of water, the whole being then boiled down<BR>until only one quarter is left; a kind of ointment,<BR>gum, resin, extract, exudation from a tree; plaster-<BR>ing, anointing; colouring or perfuming the person;<BR>dirt, uncleanness, dulness, stupidity; decay, ruin; a<BR>mark of decay (of which, according to Buddhists,<BR>there are five, viz. आयुस्-कषाय, दृष्टि˚, क्लेश˚,<BR>सत्त्व˚, कल्प˚); attachment to worldly objects;<BR>(अस्), m. passion, emotion; the Kali-yuga; the tree<BR>Bignonia Indica; N. of a teacher; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>m. f. n. the tree Grislea Tomentosa; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a plant, a small sort of Hedysarum; [cf. काषाय<BR>and पञ्च-कषाय.]<BR>—कषाय-कृत्, त्, m. the<BR>tree Symplocos Racemosa, the bark of which is used<BR>in dyeing; also रक्त-लोध्र.<BR>—कषाय-चित्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, dyed or stained of a dull red colour.<BR>—कषा-<BR>य-ता, f. contraction.<BR>—कषाय-पाण, आस्, m. pl. a<BR>nickname of the Gāndhāras (‘drinking decoctions’).<BR>—कषाय-यावनाल, अस्, m. a sort of grain.<BR>—कषाय-वासिक, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR>—कषायान्वित (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, as-<BR>tringent, harsh, styptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायित
कषायित, अस्, आ, अम्, red, coloured; prepared<BR>for dyeing or colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायिन्
कषायिन्, ई, इणी, इ, yielding a resinous exudation,<BR>astringent, dyed of a red colour, worldly-minded;<BR>(ई), m., N. of several plants, Shorea Robusta; Arto-<BR>carpus Lacucha; the wild Datura tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायीकृत
कषायी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made red.<BR>—कषायी-<BR>कृत-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, with reddened eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायीभूत
कषायी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become red, reddened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषि|कषिः
कषि कषि, &c. See under कष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषिका
कषिका कषिका, f. (said to be fr. rt. कष्),<BR>a bird in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषीका
कषीका, f. a species of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषेरुका
कषेरुका कषेरुका, f. the back-bone, the<BR>spine; [cf. कशेरुका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्कष|कष्कषः
कष्कष कष्कष, अस्, m. (fr. कष्?), Ved.<BR>a kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्ट|कष्टं|कष्टः
कष्ट कष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, bad; ill, evil, wrong;<BR>painful; grievous, severe; difficult; most grievous,<BR>most painful; mischievous, noxious, injurious; boding<BR>evil; (अम्), n. evil, difficulty, a bad state of things,<BR>misery, wretchedness, pain, suffering, hardship, un-<BR>easiness; कष्टेन, with great difficulty or effort;<BR>(अम्), ind. an exclamation of grief or sorrow, Ah!<BR>Alas! [cf. Hib. ceas, ‘sorrow, grief, sadness.’]<BR>—कष्ट-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, giving pain or trouble.<BR>—कष्ट-कारक, अस्, आ, अम्, causing trouble or<BR>annoyance; (अस्), m. the world.<BR>—कष्ट-तपस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, one who performs many penitential<BR>exercises.<BR>—कष्ट-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more difficult,<BR>inconvenient or painful.<BR>—कष्ट-लभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>difficult to be obtained.<BR>—कष्ट-श्रित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>suffering pain or misfortune, undergoing hardships,<BR>performing penance.<BR>—कष्ट-साध्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>accomplishable with difficulty.<BR>—कष्ट-स्थान, अम्,<BR>n. a bad situation, a disagreeable place or site.<BR>—कष्टागत (˚ट-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, with difficulty<BR>or hardly arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टाय
कष्टाय, nom. A. कष्टायते, -यितुम्, to have<BR>wicked intentions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टि|कष्टिः
कष्टि कष्टि. See under कष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्फिल
