कह्लण|कह्लणः
कह्लण कह्लण. See under कल्हण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्लार|कह्लारं
कह्लार कह्लार, अम्, n. the white esculent<BR>water-lily, Nymphæa Lotus; sometimes spelt कल्-<BR>हार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्व|कह्वः
कह्व कह्व, अस्, m. a kind of crane, Ardea<BR>Nivea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

का
का 1. का = 2. कद् and 1. कु, at the begin-<BR>ning of some compounds (e. g. काक्ष), and perhaps<BR>a corruption of कद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

का
का 2. का, a form for rt. कन् in the Ved.<BR>participle कायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing, desiring,<BR>loving, and in one or two other forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांशि|कांशिः
कांशि कांशि, इस्, m. a cup; [cf. कांस्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्
कांस् कांस्, cl. 1. A. कांसते, -सितुम्, to<BR>shine, glitter; [cf. काश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस
कांस कांस, अस्, ई, अम्, born in Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांसीय|कांसीयं
कांसीय कांसीय, अम्, n. white copper; [cf.<BR>the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्य|कांस्यं|कांस्यः
कांस्य कांस्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कंस), con-<BR>sisting of white copper or brass; (अम्), n. white<BR>copper or brass, queen's metal, any amalgam of zinc<BR>and copper; a musical instrument, a sort of gong or<BR>plate of bell-metal struck with a stick or rod; a kind<BR>of measure; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a drinking vessel of brass,<BR>a goblet.<BR>—कांस्य-कार, अस्, ई, m. f. a brazier, a<BR>pewterer, a worker in white or bell-metal.<BR>—कांस्य-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, made of brass.<BR>—कांस्य-ताल, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-a" target="_blank">Page0216-a+ 80</a>]<BR>a cymbal.<BR>—कांस्य-नील, अस्, m. blue vitriol con-<BR>sidered as a collyrium; N. of a monkey; occasionally<BR>written कांश्य-नील.<BR>—कांस्य-भाजन, अम्, n.<BR>brass.<BR>—कांस्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting or made<BR>of brass.<BR>—कांस्य-मल, अम्, n. verdigris.<BR>—कांस्य-<BR>माक्षिक, अम्, n. a metallic substance, probably a<BR>kind of pyrites.<BR>—कांस्याभ (˚य-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>coloured like brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यक|कांस्यकं
कांस्यक, अम्, n. brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक|काकं|काकः
काक काक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कै, to<BR>caw), a crow, (metaphorically an expression of contempt,<BR>e. g. न त्वां काकम् मन्ये, I value thee less than a<BR>crow); an impudent, insolent fellow; a lame man, a<BR>cripple; washing the head, bathing by dipping the<BR>head only into the water as crows do; a sectarial<BR>mark (तिलक); a particular measure; the plant<BR>Ardisia Humilis (see काक-जम्बु); N. of a Dvīpa<BR>or division of the world; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(ई), f. a female crow, personified as a daughter of<BR>Kaśyapa by Tāmrā, and mother of the crows; a kind<BR>of medicinal plant (= काकोली); N. of one of the seven<BR>mothers of Śiśu; (आ), f., N. of several plants, Leea<BR>Hirta, also = काक-जङ्घा, काक-नासा; Solanum<BR>Indicum, = काक-माची; Ficus Oppositifolia, = काको-<BR>डुम्बर; another medicinal plant, = काकोली; an-<BR>other plant, commonly रक्तिका; (अम्), n. a multitude<BR>or assemblage of crows; a modus coeundi.<BR>—काक-<BR>कङ्गु, उस्, f. a kind of panic-grass, Panicum Milia-<BR>ceum.<BR>—काक-कला, f. the plant Leea Hirta; [cf.<BR>काक-जङ्घा.]<BR>—काक-कूर्म-मृगाखु (˚ग-<BR>आखु), अवस्, m. pl. the crow, tortoise, deer, and<BR>mouse.<BR>—काक-कूर्मादि (˚म-आदि), अयस्, m. pl.<BR>the crow, the tortoise, and the rest.<BR>—काक-घ्नी, f.<BR>a tree, said to be a large kind of Karañja, Galedupa<BR>Arborea, = महा-करञ्ज.<BR>—काक-चण्डीश्वर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—काक-चिञ्चा, f. the shrub which<BR>yields the red and black berry used in India as a<BR>jeweller's weight, Abrus Precatorius; also काक-चिञ्चि<BR>and काक-चिञ्ची.<BR>—काक-चिञ्चिक, N. of a kind of<BR>soft substance; another reading of the word is काचि-<BR>लिन्दि.<BR>—काक-च्छद, अस्, m. a wagtail; side-locks<BR>of hair.<BR>—काक-च्छदि, इस्, m. or, according to an-<BR>other reading, काक-च्छर्दि, इस्, m. a wagtail; a<BR>crow's vomit.<BR>—काक-जङ्घा, f. the plant Leea<BR>Hirta; also Abrus Precatorius.<BR>—काक-जम्बु, उस्,<BR>f. the plant Ardisia Humilis, commonly Bhumijamb;<BR>(ऊस्), f. another species of Jambu.<BR>—काक-जात, अस्,<BR>m. the Indian cuckoo.<BR>—काक-ता, f. the state of a<BR>crow.<BR>—काक-तालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, unexpected, as in<BR>the fable of the fruit of the palm falling unexpectedly<BR>at the moment of the alighting of a crow and killing<BR>it; accidental; (अम्), ind. unexpectedly, suddenly;<BR>(अम्), n. the fable of the crow and the fruit of the<BR>palm.<BR>—काकतालीय-वत्, ind. suddenly, (said of any<BR>unexpected casualty.)<BR>—काक-तालुकिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>having the palate of a crow, contemptible, vile.<BR>—काक-तिक्ता, f. the plant Abrus Precatorius.<BR>—का-<BR>क-तिन्दुक, अस्, m. a kind of ebony, Diospyros<BR>Tomentosa.<BR>—काक-तुण्ड, अस्, m. the dark species<BR>of Agallochum; (ई), f., N. of a tree, in Hindī called<BR>Kauāḍoḍi; a sort of brass.<BR>—काक-तुण्डिका, f. the<BR>plant Abrus Precatorius.<BR>—काक-तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>like a crow, crow-like, crafty.<BR>—काक-दन्त, अस्, m.<BR>the tooth of a crow, i. e. anything impossible or not<BR>existing.<BR>—काक-दन्तकि, a patronymic from Kāka-<BR>dantaka; (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe; का-<BR>कदन्तकीय, अस्, m. a prince of the Kākadantakis.<BR>—काक-ध्वज, अस्, m. submarine fire, a personage<BR>in Hindū mythology; [cf. और्व.]<BR>—काक-नामन्,<BR>आ, m. the plant Agati Grandiflora.<BR>—काक-नाशा, f.<BR>the same plant.<BR>—काक-नास, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>commonly called Vikaṇṭaka; (आ), f. the plant Leea<BR>Hirta.<BR>—काक-नासिका, f. the plant Leea Hirta; N.<BR>of another plant, also called Rakta-trivṛt.<BR>—काक-<BR>निद्रा, f. ‘a crow's sleep,’ a light slumber, one which<BR>is easily broken.<BR>—काक-नीला, f. = काक-जम्बू.<BR>—काक-पक्ष, अस्, m. side-locks of hair on the<BR>temples of boys and young men; three or five locks<BR>on each side left when the head is first shaved and<BR>allowed to remain there, especially in persons of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-b" target="_blank">Page0216-b+ 81</a>]<BR>military caste; (also at the end of compounds काक-<BR>पक्षक.)<BR>—काक-पद, अम्, n. the foot of a<BR>crow; an incision in the skin similar to a crow's<BR>foot; the sign V in MSS. marking that something<BR>has been left out; (अस्), m. a modus coeundi.<BR>—का-<BR>क-पर्णी, f. the plant Phaseolus Trilobus.<BR>—काक-<BR>पीलु, उस्, m., N. of several plants, = काक-तिन्दुक,<BR>काक-तुण्डी, and also a variety of Abrus Precatorius.<BR>—काक-पीलुक, अस्, m. = काक-तिन्दुक.<BR>—काक-<BR>पुच्छ, अस्, m. the Kokila or Indian cuckoo, (perhaps<BR>a Prākṛt form of the next.)<BR>—काक-पुष्ट, अस्, m.<BR>the Indian cuckoo, (this bird, like the English cuckoo,<BR>being said to leave its eggs in the nests of other birds,<BR>as in that of the crow &c.)<BR>—काक-पुष्प, अम्, n.<BR>= गन्ध-पर्ण (?).<BR>—काक-पेय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>what may be drunk by a crow, epithet of a shallow<BR>river.<BR>—काक-फल, अस्, m. the tree Azadirachta<BR>Indica; (आ), f. = काक-जम्बू.<BR>—काक-बन्ध्या, f.<BR>a woman that bears only one child.<BR>—काक-भाण्डी,<BR>f. a species of Karañja.<BR>—काक-भीरु, उस्, m. an<BR>owl (‘afraid of crows’).<BR>—काक-मद्गु, उस्, m. a<BR>water-hen, a gallinule; resembling a crow in colour.<BR>—काक-मर्द, अस्, m. a kind of gourd, Cucumis<BR>Colocynthis (महा-काल).<BR>—काक-मर्दक, अस्,<BR>m. the same.<BR>—काक-माचिका or काक-माची, f. the<BR>plant Solanum Indicum, an esculent vegetable, com-<BR>monly Gūrkamai.<BR>—काक-माता, f. the same plant.<BR>—काक-मुख, आस्, m. pl. ‘crow-faced,’ N. of a<BR>mythical people.<BR>—काक-मुद्गा, f. a plant, com-<BR>monly Mugani; according to some a wild kind of<BR>bean, Phaseolus Trilobus.<BR>—काक-मृग, औ, m. du.<BR>the crow and the deer.<BR>—काक-यव, अस्, m. barren<BR>corn, the ear of which has no grains.<BR>—काक-रुद्र-<BR>संवाद, अस्, m. title of a work on omens.<BR>—काक-<BR>रुहा, f. a parasite plant, Epidendrum Tesseloides &c.<BR>—काक-वत्, ind. like a crow, in the manner of a<BR>crow.<BR>—काक-वर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—का-<BR>क-वर्णिन्, ई, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—काक-वर्तक,<BR>औ, m. du. the crow and the quail.<BR>—काक-वल्लभा,<BR>f. = काक-जम्बू.<BR>—काक-वल्लरी, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= स्वर्ण-वल्ली.<BR>—काक-व्याघ्र-गोमायु, अवस्,<BR>m. pl. the crow, the tiger, and the jackal.<BR>—काक-<BR>शब्द, अस्, m. the cawing of a crow.<BR>—काक-शिम्बी,<BR>f., N. of a plant, = काक-तुण्डी.<BR>—काक-शीर्ष, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Agati Grandiflora, commonly called Va-<BR>kapuṣpa.<BR>—काक-शीर्षि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—काक-स्त्री, f. the same plant.<BR>—काक-स्फूर्ज,<BR>अस्, m. the plant Diospyros Tomentosa.<BR>—काक-<BR>स्वर, अस्, m. a shrill tone.<BR>—काकाक्षि (˚क-अक्˚),<BR>n. the eye of a crow; काकाक्षि-न्यायेन, ind. in<BR>the manner of a crow's eye, (crows are supposed to<BR>have but one eye or visual orb, which, as occasion<BR>requires, moves from the cavity on one side into that<BR>on the other); a term for a word which follows two<BR>rules.<BR>—काकाङ्गा or ई (˚क-अङ्˚), f. the plant Leea<BR>Hirta, = काक-नासा.<BR>—काकाञ्ची, f. the plant Leea<BR>Hirta; an esculent vegetable, Solanum Indicum.<BR>—का-<BR>काण्ड (˚क-अण्˚), अस्, m., N. of two plants, Mahā-<BR>nimba and Kākatindu (?), a kind of bean; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of spider; N. of a plant; see कोलशिम्बी.<BR>—काकाण्डक, अस्, m., N. of a crow or N. of a<BR>plant; a kind of spider.<BR>—काकाण्डोला, f., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—काकादनी (˚क-अद्˚), f., N. of several<BR>plants, Abrus Precatorius; a white variety of this<BR>plant, commonly Śveta-guñjā.<BR>—काकारि (˚क-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. an owl.<BR>—काकेक्षु (˚क-इक्˚), उस्, m. a kind<BR>of reed, Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—काकेन्दु (˚क-<BR>इन्˚), उस्, m. a kind of ebony, Diospyros Melanoxylon,<BR>= काक-तिन्दुक.<BR>—काकेष्ट (˚क-इष्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>tree Melia Azadirachta.<BR>—काकोडुम्बर (˚क-उड्˚),<BR>अस्, m. or काकोडुम्बरिका, f. or काकोदुम्बरिका,<BR>f. opposite-leaved fig tree, Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR>—का-<BR>कोदर (˚क-उद्˚), अस्, m. a serpent.<BR>—काकोलूक<BR>(˚क-उल्˚), अम्, n. crow and owl.<BR>—काकोलूकिका, f.<BR>the natural enmity of the owl and crow.<BR>—काकोलू-<BR>कीय, अम्, n. = the preceding; N. of the third book<BR>of the Pañcatantra.<BR>—काकोष्ठक and काकौष्-<BR>ठक (˚क-ओष्ठ), अस्, इका, अम्, shaped like the<BR>beak of a crow; epithet of a bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकण|काकणं
काकण, अम्, n. a leprosy with black and red<BR>spots, considered incurable; (called so from its<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">Page0216-c+ 71</a>]<BR>similarity to the black and red seed of the plant<BR>Abrus Precatorius.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणन्तिका
काकणन्तिका, f. the plant Abrus Precatorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणि|काकणिः
काकणि, a sort of small coin; [cf. काकिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनन्ती
काकनन्ती, f. the plant Abrus Precatorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकायु|काकायुः
काकायु, उस्, m., N. of a plant, = काकवल्लरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाल|काकालः
काकाल, अस्, m. a raven; [cf. काक and काकोल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकीय
काकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतीयरुद्र
काकतीयरुद्र काकतीय-रुद्र, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a king of Nāgapura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकन्दि
काकन्दि काकन्दि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकन्दी
काकन्दी, f., N. of a country; Emblic Myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकन्दीय
काकन्दीय, अस्, m. a prince of the above tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकम्बीर
काकम्बीर काकम्बीर, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>tree; (according to Sāy. literally ‘a crow-bearer.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरुक काकरुक or काकरूक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>timid, afraid, a coward; naked; poor, indigent;<BR>(अस्), m. a hen-pecked husband; an owl; fraud,<BR>deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकल|काकलं|काकलः
काकल काकल, अम्, n. a jewel worn upon<BR>the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलक|काकलकः
काकलक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the top of the<BR>windpipe; the thyroid cartilage; (अस्), m. an orna-<BR>ment of the neck; a species of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलि|काकलिः
काकलि काकलि, इस्, f. a soft sweet sound<BR>[cf. कल]; N. of an Apsaras; (ई), f. a low and<BR>sweet tone; a musical instrument with a low tone<BR>played to ascertain whether a person is asleep or not.<BR>—काकली-द्राक्षा, f. a kind of grape without a<BR>stone or with a very small one.<BR>—काकली-रव, अस्,<BR>m. the Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीक|काकलीकः
काकलीक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?) a low sweet tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकार
काकार काकार, अस्, ई, अम्, scattering water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणी
काकिणी काकिणी, f. a small coin, a small<BR>sum of money equal to twenty Kapardas or cowries,<BR>or to a quarter of a Paṇa; the seed of Abrus Preca-<BR>torius used as a weight; the shell Cypræa Moneta or<BR>cowrie used as a coin; a cubit, the fourth part of a<BR>Daṇḍa or short pole; a Daṇḍa; a part of a measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणिका
काकिणिका, f. = the preceding; an atom, a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणीक
काकिणीक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the value of a Kākiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिनी
काकिनी, f. the fourth part of a Paṇa; a quarter of<BR>a Māna; the shell Cypræa Moneta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिल|काकिलः
काकिल काकिल, अस्, m. a jewel worn upon<BR>the neck; [cf. काकल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकु|काकुः
काकु काकु, उस्, f. change of the voice in<BR>fear, anger, grief, &c. [cf. सेवा-काकु]; muttering,<BR>murmuring; the tongue; stress, emphasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुत्स्थ|काकुत्स्थः
काकुत्स्थ काकुत्स्थ, अस्, m. a descendant of<BR>Kakutstha; an epithet of Anenas, Aja, Daśaratha,<BR>Rāma, Lakṣmaṇa; N. of a sovereign, also Purañjaya;<BR>(औ), du. Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुद्
काकुद् काकुद्, त्, f., Ved. and काकुद, अम्,<BR>n. the hollow of the mouth, the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुद्र
काकुद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with a palate (?),<BR>a palate (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुभ्
काकुभ्, a various reading for काकुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुभ
काकुभ काकुभ, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of<BR>Kakubh verses; a patronymic from Kakubh.<BR>—का-<BR>कुभ-बार्हत, अस्, m. (scil. प्रगाथ) a Pragātha<BR>beginning with a Kakubh and ending with a Bṛhatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोचिक|काकोचिकः
काकोचिक काकोचिक, अस्, m. or काकोची, f. or<BR>काकोचिन्, ई, m. the fish Cyprinus Cachius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोल|काकोलं|काकोलः
काकोल काकोल, अस्, m. a raven [cf. काक<BR>and काकाल]; a boar; a snake; a potter; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a poisonous substance of a black colour or the<BR>colour of a raven, whence its name; possibly the<BR>berry of the Cocculus Indicus; (अम्), n. a division<BR>of the infernal regions or hell; (अस्, ई), m. f. a<BR>vegetable substance used in medicine, described as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">Page0217-a+ 71</a>]<BR>sweet and cooling, allaying fever, removing phlegm,<BR>&c.; it is said to be a root brought from Nepal or<BR>Morung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्ष|काक्षः
काक्ष काक्ष (का-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, frowning,<BR>looking scornfully or in displeasure; (अस्), m. a glance,<BR>a wink or leer; (अम्), n. a frown, a look of dis-<BR>pleasure; [cf. कटाक्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षतव
काक्षतव काक्षतव, अम्, n. the fruit of<BR>Kakṣatu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षसेनि
काक्षसेनि काक्षसेनि, इस्, m. (a patronymic<BR>fr. कक्ष-सेन), an epithet of Abhipratārin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षि
काक्षि काक्षि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षी
काक्षी काक्षी, f. a perfume, a fragrant kind<BR>of earth; the plant Cytisus Cajan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीव|काक्षीवः
काक्षीव काक्षीव, अस्, m. the plant Hyper-<BR>anthera Moringa; N. of a son of Gautama and of<BR>Auśīnarī, (irregular patronymic fr. कक्षीवत् or<BR>काक्षीवत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवक|काक्षीवकः
काक्षीवक, अस्, m. the plant Hyperanthera Mo-<BR>ringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवत्|काक्षीवन्त्
काक्षीवत् काक्षीवत्, आन्, m. = कक्षीवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीवत
काक्षीवत, अस्, ई, अम्, composed by or relating<BR>to Kakṣīvat; (a patronymic fr. कक्षीवत्), epi-<BR>thet of Śambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काग|कागः
काग काग, अस्, m. a crow; (in the Prākṛt<BR>dialects, a raven; cf. काक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काग्नि
काग्नि काग्नि (का-अग्˚), इस्, m. a little fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्कायन
काङ्कायन काङ्कायन, अस्, m. (a patronymic<BR>fr. कङ्क), N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्ष्|कांक्ष्
काङ्क्ष् काङ्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. काङ्क्षति, च-<BR>काङ्क्ष, ep. also A. काङ्क्षते, &c.,<BR>काङ्क्षितुम्, to wish, desire; to strive to obtain;<BR>to long for, hope for (with acc.), expect; to wait; to<BR>look for anything (with dat.): Caus. काङ्क्षयति,<BR>अचकाङ्क्षत्: Desid. चिकाङ्क्षिषति: Intens. चा-<BR>काङ्क्ष्यते and चाकांष्टि; [cf. Hib. cachta,<BR>‘hunger;’ Goth. huhru-s, ‘hunger;’ hungrja, ‘to<BR>be hungry;’ Germ. Hunger.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षत्
काङ्क्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or काङ्क्षमाण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wishing, desiring, hoping, expecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षा|कांक्षा
काङ्क्षा, f. wish, inclination, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षित|कांक्षित
काङ्क्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired; expected,<BR>longed for; (अम्), n. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षिन्|कांक्षिन्
काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, desiring, expecting, longing for<BR>(with acc. or at the end of a compound).<BR>—काङ्क्षि-<BR>ता, f. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षोरु|कांक्षोरुः|काङ्क्षोरुः
काङ्क्षोरु काङ्क्षोरु, उस्, m. a heron; also<BR>written काङ्क्षारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्गा
काङ्गा काङ्गा, f., N. of a plant, Orris root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्गुक
काङ्गुक काङ्गुक, अम्, n. a kind of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच|काचं|काचः
काच काच, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कच्), glass, crystal<BR>considered as a natural production and used as a jewel<BR>or ornament; alkaline ashes, any salt of potash or<BR>soda in a glassy or crystalline state; a class of diseases<BR>of the eye, especially an affection of the optic nerve<BR>or gutta serena; a loop, a swinging shelf, a string so<BR>fastened to the yoke as to hold or support burdens<BR>&c.; the string of the scale of a balance; (अम्), n.<BR>alkaline salt, black salt; wax.<BR>—काच-कूपी, f. a glass<BR>bottle.<BR>—काच-घटी, f. a glass ewer.<BR>—काच-भा-<BR>जन, अम्, n. a vessel of glass or crystal, a cup, a<BR>goblet.<BR>—काच-मणि, इस्, m. ‘a glass jewel,’ crystal,<BR>quartz.<BR>—काच-मल, अम्, n. black salt or soda.<BR>—काच-लवण, अम्, n. black salt, a medicinal salt,<BR>prepared by calcining fossil salt and the fruit of the<BR>Emblic Myrobalan together; it consists chiefly of<BR>muriate of soda, with a small quantity of iron, lime,<BR>and sulphur, and is a tonic aperient.<BR>—काच-वक-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a glass retort.<BR>—काच-सम्भव,<BR>अम्, n. black salt.<BR>—काच-सौवर्चल, अम्, n. black<BR>salt.<BR>—काच-स्थाली, f. the trumpet flower, Bignonia<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">Page0217-b+ 73</a>]<BR>Suaveolens.<BR>—काचाक्ष (˚च-अक्˚), अस्, m. glass-eye,<BR>N. of an aquatic bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचक|काचकः
काचक, अस्, m. glass, a stone; alkaline ashes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचन|काचनं
काचन or काचनक, अम्, n. an enclosure, a<BR>string or tape which ties a parcel or bundle of papers<BR>or the leaves of a manuscript &c.; [cf. कचेल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनकिन्
काचनकिन्, ई, m. a writing, a manuscript.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित|काचितं
काचित, अस्, आ, अम्, suspended by a swing or in a loop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिघ|काचिघः
काचिघ काचिघ, अस्, m. a mouse, a rat;<BR>gold; a vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिञ्चिक
काचिञ्चिक काचिञ्चिक (a various reading for<BR>काकचिञ्चिक), a kind of soft substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित्कर
काचित्कर काचित्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. doing<BR>various things, serving various purposes; (का-चित्,<BR>Ved. for कानि-चित्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिम|काचिमः
काचिम काचिम, अस्, m. a tree considered<BR>as sacred, one growing near a temple, and being on<BR>that account an object of religious veneration or<BR>worship &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिलिन्दि
काचिलिन्दि काचिलिन्दि and काचिलिन्दिक (va-<BR>rious readings for काकचिञ्चिक), a kind of soft substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच्छ
काच्छ काच्छ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कच्छ), being<BR>on the bank of a river (not applicable to a man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच्छिक
काच्छिक, अस्, ई, अम्, being on the bank of a river<BR>(as a man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच्छप
काच्छप काच्छप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कच्छप),<BR>relating or belonging to a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच्छिम
काच्छिम काच्छिम, अस्, आ, अम्, clear (as<BR>water); [cf. अच्छ, स्वच्छ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच्छी
काच्छी काच्छी, f. a kind of fragrant earth;<BR>[cf. काक्षी from which काच्छी is derived.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काजल|काजलं
काजल का-जल, अम्, n. a little water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्च्|कांच्
काञ्च् काञ्च्, cl. 1. A. काञ्चते, -चितुम्, to<BR>shine; to bind; [cf. कच् and कञ्च्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चन|कांचन|काञ्चनं|काञ्चनः
काञ्चन, अम्, n. gold; property; wealth; the<BR>filament of the lotus; (अस्, ई, अम्), golden, made or<BR>consisting of gold; (अस्), m. several plants, Mesua<BR>Ferrea; Michelia Champaca; Ficus Glomerata; Bau-<BR>hinia Variegata; Datura Fastuosa; another plant, =<BR>पुन्नाग; N. of the fifth Buddha; N. of a son of<BR>Nārāyaṇa, author of the play Dhanañjaya-vijaya; N.<BR>of a prince [cf. काञ्चन-प्रभ]; (ई), f. turmeric;<BR>a kind of Asclepias; a yellow pigment.<BR>—काञ्चन-<BR>कदली, f. a variety of the plant Musa Sapientum.<BR>—काञ्चन-कन्दर, अस्, m. a gold mine.<BR>—काञ्च-<BR>न-कारिणी, f. the plant Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—काञ्-<BR>चन-क्षीरी, f. a kind of Asclepias, = क्षीरिणी-लता.<BR>—काञ्चन-गिरि, इस्, m. the golden mountain, an<BR>epithet of the mount Sumeru.<BR>—काञ्चन-गैरिक,<BR>अम्, n. a species of ochre.<BR>—काञ्चन-चय, अस्, m.<BR>a heap of gold.<BR>—काञ्चन-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—काञ्चन-पुष्पक, अम्, n. the plant Ta-<BR>bernæmontana Coronaria.<BR>—काञ्चन-पुष्पी, f.<BR>the plant Premna Spinosa.<BR>—काञ्चन-प्रभ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince, a son of Bhīma and father of<BR>Suhotra.<BR>—काञ्चन-भू, ऊस्, f. gold-dust; a golden<BR>or yellow soil.<BR>—काञ्चन-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, golden.<BR>—काञ्चन-माला, f., N. of the wife of Kunāla, the<BR>son of Aśoka; N. of another woman.<BR>—काञ्चन-<BR>वप्र, अस्, m. a hill or mound of gold.<BR>—काञ्चन-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—काञ्चन-सन्धि,<BR>इस्, m. a treaty of friendship between two parties on<BR>equal terms.<BR>—काञ्चन-सन्निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like<BR>gold.<BR>—काञ्चनाक्ष (˚न-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Dānava; (ई), f., N. of the river Sarasvatī.<BR>—काञ्-<BR>चनाङ्ग (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, golden-bodied.<BR>—काञ्चनाभिधान-सन्धि (˚न-अभ्˚), इस्, m.<BR>‘golden alliance,’ (lit. golden-named.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनक|काञ्चनकं|कांचनकः|काञ्चनकः
काञ्चनक, अस्, m. the tree Bauhinia Variegata,<BR>mountain ebony; the fruit of rice or grain; (अम्),<BR>n. a yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनार|कांचनार|कांचनारः|काञ्चनारः
काञ्चनार or काञ्चनाल or काञ्चनारक, अस्,<BR>m. mountain ebony, Bauhinia Variegata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनीय|कांचनीय
काञ्चनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, golden; (आ), f. a yellow<BR>pigment, commonly Go-rocanā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चि|कांचि|कांचिः|काञ्चिः
काञ्चि काञ्चि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>[cf. काञ्ची.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चिक|कांचिकं|काञ्चिकं
काञ्चिक काञ्चिक, अम्, n. sour gruel; [cf.<BR>काञ्जिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्ची|कांची
काञ्ची काञ्ची or काञ्चि, इस्, f. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कन्), a girdle, especially a woman's zone or girdle<BR>furnished with small bells and other ornaments; the<BR>plant Abrus Precatorius; N. of an ancient city situated<BR>in the peninsula and one of the seven sacred cities of<BR>the Hindūs.<BR>—काञ्चि-पुरी, f., N. of a town.<BR>—काञ्-<BR>ची-क्षेत्र, N. of a region.<BR>—काञ्ची-नगर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town.<BR>—काञ्ची-पद, अम्, n. the hips<BR>and loins; mons veneris, the pubic region.<BR>—काञ्ची-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—काञ्ची-प्रस्थ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्जिक|कांजिक|कांजिकं|काञ्जिकं
काञ्जिक काञ्जिक, अम्, n. sour gruel, the<BR>water of boiled rice in a state of spontaneous fer-<BR>mentation; (आ), f. the same; N. of two plants, =<BR>जीवन्ती-लता and पलाशी-लता.<BR>—काञ्जिक-वटक,<BR>अस्, m. a dish consisting of sour gruel, meal, and<BR>several condiments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्जी|कांजी
काञ्जी, f. sour gruel, = काञ्जिक; N. of a plant,<BR>= महाद्रोणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्जीक|कांजीकं
काञ्जीक, अम्, n. sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काट|काटः
काट काट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (a Prākṛt form fr.<BR>कर्त), Ved. deepness, a hole; (Sāy.) a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काट्य
काट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काटवेम
काटवेम काटवेम, अस्, m., N. of a com-<BR>mentator on Kālidāsa's Śakuntalā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काटुक|काटुकं
काटुक काटुक, अम्, n. (fr. कटुक), acidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठ|काठः
काठ काठ, अस्, ई, अम्, composed by Kaṭha;<BR>(अस्), m. a rock, a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठक
काठक, अस्, m., N. of a work belonging to the<BR>Brāhmaṇa literature, and derived from the Kaṭha<BR>branch of the Vedas; (अस्, ई, अम्), according to the<BR>Kaṭha portion of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठशाठिन्
काठशाठिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils of Kaṭha-<BR>śāṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन|काठिनं|काठिनः
काठिन काठिन, अम्, n. (fr. कठिन), hard-<BR>ness, sternness; (अस्), m. the date fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन्य|काठिन्यं
काठिन्य, अम्, n. hardness, rigidity, stiffness,<BR>sternness, severity; firmness of character; difficulty,<BR>obscurity (of style).<BR>—काठिन्य-फल, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Feronia Elephantum, = कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण|काणः
काण काण, अस्, आ, अम्, one-eyed, monoculous<BR>(अक्ष्णा काणः, blind of one eye); perforated, as a<BR>cowrie broken or perforated by insects; (अस्), m. a<BR>crow; [cf. एकाक्ष and काणूक.]<BR>—काण-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. one-eyedness.<BR>—काण-भूति, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>Yakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेय|काणेयः
काणेय, अस्, m. the son of a one-eyed woman;<BR>one-eyed.<BR>—काणेय-विध, अम्, n. a country inha-<BR>bited by Kaṇeyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेर|काणेरः
काणेर, अस्, m. son of a one-eyed woman; one-<BR>eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणाद
काणाद काणाद, अस्, ई, अम्, composed by or<BR>relating to Kaṇāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणूक|काणूकः
काणूक काणूक or कानूक, अस् (?), m. (said<BR>to be fr. rt. कण्), a crow; the bird which makes a<BR>hanging nest on the tāl tree; a cock; a species of<BR>goose; [cf. काण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेलीमातृ
काणेलीमातृ काणेलीमातृ, a name of re-<BR>proach, occurring generally in the voc. case; (according<BR>to native commentators) one whose mother was an<BR>unmarried woman, a bastard; (connected with the<BR>word काणेर?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्टकमर्दनिक|काण्टकमर्द्दनिक
काण्टकमर्दनिक काण्टकमर्दनिक, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. कण्टक-मर्दन), resulting from the treading<BR>down or crushing of thorns or enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्टकार
काण्टकार काण्टकार, अस्, ई, अम्, made of the<BR>wood of Kaṇṭakāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्ठेविद्धि
काण्ठेविद्धि काण्ठेविद्धि, इस्, ई or या, m. f. a<BR>patronymic fr. कण्ठे-विद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्ड|कांड|कांडं|काण्डं|कांडः|काण्डः
काण्ड काण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>2. कम्), a section, part; a single joint of the stalk<BR>or stem of a plant, i. e. the portion from one knot<BR>to another (e. g. इषुस् त्रि-काण्डा, an arrow made of<BR>a cane with three knots; but by Pāṇ. IV. 1, 21, the<BR>fem. should be त्रि-काण्डी); any part, portion or divi-<BR>sion of a work or action; any distinct portion or<BR>division of a sacrificial rite (as that belonging to the<BR>gods or to the manes); the section or chapter of a<BR>book, a separate department or subject (e. g. कर्म-<BR>काण्ड, the department of the Veda treating of sacri-<BR>ficial rites); a stalk or stem, a branch, a switch; the<BR>part of the trunk of a tree whence the branches pro-<BR>ceed; a cluster, a bundle; a multitude, heap, quantity<BR>(at end of comp.); an arrow; a long bone, a bone<BR>of the arms or legs (e. g. काण्ड-भग्न, fracture of<BR>a bone); a cane, a reed (Saccharum Sara); a particular<BR>measure; water; opportunity, occasion; a private<BR>place, privacy, a secret place; praise, flattery; a<BR>horse. (At the end of a compound काण्ड may<BR>sometimes imply depreciation or deficiency, = vile,<BR>low, bad, sinful, wicked, &c.)<BR>—काण्ड-कटुक, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Momordica Charantia, = कारवेल्ल.<BR>—काण्ड-काण्डक, अस्, m. a species of grass.<BR>—काण्ड-कार, अम्, n. the Areca or betel-nut tree,<BR>commonly Guvāka; the betel-nut.<BR>—काण्ड-कीलक,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Symplocos Racemosa.<BR>—काण्ड-<BR>कुष्कु, उस्, m. (?), N. of a man.<BR>—काण्ड-गुण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. a species of grass.<BR>—काण्ड-गोचर, अस्, m.<BR>an iron arrow.<BR>—काण्ड-तिक्त and काण्ड-तिक्तक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of gentian, Gentiana Cherayta.<BR>—काण्ड-<BR>धार, अस्, m., N. of a country; (अस्, अम्), coming<BR>from or relating to this country.<BR>—काण्ड-नील, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Symplocos Racemosa.<BR>—काण्ड-पट,<BR>अस्, ई, m. f. or काण्ड-पटक, अस्, m. (?) an outer<BR>tent, a screen surrounding a tent, a curtain.<BR>—काण्ड-<BR>पतित, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-king.<BR>—काण्ड-पात,<BR>अस्, m. an arrow's fall or flight.<BR>—काण्ड-पुङ्खा, f.,<BR>N. of a plant, = शर-पुङ्खा.<BR>—काण्ड-पुष्प,<BR>अम्, n. the flower Artemisia Indica, commonly Donā.<BR>—काण्ड-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘arrow-backed,’ one<BR>who carries arrows on his back, one of the military<BR>profession, a soldier; (अस्), m. the husband of a<BR>Vaiśyā female; an adopted son, any other than one's<BR>own son; (अम्), n. the bow of Karṇa; the bow of<BR>Kāma; [cf. काण्ड-स्पृष्ट.]<BR>—काण्ड-भग्न, अम्,<BR>n. a fracture or dislocation of the bones or limbs, com-<BR>plete fracture of a limb.<BR>—काण्ड-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of pieces of cane; (ई), f. = काण्ड-वीणा,<BR>q. v.<BR>—काण्ड-रुहा, f. a medicinal plant, = कटुकी.<BR>—काण्डर्षि (˚ड-ऋषि), इस्, m. a Ṛṣi or divine<BR>saint of a peculiar class, as Jaimini and others, who teach<BR>a peculiar Kāṇḍa or section of the Vedas.<BR>—काण्ड-<BR>लाव, अस्, आ, अम्, cutting a cane or branch, intending<BR>to do so.<BR>—काण्ड-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, armed with an<BR>arrow, an archer.<BR>—काण्ड-वीणा, f. a musical instru-<BR>ment composed of joints of reed, a reed-pipe (?)<BR>played by the Cāṇḍālas; [cf. कण्डोल-वीणा.]<BR>—काण्ड-सन्धि, इस्, m. a knot, a joint in the<BR>stem of a tree or of a reed.<BR>—काण्ड-स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, living by the military profession, living by arms,<BR>a soldier; (अस्), m. a Brāhman who lives by arms; [cf.<BR>काण्ड-पृष्ठ.]<BR>—काण्ड-हीन, अम्, n. a fragrant<BR>grass, Cyperus Pertenuis.<BR>—काण्डानुक्रम (˚ड-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. or काण्डानुक्रमणिका or काण्डा-<BR>नुक्रमणी, f. an index of the Kāṇḍas of the<BR>Taittirīya-Saṃhitā.<BR>—काण्डेक्षु (˚ड-इक्˚), उस्, m.<BR>the plant Asteracantha Longifolia and the plant<BR>Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>—काण्डे-रुहा, f., N. of a<BR>plant, = काण्ड-रुहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डनी
काण्डनी, f., N. of a plant, = सूक्ष्म-पर्णी and<BR>राम-दूती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डाल|कांडालः|काण्डालः
काण्डाल or काण्डोल, अस्, m. a reed-basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डिका|कांडिका
काण्डिका, f. a kind of corn (see लङ्का); a kind<BR>of gourd, Cucumis Utilissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डिन्
काण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. reed-shaped, hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डीर|कांडीर|कांडीरः|काण्डीरः
काण्डीर, अस्, आ, अम्, armed with arrows, an<BR>archer; (अस्), m. the plant Achyranthes Aspera and<BR>the plant Momordica Charantia; (आ and ई), f. the<BR>plant Rubia Munjista.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डेरी
काण्डेरी, f. the plant Tiaridium Indicum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डणी
काण्डणी काण्डणी, (?) f. a plant, commonly<BR>Rāmadūtī; [cf. सूक्ष्म-पर्णी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डोल|कांडोल|कांडोलः|काण्डोलः
काण्डोल काण्डोल, see above; [cf. कण्डोल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्व|काण्वः
काण्व काण्व, अस्, ई, अम् (a patronymic fr.<BR>कण्व), a descendant of Kaṇva; a follower of Kaṇva.<BR>—काण्व-शाखिन्, ई, m. a follower of the Kāṇva<BR>branch of the Veda.<BR>—काण्वी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्वक
काण्वक, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्वायन
काण्वायन, अस्, आ, अम्, a patronymic fr. काण्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातन्त्र|कातंत्रं
कातन्त्र का-तन्त्र, अम्, n. title of a grammar<BR>(= कलाप, q. v.); there are several appendices to<BR>and commentaries on this grammar, called कातन्त्र-<BR>गणधातु, ˚चतुष्टयप्रदीप, ˚चन्द्रिका, ˚धा-<BR>तुघोषा, &c.<BR>—कातन्त्र-पञ्जिका, f. title of a<BR>commentary by Trilocana-dāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर|कातरः
कातर कातर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कतर?),<BR>cowardly, discouraged, timid, depressed, perplexed,<BR>shrinking, afraid; confused, agitated, disordered; (अस्),<BR>m. a large kind of fish, Cyprinus Catla, = कातल.<BR>—कातर-ता, f. or कातर-त्व, अम्, n. cowardice,<BR>timidity, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातरायण
कातरायण, अस्, m. a patronymic fr. कातर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर्य|कातर्यं
कातर्य, अम्, n. timidity, fear, dejection, depres-<BR>sion of spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातल|कातलः
कातल कातल, अस्, m. a large kind of fish,<BR>Cyprinus Catla; N. of a man; [cf. कातर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातलायन
कातलायन, अस्, m. a patronymic fr. कातल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काति
काति काति, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. 2. का = कन्), wishing,<BR>desiring (in the compounds ऋण-काति and काम-<BR>काति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातीय|कातीयः
कातीय कातीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कात्य below),<BR>composed by Kātya (e. g. in कातीय-गृह्यसूत्र,<BR>कातीय-कल्प-सूत्र, and कातीय-सूत्र); a N. of<BR>Kātyāyana (?); a pupil of the same; also कात्या-<BR>यनीय (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्य|कात्यः
कात्य, अस्, m. a patronymic fr. कत; also = का-<BR>त्यायन (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायन|कात्यायनः
कात्यायन, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. कति or<BR>कात्य), N. of the author of several treatises on<BR>ritual, grammar, &c.; he is generally identified with<BR>Vararuci, the author of the Prākṛta-prakāśa. He is<BR>also the author of the Vārttikas or supplementary<BR>rules to Pāṇini, of the Yajur-veda Prātiśākhya, and<BR>the Śrauta-sūtras; (ई), f., N. of one of the two wives<BR>of Yājñavalkya; an epithet of Durgā; a middle-aged<BR>widow dressed in red clothes.<BR>—कात्यायन-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n. the Śrauta-sūtras of Kātyāyana.<BR>—कात्यायन-<BR>सूत्र-पद्धति, a commentary on the last by Yājñi-<BR>ka-deva.<BR>—कात्यायनसूत्र-भाष्य, अम्, n. a com-<BR>mentary on the same by Karka.<BR>—कात्यायनी-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR>—कात्यायनी-माहात्म्य,<BR>अम्, n. a part of the Skanda-purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीय|कात्यायनीयः
कात्यायनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, composed by Kātyāyana;<BR>e. g. कात्यायनीय-शास्त्रम्, ‘the law-book composed<BR>by him;’ (अस्), m. a pupil of Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातु|कातुः
कातु कातु, उस्, m. a cave; a well (?); [cf.<BR>काट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातृण|कातृणं
कातृण का-तृण, अम्, n. a species of grass,<BR>Rohisha-tṛṇa; [cf. कत्-तृण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्कृ
कात्कृ कात्-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम् (fr. कात्, an exclamation of abuse, and 1. कृ),<BR>to insult, dishonour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्कृत
कात्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, dishonoured, insulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्त्रेयक
कात्त्रेयक कात्त्रेयक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कत्-त्रि),<BR>produced from or belonging to any combination of<BR>three inferior articles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्थक्य
कात्थक्य कात्थक्य, अस्, m. (a patronymic<BR>fr. कत्थक), N. of a commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायन|कात्यायनः
कात्यायन कात्यायन. See under कातीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथक
काथक काथक and काथक्य, patronymics<BR>from Kathaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथञ्चित्क|काथंचित्क
काथञ्चित्क काथञ्चित्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कथञ्-<BR>चिद्), accomplished with difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथिक|काथिकः
काथिक काथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. कथा),<BR>belonging to a tale, told in one; knowing stories;<BR>(अस्), m. a narrator of stories.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्ब|कादंब|कादंबः|कादम्बः
कादम्ब कादम्ब, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. कद्), a kind of goose with dark-grey wings (कल-<BR>हंस); a drake or (according to some) a teal; an<BR>arrow; the plant Nauclea Cadamba; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>plant, = कदम्ब-पुष्पी; (अम्), n. the flower of<BR>the plant Nauclea Cadamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बक|कादंबकः|कादम्बकः
कादम्बक, अस्, m. an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बिनी|कादंबिनी
कादम्बिनी, f. a long line or bank of clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर|कादंबर|कादंबरं|कादम्बरं|कादम्बरः
कादम्बर कादम्बर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>surface or skim of coagulated milk; (अम्, ई), n. f. a<BR>spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the<BR>Cadamba; the rain-water which collects in clefts or<BR>hollow places of the tree Nauclea Cadamba when the<BR>flowers are in perfection, and which is supposed to be<BR>impregnated with the honey; wine, spirituous liquor<BR>in general; the fluid which issues from the temples<BR>of a rutting elephant; (ई), f. the female of the<BR>Kokila or Indian cuckoo; the female of another bird,<BR>= शारिका, i. e. Turdus Salica; an epithet of Saras-<BR>vatī; N. of a daughter of Citra-ratha and Madirā;<BR>a celebrated work of Vāṇa-bhaṭṭa, called ‘Kādambarī,’<BR>derives its name from her.<BR>—कादम्बरी-वीज, अम्,<BR>n. ferment, yeast, whatever occasions fermentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर्य|कादम्बर्य्य|कादम्बर्य्यः
कादम्बर्य, अस्, m. = कदम्ब, Nauclea Ca-<BR>damba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादाचित्क|कादाचित्कं
कादाचित्क कादाचित्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कदा-<BR>चिद्), appearing now and then, produced sometimes,<BR>occasional, incidental.<BR>—कादाचित्क-ता, f. the state<BR>of occurring occasionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादिक्रमस्तुति
कादिक्रमस्तुति कादि-क्रम-स्तुति, a work<BR>attributed to Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादिमत
कादि-मत, a Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काद्रवेय|काद्रवेयः
काद्रवेय काद्रवेय, अस्, m. (fr. कद्रू),<BR>epithet of the Nāgas or serpents supposed to people<BR>the lower regions; an epithet of Arbuda; also of<BR>Kasarṇīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानक|कानकं
कानक कानक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कनक),<BR>golden; (अम्), n. the seed of Croton Jamalgota.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानद
कानद कानद, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Dhīmarana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानन|काननं
कानन 1. कानन, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कन्), a forest, grove; a house.<BR>—काननारि (˚न-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. a species of the Mimosa tree, Śamī.<BR>—काननौकस् (˚न-ओक्˚), आस्, m. the inhabitant of<BR>a forest, a monkey; [cf. वनौकस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानन|काननं
कानन 2. कानन (क-आन्˚), अम्, n. the face<BR>of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीत
कानीत कानीत, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Pṛthu-śravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीन|कानीनः
कानीन कानीन, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. कनीन),<BR>the son or daughter of a young or unmarried woman;<BR>an epithet of Vyāsa, Karṇa, and Agniveśya; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), suitable to or designed for the eye-ball; [cf.<BR>कनीनक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीयस
कानीयस (fr. कनीयस्), less in number (used<BR>only in plur.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्त|कांत|कान्तं|कान्तः
कान्त कान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. कम्), desired,<BR>loved, dear; pleasing, agreeable; lovely, beautiful;<BR>(अस्), m. a lover, a husband; any one beloved; the<BR>moon; spring; the plant Barringtonia Acutangula<BR>[cf. हिज्जल]; iron; stone; a precious stone (in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">Page0219-a+ 77</a>]<BR>which sense it is compounded with सूर्य, चन्द्र,<BR>and अयस्); an epithet of Kṛṣṇa, and of Skanda;<BR>(आ), f. a beloved or lovely woman, a wife, a mistress;<BR>the earth; N. of a plant (commonly called प्रियङ्गु);<BR>also of another plant (= नागर-मुस्ता); large car-<BR>damoms; a kind of perfume (see रेणुका); N. of a<BR>metre of four lines of seventeen syllables each; (अम्),<BR>n. saffron; a species of iron.<BR>—कान्त-ता, f. or<BR>कान्त-त्व, अम्, n. loveliness, beauty, agreeableness.<BR>—कान्त-पक्षिन्, ई, m. a peacock (‘the beautiful<BR>bird’).<BR>—कान्त-पुष्प, अस्, m. the tree Bauhinia<BR>Variegata, mountain ebony.<BR>—कान्त-मिश्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—कान्त-लोह, अम्, n. the loadstone.<BR>—कान्त-लौह, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. steel; [cf.<BR>लोह-कान्त.]<BR>—कान्ताङ्घ्रि-दोहद (˚ता-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the tree Jonesia Aśoka (this tree being supposed to<BR>blossom upon coming in contact with the foot of a<BR>handsome female).<BR>—कान्ता-चरण-दोहद, अस्, m.<BR>= the preceding.<BR>—कान्तायस (˚त-अयस्), अम्, n. the<BR>iron stone; [cf. कान्त-लोह and अयस्-कान्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0218-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तक
कान्तक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तलक|कान्तलकः
कान्तलक, अस्, m. the tree Cedrela Toona, com-<BR>monly Tunna, the wood of which sometimes resembles<BR>mahogany.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताय
कान्ताय, nom. A. -यते, -यितुम्, to behave like<BR>a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ति|कांति|कांतिः|कान्तिः
कान्ति, इस्, f. desire, wish; loveliness, beauty;<BR>splendor; female beauty; personal decoration or<BR>embellishment; (in rhetoric) beauty enhanced by<BR>love; a lovely or desirable woman, personified as<BR>wife of the moon.<BR>—कान्ति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing<BR>beauty, beautifying, illuminating.<BR>—कान्ति-द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, giving beauty; beautifying, adorning; (आ), f.<BR>the plant Serratula Anthelmintika; (अम्), n. bile,<BR>the bilious humor.<BR>—कान्ति-दायक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>granting beauty; beautifying, adorning; (अम्), n. a<BR>fragrant wood, a kind of Curcuma from the root of<BR>which a yellow die is prepared, C. Zanthorrhiza.<BR>—कान्ति-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town in Nepal.<BR>—कान्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, lovely, beautiful, splen-<BR>did; (ती), f., N. of a metre; N. of a woman.<BR>—कान्ति-<BR>मत्-ता, f. loveliness, beauty.<BR>—कान्ति-हर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, destroying beauty, making ugly, dulling, dim-<BR>ming.<BR>—कान्ती-नगरी, f. (for कान्ति-न्˚), N. of a<BR>city of the north; [cf. कान्ति-पुर].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिक
कान्तिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तार|कांतार|कांतारं|कान्तारं|कांतारः|कान्तारः
कान्तार कान्तार, अस्, अम्, m. n. a wood or<BR>large forest; a bad or difficult road; a hole, a cavity;<BR>(अस्), m. a red variety of the sugar-cane; a bamboo;<BR>mountain ebony, Bauhinia Variegata; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of sugar-cane; (अम्), n. a symptom or symptomatic<BR>disease, a lotus.<BR>—कान्तार-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, who or<BR>what goes into a wood.<BR>—कान्तार-पथ, अस्, m.<BR>a forest-way.<BR>—कान्तार-पथिक, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>veyed on difficult forest roads.<BR>—कान्तार-वासिनी, f.<BR>an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारक|कांतारकः|कान्तारकः
कान्तारक, अस्, m. a kind of sugar-cane; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people; (इका), f. a kind of bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तोत्पाडा
कान्तोत्पाडा कान्तोत्पाडा, f. (for कान्तोत्पा-<BR>दा?), N. of a metre consisting of four lines of twelve<BR>syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्थक
कान्थक कान्थक fr. कन्था, N. of a place<BR>on the river Varṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दव|कांदव|कांदवं
कान्दव कान्दव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कन्दु),<BR>roasted or baked, in an iron pan or oven, as bread,<BR>cakes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दविक|कांदविक|कांदविकः|कान्दविकः
कान्दविक, अस्, ई, अम्, employed in baking;<BR>(अस्), m. a baker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दाविष
कान्दाविष कान्दा-विष, अम्, n., Ved. a<BR>species of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दिश्
कान्दिश् कान्दिश्, क्, क्, क्, or कान्दिशीक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, put to flight, running away, flying; (fr. कां<BR>दिशम्, ‘to which region’ shall I fly?).<BR>—कान्दिग्-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यकुब्ज|कान्यकुब्जं|कान्यकुब्जः
कान्यकुब्ज कान्यकुब्ज, अम्, n. = कन्य-<BR>कुब्ज, N. of a town; (ई), f. a princess or a female<BR>inhabitant of this town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यजा
कान्यजा कान्यजा, f. a kind of perfume,<BR>commonly Nālī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटव
कापटव कापटव, a patronymic from Kā-<BR>paṭu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटवक
कापटवक, अस्, इका, अम्, coming from the<BR>Kāpaṭavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटिक|कापटिकः
कापटिक कापटिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपट),<BR>fraudulent, dishonest; wicked, perverse, bad; (अस्),<BR>m. a flatterer, a parasite; a student, a scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापट्य|कापट्यं
कापट्य, अम्, n. wickedness, dishonesty, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथ|कापथः
कापथ का-पथ, अस्, m. a bad road; bad<BR>ways; (अम्), n. the fragrant root of Andropogon<BR>Muricatus; (अस्), m., N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापा
कापा कापा, f., Ved. a call (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाल|कापालं|कापालः
कापाल कापाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपाल), re-<BR>lating to the skull or cranium; made of skulls; (अस्),<BR>m. a follower of a certain Śaiva sect [cf. the follow-<BR>ing]; the plant Cucumis Utilissimus; (ई), f. a clever<BR>woman; (अम्), n. a kind of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिक|कापालिकः
कापालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or belonging to<BR>the skull; (अस्), m. a worshipper of Śiva of the left-<BR>hand order, characterized by carrying skulls of men<BR>as ornaments and by eating and drinking from them;<BR>N. of a mixed caste; (अस्, ई, अम्), peculiar to a<BR>Kāpālika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिन्
कापालिन्, ई, m. a N. of Śiva; N. of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Yaudhiṣṭhirī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिक
कापिक कापिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपि), shaped<BR>or behaving like a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापित्थ
कापित्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपित्थ), belonging to<BR>the tree Feronia Elephantum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापित्थक
कापित्थक, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपिल), peculiar or be-<BR>longing to Kapila (or Viṣṇu), derived from him; of<BR>a tawny colour; (अस्), m. a follower of the Sāṅkhya<BR>system of philosophy which was founded by Kapila;<BR>tawny (the colour); (अम्), n., N. of an Upa-purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिलेय
कापिलेय, a patronymic from Kapila or a metro-<BR>nymic from Kapilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिवन
कापिवन, अस्, m. (fr. कपि-वन), N. of a<BR>festival lasting two days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिश|कापिशं
कापिश, अम्, n. (fr. कपिश), a spirituous liquor,<BR>wine; (ई), f., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशायन|कापिशायनं
कापिशायन, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from Kapiśa<BR>(e. g. मधु, honey, or द्राक्षा, grape); (अस्), m. a<BR>patronymic; (अम्), n. a spirituous liquor; a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशेय|कापिशेयः
कापिशेय, अस्, m. (fr. कपिशा), a Piśāca, an imp<BR>or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिष्ठल
कापिष्ठल, अस्, m. a patronymic fr. कपिष्ठल;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; [cf. καμβισθολοι]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापी
कापी, f., N. of a woman; N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेय|कापेयं|कापेयः
कापेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपि), belonging to or re-<BR>lating to or peculiar to a monkey; a patronymic fr.<BR>कपि (a descendant of Aṅgiras being meant); (अम्),<BR>n. the monkey species; monkey tricks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्य|काप्यः
काप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, a patronymic fr. कपि (a de-<BR>scendant of Aṅgiras being meant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष|कापुरुषः
कापुरुष का-पुरुष, अस्, m. a mean con-<BR>temptible man, a coward, a wretch; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>cowardly, miserable, mean.<BR>—कापुरुष-ता, f. or<BR>कापुरुष-त्व, अम्, n. meanness, cowardliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष्य
कापुरुष्य, अम्, n. cowardice, meanness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोत|कापोतं|कापोतः
कापोत कापोत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कपोत), pecu-<BR>liar to a pigeon; of the colour of a pigeon, grey, of<BR>a dirty white colour; (अस्), m. grey (the colour),<BR>a dirty white colour; natron, fossil alkali; antimony<BR>considered as a collyrium or application to the eyes;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a plant; (अम्), n. a flock of pigeons;<BR>antimony.<BR>—कापोताञ्जन (˚त-अञ्˚), अम्, n. anti-<BR>mony especially considered as a collyrium or applica-<BR>tion to the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोतक
कापोतक, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of Kapotakīyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोतपाक्य
कापोतपाक्य, अस्, m. a prince of the Kapotapākas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकर|काप्यकरः
काप्यकर काप्यकर, अस्, m. (काप्य? -कर),<BR>a penitent, one who acknowledges his faults.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकार|काप्यकारः
काप्य-कार, अस्, m. avowal or confession of sin;<BR>a penitent, one who confesses a crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काफल|काफलः
काफल काफल, अस्, m. a bitter seed. See<BR>कट्फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काबव
काबव काबव, अस्, m., Ved. an epithet of<BR>evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्
काम् काम्, ind. an interjection used in<BR>calling out to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम|कामं|कामः
काम काम, अस्, m. (fr. 2. कम्), wish, desire,<BR>longing (e. g. प्राप्त-काम, one who has gained<BR>his wish), affection, love, the object of desire or love,<BR>the god of desire generally; Love, the god of love<BR>(son of Dharma and husband of Rati or, according<BR>to other authorities, son of Brahmā or Saṅkalpa); a<BR>N. of Agni in the Veda (either because he desires to<BR>consume all things or because he makes requests to<BR>the gods in behalf of man); a N. of Bala-deva [cf.<BR>काम-पाल]; a species of the mango tree (= महा-<BR>राज-चूत); N. of a metre consisting of four lines of<BR>two long syllables each; N. of a prince; (at the end<BR>of compounds) having a desire for, desiring (e. g.<BR>गो-काम, desiring cows; धर्म-काम, desiring<BR>justice; त्यक्तु-काम, having a desire to leave; see<BR>Gram. 871). After the phrase कामो मे, ‘my desire<BR>is,’ the potential may be used; e. g. कामो मे<BR>भुञ्जीत भवान्, my wish is that you should eat;<BR>(आ), f. wish, desire [cf. कामया]; N. of a daughter<BR>of Pṛthu-śravas and wife of Ayuta-nāyin; (अम्), n.<BR>object of desire; semen virile; N. of a Tīrtha; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), Ved. wishing, desiring. कामेन or कामात्,<BR>ind. out of affection or love for, of one's own accord,<BR>intentionally; कामाय or कामे, ind. according to<BR>one's desire; out of love for (with gen. or dat. case).<BR>—काम-कर्शन in अ-काम-कर्शन, q. v.<BR>—का-<BR>म-कला, f. an epithet of Rati, the wife of Kāma.<BR>—काम-काति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. requesting the fulfil-<BR>ment of a wish; (Sāy.) uttering wishes.<BR>—काम-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, or काम-कामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wish-<BR>ing wishes; following the dictates of passion or desire.<BR>—काम-कार, अस्, m. voluntary action, the act of<BR>following one's own inclinations, spontaneous deed;<BR>the operation or influence of desire, desire; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), following one's own inclinations, indulging one's<BR>desires.<BR>—कामकार-तस्, ind. according to one's<BR>desires or inclinations.<BR>—काम-कूट, अस्, m. the<BR>paramour of a harlot; wanton caresses, harlotry.<BR>—काम-केलि, इस्, m. amorous sport, a euphemistic<BR>term for sexual intercourse; (इस्, इस्, इ), having amo-<BR>rous sport, libidinous, wanton.<BR>—काम-क्रीडा, f.<BR>amorous sport, N. of a metre consisting of four lines<BR>of fifteen long syllables each.<BR>—काम-खड्ग-दला,<BR>f., N. of a plant; [cf. स्वर्ण-केतकी.]<BR>—काम-ग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, going or coming of one's own accord, able<BR>to move or act as one pleases; (आ), f. a libidinous<BR>woman.<BR>—काम-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, or काम-गम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or काम-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = काम-ग above;<BR>(काम-गमास्), m. pl., N. of a class of deities of<BR>the eleventh Manvantara.<BR>—काम-गिरि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—काम-गुण, अस्, m. the quality of<BR>desire, passion, affection; satiety, perfect enjoyment;<BR>an object of sense.<BR>—काम-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, mov-<BR>ing freely, unchecked, unrestrained.<BR>—काम-चरण,<BR>अम्, n. free or unchecked motion.<BR>—कामचर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. unrestrainedness.<BR>—काम-चार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>moving freely, following one's own pleasure, un-<BR>checked, unrestrained; (अस्), m. free, unrestrained<BR>motion; independant, spontaneous action; following<BR>one's own wishes or pleasures, sensuality, selfishness.<BR>—कामचार-तस्, ind. according to one's inclina-<BR>tion.<BR>—काम-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, moving according to<BR>one's inclination, acting unrestrainedly; behaving<BR>freely towards women, desirous, libidinous; self-<BR>willed; (अस्), m. a sparrow; an epithet of Garuḍa,<BR>the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR>—काम-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>or caused by passion or desire; (a son) engendered in<BR>love; (अस्), m. the son of Kāma, i. e. Aniruddha.<BR>—काम-जान, अस्, m. or (according to another<BR>reading) काम-जनि, इस्, m. the Indian cuckoo; [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-a" target="_blank">Page0220-a+ 81</a>]<BR>काम-ताल.]<BR>—काम-जाल = काम-ताल.<BR>—काम-<BR>जित्, त्, त्, त्, conquering desire; an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—काम-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having desire<BR>(personified) at the head; led by Kāma.<BR>—काम-<BR>तन्त्र, N. of a work.<BR>—काम-तरु, उस्, m. the<BR>god of love considered as a tree or parasitical plant;<BR>[cf. काम-वृक्ष.]<BR>—काम-तस्, ind. according to<BR>wish or affection, passionately, from passion or feel-<BR>ing (opposed to धर्म-तस्); of one's own accord,<BR>willingly, intentionally, by consent.<BR>—काम-ताल,<BR>अस्, m. the Indian cuckoo, (the song of this bird being<BR>poetically considered as an incentive to love.)<BR>—काम-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving what is wished, granting de-<BR>sires; an epithet of the sun, and of Skanda; (आ), f.<BR>a fabulous cow, the cow of plenty; N. of a woman.<BR>—काम-दत्ता, f. title of a work.<BR>—काम-दत्तिका,<BR>f., N. of a woman.<BR>—काम-दमिनी, f. ‘taming<BR>love,’ N. of a libidinous woman in the Pañcatantra.<BR>—काम-दम्भक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—का-<BR>म-दर्शन, अस्, ई, अम्, looking lovely.<BR>—काम-<BR>दुघ, अस्, आ, अम्, milking all desires, i. e. yielding<BR>what one wishes; (आ), f. the cow of plenty, a fabu-<BR>lous cow yielding all desires.<BR>—काम-दुह्, -धुक्,<BR>f. and काम-दुहा, f. the cow of plenty.<BR>—काम-<BR>दूतिका, f. the plant Tiaridium Indicum.<BR>—काम-<BR>दूती, f. the female of the Indian cuckoo; the plant<BR>Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—काम-देव, अस्, m. the god<BR>of love (according to some authorities a son of<BR>Sahiṣṇu and Yaśo-dharā); also a N. of Śiva; N.<BR>of a poet; N. of a king of Jayantīpurī; N. of the<BR>author of the Prāyaścitta-paddhati.<BR>—काम-दोहिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, yielding desires; an epithet of the cow of<BR>plenty, which belonged to Vasisṭha.<BR>—काम-ध-<BR>रण, अम्, n., Ved. procuring what is desired, fulfil-<BR>ment of desire.<BR>—काम-धातु, उस्, m. the region<BR>of the wishes, the seat of the Kāmāvacaras.<BR>—काम-<BR>धेनु, उस्, f. the cow of plenty, a cow belonging to<BR>the sage Vasiṣṭha, yielding all desires; title of a<BR>commentary of Vopadeva on his Kavi-kalpadruma,<BR>also called Kāvya-kāmadhenu.<BR>—कामधेनु-तन्-<BR>त्र, अम्, n. title of a work on the mystical significa-<BR>tion of the letters of the alphabet.<BR>—काम-ध्वंसिन्,<BR>ई, m. an epithet of Śiva as ‘subduing the god of love.’<BR>—काम-नाशक, अस्, इका, अम्, destroying irregular<BR>desires, subduing any sensual appetite.<BR>—कामन्-<BR>धमिन्, ई, m. a brazier; [cf. कारन्धमिन्.]<BR>—काम-पति, इस्, m. the lord of desires.<BR>—काम-<BR>पत्नी, f. the wife of Kāma, i. e. Rati.<BR>—काम-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. epithet of Bala-deva; also of Śiva; N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—काम-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, tormented<BR>with lust or irregular desires.<BR>—काम-पूर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fulfilling wishes, granting desires.<BR>—काम-प्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting desires; (अम्), n. the fulfil-<BR>ling of a desire.<BR>—काम-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, granting<BR>desires; (अस्), m. a kind of coitus.<BR>—काम-प्रश्न,<BR>अस्, m. questioning as one pleases, asking unrestrain-<BR>edly.<BR>—काम-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR>—कामप्रि, इस्, m. (fr. काम-प्र), Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic of Marutta; (Sāy.) ‘whose wishes are ful-<BR>filled.’<BR>—काम-फल, अस्, m. a species of the<BR>mango tree.<BR>—काम-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound by<BR>love; (अम्), n. a wood.<BR>—काम-भक्ष or का-<BR>म-भक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, eating anything or every-<BR>thing.<BR>—काम-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, partaking of sensual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>—काम-भोग, अस्, m. gratification of<BR>desires, sensual gratification (always used in plur.).<BR>—काम-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—काम-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of desire, answering all<BR>desires.<BR>—काम-मर्दन, अस्, m. epithet of Śiva,<BR>‘the destroyer of the god of love.’<BR>—काम-मह,<BR>अस्, m. the festival of the god of love (on the day of<BR>full moon in month Caitra or March-April).<BR>—का-<BR>म-मालिन्, ई, m. epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—काम-मूढ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, infatuated by lust.<BR>—काम-मूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. strongly affected by love.<BR>—काम-<BR>मोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome by or intoxicated<BR>with desire, love, or passion.<BR>—काम-रस, अस्, m.<BR>seminal effusion.<BR>—काम-रसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, libidi-<BR>nous.<BR>—काम-राज, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—काम-<BR>रूप, अम्, n. a shape changing at will; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>taking any shape at will; beautiful, pleasing; (अस् or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-b" target="_blank">Page0220-b+ 81</a>]<BR>आस्), m. sing. or pl. a district lying east of Bengal, the<BR>western portion of Assam.<BR>—कामरूप-धर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, taking any shape at will.<BR>—कामरूप-पति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a commentary on the work Śāradā-<BR>tilaka.<BR>—कामरूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking any shape at<BR>will; pleasing, beautiful; (ई), m. a pole-cat; a boar;<BR>a Vidyādhara, a kind of subordinate deity; (इणी), f.<BR>the plant Physalis Flexuosa.<BR>—काम-रेखा, f. a harlot,<BR>a courtezan; [cf. काम-लेखा.]<BR>—काम-लता, f. mem-<BR>brum virile; the plant Ipomœa.<BR>—काम-लेखा, f. a<BR>harlot, a courtezan; [cf. काम-रेखा.]<BR>—काम-लोल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, overcome with desire or passion.<BR>—काम-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, being in love, enamoured, wanton; con-<BR>taining the word Kāma; (ती), f. a species of Curcuma<BR>[cf. दारु-हरिद्रा]; N. of a town.<BR>—काम-वर,<BR>अस्, m. a gift chosen at will.<BR>—काम-वल्लभ, अस्,<BR>m. spring; the mango tree; (आ), f. moonlight.<BR>—काम-वश, अस्, m. subjection to love.<BR>—काम-<BR>वश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in subjection to the god of<BR>love, enamoured.<BR>—काम-वाण, अस्, m. an arrow of<BR>Kāma-deva, the deity of love.<BR>—काम-वाद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, saying anything at pleasure.<BR>—काम-वासिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, choosing one's residence at will.<BR>—काम-<BR>विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, wounded by the god of love;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—काम-विहन्तृ, ता, त्री,<BR>तृ, disappointing desires.<BR>—काम-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>displaying heroism at will, an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—काम-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a parisitical plant (= वन्-<BR>दाक).<BR>—काम-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, indulging desires,<BR>licentious, dissipated, debauched.<BR>—काम-वृद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. increase of desire or passion; (इस्, इस्, इ), in-<BR>creasing love; (इस्), m. a shrub, called in Karṇāṭaka<BR>Kāma-ja, of supposed aphrodisiac properties.<BR>—का-<BR>म-वृन्ता, f. the trumpet flower, Bignonia Suave-<BR>olens.<BR>—काम-शर, अस्, m. love's shaft; the mango<BR>tree.<BR>—काम-शास्त्र, अम्, n. a manual of pleasure<BR>or of love, title of a work of Vātsyāyana.<BR>—काम-<BR>संयोग, अस्, m. attainment of desired objects.<BR>—काम-सख, अस्, m. spring; the month Caitra;<BR>the mango tree.<BR>—काम-समूह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work of Ananta.<BR>—काम-सुत, अस्, m. the son of<BR>Kāma-deva, god of love, i. e. Aniruddha.<BR>—काम-<BR>सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, granting wishes.<BR>—काम-सूत्र, N. of<BR>a love-manual by Vātsyāyana.<BR>—काम-सेन, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of Kāmavatī; (आ), f. the wife of<BR>Nidhipati.<BR>—काम-हैतुक, अस्, ई, अम्, caused or<BR>produced by mere desire, without any real cause; of<BR>one's own accord.<BR>—कामाक्षी (˚म-अक्˚), f. a form<BR>of Durgā.<BR>—कामाख्या (˚म-आख्˚), f. a form of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—कामाग्नि (˚म-अग्˚), इस्, m. the fire of<BR>love, passion, lust, violent desire.<BR>—कामाग्नि-सन्दी-<BR>पन, अम्, n. kindling the fire of lust, an aphro-<BR>disiac.<BR>—कामाङ्कुश (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a finger-<BR>nail; the membrum virile.<BR>—कामाङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the mango tree, Mangifera Indica.<BR>—कामा-<BR>तुर (˚म-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, love-sick, in love, affected<BR>by love or desire.<BR>—कामात्म-ता, f. passion, lust;<BR>wish, desire.<BR>—कामात्मन् (˚म-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, whose<BR>very essence is desire, consisting of desire, libidi-<BR>nous, licentious; desiring, wishing for; enamoured.<BR>—कामाधिकार (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, m. the influence<BR>of passion or desire, aspiration; that part of a Śāstra<BR>which relates to human wishes or desires.<BR>—कामा-<BR>धिष्ठित (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, influenced or<BR>overcome by love.<BR>—कामानल (˚म-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the fire of love, passion, lust, violent desire.<BR>—कामान्ध (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. the Indian cuckoo<BR>(blind from love); (आ), f. musk.<BR>—कामान्निन् (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, having food at will.<BR>—कामाभि-<BR>काम (˚म-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, lustful.<BR>—कामायुध<BR>(˚म-आय्˚), अम्, n. the weapon or arrow of the god<BR>of love; membrum virile; (अस्), m. a species of the<BR>mango tree.<BR>—कामायुस् (˚म-आय्˚), उस्, m. a vul-<BR>ture; an epithet of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR>—कामारण्य (˚म-अर्˚), अम्, n. a pleasing grove<BR>or wood.<BR>—कामारि (˚म-अरि), इस्, m. a mineral<BR>substance used in medicine, a sort of pyrites (see<BR>विट-माक्षिक); an epithet of Śiva, the foe or<BR>conqueror of the god of love.<BR>—कामार्त (˚म-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted by love or passion, in love.<BR>—कामार्थिन् (˚म-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, lascivious, wanton,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">Page0220-c+ 80</a>]<BR>amorous.<BR>—कामावचर (˚म-अव्˚), आस्, m. pl. a<BR>class of deities (with Buddhists).<BR>—कामावतार<BR>(˚म-अव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a metre consisting of four<BR>lines of six syllables each; N. of a work.<BR>—कामा-<BR>वसाय (˚म-अव्˚), अस्, m. suppression or mortifi-<BR>cation of the passions, coldness, stoicism.<BR>—कामा-<BR>वसायि-ता, f. or कामावसायि-त्व, अम्, n. the power<BR>of suppressing desire, self-denial or mortification (one<BR>of the eight supernatural faculties of Śiva).<BR>—कामा-<BR>वसायितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what suppresses or<BR>destroys passion or desire.<BR>—कामावसायिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, one who suppresses desire, destructive of love or<BR>desire.<BR>—कामाशन (˚म-अश्˚), अम्, n. eating at<BR>will, unrestrained enjoyment.<BR>—कामाश्रम (˚म-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m. or कामाश्रम-पद, अम्, n. the her-<BR>mitage of the god of love.<BR>—कामासक्त (˚म-आस्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, overcome with desire or passion, im-<BR>passioned, in love.<BR>—कामासक्ति (˚म-आस्˚), इस्, f.<BR>passion, desire.<BR>—कामेप्सु (˚म-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>striving to obtain the fulfilment of a desire.<BR>—कामे-<BR>श्वर (˚म-ईश्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—कामोदक (˚म-उद्˚), अम्, n. a voluntary obla-<BR>tion of water; oblation of water to deceased friends<BR>&c. exclusive of those for whom it is directed by law.<BR>—कामोदा, f. a Rāgiṇī, one of the female personi-<BR>fications of the musical notes.<BR>—कामोपहत (˚म-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, overcome with passion or desire.<BR>—कामोपहत-चित्ताङ्ग (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one whose mind and body are overcome with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0219-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन|कामनः
कामन, अस्, आ, अम्, lustful, libidinous, desirous;<BR>(आ), f. desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामम्
कामम्, ind. (acc. c. of काम), according to wish<BR>or desire, according to inclination; agreeably to<BR>desire; at will; willingly, joyfully; (as a particle of<BR>assent) well, very well; granted; admitted that;<BR>indeed, really, surely; (implying at the same time<BR>a contradiction to what precedes) but really, but.<BR>कामम् — न or कामम् — न तु, rather — than<BR>(with pot. or impv. or fut. pass. part., e. g. कामम्<BR>आ मरणात् तिष्ठेद् गृहे कन्या — न एनाम् प्र-<BR>यच्छेत् तु गुण-हीनाय, ‘rather should a girl stay<BR>at home till her death, than that he should give her<BR>to one void of excellent qualities’); in this sense the<BR>negative sentence with न or न तु may also pre-<BR>cede or its place may occasionally be taken by an<BR>interrogative sentence (e. g. कामं नयतु मां<BR>देवः किम् अर्धेन आत्मनो हि मे, ‘rather let the<BR>god take me, what is the use to me of half my<BR>existence?’). कामम् — तु, or कामम् — किं तु,<BR>or कामम् — अथापि, or कामम् — तथापि, or का-<BR>मम् — पुनर्, well, indeed, surely, granted — how-<BR>ever, notwithstanding, nevertheless (e. g. कामं<BR>त्वया परित्यक्ता गमिष्यामि — इमं तु बालं<BR>सन्त्यक्तुं नार्हसि, ‘granted that forsaken by<BR>thee I shall go — this child however thou must not<BR>forsake;’ or the disjunctive particles are left out alto-<BR>gether).<BR>—कामङ्-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going at will;<BR>going or coming according to one's inclination or of<BR>one's own accord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामया
कामया, ind. (inst. c. of an obsolete base कामा),<BR>only used with ब्रूहि or प्रब्रूहि (e. g. कामया<BR>मे ब्रूहि देव कस् त्वम्, ‘for love of me, say, O<BR>god, who thou art’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयान
कामयान, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयितृ
कामयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, libidinous, lustful, desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामल|कामलः
कामल, अस्, आ, अम्, libidinous, lustful; (अस्), m.<BR>spring; dry and sterile soil, a desert; (अस्, आ), m. f.<BR>a form of jaundice, excessive secretion or obstruction<BR>of bile; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>daughter of Reṇu, also called Reṇukā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलायन
कामलायन or कामलायनि (a patronymic fr.<BR>कमल), an epithet of the Upakosalas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलि
कामलि, इस्, m., N. of a pupil of Vaiśampāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलिन्
कामलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from jaundice; (इनस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a school derived from Kāmali (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामि|कामिः
कामि, इस्, m. a libidinous man, a lecher; (इस्), f.<BR>an epithet of Rati, the wife of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिक|कामिकः
कामिक, अस्, आ, अम्, desired, wished for, one<BR>whose desires are fulfilled; (at the end of a compound)<BR>relating to or connected with a desire or wish; (अस्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">Page0221-a+ 77</a>]<BR>m. a kind of aquatic bird, a wild duck (कारण्डव);<BR>(आ), f. a mystical N. of the letter त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0220-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामित
कामित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished, desired; (अम्), n. a<BR>wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिन्
कामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, desirous, cupidinous; loving, fond,<BR>impassioned, wanton; (ई), m. a lover, an uxorious<BR>husband; N. of several birds, the ruddy goose, Anas<BR>Casaca; a pigeon; Ardea Sibirica; a sparrow; an<BR>epithet of Śiva; the moon (?) ; (इनी), f. a loving or<BR>affectionate woman, a timid woman; a woman in<BR>general; a climbing parasitical plant; a species of<BR>Curcuma; spirituous liquor.<BR>—कामि-ता, f. or कामि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of a lover, love, desire.<BR>—का-<BR>मिनी-कान्त, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>metre consisting of four lines of six syllables each.<BR>—कामिनीश (˚नी-ईश), अस्, m. the plant Hyper-<BR>anthera Moringa (शोभाञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामीन
कामीन or कामील, अस्, m. the plant Areca Tri-<BR>andra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुक|कामुकः
कामुक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, wishing, desirous;<BR>loving; cupidinous, lustful, libidinous; (अस्), m. a<BR>lover; a sparrow; the plant Jonesia Aśoka; the<BR>creeping plant Gærtnera Racemosa; a bow (?); (आ),<BR>f. a woman desirous of wealth, food, &c.; (ई), f. a<BR>libidinous or lustful woman.<BR>—कामुक-कान्ता, f.<BR>the plant Gærtnera Racemosa.<BR>—कामुक-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुकायन|कामुकायनः
कामुकायन, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. कामुक),<BR>N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्य|काम्यं
1. काम्य, nom. P. काम्यति (in composition with<BR>an object), to have a desire for (e. g. पुत्र-काम्यति,<BR>to have a desire for children).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्य|काम्यं
2. काम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, desirable, beautiful; amiable,<BR>lovely, agreeable; optional, supererogatory, performed<BR>for some particular object and opposed to the नित्य-<BR>कर्म or fixed and indispensable observance; relating<BR>to desire, will, &c., done through lust or passion; per-<BR>formed through the desire of some advantage (as a<BR>religious ceremony &c.); (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras,<BR>a daughter of Kardama.<BR>—काम्य-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>rites performed with a view to future fruition.<BR>—का-<BR>म्य-गिर्, ईर्, f. a pleasing sound, an agreeable speech<BR>or song.<BR>—काम्य-ता, f. loveliness, beauty.<BR>—का-<BR>म्य-त्व, अम्, n. love, desire; supererogation, will,<BR>pleasure.<BR>—काम्य-दान, अम्, n. an acceptable or<BR>desirable gift, a voluntary gift.<BR>—काम्य-मरण,<BR>अम्, n. voluntary death, suicide.<BR>—काम्य-व्रत,<BR>अम्, n. a voluntary vow.<BR>—काम्याभिप्राय (˚य-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. self-interested motive or purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यक|काम्यकः
काम्यक, अम्, n., N. of a wood; also of a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्या
काम्या, f. wish, desire, longing for, striving after,<BR>will, intention; (generally compounded with an object,<BR>e. g. पुत्र-काम्यया, through desire for a son; यत्-<BR>काम्या, irreg. inst. c. with which intention.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामठ
कामठ कामठ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कमठ),<BR>peculiar to the tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामठक
कामठक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामण्डलव
कामण्डलव कामण्डलव, अम्, n. (fr. कमण्-<BR>डलु), the business or trade of a potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामण्डलेय
कामण्डलेय, अस्, m. a patronymic fr. कमण्-<BR>डलु or कमण्डलू (a species of quadruped).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन्दकि|कामन्दकिः
कामन्दकि कामन्दकि, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>fr. कमन्दक; (ई), f., N. of a Buddhist priestess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामालिका
कामालिका कामालिका, f. a spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामालु|कामालुः
कामालु कामालु, उस्, m. the tree Bauhinia<BR>Variegata (= रक्त-काञ्चन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल|कांपिलः|काम्पिलः
काम्पिल काम्पिल, अस्, m., N. of a country<BR>believed to be situated in the north of India; (ई), f.<BR>the capital of that region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्य|काम्पिल्यः
काम्पिल्य, अस्, m., N. of a town of the Pāñcālas<BR>or N. of a region; N. of one of the five sons of<BR>Hary-aśva or Bharmyāśva, called collectively Pañcālas;<BR>N. of a plant [cf. कम्पिल and काम्पील], a perfume,<BR>commonly called Sunda Rocanī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्ल|कांपिल्ल|कांपिल्लः|काम्पिल्लः
काम्पिल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a plant, a perfume and<BR>drug so called; N. of a country said to be in the<BR>north-west of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्लक|कांपिल्लकः|काम्पिल्लकः
काम्पिल्लक, अम्, n. a kind of medicinal substance;<BR>(इका), f. a drug and perfume, commonly Sunda<BR>Rocanī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पील|काम्पीलः
काम्पील, अस्, m., N. of a plant [cf. the preced-<BR>ing]; N. of a town (?); (अस्, ई, अम्), derived from<BR>this plant.<BR>—काम्पील-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in the<BR>town Kāmpīla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पीलक|काम्पीलकः
काम्पीलक, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बल|कांबल|कांबलः|काम्बलः
काम्बल काम्बल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कम्बल),<BR>covered with a woollen blanket; (अस्), m. a carriage<BR>covered with a woollen cloth or blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बलिक|काम्बलिकः
काम्बलिक काम्बलिक, अस्, m. a sour dish<BR>prepared with milk, whey, and vinegar; gruel, barley-<BR>water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बविक|कांबविक|कांबविकः|काम्बविकः
काम्बविक काम्बविक, अस्, m. (fr. कम्बु), a<BR>dealer in shells, a vender of shell-ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बुका
काम्बुका काम्बुका, f. = कम्बुका, the plant<BR>Physalis Flexuosa (= अश्व-गन्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बुव
काम्बुव काम्बुव, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोज|कांबोज|कांबोजः|काम्बोजः
काम्बोज काम्बोज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कम्बोज),<BR>born in or coming from Kamboja; (अस्), m. a native<BR>of Kamboja, a foreign race who like the Yavanas<BR>shave the whole head, (one of the tribes was originally<BR>Kṣatriya, but degraded by omission of the necessary<BR>rites); a prince of this tribe; a horse of the Kamboja<BR>breed; the plant Rottleria Tinctoria, commonly<BR>Punnag; a kind of Mimosa, the white sort of this<BR>plant; (ई), f., N. of several plants, Glycine Debilis;<BR>a kind of Mimosa, as above; the plant Abrus Pre-<BR>catorius; the plant Serratula Anthelmintica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोजक
काम्बोजक, अस्, ई, अम्, born in or coming from<BR>Kamboja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोजि
काम्बोजि, इस्, f. (?) the plant Glycine Debilis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्ल
काम्ल काम्ल (का-अम्ल), अस्, आ, अम्, slightly<BR>acid, acidulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय 1. काय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. क), relating or<BR>devoted to the god Ka or Prajāpati; (with हविस्)<BR>clarified butter or any oblation to Brahmā; (अस्), m.<BR>scil. विधि or विवाह, one of the eight modes of<BR>marriage, = Prājāpatya; (अम्), n. with or without<BR>तीर्थ, part of the hand sacred to the creator Prajā-<BR>pati, the root of the little finger or of the last two<BR>fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय 2. काय, अस् or अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. चि),<BR>the body; the trunk of a tree; the body of a lute<BR>(i. e. the whole lute except the wires, including the<BR>gourd, neck, and belly); assemblage, collection, multi-<BR>tude; principal, capital; a house, a habitation; a<BR>butt or mark, an object to be hit or attained; natural<BR>temperament of anything or any being.<BR>—काय-<BR>कारण-कर्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. activity exhibited in bodily<BR>acts.<BR>—काय-क्लेश, अस्, m. bodily suffering, toil or<BR>pain.<BR>—काय-चिकित्सा, f. a department of medical<BR>science, treatment of the diseases which affect the<BR>whole body.<BR>—काय-बन्धन, अम्, n. a girdle.<BR>—काय-वलन, अम्, n. armour, mail.<BR>—काय-<BR>स्थ, अस्, m. the supreme being or spirit; a caste or<BR>tribe or man of that tribe; the Kāyath or writer caste<BR>proceeding from a Kṣatriya father and Śūdra mother;<BR>(ई), f. the wife of a Kāyath or scribe; (आ), f. a woman<BR>of this caste; N. of several plants, Myrobalanus Che-<BR>bula; Emblica Officinalis; Ocimum Sanctum; a drug,<BR>commonly Kākolī; cardamoms.<BR>—काय-स्थित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, situated in the body, corporeal.<BR>—कायाग्नि<BR>(˚य-अग्˚), इस्, m. the digestive faculty.<BR>—कायारो-<BR>हण (˚य-आर्˚) and कायावरोहण (˚य-अव्˚), N.<BR>of two places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक
कायक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the body &c., bodily, corporeal; (इका), f. with वृद्-<BR>धिस्, interest obtained from capital.<BR>—कायिका-<BR>वृद्धि, इस्, f. interest consisting in the use of an<BR>animal or any capital stock pawned or pledged; ser-<BR>vice rendered by the body of an animal (as a cow<BR>&c.) pledged and used by the person to whom it is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">Page0221-c+ 79</a>]<BR>pledged; or (according to some) interest, of which the<BR>payment does not affect the principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिक|कायिकः
कायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, performed with the body; cor-<BR>poreal, relating to the body; belonging to an assem-<BR>blage or multitude (especially at end of comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायमान|कायमानं
कायमान कायमान, अम्, n. a hut made of<BR>grass or thatch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायव्य
कायव्य कायव्य, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार 1. कार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कृ), at<BR>the end of a compound = making, doing, working;<BR>who or what does any act, an agent, a maker or doer,<BR>an author (e. g. कुम्भ-कार, अस्, m. a potter, a<BR>maker of earthen vessels; सुवर्ण-कार, a gold-<BR>smith; यज्ञ-कार, one who performs a sacrifice;<BR>वार्त्तिक-कार, the author of the Vārttikas); (अस्),<BR>m. act, action (e. g. काम-कार, पुरुष-कार,<BR>&c.); the term used in designating a sound or a word<BR>which is not inflected (e. g. अ-कार, the sound अ;<BR>क-कार, the sound क्; एव-कार, the word एव;<BR>फूत्-कार, the sound फूत्; cf. करण, p. 205);<BR>effort, exertion; determination; religious austerity; a<BR>husband, a master, a lord; (ई), f., N. of a plant, = का-<BR>रिका, कार्या, &c.<BR>—कार-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, working,<BR>doing work, acting as agent.<BR>—कारावर (˚र-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a man of a mixed and low caste, one born<BR>from a Niṣāda father and Vaidehī mother, employed<BR>in working in leather and hides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारक|कारकं|कारकः
1. कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, making, doing, who or<BR>what does, makes, creates, act, &c.; an agent; one<BR>who effects or produces anything; (very often in<BR>composition with that which is produced or done,<BR>e. g. सिंह-कारक, the creator of a lion; कृत्स्न-<BR>कारक, doing everything; शिल्प-कारिका, a female<BR>mechanic or doer of a mechanical art); intending<BR>to act or do; (इका), f. a female dancer; a business;<BR>trade; concise explanation and development of dif-<BR>ficult rules by metrical lines, especially in philosophy<BR>and grammar, a memorial verse or collection of such<BR>verses; or sometimes two or three Vārttikas arranged<BR>in verse; torment, torture; interest; N. of a plant;<BR>(इकास्), f. pl. Bhartṛhari's memorial verses on grammar;<BR>(अकम्), n. the relation of the noun to the verb in a<BR>sentence, the notion of a case but not co-extensive<BR>with the term case, (there are six such relations ac-<BR>cording to Pāṇini; a. कर्मन्, the object or nearest<BR>aim of an agent, the idea expressed by the acc. case;<BR>b. करण, the instrument or idea expressed by the<BR>inst. case; c. कर्तृ, the agent or doer of an action,<BR>also expressed by the inst. case, or if expressed by nom.<BR>case not considered a कारक, i. e. the agent and in-<BR>strument are both expressed by the inst. when they<BR>are not implied in the verbal termination; d. सम्-<BR>प्रदान, the recipient of the object of giving or of a<BR>gift, hence the idea expressed by the dat. case; e. अपा-<BR>दान, ablation, i. e. departure or removal from a fixed<BR>point, the idea expressed by the abl. case; f. अधि-<BR>करण, location, or the place of the action, i. e. the<BR>idea expressed by the loc. case. The idea of the geni-<BR>tive or possessive case is not considered a कारक,<BR>because it expresses the relation of two nouns to each<BR>other, but not the relation of a noun and verb.)<BR>—कारक-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, relating to one who is<BR>active in anything; instrumental, causal.<BR>—कारक-<BR>वाद, अस्, m. a treatise on logic by Rudra.<BR>—कारक-<BR>हेतु, उस्, m. the efficient or active cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारज
कारज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर-ज), of or relating to<BR>the finger-nail; (अस्), m. a young elephant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण|कारणं
1. कारण, अम्, n. cause, reason (with gen. and<BR>also often with loc.); instrument, means, motive,<BR>origin, principle, a cause (in phil.), i. e. that which<BR>is invariably antecedent to some product and is not<BR>otherwise constituted, (cause in the Nyāya philosophy<BR>is of three kinds, according to the distinction of<BR>a. समवायि, intimate or inherent, as threads are the<BR>inherent cause of cloth; b. अ-समवायि, non-intimate<BR>or non-inherent, as the conjunction of the threads is<BR>the non-intimate cause of cloth; and c. निमित्त, in-<BR>strumental, as the weaver's loom is the instrumental<BR>cause of cloth); an element, elementary matter, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">Page0222-a+ 81</a>]<BR>origin or plot of a play or poem; that on which an<BR>opinion or judgment is founded; a sign, a mark, a<BR>document, a proof; a legal instrument; an organ of<BR>sense; an action; agency, instrumentality; a father<BR>(as the cause of being); a deity as the remote or<BR>proximate cause of creation; the body; a kind of<BR>musical instrument; a sort of song; a number of<BR>scribes or कायस्थस्; (आ), f. pain, agony; casting<BR>into hell; an astronomical period; कारणात्, abl. c.<BR>from some cause or reason (e. g. कस्मात् कारणात्,<BR>‘from what cause,’ often with gen., e. g. मम का-<BR>रणात्, ‘for my sake,’ and at the end of compounds;<BR>according to native grammarians every case of कारण<BR>may be used in this manner, but only the inst.,<BR>dat., abl., and loc. occur; अ-कारणेन, without a<BR>reason; येन कारणेन, because; यस्मिन् का-<BR>रणे, from which motive, wherefore).<BR>—कारण-<BR>कारण, अम्, n. a primary cause, an elementary<BR>cause, an atom.<BR>—कारण-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, referred<BR>to its cause, resolved into its principles.<BR>—कारण-<BR>गुण, अस्, m. a quality of cause; an elementary or causal<BR>property.<BR>—कारणगुणोद्भव-गुण (˚ण-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a secondary or derivative property, as form,<BR>taste, smell, &c., produced by combinations of ele-<BR>mentary or causal particles.<BR>—कारण-तस्, ind. from<BR>a certain reason; [cf. कार्य-कारणतस्.]<BR>—कारण-<BR>ता, f. or कारण-त्व, अम्, n. causality, causation.<BR>—कारण-ध्वंस, अस्, m. the obviating or re-<BR>moving a cause or occasion.<BR>—कारण-ध्वंसक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, or कारण-ध्वंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, obvi-<BR>ating or removing the cause or reason of a thing.<BR>—कारण-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, caused.<BR>—कारण-<BR>माला, f. a series or chain of causes or events, a term<BR>for a figure in rhetoric.<BR>—कारण-वादिन्, ई, m. a<BR>complainant, a plaintiff.<BR>—कारण-वारि, इ, n. the<BR>original water which was produced at the creation,<BR>from which, as from a reservoir, the Hindūs suppose<BR>all the water in the universe to be supplied.<BR>—का-<BR>रण-विहीन, अस्, आ, अम्, without a cause or reason,<BR>unreasonable.<BR>—कारण-शरीर, अम्, n. the inner<BR>rudiment of the body or causal frame, the seat of the<BR>soul.<BR>—कारणान्वित (˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>cause or reason, following as the effect from its cause.<BR>—कारणाभाव (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्, m. absence of<BR>cause.<BR>—कारणोत्तर (˚ण-उत्त्˚), अम्, n. special<BR>plea, denial of the cause of complaint, admission of<BR>the charge generally, but denial of the issue; (thus<BR>with regard to the demand of a debt, acknowledg-<BR>ment that it was incurred, but assertion that the loan<BR>has been repaid &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0221-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणक
कारणक, at the end of compounds = कारण,<BR>cause, reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणिक|कारणिकः
कारणिक, अस्, आ and ई, अम्, causal, causative, in-<BR>vestigating, ascertaining the cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारम्
कारम्, a kind of ind. part. fr. rt. कृ at the end<BR>of compounds, e. g. स्वाहा-कारम्, नमस्-कारम्,<BR>making obeisance; also with an acc., e. g. चौरन्-<BR>कारम् आक्रोशति, he abuses a person by calling him<BR>a thief; स्वादुङ्कारम्, making anything sweet &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयत्
कारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to do, giving power<BR>or authority to do &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयमाण
कारयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, doing what is appointed,<BR>carrying into effect what has been ordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयितव्य
कारयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caused to be done,<BR>to be effected, to be made to do anything.<BR>—कार-<BR>यितव्य-दक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, clever at performing<BR>what has to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयितृ
कारयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, causing or instigating to<BR>act or do anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयिष्णु
कारयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, causing to act or perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारि|कारिः
1. कारि, इस्, इस्, m. f. an artist, an artificer, a<BR>mechanic; (इस्), f. action, act, agency, work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारित|कारितः
कारित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be made or done,<BR>brought about, effected; (आ), f., scil. वृद्धिः, interest,<BR>the amount of which is fixed by the debtor, he being<BR>forced to do so by the creditor; (अम्), n. the causal<BR>form of a verb.<BR>—कारित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>caused to be made or done.<BR>—कारितान्त (˚त-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ending with a causal affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिन्
1. कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, doing, making, effecting, produc-<BR>ing, acting, an actor; (ई), m. a mechanic, a tradesman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारु|कारुः
कारु, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार 2. कार, अस्, m. (fr. 1. कॄ, to scatter),<BR>tax, toll, royal revenue, tribute; (अस्, ई, अम्, fr. 2.<BR>कर), produced by hail; (अस्), m. a heap of snow<BR>or a mountain covered with it.<BR>—कार-कुक्षीय,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the country of king Sālva on the skirts<BR>of the Himālaya ridge in the north-west of Hindūstān;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the people of this country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारक|कारकं|कारकः
2. कारक, अम्, n. (fr. 2. करक), scil. सलिल,<BR>water produced from hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार 3. कार, अस्, m. (fr. 2. कृ, to praise),<BR>Ved. a song or hymn of praise, a battle-song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारि|कारिः
2. कारि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. raising hymns of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिन्
2. कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. rejoicing, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार 4. कार, अस्, m. (fr. 2. कॄ, to kill),<BR>killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण|कारणं
2. कारण, अम्, n. killing, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारञ्ज
कारञ्ज कारञ्ज, अस्, ई, अम्, produced by or<BR>coming from the tree Karañja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डव|कारंडव|कारंडवः|कारण्डवः
कारण्डव कारण्डव, अस्, m. a sort of duck;<BR>[cf. करण्ड.]<BR>—कारण्डव-वती, f., N. of a river (?),<BR>abounding in Kāraṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डव्यूह|कारण्डव्यूहः
कारण्डव्यूह कारण्डव्यूह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Buddha; [cf. करण्ड-व्यूह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारन्धम
कारन्धम कारन्धम, अस्, m. (fr. करन्-<BR>धम), a patronymic of Avikṣit; (अम्), n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारन्धमिन्|कारंधमिन्
कारन्धमिन्, ई, m. a brazier, a worker in mixed<BR>or white metal; a mineralogist, an assayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारपचव
कारपचव कारपचव, अस् or अम् (?), m. or<BR>n. (?), N. of a region near the Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारभ
कारभ कारभ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. करभ),<BR>produced by or coming from a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारमिहिका
कारमिहिका कारमिहिका, f. camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारम्भा|कारंभा
कारम्भा कारम्भा, f., N. of a plant bearing<BR>a fragrant seed, commonly Priyaṅgu; [cf. करम्भा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारव|कारवः
कारव का-रव, अस्, m. a crow; [‘making<BR>a discordant sound;’ cf. Lat. corvus, cornix; Gr.<BR>κόραξ, κορώνη Germ. Rabe; Eng. crow.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवल्ली
कारवल्ली कारवल्ली, f. the plant Momordica<BR>Charantia; [cf. कारवेल्ल and काण्डीर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवी
कारवी कारवी, f. the Asa Fœtida plant or<BR>its leaf, = Hiṅguparṇī; the plant Celosia Cristata; a<BR>kind of anise, Anethum Sowa; another plant, Ni-<BR>gella Indica; a kind of fennel; a kind of Cucurbitace-<BR>ous plant or small gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्ल|कारवेल्लं|कारवेल्लः
कारवेल्ल कारवेल्ल, अस्, m. a kind of gourd,<BR>Momordica Charantia; (अम्), n. the fruit of this gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्लक|कारवेल्लकः
कारवेल्लक, अस्, m. and कारवेल्लिका, f. the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारव्य
कारव्य कारव्य. See under 2. कारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्कर|कारस्करः
कारस्कर कारस्कर, अस्, m., N. of a poisonous<BR>medicinal plant; a tree in general; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people; (a various reading for कारस्कार and<BR>कारस्कृत.)<BR>—कारस्कराटिका (˚र + आटिका fr. rt.<BR>अट्), f. a centipede or worm resembling it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारा
कारा कारा, f. (fr. 1. कृ?), a prison; bind-<BR>ing, confinement, a fetter; the part of a lute below<BR>the neck, an instrument for deadening the sound of<BR>a lute; pain, affliction; a female messenger; a female<BR>worker in gold; [cf. Lith. kaliu, ‘I am a captive;’<BR>kaliny-s, ‘a captive;’ kaline, ‘a prison.’]<BR>—कारा-<BR>गार (˚रा-अग्˚), अम्, n. a gaol or place of confine-<BR>ment.<BR>—कारा-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, captive, imprisoned,<BR>confined, a prisoner.<BR>—कारा-गृह, अम्, n. a prison.<BR>—कारा-पाल, अस्, m. the guard of a prison.<BR>—कारा-<BR>वेश्मन्, अ, n. a prison, a gaol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काराधुनी
काराधुनी काराधुनी, f., Ved., (Sāy.) a<BR>musical instrument, as the conch shell and the like,<BR>(or ‘impelling the singer.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारापथ
कारापथ कारापथ, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारायिका
कारायिका कारायिका, f. a female crane, =<BR>करायिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिका
कारिका कारिका. See under 1. कार, p. 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीर
कारीर कारीर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. करीर), made<BR>of the shoots of reed; connected with the fruit of the<BR>plant Capparis Aphylla (as a sacrifice, in which this<BR>fruit is used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीर्य
कारीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with the fruit of the<BR>plant Capparis Aphylla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीष|कारीषं
कारीष कारीष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. करीष), pro-<BR>duced from or coming from dung; (अम्), n. a heap<BR>of dung, a great quantity of dried cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीषि
कारीषि, इस्, m., N. of a man; (अयस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारु|कारुः
कारु 1. कारु, उस्, उस् or ऊस्, उ (fr. 1. कृ), a<BR>maker, a doer, an agent, artificer, artisan, artist, a<BR>mechanic; terrible, horrible; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Viśva-karman, the artist of the gods; an art, a science.<BR>—कारु-चौर, अस्, m. one who commits burglary.<BR>—कारु-ज, अस्, m. the product of an artist or<BR>mechanic, a piece of mechanism, any product of<BR>manufacture; a young elephant; an ant hill, a hillock;<BR>froth, foam; sesamum growing spontaneously; the<BR>tree Mesua Ferrea; red orpiment.<BR>—कारु-हस्त, अस्,<BR>m. the hand of an artisan or artificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुक|कारुकः
कारुक, अस्, आ, m. f. an artisan, an artificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारु|कारुः
कारु 2. कारु, उस्, m. (fr. 2. कृ), Ved. one<BR>who sings or praises, a poet.<BR>—कारु-धायस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. favouring or supporting the singer; (Sāy.)<BR>arranging works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारव्य
कारव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to the singer,<BR>epithet of certain verses (ऋचस्) of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुणिक|कारुणिकः
कारुणिक कारुणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. करुण),<BR>compassionate, tender, kind.<BR>—कारुणिक-ता, f. com-<BR>passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुण्य|कारुण्यं
कारुण्य, अम्, n. compassion, tenderness, kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुण्डी|कारुंडी
कारुण्डी कारुण्डी or कारुण्डिका, f. a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारूष
कारूष कारूष, अस्, m. a prince of the<BR>Karūṣas; an epithet of Danta-vakra, the son of<BR>Kārūṣa Vṛddhaśarman; N. of a country; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a people; (अस्), m. = करूष, N. of a son<BR>of Manu; an intermediate caste, the son of the de-<BR>graded or outcast Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारूषक
कारूषक, अस्, इका, अम्, reigning over the Karūṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारेणव
कारेणव कारेणव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. करेणु),<BR>produced by or coming from the female elephant;<BR>a patronymic of Pālakāpya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोतर|कारोतरः
कारोतर कारोतर, अस्, m., Ved. a filtering<BR>vessel, a cloth for purifying the liquor called surā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोत्तम|कारोत्तमः
कारोत्तम, अस्, m. yeast, barm, the froth of the<BR>surā liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोत्तर|कारोत्तरः
कारोत्तर, अस्, m. yeast, barm, the froth which<BR>rises on the surā; a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कण|कार्क्कण
कार्कण कार्कण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृकण),<BR>caused by or relating to a pheasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कन्धव
कार्कन्धव कार्कन्धव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्-<BR>कन्धू), produced by the plant Zizyphus Jujuba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कवाकव|कार्क्कवाकव
कार्कवाकव कार्कवाकव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृ-<BR>कवाकु), relating to a cock, produced by a cock &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कश्य|कार्कश्यं|कार्क्कश्य
कार्कश्य कार्कश्य, अम्, n. (fr. कर्कश),<BR>roughness, hardness; sternness, inflexibility; firmness,<BR>solidity; rough labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कष
कार्कष कार्कष, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कषायणि
कार्कषायणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कीक|कार्क्कीक
कार्कीक कार्कीक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्क), like<BR>a white horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कोटक
कार्कोटक कार्कोटक, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ण|कार्णः|कार्ण्ण
कार्ण कार्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्ण), being in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">Page0223-a+ 77</a>]<BR>the ear, relating to the ear, auricular &c.; a patro-<BR>nymic from Karṇa; (अम्), n. the wax of the ear,<BR>an ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णच्छिद्रक|कार्णछिद्रक
कार्णच्छिद्रक, अस्, m. (fr. कर्ण-च्छिद्र), a<BR>sort of well, similar to the opening of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णवेष्टकिक
कार्णवेष्टकिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्ण-वेष्टक),<BR>ornamented with or fit for ear-rings; also read कार्-<BR>णवेष्टनिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णश्रवस
कार्णश्रवस, अम्, n. (fr. कर्ण-श्रवस्), N. of<BR>a Sāman or verse of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णिक
कार्णिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णाटभाषा
कार्णाटभाषा कार्णाट-भाषा, f. the dialect<BR>of Karṇāṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णाटक
कार्णाटक, अस्, m. a native of Karṇāṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त|कार्त्त
कार्त कार्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. कृत्), relating<BR>to or treating of the affixes called कृत्; (अस्), m. (fr.<BR>कृत), N. of a son of Dharma-netra; a patronymic<BR>occurring in the compound Kārta-kaujapau.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्तयश
कार्तयश, अम्, n. (fr. कृत + यश for यशस्),<BR>N. of a Sāman or verse of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्तयुग
कार्तयुग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृत-युग), relating<BR>to the period of time called Kṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्तवीर्य|कार्तवीर्यः|कार्त्तवीर्य्य|कार्त्तवीर्य्यः
कार्तवीर्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Kṛta-vīrya<BR>and epithet of Arjuna, a prince of the Haihayas,<BR>killed by Paraśu-rāma; N. of one of the Jaina<BR>Cakravartins or emperors of the world in Bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्तस्वर|कार्तस्वरं|कार्त्तस्वर|कार्त्तस्वरं
कार्तस्वर, अम्, n. (fr. कृत-स्वर), gold; the<BR>thorn-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्तान्तिक|कार्तांतिक|कार्तांतिकः|कार्तान्तिकः|कार्त्तान्तिक|कार्त्तान्तिकः
कार्तान्तिक, अस्, m. (fr. कृतान्त), an astrologer<BR>who foretels destinies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ति
कार्ति, इस्, m. a patronymic from Kṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्तिसिंहदेव
कार्तिसिंह-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man (कार्तिसिंह<BR>being a patronymic fr. कृति-सिंह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिक|कार्तिक|कार्तिकः|कार्त्तिकः
कार्त्तिक कार्त्तिक, अस्, m. (fr. कृत्तिका, the<BR>Pleiades), scil. मास, N. of the month Kārttika or<BR>October-November, when the moon is full and near<BR>the Pleiades, the twelfth month of the year; a metro-<BR>nymic of Skanda [cf. कार्त्तिकेय]; N. of a Varṣa;<BR>N. of a medical author; (ई), f., scil. रात्रि, the night<BR>of full moon in the month Kārttika, the day on<BR>which the moon stands in the constellation Kṛttikā.<BR>—कार्त्तिक-महिमन्, आ, m. ‘the greatness of the<BR>month Kārttika,’ title of a treatise on the festivals of<BR>that month.<BR>—कार्त्तिक-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. title of<BR>a section of the Padma-purāṇa.<BR>—कार्त्तिक-शालि, इस्,<BR>m. the rice which ripens in the beginning of the<BR>cold season and forms the principal harvest in India.<BR>—कार्त्तिक-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast on<BR>the Mugdhabodha.<BR>—कार्त्तिकोत्सव (˚क-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the day of full moon in the month Kārttika, a<BR>festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकिक|कार्तिकिक|कार्त्तिकिकः
कार्त्तिकिक, अस्, m. the month Kārttika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकेय|कार्तिकेय|कार्तिकेयः|कार्त्तिकेयः
कार्त्तिकेय, अस्, m., N. of Skanda, the god of war, so<BR>called because reared by the six Kṛttikās or Pleiades;<BR>(according to one legend he was son of Śiva without<BR>the intervention of his wife, his generative energy<BR>being cast into the fire and then received by the<BR>Ganges, whence he is sometimes described as son of<BR>Agni and Gaṅgā; when born he was fostered by the<BR>Pleiades, who offering their six breasts the child be-<BR>came six-headed. In other accounts he is described<BR>as a son of Śiva and Pārvatī or Durgā. Skanda<BR>may have been called Kārttikeya because the month<BR>Kārttikā is the best for warfare: he is sometimes<BR>described as presiding over thieves.)<BR>—कार्त्तिकेय-<BR>प्रसू, ऊस्, f. an epithet of Durgā or Pārvatī, who,<BR>according to one legend, was the mother of Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्स्न
कार्त्स्न कार्त्स्न, अम्, n. (fr. कृत्स्न), the<BR>whole, totality, all, entireness; (perhaps a wrong form<BR>for the following.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्स्न्य|कार्त्स्न्यं
कार्त्स्न्य, अम्, n. the whole, totality, all, entireness.<BR>—कार्त्स्न्येन, ind. in full, entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्दम|कार्द्दम
कार्दम कार्दम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्दम),<BR>made of mud, muddy, filled or covered with it;<BR>belonging to Prajāpati Kardama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्दमिक
कार्दमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पट|कार्पटः
कार्पट कार्पट, अस्, m. (fr. कर्पट?), a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">Page0223-b+ 77</a>]<BR>petitioner, a suitor, one who begs for employment<BR>&c.; lac, the animal dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पटिक|कार्पटिकः
कार्पटिक, अस्, m. a pilgrim, one who spends his<BR>life in pilgrimage, or who subsists by carrying water<BR>from holy rivers; a caravan of pilgrims; a parasite;<BR>an experienced man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पण्य|कार्पण्यं
कार्पण्य कार्पण्य, अम्, n. (fr. कृपण),<BR>poverty, indigence; pitiful circumstances; poorness of<BR>spirit, weakness, parsimony, niggardliness, imbecility;<BR>compassion, pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पाण|कार्पाणं
कार्पाण कार्पाण, अम्, n. (fr. कृपाण), Ved.<BR>combat, fighting, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पास|कार्पासं|कार्पासः
कार्पास कार्पास, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्पास),<BR>made of cotton, cottony; (अस्, अम्), m. n. cotton,<BR>cotton cloth, &c.; paper; (ई), f. the cotton plant,<BR>Gossypium Hirsutum.<BR>—कार्पास-नासिका, f. a spin-<BR>dle.<BR>—कार्पासास्थि (˚स-अस्˚), n. the seed of the<BR>cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासिक
कार्पासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, made of or from cotton;<BR>(आ), f. the cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म|कार्म्म|कार्म्मः
कार्म कार्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्मन्), labori-<BR>ous, industrious, occupied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मण|कार्म्मण|कार्म्मणं
कार्मण, अस्, ई, अम्, finishing a work, doing it<BR>well or completely; (अम्), n. magic, sorcery, witch-<BR>craft; performing anything by means of magical<BR>incantations.<BR>—कार्मण-त्व, अम्, n. magic, fasci-<BR>nation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मणेयक
कार्मणेयक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of<BR>a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मार|कार्मारः|कार्म्मार
कार्मार, अस्, m., Ved. = कर्मार, an artist,<BR>mechanic, a smith; a patronymic from Karmāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मारक|कार्मारकं|कार्म्मारक
कार्मारक, अम्, n. a smith's work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मिक|कार्म्मिक|कार्म्मिकः
कार्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, engaged or employed in any<BR>work, epithet of a Buddhist philosophical school;<BR>manufactured, made; worked, embroidered, inter-<BR>mixed with coloured thread (as cloth &c.); any<BR>variegated texture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मिक्य|कार्मिक्यं
कार्मिक्य, अम्, n. activity, industry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मुक|कार्म्मुक|कार्म्मुकं|कार्म्मुकः
1. कार्मुक, अस्, ई, अम्, finishing a work, doing<BR>it well or completely, fit for or able to do a work;<BR>(अस्), m. a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मुक|कार्म्मुक|कार्म्मुकं|कार्म्मुकः
कार्मुक 2. कार्मुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृमुक),<BR>consisting of the wood Kṛmuka; (अम्), n. a bow;<BR>an instrument shaped like a bow.<BR>—कार्मुक-भृत्,<BR>त्, m. the archer or Sagittarius in the zodiac; an<BR>archer in general, a soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मुकाय
कार्मुकाय, nom. A. कार्मुकायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>form a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्मुकिन्
कार्मुकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, armed with a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य|कार्य्य|कार्य्यं
कार्य कार्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fut. pass. part. fr.<BR>1. कृ), to be made, to be done, practised, performed,<BR>accomplished, &c., feasible; to be imposed (as a<BR>punishment), to be offered (as a libation) &c.; what<BR>ought to be done, fit, right; (कार्य-तम, superl.<BR>what ought chiefly to be done, i. e. first duty); (अम्),<BR>n. work or business to be done, duty, affair; a re-<BR>ligious action or performance; occupation, matter,<BR>thing, enterprise, emergency, occurrence, crisis; con-<BR>duct, deportment; business, occasion, need (with<BR>inst. case, e. g. त्रिणेन कार्यम्, there is need of a<BR>straw; न भूम्या कार्यम् अस्माकम्, we have no<BR>business whatever with the earth, the earth is not our<BR>concern); lawsuit, dispute; an operation in grammar<BR>(e. g. स्थान्य्-आश्रयं कार्यम्, an operation which<BR>is borne by or rests on the primitive form as opposed<BR>to the आदेश or substitute); an effect, the necessary<BR>result of a cause (in phil.); motive, object, aim,<BR>purpose (e. g. किं कार्यम्, for what purpose?<BR>wherefore?); cause, origin; the denouement of a<BR>drama; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = कारी, कारिका.<BR>—कार्य-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, producing an effect,<BR>efficacious.<BR>—कार्य-कर्तृ, ता, m. or कार्य-का-<BR>रक, अस्, m. an agent, a workman.<BR>—कार्य-का-<BR>रण, अम्, n. object and motive, cause and effect,<BR>cause of a special or incidental kind, originating in<BR>some act or occasion.<BR>—कार्य-कारणतस्, ind. from<BR>some special cause, with a particular design or motive.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-c" target="_blank">Page0223-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—कार्य-कारण-भाव, अस्, m. relation of cause<BR>and effect.<BR>—कार्य-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, performing a<BR>work.<BR>—कार्य-काल, अस्, m. time for action, ap-<BR>pointed time, season, opportunity.<BR>—कार्य-कुशल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, skilful or clever in work, doing it well or<BR>completely.<BR>—कार्य-क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, competent<BR>or fit for a work.<BR>—कार्य-गुरुता, f. or कार्य-<BR>गुरुत्व, अम्, n. necessity or importance of any act.<BR>—कार्य-गौरव, अम्, n. importance of an affair<BR>or business.<BR>—कार्य-चिन्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>takes care of a business, the manager of a business;<BR>prudent, considerate, cautious.<BR>—कार्य-चिन्ता, f.<BR>prudence, caution, consideration.<BR>—कार्य-च्युत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, out of work, removed from an office.<BR>—कार्-<BR>य-तस्, ind. consequently, necessarily, actually.<BR>—कार्-<BR>य-त्व, अम्, n. the being an effect, the relation or<BR>condition of an effect or of what has been effected.<BR>—कार्य-दर्शन, अम्, n. inspection of work, re-<BR>vision.<BR>—कार्य-दर्शिन्, ई, m. an inspector or super-<BR>intendent of affairs.<BR>—कार्य-निर्णय, अस्, m. ascer-<BR>tainment of the fact; settlement or decision of an<BR>affair.<BR>—कार्य-पुट, अस्, m. a man who does use-<BR>less things; a madman, a crazy or hair-brained man;<BR>an impudent or shameless fellow; an idler, one who<BR>follows unprofitable pursuits.<BR>—कार्य-प्रद्वेष,<BR>अस्, m. aversion from activity, idleness.<BR>—कार्य-<BR>प्रेष्य, अस्, m. one who is sent on any business, a<BR>messenger.<BR>—कार्य-भाजन or कार्य-पात्र, अम्,<BR>n. any one engaged in active life, one fit for business<BR>or the conduct of affairs.<BR>—कार्य-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, = कार्य-च्युत above.<BR>—१. कार्य-वत्, ind.<BR>actually, according to act or motive.<BR>—२. कार्य-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having business to transact, engaged in a<BR>business; having a cause or motive, doing one's duty.<BR>—कार्यवत्-ता, f. or कार्यवत्-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being engaged in a work, any business, act,<BR>action.<BR>—कार्य-वश, अस्, m. necessary consequence.<BR>—कार्य-वस्तु, उ, n. anything that has to be done,<BR>an aim, object.<BR>—कार्य-विपत्ति, इस्, f. failure of an<BR>action, reverse, misfortune.<BR>—कार्य-शेष, अस्, m.<BR>the remainder of a business; completion of an affair.<BR>—कार्य-सन्देह, अस्, m. uncertainty or doubt<BR>about a work, embarrassment, difficulty.<BR>—कार्य-<BR>सागर, अस्, m. ‘an ocean of business,’ heavy or<BR>weighty affairs.<BR>—कार्य-साधक, अस्, आ, अम्, effec-<BR>tive of any work, accomplishing any object, an agent.<BR>—कार्य-साधन, अम्, n. means of effecting any<BR>object, instrument, implement, aid.<BR>—कार्य-सिद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. accomplishment of a work, success, fulfilment<BR>of any object.<BR>—कार्य-स्थान, अम्, n. a place of<BR>business, an office.<BR>—कार्य-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ,<BR>obstructing or counteracting the work of others, a<BR>mar-plot.<BR>—कार्याकार्य-विचार, अस्, m. delibera-<BR>tion on the arguments for and against any act.<BR>—कार्याक्षम (˚य-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, unfit<BR>for any work, incompetent, unable.<BR>—कार्याधिप<BR>(˚य-अध्˚), अस्, m. the planet which determines or<BR>decides any inquiry or question in astrology.<BR>—कार्-<BR>यान्त (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of a business,<BR>termination of an affair.<BR>—कार्याब्धि (˚य-अब्˚), इस्,<BR>m. an ocean of business.<BR>—कार्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the object of a business or enterprise; any object<BR>or purpose; application for employment; (अम्), ind.<BR>for the sake of a business, for the sake of any<BR>particular object, to perform any work or duty.<BR>—कार्यार्थ-सिद्धि, इस्, f. the accomplishment of<BR>any object or purpose.<BR>—कार्यार्थिन् (˚य-अर्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, making a request, seeking for business, apply-<BR>ing for employment; pleading a cause in court,<BR>going to law.<BR>—कार्येश and कार्येश्वर (˚य-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. = कार्याधिप above.<BR>—कार्योद्धार (˚य-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. discharge of any duty, performance of<BR>any act.<BR>—कार्योद्युक्त (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, en-<BR>gaged in any business, intent upon any object.<BR>—कार्योद्योग (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, m. active engage-<BR>ment in any business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्यिक|कार्य्यिक
कार्यिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having business, transacting<BR>business, seeking employment &c.; engaged in a suit<BR>at law, pleading a cause in court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्यिन्|कार्य्यिन्
कार्यिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who transacts business,<BR>active, assiduous; seeking for employment; having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">Page0224-a+ 73</a>]<BR>an object; a party to a suit, either as plaintiff or<BR>defendant; (in gram.) subject to the operation of a<BR>grammatical rule, requiring an affix &c.<BR>—कार्-<BR>येक्षण (˚य-ईक्˚), अम्, n. superintendence of<BR>public affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0223-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्शकेय
कार्शकेय कार्शकेय, a patronymic from<BR>Kṛśaka.<BR>—कार्शकेयी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्शन
कार्शन कार्शन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृशन), Ved.<BR>consisting of pearl or mother-of-pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्शानव
कार्शानव कार्शानव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृशानु),<BR>fiery, hot, glaring, relating to fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्मरी
कार्श्मरी कार्श्मरी, f., N. of a plant, = कार्-<BR>ष्मर्य, काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्य|कार्श्यं|कार्श्यः
कार्श्य 1. कार्श्य, अस्, m., N. of several<BR>plants, = कार्ष्य and कार्ष्मर्य, = कर्चूर;<BR>another plant, Artocarpus Lacucha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्य|कार्श्यं|कार्श्यः
कार्श्य 2. कार्श्य, अम्, n. (fr. कृश), emacia-<BR>tion, thinness, smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष|कार्षः
कार्ष कार्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. कृष्), one who<BR>ploughs a field, a peasant, a husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षक|कार्षकः
कार्षक, अस्, m. a husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षि|कार्षिः
कार्षि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. drawing, attracting; plough-<BR>ing; (इस्), m. fire; (इस्), f. drawing, attracting;<BR>ploughing, cultivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षिक|कार्षिकः
कार्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्ष), deserving of<BR>pulling or dragging about; weighing a Karṣa; (अस्),<BR>m. a coin of the weight of one Karṣa; a husband-<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षीवण|कार्षीवणः
कार्षीवण, अस्, m. (fr. कार्षि with इ lengthened),<BR>Ved. one who ploughs a field, a husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्मन्
कार्ष्मन्, अ, n., Ved. the goal of a race-course<BR>(consisting of a line like a furrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापण|कार्षापणं|कार्षापणः
कार्षापण कार्षापण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (= कर्-<BR>षापण), a coin or weight of different values, as<BR>synonymous with Karṣa; if of gold, weighing 16<BR>Māṣas, which are variously calculated, see कर्ष;<BR>if of silver, it is in value = 16 Paṇas of Kowries, i. e.<BR>1280 Kowries, commonly termed a Kāhan; if of<BR>copper, it weighs 80 Raktikās, or the same as of gold,<BR>about 176 grains; according to some it is the same as<BR>a Paṇa of Kowries, i. e. 80 Kowries; at the end of a<BR>compound it means ‘worth so many Kārṣāpaṇas;’<BR>(अम्), n. money, gold and silver; (अस्), m. a husband-<BR>man (?); N. of a warrior-tribe; the chief of this tribe.<BR>—कार्षापणावर (˚ण-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the value of at least one Kārṣāpaṇa (as a fine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापणक|कार्षापणकः
कार्षापणक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a weight or<BR>measure of different values, as synonymous with<BR>Karṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापणिक
कार्षापणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, worth one Kārṣā-<BR>paṇa, bought &c. with one Kārṣāpaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्ण
कार्ष्ण कार्ष्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृष्ण),<BR>coming from or belonging to the black antelope;<BR>made of the skin of the black antelope; belonging<BR>to the god Kṛṣṇa or Kṛṣṇa-dvaipāyana, composed<BR>by him &c. (e. g. कार्ष्णं वेदम्, the Mahā-bhā-<BR>rata); belonging to a descendant of Kṛṣṇa; black;<BR>(ई), f. the plant Asparagus Racemosus; (अम्), n.,<BR>Ved. the skin of the black antelope; (अस्), m. the<BR>black antelope (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णाजिनि|कार्ष्णाजिनिः
कार्ष्णाजिनि, इस्, m. (fr. कृष्णाजिन), a patro-<BR>nymic from Kṛṣṇājina; N. of a teacher; N. of a<BR>philosopher; N. of the author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णायस
कार्ष्णायस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कृष्णायस), of<BR>iron, made of black iron; (अम्), n. iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णि|कार्ष्णिः
कार्ष्णि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Kṛṣṇa; an<BR>epithet of Viśvaka; N. of a Devagandharva; an<BR>epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्ण्य|कार्ष्ण्यं
कार्ष्ण्य, अम्, n. blackness, black colour, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्मन्
कार्ष्मन् कार्ष्मन्. See under कार्ष above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्मर्य
कार्ष्मर्य कार्ष्मर्य, अस्, m., Ved. the tree<BR>Gmelina Arborea.<BR>—कार्ष्मर्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्य|कार्ष्यः
कार्ष्य कार्ष्य, अस्, m. the tree Shorea<BR>Robusta.<BR>—कार्ष्य-वण, अम्, n. a forest of these<BR>trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल|कालं|कालः
काल 1. काल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. 3. कल्?; for 2.<BR>काल, ‘time,’ see next page), black, of a dark colour,<BR>especially dark-blue which is often confounded with<BR>black; (अस्), m. a black or dark-blue colour; the<BR>black part of the eye; the Indian cuckoo; the poi-<BR>sonous serpent, Coluber Naga (= काल-सर्प); the<BR>plant Cassia Sophora; a plant, a red kind of plum-<BR>bago; the resin of the plant Shorea Robusta; the<BR>planet Saturn; an epithet of Śiva; also of Rudra;<BR>N. of a son of Hrada; also of a prince; also of a<BR>brother of king Prasena-jit; also of a future Buddha;<BR>also of a Nāga-rāja; of a Rakṣas; of an enemy of<BR>Śiva; N. of a mountain; (with the Jainas) N. of<BR>one of the nine treasures; a mystical name for the<BR>letter म्; (आ), f., N. of several plants, Indigofera<BR>Tinctoria; Piper Longum; a plant nearly related to<BR>Ipomœa Turpethum, perhaps Ipomœa Atropurpurea;<BR>Nigella Indica; Rubia Munjista; Ruellia Longifolia;<BR>Physalis Flexuosa; Bignonia Suaveolens; the fruit of<BR>the Kālā (?); N. of a daughter of Dakṣa, the mother<BR>of the Kāleyas or Kālakeyas (a family of Asuras); an<BR>epithet of Durgā; (ई), f. black colour, ink or black-<BR>ing; abuse, censure, defamation; a row or succession<BR>of black clouds; night; a worm or animalcule gene-<BR>rated in the acetous fermentation of milk, = क्षीर-<BR>कीट and क्षार-कीट; N. of several plants, = का-<BR>लाञ्जनी; another plant, Cajanus Indicus; Ipomœa<BR>Turpethum; Bignonia Suaveolens; one of the seven<BR>tongues or flames of fire; a form of Durgā; one of<BR>the Mātṛs or divine mothers; N. of a female evil<BR>spirit, mother of the Kālakeyas; one of the sixteen<BR>Vidyādevīs; an epithet of Śatyavatī, the wife of king<BR>Śāntanu and mother of Vyāsa or Kṛṣṇa-dvaipāyana,<BR>but before her marriage. (After her marriage she<BR>had a son called Vicitra-vīrya, whose widows were<BR>married by Kṛṣṇa-dvaipāyana and bore to him<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and Pāṇḍu; according to other legends<BR>Kālī is the wife of Bhīma-sena and mother of Sarva-<BR>gata); N. of a river, otherwise काला गङ्गा; (अम्),<BR>n. a black kind of Agallochum; a kind of perfume<BR>(= कक्कोलक); iron; [cf. Gr. κηλίς, κελαινός<BR>Lat. caligo.]<BR>—काल-कचु, उस्, f. the plant Arum<BR>Colocasia.<BR>—काल-कण्टक, अस्, m. a gallinule; [cf.<BR>the next.]<BR>—काल-कण्ठ, अस्, m., N. of several<BR>birds, a peacock; a water fowl, a gallinule; a wag-<BR>tail; a sparrow; the plant Terminalia Tomentosa,<BR>= पीतशाल and पीतसार; an epithet of Śiva; [cf.<BR>नील-कण्ठ.]<BR>—काल-कण्ठक, अस्, m. a gallinule.<BR>—काल-कन्दक, अस्, m. a water-snake.<BR>—काल-<BR>कर्णिका or काल-कर्णी, f. misfortune (predicted as the<BR>consequence of having black ears).<BR>—काल-कलाय,<BR>अस्, m. dark pulse, Phaseolus Max.<BR>—काल-कस्तूरी, f.<BR>the plant Hibiscus Abelmoschus, the seeds smelling of<BR>musk when rubbed.<BR>—काल-कीर्ति, इस्, m., N. of a king<BR>identified with the Asura Suparṇa.<BR>—काल-कुष्ठ,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of earth brought from mountains; [cf.<BR>कङ्कुष्ठ.]<BR>—काल-कोटि, इस्, f., N. of a region.<BR>—काल-क्लीतक, अम्, n. the indigo plant.<BR>—काल-<BR>खञ्ज, आस्, m. pl. = कालकञ्ज, perhaps only a<BR>wrong reading; (अम्), n. the liver.<BR>—काल-खञ्जन,<BR>अम्, n. the liver.<BR>—काल-खण्ड, अम्, n. the liver.<BR>—काल-गङ्गा, f., N. of a river in Ceylon.<BR>—काल-<BR>गण्डिका, f., N. of a river.<BR>—काल-गन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of Cobra de Capella, = काल-कन्दक.<BR>—का-<BR>ल-घट, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—काल-जोषक,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (a various reading has<BR>कालजोषिक.)<BR>—काल-ताल, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>= तमाल.<BR>—काल-तिन्दुक, अस्, m. a kind of ebony.<BR>—काल-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—काल-<BR>तोयक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—काल-दन्तक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Nāga, a son of Vāsuki.<BR>—१. काल-<BR>नर, अस्, m., N. of a son of Sabhānara, a son of<BR>Anu; (for 2. काल-नर see under 2. काल.)<BR>—काल-<BR>नाभ, अस्, m. (नाभ = नाभि), N. of an Asura, a<BR>son of Hiraṇyākṣa; also of a son of Hiraṇya-kaśipu;<BR>also of a son of Vipra-citti and Siṃhikā.<BR>—काल-<BR>निर्यास, अस्, m. a fragrant and resinous exudation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-c" target="_blank">Page0224-c+ 81</a>]<BR>from the plant Amyris Agallocha.<BR>—काल-नेत्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, black-eyed.<BR>—काल-पर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a tree<BR>bearing dark-coloured leaves, Tabernæmontana Coro-<BR>naria, commonly called Tagara.<BR>—काल-पर्वत, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—कालपात्रिक, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>काल-पात्र), a kind of mendicant whose alms-dish<BR>is painted black.<BR>—काल-पालक, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>earth; [cf. कङ्कुष्ठ, काल-कुष्ठ.]<BR>—काल-<BR>पीलुक, अस्, m., N. of a tree; see कुपीलु.<BR>—काल-<BR>पुच्छ or काल-पुच्छक, अस्, m. a species of animal<BR>living in marshes.<BR>—काल-पुष्प, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>plant; see कलाय.<BR>—काल-पूग, अस्, m. the black<BR>multitude, i. e. the common people (?).<BR>—काल-<BR>पृष्ठ, अस्, m. a species of antelope (with a black<BR>back); a heron; (अम्), n., N. of the bow of Karṇa;<BR>a bow in general.<BR>—काल-पेशी, f., N. of a plant;<BR>see श्यामा.<BR>—काल-भाण्डिका, f. the plant Rubia<BR>Munjista.<BR>—काल-मसी, f., N. of a river; also called<BR>कालमही.<BR>—कालमान and काल-माल, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Ocimum Sanctum, a fragrant pot-herb.<BR>—काल-<BR>मुख, अस्, m. a kind of monkey; N. of a fabulous<BR>people; (आ), f., N. of a female.<BR>—काल-मुष्कक,<BR>अस्, m. the plant Bignonia Indica; see मुष्कक.<BR>—काल-मूल, अस्, m., N. of a plant, commonly<BR>Rakta-citraka.<BR>—काल-मेशिका or काल-मेषिका, f.<BR>the plant Rubia Munjista; also the plant Ipomœa<BR>Atropurpurea (?).<BR>—काल-मेषी, f., N. of several<BR>plants, Vernonia Anthelminthica; Rubia Munjista;<BR>and perhaps Ipomœa Atropurpurea.<BR>—काल-यवन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a prince of the Yavanas; a tyrannical<BR>Asura, the foe of Kṛṣṇa, destroyed by him by a<BR>stratagem.<BR>—१. काल-रात्रि, इस् or ई, f. a dark night;<BR>(for 2. see under 2. काल.)<BR>—काल-लवण, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of black factitious and purgative salt, commonly<BR>called विड्-लवण.<BR>—काल-लोचन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Daitya.<BR>—काल-लौह, अम्, n. iron.<BR>—काल-वदन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Daitya; also called शाल-वदन.<BR>—का-<BR>ल-वृक्ष and काल-वृन्त, अस्, m. a kind of vetch,<BR>Dolichos Biflorus [cf. कुलत्थ]; (ई), f. the trumpet<BR>flower, Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—काल-वेला, f. the time<BR>of Saturn, a particular time of the day at which any<BR>religious act is improper, half a watch in every day.<BR>—काल-शम्बर, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—काल-<BR>शाक, अम्, n. the pot-herb Ocimum Sanctum.<BR>—का-<BR>ल-शालि, इस्, m. a black sort of rice.<BR>—काल-शिवि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—काल-शैल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—काल-सङ्कर्षा, f. a girl nine years<BR>old, who personates Durgā at a festival in honour of<BR>this goddess.<BR>—काल-सर्प, अस्, m. the black and<BR>most poisonous variety of the Cobra, Coluber Naga.<BR>—काल-सार, अस्, m. the black antelope; (अम्), n.<BR>a yellow sort of sandal-wood.<BR>—काल-स्कन्ध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of several plants; a kind of ebony with a<BR>dark trunk, Diospyros Embryopteris; the Tamāla, a<BR>tree bearing dark blossoms, Xanthochymus Pictorius;<BR>another plant, = जीवक; another, = दुष्खदिर;<BR>the glomerous fig tree, Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—कालागुरु<BR>(˚ल-अग्˚), उ, n. a black kind of aloe wood or Agallo-<BR>chum.<BR>—कालाङ्ग (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>dark-blue body, as a sword with a dark-blue edge.<BR>—कालाजिन (˚ल-अज्˚), अस्, m., N. of a people.<BR>—कालाञ्जन (˚ल-अञ्˚), अम्, n. a black unguent;<BR>(ई), f. a small shrub used as a purgative.<BR>—कालाण्डज<BR>(˚ल-अण्˚), अस्, m. the black bird, an epithet of the<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR>—कालानुशारिवा, f., N. of two plants,<BR>= तगर; and शीतलीजटा, commonly śīulīchop.<BR>—कालानुसारक (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n., N. of a tree,<BR>= तगर; yellow sandal.<BR>—कालानुसारि, इस्, m. or<BR>कालानुसारिन् (˚ल-अन्˚), ई, m. or कालानुसारिवा, f.<BR>benzoin or benjamin.<BR>—कालानुसार्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>m. f. n. gum benjamin or benzoin; (अम्), n. a<BR>yellow fragrant wood from which a perfume is pre-<BR>pared, sandal-wood (?); N. of a tree, = तगर;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. the tree Dalbergia Sissoo.<BR>—काला-<BR>नुसार्यक, अम्, n. gum benzoin or benjamin.<BR>—कालाम्र (˚ल-आम्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Dvīpa.<BR>—कालायस (˚ल-अयस्), अम्, n. iron.<BR>—कालायस-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, of iron, consisting of iron.<BR>—का-<BR>लाशोक (˚ल-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist king.<BR>—कालासुहृद् (˚ल-अस्˚), त्, m. an enemy of Kāla,<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कालेश्वर (˚ल-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">Page0225-a+ 80</a>]<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—कालोदक (˚ल-उद्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of a dark piece of water; N. of an ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालक|कालकं|कालकः
कालक, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-blue, coloured dark-blue;<BR>dark-coloured, black; (अस्), m. a mole, a freckle,<BR>a mark; the black part of the eye; a water-snake<BR>(अलगर्द); a kind of grain; N. of a Rakṣas;<BR>also of an Asura; N. of a mountain; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a Dānava family; (आ), f., Ved. a kind of bird;<BR>N. of a female evil spirit, mother of the Kālakeyas; a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa; also of Vaiśvānara; (अम्), n. the<BR>liver; N. of a plant.<BR>—कालक-वृक्षीय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a sage.<BR>—कालकाक्ष (˚क-अक्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of an Asura.<BR>—कालकाञ्ज (˚क-अञ्ज?), अस्, m. (?),<BR>Ved., N. of an animal (‘black-spotted?’); N. of a<BR>constellation (?); N. of an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकेय
कालकेय, अस्, m. (a metronymic fr. कालका), N. of<BR>an Asura; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a Dānava family; [cf.<BR>कालकञ्ज, कालकाञ्ज, 1. कालेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिक|कालिकं|कालिकः
1. कालिक, अस्, m. a species of heron, Ardea Jacu-<BR>lator (also written कालीक); N. of a king of the Nāgas;<BR>(इका), f. blackness or black colour; ink or blacking;<BR>cloudiness, a multitude or succession of clouds, a dark<BR>cloud threatening rain; a fault or flaw in gold; the<BR>liver; a particular blood-vessel in the ear; a line of<BR>hair extending from the pudenda to the navel; a kind<BR>of spirituous liquor; a female crow; a small singing<BR>bird with black wings (Turdus Macrourus, commonly<BR>Śyāmā); a scorpion; a small worm or animalcule<BR>formed by the fermentation of milk; N. of several<BR>plants, a medicinal plant, commonly Vṛścikapattra;<BR>another plant, Valeriana Jaṭāmāṃsi; a kind of Ter-<BR>minalia; a branch of the plant Trichosanthes Diœca;<BR>a kind of fragrant earth; a N. or form of Durgā;<BR>a girl of four years old, who personates the goddess<BR>Durgā at a festival held in honour of that deity; a<BR>kind of Yoginī; a species of Kinnarī; an epithet of<BR>Durgā; N. of a female evil spirit, daughter of Vai-<BR>śvānara; (with Jainas) N. of a kind of genius who<BR>executes the commands of the fourth Arhat; N. of<BR>a river; (अम्), n. black sandal-wood.<BR>—कालिका-<BR>क्रम, अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—कालिका-ग्रन्थ,<BR>अस्, m. a medical work.<BR>—कालिका-पुराण, अम्, n.<BR>the Purāṇa of Kālikā, i. e. of Durgā, title of an Upa-<BR>purāṇa.<BR>—कालिका-मुख, अस्, m., N. of a Rakṣas.<BR>—कालिकाश्रम (˚का-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a hermit-<BR>age.<BR>—कालिकोपपुराण (˚का-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>an Upa-purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिमन्
कालिमन्, आ, m. blackness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
1. कालिय, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga or serpent inhabit-<BR>ing the Yamunā, slain by Kṛṣṇa (also written कालीय,<BR>see below).<BR>—कालिय-दमन, अस्, or कालिय-जित्, m.,<BR>N. of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu as destroyer of the serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालियक
कालियक = कालीयक below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काली
काली, f., N. of Durgā, the wife of the god Śiva.<BR>—काली-कुल-सर्वस्व, N. of a work.<BR>—काली-त-<BR>नय, अस्, m. a buffalo (‘son or favourite of Durgā,’<BR>more correctly हंसकाली-तनय).<BR>—काली-पु-<BR>राण, अम्, n. the Purāṇa of Kālī, title of an Upa-<BR>purāṇa.<BR>—काली-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. = चण्डिका-मा-<BR>हात्म्य.<BR>—काली-रहस्य, title of a work.<BR>—काली-<BR>शिव, अस्, m., N. of the author of the Kalpa-kedāra.<BR>—काली-हृदय, title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीय|कालीयं
कालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to blackness; (अम्),<BR>n. a dark kind of sandal or perhaps of Agallochum;<BR>N. of a Nāga, see 1. कालिय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयक|कालीयकं|कालीयकः
कालीयक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a species of aloe wood;<BR>a kind of turmeric (Curcuma Xanthorrhiza?), a kind<BR>of fragrant wood of a yellow colour; yellow sandal;<BR>a dark kind of sandal-wood; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga,<BR>see 1. कालिय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेय|कालेयं|कालेयः
1. कालेय, अम्, n. (for 2. see s.v.), the liver;<BR>saffron; a yellow fragrant wood; the black sandal-<BR>wood; (अस्, आ, अम्), dark-coloured; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a family of Daityas (metronymic fr. काला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयक|कालेयकं|कालेयकः
कालेयक, अस्, m. the plant Curcuma Xanthorrhiza,<BR>see कालीयक above; (अम्), n. a fragrant wood, see<BR>above; a particular part of the intestines; a disease<BR>like jaundice; (अस्), m. a dog (for कौलेयक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्यक|काल्यकः
काल्यक, अस्, m. zedoary (Curcuma Zerumbet). See<BR>काल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल|कालं|कालः
काल 2. काल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. कल्), a fixed<BR>or right point of time, a space of time, time in general,<BR>(in the Ṛg-veda this word occurs only once, in the<BR>Brāhmaṇas oftener); the proper time or fit season for<BR>(with gen., dat., loc., pot., &c., e. g. कालः प्र-<BR>स्थानस्य or प्रस्थानाय or प्रस्थाने, time for<BR>departure; क्रिया-कालः, time for action; न अयं<BR>कालो विलम्बितुम्, this is not the time to delay;<BR>कालो यद् भुञ्जीत भवान्, it is time for you to<BR>eat); the weather; time as leading to events, the<BR>causes of which are imperceptible to the mind of<BR>man; destiny, fate; time as destroying all things;<BR>death, time of death, often personified and repre-<BR>sented with the attributes of Yama, regent of the<BR>dead, or even identified with him, (hence कालम् इ<BR>or कालं कृ, to die; काल-समायुक्त, dead; काल<BR>in this sense is frequently connected with अन्तक<BR>and मृत्यु, e. g. अभ्यधावत प्रजाः काल<BR>इवान्तकः, he attacked the people like Time the<BR>destroyer, cf. कालान्तक below; काल personified<BR>is also a Devarṣi in Indra's court, and a son of<BR>Dhruva); a period of time, time of the world;<BR>measure of time, prosody; a section, a part; देश-<BR>कालौ, the right place and the right time, place and<BR>time; कालं कृ, to appoint or fix a time; उभौ<BR>कालौ, both times, sunrise and sunset; षष्ठे<BR>काले ऽह्नः, at the sixth hour of the day, at midday;<BR>षष्ठान्न-काल, one who eats only at the sixth<BR>meal-time, i. e. who passes five meals without eating<BR>and has no meal till the evening of the third<BR>day; or without अन्न, e. g. चतुर्थ-कालम्, at the<BR>fourth meal-time, i. e. at the evening of the second<BR>day; षष्ठे काले, at the evening of the third day;<BR>ऋतु-काल, the time of a woman's courses; गच्छता<BR>कालेन, in the course of time, after some time;<BR>नित्य-कालम्, constantly, always; दीर्घ-कालम्, dur-<BR>ing a long time; दीर्घेण कालेण, after a long time;<BR>कालेन, in the course of time; दीर्घस्य कालस्य,<BR>after a long time; कस्यचित् कालस्य, after some<BR>time; कालात् or कालतस्, in the course of time &c.;<BR>[cf. Goth. hveila; Mod. Germ. weile; Gr. καιρός,<BR>ὥρα (?); Lat. hora, calen-dœ: cf. also Gr. κήρ<BR>Hib. ceal, ‘death and everything terrible.’]<BR>—काल-<BR>करण, अम्, n. appointing or fixing a time.<BR>—काल-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. death.<BR>—काल-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>like death, fatal, deadly.<BR>—काल-कार, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>making or producing time.<BR>—काल-कारित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>effected or brought about by or in time.<BR>—काल-<BR>कुण्ठ, अस्, m. an epithet of Yama.<BR>—काल-कूट,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a deadly poison; see s. v.<BR>—काल-कृत्,<BR>त्, m. the sun (producing the times, i. e. seasons).<BR>—काल-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by time; fixed;<BR>appointed (as to time); lent or deposited by a giver<BR>for a certain time; (अस्), m. the sun; time (?).<BR>—काल-<BR>कौमुदी, f., N. of a work.<BR>—काल-क्रम, अस्, m.<BR>lapse of time; काल-क्रमेण, in process of time.<BR>—काल-क्रिया, f. fixing a time; title of the second<BR>chapter of the Sūrya-Siddhānta; death.<BR>—काल-<BR>क्षेप, अस्, m. allowing time to pass away, delay,<BR>loss of time; spending or passing the time; अकाल-<BR>क्षेपम्, ind. without delay.<BR>—काल-गति, इस्, f. the<BR>lapse of time.<BR>—काल-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. ‘a joint of<BR>time,’ a year.<BR>—काल-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, killing in the<BR>course of time, i. e. by degrees, slowly (as a poison).<BR>—काल-चक्र, अम्, n. the wheel of time, time<BR>represented as a wheel, which always turns round; a<BR>given revolution of time, a cycle; according to the<BR>Jainas, the wheel of time has twelve Aras or spokes<BR>and turns round once in 2000, 000,000,000, 000<BR>Sāgaras of years [cf. अव-सर्पिणी and उत्-सर्पिणी];<BR>the wheel of fortune, the vicissitudes of life, the wheel<BR>of time or fate is sometimes regarded as a weapon;<BR>with Buddhists, a Tantra; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>the sun.<BR>—काल-चोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, summoned by<BR>the angel of death.<BR>—कालचोदित-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>acting under the influence of fate.<BR>—काल-ज्ञ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who knows the fixed times or seasons;<BR>(अस्), m. an astrologer; a cock.<BR>—काल-ज्ञान, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a medical work; N. of a work by Malla-<BR>deva on the symptoms of diseases; a medical work<BR>by Śambhūnātha.<BR>—काल-ज्ञानिन्, ई, m. an epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-c" target="_blank">Page0225-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—काल-तत्त्वार्णव (˚व-अर्˚), ‘the ocean<BR>of the truth of time,’ title of a work.<BR>—काल-तरङ्ग,<BR>the first part of the Smṛty-artha-sāgara by Nṛsiṃha.<BR>—काल-ता, f. seasonableness, timeliness.<BR>—काल-<BR>तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, like death, deadly.<BR>—काल-त्रय,<BR>अम्, n. the three times, i. e. past, present, and future.<BR>—काल-दण्ड, अस्, m. the staff of death, death.<BR>—काल-दमनी, f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—काल-<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. or काल-धर्मन्, आ, m. the line<BR>of conduct suitable to any time or season; the law,<BR>rule or operation of time, death, dying; influence of<BR>time, seasonableness; effects proper to the time or<BR>season.<BR>—काल-धारणा, f. prolongation of time.<BR> — 2. काल-नर, अस्, m. ‘a time-man,’ i. e. in astro-<BR>logy the figure of a man's body on the various limbs<BR>of which the twelve signs of the zodiac are distributed<BR>for the purpose of foretelling future destinies; [cf.<BR>काल-पुरुष.]<BR>—काल-नाथ, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—काल-निधि, इस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—काल-नियोग, अस्, m. the command of time, fate,<BR>destiny.<BR>—काल-निरूपण, अम्, n. chronology.<BR>—काल-निर्णय, अस्, m. ‘determination or fixing of<BR>times,’ title of a work, also called काल-माधवीय,<BR>by Mādhavācārya.<BR>—काल-निर्णय-दीपिका, f. title<BR>of a metrical recension of the same work.<BR>—काल-<BR>निर्णय-प्रकाश, अस्, m. title of a work on juris-<BR>prudence (?).<BR>—काल-निर्वाह, अस्, m. providing for<BR>daily wants.<BR>—काल-नेमि, इस्, f. the felly or rim of<BR>the wheel of time, regarded as a terrible weapon;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of an Asura slain by Kṛṣṇa, iden-<BR>tified with Kaṃsa; N. of a Rakṣas; N. of a son<BR>of the Brāhman Yajña-soma.<BR>—काल-नेमिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of an Asura; [cf. the preceding.]<BR>—कालनेमि-<BR>रिपु, उस्, m. or कालनेमि-हन्, आ, m. or कालनेमि-<BR>हर, अस्, m. or कालनेम्य्-अरि, इस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu, the destroyer of the Asura Kāla-<BR>nemi.<BR>—काल-पक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, ripened by time,<BR>i. e. spontaneously (opposed to अग्नि-पक्व).<BR>—काल-<BR>पथ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—काल-<BR>परिवास, अस्, m. standing for a time (so as to be-<BR>come stale or fermented).<BR>—काल-पाश, अस्, m. the<BR>noose of Yama or death.<BR>—काल-पाशिक, अस्, m. a<BR>hangman, an executioner, (one who has the noose of<BR>Yama.)<BR>—काल-पुरुष, अस्, m., cf. 2. काल-नर.<BR>—काल-प्रभात, अम्, n. the dawning of the best<BR>season, the two months following the rainy season,<BR>autumn; the sultry season.<BR>—काल-प्ररूढ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, over-blown, over-ripe.<BR>—काल-भक्ष, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—काल-भृत्, त्, m. the sun;<BR>[cf. काल-कृत्.]<BR>—काल-मयूख, अस्, m. title of a<BR>part of Bhāskara.<BR>—काल-महिमन्, आ, m. or काल-<BR>माहात्म्य, अम्, n. the power or sway of time.<BR>—काल-माधव-कारिका, f. title of a work.<BR>—काल-<BR>मूर्ति, इस्, f. time personified.<BR>—काल-याप, अस्, m.<BR>allowing time to pass away, putting off, delaying,<BR>procrastination.<BR>—काल-यापन, अम्, n. passing<BR>away time, putting off, delaying.<BR>—काल-योग, अस्,<BR>m. connection with time, with fate or destiny; fate,<BR>destiny.<BR>—काल-योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, reigning over des-<BR>tiny, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—काल-योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>fighting, or one who fights in season or at the proper<BR>time.<BR>—२. काल-रात्रि, इस् or ई, f. the night of all-destroy-<BR>ing time, the night of destruction at the end of the<BR>world, often personified or identified with Durgā or<BR>with one of the Śaktis of Durgā; a particular night<BR>in the life of man, on the seventh day of the seventh<BR>month of the seventy-seventh year, after which period<BR>a man is exempt from attention to the usual ordi-<BR>nances; N. of a Brāhman woman, familiar with magic.<BR>—काल-रूप-धृष्, क्, क्, क् (the last member of<BR>the compound being by some referred to rt. धृ or<BR>दृह्), wearing the form of Yama or death.<BR>—काल-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, connected with time.<BR>—काल-विक्र-<BR>म, अस्, m. power of time, death.<BR>—काल-विधान,<BR>अम्, n. title of a work.<BR>—काल-विधवंसन, अस्, m.<BR>(scil. रस) a term for a particular drug or medicine.<BR>—काल-विप्रकर्ष, अस्, m. prolongation of time.<BR>—काल-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a work by Jīmūta-<BR>vahana.<BR>—काल-वृद्धि, इस्, f. periodical interest,<BR>payable monthly, &c.<BR>—काल-वेग, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Nāga, a son of Vāsuki.<BR>—काल-व्यापिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">Page0226-a+ 80</a>]<BR>filling all time, everlasting.<BR>—काल-संरोध, अस्,<BR>m. keeping back or retaining for a long time; lapse<BR>of a long period of time.<BR>—काल-संहिता, f., N. of<BR>an astrological work.<BR>—काल-सदृश, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>opportune, seasonable; deathlike.<BR>—काल-सम्पन्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, effected by time, dated, bearing a date.<BR>—काल-साह्वय, अस्, आ, अम्, named after Kāla.<BR>—काल-सूत्र or काल-सूत्रक, अम्, n. the thread<BR>of time or death; N. of one of the twenty-one hells.<BR>—काल-स्वरूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having the very form<BR>of death (applied to any terrific object).<BR>—काला-<BR>कृष्ट (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, led to death or de-<BR>struction, drawn to or by one's fate; produced or<BR>brought about by time.<BR>—कालाक्षरिक, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>काल+अक्षर), a scholar, a pupil who has begun<BR>to read.<BR>—कालाग्नि (˚ल-अग्˚), इस्, m. the fire that is<BR>to destroy the world; the conflagration at the end of<BR>time.<BR>—कालाग्नि-रुद्र, अस्, m. Rudra regarded as<BR>the fire that is to destroy the world; (scil. रस) N.<BR>of a particular drug or medicine.<BR>—कालाग्निरुद्रो-<BR>पनिषद् (˚र-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of several Upaniṣads.<BR>—कालातीत (˚ल-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, elapsed, passed by.<BR>—कालात्मक (˚ल-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, depending on<BR>time or destiny.<BR>—कालात्यय (˚ल-अत्˚), अस्, m. lapse<BR>of time, loss or destruction by lapse of time.<BR>—का-<BR>लात्ययोपदिष्ट (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taught or<BR>rectified by the lapse of time; term for a vain argu-<BR>ment (हेत्व्-आभास), also called अतीत-काल and बा-<BR>धित.<BR>—कालादर्श (˚ल-आद्˚), अस्, m. ‘the mirror of<BR>time,’ title of a work.<BR>—कालाध्यक्ष (˚ल-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the overseer or leader of time, an epithet of<BR>the sun.<BR>—कालानल (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, m. the fire of<BR>all-destroying time, the universal conflagration at<BR>the end of all things; N. of a son of Sabhā-nara.<BR>—कालान्तक (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, m. time regarded as<BR>the god of death.<BR>—कालान्तक-यम, अस्, m. all-<BR>destroying time in the form of Yama.<BR>—कालान्तर<BR>(˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. interval, intermediate time; period,<BR>process of time; a former or another time.<BR>—कालान्-<BR>तर-क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, able to bear an interval<BR>of delay.<BR>—कालान्तर-विष, अस्, आ, अम्, poison-<BR>ous at certain times; (अस्), m. a poisonous animal,<BR>venomous only when enraged or alarmed, as a rat &c.<BR>—कालान्तरावृत्त (˚र-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hidden<BR>or concealed by time.<BR>—कालान्तरावृत्ति-शुभा-<BR>शुभ (˚भ-अश्˚), आनि, n. pl. good and evil things<BR>occurring within the revolutions of time.<BR>—काला-<BR>वधि (˚ल-अव्˚), इस्, m. a fixed or appointed time.<BR>—कालाव्यवाय (˚ल-अव्˚), अस्, m. no interval of<BR>time.<BR>—कालाशुद्धि, इस्, m. or कालाशौच (˚ल-अश्˚),<BR>अम्, n. season of mourning or ceremonial impurity,<BR>as at the birth of a child, the death of a relation &c.,<BR>when it is considered unlawful to perform any religious<BR>rites.<BR>—काले-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced at a<BR>fixed time or at due time.<BR>—कालोत्तर (˚ल-उत्˚), N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—कालोत्पादित (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pro-<BR>duced in due season.<BR>—कालोप्त (˚ल-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sown in due season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालय
कालय, nom. P. कालयति, -यितुम्, to show or<BR>announce the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिक|कालिकं|कालिकः
2. कालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to time, connected<BR>with time, depending on time; fit for any particular<BR>season, seasonable; lasting a long time, of long<BR>standing (often at the end of a compound, e. g.<BR>आसन्न-कालिक, relating to a time near at hand,<BR>impending; मास-कालिक, monthly); अ-कालिकम्,<BR>without delay; (आ), f. price of a commodity on credit,<BR>or a price to be paid at a fixed period or by instal-<BR>ments; periodical interest paid by the month &c.;<BR>change of complexion.<BR>—कालिक-ता, f. or कालिक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. time, date, season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिनी
कालिनी, f. ‘bringing death,’ N. of the sixth lunar<BR>mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
2. कालिय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to time. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीन
कालीन, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of comp.), belonging<BR>or relating to any particular time, timely, seasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीय|कालीयं
2. कालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to time, timely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्य|काल्यं
काल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, timely, seasonable, fit for any<BR>particular season; being in a particular period; plea-<BR>sant, agreeable, auspicious (as discourse; cf. कल्य);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">Page0226-b+ 69</a>]<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man; (आ), f. a cow fit for the<BR>bull; (अम्), n. day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकञ्ज|कालकंज
कालकञ्ज कालकञ्ज or कालकञ्ज्य, आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a Dānava family, the children of Kālakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकटङ्कट|कालकटंकट|कालकटङ्कटः
कालकटङ्कट कालकटङ्कट, अस्, m. an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva; (a various reading has शालकटङ्कट);<BR>[cf. कटङ्कट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकील|कालकीलः
कालकील कालकील or कालकीलक, अस्, m. a<BR>confused or mingled sound, a tumult; [cf. कलकल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकुञ्च|कालकुंचः|कालकुञ्चः
कालकुञ्च कालकुञ्च, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूट|कालकूटं|कालकूटः
कालकूट कालकूट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. कल-<BR>कूट), a kind of poison contained in a bulbous root<BR>or tuber; a mortal or deadly poison; a poison pro-<BR>duced at the churning of the ocean, swallowed by<BR>Śiva and causing the blueness of his neck; a poison in<BR>general; (अस्), m. myrrh; N. of a country near the<BR>Himālaya and the people inhabiting it; an epithet of<BR>Yama; [cf. काल-कुण्ठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूटक|कालकूटकः
कालकूटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of poison<BR>contained in a bulbous root; a deadly poison produced<BR>at the churning of the ocean; a poison in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूटि
कालकूटि, इस्, m. a prince of the Kalakūṭas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालङ्कत|कालङ्कतः
कालङ्कत कालङ्कत, अस्, m. the plant Cassia<BR>Sophora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालञ्जर|कालंजर|कालंजरः|कालञ्जरः
कालञ्जर कालञ्जर, अस्, m., N. of a mountain<BR>in Bundalkhand considered as sacred, the modern<BR>Kallinjer; N. of the adjacent country; an assembly<BR>or meeting-place of religious mendicants; Kallinjer<BR>is one of the places at which such assemblies meet,<BR>being enumerated amongst the Tapasyasthānas or<BR>spots adapted to practices of austere devotion; an<BR>epithet of Śiva; (आ or ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालबलन
कालबलन कालबलन, अम्, n. armour, mail;<BR>(a wrong reading for काय-बलन or काय-वलन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालबव
कालबव कालबव or कालवव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालबविन्
कालबविन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालम्बी
कालम्बी कालम्बी, f. or कालम्ब्य, अस् or<BR>अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of a caravansery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालव
कालव कालव, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवेय
कालवेय कालवेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशेय|कालशेयं
कालशेय कालशेय, अम्, n. (fr. कलशि = क-<BR>लश), buttermilk, produced in a jar or pitcher by<BR>churning; also कालसेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानर
कालानर कालानर, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Sabhā-nara; [cf. काल-नर and कालानल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुनादिन्
कालानुनादिन् कालानुनादिन्, ई, m. = कला-<BR>नुनादिन्, a large black bee; a sparrow, the francoline<BR>partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाप|कालापः
कालाप कालाप, अस्, m. (fr. कलाप), the<BR>hair of the head; a serpent's hood; a demon, an<BR>imp or goblin; a student of the Kalāpa grammar;<BR>one who knows or follows this grammar; (fr. कला-<BR>पिन्), a pupil of Kalāpin; epithet of Ārāḍa, a teacher<BR>of Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालापक|कालापकं
कालापक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to the pupils<BR>of Kalāpin; (अम्), n. an assemblage of pupils of<BR>Kalāpin; N. of a grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाम
कालाम कालाम, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Ārāḍa, the teacher of Śākya-muni; [cf. कालाप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालामुख
कालामुख कालामुख, अस्, m. (fr. काल-<BR>मुख?), N. of a Śaiva sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालायनि
कालायनि कालायनि, इस्, m., N. of a pupil<BR>of Bāṣkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालायनी
कालायनी कालायनी, f. (fr. कला), an epithet<BR>of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिक|कालिकं|कालिकः
कालिक कालिक. See under 1. काल and 2.<BR>काल at page 224 and last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्ग|कालिंग|कालिङ्गं|कालिङ्गः
कालिङ्ग कालिङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. कलिङ्ग), a<BR>prince of the Kaliṅgas; (pl.) the Kaliṅgas; an ele-<BR>phant; a snake; a species of cucumber, Cucumis<BR>Usitatissimus; a poisonous plant; a sort of iron;<BR>(ई), f. a princess of the Kaliṅgas; a kind of gourd or<BR>cucumber; N. of a river; (अम्), n. the water-melon;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), produced in or belonging to the Ka-<BR>liṅga country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्गक|कालिंगक
कालिङ्गक, अस्, m. a prince of the Kaliṅgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्गिका
कालिङ्गिका, f. the plant Ipomœa Turpethum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिञ्जर
कालिञ्जर कालिञ्जर, अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain; [cf. कालञ्जर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदास|कालिदासः
कालिदास कालिदास, अस्, m. (fr. काली, the<BR>goddess Durgā, and दास, a slave, the final of काली<BR>being shortened), N. of a celebrated poet, supposed<BR>to be the author of the Śakuntalā, Vikramorvaśī,<BR>Mālavikāgnimitra, the Megha-dūta, Raghu-vaṃśa,<BR>Nalodaya, and other poems; also of the Śruta-bodha;<BR>he was one of the nine poets or gems of Vikra-<BR>māditya's court, and is supposed to have flourished<BR>in the century preceding the Christian era; the name<BR>is however applied to more persons than one, and<BR>seems, in some measure, to have been used as an<BR>honorary title; the works attributed to this author<BR>are amongst the most elegant compositions in the<BR>Sanskrit language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदासक|कालिदासकः
कालिदासक, अस्, m. = the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिनी
कालिनी कालिनी. See under 2. काल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्द|कालिंद
कालिन्द कालिन्द, अम्, n. the water-melon;<BR>(ई), f. a sort of vessel; N. of a plant [cf. कालिङ्गिका];<BR>N. of a wife of Kṛṣṇa; N. of the wife of Asita<BR>and mother of Sagara; an epithet of the river Ya-<BR>munā; (अस्, ई, अम्), connected with the river Yamunā,<BR>coming from this river; [cf. कलिन्द.]<BR>—कालिन्दी-<BR>कर्षण, अस्, m. an epithet of Bala-rāma, this hero<BR>having diverted the stream Yamunā into a new and<BR>devious channel, marked out by his ploughshare.<BR>—कालिन्दी-भेदन, अस्, m. an epithet of Bala-rāma;<BR>[cf. the preceding.]<BR>—कालिन्दी-सू, ऊस्, m. the father<BR>of the Yamunā, an epithet of Sūrya; (ऊस्), f. the<BR>mother of Yamunā, an epithet of one of the wives<BR>of Sūrya.<BR>—कालिन्दी-सोदर, अस्, m. the brother of<BR>the Yamunā, an epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दक|कालिन्दकं
कालिन्दक, अम्, n. the water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिमन्
कालिमन् कालिमन्. See under 1. काल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिम्मन्या|कालिंमन्या
कालिम्मन्या कालिम्-मन्या, f. (कालिम् instead<BR>of कालीम्), thinking one's self to be Kālī, regarding<BR>one's self as Kālī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
कालिय 3. कालिय, अस्, m. (fr. कलि; for 1.<BR>and 2. see under 1. and 2. काल), the present age,<BR>commonly called the Kali-yuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीक|कालीकः
कालीक कालीक, अस्, m. a heron; [cf. 1.<BR>कालिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीची
कालीची कालीची, f. (fr. 2. काल and अञ्च्?), the<BR>judgment-hall of Yama, regent or judge of the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीन
कालीन कालीन. See under 2. काल, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीय|कालीयं
कालीय 1. कालीय. See p. 225 and col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालुष्य|कालुष्यं
कालुष्य कालुष्य, अम्, n. (fr. कलुष), foul-<BR>ness, dirtiness, filth, turbidness, opacity; disturbance<BR>or interruption of harmony, disagreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेज
कालेज काले-ज. See under 2. काल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेय|कालेयं|कालेयः
कालेय 2. कालेय, अम्, n. (fr. कलि; for 1. see<BR>under 1. काल), the Sāman of Kali; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>belonging to Kali, the Kali age &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयक|कालेयकं|कालेयकः
कालेयक कालेयक. See under 1. काल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेश्वर
कालेश्वर कालेश्वर, कालोत्पादित, &c. See<BR>under 1. and 2. काल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालोदायिन्
कालोदायिन् कालोदायिन् ई, m., N. of a pupil<BR>of Śākya-muni; (the right reading is perhaps कालो-<BR>दयिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्प|काल्पः
काल्प काल्प, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कल्प), preceptive,<BR>ritual; relating to a Kalpa or period so called; (अस्),<BR>m. the plant Curcuma Zerumbet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पक|काल्पकः
काल्पक, अस्, m. the same plant; [cf. also काल्-<BR>यक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पनिक|काल्पनिकः
काल्पनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कल्पना), existing<BR>only in fancy; fictitious, invented; counterfeit, hypo-<BR>critical, artificial, fabricated.<BR>—काल्पनिक-ता, f. con-<BR>trivance, hypocrisy, forgery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पसूत्र
काल्पसूत्र, अस्, m. (fr. कल्प-सूत्र), one who<BR>is familiar with the Kalpasūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्य|काल्यं
काल्य काल्य. See under 2. काल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्याणिनेय
काल्याणिनेय काल्याणिनेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कल्-<BR>याणी), sprung from a virtuous or fortunate woman;<BR>(अस्), m. the son of such a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्वालीकृत
काल्वालीकृत काल्वाली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>made bald (?); [cf. Lat. calvus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव
काव काव, अम्, n. (fr. कवि), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावचिक|कावचिकं
कावचिक कावचिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कवच),<BR>relating to armour, armorial; (अम्), n. a multitude<BR>of men in armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावट
कावट कावट, अम्, n., N. of a district con-<BR>taining 100 Grāmas; [cf. कर्वट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावटिका
कावटिका, f. a district of 200 Grāmas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावरुक
कावरुक कावरुक, अस्, ई, अम्, fearful; hen-<BR>pecked; (अस्), m. an owl; (a wrong form for काक-<BR>रुक or काकरूक ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावष
कावष कावष, अम्, n. (fr. कवष), N. of<BR>a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावषेय
कावषेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of Tura in the<BR>Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावार|कावारं
कावार कावार (का-आव्˚), अम्, n. the aquatic<BR>plant Vallisneria; (ई), f. an umbrella or chattar,<BR>especially one without a stick and worn like a broad-<BR>brimmed hat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काविराज्
काविराज् का-विराज्, ट्, f. a metre consisting<BR>of 9 + 12 + 9 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावृक|कावृकः
कावृक का-वृक, अस्, m., N. of several birds;<BR>a gallinaceous fowl (= कुक्कुट, कृकवाकु); the<BR>ruddy goose, Anas Casaca (= कोक); a small singing<BR>bird, Loxia Philippensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेर|कावेरं
कावेर कावेर, अम्, n. saffron, Crocus Sa-<BR>tivus; (ई), f. turmeric; a courtezan, a harlot; N. of<BR>a river in the Dekhan (according to a legend in the<BR>Hari-vaṃśa, a daughter of Yuvanāśva and wife of Jahnu,<BR>who by her father's curse was changed from one half<BR>of the Gaṅgā into the river Kāverī, therefore also<BR>called Ardha-gaṅgā or Ardha-jāhnavī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेरक
कावेरक, अस्, m. a patronymic of Rajata-nābhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेरिका
कावेरिका, f., N. of a river, = कावेरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य काव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कवि), endowed<BR>with the qualities of a sage or poet, descended or<BR>coming from a sage; prophetic, inspired, poetical; a<BR>particular order of manes; a patronymic of Uśanas; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of Kavi; (आ), f. understanding,<BR>intelligence; a female fiend [cf. पूतना]; (अम्), n.<BR>wisdom, intelligence; prophetic inspiration; high<BR>power and art; intellect, knowledge (often used in<BR>pl.); a poem, poetical composition, a work of poetic<BR>art; term for the first tetrastich in the metre Ṣaṭ-<BR>pada; happiness, welfare.<BR>—काव्य-कल्प-लता, f.<BR>title of a work on artificial poems.<BR>—काव्यकल्प-<BR>लता-वृत्ति, इस्, f. a commentary by Amara-candra on<BR>the last work.<BR>—काव्यकल्पलतावृत्ति-परिमल,<BR>a commentary on the preceding work.<BR>—काव्य-<BR>काम-धेनु, उस्, f. title of a commentary by Vopa-<BR>deva on his work called Kavi-kalpadruma.<BR>—काव्य-<BR>चन्द्रिका, f. title of a work on artificial poems by<BR>Kavi-candra; another work on the same subject by<BR>Nyāyavāgīśa.<BR>—काव्य-चौर, अस्, m. a robber of<BR>other poems, a plagiarist.<BR>—काव्य-ता, f. or काव्य-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the condition of a poetical composition.<BR>—काव्य-देवी, f., N. of a princess, who erected a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">Page0227-b+ 77</a>]<BR>statue of Śiva, called Kāvyadevīśvara.<BR>—काव्य-प्र-<BR>काश or काव्य-प्रदीप, अस्, m. title of a work on<BR>artificial poems by Mammaṭa.<BR>—काव्य-मीमांसक,<BR>अस्, m. a poetaster, a rhetorician.<BR>—काव्य-रसिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has a taste for poetical composi-<BR>tions.<BR>—काव्य-राक्षस, अम्, n. title of an artificial<BR>poem.<BR>—काव्य-शास्त्र, अम्, n. title of a small work<BR>on poetics.<BR>—काव्य-सुधा, f. title of a commentary<BR>on a work on artificial poems.<BR>—काव्य-हास्य, अम्,<BR>n. a farce.<BR>—काव्यादर्श (˚य-आद्˚), अस्, m. a work<BR>on poetics by Daṇḍin.<BR>—काव्यालङ्कार-वृत्ति, इस्,<BR>f. a work on poetics by Vāmana.<BR>—काव्याष्टक<BR>(˚य-अष्˚), अम्, n. title of a work of Sūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्
काश् काश्, cl. 1. and 4. A. काशते and<BR>काश्यते, चकाशे or काशामास, काशिष्-<BR>यते, अकाशिष्ट, काशितुम्, to be visible, appear;<BR>to shine, be brilliant, have an agreeable appearance:<BR>Caus. काशयति, -यितुम्: Desid. चिकाशिषते: Intens.<BR>चाकशीति and चाकाश्यते, to shine brightly; to see<BR>clearly, survey; [cf. कास्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
1. काश, अस्, m. the becoming visible, appearance;<BR>splendor; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a species of grass, Saccha-<BR>rum Spontaneum, used for mats, roofs, &c.; also<BR>personified, together with the Kuśa grass, as one of<BR>Yama's attendants; (अस्), m., N. of a man; a son of<BR>Sunahotra; also of another Sunahotra, the father of<BR>Kāśi-rāja.<BR>—काश-कृत्स्न, अस्, m., N. of a gram-<BR>marian; also of a philosopher.<BR>—काशकृत्स्नि, इस्,<BR>m. (a patronymic from the preceding), N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR>—काश-पौण्ड्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of a peo-<BR>ple.<BR>—काश-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of the grass<BR>Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशक|काशकः
काशक, अस्, m. a species of grass, Saccharum<BR>Spontaneum; N. of a man, = काश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
1. काशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of compounds)<BR>shining, appearing, having the semblance of any-<BR>thing, e. g. जित-काशिन्, one who appears as a con-<BR>queror or behaves like one; (ई), m., N. of a man,<BR>a son of Brahman Kavi (Mahā-bh. XIII. 4150).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिल
काशिल, अस्, आ, अम्, made of Kāśa grass, abounding<BR>in it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिष्णु
काशिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश 2. काश, अस्, m. (wrongly spelt for<BR>कास), cough, catarrh, irritation of the throat, sneez-<BR>ing.<BR>—काश-मर्द, अस्, m. wrongly spelt for कास-<BR>मर्द, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
2. काशिन्, ई, इनी, इ (wrongly spelt for कासिन्), having<BR>a cold or cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशपरी
काशपरी काशपरी, f., N. of a region (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशफरी
काशफरी, f., N. of a region (?); (a various<BR>reading has काशफारी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशब्द
काशब्द का-शब्द, अस्, m. the noise का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशाल्मलि|काशाल्मलिः
काशाल्मलि का-शाल्मलि, इस्, f. a kind of silk-<BR>cotton tree, Bombax Heptaphyllum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि काशि, इस्, m. the clenched hand, the<BR>fist; a handful; the sun (in this sense fr. rt. काश्);<BR>(अयस्), m. pl., N. of the people of Kāśi; N. of the an-<BR>cestors of the kings of Kāśi, of the family of Bharata;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a son of Suhotra and grandfather of<BR>Dhanvantari; also N. of a son of Kāśya and grandson<BR>of Suhotra; (अयस्), m. pl. the descendants of this man;<BR>(इस् or ई), f. a celebrated city and place of pilgrimage, the<BR>modern Benares; (ई), f., N. of the wife of Sudeva<BR>and mother of Supārśva.<BR>—काशि-कन्या, f. the virgin<BR>of Kāśi, daughter of the king of Kāśi.<BR>—काशि-<BR>खण्ड, a section of the Skanda-purāṇa.<BR>—काशि-<BR>नगर, अम्, n. the city of the Kāśis, i. e. Benares.<BR>—काशि-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of several men.<BR>—काशि-<BR>प, अस्, m. a sovereign of the Kāśis.<BR>—काशि-पति,<BR>इस्, m. the ruler of the Kāśis, epithet of Divodāsa<BR>Dhanvantari, a king of Benares, author of certain<BR>medical works and teacher of the Āyur-veda; he is<BR>often confounded with his celestial namesake, the<BR>physician of the gods.<BR>—काशि-पुरी, f. the city of the<BR>Kāśis, i. e. Benares.<BR>—काशि-राज, अस्, m. a king of<BR>the Kāśis, identified with the Dānava Dīrghajihva;<BR>epithet of Divodāsa Dhanvantari; also of a grand-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">Page0227-c+ 77</a>]<BR>father of Dhanvantari.<BR>—काशि-राजन्, आ, m. = the<BR>preceding.<BR>—काशि-राम, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of a commentary on the Tithi-tattva and several<BR>other works.<BR>—काशि-विलास or काशी-विलास, अस्, m.<BR>title of a work written in Sanskrit and in one of the<BR>modern dialects.<BR>—काशी-खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>title of a section of the Skanda-purāṇa, treating of<BR>Benares.<BR>—काशी-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘a lord or master of<BR>Benares;’ an epithet of Śiva; N. of several men.<BR>—काशी-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. a section of the Brahma-<BR>vaivarta-purāṇa.<BR>—काशी-राज, अस्, m. = काशि-राज, an<BR>epithet of Divodāsa.<BR>—काशी-विलास, अस्, m. = काशि-<BR>विलास.<BR>—काशीश (˚शी-ईश), अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva;<BR>an epithet of Divodāsa or any king of Benares; (अम्),<BR>n. sulphate of iron.<BR>—काशीश्वर (˚शि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>prince of the Kāśis or a sovereign of Benares; N. of<BR>a grammarian; काशीश्वरी, f. title of a grammar com-<BR>posed by Kaśīśvara (?); काशीश्वरी-गण, title of a trea-<BR>tise on grammar.<BR>—काशी-सेतु, उस्, m. title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिक
काशिक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आ), f., scil. पुरी,<BR>the city of the Kāśis, i. e. Benares; काशिका वृत्तिः<BR>or only काशिका, f. ‘the commentary composed or<BR>used in Kāśi or Benares,’ title of a commentary on<BR>Pāṇini's grammar by Vāmana Jayāditya.<BR>—काशिक-<BR>सूक्ष्म, अम्, n. fine cotton from Kāśi.<BR>—काशिका-<BR>तिलक, N. of a poem by Nīla-kaṇṭha.<BR>—काशिका-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. an epithet of king Divodāsa, who<BR>was king of Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशेय
काशेय, a patronymic from Kāśi; (ई), f. a<BR>daughter of the king of the Kāśis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्य|काश्यं
1. काश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the race or<BR>tribe of the Kāśis, a prince of Kāśi; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>the father of Kāśyapa and ancestor of Kāśirāja Dhan-<BR>vantari; also of a son of Suhotra, and of Senā-jit;<BR>(आ), f. the daughter of a king of Kāśi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यक
काश्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the race or<BR>tribe of the Kāśis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीत
काशीत काशीत, अम्, n., N. of a verse of the<BR>Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशूकार
काशूकार काशूकार, अस्, m. the Areca or<BR>betel-nut tree; (perhaps a wrong reading for कासू-<BR>कार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मरी
काश्मरी काश्मरी, f. or काश्मर्य, अस्, m.<BR>the plant Gmelina Arborea, commonly called Gam-<BR>bhārī; [cf. also कार्श्मरी and कार्ष्मर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीर|काश्मीरं|काश्मीरः
काश्मीर काश्मीर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कश्मीर),<BR>born in or coming from Kaśmīra; (अस्), m. a king<BR>of Kaśmīra; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of Kaśmīra;<BR>the country Kaśmīra, also in sing.; (आ), f. a sort<BR>of grape; (ई), f. the tree Ficus Elastica; (अम्), n.<BR>the tuberous root of the plant Costus Speciosus;<BR>saffron; (= टङ्क.) — काश्मीर-ज, अम्, n. saffron;<BR>a sort of drug; the tuberous root of the plant Costus<BR>Speciosus; (आ), f., N. of a plant, Atis or Betula,<BR>= अति-विषा.<BR>—काश्मीर-जन्मन्, अ, n. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरक
काश्मीरक, अस्, ई, अम्, born or produced in<BR>Kaśmīra, relating to Kaśmīra; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>inhabitants of Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरिक
काश्मीरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, born or produced in<BR>Kāśmīra; काश्मीरिक-निवास, अस्, m. the residence<BR>of the Kaśmīras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्य|काश्यं
काश्य 2. काश्य, अम्, n. = कश्य, a spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यप|काश्यपं|काश्यपः
काश्यप काश्यप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कश्यप),<BR>belonging to Kaśyapa, relating to or connected with<BR>him (e. g. काश्यपी देवी or only काश्यपी, the<BR>earth); (अस्), m. a patronymic from Kaśyapa; N. of<BR>an old grammarian; an epithet of Aruṇa; a sort of<BR>deer; a fish; (अम्), n. flesh; (ई), f. the earth;<BR>(according to a legend of the Purāṇas, Paraśu-rāma,<BR>after the destruction of the Kṣatriya race and the<BR>performance of an Aśva-medha sacrifice, presented the<BR>sovereignty of the world to Kāśyapa.)<BR>—काश्यप-<BR>नन्दन, आस्, m. pl. the children of Kāśyapa,<BR>epithet of the gods.<BR>—काश्यपी-बालाक्या-माठरी-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपि|काश्यपिः
काश्यपि, इस्, m. (a patronymic fr. काश्यप), an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">Page0228-a+ 79</a>]<BR>epithet of Aruṇa, the charioteer of the sun; also of<BR>Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपिन्
काश्यपिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a school called after<BR>Kāśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपीय
काश्यपीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Buddhist school<BR>called after Kāśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपेय|काश्यपेयः
काश्यपेय, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. कश्यप),<BR>an epithet of the twelve Ādityas; also of the sun;<BR>and of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्वरी
काश्वरी काश्वरी, f. the plant Gmelina Ar-<BR>borea, = काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष|काषं|काषः
काष काष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कष्), rubbing;<BR>that against which anything is rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषाय
काषाय काषाय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कषाय),<BR>red, dyed of a reddish colour; a red cloth or garment;<BR>(ई), f. (with मक्षिका) a sort of fly or wasp.<BR>—काषाय-ग्रहण, अस्, m., N. of a Caitya, q. v.<BR>—काषाय-वसन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a dark or<BR>brown garment.<BR>—काषाय-वासिक, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषायण
काषायण, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. कषाय or<BR>काषाय), N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषायिन्
काषायिन्, इणस्, m. pl., N. of a school called<BR>from Kaṣāya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठ|काष्ठं
काष्ठ काष्ठ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. काश्;<BR>cf. काष्ठा next col.), N. of one of Kuvera's attendants;<BR>(अम्), n. a piece of wood or timber, a stick; wood<BR>or timber in general; an instrument for measuring<BR>lengths; a kind of measure; (metaphorically) a mere<BR>stick, a lanky thin man. At the beginning of a<BR>compound and before a simple verb काष्ठ may<BR>express excellence or superiority; [cf. Cambro-Brit.<BR>coed; Brit. coat; Gr. ξύ-λον.]<BR>—काष्ठ-कदली,<BR>f. the wild plantain, Musa Sapientum, (the fruit of this<BR>plant being hard and woody.)<BR>—काष्ठ-कीट, अस्,<BR>m. a small insect or worm found in decayed wood.<BR>—काष्ठ-कुट्ट or काष्ठ-कूट, अस्, m. a bird,<BR>a sort of woodpecker, Picus Bengalensis.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>कुद्दाल, अस्, m. a kind of wooden shovel or scraper<BR>used for baling water out of a boat, or for scraping<BR>and cleaning its bottom; also written ˚कुदाल or<BR>˚कूद्दाल.<BR>—काष्ठ-खण्ड, अम्, n. a stick, a<BR>spar, a piece of wood.<BR>—काष्ठ-घटित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, formed of wood, wooden.<BR>—काष्ठ-जम्बू,<BR>ऊस्, f., N. of a tree, = भूमि-जम्बू.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>तक्ष्, ट्, m. or काष्ठ-तक्षक, अस्, m. a carpen-<BR>ter.<BR>—काष्ठ-तन्तु, उस्, m. a caterpillar which<BR>secretes itself in wood and there passes into a<BR>chrysalis; a small worm found in timber.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>दारु, उस्, m. the tree Pinus Deodora.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>द्रु, उस्, m. the tree Butea Frondosa.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>धात्री-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of the plant Emblica<BR>Officinalis.<BR>—काष्ठ-पाटला, f., N. of a plant<BR>(सित-पाटलिका).<BR>—काष्ठ-पाषाण-वासस्, आंसि,<BR>n. pl. wood, stone, and clothes.<BR>—काष्ठ-पुत्त-<BR>लिका, f. a wooden image.<BR>—काष्ठ-प्रदान, अम्,<BR>n. piling up wood, forming a funeral pile.<BR>—का-<BR>ष्ठ-भार, अस्, m. a particular weight of wood.<BR>—काष्ठभारिक, अस्, m. a wood-carrier; a bearer<BR>of wood.<BR>—काष्ठ-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>become wood, or who is like a piece of wood; epithet<BR>of an ascetic, who stands without stirring; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a divine being.<BR>—काष्ठ-भृत्, see under<BR>काष्ठा.<BR>—काष्ठ-मठी, f. a funeral pile.<BR>—का-<BR>ष्ठ-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of wood, wooden,<BR>consisting of pieces of wood.<BR>—काष्ठ-मल्ल, अस्,<BR>m. a bier, a plank &c. on which dead bodies are<BR>carried.<BR>—काष्ठ-रज्जु, उस्, m. or f. (?), a rope<BR>for binding together pieces of wood.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>लेखक, अस्, m. a small worm found in wood.<BR>—काष्ठ-लोहिन्, ई, m. a club, a short cudgel,<BR>especially if armed with iron.<BR>—काष्ठ-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having wood for fuel &c.; (वत्), ind. like<BR>a piece of wood, like a stick or stock, standing<BR>petrified with fear &c.<BR>—काष्ठ-वल्लिका, f., N. of<BR>a plant, = कटुका.<BR>—काष्ठ-वाट, अस् or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?), a wall made of wood; N. of a place (?).<BR>—काष्ठ-विवर, अम्, n. the hollow of a tree.<BR>—काष्ठ-शारिवा, f., N. of a plant, = शारिवा.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">Page0228-b+ 75</a>]<BR>—काष्ठ-स्तम्भ, अस्, m. a beam of wood.<BR>—का-<BR>ष्ठागार (˚ठ-अग्˚), अस् or अम्, m. or n. a house of<BR>wood, a wooden house or enclosure.<BR>—काष्ठाम्बु-<BR>वाहिनी (˚ठ-अम्˚), f. a wooden bucket or baling<BR>vessel; [cf. अम्बु-वाहिनी.]<BR>—काष्ठालुक (˚ठ-<BR>आल्˚), अस् or अम्, m. or n. a species of Āluka.<BR>—का-<BR>ष्ठेक्षु (˚ठ-इक्˚), उस्, m. a kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठक|काष्ठकं
काष्ठक, अम्, n. aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठिक|काष्ठिकः
काष्ठिक, अस्, m. a bearer of wood; (आ), f. a<BR>small piece of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठिन्
काष्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wooden; having wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठा
काष्ठा काष्ठा, f. [cf. काष्ठ last col.], a<BR>place for running, a race-ground, course; the course,<BR>path or track of the wind and clouds in the atmos-<BR>phere; a quarter or region of the world, a cardinal<BR>point, space, tract; water; the mark, the goal; limit,<BR>boundary; the sun; a fixed place, place, site, espe-<BR>cially the situation of the lunar mansions; a measure<BR>of time, = (1/30) Kalā, = (1/15) Laghu, = (1/225) Nāḍikā, = (1/450)<BR>Muhūrta; the plant Curcuma Xanthorrhiza; N. of a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa, mother of the<BR>solidungulous quadrupeds; N. of a town.<BR>—काष्ठ-<BR>भृत्, त्, त्, त् (for काष्ठा-भृत्), Ved. leading to a<BR>mark or aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठील|काष्ठीलः
काष्ठील काष्ठील (का-अष्˚), अस्, m. a large<BR>kind of Calotropis; (आ), f. a plantain, Musa Sapientum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास्
कास् 1. कास्, cl. 1. A. कासते, चकासे or<BR>कासामास, कासिष्यते, अकासिष्ट, कासि-<BR>तुम्, to cough; to make any disagreeable sound or<BR>one indicating disease; to shine (for rt. काश्, q. v.):<BR>Caus. कासयति, -यितुम्: Desid. चिकासिषते: Intens.<BR>चाकास्यते, चाकास्ति; [cf. Lith. kòstu, kòseti; Slav.<BR>kasµjljati; Old Germ. huosto; Scot. casad.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास्
2. कास्, f., Ved. cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
1. कास, अस्, आ, m. f. cough, catarrh.<BR>—कास-कन्द,<BR>अस्, m. a species of root, = कासालु.<BR>—कास-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, producing cough or catarrh.<BR>—कास-<BR>कुण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted with cough; (अस्), m.<BR>an epithet of Yama; [cf. काश.]<BR>—कास-घ्न, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, removing or alleviating cough, pectoral; (ई),<BR>f. a sort of prickly nightshade, Solanum Jacquini.<BR>—कास-जित्, त्, f. the plant Clerodendrum Sipho-<BR>nanthus.<BR>—कास-नाशिनी, f., N. of a thorny plant,<BR>= कर्कट-शृङ्गी.<BR>—कास-मर्द, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Cassia Sophora; a remedy against cough, an acid<BR>preparation, a mixture of tamarinds and mustard;<BR>also = पटल.<BR>—कास-मर्दक, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Cassia Sophora.<BR>—कास-मर्दन, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca.<BR>—कास-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having a cough.<BR>—कासारि (˚स-अरि), इस्, m. the plant<BR>Cassia Sophora.<BR>—कासालु (˚स-आलु), उस्, m. an escu-<BR>lent root, a sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासिका
कासिका, f. cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासिन्
कासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासुन्दीवटिका
कासुन्दीवटिका, f. a remedy against cough, an<BR>acid preparation, a mixture of tamarinds and mustard;<BR>(perhaps a wrong reading for कासन्दी˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
कास 2. कास, अस्, अम्, m. n. (for काश), a<BR>species of reed or long grass, Saccharum Spontaneum;<BR>another plant, Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासर|कासरः
कासर कासर, अस्, m. a buffalo; (fr. क,<BR>water, and सर, going ?; this animal being partial to<BR>marshy places.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासार|कासारं|कासारः
कासार कासार, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. कास्), a pond, a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासीराम
कासीराम कासीराम, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(more correctly काशी-राम?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासीस|कासीसं
कासीस कासीस, अम्, n. green vitriol, green<BR>sulphate of iron; [cf. काशीश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासू
कासू कासू, ऊस्, f. (fr. rt. कास् ?), a sort of<BR>spear or lance; indistinct speech; speech in general;<BR>light, lustre; disease; devotion; understanding.<BR>—कासू-तरी, f. a short spear, a javelin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासृति|कासृतिः
कासृति का-सृति, इस्, f. a by-way, a secret path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास्तीर
कास्तीर कास्तीर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहका
काहका काहका, f. a kind of musical instru-<BR>ment; [cf. काहला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहल|काहलं|काहलः
काहल काहल, अस्, आ, अम्, dry, withered;<BR>large, excessive; mischievous; (अस्), m. a cat; a<BR>cock; a sound in general; (आ), f. a kind of musical<BR>instrument; N. of an Apsaras; (ई), f. a young<BR>woman; (अम्), n. indistinct speech; a kind of musical<BR>instrument; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. a horn, either a cow-<BR>horn or an instrument of that shape; a large drum;<BR>(अम्), ind. much, excessively.<BR>—काहला-पुष्प,<BR>अस्, m. a thorn-apple, Datura Metel, = धूस्तूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहलिन्
काहलिन्, ई, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहलि|काहलिः
काहलि काहलि, इस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहाबाह
काहाबाह काहाबाह, अम्, n., Ved. a rumbling<BR>noise in the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काही
काही काही, f. the plant Wrightia Anti-<BR>dysenterica; [cf. कुटज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहूजी
काहूजी काहूजी, ईस्, m., N. of the father of the<BR>writer Mahādeva (author of an astronomical work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कि
कि 1. कि, a pronominal base, like क and<BR>कु, in the words किम्, कियत्, किस्, कीदृक्ष, कीदृश्,<BR>कीदृश, कीवत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कि
कि 2. कि, a verbal root; [cf. चि; Lat. scio?;<BR>Hib. ci, ‘see, behold;’ ci-thi, ‘you see;’ citear, ‘it<BR>seems, appears.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंस्त्य
किंस्त्य किंस्त्य, अम्, n. a kind of fruit (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकि|किकिः
किकि किकि, इस्, m. a blue jay; the cocoa<BR>tree, Nārikela; [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकिदिव
किकिदिव, अस्, m. or किकिदिवि, इस्, m. or किकिदीवि,<BR>इस्, m. a blue jay; Ved. another kind of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकिन्
किकिन्, ई, m. or किकी, f. a blue jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकीदिव|किकीदिवः
किकीदिव, अस्, m. or किकीदिवि or किकीदीवि, इस्, m.<BR>a blue jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकिरा
