किण्व|किण्वं|किण्वः
किण्व किण्व, अस्, अम्, m. n. ferment, a drug<BR>or seed used to produce fermentation in the manufac-<BR>ture of spirits from sugar, bassia, &c.; (अम्), n. sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्विन्
किण्विन् किण्विन्, ई, m. a horse; [cf. किन्-<BR>धिन्, किल्किन्, and किल्विन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कित्
