किन्दुविल्व
किन्दुविल्व किन्दुविल्व, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>or according to various readings किन्दुविल्ल, केन्दु-<BR>विल्ल, or तिन्दुविल्ल, N. of the place where Jaya-deva<BR>was born or where his family resided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्धिन्|किंधिन्
किन्धिन् किन्धिन्, ई, m. a horse; (a various<BR>reading for किल्किन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नु|किंनु
किन्नु किन्-नु, ind. See under किम् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किप्य
किप्य किप्य, अस्, m. a kind of worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
किम् किम्, ind. (originally nom. and acc. sing.<BR>n. of 2. क, q. v.), how? whence? wherefore? why?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
किम् is much used as a particle of interrogation like<BR>the Lat. num, an, sometimes translateable by ‘whe-<BR>ther?’ but oftener serving only like a note of interro-<BR>gation to mark a question (e. g. किं व्याधा वने<BR>ऽस्मिन् सञ्चरन्ति, do hunters roam about in this<BR>wood ? In an interrogation the verb if uncom-<BR>pounded with a preposition generally retains its accent<BR>after किम्). To this sense may be referred the किम्<BR>expressing blame, deficiency, &c., at the beginning<BR>of compounds (e. g. किं-राजन्, what sort of a king?<BR>i. e. a bad king); also the किम् prefixed to verbs<BR>with a similar meaning (e. g. किम्-अधीते, he reads<BR>badly). किम् — उत or किम् — उतवा or किम् —<BR>उत — उत or किम् — अथवा — उत, whether — or —<BR>or; [cf. उत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
किम् is very frequently connected with other parti-<BR>cles, as follows: किम् अङ्ग, wherefore then? अथ<BR>किम्, how else? surely; किम् अपि, somewhat, to a<BR>considerable extent, rather, much more, still further;<BR>किम् इति, why ? (see इति); किमु or किमुत, how<BR>much more ? how much less? किं किल, what a<BR>pity! (expressing dissatisfaction); किञ्च, moreover,<BR>further; किञ्-चन (originally negative = ‘in no way’),<BR>to a certain degree, a little; किञ्चित्, somewhat, a little;<BR>किं तर्हि, how then ? but, however; किन्तु, but,<BR>however, nevertheless (bearing the same relation to तु<BR>that किञ्च bears to च); किन्-नु, whether indeed? (a<BR>stronger interrogative than किम् alone); how much<BR>more? how much less? किन् नु खलु, how possibly?<BR>(a still stronger interrogative); किम् पुनर्, how<BR>much more ? how much less? किं वा, whether?<BR>or whether ? or, (often a mere particle of interroga-<BR>tion); किं स्वित्, whether ? how? (a mere particle of<BR>interrogation like the last).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंयु
किं-यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. what wishing?<BR>—किं-<BR>राजन्, आ, m. a bad king.<BR>—किं-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of what shape?<BR>—किं-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, poor, mean,<BR>insignificant.<BR>—किं-वदन्त, अस्, m., N. of an imp<BR>or goblin who lies in wait for children.<BR>—किं-<BR>वदन्ति, इस् or ई, f. (lit. what do they say?), the<BR>common saying or rumour, report, tradition, tale.<BR>—किं-वराटक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who says ‘what<BR>is a cowrie?’ i. e. an extravagant careless man who<BR>does not value small coins.<BR>—किं-विद्, त्, त्, त्, what<BR>knowing ?<BR>—किं-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of what power?<BR>—किं-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one who says ‘what is<BR>behaviour?’ i. e. one who is not careful in his man-<BR>ners.<BR>—किं-व्यापार, अस्, आ, अम्, following what<BR>occupation?<BR>—किं-शारु, उस्, उ, m. n. the beard of<BR>corn; (उस्), m. an arrow; a heron.<BR>—किं-शिल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. (land) having small stones or gravelly<BR>particles.<BR>—किं-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of what habits? in<BR>what manner generally existing or living?<BR>—किं-<BR>शुक, अस्, m. the tree Butea Frondosa, a tree bearing<BR>beautiful red blossoms, and hence often alluded to<BR>by poets; (अम्), n. the blossom of this tree; [cf.<BR>पलाश and सु-किंशुक.]<BR>—किंशुकोदक (˚क-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. a decoction made from the blossoms<BR>of the tree Butea Frondosa and used for colouring.<BR>—किं-शुलुक, अस्, m. a variety of the tree Butea<BR>Frondosa.<BR>—किंशुलुका-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—किं-सखि, आ, m. a bad friend.<BR>—किङ्-कर,<BR>अस्, m. a servant, a slave; (Ved.) a particular part of<BR>a carriage; a kind of Rākṣasa; N. of a people;<BR>(आ), f. a female servant; (ई), f. the wife of a servant.<BR>—किङ्कर-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of a servant<BR>or slave.<BR>—किङ्कर्तव्य-ता or किङ्कार्य-ता, f. any<BR>situation or circumstances in which one asks one's self<BR>what ought to be done ? [cf. इतिकर्तव्य-ता.]<BR>—किङ्-<BR>कल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—किङ्-काम्य, nom. P.<BR>-यति, to wish what ?<BR>—किङ्-काम्या, ind. (old inst.<BR>for -काम्यया), Ved. from a desire for what?<BR>—किङ्-<BR>कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, having what reason or cause?<BR>—किङ्-क्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, one who says ‘what is<BR>a moment ?’ i. e. a lazy fellow who does not value<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-c" target="_blank">Page0229-c+ 81</a>]<BR>moments.<BR>—किङ्-गोत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to what<BR>family ? — 2. किञ्-चन, see under 2. क and किम् above.<BR>—किञ्चन-ता, f. something, somewhat.<BR>—किञ्चिज्-<BR>ज्ञ (˚चित्-ज्ञ), अस्, आ, अम्, knowing a little, a mere<BR>smatterer.<BR>—किञ्चित्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, doing anything;<BR>(अ-किञ्चित्कर, one who has not done anything<BR>wrong.)<BR>—किञ्चित्-काल, अस्, m. a little-time, some time.<BR>—किञ्चित्-परे, ind. a little after.<BR>—किञ्चित्-प्राण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a little life left.<BR>—किञ्चिन्-मात्र, अम्,<BR>n. only a little.<BR>—किञ्-छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, conver-<BR>sant with which Veda ? (which Veda does he know?)<BR>—किञ्-जप्य, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—किञ्-ज्योतिस्,<BR>इस्, इस्, इस्, having which light?<BR>—किन्-तनु, उस्, m.<BR>an insect described as having eight legs and a very<BR>slender body, a species of spider.<BR>—किन्-तमाम्,<BR>ind. whether? whether of many ?<BR>—किन्-तराम्, ind.<BR>whether ? whether of two?<BR>—किन्तु-घ्न, अस्, m. one<BR>of the eleven periods called Karaṇa (destroying every<BR>‘but’).<BR>—किन्-त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. an adj. formed<BR>from किं त्वम्, ‘what thou?’ to denote the impu-<BR>dent manner in which a drunken man asks questions.<BR>—किन्-दत, अस्, m., N. of a sacred well.<BR>—किन्-<BR>दम, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—किन्-दर्भ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—किन्-दान, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—किन्-दास, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—किन्-देवत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having what deity ?<BR>—किन्-देवत्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to or devoted to what deity?<BR>—किन्-नर, अस्, m. (what sort of man?), a mythical<BR>being with a human figure and the head of a horse,<BR>originally perhaps a kind of monkey [cf. वा-नर],<BR>in later times (like the Naras) reckoned among the<BR>Gandharvas or celestial choristers and celebrated as<BR>musicians; also attached to the service of Kuvera;<BR>(with Jainas) one of the eight orders of the Vyantaras;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a prince; an epithet of Nara, a son<BR>of Vibhīṣaṇa; (with Jainas) the N. of the attendant<BR>of the fifteenth Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī; N.<BR>of a place; a kind of musical instrument; (ई), f. a<BR>female Kinnara; the lute of the Caṇḍāla.<BR>—किन्नर-<BR>वर्ष, अस्, m. a division of the earth said to be<BR>north of the Himālaya mountains.<BR>—किन्नरेश or<BR>किन्नरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Kuvera<BR>as lord of the Kinnaras.<BR>—किन्-नामधेय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or किन्-नामन्, आ, आ, अ, having what name?<BR>—किन्-निमित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having what cause or<BR>reason? (अम्), ind. from what cause ? for what<BR>reason? why? wherefore?<BR>—किम्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having what motives or aim ? (अम्), ind. from what<BR>motive? what for? wherefore? why?<BR>—किम्-आख्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having what name?<BR>—किमिच्छक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (fr. किम् + इच्छा), what one wishes or desires,<BR>anything desired.<BR>—किम्-पच, अस्, आ, अम्, cooking<BR>what? one who cooks nothing; miserly, avaricious.<BR>—किम्-पचान, अस्, आ, अम्, miserly, niggardly,<BR>avaricious; [cf. मितम्-पच.]<BR>—किम्-पराक्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of what power? of what energy?<BR>—किम्-<BR>पर्यन्तम्, ind. to what extent? how far? how<BR>long?<BR>—किम्-पाक, अस्, आ, अम्, unripe; ignorant;<BR>stupid; not arrived at mature age, childish; (अस्),<BR>m. a Cucurbitaceous plant, Trichosanthes Palmata;<BR>also Cucumis Colocynthus [cf. महा-काल]; (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of this plant.<BR>—किम्-पुना, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—किम्-पुरुष or किम्-पूरुष, अस्, m. a<BR>mongrel being (according to the Brāhmaṇas an evil<BR>being similar to man), perhaps originally a kind of<BR>monkey; in some instances the word seems to mean<BR>merely a low and despicable man; in later times<BR>the word is usually identified with किन्-नर, though<BR>sometimes applied to other beings, in which the<BR>figure of a man and that of an animal are combined,<BR>(these beings are supposed to live on Hemakūṭa, and<BR>are regarded as the attendants of Kuvera; with Jainas<BR>the Kimpuruṣas, like the Kinnaras, belong to the<BR>Vyantaras); N. of one of the nine sons of Āgnīdhra,<BR>having the Varṣa Kimpuruṣa as his hereditary por-<BR>tion; a division of the universe, one of the nine<BR>Khaṇḍas or portions into which the world is divided,<BR>and described as the country between the Himācala<BR>and Hemakūṭa mountains, also called किम्पुरुष-<BR>वर्ष.<BR>—किम्पुरुषेश्वर (˚ष-ईश्˚), अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—किम्-प्रकारम्, ind. in what<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">Page0230-a+ 77</a>]<BR>manner?<BR>—किम्-प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>what power?<BR>—किम्-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>what strength or power?<BR>—किम्-भरा (?), f. a kind<BR>of perfume, commonly called Nalī.<BR>—किम्-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being what? (अम्), ind. how? in what<BR>manner or degree? like what?<BR>—किम्-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, Ved. consisting of what?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमीय
किमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to whom<BR>or what?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमीदिन्
किमीदिन् किमीदिन्, ई, इनी, m. f., Ved., N. of<BR>a class of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियत्|कियन्त्
कियत् कियत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. 1. कि), how<BR>great? how large? how far? how much? of what extent?<BR>of what qualities? (Ved. loc. कियाति with following<BR>आ, how long ago? since what time? e. g. कियात्य् आ<BR>प्रथमः सर्ग आसाम्, how long is it since their first<BR>creation? कियत्य् अध्वनि, at what distance? how<BR>far off? कियद् एतद् with gen., of what importance<BR>is this to any one? तेन कियान् अर्थः, what profit<BR>arises from that? कियच् चिरेण, in how long a<BR>time? कियद् दूरे, how far?); little, small, unim-<BR>portant, of small value (often in compounds, e. g.<BR>कियद्-वक्र, a little bent; कियन्-मात्र, of little<BR>importance; कियद् अपि, how large or how far soever,<BR>&c.; यावत् कियच्च, how large or how much soever,<BR>of what qualities soever; (कियत्), ind. how far?<BR>how much? how? a little; कियत्-कालम्, how long?<BR>some little time ago.<BR>—कियद्-एतिका or कियद्-एहिका,<BR>f. effort, vigorous and persevering exertions according<BR>to one's strength.<BR>—कियद्-दूर, अस्, आ, अम्, for a<BR>short distance, a little way.<BR>—कियन्-मूल्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of what value? of what price?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियाम्बु
कियाम्बु कियाम्बु, उ, n., Ved. a kind of<BR>aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियाह|कियाहः
कियाह कियाह, अस्, m. a fox, a horse of<BR>a red or bay colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियेधा
कियेधा किये-धा, आस्, आस्, अम् (fr. कियद्-धा?),<BR>Ved. containing or surrounding much, epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर|किरः
किर किर, अस्, m. (fr. 1. कॄ), a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरक|किरकः
किरक, अस्, m. a scribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरण|किरणः
किरण, अस्, m. dust, very small dust; a rein (?);<BR>a ray or beam of light, a sun or moon-beam; the<BR>sun; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—किरण-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, radiant, bright, refulgent.<BR>—किरण-मालिन्, ई,<BR>m. the sun (having a garland of rays).<BR>—किरणावली<BR>(˚ण-अव्˚), f., N. of a work by Udayana; a commen-<BR>tary by Dādābhāi on the Sūrya-Siddhānta.<BR>—किर-<BR>णावली-प्रकाश, अस्, m. title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरत्
किरत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, scattering, spreading;<BR>lighting, shedding light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरि|किरिः
किरि, इस्, m. a hog, = किटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिक
किरिक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sparkling, beaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्याणी
किर्याणी, f. a wild hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरात|किरातः
किरात किरात, अस्, m., N. of a degraded<BR>mountain-tribe, one of the barbarous tribes who in-<BR>habit woods and mountains and live by hunting (the<BR>Kirrhadæ of Arrian), having become Śūdras by their<BR>neglect of all prescribed religious rites (they are also<BR>regarded as Mlecchas); a savage; a pigmy, a dwarf;<BR>a groom, a horseman; N. of a plant, a kind of gen-<BR>tian [cf. किरात-तिक्त]; N. of Śiva, as a moun-<BR>taineer opposed to Arjuna, the account of which is<BR>the subject of the celebrated poem by Bhāravi called<BR>Kirātārjunīya; (ई), f. a woman of the Kirāta tribe;<BR>a woman who carries a fly-flap or anything to keep off<BR>flies; an epithet of the goddess Durgā; a bawd, a<BR>procuress; an epithet of the river Gaṅgā; the celes-<BR>tial Gaṅgā or river of Svarga.<BR>—किरात-तिक्त, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Agathotes Chirayta, a kind of gentian;<BR>also किरात-तिक्तक.<BR>—किरातार्जुनीय, अम्, n. (fr.<BR>˚त + अर्जुन), title of an artificial poem by Bhā-<BR>ravi, describing the combat of Arjuna with the god<BR>Śiva in the form of a wild mountaineer or Kirāta,<BR>(this combat and its result is described in the Vana-<BR>parva or third book of the Mahā-bhārata 1538-1664.)<BR>—किराताशिन् (˚त-आश्˚), ई, m. an epithet of Garuḍa,<BR>the bird of Viṣṇu (‘swallowing the Kirātas’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातक|किरातकः
किरातक, अस्, m. (at the end of compounds) the<BR>warrior or mountain-tribe of the Kirātas; N. of a<BR>plant, = किरात-तिक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराति|किरातिः
किराति, इस्, f. an epithet of the river Gaṅgā; [cf.<BR>किराती.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातिनी
किरातिनी, f., N. of a plant, the Indian spikenard;<BR>[cf. जटामांसी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरारि
किरारि किरारि, इस्, m., N. of a people; (a<BR>various reading has विरारि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिकिच्चिका
किरिकिच्चिका किरिकिच्चिका, f. a kind of musi-<BR>cal instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिटि|किरिटिः
किरिटि किरिटि, n. the fruit of the marshy<BR>date tree, Phœnix Paludosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिश
किरिश किरिश, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीट|किरीटं|किरीटः
किरीट किरीट, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. 1. कॄ), a diadem, a crest, a garland or any<BR>ornament used as a crown, a tiara; N. of a metre of<BR>four lines, each containing twenty-four syllables.<BR>—कि-<BR>रीट-धारण, अम्, n. wearing a diadem, assuming<BR>the crown.<BR>—किरीट-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, crowned, hav-<BR>ing a tiara; (ई), m. a king.<BR>—किरीट-मालिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, ornamented with a diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटिन्
किरीटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, decorated with a diadem, crested,<BR>crowned; (ई), m. a king; an epithet of Indra; one<BR>of the attendants of Śiva; a N. of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरोडाट्य
किरोडाट्य किरोडाट्य, nom. P. किरोडाट्यति,<BR>to cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मिर|किर्म्मिर
किर्मिर किर्मिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. variegated;<BR>[cf. किर्मीर below and कर्बुर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मी|किर्म्मी
किर्मी किर्मी, f. a hall, a building, an apart-<BR>ment; an image of gold, a figure of iron; the Palāśa<BR>tree, Butea Frondosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीर|किर्मीरः|किर्म्मीर|किर्म्मीरः
किर्मीर किर्मीर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. कॄ), variegated; (अस्), m. a variegated colour;<BR>the orange tree; N. of a Rākṣasa or goblin conquered<BR>by Bhīma-sena; [cf. Gr. κιῤῥός]<BR>—किर्मीर-जित्, त्, m.<BR>or किर्मीर-निसूदन, अस्, m. or किर्मीर-भिद्, त्,<BR>m. or किर्मीर-सूदन, अस्, m. or किर्मीरारि (˚र-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. an epithet of Bhīma-sena, the enemy and con-<BR>queror of the Rākṣasa Kirmīra.<BR>—किर्मीर-त्वच्, क्,<BR>m. or f. (?), the orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्मीरित|किर्म्मीरित
किर्मीरित, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्याणी
किर्याणी किर्याणी. See under किर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्
किल् किल्, cl. 6. P. किलति, चिकेल, केलितुम्,<BR>to be or become white; to freeze; to<BR>play; cl. 10. P. केलयति, -यितुम्, to send, to throw<BR>or cast; [cf. Hib. cal, ‘a joke.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
1. किल, अस्, m. play, trifling.<BR>—किल-किञ्चित, अम्,<BR>n. amorous agitation, weeping, laughing, being angry,<BR>merry, &c., in the society of a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल 2. किल, ind. (a particle of asseveration<BR>or emphasis), indeed, verily, assuredly; (or of expla-<BR>nation) namely; किल is preceded by the word on<BR>which it lays stress, and occurs very rarely at the<BR>beginning of a sentence or verse; according to native<BR>lexicographers किल may be used in communicating<BR>intelligence, and may imply ‘so said,’ ‘so reported,’<BR>‘probably,’ ‘possibly,’ ‘agreement,’ ‘dislike,’ ‘false-<BR>hood,’ ‘inaccuracy,’ and ‘reason.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल 3. किल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिल|किलकिलः
किलकिल किलकिल, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of a town; (आ), f. (an onomatopoetic word),<BR>sounds or cries expressing joy or the expression of<BR>pleasure by any sound or cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिलाय
किलकिलाय, nom. P. किलकिलायति, to raise sounds<BR>expressing joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाट|किलाटः
किलाट किलाट, अस्, ई, m. f. inspissated milk,<BR>coagulated milk; it may also be applied to cheese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाटिन्
किलाटिन्, ई, m. a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलात|किलातः
किलात किलात, अस्, m., N. of an Asura; a<BR>dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलास|किलासं
किलास किलास, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. leprous;<BR>(ई), f., Ved. a kind of spotted deer described as the<BR>vehicle of the Maruts; (अम्), n., Ved. a white leprous<BR>spot; a blotch, a scab; (in medic.) a species of leprosy<BR>resembling the so-called white leprosy, in which<BR>disease the skin becomes spotted without producing<BR>ulcers.<BR>—किलास-घ्न, अस्, m. a sort of gourd, Mo-<BR>mordica Mixta (‘what removes leprosy’).<BR>—किलास-<BR>नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. removing leprosy.<BR>—कि-<BR>लास-भेषज, अम्, n., Ved. a remedy against leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासिन्
किलासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, leprous, having blotches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्च|किलिञ्चं
किलिञ्च किलिञ्च, अम्, n. a thin plank, a<BR>board; [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्ज|किलिंज|किलिंजं|किलिञ्जः
किलिञ्ज किलिञ्ज, अस्, m. a mat; a thin<BR>plank of green wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्जक|किलिंजकः|किलिञ्जकः
किलिञ्जक, अस्, m. a mat; a screen or twist of<BR>grass or straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिनकिल
किलिनकिल किलिनकिल, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), a various reading for किलकिल; N. of a town (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिम|किलिमं
किलिम किलिम, अस्, m. a tree, a kind of fir<BR>or pine, Pinus Deodar [cf. देव-दारु]; (अम्), n.<BR>resin, the extract of the pine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्किन्
किल्किन् किल्किन्, ई, m. a horse; (also read<BR>किन्धिन् and किल्विन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्बिष|किल्बिषः
किल्बिष किल्बिष or किल्विष, अम्, n. (fr. rt.<BR>किल्?), fault, offence, sin, guilt; injustice, injury;<BR>disease, sickness.<BR>—किल्विष-स्पृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. re-<BR>moving or avoiding sins or offences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विषिन्
किल्विषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who commits an offence,<BR>wicked, culpable, criminal, sinful, (often in compounds,<BR>e. g. राज-किल्विषिन्, one who as a king commits an<BR>offence.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विन्
किल्विन् किल्विन्, ई, m. a horse; [cf. किल्किन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशल|किशलं
किशल किशल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a sprout, a<BR>shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलय|किशलयं|किशलयः
किशलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. a young shoot.<BR>—किश-<BR>लय-तल्प, अस्, m. or किशलय-शय्या, f. or किश-<BR>लय-शयन, अम्, n. a bed of young leaves &c.;<BR>see किसल, किसलय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशोर|किशोरः
किशोर किशोर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr.<BR>किम् and rt. शॄ), young, infantine; (अस्), m. a colt,<BR>the young of any animal; the sun; Benjamin or<BR>Styrax benzoin (= तैल-पर्ण्य्-ओषधि); N. of a<BR>Dānava; a youth, a lad, one from his birth to the<BR>end of his fifteenth year, a minor in law (अजात-<BR>व्यवहार) becoming after his fifteenth year subject<BR>to suits at law (or जात-व्यवहार); (ई), f. a maiden,<BR>a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्क्
किष्क् किष्क्, cl. 10. A. किष्कयते, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to injure, kill; (a various reading<BR>for हिष्क् and हिक्क्); [cf. Hib. ceasaim, ‘I torment,<BR>crucify, vex.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध|किष्किंध|किष्किंधः|किष्किन्धः
किष्किन्ध किष्किन्ध, अस्, आ or ई, m. f., N. of<BR>a mountain in the south of India, in Oḍra, containing<BR>a cave, the residence of the monkey-prince Bālin.<BR>—किष्किन्ध-पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—किष्किन्धा-काण्ड, अम्, n. title of the fourth<BR>book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्धक
किष्किन्धक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्य|किष्किंध्य|किष्किंध्यः|किष्किन्ध्यः
किष्किन्ध्य, अस्, आ, m. f. (but generally f.), N.<BR>of a mountain and of a district = किष्किन्ध above,<BR>said to be in the peninsula, in the northern part<BR>of Mysore, near the sources of the Pampā river,<BR>the territory of Bālin the monkey-king, from whom<BR>it was conquered by Rāma and transferred to Su-<BR>grīva, the brother of Bāli and rightful king. The<BR>story is told in the fourth book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>The name किष्किन्ध्या is also applied to the capital<BR>city of the district, the mountain being called<BR>Ṛṣya-mūka.<BR>—किष्किन्ध्या-काण्ड, अस्, m. title<BR>of the fourth book of the Rāmāyaṇa; also of the<BR>Adhyātma-rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—किष्किन्ध्याधिप (˚य-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. a N. of Bālin, a monkey-king slain<BR>by Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कु|किष्कुः
किष्कु किष्कु, उस्, उस्, उ, vile, bad, con-<BR>temptible; (उस्), m. f. the fore-arm, a cubit, a span;<BR>an instrument for measuring lengths = हस्त or कर<BR>= twenty-four thumbs' breadths = (1/400) of a Nalva.<BR>—किष्कु-पर्वन्, आ, m., N. of several kinds of<BR>reed, as bamboo, sugar-cane, Arundo Tibialis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किस्
किस् किस्, ind., Ved. a particle of interro-<BR>gation, ‘whether, if;’ according to native commen-<BR>tators = कर्तृ, ‘a doer;’ [cf. नकिस्, माकिस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किस|किसं
किस किस, अस्, m., N. of an attendant of<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसर
किसर किसर, अम्, n. an article for sale (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसरिक
किसरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, selling Kisara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसल|किसलं|किसलः
किसल किसल or किसलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. a<BR>sprout or shoot, the extremity of a branch bearing<BR>new leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलयित
किसलयित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with leaf-buds<BR>or young shoots; [cf. किशल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकट|कीकटः
कीकट कीकट, अस्, m., N. of a people not<BR>belonging to the Āryan race; N. of a son of Ṛṣabha;<BR>also of Saṅkaṭa; N. of a country, Behar; a horse<BR>(originally perhaps a horse of the Kīkaṭas); (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), poor, needy; miserly, avaricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकर
कीकर कीकर, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a Grāma in the word कमल-कीकर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकस|कीकसं|कीकसः
कीकस कीकस, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कक्), hard, firm; (आस्), f. pl., Ved. the breast-bone<BR>and the cartilages of the ribs connected with it,<BR>cartilagines costarum; (अम्), n. a bone in general;<BR>(अस्), m. a bone, an insect.<BR>—कीकस-मुख or<BR>कीकसास्य (˚स-आस्˚), अस्, m. a bird in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकि|कीकिः
कीकि कीकि, इस्, m. a blue jay; [cf. किकि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचक|कीचकः
कीचक कीचक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>चीक्), a hollow bamboo; a bamboo whistling or rattling<BR>in the wind, Arundo Karka, a reed; a kind of tree;<BR>N. of a people, a tribe of the Kekayas, (a Kīcaka is<BR>chief of the army of king Virāṭa, and is conquered<BR>by Bhīma-sena); N. of a Daitya or demon; a certain<BR>Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>—कीचक-जित्, त्, or कीचक-<BR>निसूदन, अस्, or कीचक-भिद्, त्, m. an epithet of<BR>Bhīma-sena, conqueror of Kīcaka.<BR>—कीचक-बध,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the killing of Kīcaka,’ title of a poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीज|कीजः
कीज कीज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट्
कीट् कीट्, cl. 10. P. कीटयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>tinge or colour; to bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट|कीटः
कीट कीट, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. a worm, an<BR>insect; an expression of contempt, e. g. पक्षि-कीट,<BR>a miserable bird; [cf. Gr. κίς.]<BR>—कीट-घ्न, अस्, m.<BR>sulphur (‘destroying insects’).<BR>—कीट-ज, अम्, n.<BR>silk; (आ), f. lac, an animal dye of a red colour.<BR>—कीट-पक्षोद्भव (˚ष-उद्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>change from the chrysalis or larva to the butterfly.<BR>—कीट-पादिका, f. the plant Cissus Pedata.<BR>—कीट-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. a butterfly.<BR>—कीट-माता, f. the plant<BR>Cissus Pedata.<BR>—कीट-शत्रु, उस्, m. (?) and कीटारि<BR>(˚ट-अरि), इस्, m. (?) a species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटक|कीटकः
कीटक, अस्, m. a worm, an insect; a kind of bard<BR>(मागध-जाति), a panegyrist, descended from a<BR>Kṣatriya father and Vaiśya mother; N. of a prince;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), hard, harsh, unfeeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीडेर|कीडेरः
कीडेर कीडेर, अस्, m. the plant Amaranthus<BR>Polygamus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीदृक्ष
कीदृक्ष कीदृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. कि or किद्<BR>and दृक्ष, rt. दृश्, see ईदृक्ष), of what kind?<BR>of what sort? of what description? of what qualities?<BR>who or what like?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीदृश्
कीदृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. ङ्, of what kind? of what sort?<BR>&c., who or what like? यादृक्-कीदृक्-च, of what-<BR>soever kind or sort.<BR>—कीदृग्-व्यापारवत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, of what profession or vocation?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीदृश|कीदृशः
कीदृश, अस्, ई, अम्, of what kind? what like?<BR>[cf. Slav. ko-lik, Them. ko-liko; Gr. πη-λίκος;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">Page0231-b+ 74</a>]<BR>Goth. hvê-leiks, Them. hvê-leika; Mod. Germ.<BR>we-lcher; Lat. quâ-lis.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीन|कीनं
कीन कीन, अम्, n. flesh; [cf. कीर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीनार|कीनारः
कीनार कीनार, अस्, m., Ved. = कीनाश (?),<BR>a cultivator of the soil; (Sāy.) a vile man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीनाश|कीनाशः
कीनाश कीनाश, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>क्लिश्; according to others fr. किम् and नाश), a<BR>labourer or cultivator of the soil; the poverty of this<BR>class of men in India was proverbial, so that कीनाश<BR>meant sometimes ‘a very poor man;’ according to<BR>native lexicographers कीनाश may be an adj. and has<BR>the following meanings, cultivating the soil; poor;<BR>covetous, niggardly; small, little, killing animals or<BR>killing secretly; (अस्), m. a kind of monkey [cf.<BR>कीश]; an epithet of Yama; a kind of Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीम्
कीम् कीम्, ind. a particle in आकीम् and मा-<BR>कीम्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर|कीरं|कीरः
कीर कीर, अस्, m. a parrot; the country and<BR>(pl.) the people of Kāśmīra; (अम्), n. flesh; [cf.<BR>कीन.]<BR>—कीर-वर्णक, अम्, n. a kind of perfume<BR>(स्थौणेयक).<BR>—कीरेष्ट (˚र-इष्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of several plants; the tree Mangifera Indica; a species<BR>of mountain Pīlū Ākhoṭa; another plant, = जल-<BR>मधूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरक|कीरकः
कीरक कीरक, अस्, m. gaining, obtaining;<BR>a Buddha; a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरि|कीरिः
कीरि कीरि, इस्, m. (fr. 2. कृ), Ved. grateful<BR>or laudatory mention or remembrance; a poem, hymn,<BR>praise; one who praises, a poet.<BR>—कीरि-चोदन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. exciting praise, exciting the praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्ण|कीर्णः|कीर्ण्ण
कीर्ण कीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कॄ), scattered,<BR>thrown, cast; covered, secret, hidden; injured, hurt;<BR>full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्णि|कीर्णिः|कीर्ण्णि
कीर्णि, इस्, f. scattering, throwing; covering, con-<BR>cealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्य
कीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, what is scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्यमाण|कीर्य्यमाण
कीर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being covered, bestrewed;<BR>being scattered; being thrown at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तन|कीर्तनं|कीर्त्तन|कीर्त्तनं
कीर्तन, कीर्ति, &c. See under rt. कॄत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्मी|कीर्म्मी
कीर्मी कीर्मी, f. a house for straw (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्शा
कीर्शा कीर्शा, f., Ved. a species of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील्
कील् कील्, cl. 1. or 10. P. कीलति, कीलयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to bind; to fasten; to stake; to<BR>pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील|कीलः
कील, अस्, आ, m. f. a sharp piece of wood, a stake,<BR>a pin, a peg, a bolt, a wedge, &c.; a lance, a pike;<BR>a post, a post in a cow-house to which cows are fas-<BR>tened, a pillar; a weapon; the elbow; a blow or<BR>punch with the elbow; a blow, a thump; a blow in<BR>copulation; flame, lambent flame; a small or minute<BR>particle; a gnomon; a position of the fœtus impeding<BR>delivery; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कील-संस्पर्श, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a plant, commonly Gāva, = Diospyros Glu-<BR>tinosa, a plant, the fruit of which yields a substance<BR>like turpentine used to cover the bottom of boats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलक|कीलकः
कीलक, अस्, m. a pin, a bolt, a wedge; a splint<BR>for confining a broken bone; a fence; also = शिवक,<BR>a pillar for cows &c. to rub themselves against, or<BR>one to which they are tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलिका
कीलिका, f. the pin of an axle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलित|कीलितः
कीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, staked, impaled; set up as a<BR>stake or pole; pierced, transfixed; pinned, fastened<BR>by a stake &c.; bound, tied, confined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलाल|कीलालं|कीलालः
कीलाल कीलाल, अस्, m. a sweet beverage;<BR>also a heavenly drink similar to Amṛta, the food of<BR>the gods; honey; (अम्), n. blood; water.<BR>—कीलाल-<BR>ज, अम्, n. flesh.<BR>—कीलाल-धि, इस्, m. the ocean.<BR>—कीलाल-प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking blood; (अस्), m.<BR>a Rākṣasa, a sort of goblin or imp.<BR>—कीलाल-पा,<BR>आस्, m., Ved. an epithet of Agni, ‘drinking the beve-<BR>rage Kīlāla;’ (आस्), m. an attendant of Yama, or N.<BR>of one of the attendants of Yama.<BR>—कीलालोधन्<BR>(˚ल-ऊधन्), आ, ध्नी, अ, Ved. carrying the beverage<BR>Kīlāla in one's udder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीवत्|कीवन्त्
कीवत् कीवत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. 1. कि; cf. कियत्),<BR>Ved. how much? how long?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीश|कीशः
कीश कीश, अस्, आ, अम्, naked; (अस्, ई), m. f. an<BR>ape, a monkey; a bird; the sun.<BR>—कीश-पर्ण, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Achyranthes Aspera (अपामार्ग); [cf.<BR>केश-पर्णी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीस्त
कीस्त कीस्त, अस्, m., Ved. one who praises,<BR>a singer, a poet; (related to कीर्ति?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु 1. कु, a pronominal base appearing in<BR>कुतस्, कुत्र, कुविद्, कुह, क्व, and as a prefix im-<BR>plying deterioration, depreciation, deficiency, want,<BR>diminution, littleness, prevention, hindrance, reproach,<BR>contempt, sin, guilt; originally perhaps कु signified<BR>how (strange!); (as a separate word कु occurs in the<BR>Vedas in the sense of ‘where?’ कु चिद्, wherever,<BR>anywhere); [cf. कु-कथा, कु-कर, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु 2. कु, उस्, f. the earth; the ground or<BR>base of a triangle or other plane figure.<BR>—कु-कील,<BR>अस्, m. a mountain (‘a pin or bolt of the earth’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु 3. कु, cl. 2. P. or cl. 1. A., Ved. कौति<BR>or कवीति, कवते, चुकाव, चुकुवे, कोतुम् or<BR>कवीतुम् (?), to sound; to sound indistinctly; to cry,<BR>moan, groan; to cry as a bird, to coo, hum as a bee<BR>&c.: Caus. कावयति: Desid. चुकूषति, -ते: Intens.<BR>चोकूयते and कोकूयते, to cry aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु 4. कु or कू, cl. 6. A. कुवते, चुकुवे,<BR>कुतुम् or कुवितुम्: Intens. चोकूयते, to cry,<BR>make a noise; to moan or groan; [cf. Hib. caoi,<BR>caoidh, ‘lamentation, mourning;’ caoidhim, ‘I la-<BR>ment, mourn, grieve.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंश्
कुंश् कुंश् or कुंस्, cl. 1. or 10. P. कुंशति,<BR>कुंशयति, or कुंसति, कुंसयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to speak; to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्
कुक् कुक्, cl. 1. A. कोकते, चुकुके, कोकितुम्,<BR>to take, accept, seize: Desid. चुकोकिषते<BR>or चुकुकिषते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक
कुक, अस्, आ, अम्, taking, accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकथा
कुकथा कु-कथा, f. a bad, miserable tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकभ|कुकभं
कुकभ कुकभ, अम्, n. a kind of spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर|कुकरः
कुकर कु-कर, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु) , having<BR>a crooked or withered arm; acting wickedly, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर्मन्|कुकर्म्मन्
कुकर्मन् कु-कर्मन्, अ, n. (see 1. कु), a<BR>wicked deed; wickedness, depravity, villainy; (आ, आ,<BR>अ), performing evil actions, wicked, depraved.<BR>—कु-<BR>कर्म-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wicked, depraved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकार्य
कु-कार्य, अम्, n. a bad action, sin, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकीर्त्ति|कुकीर्ति
कुकीर्त्ति कु-कीर्त्ति, इस्, f. (see 1. कु), ill-re-<BR>pute, notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुट|कुकुटः
कुकुट कुकुट, अस्, m., N. of a pot-herb, =<BR>सितावर, commonly सुषणिशाक, Marsilea Quadri-<BR>folia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुटुम्बिनी
कुकुटुम्बिनी कु-कुटुम्बिनी, f. a bad house-<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुद|कुकुदः
कुकुद कुकुद, अस्, m. one who gives away<BR>a girl in marriage after decoration with fit ornaments<BR>and the prescribed ceremonies; also कूकुद, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुन्दर|कुकुंदर|कुकुन्दरं|कुकुंदरः|कुकुन्दरः
कुकुन्दर कुकुन्दर or कुकुन्दुर, अम्, n.,<BR>or ए, du. n. the cavities of the loins just above the<BR>hips [cf. ककुन्दर]; (अस्), m., N. of a plant, =<BR>कुक्कुर-द्रु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुन्ध
कुकुन्ध कुकुन्ध, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>kind of evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुभा
कुकुभा कुकुभा, f. one of the female per-<BR>sonifications of music or Rāgiṇīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुर|कुकुरः
कुकुर कुकुर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कुक्),<BR>a dog; N. of a plant and perfume, = ग्रन्थि-पर्णी;<BR>N. of a prince, a son of Andhaka; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">Page0232-a+ 73</a>]<BR>descendants of this prince; N. of a people, a branch<BR>of the Yadu race or Yādavas; the country of this<BR>people; [cf. कुक्कुर and कौकुर.]<BR>—कुकुर-<BR>जिह्वा, f. a species of fish, Acheiris Kookor Zibha;<BR>the plant Leea Staphylea; another plant, Ixora<BR>Undulata.<BR>—कुकुराधिनाथ (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>lord of the Yādavas, an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूटी
कुकूटी कुकूटी, f. the plant Salmalia Mala-<BR>barica; [cf. शाल्मलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूणक
कुकूणक कुकूणक, अस्, m. a kind of disease<BR>of the eyes in infants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूनन
कुकूनन कुकूनन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (an<BR>onomatopoetic word), gargling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूरभ
कुकूरभ कुकूरभ, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूल|कुकूलं|कुकूलः
कुकूल कुकूल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. chaff,<BR>conflagration of chaff, a fire made of chaff; (अम्), n.<BR>a hole filled with stakes; armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकृत्य
कुकृत्य कु-कृत्य, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), an evil<BR>deed, evil, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकोल|कुकोलं
कुकोल कुकोल, अम्, n. the jujube, Zizyphus<BR>Jujuba; [cf. कोलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुट|कुक्कुटः
कुक्कुट कुक्कुट, अस्, m. a cock, a wild cock;<BR>a whisp of lighted straw or grass, a firebrand, a spark<BR>of fire; the offspring of a Niṣāda by a Śūdra woman<BR>or woman of the fourth caste; (इस् or ई), f. hypocrisy,<BR>interested observance of religious duties; (ई), f. a<BR>hen; a small house-lizard; the silk-cotton tree,<BR>Bombax Heptaphyllum, or the red cotton tree, Sal-<BR>malia Malabarica.<BR>—कुक्कुट-कन्थ, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a town.<BR>—कुक्कुट-ध्वनि, इस्, m. the crowing of<BR>a cock, the cackling of fowls.<BR>—कुक्कुट-पक्षक,<BR>अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), a knife shaped like the<BR>wing of a cock.<BR>—कुक्कुट-पाद, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain (cock-foot).<BR>—कुक्कुट-मण्डप, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a sanctuary in Benares standing on the<BR>right side of a statue of Śiva, a place where final<BR>emancipation may be attained; [cf. मुक्ति-मण्ड-<BR>प.]<BR>—कुक्कुट-मस्तक, अस्, m. a sort of pepper,<BR>Piper Chaba.<BR>—कुक्कुट-व्रत, अम्, n. a religious<BR>observance (worship of Śiva) on the seventh of the<BR>light fortnight of the month Bhādra, by women,<BR>especially for the sake of obtaining offspring.<BR>—कुक्-<BR>कुट-शिख, अस्, m. safflower, Carthamus Tinctorius<BR>(cockscomb).<BR>—कुक्कुटा-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—कुक्कुटाण्ड (˚ट-अण्˚), अम्, n. a fowl's egg.<BR>—कुक्कुटाण्डक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), a<BR>species of rice.<BR>—कुक्कुटाभ (˚ट-आभा), अस्, m. a<BR>kind of snake compared to a fowl (perhaps from<BR>having a crest or comb).<BR>—कुक्कुटाराम (˚ट-आर्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a grove; N. of a celebrated hermitage<BR>near Gayā.<BR>—कुक्कुटार्म (˚ट-अर्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of a place.<BR>—कुक्कुटासन (˚ट-आस्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>particular posture of an ascetic in religious medita-<BR>tion.<BR>—कुक्कुटाहि (˚ट-अहि), इस्, m. = कुक्कुटाभ<BR>above.<BR>—कुक्कुटी-व्रत, अम्, n. a ceremony in<BR>honour of Śiva and Durgā; see कुक्कुट-व्रत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटक|कुक्कुटकः
कुक्कुटक, अस्, m. a cock, a wild cock; a man of<BR>a mixed caste, one sprung from a Śūdra and a Niṣāda<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुभ|कुक्कुभः
कुक्कुभ कुक्कुभ, अस्, m. a wild cock, Pha-<BR>sianus Gallus; varnish, oily gloss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुर|कुक्कुरं|कुक्कुरः
कुक्कुर कुक्कुर, अस्, m. (a more modern form<BR>for कुकुर), a dog; N. of a Muni; also of a prince,<BR>a son of Andhaka; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (ई),<BR>f. a bitch; (अम्), n. a vegetable perfume; [cf.<BR>ग्रन्थि-पर्ण.]<BR>—कुक्कुर-द्रु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant, = ताम्र-चूड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुवाच्
कुक्कुवाच् कुक्कु-वाच्, क्, m. (fr. कुक्कु, an<BR>onomatopoetic word, and वाच्), a kind of deer, =<BR>सारङ्ग-मृग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्रिया
कुक्रिया कु-क्रिया, f. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>action; (अस्, आ, अम्), wicked, sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्ष|कुक्षः
कुक्ष कुक्ष, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कुष्),<BR>the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षि|कुक्षिः
कुक्षि, इस्, m. the belly, the cavity of the abdomen<BR>(in the earlier language generally used in dual); the<BR>interior of anything; the womb, the part of the belly<BR>containing the fœtus; a cavity in general (e. g. अद्रि-<BR>कुक्षि, cavity of a mountain); the cavity of the<BR>ocean, i. e. a bay, a gulf; a cavern; N. of a son (f.<BR>also of a daughter?) of Priya-vrata and Kāmyā; N.<BR>of Bali; of a king; of a son of Ikṣvāku and father<BR>of Vikukṣi; N. of a region; according to a native<BR>lexicographer कुक्षि means also the sheath of a<BR>sword, and steel; [cf. Lat. coxa, coxendix; Gr.<BR>κοχώνη? Old Germ. bûh; Mod. Germ. Bauch.]<BR>—कुक्षिम्-भरि, इस्, इस्, इ, one who nourishes only<BR>his belly, filling or pampering the belly, voracious,<BR>gluttonous.<BR>—कुक्षि-रन्ध्र, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>reed.<BR>—कुक्षि-शूल, अस्, m. pain in the belly, belly-<BR>ache, colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिल
कुक्षिल, अस्, m., Ved. a species of evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षितकि
कुक्षितकि कुक्षितकि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षेयु
कुक्षेयु कुक्षेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Raudrāśva; (according to others कक्षेयु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुखाटि
कुखाटि कुखाटि, इस्, f. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>खट्), wantonness, dalliance, frolic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुख्याति
कुख्याति कु-ख्याति, इस्, f. (see 1. कु), evil<BR>report, infamy; a bad reputation, disrepute, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुगणिन्
कुगणिन् कुगणिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. 1. कु + गण),<BR>belonging to an evil set of people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुगो
