कुचुमार
कुचुमार कुचुमार, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Aupaniṣadādhikaraṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचेल|कुचेलः
कुचेल कु-चेल, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>garment; (अस्, आ, अम्), badly clothed, dressed in<BR>dirty or tattered garments; (आ), f., N. of a plant,<BR>= अविकर्णी or विद्धपर्णी; (ई), f., N. of a plant,<BR>= अम्बष्ठा, commonly Ākanādi, Cissampelos<BR>Hexandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचेष्टा
कुचेष्टा कु-चेष्टा, f. (see 1. कु), an evil de-<BR>sign, a wicked contrivance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच्छ|कुच्छं
कुच्छ कुच्छ, अम्, n. the white water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्
कुज् कुज्, cl. 1. P. कोजति, कोजितुम्, to steal;<BR>cl. 6. P. कुजति, to be crooked; [cf. कुञ्ज्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज|कुजः
कुज कु-ज, अस्, m. (fr. 2. कु and rt. जन्), a<BR>tree; the son of the earth, a N. of the planet Mars;<BR>N. of a Daitya, also called Naraka, conquered by<BR>Kṛṣṇa; (आ), f. the daughter of the earth, an epithet<BR>of the goddess Durgā; also of Sītā.<BR>—कुज-पञ्-<BR>चमी, f. the fifth day of the moon occurring on a<BR>Tuesday or the day of Mars, by some thought unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजन
कुजन कु-जन, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad or<BR>wicked man, a low, mean or vulgar person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजननी
कुजननी कु-जननी, f. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजन्मन्
कुजन्मन् कु-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ (see 1. कु),<BR>low-born, of inferior origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजम्भ
कुजम्भ कु-जम्भ, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), N. of<BR>a Daitya, a younger brother of Jambha and son of<BR>Prahrāda or Prahlāda, a son of Hiraṇya-kaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजम्भल|कुजंभलः|कुजम्भलः
कुजम्भल कुजम्भल, अस्, m. a thief who<BR>breaks into a house; also कुजम्भिर and कुजम्-<BR>भिल; [cf. कुम्भिल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्जिश|कुज्जिशः
कुज्जिश कुज्जिश or कुज्झिश, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of fish; [cf. कुडिश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्झटि|कुज्झटिः
कुज्झटि कुज्झटि, इस् or ई, or कुज्झटिका, f. a<BR>fog or mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्च्|कुंच्
कुञ्च् कुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. कुञ्चति, चुकुञ्च,<BR>कुञ्चितुम्, to make crooked; to be<BR>crooked; to bend or curve, to move crookedly; to<BR>go; to go to or towards; to be or become small;<BR>to lessen, to make small; to shrink, to contract, to<BR>draw together: Caus. कुञ्चयति, -यितुम्: Desid.<BR>चुकुञ्चिषति: Intens. चोकुच्यते; [cf. Hib. cuach-<BR>aim, ‘I fold, plait;’ cuach, ‘a curl;’ cuachach,<BR>‘curled, frizzled.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चन|कुंचन|कुंचनं|कुञ्चनं
कुञ्चन, अम्, n. curving, bending, contracting;<BR>contraction; a certain disease of the eyes, contracting<BR>the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चफला
कुञ्च-फला, f. a kind of gourd, = कुष्माण्डी;<BR>(a wrong reading for कुच-फल?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चि|कुंचि|कुंचिः|कुञ्चिः
कुञ्चि, इस्, f. a measure of capacity equal to eight<BR>handfuls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चिका|कुंचिका
कुञ्चिका, f. a key; a fish, commonly Kuñciya, in<BR>shape like an eel and eaten as one, Unibranchapertura<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">Page0233-a+ 78</a>]<BR>Cuchiya, or the fish Muræna Apterygia, Synbrache<BR>[cf. कुचिक]; a plant bearing a red and black seed<BR>used as a weight, Abrus Precatorius; or another<BR>plant bearing a pungent seed, Nigella Indica; a sort<BR>of reed; the branch or shoot of a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चित|कुंचित|कुञ्चितं
कुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, curved, bent, con-<BR>tracted, &c.; (अम्), n., N. of a plant.<BR>—कुञ्चिताङ्-<BR>गुलि (˚त-अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, with bent or curved fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्ज्|कुंज्
कुञ्ज् कुञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. कुञ्जति, -जितुम्, to<BR>murmur, = कूज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्ज|कुंज|कुंजं|कुंजः|कुञ्जः
कुञ्ज कुञ्ज, अस्, अम्, m. n. a place overrun<BR>with plants or overgrown with creepers, a bower, an<BR>arbour; a cave; the lower jaw; an elephant's tusk<BR>or jaw; a tooth; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—कुञ्ज-<BR>कुटीर, अस्, m. a bower, an arbour.<BR>—कुञ्ज-वल्लरी,<BR>f., N. of a plant, = निकुञ्जिकाम्ला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जिका
कुञ्जिका, f. another N. of the plant Kuñja-vallarī;<BR>fennel-flower seed, = कुञ्चिका, Nigella Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जर|कुंजर|कुंजरः|कुञ्जरः
कुञ्जर कुञ्जर, अस्, m. (fr. कुञ्ज ?), an ele-<BR>phant; anything pre-eminent in its kind (generally<BR>in compounds, e. g. पुरुष-कुञ्जर, an eminent<BR>man); the tree Ficus Religiosa; N. of a Nāga; N.<BR>of a prince of the Sauvīraka race; N. of a mountain;<BR>of a region; hair; (आ and ई), f. a female elephant;<BR>(आ), f. the plant Bignonia Suaveolens; another plant,<BR>Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—कुञ्जर-कर, अस्, m. an<BR>elephant's trunk.<BR>—कुञ्जर-क्षार-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>a kind of radish (मूलक).<BR>—कुञ्जर-ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m. an elephant-catcher.<BR>—कुञ्जर-दरी, f. ‘ele-<BR>phant's cave,’ N. of a place.<BR>—कुञ्जर-पिप्पली, f.,<BR>N. of a plant described as bearing a fruit resembling<BR>long pepper; [cf. गज-पिप्पली.]<BR>—कुञ्जर-रूपिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, elephant-shaped.<BR>—कुञ्जरानीक (˚र-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the division of an army consisting of ele-<BR>phants, an elephant-corps.<BR>—कुञ्जराराति (˚र-अर्˚),<BR>इस्, m. a lion; the Śarabha, a fabulous animal with<BR>eight legs, (‘enemy of the elephant.’)<BR>—कुञ्जरा-<BR>लुक (˚र-आल्˚), अम्, n. a species of esculent root, a<BR>sort of yam.<BR>—कुञ्जराशन (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>holy fig tree, Ficus Religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जल|कुंजलं|कुञ्जलं
कुञ्जल कुञ्जल, अम्, n. sour gruel; [cf.<BR>काञ्जिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्
कुट् कुट्, cl. 6. P. कुटति, चुकोट, कुटि-<BR>ष्यति, अकुटीत्, कुटितुम्, to be or become<BR>crooked or curved; to bend, curve, curl; to make<BR>crooked; to be dishonest, cheat or deceive; cl. 4. P.<BR>कुट्यति, or cl. 10. A. कोटयते, -यितुम्, to break<BR>to pieces, tear asunder, divide; to speak indistinctly;<BR>to be warm, burn: Caus. कोटयति: Desid. चुकुटि-<BR>षति: Intens. चोकुट्यते; [cf. कुट्ट् and कुण्ट्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट|कुटं|कुटः
कुट, अस् or अम्, m. n. a water-pot, a jar, pitcher;<BR>(अस्), m. a fort, a stronghold; a house [cf. कुटि,<BR>कुटी, and कूट]; a hammer, a mallet for breaking<BR>small stones; a tree; a mountain; N. of a man;<BR>(अम्), n., Ved. = कृत, a work.<BR>—कुट-कारिका, f.<BR>a female servant (bringing the water-jar).<BR>—कुट-ज,<BR>अस्, m. the medicinal tree Wrightia Antidysenterica,<BR>commonly called Karaya; the seeds are used as a<BR>vermifuge [cf. इन्द्र-यव]; a N. of the sage<BR>Agastya (‘born in a water-jar’); also of Droṇa,<BR>q. v.<BR>—कुटज-मल्ली, f. a kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटक|कुटकं|कुटकः
कुटक, अस्, m., N. of a people; N. of a moun-<BR>tain; the post round which the string of the churning-<BR>stick winds [cf. कुटर and कुठर]; (अम्), n. a<BR>plough without a pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटि|कुटिः
कुटि, इस्, ई, m. f. a curvature, a curve; a hut,<BR>cottage, house, hall, shop; (ई), f. a vessel with<BR>openings used for fumigations; a bawd, a procuress<BR>or go-between; a nosegay, a bundle or tuft of flowers<BR>or vegetables; a kind of perfume, commonly Murā;<BR>spirituous liquor; (इस्), m. the body; a tree; [cf.<BR>Eng. hut; Germ. Hütte.]<BR>—कुटि-चर, अस्, m. a<BR>crocodile or porpoise.<BR>—कुटि-पार्थिव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—कुटी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, curved, curled,<BR>twisted, frizzled; (अम्), n. anything (as woollen cloth)<BR>curled or twisted.<BR>—कुटी-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, inside the<BR>house.<BR>—कुटी-गु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कुटी-<BR>चक, अस्, m. a kind of religious mendicant, one<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">Page0233-b+ 72</a>]<BR>who lives at his son's expense; (lit. ‘delighting in<BR>staying in the house.’)<BR>—कुटी-चर, अस्, m. an<BR>ascetic of a particular order, one who consigns the<BR>care of his family to his son and remains at home en-<BR>gaged solely in devotion; or one who goes begging<BR>from one house to another.<BR>—कुटी-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of a house (?).<BR>—कुटी-मुख, अस्, m., N.<BR>of one of the attendants of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिक
कुटिक, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, crooked; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटित|कुटितं
कुटित, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटितृ
कुटितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, making crooked; acting<BR>dishonestly; being bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिर|कुटिरं
कुटिर, अम्, n. a hut, a cottage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिल|कुटिलं
कुटिल, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, crooked, curved, round,<BR>running in curved lines, crisped, curled; going<BR>crookedly, tortuous; insincere, dishonest, fraudu-<BR>lent; (आ), f., N. of a plant [cf. तगरपादी]; N. of<BR>a river; (according to some) N. of the Sarasvatī;<BR>N. of a metre containing four lines of fourteen sylla-<BR>bles each; (अम्), n., N. of a plant [cf. तगर,<BR>कुञ्चित, वक्र]; a kind of perfume; tin.<BR>—कुटिल-<BR>गति, इस्, f. a species of the Atijagatī metre, = चन्-<BR>द्रिका.<BR>—कुटिल-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going crookedly,<BR>tortuous.<BR>—कुटिल-ता, f. or कुटिल-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>crookedness; guile, dishonesty.<BR>—कुटिल-पक्ष्म,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having curved eyelashes or brows.<BR>—कुटिल-स्वभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked-minded,<BR>disingenuous.<BR>—कुटिलाशय (˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ill-intentioned, malevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलक
कुटिलक, अस्, इका, अम्, bent, curved, crooked,<BR>winding; (इका), f. crouching, coming stealthily as a<BR>hunter on his prey; a peculiar movement or gesture<BR>(in theatrical language); an instrument used by a<BR>blacksmith, a blacksmith's forge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीका
कुटीका, f. a small house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीय
कुटीय, nom. P. कुटीयति, -यितुम्, to imagine<BR>one's self in a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीर|कुटीरं|कुटीरः
कुटीर, अस् or अम्, m. n. a small house, a hut, a<BR>hovel; a kind of plant; (अम्), n. sexual intercourse;<BR>exclusiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीरक|कुटीरकः
कुटीरक, अस्, m. a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्क|कुटंक|कुटंकः|कुटङ्कः
कुटङ्क कुटङ्क, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>कुट above), a roof, a thatch; [cf. कुटुङ्गक,<BR>कुडङ्ग, कुण्डङ्ग, कुटल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्ग
कुटङ्ग कुटङ्ग, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्गक|कुटंगक|कुटंगकः|कुटङ्गकः
कुटङ्गक कुटङ्गक, अस्, m. an arbour formed<BR>by creeping plants overrunning a tree; a roof or<BR>thatch; a house, a small house, a hut or cottage;<BR>[cf. कुटुङ्गक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0233-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटच|कुटचः
