कुण्ड|कुंड|कुंडं|कुण्डं|कुंडः|कुण्डः
कुण्ड कुण्ड, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. कुण्), a bowl-shaped vessel, a basin, bowl, pitcher,<BR>jar, pot, water-pot; (अम्), n. a particular measure;<BR>a clump, e. g. दर्भ-कुण्डम्, a clump of Darbha<BR>grass; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a round hole in the ground,<BR>a hole in the ground for receiving and preserving<BR>water; a hole in general (e. g. in comp. अग्नि-कुण्ड,<BR>a hole in the ground for receiving and preserving<BR>consecrated fire); a pit, a vat; a pool, a well, a spring<BR>or basin of water, especially consecrated to some holy<BR>purpose or person; (अस्), m. a son born in adultery,<BR>an adulterine, the son of a woman by another man<BR>than her husband, while the husband is alive; N. of<BR>a Nāga; a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; an epithet of Śiva;<BR>(आ), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—कुण्ड-कीट, अस्, m.<BR>the son of a woman of the Brāhmanical tribe born in<BR>adultery with a man of an inferior caste; a keeper of<BR>concubines, a man who has female slaves; a follower<BR>of the Cārvāka doctrine or the tenets of those who<BR>deny the authority of the Vedas.<BR>—कुण्ड-कील, अस्,<BR>m. a low, a vile man; see नागर.<BR>—कुण्ड-कौ-<BR>मुदी or कुण्ड-मण्डप-कौमुदी, f. title of a<BR>work by Viśvanātha.<BR>—कुण्ड-गोल, अस्, m. and<BR>कुण्ड-गोलक, अम्, n. sour rice, gruel; see काञ्जिक.<BR>—कुण्ड-ज, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कुण्ड-जठर, अस्, m., N. of an old sage; [cf.<BR>कुण्डोदर.]<BR>—कुण्ड-धार, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Nāga; also of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कुण्ड-<BR>पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, drinking out of pitchers; कुण्ड-<BR>पायिनाम् अयनम्, a particular religious ceremony<BR>[cf. कौण्डपायिन].<BR>—कुण्ड-पाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(scil. क्रतु, &c.), a particular ceremony or sacrifice<BR>at which ewers or pitchers are used for drinking;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man (?).<BR>—कुण्ड-प्रस्थ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—कुण्ड-भेदिन्, ई, m., N. of a son<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कुण्ड-मण्डप-सिद्धि, इस्, f.,<BR>N. of a work by Viṭṭhaladīkṣita.<BR>—कुण्ड-रत्ना-<BR>कर, अस्, m., N. of a work by Viśvanātha.<BR>—कुण्ड-<BR>शायिन्, ई, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कुण्-<BR>डाग्नि (˚ड-अग्˚), इस् or इ (?), m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>place; [cf. कौण्डाग्नक.]<BR>—कुण्डाशिन् (˚ड-आश्˚),<BR>ई, इनी, इ, one who is supported by a bastard; (ई), m.<BR>a pander, a pimp; N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; also<BR>of a Nāga; also of one of the attendants of Śiva.<BR>—कुण्डोद (˚ड-उद), अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—कुण्डोदर (˚ड-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Nāga; a<BR>son of Janamejaya and brother of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;<BR>also a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—कुण्डोद्द्योत-दर्-<BR>शन, N. of a work by Śaṅkara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—कुण्डोध्नी<BR>(˚ड-ऊध्˚), f. a cow with a full udder; a woman with<BR>a full bosom; [cf. ऊधस्.]<BR>—कुण्डोपधानीयक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (fr. ˚ड + उपधानीय), one who uses a<BR>pitcher as a pillow; an epithet of Pūrṇa; according<BR>to others कुण्डोपधान is the N. of a place.<BR>—कुण्डोपरथ, cf. कौण्डोपरथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0234-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डक|कुण्डकः
कुण्डक, अम्, n. a pot; (अस्), m., N. of a son<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; also of Kṣudraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0234-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिक
कुण्डिक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;<BR>(आ), f. a pitcher; a student's water-pot, the Kamandalu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0234-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिन्|कुंडिन्
कुण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with a pitcher or<BR>water-jar; (ई), m. a horse [cf. किन्धिन् &c.]; a bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0234-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिन|कुंडिन|कुंडिनं|कुण्डिनं|कुण्डिनः
कुण्डिन, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;<BR>N. of an author; (अम्), n. a city, the capital of the<BR>district Vidarbha, ruled over by Bhīma, the father-<BR>in-law of Nala, apparently the modern Kondavir in<BR>Berar; (according to some the city is also called<BR>Vidarbha, or m. pl. Vidarbhās, but this is rather the<BR>name of the territory.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डङ्ग|कुण्डङ्गः
कुण्डङ्ग कुण्डङ्ग, अस्, m. a bower, an ar-<BR>bour; (a wrong reading for कुडङ्ग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डल|कुंडल|कुंडलं|कुण्डलं|कुंडलः|कुण्डलः
कुण्डल कुण्डल, अम्, n. a ring, an ear-ring;<BR>a bracelet; a fetter, a tie, a collar; the coil of a rope;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Nāga; (आ), f., N. of a woman;<BR>N. of a river; (ई), f., N. of several plants, mountain<BR>ebony, Bauhinia Variegata [cf. काञ्चन-द्रु]; an-<BR>other plant, Cocculus Cordifolius [cf. गुडूची]; another<BR>plant, Mucuna Pruritus [cf. कपि-कच्छु]; N. of two<BR>other plants, commonly called Sarpiṇī-vṛkṣa and<BR>Kundalī-cālana.<BR>—कुण्डल-धारण, अम्, n. the<BR>wearing of ear-rings.<BR>—कुण्डल-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>wearing ear-rings.<BR>—कुण्डलाकार (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, shaped like an ear-ring or bracelet, circular,<BR>annular.<BR>—कुण्डलोद्द्योतितानन (˚ल-उद्द्योतित-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having his face radiant with glitter-<BR>ing pendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलना|कुंडलना
कुण्डलना, f. (fr. कुण्डलय, nom. fr. कुण्डल),<BR>encircling a word or the circle round any word which<BR>is to be left out in a MS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलिका
कुण्डलिका, f., N. of a metre in Prākṛt poetry;<BR>[cf. वात-कुण्डलिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलिन्|कुंडलिन्
कुण्डलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having ear-rings or decorated<BR>with ear-rings; circular, annular, spiral, winding, coil-<BR>ing; (ई), m. a snake; the spotted or painted deer; a<BR>peacock; an epithet of Varuṇa, and of Śiva; (इनी), f.<BR>the plant Cocculus Cordifolius [cf. गुडूची]; a parti-<BR>cular dish, curds boiled with ghee and spices; a Śakti<BR>or form of Durgā worshipped by the Tantrikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलीकृत|कुंडलीकृत
कुण्डली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, forming a ring, formed<BR>into a circle, coiled, curled, moving in rings or circles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलीभूत
कुण्डली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, formed into a ring,<BR>coiled, curled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डीर|कुंडीर|कुण्डीरः
कुण्डीर कुण्डीर, अस्, आ, अम्, strong, power-<BR>ful, able; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डृणाची
कुण्डृणाची कुण्डृणाची, f., Ved. a species of<BR>animal; (Sāy.) tortuous progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्
कुत् कुत् (a Sautra root, or one found in<BR>grammatical Sūtras only), to spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत|कुतः
कुत कुत, अस्, m., N. of one of the eighteen<BR>attendants of the sun, identified with the god of the<BR>ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतनय
कुतनय कु-तनय, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a de-<BR>generate son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतनु|कुतनुः
कुतनु कु-तनु, उस्, वी, उ (see 1. कु), de-<BR>formed; (उस्), m. an epithet of Kuvera or Kubera<BR>(this deity being of a monstrous appearance, having<BR>three legs and but eight teeth; see कुबेर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतप|कुतपः
कुतप कु-तप, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), slightly<BR>hot, mild, tepid; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a sort of blanket<BR>made of the hair of the mountain-goat; the eighth<BR>Muhūrta or portion of the day from the last<BR>Daṇḍa of the second watch to the first of the third<BR>or about noon; an eligible time for the performance<BR>of sacrifices to the manes; a kind of sacrificial grass,<BR>Poa Cynosuroides; grain; a daughter's son; a<BR>sister's son; a twice-born man, one of the first three<BR>classes; a Brāhman; a guest; the sun; fire; an<BR>ox; a musical instrument.<BR>—कुतप-सप्तक, अम्,<BR>n. a Śrāddha in which seven constituents occur, viz.<BR>noon, a horn platter, a Nepal blanket, silver, sacrificial<BR>grass, Sesamum, and Kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतपस्विन्
कुतपस्विन् कु-तपस्विन्, ई, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>wicked or bad ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतर्क|कुतर्कः
कुतर्क कु-तर्क, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), falla-<BR>cious argument, sophistry, fallacy, sophism.<BR>—कु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">Page0235-b+ 73</a>]<BR>तर्क-पथ, अस्, m. the way of sophists, i. e. a<BR>sophistical method of arguing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्
कुतस् कुतस्, ind. (fr. 1. कु), from where?<BR>whence? from whence? whereto? where? in which<BR>direction? wherefore? why? from what cause or<BR>motive? because; how? in what manner? in which<BR>way? how much less? much less. कुतस् is used<BR>sometimes for the abl. case of 2. क = कस्मात् (e. g.<BR>कुतः कालात्, since what time?). In अ-कुतस्, which<BR>occurs at the beginning of some compounds, कुतस्<BR>has an indefinite sense (e. g. अकुतो-मृत्यु, not<BR>fearing death from any quarter; cf. अकुतो-भय);<BR>कुतस् is also indefinite when connected with the<BR>particles अपि, चिद्, and चन (e. g. कुतो ऽपि, from<BR>any quarter, from any cause; कुतश्चिद्, from any<BR>one, from anywhere; अकुतश्चिद्-भय, not fearing<BR>danger from any quarter, not presenting danger on any<BR>side; कुतश् चन, (in Ved.) from no side, to no side;<BR>यतः कुतश्चिद्, from any person soever).<BR>—कुतस्-<BR>तराम्, ind. how? in what manner?<BR>—कुतो-नि-<BR>मित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having what cause or reason?<BR>—कुतो-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having what origin?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्त्य
कुतस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, whence come? how hap-<BR>pened?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतापस
कुतापस कु-तापस, अस्, ई, m. f. (see 1. कु),<BR>a wicked ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतित्तिरि
कुतित्तिरि कु-तित्तिरि, इस्, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>species of bird resembling the partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतीपाद
कुतीपाद कुतीपाद, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>Ṛṣis or poets of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतीर्थ
कुतीर्थ कु-तीर्थ, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुक|कुतुकं
कुतुक कुतुक, अम्, n. eagerness, vehe-<BR>mence; desire, inclination; curiosity; [cf. कौतुक<BR>and कुतूहल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुप|कुतुपं|कुतुपः
कुतुप कुतुप, अस्, m. a small leathern oil-<BR>bottle [cf. कुतू]; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the eighth Mu-<BR>hūrta or portion of the day from the last Daṇḍa of<BR>the second watch to the first of the third or about<BR>noon; an eligible time for the performance of sacri-<BR>fices to the manes; [cf. कु-तप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतू
कुतू, ऊस्, f. a leathern oil-bottle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूणक|कुतूणकः
कुतूणक कुतूणक, अस्, m. weakness of the<BR>eyes, a disease of the eyes in infants; [cf. कुकू-<BR>णक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल कुतूहल, अम्, n. (fr. the interroga-<BR>tive adv. कुतस् and हल, calling out?), curiosity,<BR>interest in any extraordinary matter; desire, in-<BR>clination; eagerness, vehemence, impetuosity; what<BR>excites curiosity or interest, anything interesting,<BR>fun; (अस्, आ, अम्), surprising, wonderful; excellent,<BR>best, praised, celebrated; [cf. कौतूहल.]<BR>—कुतू-<BR>हल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, curious, taking an interest in<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहलिन्
कुतूहलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, curious, highly interested in<BR>any extraordinary matter, inquisitive; eager, im-<BR>patient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतृण|कुतृणं
कुतृण कु-तृण, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), an<BR>aquatic plant, water house-leek, Pistia Stratiotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्थ
कुत्थ कुत्थ, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the<BR>fifteenth Yoga (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्र
कुत्र कुत्र, ind. (fr. 1. कु), where? where-<BR>to? in which case? when? कुत्र — क्व, where<BR>(this) — where (that), i. e. how distant or how dif-<BR>ferent is this from that, how little is this consistent<BR>with that? कुत्र becomes indefinite when con-<BR>nected with the particles अपि, चिद्, चन, e. g.<BR>कुत्रापि, anywhere, somewhere, to any place where-<BR>soever; कुत्र चिद्, anywhere, somewhere, whereso-<BR>ever, wherever, to any place; (sometimes कुत्र<BR>चिद् = कस्मिंश्चिद्, e. g. कुत्र चिद् अरण्ये, in a<BR>certain wood); न कुत्र चिद्, nowhere, to no place<BR>whatsoever; कुत्र चिद् — कुत्र चिद्, in one case —<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">Page0235-c+ 70</a>]<BR>in the other case; sometimes — sometimes; यत्र<BR>कुत्र च or यत्र कुत्र चिद्, wherever it be, here<BR>or there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रत्य
कुत्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, where being? where living<BR>or residing?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स्
कुत्स् कुत्स् (perhaps related to कुतस्), cl.<BR>10. P. A. कुत्सयति, -ते, -यितुम्; rarely<BR>cl. 1. P. कुत्सति, to despise, abuse, revile, contemn;<BR>[cf. Lith. kussinu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सन|कुत्सनं
कुत्सन, अस्, आ, अम्, reviling, abusive, contemp-<BR>tuous; (अम्), n. abuse, reviling, contempt, reproach;<BR>reproachful or abusive language; (आ), f. contemning,<BR>expression of contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सा
कुत्सा, f. reproach, contempt, censure.<BR>—कुत्सा-<BR>वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, censorious, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सित|कुत्सितं|कुत्सितः
कुत्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, despised, contemned, reviled;<BR>contemptible, low, mean, vile, hateful; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a grass, Cyperus.<BR>—कुत्सित-त्व, अम्, n. meanness,<BR>vileness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स्य
1. कुत्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be reproached, reviled,<BR>abused; blamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स
कुत्स कुत्स, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi with the<BR>epithet Ārjuneya, author of several hymns of the<BR>Ṛg-veda (when attacked by the demon Śuṣṇa,<BR>Indra defended him and killed the demon; but in<BR>other hymns of the Ṛg-veda, Kutsa is represented as<BR>persecuted by Indra); N. of a descendant of Aṅgiras,<BR>author of several other hymns of the Ṛg-veda;<BR>(pl.) the descendants or the family of Kutsa; light-<BR>ning, thunderbolt; [cf. कौत्स, पुरु-कुत्स, &c.]<BR>—कुत्स-कुशिकिका, f. the intermarriage of the<BR>Kutsa and Kuśika families.<BR>—कुत्स-पुत्र or कुत्स-<BR>वत्स, अस्, m. a son of Kutsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स्य
2. कुत्स्य, अस्, m. = कुत्स (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सला
कुत्सला कुत्सला, f. the indigo plant; [cf.<BR>नीली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ्
कुथ् कुथ्, cl. 4. P. कुथ्यति, चुकोथ,<BR>अकोथीत्, कोथिष्यति, कोथितुम्, to stink,<BR>to become putrid: Caus. P. कोथयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to putrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ कुथ, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. a painted or<BR>variegated cloth or blanket, serving as an elephant's<BR>housings; (अस्), m. sacrificial or Kuśa grass, Poa<BR>Cynosuroides; Śākya-muni in one of his former<BR>thirty-four births.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथुमि
कुथुमि कुथुमि, इस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0235-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

