कुन्ताप
कुन्ताप कुन्ताप, अम्, n., Ved., N. of certain<BR>organs or glands (?), twenty in number, supposed to<BR>be in the belly; N. of a section of the Atharva-veda,<BR>according to Sāyaṇācārya, thirty verses, constituting<BR>seven Sūktas of the twentieth book of this Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्ति|कुंति|कुंतिः|कुन्तिः
कुन्ति कुन्ति, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(इस्), m. sing. the prince of this people, also called<BR>Kunti-bhoja; कुन्ति is, according to different authori-<BR>ties, a son of either Dharmanetra, or of Netra and<BR>grandson of Dharma, or of Kratha, or of Vidarbha<BR>and father of Dhṛṣṭa, or of Supārśva and grandson<BR>of Sampāti and great-grandson of Garuḍa; (ई), f.<BR>a N. of Pṛthā, the daughter of a Yādava prince<BR>named Śūra, who gave her to his childless cousin<BR>Kunti or Kunti-bhoja, by whom she was adopted.<BR>She afterwards became one of the two wives of<BR>Pāṇḍu. (On one occasion before her marriage she<BR>paid such respect to the powerful sage Durvāsas that<BR>he taught her an incantation or charm, by virtue of<BR>which she was to have a child by any god she liked<BR>to invoke. Out of curiosity she invoked the Sun,<BR>by whom she had a child, cf. कर्ण; but the Sun<BR>afterwards restored to her her maidenhood. Soon<BR>after his marriage Pāṇḍu retired to the woods to<BR>indulge his passion for hunting. There he killed a<BR>male and female deer, who turned out to be a Ṛṣi<BR>and his wife in the form of these animals. The sage<BR>cursed Pāṇḍu and predicted that he would die in the<BR>embrace of one of his wives. Hence Pāṇḍu lived<BR>apart from Kunti, but with his approval she made<BR>use of her charm and had three sons, Yudhiṣṭhira,<BR>Bhīma, and Arjuna, by the three deities Dharma,<BR>Vāyu, and Indra respectively; cf. माद्री); N. of a<BR>Rākṣasī; the wife of a Brāhman; the plant Bos-<BR>wellia Thurifera; a fragrant resin (= गुग्गुलु).<BR>—कुन्ति-नन्दन, अस्, m. a son of Kuntī (the final<BR>being sometimes shortened in a comp.), either of<BR>the three elder Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>—कुन्ति-भोज, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Yādava prince, king of the Kuntis, who<BR>adopted Kuntī.<BR>—कुन्ती-सुत, अस्, m. a son of Kuntī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तिक
कुन्तिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थ्|कुंथ्
कुन्थ् कुन्थ्, cl. 1. P. कुन्थति, -थितुम्,<BR>to hurt, injure; to suffer pain, want, &c.;<BR>to be distressed; cl. 9. P. कुथ्नाति, to injure; to<BR>cling to; to twine round or be connected with, em-<BR>brace; [cf. Lat. quatio, per-cutio.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थु|कुन्थुः
कुन्थु कुन्थु, उस्, m., N. of the sixth Jaina<BR>Cakravartin or emperor in Bhārata; also of the<BR>seventeenth Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्द|कुंद|कुंदं|कुंदः|कुन्दः
कुन्द कुन्द, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. 3. कु), a kind of jasmine, Jasminum Multiflorum<BR>or Pubescens; (अस्), m. fragrant oleander, Nerium<BR>Odorum [cf. करवीर]; Olibanum, the resin of the<BR>plant Boswellia Thurifera; a turner's lathe; one of<BR>Kuvera's nine treasures; the number ‘nine;’ an epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu; N. of a mountain.<BR>—कुन्द-कर,<BR>अस्, m. a turner.<BR>—कुन्द-कुन्दाचार्य (˚द-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Pañcāstikāyasaṅgraha-<BR>sūtra.<BR>—कुन्द-माला, f. title of a work.<BR>—कुन्द-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">Page0236-c+ 73</a>]<BR>समान-दन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, one whose teeth are like<BR>the jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दक|कुन्दकः
कुन्दक, अस्, m. the plant Boswellia Thurifera;<BR>the resin of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दिनी|कुंदिनी
कुन्दिनी, f. an assemblage of lotus flowers or of<BR>jasmines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दम|कुंदम|कुंदमः|कुन्दमः
कुन्दम कुन्दम, अस्, m. a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दर|कुंदरः|कुन्दरः
कुन्दर कुन्दर, अस्, m. a sort of grass; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; [cf. कण्डुर and कुन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दु|कुंदु|कुंदुः|कुन्दुः
कुन्दु कुन्दु, उस्, m. a mouse, a rat; (उस्),<BR>f. the resin of the plant Boswellia Thurifera; gum<BR>olibanum or frankincense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुर|कुन्दुरः
कुन्दुर, अस्, m. or कुन्दुरु, उस्, m. f. the resin<BR>of the plant Boswellia Thurifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुरुक|कुन्दुरुकः
कुन्दुरुक, अस्, ई, m. f. the resin of the plant Bos-<BR>wellia Thurifera; (ई), f. the plant Boswellia Thurifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्द्र्
कुन्द्र् कुन्द्र्, cl. 10. P. कुन्द्रयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to tell a lie; [cf. कुद् and गुन्द्र्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्
कुप् 1. कुप्, cl. 4. P. (ep. also A.) कुप्यति,<BR>-ते, चुकोप, कोपिष्यति, अकुपत्, कोपि-<BR>तुम्, to be moved, excited, agitated, to swell, heave<BR>or boil with rage or emotion, to be angry, to be angry<BR>with (with dat. or gen. or acc. or with उपरि and<BR>gen., e. g. तस्मै or तस्य or तम् or तस्योपरि<BR>चुकोप, he was angry with him): Caus. कोपयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to excite, agitate, affect strongly with anger<BR>&c.; to cause to swell or heave with passion; to stir<BR>up; to provoke, make angry; to be angry: Desid.<BR>चुकुपिषति and चुकोपिषति: Intens. चोकुप्यते,<BR>चोकोप्ति; [cf. Lat. cupio; Eng. hope; Germ. hoffe.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप|कुपः
कुप, अस्, m., Ved. the beam or lever of a pair of<BR>scales.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपन
कुपन, अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपय
कुपय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. heaving, swelling with<BR>emotion; disturbed; (Sāy.) to be guarded or pro-<BR>tected (as if connected with rt. गुप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपित
कुपित, अस्, आ, अम्, provoked, incensed, offended,<BR>angry, bristling.<BR>—कुपित-वायु, उस्, m. aggravated<BR>flatulence, hypochondria.<BR>—कुपितान्तक (˚त-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. imminent or threatening death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्य|कुप्यं
कुप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excited; (अम्), n. a vile<BR>metal, any metal but silver and gold, base metal,<BR>copper, brass, &c.; zinc, lapis calaminaris, pewter,<BR>tutenag; (अस्), m., N. of a man; [cf. Lat. cuprum.]<BR>—कुप्य-शाला, f. a braziery, a foundry, a place<BR>where metallic vessels &c. are made or sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यक
कुप्यक at the end of compounds = कुप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोप|कोपः
कोप, अस्, m. passion, anger. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्
कुप् 2. कुप्, cl. 10. P. कोपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to speak, to shine; [cf. Hib. cubhas, ‘a<BR>word, a promise;’ Lat. cupo in nun-cupo; Goth.<BR>huf, ‘to lament.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपङ्क
कुपङ्क कु-पङ्क, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a slough,<BR>a heap of filth and mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपट|कुपटः
कुपट कु-पट, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (see 1.<BR>कु), miserable clothes, a miserable garment; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Dānava (covered with a miserable garment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपत
कुपत कुपत, ind. excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ|कुपथः
कुपथ कु-पथ, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>road, an evil way; bad conduct, evil way of living,<BR>immorality, profligacy; heterodox doctrine; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), walking in a bad or wrong road; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of an Asura or Dānava; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—कुपथ-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, or कुपथ-गामिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, or कुपथ-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going in a bad<BR>or wrong road, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ्य
कुपथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a bad way,<BR>literally or figuratively; unwholesome (as diet, regi-<BR>men, &c.), improper, counter-indicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपरिज्ञात
कुपरिज्ञात कु-परिज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1.<BR>कु), badly understood, wrongly comprehended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपरीक्षक
कुपरीक्षक कु-परीक्षक, अस्, इका, अम् (see<BR>1. कु), making a false estimate, not valuing rightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0236-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपरीक्षित
कु-परीक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, badly examined or<BR>tested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपाणि|कुपाणिः
कुपाणि कु-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ (see 1. कु), crooked-<BR>handed, having a deformed or maimed hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपात्र
कुपात्र कु-पात्र, अम्, n. an unfit recipient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिञ्जल
कुपिञ्जल कु-पिञ्जल, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), N.<BR>of a man; [cf. कौपिञ्जल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपित
कुपित कुपित. See under rt. कुप् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितृ
कुपितृ कु-पितृ, ता, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनी
कुपिनी कुपिनी, f. (fr. rt. 1. कुप्?), a kind of<BR>net for catching small fish, made of bamboos or rushes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनिन्
कुपिनिन्, ई, m. a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिन्द|कुपिंद|कुपिंदः|कुपिन्दः
कुपिन्द कुपिन्द, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 1.<BR>कुप्), a weaver; [cf. कुविन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपीलु|कुपीलुः
कुपीलु कु-पीलु, उस्, m. (see 1. कु), a sort<BR>of ebony tree; [cf. कारस्कर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुत्र|कुपुत्रः
कुपुत्र कु-पुत्र, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>son; a disobedient or wicked son; a son of an in-<BR>ferior degree, as an adopted son &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुरुष|कुपुरुषः
कुपुरुष कु-पुरुष, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>low, vile, or miserable man; a poltroon.<BR>—कुपु-<BR>रुष-जनिता, f., N. of a metre consisting of four<BR>lines of eleven syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपूय|कुपूयः
कुपूय कु-पूय, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), inferior,<BR>low, vile, contemptible; [cf. कपूय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्रावरण
कुप्रावरण कु-प्रावरण or कु-प्रावृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (see 1. कु), badly or miserably dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्रिय|कुप्रियः
कुप्रिय कु-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), dis-<BR>agreeable, contemptible, low, vile, last, worst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्लव|कुप्लवः
कुप्लव कु-प्लव, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a weak<BR>or frail raft or float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबधू
कुबधू कु-बधू, ऊस्, f. (see 1. कु), a wicked<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबन्ध|कुबन्धः
कुबन्ध कु-बन्ध, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a dis-<BR>graceful stigma; [cf. अङ्क-बन्ध.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबल
कुबल कुबल, कुबल-प्रस्थ, कुबलाश्व,<BR>&c. See under कुवल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबुद्धि
कुबुद्धि कु-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ (see 1. कु), a<BR>person of base or vile sentiments; stupid, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेर|कुबेरः
कुबेर कुबेर, or in later Sanskrit कुवेर, अस्,<BR>m. (said to be fr. rt. कुम्ब् or fr. 1. कु and वेर),<BR>originally N. of the chief of the evil beings or spirits<BR>of darkness with the epithet Vaiśravaṇa; afterwards<BR>the god of riches and treasure, the regent of the<BR>northern quarter of the world, which is hence called<BR>Kubera-guptā dik; (कुबेर is the son of Viśravas by<BR>Iḍaviḍā, the chief of the Yakṣas, and a friend of<BR>Rudra; he is represented as having three legs and<BR>only eight teeth); with Jainas, the attendant of the<BR>nineteenth Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī; N. of a<BR>prince of Deva-rāṣṭra; or N. of the great-grand-<BR>father of Vāṇa-bhaṭṭa, the author of the Kādambarī;<BR>or of the author of the Dattaka-candrikā; the tree<BR>Cedrela Toona; (अस्, आ, अम्), deformed, monstrous;<BR>slow, lazy; [cf. कुवेर.]<BR>—कुबेर-नलिनी, f., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR>—कुबेर-बान्धव, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva, ‘the relation of Kubera.’<BR>—कुबेर-वन, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the forest of Kubera,’ N. of a place.<BR>—कुबेर-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, m., N. of a Vaiśya.<BR>—कुबेराक्षी<BR>(˚र-अक्˚), f. the plant Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—कु-<BR>बेराचल (˚र-अच्˚), अस्, m. ‘the mountain of Kubera,’<BR>an epithet of the Kailāsa mountain.<BR>—कुबेराद्रि<BR>(˚र-अद्˚), इस्, m. an epithet of the Kailāsa mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेरक
कुबेरक, अस्, m. the tree Cedrela Toona (तुन्न);<BR>(इका), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेरिण
कुबेरिण कुबेरिण, अस्, m. (?), N. of a mixed<BR>caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज कुब्ज, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. कु and rt. उब्ज्?),<BR>hump-backed, crooked; (अस्), m. a curved sword, scy-<BR>mitar; a sort of fish, Bola Cuja; the plant Achyran-<BR>thes Aspera, = अपामार्ग; [cf. न्युब्ज and कन्य-<BR>कुब्ज; cf. also Lith. kupra, kupotas; Gr. κυφός,<BR>κύπτω Lat. gibbus, gibba, gibber; Germ. Höcker?].<BR>—कुब्ज-कण्टक, अस्, m. a white Mimosa.<BR>—कुब्-<BR>ज-किरात or कुब्ज-वामन, अम्, n. a hump-backed<BR>person and a dwarf.<BR>—कुब्जाम्रक (˚ज-आम्˚), अस्<BR>or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कुब्जा-<BR>लीढ (˚ज-आल्˚), अस्, m., N. of the founder of a sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जक|कुब्जकः
कुब्जक, अस्, आ, अम्, hump-backed, crooked; (अस्),<BR>m. the aquatic plant Trapa Bispinosa; (इका), f. in<BR>the word कुब्जिका-तन्त्र, N. of a Tantra; according<BR>to some authorities कुब्जिका कुमारी is a girl eight<BR>years old personating the goddess Durgā at a festival<BR>of this deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जित
कुब्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, curved, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्र|कुब्रं
कुब्र कुब्र, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. कुम्ब्),<BR>a forest; a hole for sacrificial fire; a ring, an ear-<BR>ring; a thread; a cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्रह्म|कुब्रह्मः
कुब्रह्म कु-ब्रह्म, अस्, m. or कु-ब्रह्मन्,<BR>आ, m. (see 1. कु), a degraded or contemptible Brāh-<BR>man, one who officiates for Śūdras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभन्यु
कुभन्यु कुभन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desirous<BR>of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभा
कुभा कुभा, f., Ved., N. of a river falling<BR>into the Indus, the Kabul river (?); [cf. κωφήν.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभार्य
कुभार्य कु-भार्य, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु),<BR>having a bad wife; (आ), f. a bad wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभुक्त
कुभुक्त कु-भुक्त, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), bad food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभृत्य
कुभृत्य कु-भृत्य, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्
कुम् कुम्, ind. an interjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमति
कुमति कु-मति, इस्, f. (see 1. कु), vile or<BR>base sentiment; slow or weak intellect; folly; (इस्,<BR>इस्, इ), or कु-मनीष, अस्, आ, अम्, or कु-मनीषिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, of slow intellect, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमन्त्र|कुमंत्र|कुमन्त्रः
कुमन्त्र कु-मन्त्र, अस्, m. bad advice; evil<BR>counsel; a charm employed to secure success in a<BR>bad enterprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमन्त्रिन्
कु-मन्त्रिन्, ई, m. a bad counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार कुमार, अस्, m. (fr. कु + मार, fr. rt.<BR>मृ ? ‘easily dying;’ by native authorities derived fr.<BR>rt. 2. कम्), a child, a new-born child (especially in the<BR>earlier language); a boy, a youth, a son; a prince,<BR>the heir-apparent associated in the kingdom with the<BR>reigning monarch (especially in theatrical language);<BR>a groom; a N. of Skanda the god of war, who is<BR>also the reputed author of certain grammatical Sūtras<BR>(see कलाप); N. of a son of Agni, who is the author<BR>of some Vedic hymns; an epithet of Agni; (with<BR>Jainas) N. of the attendant of the twelfth Arhat of<BR>the present Avasarpiṇī; N. of a Prajāpati; an epithet<BR>of Mañju-śrī; a parrot; the tree Capparis Trifoliata<BR>[cf. कुमारक]; an epithet of the river Sindhu;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (ई), f. a young girl,<BR>one from ten to twelve years old, a maiden; or (in<BR>the Tantras) any virgin up to the age of sixteen, or<BR>before menstruation has commenced; a daughter;<BR>N. of the wife of Bhīma-sena, the son of Parīkṣit;<BR>or of a daughter of Vasu-deva by Rohiṇī; an<BR>epithet of Sītā, the wife of Rāma; an epithet of<BR>the goddess Durgā; the Śyāmā, a bird so named;<BR>N. of several plants, Aloe Perfoliata, or the plant<BR>Clitoria Ternatea [cf. अपराजिता]; also the plant<BR>Jasminum Sambac, and a plant commonly called<BR>Bandhyā-karkoṭakī; the blossom of the plants Taruṇī<BR>and Modinī; great cardamoms; the most southerly<BR>of the nine portions of the known continent, or of<BR>Jambu-dvīpa, the southern extremity of the peninsula,<BR>whence the modern name Cape Comorin (Kumārī);<BR>the central part of the universe, according to Hindū<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">Page0237-c+ 78</a>]<BR>geography, Jambu-dvīpa or India; N. of a river<BR>flowing from the mountain Śuktimat; N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of sixteen syllables each;<BR>(when a name is given to a pupil to indicate his<BR>attachment to any particular master, कुमारी may be<BR>prefixed to denote that the pupil's object is to gain<BR>the affections of the master's daughter, e. g. कुमारी-<BR>दाक्ष); (अम्), n. pure gold; [Gr. κόρος, κοῦρος;<BR>μεῖραξ, μειράκιον ?].<BR>—कुमार-गुप्त, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince (‘protected by the god of war’).<BR>—कु-<BR>मार-घातिन्, ई, m. the slayer of a child.<BR>—कुमार-<BR>जीव, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = पुत्रञ्जीवक.<BR>—कु-<BR>मार-त्व, अम्, n. boyhood, youth.<BR>—कुमार-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of Nidhipati.<BR>—कुमार-<BR>दास, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कुमार-देवी, f., N. of<BR>the mother of Samudra-gupta.<BR>—कुमार-देष्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting perishable gifts; (Sāy.)<BR>granting children.<BR>—कुमार-धारा, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—कुमार-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a king, =<BR>शालिवाहन (?), also N. of a king of Guzerat (?).<BR>—कुमार-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कु-<BR>मार-भृत्या, f. care of a young child, care of a<BR>pregnant or lying-in woman, midwifery.<BR>—कुमार-<BR>ललिता, f. ‘boy's play,’ N. of a metre consisting of<BR>four lines of eight syllables each.<BR>—कुमार-वन,<BR>अम्, n. Kumāra's (i. e. Kārttikeya's) grove.<BR>—कुमार-<BR>वाहिन्, ई, m. a peacock, (‘carrying the god of war;’<BR>this god being usually represented as borne by a pea-<BR>cock.)<BR>—कुमार-व्रत, अम्, n. a vow of eternal<BR>chastity.<BR>—कुमार-सम्भव, अस्, m. ‘the birth of<BR>the god of war,’ title of a poem by Kālidāsa.<BR>—कु-<BR>मार-सू, ऊस्, m. the father of the god of war, an<BR>epithet of Agni; (ऊस्), f. the mother of the god of<BR>war, an epithet of the river Gaṅgā, also of the god-<BR>dess Durgā.<BR>—कुमार-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a minister.<BR>—कुमार-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of the author of a<BR>commentary on the Mīmāṃsā-bhāṣya.<BR>—कुमार-<BR>हारित, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR>—कुमाराभिषेक<BR>(˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘the inauguration of Kumāra,’<BR>title of the thirteenth book of the Kumāra-sambhava.<BR>—कुमारी-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—कु-<BR>मारी-पाल, अस्, m. the guardian of a virgin or bride.<BR>—कुमारी-पुत्र, अस्, m. the child of an unmarried<BR>woman.<BR>—कुमारी-पुर, अम्, n. a gynæceum.<BR>—कुमारी-पूजा, f. the worship of Kumāri or Durgā,<BR>(a ceremony performed at the great Durgā festival,<BR>when a girl between ten and twelve years old is<BR>placed on a pedestal, as the representative of the<BR>goddess, and fed with offerings made to the idol.)<BR>—कुमारी-श्वशुर, अस्, m. the father-in-law of a<BR>maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारक|कुमारकः
कुमारक, अस्, m. a child, a little boy, a boy, a<BR>lad, a youth; the pupil of the eye; N. of a Nāga;<BR>the plant Capparis Trifoliata; (इका), f. a girl from<BR>ten to twelve years old, or generally a virgin; an<BR>insect, Sphex Asiatica; double jasmine, Jasminum<BR>Sambac; large cardamoms; N. of a part of Bhārata-<BR>varṣa, a division of the known continent.<BR>—कुमा-<BR>रिका-क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a country.<BR>—कुमारिका-<BR>खण्ड, a section of the Skanda-purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारय
कुमारय, nom. P. कुमारयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>play, especially as a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारयु|कुमारयुः
कुमारयु, उस्, m. a prince, heir-apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिक
कुमारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, furnished with girls, abound-<BR>ing in them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिन्
कुमारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, abounding in girls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिल
कुमारिल, अस्, m. or कुमारिल-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a renowned teacher of the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारी
कुमारी, ई, ई, m. f. a man or woman desirous of<BR>a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार्ग
कुमार्ग कु-मार्ग, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>way, bad ways, (also used metaphorically.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमालक|कुमालकः
कुमालक कुमालक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people and country, = कुमारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमालय
कुमालय, nom. P. कुमालयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>play, especially as a child; [cf. कुमारय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमित्र
कुमित्र कु-मित्र, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0237-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुख
कुमुख कु-मुख, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्
कुमुद् कु-मुद्, त्, त्, त् (see 1. कु), unkind,<BR>unfriendly; avaricious, niggardly; (त्), n. the plant<BR>Nymphæa Esculenta, the esculent white water-lily;<BR>the plant Nymphæa Rubra, the red lotus.<BR>—कुमुद्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in lotuses; (अती), f. an<BR>assemblage of lotuses; a place or pond filled with<BR>them; the flexible stalk of a water-lily; N. of a<BR>plant bearing a poisonous fruit, Villarsia (Menyanthes)<BR>Indica; N. of a sister of the serpent-king Kumuda<BR>and wife of Kuśa; N. of the wife of Vimarṣaṇa;<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—कुमुद्वतीश (˚ती-ईश), अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of the moon; [cf. कुमुद-बन्धु and the<BR>following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद|कुमुदं|कुमुदः
कु-मुद, अस्, अम्, m. n. the esculent white water-<BR>lily, Nymphæa Esculenta (‘exciting what joy!’); red<BR>lotus, Nymphæa Rubra; (अम्), n. silver; (अस्), m.<BR>camphor; N. of a Nāga; N. of the elephant of the<BR>south-west or southern quarter; N. of a Daitya; N.<BR>of an attendant of Viṣṇu; N. of a son of Gada by<BR>Vṛhatī; N. of a confidant of king Unmattāvanti; one<BR>of the monkey-heroes of the Rāmāyaṇa; N. of a<BR>poet; N. of a mountain; N. of one of the smaller<BR>Dvīpas; (आ), f. several plants, Gmelina Arborea;<BR>Pistia Stratiotes; Desmodium Gangeticum; Grislea<BR>Tomentosa; N. of another plant, commonly called<BR>Kaṭphala; N. of a deity; (ई), f. a plant, commonly<BR>called Kaṭphala.<BR>—कुमुद-खण्ड, अम्, n. an<BR>assemblage of Kumudas.<BR>—कुमुद-घ्नी, f., N. of<BR>a plant containing a poisonous milky juice.<BR>—कु-<BR>मुद-पत्त्राभ (˚त्र-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्, resem-<BR>bling the leaves of the white water-lily.<BR>—कुमुद-<BR>बन्धु, उस्, m. or कुमुद-बान्धव, अस्, m. the<BR>moon (‘friend of the lotus;’ the white esculent lotus<BR>expanding its petals during the night and closing<BR>them in the day time; hence other similar appella-<BR>tions of the moon, as कुमुद-प्रिय, &c.).<BR>—कु-<BR>मुद-वती, f. an assemblage of Kumudas, a place<BR>abounding in them, &c.<BR>—कुमुद-सुहृद्, त्, m.<BR>the moon; [cf. कुमुद-बन्धु.]<BR>—कुमुदाकर<BR>(˚द-आक्˚), अस्, m. a number of water-lilies or place<BR>abounding in them.<BR>—कुमुदाक्ष (˚द-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Nāga; also of an attendant of Viṣṇu.<BR>—कुमुदादि (˚द-आदि), इस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Pathya.<BR>—कुमुदावास (˚द-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abounding or richly furnished with Kumudas; (अस्),<BR>m. a pool abounding in them.<BR>—कुमुदेश (˚द-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. an epithet of the moon, ‘lord of the<BR>lotus.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिक
कुमुदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, abounding with Kumudas;<BR>(इका), f., N. of a plant, commonly called Kaṭphala;<BR>a small tree, the seeds of which are aromatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनी
कुमुदिनी, f. an assemblage of Kumudas or a<BR>place abounding in them; the mother of Raghu-<BR>deva.<BR>—कुमुदिनी-नायक, अस्, m. or कुमुदिनी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. an epithet of the moon; [cf. कुमुद-<BR>बन्धु.]<BR>—कुमुदिनी-वनिता, f. any loved woman<BR>fancifully represented as an assemblage of lotus<BR>flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमेधस्
कुमेधस् कु-मेधस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (see 1. कु),<BR>of little intellect, stupid; malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमेरु|कुमेरुः
कुमेरु कु-मेरु, उस्, m. (see 1. कु), the<BR>southern hemisphere or pole, the region of the<BR>demons and Titans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमोदक|कुमोदकः
कुमोदक कुमोदक, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; [cf. कौमोदकी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्प्
कुम्प् कुम्प्, cl. 10. P. कुम्पयति, -यितुम्,<BR>another form for कुम्ब्, कुम्बयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्प|कुम्पः
कुम्प कुम्प, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked-armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्ब्
कुम्ब् कुम्ब्, cl. 6. and 10. P. कुम्बति<BR>and कुम्बयति, -यितुम्, to cover; [cf.<BR>कुम्प् and कुम्भ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्ब|कुंबः|कुम्बः
कुम्ब कुम्ब, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), Ved.<BR>a kind of head-dress for women; the upper part<BR>or top of a club; (आ), f. a thick petticoat; an en-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-b" target="_blank">Page0238-b+ 78</a>]<BR>closure round a place of sacrifice to prevent profane<BR>intrusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्बिक
कुम्बिक कुम्बिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्ब्या
कुम्ब्या कुम्ब्या or कुम्व्या, f., Ved. a kind<BR>of hymn or sacred formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भ्
कुम्भ् कुम्भ्, cl. 10. P. कुम्भयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, another form for कुम्ब्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भ|कुंभ|कुम्भं|कुंभः|कुम्भः
कुम्भ कुम्भ, अस्, m. a jar, pitcher, water-<BR>pot, ewer, a small water-jar, (often in compounds,<BR>e. g. छिद्र-कुम्भ, a perforated pitcher; आम-<BR>कुम्भ, a jar of unbaked clay; हेम-कुम्भ, a<BR>golden ewer; जल-कुम्भ, a water-pot); an urn<BR>in which the bones of a dead person are collected;<BR>the sign of the zodiac Aquarius; a measure of grain<BR>equal to twenty Droṇas, a little more than three<BR>bushels and three gallons (commonly called a comb,<BR>some make it two Droṇas or sixty-four Seers); the<BR>frontal globe on the upper part of the forehead of an<BR>elephant (there are two of these projections which<BR>swell in the rutting season); a religious exercise, viz.<BR>closing the nostrils and mouth so as to suspend<BR>breathing; the root of a plant used in medicine;<BR>the paramour of a harlot, a bully, a flash or fancy<BR>man; N. of a Muni; N. of a Dānava, son of<BR>Prahlāda and brother of Nikumbha; also of a<BR>Rākṣasa, a son of Kumbha-karṇa; N. of the<BR>father of the nineteenth Arhat of the present Avasar-<BR>piṇī; N. of a monkey; one of the thirty-four jātakas<BR>or former births of Śākya-muni; title of a work;<BR>(ई), f. a small jar or pot, an earthen cooking vessel;<BR>a vessel for preserving grain, a measure of grain; N.<BR>of several plants, a small tree, the seeds of which are<BR>used in medicine, commonly called Kaṭphala; an-<BR>other plant, Bignonia Suaveolens; another plant,<BR>Pistia Stratiotes; another plant, commonly called<BR>Romaśa; another plant, Croton Polyandrum; (आ),<BR>f. a harlot, a whore; (अम्), n. the plant Ipomœa<BR>Turpethum; a fragrant resin (गुग्गुलु), or the<BR>plant which bears it; [cf. Gr. κύμβη Lat. cymba.]<BR>—कुम्भ-कर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa, the<BR>gigantic brother of Rāvaṇa, who is described in the<BR>Yuddha-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa as sleeping for six<BR>months at a time, and then waking to gorge him-<BR>self; N. of a Muni; an epithet of Śiva; N. of a<BR>Dānava.<BR>—कुम्भकर्ण-वध, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>slaughter of Kumbhakarṇa,’ a section of the Padma-<BR>purāṇa.<BR>—कुम्भ-कामला, f. a bilious affection,<BR>a sort of jaundice together with swelling of the<BR>joints; [cf. कुम्भ-पाद.]<BR>—कुम्भ-कार, अस्,<BR>m. a potter, being according to some authorities the<BR>son of a Brāhman by a wife of the Kṣatriya caste;<BR>a serpent; a kind of wild fowl; (ई), f. the wife of a<BR>potter; N. of a girl; a mineral substance used as an<BR>application to strengthen the eyes and beautify the<BR>eyelashes; red arsenic.<BR>—कुम्भ-कारक, अस्, m.<BR>a potter; (इका), f. the wife of a potter, a woman of<BR>the potter caste; a sort of collyrium.<BR>—कुम्भ-<BR>कार-कुक्कुट, अस्, m. a kind of chicken, Phasianus<BR>Gallus.<BR>—कुम्भ-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Śambara.<BR>—कुम्भ-कोण, अस्, m. ‘brim of a jar,’<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—कुम्भ-घोण-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कुम्भ-जन्मन्, आ, m. an epithet<BR>of Agastya.<BR>—कुम्भ-तुम्बी, f. a kind of large<BR>round gourd.<BR>—कुम्भ-दासी, f. a bawd, a procuress.<BR>—कुम्भ-धर, अस्, m. the sign of the zodiac<BR>Aquarius.<BR>—कुम्भ-नाभ, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Bali.<BR>—कुम्भ-पाद, अस्, -पदी, अम्, a person<BR>with swollen legs bulging like a pitcher; [cf. कुम्-<BR>भ-कामला.]<BR>—कुम्भ-बाहु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>Daitya.<BR>—कुम्भ-मण्डूक, अस्, m. a frog in a<BR>pitcher; [cf. कूप-मण्डूक.]<BR>—कुम्भ-मुष्क,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. an epithet of certain demons, ‘hav-<BR>ing a jar-shaped scrotum.’<BR>—कुम्भ-मूर्धन्, आ,<BR>m. a fabulous being mentioned in the Hari-vaṃśa.<BR>—कुम्भ-योनि, इस्, m. ‘born in a water-jar,’ an<BR>epithet of the saint Agastya; of Vasiṣṭha; and of<BR>Droṇa, the military preceptor of the Kurus and<BR>Pāṇḍus; N. of a plant, commonly called Droṇa-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">Page0238-c+ 79</a>]<BR>puṣpī; (इस्), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—कुम्भ-राशि,<BR>इस्, m. the sign Aquarius.<BR>—कुम्भ-रेतस्, n. semen<BR>virile deposited in a Kumbha; (आस्), m. a form of<BR>Agni.<BR>—कुम्भ-लग्न, अम्, n. that time of day in<BR>which Aquarius rises above the horizon.<BR>—कुम्भ-<BR>वीजक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, commonly called<BR>Rīṭhā-karañja.<BR>—कुम्भ-शाला, f. a pottery, a pot-<BR>ter's kiln.<BR>—कुम्भ-सन्धि, इस्, m. the hollow on<BR>the top of an elephant's head, between the frontal<BR>globes.<BR>—कुम्भ-सम्भव, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>the saint Agastya; also of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—कुम्भ-<BR>सर्पिस्, इस्, n. butter placed in a jar.<BR>—कुम्भ-<BR>हनु, उस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—कुम्भाण्ड<BR>(˚भ-अण्˚), आस्, m. pl. (with Buddhists) a class of<BR>demons with testicles shaped like a Kumbha; N. of<BR>a minister of the Asura Bāṇa; (ई), f. a pumpkin<BR>gourd, (a various reading for कुष्माण्डी.)<BR>—कुम्-<BR>भी-धान्य, अस्, m. grain stored in jars sufficient<BR>(according to some) for six days, or (to others) for one<BR>year's consumption.<BR>—कुम्भी-धान्यक, अस्, m. a<BR>householder who preserves grain in store for six days<BR>&c.<BR>—कुम्भी-नस, अस्, m. a kind of large venom-<BR>ous snake; a kind of poisonous insect; (ई), f., N. of<BR>the wife of the Gandharva Aṅgāraparṇa; also of a<BR>Rākṣasī, the mother of Lavaṇa.<BR>—कुम्भीनसि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a demon.<BR>—कुम्भी-पाक, अस्, m.<BR>the contents of a cooking vessel; (अस् or आस्), m.<BR>sing. or pl. a hell, in which the wicked are baked<BR>like potters’ vessels, or cooked like the contents of a<BR>cooking vessel.<BR>—कुम्भी-वीज, अम्, n. the nut of<BR>the croton; [cf. कुम्भिनी-वीज.]<BR>—कुम्भेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ (˚भ-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कुम्-<BR>भोदर (˚भ-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of an attendant<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—कुम्भोलूक (˚भ-उल्˚), अस्, m. a kind<BR>of owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भक|कुंभक|कुंभकः|कुम्भकः
कुम्भक, अस्, m. the base of a column; stop-<BR>ping the breath by shutting the mouth and closing<BR>both nostrils with the fingers of the right hand; a<BR>religious exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिका|कुंभिका
कुम्भिका, f. a small pot or pitcher; N. of<BR>several plants, Pistia Stratiotes; another plant, Big-<BR>nonia Suaveolens; another plant, commonly called<BR>Droṇa-puṣpī; a disease of the eyes, hordeolum or stye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिन्|कुंभिन्
कुम्भिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a water-jar; shaped like<BR>a jar &c.; (ई), m., N. of a demon hostile to children;<BR>an elephant; a crocodile; a fish; a kind of poisonous<BR>insect; a sort of fragrant resin (गुग्गुलु), or the<BR>plant bearing this fragrant resin.<BR>—कुम्भि-नरक,<BR>अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of a hell, = कुम्भी-<BR>पाक (?).<BR>—कुम्भिनी-वीज, अम्, n. the croton-nut,<BR>Croton Jamalgota.<BR>—कुम्भि-पाकी, f., N. of a plant,<BR>commonly called Kaṭphala.<BR>—कुम्भि-मद, अस्, m.<BR>the juice that exudes from an elephant's temples at<BR>certain seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिल|कुंभिल|कुंभिलः|कुम्भिलः
कुम्भिल, अस्, m. a thief who breaks into a<BR>house, a plagiarist; a wife's brother; a child be-<BR>gotten at undue seasons or of an imperfect impregna-<BR>tion; a kind of fish, the gilt-head, Ophiocephalus<BR>Wrahl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीक|कुंभीक|कुंभीकः|कुम्भीकः
कुम्भीक, अस्, m. a pathic, a catamite; the plant<BR>Rottleria Tinctoria, or the plant Pistia Stratiotes, a<BR>plant the bark of which furnishes a yellow dye; (आ),<BR>f. a swelling, especially of the eyelids, similar to a<BR>seed or grain of the Kumbhīka; an affection of the<BR>eyes, hordeolum or stye, also कुम्भीक-पिडका;<BR>Ved., N. of a kind of demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीकिन्
कुम्भीकिन् ई, इनी, इ, similar to a seed or grain of<BR>the Kumbhīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0238-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीर|कुंभीर|कुंभीरः|कुम्भीरः
