कुर्वत् कुर्वत्, अन्, अती, अत् (pres. part. fr. rt.<BR>1. कृ), doing, acting, &c.; acting as a servant, an<BR>agent, a servant.<BR>—कुर्वद्-रूप, अम्, n. cause<BR>according to the Cārvākas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्वाण|कुर्व्वाण
कुर्वाण, अस्, आ, अम्, doing, making, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्
कुल् कुल्, cl. 1. P. कोलति, चुकोल, &c.,<BR>कोलितुम्, to accumulate, collect; to be of<BR>kin, to behave as a kinsman; to proceed continuously<BR>or without interruption; to count.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल|कुलं|कुलः
कुल कुल, अम्, n. (fr. rt. कुल्?), a herd, a<BR>troop, a flock, an assemblage, a multitude, a number<BR>&c. (of quadrupeds, birds, insects, &c., or of inanimate<BR>objects, e. g. गो-कुल, a herd of cows; मृग-कुल,<BR>a herd of deer; महिषी-कुल, a herd of female<BR>buffaloes; अलि-कुल, a swarm of bees; अलक-कुल,<BR>a multitude of curls); a race, family, community,<BR>tribe, caste, association, set, company (e. g. ब्राह्-<BR>मण-कुल, the caste of the Brāhmans); the resi-<BR>dence of a family, seat of a community; (in a<BR>contemptuous sense) a lot, a gang (forming a comp.<BR>with a preceding gen. sing., e. g. चौरस्य-कुल,<BR>a gang of thieves); an inhabited country; a house,<BR>an abode; a noble or eminent family or race; high<BR>station (often at the beginning of a compound =<BR>chief, principal; see कुल-गिरि below); the body; the<BR>front, fore part; a blue stone; (अस्), m. the chief of<BR>a corporation or guild; [cf. Hib. gaol, ‘a family or<BR>kindred.’] कुलि and कुली, see s. v.<BR>—कुल-कज्जल,<BR>अस्, m. disgrace of the family.<BR>—कुल-कण्टक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘a family-thorn,’ any one who is a trouble to his<BR>family.<BR>—कुल-कन्या, f. a girl of good family.<BR>—कुल-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, founding a family, the<BR>founder of a family or race, an ancestor.<BR>—कुल-<BR>कर्कटी, f. a kind of gourd; [cf. चीनाकर्कती.]<BR>—कुल-कर्तृ, ता, m. the founder of a family or<BR>race, an ancestor.<BR>—कुल-कर्मन्, अ, n. the peculiar<BR>or proper duty of a family or race, any observance or<BR>custom peculiar to a family.<BR>—कुल-कलङ्क, अस्, m.<BR>‘a family-stain,’ any one who disgraces his family.<BR>—कुल-क्षय, अस्, m. decay or downfall of a race<BR>or family; (आ), f. a sort of cowach, Mucuna Pruritus<BR>(= शूकशिम्बी).<BR>—कुल-गरिमन्, आ, m. family<BR>pride.<BR>—कुल-गिरि, इस्, m. a chief mountain, any one<BR>of the seven principal mountains of Bhārata-varṣa;<BR>see कुलाचल.<BR>—कुल-गृह, अम्, n. a noble house.<BR>—कुल-गोप, अस्, m., Ved. the protector of a<BR>domicile.<BR>—कुल-गौरव, अम्, n. family import-<BR>ance.<BR>—कुल-घ्न, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, destroying a<BR>family.<BR>—कुल-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast<BR>on the Kātantra grammar; N. of the author of the<BR>Durgāvākya-prabodha.<BR>—कुल-चूडामणि, title of a<BR>work.<BR>—कुल-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, rejected by his<BR>family.<BR>—कुल-ज or कुल-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born in<BR>a noble family, of a good or noble family, well-born,<BR>of good breed; ancestral, hereditary.<BR>—कुल-जन,<BR>अस्, m. a person belonging to a noble family, a high-<BR>born or distinguished person.<BR>—कुल-तत्त्व-विद्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, knowing the true state of a family.<BR>—कुल-तस्,<BR>ind. by birth.<BR>—कुल-तिथि, इस्, m. f. an important<BR>lunar day, the fourth, eighth, twelfth, or fourteenth<BR>day of the half-month.<BR>—कुल-तिलक, अस्, m. the<BR>glory of a family, one who does honour to a family.<BR>—कुल-दमन, अस्, आ, अम्, subduing a family,<BR>holding it in subjection.<BR>—कुल-दीप or कुल-<BR>दीपक, अस्, m. the lamp or light or glory of a race<BR>or family; (इका), f. title of a work treating on the<BR>noble families of Bengal.<BR>—कुल-दुहितृ, ता, f. the<BR>daughter of a noble family; a high-born maiden.<BR>—कुल-देवता, f. a principal deity; an epithet of<BR>the goddess Durgā.<BR>—कुल-दैव, अम्, n. family<BR>destiny; a principal deity.<BR>—कुल-धर्म, अस्, m.<BR>practice or observance peculiar to a tribe or family,<BR>peculiar duty of caste or race.<BR>—कुल-धारक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘upholder of the family,’ a son.<BR>—कुल-धुर्य,<BR>अस्, m. one who is able to support a family, a grown-<BR>up son.<BR>—कुल-नक्षत्र, अम्, n. any Nakṣatra<BR>or lunar mansion distinguished above others; any<BR>auspicious asterism.<BR>—कुल-नन्दन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing joy to a family, doing honour to a family; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-b" target="_blank">Page0240-b+ 81</a>]<BR>high-born virtuous child.<BR>—कुल-नायिका, f. a girl<BR>worshipped at the celebration of the orgies of the left-<BR>hand Śāktas.<BR>—कुल-नारी, f. a woman of good<BR>family; a high-bred virtuous woman.<BR>—कुल-नाश,<BR>अस्, m. a camel; a reprobate, an outcast.<BR>—कुल-<BR>निन्दा, f. family disgrace.<BR>—कुलन्-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>upholding a family.<BR>—कुल-प, अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>chief of a family or race or tribe.<BR>—कुल-पति, इस्,<BR>m. the head or chief of a family.<BR>—कुल-पत्त्र, अस्,<BR>m. a plant, commonly called Damanaka.<BR>—कुल-<BR>परम्परा, f. the series of generations comprising<BR>a race.<BR>—कुल-पर्वत or कुल-शैल, अस्, m. a<BR>principal mountain, any one of seven mountains in<BR>Bhārata; [cf. कुल-गिरि.]<BR>—कुल-पांसुका, f. an<BR>unchaste woman.<BR>—कुल-पालक, अस्, इका, अम्, pro-<BR>tecting a family, nourishing or providing for a family;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of orange, = कुरुम्ब, commonly<BR>कमलानेवु.<BR>—कुल-पालि, इस्, f. or कुल-पालिका,<BR>f. or कुल-पाली, f. a chaste, high-born, or noble<BR>woman.<BR>—कुल-पुत्र, अस्, m. a son of a noble<BR>family, a noble or respectable youth; (ई), f. the<BR>daughter of a good family, a high-born or respectable<BR>girl; [cf. कुल-दुहितृ.]<BR>—कुल-पुत्रक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a plant, = कुल-पत्त्र and मुनि-पुत्र.<BR>—कुलपुत्र-जन, अस्, m. the son of a good<BR>family, a noble or respectable youth.<BR>—कुल-पु-<BR>रुष, अस्, m. a man of good family, a noble or<BR>respectable man; an ancestor, any family progenitor.<BR>—कुल-पूर्वग, अस्, m. an ancestor.<BR>—कुल-<BR>प्रकाश, अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—कुल-प्रसूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, born in a noble family.<BR>—कुल-बधू,<BR>ऊस्, f. a noble, virtuous, or respectable woman; [cf. कु-<BR>ल-योषित्.]<BR>—कुल-बालिका, f. = कुल-पालिका above.<BR>—कुल-भार्या, f. a virtuous, noble, or high-bred<BR>wife.<BR>—कुल-भूभृत्, त्, m. a principal mountain,<BR>one of the seven mountains in Bhārata.<BR>—कुल-<BR>भूषण, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘family-adorning,’ a family<BR>ornament.<BR>—कुल-भृत्या, f. the nursing of a preg-<BR>nant woman; a midwife, a nurse?; [cf. कुमार-<BR>भृत्या.]<BR>—कुल-भेद-कर, अस्, m. one who<BR>causes discord in a family.<BR>—कुल-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, expelled from a family.<BR>—कुल-मर्यादा, f.<BR>family honour or respectability.<BR>—कुल-मार्ग, अस्,<BR>m. the best or principal way, the way of honesty.<BR>—कुल-मित्र, अम्, n. a friend of the family.<BR>—कु-<BR>लम्-पुन, अस्, आ, अम्, purifying a family; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—कुलम्-<BR>भर, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying or upholding a family;<BR>(अस्), m. a wrong form for कुजम्भल, a thief.<BR>—कुल-योषित्, त्, f. a woman of noble family; a<BR>virtuous high-born woman.<BR>—कुल-रक्षक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, preserving a family.<BR>—कुल-रत्न-मालिका,<BR>f. title of a work.<BR>—कुल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, be-<BR>longing to a noble family.<BR>—कुल-वधू, ऊस्, f. a<BR>virtuous wife, a respectable woman, one of good<BR>family.<BR>—कुलवधू-ता, f. virtue in a wife.<BR>—कुल-<BR>वर्णा, f. a species of the plant Convolvulus with<BR>red blossoms, = रक्त-त्रिवृत्.<BR>—कुल-वर्धन or<BR>कुल-वर्धक, अस्, आ, अम्, increasing or advancing<BR>or propagating a family.<BR>—कुल-वार, अस्, m. a<BR>principal day, i. e. Tuesday and Friday.<BR>—कुल-<BR>विद्या, f. knowledge handed down in a family.<BR>—कुल-विप्र, अस्, m. a family priest.<BR>—कुल-<BR>वृद्ध, अस्, m. the oldest member or head of a<BR>family.<BR>—कुल-वृद्धि, इस्, f. family advancement.<BR>—कुल-व्यापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, attaching or applicable to<BR>tribe or caste.<BR>—कुल-व्रत, अम्, n. a family vow.<BR>—कुल-शील, अस्, अम्, m. n. character or conduct<BR>honourable to a family.<BR>—कुल-शील-समन्वित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, endowed with a noble character or disposi-<BR>tion.<BR>—कुल-शेखर, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>Mukunda-mālā.<BR>—कुल-श्रेष्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ, well-<BR>born; of good family, eminent in a family; (ई), m.<BR>the chief of a guild; an artificer or artisan of eminent<BR>birth.<BR>—कुल-सङ्ख्या, f. ranking or being reckoned<BR>as a family, family respectability.<BR>—कुल-सत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a family sacrifice.<BR>—कुल-सन्तति, इस्, f. propa-<BR>gation of a family, posterity, descendants.<BR>—कुल-<BR>सन्निधि, इस्, m. the presence of a number of persons<BR>or of witnesses, kindred, relations.<BR>—कुल-समुद्-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, born in a noble family.<BR>—कुल-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-c" target="_blank">Page0240-c+ 81</a>]<BR>सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from a noble family;<BR>(in compounds) sprung from a family.<BR>—कुल-सार-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—कुल-सुन्दरी,<BR>f., N. of a deity.<BR>—कुल-सेवक, अस्, m. an excellent<BR>attendant or servant.<BR>—कुल-सौरभ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a plant, = मरुवक.<BR>—कुल-स्त्री, f. a woman of<BR>good family, a respectable woman, a chaste or virtuous<BR>wife.<BR>—कुल-स्थिति, इस्, f. antiquity or prosperity of<BR>a family.<BR>—कुलाकुल (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, excel-<BR>lent and not excellent, middling; of mixed character,<BR>of mixed origin; (अस्), m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—कुला-<BR>कुल-तिथि, इस्, m. f. the second, sixth, and tenth<BR>lunar days of a half-month.<BR>—कुलाकुल-नक्षत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of the lunar mansions Ārdrā, Mūlā, Abhi-<BR>jit, and Śatabhiṣā; an asterism of mixed character.<BR>—कुलाकुल-वार, अस्, m. Wednesday.<BR>—कुलाङ्-<BR>गना (˚ल-अङ्˚), f. a woman of good family, a<BR>respectable or chaste woman.<BR>—कुलाङ्गार (˚ल-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘a family firebrand,’ metaphorically a<BR>man who foments domestic dissensions or ruins his<BR>family.<BR>—कुलाचल (˚ल-अच्˚), अस्, m. a principal<BR>mountain, one of a class of seven principal mountains<BR>which are supposed to exist in each Varṣa or division<BR>of a continent; those of Bhārata-varṣa or India are<BR>Mahendra, Malaya, Sahya, Śuktimat, Ṛkṣa, Vin-<BR>dhya, and Pāripātra or Pāriyātra; N. of a Dānava.<BR>—कुलाचार (˚ल-आच्˚), अस्, m. the peculiar or proper<BR>duty of a family or caste.<BR>—कुलाचार्य (˚ल-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a family teacher, a family priest; a person<BR>well versed in the pedigrees and customs of different<BR>families and employed to contract marriages between<BR>them; a genealogist.<BR>—कुलाद्रि (˚ल-अद्˚), इस्, m. a<BR>principal mountain; one of seven principal mountains;<BR>see कुलाचल above.<BR>—कुलाधारक (˚ल-आध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a son; [cf. कुल-धारक.]<BR>—कुलान्वित (˚ल-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from a noble family.<BR>—कुला-<BR>भिमान (˚ल-अभ्˚), अम्, n. pride of birth, family<BR>pride.<BR>—कुलाभिमानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, proud of birth or of<BR>family descent.<BR>—कुलामृत (˚ल-अम्˚), अम्, n. title<BR>of a work.<BR>—कुलार्णव (˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, m. title of a<BR>work.<BR>—कुलार्णव-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—कुलालम्बिन् (˚ल-आल्˚), ई, इनी, इ, supporting or<BR>maintaining a family.<BR>—कुले-चर, अस् or अम् (?), m.<BR>or n. (?) , a kind of plant.<BR>—कुलेश्वर (˚ल-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the chief of a family or race; the lord κατ᾽ ἐξοχήν,<BR>an epithet of Śiva; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—कु-<BR>लोत्कट (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, excellent by birth, high-<BR>born; (अस्), m. a horse of good breed.<BR>—कुलोत्-<BR>कर्ष (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, m. family eminence.<BR>—कुलोत्-<BR>पन्न (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from a good<BR>family, well-born; belonging to a family (as property<BR>&c.).<BR>—कुलोद्गत (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sprung<BR>from a noble family.<BR>—कुलोद्भव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or कुलोद्भूत (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, well-born, of<BR>good family; born or produced in a family.<BR>—कुलोद्-<BR>वह (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. a chief, a leader, the head of a<BR>family.<BR>—कुलोपदेश (˚ल-उप्˚), अस्, m. family name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक|कुलकं|कुलकः
कुलक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a tribe or family, of<BR>good family, of eminent birth; (अस्), m. the chief of a<BR>guild; any artisan of eminent birth; an ant-hill, a mole-<BR>hill; a green snake (हरित-सर्प); N. of several<BR>plants, a kind of ebony, Diospyros Tomentosa; another<BR>species of ebony, commonly called Ku-pīlu; another<BR>plant, = मरुवक, शुक्लपुष्प, तिलक; (अम्),<BR>n. a multitude; a sort of gourd, Trichosanthes<BR>Diœca; a number of stanzas in grammatical con-<BR>nection, several verses in which the government of<BR>noun and verb is carried throughout, contrary to the<BR>practice of closing the sense with each verse; a kind<BR>of prose composition with few compound words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायन
कुलायन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिक|कुलिकः
कुलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, of a good family, well-born;<BR>(अस्), m. a kinsman; the chief or head man of a tribe<BR>or caste; an artist or artificer of high birth; a thorny<BR>plant, Ruellia Longifolia or Asteracantha (Ruellia)<BR>Longifolia; one of the eight chiefs of the Nāgas or<BR>serpent-race, described as having a half-moon on the<BR>top of his head and being of a dusky-brown colour.<BR>—कुलिक-वेला, f. certain portions of each day on<BR>which it is improper to begin any good business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिन्
कुलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belonging to a noble family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0240-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीन|कुलीनः
कुलीन, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of compounds),<BR>belonging to a family; of high or eminent descent,<BR>of a good family, well-born; (अस्), m. a horse of<BR>good breed; a Brāhman of the highest class in Ben-<BR>gal, i. e. a member of one of the eight principal<BR>families of the Vārendra division or of one of the<BR>six chief families of the Rāḍha or Rāṛh division as<BR>classified by Balāl Sen, Rāja of Bengal, in the twelfth<BR>century, (common names of the latter families are<BR>Mukharji, Banarji, Chatoji, &c.); a worshipper of<BR>Śakti according to the left-hand ritual; (आ), f. a<BR>variety of the Āryā metre; (अम्), n. a disease of<BR>the nails.<BR>—कुलीन-ता, f. or कुलीन-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>birth, rank, family respectability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनक|कुलीनकः
कुलीनक, अस्, आ, अम्, of good family; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of wild kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलेय
कुलेय, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of compounds) =<BR>कुलीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्य|कुल्यं|कुल्यः
1. कुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of or relating to a family or<BR>race; belonging to a congregation or corporation; of<BR>good family, well-born, well-descended; (अस्), m. a<BR>respectable man; (आ), f. a virtuous or decent woman;<BR>custom or habit of a family?; (अम्), n. friendly in-<BR>quiry after family affairs or domestic accidents, con-<BR>dolence, congratulation, &c. (For 2. 3. see col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक्क|कुलक्कः
कुलक्क कुलक्क, अस्, m. a cymbal; beating<BR>time in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलङ्गी
कुलङ्गी कुलङ्गी, f. a thorny plant; (a wrong<BR>form for कुलिङ्गी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलञ्ज|कुलञ्जः
कुलञ्ज कुलञ्ज or कुलञ्जन, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Alpinia Galanga, = गन्ध-मूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलट|कुलटः
कुलट कुलट, अस्, m. (fr. कुल and rt. अट्?),<BR>any son except one's own offspring, an adopted son,<BR>a bought son, &c.; (आ), f. an unchaste woman.<BR>—कुलटा-पति, इस्, m. the husband of an unchaste<BR>woman, a cuckold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलटी
कुलटी कुलटी, f. red arsenic, = कुनटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलति
कुलति कुलति, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलत्थ|कुलत्थः
कुलत्थ कुलत्थ, अस्, m. (fr. कुल? cf. अश्-<BR>वत्थ and कपित्थ), a kind of pulse, Dolichos<BR>Uniflorus; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. a kind<BR>of Dolichos; a blue stone used in medicine and ap-<BR>plied as a collyrium to the eyes, also as an astringent<BR>to sores &c.; a species of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलत्थिका
कुलत्थिका, f. a blue stone used as a collyrium<BR>&c.; a sort of vetch, considered as a wild sort of the<BR>Dolichos Uniflorus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलभ
कुलभ कुलभ, अस्, m., N. of a Daitya;<BR>(another reading has सुलभ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलहण्डक|कुलहंडकः|कुलहण्डकः
