कुल्या 2. कुल्या, f., N. of a drug or medi-<BR>cinal plant, Celtis Orientalis (जीवन्तिकौषधि);<BR>another plant, Solanum Longum (स्थूलावार्ताक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्लूक|कुल्लूकः
कुल्लूक कुल्लूक or कुल्लूक-भट्ट, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a celebrated scholiast on Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्व
कुल्व कुल्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bald, bare<BR>[Lat. calvus] in अति-कुल्व, too bald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्वक|कुल्वकं
कुल्वक कुल्वक, अम्, n. fur upon the tongue;<BR>[cf. कुवुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव|कुवं
कुव कुव, अम्, n. a water-lily, a lotus; [cf.<BR>कुवल, कुवलय, कुवेल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवकालुका
कुवकालुका कुवकालुका, f., N. of a vegeta-<BR>ble (घोली-शाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवङ्ग|कुवंग|कुवङ्गं|कुवङ्गः
कुवङ्ग कु-वङ्ग, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवच|कुवचः
कुवच कु-वच, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), abusive,<BR>censorius, scurrilous, using bad language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवज्रक|कुवज्रकं
कुवज्रक कु-वज्रक, अम्, n. (see 1. कु),<BR>crystal, a stone resembling a diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवद
कुवद कु-वद, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), cen-<BR>sorious; [cf. कु-वच.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवम|कुवमः
कुवम कुवम, अस्, m. a N. of Kaśyapa (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवर|कुवरः
कुवर कुवर, अस्, आ, अम्, astringent in fla-<BR>vour; [cf. तुवर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवर्ष|कुवर्षः
कुवर्ष कु-वर्ष, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a shower<BR>of rain, a sudden and violent shower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवल|कुवलं
कुवल कुवल or कुबल, अस्, ई, m. f. the<BR>jujube tree, Zizyphus Jujuba; (अम्), n. the fruit of<BR>this tree; the water-lily; a pearl; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>pearl.<BR>—कुवल-कुण, अस्, m. the time when the<BR>tree Zizyphus Jujuba bears fruits.<BR>—कुवल-प्रस्थ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR>—कुवलाश्व or कुबलाश्व<BR>(˚ल-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince with the epithet<BR>Dhundhumāra.<BR>—कुवले-शय, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu (‘resting on a water-lily’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलय|कुवलयं
कुवलय कुवलय, अम्, n. any water-lily;<BR>the blue water-lily; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the earth; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of the horse of Kuvalayāśva.<BR>—कुवलय-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—कुवलयादित्य<BR>(˚य-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince, = कुवलयापीड.<BR>—कुवलयानन्द (˚य-आन्˚), अस्, m. title of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">Page0242-a+ 68</a>]<BR>work on rhetoric by Apyadīkṣita.<BR>—कुवलयापीड<BR>(˚य-आप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Daitya, who, changed to<BR>an elephant, became the vehicle of Kaṃsa; N. of a<BR>prince; [cf. कुवलयादित्य.]<BR>—कुवलयावली (˚य-<BR>अव्˚), f., N. of a princess.<BR>—कुवलयाश्व (˚य-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a prince with the epithet Dhundhu-<BR>māra; an epithet of the prince Pratardana.<BR>—कुवल-<BR>याश्वक, अस्, m., N. of a prince with the epithet<BR>Dhundhumāra.<BR>—कुवलयाश्व-चरित, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>adventures of Kuvalayāśva,’ title of a Prākṛt poem<BR>composed by Viśvanātha Kavirāja.<BR>—कुवलयाश्वीय,<BR>अम्, n. the story of Kuvalayāśva.<BR>—कुवलयेश<BR>(˚य-ईश), अस्, m. a ruler of the earth, a king.<BR>—कु-<BR>वलयेश-ता, f. kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0241-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलयित
कुवलयित, अस्, आ, अम्, decorated with water-<BR>lilies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलयिनी
कुवलयिनी, f. an assemblage of water-lilies, a<BR>place abounding with them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाक्य
कुवाक्य कु-वाक्य, अम्, n. or कु-वाच्, क्, f.<BR>(see 1. कु), injurious or censorious language, speak-<BR>ing ill of any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाट|कुवाटः
कुवाट कुवाट, अस्, m. the fold of a door,<BR>= कवाट and कपाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाद|कुवादः
कुवाद कु-वाद, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), de-<BR>tracting, censorious, one who speaks ill of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाहुल|कुवाहुलः
कुवाहुल कुवाहुल, अस्, m. a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविक
कुविक कुविक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविद्
कुविद् कुविद्, ind. (fr. 1. कु and इद्), Ved.<BR>a particle of interrogation, ‘if, whether;’ or used in<BR>direct questions; (a verb following this particle does<BR>not lose its accent.)<BR>—कुवित्-स, अस्, m., Ved. any<BR>one, an unknown person; (Sāy.) N. of a man (‘much<BR>destroying’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविन्द|कुविंद|कुविंदः|कुविन्दः
कुविन्द कुविन्द or कुविन्दक, अस्, m. a<BR>weaver, = कुपिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविवाह|कुविवाहः
कुविवाह कु-विवाह, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>degrading or improper marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवीणा
कुवीणा कु-वीणा, f. (see 1. कु), the lute of<BR>the Cāṇḍālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवीर
कुवीर कुवीर, अस्, m. or आ, f. (?), N. of a<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवृत्तिकृत्
कुवृत्तिकृत् कुवृत्ति-कृत्, m. the plant Cæ-<BR>salpinia Bonducella (= पूतिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेणा
कुवेणा कु-वेणा, f. (see 1. कु), N. of a river;<BR>a fish-basket; (various reading for the following.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेणी
कु-वेणी, f. a fish-basket; a badly braided tress of<BR>hair; a woman with her hair badly braided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेर|कुवेरः
कुवेर कुवेर, &c. See under कुबेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेल|कुवेलं
कुवेल कुवेल, अम्, n. a water-lily, = कुव-<BR>लय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवैद्य|कुवैद्यः
कुवैद्य कु-वैद्य, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव्र
कुव्र कुव्र, अम्, n. a forest, a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश्
कुश् कुश्, cl. 4. P. कुश्यति, to embrace,<BR>enfold; (a various reading for कुस्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश|कुशं|कुशः
कुश कुश, अस्, m. (used in Sūtra works, but<BR>the word दर्भ is more common in the Brāh-<BR>maṇas), grass, especially the sacred grass used at certain<BR>religious ceremonies (i. e. Poa Cynosuroides, a grass<BR>with long stalks and numerous pointed leaves); a<BR>rope made of Kuśa grass used for connecting the yoke<BR>of a plough with the pole; N. of a son of Vasu Upa-<BR>ricara; of a soñ of Balākāśva, grandson of Balāka,<BR>father of Kuśāmba and Kuśanābha; of a son of Su-<BR>hotra [cf. काश]; of a son of Vidarbha; of a son of<BR>Rāma; of a son of Lava, king of Kaśmīra; one of the<BR>great Dvīpas or divisions of the universe, surrounded<BR>by the sea of liquified butter; (आ), f. a plank for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-b" target="_blank">Page0242-b+ 79</a>]<BR>covering anything; a piece of wood; a horse's bridle;<BR>N. of a plant, commonly called Madhukarkaṭikā;<BR>(ई), f. a sort of boat or ladle used in making libations;<BR>wrought iron; a ploughshare; a pod of cotton;<BR>(अम्), n. water; (अस्, आ, अम्), wicked, depraved;<BR>mad, inebriate.<BR>—कुश-चीर, अम्, n. a garment made<BR>of Kuśa grass; (अस्, आ, अम्), covered with a garment<BR>made of Kuśa grass; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—कुश-<BR>द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of one of the seven large Dvīpas<BR>or divisions of the universe.<BR>—कुश-धारा, f., N. of<BR>a river.<BR>—कुश-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a prince, a son<BR>of Hrasva-roman; also a grandson of the latter; N.<BR>of a grandson of Vṛṣadhvaja.<BR>—कुश-नगर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the town in which Śākya-muni died.<BR>—कुश-<BR>नाभ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kuśa.<BR>—कुश-नेत्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR>—कुश-पुष्प, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a plant (= ग्रन्थि-पर्ण), a perfume so called.<BR>—कुश-प्लवन, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—कुश-<BR>मुष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, having the hand full of sacrificial<BR>grass.<BR>—कुश-लव, औ, m. du. the two sons of<BR>Rāma, called Kuśa and Lava.<BR>—कुश-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, covered with Kuśa grass; (ती), f., N. of a town.<BR>—कुश-वारि, n. water in which Kuśa grass has<BR>been soaked.<BR>—कुश-विन्दु, अवस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—कुश-वीरा, f., N. of a river; (a various<BR>reading for कुश-चीरा.)<BR>—कुश-स्तम्ब, अस्, m. a<BR>heap of Kuśa grass; N. of a Tīrtha; N. of a prince.<BR>—कुश-स्तव, अस्, m. a bundle of Kuśa grass.<BR>—कुश-स्थल, अम्, n. an epithet of the town<BR>Kānyakubja; (ई), f. an epithet of the town Dvārakā.<BR>—कुश-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having Kuśa grass in the<BR>hand or in the paw (as applied to the tiger in the<BR>Hitopadeśa).<BR>—कुशाकर (˚श-आक्˚), अस्, m. fire (the<BR>sacrificial fire being made upon a tuft of the Kuśa grass).<BR>—कुशाक्ष (˚श-अक्˚), अस्, m. a monkey, an ape.<BR>—कुशाग्र (˚श-अग्˚), अम्, n. the sharp point of a<BR>blade of the Kuśa grass; (अस्), m., N. of a prince, the<BR>son of Bṛhadratha; (अस्, आ, अम्), sharp, shrewd,<BR>intelligent.<BR>—कुशाग्र-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, sharp as<BR>the point of Kuśa grass, shrewd, intelligent; (इस्), f.<BR>shrewdness, subtlety; also similar compounds, as कुशा-<BR>ग्र-धी, &c.<BR>—कुशाग्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, sharp as the<BR>point of Kuśa grass, subtile, penetrating.<BR>—कुशा-<BR>ग्रीय-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, of subtile intellect, subtile,<BR>sharp-sighted, intelligent, possessing mental acumen;<BR>also other similar compounds, as कुशाग्रीय-धी,<BR>कुशाग्रीय-बुद्धि, &c.<BR>—कुशाङ्कुर (˚श-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a blade of sacrificial grass.<BR>—कुशाङ्गुरीय or<BR>कुशाङ्गुरीयक (˚श-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a ring of Kuśa<BR>grass worn at religious ceremonies.<BR>—कुशारणि (˚श-<BR>अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘one who may be irritated by a Kuśa<BR>blade,’ epithet of the sage Durvāsas, famous for his<BR>irascibility.<BR>—कुशा-वती, f., N. of a town, the resi-<BR>dence of Kuśa, son of Rāma.<BR>—कुशावर्त (˚श-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Tīrtha, or passage of the Gan-<BR>ges, personified as a son of Ṛṣabha.<BR>—कुशाश्व<BR>(˚श-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कुशासन (˚श-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. a small mat of sacrificial grass on<BR>which a Brāhman sits when performing his devo-<BR>tion.<BR>—कुशे-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, lying in grass or in<BR>water; (अस्), m. a kind of tree, = कर्णिकार; the<BR>Indian crane; N. of a mountain in Kuśa-dvīpa; (अम्),<BR>n. ‘lying in water,’ a water-lily, a lotus.<BR>—कुशेशय-<BR>कर, अस्, m. the sun.<BR>—कुशोत्तर (˚श-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, covered with sacrificial grass.<BR>—कुशोदक<BR>(˚श-उद्˚), अम्, n. water in which Kuśa grass has<BR>been infused; (आ), f., N. of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशय|कुशयः
कुशय or कुशप, अस्, m. a drinking-vessel, a<BR>cup, a goblet, a cistern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशित|कुशितं
कुशित, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed or combined with<BR>water; [cf. कुषित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिन्
कुशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with Kuśa grass; (ई),<BR>m. an epithet of Vālmīki (so called with reference to<BR>Kuśa, the son of Rāma).<BR>—कुशि-ग्रामक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a village of the Mallas.<BR>—कुशि-नगर, अम्, or<BR>ई, n. or f., N. of the capital of the Mallas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशज
कुशज कुशज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(a various reading for कुशल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशण्ड
कुशण्ड कुशण्ड, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशनामन्
कुशनामन् कुशनामन्, आ, m. a camel; (pro-<BR>bably a wrong form for शिशु-नामन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशनार
कुशनार कुशनार, a various reading for<BR>कुश-धारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशय|कुशयः
कुशय कुशय or कुशप. See last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशर
कुशर कु-शर, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), Ved. a<BR>kind of reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशरीर
कुशरीर कु-शरीर, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>body; (अस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशल|कुशलं|कुशलः
कुशल कुशल, अस्, आ, अम् (connected with<BR>कुश?), right, proper, suitable, good (e. g. कुशलम्<BR>मन्, to consider good, to approve), well, healthy,<BR>in good condition; happy, prosperous; fit for, com-<BR>petent, able, skilful, expert, clever, conversant with<BR>anything (with loc., gen., inf., and in compounds, e. g.<BR>उद्गीथे or उद्गीथस्य कुशलः, clever in song;<BR>कुशलो व्याख्यातुम्, competent to explain; अश्व-<BR>कुशल, skilled in horses); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people, the inhabitants of Kuśa-dvīpa; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; N. of a prince; also of a grammarian,<BR>author of the Pañjikāpradīpa; (आ), f., N. of a woman;<BR>(ई), f. a plant, = अश्मन्तक; another plant, = क्षु-<BR>द्राम्लिका; (अम्), n. welfare, well-being; a good or<BR>happy or prosperous condition, happiness; virtue,<BR>virtuous action; cleverness, competence, ability; fitness;<BR>due order; कुशलम् प्रछ्, to ask after another's<BR>welfare, to say ‘how do you do?’ कुशलं ते, hail<BR>to thee! (used as a salutation, especially in greeting a<BR>Brāhman); कुशलम् or कुशलेन, ind. well, in a<BR>proper manner, properly, rightly; happily, cheerfully.<BR>—कुशल-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of happiness;<BR>(अस्), m. desire for happiness.<BR>—कुशल-ता, f. or<BR>कुशल-त्व, अम्, n. cleverness, ability, conversancy,<BR>experience; skilfulness, well-being.<BR>—कुशल-प्रश्न,<BR>अस्, m. friendly enquiry after a person's health or<BR>welfare; salutation, greeting, saying ‘how do you do?’<BR>—कुशल-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, wise, able, intelligent.<BR>—कुशल-सागर, अस्, m., N. of a scribe, pupil of<BR>Lāvaṇyaratna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलिन्
कुशलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, healthy, well, happy, prosperous;<BR>auspicious, favourable, good; virtuous; clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलीकृ
कुशली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>right or proper, to arrange in due order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाध्य
कुशाध्य कुशाध्य or कुशाढ्य (?), आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a people; (a various reading for कुलाद्य;<BR>cf. also कुशाण्ड.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाम्ब
कुशाम्ब कुशाम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Vasu Uparicara; N. of a son of Kuśa, who was the<BR>founder of the town Kauśāmbī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाम्बु
कुशाम्बु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Kuśa, the<BR>founder of Kauśāmbī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाल्मलि|कुशाल्मलिः
कुशाल्मलि कु-शाल्मलि, इस्, m. (see 1. कु), the<BR>plant Andersonia Rohitaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिंशपा
कुशिंशपा कु-शिंशपा, f. a kind of Sisu<BR>tree, Dalbergia Sisu, = कपिल-शिंशपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिक|कुशिकः
कुशिक कुशिक, अस्, आ, अम्, squint-eyed; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of the father of Viśvā-mitra; N. of the father of<BR>Gāthin or Gādhi or Gādhin, the latter being sometimes<BR>identified with Indra, who is called Kauśika or Kuśi-<BR>kottama; (according to the Mahā-bhārata and Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa, Viśvā-mitra is son of Gādhi and grandson of<BR>Kuśika); (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Kuśika; N. of<BR>a people; (अस्), m. a ploughshare (in this sense more<BR>properly n.); the sediment of oil; the plant Shorea<BR>Robusta; also Terminalia Bellerica (विभीतक); also<BR>Vatica Robusta (अश्व-कर्ण).<BR>—कुशिकन्-धर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशित|कुशितं
कुशित कुशित, &c. See under कुश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिम्बि
कुशिम्बि कु-शिम्बि, इस्, m. or f. (?), (see 1.<BR>कु), N. of a plant; [cf. शिम्ब, शिम्बि, and कुसिम्बी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीद|कुशीदं
कुशीद कुशीद, अम्, n. the profession of<BR>usury; red saunders; [cf. कुसीद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0242-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशील
कुशील कु-शील, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), ill-<BR>behaved, rude, wicked; evil-disposed; ill-tempered.<BR>—कुशील-ता, f. or कुशील-त्व, अम्, n. misbehaviour,<BR>misconduct; bad disposition; ill-temper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीलव|कुशीलवः
कुशीलव कुशीलव, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>कु-शील?), a bard, herald; an actor, dancer, mime;<BR>a newsmonger; an epithet of Vālmīki; (औ), m. du.<BR>the two sons of Rāma, Kuśa and Lava, who recited<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa, (probably these names were originally<BR>formed from the word Kuśīlava); [cf. कुश-लव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीवश|कुशीवशः
कुशीवश कुशीवश, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Vālmīki; [cf. कुशिन् and कुशीलव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशुम्भ|कुशुंभ|कुशुंभः|कुशुम्भः
कुशुम्भ कुशुम्भ, अस्, m. a jar; the water-<BR>pot of an ascetic; [cf. कुसुम्भ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूल|कुशूलः
कुशूल कुशूल, अस्, m. (fr. 1. कु and शूल?),<BR>a granary, a cupboard, a store-room, a place in which<BR>rice or other grain is kept; a conflagration of chaff.<BR>—कुशूल-धान्य, अम्, n. grain stored for three<BR>years' consumption.<BR>—कुशूल-धान्यक, अस्, m. a<BR>householder &c. who has three years' grain in store.<BR>—कुशूल-पूरणाढक (˚ण-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being (like to mere empty) measures filling a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशेशय|कुशेशयं|कुशेशयः
