कुश्रि|कुश्रिः
कुश्रि कुश्रि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश्रुत
कुश्रुत कु-श्रुत, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), in-<BR>distinctly heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश्वभ्र
कुश्वभ्र कु-श्वभ्र, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), a<BR>small hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्
कुष् कुष्, cl. 9. P. कुष्णाति, चुकोष,<BR>कोषिष्यति, अकोषीत्, कोषितुम्, to tear,<BR>tear asunder, to force or draw out, to extract, to expel;<BR>to test, assay, examine; to shine: Pass. कुष्यति<BR>and कुष्यते: Caus. कोषयति: Desid. चुकोषि-<BR>षति and चुकुषिषति: Intens. चोकुष्यते, चो-<BR>कोष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषण्ड
कुषण्ड कु-षण्ड, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), N. of<BR>a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषल|कुषलः
कुषल कुषल, अस्, आ, अम्, clever, expert,<BR>&c.; (a wrong reading for कुशल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषवा
कुषवा कुषवा, f., Ved., N. of a Rākṣasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषाकु|कुषाकुः
कुषाकु कुषाकु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. कुष्?),<BR>burning, scorching, inflaming; wicked, detestable;<BR>(उस्), m. fire; the sun; a monkey; [cf. कषाकु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषारु
कुषारु कुषारु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषित्
कुषित् कुषित्, ind. excellently; (for कुवित्?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषित|कुषितः
कुषित कुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed with water<BR>[cf. कुशित]; (अम्), n. happy, well, right, fortunate,<BR>auspicious, &c. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषीतक
कुषीतक कुषीतक, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>bird; N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of<BR>this man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषीद|कुषीदं
कुषीद कु-षीद, अस्, आ, अम्, indifferent, apa-<BR>thetic, inert; (अम्), n. usury; (more correctly कु-<BR>सीद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषीदिन्
कुषीदिन् कुषीदिन्, ई, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषुभ्य
कुषुभ्य कुषुभ्य, nom. P. कुषुभ्यति, to<BR>throw; to abuse; to despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषुम्भ
कुषुम्भ कुषुम्भ, अस्, m., Ved. the poison-<BR>bag of an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठ|कुष्ठं|कुष्ठः
कुष्ठ कुष्ठ, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (fr. 1. कु<BR>and स्थ?), a sort of medicinal plant (used as a remedy<BR>for the disease called तक्मन्, q. v.), Costus Speciosus<BR>or Arabicus; a sort of poison; leprosy, of which<BR>eighteen varieties are enumerated, seven severe and<BR>eleven of minor importance; (आ), f. the mouth or open-<BR>ing of a basket.<BR>—कुष्ठ-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">Page0243-b+ 71</a>]<BR>= भूम्याहुल्य.<BR>—कुष्ठ-गन्धि, n. the fra-<BR>grant bark of the plant Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—कुष्-<BR>ठ-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, curing leprosy; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a medicinal plant, commonly called Hiyāvalī [cf.<BR>हितावली]; (ई), f. an esculent root, Solanum Indicum,<BR>= काकमाची; the opposite leaved fig tree.<BR>—कुष्-<BR>ठ-चिकित्सित, अम्, n. the cure of leprosy.<BR>—कुष्ठ-<BR>नाशन, अस्, m., N. of several plants which cure<BR>leprosy; the root of Dioscorea; white pepper or<BR>mustard; another plant, = क्षीरीश-वृक्ष.<BR>—कु-<BR>ष्ठ-नाशिनी, f. a plant, commonly Hākuca, Psoralia<BR>Corylifolia.<BR>—कुष्ठ-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, full of<BR>leprosy, leprous.<BR>—कुष्ठ-रोग, अस्, m. leprosy,<BR>elephantiasis.<BR>—कुष्ठ-सूदन, अस्, m. the Cassia<BR>tree, Cassia Fistula; [cf. आरग्बध.]<BR>—कुष्ठ-<BR>हन्तृ, ता, m. a kind of bulbous plant, = हस्ति-<BR>कन्द; (त्री), f. another plant, generally called<BR>Vākucī.<BR>—कुष्ठ-हृत्, त्, m. the plant Acacia<BR>Catechu.<BR>—कुष्ठाङ्ग (˚ठ-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>leprous.<BR>—कुष्ठान्वित (˚ठ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>afflicted with leprosy.<BR>—कुष्ठारि (˚ठ-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. Acacia Catechu; another plant, Acacia Farnesiana<BR>(विट्खदिर); another plant, Trichosanthes Diœca,<BR>= पटोल; another plant, = आदित्य-पत्त्र and<BR>अर्क-पत्त्र; sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठित
कुष्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, or कुष्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>leprous, a leper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठल|कुष्ठलं
कुष्ठल कु-ष्ठल, अम्, n. (fr. 1. or 2. कु and<BR>स्थल), a bad place or spot; the surface of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठिका
कुष्ठिका कुष्ठिका, आस्, f. pl. (related to कुष्-<BR>ठा?), Ved. a part of the foot of a sacrificial animal<BR>considered worthless for sacrificial purposes; (Sāy.)<BR>the contents of the entrails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्मल|कुष्मलं
कुष्मल कुष्मल, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कुष्), cutting, dividing; a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्माण्ड|कुष्मांड|कुष्मांडः|कुष्माण्डः
कुष्माण्ड कुष्माण्ड, अस्, m. a kind of pump-<BR>kin-gourd, Benincasa Cerifera; false conception; a<BR>state of the womb in gestation (?); a particular re-<BR>ligious formula; a class of demons; one of a class<BR>of demi-gods attached to Śiva; (ई), f. the gourd Be-<BR>nincasa Cerifera, a drug; a religious ceremony, a<BR>certain rite, performed as a penance or expiation; an<BR>epithet of the wife of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्माण्डक|कुष्मांडक|कुष्मांडकः|कुष्माण्डकः
कुष्माण्डक, अस्, m. the gourd Benincasa Ceri-<BR>fera; N. of a Nāga; N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्
कुस् कुस्, cl. 4. P. कुस्यति, to embrace,<BR>surround; [cf. कुश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसचिव
कुसचिव कु-सचिव, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>bad counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसरित्
कुसरित् कु-सरित्, त्, f. (see 1. कु), a shallow<BR>stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसलम्
कुसलम् कुसलम्, ind. well, happy, &c.;<BR>(more correctly कुशल, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसहाय
कुसहाय कु-सहाय, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>bad companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसारथि
कुसारथि कु-सारथि, इस्, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>bad charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसित|कुसितः
कुसित कुसित, अस्, m. (said to be fr. कुस्),<BR>an inhabited country; N. of a country; a money-<BR>lender (?), see कुसीद.<BR>—कुसितायी, f. the wife of a<BR>money-lender (?); [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसिदायी
कुसिदायी कुसिदायी, f. the wife of a Kusida, of<BR>a money-lender (?), see कुसीदायी; a kind of demon (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसिन्ध
कुसिन्ध कुसिन्ध, अम्, n., Ved. a trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसिम्बी
कुसिम्बी कुसिम्बी, f. = शिम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीद|कुसीदं|कुसीदः
कुसीद कु-सीद, अस्, आ, अम् (see 1. कु), Ved.<BR>sitting too long in one spot (?), lazy, slothful, inert;<BR>(अम्), n. any loan or thing lent to be repaid with<BR>interest; lending money; usury, the profession of<BR>usury; (अस्, आ), m. f. a money-lender, a usurer.<BR>—कुसीद-पथ, अस्, m. usury, usurious interest,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">Page0243-c+ 79</a>]<BR>any exceeding five per cent.<BR>—कुसीद-वृद्धि, इस्,<BR>f. interest on money.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदायी
कुसीदायी, f. the wife of a usurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदिक|कुसीदिकः
कुसीदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who follows the pro-<BR>fession of usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदिन्
कुसीदिन्, ई, m. a usurer; N. of a descendant of<BR>Kaṇva, author of several hymns of the Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम|कुसुमं|कुसुमः
कुसुम कुसुम, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. कुस्), a flower; (अम्), n. fruit; the menstrual dis-<BR>charge; a term for the shorter sections of Deveśvara's<BR>Kavi-kalpalatā (the longer chapters being called<BR>Stavaka); ophthalmia, disease of the eyes; (अस्), m.<BR>a form of fire; N. of the attendant of the sixth<BR>Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR>—कुसुम-कार्-<BR>मुक or कुसुम-चाप, अस्, m. or कुसुम-धन्-<BR>वन्, आ, m. ‘having flowers for his bow,’ epithet of Kāma,<BR>the god of love.<BR>—कुसुम-केतुमण्डलिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a Kinnara.<BR>—कुसुम-कोमल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>tender as a flower.<BR>—कुसुम-चित, अस्, आ, अम्, heaped<BR>with flowers.<BR>—कुसुम-देव, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—कुसुम-नग, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—कुसुम-पुर, अम्, n., N. of the town Pāṭali-<BR>putra.<BR>—कुसुम-मध्य, अम्, n., N. of a tree<BR>bearing a large acid fruit, commonly Cālitā gāc, Cor-<BR>dia Myxa or Dillenia Indica.<BR>—कुसुम-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, consisting of flowers.<BR>—कुसुम-लता, f. a<BR>creeper in blossom.<BR>—कुसुम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, fur-<BR>nished with flowers, flowering, in flower; (ती), f. a<BR>female during menstruation; N. of the town Pāṭali-<BR>putra.<BR>—कुसुम-वाण, अस्, m. the flower-arrow of<BR>the god of love; ‘flower-arrowed,’ epithet of Kāma,<BR>the god of love, as having flowers for arrows.<BR>—कु-<BR>सुम-विचित्रा, f., N. of a metre consisting of four<BR>lines of twelve syllables each.<BR>—कुसुम-शयन,<BR>अम्, n. a couch of flowers.<BR>—कुसुम-शर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘flower-arrowed,’ epithet of the god of love.<BR>—कुसुमशर-त्व, अम्, n. the state of one who<BR>has flowers for arrows.<BR>—कुसुम-शेखर-विजय,<BR>अस्, m. title of a play.<BR>—कुसुम-सनाथ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, possessed of flowers, having flowers.<BR>—कुसुम-<BR>स्तवक, अस्, m. a bunch of flowers, a nosegay, bou-<BR>quet, a garland; N. of a metre.<BR>—कुसुमाकर<BR>(˚म-आक्˚), अस्, m. a quantity of flowers or place<BR>abounding with them, a parterre, a garden, a nosegay;<BR>spring, the vernal season.<BR>—कुसुमाञ्जन (˚म-<BR>अञ्˚), अम्, n. the calx of brass, used as a collyrium.<BR>—कुसुमाञ्जलि (˚म-अञ्˚), इस्, f. ‘handful of flow-<BR>ers,’ the title of a philosophical work written to prove<BR>the existence of a Supreme being, by Udayana Āchārya,<BR>consisting of seventy-two Kārikās divided into five<BR>chapters.<BR>—कुसुमाञ्जलि-मकरन्द, अस्, m. title<BR>of a commentary by Rucidatta on the preceding work.<BR>—कुसुमात्मक (˚म-आत्˚), अम्, n. saffron.<BR>—कु-<BR>सुमाधिप (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘the prince of<BR>flowers,’ the champa, a tree which bears a yellow<BR>fragrant flower, Michelia Champaka.<BR>—कुसुमा-<BR>धिराज् (˚म-अध्˚), ट्, m. the same plant.<BR>—कु-<BR>सुमायुध (˚म-आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘flower-armed,’ an<BR>epithet of Kāma, the god of love, his arrows being<BR>tipped with flowers.<BR>—कुसुमावचाय (˚म-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. gathering flowers.<BR>—कुसुमावतंसक (˚म-<BR>अव्˚), अम्, n. a chaplet, a crown of flowers.<BR>—कुसु-<BR>मावली (˚म-अव्˚), f. title of a medicinal work.<BR>—कुसुमासव (˚म-आस्˚), अम्, n. honey.<BR>—कु-<BR>सुमास्त्र (˚म-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘flower-arrowed,’ epi-<BR>thet of the god of love.<BR>—कुसुमेषु (˚म-इषु),<BR>उस्, m. = कुसुमास्त्र above; (उ), n. the bow of<BR>Kāma.<BR>—कुसुमोज्ज्वल (˚म-उज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bril-<BR>liant with blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमय
कुसुमय, nom. P. कुसुमयति, -यितुम्, to pro-<BR>duce flowers, cause to flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमित
कुसुमित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with flowers,<BR>flowered, budded, in flower.<BR>—कुसुमित-लता, f. or<BR>कुसुमितलता-वेल्लिता, f., N. of a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of eighteen syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम्य
कुसुम्य, nom. P. कुसुम्यति, to begin to flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाल|कुसुमालः
कुसुमाल कुसुमाल, अस्, m. a thief (fr. कु-<BR>सुम + आल, ‘living among flowers?’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम्भ|कुसुंभ|कुसुंभं|कुसुम्भं|कुसुंभः|कुसुम्भः
कुसुम्भ कुसुम्भ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">Page0244-a+ 70</a>]<BR>fr. rt. कुस्), safflower, Carthamus Tinctorius; saffron,<BR>Crocus Sativus; the water-pot of the student and<BR>Sannyāsin; (अम्), n. gold; (अस्), m. outward affec-<BR>tion, compared with the colour of safflower; N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—कुसुम्भ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished<BR>with a jar or water-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुरुविन्द
कुसुरुविन्द कुसुरुविन्द or कुसुरुबिन्द, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a descendant of Uddālaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुरुबिन्दु
कुसुरुबिन्दु or कुसुरुविन्दु, उस्, m., N. of an<BR>author of several verses of the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसू
कुसू कुसू, ऊस्, m. an earth-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसूल|कुसूलः
कुसूल कुसूल, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of spiri-<BR>tual or supernatural being; a granary &c. See<BR>कुशूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसृति|कुसृतिः
कुसृति कु-सृति, इस्, f. (see 1. कु), evil con-<BR>duct, wickedness, depravity; conjuring, sleight-of-<BR>hand, magic; (इस्, इस्, इ), going evil ways, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुभ|कुस्तुभः
कुस्तुभ कुस्तुभ, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu (derived fr. कौस्तुभ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बरी
कुस्तुम्बरी कुस्तुम्बरी, f. a pungent seed<BR>used in condiments, coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बरु
कुस्तुम्बरु कुस्तुम्बरु, उस्, m., N. of one of<BR>Kubera's attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बुरु|कुस्तुम्बुरुः
कुस्तुम्बुरु कुस्तुम्बुरु, उस्, m. (said to be fr.<BR>1. कु and तुम्बुरु), the plant coriander; (उ), n.<BR>the seed of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्त्री
कुस्त्री कु-स्त्री, f. (see 1. कु), a bad woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्मय
कुस्मय कुस्मय (fr. कु-स्मय), nom. A.<BR>कुस्मयते, to smile improperly; to see mentally,<BR>guess; to perceive, to imagine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्वप्न
कुस्वप्न कु-स्वप्न, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), a bad<BR>dream, a nightmare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्वामिन्
कुस्वामिन् कु-स्वामिन्, ई, m. (see 1. कु), a<BR>bad master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह्
कुह् कुह्, cl. 10. A. कुहयते, -यितुम्, to<BR>surprise, astonish; to excite wonder, to cheat,<BR>to deceive by trickery or jugglery, impose upon<BR>(related to गुह्?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह|कुहः
1. कुह, अस्, m. an epithet of Kuvera; a rogue, a<BR>cheat (in अ-कुह, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहक|कुहकं|कुहकः
कुहक, अस्, आ, अम्, cheating, a cheat, a rogue, a<BR>juggler; (अस्), m. a frog; N. of a king of the serpent-<BR>race; (अम्, आ), n. f. juggling, deception, sleight-of-<BR>hand, legerdemain.<BR>—कुहक-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, or<BR>कुहक-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, or कुहक-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, practising jugglery or conjuring, cheating.<BR>—कुहक-चकित, अस्, आ, अम्, afraid of a trick,<BR>suspicious, cautious, wary.<BR>—कुहक-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>living by sleight-of-hand, a conjurer, a cheat, &c.<BR>—कुहक-वृत्ति, इस्, f. juggling, conjuring, sleight-<BR>of-hand; hypocrisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहन|कुहनं|कुहनः
कुहन, अस्, आ, अम्, envious, hypocritical; (अस्),<BR>m. a mouse, a rat; a snake; N. of a man; (आ), f.<BR>hypocrisy; assumed and false sanctity; the interested<BR>performance of religious austerities; (अम्), n. a small<BR>earthen vessel; a glass vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहनिका
कुहनिका, f. hypocrisy &c.; [cf. the preceding.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह|कुहः
कुह 2. कुह, ind. (fr. 1. कु), Ved. where?<BR>कुह चिद्, wherever, anywhere, somewhere, to any<BR>place.<BR>—कुहचिद्-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. being everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहया
कुहया, ind., Ved. where?<BR>—कुहया-कृति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. where active?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकस्वन|कुहकस्वनः
कुहकस्वन कुहक-स्वन or कुहक-स्वर,<BR>अस्, m. (कुहक being here an onomatopoetic word),<BR>a wild cock, Phasianus Gallus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहर|कुहरं|कुहरः
कुहर कुहर, अस्, m. (fr. कुह् = गुह्?), N.<BR>of a serpent belonging to the Krodhavaśa race;<BR>(अम्), n. a cavity, hollow; a hole, rent; the ear;<BR>the throat or larynx; a guttural sound; proximity;<BR>copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहरित|कुहरितं
कुहरित कुहरित, अम्, n. noise, a sound in<BR>general; especially the song or cry of the Kokila or<BR>Indian cuckoo; a sound uttered in copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहलि|कुहलिः
कुहलि कुहलि, इस्, m. the leaf of the Piper<BR>Betel (commonly called Pān) with small pieces of<BR>the Areca-nut and Catechu and a little lime, which<BR>are chewed and eaten by the people of the East and<BR>especially offered to the persons present at a matri-<BR>monial ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहा
कुहा कुहा, f., N. of a plant, also called<BR>Kaṭukī.<BR>—कुहा-वती, f. an epithet of the goddess<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहारीत
कुहारीत कु-हारीत, अस्, m. (see 1. कु), N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहु|कुहुः
कुहु कुहु, उस्, f. the new moon; N. of a<BR>river; the cry of the Kokila; [cf. कुहू.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहुकुहाय
कुहुकुहाय कुहुकुहाय (fr. कुहु-कुह for<BR>कुह-कुह, where? where?), nom. A. कुहुकुहा-<BR>यते, to show one's admiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहू
कुहू कुहू, ऊस्, f. (fr. कुह् = गुह्?), the new<BR>moon, personified as a daughter of Aṅgiras; the<BR>first day of the first quarter on which the moon rises<BR>invisible; N. of one of the seven rivers of Plaksha-<BR>dvīpa; the cry or song of the Kokila or Indian<BR>cuckoo.<BR>—कुहू-कण्ठ or कुहूक, अस्, m. the<BR>Kokila or Indian cuckoo, κοκκύ<BR>—कुहू-पाल, अस्,<BR>m. the king of turtles, the tortoise supposed to up-<BR>hold the world.<BR>—कुहू-मुख or कुहू-रव, अस्,<BR>m. the Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूल|कुहूलं
कुहूल कुहूल, अम्, n. a pit filled with stakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेडिका
कुहेडिका कुहेडिका or कुहेडी or कुहेलिका, f.<BR>a fog, a mist, haze, haziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह्वान
कुह्वान कु-ह्वान, अम्, n. (see 1. कु), a dis-<BR>agreeable noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कू
कू 1. कू or कु, cl. 2. P. कौति, कवीति, or<BR>cl. 1. A. कवते, or cl. 6. A. कुवते, or cl. 9.<BR>P. A. कूनाति, -नीते, or कुनाति, -नीते, चुकाव, &c.,<BR>to sound, make a noise, cry out; to move: Caus.<BR>कावयति: Desid. चुकूषति, -ते: Intens. चोकूयते<BR>or कोकूयते, to cry aloud; [cf. Gr. κωκύω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कू
कू 2. कू, ऊस्, f. a female Piśāca or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूकुद|कूकुदः
कूकुद कूकुद, अस्, m. one who gives a girl<BR>in marriage with due ceremony and suitable decora-<BR>tions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूच|कूचः
कूच कूच, अस्, m. a breast; the female<BR>breast, especially that of a young or unmarried<BR>woman; [cf. कुच.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचका
कूचका कूचका, f. the milky juice of a<BR>bulbous plant; [? cf. कूर्चिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचक्र
कूचक्र कूचक्र, अस् or अम्? m. or n.? (for<BR>कु-चक्र), Ved. the female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचवार
कूचवार कूचवार, अस्, m. (?), N. of a region;<BR>also of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचिका
कूचिका कूचिका, f. a small brush or hair-<BR>pencil; a key; [cf. कूची and कूर्चिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचिदर्थिन्
कूचिदर्थिन् कूचिद्-अर्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ (for कु-<BR>चिद्-अर्˚), Ved. striving to get everywhere; (Sāy.)<BR>seeking (oblations) from any quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूची
कूची कूची, f. a paint brush, a pencil; [cf.<BR>कूचिका and कूर्चिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूच्छलिङ्ग
कूच्छलिङ्ग कूच्छलिङ्ग, औ, m. du. = कु-<BR>कुन्दर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूज्
कूज् कूज्, cl. 1. P. कूजति, चुकूज, कूजितुम्,<BR>to make any inarticulate or monotonous<BR>sound, to utter a cry as a bird, to coo as a pigeon,<BR>to caw as a crow, to warble; to moan, groan, &c.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">Page0244-c+ 79</a>]<BR>to utter any sound in a low and indistinct voice;<BR>to fill with sounds &c.: Caus. कूजयति: Desid.<BR>चुकूजिषति: Intens. चोकूज्यते, चोकूक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूज|कूजः
कूज, अस्, m. rumbling (as of the bowels &c.);<BR>cooing, murmuring, a warbling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजक
कूजक, अस्, इका, अम्, cooing, warbling, sounding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजत्
कूजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, cooing, warbling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजन|कूजनं
कूजन, अम्, n. rumbling of the bowels; the<BR>uttering of any inarticulate sound, cooing, moaning;<BR>the rattling of wheels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजित|कूजितं
कूजित, अस्, आ, अम्, uttered inarticulately, cooed, &c.;<BR>(अम्), n. the cry of a bird, cooing, warbling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजिन्
कूजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, making a rumbling sound in the<BR>bowels; warbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूट्
कूट् कूट्, cl. 10. P. कूटयति, to burn; to<BR>give pain, be distressed, to call, invite; to<BR>counsel, advise; A. कूटयते, to avoid or decline<BR>giving, not to give; to render indistinct or unin-<BR>telligible, to muddle, to render confused or foul; to<BR>be distressed; to despair; [cf. Eng. heat, hot; Old<BR>Island. hiti, heitr; Germ. hitze, heiss.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूट|कूटः
कूट कूट, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bone of the<BR>forehead with its projections or prominences, a horn;<BR>the crown of the head; any prominence or projec-<BR>tion (e. g. अंस-कूट, the hump of a buffalo; अक्षि-<BR>कूट, the prominence of the forehead above the eye);<BR>summit, the peak or summit of a mountain; summit,<BR>head, i. e. the highest, the most excellent, the first;<BR>a heap, a multitude (e. g. अभ्र-कूट, a multitude of<BR>clouds); a kind of vessel or implement; a hammer,<BR>an iron mallet; part of a plough, a ploughshare, the<BR>body of a plough; a trap for catching deer; a con-<BR>cealed weapon as a dagger in a wooden case, a sword-<BR>stick &c.; illusion, fraud, trick, deceit; a roguish<BR>scheme or plot; a knotty point, a puzzling question,<BR>an enigma, an obscure passage; untruth, falsehood,<BR>(or attributively) false, untrue; vile, low; uniform<BR>substance (as the ethereal element &c.); a water-<BR>jar; a kind of plant; (अस्, ई), m. f. a house, a<BR>dwelling [cf. कुट and कुटी]; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Agastya; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. not horned or cornuted,<BR>as an animal with incomplete continuations of the<BR>bone of the forehead; (अस्), m. an ox whose horns<BR>are broken.<BR>—कूट-कार, अस्, m. a rogue, a cheat, a<BR>false witness.<BR>—कूट-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, a rogue,<BR>a cheat, a false witness.<BR>—कूट-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, cheating,<BR>committing a fraud, bribing; (त्), m. a Kāyastha or<BR>man of the writer-caste; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कूट-<BR>खड्ग, अस्, m. a hidden sword, a sword-stick.<BR>—कूट-ग्रन्थ, title of a work supposed to be<BR>written by Vyāsa.<BR>—कूट-च्छद्मन्, आ, m. a rogue,<BR>a cheat.<BR>—कूट-ता, f. or कूट-त्व, अम्, n. falsehood,<BR>fraud.<BR>—कूट-तूला, f. a false pair of scales.<BR>—कूट-<BR>धर्म, अस्, आ, अम्, (a country or house) where<BR>falsehood is considered a duty.<BR>—कूट-पर्व or<BR>कूट-पूर्व, अस्, m. fever occurring in an elephant<BR>from vitiation of the three humors; (more correctly<BR>कूट-पूर्व.)<BR>—कूट-पालक, अस्, m. a bilious fever;<BR>a potter's kiln.<BR>—कूट-पाश, अस्, m. a trap.<BR>—कूट-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. a trap.<BR>—कूट-मान, अम्, n. a<BR>false measure or weight.<BR>—कूट-मुद्गर, अस्, m.<BR>a concealed weapon similar to a hammer.<BR>—कूट-<BR>मोहन, अस्, m. an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—कूट-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a trap or snare for deer, birds, &c.<BR>—कूट-युद्ध, अम्, n. a treacherous or unfair<BR>battle; (अस्, आ, अम्), fighting treacherously.<BR>—कूट-<BR>योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fighting unfairly or treacherously.<BR>—कूट-रचना, f. a laid trap.<BR>—कूट-शस्, ind. in<BR>heaps, in multitudes, by crowds.<BR>—कूट-शाल्मलि, इस्,<BR>m. f. or इका, f. a fabulous cotton-plant with sharp<BR>thorns, with which the wicked are tortured in the<BR>world of Yama; a species of the Simul silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR>—कूट-शासन, अम्, n. a forged or false grant<BR>or decree.<BR>—कूट-शैल, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—कूट-साक्षिन्, ई, m. a false witness.<BR>—कूट-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, standing at the top, keeping the highest<BR>position; standing in a multitude, standing in the<BR>midst; (in phil.) immovable, uniform, unchangeable,<BR>perpetually and universally the same, as the soul,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">Page0245-a+ 72</a>]<BR>spirit, space, ether, sound, &c.; (अम्), n. a sort of<BR>perfume, a species of dried shell-fish, commonly<BR>Nakhi; the soul.<BR>—कूटस्थ-ता, f. or कूटस्थ-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. unchangeableness, uniformity.<BR>—कूट-<BR>स्वर्ण, अम्, n. alloyed or counterfeit gold.<BR>—कूटा-<BR>क्ष (˚ट-अक्˚), अस्, m. loaded or false dice.<BR>—कूटा-<BR>गार (˚ट-आग्˚), अम्, n. an upper room, an apartment<BR>on the top of a house.<BR>—कूटार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ambiguity of meaning, fiction.<BR>—कूटार्थ-भा-<BR>षिता, f., scil. कथा, a tale, a story, a fiction.<BR>—कू-<BR>टोपाय (˚ट-उप्˚), अस्, m. trick, fraud, stratagem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटक|कूटकं|कूटकः
कूटक, अम्, n. elevation, prominence, projection;<BR>the body of a plough (i. e. the wood without the<BR>ploughshare and pole); a ploughshare; illusion, fraud,<BR>untruth, deceit; (अस्, आ, अम्), fraudulent, unfair; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a mountain; a braid or tress of hair; a<BR>perfume; see मुरा.<BR>—कूटकाख्यान (˚क-आख्˚),<BR>अम्, n. an invented tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटज|कूटजः
कूटज कूटज, अस्, m. the plant Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica; [cf. कुटज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूड्
कूड् कूड्, cl. 6. P. कूडति, -डितुम्, to eat;<BR>to graze; to become firm or fat or solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूड्य|कूड्यं
कूड्य कूड्य, अम्, n. a wall, = कुड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूण्
कूण् कूण्, cl. 10. P. A. कूणयति, -ते,<BR>-यितुम्, to draw together, contract, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणित
कूणित, अस्, आ, अम्, contracted, shut, closed.<BR>—कूणितेक्षण (˚त-ईक्˚), अस्, m. a hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणकुच्छ
कूणकुच्छ कूणकुच्छ, अस्, m., N. of one of<BR>Śiva's attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणि|कूणिः
कूणि कूणि, इस्, इस्, इ, crooked-armed, having<BR>a curved or withered arm; [cf. कुणि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणिका
कूणिका कूणिका, f. the horn of any animal;<BR>the peg of a lute; [cf. कलिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूदर|कूदरः
कूदर कूदर, अस्, m. the offspring of a<BR>Brāhman woman by a Ṛṣi, begotten during men-<BR>struation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूदी
कूदी कूदी, f., Ved. a fetter for the feet.<BR>—कूदी-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of a fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूद्दाल|कूद्दालः
कूद्दाल कूद्दाल, अस्, m. mountain ebony,<BR>Bauhinia Variegata; [cf. कुद्दाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप्
कूप् कूप्, cl. 10. P. कूपयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>be weak, to weaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप|कूपः
कूप कूप, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 3. कु;<BR>according to others perhaps fr. 1. कु and अप्;<BR>cf. अनूप, द्वीप), a hole, a hollow, a cave; a<BR>well; a post to which a boat or ship is moored;<BR>a mast (?); a tree or rock in the midst of a river; a<BR>leather oil vessel; (ई), f. a small well; the navel; a<BR>flask, a bottle; [cf. Gr. κύπη.]<BR>—कूप-कच्छप,<BR>अस्, m. a tortoise in a well; (metaphorically) a man<BR>without experience, who has seen nothing of the<BR>world.<BR>—कूप-कार, अस्, m. a well-digger.<BR>—कूप-<BR>खा, आस्, m. (rt. खन्), Ved. a well-digger.<BR>—कूप-<BR>ज, अस्, m. hair.<BR>—कूप-जल, अम्, n. well-water,<BR>spring-water.<BR>—कूप-दर्दुर or कूप-मण्डूक,<BR>अस्, m. a frog in a well, applied to a person of no ex-<BR>perience and enterprise, one who never leaves home.<BR>—कूप-राज्य, अम्, n., N. of a country.<BR>—कू-<BR>पाङ्क or कूपाङ्ग (˚प-अङ्˚), अस्, m. horripilation,<BR>erection of the hairs of the body.<BR>—कूपोदक (˚प-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. well-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपक|कूपकः
कूपक, अस्, m. a hole, a hollow, a cave; the<BR>hollow below the loins; a well, a temporary well, a<BR>hole dug for water in the dry bed of a rivulet; a<BR>stake &c. to which a boat is moored; the mast of<BR>a vessel; a rock or tree in the midst of a river;<BR>a funeral pile; a hole dug under a funeral pile; a<BR>leather oil vessel; (इका), f. a stone or rock in the<BR>middle of a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप्य
कूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a hole or well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपद
कूपद कूपद, अस्, m. = कूकुद, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपार|कूपारः
कूपार कूपार, अस्, m. the ocean, = अकूपार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपुष|कूपुषं
कूपुष कूपुष, अम्, n. the bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूबर|कूबरः
कूबर कूबर, or in the later language<BR>generally कूवर, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. the pole of a<BR>carriage or the wooden frame to which the yoke is<BR>fixed; (ई), f. a carriage covered with a cloth or blanket;<BR>(अस्), m. a hump-backed man; (अस्, ई, अम्), beautiful,<BR>agreeable, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूबरिन्
कूबरिन् or कूवरिन्, ई, m. a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूम|कूमं
कूम कूम, अम्, n. a lake, a pond, a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूमनस्
कूमनस् कू-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (for कु-मनस्,<BR>see 1. कु), Ved. wicked-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर|कूरं|कूरः
कूर कूर, अस्, m. boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्कुर
कूर्कुर कूर्कुर, अस्, m., N. of a demon who<BR>persecutes children (perhaps cough or some similar<BR>disease personified).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च|कूर्चं|कूर्चः|कूर्च्च|कूर्च्चं|कूर्च्चः
कूर्च कूर्च, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bunch of any-<BR>thing, a bundle of grass &c. (often used as a seat); a<BR>handful of Kuśa grass or peacock's feathers; certain<BR>parts of the human body, as the hands, feet, neck,<BR>and the membrum virile; the upper part of the nose,<BR>the part between the eyebrows; the beard; the tip<BR>of the thumb and middle finger brought in contact so<BR>as to pinch &c.; deceit, fraud, circumvention; false<BR>praise, unmerited commendation either of one's self<BR>or another person, boasting, flattery; hypocrisy;<BR>hardness, solidity; the mystical syllable हुम्; (अस्),<BR>m. the head; a store-room.<BR>—कूर्च-शिरस्, अस्, n. the<BR>upper part of the palm of the hand and foot; the heel.<BR>—कूर्च-शीर्ष or कूर्च-शीर्षक, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a plant, a drug, commonly called Jīvaka, one of the<BR>eight principal medicaments.<BR>—कूर्च-शेखर, अस्,<BR>m. the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—कूर्चा-मुख, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्चक|कूर्चकः|कूर्च्चक
कूर्चक, अस्, m. a bushel; a brush for cleaning<BR>the teeth, a painter's brush &c.; certain parts of the<BR>human body [cf. the preceding]; (इका), f. a painting<BR>brush or pencil; a key; a needle; a bud, a blossom;<BR>inspissated milk; (अम्), n. in त्रि-कूर्चक, scil.<BR>शस्त्र, a three-edged sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्चकिन्
कूर्चकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, stuffed, puffy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्चल
कूर्चल कूर्चल, अस्, m. (?) an animal teething<BR>for the second time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्द्
कूर्द् कूर्द् and कुर्द्, cl. 1. P. A. कूर्दति,<BR>-ते, चुकूर्दे, कूर्दिष्यते, अकूर्दिष्ट,<BR>कूर्दितुम्, to leap, jump; to play; [cf. Lat. ludo?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्द|कूर्द्द
कूर्द, अस्, m. a jump; N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्दन|कूर्दनं|कूर्द्दन|कूर्द्दनं
कूर्दन, अम्, n. leaping; playing, sport, pastime;<BR>(ई), f. the day of full moon in the month Caitra; a<BR>festival in honour of Kāma-deva or the god of love,<BR>held on the day of full moon in the month Caitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प|कूर्पं|कूर्पः|कूर्प्प
कूर्प कूर्प, अम्, n. the space between the<BR>eyebrows; [cf. कूर्च.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्पर|कूर्परः|कूर्प्पर
कूर्पर कूर्पर, अस्, आ, m. f. the elbow; the<BR>knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्पास|कूर्पासः|कूर्प्पास
कूर्पास कूर्पास, अस्, m. a cuirass or quilted<BR>jacket worn as armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्पासक|कूर्पासकः|कूर्प्पासक
कूर्पासक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bodice, a jacket<BR>with short sleeves worn next the body, especially by<BR>women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म|कूर्मः|कूर्म्म|कूर्म्मः
कूर्म कूर्म, अस्, m. a tortoise, a turtle; the<BR>earth considered as a tortoise swimming on the<BR>waters; a particular gesticulation with the fingers;<BR>one of the outer winds of the body; N. of a serpent<BR>or Kādraveya king; the second incarnation of Viṣṇu,<BR>his descent in the form of a tortoise to support the<BR>mountain Mandara at the churning of the ocean; N.<BR>of a son of Gṛtsa-mada, author of several hymns of<BR>the Ṛg-veda; (ई), f. a female tortoise; [cf. Gr.<BR>κλέμμυς, χέλυς, χέλώνη.]<BR>—कूर्म-चक्र, अम्,<BR>n. an astrological diagram.<BR>—कूर्म-पित्त, अम्, n.<BR>the bilious humor of a tortoise.<BR>—कूर्म-पुराण,<BR>अम्, n. the Purāṇa of the tortoise incarnation (one of<BR>the incarnations of Viṣṇu) or the fifteenth of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">Page0245-c+ 75</a>]<BR>eighteen Purāṇas.<BR>—कूर्म-पृष्ठ, अम्, n. the<BR>back or shell of a tortoise; (अस्), m. globe-amaranth,<BR>Gomphrena Globosa.<BR>—कूर्म-पृष्ठक, अम्, n.<BR>the cover of a dish, a lid.<BR>—कूर्मपृष्ठास्थि<BR>(˚ठ-अस्˚), n. tortoise-shell.<BR>—कूर्मपृष्ठोन्नत<BR>(˚ठ-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, raised or elevated like the<BR>back of a tortoise.<BR>—कूर्म-राज, अस्, m. the king<BR>of turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold the world.<BR>—कूर्मावतार (˚म-अव्˚), अस्, m. the tortoise<BR>incarnation (of Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्मि
कूर्मि कूर्मि. See तुवि-कूर्मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल्
कूल् 1. कूल्, cl. 1. P. कूलति, -लितुम्, to<BR>cover, hide, screen, protect; to enclose;<BR>to keep off, obstruct; [cf. Gr. κωλύω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल|कूलं
कूल, अम्, n. a declivity, slope; a shore, a<BR>bank; a heap, a mound; a pond or pool; the rear<BR>of an army; N. of a region; [cf. अज-कूला, अनु-<BR>कूल, उत्कूल, &c.; cf. also Hib. cul, ‘custody,<BR>guard, defence, the back part of anything;’ col, ‘an<BR>impediment;’ Lat. collis?].<BR>—कूलङ्-कष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, carrying or tearing away the bank; (अस्), m. the<BR>ocean, the sea; the stream or current of a river; (आ),<BR>f. a river.<BR>—कूल-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, frequenting the<BR>banks of rivers, grazing there &c.<BR>—कूल-भू, ऊस्,<BR>f. a bank, the land upon the bank or shore.<BR>—कू-<BR>लम्-उद्रुज, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking down banks, as a<BR>river &c.<BR>—कूलम्-उद्वह, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying or<BR>tearing away the bank, as a river &c.<BR>—कूल-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with shores; (ती), f. a river.<BR>—कूल-हण्डक, अस्, m. an eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलक|कूलकं|कूलकः
कूलक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. a bank, shore, dyke;<BR>a mound of earth, a heap, a pile; (अस्), m. an ant-<BR>hill; (अम्), n. the plant Trichosanthes Diœca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलिन्
कूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with banks or shores;<BR>(इनी), f. a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल्य
कूल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to a bank or<BR>shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल्
कूल् 2. कूल् or कूड्, cl. 10. P., Ved. कूल-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to burn, scorch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलिक
कूलिक कूलिक, अस्, m., N. of a prince; (आ),<BR>f. the bottom or lower part of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवर|कूवरः
कूवर कूवर. See कूबर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवार|कूवारः
कूवार कूवार, अस्, m. the ocean. See कू-<BR>पार and अकूपार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्ड|कूष्मांड|कूष्मांडः|कूष्माण्डः
कूष्माण्ड कूष्माण्ड, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>pumpkin-gourd, Benincasa Cerifera; a kind of spirit<BR>or imp, of which there exists a Gaṇa or class; a kind<BR>of spell or magical formula; (ई), f. a kind of plant<BR>[cf. ओषधि]; N. of the goddess Durgā; N. of<BR>several verses of the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्डक|कूष्माण्डकः
कूष्माण्डक, अस्, m. a kind of pumpkin-gourd,<BR>Benincasa Cerifera Savi; N. of one of Śiva's at-<BR>tendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्डिनी
कूष्माण्डिनी, f., N. of a goddess; [cf. कुष्-<BR>माण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहना
कूहना कूहना, f. hypocrisy, affectation of<BR>religious zeal or austerity; [cf. कुहना.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहा
कूहा कूहा, f. a fog, a mist, = कुज्झटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ 1. कृ. The conjugational tenses are<BR>formed in the Veda according to four different<BR>methods, as follows: I) According to the rule for<BR>cl. 2, Pres. 2nd sing. P. कर्षि, du. कृथस्, pl.<BR>कृथ; A. कृषे; Impf. 2nd sing. P. अकर्, 3rd अकर्<BR>and अकत्; 3rd du. अकर्ताम्; pl. अकर्म, अकर्त,<BR>अक्रन्; A. अक्रि, अकृथास्, अकृत, अक्राताम्,<BR>अक्रत; Impv. P. कृधि, कृतम्, कृत; A. कृष्व,<BR>कृध्वम्: Leṭ, 2nd and 3rd sing. कर्, pl. कर्म,<BR>कर्त and कर्तन, क्रन्; A. 3rd sing. कृत; 3rd<BR>pl. क्रन्त: Pot. क्रियाम; Part. nom. pl. m.<BR>क्रन्तस्; A. क्राण. II) According to the rule<BR>for cl. 1. Pres. P. करसि, करति, करथस्, कर-<BR>तस्, करन्ति; A. करसे, करते, करामहे;<BR>Impf. अकरम्, अकरस्, अकरत्; Impf. कर,<BR>करतम्, करताम्: Leṭ, करम्, कराणि, करस्,<BR>करत्, कराम, करन्; A. करामहै; Part.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0246-a" target="_blank">Page0246-a+ 81</a>]<BR>करन्ती. III) According to the rule for cl. 5, Pres.<BR>P. कृणोमि, &c.; A. कृण्वे, du. कृण्वैते; Impf.<BR>P. अकृणवम्, &c., 2nd pl. अकृणुत and अकृणो-<BR>तन; A. 3rd sing. अकृणुत; Impv. P. कृणु<BR>or कृणुहि or कृणुतात्, कृणोतु; कृणुतम्,<BR>कृणुताम्; कृणुत or कृणोत or कृणोतन;<BR>कृण्वन्तु; A. कृणुष्व, कृणुताम्, कृण्वाथाम्,<BR>कृणुध्वम्; Leṭ, कृणवस्, कृणवत् and कृण-<BR>वात्, कृणवाव, कृणवाम, कृणवाथ, कृणव-<BR>थ, कृणवन्; A. कृणवै, कृणवसे, कृण-<BR>वते, कृणवावहै, कृणवामहै, 3rd pl. कृण-<BR>वन्त or कृणवन्ते or कृण्वत: Pot. A. कृण्वीत;<BR>Part. P. कृण्वत्, A. कृण्वान. IV) According to<BR>the rule for cl. 8, (this is the usual formation in the<BR>Brāhmaṇas, Sūtras, and in classical Sanskrit), Pres.<BR>P. करोमि (ep. कुर्मि), करोषि, &c., कुर्मस्; A.<BR>कुर्वे; Impf. P. अकरवम्; A. 3rd sing. अकुरुत;<BR>Impv. P. कुरु, करोतु (in the earlier language for<BR>2nd and 3rd sing. कुरुतात्), कुरुत or कुरुतन;<BR>A. कुरुष्व, कुरुध्वम्, कुर्वताम्: Leṭ, P.<BR>करवाणि, करवस्, करवात्, &c.; A. करवै,<BR>कुरुथास्, करवावहै (ep. करवावहे), कर-<BR>वैथे, करवैते, करवामहै (ep. करवा-<BR>महे); Pot. P. कुर्याम्, A. कुर्वीय; Part. P.<BR>कुर्वत्, A. कुर्वाण: Perf. P. चकार, चकर्थ,<BR>&c.; A. चक्रे, &c.; Part. P. चकृवस् (Acc. sing.<BR>Ved. चक्रुषम्); A. चक्राण; 2nd Fut. करिष्यति;<BR>Leṭ, 2nd sing. करिष्यास्; 1st Fut. कर्ता; Prec.<BR>क्रियासम्; Aor. P., Ved. चकरम्, अचक्रिरन्,<BR>अचक्रत्; A. कृषे; Class. अकार्षीत् (poet. अका-<BR>रषीत्); Pass. Aor. reflex. अकारि and अकृत; Inf.<BR>कर्तुम्; Ved. कर्तवे, कर्तवै, कर्तोस्; Ind.<BR>Part. कृत्वा, Ved. कृत्वी and कृत्वाय; to do,<BR>make, perform, accomplish, cause, effect, prepare,<BR>undertake; to do anything for the advantage or injury<BR>of another (with gen. or loc. of the person); to<BR>execute, carry out (as an order or command); to<BR>manufacture, prepare, work at, elaborate, build; to<BR>form, construct one thing out of another (with abl.<BR>or inst. of the thing); to compose, describe; to<BR>cultivate; to make a sound, utter, pronounce (often<BR>in comp. with the sounds फट्, फुट्, भाण्, वषट्,<BR>स्वधा, स्वाहा, हिम्); to employ, use; to make<BR>use of (with inst.); to accomplish any period, bring<BR>to completion, spend (e. g. वर्षाणि दश चक्रुः,<BR>they spent ten years; क्षणं कुरु, wait a mo-<BR>ment); to place, put, lay, bring, lead, to take hold<BR>of (with acc. or loc. or inst., e. g. अर्धं कृ, to<BR>win over to one's own side or party; हस्ते or पाणौ<BR>कृ, to take by the hand, to marry; हृदयेन कृ,<BR>to place in one's heart, love); to direct the thoughts,<BR>mind &c. (मनः or मतिम् or बुद्धिम् or भा-<BR>वम् &c.) towards any object, turn the attention to,<BR>resolve upon, determine on (with loc., dat., or inf.<BR>of the object, e. g. मा शोके मनः कृथाः, do not<BR>turn your mind to grief; गमनाय मतिं चक्रे,<BR>he resolved upon going; अलाबुं स्रष्टुं चक्रे,<BR>he resolved to create a gourd); to consider, turn in<BR>the mind, think; to make, to render (with two acc.,<BR>e. g. आदित्यं काष्ठाम् अकुर्वत, they made the<BR>sun their goal); to procure for another, bestow,<BR>grant; A. to procure for one's self, appropriate,<BR>assume; to give aid, help any one to perform an<BR>action; to make liable; to injure, violate (e. g.<BR>कन्यां कृ, to violate a maiden); to appoint,<BR>institute; to give an order, commission; to cause to<BR>get rid of, free from (with abl.); to begin (e. g.<BR>चक्रे शोभयितुम् पुरीम्, he began to adorn the<BR>city); to proceed with, put in practice; to worship,<BR>sacrifice; (with numeral adverbs ending in धा)<BR>to divide, separate, or break up into parts, e. g.<BR>द्विधा कृ, to divide into two parts; सहस्रधा<BR>कृ, to break into a thousand pieces; (with adverbs<BR>ending in वत्) to make like or similar, to consider<BR>equivalent, e. g. राज्यं तृणवत् कृत्वा, valuing<BR>the kingdom like a straw; (with adverbs ending in<BR>सात्) to reduce anything to, cause to become, make<BR>subject, e. g. भस्मसात् कृ, to reduce to ashes;<BR>आत्मसात् कृ, to subject to one's self. The above<BR>senses of कृ may be variously modified or almost<BR>infinitely extended according to the noun with which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0246-b" target="_blank">Page0246-b+ 81</a>]<BR>this root is connected, as in the following exam-<BR>ples: सख्यं कृ, to contract friendship with;<BR>पूजां कृ, to honour; राज्यं कृ, to reign;<BR>स्नेहं कृ, to show affection; आज्ञां or निदेशं<BR>or शासनं or कामं or याचनां or वचः or<BR>वचनं or वाक्यं कृ, to perform any one's<BR>command or wish or request &c.; धर्मं कृ, to<BR>do one's duty; नखानि कृ, to clean one's nails;<BR>उदकं or सलिलं कृ, to offer a libation to the<BR>dead, to perform ablutions &c.; अस्त्राणि कृ, to<BR>practice the use of weapons; दर्दुरं कृ, to play<BR>on the flute; दण्डं कृ, to inflict punishment &c.;<BR>स्वरं कृ, to utter a sound; शब्दं कृ, to make<BR>a noise; कालं कृ, to bring one's time to an end,<BR>i. e. to die; चिरं कृ, to be long in doing any-<BR>thing, to delay; मनसि कृ, to take to heart, to<BR>mind, to determine, resolve upon; मनसा कृ, to<BR>place in one's mind, think of, meditate; हृदि<BR>कृ, to place in the heart, remember; वशे कृ, to<BR>place in subjection, become master of; शिरसा कृ,<BR>to place on the head; मूर्ध्ना कृ, to place on one's<BR>head, to obey, to honour: Caus. कारयति, -ते, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to cause to act or do, to cause another to perform,<BR>to have anything made or done by another (with acc.<BR>or double acc., e. g. सभां कारितवान्, he caused<BR>an assembly to be made; राज-दर्शनम् मां<BR>कारय, cause me to have an audience of the king;<BR>बानिज्यं कारयेद् वैश्यम्, he ought to cause the<BR>Vaiśya to engage in trade; or with acc. and inst.,<BR>e. g. न शक्ष्यामि किञ्चित् कारयितुं त्वया,<BR>I shall not be able to have anything done by thee);<BR>to cause to manufacture or form or cultivate; to<BR>cause to place or put, to have anything placed, put<BR>upon, &c. (e. g. तं चित्र-पटं वास-गृहे<BR>भित्ताव् अकारयत्, he had the picture placed on the<BR>wall in his house). Sometimes the Caus. of कृ is<BR>used for the simple verb or without a causal significa-<BR>tion (e. g. पदं कारयति, he pronounces a word<BR>&c.; मिथ्या कारयति, he pronounces wrongly;<BR>कैकेयीम् अनु राजानं कारय, treat or deal with<BR>Kaikeyī as the king does): Desid. चिकीर्षति, -ते, to<BR>wish to make or do; to intend to do, to design,<BR>intend, begin, strive after; to wish to sacrifice or<BR>worship: Intens. चर्कर्ति, चरिकर्ति, चरीकर्ति,<BR>चर्करीति, चरिकरीति, चरीकरीति, चेक्रीयते, Ved.<BR>3rd pl. करिक्रति, to do repeatedly; [cf. Hib. caraim,<BR>‘I perform, execute;’ ceard, ‘an art, trade, business,<BR>function;’ sucridh, ‘easy;’ Cambro-Brit. creu, ‘to<BR>form;’ Island. gerdh, ‘action;’ Old Germ. kara-<BR>wan, ‘to prepare;’ Mod. Germ. gar, ‘prepared (as<BR>food);’ Lat. creo, cœremonia, ars (for cars); Gr.<BR>κραίνω, κρόνος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
1. कृत्, त्, त्, त्, making, doing, performing, accom-<BR>plishing, effecting, manufacturing, acting; one who<BR>accomplishes or performs anything, an author; often<BR>occurring at the end of compounds, see सु-कृत्,<BR>कर्म-कृत्, पाप-कृत्, &c.; (त्), m. an affix used<BR>to form nouns from roots; a noun formed with this<BR>affix.<BR>—कृद्-अन्त, अस्, m. a word ending with a<BR>Kṛt affix (such a word would be called by Pāṇini<BR>simply कृत्).<BR>—कृल्-लोप, अस्, m. the rejection of a<BR>Kṛt affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done, made, accomplished, per-<BR>formed; prepared, made ready; obtained, gained,<BR>acquired; placed at hand; well done, proper, good.<BR>The preceding senses are mostly found in the Veda;<BR>the numerous other senses found in classical writers<BR>may be inferred from the meanings of the rt. कृ<BR>above. The neuter of कृत is used with सह<BR>or with the inst. alone in the sense of ‘done with,’<BR>‘away with,’ ‘enough of,’ ‘no need of,’ &c. (e. g.<BR>कृतं सन्देहेन, away with doubt; कृतम्<BR>परिहासेन, enough of joking). कृत is often<BR>found at the end of a compound, e. g. पूर्व-कृत,<BR>done formerly; जन्मान्तर-कृत, done in a former<BR>state of existence; (अस्), m., N. of one of the Viśva-<BR>devās; of a son of Vasu-deva; of a son of Sannati<BR>and pupil of Hiraṇya-nābha; of a son of Kṛta-ratha<BR>and father of Vibudha; of a son of Jaya and father<BR>of Haryavana; of a son of Cyavana and father of<BR>Upari-cara; (अम्), n. deed, work, action; service<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0246-c" target="_blank">Page0246-c+ 81</a>]<BR>done, kind action, benefit; consequence, result; aim,<BR>object, design; stake at a game; prize or booty<BR>gained in battle; N. of the die or of the side of a die<BR>marked with four points; (according to some) the<BR>collective name of the four dice in opposition to the<BR>fifth die, called कलि; N. of the first of the four ages<BR>of the world (also called सत्य or ‘the golden age’)<BR>comprehending together with the morning and even-<BR>ing dawn 4,800 years of men, according to the<BR>Mahā-bhārata; but according to the Purāṇas 4,800<BR>years of the gods, or 1,728000 years of men.<BR>—कृत-कपट, अस्, आ, अम्, deceiving, beguiling,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>—कृत-कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has performed what was to be done, who has<BR>done his duty; having done or discharged one's<BR>duty.<BR>—कृत-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, one who has done<BR>his work or duty; skilful, clever, able.<BR>—कृत-कल्प,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who knows the customary rites.<BR>—कृत-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose desire is<BR>attained or fulfilled.<BR>—कृत-कार्य, अम्, n. an<BR>attained object; (अस्, आ, अम्), one who has done his<BR>work or obtained his object; one who has no need of<BR>another person's aid (with inst.).<BR>—कृत-काल, अस्,<BR>m. appointed time; (अस्, आ, अम्), fixed, settled as to<BR>time; sent, deposited &c. for a certain time; one<BR>who has accomplished a certain time, who has waited<BR>a certain time.<BR>—कृत-कूर्च्छक, अस्, आ, अम्, tied<BR>up as a small bundle or brush.<BR>—कृत-कृत्य, अम्,<BR>n. what has been done and what is to be done; an<BR>attained object; (अस्, आ, अम्), having successfully<BR>accomplished a business; one who has accomplished<BR>or attained any object or purpose; contented, satis-<BR>fied; clever.<BR>—कृतकृत्य-ता, f. or कृतकृत्य-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the full discharge of any duty or realisa-<BR>tion of any object, accomplishment, attainment,<BR>success.<BR>—कृत-कोटि, इस्, m., N. of a Kāśyapa; an<BR>epithet of Upavarṣa.<BR>—कृत-कोप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>angry, indignant.<BR>—कृत-कौतुक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>playful.<BR>—कृत-क्रय, अस्, m. a purchaser, a buyer.<BR>—कृत-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has finished or<BR>accomplished any object in which he is engaged;<BR>one who has attained his end or object; one who<BR>has fulfilled his duty or performed a religious cere-<BR>mony.<BR>—कृत-क्रुध, अस्, आ, अम्, angry, resentful.<BR>—कृत-क्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, one who is waiting<BR>for the exact moment, one who waits impatiently for<BR>a person or thing, (with प्रति or with the inf. or<BR>at the end of a comp., e. g. कृत-क्षणाहं ते<BR>गमनम् प्रति, I am waiting impatiently for thy<BR>going; ते भूमिं गन्तुं कृत-क्षनाः, they<BR>are waiting for the time to proceed to the earth);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कृत-घात-यत्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, making efforts to slay, one who tries to kill.<BR>—कृत-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying past trans-<BR>actions or (benefits) done, unmindful of (services)<BR>rendered, recompensing evil for good, not acknow-<BR>ledging good offices or benefits received, ungrateful;<BR>defeating or rendering vain all previous measures.<BR>—कृतघ्न-ता, f. or कृतघ्न-त्व, अम्, n. in-<BR>gratitude.<BR>—कृत-चूड, अस्, m. a boy on whom the<BR>ceremony of tonsure has been performed.<BR>—कृत-<BR>चेतस्, आस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—कृत-च्छिद्रा, f.<BR>the plant Luffa Acutangula.<BR>—कृत-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>born, produced, generated.<BR>—कृत-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>remembering past transactions, mindful of former aid<BR>or favours, grateful; observing propriety, correct<BR>in conduct; (अस्), m. a dog; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कृतज्ञ-ता, f. or कृतज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n. gratitude.<BR>—कृतञ्-जय, अस्, m., N. of the seventeenth<BR>Vyāsa; also of a prince.<BR>—कृत-तनुत्राण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, mailed, having covered one's self with armour.<BR>—कृत-तीर्थ, अस्, m. one who has visited holy<BR>places &c., one who frequents them; a guide; an<BR>adviser, one fertile in expedients.<BR>—कृत-त्रा, f., N.<BR>of a plant, = त्रायमाणा.<BR>—कृत-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being done or effected.<BR>—कृत-दार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, married; [cf. दारक्रिया.]<BR>—कृत-दास, अस्,<BR>m. one who offers himself as a servant for a certain<BR>time, a self-engaged servant, a hired servant.<BR>—कृत-<BR>द्युति, इस्, f., N. of the wife of king Citraketu.<BR>—कृत-द्विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. angry with the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0247-a" target="_blank">Page0247-a+ 81</a>]<BR>doings of another person.<BR>—कृत-धन्वन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Kanaka.<BR>—कृत-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ,<BR>prudent, considerate; learned, educated.<BR>—कृत-<BR>ध्वंस, अस्, आ, अम्, defeated, overpowered; injured,<BR>destroyed; destroying past transactions; [cf. कृत-<BR>घ्न.]<BR>—कृत-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. furnished<BR>with banners; (अस्), m., N. of a prince, a son of<BR>Dharma-dhvaja.<BR>—कृत-ध्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, lost<BR>after being once possessed or acquired.<BR>—कृत-<BR>नख, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has cleaned his nails.<BR>—कृत-नाशक, अस्, ई, अम्, ungrateful; [cf. कृत-<BR>घ्न.]<BR>—कृत-नित्यक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, having duly<BR>attended to the daily religious observances.<BR>—कृत-<BR>निर्णेजन, अस्, m. a penitent, one who has per-<BR>formed penance or made expiation.<BR>—कृत-निश्चय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has made a resolution, resolved,<BR>determined; confident, sure, certain.<BR>—कृत-पर्व,<BR>अम्, n. (?) the golden age of the world.<BR>—कृत-<BR>पश्चात्ताप, अस्, आ, अम्, showing regret or penitence.<BR>—कृत-पुङ्ख, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘one who has fixed<BR>the feathers of his arrows,’ skilled in archery.<BR>—कृत-<BR>पुण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished in virtuous acts.<BR>—कृत-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, done formerly.<BR>—कृत-<BR>पूर्व-नाशन, अम्, n. forgetting past services, in-<BR>gratitude; [cf. कृत-घ्न.]<BR>—कृत-पूर्विन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, one by whom anything was formerly done.<BR>—कृत-पौरुष, अस्, आ, अम्, behaving gallantly.<BR>—कृत-प्रणाम, अस्, आ, अम्, making obeisance,<BR>saluting.<BR>—कृत-प्रतिकृत, अम्, n. assault and<BR>counter-assault; attack and resistance; retaliation<BR>for an assault.<BR>—कृत-प्रतिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, ful-<BR>filling a promise or agreement.<BR>—कृत-प्रयत्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, making effort, active, industrious, per-<BR>severing.<BR>—कृत-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, successful,<BR>fruitful; (अम्), n. result, consequence of an act; a<BR>poisonous substance; (आ), f., N. of a plant; [cf. कोल-<BR>शिम्बी.]<BR>—कृत-बन्धु, उस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कृत-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, laying hands upon, touch-<BR>ing.<BR>—कृत-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, one who has made<BR>a resolution, a man of resolute or firm character;<BR>resolved; informed of one's duty, one who knows<BR>how religious rites ought to be conducted; learned,<BR>wise.<BR>—कृत-ब्रह्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. one who has<BR>performed his devotions; (a deity) towards whom<BR>devotion is made, (a sacrifice) in which prayers are<BR>duly offered.<BR>—कृत-भय, अस्, आ, अम्, alarmed,<BR>apprehensive.<BR>—कृत-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>mind is directed towards anything, determined, re-<BR>solved.<BR>—कृत-भूत-मैत्र, अस्, ई, अम्, friendly<BR>to all.<BR>—कृत-भोजन, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>dined or made a meal.<BR>—कृत-मङ्गल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, blessed, consecrated.<BR>—कृत-मति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>one who has taken a resolution, one who has resolved<BR>upon anything.<BR>—कृत-मन्दार, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—कृत-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, angry, offended,<BR>indignant.<BR>—कृत-मार्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having a road<BR>or path made; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—कृत-माल,<BR>अस्, m. a species of animal; the tree Cassia Fistula.<BR>—कृत-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, skilled, clever, conver-<BR>sant.<BR>—कृत-मैत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, friendly.<BR>—कृत-<BR>यजुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. one who has uttered the<BR>sacrificial formulas.<BR>—कृत-यज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Cyavana and father of Uparicara.<BR>—कृत-<BR>यशस्, आस्, m., N. of a descendant of Aṅgiras.<BR>—कृत-युग, अम्, n. the first of the four ages<BR>of the world; the golden age; see कृत above.<BR>—कृत-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, joining in combat.<BR>—कृत-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a grandson of Maru.<BR>—कृत-रव, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding, singing.<BR>—कृत-रुच्, क्, क्, क्, splendid, brilliant.<BR>—कृत-<BR>रुष, अस्, आ, अम्, angry, displeased.<BR>—कृत-<BR>लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, marked, stamped; branded;<BR>noted for good qualities, excellent, amiable, &c.;<BR>defined, discriminated; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—कृत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, making, having done or<BR>made anything; one who holds the stake at a game.<BR>—कृत-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of several princes,<BR>especially of a son of Hṛdika, also of Kanaka or<BR>Dhanaka; N. of the father of the thirteenth Arhat<BR>of the present Avasarpiṇī.<BR>—कृत-वाप, अस्, m. a<BR>penitent who has shaven his head and chin.<BR>—कृत-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0247-b" target="_blank">Page0247-b+ 81</a>]<BR>विकार or कृत-विक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, altered, changed.<BR>—कृत-विक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, displaying valour,<BR>making vigorous efforts.<BR>—कृत-विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has acquired knowledge, well informed,<BR>scientific, a philosopher.<BR>—कृत-विवाह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>married.<BR>—कृत-विस्मय, अस्, आ, अम्, astonished,<BR>astonishing.<BR>—कृत-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being strong<BR>or powerful; (अस्), m., N. of a prince, a son of<BR>Kanaka or Dhanaka and father of Arjuna.<BR>—कृत-<BR>वेग, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कृत-वेतन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who receives wages, a hired servant or<BR>labourer.<BR>—कृत-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, grateful, observ-<BR>ant of propriety, knowing what is correct; see कृत-<BR>ज्ञ.<BR>—कृत-वेधक or कृत-वेधन, अस्, m. a<BR>plant, a sort of Ghoṣa with white flowers.<BR>—कृत-<BR>वेपथु, उस्, उस्, उ, trembling.<BR>—कृत-वेश, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, attired, ornamented, decorated.<BR>—कृत-व्य-<BR>धन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having weapons, armed.<BR>—कृत-व्यलीक, अस्, आ, अम्, annoyed, vexed,<BR>irritated.<BR>—कृत-व्रत, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Loma-harṣaṇa.<BR>—कृत-शक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, putting<BR>forth one's strength or courage.<BR>—कृत-शस्त्र-<BR>निःश्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, exercised in arms.<BR>—कृत-<BR>शिल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has learned his art or is<BR>skilled in his own trade.<BR>—कृत-शोभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>splendid, brilliant; beautiful, beautified; dexterous,<BR>handy.<BR>—कृत-शौच, अस्, आ, अम्, purified, cleansed,<BR>freed from bodily impurities, released from conven-<BR>tional defilement &c.<BR>—कृत-श्रम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has made great exertions, painstaking,<BR>laborious; (अस्), m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—कृत-सं-<BR>सर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, brought into contact, united.<BR>—कृत-संस्कार, अस्, आ, अम्, initiated, one who has<BR>undergone all the purificatory ceremonies.<BR>—कृत-<BR>सङ्कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has made a resolu-<BR>tion.<BR>—कृत-सङ्केत, अस्, आ, अम्, making an<BR>agreement or appointment.<BR>—कृत-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who never loses his self-consciousness, one<BR>who has presence of mind; aroused; restored to<BR>consciousness or animation; distinguished by appro-<BR>priate marks, devices, &c.<BR>—कृत-सन्नाह, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, cased in armour.<BR>—कृत-सन्निधान, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, brought into contact, approximated.<BR>—कृत-<BR>सम्बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, connected, allied.<BR>—कृत-<BR>सापत्निका or कृत-सापत्नी or कृत-सापत्नीका or<BR>कृत-सापत्नका or कृत-सपत्निका, f. a woman<BR>whose husband has taken another wife; a superseded<BR>wife.<BR>—कृत-स्थिति, इस्, इस्, इ, abiding, staying, taking<BR>up an abode.<BR>—कृत-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, showing<BR>affection, affectionate.<BR>—कृत-स्मर, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—कृत-स्वस्त्ययन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>blessed, commended to the protection of gods pre-<BR>vious to any journey or undertaking.<BR>—कृत-<BR>स्वेच्छाहार (˚स्व-इच्छा-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, feeding<BR>at pleasure.<BR>—कृत-हस्त or कृत-हस्तक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has exercised his hands; dexterous;<BR>skilled in archery; clever, skilful, dexterous.<BR>—कृत-<BR>हस्त-ता, f. dexterity; the being skilled in archery.<BR>—कृताकृत (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, done and not<BR>done, done in part but not completed, done and<BR>omitted, prepared and not prepared, manufactured<BR>and not manufactured; (अम्), n. what has been done<BR>and what has not been done.<BR>—कृतागम (˚त-<BR>आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has made progress,<BR>advanced, proficient.<BR>—कृतागस् (˚त-आग्˚), आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, one who has committed an offence, offending,<BR>criminal, sinful, in fault.<BR>—कृताग्नि (˚त-अग्˚), इस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Kanaka or Dhanaka.<BR>—कृताग्नि-<BR>कार्य, अस्, m. a Brāhman who has offered the usual<BR>fire-oblation.<BR>—कृताङ्क (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>marked, branded; numbered.<BR>—कृताञ्जलि (˚त-अञ्˚),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, one who joins the hands in reverence or to<BR>solicit a favour (keeping the palms from touching as if<BR>to hold alms or an offering), standing in a reverent or<BR>respectful posture; (इस्), m. a shrub used in medicine,<BR>also in magical potions &c.<BR>—कृताञ्जलिपुट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, joining the palms of the hands for obeisance,<BR>also for holding water &c.<BR>—कृतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚),<BR>आ, आ, अ, one whose spirit is disciplined, subdued,<BR>tranquil; of a self-governed spirit.<BR>—कृतानति (˚त-<BR>आन्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, bending, bowing, paying homage or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0247-c" target="_blank">Page0247-c+ 81</a>]<BR>respect.<BR>—कृतानुकर (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, imi-<BR>tating what has been done by another, following<BR>another's example, subservient, not independent.<BR>—कृतानुकूल्य (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, compliant,<BR>kind, favouring.<BR>—कृतानुकृत (˚त-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>that which is done before and after.<BR>—कृतानुव्या-<BR>ध (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mixed, combined, united.<BR>—कृतानुसार (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. established practice,<BR>usage, custom, rate.<BR>—कृतान्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, causing an end, bringing to an end, leading to<BR>any decisive termination; whose end is action; (अस्),<BR>m. destiny, fate; the inevitable result of actions done<BR>in a past existence; a N. of Yama, the god of death,<BR>(he is son of Sūrya and regent of the dead); death<BR>personified; a demonstrated conclusion, a dogma, a<BR>proved or established doctrine; a sinful or inauspicious<BR>action; Saturday, ‘closing the week,’ considered as an<BR>unlucky day; (आ), f. a kind of perfume, [cf. रेणुका.]<BR>—कृतान्त-जनक, अस्, m. a N. of the sun, as<BR>father of Yama.<BR>—कृतान्न (˚त-अन्˚), अम्, n. pre-<BR>pared or cooked food; digested food, excrement; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), eating.<BR>—कृतापकार (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>injured, wronged; discomfited, overpowered; doing<BR>wrong, offending.<BR>—कृतापकृत (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, done for and against.<BR>—कृतापदान (˚त-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, completing a great or noble work.<BR>—कृतापराध (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, guilty, cul-<BR>pable, an offender.<BR>—कृताभय (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, saved from fear.<BR>—कृताभरण (˚त-आभ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, adorned, decorated.<BR>—कृताभिसरण-<BR>वेश (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attired in the dress of a<BR>maiden who goes to meet her lover.<BR>—कृताभिषेक<BR>(˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled, inaugurated; (अस्),<BR>m. a prince &c. who has been inaugurated.<BR>—कृता-<BR>भ्यास (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, trained, exercised,<BR>practised.<BR>—कृताय (˚त-अय), अस्, m. the die called<BR>Kṛta.<BR>—कृतायास (˚त-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, labouring,<BR>suffering.<BR>—कृतार्घ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of the<BR>nineteenth Arhat of the past Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—कृतार्-<BR>तनाद (˚त-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, making cries of pain.<BR>—कृतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>attained an end or object, having accomplished a<BR>purpose or desire, successful; satisfied, contented;<BR>clever; (अस्), m. a various reading for कृतार्घ.<BR>—कृतार्थ-ता, f. or कृतार्थ-त्व, अम्, n. ac-<BR>complishment of an object, success.<BR>—कृतार्थी-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, rendered successful.<BR>—कृतार्थी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become successful.<BR>—कृतालक (˚त-<BR>अल्˚), अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's attendants.<BR>—कृता-<BR>लय (˚त-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has taken up<BR>his abode in any place (often compounded with the<BR>name of a place or country, e. g. स्वर्ग-कृतालयः,<BR>an inhabitant of heaven); (अस्), m. a frog.<BR>—कृता-<BR>लोक (˚त-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, supplied with light, lighted.<BR>—कृतावधान (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, careful,<BR>cautious, prudent, attentive.<BR>—कृतावधि (˚त-अव्˚),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, fixed, appointed, agreed upon; bounded,<BR>limited.<BR>—कृतावमर्ष (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>effacing from recollection; intolerant.<BR>—कृतावश्-<BR>यक (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having done all that is<BR>necessary.<BR>—कृतावसक्थिक (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>seated on the hams with the knees tied together or the<BR>hips and knees surrounded by a cloth.<BR>—कृतावस्थ<BR>(˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, summoned, called; made<BR>present; fixed, settled.<BR>—कृतावास (˚त-आव्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a lodging; (अस्, आ, अम्), lodging.<BR>—कृताशन<BR>(˚त-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, feeding upon.<BR>—कृतासन-<BR>परिग्रह (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, seated.<BR>—कृतास्-<BR>कन्दन (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, assailing, attacking;<BR>effacing from recollection.<BR>—कृतास्त्र (˚त-अस्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has exercised himself in throwing<BR>arrows or other weapons, skilled in archery; armed;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a warrior.<BR>—कृतास्त्र-ता, f. consum-<BR>mate skill or proficiency in the use of arms.<BR>—कृ-<BR>तास्पद (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, governed, ruled; sup-<BR>porting, resting on; residing in or on, taking up one's<BR>abode.<BR>—कृताहक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कृत + अहन्),<BR>having performed the daily ceremonies or devotions.<BR>—कृताहार or कृताहारक (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having eaten food, having made a meal.<BR>—कृताह्-<BR>वान (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, summoned, called, chal-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">Page0248-a+ 80</a>]<BR>lenged.<BR>—कृतेर्ष्य (˚त-ईर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, envious,<BR>jealous.<BR>—कृतोच्चैस्^1 (˚त-उच्˚), ind. raised on high.<BR>—कृतोत्साह (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, making effort,<BR>striving.<BR>—कृतोदक (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has performed his ablutions.<BR>—कृतोद्वाह (˚त-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, performing penance by standing<BR>with uplifted hands; married.<BR>—कृतोपकार (˚त-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, assisted, befriended; friendly, giving<BR>aid.<BR>—कृतोपचार (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, served,<BR>waited upon.<BR>—कृतोपनायन (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>student who has been invested with the sacrificial<BR>cord.<BR>—कृतोपभोग (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, used,<BR>enjoyed.<BR>—कृतौजस् (˚त-ओज्˚), आस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Kanaka or Dhanaka.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk. on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 303. note: from uććais.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक|कृतकं|कृतकः
कृतक, अस्, आ, अम्, artificial, factitious, done arti-<BR>ficially, made, prepared, not produced spontaneously;<BR>not natural, adopted (as a son); assumed, simulated,<BR>false; (अम्), ind. in a simulated manner; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Vasu-deva, also of a son of Cyavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतय
कृतय, nom. P. कृतयति, -यितुम्, to take the<BR>die called Kṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्त|कृतांत|कृतान्तः
कृतान्त, कृतार्थ. See under कृत above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृति|कृतिः
1. कृति, इस्, f. (for 2. see col. 2), doing, making, per-<BR>forming, manufacturing, composing; action, activity;<BR>creation, work, literary work; magic; enchantment;<BR>an enchantress, a witch; a kind of Anuṣṭubh metre<BR>consisting of two Pādas of twelve syllables each and<BR>a third Pāda of eight syllables; another metre, a<BR>stanza of four lines with twenty syllables in each; a<BR>square number; N. of the wife of Saṃhrāda and<BR>mother of Pañca-jana; (इस्), m., N. of several persons.<BR>—कृति-साध्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being ac-<BR>complished by exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिन्
कृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, expert; clever, skilful, knowing,<BR>wise, learned; good, virtuous; pure, pious; following,<BR>obeying, doing what is enjoined; one who has at-<BR>tained an object or accomplished a purpose, satisfied;<BR>(ई), m., N. of a son of Cyavana and father of Upari-<BR>cara; N. of a son of Sannatimat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृते
कृते and कृतेन, ind. (originally loc. and inst.<BR>fr. कृत), on account of, for the sake of, for (with<BR>gen. or in comp., e. g. मम कृते or मत्-कृते, on<BR>my account, for me).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतेयुक
कृतेयुक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नु|कृत्नुः
कृत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, working well, able to work,<BR>powerful; skilful, clever, an artificer or mechanic, an<BR>artist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be done or performed;<BR>practicable, feasible; right, proper to be done; one<BR>who may be seduced from allegiance or alliance, one<BR>who may be bribed or hired as an assassin, treacherous;<BR>(अस्), m., scil. प्रत्यय, the class of affixes forming<BR>the fut. pass. part. &c. (as तव्य, अनीय, य, एलिम,<BR>&c.); a kind of evil spirit or ghost, either with or<BR>without the addition of यक्ष, मानुष, असुर,<BR>&c.; (आ), f. action, act, deed; magic; a female deity<BR>to whom sacrifices are offered for destructive and<BR>magical purposes; N. of a river; (अम्), n. what<BR>ought to be done; duty, office; purpose, end, object;<BR>what is proper or fit; motive, cause.<BR>—कृत्य-कल्प-<BR>तरु, उस्, m. title of a work on jurisprudence.<BR>—कृत्य-कल्प-लता, f., N. of a work by Vācaspati-<BR>miśra.<BR>—कृत्य-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m. title of a work<BR>by Śivarāma.<BR>—कृत्य-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, who knows<BR>what is to be done, learned, wise.<BR>—कृत्य-तत्त्व,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the true nature of duty or obligation,’ title of<BR>a work.<BR>—कृत्य-ता, f. seduction from allegiance or<BR>alliance.<BR>—कृत्य-रत्नाकर, अस् or अम् (?), m. or<BR>n. (?), title of a work on jurisprudence.<BR>—कृत्य-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having any business or request or object;<BR>busy, active.<BR>—कृत्य-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. the right way,<BR>the manner in which any object is to be effected.<BR>—कृत्य-विद्, त्, त्, त्, one who knows what ought<BR>to be done, knowing duty, learned, wise.<BR>—कृत्य-<BR>विधि, इस्, m. the way to do anything, a rule, a pre-<BR>cept.<BR>—कृत्या-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. practising magic or<BR>sorcery, bewitching.<BR>—कृत्या-दूषण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>or कृत्या-दूषि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. counteracting magic,<BR>destroying its effect.<BR>—कृत्या-रावण, अस् or अम् (?),<BR>m. or n. (?), title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यक
कृत्यक, अस्, m. an injurer?; (आ), f. an enchan-<BR>tress, a witch, a woman who is the fatal cause of injury<BR>or destruction, the fatal destroyer, the bane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, made artificially, factitious,<BR>artificial, the reverse of what is naturally or spon-<BR>taneously produced; falsified, adopted (as a child);<BR>(अस्), m. incense, olibanum; an adopted son; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of salt, the common Bit Noben, or Bit<BR>Lavan, obtained by cooking; a sort of perfume [cf.<BR>जवादि]; a kind of collyrium [cf. रसाञ्जन].<BR>—कृत्रिम-धूप, अस्, m. incense, olibanum.^1<BR>—कृत्रिम-धूपक, अस्, m. compound perfume,<BR>containing ten or eighteen ingredients.<BR>—कृत्रिम-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. an adopted son; one of the twelve<BR>kinds recognised in law, the son made.<BR>—कृत्रिम-<BR>पुत्रक, अस्, m. a doll.<BR>—कृत्रिम-भूमि, इस्, f. a<BR>made floor.<BR>—कृत्रिम-मित्र, अस्, m. an acquired<BR>friend, one on whom benefits have been conferred,<BR>or from whom they have been received.<BR>—कृत्रिम-<BR>वन, अम्, n. a plantation, a park.<BR>—कृत्रिम-<BR>शत्रु, उस्, m. an acquired enemy.<BR>—कृत्रिमो-<BR>दासीन (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. an acquired neutral.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वन्
कृत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. causing, effecting; active,<BR>busy; practising magic or sorcery in order to bewitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वस्
कृत्वस्, ind. at the end of a numeral or numeral<BR>adjective, = fold, times (e. g. दश-कृत्वस्, ten times;<BR>बहु-कृत्वस्, many times; पञ्च-कृत्वस्, five-fold).<BR>In the earlier language कृत्वस् is used as a separate<BR>word, but native grammarians regard it only as an<BR>affix, and it is so used in classical Sanskrit; it was<BR>perhaps originally an acc. plur. fr. a noun कृतु,<BR>formed by the affix तु fr. the root 1. कृ; [cf. also<BR>कृत् in सकृत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वा
कृत्वा, ind. having made or done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वी
कृत्वी, f., N. of a daughter of Śuka, wife of<BR>Aṇuha (Nīpa) and mother of Brahma-datta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्व्य
कृत्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who is able to<BR>perform anything, strong, efficacious; having accom-<BR>plished many deeds, exerting one's power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियमाण
क्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being done, made, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ 2. कृ, cl. 3. P., Ved. चकर्ति, अकारीत्,<BR>Intens. चर्कर्ति, to make mention of, to<BR>praise, to speak highly of (with gen.); [cf. कारु,<BR>कीरि, कीर्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ 3. कृ, to injure &c. See 2. कॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृति|कृतिः
2. कृति, इस्, m. or f. (for 1. see col. 1), Ved. a<BR>kind of weapon, a sort of knife or a dagger; (इस्),<BR>f. hurt, hurting, injuring; waylaying.<BR>—कृति-कर,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—कृति-मत्, आन्, m. the<BR>founder of a race, realm, &c.; N. of a son of Yavī-<BR>nara.<BR>—कृति-रात, अस्, m., N. of a prince; [cf. कीर्त्ति-<BR>रात.]<BR>—कृति-रोमन्, आ, m., N. of a son of Kṛtirāta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृक|कृकः
कृक कृक, अस्, m. the throat, the larynx.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकण|कृकणः
कृकण कृकण, अस्, m. a kind of partridge,<BR>commonly Kaër, Perdix Sylvatica [cf. कृकर and<BR>क्रकर]; a worm; N. of a man; N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकणीय
कृकणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकणेयु
कृकणेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकदाशु
कृकदाशु कृकदाशु, उस् or ऊस्, m., Ved. one<BR>who hurts or injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकर|कृकरः
कृकर कृकर, अस्, m. a kind of partridge,<BR>commonly Kaër, Perdix Sylvatica [cf. कृकण and<BR>क्रकर]; a kind of pepper, Piper Chaba; the<BR>fragrant oleander tree [cf. करवीर]; one of the<BR>five vital airs, that which assists in digestion; an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकला
कृकला कृकला, f. long pepper; [cf. पिप्पली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलाश|कृकलाशः
कृकलाश कृकलाश or कृकलास or कृक-<BR>लासक, अस्, m. a lizard, a chameleon.<BR>—कृकलास-<BR>दीपिका, f. title of a mystical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकु|कृकवाकुः
कृकवाकु कृकवाकु, उस्, m. a cock, a gallina-<BR>ceous fowl; a peacock; a lizard, a chameleon; [with the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">Page0248-c+ 74</a>]<BR>first part of this word cf. Hib. cearc, ‘a hen.’]<BR>—कृ-<BR>कवाकु-ध्वज, अस्, m. an epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकषा
कृकषा कृकषा, f. a kind of bird; [cf. कङ्-<BR>कणहारिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाट
कृकाट कृकाट, अम्, n., Ved. the joint of<BR>the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाटक|कृकाटकं
कृकाटक, अम्, n. the neck; a part of a column;<BR>(इका), f. the back of the neck; the raised and straight<BR>part of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकालिका
कृकालिका कृकालिका, f. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकिन्
कृकिन् कृकिन्, ई, m., N. of a mythical king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकुलास
कृकुलास कृकुलास, अस्, m. a lizard, a cha-<BR>meleon; [cf. कृकलाश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र कृच्छ्र, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps fr. rt.<BR>कृष् and connected with कष्ट), causing trouble<BR>or pain, painful, attended with pain or labour; being<BR>in a difficult or painful situation; bad, miserable,<BR>evil, wicked, sinful; (अम्), ind. miserably, painfully,<BR>laboriously, with difficulty; (अस् or अम्), m. n. diffi-<BR>culty, trouble, labour, hardship, distress, calamity,<BR>pain, evil, misery, danger, sin, (often in compounds,<BR>e. g. वनवास-कृच्छ्र, the difficulties of living in<BR>a forest; मूत्र-कृच्छ्र, ischury; अर्थ-कृच्छ्रे-<BR>षु, in difficulties, in a miserable situation; प्राण-<BR>कृच्छ्र, danger of life); bodily mortification, aus-<BR>terity, penance, expiation; torment, torture; a par-<BR>ticular kind of religious penance, according to some<BR>= प्राजापत्य, according to others = सान्तपन.<BR>कृच्छ्रेण, inst. with difficulty, with great exertion,<BR>painfully, laboriously, hardly, scarcely; अल्प-कृच्-<BR>छ्रेण, with little difficulty, easily.<BR>—कृच्छ्र-कर्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. a difficult act, difficulty, labour.<BR>—कृच्-<BR>छ्र-काल, अस्, m. a season of difficulty.<BR>—कृच्छ्र-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, undergoing trouble or misery, suf-<BR>fering pain; being in difficulties, distressed.<BR>—कृच्-<BR>छ्र-ता, f. painful or dangerous state (especially in<BR>disease).<BR>—कृच्छ्र-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>life is in danger; breathing with difficulty; hardly<BR>supporting life.<BR>—कृच्छ्र-मूत्र-पुरीष-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. pain or difficulty in the evacuations.<BR>—कृच्छ्र-<BR>साध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, curable with difficulty.<BR>—कृच्-<BR>छ्रातिकृच्छ्र (˚र-अत्˚), औ, m. du. the ordinary<BR>and extraordinary penance, penance; (अस्), m. sing. a<BR>particular kind of penance, taking no sustenance but<BR>water for three, nine, twelve, or twenty-one days.<BR>—कृच्छ्रान्-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from trouble<BR>&c.<BR>—कृच्छ्राप्त (˚र-आप्˚) or कृच्छ्रोपनत<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, gained with difficulty.<BR>—कृच्-<BR>छ्रारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m., N. of a plant, a species of<BR>Vilva.<BR>—कृच्छ्रार्ध (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. an inferior<BR>penance lasting only six days.<BR>—कृच्छ्रे-श्रित्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. undergoing danger; struggling with difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्राय
कृच्छ्राय, nom. A. कृच्छ्रायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>feel pain; to have wicked designs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रिन्
कृच्छ्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, encompassed with difficulties,<BR>being in trouble, feeling pain; angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृड्
कृड् कृड्, cl. 6. P. कृडति, to become<BR>thick or coarse; to become fat or gross, to<BR>become solid; to eat; (another form for कूड्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृणञ्ज
कृणञ्ज कृणञ्ज, अस्, m. a kind of Cheno-<BR>podium, = कुणञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृणु|कृणुः
कृणु कृणु, उस्, m. a painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् 2. कृत्, (for 1. कृत् see under rt. 1. कृ<BR>at p. 246), cl. 6. P. कृन्तति, चकर्त,<BR>कर्त्स्यति and कर्तिष्यति, अकर्तीत्, कर्तितुम्,<BR>to cut, cut in pieces, cut off, divide; to tear<BR>asunder, destroy: Caus. कर्तयति, to cut, divide,<BR>&c.: Desid. चिकर्तिषति and चिकृत्सति: Intens.<BR>चरीकृत्यते, चरीकर्त्ति; [cf. Lith. kertu, inf. kirsti,<BR>‘to cut;’ Gr. κείρω, κάρσις Slav. korjû, ‘to split;’<BR>Lat. curtus, culter; Hib. ceartaighim, ‘I prune,<BR>trim, cut;’ cuirc, ‘a knife.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्त|कृत्तं
कृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, divided; desired, sought,<BR>wished for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्ति|कृत्तिः
कृत्ति, इस्, f. skin, hide; a garment made of skin;<BR>the hide or skin on which the religious student sits,<BR>sleeps, &c., usually the skin of an antelope; the birch<BR>tree; the bark of the birch tree, used for writing<BR>upon, for making hooka pipes, &c.; one of the<BR>lunar mansions, the Pleiads; a house; [cf. Hib.<BR>cart; Lat. cortex.]<BR>—कृत्ति-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince.<BR>—कृत्ति-वास, अस्, m. or कृत्ति-वासस्, आस्,<BR>m. covered with a skin, an epithet of Rudra-Śiva;<BR>(आस्), f. epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिका
कृत्तिका, आस्, f. pl., N. of a constellation, = the<BR>Pleiades, (originally the first, but in later times the<BR>third lunar mansion, having Agni as its regent; this<BR>constellation, containing six stars, is sometimes re-<BR>presented as a flame or as a kind of razor or knife;<BR>in mythology the six Kṛttikās are nymphs who<BR>became the nurses of the god of war, Kārttikeya);<BR>a vehicle, carriage, cart.<BR>—कृत्तिकाञ्जि (˚का-अञ्˚), इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, having a carriage as an emblem or sign.<BR>—कृत्तिका-भव, अस्, m. ‘being in the lunar<BR>mansion Kṛttikā,’ an epithet of Candra, the moon.<BR>—कृत्तिका-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the Kṛttikās,’ an<BR>epithet of Skanda or Kārttikeya; (the nymphs called<BR>Kṛttikās being his foster-mothers.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तत्र|कृंतत्र|कृंतत्रं|कृन्तत्रं
कृन्तत्र, अम्, n., Ved. a section, a shred, chip;<BR>a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तन|कृंतन|कृंतनं|कृन्तनं
कृन्तन, अम्, n. cutting, cutting off, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् 3. कृत्, cl. 7. P. कृणत्ति, चकर्त,<BR>कर्तिष्यति, कर्तितुम्, to twist threads, to<BR>spin; to surround, encompass; attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतद्वसु
कृतद्-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. distributing goods (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृता
कृता, f., Ved. an abyss (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स|कृत्सं|कृत्सः
कृत्स, अम्, n. water; entire, whole; [cf. the<BR>next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्न|कृत्स्नं|कृत्स्नः
कृत्स्न, अस्, आ, अम् (rarely used in pl.), all, whole,<BR>entire; (अम्), n. water; the flank or hip; the belly.<BR>—कृत्स्न-ता, f. totality, completeness.<BR>—कृत्स्न-<BR>विद्, त्, त्, त्, omniscient, knowing all things.<BR>—कृत्स्न-<BR>शस्, ind. wholly, entirely, altogether.<BR>—कृत्स्न-<BR>हृदय, अम्, n. the whole heart.<BR>—कृत्स्नायत<BR>(˚न-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. stretched out to its full<BR>length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नक
कृत्स्नक, अस्, आ, अम्, all, every.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्त|कृतांत|कृतान्तः
कृतान्त कृतान्त, कृतार्थ. See p. 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदन्त
कृदन्त कृद्-अन्त. See under 1. कृत्, p. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदर|कृदरं|कृदरः
कृदर कृदर, अम्, n., Ved. a store-room,<BR>a vessel; the lap; (अस्), m. a granary, a cupboard &c.<BR>for holding corn, grain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृधु
कृधु कृधु, उस्, उस्, उ, or कृधुक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. shortened, mutilated, small, deficient.<BR>—कृधु-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having short ears (as a sort<BR>of imp); hearing badly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तत्र|कृंतत्र|कृंतत्रं|कृन्तत्रं
कृन्तत्र कृन्तत्र. See under 2. कृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप्
कृप् 1. कृप्, प्, f., Ved. (occurring only in<BR>inst.), beautiful appearance, beauty, splendor.<BR>—कृप-<BR>नीऌअ (for कृपा-˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one whose home is<BR>splendor, dwelling in splendor, epithet of Agni; (Sāy.)<BR>the support of sacred rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप्
कृप् 2. कृप् (connected with rt. क्रप्),<BR>cl. 1. A. कर्पते, to have pity or mercy<BR>on; cl. 10. P. कृपयति or कृपापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to be weak; to pity; to mourn, grieve, lament;<BR>[cf. Gr. ἔλπω]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप|कृपः
कृप, अस्, m., N. of a man described in the Veda<BR>as a friend of Indra; (अस्), m. and (ई), f., N. of the<BR>son and daughter of the sage Śaradvat, (he performed<BR>severe penance and thereby alarmed the jealous Indra,<BR>who sent a nymph to tempt him, but without<BR>success; however, twin sons were born to the sage<BR>in a clump of grass (शर-स्तम्बे), who were found<BR>by king Śāntanu and out of pity (कृपा) taken home<BR>and reared as his own; the daughter, Kṛpī, married<BR>Droṇa, and had by him a son called Aśvatthāman;<BR>the son, Kṛpa, became one of the privy council at<BR>Hastināpur, and is sometimes called Gautama, some-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">Page0249-b+ 79</a>]<BR>times Śāradvata. According to the Hari-vaṃśa and<BR>Viṣṇu-Purāṇa, Kṛpa and Kṛpī were only distant<BR>descendants of Śaradvat. According to others, Kṛpa<BR>= Vyāsa or = a son of Kṛṣṇa.)<BR>—कृपी-पति, इस्,<BR>m. a N. of Droṇa as husband of Kṛpī.<BR>—कृपी-<BR>पुत्र or कृपी-सुत, अस्, m., a N. of Aśvatthāman<BR>as son of Kṛpī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण|कृपणः
कृपण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, inclined to grieve;<BR>pitiable, miserable, poor, wretched, feeble; low, vile;<BR>miserly, stingy; avaricious; arising from pity, caused<BR>by pity; (अम्), ind. miserably; (अस्), m. a worm; (अम्),<BR>n. wretchedness, misery; स-कृपणम्, miserably,<BR>pitiably; [cf. कार्पण्य.]<BR>—कृपण-काशिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, Ved. looking suppliantly, looking desirous; ex-<BR>pressing a desire (?).<BR>—कृपण-त्व, अम्, n. misery;<BR>wretchedness; miserable condition.<BR>—कृपण-धी,<BR>ईस्, ईस्, इ, little-minded.<BR>—कृपण-निन्दा, f. ‘censure<BR>of the miser,’ title of a chapter of the Sārṅgadhara<BR>Paddhati.<BR>—कृपण-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, little-minded.<BR>—कृपण-वत्सल, अस्, आ, अम्, kind to the poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणाय
कृपणाय, nom. A. कृपणायते, to feel<BR>miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपणिन्
कृपणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, miserable, one who is in<BR>misery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण्य
कृपण्य, nom. P. कृपण्यति, to wish, desire,<BR>be a suppliant for anything, pray for, obtain by<BR>entreaties; (in A. also कृपणते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण्यु
कृपण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one who praises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपा
कृपा, f. pity, tenderness, compassion; N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—कृपा-दृष्टि, इस्, f. a look with favour, a<BR>kind look.<BR>—कृपाद्वैत (˚पा-अद्˚), अस्, m. one<BR>of the Buddhas or deified saints of the Buddhists.<BR>—कृपान्वित (˚पा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, or कृपा-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, or कृपालु, उस्, उस्, उ, or कृपा-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, pitiful, merciful, compassionate, tender.<BR>—कृपा-<BR>मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a son of Deva-miśra.<BR>—कृपा-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, pitiless, unfeeling, unkind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाय
कृपाय, nom. A. कृपायते, -यितुम्, to mourn,<BR>grieve, lament, have pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाण|कृपाणः
कृपाण कृपाण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>कृप् for rt. कॢप्?), a sword, a scymitar, a sacrificial<BR>knife; (ई), f. a pair of shears or scissors; a dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणक|कृपाणकः
कृपाणक, अस्, m. a sword, a scymitar; (इका),<BR>f. a dagger, a knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीट|कृपीटं
कृपीट कृपीट, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 2.<BR>कृप्), underwood, wood, forest; fire-wood, wood,<BR>timber; water; the belly.<BR>—कृपीट-पाल, अस्, m.<BR>a rudder or large oar used as one; the ocean; air,<BR>wind.<BR>—कृपीट-योनि, इस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमि|कृमिः
कृमि कृमि, इस्, or क्रिमि, इस्, m. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. क्रम्; cf. क्रमि), a worm, an insect in<BR>general; a spider; an ant; lac, the red dye caused<BR>by insects; N. of a son of Uśīnara; N. of an Asura,<BR>the brother of Rāvaṇa; N. of a Nāga-rāja; (इस्), f.,<BR>N. of the wife of Uśīnara and mother of Kṛmi;<BR>[cf. Lith. kirminis, kirmele; Russ. cervj; Hib.<BR>cruimh; Cambro-Brit. pryv; Goth. vaurms,<BR>Them. vaurmi for hvaurmi; Lat. vermi-s for<BR>quermi-s; perhaps Gr. ἕλμινς for ἕρμινς.]<BR>—कृ-<BR>मि-कण्टक, अम्, n. several plants efficacious in<BR>destroying worms, Ficus Glomerata; another plant,<BR>= चित्रा or चित्राङ्ग; another plant, = विडङ्ग.<BR>—कृमि-कर, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous insect.<BR>—कृमि-कर्ण or कृमि-कर्णक, अस्, m. worms<BR>or lice generated in the external ear.<BR>—कृमि-कोश<BR>or कृमि-कोष, अस्, m. the cocoon of a silkworm.<BR>—कृमिकोशोत्थ (˚श-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, silk, silken.<BR>—कृमि-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. a disease of the eyes,<BR>caused by insects generated at the roots of the eye-<BR>lashes.<BR>—कृमि-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying worms;<BR>(ई), m. a medicinal drug, = विडङ्ग (?).<BR>—कृमि-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, vermifuge, anthelmintic; (अस्), m.<BR>a shrub used in medicine as a vermifuge, commonly<BR>Bīreng, Erycibe Paniculata, see विडङ्ग; the onion;<BR>the root of the jujube; the marking nut plant; (ई),<BR>f. turmeric.<BR>—कृमि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by<BR>worms; (आ), f. lac, a red dye produced by an insect,<BR>commonly called Lākṣā; (अम्), n. Agallochum.<BR>—कृमि-जग्ध, अम्, n. Agallochum.<BR>—कृमि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">Page0249-c+ 76</a>]<BR>जलज, अस्, m. a shell-fish, an animal living in a shell.<BR>—कृमि-दन्तक, अस्, m. tooth-ache with decay of<BR>the teeth.<BR>—कृमि-पर्वत, अस्, m. an ant-hill.<BR>—कृमि-भक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a hell.<BR>—कृमि-<BR>भोजन, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose food consists of worms;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a hell.<BR>—कृमि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>affected or covered with worms.<BR>—कृमि-रिपु, उस्, m.<BR>an anthelmintic plant, = विडङ्ग.<BR>—कृमि-रोग, अस्,<BR>m. disease caused by worms.<BR>—कृमि-वर्ण, अस् or<BR>अम् (?), m. or n. (?), red cloth.<BR>—कृमि-वारिरुह,<BR>अस्, m. a fish living in a shell.<BR>—कृमि-वृक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of plant, Koṣāmra.<BR>—कृमि-शङ्ख,<BR>अस्, m. the fish living in the conch.<BR>—कृमि-शत्रु,<BR>उस्, m. an anthelmintic plant, Erythrina Fulgens, =<BR>विडङ्ग.<BR>—कृमि-शात्रव, अस्, m. the plant Acacia<BR>Farnesiana.<BR>—कृमि-शुक्ति, इस्, f. a bivalve shell, a<BR>muscle; the animal living in a bivalve shell; an<BR>oyster.<BR>—कृमि-शैल or कृमि-शैलक, अस्, m. an<BR>ant or mole-hill; [cf. कृमि-पर्वत.]<BR>—कृमि-<BR>सरारी, f. a kind of poisonous insect.<BR>—कृमि-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—कृमि-हन्तृ, ता, त्री,<BR>तृ, or कृमि-हर, अस्, ई, अम्, anthelmintic, vermi-<BR>fuge.<BR>—कृमि-हा, f. an anthelmintic plant, = वि-<BR>डङ्ग.<BR>—कृमीश (˚मि-ईश), अस्, m., N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिक|कृमिकः
कृमिक, अस्, m. a small worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिण
कृमिण, अस्, आ, अम्, having worms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिन्
कृमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, affected with worms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिल
कृमिल, अस्, आ, अम्, having worms, wormy; (आ),<BR>f. a fruitful woman, one bearing many children; N.<BR>of a town, called after Kṛmi.<BR>—कृमिलाश्व (˚ल-<BR>अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of Bāhyāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिलिका
कृमिलिका, f. linen cloth dyed with red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमीलक|कृमीलकः
कृमीलक, अस्, m. a white sort of kidney-bean;<BR>[cf. वन-मुद्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमुक
कृमुक कृमुक, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of tree;<BR>[cf. कार्मुक and क्रमुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृव्
कृव् कृव् = 1. कृ, cl. 5. कृणोति. See p. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृवि|कृविः
कृवि कृवि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. 1. कृ), a<BR>loom (?); [cf. क्रिवि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश्
कृश् कृश्, cl. 4. P. कृश्यति, चकर्श,<BR>कर्शिष्यति, अकृशत्, कर्शितुम्, to be-<BR>come lean or thin, to become emaciated or feeble;<BR>to wane (as the moon): Caus. कर्शयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to make thin or lean, to attenuate, emaciate, to keep<BR>short of food; [cf. perhaps Lat. parco, parcus,<BR>parum, parvus, paucus; Gr. παῦρος Goth.<BR>favai; Eng. few.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश, अस्, आ, अम्, lean, emaciated, thin, spare,<BR>weak, feeble; small, little, minute, insignificant,<BR>poor; (अस्), m., N. of a man, also of a Nāga; N.<BR>of a Ṛṣi, author of a Ṛg-veda hymn; [cf. Hib.<BR>creas, ‘narrow, straight;’ caile, ‘narrowness.’]<BR>—कृश-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one who has lean<BR>cattle.<BR>—कृश-ता, f. or कृश-त्व, अम्, n. leanness,<BR>thinness.<BR>—कृश-शाख, अस्, m., N. of a plant, =<BR>पर्पट.<BR>—कृशाक्ष (˚श-अक्˚), अस्, m., a spider.<BR>—कृशाङ्ग (˚श-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, emaciate, spare,<BR>thin; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; (ई), f. a woman<BR>with a slender shape; a particular plant, commonly<BR>called Priyaṅgu.<BR>—कृशाश्व (˚श-अश्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of several persons; N. of an author of directions to<BR>players and dancers.<BR>—कृशाश्विन्, ई, m. a pupil of<BR>Kṛśāśva, a dancer, an actor, a tumbler.<BR>—कृशो-<BR>दर (˚श-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, thin-waisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशिका
कृशिका, f. the plant Salvinia Cucculata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशन|कृशनं
कृशन कृशन, अम्, n., Ved. a pearl, mother-<BR>of-pearl; gold; form, shape; (अस्, आ, अम्), yielding<BR>or containing pearls; [cf. ऊर्ध्व-कृशन and<BR>कार्शन.]<BR>—कृशना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. deco-<BR>rated with pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशनिन्
कृशनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. decorated with pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशर|कृशरः
कृशर कृशर, अस्, आ, m. f. a dish composed<BR>of milk, sesamum, and rice; rice and peas boiled<BR>together with a few spices, commonly called Khi-<BR>chree; [cf. कृसर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशला
कृशला कृशला, f. the hair of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाकु
कृशाकु कृशाकु, उस्, m. heating, grieving;<BR>(a various reading for कृशानु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानु|कृशानुः
कृशानु कृशानु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. कृश् for<BR>कृष् ?), Ved. ‘bending the bow,’ an epithet applied<BR>to a good archer, (generally connected with अस्तृ,<BR>‘an archer,’ though sometimes used alone: some<BR>regard Kṛśānu as a divine being, either similar in<BR>character to Rudra or this god himself; he is armed<BR>with the lightning and defends the ‘heavenly’ Soma<BR>from the hawk, who tries to steal and bear it from<BR>heaven to earth); a N. of Agni or fire; fire in<BR>general; N. of a plant, Plumbago Zeylanica; N. of<BR>an archer; N. of a Gandharva.<BR>—कृशानु-रेतस्,<BR>आस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानुक
कृशानुक, अस्, ई, अम्, containing the word Kṛ-<BR>śānu, as an Anuvāka or Adhyāya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्
कृष् कृष्, cl. 1. P. कर्षति, चकर्ष,<BR>कर्क्ष्यति and क्रक्ष्यति, अकृक्षत्,<BR>अकार्क्षीत् and अक्राक्षीत्, कर्ष्टुम् and क्रष्-<BR>टुम्, to draw, attract, draw to one's self, drag, pull,<BR>pull to and fro, drag away, tear; to lead or conduct<BR>(as an army); to bend (a bow); to draw into one's<BR>power, become master of, overpower; to obtain; to<BR>take away anything from any one (with two acc., e. g.<BR>अकर्षत् तं राज्यम्, he deprived him of the<BR>kingdom); cl. 6. P. A. कृषति, -ते, to draw or<BR>make furrows, to plough: Caus. कर्षयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to draw, to draw out, tear up, tear out; extract; to<BR>drag to and fro, cause pain, torture, torment; to<BR>draw or make furrows, to plough: Desid. चिकृक्षति,<BR>-ते: Intens. चरीकृष्यते, चरीकर्ष्टि or चरी-<BR>क्रष्टि; [cf. Lith. karszu, pleszau; Russ. ceshu;<BR>Lat. verro, vello; Gr. κόρος, ἕλκω ? Goth. falh.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ष|कर्षः
कर्ष, कर्षण, &c. See s. v. at p. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषक|कृषकः
कृषक, अस्, आ, अम्, attractive, drawing, who or<BR>what draws furrows or ploughs; (अस्), m. a plough-<BR>man, husbandman, farmer; a ploughshare; an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाण|कृषाणः
कृषाण, अस्, m. a ploughman, a husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषि|कृषिः
कृषि, इस्, f. ploughing, cultivation of the soil;<BR>agriculture, husbandry; the cultivation of the soil<BR>personified.<BR>—कृषि-कर्मन्, अ, n. agriculture,<BR>husbandry.<BR>—कृषि-जीविन्, ई, m. a cultivator, a<BR>farmer.<BR>—कृषि-फल, अम्, n. agricultural produce<BR>or profit.<BR>—कृषि-सेवा, f. agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिक|कृषिकः
कृषिक, अस्, m. a cultivator of the soil, a<BR>husbandman; the ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषीवल|कृषीवलः
कृषीवल, अस्, आ, अम्, one who lives by hus-<BR>bandry or agriculture; (अस्), m. a husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ट|कृष्टं
कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, ploughed or tilled, a field<BR>&c.<BR>—कृष्ट-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, grown in cultivated<BR>ground, cultivated.<BR>—कृष्ट-पच्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ripening in cultivated ground, sown or ripening after<BR>ploughing, as rice &c.; cultivated.<BR>—कृष्ट-पाक्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ripening on cultivated ground; sown or<BR>ripening after ploughing.<BR>—कृष्ट-फल, अम्, n.<BR>the product of a harvest.<BR>—कृष्ट-राधि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. successful in agriculture.<BR>—कृष्टोप्त (˚ट-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sown on cultivated ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टि|कृष्टिः
कृष्टि, अयस्, f. pl., Ved. men, races of men,<BR>sometimes with the epithet माणुषीस्; (originally<BR>the word may have meant cultivated ground, then an<BR>inhabited land, next its inhabitants, and lastly any<BR>race of men; Indra and Agni have the N. राजा<BR>कृष्टीनाम्; and पञ्च कृष्टयस्, ‘the five<BR>races,’ comprehends the whole human race, not<BR>only the Āryan tribes); according to native lexico-<BR>graphers the word means also ploughing, cultivating<BR>the soil; attracting, drawing; and (इस्), m. a teacher,<BR>a learned man or Paṇḍit.<BR>—कृष्टि-प्रा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. pervading the human race.<BR>—कृष्टि-हन्, हा,<BR>घ्नी, ह, Ved. subduing nations.<BR>—कृष्ट्य्-ओजस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. overpowering men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्य
कृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रष्टव्य
क्रष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be drawn or drawn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाणु|कृषाणुः
कृषाणु कृषाणु, उस्, m. a N. of fire; (a<BR>wrong reading for कृशानु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्कर|कृष्करः
कृष्कर कृष्कर, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; [cf. कृकर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ण|कृष्णं|कृष्णः
कृष्ण 1. कृष्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr.<BR>rt. कृष्), black, dark, dark-blue (opposed to श्वेत,<BR>शुक्ल, रोहित, and अरुण); wicked, evil; (अस्), m.<BR>black, the colour, or dark-blue, which is often con-<BR>founded with black by the Hindūs; the black ante-<BR>lope; a kind of beast of prey (described in the Veda<BR>as feeding on carrion and dead corpses); a crow; the<BR>Indian cuckoo or Kokila; the plant Carissa Carandas;<BR>the dark half of the lunar month from full to new<BR>moon [cf. कृष्ण-पक्ष below]; the fourth or<BR>Kali-yuga; N. of one of the poets of the Ṛg-veda<BR>descended from Aṅgiras; N. of a celebrated Avatār<BR>of the god Viṣṇu, or sometimes identified with<BR>Viṣṇu himself, as distinct from his ten Avatārs<BR>or incarnations. (In the earlier legends he ap-<BR>pears as a great hero and teacher; in the more<BR>recent he is deified, and is often represented as<BR>a young and amorous shepherd with flowing hair<BR>and a flute in his hand. The following are a few<BR>particulars of his birth and history as related in the<BR>Purāṇas &c.: Vasu-deva, who was a descendant of Yadu<BR>and Yayāti, had two wives, Rohiṇī and Devakī.<BR>The latter had eight sons, of whom the eighth was<BR>Kṛṣṇa. Kaṃsa, king of Mathurā and cousin of<BR>Devakī, was informed by a prediction that one of<BR>these sons would kill him. He therefore kept Vasu-<BR>deva and his wife in confinement, and slew their first<BR>six children. The seventh was Bala-rāma, who was<BR>saved by being abstracted from the womb of Devakī<BR>and transferred to that of Rohiṇī. The eighth was<BR>Kṛṣṇa, who was born with black skin and a peculiar<BR>mark on his breast. His father Vasu-deva managed<BR>to escape from Mathurā with the child, and favoured<BR>by the gods found a herdsman named Nanda, whose<BR>wife Yaśodā had just been delivered of a son, which<BR>Vasu-deva conveyed to Devakī, after substituting his<BR>own in its place. Nanda with his wife Yaśodā took<BR>the infant Kṛṣṇa and settled first in Gokula or<BR>Vraja, and afterwards in Vṛndāvana, where Kṛṣṇa<BR>and Bala-rāma grew up together, roaming in the<BR>woods and joining in the sports of the herdsmen's<BR>sons. Kṛṣṇa as a youth contested the sovereignty<BR>of Indra, and was victorious over that god, who<BR>descended from heaven to praise Kṛṣṇa, and made<BR>him lord over the cattle. Kṛṣṇa is described as<BR>sporting constantly with the Gopīs or shepherdesses,<BR>of whom a thousand became his wives, though only<BR>eight are specified, Rādhā being the favourite. Kṛṣṇa<BR>built and fortified a city called Dvāraka in Gujarāt,<BR>and thither transported the inhabitants of Mathurā<BR>after killing Kaṃsa. Kṛṣṇa had various wives be-<BR>sides the Gopīs, and by Rukmiṇī had a son Pra-<BR>dyumna, who is usually identified with Kāma-deva;<BR>with Jainas, Kṛṣṇa is one of the nine black Vasu-devas;<BR>with Buddhists he is the chief of the black demons,<BR>who are the enemies of Buddha and the white<BR>demons); N. of a king of the Nāgas; N. of an<BR>Asura or demon; N. of Arjuna, the most renowned<BR>of the Pāṇḍu princes (so named apparently from his<BR>colour as a child, see Mahā-bh. Virāṭa-parva 1389;<BR>the dual कृष्णौ = Kṛṣṇa and Arjuna); N. of<BR>Vyāsa; of Kṛṣṇa Hārīta; of a son of Śuka by<BR>Pīvarī, a teacher of the Yoga; N. of a pupil of<BR>Bharadvāja; of Dāśārha; of a son of Havirdhāna;<BR>of a son of Arjuna; of an adopted son of Asamañjas;<BR>of a chief of the Andhras; N. of the author of a com-<BR>mentary on the Mahā-bhārata; N. of a poet; N. of the<BR>author of a commentary on the Dāya-bhāga; N. of the<BR>son of Keśavārka and grandson of Jayāditya; N. of the<BR>father of Tānabhaṭṭa and uncle of Raṅganātha; N.<BR>of the father of Dāmodara and uncle of Malhaṇa; N.<BR>of the father of Prabhūjīka and uncle of Vidyādhara;<BR>N. of the father of Madana; N. of the grammarian<BR>Rāma-candra; N. of the son of Vāruṇendra and<BR>father of Lakṣmaṇa; N. of the father of Hīrabhaṭṭa,<BR>author of the commentary called Caraka-bhāṣya, and<BR>of the work Sāhitya-sudhāsamudra; N. of a hell; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of poisonous insect; several plants, as Piper<BR>Longum, the Indigo plant; a grape; a kind of<BR>perfume [cf. पर्पटी]; an epithet of Draupadī;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-c" target="_blank">Page0250-c+ 81</a>]<BR>an epithet of Durgā; N. of one of the seven tongues<BR>of fire; N. of the river Kistna; (ई), f. night; (अम्), n.<BR>blackness, darkness; the black part of the eye; a kind<BR>of demon or spirit of darkness; black pepper; black<BR>Agallochum; iron; lead; antimony; blue vitriol;<BR>[cf. कार्ष्ण, &c.; cf. also Russ. cernyi, ‘black.’]<BR>—कृष्ण-कन्द, अम्, n. the red lotus, Nymphæa<BR>Rubra.<BR>—कृष्ण-कर्कटक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>black crab.<BR>—कृष्ण-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. black-<BR>eared.<BR>—कृष्णकर्णामृत (˚ण-अम्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a poem by Vilva-maṅgala.<BR>—कृष्ण-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. making black; a peculiar manner of cauterising;<BR>(आ, आ, अ), criminal, guilty.<BR>—कृष्ण-काक, अस्, m.<BR>a raven.<BR>—कृष्ण-कापोती, f. a kind of plant; [cf.<BR>श्वेत-कापोती, कृष्ण-सर्पा.]<BR>—कृष्ण-काष्ठ,<BR>अम्, n. a black variety of Agallochum.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>केलि, इस्, m. a plant, Mirabilis Jalapa.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>कोहल, अस्, m. a gamester, a gambler.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>क्रीडित, अम्, n., N. of a poem by Keśavārka cele-<BR>brating the god Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-खण्ड, title<BR>of the fourth book of the Brahmavaivarta-purāṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-गङ्गा, f., N. of a river, = कृष्णा,<BR>कृष्ण-समुद्भवा, कृष्णवेण्या.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>गति, इस्, m. fire (‘whose way is black’); [cf. कृष्ण-<BR>याम, कृष्ण-वर्तनि, &c.]<BR>—कृष्ण-गन्धा,<BR>f. the tree Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR>—कृष्ण-गर्-<BR>भ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (clouds) having black cavities;<BR>(आस्), f. pl. = according to Sāy. the pregnant wives of<BR>the Asura Kṛṣṇa, but according to others = the<BR>waters contained in the black cavities of the clouds;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a plant, = कट्फल.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain; [cf. कृष्णाचल.]<BR>—कृष्ण-गोधा, f. a kind of poisonous insect.<BR>—कृष्ण-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. black-necked.<BR>—कृष्ण-चञ्चुक, अस्, m. a kind of pea; [cf. चण-<BR>क.]<BR>—कृष्ण-चतुर्दशी, f. the fourteenth day in the<BR>dark half of the month.<BR>—कृष्ण-चन्द, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a copyist who lived about A. D. 1730, a son<BR>of Rāma-candra.<BR>—कृष्ण-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince of the eighteenth century.<BR>—कृष्णचन्द्र-<BR>देवशर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a logician who lived<BR>about A. D. 1736.<BR>—कृष्ण-चर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>what formerly or in a former existence belonged to<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-चूडा, f. the plant Cæsalpinia<BR>Pulcherrima.<BR>—कृष्ण-चूडिका, f. the plant Abrus<BR>Precatorius.<BR>—कृष्ण-चूर्ण, अम्, n. rust of iron,<BR>iron filings.<BR>—कृष्ण-च्छवि, इस्, m. fire? [cf.<BR>कृष्णार्चिस्.]<BR>—कृष्ण-जंहस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>black-winged; (Sāy.) having a black path.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>जटा, f. a plant, Indian spikenard; [cf. जटामांसी.]<BR>—कृष्ण-जन्म-खण्ड, N. of a part of the Brah-<BR>mavaivarta-purāṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-जन्माष्टमी (˚म-<BR>अष्˚), f. the eighth day of the second half of the month<BR>Śrāvaṇa, the birthday of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-जी, ईस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—कृष्ण-जीरक, अस्, m. Kaloñji,<BR>a plant having a small black seed, which is used for<BR>medical and culinary purposes, Nigella Indica.<BR>—कृ-<BR>ष्ण-तण्डुला, f. a plant [cf. कर्ण-स्फोटा], Piper<BR>Longum.<BR>—कृष्ण-तर्कालङ्कार (˚क-अल्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a scholiast.<BR>—कृष्ण-ता, f. or कृष्ण-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. blackness.<BR>—कृष्ण-ताम्र, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of sandal-wood.<BR>—कृष्ण-तार, अस्, m. a deer, an<BR>antelope (‘black-eyed’).<BR>—कृष्ण-तिल, अस्, m.<BR>black sesamum.<BR>—कृष्ण-तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher of Rāma-tīrtha.<BR>—कृष्ण-तुण्ड, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of poisonous insect.<BR>—कृष्ण-त्रिवृता, f.,<BR>N. of a plant, a kind of Ipomœa, black Teöri.<BR>—कृष्ण-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of the author of a<BR>work on music.<BR>—कृष्ण-दन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing black teeth; (आ), f. the tree Gmelina Arborea.<BR>—कृष्ण-दर्शन, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—कृष्ण-दशन, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing black or discoloured teeth.<BR>—कृष्ण-दास, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the poem Camatkāra-candrikā;<BR>N. of the author of the work Caitanya-caritāmṛta;<BR>N. of the author of the poem Preta-tattva-nirūpaṇa;<BR>N. of a son of Harṣa, author of the Vimalanātha-<BR>purāṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-देव, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Nārāyaṇa, author of the Prayoga-sāra; N. of a copy-<BR>ist, son of Paṇḍyāpuruṣottama-deva.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>देह, अस्, आ, अम्, black-bodied; (अस्), m. a large<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-a" target="_blank">Page0251-a+ 81</a>]<BR>black bee.<BR>—कृष्ण-दैवज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कृष्ण-द्वैपायन, अस्, m., a N. of Vyāsa,<BR>considered as the compiler of the Vedas and Purāṇas,<BR>(so named because of his dark complexion and be-<BR>cause he was brought forth by Satyavatī on a dvīpa<BR>or island in the Ganges.)<BR>—कृष्ण-धत्तूर or<BR>कृष्ण-धत्तूरक, अस्, m. a dark species of<BR>Datura or thorn-apple, Datura Fastuosa.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>नगर, अम्, n., N. of a small district called after a<BR>town situated in it.<BR>—कृष्ण-पक्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>dark half of the month, the fifteen days during which<BR>the moon is on the wane, the time from full moon<BR>to new moon; one who stands on the side of<BR>Kṛṣṇa, an epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—कृष्ण-पक्षिक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of the Nāgas.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>पक्षीय, अस्, आ, अम्, pertaining to the wane of the<BR>moon.<BR>—कृष्ण-पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Prabodha-candrodaya; also of a scholiast on<BR>the Prakriyā-kaumudī.<BR>—कृष्ण-पदी, f. a female<BR>with black feet.<BR>—कृष्ण-पर्णी, f., N. of a plant,<BR>a kind of Ocimum; [cf. काल-तुलसी.]<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>पवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having black fellies, an epithet<BR>of Agni.<BR>—कृष्ण-पाक or कृष्ण-पाक-फल,<BR>अस्, m. a tree bearing a small fruit, which, when ripe,<BR>is of a black colour, commonly Karinda or Karonda,<BR>Carissa Carandas; also called कृष्ण-फल, पाक-<BR>फल, पाककृष्ण-फल, &c.<BR>—कृष्ण-पाण्-<BR>डुर, अस्, आ, अम्, greyish white.<BR>—कृष्ण-पिङ्गल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dark-brown in colour; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this man; (आ),<BR>f. an epithet of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>पिण्डीतक, अस्, m. a dark kind of Māyana, Vangueria<BR>Spinosa [cf. वराह]; also called कृष्ण-पिण्डीर.<BR>—कृष्ण-पिप्पीली, f. a kind of black ant.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>पिल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कृष्णपुरुषोत्त-<BR>मोपनिषद् (˚म-उप्˚), त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad<BR>belonging to the Atharva-veda.<BR>—कृष्ण-पुष्प,<BR>अस्, m. a black kind of Datura or thorn-apple; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a plant [cf. प्रियङ्गु].<BR>—कृष्ण-प्रुत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. moving in darkness; (Sāy.) taking or<BR>imparting a black colour.<BR>—कृष्ण-फल, अस्, m.<BR>a fruit tree, the Karinda [cf. कृष्ण-पाक]; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Vernonia Anthelmintica.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>फल-पाक, अस्, m. = कृष्ण-पाक.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>बलक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, black and white.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>भक्ति-चन्द्रिका, f. title of a play.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian; N. of a poet.<BR>—कृष्ण-भूम, अस्, आ, अम्, having a black soil,<BR>furnished with black earth.<BR>—कृष्ण-भूमि, इस्, f.<BR>a country with a dark soil, or black mould, blue clay,<BR>&c.<BR>—कृष्णभूमि-जा, f. a species of grass, de-<BR>scribed as a nourishing food for cattle (growing in a<BR>black soil).<BR>—कृष्ण-भेदी or आ, f. a medicinal<BR>plant, = कटु-रोहिणी.<BR>—कृष्ण-भोगिन्, ई, m. a<BR>black kind of snake.<BR>—कृष्ण-मण्डल, अम्, n.<BR>the black part of the eye.<BR>—कृष्ण-मत्स्य, अस्,<BR>m. ‘black-fish,’ N. of a fish.<BR>—कृष्ण-मल्लिका, f.<BR>or कृष्ण-मालुक, अस्, m. a plant, = मालूक,<BR>कृष्णार्जक.<BR>—कृष्ण-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>son of Rāma-sevaka, grandson of Devīdatta, author<BR>of the Mañjūṣākuñcikā.<BR>—कृष्ण-मिश्र, अस्, m.<BR>the author of the Prabodha-candrodaya.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having a black mouth, having<BR>black nipples; (अस्), m., N. of an Asura; N. of a<BR>sect.<BR>—कृष्ण-मुद्ग, अस्, m. a sort of pulse,<BR>Phaseolus, (वासन्त, माधव, सुराष्ट्रज.)<BR>—कृष्ण-मूली, f. a plant, = शारिवा-विशेष.<BR>—कृष्ण-मृग, अस्, m. the black antelope.<BR>—कृष्ण-मृत्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having black<BR>soil; (आ), f., N. of a Grāma.<BR>—कृष्ण-मृद्, त्,<BR>f. black soil; a country with soil of a dark colour.<BR>—कृष्ण-यजुर्वेद, अस्, m. the Black Yajur-<BR>veda.<BR>—कृष्ण-यजुर्वेदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>longing to the Black Yajur-veda.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>याम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a black path;<BR>an epithet of Agni.<BR>—कृष्ण-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. = कृष्ण-गर्भ, q. v.<BR>—कृष्ण-रक्त.<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of a dark-red colour.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>रुहा, f. a plant, = जतुका.<BR>—कृष्ण-रूप्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = कृष्ण-चर, q. v.<BR>—कृष्ण-लवण,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of black salt; a factitious salt, either<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-b" target="_blank">Page0251-b+ 81</a>]<BR>that prepared by evaporation from saline soil, or the<BR>medicinal kind, called Bit Loben or Bit Noben, a<BR>muriate of soda with a portion of sulphur and iron.<BR>—कृष्ण-लीला-तरङ्गिणी, f. title of a poem by<BR>Nārāyaṇa-tīrtha.<BR>—कृष्ण-लोह, अम्, n. the load-<BR>stone.<BR>—कृष्ण-लोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-red, of a<BR>purple colour.<BR>—कृष्ण-वक्त्र, अस्, m. the black-<BR>faced monkey.<BR>—कृष्ण-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, of a<BR>black colour, black or dark-blue; (अम्), n. the colour<BR>black.<BR>—कृष्ण-वर्तनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a<BR>black path, epithet of Agni.<BR>—कृष्ण-वर्त्मन्,<BR>आ, m. fire (‘whose way is black’); the marking nut<BR>plant, Plumbago Zeylanica; an epithet of Rāhu or<BR>the personified ascending node; a man of evil con-<BR>duct, a low man, an outcast, a profligate, a black-<BR>guard.<BR>—कृष्ण-वर्वरक, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>Varvara.<BR>—कृष्ण-वल्लिका, f., N. of a plant, =<BR>जतुका.<BR>—कृष्ण-वल्ली, f. a plant, a dark kind<BR>of Basil, Ocymum Pilosum; a kind of Śārivā.<BR>—कृष्ण-वानर, अस्, m. a black kind of monkey.<BR>—कृष्ण-विन्ना, f., N. of a river.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>विषाणा, f., Ved. the horns of the black antelope,<BR>whose inner sides are covered with dark hair.<BR>—कृष्ण-वीज, अस्, m. a red variety of the Mo-<BR>ringa plant, Rakta-śigru; (अम्), n. a water melon.<BR>—कृष्ण-वृन्ता, f. the trumpet flower, Bignonia<BR>Suaveolens; a leguminous plant, Glycine Debilis.<BR>—कृष्ण-वृन्तिका, f. the tree Gmelina Arborea;<BR>see गम्भीरा.<BR>—कृष्ण-वेणा or ई, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—कृष्ण-व्यथिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. whose path<BR>is black (?), an epithet of Agni.<BR>—कृष्ण-व्रीहि,<BR>इस्, m. a black sort of rice.<BR>—कृष्ण-शकुनि, इस्,<BR>m. a crow.<BR>—कृष्ण-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—कृष्ण-शार, अस्, m. = कृष्ण-सार,<BR>the spotted antelope.<BR>—कृष्ण-शालि, इस्, m. a sort<BR>of rice of a dark colour.<BR>—कृष्ण-शिग्रु, उस्, m. a<BR>kind of Moringa; [cf. शोभाञ्जन.]<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>शिम्बिका, f., N. of a plant, = काकाण्डी, = महा-<BR>ज्योतिष्मती.<BR>—कृष्ण-शिम्बी, f. a sort of bean,<BR>Dolichus Virosus.<BR>—कृष्ण-शृङ्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>buffalo with black horns.<BR>—कृष्ण-श्रित or कृष्-<BR>णं-श्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, worshipping or devoted to<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्ण-सख, अस्, m. a friend or fol-<BR>lower of Kṛṣṇa, especially an epithet of Arjuna;<BR>(ई), f. cummin seed.<BR>—कृष्ण-समुद्भवा, f.,<BR>N. of a river, = कृष्णा, कृष्ण-गङ्गा, कृष्ण-<BR>वेण्या.<BR>—कृष्ण-सरस्, अस्, n., N. of a lake.<BR>—कृष्ण-सर्प, अस्, m. a very poisonous snake,<BR>Cobra de Capello, Colubra Naga; (आ), f. a plant, =<BR>कृष्ण-कापोती.<BR>—कृष्ण-सर्षप, अस्, m. black<BR>mustard.<BR>—कृष्ण-सार, अस्, आ, अम्, spotted black;<BR>(अस्), m. with and without मृग, the spotted ante-<BR>lope; several plants, a kind of Euphorbia; the plant<BR>Dalbergia Sisoo; another plant, Acacia Catechu;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of Euphorbia; the plant Dalbergia<BR>Sisoo.<BR>—कृष्ण-सारङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, spotted<BR>black; (अस्), m. the spotted antelope.<BR>—कृष्ण-<BR>सारथि, इस्, m. having Kṛṣṇa for a charioteer, an<BR>epithet of Arjuna; the tree Terminalia Arjuna.<BR>—कृष्ण-सार्वभौम, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—कृष्ण-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>work Trepanakriya-kathā.<BR>—कृष्ण-सीत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. drawing black furrows; (Sāy) having a black<BR>path (as an epithet of fire).<BR>—कृष्ण-सुन्दर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of this<BR>man.<BR>—कृष्ण-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a tree which bears<BR>black blossoms, the Tamāla tree; [cf. काल-स्कन्ध.]<BR>—कृष्ण-स्वसृ, सा, f. the sister of Kṛṣṇa,<BR>an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—कृष्णागत (˚ण-आग्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, devoted to Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्णागुरु (˚ण-<BR>अग्˚), उ, n. a black variety of Agallochum or Aloe<BR>wood.<BR>—कृष्णाचल (˚ण-अच्˚), अस्, m. an epi-<BR>thet of the mountain Raivata, part of the western<BR>portion of the Vindhya chain; it is also one of the<BR>nine principal mountains that separate the nine di-<BR>visions or Varṣas of the known world.<BR>—कृष्णा-<BR>जिन (˚ण-अज्˚), अम्, n., Ved. the skin of the black<BR>antelope; (अस्), m., N. of a man (‘covered with the<BR>skin of a black antelope’); (आस्), m. pl. the descend-<BR>ants of this man.<BR>—कृष्णाजिनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, covered<BR>with the skin of a black antelope.<BR>—कृष्णाञ्जनी,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">Page0251-c+ 77</a>]<BR>f., N. of a plant, = कालाञ्जनी.<BR>—कृष्णाञ्जि (˚ण-<BR>अञ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having black marks.<BR>—कृष्णा-<BR>त्रेय (˚ण-आत्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR>—कृष्णा-<BR>ध्वन् (˚ण-अध्˚), आ, आ, अ, Ved. having a black<BR>path (an epithet of Agni).<BR>—कृष्णा-नदी, f., N.<BR>of a river, probably the Kistna in the Dekhan.<BR>—कृष्णानन्द (˚ण-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>scholiast; N. of the author of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—कृष्णाभा (˚ण-आभा), f., N. of a plant, =<BR>कालाञ्जनी.<BR>—कृष्णामिष (˚ण-आम्˚), अम्, n.<BR>iron; (probably only a various reading for कृष्णा-<BR>यस.)<BR>—कृष्णायस्, अस्, or कृष्णायस (˚ण-अय्˚),<BR>अम्, n. iron, crude or black iron.<BR>—कृष्णार्चिस्<BR>(˚ण-अर्˚), इस्, m. fire; [cf. कृष्ण-च्छवि.]<BR>—कृष्-<BR>णार्जक (˚ण-अर्˚), अस्, m. a black species of Basil,<BR>Ocimum Sanctum.<BR>—कृष्णालङ्कार (˚ण-अल्˚), अस्,<BR>m. title of a commentary.<BR>—कृष्णालु (˚ण-आलु),<BR>उस्, m. a kind of ebony.<BR>—कृष्णावतार (˚ण-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. an Avatār of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्णा-<BR>वदात, अस्, आ, अम्, black and white.<BR>—कृष्णा-<BR>वास (˚ण-आव्˚), अस्, m. the holy fig tree, Ficus<BR>Religiosa, (the abode of Kṛṣṇa.)<BR>—कृष्णाश्रित<BR>(˚ण-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to or the votary of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कृष्णेक्षु (˚ण-इक्˚), उस्, m. a sort of<BR>sugar-cane.<BR>—कृष्णैत (˚ण-एत), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>spotted black.<BR>—कृष्णोदर (˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>kind of snake.<BR>—कृष्णोदुम्बरिका (˚ण-उद्˚), f.<BR>Ficus Oppositifolia; [cf. काकोदुम्बर.]<BR>—कृष्णो-<BR>पनिषद् (˚ण-उप्˚), त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad in<BR>praise of the god Kṛṣṇa, being a part of the Gopālo-<BR>paniṣad.<BR>—कृष्णोरग (˚ण-उर्˚), अस्, m. a kind<BR>of black snake.<BR>—कृष्णो ऽस्याखरेष्ठक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, containing the words कृष्णोऽस्याखरेष्ठः<BR>(as an Adhyāya or Anuvāka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ण|कृष्णं|कृष्णः
2. कृष्ण, nom. P. कृष्णति, to behave or act<BR>like Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णक|कृष्णकं
कृष्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, black, blackish; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of plant, = कृष्ण-तण्डुला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णल|कृष्णलः
कृष्णल, अस्, अम्, m. n. the black berry of the<BR>plant Abrus Precatorius, used as a weight (the average<BR>weight being between one and two grains); a coin<BR>of about the same weight; (आ), f. a shrub bearing a<BR>small black and red berry, Abrus Precatorius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलक|कृष्णलकः
कृष्णलक, अस्, m. the black berry of the plant<BR>Abrus Precatorius or a coin of about the same<BR>weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णश
कृष्णश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. blackish; (Sāy.)<BR>extremely black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाय
कृष्णाय, nom. A. -यते, -यितुम्, to make<BR>black; to behave like Kṛṣṇa; [cf. Russ. cernjû.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिका
कृष्णिका, f. black mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिमन्
कृष्णिमन्, आ, m. blackness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिय
कृष्णिय, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man protected<BR>by the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीकरण|कृष्णीकरणं
कृष्णी-करण, अम्, n. blackening, making<BR>black.<BR>—कृष्णी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, blackened, made<BR>black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीभूत
कृष्णी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णेय
कृष्णेय, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्य
कृष्य कृष्य. See under कृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृसर|कृसरः
कृसर कृसर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>कृ), a dish consisting of sesamum and grain; a<BR>mixture of rice and peas with a few spices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
कॄ 1. कॄ, cl. 6. P. किरति, चकार, करिष्-<BR>यति and करीष्यति, अकारीत्, करितुम् and<BR>करीतुम्, to pour out, scatter, throw, cast, disperse;<BR>to strew, pour over, fill with, cover with: Caus.<BR>कारयति: Desid. चिकरिषति: Intens. चेकीर्यते,<BR>चाकर्ति; [cf. Gr. κεράω, κεράννυμι, κίρνημι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्ण|कीर्णः|कीर्ण्ण
कीर्ण, कीर्णि, &c. See s. v. at p. 231.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
कॄ 2. कॄ (or sometimes written कृ), cl. 5.<BR>and 9. P. A. कृणोति, -णुते, कृणाति, -णीते,<BR>चकार, चकरे and चक्रे, करिष्यति, -ते, अक-<BR>रीष्ट, अकरिष्ट, अकीर्ष्ट, करितुम्, करीतुम्,<BR>कर्तुम्, to hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
कॄ 3. कॄ, cl. 10. A. कारयते, -यितुम्, to<BR>know, inform; (an incorrect form for गॄ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄत्
कॄत् कॄत्, cl. 10. P. (sometimes A.) कीर्त-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अचीकृतत् or अचि-<BR>कीर्तत्, to mention, make mention of, tell, name,<BR>call, recite, repeat, relate, declare, communicate, com-<BR>memorate, celebrate, praise, glorify; [cf. Lat. celeber.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तन|कीर्तनं|कीर्त्तन|कीर्त्तनं
कीर्तन, अम्, n. mentioning, repeating, saying,<BR>telling, celebrating, praising; (आ), f. fame, glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तनीय
कीर्तनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be mentioned, to be<BR>named or repeated, to be celebrated or praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तन्य|कीर्त्तन्य
कीर्तन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, deserving to be mentioned,<BR>to be related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तयत्|कीर्त्तयत्
कीर्तयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, mentioning, relating, re-<BR>peating, celebrating, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तित|कीर्त्तित|कीर्त्तितः
कीर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, said, asserted; mentioned, re-<BR>peated; known, notorious; celebrated, praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तितव्य
कीर्तितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be mentioned or praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तेन्य
कीर्तेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. deserving to be named<BR>or praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्ति|कीर्ति|कीर्तिः|कीर्त्तिः
कीर्त्ति or कीर्ति, इस्, f. mention, making mention of,<BR>speech, report; good report, fame, renown, glory;<BR>Fame personified as daughter of Dakṣa and wife of<BR>Dharma; extension, expansion, diffusion; light,<BR>lustre; favour, approbation; sound; dirt, mud; one<BR>of the Mātṛkās or personified divine energies of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, conferring fame.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-धर, अस्, m., N. of a copyist.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-<BR>प्रताप-बल-सहित, अस्, आ, अम्, attended with<BR>fame, majesty, and power.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-भाज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>receiving fame, celebrated, famous; (क्), m. an<BR>epithet of Droṇācārya, the military preceptor of the<BR>Pāṇḍus and Kurus.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, praised,<BR>famous, celebrated; (आन्), m., N. of one of the<BR>Viśva-devās; a son of Uttāna-pāda and Sūnṛtā; also<BR>a son of Vasu-deva and Devakī; also a son of<BR>Aṅgiras.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>fame.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a prince of the<BR>Videhas, a son of Pratīndhaka; also called कृत्ति-<BR>रथ as son of Prasiddhaka.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-रात, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a prince of the Videhas, a son of Mahāndhraka.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-<BR>वास, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—कीर्त्ति-शेष, अस्, m.<BR>death (the leaving behind of nothing but fame); [cf.<BR>आलेख्य-शेष, नाम-शेष, यशः-शेष.]<BR>—कीर्त्ति-<BR>सेन, अस्, m., N. of a nephew of Vāsuki, the serpent-<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्य
कीर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised or celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्
कॢप् कॢप्, cl. 1. A. (and in Fut., Cond.,<BR>and Aor. also P.) कल्पते, चकॢपे, कल्पि-<BR>ष्यते and कल्प्स्यति, अकल्पिष्ट, अकॢप्त and<BR>अकॢपत्, कल्पितुम् and कल्प्तुम्, to be well<BR>ordered or regulated, to be well managed; to suc-<BR>ceed; to bear suitable relation to anything, to cor-<BR>respond, be adapted to, fit for, in accordance with,<BR>suitable to; to accommodate one's self to; to be fa-<BR>vourable to, to subserve, to effect or obtain for one's<BR>self; to partake of, become possessed of; to fall to the<BR>share, be shared or partaken by (with loc., e. g. यज्ञो<BR>देवेषु कल्पताम्, let the sacrifice be shared by the<BR>gods); to become, to be; to happen, occur; to de-<BR>clare as right, decide in favour of (?); to prepare,<BR>arrange; to produce, cause, effect, create (with acc.):<BR>Caus. P. A. कल्पयति, -ते, Aor. अचीकॢपत्, Ved.<BR>चाकॢपत्, चीकॢपाति, &c., to set in order, arrange,<BR>distribute, dispose; to bring into suitable connection<BR>with, to cause any one (acc.) to partake of anything<BR>(inst.); to help any one in obtaining (dat.); to pre-<BR>pare, arrange, fit out, furnish with; to consider as fit;<BR>to fix, settle; to destine or design anything for; to<BR>declare as, consider as (with two acc., e. g. मातरम्<BR>एनां कल्पयन्तु, let them consider her as their<BR>mother); to make, execute, bring about; to frame,<BR>form; to invent, compose (as a poem &c.); to per-<BR>form (as a ceremony &c.); to pronounce a formula<BR>or verse which contains the word कॢप्; to cut, pare,<BR>cut asunder (only in Prākṛt): Desid. चिकॢप्सति<BR>and चिकल्पिषते: Intens. चली˚ or चलि˚ or चल्कल्प्-<BR>यते, चल्कल्प्ति; [cf. Goth. hilpa; Eng. help;<BR>Germ. helfe; Lith. gelbmi.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्त|कॢप्तः
कॢप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, arranged, prepared, ready, at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">Page0252-b+ 74</a>]<BR>hand, in order, complete, right, perfect; made, done;<BR>formed, framed; caused, produced, effected, invented,<BR>contrived, created; fixed, settled, prescribed, ap-<BR>pointed; ascertained, determined; cut, clipt, pared,<BR>shorn.<BR>—कॢप्त-कीला, f. title-deed, lease of a house<BR>&c.<BR>—कॢप्त-केश-नख-श्मश्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>the hair, nails, and beard cut or clipt and arranged.<BR>—कॢप्त-धूप, अस्, m. frankincense, olibanum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्ति|कॢप्तिः
कॢप्ति, इस्, f., Ved. accomplishment, success;<BR>distributing, arranging, making conformable; inven-<BR>tion, contrivance; a term for certain formulas or<BR>verses containing the verb कॢप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तिक|कॢप्तिकः
कॢप्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, bought, purchased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकय|केकयः
केकय केकय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-<BR>tribe; (अस्), m. the chief of this tribe, a prince of<BR>the solar race; (ई), f. a princess of this tribe, wife of<BR>Daśa-ratha and mother of Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकर|केकरः
केकर केकर, अस्, ई, अम्, or केकराक्ष (˚र-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, squint-eyed; [cf. केदर and<BR>टेरक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकल
केकल केकल, अस्, m. a dancer; (perhaps a<BR>various reading for केलक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केका
केका केका, f. the cry of a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकावल|केकावलः
केकावल or केकिक, अस्, m., or केकिन्, ई, m. a<BR>peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकेयी
केकेयी केकेयी, f. one of Daśa-ratha's<BR>three wives, the mother of Bharata; (a wrong form<BR>for कैकेयी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचुक|केचुकं
केचुक केचुक, अस्, आ, m. f. a plant with<BR>an esculent root, Colocasia Antiquorum; (अम्), n.<BR>the esculent root of this plant; [cf. कचु, कच्वी,<BR>केमुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केणिका
केणिका केणिका, f. a tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केत|केतः
केत केत, अस्, m. (connected with 2. का or<BR>कित् = चित् ?), desire, wish, will, intention; summons,<BR>invitation; a house, an abode; apparition, form,<BR>shape; (Sāy.) wealth; atmosphere, sky.<BR>—केत-पू,<BR>ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. purifying the desire or will.<BR>—केत-<BR>वेदस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. desirous, wishful; (Sāy.)<BR>knowing the wealth of another.<BR>—केत-साप्, प्, प्, प्,<BR>Ved. obeying the will (of another), obedient; (Sāy.)<BR>touching the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतन|केतनं
केतन, अम्, n. a summons, an invitation; a<BR>house, an abode; place, site, situation; the symbol<BR>of a goddess; the ensign of a warrior, a flag or<BR>banner (e. g. वानर-केतन, one who has a monkey<BR>as his ensign or arms; see also मकर-केतन, &c.);<BR>a sign, a spot or mark; business, indispensable act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतय
केतय, nom. P. केतयति, -यितुम्, to summon,<BR>to call or invite; to counsel or advise; to fix or<BR>appoint a time; to hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतित
केतित, अस्, आ, अम्, called, summoned; dwelt,<BR>inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतक|केतकः
केतक केतक, अस्, ई, m. f. the tree Pandanus<BR>Odoratissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतलिकीर्ति
केतलिकीर्ति केतलि-कीर्ति, इस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the work Megha-mālā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतु|केतुः
केतु केतु, उस्, m. (fr. कि for rt. 2. चि), bright<BR>appearance, clearness, brightness; a ray of light;<BR>day-time; apparition, form, shape; sign, mark, ensign,<BR>flag, banner; a chief, a leader, any eminent person;<BR>intellect, judgment, discernment; any unusual or<BR>striking phenomena, a comet, meteor, falling star;<BR>the dragon's tail or descending node considered in<BR>astronomy as the ninth of the planets, and in<BR>mythology as the body of the demon Saiṃhikeya,<BR>son of Siṃhikā, which was severed from the head or<BR>Rāhu by Viṣṇu at the churning of the ocean, but<BR>was rendered immortal by having tasted the Amṛta;<BR>a pigmy race (see केतु-गण below); disease; an<BR>enemy; N. of a son of Agni, supposed to be the<BR>author of a Ṛg-veda hymn; N. of a Dānava; N. of<BR>a son of Ṛṣabha; also of a son of the fourth Manu;<BR>अरुणाः केतवः, red apparitions, a class of superhuman<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">Page0252-c+ 74</a>]<BR>spirits or demons, (a kind of sacrificial fire is called<BR>after them अग्निर् आरुणकेतुकः.)<BR>—केतु-गण, आस्,<BR>m. pl. the dwarfish inhabitants of Kuśa-dvīpa, children<BR>of Jaimini.<BR>—केतु-ग्रह, अस्, m. the descending<BR>node.<BR>—केतु-तारा, f. a comet.<BR>—केतु-धर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a man.<BR>—केतु-भ, अस्, m. a cloud.<BR>—केतु-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being or become a<BR>banner.<BR>—केतु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed with<BR>brightness, clear; clear (as a sound), penetrating;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a Dānava; of a regent of the<BR>western part of the world, a son of Rajas; of a<BR>son of Kṣema and father of Suketu; of a son of<BR>Kṣema and father of Varṣa-ketu; of a warrior; of<BR>a son of Dhanvantari; of Ambarīṣa; N. of a<BR>mountain; N. of a palace of Sunandā, the wife of<BR>Vāsu-deva; (ती), f., N. of a metre consisting of two<BR>lines of twenty-one syllables each.<BR>—केतु-माला, f.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (अम्),<BR>n. one of the nine great divisions of the known world,<BR>the western portion or Varṣa of Jambu-dvīpa,<BR>called after a son of Agnīdhra; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>boar.<BR>—केतुमालिन्, ई, or केतुमालि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>Dānava.<BR>—केतु-यष्टि, इस्, f. a flag-staff.<BR>—केतु-<BR>रत्न, अम्, n. lapis lazuli.<BR>—केतु-वसन, अस्, m.<BR>a flag.<BR>—केतु-वीर्य, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—केतु-शृङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदर|केदरः
केदर केदर, अस्, आ, अम्, squint-eyed; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a plant; [cf. केकर and टेरक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदार|केदारः
केदार केदार, अस्, m. a field, especially<BR>one under water, a meadow, a plain; a basin for<BR>water round the root of a tree, a bed in a garden or<BR>field; a mountain; a particular mountain; a parti-<BR>cular place, the modern Kedār, part of the Himālaya<BR>mountains; an epithet of Śiva as worshipped in the<BR>Himālayas; N. of the author of a work entitled<BR>Abdhi.<BR>—केदार-कटुका, f., N. of a plant, = कटुका.<BR>—केदार-कल्प, अस्, m. a part of the Skanda-purāṇa.<BR>—केदार-खण्ड, अम्, n. a small dyke or mound,<BR>earth raised to keep out water; a part of the Skanda-<BR>purāṇa.<BR>—केदार-ज, अम्, n., N. of a plant.<BR>—के-<BR>दार-नाथ, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva as worshipped<BR>in the Himālayas.<BR>—केदार-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an author.<BR>—केदार-मल्ल, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Madanapāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदारक|केदारकः
केदारक, अस्, m. a particular kind of rice, =<BR>षष्टिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन
केन केन, ind. (inst. fr. 2. क), by what?<BR>wherefore? whence?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनती
केनती केनती, f. an epithet of the wife of<BR>Kāma, the god of love; (a wrong form?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनव
केनव केनव, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Śākapūrṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनार|केनारः
केनार केनार, अस्, m. the head; a skull;<BR>the temples, the upper part of the cheek; a joint; a<BR>division of hell, a hell compared to a potter's kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनिप
केनिप केनिप, अस्, m., Ved. a sage, a wise<BR>man; [cf. आकेनिप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनिपात|केनिपातः
केनिपात केनिपात or केनिपातक, अस्, m. the<BR>helm, a rudder, a large oar used as a rudder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनेषितोपनिषद्
केनेषितोपनिषद् केनेषितोपनिषद् or केनो-<BR>पनिषद्, त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad beginning with<BR>the word केनेषितम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्दु|केन्दुः
केन्दु केन्दु, उस्, m. a kind of ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्दुक|केन्दुकः
केन्दुक, अस्, m. another variety of ebony yielding<BR>a species of tar, Diospyros Glutinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्द्र|केंद्र|केंद्रं|केन्द्रं
केन्द्र केन्द्र, अम्, n. (a word borrowed from<BR>the Gr. κέντρον), the centre of a circle; the equation<BR>of the centre; the argument of a circle; the argu-<BR>ment of an equation; the distance of a planet from<BR>the first point of its orbit in the fourth, seventh, or<BR>tenth degree; it is variously applied in composition,<BR>as पतन-केन्द्रम्, argument of the latitude;<BR>द्वितीय-केन्द्रम्, the distance of the higher apsis of<BR>a planet in any point of its orbit; शीघ्र-केन्द्रम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">Page0253-a+ 72</a>]<BR>commutation, the distance of the sun from a superior<BR>planet or of an inferior planet from the sun; मन्द-<BR>केन्द्रम्, argument of anomaly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केप्
केप् केप्, cl. 1. A. केपते, to shake or<BR>tremble [cf. कम्प् and वेप्]; to go,<BR>move, approach [cf. गेप्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केपि
केपि केपि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. unclean; (or fr. rt.<BR>कम्प्), trembling, shaking (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केमद्रुम|केमद्रुमः
केमद्रुम केमद्रुम in astronomy = the<BR>Gr. χρηματισμός<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केमुक|केमुकः
केमुक केमुक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, =<BR>केचुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केयूर|केयूरं|केयूरः
केयूर केयूर, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bracelet worn<BR>on the upper arm; (अस्), m. a kind of coitus.<BR>—केयूर-बल, अस्, m., N. of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केयूरक
केयूरक, अस्, m., N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केयूरिन्
केयूरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, decorated with a bracelet on<BR>the upper arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केरक
केरक केरक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केरल|केरलः
केरल केरल, आस्, m. pl., N. of the inha-<BR>bitants of Malabar; (अस्), m. sing. a king of the<BR>Keralas; N. of a son of Ākrīḍa, from whom the<BR>people of Kerala are derived; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>science; astronomical science; an astronomical Śāstra<BR>or treatise; a Hora or period of time equal to about<BR>one hour; (अम्), n., N. of the country inhabited by<BR>the Keralas.<BR>—केरलोत्पत्ति (˚ल-उत्˚), इस्, f., N. of<BR>a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केरलक
केरलक, आस्, m. pl., N. of the inhabitants of<BR>Malabar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केल्
केल् केल् [cf. Prākṛt कील् = क्रीड्], cl. 1. P.<BR>केलति, to shake; to go or move, move<BR>about, be frolicsome, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलक|केलकः
केलक, अस्, m. a dancer, a tumbler, one who walks<BR>or dances on the edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलाय
केलाय, nom. P. केलायति, -यितुम्, to sport, play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलि|केलिः
केलि, इस् or ई, m. f. play, sport, amorous sport,<BR>pastime, amusement; (इस्), f. the earth.<BR>—केलि-कला,<BR>f. amorous or sportive accents or address; sportive<BR>skill, wantonness; the Vīṇā or lute of Sarasvatī.<BR>—केलि-किल, अस्, m. the confidential companion of<BR>the hero of a drama, in general a sort of buffoon;<BR>one of Śiva's attendant demi-gods; (आ), f. an epithet<BR>of Rati the wife of Kāma-deva, the god of love.<BR>—केलि-कीर्ण, अस्, m. a camel.<BR>—केलि-कुञ्चिका, f.<BR>a wife's younger sister.<BR>—केलि-कोष, अस्, m. an<BR>actor, a dancer or tumbler.<BR>—केलि-गृह or केलि-<BR>निकेतन, अम्, n. a pleasure-house, a private<BR>apartment.<BR>—केलि-नागर, अस्, m. a sensualist, an<BR>enjoyer of worldly pleasures.<BR>—केलि-पर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wanton, sportive.<BR>—केलि-मण्डप, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. or केलि-मन्दिर, अम्, n. a pleasure-house, a<BR>play-room.<BR>—केलि-मुख, अस्, m. pastime, sport.<BR>—केलि-रङ्ग, अस्, m. a pleasure-ground.<BR>—केलि-<BR>रैवतक, अम्, n. title of a treatise.<BR>—केलि-वृक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. a species of the Kadamba, commonly called<BR>Kelikadamba (Nauclea Cordifolia), being abundant in<BR>the scene of Kṛṣṇa's sports with the Gopīs.<BR>—केलि-<BR>शयन, अम्, n. a pleasure-couch, a sofa.<BR>—केलि-<BR>शुषि, इस्, f. the earth.<BR>—केलि-सचिव, अस्, m. minister<BR>of the sports, master of the revels.<BR>—केलि-सदन,<BR>अम्, n. a pleasure-house, a play-room.<BR>—केलि-स्थली,<BR>f. a place of pleasure.<BR>—केली-पिक, अस्, m. a cuckoo<BR>kept for pleasure.<BR>—केली-वनी, f. a pleasure-park, a<BR>pleasure-grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिक|केलिकः
केलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, sporting, sportive; (अस्), m.<BR>the tree Jonesia Aśoka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केल
केल केल or केलु, a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलास|केलासः
केलास केलास, अस्, m. crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केव्
केव् केव्, cl. 1. A. केवते, -वितुम्, to<BR>serve, attend to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवट|केवटः
केवट केवट, अस्, m., Ved. a cave, a hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवर्त|केवर्तः|केवर्त्त|केवर्त्तः
केवर्त केवर्त, अस्, m., Ved. a fisherman,<BR>= कैवर्त, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवल|केवलं|केवलः
केवल केवल, अस्, आ (or Ved. ई), अम्, ex-<BR>clusively one's own (not common to others); peculiar;<BR>alone, only, mere, sole, one, excluding others; not<BR>connected with anything else, isolated, abstract, abso-<BR>lute; simple, pure, uncompounded, unmingled, perfect<BR>in one's self, entire, whole, all; selfish, envious;<BR>(अम्), ind. only, merely, solely, entirely, wholly,<BR>absolutely, certainly; न केवलम् — अपि, not only —<BR>but also; केवलम् — न तु, only — but not; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a prince, a son of Nara; (ई), f. the doctrine of<BR>the absolute unity of spirit; N. of a place; (अम्),<BR>n. the doctrine of the absolute unity of spirit; N. of<BR>a country.<BR>—केवल-ज्ञानिन्, ई, m., N. of the first<BR>Arhat of the last Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—केवल-तस्, ind. only.<BR>—केवल-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being alone.<BR>—केवल-द्रव्य, अम्, n. black pepper.<BR>—केवल-<BR>नैयायिक, अस्, m. a mere logician, not versed in<BR>any other science.<BR>—केवल-वैयाकरण, अस्, m.<BR>a mere grammarian, one not versed in any other<BR>science.<BR>—केवलाघ (˚ल-अघ), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>alone guilty.<BR>—केवलात्मन् (˚ल-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one<BR>whose nature or essence is absolute unity.<BR>—केवला-<BR>दिन् (˚ल-आद्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating by one's self alone<BR>or apart from others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलिन्
केवलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, alone, one, only; devoted to<BR>the doctrine of the absolute unity of spirit; (ई), m.<BR>with Jainas, an Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केविका
केविका केविका or केवी, f., N. of a flower,<BR>= कविका, commonly केवेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केश|केशः
केश केश, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. क्लिश्),<BR>the hair of the head; the mane (of a horse or lion);<BR>a kind of perfume [cf. ह्रीवेर]; an epithet of<BR>Varuṇa; of Viṣṇu; N. of a Daitya; (ई), f. a lock<BR>of hair on the crown of the head; N. of several<BR>plants, the Indigo plant; another plant, Carpopogon<BR>Pruriens; an epithet of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—केश-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. dressing or arranging the air of the<BR>head.<BR>—केश-कलाप, अस्, m. a mass or quantity of<BR>hair, a head of hair.<BR>—केश-कार, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>sugar-cane.<BR>—केश-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, dressing or ar-<BR>ranging the hair of the head.<BR>—केश-कीट, अस्, m. a<BR>louse or other insect in the hair.<BR>—केश-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a braid or tress of hair; an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—केश-गर्भक, अस्, m. a braid or tress of hair.<BR>—केश-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, pulled or seized by the<BR>hair.<BR>—केश-ग्रह, अस्, m. or केश-ग्रहण, अम्,<BR>n. pulling the hair.<BR>—केश-घ्न, अम्, n. morbid<BR>baldness, falling of the hair.<BR>—केश-चूड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has dressed his hair in a tuft or top-<BR>knot.<BR>—केश-च्छिद्, त्, m. a hair-dresser, a barber.<BR>—केश-जाह, अम्, n. the root of the hair.<BR>—केश-<BR>दृंहण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. serving for fastening the<BR>hair.<BR>—केश-धर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—केश-धृत्, त्, f., N. of a plant, the root of sweet<BR>flag.<BR>—केश-पक्ष, अस्, m. much or ornamented<BR>hair, a tuft.<BR>—केश-पङ्क्ति, इस्, f. a row or line of<BR>hair; a quantity of hair.<BR>—केश-पर्णी, f. the plant<BR>Achyranthes Aspera; also अपामार्ग.<BR>—केश-पाश,<BR>अस्, m. much or ornamented hair, a tuft; (ई), f. a<BR>lock of hair hanging down from the top of the head.<BR>—केश-बन्ध, अस्, m. a hair-band.<BR>—केश-भू,<BR>ऊस्, m. the head.<BR>—केश-भूमि, इस्, f. any place on<BR>which hair grows.<BR>—केश-मार्जक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?)<BR>a comb.<BR>—केश-मार्जन, अम्, n. a comb; cleaning<BR>the hair.<BR>—केश-मुष्टि, इस्, m. a handful of hair; N.<BR>of two plants, (also विष-मुष्टि and महा-निम्ब.)<BR>—केश-रचना, f. arranging or dressing the hair.<BR>—केश-रञ्जन or केश-राज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>vegetable, = भृङ्ग-राज.<BR>—केश-रुहा, f., N. of a<BR>plant, = भद्र-दन्तिका.<BR>—केश-रूपा, f., N. of a<BR>parasitical plant.<BR>—केश-लुञ्चक, अस्, आ, अम्, pulling<BR>the hair.<BR>—केश-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a fine head<BR>of hair; having long hair; having a mane.<BR>—केश-<BR>वपनीय, अस्, m., N. of a festival.<BR>—केश-वर्-<BR>धन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. causing the hair to grow.<BR>—केश-वर्धिनी, f., N. of a plant, a kind of Sida.<BR>—केश-वेश, अस्, m. a tress or fillet of hair.<BR>—केश-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">Page0253-c+ 79</a>]<BR>वेष्ट, अस्, m. the parting of the hair.<BR>—केश-<BR>हन्त्री, f., N. of a tree, = शमी.<BR>—केश-हस्त, अस्,<BR>m. much or ornamented hair, a tuft.<BR>—केशा-केशि,<BR>ind. hair to hair, head to head; pulling each other's<BR>hair.<BR>—केशाग्र (˚श-अग्˚), अम्, n. the top of a hair.<BR>—केशान्त (˚श-अन्˚), अस्, m. the tip or end of a<BR>hair; long hair hanging down, a lock of hair, a<BR>tuft; cutting off the hair finally, as a religious cere-<BR>mony performed upon Brāhmans at sixteen years of<BR>age, Kṣatriyas at twenty-two, and Vaiśyas at twenty-<BR>four.<BR>—केशान्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, extending to the end<BR>of the hair as far as the forehead; relating to the<BR>ceremony of final tonsure.<BR>—केशारि (˚श-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. the plant Mesua Ferrea.<BR>—केशारुहा (˚श-आर्˚),<BR>f., N. of a plant, = सह-देवी.<BR>—केशार्हा (˚श-अर्˚),<BR>f., N. of a plant, = महानीली.<BR>—केशावमर्षण<BR>(˚श-अव्˚), अम्, n. pulling the hair, especially amo-<BR>rously playing with it, rubbing it, &c.<BR>—केशोच्चय<BR>(˚श-उच्˚), अस्, m. much or handsome hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशक|केशकः
केशक, अस्, आ, अम्, skilful in dressing hair, be-<BR>stowing care upon the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशव|केशवः
केशव, अस्, आ, अम्, having long or much or hand-<BR>some hair; (अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa;<BR>N. of the author of a lexicon called Kalpa-dru; the<BR>author of the Dvaita-pariśiṣṭa; the father of Govinda<BR>and Rucikara; N. of the father of Brāhma and uncle<BR>of Maheśvara; N. of the son of Viśvadhara and<BR>brother of Karinātha; N. of the father of Vopadeva;<BR>N. of a plant, = पुन्नाग.<BR>—केशव-जातक-पद्-<BR>धत्य्-उदाहरण, अम्, n. a commentary by Viś-<BR>vanātha on the work Jātaka-paddhati.<BR>—केशव-जी-<BR>नन्द-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of an author.<BR>—केशव-<BR>दास, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—केशव-दैवज्ञ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an astronomer.<BR>—केशव-भक्ति, इस्,<BR>f. devotion to Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—केशव-मिश्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—केशव-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>grammarian.<BR>—केशवायुध (˚व-आय्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>Mango tree; any of Kṛṣṇa's weapons.<BR>—केशवार्क<BR>(˚व-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of the poem<BR>Kṛṣṇa-krīḍita, a son of Jayāditya and grandson of<BR>Rāṇiga; N. of the author of a work called Jātaka-<BR>paddhati; N. of the author of a work called Vivāha-<BR>vṛndāvana<BR>—केशवालय (˚व-आल्˚) or केशवा-<BR>वाल (?) or केशवावास (˚व-आव्˚), अस्, m. the holy<BR>fig tree, Ficus Religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशि
केशि, इस्, m., N. of an Asura; [cf. केशिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिक|केशिकः
केशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having fine or luxuriant hair,<BR>relating to the hair; (आ), f. the plant Asparagus<BR>Racemosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिन्
केशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having fine or long hair, having<BR>a mane; epithet of Indra's and Agni's horses;<BR>epithet of Rudra; (ई), m. a lion; N. of a race; N.<BR>of an Asura slain by Kṛṣṇa; an epithet of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>N. of a son of Vasu-deva and Kauśalyā; (इनी), f. the<BR>plant Chrysopogon Aciculatus; another plant, Nar-<BR>dostachys Jaṭāmāṃsī; an epithet of the goddess<BR>Durgā; N. of an Apsaras; N. of a daughter of the<BR>king of Vidarbha, wife of Sagara and mother of<BR>Asamañja; N. of the wife of Ājamīḍha (Suhotra)<BR>and mother of Jahnu; N. of the wife of Viśravas<BR>and mother of Rāvaṇa and Kumbhakarṇa; N. of a<BR>Rākṣasī; N. of a servant of Damayantī.<BR>—केशि-<BR>निसूदन or केशि-मथन or केशि-सूदन, अस्, m.<BR>or केशि-हन्, आ, m. &c. epithet of Kṛṣṇa the slayer<BR>of the Asura Keśin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केश्य|केश्यं|केश्यः
केश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in or on the hair; suit-<BR>able to the hair; (अस्), m., N. of a plant; (अम्), n.<BR>black Aloe wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशट|केशटः
केशट केशट, अस्, m. a goat; a bug; a<BR>louse; N. of a tree, commonly Sonapat, = शोणक;<BR>the parching arrow of Kāma-deva, the god of love;<BR>a brother; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशारुका
केशारुका केशारुका, f. = कशेरुका, the<BR>back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसर|केसरं|केसरः
केसर केसर or केशर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (the<BR>former form being more usual in Vedic and the latter<BR>in classical literature), the hair; the mane (of a<BR>horse or lion); the filament of a lotus or of any<BR>vegetable; a fibre (as of a Mango fruit); (अम्), n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">Page0254-a+ 74</a>]<BR>the tail of the Bos Grunniens, used as a fan for<BR>driving away flies; (अस्), m., N. of several plants,<BR>Rottleria Tinctoria; Mimusops Elengi; Mesua Ferrea;<BR>(अम्), n. the flower of these plants; gold; sulphate<BR>of iron; N. of a metre consisting of four lines of<BR>eighteen syllables each; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. Asa<BR>Fœtida; [cf. Lat. cœsaries; Angl. Sax. haer;<BR>Eng. hair; Germ. Haar.]<BR>—केसर-ग्राम, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Grāma.<BR>—केसर-प्राबन्धा, f., Ved.,<BR>N. of a woman.<BR>—केसर-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a mane.<BR>—केसर-वर, अम्, n. saffron.<BR>—केसरा-<BR>चल (˚र-अच्˚), अस्, m. ‘the filament mountain,’ N. of<BR>the mountains situated round Meru, which is called<BR>‘the seed-vessel of the earth.’<BR>—केसराम्ल (˚र-<BR>अम्˚), अस्, m. the citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरि|केसरिः
केसरि, इस्, m., N. of the father of Hanumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिन्
केसरिन् and केशरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a mane;<BR>(ई), m. a lion; a horse; N. of several plants, Rottle-<BR>ria Tinctoria; Mesua Ferrea; a citron tree; a variety<BR>of Moringa with red flowers (= रक्त-शिग्रु); N.<BR>of a man; of a monkey, husband of the mother of<BR>Hanumat.<BR>—केसरि-सुत, अस्, m., N. of Hanumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केह्लदेव
केह्लदेव केह्ल-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कै
कै कै, cl. 1. P. कायति, चकौ, कास्यति,<BR>कातुम्, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैकय|कैकयः
कैकय कैकय, अस्, m. the king of the<BR>Kekayas; (आस्), m. pl. the sons of this king; (ई), f.<BR>a daughter of this king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैकेय|कैकेयः
कैकेय, अस्, m. a descendant of Kekaya, who was<BR>prince of the Kekayas; a son of Śivi; Dṛṣṭaketu,<BR>king of the Kekayas and father of the five Kaikeyas;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the Kekayas; (ई), f. a daughter of the<BR>prince of the Kekayas, one of the wives of Daśa-<BR>ratha, mother of Bharata; a shrew, a scold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैङ्कर्य|कैंकर्यं|कैङ्कर्य्य|कैङ्कर्य्यं
कैङ्कर्य कैङ्कर्य, अम्, n. (fr. किङ्-कर), the<BR>office of a servant or slave; service, servitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैट
कैट कैट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कीट), coming from<BR>an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटज|कैटजः
कैटज कैटज, अस्, m. = कुटज, the plant<BR>Wrightia Antidysenterica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभ|कैटभः
कैटभ कैटभ, अस्, m., N. of an Asura<BR>slain by Viṣṇu; title of a class of writings; (आ and ई),<BR>f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—कैटभ-जित्, त्, m. or कै-<BR>टभ-हन्, आ, m. or कैटभारि (˚भ-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>or कैटभार्दन (˚भ-अर्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटर्य|कैटर्यः|कैटर्य्य|कैटर्य्यः
कैटर्य कैटर्य, अस्, m. a plant used in<BR>medicine, commonly Kayaphal; the Nimb tree;<BR>Mayana Vangueria Spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैडर्य|कैडर्य्य|कैडर्य्यः
कैडर्य, अस्, m., N. of two plants, = कट्फल<BR>and कटभी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतक|कैतकं
कैतक कैतक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. केतक), coming<BR>from the plant Pandanus Odoratissimus; (अम्), n.<BR>the flower of the tree Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतव|कैतवं|कैतवः
कैतव कैतव, अस्, m. (fr. कितव), a patro-<BR>nymic of Ulūka; (अम्), n. the stake in a game;<BR>gambling; deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery; the lapis<BR>lazuli.<BR>—कैतव-प्रयोग, अस्, m. a trick, a device.<BR>—कैतव-वाद, अस्, m. falsehood, evasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतवक|कैतवकं
कैतवक, अम्, n. gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतवेय
कैतवेय or कैतव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Ulūka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार|कैदारं|कैदारः
कैदार कैदार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. केदार), being<BR>on or growing in a field or meadow, especially one<BR>under water; (अस्), m. rice, corn; (अम्), n. a multi-<BR>tude of fields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदारक|कैदारकं
कैदारक or कैदारिक or कैदार्य, अम्, n. a<BR>multitude of fields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार्य|कैदार्य्य|कैदार्य्यं
कैदार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैन्नर|कैंनर
कैन्नर कैन्नर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. किन् नर),<BR>coming from Kinnara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैयट
कैयट कैयट or कैय्यट, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Jaiyaṭa, author of a commentary on Patañ-<BR>jali's Mahā-bhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरलेय
कैरलेय कैरलेय, अस्, m. a king of the<BR>Keralas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरव|कैरवं|कैरवः
कैरव कैरव, अस्, m. a gambler, a cheat,<BR>a rogue; an enemy; (अम्), n. the white esculent<BR>water-lily or lotus blossoming at night; (ई), f. moon-<BR>shine, moonlight; N. of a plant, = मेथिका.<BR>—कै-<BR>रव-बन्धु, उस्, m. an epithet of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविन्
कैरविन्, ई, m. the moon; (इणी), f. a place or<BR>pond abounding in water-lilies, an assemblage of<BR>them.<BR>—कैरविणी-खण्ड, अम्, n. a multitude of<BR>spots filled with water-lilies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैराटक|कैराटकः
कैराटक कैराटक, अस्, m. a species of<BR>vegetable poison, one of the fixed kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरात|कैरातं|कैरातः
कैरात कैरात, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. किरात), relating<BR>or belonging to the Kirātas; (अस्), m. a prince of<BR>the Kirātas; a strong man; N. of a serpent; (अम्),<BR>n. the plant Agathotes Chirayta; a kind of sandal-<BR>wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरातक
कैरातक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the Kirāta<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरातिक
कैरातिक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to the<BR>Kirātas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैराल|कैरालं
कैराल कैराल, अम्, ई, n. f., N. of a plant,<BR>used as a remedy for worms; [cf. विडङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरिशि
कैरिशि कैरिशि, इस्, m. (fr. किरिशि), a patro-<BR>nymic of Sutvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैर्मेदुर
कैर्मेदुर कैर्मेदुर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), N. of<BR>a place; (अस्, ई, अम्), coming from that place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैल|कैलं
कैल कैल, अम्, n. sport, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलकिल|कैलकिलः
कैलकिल कैलकिल, an epithet of Yavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलावत
कैलावत कैलावत, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलास|कैलासः
कैलास कैलास, अस्, m., N. of the mountain<BR>Kailāsa, the fabulous residence of Kuvera and paradise<BR>of Śiva; it is placed by the Hindūs in the Himālaya<BR>range, and is regarded as one of the loftiest peaks to<BR>the north of the Mānasa lake.<BR>—कैलास-नाथ, अस्,<BR>m. the sovereign of the Kailāsa mountain, i. e. the<BR>god Kuvera.<BR>—कैलास-निकेतन, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Kuvera of Śiva<BR>—कैलास-पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a copyist.<BR>—कैलासौकस् (˚स-ओक्˚), आस्, m. an epi-<BR>thet of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त|कैवर्तः|कैवर्त्त|कैवर्त्तः
कैवर्त कैवर्त, अस्, m. [cf. केवर्त], a<BR>fisherman, born of a prostitute by a Kṣatriya or of<BR>an Āyogava female by a Niṣāda father; (ई), f. the<BR>wife of a fisherman; a kind of grass, Cyperus Ro-<BR>tundus; [cf. परिपेल.]<BR>—कैवर्त-मुस्त or कै-<BR>वर्त-मुस्तक, अम्, n. the grass Cyperus Rotundus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्तक|कैवर्तकः|कैवर्त्तक
कैवर्तक, अस्, m. a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्तिका|कैवर्त्तिका
कैवर्तिका, f., N. of a plant, = सुरङ्गा, लता,<BR>वल्ली, दशरुहा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्तिमुस्तक|कैवर्त्तिमुस्तक|कैवर्त्तिमुस्तकं
