कैवल|कैवलं
कैवल कैवल, अम्, n. a kind of plant, used<BR>as a remedy for worms, = कैराल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवल्य|कैवल्यं
कैवल्य कैवल्य, अम्, n. (fr. केवल), perfect<BR>isolation, abstraction, detachment from all other con-<BR>nections, detachment of the soul from matter or fur-<BR>ther transmigrations; becoming one with the Supreme;<BR>eternal happiness, emancipation, beatitude; exclusive-<BR>ness, soleness, individuality, totality; (अस्, आ, अम्), con-<BR>nected with this state of mind.<BR>—कैवल्य-तन्त्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—कैवल्य-दीपिका, f., N.<BR>of a commentary by Hemādri.<BR>—कैवल्याश्रम<BR>(˚य-आश्˚), अस्, m. a pupil of Govinda, author of a<BR>commentary on the poem Ānanda-laharī.<BR>—कैव-<BR>ल्येन्द्र (˚य-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of the instructor of<BR>Rāyaṇendra.<BR>—कैवल्योपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚), त्, f.<BR>title of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशव
कैशव कैशव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. केशव), be-<BR>longing to Keśava, (Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिक|कैशिकं|कैशिकः
कैशिक कैशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. केश), hair-<BR>like, fine as a hair; (अस्), m. love, passion, lust; N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">Page0254-c+ 74</a>]<BR>subdivision of the Yādavas, descended from Kaiśika,<BR>who was son of Vidarbha and brother of Kratha; (ई),<BR>f., scil. वृत्ति, one of the four varieties of dramatic style,<BR>the graceful style, suited especially to the passion of<BR>love; N. of a place or river; an epithet of Durgā;<BR>(अम्), n. a quantity of hair, a head of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिन
कैशिन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. केशिन्), connected with<BR>Keśin Dārbhya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैश्य|कैश्यं
कैश्य, अम्, n. (fr. केश), the whole mass of<BR>hair, a head of hair, much or ornamented hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशोर|कैशोरं
कैशोर कैशोर, अम्, n. (fr. किशोर), youth,<BR>boyhood, from the age of ten to that of fifteen.<BR>—कैशोरक-वयस्, अस्, n. the age or life of a youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैष्किन्ध
कैष्किन्ध कैष्किन्ध, अस्, ई, अम्, coming<BR>from Kiṣkindhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

को
को को, a prefix in a number of words, as<BR>in को-जागर, को-मल, को-विद, &c., related to 1.<BR>कु; [cf. the prefixes क, कव, का, किम्, कु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोक|कोकः
कोक कोक, अस्, m. (an onomatopoetic word),<BR>a wolf; a cuckoo; the ruddy goose; a frog; a small<BR>lizard or chameleon; a kind of noxious parasitical<BR>animal; the wild date tree; an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>N. of a man, a son of Śoṇa; N. of a river.<BR>—कोक-<BR>देव, अस्, m. a pigeon.<BR>—कोक-नख, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people.<BR>—कोक-बन्धु, उस्, m. the friend<BR>of the Cakravāka or ruddy goose, an epithet of the<BR>sun.<BR>—कोक-यातु, उस्, m., Ved. a demon or ghost<BR>in the shape of a cuckoo.<BR>—कोक-वाच, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of animal living in caves, a fox (?).<BR>—कोक-शास्त्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a very indecent treatise on the art of<BR>love, ascribed to a Paṇḍit named Koka.<BR>—कोकाग्र<BR>(˚क-अग्˚), अस्, m., N. of a plant, = समष्ठिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकड|कोकडः
कोकड कोकड, अस्, m. an animal of a brown<BR>colour, with a bushy tail, lurking in holes, perhaps a<BR>hare or fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनद|कोकनदं
कोकनद कोकनद, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (अम्), n. the red lotus; the red water-lily.<BR>—कोकनद-च्छवि, इस्, m. the colour of the red<BR>lotus; (इस्, इस्, इ), of the colour of the red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकरक
कोकरक कोकरक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकलिक
कोकलिक कोकलिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकली
कोकली कोकली, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकामुख
कोकामुख कोकामुख, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकाह|कोकाहः
कोकाह कोकाह, अस्, m. a white horse; (per-<BR>haps a foreign word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिल|कोकिलः
कोकिल कोकिल, अस्, m. (an onomatopoetic<BR>word; but by some said to be fr. rt. कुक्), the<BR>Kokila or Koïl, the black or Indian cuckoo, Cuculus<BR>Indicus; a kind of mouse; a kind of poisonous insect;<BR>a firebrand, a lighted coal; N. of a poet; N. of a<BR>Rājaputra; (आ), f. the female of a Kokila, (the Kokila<BR>or Koïl is frequently alluded to in Hindū poetry, and<BR>its musical cry is supposed to inspire pleasing and<BR>tender emotions.)<BR>—कोकिल-नयन, अस्, m. a plant<BR>bearing a dark black flower, Capparis Spinosa; it is<BR>also applied to Barleria Longifolia; [cf. कोकिलाक्ष.]<BR>—कोकिल-मैत्रावरुण, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>the duties or office of the Maitrāvaruṇa priest at the<BR>Kaukilīṣṭi; (अम्), n. title of a treatise.<BR>—कोकिल-<BR>होत्र, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the duties or office of<BR>the Hotṛ priest at the Kaukilīṣṭi; (अम्), n. title of<BR>a treatise.<BR>—कोकिलाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>eyes like those of the Koïl,’ the plant Asteracantha<BR>Longifolia or Capparis Spinosa.<BR>—कोकिलाक्षक, अस्,<BR>m. the same plant.<BR>—कोकिला-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. title<BR>of a part of the Skanda-purāṇa.<BR>—कोकिलावास (˚ल-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. the Mango tree; [cf. आम्र.]<BR>—कोकि-<BR>लेक्षु (˚ल-इक्˚), उस्, m. the black variety of sugar-<BR>cane; [cf. कृष्णेक्षु.]<BR>—कोकिलेष्टा (˚ल-इष्˚),<BR>f., N. of a plant, = महा-जम्बू.<BR>—कोकिलोत्सव<BR>(˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, m. the Mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलक|कोकिलकः
कोकिलक, अस् or अम्, m. or n (?), N. of a metre<BR>of four lines, each containing seventeen syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोक्कट
कोक्कट कोक्कट = कोङ्कट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोक्क्वोक
कोक्क्वोक कोक्क्वोक, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Rati-rahasya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्क|कोंक|कोंकः|कोङ्कः
कोङ्क कोङ्क, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कट
कोङ्कट कोङ्कट, अस्, m., N. of a scholiast on<BR>the Amara-koṣa; (a various reading has कोक्कट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कण|कोंकण|कोङ्कणं|कोंकणः|कोङ्कणः
कोङ्कण कोङ्कण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>on the western shore of the Dekhan; (अम्), n. a<BR>kind of weapon; (आ), f. a female of the Koṅkaṇa<BR>people.<BR>—कोङ्कणा-वती, f., N. of a river.<BR>—कोङ्-<BR>कणा-सुत, अस्, m. an epithet of Paraśu-rāma, the<BR>son of Koṅkaṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणक
कोङ्कणक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people on the<BR>western shore of the Dekhan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कार
कोङ्कार कोङ्-कार, अस्, m. the sound कोम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोच|कोचः
कोच कोच, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. कुच्), drying,<BR>becoming dry; (अस्), m. drying up, desiccation,<BR>aridity; a man of mixed caste, the offspring of a<BR>fisherman by a female of the butcher tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोजागर|कोजागरः
कोजागर को-जागर, अस्, m. a kind of festi-<BR>val, the night of full moon in the month Āśvina<BR>(September — October), celebrated with various games;<BR>(according to some authorities from कः and जागर,<BR>‘who is awake?’ the exclamation of Lakṣmī, who<BR>descending on this night, promised wealth to all that<BR>were awake; hence the night is spent in festivity and<BR>games of chance in honour of the goddess.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोञ्ज
कोञ्ज कोञ्ज, अस्, m. = कौञ्च, N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट|कोटः
कोट कोट, अस्, m. (rt. कुट्), a fort, a strong-<BR>hold; a shed, a hut [cf. कुट, कुटी]; crookedness,<BR>curvature; a beard.<BR>—कोट-चक्र, अम्, n. a sort of<BR>diagram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटक|कोटकः
कोटक, अस्, ई, अम्, who or what curves or bends;<BR>(अस्), m. a builder of sheds or huts, a thatcher, a<BR>carpenter; a mixed caste, the son of a mason and of<BR>the daughter of a potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटर|कोटरं|कोटरः
कोटर, अस्, अम्, m. n. the hollow of a tree; a<BR>cave in general; (ई), f. a naked woman; an epithet<BR>of the goddess Durgā.<BR>—कोटरा-वण, अम्, n. a<BR>wood in which there are hollow trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटवी
कोटवी, f. a naked woman; a form of the goddess<BR>Durgā (represented naked).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटि|कोटिः
कोटि, इस् or ई, f. the curved end of a bow or of claws,<BR>&c.; the end or top of anything; the edge or point<BR>of a sword; the horns of the moon; the highest<BR>point, eminence, excellence; the highest number in<BR>the older system of numbers, viz. a Krore or ten<BR>millions; the complement of an arc to 90°; the side<BR>of a right-angled triangle; N. of a plant, Piring or<BR>Asparac, Medicago Esculenta, = कोटि-वर्षा.<BR>—कोटि-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—कोटि-जित्, त्, m. a<BR>conqueror of ten millions; an epithet of the poet<BR>Kālidāsa.<BR>—कोटि-ज्या, f. the cosine of an angle in a<BR>right-angled triangle.<BR>—कोटि-तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—कोटि-द्वय, अम्, n. ‘the two ends,’ i. e.<BR>two alternatives.<BR>—कोटि-पात्र, अम्, n. a rudder or<BR>large oar used as one.<BR>—कोटि-पाल, अस्, m. the guard<BR>of a stronghold? (a wrong reading for कोट्ट-पाल ?).<BR>—कोटि-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—कोटि-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with a point.<BR>—कोटि-वर्ष,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a city, Vāṇapura or Devikote, on the<BR>Coromandel coast; (आ), f. a plant used medicinally,<BR>either Medicago Esculenta or Trigonella Corni-<BR>culata.<BR>—कोटि-वेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, striking an edge or<BR>point, i. e. performing the most difficult things.<BR>—कोटि-शस्, ind. by tens of millions, in innumerable<BR>multitudes.<BR>—कोटि-श्री, f. an epithet of the goddess<BR>Durgā.<BR>—कोटी-वर्ष, अम्, n., N. of the town<BR>Vāṇapura on the Coromandel coast; (आ), f. the plant<BR>Medicago Esculenta or Trigonella Corniculata; [cf.<BR>कोटि-वर्ष.]<BR>—कोटीश्वर (˚टि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord<BR>of ten millions, a millionaire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिक|कोटिकः
कोटिक, अस्, आ, अम्, forming the highest point,<BR>top or summit of anything, placed in the highest<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">Page0255-b+ 71</a>]<BR>position, e. g. मानुष-कोटिका, a princess; (अस्),<BR>m., scil. मण्डूक, a frog; an insect, coccinella of<BR>various kinds; N. of the son of a prince.<BR>—कोटि-<BR>कास्य (˚क-आस्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of king Suratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिर|कोटिरः
कोटिर, अस्, m. the hair (collected on the forehead<BR>in the shape of a horn); an ichneumon, Viverra<BR>Ichneumon; an insect, coccinella of various kinds<BR>[cf. कोटिक]; an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिश|कोटिशः
कोटिश, अस्, m. a harrow; N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीर|कोटीरः
कोटीर, अस्, m. long entangled hair; a crest, a<BR>diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीश|कोटीशः
कोटीश, अस्, m. a harrow; [cf. कोटिश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्ट|कोट्टं|कोट्टः
कोट्ट कोट्ट, अस्, अम्, m. n. a fort, a castle, a<BR>stronghold; [cf. कोट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टवी
कोट्टवी कोट्टवी, f. (fr. को-आर्तव?), a naked<BR>woman; an epithet of Durgā; the mother of Vāṇa,<BR>an Asura; [cf. कोटवी, कौटवी, कोटरी.]<BR>—कोट्टवी-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of the town Vāṇapura on the<BR>Coromandel coast; [cf. कोटि-वर्ष and कोटी-<BR>वर्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टार|कोट्टारः
कोट्टार कोट्टार, अस्, m. a fortified town, a<BR>stronghold; a pond; the stairs of a pond; a liber-<BR>tine; [cf. कोट्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोठ|कोठः
कोठ कोठ, अस्, m. (fr. कुष्ठ), a species<BR>of leprosy with large round spots; ringworm, im-<BR>petigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोठर|कोठरः
कोठर कोठर, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = अङ्-<BR>कोट; [cf. कोटर.]<BR>—कोठर-पुष्पी, f. the plant<BR>Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोण|कोणः
कोण कोण, अस्, m. a corner, an angle<BR>(= अश्रि); an intermediate point of the compass;<BR>the quill or bow of a lute, a fiddle-stick, &c.; a sort<BR>of musical instrument, a stringed musical instrument;<BR>a drum-stick; the sharp edge of a sword; a stick, a<BR>staff, a club; a N. of Maṅgala, the planet Mars; a<BR>N. of the planet Saturn (in this sense fr. the Gr.<BR>κρόνος).<BR>—कोण-कुण, अस्, m. a bug; [cf. कोल-<BR>कुण, उत्कुण, मत्कुण.]<BR>—कोण-वादिन्, ई, m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—कोण-स्पृग्-वृत्त, अस् or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?), a circle in contact with the angles of a<BR>figure; an exterior circle; one circumscribed.<BR>—को-<BR>णा-कोणि, ind. from angle to angle, from one corner<BR>to the other, cornerwise, diagonally; athwart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणि|कोणिः
कोणि कोणि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a crooked<BR>arm; [cf. कुणि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणेरभट्ट
कोणेरभट्ट कोणेर-भट्ट, अस्, m. a N. of a<BR>son of Viṣṇu and father of Rudra-bhaṭṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोण्डभट्ट
कोण्डभट्ट कोण्ड-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोथ|कोथः
कोथ कोथ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कुथ्), afflicted<BR>with pain, churned; (अस्), m. putrefaction, corrup-<BR>tion; a sore; gangrene; a disease of the eyes,<BR>inflammation and ulceration of the angles of the<BR>eyelids; churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्ड|कोदंड|कोदंडं|कोदण्डं|कोदंडः|कोदण्डः
कोदण्ड को-दण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bow;<BR>(अस्), m. an eyebrow (shaped like a bow); a creeping<BR>plant; N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्डिन्|कोदंडिन्
कोदण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, armed with a bow; an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदार|कोदारः
कोदार कोदार, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), a kind of<BR>grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोद्रव|कोद्रवः
कोद्रव कोद्रव, अस्, m. a species of grain<BR>eaten by the poor, Paspalum Scrobiculatum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोनालक|कोनालकं|कोनालकः
कोनालक कोनालक, अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of<BR>aquatic bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोनालि
कोनालि कोनालि, इस्, m. or f. (?), a kind of<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोन्तल
कोन्तल कोन्तल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>[cf. कुन्तल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोन्व
कोन्व कोन्व, अस्, m., N. of a mountain;<BR>[cf. कोल, कोल्लक, कोलगिरि, कोल्वगिरेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोन्वशिर|कोन्वशिरः
कोन्वशिर कोन्वशिर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>degraded warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोप|कोपः
कोप कोप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कुप्), morbid<BR>irritation or disorder of the humours of the body;<BR>passion, wrath, anger, rage, (स-कोप, enraged; स-को-<BR>पम्, angrily.)<BR>—कोप-कारण, अम्, n. cause of anger.<BR> — 1. कोप-क्रम, अस्, m. one who goes to anger,<BR>an angry or passionate man.<BR>—कोप-ज्वलित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, inflamed with wrath, enraged.<BR>—कोप-तस्, ind.<BR>through anger, angrily.<BR>—कोप-दीप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>incensed or inflamed with anger.<BR>—कोप-पद, अम्,<BR>n. appearance of anger, pretended wrath.<BR>—कोप-<BR>परीत, अस्, आ, अम्, affected by anger.<BR>—कोप-लता,<BR>f., N. of a plant, = कर्ण-स्फोटा.<BR>—कोप-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, angry; passionate; (ती), f., N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of fourteen syllables each.<BR>—कोप-वश, अस्, m. subjection to anger.<BR>—कोप-<BR>वेग, अस्, m. violence, impetuosity of passion; N. of<BR>a Ṛṣi.<BR>—कोप-समन्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, affected by<BR>anger.<BR>—कोपाकुल (˚प-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, furious,<BR>enraged.<BR>—कोपा-कोपि, ind. in mutual anger, in<BR>reciprocal wrath.<BR>—कोपाविष्ट (˚प-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>affected with anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपन|कोपनः
कोपन, अस्, आ, अम्, inclined to passion, passionate,<BR>wrathful, angry; irritating, causing morbid irritation<BR>or disorder of the humours; (अस्), m., N. of an Asura;<BR>(अम्), n. irritating; becoming angry; (आ), f. a pas-<BR>sionate woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपनक|कोपनकः
कोपनक, अम्, n. a kind of perfume; [cf. चोरक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपयिष्णु
कोपयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, intending to exasperate,<BR>inclined to make angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपित
कोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, enraged, furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपिन्
कोपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, angry, passionate, wrathful; (at<BR>the end of a compound) irritating, stirring up; (ई),<BR>m. a bird called the water-pigeon (जल-पारावत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपक्रम|कोपक्रमं|कोपक्रमः
कोपक्रम 2. कोपक्रम (क-उप्˚), अम्, n.<BR>Brahmā's creation; see 3. क. (For 1. कोप-क्रम<BR>see under कोप above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपज्ञ
कोपज्ञ कोपज्ञ (क-उप्˚), अम्, n. Brahmā's<BR>creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोम
कोम कोम, अम्, n. = क्लोम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमल|कोमलं|कोमलः
कोमल को-मल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. को = कु and<BR>मल fr. rt. म्लै, ‘easily fading away?’), tender,<BR>soft (opposed to कर्कश); bland, sweet, low;<BR>pleasing, agreeable, beautiful; (आ), f., N. of a plant;<BR>(अम्), n. water.<BR>—कोमल-गीत or कोमल-गीतक,<BR>अम्, n. a pleasing song.<BR>—कोमल-ता, f. or कोमल-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. softness, tenderness, agreeableness.<BR>—कोमल-स्वभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, tender-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलक|कोमलकं
कोमलक, अम्, n. the fibres of the stalk of a<BR>lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमासिका
कोमासिका कोमासिका, f. a budding fruit;<BR>[cf. जालिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोम्य
कोम्य कोम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = काम्य,<BR>lovely (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टि|कोयष्टिः
कोयष्टि को-यष्टि, इस्, or कोयष्टिक, अस्, m.<BR>the lapwing; a small white crane, commonly called a<BR>paddy-bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोर|कोरः
कोर कोर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. कुर्), a<BR>movable joint, as the fingers, the knee, &c.; amphi-<BR>arthrosis; a bud (see the next).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरक|कोरकं|कोरकः
कोरक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bud, an unblown flower;<BR>the fibres of the stalk of a lotus; a species of perfume,<BR>commonly Cor (चोर); another perfume, a berry<BR>containing a resinous and fragrant substance; [cf.<BR>कक्कोलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरकित
कोरकित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with buds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरित
कोरित, अस्, आ, अम्, budded, sprouted; ground,<BR>pounded, comminuted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरङ्गी
कोरङ्गी कोरङ्गी, f. small cardamoms; [cf.<BR>एला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरदूष|कोरदूषः
कोरदूष कोर-दूष or कोरदूषक, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of grain eaten especially by the poor, Paspalum<BR>Scrobiculatum. See कोद्रव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरली
कोरली कोरली or कोरिला, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल|कोलं|कोलः
कोल कोल, अस्, m. a hog; a raft, a float,<BR>a boat; a kind of weapon; the breast, the haunch,<BR>the hip or flank, the lap [cf. क्रोड]; an embrace,<BR>embracing; N. of a plant (= चित्र, चित्रक); the<BR>planet Śani or Saturn; N. of a son of Ākrīḍa; N. of<BR>a degraded warrior-tribe; an outcast, one of a tribe<BR>degraded by Sagara from the military order; a man<BR>of a mixed caste; a barbarian, a Kol, a tribe inhabit-<BR>ing the hills and forests in central India; (आ or ई), f.<BR>the jujube tree, Zizyphus Jujuba; (आ), f. Piper<BR>Longum, and Piper Chaba (चव्य); (अम्), n. the<BR>fruit of the jujube; black pepper; the weight of one<BR>Tola; [cf. Lith. kuilys, kiaule; Hib. cullach; Gr.<BR>χοῖρος.]<BR>—कोल-कन्द, अस्, m. a sort of bulbous<BR>plant, used as a remedy for worms; [cf. कृमि-घ्न,<BR>पञ्जल, &c.]<BR>—कोल-कर्कटिका, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= मधु-खर्जूरिका.<BR>—कोल-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—कोल-दल, अम्, n. a kind of perfume,<BR>= नखी.<BR>—कोल-नासिका, f., N. of a plant, = वङ्-<BR>किणी.<BR>—कोल-पुच्छ, अस्, m. a heron.<BR>—कोल-मूल,<BR>अम्, n. the root of long pepper.<BR>—कोल-वल्ली, f. the<BR>plant Pothos Officinalis, a plant with a pungent fruit<BR>resembling pepper, = गज-पिप्पली; another plant,<BR>Piper Chaba (चव्य).<BR>—कोल-शिम्बी, f., N. of a<BR>plant, commonly called Ālakuśī, Carpopogon Pruri-<BR>ens; [cf. कृत-फला, खट्वा, &c.]<BR>—कोला-कोलि,<BR>ind. with mutual embraces.<BR>—कोलाञ्च (˚ल-अञ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a N. of Kaliṅga, the Coromandel coast from<BR>Cuttack to Madras; but, according to some, this<BR>place is in Gangetic Hindūstan, with Kanouj for the<BR>capital.<BR>—कोला-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलक|कोलकं|कोलकः
कोलक, अस्, m., N. of two plants, = अङ्कोठ and<BR>बहु-वार; (अम्), n. a kind of perfume, = कक्को-<BR>लक; black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलकिल
कोलकिल कोलकिल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a town; (also read किलकिल, किलिनकिल,<BR>कोलिकिल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलकुण|कोलकुणः
कोलकुण कोलकुण, अस्, m. a bug; [cf.<BR>कोणकुण, उत्कुण, मत्कुण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलम्बक|कोलंबक|कोलंबकः|कोलम्बकः
कोलम्बक कोलम्बक, अस्, m. (fr. को + लम्-<BR>बक ?), the body of a lute, the whole of it except<BR>the strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाहल|कोलाहलं|कोलाहलः
कोलाहल कोलाहल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (an<BR>onomatopoetic word), a loud and confused sound,<BR>an uproar, a great and indistinct noise (of men,<BR>animals, &c.); (अस्), m., N. of a personified moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलि|कोलिः
कोलि कोलि, इस्, इस् or ई, m. f. the jujube tree,<BR>Zizyphus Jujuba; [cf. कर्कन्धु.]<BR>—कोलि-सर्प,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a degraded warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलिकिल
कोलिकिल कोलिकिल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a town (?); [cf. कोलकिल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलित
कोलित कोलित, अस्, m. an epithet of Maud-<BR>galyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलुह
कोलुह कोलुह, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलूक
कोलूक कोलूक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N.<BR>of a country; also कोलूत and शैलूत; [cf. उलूक,<BR>उलूट, उतूल, कुलूट, कुलूत, कौलूत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल्या
कोल्या कोल्या, f. Piper Longum; [cf. कोला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल्लक
कोल्लक कोल्लक, अस्, m., N. of a mountain;<BR>[cf. कोन्व, कोन्वशिर, कोल, कोलगिरि, कोल्वगि-<BR>रेय.]<BR>—कोल्ल-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल्वगिरेय
कोल्वगिरेय कोल्व-गिरेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविद|कोविदः
कोविद को-विद, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. को and rt.<BR>विद्, to know), experienced, skilled, learned, wise<BR>(with loc., gen., and at the end of comp., e. g. अश्वेषु<BR>or अश्वानाम् or अश्व-कोविद, skilled in horses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविदार|कोविदारं|कोविदारः
कोविदार को-विदार, अस्, m. a tree, Bauhinia<BR>Variegata; also one of the trees of paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोश|कोशं|कोशः
कोश कोश, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. कुश् or<BR>कुष् ?, related to कुक्षि and कोष्ठ?; in the earlier<BR>literature generally spelt कोश; later books read both<BR>कोश and कोष), a cask, a vessel for holding liquids;<BR>(metaphorically) a cloud; a pail; a bucket; a drink-<BR>ing-vessel, a cup, a vessel in general; a box, a cup-<BR>board, a drawer, a trunk; the interior or inner part<BR>of a carriage; a sheath, a scabbard, &c.; a case, a<BR>covering, a cover; store-room, store, provisions; a<BR>treasury, the apartment where money or plate is kept;<BR>treasure, accumulated wealth, money; gold or silver,<BR>wrought or unwrought, as plate, jewellery, &c.; a<BR>kind of bandage (in surgery); a dictionary, lexicon,<BR>or vocabulary; a bud; the sheath or integument of a<BR>plant; a pod or any similar seed-vessel; a nutmeg,<BR>a nut-shell; the inner part of the fruit Artocarpus<BR>Integrifolia; the cocoon of a silk-worm; the vulva,<BR>the womb; the penis; a testicle or the scrotum;<BR>an egg; (in the Vedānta philosophy) a term for<BR>the three sheaths or succession of cases which make<BR>up the various frames of the body enveloping the<BR>soul, (these are, 1. the आनन्द-मयः कोशः or<BR>‘sheath of pleasure,’ forming the कारण-शरीर or<BR>‘causal frame;’ 2. the विज्ञान-मयः or बुद्धि-<BR>मयः or मनो-मयः or प्राण-मयः कोशः,<BR>‘the sheath of intellect or will or life,’ forming the<BR>सूक्ष्म-शरीर or ‘subtile frame;’ 3. the अन्न-<BR>मयः कोशः, ‘the sheath of nourishment,’ forming<BR>the स्थूल-शरीर or ‘gross frame’); a ball or globe<BR>(e. g. सूत्र-कोष, a ball of thread; नेत्र-कोष,<BR>the eye-ball &c.); judicial trial, ordeal by fire, water,<BR>poison, the balance, heated balls of iron, boiling oil<BR>&c., attesting a deity with thrice-repeated drinking<BR>of the water in which some idol has been washed;<BR>the water used at an ordeal; an oath; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>river; (ई), f. a bud; a seed-vessel; the beard of corn;<BR>a shoe, a sandal; [cf. Hib. gucog, ‘a bud, a sprout;’<BR>Gr. κόκκος]<BR>—कोश-कार, अस्, m. one who makes<BR>scabbards, cases, boxes, &c.; the compiler of a diction-<BR>ary, a lexicographer; the silk-worm or the insect<BR>while in its cocoon; a chrysalis or pupa; a variety of<BR>sugar-cane or sugar-cane in general.<BR>—कोश-कारक,<BR>अस्, m. a silk-worm.<BR>—कोश-कृत्, त्, m. a kind of<BR>sugar-cane.<BR>—कोश-गृह, अम्, n. a treasury; a room<BR>in which valuable garments, precious stones &c. are<BR>kept.<BR>—कोश-ग्रहण, अम्, n. undergoing an ordeal.<BR>—कोश-चञ्चु, उस्, m. the Indian crane.<BR>—कोश-<BR>नायक, अस्, m. a chief over treasure, a treasurer; an<BR>epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—कोश-पाल, अस्, m. the guardian<BR>of a treasure.<BR>—कोश-पेटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a chest<BR>or strong box in which treasure is kept.<BR>—कोश-<BR>फल, अस्, m. a kind of creeping plant [cf. घोषक];<BR>(आ), f. a Cucurbitaceous plant, = पीत-घोषा; the<BR>plant Cucumis Utilissimus, = त्रपुषी; (अम्), n. a<BR>kind of perfume, a berry containing a waxy and<BR>fragrant substance; a nutmeg.<BR>—कोश-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, treasured, stored, accumulated.<BR>—कोश-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessing treasures, rich, wealthy; (ती), f., N.<BR>of a kind of plant.<BR>—कोश-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in<BR>a shell, wrapped up in a sheath or shell, incased; (ई),<BR>m. any animal so incased, a chrysalis or pupa.<BR>—कोश-<BR>वृद्धि, इस्, f. swelled testicle, enlargement of the<BR>scrotum from hernia or hydrocele &c.<BR>—कोश-<BR>वेश्मन्, अ, n. a treasury.<BR>—कोश-शायिका, f. a clasp-<BR>knife or one lying in a sheath.<BR>—कोश-शुद्धि, इस्,<BR>f. purification by ordeal.<BR>—कोश-स्कृत्, त्, m. a silk-<BR>worm.<BR>—कोश-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, incased, sheathed,<BR>enveloped in a sheath or shell &c.; (अस्), m. any<BR>shelled insect or animal, as a snail &c.; a pupa or<BR>chrysalis; the silk-worm in its cocoon.<BR>—कोश-हीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, without treasure, deprived of riches,<BR>poor.<BR>—कोशांश (˚श-अं˚), अस्, m. part of a trea-<BR>sure, a portion of any one's wealth.<BR>—कोशागार<BR>(˚श-आग्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. a treasure-house, store-room,<BR>treasury.<BR>—कोशाङ्ग (˚श-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>reed or grass, commonly Ikāda; [cf. उत्कट.]<BR>—कोशाधिपति (˚श-अध्˚), इस्, or कोशाधीश or<BR>कोशाध्यक्ष (˚श-अध्˚), अस्, m. a superintendent<BR>of the treasury, a treasurer, a paymaster; an epithet<BR>of Kuvera.<BR>—कोशापहरण (˚श-अप्˚), अम्, n. car-<BR>rying off treasure.<BR>—कोशाम्र (˚श-आम्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">Page0256-c+ 72</a>]<BR>of a plant, = कृमि-वृक्ष, सुकेशक, commonly<BR>कोशाम; (अम्), n. the fruit of this plant, Vulg.<BR>keuḍā (= keurā? Sonneratia Apetala?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशक|कोशकः
कोशक, अस्, m. an egg, a testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशयी
कोशयी, f., Ved. a chest, a box; the interior of a<BR>carriage (?). According to Sāy. = कोश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशिका
कोशिका, f. a drinking-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशिन्
कोशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, incased (आम-कोशिन्, having the<BR>cavity of the ear filled up); (ई), m. the mango tree;<BR>[cf. आम्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशिला
कोशिला, f. a kind of bean [cf. मुद्ग-पर्णी]; N.<BR>of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशल|कोशलः
कोशल कोशल and कोशला. See under<BR>कोसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलिक|कोशलिकं
कोशलिक कोशलिक, अम्, n. a bribe; (wrong<BR>reading for कौशलिक, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातक|कोशातकः
कोशातक कोशातक or कोषातक, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>कोश?), hair; (ई), f. several Cucurbitaceous plants,<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca, Luffa Acutangula, and Luffa<BR>Pentandra; the fruits of these plants; a moonlight<BR>night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातकिन्
कोशातकिन् कोशातकिन्, ई, m. (fr. the pre-<BR>ceding ?), trade, business; a trader, a merchant;<BR>submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोश्य
कोश्य कोश्य, औ or ए (?), m. or n. (?), du.,<BR>Ved. two lumps of flesh near the heart of a sacrificial<BR>horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष|कोषं|कोषः
कोष कोष with its compounds, see under<BR>कोश, for which कोष is only a later form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषला
कोषला कोषला, wrongly spelt for कोसला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषातक|कोषातकः
कोषातक कोषातक = कोशातक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठ|कोष्ठः
कोष्ठ कोष्ठ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कुष्; probably<BR>related to कुक्षि and कोश), any one of the viscera<BR>of the body, as the stomach, heart, lungs, &c., but<BR>particularly the stomach; the belly, bowels, abdomen;<BR>an inner apartment; a granary, a place in which grain<BR>is kept, a store-room, a treasury; (अम्), n. a sur-<BR>rounding wall; a kind of vessel; the shell of any-<BR>thing; (अस्, आ, अम्), own.<BR>—कोष्ठ-कोटि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR>—कोष्ठ-पाल, अस्, m.<BR>a municipal officer, a constable; a watch, a guard,<BR>the watch of a city; a storekeeper, a treasurer.<BR>—कोष्ठ-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—कोष्-<BR>ठ-शुद्धि, इस्, f. dejection by stool, evacuation of<BR>the bowels.<BR>—कोष्ठागार (˚ठ-अग्˚ or आग्˚), अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a store-room, a store; a treasury.<BR>—कोष्ठागारिक, अस् or आ (?), m. or f. (?), a kind<BR>of animal, any animal living in a shell.<BR>—कोष्ठा-<BR>गारिन्, ई, m. a kind of poisonous insect.<BR>—कोष्-<BR>ठाग्नि (˚ठ-अग्˚), इस्, m. the digestive faculty, the<BR>gastric juice.<BR>—कोष्ठी-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work on astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठक|कोष्ठकः
कोष्ठक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a granary,<BR>a treasury [cf. अन्न-कोष्ठक]; a surrounding<BR>wall; (अम्), n. a brick trough for watering cattle;<BR>N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठकीकृ
कोष्ठकी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to surround, enclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठिल
कोष्ठिल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठ्य
कोष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proceeding from the chest<BR>or interior of the body, emitted (as a sound) from<BR>the centre of the lungs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ण|कोष्णं
कोष्ण कोष्ण (का-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mode-<BR>rately warm, tepid, warm; (अम्), n. warmth; [cf.<BR>कवोष्ण, कदुष्ण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोसल|कोसलः
कोसल कोसल, अस्, m. (in later books gene-<BR>rally spelt कोशल), N. of a country and the warrior-<BR>tribe inhabiting it, descendants of Māthava Videgha;<BR>(आ), f., N. of the capital of this country or Ayodhyā,<BR>the modern Oude.<BR>—कोसलात्मजा (˚ल-आत्˚), f. the<BR>daughter of the king of the Kosalas, an epithet of a<BR>wife of Daśa-ratha, the mother of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहड
कोहड कोहड, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf.<BR>कौहड and कोहल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहल|कोहलः
कोहल कोहल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. को + हल? cf.<BR>कुतूहल), speaking indistinctly; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>musical instrument; a sort of spirituous liquor; N. of<BR>a saint or Muni, the inventor or first teacher of the<BR>drama, also a writer on music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहलीय
कोहलीय, अम्, n. title of Kohala's work on music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहित
कोहित कोहित, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकुट्टक
कौकुट्टक कौकुट्टक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (variously written कौकुन्तक and कौ-<BR>कुन्दक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकुर
कौकुर कौकुर, आस्, m. pl. (fr. कुकुर), N.<BR>of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकुवादि
कौकुवादि कौकुवादि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकूस्त
कौकूस्त कौकूस्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकृत्य|कौकृत्यं
