कौण्डिल्यक
कौण्डिल्यक कौण्डिल्यक, अस्, m. (or कौण्-<BR>डिन्यक ?), a kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्डोपरथ
कौण्डोपरथ कौण्डोपरथ, आस्, m. pl. (fr.<BR>कुण्डोपरथ), N. of a warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्डोपरथीय
कौण्डोपरथीय, अस्, m. a prince of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्य|कौण्यं
कौण्य कौण्य, अम्, n. (fr. कुणि), distortion or<BR>paralysis of the hands; the being maimed or handless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुक|कौतुकं
कौतुक कौतुक, अम्, n. (fr. कुतुक), curi-<BR>osity, interest in anything, vehement desire for, wish,<BR>inclination; eagerness, vehemence, impatience; any-<BR>thing causing curiosity, admiration or interest, any<BR>singular or surprising object, a wonder; festivity,<BR>gaiety, a festival, a show, a solemn ceremony, espe-<BR>cially the ceremony with the marriage-thread or ring<BR>preceding a marriage; the marriage-thread or ring;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">Page0257-c+ 71</a>]<BR>joy, pleasure, happiness, enjoyment; sport, pastime;<BR>public diversion; song, dance, show or spectacle;<BR>season of enjoyment; kind or friendly greeting,<BR>civility, salutation.<BR>—कौतुक-क्रिया, f. a solemn<BR>ceremony, a marriage ceremony.<BR>—कौतुक-गृह,<BR>अम्, n. the house in which a marriage takes place.<BR>—कौतुक-तोरण, अस्, अम्, m. n. a triumphal<BR>arch erected at certain festivals.<BR>—कौतुक-मङ्-<BR>गल, अम्, n. a solemn ceremony.<BR>—कौतुकागार<BR>(˚क-अग्˚, or आग्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. a room for festivity,<BR>a room in which a marriage ceremony takes place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकित
कौतुकित, अस्, आ, अम्, eagerly interested, eager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकिन्
कौतुकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, festive, gay, jocose, a jester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहल|कौतूहलं
कौतूहल कौतूहल, अम्, n. (fr. कुतूहल),<BR>curiosity, interest in anything, vehement desire for<BR>anything, eagerness, vehemence; anything causing<BR>curiosity, any unusual phenomenon; a solemn cere-<BR>mony.<BR>—कौतूहल-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, curious, in-<BR>quisitive.<BR>—कौतूहलान्वित (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>eager, vehement, curious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतोमत
कौतोमत कौतोमत, अम्, n. (fr. कुतस् + मत),<BR>N. of a Sūkta (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौत्स|कौत्सं|कौत्सः
कौत्स कौत्स, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुत्स), composed<BR>by Kutsa; (अम्), n. a Sūkta or Sāman composed by<BR>Kutsa; (अस्), m. a patronymic from Kutsa; N. of a<BR>teacher; N. of a pupil of Vara-tantu; the son-in-law<BR>of Bhagīratha; a patronymic of Jaimini; N. of a<BR>degraded family.<BR>—कौत्सी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौथुम|कौथुमः
कौथुम कौथुम, आस्, m. pl. the pupils of<BR>Kuthumin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौदालिक|कौदालिकः
कौदालिक कौदालिक or कौदालीक, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. कुदाल), a man of a mixed caste, the son of a<BR>fisherman by a woman of the washerman caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रविक|कौद्रविकं
कौद्रविक कौद्रविक, अम्, n. (fr. कोद्रव),<BR>sochal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रवीण|कौद्रवीणं
कौद्रवीण, अस्, आ, अम्, sown with Kodrava (as<BR>a field &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्य|कौनख्यं
कौनख्य कौनख्य, अम्, n. (fr. कु-नखिन्),<BR>the condition of one who has a disease of the nails;<BR>ugliness of the nails.<BR>—कौनख्यादिक (˚य-आद्˚),<BR>अम्, n. neglect of personal decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तिक|कौंतिक|कौंतिकः|कौन्तिकः
कौन्तिक कौन्तिक, अस्, m. (fr. कुन्त), a<BR>spearman, a soldier armed with a spear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्ती
कौन्ती कौन्ती, f. (fr. कुन्त or कुन्ति), a sort<BR>of perfume, commonly रेणुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तेय|कौंतेय|कौंतेयः|कौन्तेयः
कौन्तेय कौन्तेय, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr.<BR>कुन्ती), a N. of Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhīma-sena, and Arjuna;<BR>N. of a tree = अर्जुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्त्य
कौन्त्य कौन्त्य, अस्, m. a king of the Kuntis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्द
कौन्द कौन्द, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुन्द), relating<BR>to or coming from jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौप|कौपं
कौप कौप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कूप), coming<BR>from a well or cistern; (अम्), n. well-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपीन|कौपीनं
कौपीन, अम्, n. the pudenda; a privity, a privy<BR>part; a small piece of cloth worn over the privities<BR>by poor persons; a wrong or improper act, sin.<BR>—कौपीन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has only a<BR>piece of cloth over the privities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौप्य
कौप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from a well or cistern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपोदकी
कौपोदकी कौपोदकी, f. the mace of Kṛṣṇa,<BR>= कौमोदकी; [also कौपादकी ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौब्ज्य|कौब्ज्यं
कौब्ज्य कौब्ज्य, अम्, n. (fr. कुब्ज), crooked-<BR>ness, hump-backedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौम
कौम कौम, अम्, n., N. of a Vedic treatise,<BR>so named from its author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमार|कौमारं
कौमार कौमार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुमार or<BR>कुमारी), juvenile, youthful, girlish, belonging to a<BR>youth or young girl, maiden, maidenly, virgin, (कौ-<BR>मारी भार्या, a virgin wife, one who has not had a<BR>husband previously; कौमारः पतिः, a man who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">Page0258-a+ 76</a>]<BR>marries a virgin; कौमारं व्रतम्, a vow of<BR>abstinence); soft, tender; relating to the god of<BR>war or Sanat-kumāra, belonging or peculiar to them;<BR>(ई), f. one of the seven divine Mātṛs, the divine<BR>mothers or personified energies of the gods, the<BR>energy or शक्ति of Kumāra or Kārttikeya the god of<BR>war; a kind of bulbous plant, = वाराही-कन्द; (अम्),<BR>n. childhood, youth from birth to the age of five;<BR>maidenhood to the age of sixteen.<BR>—कौमार-<BR>पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—कौमार-<BR>भृत्य, अम्, n. the rearing and education of chil-<BR>dren, a department of medical science; [cf. कुमार-<BR>भृत्या.]<BR>—कौमारराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. कुमार-<BR>राज = राज-कुमार, युव-राज), the position of<BR>an heir-apparent; [cf. यौवराज्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारक|कौमारकं
कौमारक, अम्, n. childhood, the juvenile age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारिक|कौमारिकः
कौमारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, endowed with girls;<BR>(अस्), m. a father of girls.<BR>—कौमारिक-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुद|कौमुदः
कौमुद कौमुद, अस्, m. (fr. कुमुद), the<BR>month Kārttika, October-November; (ई), f. moon-<BR>light, moonshine (from its causing the Kumudas to<BR>blossom); elucidation, (the word Kaumudī being<BR>metaphorically used like other words of similar im-<BR>port (चन्द्रिका) at the end of the title of grammatical<BR>commentaries and other explanatory works to imply<BR>that the book so designated throws much light on<BR>the subject of which it treats, e. g. पदार्थ-कौ-<BR>मुदी, प्रक्रिया-क्˚, लघु-क्˚, वैषम्य-क्˚, सिद्-<BR>धान्त-क्˚); the day of full moon in the month<BR>Kārttika, sacred to the god Kārttikeya; the day of<BR>full moon in the month Āśvina; a festival in honour<BR>of Kārttikeya held on the full moon of the month<BR>Kārttika; a festival in general; N. of a metre con-<BR>sisting of two lines of twenty-four syllables each; N.<BR>of a river.<BR>—कौमुदी-चार, अस्, अम्, m. n. the day<BR>of full moon in the month Āśvina.<BR>—कौमुदी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. the moon.<BR>—कौमुदी-वृक्ष, अस्,<BR>m. the stick or stand of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदिक
कौमुदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a water-lily,<BR>abounding with them; (इका), f., N. of a female<BR>friend of Umā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदकी
कौमोदकी कौमोदकी, f. (fr. कुमोदक),<BR>N. of the club or mace of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa, given<BR>to him by Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदी
कौमोदी, f. the club or mace of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौम्भ
कौम्भ कौम्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुम्भ), put<BR>into a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौम्भकारक
कौम्भकारक, made by a potter (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौम्भकारि
कौम्भकारि, इस्, m. or कौम्भकार्य, अस्, m.<BR>the son of a potter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरम
कौरम कौरम, अस्, m., N. of a man; (a<BR>various reading has कौरुम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरयाण
कौरयाण कौरयाण, अस्, m. (fr. कुरयाण),<BR>a patronymic of Pāka-sthāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव|कौरवः
कौरव कौरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुरु), belong-<BR>ing to the Kurus &c.; (अस्), m. a patronymic from<BR>Kuru; a descendant of Kuru; also कौरवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरवायणि
कौरवायणि, इस्, or कौरवेय, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Kuru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव्य|कौरव्यः
कौरव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Kuru; a<BR>descendant of Kuru; N. of a Nāga, father of Ulūpī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव्यायणी
कौरव्यायणी, f. a female descendant of Kuru.<BR>—कौरव्यायणी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरुकत्य
कौरुकत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the family<BR>of the Kurus and Katas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरुकुल्लक
कौरुकुल्लक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Buddhist sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरुपञ्चाल
कौरुपञ्चाल, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the race<BR>of the Kurus and Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरुपथि
कौरुपथि, इस्, m. (fr. कुरु-पथ), N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्पर
कौर्पर कौर्पर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कूर्पर),<BR>being at the elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्प्य|कौर्प्यः
कौर्प्य कौर्प्य, अस्, m. (a word borrowed from<BR>the Gr. σκοπρίος), the sign of the zodiac Scorpio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्म|कौर्मः|कौर्म्म
कौर्म कौर्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कूर्म), belong-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">Page0258-b+ 75</a>]<BR>ing or relating to a tortoise, connected with a tortoise,<BR>acting as one; belonging or relating to the Avatāra<BR>of Viṣṇu as a tortoise; (अस्), m., N. of a Kalpa,<BR>the day of full moon of Brahmā; (अम्), n., scil.<BR>पुराणम्, title of a Purāṇa on the subject of Viṣṇu's<BR>descent as a tortoise.<BR>—कौर्मोपपुराण (˚म-<BR>उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल|कौलः
कौल कौल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुल), belonging<BR>or relating to a family, ancestral, extending over a<BR>whole family or race, sprung from a noble family, of<BR>a good family, well-born; (अस्), m. a worshipper of<BR>Śakti according to the left-hand ritual; (अम्), n. the<BR>doctrine and practices of the left-hand Śāktas.<BR>—कौ-<BR>लोपनिषद् (˚ल-उप्˚), त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलकेय|कौलकेयः
कौलकेय, अस्, ई, अम्, sprung from a noble family,<BR>of a good family, well-born; (अस्), m. a bastard;<BR>(wrong form for कौलटेय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलत्थ
कौलत्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुलत्थ), made or<BR>prepared with or consisting of Dolichos Uniflorus;<BR>(अम्), n. a drink prepared with Kulattha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलत्थीन|कौलत्थीनं
कौलत्थीन, अस्, आ, अम्, sown with Dolichos<BR>Uniflorus (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिक|कौलिकः
कौलिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a family or<BR>race, customary in a family, ancestral, heritable in<BR>the family; (अस्), m. a weaver; a heretic, an im-<BR>postor; a follower of the left-hand Śākta ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन|कौलीनं|कौलीनः
कौलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, peculiar or belonging to a<BR>noble family; (अस्), m. the son of a female beggar;<BR>a follower of the left-hand Śākta ritual; (अम्), n.<BR>rumour, report; evil report, detraction; family scan-<BR>dal; combat of animals, of birds, snakes, &c.; cock-<BR>fighting, &c.; contention of animals as a species of<BR>gambling; a privity, a privy part, the pudenda; high<BR>birth, family descent; an improper act, a bad deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन्य|कौलीन्यं
कौलीन्य, अम्, n. high birth, nobility; family<BR>honour; family trouble, family scandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेय|कौलेयः
कौलेय, अस्, ई, अम्, sprung from a noble family;<BR>of the left-hand Śākta sect; [cf. कौल, कौलिक,<BR>कौलीन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेयक|कौलेयकः
कौलेयक, अस्, ई, अम्, sprung from a noble<BR>family, of good parentage; pertaining to a family;<BR>(अस्), m. a dog (a domestic animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्य|कौल्यः
कौल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from a noble family,<BR>of good family or parentage; of the left-hand<BR>Śākta sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटिनेय|कौलटिनेयः
कौलटिनेय कौलटिनेय, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr.<BR>कुलटा), the son or daughter of a female beggar; a<BR>bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेय|कौलटेयः
कौलटेय, अस्, ई, m. f. the child of a female beggar;<BR>a bastard, the child of a disloyal wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेर|कौलटेरः
कौलटेर, अस्, आ, m. f. a bastard, son or daughter<BR>of a disloyal wife; the child of a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलव|कौलवः
कौलव कौलव, अस्, m., N. of the third<BR>Karaṇa or astronomical period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलाल|कौलालः
कौलाल कौलाल, अस्, m., Ved. a potter, =<BR>कुलाल; the son of a potter.<BR>—कौलाल-चक्र, अम्,<BR>n. a potter's wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालक
कौलालक, अस्, ई, अम्, made by a potter, pertaining<BR>to a potter; (अम्), n. earthenware, porcelain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलितर
कौलितर कौलितर, अस्, m., Ved. an epithet<BR>of the demon Śambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिशिक
कौलिशिक कौलिशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुलिश),<BR>resembling a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीक
कौलीक कौलीक, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीरा
कौलीरा कौलीरा, f. (fr. कुलीर), N. of a<BR>plant, = कर्कट-शृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलूत|कौलूतः
कौलूत कौलूत, अस्, m. a king of the Ku-<BR>lūtas; (a various reading has कौलूभ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्मलबर्हिष
कौल्मलबर्हिष कौल्मलबर्हिष, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Sāman called after Kulmala-barhiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्माषी
कौल्माषी कौल्माषी, f. (fr. कुल्माष), a<BR>day of full moon on which Kulmāṣa is eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्माषीण|कौल्माषीणं
कौल्माषीण, अस्, आ, अम्, sown with or fit for<BR>Kulmāṣa (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवल|कौवलं
कौवल कौवल, अम्, n. = कुवल, the fruit<BR>of the tree Zizyphus Jujuba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवेर|कौवेरं
कौवेर कौवेर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुवेर), relat-<BR>ing or belonging to Kuvera, coming from him; (ई),<BR>f., scil. दिश्, the region of Kuvera, the north quarter;<BR>the शक्ति or female energy of Kuvera; (अम्), n. a<BR>plant, a kind of Costus, Costus Speciosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश|कौशं
कौश 1. कौश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुश), made of<BR>Kuśa grass; (अम्), n., scil. नगर, the town of<BR>Kuśa, an epithet of Kānyakubja.<BR>—कौशाम्भस्<BR>(˚श-अम्˚), अस्, n. Kuśa grass boiled in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश्य
कौश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, made of Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश|कौशं
कौश 2. कौश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कोश), silken,<BR>silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिक|कौशिकः
1. कौशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, being in a sheath or scab-<BR>bard, sheathed, incased; silken, silk; (अस्), m. one<BR>who is versed in dictionaries; the compiler of a<BR>dictionary, a lexicographer; the fragrant substance<BR>bdellium; marrow; (आ), f. a drinking-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेय|कौशेयं
कौशेय or कौषेय, अस्, ई, अम्, silken, of silk;<BR>(अम्), n. silk, a silk cloth, a silk petticoat or trowsers,<BR>a woman's lower garments of silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल|कौशलं
कौशल कौशल, अम्, n. (fr. कुशल), well-<BR>being, welfare, good fortune, happiness, prosperity;<BR>skilfulness, cleverness, experience; (ई), f. friendly<BR>inquiry, greeting, salutation; a respectful present, a<BR>Nazr; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिका
कौशलिका, f. a present, a respectful gift or offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्य|कौशल्यं
कौशल्य, अम्, n. welfare, well-being, good for-<BR>tune, prosperity; cleverness, experience; (आ), f. see<BR>कौसल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्ब
कौशाम्ब कौशाम्ब, अम्, n. (fr. कुशाम्ब),<BR>N. of a realm; (ई), f., N. of an ancient city on the<BR>Ganges in the lower part of the Doab, in the vicinity<BR>of Kurrah; also वत्स-पत्तन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्बेय|कौशांबेय
कौशाम्बेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Kuśāmba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्ब्य
कौशाम्ब्य, अस्, m. the chief of Kauśambī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाश्वी
कौशाश्वी कौशाश्वी, f., N. of a town built<BR>by Kuśāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिक|कौशिकः
कौशिक 2. कौशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुशिक),<BR>of the family of Kuśika &c.; (अस्), m. a patronymic<BR>of Viśvā-mitra, who was the son or grandson of Ku-<BR>śika; N. of a teacher, author of the Sūtras of the<BR>Atharva-veda; a brother of Paippalādi; N. of a<BR>grammarian; N. of one of Jarāsandha's generals; an<BR>epithet of Indra (as originally perhaps belonging to the<BR>Kuśikas or friendly to them); N. of a son of Vasu-<BR>deva; N. of an Asura; an epithet of Śiva; N. of<BR>the plant Vatica Robusta [cf. कुशिक and अश्व-<BR>कर्ण]; an ichneumon; an owl; love, passion; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a river in Bahar, commonly called Kosi or<BR>Koosa, created by Viśvā-mitra, or identified with<BR>Satyavatī, the sister of Viśvā-mitra; an epithet of the<BR>goddess Durgā; N. of a Buddhist female beggar<BR>or परि-व्राजिका; (अस्, ई, अम्), coming from an owl.<BR>—कौशिक-प्रिय, अस्, m. an epithet of Rāma.<BR>—कौशिक-फल, अस्, m. the cocoa-nut tree, (said<BR>to have been created by the sage Viśvā-mitra when<BR>endeavouring to form a human being in rivalry of<BR>Brahmā, the nut being the rudiment of the head.)<BR>—कौशिकाङ्गुलि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR>—कौशि-<BR>कात्मज (˚क-आत्˚), अस्, m. Indra's son, an epithet of<BR>Arjuna.<BR>—कौशिकायुध (˚क-आय्˚), अम्, n. the bow<BR>of Indra, the rainbow.<BR>—कौशिकाराति (˚क-अर्˚), इस्,<BR>m. an enemy of owls, a crow; also कौशिकारि, &c.<BR>—कौशिकी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR>—कौ-<BR>शिक्य्-ओज अस्, m. (ओज = ओजस्), N. of a tree, = शाखोटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकायनि
कौशिकायनि, इस्, m. (a patronymic fr. कौशिक),<BR>N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकिन्
कौशिकिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils of Kauśika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकार
कौशिकार कौशिकार, अस्, m. = कोश-कार,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिज
कौशिज कौशिज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीतकी
कौशीतकी कौशीतकी = कौषीतकी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीधान्य|कौशीधान्यं
कौशीधान्य कौशीधान्य, अम्, n. (fr. कोशी-<BR>धान्य), a leguminous plant, pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीलव|कौशीलवं
कौशीलव कौशीलव or कौशीलव्य, अम्, n. (fr.<BR>कुशीलव), the profession of an actor, a dancer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेय|कौशेयं
कौशेय कौशेय. See under 2. कौश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश्य
कौश्य कौश्य. See under 1. कौश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषारव
कौषारव कौषारव, अस्, m. (fr. कुषारु),<BR>a patronymic of Maitreya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषीतक
कौषीतक कौषीतक, अस्, m. (fr. कुषीतक),<BR>a patronymic of Kahoḍa; (ई), f. a patronymic of the<BR>wife of Agastya; N. of a school derived from Kuṣī-<BR>taka; (अम्), n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषीतकि
कौषीतकि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Kuṣītaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषीतकिन्
कौषीतकिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils of Kauṣī-<BR>taka.<BR>—कौषीतकि-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषीतकेय
कौषीतकेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of a Kāśyapa;<BR>a patronymic of Kahoḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषेय|कौषेयं
कौषेय कौषेय. See under 2. कौश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौष्ठ
कौष्ठ कौष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कोष्ठ), being<BR>in a store-room, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौष्ठ्य
कौष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the stomach or<BR>abdomen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौष्ठिल
कौष्ठिल कौष्ठिल in महा-कौष्ठिल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Buddhist author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौष्य
कौष्य कौष्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Koṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसलक
कौसलक कौसलक, आस्, m. pl. (fr. कोसल),<BR>N. of a people; (sometimes spelt कौशलक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसलेय
कौसलेय, अस्, m. (fr. कौसल्या), a metronymic<BR>of Rāma as son of Kausalyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्य|कौसल्यं|कौसल्यः
कौसल्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. कोसल), belonging to<BR>the people of the Kosalas; (अस्), m. a prince of the<BR>Kosalas; (आ), f. the daughter of a prince of the<BR>Kosalas, the wife of Pūru and mother of Janamejaya;<BR>the wife of Satvat; the wife of Daśa-ratha and mother<BR>of Rāma; epithet of the mother of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;<BR>of the mother of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—कोसल्या-नन्दन, अस्,<BR>m. and कोसल्या-मातृ, ता, m. an epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्यायनि
कौसल्यायनि, इस्, m. a metronymic of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसिद
कौसिद कौसिद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुसिद), relat-<BR>ing or belonging to or coming from a Kusida, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद
कौसीद कौसीद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुसीद), con-<BR>nected with or relating to a loan; usurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद्य|कौसीद्यं
कौसीद्य, अम्, n. sloth, indolence; the practice<BR>of usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम|कौसुमं
कौसुम कौसुम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुसुम),<BR>flowery, flowering; (अम्), n. the ashes of brass, used<BR>as a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुमायुध
कौसुमायुध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुसुमायुध),<BR>relating to the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम्भ|कौसुंभ|कौसुम्भः
कौसुम्भ कौसुम्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कुसुम्भ),<BR>prepared with safflower; dyed with safflower, orange,<BR>red; (अस्), m. wild safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुरुबिन्द
कौसुरुबिन्द कौसुरुबिन्द, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>कुसुरुबिन्द), N. of a Daśa-rātra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसृतिक|कौसृतिकः
कौसृतिक कौसृतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कु-सृति),<BR>following evil courses, fraudulent; a cheat, a knave;<BR>(अस्), m. a juggler, a conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभ|कौस्तुभः
कौस्तुभ कौस्तुभ, अस्, m. (fr. कुस्तुभ ?),<BR>N. of a celebrated jewel obtained with thirteen other<BR>precious things at the churning of the ocean and<BR>suspended on the breast of Kṛṣṇa; a manner of<BR>joining the fingers; (अम्), n. a kind of oil (सर्ष-<BR>पोद्भव).<BR>—कौस्तुभ-लक्षण, अस्, or कौ-<BR>स्तुभ-लक्षक, अस्, m. or कौस्तुभ-वक्षस्, आस्,<BR>m. a N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्थलपुर
कौस्थलपुर कौस्थलपुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौहलिय
कौहलिय कौहलिय or कौहलीय (?), आस्,<BR>m. pl., N. of a school called after Kohala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौहलीपुत्र
कौहली-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नंस्
क्नंस् क्नंस्, cl. 1. 10. P. क्नंसति, क्नं-<BR>सयति, to speak; to shine; [cf. कुंश्, कुंस्,<BR>क्नस्, क्रंश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नथ्
क्नथ् क्नथ्, cl. 1. P. क्नथति, -थितुम्, to<BR>hurt, injure; to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नस्
क्नस् क्नस्, cl. 4. P. क्नस्यति, -सितुम्, to<BR>be crooked (in mind or body); to shine:<BR>Caus. क्नसयति, -यितुम्, to shine; [cf. कुंश्, कुंस्,<BR>क्नंस्, क्रंश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नु
क्नु क्नु or क्नू, cl. 9. P. A. क्नुनाति, -नीते,<BR>or क्नूनाति, -नीते, to sound, make a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूय्
क्नूय् क्नूय्, cl. 1. A. क्नूयते, चुक्नूये,<BR>क्नूयितुम्, to be wet; to make a creaking<BR>sound; to stink: Caus. P. क्नोपयति, अचुक्नुपत्,<BR>यितुम्, to make wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूत
क्नूत, अस्, आ, अम्, stinking, noisy, wet (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूयितृ
क्नूयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, stinking, emitting a stench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्मर्
क्मर् क्मर्, cl. 1. P. क्मरति, to be crooked<BR>in person, to be crooked in mind, to be<BR>fraudulent or crafty; [cf. ह्वृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्य
क्य क्य, अम्, n., Ved. (according to Sāy. fr. 3.<BR>क = प्रजा-पति), anything agreeable to Prajā-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रंश्
क्रंश् क्रंश्, cl. 1. P. (?) क्रंशति, to illu-<BR>minate; [cf. क्नंस् and क्नस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकच|क्रकचः
क्रकच क्रकच, अस्, अम्, m. n. (an onoma-<BR>topoetic word), a saw; (अस्), m. the plant Capparis<BR>Aphylla, = करीर; N. of a part of hell; (आ), f. the<BR>tree Pandanus Odoratissimus, = केतक; [cf. क्र-<BR>कर.]<BR>—क्रकच-च्छद, अस्, m. the tree Pandanus<BR>Odoratissimus.<BR>—क्रकच-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the teak<BR>tree.<BR>—क्रकच-पाद्, त्, m. a lizard, a chameleon.<BR>—क्रकच-पृष्ठी, f. a small fish with numerous<BR>small spines in the back, Cojus Cobojus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकण|क्रकणः
क्रकण क्रकण, अस्, m. a kind of partridge,<BR>commonly Kayar, Perdix Sylvatica; [cf. कृकण and<BR>क्रकर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकर|क्रकरः
क्रकर क्रकर, अस्, m. (an onomatopoetic<BR>word), a kind of partridge, Perdix Sylvatica; the<BR>plant Capparis Aphylla (see करीर); a saw; a poor<BR>man; disease; [cf. क्रकच.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकुच्छन्द|क्रकुछन्द
क्रकुच्छन्द क्रकुच्छन्द, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Buddha, a predecessor of Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रक्षमाण
क्रक्षमाण क्रक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (a part.<BR>fr. an obsolete rt. क्रक्ष्), Ved. roaring, raving (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतु|क्रतुः
क्रतु क्रतु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. 1. कृ, but<BR>perhaps rather fr. 2. कृ), plan, design, intention,<BR>purpose; resolution, determination; desire, will (in<BR>this sense often occurring in the Vedic inst. case,<BR>क्रत्वा, willingly, readily); power, ability, adequacy,<BR>efficiency, deliberation, consultation; intelligence, un-<BR>derstanding (e. g. भद्रः क्रतुः, right judgment,<BR>good understanding; frequently found in conjunction<BR>with the almost synonymous word दक्ष, e. g.<BR>दक्ष-क्रतू or क्रतु-दक्षौ, ability and in-<BR>telligence, intelligence and power); inspiration; en-<BR>lightenment; a sacrificial rite or ceremony; sacrifice,<BR>offering, worship; an Aśvamedha sacrifice; (क्रतु,<BR>as intelligence personified, is a son of Brahmā, and<BR>one of the Prajā-patis or ten principal Ṛṣis or saints<BR>mentioned in Manu 1. 35; he is said to be married<BR>to Kriyā and father of the 60, 000 Vālikhilyas, or<BR>according to other authorities the husband of Haya-<BR>śirā); N. of one of the Viśva-devās; also of a<BR>son of Ūru and Āgneyī; N. of the author of<BR>a Dharma-śāstra; [cf. अ-क्रतु, अद्भुत-क्रतु,<BR>अभि-क्रतु, &c.; cf. also Gr. κράτος]<BR>—क्रतु-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. a sacrificial ceremony.<BR>—क्रतु-<BR>च्छद, अस्, m. one skilled (?) in sacrifice; a Jina;<BR>(in the latter sense a wrong form for क्रकु-च्छन्द.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">Page0259-c+ 78</a>]<BR>—क्रतु-जित्, त्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—क्रतु-तुल्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, equal to an Aśvamedha in merit.<BR>—क्रतु-<BR>द्रुह्, -ध्रुक्, m. an enemy of sacrifices, an Asura.<BR>—क्रतु-द्विष्, ट्, m. hating sacrifices, an Asura, a<BR>Daitya or demon.<BR>—क्रतु-ध्वंसिन्, ई, m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva as ‘destroyer of Dakṣa's sacrifice.’<BR>—क्रतु-पति, इस्, m. the performer of a sacrifice.<BR>—क्रतु-पशु, उस्, m. a sacrificial animal; a horse,<BR>especially one fit for an Aśvamedha.<BR>—क्रतु-पा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. watching one's sentiments or intentions.<BR>—क्रतु-पुरुष, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—क्रतु-प्रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, or क्रतु-प्रावन्, आ, आ,<BR>अ, Ved. becoming inspired or enlightened; (Sāy.)<BR>fulfilling religious rites.<BR>—क्रतु-फल, अम्, n. the<BR>reward of a sacrifice, the object for which it is per-<BR>formed.<BR>—क्रतु-भुज्, क्, m. one who eats the sacri-<BR>fice, a god, a deity.<BR>—क्रतु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>intelligent, prudent, wise; inspired, enlightened;<BR>(Sāy.) having religious rites; (आन्), m., N. of a son<BR>of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—क्रतु-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, endowed<BR>with intelligence.<BR>—क्रतु-राज्, ट्, m. the chief of<BR>sacrifices, the most excellent sacrifice.<BR>—क्रतु-राज,<BR>अस्, m. the chief of sacrifices, the Rājasūya sacrifice,<BR>performed by a monarch who has made all the<BR>princes of the world tributary to himself.<BR>—क्रतु-<BR>विक्रयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or क्रतु-विक्रायक, अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, one who sells the possible benefits of a sacrifice<BR>performed by himself.<BR>—क्रतु-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>prudent, wise; causing inspiration, inspiring; (Sāy.)<BR>acquainted with religious rites; granting knowledge;<BR>(त्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—क्रतु-सङ्ख्या, f., N. of<BR>the thirteenth of Kātyāyana's Pariśiṣṭas.<BR>—क्रतु-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. title of a Pariśiṣṭa of the Sāma-<BR>veda.<BR>—क्रतु-सिद्धि, इस्, f. completion of a sacri-<BR>fice, attainment of the object for which it is performed.<BR>—क्रतु-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, causing intelligence or in-<BR>spiration.<BR>—क्रतूत्तम (˚तु-उत्˚), अस्, m. the chief<BR>of sacrifices, the Rājasūya sacrifice.<BR>—क्रत्वा-मघ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving readily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतूय
क्रतूय, nom. P., Ved. क्रतूयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>exert the intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथ्
क्रथ् क्रथ्, cl. 1. P. क्रथति, -थितुम्, to<BR>hurt, kill; cl. 10. P. क्राथयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to hurt, injure, kill (with gen. of the person); to<BR>amuse, to delight repeatedly; [cf. क्नथ् and क्लथ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथ
क्रथ क्रथ, अस्, m., N. of a race belonging<BR>to the Yādava people, derived from Kratha, a son of<BR>Vidarbha and brother of Kaiśika; N. of an Asura;<BR>[cf. the next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथन|क्रथनं
क्रथन क्रथन, अस्, m., N. of an Asura;<BR>N. of a Nāga, a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; N. of a<BR>monkey; (अम्), n. slaughter, killing; hemorrhage (?);<BR>snoring, stertor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथनक|क्रथनकं
क्रथनक क्रथनक, अस्, m., N. of a camel<BR>in the Pañca-tantra; (अम्), n. a black sort of Agallo-<BR>chum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्द्|क्रंद्
क्रन्द् क्रन्द् or क्रद्, cl. 1. P. A. क्रन्दति,<BR>-ते, or क्रदते, चक्रन्द, चक्रदे,<BR>क्रन्दिष्यति, -ते, अक्रन्दीत् (Ved. Aor. अक्रन्),<BR>क्रन्दितुम्, to neigh (as a horse); to roar (meta-<BR>phorically applied to the clouds and to wind and<BR>water); to creak (as a wheel); to cry piteously, to<BR>weep, shed tears; to grieve, be confused with sorrow;<BR>to call out piteously to any one (with acc.); to cry<BR>out: Caus. क्रन्दयति, -यितुम्, to cause to roar or<BR>shake; to cause to weep or lament; to roar, rave:<BR>Desid. चिक्रन्दिषति, -ते: Intens. चाक्रन्द्यते,<BR>चाक्रन्ति, Ved. कनिक्रन्ति (part. कनिक्रदत्,<BR>कनिक्रद्यमान), to neigh, roar, rave, cry out; to<BR>shake; to creak; [cf. Goth. grêta, ‘to lament.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्द|क्रंदः|क्रन्दः
क्रन्द, अस्, m., Ved. neighing; a cry, calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्ददिष्टि
क्रन्दद्-इष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. moving with a<BR>great noise or roaring, an epithet of Vāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दन|क्रंदन|क्रन्दनं|क्रंदनः|क्रन्दनः
क्रन्दन, अस्, m. a cat; (अम्), n. crying out,<BR>calling; mutual daring or defiance, challenging; weep-<BR>ing, lamenting, sobbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दनु
क्रन्दनु, उस्, m., Ved. roaring, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दस्|क्रंदस्
क्रन्दस्, अस्, n., Ved. battle-cry; (असी), du. two<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">Page0260-a+ 79</a>]<BR>contending armies shouting defiance; (Sāy.) heaven<BR>and earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दित|क्रंदित|क्रन्दितं
क्रन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, wept, called or cried out;<BR>(अम्), n. weeping, calling; mutual daring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्द्य
क्रन्द्य, अम्, n., Ved. neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रप्
क्रप् क्रप्, cl. 1. A. क्रपते, चक्रपे,<BR>क्रपिष्यते, अक्रपिष्ट, क्रपितुम्, to<BR>long for; to mourn; to lament, implore; to com-<BR>passionate, pity; to go; [cf. कृप्, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम्
क्रम् क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A., 4. P. क्रामति<BR>(ep. also क्रमति), क्रमते (ep. also<BR>क्रामते), क्राम्यति and क्रम्यति (?), चक्राम,<BR>चक्रमे, क्रमिता, क्रमिष्यति and क्रंस्यते,<BR>अक्रमीत् and अक्रंस्त, क्रमितुम् (according to<BR>some also क्रान्तुम्), to step, walk, go, go towards,<BR>approach (with acc.); to approach in order to ask for<BR>assistance (with loc., e. g. तस्मिन् क्रमे, I go to<BR>him for assistance); to go across, go over; to ascend;<BR>to have sexual intercourse with; to excel; to per-<BR>vade, take possession of; to fill; to fulfil, accomplish;<BR>to undertake, strive after; A. to proceed well, to gain<BR>a footing, to succeed, have effect; (in gram.) to be<BR>liable to the peculiar arrangement of a Vedic text<BR>called Krama; to be doubled (as a letter or word) in<BR>connection with this arrangement; A. to read ac-<BR>cording to the Krama arrangement of a Vedic text:<BR>Caus. क्रमयति, -यितुम्, to cause to step; क्रम-<BR>यति or क्रामयति, to make liable to the peculiar<BR>arrangement called Krama; to double (a letter or<BR>word) in connection with this arrangement: Intens.<BR>चङ्क्रम्यते or चङ्क्रन्ति, to step to and fro, to<BR>walk, wander about: Desid. चिक्रमिषति, चिक्रं-<BR>सते; [cf. Lat. gra-dus, gra-dior, gran-dis; Goth.<BR>hlaupa, ‘to run;’ Old Germ. hlaufu, hloufu;<BR>laufu, loufu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्तृ
क्रन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, going, a goer, who or what<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम|क्रमः
क्रम, अस्, m. a step; going, proceeding; course<BR>(e. g. काल-क्रमात्, in course of time); passing; the<BR>foot; a position taken (by an animal &c.) before<BR>making a spring or attacking; uninterrupted or<BR>regular progress, order, series, regular arrangement,<BR>hereditary descent, succession (e. g. वर्ण-क्रमेण,<BR>in the order of the tribes or castes; क्रमेण, in<BR>regular course, by degrees, according to order, rank,<BR>or series); method, manner (e. g. येन क्रमेण,<BR>in which manner; तद्-अनुसरण-क्रमेण, in a<BR>manner corresponding to that); an undertaking,<BR>enterprise, intention; a peculiar manner or method<BR>of reading and writing Vedic texts, i. e. ‘pro-<BR>gressing step by step,’ so called because the reading<BR>proceeds from the first member (either word or letter)<BR>to the second, then the second is repeated and con-<BR>nected with the third, the third repeated and con-<BR>nected with the fourth, and so on, (this manner of<BR>reading or writing in relation to words is called<BR>पद-क्रम; in relation to conjunct consonants<BR>वर्ण-क्रम); a term for the words or letters<BR>themselves when combined or arranged in this man-<BR>ner; power, strength.<BR>—क्रम-काल, अस्, m. the<BR>time of the Krama arrangement.<BR>—क्रम-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced by the Krama arrangement.<BR>—क्रम-<BR>जित्, त्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—क्रम-ज्या, f. the sine<BR>of a planet; declination; [cf. क्रान्ति-ज्या.]<BR>—क्रम-<BR>तस्, ind. gradually, successively, in order.<BR>—क्रम-<BR>त्रैराशिक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a particular<BR>method of applying the direct rule of three (opposed<BR>to व्यस्त˚ or विलोम-त्रैराशिक).<BR>—क्रम-पद,<BR>अम्, n. the conjunction of words in the Krama reading,<BR>more usually written पद-क्रम.<BR>—क्रम-पाठ,<BR>अस्, m. the Krama reading, i. e. a peculiar ‘step by step’<BR>arrangement of a Vedic text made to secure it from all<BR>possible error by, as it were, combining the Saṃhitā-<BR>pāṭha and the Pada-pāṭha, i. e. by giving the words<BR>both as connected and unconnected with following and<BR>preceding words; see under क्रम above.<BR>—क्रम-<BR>पूरक, अस्, m., N. of a tree, = वक.<BR>—क्रम-<BR>प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, obtained by succession or here-<BR>ditary descent.<BR>—क्रम-भङ्ग, अस्, m. interruption<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">Page0260-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of order, irregularity.<BR>—क्रम-योग, अस्, m. succes-<BR>sion, regular order, successive or methodical practice;<BR>(एन), ind. in regular manner.<BR>—क्रम-वत्, ind. in the<BR>manner of the Krama arrangement.<BR>—क्रम-वर्त,<BR>अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a district in Kaśmīra.<BR>—क्रम-शस्, ind. gradually, by degrees; regularly,<BR>seriatim.<BR>—क्रम-शास्त्र, अम्, n. rules relating to<BR>the Krama arrangement.<BR>—क्रम-संहिता, f. a<BR>collection of Vedic texts arranged according to the<BR>Krama method.<BR>—क्रमसंहितोदाहरण (˚ता-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. an example from a Krama-saṃhitā.<BR>—क्रम-सङ्ग्रह, title of a treatise; [cf. कृत-<BR>दास.]<BR>—क्रम-सन्दर्भ-प्रभास, title of a<BR>chapter (खण्ड) in a particular work.<BR>—क्रमागत<BR>(˚म-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, descended or inherited lineally,<BR>what comes from one's ancestors in regular succession,<BR>arrived in due course or succession.<BR>—क्रमागत-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. hereditary succession or possession.<BR>—क्रमादित्य (˚म-आद्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>king Skanda-gupta.<BR>—क्रमाध्ययन (˚म-अध्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the Krama reading or arrangement; see क्र-<BR>म-पाठ above.<BR>—क्रमाध्यायिन् (˚म-अध्˚), ई,<BR>m. one who reads the Krama arrangement of a Vedic<BR>text.<BR>—क्रमानुयायिन् (˚म-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, follow-<BR>ing the methodical order.<BR>—क्रमानुसार or क्र-<BR>मान्वय (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. regular order, due<BR>arrangement.<BR>—क्रमायात (˚म-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>descended or inherited lineally, coming from one's<BR>ancestors in regular succession; one who has acceded<BR>to the throne by succession; proceeding in regular<BR>order.<BR>—क्रमावसान (˚म-अव्˚), अम्, n. the end<BR>of a word in the Krama arrangement of a Vedic text.<BR>—क्रमोक्त (˚म-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, enjoined for<BR>the Krama arrangement.<BR>—क्रमोद्वेग (˚म-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमक|क्रमकः
क्रमक, अस्, आ, अम्, going, proceeding; orderly,<BR>methodical; (अस्), m. a student who goes through a<BR>regular course of study, one who proceeds methodi-<BR>cally; one who reads or knows the Krama arrange-<BR>ment of a text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमण|क्रमणः
क्रमण, अस्, m. a step; the foot; a horse; N.<BR>of a son of Bhajamāna; (अम्), n. stepping, walking,<BR>going; transgressing; proceeding; approaching or<BR>undertaking anything; treatment of words or letters<BR>according to the Krama arrangement, doubling letters,<BR>words, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमणीय
क्रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone to, to be gone<BR>beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमदीश्वर
क्रमद्-ईश्वर, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>grammar called Saṅkṣipta-sāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रममाण
क्रममाण, अस्, आ, अम्, going, proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमिक
क्रमिक, अस्, आ, अम्, proceeding in a fixed order<BR>or methodically; successive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमितृ
क्रमितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, stepping, walking, going,<BR>who or what goes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम्य
क्रम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by the Krama<BR>arrangement, arising by the Krama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रा
क्रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of some compounds)<BR>stepping, going; [cf. उदधि-क्रा, दधि-क्रा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्त|क्रांत|क्रान्तः
क्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, going, gone or going<BR>over or across; spread, extended; attacking, invading,<BR>gone to or against; overcome, surpassed; (अस्), m.<BR>a horse; (in astronomy) declination; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a plant, a kind of Solanum [cf. बृहती]; a species<BR>of the Atyaṣṭī metre [cf. कान्ता]; (अम्), n. a step,<BR>(विष्णोः क्रान्तम्, ‘the step of Viṣṇu,’ N. of a<BR>Soma ceremony); a certain aspect in astronomy<BR>when the moon is in conjunction with a planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्ति|क्रांति|क्रांतिः|क्रान्तिः
क्रान्ति, इस्, f. going, proceeding, a step; overcom-<BR>ing, surpassing; attacking; declination of a planet;<BR>the sun's course on the globe, the ecliptic.<BR>—क्रान्ति-<BR>कक्ष, अस्, m. the course of the sun, the ecliptic.<BR>—क्रान्ति-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. a figure described by the<BR>ecliptic.<BR>—क्रान्ति-ज्या, f. the sine of the declina-<BR>tion or of the ecliptic.<BR>—क्रान्ति-पात, अस्, m. the<BR>intersection of the ecliptic and equinoctial circles, the<BR>equinoctial points or nodes of the ecliptic.<BR>—क्रान्ति-<BR>पात-गति, इस्, f. motion of the nodes of the ecliptic,<BR>precession of the equinox.<BR>—क्रान्ति-भाग, अस्, m.<BR>the declination of a point of the ecliptic.<BR>—क्रान्ति-<BR>मण्डल or क्रान्ति-वृत्त, अम्, n. the ecliptic.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">Page0260-c+ 71</a>]<BR>—क्रान्ति-वलय, अस्, m. the ecliptic; the space<BR>within the tropics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तु|क्रांतुः|क्रान्तुः
क्रान्तु, उस्, m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रामत्
क्रामत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going, proceeding over or<BR>across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमि|क्रमिः
क्रमि क्रमि, इस्, m. = कृमि, a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमु|क्रमुः
क्रमु क्रमु, उस्, m. the betel-nut tree,<BR>Areca Faufel or Catechu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुक|क्रमुकः
क्रमुक, अस्, m., N. of several plants, the Areca<BR>or betel-nut tree, Areca Faufel or Catechu; the mul-<BR>berry tree, Morus Indica (= ब्रह्म-दारु); another<BR>tree, a red sort of Lodhra (पट्टिका-लोध्र); a kind<BR>of fragrant grass, Bhadra-mustaka; the fruit of the<BR>cotton tree; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (ई), f. the<BR>betel-nut tree, Areca Faufel or Catechu.<BR>—क्रमुक-<BR>फल, अम्, n. the Areca-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेल|क्रमेलः
क्रमेल क्रमेल or क्रमेलक, अस्, m. the<BR>camel; [cf. Gr. κάμηλος Lat. camelus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय|क्रयः
क्रय क्रय, &c. See under rt. क्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयशीर्ष|क्रयशीर्षं
क्रयशीर्ष क्रयशीर्ष, अम्, n. = कपि-शीर्ष,<BR>the coping of a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रवण
क्रवण क्रवण, अस्, m., Ved. a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रविस्
क्रविस् क्रविस्, इस्, n., Ved. (or क्रवि in the<BR>comp. अ-क्रवि-हस्त, q. v.), raw flesh, carrion; [cf.<BR>Gr. κρέας; cf. also क्रूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रविष्णु
क्रविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of raw flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्य|क्रव्यं
क्रव्य, अम्, n. flesh, raw flesh, carrion; [cf.<BR>Lith. krauja-s, ‘blood;’ Russ. krovj; Hib. cru;<BR>Old Germ. hreo; Gr. κρέας; Lat. cruor, cruentus,<BR>crûdus, caro.]<BR>—क्रव्य-घातन, अस्, m. a deer, an<BR>antelope; (killed for its flesh.)<BR>—क्रव्य-भुज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, carnivorous, eating carrion; (क्), m. a Rākṣasa.<BR>—क्रव्य-भोजन, अस्, आ, अम्, carnivorous.<BR>—क्र-<BR>व्य-मुख, अस्, m. (?) having flesh in one's mouth,<BR>N. of a wolf in the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—क्रव्य-वाहन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. carrying corpses, an epithet of Agni<BR>(opposed to हव्य-वाहन).<BR>—क्रव्याद् (˚य-अद्),<BR>त्, त्, त्, consuming flesh or corpses, epithet of the fire<BR>of the funeral pile, or Agni in one of his terrible<BR>forms; epithet of a Yātu-dhāna and other evil beings,<BR>imps, and goblins; N. of a Rakṣas; a beast of prey,<BR>a carnivorous animal.<BR>—क्रव्याद (˚य-अद), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, carnivorous, an eater of flesh; (अस्), m. a goblin,<BR>a Rākṣasa; a lion, a hawk; the fire of the funeral<BR>pile; N. of a people.<BR>—क्रव्याशिन् (˚य-आश्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, carnivorous; (ई), m. a demon; an anthropophagus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रशय
क्रशय क्रशय (fr. कृश), nom. P. क्रश-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to emaciate, make thin or lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रशित
क्रशित, अस्, आ, अम्, emaciated, made thin or lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रशिमन्
क्रशिमन्, आ, m. leanness, emaciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रष्टव्य
क्रष्टव्य क्रष्टव्य. See rt. कृष्, p. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्राकचिक|क्राकचिकः
क्राकचिक क्राकचिक, अस्, m. (fr. क्रकच),<BR>a sawyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्राथ|क्राथः
क्राथ क्राथ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. क्रथ्), killing,<BR>murder; N. of a prince; of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;<BR>of a Nāga; of a monkey; a patronymic from Kratha;<BR>[cf. क्रथन.]<BR>—क्राथेश्वर (˚थ-ईश्˚) or क्रो-<BR>धेश्वर (˚ध-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Āpastamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्त|क्रांत|क्रान्तः
क्रान्त क्रान्त, क्रान्ति, &c. See under क्रम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रायक|क्रायकः
क्रायक क्रायक. See under rt. क्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमि|क्रिमिः
क्रिमि क्रिमि, इस्, m. a worm, an insect, &c.,<BR>and the words derived and compounded with क्रिमि.<BR>See under कृमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिय|क्रियः
क्रिय क्रिय, अस्, m. (a word borrowed from<BR>the Gr. κριός), the sign of the zodiac Aries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियमाण
क्रियमाण क्रियमाण. See rt. 1. कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिया
क्रिया क्रिया, f. (fr. rt. 1. कृ), doing, per-<BR>forming, performance; business; an act, action, un-<BR>dertaking; activity; work; labour; bodily action,<BR>exercise of the limbs; a literary work; medical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-a" target="_blank">Page0261-a+ 81</a>]<BR>treatment or practice; applying a remedy, cure (e. g.<BR>समक्रिय-त्व, the being treated according to one<BR>and the same system of medicine; विषमक्रिय-<BR>त्व, the being treated according to different methods);<BR>a religious rite or ceremony, sacrificial act, sacrifice;<BR>obsequies, rites performed immediately after death;<BR>purificatory rites, as ablution &c.; (religious action is<BR>sometimes personified as a daughter of Dakṣa and<BR>wife of Dharma, or a daughter of Kardama and wife<BR>of Kratu); judicial investigation by human means, as<BR>by witnesses, documents, &c., or by superhuman or<BR>ordeals of various kinds; (in grammar) action (as<BR>the general idea expressed by any verb); a verb, (ac-<BR>cording to later grammarians a verb is of two kinds,<BR>सकर्म-क्रिया, active, and अकर्म-क्रिया, intran-<BR>sitive); a noun of action; native lexicographers give<BR>also the following meanings to क्रिया, — atonement;<BR>disquisition; study; means, expedient; instrument,<BR>implement.<BR>—क्रिया-कर, अस्, m. one who per-<BR>forms an action, a student.<BR>—क्रिया-कर्तृ, ता, m.<BR>the doer of an action, an agent.<BR>—क्रिया-कलाप,<BR>अस्, m. title of a grammar; the great body of cere-<BR>monies enjoined in the Hindū laws, a number of<BR>actions of any kind; all the particulars or points of<BR>any business.<BR>—क्रिया-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, one who<BR>does any act, an agent, a performer; (अस्), m. a<BR>beginner, a novice, a tyro, a student; an agreement.<BR>—क्रिया-कौमुदी, f. title of a work by Govindā-<BR>nanda.<BR>—क्रिया-तन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘a Tantra of action,’<BR>one of the four classes of Tantras with Buddhists.<BR>—क्रिया-द्वेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who is averse to<BR>the part of a lawsuit or judicial trial called क्रिया,<BR>i. e. to witnesses, documents, ordeals, &c.; (ई), m.<BR>one of the five kinds of witnesses, he whose testi-<BR>mony is hurtful to the cause.<BR>—क्रिया-द्वैत, अम्,<BR>n. efficient cause, as resigning all to God.<BR>—क्रिया-<BR>निबन्ध, title of a work.<BR>—क्रिया-निर्देश, अस्, m.<BR>evidence.<BR>—क्रियानुरूप (˚या-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>conformable to the act, according to the action.<BR>—क्रियान्वित (˚या-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, practising<BR>ritual observances.<BR>—क्रिया-पटु, उस्, उस्, उ, clever,<BR>dextrous.<BR>—क्रिया-पथ, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>manner of medical treatment or application of reme-<BR>dies.<BR>—क्रिया-पद, अम्, n. a verb.<BR>—क्रिया-पर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, attentive to or diligent in the performance<BR>of one's duties.<BR>—क्रियापवर्ग (˚या-अप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>end of an affair, liberation from ceremonial acts.<BR>—क्रिया-पाद, अस्, m. the third division of a suit<BR>at law, witnesses, written documents and other proofs<BR>adduced by the complainants, the rejoinder of the<BR>plaintiff.<BR>—क्रिया-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m. course of pro-<BR>ceeding.<BR>—क्रिया-फल, अम्, n. result or conse-<BR>quence of acts.<BR>—क्रियाभ्युपगम (˚या-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. special compact or agreement.<BR>—क्रियाम्-<BR>बुधि (˚या-अम्˚), इस्, m. title of a work of Prāṇa-<BR>kṛṣṇa.<BR>—क्रिया-योग, अस्, m. the connection with<BR>an action or verb; the employment of expedients or<BR>instruments; the practical form of the Yoga system<BR>of philosophy, devotion by due performance of the<BR>duties of every day life, active devotion.<BR>—क्रियायोग-<BR>सार, अस्, m. a section of the Padma-purāṇa.<BR>—क्रिया-<BR>लोप, अस्, m. discontinuance or loss of any of the<BR>essential ceremonies of the Hindū religion.<BR>—क्रिया-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who performs an action, active,<BR>busy, engaged in a business, understanding business,<BR>fit for it, possessed of worldly knowledge; performing<BR>ceremonies in the right manner, celebrating religious<BR>rites.<BR>—क्रिया-वश, अस्, आ, अम्, subject to the in-<BR>fluence of acts; (अस्), m. necessity, necessary influence<BR>of acts done or to be done.<BR>—क्रियावसन्न (˚या-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who loses a lawsuit through the<BR>statements of the witnesses &c.<BR>—क्रिया-वाचक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or क्रिया-वाचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, expressing an<BR>action (as a verbal noun).<BR>—क्रिया-वादिन्, ई, m. a<BR>plaintiff; one who states the arguments in a lawsuit.<BR>—क्रिया-विधि, इस्, m. a rule of action; conduct of<BR>affairs, mode of performing any rite.<BR>—क्रियाविधि-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, conversant with business, under-<BR>standing the ritual &c.<BR>—क्रिया-विशाल, अम्, n. title<BR>of the thirteenth of the fourteen Pūrvas or most<BR>ancient Jaina writings.<BR>—क्रिया-विशेषण, अम्, n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">Page0261-b+ 78</a>]<BR>that which defines an action more closely; an adverb.<BR>—क्रिया-शक्ति, इस्, f. capability to act; the power<BR>of action.<BR>—क्रिया-समभिहार, अस्, m. repetition<BR>of any act, doing anything repeatedly.<BR>—क्रिया-सार,<BR>अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—क्रिया-स्थानक-विचार,<BR>अस्, m. title of a Jaina work.<BR>—क्रियेन्द्रिय (˚या-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, m. an organ of action, as the hand, foot,<BR>voice, organ of generation and that of excretion;<BR>also called कर्मेन्द्रिय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिवि|क्रिविः
क्रिवि क्रिवि, इस्, m., Ved. a leather bag,<BR>metaphorically ‘a cloud;’ N. of an Asura; a cistern,<BR>a well; the original name of the Pañcālas; [cf.<BR>क्रैव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्री
क्री 1. क्री, cl. 9. P. A. क्रीणाति, क्रीणीते,<BR>चिक्राय, चिक्रिये, क्रेष्यति, -ते, अक्रैषीत्,<BR>अक्रेष्ट, क्रेतुम्, to buy, purchase (with inst. of<BR>the price, and abl. or gen. of the person from which<BR>anything is bought, e. g. क इमम् इन्द्रं दश-<BR>भिर् धेनुभिर् मम क्रीणाति, who will buy this<BR>Indra of me for ten cows ? यम् माता-पित्रोर् अन्तिकात्<BR>or सकाशात् क्रीणीयात्, whom he may buy from his<BR>father and mother; क्रीणीष्व तद् दशभिः सुवर्-<BR>णैः, buy that for ten suvarṇas); to barter or ex-<BR>change; to win: Caus. क्रापयति, -यितुम्, अचि-<BR>क्रपत्: Desid. चिक्रीषति, -ते: Intens. चेक्रीयते,<BR>चेक्रयीति, चेक्रेति; [cf. Hib. creanaim, ‘I buy, I pur-<BR>chase;’ Gr. πρίαμαι, πέρνημι Lith. prekis, perku (?);<BR>Lat. pretium; Eng. hire.]<BR>—क्र्य्-आदि, अयस्, m.<BR>pl. the roots beginning with क्री, i. e. those of the<BR>ninth class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय|क्रयः
क्रय, अस्, m. buying, purchase.<BR>—क्रय-क्रीत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bought, purchased.<BR>—क्रय-द्रव्य,<BR>अम्, n. anything for which anything else is bought<BR>or exchanged.<BR>—क्रय-लेख्य, अम्, n. deed of sale,<BR>conveyance, &c.<BR>—क्रय-विक्रय, औ, m. du. buy-<BR>ing and selling, trade, traffic.<BR>—क्रयविक्रयिक,<BR>अस्, m. a trader or merchant, a dealer.<BR>—क्रयवि-<BR>क्रयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who buys or sells, one who<BR>strikes a bargain.<BR>—क्रयारोह (˚य-आर्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>market, a fair (where goods are piled up for sale).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयण|क्रयणं
क्रयण, अम्, n. buying, purchasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयणीय
क्रयणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bought or purchased,<BR>purchasable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयाणक
क्रयाणक, अस्, इका, अम्, what is sold, fit to<BR>be sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिक|क्रयिकः
क्रयिक, अस्, आ, अम्, buying, purchasing; (अस्),<BR>m. a trader, a dealer, a purchaser, a buyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिन्
क्रयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, a buyer, a purchaser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय्य|क्रय्यं
क्रय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, exhibited for sale, purchasable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रायक|क्रायकः
क्रायक, अस्, m. a buyer or purchaser; a dealer,<BR>a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्री
2. क्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, (at the end of some compounds)<BR>buying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीत|क्रीतः
क्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, bought, purchased; (अस्), m. a<BR>son, one of the twelve kinds acknowledged by the<BR>ancient Hindū law, viz. one purchased from his natural<BR>parents.<BR>—क्रीतानुशय (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. repenting<BR>a purchase, returning a purchase upon the seller,<BR>admissible in some cases by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीतक|क्रीतकः
क्रीतक, अस्, आ, अम्, acquired by purchase; (अस्),<BR>m. a son bought from his natural parents and adopted<BR>as male issue; also क्रीत-पुत्र (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेणि|क्रेणिः
क्रेणि, इस्, m. and क्रेणी, f. buying, purchasing,<BR>purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतव्य|क्रेतव्यं
क्रेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bought, purchasable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतृ
क्रेतृ, ता, m. a buyer, purchaser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेय|क्रेयं
क्रेय, अस्, आ, अम्, purchasable, to be bought.<BR>—क्रेय-द, अस्, आ, अम्, one who exhibits anything<BR>for sale, a seller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड्
क्रीड् क्रीड्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) क्रीडति,<BR>चिक्रीड, क्रीडिष्यति, अक्रीडीत्, क्रीडितुम्,<BR>to play, sport, amuse one's self, frolic, gambol, dally,<BR>(used of men, animals, the wind and waves, &c.);<BR>to jest, joke with (with inst. or with सह and inst.,<BR>e. g. द्रोणेन or द्रोणेन सह क्रीडति, he sports<BR>with Droṇa): Caus. क्रीडयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>play, to allow to play: Desid. चिक्रीडिषति: Intens.<BR>चेक्रीड्यते, चेक्रीट्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड|क्रीडः
क्रीड, अस्, आ, अम्, playing, sporting; (अस्, आ),<BR>m. f. sport, play, pastime, pleasure, amusement (often<BR>in compounds, e. g. क्रीडा-मुदः, f. pl. the pleasures<BR>of play, or of amorous sport; कृष्ण-क्रीडा, sport<BR>with Kṛṣṇa; जल-क्रीडा, playing about in water);<BR>disrespect shown by jest or joke.<BR>—क्रीडा-कानन,<BR>अम्, n. a pleasure-grove.<BR>—क्रीडाकूत (˚डा-आक्˚),<BR>अम्, n. sportive or wanton purpose or desire.<BR>—क्रीडा-कोप, अस्, m. assumed anger, anger in<BR>sport.<BR>—क्रीडा-कौतुक, अम्, n. wanton curiosity;<BR>sport, play, pastime, enjoyment; lasciviousness, sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>—क्रीडा-खण्ड, title of the second part<BR>of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—क्रीडा-गृह, अम्, n. a<BR>pleasure-house, a house for amusement.<BR>—क्रीडा-<BR>चङ्क्रमण, अम्, n. (?), N. of a place.<BR>—क्रीडा-<BR>चन्द्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of eighteen syllables each; N.<BR>of a poet.<BR>—क्रीडा-नारी, f. a harlot, a courtezan.<BR>—क्रीडा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of play or<BR>sport.<BR>—क्रीडा-मयूर, अस्, m. a peacock kept for<BR>pleasure or amusement.<BR>—क्रीडा-मृग, अस्, m. any<BR>animal kept for pleasure, a toy-deer, a toy-animal of<BR>any kind.<BR>—क्रीडा-रत्न, अम्, n. the gem of sports,<BR>copulation.<BR>—क्रीडा-रथ, अस्, m. a cart, a carriage<BR>used for amusements.<BR>—क्रीडा-रसातल, अम्, n.<BR>title of a work in the Sāhitya-darpaṇa.<BR>—क्रीडा-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, sportive, playful.<BR>—क्रीडा-वन, अम्,<BR>n. a pleasure-garden, a park.<BR>—क्रीडा-वेश्मन्,<BR>अ, n. a pleasure-house, a house for amusement.<BR>—क्रीडा-शकुन्त, अस्, m. a bird kept for pleasure<BR>or amusement.<BR>—क्रीडा-शैल, अस्, m. a pleasure-<BR>mountain, a pleasure-mound or hillock in a garden.<BR>—क्रीडा-सरस्, अस्, n. a pleasure-lake.<BR>—क्रीडा-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. or क्रीडोद्देश (˚डा-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a play-ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडक|क्रीडकः
क्रीडक, अस्, m. a player, one who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडत्
क्रीडत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, playing, sporting, gamboling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडन|क्रीडनं
क्रीडन, अम्, n. playing, play, sporting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनक|क्रीडनकं|क्रीडनकः
क्रीडनक, अस्, इका, अम्, playing, sporting; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. or n. (?), a plaything, a toy for children.<BR>—क्रीडनक-ता, f. the state of a plaything; क्रीड-<BR>नकतया, after the manner of a plaything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनीय|क्रीडनीयं
क्रीडनीय or क्रीडनीयक, अम्, n. a plaything,<BR>toy, a doll.<BR>—क्रीडनीयक-सन्निभ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>like a toy or doll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडमान
क्रीडमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sporting, playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडि
क्रीडि or क्रीऌइ, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. playing, sporting;<BR>epithet of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडितृ
क्रीडितृ, ता, m. a player, one who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडिन्
क्रीडिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. playing, sporting; epithet<BR>of the Maruts or winds; (ई), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडु
क्रीडु or क्रीऌउ, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. playing, effer-<BR>vescing (?); epithet of the Soma.<BR>—क्रीडु-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. playing, playful; epithet of flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च्|क्रुंच्
क्रुञ्च् 1. क्रुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. क्रुञ्चति, -चितुम्,<BR>to curve or make crooked; to be or be-<BR>come crooked, to move crookedly; to be or become<BR>small, to shrink; to make small, to lessen; to go<BR>towards, approach, arrive at; [cf. Hib. cruinn,<BR>‘rotundus.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुक्त
क्रुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, crooked, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च्|क्रुंच्
2. क्रुञ्च्, ङ्, m., Ved. a kind of snipe, a curlew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुञ्च, अस्, m. a kind of snipe, a curlew; N. of<BR>a mountain; (आ), f. a female snipe or curlew; a<BR>kind of Vīṇā or lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्चकीया
क्रुञ्चकीया, f., N. of a place in India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्च|क्रौंच|क्रौंचः|क्रौञ्चः
क्रौञ्च, अस्, m. a curlew, heron, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुड्
क्रुड् क्रुड्, cl. 6. P. क्रुडति, -डितुम्, to<BR>sink, dive; to be or become thick; (another<BR>form for भृड्); [cf. कूड् and क्रूड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्
क्रुध् 1. क्रुध्, cl. 4. P. (rarely A.) क्रुध्-<BR>यति, -ते, चुक्रोध, क्रोत्स्यति, अक्रुधत्,<BR>क्रोद्धुम्, to become angry, to be wrathful or<BR>angry with (with dat. or gen. or acc. or with उपरि and<BR>gen., e. g. पुत्राय or पुत्रस्य or पुत्रम् or पुत्र-<BR>स्योपरि चुक्रोध, he was angry with his son: Caus.<BR>क्रोधयति, -यितुम्, to make angry, provoke, irritate;<BR>Desid. चुक्रुत्सति: Intens. चोक्रुध्यते, चोक्रोद्धि;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">Page0262-a+ 78</a>]<BR>[cf. Lith. rus-tus, ‘angry;’ rus-tybê, ‘anger;’ Lat.<BR>crudelis (?); Gr. κότος; Germ. groll; Hib. cor-<BR>ruidhe, ‘anger, wrath, motion;’ corruigh, ‘fury,<BR>resentment.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुद्ध|क्रुद्धः
क्रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, irritated, provoked, angry,<BR>wrathful; fierce, cruel; (अम्), n. anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्
2. क्रुध्, त्, f. or क्रुधा, f. anger, wrath, passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्मिन्
क्रुध्मिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. wrathful, irritable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्यत्
क्रुध्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being angry, feeling pro-<BR>voked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोध|क्रोधः
क्रोध, अस्, m. anger, wrath, passion; anger<BR>personified as a child of Lobha and Nikṛti; or of<BR>death; or of Brahmā; N. of a Dānava; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a daughter of Dakṣa.<BR>—क्रोध-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>proceeding from or engendered by wrath, (especially<BR>applicable to eight vices, hatred, envy, oppression,<BR>violence, &c.)<BR>—क्रोध-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, a person<BR>of angry disposition; passionate, angry.<BR>—क्रोध-<BR>मूर्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome or infatuated with<BR>anger, passionate, angry; (अस्), m. a kind of perfume,<BR>commonly called Cor, = चोर.<BR>—क्रोध-वर्जित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, free from wrath, mild, calm.<BR>—क्रोध-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—क्रोध-वश,<BR>अस्, m. the power of anger; (अस्, आ, अम्), over-<BR>powered by anger, passionate, violent; N. of several<BR>kinds of evil spirits; (अस्), m., N. of a Rakṣas; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa.<BR>—क्रोधवश-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, subject to anger,<BR>under the influence of anger.<BR>—क्रोध-समन्वित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filled with anger.<BR>—क्रोध-हन्तृ, ता,<BR>m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—क्रोधान्वित (˚ध-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wrathful, angry.<BR>—क्रोधामर्ष-जिह्म-<BR>भ्रू (˚ध-अम्˚), ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, bending the brow with<BR>anger and impatience.<BR>—क्रोधोज्झित (˚ध-उज्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, free from wrath, composed, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधन|क्रोधनः
क्रोधन, अस्, आ, अम्, inclined to wrath, passionate,<BR>angry; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Kauśika and pupil<BR>of Garga; also of a son of Ayuta and father of<BR>Devātithi; (आ), f. a passionate woman, a vixen;<BR>(अम्), n. the being angry, anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधनीय
क्रोधनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, anything which may<BR>produce anger, provocative; (अम्), n. an injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधालु
क्रोधालु, उस्, उस्, उ, passionate, violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधिन्
क्रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, passionate, angry; (ई), m. a<BR>buffalo; a dog; (इनी), f. mystical name of the<BR>letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधिष्ठ
क्रोधिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, very irate or wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुन्थ्|क्रुंथ्
क्रुन्थ् क्रुन्थ्, cl. 9. P. क्रुथ्नाति, क्रुन्-<BR>थितुम्, to embrace, to cling or adhere<BR>to; to be distressed, to pain, injure, kill, suffer pain,<BR>be distressed; (another form for कुन्थ्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुमु|क्रुमुः
क्रुमु क्रुमु, उस्, f., Ved., N. of a river, a<BR>tributary of the Indus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुमुक|क्रुमुकः
क्रुमुक क्रुमुक, अस्, m., Ved. a piece of<BR>wood or match used to catch the sacrificial fire when<BR>kindled by friction; [cf. कृमुक, क्रमुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश्
क्रुश् क्रुश्, cl. 1. P. (rarely A.) क्रोशति,<BR>-ते, चुक्रोश, क्रोक्ष्यति, अक्रुक्षत्,<BR>क्रोष्टुम्, to cry out, shriek, yell, bawl, call out, halloo;<BR>to exclaim; to cry, lament; to weep; to sound, make<BR>a singing noise (as the ear): Caus. क्रोशयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्: Desid. चुक्रुक्षति: Intens. चोक्रुश्यते,<BR>चोक्रुशीति; [cf. Lith. klykiu, ‘to cry;’ kryksztauju;<BR>Hib. cruisigh, ‘music, song;’ Lat. crocis, crocito;<BR>Gr. κρώζω, κράζω, κραγγή; Goth. krukya.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश्वन्
क्रुश्वन्, आ, m. a jackal; [cf. क्रोष्टु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुष्ट|क्रुष्टं
क्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, calling out, crying out,<BR>scolding; wept, cried; cried aloud, bawled; called<BR>at, abused; (अम्), n. crying, weeping, sobbing;<BR>noise, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोश|क्रोशः
क्रोश, अस्, m. a cry, a yell, a shriek, a shout, a call,<BR>calling out, a noise (e. g. कर्ण-क्रोश, a noise in<BR>the ears); the range of the voice in calling or hallooing,<BR>a measure of distance, an Indian league, commonly<BR>called a Kos, = 1000 Daṇḍas, = 4000 Hastas, = (1/4) Yo-<BR>jana; according to other authorities = 2000 Daṇḍas,<BR>= 8000 Hastas, = (1/2) Gavyūti; (अम्), n., N. of a Sā-<BR>man.<BR>—क्रोश-ताल, अस्, m. a large or double drum.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">Page0262-b+ 79</a>]<BR>—क्रोश-ध्वनि, इस्, m. a large drum.<BR>—क्रोश-<BR>मात्र-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone the length of a Krośa.<BR>—क्रोश-मात्र-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing at the<BR>distance of a Krośa.<BR>—क्रोश-युग, अम्, n. a measure<BR>of two Krośas, = 4000 yards or about 2(1/2) miles;<BR>(this seems to correspond to the modern Krośa,<BR>but the standard varies.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशत्
क्रोशत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, crying, calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशन
क्रोशन, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what cries; (अम्),<BR>n. crying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशिन्
क्रोशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crying out, calling out, weeping<BR>(e. g. उष्ट्र-क्रोशिन्, making sounds like a camel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्ट
क्रोष्ट, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टु
क्रोष्टु (मुस्त् form strong cases and मय् form<BR>weak cases from क्रोष्टृ, Gram. 128. c), a<BR>jackal; N. of a son of Yadu and father of Vṛjinīvat<BR>(in this last sense nom. sing. क्रोष्टा or क्रोष्टुस्).<BR>—क्रोष्टु-कर्ण, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—क्रोष्टु-पाद, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of this man.<BR>—क्रोष्टु-<BR>पुच्छिका or क्रोष्टु-पुच्छी, f. the plant Hemionitis<BR>Cordifolia; [cf. क्रोष्टुक-पुच्छिका or क्रोष्टु-<BR>विन्ना.]<BR>—क्रोष्टु-फल, अस्, m. the tree Ter-<BR>minalia Catappa, = इङ्गुद.<BR>—क्रोष्टु-मान and<BR>क्रोष्टु-माय, अस्, m., N. of two men; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of these men.<BR>—क्रोष्टु-विन्ना,<BR>f. a plant, either Chaculiya, Hemionitis Cordifolia (पृ-<BR>श्नि-पर्णी), or Ramvāsac; [cf. शृगाल-विन्ना.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुक
क्रोष्टुक, अस्, m. a jackal; N. of a man, cf.<BR>क्रौष्टुकि; (ई), f. a female jackal; a daughter of<BR>Krodha-vaśā and mother of the yellow apes.<BR>—क्रो-<BR>ष्टुक-पुच्छिका, f. a plant, commonly Chaculiya,<BR>Hemionitis Cordifolia; or, according to some, Ram-<BR>vāsac; [cf. क्रोष्टु-विन्ना.]<BR>—क्रोष्टुक-मान, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—क्रोष्टुक-मेखला, f. the plant<BR>Hemionitis Cordifolia.<BR>—क्रोष्टुक-शिरस्, अस्, n. a<BR>disease of the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टृ
क्रोष्टृ, टा, m. (not used in the weakest cases,<BR>cf. क्रोष्टु), a jackal; N. of a son of Yadu and<BR>father of Vṛjinīvat; (ट्री), f. the female of a jackal;<BR>a kind of Convolvulus; N. of another plant, [cf.<BR>लाङ्गली.]<BR>—क्रोष्टेक्षु, उस्, m. (fr. क्रोष्टा =<BR>क्रोष्टृ and इक्षु?), a kind of sugar-cane, =<BR>श्वेतेक्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूड्
क्रूड् क्रूड्, cl. 10. P. क्रूडयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make thick; [cf. कूड्, क्रुड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर|क्रूरः
क्रूर क्रूर, अस्, आ, अम् (related to क्रविस्, क्र-<BR>व्य), wounded, hurt, sore; bloody; raw; cruel, fierce,<BR>ferocious, hard-hearted; pitiless; hard, harsh, rough;<BR>formidable, terrible; inauspicious (opposed to सौम्य<BR>and अ-क्रूर, and epithet of the first, third, fifth,<BR>seventh, ninth, and eleventh signs of the zodiac, which<BR>are supposed to have a malignant influence); mis-<BR>chievous, destructive; hard, solid; strong (as a bow,<BR>opposed to मन्द); hot, sharp, disagreeable; (अम्),<BR>ind. in a formidable manner; (अस्, अम्), m. n. boiled<BR>rice; (अस्), m. a hawk; a heron; two plants, red<BR>oleander, = रक्त-करवीर, and another plant, = भू-<BR>ताङ्कुश; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = रक्त-पुनर्नवा;<BR>(अम्), n. a wound, a sore; blood-shedding, slaughter,<BR>cruelty, any horrible deed; any frightful apparition.<BR>—क्रूरकर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, perpetrating cruel<BR>actions; a rapacious animal.<BR>—क्रूर-कर्मन्, अ,<BR>n. a bloody or terrible deed; any hard or difficult<BR>labour; (आ, आ, अ), performing bloody or terrible deeds,<BR>fierce, cruel, unrelenting; (आ), m., N. of a plant, = क-<BR>टुतुम्बिनी = कटुतुम्बी (?).<BR>—क्रूर-कृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>performing bloody or terrible deeds, fierce, cruel, un-<BR>relenting.<BR>—क्रूर-कोष्ठ, अस्, m. torpid or costive<BR>bowels unaffected by strong purgatives; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>one whose bowels are torpid or costive.<BR>—क्रूर-<BR>गन्ध, अस्, m. sulphur; (आ), f., N. of a tree, =<BR>कन्थारी.<BR>—क्रूर-चरित, अस्, आ, अम्, cruel, fero-<BR>cious, addicted to cruel practices.<BR>—क्रूर-ता, f. or<BR>क्रूर-त्व, अम्, n. cruelty, fierceness.<BR>—क्रूर-दन्ती,<BR>f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—क्रूर-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, evil-<BR>eyed, of terrible aspect, mischievous, villainous, cruel;<BR>(क्), m. an epithet of the planet Śani or Saturn; also<BR>an epithet of the planet Mars.<BR>—क्रूर-धूर्त, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">Page0262-c+ 74</a>]<BR>m. a kind of thorn-apple; [cf. कृष्ण-धत्तूरक.]<BR>—क्रूर-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, or क्रूर-मानस, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, cruel-minded.<BR>—क्रूर-रव, अस्, m. a<BR>jackal (?).<BR>—क्रूर-राविन्, ई, m. a raven.<BR>—क्रूर-<BR>लोचन, अस्, m. an epithet of the planet Saturn (of<BR>an evil or inauspicious aspect).<BR>—क्रूर-सर्प-वत्,<BR>ind. like an enraged serpent.<BR>—क्रूराकृति (˚र-आक्˚),<BR>इस्, m. an epithet of Rāvaṇa, the ruler of Laṅkā.<BR>—क्रूराक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a minister<BR>of the owl-king Ari-mardana.<BR>—क्रूराचार (˚र-<BR>आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, following cruel or savage practices.<BR>—क्रूरात्मन् (˚र-आत्˚), आ, m. an epithet of the<BR>planet Saturn; [cf. क्रूर-दृश् and क्रूर-लोचन.]<BR>—क्रूराशय (˚र-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>bowels are torpid or costive; containing fierce animals<BR>(as a river &c.); of a terrible or fierce disposition.<BR>—क्रूरोपसंहत (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>nected with cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर्च|क्रूर्च्च
क्रूर्च क्रूर्च, अस्, अम्, m. n. the beard; [cf.<BR>कूर्च.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेणि|क्रेणिः
क्रेणि क्रेणि, क्रेतव्य, &c. See rt. क्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रैडिन
क्रैडिन क्रैडिन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्रीडिन्, q. v.),<BR>Ved. belonging to the Maruts or winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रैडिनीया
क्रैडिनीया, f., scil. इष्टि, the Iṣṭi or sacrificial<BR>oblation, sacred to the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रैव्य
क्रैव्य क्रैव्य, अस्, m. (fr. क्रिवि), a king of<BR>the Krivis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्च|क्रोंच|क्रोंचः|क्रोञ्चः
क्रोञ्च क्रोञ्च, &c. Cf. क्रौञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोठिन्
क्रोठिन् क्रोठिन्, ई, m. (?), N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोड|क्रोडं|क्रोडः
क्रोड क्रोड, अस्, अम्, आ, m. n. f. (m. in the<BR>earlier language; n. in later works; also f. according<BR>to the lexicographers), the breast, the chest, the<BR>bosom, (at the end of compounds the fem. can only<BR>end in आ, e. g. कल्याण-क्रोडा, a woman with a<BR>well-formed breast), the flank, the hollow above the<BR>hip; the lap; the interior of anything, the inner<BR>part, a cavity, a hollow [cf. उदर and गर्भ];<BR>(अस्), m. a hog; the esculent bulb of a kind of plant,<BR>= वाराही-कन्द, [cf. क्रोड-कन्या]; N. of Śani or<BR>the planet Saturn; (आ), f. a plant, = क्रोड-चूडा.<BR>—क्रोड-कन्या, f. the esculent bulb of a kind of<BR>plant; [cf. क्रोड.]<BR>—क्रोड-चूडा, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= महा-श्रावणिका.<BR>—क्रोड-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>marginal writing omitted in its proper place, a post-<BR>script to a letter, a supplement, a codicil to a will.<BR>—क्रोड-पर्णी, f. a prickly nightshade, Solanum<BR>Jacquini, = कण्टकारिका.<BR>—क्रोड-पाद, अस्, m. a<BR>turtle, a tortoise.<BR>—क्रोडाङ्क (˚ड-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>tortoise.<BR>—क्रोडाङ्घ्रि (˚ड-अङ्˚), इस्, m. a turtle or<BR>tortoise.<BR>—क्रोडी-मुख, अस्, m. (?) a rhinoceros.<BR>—क्रोडेष्टा (˚ड-इष्˚), f. a kind of grass, = मुस्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीकृ
क्रोडी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to fold to<BR>the breast, clasp to the bosom, clasp, embrace.<BR>—क्रोडी-करण, अम्, n. folding to the breast, em-<BR>bracing.<BR>—क्रोडी-कृति, इस्, f. embracing, embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौड
क्रौड, अस्, ई, अम्, fit for or belonging to a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोणकवर्ण
क्रोणकवर्ण क्रोणक-वर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोथ|क्रोथः
क्रोथ क्रोथ, अस्, m. (fr. क्रुथ् for rt.<BR>क्रुन्थ्?), killing, slaying, murder; [cf. क्राथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोध|क्रोधः
क्रोध क्रोध, &c. See under 1. क्रुध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोश|क्रोशः
क्रोश क्रोश, क्रोष्टु. See under क्रुश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्च|क्रौंच|क्रौंचः|क्रौञ्चः
क्रौञ्च क्रौञ्च, अस्, m. (fr. rt. क्रुञ्च्, q. v.),<BR>a kind of curlew or heron (Ardea Jaculator); the<BR>emblem of the fifth Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī;<BR>(ई), f. the female curlew; a daughter of Tāmrā and<BR>mother of the curlews; (अस्), m. a mountain, part of<BR>the Himālaya range, situated in the eastern part of the<BR>chain on the north of Asam; one of the Dvīpas or<BR>principal divisions of the world, surrounded by the<BR>sea of curds; N. of a Rakṣas; N. of a pupil of<BR>Śāka-pūrṇi; (अम्), n., scil. अस्त्र, N. of a mystical<BR>weapon; N. of a Sāman; also of a particular Vedic<BR>formula.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-दारण or क्रौञ्च-सूदन,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">Page0263-a+ 73</a>]<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of the god of war, Kārttikeya, who<BR>tore asunder the mountain Krauñca.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-<BR>द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of a Dvīpa, = क्रौञ्च.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-<BR>पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, an epithet of horses, ‘the flanks<BR>of which are similar to the wings of a curlew.’<BR>—क्रौञ्च-पदा, f., N. of a metre consisting of<BR>four lines of twenty-five syllables each.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-<BR>पदी, f., N. of a place.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-पुर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-बन्ध, अस्, m. a parti-<BR>cular kind of knot.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-रन्ध्र, अम्, n. the<BR>Krauñca pass, caused by the deity Kārttikeya and by<BR>Paraśu-rāma; see क्रौञ्चारि below.<BR>—क्रौञ्च-वत्,<BR>आन्, m., N. of a mountain, = क्रौञ्च.<BR>—क्रौञ्चा-<BR>दन (˚च-अद्˚), अम्, n. the fibres of the stalk of the<BR>lotus (मृणाल); N. of several plants, = घेञ्चुली;<BR>another plant, = चिञ्चोटक; long pepper; (ई), f. the<BR>seed of the lotus.<BR>—क्रौञ्चारण्य (˚च-अर्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a forest.<BR>—क्रौञ्चाराति (˚च-अर्˚), इस्, m. an<BR>epithet of the deity Kārttikeya.<BR>—क्रौञ्चारि (˚च-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. an epithet of the deity Kārttikeya and<BR>of the hero and Avatāra Paraśu-rāma, who with his<BR>arrows made a pass or defile through the Krauñca<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चिकीपुत्र
क्रौञ्चिकी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौड
क्रौड क्रौड. See under क्रोड last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौर्य|क्रौर्यं|क्रौर्य्य
क्रौर्य क्रौर्य, अम्, n. (fr. क्रूर), cruelty,<BR>fierceness, anger; hard-heartedness; terribleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौशशतिक|क्रौशशतिकः
क्रौशशतिक क्रौशशतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्रोश<BR>+ शत), one who goes a hundred Krośas or leagues;<BR>one who deserves to be approached from a distance of a<BR>hundred Krośas or leagues (as a religious teacher &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौष्टिक
क्रौष्टिक क्रौष्टिक, अस्, m. a wrong form for<BR>क्रौष्टुकि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौष्टुकर्ण
क्रौष्टुकर्ण क्रौष्टुकर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, coming<BR>from Kroṣṭu-karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौष्टुकि|क्रौष्टुकिः
क्रौष्टुकि क्रौष्टुकि, इस्, m. (a patronymic<BR>fr. क्रोष्टुक), N. of a grammarian; N. of an<BR>astrologer; N. of a warrior-tribe belonging to the<BR>Trigarta-ṣaṣṭhās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौष्टुकीय
क्रौष्टुकीय, अस्, m. a prince of the warrior-<BR>tribe called Krauṣṭuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्र्यादि
क्र्यादि क्र्य्-आदि, a term of grammar to de-<BR>note the roots of the ninth class of which क्री is the<BR>first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लथ्
क्लथ् क्लथ्, cl. 1. P., Ved. क्लथति, -थि-<BR>तुम्, to turn round, revolve, to form into<BR>clots or lumps; to kill or hurt; [cf. Lat. clades.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लथन
क्लथन, अम्, n., Ved. turning round, forming<BR>into clots or lumps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लदीवत्|क्लदीवन्त्
क्लदीवत् क्लदीवत्, आन्, अती, अत् (rt. क्लिद्?),<BR>Ved. wet, moist (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लन्द्|क्लंद्
क्लन्द् क्लन्द् or क्लद् [cf. rt. क्रन्द्], cl. 1.<BR>P. क्लन्दति, चक्लन्द, क्लन्दिष्यति,<BR>क्लन्दितुम्, to call; to lament; to weep; cl. 1. A.<BR>क्लन्दते or क्लदते &c., to be confounded or<BR>troubled; to grieve; [cf. Hib. glaodhaim, ‘I call,<BR>bawl, roar, shout;’ Gr. κλάζω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लन्द
क्लन्द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. क्लन्द् for क्रन्द्?), Ved.<BR>crying, noisy (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लप्
क्लप् क्लप्, cl. 10. P. क्लापयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>speak barbarously; (another form for ह्लप्);<BR>[cf. Lith. kalpu, ‘to speak.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम्
क्लम् क्लम् [cf. rt. श्रम्, the rt. क्लम्<BR>seems principally confined to the later arti-<BR>ficial poems], cl. 1. 4. P. क्लामति, क्लाम्यति, च-<BR>क्लाम, क्लमिष्यति, क्लमितुम्, to be or become<BR>fatigued, to be weary or tired or exhausted; to be de-<BR>pressed; [cf. Gr. κάμνω; Lat. lentus for clentus (?);<BR>Germ. lahm; Old Germ. lam; Lith. lumas.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम|क्लमः
क्लम, अस्, m. fatigue, exhaustion, languor,<BR>weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथ|क्लमथः
क्लमथ, अस्, m. fatigue, exhaustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथु|क्लमथुः
क्लमथु, उस्, m. fatigue, languor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमिन्
क्लमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, becoming tired, languishing,<BR>exhausted, weary.<BR>—क्लमि-ता, f. or क्लमि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. exhaustion, languor^1, fatigue.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्त|क्लांत|क्लान्तः
क्लान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, tired, fatigued, exhausted,<BR>languishing; wearied; depressed in spirits or ex-<BR>hausted; dried up, withering; thin, emaciated.<BR>—क्लान्त-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, low-spirited, languid,<BR>melancholy.<BR>—क्लान्त-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>weary face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्ति|क्लांति|क्लांतिः|क्लान्तिः
क्लान्ति, इस्, f. fatigue, weariness.<BR>—क्लान्ति-च्छिद्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, relieving fatigue, refreshing, invigorating.<BR>—क्लान्ति-च्छेद, अस्, m. refreshing, restoring, re-<BR>moving fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लव्
क्लव् क्लव्, cl. 1. A. क्लवते, to fear, be<BR>afraid: Caus. क्लवयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिद्
क्लिद् क्लिद्, cl. 4. P. क्लिद्यति, चिक्लेद,<BR>क्लेदिष्यति and क्लेत्स्यति, अक्लिदत्,<BR>क्लेदितुम् and क्लेत्तुम्, to be or become wet or<BR>damp: Caus. P. क्लेदयति, -यितुम्, to bedew, wet,<BR>moisten: Desid. चिक्लेदिषति चिक्लिदिषति, चिक्लित्-<BR>सति: Intens. चेक्लिद्यते, चेक्लेत्ति; [cf. Gr. κλύζω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्न|क्लिन्नं
क्लिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, moistened, wet; running (as<BR>an eye).<BR>—क्लिन्न-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having moist<BR>eyes, pitiful.<BR>—क्लिन्न-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. excess of the<BR>lacrymal discharge, watering of the eyes.<BR>—क्लिन्न-<BR>हृद्, त्, त्, त्, tender-hearted.<BR>—क्लिन्नाक्ष (˚न-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having moist eyes, blear-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेद|क्लेदः
क्लेद, अस्, m. wetness, dampness, moisture; run-<BR>ning, discharge from a sore.<BR>—क्लेद-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, moist, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदक|क्लेदकः
क्लेदक, अस्, आ, अम्, wetting, moistening, making<BR>wet or moist; (अस्), m. phlegm in the stomach,<BR>excess of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन्
क्लेदन्, आ, m. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन|क्लेदनः
क्लेदन, अस्, ई, अम्, moistening, making wet;<BR>(अस्), m. phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humor<BR>[cf. कफ]; a species of phlegm; (अम्), n. wet-<BR>ting, moistening; oozing, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदु|क्लेदुः
क्लेदु, उस्, m. the moon; a morbid combination<BR>of the three humors of the body (सन्निपात), com-<BR>plication of disorders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेद्य
क्लेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be moistened, to be wetted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्द्|क्लिंद्
क्लिन्द् क्लिन्द्, cl. 1. P. A. क्लिन्दति, -ते, to<BR>lament; [cf. क्रन्द् and क्लन्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिब्
क्लिब् क्लिब्, प्, f. (?), Ved. accomplishment<BR>(fr. कॢप्?); (Sāy.) the created world; (a various<BR>reading has कॢब्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिश्
क्लिश् क्लिश्, cl. 9. P. क्लिश्नाति, चिक्लेश, क्ले-<BR>शिष्यति and क्लेक्ष्यति, अक्लेशीत् and<BR>अक्लिक्षत्, क्लेशितुम् and क्लेष्टुम्, to torment,<BR>torture, trouble, molest; to cause pain, afflict, dis-<BR>tress; to suffer, feel pain, suffer distress; cl. 4. A.<BR>क्लिश्यते, चिक्लिशे, क्लेशिष्यते, अक्लेशिष्ट, क्लेशि-<BR>तुम्, to be tormented or molested; to be afflicted,<BR>feel pain, suffer: Caus. P. A. क्लेशयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>to torment, molest: Desid. चिक्लिक्षति, चिक्लिशिषति,<BR>चिक्लेशिषति, चिक्लिशिषते, चिक्लेशिषते: Intens.<BR>चेक्लिश्यते, चेक्लेष्टि; [cf. Cambro-Brit. glœsi, ‘to<BR>pain, to cause a pang, to suffer a pang.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशित|क्लिशितः
क्लिशित or क्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, molested, tor-<BR>mented, distressed, afflicted; wearied, hurt, injured;<BR>being in a bad condition, worn; put to shame; con-<BR>tradictory, inconsistent; connected with pain or<BR>suffering; (अम्), ind. in distress.<BR>—क्लिशित-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, suffering pain or distress.<BR>—क्लिष्ट-वर्त्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. a disease of the eyelids; [cf. क्लिन्न-<BR>वर्त्मन्.]<BR>—क्लिष्ट-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, leading a<BR>wretched life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिश्यमान
क्लिश्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्टि|क्लिष्टिः
क्लिष्टि, इस्, f. affliction, calamity, distress; service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश, अस्, m. pain, affliction, distress; pain from<BR>disease, anguish; wrath, anger; worldly occupation;<BR>care, trouble.<BR>—क्लेश-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, causing pain,<BR>afflicting.<BR>—क्लेश-क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, capable of<BR>enduring pain and trouble.<BR>—क्लेश-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>distressing.<BR>—क्लेश-नाशन, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying<BR>or palliating trouble.<BR>—क्लेश-प्रहाण, अम्, n. ter-<BR>mination of distress, especially of worldly cares and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">Page0263-c+ 73</a>]<BR>passions.<BR>—क्लेश-भागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having trouble.<BR>—क्लेश-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, having trouble.<BR>—क्लेशा-<BR>पह (˚श-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, allaying pain or suffer-<BR>ing, consolatory, consoling; palliative; (अस्), m. a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशक
क्लेशक, अस्, ई, अम्, giving pain, troublesome,<BR>annoying, afflicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशित|क्लेशितः
क्लेशित, अस्, आ, अम्, pained, distressed, afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशिन्
क्लेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, connected with pain, causing pain<BR>or suffering; hurting, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेष्टृ
क्लेष्टृ, टा, m. one who causes pain or suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीत
क्लीत क्लीत, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतक
क्लीतक क्लीतक, अम्, n. a kind of plant with<BR>a poisonous root, Glycyrrhiza Glabra ?. (काल-क्ली-<BR>तक, अम्, n. the Indigo plant.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतकिका
क्लीतकिका, f. the Indigo plant, Indigofera Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतनक
क्लीतनक क्लीतनक, अम्, n. a kind of plant,<BR>= अति-रसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब्
क्लीब् क्लीब् or क्लीव्, cl. 1. A. क्लीबते or<BR>क्लीवते, चिक्लीबे, क्लीबिष्यते, क्लीबितुम्<BR>(according to some also क्लीवायते), to be impotent,<BR>to behave like one who is impotent or like a eunuch;<BR>to be timorous, to be modest or unassuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब|क्लीबः
क्लीब or क्लीव, अस्, आ, अम्, impotent, emasculated,<BR>a eunuch; unmanly, timorous, timid; weak, weak-<BR>minded, base; idle, slothful; a coward; of the<BR>neuter gender; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the neuter gender;<BR>[cf. Hib. cailltean, ‘eunuch;’ caillte, ‘castrated;’<BR>caillim, ‘I geld, castrate, destroy;’ cailleadh, ‘emas-<BR>culation.’]<BR>—क्लीब-ता, f. or क्लीब-त्व, अम्, n. impo-<BR>tence, the being neuter.<BR>—क्लीब-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. similar to a eunuch.<BR>—क्लीब-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. the<BR>neuter gender.<BR>—क्लीव-वत्, ind. like a base man,<BR>like a weak-minded, effeminate person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैब्य|क्लैब्यं
क्लैब्य or क्लैव्य, अम्, n. absence of virility,<BR>impotence, unmanly behaviour, unmanliness, weak-<BR>ness, timidity, cowardice; the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लु
क्लु क्लु, cl. 1. A. क्लवते, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश्
क्लेश् क्लेश्, cl. 1. A. क्लेशते, चिक्लेशे, क्लेशि-<BR>तुम्, to speak articulately; to impede or<BR>obstruct; to strike, kill; to distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश क्लेश. See under rt. क्लिश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैतकिक|क्लैतकिकं
क्लैतकिक क्लैतकिक, अम्, n. a fermented<BR>liquor prepared from the root of the plant Klītaka<BR>(क्लीतकिका?), wine, spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैब्य|क्लैब्यं
क्लैब्य क्लैब्य or क्लैव्य. See under क्लीब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोम|क्लोमं
क्लोम क्लोम, अम्, n. or क्लोमन्, आ, अ, m. n.<BR>(in the earlier language m.; in the later n.), the<BR>bladder; the lungs, the right lung; bile (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोश|क्लोशः
क्लोश क्लोश, अस्, m., Ved. = क्रोश, calling<BR>out to; (Sāy.) fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्व
क्व क्व, ind. (fr. 1. कु; according to Pāṇ.<BR>V. 3, 12, VII. 2, 104, formed first fr. किम् and then<BR>fr. the substitute कु with affix अत्), where? in what<BR>place? whither? how? when? (rarely) how much<BR>less! [cf. कुतस्]; connected with the particles इद्,<BR>स्विद्, नु, &c., in the same manner as 2. क, q. v.<BR>(e. g. क्व नु ते क्षत्रियाः शूराः, where now are<BR>those Kṣatriya heroes ?); क्व appears to be used as<BR>a loc. of 2. क in Manu X. 66. (e. g. क्व श्रेयस्-<BR>त्वम्, in whom is the preference?); क्व with भू,<BR>अस्, or गत, may denote, how is it with? what has<BR>become of? (e. g. क्व अहम् भवानि, what will<BR>become of me? क्व गतस् तव मय्य् अनुरागः,<BR>what has become of your affection for me?), or क्व<BR>alone may have the same meaning (e. g. क्व सुखम्,<BR>where is happiness? i. e. there is no such thing as<BR>happiness); क्व — क्व or कुत्र — क्व implies ex-<BR>cessive incongruity, where is this? where is that?<BR>how distant is this from that, how little does this<BR>agree with that (e. g. क्व शूर्य-प्रभवो वंशः<BR>क्व च अल्प-विषया मतिः, how can my limited<BR>intellect describe the solar race?); क्वापि (क्व अपि),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">Page0264-a+ 74</a>]<BR>anywhere, somewhere, to some place, to any place,<BR>in a certain place; sometimes; क्व च, anywhere,<BR>somewhere, at any time; क्व च न, anywhere<BR>(originally negative); न क्वचन, nowhere; क्व-<BR>चिद्, anywhere, somewhere, to any place, in a certain<BR>place; in a certain case, sometimes; at some time,<BR>once upon a time; क्वचिद् — क्वचिद्, here — there,<BR>here and there, in various places; now — then, now<BR>and then; न क्वचिद्, nowhere, never, by no means;<BR>यत्र क्वापि or यत्र क्वच, wherever, whereso-<BR>ever, to whatsoever place, anywhere; यत्र क्व-<BR>चन, to whatsoever place, hither and thither, any-<BR>where; whenever, at any time, when, in any case or<BR>matter whatever; यत्र क्व वाथ — तत्र तत्रापि,<BR>wherever — there.<BR>—क्व-जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, where<BR>born?<BR>—क्व-निवास, अस्, आ, अम्, where dwelling?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वत्य
क्वत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, or क्वत्यक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>of or belonging to where or what place? being<BR>where?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वङ्गु|क्वङ्गुः
क्वङ्गु क्वङ्गु, उस्, m. = कङ्गु, a sort of<BR>Panic, Panicum Italicum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण्
क्वण् क्वण्, cl. 1. P. क्वणति, चक्वाण,<BR>क्वणितुम्, to sound; to hum (as a bee);<BR>to make any sound; to tinkle: Caus. क्वणयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to sound, to make sound, to twang,<BR>to produce a sound with anything; e. g. नूपुरैः,<BR>with anklet ornaments; [cf. Lat. cano; Goth. hana,<BR>‘a cock.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण|क्वणः
क्वण, अस्, m. the sound or tone of any musical<BR>instrument; sound in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणत्
क्वणत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणन|क्वणनं|क्वणनः
क्वणन, अम्, n. sounding, the sound of any<BR>musical instrument; (अस्), m. a small earthen pot or<BR>boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणित|क्वणितं
क्वणित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, twanged (as a<BR>stringed instrument); (अम्), n. sound, twang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाण|क्वाणः
क्वाण, अस्, m. the sound of a musical instrument;<BR>sound in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथ्
क्वथ् क्वथ्, cl. 1. P. क्वथति, चक्वाथ,<BR>क्वथिष्यति, अक्वथीत्, क्वथितुम्, to<BR>boil, stew, decoct, prepare by heat; to digest: Caus.<BR>क्वाथयति, -यितुम्, to cause to boil, to boil, decoct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथ|क्वथः
क्वथ, अस्, m. a decoction, an extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथन|क्वथनं
क्वथन, अम्, n. boiling, decocting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथित|क्वथितः
क्वथित, अस्, आ, अम्, boiled, decocted, stewed,<BR>digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथ|क्वाथः
क्वाथ, अस्, m. a decoction, any solution or infusion<BR>prepared with a continued or gentle heat; the mixture<BR>of the materials for a decoction; pain, sorrow, cala-<BR>mity, distress.<BR>—क्वाथोद्भव (˚थ-उद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced by boiling; (अम्), n. blue vitriol used<BR>as a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वधःस्थ
क्वधःस्थ क्व्-अधः-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. कु-<BR>अधस्-स्थ), Ved. standing below on the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वयि
क्वयि क्वयि, इस्, m., Ved. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वल
क्वल क्वल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), Ved. a<BR>substance used for coagulating other substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाचित्क
क्वाचित्क क्वाचित्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्व-चित्),<BR>met with somewhere or occasionally; rare, un-<BR>common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथि
क्वाथि क्वाथि, इस्, m., Ved. an epithet of<BR>Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वापि
क्वापि क्वापि, ind. somewhere, &c. See क्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वेल्
क्वेल् क्वेल्, cl. 1. P. क्वेलति, to shake or<BR>move; (a less correct form for क्ष्वेल्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्शा
क्शा क्शा, a root forming, according to<BR>native grammarians, some tenses of ख्या<BR>and चक्ष् (e. g. the Fut. क्शास्यति; Inf. क्शातुम्;<BR>Aor. अक्शासीत्, अक्शास्त; Perf. चक्शे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष|क्षः
क्ष क्ष, अस्, m. (fr. 4. क्षि), destruction; loss,<BR>disappearance; destruction of the world; lightning; a<BR>field; the protector or cultivator of a field, a peasant,<BR>a husbandman; a demon or Rakṣas; the fourth in-<BR>carnation of Viṣṇu as the man-lion or नर-सिंह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षज्
क्षज् क्षज् or क्षञ्ज्, cl. 1. A. क्षजते<BR>or क्षञ्जते, चक्षञ्जे, क्षञ्जितुम्, to<BR>go, approach; to give; cl. 10. P. क्षञ्जयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to live in distress; to live in pain or want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण्
क्षण् क्षण्, क्षणन. See क्षन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण|क्षणं|क्षणः
क्षण क्षण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be a<BR>corruption of ईक्षण, a glance, and not used in the<BR>earlier literature; native lexicographers make this<BR>word m. only), any instantaneous point of time, an<BR>instant, the twinkling of an eye, a moment (e. g.<BR>क्षणम्, acc., or क्षणेन, inst. for an instant, in<BR>a moment; क्षणात्, abl. after an instant, immedi-<BR>ately, directly, at once; क्षणे क्षणे, every instant,<BR>every moment; तत्-क्षणम्, that very moment,<BR>in that same moment, immediately; तत्-क्षणात्,<BR>immediately upon that); a moment regarded as a<BR>measure of time, equal to thirty Kalas or four minutes,<BR>or according to other authorities equal to (4/5) or (2/3) (4/5)<BR>seconds; a leisure moment, a vacant instant, leisure,<BR>(क्षणं कृ, to have leisure for, wait patiently for;<BR>cf. कृत-क्षण); a fit or suitable moment, an<BR>opportunity, (क्षणं कृ or दा, to give an oppor-<BR>tunity); a festival; a certain day of the fortnight, as<BR>the full moon, change of the moon, &c.; dependance,<BR>servitude; the centre, the middle.<BR>—क्षण-क्षेप,<BR>अस्, m. a momentary delay.<BR>—क्षण-द, अस्, m. an<BR>astrologer; (आ), f. night (giving leisure); turmeric;<BR>(अम्), n. night-blindness; water.<BR>—क्षणदा-कर,<BR>अस्, m. the moon.<BR>—क्षणदा-चर, अस्, ई, m. f. a<BR>night-walker, a Rakṣas, a fiend, a goblin.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>णदान्ध्य (˚द-आन्˚), अम्, n. night-blindness, nycta-<BR>lopsis; [cf. क्षपान्ध्य, नक्तान्ध्य.]<BR>—क्षण-<BR>दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, momentarily visible, seen for<BR>an instant.<BR>—क्षण-द्युति, इस्, f. momentary flash,<BR>lightning; [cf. अचिर-द्युति and क्षण-प्रभा.]<BR>—क्षण-निश्वास, अस्, m. a porpoise, the Gangetic<BR>porpoise.<BR>—क्षण-प्रकाशा, f. lightning.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>ण-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, gleaming or flashing for an<BR>instant; (आ), f. lightning.<BR>—क्षण-भङ्गुर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, perishing in an instant, transient, frail, perish-<BR>able.<BR>—क्षण-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, momentary, short-<BR>lived.<BR>—क्षण-मात्रम्, ind. for an instant merely,<BR>only for a moment.<BR>—क्षण-मात्रानुरागिन् (˚त्र-<BR>अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, one whose affection lasts only a mo-<BR>ment.<BR>—क्षण-रामिन्, ई, m. a pigeon.<BR>—क्षण-<BR>विघ्न, अम्, n. a momentary hindrance.<BR>—क्षण-<BR>विध्वंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, collapsing or perishing in a<BR>moment; (ई), m. the name of a sect of atheistic<BR>philosophers who deny the continued identity of any<BR>part of nature, and maintain that the universe perishes<BR>and undergoes a new creation every instant.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>णान्तर (˚ण-अन्˚), अम्, n. the interval of a moment;<BR>(ए), ind. after a little while, the next moment, there-<BR>upon.<BR>—क्षणार्ध (˚ण-अर्˚), अम्, n. half the<BR>measure of time called Kṣaṇa, half a moment, a<BR>small space of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिक|क्षणिकः
क्षणिक, अस्, आ, अम्, momentary, transient; (आ),<BR>f. lightning.<BR>—क्षणिक-त्व, अम्, n. momentary<BR>duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणित
क्षणित, अस्, आ, अम्, having a leisure moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिन्
क्षणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a leisure moment;<BR>momentary, transient; (इनी), f. the night; [cf.<BR>क्षण-दा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणतु|क्षणतुः
क्षणतु क्षणतु, &c. See under rt. क्षन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तृ
क्षत्तृ क्षत्तृ. See under rt. क्षद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्र|क्षत्त्रं|क्षत्त्रः|क्षत्रं|क्षत्रः
क्षत्र क्षत्र, अम्, अस्, n. m. (probably fr.<BR>rt. 1. क्षि; the m. form does not appear to occur),<BR>dominion, supremacy, power, might (whether human<BR>or supernatural, in the Veda especially applied to the<BR>power of Varuṇa-Mitra and Indra); government,<BR>governing body, the military or reigning order (the<BR>members of which in the earliest times, as represented<BR>by the Vedic hymns, were generally called Rājanya,<BR>not Kṣatriya; afterwards, when the difference be-<BR>tween Brahman and Kṣatra or the priestly and civil<BR>authorities became more distinct, the reigning or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">Page0264-c+ 80</a>]<BR>military caste accepted the title Kṣatriya); a man<BR>of the second or Kṣatriya caste, a warrior, a soldier<BR>(in this sense fancifully derived in Raghu. II. 53. fr.<BR>क्षतात् त्र fr. rt. त्रै, i. e. a preserver from injury);<BR>(ई), f. a woman of the second caste; the rank of a<BR>member of the reigning or military order, the<BR>authority of the second caste; wealth; water; the<BR>body; N. of a plant, = तगर; [cf. तुवि-क्षत्र,<BR>देव-क्षत्र, &c.]<BR>—क्षत्र-धर्म, अस्, m.<BR>the duty of a Kṣatriya, bravery, military conduct.<BR>—क्षत्र-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having the duties of a<BR>soldier or of the second caste; (आ), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—क्षत्रधर्मानुग (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>following or observing the duty of a soldier.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>त्र-धृति, इस्, f. the support of supreme power; N.<BR>of a particular part of the Rāja-sūya ceremony.<BR>—क्षत्र-प, अस्, m. a governor, a Satrap (a word<BR>found on coins).<BR>—क्षत्र-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the<BR>possessor of dominion.<BR>—क्षत्र-बन्धु, उस्, ऊस् or<BR>उस्, उ, one who belongs to the military order or second<BR>caste; (उस्), m. a member of the Kṣatriya caste; a<BR>mere Kṣatriya, i. e. a Kṣatriya by birth but not by<BR>his actions (a term of abuse).<BR>—क्षत्रबन्धु-वत्,<BR>ind. like a warrior.<BR>—क्षत्र-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>one who holds or confers dominion.<BR>—क्षत्र-<BR>योग, अस्, m., Ved. union of the princely order.<BR>—क्षत्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed with princely<BR>dignity.<BR>—क्षत्र-वनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. favourable<BR>to the princely order.<BR>—क्षत्र-वर्धन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, Ved. promoting dominion.<BR>—क्षत्र-विद्या, f.<BR>the knowledge or science possessed by the Kṣatriya<BR>or military order.<BR>—क्षत्र-वृक्ष, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a tree, = मुचुकुन्द.<BR>—क्षत्र-वृद्ध, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—क्षत्र-वृद्धि, इस्, m., N. of one<BR>of the sons of Manu Raucya.<BR>—क्षत्र-वृध्, त्,<BR>m., N. of a prince, = क्षत्र-वृद्ध.<BR>—क्षत्र-<BR>वेद, अस्, m., the Veda of the Kṣatriya or military<BR>order.<BR>—क्षत्र-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. possessing<BR>sovereignty; (Sāy.) possessed of power.<BR>—क्षत्र-<BR>सव, अस्, m., N. of a sacrificial ceremony.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>त्रायतनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. क्षत्र + आयतन),<BR>Ved. based on the Kṣatra or kingly power.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>त्रोपक्षत्र (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—क्षत्रौजस् (˚र-ओज्˚), आस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिण
क्षत्रिण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिन्
क्षत्रिन्, ई, m. a man of the military order or<BR>second caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिय|क्षत्त्रियः|क्षत्रियः
क्षत्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, governing, endowed with<BR>sovereignty; (अस्), m. a member of the military<BR>or reigning order which in later time constituted the<BR>second caste; (आ), f. a woman of the military<BR>order or of the second caste; (ई), f. the wife of a<BR>man of the second caste; (अम्), n. the power or<BR>rank of this order.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-जाति, इस्, f. the mili-<BR>tary tribe or caste.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-ता, f. or क्षत्रिय-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the order or rank of a Kṣatriya.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-धर्म, अस्, m. the duty or occupa-<BR>tion of the warrior-tribe, war, government, &c.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having the duties<BR>of a soldier or of the second caste.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-<BR>प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, mostly consisting of the military<BR>tribe.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-मर्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying<BR>or destroyer of Kṣatriyas.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-राज, अस्, m.<BR>the chief of Kṣatriyas.<BR>—क्षत्रियर्षभ (˚य-<BR>ऋष्˚), अस्, m. best of Kṣatriyas.<BR>—क्षत्रिय-<BR>हण, अस्, m. one who destroys the military caste.<BR>—क्षत्रियान्तकर (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, m. one who<BR>destroys the Kṣatriyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियका
क्षत्रियका or इका, f. a woman belonging to the<BR>military or reigning order, a woman of the second<BR>caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियाणी
क्षत्रियाणी, f. a woman belonging to the mili-<BR>tary caste; the wife of a man of the second caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद्
क्षद् क्षद्, cl. 1. A., Ved. क्षदते,<BR>चक्षदे, to cut, dissect, cut to pieces,<BR>divide; to kill; to carve (meat), to distribute (food);<BR>to take (food), to consume, eat. (As a Sautra root<BR>क्षद् means ‘to cover, protect, shelter.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तृ
क्षत्तृ, ता, m. one who cuts anything, one who<BR>carves or distributes; an attendant; a door-keeper,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">Page0265-a+ 78</a>]<BR>a porter; a charioteer, a coachman; [cf. अनु-क्षत्-<BR>तृ]; one who fights from a chariot; the son of a<BR>Śūdra man and a Kṣatriya woman, or the son of a<BR>Kṣatriya man and a Śūdra woman (called Ugra<BR>in Manu X. 9), or the son of a Śūdra man and<BR>Vaiśya woman (called Āyogava in Manu X. 12);<BR>the son of a female slave; (the proper employment of<BR>a Kṣattṛ is said to be catching animals that live in<BR>holes); a N. of Vidura as the son of a female slave,<BR>his father being the celebrated Vyāsa (see Mahā-bh.<BR>1. 7381); an epithet of Brahmā; a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदत्
क्षदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, carving, dividing, tearing;<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदन|क्षदनं
क्षदन, अम्, n. the act of carving, dividing,<BR>tearing; eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद्मन्
क्षद्मन्, अ, n., Ved. a carving knife; pieces of<BR>food cut off or carved; (according to Schol.) water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्
क्षन् क्षन् or क्षण्, cl. 8. P. A. क्ष-<BR>णोति, -णुते, चक्षाण, चक्षणे, क्ष-<BR>णिष्यति, -ते, अक्षणीत्, क्षणितुम्, P. to hurt,<BR>injure, wound, break; A. to hurt one's self, be injured<BR>or wounded: Caus. क्षाणयति, -यितुम्: Desid.<BR>चिक्षणिषति, -ते: Intens. चङ्क्षण्यते, चङ्क्-<BR>षन्ति; [cf. Gr. καίνω, κανῶ; καίνυται = क्षणुते;<BR>ξαίνω; perhaps also σίνομαι for ξίνομαι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणतु|क्षणतुः
क्षणतु, उस्, m. a wound or sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणन|क्षणनं
क्षणन, अम्, n. hurting, injuring; killing,<BR>slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणनु
क्षणनु, उस्, m. a wound, a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत|क्षतं
क्षत, अस्, आ, अम्, wounded, hurt, hit, injured,<BR>broken, torn, rent, destroyed, impaired, violated;<BR>diminished, trodden or broken down; (अम्), n. a<BR>hurt, wound, sore, contusion.<BR>—क्षत-कास, अस्, m.<BR>a cough produced by an injury; [cf. क्षत-ज, &c.]<BR>—क्षत-घ्न, अस्, m., N. of a plant, commonly<BR>Kukuraśoṅkhā, Conyza Lacera; (आ or ई), f. a kind<BR>of insect; lac, the animal dye.<BR>—क्षत-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced by a wound or injury of any kind (e. g.<BR>कास, a kind of cough); (अम्), n. blood; pus, matter.<BR>—क्षत-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, dimmed, obscured (as<BR>light or power).<BR>—क्षत-पुण्य-लेश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the stock of merit exhausted.<BR>—क्षत-योनि,<BR>इस्, f. a woman who has been violated, one no longer<BR>a virgin.<BR>—क्षत-विक्षत, अस्, आ, अम्, mangled,<BR>covered with cuts and wounds.<BR>—क्षत-विध्वंसिन्,<BR>ई, m. a sort of pot-herb, Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR>—क्षत-वृत्ति, इस्, f. destitution, the being without<BR>the means of support, living on what one can get.<BR>—क्षत-व्रण, अस्, m. a sore produced by an<BR>injury.<BR>—क्षत-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, a violator of a<BR>vow or religious engagement.<BR>—क्षत-हर, अम्,<BR>n. Agallochum or Aloe wood.<BR>—क्षतारि (˚त-अरि),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, victorious, triumphant.<BR>—क्षतोत्थ (˚त-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced by injury.<BR>—क्षतोदर<BR>(˚त-उद्˚), अम्, n. flux, dysentery.<BR>—क्षतोद्भव<BR>(˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced by injury; (अम्),<BR>n. (?) blood; [cf. क्षत-ज.]<BR>—क्षतौजस् (˚त-<BR>ओज्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, weakened, reduced, impaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षति|क्षतिः
क्षति, इस्, f. injury, hurt, a wound; destruction;<BR>damage, disadvantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् 1. क्षप्, cl. 1. P. A. क्षपति, -ते, to<BR>be abstinent, to fast, to do penance: Caus.<BR>क्षपयति, -यितुम्, to regret sorrowfully, miss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण|क्षपणः
1. क्षपण, अस्, m. a Buddhist mendicant; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), shameless, impudent?; (अम्), n. abstinence,<BR>chastisement of the body, defilement, impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणक|क्षपणकः
क्षपणक, अस्, m. a mendicant, especially a<BR>Buddhist mendicant, who wears no garments; also<BR>a Jaina mendicant; (अस्), m., N. of an author<BR>supposed to have lived at the court of king Vikra-<BR>māditya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् 2. क्षप्, cl. 10. P. क्षपयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to send, throw, cast, direct, &c.;<BR>[cf. Goth. skapa.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपयत्
क्षपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, casting, sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपित
क्षपित, अस्, आ, अम्, sent, cast, directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् 3. क्षप्. See Caus. of rt. 4. क्षि,<BR>‘to destroy.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
4. क्षप्, प्, f., Ved. night; a measure of time<BR>equivalent to a whole day of twenty-four hours;<BR>darkness; water; क्षपः or क्षपा, ind. at<BR>night; [cf. Lat. crepus-culum; Gr. κνέφος, κνέφας.]<BR>—क्षपोत्यय (˚पस्-अत्˚), अस्, m. the end of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण|क्षपणः
2. क्षपण, अस्, आ, अम्, destructive, one who<BR>destroys; (अम्), n. destroying, diminishing, suppress-<BR>ing, expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपा
क्षपा, f. night (Ved. only used in inst. pl.<BR>क्षपाभिस्); turmeric.<BR>—क्षपा-कर, अस्, m.<BR>‘making the night,’ the moon.<BR>—क्षपा-घन,<BR>अस्, m. a dark cloud or dark nocturnal clouds.<BR>—क्ष-<BR>पा-चर, अस्, m. a night-walker; a fiend, a goblin.<BR>—क्षपाट (˚पा-अट), अस्, m. a night-walker; a<BR>Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>—क्षपा-नाथ, अस्,<BR>m. the moon.<BR>—क्षपान्त (˚पा-अन्˚), अस्, m. dawn,<BR>day-break.<BR>—क्षपान्ध्य (˚पा-आन्˚), अम्, n. night-<BR>blindness, nyctalopsis; [cf. क्षणदान्ध्य, नक्-<BR>तान्ध्य.]<BR>—क्षपा-पति, इस्, m. the moon; cam-<BR>phor.<BR>—क्षपाह (˚पा-अहन्), अम्, n. a day and night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणी
क्षपणी क्षपणी, f. = क्षेपणी, an oar, a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण्यु|क्षपण्युः
क्षपण्यु क्षपण्यु, उस्, m. an offence, a<BR>transgression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
क्षम् 1. क्षम्, cl. 1. A., 4. P. क्षमते,<BR>क्षाम्यति (ep. also 1. P. and Ved. 2. P.<BR>क्षमति, क्षमिति), चक्षमे, चक्षाम, क्ष-<BR>मिष्यते, -ति, and क्षंस्यते, -ति, अक्षमिष्ट,<BR>अक्षंस्त, अक्षमत्, क्षमितुम् and क्षन्तुम्,<BR>to be patient or composed, to suppress anger, keep quiet;<BR>to submit to (with dat.); to bear patiently, endure, put<BR>up with, suffer; to pardon, forgive (with gen. or dat.<BR>of the person, e. g. क्षमस्व तद् मे, forgive me<BR>that); to allow, permit, suffer; to resist; to be com-<BR>petent or able to do anything (with inf.): Caus.<BR>क्षमयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to ask pardon for anything<BR>(with double acc., e. g. तत् क्षमये भवन्तम्,<BR>I ask you to pardon that); to suffer or bear patiently:<BR>Desid. चिक्षमिषते, -ति, and चिक्षंसते, -ति:<BR>Intens. चङ्क्षम्यते, चङ्क्षन्ति; [cf. Goth.<BR>hramja (?); Angl. Sax. hremman, ‘to hinder,<BR>disquiet.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तव्य|क्षंतव्य
क्षन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne or endured,<BR>bearable, to be suffered or submitted to patiently, to<BR>be pardoned or forgiven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तृ|क्षंतृ
क्षन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, pardoning, bearing patiently,<BR>submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
2. क्षम्, f. (making क्षास् in the nom. case),<BR>Ved. the ground, the earth, χθών; [cf. χαμαί. &c.]<BR>—क्ष-पावत्, आन्, m., Ved. an earth-protector,<BR>a ruler, a governor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम, अस्, आ, अम्, patient; enduring, suffering,<BR>bearing, submissive, resisting; adequate, competent, able,<BR>fit for (with inf. or at the end of a compound, वयं<BR>त्यक्तुं क्षमाः, we are able to quit; गमन-<BR>क्षम, able to go); friendly; favourable; bear-<BR>able, tolerable; fit, appropriate, becoming suitable,<BR>proper for (with gen. of the person, e. g. क्ष-<BR>मं कौरवाणाम्, proper for the Kauravas; or with<BR>inf., e. g. न स क्षमः कोपयितुम्, he is not a<BR>fit object for anger); (अस्), m. a N. of Śiva, ‘the<BR>patient;’ (आ), f. patience, forbearance, indulgence; per-<BR>sonified as a daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Pulaha;<BR>resistance; the earth; an epithet of Durgā; N. of a<BR>female shepherd; the tree Acacia Catechu (खदिर);<BR>N. of a species of the Atijayatī metre [cf. उत्पलिनी];<BR>night (wrong form for क्षपा); (अम्), n. propriety,<BR>fitness; [cf. Hib. cam, ‘strong, stout, mighty; power,<BR>might;’ cama, ‘brave.’]<BR>—क्षम-ता, f. or क्ष-<BR>म-त्व, अम्, n. ability, fitness, capability.<BR>—क्षम-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, knowing what is proper or right.<BR>—क्षमा-कल्याण, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Jinalābhasūri, who composed 1794 A. D. a com-<BR>mentary on the Jīva-vicāra.<BR>—क्षमा-तल, अम्, n.<BR>the earth.<BR>—क्षमा-दंश, अस्, m., N. of a tree,<BR>= शिग्रु.<BR>—क्षमान्वित (˚मा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>endowed with patience, patient, enduring, forgiving.<BR>—क्षमा-पति, इस्, m. lord of the earth, a king.<BR>—क्षमापन्न (˚मा-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, forbearing,<BR>patient.<BR>—क्षमा-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, very patient, for-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">Page0265-c+ 77</a>]<BR>bearing.<BR>—क्षमा-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, patient; (क्), m.<BR>a king, a prince.<BR>—क्षमा-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, en-<BR>dowed with patience, patient, enduring.<BR>—क्षमा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, patient, enduring, forbearing; (अती),<BR>f., N. of the wife of Nidhi-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमणीय
क्षमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be suffered, to be<BR>patiently borne; to be pardoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमा
क्षमा (inst. case of 2. क्षम्), on the earth, on<BR>the floor (included by Pāṇini among the indeclinables<BR>with स्वर्, दिवा, &c.); [cf. Gr. χαμαί, χαμᾶ-ζε,<BR>χαμά-θεν, χθαμαλός.]<BR>—क्षमा-चर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. being in the ground or under the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमापय
क्षमापय, nom. P. A. -पयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>to ask any one's (acc.) pardon, to beg forgiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमितव्य
क्षमितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be endured, to be<BR>patiently borne, to be pardoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमितृ
क्षमितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, patient, enduring, for-<BR>bearing, indulgent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमिन्
क्षमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, patient, enduring, forbearing,<BR>indulgent; capable, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्य
क्षम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the earth,<BR>terrestrial; χθόνιος.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्त|क्षांत|क्षान्तः
क्षान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, borne, endured; patient,<BR>enduring; (अस्), m., N. of a man; of a hunter; epi-<BR>thet of Śiva [cf. क्षम]; (आ), f. the earth, ‘the<BR>patient one.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्ति|क्षांति|क्षांतिः|क्षान्तिः
क्षान्ति, इस्, f. patience, forbearance, endurance,<BR>indulgence, patient waiting for anything.<BR>—क्षान्ति-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, patient, enduring, indulgent.<BR>—क्षान्ति-वादिन्, ई, m., N. of a Ṛṣi; N. of<BR>Śākya-muni in one of his former births.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तु|क्षांतु|क्षान्तुः
क्षान्तु, उस्, उस्, उ, patient, enduring; (उस्), m.<BR>a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम्य
क्षाम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne; to be pardoned<BR>or overlooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमुद
क्षमुद क्षमुद, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a<BR>particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्प्
क्षम्प् क्षम्प्, cl. 1. or 10. P. क्षम्पति<BR>or क्षम्पयति, -यितुम्, to suffer, bear;<BR>[cf. 1. क्षम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
क्षय क्षय. See under rt. 2. क्षि and rt.<BR>4. क्षि, p. 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयथु|क्षयथुः
क्षयथु क्षयथु, उस्, m. cough; (a wrong<BR>form for क्षवथु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयद्वीर
क्षयद्वीर क्षयद्-वीर. See under 1. क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर्
क्षर् क्षर्, cl. 1. P. क्षरति, चक्षार,<BR>क्षरिष्यति, अक्षारीत्, क्षरितुम् (ep.<BR>cl. 1. A. क्षरते, Ved. cl. 2. P. क्षरिति, Ved.<BR>inf. क्षरध्यै), to flow, stream, glide; to flow<BR>away; to stream forth; pour out (either in active<BR>or neuter sense); to drop, distil, trickle, ooze,<BR>run; to melt away, wane, perish, be destroyed; to<BR>fall or slip from, to be deprived of (with abl.):<BR>Caus. क्षारयति, -यितुम्: Desid. चिक्षरिषति:<BR>Intens. चाक्षर्यते, चाक्षर्ति; [cf. Lat. scateo ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, melting away, perishable;<BR>(अस्), m. a cloud; (अम्), n. water; a body.<BR>—क्षर-<BR>ज or क्षरे-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by distillation.<BR>—क्षर-पत्त्रा, f., N. of a plant, = द्रोण-पुष्पी.<BR>—क्षर-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, mutable, dissoluble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरक
क्षरक, अस्, इका, अम्, pouring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरण|क्षरणं
क्षरण, अम्, n. the act of flowing, trickling,<BR>distilling, dropping (e. g. अङ्गुली-क्षरण, perspira-<BR>tion of the fingers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरत्
क्षरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flowing, running, trickling,<BR>oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरित
क्षरित, अस्, आ, अम्, dropped, liquefied, oozed,<BR>trickling, flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरिन्
क्षरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, flowing, dropping, trickling;<BR>(ई), m. the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षार|क्षारं|क्षारः
क्षार, अस्, आ, अम्, caustic, biting, corrosive, acid,<BR>pungent, saline (according to some in these senses fr.<BR>rt. क्षै), anything converted to alkali or ashes by<BR>distillation; (अस्), m. juice, essence; treacle, molasses;<BR>any corrosive or acid or saline substance, especially an<BR>alkali such as soda or potash; caustic alkali, one<BR>species of cautery; glass; a rogue, a cheat; (अम्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">Page0266-a+ 77</a>]<BR>n. a factitious or medicinal salt, commonly black<BR>salt [cf. विड्-लवण and कृष्ण-लवण]; water.<BR>—क्षार-कर्दम, अस्, m. a pool of saline or acid<BR>mud; N. of a hell.<BR>—क्षार-कर्मन्, अ, n. apply-<BR>ing caustic alkali (Lapis Infernalis) to proud flesh &c.;<BR>or applying acid remedies in general.<BR>—क्षार-<BR>कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be treated with caustic alkali.<BR>—क्षार-तैल, अम्, n. oil cooked with alkaline<BR>ingredients.<BR>—क्षार-त्रय or क्षार-त्रितय,<BR>अम्, n. natron, saltpetre, and borax.<BR>—क्षार-दला,<BR>f. a kind of pot-herb, = चिल्ली.<BR>—क्षार-द्रु, उस्, m.<BR>the tree Bignonia Suaveolens; [cf. घण्टा-पाटलि.]<BR>—क्षार-नदी, f. a river in hell, the water of which<BR>is alkaline.<BR>—क्षार-पत्त्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>or क्षार-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. the pot-herb Cheno-<BR>podium Album.<BR>—क्षार-पाल, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Ṛṣi.<BR>—क्षार-भूमि, इस्, f. a saline soil.<BR>—क्षार-मध्य, अस्, m. the plant Achyranthes<BR>Aspera [cf. अपामार्ग]; its alkaline ashes make it<BR>useful in washing clothes.<BR>—क्षार-मृत्तिका, f.<BR>saline soil, especially an impure sulphate of soda.<BR>—क्षार-मेलक, अस्, m. an alkaline substance.<BR>—क्षार-मेह, अस्, m. a morbid state of the urine,<BR>in which its smell and taste resemble that of potash.<BR>—क्षार-रस, अस्, m. a saline or alkaline flavour.<BR>—क्षार-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the tree Bignonia Suave-<BR>olens [cf. क्षार-द्रु]; any tree yielding abundant<BR>potash.<BR>—क्षार-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. the tree Butea<BR>Frondosa; also = क्षार-वृक्ष; (अम्), n. alkaline<BR>earth; [cf. वज्र-क्षार.]<BR>—क्षार-षट्क, अम्,<BR>n. six kinds of trees distinguished by their juice, as<BR>the Butea Frondosa, Grislea Tomentosa, Achyranthes<BR>Aspera, Cowach, Ghaṇṭā-pāṭali, Coraya.<BR>—क्षार-<BR>समुद्र, अस्, m. or क्षार-सिन्धु, उस्, m. the salt<BR>ocean.<BR>—क्षार-सूत्र, अम्, n. acid thread, applied<BR>to fistulas &c.<BR>—क्षाराक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having an artificial eye made of glass.<BR>—क्षारागद<BR>(˚र-अग्˚), अस्, m. remedy prepared by extracting the<BR>alkaline particles from the ashes of plants.<BR>—क्षा-<BR>राच्छ (˚र-अच्छ), अम्, n. sea-salt.<BR>—क्षाराञ्जन<BR>(˚र-अञ्˚), अम्, n. an alkaline unguent.<BR>—क्षा-<BR>राम्बु (˚र-अम्˚), उ, n. or क्षारोद (˚र-उद), अस्,<BR>m. or क्षारोदक (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n. an alkaline<BR>juice or fluid.<BR>—क्षाराम्बुधि (˚र-अम्˚), क्षा-<BR>रोदधि (˚र-उद्˚), इस्, m. the salt ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारक|क्षारकः
क्षारक, अस्, m. alkali; a juice, essence; a<BR>blossom, a new-blown flower or a young fruit; a<BR>bud or a multitude of young buds; a cage or basket<BR>or net for birds or fish; a washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारण|क्षारणं
क्षारण, अम्, आ, n. f. accusing of unfaithfulness;<BR>(अम्), n. converting to alkali or ashes; distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारय
क्षारय, nom. P. क्षारयति, -यितुम्, to fur-<BR>nish or mix with acid substances; to torture a person<BR>with acid substances; to speak ill of a person; to<BR>abuse, accuse, calumniate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारिका
क्षारिका, f. hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारित|क्षारितः
क्षारित, अस्, आ, अम्, distilled from saline matter,<BR>strained through alkaline ashes &c.; calumniated,<BR>falsely accused (especially of adultery), accused of a<BR>crime, guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षल्
क्षल् 1. क्षल्, cl. 1. P. क्षलति, -लितुम्,<BR>to flow; to collect; [cf. क्षर्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षल्
क्षल् 2. क्षल् (related to rt. क्षर्), cl.<BR>10. P. क्षालयति, अचिक्षलत्, -यितुम्,<BR>to wash, wash off, purify, cleanse, clean, make clean;<BR>to wipe away; [cf. Lith. skalauju, ‘to wash off;’<BR>skalbju, ‘to wash;’ Mod. Germ. spüle?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालन|क्षालनं
क्षालन, अम्, n. washing, washing off, cleansing<BR>with water; sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनीय
क्षालनीय or क्षालितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>washed, to be cleansed with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालयत्
क्षालयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, washing, cleansing,<BR>sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालित|क्षालितं
क्षालित, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed, cleaned, washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षव|क्षवः
क्षव क्षव. See under rt. 1. क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाति
क्षाति क्षाति, इस्, f. (fr. क्षै), Ved. singeing,<BR>scorching, heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्त्र
क्षात्त्र क्षात्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. क्षत्तृ), Ved.<BR>a community or number of attendants or servants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्र
क्षात्र क्षात्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्षत्र), be-<BR>longing or relating to or peculiar to the second or<BR>military tribe; (अम्), n. the second or military tribe;<BR>the dignity of a ruler or governor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्रि|क्षात्रिः
क्षात्रि, इस्, m. the son of a man of the second<BR>caste (by a woman of another caste ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्त|क्षांत|क्षान्तः
क्षान्त क्षान्त, &c. See under 1. क्षम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम|क्षामः
क्षाम क्षाम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. क्षै),<BR>scorched, singed; dried up, emaciated, wasted, fallen<BR>away, thin, slim, slender; weak, debilitated, infirm,<BR>slight.<BR>—क्षाम-ता, f. or क्षाम-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>emaciation, thinness, slenderness; debility.<BR>—क्षा-<BR>म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. scorching, singeing, dry-<BR>ing up; epithet of Agni; (ती), f., scil. इष्टि, N. of a<BR>particular sacrificial ceremony.<BR>—क्षामास्य (˚म-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. any diet or any state of the body (as<BR>menstruation) incompatible with a particular medical<BR>treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामन्
क्षामन् क्षामन्, अ, n. (occurring only in<BR>nom., acc., loc. sing.), Ved. earth, soil, ground; [cf. 2.<BR>क्षम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामाप्रस्थ
क्षामाप्रस्थ क्षामा-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षार|क्षारं|क्षारः
क्षार क्षार. See under rt. क्षर्, p. 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालन|क्षालनं
क्षालन क्षालन, &c. See under 2. क्षल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षास्
क्षास् क्षास्, nom. case of 2. क्षम्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि 1. क्षि, cl. 1. P., Ved. क्षयति (only<BR>the pres. seems to occur), to possess, have<BR>power over, rule, govern, be master of (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयत्
क्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, possessing, ruling, govern-<BR>ing.<BR>—क्षयद्-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ruling or<BR>governing men; an epithet of Indra, Rudra, and<BR>Pūṣan; (Sāy. as if fr. 2. क्षि), possessed of abiding<BR>or of going heroes such as sons &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्
1. क्षित्, त्, त्, त्, ruling, a ruler, a governor, a<BR>sovereign, (used in comp., e. g. मही-क्षित्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि 2. क्षि, cl. 2. 6. P., Ved. क्षेति,<BR>क्षियति, चिक्षाय, क्षेष्यति, क्षेतुम्,<BR>to abide, stay, dwell, reside (used especially of an<BR>undisturbed or secret residence); to inhabit; to re-<BR>main; to be quiet; to go, move, approach: Caus.<BR>क्षययति or क्षेपयति, -यितुम्, to make a<BR>person live quietly; to pacify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
1. क्षय, अस्, m. (for 2. see under rt. 4. क्षि<BR>below), an abode, residence, habitation, dwelling-<BR>place, seat, house [cf. उरु-क्षय]; family, race;<BR>the house of Yama, god of death; dominion (?).<BR>—क्षय-तरु, उस्, m. the plant Bignonia Suave-<BR>olens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयण|क्षयणः
1. क्षयण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. habitable (?); (अस्),<BR>m. a place with tranquil water; a bay, harbour (?);<BR>(अम्), n. a dwelling-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयस्
क्षयस्, अस्, n. a dwelling-place, habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
3. क्षि, इस्, f. abode, residence; going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्
2. क्षित्, त्, त्, त्, dwelling, an inhabitant, (at the end<BR>of several compounds, e. g. अन्तरिक्ष-क्षित्, an<BR>inhabitant of the air &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिता
क्षिता, f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिति|क्षितिः
1. क्षिति, इस्, f. (for 2. see under rt. 4. क्षि below),<BR>an abode, a dwelling, habitation, house, residence<BR>[cf. उरु-क्षिति]; the earth, the soil of the earth;<BR>(अयस्), f. pl., Ved. settlements, colonies, races of<BR>men, nations, men in general; the families of the<BR>gods.<BR>—क्षिति-कण, अस्, आ, m. f. a particle of<BR>earth, dust.<BR>—क्षिति-कम्प, अस्, m. an earthquake.<BR>—क्षिति-क्षम, अस्, m. the tree Mimosa Khayar;<BR>[cf. खदिर.]<BR>—क्षिति-क्षित्, त्, m. a ruler of the<BR>earth; a king, a prince.<BR>—क्षिति-खण्ड, अस्, m. a<BR>clod or lump of earth.<BR>—क्षिति-गर्भ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—क्षिति-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, earth-born,<BR>produced of or in the earth; (अस्), m. a tree; a kind<BR>of snail (= भू-नाग); an earth-worm; N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-c" target="_blank">Page0266-c+ 80</a>]<BR>planet Mars; an epithet of the demon Naraka; (आ),<BR>f. an epithet of Sītā, the wife of Rāma; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a circle of the sky.<BR>—क्षिति-जन्तु, उस्, m. a kind<BR>of snail (= भू-नाग); an earth-worm.<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>तल, अम्, n. the surface of the earth, the region<BR>below the earth.<BR>—क्षिति-देव, अस्, m. the ‘earth-<BR>god,’ an epithet of a king.<BR>—क्षिति-देवता, f. the<BR>deity of the earth, epithet of a Brāhman.<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>धर, अस्, m. ‘earth-supporter,’ a mountain.<BR>—क्षिति-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, carrying soil or earth.<BR>—क्षिति-धेनु, उस्, f. the earth considered as a<BR>milch-cow.<BR>—क्षिति-नन्द, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—क्षिति-नाग, अस्, m. a kind of snail (= भू-नाग)<BR>or rather snail-shell; an earth-worm (?).<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of the earth,’ a king.<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>प, अस्, m. ‘earth-protector,’ a king.<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>पति, इस्, m. lord of the earth, a king, a sovereign.<BR>—क्षिति-पाल, अस्, m. ‘earth-protector,’ a king,<BR>a prince.<BR>—क्षिति-पीठ, अम्, n. the surface of the<BR>earth.<BR>—क्षिति-पुत्र, अस्, m. a son of the earth, an<BR>epithet of Naraka.<BR>—क्षिति-प्रतिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dwelling or abiding on the earth.<BR>—क्षिति-भुज्, क्,<BR>m. one who enjoys the earth, a king.<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘earth-supporter,’ a mountain; a king.<BR>—क्षिति-मण्डल, अम्, n. the earth, the globe.<BR>—क्षिति-रुह्, ट्, or क्षिति-रुह, अस्, m. a<BR>plant, a tree.<BR>—क्षिति-लव-भुज्, क्, m. one who<BR>possesses a small tract of the earth, a petty prince.<BR>—क्षिति-वदरी, f., N. of a plant, = भू-वदरी.<BR>—क्षिति-वर्धन, अस्, m. a corpse.<BR>—क्षिति-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. (patient) behaviour like that of the<BR>earth.<BR>—क्षितिवृत्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, patient like<BR>the earth.<BR>—क्षिति-व्युदास, अस्, m. a cave within<BR>the earth.<BR>—क्षिति-सुत, अस्, m. an epithet of the<BR>demon Naraka; also of the planet Mars; [cf. क्षिति-<BR>पुत्र.]<BR>—क्षितीश (˚ति-ईश), अस्, m. a ruler of the<BR>earth, a king.<BR>—क्षितीश-वंशावली-चरित, अम्, n.<BR>‘genealogy and history of the kings,’ title of a work<BR>composed in the last century, being a family chronicle<BR>of the viceroys of a part of Bengal.<BR>—क्षितीश्वर<BR>(˚ति-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a king.<BR>—क्षित्य्-अदिति, इस्, f. the<BR>Aditi of the earth, an epithet of Devakī, the mother<BR>of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्वन्
क्षित्वन्, आ, m. air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि 4. क्षि, cl. 1. 5. 9. P. क्षयति, क्षि-<BR>णोति, क्षिणाति, चिक्षाय, क्षेष्यति, अक्षै-<BR>षीत्, क्षेतुम्, to destroy, corrupt, ruin, to make an<BR>end of; to kill, injure: Pass. क्षीयते, to wane; to<BR>decrease; to be diminished, waste away, perish: Caus.<BR>क्षययति or क्षपयति or Ved. क्षापयति,<BR>यितुम्, to destroy, ruin, make an end of, finish; to<BR>weaken: Desid. चिक्षीषति: Intens. चेक्षीयते,<BR>चेक्षयीति, चेक्षेति; [cf. Gr. κτίννυμι?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
2. क्षय, अस्, m. (for 1. see under 2. क्षि last<BR>col.), loss, waste, wane, diminution, destruction, decay<BR>wasting or wearing away; fall (as of prices, opposed to<BR>वृद्धि, e. g. क्षयो वृद्धिश् च पण्यानाम्, the<BR>fall and rise in the price of commodities); removal;<BR>end, termination (e. g. निद्रा-क्षय, the end of<BR>sleep; दिन-क्षये, at the end of day; जीवित-<BR>क्षये, at the end of life; क्षयं या or गम्, to<BR>become less, be diminished, go to destruction, come<BR>to an end, perish); consumption, pthisis pulmonalis;<BR>sickness in general; the destruction of the universe;<BR>(in algebra) a negative quality, a minus.<BR>—क्षय-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing destruction or ruin, de-<BR>structive, ruinous, terminating; liberating from ex-<BR>istence.<BR>—क्षय-काल, अस्, m. the end of all things,<BR>the period of destruction.<BR>—क्षय-कास, अस्, m. a<BR>consumptive or phthisical cough.<BR>—क्षय-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, or क्षयङ्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing ruin or<BR>loss; destructive.<BR>—क्षय-नाशिनी, f. the plant<BR>Celtis Orientalis, = जीवन्ती (‘removing consump-<BR>tion’).<BR>—क्षय-पक्ष, अस्, m. the dark fortnight,<BR>that of the moon's wane.<BR>—क्षय-युक्ति, इस्, f. or<BR>क्षय-योग, अस्, m. necessity or opportunity of<BR>destroying.<BR>—क्षय-रोग, अस्, m. consumption.<BR>—क्षयरोगि-त्व, अम्, n. or क्षयरोगि-ता, f.<BR>consumption.<BR>—क्षय-रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, consumptive.<BR>—क्षय-वायु, उस्, m. the wind that is to blow at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">Page0267-a+ 79</a>]<BR>the end of the world.<BR>—क्षय-सम्पद्, त्, f. total<BR>loss, ruin, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयण|क्षयणः
2. क्षयण, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, annihilating,<BR>driving away, dispersing; (often at the end of com-<BR>pounds, e. g. असुर-क्षयण, पिशाच-क्षयण,<BR>&c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयथु|क्षयथुः
क्षयथु, उस्, m. consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षययितव्य
क्षययितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिन्
क्षयिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wasting, decaying, fragile;<BR>consumptive.<BR>—क्षयि-त्व, अम्, n. fragility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिष्णु
क्षयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, destroying, wasting, decay-<BR>ing, perishing; perishable, fragile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय्य|क्षय्यं
क्षय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, perishable, decaying; [cf.<BR>अ-क्षय्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
5. क्षि, इस्, f. destruction; waste, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित|क्षितः
क्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, wasted, decayed, exhausted;<BR>weakened; poor, miserable.<BR>—क्षितायुस् (˚त-आय्˚),<BR>उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. one whose life goes to an end, one<BR>whose life is forfeited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिति|क्षितिः
2. क्षिति, इस्, f. (for 1. see under rt. 2. क्षि above),<BR>loss, destruction; wane; a period of the destruction<BR>of the universe, the end of the world; a kind of<BR>perfume = रोचना; (इस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिया
क्षिया, f. loss, waste, destruction; offence against<BR>the customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण, अस्, आ, अम्, diminished, wasted, expended,<BR>worn away; lost, destroyed; injured, broken, torn;<BR>subdued, suppressed; thin, emaciated, feeble; delicate,<BR>slender, poor, miserable.<BR>—क्षीण-गति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>with slackened or diminished motion or progress.<BR>—क्षीण-तमस्, आस्, m., N. of a Vihāra.<BR>—क्षीण-<BR>ता, f. or क्षीण-त्व, अम्, n. the state of wasting<BR>away, diminution, decay; the state of being worn<BR>away or injured; emaciation, thinness; slenderness.<BR>—क्षीण-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, impoverished.<BR>—क्षी-<BR>ण-पाप, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose sins are destroyed;<BR>one who is purified after having suffered the con-<BR>sequences of sin.<BR>—क्षीण-पुण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose merit is lost; one who has enjoyed the fruits<BR>of merit and is doomed to labour for more in another<BR>birth.<BR>—क्षीण-मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, slender-waisted.<BR>—क्षीण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, wasted, decayed.<BR>—क्षी-<BR>ण-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, inhabiting a dilapidated house;<BR>(ई), m. a dove or pigeon.<BR>—क्षीण-विक्रान्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has lost courage, destitute of prowess.<BR>—क्षीण-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, out of employ, having<BR>no means of subsistence or maintenance.<BR>—क्षीण-<BR>शक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, one whose strength is wasted, weak,<BR>impotent.<BR>—क्षीण-शरीर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a thin<BR>or emaciated body.<BR>—क्षीण-सुकृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having one's stock of merit exhausted.<BR>—क्षीणाङ्ग<BR>(˚ण-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having emaciated limbs.<BR>—क्षीणाज्य-कर्मन् (˚ण-आज्˚), आ, m. a Buddhist.<BR>—क्षीणाष्ट-कर्मन् (˚ण-अष्˚), आ, m. (with<BR>Jainas) an Arhat or inspired teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीयमाण
क्षीयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, perishing, wasting away,<BR>decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेय
क्षेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed or removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिण्
क्षिण् क्षिण्, cl. 5. P. A. क्षिणोति, -णुते,<BR>क्षेणोति, -णुते (?), to kill, to hurt, = 4.<BR>क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिद्र|क्षिद्रः
क्षिद्र क्षिद्र, अस्, m. disease; the sun; a<BR>horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्
क्षिप् 1. क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A., 4. P. क्षि-<BR>पति, -ते, क्षिप्यति, चिक्षेप, चिक्षिपे,<BR>क्षेप्स्यति, -ते, अक्षैप्सीत्, अक्षिप्त, क्षेप्तुम्,<BR>to throw, cast, send, despatch; to put or place any-<BR>thing on or in (with loc.), pour on, scatter, strew;<BR>to fix or attach to; to throw away, cast away, get<BR>rid of; to reject, disdain; to lay (the blame) on; to<BR>strike, hit; to strike down, ruin, destroy; to utter<BR>abusive words, insult, revile, abuse, scold; A. to<BR>throw at each other, destroy one another: Caus. P.<BR>क्षेपयति, -यितुम्, to cause to cast &c.; to hurt,<BR>injure: Desid. चिक्षिप्सति, -ते: Intens. चेक्षिप्-<BR>यते, चेक्षेप्ति; [cf. Lat. sipo, dissipo, for xipo;<BR>Gr. ῥίπτω for κρίπτω Cambro-Brit. hipiaw, ‘to<BR>cast or dash suddenly;’ Goth. vairpa; Germ.<BR>werfe ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्
2. क्षिप्, प्, f. (only used in nom. and inst. pl.<BR>क्षिपस् and क्षिपाभिस्), Ved. the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप|क्षिपः
क्षिप, अस्, आ, अम्, a thrower, striking, hitting;<BR>(अस्), m. throwing, casting, insulting, reviling; (आ),<BR>f. sending, casting, throwing, &c.; night; (a wrong<BR>form for क्षपा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपक|क्षिपकः
क्षिपक, अस्, m. an archer, a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण|क्षिपणं
क्षिपण, अम्, n. sending, despatching, throwing,<BR>casting; reviling, abusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणि|क्षिपणिः
क्षिपणि, इस्, m. a stroke or blow with a whip; a<BR>missile weapon; (इस् or ई), f. an oar; a kind of net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणु|क्षिपणुः
क्षिपणु, उस्, m. an archer; a weapon; air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण्यु|क्षिपण्युः
क्षिपण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. क्षिपण?), fragrant,<BR>sweet-smelling; diffusive, what may be sent or scat-<BR>tered; (उस्), m. the body; spring, the season of<BR>spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपत्
क्षिपत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, throwing, casting;<BR>abusing, reproaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपति|क्षिपतिः
क्षिपति or क्षिपस्ति, ई, du., Ved. the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्त|क्षिप्तः
क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown, cast; sent, despatched,<BR>dismissed, &c.; (आ), f. night, (like क्षिपा, a wrong<BR>form for क्षपा); (अम्), n. a wound caused by<BR>shooting or throwing.<BR>—क्षिप्त-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>distracted in mind, absent.<BR>—क्षिप्तचित्त-ता, f.<BR>absence of mind.<BR>—क्षिप्त-देह, अस्, आ, अम्, pros-<BR>trating the body, lying down.<BR>—क्षिप्त-भेषज,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. healing wounds caused by missile<BR>weapons.<BR>—क्षिप्त-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, of despicable<BR>descent (?), such a man is not allowed to become a<BR>Ṛtvij.<BR>—क्षिप्त-लगुड, अस्, आ, अम्, flinging the<BR>staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्ति|क्षिप्तिः
क्षिप्ति, इस्, f. throwing; sending; solving a<BR>riddle; explaining or understanding a hidden mean-<BR>ing; the quantity to be added to the square of the<BR>least root multiplied by the multiplicator, to render<BR>it capable of yielding an exact square root; (in the<BR>latter sense also क्षिप्तिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्नु|क्षिप्नुः
क्षिप्नु (or क्षिप्णु?), उस्, उस्, उ, throwing,<BR>casting, throwing obstacles in the way; obstructive,<BR>scornful, or fond of abusing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्यत्
क्षिप्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, throwing, sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्यमाण
क्षिप्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, throwing, tossing;<BR>casting aside, throwing off; sending, directing; being<BR>thrown, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्र|क्षिप्रं
क्षिप्र, अस्, आ, अम् (compar. क्षेपीयस्, superl.<BR>क्षेपिष्ठ), springing, flying back with a spring,<BR>elastic (as a bow); quick, speedy, swift; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa; (अम्), n. a measure of time<BR>equal to (1/15) Muhūrta or 15 Etarhis; the part of the<BR>hand between the thumb and fore-finger and the cor-<BR>responding part of the foot; (अम्), ind. quickly,<BR>immediately, directly; (आत्), ind. shortly afterwards,<BR>thereupon; (ए), ind. directly, immediately; [cf. Gr.<BR>κραιπνός.]<BR>—क्षिप्र-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting or work-<BR>ing quickly, skilful.<BR>—क्षिप्र-धन्वन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>armed with an elastic bow or one which flies back<BR>with a spring.<BR>—क्षिप्र-पाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ripening<BR>quickly; (ई), m. the tree Hibiscus Populneoides; [cf.<BR>गर्दभाण्ड.]<BR>—क्षिप्र-श्येन, अस्, m. a species<BR>of bird.<BR>—क्षिप्र-सन्धि, इस्, m. a species of<BR>Sandhi produced by changing the first of two con-<BR>current vowels to its semivowel; also the Svarita<BR>accent on a syllable formed by this kind of Sandhi;<BR>[cf. क्षैप्र.]<BR>—क्षिप्र-हस्त, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Rakṣas (swift-handed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप|क्षेपः
क्षेप, अस्, m. throwing, casting, tossing; a<BR>throw, cast; a stroke of an oar &c.; sending, dis-<BR>missing, striking down, depression; laying on (as<BR>paint &c.), besmearing; transgressing; passing away<BR>time; delay, procrastination, dilatoriness; insult, in-<BR>vective, abuse, reviling; disrespect, contempt; pride,<BR>haughtiness; a nosegay, a clump of flowers; (in<BR>arithmetic) an additive quantity, addendum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपक|क्षेपकः
क्षेपक, अस्, आ, अम्, a thrower, sender; inserted,<BR>interpolated; abusive, disrespectful; (अस्), m. a spu-<BR>rious or interpolated passage; an additive quantity,<BR>addendum; N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपण|क्षेपणं
क्षेपण, अम्, n. the act of throwing, casting,<BR>shooting off (of an arrow &c.); sending, directing;<BR>sending away; passing away time, spending time;<BR>omitting; abusing; a sling; (ई), f. a sling or any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">Page0267-c+ 76</a>]<BR>instrument with which missiles are thrown; an oar;<BR>a kind of net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपणि|क्षेपणिः
क्षेपणि, इस्, f. an oar; a net, a fishing-net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपणीय|क्षेपणीयं
क्षेपणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown or cast;<BR>(अम्), n. a sling, any instrument for casting missiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिमन्
क्षेपिमन्, आ, m. great velocity, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिष्ठ|क्षेपिष्ठः
क्षेपिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (see क्षिप्र), quickest,<BR>speediest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपीयस्
क्षेपीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (see क्षिप्र), more<BR>quick, speedier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्तव्य
क्षेप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cast or thrown, to<BR>be reviled or abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्तृ
क्षेप्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a thrower, caster, sender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्य
क्षेप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown; to be thrown<BR>round (as a garment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिया
क्षिया क्षिया. See under rt. 4. क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिल्लिका
क्षिल्लिका क्षिल्लिका, f., N. of the grand-<BR>mother of king Cakra-varman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिव्
क्षिव् क्षिव्, cl. 1. 4. P. क्षेवति, क्षी-<BR>व्यति, to eject from the mouth, spit, spit<BR>out, vomit; [cf. ष्ठिव् and क्षीव्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षी
क्षी क्षी, another form for 4. क्षि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीज्
क्षीज् क्षीज्, cl. 1. P. क्षीजति, चिक्षीज,<BR>क्षीजितुम्, to sound inarticulately, to sigh<BR>or groan as in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीजन|क्षीजनं
क्षीजन, अम्, n. the whistling of hollow reeds or<BR>bamboos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण क्षीण. See under 4. क्षि 1st col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब्
क्षीब् क्षीब् and क्षीब. See क्षीव्, क्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीर|क्षीरः
क्षीर क्षीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably fr.<BR>क्षर्, but according to Uṇādi IV. 34. fr. घस्),<BR>milk, thickened milk; the milky juice or sap of<BR>plants; the resin of the plant Pinus Longifolia;<BR>water; (अस्), m., N. of a grammarian [cf. क्षीर-<BR>स्वामिन्]; (आ), f., N. of a plant [cf. काकोली]; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of several plants containing a milky sap; a small<BR>shrub, Asclepia Rosea, also दुग्धिका; a species of<BR>Mimosa, M. Kauki [cf. क्षीरिका]; gigantic swallow-<BR>wort; Euphorbia &c.<BR>—क्षीर-कञ्चुकिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a reed, Lipeocercis Serrata (क्षीरीश).<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>कण्ठ or क्षीर-कण्ठक, अस्, m. an infant, a<BR>young child, ‘having milk in its throat.’<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>कन्द, अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of pot-herb, black Bhuin-<BR>coönra, Convolvulus Paniculatus; [cf. क्षीर-विदा-<BR>री.]<BR>—क्षीर-कलम्भ, see क्षैरकलम्भि.<BR>—क्षीर-काकोलिका or क्षीर-काकोली, f. a drug, one<BR>of the eight principal medicaments of the Hindūs; it<BR>is a root from the Himālaya yielding a milky juice;<BR>[cf. काकोली.]<BR>—क्षीर-काण्डक, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Tithymalus Antiquorum (स्नुही), and Calotropis<BR>Gigantea (अर्क).<BR>—क्षीर-काष्ठा, f., N. of a<BR>plant, = वटी.<BR>—क्षीर-कीट, अस्, m. an insect or<BR>animalcule generated by the fermentation of milk.<BR>—क्षीर-क्षव, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = दुद्घ-<BR>पाषाण.<BR>—क्षीर-खर्जूर, अस्, m. a species of<BR>Datura tree.<BR>—क्षीर-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>certain Brāhman who was born again as a flamingo.<BR>—क्षीर-घृत, अम्, n. purified butter mixed<BR>with milk.<BR>—क्षीर-ज, अम्, n. coagulated milk.<BR>—क्षीर-तरङ्गिणी, f. title of a grammar com-<BR>posed by Kṣīra-svāmin.<BR>—क्षीर-तैल, अम्, n.<BR>a kind of unguent prepared with milk, oil, &c.<BR>—क्षीर-तोयधि, इस्, m. the ocean of milk.<BR>—क्षीर-द, अस्, आ, अम्, milk-giving, what yields<BR>milk.<BR>—क्षीर-दल, अस्, m. the plant Calotropis<BR>Gigantea (= अर्क), the leaves &c. of which yield a<BR>milky juice.<BR>—क्षीर-दात्री, f. yielding milk as a<BR>cow.<BR>—क्षीर-द्रुम, अस्, m. the tree Ficus Re-<BR>ligiosa; [cf. अश्वत्थ.]<BR>—क्षीर-धर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—क्षीर-धात्री, f. a wet-nurse.<BR>—क्षीर-धेनु, उस्, f. a milch-cow, symbolically<BR>represented by milk &c. offered as a gift to a Brāh-<BR>man.<BR>—क्षीर-नाश, अस्, m. the tree Trophis Aspera<BR>(= शाखोट).<BR>—क्षीर-निधि, इस्, m. the ocean of<BR>milk.<BR>—क्षीर-नीर, अम्, n. milk and water; em-<BR>bracing, embrace (i. e. a union like the mixing of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-a" target="_blank">Page0268-a+ 81</a>]<BR>milk and water).<BR>—क्षीर-प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking<BR>milk, who or what drinks milk; epithet of a class of<BR>ascetics; an infant, a young child.<BR>—क्षीर-पर्णिन्,<BR>ई, m. the plant Calotropis Gigantea; [cf. अर्क and<BR>क्षीर-दल.]<BR>—क्षीर-पलाण्डु, उस्, m. a kind of<BR>onion.<BR>—क्षीर-पाक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. cooked in<BR>milk.<BR>—क्षीर-पाण, आस्, m. pl. the milk-drinkers,<BR>an epithet of the Uśīnaras; (अम्), n. drinking milk;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), any vessel out of which milk is drunk.<BR>—क्षीर-पाणि, इस्, m., N. of a physician.<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>पायिन्, ई, इणी, इ, drinking or sucking milk; drinking<BR>or imbibing water repeatedly; (इणस्), m. pl. the<BR>milk-drinkers, an epithet of the Uśīnaras.<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, supported by milk, receiving<BR>wages in the form of milk.<BR>—क्षीर-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, composed of milk.<BR>—क्षीर-मोचक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of Moringa, M. Hyperanthera; [cf. मोचक.]<BR>—क्षीर-मोरट, अस्, m. a kind of creeping plant;<BR>[cf. सितद्रु, सुदल, क्षीरक.]<BR>—क्षीर-यष्-<BR>टिक, अम्, n. a dish of liquorice and milk; (perhaps<BR>a wrong form for क्षीर-षष्टिक?).<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>लता, f. the plant Batatas Paniculata; [cf. क्षीर-<BR>विदारी.]<BR>—क्षीर-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. furnished<BR>with milk; (ती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—क्षीर-वल्ली,<BR>f. the dark Bhuincoönra, Convolvulus Paniculatus.<BR>—क्षीर-वारि, इस्, m. the sea of milk; [cf. क्षी-<BR>रोद.]<BR>—क्षीर-वारिधि, इस्, m. the sea of milk.<BR>—क्षीर-विकृति, इस्, f. inspissated milk.<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>विदारिका or क्षीर-विदारी, f. the plant Batatas<BR>Paniculata.<BR>—क्षीर-विषाणिका, f. the plants Tragia<BR>Involucrata (= वृश्चिकाली) and क्षीर-काकोली.<BR>—क्षीर-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the glomerous fig tree,<BR>Ficus Glomerata [cf. उदुम्बर]; a common N. for<BR>the four trees न्यग्रोध, उदुम्बर, अश्वत्थ,<BR>and मधूक.<BR>—क्षीर-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, living<BR>upon milk in consequence of a vow.<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>शर, अस्, m. cream, the surface or skim of milk,<BR>curds; [cf. आमिक्षा.]<BR>—क्षीर-शीर्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>resin of the plant Pinus Longifolia; [cf. श्री-वास.]<BR>—क्षीर-शुक्रा, f. = क्षीर-विदारी and क्षीर-<BR>काकोली.<BR>—क्षीर-शुक्ल, अस्, m. the plant Trapa<BR>Bispinosa [cf. जल-कण्टक]; another plant, =<BR>राजादनी; (आ), f. the plant Batatas Paniculata.<BR>—क्षीर-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. mixed with milk.<BR>—क्षीर-षष्टिक, अम्, n. Ṣaṣṭika rice cooked<BR>in milk.<BR>—क्षीर-सन्तानिका, f. curds mixed with<BR>milk; (a various reading has ˚सन्तालिका.)<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>समुद्र, अस्, m. the sea of milk in Śveta-dīpa.<BR>—क्षीर-सर्पिस्, इस्, n. clarified butter mixed with<BR>milk.<BR>—क्षीर-सागर, अस्, m. the ocean of milk;<BR>also N. of a place.<BR>—क्षीरसागर-सुता, f. an epi-<BR>thet of Lakṣmī as produced from the ocean of<BR>milk.<BR>—क्षीर-सार, अस्, m. essence of milk, any<BR>product of milk, (in Hindī पालजिनु), butter.<BR>—क्षीर-स्फटिक, अस्, m. a precious stone, de-<BR>scribed as a kind of milky crystal (opal or cat's eye?);<BR>[cf. आकाश-स्फटिक and तैल-स्फटिक.]<BR>—क्षीर-<BR>स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a grammarian and commen-<BR>tator on the Amara-koṣa.<BR>—क्षीर-ह्रद, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—क्षीराद (˚र-अद), अस्, m. an<BR>infant at the breast, a sucking child.<BR>—क्षीरान्-<BR>नाद (˚र-अन्न-अद), अस्, m. an infant which is<BR>both fed and suckled.<BR>—क्षीराब्धि (˚र-अब्धि),<BR>इस्, m. the sea of milk, one of the seven seas sur-<BR>rounding the seven divisions of the terrestrial world.<BR>—क्षीराब्धि-ज, अस्, m. the moon; the Amṛta<BR>or any one of the precious objects produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean; an epithet of Śeṣa; an<BR>epithet of Tārkṣya; (आ), f. an epithet of Lakṣmī;<BR>(अम्), n. sea-salt, a pearl.<BR>—क्षीराब्धि-तनया, f.<BR>or क्षीराब्धि-मानुषी, f. an epithet of Lakṣmī as<BR>the daughter of the ocean of milk.<BR>—क्षीराह्व or<BR>क्षीराह्वय (˚र-आह्˚), अस्, m. the resin of the<BR>plant Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—क्षीरोद (˚र-उद), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, containing milk instead of water; (अस्), m.<BR>the sea of milk; the sea in general.<BR>—क्षीरोद-<BR>तनया, f. the daughter of the sea of milk; an epi-<BR>thet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—क्षीरोद-तनया-पति, इस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—क्षीरोदधि (˚र-उद्˚), इस्,<BR>m. the sea of milk.<BR>—क्षीरोद-नन्दन, अस्, m.<BR>the son of the sea of milk, an epithet of the moon.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">Page0268-b+ 77</a>]<BR>—क्षीरोद-मथन, अम्, n. the churning of the<BR>ocean of milk undertaken by the Devas and Asuras<BR>to obtain the Amṛta &c.<BR>—क्षीरोर्मि (˚र-ऊर्˚), इस्,<BR>m. a wave of milk, a wave of the sea of milk.<BR>—क्षीरौदन (˚र-ओद्˚), अस्, m. rice boiled with<BR>milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरक|क्षीरकः
क्षीरक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = क्षीर-<BR>मोरट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरय
क्षीरय, nom. P. क्षीरयति, -यितुम्, to have<BR>the appearance of milk, look like milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरस|क्षीरसः
क्षीरस, अस्, m. = क्षीर-सार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरस्य
क्षीरस्य, nom. P. क्षीरस्यति, -यितुम्, to long<BR>for milk or for the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरावी
क्षीरावी or क्षीराविका, f. a sort of Asclepias, A.<BR>Rosea, = दुग्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिक
क्षीरिक, अस्, m. a kind of serpent; a kind of<BR>tree (आ), f. a dish prepared with milk; a kind of<BR>Datura tree; [cf. क्षीर-खर्जूर and पिण्ड-<BR>खर्जूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिन्
क्षीरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, milky, yielding milk, abounding<BR>in milk, having plenty of milk; containing milky<BR>juice or sap (as a tree); (ई), m. a species of tree,<BR>the Udumbara (?); according to native lexicographers<BR>many plants have this epithet; (इणी), f. a tree bear-<BR>ing an edible fruit, = Mimusops Kauki; a species of<BR>the moon-plant or acid Asclepias used in medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरीय
क्षीरीय, nom. P. क्षीरीयति, -यितुम्, to desire<BR>milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरीश|क्षीरीशः
क्षीरीश, अस्, m. = क्षीर-कञ्चुकिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरेयी
क्षीरेयी, f. an oblation of milk, rice, and sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव्
क्षीव् क्षीव्, cl. 1. 4. P. क्षीवति, क्षेवति<BR>and क्षीव्यति, -वितुम्, to spit, sputter,<BR>eject from the mouth; to be drunk or intoxicated;<BR>[cf. क्षिव्, क्षेव्, क्षीब्, ष्ठिव्; cf. also Hib.<BR>siobhas, ‘rage, madness.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव|क्षीवः
क्षीव or क्षीब, अस्, आ, अम्, excited, drunk,<BR>intoxicated.<BR>—क्षीव-ता, f. or क्षीव-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>intoxication, drunkenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षु|क्षुः
क्षु 1. क्षु, cl. 2. P. क्षौति, चुक्षाव,<BR>क्षविष्यति, अक्षावीत्, क्षवितुम्, to<BR>sneeze, to make any sound like sneezing; to cough:<BR>Caus. क्षावयति: Desid. of Caus. चुक्षावयिषति;<BR>[cf. Lith. czaudmi.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षव|क्षवः
क्षव, अस्, m. sneezing, cough, catarrh; a black<BR>species of mustard, Sinapis Dichotoma; [cf. राजिका.]<BR>—क्षव-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, anything which causes sneez-<BR>ing; making a sneeze, sneezing, coughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवक|क्षवकं|क्षवकः
क्षवक, अस्, m. the plant Achyranthes Aspera,<BR>= अपामार्ग, black mustard; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>pot-herb; (इका), f. a kind of Solanum; a species of<BR>rice; a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवथु|क्षवथुः
क्षवथु, उस्, m. sneezing; catarrh; cough;<BR>irritation of the throat; sore throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्
क्षुत्, त्, f. a sneeze, sneezing.<BR>—क्षुत्-करी, f., N.<BR>of a plant, commonly कङ्कालिका, black mustard (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत|क्षुतं|क्षुतः
क्षुत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has sneezed; sneezed<BR>upon; (as a less correct form for क्ष्णुत), sharp;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. a sneeze, sneezing, cough.<BR>—क्षुत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, sneezing.<BR>—क्षुता-<BR>भिजनन (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m. black mustard; [cf.<BR>क्षुधाभिजनन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुतक|क्षुतकः
क्षुतक, अस्, m. black mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुति|क्षुतिः
क्षुति, इस्, f. sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुवत्
क्षुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, sneezing, coughing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षु|क्षुः
क्षु 2. क्षु, n. (fr. घस्?), Ved. food.<BR>—क्षु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. abounding in food,<BR>nourishing, nutritious; strong; powerful, robust,<BR>valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण|क्षुणः
क्षुण क्षुण, अस्, m. the soap-berry plant,<BR>Sapindus Saponaria; [cf. अरिष्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्ण|क्षुण्णं
क्षुण्ण क्षुण्ण. See below under क्षुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्
क्षुद् क्षुद्, cl. 7. P. A. and Ved. cl. 1. P.<BR>क्षुणत्ति, क्षुन्ते, क्षोदति, चुक्षोद,<BR>चुक्षुदे, क्षोत्स्यति, -ते, अक्षुदत्, अक्षौत्सीत्,<BR>अक्षुत्त, क्षोत्तुम्, to strike against, stamp or<BR>trample upon, pound; to bruise, crush, shiver, shatter,<BR>reduce to powder, dash to pieces, shake by stamping<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-c" target="_blank">Page0268-c+ 80</a>]<BR>on; A. to move, to be agitated or shaken: Caus. P.<BR>क्षोदयति, -यितुम्, to crush, pound, comminute,<BR>pulverize, reduce to powder, diminish; shake or<BR>agitate by stamping; [cf. Gr. ξύω, ξέω, for ξεύω,<BR>ξυστός, ξεστός; Lith. skausti?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्ण|क्षुण्णं
क्षुण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, pounded, bruised, crushed,<BR>stamped or trampled upon; broken to pieces, pul-<BR>verized, shattered, pierced; violated (as a vow); ex-<BR>ercised, practised, skilful; one versed in sacred science<BR>but unable to explain or teach it; defeated, overcome.<BR>—क्षुण्ण-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, contrite in heart,<BR>penitent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्णक|क्षुण्णकः
क्षुण्णक, अस्, m. a kind of drum beaten at a<BR>funeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद|क्षुदः
क्षुद, अस्, m. flour, meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्र|क्षुद्रः
क्षुद्र, अस्, आ, अम् (compar. क्षोदीयस्, superl.<BR>क्षोदिष्ठ), minute, diminutive, tiny, very small,<BR>small, little, trifling; mean, low, vile, niggardly, base,<BR>avaricious; wicked; cruel; poor, indigent; (अस्), m.<BR>a small particle of rice; a bee or wasp; the plant<BR>Artocarpus Lacucha [cf. लकुच and डहु]; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>a peculiar class of writings, see क्षुद्र-कल्प; (आ),<BR>f. a woman maimed or crippled; a base or despicable<BR>woman; a whore, a harlot; a dancing girl; a quarrel-<BR>some woman; a bee, fly, gnat; several plants, Sola-<BR>num Jacquini, = वृहती; also = चाङ्गेरिका; also =<BR>गवेधुका; (अम्), n., Ved. a particle of dust, flour,<BR>meal; [cf. Lith. kûdikis, ‘an infant;’ Pers. كودك<BR>kūdak, ‘small, a boy.’]<BR>—क्षुद्र-कण्टकारी, f. the<BR>plant Solanum Jacquini, = अग्नि-दमनी.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>कण्टकी, f. a kind of Solanum, = बृहती.<BR>—क्षु-<BR>द्रक-मानस, अम्, n., N. of a lake.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>कम्बु, उस्, m. a small shell.<BR>—क्षुद्र-कल्प, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the smaller ritual,’ title of a class of works.<BR>—क्षुद्र-कारलिका, f. (for क्षुद्र-करालिका?),<BR>and क्षुद्र-कारवेल्ली, f. a kind of Cucurbitaceous<BR>plant.<BR>—क्षुद्र-कुलिश, अस्, m. a precious stone;<BR>[cf. वैक्रान्त.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-कुष्ठ, अम्, n. a mild<BR>form of leprosy, (comprising eleven varieties, whereas<BR>the महा-कुष्ठ contains seven severe forms of<BR>leprosy.)<BR>—क्षुद्र-क्षुर and क्षुद्र-गोक्षु-<BR>रक, अस्, m. a variety of the plant Asteracantha<BR>Longifolia.<BR>—क्षुद्र-घण्टिका, f. a tinkling orna-<BR>ment, a girdle of small bells.<BR>—क्षुद्र-घोली, f.,<BR>N. of a plant, = चिविल्लिका.<BR>—क्षुद्र-चञ्चु, उस्, f.,<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>—क्षुद्र-चन्दन, अम्, n. red<BR>sandal-wood.<BR>—क्षुद्र-चिर्भिटा, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= गोपाल-कर्कटी.<BR>—क्षुद्र-चूड, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of small bird, commonly called गोसालिक.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>जन्तु, उस्, m. any small animal; a kind of worm,<BR>Julus (शत-पदी).<BR>—क्षुद्र-जातीफल, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of Myrobalan; [cf. आमलक.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>जीर, अस्, m. small cummin.<BR>—क्षुद्र-जीवा, f., N.<BR>of a plant, = जीवन्ती.<BR>—क्षुद्रञ्-चर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>following small or minute or trifling matters.<BR>—क्षु-<BR>द्र-तण्डुल, अस्, m. a grain of rice.<BR>—क्षुद्र-ता,<BR>f. or क्षुद्र-त्व, अम्, n. minuteness, smallness;<BR>inferiority, insignificance; meanness.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>तुलसी, f. a kind of Ocimum, = अर्जक.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>दंशिका or क्षुद्र-दंशी, f. a small gad-fly.<BR>—क्षुद्र-दुरालभा, f., N. of a thorny plant<BR>much eaten by camels.<BR>—क्षुद्र-दुःस्पर्शा, f. the<BR>plant Solanum Jacquini, = अग्नि-दमनी.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>धात्री, f., N. of a plant; [cf. कर्कट.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>धान्य, अम्, n. shrivelled grain.<BR>—क्षुद्र-नासिक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, having a small nose.<BR>—क्षुद्र-पक्-<BR>षिक, अस्, m. a small bird.<BR>—क्षुद्र-पत्त्रा, f. a<BR>kind of wood-sorrel, Oxalis Monadelpha, = चाङ्गेरी;<BR>(ई), f., N. of another plant, = वचा.<BR>—क्षुद्र-प-<BR>नस, अस्, m. the plant Artocarpus Lacucha (लकुच).<BR>—क्षुद्र-पर्ण, अस्, m. a kind of Ocimum,<BR>= अर्जक.<BR>—क्षुद्र-पाषाण-भेदा or ई, f.,<BR>N. of a plant, = चतुः-पत्त्री, पार्वती, नग-भू,<BR>&c.<BR>—क्षुद्र-पिप्पली, f. wild pepper (= वन-<BR>पिप्पली).<BR>—क्षुद्र-पृषती, f., Ved. covered<BR>with small spots.<BR>—क्षुद्र-पोतिका, f., N. of a pot-<BR>herb.<BR>—क्षुद्र-फलक, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>= जीवन, Celtis Orientalis.<BR>—क्षुद्र-फला, f., N.<BR>of several plants, Ardisia Solanacea, = भूमि-जम्बु,<BR>and others.<BR>—क्षुद्र-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, of little<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-a" target="_blank">Page0269-a+ 81</a>]<BR>understanding, simple, silly, ignorant; (इस्), m., N.<BR>of a jackal in the Hitopadeśa.<BR>—क्षुद्रबुद्धि-<BR>नामन्, आ, आ, अ, named Kṣudra-buddhi.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>भण्टाकी, f., N. of a plant, a kind of Solanum, =<BR>बृहती; [cf. क्षुद्र-कण्टकी.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-मीन,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—क्षुद्र-मुस्ता, f. the<BR>plant Scirpus Kysoor; [cf. कसेरु.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>रस, अस्, m. honey; (आ), f. the plant Pongamia<BR>Glabra; [cf. करञ्ज.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-रोग, अस्, m. a<BR>minor disease, one of little importance; a name<BR>applied to various local diseases, especially exanthemas<BR>of different kinds; there are forty-four such diseases.<BR>—क्षुद्ररोगिक, अस्, आ, अम्, affected with such<BR>a disease.<BR>—क्षुद्र-वंशा, f., N. of a plant, Dios-<BR>corea, = वराह-क्रान्ता.<BR>—क्षुद्र-वर्वणा, f. a<BR>small gad-fly; [cf. वरटा.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-वल्ली, f., N.<BR>of a pot-herb; [cf. मूल-पोती.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-वार्ताकिनी,<BR>f. a kind of Solanum with white blossoms, = श्वेत-<BR>कण्टकारी.<BR>—क्षुद्र-वार्ताकी, f. a kind of Sola-<BR>num, = बृहती.<BR>—क्षुद्र-शङ्ख, अस्, m. a small<BR>conch shell.<BR>—क्षुद्र-शर्करा or क्षुद्र-शर्-<BR>करिका, f. a kind of sugar-cane, = यावनाल-शर्-<BR>करा.<BR>—क्षुद्र-शार्दूल, अस्, m. a kind of tiger,<BR>= चित्र-व्याघ्र.<BR>—क्षुद्र-शीर्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>tree Celosia Cristata, = मयूर-शिखा.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>शुक्ति, इस्, m. a bivalve shell, = जल-शुक्ति.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>श्यामा, f., N. of a plant, = कटभी.<BR>—क्षुद्र-<BR>श्लेष्मान्तक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = भूकर्बु-<BR>दारक.<BR>—क्षुद्र-श्वास, अस्, m. short breath.<BR>—क्षुद्र-श्वेता, f., N. of a plant; [cf. महा-<BR>श्वेता.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-सहा, f. the plant Phaseolus Tri-<BR>lobus; the Coloquintida, = इन्द्र-वारुणी; [cf. म-<BR>हा-सहा.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-सुवर्ण, अम्, n. bad gold,<BR>prince's metal.<BR>—क्षुद्र-हन्, आ, m. killing the<BR>wicked; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—क्षुद्र-हिङ्गुलिका,<BR>f. a small species of prickly nightshade, Solanum<BR>Jacquini; [cf. कण्टकारी.]<BR>—क्षुद्र-हिङ्गुली, f.<BR>= the preceding.<BR>—क्षुद्राग्निमन्थ (˚र-अग्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the plant Premna Spinosa used for kindling<BR>fire; [cf. अरणि.]<BR>—क्षुद्राञ्जन (˚र-अञ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a kind of unguent applied to the eyes in certain<BR>diseases.<BR>—क्षुद्राण्ड (˚र-अण्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>born from minute eggs.<BR>—क्षुद्राण्ड-मत्स्य-<BR>सङ्घात, अस्, m. small fry.<BR>—क्षुद्रान्त्र<BR>(˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. the small cavity of the heart.<BR>—क्षुद्रापामार्ग (˚र-अप्˚), अस्, m., N. of the<BR>plant Desmochæta Atropurpurea (= रक्तापामार्ग),<BR>a biennial plant.<BR>—क्षुद्रामलक (˚र-आम्˚),<BR>अम्, n. Myrobalan (आमलक).<BR>—क्षुद्रामलक-<BR>सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = कर्कट.<BR>—क्षु-<BR>द्राम्र (˚र-आम्˚), अस्, m., N. of a plant, = कोशाम्र.<BR>—क्षुद्राम्लपनस or क्षुद्राम्बुपनस (˚र-<BR>अम्˚), अस्, m. the plant Artocarpus Lacucha (लकुच).<BR>—क्षुद्राम्ला (˚र-अम्˚), f. wood-sorrel, Oxalis<BR>Corniculata (= अम्ललोणिका); another plant, = श-<BR>शाण्डुली.<BR>—क्षुद्राम्लिका (˚र-अम्˚), f. a kind of<BR>wood-sorrel or Oxalis, = चाङ्गेरी.<BR>—क्षुद्रेङ्गुदी<BR>(˚र-इङ्˚), f., N. of a plant, = यवास.<BR>—क्षुद्रेर्-<BR>वारु (˚र-इर्˚), उस्, m., N. of a plant, = गोपाल-<BR>कर्कटी.<BR>—क्षुद्रोदुम्बरिका (˚र-उद्˚), f. the<BR>plant Ficus Oppositifolia; [cf. काकोदुम्बरिका.]<BR>—क्षुद्रोपोदक-नाम्नी (˚र-उप्˚), f., N. of a<BR>pot-herb; [cf. मूल-पोती.]<BR>—क्षुद्रोपोदकी (˚र-<BR>उप्˚), f., N. of a pot-herb, = सूक्ष्म-पत्त्रा and<BR>मण्टपी.<BR>—क्षुद्रोलूक (˚र-उल्˚), अस्, m. a small<BR>kind of owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रक|क्षुद्रकः
क्षुद्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, small, minute; (अस्),<BR>m. a species of plant; N. of a prince, a son of<BR>Prasenajit; title of a collection of Buddhist works,<BR>= विनय-क्षुद्रक-वस्तु; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people living by warfare, the Ὀξυδρακοι.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रल
क्षुद्रल, अस्, आ, अम्, minute, small, unimportant<BR>(applied especially to animals and diseases).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रिका
क्षुद्रिका, f. a kind of gad-fly, = दंश; small<BR>bells employed for ornament; [cf. क्षुद्र-घण्-<BR>टिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोत्तृ
क्षोत्तृ, ता, m. a pestle, any implement for<BR>grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोद|क्षोदः
क्षोद, अस्, m. pounding, grinding; the stone or<BR>slab on which anything is ground or powdered, a<BR>mortar &c., any pounded or ground or pulverized<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">Page0269-b+ 77</a>]<BR>substance, flour, meal, dust, a particle, a small piece or<BR>fragment.<BR>—क्षोद-रज, अस्, आ, अम्, ground to dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदस्
क्षोदस्, अस्, n., Ved. water in agitation, swell of<BR>the sea, rushing or stream of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदित|क्षोदितं
क्षोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, pounded, ground, com-<BR>minuted; (अम्), n. powder, dust, flour, meal, any<BR>substance pulverized or ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिमन्
क्षोदिमन्, आ, m. minuteness, excessive smallness<BR>or inferiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिष्ठ|क्षोदिष्ठः
क्षोदिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of क्षुद्र),<BR>finely pounded, very small, very minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदीयस्
क्षोदीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of क्षुद्र),<BR>more minute, very fine, very minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोद्य|क्षोद्यः
क्षोद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stamped or trampled<BR>on or pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध्
क्षुध् 1. क्षुध्, cl. 4. P. क्षुध्यति,<BR>चुक्षोध, क्षोद्धुम्, to feel hungry;<BR>to be hungry, hunger; [cf. Goth. grêdôn, ‘to be<BR>hungry.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध्
2. क्षुध्, त्, f. hunger.<BR>—क्षुत्-क्षाम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, emaciated by hunger.<BR>—क्षुत्-तृट्-परीत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, hungry and thirsty.<BR>—क्षुत्-तृड्-उद्भव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, beginning to feel hungry and thirsty.<BR>—क्षुत्-तृषान्वित (˚षा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suffer-<BR>ing from hunger and thirst.<BR>—क्षुत्-तृष्णोपपीडित<BR>(˚णा-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, hungry and thirsty.<BR>—क्षुत्-<BR>परीत, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome with hunger.<BR>—क्षुत्-<BR>पिपासा-परिश्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, wearied by hunger<BR>and thirst.<BR>—क्षुत्-पिपासा-परीताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one whose body is affected with hunger<BR>and thirst.<BR>—क्षुत्-पिपासार्त (˚सा-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>afflicted with hunger and thirst.<BR>—क्षुत्-पिपासित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, hungry and thirsty.<BR>—क्षुत्-प्रतीकार,<BR>अस्, m. allaying hunger, eating.<BR>—क्षुद्-रोग, अस्,<BR>m. pain of hunger.<BR>—क्षुद्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, hungry.<BR>—क्षुन्-निवृत्ति, इस्, f. cessation of hunger, ap-<BR>peasing of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधा
क्षुधा, f. hunger; mystical N. of the letter य्.<BR>—क्षुधा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing hunger, in-<BR>creasing appetite.<BR>—क्षुधा-कुशल, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a tree, = विल्वान्तर-वृक्ष.<BR>—क्षुधा-ध्वंस,<BR>अस्, m. allaying hunger.<BR>—क्षुधान्वित (˚धा-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted with hunger.<BR>—क्षुधा-<BR>पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, hungry, starving.<BR>—क्षुधा-<BR>भिजनन (˚धा-अभ्˚), अस्, m. black mustard; [cf.<BR>क्षुताभिजनन.]<BR>—क्षुधा-मार, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>death caused by starvation.<BR>—क्षुधार्त (˚धा-<BR>आर्˚) or क्षुधार्दित (˚धा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>hungry, hungered.<BR>—क्षुधाविष्ट (˚धा-आव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, affected by hunger.<BR>—क्षुधा-शान्ति,<BR>इस्, f. allaying hunger, satiety, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधालु
क्षुधालु, उस्, उस्, उ, hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधित|क्षुधितः
क्षुधित, अस्, आ, अम्, hungry, hungered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोधुक
क्षोधुक, अस्, इका, अम्, Ved. hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधुन|क्षुधुनः
क्षुधुन क्षुधुन, अस्, m., N. of a savage<BR>and barbarous race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुप्
क्षुप् क्षुप्, a Sautra root (i. e. one used in<BR>grammatical Sūtras only), to depress, feel depressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुप|क्षुपः
क्षुप क्षुप, अस्, m. [cf. क्षुम्प], a bush,<BR>a shrub; a small tree, one with short branches and<BR>roots; N. of an old king, a son of Prasandhi and<BR>father of Ikṣvāku; N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa from<BR>Satya-bhāmā; N. of a mountain westward from<BR>Dvārakā.<BR>—क्षुप-डोडमुष्टि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>—क्षुपालु (˚प-आलु), उस्, m. a kind of<BR>bulbous plant, = पानीयालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुपक|क्षुपकः
क्षुपक, अस्, आ, m. f. a bush, a shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ्
क्षुभ् 1. क्षुभ्, cl. 9. 4. P., 1. A. क्षुभ्-<BR>नाति, क्षुभ्यति, क्षोभते, चुक्षो-<BR>भ, चुक्षुभे, क्षोभिष्यति, -ते, अक्षोभीत्,<BR>अक्षुभत् and अक्षोभिष्ट, क्षोभितुम्, to<BR>shake, tremble, to be agitated or disturbed; to be<BR>unsteady; to stumble (literally or metaphorically):<BR>Caus. क्षोभयति, -यितुम्, to agitate, cause to<BR>shake, disturb, stir up, excite: Desid. चुक्षुभि-<BR>षति, -ते, or चुक्षोभिषति, -ते: Intens. चोक्षु-<BR>भ्यते, चोक्षोब्धि; [cf. Cambro-Brit. hwbiau, ‘to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">Page0269-c+ 78</a>]<BR>make a sudden push;’ Gr. κοῦφος; Mod. Germ.<BR>schiebe.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुब्ध|क्षुब्धः
क्षुब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, shaken, tossed,<BR>stirred up; agitated (mentally), excited, disturbed;<BR>(अस्), m. the churning-stick; a kind of coitus.<BR>—क्षुब्ध-ता, f. agitation.<BR>—क्षुब्धार्णव<BR>(˚ध-अर्˚), अस्, m. a stormy ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ्
2. क्षुभ्, प्, f., Ved. a blow, a shake, a push.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभा
क्षुभा, f. a kind of weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभित|क्षुभितः
क्षुभित, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated, tossed, set in<BR>motion; agitated (mentally), disturbed, anxious;<BR>frightened, alarmed, afraid; angry, enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभ|क्षोभः
क्षोभ, अस्, m. shaking, agitation, disturbance,<BR>tossing, trembling, emotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभक|क्षोभकः
क्षोभक, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, causing agitation;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a mountain in Kāmākhyā, a place<BR>sacred to the goddess Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभण|क्षोभणं|क्षोभणः
क्षोभण, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, agitating, dis-<BR>turbing, causing emotion; (अस्), m., N. of one of<BR>the five arrows of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभ्य
क्षोभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shaken or agitated or<BR>disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुमत्|क्षुमन्त्
क्षुमत् क्षु-मत्. See under 2. क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुमा
क्षुमा क्षुमा, f., Ved. an epithet of an<BR>arrow, according to the scholiast ‘causing to tremble’<BR>(for क्षुभा?); N. of several plants; linseed, Linum<BR>Usitatissimum; a sort of flax, Bengal San (शण);<BR>the Indigo plant; a sort of creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौम|क्षौमं|क्षौमः
क्षौम, &c. See s. v., p. 271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुम्प्
क्षुम्प् क्षुम्प्, cl. 1. P. क्षुम्पति, to<BR>go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुम्प
क्षुम्प क्षुम्प, अस्, m. [cf. क्षुप], Ved. a<BR>bush, a shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर्
क्षुर् क्षुर्, cl. 6. P. क्षुरति, चुक्षोर,<BR>क्षोरितुम्, to cut, dig, scratch; to make<BR>lines or furrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर|क्षुरः
क्षुर, अस्, m. (connected with the preceding,<BR>perhaps related to क्षर् ?; cf. Gr. ξυρόν), a razor;<BR>a razor-like barb or sharp blade attached to an arrow;<BR>N. of several plants, Asteracantha Longifolia; also<BR>Tribulus Lanuginosus, see गो-क्षुर; also = महा-<BR>पिण्डीतक, and Saccharum Sara (शर); the hoof of<BR>a cow &c.; a horse's hoof; the foot of a bedstead<BR>[cf. खुर]; (ई), f. a knife, a dagger; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>Ved. (Sāy.) having claws.<BR>—क्षुर-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>the operation of shaving.<BR>—क्षुर-कॢप्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, shaved.<BR>—क्षुर-क्रिया, f. the operation of<BR>shaving, the employment of a razor.<BR>—क्षुर-<BR>चतुष्टय, अम्, n. four things necessary for shaving.<BR>—क्षुर-धान, अम्, n. a razor-case.<BR>—क्षुर-<BR>धार, अस्, आ, अम्, razor-edged, sharp as a razor;<BR>any very sharp instrument for cutting.<BR>—क्षुर-<BR>धारा, f. the edge of a razor; N. of a hell.<BR>—क्षु-<BR>रधाराभ (˚र-आभा), अस्, आ, अम्, sharp as a razor.<BR>—क्षुर-पत्त्र, अस्, m., N. of the plant Saccharum<BR>Sara (शर).<BR>—क्षुर-पत्त्रिका, f., N. of a pot-herb,<BR>= पालङ्क्य.<BR>—क्षुर-पवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. sharp-<BR>angled, sharp-edged, very sharp; (इस्), m., N. of a<BR>sacrifice performed in one day (एकाह).<BR>—क्षुर-<BR>प्र, अस्, m. a razor shot as an arrow; a kind of<BR>arrow, one with a sharp horse-shoe-shaped head; a<BR>sort of hoe or weeding spade.<BR>—क्षुर-प्रग,<BR>अम्, n. according to some authorities = क्षुर-प्र.<BR>—क्षुर-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a razor-case.<BR>—क्षुर-<BR>भृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. furnished with sharp angles.<BR>—क्षुर-मर्दिन्, ई, m. a barber.<BR>—क्षुराङ्ग<BR>(˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a plant; [cf. गो-क्षुरक.]<BR>—क्षुरार्पण (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरक|क्षुरकः
क्षुरक, अस्, m., N. of several plants, = Astera-<BR>cantha Longifolia; also Tribulus Lanuginosus [cf.<BR>गो-क्षुर]; also = तिलक; also another plant,<BR>= भूताङ्कुश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिका
क्षुरिका, f. a small razor; a knife, a dagger; a<BR>sort of earthen vessel, a kind of pot-herb (= पालङ्-<BR>क्य).<BR>—क्षुरिका-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the plant Saccha-<BR>rum Sara (शर).<BR>—क्षुरिकोपनिषद् (˚का-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f. title of an Upaniṣad belonging to the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिन्
क्षुरिन्, ई, m. a barber; (इणी), f. the wife of a<BR>barber; a kind of yam, see वराह-क्रान्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौर|क्षौरं
क्षौर, &c. See s. v., p. 271.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुलिक
क्षुलिक क्षुलिक, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्ल|क्षुल्लः
क्षुल्ल क्षुल्ल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. क्षुद्र ?),<BR>small, little, minute.<BR>—क्षुल्ल-तात, अस्, m. the<BR>younger brother of a father.<BR>—क्षुल्ल-तातक,<BR>अस्, m. the brother of a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लक|क्षुल्लकः
क्षुल्लक, अस्, आ, अम्, little, small; low, vile,<BR>poor, indigent; wicked, malicious, abandoned; hard;<BR>young, youngest; pained, distressed; (अस्), m. a<BR>small shell; N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुवत्
क्षुवत् क्षुवत्. See under rt. 1. क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेड
क्षेड क्षेड, क्षेडित, = क्ष्वेड, क्ष्वेडित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्र|क्षेत्रं
क्षेत्र क्षेत्र, अम्, n. (fr. 1. or 2. क्षि),<BR>landed property, land, soil, a field (e. g. क्षेत्रं<BR>कृ, to cultivate the soil; क्षेत्रस्य पति, lord of<BR>the soil, N. for a kind of genius or tutelary deity<BR>regarded in the Veda as the guardian of cultivated<BR>fields); place, region, country; a sacred spot or dis-<BR>trict, a place of pilgrimage, as Benares &c.; an<BR>enclosed plot of ground, portion of space, superficies,<BR>circuit, circumference; fertile soil; the fertile womb,<BR>a wife; place of origin; department, sphere of action,<BR>the body considered as the field of the indwelling<BR>and working of the soul; a sign of the zodiac; (in<BR>geometry) a plane figure, as a triangle, circle, &c.<BR>enclosed by lines, any figure considered as having<BR>geometrical dimensions; a diagram; a house, town;<BR>[cf. अन्य-क्षेत्र, कुरु-क्षेत्र, &c.; cf. also<BR>Goth. haithi, Them. haithjo; Germ. Heide.]<BR>—क्षेत्र-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, cultivating a field; a<BR>husbandman.<BR>—क्षेत्र-कर्कटी, f. a kind of gourd;<BR>[cf. बालुकी.]<BR>—क्षेत्रकर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, one who<BR>cultivates the soil, a husbandman.<BR>—क्षेत्र-कर्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. cultivation of the soil.<BR>—क्षेत्र-गणित,<BR>अम्, n. geometry.<BR>—क्षेत्र-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, geo-<BR>metrical.<BR>—क्षेत्रगतोपपत्ति (˚त-उप्˚), इस्, f.<BR>geometrical proof.<BR>—क्षेत्र-चिर्भिटा, f. a kind of<BR>gourd, = चिर्भिटा.<BR>—क्षेत्र-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, pro-<BR>duced in a field, as corn &c.; born from the body;<BR>(अस्), m., scil. पुत्र, a son, the offspring of the wife<BR>by a kinsman or person duly appointed to raise up<BR>issue to the husband, (this is one of the twelve kinds<BR>of issue allowed by the old Hindū law); (आ), f., N.<BR>of several plants, = श्वेत-कण्टकारी, शशाण्डुली,<BR>गोमूत्रिका, शिल्पिका, चणिका.<BR>—क्षेत्र-जात, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, begotten on the wife of another.<BR>—क्षेत्र-<BR>जेष, अस्, m., Ved. contest for landed property,<BR>acquisition of land.<BR>—क्षेत्र-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing localities; familiar with the cultivation of<BR>the soil, a husbandman &c.; clever, dexterous, skil-<BR>ful, cunning; (अस्), m. ‘knowing the body,’ i. e. the<BR>soul, the conscious principle in the corporeal frame;<BR>a libertine, a whoremonger; a form of Śiva; N.<BR>of a prince; (आ), f. a girl fifteen years old who<BR>personates the goddess Durgā at a festival of this<BR>deity.<BR>—क्षेत्र-तत्त्व, अम्, n. a part of the work<BR>Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—क्षेत्र-तर, अम्, n., Ved. a spot<BR>very fit for cultivation or for habitation.<BR>—क्षेत्र-<BR>ता, f. the state of being a seat or residence, a seat,<BR>a place of residence.<BR>—क्षेत्र-दूती, f. a kind of<BR>Solanum (श्वेत-कण्टकारी).<BR>—क्षेत्र-देवता, f.<BR>‘the deity of the fields,’ epithet of a serpent in the<BR>Pañca-tantra.<BR>—क्षेत्र-पति, इस्, m. the owner of a<BR>field, a landowner, a landlord, a farmer; [cf. क्षै-<BR>त्रपत, क्षैत्रपत्य, p. 271, and क्षेत्रस्य-<BR>पति above.]<BR>—क्षेत्र-पद, अम्, n. a place<BR>sacred to a deity.<BR>—क्षेत्र-पर्पटी, f., N. of<BR>a shrub, Oldenlandia Biflora or another species.<BR>—क्षेत्र-पाल, अस्, m. a man employed to guard<BR>fields from depredation; a deity protecting the<BR>fields; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—क्षेत्र-फल, अम्,<BR>n. (in geometry) the superficial contents of a figure.<BR>—क्षेत्र-भक्ति, इस्, f. the division of a field.<BR>—क्षेत्र-भूमि, इस्, f. cultivated land.<BR>—क्षेत्र-<BR>यमानिका, f., N. of a plant, = वचा.<BR>—क्षेत्र-<BR>रक्ष, अस्, m. a man employed to guard fields<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">Page0270-b+ 79</a>]<BR>from depredation.<BR>—क्षेत्र-राशि, इस्, m. quantity<BR>represented by geometrical figures.<BR>—क्षेत्र-रुहा,<BR>f. a kind of gourd, = बालुकी.<BR>—क्षेत्र-वसुधा, f.<BR>cultivated land.<BR>—क्षेत्र-विद्, त्, त्, त्, familiar with<BR>localities; experienced, clever, skilful; (त्), m. a<BR>husbandman; a sage, one who possesses spiritual<BR>knowledge; the soul.<BR>—क्षेत्र-व्यवहार, अस्, m.<BR>drawing a figure in geometry; geometrical demon-<BR>stration.<BR>—क्षेत्र-सम्भव, अस्, m., N. of either<BR>of the shrubs Cañcu and Bhiṇḍā; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>gourd, = शशाण्डुली.<BR>—क्षेत्र-सम्भूत, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of grass, = कुन्दर.<BR>—क्षेत्र-साति, इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. acquisition of field or land.<BR>—क्षेत्र-साधस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. arriving at or coming to a place.<BR>—क्षेत्र-सीमा, f. the boundary of a meadow or<BR>field or holy place.<BR>—क्षेत्र-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>residing at a sacred place.<BR>—क्षेत्राजीव (˚र-आज्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who gains a livelihood by cultivating<BR>the soil; a cultivator, a peasant.<BR>—क्षेत्राधिदेवता<BR>(˚र-अध्˚), f. the tutelary deity of any consecrated<BR>piece of ground.<BR>—क्षेत्राधिप (˚र-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. = the preceding; the regent of a sign of the<BR>zodiac.<BR>—क्षेत्रामलकी, the plant Flacourtia Ca-<BR>taphracta; [cf. भूम्य्-आमलकी.]<BR>—क्षेत्रा-सा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. acquiring or gaining land.<BR>—क्षेत्रे-<BR>क्षु (˚र-इक्˚), उस्, m. a kind of grain, = यावनाल.<BR>—क्षेत्रोपेक्ष (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Śvaphalka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिक|क्षेत्रिकः
क्षेत्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having a field, relating to a<BR>field &c., agrarian; (अस्), m. the owner of a field, a<BR>farmer, a cultivator, a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिन्
क्षेत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, owning a field, cultivating land,<BR>agricultural; (ई), m. an agriculturist, a husbandman,<BR>a cultivator; a husband; the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिय|क्षेत्रियं|क्षेत्रियः
क्षेत्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a field, belonging<BR>to land; curable in a future body, i. e. incurable in<BR>the present life; (आणि), n. pl. the environs of any<BR>place; (अम्), n. a chronic or organic disease, an<BR>incurable one; meadow grass, herbage, pasturage;<BR>(अस्), m. a medicament, anything fit to be adminis-<BR>tered in medicine (?); an incurable disease; one who<BR>has carnal knowledge of other men's wives, an<BR>adulterer; physicking, operating.<BR>—क्षेत्रिय-ना-<BR>शन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. removing a chronic disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रीय
क्षेत्रीय, nom. P. क्षेत्रीयति, to desire another<BR>man's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेद
क्षेद क्षेद, अस्, m. (?) sorrowing, moan-<BR>ing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप|क्षेपः
क्षेप क्षेप, क्षेपक, क्षेपण, क्षेपणि,<BR>&c. See under rt. क्षिप् at p. 267.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम|क्षेमं|क्षेमः
क्षेम क्षेम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. क्षि), habit-<BR>able, giving rest, giving ease or security or comfort;<BR>conferring happiness; at ease, prosperous, safe, secure,<BR>well, happy, right; (अस्, अम्), m. n. (Ved. always m.)<BR>basis, foundation; residence, place of rest; abiding<BR>at ease; safety, tranquillity, peace, rest, security, any<BR>secure, easy or comfortable state, well-being, weal,<BR>happiness (e. g. क्षेमेण, at ease, in security,<BR>safely; क्षेमे — योगे, Ved. both in rest and exertion<BR> — in enjoying and acquiring); preserving, protecting,<BR>keeping what is acquired; final emancipation, eternal<BR>happiness; (अस्), m. a kind of perfume (= चण्डा);<BR>ease or prosperity personified as a son of Dharma<BR>and Śānti; also a son of Titikṣā; N. of a prince,<BR>a son of Śuci and father of Suvrata; N. of a son of<BR>the third Manu Sāvarṇa; N. of a kind of college or<BR>association [cf. मठ]; the proper term (according<BR>to Manu II. 127) of civil address to a Vaiśya, asking<BR>him whether his property is secure; (आ), f., N. of an<BR>Apsaras; an epithet of Durgā; N. of another deity;<BR>a kind of perfume; (अम्), n., N. of one of the seven<BR>Varṣas in Jambu-dvīpa.<BR>—क्षेम-कर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing peace and security, conferring happiness or<BR>good fortune, propitious.<BR>—क्षेम-कर्ण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Maheśa, who composed, A. D. 1570,<BR>the work Rāga-mālā.<BR>—क्षेम-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>one whose work is peace and security, creating tran-<BR>quillity and security; (आ), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—क्षेम-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. longing for rest.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">Page0270-c+ 76</a>]<BR>—क्षेम-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, granting peace and<BR>security, conferring happiness or good fortune, pro-<BR>pitious, auspicious.<BR>—क्षेम-कुतूहल, अम्, n. title<BR>of a medical work of Kṣema-śarman.<BR>—क्षेम-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing peace and security.<BR>—क्षेम-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a king of Kāśmīra.<BR>—क्षेमङ्-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, promoting well-being, causing<BR>peace and security, propitious, &c.; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a king of Trigarta; N. of a mythical Buddha; N.<BR>of a son of Brahma-datta (Udayana); (ई), f. the<BR>Brāhmaṇī kite or Coromandel eagle, considered as a<BR>bird of good omen, Falco Ponticerianus; a form of<BR>the goddess Durgā; N. of another goddess; N. of<BR>a sister of Kṣemaṅ-kara.<BR>—क्षेम-जित्, त्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—क्षेम-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, better,<BR>happier.<BR>—क्षेम-दर्शिन्, ई, m., N. of a prince of<BR>the Kosalas.<BR>—क्षेमदर्शीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating<BR>to this prince.<BR>—क्षेम-धन्वन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>prince, a son of Puṇḍarīka.<BR>—क्षेम-धर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—क्षेम-धूर्त, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people.<BR>—क्षेम-धूर्ति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a warrior.<BR>—क्षेम-धृत्वन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>man with the patronymic Pauṇḍarīka.<BR>—क्षेम-<BR>फला, see क्षेमा-फला.<BR>—क्षेम-भूमि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince.<BR>—क्षेम-मूर्ति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a prince.<BR>—क्षेम-युक्तम्, ind. both quietly and<BR>energetically; in rest and exertion.<BR>—क्षेम-राज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—क्षेम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>accompanied with tranquillity and security; prosper-<BR>ous, happy; (ती), f., N. of a woman.<BR>—क्षेम-<BR>वृद्धि, इस्, m., N. of a general of the Śālvas.<BR>—क्षेम-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of an author.<BR>—क्षेमादित्य (˚म-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—क्षेमाधि (˚म-आधि), इस्, m., N. of a prince<BR>of Mithilā.<BR>—क्षेमा-फला, f. the tree Ficus<BR>Oppositifolia; [cf. उदुम्बर.]<BR>—क्षेमारि (˚म-<BR>अरि), इस्, m., N. of a prince of Mithilā, = क्षेमाधि.<BR>—क्षेमार्चिस् (˚म-अर्˚), इस्, m. = क्षेम-जित्.<BR>—क्षेमेन्द्र (˚म-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of a list of regents of Kāśmīra; N. of a lexico-<BR>grapher; also of the author of a Buddhist work.<BR>—क्षेमेन्द्र-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a work by<BR>Kṣemendra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमक|क्षेमकः
क्षेमक, अस्, m. a kind of perfume, = चौर;<BR>N. of a Nāga; N. of a Rakṣas; N. of an attendant<BR>of Śiva; N. of an old king; of a son of Alarka; of<BR>the last descendant of Parīkṣit in the Kali-yuga; N.<BR>of a son of Nirāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमयत्
क्षेमयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. resting; granting<BR>rest or an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमिन्
क्षेमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, enjoying peace and security,<BR>safe, secure, happy, well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम्य|क्षेम्यं|क्षेम्यः
क्षेम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, resting, at leisure, at ease;<BR>habitable, comfortable; healthy, salubrious; lucky,<BR>prosperous, thriving; giving peace and tranquillity;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Śiva; N. of several princes, a son of<BR>Sunītha and father of Ketumat; of a son of Ugrā-<BR>yudha and father of Suvīra; of a son of Śuci and<BR>father of Suvrata; (अम्), n., Ved. resting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेय
क्षेय क्षेय. See under rt. 4. क्षि, p. 266.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेव्
क्षेव् क्षेव्, cl. 1. P. क्षेवति, another<BR>form for क्षिव् or क्षीव्, ‘to spit,’ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षै
क्षै क्षै, cl. 1. P. क्षायति, चक्षौ, क्षा-<BR>स्यति, क्षातुम्, to wane; to waste away, dry<BR>up, decline, become emaciated; [cf. 4. क्षि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम|क्षामः
क्षाम, अस्, आ, अम्, wasted, dried up. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैण्य|क्षैण्यं
क्षैण्य क्षैण्य, अम्, n. (fr. क्षीण), destruc-<BR>tion, wasting away; leanness, slenderness, emaciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत
क्षैत क्षैत, अस्, m. (fr. 1. क्षिति), Ved. the<BR>chief of a race, a prince.<BR>—क्षैत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. princely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्र|क्षैत्रं
क्षैत्र क्षैत्र, अम्, n. (fr. क्षेत्र), a mul-<BR>titude of fields &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रजित्य
क्षैत्रजित्य, अम्, n. (fr. क्षेत्र-जित्), Ved.<BR>acquisition of land, a victorious battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रज्ञ|क्षैत्रज्ञं
क्षैत्रज्ञ or क्षैत्रज्ञ्य, अम्, n. (fr. क्षेत्र-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">Page0271-a+ 71</a>]<BR>ज्ञ), spirituality, the nature of the soul; the know-<BR>ledge of the soul &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रपत्य
क्षैत्रपत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. क्षेत्र-पति),<BR>Ved. belonging to the lord of the soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैप्र|क्षैप्रं
क्षैप्र क्षैप्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्षिप्र), a<BR>term for a kind of Sandhi, produced by changing the<BR>first of two concurrent vowels to its semivowel;<BR>the Svarita accent on a syllable formed with this<BR>Sandhi; (अम्), n. quickness, speediness.<BR>—क्षैप्र-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, joined by the Kṣaipra Sandhi.<BR>—क्षैप्र-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, containing a semi-<BR>vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैरकलम्भि
क्षैरकलम्भि क्षैरकलम्भि, इस्, m. (a pa-<BR>tronymic fr. क्षीर-कलम्भ), N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैरेय
क्षैरेय क्षैरेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्षीर), pre-<BR>pared with milk, milky; (ई), f. milk and rice or any<BR>preparation of or dish prepared with milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोट्
क्षोट् क्षोट्, cl. 10. P. क्षोटयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to throw, cast; [cf. खोट् and खोड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोड|क्षोडः
क्षोड क्षोड, अस्, m. the post to which an<BR>elephant is fastened; [cf. अ-क्षोभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोण
क्षोण क्षोण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. immovable;<BR>or (अस्), m. a kind of lute; (perhaps the word is re-<BR>lated to the following.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोणी
क्षोणी क्षोणी, f., Ved. the earth; (यौ),<BR>du. heaven and earth; (according to some the sing. of<BR>this word and sometimes the plur. may be used col-<BR>lectively, and the original meaning may be ‘a multitude<BR>of men’ or ‘the people’ (as opposed to the chief); the<BR>du. may then mean ‘the two sets of people,’ i. e. the<BR>inhabitants of heaven and earth; sometimes a form<BR>क्षोणि occurs); [cf. Gr. χθών.]<BR>—क्षोणी-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, containing the earth in himself, ‘the<BR>source of everything in the earth;’ an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu in his fish-incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोत्तृ
क्षोत्तृ क्षोत्तृ. See under rt. क्षुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोद|क्षोदः
क्षोद क्षोद. See under rt. क्षुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोधुक
क्षोधुक क्षोधुक. See under rt. 1. क्षुध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभ|क्षोभः
क्षोभ क्षोभ, क्षोभण, &c. See under<BR>rt. 1. क्षुभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोम|क्षोमं|क्षोमः
क्षोम क्षोम, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. क्षु), a room on the top of a house; (अम्), n.<BR>wove silk; [cf. क्षौम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोमक|क्षोमकः
क्षोमक क्षोमक, अस्, m. a kind of perfume<BR>(गणहासक); [cf. क्षेम and क्षौमक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणी
क्षौणी क्षौणी, ई or इस्, f. the earth; [cf.<BR>क्षोणी.]<BR>—क्षौणी-तल, अम्, n. the surface of<BR>the earth.<BR>—क्षौणी-प्राचीर, अस्, m. the ocean.<BR>—क्षौणी-भुज्, क्, m. earth-possessor, a king;<BR>[cf. क्षिति-भुज्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्र|क्षौद्रं|क्षौद्रः
क्षौद्र क्षौद्र, अस्, m. (fr. क्षुद्र and<BR>क्षुद्रा), the tree Michelia Champaca (चम्पक);<BR>N. of a mixed caste, the son of a Vaideha and a<BR>Māgadhī; (अम्), n. smallness, minuteness; N. of a<BR>Sūtra of the Sāma-veda; honey, a species of honey;<BR>water.<BR>—क्षौद्र-ज, अम्, n. wax.<BR>—क्षौद्र-<BR>धातु, उस्, m. a kind of mineral substance; [cf. मा-<BR>क्षिक.]<BR>—क्षौद्र-प्रिय, अस्, m., N. of a tree;<BR>[cf. जल-मधूक.]<BR>—क्षौद्र-मेह, अस्, m.<BR>the disease diabetes mellitus.<BR>—क्षौद्रमेहिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, affected with this disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रेय|क्षौद्रेयं
क्षौद्रेय, अम्, n. wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रक्य|क्षौद्रक्यं
क्षौद्रक्य क्षौद्रक्य, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. क्षु-<BR>द्रक), a prince or princess of the Kṣudrakas, a<BR>man belonging to the Kṣudrakas; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>small, minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रकमालवी
क्षौद्रकमालवी, f., scil. सेना, the army of<BR>Kṣudraka and Mālava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौम|क्षौमं|क्षौमः
क्षौम क्षौम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. क्षुमा), made<BR>of linen, linen, covered with linen; prepared from<BR>linseed (as oil); (अम्), n. linen cloth or garment;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">Page0271-b+ 75</a>]<BR>linseed; (ई), f. lin or flax, Linum Usitatissimum;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. wove silk; an airy room on the<BR>top of a house; an apartment on the roof; the back<BR>of an edifice; a fortified place in front of a building;<BR>a building of a particular form; [cf. क्षोम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौमक|क्षौमकः
क्षौमक, अस्, ई, अम्, linen; (अस्), m. a parti-<BR>cular perfume; [cf. चोर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौर|क्षौरं
क्षौर क्षौर, अम्, n. (fr. क्षुर), shaving<BR>the head, shaving in general; (ई), f. a razor.<BR>—क्षौ-<BR>र-करण, अम्, n. the operation of shaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौरपव्य|क्षौरपव्यं
क्षौरपव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. क्षुर-पवि),<BR>formed out of razors and thunderbolts, very sharp,<BR>very hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौरिक|क्षौरिकः
क्षौरिक, अस्, m. a barber, a shaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णु
क्ष्णु क्ष्णु, cl. 2. P. क्ष्णौति, चुक्ष्णाव,<BR>क्ष्णवितुम्, to whet, sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णुत्
क्ष्णुत्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of compounds) sharp<BR>(e. g. उभयतः-क्ष्णुत्, sharp on both sides).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णुत|क्ष्णुतः
क्ष्णुत, अस्, आ, अम्, whetted, sharpened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णोत्र|क्ष्णोत्रं
क्ष्णोत्र, अम्, n., Ved. a grind-stone, a whet-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मा
क्ष्मा क्ष्मा, f. (fr. rt. क्षम्), the earth,<BR>(Ved. only inst. sing. क्ष्मया); [cf. क्षमा.]<BR>क्ष्मा-ज, अस्, m. ‘earth-born,’ the planet Mars.<BR>—क्ष्मा-तल, अम्, n. the surface of the earth.<BR>—क्ष्मा-धृति, इस्, m. one who has to support the<BR>earth, a king.<BR>—क्ष्मा-प, अस्, m. earth-protector,<BR>a king.<BR>—क्ष्मा-पति, इस्, m. lord of the earth, a<BR>king.<BR>—क्ष्मा-पाल, अस्, m. earth-protector, a king.<BR>—क्ष्मा-भुज्, क्, m. possessor of the earth, a king.<BR>—क्ष्मा-भृत्, त्, m. supporter of the earth; a<BR>mountain; a king.<BR>—क्ष्मा-वृष, अस्, m. ‘earth-<BR>bull,’ i. e. a mighty king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माय्
क्ष्माय् क्ष्माय्, cl. 1. A. क्ष्मायते, च-<BR>क्ष्माये, क्ष्मायितुम्, to shake,<BR>tremble: Caus. क्ष्मापयति, -यितुम्, अचिक्ष्म-<BR>पत्, to cause to shake, to make tremble: Desid.<BR>चिक्ष्मायिषते: Intens. चाक्ष्माय्यते, चाक्ष्-<BR>माति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मायित|क्ष्मायितः
क्ष्मायित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, made to tremble,<BR>trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मायितृ
क्ष्मायितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, trembling, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मील्
क्ष्मील् क्ष्मील्, cl. 1. P. क्ष्मीलति, चिक्ष्-<BR>मील, क्ष्मीलितुम्, to wink, to<BR>twinkle, to close the eyelids; [cf. मील्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्रौम्
क्ष्रौम् क्ष्रौम्, ind. a mystical exclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विङ्का
क्ष्विङ्का क्ष्विङ्का, f., Ved. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विड्
क्ष्विड् क्ष्विड् or क्ष्विद्, cl. 1. P. क्ष्वे-<BR>डति or क्ष्वेदति, -डितुम् or -दितुम्,<BR>to utter an inarticulate sound, to hum, murmur, growl,<BR>roar, hiss, whiz, whistle; A. क्ष्वेडते or क्ष्वेदते,<BR>or cl. 4. P. क्ष्विद्यति, to be wet or unctuous; to<BR>exude, discharge juice, emit sap: Caus. क्ष्वेडयति<BR>or -दयति, -यितुम्, to sound inarticulately, hum, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विण्ण|क्ष्विण्णः
क्ष्विण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded inarticulately; soft,<BR>unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेड|क्ष्वेडं|क्ष्वेडः
क्ष्वेड, अस्, आ, अम् (in some senses perhaps con-<BR>nected with rt. क्ष्वेल्), curved, crooked, bending,<BR>bent; wicked, depraved; difficult to be approached;<BR>(अस्), m. singing or buzzing in the ear from harden-<BR>ing of the wax &c.; sound, noise; venom, poison;<BR>a Cucurbitaceous plant, Luffa Pentandra or Acutangula,<BR>= पीतघोषा; a mystical N. of the letter म्; (अम्),<BR>n. the flower of the Ghoṣa plant; the fruit of a red<BR>kind of swallow-wort; (आ), f. the roaring of a lion,<BR>a war-whoop, a battle-cry; a bamboo rod or stake;<BR>a kind of Cucurbitaceous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेडन|क्ष्वेडनं
क्ष्वेडन, अम्, n. murmuring, hissing, whistling,<BR>sibilating; a hissing pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेडित|क्ष्वेडितं|क्ष्वेडितः
क्ष्वेडित, अस्, अम्, m. n. humming, murmuring,<BR>growling; a growl, roar; a battle-cry, a war-whoop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेडिन्
क्ष्वेडिन्, ई, इनी, इ, humming, murmuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेल्
क्ष्वेल् क्ष्वेल्, cl. 1. P. क्ष्वेलति, &c.,<BR>to leap, jump; to play; to go, move;<BR>to shake, tremble; [cf. Old Germ. suillu, sual,<BR>suall.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेलिका
क्ष्वेलिका, f. or क्ष्वेलित, अस्, अम्, m. n. or<BR>क्ष्वेल्य, अम्, n. play, jest, joke, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख 1. ख, the second consonant of the<BR>alphabet, being the aspirate of the preceding conso-<BR>nant, and having the sound of kh in inkhorn.<BR>—ख-<BR>कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख 2. ख, अस्, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख 3. ख, अम्, n. (fr. rt. खन्), a cavity,<BR>hollow, cave, cavern, aperture; an aperture of the<BR>human body (of which there are nine, as the mouth,<BR>the two ears, the two eyes, the two nostrils, and the<BR>organs of excretion and generation); the glottis (in<BR>anatomy); an organ of sense; the hole made by<BR>an arrow, a wound; the hole in the nave of a<BR>wheel through which the axis runs; vacuity, empty<BR>space, air, ether, sky, heaven; the character in arith-<BR>metic which expresses nothing, a cypher; a dot,<BR>Anusvāra, represented by a circle (विन्दु); a city, a<BR>field; happiness, pleasure, auspiciousness [cf. सुख<BR>and दुःख]; understanding, knowledge; action;<BR>the tenth from any given constellation or the sun's<BR>entrance into it; talc; Brahma, the supreme spirit;<BR>(आ), f. a fountain, a well; [cf. Gr. χάος; Lat.<BR>halo.]<BR>—ख-कामिनी, f. the female of the Falco<BR>Cheela (चिल्ल); an epithet of Durgā (चर्चिका).<BR>—ख-कुन्तल, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—ख-<BR>खोल्क, अस्, m. ‘sky-meteor,’ an epithet of the sun.<BR>—खखोल्कादित्य (˚क-आद्˚), अस्, m. a form of<BR>the sun.<BR>—ख-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, moving in the air;<BR>(अस्), m. a bird; air, wind; the sun; a planet; a<BR>grasshopper; a deity; an arrow.<BR>—ख-गङ्गा, f.<BR>the Gaṅgā (Ganges) of the sky.<BR>—ख-गण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a prince, a son of Vajra-nābha.<BR>—ख-गति,<BR>इस्, f. flight in the air; N. of a metre, [cf. अश्व-<BR>गति.]<BR>—खग-पति, इस्, m. the chief of the birds,<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa, the vehicle of Viṣṇu.<BR>—ख-<BR>गम, अस्, आ, अम्, moving in the air, flying, an epi-<BR>thet of the Gandharvas and of missile weapons; (अस्),<BR>m. a bird; N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—ख-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a mythical person with Buddhists.<BR>—खग-<BR>वक्त्र, अस्, m. the tree Artocarpus Lacucha (लकुच).<BR>—खग-वती, f. the earth.<BR>—खग-शत्रु, उस्,<BR>f. a plant, commonly called Chakulīya, Hemionitis<BR>Cordifolia; [cf. पृश्नि-पर्णी.]<BR>—खग-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. the hollow of a tree; a bird's nest.<BR>—खगा-<BR>धिप (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m. the chief of the birds,<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—खगान्तक (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a hawk, a falcon (a destroyer of birds).<BR>—ख-<BR>गाभिराम (˚ग-अभ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—खगासन (˚ग-आस्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of the<BR>mountain Udaya, the eastern mountain, on which the<BR>sun rises; an epithet of Viṣṇu (‘sitting on a bird,’<BR>i. e. on Garuḍa).<BR>—ख-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, (in arith-<BR>metic or algebra) having a cypher as multiplier.<BR>—खगेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚), अस्, m. the chief of the<BR>birds, an epithet of Garuḍa; N. of a prince.<BR>—ख-<BR>गेन्द्र-ध्वज, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—ख-<BR>गेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the chief of the birds,<BR>epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—ख-गोल, अस्, m. the vault or<BR>circle of the heaven, the celestial sphere.<BR>—खगोल-<BR>विद्या, f. knowledge of the celestial sphere, astronomy.<BR>—ख-चमस, अस्, m. the moon (‘the drinking-<BR>vessel in the sky’).<BR>—ख-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, moving<BR>in the air, flying; (अस्), m. a bird; a cloud; the<BR>wind; the sun; a Rakṣas or demon; an aerial<BR>spirit; N. of a people.<BR>—ख-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, moving<BR>in the air, flying, an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—ख-जल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘air-water,’ i. e. dew, rain, frost, hoar-frost.<BR>—ख-जित्, त्, m. a Buddha, one of the seven teachers<BR>or saints of the Buddha sect.<BR>—ख-ज्योतिस्, इस्, m. a<BR>shining flying insect, a fire-fly, &c.<BR>—ख-तमाल,<BR>अस्, m. a cloud; smoke.<BR>—ख-तिलक, अस्, m. the<BR>sun.<BR>—ख-दूर-वासिनी, f., N. of one of the female<BR>deities or Śaktis with Buddhists.<BR>—ख-द्योत, अस्,<BR>m. a shining flying insect, a fire-fly, the sun; (आ), f.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-a" target="_blank">Page0272-a+ 75</a>]<BR>scil. द्वार्, the door which shines like a shining insect,<BR>an eye.<BR>—ख-द्योतक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a<BR>kind of plant with a poisonous fruit.<BR>—ख-द्योतन,<BR>अस्, m. the sun.<BR>—ख-धूप, अस्, m. a rocket, fire-<BR>work.<BR>—ख-पराग, अस्, m. darkness.<BR>—ख-<BR>पुष्प, अम्, n. a flower in the sky, a term for any-<BR>thing impossible.<BR>—ख-भ, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a planet.<BR>—ख-भ्रान्ति, इस्, f. a kind of falcon, a<BR>kite; [cf. चिल्ल.]<BR>—ख-मणि, इस्, m. the jewel of<BR>the sky, the sun.<BR>—ख-मीलन, अम्, n. sleepiness,<BR>lassitude, weariness.<BR>—ख-मूर्ति, इस्, f. a celestial<BR>appearance or person.<BR>—खमूर्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having a divine or celestial person or form.<BR>—ख-<BR>मूलि, इस्, इका or ई, f. an aquatic plant, Pistia Stratiotes<BR>(कुम्भिका).<BR>—ख-वल्ली, f., N. of a parasitic plant,<BR>= आकाश-वल्ली.<BR>—ख-वारि, इ, n. rain-water, dew,<BR>vapour, &c.<BR>—ख-वाष्प, अस्, m. snow, hoar-frost,<BR>dew.<BR>—ख-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, resting or dwelling in<BR>the air.<BR>—ख-शरीर, अम्, n. a celestial or immortal<BR>body.<BR>—खशरीरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, gifted with an etherial<BR>body, having a heavenly form.<BR>—ख-श्वास, अस्, m.<BR>wind, air.<BR>—ख-सम, अस्, m. a Buddha or deified<BR>Bauddha saint.<BR>—ख-समुत्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>in the sky.<BR>—ख-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>in the sky, aerial, etherial; (आ), f. spikenard, = आकाश-<BR>मांसी.<BR>—ख-सर्पण, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha or<BR>Bauddha saint; (अम्), n. gliding through the air.<BR>—ख-सिन्धु, उस्, m. the moon.<BR>—ख-स्तनी, f.<BR>the earth.<BR>—ख-स्फटिक, अम्, n. aerial crystal,<BR>a N. for the sun and moon-gem, सूर्य-कान्त<BR>and चन्द्र-कान्त; [cf. आकाश-स्फटिक.]<BR>—ख-<BR>हर, अस्, आ, अम्, (in arithmetic) having a cypher<BR>for its denominator (as a fraction).<BR>—खात्मन् (ख-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having the air as one's nature.<BR>—खा-<BR>पगा (ख-आप्˚), f. a stream in the air, an epithet of<BR>the Ganges.<BR>—खे-गमन, अस्, m. a kind of galli-<BR>nule, = काल-कण्ठ.<BR>—खे-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, moving<BR>in the air, flying, aerial; (अस्), m. a bird; a Gan-<BR>dharva; a Rakṣas; a Vidyādhara; an epithet of Śiva;<BR>a planet; quicksilver; (ई), f. a semi-divine female<BR>able to fly; an epithet of Durgā; (अम्), n. green<BR>vitriol.<BR>—खेचर-त्व, अम्, n. capability of flying.<BR>—खे ऽट (खे-अट), अस्, m. a planet; the ascend-<BR>ing node or Rāhu.<BR>—खे-परिभ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>flying about in the air.<BR>—खे-शय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>lying in the air.<BR>—खोल्क (ख-उल्का), अस्, m. a<BR>meteor; a planet; [cf. ख-खोल्क.]<BR>—खोल्मुक<BR>(ख-उल्˚), अस्, m. the planet Mars; [cf. गगनोल्-<BR>मुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

