खटक, अस्, m. a go-between, a man whose<BR>business is to negociate marriages [cf. घटक]; the<BR>half-closed hand; the doubled fist of wrestlers or<BR>boxers.<BR>—खटका-मुख, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a particular position of the hand in shooting; (अस्),<BR>m. a man in the attitude of shooting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटिक|खटिकः
खटिक, अस्, m. the hand half-closed, the fist;<BR>(आ), f. chalk [cf. कक्खटी, कठिनी, &c.]; the ex-<BR>ternal opening of the ear; the plant Andropogon<BR>Muricatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटक्किका
खटक्किका खटक्किका, f. a side door; [cf.<BR>खडक्किका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटखटाय
खटखटाय खटखटाय (an onomatopoetic<BR>word), A. -टायते, -यितुम्, to spring or issue forth<BR>with a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटिनी
खटिनी खटिनी or खटी, f. chalk; (some<BR>books read खठिनी); [cf. कठिनी, खटिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटू
खटू खटू (?), an ornament worn on the<BR>wrist or ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्ट्
खट्ट् खट्ट्, cl. 10. P. खट्टयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cover, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टन|खट्टनः
खट्टन खट्टन, अस्, m. a dwarf [cf. खट्टे-<BR>रक]; (अस्, आ, अम्), dwarfish, short of stature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टा
खट्टा खट्टा, f. a bedstead; a kind of grass,<BR>Andropogon Serratus; (a wrong reading for खट्वा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टाश|खट्टाशः
खट्टाश खट्टाश, अस्, m. the civet or zebet<BR>cat, Viverra Zibetha; (ई), f. the same or (according<BR>to another authority) a different animal; (some write<BR>the word खट्टास.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टि|खट्टिः
खट्टि खट्टि, इस्, ई, m. f. a bier, the bed on<BR>which the corpse is carried to the pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टिक|खट्टिकः
खट्टिक खट्टिक, अस्, m. a butcher, a hunter,<BR>a fowler, one who lives by killing and selling game;<BR>the cream on the milk of a buffalo-cow; (आ), f. a<BR>small bedstead, a cot; a bier or bed on which the<BR>corpse is carried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टेरक|खट्टेरकः
खट्टेरक खट्टेरक, अस्, आ, अम्, dwarfish,<BR>dwarf; [cf. खट्टन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वा
खट्वा खट्वा, f. (said to be fr. rt. खट्), a<BR>bedstead, a couch, a cot; a swing, a hammock; a<BR>kind of bandage; N. of a plant, = कोलशिम्बी.<BR>—ख-<BR>ट्वाङ्ग (˚वा-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a club shaped like the foot<BR>of a bedstead,’ i. e. a club or staff with a skull at the<BR>top considered as the weapon of Śiva and carried by<BR>ascetics and Yogis; wood from a funeral pile; N. of<BR>a king of the solar line, = Dilīpa; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—खट्वाङ्ग-धार, अस्, m. or खट्वाङ्ग-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘staff-bearer,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—खट्वाङ्ग-वन, अम्, n., N. of a forest.<BR>—ख-<BR>ट्वाङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the staff described above; (ई),<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—खट्वाप्लुत (˚वा-आप्˚) or<BR>खट्वारूढ (˚वा-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted on a<BR>bed, lying on a bed: low, vile, abandoned, iniquitous;<BR>erring, going wrong; silly, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्विका
खट्विका, f. a small bedstead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्
खड् खड्, cl. 10. P. खाडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to divide, tear, break, break off a part or<BR>piece; [cf. खण्ड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड|खडं|खडः
खड, अस्, m. breaking, dividing; buttermilk<BR>boiled with acid vegetables and spices; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a kind of small grass, straw; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—खडोन्मत्ता (˚ड-उन्˚), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडक्किका
खडक्किका खडक्किका, f. a private or back<BR>door, a small or venetian door or window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडतू
खडतू खडतू, ऊस्, m. a kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडिका
खडिका खडिका or खडी, f. chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडु|खडुः
खडु खडु, उस्, or खडू, ऊस्, m. or f. a bier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्ग|खड्गं|खड्गः
खड्ग खड्ग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. खड्<BR>for खण्ड्), a sword, a scymitar; a large sacrificial<BR>knife; the horn of a rhinoceros; a rhinoceros; one<BR>of the Buddhas or Buddhist saints, a Pratyeka-buddha,<BR>so called because he walks alone like a rhinoceros [cf.<BR>एक-चर and एक-चारिन्]; (अम्), n. iron.<BR>—खड्ग-<BR>कोश, अस्, m. the sheath of a sword, a scabbard; a<BR>creeping plant, Scirpus Maximus.<BR>—खड्ग-चर्म-<BR>धर, अस्, m. a soldier armed with a sword and shield.<BR>—खड्ग-दृह्, -धृक्, क्, क्, grasping a scymitar.<BR>—खड्ग-धर, अस्, m. a swordsman.<BR>—खड्ग-<BR>धेनु, उस्, f. a female rhinoceros; a small knife or<BR>sword, = असि-धेनु.<BR>—खड्ग-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of creeper, Scirpus Maximus; N. of a mythical<BR>tree in hell bearing swords for leaves; (अम्), n. the<BR>blade of a sword.<BR>—खड्ग-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, sword in<BR>hand.<BR>—खड्ग-पात्र, अम्, n. a vessel formed of<BR>buffalo's horns, a large salver or charger on which<BR>the sacrificial knife is laid.<BR>—खड्ग-पिधान or<BR>खड्ग-पिधानक, अम्, n. a scabbard, the sheath<BR>of a sword.<BR>—खड्ग-पुत्रिका, f. a small sword, a<BR>knife.<BR>—खड्ग-प्रहार, अस्, m. a sword-cut.<BR>—खड्ग-फल, अम्, n. a sword-blade.<BR>—खड्ग-<BR>मांस, अस्, m. buffalo-beef.<BR>—खड्ग-लेखा, f. a<BR>row of swords.<BR>—खड्ग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, armed<BR>with a sword.<BR>—खड्गाघात (˚ग-आघ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a sword-cut.<BR>—खड्गाधार (˚ग-आध्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>sheath, a scabbard.<BR>—खड्गाभिहत (˚ग-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, cut or struck with a sword.<BR>—खड्गा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">Page0273-a+ 80</a>]<BR>मिष (˚ग-आम्˚), अम्, n. buffalo's flesh.<BR>—खड्गाह्व<BR>(˚ग-आह्˚), अस्, m. a rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गट|खड्गटः
खड्गट, अस्, m. a large kind of reed, Saccharum<BR>Spontaneum; [cf. बृहत्-काश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गारीट|खड्गारीटः
खड्गारीट or खड्गाराट (?), अस्, m. a shield<BR>or the blade of a sword (?); one who observes a<BR>particular religious penance peculiar to Buddhists,<BR>viz. rubbing the feet backwards and forwards on the<BR>edge of a sword made red hot; [cf. असि-धारा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिक|खड्गिकः
खड्गिक, अस्, m. a swordsman; a butcher, a<BR>vender of flesh meat; the cream of buffalo's milk;<BR>[cf. खट्टिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिन्
खड्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, armed with a sword, a swords-<BR>man; (ई), m. a rhinoceros; N. of a Jina or Jaina<BR>saint.<BR>—खड्गि-मार, अस्, m. a kind of creeper,<BR>Scirpus Maximus, = खड्ग-कोश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गीक|खड्गीकं
खड्गीक, अम्, n. a sickle, a small scythe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खणखणाय
खणखणाय खणखणाय (an onomato-<BR>poetic word), A. खणखणायते, -यितुम्, to utter<BR>or give out any peculiar sound; to tick, tinkle,<BR>crack, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खणखणायमान
खणखणायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, tinkling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड्|खंड्
खण्ड् खण्ड्, cl. 1. A., 10. P. खण्डते,<BR>डितुम्, खण्डयति, -यितुम्, to break,<BR>tear, break in pieces, crush, cut, divide; destroy,<BR>annihilate, defeat, conquer; disappoint, frustrate,<BR>interrupt, disturb, deceive, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड|खंड|खण्डं|खण्डः
खण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, broken, torn asunder, divided,<BR>having chasms, gaps, or breaks; deficient, defective,<BR>crippled; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a break, a gap, a chasm,<BR>a fissure, a fracture (e. g. केदार-खण्ड, a gap or<BR>fracture in the embankment of a field); a piece,<BR>part, fragment, portion; a section of a work, part,<BR>chapter; a party number, multitude, assemblage; a<BR>term in an equation; (अस्), m. treacle or molasses<BR>partially dried, candied sugar; a flaw in a jewel; N.<BR>of a people; (अम्), n. a kind of salt (विड्-लवण),<BR>black salt; a sort of sugar-cane; [cf. उत्तर-खण्ड,<BR>कर्क˚, काल˚, काशी˚.]<BR>—खण्ड-कटक, अस् or<BR>अम्, m. or n. (?), title of an astronomical work com-<BR>posed by Brahma-gupta.<BR>—खण्ड-कथा, f. a<BR>fragmentary tale; a tale or story divided into<BR>sections (?).<BR>—खण्ड-कर्ण, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>bulbous plant; sweet potato.<BR>—खण्ड-काव्य, अम्,<BR>n. a fragmentary poem; a poem interspersed with<BR>prose (?).<BR>—खण्ड-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—खण्ड-ज, अस्, m. a kind of sugar, treacle,<BR>molasses, = गुड, यवास-शर्करा.<BR>—खण्ड-<BR>जोद्भवज (˚ज-उद्˚), अस्, m. a kind of candied<BR>sugar prepared from Khaṇḍaja.<BR>—खण्ड-ता, f. the<BR>being divided, division.<BR>—खण्ड-देव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of the author of a commentary on Jaimini's Nyāya-<BR>sūtras, called Bhāṭṭadīpikā; also of the Mīmāṃsā-<BR>Kaustubha.<BR>—खण्ड-द्रव्य, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—खण्ड-धारा, f. shears, scissors; a kind of<BR>dance or air (?).<BR>—खण्ड-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a bundle<BR>of various leaves.<BR>—खण्ड-परशु, उस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva as cutting his foes to pieces with his<BR>axe.<BR>—खण्ड-पर्शु, उस्, m. a N. of Śiva; of<BR>Paraśu-rāma; of Rāhu; an elephant with a broken<BR>tusk; a spreader of unguents or fragrant powders &c.;<BR>a drug, commonly called Khandāmalaki (see खण्डा-<BR>मलक).<BR>—खण्ड-पाणि, इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—खण्ड-पाल, अस्, m. a confectioner, seller of<BR>sweetmeats (for खण्ड-पाण?).<BR>—खण्ड-प्र-<BR>लय, अस्, m. a partial destruction of the universe in<BR>which all the spheres beneath Svarga or heaven are<BR>dissolved in one common ruin; a quarrel; the dis-<BR>solution of the bands of friendship or of society; (in<BR>the latter sense more correctly खण्ड-प्रणय.)<BR>—खण्ड-प्रशस्ति, इस्, f., N. of a poem attributed<BR>to Hanumat; an older N. for the play Hanuman-nā-<BR>ṭaka.<BR>—खण्ड-फण, अस्, m. a kind of serpent.<BR>—खण्ड-मण्डल, अम्, n. a segment of a circle,<BR>part of a circle, an incomplete sphere; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>gibbous, not full or round.<BR>—खण्ड-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, consisting of pieces.<BR>—खण्ड-मोदक, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of sugar, granulated or candied (यवास-<BR>शर्करा).<BR>—खण्ड-लवण, अम्, n. a kind of salt<BR>(विड्-लवण), black salt.<BR>—खण्ड-शर्करा, f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">Page0273-b+ 78</a>]<BR>candied sugar or sugar in pieces.<BR>—खण्ड-शस्, ind.<BR>in pieces, by pieces, bit by bit, piece by piece, piece-<BR>meal; खण्डशः कृ, to divide or cut into pieces;<BR>खण्डशो भू, to be divided, to be separated into<BR>pieces.<BR>—खण्ड-शाखा, f., N. of a plant, = महि-<BR>ष-वल्ली.<BR>—खण्ड-शीला, f. a loose woman, an un-<BR>chaste wife.<BR>—खण्ड-सर, अस्, m. a kind of sugar<BR>(यवास-शर्करा), candied sugar.<BR>—खण्डाभ्र<BR>(˚ड-अभ्˚), अम्, n. scattered clouds; a bite, the<BR>impression of the teeth in amorous sport.<BR>—खण्डा-<BR>मलक (ड-आम्˚), अम्, n. myrobalan cut up into<BR>small pieces (to be used as a medicine).<BR>—खण्डाली<BR>(˚ड-आली), f. a measure for oil; a pond; a woman<BR>whose husband has been guilty of infidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डक|खंडक|खण्डकः
खण्डक, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking to pieces, de-<BR>stroying, removing, rendering ineffectual; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a fragment, a part, a piece; (अस्), m. treacle<BR>or molasses partially dried, candied sugar; one who<BR>has no nails; pared or clipped finger-nails (?); N. of<BR>a metre, = आर्या-गीति; a kind of dance or tune (?);<BR>[cf. खण्ड-धारा.]<BR>—खण्डकालु or खण्ड-<BR>कालुक (˚क-आलु), अम्, n. an esculent root, sweet<BR>potato.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डन|खंडन|खण्डनं
खण्डन, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking, dividing, cutting,<BR>reducing to pieces, destroying, annihilating, removing;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of breaking or cutting or dividing,<BR>hurting, injuring, injury; interrupting, disappointing,<BR>frustrating; cheating, deceiving; refuting (in argu-<BR>ment); rebellion, opposition; discarding, dismissal.<BR>—खण्डन-कार, अस्, m. an epithet of Harṣa.<BR>—खण्डन-कृत्, त्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—खण्डन-खण्डकाद्य (˚क-आद्˚), अम्, n. title<BR>of a work on logic by Harṣa.<BR>—खण्डन-रत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, skilful in cutting or destroying, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डनीय|खंडनीय
खण्डनीय or खण्डितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>broken or divided, frangible, fragile, brittle; destruc-<BR>tible, refutable, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डल|खंडल|खंडलं|खंडलः|खण्डलः
खण्डल or खण्डव, अस्, अम्, m. n. a piece,<BR>a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिक|खंडिकः|खण्डिकः
खण्डिक, अस्, m. a sugar-boiler, a sugar-baker (?);<BR>pease; the armpit; N. of a man; (आ), f. the pod of<BR>pease; a kind of air or tune in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डित|खंडित|खण्डितं
खण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, torn, broken in pieces,<BR>scattered, dispersed, destroyed; broken as allegiance,<BR>disobeyed against, rebelled; refuted, controverted;<BR>disappointed, betrayed, abandoned as a lover; (आ), f.<BR>a woman whose husband or lover has been guilty of<BR>infidelity.<BR>—खण्डित-विग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, maimed,<BR>mutilated.<BR>—खण्डित-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>manner of life is dissolute, an immoral man.<BR>—खण्-<BR>डिताशंस (˚त-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, disappointed, foiled,<BR>frustrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिन्|खंडिन्
खण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, consisting of pieces, in pieces<BR>or parts; divided, comminuted; (ई), m. a wild kind<BR>of kidney-bean, = Vana-mudga; a N. of Harṣa;<BR>(इनी), f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डीकृ|खंडीकृ
खण्डी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to divide or break into small pieces, to cut up,<BR>tear to pieces &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डीर|खण्डीरः
खण्डीर, अस्, m. a kind of kidney-bean, Pīta-<BR>mudga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डु
खण्डु = खण्ड, a kind of sugar (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डेराय
खण्डेराय, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड्य|खंड्य
खण्ड्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken or divided,<BR>fragile, destructible, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

