खाण्डव|खांडव|खाण्डवं|खांडवः|खाण्डवः
खाण्डव, अस्, m. (fr. खण्डु), sugar-candy,<BR>sugar-plums, sweetmeats; N. of a region; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a forest in Kuru-kṣetra, sacred to Indra and<BR>burnt by the god of fire, Agni, with the assistance<BR>of Arjuna and Kṛṣṇa (see Mahā-bh. I. 8207).<BR>—खाण्डव-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a town<BR>situated in the Khāṇḍava forest, founded by the<BR>Pāṇḍavas, = इन्द्र-प्रस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डवायन
खाण्डवायन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a family of<BR>Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0275-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डविक|खांडविक|खांडविकः|खाण्डविकः
