गवेडु|गवेडुः
गवेडु गवेडु, उस्, m. a cloud; (उस्), f. or<BR>गवेडुका, f. a kind of grass, Coix Barbata; [cf. the<BR>following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेधु|गवेधुः
गवेधु गवेधु, उस्, f. the grass Coix Barbata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेधुक|गवेधुकं
गवेधुक, अस्, m. a kind of serpent; (आ), f. a<BR>species of grass, Coix Barbata; according to some<BR>authorities also Hedysarum Lagopodioides [cf. गवे-<BR>शका]; (अम्), n. red chalk; [cf. गवीधुक, गवेडु,<BR>गवेरुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेरुक|गवेरुकं
गवेरुक गवेरुक, अम्, n. red chalk; [cf.<BR>गवेधुक, n.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेशका
गवेशका गवेशका, f. the plant Hedysarum<BR>Lagopodioides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्
गह् गह् (connected with गाह्), cl. 10. P.<BR>गहयति, -यितुम्, to be thick or imper-<BR>vious (?); to enter deeply into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह, अस्, m. a cave; a forest (?); [cf. दुर्-गह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहन|गहनं|गहनः
गहन, अस्, आ, अम्, deep, dense, thick, imper-<BR>vious, impenetrable, inexplicable, hard to be under-<BR>stood, inaccessible; (अम्), n. an abyss, a depth; an<BR>inaccessible place, a hiding-place, a thicket, a wood,<BR>impenetrable darkness; a cave; pain, distress; [cf.<BR>गभीर.]<BR>—गहन-त्व, अम्, n. density; imper-<BR>viousness, impenetrability.<BR>—गहन-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having hiding-places or thickets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहनाय
गहनाय, nom. A. गहनायते, -यितुम्, to have<BR>treacherous intentions towards another, (originally, to<BR>lie hid, lie in wait for a person in a secret place, lie<BR>in ambush.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहीय
गहीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a cave or a thicket;<BR>deep, difficult of access, impervious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्मन्
गह्मन्, अ, n., Ved. depth; [cf. गम्भन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्वर|गह्वरं|गह्वरः
गह्वर, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (related to गभीर and<BR>गहन), deep, impervious, impenetrable; (अम्), n.<BR>an abyss, a depth; water; a hiding-place, a thicket;<BR>a wood; an impenetrable secret, a riddle; a cave,<BR>cavern; hypocrisy; weeping; a deep sigh; (ई), an<BR>abyss, a cave, a cavern, a grotto, a recess in a rock<BR>or mountain &c.; (अस्), m. an arbour, a bower.<BR>—गह्वरे-ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being at the bot-<BR>tom or lowest depths, being in the secret recesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्वरित
गह्वरित, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a hiding-place,<BR>concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा 1. गा, cl. 1. or 2. A., 3. P. गाते, जिगाति,<BR>जगौ, अगात्, गास्यति, गातुम् (Ved. गातवे),<BR>(in classical Sanskrit only the aorist of the simple<BR>verb seems to occur), to go, go towards, to come,<BR>approach; to come into any state or condition,<BR>undergo, obtain: Pass. गीयते: Desid. जिगासति or<BR>जिगीषति (?): Intens. जेगीयते: [cf. Gr. βίβημι, ἔβην;<BR>Old Germ. gâm, gâs, gât, &c.; Goth. ga-tvo; Eng.<BR>to go; Germ. gehen; Lith. gaju.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
2. गा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of compounds)<BR>going; [cf. अ-गा, अग्रे-गा, पुरो-गा, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातु|गातुः
1. गातु, उस्, m. (for 2. see col. 3), Ved. going, motion,<BR>unimpeded motion; free space for moving, place of<BR>abode; the earth; a refuge; way, course; egress,<BR>access; progress, increase, welfare; [cf. अरिष्ट-गातु<BR>and तुर-गातु.]<BR>—गातु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. spa-<BR>cious, commodious.<BR>—गातु-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. clearing<BR>the way for unimpeded motion or progress; finding<BR>or opening a way, promoting progress or welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातुय
गातुय or गातूय, nom. P., Ved. गातुयति or<BR>गातूयति, to desire unimpeded motion or free space<BR>for moving, to wish to obtain free progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्र|गात्रं
गात्र, अम्, n. ‘the instrument of moving,’ a limb<BR>or member of the body; the body; the fore-quarter<BR>of an elephant (according to some also n. and f. in<BR>this meaning); (अस्), m., N. of a son of Vaśiṣṭha;<BR>(आ), f. earth.<BR>—गात्र-कर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, emaciating<BR>the body.<BR>—गात्र-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Lakṣmaṇā.<BR>—गात्र-भङ्गा, f. a<BR>kind of cowach, Mucuna Pruritus (= शूक-शिम्बी).<BR>—गात्र-मार्जनी, f. a towel.<BR>—गात्र-यष्टि, इस्,<BR>m. a thin or slender body.<BR>—गात्र-रुह, अम्, n.<BR>the hairs on the body; [cf. अङ्ग-रुह.]<BR>—गात्र-<BR>लता, f. a flexuous or tender body.<BR>—गात्र-वत्, आन्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">Page0287-b+ 73</a>]<BR>m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa and Lakṣmaṇā; (ती), f.,<BR>N. of a daughter of Kṛṣṇa and Lakṣmaṇā.<BR>—गात्र-<BR>विन्द, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa and Lakṣ-<BR>maṇā.<BR>—गात्र-वैरूप्यता, f. deformity of the<BR>limbs.<BR>—गात्र-सङ्कोचिन्, ई, m. the pole-cat, Viverra<BR>Putorius, (which draws up or contracts its body in<BR>order to spring.)<BR>—गात्र-सम्प्लव, अस्, m. a small<BR>bird, the diver, Pelicanus Fusicollis; [cf. प्लव.]<BR>—गात्र-स्पर्श, अस्, m. contact of the limbs.<BR>—गात्रानुलेपनी (˚र-अन्˚), f. fragrant unguents<BR>&c. smeared upon the body, perfume for the person.<BR>—गात्रावरण (˚र-आव्˚), अम्, n. a shield.<BR>—गा-<BR>त्रोत्सादन (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n. cleaning the person<BR>with perfumes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रक|गात्रकं
गात्रक, अम्, n. the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रय
गात्रय, nom. A. गात्रयते, -यितुम्, to be<BR>loosened, or to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाय|गायः
1. गाय, अस्, आ, अम्, going, striding; (अम्), n.<BR>going, motion; [cf. उरु-गाय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा 3. गा, आस्, आस्, अम् (fr. rt. गै), singing,<BR>at the end of a compound [cf. साम-गा]; (आ), f. a<BR>song; a verse or metrical composition; [cf. गाथा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गागनायस
गागनायस गागनायस, अम्, n. (fr. गगन<BR>+ अयस्), meteoric iron (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्ग|गांग|गाङ्गं|गाङ्गः
गाङ्ग गाङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गङ्गा), being in or<BR>on the Ganges, coming from or belonging or relating to<BR>the Ganges; (अम्), n., scil. अम्बु, rain-water of a pecu-<BR>liar kind (supposed to be from the heavenly Ganges);<BR>(अस्), m. a metronymic of Skanda or Kārttikeya;<BR>also of Bhīṣma; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—गाङ्ग-देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—गाङ्गौघ<BR>(˚ग-ओघ), अम्, n. the current of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गायनि|गांगायनि|गांगायनिः|गाङ्गायनिः
गाङ्गायनि, इस्, m. a metronymic of Bhīṣma;<BR>also of Skanda or Kārttikeya; (गङ्गा was the first<BR>wife of Śāntanu, and bore to him the hero Bhīṣma,<BR>before his marriage with Satyavatī; she was also the<BR>receiver of the vivifying principle of Śiva first cast<BR>into Agni, from which principle was generated Kārtti-<BR>keya the god of war); also an epithet of Citra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेय|गांगेय|गाङ्गेयं|गाङ्गेयः
गाङ्गेय, अस्, ई, अम्, being in or on the Ganges;<BR>(अस्), m. a metronymic of Skanda; also of Bhīṣma;<BR>the Hilsa or Illias fish, Clupanodon Ilisha [cf. इल्लिश];<BR>the root of a kind of grass [cf. भद्र-मुस्ता]; (अम्),<BR>n. the root of Scirpus Kysoor or Cyperus Hexastachyus<BR>Communis, = कशेरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्ग्य
गाङ्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being on the Ganges; a<BR>metronymic from Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्ग्यायनि
गाङ्ग्यायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Gāṅgya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गट|गांगट|गांगटः|गाङ्गटः
गाङ्गट गाङ्गट or गाङ्गटक or गाङ्गटेय,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of prawn or shrimp; [cf. गङ्गाटेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेरुकी
गाङ्गेरुकी गाङ्गेरुकी, f. the plant Uraria<BR>Lagopodioides; (अम्), n. the seed of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेष्ठी
गाङ्गेष्ठी गाङ्गेष्ठी, f. the shrub Guilandina<BR>Bonducella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाञ्जिकाय|गांजिकाय|गांजिकायः|गाञ्जिकायः
गाञ्जिकाय गाञ्जिकाय, अस्, m. a quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाडव|गाडवः
गाडव गाडव, अस्, m. a cloud; [cf. गवेडु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढ|गाढं
गाढ गाढ. See under rt. गाह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणगारि
गाणगारि गाणगारि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher;<BR>[cf. गणकारि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणपत
गाणपत गाणपत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गण-पति),<BR>relating to the leader of a troop or to the god Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणपत्य|गाणपत्यः
गाणपत्य, अस् (f. -ती), अम्, relating to the leader of<BR>a troop or to the god Gaṇeśa; (अस्), m. a worshipper<BR>of Gaṇeśa; (अम्), n. worship of him, chieftainship,<BR>presidency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणिक
गाणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गण), familiar with the<BR>Gaṇas (in grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणिक्य|गाणिक्यं
गाणिक्य, अम्, n. (fr. गणिका), an assemblage of<BR>harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणेश|गाणेशः
गाणेश, अस्, m. (fr. गणेश), a worshipper of<BR>Gaṇeśa.<BR>—गाणेशोपपुराण (˚श-उप्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डिव|गांडिव|गांडिवं|गांडिवः|गाण्डिवः
गाण्डिव गाण्डिव. See under गाण्डी next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डी
गाण्डी गाण्डी, f., N. of a plant, from which<BR>the bow Gāṇḍīva was made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डिव|गांडिव|गांडिवं|गांडिवः|गाण्डिवः
गाण्डिव or गाण्डीव, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bow of<BR>Arjuna; presented by Soma to Varuṇa, by him to<BR>Agni, and by Agni to Arjuna, (also said to have<BR>belonged to Prajā-pati, Brahmā, and Siva); a bow<BR>in general.<BR>—गाण्डीव-धन्वन्, आ, m. an epithet<BR>of Arjuna.<BR>—गाण्डीव-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, discharged<BR>from the bow Gāṇḍīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डीविन्|गांडीविन्
गाण्डीविन्, ई, m. an epithet of Arjuna; the tree<BR>Terminalia Arjuna; [cf. अर्जुन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डीर
गाण्डीर गाण्डीर, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from<BR>the plant Gaṇḍīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातव्य
गातव्य गातव्य. See under rt. गै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातागतिक
गातागतिक गातागतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गता-<BR>गत), caused by going and coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातानुगतिक
गातानुगतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गतानुगत), caused<BR>by following or imitating what precedes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातु|गातुः
गातु 2. गातु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. गै), a song; a<BR>singer; a Gandharva or celestial chorister; the male<BR>Koïl or Indian cuckoo; a bee; N. of a descendant of<BR>Atri, author of a hymn of the Ṛg-veda; (उस्, उस्, उ),<BR>angry, wrathful. (For 1. गातु see under 1. गा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातृ
गातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a singer; angry; (ता), m. a<BR>Gandharva; the male Koïl or Indian cuckoo; a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथ|गाथः
गाथ, अस्, m. (also अम्, n. ?), singing, a song;<BR>(आ), f. a verse; (in the terminology of the Brāhmaṇas<BR>and liturgical books) a verse which is neither Ṛc,<BR>nor Sāman, nor Yajus, a religious verse, but not one<BR>belonging to the Vedas; a stanza; a song, a chant or<BR>verse to be chanted or sung; (with Buddhists) a<BR>metrical Sūtra; N. of the Āryā metre; also of a<BR>metre not enumerated in the regular treatises on<BR>prosody.<BR>—गाथ-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of songs.<BR>—गाथा-कार, अस्, m. an author of songs, hymns,<BR>verses; a singer, a reciter.<BR>—गाथा-नी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved.<BR>leading the song, leading a choir.<BR>—गाथान्तर<BR>(˚था-अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Kalpa, the fourth day in<BR>Brahmā's month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथक|गाथकः
गाथक, अस्, m. a singer, a musician; a chanter<BR>of the Purāṇas or sacred poems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथिक|गाथिकः
गाथिक, अस्, m. one who recites Gāthas, hymns<BR>or verses; (आ), f. a song, hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथिन्
गाथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, familiar with or knowing songs<BR>or hymns, a singer; (ई), m., N. of a son of Kuśika<BR>and father of Viśvā-mitra; (इनस्), m. pl. the de-<BR>scendants of this man; (इनी), f., N. of a metre,<BR>containing 12 + 18 + 12 + 20 or 32 + 29 syllabic<BR>instants; [cf. वीणा-गाथिन्.]<BR>—गाथि-ज, अस्, m. the<BR>son of Gāthin, i. e. Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथिन
गाथिन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Gāthin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्र|गात्रं
गात्र गात्र. See col. 1. under rt. 1. गा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथ|गाथः
गाथ गाथ. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाद्गद्य
गाद्गद्य गाद्गद्य, अम्, n. (fr. गद्गद),<BR>stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाध्
गाध् गाध् [cf. गाह्, to which this root<BR>is related], cl. 1. A. गाधते, जगाधे,<BR>गाधिष्यते, अगाधिष्ट, गाधितुम्, to stand firmly,<BR>to stay, remain; to set out; to seek, to search or inquire<BR>for, to desire; to compile, string or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाध|गाधः
गाध, अस्, आ, अम्, any place offering firm standing-<BR>ground, fordable (as a river), not very deep, shallow;<BR>(अम्), n. ground for standing on in water, a shallow<BR>place, a ford (sometimes also m.); bottom, soundings;<BR>a place, site; desire of gain, cupidity, covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधि|गाधिः
गाधि गाधि, इस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Viśvā-mitra and king of Kānyakubja, also called<BR>गाधिन्; (अयस्), m. pl. the descendants of Gādhi.<BR>—गाधि-ज, अस्, m. Gādhi's son, a N. of Viśvā-<BR>mitra. गाधिन्, ई, m. (a later form for गाथिन्,<BR>q. v.), = गाधि.<BR>—गाधि-नगर, अम्, n. Gādhi's<BR>city, an epithet of Kānyakubja.<BR>—गाधि-नन्दन,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Gādhi, an epithet of Viśvā-mitra;<BR>also गाधि-पुत्र, अस्, m., गाधि-भू, ऊस्, m., गाधि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">Page0288-a+ 75</a>]<BR>सूनु, उस्, m.<BR>—गाधि-पुर, अम्, n. Gādhi's city,<BR>an epithet of Kānyakubja; [cf. गाधि-नगर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधेय|गाधेयः
गाधेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of Viśvā-mitra;<BR>(ई), f. a patronymic of Satyavatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान|गानं
गान गान, अम्, n. (fr. गै), singing, a song;<BR>a sound; [cf. अरण्य-गान, ऊह-ग्˚, ऊह्य-ग्˚.]<BR>—गान-बन्धु, उस्, m. a friend of songs; N. of a<BR>man (?).<BR>—गान-विद्या, f. the science of vocal music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गानीय
गानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, musical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गानिनी
गानिनी गानिनी, f. Orris root [cf. वचा], a<BR>medicinal plant (supposed to be of use in clearing<BR>the voice; fr. गान?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्तु|गांतुः|गान्तुः
गान्तु गान्तु, उस्, m. (fr. 1. गम्), one who<BR>goes or moves, a goer, a traveller; a singer (in this<BR>sense a wrong form for 2. गातु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्त्री|गांत्री
गान्त्री, f. = गन्त्री, a carriage drawn by oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दम|गांदम
गान्दम गान्-दम, अस्, m. (गान् = गाम्, acc.<BR>fr. गो), N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दिक
गान्दिक गान्दिक, अस्, ई, अम्, born in Gandikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दिनी|गांदिनी
गान्दिनी गान्दिनी, f., N. of a princess of<BR>Kāśi who was the wife of Śvaphalka and mother of<BR>Akrūra (also called गान्दी); an epithet of the river<BR>Ganges or the goddess Gaṅgā; (also read गान्धिनी.)<BR>—गान्दिनी-सुत, अस्, m. a son of Gāndinī, epithet<BR>of Akrūra and of Bhīṣma; [cf. गाङ्गेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दी|गांदी
गान्दी. See गान्दिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्व|गांधर्व|गान्धर्वः|गान्धर्व्वं|गान्धर्व्वः
गान्धर्व गान्धर्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गन्धर्व),<BR>belonging or relating to the Gandharvas (especially<BR>गान्धर्वो विवाहः or विधिः, the form of marriage<BR>called after the Gandharvas, that which requires only<BR>mutual agreement; see गन्धर्व-विवाह); relat-<BR>ing to the Gandharvas as heavenly choristers (e. g.<BR>गान्धर्व-कलाः, song, music, &c.; गान्धर्वो<BR>वेदः or गान्धर्व-वेदः, the Veda of music,<BR>musical science considered as an appendix of the Sāma-<BR>veda and ascribed to Bharata); (अस्), m. a singer in<BR>general; N. of a people in the north-east of Madhya-<BR>deśa; (ई), f. = वाच्, speech, according to the legend<BR>that the gods gave speech to the Gandharvas and<BR>received from them the Soma in return; an epithet<BR>of the goddess Durgā; (अम्), n. the art of the<BR>Gandharvas, song, music, dance; N. of one of the<BR>nine sections of Bhārata-varṣa; [cf. गन्धर्व-<BR>खण्ड.]<BR>—गान्धर्व-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>mind is possessed by the Gandharvas; [cf. गन्धर्-<BR>व-गृहीत.]<BR>—गान्धर्व-शाला, f. music-hall, a<BR>concert-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्विक|गांधर्विक|गांधर्विकः|गान्धर्विकः
गान्धर्विक, अस्, m. a singer; (also read गान्-<BR>धर्वक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धार|गांधार|गान्धारं|गांधारः|गान्धारः
गान्धार गान्धार, अस्, m. a prince of the<BR>Gāndhāris; the third of the seven primary notes<BR>of music; minium or red lead; (ई), f. a princess<BR>of the Gāndhāris (especially the wife of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra); N. of a Vidyā-devī; N. of a Rāgiṇī (?);<BR>with Jainas, a divine being fulfilling the commands<BR>of the twenty-first Arhat of the present Avasarpiṇī;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people and their country,<BR>commonly called Kandahar, and lying between the<BR>north of India and Persia [cf. गन्धार, गन्धारि,<BR>गान्धारि]; (ई), f., N. of two plants, Hedysarum<BR>Alhagi and Prickly Nightshade, = यवास and<BR>दुर्-आलभा; (अम्), n. gum myrrh; [cf. गन्ध-<BR>रस.]<BR>—गान्धार-राज, अस्, m. the king of Gān-<BR>dhāra, whose name was Su-bala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारक
गान्धारक, आस्, m. pl. = गान्धार, N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारि|गांधारि|गांधारिः|गान्धारिः
गान्धारि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (इस्), m.<BR>a metronymic of Duryodhana; [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारेय|गांधारेय|गांधारेयः|गान्धारेयः
गान्धारेय, अस्, m. a metronymic of Duryodhana,<BR>the son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धिक|गांधिक|गांधिकः|गान्धिकः
गान्धिक गान्धिक, अस्, m. (fr. गन्ध), a<BR>vender of perfumes, a perfumer; a scribe, a clerk; a<BR>kind of worm having a strong fetid smell, commonly<BR>गान्धिपोका, a tree-bug; (अम्), n. fragrant wares,<BR>perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धिनी
गान्धिनी गान्धिनी, f. See under गान्दिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामिक
गामिक गामिक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. गम्, used at<BR>the end of compounds), going, leading to (as a way).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामिन्
गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going, moving on, or in, or<BR>towards, or in any peculiar manner, &c.; going to,<BR>having intercourse with; reaching to, extending to;<BR>coming to one's share, due; attaining, obtaining;<BR>directed towards; relating to; [cf. अग्र-गामिन्,<BR>अन्त-ग्˚, अन्य-ग्˚, आशु-ग्˚, ऋतु-ग्˚, काम-ग्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामुक|गामुकः
गामुक, अस्, आ, अम्, going, locomotive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाम्भीर्य|गांभीर्य|गांभीर्यं|गाम्भीर्य्य|गाम्भीर्य्यं
गाम्भीर्य गाम्भीर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. गम्भीर),<BR>being deep down, being in the depths; (अम्), n.<BR>deepness, depth (of water, sound, &c.); depth or<BR>profundity of character, earnestness, sagacity; the<BR>deep sound of the voice of a Jaina saint, like distant<BR>thunder or the muttering of clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाम्मन्य|गांमन्य
गाम्मन्य गाम्-मन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, thinking<BR>one's self a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाय|गायः
गाय 2. गाय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गय), relating<BR>to Gaya, coming from him, &c. (For 1. गाय see<BR>under 1. गा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाय|गायः
गाय 3. गाय, अम्, n. (fr. rt. गै), a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायक|गायकः
गायक, अस्, ई, अम्, singing, one who sings;<BR>(अस्), m. a singer.<BR>—गायक-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a copyist who lived A. D. 1670.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्
गायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, singing; (अन्ती), f., N. of<BR>Gaya's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्र|गायत्रं|गायत्रः
गायत्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. a song, hymn; (ई), f. an<BR>ancient metre of twenty-four syllables, variously ar-<BR>ranged, but generally as a triplet of three divisions of<BR>eight syllables each; a hymn composed in the Gāyatrī<BR>metre; the Gāyatrī (i. e. Ṛg-veda III. 62, 10, तत्<BR>सवितुर् वरेण्यम् भर्गो देवस्य धीमहि<BR>धियो यो नः प्रचोदयात्. This is a very sacred<BR>verse repeated by every Brāhman at his morning and<BR>evening devotions. From being addressed to Savitṛ<BR>or the Sun as generator, it is also called Sāvitrī. The<BR>Gāyatrī verse is personified as a goddess, the wife of<BR>Brahmā and mother of the four Vedas; and is often<BR>mentioned in connection with the Amṛta, both<BR>together constituting as it were the essence and type<BR>of sacred hymns in general. The Gāyatrī personified<BR>is also considered as the mother of the first three<BR>classes, in their capacity of twice born). According to<BR>the system of the Tāntrikas, a number of mystical<BR>verses are called Gāyatrīs, and each deity has one in<BR>particular; (अम्), n. a hymn composed and recited<BR>in the metre Gāyatrī; (अस्, ई, अम्), consisting in the<BR>Gāyatrī, connected with it, formed in accordance with<BR>it (e. g. in accordance with the number of syllables of<BR>a Gāyatrī verse &c.); (ई), f. the tree Acacia Catechu,<BR>= खदिर; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—गायत्र-<BR>काकुभ, अस्, m. a Pragātha beginning with a<BR>Gāyatrī and ending with a Kakubh.<BR>—गायत्र-<BR>च्छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one to whom the Gāyatrī<BR>metre belongs or to whom it is sacred &c.; relating<BR>to the Gāyatrī metre.<BR>—गायत्र-पार्श्व, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR>—गायत्र-बार्हत, अस्, m. a Pra-<BR>gātha beginning with a Gāyatrī and found where the<BR>Bṛhatī metre predominates.<BR>—गायत्र-वर्तनि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. moving in Gāyatrī measures.<BR>—गायत्र-वे-<BR>पस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. inciting or inspiring to sing hymns.<BR>—गायत्री-भाष्य, अम्, n. title of a commentary<BR>on the Gāyatrī.<BR>—गायत्री-मन्त्र, अस्, m. prayers<BR>connected with the Gāyatrī.<BR>—गायत्री-वल्लभ,<BR>अस्, m. a friend of the Gāyatrī, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—गायत्री-सामन्, अ, n., N. of several verses of the<BR>Sāma-veda, recited in the Gāyatrī metre.<BR>—गायत्र्य्-<BR>आसित, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रि
गायत्रि, इस्, f. = गायत्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रिन्
गायत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who sings hymns; (ई), m.<BR>the tree Acacia Catechu.<BR>—गायत्रि-सार, अस्, m.<BR>Catechu, Terra Japonica; [cf. खदिर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्र्य
गायत्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, epithet of a kind of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायन|गायनः
गायन, अस्, ई, अम्, singing, a singer; (अस्), m. a<BR>singer, a talker, a gossip; N. of an attendant of<BR>Skanda; (अम्), n. singing, song; professing or prac-<BR>tising singing as a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायन्तिका
गायन्तिका, f. (fr. गायन्ती), N. of a place on the<BR>Himālaya mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार
गार गार, अस्, m., N. of a Sāman, com-<BR>posed by Gara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारित्र|गारित्रं
गारित्र गारित्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 2. गॄ), rice,<BR>corn, grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुड|गारुडं|गारुडः
गारुड गारुड, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गरुड), shaped<BR>like the bird Garuḍa, coming from or relating to<BR>Garuḍa; (ई), f., N. of a creeper [cf. पाताल-गरुडी];<BR>(अम्), n. an emerald; gold; a Mantra or charm<BR>against poison.<BR>—गारुड-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of<BR>the seventeenth Purāṇa relating the birth of Garuḍa<BR>from Vinatā. It is doubtful whether a genuine Gā-<BR>ruḍa-Purāṇa exists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडिक|गारुडिकः
गारुडिक, अस्, m. a charmer, a dealer in antidotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुत्मत|गारुत्मतं
गारुत्मत गारुत्मत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गरुत्-<BR>मत्), shaped like the bird Garuḍa, sacred to Garuḍa<BR>&c.; (अम्), n. an emerald; [cf. गरुडाङ्कित, &c.]<BR>—गारुत्मत-पत्त्रिका, f., N. of a plant; [cf.<BR>पाची and मरकत-पत्त्री.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग|गार्गः|गार्ग्ग
गार्ग गार्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गार्ग्य below,<BR>which is derived fr. गर्ग), coming from or con-<BR>nected with Gārgya; a contemptuous metronymic<BR>from Gārgī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गक|गार्गकः|गार्ग्गक
गार्गक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to Gārgya,<BR>worshipping Gārgya; (अम्), n. a multitude or assem-<BR>blage of the descendants of Garga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गिक
गार्गिक, अस्, m. a metronymic from Gārgī, ex-<BR>pressing contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गिका
गार्गिका, f. descent from Garga, the relation to<BR>the school of Gārgya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गी
गार्गी, f. the wife of Gārgya; an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—गार्गी-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of Gārgī; N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR>—गार्गीपुत्रकायणि or गार्गीपुत्रायणि or<BR>गार्गीपुतृ, इस्, m. a descendant of the son of Gārgī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गीभूत
गार्गी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has become a<BR>Gārgya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गीय
1. गार्गीय, nom. P. गार्गीयति, to act like a<BR>Gārgya; A. गार्गीयते, to behave like a Gārgya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गीय
2. गार्गीय, अस्, आ, अम्, composed by Garga; com-<BR>ing from Gārgya; (आस्), m. pl. the pupils of the<BR>descendants of Garga; the pupils of Gārgyāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गेय
गार्गेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Gārgī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्य|गार्ग्यः
गार्ग्य, अस् (f. गी), अम्, descended from Garga, as<BR>a son or daughter; (अस्), m., N. of several teachers of<BR>grammar, of the ritual, &c.; according to Durga, a<BR>Gārgya is the author of the Pada-pāṭha of the Sāma-<BR>veda; N. of a king of the Gandharvas; N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—गार्ग्य-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n. title of a Pari-<BR>śiṣṭa of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्यायण
गार्ग्यायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Gārgya,<BR>N. of a teacher; (ई), f. = गार्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्यायणीय
गार्ग्यायणीय, आस्, m. pl. the pupils of Gārgyāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्त्समद
गार्त्समद गार्त्समद, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Gṛtsa-mada; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्दभ|गार्द्दभ
गार्दभ गार्दभ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गर्दभ),<BR>belonging to or coming from or relating to an ass;<BR>asinine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्दभरथिक|गार्द्दभरथिक
गार्दभरथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गर्दभ-<BR>रथ), fit for a donkey-cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध्य
गार्द्ध्य गार्द्ध्य, अम्, n. (fr. गृद्ध, rt.<BR>गृध्), desire, greediness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ध्र|गार्ध्रः
गार्ध्र (or wrongly spelt गार्ध), अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. गृध्र), derived from a vulture, vulturous, vul-<BR>turine; rapacious, greedy (?); (अस्), m. an arrow;<BR>desire, greediness, cupidity (in the latter sense the<BR>word गार्ध्र is probably a wrong reading for<BR>गार्द्ध्य).<BR>—गार्ध्र-पक्ष, or गार्ध्र-पत्-<BR>त्र, or गार्ध्र-वाजित, or गार्ध्र-राजित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (?), or गार्ध्र-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, decorated<BR>with vulture's feathers (especially an arrow so deco-<BR>rated); [cf. गृध्र-वाज and गृध्र-वाजित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भ
गार्भ गार्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गर्भ), born<BR>from the womb; fetal, uterine; relating to or con-<BR>nected with gestation, also to conception (as any act<BR>or ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिक
गार्भिक, अस्, ई, अम्, fetal, uterine; relating to or<BR>connected with gestation or the fœtus in the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण|गार्भिणं
गार्भिण, अम्, n. (fr. गर्भिणी), a number or<BR>assemblage of pregnant women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण्य|गार्भिण्यं
गार्भिण्य, अम्, n. an assemblage of pregnant<BR>women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्मुत
गार्मुत गार्मुत, अम्, n. (fr. गर्मुत्), honey (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ष्टेय
गार्ष्टेय गार्ष्टेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गृष्टि),<BR>Ved. born from a heifer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत|गार्हपतं
गार्हपत गार्हपत, अम्, n. (fr. गृह-पति),<BR>the position and dignity of a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत्य|गार्हपत्यः
गार्हपत्य, अस्, m., scil. अग्नि, a sacred fire, per-<BR>petually maintained by a householder, received from<BR>his father and transmitted to his descendants, and<BR>from which fires for sacrificial purposes are lighted;<BR>the place where this sacred fire is kept; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a class of manes; (अम्), n. the government<BR>of a family, position of a householder, a household.<BR>—गार्हपत्यागार (˚य-आग्˚), अस्, m. the place in<BR>which the Gārhapatya fire is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हमेध|गार्हमेधः
गार्हमेध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गृह-मेध), fit<BR>or proper for a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हस्थ्य|गार्हस्थ्यं
गार्हस्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. गृह-स्थ), fit for<BR>or incumbent on a householder; (अम्), n. the order<BR>or estate of a householder, of the father or mother of<BR>a family; household, domestic affairs, the house with<BR>its contents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ह्य
गार्ह्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. गृह), domestic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाल|गालः
गाल गाल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. गल्), flowing,<BR>liquefying; dropping; a flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालन|गालनं
गालन, अम्, n. straining fluids; fusing, lique-<BR>fying, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालव|गालवः
गालव, अस्, m. the tree Symplocos Racemosa, the<BR>bark of which is used in dyeing, Lodh; a pale species<BR>of the same, = श्वेत-लोध्र; also a kind of ebony,<BR>Diospyros Glutinosa [cf. केन्दुक]; N. of an old<BR>sage and preceptor, according to the Hari-vaṃśa a son,<BR>and according to the Mahā-bhārata a pupil of Viśvā-<BR>mitra; N. of the author of a Dharma-śāstra; N. of a<BR>grammarian; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Gālava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालवि
गालवि, a patronymic from Gālava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालि|गालिः
गालि, इस्, f. a curse, execration or imprecation.<BR>—गालि-प्रदान, अम्, n. cursing, reviling, abusing.<BR>—गालि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, uttering curses or execra-<BR>tions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालित|गालितः
गालित, अस्, आ, अम्, distilled, strained, dropped,<BR>melted, fused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिन्
गालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, distilling, fusing, liquefying; abus-<BR>ing, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिनी
गालिनी, f. a particular gesticulation or position of<BR>the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोडय
गालोडय गालोडय, A. -डयते, -यितुम्, to<BR>examine, investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोडित|गालोडितः
गालोडित, अम्, n. examination, investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोड्य|गालोड्यं
गालोड्य गालोड्य, अम्, n. the seed of the<BR>lotus; [cf. अङ्कलोड्य, अङ्गलोड्य, गलोड्य, गि-<BR>लोड्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गावल्गणि|गावल्गणिः
गावल्गणि गावल्गणि, इस्, m. (fr. गवल्गण),<BR>a patronymic of Sañjaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाविष्ठिर
गाविष्ठिर गाविष्ठिर and गाविष्ठिरायण,<BR>two patronymics from Gavi-ṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह्
गाह् गाह्, cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.) गाहते,<BR>-ति, जगाहे, गाहिष्यते, अगाहिष्ट, गा-<BR>हितुम् or गाढुम्, to dive into, bathe in, plunge<BR>into, penetrate, enter deeply into; roam, range, rove;<BR>to be absorbed in (with acc.); to hide one's self in:<BR>Caus. गाहयति, -यितुम्, अजीगहत्: Desid. जिगा-<BR>हिषते and जिघाक्षते: Intens. जागाह्यते and<BR>जागाढि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढ|गाढं
गाढ, अस्, आ, अम्, dived into, bathed in, entered<BR>into; deeply entered, closely pressed together, tightly<BR>drawn, closely fastened, close, fast (opposed to शि-<BR>थिल); thick, dense; deep (as sleep); strong, vehe-<BR>ment, firm; (अम्), ind. excessively, much, very<BR>much, heavily, closely, firmly, strongly, &c.<BR>—गाढ-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m. an ear penetrated by sound, an attentive<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">Page0289-b+ 78</a>]<BR>ear.<BR>—गाढ-ता, f. or गाढ-त्व, अम्, n. intensity,<BR>closeness; firmness, hardness; excess.<BR>—गाढ-<BR>मुष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, close-fisted, avaricious, niggardly,<BR>miserly; (इस्), m. a scymitar, a large sacrificial knife.<BR>—गाढ-शोक-प्रहार, अस्, आ, अम्, inflicting the<BR>keenest anguish.<BR>—गाढाङ्गद (˚ढ-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having closely fitting bracelets.<BR>—गाढा-<BR>लिङ्गन (˚ढ-आल्˚), अम्, n. a close embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढीकरण
गाढी-करण, अम्, n. making stiff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह|गाहः
गाह, अस्, ई, अम्, diving into, bathing; (अस्), m.<BR>depth, interior, innermost recess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहन|गाहनं
गाहन, अम्, n. the act of diving into, plunging,<BR>bathing, penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहनीय
गाहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dived into or pene-<BR>trated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहित
गाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, bathed in, plunged into, im-<BR>mersed, entered deeply into, penetrated; shaken,<BR>agitated, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहितृ
गाहितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who plunges into water,<BR>a bather, diver; one who penetrates; shaking,<BR>agitating; destroying, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिन्दुक|गिंदुक|गिंदुकः|गिन्दुकः
गिन्दुक गिन्दुक, अस्, m. a ball for playing<BR>with; [cf. गेन्दुक and कन्दुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर्
गिर् 1. गिर्, ईर्, ईर्, ईर् (fr. 1. गॄ), Ved. ad-<BR>dressing, invoking, praising; (ईर्), f. invocation, ad-<BR>dressing with praise, praise, verse, song; speech,<BR>speaking, language, voice, words (e. g. मानुषीं<BR>गिरं कृ, to assume a human voice; गिराम् प्र-<BR>भविष्णुः, ‘lord of speech or words,’ an epithet of<BR>Bṛhaspati, regent of the planet Jupiter); a N. of<BR>Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech; fame, celebrity;<BR>[cf. Hib. gair, ‘an outcry, a shout;’ Gr. γῆρυς.]<BR>—१. गिर्-ईश, अस्, m. an epithet of Bṛhaspati; [cf.<BR>गीष्-पति.]<BR>—गिर्-वणस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. delighting<BR>in invocations, fond of praise, an epithet of Indra and<BR>Agni.<BR>—गिर्-वणस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. fond of hymns<BR>or praise, an epithet of Indra.<BR>—गिर्-वन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>Ved. addressed with many invocations, receiving much<BR>praise.<BR>—गिर्व-वाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. bearing one who is<BR>addressed with many hymns.<BR>—गिर्-वाहस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. one to whom invocations are addressed,<BR>praised in song, an epithet of Indra &c.<BR>—गीः-<BR>पति = गीष्-पति.<BR>—गी-रथ (गिर्-र˚), अस्, m. ‘the<BR>vehicle of words,’ an epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR>—गीर्-<BR>देवी, f. the goddess of speech, Sarasvatī.<BR>—गीर्-पति<BR>= गीष्-पति.<BR>—गीर्-लता, f., N. of a plant, = महा-<BR>ज्योतिष्मती.<BR>—गीर्-वाण, अस्, m. a god, a deity<BR>(‘whose arrow is speech;’ or perhaps only a cor-<BR>ruption fr. गिर्-वणस्.)<BR>—गीर्वाण-कुसुम, अम्, n.<BR>the flower of the gods, cloves.<BR>—गीष्-पति, इस्, m.<BR>the lord of speech, a N. of Bṛhaspati, the regent of<BR>the planet Jupiter and preceptor of the gods; a Paṇḍit,<BR>a learned man.<BR>—गीस्-तरा, f. excellent speech, a<BR>good voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरा
गिरा, f. speech, speaking; voice.<BR>—गिरा-वृध्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. delighting in being praised; (Sāy.)<BR>thriving by praise (as a god).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर्
गिर् 2. गिर् (fr. 2. गॄ), swallowing, (at the<BR>end of compounds, e. g. in गर-गिर् and मुहुर्-गिर्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर
1. गिर, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरित|गिरितः
गिरित, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowed, eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर
गिर 2. गिर, at the end of an adverbial<BR>compound = गिरि (e. g. अनु-गिरम्, near the moun-<BR>tain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरि|गिरिः
गिरि गिरि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 2. गॄ;<BR>perhaps originally गरि or गरु, and related to गुरु,<BR>गरिमन्), a hill, a mountain, a rock, an elevation,<BR>a rising-ground (in the foregoing senses often con-<BR>nected in the Veda with पर्वत, e. g. पर्वतो<BR>गिरिः, explained by Sāy. as a mountain having<BR>many parts); a cloud (this last sense is often given<BR>to गिरि by the commentators on Vedic works); a term<BR>for the number eight, because of the eight mountains<BR>surrounding the mountain Meru; a wooden ball, with<BR>which children play [cf. गिरिक and गिरि-गुड]; a<BR>disease of the eyes; a peculiar defect in quicksilver;<BR>a honorific title given to one of the ten orders of the<BR>Das-nāmī Gosains; N. of a son of Śvaphalka [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-c" target="_blank">Page0289-c+ 81</a>]<BR>गिरि-क्षिप]; (इस्), f. swallowing; a rat, a small<BR>rat, a mouse [cf. गिरिका]; (इस्, इस्, इ), venerable,<BR>respectable, worshipful; [cf. Zend gairi; Slav.<BR>gora; Afghan. ghur; cf. also गरीयस्, गरिष्ठ,<BR>गरिमन्.]<BR>—गिरि-कच्छप, अस्, m. a kind of tor-<BR>toise living in mountains.<BR>—गिरि-कण्टक, अस्, m.<BR>Indra's thunderbolt.<BR>—गिरि-कदम्ब or गिरि-क-<BR>दम्बक, अस्, m. a species of the Kadamba tree,<BR>mountain Kadamba; [cf. नीप and धारा-क-<BR>दम्ब.]<BR>—गिरि-कदली, f. the mountain or wild<BR>Kadalī.<BR>—गिरि-कन्दर, अस्, m. a cave, a cavern.<BR>—गिरि-कर्णा, f. the plant Clitoria Ternatea; [cf.<BR>अ-पराजिता.]<BR>—गिरि-कर्णिका, f. the earth; the plant<BR>Clitoria Ternatea; a species of Kiṇihī with white<BR>blossoms.<BR>—गिरि-कर्णी, f. the plant Clitoria Ternatea<BR>[cf. the preceding]; another plant, Alhagi Maurorum<BR>= कच्छुरा.<BR>—गिरि-काण, अस्, m. a blind or one-<BR>eyed man, one blind from a particular disease.<BR>—गिरि-कानन, अम्, n. a mountain-grove.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>कूट, अम्, n. the summit of a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>क्षित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. living in mountains or on high,<BR>as Viṣṇu; (त्), m., N. of an Auccāmanyava; [cf.<BR>गैरिक्षित.]<BR>—गिरि-क्षिप, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Śvaphalka; [cf. अरिक्षिप and गिरि.]<BR>—गिरि-गङ्गा,<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR>—गिरि-गुड, अस्, m. a ball for play-<BR>ing with.<BR>—गिरि-गुहा, f. a mountain-cave.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>गैरिक-धातु, उस्, m. = गैरिक, red chalk.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>गैरिकधातु-वत्, ind. like red chalk.<BR>—गिरि-चर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. living in or inhabiting mountains.<BR>—गिरि-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, living in mountains.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, mountain-born, mountaineer; (अस्),<BR>m. the Mahwa tree, Bassia, = मधूल; N. of a man<BR>with the patronymic Bābhravya; (आ), f., N. of several<BR>plants, viz. a kind of lemon tree; a plant considered<BR>as a white species of Rasnā [cf. रस्ना]; the shaddock<BR>or pumple-mouse, Citrus Decumana; also = श्वेत-<BR>वुह्ना, क्षुद्र-पाषाण, गिरि-कदली, कारी, त्रा-<BR>यमाणा; a kind of jasmine, मल्लिका; a N. of the<BR>goddess Pārvatī, as the daughter of the personified<BR>Himālaya mountain; (अम्), n. talc; benzoin or gum<BR>benjamin; it is also confounded with another gum<BR>resin called styrax; red chalk; bitumen; iron.<BR>—गिरिजा-कुमार, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Śaṅka-<BR>rācārya.<BR>—गिरिजा-पति, इस्, m. an epithet of Śiva,<BR>the husband of Pārvatī.<BR>—गिरिजामल (˚ज-अम्˚),<BR>अम्, n. talc.<BR>—गिरि-जाल, अम्, n. a range of moun-<BR>tains.<BR>—गिरिजा-सुत, अस्, m., N. of the chief of a<BR>sect worshipping Gaṇeśa.<BR>—गिरि-ज्वर, अस्, m. Indra's<BR>thunderbolt; [cf. गिरि-कण्टक.]<BR>—गिरि-णद्ध or<BR>गिरि-नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, enclosed by a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-णितम्ब or गिरि-नितम्ब, अस्, m. the declivity<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ruling over<BR>mountains; epithet of Rudra-Śiva.<BR>—गिरि-दुर्ग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or अम्, n. of difficult access in consequence<BR>of being surrounded by mountains; a hill-fort or any<BR>stronghold amongst mountains.<BR>—गिरि-द्वार, अम्,<BR>n. a mountain-pass.<BR>—गिरि-धर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>copyist of the seventeenth century.<BR>—गिरि-धातु,<BR>उस्, m. different kinds of earth or minerals in the<BR>interior of a mountain; red chalk.<BR>—गिरि-ध्वज,<BR>अस्, m. Indra's thunderbolt; [cf. गिरि-कण्टक and<BR>गिरि-ज्वर.]<BR>—गिरि-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a town<BR>in Dakṣiṇā-patha.<BR>—गिरि-नदी or गिरि-णदी, f. a<BR>mountain-torrent.<BR>—गिरि-नन्दिनी, f. daughter of a<BR>mountain, a mountain-stream.<BR>—गिरि-निम्नगा, f. a<BR>mountain-torrent.<BR>—गिरि-निम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant, = महारिष्ट.<BR>—गिरि-पीलु, उस्, m., N. of<BR>a fruit tree, = परुष.<BR>—गिरि-पुर, अम्, n. moun-<BR>tain-town or N. of a town.<BR>—गिरि-पुष्पक, अम्,<BR>n. a fragrant resin, benzoin.<BR>—गिरि-पृष्ठ, अम्, n.<BR>the top of a hill.<BR>—गिरि-प्रपात, अस्, m. the declivity<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-प्रस्थ, अस्, m. the table-land<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of or<BR>frequenting mountains; (आ), f. the female of the<BR>Bos Grunniens.<BR>—गिरि-बान्धव, अस्, m. a friend of<BR>the mountains, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—गिरि-बुध्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. resting on a mountain, produced<BR>on a hill; [cf. अद्रि-बुध्न.]<BR>—गिरि-भिद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>breaking through the mountains, as a river; (त्), f.<BR>the plant Plectranthus Scutellarioides.<BR>—गिरि-भू,<BR>ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, mountain-born, mountaineer; (ऊस्), f., N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">Page0290-a+ 77</a>]<BR>of a plant, = क्षुद्र-पाषाण-भेदा; a small<BR>stone (?); an epithet of Pārvatī, the wife of Śiva.<BR>—गिरि-भ्रज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. breaking forth from<BR>mountains; (Sāy.) falling from the clouds.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>मल्लिका, f. the plant Wrightia Antidysenterica; [cf.<BR>कुट-ज.]<BR>—गिरि-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having the size<BR>or dimensions of a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-मान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the extent or dimensions of a mountain;<BR>(अस्), m. a large and powerful elephant.<BR>—गिरि-माल<BR>and गिरि-मालक, अस्, m., N. of a tree.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>मृद्, त्, f. red chalk, mountain soil; [cf. गैरिक.]<BR>—गिरिमृद्-भव, अम्, n. red chalk.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>मेद, अस्, m. a fetid Mimosa, = अरि-मेद.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>राज्, ट्, m. the king of the mountains, the Himavat (?).<BR>—गिरि-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living on or in mountains,<BR>being or produced in them; (ई), m. a kind of bulb-<BR>ous plant, a large kind of Arum.<BR>—गिरि-व्रज, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the capital of Magadha.<BR>—गिरि-श, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or (अस्), m. inhabiting or frequenting moun-<BR>tains, an epithet of Rudra-Śiva.<BR>—गिरि-शन्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. inhabiting or frequenting mountains.<BR>—गिरि-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. inhabiting mountains.<BR>—गिरि-शाल, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR>—गिरि-शालिनी,<BR>f. the plant Clitoria Ternatea.<BR>—गिरि-शृङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Gaṇeśa; the peak of a mountain.<BR>—गिरि-षद्, त्, त्, त्, sitting on mountains; an epi-<BR>thet of Rudra.<BR>—गिरि-ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, or गिरि-<BR>ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. स्था), inhabiting or frequenting<BR>mountains; epithet of the Maruts and of the Soma<BR>plant which is found in mountains.<BR>—गिरि-सर्प,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of snake.<BR>—गिरि-सानु, उ, n. table-<BR>land.<BR>—गिरि-सार, अस्, m. iron; tin; an epithet of<BR>the Malaya mountains, situated in the south of India.<BR>—गिरिसार-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of iron, iron.<BR>—गिरि-सुता, f. the daughter of the mountain Hima-<BR>vat; an epithet of Pārvatī, the wife of Śiva.<BR>—गिरि-<BR>सेन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—गिरि-स्रवा, f. a<BR>mountain-stream, a torrent.<BR>—गिरि-ह्वा, f. another<BR>N. of the plant गिरि-कर्णिका, Clitoria Ternatea.<BR>—गिरीन्द्र (˚रि-इन्˚), अस्, m. a prince among the<BR>mountains, a high mountain; a term for the number<BR>eight; [cf. गिरि.] — 2. गिरीश (˚रि-ईश), अस्, m. the<BR>prince of the mountains, a N. of the Himālaya, the<BR>snowy mountains on the north of Hindūstan, or<BR>the range personified; an epithet of Śiva; a N. of the<BR>eleventh Rudra: (for 1. गिरीश see under 1. गिर्.)<BR>—गिर्य्-आह्वा, f. = गिरि-ह्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिक|गिरिकः
गिरिक, अस्, m. the inhabitant of a mountain (?);<BR>a N. of Śiva; a ball for playing with [cf. गिरि and<BR>गिरियक]; N. of a chief of the Nāga or serpent-<BR>race; N. of a certain weaver in a Buddhist work;<BR>also called चण्डगिरिक; (आ), f. a mouse, a small<BR>rat; N. of the wife of Vasu, daughter of the moun-<BR>tain Kolāhala and of the river Śaktimatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरियक|गिरियकः
गिरियक or गिरियाक or गिरीयक, अस्, m. a ball<BR>for playing with; [cf. गिरि and गिरि-गुड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिश|गिरिशः
गिरि-श. See under गिरि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरित|गिरितः
गिरित गिरित. See under 2. गिर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरीश|गिरीशः
गिरीश 1. 2. गिरीश, &c. See under 1. गिर्<BR>and under गिरि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिल|गिलः
गिल गिल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. गॄ), who or<BR>what swallows; (अस्), m. the citron tree, = जम्बीर.<BR>—गिल-गिल, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowing; [cf. तिमिङ्गिल-<BR>गिल.]<BR>—गिल-ग्राह, अस्, m. a crocodile, a shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलत्|गिलन्त्
गिलत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, swallowing, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलन|गिलनं
गिलन, अम्, n. swallowing; also गिरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलायु|गिलायुः
गिलायु, उस्, m. hard tumor in the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलि|गिलिः
गिलि, इस्, f. swallowing, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलित|गिलितं
गिलित, अस्, आ, अम्, eaten, swallowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलोड्य
गिलोड्य गिलोड्य, N. of a plant; [cf.<BR>अङ्गलोड्य, गलोड्य, गालोड्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिष्णु|गिष्णुः
गिष्णु गिष्णु, उस्, m. (probably a corrupt<BR>form of गेष्णु; rt. गै), a professional singer; a<BR>Brāhman versed in the Sāma-veda, a chanter of that<BR>Veda; an actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीःपति
गीःपति गीः-पति, गीष्-पति. See 1. गिर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीत|गीतं
गीत गीत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. गै), sung,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">Page0290-b+ 75</a>]<BR>chanted, sounded, &c.; (आ), f. a song, a sacred<BR>song or poem, religious doctrines declared in me-<BR>trical form by an inspired sage [cf. the titles Śiva-<BR>gītā, Rāma-gītā, Bhagavad-gītā, which last is also<BR>often called the Gītā]; N. of a metre; (अम्), n.<BR>singing, song either general or particular.<BR>—गीत-<BR>कण्डिका, f. a Pariśiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—गीत-<BR>क्रम, अस्, m. the arrangement of a song.<BR>—गीत-<BR>गङ्गाधर, title of a poem by Kalyāṇa.<BR>—गीत-<BR>गिरीश, title of a poem by Rāma.<BR>—गीत-गोविन्द,<BR>अस्, m. Govinda (i. e. Kṛṣṇa) celebrated in song; title<BR>of a lyrical drama by Jaya-deva, supposed to have<BR>been written about the twelfth or thirteenth century<BR>of our era; it is a mystical erotic poem, describing<BR>the loves of Kṛṣṇa and the Gopīs, especially of<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Rādhā, who is supposed to typify the<BR>human soul.<BR>—गीत-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, versed in the art<BR>of singing, acquainted with songs.<BR>—गीत-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, fond of songs; (आ), f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—गीत-मोदिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, gladdening with songs; (ई), m. a Kinnara or<BR>celestial chorister.<BR>—गीत-वादन, अम्, n. the sing-<BR>ing of a song.<BR>—गीत-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the science of<BR>music.<BR>—गीतायन (˚त-अय्˚), अम्, n. a procession<BR>accompanied with songs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतक|गीतकं
गीतक, अम्, n. a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीति|गीतिः
गीति, इस्, f. song, singing; a kind of poetical metre,<BR>a form of the Āryā metre, in which the stanza con-<BR>sists of four lines of twelve and eighteen syllabic<BR>instants alternately.<BR>—गीति-विशेष, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>song.<BR>—गीत्य्-आर्या, f., N. of a metre of four lines of<BR>sixteen short syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतिका
गीतिका, f. a short song, a small hymn; N. of a<BR>metre consisting of four lines of twenty syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतिन्
गीतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who recites in a singing<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीथा
गीथा, f. a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीरथ|गीरथः
गीरथ गीरथ, &c. See under 1. गिर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्ण|गीर्णः|गीर्ण्ण
गीर्ण 1. गीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. गॄ), praised.<BR>1. गीर्णि, इस्, f. praise, applause; fame, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्ण|गीर्णः|गीर्ण्ण
