गु
गु 5. गु (at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR>= गो, a cow, cattle, earth, ray, &c., see गो, (e. g.<BR>दश-गु, possessing ten cows; सहस्र-गु, possess-<BR>ing 1000 cows; चलद्-गु, one under whom the earth<BR>trembles, &c.); [cf. अनु-गु, अरिष्ट-गु, उष्ण-गु,<BR>कृश-गु, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुग्गुल|गुग्गुलः
गुग्गुल गुग्गुल, अस्, m. or गुग्गुलु, उ, उस्,<BR>n. m. (but always m. in the later language), a fragrant<BR>gum resin, bdellium or the exudation of the Amyris<BR>Agallochum, a perfume and medicament; sometimes<BR>with the epithet सैन्धव or समुद्रिय, i. e.<BR>‘obtained near rivers or the sea,’ (perhaps some<BR>other substance coming from rivers or the sea?);<BR>a species of Morunga with red flowers, Morunga<BR>Hyperanthera; (ऊ, ऊस्), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुग्गुलुक|गुग्गुलुकः
