गुज्
गुज् गुज्, cl. 6. and 1 (?). P. गुजति<BR>and गोजति (?), जुगोज, गुजितुम्; oftener<BR>गुञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. गुञ्जति, जुगुञ्ज, गुञ्जितुम्, to sound<BR>inarticulately; to buz, hum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्ज|गुंज|गुंजः|गुञ्जः
गुञ्ज, अस्, m. humming; a bunch, a bundle, a<BR>cluster of blossoms, bunch of flowers, nosegay, =<BR>गुच्छ; (आ), f. humming, a low murmuring sound;<BR>a kettle-drum; a small shrub, Abrus Precatorius,<BR>bearing a red and black berry, which forms the<BR>smallest of the jeweller's weights; either the berry<BR>which averages about 1(5/16) grains troy or the artificial<BR>weight called by this name, weighing about 2(3/16) grains;<BR>= (1/5) Ādya-māṣaka, = (1/5) Māṣaka, = 3 or 2 barley-<BR>corns, = 4 grains of rice, = 2 grains of wheat; (with<BR>physicians 7 Guñjās = 1 Māṣa, with lawyers 7(1/2)<BR>Guñjās); a kind of plant with a poisonous root;<BR>a tavern; reflection, meditation.<BR>—गुञ्ज-कृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘making a humming,’ a large black bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जत्
गुञ्जत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, buzzing, humming, making<BR>a low murmuring sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जन|गुंजन|गुंजनं|गुञ्जनं
गुञ्जन, अम्, n. sounding low and deep, as<BR>buzzing, murmuring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जिका|गुंजिका
गुञ्जिका, f. the seed of the plant Abrus Precatorius,<BR>[cf. गुञ्जा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जित|गुंजित|गुंजितं|गुञ्जितं
गुञ्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, uttered in a low tone, mur-<BR>mured, &c.; (अम्), n. sounding, murmuring, buzzing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

