गुलुच्छ गुलुच्छ or गुलुञ्च or गुलुञ्छ or<BR>गुलुञ्छक, अस्, m. a bunch, a nosegay, a cluster<BR>of blossoms; [cf. गुच्छ, गुत्स, गुलञ्चकन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुह
गुलुह गुलुह, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people in<BR>Madhya-deśa; [cf. गुडुह, गुरुह, गुलह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्गुलु
गुल्गुलु गुल्गुलु, उस्, उ, m. n. bdellium; [cf.<BR>गुग्गुलु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्फ|गुल्फः
गुल्फ गुल्फ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. गल्),<BR>the ancle; [cf. विगुल्फ and कुल्फ.]<BR>—गुल्फ-<BR>जाह, अम्, n. the root of the ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्म|गुल्मं|गुल्मः
गुल्म गुल्म, अस्, अम्, m. n. a cluster or<BR>clump of trees, a thicket, a bush, a shrub; a troop<BR>or guard of soldiers, a body of troops, a division of<BR>an army, consisting of 45 foot, 27 horse, 9 chariots,<BR>and 9 elephants; or of 135 foot, 81 horse, 27 cha-<BR>riots, and 27 elephants; a fort, an intrenchment;<BR>disciplining an army, keeping it in a posture of de-<BR>fence; the spleen; a chronic enlargement of the<BR>spleen or as variously situated any glandular enlarge-<BR>ment in the abdomen, as that of the mesenteric<BR>gland &c., so as to be perceived externally; a wharf<BR>or stairs, a Ghaṭ; (ई), f. a cluster or clump or trees,<BR>a multitude of thickets; Emblic Myrobalan; jujube;<BR>small cardamoms; a tent.<BR>—गुल्म-केतु, उस्, m. a<BR>small sort of cane or reed, sorrel.<BR>—गुल्म-केश, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having bushy hair.<BR>—गुल्म-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>fresh ginger.<BR>—गुल्म-वल्ली, f. the plant Sarcostemma<BR>Viminale.<BR>—गुल्म-वात, अस्, m. or गुल्मोदर<BR>(˚म-उद्˚), अम्, n. a disease of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मक
गुल्मक, अस्, m., N. of a son of the Brāhman<BR>Soma-śarman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मिन्
गुल्मिन्, ई, इनी, इ, composed of different divisions<BR>(a force &c.); growing in a clump or cluster,<BR>clustered, bushy; having the spleen, affected by that<BR>disease; (नी), f. a spreading creeper or any creeping<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्य|गुल्यः
गुल्य गुल्य. See under गुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुवाक|गुवाकः
गुवाक गुवाक, अस्, m. the betel-nut tree,<BR>Areca Faufel or Catechu; [cf. गूवाक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुष्पित
गुष्पित गुष्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. interlaced,<BR>intwined, tied together &c.; [cf. गुफ् and गुम्फ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्
गुह् 1. गुह्, cl. 1. P. A. गूहति, -ते, जुगूह,<BR>जुगुहे, गूहिष्यति or घोक्ष्यति, -ते,<BR>अगूहीत्, अघुक्षत्, अगूढ, अघुक्षत, अगू-<BR>हिषि, अघुक्षि, गूहितुम् or गोढुम्, to cover,<BR>conceal, hide, hide away, keep secret; to cover with<BR>clothes: Caus. गूहयति, -यितुम्, अजूगुहत्: Desid.<BR>जुघुक्षति, -ते, to wish to conceal or hide away:<BR>Intens. जोगुह्यते, जोगुहीति or जोगोढि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्
2. गुह्, घुट्, f., Ved. a hiding-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह|गुहः
गुह, अस्, m. a N. of Skanda or Kārttikeya, the<BR>god of war (as reared in a secret place); an epithet<BR>of Śiva; of Viṣṇu; N. of a king of the Niṣādas, a<BR>friend of Rāma; a N. or title proper to persons of<BR>the writer-caste; a horse, a swift horse; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people in the south of India.<BR>—गुह-गुप्त,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—गुह-चन्द्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—गुह-देव, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a teacher.<BR>—गुह-राज, अस्, m. a peculiar form or<BR>construction of a temple.<BR>—गुह-शिव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king of Kaliṅga.<BR>—गुह-षष्ठी, f. the sixth<BR>day in the former half of Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>—गुह-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहदवद्य
गुहद्-अवद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. concealing or<BR>removing deficiencies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहलु
गुहलु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहा
गुहा, f. a cave, a cavern, a hiding-place; a<BR>pit, a hole in the ground; the plant Hemionitis<BR>Cordifolia; another plant, = शाल-पर्णी; (आ), ind. in<BR>a hiding-place, in secret, secretly (opposed to आविस्).<BR>गुहा धा or गुहा निधा or गुहा कृ, Ved. to<BR>conceal, remove.<BR>—गुहा-गृह, अम्, n. a cavern.<BR>—गुहा-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going in secret or secretly,<BR>going in the interior.<BR>—गुहा-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>wide-mouthed, open-mouthed.<BR>—गुहा-शय, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, lying in a secret place, being in the interior or<BR>in the heart; living in hiding-places or in caverns;<BR>(अस्), m. a tiger; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—गुहा-<BR>हित, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a secret or hidden place,<BR>placed in the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिन|गुहिनं
गुहिन, अम्, n. a wood, a thicket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिल|गुहिलं
गुहिल, अम्, n. wealth, property; a wood (?);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहेर|गुहेरः
गुहेर, अस्, m. a guardian, a protector; a smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्य|गुह्यं|गुह्यः
गुह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be covered or concealed, to<BR>be hidden, to be kept hidden or secret, concealable,<BR>private; secret, solitary, retired; mysterious, mysti-<BR>cal; (अम्), ind. secretly, privately; (अस्), m. hypo-<BR>crisy; a tortoise; an epithet of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. a<BR>secret, a mystery; a privity, an organ of generation,<BR>&c.; the anus.<BR>—गुह्य-काली, f. ‘the mysterious<BR>Durgā,’ title of a poem in honour of this deity.<BR>—गुह्य-गुरु, उस्, m. the mysterious Guru, an<BR>epithet of Śiva, this deity being considered as the<BR>especial teacher of the Tantras or Hindū mystical<BR>and magical works; [cf. गृह्य-गुरु.]<BR>—गुह्य-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—गुह्य-दीपक,<BR>अस्, m. a flying insect which gives out light; the fire-<BR>fly.<BR>—गुह्य-निष्यन्द, अस्, m. urine.<BR>—गुह्य-<BR>पति, इस्, m. lord of the mysteries, an epithet of<BR>Vajra-dhara.<BR>—गुह्य-पिधान, अम्, n. a covering<BR>over the privities.<BR>—गुह्य-पुष्प, अस्, m. the tree<BR>with concealed blossoms, Ficus Religiosa; [cf. अश्वत्-<BR>थ.]<BR>—गुह्य-भाषित, अम्, n. secret speech, a<BR>Mantra, a mystical prayer or incantation; a secret.<BR>—गुह्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, containing mysteries.<BR>—गुह्य-वीज, अस्, m. a kind of grass, = भू-तृण.<BR>—गुह्येश्वरी (˚य-ईश्˚), f. the mysterious deity,<BR>i. e. Prajñā, the female energy of the Ādi-buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यक|गुह्यकः
गुह्यक, अस्, m. a N. of a class of demi-gods who<BR>like the Yakṣas are attendants of Kuvera or the god<BR>of wealth, and guardians of his treasures; they may<BR>have received their name from living in mountain<BR>caverns.<BR>—गुह्यकाधिपति (˚क-अध्˚), इस्, m. or<BR>गुह्यकाधिप, अस्, m. or गुह्यकेश्वर (˚क-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Kuvera, the deity of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढ|गूढं|गूढः
गूढ (or Ved. गूऌह), अस्, आ, अम्, covered,<BR>hidden, concealed, invisible, secret, private; dis-<BR>guised; (अम्), n. a solitary or private place; a private<BR>part; a mystery.<BR>—गूढ-चार, अस्, ई, अम्, one<BR>who goes about secretly or unknown; (अस्), m. a<BR>secret emissary.<BR>—गूढ-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going<BR>about secretly or privately; (ई), m. a secret emissary,<BR>a spy.<BR>—गूढ-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born privately; (अस्),<BR>m. the son of a concealed birth, born secretly of a<BR>woman whose husband is absent, the real father<BR>being unknown; (this is one of the twelve forms<BR>particularized in Hindū law, the child belonging to<BR>the husband of the disloyal wife); [cf. गूढोत्-<BR>पन्न.]<BR>—गूढ-ता, f. concealment, secrecy;<BR>गूढतया, privately, secretly.<BR>—गूढ-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. concealment, secrecy.<BR>—गूढ-नीड, अस्, m. the<BR>wagtail.<BR>—गूढ-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the plant Capparis<BR>Aphylla, = करीर; another plant, Alangium Hexa-<BR>petalum, = अङ्कोठ.<BR>—गूढ-पथ, अस्, m. a<BR>hidden path; the mind, intellect; a bye-path, a<BR>private way.<BR>—गूढ-पाद्, त्, m. a snake.<BR>—गूढ-<BR>पाद, अस्, आ, अम्, having hidden feet; (अस्), m. a<BR>snake.<BR>—गूढ-पुरुष, अस्, m. a spy, a secret<BR>emissary, a disguised agent.<BR>—गूढ-पुष्पक, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Mimusops Elengi, = वकुल.<BR>—गूढ-<BR>फल, अस्, m. the jujube, = बदर.<BR>—गूढ-<BR>भाषित, अम्, n. secret intelligence, private com-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">Page0294-c+ 72</a>]<BR>munication.<BR>—गूढ-मार्ग, अस्, m. a subterranean<BR>passage, a bye-road or secret way; a defile.<BR>—गूढ-<BR>मैथुन, अस्, m. a crow (copulating in secret).<BR>—गूढ-वर्चस्, आस्, m. a frog.<BR>—गूढ-वल्लिका,<BR>f. Alangium Hexapetalum, = अङ्कोठ.<BR>—गूढ-<BR>साक्षिन्, ई, m. a concealed witness, one placed by<BR>the plaintiff so as to overhear what has been said<BR>by the defendant.<BR>—गूढागूढ-ता, f. or गूढा-<BR>गूढ-त्व, अम्, n. (fr. गूढ + अगूढ), conceal-<BR>ment and publicity.<BR>—गूढाङ्ग (˚ढ-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a tortoise.<BR>—गूढाङ्घ्रि (˚ढ-अङ्˚), इस्, m. a<BR>snake.<BR>—गूढार्चि (˚ढ-अर्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, of con-<BR>cealed glory.<BR>—गूढार्थ-दीपिका (˚ढ-अर्˚), f.<BR>‘light for the hidden meaning,’ title of a commen-<BR>tary.<BR>—गूढोत्पन्न (˚ढ-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, born<BR>secretly; (अस्), m. = गूढ-ज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहन|गूहनं
गूहन, अम्, n. concealing, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहमान
गूहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, hiding, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहयित्वा
गूहयित्वा, ind. having concealed, having hidden<BR>or disguised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहितव्य
गूहितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be hidden or concealed,<BR>to be kept secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहेर|गुहेरः
गुहेर गुहेर. See under rt. 1. गुह् last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गू
गू 1. गू, cl. 6. P. गुवति, to void by stool;<BR>(another form for 4. गु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूथ|गूथं|गूथः
गूथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. feces, ordure.<BR>—गूथ-<BR>लक्त, अस्, m. a small bird, considered to be a species<BR>of the Mayna, Turdus Salica; [cf. साल्विक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गून|गूनः
गून, अस्, आ, अम्, voided (as ordure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गू
गू 2. गू (fr. rt. 1. गम्), going, (in अग्रे-गू,<BR>q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढ|गूढं|गूढः
गूढ गूढ. See under rt. 1. गुह् last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्
गूर् गूर् = गुर्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूरण|गूरणं
गूरण, अम्, n. = गुरण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्ण|गूर्ण्ण
गूर्ण or गूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. approved, wel-<BR>come, agreeable, thankful (Lat. gratus).<BR>—गूर्त-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. with grateful mind; (Sāy.)<BR>with prepared mind.<BR>—गूर्त-वचस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>speaking agreeably.<BR>—गूर्त-श्रवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>of whom or of what one likes to hear or to speak.<BR>—गूर्ता-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. possessing agreeable<BR>things; (Sāy.) bestowing treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्ति|गूर्तिः|गूर्त्ति
गूर्ति, इस्, f., Ved. approval, praise, a flattering ex-<BR>pression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्द्
गूर्द् गूर्द् or गुर्द्, cl. 1. A. गूर्दते or<BR>गुर्दते, जुगूर्दे, गूर्दितुम्, to play,<BR>sport; to jump, leap; cl. 10. P. गूर्दयति or गुर्द-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to play, sport; to dwell, inhabit; [cf.<BR>कूर्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्द|गूर्दः|गूर्द्द
गूर्द, अस्, m. a jump; प्रजापतेर् गूर्दः or<BR>प्रजापतेः कूर्दः, N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्ध्
गूर्ध् गूर्ध्, cl. 10. P., Ved. गूर्धयति,<BR>यितुम्, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूवाक|गूवाकः
गूवाक गूवाक, अस्, m. = गुवाक, the betel-<BR>nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूषणा
गूषणा गूषणा, f. the eye in a peacock's<BR>tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0294-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहन|गूहनं
