गोतम|गोतमः
गोतम गोतम, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi be-<BR>longing to the family of Aṅgiras, with the patronymic<BR>Rāhūgaṇa, author of several hymns of the Vedas;<BR>N. of a lawyer; N. of a sage, the founder of the<BR>Nyāya philosophy; N. of the twentieth Vyāsa in<BR>the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa; of a king of Potāla, son of<BR>Karṇika; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Gotama.<BR>—गोतम-स्तोम, अस्, m., N. of an Ekāha sacrifice.<BR>—गोतम-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a Jaina saint; [cf.<BR>गन्तम-स्वामिन्.]<BR>—गोतमान्वय (˚म-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a descendant of Gotama, epithet of Śākya-muni,<BR>the founder of the Buddhist religion.<BR>—गोतमी-<BR>पुत्व, अस्, m., N. of a prince; (also गोमति-पुत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

