गौङ्गव
गौङ्गव गौङ्गव, अम्, n. (fr. गुङ्गु), N. of<BR>several Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0300-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौञ्जिक|गौंजिक|गौंजिकः|गौञ्जिकः
गौञ्जिक गौञ्जिक, अस्, m. (fr. गुञ्जा), a<BR>goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0300-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौड|गौडः
गौड गौड, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गुड), prepared<BR>from sugar or molasses; (ई), f. rum or spirit distilled<BR>from molasses; one of the Rāgiṇīs, the wife of the<BR>Rāga Megha; a style of poetry, the bold and spirited<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">Page0301-a+ 75</a>]<BR>style; the Bengal dialect; (अम्), n. sweetmeats;<BR>(अस्), m., scil. देश, or (अम्), n., scil. राष्ट्र,<BR>the sugar country; N. of a country, ‘the district of<BR>Gaur,’ the central part of Bengal, extending from<BR>Vaṅga to the borders of Orissa, (the ruins of its<BR>capital called by the same name are still extensive);<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of this country; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Rāga; N. of a lexicographer.<BR>—गौड-देश,<BR>अस्, m. the country Gauḍa.<BR>—गौड-पाद, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a commentator on several Upaniṣads and on<BR>the Sāṅkhya-kārikā.<BR>—गौड-पुर, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a town.<BR>—गौड-भृत्य-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—गौडाभिनन्द or गौडाभिनन्दन<BR>(˚ड-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0300-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौडक
गौडक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people living to the<BR>east of Madhya-deśa.<BR>—गौडक-मृग, अस्, m. a<BR>wild horse; [cf. गौर-खर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौडिक|गौडिकं|गौडिकः
गौडिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to sugar or molasses,<BR>fit for the preparation of sugar, prepared with sugar<BR>or molasses; (अम्), n. rum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौडीय
गौडीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Gauḍa or Bengal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौडन
गौडन गौडन = गोदन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौण|गौणः
गौण गौण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गुण), subordinate,<BR>secondary, unessential; metaphorical, figurative; second-<BR>ary as applied to the month reckoned from full moon<BR>to full moon; having qualities, attributive, adjective;<BR>relating to multiplication or enumeration; गौणं<BR>कर्म, the less immediate object of an action in a<BR>sentence.<BR>—गौण-त्व, अम्, n. the state of an adjec-<BR>tive or subordinate word.<BR>—गौण-पक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>the minor or weaker side of an argument &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौणिक
1. गौणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the three<BR>qualities (of सत्त्व, रजस्, and तमस्), having<BR>qualities, relating to or connected with qualities;<BR>subordinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौण्य|गौण्यं
गौण्य, अम्, n. subordination; the state of being<BR>unessential &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौणिक
गौणिक 2. गौणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गोणी), re-<BR>sembling a sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतम|गौतमः
गौतम गौतम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गोतम), re-<BR>lating to Gotama (e. g. with पद-स्तोभाः, N. of a<BR>Sāman); (अस्), m., N. of Buddha or Śākya-muni<BR>the founder of the Buddhist religion; N. of a teacher<BR>of ritual; N. of a grammarian; of a legislator; a patro-<BR>nymic of Kuśri, of Aruṇa, of Uddālaka, of Śaradvat,<BR>of Śatānanda; the father of Ekata, Dvita, and Trita<BR>(Mahā-bh. IX. 2073); N. of the first pupil of the<BR>last Jina; a kind of poison, one of the fixed kinds;<BR>(ई), f. a patronymic of Kṛpī and other women; an<BR>epithet of Durgā; N. of a Rākṣasī or female gob-<BR>lin; N. of a river, = गोमती; a kind of yellow pig-<BR>ment or dye, = गो-रोचना; turmeric; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a Sāman; fat; [cf. मेदस्, and भारद्वाज,<BR>‘bone.’]<BR>—गौतम-सम्भवा, f. an epithet of<BR>the river Godāvarī.<BR>—गौतम-सरस्, अस्, n., N. of<BR>a lake.<BR>—गौतम-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a Jaina<BR>teacher; [cf. गोतम-स्वामिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतमक
गौतमक, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Nāgas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतमि
गौतमि, a patronymic = गौतम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतमीय
गौतमीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Gautama,<BR>coming from him &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतमस
गौतमस गौतमस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-तमस्?),<BR>epithet of two verses of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौदानिक
गौदानिक गौदानिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>the ceremony called Godāna (q. v.), performing it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधार|गौधारः
गौधार गौधार, अस्, m. (fr. गोधा), an<BR>Iguana (considered as the offspring of the alligator on<BR>account of its smaller size and similar shape); also<BR>गौधेय and गौधेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधेरक
गौधेरक, अस्, m. a kind of small venomous<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधूम
गौधूम गौधूम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-धूम),<BR>coming from wheat, made of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधूम्र
गौधूम्र गौधूम्र, a various reading for<BR>गौतम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपत्य
गौपत्य गौपत्य, अम्, n. (fr. गो-पति), Ved.<BR>the possession of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपवन
गौपवन, a patronymic from Gopa-vana; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपायन
गौपायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Gopa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपिक|गौपिकः
गौपिक, अस्, m. (fr. गोपिका), the son of a herds-<BR>man's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपुच्छ
गौपुच्छ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-पुच्छ), like a<BR>cow's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपुच्छिक
गौपुच्छिक, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging to a<BR>cow's tail, bought for a cow's tail &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौमत
गौमत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-मती), being in the<BR>river Gomatī; (ई), f., N. of a river; (the latter being<BR>a wrong reading for गौतमी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौर|गौरं|गौरः
गौर गौर, अस्, ई, अम् (said to be fr. rt. 3. गु),<BR>white, yellowish, reddish, pale red; shining, brilliant,<BR>pure, clean, beautiful; (अस्), m. white, yellowish, &c.<BR>(the colour); a kind of buffalo, the Bos Gaurus,<BR>often classed with the Gavaya; white mustard, the<BR>seed of it used as a weight, = 3 Rāja-sarṣapas [cf.<BR>गौर-सर्षप]; the plant Grislea Tomentosa<BR>(= धव); the moon; the planet Jupiter; N.<BR>of a Yoga teacher, a son of Śuka and Pīvarī; an<BR>epithet of the saint Caitanya; (ई), f. the female of<BR>the Bos Gaurus; the Vāc or voice of the middle<BR>region of the air; turmeric, = रजनी, and N. of<BR>several other plants, = प्रियङ्गु, मञ्जिष्ठा, &c.;<BR>a yellow pigment or dye, = गो-रोचना; a girl eight<BR>years old, any young girl prior to menstruation, a<BR>maid, a virgin; the earth; ‘the brilliant goddess,’<BR>N. of the goddess Pārvatī or daughter of Himālaya<BR>and wife of Śiva; N. of the wife of Varuṇa; N. of<BR>the mother of Śākya-muni [cf. माया]; N. of one<BR>of the sixteen Vidyā-devīs; N. of the wife of Prasena-<BR>jit (or Yuvanāśva), who incurring the curse of her<BR>husband was changed into the river Bāhu-dā; N. of<BR>the wife of Vi-rajas and mother of Su-dhāman; N. of a<BR>river; N. of a Rāgiṇī, the wife of the Rāga Mālava;<BR>N. of several metres, one consisting of four lines of<BR>twelve syllables each; another consisting of four lines<BR>of thirteen syllables each; another consisting of four<BR>lines of twenty-six long syllables each; (अम्), n.<BR>white mustard; the filament of a lotus; saffron;<BR>gold; [cf. Lat. gilvus; Lith. geltônas, giele; Russ.<BR>schiltyi; Germ. gelb ?].<BR>—गौर-खर, अस्, m.<BR>a wild donkey; [cf. गौडक-मृग.]<BR>—गौर-<BR>ग्रीव, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people in Madhya-deśa.<BR>—गौरग्रीवीय, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to this<BR>people.<BR>—गौर-चन्द्र, अस्, m. an epithet of the<BR>saint Caitanya.<BR>—गौर-जीरक, अस्, m. white cumin.<BR>—गौर-तित्तिरि, इस्, m. a kind of partridge.<BR>—गौर-<BR>त्वच्, क्, m. the plant Terminalia Catappa; [cf.<BR>इङ्गुद.]<BR>—गौर-पृष्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—गौर-मुख, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Śamīka,<BR>a Purohita of king Ugra-sena.<BR>—गौर-मृग, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. the Bos Gaurus.<BR>—गौर-वाहन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—गौर-शाक, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>a kind of Madhūka.<BR>—गौर-शिरस्, आस्, m., N. of a<BR>Muni.<BR>—गौर-सर्षप, अस्, m. white mustard,<BR>Sinapis Glauca; the white mustard seed considered<BR>as a measure of weight.<BR>—गौर-सुवर्ण, अम्, n.<BR>a kind of vegetable; [cf. पत्त्रशाक-विशेष, =<BR>कटु-शृङ्गाल and गन्ध-शाक.]<BR>—गौराङ्ग<BR>(˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of the saint Caitanya;<BR>[cf. गौर and गौर-चन्द्र.]<BR>—गौराजाजी (˚र-<BR>अज्˚), f. white cumin.<BR>—गौरार्द्रक (˚र-आर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a kind of poison.<BR>—गौरावस्कन्दिन् (˚र-अव्˚),<BR>ई, m. an epithet of Indra.<BR>—गौराश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince.<BR>—गौरास्य (˚र-आस्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>kind of black monkey with a white face.<BR>—गौरा-<BR>हिक (˚र-अहि), अस्, m. a kind of serpent.<BR>—गौरि-<BR>वीति, इस्, m. (for गौरी-व्˚), N. of a Ṛṣi, a descend-<BR>ant of Śakti.<BR>—गौरी-कल्प, अस्, m., N. of a Kalpa,<BR>the thirteenth day of the dark half in Brahmā's<BR>month.<BR>—गौरी-कान्त, अस्, m., N. of a commentator<BR>on the Tarka-bhāṣā.<BR>—गौरीकान्त-सार्वभौम,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentary called Ānanda-laharī-<BR>tarī.<BR>—गौरी-गुरु, उस्, m. the father of Gaurī, an<BR>epithet of the Himālaya.<BR>—गौरी-ज, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Kārttikeya; (अम्), n. talc.<BR>—गौरी-नाथ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">Page0301-c+ 74</a>]<BR>अस्, m. the husband of Gaurī, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—गौरी-पट्ट, अस्, m. the horizontal plate of the<BR>Liṅga, typical of the female organ.<BR>—गौरी-पति, इस्,<BR>m. the husband of Gaurī, an epithet of Śiva; N. of<BR>the father of the scholiast Vaṭeśvara.<BR>—गौरी-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. son of Gaurī, an epithet of the deity Kārtti-<BR>keya.<BR>—गौरी-पुष्प, अस्, m., N. of a plant, =<BR>गौरी or प्रियङ्गु.<BR>—गौरी-पूजा, f. the adoration<BR>of Gaurī, N. of a festival on the fourth day in the<BR>last half of month Māgha.<BR>—गौरी-भर्तृ, ता, m.<BR>the husband of Gaurī, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—गौरी-<BR>मन्त्र, अस्, m. a prayer to Gaurī.<BR>—गौरी-ललित,<BR>अम्, n. yellow orpiment.<BR>—गौरी-वर, अस्, m. the<BR>lover of Gaurī, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—गौरीवित,<BR>अम्, n. (fr. गौरि-वीति, q. v.), N. of a Sāman.<BR>—गौरी-<BR>विवाह, अस्, m. the marriage of Gaurī.<BR>—गौरी-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n. the vow of Gaurī, a kind of rite in<BR>honour of Gaurī.<BR>—गौरीश (˚री-ईश), अस्, m. the<BR>lord of Gaurī, an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरिक
गौरिक, अस्, m. white mustard; a metronymic<BR>of Māndhātṛ; (आ), f. a virgin, a young girl, one<BR>eight years old or in whom menstruation has not yet<BR>commenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरिल|गौरिलः
गौरिल, अस्, m. white mustard; iron or steel<BR>filings or dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरक्ष्य|गौरक्ष्यं
गौरक्ष्य गौरक्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. गो-रक्ष),<BR>the office of a herdsman, breeding cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरव|गौरवं
गौरव गौरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गुरु), relating<BR>or belonging to a Guru or teacher; (अम्), n. weight,<BR>heaviness; length in prosody; importance, high value<BR>or estimation; cumbrousness; gravity, respectability,<BR>venerableness; dignity; respect shown to a person<BR>(e. g. मातृ-गौरवात्, out of respect for one's<BR>mother).<BR>—गौरव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, important.<BR>—गौरवासन (˚व-आस्˚), अम्, n. a seat of honour.<BR>—गौरवेरित (˚व-ईर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, praised, famed,<BR>celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरवित|गौरवितः
गौरवित, अस्, आ, अम्, highly esteemed or valued,<BR>venerable, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरि
गौरि गौरि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरुतल्पिक|गौरुतल्पिकः
गौरुतल्पिक गौरुतल्पिक, अस्, m. (fr. गुरु-<BR>तल्प), the violator of the bed of a Guru or religious<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौलक्षणिक|गौलक्षणिकः
गौलक्षणिक गौलक्षणिक, अस्, m. (fr. गो-<BR>लक्षण), one who knows the good marks of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौलोमन
गौलोमन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-लोमन्), resembling<BR>cow's hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौला
गौला गौला, f. = गौरा = गौरी, N. of the<BR>daughter of Himālaya and wife of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौलिक|गौलिकः
गौलिक गौलिक, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>= गौलिह and गौलीढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौल्मिक|गौल्मिकः
गौल्मिक गौल्मिक, अस्, m. (fr. गुल्म), a<BR>single soldier of a troop, one of a body of soldiers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौल्य|गौल्यं
गौल्य गौल्य, अम्, n. (fr. गुल = गुड),<BR>syrup; spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौशकटिक
गौशकटिक गौशकटिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-<BR>शकट), possessing a carriage drawn by oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौशतिक|गौशतिकः
गौशतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-शतम्), possessing<BR>a hundred oxen or cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौशृङ्ग
गौशृङ्ग, अम्, n. (fr. गो-शृङ्ग), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौषूक्त
गौषूक्त, अम्, n. (fr. गोषूक्तिन्), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौषूक्ति
गौषूक्ति (fr. गौषूक्त), N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौष्ठीन|गौष्ठीनं
गौष्ठीन, अम्, n. (fr. गोष्ठ), the site of an<BR>old and abandoned cow-pen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौसहस्रिक
गौसहस्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. गो-सहस्र), pos-<BR>sessing a thousand cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्धि|ग्धिः
ग्धि ग्धि, इस्, f. (fr. घस्), Ved. eating,<BR>consuming; [cf. सग्धि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्ना
ग्ना ग्ना, f. (generally used in plur., but<BR>according to some in Ṛg-veda IV. 9, 4, the nom.<BR>sing. ग्नास् occurs; the word seems to be derived<BR>from ज्ञा rather than from जन्, and to mean originally<BR>‘a wise female.’ In the Nighaṇṭavas it is enumerated<BR>among the synonyms of वाच्, ‘the voice.’ By Yāska<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">Page0302-a+ 80</a>]<BR>in Nirukta III. 21. it is said to be derived from<BR>गम्, ‘to approach,’ and to mean ‘a female or<BR>woman’ in general), Ved. a semi-divine or super-<BR>human female, a kind of goddess or female genius;<BR>a woman.<BR>—ग्ना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. (Sāy.) ac-<BR>companied by women or wives. According to some<BR>the neut. may be ग्ना-वस्; but Sāy. in Ṛg-veda II.<BR>1, 5, considers ग्नावस् a nom. pl., and interprets it to<BR>mean ‘words of praise.’<BR>—ग्नास्-पति, इस्, m., Ved.<BR>the husband of divine wives, or of a divine wife;<BR>(perhaps ग्नास् is here a shortened genitive.)<BR>—ग्नास्-<BR>पत्नी, f. a divine wife, the wife of a deity; (Sāy.)<BR>a kind of female genius protecting women; (perhaps<BR>ग्नास् is here the nominative in apposition to पत्नी,<BR>i. e. a divine female who is a wife.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथ्
ग्रथ् 1. ग्रथ् or ग्रन्थ्, cl. 9. and 1. P.<BR>ग्रथ्नाति, ग्रन्थति, जग्रन्थ; pl.<BR>जग्रन्थुस् and ग्रेथुस्; ग्रन्थिष्यति, अग्रन्थीत्,<BR>ग्रन्थितुम्; A. ग्रथ्नीते, ग्रन्थते, अग्रन्-<BR>थिष्ट; cl. 1. P. A. also ग्रथति, ग्रथते; to<BR>fasten, tie or string together; to wind round; to<BR>arrange, connect in a regular series; to string words<BR>together, compose, write (as a literary work); to set<BR>or strew with: Caus. P. ग्रन्थयति and ग्राथ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्; [cf. Lat. glut-en ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथन|ग्रथनं
ग्रथन, अम्, n. coagulation, thickening, be-<BR>coming obstructed or clogged with knotty lumps;<BR>(आ), f. tying, binding, stringing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथित|ग्रथितं
ग्रथित, अस्, आ, अम्, strung, tied, bound, con-<BR>nected, tied together or in order, wound, arranged,<BR>classed, collected; set with, strewn with; artificially<BR>composed or put together (as the plot of a play);<BR>difficult to be unravelled, having knots, knotty, formed<BR>into lumps, coagulated, thickened, clogged; hardened;<BR>hurt, injured; seized, taken possession of; overcome;<BR>(अम्), n. a tumor with hard lumps or knots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथ्न|ग्रथ्नः
ग्रथ्न, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a bunch, a tuft;<BR>(perhaps for ग्रन्थ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थ|ग्रंथ|ग्रंथः|ग्रन्थः
ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. tying, binding, stringing together<BR>(literally or metaphorically); an artificial arrangement<BR>of words, a verse, composition, treatise, literary pro-<BR>duction, a book or composition in prose or verse,<BR>a section; the book or sacred scriptures of the Śikhs<BR>containing short moral poems by Nānak Shāh and<BR>others; a metre of thirty-two syllables; wealth,<BR>property; [cf. उत्तर-ग्रन्थ, निर्-ग्र्˚, षड्-ग्र्˚.]<BR>—ग्रन्थ-करण, अम्, n. composing books or<BR>treatises, composition.<BR>—ग्रन्थ-कर्तृ, ता, or<BR>ग्रन्थ-कार, अस्, m. a book-maker, the author of<BR>a book or treatise.<BR>—ग्रन्थ-कुटी or ग्रन्थ-कूटी,<BR>f. a library; an office, a study.<BR>—ग्रन्थ-कृत्, त्,<BR>m. the writer of a book, author or composer of a<BR>treatise.<BR>—ग्रन्थ-विस्तर, अस्, m. a multitude of<BR>scientific treatises.<BR>—ग्रन्थ-विस्तार, अस्, m. dif-<BR>fuseness of style, voluminousness.<BR>—ग्रन्थ-सन्धि,<BR>इस्, m. a section or chapter of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थन|ग्रंथन|ग्रंथनं|ग्रन्थनं
ग्रन्थन, अम्, आ, n. f. stringing, tying or con-<BR>necting together either as a chaplet or a book, ar-<BR>ranging, composing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थि|ग्रंथि|ग्रंथिः|ग्रन्थिः
1. ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. a knot, a tie, the knot of a cord<BR>&c., a knot, bunch or protuberance of any kind<BR>(especially if produced by tying several things to-<BR>gether), a knot tied in the end of a garment for<BR>keeping money &c.; the joint or knot of a reed or<BR>cane &c., a joint or articulation of the body; a com-<BR>plaint, knotting, i. e. swelling and hardening of the<BR>vessels as in varicocele; a knot tied closely and<BR>therefore difficult to be undone; N. of several plants<BR>and bulbous roots, = ग्रन्थि-पर्ण, हितावली, भ-<BR>द्र-मुस्ता, पिण्डालु; [cf. उदर-ग्˚, कटु-ग्˚,<BR>काल-ग्˚, &c.]<BR>—ग्रन्थि-च्छेदक, अस्, m. a purse-<BR>cutter, a cut-purse, pickpocket; [cf. ग्रन्थि-भेद.]<BR>—ग्रन्थि-त्व, अम्, n. state of becoming knotty;<BR>hardening.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-दल, अस्, m. a kind of per-<BR>fume, = चोरक; (आ), f., N. of a kind of bulbous<BR>root.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-दूर्वा, f., N. of a plant, = माला-<BR>दूर्वा.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a kind of perfume,<BR>= चोरक.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-पर्ण, अस्, m. a kind of per-<BR>fume, = चोरक; (आ), f. a kind of plant, = जतुका;<BR>(ई), f. a kind of Dūrvā grass, = गण्ड-दूर्वा; (अम्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">Page0302-b+ 78</a>]<BR>n. a kind of fragrant plant.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-फल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of several plants, = Feronia Elephantum, =<BR>कपित्थ; another plant, Vanguiera Spinosa, = म-<BR>दन; another plant, = शाकुरुण्ड.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-<BR>बन्धन, अम्, n. tying a knot; a ligament; tying<BR>together the garments of the bride and bridegroom<BR>at the marriage ceremony.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-बर्हिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a plant, = ग्रन्थि-पर्ण.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-भेद,<BR>अस्, m. a purse-cutter, cut-purse; [cf. ग्रन्थि-च्छे-<BR>दक.]<BR>—ग्रन्थि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, tied, bound;<BR>knotty, bulbous; (आन्), m. the plant Heliotropium<BR>Indicum; [cf. अस्थि-संहारी.]<BR>—ग्रन्थिमत्-फल,<BR>अस्, m. the plant Artocarpus Lacucha (लकुच).<BR>—ग्रन्थि-मूल, अम्, n. garlic, = गृञ्जन; (आ),<BR>f. a kind of Dūrvā grass, = माला-दूर्वा.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-<BR>मोचक, अस्, m. a cut-purse, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिक|ग्रंथिक|ग्रन्थिकं|ग्रंथिकः|ग्रन्थिकः
ग्रन्थिक, अस्, m. an astrologer (one who under-<BR>stands the joints or divisions of time, of the year, &c.;<BR>cf. काल-ग्रन्थि, ‘a year’), a fortune-teller; a N.<BR>assumed by Nakula, the fourth son of Pāṇḍu, when<BR>he became master of the horse to king Virāṭa; a<BR>kind of disease of the outer ear; (अम्), n. (according<BR>to some) m., N. of the plant Capparis Aphylla; the<BR>root of long pepper; (अम्), n., N. of a plant, =<BR>ग्रन्थि-पर्ण; a kind of resin, bdellium; [cf.<BR>गुग्गुलु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थित|ग्रंथित|ग्रन्थितं
ग्रन्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, strung, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिन्|ग्रंथिन्
ग्रन्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who reads books, bookish,<BR>well-read, learned; relating or belonging to a book,<BR>one who possesses many books.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिल|ग्रंथिल|ग्रन्थिलं|ग्रन्थिलः
ग्रन्थिल, अस्, आ, अम्, knotted, knotty; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of several plants and roots, = Flacourtia Sapida;<BR>another plant, Capparis Aphylla; also = तण्डुलीय-<BR>शाक = हितावली = पिण्डालु = वि-कण्टक; also = चो-<BR>रक, a kind of perfume; (आ), f., N. of several plants,<BR>= गण्ड-दूर्वा, माला-दूर्वा, भद्र-मुस्ता;<BR>(अम्), n. the root of long pepper; green or undried<BR>ginger, = आर्द्रक.<BR>—ग्रन्थि-हर, अस्, m. a coun-<BR>sellor, a minister (one who unravels the knots of<BR>business).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थीक|ग्रन्थीकं
ग्रन्थीक, अम्, n. the root of long pepper, =<BR>ग्रन्थिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथ्
ग्रथ् 2. ग्रथ् or ग्रन्थ्, cl. 1. A. ग्र-<BR>थते and ग्रन्थते, to be crooked (literally<BR>or metaphorically), to be wicked; to curve, bend or<BR>make crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथिन्
ग्रथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, false; (Sāy.) talkative, stringing<BR>(too many) words together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थि|ग्रंथि|ग्रंथिः|ग्रन्थिः
2. ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. crookedness, distortion; falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रप्स्
ग्रप्स् ग्रप्स्. See ग्लप्स्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रभ्
ग्रभ् ग्रभ्. See ग्रह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्
ग्रस् 1. ग्रस्, cl. 1. P. A. ग्रसति, -ते, ज-<BR>ग्रास, जग्रसे, ग्रसिष्यति, -ते, अग्रसीत्,<BR>अग्रसिष्ट, ग्रसितुम्, to seize with the mouth, take<BR>into the mouth, swallow, devour, eat, consume; to<BR>swallow up, cause to disappear; to seize; to eclipse;<BR>to swallow or mouth or slur over words, pronounce<BR>indistinctly: Caus. P. ग्रासयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>swallow, cause to devour; to consume, swallow, eat:<BR>Desid. जिग्रसिषते, -ति: Intens. जाग्रस्यते, जा-<BR>ग्रस्ति; [cf. Lat. gra-men; Germ. gras, grasen;<BR>Eng. grass; Gr. γραίνω].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्
2. ग्रस्, अस्, अस्, अस्, (at the end of compounds) seizing<BR>with the mouth, devouring, swallowing (e. g. पिण्ड-<BR>ग्रस्, devouring a mouthful; see Gram. 164. b).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसन|ग्रसनं
ग्रसन, अम्, n. swallowing, eating; taking, seiz-<BR>ing; a kind of partial eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसमान
ग्रसमान, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowing, devouring;<BR>receiving, listening to anything eagerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसिष्ठ
ग्रसिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. swallowing most,<BR>devouring very much; (Sāy. = भक्षयितृ-तम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसिष्णु
ग्रसिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, accustomed to swallow or<BR>devour or seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्त|ग्रस्तं
ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowed, eaten; taken,<BR>seized; involved in, affected by; possessed by (e. g.<BR>ग्रह-ग्रस्त, seized or possessed by a demon;<BR>दारिद्र्य-ग्रस्त, poverty-stricken); seized (as the<BR>sun or moon by Rāhu); eclipsed (e. g. राहु-ग्रस्त,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-c" target="_blank">Page0302-c+ 80</a>]<BR>q. v.); inarticulately pronounced, slurred, uttered with<BR>the omission of a letter or syllable.<BR>—ग्रस्तास्त (˚त-<BR>अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, commenced and ended as an eclipse;<BR>(अम्), n. the setting of the sun or moon while<BR>eclipsed.<BR>—ग्रस्तोदय (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, m. the rising<BR>of the sun or moon while eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्ति|ग्रस्तिः
ग्रस्ति, इस्, f. the act of swallowing or devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्य
ग्रस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be swallowed, eaten or seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रास|ग्रासः
ग्रास, अस्, m. a mouthful or a quantity of anything<BR>equivalent to a mouthful, a lump of rice &c. of the<BR>size of a peacock's egg; food, nourishment; the<BR>erosion, the morsel bitten; the quantity eclipsed;<BR>the act of swallowing; the swallowing of the sun<BR>and moon (by Rāhu), an eclipse; slurring, uttering<BR>with the omission of a letter or syllable, a fault in<BR>the pronunciation of the gutturals; (in geom.) a<BR>piece cut out by the intersection of two circles.<BR>—ग्रास-शल्य, अम्, n. any extraneous substance<BR>lodged in the throat.<BR>—ग्रासाच्छादन (˚स-आच्˚),<BR>अम्, n. bare subsistence, food and clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रासीकृ
ग्रासी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to swallow, devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह्
ग्रह् ग्रह् or ग्रभ् (the latter being the<BR>more ancient form used especially in the<BR>Ṛg-veda), cl. 9. P. A. गृह्णाति, गृह्णीते (Ved.<BR>गृभ्णाति, -णीते); Impf. 1st sing. अगृह्णाम् (irreg.<BR>अगृह्णम्), 2nd sing. Impv. P. गृहाण (Ved.<BR>गृभ्णान and गृह्णान, other forms गृह्णाहि and<BR>गृह्णीहि, 3rd sing. गृह्णीतात्), जग्राह (Ved. Perf.<BR>जग्रभ, 1st pl. जगृभ्म), जगृहे (Ved. 3rd pl.<BR>जगृभ्रे), ग्रहीष्यति, -ते, अग्रहीत्, अग्रहीष्ट<BR>(Ved. Aor. 1st sing. अग्रभम्, 3rd sing. अग्रभीत्,<BR>3rd pl. अगृभ्रन्, अगृभीषत; also 1st sing.<BR>अजग्रभम्), ग्रहीतुम्, to seize, take, receive,<BR>accept, take by the hand, adopt, catch, grasp, hold,<BR>lay hold of (e. g. पक्षं ग्रह्, to take a side, adopt<BR>a party; पाणिं ग्रह्, to take by the hand in the<BR>marriage ceremony, hence to marry); to seize, arrest,<BR>stop; to take captive, take prisoner, capture, im-<BR>prison; to take possession of, gain over, captivate;<BR>to seize, overpower (especially said of diseases and<BR>demons and the punishments of Varuṇa); to seize,<BR>eclipse (the sun and moon being supposed by the<BR>Hindūs to be seized by Rāhu); to abstract, take<BR>away (by robbery); to lay the hand on, gain, win,<BR>obtain, receive, accept; to conceive; to acquire by<BR>purchase (with inst. of the price); to choose; to<BR>take up (as a fluid with any small vessel), to draw<BR>water; to catch, intercept; pluck, pick, gather; to<BR>collect a store of anything; to use, put on (as clothes<BR>&c.); to assume (as a shape); to place upon; to<BR>withdraw, draw back; to include; to take on one's<BR>self, undertake, undergo, begin; to receive hospitably<BR>(as a guest); to take back (as a divorced wife); to take<BR>into the mouth, mention, name [cf. नाम-ग्रहण,<BR>नाम-ग्राहम्, &c.]; to perceive with the organs of<BR>sense, observe, recognize; to receive into the mind,<BR>apprehend, understand, learn; to accept, admit, approve;<BR>to obey, follow; to take for, consider as; to take in<BR>a particular sense or meaning: Pass. गृह्यते, 1st<BR>Fut. ग्रहीता and ग्राहिता, 2nd Fut. ग्रहीष्यते and<BR>ग्राहिष्यते, Aor. 3rd sing. अग्राहि, 3rd du. अग्र-<BR>हीषाताम् and अग्राहिषाताम्: Caus. P. ग्राह-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, अजिग्रहत्, to cause to take or seize<BR>or lay hold of; to give away a girl (acc.) in marriage<BR>to any one (acc.); to cause any one to be captured;<BR>to cause to take away; to make one take, to deliver<BR>over to; (with आसनम् and acc.) to cause to take a<BR>seat, to bid any one sit down by the side of; to<BR>make any one choose; to cause a person to undertake<BR>or be occupied with (inst.); to make a person learn,<BR>to teach, make any one acquainted or familiar with<BR>(two acc.); to become familiar with: Desid. जिघृ-<BR>क्षति, -ते, to be about to seize or take; to be<BR>about to take away; to desire to take, to wish to<BR>perceive (with the organs of sense), to strive to<BR>apprehend or recognize: Intens. जरीगृह्यते, जा-<BR>ग्राढि (Gram. 711): [cf. Zend gerep, geurv;<BR>Goth. greipa; Germ. greife; Lith. grêbju, pa-<BR>grêbju; Slav. grabljû; Hib. grabaim, ‘I devour,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">Page0303-a+ 81</a>]<BR>stop, interrupt, disturb;’ gabhaim, ‘I take, receive,<BR>conceive;’ Gr. γρῖφος, γρῖπος: cf. also Lat. gero;<BR>Pol. garniac.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्
गृह्, गृह, &c. See s. v. at p. 295.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीत|गृहीतं
गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, grasped, taken, seized, caught,<BR>held, laid hold of; obtained, acquired, gained; robbed;<BR>received, accepted, conceived; collected; agreed, pro-<BR>mised; perceived, known, understood, ascertained,<BR>learnt, &c.; [cf. ग्रह् above.]<BR>—गृहीत-खड्ग-<BR>चर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, grasping sword and shield.<BR>—गृहीत-गर्भा, f. one who has conceived an<BR>embryo, a pregnant woman.<BR>—गृहीत-चेतस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, one whose mind or heart is captivated.<BR>—गृ-<BR>हीत-दिश्, क्, क्, क्, running away, flying; flown,<BR>escaped, retreated.<BR>—गृहीत-देह, अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>carnate.<BR>—गृहीत-नामन्, आ, आ, अ, one who has<BR>received a name (e. g. सु-गृहीत-नामन्, one who<BR>has received a good name, one named in accordance<BR>with the ordinances).<BR>—गृहीत-विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has acquired knowledge, versed in science,<BR>learned, studied.<BR>—गृहीत-वेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has received his wages, paid, remunerated.<BR>—गृहीत-शर-कार्मुक, अस्, आ, अम्, handling<BR>arrows and bows.<BR>—गृहीत-शरावाप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>taking a bow.<BR>—गृहीत-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose heart is taken possession of or captivated;<BR>captivating the heart.<BR>—गृहीतामिष (˚त-आम्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, seizing prey.<BR>—गृहीतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, comprehending the sense or meaning.<BR>—गृहीतास्त्र (˚त-अस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>taken up arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतव्य
गृहीतव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (an incorrect form for<BR>ग्रहीतव्य), to be seized or taken; to be under-<BR>stood, meant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतिन्
गृहीतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, seizing, one who has grasped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतृ
गृहीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (incorrect for ग्रहीतृ),<BR>seizing, grasping, disposed to seize or take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीत्वा
गृहीत्वा, ind. having taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहु
गृहु, उस्, m., Ved. one who receives alms,<BR>a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्णत्
गृह्णत्, अन्, अती, अत्, taking, seizing, accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्य|गृह्यं|गृह्यः
2. गृह्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. गृह्य see s. v. at<BR>p. 296), to be taken or received; to be seized, to<BR>be observed, perceptible, perceivable; to be ac-<BR>knowledged or admitted; to be adopted as faith or<BR>belief, to be trusted, to be relied on, to be honoured;<BR>taking the side of, adopting or choosing as best (e. g.<BR>अर्जुन-गृह्य, taking the side or adhering to the<BR>party of Arjuna); dependant, subservient; (अस्), m.<BR>the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्य|गृह्यं|गृह्यः
3. गृह्य, irreg. ind. part. having taken, carrying<BR>along, together with, with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रभ
ग्रभ, अस्, m., Ved. the taking possession of;<BR>one who lays hold of (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रभण
ग्रभण, अम्, n. seizing, that by which anything<BR>is seized (?).<BR>—ग्रभण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>anything furnished with a handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रभीतृ
ग्रभीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who seizes; [cf.<BR>ग्रहीतृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह|ग्रहः
ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, seizing, laying hold of, holding;<BR>taking, collecting, gathering; (अस्), m. one who<BR>seizes; the power that seizes and obscures the sun<BR>and moon and causes eclipses, especially Rāhu or the<BR>ascending node; a planet (as seizing or influencing<BR>the destinies of men in a supernatural manner;<BR>sometimes five planets are enumerated, viz. Mars,<BR>Mercury, Jupiter, Venus, and Saturn; sometimes<BR>seven, i. e. the preceding with Rāhu and Ketu or<BR>the ascending and descending nodes; sometimes<BR>nine, i. e. the sun and moon together with the<BR>preceding: the planets are either auspicious, शुभ-<BR>ग्रहास्, सद्-ग्रहास्; or inauspicious, क्रूर-ग्रहास्,<BR>पाप-ग्रहास्; in the system of the Jainas the planets<BR>constitute one of the five classes of the Jyotiṣka);<BR>the place of a planet in the fixed zodiac, a N. for the<BR>number nine; N. of certain evil demons or spirits<BR>who seize or exercise a bad influence on the body and<BR>mind of man, (they cause insanity &c.; the Hindūs<BR>consider that it falls within the province of medical<BR>science to expel these demons; those which especially<BR>seize children and cause convulsions &c. are divided<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-b" target="_blank">Page0303-b+ 81</a>]<BR>into nine classes, according to the number of the planets,<BR>cf. पूतना); any state of mind which proceeds from<BR>magical influences and takes possession of the whole<BR>man; a crocodile, a shark; a house (= गृह, in अ-ग्र-<BR>ह, खर-ग्˚, ग्रह-द्रुम, ग्रह-पति); anything<BR>seized, spoil, booty, prey; as much as can be taken<BR>with a ladle, spoon &c. out of a larger vessel, a ladle-<BR>ful, spoonful, &c.; any ladle or vessel employed for<BR>taking up a portion of fluid out of a larger vessel,<BR>(especially applied to the vessels used for taking up<BR>the Soma; cf. सोम-ग्रह); the middle of a bow<BR>or that part which is grasped when the bow is used;<BR>grasp, seizing, laying hold of, the drawing up or<BR>taking up of water &c. [cf. नीर-ग्रह]; seizure<BR>in general (e. g. अङ्ग-ग्रह, spasm of the limbs),<BR>seizure of the sun or moon, eclipse; a movable point<BR>in the heavens; stealing, robbing; taking, receiving,<BR>reception, receipt; keeping back, obstructing; men-<BR>tion, nomination; apprehension, perception, intelli-<BR>gence, understanding; an organ or instrument of<BR>apprehension (of which according to the Upaniṣads<BR>there are eight, viz. Prāṇa, Vāc, Jihvā, Cakṣus,<BR>Śrotra, Manas, Hastau, and Tvac); insisting upon,<BR>tenacity, perseverance, purpose, design, favour, pa-<BR>tronage; a N. of the fourth or fifth book of the<BR>Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa; [cf. गुद-ग्रह, शिरो-ग्र्˚,<BR>हनु-ग्र्˚, हृद्-ग्र्˚.]<BR>—ग्रह-कल्लोल, अस्, m. the<BR>wave (or enemy ?) of the planets, an epithet of<BR>Rāhu.<BR>—ग्रह-गण, अस्, m. the whole number of<BR>planets taken collectively.<BR>—ग्रह-गणित, अम्, n.<BR>= गणित, the astronomical part of a Jyotiḥ-śāstra.<BR>—ग्रह-चिन्तक, अस्, m. an astrologer.<BR>—ग्रह-<BR>ता, f. or ग्रह-त्व, अम्, n. state of being a planet.<BR>—ग्रह-दशा, f. the aspect of the planets.<BR>—ग्रह-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. the creeper Gymnema Sylvestre, = शा-<BR>क-वृक्ष; [cf. गृह-द्रुम.]<BR>—ग्रह-नायक,<BR>अस्, m. the leader of the planets; the planet Saturn;<BR>the sun.<BR>—ग्रह-नाश or ग्रह-नाशन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the plant Alstonia Scholaris, commonly छा-<BR>तिन.<BR>—ग्रह-निग्रह, औ, m. du. favour and<BR>punishment.<BR>—ग्रह-नेमि, इस्, m. the moon.<BR>—ग्रह-पति, इस्, m. the chief of the planets, the<BR>sun; the plant Calotropis Gigantea [cf. अर्क], =<BR>गृह-पति.<BR>—ग्रह-पीडन, अम्, n. or ग्रह-<BR>पीडा, f. the pain or oppression caused by a planet; the<BR>obscurity caused by Rāhu, an eclipse; the influence of<BR>an unpropitious planet.<BR>—ग्रह-पुष, अस्, m. the<BR>sun (cherishing the planets with his light).<BR>—ग्रह-<BR>पूजा, f. worship of the sun and other planets.<BR>—ग्रह-भक्ति, इस्, f. distribution among the<BR>planets, division of countries &c. with respect to<BR>the presiding planets; title of the sixteenth chapter<BR>in Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-saṃhitā.<BR>—ग्रह-भीति-<BR>जित्, त्, m., N. of a perfume (‘conquering the fear<BR>of the demons’).<BR>—ग्रह-भोजन, अस्, m. a horse.<BR>—ग्रह-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of planets.<BR>—ग्रह-मर्दन, अम्, n. friction or opposition<BR>between the planets.<BR>—ग्रह-यज्ञ or ग्रह-<BR>याग, अस्, m. worship or sacrifice offered to the<BR>planets.<BR>—ग्रहयज्ञ-तत्त्व, अम्, n. title of a<BR>part of the Smṛti-tattva.<BR>—ग्रह-युति, इस्, m. con-<BR>junction of the planets.<BR>—ग्रह-युद्ध, अम्, n.<BR>strife or opposition of the planets; title of the<BR>seventeenth Adhyāya of Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-<BR>saṃhitā.<BR>—ग्रह-राज, अस्, m. the king of the<BR>planets; the sun; the moon; the planet Jupiter or<BR>its regent.<BR>—ग्रह-लाघव, अम्, n. title of an<BR>astronomical work of the sixteenth century.<BR>—ग्रह-<BR>वर्ष, अस्, m. a planetary year; title of the nine-<BR>teenth Adhyāya of Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-saṃhitā,<BR>which describes the good or evil fortune belonging<BR>to certain days, months or years ruled over by par-<BR>ticular planets.<BR>—ग्रह-विप्र, अस्, m. an astrologer.<BR>—ग्रह-विमर्द, अस्, m. friction of the planets,<BR>opposition, = ग्रह-मर्दन.<BR>—ग्रह-शान्ति, इस्,<BR>f. propitiation of the planets by sacrifices &c.<BR>—ग्रह-<BR>शृङ्गाटक, अम्, n. triangular position of the planets<BR>with reference to each other; title of the twentieth<BR>Adhyāya in Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-saṃhitā, treating<BR>also of many other positions of the planets.<BR>—ग्रह-<BR>समागम, अस्, m. conjunction of the planets; also<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">Page0303-c+ 81</a>]<BR>in the comp. शशि-ग्रह-समागम, conjunction<BR>of the moon with asterisms or planets.<BR>—ग्रहा-<BR>धार (˚ह-आध्˚), अस्, m. the polar star as the fixed<BR>centre of the planets.<BR>—ग्रहाधीन (˚ह-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, subject to planetary influence.<BR>—ग्रहामय<BR>(˚ह-आम्˚), अस्, m. epilepsy, convulsions, demoniacal<BR>possession, which is supposed to cause the complaint.<BR>—ग्रहाराम-कुतूहल or करण-कुतूहल, अम्,<BR>n., N. of an astronomical work by Bhāskara.<BR>—ग्र-<BR>हालुञ्चन (˚ह-आल्˚), अम्, n. pouncing on prey,<BR>seizing and tearing it to pieces.<BR>—ग्रहावमर्दन<BR>(˚ह-अव्˚), अम्, n. friction of the planets, opposition;<BR>[cf. ग्रह-मर्दन.]<BR>—ग्रहाशिन् (˚ह-आश्˚), ई, m.<BR>the plant Echites Scholaris; [cf. ग्रह-नाश.]<BR>—ग्र-<BR>हाश्रय (˚ह-आश्˚), अस्, m. the polar star; [cf. ग्र-<BR>हाधार.]<BR>—ग्रहाह्वय (˚ह-आह्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a plant; [cf. भूताङ्कुश.]<BR>—ग्रहेश (˚ह-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the chief of the planets, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहक|ग्रहकः
ग्रहक, अस्, m. a prisoner; [cf. ग्राहक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहण|ग्रहणं
ग्रहण, अस्, आ, अम्, seizing, holding; (अम्), n.<BR>the hand; an organ of sense; a prisoner, captive;<BR>mentioning, naming, mention, a word mentioned<BR>(e. g. वचन-ग्रहण, the word वचन); seizing,<BR>holding, taking, catching, seizure; taking by the hand,<BR>marrying; receiving, acceptance; taking captive, cap-<BR>tivating, overpowering, imprisonment; seizure of the<BR>sun or moon, eclipse; gaining, obtaining, purchasing;<BR>choosing; taking or drawing up; attraction; putting<BR>on; containing, enclosing; undertaking, undergoing;<BR>service; mentioning with praise, respect; perceiving,<BR>understanding, comprehension, the taking or receiv-<BR>ing of instruction, or the acquirement of any science;<BR>acceptation, meaning; assent, agreement; inviting,<BR>calling, addressing; the taking up of sound, echo;<BR>an organ of sense; [cf. कर-ग्रहण, केश-ग्˚,<BR>गर्भ-ग्˚, चक्षुर्-ग्˚, नाम-ग्˚, पाणि-ग्˚, पुनर्-<BR>ग्˚.]<BR>—ग्रहणान्त (˚ण-अन्˚), अम्, n. close of study,<BR>acquirement of science &c.<BR>—ग्रहणान्तिक (˚ण-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. termination of holy study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणक
ग्रहणक, अम्, n. containing, involving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणि|ग्रहणिः
ग्रहणि, इस् or ई, f. an imaginary organ supposed<BR>to lie between the stomach and the intestines; the<BR>small intestines or that part of the alimentary canal<BR>where the bile assists digestion and from which vital<BR>warmth is diffused; diarrhœa, dysentery.<BR>—ग्रहणी-<BR>दोष, अस्, m. a morbid affection of the Grahaṇī,<BR>diarrhœa.<BR>—ग्रहणी-प्रदोष, अस्, m. a morbid<BR>affection of the Grahaṇī.<BR>—ग्रहणी-रुज्, क्, f. or<BR>ग्रहणी-रोग, अस्, m. a morbid affection of the<BR>Grahaṇī, diarrhœa.<BR>—ग्रहणीरोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, affected<BR>with diarrhœa.<BR>—ग्रहणी-हर, अम्, n. cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीय
ग्रहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, acceptable, to be taken or<BR>received or understood.<BR>—ग्रहणीय-ता, f. or ग्र-<BR>हणीय-त्व, अम्, n. acceptableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयाय्य
ग्रहयाय्य, another form for गृहयाय्य,<BR>lord of a house, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयालु
ग्रहयालु, उस्, उस्, उ, for गृहयालु, taking,<BR>receiving, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहि
ग्रहि, at the end of a compound in फले-ग्रहि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहिल
ग्रहिल, अस्, आ, अम्, taking, accepting, acknow-<BR>ledging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहिष्णु
ग्रहिष्णु, at the end of a compound in फल-<BR>ग्रहिष्णु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहीतव्य
ग्रहीतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taken or received,<BR>acceptable, to be accepted; to be taken up or drawn<BR>(as a fluid); to be apprehended or perceived, to be<BR>learned or acquired; (अम्), n. the being obliged to<BR>take or receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहीतृ
ग्रहीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a taker, seizer, accepter,<BR>receiver, purchaser; perceiver, perceiving, observant;<BR>taking, disposed to take; [cf. पाणि-ग्रहीतृ and<BR>गृहीतृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह्य
ग्रह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to or fit for<BR>a Graha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राभ
ग्राभ, अस्, m., Ved. one who seizes, what is<BR>seized; grasp, seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह|ग्राहं|ग्राहः
ग्राह, अस्, ई, अम्, seizing, holding, catching,<BR>taking, receiving, acceptance (e. g. ऋक्थ-ग्राह,<BR>receiving inherited property; योषिद्-ग्राह, taking<BR>a wife); [cf. कर्ण-ग्राह, गिल-ग्˚, धनुर्-ग्˚,<BR>पाणि-ग्˚, पार्ष्णि-ग्˚, &c.]; (अस्), m. a rapacious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">Page0304-a+ 80</a>]<BR>animal living in fresh or sea water; a crocodile, a<BR>shark, a serpent; (according to some the Gangetic<BR>alligator or Lacerta Gangetica, according to others<BR>the water elephant or hippopotamus); any large<BR>fish or marine animal; (ई), f. a female crocodile;<BR>(अस्), m. a prisoner; seizure, grasping, laying hold of;<BR>morbid affection, disease; beginning, undertaking;<BR>mentioning; [cf. नाम-ग्राह; cf. also असद्-ग्राह<BR>and स्वयं-ग्राह.]<BR>—ग्राह-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>containing or abounding with alligators &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहक|ग्राहकः
ग्राहक, अस्, इका, अम्, receiving, accepting, one<BR>who takes or seizes; a purchaser, buyer; containing,<BR>enclosing; perceiving, observing; taking away, per-<BR>suading; (अस्), m. a police-officer, a constable, a<BR>bailiff; a hawk, a falcon [cf. Gr. γρύφ; Germ. greif];<BR>a kind of vegetable, = सितावर; N. of an attendant<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहम्
ग्राहम्, ind. part. taking, seizing, mentioning,<BR>(often at the end of compounds, e. g. जीव-ग्राहम्,<BR>taking alive; cf. also नाम-ग्राहम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहि|ग्राहिः
ग्राहि, इस्, f., Ved. a female spirit of evil, seizing<BR>men and causing death and disease, (Sleep is described<BR>as her son); deprivation of sensation, a swoon, faint-<BR>ing fit.<BR>—ग्राहि-फल, अम्, n. the tree Feronia<BR>Elephantum; [cf. कपित्थ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहित
ग्राहित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to take or seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहिन्
ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, seizing, taking, holding, laying<BR>hold of; catching, engaged in catching; picking,<BR>gathering; containing, holding; drawing, attracting,<BR>fascinating, alluring; gaining, obtaining, acquiring;<BR>choosing; searching through, scrutinizing; perceiv-<BR>ing, observing; accepting, taking to heart; astringent;<BR>obstructing, binding, constipating; (ई), m. the plant<BR>Feronia Elephantum [cf. कपित्थ]; (इणी), f. a small<BR>kind of Yavāśa; a kind of Hedysarum, = क्षुद्र-<BR>दुरालभा, ताम्र-मूला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहुक
ग्राहुक, अस्, ई, अम्, seizing, laying hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह्य|ग्राह्यः
ग्राह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be seized, taken, held; to<BR>be captured or imprisoned; to be carried away; to<BR>be picked or gathered, acceptable; to be received,<BR>accepted, gained; to be perceived, observed; to be<BR>taken in marriage; to be received in a friendly or<BR>hospitable manner; to be insisted upon; to be<BR>understood, perceivable; to be considered; to be<BR>understood in a particular sense, meant; to be ac-<BR>cepted as a rule or law, to be acknowledged or<BR>assented to, to be attended to or obeyed, to be<BR>admitted in evidence; acceptable, agreeable; (अम्),<BR>n. a present; [cf. दुर्-ग्राह्य, सुख-ग्राह्य,<BR>स्वयं-ग्राह्य.]<BR>—ग्राह्य-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, uttering<BR>agreeable speech, praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह्यक
ग्राह्यक, अस्, इका, अम्, to be perceived; to be<BR>discerned or distinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम|ग्रामः
ग्राम ग्राम, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. ग्रस्<BR>or fr. ग्रह्), an inhabited place, a village, a hamlet,<BR>an inhabited and unfortified place in the midst of fields<BR>and cultivated land, a municipal and fiscal division, a<BR>township (opposed to अरण्य, and in later Sanskrit also<BR>to पुर, नगर, and पत्तन); the collective in-<BR>habitants of a place, a community, race; any number<BR>of men associated together, a troop, multitude, collec-<BR>tion, especially a troop of soldiers; a number of tunes,<BR>a scale in music, a gamut; (at the end of a compound)<BR>a multitude, a class, a collection or number in general;<BR>[cf. अरिष्ट-ग्राम, महा-ग्˚, शूर-ग्˚, सङ्ग्राम;<BR>cf. also Lith. kiêma-s; Hib. gramaisg, ‘the mob;’<BR>gramasgar, ‘a flock, company.’]<BR>—ग्राम-कण्टक,<BR>अस्, m. the village-pest or tale-bearer.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, one who wishes to take posses-<BR>sion of a village; desirous of villages; fond of living<BR>in villages.<BR>—ग्राम-कुक्कुट, अस्, m. a village cock,<BR>a tame or domestic cock.<BR>—ग्राम-कुमार, अस्, m.<BR>a village boy.<BR>—ग्राम-कुलाल, अस्, m. a village<BR>potter.<BR>—ग्राम-कूट, अस्, m. the noblest man in a<BR>village, a Śūdra or man of the fourth tribe.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>ग, अस्, आ, अम्, or ग्राम-गमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who or<BR>what goes to a village, (Pāṇ. II. 1, 24.)<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>गृह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being outside a village, (lit. ad-<BR>joining the houses of a village.)<BR>—ग्राम-गेय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be sung in a village.<BR>—ग्रामगेय-गान, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-b" target="_blank">Page0304-b+ 81</a>]<BR>n. one of the four books into which the Sāma-veda<BR>when arranged for chanting is distributed.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>गोदुह्, -धुक्, m. the herdsman of a village.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>घात, अस्, m. plundering a village.<BR>—ग्राम-घातिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, devastating or plundering a village.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>घोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. sounding among men or<BR>armies, as a drum.<BR>—ग्रामङ्-गमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who<BR>or what goes to a village.<BR>—ग्राम-चर्या, f. the<BR>customs of social life, social intercourse.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>चैत्य, अस्, m. the sacred tree of a village.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, village-born, village-produced; rustic,<BR>village, grown in cultivated ground.<BR>—ग्रामज-<BR>निष्पावी, f. a kind of pulse.<BR>—ग्राम-जात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, rustic, village-born, produced in a village, grown<BR>in cultivated ground.<BR>—ग्राम-जाल, अम्, n. a num-<BR>ber of villages, a district.<BR>—ग्रामजालिन्, ई, m. the<BR>governor of a province.<BR>—ग्राम-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>conquering or gaining villages; conquering troops;<BR>(Sāy.) either conquering villages or dispersing mul-<BR>titudes.<BR>—ग्रामण, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from a<BR>Grāma-ṇī.<BR>—ग्राम-णी, ईस्, ईस्, इ (for ग्राम-नी), the<BR>leader or chief of a village or community, the lord<BR>of the manor, the squire, the leader of a troop or<BR>army; a chief, a superintendent; best, pre-eminent,<BR>excellent; one who only thinks of enjoyment (?),<BR>the village barber (as the chief person of a village);<BR>a groom (?); N. of a Gandharva chief; N. of one of<BR>the attendants of Śiva; N. of certain beings who<BR>together with the Ṛṣis, Gandharvas, Apsarasas,<BR>Nāgas, Yātu-dhānas, and Bālakhilyas are by some<BR>supposed to be attendant upon the Sun; N. of a<BR>place; (ईस्), f. a female peasant or villager; a whore,<BR>a harlot; the Indigo plant.<BR>—ग्रामणी-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the position or condition of a chief or leader of a<BR>village.<BR>—ग्रामणीथ्य, अम्, n. the station of the<BR>chief of a village or community.<BR>—ग्रामणी-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. the son of a harlot, a bastard.<BR>—ग्रामणीय,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (अम्), n. = ग्रामणीथ्य.<BR>—ग्रामणी-सव, अस्, m., N. of an Ekāha sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>—ग्राम-तक्ष, अस्, m. a village carpenter.<BR>—ग्राम-तस्, ind. from the village.<BR>—ग्राम-ता,<BR>f. or ग्राम-त्व, अम्, n. a multitude of villages.<BR>—ग्राम-दशेश (˚श-ईश), अस्, or ग्रामदशा-<BR>धिपति (˚श-अध्˚), इस्, m. the head of ten villages.<BR>—ग्राम-देवता, f. the tutelary deity of a villages.<BR>—ग्राम-द्रुम, अस्, m. a single tree in a village<BR>held sacred by the inhabitants.<BR>—ग्राम-धरा, f.<BR>supporting a village or villages, N. of a rock.<BR>—ग्राम-धर्म, अस्, m. the observances or cus-<BR>toms of a village.<BR>—ग्राम-नापित, अस्, m. the village<BR>barber.<BR>—ग्राम-निवासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in villages,<BR>tame.<BR>—ग्राम-पाल, अस्, m. the guardian of a<BR>village.<BR>—ग्राम-पुत्र, अस्, m. a village boy.<BR>—ग्राम-प्रेष्य, अस्, m. the messenger or ser-<BR>vant of a community or village.<BR>—ग्राम-बाल-<BR>जन, अस्, m. a young peasant.<BR>—ग्राम-भृत,<BR>अस्, m. a village messenger or servant.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>मद्गुरिका, f. a kind of fish, Silurus Singio (=<BR>शृङ्गी); a riot, a fray, a village tumult; [cf. ग्राम-<BR>युद्ध.]<BR>—ग्राम-महिषी, f. a tame buffalo.<BR>—ग्राम-मुख, अम्, n. a market town, a fair,<BR>a market.<BR>—ग्राम-मृग, अस्, m. ‘the village<BR>animal,’ a dog.<BR>—ग्राम-मौख्य, head of a vil-<BR>lage; (probably incorrect for ग्राम-सौख्य, see<BR>ग्राम-सुख.)<BR>—ग्राम-याजक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>offering sacrifices for a whole village or community;<BR>(अस्), m. the village priest, one who conducts the<BR>ceremonies for any or all classes and is consequently<BR>considered as a degraded Brāhman; it also applies<BR>to the attendant of an idol.<BR>—ग्राम-याजिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, offering sacrifices for a whole village or community.<BR>—ग्राम-युद्ध, अम्, n. a riot, a fray, a village<BR>war.<BR>—ग्राम-रथ्या, f. a village street.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>लुण्टन, अम्, n. plundering or pillaging a village.<BR>—ग्राम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with villages.<BR>—ग्राम-वास, अस्, m. living in a village; a villager;<BR>[cf. ग्रामे-वास.]<BR>—ग्राम-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living<BR>in villages, tame; (इनस्), m. pl. the inhabitants<BR>of a village, the villagers; [cf. ग्रामे-वासिन् and<BR>ग्राम्य.]<BR>—ग्राम-वास्तव्य, अस्, m. the inhabitant<BR>of a village.<BR>—ग्राम-विशेष, अस्, m. variety of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">Page0304-c+ 81</a>]<BR>scales in music.<BR>—ग्राम-शत, अम्, n. a hundred<BR>villages, a province.<BR>—ग्रामशतेश (˚त-ईश), अस्,<BR>m. or ग्रामशताधिपति (˚त-अध्˚), इस्, m. or ग्रा-<BR>मशताध्यक्ष (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, m. the governor<BR>of a province.<BR>—ग्राम-सङ्कर, अस्, m. the com-<BR>mon sewer or drain of a village.<BR>—ग्राम-सङ्घ,<BR>अस्, m. a village corporation, a municipality.<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>सिंह, अस्, m. a dog.<BR>—ग्राम-सुख, अम्, n. the<BR>pleasure of a villager; [cf. ग्राम्य-सुख.]<BR>—ग्राम-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being or residing in a village, be-<BR>longing to a village, rustic, &c.; (अस्), m. a village.<BR>—ग्राम-हासक, अस्, m. a sister's husband.<BR>—ग्रा-<BR>माचार (˚म-आच्˚), अस्, m. village observances, cus-<BR>toms, &c.<BR>—ग्रामाधान (˚म-आध्˚), अम्, n. hunt-<BR>ing; a village (?).<BR>—ग्रामाधिकृत (˚म-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>or ग्रामाधिपति (˚म-अध्˚), इस्, or ग्रामाध्यक्ष<BR>(˚म-अध्˚), अस्, or ग्रामाधिकारिन् (˚म-अध्˚),<BR>ई, m. superintendent or chief of a village.<BR>—ग्रा-<BR>मान्त (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, m. the border of a village;<BR>space near a village; (ए), ind. in the neighbourhood<BR>of a village.<BR>—ग्रामान्तर (˚म-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>another village.<BR>—ग्रामान्तिक, अम्, n. the neigh-<BR>bourhood of a village.<BR>—ग्रामान्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>situated in the neighbourhood of a village; (अम्), n.<BR>space near a village.<BR>—ग्रामे-वास, अस्, m. a village<BR>abode; a villager; [cf. ग्राम-वास.]<BR>—ग्रामे-<BR>वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, living in a village, tame; (इनस्),<BR>m. pl. the villagers.<BR>—ग्रामेश (˚म-ईश), अस्, m.<BR>the head man of a village.<BR>—ग्रामेश्वर (˚म-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the head man or ruler over a village; the lord<BR>of the manor or squire.<BR>—ग्रामोपाध्याय (˚म-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. the village priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामक|ग्रामकः
ग्रामक, अस्, m. a village &c., see ग्राम; the<BR>collective department or range of celestial pleasures;<BR>N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामय
ग्रामय, nom. P. ग्रामयति, -यितुम्, to invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिक|ग्रामिकः
ग्रामिक, अस्, ई, अम्, village, rude, rustic; (in<BR>music) chromatic; (अस्), m. the head man of a<BR>village; a villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिन्
ग्रामिन्, ई, इणी, इ, surrounded by a village com-<BR>munity, pertaining to a village, rustic, rural, village;<BR>(ई), m. a villager, a peasant; the head man of a<BR>village; (इणी), f. the Indigo plant.<BR>—ग्रामि-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. the son of a villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीण|ग्रामीणः
ग्रामीण, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a village; pro-<BR>duced in or peculiar to a village; vulgar, rude; (in<BR>music) chromatic; a villager, a rustic; (अस्), m. a<BR>dog; a hog; a crow; (आ), f. the Indigo plant; a<BR>kind of vegetable; [cf. पालङ्क्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीय|ग्रामीयः
ग्रामीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a village or to<BR>the same village community; produced in or derived<BR>from a village; (अस्), m. a villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीयक|ग्रामीयकः
ग्रामीयक, अस्, m. the member of a community,<BR>a villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेय
ग्रामेय, अस्, ई, अम्, village-born, a villager, a rustic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेयक|ग्रामेयकः
ग्रामेयक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to a village,<BR>a villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्य|ग्राम्यः
ग्राम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or used in a village,<BR>produced in a village; living in a village, a villager,<BR>rustic, homely, vulgar, clownish, rude; living in a<BR>village, i. e. among men, domesticated, tame (as an<BR>animal), cultivated (as a plant, opposed to वन्य or<BR>अरण्य, wild); allowed in a village, relating to the<BR>sensual pleasures of a village; relating to a musical<BR>scale; (अस्), m. a hog, a tame or village hog; (आ),<BR>f. the Indigo plant, and Phaseolus Radiata; [cf. निष्-<BR>पावी]; (अम्), n. rustic or homely speech; the<BR>Prākṛt and the other dialects of India as contra-<BR>distinguished from the Sanskrit; food prepared in a<BR>village; sensual pleasure, sexual intercourse.<BR>—ग्रा-<BR>म्य-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of onion, = स्थल-<BR>कन्द; (perhaps rather अग्राम्य-कन्द.)<BR>—ग्रा-<BR>म्य-कर्कटी, f. a kind of pumpkin-gourd, Benincasa<BR>Cerifera.<BR>—ग्राम्य-कर्मन्, अ, n. the occupation<BR>of a villager, sensual pleasure and sexual intercourse.<BR>—ग्राम्य-कुङ्कुम, अम्, n. a yellow dye, saf-<BR>flower, Carthamus Tinctorius.<BR>—ग्राम्य-गज, अस्, m.<BR>a village-born or tame elephant.<BR>—ग्राम्य-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m. the right of a villager or townsman (as opposed<BR>to the right of a recluse), sexual intercourse, copula-<BR>tion; the duties of a villager.<BR>—ग्राम्यधर्मिन्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">Page0305-a+ 78</a>]<BR>ई, इणी, इ, addicted to sexual intercourse, libidinous.<BR>—ग्राम्य-पशु, उस्, m. a domestic animal; (some-<BR>times applied contemptuously to a man.)<BR>—ग्राम्य-<BR>बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, clownish, ignorant.<BR>—ग्राम्य-<BR>मद्गुरिका, f. a kind of fish, Silurus Singio, =<BR>ग्राम-मद्गुरिका.<BR>—ग्राम्य-मांस, अम्, n. the<BR>flesh of tame animals.<BR>—ग्राम्य-मृग, अस्, m. a<BR>dog; [cf. ग्राम-मृग.]<BR>—ग्राम्य-राशि, इस्, m. a<BR>N. of several of the signs of the zodiac.<BR>—ग्राम्य-<BR>वल्लभा, f. a kind of vegetable.<BR>—ग्राम्य-वादिन्,<BR>ई, m. the judge of a village, a village bailiff.<BR>—ग्राम्य-शूकर, अस्, m. a village hog, a tame<BR>hog, a pig.<BR>—ग्राम्य-सुख, अम्, n. the pleasure<BR>of a villager, sleeping, sexual intercourse.<BR>—ग्राम्या-<BR>श्व (˚य-अश्˚), अस्, m. an ass.<BR>—ग्राम्येहोपरम<BR>(˚य-ईहा-उप्˚), अस्, m. ceasing from sensual desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रावन्
ग्रावन् ग्रावन्, आ, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>ग्रह्), a stone for pressing out the Soma, (according<BR>to the commentators on the Brāhmaṇas there existed<BR>five such stones, but in earlier times probably only<BR>two were used); a stone or rock in general; a moun-<BR>tain; a cloud; also = ग्राव-स्तुत् below; (आ, आ, अ),<BR>hard, solid.<BR>—ग्राव-ग्राभ, अस्, m., Ved. a person<BR>who uses the Soma stones.<BR>—ग्राव-रोहक, अस्, m.<BR>the shrub Physalis Flexuosa; [cf. अश्व-गन्धा.]<BR>—ग्राव-स्तुत्, त्, m. he who praises the Soma<BR>stones; N. of one of the sixteen priests (called<BR>after the hymn addressed to the Soma stones).<BR>—ग्राव-स्तोत्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging<BR>to the praise of the Soma stones; (अम्), n. the<BR>duties of the Grāva-stut.<BR>—ग्राव-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. handling the Soma stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रास|ग्रासः
ग्रास ग्रास. See under rt. ग्रस्, p. 302.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह|ग्राहं|ग्राहः
ग्राह ग्राह. See under rt. ग्रह्, p. 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवा
ग्रीवा ग्रीवा, f. (said to be fr. 2. गॄ), the back<BR>part of the neck, the nape, the tendon of the trapezium<BR>muscle, the neck (in the earlier literature always pl.),<BR>the neck-part of the hide of an animal; [cf. असित-<BR>ग्रीव, ऋक्ष-ग्˚, कम्बु-ग्˚, कल्माष-ग्˚; cf. also<BR>Lith. galwà; Russ. glava and golova.]<BR>—ग्रीवा-<BR>क्ष (˚वा-अक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—ग्रीवा-<BR>घण्टा, f. a bell hanging down from the neck of a<BR>horse.<BR>—ग्रीवा-बिल, अम्, n. the hollow in the back<BR>part or nape of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवालिका
ग्रीवालिका, f. the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीविन्
ग्रीविन्, ई, इणी, इ, long-necked, handsome-necked;<BR>(ई), m. a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव|ग्रैवं
ग्रैव, अस्, ई, अम्, being on or belonging to the<BR>neck, representing the neck, being on the neck;<BR>(अम्), n. a necklace, a close necklace or collar; a<BR>chain worn round the neck of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेय|ग्रैवेयं
ग्रैवेय, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the neck; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. a collar, a necklace; a chain on the neck<BR>of an elephant or horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेयक|ग्रैवेयकं
ग्रैवेयक, अस्, अम्, m. n. an ornament of the<BR>neck, a chain worn round the neck of an elephant;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. a class of deities (nine in number), who<BR>have their seat on the neck of the Loka-puruṣa or<BR>who form his necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव्य
ग्रैव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्म|ग्रीष्मः
ग्रीष्म ग्रीष्म, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>ग्रस्), hot, warm; (अस्), m. the summer, the hot<BR>season, consisting of the months Śuci and Śukra or<BR>Jyeṣṭha and Āṣāḍha (from the middle of May to<BR>the middle of July); heat, warmth; N. of a man;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a tree [cf. लोध्र]; (ई), f. the tree<BR>Jasminum Sambac; [cf. नव-मल्लिका; cf. also Hib.<BR>gris, ‘fire;’ griosgaim, ‘I fry, boil;’ griosach,<BR>‘burning embers;’ Lith. karsztas and karsztis.]<BR>—ग्रीष्म-काल, अस्, m. the hot season (see above).<BR>—ग्रीष्मकालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, pertaining to the hot<BR>season.<BR>—ग्रीष्म-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by heat,<BR>produced in the hot season; (आ), f. a kind of fruit-<BR>tree, Anona Reticulata; [cf. लवनी.]<BR>—ग्रीष्म-<BR>धान्य, अम्, n. summer corn.<BR>—ग्रीष्म-पुष्पी,<BR>f., N. of a plant, = करुणी.<BR>—ग्रीष्म-भव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced by heat or in the hot season; (आ),<BR>f. Jasminum Sambac.<BR>—ग्रीष्म-सुन्दरक, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">Page0305-b+ 72</a>]<BR>m. a kind of pot-herb, Erythræa Centaureoides,<BR>commonly called गिमा; also the plant Pharnaceum<BR>Mollugo.<BR>—ग्रीष्म-हास, अस्, m. the flocculent<BR>seeds, down, &c., blown about in the air in summer<BR>(compared from their white colour to ‘the smiles of<BR>the season’).<BR>—ग्रीष्मोद्भव (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced by heat or in the hot season; (आ), f.<BR>double jasmine, Jasminum Sambac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्म
ग्रैष्म, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the summer, be-<BR>longing to the hot weather, produced by heat or the<BR>hot season, sown in summer; (ई), f. Jasminum<BR>Sambac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्मक
ग्रैष्मक, अस्, इका, अम्, sown in summer; to<BR>be paid in summer (as a debt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्मिक
ग्रैष्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>summer, growing in summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रुच्
ग्रुच् ग्रुच्, cl. 1. P. ग्रोचति, जुग्रोच,<BR>अग्रुचत् and अग्रोचीत्, ग्रोचितुम्, to steal,<BR>rob; to go; [cf. ग्लुच्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव|ग्रैवं
ग्रैव ग्रैव. See under ग्रीवा last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्म
ग्रैष्म ग्रैष्म. See under ग्रीष्म above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लप्
ग्लप् ग्लप्. Cf. ग्लै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लप्स
ग्लप्स ग्लप्स, अस्, अम्, m. n. a branch (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस्
ग्लस् ग्लस्, cl. 1. A. ग्लसते, = ग्रस्, to<BR>eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस्त|ग्लस्तः
ग्लस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, = ग्रस्त, eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह्
ग्लह् ग्लह्, cl. 1. A. ग्लहते, जग्लहे, ग्ल-<BR>हितुम् and ग्लाढुम्, to gamble, play with<BR>dice, win by gambling; (= rt. ग्रह्) to take, re-<BR>ceive, accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह|ग्लहः
ग्लह, अस्, m. a dice-player, the stake in playing,<BR>a wager, bet; the prize or object fought for in a<BR>contest, the person aimed at; a die; a dice-box;<BR>cast of the dice, game at dice; gaming, playing<BR>with dice; contention; a chess-man; ग्लहं दिव्,<BR>to play at dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लहन
ग्लहन, अम्, n., Ved. playing at dice, casting<BR>the dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लान|ग्लानः
ग्लान ग्लान, ग्लानि, &c. See under rt. ग्लै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुच्
ग्लुच् ग्लुच्, cl. 1. P. ग्लोचति, जुग्लोच, अग्लु-<BR>चत् and अग्लोचीत्, ग्लोचितुम्, to steal or rob;<BR>to go; [cf. ग्रुच् and ग्लुञ्च्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुचुक
ग्लुचुक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुञ्च्|ग्लुंच्
ग्लुञ्च् ग्लुञ्च्, cl. 1. P. प्लुञ्चति, जुग्लुञ्च,<BR>अग्लुञ्चत् and अग्लुञ्चीत्, ग्लुञ्चितुम्, to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेप्
ग्लेप् ग्लेप्, cl. 1. A. ग्लेपते, &c., to be<BR>poor or miserable; to shake, tremble;<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेव्
ग्लेव् ग्लेव्, cl. 1. A. ग्लेवते, to serve,<BR>worship, gratify by service or devotedness;<BR>[cf. गेव्, खेव्, सेव्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेष्
ग्लेष् ग्लेष्, cl. 1. A. ग्लेषते, to seek,<BR>investigate; [cf. गेष् and गवेष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लै
ग्लै ग्लै, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) ग्लायति, -ते,<BR>जग्लौ, ग्लास्यति, अग्लासीत्, ग्लातुम्, to feel<BR>aversion or dislike, to be averse or reluctant, be un-<BR>willing, disinclined to do anything (with inf., e. g.<BR>ग्लायति भोक्तुम्, he dislikes to eat); to be languid<BR>or weary, to feel tired, to be exhausted, to fade away,<BR>lose one's strength, faint, despond, wane: Caus. P.<BR>ग्लापयति or ग्लपयति (but the latter form never<BR>used with prepositions), to make unwilling or averse,<BR>to exhaust, tire; to injure; to cause to perish; (with<BR>or without मनस्) to make desponding; to become<BR>cast down or desponding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लपन|ग्लपनं
ग्लपन, अम्, n. the act of wearying, making<BR>tired, exhaustion, relaxation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लातृ
ग्लातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who is tired or exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लान|ग्लानः
ग्लान, अस्, आ, अम्, wearied, languid, feeble, emaci-<BR>ated, exhausted by fatigue or disease; sick; (अम्),<BR>n. exhaustion, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लानि|ग्लानिः
ग्लानि, इस्, f. unwillingness, displeasure, depression<BR>of mind, exhaustion, fatigue of body, lassitude, lan-<BR>guor; debility; sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लान्य
ग्लान्य, अम्, n. decrease of strength, languor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लायत्
ग्लायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being exhausted, wearied,<BR>languid, faint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लाव
ग्लाव, अस्, m., N. of a man (with the metronymic<BR>Maitreya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लाविन्
ग्लाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, displeased, averse, inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लास्नु|ग्लास्नुः
ग्लास्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, exhausted by fatigue or disease,<BR>languid, wearied; [cf. Lat. lassus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेय|ग्लेयः
ग्लेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wearied or exhausted, ex-<BR>haustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौ
ग्लौ ग्लौ, औस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. ग्लै),<BR>Ved. a round lump, a wen-like excrescence; or (ac-<BR>cording to other authorities) certain arteries or vessels<BR>of the heart, or perhaps certain lumps, parts of the flesh<BR>of the sacrificial victim [perhaps related to ग्लोबुस्<BR>and ग्लोमुस्, cf. also गुड and गोल]; the moon;<BR>camphor; the earth. ग्लौ-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to transform into the moon. ग्लौ-अस्,<BR>cl. 2. P. -अस्ति and ग्लौ-भू, cl. 1. P. भवति,<BR>वितुम्, to become (like) the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौचुकायनक
ग्लौचुकायनक ग्लौचुकायनक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>belonging to Glucukāyani [cf. ग्लुचुक], a worship-<BR>per of Glucukāyani; [cf. the Gr. Γλαυκανῖκαι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्व
ग्व ग्व (at the end of a compound) in<BR>अतिथि-ग्व, एत-ग्व, दश-ग्व, नव-ग्व, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्विन्
ग्विन् ग्विन्. Cf. शत-ग्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ 1. घ, the fourth consonant of the<BR>Sanskrit alphabet, being the aspirate of the preceding<BR>letter, and having the sound of gh in loghouse.<BR>—घ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ 2. घ, ind. (a particle used to lay stress<BR>on a word), at least, surely, verily, indeed, (cor-<BR>responding to the Gr. γε.) This word occurs often<BR>in the Ṛg-veda, elsewhere rarely; the final vowel is<BR>generally lengthened in the Saṃhitā, but the original<BR>form given in the Pada-pāṭha is always घ; it is<BR>connected with other particles (as चिद्, उत, इद्), and<BR>appears often after pronouns at the beginning of a<BR>Pāda, after prepositions, and after the negative<BR>particle न. Frequently this particle occurs in the<BR>clause which depends on a conditional or relative<BR>sentence (e. g. आ घा गमद् यदि श्रवत्, he will<BR>surely come when he hears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ 3. घ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हन्), striking,<BR>killing [cf. जीव-घ, ताड-घ, पाणि-घ, राज-<BR>घ]; (अस्), m. a rattling, gurgling, or tinkling<BR>sound; a bell; (आ), f. striking, killing, a stroke; a<BR>tinkling ornament worn by women round the waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ 4. घ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. घृ), wetting,<BR>sprinkling (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घंष्
घंष् घंष् and घंस्, cl. 1. A. घं-<BR>षते, घंसते, to diffuse lustre or splen-<BR>dor; to flow; to stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घग्घ्
घग्घ् घग्घ् and घघ्, cl. 1. P. घग्-<BR>घति and घघति, to laugh; laugh at;<BR>deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्
घट् घट् or घण्ट्, cl. 1. A. घटते, ज-<BR>घटे, घटिष्यते, अघटिष्ट, घटितुम्,<BR>to be intently occupied about anything, to be busy<BR>with, to strive or endeavour after, to exert one's self<BR>for (with loc., dat., acc., or inf., e. g. अस्माकम्<BR>अर्थे घटते, he is occupied about our business;<BR>तां त्रातुं घटस्व, strive to rescue her); to<BR>reach, come to; to happen, take place, be possible:<BR>Caus. घटयति, -यितुम्, to join together, connect,<BR>bring together, unite; to put on, place on, lay on<BR>(with loc.); to bring near, place near, procure; to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-a" target="_blank">Page0306-a+ 81</a>]<BR>effect, accomplish, produce, make, form, fashion; to<BR>impel; to exert one's self; to rub, graze, touch,<BR>move, agitate; घाटयति, -यितुम्, to hurt, injure;<BR>to unite or put together; to speak, shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट|घटः
घट, अस्, आ, अम्, exerting one's self, intently<BR>occupied or busy with; (अस्), m. a jar, pitcher, jug,<BR>large earthen water-jar, ewer, watering-pot; an attri-<BR>bute of the nineteenth Arhat of the Jainas (?);<BR>the sign of the zodiac Aquarius; a measure equal to<BR>1 Droṇa, or (according to other authorities) equal to<BR>20 Droṇas; a part of a column; a peculiar form of<BR>a temple; an elephant's frontal sinus; a border;<BR>suspending the breath as a religious exercise [cf.<BR>कुम्भ]; (आ), f. effort, endeavour, an assembly; a<BR>number, a collection, an assemblage; a troop of<BR>elephants assembled for martial purposes; (ई), f. a<BR>small water-jar, a ewer (in this sense also घटि, इस्,<BR>f.); a period of time = 24 minutes; the Gharī or<BR>Indian clock, a plate of iron or mixed metal on<BR>which the hours are struck; [cf. कुम्भ and दुर्-<BR>घट.]<BR>—घट-कर्पर, अस्, m. the fragments of<BR>a pot; N. of the author of a highly artificial poem,<BR>which is also called घट-कर्परम्, n., (according<BR>to other authorities the title of the poem is Yamaka-<BR>kāvya); the poet Ghaṭa-karpara appears among the<BR>nine gems of king Vikramāditya.<BR>—घट-कार, अस्,<BR>m. or घट-कृत्, त्, m. a potter.<BR>—घट-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, who or what takes a water-pot, a water-<BR>bearer.<BR>—घट-दासी, f. a bawd or procuress.<BR>—घ-<BR>ट-प्रक्षयण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—घट-<BR>भव = घटोद्भव (?).<BR>—घट-भेदनक,<BR>अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), an instrument used in<BR>making pots.<BR>—घट-योनि, इस्, m. an epithet of<BR>the sage Agastya, q. v. (born in a water-jar).<BR>—घट-<BR>राज, अस्, m. a large water-jar of baked clay.<BR>—घट-<BR>सृञ्जय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—घट-<BR>स्थापन, अम्, n. placing a water-pot as a type of<BR>Durgā, an essential part of various Tāntrika cere-<BR>monies.<BR>—घटाटोप (˚ट-आट्˚), अस्, m. a covering<BR>for a carriage or any article of furniture.<BR>—घटाभ<BR>(˚ट-आभा), अस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR>—घटिन्-<BR>धम, अस्, आ, अम्, (घटिन् = घटिम् = घटीम्),<BR>one who blows into a jar or pot; (अस्), m. a potter.<BR>—घटिन्-धय, अस्, आ, अम्, one who drinks<BR>a pitcherful.<BR>—घटी-कार, अस्, m. a potter.<BR>—घटी-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what takes a<BR>small jar &c.; (अस्), m. a water-carrier.<BR>—घटी-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. (occasionally, to suit the metre,<BR>घटि-यन्त्र), the rope and bucket of a well, or<BR>any machine for raising water; [cf. अर-घट्ट and<BR>अर-घट्टक.]<BR>—घटोत्कच (˚ट-उत्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Rākṣasa, son of Bhīma or Bhīma-sena and of the<BR>Rākṣasī Hiḍimbā, slain by Karṇa; N. of a Gupta<BR>king.<BR>—घटोत्कचान्तक (˚च-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘the<BR>slayer of Ghaṭotkaca,’ epithet of Karṇa, natural<BR>brother of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—घटोदर (˚ट-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of an attendant of Varuṇa, also of a<BR>Rākṣasa and of a Daitya; [cf. कुम्भोदर.]<BR>—घटोद्भव (˚ट-उद्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Agastya, q. v.<BR>—घटोध्नी (˚ट-ऊध्˚), f. a cow<BR>with a full udder; [see ऊधस्, पीनोध्नी, &c.;<BR>Gram. 778.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटक|घटकः
घटक, अस्, इका, अम्, exerting one's self; form-<BR>ing a constituent part, constituting a substantial part;<BR>(अस्), m. a tree that produces fruit without apparent<BR>flowers; a match-maker, an agent, who ascertains<BR>or invents genealogies and negociates matrimonial<BR>alliances, a genealogist; [cf. घट-दासी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटन|घटनं
घटन, अम्, आ, n. f. striving after, effort, exer-<BR>tion; motion; happening, occurring; accomplish-<BR>ment; making, effecting, forming, fashioning; join-<BR>ing, mixing, assembling, bringing together, bringing<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटयितव्य
घटयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be joined or united;<BR>to be locked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिक|घटिकं|घटिकः
घटिक, अस्, आ, अम्, crossing a river on a jar (?);<BR>(अस्), m. a waterman; (आ), f. a water-jar, a bucket,<BR>a pot; a period of time = 24 minutes [cf. घटी];<BR>(according to other authorities equal to 1 Muhūrta,<BR>i. e. 48 minutes, or = 1 Kalā); the ancle [cf. घुटिका];<BR>(अम्), n. the hip, the posteriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटित
घटित, अस्, आ, अम्, planned, devised, attempted;<BR>happened, occurred; joined, united, connected, con-<BR>tiguous, in contact with; produced, effected, exerted;<BR>made, made of. घटित-त्वात्, from the taking<BR>place, because of the occurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिन्
घटिन्, ई, m. the sign of the zodiac Aquarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटरिका
घटरिका घटरिका, in अव-घटरिका, f. a<BR>a kind of Vīṇā or Indian lute; [cf. घाटरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिघट|घटिघटः
घटिघट घटिघट, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; [cf. घण्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट्
घट्ट् घट्ट्, cl. 1. A. and 10. P. घट्टते,<BR>घट्टयति, जघट्टे, घट्टितुम्, to rub<BR>(the hands) over, touch, shake, cause to move; to<BR>stir round, stir about; to press down, to smooth; to<BR>touch with words, to speak of spitefully or malig-<BR>nantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट|घट्टः
घट्ट, अस्, m. a Ghaṭ, a quay or landing-place,<BR>steps on the side of a river &c. leading to the water's<BR>edge, a bathing-place; (आ), f. a kind of metre; (ई),<BR>f. a small or inferior landing-place, private stairs &c.;<BR>[cf. अर-घट्ट and अर-घट्टक.]<BR>—घट्ट-गा,<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR>—घट्ट-जीविन्, ई, m. a ferry-man<BR>(commonly Pāṭuni, the son of a washerman and of<BR>a Vaiśya woman); an attendant at a landing-place<BR>who takes care of the clothes of the bathers &c.<BR>—घट्टानन्द (˚ट्टा-आन्˚), अस् or अम् (?), m. or<BR>n. (?), a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टन|घट्टनं
घट्टन, अम्, आ, n. f. pushing, touching, rubbing<BR>or striking together, going, moving, practice, busi-<BR>ness, means of living; stirring round or about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टितृ
घट्टितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who exerts himself,<BR>(the sense of this word connects it with rt. घट्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्
घण् घण्, cl. 8. P. A. घणोति, -णुते, &c.,<BR>to shine; (a various reading for घृण्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ट्|घंट्
घण्ट् घण्ट्, cl. 1. P. and 10. P. घण्टति<BR>and घण्टयति, &c., to speak; shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ट|घंट|घण्टः
घण्ट घण्ट, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. हन्,<BR>perhaps related to घट above), a N. of Śiva [cf.<BR>अ-घण्ट, धटिन् or घटिन् (?), घण्टिन्, and<BR>चण्डिक-घण्ट], a kind of dish [cf. मत्स्य-<BR>घण्ट]; a sort of sauce, vegetables made into a<BR>pulp and mixed with turmeric and mustard seeds and<BR>capsicums; (आ), f. a bell; also a plate of iron or mixed<BR>metal struck as a clock, (a form घण्टी occurs in<BR>क्षुद्र-घण्टी, a small bell); N. of several plants,<BR>= घण्टा-पाटलि; another plant, Sida Cordifolia<BR>and Rhombifolia; also Uraria Lagopodioides; also<BR>Achyranthes Aspera [cf. अपामार्ग]; (ई), f. a N. of<BR>Durgā, as having a clear voice (?).<BR>—घण्ट-फ-<BR>लक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), a shield with a<BR>ringing sound, or a shield furnished with small bells.<BR>(घण्ट = घण्टा ?).<BR>—घण्टा-कर्ण, अस्, m.<BR>one who has ears as broad as a bell, or whose ears<BR>are decorated with bells; N. of an attendant of<BR>Skanda; also one of Śiva's attendants, who is sup-<BR>posed to preside over cutaneous complaints, and is<BR>worshipped for exemption from them in the month<BR>Caitra; N. of a Piśāca attendant on Kuvera.<BR>—घण्टागार (˚टा-आग्˚), अम्, n. a belfry.<BR>—घण्टा-ताड, अस्, m. a bell-man, one who strikes<BR>a bell or Gharī.<BR>—घण्टा-ताडन, अम्, n. striking<BR>a bell.<BR>—घण्टा-नाद, अस्, m. the sound of a bell<BR>&c.<BR>—घण्टा-पथ, अस्, m. the chief road through<BR>a village, a highway, (i. e. the bell-road, or that by<BR>which elephants &c., decorated with tinkling orna-<BR>ments, proceed); N. of Mallinātha's commentary on<BR>the Kirātārjunīya.<BR>—घण्टा-पाटलि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant, commonly called Ghaṇṭāpārali, a species of the<BR>trumpet-flower with bell-shaped blossoms, Bignonia<BR>Suaveolens.<BR>—घण्टाभ (˚टा-आभा), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Daitya; (a various reading for घटाभ, q. v.)<BR>—घण्टा-रव, अस्, m. the sound of a bell; (आ), f.<BR>Crotolaria of various species.<BR>—घण्टाली (˚टा-आली),<BR>f., N. of several cucurbitaceous plants; [cf. कोशातकी.]<BR>—घण्टा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with a bell or<BR>with bells.<BR>—घण्टा-वाद्य, अम्, n. the sound of<BR>a clock.<BR>—घण्टा-वीज, अम्, n. the tree Croton<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">Page0306-c+ 79</a>]<BR>Jamalgota, commonly Jamālgoṭā; the nut of this<BR>tree.<BR>—घण्टा-शब्द, अस्, m. bell-metal, brass;<BR>the sound of a bell.<BR>—घण्टा-स्वन, अस्, m. the<BR>sound of a bell or clock.<BR>—घण्टेश्वर (˚टा-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Maṅgala (Mars) and Medhā.<BR>—घण्टोदर (˚ट-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of an attend-<BR>ant of Varuṇa &c.; (a various reading for घटो-<BR>दर, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टक|घण्टकः
घण्टक or घण्टाक, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>= घण्टा-पाटलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिका|घंटिका
घण्टिका, f. a small bell [cf. क्षुद्र-घण्टिका];<BR>the uvula or soft palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिन्|घंटिन्
घण्टिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with bells, sounding<BR>like a bell; an epithet of Śiva; [cf. घण्ट.]<BR>—घण्टिनी-वीज, अम्, n. the tree Croton Jamalgota;<BR>[cf. घण्टा-वीज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टु|घंटुः|घण्टुः
घण्टु, उस्, m. a string of bells tied on an ele-<BR>phant's chest &c. by way of ornament; heat, light,<BR>&c.; [cf. निघण्टु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाण्टिक|घांटिक|घांटिकः|घाण्टिकः
घाण्टिक, अस्, m. a bell-ringer, a strolling ballad-<BR>singer who carries a bell; a bard who sings in chorus,<BR>and especially in honour of the gods, ringing a bell<BR>in presence of their images; the plant Datura<BR>Fastuosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ड|घंडः|घण्डः
घण्ड घण्ड, अस्, m. a bee; [cf. घुण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घतन
घतन घतन. See घातन under घात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घन|घनं|घनः
घन घन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हन्), who or<BR>what slays or strikes or crushes (in these senses Ved.);<BR>compact, solid, material, hard, firm; coarse, gross;<BR>viscid, thick, inspissated; full, densely packed; fol-<BR>lowing closely or in uninterrupted series, uninter-<BR>rupted, permanent, eternal; impenetrable; dark;<BR>deep (as sound); taken in the mass, collective, com-<BR>plete, all; very, much; auspicious, fortunate; (अस्), m.<BR>slaying; an iron club, mace, weapon shaped like a<BR>hammer (in these senses Ved.); any compact mass or<BR>substance; a cloud; talc; the bulbous root of the<BR>plant Cyperus Hexastychus Communis; phlegm [cf.<BR>कफ]; the body; the cube of a number (in<BR>arithmetic), a solid body or cube (in geometry);<BR>extension, diffusion; a collection, multitude, as-<BR>semblage, mass, quantity; a method of reciting the<BR>Ṛg and Yajur-veda; (आ), f., N. of two plants, =<BR>माष-पर्णी and रुद्र-जटा; (अम्), n. a cymbal,<BR>a bell, a gong, &c.; any brazen or metallic instru-<BR>ment or plate which is struck as a clock &c.;<BR>iron; tin; skin, rind, bark, the fragrant bark of<BR>Laurus Cassia; a mode of dancing, neither quick<BR>nor slow.<BR>—घन-कफ, अस्, m. hail; [cf.<BR>घनोपल.]<BR>—घन-काल, अस्, m. the rainy sea-<BR>son.<BR>—घन-गर्जित, अम्, n. the roar of thunder,<BR>a deep loud roar.<BR>—घन-गोलक, अस्, m. an alloy<BR>of gold and silver.<BR>—घन-घन, अस्, m. the cube<BR>of a cube.<BR>—घन-घनौघ (˚न-ओघ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a gathering of dark clouds.<BR>—घन-चय, अस्, m. a<BR>collection of clouds, cumulus.<BR>—घन-च्छद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, involved in clouds.<BR>—घन-जम्बाल, अस्,<BR>m. a quantity of mire, a slough.<BR>—घन-जाल, अम्,<BR>n. a gathering of clouds.<BR>—घन-ज्वाला, f. lightning,<BR>a flash of lightning.<BR>—घन-ता, f. compactness.<BR>—घन-ताल, अस्, m. a kind of bird, = सारङ्ग;<BR>[cf. also घन-तोल.]<BR>—घन-तिमिर, अम्, n. the<BR>darkness of clouds, great darkness.<BR>—घन-तोय,<BR>अस्, m. a particular sea having thick water; [cf.<BR>घनोद.]<BR>—घन-तोल, अस्, m. the bird Cātaka.<BR>—घन-त्व, अम्, n. or घन-ता, f. compactness,<BR>firmness; thickness, coarseness, solidity.<BR>—घन-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of a plant; [cf. वि-कण्टक.]<BR>—घन-धातु, उस्, m. lymph.<BR>—घन-ध्वनि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, roaring, who or what makes a roaring; (इस्),<BR>m. a deep and low tone, a roar; the muttering of<BR>thunder clouds.<BR>—घन-नाभि, इस्, m. smoke<BR>(being supposed to be a principal ingredient in<BR>clouds).<BR>—घन-नीहार, अस्, m. thick hoar-frost or<BR>mist.<BR>—घन-पत्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a plant, =<BR>पुनर्-नवा.<BR>—घन-पद, अम्, n. the cube root.<BR>—घन-पदवी, f. the path of the clouds, the<BR>sky.<BR>—घन-पयोधर, अस्, m. a firm breast.<BR>—घन-पल्लव, अस्, m. the plant Guilandina<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-a" target="_blank">Page0307-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Moringa; [cf. शोभाञ्जन.]<BR>—घन-पाषण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. a peacock, (this bird being supposed to de-<BR>light in cloudy and rainy weather.)<BR>—घन-फल,<BR>अम्, n. (in geom.) the solid or cubical contents of a<BR>body or of an excavation compared to a cube;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a plant; [cf. वि-कण्टक.]<BR>—घन-<BR>मल, अम्, n. deep (thunder) and sin.<BR>—घन-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. (in arithm.) cube root; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a plant; [cf. मोरट.]<BR>—घन-रव, अस्, m. the<BR>roaring of clouds, thunder.<BR>—घन-रस, अस्, m.<BR>a thick juice; extract, decoction; camphor; N. of<BR>two plants, = मोरट and पीलु-पर्णी; (अस् or अम्),<BR>m. n. the fluid of the clouds, water.<BR>—घन-रुच्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, shining like a cloud (with lightning), cloud-<BR>like.<BR>—घन-रुचिर-कलाप, अस्, m. (a peacock)<BR>having a tail glistening like a cloud.<BR>—घन-वर,<BR>अम्, n. the face; [cf. घनोत्तम.]<BR>—घन-वर्ग,<BR>अस्, m. the square of a cube; the sixth power.<BR>—घन-<BR>वर्त्मन्, अ, n. the path of the clouds, the sky, air.<BR>—घन-रल्लिका, f. lightning; (the creeper of the<BR>clouds.)<BR>—घन-वल्ली, f. lightning; N. of a plant,<BR>= अमृत-सवा.<BR>—घन-वात, अस्, m. a thick op-<BR>pressive atmosphere or air (constituting a kind of hell);<BR>one of the regions of hell (?).<BR>—घन-वास, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of pumpkin-gourd; [cf. कुष्माण्ड.]<BR>—घन-<BR>वाहन, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva, and also of Indra<BR>(who rides on the clouds).<BR>—घन-वीथि, इस्, f. the<BR>path of the clouds, the air; a line of clouds.<BR>—घन-<BR>व्यपाय, अस्, m. the disappearance of the clouds;<BR>autumn.<BR>—घन-व्यूह, अस्, m., N. of a Sūtra work.<BR>—घन-शब्द, अस्, m. the noise of clouds, thun-<BR>der.<BR>—घन-श्याम, अस्, आ, अम्, deep black, dark<BR>(as heavy clouds); (अस्), m. an epithet of Rāma,<BR>and also of Kṛṣṇa; N. of a copyist of the last<BR>century, with the epithet Tripāṭhin.<BR>—घन-सं-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. profound secrecy.<BR>—घन-समय, अस्,<BR>m. the rainy season.<BR>—घन-सार, अस्, m. camphor;<BR>mercury, or some peculiar form of it (?); water; a<BR>kind of tree.<BR>—घन-स्कन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant; [cf. कोशाम्र.]<BR>—घन-स्वन, अस्, m. low<BR>thunder, the muttering of clouds; the plant Ama-<BR>ranthus Polygamus.<BR>—घन-हस्त-सङ्ख्या, f. (in<BR>geom.) the contents of an excavation; or of a solid<BR>alike in figure.<BR>—घनाकर (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>rainy season.<BR>—घनागम (˚न-आग्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>approach of the clouds, the rainy season.<BR>—घना-<BR>घन, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of slaughter, easily striking<BR>down, fond of strife, mischievous, cruel; even, uni-<BR>form, without spaces or interstices, compact; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Indra; a vicious elephant, or one<BR>in rut; a thick or rainy cloud; mutual collision or<BR>contact; (आ), f. Solanum Indicum; [cf. काक-माची.]<BR>—घनाज्ञान (˚न-अज्˚), अम्, n. gross ignorance.<BR>—घनाञ्जनी (˚न-अञ्ज्˚), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—घनात्यय (˚न-अत्य्˚), अस्, m. the disappearance<BR>or departure of the clouds, the season succeeding<BR>the rains, autumn.<BR>—घनान्त (˚न-अन्त), अस्, m.<BR>the end of the rains, autumn.<BR>—घनामय (˚न-<BR>आम्˚), अस्, m. the date tree, Phœnix Sylvestris; [cf.<BR>खर्जूर.]<BR>—घनामल (˚न-अम्˚), अस्, m. a kind<BR>of pot-herb, Chenopodium Album; [cf. वास्तूक.]<BR>—घनाम्बु (˚न-अम्˚), n. rain.<BR>—घनारुण<BR>(˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deep red.<BR>—घनारुद्ध<BR>(˚न-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, overspread with clouds.<BR>—घ-<BR>नावरुद्ध (˚न-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘the abode<BR>of clouds, overspread with clouds.<BR>—घनाश्रय<BR>(˚न-आश्˚), अस्, m. ether, the atmosphere, the heavens,<BR>the firmament.<BR>—घनोत्तम (˚न-उत्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>face (the best part of the घन or body); [cf.<BR>घन-वर.]<BR>—घनोद (˚न-उद), अस्, m. a par-<BR>ticular sea having thick or viscid water; [cf. घन-<BR>तोय.]<BR>—घनोदधि (˚न-उद्˚), इस्, m. the viscid<BR>sea (constituting a kind of hell); a division of hell (?).<BR>—घनोपरद्ध (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, clouded,<BR>overcast.<BR>—घनोपल (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, m. hail; [cf.<BR>घन-कफ.]<BR>—घनौघ (˚न-ओघ), अस्, m.<BR>a gathering of clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनीकृ
घनी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to harden,<BR>thicken, solidify, congeal.<BR>—घनी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>hardened, compacted, made solid or firm; congealed,<BR>thickened, condensed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनीभाव
घनी-भाव, अस्, m. the becoming hardened,<BR>compact or thick, thickening.<BR>—घनी-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, become thick, thickened, condensed, thick,<BR>congealed, inspissated, compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनीय
घनीय, nom. P. घनीयति, -यितुम्, to long for<BR>solid food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घम्ब्|घंब्
घम्ब् घम्ब्, cl. 1. A. घम्बते, &c., to<BR>move, go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्
घर् घर्, cl. 10. P. घारयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घरट्ट|घरट्टः
घरट्ट घरट्ट, अस्, m. a grindstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घट|घर्घटः
घर्घट घर्घट, अस्, m. a kind of fish,<BR>Pimelodus Gagora or Tengara; [cf. गर्गर, गर्-<BR>गरक, गर्गाट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घर|घर्घरः
घर्घर घर्घर, अस्, आ, अम् (an onomato-<BR>poetic word implying an indistinct sound, especially<BR>in the throat), uttered with an indistinct gurgling or<BR>purring sound; (अस्), m. an indistinct murmur, a<BR>low murmuring or gurgling sound, the crackling of fire,<BR>rattling of a carriage, creaking, &c.; laughter, mirth; an<BR>owl; a fire of straw or chaff; a door, gate; a sliding<BR>or folding door or curtain (?); the pass of a moun-<BR>tain (?); the N. of a river, the Gogra or Ghogra;<BR>(आ), f. a bell hanging on the neck of a horse; (आ, ई),<BR>f. a bell used as an ornament; a girdle of small bells<BR>or tinkling ornaments worn by women; a kind of<BR>lute; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. one of the tones or notes<BR>in music.<BR>—घर्घरा-रव, अस्, m. a tinkling<BR>sound, the sound of small bells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घरक|घर्घरकः
घर्घरक, अस्, m., N. of a river, = घर्-<BR>घर; (इका), f. bells used as an ornament; a short<BR>stick for striking several kinds of musical instruments;<BR>a kind of musical instrument; fried grain; N. of a<BR>river; an ornament of small bells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घरित|घर्घरितं
घर्घरित, अम्, n. the grunting of a pig &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घुर्घा
घर्घुर्घा घर्घुर्घा, f. a sort of insect<BR>found in wood, = यम-कीट; [cf. घुर्घुर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ब्
घर्ब् घर्ब्, cl. 1. P. घर्बति, -बितुम्, to<BR>move, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म|घर्मः|घर्म्म|घर्म्मः
घर्म घर्म, अस्, m. (fr. rt. घृ or घृण्),<BR>heat, warmth (of the sun as well as of fire), sunshine;<BR>the hot season, internal heat; sweat, perspiration; a<BR>cauldron, a boiler, saucepan, &c., especially the vessel<BR>in which the milk-offering to the Aśvins is boiled;<BR>a cavity in the earth shaped like a cauldron or boiler,<BR>an excavation; a crater; hot milk or any other hot<BR>beverage offered as an oblation, especially to the<BR>Aśvins; N. of a son of Anu and father of Ghṛta;<BR>घर्म-तनू, du., N. of a Sāman; [cf. Gr. θέρμη;<BR>Zend garĕma; Goth. varmja; Germ. warm.]<BR>—घर्म-चर्चिका, f. eruptions caused by heat and<BR>suppressed perspiration.<BR>—घर्म-च्छेद, अस्, m.<BR>cessation of the heat.<BR>—घर्म-तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>perspiring.<BR>—घर्म-दीधिति, इस्, m. ‘having warm<BR>rays,’ the sun; [cf. शीतांशु.]<BR>—घर्म-दुघ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, or घर्म-दुह्, -धुक्, क्, क्, Ved. giving<BR>warm milk or the substance used for the offering.<BR>—घर्म-द्युति, इस्, m. ‘having warm radiance,’<BR>the sun.<BR>—घर्म-पयस्, अस्, n. perspiration; warm<BR>water.<BR>—घर्म-पावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. drinking<BR>hot milk.<BR>—घर्म-मास, अस्, m. a month of the<BR>hot season.<BR>—घर्म-रश्मि, इस्, m. the sun; heat,<BR>radiance; [cf. घर्म-दीधिति.]<BR>—घर्म-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of heat, an epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—घर्म-विचर्चिका, f. cutaneous eruptions<BR>or pimples from heat and suppressed perspiration; [cf.<BR>घर्म-चर्चिका.]<BR>—घर्म-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sitting<BR>near the fire or living in the heat (of the sky), an<BR>epithet of the manes.<BR>—घर्म-स्तुभ्, प्, प्, प्, Ved.<BR>assuaging the heat, an epithet of the Maruts.<BR>—घर्-<BR>म-स्वरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. breathing out heat;<BR>(Sāy.) sounding high or shrill (= दीप्त-ध्वनि).<BR>—घर्म-स्वेद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. perspiring with<BR>heat, or one whose sweat is milk; (Sāy.) coming<BR>with splendor or showering down water or coming<BR>to the oblation.<BR>—घर्मांश (˚म-अंशु), उस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">Page0307-c+ 77</a>]<BR>the sun; [cf. घर्म-दीधिति.]<BR>—घर्मून्त (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of the hot season, the beginning<BR>of the rainy season.<BR>—घर्मान्त-कामुकी, f. a<BR>small white bird, a kind of crane; [cf. रलाका.]<BR>—घर्माम्बु (˚म-अम्˚), n. sweat, perspiration.<BR>—घर्माम्भस् (˚म-अम्˚), अस्, n. perspiration.<BR>—घर्मार्त (˚म-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suffering<BR>from heat.<BR>—घर्मोदक (˚म-उद्˚), अम्, n. warm<BR>water, perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्मिन्
घर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. one who has prepared the<BR>Gharma offering, engaged in preparing the Gharma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्य
घर्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the Gharma<BR>or milk-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ष|घर्षः
घर्ष घर्ष, घर्षण, &c. See under<BR>rt. घृष्, p. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्
घस् घस् (according to Pāṇini II. 4, 37,<BR>a defective verb only used to supply certain<BR>tenses of अद्, such as the Aor. and Desid.), cl. 2. and<BR>1. P. घस्ति and घसति: Impf. 2nd sing. अघस् or<BR>अघत्; 2nd pl. अघस्त: Perf. जघस, जघसिथ,<BR>जघास; 3rd pl. जक्षुस् (Part. Perf. जक्षिवस्,<BR>fem. जक्षुषी); अघसत्, घत्स्यति, घस्तुम्, to<BR>consume, devour, eat: Desid. जिघत्सति, to wish to<BR>consume or devour, wish to eat; [cf. rt. जक्ष् and<BR>ग्रस्; cf. also Gr. γαστήρ; Lat. gustus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस|घसः
घस, अस्, m. the eater or devourer; N. of a<BR>kind of demon; also of a Rākṣasa; [cf. महा-घस<BR>and प्र-घस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घसि|घसिः
घसि, इस्, m., Ved. food, victuals; [cf. घासि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्मर|घस्मरः
घस्मर, अस्, आ, अम्, voracious, gluttonous;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a deer (or a Brāhman changed into<BR>a deer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्र|घस्रं|घस्रः
घस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, hurtful, injurious, mischievous,<BR>= हिंस्र; (अस्), m. a day [cf. घ्रंस]; (अम्), n.<BR>saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घास|घासः
घास, अस्, m. food, meadow or pasture grass;<BR>[cf. अश्व-घास and पूति-घास.]<BR>—घास-कूट,<BR>अम्, n. a hay-rick.<BR>—घास-स्थान, अम्, n. pasture,<BR>pasturage, food.<BR>—घासे-अज्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. im-<BR>pelling to consume, i. e. inviting or exciting appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घासक
घासक, (at the end of an adj. comp.) food, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घासि|घासिः
घासि, इस्, m. fire or its deity (the all-consuming).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाट|घाटः
घाट घाट, अस्, आ, m. f. the nape or back<BR>of the neck, the cervical ligament; (अस्), m. a pitcher,<BR>a pot (? for घट); [cf. कर-घाट.]<BR>—घाट-<BR>कर्करी, f. a kind of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाटरी
घाटरी, f. a kind of lute; [cf. घटरिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाटिक
घाटिक, अस्, m. = घाण्टिक; (आ), f. the nape or<BR>back of the neck; also incorrectly used for घ-<BR>टिका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाटाल
घाटाल घाटाल, अस्, आ, अम् (a wrong form<BR>for घण्टाल), bell-shaped (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाण्टिक|घांटिक|घांटिकः|घाण्टिकः
घाण्टिक घाण्टिक. See under घण्टा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात|घातः
घात घात, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हन्), killing;<BR>(अस्), m. a blow, a bruise, slaying killing, murdering,<BR>slaughter; striking, wounding, hurting, destruction;<BR>an arrow; the product (of a sum in multiplication);<BR>[cf. कर्म-घात and ग्राम-घात.]<BR>—घात-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, murderous, destructive.<BR>—घात-<BR>चन्द्र, अस्, m. the moon when in an inauspicious<BR>mansion.<BR>—घात-तिथि, इस्, f. an inauspicious lunar<BR>day.<BR>—घात-नक्षत्र, अम्, n. an inauspicious<BR>Nakṣatra.<BR>—घात-वार, अस्, m. an inauspicious day<BR>of the week.<BR>—घात-स्थान, अम्, n. a slaughter-<BR>house, a place of execution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातक|घातकः
घातक, अस्, ई, अम्, killing, a killer, a murderer;<BR>destroying, a destroyer (used at the end of comp.;<BR>cf. विश्वास-घातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातन|घातनं|घातनः
घातन or घतन, अस्, आ, अम्, killing, a mur-<BR>derer, a killer; (अस्), m., N. of certain inhabitants of<BR>hell; (ई), f. a kind of club; (अम्), n. striking, slaying,<BR>killing, slaughter, immolating.<BR>—घातन-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. a place of slaughter, a slaughter-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातयत्
घातयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, striking, hurting, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातव्य
घातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be killed, what may or<BR>ought to be killed &c., deserving death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाति|घातिः
घाति, इस्, m. striking, killing in general; catching<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">Page0308-a+ 72</a>]<BR>or killing birds, fowling [cf. नि-घाति, घाति-पक्षिन्,<BR>घाति-विहग]; (इस्), f. a bird-net.<BR>—घाति-पक्षिन्,<BR>ई, m. or घाति-विहग, अस्, m. a hawk or falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातिन्
घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, killing, murderous, who or what<BR>strikes or kills, a murderer; destroying, destructive,<BR>felonious; [cf. अन्धक-घातिन्, अमित्र-घ्˚, अर्ध-<BR>क-घ्˚, कुमार-घ्˚, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातुक|घातुकः
घातुक, अस्, ई, अम्, killing, tearing asunder,<BR>hurting, hurtful, mischievous; cruel, savage, violent,<BR>ferocious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात्य|घात्यं
घात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be killed, proper or fit to<BR>be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार|घारः
घार घार. See under rt. घृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार्तिक|घार्तिकः|घार्त्तिक|घार्त्तिकः
घार्तिक घार्तिक, अस्, m. (fr. घृत), pulse<BR>ground and fried with clarified butter, a cake pre-<BR>pared with Ghṛta or clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार्तेय|घार्त्तेय
घार्तेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe; (अस्),<BR>m. the prince of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घास|घासः
घास घास. See under rt. घस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घिण्ण्
घिण्ण् घिण्ण्, cl. 1. A. घिण्णते, जिघिण्णे,<BR>घिण्णितुम्, to take, grasp; [cf. घुण्ण्<BR>and घृण्ण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घु|घुः
घु 1. घु, cl. 1. A. घवते, &c., to utter<BR>a peculiar sound, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घु|घुः
2. घु, उस्, m. a kind of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुंष्
घुंष् घुंष्, cl. 1. A. घुंषते, &c., to<BR>diffuse lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुट्
घुट् घुट्, cl. 6. P. घुटति, जुघोट, घु-<BR>टितुम्, to strike again or retaliate, to resist,<BR>oppose; to protect, preserve; cl. 1. A. घोटते, जुघुटे,<BR>घोटिष्यते, अघुटत् and अघोटिष्ट, घोटितुम्, to<BR>come back, to return; to barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुट|घुटः
घुट, अस्, m. or घुटि, इस्, f. or घुटी, f. the ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुटिक|घुटिकः
घुटिक, अस्, आ, m. f. the ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ट|घुंट|घुंटः|घुण्टः
घुण्ट, अस्, m. or घुण्टक, अस्, m. or घुण्टिका,<BR>f. the ancle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुड्
घुड् घुड्, cl. 6. P. घुडति, &c., to pre-<BR>vent, defend, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्
घुण् घुण् (related to घूर्ण्; cf. घोल्),<BR>cl. 1. A. घोणते, जुघुणे, घोणितुम्,<BR>&c., or cl. 6. P. घुणति, जुघोण, &c., to move to and<BR>fro, stagger, shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण|घुणः
घुण, अस्, m. a peculiar kind of insect found<BR>in timber; the pangolin or armadillo.<BR>—घुण-<BR>कीटक, अस्, m. = the preceding.<BR>—घुण-वल्लभा,<BR>f., N. of a plant; [cf. अति-विषा.]<BR>—घुणाक्षर<BR>(˚ण-अक्˚), अम्, n. an incision in wood or in the leaf<BR>of a book caused by an insect or book-worm and<BR>resembling somewhat the form of a letter.<BR>—घुणा-<BR>क्षर-न्यायेन, ind. in a fortuitous and unexpected<BR>manner, by a happy chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुणि
घुणि, इस्, इस्, इ, worm-eaten (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ड|घुंड|घुंडः|घुण्डः
घुण्ड, अस्, m. a large black bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्टिक|घुंटिकं|घुण्टिकं
घुण्टिक घुण्टिक, अम्, n. cow-dung found<BR>in thickets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ण्
घुण्ण् घुण्ण्, cl. 1. A. घुण्णते, जुघुण्णे,<BR>घुण्णितुम्, to seize; [cf. घिण्ण् and<BR>घृण्ण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर्
घुर् घुर्, cl. 6. P. घुरति, &c., to frighten<BR>with cries, to cry out through fear, utter<BR>cries of distress; to be frightful or terrible; to<BR>sound; [cf. घोर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुरण|घुरणः
घुरण, अस्, m. sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुरघुराय
घुरघुराय घुरघुराय, nom. A. -घुरा-<BR>यते, to utter gurgling sounds, to wheeze, snort or<BR>grunt like a hog; [cf. घर्घर and the next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर्घुर|घुर्घुरः
घुर्घुर घुर्घुर, अस्, m. (an onomatopoetic<BR>word), a kind of worm, burrowing in the skin,<BR>guinea-worm, Dracunculus; (ई), f. the mole-cricket<BR>[cf. मृत्-किरा]; (आ), f. growling, as of a dog or cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर्घुरक|घुर्घुरकः
घुर्घुरक, अस्, m. or (इका), f. a gurgling or<BR>murmuring sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर्घुराय
घुर्घुराय, nom. A. घुर्घुरायते, to whis-<BR>tle, murmur, hum, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुलघुलारव|घुलघुलारवः
घुलघुलारव घुलघुला-रव, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुलञ्च|घुलञ्चः
घुलञ्च घुलञ्च, अस्, m. Coix Barbata; [cf.<BR>गवेधुका. ]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्
घुष् 1. घुष्, cl. 1. P. घोषति, जुघोष,<BR>घोषिष्यति, अघोषीत् and अघुषत्,<BR>घोषितुम्, to sound, make any sound or noise;<BR>to cry or proclaim aloud, call out, announce publicly,<BR>declare; to fill with cries; (according to some) to kill:<BR>Caus. घोषयति, -यितुम्, अजूघुषत्, to proclaim<BR>aloud, call to, invite; to cause to proclaim aloud;<BR>to praise: Desid. जुघुषिषति or जुघोषिषति:<BR>Intens. जोघुष्यते, जोघोष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष
घुष, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुषित|घुषितं
घुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, declared, proclaimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्ट|घुष्टं
घुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, proclaimed.<BR>—घु-<BR>ष्टान्न (˚ट-अन्न), अम्, n. food given away by<BR>proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्ट्र|घुष्ट्रं
घुष्ट्र, अम्, n. a cart, a carriage; (fr. घुष्,<BR>in the sense ‘to creak ?’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्य
घुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, giving out sounds; to be<BR>proclaimed aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोष|घोषं|घोषः
घोष, अस्, m. indistinct noise, tumult; the con-<BR>fused cries of a multitude, battle-cry, cries of victory,<BR>cries of woe or distress, any cry or sound; an exclama-<BR>tion, the roar of animals; the sound of a drum or<BR>of a conch-shell, of the Soma stones, of a carriage,<BR>&c.; the whizzing or whir of a bow-string, crackling<BR>of fire, singing in the ear; roaring of a storm, of<BR>thunder, of water, &c.; the sound of the recital<BR>of prayers; rumour, report; a proclamation; (in<BR>grammar) the soft sound or low murmur heard in the<BR>articulation of the soft or sonant consonants ग्, घ्,<BR>ज्, झ्, ड्, ढ्, द्, ध्, ब्, भ्, ङ्, ञ्, ण्, न्, म्, ह्, य्, र्, ल्, व्,<BR>the vowels, and Anusvāra, which with the Yamas of<BR>the first ten of the soft consonants make up altogether<BR>forty sounds, (the absence of this soft sound or murmur<BR>being called अ-घोष, q. v., and applied to क्, ख्,<BR>च्, छ्, ट्, ठ्, त्, थ्, प्, फ्, the sibilants, Visarga, the<BR>Jihvā-mūlīya, and the Upadhmānīya, which with<BR>the Yamas of the first ten consonants make up<BR>twenty-six sounds); a vowel; a station of herdsmen;<BR>a herdsman; a gnat, a musquito; a creeping plant<BR>bearing white or yellow flowers, Luffa Fœtida or a<BR>similar plant [cf. घोषक]; brass, bell-metal,<BR>tutenag, &c.; N. of a man; an epithet of Śiva;<BR>a son of Lambā, daughter of Dakṣa, and wife of<BR>Dharma; N. of an Arhat; N. of a prince of the<BR>Kāṇva dynasty (for घोष-वसु); a common N.<BR>for a Kāyastha or one of the writer-caste, &c.; N.<BR>of a country; a station of herdsmen in general; (ई), f.<BR>a kind of fennel, Anethum Sowa, another plant = कर्-<BR>कट-शृङ्गी; N. of a woman, said to be a daughter<BR>of Kakṣīvat; [cf. आत्म-घोष, इन्द्र-घ्˚, उच्चैर्-<BR>घ्˚, ज्या-घ्˚, पद्-घ्˚, मधु-घ्˚, महा-घ्˚.]<BR>—घोष-कृत्, त्, m. a person making a noise.<BR>—घोष-कोटि, इस्, f., N. of the peak of a mountain.<BR>—घोष-बुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. made attentive<BR>by the sound.<BR>—घोष-मति, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—घोष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, sounding, making a<BR>noise; (in grammar) sonant, uttered with the soft arti-<BR>culation, see above; (वान्), m., N. of a man; (वती),<BR>f. a lute (वीणा); a peculiar kind of lute or N. of<BR>a lute.<BR>—घोष-वर्ण, अस्, m. a sonant letter.<BR>—घोष-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a prince of the<BR>Kāṇva dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषक|घोषकः
घोषक, अस्, m. a crier, a proclaimer (e. g. in<BR>पटह-घ्˚, q. v.); the creeping plant Luffa Fœtida<BR>or a similar plant.<BR>—घोषकाकृति (˚क-आक्˚), इस्,<BR>m. a plant with white blossoms, similar to the Gho-<BR>shaka, and perhaps a species of it, commonly called<BR>Hātīghoṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषण|घोषणं
घोषण, अस्, आ, अम्, sounding; (अम्, आ), n. f.<BR>speaking loud, making a great noise; crying, pro-<BR>claiming aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषणीय
घोषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be proclaimed aloud,<BR>to be publicly announced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषयित्नु|घोषयित्नुः
घोषयित्नु, उस्, m. a crier, a proclaimer, a<BR>herald; a Brāhman; the Koïl or Indian cuckoo; a<BR>captive (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषि
घोषि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (according to Sāy.) either<BR>‘accompanied with noise,’ or ‘to be proclaimed<BR>aloud;’ but घोषि might also be considered as the<BR>3rd pers. sing. of the Aor. Pass. fr. rt. घुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषिन्
घोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, sounding, noisy; (in grammar)<BR>having the soft sound or articulation, sonant, (opposed<BR>to अ-घोष); [cf. ग्राम-घोषिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्
घुष् 2. घुष् = घृष्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुसृण|घुसृणं
घुसृण घुसृण, अम्, n. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूक|घूकः
घूक घूक, अस्, m. an owl.<BR>—घूकारि (˚क-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. a crow (enemy of the owl).<BR>—घूकावास<BR>(˚क-आव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a tree; [cf. शाखोट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्
घूर् घूर्, cl. 4. A. घूर्यते, &c., to kill,<BR>hurt, or injure; to become old, to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण्
घूर्ण् घूर्ण्, cl. 6. P. or 1. A. घूर्णति or<BR>घूर्णते, &c., to move to and fro, to shake,<BR>to be agitated, to tremble, roll about, cause to whirl,<BR>whirl, turn round: Caus. P. घूर्णयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to move to and fro or shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण|घूर्णः|घूर्ण्ण
घूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, moving to and fro;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of pot-herb, Chironia Centauroides;<BR>turning round, whirling, rolling, &c.<BR>—घूर्ण-<BR>वायु, उस्, m. a whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णन|घूर्णनं|घूर्ण्णन
घूर्णन, अम्, आ, n. f. shaking, revolving, whirl-<BR>ing, turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णमान
घूर्णमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being agitated, shaking,<BR>trembling, revolving, turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णायमान|घूर्णायमानः|घूर्ण्णायमान
घूर्णायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, whirling, revolving,<BR>rolling, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णि|घूर्णिः|घूर्ण्णि
घूर्णि, इस्, f. rolling, revolving, going round or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णिका|घूर्ण्णिका
घूर्णिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णित|घूर्णितः|घूर्ण्णित
घूर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, rolling, turning, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण्यमान|घूर्ण्यमानः
घूर्ण्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being agitated, set in<BR>motion, made to go round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृ
घृ घृ, cl. 1. 3. 10. P. घरति, जिघर्ति,<BR>घारयति, जघार, घरिष्यति, अघार्-<BR>षीत्, घर्तुम्, &c., to sprinkle, besprinkle, sprinkle<BR>over; to wet or moisten; to distil; cl. 3. P., 5. P. A.<BR>जिघस्ति, घृणोति, -णुते, or घर्णोति, -णुते, to<BR>shine; to burn; [cf. घृण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार|घारः
घार, अस्, m. sprinkling, besprinkling, wetting;<BR>(ई), f. a kind of metre consisting of four lines of four<BR>syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृत|घृतः
घृत, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled; illumined; (अम्),<BR>n. clarified butter or butter which has been boiled<BR>gently and allowed to cool; it is then used for culinary<BR>and religious purposes and is highly esteemed by the<BR>Hindūs; it is now commonly called Ghee (घि or<BR>घी); butter, fat, fat as an emblem of fertility,<BR>especially fluid grease; cream; rain or rather fertil-<BR>izing rain, considered as the fat which drops from<BR>heaven, water; (आ), f. a kind of tree [cf. घृत-<BR>मण्डा]; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Dharma, grand-<BR>son of Anu and father of Duduha.<BR>—घृत-करञ्ज,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of Karañja, = घृत-पर्णक, तप-<BR>स्विन्, प्र-कीर्य, वि-रोचन, विषारि.<BR>—घृत-कु-<BR>मारी or घृत-कुमारिका, f. the plant Aloe Indica,<BR>(this plant being supposed to resemble a virgin in<BR>delicacy and elegance.)<BR>—घृत-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a<BR>jar of ghee.<BR>—घृत-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one<BR>whose locks are unctuous, dropping with butter.<BR>—घृत-कौशिक, अस्, m., N. of a religious teacher.<BR>—घृत-च्युता, f., N. of a river; [cf. घृत-श्चुत्.]<BR>—घृत-दीधिति, इस्, m. fire, the deity of fire (as<BR>receiving the clarified butter offered in sacrifice);<BR>another reading has धृत-दीधिति.<BR>—घृत-दुह्,<BR>धुक्, क्, क्, Ved. giving butter or cream.<BR>—घृत-<BR>धारा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—घृत-निर्णिज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>Ved. having a garment of fat, covered with fat; (Sāy.)<BR>shining with butter mixed (with the Soma).<BR>—घृत-<BR>प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking Ghṛta, epithet of a class of<BR>Ṛṣis.<BR>—घृत-पदी, adj. f., Ved. (according to the<BR>Brāhmaṇas) one whose path is Ghṛta; or, perhaps,<BR>one whose foot (पाद्) drops with Ghṛta, an epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-a" target="_blank">Page0309-a+ 81</a>]<BR>of Iḷā.<BR>—घृत-पर्णक, अस्, m. = घृत-करञ्ज;<BR>[cf. घृत-पूर्णक.]<BR>—घृत-पशु, उस्, m. ghee<BR>or clarified butter made into or supposed to resemble<BR>an animal to be offered at a sacrifice, a sacrificial<BR>victim represented by ghee.<BR>—घृत-पावन्, आ, अरी,<BR>अ, Ved. drinking butter &c.<BR>—घृत-पीत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, = पीत-घृत, one who has drunk butter &c.<BR>—घृत-पू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. clarifying butter &c.<BR>—घृत-पूर, अस्, m. a sweetmeat composed of<BR>flour, milk, cocoa-nut, and ghee, &c.<BR>—घृत-<BR>पूर्णक, अस्, m. a sweetmeat composed of flour,<BR>milk, cocoa-nut, and ghee, &c.; the tree Pongamia<BR>Glabra; [cf. करञ्ज; cf. also घृत-पर्णक.]<BR>—घृत-पृच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. sprinkling unctuous or<BR>fertilizing fluid; (Sāy.) accompanied with fertilizing<BR>fluid.<BR>—घृत-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one whose<BR>back or surface consists of Ghṛta; especially an epi-<BR>thet of Agni or his horses; (Sāy.) having a brilliant<BR>form or shining body; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Pri-<BR>ya-vrata by Barhiṣmatī, and sovereign of Krauñca-<BR>dvīpa, also a N. of fire.<BR>—घृत-प्रतीक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. one whose form is brilliant with Ghṛta;<BR>an epithet of Agni and of Uṣas.<BR>—घृत-प्रयस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. relishing Ghṛta; (Sāy.) receiving<BR>oblations of food mixed with Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-प्र-<BR>सत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. propitiated with Ghṛta;<BR>epithet of Agni.<BR>—घृत-प्राश, अस्, m. swallowing<BR>ghee.<BR>—घृत-प्राशन, अम्, n. tasting or swallow-<BR>ing ghee.<BR>—घृत-प्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. satisfied with<BR>butter, an epithet of Agni.<BR>—घृत-प्रुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved.<BR>sprinkling fat &c., filling with Ghṛta, i. e. spreading<BR>welfare and gifts.<BR>—घृत-प्लत, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled<BR>or smeared with ghee.<BR>—घृत-भृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>baked or stewed in grease.<BR>—घृत-मण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. the scum of melted butter, the fattiest part of<BR>grease; (आ), f. a kind of medicinal plant (the scum<BR>of its infusion resembling ghee); [cf. काकली.]<BR>—घृत-मण्डलिका, f., N. of a plant, = हंस-<BR>पदी.<BR>—घृतमण्डोद (˚ड-उद), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a lake on the mountain Mandara.<BR>—घृत-योनि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. an epithet of Agni, abiding or living in<BR>Ghṛta &c.; producing fertilizing rain or welfare and<BR>happiness generally; (Sāy.) whose source is Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-रौढीय, आस्, m. pl. the Rauḍhīyas who<BR>are desirous of Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-लेखनी, f. a ladle<BR>for ghee.<BR>—घृत-लोलीकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed with<BR>ghee, steeped in it.<BR>—घृत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>greasy, abounding in fat; mixed or smeared with<BR>butter; an epithet, especially of Agni and Soma;<BR>containing the word Ghṛta (as a verse); (वत्), ind.<BR>like clarified butter.<BR>—घृत-वर, अस्, m. a sweet-<BR>meat, or flour &c. baked with ghee and sugar.<BR>—घृत-वर्तनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. whose tracks are in<BR>Ghṛta or sprinkle Ghṛta, an epithet of the chariot<BR>of the Aśvins.<BR>—घृत-वर्ति, इस्, f. a wick fed with<BR>grease.<BR>—घृत-विक्रयिन्, ई, m. a vender of ghee.<BR>—घृत-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. delighted with<BR>Ghṛta, nourished with it; an epithet of Agni.<BR>—घृत-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, living only upon Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-श्चुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sprinkling ghee.<BR>—घृत-<BR>श्चुन्-निधन, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—घृत-<BR>श्च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. distilling ghee.<BR>—घृतश्च्युन्-नि-<BR>धन, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—घृत-श्री, ईस्,<BR>ईस्, इ, Ved. mixed with Ghṛta, mixing ghee; (Sāy.)<BR>having recourse to Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-सद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. abiding in Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-स्थला, f., N. of<BR>an Apsaras; [cf. ऋत-स्थला and क्रतु-स्थला.]<BR>—घृत-स्ना, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. dropping fat.<BR>—घृत-<BR>स्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. bathed in Ghṛta, sprinkling it;<BR>epithet of Mitrā-Varuṇa, and of heaven and earth;<BR>one whose surface consists of Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-स्पृश्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, who or what touches Ghṛta.<BR>—घृत-ह्रद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (a lake) consisting of Ghṛta.<BR>—घृताक्त (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, anointed with<BR>clarified butter, smeared with Ghṛta.<BR>—घृताचि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a man, (derived fr. the following.)<BR>—घृताची (˚त + rt. अच्), adj. f. greasy, abounding<BR>in Ghṛta; filled with grease; sprinkling Ghṛta or<BR>fertilizing fluid, shining with it, (often with and<BR>without जुहा, f. or the sacrificial ladle with which<BR>the Ghṛta is taken up, poured out, &c.); an epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">Page0309-b+ 75</a>]<BR>of Sarasvatī &c.; (ई), f. the night (considered as moist<BR>and dewy); a kind of serpent (shining like grease);<BR>N. of an Apsaras, loved by Bharad-vāja, or Vyāsa, or<BR>Viśvā-mitra; wife of Pra-mati and mother of Ruru;<BR>(according to other authorities) the wife of Raudrāśva<BR>or Kuśa-nābha.<BR>—घृताची-गर्भ-सम्भवा, f.<BR>large cardamoms.<BR>—घृतान्न (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. eating grease.<BR>—घृताभ्यक्त (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, smeared with ghee.<BR>—घृतार्चिस् (˚त-अर्˚),<BR>इस्, m. flaring or blazing fire.<BR>—घृतावनि (˚त-<BR>अव्˚), इस्, f. the spot on the sacrificial post which<BR>is smeared with Ghṛta.<BR>—घृता-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>delighted with butter; (Sāy.) increasing the Ghṛta.<BR>—घृतासुति (˚त-आस्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. receiving the<BR>Ghṛta oblation, one whose food is Ghṛta; epithet of<BR>Mitrā-Varuṇa, Viṣṇu, Indrā-Viṣṇu.<BR>—घृताह-<BR>वन (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one to whom the<BR>Ghṛta oblation belongs; epithet of Agni.<BR>—घृता-<BR>हुत (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one to whom<BR>Ghṛta is offered.<BR>—घृताहुति (˚त-आह्˚), इस्, f.<BR>the Ghṛta oblation.<BR>—घृताह्व (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, m.<BR>and घृताह्वय (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, m. the resin of<BR>the tree Pinus Longifolia, turpentine.<BR>—घृतोद<BR>(˚त-उद), अस्, आ, अम्, having Ghṛta as water;<BR>(अस्), m. the sea of Ghṛta surrounding Kuśa-dvīpa.<BR>—घृतोदङ्क (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, m. a leather vessel<BR>for holding ghee.<BR>—घृतौदन (˚त-ओद्˚), अम्,<BR>n. rice sprinkled with Ghṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतिन्
घृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, containing Ghṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतेयु
घृतेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva [cf.<BR>घृताची]; according to other authorities कृतेयु<BR>or कृकणेयु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतेली
घृतेली, f. a cock-roach; [cf. तैलपायिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृत्य
घृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. consisting of Ghṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृङ्
घृङ् 1. घृङ्, ind. an onomatopoetic sound.<BR>—घृङ्-करिक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, bleating, making the<BR>cry of a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृण्
घृण् 2. घृण् (allied to rt. घृ), cl. 8. P.<BR>A. घर्णोति, -णुते, or घृणोति, -णुते,<BR>to shine, burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृण|घृणः
घृण, अस्, m. heat, ardour, sunshine; (आ), f. a<BR>warm feeling towards others, compassion, tenderness,<BR>pity; reproach, blame, censure, aversion, contempt;<BR>[cf. निर्-घृण and हृणीया.]<BR>—घृणार्चिस् (˚ण-<BR>अर्˚), इस्, m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणालु
घृणालु, उस्, उस्, उ, compassionate, pitiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणि|घृणिः
घृणि, इस्, m. heat, ardour, sunshine; a ray of<BR>the sun or moon, the sun; a wave, water; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>displeasing, disagreeable.<BR>—घृणी-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. burning, shining; (आन्), m. a kind of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणित
घृणित, अस्, आ, अम्, pitied; reproached, abused, hated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणिन्
घृणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, merciful, tender-hearted, com-<BR>passionate; censorious, abusive.<BR>—घृणि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. mercifulness, compassion, pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणावास|घृणावासः
घृणावास घृणावास, अस्, m. (probably for<BR>घन-वास), a kind of pumpkin-gourd; [cf. कुष्-<BR>माण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृण्ण्
घृण्ण् घृण्ण्, cl. 1. A. घृण्णते, to seize;<BR>[cf. घिण्ण् and घुण्ण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृत्सतमस्
घृत्सतमस् घृत्सतमस्, आस्, m., N. of a<BR>man (for गृत्स-तम ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृत्समद
घृत्समद घृत्समद, a wrong form for<BR>गृत्स-मद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्
घृष् 1. घृष् = हृष्, to be joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृषु
घृषु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. lively, agile, mirthful,<BR>sportive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्वि|घृष्विः
1. घृष्वि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. lively, gay, merry, spor-<BR>tive; (Sāy.) crushing, (as if fr. 2. घृष्.)<BR>—घृष्वि-<BR>राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. frolicsome with joy; (Sāy.)<BR>whose gifts touch each other or come closely together,<BR>(as if fr. 2. घृष्); epithet of the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्
घृष् 2. घृष्, cl. 1. P. घर्षति, जघर्-<BR>ष, घर्षिष्यति, घर्षितुम्, to rub,<BR>grind, brush, polish, furbish; crush, pound: Caus. P.<BR>घर्षयति, -यितुम्, to rub, grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ष|घर्षः
घर्ष, अस्, m. rubbing, grinding, friction, brushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षक|घर्षकः
घर्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbing; (अस्), m. a polisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षण|घर्षणं
घर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbing, rubbing so as<BR>to make sore; (अम्), n. the act of grinding or rub-<BR>bing, pounding, brushing, friction; (ई), f. turmeric.<BR>—घर्षणाल (˚ण-आल = आलय), अस्, m. a wooden<BR>roller or pestle for grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षणीय
घर्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be rubbed or cleaned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षित
घर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed, ground, brushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षिन्
घर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, grinding, rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्ट|घृष्टः
घृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed, ground, pounded;<BR>frayed, grazed, rubbed so as to be sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्टि|घृष्टिः
घृष्टि, इस्, m. a hog [cf. गृष्टि and 2. घृष्वि];<BR>(इस्), f. grinding, pounding; emulation, contest; N.<BR>of a plant, = वाराही, Lycopodium Imbricatum; N. of<BR>another plant, Clitorea Ternatea; [cf. विष्णु-क्रान्ता.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्वि|घृष्विः
2. घृष्वि, इस्, m. a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्ठिला
घृष्ठिला घृष्ठिला, f., N. of a plant re-<BR>lated to the plant Hemionitis Cordifolia; [cf. पृश्नि-<BR>पर्णी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घेञ्चुलिका
घेञ्चुलिका घेञ्चुलिका or घेञ्चुली, f., N. of<BR>an esculent root, Arum Oxicense, = क्रौञ्चादन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोङ्घ|घोंघः|घोङ्घः
घोङ्घ घोङ्घ, अस्, m. intermediate space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोट|घोटः
घोट घोट, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. घुट्),<BR>a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोटक|घोटकः
घोटक, अस्, m. a horse; (इका), f. a mare; the<BR>plant Cucumis Utilissimus (कर्कटी); [cf. तुरङ्गी.]<BR>—घोटक-मुख, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Kanyā-samprayuktakādhikaraṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोडाचोलिन्
घोडाचोलिन् घोडाचोलिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणस|घोणसः
घोणस घोणस, अस्, m. = गो-नस, a kind of<BR>serpent; (other authorities have घोनस.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणा
घोणा घोणा, f. (corrupted fr. घ्राणा ?),<BR>the nose; the nose or nostrils of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणिन्
घोणिन्, ई, m. a hog (as having a large snout).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोण्टा|घोंटा
घोण्टा घोण्टा, f. the jujube, Zizyphus<BR>Jujuba, = वदर, वदरी; the betel-nut tree, see<BR>गुवाक; a timber tree, Schrebera Sweietenoides.<BR>—घोण्टा-फल, अस्, m. a kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोनस|घोनसः
घोनस घोनस, अस्, m. a large kind of<BR>snake; [cf. घोणस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोर|घोरं|घोरः
घोर घोर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. हन्<BR>with substitution of घुर् for हन्), venerable, awful,<BR>sublime (in these senses Ved); terrific, frightful, terri-<BR>ble, horrible, dreadful, awful, violent, vehement; (अस्),<BR>m. the terrible, an epithet of Śiva; N. of an Āṅgi-<BR>rasa, a son of Aṅgiras; N. of Kutsa; (आ), f. the night;<BR>a kind of creeper, = देव-दाली; (scil. गति), N. of<BR>one of the seven stations of the planet Mercury;<BR>(अम्), n. venerableness; awfulness, horror; a horrible<BR>action, magic formulas and charms; poison; saffron;<BR>[cf. धीर and गौर.]<BR>—घोर-घुष्य, अम्, n.<BR>brass; (a various reading for घोर-पुष्प); [cf.<BR>घोष.]<BR>—घोर-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. of<BR>frightful appearance, having terrific eyes.<BR>—घोर-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more terrible, very awful.<BR>—घोर-<BR>ता, f. or घोर-त्व, अम्, n. horribleness, horror.<BR>—घोर-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, of horrible or fright-<BR>ful appearance, terrific; (अस्), m. an owl.<BR>—घोर-<BR>पुष्प, अम्, n. brass, bell-metal; [cf. घोर-<BR>घुष्य.]<BR>—घोर-रासन, अस्, m. a jackal; (a<BR>wrong reading for घोर-वाशन.)<BR>—घोर-रासिन्,<BR>ई, m. a jackal (? for घोर-वाशिन्).<BR>—घोर-रूप,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, frightful, hideous; (अम्), n. a hideous<BR>appearance.<BR>—घोर-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, frightful, hor-<BR>rible, hideous.<BR>—घोर-वर्पस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. of<BR>frightful or hideous appearance of shape; an epithet<BR>of the Maruts.<BR>—घोर-वाशन, अस्, m. or घोर-<BR>वाशिन्, ई, m. a jackal; [cf. घोर-रासन.]<BR>—घोर-<BR>सङ्काश, अस्, आ, अम्, dreadful, terrible.<BR>—घोर-<BR>स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, of dreadful sound.<BR>—घोराकृति<BR>(˚र-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, frightful, hideous, of terrible<BR>aspect or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरक
घोरक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घौर
घौर, अम्, n. horror, horribleness; (अस्), m. a<BR>patronymic from Ghora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोल्
घोल् घोल् (substituted in Prākṛt for<BR>घुण् = घूर्ण्), cl. 10. P. घोलयति,<BR>यितुम्, to mix, to stir together into a semi-fluid<BR>substance; Bengālī gholāïte.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोल|घोलं|घोलः
घोल, अम्, n. buttermilk; (ई), f. a kind of plant<BR>or vegetable; [cf. अरण्य-घोली, क्षुद्र-घ्˚,<BR>वन-घ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोलि
घोलि, इस्, and घोलिका, f. = घोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोष|घोषं|घोषः
घोष घोष. See under rt. 1. घुष्, p. 308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषातकी
घोषातकी घोषातकी, f., N. of a plant, =<BR>श्वेत-घोषा; [cf. हस्ति-घोषातकी and कोशातकी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घौर
घौर घौर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्न
घ्न घ्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. हन्, and used at<BR>the end of compounds to express) killing, striking,<BR>a killer, destructive, destroying, removing; see अर्थ-<BR>घ्न, ज्वर-घ्न, शत्रु-घ्न, गो-घ्न, दण्ड-<BR>घ्न; (also to express) multiplied by; see द्वि-<BR>चतुर्-घ्न. In a few compounds the fem. may<BR>end in आ [cf. कुल-घ्ना]; (अम्), n. killing, de-<BR>struction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्नत्|घ्नन्त्
घ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत् (pres. part.), striking, beating,<BR>hurting, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्नी
घ्नी = घ्न, m., in अहि-घ्नी and श्व-घ्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्न्य
घ्न्य, used in a few compounds, see अ-घ्न्य<BR>and अति-घ्न्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रंस्
घ्रंस् घ्रंस्, न्, m., Ved. the heat of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रंस|घ्रंसः
घ्रंस, अस्, m., Ved. the heat of the sun, sun-<BR>shine, brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रा
घ्रा घ्रा, cl. 1. P., ep. also cl. 1. A. and<BR>2. P. जिघ्रति, -ते, घ्राति, जघ्रौ, घ्रा-<BR>स्यति, अघ्रात् and अघ्रासीत्, घ्रातुम्, to smell,<BR>perceive odour, be eager for; to smell at, snuffle at;<BR>to kiss: Caus. P. घ्रापयति, अजिघ्रपत् and<BR>अजिघ्रिपत्, to cause to smell at: Desid. जिघ्रासति:<BR>Intens. जेघ्रीयते, जाघ्रेति and जाघ्राति; du.<BR>जाघ्रीतस्; [cf. Lat. fra-grare; Hib. gros, ‘a<BR>snout (?);’ Germ. riechen; Old Germ. riuhu; Lith.<BR>kwepju, kwapas; Gr. ἄρωμα; ῥίς, ῥιν-ος.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रति
घ्रति, इस्, f. the nose (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राण|घ्राणं|घ्राणः
घ्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, smelled; (अस् or अम्), m. n.<BR>smell; smelling; (अम्), n. odour; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n.<BR>the nose; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—घ्राण-चक्षुस्,<BR>उस्, उस्, उस्, using the nose for eyes, blind.<BR>—घ्राण-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, caused or effected by the nose.<BR>—घ्राण-तर्पण, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasant to the<BR>nose, fragrant; (अम्), n. fragrance, odour; a fra-<BR>grance, a perfume.<BR>—घ्राण-दुःख-दा, f., N. of<BR>a plant which causes sneezing (giving pain to the<BR>nose).<BR>—घ्राण-पाक, अस्, m. a disease of the nose,<BR>= नासा-पाक, q. v.<BR>—घ्राण-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of<BR>one of the attendants of Skanda (‘using the nose<BR>for ears’ [cf. घ्राण-चक्षुस्] or ‘renowned for<BR>his nose’).<BR>—घ्राणेन्द्रिय (˚ण-इन्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>organ or sense of smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात|घ्रातः
घ्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, smelled, smelled at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रातव्य
घ्रातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smelled or smelled<BR>at; (अम्), n. odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राति|घ्रातिः
घ्राति, इस्, f. smell; smelling, snuffling at; the<BR>nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रातृ
घ्रातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who smells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात्वा
घ्रात्वा, ind. having smelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रेय
घ्रेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be smelled, what may be<BR>smelled or snuffled at; (अम्), n. odour, smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ 1. ङ, the fifth consonant of the San-<BR>skṛt alphabet, and the nasal of the first class. No<BR>real word in use begins with this letter; it is usually<BR>found as the first member of a compound consonant<BR>preceded by a vowel; the sound of ङ् corresponds to<BR>that of न्ग् in song.<BR>—ङ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or<BR>sound ङ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ 2. ङ, अस्, m. an object of sense; desire,<BR>wish for any sensual object; an epithet of Śiva;<BR>(Bhairava.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङु
ङु ङु, cl. 1. A. ङवते, ङुङुवे, to sound:<BR>Desid. ञुङूषते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च 1. च, the twentieth letter of the alphabet,<BR>and first of the second or palatal class of consonants,<BR>having the simple sound of ch in church.<BR>—च-कार,<BR>अस्, m. the letter or sound च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च 2. च, ind. (a particle and conjunction<BR>usually translateable by) and, both, also, moreover,<BR>as well as. This conjunction, like the Lat. que and<BR>Gr. τε, is usually placed as an enclitic after the word<BR>which it connects with what precedes, and when used<BR>with the personal pronouns these must appear in<BR>their fuller accented forms (e. g. तव च मम च,<BR>both of thee and of me, not ते च मे च). It con-<BR>nects whole sentences as well as parts of sentences,<BR>and seems to have been originally placed after both<BR>the words or clauses which it joins together, for in<BR>the Ṛg-veda the double च occurs much more fre-<BR>quently than the single (e. g. अहं च त्वं च,<BR>I and thou). The double च may also be used<BR>somewhat redundantly in classical Sanskrit (e. g. क्व<BR>हरिणकानां जीवितं चातिलोलं क्व च वज्र-<BR>साराः शरास् ते, where is both the frail existence of<BR>fawns and where are thy adamantine arrows ?). In the<BR>later literature, however, the first च is more usually<BR>omitted (e. g. अहं त्वं च), and when more than<BR>two things are enumerated only one च is often found<BR>(e. g. तेजसा यशसा लक्ष्म्या स्थित्या च परया,<BR>in glory, in fame, in beauty, and in high condition).<BR>Elsewhere, when more than two things are enume-<BR>rated, च is placed after some and omitted after others<BR>(e. g. ऋण-दाता च वैद्यश्च श्रोत्रियो नदी, both<BR>the payer of a debt and a physician [and] a Brāhman<BR>[and] a river). In the Veda and even in classical<BR>Sanskrit, when the double च would generally be<BR>used, the second may occasionally be omitted (e. g.<BR>इन्द्रश्च सोमः, both Indra [and] Soma; दुर्-<BR>भेद्यश्च आशु-सन्धेयः, both difficult to be<BR>divided [and] quickly to be united). Rarely च may<BR>imply a reference to certain other words which are<BR>not expressed (e. g. कमण्डलौ च करकः, the<BR>word करक has the meaning ‘pitcher’ and other<BR>meanings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च may be used for वा and is then translateable by<BR>‘either,’ ‘or’ (e. g. इह चामुत्र वा, either here or<BR>hereafter; स्त्री वा पुमान् वा यच्चान्यत् सत्त्वम्,<BR>either a woman or a man or any other being); and<BR>when a negative particle is joined with च the<BR>two may then be translated by ‘neither,’ ‘nor.’<BR>Occasionally one च or one न may be omitted (e. g.<BR>न च परिभोक्तुं नैव शक्नोमि हातुम्, I am<BR>able neither to enjoy nor to abandon; न पूर्वाह्णे<BR>न च पराह्णे, neither in the forenoon nor in the<BR>afternoon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च is often joined to the adverbs एव, अपि, तथा,<BR>तथैव, &c., either with or without a negative<BR>particle (e. g. वैरिणं नोपसेवेत सहायं<BR>चैव वैरिणः, one ought not to serve either an<BR>enemy or the ally of an enemy). See एव, अपि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च sometimes = एव, even, indeed, certainly, just,<BR>&c. (e. g. सु-चिन्तितं चौषधं न नाम-<BR>मात्रेण करोत्य् अ-रोगम्, even a well-devised<BR>remedy does not cure a disease by its mere name;<BR>यावन्त एव ते तावांश्च स, as great as they [were]<BR>just so great was he).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च may occasionally be disjunctive and be trans-<BR>lated by ‘but,’ ‘on the contrary,’ ‘on the other<BR>hand,’ ‘yet,’ ‘nevertheless’ (e. g. वरम् आद्यौ न<BR>चान्तिमः, better the two first but not the last;<BR>शान्तम् इदम् आश्रम-पदं स्फुरति च बाहुः,<BR>this hermitage is tranquil yet my arm throbs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चच
च — च may be used to express immediate<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">Page0310-c+ 76</a>]<BR>connection between two acts or their simultaneous<BR>occurrence (e. g. मम च मुक्तं तमसा<BR>मनो मनसिजेन धनुषि शरश्च निवेशितः,<BR>no sooner is my mind freed from darkness than a<BR>shaft is fixed on his bow by the heart-born god).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च rarely = चेत्, if (e. g. जीवितुं चेच्छसे, if thou<BR>wishest to live).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च may be used as an expletive (e. g. अन्यैश्च<BR>क्रतुभिश्च, and with other sacrifices). The native<BR>dictionaries assign to च the following significations<BR>or forces: — conjunction (अन्व्-आचय), collective com-<BR>bination (सम्-आहार), mutual connection (इतरे-<BR>तर), and aggregation (सम्-उच्चय). For the<BR>meaning of च after an interrogative see 2. क,<BR>2. कथा, &c.; [cf. Gr. τε; Lat. que, pe (in nempe,<BR>&c.); Goth. uh; Zend ca; Old Pers. câ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च 3. च, अस्, आ, अम्, seedless; bad, vile,<BR>mischievous; (अस्), m. a thief; a tortoise; the moon;<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्
चक् चक्, cl. 1. P. A. चकति, -ते, चचाक,<BR>चेके, अचकीत् and अचाकीत्, चकितुम्, to be<BR>satiated, to be contented, to be satisfied; to repel,<BR>resist; to shine [cf. कन् and 2. कम्]: Caus. चक-<BR>यति and चाकयति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकित|चकितं
चकित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, trembling; fearful,<BR>timid; startled, frightened, afraid of.<BR>—चकित-चकि-<BR>तम्, ind. with great alarm; (अम्), n. trembling,<BR>timidity, alarm; स-चकितम्, tremblingly; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a metre consisting of four lines of sixteen syllables<BR>each.<BR>—चकित-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, faint-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकास्
चकास् 1. चकास् [cf. rt. काश्], cl. 2. P.<BR>चकास्ति, 3rd pl. चकासति, Impf. 2nd<BR>sing. अचकास् or अचकत्, 3rd sing. अचकात्, Impv.<BR>2nd sing. चकाधि or चकाद्धि, Perf. चकासाञ्-<BR>चकार, 1st Fut. चकासिता, Aor. अचकासीत्, to shine,<BR>to be bright: Caus. चकासयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अचीचकासत् or अचचकासत्, to cause to shine, make<BR>bright, illuminate: Desid. चिचकासिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकास्
2. चकास्, आस्, आस्, आस्, shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासयत्
चकासयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, illuminating, beautifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासित
चकासित, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminated, shining, splendid,<BR>beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोर|चकोरः
चकोर चकोर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. चक्,<BR>to be satisfied, i. e. with moon-beams), the bartavelle<BR>or Greek partridge, Perdix Rufa or Tetrao Rufus,<BR>(this bird is fabled to subsist upon moon-beams,<BR>hence ‘an eye drinking the nectar of a moon-like<BR>face’ is poetically called चक्षुश्-चकोर; the eyes<BR>of the Cakora are said to turn red when it looks<BR>on poisoned food, see Schol. to Manu VII. 217); N.<BR>of a people; also of a prince; and of a mountain.<BR>—चकोर-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, having eyes like those of a<BR>partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरक|चकोरकः
चकोरक, अस्, m. the Greek partridge; [cf. the<BR>preceding.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्क्
चक्क् चक्क्, cl. 10. P. चक्कयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to suffer; to give or inflict pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्क
चक्क चक्क, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्कल
चक्कल चक्कल, अस्, आ, अम्, round, circular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्नस|चक्नसः
चक्नस चक्नस, अस्, m. (fr. rt. क्नस्), crooked-<BR>ness, dishonesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्र|चक्रं|चक्रः
चक्र चक्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. क्रम् or rt. 1. कृ?<BR>reduplicated), the wheel of a carriage, the wheel of the<BR>Sun's chariot, or (metaphorically) the wheel of Time<BR>(in these senses sometimes अस्, m. in Ved.); a potter's<BR>wheel; a discus or sharp circular missile weapon (espe-<BR>cially applied to the favourite weapon of Viṣṇu); an<BR>oil-mill; a circle; any circle or ring (e. g. कलाप-<BR>चक्र, the circle of a peacock's tail); a form of<BR>military array (in a circle); circular flight (of a bird<BR>&c.); a circle or depression of the body for mystical,<BR>astrological, or chiromantic purposes, (six of these<BR>are enumerated one above the other, viz. 1. मूला-<BR>धार, the parts about the pubis; 2. स्वाधिष्ठान,<BR>the umbilical region; 3. मणि-पूरम्, the pit of<BR>the stomach or epigastrium; 4. अनाहतम्, the root<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-a" target="_blank">Page0311-a+ 81</a>]<BR>of the nose; 5. वि-शुद्धम्, the hollow between<BR>the frontal sinuses; 6. आज्ञाख्यम्, the fontenelle or<BR>union of the coronal and sagittal sutures: various facul-<BR>ties and divinities are supposed to be present in these<BR>hollows); a general N. for a diagram of various circular<BR>forms used for astrological or astronomical purposes, a<BR>sphere or astronomical circle in general (e. g. राशि-<BR>चक्रम्, the zodiac); a cycle, a cycle of years, the cycle<BR>of the seasons; the horizon; a particular constellation<BR>in the form of a hexagon; a troop, a multitude (in<BR>this sense m. and n.); an army, a host; a province,<BR>number of villages, region, district, circuit; range, de-<BR>partment in general; section of a book; the wheel<BR>of a monarch's chariot rolling over his dominions,<BR>sovereignty; a realm; a whirlpool; the winding of<BR>a river; the convolutions or spiral marks of the<BR>Śāla-grāma or ammonite, a kind of petrified shell;<BR>the flower of the plant Tagara; N. of a particular<BR>plant or drug; a crooked or fraudulent device [cf.<BR>चक्रिका]; N. of a metre consisting of four lines of<BR>fourteen syllables each, = चक्र-पात; the ruddy goose<BR>or Brāhmany duck, Anas Casarca (in this sense m.);<BR>N. of a people (m. pl.); N. of a man (m.); of a<BR>Nāga (m.); N. of one of the attendants of Skanda<BR>(m.); N. of a mountain (m.); (ई), f., Ved. a wheel;<BR>(आ), f., N. of two plants, = कर्कट-शृङ्गी and<BR>नागर-मुस्ता. At the end of an adj. comp. the f.<BR>will end in आ; [cf. अ-चक्र, उच्चा-च्˚, एक-च्˚, काल-<BR>च्˚, कू-च्˚, दण्ड-च्˚, धर्म-च्˚, स-च्˚, &c.; cf.<BR>also Gr. κύκλος.]<BR>—चक्र-कारक, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of perfume, apparently a dried shell-fish, see नखी.<BR>—चक्र-कुल्या, f., N. of a plant [cf. चित्र-पर्णी]<BR>said to be a species of fern, commonly Cākuliya<BR>(Hemionites Cordifolia).<BR>—चक्र-गज, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a plant, = चक्र-मर्द.<BR>—चक्र-गण्डु, उस्, m.<BR>a round pillow.<BR>—चक्र-गति, इस्, f. rotation, revolu-<BR>tion.<BR>—चक्र-गुच्छ, अस्, m. the tree Jonesia Aśoca;<BR>[cf. अशोक.]<BR>—चक्र-गोप्तृ, ता, m. the protector of<BR>a wheel; (तारौ), m. du. two men whose business<BR>is to preserve the wheels of a carriage from damage;<BR>[cf. चक्र-रक्ष.]<BR>—चक्र-ग्रहण, अम्, ई, n.<BR>f. (?) ‘an army-holder,’ a rampart, an intrenchment.<BR>—चक्र-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going in a circle, epithet<BR>of a class of superhuman beings; a juggler, = चक्रा-<BR>ट (?).<BR>—चक्र-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going in a circle,<BR>walking from one place to another.<BR>—चक्र-चूडा-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. a round jewel in a coronet or diadem;<BR>a honorific title of Vopa-deva; N. of a man.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>जीवक, अस्, m. or चक्र-जीविन्, ई, m. a potter (who<BR>lives by his wheel).<BR>—चक्र-तलाम्र (˚तल-आम्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a kind of mango tree.<BR>—चक्र-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—चक्र-तैल, अम्, n. oil pre-<BR>pared from the plant Cakra (चक्र-मर्द ?).<BR>—चक्र-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m. a hog (having curved<BR>tusks).<BR>—चक्र-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—चक्र-दन्ती, f., N. of a plant; [cf. दन्ती.]<BR>—चक्रदन्ती-वीज, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = जय-<BR>पाल and दन्ती-वीज.<BR>—चक्र-दीपिका, f., N. of a<BR>literary work.<BR>—चक्र-दृश्, क्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—चक्र-देव, अस्, m., N. of a warrior.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>द्वार, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—चक्र-धनुस्,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—चक्र-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bearing a wheel, having a wheel, a wheel-bearer;<BR>carrying a discus; driving in a carriage; (अस्), m. a<BR>N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (as holding a discus in one<BR>hand); a sovereign, ruler, the governor of a province,<BR>the owner of many villages; a village tumbler or<BR>juggler; a snake; N. of a man.<BR>—चक्र-धर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a prince of the Vidyā-dharas.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>धार = चक्र-धर above.<BR>—चक्र-धारा, f.<BR>the periphery of a wheel.<BR>—चक्र-नख, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of perfume, = व्याघ्र-नख.<BR>—चक्र-नदी<BR>or चक्र-णदी, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चक्र-नाभि,<BR>इस्, f. the nave of a wheel.<BR>—चक्र-नामन्, आ, m. a<BR>pyritic ore of iron, see माक्षिक.<BR>—चक्र-नायक,<BR>अस्, m. the leader of a troop; a kind of perfume, =<BR>चक्र-नख.<BR>—चक्र-नारायणी-संहिता, f., N.<BR>of a literary work.<BR>—चक्र-नेमि, इस्, f., N. of one<BR>of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—चक्र-पद्-<BR>माट, अस्, m., N. of the plant Cassia Tora, = चक्र-<BR>मर्द.<BR>—चक्र-परिव्याध, अस्, m. the plant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-b" target="_blank">Page0311-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Cathartocarpus Fistula; [cf. आरग्बध.]<BR>—चक्र-<BR>पर्णी, f. a plant, commonly Cākuliya, Hemionites<BR>Cordifolia; [cf. चक्र-कुल्या.]<BR>—चक्र-पाणि, इस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (holding a discus<BR>in one hand); N. of an author; (sometimes चक्र-<BR>पाणिन्.).<BR>—चक्रपाणि-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of an author<BR>of a lexicon; [cf. चन्द्रोदय.]<BR>—चक्र-पात, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of metre, = चक्र.<BR>—चक्र-पाद or<BR>चक्र-पादक, अस्, m. a carriage (having wheels for<BR>feet); an elephant (having circular feet).<BR>—चक्र-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. the superintendent of a province; one<BR>who carries a discus; a circle; the horizon.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town built by Cakra-mardikā.<BR>—चक्र-पुष्करिणी, f., N. of a sacred tank at<BR>Kāśi or Benares; [cf. चक्र-तीर्थ and मणि-<BR>कर्णिका.]<BR>—चक्र-फल, अम्, n. a missile weapon,<BR>a kind of discus.<BR>—चक्र-बान्धव, अस्, m. the<BR>sun (‘friend of the ruddy goose,’ these birds being<BR>supposed to couple only in the day-time).<BR>—चक्र-<BR>बाल and चक्र-वाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a ring, circle<BR>[cf. बाली and वालक]; the horizon (usually n.); a<BR>mass, a multitude, a number, assemblage; (अस्), m.<BR>a mythical range of mountains supposed to encircle<BR>the orb of the earth like a wall and to be the limit<BR>of light and darkness (perhaps a bank of clouds<BR>shaped like mountains on the horizon); [cf. चक्र-<BR>वाट and चक्र-वाड.]<BR>—चक्र-बालधि, इस्, m. a<BR>dog, ‘having a curved tail.’<BR>—चक्र-भानु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—चक्र-भृत्, त्, m. ‘discus-<BR>bearer,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—चक्र-भेदिनी, f.<BR>night (‘dividing the ruddy geese,’ the male and<BR>female of these birds being condemned to be sepa-<BR>rated at night); [cf. चक्र-बान्धव.]<BR>—चक्र-<BR>भ्रमि, इस्, m. f. (?) a grindstone.<BR>—चक्र-भ्रान्ति,<BR>इस्, f. the whirling round of the wheels (of a chariot).<BR>—चक्र-मठ, अस्, m., N. of a college built in a<BR>circular form by Cakra-varman.<BR>—चक्र-मण्डलिन्,<BR>ई, m. a large snake, the Boa Constrictor, (the body<BR>of the snake or its spots being compared to a<BR>wheel.)<BR>—चक्र-मन्द, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—चक्र-मर्द, अस्, m. the plant Cassia Tora.<BR>—चक्र-मर्दक, अस्, m. Cassia Tora; (इका),<BR>f., N. of the wife of Lalitāditya.<BR>—चक्रम्-आसज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. stopping the wheels (of the chariot).<BR>—चक्र-मुख, अस्, m. ‘having a curved mouth,’<BR>a hog.<BR>—चक्र-मुषल, अस्, आ, अम्, (a battle) car-<BR>ried on with the discus and club.<BR>—चक्र-मेलक,<BR>अस् or अम् (?), m. or n., N. of a place in Kaśmīra.<BR>—चक्र-मौलि, इस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>यान, अम्, n. any wheel-carriage.<BR>—चक्र-योग,<BR>अस्, m. applying a splint or similar instrument by<BR>means of pulleys in case of dislocation of the thigh.<BR>—चक्र-रक्ष, अस्, m. = चक्र-गोप्तृ, q. v.<BR>—चक्र-रद, अस्, m. a hog, a boar (‘having<BR>curved tusks’); [cf. चक्र-मुख.]<BR>—चक्र-लक्-<BR>षणा, f. the plant Cocculus Cordifolius, = गुडूची.<BR>—चक्र-लताम्र, अस्, m. a kind of mango tree;<BR>(another reading for चक्र-तलाम्र.)<BR>—चक्र-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with wheels, wheeled; armed<BR>with a discus; circular, being in the form of a ring<BR>or circle; (आन्), m. the proprietor of an oil-mill or<BR>one in which seeds are bruised; an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; a sovereign, an emperor; N. of a moun-<BR>tain; (वत्), ind. like a wheel, in rotation, going<BR>round or revolving like a wheel.<BR>—चक्रवर्ति-ता, f.<BR>or चक्रवर्ति-त्व, अम्, n. the mark or state of a<BR>universal emperor; see the next.<BR>—चक्र-वर्तिन्, ई,<BR>m. a ruler the wheels of whose chariot roll every-<BR>where without obstruction; an emperor, a sovereign<BR>of the world, a supreme ruler, the ruler of a Cakra<BR>or country described as extending from sea to sea,<BR>(twelve princes beginning with Bharata are especially<BR>considered as Cakra-vartins); (ई, इनी, इ), supreme,<BR>holding the highest rank; (इनी), f. a fragrant plant,<BR>commonly Cakāvat [cf. जनी]; the plant Nardos-<BR>tachys Jaṭāmāṃsī; another plant, = अलक्तक.<BR>—च-<BR>क्र-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king of Kaśmīra; [cf.<BR>चाक्रवर्मण.]<BR>—चक्र-वाक, अस्, m. the ruddy<BR>goose, commonly called the Brāhmany duck, Anas<BR>Casarca; (ई), f. the female of this bird; [cf. चक्र,<BR>चक्र-साह्वय, चक्राह्व, चक्राह्वय, &c.]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-c" target="_blank">Page0311-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—चक्रवाक-बन्धु, उस्, m. the sun; [cf. चक्र-<BR>बान्धव.]<BR>—चक्रवाक-वती, f. probably N. of a<BR>river (abounding in Cakra-vākas).<BR>—चक्रवाकिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, filled with Cakra-vākas.<BR>—चक्रवाकोपकू-<BR>जित (˚क-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, made resonant with the<BR>cooing or cry of the Cakra-vāka.<BR>—चक्र-वाट, अस्,<BR>m. a limit, a boundary; a lamp-stand; engaging in an<BR>action; [cf. चक्र-बाल.]<BR>—चक्र-वाड, अस्, m. a<BR>fabulous range of mountains, see चक्र-बाल; (अम्),<BR>n. a circle.<BR>—चक्र-वात, अस्, m. a whirlwind, a<BR>hurricane, = चक्र-वाल; [cf. चक्र-बाल.]<BR>—चक्र-<BR>विमल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a plant.<BR>—चक्र-वृद्धि, इस्, f. interest upon interest;<BR>wages for transporting goods in a carriage.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>व्यूह, अस्, m. any circular array of troops.<BR>—चक्र-<BR>शत-पत्त्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a plant.<BR>—चक्र-श्रेणी, f. = अज-शृङ्गी, the plant Odina<BR>Pinnata, bearing a curved fruit.<BR>—चक्र-संवर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddha, = वज्र-टीक.<BR>—चक्र-सक्-<BR>थ, अस्, आ, अम्, having crooked thighs, bow-legged.<BR>—चक्र-सञ्जञ, अम्, n. tin.<BR>—चक्र-साह्वय,<BR>अस्, m. = चक्र, = चक्र-वाक, Anas Casarca.<BR>—चक्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of the son of Tārā-<BR>candra and father of Siṃha.<BR>—चक्र-स्वामिन्, ई, m.<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; [cf. चक्र-धर.]<BR>—चक्र-<BR>हस्त, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu (‘discus-handed’).<BR>—चक्र-ह्रद, अस्, m., N. of a lake.<BR>—चक्रा-<BR>कार, अस्, आ, अम्, or चक्राकृति (˚र-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>circular, round.<BR>—चक्राकी, a various reading for<BR>चक्राङ्की, q. v.<BR>—चक्राङ्किता (˚र-अङ्˚), f. a kind<BR>of plant.<BR>—चक्राङ्की, f. a goose; [cf. चक्राङ्ग.]<BR>—चक्राङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a gander (having a<BR>curved neck); a carriage [cf. चक्र-पाद]; (ई), f.<BR>a goose; N. of several plants, = कटु-रोहिणी; N. of<BR>another plant, = Enhydra Heloncha (हिल-मोचिका);<BR>another plant, = कर्कट-शृङ्गी; another plant,<BR>Cocculus Tomentosus, = वृष-पर्णी or सु-दर्-<BR>शना; another plant, Rubia Munjista (मञ्जिष्ठा);<BR>(अम्), n. a parasol.<BR>—चक्राट (˚र-अट), अस्, m. a<BR>juggler, a snake-catcher, snake-charmer, one who<BR>exhibits snakes and pretends to cure their bites; a<BR>knave, a cheat, a rogue; a gold coin or certain weight<BR>of gold, a Dīnār.<BR>—चक्राधिवासिन् (˚र-अध्˚), ई,<BR>m. the orange-tree.<BR>—चक्रायुध (˚र-आय्˚), अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (whose weapon is<BR>the discus).<BR>—चक्रायोध्य (˚र-अय्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—चक्रावर्त (˚र-आव्˚), अस्, m. turning<BR>round, whirling or rotatory motion.<BR>—चक्राह्व<BR>(˚र-आह्˚), अस्, m. = चक्र-वाक, Anas Casarca; =<BR>चक्र-मर्द, Cassia Tora; (आ), f. Cocculus To-<BR>mentosus; [cf. चक्राङ्गा.]<BR>—चक्राह्वय (˚र-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, m. = चक्राह्व, Anas Casarca.<BR>—चक्री-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with wheels, wheeled;<BR>(आन्), m. an ass; N. of a king.<BR>—चक्रेश्वर (˚र-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. lord of the discus, an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>(ई), f. a female deity peculiar to the Jainas, one of<BR>their Vidyā-devīs or goddesses of wisdom, executing<BR>the orders of the first Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रक|चक्रकः
चक्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, resembling a wheel or circle,<BR>wheel-shaped, circular; (अस्), m. a logical form or<BR>proposition, arguing in a circle; a kind of serpent;<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi; (आ), f. a kind of plant having great<BR>curative properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रला
चक्रला, f. a kind of Cyperus, = उच्चटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिक|चक्रिकः
चक्रिक, अस्, m. a discus-bearer; (आ), f. a heap,<BR>a troop; a crooked or fraudulent device; the<BR>knee (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिन्
चक्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a wheel or wheels,<BR>wheeled; having or holding a discus, an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; driving in a carriage; circular;<BR>(ई), m. a potter; an oil-grinder; a sovereign of the<BR>world, an emperor, a Cakra-vartin; the governor of<BR>a province; a kind of juggler or tumbler who ex-<BR>hibits tricks with a discus or a wheel (?); one who<BR>offers sacrifices for a whole village (?); an informer;<BR>an ass; the ruddy goose, Anas Casarca; a crow; a<BR>snake; the plant Cassia Tora, = चक्र-मर्द;<BR>another plant, Dalbergia Ougeinensis; a kind of<BR>perfume; [cf. स-चक्रिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिय
चक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, going in a carriage, being<BR>on a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रीकृ
चक्री-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to make round or circular, to curve or bend (as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राण|चक्राणः
चक्राण चक्राण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कृ),<BR>having done, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रि|चक्रिः
चक्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. doing, making, active, an<BR>agent; (इस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रु|चक्रुः
चक्रु, उस्, m. a doer, a maker, an agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ष्
चक्ष् चक्ष् (perhaps a reduplicated form<BR>of काश् = क्शा, which according to some is<BR>the original root. According to Pāṇini the rt.<BR>चक्ष् can only be used in the conjugational tenses<BR>and optionally in the Perf. In the non-conjugational<BR>tenses and optionally in the Perf. the rt. ख्या is<BR>substituted), cl. 2. A. Pres. चष्टे, Perf. चचक्षे.<BR>Other forms are exceptionally found, e. g. 2nd sing.<BR>Pres. P. चक्षि, 2nd pl. Impv. P. (with आ) चक्षत,<BR>Impf. अचक्षम्, Aor. अचचक्षम्, Inf. चष्टुम्,<BR>Ved. Inf. चक्षे, to appear, become visible: to see,<BR>look at, perceive, observe; to speak, say, tell, in-<BR>form; to eat, (a wrong form for जक्ष्): Pass.<BR>चक्ष्यते. The rt. चक्ष् appears like ख्या, to<BR>combine the two distinct meanings of seeing and<BR>speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षण|चक्षणं
चक्षण, अम्, n., Ved. appearing, becoming<BR>visible, appearance, aspect; speaking, saying; eating<BR>a relish to promote drinking, (a wrong form for ज-<BR>क्षण?); [cf. विश्व-चक्षण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षणि
चक्षणि, इस्, m., Ved. an illuminator, irradiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षन्
चक्षन्, अ, n., Ved. the eye, (du. चक्षणी,<BR>the eyes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षस्
चक्षस्, आस्, m. a teacher, a spiritual teacher, an<BR>instructor in sacred science; an epithet of Bṛhaspati,<BR>the teacher of the gods; (अस्), n. radiance, clearness;<BR>the act of seeing, being seen, (चक्षसे, dat. = inf. to<BR>see, to be seen); look, sight, the eye; [cf. अपाक-<BR>चक्षस्, ईय-च्˚, उपाक-च्˚, उरु-च्˚, घोर-च्˚, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षु|चक्षुः
चक्षु, उस् or उ, m. or n. (?), Ved. the eye; (उस्),<BR>m., N. of a prince; N. of a river.<BR>—चक्षु-प, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince; (a various reading has चाक्षुष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुस्
चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, seeing; (उस्), m., N. of a<BR>Marut; also of a Ṛṣi with the patronymic Mānava;<BR>N. of a son of Anu; (उस्), f., N. of a river [cf. चक्षु<BR>and सु-चक्षुस्]; (उस्), n. light, clearness; the act<BR>of seeing, faculty of seeing, sight, aspect, a look; the<BR>eye; often at the end of a compound (e. g. घ्राण-<BR>चक्षुस्, one who uses his nose for eyes; चार-<BR>चक्षुस्, one who sees by means of his spies;<BR>धर्म-चक्षुस्, one who has an eye for justice);<BR>[cf. अ-चक्षुस्, अघोर-च्˚, &c.; cf. also Zend चस्-<BR>मन्.]<BR>—चक्षुः-पथ, अस्, m. ‘the path of the<BR>eyes,’ the horizon, the range of sight (e. g. चक्षुः-<BR>पथम् प्राप्, to become visible; चक्षुः-पथाद्<BR>अपगम्, to vanish from the sight).<BR>—चक्षुः-<BR>पीडा, f. pain of the eyes.<BR>—चक्षुः-श्रवस्, आस्, or<BR>चक्षुः-श्रुति, इस्, m. a snake (using its eyes for<BR>ears).<BR>—चक्षुः-सामन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman (=<BR>प्रजापतेस् सामन्).<BR>—चक्षुर्-इन्द्रिय, अम्, n. the<BR>sense of seeing.<BR>—चक्षुर्-गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, com-<BR>ing within range of the eye.<BR>—चक्षुर्-ग्रहण,<BR>अम्, n. morbid affection of the eyes.<BR>—चक्षुर्-दा,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. giving sight.<BR>—चक्षुर्-दान,<BR>अम्, n. the ceremony of anointing the eyes of an<BR>image at the time of consecration.<BR>—चक्षुर्-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, promoting sight.<BR>—चक्षुर्-मन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. bewitching with the eye.<BR>—चक्षुर्-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, resembling the eye.<BR>—चक्षुर्-मल, अम्,<BR>n. the excretion of the eyes.<BR>—चक्षुर्-लोक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, seeing with the eyes.<BR>—चक्षुर्-वन्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. suffering from disease of the eyes.<BR>—च-<BR>क्षुर्-वर्धनिका, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चक्षुर्-<BR>वहन, अम्, n., N. of a plant, = मेष-शृङ्गी.<BR>—चक्षुर्-विषय, अस्, m. the horizon, visibility;<BR>presence, sight, ken; an object of sight, any visible<BR>object.<BR>—चक्षुर्-हन्, आ, -घ्नी, अ, killing with a<BR>look.<BR>—चक्षुश्-चित्, त्, त्, त्, collecting the faculty of<BR>sight.<BR>—चक्षुष्-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wishing<BR>for the faculty of seeing.<BR>—चक्षुष्-टस्, ind. away<BR>from the eye.<BR>—चक्षुष्-पति, इस्, m. the lord of the<BR>eyes.<BR>—चक्षुष्-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. protecting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">Page0312-b+ 76</a>]<BR>the eye-sight.<BR>—चक्षुष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed<BR>with the faculty of seeing, seeing, furnished with eyes;<BR>representing the eye.<BR>—चक्षुष्मत्-ता, f. the<BR>state of one who sees, the faculty of seeing.<BR>—च-<BR>क्षू-रोग, अस्, m. disease of the eye, ophthalmia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुष
चक्षुष, at the end of a compound = चक्षुस्,<BR>eye (e. g. स-चक्षुष, having eyes); (अस्), m., N.<BR>of the father of Manu Cākṣuṣa; (a wrong reading<BR>for चक्षुस्?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुष्य|चक्षुष्यं|चक्षुष्यः
चक्षुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing or agreeable to<BR>the eyes, agreeable, pleasing, good-looking, beautiful;<BR>(अस्), m. a collyrium or application to the eyes, ex-<BR>tracted from the Amomum Antorhiza; N. of the plant<BR>Pandanus Odoratissimus, = केतक; another plant,<BR>Hyperanthera Moringa; (आ), f. a kind of collyrium,<BR>the calx of brass or a blue stone used thus; a pleasing<BR>or interesting woman; the plant Pandanus Odora-<BR>tissimus; also of Glycine Labialis, and of Odina<BR>Pinnata; (अम्), n. two kinds of collyrium, = खर्-<BR>परीतुत्थ and सौवीराञ्जन; N. of a small shrub,<BR>= प्रपौण्डरीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चघ्
चघ् चघ्, cl. 5. P. चघ्नोति, &c., to smite<BR>or slay, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्कुण|चंकुणः|चङ्कुणः
चङ्कुण चङ्कुण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>चक्), a carriage, a tree; (अम्), n. any vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमण|चंक्रमण|चंक्रमणं|चङ्क्रमणं
चङ्क्रमण चङ्क्रमण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens.<BR>of rt. क्रम्), going about, taking exercise; who or<BR>what goes slowly or crookedly; (अम्), n. going about,<BR>walking, proceeding, going tortuously or slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमा|चंक्रमा
चङ्क्रमा, f. going about, walking, going tor-<BR>tuously or slowly.<BR>—चङ्क्रमा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>who or what moves slowly or crookedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्ग|चंग|चङ्गः
चङ्ग चङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, handsome, beautiful;<BR>dexterous, clever; sound, healthy; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चचेण्डा
चचेण्डा चचेण्डा, f., N. of a fruit-bearing<BR>creeper, = बृहत्-फल, वेश्म-कूल, श्वेत-राजी,<BR>commonly चिचिडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चच्चपुट
चच्चपुट चच्चपुट or (according to another<BR>authority) चच्चत्पुट, अस्, m. a kind of time in<BR>music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्च्|चंच्
चञ्च् चञ्च्, cl. 1. P. चञ्चति, चचञ्च,<BR>चञ्चितुम्, &c., to leap, jump; to go,<BR>move; to dangle; [cf. Hib. ceangtha, ‘they go, travel;<BR>ceangastair, ‘walking, pacing;’ Lat. cunctari ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्च|चंच|चंचः|चञ्चः
चञ्च, अस्, m. a basket; (आ), f. anything made of<BR>cane, a mat, a stool &c. made of reeds or basket-<BR>work; a straw-man, a doll; a puppet of grass or<BR>reeds; a contemptuous epithet of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चत्
चञ्चत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, leaping, going, moving;<BR>dangling; unsteady, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चत्क|चंचत्क
चञ्चत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, leaping, jumping, trembling,<BR>moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चु|चंचु|चञ्चुः
चञ्चु, उस्, उस्, उ, renowned, celebrated, known;<BR>clever [cf. चञ्चु-ता, चुञ्चु, चण, and अक्षर-<BR>चञ्चु]; (उस्), m. a deer; N. of several plants, the<BR>castor-oil plant, Ricinus Communis (एरण्ड); also<BR>= रक्तैरण्ड and क्षुद्र-चञ्चु, = गोनाडीक;<BR>N. of a son of Harita; (उस्), f. a beak, bill; a kind of<BR>vegetable, = चञ्चू, चञ्चु-पत्त्र, &c.<BR>—चञ्चु-ता,<BR>f. celebrity, cleverness, activity; the state of a beak.<BR>—चञ्चु-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a kind of vegetable, =<BR>चञ्चु, f.<BR>—चञ्चु-पुट, अस्, अम्, m. n. the bill of<BR>a bird when shut.<BR>—चञ्चु-प्रहार, अस्, m. a peck<BR>with the beak.<BR>—चञ्चु-भृत्, त्, m. ‘having a beak,’<BR>a bird.<BR>—चञ्चु-मत्, आन्, अती, m. f. ‘possessed of a<BR>beak,’ a bird.<BR>—चञ्चु-सूचि, इस्, m. the tailor-bird,<BR>Sylvia Sutoria; also चञ्चुसूचिक, अस्, m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुका|चंचुका
चञ्चुका, f. a beak, bill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुर|चंचुर|चञ्चुरः
1. चञ्चुर, अस्, m. a kind of vegetable, = चञ्चु,<BR>f.; [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चू|चंचू
चञ्चू, ऊस्, f. a beak, the bill of a bird; a kind of<BR>vegetable. See चञ्चु above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चूक
चञ्चूक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people to the south-<BR>west of Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चरिन्|चंचरिन्
चञ्चरिन् चञ्चरिन्, ई, m. or चञ्चरी, f. or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">Page0312-c+ 75</a>]<BR>चञ्चरीक, अस्, m. (fr. Intens. of rt. चर्), a bee.<BR>—चञ्चरीकावली (˚क-आवली), f. a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines of thirteen syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुर|चंचुर|चञ्चुरः
2. चञ्चुर, अस्, आ, अम्, going repeatedly, expert<BR>in, conversant with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुरी
चञ्चुरी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, constantly practising or en-<BR>gaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चूर्गमाण
चञ्चूर्गमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, following evil practices,<BR>behaving ill, addicted to wickedness, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चल|चंचल|चञ्चलं|चञ्चलः
चञ्चल चञ्चल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of rt.<BR>चल्), moving to and fro, movable, unsteady, shaking,<BR>trembling; unsteady, inconstant, inconsiderate, quiver-<BR>ing, flickering, playing, moving irregularly; fickle;<BR>(अस्), m. the wind; a lover, a libertine, a lecher;<BR>(आ), f. lightning; long pepper; fortune, Lakṣmī or<BR>the goddess of fortune; N. of a metre consisting of<BR>four lines of sixteen syllables each.<BR>—चञ्चल-ता, f.<BR>or चञ्चल-त्व, अम्, n. movableness, unsteadiness,<BR>inconstancy, fickleness.<BR>—चञ्चल-हृदय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, capricious, fickle, false-hearted.<BR>—चञ्चला-<BR>क्षिका (˚ल-अक्षि), f., N. of a metre consisting of<BR>four lines of twelve syllables each.<BR>—चञ्चलाख्य<BR>(˚ल-आख्˚), अस्, m. incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चु|चंचु|चञ्चुः
चञ्चु चञ्चु. See under rt. चुञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुर|चंचुर|चञ्चुरः
चञ्चुर चञ्चुर. See under चञ्च् and चञ्चरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुल
चञ्चुल चञ्चुल, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of this man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चट्
चट् चट् (fr. rt. चत् and चल् and उच्-चट्),<BR>cl. 1. P. चटति, &c., to break, break off, fall<BR>off, separate; to rain; to cover; (in the last two senses<BR>a various reading for कट्): Caus. P. चाटयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to break, pierce; to kill, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटक|चटकः
चटक, अस्, m. a sparrow; N. of a poet; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. a nickname of the pupils of Vaiśampāyana<BR>(also written चरक); (आ), f. a hen-sparrow; a<BR>young hen-sparrow; Turdus Macrourus, = श्यामा;<BR>the root of long pepper, = चटका-शिरस्; (इका), f.<BR>a hen-sparrow; the root of long pepper.<BR>—चटका-<BR>शिरस्, n. the root of long pepper.<BR>—चटिका-शिर,<BR>अस्, m. or चटिका-शिरस्, n. the root of long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटन|चटनं
चटन, अम्, n. cracking, splitting; falling off in<BR>small pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटु|चटुः
चटु, उस्, उ, m. n. kind or flattering discourse; a<BR>scream, screech; a devotional posture among ascetics;<BR>(उस्), m. the belly.<BR>—चटु-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a place.<BR>—चटु-लालस, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased with or<BR>desirous of flattery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुल|चटुलः
चटुल, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, tremulous, moving,<BR>movable, shaking, unsteady; kind, fine, beautiful;<BR>(आ), f. lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुलोल
चटुलोल or चटुल्लोल, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps a cor-<BR>ruption of चटुल-लोल), moving gracefully; tremulous<BR>and beautiful, beautiful as a soft swimming eye &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटचटा
चटचटा चटचटा, ind. an onomatopoetic<BR>word for the clashing of weapons, the crackling of<BR>fire, rattling of violent rain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटचटाय
चटचटाय, A. -यते, to crackle, rattle, to make<BR>any sharp sound rapidly repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटचटायन|चटचटायनं
चटचटायन, अम्, n. crackling, a rattling sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्
चण् चण् [cf. rt. चन् and वण् and वन्],<BR>cl. 1. P. चणति, &c., to sound, to give; to<BR>go, to injure, hurt, kill: Caus. चणयति or चाण-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अचीचणत् and अचचाणत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण|चणः
चण चण, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a com-<BR>pound) renowned, famous for, known [cf. विद्या-<BR>चण and अक्षर-चण]; (अस्), m. = चणक, the<BR>chick-pea.<BR>—चण-द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>= क्षुद्र-गोक्षुर; (also written चणी-द्रम.)<BR>—चण-पत्त्री, f., N. of a plant; [cf. रुदन्ती.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणक|चणकः
चणक, अस्, m. the chick-pea (Cicer Arietinum);<BR>N. of a Muni, the father of Cāṇakya; (अका), f.<BR>linseed, Linum Usitatissimum (अतसी), [cf. चण्डिका];<BR>(इका), f. a kind of grass, = क्षेत्र-जा, गो-दग्धा,<BR>सु-नीला, हिमा.<BR>—चणकात्मज (˚क-आत्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a sage, also called Cāṇakya or Vatsyāyana.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-a" target="_blank">Page0313-a+ 80</a>]<BR>—चणकाम्लक (˚क-अम्ल), अम्, n. = चणक-<BR>लवण, pease with salt, sour pease.<BR>—चणकाम्ल-<BR>वार्, र्, n. acid drops of water on the leaves of the<BR>cicer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्ड्
चण्ड् चण्ड्, cl. 1. and 10. A. चण्डते and<BR>चण्डयते, -यितुम्, to be angry; to be<BR>wrathful or passionate; [cf. Goth. hata; Eng. hate;<BR>Germ. hasse; Lat. odi ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्ड|चंड|चण्डं|चण्डः
चण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, fierce, violent, impetuous, hot,<BR>warm, ardent with passion, passionate, wrathful, angry,<BR>cruel; active, quick; mischievous, evil; pungent,<BR>acrid; circumcised; चण्डम्, ind. violently, passion-<BR>ately, fiercely, in anger; (अस्), m. an evil being, a<BR>demon, (चण्डस्य नप्त्यः, the daughters of<BR>Caṇḍa, a class of female demons); an epithet of<BR>Śiva; also of Skanda; N. of a Daitya; of an<BR>attendant of Yama; or of Śiva; the tamarind tree;<BR>(आ), f. a N. of the goddess Durgā, applied especially<BR>to her incarnation for the purpose of destroying the<BR>Asura or demon called Mahiṣa, (this exploit forms<BR>the subject of a section of the Mārkaṇḍeya-Purāṇa,<BR>and is particularly celebrated in Bengal at the Durgā-<BR>pūjā, or festival held in honour of the goddess,<BR>towards the close of the year, about Oct.-Nov.); N.<BR>of one of the eight Nāyikās or Śaktis of Durgā; N.<BR>of a goddess fulfilling the orders of the twelfth Arhat of<BR>the present Ava-sarpiṇī; N. of a river; N. of several<BR>prickly plants, = ओषधि, Andropogon Aciculatus;<BR>Mucuna Pruritus (कपि-कच्छु); Salvinia Cucculata<BR>(आखु-कर्णी), = श्वेत-दूर्वा and = लिङ्गिनी; a per-<BR>fume, commonly Chor; (ई), f. a N. of Durgā; a<BR>passionate woman, a vixen; a term of endearment<BR>applied to a mistress; N. of the wife of Uddālaka;<BR>N. of a metre consisting of four lines of thirteen<BR>syllables each; (अम्), n. heat, warmth; passion,<BR>wrath; [cf. अ-चण्डी, उच्-चण्ड, प्र-च्˚, चाण्ड.]<BR>—चण्ड-कर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—चण्ड-कोलाहला, f. a kind of musical instrument.<BR>—चण्ड-कौशिक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kakṣī-<BR>vat; (अम्), n. (?) title of a drama.<BR>—चण्ड-गिरिक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चण्ड-घण्टा, f., a N.<BR>of Durgā.<BR>—चण्ड-ता, f. and चण्ड-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>warmth, pungency; warmth of temper, passionate-<BR>ness.<BR>—चण्ड-तुण्डक, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>—चण्ड-दीधिति, इस्, m. ‘having hot rays,’<BR>the sun; [cf. चण्डांशु.]<BR>—चण्ड-नायिका, f. an<BR>epithet of the goddess Durgā; N. of one of the<BR>eight Nāyikās or Śaktis of Durgā.<BR>—चण्ड-बल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the monkey followers of Rāma.<BR>—चण्ड-भानु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चण्ड-<BR>भार्गव, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman of the family<BR>of Cyavana.<BR>—चण्ड-महावीर-तन्त्र, अस्, m. title<BR>of a Buddhist work, = कल्लवीर-तन्त्र.<BR>—चण्ड-<BR>महासेन, अस्, m., N. of a king of Ujjayinī.<BR>—चण्ड-<BR>मुण्डा, f. a form of Durgā; [cf. चर्म-मुण्ड<BR>and चामुण्डा.]<BR>—चण्ड-मृग, अस्, m. a wild<BR>animal; epithet of a passionate man.<BR>—चण्ड-रव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a jackal.<BR>—चण्ड-रुद्रिका, f. know-<BR>ledge of mystical nature, acquired by worship of the<BR>Nāyikās.<BR>—चण्ड-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, violent, warm,<BR>passionate; (वती), f. an epithet of Durgā; N. of<BR>one of the eight Nāyikās or Śaktis of Durgā.<BR>—चण्ड-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a prince (probably<BR>a corruption of चन्द्र-वर्मन्).<BR>—चण्ड-विक्र-<BR>म, अस्, आ, अम्, of impetuous valour; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—चण्ड-वृष्टि-प्रयात, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a metre of four lines of twenty-seven syllables<BR>each.<BR>—चण्ड-वेग, अस्, आ, अम्, having an impetuous<BR>course or current, violent; (अस्), m., N. of a Gandharva<BR>chief.<BR>—चण्ड-शक्ति, इस्, m., N. of a Daitya.<BR>—चण्डांशु (˚ड-अं˚), उस्, m., the sun (‘having<BR>hot rays;’ cf. चण्ड-दीधिति).<BR>—चण्डादित्य-<BR>तीर्थ (˚ड-आद्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—चण्डा-<BR>शोक (˚ड-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince, also called<BR>Kāmāśoka, and as a protector of Buddhism, Dharmā-<BR>śoka.<BR>—चण्डी-कुसुम, अस्, m. red oleander; [cf.<BR>रक्त-करवीर.]<BR>—चण्डी-दास, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of a commentary called Kāvya-prakāśa-ṭīkā.<BR>—चण्डी-देवी-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR>—चण्डी-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. = चण्डिका-माहात्म्य.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">Page0313-b+ 77</a>]<BR>—चण्डीश (˚डी-ईश), अस्, m. the husband of Caṇḍī,<BR>Śiva.<BR>—चण्डेश्वर (˚डा-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘Caṇḍā's<BR>lord,’ an epithet of Śiva; N. of a writer on juris-<BR>prudence; also of an astronomer.<BR>—चण्डोग्रा (˚ड-<BR>उग्˚), f., N. of one of the eight Nāyikās, or Śaktis<BR>of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डि|चंडिः|चण्डिः
चण्डि, इस्, f. = चण्डी, a N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिका|चंडिका
चण्डिका, f. a N. of Durgā; a N. of the Devī-<BR>māhātmya; Linum Usitatissimum; [cf. उमा, देवी,<BR>हैमवती, चणका.]<BR>—चण्डिक-घण्ट, अस्, m.<BR>(? fr. चण्डिका + घण्ट, q. v.), a N. of Śiva.<BR>—चण्डिका-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. a section of the<BR>Mārkaṇḍeya-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिन्
चण्डिन्, ई, m., N. of an author; [cf. चामुण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिमन्|चंडिमन्
चण्डिमन्, आ, m. passion, violence, cruelty; heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिल|चंडिल|चंडिलः|चण्डिलः
चण्डिल, अस्, m., N. of Rudra; a barber; a kind<BR>of pot-herb [cf. वास्तूक]; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डीकृ|चंडीकृ
चण्डी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to enrage,<BR>make angry or violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डात|चंडात|चंडातः|चण्डातः
चण्डात चण्डात, अस्, m. fragrant oleander,<BR>Nerium Odorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डातक|चंडातक|चंडातकं|चण्डातकं|चंडातकः|चण्डातकः
चण्डातक चण्डातक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr.<BR>चण्ड ?), a short petticoat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डाल|चंडाल|चण्डालः
चण्डाल चण्डाल, अस्, m. (fr. चण्ड ?, cf.<BR>चाण्डाल), an outcast, a Caṇḍāla, the generic name<BR>for a man of the lowest and most despised of the<BR>mixed tribes, born from a Śūdra father and Brāhman<BR>mother.<BR>—चण्डाल-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of bulbous<BR>plant.<BR>—चण्डाल-ता, f. or चण्डाल-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state or condition of a Caṇḍāla.<BR>—चण्डाल-वल्लकी,<BR>f. the lute of the Caṇḍāla, a common lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डालिका|चंडालिका
चण्डालिका, f. the lute of the Caṇḍāla, a common<BR>or vulgar lute; an epithet of Durgā; a kind of plant.<BR>—चण्डालिका-बन्ध, अस्, m. a kind of knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डु|चंडुः|चण्डुः
चण्डु चण्डु, उस्, m. a rat; a small monkey,<BR>Simia Erythræa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्
चत् चत्, cl. 1. P. A. चतति, -ते, occurring<BR>only in pres. part. and past. and fut. pass.<BR>part. (see below), Ved. to hide one's self; to go; to<BR>ask, beg, solicit [cf. चद्]: Caus. P. A. चातयति, -ते,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to hide; to scare, frighten away;<BR>[cf. Gr. χατέω, χατίζω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतत्
चतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, hiding one's self; (Sāy.)<BR>going, residing in, being in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतित
चतित, or Ved. चत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, hidden, made<BR>to disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतिन्
चतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. hiding one's self; (Sāy.)<BR>destroying enemies, frightening away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्य
चत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be hidden^1 &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातक|चातकः
चातक, अस्, m. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातन
चातन, अस्, आ, अम्, driving away, removing [cf.<BR>अभिशस्ति-च्˚, अमीव-च्˚, अराय-च्˚]; (अम्), n., scil.<BR>सूक्तम्, certain verses of the Atharva-veda, the object<BR>of which is to avert evil demons; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>the supposed Ṛṣi of these verses of the Atharva-<BR>veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्
चतुर् चतुर्, चत्वारस् m. pl.,<BR>चत्वारि n. pl. (said to be fr. rt. चत्), four. In Vedic<BR>Sanskrit the inst., dat., abl., and loc. have the accent<BR>on the penultimate; in the later language either on<BR>the penultimate or on the last syllable. A Vedic form<BR>of the gen. pl. fem. चतसॄणाम् for चतसृणाम्<BR>occurs sometimes in Epic poetry; [cf. Gr. τέσσαρες,<BR>τέτταρες; Æol. πίσυρες; Goth. fidvor; Cambro-<BR>Brit. pedwar, pedair; Lat. quatuor; Lith. keturi;<BR>Slav. cetyrje; Hib. ceathair, ceteora; Zend cathru.]<BR>—चतुः-पञ्च, अस्, आ, अम्, four or five; also चतुः-<BR>पञ्चन्.<BR>—चतुःपञ्चाश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 54th.<BR>—चतुः-पञ्चाशत्, त्, f., 54.<BR>—चतुःपञ्चासद्-<BR>अधिक-शत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 154th.<BR>—चतुः-<BR>पत्त्री, f., N. of a plant, = क्षुद्र-पाषाण-भेदी.<BR>—चतुः-पर्णी, f. a kind of sorrel (क्षुद्राम्लिका).<BR>—चतुः-पार्श्व, अम्, n. the four sides of a square.<BR>—चतुः-पुण्ड्र, अस्, m., N. of a shrub, = भिण्डा.<BR>—चतुः-फला, f. Uraria Lagopodioides (= नाग-<BR>बला).<BR>—चतुः-शत, अम्, n., 104; 400.<BR>—चतुः-<BR>शत-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 104th.<BR>—चतुः-शाल, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-c" target="_blank">Page0313-c+ 81</a>]<BR>आ, अम्, having four halls; built in a square; (अम्,<BR>आ), n. f. or चतुः-शालक, अम्, n. a square of four<BR>houses; a quadrangle enclosed by four buildings.<BR>—च-<BR>तुः-शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, four-horned; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—चतुः-श्रोत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>four ears.<BR>—चतुःषष्ट, अस्, ई, अम्, the 64th;<BR>having 64 added.<BR>—चतुः-षष्टि, इस्, f., 64; a N.<BR>for the Ṛg-veda which consists of 64 Adhyāyas;<BR>the 64 arts [cf. कला].<BR>—चतुःषष्टि-तम, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, the 64th.<BR>—चतुः-सन, अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>taining the four sons of Brahmā, whose names begin<BR>with Sana (सनक, सनन्द, सनातन, सनत्कु-<BR>मार).<BR>—चतुःसप्तत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 74th.<BR>—चतुः-सप्तति, इस्, f., 74.<BR>—चतुःसप्तति-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 74th.<BR>—चतुः-सम, अम्, n. an<BR>unguent of four ingredients, sandal, agallochum,<BR>saffron, and musk; (अस्, आ, अम्), one whose body<BR>has four smooth places.<BR>—चतुः-सहस्र, अम्, n.,<BR>1004; 4000.<BR>—चतुः-सीमा, f. a border or boun-<BR>dary on all four sides.<BR>—चतुः-स्रक्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>quadrangular.<BR>—चतुर्-अंश, अस्, m. a fourth part.<BR>—चतुर्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having four eyes.<BR>—चतुर्-अक्षर, अम्, n. an aggregate or com-<BR>bination of four syllables; (अस्, आ, अम्), consisting of<BR>four syllables.<BR>—चतुर्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting<BR>of four members, quadripartite; (चतुर्-अङ्गम्<BR>बलम्, an entire or complete army, comprising<BR>elephants, chariots, cavalry, and infantry); (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Loma-pāda or Roma-pāda; the plant<BR>Cucumis Utilissimus [cf. घोटिका]; (आ), f., scil.<BR>सेना, an entire army &c.; (अम्), n. an entire army<BR>&c.; a sort of chess.<BR>—चतुरङ्ग-बल, अम्, n. an<BR>entire army &c.; [cf. the preceding.]<BR>—चतुरङ्ग-<BR>बलाध्यक्ष (˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, m. the commander-<BR>in-chief of a complete army.<BR>—चतुरङ्ग-सैन्य,<BR>अम्, n. an entire army; [cf. चतुर्-अङ्ग.]<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>अङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having four parts or members,<BR>quadripartite; (इणी), f. a complete army.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>अङ्गुल, अम्, n. the four fingers of the hand (with-<BR>out the thumb); four fingers broad, four inches;<BR>(अस्), m. the plant Cathartocarpus Fistula.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>अध्यायिका, अम्, f. n. a collection of four Adhyāyas.<BR>—चतुर्-अनीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having four faces,<BR>facing the four quarters.<BR>—चतुर्-अनुगान, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Sāman.<BR>—चतुर्-अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bordered on all<BR>four sides; (आ), f. the earth.<BR>—चतुरन्तेश (˚ता-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. lord of the earth, a king.<BR>—चतुर्-अवत्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (see अव-दो), divided into four parts;<BR>(अम्), n. division into four parts.<BR>—चतुर्-अवत्तिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ (see अव-दो), one who is accustomed to<BR>offer the havis in four portions.<BR>—चतुरशीत, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, the 84th.<BR>—चतुर्-अशीति, इस्, f., 84.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>अशीति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 84th.<BR>—चतुर्-अश्र or<BR>चतुर्-अस्र or चतुर्-अस्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, four-<BR>cornered, quadrangular; regular; (अस्), m. a quadran-<BR>gular figure; a square; (in astronomy) N. of the<BR>fourth and eighth lunar mansions; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>various Ketus.<BR>—चतुर्-अश्व, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—चतुर्-अस्रक, अस्, m., N. of various postures in<BR>acting; see चतुर्-अश्र.<BR>—चतुर्-अह, अम्, n. a period<BR>of four days; (अस्), m. a Soma sacrifice lasting four days;<BR>[cf. अत्रि-चतुर्-अह.]<BR>—चतुर्-आत्मन्, आ, आ, अ, re-<BR>presenting four persons; having four faces.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>आनन, अस्, आ, अम्, having four faces; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—चतुर्-आनर्तन, अम्, n. a<BR>dance by four, or in four divisions.<BR>—चतुर्-इडस्-<BR>पद-स्तोभ, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>उत्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, increasing by four.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>उषण, अम्, n. the four hot spices, black pepper,<BR>long pepper, dry ginger, and the root of long pepper;<BR>[cf. त्र्य्-ऊषण and चतुर्-जातक.]<BR>—चतुर्-गति,<BR>इस्, m. a tortoise (going on four feet).<BR>—चतुर्-गर,<BR>अम्, n. a carriage drawn by four oxen.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, four times, four-fold, quadruple.<BR>—चतुर्-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken up (or ladled<BR>out, as a fluid) four times; (अम्), n. taking up (any<BR>fluid) four times.<BR>—चतुर्-ग्राम, अस् or अम् (?),<BR>m. or n. (?), N. of a country.<BR>—चतुर्-जातक, अम्,<BR>n. = चातुर्जातक, = कटु-चातुर्जातक, q. v.<BR>—च-<BR>तुर्णवत, अस्, ई, अम्, with 94 added (e. g. चतुर्-<BR>णवतं शतम् = 194); [cf. चतुर्-नवत.]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-a" target="_blank">Page0314-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—चतुर्-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m. ‘having four tusks;’ N. of<BR>Viṣṇu; of one of the attendants of Skanda; of a<BR>Dānava.<BR>—चतुर्-दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, four-toothed.<BR>—चतुर्-दन्त, अस्, m. ‘having four tusks,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Airāvata, the elephant of Indra; N. of an ele-<BR>phant mentioned in the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—चतुर्दश,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the fourteenth; consisting of fourteen; (ई),<BR>f., scil. रात्रि, the fourteenth day in a lunar fortnight.<BR>—चतुर्दश-धा, ind. fourteen-fold.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>दशन्, अ, pl. fourteen; [cf. Lat. quatuordecim;<BR>Lith. keturôlika.]<BR>—चतुर्दशम, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>fourteenth.<BR>—चतुर्दश-मत-विवेक, अस्, m. title<BR>of a work by Śaṅkara.<BR>—चतुर्दशिक, अस् or अम्,<BR>m. or n. (?), a feast on the fourteenth day of a lunar<BR>fortnight.<BR>—चतुर्-दारिक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of the fifth Lambaka in the Kathā-sarit-sāgara.<BR>—चतुर्-दिक्षु or चतुर्-दिशम्, ind. towards the<BR>four quarters, on all sides, all around.<BR>—चतुर्-दोल,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a royal litter.<BR>—चतुर्-द्वीप-चक्र-<BR>वर्तिन्, ई, m. the sovereign of the four Dvīpas.<BR>—चतुर्-धा, ind. in four parts, four-fold; [cf. Hib.<BR>ceathardha; Gr. τέτραχα.]<BR>—चतुर्धा-भू, cl. 1.<BR>P. -भवति, -वितुम्, to be divided into four parts.<BR>—चतुर्धा-शान्ति, इस्, f. a religious ceremony per-<BR>formed at the time of making the stated offerings to<BR>deceased ancestors.<BR>—चतुर्नवत, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>94th.<BR>—चतुर्-नवति, इस्, f., 94.<BR>—चतुर्नवति-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 94th.<BR>—चतुर्-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>four-armed; an epithet of Viṣṇu and Śiva; [cf. च-<BR>तुर्-भुज.]<BR>—चतुर्-भद्र, अम्, n. the aggregate of<BR>four objects of human wishes, viz. धर्म, virtue;<BR>काम, pleasure; अर्थ, wealth; and मोक्ष, final<BR>beatitude.<BR>—चतुर्-भाग, अस्, m. the fourth part, a<BR>quarter.<BR>—चतुर्-भुज, अम्, n. (generally in com-<BR>pounds), four arms; (अस्, आ, अम्), having four arms;<BR>quadrangular; (अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa; a square; N. of a Dānava; N. of the<BR>instructor of Rāmānanda; N. of the father of Śiva-<BR>datta.<BR>—चतुर्भुज-भट्टाचार्य (˚ट-आच्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author.<BR>—चतुर्-भूगस्, आन्, असी, अस्, con-<BR>taining four (syllables) more.<BR>—चतुर्-महाराज, आस्,<BR>m. pl. the four great kings or gods of the highest of<BR>the six Buddhist heavens.<BR>—चतुर्महाराज-कायिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the group of the four great<BR>kings; epithet of a class of deities with Buddhists;<BR>also चतुर्महाराजिक.<BR>—चतुर्-मास, अम्, n. a<BR>period of four months.<BR>—चतुर्-मुख, अम्, n. (in<BR>compounds), four faces; (अस्, ई, अम्), having four<BR>faces; (an arrow) having four points; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Brahmā, of Viṣṇu, Śiva, and of a Dānava;<BR>a preparation of mercury (?).<BR>—चतुर्मुख-रस,<BR>अस्, m. a preparation of great curative power.<BR>—च-<BR>तुर्-युग, अम्, n. the aggregate of the four Yugas<BR>or ages of the world, a Mahā-yuga or 4,320,000<BR>years; (अस्, आ, अम्), drawn by four (oxen &c.);<BR>comprehending the four Yugas or ages of the world.<BR>—चतर्-युज्. क्, क्, क्, drawn by four (oxen &c.).<BR>—चतुर्-वक्त्र, अस्, m. ‘four-faced,’ N. of Brahmā;<BR>of a Dānava.<BR>—चतुर्-वय, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. four-fold.<BR>—चतुर्-वर्ग, अस्, m. a collection of four things,<BR>the four objects of human pursuit collectively; see<BR>चतुर्-भद्र.<BR>—चतुर्वर्ग-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m.<BR>title of a work.<BR>—चतुर्-वर्ण, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>the four classes or castes of Hindūs, viz. Brāhmans,<BR>Kṣatriyas, Vaiśyas, and Śūdras; four principal<BR>colours; four letters.<BR>—चतुर्वर्ण-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, consisting of the four castes.<BR>—चतुर्वर्ण्य,<BR>अम्, n. the system of the four castes.<BR>—चतुर्-वर्-<BR>षिका, f., scil. गो, a cow four years old.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>वाहिन्, ई, m., scil. रथ, a carriage drawn by four<BR>(horses &c.).<BR>—चतुर्विंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 24th;<BR>having 24 added (e. g. चतुर्विंशं शतम्, 124);<BR>consisting of 24; (अस्), m., N. of a Stoma; (अम्), n.,<BR>scil. अहन्, N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—चतुर्-विंशति, इस्, f.,<BR>24; the 24th year (e. g. आ-चतुर्विंशं शतम्, to the<BR>24th year); title of a work.<BR>—चतुर्विंशतिक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of 24.<BR>—चतुर्विंशति-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 24th.<BR>—चतुर्विंशति-मत, अम्, n.<BR>‘24 sects,’ title of a work.<BR>—चतुर्विंशतिमत-<BR>व्याख्या, f. a commentary by Bhaṭṭoji-dīkṣita.<BR>—चतुर्विंशत्य्-अवतार-चरित्र, अम्, n. ‘history<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-b" target="_blank">Page0314-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of 24 incarnations’ by Narahara-dāsa.<BR>—चतुर्विंशा-<BR>क्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, containing 24 syllables.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, familiar with the four Vedas; (अस्),<BR>m. one who has studied the four Vedas.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>विध, अस्, आ, अम्, four-fold; of four sorts or kinds,<BR>in four ways.<BR>—चतुर्-वीज, अम्, n. the four kinds of<BR>seed, i. e. the seed of Kālājājī, Candra-śūra, Me-<BR>thikā, and Yavānikā.<BR>—चतुर्-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. an epithet applied to a particular unguent; also<BR>to a Soma sacrifice which lasts four days.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>वेद, आस्, m. pl., the four Vedas, viz. the Ṛg-veda,<BR>Yajur-veda, Sāma-veda, and Atharva-veda; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), containing the four Vedas; familiar with the<BR>four Vedas; (आस्), m. pl. a class of manes.<BR>—चतुर्-<BR>वेदिन्, ई, इणी, इ, familiar with the four Vedas.<BR>—चतुर्-व्यूह, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; [cf.<BR>नव-व्यूह.]<BR>—चतुर्-हनु, उस्, m. ‘having four<BR>jaws,’ N. of a Dānava.<BR>—चतुर्-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>four-armed.<BR>—चतुर्-हायण, अस्, ई, अम्, four years<BR>old; (ई), f. a cow of four years.<BR>—चतुर्-होतृ, ता<BR>or तारस्, m. sing. or plur., N. of a certain liturgical<BR>section of Vedic works intended for recitation; con-<BR>taining the four chief priests.<BR>—चतुर्-होत्र, अस्, m.<BR>comprehending the four chief priests.<BR>—चतुर्हो-<BR>त्रक, अम्, n. the four chief priests; the duties of<BR>these priests.<BR>—चतुश्चत्वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 44th;<BR>having 44 added; containing 44; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>Stoma.<BR>—चतुश्-चत्वारिंशत्, त्, f., 44.<BR>—चतुष्-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, four-eared; heard by four ears<BR>only; (ई), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attendant on<BR>Skanda.<BR>—चतुष्कर्ण-ता, f. the state of being<BR>heard by only four ears, a secret.<BR>—चतुष्-कोण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, square, quadrangular; (अस्), m. a quadrangular<BR>figure, a square, a tetragon.<BR>—चतु-ष्टोम, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. चतुर् and स्तोम), a Stoma consisting of four<BR>parts; (अस्, आ, अम्), connected with such a Stoma.<BR>—चतुष्-पथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. a place where four<BR>roads meet, a cross-way; (अस्), m. a Brāhman (so<BR>called from the four आश्रमास्, q. v.).<BR>—चतुष्पथ-<BR>निकेता or चतुष्पथ-रता, f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attendant on Skanda.<BR>—चतुष्-पद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having four feet; consisting of four Pādas;<BR>(in arithmetic or algebra) tetranomial; (अस्), m. an<BR>animal with four legs, a quadruped; (in astron.) a<BR>term for certain signs of the zodiac; N. of a par-<BR>ticular Karaṇa; a kind of coitus; N. of a shrub;<BR>(आ), f. a metre containing 30+4+4 syllabic instants;<BR>(अम्), n. a conjunction of four Pādas.<BR>—चतुष्प-<BR>दिका, f., N. of a metre containing 30 + 4 + 4 syllabic<BR>instants.<BR>—चतुष्-पाटी, f. a river (winding four<BR>ways ?).<BR>—चतुष्-पाठी, f. a school for Brāhmans<BR>in which the four Vedas are repeated.<BR>—चतुष्-पाणि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, four-handed; (इस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—चतुष्-पाद्, -पात्, -पदी, -पत्, quadruped; hav-<BR>ing made four steps; consisting of four members,<BR>divided into four parts, consisting of four parts;<BR>(-पात्), m. a quadruped; anything which has four<BR>parts or members; a judicial procedure, consisting of<BR>four processes, plea, defence, rejoinder, and sentence;<BR>(-पदी), f. a female quadruped; (-पत्), n. the quadru-<BR>peds collectively, the animals.<BR>—चतुष्-पाद, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, quadruped; divided into four parts, consisting<BR>of four parts; (अस्), m. a quadruped.<BR>—चतुष्-<BR>पार्श्व, अम्, n. the four sides of anything.<BR>—चतु-<BR>स्तन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चतुः-स्तन), having four<BR>nipples.<BR>—चतुस्त्रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 34th; having<BR>34 added; containing 34.<BR>—चतुस्त्रिंशज्-जातक-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, m. a Buddha.<BR>—चतुस्-त्रिंशत्, त्, f., 34.<BR>—चतुस्-सम, see चतुः-सम.<BR>—चतू-राजी, f.<BR>(fr. चतुर् + राजन्), the four kings; N. of the<BR>luckiest or most desired termination of the game<BR>called Caturaṅga, by which one king gains the four<BR>thrones.<BR>—चतू-रात्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चतुर् + रात्र),<BR>lasting four days (lit. nights); (अस् or अम्), m. n., N.<BR>of a certain ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर|चतुरः
1. चतुर, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of some com-<BR>pounds) = चतुर्, four; see अ-च्˚, उप-च्˚, त्रि-च्˚.<BR>(For 2. चतुर see next col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थ|चतुर्थः
चतुर्थ, अस्, ई, अम्, fourth, the fourth; (अस्), m.<BR>the fourth letter in every class of consonants, i. e. घ्,<BR>झ्, ढ्, ध्, भ्; (ई), f., scil. रात्रि, the fourth day<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">Page0314-c+ 77</a>]<BR>in a lunar fortnight; (scil. विभक्ति), the termination<BR>of the fourth case, the fourth case, the dative case;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), constituting the fourth part; (अम्), n.<BR>a quarter; [cf. Lith. ketwirtas; Slav. cetvertyi,<BR>cetvertaja; Gr. τέταρος; Lat. quartus; Goth.<BR>fidvorda (?); Germ. vierter.]<BR>—चतुर्थ-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. the ceremonies performed on the fourth day of<BR>a marriage.<BR>—चतुर्थ-कालम्, ind. at the fourth<BR>meal, at the evening of every second day of a person's<BR>fasting.<BR>—चतुर्थकालिक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who passes<BR>three meals without eating and partakes only of the<BR>fourth.<BR>—चतुर्थ-फल, अम्, n. the second in-<BR>equality or equation of a planet.<BR>—चतुर्थ-भक्त,<BR>अम्, n. consuming the fourth meal (after having passed<BR>three without eating).<BR>—चतुर्थ-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, re-<BR>ceiving the fourth part as a toll from one's subjects (as<BR>a king).<BR>—चतुर्थ-स्वर, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—चतुर्थांश (˚थ-अं˚), अस्, m. a quarter, a<BR>fourth part; (अस्, आ, अम्), receiving a quarter.<BR>—च-<BR>तुर्थाश्रम (˚थ-आश्˚), अस्, m. the fourth order<BR>of a Brāhman's life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थक|चतुर्थकः
चतुर्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, the fourth; returning or<BR>repeated every four days as a fever, quartan; (इका),<BR>f. a weight equal to four Karṣas or one Pāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्य
चतुर्य, nom. P. चतुर्यति, to wish for four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्क|चतुष्कं
चतुष्क, अस्, आ, अम्, four, consisting of four,<BR>increased by four (e. g. चतुष्कं शतम् = 104<BR>or four per cent; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (ई), f. a<BR>large four-sided pond or tank; a bed or musquito-<BR>curtain; (अम्), n. the number four; a collection of<BR>four; a cross-way; a quadrangular court-yard [cf.<BR>चत्वर]; a hall resting on four columns; a neck-<BR>lace of four strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्किका
चतुष्किका, f. the number four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्किन्
चतुष्किन्, ई, इणी, इ, having four (parts &c.) of<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्टय|चतुष्टयं
चतुष्टय, अस्, ई, अम्, four-fold, consisting of<BR>four; (अम्), n. the number four, a collection of four,<BR>an aggregate of four, a quaternion; a square; a<BR>collection of Sūtras consisting of four sections; the<BR>first, fourth, seventh, and tenth signs of the zodiac;<BR>the centre of a circle.<BR>—चतुष्टय-समास, आस्,<BR>m. pl. four classes of compounds, viz. Avyayī-bhāva,<BR>Tat-puruṣa, Dvandva, and Bahu-vrīhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुस्
चतुस्, ind. four times; [cf. Zend cathrus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वर|चत्वरं
चत्वर, अम्, n. a quadrangular place or court-<BR>yard, a place in which many ways meet; a levelled<BR>spot of ground prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>—चत्वर-<BR>वासिनी, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attendant on<BR>Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वारिंश
चत्वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the next), the 40th;<BR>having 40 added; consisting of 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वारिंशत्
चत्वारिंशत्, त्, f. (said to be fr. चत्वारि, n. pl.<BR>+ दशत्, a decad), 40; [cf. Lat. quadraginta;<BR>Gr. τεσσαράκοντα.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वारिंशति
चत्वारिंशति, इस्, f. = the preceding (in द्वा-चत्वा-<BR>रिंशति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर|चतुरः
चतुर 2. चतुर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr.<BR>rt. चत्; for 1. see under चतुर् above), swift, quick;<BR>dexterous, clever, skilful, ingenious; charming, agree-<BR>able; visible, perceptible; (अस्), m. a round pillow,<BR>one for the cheek; (अम्), n. skilfulness, cleverness;<BR>an elephant's stable; [cf. चातुर.]<BR>—चतुर-ता, f.<BR>cleverness, skilfulness, cunningness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरक
चतुरक, अस्, m., N. of a jackal; (इका), f., N.<BR>of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थ|चतुर्थः
चतुर्थ चतुर्थ. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुल|चतुलः
चतुल चतुल, अस्, आ, अम्, depositing, placing,<BR>fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वारिंशत्
चत्वारिंशत् चत्वारिंशत्. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वाल|चत्वालः
चत्वाल चत्वाल, अस्, m. a hole in the ground<BR>&c. prepared for an oblation with fire, or for the sacri-<BR>ficial fire; the womb; Kuśa grass; [cf. चात्वाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चद्
चद् चद्, cl. 1. P. A. चदति, -ते, to ask<BR>or beg, to solicit; [cf. चत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चदिर|चदिरः
चदिर चदिर, अस्, m. the moon; camphor;<BR>an elephant; a snake; [cf. चन्दिर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्
चन् 1. चन्, cl. 1. P. चनति, to sound,<BR>utter a sound; cl. 1. P. or Caus. चनति or<BR>चनयति, -यितुम्, to hurt, injure, wound, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्
चन् 2. चन् (related to rt. कन्, only found<BR>in the Ved. Aor. 2nd du. चनिष्टम्), to<BR>delight in anything, be satisfied with (with loc.), to<BR>love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चनस्
चनस्, अस्, n., Ved. delight, satisfaction; (Sāy.)<BR>food; (only found connected with rt. धा, in) चनो<BR>धा, to delight in, be satisfied with, to find anything<BR>acceptable or agreeable (with acc. or loc.), to enjoy;<BR>(Sāy.) to grant food.<BR>—चनो-धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>satisfied, gracious; (according to schol.) giving food.<BR>—चनो-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. made favourable or<BR>inclined to do anything, willing to do anything;<BR>(Sāy.) having food given to one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चनसित
चनसित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चनस्य below), Ved.<BR>delighted, satisfied, gracious.<BR>—चनसित-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. containing the word चनसित; agree-<BR>able (as speech or words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चनस्य
चनस्य, nom. P., Ved. चनस्यति, to delight in,<BR>be satisfied with; (Sāy.) to like; to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चनिष्ठ
चनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of rt. 2. चन्), Ved.<BR>very favourable, very gracious; very acceptable;<BR>(Sāy.) containing or granting much food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन
चन चन (originally for च+न), ind. and<BR>not, also not, even not, not even; even, also, and.<BR>This particle is placed after the word to which it<BR>gives force; and in Vedic Sanskrit is generally, but<BR>not always, found without any other negative particle,<BR>whereas in the later language another negative is<BR>usually added (e. g. आपश् चन प्र मिनन्ति व्रतं<BR>वाम्, not even the waters violate your ordinance;<BR>नाह विव्याच पृथिवी चनैनम्, the earth even<BR>does not contain him). When चन is added to the<BR>interrogatives क, कतर, कतम, कद्, किम्,<BR>कथम्, कदा, कुतस्, क्व, it makes them in-<BR>definite; see 2. क, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्|चंद्
चन्द् चन्द् (originally श्चन्द् ?), cl. 1. P.<BR>चन्दति, to shine, to be bright; to glad-<BR>den; (only the Ved. part. of the Intens. चनिश्चदत्<BR>seems to occur); [cf. Lat. candeo and candela.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द|चंद|चंदः|चन्दः
चन्द, अस्, m. the moon; N. of the author of<BR>the work Pṛthivī-rājarāsaka; [cf. चन्द्र below;<BR>cf. also Hib. canu, ‘full moon.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दक|चंदकः|चन्दकः
चन्दक, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, joy-inspiring; (अस्),<BR>m. the moon, moonlight; a small silvery fish of a<BR>genus allied to the Zeus or Chanda; (a various reading<BR>has चन्द्रक.)<BR>—चन्दक-पुष्प, अम्, n. cloves;<BR>(a wrong form for चन्दन-पुष्प.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दन|चंदन|चंदनं|चन्दनं|चंदनः|चन्दनः
चन्दन, अस्, अम्, m. n. sandal or Sirium Myrti-<BR>folium; either the tree, the wood, or the unctuous<BR>preparation of the wood held in high estimation as<BR>perfumes; anything which is the most excellent of<BR>its kind; (अम्), n. a kind of grass, = भद्र-काली;<BR>red sandal-wood; (अस्), m., N. of a divine being with<BR>Buddhists; of a prince; of an ape; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>plant [cf. चन्दन-गोपी and चन्दन-शारिवा]; N. of<BR>a river; (ई), f., N. of a river; [cf. कु-चन्दन, पीत-<BR>च्˚, रक्त-च्˚, श्वेत-च्˚, हरि-च्˚.]<BR>—चन्दन-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. the Malaya mountain, part of the southern<BR>range of the Ghaṭs, where sandal-wood is found.<BR>—चन्दन-गोपी, f. a kind of plant, = शारिवा-<BR>विशेष; [cf. चन्दना.]<BR>—चन्दन-दास, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—चन्दन-पाल, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—चन्दन-पुष्प, अम्, n. cloves.<BR>—चन्दन-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of sandal-wood.<BR>—चन्दन-वारि, इ, n. sandal-water.<BR>—चन्दन-<BR>शारिवा, f., N. of a plant, a kind of Śārivā.<BR>—चन्-<BR>दन-सार, अस्, m. the most excellent sandal-wood;<BR>a kind of alkali (वज्र-क्षार).<BR>—चन्दनाग्र<BR>(˚न-अग्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चन्दनाचल<BR>(˚न-अच्˚), अस्, m. or चन्दनाद्रि (˚न-अद्˚), इस्, m.<BR>= चन्दन-गिरि.<BR>—चन्दना-वती, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चन्दनोदक (˚न-उद्˚), अम्, n. sandal-water.<BR>—चन्दनोदक-दुन्दुभि, इस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Bhava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनक
चन्दनक, अस्, m., N. of a man mentioned in<BR>the Mṛcchakaṭika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनिन्|चंदनिन्
चन्दनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, rubbed with or smelling of<BR>sandal-wood, imbued with sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनीया|चंदनीया
चन्दनीया, f. a kind of yellow pigment; [cf.<BR>गो-रोचना.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दला
चन्दला, f., N. of a woman; [cf. चन्द्रला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दिर|चंदिर|चंदिरः|चन्दिरः
चन्दिर, अस्, m. the moon; an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्र|चंद्र|चन्द्रं|चन्द्रः
चन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम् (originally श्चन्द्र; cf. अश्व-<BR>श्चन्द्र, पुरु-श्च्˚, &c.), Ved. glittering, shining<BR>(as gold), having the brilliancy or hue of light;<BR>(अस्), m. the moon (regarded as a planet), the moon<BR>personified or regarded as a deity; any eminent or<BR>illustrious person (at end of comp., e. g. पुरुष-<BR>चन्द्र, a moon of men, an excellent or eminent<BR>man, the moon being regarded as the most beautiful<BR>of the planets); a lovely or agreeable phenomenon<BR>of any kind, anything which gives pleasure; a spot<BR>similar to the moon; the eye in a peacock's tail;<BR>the symbol or mark of the Visarga; gold; a reddish<BR>kind of pearl; water; camphor; a particular plant,<BR>= काम्पिल्ल; N. of a metre consisting of four lines<BR>of nineteen syllables each; N. of a Daitya, = Can-<BR>dra-varman, king of the Kāmbojas; also of a son<BR>of Viśva-gandhi and father of Yuvanāśva; N. of a<BR>grammarian; of a king; of one of the ancestors of<BR>the Gauḍa Brāhmans, and of several other men; one<BR>of the eighteen minor Dvīpas or divisions of the<BR>known continent; N. of one of the principal branches<BR>of the river Candra-bhāgā; N. of a mountain; (आ),<BR>f. a hall covered only at the top; an awning, a<BR>canopy; small cardamoms; Cocculus Cordifolius, =<BR>गुडूची; (ई), f. Serratula Anthelmintica, = वाकुची;<BR>(अम्), n. gold; a kind of sour rice-gruel, = चुक्र;<BR>N. of a Sāman; [cf. अर्ध-चन्द्र.]<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>कला, f. a digit or one-sixteenth of the moon's disc,<BR>(each digit is personified as a female divinity, and<BR>worshipped in Tantrika ceremonies); the crescent<BR>before or after the new moon; a kind of fish, =<BR>वाचा or बाचा, Pimelodus Vacha; title of a drama.<BR>—चन्द्र-कवि, इस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>काटुकि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चन्द्र-कान्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, lovely as the moon; (अस्), m. a fabulous<BR>gem, the moon-stone, supposed to be formed from the<BR>congelation of the rays of the moon and to dissolve<BR>under the influence of its light; a kind of crystal or<BR>jasper may perhaps be meant; (अम्, अस्), n. m. the<BR>white eatable water-lily, blossoming during the night;<BR>(अम्), n. sandal-wood; (आ), f. the wife of the moon;<BR>the night.<BR>—चन्द्र-कान्ति, इस्, f. the brilliancy or lus-<BR>tre of the moon, moonlight.<BR>—चन्द्र-कालानल (˚ल-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. a kind of diagram.<BR>—चन्द्र-कीर्त्ति, इस्,<BR>m., N. of an author.<BR>—चन्द्र-कुल, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a town.<BR>—चन्द्र-कुल्या, f., N. of a river in Kaś-<BR>mīra.<BR>—चन्द्र-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a man; also of<BR>a son of Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—चन्द्र-कोष, अस्, m. title<BR>of a lexicon.<BR>—चन्द्र-गर्भ, अस्, m. title of a<BR>Buddhist Sūtra work.<BR>—चन्द्र-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of<BR>a mountain; also of a prince.<BR>—चन्द्र-गुप्त, अस्,<BR>m. ‘moon-protected,’ N. of a renowned king, the<BR>Σανδο-κυπτος or Σανδρο-κοττος of the Greeks, who<BR>is supposed to have reigned at Pāṭali-putra, or the mo-<BR>dern Patna, about 315 B. C., (he was installed by the<BR>Brāhman Cāṇakya after causing the death of Nanda,<BR>and was the founder of a new dynasty); N. of two kings<BR>of the Gupta dynasty; the registrar of Yama's court<BR>(in the latter sense a wrong form for चित्र-गुप्त).<BR>—चन्द्र-गोमिन्, ई, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR>—चन्-<BR>द्र-गोल, अस्, m. the lunar orb or sphere.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>गोल-स्थ, अस्, m. ‘dwelling in the lunar sphere,’ a<BR>deceased progenitor, the manes.<BR>—चन्द्र-गोलिका, f.<BR>moonlight.<BR>—चन्द्र-ग्रहण, अम्, n. an eclipse<BR>of the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-चञ्चल, अस्, आ, m. f. a<BR>small fish called Chanda, = चन्द्रक.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>चूड, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva (whose diadem is a<BR>crescent), [cf. चन्द्र-मौलि, चन्द्र-शेखर, &c.];<BR>N. of an author.<BR>—चन्द्र-चूडामणि, इस्, m. title<BR>of a literary work.<BR>—चन्द्र-चूडाष्टक (˚ड-<BR>अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of a hymn.<BR>—चन्द्र-ज, अस्, m.<BR>the son of the moon, an epithet of Budha (Mercury).<BR>—चन्द्र-तापन, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—चन्द्र-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. offering<BR>anything bright (as gold &c.) in sacrifice.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-c" target="_blank">Page0315-c+ 81</a>]<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—चन्द्र-दार,<BR>आस्, m. pl. the twenty-seven lunar mansions, which,<BR>in mythology, are so many nymphs, daughters of<BR>Dakṣa, and wedded to Candra or the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-देव, अस्, m., N. of a warrior; N. of<BR>a Brāhman of Kaśyapa's family; N. of a poet.<BR>—चन्द्र-द्युति, इस्, m. sandal-wood; [cf. चन्द-<BR>न.]<BR>—चन्द्र-ध्वज-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a Samā-<BR>dhi.<BR>—चन्द्र-नाभ, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—चन्द्र-निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like the moon, bright,<BR>handsome.<BR>—चन्द्र-निर्णिज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. one who<BR>has a brilliant garment or appearance; (Sāy.) having<BR>a shape like the moon or whose form causes delight.<BR>—चन्द्र-पञ्चङ्ग, अम्, n. the luni-solar calendar.<BR>—चन्द्र-पाद, अस्, m. a moon-beam. a ray of the<BR>moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son of the moon,’<BR>a N. of Budha or Mercury.<BR>—चन्द्र-पुर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a town; [cf. चान्द्रपुर.]<BR>—चन्द्र-पुष्पा,<BR>f. a kind of solanum; [cf. श्वेत-कण्टकारी.]<BR>—चन्द्र-प्रकाश, अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—चन्-<BR>द्र-प्रभ, अस्, m., N. of the Arhat of the present<BR>Ava-sarpiṇī; N. of a king; N. of several persons;<BR>(आ), f. moonlight; the plant Serratula Anthelmintica,<BR>= वाकुची; a compound of various drugs used in<BR>jaundice, piles, &c.; N. of a woman.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, splendid as the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-प्रभास्वर-राज, अस्, m., N. of several<BR>Buddhas.<BR>—चन्द्र-प्रिय, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—चन्द्र-बाला, f. large cardamoms.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>बाहु, उस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—चन्द्र-बुध्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a bright standing-ground;<BR>(Sāy.) the ground or cause of joy to all creatures.<BR>—चन्द्र-भ, अस्, m., N. of an attendant of<BR>Skanda.<BR>—चन्द्र-भागा, f., N. of a river, the<BR>Chenab, one of the five streams of the Pañjāb.<BR>—चन्द्र-भास, अस्, m. a sword; [cf. चन्द्र-<BR>हास.]<BR>—चन्द्र-भूति, इ, n. silver.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. = चन्द्र-कान्त, the moon-gem.<BR>—चन्द्र-मण्डल, अम्, n. the orb or disc of<BR>the moon; the lunar sphere; a halo round the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-मनस्, आस्, m., N. of one of the ten<BR>horses of the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-मस्, आस्, m. (fr.<BR>चन्द्र+मस्, derived fr. rt. मा), the moon, the<BR>deity of the moon; a month.<BR>—चन्द्र-मा, f., N.<BR>of a river.<BR>—चन्द्र-माला, f., N. of a metre; N.<BR>of a river.<BR>—चन्द्र-मुख, अस्, m. ‘moon-faced,’<BR>N. of a man; (ई), f. a metre consisting of four lines<BR>of ten syllables each; a lovely woman, whose face is<BR>fair as the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-मौलि, इस्, m. ‘moon-<BR>crested,’ an epithet of Śiva, (this deity being repre-<BR>sented with a crescent on his forehead); [cf. चन्द्र-<BR>चूड]<BR>—चन्द्र-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a<BR>brilliant carriage.<BR>—चन्द्र-राज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>minister of king Harṣa.<BR>—चन्द्र-रेखा, f. a digit<BR>of the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-रेणु, उस्, m. a plagiarist, a<BR>poetical thief (who has only the dust of the moon).<BR>—चन्द्र-लेख, अस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa; (आ),<BR>f. a digit of the moon; the plant Serratula Anthel-<BR>mintica, = वाकुची; N. of a metre consisting of four<BR>lines of thirteen syllables each; N. of another metre<BR>of four lines of fifteen syllables each; N. of a daughter<BR>of the Nāga Su-śravas; also of the wife of Kṣema-<BR>gupta; N. of the daughter of king Vīra-siṃha, also<BR>called Śaśi-kalā.<BR>—चन्द्र-लोक, अम्, n. the sphere<BR>or heaven of the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-लोचन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Dānava.<BR>—चन्द्र-लोहक or चन्द्र-लौह<BR>or चन्द्र-लौहक, अम्, n. silver.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>वंश, अस्, m. the race of the moon, the lunar race<BR>of kings or the second great line of Kṣatriya or<BR>royal dynasties in India. (The progenitor of the<BR>lunar race of kings who reigned at ancient Delhi or<BR>Hāstina-pura was Soma the Moon, the child of the<BR>Ṛṣi Atri and father of Budha. The latter married<BR>Iḷā, daughter of the solar king Ikṣavāku, and had by<BR>her a son, Aila or Purūravas. This last had a son<BR>by Urvaśī, named Āyus, from whom came Nahuṣa,<BR>father of Yayāti. The latter had two sons, Puru and<BR>Yadu, from whom proceeded the two branches of the<BR>lunar line. In the line of Yadu was born Kṛṣṇa<BR>and Bala-rāma; in that of Puru came Dushyanta,<BR>the hero of the Śakuntalā and father of the great<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-a" target="_blank">Page0316-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Bharata. Ninth from Bharata came Kuru, and<BR>fourteenth from him Śāntanu, who had a son<BR>Vicitra-vīrya and a step-son Vyāsa. The latter<BR>married the two widows of his half-brother, and had<BR>by them Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and Pāṇḍu, the wars of<BR>whose sons form the subject of the Mahā-bhārata);<BR>[cf. सूर्य-वंश.]<BR>—चन्द्रवंशिन्, ई, m. one of<BR>the lunar dynasty.<BR>—चन्द्र-वक्त्रा, f., N. of a<BR>town.<BR>—चन्द्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. brilliant,<BR>golden, abounding in gold; illuminated by the moon;<BR>(ती), f., N. of a daughter of Su-nābha and wife of<BR>Gada; N. of a princess; the wife of a potter; N. of<BR>a town or district.<BR>—चन्द्र-वत्स, आस्, m., N. of<BR>a people.<BR>—चन्द्र-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, moon-<BR>faced, having a face fair as the moon.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of brilliant or bright colour.<BR>—चन्द्र-वर्त्मन्, अ, n., N. of a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of twelve syllables each.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a king of the Kāmbojas; also<BR>of a prince conquered by Samudra-gupta.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>वल्लरी, f. a kind of Asclepias, = सोम-वल्लरी or<BR>ब्रह्मी-शाक.<BR>—चन्द्र-वल्ली, f., N. of several<BR>plants, = प्र-सारणी, माधवी, and सोम-लता.<BR>—चन्द्र-वसा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चन्द्र-विन्दु,<BR>उस्, m. the sign for the nasal Z.<BR>—चन्द्र-विमल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Samādhi (pure as the moon).<BR>—चन्द्र-विमल-सूर्य-प्रभास-श्री, ईस्, m., N.<BR>of a Buddha (the beauty of whom is spotless like the<BR>moon and brilliant as the sun).<BR>—चन्द्र-विहङ्-<BR>गम, अस्, m. a kind of crane, Ardea Nivea.<BR>—चन्द्र-व्रत, अम्, n. a kind of vow or penance<BR>[cf. चान्द्रायण]; a regal property or virtue.<BR>—चन्द्र-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—चन्-<BR>द्र-शाला, f. an upper room, an apartment on the<BR>house-top; moonlight.<BR>—चन्द्र-शालिका, f. a room<BR>on the top of a house.<BR>—चन्द्र-शिला, f. a kind of<BR>gem, moon-stone [cf. चन्द्र-कान्त]; N. of one of<BR>the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—चन्द्र-शुक्ल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the eight Upa-dvīpas in Jambu-<BR>dvīpa.<BR>—चन्द्र-शूर, अम्, n. a kind of fruit, =<BR>चन्द्रिका, कारवी, &c., commonly हालिम्, Lepidium<BR>Sativum.<BR>—चन्द्र-शेखर, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva [cf. चन्द्र-मौलि]; N. of a prince whose<BR>minister was the father of Viśva-nātha, the author<BR>of the Sāhitya-darpaṇa; or N. of that minister; N.<BR>of a commentator on Kālidāsa's Śakuntalā (perhaps<BR>identical with the minister of the same name); N. of<BR>the author of the play Madhurā-niruddha; N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—चन्द्रशेखर-चम्पू-प्रबन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—चन्द्र-श्री, ईस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince.<BR>—चन्द्र-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, m. ‘having any name<BR>of the moon,’ camphor.<BR>—चन्द्र-सम्भव, अस्,<BR>m. son of the moon, i. e. Budha, the planet Mercury;<BR>(आ), f. small cardamoms.<BR>—चन्द्र-सरस्, अस्, n.<BR>‘moon-lake,’ N. of a lake.<BR>—चन्द्र-सालोक्य, अम्, n.<BR>attainment of the lunar heaven.<BR>—चन्द्र-सिंह, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king, son of Darpa-nārāyaṇa.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. = चन्द्र-ज.<BR>—चन्द्र-सुरस, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Vitex Negundo.<BR>—चन्द्र-सूर्य, औ,<BR>m. du. moon and sun.<BR>—चन्द्र-सूर्य-जिह्मीकर-<BR>प्रभ, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha (whose splendor<BR>obscures moon and sun).<BR>—चन्द्र-सूर्य-प्रदीप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddha (illuminating moon and<BR>sun).<BR>—चन्द्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a prince, son<BR>of Samudra-sena.<BR>—चन्द्र-हन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>Dānava.<BR>—चन्द्र-हनु, उस्, and चन्द्र-हन्तृ,<BR>ता, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—चन्द्र-हास, अस्, m. a<BR>glittering scimitar [‘deriding the moon;’ cf. चन्द्र-<BR>भास]; the sword of Rāvaṇa; N. of a prince; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Cocculus Cordifolius [cf. गुडूची]; (अम्), n.<BR>silver.<BR>—चन्द्राकर (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चन्द्राकृति (˚र-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, moon-shaped;<BR>like the moon (in roundness, &c.).<BR>—चन्द्राग्र (˚र-<BR>अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a brilliant beginning;<BR>(Sāy.) having joy or gold at the head or as the chief<BR>subject.<BR>—चन्द्राङ्गद (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of king Indra-sena.<BR>—चन्द्रातप (˚र-आत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. moonlight; an open hall, one only furnished with a<BR>roof; an awning.<BR>—चन्द्रात्मज (˚र-आत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the son of the moon, the planet Mercury.<BR>—चन्द्रा-<BR>नन (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, moon-faced; (अस्), m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">Page0316-b+ 78</a>]<BR>an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—चन्द्रापीड (˚र-आप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva; N. of a son of Janamejaya;<BR>of a king of Kaśmīra, the brother of Tārā-pīḍa; of<BR>a son of king Tārā-pīḍa.<BR>—चन्द्राभ-वक्त्र<BR>(˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, whose face is moon-like.<BR>—चन्द्राभास (˚र-आभ्˚), अस्, m. a false moon,<BR>an appearance in the sky like the real moon.<BR>—चन्द्रार्क (˚र-अर्˚), औ, m. du. moon and sun;<BR>(ई), f. title of an astronomical work by Dina-kara.<BR>—चन्द्रार्क-दीप, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha, =<BR>चन्द्र-सूर्य-प्रदीप.<BR>—चन्द्रार्ध (˚र-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a half-moon.<BR>—चन्द्रार्ध-कृतशेखर,<BR>अस्, m. an ascetic who imitates the appearance of Śiva.<BR>—चन्द्रार्ध-चूदामणि, इस्, m. or चन्द्रार्ध-<BR>मौलि, इस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—चन्द्रालोक<BR>(˚र-आल्˚), अस्, m. title of a work on rhetoric by<BR>Jaya-deva.<BR>—चन्द्रावती, f., N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage; N. of the wife of king Dharma-sena.<BR>—चन्द्रावर्ता (˚र-आव्˚), f. a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of fifteen syllables each.<BR>—चन्द्रावली<BR>(˚र-आव्˚), f., N. of one of Kṛṣṇa's female com-<BR>panions.<BR>—चन्द्रावलोक (˚र-अव्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a prince.<BR>—चन्द्राश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Dhundhu-māra.<BR>—चन्द्रास्पदा (˚र-आस्˚), f.,<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>—चन्द्राह्वय (˚र-आह्˚), अस्, m.<BR>camphor.<BR>—चन्द्रेष्टा (˚र-इष्˚), f. an assemblage<BR>of lotuses blossoming during the night (lit. ‘loved<BR>by the moon’).<BR>—चन्द्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>moon-rise; an awning, a cloth or sheet spread over<BR>the large open courts of Hindū houses upon festive<BR>occasions; a mercurial preparation used in medicine;<BR>N. of a warrior on the side of the Pāṇḍavas; (आ), f.<BR>a medicine for the eyes.<BR>—चन्द्रोन्मीलन (˚र-<BR>उन्˚), अम्, n. title of a work.<BR>—चन्द्रोपल (˚र-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. the moon-gem; [cf. चन्द्र-कान्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रक|चंद्रक|चन्द्रकं|चंद्रकः|चन्द्रकः
चन्द्रक, अस्, m. the moon (generally at the end<BR>of adj. comp.); a spot similar to the moon; the eye<BR>in a peacock's tail; a finger-nail; a fish called Chanda;<BR>N. of a poet; of a minister; of an owl; (इका), f.<BR>moonlight, moonshine, illumination, elucidation (used<BR>at the end of the title of some commentaries and<BR>original works to imply that the work so designated<BR>is intended to elucidate the subject of which it<BR>treats, e. g. अलङ्कार-चन्द्रिका, कातन्त्र-च्˚,<BR>काव्य-च्˚, &c.; cf. कौमुदी, दीपिका, &c.); a kind<BR>of fish, = चन्द्रक; large or small cardamoms; N.<BR>of several plants, = कर्ण-स्फोटा, मल्लिका, श्वेत-<BR>कण्टकारी, मेथिका, चन्द्र-शूरा; N. of a metre,<BR>= उत्पलिनी; N. of a woman; N. of a river, =<BR>चन्द्र-भागा; (अम्), n. black pepper.<BR>—चन्द्र-<BR>क-वत्, आन्, m. a peacock.<BR>—चन्द्रिका-द्रव, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of gem, the moon-stone (melting in the<BR>moonlight).<BR>—चन्द्रिका-पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, drinking<BR>moonlight or the moon-beams; (ई), m. the bird<BR>Cakora.<BR>—चन्द्रिकाम्बुज (˚का-अम्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>white lotus, blossoming in the moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकित
चन्द्रकित, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with brilliant<BR>spots similar to the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकिन्|चंद्रकिन्
चन्द्रकिन्, ई, m. a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रट|चन्द्रटः
चन्द्रट, अस्, m., N. of an ancient physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमस्|चंद्रमस्
चन्द्र-मस्. See under चन्द्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रला
चन्द्रला, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्राय
चन्द्राय, nom. A. चन्द्रायते, to play the part<BR>of the moon, to represent the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिन्|चंद्रिन्
चन्द्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. golden, possessing gold;<BR>(ई), m. the son of the moon, the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिमा|चंद्रिमा
चन्द्रिमा, f. (fr. चन्द्र; cf. पूर्णिमा), moon-<BR>light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिल|चंद्रिल|चंद्रिलः|चन्द्रिलः
चन्द्रिल, अस्, m. a barber; a N. of Śiva; a pot-<BR>herb, Chenopodium Album.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमह|चंद्रमहः|चन्द्रमहः
चन्द्रमह चन्द्रमह, अस्, m. a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चप्
चप् चप्, cl. 1. P. चपति, to caress, coax,<BR>soothe, or console; cl. 10. P. चपयति, &c.,<BR>to grind, pound, knead; to cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपट|चपटः
चपट चपट, अस्, m. the palm with ex-<BR>tended fingers; [cf. चपेट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपल|चपलं|चपलः
चपल चपल, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>चुप्, connected with rt. कम्प्), moving to and fro,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">Page0316-c+ 79</a>]<BR>shaking, trembling, tremulous, unsteady, agitated,<BR>wavering; wanton, fickle, inconstant, variable; in-<BR>considerate, careless, thoughtless, ill-mannered, rude,<BR>impertinent; active, quick, swift, agile, expeditious;<BR>momentary, instantaneous; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>animal (= मूषिक); a fish; black mustard; quick-<BR>silver; a kind of perfume, = चोरक; a kind of<BR>stone; N. of a prince; also of a superhuman being;<BR>(आ), f. lightning; long pepper; the tongue; a dis-<BR>loyal wife, a whore; spirituous liquor, especially the<BR>intoxicating drink made from hemp; the goddess<BR>Lakṣmī or fortune; N. of two metres; one of the<BR>personifications of the fifth note in music.<BR>—चपल-<BR>ता, f. or चपल-त्व, अम्, n. trembling; fickleness,<BR>inconstancy, rudeness.<BR>—चपलताशय (˚ता-आश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. indigestion, flatulence.<BR>—चपलाङ्ग (˚ल-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. Delphinus Gangeticus.<BR>—चपला-जन,<BR>अस्, m. a fickle or unsteady woman; the goddess of<BR>fortune.<BR>—चपलात्मक (˚ल-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>a fickle or inconstant nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलक
चपलक, अस्, आ, अम्, wanton, fickle, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलाय
चपलाय, nom. A. चपलायते, to move to and<BR>fro, tremble, become unsteady, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेट|चपेटः
चपेट चपेट, अस्, m. a palm of the hand<BR>with the fingers extended; [cf. चपट and चर्पट.]<BR>—चपेटाघात (˚ट-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a blow or slap<BR>with the open hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेटिका
चपेटिका, f. a slap with the open hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चप्य
चप्य चप्य, अम्, n., Ved. a kind of sacrificial<BR>vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्
चम् चम्, cl. 1. P. चमति, चचाम, अच-<BR>मीत्, चमितुम्, Ved. cl. 5. P. चम्नोति, to<BR>sip, drink; to take anything into the mouth, as food,<BR>(generally applied to liquids, but occasionally used of<BR>solid food); to eat: Pass. Aor. अचमि (used im-<BR>personally): Caus. चामयति: Desid. चिचमिषति:<BR>Intens. चञ्चम्यते or चञ्चन्ति; [cf. Hib. toimhil,<BR>‘eatings;’ toimhlim, ‘I eat, waste, spend, consume.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमर|चमरं|चमरः
चमर, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. rt. चम्, in the sense of<BR>eating), a kind of deer, or rather the Bos Grunniens<BR>(erroneously classed by the Hindū writers amongst<BR>deer), highly valued for its bushy tail; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. a chowrie or long brush, most usually made of the<BR>tail of the Yak or Bos Grunniens, and employed to<BR>whisk off insects, flies, &c.; it is also one of the<BR>insignia of royalty [cf. चामर]; a particular high<BR>number; (अस्), m., N. of a Daitya; (ई), f. a com-<BR>pound pedicle.<BR>—चमर-पुच्छ, अम्, n. the tail<BR>of the Bos Grunniens; (अस्), m. a small animal with<BR>a bushy tail living in holes, a squirrel or perhaps<BR>fox (कोकड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमरिक|चमरिकः
चमरिक, अस्, m. a kind of ebony, Bauhinia<BR>Variegata, growing in clusters resembling a chowrie;<BR>[cf. कोविदार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमस|चमसं|चमसः
चमस, अस्, ई, m. f. a vessel used at sacrifices for<BR>drinking the juice of the Soma, a kind of flat dish,<BR>pan, or cup; (according to others) a kind of ladle or<BR>spoon, (according to the Brāhmaṇas and Scholiasts<BR>these vessels are generally of a square shape, made of<BR>wood and furnished with a handle, but sometimes<BR>also round or of other shapes); a cake made of<BR>barley, rice, or lentils, ground to meal: a sweetmeat,<BR>or flour, sesamum, &c., mixed up with sugar into a<BR>kind of cake; a plant, commonly Khetpāpara,<BR>Mollugo Pentaphylla; (अस्), m., N. of a man; also<BR>of a son of Ṛṣabha; = चमसोद्भेद, q. v.<BR>—च-<BR>मसाध्वर्यु (˚स-अध्˚), उस्, m., Ved. the priest<BR>who manages the drinking-vessels.<BR>—चमसोद्भेद<BR>(˚स-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a place of pilgrimage, held<BR>sacred on account of the supposed bursting forth of the<BR>river Sarasvatī; also चमसोद्भेदन, अम्, n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमसि|चमसिः
चमसि, इस्, f. = चमसी, a kind of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमसिन्
चमसिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमू
चमू, ऊस्, f., Ved. (loc. चमू or चम्वि; du.<BR>चम्वा; pl. चम्वस्), a vessel, a dish, (applied<BR>especially to the vessels or reservoirs into which the<BR>Soma is poured; these are generally two in number,<BR>and called चम्वा, Ved. du.), metaphorically the two<BR>grand receptacles of all living beings, or heaven and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">Page0317-a+ 77</a>]<BR>earth (चम्वौ, du., Naigh. III. 30); a grave; an<BR>army; a squadron, a division of an army consisting<BR>of 129 elephants, as many cars, 2187 horse, and<BR>3685 foot.<BR>—चमू-चर, अस्, m. a soldier, a warrior.<BR>—चमू-नाथ or चमू-प, अस्, m. the leader of<BR>an army, a general.<BR>—चमू-पति, इस्, m. a general<BR>of division, any general.<BR>—चमू-षद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>lying on a dish.<BR>—चमू-हर, अस्, m., N. of one of<BR>the Viśve-devās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमक
चमक चमक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमकसूक्त
चमकसूक्त चमक-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of several<BR>verses of the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā, so called because<BR>the words च मे are repeated in them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमीकार
चमी-कार, अस्, m. reciting the Camaka-sūkta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमीकृ
चमी-कृ, cl. 8. P., Ved. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>recite the verses containing the words च मे over<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्
चमत् चमत्, ind. an interjection of surprise.<BR>—चमत्-करण, अम्, n. admiration; astonishing,<BR>producing wonder, causing surprise; festival, spectacle;<BR>high poetical composition.<BR>—चमत्-कार, अस्, m.<BR>admiration, astonishment, surprise; show, spectacle;<BR>row, riot, festive or angry turbulence; elaborate<BR>style or high poetical composition; N. of the tree<BR>Achyranthes Aspera; [cf. अपामार्ग.]<BR>—चमत्-<BR>कार-चन्द्रिका, f. title of a grammar; title of a<BR>Bengālī poem by Kṛṣṇa-dāsa.<BR>—चमत्कार-चिन्ता-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—चमत्-कारित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, astonished.<BR>—चमत्-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, aston-<BR>ishing, surprising, unusual.<BR>—चमत्-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, astonished, surprised.<BR>—चमत्-कृति, इस्, f. ad-<BR>miration, astonishment, surprise, &c.; [cf. चमत्-<BR>कार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमीकृ
चमीकृ चमी-कृ. See under चमक-सूक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमू
चमू चमू. See under चम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूरु|चमूरुः
चमूरु चमूरु, उस्, m. a kind of deer; [cf.<BR>समूरु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्प्|चंप्
चम्प् चम्प्, cl. 10. P. चम्पयति, to go,<BR>move; (a various reading for छम्प्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्प|चंपः|चम्पः
चम्प, अस्, m. (said to come fr. the last rt.),<BR>the plant Bauhinia Variegata, mountain ebony [cf.<BR>कोविदार]; N. of a son of Pṛthulākṣa and founder<BR>of the town Campā; (आ), f., N. of a town in Aṅga,<BR>the modern Bhāgalpur or a place in its vicinity,<BR>founded by Campa, and the residence of Karṇa;<BR>also of Brahma-datta.<BR>—चम्प-करम्भा, f. a<BR>kind of plantain.<BR>—चम्प-कुन्द, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>fish, commonly चान्द-कुडा.<BR>—चम्प-कोष, अस्,<BR>m. the Jāka or bread-fruit tree.<BR>—चम्पाधिप (˚पा-<BR>अध्˚) or चम्पेश (˚पा-ईश), अस्, m., N. of Karṇa,<BR>natural brother of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>—चम्पा-वती, f., N. of<BR>a town; N. of the wife of Nidhi-pati.<BR>—चम्पोप-<BR>लक्षित (˚पा-उप्˚), अस्, m. the district of Campā<BR>or Bhāgalpur; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पक|चंपक|चम्पकं|चंपकः|चम्पकः
चम्पक, अस्, m. a tree bearing a yellow fragrant<BR>flower, Michelia Champaka; a kind of perfume; a<BR>variety of the jack or bread-fruit tree [cf. चम्पकालु];<BR>N. of the father of Kalhaṇa; N. of a man; N. of a<BR>country; (आ), f., N. of a town; (अम्), n. the flower<BR>of the Campaka tree; the fruit of a variety of the<BR>banana or plantain; commonly चाम्पाकला.<BR>—चम्-<BR>पक-गन्ध, अम्, n. a kind of incense.<BR>—चम्प-<BR>क-चतुर्दशी, f., N. of a festival, the fourteenth day<BR>in the light half of the month Jyaiṣṭha.<BR>—चम्पक-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—चम्पक-प्रभु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of the father of Kalhaṇa.<BR>—चम्पक-<BR>माला, f., N. of a metre consisting of four lines of<BR>ten syllables each.<BR>—चम्पक-वती, f., N. of a<BR>wood in Magadha.<BR>—चम्पकारण्य (˚क-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the Campaka forest; N. of a place of pil-<BR>grimage.<BR>—चम्पका-वती or चम्पकावली (˚क-<BR>आव्˚), f. = चम्पक-वती.<BR>—चम्पकोल्व (˚क-उल्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the Jāḳa or bread-fruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पकालु|चंपकालु|चंपकालुः|चम्पकालुः
चम्पकालु, उस्, m. the Jāka or Indian bread-fruit<BR>tree, Artocarpus Integrifolia; [cf. चम्पकोल्व, चम्-<BR>पालु, चम्पक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पालु|चंपालु|चंपालुः|चम्पालुः
चम्पालु, उस्, m. the Jāka or bread-fruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पू|चंपू
चम्पू चम्पू, ऊस्, f. a kind of elaborate<BR>and highly artificial composition in which the same<BR>subject is continued through alternations in prose and<BR>verse (गद्य and पद्य); [cf. गङ्गा-चम्पू and<BR>नल-चम्पू.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्ब्|चंब्
चम्ब् चम्ब्, cl. 1. P. चम्बति, &c., to go,<BR>to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्रिष्
चम्रिष् चम्रिष्, f., Ved. (Sāy.) libations<BR>(contained) in the sacrificial ladles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्रीष
चम्रीष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. contained in the<BR>sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय्
चय् चय्, cl. 1. A. चयते, &c., to go, go<BR>to or towards, move; [cf. Gr. κίω, κινέω;<BR>Lat. cieo, cio, citus; Hib. cai, ‘a way, a road;’<BR>Lith. koja, ‘foot;’ kettur-kojis, ‘quadruped.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
चय 1. चय. See under 1. चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
चय 2. चय. See under 3. चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्
चर् चर्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) चरति, -ते,<BR>चचार, चेरे, चरिष्यति, -ते, अचारीत्, चरि-<BR>तुम् (ep. चर्तुम्, Ved. चरध्यै, चरितवे, च-<BR>रसे), to move one's self, go, walk, move, stir, drive<BR>(in a carriage &c.), roam about, walk about, wander,<BR>(in these senses applied to men, animals, water, ships,<BR>stars, &c.); to graze; to spread, be diffused; to be<BR>active; move or travel through, pervade, go along,<BR>follow; to behave, conduct one's self; to live, be,<BR>remain in any position, act; to be engaged in,<BR>occupied with, busy one's self with (with inst., e. g.<BR>यज्ञेन चरति, he is engaged in a sacrifice); to<BR>undertake, set about, undergo, observe, practise, do<BR>or act in general (e. g. व्रतानि चेरुः, they observed<BR>vows; and in this sense applied rather vaguely to<BR>express various ideas, e. g. विघ्नं चरति, he puts<BR>a hindrance; भैक्षं चरति, he begs; विवादं<BR>चरति, he is engaged in a lawsuit; मृगयां<BR>चरति, he hunts; सम्बन्धांश् चरति, he enters<BR>into connections; मार्गं चचार वाणैः, he<BR>made a way with arrows); to continue performing<BR>or being (with a part., e. g. अर्चन्तश् चेरुः, they<BR>continued worshipping; स्वामिनम् अवज्ञाय चरेत्,<BR>he may go on despising his master); to exercise the<BR>body with penance, e. g. तपसा इन्द्रियाणि चरेत्,<BR>he should exercise his organs with penance; (with or<BR>without मिथुन) to perform the act of copula-<BR>tion, to have sexual intercourse with, have to do<BR>with; to make or render (with two acc., e. g. न-<BR>रेन्द्रं सत्य-स्थं चराम, let us make the<BR>king keep his word); to act as a spy; to consume,<BR>eat (e. g. मांसं चरेत्, let him eat flesh): Caus.<BR>चारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to move or walk about;<BR>to pasture; to send, direct, turn, move; to cause to<BR>pervade; to drive away; to cause to practise or per-<BR>form; to cause to copulate; to obtain knowledge of,<BR>acquaint one's self with (with acc.); to doubt [cf.<BR>वि-चर्]: Desid. चिचरिषति, to wish to act or con-<BR>duct one's self; to be willing to deal with, to have<BR>intercourse with: Intens. चर्चरीति, चञ्चूर्यते,<BR>चञ्चुरीति, चञ्चूर्ति, to move quickly or repeat-<BR>edly, to walk about, pervade; to act wantonly or<BR>coquettishly; [cf. Lat. curro, currus; properus (?):<BR>Hib. cara, ‘a leg or haunch;’ carachadh, ‘moving;’<BR>carachd, ‘motion:’ Gr. κύρω, κυρέω: Goth. fara:<BR>Germ. fahren: Old Germ. hor-sc: Eng. horse: Lith.<BR>kieláuju, kielias, kielione: Old Pers. cartanay.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर|चरः
चर, अस्, ई, अम्, moving, walking, going; loco-<BR>motive, any animal (so named as moving in contra-<BR>distinction to plants); movable, trembling, shaking,<BR>unsteady; (at the end of comp.) going, walking,<BR>wandering, being, living [cf. अधश्-चर, अन्त-<BR>चर, अप्-च्˚, उपरि-च्˚, एक-च्˚, &c.]; following;<BR>performing, practising (e. g. व्रत-चर, practising<BR>vows). Sometimes चर is placed at the end of a<BR>word as an affix in the sense of ‘having been formerly,’<BR>e. g. आढ्य-चर, one who has been rich formerly;<BR>देवदत्त-चर, having been formerly possessed by<BR>Devadatta; (अस्), m. a spy, a secret emissary or<BR>agent; a wagtail; a kind of small shell, Cypræa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-c" target="_blank">Page0317-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Moneta [cf. कपर्द]; a game played with dice and<BR>men similar to backgammon; the planet Mars; a<BR>cowrie; the seventh Karaṇa in astrology; the Karaṇas<BR>collectively; the difference of time between the rising<BR>of a heavenly body at Laṅkā or Ceylon, over which<BR>the first meridian passes, and that of its rising at any<BR>particular place; a term for particular lunar mansions<BR>and for a particular number of the signs of the zodiac.<BR>—चर-गृह, अम्, n. a moving or varying sign of<BR>the zodiac, i. e. the first, fourth, seventh, and tenth.<BR>—चर-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चर-द्रव्य,<BR>आणि, n. pl. movables, goods and chattels.<BR>—चर-<BR>पुष्ट, अस्, m. a mediator (lit. ‘nourished by a<BR>spy’).<BR>—चर-भ, अम्, n. a moving or varying<BR>sign of the zodiac, i. e. the first, fourth, seventh, and<BR>tenth; [cf. चर-गृह.]<BR>—चर-भवन, अम्, n.<BR>a moving or varying sign of the zodiac; [cf. the<BR>preceding.]<BR>—चर-मूर्ति, इस्, f. an idol which is<BR>carried about in procession.<BR>—१. चराचर (˚र-अच्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, movable and immovable, locomotive and<BR>stationary, moving and fixed (as animals and plants);<BR>(अम्), n. the aggregate of all created things, whether<BR>animate or inanimate; the world; sky, atmosphere;<BR>heaven, paradise; (ई), f. a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरक|चरकः
चरक, अस्, m. a wanderer, a wandering religious<BR>student; a spy or secret emissary; N. of a Muni and<BR>physician, (a legend relates that the serpent-king<BR>Śeṣa, who was himself the recipient of the Āyur-veda,<BR>once visited the earth, and finding it full of sickness and<BR>suffering became moved with pity, and determined<BR>to devise a scheme for alleviating disease; hence he<BR>became incarnate as the son of a Muni and was called<BR>Caraka because he had visited the earth as a kind of spy<BR>or चर; he then composed a new book on medicine,<BR>based on older works of Agni-veśa and other pupils<BR>of Ātreya, which book was called after him); a kind<BR>of plant, cf. पर्पट; (अम्), n. the title of the<BR>treatise on medicine written by Caraka; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a branch of the Black Yajur-veda, the practices<BR>and rites enjoined by which are different in some<BR>respects from those in the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa; (ई),<BR>f. a kind of poisonous fish; N. of an evil spirit.<BR>—चरक-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. Caraka's book.<BR>—च-<BR>रक-तन्त्र-व्याख्या, f. title of a commentary by<BR>Haricandra.<BR>—चरक-भाष्य, अम्, n. title of a<BR>commentary by an author named Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण|चरणं|चरणः
चरण, अस्, m. a foot soldier; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a<BR>foot; a pillar, a support, a prop; the root of a tree;<BR>a single line of a verse, the fourth part of a stanza;<BR>(in prosody) a dactyl; a sect, a school, a branch of<BR>the Vedas; a race, a family; (अम्), n. moving,<BR>going round or about, wandering, roaming, grazing;<BR>course; acting, dealing, managing, conduct, per-<BR>formance; fixed or instituted observances for any<BR>class, age, or condition (as priesthood, manhood,<BR>&c.); behaving, conduct of life, good or moral<BR>conduct; practising, accomplishing; consuming, eat-<BR>ing; a particular high number; [cf. द्वि-चरण,<BR>पुरश्-चरण, रथ-च्˚; cf. also Gr. and Lat.<BR>πέρνα, perna; Goth. fairzna; Germ. Ferse;<BR>Lith. kulnis; Hib. cairine; Lat. crus ?].<BR>—चर-<BR>ण-कमल or चरण-किशलय, अम्, n. a lotus-<BR>foot (lit. foot-lotus), a beautiful foot, the foot of a lover,<BR>of a deity, &c.<BR>—चरण-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen<BR>at one's feet, prostrate.<BR>—चरण-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m.<BR>the joint of the foot, the ancle.<BR>—चरण-दास, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the Guruśiṣya-saṃvāda<BR>and of the poems entitled Nāciketūpākhyāna.<BR>—चरण-न्यास, अस्, m. the trace of a foot, foot-<BR>step.<BR>—चरण-प, अस्, m. a tree.<BR>—चरण-पतन,<BR>अम्, n. falling at the feet, prostration.<BR>—चरण-<BR>पतित, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen at the feet, prostrate.<BR>—चरण-पद्म, अस् or अम्, m. n. a lotus (like)<BR>foot, the foot of a deity or lover.<BR>—चरण-पर्वन्,<BR>अ, n. ‘foot-joint,’ the ancle.<BR>—चरण-पात, अस्, m.<BR>tread, trampling; foot-fall.<BR>—चरण-युग, अम्, n.<BR>both the feet; two lines of a stanza.<BR>—चरण-<BR>व्यूह, अस्, m. title of a treatise.<BR>—चरण-शुश्रूषा,<BR>f. prostration.<BR>—चरण-सेवा, f. service, devotion.<BR>—चरणानमित (˚ण-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bent or<BR>bowed under the feet, trodden down.<BR>—चरणा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">Page0318-a+ 81</a>]<BR>भरण (˚ण-आभ्˚), अम्, n. an ornament for the<BR>feet.<BR>—चरणामृत (˚ण-अम्˚), अम्, n. foot-nectar,’<BR>the water in which the feet of a Brāhman or spiritual<BR>guide have been washed.<BR>—चरणायध (˚ण-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the feet for weapons; (अस्), m. a<BR>cock.<BR>—चरणारविन्द (˚ण-अर्˚), अम्, n. the lotus<BR>(like) foot (of a deity, lover, &c.).<BR>—चरणार्ध<BR>(˚ण-अर्˚), अम्, n. the half of the foot; half of the<BR>fourth of a stanza.<BR>—चरणास्कन्दन (˚ण-आस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. trampling, treading down with the feet.<BR>—च-<BR>रणोदक (˚ण-उद्˚), अम्, n. water in which the<BR>feet of a venerable Brāhman or spiritual teacher have<BR>been washed.<BR>—चरणोपग (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>in contact with the feet, at the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणीय
चरणीय, nom. A., Ved. चरणीयते, to follow,<BR>perform, be engaged in, carry on; (Sāy.) to desire<BR>to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण्य
1. चरण्य, nom. P. चरण्यति, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण्य
2. चरण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, foot-like, like a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण्यु
चरण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. moving, movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरत्
चरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going, moving, going on; pro-<BR>ceeding, acting, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरथ|चरथः
चरथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. moving, living; capable of<BR>moving, movable; (अस्, अम्), m. n. going, moving, wan-<BR>dering; movableness; liveliness, life; a going, a way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चराचर|चराचरं|चराचरः
2. चराचर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चर् reduplicated; for<BR>1. see P. 317, col. 3), moving locomotive, running;<BR>trembling, shaking, unsteady; wished, desired; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a small shell; [cf. कपर्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरि|चरिः
चरि, इस्, m. an animal in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित|चरितं
चरित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, gone to, attained, prac-<BR>tised; (अम्), n. going, moving, course; acting, doing,<BR>practice, behaviour, acts, deeds, practices, adventures,<BR>‘res gestæ;’ story; nature; fixed institute, proper or<BR>peculiar observance; [cf. उत्तर-राम-चरित, दुश्-<BR>चरित, सच्-च्˚, सह-च्, सु-च्˚.]<BR>—चरित-गुणत्व,<BR>अम्, n. (?) accompaniment, assistance; meritorious<BR>conduct.<BR>—चरित-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, (at the end of<BR>compounds) containing or relating deeds or adven-<BR>tures, made up of deeds.<BR>—चरित-व्रत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, performing an act of devotion.<BR>—चरितार्थ<BR>(˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attaining one's object, success-<BR>ful in an undertaking, satisfied, effected, successful.<BR>—चरितार्थ-त्व, अम्, n. the attainment of an aim,<BR>successfulness, success.<BR>—चरितार्थय, nom. P. चरि-<BR>तार्थयति, to cause a person to attain his aim.<BR>—च-<BR>रितार्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, desirous of success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितव्य
चरितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone, to be managed;<BR>to be followed or observed; to be practised or per-<BR>formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितिन्
चरितिन्. Cf. दुश्-चरितिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित्र|चरित्रं
चरित्र, अम्, n. a foot, leg; going; acting, behaving,<BR>behaviour, habit, practice, acts, deeds, proceedings,<BR>exploits; instituted and peculiar observance or con-<BR>duct; adventures, story, history or account of any<BR>one's deeds or exploits; nature, disposition; (आ), f.<BR>the tamarind tree; [cf. चारित्र.]<BR>—चरित्र-बन्-<BR>धक, अस्, m. a friendly pledge, one of unequal<BR>value to the loan.<BR>—चरित्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, expe-<BR>rienced, familiar with customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरिष्णु|चरिष्णुः
चरिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, capable of moving, movable,<BR>locomotive, active, unsteady, wandering about; (उस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Manu Sāvarṇa; also of a son of<BR>Kīrttimat and Dhenukā.<BR>—चरिष्णु-धूम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having moving smoke, whose smoke goes<BR>everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरीत्र|चरीत्रं
चरीत्र, अम्, n. behaviour, conduct, practice; [cf.<BR>चरित्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्तव्य
चर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be practised &c.; [cf.<BR>चरितव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्य|चर्य्य
चर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone; to be practised or<BR>performed &c.; (आ), f. going about, wandering, walk-<BR>ing about, driving or going in a carriage; pervading,<BR>visiting; course; proceeding, behaviour; due and<BR>regular observance of all rites or customs, following<BR>the rules of studentship; practising religious austeri-<BR>ties, wandering about as a mendicant; performing,<BR>practising, engaging in, practice, conduct [cf. कु-<BR>चर्या]; behaviour, deportment, usage; eating; (अम्),<BR>n. going about, wandering, driving in a carriage &c.;<BR>proceeding, behaviour, conduct; [cf. ब्रह्म-चर्य,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">Page0318-b+ 76</a>]<BR>भिक्षा-च्˚, भैक्ष्य-च्˚.]<BR>—चर्यावतार (˚या-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. title of a Buddhist work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार|चारं|चारः
चार, अस्, m. a spy &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरट|चरटः
चरट चरट, अस्, m. a wagtail; (ई), f. =<BR>चरण्टी, चिरिण्टी, चिरण्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरम|चरमः
चरम चरम, अस्, आ, अम्, m. pl. चरमे or<BR>चरमास्, (said to be fr. rt. चर्), last, hinder, ultimate,<BR>final; outermost; western, west; lowest, least; imme-<BR>diately following; (अस् or अम्), m. or n. (?), a particular<BR>high number; (अम्), ind. at last, at the end; चरमा<BR>क्रिया, the final ceremony, the funeral ceremony.<BR>—चरम-काल, अस्, m. the last moments, the<BR>hour of death.<BR>—चरम-क्ष्माभृत्, त्, m. the<BR>western mountain behind which the sun and moon<BR>are supposed to set.<BR>—चरम-वैयाकरण, अस्,<BR>m. an ignorant grammarian.<BR>—चरम-शैर्षिक,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, having the head towards the west.<BR>—च-<BR>रमाचल (˚म-अच्˚), अस्, m. or चरमाद्रि (˚म-<BR>अद्˚), इस्, m. = चरम-क्ष्माभृत् above.<BR>—चर-<BR>माजा (˚म-अजा), f., Ved. the last or smallest she-goat.<BR>—चरमावस्था (˚म-अव्˚), f. the last state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरम्य
चरम्य, nom. P. चरम्यति, to be the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरव्य
चरव्य चरव्य. See below under चरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरु|चरुः
चरु चरु, उस्, m. a kind of vessel in which a<BR>particular oblation is prepared, a saucepan, pot, kettle;<BR>a cloud; an oblation of rice, barley, and pulse, boiled<BR>with butter and milk for presentation to the gods or<BR>manes.<BR>—चरु-चेलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having portions of<BR>offerings on the clothes (?); an epithet of Śiva;<BR>(perhaps a wrong form for चारुचेलिन्.)<BR>—चरु-<BR>व्रण, अस्, m. a kind of cake.<BR>—चरु-श्रपण,<BR>अम्, n. sprinkling an oblation of milk and ghee.<BR>—चरु-स्थाली, f. the vessel in which an oblation is<BR>prepared, made either of clay or of udumbara-wood.<BR>—चरु-होम, अस्, m. an oblation of a meat-offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरव्य
चरव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, destined for the Caru oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्करीत
चर्करीत चर्करीत, अम्, n. (fr. 1. कृ, to do),<BR>a term used by Yāska and others for the intensive<BR>verb formed without the syllable य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्कृति|चर्कृतिः
चर्कृति चर्कृति, इस्, f. (fr. 2. कृ), Ved.<BR>praising, mention, glory, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्कृत्य
चर्कृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be mentioned with<BR>praise, worthy of praise, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्घ्
चर्घ् चर्घ्, cl. 1. P. चर्घति, &c., to go<BR>or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च्
चर्च् चर्च्, cl. 10. P. चर्चयति, to repeat<BR>(a word in reciting the Veda), to read,<BR>recite, study, peruse carefully, consider; cl. 1. or 6. P.<BR>चर्चति, &c., to speak, say, abuse, reprove, condemn,<BR>censure, menace; to injure or hurt, to inquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च|चर्चः|चर्च्च
चर्च, अस्, m. considering, deliberation, i. e. re-<BR>peating over in thought; (आ), f. repetition of a word,<BR>recitation, incidental mention, popular talk, alternate<BR>recitation of a poem by two persons; reflection, con-<BR>sideration; the exercise of judgment or deliberation,<BR>inquiry, investigation; an epithet of the goddess<BR>Durgā; covering or cleansing the body with unguents,<BR>smearing with ointment; bribery (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चक
चर्चक, अस्, आ, अम्, repeating, the repeater (of a<BR>word in the recitation of the Veda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चन|चर्चनं
चर्चन, अम्, n. repeating, repetition; covering<BR>the body with unguents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चाय
चर्चाय, nom. P. चर्चायते, to undergo repe-<BR>tition, to be repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चि|चर्चिः
चर्चि, इस्, f., Ved. repetition of words in recitation;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिका|चर्च्चिका
चर्चिका, f. deliberation, inquiry; cleaning the<BR>person with perfumes, an epithet of the goddess<BR>Durgā or Cāmuṇḍā; [cf. घर्म-चर्चिका and वि-<BR>चर्चिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिक्य|चर्चिक्यं
चर्चिक्य, अम्, n. anointing the body, an unguent,<BR>= चार्चिक्य and चर्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चित|चर्च्चितं
चर्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, perfumed, anointed, smeared<BR>with sandal &c., covered with anything; inquired<BR>into or after, investigated; sought, desired; (अम्), n.<BR>the being covered or anointed (with anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चर
चर्चर चर्चर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. चर्), Ved.<BR>going; (ई), f. a kind of song; striking the hands to<BR>beat time; musical symphony; the recitation of<BR>scholars; festive cries or merriment, festive sport; a<BR>festival; flattery, dishonest praise; a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines of eighteen syllables each;<BR>curled or woolly hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरिका
चर्चरिका, f. a kind of gesture, gesticulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरीक|चर्चरीकः|चर्च्चरीकः
चर्चरीक, अस्, m. a pot-herb; decoration or curling<BR>of the hair [cf. चर्चरी]; a form of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चस्
चर्चस् चर्चस्, आस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>nine treasures of Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्तन
चर्तन चर्तन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. चृत्), Ved.<BR>stringing together; (अम्), n. a hook, a pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्त्य|चर्त्त्यः
चर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be strung or tied in regular<BR>order; to be hurt or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्तव्य
चर्तव्य चर्तव्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्पट|चर्पटः
चर्पट चर्पट, अस्, m. the open palm of the<BR>hand with fingers extended; a kind of plant, Mollugo<BR>Pentaphylla; a quantity of bubbles or specks (स्फार-<BR>विपुल); (ई), f. a thin cake or biscuit of flour; [cf.<BR>पर्पटी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्पटि
चर्पटि चर्पटि, इस्, m., N. of an author;<BR>(also read चर्पटिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ब्
चर्ब् चर्ब्, cl. 1. P. चर्बति, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्भट|चर्भटः
चर्भट चर्भट, अस्, m. a kind of cucumber,<BR>Cucumis Utilissimus [cf. एर्वारु; cf. also चिर्भटी<BR>and चिर्भिटा]; (ई), f. = चर्चरी, the noise of merri-<BR>ment or festivity, cries of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म|चर्मं|चर्म्म|चर्म्मं
चर्म चर्म, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. चर्),<BR>Ved. a hide, a skin; a shield. See चर्मन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मण्य|चर्म्मण्य
चर्मण्य, अम्, n. (fr. the next), leather-work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मन्|चर्म्मन्
चर्मन्, अ, n. skin, leather, hide bark, parchment,<BR>&c.; the hide of an antelope &c. used as a seat or<BR>bed by the religious student; a shield; [cf. गल-चर्-<BR>मन्, दुश्-चर्मन्, &c.; cf. also Lat. corium, cal-<BR>ceus (?); Hib. croicionn; Gr. πέλμα.]<BR>—चर्म-<BR>करण, अम्, n. working in skins or leather.<BR>—चर्-<BR>म-कशा or चर्म-कषा or चर्म-कसा, f. ‘skin-<BR>injurer,’ a plant, commonly called Carmakaṣā or Car-<BR>maghās, Mimosa Abstergens; a particular kind of per-<BR>fume.<BR>—चर्म-कार, अस्, m. a shoe-maker, a currier or<BR>worker in leather, the offspring of a Caṇḍāla woman<BR>by a man of the fisherman caste, or of a Vaideha<BR>female by a Niṣāda; (ई), f. the wife of the preceding;<BR>N. of a plant, = चर्म-कशा.<BR>—चर्म-कारक, अस्,<BR>m. a worker in leather.<BR>—चर्म-कारिन्, ई, m. a currier,<BR>skinner, shoe-maker, worker in hides or leather.<BR>—चर्-<BR>म-कार्य, अम्, n. working in leather or skins.<BR>—चर्-<BR>म-कील, अस्, अम्, m. n. a wart; excrescences con-<BR>sidered as a kind of hemorrhoids.<BR>—चर्म-कृत्, त्,<BR>m. a shoe-maker.<BR>—चर्म-खाण्डिक, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people; (perhaps for चर्म-खण्डिक ?);<BR>[cf. चर्म-मण्डल and चर्म-रङ्ग.]<BR>—चर्म-<BR>ग्रीव, अस्, m., N. of one of the attendants of Śiva.<BR>—चर्म-चटक, अस्, आ, m. f. or चर्म-चटिका, f.<BR>or चर्म-चटी, f. a bat.<BR>—चर्म-चित्रक, अम्, n.<BR>white leprosy (श्वेत-कुष्ठ).<BR>—चर्म-चेल, अस्<BR>or अम्, m. or n. (?), a garment with the hide turned<BR>outwards.<BR>—चर्म-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, coming forth<BR>from the skin, produced by or from the skin; (अम्),<BR>n. the hairs of the body; blood.<BR>—चर्मण्-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. furnished with hide, covered with skin<BR>or leather; (ती), f. the plantain tree, Musa Sapientum<BR>[cf. कदल]; a river that flows through Bundelkhand<BR>into the Ganges, the modern Chambal.<BR>—चर्म-<BR>तरङ्ग, अस्, m. a wrinkle, a fold of skin.<BR>—चर्म-<BR>तिल, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with pimples resembling<BR>the seeds of sesamum.<BR>—चर्म-दण्ड, अस्, m. ‘a<BR>leather stick,’ a whip.<BR>—चर्म-दल, अम्, n. a form<BR>of leprosy or cutaneous disease.<BR>—चर्म-दूषिका,<BR>f. a kind of leprosy with red spots, cutaneous disease.<BR>—चर्म-द्रुम, अस्, m., N. of a tree; [cf. भूर्ज.]<BR>—चर्म-नासिका, f. ‘a leather thong,’ a whip.<BR>—चर्म-पट्टिका, f. a flat piece of leather for play-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">Page0319-a+ 77</a>]<BR>ing upon with dice, a leather backgammon board &c.<BR>—चर्म-पत्त्रा, f. a bat, the small house-bat.<BR>—चर्म-पादुका, f. a leather shoe.<BR>—चर्म-<BR>प्रभेदिका, f. a shoe-maker's awl.<BR>—चर्म-प्रसे-<BR>वक, अस्, इका, m. f. a bellows.<BR>—चर्म-बन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. a leather band or strap.<BR>—चर्म-मण्डल,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—चर्म -मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, made of skin or leather, leathern, encased in<BR>leather.<BR>—चर्म-मुण्डा, f. a form of the goddess<BR>Durgā, commonly चामुण्डा and चण्ड-मुण्डा.<BR>—चर्म-म्न, अस्, m., Ved. a tanner.<BR>—चर्म-<BR>यष्टि, इस्, f. a whip; [cf. चर्म-दण्ड.]<BR>—चर्म-<BR>रङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a people in the north-west of<BR>Madhya-deśa; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = आवर्तकी.<BR>—चर्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, covered with hides or<BR>skins; (आन्), m., N. of a warrior.<BR>—चर्म-वसन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, clothed in skin; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; [cf. कृत्ति-वासस्.]<BR>—चर्म-वाद्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘skin-instrument,’ i. e. a drum, tabour, &c.<BR>—चर्म-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a tree; [cf. चर्मिन्.]<BR>—चर्-<BR>म-सम्भवा, f. cardamoms.<BR>—चर्म-सार, अस्,<BR>m. lymph, serum.<BR>—चर्माच्छादित (˚म-आच्छ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, covered with skin.<BR>—चर्मान्त (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. a piece or strap of leather.<BR>—चर्माम्-<BR>भस् (˚म-अम्˚), अस्, n. lymph, serum.<BR>—चर्माव-<BR>कर्तन (˚म-अव्˚), अम्, n. working in leather or<BR>skins.<BR>—चर्मावकर्तिन् (˚म-अव्˚), ई, m. a worker<BR>in leather or skins, a shoe-maker, a man of the lowest<BR>caste.<BR>—चर्मावकर्त्तृ (˚म-अव्˚), ता, m. a shoe-<BR>maker.<BR>—चर्मावनद्ध (˚म-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>covered with skin, bound with leather, &c.<BR>—चर्मा-<BR>वृत (˚म-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, covered with skin or<BR>parchment.<BR>—चर्मासि-मत् (˚म-असि-), आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, possessed of shield and sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मरु|चर्मरुः|चर्म्मरु|चर्म्मरुः
चर्मरु, उस्, m. a shoe-maker, a worker in<BR>leather; [cf. चर्मार and चर्म-कार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मार|चर्मारः|चर्म्मार|चर्म्मारः
चर्मार, अस्, m. a worker in leather, a shoe-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मिक|चर्म्मिक
चर्मिक, अस्, आ, अम्, armed with a shield, a<BR>shield-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मिन्|चर्म्मिन्
चर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, covered with skin or parchment,<BR>having a hide or skin; leather, leathern, made of<BR>leather, &c.; armed with a shield; (ई), m. a soldier<BR>armed with a shield, a shield-bearer; N. of a tree,<BR>the bark of which is used for writing upon, &c. [cf.<BR>भूर्ज]; a plantain; N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मरी|चर्म्मरी
चर्मरी चर्मरी, f., N. of a plant with a<BR>poisonous fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्य|चर्य्य
चर्य चर्य. See p. 318, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्
चर्व् चर्व् [cf. चूर्ण्]. cl. 1. 10. P. चर्वति,<BR>चर्वयति, &c., to bruise, crush, grind with<BR>the teeth, chew, champ, masticate; to eat; sup up, suck:<BR>Pass. चर्व्यते; [cf. Hib. carbad, ‘the jaw;’ carbal,<BR>‘the palate of the mouth;’ creimim, ‘I gnaw;’ creim,<BR>‘corrosion;’ Lith. kramtan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वण|चर्वणं|चर्व्वण|चर्व्वणं
चर्वण, अस्, आ, अम्, chewing; (अम्), n. chewing,<BR>masticating; sipping, tasting; food which must be<BR>chewed, solid food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वणीय
चर्वणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, masticable, proper to be<BR>chewed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वित|चर्व्वित|चर्व्वितं
चर्वित, अस्, आ, अम्, chewed, eaten.<BR>—चर्वित-<BR>चर्वण, अम्, n. chewing the chewed; seeking<BR>happiness where others have sought it in vain; repe-<BR>tition of the same act, tautology, tedious reiteration.<BR>—चर्वित-पात्र or चर्वित-पात्रक, अम्, n. a<BR>spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्य|चर्व्व्य|चर्व्व्यं
चर्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be chewed, chewable;<BR>(अम्), n. solid food requiring mastication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वन्|चर्व्वन्
चर्वन् चर्वन्, आ, m. a blow with the flat of<BR>the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्षणि|चर्षणिः
चर्षणि चर्षणि, इस्, इस्, इ (said by some to<BR>be derived fr. कृष्; by other native commentators<BR>connected with rt. चक्ष्. to see, and so probably<BR>derived by Yāska, who explains चर्षणि by चायितृ,<BR>q. v.; other scholars connect it with rt. चर्), Ved.<BR>seeing, observing; discerning, moving, movable, run-<BR>ning, going in a carriage, agile, active, swift; (अयस्),<BR>f. pl. men, people, race, nation (e. g. पञ्च चर्ष-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-b" target="_blank">Page0319-b+ 80</a>]<BR>णयस्, the five races of men, the five nations; cf.<BR>कृष्टि, क्षिति, जन); ‘beings endowed with dis-<BR>cernment,’ N. of the children of Aryaman and Mā-<BR>trikā, who are regarded in the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa as<BR>the progenitors of the human race; (ई), f. a disloyal<BR>wife; N. of the wife of Varuṇa and mother of<BR>Bhṛgu; [cf. वि-च्˚ and विश्व-च्˚.]<BR>—चर्षणि-प्रा,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. governing men or people or races<BR>of men, epithet of Indra.<BR>—चर्षणी-धृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. supporting or protecting men or races of men;<BR>epithet of Indra, Mitra, Varuṇa, and the Viśve-devās.<BR>—चर्षणी-धृति, इस्, f., Ved. support or protection<BR>of men or races.<BR>—चर्षणी-सह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. ruling<BR>over or overpowering men; (Sāy.) overpowering<BR>enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल्
चल् चल् [cf. चट् and चर्], cl. 1. P.<BR>(sometimes A.) चलति, -ते, चचाल, च-<BR>लिष्यति, अचालीत्, चलितुम्, to move one's self, be<BR>moved; to stir, tremble, shake, quiver, throb, palpi-<BR>tate, be agitated; totter; to move on or forward,<BR>proceed, go away; to start off, set out, depart; to<BR>walk, march; to be moved from one's usual course,<BR>to be disturbed, become confused or disordered; to<BR>go astray; to turn away from the right course, swerve,<BR>deviate from (with abl., e. g. चलति धर्मात्, he<BR>swerves from virtue); fall off, leave off (with abl.);<BR>to sport about, frolic, play, wanton: Caus. P. चल-<BR>यति or चालयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to move, to<BR>move, shake, jog, nudge, push, agitate, disturb; to turn<BR>off from, to cause to deviate, lead away from; cause to<BR>fall; drive away, remove or expel from; to cherish,<BR>foster, (wrong form for बल्): Pass. of Caus. चाल्यते,<BR>to be moved: Desid. चिचलिषति: Intens. चञल्यते<BR>or चाचल्यते, चाचल्ति; [cf. Gr. κέλω, κέλλω, ὀ-<BR>κέλλω, κέλης; Lat. celer, pro-cello, ex-cello, prœ-<BR>cello; calco, calc-s, calcar; Hib. caill, ‘a path;’<BR>Germ. falle; Gr. πάλλω, πέλω; Lat. pello.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल|चलं|चलः
चल, अस्, आ, अम्, moving, trembling, tremulous,<BR>movable, shaking, loose, unfixed, unsteady, fickle,<BR>fluctuating, perishable, disturbed, confused; (अस्), m.<BR>agitation, shaking, trembling; wind; quicksilver;<BR>(आ), f. lightning; incense; fortune or Lakṣmī the<BR>goddess of fortune; N. of a metre consisting of four<BR>lines of eighteen syllables each; [cf. अ-चल, निश्-<BR>चल, चाल.]<BR>—चल-कर्ण, अस्, m. the true distance<BR>of a planet from the earth.<BR>—चल-कृति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>unsteady, wanton.<BR>—चल-केतु, उस्, m. (in astron.)<BR>N. of a moving Ketu.<BR>—चल-चञ्चु, उस्, m., N. of<BR>the Greek partridge, Perdix Rufa; [cf. चकोर.]<BR>—चल-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fickle-minded, inconstant;<BR>(अम्), n. fickleness, mutability.<BR>—चलचित्त-ता, f. or<BR>चलचित्त-त्व, अम्, n. fickleness of mind, unsteadi-<BR>ness, inconstancy, mutability, frivolity.<BR>—चल-ता, f.<BR>or चल-त्र, अम्, n. shaking, trembling, a tremulous<BR>motion, pulsation.<BR>—चल-दन्त, अस्, m. a loose<BR>tooth.<BR>—चल-दल, अस्, m. the holy fig-tree, Ficus<BR>Religiosa; [cf. अश्वत्थ.]<BR>—चल-पत्त्र, अस्, m.<BR>the Ficus Religiosa; [cf. अश्वत्थ.]<BR>—चल-सन्धि,<BR>इस्, m. movable articulation of the bones, Diarthrosis.<BR> — 1. चलाचल (˚ल-अच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, movable and<BR>immovable, locomotive and stationary.<BR>—चलातङ्क<BR>(˚ल+आत्˚), अस्, m. rheumatism.<BR>—चलात्मन् (˚ल-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, fickle-minded, inconstant.<BR>—चलेन्द्रिय<BR>(˚ल-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having unsteady organs, sensi-<BR>tive, sensual, not having subdued senses or passions.<BR>—चलेषु (˚ल-इषु), उस्, उस्, उ, one whose arrow<BR>wavers or flies unsteadily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्
चलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going, moving.<BR>—चलत्-पदम्.<BR>ind. moving, walking.<BR>—चलत्-पूर्णिमा, f. a small<BR>fish called Chanda, = चन्द्र-चञ्चल.<BR>—चलद्-<BR>अङ्ग or चलद्-अङ्गक, अस्, m. a fish, a sort of gilt-<BR>head, commonly Ceṅgā, Ophiocephalus Aurantiacus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलन|चलनं|चलनः
चलन, अस्, आ, अम्, moving, movable, trembling<BR>tremulous, shaking; (अस्), m. a foot; a deer, an<BR>antelope; (ई), f. a short petticoat worn by common<BR>women; the rope for tying an elephant; (अम्), n. a<BR>shaking motion, shaking, trembling; walking about,<BR>wandering, roaming; turning off from, leaving off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलनक|चलनकं|चलनकः
चलनक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. a short petticoat<BR>worn by women of low rank; (इका), f. silken fringes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलनीय
चलनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be moved or shaken,<BR>movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलमान
चलमान, अस्, आ, अम्, going, moving, proceeding,<BR>shaking, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलस्
चलस्, अस्, n. wood-sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलाचल|चलाचलः
2. चलाचल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. चल् with reduplica-<BR>tion), moving to and fro, movable, tremulous, unfixed,<BR>unsteady, shaking, loose; variable; (अस्), m. a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलित|चलितं
चलित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, departed, proceeded (often<BR>used like a past tense, e. g. स चलितः, he started off,<BR>he departed); shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलितव्य
चलितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone away; to be<BR>moved, movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलु|चलुः
चलु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. चल्), water hastily<BR>taken up in the hollowed palm of the hand for rincing<BR>the mouth &c.; a handful or mouthful of water; [cf.<BR>गण्डूष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलुक|चलुकः
चलुक, अस्, m. = the preceding; also a small pot,<BR>a gallipot, &c.; N. of a man; [cf. चुलुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलद्विष|चलद्विषः
चलद्विष चलद्विष, अस्, m. the Kokila or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलि|चलिः
चलि चलि, इस्, m. a cover, a wrapper, a<BR>surtout; [cf. चोल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चवि|चविः
चवि चवि, इस्, ई, f. or चविक, अम्, आ, n. f. or<BR>चव्या, अम्, f. n. a species of the pepper plant, Piper<BR>Chaba; Orris root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चशाति
चशाति चशाति, a wrong reading for व-<BR>शाति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चष्
चष् चष्, cl. 1. P. A. चषति, -ते, to eat;<BR>to kill, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषक|चषकं|चषकः
चषक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a vessel used for drinking<BR>spirits, a wine glass &c., any drinking-vessel; spirituous<BR>liquor; honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषति|चषतिः
चषति, इस्, m. eating; killing; decay, infirmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषाल|चषालः
चषाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a wooden ring on the top<BR>of a sacrificial post; an iron ring at the base of the<BR>post; (अस्), m. a hive.<BR>—चषाल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. furnished with a Caṣāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चष्ट
चष्ट चष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (past passive part.<BR>fr. चक्ष् ?), spoken, asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चष्टान
चष्टान चष्टान, अस्, m., N. of a prince,<BR>(= Τιαστανος ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चह्
चह् चह् [cf. चप्], cl. 1. 10. P. चहति,<BR>अचहीत्, चहयति, -यितुम्, to be wicked,<BR>commit wickedness; to cheat; to be proud; cl. 10.<BR>P. चहयति, to grind, pound, knead; [cf. Hib.<BR>cagnaim, ‘I chew, gnaw.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाकचिच्चा
चाकचिच्चा चाकचिच्चा, f., N. of a plant, =<BR>श्वेत-वह्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्र
चाक्र चाक्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चक्र), carried<BR>on (as a battle) with the discus; circular, belonging<BR>to a wheel &c.; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रवर्मण|चाक्रवर्म्मण
चाक्रवर्मण, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. चक्र-<BR>वर्मन्), N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रवाकेय
चाक्रवाकेय, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n.? (fr. चक्र-<BR>वाक), N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रायण|चाक्रायणः
चाक्रायण, अस्, m. a patronymic of Uṣasta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रिक|चाक्रिकः
चाक्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, circular; belonging to a wheel<BR>or discus; relating to a company or circle; (अस्), m.<BR>a potter; an oil-maker; a proclaimer; a chorister,<BR>a bard who chants in chorus the praises of kings,<BR>heroes, gods, &c.; a coachman, a driver; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. companions, followers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रिण|चाक्रिणः
चाक्रिण, अस्, m. the son of a potter or oil-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रेय
चाक्रेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a wheel or discus;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. or n. (?), N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्षुष|चाक्षुषं|चाक्षुषः
चाक्षुष चाक्षुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चक्षुस्),<BR>consisting in sight, depending on or produced from<BR>it; belonging to the eye. visual, optical, perceptible by<BR>the eye, visible, seen; relating to Manu Cākṣuṣa;<BR>चाक्षुषी विद्या, that magical science which gives<BR>the power of seeing anything; (अस्), m., N. of the<BR>sixth Manu who with five other Manus is a son of<BR>Manu Svāyambhuva, or according to other authorities<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">Page0320-a+ 71</a>]<BR>a son of Viśva-karman and Ākṛti, or a son of<BR>Cakṣus; N. of a son of Ripu and Bṛhatī, (according<BR>to some he is called Cakṣuṣa, and is father of Manu<BR>Cākṣuṣa); N. of a son of Kakṣeyu and brother<BR>of Sabhānara; also of a son of Anu and brother of<BR>Sabhānara; also of a son of Khanitra; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a class of deities in the fourteenth Manvantara;<BR>(अम्), n. knowledge which depends on vision.<BR>—चाक्षुष-ज्ञान, अम्, n. ocular evidence.<BR>—चा-<BR>क्षुष-त्व, अम्, n. perceptibility by sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्ष्म
चाक्ष्म चाक्ष्म, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. क्षम्), Ved.<BR>forbearing, gracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाङ्ग|चांग|चांगः|चाङ्गः
चाङ्ग चाङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. चङ्ग), wood-sorrel;<BR>whiteness or beauty of the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाङ्गेरी
चाङ्गेरी, f. wood-sorrel, Oxalis Pusilla; [cf. कु-<BR>चाङ्गेरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाचपुट|चाचपुटः
चाचपुट चाचपुट, अस्, m. a kind of time in<BR>music; [cf. चच्चपुट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाचलि
चाचलि चाचलि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. Intens. of rt. चल्),<BR>moving much or repeatedly; [cf. वि-चाचलि and अ-विच्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाञ्चल्य|चांचल्य|चांचल्यं|चाञ्चल्यं
चाञ्चल्य चाञ्चल्य, अम्, n. (fr. चञ्चल),<BR>tremulousness, unsteadiness; transitoriness, fugitive-<BR>ness, fidgetiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाट|चाटः
चाट चाट, अस्, m. (fr. चट् = चत् ?), a cheat,<BR>a rogue, a speculator, one who makes away with<BR>or embezzles money &c. entrusted to him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटकैर|चाटकैरः
चाटकैर चाटकैर, अस्, m. (fr. चटक or<BR>चटका), a young sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटलिका
चाटलिका चाटलिका, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटिग्राम
चाटिग्राम चाटिग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटु|चाटुः
चाटु चाटु, उस्, उ, m. n. (said to be fr. rt. चट्),<BR>pleasing or grateful words or discourse, flattery,<BR>flattering, coaxing; distinct or clear speech; [cf.<BR>चतु.]<BR>—चाटु-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, speaking agreeably<BR>or kindly, flattering, complying with a request,<BR>humouring, complaisant; (अस्), m. a flatterer.<BR>—चाटु-<BR>कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking agreeably, flattering.<BR>—चाटु-पटु, उस्, m. a jester, a buffoon, one who<BR>makes compliments (?).<BR>—चाटु-लोल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>elegantly tremulous.<BR>—चाटु-वटु, उस्, m. a jester;<BR>[cf. चाटु-पटु.]<BR>—चाटु-शत, अम्, n. repeated coax-<BR>ing, a hundred entreaties.<BR>—चाटूक्ति (˚टु-उक्ति), इस्,<BR>f. agreeable language, flattery, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुक|चाटुकः
चाटुक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), pleasing or<BR>grateful discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणकीन|चाणकीनं
चाणकीन चाणकीन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चणक),<BR>fit for or sown with the chick-pea (a field &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणक्य|चाणक्यः
चाणक्य चाणक्य, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr.<BR>चणक, N. of a Muni), N. of the sage Vātsyāyana;<BR>N. of a celebrated Brāhman also called Viṣṇu-gupta,<BR>the reputed author of a work on morals and the princi-<BR>ples of government. He is said to have destroyed<BR>the Nanda dynasty and to have made Candra-gupta<BR>(q. v.) king, whose minister he became. From the<BR>tone of his advice to princes he has been styled the<BR>Machiavelli of India; (अम्), n., scil. शास्त्रम्, the<BR>work of Cāṇakya, on morals and polity.<BR>—चाणक्य-<BR>मूलक, अम्, n. a kind of radish; [cf. कौटिल्य.]<BR>—चाणक्य-श्लोक, आस्, m. pl. detached stanzas on<BR>morals and the principles of government, supposed<BR>to be written by the Brāhman Cāṇakya or compiled<BR>by him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणक
चाणक, अस्, ई, अम् (an adj. formed fr. चाणक्य),<BR>relating to Cāṇakya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणूर|चाणूरः
चाणूर चाणूर, अस्, m., N. of a prince; also<BR>of a wrestler in the service of Kaṃsa, slain by Kṛṣṇa,<BR>and identified with the Daitya Varāha.<BR>—चाणूर-<BR>सूदन, अस्, m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्ड|चांडं
चाण्ड चाण्ड, अम्, n. (fr. चण्ड), violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्डाल|चांडाल|चांडालः|चाण्डालः
चाण्डाल चाण्डाल, अस्, m. = चण्डाल, a name<BR>of an impure or degraded tribe, a Caṇḍāla, a Pariah,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">Page0320-b+ 79</a>]<BR>an outcast; (ई), f. a woman of the same tribe; N. of<BR>a plant, = लिङ्गिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्डालिका|चांडालिका
चाण्डालिका, f. a vulgar lute, the lute of the<BR>Caṇḍāla; a N. of Durgā; a kind of herb; [cf.<BR>चण्डालिका.]<BR>—चाण्डालिकाश्रम (˚का-आश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>N. of the hermitage of Cāṇḍālikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातक|चातकः
चातक चातक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. चत्),<BR>N. of the bird Cuculus Melanoleucus, according to<BR>the legend living only upon rain-drops; [cf. Lat.<BR>cot-urnix.]<BR>—चातकानन्दन (˚क-आन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the rainy season.<BR>—चातकाष्टक (˚क-अष्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the eight verses on the Cātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातन
चातन चातन. See under rt. चत् at p. 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर|चातुरः
चातुर 1. चातुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्), re-<BR>lating to four; (a carriage &c.) drawn by four; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a poem by Nara-siṃha; (अम्), n. a carriage,<BR>a cart holding four people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुःसागरिक
चातुःसागरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुः-सागर),<BR>belonging to the four oceans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरक्ष|चातुरक्षं|चातुरक्षः
चातुरक्ष, अम्, n. (fr. चतुर्-अक्ष), four casts<BR>in playing at dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरर्थिक|चातुरर्थिकः
चातुरर्थिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-अर्थ), used<BR>in four particular senses or meanings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुराश्रमिक
चातुराश्रमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or चातुराश्रमिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ (fr. चतुर्-आश्रम), being in one of the<BR>four periods or orders [cf. आश्रम] of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुराश्रम्य|चातुराश्रम्यं
चातुराश्रम्य, अम्, n. the four periods of the<BR>life of a Brāhman collectively; the aggregate of the<BR>four orders of student, householder, ascetic, and<BR>mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्जातक|चातुर्जातकं
चातुर्जातक, अम्, n. = कटु-चातुर्जातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थक|चातुर्थकः
चातुर्थक, अस्, इका, अम्, quartan, appearing<BR>every fourth day; (अस्), m. a quartan ague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थाह्निक
चातुर्थाह्निक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्थ-अहन्),<BR>belonging to the fourth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थिक
चातुर्थिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the fourth<BR>or to the fourth day; (अस्), m. a quartan ague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्दश|चातुर्द्दश
चातुर्दश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्दशी), appearing<BR>on the fourteenth day of the half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्दशिक|चातुर्दशिकः|चातुर्द्दशिक
चातुर्दशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, reading the holy scrip-<BR>tures on the fourteenth day of the half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्दैव
चातुर्दैव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-देव), sacred to<BR>four deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्भद्र|चातुर्भद्रं
चातुर्भद्र, अम्, n. (fr. चतुर्-भद्र), an<BR>assemblage of four medicinal plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्भुजि
चातुर्भुजि, इस्, m. a son of Catur-bhuja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्भौतिक
चातुर्भौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-भूत),<BR>consisting of four elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्महाराजकायिक
चातुर्महाराजकायिक or चातुर्महाराजिक =<BR>चतुर्महाराजकायिक; also an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास|चातुर्म्मास
चातुर्मास, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-मास), produced<BR>in four months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मासक
चातुर्मासक, अस्, इका, अम्, or चातुर्मासिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, one who performs the Cāturmāsya sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मासी
चातुर्मासी, f., scil. पौर्णमासी, the day of full<BR>moon at the Cāturmāsya sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास्य|चातुर्मास्यं|चातुर्म्मास्य|चातुर्म्मास्यं
चातुर्मास्य, अम्, n., N. of three sacrifices be-<BR>longing to the subdivision called Havir-yajña and<BR>performed (every four months) at the beginning of<BR>the three seasons, viz. the वैश्वदेवम् on the full<BR>moon in Phalguna, वरुण-प्रघासाः in Aṣāḍha,<BR>and साकमेधाः in Kṛttikā; (अस्, आ, अम्), belong-<BR>ing to the Cāturmāsya sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वर्ण्य|चातुर्व्वर्ण्यं
चातुर्वर्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चतुर्-वर्ण), suited<BR>to the four tribes or castes, belonging to them (?);<BR>(अम्), n. the aggregate of the four original castes,<BR>viz. the Brāhman, Kṣatriya, Vaiśya, and Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विंशिक
चातुर्विंशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्विंश), be-<BR>longing to the twenty-fourth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विद्य
चातुर्विद्य, अस्, दी, अम् (fr. चतुर्-विद्या), familiar<BR>with the four Vedas; (अम्), n. the four Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विध्य|चातुर्विध्यं
चातुर्विध्य, अम्, n. (fr. चतुर्-विध), four kinds<BR>collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वैद्य|चातुर्व्वैद्यः
चातुर्वैद्य, अस्, दी, अम् (fr. चतुर्-वेद), versed<BR>in or familiar with the four Vedas; (अम्), n. know-<BR>ledge of the four Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होतृक
चातुर्होतृक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-होतृ), belong-<BR>ing to the Catur-hotṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होत्र
चातुर्होत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-होतृ), conducted<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">Page0320-c+ 77</a>]<BR>or performed by the four chief priests, viz. the Hotṛ,<BR>Adhvaryu, Udgātṛ, and Brahman; (अम्), n. a sacrifice<BR>performed by four priests; the office or duties of the<BR>four chief priests; the four chief priests collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होत्रिय|चातुर्होत्रियः
चातुर्होत्रिय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुर्-होतृ), a sacri-<BR>fice &c. at or in which the four chief priests are<BR>employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुष्काण्डिक|चातुष्कांडिक
चातुष्काण्डिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुष्-काण्ड),<BR>divided into four parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुष्टय
चातुष्टय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चतुष्टय), knowing<BR>or familiar with the Catuṣṭaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुष्प्राश्य
चातुष्प्राश्य, अस्, शी, अम् (fr. चतुः + प्राश),<BR>enough for four persons to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्वारिंश
चात्वारिंश, अम्, n. (fr. चत्वारिंशत्), title of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa consisting of forty Adhyāyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्वारिंशत्क
चात्वारिंशत्क, अस्, ई, अम्, bought for forty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर|चातुरः
चातुर 2. चातुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. चतुर),<BR>clever, able, ingenious, shrewd, sagacious; speaking<BR>well or kindly, flattering; perceptible, visible; govern-<BR>ing, ruling; (अस्), m. a small round pillow, see below;<BR>(ई), f. dexterity, ability, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरक|चातुरकः
चातुरक, अस्, आ, अम्, flattering; perceptible;<BR>governing; (अस्), m. a small round pillow for resting<BR>the cheek upon; [cf. गल्ल-चातुरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरिक|चातुरिकः
चातुरिक, अस्, m. a charioteer, a coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्य|चातुर्यं|चातुर्य्य
चातुर्य, अम्, n. dexterity, cleverness, ability,<BR>shrewdness; amiableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्र|चात्रं
चात्र चात्र, अम्, n. (sometimes read चत्र),<BR>a cylinder of catechu-wood twelve Aṅgulas long,<BR>tipped at both ends with iron and furnished with an<BR>iron bolt, (this and another piece of wood called<BR>Auvīlī are used for producing the sacred fire.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्वाल|चात्वालं|चात्वालः
चात्वाल चात्वाल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. the hole<BR>formed in the ground by excavating the earth to con-<BR>struct the Uttara-vedi or north altar; (अस्), m. a<BR>hollow place dug in the ground to receive a burnt-offer-<BR>ing; any hole in the ground; [cf. चत्वाल.]<BR>—चा-<BR>त्वाल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, (a sacrifice) at which the<BR>Cātvāla is excavated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्दनिक|चांदनिक
चान्दनिक चान्दनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चन्दन),<BR>made of or derived from sandal, perfumed with it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्र|चांद्र|चान्द्रं|चान्द्रः
चान्द्र चान्द्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चन्द्र), lunar,<BR>relating to the moon, regulated by it, &c.; (अस्), m.<BR>a month, a lunar month (called Gauṇa, q. v., if<BR>reckoned from full moon to full moon, and Mukhya<BR>if reckoned from new moon to new moon); the<BR>light fortnight or half month, during which the moon<BR>is on the increase; the Candra-kānta or moon-gem;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the pupils of the grammarian Candra;<BR>(ई), f. moonlight; a kind of solanum [cf. श्वेत-<BR>कण्टकारी]; N. of a princess; (अम्), n., scil. व्र-<BR>तम्, the Cāndrāyaṇa penance, see below.<BR>—चान्-<BR>द्र-मास, अस्, m. a lunar month; [cf. चान्द्र<BR>above.]<BR>—चान्द्र-वत्सर, अस्, m. the lunar year.<BR>—चान्द्र-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra work.<BR>—चान्द्राख्य (˚र-आख्˚), अम्, n. fresh ginger;<BR>[cf. चान्द्रक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रक|चांद्रक|चांद्रकं|चान्द्रकं
चान्द्रक, अम्, n. dried ginger; [cf. शुण्ठी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रपुर
चान्द्रपुर, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of Candra-<BR>pura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रभागा|चांद्रभागा
चान्द्रभागा or ई f. = चन्द्र-भागा, the Che-<BR>nāb, a river in the Pañjāb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमस|चांद्रमस|चान्द्रमसं|चान्द्रमसः
चान्द्रमस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चन्द्रमस्), lunar,<BR>relating or belonging to the moon; (ई), f., N. of the<BR>wife of Bṛhaspati; (अम्), n., N. of the fifth lunar<BR>mansion, the constellation Mṛga-śiras; the stars in<BR>Orion.<BR>—चान्द्रमसायन, अस्, or चान्द्रमसा-<BR>यनि, इस्, m. (fr. चन्द्रमस्), ‘descendant of the<BR>moon,’ a N. of Buddha, regent of Mercury and son of<BR>the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रव्रतिक|चांद्रव्रतिक|चान्द्रव्रतिकः
चान्द्रव्रतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चन्द्र-व्रत),<BR>acting in the manner of the moon, having the<BR>character of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायण|चांद्रायण|चांद्रायणं|चान्द्रायणं
चान्द्रायण, अम्, n., scil. व्रतम्, a religious<BR>observance or expiatory penance regulated by the<BR>moon's age, (it consists in diminishing the daily con-<BR>sumption of food every day by one mouthful for the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">Page0321-a+ 74</a>]<BR>dark half of the month, beginning with 15 at the<BR>full moon until the quantity is reduced to O at the<BR>new moon, and then increasing it in like manner<BR>during the fortnight of the moon's increase: if this<BR>penance begins with the full moon, it is called<BR>Pipīlikā-madhya, i. e. having the middle thin like<BR>an ant; if with the new moon, beginning with O<BR>and increasing to 15, it is called Yava-madhya or<BR>Yava-madhyama, i. e. having the middle thick like a<BR>barley-corn); (आस्), m. pl., N. of various persons.<BR>—चान्द्रायण-भक्त, अम्, n. the country in-<BR>habited by the Cāndrāyaṇas.<BR>—चान्द्रायण-वि-<BR>धान or चान्द्रायण-व्रत, अम्, n. the penance<BR>called Cāndrāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायणिक|चांद्रायणिक
चान्द्रायणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, performing or a per-<BR>former of the Cāndrāyaṇa, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्धनायन
चान्धनायन चान्धनायन, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>ancient preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाप|चापं|चापः
चाप चाप, अस्, अम्, m. n. (perhaps fr. rt.<BR>कप् = कम्प्), a bow; (in geometry) an arc or por-<BR>tion of a circle; the sign of the zodiac Sagittarius;<BR>a rainbow [cf. इन्द्र-चाप and शक्र-चाप]; N. of<BR>a particular constellation; [cf. धनुस्.]<BR>—चाप-<BR>दासी, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चाप-पट, अस्, m. the tree<BR>Buchanania Latifolia (पियाल); [cf. धनु and<BR>पट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापिन्
चापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, armed with a bow; (ई), m. the<BR>sign of the zodiac Sagittarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल|चापलं
चापल चापल, अम्, n. (fr. चपल), fickle-<BR>ness, unsteadiness, mobility, quick movement, swift-<BR>ness, transitoriness; agitation, tremour; inconsiderate<BR>conduct, impertinence, inconsiderateness.<BR>—चापला-<BR>श्रय (˚ल-आश्˚), अम्, n. (?) unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल्य|चापल्यं
चापल्य, अम्, n. fickleness; unsteadiness, transi-<BR>toriness; quickness, agitation, flurry; inconsiderate<BR>conduct, inconsiderateness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापाल
चापाल चापाल, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>Caitya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाबुका
चाबुका चाबुका, f. a small circular pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामर|चामरं|चामरः
चामर चामर, अम्, आ or ई, अस्, n. f. m. a<BR>chowrie, the bushy tail of the Bos Grunniens, used as<BR>a fly-flap or fan, and as one of the insignia of royalty;<BR>also used for a kind of streamer or plume on the<BR>heads of horses; (अम्), n., N. of a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of fifteen syllables each.<BR>—चामर-<BR>ग्राह, अस्, m. a person who carries a Cāmara.<BR>—चामर-पुष्प, अस्, m., N. of several plants,<BR>Magnifera Indica [cf. आम्र]; the betel-nut tree,<BR>Areca Faufel or Catechu [cf. पूग]; the Pandanus<BR>Odoratissimus [cf. केतक]; a kind of grass, Saccha-<BR>rum Spontaneum [cf. काश].<BR>—चामर-पुष्पक,<BR>अस्, m. or चामर-साह्वय, अस्, m. a kind of grass,<BR>Saccharum Spontaneum; [cf. काश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरिक|चामरिकः
चामरिक, अस्, m. a person who carries a Cāmara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरिन्
चामरिन्, ई, m. a horse (either from his bushy<BR>tail which he uses to whisk off flies or from his<BR>having a Cāmara as his crest; see above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामीकर|चामीकरं
चामीकर चामीकर, अम्, n. gold; the thorn-<BR>apple.<BR>—चामीकर-प्रख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, like gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामुण्डा|चामुंडा
चामुण्डा चामुण्डा, f. a form of Durgā; one<BR>of the seven Mātṛs; (अस्), m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पिला|चांपिला
चाम्पिला चाम्पिला, f. a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पेय|चांपेय|चांपेयः|चाम्पेयः
चाम्पेय चाम्पेय, अस्, m. (fr. चम्पा), N. of<BR>two trees, Michelia Champaka and Mesua Ferrea;<BR>a stamen or filament, especially of the lotus flower;<BR>a prince of Campā; N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पेयक|चांपेयकं|चाम्पेयकं
चाम्पेयक, अम्, n. a stamen or filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्य|चाम्यं
चाम्य चाम्य, अम्, n. (fr. rt. चम्), food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाय्
चाय् चाय्, cl. 1. P. A. चायति, -ते, to ob-<BR>serve, discern, perceive; to worship, re-<BR>vere; [cf. 4. चि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चायमान
चायमान, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic of Abhyā-<BR>vartin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चायितृ
चायितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. observing, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चायु
चायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. showing respect or reverence,<BR>honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार|चारं|चारः
चार चार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. चर्), = चर, a<BR>spy, scout, secret agent or emissary, messenger;<BR>going, motion, progression, course; wandering about,<BR>travelling; proceeding; performing, practising; bind-<BR>ing, a bond, fetter; a prison, a house of confinement;<BR>the tree Buchanania Latifolia, = पियाल; (अम्), n. a<BR>factitious poison, (for वार); [cf. Lat. carcer.]<BR>—चार-काण्ड, अम्, n. ascensional difference (in<BR>astronomy).<BR>—चार-चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, ‘spy-eyed,’<BR>i. e. a king or minister who uses spies as his eyes,<BR>one who employs spies or agents and sees through<BR>their medium; (उस्), n. espionage.<BR>—चार-चण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, graceful in gait or motion.<BR>—चार-चुञ्चु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, graceful in walking, of graceful carriage.<BR>—चार-ज्या, f. the sine of the ascensional difference.<BR>—चार-पथ, अस्, m. a place where two roads<BR>meet.<BR>—चार-भट, अस्, m. a valorous warrior.<BR>—चार-वायु, उस्, m. summer air, zephyr.<BR>—चारान्-<BR>तरित (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m. a secret emissary or spy.<BR>—चारेक्षण (˚र-ईक्˚), अस्, m. a statesman, a<BR>minister or king (who employs spies).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारक|चारकः
चारक, अस्, इका, अम्, acting, setting to work,<BR>proceeding; composed by Caraka; (अस्), m. a spy,<BR>a secret agent or emissary; a driver, a herdsman,<BR>a leader; an associate, a companion; a groom, a<BR>horseman, a cavalier; a wandering Brāhmanical stu-<BR>dent; a fetter, a bond, a prison; the plant Bucha-<BR>nania Latifolia (= चार); N. of a man; (इका), f. a<BR>female attendant; a cock-roach.<BR>—चारक-त्रिरात्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारकीण
चारकीण, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for a wandering Brāh-<BR>manical student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारण|चारणः
चारण, अस्, m. a wanderer, a pilgrim; a wandering<BR>actor or singer, an actor of note, a dancer, a mime,<BR>a bard, a herald; a celestial singer, a panegyrist of<BR>the gods; a reader of scripture; a spy; N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—चारण-त्व, अम्, n. dancing (the art).<BR>—चारण-दारा, आस्, f. pl. female dancers, actresses,<BR>&c.<BR>—चारण-विद्य or चारण-वैद्य or चारणा-<BR>विद्य, आस्, m. pl., N. of a branch of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारथ
चारथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. going, wandering or<BR>moving about, going in a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारयित्वा
चारयित्वा, ind. having enjoined or prescribed,<BR>having caused to observe; having made to go &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारायण
चारायण, अस्, ई, m. f. a patronymic from Cara;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the author of the Sādhāraṇādhi-<BR>karaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारायणक
चारायणक, अस्, इका, अम्, derived from the<BR>Cārāyaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारायणीय
चारायणीय, आस्, m. pl. the pupils of Cārāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित
चारित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to go; distilled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारितार्थ्य|चारितार्थ्यं
चारितार्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. चरितार्थ), attainment<BR>of an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्र|चारित्रं
चारित्र, अस्, m., N. of a Marut; (आ), f. the tama-<BR>rind tree; (अम्), n. proceeding, manner of acting,<BR>conduct; good conduct, behaviour; good name or<BR>character, reputation; peculiar observance or practice,<BR>peculiarity of customs or conditions; a ceremony.<BR>—चारित्र-कवच, अस्, आ, अम्, cased in the armour<BR>of chastity.<BR>—चारित्र-वती, f., N. of a Samādhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्र्य
चारित्र्य, अम्, n. becoming or honourable practices,<BR>moral conduct, instituted observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिन्
चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, (generally at the end of a comp.)<BR>moving, walking or wandering about, living, being<BR>(e. g. पाद-चारिन्, going on foot; निमेषान्तर-<BR>चारिन्, going in an instant, arriving after a short<BR>interval &c.), [cf. अम्बु-चारिन्, एक-च्˚, ख-च्˚, &c.];<BR>acting, proceeding, doing, practising; living on; (ई),<BR>m. a foot soldier; (इणी), f., N. of a plant, = करुणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारटिका
चारटिका चारटिका, f. a kind of perfume,<BR>= नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारटी
चारटी चारटी, f., N. of two plants, = पद्-<BR>म-चारिणी an भूम्य्-आमली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारभट|चारभटः
चारभट चारभट, अस्, m. a courageous<BR>man, a hero, a chief, a warrior; (ई), f. courage; [cf.<BR>आरभट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिवाच्
चारिवाच् चारिवाच्, क्, f., N. of a plant, =<BR>कर्कट-शृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारु|चारुः
चारु चारु, उस्, वी, उ (said to be fr. rt. चर्,<BR>perhaps connected with 2. चन्), agreeable, welcome,<BR>approved, esteemed, beloved, dear (with dat. or loc. of<BR>the person, e. g. वरुणाय or वरुणे चारुः, dear to<BR>Varuṇa), pleasing, lovely, beautiful, pretty, elegant;<BR>(उस्), m. an epithet of Bṛhaspati; N. of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Rukmiṇī; of a Cakra-vartin; (री), f. a<BR>beautiful woman; splendor; moonlight; intelligence;<BR>N. of the wife of Kuvera; (उ), n. a various reading<BR>for वर, saffron; [cf. Eng. fair; Brit. kaer.]<BR>—चारु-कर्ण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having beautiful<BR>ears.<BR>—चारु-केशरा, f. a kind of grass, Cyperus, =<BR>नागर-मुस्ता; a kind of tree, = तरुणी.<BR>—चारु-<BR>गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa and Ruk-<BR>miṇī.<BR>—चारु-गीति, इस्, f. a kind of metre, a sort of<BR>Gīti, containing 29+32 syllabic instants.<BR>—चारु-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa and Rukmiṇī.<BR>—चारु-घोण, अस्, आ, अम्, handsome-nosed.<BR>—चारु-<BR>चित्र, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—चारु-<BR>ता, f. or चारु-त्व, अम्, n. loveliness, beauty.<BR>—चारु-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—चारुदत्त-ना-<BR>मन्, आ, m. named Cāru-datta.<BR>—चारु-दन्त, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having beautiful teeth,’ N. of a merchant's son.<BR>—चारु-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, good-looking.<BR>—चारु-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चारु-देष्ण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Gaṇḍūṣa; also of a son of Kṛṣṇa by<BR>Rukmiṇī.<BR>—चारु-धामन्, आ, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—चारु-धामा or चारु-धारा, f. an epithet of<BR>Śacī, the wife of Indra.<BR>—चारु-धिष्ण्य, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the Saptarṣayas in the eleventh Man-<BR>vantara.<BR>—चारु-नालक, अम्, n. a kind of lotus with<BR>red flowers.<BR>—चारु-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having beautiful<BR>eyes; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—चारु-पद, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Namasyu.<BR>—चारु-पर्णी, f., N.<BR>of a plant, = प्र-सारणी.<BR>—चारु-पुट, अस्, m. a<BR>particular time in music.<BR>—चारु-प्रतीक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. of lovely appearance.<BR>—चारु-फला, f. a<BR>vine, a grape.<BR>—चारु-बाहु, उस्, or चारु-भद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa by Rukmiṇī.<BR>—चारु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, lovely, beautiful; (आन्),<BR>m., N. of a Cakra-vartin; (ती), f., N. of a daughter<BR>of Kṛṣṇa by Rukmiṇī.<BR>—चारु-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>handsome-faced, fair, beauteous; (ई), f., N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of ten syllables each.<BR>—चारु-<BR>यशस्, आस्, m. ‘of fair fame,’ N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa<BR>by Rukmiṇī; [cf. चारु.]<BR>—चारु-रथ, अस् or अम्,<BR>m. or n. (?), N. of a forest.<BR>—चारु-रावा, f. an epithet<BR>of Śacī, the wife of Indra.<BR>—चारु-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>lovely-eyed, having beautiful eyes; (अस्), m. a deer,<BR>antelope; (आ), f. a woman with fine eyes.<BR>—चारु-वक्-<BR>त्र, अस्, m. ‘handsome-faced,’ N. of one of Skanda's<BR>attendants.<BR>—चारु-वर्धना, f. a woman.<BR>—चारु-<BR>विन्द, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa by Rukmiṇī.<BR>—चारु-वेश, अस्, m. ‘well-dressed,’ = the preceding.<BR>—चारु-व्रता, f. a female who fasts for a whole<BR>month.<BR>—चारु-शिला, f. ‘beautiful stone,’ a jewel, a<BR>gem.<BR>—चारु-शीर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चारु-<BR>शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a lovely nature, beautiful.<BR>—चारु-<BR>श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa by Rukmiṇī.<BR>—चारु-सर्वाङ्ग-दर्शन (˚व-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a beautiful appearance in all the limbs.<BR>—चारु-<BR>हासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smiling sweetly; (इनी), f., N. of a<BR>metre containing 4 × 14 syllabic instants.<BR>—चार्व्-<BR>अङ्गी, f. a beautifully formed woman.<BR>—चार्व्-आघाट<BR>or चार्व्-आघात, अस्, आ, अम्, destructive of beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुक|चारुकः
चारुक, अस्, m. the seed of Saccharum Śara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्चिक
चार्चिक चार्चिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चर्चा), con-<BR>versant with the repetitions (in the recitation of the<BR>Veda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्चिक्य|चार्चिक्यं|चार्च्चिक्य|चार्च्चिक्यं
चार्चिक्य, अम्, n. perfuming the person, smearing<BR>it with sandal &c.; unguent; [cf. चर्चिक्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म|चार्म्म|चार्म्मः
चार्म चार्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चर्मन्), made<BR>of hide or leather, leathern; covered with leather (as<BR>a car &c.); defended by a hide or skin; shielded,<BR>having a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मण|चार्म्मण|चार्म्मणं
चार्मण, अस्, ई, अम्, covered with skin or leather;<BR>(अम्), n. a multitude of hides or of shields &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिक|चार्म्मिक
चार्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, leather, made of leather, be-<BR>longing to the skin &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिकायणि|चार्म्मिकायणि
चार्मिकायणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Carmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिण|चार्मिणं|चार्म्मिण|चार्म्मिणं
चार्मिण, अम्, n. a number of men armed with<BR>shields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्य
चार्य चार्य, अस्, m., N. of a despised caste,<BR>the son of an outcast Vaiśya; (perhaps for अचार्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्वाक|चार्वाकः|चार्व्वाक|चार्व्वाकः
चार्वाक चार्वाक, अस्, m. (fr. चारु + वाक),<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa described in the Mahā-bh. Śānti-<BR>parva 1414, &c., as a friend of Duryodhana and an<BR>enemy of the Pāṇḍavas; (having taken the shape of<BR>a mendicant Brāhman, when Yudhiṣṭhira entered<BR>Hāstina-pura in triumph, he reviled him and the<BR>assembled Brāhmans, but was soon detected; and<BR>the real Brāhmans, filled with fury, killed him on the<BR>spot); N. of a sophistical philosopher who probably<BR>lived before the composition of the Rāmāyaṇa; see<BR>जावालि. He was a sceptic in matters of Hindū<BR>faith, and considered by the orthodox as an atheist<BR>or materialist; according to some, the sceptical<BR>doctrines of the Indian materialists were handed<BR>down to Cārvāka and his followers by Vācas-pati<BR>or Bṛhaspati, and the aphorisms of Bṛhaspati<BR>(Bārhaspatya sūtras) are said to embody their<BR>opinions; (अस्, ई, अम्), derived from or composed by<BR>Cārvāka.<BR>—चार्वाक-दर्शन, अम्, n. the doctrine<BR>of Cārvāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाल|चालः
चाल चाल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. चल्), the thatch<BR>or roof of a house; the blue jay; shaking, the being<BR>movable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालक|चालकः
चालक, अस्, m. a restive elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालन|चालनं
चालन, अम्, n. causing to move or go, causing to<BR>pass through a sieve, sifting, shaking, moving to<BR>and fro, wagging (as the tail), loosening; muscular<BR>action; (ई), f. a sieve, a strainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालनीय
चालनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be moved, capable of<BR>being moved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाल्य
चाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be moved; to be loosened<BR>or shaken or led away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालिक्य|चालिक्यः
चालिक्य चालिक्य, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाष|चाषः
चाष चाष, अस्, m. the blue jay, Coracias<BR>Indica; (according to some) a kingfisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चास|चासः
चास, अस्, m. the blue jay, Coracias Indica; sugar-<BR>cane.<BR>—चास-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having a face like<BR>that of a jay; (अस्), m., N. of one of the attendants of<BR>Skanda; (आस्), m. pl. a class of demons or evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चि
चि 1. चि, cl. 5. P. A. चिनोति, -नुते, चिकाय<BR>and चिचाय, चिक्ये and चिच्ये, चेष्यति, -ते,<BR>अचैषीत्, चेतुम्, to arrange in order, place in a line,<BR>heap up, pile up, construct (as a sacrificial altar, used<BR>in P. if the priests construct the altar for another, in<BR>A. if the sacrificer builds it for himself); to collect,<BR>gather together, accumulate, gain for one's self; to<BR>cover, inlay, set with (with inst., e. g. रत्नैः, with<BR>jewels): Caus. चाययति or चापयति, or चययति<BR>or चपयति: Desid. चिकीषति, and चिचीषति, to<BR>wish to pile up: Caus. of the Desid. चिचीषयति,<BR>to cause a person to wish to arrange in order or<BR>pile up: Intens. चेचीयते; [cf. Cambro-Brit. cai,<BR>‘collection;’ Lat. cumulus; Pol. kupa; Germ.<BR>Haufen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
1. चय, अस्, m. stacked wood; a mound of earth<BR>raised to form the foundation of a building; a ram-<BR>part or mound of earth raised from the ditch of a<BR>fort; the gate of a fort; any edifice; a seat, a stool;<BR>a cover, a covering; a heap, pile, collection, a multi-<BR>tude, an assemblage, aggregation; the amount or<BR>augment by which each term increases, the common<BR>increase or difference of the terms; [cf. अग्नि-चय;<BR>cf. also Cambro-Brit. cai, ‘collection;’ Hib. scea,<BR>‘plenty, abundance.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयन|चयनं
चयन, अम्, n. the act of collecting, gathering,<BR>heaping up, aggregation; stacking wood; stacked<BR>wood; [cf. अग्नि-चयन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयनीय
चयनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be collected or gathered,<BR>to be heaped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिचीषत्
चिचीषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing to gather or collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
1. चित्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of compounds) piling up<BR>(e. g. अग्नि-चित्, q. v.); forming a layer or stratum,<BR>piled up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित|चितः
चित, अस्, आ, अम्, piled, heaped; collected, gathered,<BR>accumulated; covered, veiled, concealed; (आ), f. a<BR>layer, a pile of wood, a funeral pile, pyre; a heap, an<BR>assemblage, a multitude; (अम्), n. a building (e. g.<BR>पक्वेष्टक-चित, a building of burnt bricks).<BR>—चित-<BR>विस्तर, अस्, m. a kind of ornament.<BR>—चिताग्नि (˚त-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m. the funeral fire.<BR>—चिता-चूडक, अम्, n.<BR>a mark where a funeral pile has been, a mausoleum,<BR>a monument, &c.<BR>—चितैध (˚त-एध), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. belonging or referring to a funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिति|चितिः
1. चिति, इस्, f. a stratum, layer of wood or bricks<BR>&c.; a pile, a stack; a funeral pile; an oblong with<BR>quadrangular sides; collecting, gathering; a heap, a<BR>quantity, a multitude; N. of the eighth or tenth<BR>book of the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa; [cf. अमृत-चिति.]<BR>—चिति-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चितिका
चितिका, f. a stack, a pile; a funeral pile; a small<BR>chain worn as an ornament round the loins, a kind<BR>of girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चितीक
चितीक (at the end of an adj. comp. after a<BR>numeral) = चिति, a layer (e. g. पञ्च-चितीक, त्रि-च्˚,<BR>एक-च्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्य|चित्यं|चित्यः
चित्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be arranged in order or built<BR>up; (scil. अग्नि, fire), placed or constructed upon a<BR>foundation or basis (as of stones &c.); (आ), f. piling<BR>up, building (an altar &c.); a funeral pile; (अम्), n.<BR>the place at which a corpse has been burnt and where<BR>a monument has been erected; a monument or any<BR>mark of the site of a funeral pile.<BR>—चित्याधिरोहण<BR>(˚य-अध्˚), अम्, n. burning with a husband's corpse.<BR>—चित्यारोहण (˚य-आर्˚), अम्, n. ascending the<BR>funeral pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्वत्
1. चिन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, gathering, collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिति|चितिः
चिति, इस्, f., Ved. gathering, collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतव्य
