चिकितायन
चिकितायन, अस्, m. a descendant of Cikita; [cf.<BR>चैकितायन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिति
चिकिति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. knowing, acquainted with,<BR>experienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकितु
चिकितु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. understanding, knowing,<BR>experienced; (उस्), f. understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्वन्
चिकित्वन्, आ, m., Ved. understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्वस्
चिकित्वस्, वान्, उषी, वस्, one who has observed,<BR>observing, attending to, attentive, knowing, under-<BR>standing, experienced, conversant with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्वित्
चिकित्वित्, ind., Ved. with intelligence, intelligently;<BR>with deliberation, deliberately; (Sāy.) making known<BR>(= ज्ञापयन्तीम् in Ṛg-veda IV. 52, 4).<BR>—चिकित्विन्-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one whose mind is attentive;<BR>coming from an intelligent mind, well considered;<BR>(Sāy.) one who knows all hearts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सक|चिकित्सकः
चिकित्सक, अस्, m. a physician, doctor, practiser in<BR>medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सन|चिकित्सनं
चिकित्सन, अम्, n. healing, practising medicine,<BR>medical attendance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सा
चिकित्सा, f. the practice or science of medicine,<BR>healing, curing, administering or applying remedies;<BR>(in the system of medicine) one of the six sections,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">Page0323-b+ 81</a>]<BR>therapeutics.<BR>—चिकित्सा-कलिका, f. title of a medical<BR>work by Tīśaṭa.<BR>—चिकित्साकलिका-टीका, f. a com-<BR>mentary on the last work by Candraṭa.<BR>—चिकित्सा-<BR>कौमुदी, f. title of a medical work by Kāśī-rāja.<BR>—चिकित्सा-तत्त्व-ज्ञान, अम्, n. title of a medical<BR>work by Dhanvantari.<BR>—चिकित्सा-दर्पण, अम्, n.<BR>title of a medical work by Divodāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सित|चिकित्सितं
चिकित्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, treated medically, remedied,<BR>healed, physicked, cured; (अम्), n. healing, reme-<BR>dying, medical attendance; pl. the chapters of the<BR>therapeutical section of medicine; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सु
चिकित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. wise, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्स्य
चिकित्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be treated medically, to<BR>be cured, curable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
5. चित्, त्, f. thought, intelligence, intellect, under-<BR>standing, mind; the soul, heart.<BR>—चिच्-चन्द्रिका, f.<BR>title of a commentary on the Prabodha-candrodaya<BR>by Gaṇeśa.<BR>—चिच्-छक्ति (चित्+शक्ति), इस्, f. mental<BR>power, intellectual capacity.<BR>—चिच्-छुक (चित्-शु˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a scholiast on the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa;<BR>(ई), f. or चित्-सुखी, f. the commentary written by<BR>this scholiast.<BR>—चित्-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the lord of<BR>thought.<BR>—चित्-प्रवृत्ति, इस्, f. thinking, reflection.<BR>—चित्-स्वरूप, अम्, n. pure intelligence, an epithet<BR>of the Supreme.<BR>—चिद्-अचिच्छक्ति-युक्त (-अचित्-<BR>श˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having power over matter and<BR>spirit.<BR>—चिद्-अम्बर, अस्, m., N. of the author of a<BR>law-book.<BR>—चिद्-अस्थि-माला, f. title of a commen-<BR>tary on a grammatical work.<BR>—चिद्-आत्मक, अम्, n.<BR>consciousness, perception.<BR>—चिद्-आत्मन्, आ, m. the<BR>thinking principle, pure intelligence, spirit.<BR>—चिद्-<BR>उल्लास, अस्, आ, अम्, gladdening the mind or heart.<BR>—चिद्-गगन-चन्द्रिका, f. title of a literary work.<BR>—चिद्-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of intelligence;<BR>wise, intelligent, of liberal or expansive mind;<BR>amiable, good-hearted; (अम्), n. pure intelligence,<BR>the Supreme Being as identified with intellect or<BR>intelligence.<BR>—चिद्-विलास, अस्, m. a pupil of Śaṅ-<BR>karācārya.<BR>—चिन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, spiritual, ‘all<BR>intelligence,’ as an epithet of the Deity; (अम्), n.<BR>pure intelligence.<BR>—चिन्-मात्र, अम्, n. pure in-<BR>telligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिति|चितिः
2. चिति, इस्, f. understanding; (इस्), m. the thinking<BR>mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्त|चित्तं
चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, perceived, observed, considered;<BR>reflected upon; resolved; intended, aimed at, under-<BR>stood; visible, perceptible; (अम्), n. attending, ob-<BR>serving; thinking, reflecting, imagining, thought;<BR>intention, aim, wish; the heart considered as the<BR>seat of intellect; the mind, the reasoning faculty;<BR>intellect, reason; reason personified; [cf. अ-चित्त,<BR>इह-च्˚, चल-च्˚, पूर्व-च्˚, प्रायश्-च्˚, &c.]<BR>—चित्त-<BR>कलित, अस्, आ, अम्, anticipated, expected, calculated;<BR>known.<BR>—चित्त-गर्भा, f., Ved. visibly pregnant.<BR>—चित्त-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, proceeding or acting accord-<BR>ing to the wish of another (with gen.)<BR>—चित्त-जन्मन्,<BR>आ, m. produced within the mind, love, the god of love;<BR>[cf. चित्त-भू, चित्त-योनि, मनसि-ज.]<BR>—चित्त-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing the hearts, heart-searching.<BR>—चित्तज्ञ-ता, f. knowledge of the heart.<BR>—चित्त-<BR>नाश, अस्, m. loss of conscience.<BR>—चित्त-निर्व्रित्ति,<BR>इस्, f. contentment of mind, happiness.<BR>—चित्त-<BR>प्रमाथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, moving or touching the heart,<BR>exciting passion or love, afflicting the mind.<BR>—चित्त-<BR>प्रशम, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied in mind, composed,<BR>complacent, tranquil, content.<BR>—चित्त-प्रसन्न-ता,<BR>f. happiness of the mind, gaiety, joy.<BR>—चित्त-प्र-<BR>सादन, अम्, n. gladdening of the mind.<BR>—चित्त-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the thoughts, felt, per-<BR>ceived.<BR>—चित्त-भेद, अस्, m. inconsistency, con-<BR>trariety of purpose or will.<BR>—चित्त-भू, ऊस्, m. love,<BR>the god of love.<BR>—चित्त-भ्रम-चिकित्सा, f. ‘medical<BR>treatment of mental derangement,’ a chapter of the<BR>medical work Vaidya-vallabha.<BR>—चित्त-मोह, अस्,<BR>m. confusion or infatuation of mind.<BR>—चित्त-योनि,<BR>इस्, m. love; see चित्त-जन्मन्.<BR>—चित्त-राग, अस्,<BR>m. affection, passion, desire.<BR>—चित्त-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, endowed with understanding, reasonable; kind-<BR>hearted, amiable.<BR>—चित्तवत्-कर्तृक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(a root) employing an intelligent agent (e. g. देव-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-c" target="_blank">Page0323-c+ 81</a>]<BR>दत्तः पचति, Deva-datta cooks).<BR>—चित्त-विकार,<BR>अस्, m. change of thoughts or feelings, disturbance of<BR>mind.<BR>—चित्त-विकारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, changing a person's<BR>character or feeling.<BR>—चित्त-विनाशन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>destroying the conscience.<BR>—चित्त-विप्लव, अस्, m.<BR>disturbance of mind, madness, insanity.<BR>—चित्त-<BR>विभ्रम, अस्, m. derangement of mind, madness.<BR>—चित्त-विश्लेष, अस्, m. parting of hearts, breach<BR>of friendship.<BR>—चित्त-वृत्ति, इस्, f. disposition of<BR>mind, feeling; inward purpose, emotion; thinking,<BR>imagining.<BR>—चित्त-वेदना, f. anxiety, affliction.<BR>—चित्त-वैकल्य, अम्, n. bewilderment of mind,<BR>distraction, perplexity.<BR>—चित्त-संहति, इस्, f. a<BR>multitude of thoughts or emotions, many minds.<BR>—चित्त-सङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, pervading the heart,<BR>penetrating the soul, knowing the thoughts.<BR>—चित्त-<BR>समुन्नति, इस्, f. pride of heart, arrogance, hau-<BR>teur, haughtiness.<BR>—चित्त-स्थ or चित्त-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fixed in the mind, being in the heart;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Samādhi.<BR>—चित्त-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>stealing the heart, fascinating, agreeable, beautiful.<BR>—चित्त-हृत्, त्, त्, त्, fascinating, winning.<BR>—चित्ता-<BR>नुवर्तिन् (˚त-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, gratifying wishes,<BR>humouring.<BR>—चित्तापहारक (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, or चित्तापहारिन् (˚त-अप्˚), ई, इणी, इ, heart-<BR>stealing, captivating, attractive.<BR>—चित्ताभोग (˚त-<BR>आभ्˚), अस्, m. full consciousness, consciousness of<BR>pleasure or pain, the attention of the mind to its<BR>own sensations.<BR>—चित्तासङ्ग (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, m.<BR>attachment, affection, love.<BR>—चित्तैक्य (˚त-ऐक्˚),<BR>अम्, n. unanimity, harmony, agreement.<BR>—चित्तोन्-<BR>नति (˚त-उन्˚), इस्, f. pride of heart, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्ति|चित्तिः
1. चित्ति, इस्, f. thinking, thought, reflection; under-<BR>standing, wisdom; thoughts, devotion (in pl.); inten-<BR>tion; a wise person; thought personified as the wife<BR>of Atharvan and mother of Dadhyac; [cf. अ-चित्ति,<BR>पूर्व-चित्ति, प्रायश्-चित्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तिन्
चित्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. intelligent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तीकृ
चित्ती-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>make anything an object of thought or reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तीकृत
चित्ती-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed in the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, perceptible, visible, conspicuous,<BR>excellent, distinguished; bright, clear, bright-coloured;<BR>variegated, spotted, speckled; rough, agitated (as the<BR>sea, opposed to सम); clear, loud, perceptible (as<BR>a sound); various, different, manifold; strange,<BR>wonderful, surprising, (किम् अत्र चित्रम्, what is<BR>there surprising in that? there is nothing strange in<BR>that); containing the word चित्र; (अस्), m. variety<BR>of colour; N. of several plants, viz. Plumbago Zey-<BR>lanica, Ricinus Communis, Jonesia Aśoka; a form<BR>of Yama; N. of a king; of a descendant of Gaṅga<BR>and of Gauśra; of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a king<BR>of Draviḍa; (आ), f. Spica Virginis, a star in the<BR>virgin's spike, a constellation; (according to the<BR>more ancient reckoning the twelfth, according to the<BR>new the fourteenth lunar mansion); a kind of snake;<BR>N. of several plants, viz. Anthericum Tuberosum or<BR>Salvinia Cucculata, Cucumis Maderaspatanus, a kind<BR>of cucumber; also = दन्ती; Ricinus Communis; the<BR>Myrobalan tree; also = मृगेर्वारु and गण्ड-<BR>दूर्वा; Rubia Munjista; N. of a metre, a kind of<BR>Mātrāsamaka, containing 4 × 16 syllabic instants;<BR>another metre consisting of four lines of fifteen<BR>syllables each; another metre consisting of four lines<BR>of sixteen syllables each; worldly illusion, unreality;<BR>N. of an Apsaras; also of a sister of Kṛṣṇa and<BR>wife of Arjuṇa, = सु-भद्रा; also of a daughter of<BR>Gada, or (according to a various reading) of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>also of a river; (अम्), n. anything bright or coloured<BR>which strikes the eyes; a brilliant ornament, an<BR>ornament; a bright or extraordinary appearance, a<BR>wonder; the ether, sky, heaven; a spot; a circular<BR>ornament, a sectarial mark on the forehead; white<BR>or spotted leprosy; a picture, painting, sketch, de-<BR>lineation: variety of colour; various modes of writing<BR>or arranging verses in the shape of mathematical or<BR>other fanciful figures, (this is done either by leaving<BR>out syllables which occur repeatedly, or by represent-<BR>ing words in a shortened form); playing upon words,<BR>punning in the form of question and answer, facetious<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0324-a" target="_blank">Page0324-a+ 81</a>]<BR>conversation, conundrums, riddles, &c.; [cf. अ-चित्र,<BR>दानु-च्˚, वि-च्˚, चैत्र; cf. also Lith. kytras.]<BR>—चित्र-कण्ठ, अस्, m. ‘having a speckled throat,’<BR>a pigeon.<BR>—चित्र-कथालाप-सुख (˚था-आल्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, happy in telling charming stories.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>कम्बल, अस्, m. a variegated carpet; a painted cloth<BR>used as an elephant's housing.<BR>—चित्र-कर, अस्, m.<BR>a painter; [cf. चित्र-कार and चित्र-कृत्.]<BR>—चित्र-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m. ‘strange-ear,’ N. of a camel.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. any extraordinary act, a wonderful deed;<BR>magic; ornamenting, decorating; painting, a paint-<BR>ing, picture; (आ), m. working wonders, a magician;<BR>a painter; the tree Dalbergia Ougeinensis; [cf. चित्र-<BR>कृत्.]<BR>—चित्रकर्म-विद्, त्, m. skilled in the art of<BR>painting; a painter, a magician.<BR>—चित्र-काय, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a striped or speckled body,’ a tiger, a leopard,<BR>panther.<BR>—चित्र-कार, अस्, m. a painter; [cf. चित्र-<BR>कर.]<BR>—चित्र-कुण्डल, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—चित्र-कूट, अस्, m. ‘wonderful peak,’<BR>N. of a hill and district, the modern Chitrakote or<BR>Chatarcot (near Kampta), situated on the river Pai-<BR>suni (Piśunī) about fifty miles S. E. of the town of<BR>Bandah in Bundelkhund, lat. 25. 12, long. 80. 47.<BR>It was the first habitation of Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa<BR>in their exile after leaving Ayodhyā, and as the holiest<BR>spot of the worshippers of Rāma is crowded with<BR>temples and shrines; N. of a town.<BR>—चित्र-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, astonishing, surprising; (त्), m. a painter; the<BR>tree Dalbergia Ougeinensis; [cf. चित्र-कर्मन्.]<BR>—चित्र-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Garuḍa; also<BR>of Vasiṣṭha; also of Lakṣmaṇa; also of Deva-<BR>bhāga; also of a king of the Śūra-senas.<BR>—चित्र-कोल,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of lizard.<BR>—चित्र-क्रिया, f. painting.<BR>—चित्र-क्षत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one whose do-<BR>minion is brilliant (as Agni); (Sāy.) having various<BR>power or one whose wealth is visible.<BR>—चित्र-ग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, represented in a picture, painted.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, coloured, variegated; represented<BR>in a picture, painted, delineated.<BR>—चित्र-गन्ध,<BR>अम्, n. yellow orpiment.<BR>—चित्र-गुप्त, अस्, m., N.<BR>of one of the beings recording the vices and virtues<BR>of mankind in Yama's world; N. of a mixed caste, a<BR>secretary or writer of a man of rank; a form of Yama;<BR>N. of the sixteenth Arhat of the future Utsarpiṇī.<BR>—चित्र-गृह, अस्, m. a painted room, or one<BR>ornamented with pictures; [cf. चित्र-शाला.]<BR>—चित्र-<BR>गो, औस्, औस्, उ, having a brindled cow.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘speckled-neck,’ N. of a pigeon-king.<BR>—चित्र-चाप, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra.<BR>—चित्र-जल्प, अस्, m. talking on various<BR>things, talking incoherently.<BR>—चित्र-तण्डुल, अम्,<BR>आ, n. f. a medicinal plant said to possess anthelmintic<BR>virtues; [cf. विड्-अङ्ग.]<BR>—चित्र-तल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>painted or variegated on the surface.<BR>—चित्र-त्वच्,<BR>क्, m. ‘having curious bark,’ the birch or bhūrja tree.<BR>—चित्र-दण्डक, अस्, m. the cotton plant, Arum<BR>Campanulatum; [cf. ओल.]<BR>—चित्र-दर्शन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Brāhman changed into a bird (‘having varie-<BR>gated eyes’).<BR>—चित्र-दीप, अस्, m. title of a philo-<BR>sophical work.<BR>—चित्र-दृशीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>looking brilliant or shining.<BR>—चित्र-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the attendants of Skanda; (ई), f., N. of<BR>a plant, = महेन्द्र-वारुणी.<BR>—चित्र-धर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a prince identified with the Asura Virū-<BR>pākṣa.<BR>—चित्र-धा, ind. in a manifold way.<BR>—चित्र-ध्रजति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. making a bright<BR>line, an epithet of Agni; (Sāy.) having a wonderful<BR>course.<BR>—चित्र-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—चित्र-नेत्रा, f. a small bird called Maina, =<BR>सारिका; [cf. चित्र-लोचना and चित्राक्षी.]<BR>—चित्र-<BR>न्यस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, represented in a picture, painted.<BR>—चित्र-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having variegated wings;<BR>(अस्), m. the francoline partridge; N. of a demon<BR>causing head-ache.<BR>—चित्र-पट or चित्र-पट्ट, अस्<BR>or अम्, m. or n. (?), a painting, a picture.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>पट्ट-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘committed to a picture,’<BR>painted.<BR>—चित्र-पत्त्रिका, f., N. of a plant, =<BR>कपित्थ-पर्णी and द्रोण-पुष्पी.<BR>—चित्र-पत्त्री,<BR>f., N. of an aquatic plant; [cf. जल-पिप्पली.]<BR>—चित्र-<BR>पद, अस्, आ, अम्, divided into various parts; full of<BR>graceful words or expressions; (आ), f., N. of the plant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0324-b" target="_blank">Page0324-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Cissus Pedata [cf. गोधापदी]; N. of a metre con-<BR>sisting of four lines of eight syllables each; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a metre consisting of four lines of twenty-<BR>three syllables each.<BR>—चित्रपद-क्रमम्, ind. at<BR>a good or brisk pace.<BR>—चित्र-पर्णिका, f., N. of a<BR>plant, commonly Cākulīya, Hemionites Cordifolia;<BR>Bengal madder, Rubia Munjista, = अति-गुहा, घृष्-<BR>ठिला, त्रि-पर्णी, दीर्घ-पत्त्रा, &c.<BR>—चित्र-पर्णी,<BR>f., N. of several plants, = पृश्नि-पर्णी, कर्ण-<BR>स्फोटा, जल-पिप्पली, द्रोण-पुष्पी; also = Rubia<BR>Munjista.<BR>—चित्र-पाटल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>—चित्र-पादा, f. a small bird com-<BR>monly called Maina; [cf. सारिका.]<BR>—चित्र-पिच्छक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a variegated tail,’ a peacock.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>पुङ्ख, अस्, m. ‘having variegated feathers,’ an<BR>arrow.<BR>—चित्र-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>पुष्पी, f., N. of a shrub, = अम्बष्ठा.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>पृष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘speckled-back,’ a sparrow.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>प्रतिकृति, इस्, f. a representation in colours, a paint-<BR>ing, a picture.<BR>—चित्र-प्रिय-कथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>speaking very kindly.<BR>—चित्र-फल, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of fish, commonly Chitala, Mystus Chitala; a kind of<BR>cucumber, Cucumis Sativus; (आ), f. a kind of fish,<BR>commonly Phalaï, = फलकिन्, महोन्मद, राज-<BR>ग्रीव, Mystus Karpirat; N. of several plants, =<BR>चिर्भिटा, मृगेर्वारु, महेन्द्र-वारुणी, वार्ताकी,<BR>कण्टकारी; (ई), f. the above fish.<BR>—चित्र-फ-<BR>लक, अम्, n. a tablet for painting, a picture, a<BR>painting; (अस्), m. a kind of fish; see above.<BR>—चित्र-बर्ह, अस्, m. ‘having a variegated tail,’<BR>a peacock; N. of a son of Garuḍa.<BR>—चित्र-बर्हिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, having a variegated tail.<BR>—चित्र-बर्हिस्,<BR>इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having a brilliant or shining litter<BR>(i. e. bed of stars), an epithet of Pūṣan and the<BR>moon; (Sāy.) strewed with various grasses (as the<BR>ground).<BR>—चित्र-बाहु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—चित्र-भानु, उस्, उस्, उ, of varie-<BR>gated lustre, shining with light; epithet of Agni,<BR>Savitṛ, the Aśvins, &c.; (उस्), m. a N. of fire; of Śiva;<BR>the plant Plumbago Zeylanica; the sun; N. of the<BR>Calotropis Gigantea (= अर्क); the first year of the<BR>first cycle of Jupiter; an epithet of Bhairava, a form of<BR>Śiva; N. of the father of Vāṇa-bhaṭṭa, the author of<BR>the Kādambarī.<BR>—चित्र-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>into a picture, painted.<BR>—चित्र-भेषजा, f. the tree<BR>Ficus Oppositifolia; [cf. काकोडुम्बर.]<BR>—चित्र-<BR>मण्डल, अस्, m. a kind of snake.<BR>—चित्र-महस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having extraordinary abundance;<BR>(Sāy.) having conspicuous brightness or splendor.<BR>—चित्र-मृग, अस्, m. the spotted antelope.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>मेखल, अस्, m. ‘girdled with spots,’ a peacock.<BR>—चित्र-यज्ञ, अस्, m. title of a comedy by Vaidya-<BR>nātha.<BR>—चित्र-यान, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>याम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a splendid or brilliant<BR>course (as Agni).<BR>—चित्र-योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fighting<BR>in a wonderful manner or in various ways; (ई), m.<BR>an epithet of Arjuna; the tree Terminalia Arjuna.<BR>—चित्र-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a bright or splen-<BR>did chariot (as Agni); (अस्), m. ‘having a variegated<BR>car,’ the sun; the king of the Gandharvas; N. of a<BR>snake-demon; of a Vidyā-dhara; of a son of Gada<BR>or (according to a various reading) of Kṛṣṇa; of a<BR>king; of a king of the Aṅgas; of a descendant of<BR>Aṅga and son of Dharma-ratha; of a son of Ushadgu;<BR>of Vṛṣṇi; of Gaya; of Su-pārśvaka; of Ukta; of<BR>a prince of Mṛttikāvatī; of a Sūta; and of others;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river; [cf. चैत्ररथ.]<BR>—चित्र-<BR>रश्मि, इस्, m., N. of a Marut (‘having variegated<BR>rays’).<BR>—चित्र-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting wonderful<BR>or excellent gifts, epithet of the Aśvins.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. bestowing excellent favour;<BR>(Sāy.) having wonderful wealth.<BR>—चित्र-रेफ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Medhātithi, king of Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—चित्र-लता, f. the plant Rubia Munjista; [cf.<BR>चित्र-पर्णी.]<BR>—चित्र-लिखन, अम्, n. ‘variegated<BR>drawing,’ paining.<BR>—चित्र-लिखित, अस्, आ, अम्, repre-<BR>sented, delineated (as in a picture), painted; motion-<BR>less, dumb (as a picture or statue).<BR>—चित्र-लेखक,<BR>अस्, m. a painter.<BR>—चित्र-लेखनिका, f. a painter's<BR>brush.<BR>—चित्र-लेखा, f. a picture, a portrait; N. of<BR>a metre of four lines of seventeen syllables each;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0324-c" target="_blank">Page0324-c+ 81</a>]<BR>another metre of the same sort; N. of a metre of<BR>four lines of eighteen syllables each; N. of an Apsaras<BR>born from Brahmā's hand, (she was a friend of Ūṣā<BR>and skilful in painting); N. of a daughter of Kum-<BR>bhāṇḍa, minister of king Vāṇa, also a friend of<BR>Ūṣā.<BR>—चित्रलेखा-द्वितीया, f. having Citralekhā<BR>as a second, accompanied by Citralekhā.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>लोचना, f. ‘having variegated eyes,’ a small bird,<BR>commonly called Maina, = सारिका; [cf. चित्र-नेत्रा<BR>and चित्राक्षी.]<BR>—चित्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, decorated<BR>with paintings or ornaments; containing the word<BR>चित्र; (ती), f., N. of a metre of four lines of thirteen<BR>syllables each; N. of a daughter of Gada or (accord-<BR>ing to others) of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—चित्र-वदाल, अस्, m.<BR>the sheat-fish, Silurus Pelorius, = पाठीन.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>वन, अम्, n. wonderful wood,’ N. of a wood<BR>near the Gaṇḍakī; [cf. चित्रक.]<BR>—चित्र-वर्मन्,<BR>आ, m. ‘having variegated arrows,’ N. of a son of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; also of a king of the Kulūtas; N. of<BR>a king of Mathura and Campāvatī.<BR>—चित्र-वर्षिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, raining in an unusual manner.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>वल्लिक, अस्, m. a kind of sheat-fish, Silurus Boalis;<BR>[cf. चित्र-वदाल.]<BR>—चित्र-वल्ली, f., N. of two<BR>plants, = मृगेर्वारु and महेन्द्र-वारुणी.<BR>—चि-<BR>त्र-वहा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चित्र-वाज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>decorated with variegated feathers; possessed of ex-<BR>cellent power; (Sāy.) making wonderful progress or<BR>having wonderful riches or strength; (अस्), m. a cock.<BR>—चित्र-वाण, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra.<BR>—चित्र-वाहन, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Maṇi-pūra.<BR>—चित्र-विचित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, variously<BR>coloured, variegated, multiform.<BR>—चित्र-विद्या, f. the<BR>art of painting.<BR>—चित्र-वीर्य, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Ricinus, = रक्तैरण्ड.<BR>—चित्र-वृत्ति, इस्, f. any<BR>astonishing act or practice.<BR>—चित्र-वेगिक, अस्, m.<BR>‘having wonderful velocity,’ N. of a Nāga.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>वेश, अस्, m. ‘having a variegated dress,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—चित्र-शाला, f. a painted room, or one<BR>decorated with pictures [cf. चित्र-गृह]; N. of a<BR>metre consisting of four lines of eighteen syllables<BR>each.<BR>—चित्रशिखण्डि-ज or चित्रशिखण्डि-प्र-<BR>सूत, अस्, m. epithet of Bṛhaspati or the planet<BR>Jupiter (regarded as the son of the Citraśikhaṇḍinas,<BR>but more properly of Aṅgiras).<BR>—चित्र-शिखण्डिन्,<BR>इनस्, m. pl. ‘having bright crests,’ an epithet of the<BR>seven Ṛṣis, Marīci, Atri, Aṅgiras, Pulastya, Pulaha,<BR>Kratu, and Vasiṣṭha, as represented in the seven<BR>principal stars of the Great Bear.<BR>—चित्र-शिरस्, आस्,<BR>m. ‘having a variegated head,’ a kind of venomous<BR>insect [cf. चित्र-शीर्षक]; N. of a Gandharva.<BR>—चित्र-शीर्षक, अस्, m. a kind of venomous insect.<BR>—चित्र-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. shining brilliantly;<BR>epithet of Agni.<BR>—चित्र-श्रवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>uttering loud cries, songs, &c.; worthy of loud praise;<BR>(Sāy.) having wonderful fame.<BR>—चित्र-श्री, ईस्, f.<BR>great beauty, the beauty of variegated colours.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>संस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, represented in a picture, deli-<BR>neated, painted; [cf. चित्र-गत, चित्र-स्थ, &c.]<BR>—चित्र-सङ्ग, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>metre of four lines of sixteen syllables each.<BR>—चित्र-<BR>सर्प, अस्, m. a kind of snake, the large speckled<BR>snake (Mālu-dhāna).<BR>—चित्र-सेन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>furnished with a brilliant spear; (Sāy.) having a<BR>bright weapon; (अस्), m., N. of a snake-demon;<BR>also of a leader of the Gandharvas who was a son of<BR>Viśvā-vasu; one of the judges or recorders of hell;<BR>N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a son of Parīkṣit;<BR>of a son of Sambara; of a son of Nariṣyanta; of a<BR>son of the thirteenth Manu; of a son of Gada; N.<BR>of an adversary of Kṛṣṇa; of Jarā-sandha's general<BR>who is also called Ḍimbhaka; (आ), f., N. of an<BR>Apsaras; also of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda; N. of a river.<BR>—चित्रसेन-भट्ट, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of a commentary entitled Piṅgala-<BR>chando-grantha-ṭīkā.<BR>—चित्र-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, repre-<BR>sented in a picture, painted; [cf. चित्र-गत and<BR>चित्र-संस्थ.]<BR>—चित्र-हस्त, अम्, n. a particular<BR>position of the hands in fighting.<BR>—चित्राकृति (˚र-<BR>आक्˚), इस्, f. a painted resemblance, portrait, picture.<BR>—चित्राक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘having variegated<BR>eyes,’ N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; also of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">Page0325-a+ 81</a>]<BR>descendant of Parīkṣit; also of a Nāga-rāja; (ई),<BR>f. a kind of bird, commonly called Maina; [cf. सा-<BR>रिका, चित्र-नेत्रा, चित्र-लोचना.]<BR>—चित्रा-क्षुप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a plant, = द्रोण-पुष्पी.<BR>—चित्राङ्ग<BR>(˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a variegated or spotted<BR>body, striped, painted; (अस्), m. a kind of snake;<BR>the plant Plumbago Zeylanica; another plant, =<BR>रक्त-चित्रक; N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; an<BR>epithet of Arjuna; N. given to various animals in<BR>fables; (ई), f. a kind of worm or ear-wig, Julus Cor-<BR>nifex; the plant Rubia Munjista; (अम्), n. vermilion;<BR>yellow orpiment.<BR>—चित्राङ्गद (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, decorated with brilliant or variegated bracelets;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Śāntanu; of a king of the<BR>Daśārṇas; of a Vidyā-dhara; of a Gandharva or<BR>chief of the Gandharvas; a judge and recorder of the<BR>deeds of men in Yama's kingdom or the lower<BR>regions; a secretary of a person of rank (?); (आ),<BR>f., N. of an Apsaras; a daughter of king Citra-<BR>vāhana, wife of Arjuna and mother of Babhru-vāhana.<BR>—चित्राङ्गद-सू, ऊस्, f. the mother of Citrāṅgada,<BR>an epithet of Satyavatī, the mother of Vyāsa.<BR>—चित्रा-<BR>टीर, अस्, m. (fr. चित्रा +?), the moon; the forehead<BR>spotted with the blood of a goat slain in honour of<BR>the demon Ghaṇṭā-karṇa.<BR>—चित्रान्न (˚र-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. variegated rice, rice dressed with coloured<BR>condiments.<BR>—चित्रापूप (˚र-अप्˚), अस्, m. a kind<BR>of cake (lit. speckled cake, plum cake ?).<BR>—चित्रा-<BR>मघ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bestowing brilliant gifts,<BR>an epithet of Uṣas; (Sāy.) having wonderful wealth.<BR>—चित्रायस (˚र-अय्˚), अम्, n. steel.<BR>—चित्रायुध<BR>(˚र-आय्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—चित्रायुस् (˚र-आय्˚), उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. possessed of<BR>excellent vital power; (Sāy.) making wonderful pro-<BR>gress or having excellent food.<BR>—चित्रारम्भ (˚र-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, m. the outline of a picture, a sketch,<BR>drawing; (अस्, आ, अम्), represented in a picture.<BR>—चित्रार्पित (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, committed to<BR>a picture, painted.<BR>—चित्रा-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>rich in brilliant ornaments; decorated with shining<BR>stars, an epithet of the night.<BR>—चित्राश्व (˚र-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘having painted horses,’ epithet of Satyavat as<BR>fond of painting horses.<BR>—चित्रेश (˚रा-ईश), अस्, m. lord<BR>of Citrā, i. e. the moon.<BR>—चित्रोक्ति (˚र-उक्˚), इस्, f.<BR>a marvellous voice or speech, a voice from heaven,<BR>the voice of an invisible speaker; a surprising tale;<BR>agreeable or eloquent discourse.<BR>—चित्रोति (˚र-ऊति),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. one who gives excellent proofs of his<BR>love, one who bestows pleasure or happiness; (Sāy.)<BR>granting wonderful assistance.<BR>—चित्रोपला (˚र-<BR>उप्˚), f., N. of a river.<BR>—चित्रौदन (˚र-ओद्˚),<BR>अम्, n. boiled rice coloured with turmeric &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रक|चित्रकं|चित्रकः
चित्रक, अस्, m. a painter; a tiger, a panther, the<BR>Chīta or small hunting leopard; a kind of snake;<BR>the plant Plumbago Zeylanica; also Ricinus Com-<BR>munis or the castor-oil plant; N. of a son of Vṛṣṇi<BR>or of Pṛśni; N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; also of<BR>a Nāga; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (अम्), n. a<BR>sectarial mark on the forehead; a particular manner<BR>of fighting; the fruit of the plant Plumbago Zeylanica;<BR>N. of a wood near the mountain Raivataka; [cf.<BR>चित्र-वन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रय
चित्रय, nom. P. चित्रयति, to make variegated,<BR>paint with various colours, decorate; to regard as a<BR>wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रल|चित्रलः
चित्रल, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, spotted; (अस्), m. a<BR>variegated colour; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = गो-रक्षी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिक|चित्रिकः
चित्रिक, अस्, m. = चैत्रिक, the month Caitra or<BR>Cheyt (March-April).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रित
चित्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, spotted, striped;<BR>painted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिन्
चित्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, containing wonders, wonderful;<BR>variegated; having variegated (black and grey) hair;<BR>(इण्यस्), f. pl. wonderful deeds; (इणी), f., N. for a<BR>woman endowed with various talents and excellencies,<BR>one of the four divisions into which women are<BR>classed by erotic writers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिय
4. चित्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. variegated (?), epithet of<BR>a species of Aśvattha; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकरण|चित्रीकरणं
चित्री-करण, अम्, n. and चित्री-कार, अस्, m.<BR>wondering, wonder, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकृ
चित्री-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to feel wonder; to make a picture, change into a<BR>picture, paint, variegate, embellish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकृत
चित्री-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, painted, variegated, em-<BR>bellished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीय
चित्रीय, nom. A. चित्रीयते, -यितुम्, to wonder,<BR>be surprised; to become a wonder to any one (with<BR>gen.); to cause surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीयमाण
चित्रीयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming a wonder,<BR>causing wonder or astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र्य
चित्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. brilliant; (Sāy.) to be<BR>honoured, to be thought highly of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेकित
चेकित, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेकितान|चेकितानः
चेकितान, अस्, m. ‘the intelligent one,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva; N. of a prince and ally of the Pāṇḍus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतक
चेतक, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to think, reminding;<BR>what thinks or feels, sentient; (ई), f. the yellow<BR>myrobalan, = हरीतकी, Terminalia Chebula; or =<BR>जाती-फल, Jasminum Grandiflorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतन|चेतनः
चेतन, अस्, ई, अम्, visible, conspicuous, distin-<BR>guished, excellent; percipient, observing, conscious,<BR>sentient, intelligent; alive, living, feeling; (अस्), m.<BR>a living and sentient being, a man; self, soul, mind;<BR>(आ), f. consciousness, understanding, sense, intelli-<BR>gence, wisdom, reflection; (अम्), n. appearance;<BR>the thinking principle, the mind; [cf. अ-चेतन,<BR>निश्-च्˚, वि-च्˚, स-च्˚, चैतन्य.]<BR>—चेतन-ता, f. or<BR>चेतन-त्व, अम्, n. consciousness, the state or con-<BR>dition of an observing and conscious being.<BR>—चेतना-<BR>चेतन (˚न-अच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, animate and inanimate.<BR>—चेतना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having consciousness,<BR>knowing, understanding, reasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतनकी
चेतनकी, f. = चेतकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतनीया
चेतनीया, f. a kind of medicinal herb, = ऋद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतय
चेतय, अस्, आ, अम्, observing, conscious, sentient,<BR>living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयमान
चेतयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sentient, reflecting,<BR>conscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयान
चेतयान, अस्, आ, अम्, understanding, having sense,<BR>sensible, conscious, sentient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयितव्य
चेतयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be observed or thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयितृ
चेतयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, observing, perceiving,<BR>sentient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस्
चेतस्, अस्, n. bright appearance, Ved. (Sāy. a re-<BR>verent mind); consciousness, intelligence, the sentient<BR>or thinking soul, heart, mind, intellect, the faculty<BR>of reasoning or understanding; will; [cf. अ-चेतस्,<BR>दभ्र-च्˚, धीर-च्˚, नाना-च्˚, लघु-च्˚, वि-च्˚, स-<BR>च्˚, सु-च्˚.]<BR>—चेतो-भव, अस्, m. or चेतो-भू, ऊस्, m.<BR>love, the deity of love.<BR>—चेतो-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>endowed with consciousness, living.<BR>—चेतो-विकार,<BR>अस्, m. disturbance of mind, emotion.<BR>—चेतो-विकारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, disturbed in mind, moved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस
चेतस at the end of an adv. comp. = चेतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेत्तृ
चेत्तृ, ता, m., Ved. an observer, a guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेत्य
चेत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. observable, perceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतन्य|चैतन्यं|चैतन्यः
चैतन्य, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
चित् 6. चित्, an interjection.<BR>—चित्-कार, अस्,<BR>m. or चित्कार-शब्द, अस्, m. a cry, scream, bray.<BR>—चित्कार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, accompanied by cries<BR>or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
