चूति|चूतिः
चूति, इस्, f. the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्
चूर् चूर्, cl. 4. A. चूर्यते, चुचूरे, चूरितुम्,<BR>to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूरी
चूरी चूरी, f. (a various reading for चुरी), a<BR>small well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूरिका
चूरिका, f. = चूरी, above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूरु
चूरु चूरु, उस्, m. a kind of worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण्
चूर्ण् चूर्ण् (perhaps more properly re-<BR>garded as a nom. fr. चूर्ण below), cl. 10.<BR>P. चूर्णयति, -यितुम्, to reduce to powder or flour,<BR>to crumble, pulverize, grind, pound, knead, crush,<BR>bruise, split, crumple; [cf. Hib. coirneach, ‘a part;’<BR>crinim, ‘I gnaw, bite.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्ण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be connected in the<BR>first instance with rt. चर्व्), powder, any minute<BR>particle of substance; flour; aromatic powder, pulvil,<BR>pounded sandal; pounded camphor; (अस्), m. chalk,<BR>lime.<BR>—चूर्ण-कार, अस्, m. a lime-burner, maker of<BR>lime, considered as a man of mixed caste.<BR>—चूर्ण-<BR>कुन्तल, अस्, m. a lock of hair, a curl, curly hair.<BR>—चूर्ण-खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. a pebble, gravel,<BR>hardened fragments of earth or brick; limestone<BR>nodule, commonly known in India by the name of<BR>Concar or कर्कर.<BR>—चूर्ण-ता, f. or चूर्ण-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. pulverulence, comminution, the state of dust or<BR>powder.<BR>—चूर्ण-पद, अम्, n. a peculiar exercise or<BR>movement, walking backwards and forwards at various<BR>paces.<BR>—चूर्ण-पारद, अस्, m. vermilion.<BR>—चूर्ण-<BR>मुष्टि, इस्, f. a handful of powder or perfume.<BR>—चूर्ण-योग, आस्, m. pl. a fragrant compound, per-<BR>fumed powder: [cf. वास-योग.]<BR>—चूर्ण-शस्, ind.<BR>in powder, (ground) to powder (e. g. चूर्णशः कृ,<BR>to reduce to powder).<BR>—चूर्ण-शाकाङ्क (˚क-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a kind of vegetable; [cf. गौर-सुवर्ण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णक|चूर्णकं|चूर्णकः
चूर्णक, अस्, m. grain fried and pounded; a kind<BR>of grain belonging to the class called Ṣaṣṭika;<BR>(अम्), n. a fragrant powder; a kind of easy prose not<BR>abounding in compound words; expounding in prose<BR>the purport of a foregoing verse, giving the order or<BR>interpretation of the words; [cf. चूर्णिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णन|चूर्णनं
चूर्णन, अम्, n. rubbing, pounding, pulverizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णि|चूर्णिः
चूर्णि, इस्, f. (said by some to come fr. rt. चर्), a<BR>sum of 100 kapardas or cowries, i. e. the small shell<BR>Cypræa Moneta, used as a coin; (इस् or ई), f., N. of<BR>Patañjali's great commentary or Mahā-bhāṣya, on the<BR>Sūtras of Pāṇini, perhaps so named because Patañjali<BR>notices every minute point of difficulty in Pāṇini's<BR>grammar [cf. एक-चूर्णि]; a selection or picking out<BR>of an unanswerable argument; (ई), f., N. of a river<BR>near the Grāma Rāṇāghaṭṭa.<BR>—चूर्णि-कृत्, त्, m. an<BR>epithet of Patañjali, the author of the Mahā-bhāṣya;<BR>an annotator, commentator in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिका
चूर्णिका, f. fried and pounded rice, or grain of any<BR>kind; a kind of cake; a sort of metre; a kind of<BR>easy prose; [cf. चूर्णक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णित
चूर्णित, अस्, आ, अम्, ground, pulverized, pounded,<BR>reduced to dust or powder; bruised, smashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिन्
चूर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, made or mixed up with anything<BR>powdered or pounded, covered with it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णीकृ
चूर्णी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to reduce to dust or powder, pulverize, pound, grind,<BR>beat to pieces, bruise, smash.<BR>—चूर्णी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, pulverized, ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णीभू
चूर्णी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to be-<BR>come dust or powder, fly off into minute particles.<BR>—चूर्णी-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming dust or<BR>pulverized, crumbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ति|चूर्तिः|चूर्त्ति
चूर्ति चूर्ति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. चर्), going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूल|चूलः
चूल चूल, अस्, m. (= चूड, q. v.), N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">Page0329-b+ 71</a>]<BR>man; (आ), f. an upper room, a room on the top of a<BR>house; a crest, see चूडा; the top part or crest of a<BR>comet; [cf. उच्-चूल; cf. also Gr. σκόλλυς.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिक|चूलिकं
चूलिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. the<BR>crest or comb of a cock; the root of an elephant's<BR>ear; N. of a metre; a particular part or division of<BR>a drama, the body of a drama, the inferior personages<BR>of the drama collectively; title of a Jaina work form-<BR>ing one of the five parts of the Dṛṣṭi-vāda; (अम्),<BR>n. cakes of flour fried with ghee.<BR>—चूलिका-पैशाची,<BR>f., N. of a particular dialect in the drama.<BR>—चूलिको-<BR>पनिषद् (˚का-उप्˚), त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिन्
चूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a crest (as a bird) or an<BR>ornament on the head; (ई), m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्
चूष् चूष्, cl. 1. P. चूषति, चुचूष, चू-<BR>षिष्यति, चूषितुम्, to suck, suck out:<BR>Pass. चूष्यते, to be sucked up or dried up (by in-<BR>ternal inflammations &c.): Caus. चूषयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to suck up; [cf. Lat. sugere, succus; Germ. saugen;<BR>Iceland. siuga.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूषणीय
चूषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, capable of being sucked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूषा
चूषा, f. a leathern girth; a girdle; sucking (?);<BR>[cf. बूषा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूषित
चूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, sucked, sucked up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्य|चूष्यं
चूष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sucked, suckable; (अम्),<BR>n. anything that can be sucked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष|चोषः
चोष, अस्, m. sucking, suction; burning (of the<BR>skin), heat, inflammation, dryness; drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोषण|चोषणं
चोषण, अम्, n. sucking, suction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष्य|चोष्यं
चोष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sucked out; [cf. चूष्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृत्
चृत् चृत्, cl. 6. P. चृतति, चचर्त, चर्तिष्-<BR>यति or चर्त्स्यति, चर्तितुम्, to tie, con-<BR>nect together; to hurt, wound, kill; cl. 1. 10. P.<BR>चर्तति, चर्तयति, &c., to light, kindle; (a various<BR>reading for छृद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृप्
चृप् चृप्, cl. 1. 10. P. चर्पति, चर्पयति,<BR>&c., to light, kindle; (a various reading for<BR>छृद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेक
चेक चेक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of<BR>a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेकित
चेकित चेकित, &c. See under 4. चित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेक्रिय
चेक्रिय चेक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of rt.<BR>1. कृ), doing much or often, active, industrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेच्चेत्
चेच्चेत् चेच्चेत् (चेत्-चेत्), ind. an interjection;<BR>hush! be quiet!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेट|चेटः
चेट चेट, अस्, m. (fr. rt. चिट्), a servant, a<BR>slave, (गर्भ-चेट, a slave by birth); (ई), f. a<BR>female servant or slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटक|चेटकः
चेटक, अस्, m. a servant, a slave, a minister who<BR>fulfils an appointed duty; a paramour; (इका), f. a<BR>female slave or servant, a servant girl, a little maid-<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेड|चेडः
चेड, अस्, m. (for चेट above), a servant; (ई), f. a<BR>female servant or slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेडक|चेडकः
चेडक, अस्, m. a servant; (इका), f. a female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेत्
चेत् चेत्. See चेद् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतक
चेतक चेतक. See p. 325, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतव्य
चेतव्य चेतव्य. See p. 322, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस्
चेतस् चेतस्, &c. See p. 325, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतसक
चेतसक चेतसक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतिष्ठ
चेतिष्ठ चेतिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (superl. of<BR>चित्र, q. v.), very brilliant &c., especially an epithet<BR>of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतृ
चेतृ चेतृ, चेत्या. See 2. and 3. चि, p. 322.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेद्
चेद् चेद् (originally 2. च + इद्), a compound<BR>particle, never found at the beginning of a sentence<BR>or verse. In the Veda it is sometimes used as a<BR>conjunction, like the simple च, in the sense of ‘and,’<BR>‘also,’ ‘even.’ But in Vedic as well as classical<BR>Sanskrit the most usual sense of चेद् is ‘if,’ ‘although,’<BR>‘provided that,’ ‘when,’ and in these senses it may<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">Page0329-c+ 74</a>]<BR>be joined with the present indicative (e. g. मह्यं<BR>चेद् ददाति तत्, if he gives that to me); or with<BR>the future (e. g. तृष्णां चेत् त्यक्ष्यति, if he<BR>shall abandon avarice); or with the conditional (e. g.<BR>वृष्टिश् चेद् अभविष्यत्, if there should have been<BR>rain); or with the potential (e. g. गच्छेच् चेत्, if<BR>he should go); or with the perfect (e. g. स चेन् म-<BR>मार, when he died); or with a participle (e. g.<BR>कर्तव्यं चेत् प्रियम् मह्यम्, if a kindness is<BR>to be done to me). It should be observed that in<BR>the Veda the verb which depends on चेद् retains<BR>its accent.<BR>The negative particle न may be prefixed to चेद्<BR>either immediately or separated from it (e. g. न<BR>चेद् वचः करिष्यति or न करिष्यति चेद् वचः,<BR>if he should not make a speech); and frequently the<BR>negative नो is used in connection with चेद्, the<BR>verb being understood (e. g. दूरम् अपसर नो<BR>चेद् धन्तव्योऽसि मया, depart to a distance, if not,<BR>i. e. if thou departest not, thou art to be killed by me).<BR>Sometimes नो चेद् = अपि न, would that not! (e. g.<BR>नो चेद् एवं कुर्यात्, would that he did not so!).<BR>Rarely यदि and चेद् are joined together, when चेद्<BR>may be translated by ‘that is,’ ‘that is to say,’ ‘namely’<BR>(e. g. यदि चेद् राज्यम् अवाप्स्यति, if, that is, he<BR>shall obtain the kingdom). In the argumentative<BR>writings of native commentators चेद् preceded by इति<BR>and followed by न is often placed at the end of an<BR>objector's statement (e. g. ‘ऋग्-वेदम् अध्येमि’<BR>इत्यादि वाक्यम् प्रमाणम् इति चेन् न, if it be urged<BR>that the text ‘I peruse the Ṛg-veda’ is a proof, no,<BR>it is not so). अथ चेद्, but if; [cf. नेद्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदार
चेदार चेदार, अस्, m. (a wrong reading for<BR>वेदार), a lizard, a chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदि|चेदिः
चेदि चेदि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a people who<BR>lived in Bandela-khaṇḍa (Bundelkhand) and were re-<BR>nowned in epic poetry for their attachment to ancient<BR>laws and institutions; their capital was Śuktimatī, and<BR>some of their kings were Vasu Upari-cara, Su-bāhu,<BR>Dhṛṣṭa-ketu, Dama-ghoṣa, Śiśu-pāla, &c.; their<BR>ancestor who was a son of Kaiśika or Uśika is also<BR>called Cedi; their country is supposed by some to<BR>be the same as the modern Chandail.<BR>—चेदि-प,<BR>अस्, m. a prince of the Cedis.<BR>—चेदि-पति, इस्, m. a<BR>N. of Vasu Upari-cara; a N. of Śiśu-pāla.<BR>—चेदि-<BR>भूभृत्, त्, or चेदि-राज, अस्, m. a N. of Śiśu-pāla,<BR>a king of the Cedayas slain by Kṛṣṇa; see शिशु-<BR>पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदिक|चेदिकः
चेदिक चेदिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>living in the south-east of Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेय
चेय चेय. See 1. चि, p. 322, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेर
चेर चेर, N. of a kingdom in the south<BR>of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेरु
चेरु चेरु, उस्, उस्, उ (rt. चर्), Ved. perform-<BR>ing a holy work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्
चेल् चेल्, cl. 1. P. चेलति, to shake or<BR>tremble; to go or move; [cf. चल्, चेल्ल्,<BR>केल्, खेल्, वेल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल|चेलं
चेल चेल, अम्, n. (fr. rt. चिल्; according to<BR>the scholiasts also चेली, f.), cloth, clothes, a garment,<BR>raiment; (at the end of a comp. चेल, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>expresses) vile, wicked, bad (e. g. भार्या-चेल, अम्,<BR>n. the garment or the mere outward appearance of<BR>a wife, a bad wife); [cf. चैल; cf. also caille, ‘a veil<BR>or cowl.’]<BR>—चेल-गङ्गा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चेल-<BR>प्रक्षालक, अस्, m. a washerman.<BR>—चेलाशक<BR>(˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, m. a moth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलिका
चेलिका, f. a particular part of a woman's dress, a<BR>corset, a bodice, stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलक
चेलक चेलक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलान|चेलानः
चेलान चेलान, अस्, m. a kind of cucumber,<BR>commonly चेलना; [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलाल|चेलालः
चेलाल चेलाल, अस्, m. a kind of cucumber,<BR>Cucumis Sativus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0329-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलिचीम
चेलिचीम चेलिचीम or चेलीम = चिलिचिम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलुक|चेलुकः
चेलुक चेलुक, अस्, m. a Buddhist novice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्ल्
चेल्ल् चेल्ल्, cl. 1. P. चेल्लति, a various<BR>reading for चेल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेवी
चेवी चेवी, f. one of the Rāgiṇīs or female<BR>personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट्
चेष्ट् चेष्ट्, cl. 1. P. A. चेष्टति, -ते, चि-<BR>चेष्टे, चेष्टिष्यते, चेष्टितुम्, to move<BR>the limbs, to move, stir, make effort, exert one's self,<BR>struggle, strive, endeavour, be active, be busy or occu-<BR>pied; to act, do, perform, prepare; to frequent: Caus.<BR>P. A. चेष्टयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to move, set<BR>in motion, move, impel, drive; [cf. Lat. quœro;<BR>Cambro-Brit. cais.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट|चेष्टं
चेष्ट, अम्, n. moving the limbs, gesture; acting;<BR>(आ), f. moving any member of the body; gesture,<BR>action, activity; effort, endeavour, exertion, bodily<BR>effort; doing, performing, behaving, manner of exist-<BR>ence; [cf. कर्म-चेष्टा, अचेष्ट-ता, निश्-चेष्ट.]<BR>—चेष्टा-नाश, अस्, m. the ceasing of every motion<BR>or action, destruction of the world.<BR>—चेष्टा-निरू-<BR>पण, अम्, n. observing a person's actions.<BR>—चेष्-<BR>टार्ह (˚टा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of effort.<BR>—चेष्टा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having motion, full of activity, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टक|चेष्टकः
चेष्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, making effort or exertion;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टन|चेष्टनं
चेष्टन, अस्, आ, अम्, making effort, who or what<BR>acts or attempts any act; (अम्), n. motion; per-<BR>forming, doing; effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टमान
चेष्टमान, अस्, आ, अम्, moving, stirring, struggling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टयितृ
चेष्टयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, moving, impelling, causing<BR>to act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टित|चेष्टितं
चेष्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, done with effort, exerted, done,<BR>set in motion, &c.; (अम्), n. motion, gesture, act,<BR>function; doing, action, behaviour, manner of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टितव्य
चेष्टितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be acted; to be managed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैकित
चैकित चैकित, अस्, ई, अम्, an adjective de-<BR>rived fr. चैकित्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैकितान
चैकितान, अस्, m. a patronymic from Cikitāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैकितान
चैकितान, अस्, m. a patronymic from the preced-<BR>ing, or from Cekitāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैकितायन
चैकितायन, अस्, m. a patronymic of Dālbhya (fr.<BR>चिकितायन or चेकित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैकित्य
चैकित्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Cekita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैकीर्षत
चैकीर्षत चैकीर्षत, अस्, ई, अम्, = चिकीर्षत्,<BR>wishing to do &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैटयत
चैटयत चैटयत, अस्, m., N. of a man and<BR>his descendants.<BR>—चैटयत-विध, अम्, n. the<BR>district inhabited by the Caiṭayatas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैटयतायनि
चैटयतायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Caiṭa-<BR>yata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतन्य|चैतन्यं|चैतन्यः
चैतन्य चैतन्य, अम्, n. (fr. चेतन), intel-<BR>ligence, mental perception, feeling, consciousness,<BR>sense, sensation, soul, spirit, the deity considered as<BR>the essence of all being and source of all sensation;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a modern reformer of the Vaiṣṇava<BR>faith, who is regarded in Bengal as an Ava-tāra of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; he was born about 1484 A. D., and his<BR>life is described by Kṛṣṇa-dāsa in a work named<BR>Caitanya-caraṇāmṛta or Caitanya-caritāmṛta.<BR>—चै-<BR>तन्य-चन्द्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘the moon-<BR>rise of Caitanya,’ title of a play.<BR>—चैतन्य-युक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with consciousness, sentient.<BR>—चैतन्यामृत (˚य-अम्˚), अम्, n. title of a<BR>grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतसिक
चैतसिक चैतसिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चेतस्), re-<BR>lating to the mind or heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतिक
चैतिक चैतिक, आस्, m. pl. (fr. 2. चैत्य?),<BR>N. of a Buddhist school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्त
चैत्त चैत्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चित्त), mental,<BR>belonging to thought or intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्तिक
चैत्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, mental, intellectual, belonging<BR>to thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्य|चैत्यं|चैत्यः
चैत्य 1. चैत्य, अस्, m. (fr. 5. चित् or 2. चिति),<BR>the individual soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्य|चैत्यं|चैत्यः
चैत्य 2. चैत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चिता), relating<BR>to a funeral pile or grave; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a<BR>monument, a tombstone, a column &c. erected in<BR>memory of some deceased person or on the site of a<BR>funeral pile; a pile of stones forming a landmark<BR>or boundary; a sacred tree, a religious fig-tree &c.<BR>growing in or near a village and held in veneration<BR>by the villagers; a place of sacrifice or religious<BR>worship, an altar, a shed kept for sacrifices &c.; a<BR>sacred building peculiar to the Jainas, a Jaina temple;<BR>a Jaina or Buddhist image; (अस्), m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—चैत्य-तरु, उस्, m. a fig-tree standing on a<BR>sacred spot.<BR>—चैत्य-द्रु, उस्, m., N. of the Ficus<BR>Religiosa [cf. अश्वत्थ]; a large tree in a village.<BR>—चैत्य-द्रुम, अस्, m. = चैत्य-तरु.<BR>—चैत्य-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. the guardian of a sanctuary.<BR>—चैत्य-<BR>मुख, अस्, m. an hermit's water-pot.<BR>—चैत्य-<BR>यज्ञ, अस्, m. a sacrificial ceremony performed at<BR>monuments.<BR>—चैत्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing<BR>a sanctuary.<BR>—चैत्य-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a fig-tree<BR>standing on a sacred spot; the tree Ficus Religiosa.<BR>—चैत्य-शैल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a Buddhist school;<BR>[cf. चैतिक.]<BR>—चैत्य-स्थान, अम्, n. a place made<BR>sacred by a monument or a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यक
चैत्यक, अस्, m., N. of one of the five moun-<BR>tains surrounding the town Giri-vraja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्र|चैत्रं|चैत्रः
चैत्र चैत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चित्र and चित्रा),<BR>made of the tree called Citra or Citrā; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a spring month or the month in which the<BR>full moon stands in the constellation Citrā (March-<BR>April); N. of the sixth year in the cycle of Jupiter;<BR>a Buddhist or Jaina religious mendicant; a common<BR>N. for a man, used like Deva-datta as a general desig-<BR>nation for any person; a metronymic (from Citrā) for<BR>the son of Budha and grandfather of Su-ratha; one of<BR>the seven ranges of mountains dividing the continent<BR>into divisions or Varṣas; (ई), f., scil. पौर्णमासी,<BR>the day of full moon in the month Caitra and the<BR>sacrifice offered on that day; (अम्), n. a monument<BR>erected to the dead, a column or block of wood, a<BR>tree &c. so considered; [cf. 2. चैत्य.]<BR>—चैत्र-<BR>वती, f., N. of a river.<BR>—चैत्र-सख, अस्, m. the<BR>friend of the month Caitra, i. e. the god of love.<BR>—चैत्रावली (˚र-आव्˚), f. the day of full moon in<BR>the month Caitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रक|चैत्रकः
चैत्रक, अस्, m. the month Caitra; (a patronymic<BR>fr. चित्रा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रकूटी
चैत्रकूटी, f. (fr. चित्र-कूट), title of a com-<BR>mentary on a grammatical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथ|चैत्ररथं
चैत्ररथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चित्र-रथ), treating<BR>of the Gandharva Citra-ratha; (अस्), m. a patronymic<BR>from Citra-ratha; N. of a Dvyaha ceremony; a<BR>facetious expression for the pubes of a woman,<BR>‘Citra-ratha's wood;’ (ई), f. a patronymic of a<BR>daughter of Śaśa-vindu; (अम्), n., scil. वन, the<BR>grove of the deity Kuvera cultivated by the Gan-<BR>dharva Citra-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथि
चैत्ररथि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Śaśa-vindu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथ्य|चैत्ररथ्यं
चैत्ररथ्य, अम्, n. the grove of the deity<BR>Kuvera cultivated by the Gandharva Citra-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रवाहनी
चैत्रवाहनी, f. (fr. चित्र-वाहन), a patronymic<BR>of Citrāṅgadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रायण
चैत्रायण, a patronymic from Citra; N. of a<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रि|चैत्रिः
चैत्रि, इस्, m. the month Caitra; (a various reading<BR>for चैत्रिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिक|चैत्रिकः
चैत्रिक, अस्, m. and चैत्रिन्, ई, m. the month<BR>Caitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैदिक
चैदिक चैदिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. चेदि), an<BR>adjective derived fr. चेदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैद्य|चैद्यः
चैद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Cedis, a<BR>prince of the Cedis; (अस्), m. a N. of Śiśu-pāla, son<BR>of Dama-ghoṣa and sovereign of Cedi or Chandail,<BR>and adversary of Kṛṣṇa; (आस्), m. pl. the Cedi<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैन्तित
चैन्तित चैन्तित, अस्, m. a metronymic from<BR>Cintitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैल|चैलः
चैल चैल, अम्, n. = चेल, a piece of cloth,<BR>clothes, a garment; (अस्), m. a moth; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>cloth, made of cloth; bred in clothes (as insects,<BR>lice, &c.).<BR>—चैल-धाव, अस्, m. a washerman,<BR>—चैलाशक (˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, m. a kind of goblin<BR>feeding on moths and lice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलक|चैलकः
चैलक, अस्, m. a Buddhist mendicant having only<BR>a piece of cloth round the middle of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलिक|चैलिकः
चैलिक, अस्, m. a piece of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलकि
चैलकि चैलकि, इस्, m. (fr. चेलक), a patro-<BR>nymic of Jīvala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोकुटि
चोकुटि चोकुटि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोक्ष|चोक्षः
चोक्ष चोक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चुक्षा ?), pure,<BR>clean; honest; clever, dexterous; pleasing, delight-<BR>ful, beautiful; sung (?); sharp, pungent, keen; [cf.<BR>चौक्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोच|चोचं
चोच चोच, अम्, n. the bark of Cinnamon<BR>Albiflorum or of another kind of cinnamon; bark,<BR>rind in general; skin, hide; the uneatable part of a<BR>fruit; the fruit of the fan-palm; the cocoa-nut; a<BR>banana or plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोचक|चोचकं|चोचकः
चोचक, अम्, n. the bark of Cinnamon Albiflorum<BR>or of another kind of cinnamon; bark, rind in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोटी
चोटी चोटी, f. a petticoat; [cf. शाटी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोड|चोडः
चोड चोड, अस्, m. = चूड, a sort of knob or<BR>protuberance on a brick or tile; a bodice or jacket;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people [cf. चोल]; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोद|चोदः
चोद चोद, चोद्य. See चुद्, p. 327, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोपक
चोपक चोपक. See 1. चुप्, p. 328, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोर|चोरः
चोर चोर, &c. See rt. चुर्, p. 328, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोल|चोलः
चोल चोल, अस्, ई, m. f. a short jacket, a<BR>bodice; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people in southern<BR>India on the Coromandel coast, in the province now<BR>called Tāñjora; (अस्), m. a prince of the Colas; the<BR>ancestor of this people is also called Cola and was<BR>a son of Ā-krīḍa; (अम्), n. clothes, a garment.<BR>—चोलोण्डुक (˚ल-उण्˚), अस्, m. a diadem, a fillet<BR>for the head, a turban or tiara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलक|चोलकं|चोलकः
चोलक, अस्, m. a breastplate, a cuirass; N. of a<BR>people, = the preceding; (अम्), n. bark, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलकिन्
चोलकिन्, ई, m. a cuirassier, a soldier armed with a<BR>breastplate; the shoot of a bamboo; the orange<BR>tree; the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष|चोषः
चोष चोष, &c. See चूष्, p. 329, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोस्क|चोस्कः
चोस्क चोस्क, अस्, m. a horse peculiar to the<BR>Indus district; a horse of a particular and good breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्र्य
चौक्र्य चौक्र्य, अम्, n. (fr. चुक्र), sourness,<BR>acidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्ष|चौक्षं
चौक्ष चौक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चुक्षा; cf. चो-<BR>क्ष), pure, clean; honest (?); agreeable, pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौड
चौड चौड, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चूडा), crested,<BR>relating to a crest; relating to tonsure; (अम्), n.<BR>the ceremony of tonsure; [cf. चौल.]<BR>—चौड-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. the rite of tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौण
चौण चौण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people in<BR>the west of Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौण्ट्य
चौण्ट्य चौण्ट्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. चुण्टी), coming<BR>from a pond or well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौण्डपाचार्य
चौण्डपाचार्य चौण्डपाचार्य (˚प-आच्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Ārya who was the author of a<BR>commentary called Prayoga-ratna-mālā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौदायनि
चौदायनि चौदायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Coda (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0330-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौपयत
चौपयत चौपयत, अस्, त्या, m. f. a patro-<BR>nymic from Copayat fr. rt. चुप् (?).<BR>—चौपयत-<BR>विध, अम्, n. the district inhabited by the Caupa-<BR>yatas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौपयतायनि
चौपयतायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Cau-<BR>payata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौपायन
चौपायन चौपायन, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Cupa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर|चौरः
चौर चौर. See p. 328, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरोल
चौरोल चौरोल, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौल
चौल चौल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. चूला = चूडा), re-<BR>lating to a crest or top-knot &c.; (अम्), n. ton-<BR>sure; [cf. Gr. σκόλλυς.]<BR>—चौल-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>the ceremony of tonsure, cutting off all the hair from<BR>the head of a child three years old except one lock<BR>on the crown; [cf. चूडा, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौलुक्य|चौलुक्यः
चौलुक्य चौलुक्य, अस्, m. (fr. चुलुक), a<BR>patronymic of Kumāra-pāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौलुक
चौलुक, अस्, ई, अम्, an adjective derived from the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौहित्थ
चौहित्थ चौहित्थ, अस्, m., N. of a Paṇḍit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवन|च्यवनं|च्यवनः
च्यवन च्यवन. See below under 1. च्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
च्यु 1. च्यु, cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.) च्यवते,<BR>-ति, चुच्युवे, च्योष्यते, अच्योष्ट, च्योतुम्,<BR>to move to and fro, shake about, move, stir, move<BR>from one's place, go away, retire from (with abl.);<BR>to fly from (the hand or the bow-string, as a spear or<BR>arrow); to fall off from, deviate from, abandon (duty<BR>&c.); to be deprived of, lose (with abl., e. g. राज्याच्<BR>च्यवते, he loses the kingdom); to fall away, fade<BR>away, disappear, vanish, perish, wane, fail; to come<BR>forth from, come out of, flow out, drop from, trickle,<BR>stream forth from (in this sense cf. 2. च्युत्); to fall<BR>down, fall, slip, slide; to sink down, sink (literally<BR>and metaphorically); to decrease; to cause to move<BR>or shake about; to bring about, create, make; to<BR>cause to go away, to make forget: Caus. P. च्याव-<BR>यति, (in the Pada-pāṭha च्यवयति), -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to move, excite, agitate; A. to move one's self,<BR>be shaken or moved; P. to loosen, to remove from<BR>a place, drive away, expel from, remove; to deprive<BR>a person of anything (with two acc., e. g. देवी न<BR>च्यावयेद् राजानम् प्राणान्, let not the goddess<BR>deprive the king of life); to cause to fall: Desid. of<BR>Caus. चिच्यावयिषति and चुच्यावयिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यव
च्यव. Cf. भुवन-च्यव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवन|च्यवनं|च्यवनः
च्यवन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to move, moving,<BR>shaking; (अस्), m., N. of a disease or of the demon<BR>causing it; N. of a Ṛṣi who was a son of Bhṛgu<BR>and author of several hymns [cf. च्यवान, which is<BR>the original form]; N. of an astronomer; also of<BR>one of the seven sages under Manu Svārociṣa; of a<BR>son of Mitrāyu; of Suhotra; of a physician; (अम्),<BR>n. moving, motion; departure from, deprivation,<BR>being deprived of; sinking, falling, perishing, dying;<BR>trickling, flowing; [cf. दुश्-च्यवन.]<BR>—च्यवन-<BR>नघुष-संवाद, अस्, m. an episode of the<BR>thirteenth book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—च्यवन-<BR>प्राश, अस्, m., N. of an electuary (अव-लेह).<BR>—च्य-<BR>वन-समागम, अस्, m. a chapter of the Padma-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—च्यवनोपाख्यान (˚न-उप्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>story of Cyavana, a chapter of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवस्
च्यवस् in तृषु-च्यवस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवान
च्यवान, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi restored to youth<BR>by the Aśvins; [cf. च्यवन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्याव
च्याव in दुश्-च्याव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावन
च्यावन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to move or fall;<BR>(अम्), n. expulsion, driving away; N. of a Sāman;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic from Cyavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावयितृ
च्यावयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who causes to move<BR>or fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावित
च्यावित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to fall, expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत्
1. च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of compounds) shaking,<BR>causing to fall, removing, destroying; dropping, dis-<BR>tilling; [cf. अच्युत-च्युत्, ऋण-च्˚, धन्व-च्˚, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, moved, shaken; deviated from,<BR>erred, strayed; deprived; removed, expelled, ba-<BR>nished; fallen from, fallen off, broken, disordered;<BR>lost; fallen (e. g. नभश्-च्युत, fallen from the<BR>sky), dropped, oozed out; (in Rāmāyaṇa II. 91, 64,<BR>मधु-च्युत is probably a wrong form for मधु-<BR>च्युत्.)<BR>—च्युत-कूट, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—च्युत-पथक, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Śākya-<BR>muni.<BR>—च्युताचार (˚त-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deviating<BR>from duty.<BR>—च्युताधिकार (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dismissed from an office &c., deprived of a right.<BR>—च्युतोत्साह (˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>spent his energies, exhausted, incapable of effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युति|च्युतिः
च्युति, इस्, f. quick motion; falling, a fall; falling<BR>from, deviating from (rectitude &c.); vanishing,<BR>perishing, dying; coming or streaming forth from;<BR>falling, gliding, dropping, dripping, oozing; the<BR>vulva; the anus; [cf. चुत, चुति, चूत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यौत्न|च्यौत्नः
च्यौत्न, अस्, ई, अम्, animating, inspiring, pro-<BR>moting; a mover, goer; oviparous; abandoned,<BR>wicked, void of virtue or purity; (अम्), n. shaking,<BR>concussion; enterprise, exertion, contrivance, manage-<BR>ment, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
च्यु 2. च्यु [cf. च्युस्], cl. 10. P. च्यावयति,<BR>यितुम्, to laugh; to suffer, bear (?); [cf.<BR>Hib. tibhim, ‘I laugh, joke.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत्
च्युत् 2. च्युत्, cl. 1. P. च्योतति, चुच्योत,<BR>च्योतिष्यति, अच्युतत् and अच्योतीत्, च्योति-<BR>तुम्, to drop, sprinkle, flow, trickle, ooze, exude; to<BR>wet thoroughly, moisten; to fall down; to cause to<BR>drop or stream forth; [cf. श्चुत्, श्च्युत्, and 1. च्यु<BR>for 1. च्युत्; cf. also Hib. cioth, ‘a heavy shower;’<BR>ciothmhar, ‘showery.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योत|च्योतं
च्योत, अम्, n. sprinkling, pouring, dropping, fall-<BR>ing, dripping (as any unctuous substance), oozing,<BR>trickling, &c.; [cf. श्च्योत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युप|च्युपः
च्युप च्युप, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 1. च्यु),<BR>the face, mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युस्
च्युस् च्युस् [cf. 2. च्यु above], cl. 10. P.<BR>च्योसयति, -यितुम्, to laugh; to bear; to<BR>leave; to loose; to hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यूत|च्यूतः
च्यूत च्यूत, अस्, m. (for चूत), the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यौत्न|च्यौत्नः
च्यौत्न च्यौत्न. See under 1. च्यु above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ 1. छ, the seventh consonant of the<BR>Sanskrit alphabet, being the aspirate of the preceding<BR>letter, and having the sound of ch in church-hill.<BR>—छ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ 2. छ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. छो), cutting,<BR>dividing; a part, a fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ 3. छ, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps connected<BR>with छो), pure, clean; trembling, tremulous, un-<BR>steady; (आ), f. covering, concealing (in this sense<BR>connected with rt. छद्); an infant, a child, any<BR>young animal (?); [cf. छा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छग|छगः
छग छग, अस्, आ, m. f. (said to be fr. rt. छो),<BR>a goat; [cf. छाग; cf. also Germ. Bock; Angl. Sax.<BR>bucca; Old Germ. boch, poch, pog; Lat. caper;<BR>hircus (?); Hib. gabhar.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगल|छगलं|छगलः
छगल, अस्, m. a goat; a N. of Atri; of a<BR>Muni; of a country; (आ, ई), f. a she-goat; a kind of<BR>convolvulus, see the next; (अम्), n. blue cloth or<BR>raiment; [cf. छागल.]<BR>—छगलाङ्घ्री (˚ल-अङ्˚)<BR>or छगलाण्डी (˚ल-अण्˚), f. a plant, see the next.<BR>—छगलान्त्रिका or छगलान्त्री (˚ल-अन्˚), f.<BR>the plant Argyreia Speciosa or Argentea; a wolf;<BR>[cf. अजान्त्री.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलक|छगलकः
छगलक, अस्, m. a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलिन्
छगलिन्, ई, m., N. of a preceptor who was him-<BR>self a pupil of Kalāpin; [cf. छागलेयिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगण|छगणं|छगणः
छगण छगण, अस्, अम्, m. n. dried cow-<BR>dung; [cf. छागण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छज्जू
छज्जू छज्जू, ऊस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटा
छटा छटा, f. a mass, lump, assemblage,<BR>number; a collection of rays of light, light, lustre,<BR>splendor; a straight or continuous line; [cf. जटा.]<BR>—छटा-फल, अस्, m. the betel-nut tree, palmyra<BR>tree.<BR>—छटाभा (˚टा-आभा), f. lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छण्डक
छण्डक छण्डक, a wrong form for छन्-<BR>दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
छद् 1. छद्, cl. 10. P. (ep. also A.) छाद-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम् (also said to form छन्द-<BR>यति and cl. 1. P. छदति, but these forms do not<BR>seem to occur; in the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa a form<BR>छदयति is found), to cover, cover over, clothe,<BR>veil; to use anything as a cover, spread as a cover,<BR>cover one's self; to hide, conceal, keep secret; to<BR>protect: Desid. चिच्छादयिषति; [cf. Hib. scailim,<BR>‘I shade, shelter;’ scailein, ‘a fan, umbrella,’ &c.:<BR>Gr. σκιά, σκοτός: Goth. scadus: Lith. skyda;<BR>Germ. Schild; schale: Goth. skal-ja: Lat.<BR>squāma; spolium.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्र
छत्त्र, अस्, m. (often spelt छत्र), a mush-<BR>room; N. of a kind of grass, = भू-तृण; a bee-<BR>hive of a conical or umbrella form; (आ), f., N. of<BR>several plants, viz. Anethum Sowa; also = अति-<BR>च्छत्त्र; coriander; N. of a plant supposed to<BR>grow in Kaśmīra; the plant Rubia Munjista; a<BR>mushroom; (अम्), n. a parasol, an umbrella, called<BR>Chattar by the natives, and regarded as an ensign of<BR>royal or delegated power; N. of a constellation;<BR>concealing the faults of a teacher (this meaning is<BR>invented for the explanation of the word छात्त्र);<BR>[cf. अति-च्छत्र, आकृति-च्छत्त्रा, गोमय-च्छ्˚.]<BR>—छत्त्र-गुच्छ, अस्, m. the grass Scirpus Kysoor<BR>(कशेरु), = गुण्ड-तृण.<BR>—छत्त्र-गृह, अम्, n.<BR>the room in which the parasol (or badge of royalty)<BR>is kept.<BR>—छत्त्र-चक्र, अम्, n. an astrological<BR>diagram.<BR>—छत्त्र-धार, अस्, ई, अम्, bearing a<BR>parasol or umbrella, having or possessing one; (अस्),<BR>m. the bearer of a parasol.<BR>—छत्त्र-धारण,<BR>अम्, n. carrying or using a parasol or umbrella;<BR>carrying one as a type of royal authority.<BR>—छत्त्र-<BR>धार-त्व, अम्, n. the office of a parasol-bearer.<BR>—छत्त्र-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, = छत्र-धार above;<BR>(ई), m., N. of a son of Horila-siṃha.<BR>—छत्त्र-<BR>पति, इस्, or sometimes छत्त्र-प, अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>the umbrella or parasol,’ title of an ancient king in<BR>Jambu-dvīpa, or of any king over whom a parasol<BR>is carried as a mark of dignity, (whence the title<BR>Satrap is probably derived.)<BR>—छत्त्र-पत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the plant Ketmia Mutabilis.<BR>—छत्त्र-<BR>पुष्पक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = तिलक.<BR>—छत्-<BR>त्र-भङ्ग, अस्, m. breaking or destruction of the<BR>royal parasol, loss of dominion or empire, deposition,<BR>&c.; wilfulness, independence; a forlorn condition,<BR>widowhood.<BR>—छत्त्र-युक्ति, इस्, f. a chapter in king<BR>Bhoja's work called Yukti-kalpa-taru.<BR>—छत्त्र-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with an umbrella; (ती), f., N.<BR>of a country or town.<BR>—छत्त्रातिच्छत्त्र (˚र-अत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, m. f. a fragrant grass described as growing<BR>in marshy ground, = छत्त्रक and अति-च्छत्त्रा.<BR>—छत्त्रा-धान्य, अम्, n. coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रक
छत्त्रक, अस्, m. a temple in honour of Śiva of<BR>a spherical or umbrella shape; a beehive of a conical<BR>form; the plant Asteracantha Longifolia; a mush-<BR>room; a kingfisher; (इका), f. a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्राक
छत्त्राक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = जाल-वर्वू-<BR>रक; (ई), f., N. of a plant, = रास्ना; (अम्), n. a<BR>mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रिक
छत्त्रिक, अस्, m. the bearer of a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रिण
छत्त्रिण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्रिन्
छत्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bearing or having a parasol or<BR>umbrella, belonging to one; (ई), m. a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्त्वर
छत्त्वर, अस्, m. a house, a dwelling; a bower,<BR>an arbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
2. छद्, त्, त्, त्, (in compounds) concealing, hiding;<BR>[cf. धाम-च्छद्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0331-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद|छदः
छद, अस्, m. a cover, covering (e. g. अल्प-च्छद,<BR>scantily covered or dressed; घन-च्छद, con-<BR>cealed by clouds); a wing; a leaf; N. of two plants,<BR>= ग्रन्थि-पर्ण and = तमाल; [cf. Hib. sgiath,<BR>‘a wing.’]<BR>—छद-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the tree Sym-<BR>plocos Racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदन|छदनं
छदन, अम्, n. a cover, covering, a sheath, a<BR>scabbard; a wing; a leaf; the leaf of Laurus Cassia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदि|छदिः
छदि = छदिस्, the roof of a carriage; a wing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिस्
छदिस्, इस्, n. (f. ?), Ved. a cover, the roof of a<BR>carriage, the thatch or roof of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मन्
छद्मन्, अ, n. the thatch or roof of a house;<BR>external covering, a deceptive dress, disguise,<BR>masquerade; plea, pretext, pretence, trick, deceit;<BR>fraud, craft, dishonesty; [cf. Old Germ. scerm;<BR>Germ. Schirm.]<BR>—छद्म-तापस, अस्, m. a re-<BR>ligious hypocrite, a false ascetic.<BR>—छद्म-रू-<BR>पेण, ind. in disguise, incognito.<BR>—छद्म-वेश,<BR>अस्, m. a deceptive dress, disguise.<BR>—छद्म-वेशिन्,<BR>ई, m. dressed in disguise, a player, a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मिका
छद्मिका, f. the plant Cocculus Cordifolius;<BR>[cf. गुडूची.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मिन्
छद्मिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) dis-<BR>guised, in an assumed dress or garb (e. g. ब्राह्मण-<BR>च्छद्मिन्, disguised as a Brāhman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्न|छन्नं|छन्नः
छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, clad, concealed,<BR>secret, clandestine, private, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्त्र
छात्त्र, अस्, m. a pupil, scholar, disciple, tyro,<BR>novice, (as carrying his teacher's umbrella or as con-<BR>cealing his faults ?); (अम्), n. a kind of honey.<BR>—छात्त्र-गण्ड, अस्, m. an indifferent poetical<BR>scholar knowing only the beginnings of verses.<BR>—छात्त्र-गोमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, any one attendant on a<BR>pupil.<BR>—छात्त्र-ता, f. condition of a pupil, pupilage.<BR>—छात्त्र-दर्शन, अम्, n. fresh butter prepared<BR>from milk one day old (‘looked at by the pupils’).<BR>—छात्त्र-व्यंसक, अस्, m. a knavish or roguish<BR>pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्त्रक
छात्त्रक, अम्, n. honey in the comb or hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्त्रिक्य
छात्त्रिक्य, अम्, n. the office of a parasol-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद|छादं
छाद, अम्, n. thatch, a roof; (an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादन|छादनं|छादनः
छादन, अस्, m. the plant Barleria Cærulea, =<BR>नीलाम्लान; (ई), f. hide, skin; (अम्), n. covering,<BR>a cover, screen; hiding, concealing; darkening;<BR>clothes; a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादयत्
छादयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, covering, veiling, shrouding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादित|छादितः
छादित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, hidden, concealed;<BR>cut, divided (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादिन्
छादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) hiding,<BR>covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादिषेय
छादिषेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छदिस्), suitable for<BR>the roof of a carriage or for the thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिक|छाद्मिकः
छाद्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छद्मन्), fraudulent,<BR>dishonest; (अस्), m. a rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्यमान
छाद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
छद् 3. छद् or छन्द्, cl. 10. P. A. छद-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, cl. 1. P. and 10. P. A., Ved.<BR>छन्दति, छन्दयति, -ते, चच्छन्द, Aor. अच्-<BR>छान्, छन्तुम्, to seem, appear, be considered or<BR>esteemed as; to seem good, please, be pleasant: A.<BR>छन्दयते, to be pleased with, delight in, approve<BR>of (with acc. or loc.); (Sāy.) to render celebrated<BR>or honoured: P. छन्दयति, to gratify a person<BR>(acc. or sometimes gen.) with anything (e. g. वरेण,<BR>with a boon), to present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
4. छद्, त्, त्, त्, (in compounds) pleased with &c.;<BR>[cf. कवि-च्छद्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द|छंद|छन्दः
छन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, alluring, inviting;<BR>praising, a praiser; (अस्), m. appearance, look, shape;<BR>pleasure, delight, appetite, liking, fondness for, fancy,<BR>whim, predilection, desire, wish, subjection, will, free<BR>will, arbitrary choice; wilfulness, wilful conduct (e. g.<BR>मच्-छन्दात्, according to my wish or will, at my<BR>pleasure; स्व-च्छन्द, following one's own will,<BR>independent; अ-स्वच्छन्द, dependent; स्व-च्छन्-<BR>दम्, according to one's own wish; स्व-च्छन्दात्,<BR>willingly; अ-च्छन्देन, against the will); mean-<BR>ing, intention, purport, opinion; poison; (एन),<BR>ind. at the will of, according to wish or will, at one's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">Page0332-b+ 81</a>]<BR>pleasure; [cf. इन्द्र-च्छन्द, कलाप-च्˚, देव-च्˚,<BR>विजय-च्˚, all meaning pearl-ornaments or neck-<BR>laces of various kinds; cf. also Lat. spons, sponte.]<BR>—छन्द-तस्, ind. at will, at pleasure, according to<BR>one's own wish or desire.<BR>—छन्दानुवर्तिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, indulging the humour, complying with the wishes.<BR>—छन्दानुवृत्त (˚द-अन्˚), अम्, n. indulgence<BR>of whims, humouring, compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दक|छंदकः|छन्दकः
छन्दक in सर्व-च्छन्दक, epithet of Nārā-<BR>yaṇa, ‘assuming every shape?;’ (अस्), m., N. of the<BR>charioteer of Śākya-siṃha; [cf. छण्डक.]<BR>—छन्-<BR>दक-निवर्तन, ‘the return of Chandaka,’ N. of<BR>a Caitya.<BR>—छन्दक-पातन or छन्द-पातन,<BR>अस्, m. a hypocrite, a pretended or false ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दन|छंदन
छन्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्|छंदस्
छन्दस्, अस्, n. desire, longing for, delight,<BR>pleasure, wish, will; free will; meaning, intention,<BR>purport, object; a sacred hymn or verse as distin-<BR>guished from the verses of the four Vedas, a verse<BR>which is neither Ṛc, nor Sāman, nor Yajus, nor<BR>Ātharvaṇa, originally perhaps a hymn or verse used<BR>in incantations; the sacred text of the Vedic hymns;<BR>metre in general, supposed to consist of three or<BR>seven typical forms; metrical science, prosody.<BR>—छन्दः-प्रकरण, अम्, n. a chapter on metre.<BR>—छन्दः-प्रशस्ति or छन्द-प्रशस्ति, इस्, f. a<BR>work by Harṣa.<BR>—छन्दः-शास्त्र, अम्, n. metrical<BR>science, a work on metre by Piṅgala.<BR>—छन्दः-<BR>सङ्ग्रह and छन्दः-सार, अस्, m. a work giving<BR>a summary of metres.<BR>—छन्दः-सिद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>a chapter of the Kāvya-kalpa-latā-vṛtti-parimala.<BR>—छन्दः-स्तुत्, त्, त्, त्, or छन्दः-स्तुभ्, प्, प्,<BR>प्, Ved. praising in hymns.<BR>—छन्दश्-चूडामणि,<BR>इस्, m. a work by Hema-candra.<BR>—छन्दस्-कृत,<BR>अम्, n. any metrical part of the Vedas or other sacred<BR>compositions.<BR>—छन्दस्-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>one whose wing is sacred song, (borne aloft on the<BR>wings of praise ?).<BR>—छन्दस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. pleasing, lovely.<BR>—छन्दो-ग, अस्, m. (rt.<BR>गै), a reciter or singer in metre, a chanter of<BR>the Sāma-veda, generally the same as the Udgātṛ<BR>priest.<BR>—छन्दोग-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n. title of<BR>a work by Kātyāyana giving a supplement to<BR>Gobhila's Sūtras.<BR>—छन्दोग-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n.<BR>the Brāhmaṇa of the Udgātṛ priests attached to the<BR>Sāma-veda. Some authorities give eight of these<BR>Brāhmaṇas, the principal being called Prauḍha or<BR>Pañcaviṃśa, as consisting of twenty-five sections.<BR>—छन्दोग-माहकि, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—छन्दोग-शाखा, f. a branch of the Sāma-veda.<BR>—छान्दोग-श्रुति, इस्, f. the Veda of the Chandogas,<BR>the Sāma-veda.<BR>—छन्दोगाह्निक-पद्धति (˚ग-<BR>अह्˚), title of a work by Rāma-kṛṣṇa.<BR>—छन्दो-<BR>गोविन्द, title of a work on metre by Gaṅgā-dāsa.<BR>—छन्दो-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man, = मतङ्ग.<BR>—छन्दो-नामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having the name<BR>of metre, metrical.<BR>—छन्दोनुवृत्त (˚दस्-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. conforming to one's humour, humouring,<BR>indulgence.<BR>—छन्दो-भङ्ग, अस्, m. violation of<BR>the laws of metre.<BR>—छन्दो-भाषा, f. the language<BR>of the Vedas (?).<BR>—छन्दो-मञ्जरि, इस् or ई, f. title<BR>of a work on metre by Gaṅgā-dāsa.<BR>—छन्दो-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. consisting of or containing<BR>sacred hymns.<BR>—छन्दो-मान, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>measure of metre, i. e. a syllable regarded as the<BR>metrical unit.<BR>—छन्दो-मार्तण्ड, अस्, m. title of<BR>a work on metre.<BR>—छन्दो-माला, f. title of a work<BR>on metre.<BR>—छन्दो-रुट्-स्तोम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Ṣaḍaha rite.<BR>—छन्दो-विचिति, इस्, f. ‘examination<BR>of metres,’ title of a treatise on metre.<BR>—छन्दो-<BR>विवृति, इस्, f. ‘explanation of metres,’ title of Piṅ-<BR>gala's work on metre.<BR>—छन्दो-वृत्त, अम्, n. a<BR>metre in general, any metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्य|छंदस्य
छन्दस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. taking the form of<BR>hymns, metrical, fit for hymns, relating to the Vedic<BR>hymns; made or done according to one's wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दित|छंदित
छन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, gratified, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दु|छंदु
छन्दु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. pleasing, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोम
छन्दोम, अस्, m., N. of the eighth, ninth, and<BR>tenth day in a sacrificial ceremony which lasts<BR>twelve days (द्वादशाह).<BR>—छन्दोम-त्रिककुद्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">Page0332-c+ 70</a>]<BR>त्, m., N. of a Soma ceremony lasting three days.<BR>—छन्दोम-दशाह, अस्, m., N. of a Daśa-rātra.<BR>—छन्दोम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. accompanied<BR>by a Chandoma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
छद् 5. छद्, cl. 1. P. छदति, &c., to<BR>nourish, strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
छद् 6. छद्, cl. 1. and 10. P. छन्दति and<BR>छन्दयति, &c., to kindle; (a various<BR>reading for छृद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मट्
छद्मट् छद्मट्, ind. = छम्बट् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्वर
छद्वर छद्वर, अस्, m. a tooth (?); a bower;<BR>[cf. छत्त्वर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छनच्छन्
छनच्छन् छनच्छन्, ind. an imitative<BR>sound expressive of the noise of falling drops, of<BR>sobbing &c.; (according to some a reduplicated form<BR>of छनत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्न|छन्नं|छन्नः
छन्न छन्न. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्
छम् छम्, cl. 1. P. छमति, &c., to eat;<BR>[cf. चम्, जम्, झम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमच्छमिकारत्न|छमछमिकारत्न
छमच्छमिकारत्न छमच्छमिका-रत्न, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमच्छमित
छमच्छमित छमच्छमित, अम्, n. (an ono-<BR>matopoetic word with the termination of the past<BR>pass. part.), crackling, rattling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमण्ड|छमंड|छमंडः|छमण्डः
छमण्ड छमण्ड, अस्, m. an orphan, a<BR>fatherless son; a single man, one who has no kins-<BR>men; [cf. छेमण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्प्|छंप्
छम्प् छम्प्, cl. 1. 10. P. छम्पति,<BR>छम्पयति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्बट्
छम्बट् छम्बट्, ind., Ved. (used with rt.<BR>कृ, especially in sacrificial language), to make a<BR>failure, fail in obtaining or accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द्
छर्द् छर्द्, cl. 10. P. छर्दयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to vomit, be sick; [cf. छृद्; cf. also Hib.<BR>sceithim, ‘I vomit, spew;’ Lat. screo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द|छर्दः|छर्द्द|छर्द्दं
छर्द, अस्, m. (a various reading for छर्दि),<BR>vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दन|छर्दनं|छर्दनः|छर्द्दन|छर्द्दनं
छर्दन, अस्, m., N. of a plant (= अलम्बुष);<BR>of a Rākṣasa; another plant, = निम्ब; the plant<BR>Vangueria Spinosa; (अम्), n. vomiting, sickness;<BR>retching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दि|छर्दिः|छर्द्दि|छर्द्दिः
छर्दि, इस्, f. sickness, vomiting.<BR>—छर्दि-घ्न,<BR>अस्, m. ‘anti-emetic,’ N. of a tree, = निम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिका|छर्द्दिका
छर्दिका, f. sickness, vomiting; a plant, =<BR>विष्णु-क्रान्ता.<BR>—छर्दिका-रिपु, उस्, m. small<BR>cardamoms (‘anti-emetic’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिस्
1. छर्दिस्, इस्, f. n. vomiting. (For 2. छर्दिस् see<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दीका
छर्दीका, f. vomiting, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दापनिका|छर्द्दापनिका
छर्दापनिका छर्दापनिका, f. a kind of cu-<BR>cumber, = कर्कटी; (a corruption of छर्दापन-<BR>यिका ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिस्
छर्दिस् 2. छर्दिस्, इस्, n. (fr. 1. छद् ?), Ved.<BR>a fence, a secure place, secure residence; a house;<BR>[cf. छदिस्.]<BR>—छर्दिष्-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. pro-<BR>tecting a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्
छल् छल्, छलयति. See under छल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल|छलं|छलः
छल छल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably fr. 1.<BR>छद्), fraud, deceit, deception, sham, guise, dis-<BR>guise, pretence, pretext, delusion, illusion, semblance,<BR>counterfeit appearance, fiction, feint, circumvention,<BR>trick, stratagem; fallacy (e. g. वाक्-छलैः, with<BR>fallacious words); wickedness; design, device; in-<BR>tention; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Dala and descendant<BR>of Kuśa; छलात्, through deceit or fraud, deceitfully;<BR>छलेन, deceitfully, illusively, under the disguise or<BR>pretext or pretence of; उपदा-छलेन, under pre-<BR>tence of gifts of honour, i. e. with feigned gifts;<BR>रजश्-छलेन, under the semblance of dust; [cf.<BR>Lat. scelus.]<BR>—छल-कारक, अस्, आ, अम्, or छल-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">Page0333-a+ 73</a>]<BR>कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, practising fraud or deceit, fraudulent.<BR>—छल-ता, f. fraud, deception, deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0332-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलक
छलक, अस्, इका, अम्, delusive, deceptive, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलन|छलनं
छलन, अम्, आ, n. f. deceiving, deluding, trick-<BR>ing, cheating, outwitting, feigning.<BR>—छलना-पर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, deceitful, cunning, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलय
छलय, nom. P. छलयति, -यितुम्, to deceive,<BR>cheat, delude, circumvent, outwit, feign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलयत्
छलयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, deceiving, cheating, de-<BR>luding, outwitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलित
छलित, अस्, आ, अम्, deceived, cheated, deluded;<BR>feigned.<BR>—छलित-राम, अस्, m. ‘Rāma the out-<BR>witted,’ title of a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिन्
छलिन्, ई, m. cheating, a cheat; a swindler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिक|छलिकं
छलिक छलिक, अम्, n. a song consisting<BR>of four parts and recited with certain gestures or<BR>gesticulation; [cf. छालिक्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलितक
छलितक छलितक, अस्, m., N. of a man,<BR>the builder of a sanctuary which was called after him;<BR>(अम्), n. = छलिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्लि|छल्लिः
छल्लि छल्लि, इस्, f. skin, bark, rind, = छल्ली;<BR>[cf. छवि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्लित
छल्लित छल्लित in अस्थि-च्छल्लित, elevation<BR>of a small portion of the bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्ली
छल्ली छल्ली, f. skin, bark, rind [cf. छल्लि<BR>and छवि]; a spreading creeper (वीरुध्); a kind<BR>of flower; offspring, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छवि|छविः
छवि छवि, इस्, or छवी, f. (the latter only<BR>in Ved.; said to be fr. rt. छो), skin, hide; hue,<BR>colour of the skin, colour in general; beauty, splen-<BR>dor, brilliance; light, lustre; [cf. कृष्ण-च्छवि;<BR>cf. also Old Germ. scieri, ‘lucid;’ Hib. sceimh,<BR>‘beauty, bloom;’ sceimheach, ‘handsome.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छविल्लाकर|छविल्लाकरः
छविल्लाकर छविल्लाकर, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>historian of Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छष्
छष् छष्, cl. 1. P. A. छषति, -ते, to<BR>hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छा
छा छा, आस्, m. a young animal; [cf. 2. छ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग|छागः
छाग छाग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. छो),<BR>a goat; the sign of the zodiac Aries; N. of one of<BR>the attendants of Śiva; (ई), f. a she-goat; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), coming from or relating to a goat or she-<BR>goat.<BR>—छाग-भोजिन्, ई, m. a wolf, (‘goat-eater.’)<BR>—छाग-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, like a goat or she-goat.<BR>—छाग-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—छाग-<BR>मित्रिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, relating to Chāga-mitra.<BR>—छाग-रथ, अस्, m. Agni the god of fire (whose<BR>vehicle is the goat).<BR>—छाग-लक्षण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Pariśiṣṭa attributed to Kātyāyana.<BR>—छाग-<BR>वाहन, अस्, m. Agni the deity of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागल|छागलः
छागल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छगल), coming from<BR>or relating to a goat or to a she-goat, caprigenous;<BR>born in Chagala; (अस्), m. a goat; a kind of fish,<BR>= छागलक; a patronymic from Chagala (when<BR>a descendant of Atri is to be designated); N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—छागलान्त्रिका, f. a kind of plant, =<BR>छगलान्त्रिका.<BR>—छागलान्त्री (˚ल-अन्˚), f. a wolf;<BR>also = छगलान्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलक|छागलकः
छागलक, अस्, m. a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलि
छागलि, इस्, m. a metronymic from Chagalā and a<BR>patronymic from Chagala; a descendant of Atri; N.<BR>of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलेय
छागलेय, N. of a place; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>school; (अस्), m., N. of the author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलेयिन्
छागलेयिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils of Chagalin;<BR>the Sūtras of the pupils of Chagalin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागिका
छागिका, f. a she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागेय
छागेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग्यायनि
छाग्यायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Chāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागण|छागणः
छागण छागण, अस्, m. a fire of dried cow-<BR>dung (छगण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलेय
छागलेय छागलेय. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाछिका|छाच्छिका
छाछिका छाछिका, f., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाटा
छाटा छाटा, f. title of a commentary on<BR>the Mugdha-bodha; [cf. छटा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात|छातः
छात छात. See p. 334, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्त्र
छात्त्र छात्त्र. See p. 332, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद|छादं
छाद छाद. See p. 332, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्द
छान्द छान्द, अस्, ई, अम्, adj. fr. छन्द or<BR>छन्दस् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दड
छान्दड छान्दड, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दस|छांदस|छान्दसः
छान्दस छान्दस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छन्दस्),<BR>Vedic, having the sacred text of the Veda as (its)<BR>subject, peculiar to the Veda, relating or belonging to<BR>the Vedic hymns; studying the holy text of the<BR>Vedic hymns, a priest familiar with it; metrical, re-<BR>lating to poetical metre; (अस्), m. a priest conversant<BR>with the Veda or sacred hymns.<BR>—छान्दस-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the being Vedic, the being metrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दसक
छान्दसक, अम्, n. the being Vedic or metrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दसीय|छांदसीय
छान्दसीय, अस्, आ, अम्, metrical, familiar with<BR>metres, a metrical scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोग
छान्दोग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छन्दो-ग), relating to<BR>the Chando-gas.<BR>—छान्दोग-ब्राह्मण, see छन्-<BR>दोग-ब्राह्मण.<BR>—छान्दोग-सूत्र, अम्, n. a Sūtra<BR>work of the Chando-gas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोग्य|छान्दोग्यं
छान्दोग्य, अम्, n. (fr. छन्दो-ग), the doctrine<BR>of the Chando-gas or Udgātṛ priests contained in<BR>a Brāhmaṇa of the Sāma-veda; see छन्दोग-<BR>ब्राह्मण.<BR>—छान्दोग्य-मन्त्र-भाष्य, अम्, n.<BR>a commentary by Guṇa-viṣṇu on the prayers and texts<BR>in Gobhila's Gṛhya-sūtras.<BR>—छान्दोग्योपनिषद्<BR>(˚य-उप्˚), त्, f. title of the Upaniṣad attached to<BR>the Sāma-veda.<BR>—छान्दोग्योपनिषद्-भाष्य,<BR>अम्, n. a commentary on the above Upaniṣad by<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोभाष
छान्दोभाष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छन्दो-भाषा),<BR>relating to the language of the Vedas (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोम
छान्दोम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छन्दोम), taken from<BR>the Chandomas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोमान
छान्दोमान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छन्दो-मान), re-<BR>lating to a syllable regarded as the measure of metre<BR>or metrical unity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोमिक|छांदोमिक
छान्दोमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. छन्दोम), belong-<BR>ing to the Chandomas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाया
छाया छाया, f. (said to be fr. rt. छो, to<BR>cut off the light; perhaps a corruption of छद्या fr.<BR>rt. 1. छद्), shade, shadow, dark shadow, a shady<BR>place, (in the Naighaṇṭuka III. 4. = a screened or<BR>covered place, i. e. a house); a reflected image, re-<BR>flection; a shadowy fancy, hallucination; shading or<BR>blending of colours, play of light or colours, lustre,<BR>light, beauty; colour, the colour of the face, com-<BR>plexion, the features; a kind of metre consisting of<BR>four lines of nineteen syllables each; Shadow personi-<BR>fied, and like Sañjñā wife of the Sun and mother of the<BR>planet Saturn; the sun; the shadow of a gnomon as<BR>indicating the sun's position; a screen, protection,<BR>nourishing, cherishing; a row, line, straight or con-<BR>tinuous line; nightmare; a bribe; a N. of the goddess<BR>Durgā; (अम्), n. shade, shadow (at the end of a<BR>Tat-puruṣa compound); (अस्), m. one who grants<BR>shade.<BR>—छाया-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing shadow,<BR>shadowing, shading; (अस्), m. a parasol or umbrella-<BR>bearer; a species of metre.<BR>—छाया-ग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>‘receiving the shadow or image,’ a mirror, a sun-<BR>dial (?); [cf. छाया-यन्त्र.]<BR>—छायाङ्क (˚या-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. the moon (containing the image of a<BR>hare or deer, i. e. marked like a hare or deer); [cf.<BR>छाया-भृत् and छाया-मृग-धर.]<BR>—छाया-<BR>तनय, अस्, m. the son of Chāyā, an epithet of<BR>Saturn.<BR>—छाया-तरु, उस्, m. a large umbrageous tree,<BR>(giving abundant shade or shelter.)<BR>—छायात्मज<BR>(˚या-आत्˚), अस्, m. the son of Chāyā, an epithet of<BR>Saturn.<BR>—छायात्मन् (˚या-आत्˚), आ, m. a reflected<BR>image or form (lit. ‘shadow-self,’ the shadow or re-<BR>flected image of one's own person).<BR>—छाया-द्रुम,<BR>अस्, m. an umbrageous tree; see छाया-तरु.<BR>—छाया-<BR>द्वितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by one's shadow.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">Page0333-c+ 76</a>]<BR>—छाया-पथ, अस्, m. ether, the atmosphere or<BR>firmament.<BR>—छाया-पुरुष, अस्, m. Puruṣa in<BR>the form of a shadow.<BR>—छाया-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>divided in radiance, reflecting light from various<BR>surfaces.<BR>—छाया-भृत्, त्, m. the moon; [cf.<BR>छायाङ्क.]<BR>—छाया-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, shadowy,<BR>casting a shadow, reflected.<BR>—छाया-मान, अम्, n.<BR>an instrument that measures a shadow.<BR>—छाया-<BR>मित्र, अम्, n. a chattar or parasol (friend of the<BR>shade).<BR>—छाया-मृग-धर, अस्, m. ‘possessing<BR>the image of a deer,’ the moon; [cf. छायाङ्क.]<BR>—छाया-यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘shadow instrument,’ a sun-<BR>dial.<BR>—छाया-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, shadowy, possessing<BR>or granting shade.<BR>—छाया-व्यवहार, अस्, m.<BR>measuring or calculating the shadow cast by the sun<BR>on the dial.<BR>—छाया-सुत, अस्, m. the son of Chāyā,<BR>an epithet of Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायक
छायक, अस्, इका, अम्, Ved. shadowy (as a demon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छालिक्य
छालिक्य छालिक्य, अम्, n., N. of a kind of<BR>song; [cf. छलिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छि|छिः
छि छि, इस्, m. abuse, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कन
छिक्कन छिक्कन, अम्, n. (an onomatopoetic<BR>word with the affix of a noun of action), sneezing;<BR>(ई), f. the plant Artemisia Sternutatoria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्का
छिक्का, f. sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्किक
छिक्किक, अस्, आ, अम्, sneezing, sternutatory; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Artemisia Sternutatoria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कर
छिक्कर छिक्कर, अस्, m. a kind of animal;<BR>(perhaps an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कार
छिक्कार छिक्कार, अस्, m. a kind of antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित|छितं
छित छित. See rt. छो, p. 334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् 1. छिद्, cl. 7. P. A. छिनत्ति, छिन्त्ते,<BR>चिच्छेद, चिच्छिदे, छेत्स्यति, -ते, अच्छि-<BR>दत् or अच्छैत्सीत्, अच्छित्त, छेत्तुम्, to cut, cut off,<BR>amputate, cut through, hew, chop, rend, split, pierce,<BR>separate, divide, unfasten; to take away, remove, de-<BR>prive of; to interrupt, disturb; to destroy, annihilate,<BR>efface, blot out: Pass. छिद्यते, to be split, to be<BR>cut, to break, be torn, &c.: Caus. P. छेदयति,<BR>यितुम्; Aor. अचिच्छिदत्, to cut off; to cause to<BR>cut off or through: Desid. चिच्छित्सति, -ते: Intens.<BR>चेच्छिद्यते, चेच्छिदीति, चेच्छेत्ति; [cf. Lat. scindo:<BR>Gr. σχίζω, σχίδη, σχέδη, σχινδαλμός, σκινδαλμός,<BR>σκίδνημι; σκάζω (?): Goth. skeida: Germ. scheide:<BR>Old Germ. schîte; splitar: Mod. Germ. splitter:<BR>Hib. scaithim, ‘I cut off, lop,’ &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्ति|छित्तिः
छित्ति, इस्, f. cutting, division; N. of a tree, =<BR>करञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्त्वर
छित्त्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, cutting or fit for cutting (as<BR>a weapon &c.), trenchant; hostile, inimical, a foe;<BR>roguish, fraudulent, knavish, a knave; [cf. छत्-<BR>त्वर and छिदुर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्त्वा
छित्त्वा, ind. having cut, amputated, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
2. छिद्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of a compound) cutting,<BR>cutting through, tearing asunder, splitting, piercing<BR>[cf. उख-च्छिद्, केश-च्छिद्, पक्ष-च्छिद्]; de-<BR>stroying, annihilating, removing [cf. दुःख-च्छिद्];<BR>(त्), m. the divisor, denominator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदक|छिदकं
छिदक, अम्, n. Indra's thunderbolt or diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदा
छिदा, f. cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदि|छिदिः
छिदि, इस्, इस्, इ, cutting or tearing off, splitting;<BR>(इस्), f. an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिर|छिदिरः
छिदिर, अस्, m. an axe; a sword; fire; a rope,<BR>cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदुर|छिदुरः
छिदुर, अस्, आ, अम्, cutting, dividing, what cuts<BR>or divides; easily breaking; hostile, a foe; roguish,<BR>a knave; [cf. छित्त्वर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्यमान
छिद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being cut, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, containing holes, pierced;<BR>(अम्), n. a hole, slit, incision, cleft, opening, fissure,<BR>crack, perforation, vacuity, interruption, (छिद्रं<BR>दैव-कृतम्, the opening or hole made by nature,<BR>the cartilage of the ear, the pupil of the eye, &c.);<BR>defect, fault, blemish, flaw (moral or physical); a<BR>vulnerable or weak point, weak side, foible, imper-<BR>fection, infirmity; (in astronomy) N. of the eighth<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">Page0334-a+ 80</a>]<BR>house; [cf. अ-च्छिद्र, कर्ण-च्छ्˚, कृत-च्छ्˚, गृ-<BR>ह-च्छ्˚, निश्-छ्˚.]<BR>—छिद्र-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>the ears bored or pierced.<BR>—छिद्र-ता, f. the state of<BR>being perforated, the quality of being perforated or<BR>pervaded by everything.<BR>—छिद्र-दर्शन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, exhibiting faults or deficiencies, (अ-च्छिद्रदर्-<BR>शन, faultless); (अस्), m., N. of a Cakra-vāka that<BR>had been a Brāhman in a former birth.<BR>—छिद्र-<BR>दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, observing faults or deficiencies,<BR>a captious critic; (ई), m., N. of a Cakra-vāka; see<BR>above.<BR>—छिद्र-वैदेही, f. the plant Scindapsus<BR>Officinalis, = गज-पिप्पली.<BR>—छिद्रात्मन् (˚र-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one who exposes his weak points to<BR>attack.<BR>—छिद्रानुसन्धानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or छिद्रा-<BR>नुसारिन् or छिद्रान्वेषिन् (˚र-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, look-<BR>ing out for faults or flaws, picking holes, a censorious<BR>or captious critic.<BR>—छिद्रान्तर् (˚र-अन्˚), अः, m.<BR>‘internally hollow,’ cane or reed.<BR>—छिद्रान्वेषण<BR>(˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. the searching for faults, picking<BR>holes; [cf. छिद्रानुसन्धानिन् above.]<BR>—छिद्रा-<BR>फल, अम्, n. a kind of fruit; [cf. माया-<BR>फल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रय
छिद्रय, nom. P. छिद्रयति, -यितुम्, to pierce,<BR>perforate, bore, make openings or holes, to perforate<BR>the ears for rings &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रापय
छिद्रापय, nom. P. -पयति, -यितुम्, to pierce,<BR>perforate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रित|छिद्रितः
छिद्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced, perforated, having<BR>holes, orifices or openings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रिन्
छिद्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having holes, hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्वर
छिद्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, = छित्त्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्दक
छिन्दक, अस्, m., N. of a family or race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्न|छिन्नं
छिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, divided, torn, broken, de-<BR>stroyed; decaying, declining, exhausted, tired; (आ), f.<BR>a whore, a harlot; the tree Cocculus Cordifolius, =<BR>गुडूची.<BR>—छिन्न-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, having the ears<BR>cut off.<BR>—छिन्न-केश, अस्, आ, अम्, having the hair cut,<BR>shorn, shaven.<BR>—छिन्न-ग्रन्थिनिका, f. a kind of<BR>bulbous plant, = त्रि-पर्णिका.<BR>—छिन्न-द्रुम, अस्,<BR>m. a riven tree.<BR>—छिन्न-धन्वन्, आ, m. a warrior<BR>whose bow has been cut or broken by his enemy's<BR>arrow.<BR>—छिन्न-नासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>nose cut off, noseless.<BR>—छिन्न-नास्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the nose-rein (or cord passing through the<BR>nose) cut or broken.<BR>—छिन्न-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the wings clipped or torn off.<BR>—छिन्न-पत्-<BR>त्री, f., N. of a plant, = अम्बष्ठा.<BR>—छिन्न-बन्-<BR>धन, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed from bonds, liberated.<BR>—छिन्न-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced through and<BR>through, cut up, destroyed, scattered.<BR>—छिन्न-भू-<BR>यिष्ठधूम, अस्, आ, अम्, bursting through the thick<BR>smoke, scattering the mass of smoke.<BR>—छिन्न-<BR>मस्त or छिन्न-मस्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, decapitated;<BR>(आ), f. a headless form of Durgā.<BR>—छिन्न-<BR>मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, cut up by the root.<BR>—छिन्न-<BR>रुह, अस्, m., N. of a tree, = तिलक; (आ), f.<BR>N. of several plants, viz. Cocculus Cordifolius;<BR>incense, = शल्लकी; also = स्वर्ण-केतकी.<BR>—छिन्-<BR>न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having cut or cut off.<BR>—छिन्न-<BR>वेशिका, f. the plant Clypea Hernandifolia, = पाठा.<BR>—छिन्न-श्वास, अस्, m. interrupted or irregular<BR>breathing, a kind of asthma; (अस्, आ, अम्), breathing<BR>at irregular intervals.<BR>—छिन्न-संशय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one whose doubts are dispelled, freed from doubt;<BR>confirmed, confident.<BR>—छिन्नोद्भवा (˚न-उद्˚), f.<BR>the plant Cocculus Cordifolius, = गुडूची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नक
छिन्नक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a little cut off, in-<BR>cised; (Compar. छिन्नक-तर = छिन्नतरक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तव्य
छेत्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut, to be cut off &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तृ
छेत्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what cuts, a cutter, a<BR>wood-cutter; destroying, removing, solving, a resolver<BR>of (doubts &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद|छेदः
छेद, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comp.) cutting,<BR>cutting off [cf. स्थाणु-च्छेद]; (अस्), m. a cutting<BR>or dividing, divisor, the denominator of a fraction;<BR>a distinguishing mark [cf. भक्ति-च्छेद]; a cut, a<BR>section, a piece, portion, a part cut off or broken off;<BR>an incision, cleft; slit; cutting, dividing, tearing off;<BR>solving, dissipating (doubt &c.); destruction, inter-<BR>ruption, vanishing; cessation, deprivation, want, de-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">Page0334-b+ 72</a>]<BR>ficiency.<BR>—छेद-कर, अस्, आ and ई, अम्, cutting;<BR>(अस्), m. a wood-cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदक|छेदकः
छेदक, अस्, इका, अम्, cutting off, dividing; the<BR>denominator of a fraction; [cf. ग्रन्थि-च्छेदक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदन|छेदनं
छेदन, अस्, ई, अम्, cutting asunder, splitting;<BR>destroying, solving, removing; (अम्), n. cutting,<BR>cutting off, amputation, dividing, tearing asunder,<BR>splitting; division; a section, a part, a portion; de-<BR>struction, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदनीय|छेदनीयः
छेदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut or divided,<BR>divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदि|छेदिः
छेदि, इस्, इस्, इ, cutting off; breaking; (इस्), m. a<BR>carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदित|छेदितं
छेदित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदितव्य
छेदितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut or divided, divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदिन्
छेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, cutting off, tearing off or asun-<BR>der; destroying, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद्य
छेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cut or divided, divisible;<BR>to be cut off or amputated, to be split, to be muti-<BR>lated; (अम्), n. amputation, excision; [cf. कुड्य-<BR>च्छेद्य and पत्त्र-च्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छैदिक|छैदिकः
छैदिक, अस्, m. a ratan, a cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिप्पिका
छिप्पिका छिप्पिका, f. a kind of bird (?);<BR>[cf. चिप्पिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिलिहिण्ड|छिलिहिण्डः
छिलिहिण्ड छिलिहिण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a plant,<BR>= पाताल-गरुड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुच्छुन्दर|छुच्छुन्दरः|छुछुंदर|छुछुन्दर|छुछुंदरः
छुच्छुन्दर छुच्छुन्दर, अस्, m. or (इ, इस् or<BR>ई), f. the musk-rat or shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुच्छू
छुच्छू छुच्छू, ऊस्, f. or छुच्छू-पिङ्गला, f.<BR>a kind of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुट्
छुट् छुट् (a various reading for चुट्), cl.<BR>6. 10. P. छुटति, छोटयति, &c., to cut;<BR>[cf. Hib. sgoth, ‘a cut;’ sgothan, ‘a small flock.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुड्
छुड् छुड् (a various reading for थुड्),<BR>cl. 6. P. छुडति, &c., to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुड्ड
छुड्ड छुड्ड, अस्, m., N. of several men;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुद्र|छुद्रं
छुद्र छुद्र, अम्, n. retaliation, counter-<BR>action, remedying; a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप्
छुप् छुप्, cl. 6. P. छुपति, चुच्छोप,<BR>छोप्स्यति, अच्छौप्सीत्, छोप्तुम्, to touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप|छुपः
छुप, अस्, m. touch, touching; a small tree, a<BR>shrub, a bush; air, wind; war, combat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुबुक|छुबुकं
छुबुक छुबुक, अम्, n., Ved. the chin;<BR>[cf. चिवुक and चुबुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुर्
छुर् छुर्, cl. 6. P. छुरति, चुच्छोर,<BR>छुरितुम्, &c., to cut, engrave, incise,<BR>etch: Caus. छुरयति and छोरयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>inlay, veneer, to set with mosaic ornaments; [cf.<BR>क्षुर्; cf. also Hib. scuirim or sguirim, ‘I cease,<BR>desist,’ cf. छेद; Old Germ. scar, sciru, &c.;<BR>Mod. Germ. Schere.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरा
छुरा, f. lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरिका
छुरिका, f. a knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरित|छुरितं
छुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, inlaid, set, coated, spread;<BR>blended, intermingled.<BR>—छुरितोदर (˚त-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, pierced through the belly; transfixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरी
छुरी, f. a knife, = क्षुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छूरिका
छूरिका, f. = छुरिका in छूरिका-पत्त्री, N. of a<BR>plant, = श्वेता, Andropogon Aciculatus; the mouth<BR>of a cow; (other readings have खुरिका, स्फुरिका,<BR>स्थुरिका, स्थूरिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छूरी
छूरी, f. = छुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोरण|छोरणं
छोरण, अम्, n. abandoning, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृद्
छृद् छृद्, cl. 7. P. छृणत्ति, चच्छर्द,<BR>छर्दिष्यति or छर्त्स्यति, छर्दितुम्,<BR>to pour out; P. and A. छृणत्ति, छृन्त्ते, &c., to<BR>play, shine; to vomit; cl. 1. P. छर्दति, &c., to<BR>kindle: Caus. छर्दयति, to pour out; to spit<BR>out, eject, vomit; to cause to spit; to kindle: Desid.<BR>चिच्छर्दिषति, -ते, or चिच्छृत्सति, -ते: Intens.<BR>चरीच्छृद्यते, चरिच्छर्त्ति; [cf. छर्द्; cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">Page0334-c+ 65</a>]<BR>also Lat. splendeo; Lith. spindẓiu, spindulys,<BR>skaistus, skaistas; Germ. glänzen ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृप्
छृप् छृप् (a various reading for छृद्),<BR>cl. 1. 10. P. छर्पति, छर्पयति, &c.,<BR>to kindle, inflame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेक|छेकः
छेक छेक, अस्, आ, अम्, tame, domesticated<BR>(as a bird or beast); citizen, town-bred, shrewd,<BR>sharp, smart, trained in the acuteness and vice of<BR>towns; (with अनु-प्रास), a kind of alliteration, repe-<BR>tition of two or more consonants in different words;<BR>(अस्), m. a bee.<BR>—छेकोक्ति (˚क-उक्˚), इस्, f. indirect<BR>speech, insinuation, double entendre, hint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेकाल
छेकाल or छेकिल, अस्, आ, अम्, = छेक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तव्य
छेत्तव्य छेत्तव्य. See under 1. छिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेमण्ड|छेमंड|छेमंडः|छेमण्डः
छेमण्ड छेमण्ड, अस्, m. a fatherless child;<BR>[cf. छमण्ड and काचिघ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेलु|छेलुः
छेलु छेलु, उस्, m. the plant Vernonia<BR>Anthelmintica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छैदिक|छैदिकः
छैदिक छैदिक. See under 1. छिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छो
छो छो, cl. 4. P. छ्यति, चच्छौ, छास्-<BR>यति, अच्छात् or अच्छासीत्, छातुम्, to cut,<BR>divide, mow, reap: Caus. P. छाययति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात|छातः
छात or छित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, divided, thin,<BR>feeble, emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोज
छोज छोज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिका
छोटिका छोटिका, f. snapping the thumb<BR>and forefinger together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिन्
छोटिन् छोटिन्, ई, m. (said to be fr. rt. छो),<BR>a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोरण|छोरणं
छोरण छोरण. See under rt. छुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोलङ्ग|छोलंगः|छोलङ्गः
छोलङ्ग छोलङ्ग, अस्, m. = मातुलु ग, a<BR>citron, lime; [cf. अम्बु-केशर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ्यु
छ्यु छ्यु, cl. 1. A. छ्यवते, &c., to go,<BR>move, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज 1. ज, the third letter of the second or<BR>palatal class of consonants, having the sound of ज् in<BR>जुम्प्.<BR>—ज-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज 2. ज, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. जन्, and used<BR>at the end of comp.), born from, descended from, a<BR>son or daughter of, produced or caused by, born in,<BR>produced in or at or upon, growing in, living at,<BR>being at [cf. अत्रि-दृग्-ज, धृतराष्ट्र-ज, आत्म-<BR>ज, अण्ड-ज, कुल-ज, वन-ज, सरसि-ज, अग्र-ज,<BR>अवर-ज, एक-ज, &c.]; prepared from, made of or<BR>with; belonging to, connected with, peculiar to [cf.<BR>अन्न-ज and शक्र-ज]; (अस्), m. a father, pro-<BR>genitor; birth, production; [cf. जा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज 3. ज, अस्, आ, अम् (connected with the<BR>preceding by some lexicographers, but the meanings<BR>appear to be artificial), speedy, swift; victorious,<BR>triumphant, conquering; eaten; (अस्), m. speed;<BR>enjoyment; light, lustre; poison; a Piśāca; a N.<BR>of Viṣṇu; also of Śiva; (आ), f. a husband's brother's<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंस्
जंस् जंस्, cl. 10. P. जंसयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>protect; to liberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंह्
जंह् जंह्, Ved. only in Intens. जङ्गहे,<BR>to strike with the wings or feet, to kick;<BR>(Sāy. who derives this word from ग्रह्), to hold<BR>tight, hold fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंहस्
जंहस्, अस्, n., Ved. flapping of the wings; (Sāy.)<BR>velocity, speed; [cf. कृष्ण-जंहस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक
जक जक, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जकुट|जकुटं|जकुटः
जकुट जकुट, अस्, m. a dog; the Malaya<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">Page0335-a+ 78</a>]<BR>mountains; (अम्), n. a pair; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the<BR>egg-plant, Solanum Melongena, or its flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्
जक्ष् 1. जक्ष् (probably a reduplicated<BR>form of घस्, q. v.), cl. 2. P. जक्षिति, 3rd<BR>pl. जक्षति (Gram. 290. ब्); Impf. अजक्षीत् and<BR>अजक्षत् (Pāṇ. VII. 3, 98, 99), 3rd pl. अजक्षुस्;<BR>जजक्ष, जक्षिष्यति; Aor. अजक्षीत्, 3rd pl.<BR>अजक्षिषुस्; जक्षितुम् or जग्धुम्, (Pres. part.<BR>nom. sing. m. जक्षत्, Pāṇ. VII. 1, 78), to eat,<BR>consume, destroy; to wish to eat: Caus. जक्ष-<BR>यति, अजजक्षत्: Desid. जिजक्षिषति: Intens.<BR>जाजक्ष्यते, जाजष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षण|जक्षणं
जक्षण, अम्, n. eating, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षि|जक्षिः
जक्षि, इस्, f. eating, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षिवस्
जक्षिवस्, आन्, उषी, अत् (perf. part. fr. rt. घस्),<BR>one who has eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्ध|जग्धं
जग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, eaten; (अम्), n. a place where a<BR>person has eaten.<BR>—जग्ध-पाप्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. one<BR>whose sin or wickedness is consumed or blotted out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्धि|जग्धिः
जग्धि, इस्, f. eating, consuming; food, victuals;<BR>[cf. कल्य-जग्धि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्
जक्ष् 2. जक्ष् (reduplicated fr. rt. हस्),<BR>cl. 2. P., Ved. जक्षिति, &c., to laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष
जक्ष जक्ष, अस्, m. a Prākṛt form for यक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्म|जक्ष्मः
जक्ष्म, अस्, m. and जक्ष्मन्, आ, m. two<BR>Prākṛt forms for यक्ष्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्
जगत् जगत्, अत्, अती, अत् (reduplicated form<BR>fr. rt. गम्), moving, movable, locomotive, transitory;<BR>(त्), n. that which moves or is alive, men and animals,<BR>or animals as opposed to men; (in the later language)<BR>the world, the earth, the universe; (ती), n. du. heaven<BR>and the lower world; जगन्ति, n. pl. the worlds;<BR>(त्), m. air, wind; (ती), f. a female animal, a cow,<BR>(metaphorically ‘milk, water’); the earth; the site<BR>of a house; people, mankind; the world, the uni-<BR>verse; a particular metre consisting of four lines of<BR>twelve syllables each; a general name for any metre<BR>containing 4 × 12 syllables; a sacrificial brick named<BR>after the metre Jagatī; a field planted with Jambū.<BR>—जगच्-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. ‘the eye of the universe,’<BR>the sun.<BR>—जगच्-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a commentary<BR>by Bhaṭṭotpala on the work Vṛhaj-jātaka; (this com-<BR>mentary is also called Cintā-maṇi.)<BR>—जगच्-छन्दस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, one to whom the metre Jagatī belongs,<BR>or to whom it is chiefly addressed &c.<BR>—जगज्-जीव,<BR>अस्, m. living in the world, a living being.<BR>—जगज्-<BR>जीवन-दास, अस्, m., N. of the author of three<BR>poems entitled Jñāna-prakāśa, Prathama-grantha, and<BR>Mahā-pralaya.<BR>—जगती-धर, अस्, m. ‘supporter of<BR>the world,’ a mountain; N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ज-<BR>गती-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the earth,’ a king.<BR>—ज-<BR>गती-पाल, अस्, m. ‘earth-protector,’ a king.<BR>—जगती-<BR>भर्तृ, ता, m. ‘supporter of the earth,’ king.<BR>—जगती-भुज्, क्, m. one who enjoys or possesses<BR>the earth, a king.<BR>—जगती-रुह, अस्, m. ‘growing<BR>on the earth,’ a tree.<BR>—जगती-वराह, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Sāman.<BR>—जगत्-कर्तृ, ता, m. the creator of<BR>the world; Brahmā.<BR>—जगत्-कारण, अम्, n. the<BR>cause of the universe.<BR>—जगत्-कृत्स्न, अम्, n. the<BR>whole world, the universe.<BR>—जगत्-क्षय, अस्, m.<BR>the destruction of the world.<BR>—जगत्-त्रय, अम्, n.<BR>the three worlds, or heaven, earth, and the lower<BR>world (पाताल).<BR>—जगत्-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>world,’ an epithet of Śiva, also of Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa; a king.<BR>—जगत्-प्रभु, उस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>the world,’ an epithet of Brahmā, of Śiva, of Viṣṇu;<BR>an Arhat of the Jainas.<BR>—जगत्-प्रसिद्ध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, known throughout the world, notorious.<BR>—ज-<BR>गत्-प्राण, अस्, m. the breath of the world, wind,<BR>air.<BR>—जगत्-समग्र, अम्, n. the entire world, the<BR>universe.<BR>—जगत्-सर्व, अम्, n. the whole world.<BR>—जगत्-साक्षिन्, ई, m. the witness or spectator of<BR>the world, the sun.<BR>—जगत्-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Māna-siṃha and father of Mahā-siṃha.<BR>—ज-<BR>गत्-स्रष्ट्टि, टा, m. the creator of the world;<BR>Brahmā; Śiva.<BR>—जगत्-स्वामिन्, ई, m. lord of the<BR>world, the supreme deity; N. of an image of the<BR>sun in Dvādaśādityāśrama; N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—जगद्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-b" target="_blank">Page0335-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अन्त, अस्, m. the end of the world.<BR>—जगद्-अन्तक,<BR>अस्, m. the destroyer of the world.<BR>—जगदन्त-<BR>कान्तक (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m. destroying the destroyer<BR>of the world.<BR>—जगद्-अम्बा, f. the mother of the<BR>world, a N. of Durgā.<BR>—जगद्-आत्मक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose self is the world, identical with the world.<BR>—जगद्-आत्मन्, आ, m. the soul of the world, the<BR>supreme spirit.<BR>—जगद्-आदि-ज, अस्, m. the first-born<BR>of the world, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—जगद्-आधार,<BR>अस्, m. ‘stay or supporter of the universe,’ an epithet<BR>of Time; also of the Jina Vīra; air, wind.<BR>—जगद्-<BR>आनन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoicing the world.<BR>—जगद्-<BR>आयु, उस्, m. or जगद्-आयुस्, उस्, m. the life-spring of<BR>the world, an epithet of the wind.<BR>—जगद्-ईश, अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of the universe,’ and epithet of Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa, also of Śiva and Brahmā; N. of a man;<BR>N. of the author of a commentary entitled Anumāna-<BR>dīdhiti-ṭippanī.<BR>—जगद्-ईश्वर, अस्, m. the lord of<BR>the universe; an epithet of Śiva; a king; N. of the<BR>author of the play Hāsyārṇava.<BR>—जगद्-उद्धार,<BR>अस्, m. the salvation or deliverance of the world.<BR>—जगद्-एकनाथ, अस्, m. the sole monarch<BR>of the world; an epithet of Raghu.<BR>—जगद्-एक-<BR>पावन, अस्, ई, अम्, the sole purifier of the world.<BR>—जगद्-गुरु, उस्, m. the father of the world; an<BR>epithet of Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Śiva, and Rāma (as an<BR>incarnation of Viṣṇu).<BR>—जगद्-गौरी, f. an epithet<BR>of Manasādevī, the deified wife of the sage Jaratkāru<BR>and sister of the Nāgas or serpent-race.<BR>—जगद्-<BR>घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying the world, destructive,<BR>hostile to mankind.<BR>—जगद्-दीप, अस्, m. ‘illumi-<BR>nator of the world,’ an epithet of the sun.<BR>—जगद्-<BR>द्वीप, अस्, m. wrong reading for जगद्-वीज, q. v.<BR>—जगद्-धर, अस्, m. ‘supporter or sustainer of<BR>the world,’ N. of the author of a commentary on the<BR>plays Mālatī-mādhava and Veṇī-saṃhāra, a son of<BR>Ratna-dhara and grandson of Vidyā-dhara.<BR>—ज-<BR>गद्-धातृ, ता, m. ‘maintainer of the world,’ an<BR>epithet of Brahmā and of Viṣṇu; (त्री), f. ‘fosterer<BR>of the world,’ an epithet of Sarasvatī and Durgā.<BR>—जगद्-बल, अस्, m. ‘the strength of the world,’<BR>or ‘surrounding the world,’ (fr. rt. वल्), wind, air.<BR>—जगद्-योनि, इस्, m. ‘the womb or place of pro-<BR>duction of the world,’ an epithet of Śiva, Viṣṇu,<BR>Kṛṣṇa, and Brahmā; (इस्), f. the mother of all<BR>living beings, the earth.<BR>—जगद्-वन्द्य, अस्, m.<BR>‘to be praised or adored by the world,’ an epithet<BR>of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—जगद्-वहा, f. ‘bearer of all living<BR>beings,’ the earth.<BR>—जगद्-विनाश, अस्, m. the de-<BR>struction of the world, the expiration of a Yuga or<BR>period of the world's existence.<BR>—जगद्-वीज, अम्, n.<BR>seed or first principle of the world, epithet of Śiva.<BR>—जगन्-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘the lord of the world,’ a N.<BR>of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; also of Rāma and of Dattātreya<BR>(both incarnations of Viṣṇu); N. of a celebrated<BR>idol; also of a temple, and the surrounding district<BR>on the Coromandel coast near Cuttack in Orissa,<BR>where Viṣṇu is especially worshipped as Jagan-nāth;<BR>(pilgrimages are made from all parts of India to the<BR>idol of Jagannāth there enshrined; see जगन्नाथ-<BR>क्षेत्र and पुरुषोत्तम-क्षेत्र); N. of the<BR>author of a work entitled Rekhā-gaṇita; the author<BR>of the poem Bhāminī-vilāsa; N. of a son of Rudra<BR>who compiled at the end of the last century the work<BR>Vivāda-bhaṅgārṇava; (औ), m. du. epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>and Śiva; (आ), f. epithet of Durgā.<BR>—जगन्नाथ-<BR>क्षेत्र, अम्, n. the shrine of Jagannātha and sur-<BR>rounding district, see above.<BR>—जगन्नाथ-वल्ल-<BR>भ-नाटक, अम्, n. title of a play.<BR>—जगन्-निवास,<BR>अस्, m. the abode of the world, an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>or Kṛṣṇa; worldly existence.<BR>—जगन्-मणि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a copyist.<BR>—जगन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>taining the whole world.<BR>—जगन्-मातृ, ता, f.<BR>‘mother of the world,’ epithet of Durgā and<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्वस्
जगन्वस्, वान्, ग्मुषी, वत् (perf. part.), one<BR>who has gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मि|जग्मिः
जग्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. going, being in constant<BR>motion; going to, hastening towards (with acc. or<BR>loc.); (इस्), m. the wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मिवस्
जग्मिवस्, वान्, मुषी, वत्, who or what has gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गम|जंगम|जङ्गमः
जङ्गम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of rt. गम्),<BR>moving, movable, locomotive, that which has motion<BR>as opposed to that which is stationary, living; a<BR>living being (= जगत् in the earlier language); de-<BR>rived from living beings; [cf. Goth. gagga; Germ.<BR>Gang.]<BR>—जङ्गम-कुटी, f. a parasol, a chattar or<BR>umbrella (‘movable house’).<BR>—जङ्गम-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of having motion, movableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद|जगदः
जगद जगद, अस्, m. an attendant, a<BR>guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्दल
जगद्दल जगद्दल, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>the Darads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगनु|जगनुः
जगनु जगनु or जगन्नु, उस्, m. a living<BR>being, an animal; an insect; fire or its deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगर|जगरः
जगर जगर, अस्, m. armour, mail; [cf.<BR>जागर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगल|जगलः
जगल जगल, अस्, आ, अम्, fraudulent, knav-<BR>ish; (अस्), m. a kind of intoxicating beverage, any<BR>fluid suitable for distillation; the plant Vangueria<BR>Spinosa, = मदन-वृक्ष; armour, mail [cf. ज-<BR>गर]; (अम्), n. cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगुरि
जगुरि जगुरि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. गम् or गा),<BR>Ved. leading, conducting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्गिक
जग्गिक जग्गिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्ध|जग्धं
जग्ध जग्ध. See under 1. जक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मि|जग्मिः
जग्मि जग्मि, जग्मिवस्. See under जगत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन|जघनं
जघन जघन, अस्, अम्, m. n. in the later<BR>language always n. (probably a reduplicated form of<BR>rt. हन्, but by some connected with जंह्), the<BR>hinder part, the buttock, the hip and loins, the<BR>pudenda, mons veneris; rear-guard, reserve of an<BR>army; [cf. जङ्घा.]<BR>—जघन-कूपक, औ, m.<BR>du. the hollow of the loins of a handsome woman.<BR>—जघन-गौरव, अम्, n. the weight of the<BR>hips.<BR>—जघन-चपला, f. a libidinous woman<BR>(moving the hips); a woman active in dancing; a<BR>species of the Āryā metre.<BR>—जघन-तस्, ind.<BR>behind, on the hinder part, after; [cf. अग्र-तस्.]<BR>—जघनार्ध (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m. the hinder part<BR>(opposed to पूर्वार्ध); rear-guard, reserve of an<BR>army.<BR>—जघने-फला, f. the opposite-leaved fig-<BR>tree, Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनिन्
जघनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having stout hips or large<BR>buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनेन
जघनेन, ind. behind, (with gen. or acc.) back-<BR>wards, away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्य|जघन्यः
जघन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, hindmost, hinder, last,<BR>latest, lowest, low, worst, vilest, vile, base, shortest,<BR>least, least important; of low origin or rank; (अस्),<BR>m. a Śūdra or man of the lowest class; N. of the<BR>attendant of Mālavya, who was one of the five princes<BR>born under particular constellations; (अम्), n. the<BR>penis; (अम् or ए), ind. after, behind, last; जघन्ये<BR>कृ, to leave behind, turn the back on; [cf. Hib.<BR>deaghanach, ‘last.’]<BR>—जघन्य-गुण-वृत्ति-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to low pursuits, chiefly familiar<BR>with the lowest of the three Guṇas.<BR>—जघन्य-च-<BR>पला, f. a species of the Āryā metre; [cf. जघन-<BR>चपला.]<BR>—जघन्य-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, last born, young-<BR>est; low-born; (अस्), m. a younger brother; a Śūdra.<BR>—जघन्य-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, lower, inferior.<BR>—ज-<BR>घन्य-तस्, ind. behind, at the back, after.<BR>—जघन्य-<BR>शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, lying down last, going to bed last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्वस्
जघन्वस् जघन्वस्, वान्, घ्नुषी, वत् (fr.<BR>rt. हन्), who or what has killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नि|जघ्निः
जघ्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, striking, killing; (इस्), m. a<BR>weapon, offensive instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्निवस्
जघ्निवस्, वान्, घ्नुषी, वत् (perf. part.), =<BR>जघन्वस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नु|जघ्नुः
जघ्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, striking, beating, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्रि
जघ्रि जघ्रि, इस्, इस्, इ (reduplicated form fr.<BR>rt. घृ), Ved. pouring out, sprinkling about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्क्ष्
जङ्क्ष् जङ्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. जङ्क्षति, a various<BR>reading for क्षज् or क्षञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्ग|जङ्गः
जङ्ग जङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गपूग
जङ्गपूग जङ्गपूग, अस्, m. wickedness,<BR>sin (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गम|जंगम|जङ्गमः
जङ्गम जङ्गम. See p. 335, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गल|जंगल|जङ्गलं|जङ्गलः
जङ्गल जङ्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, arid, sterile,<BR>desert; (अस्), m. a desert, waste or overgrown land,<BR>any arid or sterile region, any wild or uninhabited<BR>country, a jungle; (अस्, अम्), m. n. flesh, meat; [cf.<BR>जाङ्गल and जङ्गुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गाल|जंगाल|जंगालः|जङ्गालः
जङ्गाल, अस्, m. a land-mark, a limit, a boundary,<BR>a ridge of earth running along the edge of a field for<BR>collecting water and forming a passage over it, a balk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गुल|जंगुल|जंगुलं
जङ्गुल, अम्, n. poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गिड|जङ्गिडः
जङ्गिड जङ्गिड, अस्, m., N. of a plant<BR>which is worn as an amulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घ
जङ्घ जङ्घ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. जन्,<BR>or corrupted from जङ्गा fr. rt. गा, to go, or fr. rt.<BR>जंह्; cf. जघन), N. of a Rakṣas; (आ), f. the<BR>shank or lower part of the leg from the ankle to the<BR>knee; (in the earlier language also) the upper part<BR>of the leg; a part of a bedstead; [cf. Old Germ.<BR>scinkel; Germ. Schenkel.]<BR>—जङ्घा-कर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, or जङ्घा-करिक, अस्, आ, अम्, active with the<BR>legs, running quickly, a runner.<BR>—जङ्घा-कारिक,<BR>अस्, m. a runner, a courier, an express.<BR>—जङ्घा-<BR>त्राण, अम्, n. armour or protection for the legs,<BR>cuisses or greaves.<BR>—जङ्घा-बन्धु, उस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—जङ्घा-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. his descendants.<BR>—जङ्घारि (˚घा-अरि), इस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाल|जंघाल|जङ्घालः
जङ्घाल, अस्, आ, अम्, running swiftly, quick, rapid,<BR>going quickly; (अस्), m. a courier; a deer, an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घिका
जङ्घिका, f. a diminutive fr. जङ्घा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घिल|जंघिल
जङ्घिल, अस्, आ, अम्, running swiftly, quick, rapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्
जज् जज्, cl. 1. P. जजति, &c., to fight;<BR>[cf. जञ्ज्; cf. also Hib. fighim, ‘I fight;’<BR>Germ. fechte; Old Germ. vihtu; Lat. pugno.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज|जजं|जजः
जज, अस्, m. a warrior.<BR>—जजौजस् (˚ज-ओज्˚), अस्,<BR>n. prowess, valour; [cf. जाजिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्ज
जज्ज जज्ज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्जल
जज्जल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्ञि
जज्ञि जज्ञि, इस्, इस्, इ (reduplicated form fr.<BR>rt. जन्), germinating, shooting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जझ्झती
जझ्झती जझ्झती, ईस्, f. pl., Ved. (scil. आपस्),<BR>dashing, splashing or rushing waters; (an onomato-<BR>poetic word formed like a pres. part. from a supposed<BR>rt. जझ्झ्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जञ्ज्|जंज्
जञ्ज् जञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. जञ्जति, &c., = जज्,<BR>to fight; [cf. Lith. ẓinczíju.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जञ्जणाभवत्|जञ्जणाभवन्त्
जञ्जणाभवत् जञ्जणा-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्,<BR>Ved. glittering, flashing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जञ्जपूक|जंजपूक|जञ्जपूकः
जञ्जपूक जञ्जपूक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens.<BR>of rt. जप्), muttering prayers repeatedly, muttering<BR>incantations or charms; (अस्), m. an ascetic, a devotee,<BR>one who mutters prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट्
जट् जट् (probably a rt. derived fr. जट<BR>below), cl. 1. P. जटति, &c., to clot, to form<BR>into a concrete mass, to become twisted together or<BR>entangled and matted as hair; [cf. झट्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट
जट जट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. जन् ?), wearing<BR>twisted or entangled locks of hair; (आ), f. the hair<BR>matted and twisted together as worn by the god<BR>Śiva and by ascetics and persons in mourning; the<BR>long tresses of hair twisted or braided together, and<BR>coiled in a knot over the head so as to project like<BR>a horn from the forehead, or at other times allowed<BR>to fall carelessly over the back and shoulders; a<BR>fibrous root, a root in general; N. of several plants,<BR>= जटा-मांसी; Mucuna Pruritus, Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta; Asparagus Racemosus; also = रुद्र-जटा<BR>[cf. कृष्ण-जटा]; N. of a Pāṭha or arrangement<BR>of the Vedic text so called from a peculiar repetition<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">Page0336-b+ 79</a>]<BR>and inversion of the words, (it is a still more artificial<BR>arrangement than the Krama-pāṭha, each pair of words<BR>being repeated three times and one repetition being<BR>in inverted order.)<BR>—जटा-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, matting<BR>the hair.<BR>—जटा-चीर or जटाटीर, अस्, m. a N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—जटा-जूट, अस्, m. the long tresses of hair<BR>twisted on the top of the head; a quantity of twisted<BR>hair; Śiva's hair.<BR>—जटा-ज्वाल, अस्, m. ‘having a<BR>flame like a tuft,’ a lamp.<BR>—जटा-टङ्क, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; [cf. कटङ्कट.]<BR>—जटा-धर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, wearing twisted or matted hair; (अस्), m.<BR>any mendicant or ascetic wearing the Jaṭā; an epithet<BR>of Śiva; N. of one of the attendants of Skanda; N.<BR>of a Buddha; N. of a lexicographer; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people in the south of India.<BR>—जटा-धारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, wearing matted or braided hair.<BR>—जटा-<BR>पाठ, अस्, m. the Jaṭā reading or arrangement of<BR>the Vedic text, see above.<BR>—जटा-बन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>the knot or coil of matted hair.<BR>—जटा-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. braided or twisted hair forming a coil on<BR>the top of the head.<BR>—जटा-मांसी, f. the plant<BR>Nardostachys Jaṭāmāṃsi.<BR>—जटा-मालिन्, ई, m., N. of<BR>a form of Śiva, ‘garlanded with matted hair.’<BR>—जटा-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, wearing the Jaṭā, wearing knotted or<BR>clotted hair; (ती), f. = जटा-मांसी.<BR>—जटा-वल्ली, f.,<BR>N. of two plants, = रुद्र-जटा and गन्ध-मांसी.<BR>—जटासुर (˚टा-अस्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Rakṣas<BR>killed by Bhīma-sena; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people<BR>living in the north-east of Madhya-deśa.<BR>—जटे-<BR>श्वर-तीर्थ (˚टा-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटायु|जटायुः
जटायु, उस्, and जटायुस्, उस्, m., N. of a fabulous<BR>bird, the king of the vultures (गृध्र-राज), son<BR>of Aruṇa and Śyenī (or according to the Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>son of Garuḍa), and younger brother of Sampāti.<BR>(It is related in Chap. XX of the Araṇya-kāṇḍa of<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa, that whilst Rāma was on his way to<BR>Pañcavatī he met Jaṭāyus, who declared his intention<BR>of aiding Rāma, out of regard for his father Daśa-<BR>ratha. Accordingly when Rāvaṇa carried off Sītā,<BR>the semi-divine bird attempted to rescue her, but<BR>was defeated and mortally wounded by Rāvaṇa;<BR>Chap. LVI); bdellium, see गुग्गुलु; N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाल|जटालः
जटाल, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a coil of twisted or<BR>clotted hair; (अस्), m. bdellium; a kind of Curcuma<BR>(कर्चूर); the plant Bignonia Suaveolens; the Indian<BR>fig-tree or वट; (आ), f. = जटा-मांसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटालक
जटालक, अस्, इका, अम्, wearing knotted or matted<BR>hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटि|जटिः
जटि, इस्, f. clotted or twisted hair, an assemblage,<BR>multitude; the waved-leaf fig-tree, Ficus Venosa (=<BR>प्लक्ष); [cf. जटी and धुर्जटि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिक
जटिक, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing twisted or braided hair<BR>(= जटिन् ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिन्
जटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing the Jaṭā, having twisted<BR>hair; (ई), m. an epithet of Śiva; N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Skanda; an elephant sixty years old;<BR>waved-leaf fig-tree (= प्लक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिल|जटिलः
जटिल, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing the Jaṭā, having clotted<BR>or entangled hair; complicated, twisted together,<BR>intermixed, confused; (अस्), m. a lion; a goat with<BR>certain marks; N. of a man; (आ), f., N. of a woman<BR>with the patronymic Gautamī said to have had seven<BR>husbands, mother-in-law of Rādhikā; N. of several<BR>plants, = जटा-मांसी; long pepper; also = उच्चटा;<BR>= वचा, Acorus Calamus; = दमनक.<BR>—जटिल-<BR>स्थल, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिलक
जटिलक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>descendants of this man; (इका), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिलीकृ
जटिली-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to twist together, form into a clotted mass, to<BR>braid; to complicate, interweave, wrap round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिलीभाव|जटिलीभावः
जटिली-भाव, अस्, m. the being twisted together,<BR>complication, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटी
जटी, f. the waved-leaf fig-tree [cf. जटि]; also =<BR>जटा-मांसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाटीर|जटाटीरः
जटाटीर जटाटीर. See जटा-चीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटुल|जटुलः
जटुल जटुल, अस्, m. a freckle, a mark;<BR>[cf. जडुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठर|जठरं|जठरः
जठर जठर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>जन्), hard, firm; old; bound, tied (?); yellowish (?);<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people in the south-east of<BR>Madhya-deśa; (अस्), m., N. of a mountain; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. the stomach, belly, abdomen, viscera,<BR>bowels; the womb; a hole, cavity; the interior of<BR>anything; the bosom; certain morbid affections of<BR>the bowels; Ved. course (?); [cf. Goth. qvithrs,<BR>Them. qvithra; Lat. venter ?].<BR>—जठर-गद,<BR>अस्, m. a morbid affection of the abdomen or bowels,<BR>dropsy (?).<BR>—जठर-ज्वाला, f. belly-ache, colic, en-<BR>teritis.<BR>—जठर-नुद्, त्, m. the plant Cathartocar-<BR>pus Fistula; [cf. आरग्बध.]<BR>—जठर-यन्त्रणा<BR>or जठर-यातना, f. pain endured by the child in<BR>the womb before birth.<BR>—जठर-रोग, अस्, m. =<BR>जठर-गद above.<BR>—जठर-व्यथा, f. stomach-<BR>ache, colic.<BR>—जठर-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, or जठर-<BR>स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or जठर-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being in the belly, being in the womb.<BR>—जठराग्नि<BR>(˚र-अग्˚), इस्, m. the digestive fire of the stomach, the<BR>gastric juice [cf. अग्नि and जाठर]; a N. of Agastya<BR>in a former birth; [cf. दह्राग्नि.]<BR>—जठरामय<BR>(˚र-आम्˚), अस्, m. dropsy, water in the abdomen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरिन्
जठरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a large belly; abdo-<BR>minal, = उदरिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरीकृत
जठरी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, contained in the belly;<BR>concealed in the bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठल|जठलं
जठल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), Ved. = जठर; (Sāy.)<BR>the cavity or receptacle of waters, the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जड|जडं|जडः
जड जड, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps corrupted fr.<BR>rt. जल्, cf. जल), cold, frigid, chilly; stiff; stunned, para-<BR>lyzed, motionless, apathetic, senseless, stupid, idiotic,<BR>irrational, dumb; stunning, stupefying; (अस्), m. ‘the<BR>stupid one,’ an epithet of Su-mati who, though intelli-<BR>gent, simulated stupidity; cold, frost, winter; idiocy,<BR>fatuity, stupidity; dulness, apathy, sluggishness of<BR>mind or body; (आ), f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus;<BR>also the plant Flacourtia Cataphracta [cf. जटा];<BR>(अम्), n. water [cf. जल]; lead; [cf. Hib. fiod,<BR>fuar.]<BR>—जड-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, working slowly or<BR>stupidly, dilatory.<BR>—जड-ता, f. or जड-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>coldness, chilliness, frigidness, apathy, stupidity, stupe-<BR>faction, despair.<BR>—जड-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, stupid, idiotic.<BR>—जड-भरत, अस्, m. ‘the stupid Bharata,’ N. of<BR>a man simulating stupidity; an idiot in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडिमन्
जडिमन्, आ, m. frigidity, stupefaction, insensibility,<BR>stupidity, dulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीकृ
जडी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to stun,<BR>stupify, benumb, congeal.<BR>—जडी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>stunned, rendered cold or torpid or insensible, stupe-<BR>fied, confounded, paralyzed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीभू
जडी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -वितुम्, to become<BR>insensible or stupid or frozen or rigid.<BR>—जडी-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. frigidity, coldness, apathy, stupidity.<BR>—जडी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become torpid, stunned, stupefied,<BR>paralyzed, infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडुल|जडुलः
जडुल जडुल, अस्, m. a freckle, a mark;<BR>[cf. जटुल and जतु-मणि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतु|जतुः
जतु जतु, उ, n. (said to be fr. rt. जन्), lac,<BR>a red dye or pigment formed by an insect analogous<BR>to cochineal, a kind of gum; (ऊ, ऊस्), f. a bat.<BR>—जतु-कारी, f. or जतु-कृत्, त्, f. a kind of fragrant<BR>tree, = जतुका, (‘making lac,’ the lac insect forming<BR>its nest in this tree.)<BR>—जतु-कृष्णा, f. = पर्पटी.<BR>—जतु-गृह, अम्, n. a house plastered with lac,<BR>resin, and other combustible substances, (such a house<BR>was built for the reception of the Pāṇḍava princes in<BR>Vāraṇāvata by Purocana, at the instigation of Dur-<BR>yodhana, the object being to burn them alive when<BR>they were asleep after a festival. Warned, however,<BR>by Vidura, they discovered the dangerous character of<BR>their abode, and dug an underground passage by<BR>which to escape from the interior. Next having<BR>invited an outcaste woman with her five sons to a<BR>feast, they first stupefied them with wine, and then<BR>having burnt Purocana in his own house, set fire to<BR>the house of lac and, leaving the charred bodies of<BR>the woman and her sons inside, escaped by the under-<BR>ground passage; see Mahā-bh. I. 5864.)<BR>—जतु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">Page0337-a+ 79</a>]<BR>गेह, अम्, n. = जतु-गृह.<BR>—जतु-पुत्रक, अस्,<BR>m. a man at chess or backgammon &c. (coloured<BR>with lac).<BR>—जतु-मणि, इस्, m. a mole, a natural<BR>mark on the body.<BR>—जतु-मुख, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of rice.<BR>—जतु-रस, अस्, m. lac, the dye.<BR>—जतु-<BR>वेश्मदाह, अस्, m. the conflagration of the house<BR>of lac.<BR>—जतु-वेश्मन्, अ, n. = जतु-गृह, q. v.<BR>—जतू-कर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a man; (a various<BR>reading for जातूकर्ण.)<BR>—जत्व्-अश्मक, अम्, n. red<BR>arsenic; [cf. शिला-जतु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुक|जतुकं
जतुक, अम्, n. lac, see जतु; Asa Fœtida [cf.<BR>जातुक]; (आ), f. lac; a kind of fragrant plant or tree,<BR>= जतु-कृत्, जतूका, जनी, &c.; also = पर्पटी; a<BR>bat; [cf. जतुनी, जतूका, अश्म-जतुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुनी
जतुनी, f. a bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतूका
जतूका, f. a kind of fragrant plant; a bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जत्रु
जत्रु जत्रु, उस्, उ, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>जन्; in the earlier language m. and pl. only), the<BR>continuations of the vertebræ; (in later Sanskrit) the<BR>collar-bone, clavicle; ऊर्ध्व-जत्रु, the part of the<BR>body above the collar-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जत्रुक|जत्रुकं
जत्रुक, अम्, n. the collar-bone, the clavicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्
जन् जन्, cl. 1. 3. P. जनति, जजन्ति, जजान,<BR>जनिष्यति, जनितुम्, to generate, beget,<BR>(in these senses Ved.); cl. 4. A. जायते, जज्ञे, जनिष्-<BR>यते, अजनिष्ट and अजनि, जनितुम् (Ved. जनितोस्),<BR>to be born or produced, to come into existence; to<BR>grow (as plants &c.); to be born again; to be, be-<BR>come, take place, happen; to be possible, applicable,<BR>suitable, &c.; to be born for or destined for anything<BR>(with acc., e. g. तं लोकं जायते, he is born for that<BR>world, Ved.): Caus. जनयति, -ते, अजीजनत्, जन-<BR>यितुम् (Ved. जनयितवै), to generate, beget,<BR>bring forth, produce, create, cause, occasion; to<BR>cause to be born; to assign, procure: Desid. जिजनि-<BR>षति: Intens. जञ्जन्यते and जाजायते, जञ्जन्ति,<BR>जाजाति; [cf. Gr. γίγνομαι; Lat. gigno, genui,<BR>(g)nascor; Hib. genim, ‘I beget, generate;’ Lith.<BR>gemù; Goth. kin in keina, kain; Germ. Kind, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन|जनः
जन, अस्, m. a created being, a creature, a living<BR>being, man; a person or individual in general, (used<BR>collectively in sing. as well as in pl., e. g. दैव्यो<BR>जनः or दिव्यो जनः, the gods collectively; often<BR>at the end of a compound, e. g. प्रेष्य-जन, a<BR>servant; स्वजन-जन, a relation; दास-जन, a<BR>slave; सखी-जन, a female friend); people, race,<BR>tribe, subjects, nation (e. g. पञ्च जनाः, the five races<BR>of men or nations; cf. चर्षणि and कृष्टि); the<BR>person nearest to the speaker (hence अयं जनः =<BR>this person, these persons, often = I, I myself, we our-<BR>selves; cf. hic homo); a common person, one of the<BR>people; the world beyond the Mahar-loka, the heaven<BR>of deified mortals or the people living in it [cf. जन-<BR>लोक]; N. of a man with the patronymic Śārkarā-<BR>kṣya; (आ), f. birth, production; [cf. अन्तःपुर-<BR>जन, इतर-जन, कुल-जन, गुरु-जन, तिरो-<BR>जन, &c.; cf. also Hib. duine, man either male or<BR>female; Goth. qvinô; Slav. schena.]<BR>—जनं-<BR>सह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. subduing all creatures, epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>—जन-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, containing cere-<BR>monial ordinances for mankind, (जनकल्पा ऋचः,<BR>applied to several verses of the Atharva-veda);<BR>similar to mankind.<BR>—जनङ्-गम, अस्, m. a<BR>Cāṇḍāla, a man of a low or degraded tribe; [cf.<BR>जलङ्-गम.]<BR>—जन-चक्षुस्, उस्, n. the eye of all<BR>creatures, the sun; [cf. जगच्-चक्षुस्.]<BR>—जन-ता,<BR>f. a number of men, an assemblage of people, a<BR>community; people, subjects; mankind, manhood;<BR>birth, generation.<BR>—जन-त्रय, अम्, n. three per-<BR>sons.<BR>—जन-त्रा, f. (for जल-त्रा ?), an umbrella, a<BR>parasol.<BR>—जन-देव, अस्, m. a king.<BR>—जनन्-<BR>तप, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—जन-पद, अस्,<BR>m. a community, nation, people (sing. or pl.);<BR>the people (as opposed to the sovereign); an empire,<BR>an inhabited country; man, mankind; [cf. जान-<BR>पद.]<BR>—जनपदाधिप (˚द-अध्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>ruler of a people or empire, a prince, a king.<BR>—ज-<BR>नपदायुत (˚द-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, crowded with<BR>people, populous.<BR>—जनपदिन्, ई, m. the ruler of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-b" target="_blank">Page0337-b+ 81</a>]<BR>an empire, a prince, king.<BR>—जनपदेश्वर (˚द-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord of a country.<BR>—जन-प्रवाद,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the talk of men,’ rumour, report.<BR>—जन-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of mankind; philanthropic;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; coriander-seed; the<BR>tree Morunga Hyperanthera, = शोभाञ्जन.<BR>—जन-<BR>भक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. devouring men; (Sāy.)<BR>loving men or to be loved by men.<BR>—जन-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. supporting men.<BR>—जन-मरक, अस्, m.<BR>‘men-killer,’ an epidemic disease.<BR>—जन-मर्यादा,<BR>f. popular observance, established usage.<BR>—जनम्-<BR>एजय, अस्, m. ‘causing men to tremble,’ N. of a<BR>celebrated king to whom Vaiśampāyana recited the<BR>Mahā-bhārata, (he was great-grandson to Arjuna, as<BR>being son and successor to Parikṣit, who was son of<BR>Abhi-manyu, who was son of Arjuna); N. of a son of<BR>Kuru; of a son of Puru; of Purañ-jaya; of Soma-<BR>datta; of Su-mati; N. of a Nāga.<BR>—जन-मोहिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, infatuating men.<BR>—जन-योपन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. impeding or perplexing men, causing them to<BR>suffer; (Sāy.) gladdening men.<BR>—जन-रञ्जन,<BR>अम्, n. gratifying the people, courting popular favour.<BR>—जन-रव, अस्, m. rumour, report; calumny,<BR>scandal.<BR>—जन-राज्, ट्, or जन-राजन्, आ, m., Ved.<BR>king of men, ruler of men.<BR>—जन-लोक, अस्, m. one of<BR>the seven Lokas or divisions of the universe, the fifth<BR>or next above Mahar-loka, where the sons of Brahmā<BR>and other pious men reside; [cf. जनस्.]<BR>—जन-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable to men; a favourite<BR>with men, fond of men; (अस्), m., N. of a plant, =<BR>श्वेत-रोहित.<BR>—जन-वाद, अस्, m. ‘the talk of<BR>men,’ news, rumour, report, scandal; [cf. जने-वाद<BR>and जनो-वाद.]<BR>—जन-वादिन्, ई, m., Ved. a talker,<BR>newsmonger, gossip, tattler.<BR>—जन-विद्, त्, त्, त्, pos-<BR>sessing men.<BR>—जन-व्यवहार, अस्, m. popular<BR>practice or usage.<BR>—जन-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. coming<BR>or going to men; epithet of Pūṣan.<BR>—जन-श्रुत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, known among men; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man; (आ), f., N. of a woman.<BR>—जन-श्रुति, इस्,<BR>f. rumour, news, tidings, intelligence.<BR>—जन-सं-<BR>सद्, त्, f. an assembly of men.<BR>—जन-सङ्क्षय,<BR>अस्, m. destruction of men.<BR>—जन-सम्बाध, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, densely crowded with people (a place).<BR>—जन-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, living or abiding among men.<BR>—जन-स्थान, अम्, n. ‘the resort of demons,’ N.<BR>of a part of the Daṇḍaka forest in the Dakhin.<BR>—जनस्थान-रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, growing in Jana-<BR>sthāna.<BR>—जनाकीर्ण (˚न-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, crowded<BR>with people.<BR>—जनाचार (˚न-आच्˚), अस्, m. popular<BR>usage or custom, propriety, decorum, good conduct.<BR>—जनातिग (˚न-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, superhuman,<BR>superior.<BR>—जनाधिनाथ (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. su-<BR>preme lord of men, a king; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—जनाधिप (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. a ruler of men,<BR>a prince, a king.<BR>—जनान्त (˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>place removed from men, an uninhabited place; a<BR>region; personal proximity; an epithet of Yama,<BR>the destroyer of men.<BR>—जनान्तिक (˚न-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. secret communication, whispering, speaking aside<BR>to another; (अम्), ind. (as a stage-direction) speak-<BR>ing aside, aside.<BR>—जनायन (˚न-अय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. leading to men.<BR>—जनार्णव (˚न-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘ocean of men,’ a large concourse of people, a<BR>caravan.<BR>—जनार्थ-शब्द (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m. a family<BR>appellation, a gentile noun.<BR>—जनार्दन (˚न-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (exciting<BR>or agitating men); N. of several men.<BR>—जनार्-<BR>दन-विबुध, अस्, m., N. of the author of a com-<BR>mentary called Bhāvārtha-dīpikā.<BR>—जनाव् (˚न-अव्),<BR>औस्, m., Ved. a preserver or protector of mankind.<BR>—जनाशन (˚न-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘man-eater,’ a wolf.<BR>—जनाश्रय (˚न-आश्˚), अस्, m. an asylum or shelter<BR>for men, an inn, caravansary.<BR>—जना-षह् (in some<BR>forms जना-सह्), षाट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. subduing men.<BR>—जनेन्द्र (˚न-इन्˚), अस्, m. the prince or lord of<BR>men, a king.<BR>—जने-वाद, अस्, m. rumour, report;<BR>[cf. जन-वाद.]<BR>—जनेश or जनेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. lord of men, a king.<BR>—जनेष्ट (˚न-इष्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, desired or praised by mankind; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of jasmine (मुद्गर); (आ), f., N. of a fra-<BR>grant plant, = जतुका; N. of a medicinal plant, =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">Page0337-c+ 81</a>]<BR>वृद्धि; turmeric, = हरिद्रा; the flower of Jas-<BR>minum Grandiflorum, = जाती-पुष्प.<BR>—जनोदाह-<BR>रण (˚न-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘laudation of men,’ glory,<BR>fame.<BR>—जनौ, cf. जनाव्.<BR>—जनौघ (˚न-ओघ),<BR>अम्, n. a multitude of people, a crowd, a mob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनक|जनकः
जनक, अस्, इका, अम्, generative, generating, be-<BR>getting, producing, causing; (अस्), m. a father, a<BR>progenitor; N. of two kings of Videha or Mithilā,<BR>one a son of Mithi and father of Udāvasu, the other<BR>a son of Hrasva-roman and father of Rāma's wife Sītā,<BR>who is therefore called जनक-तनया, जनक-<BR>नन्दिनी, जनक-सुता, and जनकात्मजा; N. of a<BR>disciple of Bhagavat and of several others; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of Janaka; (इका), f. a daughter-<BR>in-law [cf. जनि and जनी]; a mother.<BR>—जनक-<BR>काण, अस्, m. ‘the one-eyed Janaka,’ N. of a man.<BR>—जनक-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of several persons.<BR>—जनक-ता, f. or जनक-त्व, अम्, n. generative-<BR>ness, productiveness, paternity.<BR>—जनक-भद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—जनक-राज, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—जनक-सप्तरात्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Saptāha.<BR>—जनक-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—जनकात्मजा (˚क-आत्˚), f., see above.<BR>—जन-<BR>केश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनत्
जनत्, ind. a sacred exclamation used in religious<BR>ceremonies (like ॐ &c.) without any definite<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनन|जननं|जननः
जनन, अस्, ई, अम्, generating, begetting, pro-<BR>ducing, causing; (अस्), m. a parent, progenitor, a<BR>creator; (ई), f. a mother; a queen-mother; a bat;<BR>lac; N. of several plants, = जनी, यूथिका, कटुका,<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा; tenderness, compassion; (अम्), n.<BR>birth, production, causation, coming into existence,<BR>life (e. g. पूर्वे जनने, in a former birth, i. e. in a<BR>former life); race, lineage, family; [cf. इन्द्र-ज-<BR>नन and मेधा-जनन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननि|जननिः
जननि, इस्, f. = जननी, a mother; birth; N. of<BR>a plant, = जनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननीय
जननीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be produced, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयत्
जनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, begetting, generating,<BR>engendering, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयति|जनयतिः
जनयति, इस्, f., Ved. generation, engendering,<BR>production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयन्त|जनयंत
जनयन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, generating, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितव्य
जनयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be engendered,<BR>generated, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितृ
जनयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, generating, begetting,<BR>producing, who or what produces; (ता), m. a pro-<BR>genitor, a father; (त्री), f. a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयिष्णु|जनयिष्णुः
जनयिष्णु, उस्, m. a progenitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनर्
जनर्. See जनस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्
जनस्, अस्, n., Ved. race, class of beings; (Sāy.)<BR>generator, parent; (अस्) or जनर्, ind. (before soft<BR>letters generally जनर्), N. of one of the seven worlds<BR>or divisions of the universe; see जन and जन-लोक.<BR>—जनो-लोक, अस्, m. the world described above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनि|जनिः
जनि, इस्, or जनी, f. a woman, wife, mother; any<BR>female animal, (in the Veda perhaps metaphorically =<BR>the fingers, e. g. जनिभिः समिद्ध, kindled by the<BR>fingers); the wife of a son or brother's son; birth,<BR>production; birthplace; a kind of fragrant plant; [cf.<BR>Hib. gean, ‘a woman;’ Goth. qvêns, qveins; Eng.<BR>queen.]<BR>—जनि-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wishing for a<BR>wife.<BR>—१. जनि-त्व or जनि-त्वन, अम्, n. the state<BR>of a wife, wedlock, conjugal state.<BR>—जनि-दा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. giving a wife.<BR>—जनि-नीलिका, f., N. of a<BR>plant, = महा-नीली.<BR>—जनि-मत् or जनि-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. having a wife, relating to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिक
जनिक, अस्, आ, अम्, producing, generating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित|जनितं
जनित, अस्, आ, अम्, engendered, begotten; pro-<BR>duced, occasioned; occurring.<BR>—जनित-स्वन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, making a noise, sounding.<BR>—जनितोद्यम<BR>(˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, making exertion, energetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितव्य
जनितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितृ
जनितृ, ता, m. a father, progenitor; (त्री), f. a<BR>mother; [cf. Lat. genitor; Gr. γενέτωρ, γενετήρ;<BR>Hib. genteoir, ‘a begetter, sower, planter;’ Lat.<BR>genitrix; Gr. γενέτειρα.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्र|जनित्रं
जनित्र, अम्, n., Ved. a birthplace, place of ori-<BR>gin, home; origin, generative or procreative matter;<BR>N. of a Sāman; (आणि), n. pl. parents, relatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्व|जनित्वः
2. जनित्व, अस्, आ, अम्, = जनितव्य, to be born or<BR>produced; (अस्), m. father; (आ), f. mother; (औ),<BR>m. du. father and mother, parents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिमन्
जनिमन्, अ, n. (said to be also m.), Ved. birth,<BR>generation, engenderment, production; offspring, de-<BR>scendants; a creature, being; gender, sex, genus, kind,<BR>race; [cf. Hib. geineamhuin, ‘birth, conception.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिष्ठ
जनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. a superl. fr. जनितृ (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिष्य
जनिष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनीन
जनीन, अस्, आ, अम्, suitable for men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनीय
जनीय, nom. P., Ved. जनीयति or जनियति, to<BR>wish for a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनु|जनुः
जनु, उस्, and जनू, ऊस्, f. birth; [cf. जनुस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनुस्
जनुस्, उस्, n. (Ved. Nom. m. जनूस्, Acc. जनु-<BR>षम्, Inst. जनुषा), birth, production, descent;<BR>nativity; birthplace; a creature, being; creation;<BR>genus, class, kind; जनुषा, ind., Ved. by birth,<BR>from birth (e. g. जनुषान्ध, blind from birth),<BR>by nature, naturally, originally, essentially, necessa-<BR>rily, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तु|जंतु|जंतुः|जन्तुः
जन्तु, उस्, m. a creature, a living being, man,<BR>person; people, mankind; any animal, (usually beings<BR>of the lowest organization, such as worms, insects,<BR>&c.); N. of a son of Somaka; [cf. क्षिति-जन्तु,<BR>क्षुद्र-ज्˚, जल-ज्˚.]<BR>—जन्तु-कम्बु, उ, n. any<BR>animal living in a shell, as a snail; a snail's shell.<BR>—जन्तु-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, killing worms; N. of<BR>several vermifuge plants; (अस्), m. the citron; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a plant, = विडङ्ग; (अम्), n. = विडङ्ग;<BR>Asa Fœtida.<BR>—जन्तु-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying<BR>worms; (अम्), n. Asa Fœtida.<BR>—जन्तु-पादप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a tree, = कोशाम्र.<BR>—जन्तु-फल,<BR>अस्, m. the glomerous fig-tree, Ficus Glomerata; [cf.<BR>उदुम्बर.]<BR>—जन्तु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing<BR>worms or insects.<BR>—जन्तु-मारिन्, ई, m. or (ई), f.<BR>‘destroying worms,’ the citron.<BR>—जन्तु-हन्त्री, f.,<BR>N. of a vermifuge, = विडङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुक
जन्तुक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. his<BR>descendants; (आ), f. lac, gum; a kind of Asa Fœtida;<BR>[cf. जतुका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुला
जन्तुला, f. the plant Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्त्व
जन्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्म|जन्मं
जन्म, अम्, n. = जन्मन्, birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मन्
जन्मन्, अ, n. birth, production, origin, (in comp.)<BR>born from (e. g. शूद्र-जन्मन्, born from a Śūdra);<BR>existence, life (e. g. दृष्टादृष्ट-जन्मन्, pre-<BR>sent and future life); nativity; birthplace, home; a<BR>progenitor, father; natal star; (in astrology) N. of the<BR>first mansion or Nakṣatra; a creature, being; people;<BR>the people of a household, kind, race (e. g. उभे<BR>जन्मनी or उभयं जन्म, both races or both<BR>kinds of living beings, i. e. gods and men or men<BR>and animals); nature, quality, custom, manner (e. g.<BR>प्रत्नेन जन्मना, according to ancient custom);<BR>= उदक, water (?); [cf. जनिमन्, अग्र-जन्मन्,<BR>अन्त्य-ज्˚, कश्मीर-ज्˚, काश्मीर-ज्˚, द्वि-ज्˚, &c.; cf. also<BR>Lat. ger-men; Hib. geanamhuin, ‘engendering.’]<BR>—जन्म-काल, अस्, m. time or hour of birth.<BR>—जन्म-कील, अस्, m. ‘pillar or stay of birth,’ an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—जन्म-कृत्, त्, m. a progenitor,<BR>a father.<BR>—जन्म-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. birthplace.<BR>—जन्म-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m. title of a work on<BR>nativities.<BR>—जन्म-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, the eldest<BR>by birth, the first-born.<BR>—जन्म-तिथि, इस्, m. the<BR>lunar day on which a birth occurs, birthday.<BR>—जन्-<BR>म-द, अस्, m. ‘a birth-giver,’ a father, progenitor.<BR>—जन्म-दिन, अम्, n. or जन्म-दिवस, अस्, m.<BR>a birthday.<BR>—जन्म-नक्षत्र, अम्, n. the natal<BR>star, the constellation under which a person is born;<BR>[cf. जन्म-राशि and जन्मर्क्ष.]<BR>—जन्म-ना-<BR>मन्, अ, n. the name received at birth (i. e. on the<BR>twelfth day after).<BR>—जन्म-प, अस्, m. the regent<BR>of a planet under which a person is born.<BR>—जन्म-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. or जन्म-पत्त्रिका, f. a horoscope,<BR>the paper or scroll on which are recorded the year,<BR>lunar day, configuration, and relative position of the<BR>planets &c., of the birth of a particular individual, a<BR>table of his fortunes throughout life.<BR>—जन्म-पा-<BR>दप, अस्, m. the tree under which a person is born,<BR>a family-tree.<BR>—जन्म-प्रतिष्ठा, f. birthplace; a<BR>mother.<BR>—जन्म-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a work<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">Page0338-b+ 78</a>]<BR>by Vi-budha.<BR>—जन्म-प्रभृति, ind. ever since<BR>birth.<BR>—जन्म-भाज्, क्, m. a creature, a living being<BR>(possessing birth).<BR>—जन्म-भाषा, f. mother-tongue.<BR>—जन्म-भूमि, इस्, f. birthplace, native country.<BR>—जन्म-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, possessing birth, enjoying<BR>life.<BR>—जन्म-योग, अस्, m. a horoscope.<BR>—जन्म-<BR>राशि, इस्, m. or जन्म-लग्न, अम्, n. the sign of the<BR>zodiac under which a person is born.<BR>—जन्म-रोगिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, sickly from birth.<BR>—जन्मर्क्ष (˚म-<BR>ऋक्˚), अम्, n. the constellation under which a person<BR>is born; N. of the first Nakṣatra.<BR>—जन्म-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessing birth, born, mortal, living.<BR>—जन्म-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. ‘the path of birth,’ the<BR>vulva.<BR>—जन्म-वसुधा, f. native country, home.<BR>—जन्म-वैलक्षण्य, अम्, n. acting in a manner<BR>contrary to or unbecoming one's birth.<BR>—जन्म-<BR>शय्या, f. the bed on which a person is born.<BR>—जन्-<BR>म-शोधन, अम्, n. discharging the obligations<BR>derived from birth.<BR>—जन्म-साफल्य, अम्, n. at-<BR>tainment of the object or end of existence.<BR>—जन्म-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. birthplace, native land, home; the<BR>womb.<BR>—जन्माधिप (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, m. lord of<BR>birth, an epithet of Śiva; the regent of a constellation<BR>under which a person is born; [cf. जन्म-प.]<BR>—जन्मान्तर (˚म-अन्˚), अम्, n. another birth,<BR>another life; the preceding life; the future life;<BR>regeneration; the other world.<BR>—जन्मान्तर-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, committed in another birth.<BR>—जन्मान्-<BR>तरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or done in another<BR>life.<BR>—जन्मान्ध (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blind<BR>from birth, born blind.<BR>—जन्माष्टमी (˚म-अष्˚),<BR>f. the birthday of Kṛṣṇa, the eighth day in the dark<BR>half of the month Śrāvaṇa or Bhādra, on which<BR>Kṛṣṇa was born.<BR>—जन्मास्पद (˚म-आस्˚), अम्,<BR>n. birthplace; [cf. भवास्पद.]<BR>—जन्मेश (˚म-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. the regent of a constellation under<BR>which any one is born; [cf. जन्म-प.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मिन्
जन्मिन्, ई, m. a creature, a living being, a man,<BR>an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मेजय|जन्मेजयः
जन्मेजय. See जनम्-एजय under जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be born or produced, pro-<BR>ducible; born, produced; (often at the end of a<BR>comp.) born from, arising or produced from, occa-<BR>sioned by; generating; (अस्), m. a father; (अम्), n.<BR>the body; a portent occurring at birth; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>belonging to a race or family; national; belonging<BR>to the same country; vulgar, common, belonging to<BR>or relating to men or to the people, fit for men;<BR>(अस्), m. the friend or attendant or companion<BR>of a bridegroom; a common man; (आ), f. the<BR>friend of a mother; the relation or companion of a<BR>bride, a bridesmaid; pleasure, happiness; affection;<BR>(अम्), n. people; a community, nation; fighting,<BR>war, combat; a market, a fair; rumour, report;<BR>censure, abuse.<BR>—जन्य-ता, f. the state of anything<BR>that is to be born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्यु|जन्युः
जन्यु, उस्, m. birth; a creature, an animal, a living<BR>and sentient being; fire; an epithet of Brahmā; N.<BR>of one of the seven sages of the fourth Manvantara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात|जातं|जातः
जात, अस्, आ, अम्, born &c. See p. 344.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायमान
जायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being born, coming into life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकरी
जनकरी जनकरी, f. or जनकारिन्, ई, m.<BR>a red substance called lac. See अलक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमेजय|जनमेजयः
जनमेजय जनम्-एजय. See जन, p. 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्तिक|जनांतिक
जनान्तिक जनान्तिक. See जन, p. 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तु|जंतु|जंतुः|जन्तुः
जन्तु जन्तु, जन्मन्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्
जप् जप्, cl. 1. P. जपति, जजाप, जपिष्-<BR>यति, अजपीत् and अजापीत्, जपितुम्, to utter<BR>in a low voice or under-tone, to mutter, whisper,<BR>repeat internally, talk to one's self; to mutter prayers<BR>or incantations, whisper magical spells or charms;<BR>to pray to any one in a low voice (e. g. शिवो जप्यते,<BR>Śiva is addressed with muttered prayers); to invoke<BR>or call upon in a low voice: Caus. जापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>अजीजपत्: Desid. जिजपिषति: Intens. जञ्जप्यते,<BR>जञ्जपीति; [cf. जल्प्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप, अस्, आ, अम्, muttering, whispering, uttering<BR>in a low voice [cf. कर्णे-जप]; (अस्), m. mutter-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">Page0338-c+ 78</a>]<BR>ing prayers, repeating in a murmuring tone passages<BR>from scripture, charms, names of a deity, &c.; counting<BR>silently the beads of a rosary, &c.; a muttered prayer<BR>or spell; [cf. जाप.]<BR>—जप-ता, f. the state of a<BR>mutterer or of one who mutters prayers.<BR>—जप-<BR>परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to repetition of prayers,<BR>engaged in muttering prayers.<BR>—जप-माला, f. a<BR>rosary used for counting muttered prayers.<BR>—जप-<BR>यज्ञ, अस्, m. muttering prayers as a religious rite or<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—जप-होम, अस्, m. a sacrifice which con-<BR>sists in muttering prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपत्
जपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, muttering prayers in a low tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपन|जपनं
जपन, अम्, n. the muttering or whispering of<BR>prayers or spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपनीय
जपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be uttered in a low<BR>voice, to be whispered, to be muttered or repeated<BR>inaudibly, to be meditated on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित
जपित, अस्, आ, अम्, muttered, whispered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित्वा
जपित्वा, ind. having muttered or repeated in a<BR>low tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपिन्
जपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, uttering prayers in a low voice,<BR>muttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्तव्य
जप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be muttered or whispered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्त्वा
जप्त्वा, ind. having muttered or repeated inaudibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्य|जप्यः
जप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be repeated in an under-<BR>tone, to be muttered or whispered; (अम्, अस्), n. m.<BR>a prayer to be uttered in a low voice, a muttered<BR>prayer; [cf. जाप्य, किञ्-जप्य, ध्यान-जप्य.]<BR>—जप्येश्वर-तीर्थ (˚य-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्यक
जप्यक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपा
जपा जपा, f. the China rose, either the<BR>flower or plant; [cf. जवा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपिल
जपिल जपिल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N.<BR>of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जबारु
जबारु जबारु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. जव?), Ved.<BR>hastening, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जबाल
जबाल जबाल, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ् 1. जभ् or जम्भ्, cl. 1. A. जभते<BR>or जम्भते, &c., to snap at, seize with<BR>the mouth: Caus. P. जम्भयति, -यितुम्, to crush,<BR>destroy: Intens. जञ्जभ्यते, जञ्जभीति, to open<BR>the jaws wide, snap at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जब्धृ
जब्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, snatching at, seizing<BR>with the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ|जंभ|जंभः|जम्भः
जम्भ, अस्, m. the jaws (generally used in plur.);<BR>the mouth, a tooth, an eye-tooth, tusk; one who<BR>crushes or devours, as a demon; N. of several demons;<BR>a leader of the demons in the war against the gods<BR>under Indra; N. of a son of Pra-hrāda; of a son of<BR>Hiraṇya-kaśipu; N. of the father-in-law of Hiraṇya-<BR>kaśipu; N. of the father of Sunda; the citron tree,<BR>= जम्भीर, जम्भल, जम्बीर; eating, food;<BR>biting asunder, opening by biting, explanation, inter-<BR>pretation; a quiver; a part, a portion; (आ), f. opening<BR>of the mouth; [cf. अन्तर्-जम्भ, कु-ज्˚, तपुर्-ज्˚,<BR>तिग्म-ज्˚, तृष्ट-ज्˚, &c.; cf. also Gr. γαμφηλαί.]<BR>—जम्भ-कुण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—जम्-<BR>भ-द्विष्, ट्, m. the enemy of Jambha, an epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>—जम्भ-भेदिन्, ई, m. the destroyer of<BR>Jambha, a N. of Indra.<BR>—जम्भ-सुत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. pressed with the jaws, chewed.<BR>—जम्भारि<BR>(˚भ-अरि), इस्, m. ‘the enemy of Jambha,’ Indra;<BR>Indra's thunderbolt; fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भक|जंभक|जम्भकः
जम्भक, अस्, आ, अम्, crushing, devouring; killing,<BR>destroying; biting asunder; explaining, interpreting;<BR>opening, expanding; yawning; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>demon or of a despised tribe of men; N. of several<BR>evil spirits supposed to reside in various magical<BR>weapons; N. of a verse addressed to them; N. of a<BR>demon conquered by Kṛṣṇa; N. of an attendant of<BR>Śiva; a lime or citron; (आ), f. opening the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भन्
जम्भन् = जम्भ in तृण-जम्भन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भन|जंभनं
1. जम्भन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. crushing, destroying;<BR>one who crushes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ्य
जम्भ्य, अस्, m., Ved. an incisor (tooth) or per-<BR>haps a grinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ् 2. जभ् or जम्भ्, cl. 1. P. जभति or<BR>जम्भति, a various reading for यभ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भन|जंभनं
2. जम्भन, अम्, n. sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्य
जभ्य जभ्य, अस्, m., Ved. a species of<BR>animal destructive to grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्
जम् 1. जम्, cl. 1. P. जमति, जजाम,<BR>जमितुम्, to eat, consume; to go (?);<BR>to blaze (?); [cf. Hib. diamanu, ‘food, sustenance;’<BR>gion, ‘the mouth:’ Old Germ. gouma, kouma, ‘food;’<BR>gaumo, ‘the palate:’ Mod. Germ. Gaumen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमत्
जमत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. blazing.<BR>—जमद्-<BR>अग्नि, इस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi often mentioned together<BR>with Viśvā-mitra as an adversary of Vasiṣṭha, and<BR>according to some a descendant of Bhṛgu; in epic<BR>poetry a son of Bhārgava Ṛcīka and father of<BR>Paraśu-rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमन|जमनं
जमन, अम्, n. eating; food, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्
जम् 2. जम्, Ved. (used in Inst. ज्मा and<BR>Abl. Gen. ज्मस्), the earth; ज्मा, on earth; [cf. गम्<BR>and क्षम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमज
जमज जम-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, = यम-ज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमदग्नि|जमदग्निः
जमदग्नि जमद्-अग्नि. See जमत् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्पती|जंपती
जम्पती जम्पती (fr. दम्पती ?, but accord-<BR>ing to some जम् is fr. जाया; cf. Hib. gamh; Gr.<BR>γάμος ?), m. du. wife and husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बाल|जंबाल|जंबालः|जम्बालः
जम्बाल जम्बाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. mud, clay;<BR>an aquatic plant, Vallisneria; (अस्), m. a fragrant<BR>plant, Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बालिनी|जंबालिनी
जम्बालिनी, f. a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बिर|जम्बिरः
जम्बिर जम्बिर, अस्, m. = जम्बीर, the citron<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बीर|जंबीर|जंबीरः|जम्बीरः
जम्बीर, अस्, m. the citron tree or common<BR>lime; a plant called by some a sort of basil with<BR>small leaves, a kind of Ocimum, = मरुवक or<BR>प्रस्थ-पुष्प; (अम्), n. a citron; [cf. जम्-<BR>भीर, जम्भ, जम्भल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बीरक
जम्बीरक, अस्, m. a kind of Ocimum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बु|जंबु|जम्बुः
जम्बु जम्बु, उस्, or जम्बू, ऊस्, f. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. 1. जम्), a fruit tree, the rose apple, Eugenia<BR>Jambolana, or another species of Eugenia; (ऊस्, उ),<BR>f. n. its fruit; (उस्, उ), m. n., N. of a Dvīpa [cf.<BR>जम्बु-द्वीप]; N. of a fabulous river, said to flow<BR>from the mountain Meru and to be formed by the<BR>juice of the fruits of an immense Jambu tree on that<BR>mountain; [cf. आढक-जम्बु, काक-ज्˚, गोरक्ष-<BR>ज्˚.]<BR>—जम्बु-द्वीप or जम्बू-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of<BR>one of the seven continents or rather large islands<BR>surrounding the mountain Meru; it is so named<BR>either from the Jambu trees abounding in it, or from<BR>an enormous Jambu tree on Mount Meru visible like<BR>a standard to the whole continent, and implies<BR>(according to the Purāṇas) the central division of the<BR>world, or the known world, including India; with<BR>Buddhists it is confined to India; with Jainas it is<BR>one of the five divisions of India.<BR>—जम्बु-ध्वज,<BR>अस्, m. another N. for Jambu-dvīpa (‘having the<BR>Jambu tree as its standard’); N. of a Nāga.<BR>—जम्बु-पर्वत, अस्, m. another N. for Jambu-<BR>dvīpa.<BR>—जम्बु-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR>—जम्बु-मत्, आन्, m. a mountain; a monkey;<BR>(ती), f. an Apsaras or heavenly nymph; [cf. जाम्ब-<BR>वत् and जम्बु-वत्.]<BR>—जम्बु-माल, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—जम्बु-मालिन्, ई, m., N. of a Rakṣas.<BR>—जम्बु-रुद्र, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-king.<BR>—जम्बु-वन-ज, अम्, n. the white flower of the<BR>China rose.<BR>—जम्बु-सर, अस्, m., N. of a town in<BR>Gurjara (Jumbooseer between Cambay and Baroch).<BR>—जम्बू-खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. another N. for<BR>Jambu-dvīpa.<BR>—जम्बूखण्ड-विनिर्माण-पर्वन्,<BR>अ, n. the first six Adhyāyas of the sixth book of<BR>the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—जम्बूनद-प्रभ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a future Buddha.<BR>—जम्बू-नदी, f., N. of one<BR>of the seven arms of the heavenly Gaṅgā.<BR>—जम्बू-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, अम्, m. n., N. of a Tīrtha (the way<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">Page0339-b+ 76</a>]<BR>leading to the sacred Jambu on Meru).<BR>—जम्बू-<BR>स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of the last Arhat of the Jainas.<BR>—जम्ब्व्-ओष्ठ = जाम्बवौष्ठ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुक|जंबुक|जंबुकः|जम्बुकः
जम्बुक जम्बुक, अस्, m. a jackal; a low<BR>man; N. of one of the attendants of Skanda; an<BR>epithet of Varuṇa; the plant Eugenia (commonly<BR>called गोलाप जाम); or perhaps a kind of Śyoṇāka;<BR>(आ), f. a female jackal; [cf. जम्बूक.]<BR>—जम्बु-<BR>केश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूक|जंबूक|जंबूकः|जम्बूकः
जम्बूक, अस्, m. a jackal; a low man; N. of one<BR>of the attendants of Skanda; an epithet of Varuṇa;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of grape without stones, = काकली-<BR>द्राक्षा; [cf. जम्बुक and गृध्र-जम्बूक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुल|जंबुलः|जम्बुलः
जम्बुल जम्बुल, अस्, m. a kind of disease of<BR>the outer ear; the plant Eugenia Jambolana [cf.<BR>जम्बु]; another plant, Pandanus Odoratissimus;<BR>[cf. केतक; cf. also जम्बूल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूल|जंबूल|जम्बूलः
जम्बूल, अस्, m. the plant Pandanus Odoratissi-<BR>mus; the plant Eugenia Jambolana [cf. जम्बू];<BR>(अम्), n. jests addressed to the bridegroom by his<BR>female relatives and friends; [cf. the following.]<BR>—जम्बूल-मालिका, f. a garland of Jambūla flowers;<BR>brightness of countenance in a bride and bridegroom;<BR>jesting compliments addressed to the bride and bride-<BR>groom by the female relatives of the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ|जंभ|जंभः|जम्भः
जम्भ जम्भ. See under 1. जभ्, p. 338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भन|जंभनं
जम्भन जम्भन. See under 1. and 2. जभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भर|जंभर|जंभरः|जम्भरः
जम्भर जम्भर, अस्, m. the lime or citron<BR>tree; [cf. the following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भल|जंभलः|जम्भलः
जम्भल, अस्, m. the lime or citron tree [cf.<BR>जम्बीर]; N. of a Jina or deified Jaina saint; N.<BR>of a man; (आ), f. a female Rākṣasī, by meditating<BR>on whom women become pregnant.<BR>—जम्भल-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of the supposed author of the<BR>Vetāla-pañca-viṃśati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भिन्|जंभिन्
जम्भिन्, ई, m. the lime or citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भीर|जंभीर|जंभीरः|जम्भीरः
जम्भीर, अस्, m. the lime or citron tree, appa-<BR>rently of more than one species; a plant considered<BR>to be a kind of basil with small leaves; [cf. जम्-<BR>बीर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भलिका
जम्भलिका जम्भलिका, f. a kind of song.<BR>(जम्भालिका appears to be incorrect.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्व|जम्वः
जम्व जम्व, अस्, m. mud, mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय|जयः
जय जय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. जि), conquering,<BR>winning, (used at the end of comp.; cf. कृतञ्-जय,<BR>धनञ्-ज्˚, पुरञ्-ज्˚, &c.); (अस्), m. conquest, vic-<BR>tory, triumph, winning, being victorious (in battle, in<BR>playing with dice or in a lawsuit; इन्द्रियाणां<BR>जयः, victory over or restraint of the senses; आत्म-<BR>जय, self-restraint; प्राण-जय, victory over life,<BR>i. e. resigning it willingly; रुग्-जय, healing of a<BR>disease); a verse or formula causing victory; the<BR>plant Premna Spinosa or Longifolia; a yellow variety<BR>of Phaseolus Mungo; N. of the third year of the<BR>sixth lustrum of the cycle of Jupiter; an epithet of<BR>the sun; a class of deities (pl.); N. of a son of<BR>Indra; of an attendant of Viṣṇu; N. of a Nāga;<BR>of a Dānava; of a Ṛṣi under the tenth Manu; of<BR>a son of Vatsara by Svar-vīthi; of a son of Viśvā-<BR>mitra; of a son of Purū-ravas and Urvaśī; N. of an<BR>ancient king; of the eleventh Cakra-vartin in Bhā-<BR>rata; of a hero on the side of the Pāṇḍus; a N.<BR>assumed by Yudhi-ṣṭhira at the court of king Virāṭa;<BR>N. of several other persons; (आ), f., N. of several<BR>plants, viz. = जयन्ती, Sesbania Ægyptiaca, Premna<BR>Spinosa or Longifolia, Terminalia Chebula; also =<BR>नील-दूर्वा, शान्ता, and वि-जया; the third, eighth,<BR>or thirteenth lunar days of either half-month; a N.<BR>of Durgā; N. of a daughter of Dakṣa; of a wife<BR>of Śiva; of a confidential female attendant of Durgā<BR>and wife of Puṣpa-danta; of a Buddhist deity; of<BR>the mother of the twelfth Arhat of the present Ava-<BR>sarpiṇī; of one of the seven kumārīs on the standard<BR>of Indra.<BR>—जय-करण, अम्, n. obtaining a victory,<BR>conquering.<BR>—जय-काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, desirous of<BR>victory.<BR>—जय-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, gaining a victory,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-c" target="_blank">Page0339-c+ 81</a>]<BR>victorious.<BR>—जय-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing or granting<BR>victory.<BR>—जय-कोलाहल, अस्, m. a shout of victory;<BR>a kind of dice; [cf. जय-पुत्रक.]<BR>—जय-क्षेत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—जय-गत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>conquering, victorious.<BR>—जय-गर्व, अस्, m. pride<BR>of conquest, exultation.<BR>—जय-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a poet.<BR>—जय-घोष, अस्, m. or जय-घोषण,<BR>अम् or आ, n. f. a shouting to proclaim victory, a cry<BR>of victory.<BR>—जय-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the work Gośṛṅga-svayambhū-caitya-bhaṭṭārakod-<BR>deśa; N. of a king of Gauḍa; of a king of Kānyakubja.<BR>—जय-चर्या, f. a work on omens by Nara-hari.<BR>—जय-ढक्का, f. a large kettle-drum beaten as<BR>a sign of victory.<BR>—जय-तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>scholiast.<BR>—जय-द, अस्, आ, अम्, granting victory;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a tutelary deity in the family of Vāma-<BR>deva.<BR>—जय-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of the son of Indra;<BR>of a Bodhi-sattva; of a certain king; of a minister<BR>of king Jayā-pīḍa; of a physician.<BR>—जय-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the Gīta-govinda; also of<BR>the Prasanna-rāghava-nāṭaka; also of the grammar<BR>entitled Īṣat-tantra.<BR>—जय-देवक, अस्, m. = जय-<BR>देव, N. of a Muhūrta.<BR>—जय-धर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a hero on the side of the Kurus.<BR>—जय-<BR>ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kārtavīrya Arjuna<BR>and father of Tāla-jaṅgha.<BR>—जय-ध्वनि, इस्, m. a<BR>shout or cry of victory.<BR>—जय-नारायण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the author of the poem Kāśī-khaṇḍa.<BR>—जय-<BR>नृसिंह, अस्, m., N. of a deity.<BR>—जय-पत्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>a written account of a victory, record of victory.<BR>—ज-<BR>य-पाल, अस्, m. ‘guardian of victory,’ an epithet of<BR>Brahmā, also of Viṣṇu; a king; N. of several<BR>kings; the plant Croton Jamalgota.<BR>—जय-पुत्र-<BR>क, अस्, m. a kind of dice; [cf. जय-कोलाहल and<BR>जतु-पुत्रक.]<BR>—जय-पुर, अम्, n. ‘town of<BR>victory,’ N. of a fortress in Kaśmīra; also of a small<BR>state in Marwur.<BR>—जय-प्रस्थान, अम्, n. march<BR>to victory.<BR>—जय-प्रिय, अस्, m., N. of a hero on<BR>the side of the Pāṇḍavas; (आ), f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs in attendance on Skanda.<BR>—जय-मङ्गल,<BR>अस्, m. a royal elephant; a remedy for fever, a<BR>febrifuge; N. of a commentator on the Bhaṭṭi-<BR>kāvya; (आ), f., N. of a commentary on the Bhaṭṭi-<BR>kāvya composed by Jaya-maṅgala; (अम्), n. a cheer<BR>of victory; [cf. जयाशिस्.]<BR>—जय-मति, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—जय-मती, f., N. of several<BR>women; [cf. जय-वत्.]<BR>—जय-माधव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—जय-यज्ञ, अस्, m. the Aśva-medha<BR>or sacrifice of a horse as a mark of dominion.<BR>—ज-<BR>य-राज, अस्, m., N. of several men.<BR>—जय-रात,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a warrior who took the side of the<BR>Kuru princes.<BR>—जय-राम, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Nyāya-siddhānta-mālā; N. of several<BR>other men.<BR>—जय-लक्ष्मी, ईस्, f. victory, the god-<BR>dess of victory; N. of a woman.<BR>—जय-लेख, अस्,<BR>m. record of victory; [cf. जय-पत्त्र.]<BR>—जय-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, victorious, triumphant; [cf. जय-<BR>मती and जया-वती.]<BR>—जय-वर्धन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—जय-वर्म-देव, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—जय-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, conferring victory,<BR>victorious.<BR>—जय-वाद्य, अम्, n. a drum or other<BR>instrument sounded to proclaim victory.<BR>—जय-<BR>वाराह-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—जय-<BR>वाहिनी, f., N. of the wife of Indra.<BR>—जय-शब्द,<BR>अस्, m. a shout or song of victory, or the exclamation<BR>Jaya, Jaya repeated like the Io of the Greeks as in<BR>जय-जय देव हरे, &c.<BR>—जय-शर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—जय-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, victorious,<BR>triumphant.<BR>—जय-शृङ्ग, अम्, n. a horn blown<BR>to announce a victory.<BR>—जय-श्री, ईस्, f. victory,<BR>glory; the goddess of victory.<BR>—जय-सिंह, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of several men; N. of a king of Kaśmīra; [cf.<BR>जया-सिंह.]<BR>—जय-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Magadha; also of a son of Adīna or Ahīna; of a son<BR>of Sārvabhauma; N. of the father of the Āvantyau;<BR>also of the son of Mahendra-varman; N. of a<BR>Buddhist; (आ), f., N. of a female door-keeper; [cf.<BR>जयत्-सेन.]<BR>—जय-स्कन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>minister of king Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—जय-स्तम्भ,<BR>अस्, m. a trophy; a column erected to commemorate<BR>a victory.<BR>—जय-स्वामिन्, ई, m. the lord of victory;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-a" target="_blank">Page0340-a+ 81</a>]<BR>an epithet of Śiva; N. of a scholiast on the<BR>Chandoga-sūtras and of the author of a commentary<BR>on the Āśvalāyana-Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—जयस्वामि-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town founded by Jushka.<BR>—जया-<BR>कर (˚य-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘a mine of victory,’ N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—जयादित्य (˚य-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king;<BR>N. of the author of the Kāśikā-vṛtti.<BR>—जया-देवी, f.,<BR>N. of a Buddhist deity [cf. जया]; N. of a woman.<BR>—जयानन्द (˚य-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—जयानन्द-वार, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—जया-<BR>नीक (˚य-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a warrior on the side<BR>of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—जयान्तराय (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>an impediment or hindrance to victory.<BR>—जयापीड<BR>(˚य-आप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king of Kaśmīra.<BR>—जया-भट्टारिका, f., N. of a place.<BR>—जयारव<BR>(˚य-आर्˚), अस्, m. song of victory; [cf. जय-शब्द.]<BR>—जयावघोष (˚य-अव्˚), अस्, m. proclamation of<BR>victory, cheering.<BR>—जया-वती, f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attending on Skanda; [cf. जय-मती and<BR>जय-वत्.]<BR>—जयावह (˚य-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>ferring victory, victorious; (आ), f. a kind of Croton;<BR>[cf. भद्र-दन्तिका.]<BR>—जयाशिस् (˚य-आश्˚), ईस्, f.<BR>a prayer for victory; congratulations after a victory;<BR>cheer of victory.<BR>—जयाश्रय (˚य-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘the asylum of victory,’ favoured by victory; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of grass; [cf. जरडी.]<BR>—जयाश्व (˚य-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a hero on the side of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—जया-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—जयाह्वा (˚य-<BR>आह्˚), f. = जयावहा, q. v.<BR>—जयेन्द्र (˚य-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king of Kaśmīra; also of another<BR>person; a vihāra built by the latter is called Ja-<BR>yendra-vihāra.<BR>—जयेश्वर (˚य-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a sanctuary built by Jayā-devī.<BR>—जयोद्धुर<BR>(˚य-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, exulting in victory.<BR>—जयोल्-<BR>लास-निधि (˚य-उल्˚), इस्, m. title of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयक
जयक, अस्, आ, अम्, victorious; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयत्|जयन्त्
जयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, conquering, defeating; ex-<BR>celling.<BR>—जयत्-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Magadha; of a son of Sārvabhauma; of Nadīna; a<BR>N. assumed by the fourth (?) son of Pāṇḍu; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; [cf.<BR>जय-सेन.]<BR>—जयद्-बल, अस्, m. a N. assumed<BR>by one of the youngest Pāṇḍu princes at the court of<BR>king Virāṭa.<BR>—जयद्-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>the Sindhus and Sauvīras fighting on the side of the<BR>Kuru princes; a son of Vṛhan-manas; a son of Vṛhat-<BR>karman; of Vṛhat-kāya; of the tenth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन|जयनं
जयन, अम्, n. conquering, subduing; armour<BR>for cavalry, elephants, &c.; (ई), f., N. of a daughter<BR>of Indra; [cf. जयन्ती.]<BR>—जयन-युज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>caparisoned (as a war horse), victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन्त|जयंत|जयंतः|जयन्तः
जयन्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of Indra; an epithet<BR>of Śiva; N. of a Rudra; N. of a son of Dharma by<BR>Marutvatī (he was a part of Vāsudeva and = उपेन्द्र);<BR>a class of deities (with Jainas) forming a subdivision of<BR>the Anuttaras; the moon; the assumed N. of Bhīma<BR>at the court of king Virāṭa; N. of a minister of<BR>Daśa-ratha; also of a Gandharva, the father of Vikra-<BR>māditya; of a king of Gauḍa; of a Brāhman of<BR>Kaśmīra; of an author of a grammatical work; N.<BR>of a mountain; (ई), f. a flag, a banner; the plant<BR>Sesbania Ægyptiaca, = जीवन्ती; blades of barley<BR>planted at the commencement of the Daśaharā and<BR>gathered at its close; a particular combination in<BR>astronomy, or the rising of the asterism Rohiṇī at<BR>midnight, on the eighth of the dark half of Srāvaṇa,<BR>or in fact on the birthday of Kṛṣṇa, which is then<BR>particularly sacred; an epithet of Durgā; of Dāk-<BR>ṣāyaṇī (the wife of Śiva) in Hastinā-pura; N. of the<BR>tutelary deity of Vasūdreka; N. of the daughter of<BR>Indra; N. of the wife of Ṛṣabha received by him<BR>from Indra; N. of a river; N. of a country.<BR>—ज-<BR>यन्त-पत्त्र, अम्, n. ‘leaf of victory or triumph;’<BR>(in law) the sealed and written award of the judge in<BR>favour of either party; (in historical tradition) the<BR>label on the forehead of a horse turned loose for<BR>the Aśva-medha sacrifice.<BR>—जयन्त-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—जयन्त-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of the<BR>author of a small treatise on the Vedic accent.<BR>—ज-<BR>यन्ती-पुरी, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयितृ
जयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a victor, conqueror, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, conquering, victorious, a con-<BR>queror; gaining the victory, winning in a suit at<BR>law; granting victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिष्णु
जयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, habitually victorious, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयुस्
जयुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्य|जय्यः
जय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be conquered or gained,<BR>conquerable, vulnerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर|जरः
जर जर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. जॄ), becoming<BR>old or worn out, old; wearing out; causing old age,<BR>producing decay, consuming; (अस्), m. wearing out,<BR>wasting; (आ), f. the becoming old, old age; old age<BR>personified as a daughter of Death; decrepitude, the<BR>general debility consequent upon old age; digestion;<BR>a kind of date tree, = क्षीरिका; N. of a Rākṣasī<BR>worshipped for having united the two halves into<BR>which Jarā-sandha (q. v.) was divided at his birth;<BR>[cf. वि-जर.]<BR>—जरातुर (˚रा-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>firm, decrepit, debilitated, old.<BR>—जरा-परिणत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, stooping, bent down with age or infirmity.<BR>—जरा-पुष्ट, अस्, m. = जरा-सन्ध.<BR>—जरा-<BR>भीरु, उस्, m. love or the deity Kāma (‘afraid of<BR>old age’).<BR>—जरा-मृत्यु, ऊ, m. du. old age and<BR>death; (उस्, उस्, उ), one who dies from old age.<BR>—जरा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, aged, old.<BR>—जरावस्था<BR>(˚रा-अव्˚), f. state of old age, decrepitude.<BR>—जरा-<BR>सन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a celebrated king and warrior,<BR>sovereign of Magadha and Cedi, son of Bṛhad-ratha,<BR>father-in-law to Kaṃśa, and enemy of Kṛṣṇa; he<BR>was slain in single combat by Bhīma; (according to<BR>a legend, he was born divided in two halves, which<BR>were put together by the Rākṣasī Jarā, q. v.; he is<BR>also identified with the Dānava Vipracitti, and men-<BR>tioned among the hundred sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.)<BR>—जरासन्ध-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of Jarā-sandha,’<BR>N. of Bhīma-sena, the second of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठ|जरठः
जरठ, अस्, आ, अम्, old, decayed, infirm; bent,<BR>bowed down, drooping; hard, solid; hard-hearted,<BR>harsh, cruel; pale, yellowish-white (the colour of old<BR>leaves); (अस्), m. decrepitude, old age; [cf. Germ.<BR>hart; Goth. hardus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण|जरणं|जरणः
जरण, अस्, आ, अम्, old, decayed, infirm; solvent,<BR>promoting digestion; (अस्, अम्), m. n. several medi-<BR>cinal plants or drugs used for promoting digestion, =<BR>जीरक, cumin-seed; कृष्ण-जीरक, Nigella Indica;<BR>= कास-मर्द and = कुष्ठौषधि; Asa Fœ-<BR>tida; a sort of salt, Bit-lobon or Bit-lavana; (आ), f.<BR>old age; the plant Nigella Indica; (अम्), n. old age,<BR>becoming old and infirm; one of the ten ways in<BR>which an eclipse is supposed to end.<BR>—जरण-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. the tree Vatica Robusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणा
1. जरणा. See under जरण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्ड|जरंड|जरण्डः
जरण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, decayed, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्या
जरण्या, f., Ved. decrepitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्|जरन्त्
जरत्, अन्, अन्ती (or अती ?), अत्, old, ancient, advanced<BR>in years, infirm, decayed; (अन्), m. an old man; (ती),<BR>f. an old woman; [cf. Gr. γέρων; Hib. gearait, ‘a<BR>saint, a holy man;’ Germ. krank ?].<BR>—जरत्-कारु,<BR>उस्, उस्, m. f., N. of an ancient Ṛṣi of the family of<BR>Yāyāvara, and of his wife who was a sister of the ser-<BR>pent-prince Vāsuki, both being the parents of Āstīka;<BR>(उस्), m. the Vyāsa of the twenty-seventh Dvāpara.<BR>—जरत्कारु-प्रिया, f. the wife of Jarat-kāru exer-<BR>cising a peculiar power over serpents, see the preceding.<BR>—जरद्-अष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. reaching to a great<BR>age, very old; (इस्), f. longevity.<BR>—जरद्-गव, अस्,<BR>m. an old bull or ox; N. of a vulture; (ई), f. an old<BR>cow; [cf. गो-जर.]<BR>—जरद्गव-वीथि, इस्, f. ‘the<BR>course of the old bull,’ N. of a part of the moon's path<BR>occupied by the constellations Vi-śākhā, Anu-rādhā,<BR>and Jyeṣṭhā.<BR>—जरद्-योषा, f. an old woman.<BR>—ज-<BR>रद्-विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. (Sāy.) seizing on and devouring<BR>dry (wood) or consuming water (applied to Agni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरतिका
जरतिका, f. an old woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरतिन्
जरतिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरन्त|जरंत|जरन्तः
जरन्त, अस्, m. an old man; a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरयितृ
जरयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, consuming, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरयु
जरयु, उस्, उस्, उ, becoming old; [cf. अ-जरयु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरस्
जरस्, आ, f. (only जरस् before vowel-terminations,<BR>Gram. 171), the becoming old, decay, decrepitude, old<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">Page0340-c+ 76</a>]<BR>age; (आ), m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa by Turī; N. of<BR>the hunter who wounded Kṛṣṇa; [cf. Gr. γῆρας.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरस
जरस at the end of an adv. comp. = जरस्; [cf.<BR>आ-जरसम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरसान|जरसानः
जरसान, अस्, m. a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरा
1. जरा, f. old age &c. See under जर, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायणि|जरायणिः
जरायणि, इस्, m. = जरा-सन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायु|जरायुः
जरायु, उस्, उस्, उ, withering, dying away; (उ),<BR>n. the slough or cast-off skin of a serpent; the<BR>membrane which envelopes the fetus, the outer skin<BR>of the embryo or chorion, (the inner or amnion is<BR>called उल्व); after-birth, secundines; (उस्), m., N.<BR>of a plant, = अग्नि-जार; also = जटायु; (उस्), f., N.<BR>of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; [cf.<BR>ज्योतिर्-जरायु and निर्-जरायु.]<BR>—जरायु-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, born from the womb, viviparous, born alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरित
जरित, अस्, आ, अम्, old, decayed; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>Śārṅgikā (or kind of bird), the mother of four sons<BR>at once by the Ṛṣi Manda-pāla in the form of a<BR>male Sārṅgaka.<BR>—जरितारि (˚त-अरि), इस्, m., N. of<BR>the eldest son of Manda-pāla by Jaritā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरिन्
जरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, old, ancient, infirm, decayed; (ई),<BR>m. an old man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरिमन्
जरिमन्, आ, m., Ved. old age; decrepitude,<BR>death from old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरूथ|जरूथं|जरूथः
1. जरूथ, अम्, n. skinniness, flesh flaccid with<BR>old age; flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जर|जर्ज्जरः
जर्जर, अस्, आ, अम्, old, infirm, decrepit, decayed;<BR>torn or broken in pieces, split up into small particles,<BR>divided in parts or pieces, broken; perforated,<BR>wounded, hurt; dull, hollow (as the sound of a<BR>broken vessel); (अम्), n. Indra's banner or emblem;<BR>= सैवल, an aquatic plant.<BR>—जर्जर-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being old or decayed or perforated &c.<BR>—जर्ज-<BR>रानना (˚र-आन्˚), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरित
जर्जरित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn in pieces, worn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीक|जर्ज्जरीकः
जर्जरीक, अस्, आ, अम्, old, decayed; ragged,<BR>perforated, full of holes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीकृत|जर्ज्जरीकृत
जर्जरी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, wounded, disabled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ण|जर्णः
जर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, old, decayed; (अस्), m. the<BR>(waning) moon; a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरडी
जरडी जरडी, f. a kind of grass; [cf.<BR>गर्मोटिका, जयाश्रया, सुनाला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणा
जरणा 2. जरणा, f. (fr. 3. जॄ), Ved. roaring,<BR>crackling, sounding; (Sāy.) invoking, praising; [cf.<BR>1. जरण, col. 2.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणिप्रा
जरणि-प्रा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. moving on with<BR>noise; (Sāy.) increasing the wealth of the praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणीय
जरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be addressed with praise<BR>or invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्यु
जरण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. invoking aloud; (Sāy.)<BR>desiring praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरमाण
जरमाण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरा
2. जरा, f., Ved. crackling, roaring; invoking,<BR>greeting; praise; [cf. 1. जरा above.]<BR>—जरा-बोध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. attending to invocation or praise.<BR>—जराबोधीय, अम्, n., N. of several Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरितृ
जरितृ, ता, m., Ved. an invoker, singer, praiser,<BR>worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरूथ|जरूथं|जरूथः
2. जरूथ, अस्, m., Ved. one who roars or makes<BR>a noise; N. of a demon conquered by Agni; (Sāy.)<BR>speaking harshly or to be invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च्
जर्च् जर्च्, cl. 1. 6. P. जर्चति, &c., to say,<BR>speak; to reprove, abuse, blame; to<BR>threaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्छ्
जर्छ् जर्छ्, cl. 1. 6. P. जर्च्छति, &c., to<BR>say, speak; to blame; [cf. चर्च्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ज्
जर्ज् जर्ज्, cl. 1. 6. P. जर्जति, &c., to say;<BR>to blame, reprove; to kill or hurt (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जित
जर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn to pieces, wounded;<BR>(perhaps a wrong form for जर्जरित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जर|जर्ज्जरः
जर्जर जर्जर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्झ्
जर्झ् जर्झ्, cl. 1. 6. P. जर्झति, to say or<BR>speak; to blame; to threaten; [cf. जर्च्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त|जर्त्तः
