जर्तिक|जर्त्तिक
जर्तिक जर्तिक, आस्, m. pl. = बाहीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्तिल|जर्तिलः|जर्त्तिल|जर्त्तिलः
जर्तिल जर्तिल, अस्, m. wild sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्तु|जर्तुः|जर्त्तु|जर्त्तुः
जर्तु जर्तु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. जन्),<BR>the vulva; an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्स्
जर्त्स् जर्त्स्, cl. 1. P. जर्त्सति, &c., to say,<BR>speak; to blame, censure, abuse; to<BR>protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्भरि
जर्भरि जर्भरि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. भृ ?), Ved.<BR>supporting (?). According to Sāy. जर्भरी = भर्-<BR>तारौ, supporters (epithet of the Aśvins).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्य
जर्य जर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. जॄ), becoming<BR>old; [cf. अ-जर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्वर
जर्वर जर्वर, अस्, m., N. of a priest assist-<BR>ing at a sacrifice by which the serpent-race overcame<BR>death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्हिल|जर्हिलः
जर्हिल जर्हिल, अस्, m. wild sesamum; [cf.<BR>जर्तिल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्
जल् जल्, cl. 1. P. जलति, &c., to be rich<BR>or wealthy; to cover, hide, or veil; to<BR>cover as with a net, encompass; to be sharp; to be<BR>cold, stiff, dull, dumb; cl. 10. P. जालयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cover; [cf. Lat. galea.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
1. जल, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. the preceding rt.;<BR>perhaps connected with गल्; cf. जड), cold, stupid,<BR>apathetic, idiotic; (अस्), m., N. of a man with the<BR>patronymic Jātukarṇya; (आ), f., N. of a river;<BR>(अम्), n. water, any fluid; a kind of fragrant medi-<BR>cinal plant, = ह्रीवेर; the embryo or uterus of a<BR>cow; frigidity (moral, mental, or physical); [cf. Lat.<BR>gelu; Goth. kalds; Lith. sẓala, szattas; Russ.<BR>cholodnyi; Hib. gil.]<BR>—जल-कण्टक, अस्, m. a<BR>crocodile; ‘water-thorn,’ the plant Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—जल-कपि, इस्, m. the Gangetic porpoise, Delphinus<BR>Gangeticus (‘water-monkey’).<BR>—जल-कपोत, अस्,<BR>m. ‘water-pigeon,’ N. of a particular species of bird.<BR>—जल-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, making or pouring forth<BR>water; (अस्), m. rent or tax derived from water for<BR>fisheries &c.<BR>—जल-करङ्क, अस्, m. a shell, a<BR>conch; a cocoa-nut; a cloud; a wave; a lotus.<BR>—जल-कल्क, अस्, m. ‘water-sediment,’ mud, mire.<BR>—जल-कल्मष, अस्, m. the poison produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean.<BR>—जल-काक, अस्, m. ‘a water-<BR>crow,’ the diver bird.<BR>—जल-काङ्क्ष, अस्, m. ‘de-<BR>sirous of water,’ an elephant; [cf. जलाकाङ्क्ष.]<BR>—जल-काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, desirous of water, fond<BR>of water; (ई), m. an elephant.<BR>—जल-कान्त, अस्, m.<BR>the wind (‘the water-lover’).<BR>—जल-कान्तार, अस्,<BR>m. a N. of Varuṇa (‘whose grove or garden is<BR>water’).<BR>—जल-कामुक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, =<BR>कुटुम्बिनी.<BR>—जल-किराट, अस्, m. (किराट for कि-<BR>रात ?), a shark or (according to some) a large<BR>alligator.<BR>—जल-कुक्कुट, अस्, m. a water-fowl or<BR>other water-bird; (ई), f. the black-headed gull; [cf.<BR>गङ्गाचिल्ली.]<BR>—जल-कुक्कुभ, अस्, m. a species of<BR>aquatic bird, = कोयष्टि.<BR>—जल-कुन्तल, अस्, m.<BR>‘water-hair,’ N. of an aquatic plant, Blyxa Octandra;<BR>[cf. जल-केश.]<BR>—जल-कुब्जक, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>aquatic plant, Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—जल-कूपी, f. a<BR>spring, well; pond, pool; whirlpool.<BR>—जल-कूर्म,<BR>अस्, m. the Gangetic porpoise.<BR>—जल-कृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>causing rain.<BR>—जल-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>comet.<BR>—जल-केलि, इस्, इस्, m. f. playing or gambol-<BR>ing in water, splashing one another with water.<BR>—जलकेलि-वर्णन, अम्, n. title of the third<BR>chapter of Hari-nātha's poem Rāma-vilāsa-kāvya.<BR>—जल-केश, अस्, m. ‘water-hair,’ the plant Blyxa<BR>Octandra; [cf. जल-कुन्तल.]<BR>—जल-क्रिया, f. a<BR>funeral ceremony, offering libations, presenting water<BR>to the manes of the deceased.<BR>—जल-क्रीडा, f. sport-<BR>ing or gamboling in water, bathing for pleasure or<BR>amusement; [cf. जल-केलि.]<BR>—जल-खग, अस्, m.<BR>an aquatic bird.<BR>—जल-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, making<BR>the water fragrant (?) or turbid (?).<BR>—जल-गन्धे-<BR>भ, अस्, m. ‘a scented elephant frequenting water,’<BR>N. of a species of animal.<BR>—जल-गर्भ, अस्, m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-b" target="_blank">Page0341-b+ 81</a>]<BR>N. of a son of Jala-vāhana, = Ānanda in a former<BR>birth.<BR>—जल-गुल्म, अस्, m. a turtle, tortoise; a<BR>quadrangular tank, a piece of water; a whirlpool.<BR>—जलङ्-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, aquatic, frequenting water,<BR>going in water; (अस्), m. the colocynth (महा-<BR>काल).<BR>—जलङ्-गम, अस्, m. a Cāṇḍāla, an outcast;<BR>(a various reading for जनङ्-गम.)<BR>—जल-च-<BR>त्वर, अम्, n. a square tank.<BR>—जल-चर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, going in water, aquatic, amphibious; (अस्), m.<BR>an aquatic animal.<BR>—जलचर-जीव, अस्, m. a fisher-<BR>man; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of the east coast.<BR>—जलचराजीव (˚र-आज्˚), अस्, m. a fisherman.<BR>—जल-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, living in or near water,<BR>frequenting water; (ई), m. an aquatic animal, a fish.<BR>—जल-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced or born in water,<BR>living or growing in water; coming from or peculiar<BR>to water; (अस्), m. an aquatic animal, a fish; sea-salt,<BR>= लोनार, a collective N. for several signs of the<BR>zodiac; (आ), f. a kind of plant, = क्लीतक; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a shell; the conch-shell used as a trumpet;<BR>(अम्), n. a pearl, a shell or other product of the sea;<BR>the lotus (Nelumbium); N. of several other plants,<BR>= हिज्जल, शैवल, वानीर, कुपीलु.<BR>—जलज-<BR>कुसुम, अम्, n. ‘water-flower,’ the lotus.<BR>—जलज-<BR>कुसुम-योनि, इस्, m. ‘born from a lotus-flower,’ a<BR>N. of Brahmā.<BR>—जलज-द्रव्य, अम्, n. a pearl, a<BR>shell or other product of the sea.<BR>—जल-जन्तु, उस्,<BR>m. a fish or any marine or aquatic or amphibious<BR>animal.<BR>—जल-जन्तुका, f. a leech.<BR>—जल-जन्मन्,<BR>अ, n. ‘water-born,’ the lotus (Nelumbium).<BR>—जलजा-<BR>जीव (˚ज-आज्˚), अस्, m. a fisherman; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>inhabitants of the eastern coast; [cf. जलचर-जीव.]<BR>—जलजासन (˚ज-आस्˚), अस्, m. a N. of Brahmā<BR>(sitting on the lotus).<BR>—जल-जिह्व, अस्, m. a croco-<BR>dile (‘having a cold tongue?’).<BR>—जल-जीविन्, ई, m.<BR>a fisherman.<BR>—जल-डिम्ब, अस्, m. a bivalve shell.<BR>—जल-तरङ्ग, अस्, m. a wave; a metal cup filled<BR>with water producing harmonic notes like a musical<BR>glass.<BR>—जल-ता, f. the state of water.<BR>—जल-ताडन,<BR>अम्, n. beating water, any fruitless action.<BR>—जल-<BR>तापिक, अस्, m. the Hilsa or sable fish, Clupanodon<BR>Ilisha (also called जल-तापिन्); another kind of fish,<BR>commonly Caöuchi, Cyprinus Cachius.<BR>—जल-ताल,<BR>अस्, m. the Ilisha or Hilsa fish.<BR>—जल-तिक्तिका, f.<BR>Boswellia Murifera.<BR>—जल-तुरग, अस्, m. ‘water-<BR>horse,’ hippopotamus (?).<BR>—जल-त्रा, f. ‘water-guard,’<BR>an umbrella.<BR>—जल-त्रास, अस्, m. hydrophobia.<BR>—ज-<BR>ल-त्रासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having hydrophobia, hydrophobic.<BR>—जल-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving or pouring forth<BR>water; (अस्), m. a cloud; a fragrant grass, Cyperus<BR>Rotundus [cf. मुस्तक]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>school of the Atharva-veda; N. of a Varṣa in<BR>Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—जलद-क्षय, अस्, m. disappear-<BR>ance of the clouds, autumn.<BR>—जलद-पङ्क्ति,<BR>इस्, f. a line or long succession of clouds.<BR>—जल-<BR>दर्दुर, अस्, m. a water-pipe, a kind of musical<BR>instrument.<BR>—जलद-संहति, इस्, f. the gathering<BR>of clouds, cloudiness.<BR>—जलदागम (˚द-आग्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the arrival or approach of clouds, the rainy season.<BR>—जल-दान, अम्, n. the giving of water.<BR>—जल-<BR>दाभ (˚द-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्, cloud-like, dark,<BR>black.<BR>—जलदाशन (˚द-अश्˚), अस्, m. the tree<BR>Shorea Robusta, = शाल.<BR>—जल-देव, अम्, n., scil.<BR>भ or नक्षत्र, the constellation Aṣāḍhā,<BR>having the water as its deity.<BR>—जल-देवता, f. a<BR>water-goddess, naiad.<BR>—जल-द्रव्य, अम्, n. a pearl,<BR>a shell or other product of the sea; [cf. जलज-<BR>द्रव्य.]<BR>—जल-द्रोणी, f. a bucket.<BR>—जल-द्वीप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an island.<BR>—जल-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>holding or carrying or having water; (अस्), m. a<BR>cloud; the ocean; a kind of grass, Cyperus Ro-<BR>tundus; the plant Dalbergia Ougeinensis; N. of a<BR>metre containing 4 × 32 syllabic instants.<BR>—जल-<BR>धर-गर्जित-घोष-सुस्वर-नक्षत्र-राज-<BR>सङ्कुसुमिताभिज्ञ (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Buddha (having a voice musical as the sound of the<BR>thunder of the clouds and conversant with the<BR>appearance of the regents of the Nakṣatras).<BR>—ज-<BR>लधर-माला, f. a row of clouds; a metre con-<BR>sisting of four lines of twelve syllables each.<BR>—जल-<BR>धार, अस्, m., N. of a mountain; N. of a Varṣa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-c" target="_blank">Page0341-c+ 81</a>]<BR>in Śāka-dvīpa; (आ), f. a stream of water.<BR>—जल-<BR>धि, इस्, m. the ocean; a large number, 100 billions.<BR>—जलधि-गा, f. ‘going to the ocean,’ a river.<BR>—जलधि-जा, f. ‘ocean-born,’ N. of the goddess<BR>Lakṣmī (as one of the fourteen precious things re-<BR>covered at the churning of the ocean).<BR>—जलधि-<BR>रसन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘ocean-girt,’ an epithet of the<BR>earth.<BR>—जलधि-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>from the ocean, marine.<BR>—जल-नकुल, अस्, m. an<BR>otter.<BR>—जल-नर, अस्, m. ‘water-man,’ merman, N.<BR>of a particular animal.<BR>—जल-नाडी, f. a water-course.<BR>—जल-निधि, इस्, m. ‘treasure of water,’ the ocean,<BR>sea.<BR>—जल-निर्गम, अस्, m. a drain, a water-course,<BR>a pipe along a wall or building for carrying off water,<BR>a water-fall, the descent of a spring &c. into a river<BR>below.<BR>—जल-निवह, अस्, m. a quantity of water.<BR>—जल-नीलिका or जल-नीली, f. the aquatic plant<BR>Blyxa Octandra.<BR>—जलन्-धम, अस्, m., N. of one<BR>of the attendants of Skanda; also of a Dānava; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Kṛṣṇa by Satya-bhāmā.<BR>—जलन्-धर, अस्, m. ‘water-bearer,’ N. of a<BR>man; N. of an Asura fabled to have been produced<BR>by the contact of a flash from Śiva's eye with the<BR>ocean and adopted by the god of the waters; he is<BR>so called as having on a particular occasion caught<BR>the water which flowed from Brahmā's eye.<BR>—ज-<BR>लन्धर-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—जलन्-<BR>धर-वध, अस्, m. title of a chapter of the Liṅga-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—जल-पक्षिन्, ई, m. a water-bird.<BR>—जल-<BR>पटल, अम्, n. a sheet of water, a cloud.<BR>—जल-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the waters,’ i. e. Varuṇa or the<BR>Hindū Neptune; the ocean.<BR>—जल-पथ, अस्, m.<BR>a sea voyage.<BR>—जल-पद्धति, इस्, f. a water-course,<BR>gutter, drain.<BR>—जल-पात्र, अम्, n. a drinking-vessel.<BR>—जल-पाद, अस्, m. (for जाल-पाद ?), N. of a<BR>frog-king.<BR>—जल-पान, अम्, n. the drinking of<BR>water; (in Bengal = refreshment, luncheon.)<BR>—जल-<BR>पारावत, अस्, m. ‘an aquatic pigeon,’ N. of a<BR>particular bird.<BR>—जल-पित्त, अम्, n. fire (‘the bile<BR>of water’).<BR>—जल-पिप्पली, f. an aquatic plant,<BR>Commelina Salicifolia, and another species.<BR>—जल-<BR>पिप्पिका, f. a fish.<BR>—जल-पुष्प, अम्, n. an<BR>aquatic flower.<BR>—जल-पूर, अस्, m. the full bed or<BR>stream of a river, a full stream.<BR>—जल-पृष्ठजा,<BR>f. the plant Blyxa Octandra, or Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—जल-प्रपात, अस्, m. a water-fall.<BR>—जल-प्र-<BR>लय, अस्, m. destruction by water.<BR>—जल-प्रान्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the water's edge,’ shore, bank of a river.<BR>—जल-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding with water;<BR>(अम्), n. a country abounding with water.<BR>—जल-<BR>प्रिय अस्, आ, अम्, fond of water, frequenting water;<BR>(अस्), m. the bird Cātaka, Cuculus Melanoleucus; a<BR>fish; (आ), f. an epithet of Dākṣāyaṇi.<BR>—जल-प्लव,<BR>अस्, m. an otter.<BR>—जल-प्लावन, अम्, n. immersion<BR>under water, an inundation, a deluge.<BR>—जल-फल,<BR>अस्, m. the water-nut, Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—जल-बन्-<BR>धक, अस्, m. ‘water-barrier,’ a dam, a dike, rocks<BR>or stones impeding a current.<BR>—जल-बन्धु, उस्,<BR>m. a fish (‘friend of water’).<BR>—जल-बालक or जल-<BR>वालक, अस्, m. an epithet of the Vindhya mountains;<BR>(इका), f. lightning (surrounded by water, i. e. clouds ?).<BR>—जल-बिम्ब, a kind of plant (?).<BR>—जल-बुद्बुद,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a bubble of water.<BR>—जल-ब्रह्मी, f.<BR>a kind of pot-herb, Hingcha Repens.<BR>—जल-भा-<BR>जन, अम्, n. a vessel for water, water-pot.<BR>—जल-<BR>भीति, इस्, f. hydrophobia.<BR>—जल-भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>aquatic, produced in or by water; (ऊस्), m. a cloud;<BR>N. of a plant, = कञ्चट^1.<BR>—जल-भूषण, अस्, m.<BR>wind (‘decorating the water’).<BR>—जल-भृत्, त्, m.<BR>a cloud (‘water-bearing’).<BR>—जल-मक्षिका, f. a<BR>water-insect.<BR>—जल-मग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, immersed<BR>in water.<BR>—जल-मद्गु, उस्, m. a kingfisher.<BR>—ज-<BR>ल-मधूक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = कीरेष्ट,<BR>क्षौद्र-प्रिय, &c.<BR>—जल-मन्दिर, अम्, n. =<BR>जल-यन्त्र-गृह.<BR>—जल-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed<BR>of water, consisting of water, watery.<BR>—जल-मसि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘water-ink,’ a dark cloud.<BR>—जल-मात्रेण,<BR>ind. by mere water.<BR>—जल-मार्ग, अस्, m. a water-<BR>course, a drain or canal leading from a pond &c.<BR>—जल-मार्जार, अस्, m. ‘water-cat,’ an otter.<BR>—जल-मुच्, क्, क्, क्, shedding water; (क्), m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-a" target="_blank">Page0342-a+ 81</a>]<BR>a cloud.<BR>—जल-मूर्ति, इस्, m. Śiva, of whom one<BR>form is water, (implying his presence in all matter.)<BR>—जल-मूर्तिका, f. hail (a form of water).<BR>—जल-<BR>मोद, अम्, n. ‘delighting in water,’ the fragrant<BR>root of Andropogon Muricatus, = उशीर.<BR>—जलम्-<BR>बल (?), अम्, n. a stream; collyrium.<BR>—जल-यन्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. a water-engine, a machine for raising water<BR>&c., any contrivance connected with that element;<BR>a water-clock, a clepsydra.<BR>—जल-यन्त्रक, अम्, n.<BR>a machine for raising water &c.<BR>—जलयन्त्र-गृह<BR>or जलयन्त्र-निकेतन or जलयन्त्र-मन्दिर,<BR>अम्, n. a house or fabric erected in the midst of<BR>water; subterranean apartments constructed in the<BR>bank of a river to serve as a retreat in the hot season,<BR>a summer-house &c.<BR>—जल-यात्रा, f. a voyage.<BR>—ज-<BR>ल-यान, अम्, n. ‘a water vehicle,’ a ship.<BR>—जल-<BR>रङ्क, अस्, m. or जल-रञ्ज, अस्, m. a species of Vaka<BR>or crane (Ardea Nivea).<BR>—जल-रङ्कु, उस्, m. a<BR>kind of gallinule.<BR>—जल-रण्ड, अस्, m. a whirlpool;<BR>a drop, drizzle, thin sprinkling of water; a snake;<BR>[cf. जल-रुण्ड.]<BR>—जल-रस, अस्, m. sea-salt.<BR>—ज-<BR>ल-राक्षसी, f. ‘the water Rākṣasī,’ also called<BR>Su-rasā, a female demon described in Rāmāyaṇa<BR>V. 6. as the mother of the Nāgas; she placed herself<BR>in the way of Hanumat in his flight across the straits<BR>between the continent and Ceylon, and in order to<BR>prevent his crossing attempted to swallow him bodily.<BR>He escaped by reducing himself to the size of a<BR>thumb, darting through her huge body and coming<BR>out at her right ear.<BR>—जल-राशि, इस्, m. a sheet of<BR>water, a quantity of water; the ocean.<BR>—जल-रुण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. = जल-रण्ड.<BR>—जल-रुह्, ट्, m. ‘growing in<BR>water,’ a lotus (Nelumbium).<BR>—जल-रुह, अस्, m.<BR>an aquatic animal; (अम्), n. the lotus (Nelumbium).<BR>—जल-रूप, अस्, m. the fish of Kāma-deva, =<BR>मकर.<BR>—जल-लता, f. ‘water-creeper,’ a wave, a<BR>billow.<BR>—जल-लव-मुच्, क्, क्, क्, discharging drops<BR>of water.<BR>—जल-लोहित, अस्, m. a Rākṣasa (having<BR>water for blood).<BR>—जल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding<BR>in water.<BR>—जल-वरण्ट, अस्, m. a watery pustule.<BR>—जल-वल्कल, अम्, n., N. of the aquatic plant<BR>Pistia Stratiotes.<BR>—जल-वल्ली, f. the water-nut,<BR>Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—जल-वादित, अम्, n. water-music,<BR>a kind of music in which water is used.<BR>—जल-<BR>वाद्य, अम्, n. a kind of musical instrument in which<BR>water is used.<BR>—जल-वायस, अस्, m. ‘a water-crow,’<BR>the diver bird.<BR>—जल-वालक, cf. जल-बालक.<BR>—जल-वास, अस्, m. residence in water; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), living or residing in water; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>root, = विष्णु-कन्द; (अम्), n. the root of Andro-<BR>pogon Muricatus, = उशीर.<BR>—जल-वाह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>carrying water; (अस्), m. a water-bearer, a cloud.<BR>—जल-वाहक, अस्, m. a water-bearer, or carrier.<BR>—जल-वाहन, अस्, m. a water-carrier; N. of a<BR>physician, = Śākya-muni in a former birth; (अम्),<BR>n. flowing of water; (ई), f. a water-course, aqueduct.<BR>—जल-विडाल, अस्, m. an otter.<BR>—जल-विन्दु, उस्,<BR>m. a drop of water; N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—जलविन्दु-<BR>जा, f. a kind of sugar.<BR>—जल-विल्व, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Pistia Stratiotes; a tortoise; a crab; a quadrangular<BR>pond.<BR>—जल-विषुव, अम्, n. the autumnal equinox,<BR>the moment of the sun's entering Libra; a kind of<BR>circle or cycle.<BR>—जल-विहङ्गम, अस्, m. a water-<BR>fowl.<BR>—जल-वीर्य, अस्, m., N. of a son of Bharata.<BR>—जल-वृश्चिक, अस्, m. ‘water-scorpion,’ a prawn<BR>or shrimp.<BR>—जल-वेतस, अस्, m. a kind of cane, =<BR>वानीर.<BR>—जल-व्यथ or जल-व्यध, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of fish, Esox Cancila.<BR>—जल-व्याल, अस्, m. a<BR>water-snake; a marine monster.<BR>—जल-शय or ज-<BR>ल-शयन, अस्, or जल-शायिन्, ई, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu, who is supposed to sleep, reposing on his<BR>serpent-couch above the waters, during the four<BR>months of the periodical rains; also during the inter-<BR>vals of the submersion of the world; [cf. जले-शय.]<BR>—जलशायि-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—जल-<BR>शुक्ति, इस्, f. a bivalve shell.<BR>—जल-शुचि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>cleansed by water, bathed, washed.<BR>—जल-शूक, अम्,<BR>n. the plant Blyxa Octandra, a green moss-like sub-<BR>stance growing on the surface of stagnant water,<BR>duckweed.<BR>—जल-शूकर, अस्, m. a crocodile (‘water-<BR>hog’).<BR>—जल-शोष, अस्, m. drying up of water, drought.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-b" target="_blank">Page0342-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—जल-संसर्ग, अस्, m. mixing with water, dilu-<BR>tion.<BR>—जल-सन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a prince, a son<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—जल-समुद्र, अस्, m. the sea<BR>of fresh water.<BR>—जल-सम्पर्क, अस्, m. mixture or<BR>dilution with water.<BR>—जल-सर्पिणी, f. ‘water-glider,’<BR>a leech.<BR>—जल-सात्, ind. to the state of water (e. g.<BR>जलसात् कृ, to reduce to water; जलसात् सम्पद्-<BR>यते, it is turned into water).<BR>—जल-सिक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, sprinkled with water, wetted.<BR>—जल-सूचि, इस्,<BR>m. the Gangetic porpoise, Delphinus Gangeticus; a<BR>crow; a fish, a small sort of pike, Esox Cancila; a<BR>leech; a water-nut, Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—जल-सेक,<BR>अस्, m. sprinkling with water.<BR>—जल-स्थ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, standing or abiding or situated in water; (आ), f.<BR>a kind of grass, = गण्ड-दूर्वा.<BR>—जल-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. or जल-स्थाय, अस्, m. a reservoir, a pond,<BR>a lake.<BR>—जल-ह, अम्, n. a small water (or summer)<BR>house; [cf. जलयन्त्र-गृह.]<BR>—जल-हरण, अम्,<BR>n. a metre consisting of 4 × 32 syllabic instants.<BR>—जल-<BR>हस्तिन्, ई, m. a water-elephant; hippopotamus (?).<BR>—ज-<BR>ल-हार, अस्, ई, m. f. a water-carrier.<BR>—जल-हारिणी, f.<BR>a water-course, drain, a channel for water.<BR>—जल-हास<BR>or जल-हासक, अस्, m. cuttle-fish bone, considered<BR>as the indurated foam of the sea.<BR>—जल-ह्रद, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—जलाकर (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, m. a source<BR>of water, a spring, a fountain.<BR>—जलाका, f. = जलौका,<BR>a leech.<BR>—जलाकाङ्क्ष (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, m. = जल-<BR>काङ्क्ष, an elephant.<BR>—जलाक्षी (˚ल-अक्˚), f. an<BR>aquatic plant, Commelina Salicifolia.<BR>—जलाखु (˚ल-<BR>आखु), उस्, m. ‘water-mole,’ an otter.<BR>—जलाञ्चल<BR>(˚ल-अञ्˚), अम्, n. a spring, well; natural water-course;<BR>the plant Blyxa Octandra.<BR>—जलाञ्जलि (˚ल-अञ्˚),<BR>इस्, f. a handful of water, or water held in the palms<BR>of the hand, as presented to the manes of a dead<BR>person &c.<BR>—जलाटन (˚ल-अट्˚), अस्, m. ‘water-<BR>goer,’ a heron; (ई), f. a leech.<BR>—जलाढ्य (˚ल-<BR>आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, watery, marshy.<BR>—जलाणुक<BR>(˚ल-अण्˚), अम्, n. the fry of fish.<BR>—जलाण्टक, अस्,<BR>m. a shark or (according to some) a large alligator<BR>&c.<BR>—जलाण्डक (˚ल-अण्˚), अम्, n. the fry of fish.<BR>—जलात्मिका (˚ल-आत्˚), f. a leech; a well (in the<BR>latter sense a various reading for जलाम्बिका).<BR>—ज-<BR>लात्यय (˚ल-अत्˚), अस्, m. the passing away of the<BR>water (or clouds), autumn.<BR>—जलादर्श (˚ल-आद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a watery mirror, water reflecting any object<BR>like a mirror.<BR>—जलाधार (˚ल-आध्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>pond, a lake, a reservoir, any receptacle of water.<BR>—जलाधिदैवत (˚ल-अध्˚), अम्, n., scil. भ or<BR>नक्षत्र, the constellation Aṣāḍhā (having the<BR>water as its deity; cf. जल-देव); (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Varuṇa (?).<BR>—जलाधिप (˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, or जला-<BR>धिपति (˚ल-अध्˚), इस्, or जलाध्यक्ष (˚ल-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Varuṇa, lord of the waters.<BR>—जलानुसार (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, m. going or acting<BR>like water.<BR>—जलान्तक (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Kṛṣṇa by Satya-bhāmā; (अस्, आ, अम्), having<BR>water in the interior (अन्त); containing water.<BR>—जलापस्पर्शन (˚ल-अप्˚), अम्, n. touching<BR>water, use of water.<BR>—जलाभिषेक (˚ल-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. sprinkling with water.<BR>—जलाम्बर (˚ल-अम्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man, = Rāhala-bhadra in a former<BR>birth.<BR>—जलाम्बिका (˚ल-अम्˚), f. a well; [cf. जलात्-<BR>मिका.]<BR>—जलाम्बु-गर्भा (˚ल-अम्˚), f., N. of a<BR>woman, = Gopā in a former birth.<BR>—जलायुका (˚ल-<BR>आयु) or 1. जलालुका or जलालोका or जलावुका or<BR>जलासुका, f. a leech (living in water).<BR>—जलार्क<BR>(˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, m. the sun reflected in water.<BR>—जलार्-<BR>णव (˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, m. the rainy season; the sea of<BR>fresh water.<BR>—जलार्थिन् (˚ल-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, desirous<BR>of water, thirsty.<BR>—जलार्द्र (˚ल-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>wet, charged with aqueous moisture; (अस्, आ), m. f.<BR>wet cloth or clothes.<BR>—जलालु (˚ल-आलु), उस्, m. a<BR>kind of bulbous plant.<BR>—जलावतार (˚ल-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a landing-place at a river's side.<BR>—जलावर्त (˚ल-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘the turning round of water,’ an eddy, a<BR>whirlpool.<BR>—जलाविल (˚ल-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, stained<BR>or soiled with water.<BR>—जलाशय (˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, resting or lying in water; stupid, dull, apathetic,<BR>cold; (अस्), m. a pond, a tank, a lake, a reservoir or<BR>any piece of water; a fish; the water-nut, Trapa<BR>Bispinosa; (आ), f. a kind of plant, = गुण्डाला; (अम्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">Page0342-c+ 79</a>]<BR>n. the root of Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—जलाशयान्-<BR>तर (˚य-अन्˚), अम्, n. another lake.<BR>—जलाशयोत्-<BR>सर्ग-तत्त्व (˚य-उत्˚), अम्, n. a part of the Smṛti-<BR>tattva.<BR>—जलाशयोत्सर्ग-विधि, इस्, m. title of a work<BR>by Kamalākara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—जलाशायिन् (˚ल-आश्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, lying or sleeping in water as a penance.<BR>—जलाश्रय<BR>(˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, m. a piece of water, a pond, a lake; a<BR>water-house; (आ), f. a kind of crane; a kind of grass.<BR>—जला-षह् or जला-सह्, -षाट्, ट्, ट्, subduing water.<BR>—जलाष्ठीला (˚ल-अष्˚) or ई, f. a large square pond.<BR>—जला-साह, अस्, आ, अम्, = जला-षह्.<BR>—जलासुका,<BR>f., see जलायुका.<BR>—जलाह्वय (˚ल-आह्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>lotus (Nelumbium).<BR>—जले-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, living<BR>or going in water; (अस्), m. an aquatic animal; a<BR>fish; any kind of water-fowl.<BR>—जलेच्छया, f. the<BR>plant Heliotropium Indicum; [cf. हस्ति-शुण्डा.]<BR>—जले-जात, अम्, n. a lotus (Nelumbium).<BR>—जलेन्-<BR>द्र (˚ल-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘chief of waters,’ the sea; the<BR>ocean of fresh water; Varuṇa, the regent of the<BR>waters; N. of a Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>—जलेन्धन<BR>(˚ल-इन्˚), अम्, n. submarine fire.<BR>—जलेभ (˚ल-<BR>इभ), अस्, m. a water-elephant; [cf. जल-हस्तिन्.]<BR>—जले-रुह, अस्, m., N. of a king of Orissa; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a plant, = कुटुम्बिनी.<BR>—जले-वाह, अस्,<BR>m. a diver (by caste or business).<BR>—जलेश (˚ल-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. the sea, ocean; lord of the waters, i. e.<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>—जले-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, resting or abiding<BR>in water; (अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; a fish.<BR>—जलेश्वर (˚ल-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of waters,’ the<BR>sea, the ocean; the deity of the waters, i. e. Varuṇa;<BR>N. of a sanctuary.<BR>—जलोक, अस्, m., N. of a king<BR>of Kaśmīra; (आ), f. a leech; see जलौकस्.<BR>—जलो-<BR>किका, f. a leech; see जलौकस्.<BR>—जलोच्छ्वास (˚ल-<BR>उच्˚), अस्, m. a drain or channel made for carrying<BR>off an excess of water, or a similar channel made<BR>naturally by the overflow of a river &c.<BR>—जलोदर<BR>(˚ल-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘water-belly,’ dropsy.<BR>—जलोद्-<BR>धत-गति (˚ल-उद्˚), इस्, f., N. of a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of twelve syllables each.<BR>—जलोद्भव<BR>(˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced in water,<BR>aquatic, marine; (अस्), m. ‘origin of the waters,’ N.<BR>of a place; an aquatic animal; N. of a water-demon<BR>slain by Kaśyapa; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = लघु-<BR>ब्राह्मी, benzoin.<BR>—जलोद्भूत (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, born in or produced from water; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a plant, = गुण्डाला.<BR>—जलोन्नाद (˚ल-उन्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the attendants of Śiva.<BR>—जलोरगी<BR>(˚ल-उर्˚), f. ‘water-snake,’ a leech.<BR>—जलौक, अस्,<BR>m. a leech; (आ), f. a leech; [cf. the next.]<BR>—ज-<BR>लौकस् (˚ल-ओक्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, living in water, an<BR>inhabitant of the water, an aquatic animal; (आस्), m.,<BR>N. of a king of Kaśmīra; (आस्), f. a leech (said to<BR>be used in plur. only).<BR>—जलौकस, अस्, आ, अम्, m.<BR>f. n. a leech.<BR>—जलौघ (˚ल-ओघ), अस्, m. a<BR>quantity of water.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk. on 20161122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/320. note: from guttural to palatal nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
2. जल, nom. P., Ved. जलति, to become water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक|जलकं
जलक, अम्, n. a conch, a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाय
जलाय, nom. A. -यते, -यितुम्, to become water,<BR>appear as water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलालुक|जलालुकं
2. जलालुक, अम्, n. a lotus root; [cf. जलायुका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलिका
जलिका or जलुका or जलूका, f. a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेयु
जलेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेला
जलेला, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda; (or perhaps for two words जला इला.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलालुद्दीनकबरशाह
जलालुद्दीनहकबरशाह m. = जलालुऽद्दीन्<BR>अक्बर् षाह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाष
जलाष जलाष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. mitigating,<BR>pacifying, appeasing, healing, comforting; (अम्), n.<BR>water; happiness, comfort.<BR>—जलाष-भेषज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. possessed of healing medicines, an<BR>epithet of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प्
जल्प् जल्प् [cf. जप् and लप्], cl. 1. P.<BR>(ep. also A.) जल्पति, -ते, जजल्प,<BR>जल्पिष्यति, जल्पितुम्, to speak inarticulately, mur-<BR>mur; chatter, prattle, babble, wrangle; to speak,<BR>say; to address a person, speak with; to speak of<BR>or about (with acc.); to praise: Caus. P. जल्पयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to speak; [cf. Lith. kalbu, ‘to<BR>speak;’ kalba, ‘speech:’ Hib. gaill, ‘speech.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प|जल्पः
जल्प, अस्, m. talk, speech; prate, babble, gossip,<BR>chatter, discourse; debate, disputation, wrangling dis-<BR>cussion, an argument in which a disputant tries to<BR>assert his own opinion and to refute that of his ad-<BR>versary by overbearing reply or wrangling rejoinder;<BR>[cf. चित्र-जल्प.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पक
जल्पक, अस्, इका, अम्, a talker, chatterer, talka-<BR>tive, one who talks much or idly, garrulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पन|जल्पनं
जल्पन, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, saying, talking;<BR>(अम्), n. talking, saying; chattering, prattling,<BR>garrulity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पाक|जल्पाकः
जल्पाक, अस्, ई, अम्, a chatterer, talking much and<BR>foolishly, or improperly; [cf. जल्पक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पि|जल्पिः
जल्पि, इस्, f., Ved. inarticulate speech, murmuring;<BR>speaking in a low voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पित|जल्पितं
जल्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, said, told, spoken; (अम्), n.<BR>talk, babbling, gossip; talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पितृ
जल्पितृ, ता, तृ, or जल्पिन्, ई, इनी, इ, a talker,<BR>speaker, chatterer; saying, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्लालदीन्द्र
जल्लालदीन्द्र जल्लालदीन्द्र, अस्, m. = जलालु<BR>ऽद्दीन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जळ्हु
जळ्हु जऌहु, उस्, उस्, उ (related to जड ?),<BR>Ved. deprived of splendor or without sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव जव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. जु or जू), speed,<BR>quickness, velocity, rapidity, swiftness; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>swift, expeditious; (आ), f. the China rose, Hibiscus<BR>Rosa Sinensis; [cf. जपा.]<BR>—जव-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessed of fleetness.<BR>—जव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, quick,<BR>swift, fleet.<BR>—जवाधिक (˚व-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>quick, extremely swift; (अस्), m. a fleet horse, a<BR>courser.<BR>—जवानिल (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. a strong<BR>wind, gale, hurricane.<BR>—जवा-पुष्प, अस्, m. the<BR>China rose, the plant or its flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवन|जवनं|जवनः
1. जवन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to hasten; quick,<BR>swift, fleet; (अस्), m. a courser, a fleet horse; a kind<BR>of deer; N. of one of the attendants of Skanda; (ई),<BR>f. a screen surrounding a tent, a Kanāt; N. of a<BR>plant; (अम्), n. speed, velocity; [cf. धी-जवन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिका
जवनिका, f. a wall or screen of cloth surrounding<BR>a tent, an outer tent, &c.; a curtain, a screen in<BR>general; the sail of a boat; [cf. यवनिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिमन्
जवनिमन्, आ, m. quickness, speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवस्
जवस्, अस्, n., Ved. quickness, velocity; [cf. अ-<BR>जवस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन्
जविन्, ई, इनी, इ, quick, fleet, expeditious; (ई), m.<BR>a horse, a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन
जविन, अस्, आ, अम्, rapid, quick; (अस्), m. = को-<BR>कड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविष्ठ
जविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. quickest, fleetest;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवीयस्
जवीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. quicker, speedier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवन|जवनं|जवनः
जवन 2. जवन, अस्, m., N. of a people<BR>whose country is by some thought to be identical<BR>with Ionia or Greece, = यवन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनाल|जवनालं
जवनाल जवनाल, अम्, n. a sort of grain,<BR>Andropogon Bicolor; [cf. यवनाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवस|जवसं|जवसः
जवस जवस, अस्, m. meadow or pasture<BR>grass; [cf. यवस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवादि
जवादि जवादि, इ, n. a kind of perfume, =<BR>कृत्रिम, गन्ध-राज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवाल
जवाल जवाल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविपुला
जविपुला ज-विपुला, f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष्
जष् जष्, cl. 1. P. A. जषति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to kill, wound, hurt, injure; [cf. Hib. gus,<BR>‘death.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष
जष जष, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of aquatic<BR>animal; [cf. झष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्
जस् जस्, cl. 1. A. P., cl. 4. P., Ved. ज-<BR>सते, -ति, जस्यति, जजास, जसितुम्, to be<BR>exhausted or tired; cl. 4. P. to set free, release,<BR>liberate, let loose: Caus. P. जासयति, -यितुम्, अजी-<BR>जसत्, to exhaust, weaken, cause to expire; cl. 10. 1.<BR>P. जासयति, जसति, &c., to hurt, injure; to strike,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">Page0343-b+ 72</a>]<BR>punish with blows; to slight or disregard, treat<BR>irreverently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसु|जसुः
जसु, उस्, f., Ved. exhaustion, weakness; a hiding-<BR>place, cover (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुरि|जसुरिः
जसुरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. exhausted, weak; (इस्), m.<BR>Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्र|जस्रं
जस्र, अम्, n. exhaustion, fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्वन्
जस्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. needy, poor, hungry;<BR>(Sāy.) causing to waste away, destroying; [cf. अ-<BR>जस्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्सराज
जस्सराज जस्स-राज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहक|जहकः
जहक जहक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हा), aban-<BR>doning, one who leaves or abandons; (अस्), m. time;<BR>a child; the slough of a snake; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>weasel or polecat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्
जहत्, अत्, अती, अत्, leaving, quitting, foregoing.<BR>—जहत्-स्वार्था, f., scil. लक्षणा, a particular<BR>figure of speech, a word losing its original meaning<BR>and taking a different sense; irony.<BR>—जहल्-<BR>लक्षणा, f. = the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहा
जहा जहा, f. a plant, commonly Muṇḍirī;<BR>also कदम्ब-पुष्पी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहानक|जहानकः
जहानक जहानक, अस्, m. the period of the<BR>total destruction of the world; [cf. जिहानक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहिजोड
जहिजोड जहि-जोड, अस्, आ, अम् (जहि impv. fr.<BR>rt. हन् and जोड), one who is in the habit of hitting<BR>his chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहिस्तम्भ
जहि-स्तम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, one who is constantly<BR>striking against a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहु|जहुः
जहु जहु, उस्, m. a young animal; N. of a<BR>son of Puṣpa-vat and descendant of Ṛṣabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नु|जह्नुः
जह्नु जह्नु, उस्, m., N. of an ancient king<BR>and sage who adopted the Gaṅgā as his daughter,<BR>(the river Ganges, when brought down from heaven<BR>by the austerities of Bhagīratha, was forced to flow<BR>over the earth and to follow him to the ocean, and<BR>thence to the lower regions, for the purpose of<BR>watering the ashes of Sagara's sons. In its course it<BR>inundated the sacrificial ground of Jahnu, who there-<BR>fore drank up its waters, but consented at the prayer<BR>of Bhagīratha to discharge them from his ears.<BR>Hence the river is regarded as his daughter, and is<BR>called Jāhnavī); N. of a son of Aja-mīḍha, of a son<BR>of Su-hotra, of Kuru, and of Hotraka; N. of an<BR>ancestor of the Kuśikas; a N. of Viṣṇu; (अवस्),<BR>m. pl. the descendants of Jahnu.<BR>—जह्नु-कन्या, f.<BR>or जह्नु-तनया, f. or जह्नु-सुता, f. ‘daughter<BR>of Jahnu,’ N. of Gaṅgā or the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नावी
जह्नावी, f., Ved. the family of Jahnu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्मन्
जह्मन् जह्मन्, अ, n. water (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्ल
जह्ल जह्ल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जा
जा जा, आस्, आस्, अम् (fr. rt. जन्, and used in<BR>Ved. for 2. ज, which appears rarely in the Veda),<BR>born, produced, &c. [cf. अग्नि-जा, अग्र-जा, अद्रि-जा,<BR>इन्द्र-जा, गो-जा, &c.], see 2. ज; (आस्), m. f., Ved.<BR>offspring, descendants; (आ), f. a race, tribe.<BR>—जास्-<BR>पति, इस्, m. (जास् gen. fr. जा ?), the father or head of<BR>a family or house.<BR>—जास्पत्य, अम्, n., Ved. the state<BR>or condition of the father of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांहगिरि
जांहगिरि जांहगिरि, इस्, m. = jahāngīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागत|जागतं
जागत जागत, अस्, ई, अम्, composed in the<BR>Jagatī metre, consisting of it, conforming to it;<BR>chiefly praised in the Jagatī metre (each deity having<BR>his own peculiar metre); (अम्), n. the Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागुड|जागुडं|जागुडः
जागुड जागुड, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of their country, renowned for its<BR>saffron; (अम्), n. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृ
जागृ जागृ, cl. 2. P. जागर्ति, जजागार or<BR>जागराञ्-चकार, जागरिष्यति, जागरि-<BR>तुम्, to be awake, to watch, be watchful, attentive,<BR>intent; to foresee, provide; to sit up during the<BR>night: Caus. जागरयति, Aor. Ved. 2nd and 3rd sing.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">Page0343-c+ 76</a>]<BR>अजीगर्, 2nd du. जिगृतम्, 2nd pl. जिगृत, to awaken:<BR>Desid. जिजागरिषति; [cf. Gr. ἐγείρω; Lat. vigil,<BR>vigilo; Old Germ. wachar, wachem; Goth. waka.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर|जागरः
जागर, अस्, आ, m. f. waking, wakefulness, vigilance;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), waking, awake; (अस्), m. a vision in a<BR>waking state; = जगर, mail, armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरक
जागरक, अस्, m. waking, awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरण|जागरणं
जागरण, अस्, आ, अम्, waking, remaining awake;<BR>(अम्), n. waking, watchfulness; keeping watch, sit-<BR>ting up at night as part of a religious ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरित
जागरित, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has been long awake<BR>or is exhausted with sleeplessness; (अम्), n. waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरितृ
जागरितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, wakeful, awake, vigilant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरिन्
जागरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wakeful, awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरिष्णु
जागरिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, very wakeful or sleepless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरूक|जागरूकः
जागरूक, अस्, आ, अम्, wakeful, waking, sleepless,<BR>watchful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्तव्य
जागर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be awake or awaked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्ति|जागर्तिः|जागर्त्ति|जागर्त्तिः
जागर्ति, इस्, f. waking, vigilance; keeping watch,<BR>watchfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्या|जागर्य्या
जागर्या, f. wakefulness, waking, watching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृतव्य
जागृतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be awake. See जा-<BR>गर्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृवि|जागृविः
जागृवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. watchful, attentive; awake;<BR>not extinguished, clear, bright (as fire); active, ani-<BR>mating, exciting; (इस्), m. fire or its deity; a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रत्
जाग्रत्, अत्, अती, अत्, watching, being awake.<BR>—जा-<BR>ग्रत्-स्वप्न, औ, m. du. a state of waking and sleep;<BR>(अस्), m. Ved. dreaming in a waking state, day-dream,<BR>hallucination; (अस्, आ, अम्), occurring in a state of<BR>waking and sleep (?).<BR>—जाग्रद्-अवस्था or जाग्रद्-<BR>दशा, f. a state of wakefulness.<BR>—जाग्रद्-दुःष्वप्-<BR>न्य, अम्, n., Ved. a disagreeable dream or vision<BR>while in a waking state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रिया
जाग्रिया, f. waking, watching, wakefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाघनी
जाघनी जाघनी, f. (fr. जघन), a tail;<BR>the thigh, leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गल|जांगल|जाङ्गलं|जाङ्गलः
जाङ्गल जाङ्गल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जङ्गल),<BR>arid; sparingly grown with trees &c. but nevertheless<BR>fertile; rural, picturesque, diversified with hill, vale,<BR>wood, and water; found or existing in such a district;<BR>desert, covered with jungle; wild, not tame (as an<BR>animal &c.); savage, barbarous; (अस्), m. the franco-<BR>line partridge; N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (ई), f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus; (अम्), n.<BR>flesh; game, the flesh of deer &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गलि|जांगलिः|जाङ्गलिः
जाङ्गलि, इस्, m. a snake-catcher; [cf. जाङ्गुलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गलिक|जांगलिकः|जाङ्गलिकः
जाङ्गलिक, अस्, m. a snake-charmer, = जङ्गुलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुल|जांगुल|जांगुलं|जाङ्गुलं
जाङ्गुल, अम्, n. poison, venom, = जङ्गुल; the<BR>fruit of the Jālinī, a kind of cucumber; (ई), f.<BR>knowledge of poisons, the possession of charms or<BR>drugs and employment of them as antidotes; a pot-<BR>herb, Luffa Acutangula; an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलि|जांगुलि|जांगुलिः|जाङ्गुलिः
जाङ्गुलि, इस्, m. a snake-catcher, a dealer in anti-<BR>dotes, a conjuror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलिक|जांगुलिक|जांगुलिकः|जाङ्गुलिकः
जाङ्गुलिक, अस्, m. a snake-catcher, a snake-doctor,<BR>one who pretends by charms to cure the bite of snakes<BR>or other venomous animals, a dealer in antidotes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घनी
जाङ्घनी जाङ्घनी, f. (fr. जङ्घा), the thigh;<BR>(perhaps a wrong form for जाघनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घाप्रहतिक
जाङ्घाप्रहतिक or जाङ्घाप्रहृतिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. जङ्घा-प्रहत or -प्रहृत), produced<BR>by a blow with the leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घालायन
जाङ्घालायन, अस्, m. (fr. जङ्घाल), N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घि
जाङ्घि, a patronymic from Jaṅgha or metronymic<BR>from Jaṅghā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घिक|जांघिक|जाङ्घिकः
जाङ्घिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जङ्घा), swift of foot,<BR>a courier; relating to or belonging to the leg; (अस्),<BR>m. a courier, a running footman, an express; a<BR>camel; a kind of antelope; [cf. कपि-जाङ्घिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजनाग
जाजनाग जाजनाग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजमत्
जाजमत् जाजमत्, अत्, अती, अत् (fr. Intens. of<BR>1. जम्, p. 339), excessively or repeatedly devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजल
जाजल जाजल, आस्, and जाजलिन्, इनस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a school of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजलि
जाजलि जाजलि, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0343-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजिन्
जाजिन् जाजिन्, ई, m. a warrior, a combatant;<BR>[cf. जज् and जज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाज्वल्यमान|जाज्वल्यमानः
जाज्वल्यमान जाज्वल्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>Intens. of rt. ज्वल्), shining, flaming, blazing, re-<BR>splendent, effulgent, dazzling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटलि|जाटलिः
जाटलि जाटलि, इस्, ई, m. f. the plant Big-<BR>nonia Suaveolens; (other readings have पाटलि and<BR>झाटलि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटालिका
जाटालिका जाटालिका, f. (fr. जटाल or जटा-<BR>लक), N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटिकायन
जाटिकायन जाटिकायन, अस्, m. (fr. जटिक),<BR>N. of the author of a hymn of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाठर|जाठरः
जाठर जाठर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जठर),<BR>stomachic, abdominal, visceral, being in the stomach<BR>or belly, relating to it, relating to the womb, e. g.<BR>जाठरोऽग्निः, the fire in the stomach, the digestive<BR>faculty, gastric juice, hunger; (अस्), m. ‘offspring of<BR>the womb,’ a child; N. of an attendant of Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाठर्य|जाठर्य्य
जाठर्य, अम्, n. morbid affection of the abdomen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्य|जाड्यं
जाड्य जाड्य, अम्, n. (fr. जड), coldness,<BR>frigidity; stiffness, inactivity, apathy, sluggishness, in-<BR>sensibility; absence of feeling in the tongue, taste-<BR>lessness; dulness or coldness of intellect, stupidity,<BR>folly.<BR>—जाड्यारि (˚य-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of cold-<BR>ness,’ the citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात|जातं|जातः
जात जात, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. जन्), born,<BR>brought into existence, brought forth, engendered<BR>(e. g. मास-जात, born a month ago, one month<BR>old; पुत्रो-जातः, a son only by birth, not by quali-<BR>ties); grown, produced, arisen, caused, occasioned,<BR>appearing, appeared, apparent, manifest; happened;<BR>become, present; ready at hand, collected, stored up,<BR>possessed, felt, experienced, inspired, with, affected<BR>by, (often at the beginning of an adjective compound,<BR>see examples below; also at the end of a comp., e. g.<BR>पुत्र-जात, having a son born; श्मश्रु-जात, having<BR>a beard; दन्त-जात, having teeth just growing);<BR>(अस्), m. male issue, a son; a living being (used of<BR>men and gods, but especially of the former); (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a race of the Haihayas; (आ), f. female<BR>offspring, a daughter; जाते, O daughter! (अम्), n.<BR>a living being, a creature; birth, production, origin;<BR>race, kind, sort, class, species; a multitude or collec-<BR>tion of things forming a class (e. g. कर्म-जातम्,<BR>the whole aggregate of actions; सुख-जातम्,<BR>everything included under the name pleasure); in-<BR>dividuality, specific condition; [cf. Gr. γετος; Germ.<BR>Kind; Lith. gentis.]<BR>—जात-कर्मन्, अ, n. a<BR>ceremony at the birth of a child when the navel<BR>string is divided, (it consists in touching the infant's<BR>tongue thrice with ghee after appropriate prayers);<BR>delivery of a new-born infant.<BR>—जात-कलाप, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having a tail (as a peacock).<BR>—जात-काम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fallen in love.<BR>—जात-कोप or जात-क्रो-<BR>ध, अस्, आ, अम्, enraged.<BR>—जात-कौतुक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, delighted.<BR>—जात-कौतूहल, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>eagerly desirous.<BR>—जात-क्षोभ, अस्, आ, अम्, agitated.<BR>—जात-दन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, (a child) that has a tooth<BR>or teeth growing; having teeth.<BR>—जात-पक्ष, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, whose wings have grown, possessing wings.<BR>—जात-पाश, अस्, आ, अम्, having fetters, fettered.<BR>—जात-पुत्रा, f. a woman who has borne a son or<BR>sons.<BR>—जात-प्रत्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, inspired with<BR>confidence, confiding, believing.<BR>—जात-बल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, possessing strength, strong.<BR>—जात-भी, ईस्, f.<BR>‘fearful,’ N. of a woman.<BR>—जात-मन्मथ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being in love, fallen in love, loving.<BR>—जात-मात्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, just born, merely born; (अम्), n. as soon<BR>as born, the instant of birth.<BR>—जात-रजस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, having the catamenia.<BR>—जात-रस, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having taste or flavour.<BR>—जात-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>embodied, having assumed a shape or form, beautiful,<BR>brilliant, golden (?); (अम्), n. the form in which a<BR>person is born, nakedness; gold; the thorn-apple.<BR>—जातरूप-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, quite naked.<BR>—जा-<BR>तरूप-परिष्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned with gold.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-b" target="_blank">Page0344-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—जातरूप-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, golden.<BR>—जातरूप-<BR>शिल, अस्, m., N. of a golden mountain.<BR>—जात-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, containing the word जात or any other<BR>form derived from जन्.<BR>—जात-वास-गृह, अम्, n.<BR>the room in which a child is born, the room of a<BR>lying-in woman.<BR>—जात-विद्या, f., Ved. a know-<BR>ledge of what exists or of the origin and nature of<BR>all things.<BR>—जात-विभ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, flurried,<BR>precipitate.<BR>—जात-विश्वास, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>confidence excited.<BR>—जात-वेदस्, आस्, m., Ved. an<BR>epithet of Agni; (the meaning is explained in five<BR>ways: 1. ‘knowing all created beings;’ 2. ‘possess-<BR>ing all creatures or everything existent;’ 3. ‘known<BR>by created beings;’ 4. ‘possessing वेदस् = riches;’<BR>5. ‘possessing वेदस् = wisdom:’ other derivations<BR>and explanations are found in the Brāhmaṇas, but the<BR>exact sense of this word seems to have been very<BR>early lost, and of the five explanations given above<BR>only the first two would seem to be admissible for<BR>the Vedic texts; in one passage a form जात-वेद<BR>seems to occur.)<BR>—जातवेदस, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>Jāta-vedas; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—जातवेद-<BR>सीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to Jāta-vedas.<BR>—जात-वेपथु, उस्, उस्, उ, affected with tremor.<BR>—जात-वेश्मन्, अ, n. the room in which a child is<BR>born, the room of a lying-in woman.<BR>—जात-श्मश्रु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, one whose beard has grown.<BR>—जात-श्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, wearied, exhausted.<BR>—जात-संवृद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, born and grown up.<BR>—जात-सङ्कल्प,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, feeling a desire or passion for.<BR>—जात-<BR>साध्वस, अस्, आ, अम्, afraid.<BR>—जात-सेन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—जातसेन्य, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from the last.<BR>—जात-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, enamoured,<BR>feeling love or affection for.<BR>—जात-स्पृह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, desirous, wishing for.<BR>—जात-हर्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, rejoiced, glad.<BR>—जात-हार्द, अस्, ई, अम्, feeling<BR>affection, becoming attached.<BR>—जातागस् (˚त-आग्˚),<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, offending, sinning, committing fault; also<BR>जातापराध, जात-दोष, &c.<BR>—जातापत्या (˚त-<BR>अप्˚), f. a mother, a woman who has borne a child.<BR>—जातामर्ष (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>anger roused, vexed, enraged, put in a passion.<BR>—जाताश्रु (˚त-अश्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, weeping, shedding<BR>tears.<BR>—जातेष्टि (˚त-इष्˚), इस्, f. rites or sacrifice<BR>performed at the birth of a child.<BR>—जातोक्ष (˚त-<BR>उक्˚), अस्, m. a young bullock, an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातक|जातकं|जातकः
जातक, अस्, आ, अम्, born, produced; (अस्), m. a<BR>new-born child; a mendicant; (अम्), n. = जात-<BR>कर्मन्, a ceremony performed after the birth of a<BR>child; nativity, astrological calculation of a nativity;<BR>(with Buddhists) a former birth of Śākya-muni and<BR>its history; an aggregate or a collection of similar<BR>things; [cf. चतुर्-जातक.]<BR>—जातक-ध्वनि, इस्,<BR>m. a leech.<BR>—जातक-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work<BR>on nativities by Ananta; another work by Keśava.<BR>—जातक-मुक्तावली, f. title of an astrological<BR>work by Śiva-dāsa.<BR>—जातकाम्भोनिधि (˚क-अम्˚),<BR>इस्, m. title of an astrological work by Bhadra-bāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातायन
जातायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Jāta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाति|जातिः
जाति, इस्, f. birth, production; the form of existence,<BR>whether as a man or animal, which is fixed by birth;<BR>position assigned by birth; rank; family, race, lineage;<BR>kind, sort, genus, species, class, tribe, caste; the cha-<BR>racter or peculiarities of a species, the genuine or<BR>true state of anything; reduction of fractions to a<BR>common denominator; false generalization; a futile<BR>answer, a self-confuting reply; a particular figure of<BR>speech in rhetoric; a class of metres; a manner of<BR>singing; a fire-place; N. of several plants, = Jas-<BR>minum Grandiflorum; Emblica Officinalis; mace,<BR>nutmeg; [cf. अन्त्य-जाति, एक-जाति, द्वि-जाति; cf. also<BR>Lat. gens; Lith. pri-gentis.]<BR>—जाति-कोश or जाति-<BR>कोष or जाती-कोश, अम्, n. a nutmeg; (ई), f. the<BR>outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR>—जाति-त्व, अम्, n. or<BR>जाति-ता, f. distinction or nature of caste or tribe;<BR>special or generic property.<BR>—जाति-धर्म, अस्, m.<BR>the duty of caste, the law or usage of caste (e. g.<BR>sacred study is the caste-duty of the Brāhman, fight-<BR>ing of the Kṣatriya, &c.); generic or specific<BR>property.<BR>—जाति-ध्वंस, अस्, m. the loss of caste<BR>or its privileges.<BR>—जातिन्-धर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">Page0344-c+ 77</a>]<BR>physician, = Śuddhodana in a former birth.<BR>—जाति-<BR>पत्त्री or जाती-पत्त्री, f. the outer skin of the nut-<BR>meg.<BR>—जाति-फल or जाती-फल, अम्, n. a nutmeg;<BR>[cf. क्षुद्रजाती-फल.]<BR>—जाति-ब्राह्मण, अस्, m.<BR>a Brāhman by birth but not by knowledge.<BR>—जाति-<BR>भ्रंश, अस्, m. loss of rank or caste.<BR>—जाति-<BR>भ्रंश-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing loss of caste;<BR>forbidden, improper; (अम्), n. doing an act pro-<BR>hibited to a particular caste.<BR>—जाति-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fallen from caste, outcast.<BR>—जाति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>of high rank, obtaining a high position.<BR>—जाति-मह,<BR>अस्, m. birthday-festival.<BR>—जाति-मात्र, अम्, n. mere<BR>birth, position in life obtained by mere birth; caste<BR>only, but not the performance of the especial duties;<BR>species, genus.<BR>—जातिमात्रोपजीविन् (˚र-उप्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, or जातिमात्र-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, (a Brāhman)<BR>who lives only by his caste (without any sacerdotal<BR>acts).<BR>—जाति-माला, f. ‘garland of the castes,’ title<BR>of a work treating of the different castes.<BR>—जाति-<BR>लक्षण, अम्, n. specific or generic distinction,<BR>characteristic, mark of tribe or caste.<BR>—जाति-वचन,<BR>अम्, n. the idea of species or genus.<BR>—जाति-वाचक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, expressing genus, generic (as a name).<BR>—जाति-विवेक, अस्, m. title of a literary work.<BR>—जाति-वैर, अम्, n. natural enmity, innate or<BR>instinctive hostility.<BR>—जाति-वैलक्षण्य, अम्, n.<BR>inconsistency, incompatibility, conduct or quality at<BR>variance with birth or tribe.<BR>—जाति-शब्द, अस्, m. a<BR>word expressing the idea of species or genus.<BR>—जाति-<BR>सम्पन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from a good family,<BR>belonging to a noble family.<BR>—जाति-सार, अस्, m.<BR>nutmeg.<BR>—जाति-स्मर, अस्, आ, अम्, recollecting a<BR>former existence, remembering one's condition in a<BR>former life; N. of a Tirtha.<BR>—जाति-स्मरण, अम्,<BR>n. recollection of a former existence.<BR>—जाति-स्व-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. specific or generic character or nature.<BR>—जाति-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, of low birth or descent,<BR>void of caste, outcast, having a low position.<BR>—जाती-<BR>रस, अस्, m. gum myrrh.<BR>—जात्य्-अन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>blind from birth, born blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीय|जातीयः
जातीय, अस्, आ, अम् (used at the end of a compound<BR>and by native grammarians considered as an affix),<BR>relating or belonging to any species, genus, tribe,<BR>order, family, race, &c. (e. g. अश्व-जातीय, belonging<BR>to the horse-kind; वृक्ष-जातीय, belonging to<BR>trees); [cf. वि-जातीय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीयक
जातीयक, अस्, आ, अम्, = जातीय; (e. g. एवं-जाती-<BR>यक, of such a kind, of such a tribe or race.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्य|जात्यः
जात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a family or caste;<BR>of the same family, related; sprung from a noble<BR>family, noble; well-born, legitimate, born of parents<BR>of the same caste, genuine (γνήσιος); best, excellent;<BR>pleasing, beautiful; (in mathematics) rectangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूप|जातरूपं
जातरूप जात-रूप. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाति|जातिः
जाति जाति. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातु
जातु जातु, ind. (fr. जन् ?; cf. जनुषा under<BR>जनुस्), at all, ever; possibly, perhaps; sometimes,<BR>some day, once, once upon a time (e. g. किं तेन<BR>जातु जातेन, what is the use at all of him born ?).<BR>जातु is said to be used in connection with the<BR>potential in the sense of ‘not allowing’ (e. g. जातु<BR>वृषलं याजयेन् न मर्षयामि, I suffer not<BR>that he should cause an outcast to sacrifice), or with<BR>a present indicative to express censure (e. g. जातु<BR>याजयति वृषलम्, ought he to cause an outcast<BR>to sacrifice ?). In the Veda when जातु stands at the<BR>beginning of a sentence the verb which follows re-<BR>tains its accent. न जातु, not at all, by no means,<BR>never; अपि जातु, perhaps, possibly; जातु-चित्, at<BR>some time or other, some day, one day.<BR>—जातू-<BR>ष्ठिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. eminently strong; (Sāy.)<BR>always strong; or (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुक|जातुकं
जातुक जातुक, the plant from which the<BR>Asa Fœtida is obtained; (अम्), n. Asa Fœtida; [cf.<BR>जतुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुधान|जातुधानः
जातुधान जातुधान, अस्, m. = यातु-धान,<BR>a Rākṣasa, an imp, ogre or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0344-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुष|जातुषं
जातुष जातुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जतु), made of<BR>lac or gum, covered with lac or with any artificial<BR>form or condition of it; sticky, adhesive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातू
जातू जातू, Ved. (Sāy.) = अशनि, a thunder-<BR>bolt.<BR>—जातू-भर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. (Sāy.) armed<BR>with the thunderbolt or nourishing created beings;<BR>[cf. जातू and जात.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूकर्ण|जातूकर्णः
जातूकर्ण जातूकर्ण, अस्, m. (fr. जतू-कर्ण ?),<BR>N. of an ancient preceptor; N. of a physician; and<BR>of the author of a law-book; an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूकर्ण्य
जातूकर्ण्य, अस्, m., N. of several preceptors and<BR>grammarians; N. of the author of a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जान|जानं
जान जान, अम्, n. (fr. rt. जन्), Ved. pro-<BR>duction, birth, origin, birthplace; (अस्), m. a patro-<BR>nymic of Vṛśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानक
जानक, अस्, m. (fr. जनक), a patronymic of<BR>Kratu-vid; also of Āya-sthūṇa; (ई), f. a patronymic<BR>of Sītā, the wife of Rāma; N. of a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of twenty-four syllables each.<BR>—जानकी-<BR>नाथ or जानकीश (˚की-ईश), अस्, m. the husband<BR>of Sītā, i. e. Rāma.<BR>—जानकीनाथ-शर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—जानकी-राघव, अम्, n. title of a<BR>play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानकि
जानकि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Kratu-jit; also of<BR>Āya-sthūṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानन्तपि|जानंतपि|जानंतपिः
जानन्तपि, इस्, m. (fr. जनन्-तप), a patronymic<BR>of Aty-arāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपद|जानपदः
जानपद, अस्, m. (fr. जन-पद), one who be-<BR>longs to a country, a subject; (अस्, ई, अम्), living in<BR>the country, an inhabitant of the country (opposed<BR>to पौर, inhabiting a town); a peasant, rustic, be-<BR>longing to or suited for the inhabitants of the<BR>country; (आ), f. a popular expression; N. of a place;<BR>N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदिक
जानपदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a country or<BR>to the subjects of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानराज्य
जानराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. जन-राजन्), Ved. sove-<BR>reignty, supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानवादिक
जानवादिक or जानेवादिक or जानोवादिक, अस्,<BR>ई, अम् (fr. जन-वाद, जने-वाद, and जनो-वाद),<BR>knowing the popular report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानश्रुति|जानश्रुतिः
जानश्रुति, इस्, m. a patronymic from Jana-śruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानश्रुतेय
जानश्रुतेय, अस्, m. (fr. जन-श्रुता or जान-<BR>श्रुति), a patronymic of Aupāvi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानायन
जानायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Jana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानार्दन
जानार्दन, अस्, m. (fr. जनार्दन), a patronymic<BR>of Pra-dyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुक
1. जानुक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. जन्), bringing forth.<BR>(For 2. जानुक see under जानु below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानत्
जानत् जानत्, अन्, अती, अत् (fr. rt. 1. ज्ञा),<BR>knowing, understanding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानन्ति
जानन्ति, इस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानान
जानान, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानि
जानि जानि (at the end of an adj. comp. =<BR>जनि or जान for जाया), a wife (e. g. अनन्य-जानि,<BR>having no other wife); [cf. अ-जानि, अरुन्धती-ज्˚,<BR>द्वि-ज्˚, &c.; cf. also Goth. qvêns.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानु
जानु जानु, उस्, उ, m. n. (fr. rt. जन् ?), the<BR>knee; जानुभ्याम् अवनीं गम्, to fall to the ground<BR>on one's knees; [cf. Lat. genu; Gr. γόνυ; Goth.<BR>kniu; Germ. Knie; Hib. glun (?); Slav. koljeno;<BR>Lith. kiélis.]<BR>—जानु-जङ्घ, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—जानु-दघ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, up to the knees.<BR>—जा-<BR>नुप्रहृतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, produced by a blow with<BR>the knee; [cf. जाङ्घाप्रहृतिक.]<BR>—जानु-फ-<BR>लक or जानु-मण्डल, अम्, n. the knee-pan or<BR>patella.<BR>—जानु-विजानु, उ, n. contracting and ex-<BR>tending the knees, a peculiar position in fighting.<BR>—जानु-सन्धि, इस्, m. the knee-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुक
2. जानुक, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of an adj. comp.<BR>= जानु, the knee (e. g. ऊर्ध्व-जानुक, having the<BR>knees raised).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानेवादिक
जानेवादिक जानेवादिक. See जानवादिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जान्धित|जांधित
जान्धित जान्धित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. जन and<BR>धित = हित ?), Ved. ‘agreed upon by men,’ custom-<BR>ary, usual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जान्य
जान्य जान्य, अस्, m. (fr. जानि ?), N. of an<BR>ancient sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप|जापः
जाप जाप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. जप्), muttering,<BR>whispering, muttering prayers or telling beads, reciting<BR>passages of the Vedas &c. inaudibly; a prayer uttered<BR>in this manner; [cf. कर्ण-जाप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापक|जापकः
जापक, अस्, इका, अम्, muttering prayers, one who<BR>mutters prayers; relating to a muttered prayer;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of fragrant wood; (a various reading<BR>has जायक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापिन्
जापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of an adj. comp.) re-<BR>citing in a low voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप्य
जाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be muttered, to be repeated<BR>in a low voice; (अम्), n. a prayer to be muttered<BR>inaudibly, the muttering of prayers &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापन|जापनं
जापन जापन, अम्, n. (a Prākṛt form for<BR>यापन), declining, rejection, dissent; dismissing,<BR>sending away; completing, finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबाल|जाबालः
जाबाल 1. जाबाल, अस्, m. (fr. जबाला), a<BR>metronymic of Mahā-śāla; also of Satya-kāma; the<BR>author of a law-book; also of a medicinal work;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a school of the Yajur-veda.<BR>—जा-<BR>बालोपनिषद् (˚ल-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad<BR>belonging to the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालायन
जाबालायन, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालि|जाबालिः
जाबालि, इस्, m., N. of an ancient sage; also of the<BR>author of a law-book; N. of an infidel Brāhman who<BR>was one of the priests of king Daśa-ratha and after<BR>his death tried ineffectually to shake the resolution<BR>of Rāma and induce him to take the throne offered<BR>to him by his dutiful younger brother Bharata; (his<BR>speech, which is given in Rāmāyaṇa II. 108, con-<BR>tains doctrines very similar to those of the Cārvākas<BR>or materialists.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालिन्
जाबालिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबाल|जाबालः
जाबाल 2. जाबाल, अस्, m. (a corruption of<BR>अजा-पाल), a goat-herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न
जामदग्न जामदग्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जमद्-<BR>अग्नि), derived from or produced by Jamad-agni;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Catur-aha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्निय
जामदग्निय and जामदग्नेय, a patronymic<BR>from Jamad-agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्य|जामदग्न्यः
जामदग्न्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Jamad-<BR>agni or to his son Jāmadagnya; a patronymic; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a Catur-aha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामर्य
जामर्य जामर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (Sāy.) from<BR>जा-अमर्य, making creatures immortal; but per-<BR>haps connected with a rt. जम् for चम् and used as<BR>an epithet of milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामल|जामलः
जामल जामल = यामल in कृष्ण-जामल<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामा
जामा जामा, f. (fr. rt. जन्), a daughter-<BR>in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जा-मातृ, ता, m. (‘the maker of [new] offspring,’<BR>or perhaps related to जामि below), a daughter's<BR>husband, a son-in-law; a husband, a lord or master;<BR>a friend; the sunflower, Heliantus Annuus; [cf.<BR>यामातृ; cf. also Lat. gener (?); Gr. γάμβρος.]<BR>—जामातृ-त्व, अम्, n. the relationship of a<BR>daughter's husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृक|जामातृकः
जामातृक, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or belonging<BR>to a daughter's husband; (अस्), m. a daughter's<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. related by blood, con-<BR>sanguineous, (rarely applied to a brother but often to<BR>a sister either with or without the word स्वसृ); re-<BR>lated like brother and sister; (in Vedic language the<BR>fingers are sometimes called जामयः or ‘the sisters;’<BR>the सप्त जामयः or ‘seven sisters’ are the seven<BR>Dhītayas or acts of devotion in the Soma wor-<BR>ship); related in general, belonging to, peculiar<BR>to, customary, usual; (इस्), f. a sister, a virtuous and<BR>respectable woman; (more properly) a female rela-<BR>tive of the head of a family, a daughter-in-law; N.<BR>of a deity; N. of an Apsaras; (ई), n. blood-relation-<BR>ship, consanguinity, the relation of brother and sister,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">Page0345-c+ 73</a>]<BR>relation in general, descent; (in grammar and in the<BR>sacrificial language) tautology, repetition; water;<BR>[cf. अ-जामि and देव-ज्˚.]<BR>—जामि-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>creating relationship.<BR>—जामि-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. con-<BR>sanguinity, relationship.<BR>—जामि-वत्, ind., Ved. like<BR>a sister or brother.<BR>—जामि-शंस, अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>curse pronounced by a brother or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामेय|जामेयः
जामेय, अस्, m. a sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामित्र|जामित्रं
जामित्र जामित्र, अम्, n. (fr. the Gr. διάμετρον,<BR>in astronomy) the seventh lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बव|जांबव|जांबवं|जाम्बवं
जाम्बव जाम्बव, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from or<BR>belonging to the Jambū tree; (अस्), m. = जाम्बवत्,<BR>q. v.; (ई), f., N. of a plant, = नाग-दमनी; (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of the Jambū tree, the rose-apple; gold;<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—जाम्बवौष्ठ (˚व-ओष्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a cauterizing needle or probe; also जाम्बवोष्ठ,<BR>जाम्बोष्ठ, जाम्बौष्ठ, and जम्ब्व्-ओष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवक
जाम्बवक, अस् or अम् (?), m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवत्|जांबवत्|जाम्बवन्त्
जाम्बवत्, आन्, m. (for जाम्बव-वत् ?), N. of the<BR>chief of the bears who, with the monkeys, was an ally<BR>of Rāma and therefore sometimes called a monkey;<BR>he was a son of Pitāmaha and father of Jāmbavatī<BR>who was wife of Kṛṣṇa and mother of Śāmba; (ती),<BR>f., N. of the daughter of Jāmbavat, wife of Kṛṣṇa<BR>and mother of Śāmba; N. of a plant, = जम्बू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बुवत्|जाम्बुवन्त्
जाम्बुवत्, आन्, m. = जाम्बवत्; (ती), f. = जाम्ब-<BR>वती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बीर|जांबीर|जांबीरं
जाम्बीर जाम्बीर, अम्, n. (fr. जम्बीर), a<BR>citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बील|जांबील|जांबीलं
जाम्बील जाम्बील, अस्, m., Ved. the knee-<BR>bone, knee-pan; (said by some to be so called from<BR>its similarity to a citron, by others considered as<BR>a corruption fr. जानु and बिल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बुक
जाम्बुक जाम्बुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जम्बुक),<BR>coming from or belonging to a jackal; जाम्बुकं<BR>वचस्, a jackal's cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूनद|जांबूनद|जांबूनदं|जाम्बूनदं
जाम्बूनद जाम्बूनद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जम्बू-<BR>नदी), coming from or belonging to the river<BR>Jambū, epithet of a kind of gold; made of the<BR>gold called Jāmbūnada, golden; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a son of Janam-ejaya; N. of a mountain; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a river; (अम्), n. gold from the Jambū.<BR>river, any gold, a golden ornament; N. of a lake;<BR>the thorn-apple.<BR>—जाम्बूनद-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of the gold called Jāmbūnada, golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्भ
जाम्भ जाम्भ, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Jambha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायक|जायकं
जायक जायक, अम्, n. a kind of yellow<BR>fragrant wood; [cf. जापक and जाषक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायद्रथ
जायद्रथ जायद्रथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जयद्-<BR>रथ), belonging to Jayad-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायन्तीपुत्र
जायन्ती-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायन्तेय|जायन्तेयः
जायन्तेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Jayantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायमान
जायमान जायमान. See p. 338. col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया जाया, f. (fr. rt. जन्, to bring forth;<BR>cf. Manu IX. 8), a wife, one wedded lawfully or<BR>according to the ritual, a consort; (in astronomy) N.<BR>of the seventh mansion.<BR>—जाया-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>a wife-murderer; (अस्), m. a mole or mark on the<BR>body indicative of the death of a wife.<BR>—जायाजीव<BR>(˚या-आज्˚), अस्, m. a dancer, an actor (who gets a liveli-<BR>hood by his wife).<BR>—जाया-त्व, अम्, n. the character<BR>or attributes of a wife.<BR>—जायानुजीविन् (˚या-अन्˚), ई,<BR>m. an actor, a dancer, a mime; the husband of a<BR>harlot; a needy man, a pauper; a kind of crane,<BR>the Vaka or Ardea Nivea.<BR>—जाया-पति, ई, m. du.<BR>husband and wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायान्य
जायान्य जायान्य, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>disease; [cf. जायेन्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायिन्
जायिन् जायिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. rt. 1. जि), conquer-<BR>ing, subduing; (ई), m. a stanza repeated, the burden<BR>of a song; [cf. ध्रुवक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0345-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायु|जायुः
जायु, उस्, उस्, उ, victorious, striving to conquer or<BR>gain; (उस्), m. a medicine, medicament; a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायेन्य
जायेन्य जायेन्य, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>disease; [cf. जायान्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार|जारः
जार जार, जारक, &c. See p. 350, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारुधि
जारुधि जारुधि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारूथी
जारूथी जारूथी, f., N. of a river (?); [cf.<BR>जरूथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारूथ्य
जारूथ्य जारूथ्य or जारुथ्य. This word<BR>is generally found connected with अश्व-मेध, the<BR>horse sacrifice, but the meaning is doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारुत्थ
जारुत्थ, अस्, m. (is said to mean) a sacrifice in<BR>which three offerings are made, or in which the sun<BR>is thrice worshipped in his southern declination (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार्तिक
जार्तिक जार्तिक, आस्, m. pl. a various read-<BR>ing for जर्तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार्य
जार्य जार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to<BR>Sāy.) ‘to be praised’ (as if fr. 3. जॄ); but perhaps<BR>rather (अम्), n. familiarity, intimacy, (fr. जार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार्यक
जार्यक जार्यक, अस्, m. a particular animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल|जालं|जालः
जाल जाल, अम्, n. (fr. rt. जल् and connected<BR>with 1. जाल), a net (for catching birds &c.); a web, a<BR>spider's web, cobweb, net-work, any reticulated or<BR>woven texture, a wire net, reticulated or chain-armour,<BR>a coat of mail, a helmet made of wire; a lattice, an<BR>eyelet or loophole, a window; a collection, multitude,<BR>assemblage; the membrane which unites the toes of<BR>many water-birds; the membrance between the fingers<BR>and toes of divine beings and godlike or heroic per-<BR>sonages; a disease of the eyes in which the blood-<BR>vessels are filled with blood and look like net-work;<BR>an unblown flower; magic; conjuring, illusion, de-<BR>ception; pride, arrogance; (wrong reading for जात),<BR>kind; (अस्), m. the tree Nauclea Cadamba, the young<BR>fruit of a gourd or cucumber; (ई), f. a small cucumber,<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca, any medicament or drug.<BR>—जाल-कर्मन्, अ, n. the occupation of catching<BR>fish, fishing.<BR>—जाल-कारक, अस्, m. a web-maker,<BR>a spider, a net-maker.<BR>—जाल-कीट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an Udīcya-grāma.<BR>—जाल-क्षीर्य, अम्, n. a kind<BR>of plant containing a poisonous juice.<BR>—जाल-गर्-<BR>दभ, अस्, m. a kind of pimple or boil; [cf. गर्-<BR>दभ-गद, &c.]<BR>—जाल-गोणिका, f. a kind of<BR>churning-vessel.<BR>—जाल-दण्ड, अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>pole of a net.<BR>—जाल-पदी, f., N. of a place.<BR>—जाल-<BR>पाद्, त्, m. a goose (‘web-foot’).<BR>—जाल-पाद, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, having a web-like membrane between the<BR>toes, web-footed; (अस्), m. a web-footed bird; N.<BR>of a frog; of a magician.<BR>—जाल-प्राया, f. armour,<BR>iron net-work, chain-armour.<BR>—जाल-बद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, caught in a net, snared.<BR>—जाल-भुज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the rudiments of a web-like membrane<BR>between the fingers.<BR>—जाल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, fur-<BR>nished with a net or net-like texture, reticulated;<BR>covered with iron net work or retiform armour; (ac-<BR>cording to some) cunning, deceptive.<BR>—जाल-वर्-<BR>वूरक, अस्, m., N. of a plant, a kind of Varvūra.<BR>—जालाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), अम्, n. (?) a loophole, eye-<BR>lethole, window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालक|जालकं|जालकः
जालक, अम्, n. a net, woven texture, web; mul-<BR>titude, assemblage; a lattice; an eyelet or loophole;<BR>a nest; a collection or bundle of buds, a germ, an<BR>unblown flower; a plantain, the fruit; illusion; pride;<BR>(अस्), m. a window, a lattice, a loop or eyelethole;<BR>N. of a tree; (इका), f. a net (for catching birds &c.);<BR>chain-armour, armour; a spider; a leech; a kind of<BR>cloth or raiment, woollen cloth; plantain; iron; a<BR>widow, (perhaps so called from the net or braid worn<BR>by widows.)<BR>—जालक-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, veiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालाय
जालाय, nom. A. जालायते, to be like a net, to<BR>form a net-like enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिक|जालिकः
जालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who uses nets to gain a<BR>livelihood, a fisherman, a fowler, birdcatcher, any<BR>hunter using nets; (अस्), m. a spider; the president<BR>of a district, governor of a province; a cheat, a<BR>rogue, a vagabond, a conjurer or juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिन्
जालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a net; retiform; having a<BR>window; illusory, deceptive; (इनी), f., scil. पिडका,<BR>a term applied to certain boils or pustules which<BR>make their appearance in the disease called Pra-meha;<BR>a painted room or one ornamented with pictures; =<BR>श्वेत-घोषा, घोषातकी, कोशातकी, a species of<BR>melon or gourd (the rind of which is reticulated like<BR>a net).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्य
जाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to be caught in a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकि
जालकि जालकि, अयस्, m. pl., N. of a sub-<BR>division of the Trigarta people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकीय
जालकीय, अस्, m. a prince of the above people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिनी
जालकिनी जालकिनी, f. a sheep, an ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धर|जालंधर|जालंधरः|जालन्धरः
जालन्धर जालन्धर, अस्, m. (fr. जलन्-<BR>धर), N. of a country situated in the north-west<BR>of India, apparently part of Lahore, and perhaps the<BR>modern Jallindhar or Julinder; (आस्), m. pl. its inha-<BR>bitants.<BR>—जालन्धरोपाख्यान (˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n.<BR>title of an episode of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धरायण|जालंधरायण
जालन्धरायण, a patronymic from Jalan-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धरायणक|जालंधरायणक
जालन्धरायणक, अस्, इका, अम्, inhabited by<BR>the Jālandharāyaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धरि|जालंधरि
जालन्धरि, इस्, m., N. of a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालह्रद
जालह्रद, अस्, m. a patronymic from Jala-hrada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालमानि
जालमानि जालमानि, इस्, m. a patronymic;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl., N. of a subdivision of the Trigarta<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालमानीय
जालमानीय, अस्, m. a prince of the above people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालवाल
जालवाल जालवाल, अस्, m. a kind of fish,<BR>= वादाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालाष|जालाषं
जालाष जालाष, अम्, n. (fr. जलाष), Ved.<BR>a particular drug or anodyne with soothing qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालोर|जालोरः
जालोर जालोर, अस्, m., N. of an Agra-hāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म जाल्म, अस्, ई, अम्, cruel, harsh, severe;<BR>inconsiderate, rash, acting without thinking; (अस्, ई),<BR>m. f. a despised or contemptible person, a rogue; a<BR>wretch, a miscreant, a low man, one of a degraded<BR>tribe or occupation; one who reads or recites badly<BR>(Pāṇ. VI. 2, 158); [cf. Hib. galmha, ‘hardness,<BR>hardihood, rigour, valour.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मक
जाल्मक, अस्, इका, अम्, base, despised, contempti-<BR>ble, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावड
जावड जावड, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf.<BR>भावड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावत्|जावन्त्
जावत् जा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing<BR>offspring, granting offspring; (Sāy.) received by<BR>praiseworthy persons (epithet of the Soma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावन्य|जावन्यं
जावन्य जावन्य, अम्, n. (fr. जवन), quick-<BR>ness, swiftness, rapidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावालि
जावालि जावालि. See जाबालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाषक|जाषकं
जाषक जाषक, अम्, n. (a various reading<BR>for जायक), a kind of yellow fragrant wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाष्कमद|जाष्कमदः
जाष्कमद जाष्कमद, अस्, m., Ved. a par-<BR>ticular species of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जासट
जासट जासट, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जास्पति|जास्पतिः
जास्पति जास्-पति, जास्पत्य. See under<BR>जा at p. 343.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह|जाहं
जाह जाह, अम्, n. (used at the end of a<BR>comp. and considered as an affix), the root or point<BR>of issue of certain parts of the body (e. g. ओष्ठ-<BR>जाह, the point of issue of the lips; cf. अक्षि-ज्˚,<BR>कर्ण-ज्˚, केश-ज्˚, नख-ज्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहक|जाहकः
जाहक जाहक, अस्, m. a kind of animal;<BR>a polecat, a cat; Lemur Tardigradus; a leech; a<BR>bed, a cot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहुष|जाहुषः
जाहुष जाहुष, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man<BR>protected by the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नव
जाह्नव जाह्नव, अस्, m. (fr. जह्नु), a patro-<BR>nymic of Viśvā-mitra; also of Su-ratha; N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">Page0346-c+ 80</a>]<BR>Catur-aha ceremony; (ई), f. the daughter of Jahnu,<BR>an epithet of the river Gaṅgā or Ganges.<BR>—जाह्नवी-<BR>फेन-लेखा, f. a streak of the foam of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवीय
जाह्नवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the river Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि 1. जि, cl. 1. P. A. जयति, -ते, जिगाय,<BR>जिग्ये, जेष्यति, -ते, अजैषीत्, अजेष्ट, जे-<BR>तुम् (Ved. Inf. जेतवे and जिषे), to win or acquire<BR>by conquest (or in gambling), to conquer, defeat,<BR>vanquish, overcome; excel, surpass; to vanquish in<BR>a game or in a suit at law; to convict; to conquer<BR>the passions; overcome a disease &c.; to expel from<BR>(with abl.); to be victorious, to gain the upper hand:<BR>Pass. जीयते: Caus. जापयति, -यितुम्; Aor. अजी-<BR>जपत्, to cause to conquer or win: Pass. of Caus.<BR>जाप्यते, to be made to conquer: Desid. जिगीषति,<BR>to wish to win, obtain, conquer, vanquish or excel<BR>&c., to vie with, emulate; to seek for prey: Intens.<BR>जेजीयते, जेजयीति, जेजेति; [cf. Lith. galu, galybê;<BR>Hib. gar, ‘profit, advantage, gain, good.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय|जयः
जय, अस्, आ, अम्, conquering; (अस्), m. conquest,<BR>see s. v. at p. 339.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
2. जि, इस्, इस्, इ, victorious, conquering, a victor;<BR>(इस्), m. a Piśāca, a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषत्
जिगीषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, wishing or striving to<BR>overcome, emulous, ambitious, a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषमाण
जिगीषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, striving to win.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा, f. desire of gaining or obtaining; desire<BR>of conquering or vanquishing or overpowering;<BR>military ardour; wish to excel, emulation, rivalry;<BR>eminence; usage, profession or habit of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषु
जिगीषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to gain or obtain,<BR>seeking for; striving to conquer or overcome, or to<BR>excel, vying or contending with; (उस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—जिगीषु-ता, f. desire of conquering, emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिग्यु
जिग्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. victorious, triumphant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्
जित्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of a comp.) winning, van-<BR>quishing, conquering, removing (e. g. शत्रु-जित्, van-<BR>quishing enemies); [cf. अनन्त-जित्, अभिमाति-ज्˚,<BR>अश्व-ज्˚, उग्र-ज्˚.] — 1. जित्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, (at end<BR>of comp.) most victorious, first of conquerors; [cf. 2.<BR>जित्तम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित|जितः
जित, अस्, आ, अम्, conquered, vanquished, subdued;<BR>surpassed, overcome, subject to, enslaved by (e. g.<BR>काम-जित, under the dominion of lust); won,<BR>gained, obtained; (अस्), m. one of the attendants<BR>upon a Jina or Jaina saint; (a wrong form for अ-जित.)<BR>—जित-काशि, इस्, m. the fist doubled.<BR>—जित-काशिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, appearing victorious.<BR>—जित-कोप or जित-<BR>क्रोध, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has subdued anger,<BR>imperturbable, not to be roused to wrath.<BR>—जित-<BR>क्लम, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has overcome fatigue.<BR>—जित-नेमि, इस्, m. a staff made of the wood of the<BR>religious fig-tree (carried during the performance of<BR>certain vows).<BR>—जित-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, one who<BR>has subdued his wrath; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—जित-लोक, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has con-<BR>quered heaven, epithet of a class of manes.<BR>—जित-<BR>वती, f., N. of a daughter of Uśīnara.<BR>—जित-व्रत,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Havir-dhāna.<BR>—जित-शत्रु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, one whose enemies are conquered, con-<BR>quering foes, victorious, triumphant; (उस्), m., N. of<BR>a Buddha; the father of A-jita, the second Arhat of<BR>the present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—जित-श्रम, अस्, m. one<BR>who has conquered toil, free from worldly cares, a<BR>stoic.<BR>—जित-स्वर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has con-<BR>quered or won heaven.<BR>—जिताक्षर (˚त-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘one who has mastered the letters,’ reading<BR>well or readily.<BR>—जितात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, self-<BR>subdued, void of passion; (आ), m., N. of one of the<BR>Viśve-devas.<BR>—जितामित्र (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has conquered an enemy, triumphant, victorious;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—जितारि (˚त-अरि),<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, triumphant over an enemy; (इस्), m., N. of<BR>a son of Avikṣit; a Buddha; N. of the father of<BR>Śam-bhava, the third Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—जिताहव (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>won a battle, victorious, triumphant.<BR>—जिताहार<BR>(˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who by abstraction is able<BR>to do without food.<BR>—जितेन्द्रिय (˚त-इन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">Page0347-a+ 72</a>]<BR>अम्, one who has conquered his passions or subdued<BR>the senses, calm, impassive, unmoved; (अस्), m. an<BR>ascetic, a sage; N. of a man.<BR>—जितेन्द्रिय-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. subjugation of the senses or passions.<BR>—जितेन्द्रि-<BR>याह्व (˚य-आह्˚), अस्, m., N. of a plant, = काम-<BR>वृद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0346-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिति|जितिः
जिति, इस्, f. gaining, obtaining, a victory, conquest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्य|जित्यः
जित्य, अस्, आ, अम्, conquerable, vincible; (आ), f.<BR>victory, acquisition, gain; a ploughshare; (अस्), m.<BR>a harrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वन्
जित्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, victorious; (आ), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वर|जित्वरः
जित्वर, अस्, ई, अम्, victorious, triumphant; (ई),<BR>f. ‘Victrix,’ N. of the city Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वा
जित्वा, ind. having conquered or excelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतव्य
जेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be conquered or overcome,<BR>conquerable, vincible; to be surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेय|जेयः
जेय, अस्, आ, अम्, = जेतव्य above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिकण
जिकण जिकण, अस्, m., N. of a lawyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगत्नु|जिगत्नुः
जिगत्नु जिगत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ (reduplicated<BR>form fr. rt. गम्), going quickly, fleet; (उस्), m.<BR>breath, life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषत्
जिगमिषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. Desid. of rt. गम्),<BR>wishing or endeavouring to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषा
जिगमिषा, f. wish to go or move, intention to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषु
जिगमिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to go, intending<BR>or purposing to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगरिषु
जिगरिषु जिगरिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. 2. गॄ), wishing to swallow or devour, desirous of<BR>seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगर्ति|जिगर्त्ति
जिगर्ति, इस्, m., Ved. a swallower, devourer;<BR>swallowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा जिगीषा. See p. 346, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्नु|जिघत्नुः
जिघत्नु जिघत्नु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. हन्), Ved.<BR>endeavouring to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसक|जिघांसकः
जिघांसक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. Desid. of rt. हन्),<BR>wishing or endeavouring to kill, revengeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसा
जिघांसा, f. wish or intention to strike, slay, or<BR>destroy; malice, revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसिन्
जिघांसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, intending to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसीयस्
जिघांसीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of the last),<BR>more intent on slaughter, very desirous of killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसु|जिघांसुः
जिघांसु, उस्, उस्, उ, intending or seeking to kill<BR>or slay, desirous of destroying, malicious, murderous,<BR>revengeful; (उस्), m. an unrelenting foe, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सत्
जिघत्सत् जिघत्सत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. Desid.<BR>of rt. घस्), wishing to eat, hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सा
जिघत्सा, f. desire of eating, hunger, voracity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सु|जिघत्सुः
जिघत्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, hungry, voracious; (उस्), f.<BR>an epithet of evil demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षत्
जिघृक्षत् जिघृक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or जि-<BR>घृक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Desid. of rt. ग्रह्),<BR>wishing or intending to take or seize, greedy,<BR>avaricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षा
जिघृक्षा, f. wish or intention to take or seize,<BR>greediness, covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षु
जिघृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or intending to<BR>take or seize, covetous, avaricious; wishing to rob or<BR>deprive of; wishing to take up (a fluid); wishing to<BR>gather; wishing to learn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्र|जिघ्रः
जिघ्र जिघ्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. घ्रा), smell-<BR>ing, a smeller; observing, conjecturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्रत्
जिघ्रत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, smelling, smelling at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्गशल्य
जिङ्गशल्य जिङ्गशल्य, अस्, m. the tree Mi-<BR>mosa Catechu; [cf. जिह्म-शल्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्गिनी
जिङ्गिनी जिङ्गिनी, f., N. of a plant, = झिङ्-<BR>गिनी, झिङ्गी, प्र-मोदिनी, सुनिर्यासा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्गी
जिङ्गी जिङ्गी, f. the plant Rubia Munjista.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीविषा
जिजीविषा जिजीविषा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>जीव्), desire to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीविषु
जिजीविषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to live, desirous of<BR>life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञापयिषु
जिज्ञापयिषु जिज्ञापयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid.<BR>of Caus. of 1. ज्ञा), wishing to make known, seeking<BR>to inform, communicative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासक
जिज्ञासक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Desid. of 1. ज्ञा),<BR>wishing to know, = जिज्ञासु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासन
जिज्ञासन, अम्, n. desire of knowing or becoming<BR>acquainted with, examining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासनीय
जिज्ञासनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, = जिज्ञास्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासमान
जिज्ञासमान, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of knowing,<BR>inquiring, testing, investigating, proving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासा
जिज्ञासा, f. desire of knowing or becoming ac-<BR>quainted with, inquiring; inquisitiveness; search,<BR>investigation, examination, test.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासित|जिज्ञासितः
जिज्ञासित, अस्, आ, अम्, investigated, asked, inquired,<BR>sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासु|जिज्ञासुः
जिज्ञासु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of knowing, wishing<BR>to become acquainted with, inquiring, inquisitive,<BR>curious, examining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञास्य|जिज्ञास्यः
जिज्ञास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, deserving of being inquired<BR>into, desirable to be known, worthy of being in-<BR>vestigated; an object for inquiry, to be investigated<BR>or examined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञु
जिज्ञु, उस्, उस्, उ, = जिज्ञासु (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिडधन
जिडधन जिडधन, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Paramānanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित|जितः
जित जित, &c. See under rt. 1. जि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्तम|जित्तमः
जित्तम 2. जित्तम or जितुम or जित्म, अस्,<BR>m. (a word borrowed fr. the Gr. διδύμοι), the sign<BR>of the zodiac Gemini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन|जिनः
जिन जिन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. जि), victorious,<BR>triumphant; (अस्), m. ‘the overcomer of all things,’<BR>a generic term applied to a Buddha or chief saint of<BR>the Bauddha sect in the same manner as to a Jaina<BR>saint; a N. applied to an Arhat who is a kind of<BR>sovereign pontiff or saint of the Jainas and regarded<BR>by them as superior to the gods of other sects;<BR>(twenty-four Jinas are supposed to flourish in each<BR>of the three Ava-sarpiṇīs or Jaina ages, past, present,<BR>and to come, making seventy-two in all; they are<BR>all born in Āryāvarta); N. of a Bodhi-sattva; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; any very old man; [cf. जीन and<BR>जीर्न.]<BR>—जिन-त्रात or जिन-दत्त or जिन-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, or जिन-बन्धु, उस्, m., N. of various persons<BR>mentioned in Buddhist writings.<BR>—जिन-धर्म,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Jaina work.<BR>—जिन-भक्ति-सूरि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a preceptor of Jina-lābha-sūri.<BR>—जिन-<BR>मित्र, अस्, m., N. of one of the translators of the<BR>Lalita-vistara.<BR>—जिन-लाभ-सूरि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>pupil of Jina-bhakti-sūri and preceptor of Kṣamā-<BR>kalyāṇa.<BR>—जिन-वक्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—जिन-श्री, ईस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—जिन-सद्मन्,<BR>अ, n. a Jaina temple or monastery.<BR>—जिन-सेन, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the work Triṣaṣṭi-lakṣaṇa-<BR>mahāpurāṇa-saṅgraha.<BR>—जिनाङ्कुर (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—जिनाधार (˚न-आध्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—जिनेन्द्र (˚न-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a Jaina saint, a Buddha; N. of a grammarian.<BR>—जिनेन्द्र-न्यास, अस्, m. title of the work of<BR>Jinendra-buddhi.<BR>—जिनेन्द्र-बुद्धि or जिनेन्द्र-<BR>भूति, इस्, m., N. of a writer on grammar.<BR>—जिने-<BR>श्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m. an Arhat of the Jainas; N.<BR>of the twentieth Arhat of the past Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR>—जि-<BR>नोत्तम (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, m. an Arhat of the Jainas.<BR>—जिनोरस (˚न-उर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनयोनि|जिनयोनिः
जिनयोनि जिन-योनि, इस्, m. (for अजिन-योनि,<BR>q. v.), a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्दुराज|जिन्दुराजः
जिन्दुराज जिन्दु-राज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्व्
जिन्व् जिन्व् (connected with जीव् and जू ?),<BR>cl. 1. P., Ved. जिन्वति, जिजिन्व, जिन्वि-<BR>ष्यति, जिन्वितुम्, to move one's self, be active or<BR>lively; to urge on, cause to move quickly, impel, in-<BR>cite, excite; to refresh, animate; to promote, help,<BR>favour; to help any one (acc.) to anything (dat.),<BR>cause to obtain, grant, confer; to please, satisfy,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">Page0347-c+ 71</a>]<BR>gladden, gratify, make happy or contented; to re-<BR>ceive favourably (a request &c.): cl. 10. P. जिन्व-<BR>यति, a various reading for जुञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्व
जिन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, in धियञ्-जिन्व, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम्
जिम् जिम् [cf. छम्, जम्, झम्], cl. 1. P.<BR>जेमति, &c., to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमन|जेमनं
जेमन, अम्, n. eating; food, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम्भ
जिम्भ जिम्भ, perhaps for जृम्भ in जिम्-<BR>भ-जिह्व-ता, swelling of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरण
जिरण जिरण, अस्, m. = जरण, जीरक,<BR>जीरण, cumin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरि
जिरि जिरि, cl. 5. P. जिरिणोति, &c., to hurt,<BR>injure, wound, kill; [cf. चिरि; cf. also<BR>Hib. gearaim, ‘I sharpen, whet, cut, bite.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिल्लिक|जिल्लिकः
जिल्लिक जिल्लिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवाजिव|जिवाजिवः
जिवाजिव जिवाजिव, अस्, m. a pheasant; [cf.<BR>जीवञ्-जीव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव्रि|जिव्रिः
जिव्रि जिव्रि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. 1. जॄ), Ved. old,<BR>worn out, decayed, decrepit; (इस्), m. time; a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्
जिष् जिष्, cl. 1. P. जेषति, &c., to<BR>sprinkle; [cf. विष् and मिष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्णु|जिष्णुः
जिष्णु जिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. 1. जि), vic-<BR>torious, triumphant, gaining, winning; (with acc. or<BR>at end of comp.) vanquishing, conquering, excelling;<BR>(उस्), m. the sun; an epithet of Indra, of Viṣṇu,<BR>and of Arjuna; N. of a Vasu; N. of a son of Manu<BR>Bhautya, N. of the father of Brahma-gupta; [cf.<BR>परा-जिष्णु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहान
जिहान जिहान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हा, जिहीते),<BR>going, going to, attaining, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहानक|जिहानकः
जिहानक, अस्, m. the destruction of the world;<BR>[cf. जहानक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहासा
जिहासा जिहासा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. हा, ज-<BR>हाति), desire of abandoning or giving up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहासु
जिहासु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of abandoning or<BR>giving up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षा
जिहीर्षा जिहीर्षा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. हृ),<BR>desire of seizing, taking, or robbing; wish to take<BR>away or remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षु
जिहीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to seize, desirous of<BR>taking or carrying or removing, wishing to rob or<BR>appropriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्ष्य
जिहीर्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, desirable to be taken away<BR>or brought near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्म|जिह्मं|जिह्मः
जिह्म जिह्म, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps related to<BR>rt. ह्वृ; but said to be fr. rt. हा, जहाति, and to<BR>denote originally quitting the upright direction or<BR>leaning out of the perpendicular), sloping, oblique,<BR>transverse, diagonal, athwart, squinting (as the eye),<BR>crooked, awry, not straight (opposed to ऋजु),<BR>tortuous, going irregularly; (जिह्मम् इ or गम्,<BR>to go crookedly, turn off from the right way);<BR>curved, bent; morally crooked, deceitful, deceptive,<BR>illusory, false, untrue, unfair, dishonest; slow, lazy;<BR>(अम्), n. falsehood, dishonesty; the plant Tabernæ-<BR>montana Coronaria (तगर); [cf. Hib. giomh, ‘a<BR>lock of hair, a fault.’]<BR>—जिह्म-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>tortuously or crookedly, moving slowly; (अस्), m. a<BR>snake.<BR>—जिह्म-गति, इस्, इस्, इ, going tortuously.<BR>—जिह्-<BR>म-ता, f. or जिह्म-त्व, अम्, n. crookedness, curva-<BR>ture; dishonesty, falsehood.<BR>—जिह्म-बार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having an aperture on one side; (Sāy.) having<BR>an opening below; having its door closed.<BR>—जिह्म-<BR>मीन, अस्, m. appearing in the deceptive shape of a<BR>fish.<BR>—जिह्म-मोहन, अस्, m. a frog.<BR>—जिह्म-<BR>योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fighting unfairly; (ई), m. epithet<BR>of Bhīma, who in his great battle with Dur-yodhana<BR>struck him an unfair blow with his club on the<BR>thighs; (see Śalya-parva 3345.)<BR>—जिह्म-शल्य,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Acacia Catechu; [cf. खदिर.]<BR>—जिह्म-शी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. lying crookedly or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">Page0348-a+ 77</a>]<BR>diagonally (on the ground &c.).<BR>—जिह्माक्ष (˚म-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, crooked-eyed, squinting.<BR>—जिह्-<BR>माशिन् (˚म-आश्˚), ई, m. ‘eating crookedly,’ N. of a<BR>man; (perhaps a wrong reading for जिह्वाशिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0347-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्माय
जिह्माय, nom. P., Ved. -यति, -यितुम्, to go<BR>crookedly or in crooked ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मित
जिह्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, bowed, curved; turned<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मीकृ
जिह्मी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>crooked, bend.<BR>—जिह्मी-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, making<BR>crooked or oblique, causing to bend; (metaphori-<BR>cally) obscuring.<BR>—जिह्मी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>crooked, bent, bowed down (with fear &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्व|जिह्वं|जिह्वः
जिह्व जिह्व, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. जि, per-<BR>haps fr. rt. ह्वे; cf. 1. जुहू), the tongue; (आ), f. the<BR>tongue; the tongue or tongues of Agni, i. e. various<BR>forms of flame, (sometimes three are mentioned,<BR>sometimes seven, the names of which are given as fol-<BR>lows: काली, कराली, मनो-जवा, सु-लोहिता, सुधूम्र-<BR>वर्णा, स्फुलिङ्गिनी, विश्व-रूपी; or are identified<BR>with the seven winds, प्र-वह, आ-वह, उद्-वह,<BR>सं-वह, वि-वह, परि-वह, and नि-वह. The<BR>horses of Agni or वह्नयः are said to be सप्त-<BR>जिह्वाः, having seven tongues); the root of the plant<BR>Tabernæmontana Coronaria; [cf. जिह्म; cf. also Lat.<BR>lingua ?; Goth. tuggô; Germ. Zunge; Hib. teanga ?].<BR>—जिह्वा-कात्य, अस्, m., N. of a man, the voracious<BR>Kātya.<BR>—जिह्वाग्र (˚वा-अग्˚), अम्, n. the tip of the<BR>tongue.<BR>—जिह्वा-तल, अम्, n. the surface of the<BR>tongue.<BR>—जिह्वा-निर्लेखन and जिह्वा-निर्लेख-<BR>निक, अम्, n. scraping the tongue; a tongue-scraper;<BR>[cf. जिह्वोल्लेखन.]<BR>—जिह्वा-प, अस्, m. (‘drinking<BR>with the tongue’), a dog; a cat; a tiger; a panther,<BR>the hunting leopard; a bear.<BR>—जिह्वा-प्रथन,<BR>अम्, n. expansion or too great flattening of the<BR>tongue (a defect in pronunciation).<BR>—जिह्वा-मल,<BR>अम्, n. the fur of the tongue.<BR>—जिह्वा-मूल, अम्,<BR>n. the root of the tongue.<BR>—जिह्वामूलीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>belonging to or uttered from the root of the tongue,<BR>a term applied to the vowels ऋ, ऌ, the Visarga be-<BR>fore क्, ख्, and the guttural class of consonants, but<BR>especially to the Visarga before क्, ख्.<BR>—जिह्वा-रद,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a tongue-like beak,’ a bird.<BR>—जिह्वा-<BR>लिह्, ट्, m. ‘licking with the tongue,’ a dog.<BR>—जिह्वा-<BR>लौल्य, अम्, n. greediness.<BR>—जिह्वा-वत्, आन्, m., N.<BR>of a preceptor.<BR>—जिह्वा-शत, अम्, n. a hundred<BR>tongues.<BR>—जिह्वा-शल्य, अस्, m. = जिह्म-शल्य, q. v.<BR>—जिह्वा-शोधन, अम्, n. cleaning of the tongue.<BR>—जिह्वास्वाद (˚वा-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘tasting with the<BR>tongue,’ licking, lapping.<BR>—जिह्वोल्लेखन (˚वा-<BR>उल्˚), अम्, n. scraping the tongue; (ई and इका), f. a<BR>tongue-scraper made of a thin piece of wood of the<BR>Mimusops Kauki or other trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वक
जिह्वक at the end of an adj. comp. in अ-जिह्-<BR>वका, f. tongueless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वल|जिह्वलः
जिह्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, voracious, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्विका
जिह्विका, f. a diminutive fr. जिह्वा; [cf. अधो-<BR>जिह्विका, अलि-ज्˚, उप-ज्˚, प्रति-ज्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वु
जिह्वु जिह्वु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जी
जी जी, in कृष्ण-जी and केशव-जी-नन्द-<BR>शर्मन्, = the Bengālī जी (fr. जीव, life, soul ?), sir,<BR>master, madam, attached to names and titles as a<BR>mark of endearment or respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीत
जीत जीत, &c. See rt. 1. ज्या, p. 352.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीति|जीतिः
जीति, इस्, f. fading away. See अ-जीति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीन|जीनः
जीन, अस्, आ, अम्, old, aged; a leather bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूत|जीमूतः
जीमूत जीमूत, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>जि), a cloud; a mountain; N. of the sun; N. of<BR>Indra; a nourisher, a sustainer; the plant Lipeo-<BR>cercis Serrata; also Luffa Fœtida or a similar plant;<BR>a kind of Cyperus; a kind of metre; N. of an<BR>ancient sage; of a certain wrestler; of a son of<BR>Vyoman.<BR>—जीमूत-कुट, अस्, m. a small hill near<BR>a mountain.<BR>—जीमूत-केतु, उस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of a prince of the Vidyā-dharas.<BR>—जीमूत-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. Curcuma Amhaldi or Zerumbet.<BR>—जीमूत-वाहन, अस्, m. an epithet of Indra; N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">Page0348-b+ 78</a>]<BR>of a son of king Śāli-vāhana; N. of a son of Jīmūta-<BR>ketu; N. of a lawyer, author of the Dāya-bhāga.<BR>—जीमूत-वाहिन्, ई, m. smoke.<BR>—जीमूत-स्वन-<BR>सन्निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like the sound of a cloud.<BR>—जीमूताष्टमी (˚त-अष्˚), f., N. of a festival in<BR>honour of Jīmūta-vāhana, son of Śāli-vāhana, on<BR>the eighth day in the dark half of month Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतक
जीमूतक, अस्, m. the plant Lipeocercis Serrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर|जीरः
जीर जीर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. जिन्व्),<BR>Ved. quick, speedy, lively, active, busy; driving,<BR>exciting; गो-जीर, exciting (the milk of) the cows;<BR>(अस्), m. quick motion or movement (especially of<BR>the Soma stones); a sword, a scymitar, a sacrificial<BR>knife; Panicum Miliaceum; cumin-seed, (in this<BR>latter sense said to be fr. rt. जु or 1. जॄ.)<BR>—जीर-<BR>दानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. dropping, trickling, drizzling,<BR>sprinkling or scattering in small drops; causing to<BR>flow abundantly; (Sāy.) ‘granting a victorious dis-<BR>position’ (as if fr. rt. 1. जि).<BR>—जीराध्वर (˚र-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having animated or vigorous rites;<BR>(Sāy.) free from injury or molestation.<BR>—जीराश्व<BR>(˚र-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having lively or fleet<BR>horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरक|जीरकः
जीरक or जीरण, अस्, m. cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरि|जीरिः
जीरि, इस्, m. f., Ved. quick or flowing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरिका
जीरिका, f., N. of a plant, = जीर्ण-पत्त्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्ण|जीर्णं|जीर्णः
जीर्ण जीर्ण. See under rt. 1. जॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्वि|जीर्विः
जीर्वि जीर्वि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. जॄ),<BR>an axe; a cart; the body; an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्
जीव् जीव्, cl. 1. P. (poet. also A.) जीवति,<BR>-ते, जिजीव, जीविष्यति, जीवितुम्, to live,<BR>be alive; to revive, return to life; to make a liveli-<BR>hood, live by (with inst.): Caus. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>जीवयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to make alive, restore to life,<BR>vivify; to support life, to keep alive; to nourish,<BR>nurture, bring up; (a Causal form जीवापयति<BR>occasionally occurs, meaning ‘to restore to life’):<BR>Desid. जिजीविषति (Ved. जुज्यूषति or जिज्यूषति),<BR>to wish to live, to seek a livelihood, wish to live by<BR>(with inst.); [cf. Lith. gywénu, ‘to live;’ gywas,<BR>‘alive:’ Slav. schivû, ‘to live:’ Goth. qvivs: Old Germ.<BR>qveh: Angl. Sax. cvic: Eng. quick: Lat. vivo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव, अस्, आ, अम्, living, existing, a living being;<BR>causing to live, vivifying; (अस्), m. the principle of<BR>life, the vital breath, the living or personal soul in-<BR>corporated in the body and imparting to it life, motion,<BR>and sensation, (hence also called जीवात्मन्; it is<BR>distinguished from the परमात्मन् or supreme<BR>soul, q. v.); livelihood, profession, specific occupa-<BR>tion; a kind of plant; an epithet of Bṛhaspati as<BR>regent of the planet Jupiter; or as regent of the<BR>Nakṣatra Tiṣya or Puṣya; the third lustrum in<BR>the cycle of Jupiter which lasts sixty years; N. of<BR>one of the eight Maruts; an epithet of Karṇa; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. life, existence; (आ), f. the living or life-<BR>giving element, i. e. water; the earth; a bow-string;<BR>(in geometry) the chord of an arc, the sine of an<BR>arc; the tinkling of metallic ornaments; N. of two<BR>plants, = जीवन्ती and वचा; [cf. Lith. gywas, ‘alive;’<BR>Goth. qvivs; Lat. vivus; Gr. βίος; Hib. beo,<BR>‘living, alive.’]<BR>—जीव-गृभ्, -घृप्, प्, प्, Ved.<BR>taking alive, seizing beings alive.<BR>—जीव-ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. filling (a cup) with the living Soma, i. e.<BR>with the plant in its unpressed state.<BR>—जीव-ग्राह,<BR>अस्, m. a prisoner, one taken alive; जीव-ग्राहं<BR>ग्रह्, to capture alive.<BR>—जीव-घोष-स्वामिन्, ई,<BR>m., N. of a grammarian.<BR>—जीव-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born<BR>alive.<BR>—जीव-जीव or जीव-जीवक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>bird; see the next.<BR>—जीवञ्-जीव, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>bird supposed to be a pheasant; the Chakor or<BR>Greek partridge; a kind of tree.<BR>—जीव-तोका, f. a<BR>woman whose children are living.<BR>—जीव-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of life or existence.<BR>—१. जीव-द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (rt. दा), ‘life-giving,’ who or what gives life;<BR>(अस्), m. a physician, a practitioner of medicine.<BR>—२.<BR>जीव-द, अस्, m. (rt. दो), ‘cutting off life,’ an enemy.<BR>—जीव-दशा, f. mortal existence.<BR>—जीव-दात्री, f.<BR>‘life-giver,’ a kind of medicinal plant, = ऋद्धि.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-c" target="_blank">Page0348-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—जीव-दान, अम्, n. ‘giving life,’ ‘rescuing from<BR>sickness,’ title of a manual of medicine composed by<BR>Cyavana.<BR>—जीव-दानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. a wrong<BR>form for जीर-दानु, q. v.<BR>—जीव-दामन्, आ, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—जीव-दायक, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘life-giving.’<BR>—जीव-धन, अम्, n. ‘living wealth,’ property in<BR>living creatures, live stock, wealth in flocks and<BR>herds.<BR>—जीव-धन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘supporting living<BR>beings;’ (Sāy.) ‘satiating living beings,’ an epithet of<BR>Soma, and of Prajā-pati.<BR>—जीव-धानी, f. ‘receptacle<BR>of living beings,’ an epithet of the earth.<BR>—जीव-नश्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, or ट्, ट्, ट्, (a sacrifice &c.) where living beings<BR>are killed.<BR>—जीव-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a writer on<BR>astronomy; N. of a physician.<BR>—जीव-नाय or जीव-<BR>नायक, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—जीव-नाशम्, ind.<BR>with नश्, to lose one's life, die, perish.<BR>—जीव-<BR>निकाय, अस्, m. a being endowed with life.<BR>—जीव-<BR>नेत्री, f., N. of a plant, = सैंहली.<BR>—जीव-पति, इस्,<BR>m. a living husband.<BR>—जीव-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a fresh leaf.<BR>—जीवपत्त्र-प्रचायिका, f. gathering fresh leaves,<BR>a sort of game.<BR>—जीव-पत्नी, f. a woman whose hus-<BR>band is alive.<BR>—जीव-पितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or जीव-<BR>पितृक, अस्, आ, अम्, a son or daughter whose father<BR>is still alive.<BR>—जीव-पीत-सर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>one whose rays are drunk by living beings; (Sāy.)<BR>one whose creation is enjoyed by all.<BR>—जीव-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, one whose sons or children are living;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of plant.<BR>—जीव-पुत्रक, अस्, m.<BR>a tree, commonly Ingua; another plant bearing<BR>seeds used in rosaries, commonly Jiyaputa, Nageia<BR>Putranjiva.<BR>—जीवपुत्र-प्रचायिका, f. the gathering<BR>of the above plant, a sort of game.<BR>—जीव-पुरा,<BR>f., Ved. the abode of living beings or men.<BR>—जीव-<BR>पुष्प, अम्, n. ‘flower of life,’ N. of a plant<BR>and metaphorically applied to the head; N. of<BR>two plants, = दमनक and फणिज्झक; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a plant, = बृहज्-जीवन्ती.<BR>—जीव-प्रिया, f. the<BR>tree Terminalia Chebula, = हरीतकी.<BR>—जीव-बध,<BR>अस्, m. destruction of living beings.<BR>—जीव-बर्हिस्,<BR>इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having a living, i. e. fresh bed of<BR>sacrificial grass.<BR>—जीव-भद्रा, f. a kind of plant,<BR>= जीवन्ती; a kind of medicinal plant, = वृद्धि.<BR>—जीव-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become alive, endowed<BR>with life.<BR>—जीव-भोजन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving<BR>enjoyment to living beings; (अम्), n. the pleasure or<BR>enjoyment of living beings.<BR>—जीव-मन्दिर, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the mansion of the soul,’ the body.<BR>—जीव-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, animated, endowed with life.<BR>—जीव-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—जीव-<BR>याज, अस्, m., Ved. the sacrifice of living beings.<BR>—जीव-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, enclosing a soul (as a body<BR>or a sentient being).<BR>—जीव-रक्त, अम्, n. living<BR>blood, menstrual blood.<BR>—जीव-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>lifeless.<BR>—जीव-लोक, अस्, m. the world or habitation<BR>of living beings (opposed to the world of deceased<BR>ancestors), living beings, mankind.<BR>—जीव-लौकिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, peculiar to the world of living beings or<BR>to men.<BR>—जीव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, animated, living;<BR>—जीव-वल्ली, f., N. of a plant.<BR>—जीव-विचार, अस्,<BR>m. title of a Jaina work.<BR>—जीवविचार-प्रकरण,<BR>अम्, n. title of a Jaina work by Śānti-sūri.<BR>—जीव-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. breeding or keeping cattle.<BR>—जीव-<BR>शंस, अस्, m., Ved. rule over living beings; (Sāy.)<BR>to be praised by living beings.<BR>—जीव-शर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of an astronomer.<BR>—जीव-शाक, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of pot-herb growing in Mālava.<BR>—जीव-शुक्ला,<BR>f. a kind of plant.<BR>—जीव-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, one to<BR>whom only life is left or who has escaped with his<BR>life and nothing more.<BR>—जीव-शोणित, अम्, n. living,<BR>i. e. healthy blood.<BR>—जीव-श्रेष्ठा, f. a kind of<BR>medicinal plant.<BR>—जीव-सङ्क्रमण, अम्, n. me-<BR>tempsychosis.<BR>—जीव-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a shrub,<BR>= काम-वृद्धि.<BR>—जीव-साधन, अम्, n. ‘means<BR>of subsistence,’ rice, grain.<BR>—जीव-साफल्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘fruitfulness of life,’ realisation of a life's wishes.<BR>—जीव-सुत, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose children are all<BR>alive.<BR>—जीव-सू, ऊस्, f. the mother of living offspring.<BR>—जीव-स्थान, अम्, n. a joint, an articulation.<BR>—जीवाजीवाधार (˚व-अजीव-आध्˚), अस्, m. the world<BR>of organic beings and of inorganic matter.<BR>—जीवा-<BR>जीवाधार-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. the material world, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-a" target="_blank">Page0349-a+ 81</a>]<BR>receptacle of inorganic beings and inorganic substances.<BR>—जीवात्मन् (˚व-आत्˚), आ, m. the living or individual<BR>soul enshrined in the human body (distinguished from<BR>the परमात्मन् or supreme soul), the vital principle<BR>or spirit, that principle of life which renders the body<BR>capable of motion or sensation; [cf. जीव.]<BR>—जीवा-<BR>दान (˚व-आद्˚), अम्, n. abstracting living or healthy<BR>blood, bleeding.<BR>—जीवाधान (˚व-आध्˚), अम्, n.<BR>preservation of life.<BR>—जीवान्तक (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>fowler, a birdcatcher; a destroyer of life, a slayer, a<BR>murderer.<BR>—जीवाभिगम-सूत्र (˚व-अभ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>title of a Jaina work.<BR>—जीवाश (˚व-आश), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>hoping for life; (आ), f. hope of living.<BR>—जीवास्तिकाय<BR>(˚व-अस्˚), अस्, m. (with Jainas) the category of ‘soul.’<BR>—जीवेन्धन (˚व-इन्˚), अम्, n. glowing fire-wood,<BR>burning wood.<BR>—जीवोत्सर्ग (˚व-उत्˚), अस्, m. aban-<BR>donment of life, voluntary death.<BR>—जीवोर्णा (˚व-<BR>ऊर्˚), f. the wool of a living animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवक|जीवकः
जीवक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) living,<BR>living by, making a livelihood by, causing to live,<BR>generating; one who lives a long time or for whom<BR>a long life is desired [cf. आयुष्-मत्]; (अस्), m. a living<BR>being; a servant, slave, one who makes a livelihood<BR>by service; a mendicant, one who lives by begging;<BR>an usurer, one who lives by lending money at high<BR>interest; a snake-catcher, one whose business is to<BR>catch snakes and cure their bites &c.; a tree; N. of<BR>several plants, = Terminalia Tomentosa, Coccinia<BR>Grandis, a cucurbitaceous plant; a medicinal plant,<BR>commonly called by the same name Jīvaka and con-<BR>sidered as one of the eight principal drugs classed<BR>together under the name Aṣṭa-varga; N. of a man;<BR>(इका), f. the living or life-giving element (i. e. water);<BR>living, means of living, livelihood; N. of a plant,<BR>= जीवन्ती; [cf. अज-जीवक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्|जीवन्त्
जीवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, living, alive; जीवन्न् एव,<BR>during life.<BR>—जीवत्-तोका, f. a woman whose children<BR>are living.<BR>—जीवत्-पति, इस्, or जीवत्-पत्नी, f. a wife<BR>whose husband is alive.<BR>—जीवत्-पितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or<BR>जीवत्-पितृक, अस्, आ, अम्, a son or daughter whose<BR>father is alive; [cf. जीव-पितृ.]<BR>—जीवत्पितृक-<BR>निर्णय, अस्, m. title of a work by Rāma-kṛṣṇa.<BR>—जीवन्-मुक्त, अस्, m. a man purified by knowledge of<BR>Brahma and exonerated whilst living from future birth<BR>and all ritual ceremonies.<BR>—जीवन्-मुक्ति, इस्, f. libera-<BR>tion in the present state of life. In the Vedānta system<BR>a secondary sort of liberation which conducts the soul<BR>after death to live with Brahma, not however divested<BR>of a subtile corporeal frame.<BR>—जीवन्मुक्ति-विवेक, अस्,<BR>m. title of a philosophical treatise.<BR>—जीवन्-मृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, at once alive and dead, dead while alive, (said<BR>of one whose character is lost or of a madman &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथ|जीवथः
जीवथ, अस्, आ, अम्, long-lived; virtuous, pious;<BR>(अस्), m. life, existence, breath; a tortoise; a pea-<BR>cock; a cloud; virtue, piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन|जीवनं|जीवनः
जीवन, अस्, ई, अम्, enlivening, vivifying, giving<BR>life; (अस्), m. a living being, an animal; wind; a<BR>son; a kind of drug, = जीवक; N. of a plant, =<BR>क्षुद्र-फलक; N. of the author of the work<BR>Mānasa-nayana; (आ), f. a kind of medicinal plant;<BR>(ई), f., N. of several plants and drugs, = जीवन्ती,<BR>काकोली, a kind of jasmine &c.; (अम्), n. life, existence,<BR>living, livelihood, profession (often at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. मृग-जीवन, living by hunting); en-<BR>livening, making alive; the life-giving element (water);<BR>butter made from new milk or milk one day old; mar-<BR>row.<BR>—जीवन-ता, f. life, mode of life.<BR>—जीवन-योनि,<BR>इस्, m. source of life.<BR>—जीवन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed<BR>of or relating to life.<BR>—जीवन-विडम्बन, अम्, n.<BR>disappointment in life, living in vain.<BR>—जीवन-हेतु,<BR>उस्, m. object of life, cause of living.<BR>—जीवना-<BR>घात (˚न-आघ्˚), अम्, n. ‘that which destroys life,’<BR>poison.<BR>—जीवनान्त (˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. end of life,<BR>death.<BR>—जीवनावास (˚न-आव्˚), अस्, m. Varuṇa, the<BR>regent of water.<BR>—जीवनोपाय (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>livelihood, means of subsistence.<BR>—जीवनौषध<BR>(˚न-औष्˚), अम्, n. an invigorating or life-giving<BR>medicine, a drug for reviving the dead; elixir vitæ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनक|जीवनकं
जीवनक, अस्, इका, अम्, enlivening; (अम्), n.<BR>food; (इका), f. the tree Terminalia Chebula, =<BR>हरीतकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनस्या
जीवनस्या, f., Ved. desire of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनीय|जीवनीयं
जीवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lived; supporting life,<BR>N. of a particular class of drugs; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>plant, = जीवन्ती; (अम्), n. a form of milk, milk<BR>fresh from the cow; water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्त|जीवंत|जीवन्तः
जीवन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, living, existent, long-lived;<BR>(अस्), m. life, existence; a medicament, a drug; a<BR>kind of pot-herb (जीव-शाक); N. of a man; (ई), f.<BR>a kind of medicinal plant, also eaten as a vegetable,<BR>= Pæderia Fœtida (?); also = गुडूची, Cocculus Cor-<BR>difolius and = वन्दा, a parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्तिक|जीवंतिक|जीवंतिकः|जीवन्तिकः
जीवन्तिक, अस्, m. a fowler, a birdcatcher; see<BR>जीवान्तक; (इका), f. a parasitical plant, Epidendron<BR>Tesseloides, and other species; a plant Menispermum<BR>Glabrum; a kind of pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमान
जीवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, living, alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवल
जीवल, अस्, आ, अम्, full of life, animating; (अस्), m.<BR>a kind of plant; N. of a man; (आ), f. a kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवातु|जीवातुः
जीवातु, उस्, f. life, existence; (उस्, उ), m. n. victuals,<BR>food, boiled rice; a medicine for restoring life; [cf.<BR>Lat. victus.]<BR>—जीवातु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, animated,<BR>living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविका
जीविका, see under जीवक.<BR>—जीविकापन्न (˚का-<BR>आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having obtained subsistence.<BR>—जीवि-<BR>का-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having obtained a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवित|जीवितं
जीवित, अस्, आ, अम्, lived, lived through (as a period<BR>of time), living, alive, existent; revivified, returned<BR>to life; animated, enlivened; (अम्), n. a living being;<BR>living, life, existence; duration of life; livelihood,<BR>means of existence; [cf. Lith. gywata; Slav. schi-<BR>vot; Lat. vita for vivita.]<BR>—जीवित-काल, अस्, m.<BR>life-time, period or duration of life, a life.<BR>—जीवित-<BR>ज्ञा, f. an artery, a vessel of the body.<BR>—जीवित-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of life,’ a husband.<BR>—जीवित-<BR>योपन, अस्, आ, अम्, oppressing or molesting living<BR>beings.<BR>—जीवित-व्यय, अस्, m. casting away life,<BR>sacrifice of life.<BR>—जीवित-संशय, अस्, m. risk<BR>of life, fear of death.<BR>—जीवित-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, de-<BR>stroying life.<BR>—जीवितान्त (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. end of<BR>life, death.<BR>—जीवितान्तक (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. putting<BR>an end to life, an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—जीविताशा (˚त-आशा),<BR>f. hope of life; love of life.<BR>—जीवितेप्सु (˚त-ईप्˚), उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, seeking to save (one's) life.<BR>—जीवितेश (˚त-<BR>ईश), अस्, आ, अम्, presiding over life; (अस्), m. ‘the<BR>lord or master of existence,’ a lover, a husband; an<BR>epithet of Yama the regent of death; the sun; the<BR>moon; a drug to revive the dead.<BR>—जीवितेश्वर<BR>(˚त-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of life,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्य
जीवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lived, to be kept<BR>alive; (अम्), n. the possibility of living; possible<BR>return to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविन्
जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living, alive, animate; living upon<BR>or by; (ई), m. a living being.<BR>—जीवि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>life, existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्य|जीव्यं
जीव्य, अम्, n. life; (आ), f. several plants, = जीवन्ती,<BR>गोक्षुर-दुग्धा; Terminalia Chebula, = हरीतकी.<BR>—जीव्योपाय (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m. means of existence,<BR>subsistence, livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जु
जु जु, see 1. जू. The form of this root<BR>given in the Dhātu-pāṭha is जु, but the deri-<BR>vatives from it have the vowel long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुकुट|जुकुटः
जुकुट जुकुट, अस्, m. a dog [cf. कुक्कुट];<BR>the Malaya range of mountains; (अम्), n. the egg-<BR>plant, Solanum Melongena; [cf. जकुट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुपिषु
जुगुपिषु जुगुपिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. गुप्), intending or wishing to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सन|जुगुप्सनं
जुगुप्सन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a dislike, detesting;<BR>(अम्), n. censure, abuse, reproach, reviling, dislike,<BR>horror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सा
जुगुप्सा, f. censure; dislike, aversion, abhorrence,<BR>disgust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सित
जुगुप्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, reviled, blamed, censured,<BR>abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सु
जुगुप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, having a dislike or disgust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुर्वणि
जुगुर्वणि जुगुर्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ (reduplicated<BR>form fr. rt. 1. गॄ), Ved. fond of praise, wishing to<BR>praise; (Sāy.) favouring the praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्ग्|जुंग्
जुङ्ग् जुङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. जुङ्गति, &c., to quit,<BR>abandon; to except, exclude; [cf. युङ्ग्<BR>and वुङ्ग्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्ग|जुङ्गः
जुङ्ग, अस्, आ, m. f. or जुङ्गक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant, Argyreia Speciosa or Argentea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्गित|जुंगित|जुङ्गितः
जुङ्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, deserted, injured, abandoned,<BR>outcast; (अस्), m. a man of a degraded caste, a<BR>Cāṇḍāla &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुञ्च्
जुञ्च् जुञ्च् (?), cl. 1. 10. P. जुञ्चति, जुञ्च-<BR>यति, &c., to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुट्
जुट् जुट्, cl. 6. P. जुटति, &c., a various<BR>reading for जुड्, to bind; [cf. जट्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटक|जुटकं
जुटक, अम्, n. [cf. जटा and जूटक], a braid of<BR>hair, any knot or fillet of hair; (इका), f. = चूडा, a<BR>tuft of hair on the top of the head; the matted hair<BR>of Śiva or of ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुड्
जुड् जुड्, cl. 6. P. जुडति, &c., to bind, to<BR>join together; cl. 10. P. जोडयति, &c., to<BR>send, cast or throw, direct; to grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुत्
जुत् जुत्, cl. 1. A. जोतते, to shine; [cf.<BR>ज्युत्, द्युत्, युत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुतुम
जुतुम जुतुम and जुथुम, two incorrect<BR>readings for जितुम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुन्
जुन् जुन्, cl. 6. P. जुनति, &c., to go; (a<BR>various reading has जुड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुमर
जुमर जुमर, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुम्बक|जुंबकः|जुम्बकः
जुम्बक जुम्बक, अस्, m., Ved., N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर् 1. जुर् (related to 1. जॄ), cl. 6. 4. P.,<BR>Ved. जुरति, जूर्यति, जुजोर (?), &c., to<BR>decay, become old or decrepit, to grow old, perish;<BR>also जूर्, cl. 4. A. जूर्यते, to grow old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
2. जुर्, ऊर्, m. an old man; [cf. 2. जू.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्य
जुर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming old; [cf. अ-जुर्य<BR>and जूर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ण
जूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, decayed, old.<BR>—जूर्णाख्य<BR>(˚ण-आख्˚), अस्, m. the plant Saccharum Cylindricum,<BR>commonly Ulū.<BR>—जूर्णाह्वय (˚ण-आह्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the plant Andropogon Saccharatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णी
जूर्णी, f., Ved., N. of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्य|जूर्य्य
जूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. becoming old, aged,<BR>weak, an old man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्व्
जुर्व् जुर्व्. See जूर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुल्
जुल् जुल्, cl. 10. P. जोलयति, &c., to re-<BR>duce to powder, grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुवस्
जुवस् जुवस्. See under rt. जू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् 1. जुष्, cl. 6. A. (ep. also P.) जुषते,<BR>-ति, जुजुषे, जोषिष्यते, अजोषिष्ट, जो-<BR>षितुम्, to be pleased or satisfied, to be propitiated<BR>or propitious; to be favourable; to like, be fond of,<BR>to have pleasure in, delight in (with acc. or gen.);<BR>to enjoy; to show one's self favourable towards<BR>(with acc.); to have pleasure in granting (with loc. of<BR>the person); to devote one's self to, practise, undergo,<BR>suffer; to delight in visiting, frequent, visit, inhabit,<BR>enter; happen to; to have pleasure in performing<BR>(with dat., e. g. जुषते कर्मणे, he likes to engage<BR>in any act); to choose; to give pleasure to (with loc.<BR>of the person): Caus. जोषयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to<BR>like, be fond of, love, behave kindly towards (with<BR>acc.); fondle, cherish; to delight in, approve of,<BR>choose: Desid. जुजुषिषते or जुजोषिषते: Intens.<BR>जोजुष्यते, जोजोष्टि; [cf. Zend zaosha, ‘will, de-<BR>sire;’ Hib. gus, ‘a desire, inclination;’ Goth. kus, ‘to<BR>choose,’ kiusu, kaus, kusum; Germ. kiese; Lat.<BR>gus-tus; Gr. γεύω, γεύομαι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
2. जुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, liking, fond of, devoted to (with<BR>acc.); visiting, approaching; [cf. स-जुष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुषाण
जुषाण, अस्, m., N. of a sacrificial formula con-<BR>taining the word जुषाण, pres. part. of rt. 1. जुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ट|जुष्टं
जुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, gratified, pleased, propitiated,<BR>propitious, favourable; liked, wished, loved, agreeable,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">Page0350-a+ 72</a>]<BR>usual; frequented, visited; served, obliged, worshipped,<BR>gratified by service; practised; furnished with, pos-<BR>sessed of; (अम्), n. the crumbs or remnants of a<BR>meal or its leavings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0349-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्टि
जुष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. love, service, favour, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्य|जुष्यः
जुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be served or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोष|जोषं|जोषः
जोष, जोषण, &c. See p. 351, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् 3. जुष्, cl. 1. 10. P. जोषति, जोष-<BR>यति, &c., to reason, think, conceive, ima-<BR>gine, investigate, examine; to injure, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्क|जुष्कः
जुष्क जुष्क, अस्, m., N. of one of the three<BR>Turuṣka kings in Kaśmīra.<BR>—जुष्क-पुर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town founded by Jushka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्कक|जुष्ककः
जुष्कक जुष्कक, अस्, m. = यूष, the water<BR>of boiled pulse, pease-soup, porridge, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहु
जुहु जुहु = 2. जुहू below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुराण|जुहुराणः
जुहुराण जुहुराण, अस्, m. (a corrupt form,<BR>said to be fr. rt. हुर्छ्; or fr. rt. ह्वृ), the moon;<BR>[cf. जुहूराण below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवाण
जुहुवाण जुहुवाण, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हु; a cor-<BR>rupt form), fire, (also spelt जुहूवाण); a sacrificing<BR>priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवान|जुहुवानः
जुहुवान, अस्, m. (perf. part. fr. rt. हु), fire;<BR>a tree; a hard-hearted man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूराण|जुहूराणः
जुहूराण, अस्, m. (a corrupt form), fire; a sacri-<BR>ficing priest; the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहू
जुहू 1. जुहू, ऊस्, f. (fr. rt. ह्वे), a tongue;<BR>especially the tongue or tongues of Agni, the flames;<BR>सप्त जुह्वः, the seven tongues of Agni; see जिह्वा.<BR>जुहू personified is the wife of Brahmā and goddess<BR>of speech; [cf. सरस्वती.]<BR>—जुहू-वत्, आन्, m. fire<BR>or its deity Agni.<BR>—जुह्व्-आस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>tongue-mouthed, whose mouth consists of tongues<BR>or is full of them, an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहू
जुहू 2. जुहू, ऊस्, f. (fr. rt. हु), a wooden<BR>ladle or vessel of the shape of a semicircle or crescent,<BR>used for pouring the sacrificial butter into the fire;<BR>that part of the frame enshrining the supreme spirit<BR>which faces the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहोति|जुहोतिः
जुहोति जुहोति, इस्, m. (fr. rt. हु), a technical<BR>name for those sacrificial ceremonies to which the<BR>verb जुहोति and not यजति is applied.<BR>—जुहोत्य्-आदि,<BR>अयस्, m. pl. the roots beginning with हु, to sacrifice,<BR>i. e. the roots of the third class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुह्वत्
जुह्वत्, अत्, अती, अत्, sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू 1. जू (or according to the Dhātu-pāṭha<BR>जु), cl. 1. P. A., 9. P. जवति, -ते, जुनाति, &c.,<BR>to press forwards, hurry on, move on quickly, be<BR>quick; to impel quickly, urge or drive on, incite; to<BR>excite, promote, animate, inspire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुवस्
जुवस्, अस्, n., Ved. quickness, speed, liveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
2. जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. quick, speedy; (according<BR>to Sāy. जूः may also be the Nom. c. of जुर्, old); in-<BR>citing, pressing, driving; (ऊस्), f. speed, expedition,<BR>velocity, going, motion; the atmosphere; a female<BR>demon or goblin; an epithet of the goddess Sarasvatī;<BR>a spot or mark on the forehead of horses and oxen;<BR>[cf. कशो-जू and मनो-जू.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूत
जूत, अस्, आ, अम्, moved quickly, impelled, urged,<BR>pressed, (at the end of comp. in अद्रि-जूत, इन्द्र-ज्˚,<BR>देव-ज्˚), &c., q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूति|जूतिः
जूति, इस्, f. going on, proceeding, moving; quick-<BR>ness, speed, velocity; flowing without obstruction or<BR>interruption; impulse, incitement, instigation, anima-<BR>tion; inclination, impulse, energy.<BR>—जूति-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. impetuous, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूक|जूकः
जूक जूक (a word borrowed fr. the Gr.<BR>ζυγόν), the sign of the zodiac Libra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूट|जूटः
जूट जूट, अस्, m. the matted hair of Śiva,<BR>the twisted or clotted hair of an ascetic; [cf. जटा<BR>and चूड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूटक|जूटकं
जूटक, अम्, n. twisted or braided hair; [cf. जटा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूतिका
जूतिका जूतिका, f. a kind of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूमरनन्दिन्
जूमरनन्दिन् जूमर-नन्दिन्, ई, m., N. of<BR>the author of a commentary on the grammar entitled<BR>Saṅkṣipta-sāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्
जूर् जूर्, cl. 4. A. जूर्यते, &c., to hurt,<BR>injure, wound, kill; to be angry with (with<BR>dat.); to grow old. See rt. 1. जुर्, p. 349.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ण
जूर्ण जूर्ण, जूर्य. See rt. 1. जुर्, p. 349.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णि|जूर्णिः
जूर्णि 1. जूर्णि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. जुर् = गुर्), Ved.<BR>skilfully praising, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्व्
जूर्व् जूर्व् (connected with rt. ज्वर्), cl. 1.<BR>P., Ved. जूर्वति, &c., to consume by heat,<BR>singe, burn; to hurt, kill; [cf. Hib. gearbaim, ‘I<BR>grieve, hurt, wound;’ cf. also rt. ज्वल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णि|जूर्णिः
2. जूर्णि, इस्, f., Ved. glowing fire, a blaze, a fiery<BR>weapon; anger [cf. जूर्]; speed (perhaps for जूति);<BR>fever [cf. ज्वर]; disease, sickness; the body; the<BR>sun; Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णिन्
जूर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. surrounded by glowing<BR>fire, glowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ति|जूर्तिः|जूर्त्ति|जूर्त्तिः
जूर्ति, इस्, f. fever; feverish or morbid heat; [cf.<BR>Hib. gurt, ‘pain, trouble, fierceness.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष्
जूष् जूष् (a various reading for यूष्), cl.<BR>1. P. जूषति, &c., to kill, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष|जूषं|जूषः
जूष, अम्, n. the water of boiled pulse, pease-<BR>soup, porridge, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषण|जूषणं
जूषण, अम्, n. the plant Grislea Tomentosa,<BR>commonly Dhäiphula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृ
जृ जृ, cl. 1. P. जरति, &c., to surpass,<BR>excel; make low, depress, humiliate; [cf.<BR>Germ. kurz; Scot. gearr, goirid, ‘short.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृङ्गि
जृङ्गि जृङ्गि, अयस्, or जृङ्गिन्, इणस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a particular race or people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृभ्
जृभ् जृभ् or जृम्भ्, cl. 1. A. (poet. also<BR>P.) जृम्भते, -ति, or जर्भते, जजृम्भे,<BR>जृम्भिष्यते, जृम्भितुम्, to open the mouth, yawn,<BR>gape; to gape open, open (as a flower), burst open; fly<BR>back or recoil (as a bow); to unfold, spread, extend,<BR>expand, occupy a larger circuit; to spread (as sound);<BR>to feel at ease: Caus. जृम्भयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to gape or yawn, cause to expand or unfold;<BR>[cf. Old Germ. chliupu, ‘to split;’ Germ. klaffe,<BR>kluft; Goth. graba; Germ. grabe; Gr. γράφω;<BR>Hib. grabhaim, grafain, grafan; cf. also 1. जभ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भ|जृंभ|जृंभं|जृंभः|जृम्भः
जृम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. gaping, yawning;<BR>bursting open; blossoming, swelling, blowing, being<BR>puffed up; expansion, stretching, expanding; (अस्),<BR>m. a particular animal.<BR>—जृम्भा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>yawning, gaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भक|जृंभकः|जृम्भकः
जृम्भक, अस्, m. a yawner, a sort of demon or<BR>spirit; N. of certain magical formularies for exorcising<BR>the evil spirits supposed to possess weapons; (इका),<BR>f. gaping, yawning; (अम्), n. swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भण|जृंभण|जृम्भणं
जृम्भण, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to gape or yawn;<BR>(अम्), n. gaping, yawning; stretching the limbs;<BR>bursting or gaping open, blossoming, blooming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भमाण
जृम्भमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, gaping, yawning;<BR>opening, blossoming, blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भित|जृंभित|जृम्भितं
जृम्भित, अस्, आ, अम्, opened, expanded; opened (as<BR>a flower), blown; enlarged, increased; done, exerted;<BR>(अम्), n. gaping, yawning; bursting, opening, expansion,<BR>unfolding; developing, coming into view, swelling;<BR>exertion; wish, active search for; a kind of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भिन्
जृम्भिन्, ई, इणी, इ, yawning, gaping; expanding,<BR>blossoming; (इणी), f. the plant Mimosa Octandra,<BR>= एलापर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ 1. जॄ, cl. 4. 9. 1. P. जीर्यति, जृणाति, जर-<BR>ति, जजार, जरिष्यति and जरीष्यति, अजारीत्<BR>and अजरत्, जरितुम् and जरीतुम्, to grow old,<BR>become decrepit, decay, wear out, wither; to be<BR>consumed, perish; to break up or fall to pieces; to<BR>be dissolved or digested; (cl. 1. P.) to make old or de-<BR>crepit; to cause to grow old; cl. 10. P. जारयति,<BR>यितुम्, to become old: Caus. P. जरयति, -यितुम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">Page0350-c+ 78</a>]<BR>to make old, wear out, consume, cause to be con-<BR>sumed; to cause to be digested; to digest: Desid.<BR>जिजरिषति, जिजरीषति, जिजीर्षति: Intens. जेजीर्-<BR>यते, जाजर्ति; [cf. Hib. crionaim, ‘I dry, wither;’<BR>criona, ‘old, ancient:’ Gr. γέρων, γεραιός, γραῦς,<BR>γῆρας: Lat. grânum for gârnum: Goth. kaurn:<BR>Germ. Korn: Lith. girna.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर|जरः
जर, जरथ, जरण, जरस्, &c. See p. 340.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार|जारः
जार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. becoming old; (अस्), m. a<BR>paramour, gallant, lover, (in the Veda applied to Agni<BR>or to the Sun as the paramour of the dawn); a<BR>confidential friend; (ई), f. a particular herb or medi-<BR>cament; a N. of Durgā; [cf. Goth. hôrs; Germ.<BR>Hure.]<BR>—जार-गर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, pregnant by a<BR>paramour.<BR>—जार-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, a bastard, the child<BR>of a woman by her paramour.<BR>—जार-जात or जार-<BR>जातक, अस्, आ, अम्, a bastard; (अस्), m. a plagiarist.<BR>—जार-ता, f. an intrigue, love-affair.<BR>—जार-द्वय,<BR>अम्, n. a couple of gallants.<BR>—जार-भरा, f. an<BR>adulteress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारक
जारक, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to decay; promoting<BR>digestion, digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारण|जारणं
जारण, अम्, n. the act of causing to decay; pro-<BR>moting digestion; calcining or oxidizing metals; a<BR>condiment, a digester; (ई), f. a kind of cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारतिनेय
जारतिनेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Jaratī; a<BR>patronymic from Jaratin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारत्कारव
जारत्कारव, अस्, m. a patronymic from Jarat-<BR>kāru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारद्गव
जारद्गव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जरद्-गव), scil.<BR>वीथि, the path of the old ox, (according to Varāha-<BR>mihira the portion of the moon's path occupied by<BR>the constellations Śravaṇā, Dhaniṣṭhā, and Śata-<BR>bhiṣaj, or according to other authorities that occupied<BR>by Vi-śākhā, Anu-rādhā, and Jyeṣṭhā.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारमाण्य
जारमाण्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Jaramāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारासन्धि
जारासन्धि, इस्, m. (fr. जरा-सन्ध), a patro-<BR>nymic of Saha-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारिणी
जारिणी, f., Ved. a woman who has a paramour,<BR>enamoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारुज
जारुज, अस्, आ, अम्, = जरायु-ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्ण|जीर्णं|जीर्णः
जीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, old, ancient; worn out, wasted,<BR>withered, decayed, ruined, in ruins; digested; (अस्),<BR>m. an old man; a tree; cumin-seed; (आ), f. large<BR>cumin-seed; (अम्), n. decrepitude, old age; benja-<BR>min.<BR>—जीर्ण-ज्वर or जीर्णामय-ज्वर, अस्, m. a<BR>lingering fever with diminishing intensity.<BR>—जीर्ण-<BR>ज्वरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, affected with the above fever.<BR>—जीर्ण-टीका, f. ‘the ancient commentary,’ title of<BR>an astronomical work.<BR>—जीर्ण-ता, f. or जीर्ण-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. old age; infirmity, decay.<BR>—जीर्ण-दारु,<BR>उस्, m. the plant Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR>—जीर्ण-<BR>पत्त्रिका, f. ‘having withered leaves,’ N. of a plant,<BR>= वंश-पत्त्री.<BR>—जीर्ण-पर्ण, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>‘having withered leaves,’ the plant Nauclea Cadamba.<BR>—जीर्ण-फञ्जी, f. = जीर्ण-दारु.<BR>—जीर्ण-बुध्न,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of Lodhra.<BR>—जीर्ण-बुध्नक, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of Cyperus.<BR>—जीर्ण-वज्र, अम्, n. a gem,<BR>said to be a sort of diamond.<BR>—जीर्ण-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, old decayed.<BR>—जीर्ण-वस्त्र, अम्, n. old, worn<BR>or tattered raiment; (अस्, आ, अम्), wearing old clothes.<BR>—जीर्ण-वाटिका, f. a ruined house.<BR>—जीर्ण-व्रध्-<BR>नक, अस्, m. a fragrant grass, Cyperus Rotundus.<BR>—जीर्णोद्धार (˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, m. the repairing of<BR>what is worn out, renewal, repairs.<BR>—जीर्णोद्धृत<BR>(˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, rescued from decay, repaired.<BR>—जीर्णोद्यान (˚ण-उद्˚), अम्, n. a neglected garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णक
जीर्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, almost dried up or withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णि|जीर्णिः
जीर्णि, इस्, इस्, इ, decrepit with age; (इस्), f. old age,<BR>infirmity, decay; digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ 2. जॄ, cl. 1. A., Ved. जरते, &c., to<BR>move, approach, come near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ 3. जॄ, cl. 1. A., Ved. जरते, to crackle<BR>(as fire); to roar; to call out to, address, in-<BR>voke, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरणा
जरणा, जरितृ, जरूथ, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतव्य
जेतव्य जेतव्य. See p. 347, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतृ
जेतृ जेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. rt. 1. जि), victorious,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">Page0351-a+ 71</a>]<BR>triumphant; surpassing, excelling; gaining; (ता),<BR>m. a victor, conqueror; N. of a Vedic poet who was<BR>son of Madhu-cchandas; N. of a prince who had a<BR>garden near Śrāvastī in which Śākya-muni pro-<BR>mulgated his doctrines.<BR>—जेत-वन, अम्, n. (for<BR>जेतृ+वन), the wood of Jetṛ, N. of a grove or<BR>garden near Śrāvastī where Śākya-muni or Buddha<BR>promulgated his doctrines.<BR>—जेतवनीय, आस्, m. pl.<BR>N. of a Buddhist school.<BR>—जेत-साह्वय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>called after Jetṛ.<BR>—जेताराम, अस्, m. (for जेतृ+<BR>आर्˚), = जेत-वन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0350-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेत्व
जेत्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be gained or conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमन्
जेमन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. surpassing, excelling; (आ),<BR>m. excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष
जेष, अस्, m., Ved. winning, gaining, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्ताक|जेंताक|जेंताकः|जेन्ताकः
जेन्ताक जेन्ताक, अस्, m. a dry hot bath or<BR>heated chamber for inducing perspiration in rheuma-<BR>tism, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्य
जेन्य जेन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. जन), Ved. of<BR>noble origin (γενναῖος); genuine, true.<BR>—जेन्या-<BR>वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having genuine or true wealth,<BR>an epithet of the Aśvins; also of Indra and Agni;<BR>(Sāy.) having acquired wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमन|जेमनं
जेमन जेमन. See under rt. जिम्, p. 347.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेय|जेयः
जेय जेय. See p. 347, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेलक
जेलक जेलक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष्
जेष् जेष्, cl. 1. A. जेषते, &c., to move,<BR>go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष
जेष जेष. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेह्
जेह् जेह् (related to 1. जभ् and जृभ्),<BR>cl. 1. A., Ved. जेहते, जिजेहे, जेहिष्यते,<BR>जेहितुम्, to open the mouth, breathe heavily, gasp,<BR>gape, open wide, yawn; (Sāy.) to reach, go towards,<BR>strive after: Caus. जेहयति, अजिजेहत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेहमान
जेहमान, अस्, आ, अम्, gaping, opening wide;<BR>(Sāy.) going towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जै
जै जै, cl. 1. P. जायति, जजौ, जास्यति, जा-<BR>तुम्, to wane, decline, fade away, perish; [cf.<BR>1. ज्या.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैगीषव्य|जैगीषव्यः
जैगीषव्य जैगीषव्य, अस्, m. (fr. जिगीषु),<BR>N. of an ancient Ṛṣi often named in connection<BR>with Asita Devala.<BR>—जैगीषव्येश्वर (˚य-ईश्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga in Vārāṇasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्र|जैत्रं|जैत्रः
जैत्र जैत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. 1. जि), victorious,<BR>triumphant, leading to victory, overcoming, surpass-<BR>ing, superior; (अस्), m. a conqueror, victor; N. of a<BR>son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; (ई), f. the plant Sesbania<BR>Ægyptiaca; (अम्), n. victory, triumph, superiority.<BR>—जैत्र-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a triumphant<BR>car; (अस्), m. a victor, a conqueror, a hero; a<BR>triumphant car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्रायणि
जैत्रायणि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Jaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैन|जैनः
जैन जैन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जिन), relating to<BR>the Jinas; (अस्), m. a Jaina, a teacher of heterodox<BR>notions, the chief of which are the supremacy of<BR>certain Jinas or great saints over the gods of the<BR>Hindūs, a denial of the divine authority of the Vedas,<BR>and a disregard of the distinction of castes; N. of a<BR>prince of Kaśmīra.<BR>—जैन-तरङ्गिणी, f. a history<BR>of Kaśmīra by Śrīvara.<BR>—जैनाश्रम (˚न-आश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a Jaina monastery.<BR>—जैनेन्द्र (˚न-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैन्य
जैन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the Jainas (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैपाल|जैपालः
जैपाल जैपाल, अस्, m. (= जय-पाल), a<BR>plant, Croton Tiglium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमन्त
जैमन्त जैमन्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमन्तायन
जैमन्तायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Jai-<BR>manta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनि|जैमिनिः
जैमिनि जैमिनि, इस्, m., N. of a celebrated<BR>saint and philosopher, the pupil of Vyāsa and founder<BR>of the Pūrva (or Karma) Mimāṃsā school. He is said<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">Page0351-b+ 70</a>]<BR>to have acted as Udgātṛ at the sacrifice of Janam-<BR>ejaya (Mahā-bh. I. 2046), and to have received<BR>the Sāma-veda from Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनीय
जैमिनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Jaimini; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a school of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमूत
जैमूत जैमूत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जीमूत), relating<BR>to Jīmūta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैयट|जैयटः
जैयट जैयट, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Kaiyaṭa; (sometimes spelt जैगट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैय्यट|जैय्यटः
जैय्यट, अस्, m., N. of a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैव
जैव जैव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जीव), relating to<BR>Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवन्तायन
जैवन्तायन, अस्, m. or जैवन्तायनि, इस्, m.<BR>or जैवन्ति, इस्, m. a patronymic from Jīvanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवलि
जैवलि, इस्, m. (fr. जीवल), a patronymic of Pra-<BR>vāhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक, अस्, ई, अम्, long-lived, one for whom<BR>long life is desired; thin, lean; (अस्), m. the moon;<BR>camphor (as a synonym of the moon); a peasant; a<BR>drug, medicament; a son; [cf. जीवातु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवि
जैवि, इस्, m. or जैवेय, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Jīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैष्णव
जैष्णव जैष्णव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जिष्णु), re-<BR>lating to a conqueror, relating to Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्म्य|जैह्म्यं
जैह्म्य जैह्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. जिह्म), crooked-<BR>ness (moral or physical), deceit, falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्व
जैह्व जैह्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. जिह्वा), belonging<BR>or relating to the tongue, lying on the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्वाकात
जैह्वाकात, अस्, ई, अम्, an adj. derived fr. जिह्वा-<BR>कात्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्व्य|जैह्व्यं
जैह्व्य, अम्, n. the pleasure of taste (derived<BR>from the tongue), pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोगू
जोगू जोगू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (fr. rt. गु), Ved. praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्ग|जोंगं
जोङ्ग जोङ्ग or जोङ्गक, अम्, n. aloe wood,<BR>Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गट|जोंगट|जोंगटः|जोङ्गटः
जोङ्गट जोङ्गट, अस्, m. longing, earnest<BR>wish, eager desire, the longing of a pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोटिङ्ग|जोटिंग|जोटिंगः|जोटिङ्गः
जोटिङ्ग जोटिङ्ग, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva;<BR>a devotee, an ascetic who subjects himself to the<BR>severest penances; the sacrificial cord (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोड|जोडः
जोड जोड, the chin; [cf. जहि-जोड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोनराज|जोनराजः
जोनराज जोन-राज, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Rāja-taraṅgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोन्नाला
जोन्नाला जोन्नाला, f. = यवनाल, the plant<BR>Andropogon Saccharatus; also जोन्ताला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोल
जोल जोल, N. of a mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोष|जोषं|जोषः
जोष जोष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. जुष्), satisfac-<BR>tion, approval, pleasure, enjoyment, felicity, happiness;<BR>(जोषम् आ, Ved. to one's satisfaction, abundantly;<BR>अनु जोषम्, according to one's pleasure, willingly);<BR>(अम्), ind. according to one's wish or liking, happily,<BR>with ease, without effort; well; silently; जोषम्<BR>आस्, to remain quiet or silent; जोषम् आस्स्व, be<BR>thou quiet, keep thou silent; [cf. अ-जोष.]<BR>—जोष-<BR>वाक, अस्, m., Ved. unintelligible words, chattering<BR>nonsense; (Sāy.) words which ought to please but<BR>do not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषण|जोषणं
जोषण, अम्, n. liking; satisfaction, approval;<BR>choosing; (आ), f. the expression of satisfaction by the<BR>word जुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषयितव्य
जोषयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made dear or<BR>agreeable, to be reflected upon or thought about,<BR>obscure, unintelligible (in words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषयितृ
जोषयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or जोष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ,<BR>loving, cherishing, fostering, taking care of; (Sāy.)<BR>serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषस्
जोषस् in वि-जोषस्, स-जोषस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोष्य
जोष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. delightful, agreeable, wel-<BR>come, satisfactory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषा
जोषा जोषा, f. = योषा, a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिका
जोषिका जोषिका, f. = जालिका, a cluster of<BR>young buds, a bud, a germ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषित्
जोषित् जोषित् or जोषिता, f. = योषित्, a<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोहूत्र
जोहूत्र जोहूत्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. ह्वे), Ved.<BR>making a loud noise, neighing; calling out, challeng-<BR>ing to battle, neighing (as a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जौमर
जौमर जौमर, अम्, n., scil. व्या-करण,<BR>the grammar composed by Jumara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जौलायनभक्त
जौलायनभक्त जौलायन-भक्त, अम्, n. the<BR>district inhabited by the Jaulāyanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जौहोत्यादिक
जौहोत्यादिक जौहोत्यादिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>जुहोत्य्-आदि), belonging to the class of roots begin-<BR>ning with हु, i. e. to the third class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ 1. ज्ञ = ज्ञु = जानु, the knee, in ऊर्-<BR>ध्व-ज्ञ. (For 2. ज्ञ see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञा
ज्ञा 1. ज्ञा, cl. 9. P. A. जानाति, जानीते, ज-<BR>ज्ञौ, जज्ञे, ज्ञास्यति, -ते, अज्ञासीत्, अज्ञास्त,<BR>ज्ञातुम्, [irreg. forms, जानथ for जानीथ Mahā-<BR>bh. II. 842, जानत for जानीत II. 2397, जिजाहि for<BR>जाज्ञाहि = जानीहि, know thou, XIII. 4495, अभ्य्-अनु-<BR>जानिथास् for अभ्य्-अन्व्-अजानीथास् XIV. 1641, जान-<BR>मान pres. part.], to know, have knowledge, become<BR>acquainted with; to perceive, apprehend, understand,<BR>experience; to recognise; to ascertain, investigate;<BR>to know as, know or perceive that, regard or consider<BR>as (with acc. of the object and predicate, e. g. तस्य<BR>मां तनयां जानीत, know me to be his daughter);<BR>to be conversant or familiar with; to visit as a friend<BR>(Ved.); to acknowledge, approve, allow, permit; to<BR>recognise as one's own, take possession of; to act, en-<BR>gage in (with gen. of the instrument, e. g. सर्पिषो for<BR>सर्पिषा जानीते, he engages in sacrifice with clarified<BR>butter): Caus. ज्ञापयति or ज्ञपयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अजिज्ञपत्, to make known, teach, make acquainted<BR>with, inform, announce, notify; to give information;<BR>A. to request, ask: Desid. A. जिज्ञासते (ep. also P.),<BR>to wish to know, &c.; to investigate, examine, wish<BR>to learn; to conjecture, suppose: Desid. of Caus.<BR>जिज्ञापयिषति and जिज्ञपयिषति and ज्ञीप्सति, to<BR>wish to make known or inform: Pass. of Desid. of<BR>Caus. ज्ञीप्स्यते, to be wished or intended to be in-<BR>formed: Intens. जाज्ञायते, जाज्ञाति, जाज्ञेति; [cf.<BR>Lat. gna, gno, in gnârus, (g)nosco, cognosco,<BR>ignoro; perhaps gloria for gnoria: Gr. γνω in<BR>γνῶθι, ἔγνων, γνῶσις; (γ)νοέω, (γ)νοῦς; γιγνώ-<BR>σκω: Old Germ. chna, chnâta, chnât: Eng. know:<BR>Goth. kaun: Old Germ. chan: Germ. kann,<BR>kenne: Lith. zinnaù, ‘I know;’ zinne, sazinne:<BR>Slav. najû: Hib. gnia, ‘knowledge;’ gnic; gno,<BR>‘ingenious;’ gnas, ‘custom, use.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
2. ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what knows, a knower,<BR>knowing, familiar with (often in comp., e. g. धर्म-<BR>ज्ञ, familiar with the law; सर्व-ज्ञ, knowing<BR>everything); intelligent, wise; (अस्), m. a wise and<BR>learned man, especially one possessed of sacred learn-<BR>ing or religious knowledge; the sentient soul; Budha<BR>who was first of the lunar line and regent of the planet<BR>Mercury; the planet Mars or its regent; an epithet<BR>of Brahmā; [cf. Lat. beni-gnus, mali-gnus.]<BR>—ज्ञ-<BR>ता, f. (at the end of a comp.) knowledge of, familiarity<BR>with; intelligence.<BR>—ज्ञम्मन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, think-<BR>ing one's self wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञक
ज्ञक, अस्, अका or इका, m. f. a diminutive fr. 2. ज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञपित|ज्ञपितः
ज्ञपित, अस्, आ, अम्, made known, informed,<BR>taught, expounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्त|ज्ञप्तः
ज्ञप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, made known, = ज्ञपित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्ति|ज्ञप्तिः
ज्ञप्ति, इस्, f. understanding, apprehension, the<BR>exercise of the intellectual faculty; promulgating,<BR>making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञा
2. ज्ञा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) know-<BR>ing, familiar with [cf. ऋत-ज्ञा, पद-ज्ञा, and 2.<BR>ज्ञ]; (आ), f. in epic poetry sometimes a shortened<BR>form of आ-ज्ञा, the initial vowel of the latter being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">Page0352-a+ 81</a>]<BR>irregularly elided after a preceding final ए and ओ (e. g.<BR>तेऽज्ञया, by thy order, Mahā-bh. 1. 3168).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0351-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात|ज्ञातं
ज्ञात, अस्, आ, अम्, known, ascertained, compre-<BR>hended, perceived, understood; आं ज्ञातम्, Ah!<BR>I know (lit. it is known).<BR>—ज्ञात-नन्दन, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Vīra, the twenty-fourth Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—ज्ञात-मात्रे, ind. on its being<BR>ascertained merely.<BR>—ज्ञात-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. a<BR>man completely versed in any science or Śāstra.<BR>—ज्ञाताधर्म-कथा (˚त-अध्˚ or ˚ता-ध˚ ?),<BR>f. title of one of the twelve sacred books of the<BR>Jainas.<BR>—ज्ञातान्वय (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘of known<BR>lineage,’ a name of Vardhamāna, the last Jina or<BR>Jaina pontiff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातक
ज्ञातक, अस्, आ, अम्, known, &c. See ज्ञात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातल
ज्ञातल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातलेय
ज्ञातलेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातव्य|ज्ञातव्यं
ज्ञातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be known or understood,<BR>to be investigated or inquired after; perceptible, con-<BR>ceivable; to be considered as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाति|ज्ञातिः
ज्ञाति, इस्, m. a paternal relation, a kinsman in ge-<BR>neral, a father, a brother; a distant kinsman, one<BR>who does not participate in the oblations offered to de-<BR>ceased ancestors; (इस्), f., N. of a woman; (according<BR>to the Schol. ज्ञाति is a paternal, and सम्-बन्धिन् a<BR>maternal relation; the original meaning of ज्ञाति may<BR>be ‘intimately acquainted;’ cf. Gr. γνωτός, γνωτή;<BR>Goth. knôdi.)<BR>—ज्ञाति-कर्मन्, अ, n. or ज्ञाति-<BR>कार्य, अम्, n. the act or duty of a kinsman.<BR>—ज्ञाति-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. relationship, consanguinity.<BR>—ज्ञाति-<BR>द्रव्य-विनाकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of relations<BR>and wealth.<BR>—ज्ञाति-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a<BR>relative; an epithet of Pūrṇa.<BR>—ज्ञाति-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the condition of a kinsman, relationship, kin.<BR>—ज्ञाति-भेद, अस्, m. dissension among relatives.<BR>—ज्ञाति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has near rela-<BR>tions.<BR>—ज्ञाति-मुख, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the<BR>appearance or character of a relative.<BR>—ज्ञाति-विद्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, one who has or makes near relations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातृ
ज्ञातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, knowing, wise, intelligent,<BR>a knower; (ता), m. an acquaintance; a bail, a<BR>surety; [cf. Gr. γνωστήρ.]<BR>—ज्ञातृ-त्व, अम्, n. or<BR>ज्ञातृ-ता, f. knowledge, information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातेय|ज्ञातेयं
ज्ञातेय, अम्, n. relationship, affinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात्र
ज्ञात्र, अम्, n., Ved. the faculty of perception,<BR>intelligence, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात्वा
ज्ञात्वा, ind. having known, having ascertained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञान|ज्ञानं
ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowing, understanding, becoming<BR>acquainted with, knowledge; sacred or religious<BR>knowledge, especially that which is derived from<BR>meditation on the higher truths of religion and<BR>philosophy and which teaches man his own nature<BR>and how he may be reunited to the supreme spirit;<BR>knowledge about anything, cognizance, consciousness<BR>(e. g. तस्य ज्ञानात्, with his knowledge; अ-ज्ञानात्<BR>तस्य, without his knowledge or cognizance; ज्ञा-<BR>नाद् अ-ज्ञानाद् वा, knowingly or ignorantly; विगत-<BR>ज्ञान, one who has lost consciousness); conscience;<BR>organ of intelligence, sense.<BR>—ज्ञान-कन्द, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—ज्ञान-काण्ड, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. that inner or esoteric portion of the Veda<BR>which relates to true spiritual knowledge or the<BR>knowledge of the supreme spirit as distinguished<BR>from the knowledge of ceremonies; [cf. कर्म-<BR>काण्ड.]<BR>—ज्ञान-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>preceptor.<BR>—ज्ञान-केतु, उस्, m. a mark of intelli-<BR>gence; (उस्, उस्, उ), furnished with marks of in-<BR>telligence.<BR>—ज्ञानकेतु-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>divine being.<BR>—ज्ञान-खण्ड, title of a part of the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—ज्ञान-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, attainable<BR>by the understanding.<BR>—ज्ञान-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘filled<BR>with knowledge,’ N. of a scholar; also of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—ज्ञान-चक्षुस्, उस्, n. the eye of intelligence,<BR>inner eye, mind's eye, intellectual vision.<BR>—ज्ञान-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n. true knowledge, knowledge of God.<BR>—ज्ञान-तपस्, अस्, n. penance consisting in the cul-<BR>tivation of true knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-तस्, ind. know-<BR>ingly, intuitively, designedly; ज्ञानतोऽज्ञानतो वा,<BR>knowingly or unknowingly.<BR>—ज्ञान-द, अस्, m. an<BR>imparter of knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘given<BR>by knowledge,’ N. of a scholar.<BR>—ज्ञान-दर्पण,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-b" target="_blank">Page0352-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. ‘mirror of true knowledge,’ a N. of Mañju-<BR>śrī.<BR>—ज्ञान-दीप, अस्, m. the lamp of knowledge,<BR>knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-दुर्बल, अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>ficient in knowledge, ignorant.<BR>—ज्ञान-निश्चय,<BR>अस्, m. soundness of knowledge, certainty, ascertain-<BR>ment.<BR>—ज्ञान-निष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged in<BR>cultivating true knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञानपत, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>an adj. derived from the next.<BR>—ज्ञान-पति, इस्, m.<BR>the lord of knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-पर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>versed in spiritual wisdom.<BR>—ज्ञान-पावन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, purifying knowledge, refining the understanding;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—ज्ञान-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>preceded by knowledge or wisdom.<BR>—ज्ञान-प्र-<BR>काश, अस्, m. title of a poem by Jagajjīvana-dāsa.<BR>—ज्ञान-प्रदीप, अस्, m. title of the second book<BR>of the Yoga-sāra-saṅgraha.<BR>—ज्ञान-प्रभ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man; also of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ज्ञान-प्र-<BR>वाद, अम्, n. title of one of the fourteen Pūrvas or<BR>older writings of the Jainas.<BR>—ज्ञान-प्रस्थान,<BR>अम्, n. ‘system or method of knowledge,’ title of a<BR>Buddhist work.<BR>—ज्ञान-बोधिनी, f. ‘awakening<BR>knowledge,’ title of a philosophical treatise composed<BR>by Śaṅkara.<BR>—ज्ञान-भास्कर, अस्, m. ‘sun of<BR>knowledge,’ title of a medical compilation.<BR>—ज्ञान-<BR>मण्डप, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘temple of knowledge,’ N.<BR>of a temple.<BR>—ज्ञान-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>of knowledge, containing knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-<BR>मुक्तावली, f. ‘necklace of knowledge,’ title of an<BR>astronomical work.<BR>—ज्ञान-मुद्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the impress of wisdom, wise.<BR>—ज्ञान-मूल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, founded on spiritual knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-<BR>मेरु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—ज्ञान-रत्नावली, f.<BR>title of a book.<BR>—ज्ञान-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of know-<BR>ledge,’ N. of the author of the Siddhānta-sundara.<BR>—ज्ञानर्षि-भास्कराचार्य (˚न-ऋष्˚, ˚र-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—ज्ञान-लक्षण, अम्, आ,<BR>n. f. indication, sign, means of knowing or inferring;<BR>(in logic) sign or proof or characteristic of knowledge;<BR>subsequent derived from antecedent knowledge.<BR>—ज्ञान-वज्र, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist author.<BR>—ज्ञान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, endowed with knowledge<BR>or science, knowing, familiar with, intelligent, wise,<BR>learned, having spiritual knowledge; (आन्), m., N. of<BR>a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ज्ञान-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>poet.<BR>—ज्ञान-वापी, f. ‘pool of divine knowledge,’<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—ज्ञान-विज्ञान, अम्, n. sacred and<BR>miscellaneous knowledge; the Vedas with the sup-<BR>plementary branches of knowledge, medicine, arms,<BR>&c.<BR>—ज्ञान-विभूति-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘filled with<BR>superhuman knowledge,’ N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ज्ञान-विलास-काव्य, अम्, n. title of a poem.<BR>—ज्ञान-शक्ति, इस्, f. capacity of knowing.<BR>—ज्ञा-<BR>न-शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘the science of knowing<BR>the future,’ a manual of fortune-telling.<BR>—ज्ञान-<BR>श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, pre-eminent in wisdom.<BR>—ज्ञा-<BR>न-हस्तिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—ज्ञानाकर<BR>(˚न-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘mine of knowledge,’ N. of a<BR>son of Buddha Mahābhijñājñānābhibhū; N. of a<BR>Buddha.<BR>—ज्ञानात्मन् (˚न-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, all-wise.<BR>—ज्ञानानन्द (˚न-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘joy of know-<BR>ledge,’ N. of an author.<BR>—ज्ञानानुत्पाद (˚न-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. non-production of knowledge, folly, ignorance.<BR>—ज्ञानामृत (˚न-अम्˚), अम्, n. ‘nectar of<BR>knowledge,’ title of a grammar.<BR>—ज्ञानार्णव (˚न-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘ocean of knowledge,’ title of a manual<BR>of medicine composed by Yama-rāja; title of a<BR>prayer-book.<BR>—ज्ञानावरणीय (˚न-आव्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be covered or obstructed by knowledge, (an<BR>act which is considered) to be impeded by knowledge;<BR>also written ज्ञानवरणीय.<BR>—ज्ञानावलोकालङ्का-<BR>र (˚न-अवलोक-अल्˚), अस्, m. title of a Buddhist work.<BR>—ज्ञानावस्थित (˚न-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, engaged in<BR>cultivating wisdom.<BR>—ज्ञानेन्द्र-सरस्वती (˚न-<BR>इन्˚), m., N. of a scholiast on the Siddhānta-kaumudī.<BR>—ज्ञानेन्द्रिय (˚न-इन्˚), अम्, n. an organ of per-<BR>ception or sensation, of which there are five, viz.<BR>the skin, tongue, eye, ear, and nose; see इन्द्रिय.<BR>—ज्ञानोद-तीर्थ (˚न-उद्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha; ‘the Tīrtha of the waters of knowledge.’<BR>—ज्ञानोल्का (˚न-उल्˚), f. ‘the meteor of know-<BR>ledge,’ N. of a Samādhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानिक
ज्ञानिक, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of comp. = ज्ञान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानिन्
ज्ञानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, endowed with knowledge or<BR>intelligence, intelligent, wise, a knower; (ई), f. an<BR>astrologer, a fortune-teller, a man prescient of future<BR>events; a sage, one possessing religious wisdom.<BR>—ज्ञानि-त्व, अम्, n. prescience, fortune-telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानीय
ज्ञानीय, nom. P. ज्ञानीयति, -यितुम्, to wish for<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापक|ज्ञापकः
ज्ञापक, अस्, आ, अम्, making or causing to know,<BR>teaching, designing, informing; (अस्), m. a teacher,<BR>an instructor; a commander, a master; a master of<BR>requests, an officer of the court of a Hindū prince;<BR>(अम्), n. a significant expression or one which gives<BR>some particular information, a precept, a rule, a name<BR>given to those rules of Pāṇini which imply or indi-<BR>cate some other grammatical laws than those which<BR>would follow from the mere words of the Jñāpaka<BR>rules themselves.<BR>—ज्ञापक-समुच्चय, अस्, m.<BR>a work by Puruṣottama-deva giving a collection of<BR>the Jñāpaka rules contained in Pāṇini's grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापन|ज्ञापनं
ज्ञापन, अम्, n. making known, announcing,<BR>apprizing, informing, teaching, notification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापनीय
ज्ञापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made known or<BR>announced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापित
ज्ञापित, अस्, आ, अम्, made known, informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाप्ति|ज्ञाप्तिः
ज्ञाप्ति, इस्, f. making known, apprizing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाप्य
ज्ञाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made known or in-<BR>formed, to be told.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञास्
ज्ञास्, m., Ved. a near relative; [cf. ज्ञाति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञीप्स्यमान
ज्ञीप्स्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being intended to be<BR>informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञेय|ज्ञेयं
ज्ञेय, अस्, आ, अम्, cognizable, to be ascertained or<BR>investigated, to be learned or understood, to be per-<BR>ceived or inquired about; to be regarded as.<BR>—ज्ञेय-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, understanding what is to be under-<BR>stood; the mind.<BR>—ज्ञेय-ता, f. or ज्ञेय-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. perceptibility, intelligibleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञु
ज्ञु ज्ञु = जानु, the knee, in अभि-ज्ञु, ऊर्-<BR>ध्व-ज्ञु, &c.<BR>—ज्ञु-बाध्, -भात्, त्, त्, Ved. bending<BR>the knees; [cf. Gr. πρόχνυ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्मन्
ज्मन् ज्मन् (fr. जम् = गम्), only occurring<BR>in the Ved. loc. ज्मन्, in (his) course or way;<BR>(Sāy.) in the sky; on the earth; [cf. उरु-ज्मन् and<BR>पृथु-ज्मन्.]<BR>—ज्म-या, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. going<BR>on or following a course; (Sāy.) on the earth (as if<BR>ज्मया).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्मायत्|ज्मायन्त्
ज्मायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (pres. part. of a nom. fr.<BR>ज्मन्), Ved. making a way or course; (Sāy.) going<BR>on or reaching the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या 1. ज्या, cl. 9. P., 4. A. जिनाति, जीयते,<BR>जिज्यौ, जिज्ये, ज्यास्यति, -ते, अज्यासीत्, ज्या-<BR>तुम्, to overpower, oppress, to deprive of property,<BR>&c., (in the Veda often connected with rt. हन्, e. g.<BR>जीयते हन्ति, ‘he oppresses and kills;’ and in the<BR>Brāhmaṇas applied to the oppressions of the Brāhmans<BR>and Vaiśyas by the Kṣatriyas); (cl. 4. A.) to be<BR>oppressed, treated badly, deprived of property, &c.;<BR>(cl. 9. P.) to become old: Caus. ज्यापयति, see<BR>ज्यापय below: Desid. P. जिज्यासति, to wish to over-<BR>power or oppress: Intens. जेजीयते, जाज्याति; [cf.<BR>Gr. βιάω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीत
जीत or जीन, अस्, आ, अम्, oppressed, overpowered;<BR>become old. See also under जीत, p. 348, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्य
ज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
2. ज्या, f. overpowering force or strength (βία, cf.<BR>परम-ज्या); excessive demand, importunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यान|ज्यानं
ज्यान, अम्, n., Ved. oppression, tyrannizing over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानि|ज्यानिः
ज्यानि, इस्, f. oppression; deprivation, loss; decay,<BR>infirmity, old age; quitting, abandoning; a river,<BR>a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यापय
ज्यापय, nom. P. ज्यापयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>old, to call a person old, (supposed to be a nom. fr.<BR>ज्य substituted for वृद्ध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायस्
ज्यायस्, आन्, असी, अस् (considered by grammarians to<BR>be a compar. of प्र-शस्य and वृद्ध, for which<BR>ज्य is substituted), superior, more excellent, greater,<BR>larger, stronger; elder, senior, elder born (opposed<BR>to कनीयस् and अणीयस्); a master; most excellent;<BR>(in law) one who is of age and answerable for his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">Page0353-a+ 80</a>]<BR>own conduct.<BR>—ज्यायस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having<BR>or acknowledging a senior or superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0352-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायस
ज्यायस, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. greater in number (op-<BR>posed to कानीयस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायिष्ठ
ज्यायिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (irreg. superl.), the most<BR>excellent; noblest, first, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येय
ज्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be oppressed, to be deprived<BR>of (property &c.); the most excellent, first, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठ|ज्येष्ठः
ज्येष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, the most excellent, noblest,<BR>pre-eminent; first, chief; best, greatest; eldest, very<BR>old, elder, senior, elder born; an elder brother; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a month, for ज्यैष्ठ, q. v.; N. of a<BR>man; (आ), f., N. of the sixteenth or (according to<BR>more modern reckoning) eighteenth lunar mansion<BR>sacred to Indra; the eighth year of a Jupiter<BR>cycle of twelve years; the middle finger; a small<BR>house-lizard; an epithet of the Gaṅgā; a kind of<BR>heroine; misfortune personified as a goddess and the<BR>elder sister of Lakṣmī; (ई), f. a small house-lizard;<BR>(अम्), n. the most excellent, the first, the head; tin;<BR>(अम्), ind. most, extremely; [cf. Hib. gast, ‘an old<BR>woman;’ giostaire, ‘an active old man;’ giostai-<BR>reas, ‘old age.’]<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-घ्नी, f., Ved. = ज्ये-<BR>ष्ठा, the sixteenth lunar mansion.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. best of all; first of all; oldest<BR>of all.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, elder, an elder<BR>one.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-तस्, ind., Ved. according to seniority,<BR>(reckoning) from the eldest.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-ता, f. or<BR>ज्येष्ठ-त्व, अम्, n. superiority; primogeniture,<BR>seniority.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-तात, अस्, m. a father's elder<BR>brother.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-ताति, इस्, f., Ved. superiority;<BR>superior.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-पुष्कर, अम्, n., N. of a renowned<BR>place of pilgrimage.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-बला, f., N. of a<BR>plant, a kind of Balā, = महा-बला, सह-देवी.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-भार्या, f. an elder brother's wife, the<BR>elder, senior or chief wife.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-राज्, ट्, m., Ved.<BR>a sovereign.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-ललिता, f. a particular vow to<BR>be observed in the month Jyeṣṭha (Jyaiṣṭha).<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-वर्ण, अस्, m. one of the first caste, a<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, behaving like<BR>the first-born or eldest brother; (इस्), f. the duties of<BR>seniority.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-श्वश्रू, ऊस्, f. a wife's elder<BR>sister.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-सामन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman;<BR>(आ, आ, अ), a chanter of the Jyeṣṭha-Sāman.<BR>—ज्ये-<BR>ष्ठसामिक, अस्, आ, अम्, an adj. derived from the<BR>last.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-स्तोम, अस्, m., N. of an Ekāha<BR>ceremony.<BR>—ज्येष्ठ-स्थान, अम्, n., N. of a place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—ज्येष्ठांश (˚ठ-अं˚), अस्, m.<BR>the eldest brother's share; the right of primogeniture<BR>or the right of the eldest son to a larger portion of<BR>the patrimonial property than his brothers, — a right<BR>formerly recognized but now obsolete; the best share.<BR>—ज्येष्ठा-मूल or ज्येष्ठा-मूलीय, अस्, m. the<BR>month Jyaiṣṭha.<BR>—ज्येष्ठाम्बु (˚ठ-अम्˚), उस्,<BR>m. the scum of boiled rice or water in which grain<BR>has been washed.<BR>—ज्येष्ठाश्रम (˚ठ-आश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the most excellent order or period in the religious<BR>life of a Brāhman, viz. that of a householder; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), being in that period.<BR>—ज्येष्ठाश्रमिन्, ई,<BR>m. a Brāhman in the order of a householder.<BR>—ज्ये-<BR>ष्ठेश्वर (˚ठ-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga in<BR>Vārāṇasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठिला
ज्येष्ठिला, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ|ज्यैष्ठः
ज्यैष्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a month (May — June),<BR>the month in which the full moon stands in the<BR>constellation Jyeṣṭhā; (ई), f. the full moon in the<BR>month Jyaiṣṭha; a small house-lizard.<BR>—ज्यैष्ठ-<BR>सामन्, a wrong form for ज्येष्ठ-सामन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठिनेय
ज्यैष्ठिनेय, अस्, ई, अम्, born from the elder or<BR>principal wife; ज्यैष्ठिनेयो ज्येष्ठः, the eldest<BR>son and at the same time the son of the father's<BR>first wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ्य|ज्यैष्ठ्यं
ज्यैष्ठ्य, अम्, n. pre-eminence, sovereignty; pre-<BR>cedence, priority of birth, primogeniture, seniority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या 3. ज्या, f. (perhaps fr. rt. 1. ज्या), the<BR>string of a bow, a bow-string; the chord of an arc, a<BR>sine in geometry; [cf. अधि-ज्य, उज्-ज्य, &c.; cf.<BR>also Gr. βιός.]<BR>—ज्या-कार, अस्, m., Ved. one who<BR>makes bow-strings.<BR>—ज्या-घोष, अस्, m. the twang<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">Page0353-b+ 79</a>]<BR>of a bow.<BR>—ज्या-पाश, अस्, m. a bow-string.<BR>—ज्या-<BR>पिण्ड or ज्या-पिण्डक, a sine expressed in figures.<BR>—ज्या-मघ, अस्, m., N. of the father of Vi-<BR>darbha.<BR>—ज्यार्ध (ज्या-अर्˚), अस्, m. the sine of an<BR>arc.<BR>—ज्यार्ध-पिण्ड, a sine expressed in figures.<BR>—ज्या-वाज, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the elasticity<BR>of a bow-string; (Sāy.) a stout or strong bow (as if<BR>a substantive).<BR>—ज्या-वाणेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>warrior-tribe; (अस्), m. a prince of this tribe.<BR>—ज्या-<BR>ह्रोड, अस्, m. a peculiar kind of bow; (औ), m.<BR>du., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—ज्योत्पत्ति (ज्या-उत्˚), इस्, f.<BR>‘the calculation of the length of a chord,’ derivation<BR>of (semi)-chords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यका
ज्यका, f. a bow-string; the chord of an arc in<BR>geometry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्याका
ज्याका, f., Ved. a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्याय
ज्याय, nom. A. ज्यायते, to represent a bow-<BR>string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या 4. ज्या, f. the earth; a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यु
ज्यु ज्यु, cl. 1. A. ज्यवते, &c., to go,<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युत्
ज्युत् ज्युत् (for द्युत्), cl. 1. A. P. ज्योतते,<BR>-ति, to shine: Caus. P. ज्योतयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to shine upon, illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युति|ज्युतिः
ज्युति, इस्, f. (for द्युति), light.<BR>—ज्युति-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, shining, full of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योता
ज्योता, f., Ved. ‘the brilliant or shining one,’ one<BR>of the mystical names of the cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष|ज्योतिषं|ज्योतिषः
ज्योतिष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. ज्योतिस्), relating to the<BR>heavenly bodies, astronomical, astrological; (अस्), m.<BR>an astronomer, astrologer; N. of certain magical<BR>formularies for exorcising the evil spirits supposed to<BR>possess weapons; (अम्), n. astronomy, astrology, the<BR>science of the course of the heavenly bodies and divi-<BR>sions of time resting thereon; N. of one of the six<BR>Vedāṅgas or of a short tract which gives only<BR>such a knowledge of the heavenly bodies as was<BR>required for fixing the days and hours of the Vedic<BR>sacrifices; (ई), f. a star, a planet, an asterism.<BR>—ज्यो-<BR>तिष-तत्त्व, अम्, n. or ज्योतिष-रत्नमाला, f., N.<BR>of two works on astronomy.<BR>—ज्योतिष-विद्या, f. astro-<BR>nomical science.<BR>—ज्योतिष-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. the<BR>whole science of astronomy.<BR>—ज्योतिषी-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. shining, brilliant; (आन्), m., N. of a par-<BR>ticular sun or form of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषिक|ज्योतिषिकः
ज्योतिषिक, a wrong form for ज्यौतिषिक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्क|ज्योतिष्कः
ज्योतिष्क, अस्, m. a luminary, a heavenly body;<BR>the luminaries regarded by the Jainas as a class of deities<BR>arranged under five heads, viz. sun, moon, the planets,<BR>fixed stars, and lunar mansions; the plant Premna<BR>Spinosa; the plant Plumbago Zeylanica; the seed of<BR>Trigonella Fœnum Græcum; N. of a Nāga; N. of<BR>a man; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = ज्योतिष्मती; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a luminous weapon with which Arjuna<BR>destroyed Tamas or darkness personified (see Mahā-<BR>bh. Droṇa-parva 1325); N. of the shining peak of<BR>the Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्
ज्योतिस्, इस्, n. light in various forms and under various<BR>aspects, as the light of the sun, of dawn, of fire, of<BR>lightning, &c.; brightness or clearness of the sky,<BR>daylight (opposed to Tamas); lightning; light ap-<BR>pearing in three forms, viz. fire on the earth, ether<BR>or air in the intermediate region, and sun in the sky;<BR>a glance of the eye, the faculty of seeing, the eye;<BR>the heavenly bodies, the planets and stars (in this<BR>sense pl., e. g. ज्योतिषाम् अयनम्, the course of the<BR>heavenly bodies); sun and moon (in this sense du.,<BR>e. g. ज्योतिषोर् उपसर्गाः, eclipses &c. of the sun<BR>and moon); the light of heaven, the celestial world;<BR>light as the divine principle of life or as the source<BR>of intelligence, intelligence; light as a type of<BR>freedom, of bliss and of victory, [cf. Lat. lux and Gr.<BR>φάος, φῶς]; N. of the Jyotiṣṭoma as applied to<BR>the first and sixth days of the Abhi-plava ceremony<BR>which lasts six days; N. of certain formularies containing<BR>the word ज्योतिस्; a kind of metre consisting of thirty-<BR>two short and sixteen long syllables; the science of<BR>the course of the heavenly bodies, &c., see ज्योतिष;<BR>a mystical term for the letter र्; (इस्), m. fire; the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-c" target="_blank">Page0353-c+ 81</a>]<BR>sun; N. of the plant Trigonella Fœnum Græcum;<BR>N. of a son of Manu Svārociṣa; also of Marut;<BR>[cf. चित्र-ज्योतिस् and दक्षिणा-ज्˚.]<BR>—ज्योतिः-शास्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. the science of astronomy; a work upon<BR>astronomy.<BR>—ज्योतिः-सामन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—ज्योतिः-सिद्धान्त, अस्, m. title of an astronomical<BR>work.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-अग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. preceded by<BR>light or life.<BR>—ज्योतिरथ्या, f., N. of a river; (a wrong<BR>form for ज्योती-रथा.)<BR>—ज्योतिर्-अनीक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having a shining face or appearance.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-<BR>इङ्ग or ज्योतिर्-इङ्गण, अस्, m. ‘moving light,’ a fire-<BR>fly.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-ईश or ज्योतिर्-ईश्वर, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Dhūrta-samāgama.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-गण, अस्,<BR>m. the heavenly bodies collectively.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-जरायु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. surrounded by a brilliant covering;<BR>(Sāy.) brilliant (among the clouds) like an embryo.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-ज्ञ, अस्, m. ‘star-knower,’ an astrologer,<BR>one versed in astronomy.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-ज्वलनार्चि-श्री-<BR>गर्भ (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-धामन्, आ, m., N. of one of the seven<BR>sages in the Manv-antara of Tāmasa.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-भास-<BR>मणि, इस्, m. a kind of gem.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-भासिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, brilliant with light.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-मण्डल, अम्,<BR>n. the stellar sphere.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of light, brilliant, abounding with stars, starry.<BR>—ज्योतिर्मिलिन्, ई, m. (for -मालिन् ?), a fire-fly.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-मुख, अस्, m., N. of one of the monkey-<BR>followers of Rāma.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-लिङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of<BR>several Liṅga temples.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-लेखावलयिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, studded with rows of stars.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-लोक, अस्,<BR>m. the world of light.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing<BR>the stars, an astronomer; creating light (in this<BR>sense rt. 3. विद्, to find).<BR>—ज्योतिर्-विद्या, f. the<BR>science of astronomy, astrology.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-वीज, अम्,<BR>n. ‘seed of light,’ a fire-fly.<BR>—ज्योतिर्-हस्ता, f. an<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—ज्योतिश्-चक्र, अम्, n. ‘circle of<BR>the luminaries,’ the zodiac.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-कण, अस्, m.<BR>a spark of fire.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-कर, अस्, m. ‘light-causer,’<BR>a kind of flower.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, like<BR>flame or fire, blazing, radiant.<BR>—ज्योतिष्कल्प-लता,<BR>f. title of an astrological work.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make light, illumine.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. creating light.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-<BR>टम, अस्, आ, अम्, diffusing the most brilliant light.<BR>—ज्योतिष्टोम, अस्, m. (fr. ज्योतिस्-स्तोम), a Soma<BR>ceremony considered as the typical form of a whole<BR>class of ceremonies; it consists of either four or seven<BR>subdivisions, viz. the Agni-ṣṭoma, Ukthya, Ṣoḍa-<BR>śin, Ati-rātra, or in addition to these the Atyagni-<BR>ṣṭoma, Vāja-peya, and Aptor-yāma.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-ट्व,<BR>अम्, n. luminousness, illumination; the condition of<BR>light.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having brilliant<BR>wings.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-प्रभ, अस्, m. ‘brilliant with light,’<BR>N. of a kind of flower; N. of a Buddha; also of a<BR>Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ज्योतिष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, luminous,<BR>brilliant, shining, belonging to the world of light,<BR>heavenly, celestial; ज्योतिष्मती त्रिष्टुप्, a form of<BR>the Triṣṭubh metre, containing three Pādas of twelve<BR>syllables each and one Pāda of eight syllables; (आन्),<BR>m. the sun; N. of one of the seven suns appearing<BR>at the destruction of the world; N. of the third foot<BR>of Brahmā; N. of a son of Manu Svāyambhuva;<BR>also of Manu Sāvarṇa; N. of a king of Kuśa-dvīpa;<BR>also of a son of Priya-vrata; N. of a mountain; (ती),<BR>f. the night (as illumined by the stars), heart-pea,<BR>Cardiospermum Halicacabum.<BR>—ज्योतिस्-सात्, ind. to<BR>flame, to fire or light; ज्योतिस्सात् कृ, to light,<BR>illumine, set on fire.<BR>—ज्योती-रत, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>serpent-demon.<BR>—ज्योती-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, whose<BR>chariot is light; (Sāy.) bearing fire or the oblation<BR>like a chariot; (अस्), m. the pole-star or in mythology<BR>Dhruva, son of Uttāna-pāda; a kind of serpent;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river which joins the Śoṇa or Sone.<BR>—ज्योती-रस, अस्, m. a kind of gem.<BR>—ज्योती-रूप-<BR>स्वयम्भू, ऊस्, m. Svayambhū (Brahmā) in the<BR>form of light.<BR>—ज्योती-रूपेश्वर (˚प-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्ना
ज्योत्स्ना, f. a moonlight night; moonlight; light,<BR>splendor in general; N. of one of the bodies of<BR>Brahmā; N. of one of the sixteen Kalās of the<BR>moon; an epithet of Durgā; N. of two plants, =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">Page0354-a+ 75</a>]<BR>ज्योत्स्नी and घोषातकी.<BR>—ज्योत्स्ना-काली, f., N. of a<BR>daughter of the moon and wife of Puṣkara who was<BR>a son of Varuṇa.<BR>—ज्योत्स्ना-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘a friend of<BR>the moonlight,’ the bird Chakora or Greek partridge.<BR>—ज्योत्स्ना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, illuminated by the moon,<BR>shining, brilliant.<BR>—ज्योत्स्ना-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>tree or tripod of a lamp, a lamp-stand, candlestick.<BR>—ज्योत्स्नेश (˚ना-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord or husband of<BR>the moonlight,’ the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0353-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्निका
ज्योत्स्निका, f., N. of a plant, = कोषातकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नी
ज्योत्स्नी, f. a moonlight night; a small cucumber,<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca; a kind of perfume, = रेणुका;<BR>(a wrong form for ज्यौत्स्नी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौतिष
ज्यौतिष, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौतिषिक|ज्यौतिषिकः
ज्यौतिषिक, अस्, m. one who knows the Jyotiṣa,<BR>an astronomer, astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्न|ज्यौत्स्नः
ज्यौत्स्न, अस्, ई, अम्, luminous especially with<BR>moonlight; (अस्), m. the time of moonlight, the<BR>light half of a month; (ई), f. a full moon night; N.<BR>of a plant, = पटोलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्निका
ज्यौत्स्निका, f. a moonlight night; (perhaps an<BR>incorrect form for ज्योत्स्निका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यो
ज्यो ज्यो, cl. 1. A. ज्यवते, &c., to advise,<BR>instruct, order; observe a vow or any reli-<BR>gious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योक्
ज्योक् ज्योक्, ind. long, for a long time, for<BR>a long while; ज्योक्तमाम्, superl. ind. for the longest<BR>time, longest.<BR>—ज्योग्-जीवातु, उस्, f. long life; ज्योक्<BR>कृ, to be long about anything, delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योडि
ज्योडि ज्योडि, in names of plants. Cf. कर-<BR>ज्योडि and हस्त-ज्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतयमानक
ज्योतयमानक ज्योतयमानक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>Ved. shining (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिक
ज्योतिक ज्योतिक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga;<BR>(perhaps a wrong reading for ज्योतिष्क.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्
ज्योतिस् ज्योतिस्, &c. See p. 353, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौ
ज्यौ ज्यौ, औस्, m. (a word borrowed fr. the<BR>Gr. Ζεύς), the planet Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रि
ज्रि 1. ज्रि, cl. 1. P. ज्रयति, &c., to over-<BR>power, conquer; to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रय
ज्रय. Cf. पृथु-ज्रय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रयस्
ज्रयस्, अस्, n., Ved. a plain, expanse, space; (Sāy.)<BR>speed; splendor; overpowering; [cf. Zend zarajo.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रयसान
ज्रयसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. spreading, expanding,<BR>occupying space; (Sāy.) going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रि
2. ज्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, in उरु-ज्रि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रि
ज्रि 3. ज्रि or ज्री [cf. rt. 1. जॄ], cl. 1. 10.<BR>9. P. ज्रयति, ज्राययति, ज्रिणाति, &c., to<BR>grow old, to be or become old or decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर्
ज्वर् ज्वर्, cl. 1. P. ज्वरति, जज्वार, ज्वरि-<BR>ष्यति, अज्वारीत्, ज्वरितुम्, to be feverish,<BR>to be hot with fever or passion, to be diseased &c.:<BR>Caus. P. ज्वरयति, -यितुम्, to make feverish: Desid.<BR>जिज्वरिषति: Intens. जाज्वर्यते, जाजूर्ति; [cf. Lat.<BR>a-ger; Hib. gurt, ‘pain, trouble, fierceness;’ Germ.<BR>schwer; Old Germ. swâr, swâri; Germ. quâlen ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ण
जूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्. See rt. 1. जुर्, p. 349, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर|ज्वरः
ज्वर, अस्, m. fever of different kinds (called after<BR>the different doṣas or humors of the body which<BR>are supposed to be affected by them; fever is called<BR>the leader and king of all diseases); fever of the<BR>soul, mental pain, affliction, grief, trouble, sorrow,<BR>distress; (आ), f. fever; (अस्, आ, अम्), heated, raging<BR>(with fever, passion, &c.), excited, inflamed.<BR>—ज्वर-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, febrifuge, anti-febrile, dispelling<BR>fever or ague; (अस्), m. or according to some (ई), f.<BR>the plant Cocculus Cordifolius, = गुडूची; the plant<BR>Chenopodium Album, = वास्तूक.<BR>—ज्वर-चिकित्सा,<BR>f. medical treatment of fever.<BR>—ज्वर-नाशक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, febrifuge.<BR>—ज्वर-निर्णय, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a medical work.<BR>—ज्वर-प्रतीकार, अस्, m. cure<BR>of fever.<BR>—ज्वर-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, febrifuge;<BR>(त्री), f. the plant Rubia Munjista.<BR>—ज्वराग्नि (˚र-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m. feverish heat, the hot paroxysm in<BR>fever.<BR>—ज्वराङ्कुश (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a febrifuge;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">Page0354-b+ 80</a>]<BR>the plant Andropogon Jvarancusa; title of a work<BR>on medicine.<BR>—ज्वराङ्गी (˚र-अङ्˚), f., N. of a<BR>plant, = भद्र-दन्तिका.<BR>—ज्वरान्तक (˚र-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, febrifuge, dispelling fever; (अस्), m.<BR>the plant Cathartocarpus Fistula; a kind of Nimba<BR>growing in Nepal.<BR>—ज्वरान्वित (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>suffering from fever or ague.<BR>—ज्वरापह (˚र-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, febrifuge; (आ), f. a febrifuge, the plant<BR>Medicago Esculenta, = विल्ल-पत्त्री (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरित|ज्वरितः
ज्वरित, अस्, आ, अम्, or ज्वरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, febrile,<BR>feverish, affected with fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वार
ज्वार. See नव-ज्वार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल्
ज्वल् ज्वल्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) ज्वलति,<BR>-ते, जज्वाल, ज्वलिष्यति, अज्वालीत्, ज्वलि-<BR>तुम्, to burn brightly, blaze, flame, glow, shine; to<BR>burn (as a wound); to be ardent: Caus. P. ज्वाल-<BR>यति and ज्वलयति, -यितुम्, to set on fire, light,<BR>kindle, make radiant, illuminate: Desid. जिज्वलि-<BR>षति: Intens. जाज्वल्यते, जाज्वल्ति, to flame vio-<BR>lently, shine strongly, be brilliant; [cf. Hib. gual-<BR>laim, ‘I blacken, burn;’ gual, ‘coal, coals, fire:’<BR>Germ. Kohle: Old Germ. colo: Eng. coal: Lith.<BR>swelù: Old Germ. wallu, walm, wâli.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल|ज्वलः
ज्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, flaming, blazing, shining, bril-<BR>liant; (अस्), m. flame, blaze, light.<BR>—ज्वल-मुखी,<BR>f., N. of a tutelary deity in the family of Lomaśa;<BR>[cf. ज्वाला-मुखी.]<BR>—ज्वलानन (˚ल-आन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the face flaming.<BR>—ज्वला-रासभका-<BR>मय, अस्, m. = जाल-गर्दभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलका
ज्वलका, f. a large flame or blaze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलत्|ज्वलन्त्
ज्वलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, burning, blazing; shining,<BR>radiant, brilliant.<BR>—ज्वलन्-मणि, इस्, इस्, इ, blazing<BR>with jewels; (इस्), m. a brilliant gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलन|ज्वलनः
ज्वलन, अस्, आ, अम्, inflammable, combustible,<BR>flaming, shining; (अस्), m. fire; a N. of the numeral 3;<BR>corrosive alkali; the plant Plumbago Zeylanica; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a daughter of Takṣaka and wife of Ṛceyu [cf.<BR>ज्वाला]; (अम्), n. burning, blazing.<BR>—ज्वलनाश्मन्<BR>(˚न-अश्˚), आ, m. the sun-stone; [cf. सूर्य-कान्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलनीय
ज्वलनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be burnt, combustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलयत्
ज्वलयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, kindling, burning, illu-<BR>mining, blazing, radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलित|ज्वलितः
ज्वलित, अस्, आ, अम्, kindled, burnt, blazing, flam-<BR>ing; (तृणेषु ज्वलितं त्वया, you have lighted a<BR>fire in the grass, i. e. you have had easy work.)<BR>—ज्वलित-नयन, अस्, आ, अम्, fiery-eyed, looking<BR>angrily or fiercely; also ज्वलित-चक्षुस्, ज्वलित-<BR>नेत्र, &c.<BR>—ज्वलितानन (˚त-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the face flaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलिन्
ज्वलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, burning, flaming, shining; (इनी),<BR>f. the plant Sanseviera Zeylanica, = मूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वाल|ज्वालः
ज्वाल, अस्, ई, अम्, burning, blazing; (अस्), m. light,<BR>flame, a torch; (आ), f. a blaze, flame, illumination;<BR>burnt rice; N. of a daughter of Takṣaka and wife<BR>of Ṛkṣa; [cf. Hib. gual, ‘coal.’]<BR>—ज्वाला-खर-<BR>गद and ज्वाला-गर्दभक, अस्, m. = जाल-गर्द-<BR>भ.<BR>—ज्वालाग्नि (˚ल-अग्˚), इस्, m. blazing fire, flame.<BR>—ज्वाला-जिह्व, अस्, m. ‘flame-tongued,’ N. of fire;<BR>N. of an attendant of Skanda; of Śiva; of a Dānava.<BR>—ज्वाला-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘flame-marked,’ fire.<BR>—ज्वा-<BR>ला-मुख, अस्, m. ‘flame-mouthed,’ a class of demons;<BR>(ई), f. a volcano; any place where subterranean fire<BR>or inflammable gas breaks forth, such places being<BR>held sacred by the Hindūs as indicating the presence<BR>of a form of Durgā; (a celebrated Jvālā-mukhī exists<BR>in the hills north-east of the Pañjāb to which pilgrim-<BR>ages are made; the soil abounds with carburetted<BR>hydrogen gas which takes fire upon coming in con-<BR>tact with the external air. According to the legend,<BR>the flame proceeds from the fire which the wife of<BR>Śiva created and in which she burned herself. Śiva<BR>finding that this flame was about to consume the<BR>world, buried it in the hollow of the mountain.<BR>According to another legend, the tongue of Pārvatī<BR>fell at this place. There is a similar volcanic region<BR>in Chinese Tartary where fire is produced by digging<BR>into the earth.)<BR>—ज्वाला-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘flame-liṅga,’<BR>N. of a temple of Śiva.<BR>—ज्वाला-वक्त्र, अस्, m. ‘flame-<BR>mouthed,’ N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR>—ज्वालेश्वर<BR>(˚ल-ईश्˚), N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालिन्
ज्वालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, flaming, blazing; (इनी), f. mystical<BR>name of the letter व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ 1. झ, the ninth consonant of the<BR>Sanskrit alphabet and the aspirate of the preceding<BR>letter.<BR>—झ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound झ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ 2. झ, अस्, आ, अम्, asleep, sleeping; lost,<BR>destroyed; (अस्), m. a peculiar sound; playing a tune,<BR>beating time; a sound like the splashing of water or<BR>the clashing of symbols, jingling, clanking, &c.;<BR>wind accompanied by rain; a stray, a thing lost or<BR>mislaid; a N. of a chief of the Daityas or demons;<BR>an epithet of Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods;<BR>(आ), f. the descent of a cascade, a water-fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झगझगाय
झगझगाय झगझगाय, nom. A. झगझ-<BR>गायते, to sparkle, flash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झङ्कार|झंकार|झंकारः|झङ्कारः
झङ्कार झङ्-कार, अस्, m. or झङ्-कारित, अम्,<BR>n. (fr. the imitative word झम्), a low murmuring<BR>sound, as the buzzing or humming of bees &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झन|झंझन|झंझनं
झञ्झन झञ्झन, अम्, n. (onomatopoetic),<BR>an indistinct noise like the jingling and clanking of<BR>metal ornaments, any ringing or rattling sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झा|झंझा
झञ्झा, f. the noise of the wind or of falling<BR>rain; wind, wind and rain, a hurricane, a gale; a<BR>clang or sharp clanking sound, jingling; raining in<BR>large drops; a stray, anything lost.<BR>—झञ्झानिल<BR>(˚झा-अन्˚), अस्, m. wind with rain, a high wind in<BR>the rainy season, a typhoon or the sort of tempest<BR>frequent during the south-west monsoon.<BR>—झञ्झा-<BR>वात, अस्, m. wind with rain, a storm, a squall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झट्
झट् झट्, cl. 1. P. झटति, &c., to become<BR>matted together or entangled (as hair), to<BR>become confused or intermixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटा
झटा, f. the plant Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटि|झटिः
झटि, इस्, m. a small tree, a shrub, a bush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाट|झाटः
झाट, अस्, m. an arbour, bower, place overgrown<BR>with creepers; a wood, a thicket; cleaning sores or<BR>wounds; (आ or ई), f. jasmine, Jasminum Auriculatum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटल|झाटलः
झाटल, अस्, m. the tree Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटिका
झाटिका or झाटीका, f. = झाटा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटिति
झटिति झटिति, ind. (fr. झट्, an onomato-<BR>poetic word with इति; cf. पटिति), quickly, speedily,<BR>instantly; at once; on the spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झणझण|झणझणं
झणझण झणझण or झणझणा (an ono-<BR>matopoetic word), the jingling or tinkling of orna-<BR>ments; [cf. छनच्छन् and झलज्झला.]<BR>—झण-<BR>झणी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, rattling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झणझणाय
झणझणाय, nom. A. -यते, &c., to jingle,<BR>tinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झणझणायित
झणझणायित, अम्, n. jingling, tinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झणत्कार|झणत्कारः
झणत्कार झणत्-कार or झनत्-कार, अस्,<BR>m. (fr. the imitative sound झणत् and कार), the<BR>jingling, tinkling, or clinking of metallic ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झनज्झना
झनज्झना झनज्झना, flapping noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्
झम् झम्, cl. 1. P. झमति, &c. = छम्<BR>and जम्, to eat, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्प|झंप|झंपः|झम्पः
झम्प झम्प, अस्, आ, m. f. a spring, a jump,<BR>jumping, springing, plunging.<BR>—झम्पाशिन् (˚प-<BR>आश्˚), ई, m. a kingfisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पाक|झंपाक|झंपाकः|झम्पाकः
झम्पाक, अस्, m. or झम्पारु, उस्, m. a<BR>monkey, an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पिन्|झंपिन्
झम्पिन्, ई, m. ‘a leaper,’ an ape, a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर|झरः
झर झर, अस्, आ or ई, m. f. a cascade, a<BR>water-fall; (ई), f. a river; [cf. निर्-झर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झरत्
झरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flowing or falling down;<BR>[cf. क्षर्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्च्
झर्च् झर्च्, cl. 6. P. झर्चति, or झर्छ्,<BR>cl. 6. P. झर्छति, or झर्झ्, cl. 6. P.<BR>झर्झति, to speak; to blame, menace; injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झर|झर्झरः
झर्झर झर्झर, अस्, ई, m. f. (said to be fr.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">Page0355-a+ 70</a>]<BR>the last), a sort of drum; (अस्), m. the Kali-yuga,<BR>the present Yuga or age of the world; N. of a<BR>Daitya, a son of Hiraṇyākṣa; N. of a river; (आ),<BR>f. a whore [cf. ऋच्छरा]; (अम्), n. a sound as of<BR>splashing or dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0354-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरक|झर्झरकः
झर्झरक, अस्, m. the fourth or present age of<BR>the world, the Kali-yuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरिन्
झर्झरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, furnished with a drum; epi-<BR>thet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरीक|झर्झरीकः
झर्झरीक झर्झरीक, अस्, m. the body; a<BR>region, a country; a picture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलक्का
झलक्का झलक्का, f. a large flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलज्झला
झलज्झला झलज्झला, f. an onomatopoetic<BR>word for the noise of falling drops, the flapping of<BR>an elephant's ears, or of flaccid breasts, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलरी
झलरी झलरी, f. = झर्झर, a sort of<BR>drum; a curl; [cf. झल्लरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झला
झला झला, f. a girl, a daughter; sun-<BR>shine, splendor, brilliant or glittering light; a cricket;<BR>[cf. झिल्ली; cf. also rt. ज्वल्; Hib. gal, ‘heat;’<BR>galla, ‘fairness, brightness, beauty;’ gallad, ‘a lass,<BR>a young girl.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलि|झलिः
झलि झलि, इस्, f. the areca-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्ल|झल्लः
झल्ल झल्ल, अस्, m. a prize-fighter, a cudgel-<BR>player, a man of a tribe following the profession of<BR>a Jhalla; a designation of one of the degraded classes<BR>sprung from an outcast Kṣatriya; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लक|झल्लकं
झल्लक झल्लक, अम्, n. (fr. झल्ल, imitative<BR>sound), cymbals; (ई), f. a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लकण्ठ|झल्लकंठ|झल्लकंठः|झल्लकण्ठः
झल्लकण्ठ झल्लकण्ठ, अस्, m. a pigeon;<BR>[cf. झिल्ली-कण्ठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लना
झल्लना झल्लना, f. a particular Prākṛt<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लरी
झल्लरी झल्लरी, f. (fr. झल्ल, imitative<BR>sound; cf. झलरी), a kind of musical instrument,<BR>a sort of drum or cymbal; a curl, a lock of hair;<BR>moisture; purity; a ball &c. of perfumed substances<BR>used for cleaning the hair; [cf. झलरी and झिल्लरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लिका
झल्लिका झल्लिका, f. a rag or cloth used for<BR>applying colour or perfumes; dirt rubbed off the body<BR>by the application of perfumes; light, splendor, lustre;<BR>[cf. झिल्लिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लीषक
झल्लीषक झल्लीषक, a sort of musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लोल|झल्लोलः
झल्लोल झल्लोल, अस्, m. a ball or protuber-<BR>ance at the lower end of a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झष्
झष् झष्, cl. 1. P. A. झषति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to take; to put on, wear, cover; (only P.)<BR>to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झष|झषं|झषः
झष, अस्, m. a large fish, a fish in general; the<BR>sign of the zodiac Pisces; a forest, a thicket; a<BR>forest overgrown with grass; heat, warmth; (आ), f.<BR>the plant Uraria Lagopodioides; (अम्), n. a desert.<BR>—झष-केतन or झष-ध्वज, अस्, m. a N.<BR>of Kandarpa or the god of love; love.<BR>—झषाङ्क<BR>(˚ष-अङ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Aniruddha or the<BR>son of Kāma.<BR>—झषाशन (˚ष-अश्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>Gangetic porpoise, Delphinus Gangeticus.<BR>—झषो-<BR>दरी (˚ष-उद्˚), f. an epithet of Satyavatī, the wife<BR>of Sāntanu and mother of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0355-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाङ्कृत|झांकृतं|झाङ्कृतं
