ठिण्ठा ठिण्ठा, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड|डः
ड 1. ड, the third letter of the cerebral<BR>class of consonants, having much the sound of द् in<BR>drum, but properly pronounced by keeping back the<BR>tip of the tongue and slightly turning it upwards. In<BR>Bengal ड् is often confounded in pronunciation with a<BR>hard र्.<BR>—ड-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड|डः
ड 2. ड, अस्, m. a sound; a kind of drum<BR>or tabor; fear; submarine fire; an epithet of Śiva;<BR>(आ), f. a Ḍākinī, i. e. a kind of female imp or goblin;<BR>a basket &c. carried by means of a sling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डक्कारी
डक्कारी डक्कारी, f. the lute of the Cāṇḍālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डङ्गर
डङ्गर डङ्गर, अस्, m. = डिङ्गर, throwing,<BR>casting; (ई), f. a kind of gourd; (also डङ्गारी, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डप्
डप् डप्, cl. 10. A. डापयते, &c., to col-<BR>lect, accumulate, heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्
डम् डम्, cl. 1. P. डमति, &c., to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम|डमः
डम डम, अस्, m. a despised mixed caste<BR>(commonly Ḍom), the son of a Cāṇḍālī and a Leṭa,<BR>employed to clear away filth &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमर|डमरं|डमरः
डमर डमर, अस्, आ, m. f. a riot, tumult,<BR>affray, a conflict without weapons; terrifying an<BR>enemy by shouts and gestures; petty or predatory<BR>warfare carried on by detachments or between<BR>villages and not kings; (अम्), n. flight, rout, running<BR>away through fear; [cf. डामर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरिन्
डमरिन् डमरिन्, ई, m. (?) a sort of drum,<BR>= the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरु|डमरुः
डमरु, उस्, m. a musical instrument, a sort of<BR>small drum shaped like an hour-glass and held in one<BR>hand; anything surprising, any strange occurrence &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरुक
डमरुक, अम्, n. a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्प्|डंप्
डम्प् डम्प्, cl. 10. A. डम्पयते, &c. (a<BR>various reading for डप्), to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्ब्|डंब्
डम्ब् डम्ब्, cl. 10. P. डम्बयति, &c., to<BR>throw, cast, send; order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्बर|डंबर|डम्बरः
डम्बर डम्बर, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Skanda; an assemblage, collection,<BR>mass; (अस्, आ, अम्), famous, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्भ्|डंभ्
डम्भ् डम्भ्, cl. 10. A. डम्भयते, &c.<BR>(various reading for डप्), to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डयन|डयनं
डयन डयन. See rt. डी, p. 357, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डलक|डलकं
डलक डलक or डल्लक, अम्, n. a sling, a<BR>basket, a Dūlī carried on men's shoulders by means<BR>of a stick and ropes like the beam and strings of a<BR>balance, (presents of fruit, sweetmeats, &c., are usu-<BR>ally sent in this manner); (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डलन
डलन डलन or डल्लन, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>scholiast on the medical work of Su-śruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डवित्थ|डवित्थः
डवित्थ डवित्थ, अस्, m., N. of a man; a<BR>wooden antelope (?); [cf. डित्थ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डहु|डहुः
डहु डहु, उस्, or ऊ, ऊस्, m. the plant Arto-<BR>carpus Lacucha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाकिनी
डाकिनी डाकिनी, f. a kind of female imp or<BR>evil being attending Kālī and feeding on human<BR>flesh; N. of a place; [cf. शाकिनी.]<BR>—डाकिनी-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the condition of a female demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाङ्कृति|डांकृतिः
डाङ्कृति डान्-कृति, इस्, f. (fr. डाम्, imitative<BR>sound, and 1. कृति), a sound, the clang of a bell,<BR>ding-dong, &c.; [cf. टाङ्-कार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाङ्गरी
डाङ्गरी डाङ्गरी, f. = डङ्गरी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डामर|डामरः
डामर डामर, अस्, m. affray, riot, conflict<BR>without weapons &c. [cf. डमर]; rout, uproar,<BR>the bustle and confusion of festivity or strife; any<BR>surprising thing, sight, or occurrence; a N. common<BR>to six Tantras, viz. the Yoga-ḍāmara, Śiva-ḍ˚, Durgā-<BR>ḍ˚, Sārasvata-ḍ˚, Brahma-ḍ˚, and Gandharva-ḍ˚; N.<BR>of one of the attendants of Śiva; N. of a race or<BR>mixed caste; (अस्, आ, अम्), riotous; [cf. उड्-डामर.]<BR>—डामर-त्व, अम्, n. the state of one who excites<BR>awe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डालिम|डालिमः
डालिम डालिम, अस्, m. = दाडिम, a pome-<BR>granate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहल|डाहलः
डाहल डाहल, अस्, m., N. of a people and<BR>their country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहुक|डाहुकः
डाहुक डाहुक, अस्, m. a gallinule; [cf.<BR>दात्यूह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0356-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिक्करी
डिक्करी डिक्करी, f. a young woman; (wrong<BR>form for दिक्करी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिङ्गर|डिंगर|डिंगरः|डिङ्गरः
डिङ्गर डिङ्गर, अस्, m. a servant, a slave;<BR>a rogue, a cheat; a low or depraved man; a fat<BR>man; throwing, flinging; invective, insult (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिडका
डिडका डिडका, f. perhaps a wrong form<BR>for डिम्भका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिडिम
डिडिम डिडिम or डिडिमाणक, a kind of<BR>bird; [cf. टिट्टिभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिक|डिंडिक|डिण्डिकः
डिण्डिक डिण्डिक, अस्, m., N. of a mouse<BR>whose story is told^1 in the Mahā-bh. Udyoga-parva 5440.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिम|डिंडिम|डिंडिमः|डिण्डिमः
डिण्डिम डिण्डिम, अस्, m. a musical instru-<BR>ment, a kind of small drum or tabor; a plant bearing<BR>a small fruit, Carissa Carandas.<BR>—डिण्डिमेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ (˚म-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिर|डिंडिर|डिंडिरः|डिण्डिरः
डिण्डिर डिण्डिर, अस्, m. cuttle-fish bone<BR>considered to be the foam of the sea; [cf. हिण्डिर<BR>and डिण्डीर.]<BR>—डिण्डिर-मोदक, अम्, n. garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिश|डिण्डिशः
डिण्डिश डिण्डिश, अस्, m. = टिण्डिश = तिन्दिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डीर|डिंडीर|डिंडीरः|डिण्डीरः
डिण्डीर डिण्डीर, अस्, m. cuttle-fish bone<BR>held to be the foam of the sea; [cf. डिण्डिर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डित्थ|डित्थः
डित्थ डित्थ, अस्, m., N. of a man; a wooden<BR>elephant; a good-looking dark-coloured young man<BR>who is conversant with every branch of learning;<BR>[cf. डवित्थ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिप्
डिप् डिप् or डिम्प् or डिम्भ्, cl. 10. A. डे-<BR>पयते or डिम्पयते or डिम्भयते, to<BR>collect, heap together; डिप्, cl. 4. 6. 10. P. डिप्यति,<BR>डिपति, डेपयति, to throw, cast, send or order; to<BR>direct; also डिम्ब्, cl. 10. A. डिम्बयते; [cf. rt. टिप्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्
डिम् डिम् (a Sautra root or one not occur-<BR>ring in the Dhātu-pāṭha), to hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम|डिमः
डिम डिम, अस्, m. a dramatic entertainment,<BR>dramatic exhibition of battle or siege, such as the<BR>Tripura-dāha, in which the destruction of the three<BR>cities of Tripura by Śiva is dramatised; a kind of<BR>mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्ब|डिंब|डिम्बं|डिंबः|डिम्बः
डिम्ब डिम्ब, अस्, m. affray, riot, conflict<BR>without weapons, mutual defiance, petty and predatory<BR>war, &c. [cf. डमर]; sound or noise occasioned<BR>by terror; an egg; a chrysalis; the embryo in the<BR>first stage of its existence; a new-born child, any young<BR>animal; the bladder, the spleen, the lungs; the<BR>uterus; a globe or ball.<BR>—डिम्ब-युद्ध, अम्, n.<BR>or डिम्बाहव (˚ब-आह्˚), अस्, m. petty warfare,<BR>affray, skirmish, riot, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्बिका|डिंबिका
डिम्बिका डिम्बिका, f. a libidinous woman;<BR>a bubble; a kind of water-fly; = शोणक, Calosanthes<BR>Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्भ्
डिम्भ् डिम्भ् or डिम्ब्. See rt. डिप् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्भ|डिंभ|डिंभः|डिम्भः
डिम्भ डिम्भ, अस्, m. a new-born child,<BR>any young animal; a fool, an idiot, a blockhead;<BR>(आ), f. an infant.<BR>—डिम्भ-चक्र, अम्, n. a mystical<BR>circle; a diagram for telling fortunes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्भक|डिंभक|डिंभकः|डिम्भकः
डिम्भक, अस्, इका, m. f. a new-born child, young<BR>animal; (अस्), m., N. of a general of Jarā-sandha,<BR>younger brother of Haṃsa and son of Brahma-datta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डी
डी डी, cl. 1. 4. A. डयते, डीयते, डिड्ये,<BR>डयिष्यते, अडयिष्ट, डयितुम्, to fly, pass<BR>through the air; to go: Caus. P. डाययति, -यितुम्,<BR>अडीडयत्: Desid. डिडयिषते: Intens. डेडीयते,<BR>डेडयीति or डेडेति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डयन|डयनं
डयन, अम्, n. flying in the air, the flight of a<BR>bird; a car or litter carried upon men's shoulders,<BR>a palanquin, a Dūlī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डयमान
डयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, flying, passing through<BR>the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीतर
डीतर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. following one another<BR>quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीन|डीनं
डीन, अस्, आ, अम्, flown, flying; (अम्), n. flying,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">Page0357-b+ 64</a>]<BR>the flight of a bird.<BR>—डीन-डीनक, अस्, m. flying<BR>reiteratedly.<BR>—डीनावडीन (˚न-अव्˚), अम्, n. flying<BR>up and down; flying badly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुडुभ
डुडुभ डुडुभ or डुडुम, अस्, m. or डुण्डु,<BR>उस्, f. or डुण्डुभ, अस्, m. a kind of snake (Am-<BR>phisbæna) or lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डौण्डुभ
डौण्डुभ, अस्, ई, अम्, of or belonging to an<BR>Amphisbæna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डुल|डुंडुलः|डुण्डुलः
डुण्डुल डुण्डुल, अस्, m. a small owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुन्दुक|डुंदुकः|डुन्दुकः
डुन्दुक डुन्दुक, अस्, m. a gallinule, = डाहुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलि|डुलिः
डुलि डुलि, इस्, f. a small turtle, a female<BR>turtle, = दुलि, कमठी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलिका
डुलिका डुलिका, f. a kind of wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुली
डुली डुली, f. a kind of pot-herb, = चिल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोडी
डोडी डोडी, f. a sort of shrub, = जीवन्ती,<BR>जीवनी, &c.; [cf. क्षुपडोड-मुष्टि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोम|डोमः
डोम डोम, अस्, m. a man of low caste, a<BR>Ḍom; [cf. डम, डोम्ब; cf. also the N. for the<BR>Gypsies, रोम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोम्ब
डोम्ब डोम्ब, अस्, m. a man of low caste<BR>obtaining a livelihood by singing and music &c.; N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोर|डोरं|डोरः
डोर डोर or डोरक, अम्, n. a fillet of<BR>thread or cord tied round the arm or wrist; the<BR>string for tying a packet or parcel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोरडी
डोरडी डोरडी, f. a kind of Solanum, =<BR>वृहती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डौण्डुभ
डौण्डुभ डौण्डुभ (scil. रूप), the form of<BR>an Amphisbæna. See under डुडुभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड्वल्
ड्वल् ड्वल्, Caus. P. ड्वालयति, &c., to<BR>mix; [cf. rt. ट्वल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढ|ढः
ढ 1. ढ, the aspirate of the preceding<BR>letter; its use as an initial letter is very limited, and<BR>several of the words in which it occurs can scarcely<BR>be regarded as pure Sanskrit.<BR>—ढ-कार, अस्, m.<BR>the letter or sound ढ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढ|ढः
ढ 2. ढ, अस्, m. an imitative sound; a<BR>large drum; a dog's tail; a dog; a serpent; void of<BR>qualities (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्क|ढक्कः
ढक्क ढक्क, अस्, m., N. of a city or district<BR>(commonly ढाका or धक्क; the word is said also<BR>to signify a large sacred building); (आ), f. a large or<BR>double drum, a Ḍhāk; coveting; disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्कन
ढक्कन ढक्कन, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(also written टक्कन, ढक्कम, थक्कन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्कारी
ढक्कारी ढक्कारी, f. an epithet of the god-<BR>dess Tāriṇī or Tārā, a Tāntrika form of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढङ्क
ढङ्क ढङ्क, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढण्ठी
ढण्ठी ढण्ठी, इस्, f. = वाक्य-विशेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढामरा
ढामरा ढामरा, f. a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढाल|ढालं
ढाल ढाल, अम्, n. a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढालिन्
ढालिन्, ई, m. a warrior armed with a shield, a<BR>shield-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढ्
ढुण्ढ् ढुण्ढ्, ढुण्ढति (properly a<BR>Sautra root not occurring in the Dhātu-<BR>pāṭha), to search, seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढन|ढुंढनं
ढुण्ढन, अम्, n. seeking, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढि|ढुंढि|ढुंढिः|ढुण्ढिः
ढुण्ढि, इस्, m. an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—ढुण्ढि-<BR>राज, अस्, m., N. of an author who was the father<BR>of Bāla-Kṛṣṇa and uncle of Śaṅkara-dīkṣita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढित
ढुण्ढित, अस्, आ, अम्, sought, inquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढेङ्क
ढेङ्क ढेङ्क, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढोल|ढोलः
ढोल ढोल, अस्, m. a large drum or tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौक्
ढौक् ढौक्, cl. 1. A. ढौकते, डु-<BR>ढौके, ढौकिष्यते, अढौकिष्ट,<BR>ढौकितुम्, to go, move, approach: Caus. ढौ-<BR>कयति, -यितुम्, अडुढौकत्, to bring near, cause<BR>to approach, offer: Desid. डुढौकिषते: Intens.<BR>डोढौक्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौकन|ढौकनं
ढौकन, अम्, n. offering; a present, a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण|णः
ण 1. ण, the nasal ण् belonging to the<BR>third or cerebral class of consonants.<BR>—ण-कार, अस्,<BR>m. the letter or sound ण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण|णः
ण 2. ण, अस्, m. knowledge; certainty,<BR>ascertainment; ornament; a water or summer-house;<BR>a bad man; a N. of Vindu-deva, said to be a Jaina<BR>deity; an epithet of Śiva; the sound of negation;<BR>gift, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णद्
णद् णद्, णम्, णश्, &c. Many roots which<BR>really begin with the dental न् are written in<BR>native grammars and the Dhātu-pāṭha with the cerebral<BR>ण् to show that the nasal is liable to be cerebralized<BR>when preceded by prepositions like प्र, परि, &c.<BR>These roots will be found in the present Dictionary<BR>under the dental न्. See नद्, नम्, नश्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण्य|ण्यः
ण्य ण्य, अस्, m., N. of an ocean in Brahma-<BR>loka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त|तं|तः
त 1. त, the first consonant of the fourth<BR>or dental class, the sound of which is more dental<BR>than the English त्.<BR>—त-कार, अस्, m. the letter or<BR>sound त्.<BR>—त-वर्ग, अस्, m. the dental class of letters.<BR>—तवर्गीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the dental class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त|तं|तः
त 2. त, the base of the third personal<BR>pronoun in all the cases except the nom. sing. masc.<BR>and fem. See तद्, p. 360.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त|तं|तः
त 3. त, अस्, m. a tail; any tail except that<BR>of the Bos Gaurus; the tail of a jackal; the breast;<BR>the womb; the hip or flank; a warrior; a thief; a<BR>wicked man; an outcast, a barbarian or Mleccha; a<BR>Buddha; a jewel; nectar, the food of the immortals;<BR>(आ, अम्), f. n. passing, crossing; virtue, sanctity;<BR>(आ), f., N. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंस्
तंस् तंस्, cl. 1. A., Ved. तंसते, ततस्रे,<BR>&c., to shake, move to and fro; to pour<BR>out (metaphorically a wish); to request: Caus. P.<BR>तंसयति, -यितुम्, to move to and fro, shake; cl.<BR>1. 10. P. तंसति, तंसयति, to decorate; [cf. Old<BR>Pruss. teisint, ‘to honour;’ teisi, ‘honour.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंसु
तंसु तंसु, उस्, m., N. of a prince of the<BR>lunar race, a son of Matināra (or Rantināra); in<BR>some places he is called Taṃsu-rodha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्
तक् तक्, cl. 1. 2. P., Ved. तकति, तक्ति,<BR>तताक, तकिष्यति, अतकीत् and अताकीत्,<BR>तकितुम्, to fly (as an arrow or bird), fly at, rush or<BR>pounce upon; to laugh at or deride; to bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकवान
तकवान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rushing, darting along,<BR>moving quickly; (Sāy.) shaking, moving with dif-<BR>ficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकु
तकु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. rushing, moving quickly;<BR>(Sāy.) approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्त
तक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rushing or darting along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्मन्
1. तक्मन्, आ, m., Ved. (especially in the Atharva-<BR>veda), a kind of disease, or probably a whole class of<BR>diseases, accompanied by eruptions of the skin.<BR>—तक्म-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. removing the<BR>disease called Takman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्य|तक्यः
तक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne or endured;<BR>laughable, ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्व
तक्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. quick (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्वन्
तक्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. rushing, darting, pouncing<BR>on; (आ), m. a bird, especially a bird of prey; (Sāy.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">Page0358-a+ 75</a>]<BR>a fleet horse; a thief.<BR>—तक्व-वी, ईस्, m., Ved. a<BR>bird, bird of prey, or a particular bird.<BR>—तक्ववीय,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. rapid flight, rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0357-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक
तक तक, अस्, आ, अत् (fr. तद् with अक् inserted<BR>after त्), that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकरी
तकरी तकरी, f., Ved. a particular part of<BR>the pudenda of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकिल|तकिलः
तकिल तकिल, अस्, आ, अम्, fraudulent, crafty,<BR>a rogue or cheat; (आ), f. a medicament, drug; a<BR>kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्कोल
तक्कोल तक्कोल, the tree Pimenta Acris,<BR>commonly called Kaṅkola.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्मन्
तक्मन् 2. तक्मन्, अ, n. = तोक्मन् = अपत्य,<BR>offspring, a child; [cf. Gr. τέκνον; cf. also 1. तक्-<BR>मन् under rt. तक्, p. 357, col. 3.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्र|तक्रं
तक्र तक्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. तञ्च्), buttermilk<BR>which is half water; (according to others) with a<BR>fourth or three parts of water.<BR>—तक्र-कूर्चिका, f.<BR>inspissated buttermilk.<BR>—तक्र-भिद्, त्, n. (?) the<BR>fruit of Feronia Elephantum.<BR>—तक्र-मांस, अम्,<BR>n. meat fried with ghee, turmeric, Asa Fœtida, &c.,<BR>and eaten with buttermilk.<BR>—तक्र-सार, अम्, n.<BR>fresh butter.<BR>—तक्राट (˚र-अट), अस्, m. a<BR>churning-stick; [cf. दधि-चार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष्
तक्ष् 1. तक्ष्, cl. 1. 5. P. (sometimes A.)<BR>तक्षति, -ते, तक्ष्णोति, -णुते, ततक्ष,<BR>-षे, तक्षिष्यति or तक्ष्यति, -ते, अतक्षीत्,<BR>तक्षितुम् or तष्टुम्, to form by cutting, plane,<BR>chisel, pare, chip, chop, slice, split; to cut, wound;<BR>to make thin; to fashion, form (out of wood &c.),<BR>to make, create in general; to form in the mind, in-<BR>vent; to make one's own, appropriate; to cover; to<BR>skin, peel: Caus. तक्षयति, -यितुम्, अततक्षत्:<BR>Desid. तितक्षिषति or तितक्षति (?): Intens. तात-<BR>क्ष्यते, तातष्टि; [cf. Lith. taszau: Russ. tesatj:<BR>Pol. cieśla: Lat. tignum: Old Pruss. tikint, ‘to<BR>make;’ tikinnimai, teikusna: Gr. τίκτω, τέκνον,<BR>τεύχω, τάσσω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष्
2. तक्ष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, (at the end of a comp.) paring,<BR>cutting, forming by cutting, working; [cf. काष्ठ-<BR>तक्ष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष
तक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, cutting off, cutting through;<BR>(अस्), m. (at the end of a comp.) = तक्षन्, a car-<BR>penter [cf. कौट-तक्ष and ग्राम-त्˚]; N. of a<BR>serpent-demon; N. of a son of Bharata; N. of a<BR>son of Vṛka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षक|तक्षकः
तक्षक, अस्, m. a cutter, one who cuts off, a<BR>wood-cutter, a carpenter; the divine architect or<BR>artist Viśva-karman; the Sūtra-dhāra or manager<BR>and chief actor in the prelude of a drama; one of the<BR>principal Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla; N. of a son<BR>of Prasena-jit and father of Bṛhad-bala; N. of a<BR>particular tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षकीया
तक्षकीया, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षण|तक्षणं
तक्षण, अम्, n. cutting, paring, peeling, planing;<BR>(ई), f. a carpenter's adze or similar instrument for<BR>cutting, an axe &c; (अस्), m. a cutter, an abrader;<BR>(in mathem.) the divisor employed in certain com-<BR>putations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षन्
तक्षन्, आ, m. (Ved. acc. तक्षाणम् or तक्ष-<BR>णम्), a wood-cutter, a carpenter; N. of a preceptor;<BR>[cf. Gr. τέκτω.]<BR>—तक्ष-शिला, f., N. of a city of<BR>the Gandhāras, the Τάξιλα of Ptolemy in the Pañjāb;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of this city.<BR>—तक्ष-<BR>शिला-वती, f., N. of a district.<BR>—तक्षायस्कार<BR>(˚ष-अय्˚), अम्, n. a carpenter and a blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षितृ
तक्षितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who cuts, pares, &c.;<BR>a cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष्य
तक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be formed or fashioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगडवल्ली
तगडवल्ली तगड-वल्ली, f. (तगड = तगर),<BR>the shrub Cassia Auriculata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगर|तगरं|तगरः
तगर तगर, अम्, n. the shrub Tabernæ-<BR>montana Coronaria and a fragrant^1 powder prepared<BR>from it; N. of a town; (अस्), m. a thorny shrub,<BR>Vangueria Spinosa; another plant, commonly Taga-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">Page0358-b+ 72</a>]<BR>ra-mūla; [cf. काल-पर्ण, कटु-च्छद, मदन-<BR>वृक्ष.]<BR>—तगर-पादिका, अम्, f. n. or तगर-<BR>पादी, f. the plant Tabernæmontana Coronaria and<BR>its powder.<BR>—तगर-शिखिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगरिक
तगरिक, अस्, ई, m. f. a seller of Tagara powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्क्|तंक्
तङ्क् तङ्क्, cl. 1. P. तङ्कति, ततङ्क,<BR>तङ्कितुम्, to live in distress, be in poverty<BR>or pain; to go (?); [cf. Hib. teicheamh, ‘a going,<BR>passage;’ tochamhlaim, ‘I march;’ tochar, ‘a<BR>causeway, pavement;’ toichim, ‘going, departing:’<BR>Lith. tekù, ‘I run;’ tákas, ‘a path;’ tekûnas, ‘a<BR>runner:’ Slav. takû, ‘I run.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्क|तंक|तंकः|तङ्कः
1. तङ्क, अस्, m. grief produced by separation from a<BR>beloved object; fear, terror; [cf. आ-तङ्क, तपस्-तङ्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्क|तंक|तंकः|तङ्कः
तङ्क 2. तङ्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. (for टङ्क), an<BR>axe, a stone-cutter's chisel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्ग्|तंग्
तङ्ग् तङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. तङ्गति, &c., to go,<BR>move; to stumble; to shake, tremble; [cf.<BR>Hib. tagaidh, ‘advance;’ tigim, ‘I come, go.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्गण
तङ्गण तङ्गण, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>in the upper part of the valley of the Sarayū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्गल्व
तङ्गल्व तङ्गल्व, अस्, m., Ved., N. of an<BR>evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तच्छील
तच्छील तच्छील. See तद्, p. 360, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तज्ज
तज्ज तज्-ज, तज्-जय, &c. See तद्, p. 360.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तज्वी
तज्वी तज्वी, f. = हिङ्गु-पत्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्च्|तंच्
तञ्च् 1. तञ्च् or तञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. तनक्ति,<BR>ततञ्च, तङ्क्ष्यति and तञ्चिष्यति,<BR>अताङ्क्षीत् and अतञ्चीत्, तङ्क्तुम् and तञ्चितुम्, to<BR>contract, shrink: Caus. तञ्चयति, -यितुम्: Desid.<BR>तितङ्क्षति or तितञ्चिषति: Intens. तातच्यते,<BR>तातङ्क्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्च्|तंच्
तञ्च् 2. तञ्च्, cl. 1. P. तञ्चति, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्ज्|तंज्
तञ्ज् तञ्ज्, a various reading for 1. तञ्च्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट्
तट् तट्, cl. 1. P. तटति, &c., to rumble,<BR>groan; to be raised or elevated, rise; cl. 10.<BR>P. ताटयति, to beat, strike; (a various reading for<BR>तड्); [cf. Lith. tesiu, ‘to raise.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट|तटं|तटः
तट, अस्, आ, m. f. a slope, an acclivity, declivity,<BR>precipice; the sky or horizon (as appearing to slope);<BR>(अस्, आ or ई, अम्), m. f. n. a shore or bank; a term<BR>applied to certain parts of the human body which<BR>have, as it were, sloping sides (e. g. श्रोणि-तट,<BR>स्तन-तट, q. v.); (अम्), n. a field; [cf. अ-तट,<BR>उत्-तट, पुर-तटी.]<BR>—तट-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situ-<BR>ated on a declivity, or on a bank or shore; standing<BR>near; indifferent, not partaking of or engaging in,<BR>alien, neuter; (अस्), m. an indifferent person, one<BR>neither a friend nor a foe; (अम्), n. that property<BR>which is distinct from the nature of anything and yet<BR>is the faculty by which it is known, spiritual essence<BR>unconnected with bodily wants or passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटक|तटकं
तटक, अम्, n. a shore or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटाक|तटाकं|तटाकः
तटाक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a pond deep enough for<BR>the lotus and other aquatic flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटिनी
तटिनी, f. a river (as having a bank).<BR>—तटिनी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘the lord of the rivers,’ the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट्य|तट्यः
तट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, living on hills or slopes,<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटतट
तटतट तटतट (an onomatopoetic word to<BR>express a particular noise), rumbling, thundering, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तड्
तड् तड्, cl. 10. P. ताडयति, -यितुम्, अती-<BR>तडत् (redupl. perf. तताड), to beat, strike,<BR>hit, knock; to strike with arrows, wound, punish; to<BR>strike a musical instrument; (in astronomy) to strike<BR>against, touch, partially obscure or eclipse; (in arith-<BR>metic) to multiply; to speak; to shine; [cf. Hib.<BR>tathaim, ‘I kill, destroy;’ tathog, ‘a clash, a slap.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्
तडित्, त्, f., Ved. (in Ṛg-veda तऌइत्), lightning;<BR>तऌइत् or तऌइतस्, ind. closely, near, (as it were<BR>striking against.)<BR>—तडित्-कुमार, आस्, m. pl. (with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">Page0358-c+ 72</a>]<BR>Jainas) N. of a class of deities belonging to the<BR>Bhavana-patis.<BR>—तडित्-प्रभा, f., N. of one of<BR>the Mātṛs attendant on Skanda.<BR>—तडित्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having lightning, emitting lightning,<BR>flashing; (आन्), m. a cloud, a kind of Cyperus, =<BR>मुस्तक.<BR>—तडिद्-गर्भ, अस्, m. a cloud, ‘con-<BR>taining lightning.’<BR>—तडिन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of lightning, flashing like lightning.<BR>—तडिन्-<BR>मालावलम्बिन् (˚ला-अव्˚), ई, इनी, इ, having garlands<BR>of lightning hanging down.<BR>—तडिल्-लता, f. forked<BR>lightning.<BR>—तडिल्-लेखा, f. a line or streak of lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडग|तडगः
तडग तडग, अस्, m. = तडाग, a pool, lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाक|तडाकः
तडाक तडाक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. तड्),<BR>= तडाग, a pond or pool deep enough for the lotus;<BR>(आ), f. a blow; a bank, a shore; splendor, lightning (?);<BR>[cf. तटाक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाकिन्
तडाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having pools or lakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाग|तडागं|तडागः
तडाग, अस्, अम्, m. n. a pond or pool deep enough<BR>for the growth of the lotus &c.; a tank; a trap for<BR>catching deer.<BR>—तडाग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>pools or lakes; (आन्), m., scil. देश, a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाघात|तडाघातः
तडाघात तडाघात, अस्, m. a blow from an<BR>elephant's uplifted trunk; probably a wrong form<BR>for ताडाघात (ताड-आघात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्
तडित् तडित्. See तड्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्ड्|तंड्
तण्ड् तण्ड् (connected with तड्), cl. 1. A.<BR>तण्डते, &c., to beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्ड
तण्ड तण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डक|तंडक|तंडकः|तण्डकः
तण्डक तण्डक, अस्, अम्, m. n. complete per-<BR>formance or preparation; decoration; the upright<BR>post of a house; composition abounding in compound<BR>words; (अस्), m. a juggler, a cheat; the trunk of a<BR>tree; froth, foam; a wagtail; [cf. ताण्डक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डि
तण्डि तण्डि, इस्, m., N. of a man; also of<BR>a Ṛṣi in the Kṛta-yuga who saw and praised Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डिन्
तण्डिन् तण्डिन्, ई, m., N. of the author of<BR>a work on prosody quoted by Piṅgala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डु|तण्डुः
तण्डु तण्डु, उस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's<BR>door-keepers and one of the original teachers of the<BR>arts of dancing and mimicry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुरीण|तंडुरीणः|तण्डुरीणः
तण्डुरीण तण्डुरीण, अस्, m. one not a citizen,<BR>a barbarian; a fool, a blockhead; the water in which<BR>rice has been soaked or steeped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुल|तंडुल|तंडुलः|तण्डुलः
तण्डुल तण्डुल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. तड्, cf. तण्ड्), grain after threshing and winnowing,<BR>especially rice; rice used as a weight; (अस्, आ), m. f. a<BR>vermifuge plant or its seed [cf. तण्डुलु, विडङ्ग];<BR>(अस्), m. a pot-herb, a sort of amaranth, = तण्डुलीय;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of plant, = ओदनाह्वया, ओदनिका,<BR>महा-समङ्गा; a sort of Sida; (ई), f., N. of<BR>several plants, = यव-तिक्ता, शशाण्डुली, तण्डुलीय.<BR>—तण्डुल-कण, अस्, m. a grain of rice.<BR>—तण्डुल-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet of Kaśmīra.<BR>—तण्डुल-<BR>फला, f. long pepper.<BR>—तण्डुलाम्बु (˚ल-अम्˚),<BR>उ, n. rice-water or gruel.<BR>—तण्डुलोत्थ (˚ल-उत्˚),<BR>अम्, n. or तण्डुलोदक (˚ल-उद्˚), अम्, n. water in<BR>which rice has been boiled, rice-gruel.<BR>—तण्डु-<BR>लौघ (˚ल-ओघ), अस्, m. a prickly sort of bamboo,<BR>Bambusa Spinosa; a heap of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीक|तण्डुलीकः
तण्डुलीक, अस्, m. a kind of pot-herb, Amaranthus<BR>Polygonoides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीय|तण्डुलीयः
तण्डुलीय, अस्, m. a kind of pot-herb, Amaranthus<BR>Polygonoides; a vermifuge plant [cf. विडङ्ग]; a<BR>mineral, iron pyrites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीयक|तण्डुलीयकः
तण्डुलीयक, अस्, m. Amaranthus Polygonoides;<BR>a vermifuge seed; [cf. विडङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलु|तण्डुलुः
तण्डुलु, उस्, m. a plant the seeds of which are<BR>used as a vermifuge; [cf. विडङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलेर|तण्डुलेरः
तण्डुलेर, अस्, m. Amaranthus Polygonoides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डूलिकाश्रम
तण्डूलिकाश्रम तण्डूलिकाश्रम (˚क-आश्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a hermitage, Mahā-bh. Vana-parva 4084.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्
तत् 1. तत् for तद्, that. See तद्, p. 360.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्
तत् 2. तत्, 2. तत. See rt. 3. तन्, p. 361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत 1. तत, अस्, m. (connected with तात, said<BR>to be fr. rt. 3. तन्), Ved. father (a familiar expression<BR>corresponding to नना, mother).<BR>—तत-तत, अस्,<BR>m. father of fathers.<BR>—तता-मह, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>grandfather; [cf. प्र-ततामह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततत्व
ततत्व ततत्व, अम्, n. slow time in music;<BR>[cf. तत्त्व.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततनुष्टि
ततनुष्टि ततनुष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. 3. तन् ?),<BR>Ved. fond of ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततम|ततमः
ततम ततम, अस्, आ, अत् (fr. तद्), that one<BR>(of many).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततर|ततरः
ततर, अस्, आ, अत्, that one (of two).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्
ततस् ततस्, ind. (fr. the pronom. base 2. त;<BR>correlative of यतस्, and often used for the abl. cases<BR>तस्मात्, तस्याः, &c., of the pronoun तद्, but oftener<BR>as an adverb), from that place, thence; in that place,<BR>there, thither (e. g. तत आ-याहि, come from that<BR>place); thereupon, then, after that, afterwards (e. g.<BR>ततः किम्, what happened then ?); from that, in<BR>consequence of that; for that reason, therefore, conse-<BR>quently; beyond that, besides that, further, moreover.<BR>ततस्-ततस्, from that and that place, here and there,<BR>hither and thither, from all sides, to every place, every-<BR>where. ततस् ततस्, (in dramatic poetry) what then?<BR>what took place after that? यतो-यतस् — ततस्-ततस्,<BR>from whatever place — to that place; wherever — there;<BR>इतस्-ततस्, from this place and that, here and there,<BR>hither and thither, see, s. v.; यतस्-ततस्, from which<BR>place soever, from any one whatever; ततः क्षणात्,<BR>immediately afterwards; ततः परम्, thereupon,<BR>afterwards; ततः पश्चात्, after that; ततः-प्र-<BR>भृति, thenceforth, thenceforward, from that time<BR>forward; ततो ऽन्यतस्, to some other place, i. e.<BR>to another place than that; [cf. Gr. τότε, τόθεν;<BR>Slav. ot-tûdû.]<BR>—ततो-भवत्, आन्, m. His Highness<BR>from there, His Highness there, Your Honour there;<BR>[cf. तत्र-भवत् and अत्र-भवत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्त्य|ततस्त्यं
ततस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from that, proceeding<BR>thence; of or belonging to that, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति 1. तति (fr. the pronom. base 2. त), pl.<BR>(in nom. and acc. without termination), so many.<BR>(For 2. तति see p. 361, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततिथ
ततिथ, अस्, ई, अम् (correlative of यतिथ), so<BR>maniest, that one of a number; e. g. ततिथी समा,<BR>that year (out of a number of years).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततिधा
ततिधा, ind., Ved. in so many parts, of such a<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततुरि|ततुरिः
ततुरि ततुरि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. तॄ), preserving,<BR>cherishing, conquering; an epithet of Agni and Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततृपि
ततृपि ततृपि for तातृपि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कर
तत्कर तत्-कर, तत्-काल, तत्-क्रिय, &c.<BR>These and other similar compounds will be found<BR>under तद्, p. 360, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्व|तत्त्वं
तत्त्व तत्त्व, अम्, n. (fr. तद्), the state of<BR>being that, true state, real state, truth, reality, opposed<BR>to what is illusory or fallacious; essential nature; the<BR>real nature of the human soul as being one and the<BR>same with the supreme spirit pervading the universe;<BR>(in philosophy) truth, reality, a true principle, first<BR>principle, (the number of these first principles varies<BR>according to the different systems; the Sāṅkhya<BR>phil. has twenty-five Tattvas, viz. A-vyakta or ‘the<BR>undiscrete;’ Buddhi, ‘intellect;’ Ahaṅkāra, ‘indi-<BR>viduality;’ the five Tan-mātras or ‘subtile elements;’<BR>the five Mahā-bhūtas or ‘gross elements;’ the eleven<BR>organs, including Manas or ‘mind;’ and, lastly, Puruṣa<BR>or ‘soul:’ hence तत्त्व is sometimes a term for<BR>‘twenty-five.’ The Māheśvaras admit only five<BR>Tattvas, viz. the five elements. In the Vedānta phil.<BR>तत्त्व is regarded as made up of तद् and त्वम्,<BR>‘this — thou,’ and called महा-वाक्य, ‘the great<BR>word,’ by which the identity of the whole world with<BR>the one eternal Brahma is expressed); an element<BR>or elementary property; the essence or substance of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-b" target="_blank">Page0359-b+ 79</a>]<BR>anything, sum and substance; slow time in music, a<BR>musical instrument; (एन), ind. according to the true<BR>state or nature of anything, in truth, truly, really,<BR>accurately.<BR>—तत्त्व-कौमुदी, f. ‘moonlight of the<BR>Tattvas,’ or साङ्ख्य-तत्त्वकौमुदी, title of a<BR>commentary on the Sāṅkhya-kārikā.<BR>—तत्त्व-<BR>चन्द्र, अस्, m. ‘the moon of truth,’ title of a<BR>commentary on the grammar Prakriyā-kaumudī.<BR>—तत्त्व-चिन्तामणि, इस्, m. title of a philosophical<BR>work by Gaṅgeśa.<BR>—तत्त्व-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>तत्त्व-ज्ञानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, knowing the truth or true<BR>nature of anything; acquainted with the true princi-<BR>ples of philosophy, understanding the principles of a<BR>science thoroughly; (अस्), m. a Brāhman.<BR>—तत्त्व-<BR>ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of the truth; a thorough<BR>knowledge of the principles of a science, insight into<BR>the true principles of philosophy.<BR>—तत्त्व-तस्, ind.<BR>truly, really, actually, accurately, according to the truth,<BR>fully.<BR>—तत्त्व-ता, f. truth, reality.<BR>—तत्त्व-दर्श,<BR>अस्, m. ‘perceiving truth,’ N. of one of the seven Ṛṣis<BR>under Manu Deva-sāvarṇi.<BR>—तत्त्व-दर्शिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘perceiving truth,’ N. of one of the sons of Manu<BR>Raivata; N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—तत्त्व-दीपन, अम्,<BR>n. ‘light of the Tattvas,’ title of a work.<BR>—तत्त्व-<BR>निकष-ग्रावन्, आ, m. the touchstone of principle.<BR>—तत्त्व-न्यास, अस्, m. ‘the imposition of truth or<BR>of the true principles,’ N. of a ceremony performed<BR>in honour of Viṣṇu; it consists in the application of<BR>mystical letters and other marks to the different<BR>parts of the body while certain prayers are recited.<BR>—तत्त्व-प्रकाश, अस्, m. ‘light of the true princi-<BR>ples,’ title of a philosophical commentary.<BR>—तत्त्व-<BR>बोधिनी, f. ‘revealing truth,’ title of a commentary<BR>on the Siddhānta-kaumudī by Jñānendra-sarasvatī.<BR>—तत्त्व-भाव, अस्, m. true being or nature.<BR>—तत्त्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing truth or the<BR>reality of things.<BR>—तत्त्व-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing the<BR>truth or first principles, knowing things as they are.<BR>—तत्त्व-विन्दु, उस्, m. ‘drop of truth,’ title of a<BR>philosophical treatise.<BR>—तत्त्व-विवित्सा, f. desire of<BR>knowing the truth or God.<BR>—तत्त्व-विवेक, अस्, m.<BR>or सिद्धान्त-तत्त्वविवेक, ‘sifting of established<BR>truths,’ title of an astronomical work.<BR>—तत्त्ववि-<BR>वेक-दीपन, अम्, n. ‘light of the investigation of<BR>truth,’ title of a philosophical work.<BR>—तत्त्व-<BR>सञ्चय, अस्, m. ‘collection of truths,’ title of a<BR>Buddhist work.<BR>—तत्त्व-सत्य-शास्त्र, अम्, n. title<BR>of a work by Guṇa-prabha.<BR>—तत्त्व-समास, अस्,<BR>m. ‘compendium of the Tattvas or principles,’ the<BR>title of the Sāṅkhya-sūtras ascribed to Kapila.<BR>—तत्त्वाभियोग (˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, m. a positive<BR>charge or declaration.<BR>—तत्त्वार्थ (˚व-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the exact truth, reality, truth.<BR>—तत्त्वार्थ-<BR>कौमुदी (˚व-अर्˚), f. the title of a commentary by<BR>Govindānanda on the Prāyaścitta-viveka.<BR>—तत्त्वार्-<BR>थ-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing the exact truth, knowing<BR>the reality.<BR>—तत्त्वार्थ-सूत्र (˚व-अर्˚), अम्, n.<BR>title of a Jaina work.<BR>—तत्त्वावबोध (˚व-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. perception of truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र तत्र, ind. (fr. the pronom. base 2. त;<BR>correlative of यत्र, and often used for the loc. cases<BR>तस्मिन्, तस्याम्, &c., of the pronoun तद्, but oftener<BR>as an adverb), in that place, there, yonder, thither,<BR>to that place; in that, therein; on that occasion, in<BR>that case, under those circumstances, then; therefore;<BR>तत्र तत्र, in that and that place, here and there,<BR>hither and thither, to every place; यत्र तत्र,<BR>indiscriminately; [cf. Goth. thathrô.]<BR>—तत्र-<BR>भवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, ‘Your Honour there,’ venera-<BR>ble, respectable, reverend; a respectful title given<BR>in dramatic language to absent persons; [cf. अत्र-<BR>भवत्.]<BR>—तत्र-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, there standing,<BR>dwelling there, situated there, belonging to that place,<BR>a by-stander.<BR>—तत्रापि (˚त्र-अपि), ind. there also,<BR>even there, nevertheless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रत्य|तत्रत्यः
तत्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, produced there or in that<BR>place, relating to that place, of that place, being there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्व|तत्वं
तत्व तत्व, a less correct form for तत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा तथा, ind. (fr. the pronom. base 2. त<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-c" target="_blank">Page0359-c+ 81</a>]<BR>and correlative of यथा), in that manner, so, thus,<BR>(the correlative standing in the preceding clause, e. g.<BR>यथा प्रियं तथाऽस्तु, as is agreeable so let it<BR>be; or in the subsequent clause, e. g. तथा प्रयत्-<BR>नम् आतिष्ठेद् यथा न पीडयेद् आत्मानम्, he<BR>should so make effort as that he may not injure him-<BR>self.) यथा-तथा, in whatever way, in any way;<BR>by all means. यथा-यथा — तथा-तथा, in what-<BR>ever manner — in that manner; in whatever degree —<BR>in that degree; the more — the more, (यथा यथा<BR>पुरुषः शास्त्रं समधि-गच्छति तथा तथा<BR>वि-जानाति, the more a man studies a book the more<BR>he understands it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा followed by इति is also used as a particle of<BR>assent, agreement, or promise, to express ‘so be it,’<BR>‘yes,’ ‘so it shall be,’ &c. (e. g. तथेत्य् उक्त्वा, having<BR>said, ‘so be it’ or ‘yes;’ तथेति प्रति-ज्ञाय, having<BR>promised, ‘so it shall be’); also in forms of adjura-<BR>tion (e. g. यथा ऽहम् अन्यं न चिन्तये तथा<BR>ऽयम् पततां क्षुद्रः परासुः, as surely as I<BR>do not think on any other man, so surely let this<BR>wretch fall dead).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा is frequently used as a conjunction to ex-<BR>press ‘so also,’ ‘in like manner,’ ‘and also’ (e. g.<BR>सुखं सेवेद् दुःखं तथा, let him make use of<BR>prosperity and also adversity). तथा हि, for so,<BR>for thus (it has been said), for instance; तथा च,<BR>and likewise; and so it has been said; (this and the<BR>preceding are often used in introducing quotations.)<BR>तथापि (तथा-अपि), even thus, even so, neverthe-<BR>less, yet, still, notwithstanding; यद्यपि — तथापि,<BR>even if — yet; although — nevertheless. तथैव (त-<BR>था-एव), even so, even thus, exactly so, in like man-<BR>ner.<BR>—तथा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, thus done or made.<BR>—तथा-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, so intending, having<BR>such an aim.<BR>—तथा-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, being in such<BR>a state or condition; of such a quality or nature;<BR>(अस्), m. a Buddha; a Jina; N. of a prince.<BR>—त-<BR>थागत-कूप, अस्, m. ‘the well of the Tathā-gata,’<BR>N. of a well.<BR>—तथागत-गर्भ, अस्, m. title of<BR>a Buddhist Sūtra work; N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—त-<BR>थागत-गुण-ज्ञानाचिन्त्य-विषयावतार-निर्-<BR>देश (˚न-अचिन्त्य-विषय-अव्˚), अस्, m. title of a<BR>Buddhist Sūtra work; direction (निर्-देश) how to<BR>attain (अव-तार) to the inconceivable subject (अचिन्-<BR>त्य-विषय) of the qualities (गुण) and to the<BR>knowledge (ज्ञान) of a Tathā-gata.<BR>—तथागत-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a man; N. of a king.<BR>—त-<BR>थागत-गुह्यक, अम्, n. ‘the mystery of a Tathā-<BR>gata,’ title of one of the nine works highly revered<BR>by the Buddhists of Nepal.<BR>—तथागत-भद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Nāgārjuna.<BR>—तथा-गुण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with such qualities.<BR>—तथा-ता,<BR>f. or तथा-त्व, अम्, n. such a state of things, such a<BR>condition; true state of things, true, nature; the<BR>being so; the case or circumstances being admitted<BR>to be as stated.<BR>—तथा-प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having such power.<BR>—तथा-भाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, of<BR>such a nature; about to be so or of such a kind.<BR>—तथा-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, of such qualities, of<BR>such a kind or nature.<BR>—तथा-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>‘so-facing,’ turning the face in the same direction.<BR>—तथायत (˚था-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘so-directed,’<BR>turned towards the same point.<BR>—तथा-राज, अस्, m.<BR>a Buddha or Jina; [cf. तथा-गत.]<BR>—तथा-रूप,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or तथा-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, of such a<BR>form, thus shaped, so formed, looking thus.<BR>—त-<BR>था-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, professing to be so and so.<BR>—तथा-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of such a sort or kind,<BR>being in such a condition or state, of such qualities;<BR>(अम्), ind. thus, in this manner; likewise, equally.<BR>—तथा-विधेय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to such a sort<BR>or kind, being of such a kind or nature.<BR>—तथा-<BR>व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, observing such conduct or practices,<BR>so acting.<BR>—तथा-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, behaving or con-<BR>ducting one's self thus.<BR>—तथास्तु (˚था-अस्˚), ind.<BR>so be it.<BR>—तथा-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, uttered with<BR>the same accent.<BR>—तथेति, see तथा followed by<BR>इति above.<BR>—तथैव (˚था-एव), ind., see तथा<BR>above.<BR>—तथोत्साह (˚था-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, making<BR>so great efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्य|तथ्यं
तथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘being really so,’ true, real,<BR>genuine; (अम्), n. truth, reality; तथ्येन or तथ्-<BR>यतस्, ind. according to truth.<BR>—तथ्य-वादिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, speaking the truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्य|तथ्यं
तथ्य तथ्य. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् तद्, सस्, सा, तद् or तत्, (the actual<BR>base of this pronoun in all the cases except the nom.<BR>sing. m. and f. is त, but the neut. तद् represents<BR>the base in compounds and in the derivative तदीय.<BR>In the Veda the nom. and acc. du. m. may be ता as<BR>well as तौ, the nom. plur. n. ता as well as तानि, and<BR>the inst. plur. m. or n. तेभिस् as well as तैस्), he,<BR>she, it, that, this, (often occurring as a correlative of<BR>the relative pronoun य, ‘who, which,’ the relative<BR>generally standing in the preceding clause, e. g. यस्य<BR>बुद्धिः स बलवान्, of whom there is intellect he<BR>is strong, see Gram. 799.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् is sometimes used, for the sake of emphasis, in<BR>connection with the first and second personal pronouns,<BR>with other demonstratives and with relatives like the<BR>Lat. ille (e. g. सोऽहम्, I that very person, I myself;<BR>ते वयम्, we those very persons; ताव् इमौ, those<BR>very two; तद् एतद्, that very thing; यत् तत् का-<BR>रणम्, that very reason which; या सा श्रीः, that<BR>very fortune which).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् is repeated in the sense of ‘this and that,’<BR>‘this or that,’ ‘various,’ ‘different’ (e. g. तं तं<BR>देशं जगाम, he went to this and that place;<BR>तासु तासु योनिषु, in different or various birth-<BR>places).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् is used in connection with a relative pronoun<BR>in the sense of ‘whosoever,’ ‘whichsoever,’ ‘every’<BR>(e. g. यस्मिंस् तस्मिन् कुले, in any family whatever).<BR>Sometimes both the demonstrative and the relative<BR>are repeated (e. g. यद्यत् कर्म पर-वशं तत्-<BR>तद् वर्जयेत्, whatever action depends on another,<BR>that he should avoid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद्, n., may be used to signify ‘this world’ [cf.<BR>इदम्]; also to denote ‘the supreme spirit or Brahma’<BR>(opposed to त्वम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद्, ind. there, thither, in that place, to that spot<BR>(e. g. तमांसि यत्र गच्छन्ति तत् क्रव्यादो<BR>अजीगमम्, where dark shades prevail there I caused<BR>the flesh-eaters to go); then, at that time, in that<BR>case (e. g. यदि मां न विहातुम् इच्छसि तत्<BR>किम्-अर्थम् पन्थाः समुप-दिश्यते, if thou dost<BR>not wish to leave me why is the road pointed out?);<BR>thus, in this manner, with regard to that, in connec-<BR>tion with that (often so used in the Brāhmaṇas, e. g.<BR>तद् एतौ श्लोकौ भवतः, with reference to that<BR>there are these two verses); on that account, for<BR>that reason, therefore, consequently (in this sense<BR>commonly used in classical Sanskrit, e. g. यद् — तद्<BR>or येन — तद्, because — therefore); now, so also,<BR>equally, in like manner (often connecting two sen-<BR>tences or clauses in the Brāhmaṇas). तद् अपि, and<BR>also, and equally; nevertheless, notwithstanding<BR>(यद्य् अपि — तद् अपि, even if — nevertheless); तद्<BR>यथा, in such a manner as follows, as here follows,<BR>namely; तच्चापि, and also, and likewise; [cf.<BR>Lith. tas, ta, ‘this;’ Goth. tha (the base of<BR>the article), masc. sa, fem. sô; Gr. ὁ, ἡ, τό;<BR>Slav. t', ta, to; Lat. is-te, is-ta, is-tud, tam, tum,<BR>tunc; Hib. so ‘this,’ se ‘he,’ si ‘she.’]<BR>—तच्-<BR>छील (तद्-शि˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an inclination for<BR>that, accustomed to that; [cf. ताच्छीलिक and ताच्-<BR>छील्य.]<BR>—तज्-ज (तद्-ज), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘produced<BR>at that moment,’ immediate, instantaneous.<BR>—तज्-<BR>जय (तद्-ज˚), अस्, m. the conquest of that.<BR>—तज्-<BR>ज-लान् (तद्-ज-ल-अन्), न्, न्, न्, produced, absorbed,<BR>and breathing in that.<BR>—तज्-ज्ञ (तद्-ज्ञ), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, knowing that, knowing, experienced in or fami-<BR>liar with; (अस्), m. a knowing or intelligent man,<BR>(in this and other compounds तद् often loses its<BR>meaning and becomes redundant; cf. तत्-पर, तद्-<BR>भाव, &c.)<BR>—तत्-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, performing a<BR>particular work or service, serving, obeying, a servant.<BR>—तत्-कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper or necessary to<BR>be done with reference to present circumstances; [cf.<BR>इति-कर्तव्य.]<BR>—तत्-काल, अस्, m. that time (op-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-b" target="_blank">Page0360-b+ 81</a>]<BR>posed to एतत्-काल, this time); present time, time<BR>being, the time referred to or spoken of, the same<BR>time, the time when an act occurs; (अम्), ind. at<BR>that time, at a certain time; directly, immediately;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), happening at the same time or imme-<BR>diately; [cf. तात्कालिक.]<BR>—तत्काल-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ,<BR>wise or intelligent for the time being, having presence<BR>of mind, &c.<BR>—तत्काल-लवण, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>salt prepared artificially, = विड्-लवण.<BR>—तत्कालोत्-<BR>पन्न-धी (˚ल-उत्˚), ईस्, ईस्, इ, possessed of presence<BR>of mind.<BR>—तत्-कुलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>that family or caste.<BR>—तत्-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, per-<BR>forming a particular work or service; working without<BR>hire or wages.<BR>—तत्-क्षण, अस्, m. time present,<BR>time being; the same moment; a measure of time,<BR>= 120 Kṣaṇas, = (1/60) Lava; (अम् or आत्), ind. at<BR>the same moment, immediately, directly.<BR>—तत्क्ष-<BR>ण-भङ्गुर, अस्, आ, अम्, vanishing immediately,<BR>transient.<BR>—तत्-तृतीय, अस्, आ, अम्, doing that for<BR>the third time.<BR>—तत्-पद, अम्, n. the place or<BR>position of that; the word तद्; (अस्), m. the tree<BR>Ficus Religiosa.<BR>—तत्-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, following<BR>that or thereupon, coming after, inferior; having that<BR>as one's highest object or aim, totally devoted or<BR>addicted to anything, attending to anything closely,<BR>eagerly engaged in (with loc. or in composition);<BR>diligent; (अस्), m. the thirtieth part of the twinkling<BR>of the eye; (with reference to the redundant use of<BR>तद् cf. तज्-ज्ञ, तद्-गत, तद्-भाव, तात्पर्य.)<BR>—तत्पर-ता, f. or तत्पर-त्व, अम्, n. entire de-<BR>votion or addiction to; the state of following after or<BR>behind, inferiority.<BR>—तत्-परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, at-<BR>tached or addicted to any particular thing or person.<BR>—तत्-पुरुष, अस्, m. the original or supreme<BR>spirit; the servant or attendant of him; a class of<BR>compounds in which the last member is defined or<BR>qualified by the first without losing its original inde-<BR>pendance, i. e. continues the principal member of the<BR>compound and preserves its original grammatical charac-<BR>ter whether as a noun, adjective, or participle, whereas<BR>in a Bahu-vrīhi compound the last member loses its<BR>independance as well as its original grammatical cha-<BR>racter and serves together with the first member<BR>only to qualify or define another word; the Karma-<BR>dhāraya and Dvigu compounds are considered as<BR>subdivisions of the Tat-puruṣa class. The word<BR>तत्-पुरुष, ‘his servant,’ is itself an example of<BR>this class of compounds. The stock example is<BR>दिव्य-कुसुमम्, ‘heavenly flower,’ which belongs<BR>to the Karma-dhāraya subdivision.<BR>—तत्-पूर्व, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, occurring or happening for the first time;<BR>prior, former.<BR>—तत्पूर्व-सङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, then<BR>first restrained.<BR>—तत्-प्रकार, अस्, आ, अम्, of that<BR>kind, of that sort.<BR>—तत्-प्रथम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>doing that for the first time.<BR>—तत्-प्रभाते, ind.<BR>early on the next morning.<BR>—तत्-फल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having that as a fruit or reward; having as a result<BR>or consequence; (अस्), m. the white water-lily; a<BR>kind of medicinal plant (कुष्ठ); a kind of per-<BR>fume (= चौर).<BR>—तत्-समनन्तरम्, ind. im-<BR>mediately upon that or afterwards; [cf. तद्-अनन्-<BR>तरम्.]<BR>—तत्-साधु-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, accomplishing<BR>or performing that.<BR>—तत्-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being on<BR>or in that, connected with that; (अस्), m. a particular<BR>mode of multiplication.<BR>—तद्-अतिपात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>transgressing that, going beyond the bounds.<BR>—तद्-<BR>अनन्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, nearest or next to that; (अम्),<BR>ind. immediately upon that, thereupon, then (प्राक् —<BR>तद्-अनन्तरम्, first — afterwards; प्रथमम् —<BR>—तद्-अनन्तरम् — तृतीयम् — अतः परम्, first<BR> — afterwards — thirdly — further; [cf. तत्-समनन्-<BR>तरम्.]<BR>—तद्-अनु, ind. after that, afterwards.<BR>—तद्-अनुसरण-क्रमेण, ind. in a manner<BR>conformably to that, subsequently to that.<BR>—तद्-<BR>अन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, coming to an end or perishing in<BR>that, ending thus, thus terminating.<BR>—तद्-अन्न,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. accustomed to that food.<BR>—तद्-<BR>अन्यत्, ind. other than that, different from that.<BR>—तद्-अपस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. doing that work,<BR>having that occupation, accustomed to do that; (अस्),<BR>ind. in the usual way.<BR>—तद्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, des-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-c" target="_blank">Page0360-c+ 81</a>]<BR>tined or intended for that, on that account, with that<BR>object; having that meaning; (अम्), ind. on that<BR>account, with that object, for that end, therefore;<BR>[cf. तादर्थ्य.]<BR>—तद्-अर्थीय, अस्, आ, अम्, destined<BR>or intended for that, undertaken for that end.<BR>—तद्-<BR>अर्पण, अम्, n. delivery of that, delivering or returning<BR>any article.<BR>—तद्-अर्ह, अस्, आ, अम्, meriting that.<BR>—तद्-अवधि, इस्, m. that limit, that period; (इ),<BR>ind. so far, up to that period; from that time.<BR>—तद्-<BR>अवस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, so situated, thus circumstanced,<BR>in that condition.<BR>—तद्-आकार, अस्, आ, अम्, having that<BR>appearance or aspect.<BR>—तद्-आमुख, अम्, n. com-<BR>mencement, beginning.<BR>—तद्-इद्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. intent on that particular object.<BR>—तद्-एकचित्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having all the thoughts fixed on that<BR>(person or thing).<BR>—तदेवोपनिषद् (तद्-एव-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f. title of an Upaniṣad beginning with the words<BR>तद् एव.<BR>—तद्-ओकस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. rejoicing or<BR>delighting in that, at home in it; (Sāy.) having that<BR>as one's dwelling-place.<BR>—तद्-ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>endowed with such strength.<BR>—तद्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>gone to that, directed towards that, devoted to, intent<BR>on; (अस्), m. (?) the continued multiplication of four<BR>or more like quantities; [cf. तज्-ज्ञ, तत्-पर, तद्-<BR>भाव.]<BR>—तद्-गुण, अस्, m. the quality of that<BR>(person or thing), quality or virtue of anything; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), possessing these qualities; (अस्), m. a figure<BR>of speech in rhetoric, transferring the qualities of one<BR>thing to another.<BR>—तद्गुण-संविज्ञान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, a term applied to those Bahu-vrīhi compounds<BR>in which the qualities implied in the name are per-<BR>ceived along with the thing itself (e. g. दीर्घ-कर्-<BR>णम् आ-नय, bring दीर्घ-कर्ण, ‘long-ear,’<BR>where the long ears accompany and mark the indi-<BR>vidual. An example of the अ-तद्गुण-संविज्ञान<BR>would be दृष्ट-सागरम् आ-नय, bring the man<BR>who has seen the ocean).<BR>—तद्-दिन, अम्, n. that<BR>day; (अम्), ind. during the day, every day, day by<BR>day, on a certain day.<BR>—तद्-दुःख, अम्, n. that<BR>grief, grief for that or of that.<BR>—तद्-द्वितीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, doing that for the second time.<BR>—तद्-धन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, miserly, niggardly.<BR>—तद्-धर्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, having that business, accomplishing that business;<BR>[cf. ताद्धर्म्य.]<BR>—तद्-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, obey-<BR>ing the laws of him or that.<BR>—तद्-धित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (fr. तद्-हित), good for that, salutary; (अम्), n.<BR>the welfare of any one; (अस्), m., scil. प्रत्ययः,<BR>an affix which forms nouns from other nouns, (whereas<BR>a Kṛt affix forms nouns from roots); a noun formed<BR>by a Taddhita affix, a derivative noun.<BR>—तद्-बल,<BR>अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of arrow.<BR>—तद्-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>the becoming that, becoming (in general), e. g.<BR>अभूत-तद्भाव, the becoming what one was not<BR>formerly.<BR>—तद्-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, different or<BR>distinct from that.<BR>—तद्-रस, अस्, m. the spirit<BR>thereof.<BR>—तद्-राज, अस्, m., scil. प्रत्ययः, an affix<BR>added to a proper name to form from it the name of<BR>a king or chief (e. g. fr. अङ्ग is formed आङ्ग, ‘king<BR>of the Aṅgas,’ by the Tad-rāja affix अञ्).<BR>—तद्-<BR>रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, thus shaped, so formed.<BR>—तद्र्यञ्च्,<BR>अङ्, द्रीची, अक् (fr. तद्, with अद्रि substituted for अद्,<BR>and rt. अञ्च्), extending thither; [cf. देवद्र्यञ्च्, &c.]<BR>—तद्-वचः-प्रतीत, अस्, आ, अम्, believing his words.<BR>—तद्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having or containing that,<BR>possessed of that; (वत्), ind. like that, in that manner,<BR>thus; in like manner, equally, likewise, also; (यद्वत् —<BR>तद्वत् or यथा — तद्वत्, as — so.)<BR>—तद्वत्-ता, f.<BR>conformity, agreement.<BR>—तद्-वश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>longing for or desiring that.<BR>—तद्-वाचक, अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, signifying that.<BR>—तद्-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing that,<BR>familiar with that; knowing the truth, a knowing<BR>man.<BR>—तद्-विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing a knowledge<BR>of that.<BR>—तद्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of that kind, cor-<BR>responding to that, conformable to that.<BR>—तद्विध-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. correspondence or conformity with that.<BR>—तद्-विषय or तद्-विषयक, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing that for its object, attending to that business,<BR>relating to that.<BR>—तन्-न, ind. not that, not so.<BR>—तन्-नाश, अस्, m. destruction of that.<BR>—तन्-म-<BR>ध्य-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated in the midst of that.<BR>—तन्-मध्यात्, ind. from the midst thereof,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">Page0361-a+ 79</a>]<BR>from amongst them.<BR>—तन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made<BR>up of that, having the nature of that, absorbed or<BR>contained in or identical with that, become one<BR>with.<BR>—तन्मय-ता, f. or तन्मय-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being contained in or identical with that.<BR>—तन्-<BR>मरण, अम्, n. his death.<BR>—तन्-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>only so much or so little; consisting of rudimentary<BR>atoms or elementary matter; (अम्), n. merely that,<BR>only a trifle; that in which its own peculiar property<BR>resides without any change or variety, i. e. a subtile<BR>element or a rudiment of elementary matter, (of<BR>these there are five, viz. शब्द-त्˚, स्पर्श-त्˚, रूप-<BR>त्˚, रस-त्˚, and गन्ध-त्˚, from which the five<BR>Mahā-bhūtas or grosser elements are produced. In<BR>this sense also according to some तन्-मात्रा, f.)<BR>—तन्मात्र-ता, f. or तन्मात्र-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of a Tanmātra.<BR>—तन्मात्र-सर्ग, अस्, m. (in<BR>the Sāṅkhya phil.) the rudimental creation.<BR>—तन्-<BR>मात्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of rudimentary atoms<BR>or elementary matter.<BR>—तन्-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, im-<BR>plying the doing of that which the base indicates (?),<BR>(e. g. the nominal अघाय, to act wickedly, is a<BR>तन्-मानिन्.)<BR>—तल्-लक्षण (तद्-ल˚), अम्, n. the<BR>mark of him, a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदा
तदा, ind. at that time, then; in that case; (some-<BR>times used rather redundantly in epic poetry, e. g.<BR>ततो ऽन्तरीक्षगो वाचं व्या-जहार नलं<BR>तदा, upon that the bird addressed words to Nala<BR>then); यदा तदा, at any time whatsoever; तदा<BR>प्रभृति, from that time forward; यद् — तदा or<BR>यत्र — तदा or यदा — तदा or यदि — तदा, when<BR> — then; if — then, &c.; यतस् — तदा, from the time<BR>when — then, i. e. ever since; यर्ह्य् एव — तदैव,<BR>at what time — at that very time, i. e. at the very<BR>time when.<BR>—तदा-त्व, अम्, n. ‘the state of then,’<BR>that time, present time, time being, present state or<BR>circumstances, (usually in connection with आयति,<BR>future time.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानीम्
तदानीम्, ind. at that time, then [cf. इदानीम्];<BR>यदा — तदानीम्, when — then.<BR>—तदानीन्-तन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, of that time, belonging to that time.<BR>—तदानीन्-दुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. milked at that<BR>time or at the time spoken of, just milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदीय
तदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to him or her or<BR>that or them; his, hers, its, theirs; such (e. g. चिन्तया<BR>तदीयया, with a thought such as that).<BR>—तदीय-<BR>सङ्ग, अस्, m. meeting with her, union with her.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् 1. तन् (= स्तन्), cl. 4. P., Ved. तन्-<BR>यति, to resound, sound aloud, roar; [cf. Gr.<BR>τόνος; Lat. tonare; Angl. Sax. thunor; Eng.<BR>thunder.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयित्नु
तनयित्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. roaring, thundering;<BR>[cf. स्तनयित्नु, तन्यता, तन्यतु, तन्यु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् 2. तन्, cl. 1. and 10. P. तनति and<BR>तानयति, &c., to confide, belive or have<BR>faith in; to aid, assist; to be harmless; to pain or<BR>afflict with disease (?); [cf. rt. 1. चन् and वन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् 3. तन्, cl. 8. P. A. तनोति, तनुते, त-<BR>तान (2nd sing. ततन्थ or तेनिथ),<BR>तेने, तनिष्यति, -ते, अतानीत् and अतनीत्, अतत and<BR>अतनिष्ट, तनितुम्, to extend, stretch, spread, be<BR>diffused over, shine (as light), extend towards, reach<BR>to; protract, prolong, lengthen out, augment; to<BR>lengthen, be lengthened out, be protracted, continue,<BR>endure, last; to stretch (a cord), extend or bend (a<BR>bow), spread or spin out, weave; to emboss, chase;<BR>to prepare (a way for); direct one's way towards; to<BR>propagate, be propagated; to accomplish, perform (as<BR>a ceremony), to sacrifice; to compose (a literary work);<BR>to bestow, grant, cause, prepare: Pass. तन्यते or<BR>तायते, to be extended; to increase, &c.: Caus. तान-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, अतीतनत्: Desid. तितनिषति, तितंसति,<BR>तितांसति: Intens. तन्तन्यते, तन्तनीति, तन्तन्ति;<BR>[cf. Gr. τείνω: Lat. tendo, tenuis, tener:<BR>Goth. thanja: Russ. tonju: Lith. tempju: Hib.<BR>tana, ‘thin, slender, lean;’ tanaighim, ‘I make<BR>thin.’]<BR>—तन्-आदि, अयस्, m. pl., scil. धातवस्, the<BR>roots beginning with तन्, i. e. the eighth class of<BR>roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्
2. तत्, त्, त्, त्, at the end of a comp.; [cf. परी-<BR>तत्.] (For 1. तत् see p. 358, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
2. तत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 359), extended,<BR>stretched, spread, diffused, expanded; spreading or<BR>reaching over, extending to; covered over, concealed;<BR>protracted, continued; bent (as a bow); spreading, wide,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. wind, air; (अम्), n. any stringed musical<BR>instrument; a kind of metre consisting of four lines<BR>of twelve syllables each.<BR>—तत-चिह्न, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having marks drawn along, distinctly marked.<BR>—त-<BR>त-पत्त्री, f. the plantain tree, Musa Sapientum;<BR>[cf. कदल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
2. तति, इस्, f. (for 1. see p. 359, col. 1), a series,<BR>a line, a row or range; a number, a crowd, a troop;<BR>a sacrificial act, a ceremony; [cf. तन्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
4. तन् (probably f., but occurring only in dat., inst.,<BR>and abl.), Ved. continuation, diffusion, propagation,<BR>offspring, posterity, descendants; (तन्वे तने च, for<BR>one's own person and one's children); तना (inst.<BR>used as an adv.), in uninterrupted succession or series,<BR>one after another, continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन|तनः
तन, अस्, m., Ved. a descendant; (आ, अम्), f. n.<BR>offspring, a descendant, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनय|तनयः
तनय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. propagating or extend-<BR>ing a family, belonging to one's own family; (तो-<BR>कं तनयम्, a child which propagates the family);<BR>(अस्), m. a male descendant, a son; N. of one of the<BR>seven sages in the eleventh Manv-antara with the<BR>patronymic Vāsiṣṭha; (in astrology) N. of the fifth<BR>lunar mansion; (औ), m. du. a son and a daughter;<BR>(आ), f. a daughter; N. of a plant, = चक्र-कुल्या;<BR>(अम्), n. posterity, family, race, offspring, child,<BR>descendant; (according to the scholiasts तनय is a<BR>grandchild and तोक a child); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—तनय-भवन, अस्, m. (in astrology)<BR>N. of the fifth lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयीकृत
तनयी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनस्
तनस्, अस्, n., Ved. offspring, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिमन्
तनिमन्, आ, m. (fr. तनु below), thinness, slen-<BR>derness, minuteness; (अ), n. the liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिष्ठ|तनिष्ठः
तनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of तनु), thinnest,<BR>very thin, smallest, least; very minute or delicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनीयस्
तनीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of तनु), thinner,<BR>more minute, smaller, less, very thin, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनु|तनुः
तनु, उस्, उस्, or वी or ऊस्, उ, thin, slender, slim,<BR>attenuated, emaciated, small, minute; delicate, fine,<BR>having minute interstices (as a web); little, un-<BR>important; shallow (as a river); spare; (उस्), m.,<BR>N. of a certain Ṛṣi with a very emaciated body<BR>[cf. तानव्य]; (उस् or तनू, ऊस्), f. (the latter form<BR>only being used in the earlier language), the body,<BR>the person (applied also to gods); one's own person,<BR>self (often used in the Veda like a reflexive pronoun,<BR>e. g. यजस्व तन्वम्, worship thy own person or<BR>thyself; cf. आत्मन्); outward form or manifestation;<BR>nature, form, or character of anything; appearance; (उस्),<BR>f. the skin; N. of the first lunar mansion; (वी), f. a<BR>delicate or slender or graceful woman; N. of one of the<BR>wives of Kṛṣṇa; a kind of plant [cf. शाल-पर्णी];<BR>a stanza of four lines and twenty-four syllables in<BR>each; [cf. Gr. τανυ- Lat. tenuis; Old Germ.<BR>dunni; Germ. dūnn; Hib. tana; Eng. thin.]<BR>—तनु-कूप, अस्, m. a pore of the skin, (lit. well<BR>of the skin.)<BR>—तनु-क्षीर, अस्, m. the tree Spon-<BR>dias Magnifera; [cf. आम्रातक.]<BR>—तनु-गृह,<BR>अम्, n. (in astrology) N. of the first lunar mansion.<BR>—तनु-च्छद्, त्, त्, त्, or तनु-च्छद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>covering the body, protecting, clothing; (त्), f. or<BR>(दस्), m. armour, attire.<BR>—तनु-च्छाय, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of Acacia, = जाल-वर्वूरक.<BR>—तनु-ज, अस्,<BR>m. a son; (आ), f. a daughter; [cf. तनू-ज and आत्म-<BR>ज.]<BR>—तनुज-त्व, अम्, n. sonship.<BR>—तनु-तर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, thinner, more minute; [cf. तनीयस्.]<BR>—तनु-ता, f. thinness, tenuity, extenuation, little-<BR>ness, diminutiveness.<BR>—तनु-त्यज्, क्, क्, क्, giving<BR>up one's person, dying; risking one's life, facing<BR>death with courage; [cf. तनू-त्यज्.]<BR>—तनु-त्याग,<BR>अस्, m. giving up one's own self, risking one's life;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), giving scantily, spending little, nig-<BR>gardly, sparing.<BR>—तनु-त्र, अम्, n. armour, mail<BR>(‘protecting the body’).<BR>—तनुत्र-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-c" target="_blank">Page0361-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अत्, having armour, defended.<BR>—तनु-त्राण, अम्, n.<BR>(‘protection for the body’), armour, mail.<BR>—तनु-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. thinness.<BR>—तनु-त्वच्, क्, n. (?) the cinna-<BR>mon tree; the plant Cassia Senna.<BR>—तनु-त्वचा, f.<BR>the plant Premna Spinosa; [cf. क्षुद्राग्नि-मन्-<BR>थ.]<BR>—तनु-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the tree Terminalia<BR>Catappa [cf. इङ्गुद], commonly Hiṅganabeṭa;<BR>leafy orpiment.<BR>—तनु-भव, अस्, m. a son; [cf.<BR>तनू-ज and तनूद्भव.]<BR>—तनु-भस्त्रा, f. the<BR>nose (‘the bellows of the body’).<BR>—तनु-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. thinness.<BR>—तनु-भूमि, इस्, f. ‘the stage of per-<BR>sonality,’ one of the periods in the life of a Buddhist<BR>Śrāvaka.<BR>—तनु-भृत्, त्, m. any being furnished<BR>with a body, especially a human being.<BR>—तनु-मत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, embodied, corporeal.<BR>—तनु-मध्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a slender or elegant waist; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a metre of four lines, each consisting of two<BR>short syllables between four long ones (¯¯˘˘¯¯);<BR>[cf. तनु-शिरस्.]<BR>—तनु-मध्यम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>slender-waisted.<BR>—तनु-रस, अस्, m. perspiration,<BR>sweat.<BR>—तनु-रुह्, ट्, or तनु-रुह, अम्, n. the<BR>hair or down of the body; [cf. तनू-रुह.]<BR>—तनु-<BR>वात, अस्, m. a very thin or rarefied atmosphere (con-<BR>stituting a kind of hell; opposed to घन-वात, q. v.);<BR>according to others, a peculiar division of hell.<BR>—त-<BR>नु-वार, अम्, n. (fr. तनु and वार fr. rt. वृ, to<BR>cover, protect), armour, mail.<BR>—तनुवार-भस,<BR>अस्, m. (?) a man in armour, a warrior.<BR>—तनु-वीज,<BR>अस्, m. the jujube; [cf. राज-बदर.]<BR>—तनु-<BR>व्रण, अस्, m. a pimple, a pustule, a boil, elephanti-<BR>asis.<BR>—तनु-शरीर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a delicate<BR>body, delicately formed.<BR>—तनु-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>‘having a small head,’ N. of a subdivision of the<BR>Uṣṇih metre, consisting of three Pādas of eleven,<BR>eleven, and six syllables; [cf. तनु-मध्या.]<BR>—त-<BR>नु-सञ्चारिणी, f. a young woman, a girl, one ten<BR>years old (‘moving the body coquettishly?’).<BR>—तनु-<BR>ह्रद, अस्, m. the anus, the rectum; [cf. तनू-<BR>ह्रद.]<BR>—तनू-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced or born on<BR>or from the body; belonging to the person; (अस्),<BR>m. a son; N. of a Sādhya; (आ), f. a daughter; [cf.<BR>तनु-ज.]<BR>—तनू-जनि, इस्, m. a son.<BR>—तनू-जन्-<BR>मन्, आ, m. a son.<BR>—तनूजाङ्ग (˚ज-अङ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a wing, the feathers (‘member produced on the<BR>body’); [cf. तनू-रुह.]<BR>—तनू-तल, अस्, m. a<BR>measure of length equal to the arms extended, a<BR>fathom.<BR>—तनू-त्यज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. giving up one's<BR>person, risking one's life, rash, foolhardy.<BR>—तनू-<BR>दूषि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. destroying the person.<BR>—तनू-<BR>देवता, f. a form of fire deified.<BR>—तनू-देश, अस्, m. a<BR>region or part of the body.<BR>—तनूद्भव (˚नु-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a son; [cf. तनु-भव.]<BR>—तनून (˚नु-<BR>ऊन), अस्, m. ‘the bodiless one,’ the wind.<BR>—तनू-<BR>नप, अम्, n. clarified butter, ghee; (this word<BR>owes its existence to a wrong derivation of the<BR>following word from तनूनप-अद्, ‘eating the<BR>clarified butter.’)<BR>—तनू-नपात्, त्, m. one of the<BR>sacred names of Fire, ‘the son or descendant of him-<BR>self,’ so called because fire need not necessarily be<BR>derived from other fire, but is sometimes self-gene-<BR>rated as in the lightning or by the attrition of the<BR>Araṇis, q. v.; (for a fanciful derivation see the pre-<BR>ceding. Agni appears chiefly as Tanū-napāt in some<BR>verses of the Āprī hymns; see आ-प्री); the plant<BR>Plumbago Zeylanica.<BR>—तनूनपात्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>containing the word तनू-नपात्.<BR>—तनू-नप्तृ,<BR>ता, m., Ved. = तनू-नपात्; [cf. तानूनप्त्र.]<BR>—तनू-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. protecting the person,<BR>preserving the life.<BR>—तनू-पान, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>protecting the person or life; (अम्), n. protection of<BR>the person.<BR>—तनू-पावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. protect-<BR>ing the person or life.<BR>—तनू-पृष्ठ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Soma sacrifice.<BR>—तनू-बल, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>strength of the body, one's own strength.<BR>—तनू-<BR>रुच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. brilliant in person (as Agni);<BR>brilliant with arms (?).<BR>—तनू-रुह, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>the hair of the body; the wing or feathers of a bird;<BR>(अस्), m. a son; [cf. तनु-रुह, तनु-ज, तनु-<BR>जाङ्ग.]<BR>—तनूर्ज (˚नु-ऊर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>the third Manu.<BR>—तनू-वशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having<BR>power over the body, an epithet of Agni.<BR>—तनू-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">Page0362-a+ 81</a>]<BR>शुभ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. decorating the person,<BR>adorning the body.<BR>—तनू-हविस्, इस्, n., N. of<BR>three oblations offered to the three tanūs or forms<BR>(of Agni).<BR>—तनू-ह्रद, अस्, m. the anus, the<BR>rectum; [cf. तनु-ह्रद.]<BR>—तन्व्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having slender limbs, delicate, slim; (ई), f. a<BR>delicate or slender woman; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुक
तनुक, अस्, आ, अम्, thin, small; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>several plants, Grislea Tomentosa, Terminalia Bel-<BR>lerica; the cinnamon tree; (आ), f. the tree Diospyros<BR>Embryopteris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुल|तनुलः
तनुल, अस्, आ, अम्, spread, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुस्
तनुस्, उस्, n. the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनू
तनू, ऊस्, f. the body. See तनु, p. 361, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूकृ
तनू-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to make thin or fine, to attenuate, diminish, emaciate;<BR>to pare.<BR>—तनू-करण, अम्, n. making thin, at-<BR>tenuation, diminishing, weakening.<BR>—तनू-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. shaping or forming the person, preserving<BR>the life; (Sāy.) forming offspring, granting children.<BR>—तनू-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made delicate or thin,<BR>pared.<BR>—तनू-कृथ, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), Ved.<BR>preservation of the person; (Sāy.) on account of his<BR>son (in loc. case).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्ति|तंतिः|तन्तिः
तन्ति, इस्, f. a thread, cord, line, string; a series,<BR>a line, row; expansion, extension; N. of a woman;<BR>(इस्), m. a weaver.<BR>—तन्ति-पाल or तन्ति-पालक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘a guardian of the rows (of calves),’ a N.<BR>assumed by Saha-deva when living with king Virāṭa;<BR>(also applied to Nakula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्ती
तन्ती, f. a leading cow (i. e. one going at the head<BR>of the Tantayas or lines of calves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तु|तंतु|तंतुः|तन्तुः
तन्तु, उस्, m. a thread, cord, wire, string, line,<BR>the warp of a web; N. of the Supreme Being; a cob-<BR>web; a filament, fibre, sprig; a line of descendants,<BR>propagation of offspring, issue, race; a shark [cf. तन्-<BR>तुण and तन्तु-नाग]; N. of a man; [cf. काष्ठ-<BR>तन्तु, वर-त्˚, सप्त-त्˚.]<BR>—तन्तु-काष्ठ, अम्,<BR>n. a piece of fibrous wood, or a brush used by weavers<BR>for cleaning the threads of the woof; [cf. तन्त्र-<BR>काष्ठ.]<BR>—तन्तु-कीट, अस्, m. a silk-worm.<BR>—तन्-<BR>तु-नाग, अस्, m. a shark.<BR>—तन्तु-निर्यास, अस्, m.<BR>the palmyra tree [cf. ताल]; (fr. तन्तु, a thread,<BR>and निर्-यास, exudation, alluding to the stringy or<BR>adhesive nature of this tree.)<BR>—तन्तु-पर्वन्, अ,<BR>n. ‘the festival of the thread,’ the anniversary of the<BR>day of full moon in the month Śrāvaṇa, when<BR>Kṛṣṇa was invested with the Brāhmanical cord.<BR>—तन्तु-भ, अस्, m. mustard-seed, Sinapis Dicho-<BR>toma, also तन्तुक; a calf.<BR>—तन्तु-मत्, आन्, m.<BR>an epithet of Agni, perhaps ‘uninterrupted like a<BR>thread;’ (ती), f., N. of the mother of Murāri.<BR>—तन्तु-वर्धन, अस्, m. ‘increasing a race,’ a N.<BR>of Viṣṇu; also of Śiva.<BR>—तन्तु-वाद्य, अम्, n. a<BR>stringed musical instrument in general.<BR>—तन्तु-<BR>वान, अम्, n. weaving.<BR>—तन्तु-वाप, अस्, m. a<BR>weaver; a loom; weaving.<BR>—तन्तु-वाय, अस्, m. a<BR>weaver; a spider; weaving; [cf. तन्त्र-वाय.]<BR>—तन्तुवाय-दण्ड, अस्, m. a loom.<BR>—तन्तु-<BR>विग्रहा, f. the banana or plantain, Musa Sapientum.<BR>—तन्तु-शाला, f. a weaver's shop.<BR>—तन्तु-सन्तत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, woven, sewn; (अम्), n. wove cloth.<BR>—तन्तु-सन्तति, इस्, f. or तन्तु-सन्तान, अस्, m.<BR>sewing, weaving.<BR>—तन्तु-सार or तन्तु-सारक, अस्,<BR>m. the areca or betel-nut tree (as having a fibrous<BR>pith).<BR>—तन्त्व्-अग्र, अम्, n. the end of a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुक|तंतुक|तंतुकः|तन्तुकः
तन्तुक, अस्, m. (at the end of an adj. comp.), a<BR>thread, a rope; a kind of serpent; mustard-seed,<BR>Sinapis Dichotoma, = तन्तु-भ; (ई), f. a vein or<BR>any tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुण|तंतुणः|तन्तुणः
तन्तुण, अस्, m. a shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुर|तंतुर|तंतुरं|तन्तुरं
तन्तुर or तन्तुल, अम्, n. the filaments or<BR>fibrous root of a lotus; (अस्), m. = तण्डुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्र|तंत्र|तंत्रं|तन्त्रं
तन्त्र, अम्, n. an implement of weaving, a loom;<BR>a thread; the warp or threads extended lengthwise<BR>in a loom; an uninterrupted series (e. g. देह-तन्त्र,<BR>assuming a series of bodies); posterity; the leading<BR>or principal action of a ceremony, characteristic or<BR>prevalent features, the regular order of ceremonies or<BR>rites, system, framework, ritual; chief or essential part,<BR>main point; principal doctrine, rule, theory; model,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">Page0362-b+ 80</a>]<BR>typical form, science; a scientific work; any scientific<BR>chapter of a work (especially the first section of a<BR>Jyotiḥ-śāstra or treatise on astronomy); a religious<BR>treatise teaching magical and mystical formularies<BR>for the worship of the deities, or the attainment<BR>of superhuman power; it is mostly in the form of<BR>a dialogue between Śiva and Durgā, who are the<BR>peculiar gods of the Tāntrikas, (these works are very<BR>numerous, and their authority, in many parts of<BR>India, seems to have superseded that of the Vedas:<BR>they are said to comprise five subjects, viz. 1. the<BR>creation, 2. the destruction of the world, 3. the<BR>worship of the gods, 4. the attainment of all objects,<BR>especially of six superhuman faculties, 5. the four<BR>modes of union with the supreme spirit by medita-<BR>tion; a variety of subjects are, however, introduced<BR>into many of them, whilst some are limited to a<BR>single topic, as the mode of breathing in certain rites,<BR>the language of birds, beasts, &c.); a cause which<BR>leads to two or more results; the cause of more than<BR>one effect; a medicament, a drug; a chief remedy<BR>or ‘charm’ considered as producing medicinal effects;<BR>a spell; oath or ordeal; raiment, vesture; sup-<BR>porting a family; necessary or indispensable act or<BR>provision; the right way of doing anything; royal<BR>retinue, a court, train; an army; providing for the<BR>security and prosperity of a kingdom; a realm, a<BR>country; subservience, service, dependance; decora-<BR>tion, hanging with trophies, garlands, &c.; heap,<BR>multitude; wealth; a house; happiness, felicity; (अस्),<BR>m. a weaver (?); (तन्त्री, ईस् or ई), f. any string,<BR>cord, or rope; a bow-string; the wire or string of<BR>a lute; (metaphorically) the strings of the heart;<BR>any tubular vessel of the body, a sinew; a tail; the<BR>plant Cocculus Cordifolius [cf. तन्त्रिका and तन्-<BR>त्रक]; a young woman or girl with peculiar quali-<BR>ties; N. of a river.<BR>—तन्त्रेण, ind. in such a way<BR>as to hold good or remain.<BR>—तन्त्र-काष्ठ, अम्,<BR>n. a fibrous stick or brush used by weavers for clean-<BR>ing the threads of the woof; [cf. तन्तु-काष्ठ.]<BR>—तन्त्र-कौमुदी, f., तन्त्र-गन्धर्व, तन्त्र-<BR>गर्भ, तन्त्र-चूडामणि, titles of different Tantra<BR>works.<BR>—तन्त्र-ता, f. or तन्त्र-त्व, अम्, n. ar-<BR>ranging into a system; dependance, subservience;<BR>the quality or character of a Tantra; comprehending<BR>several rites in one, performance of one ceremony,<BR>or penance in lieu of a number.<BR>—तन्त्र-प्रकाश,<BR>अस्, m. title of a literary work.<BR>—तन्त्र-प्रदीप,<BR>अस्, m. title of a commentary on the Dhātu-pāṭha.<BR>—तन्त्र-भेद, title of a Tantra.<BR>—तन्त्र-रत्न,<BR>अम्, n. title of a work by Pārtha-sārathi.<BR>—तन्त्र-<BR>राज, अस्, m. title of a work.<BR>—तन्त्र-वाप, अस्,<BR>m. a weaver; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a loom, weaving;<BR>[cf. the next.]<BR>—तन्त्र-वाय, अस्, m. a weaver; a<BR>spider; [cf. तन्तु-वाय.]<BR>—तन्त्र-वार्त्तिक =<BR>मीमांसा-तन्त्र-वार्त्तिक.<BR>—तन्त्र-सार, अस्, m.<BR>‘the essence of the Tantras,’ title of a compilation.<BR>—तन्त्र-हृदय, अम्, n. title of a Tantra work.<BR>—तन्त्री-मुख, अस्, m. a peculiar position of the<BR>hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रक|तंत्रक|तन्त्रकं|तंत्रकः|तन्त्रकः
तन्त्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, new and unbleached (as<BR>cloth), recently from the loom; (at the end of a<BR>comp.) = तन्त्र; (इका), f. the plant Cocculus Cor-<BR>difolius; [cf. तन्त्री.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रण|तंत्रण|तंत्रणं
तन्त्रण, अम्, n. (fr. तन्त्रय), maintenance of<BR>order, discipline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रय
तन्त्रय (fr. तन्त्र), nom. P. तन्त्रयति, to<BR>perform or go through in order; to maintain by disci-<BR>pline, keep in order; A. तन्त्रयते, to support a<BR>family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रायिन्|तंत्रायिन्
तन्त्रायिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. drawing out a thread;<BR>going continuously (as the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिन्|तंत्रिन्
तन्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having threads, made of threads,<BR>spun, wove; chorded, having chords or wires (as an<BR>instrument); having a Tantra, following one; (ई), m.<BR>a musician; a soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्र|तंद्र
1. तन्द्र, अम्, n., Ved. a series, a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वत्|तन्वन्त्
तन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, stretching, extending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनक
तनक तनक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a re-<BR>ward; (perhaps a wrong reading for वेतनक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनबाल
तनबाल तनबाल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; [cf. तालवन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयित्नु
तनयित्नु तनयित्नु. See 1. तन्, p. 361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनु|तनुः
तनु तनु. See p. 361, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनोनु
तनोनु तनोनु, a kind of rice (= षष्टिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तस्य
तन्तस्य तन्तस्य, nom. P. तन्तस्यति, to<BR>grieve, be distressed; to afflict; [cf. rt. तंस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्ति|तंतिः|तन्तिः
तन्ति तन्ति, तन्तु, तन्त्र, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रा|तंत्रा
तन्त्रा तन्त्रा, f. a wrong form for तन्द्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रि|तंत्रि|तंत्रिः|तन्त्रिः
तन्त्रि तन्त्रि, इस्, f. another form for तन्त्री,<BR>see col. 2; (also a wrong form for तन्द्रि.)<BR>—तन्-<BR>त्रि-पालक, अस्, m. an epithet of Jayad-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिज
तन्त्रिज तन्त्रिज, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kanavaka; (another reading has तन्द्रिज.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रित
तन्त्रित तन्त्रित, तन्त्रि-ता, wrong forms for<BR>तन्द्रित, तन्द्रि-ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिपाल
तन्त्रिपाल तन्त्रिपाल, अस्, m. a N. assumed<BR>by Saha-deva [cf. तन्ति-पाल]; N. of a son of<BR>Kanavaka; (another reading has तन्द्रिपाल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिल्लक
तन्त्रिल्लक तन्त्रिल्लक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्री|तंत्री
तन्त्री तन्त्री. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्वग्र
तन्त्वग्र तन्त्व्-अग्र. See तन्तु, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्
तन्द् तन्द्, cl. 1. A., Ved. तन्दते, &c.,<BR>to relax, give away, become relaxed, to<BR>grow fatigued; (Sāy.) to make languid or fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्र|तंद्र
2. तन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, tired, fatigued; lazy; (आ), f.<BR>lassitude, exhaustion, weariness, syncope; sleepiness,<BR>sluggishness. (For 1. तन्द्र see col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रय
तन्द्रय (fr. the preceding), nom. A. तन्द्र-<BR>यते, to grow fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रयु
तन्द्रयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. fatigued, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्राय
तन्द्राय, another form for तन्द्रय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रालु|तंद्रालु|तन्द्रालुः
तन्द्रालु, उस्, उस्, उ, tired, wearied, sleepy, over-<BR>come with sleep or fatigue, slothful, sluggish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रि|तंद्रि|तंद्रिः|तन्द्रिः
तन्द्रि, इस् (?) and ई, ईस् or ई, m. (?), f. sleepiness,<BR>drowsiness, fatigue, lassitude; fainting, exhaustion.<BR>—तन्द्रि-ज or तन्द्रि-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Kanavaka; [cf. तन्त्रि-पाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिका|तंद्रिका
तन्द्रिका, f. sloth, sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रित|तंद्रित
तन्द्रित, only in अ-तन्द्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, indefa-<BR>tigable, unremitting; [cf. अ-तन्द and तन्त्रित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिन्|तंद्रिन्
तन्द्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, weary, lazy.<BR>—तन्द्रि-ता, f.<BR>lassitude, exhaustion, weariness, sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्र्
तन्द्र् तन्द्र् (a Sautra root), to be dis-<BR>turbed in mind, become bewildered, be<BR>exhausted or fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्र|तंद्र
तन्द्र 1. and 2. तन्द्र. See above and col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रवाय|तन्द्रवायः
तन्द्रवाय तन्द्रवाय, a wrong form for<BR>तन्त्र-वाय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्नी
तन्नी तन्नी, f. or तन्नि, इस् (?), f. the plant<BR>Hemionitis Cordifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मय
तन्मय तन्-मय. See p. 361, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्र|तन्मात्रं
तन्मात्र तन्-मात्र. See p. 361, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्यता
तन्यता तन्यता, f., Ved. or तन्यतु, उस्, m.,<BR>Ved. (fr. rt. 1. तन्), roaring, thundering, thunder;<BR>wind; night; a musical instrument (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्यु
तन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. making a roaring sound,<BR>epithet of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्लीक
तन्लीक तन्लीक (?), an areca seller, a desig-<BR>nation of one of the inferior castes of Hindūs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्व
तन्व तन्व, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf.<BR>तान्व.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वङ्ग|तन्वंग
तन्वङ्ग तन्व्-अङ्ग. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वत्|तन्वन्त्
तन्वत् तन्वत्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्विन्
तन्विन् तन्विन्, ई, m., N. of a son of Manu<BR>Tāmasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0362-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
तप् 1. तप् [cf. 2. पत्], cl. 4. A. तप्यते,<BR>&c., to rule, govern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
तप् 2. तप्, cl. 1. P. (rarely A.) तपति,<BR>-ते, तताप, तप्स्यति (ep. also तपिष्यति),<BR>अताप्सीत्, तप्तुम्, to give out heat, be hot; to<BR>shine; to heat, make hot or warm; to shine upon;<BR>to be burnt; to burn, to consume or destroy by<BR>heat; to suffer pain; to cause pain or distress; to<BR>injure, hurt, damage, spoil; to torment one's self,<BR>mortify the body, undergo penance, (often with<BR>तपस्, e. g. तपस् तताप, he performed penance);<BR>cl. 4. P. तप्यति (rarely used), to warm one's self,<BR>become hot: Pass. तप्यते, to be heated, to suffer<BR>or feel pain; to be injured or hurt; to suffer pain<BR>voluntarily, undergo severe penances, (often with<BR>तपस्, e. g. तपस् तप्यामहे, we undergo penance);<BR>Caus. P. A. तापयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to make warm<BR>or hot; to burn, consume by heat, cause pain,<BR>trouble, distress; to torment one's self, undergo<BR>penance: Desid. तितप्सति, -ते: Intens. तातप्यते,<BR>तातप्ति, to feel violent pain, suffer torment, be in<BR>great anxiety or distress; [cf. Lat. tepeo: Gr. τέφρα,<BR>rt. ταφ, θάπτω: Russ. tepl, ‘warm;’ teplota,<BR>‘warmth:’ Hib. tebhot, ‘intense heat:’ Old Germ.<BR>damf: Lat. tempus ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
3. तप्, प्, प्, प्, warming one's self; [cf. अग्नि-तप्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप, अस्, आ, अम्, warming; burning, consuming<BR>by heat [cf. ललाटन्-तप]; causing pain or trouble,<BR>distressing [cf. जनन्-तप and परन्-तप]; (अस्),<BR>m. heat, warmth, fire [cf. आ-तप]; the sun; the<BR>hot season; religious austerity, penance, mortifica-<BR>tion (= तपस्); a peculiar form of fire which<BR>generated the seven mothers of Skanda; N. of one<BR>of the attendants of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of one of the<BR>eight deities of the Bodhi-druma; [cf. अ-तप and<BR>ताप.]<BR>—तप-रुज्, क्, f. the pain of penance.<BR>—त-<BR>पात्मक (˚प-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, practising austeri-<BR>ties.<BR>—तपात्यय (˚प-अत्˚), अस्, m. the end of the<BR>heat, the beginning of the rainy season.<BR>—तपान्त<BR>(˚प-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of the heat, the beginning<BR>of the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपत्|तपन्त्
तपत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, heating or warming; per-<BR>forming penance &c.<BR>—तपताम्-पति, इस्, m. ‘the<BR>chief of burners,’ the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपती
तपती, f. ‘the warming one,’ N. of a daughter<BR>of the Sun and of his wife Chāyā, married to Saṃ-<BR>varaṇa and mother of Kuru; N. of a river, commonly<BR>called Taptī; [cf. तापत्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन|तपनः
तपन, अस्, आ, अम्, warming, burning, shining,<BR>an epithet of the sun; causing pain or distress; (अस्),<BR>m. the sun; N. of a divine being (perhaps the sun)<BR>who fights with Garuḍa; N. of one of the five fires in<BR>the Svāhā-kāra; N. of a Rakṣas; a N. of Agastya;<BR>heat, burning, the hot season; N. of a burning hell;<BR>N. of several plants, viz. Semecarpus Anacardium<BR>[cf. अरुष्-कर]; Calotropis Gigantea (अर्क), the<BR>white variety of it; Premna Spinosa (क्षु-<BR>द्राग्नि-मन्थ); Cassia Senna; the sun-stone [cf.<BR>सूर्य-कान्त, तपन-मणि, तपनोपल]; (ई), f.<BR>heat; the root of Bignonia Suaveolens; N. of a<BR>river, = तापी and तपनात्मजा, according to some<BR>authorities = गोदावरी; (अम्), n. the being hot,<BR>burning; pining, grieving, mental distress; [cf. राम-<BR>तपन, ‘the distress of Rāma,’ N. of an Upaniṣad;<BR>त्रिपुरा-त्˚, गोपाल-त्˚; cf. also तापन.]<BR>—तपन-<BR>कर, अस्, m. a ray, a sunbeam.<BR>—तपन-च्छद,<BR>अस्, m. the sunflower, = आदित्य-पत्त्र.<BR>—तपन-<BR>तनय, अस्, m. ‘the son of the Sun,’ a N. of Karṇa;<BR>(आ), f. ‘the daughter of the Sun,’ the Yamunā river;<BR>the Taptī river [cf. तपनात्मजा]; N. of a tree;<BR>[cf. शमी.]<BR>—तपन-मणि, इस्, m. the sun-stone;<BR>[cf. सूर्य-कान्त.]<BR>—तपनांशु (˚न-अं˚), उस्,<BR>m. a ray of the sun, a sunbeam.<BR>—तपनात्मजा<BR>(˚न-आत्म-जा), f. ‘the daughter of the Sun,’ N. of a<BR>river, = तपनी and तापी, according to some authori-<BR>ties = गोदावरी [cf. तपनी and तपन], and<BR>यमुना.<BR>—तपनेष्ट (˚न-इष्˚), अम्, n. copper<BR>(‘loved by the rays of the sun,’ i. e. easily heated or<BR>coloured by them).<BR>—तपनोपल (˚न-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the sun-stone; [cf. सूर्य-कान्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीय|तपनीयं
तपनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be heated; to be suffered<BR>or practised as penance; (अम्), n. gold purified with<BR>fire, gold in general; a sort of rice.<BR>—तपनीय-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of purified gold, golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीयक|तपनीयकं
तपनीयक, अम्, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन्तक
तपन्तक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्
तपस्, अस्, n. warmth, heat, fire, (पञ्च तपांसि,<BR>the five fires to which an ascetic is exposed in the<BR>hot season, viz. four fires lighted in the several<BR>quarters and the sun burning from above); pain,<BR>suffering; religious austerity, penance, mortification,<BR>the practice of mental or personal self-denial or the<BR>infliction of bodily tortures; the meditation connected<BR>with such a practice; moral virtue, merit; special<BR>observance or duty of any particular caste (e. g. the<BR>Tapas of a Brāhman is sacred learning; of a Kṣa-<BR>triya, the protection of subjects; of a Vaiśya, giving<BR>alms to Brāhmans; of a Śūdra, service; and of a<BR>Ṛṣi or saint, feeding upon herbs and roots); a<BR>particular month of the cold season intervening<BR>between winter and spring (= Māgha or January-<BR>February, the month of religious austerities; cf. त-<BR>पस्य); one of the seven worlds, the region above<BR>the Jana-loka, inhabited by saints or devotees after<BR>death [cf. तपो-लोक]; (in astrology) the ninth lunar<BR>mansion, = धर्म; N. of a long period of time, a<BR>Kalpa; (आस्, अस्), m. n. the cold or dewy season (=<BR>शिशिर); the winter (= हिमर्तु); the hot season.<BR>—तपः-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, undergoing religious<BR>austerities or penance &c.; (अस्), m. a kind of fish,<BR>Polynemus Risua or Paradiseus, (this fish is also<BR>called Tapasyā-matsya); [cf. तपस्-विन्.]<BR>—तपः-<BR>कृश, अस्, आ, अम् emaciated by austerities.<BR>—तपः-<BR>क्लेश-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, patient of austerities, enduring<BR>the pain of penance.<BR>—तपः-प्रभाव, अस्, m. the<BR>efficacy of devotion.<BR>—तपः-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>clined to religious austerities.<BR>—तपः-समाधि, इस्,<BR>m. the practice of penance.<BR>—तपः-साध्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be accomplished by penance.<BR>—तपः-सिद्ध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished by penance.<BR>—तपः-स्थली,<BR>f. ‘the seat of religious austerity or piety,’ a N. of<BR>Benares.<BR>—तपश्-चरण, अम्, n. or तपश्-चर्या,<BR>f. the practice of penance.<BR>—तपश्-चित्, त्, त्, त्, accu-<BR>mulating religious merit by austerities; (तस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a class of deities; तपश्चिताम् अयनम्, N.<BR>of a religious ceremony which lasts several days.<BR>—तपसो-मूर्ति, इस्, m., N. of one of the seven<BR>sages in the twelfth Manv-antara; [cf. तपो-मूर्ति.]<BR>—तपस्-तक्ष, अस्, m. ‘destroying religious<BR>penance,’ an epithet of Indra as disturbing the<BR>austerities of ascetics lest they should acquire too<BR>great power; (other authorities explain the word<BR>‘emaciating himself by his devotions;’ and others<BR>read तपस्-तङ्क, ‘afraid of austerities’ or ‘the axe<BR>of austerities.’)<BR>—तपस्-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>place of pilgrimage.<BR>—तपस्-पति, इस्, m. the lord<BR>of penance.<BR>—तपस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. burning,<BR>hot; ascetic, devout; [cf. तपो-वत्.]<BR>—तपस्वि-ता,<BR>f. devout austerity, religious penance, bodily morifica-<BR>tion.<BR>—तपस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, distressed, wretched,<BR>poor, miserable, pitiable; practising austerities, de-<BR>vout; a mendicant, a pauper; an ascetic, a religious<BR>man engaged in the practice of rigorous and devout<BR>penance; (ई), m., N. of a son of Manu Cākṣuṣa<BR>and Naḍvalā; N. of one of the seven sages of the<BR>twelfth Manv-antara; an epithet of Nārada; the<BR>mango fish, Polynemus Risua [cf. तपः-कर]; N.<BR>of a tree, a kind of Karañja (घृत-करञ्ज);<BR>(इनी), f. a female devotee, a woman leading a re-<BR>ligious life; a poor wretched woman; spikenard,<BR>Valeriana Jaṭāmānsi; another plant, Helleborus Niger,<BR>= कटु-रोहिणी; also = महा-श्रावणिका.<BR>—तप-<BR>स्वि-पत्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a plant, = दमनक; [cf.<BR>तपो-धन.]<BR>—तपो-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. born from<BR>heat; one who practises religious austerities.<BR>—तपो-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, granting piety; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha in Magadha.<BR>—तपो-दान, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—तपो-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, rich in religious<BR>penance; ascetic, pious; a very treasure of mortifica-<BR>tions and austerities, a devotee, an ascetic, performing<BR>religious penance; consisting in religious penance;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">Page0363-c+ 81</a>]<BR>granting religious merit or piety; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>son of Manu Tāmasa; N. of a plant, = दमनक,<BR>commonly दवणा, Artemisia [cf. तपस्वि-पत्त्र];<BR>(आ), f. the plant Sphæranthus Mollis, = मुण्डीरी,<BR>commonly मुण्डी.<BR>—तपो-धर्म, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a son of the thirteenth Manu.<BR>—तपो-धामन्, अ,<BR>n. ‘the abode of penance,’ N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—तपो-धृति, इस्, m., N. of one of the seven sages<BR>of the twelfth Manv-antara.<BR>—तपो-नित्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>devoting one's self uninterruptedly to religious auste-<BR>rities or penance; (अस्), m., N. of a man with the<BR>patronymic Pauruśiṣṭi.<BR>—तपो-निधि, इस्, m. a<BR>treasury of religious austerities and penance, a very<BR>treasure of merit derived from self-mortification, an<BR>eminently pious man.<BR>—तपो-निष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>performing penance, practising austerities.<BR>—तपो-<BR>ऽनुभाव (˚पस्-अन्˚), अस्, m. the influence of re-<BR>ligious penance.<BR>—तपो-बल, अम्, n. the power<BR>acquired by religious austerities.<BR>—तपो-भङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. interruption of religious penance.<BR>—तपो-<BR>भृत्, त्, त्, त्, undergoing penance, ascetic, pious; an<BR>ascetic, a pious man.<BR>—तपो-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting in religious penance, containing it; practising<BR>austerities, devout.<BR>—तपो-मूर्ति, इस्, f. an incarna-<BR>tion of religious austerity or penance; an ascetic;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of one of the seven sages of the twelfth<BR>Manv-antara; [cf. तपसो-मूर्ति.]<BR>—तपो-मूल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, founded on religious austerity or penance;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Manu Tāmasa.<BR>—तपो-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, employed in penitential exercises,<BR>ascetic, pious.<BR>—तपो-रति, इस्, इस्, इ, rejoicing in re-<BR>ligious austerity; (इस्), m., N. of a son of Manu<BR>Tāmasa.<BR>—तपो-रवि, इस्, m. ‘the sun of the ascetics,’<BR>N. of one of the seven sages in the twelfth Manv-<BR>antara.<BR>—तपो-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of penance,’ the<BR>moon.<BR>—तपो-राशि, इस्, m. ‘a heap of religious<BR>austerities;’ an ascetic.<BR>—तपो-लोक, अस्, m. one of<BR>the seven worlds, that which is situated above the<BR>Jana-loka; [cf. तपस्.]<BR>—तपो-वट, अस्, m. ‘en-<BR>closure or district of religious penance,’ a N. applied<BR>to Brahmāvarta, i. e. the holy land situated in central<BR>India.<BR>—तपो-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, ascetic, pious; [cf.<BR>तपस्-वत्.]<BR>—तपो-वन, अस्, m. ‘penance-grove,’<BR>a sacred grove in which ascetics perform their re-<BR>ligious austerities.<BR>—तपो-वास, अस्, m. a place of<BR>religious austerity.<BR>—तपो-विशेष, अस्, m. excellence<BR>of devotion.<BR>—तपो-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, rich in<BR>religious austerity or penance, very ascetic or pious.<BR>—तपो-व्रात, अस्, m. a multitude of penances.<BR>—तपो-ऽशन (˚पस्-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>food is religious austerity; (अस्), m., N. of one of<BR>the seven sages of the twelfth Manv-antara; also of<BR>a son of Manu Tāmasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपसीवन्
तपसीवन्, आ, अरी, अ, causing pain (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
1. तपस्य, nom. P. तपस्यति, to undergo reli-<BR>gious austerities, do penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
2. तपस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by heat; (अस्),<BR>m. the month Phālguna (February-March), the<BR>second month of the season intervening between<BR>winter and spring; a N. of Arjuna; N. of a son of<BR>Manu Tāmasa; (आ), f. devout austerity, religious<BR>penance; (अम्), n. devout austerity, mortification,<BR>religious penance; the flower of Jasminum Multi-<BR>florum or Pubescens (कुन्द-पुष्प).<BR>—तपस्या-<BR>मत्स्य, the mango fish; [cf. under तपः-कर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपित|तपितं
तपित, अस्, आ, अम्, heated, burnt, refined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपिष्ठ
तपिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 2. तप् with the superl.<BR>affix), Ved. extremely hot, burning; [cf. तपीयस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपिष्णु
तपिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, warming, heating, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपीयस्
तपीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (fr. 2. तप् with the compar.<BR>affix), extremely ascetic, most devoted to religious<BR>austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपु|तपुः
तपु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. burning hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुषि
तपुषि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुषी
तपुषी, f. the heat of anger or wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुस्
तपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, Ved. burning hot; (उस्), m.<BR>fire; the sun; an enemy (who causes pain); (उस्),<BR>n. heat, pain.<BR>—तपुर्-अग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>a burning point or extremity (as a spear).<BR>—तपुर्-<BR>जम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having burning jaws, an<BR>epithet of Agni.<BR>—तपुर्-मूर्धन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">Page0364-a+ 78</a>]<BR>having a burning head, an epithet of Agni; (आ), m.,<BR>N. of an author of a hymn of the Ṛg-veda who was<BR>a son of Bṛhaspati.<BR>—तपुर्-वध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having burning weapons.<BR>—तपुष्-पा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. (Sāy.) protecting from pain; (perhaps<BR>rather) drinking warm (beverages).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0363-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त|तप्तः
तप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, heated, inflamed, burnt; hot;<BR>red-hot; fused, melted, molten; burnished; scorched<BR>by pain or sorrow, distressed, afflicted; inflamed with<BR>anger, incensed; undergone or performed (as penance).<BR>—तप्त-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a heated or red-hot jar;<BR>N. of a particular hell; (अस्, आ, अम्), having hot jars.<BR>—तप्त-कूप, ‘hot-well,’ N. of a hell; (perhaps a<BR>wrong reading for the preceding.)<BR>—तप्त-कृच्छ्र,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. a sort of penance which consists in<BR>drinking hot water, milk, and ghee for three days<BR>each, and inhaling hot air for three days.<BR>—तप्त-<BR>तपस्, आस्, m. one who has performed penance, an<BR>ascetic.<BR>—तप्त-पाषाण-कुण्ड, अम्, n. ‘a pit<BR>filled with burning stones,’ N. of a hell.<BR>—तप्त-<BR>बालुक, अस्, आ, अम्, having hot or burning gravel;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a hell.<BR>—तप्त-रूप or तप्त-<BR>रूपक, अम्, n. silver.<BR>—तप्त-लोमश, green<BR>vitriol.<BR>—तप्त-लोह, अम्, n. ‘glowing iron,’ N. of<BR>a hell.<BR>—तप्त-शूर्मि or तप्त-सूर्मि, इस्, f. ‘a red-<BR>hot iron statue,’ N. of a hell in which the wicked are<BR>made to embrace red-hot images.<BR>—तप्तशूर्मि-<BR>कुण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a hell.<BR>—तप्त-सुरा-कुण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. ‘a jar or hole filled with burning spirituous<BR>liquor,’ N. of a hell.<BR>—तप्त-हेम-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>like or consisting of melted gold.<BR>—तप्तान्न (˚त-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. hot food, hot rice.<BR>—तप्तायन (˚त-<BR>अय्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. serving as a dwelling-place for<BR>the distressed (as the earth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तव्य
तप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be performed as a reli-<BR>gious penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तृ
तप्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, making warm or hot, heating,<BR>a heater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त्वा
तप्त्वा, ind. having heated, having performed<BR>penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्य
तप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, performing religious austerity,<BR>doing penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्यति
तप्यति, इस्, f., Ved. heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्यतु
तप्यतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. hot, glowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्स्यत्
तप्स्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, practising or intend-<BR>ing to practise austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपश
तपश तपश, अस्, m. the moon; [cf. the<BR>following.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस|तपसः
तपस तपस, अस्, m. (said to be fr. 2. तप्),<BR>the moon; a bird; [cf. the preceding.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तबलाकृति
तबलाकृति तबलाकृति, इस्, f. (fr. तबल?<BR>and आकृति), N. of a kind of creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्
तम् तम्, cl. 4. P. (rarely A.) ताम्यति,<BR>ताम्यते, तताम, तमितुम्, to gasp for<BR>breath (as one suffocating), choke, be suffocated,<BR>breathe with difficulty; to faint away; to be exhausted,<BR>perish; to be distressed in body or mind; to be<BR>disturbed or perplexed; to stop, become immovable<BR>or stiff; to wish, desire: Caus. तमयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to suffocate, deprive of breath; [cf. Lat. temere,<BR>tabeo (?); Old Germ. damf; Russ. tomlju.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
1. तम, अस्, m. darkness &c., = तमस् in its<BR>various meanings; also = तमाल; (आ), f. night, =<BR>तमाल, Phyllanthus Emblica; (अम्), n. darkness,<BR>gloom; the point of the foot.<BR>—तमाह्वय (˚म-<BR>आह्˚), a kind of plant, = तालीश-पत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमक|तमकः
तमक, अस्, m. oppression (of the chest), a kind<BR>of asthma; [cf. प्र-तमक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमका
तमका, f. = तमा, तमालका, ˚की, तमाली, त-<BR>मालिनी, Phyllanthus Emblica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमत|तमतः
तमत, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous, cupidinous, longing<BR>or hankering after; wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमन|तमनं
तमन, अम्, n. the becoming breathless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस्, अस्, n. darkness, gloom; the darkness of<BR>hell, hell itself or a peculiar division of hell; the<BR>obscuration of the sun or moon in eclipses, darkness<BR>personified as Rāhu or the ascending node; mental<BR>darkness, illusion, error (constituting one of the five<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-b" target="_blank">Page0364-b+ 81</a>]<BR>forms of अ-विद्या in the Sāṅkhya phil.), sin, sorrow;<BR>(in the Sāṅkhya phil.) darkness or ignorance as one<BR>of the three qualities or constituents of everything in<BR>creation, the other two being सत्त्व and रजस्, see<BR>गुण; as an inherent quality of nature तमस् is<BR>heavy and obstructive, and predominates in earth<BR>and water, whence they fall and tend downwards;<BR>in living beings it is the cause of ignorance, illusion,<BR>lust, anger, pride, sorrow, dulness, and stolidity;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a descendant of Gṛtsa-mada, a son<BR>of Śravas and father of Pra-kāśa; N. of a son of<BR>Pṛthu-śravas and father of Uśanas; [cf. Lith. tamsa,<BR>‘darkness;’ tamsus, ‘obscure:’ Russ. temnyi, ‘dark;’<BR>temno-ta, ‘darkness:’ Hib. teim, ‘dark, obscure;’<BR>teimhen, ‘darkness;’ teimheal, ‘an eclipse, dark-<BR>ness:’ Old Germ. demar: Old Sax. thim: Angl.<BR>Sax. dim: Lat. tenebrœ?].<BR>—तमः-प्रभा or<BR>तम-प्रभा, f., or तम-प्रभ or तमः-<BR>प्रभ, अस्, m. a hell, one of the lowermost di-<BR>visions of the infernal regions.<BR>—तमः-प्रवेश,<BR>अस्, m. groping in the dark; mental perplexity or<BR>aberration.<BR>—तमः-स्थित, अम्, n. ‘situated in<BR>darkness,’ N. of a hell, one of the lowest divisions<BR>of hell.<BR>—तमसा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, or तमस्-<BR>कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, like darkness, black, gloomy.<BR>—तमस्-काण्ड, अस्, m. or तमस्-तति, इस्, f. great<BR>or spreading darkness.<BR>—तमस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, hav-<BR>ing darkness, dark, gloomy; (ती), f. night.<BR>—तमस्-<BR>विन्, ई, इनी, इ, dark, gloomy; (नी), f. night; turmeric.<BR>—तमो-गा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. roaming in the dark-<BR>ness, concealing himself in darkness, an epithet of<BR>Śuṣṇa.<BR>—तमो-गु, उस्, m. an epithet of Rāhu, the<BR>personified ascending node, the causer of darkness.<BR>—तमो-गुण, अस्, m. the quality of darkness or<BR>ignorance; see above under तमस्.<BR>—तमोगुणिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, having the quality of तमस् predominant<BR>in the temperament, irascible, ignorant, proud, &c.<BR>—तमो-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying darkness;<BR>(अस्), m. the sun; the moon; fire; an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; an epithet of Śiva; a Buddha.<BR>—तमो-<BR>ज्योतिस्, इस्, m. ‘light in darkness,’ a fire-fly.<BR>—तमो-<BR>दर्शन, bilious fever.<BR>—तमो-नुद्, त्, त्, त्, dis-<BR>persing darkness; (त्), m. a shining body; the sun;<BR>the moon; fire; a lamp; light.<BR>—तमो-नुद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dispersing darkness; (अस्), m. the sun; the moon.<BR>—तमो-ऽन्तकृत् (˚मस्-अन्˚), त्, त्, त्, making an end<BR>of darkness; (त्), m., N. of one of the attendants<BR>of Skanda.<BR>—तमो-ऽन्त्य (˚मस्-अन्˚), अस्, m. one<BR>of the ten ways in which an eclipse may happen.<BR>—तमो-ऽपह (˚मस्-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, removing<BR>darkness physical or moral, illumining, enlightening;<BR>(अस्), m. the sun; the moon; fire; a Buddha.<BR>—तमो-भिद्, त्, त्, त्, dispersing darkness; (त्), m.<BR>a fire-fly.<BR>—तमो-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘become dark-<BR>ness,’ dark, covered with darkness; ignorant.<BR>—त-<BR>मो-मणि, इस्, m. ‘the jewel of darkness,’ a kind of<BR>gem; a fire-fly.<BR>—तमो-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>or composed of darkness, derived from it, covered<BR>with it; (अस्), m. the mind enveloped with darkness,<BR>vexation, anger, one of the five forms of अ-विद्या in<BR>the Sāṅkhya phil.<BR>—तमो-ऽरि (˚मस्-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>the enemy of darkness, the sun.<BR>—तमो-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, dark, gloomy; [cf. तमस्-वत्.]<BR>—तमो-<BR>विकार, अस्, m. disease, sickness, (as a modification<BR>of the Guṇa तमस्.)<BR>—तमो-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>obscured, clouded; overcome with or influenced by<BR>rage, fear, &c., or any of the effects of the property<BR>of darkness.<BR>—तमो-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. rejoicing or<BR>delighting in darkness; (Sāy.) growing in the dark-<BR>ness, increasing by the darkness.<BR>—तमो-हन्, आ,<BR>-घ्नी, अ, Ved. striking down or dispersing darkness.<BR>—तमो-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, removing darkness, illu-<BR>minating; (अस्), m. the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस|तमसं|तमसः
तमस, अस्, ई, अम्, dark-coloured; (अस्), m.<BR>darkness; a well; (आ), f., N. of a river, the Tamasā<BR>or Tonse, falling into the Ganges below Pratiṣṭhāna;<BR>(अम्), n. darkness (at end of comp., cf. अन्ध-त्˚,<BR>अव-त्˚, वि-त्˚, सन्-त्˚); a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्क
तमस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of an adj. comp.<BR>= तमस्; [cf. निस्-तमस्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाल|तमालं|तमालः
तमाल, अस्, m., N. of a tree with a very dark bark<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">Page0364-c+ 68</a>]<BR>(but white blossoms), Xanthochymus Pictorius; N.<BR>of various other plants, = वरुण and कृष्ण-ख-<BR>दिर; (अस्), m. the sectarial mark made with sandal<BR>(or perhaps the juice of the Tamāla fruit) upon the<BR>forehead; a sword, a scymitar or large sacrificial<BR>knife; (ई), f., N. of several plants, = ताम्र-वल्ली;<BR>Phyllanthus Emblica; also = वरुण; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. the bark of the bamboo; (अम्), n. the leaf of<BR>the Laurus Cassia, = पत्त्रक = तमाल-पत्त्र.<BR>—तमाल-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the leaf of the Xantho-<BR>chymus Pictorius; the leaf of the Laurus Cassia, Mala-<BR>bathron; a sectarial mark on the forehead; the tree<BR>Xanthochymus Pictorius.<BR>—तमालपत्त्र-चन्द-<BR>न-गन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालक|तमालकं|तमालकः
तमालक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the tree Xanthochymus<BR>Pictorius; the bark of a bamboo; (इका), f., N. of two<BR>plants, = ताम्र-वल्ली and भूम्य्-आमली, Phyllanthus<BR>Emblica; N. of a place, = ताम-लिप्त [cf. तमालिनी];<BR>N. of a woman; (अम्), n. the leaf of the Laurus<BR>Cassia; a sort of pot-herb, Marsilea Dentata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालिनी
तमालिनी, f. a place overgrown with Tamāla trees;<BR>N. of a country, = ताम-लिप्त; N. of a plant, =<BR>भूम्य्-आमली, Phyllanthus Emblica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र, अम्, n. darkness, a dark night; darkness<BR>of mind, illusion; anger, wrath; (आ), f. a dark night,<BR>or one during the wane of the moon; great or ex-<BR>tensive darkness, the night of new moon, any night;<BR>(अस्), m. the dark half of the month, from the full<BR>to the change; [cf. सु-तमिस्र, तामिस्र, तमि-<BR>षीचि.]<BR>—तमिस्र-पक्ष, अस्, m. the fortnight of<BR>the moon's wane, the time from full moon to new<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम 2. तम (for 1. see under rt. तम्, col. 1),<BR>a Taddhita affix, the termination of the superlative<BR>degree, used also as an independent word in the<BR>sense of इष्ट-तम, most desired, and sometimes<BR>added adverbially in the form तमाम्; [cf. तार-<BR>तम्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमङ्ग|तमंगः|तमङ्गः
तमङ्ग तमङ्ग, अस्, m. a platform, stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमङ्गक|तमंगकः|तमङ्गकः
तमङ्गक, अस्, m. the flat and projecting roof<BR>of a house, a sort of balcony or terrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमर|तमरं
तमर तमर, अम्, n. tin; lead (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमराज|तमराजः
तमराज तमराज, अस्, m. a kind of sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाल|तमालं|तमालः
तमाल तमाल. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाह्वय
तमाह्वय तमाह्वय. See 1. तम, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमि|तमिः
तमि तमि, इस्, or तमी, f. the night; tur-<BR>meric; [cf. 1. तम and तमस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिषीचि
तमिषीचि तमिषीचि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. तम् ?),<BR>Ved. oppressing, stunning, afflicting, confusing, dis-<BR>turbing; (Sāy.) powerful, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र तमिस्र. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमुष्टुहीय
तमुष्टुहीय तमुष्टुहीय, अस्, आ, अम्, N. of a<BR>Sūkta beginning with the words तम् उ ष्टुहि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोलिप्ती
तमोलिप्ती तमोलिप्ती, f., N. of a country,<BR>the district of Tumlook in Bengal, = ताम-लिप्त,<BR>commonly called तमोलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्पा
तम्पा तम्पा, f. a cow; [cf. तम्बा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्ब्
तम्ब् तम्ब्, cl. 1. P. तम्बति, &c., to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्बा|तंबा
तम्बा तम्बा, f. a cow; [cf. तम्पा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्बीर
तम्बीर तम्बीर or तम्वीर, in astrology<BR>تمْوير the fourteenth Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्र
तम्र तम्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तम्), Ved.<BR>oppressing, darkening; (Sāy.) causing to languish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय्
तय् तय्, cl. 1. A. तयते, तेये, तयितुम्,<BR>to go, move; to guard, preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय|तयः
तय, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what protects; (अस्), m.<BR>protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर 1. तर, a Taddhita affix, the termina-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">Page0365-a+ 80</a>]<BR>tion of the comparative degree, sometimes added ad-<BR>verbially in the form तराम्; [cf. कष्ट-तर, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर 2. तर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. तॄ), who or<BR>what passes over or beyond, crossing; surpassing;<BR>conquering, overpowering; excelling; to be crossed,<BR>to be overcome [cf. दुस्-तर and दुष्-टर]; (अस्),<BR>m. passing over, crossing, passage; freight; a road (?);<BR>a ferry-boat, raft (?); a tree (?); a sort of magical spell<BR>against the evil spirits supposed to possess certain wea-<BR>pons; N. of a man; (for तरी see तरि next col.)<BR>—तर-पण्य, अम्, n. ferriage, freight, the price<BR>or fare paid at a ferry.<BR>—तर-पण्यिक, अस्, m. one<BR>who receives the ferriage or freight.<BR>—तर-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. a landing-place, a wharf or stairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरंगः|तरङ्गः
1. तरङ्ग, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. तरम् + ग), a<BR>wave; a name given to sections of certain literary<BR>works (especially when the title contains such a word<BR>as ‘sea,’ ‘river,’ &c., e. g. of the Kathā-sarit-sāgara<BR>and Rāja-taraṅgiṇī); a jumping motion, a leap, a<BR>jump, the gallop of a horse, waving, moving to and<BR>fro; cloth or clothes; [cf. उत्-तरङ्ग and चर्म-<BR>तरङ्ग.]<BR>—तरङ्ग-भीरु, उस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of the fourteenth Manu.<BR>—तरङ्गापत्रस्त (˚ग-<BR>अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, a little afraid of waves (Pāṇ. II. 1, 38).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरंगः|तरङ्गः
2. तरङ्ग, nom. P. तरङ्गति, -गितुम्, to move<BR>like a billow, wave, move to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गक|तरंगक
तरङ्गक, अस्, m. a wave; [cf. नारी-तरङ्गक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गित|तरंगित
तरङ्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, wavy, billowy, tossing with<BR>waves; overflowing; (अम्), n. waving, moving to<BR>and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गिन्|तरंगिन्
तरङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, wavy, moving like a billow,<BR>moving restlessly^1 to and fro, unsteady; (इणी), f. a<BR>river; (sometimes at the end of the title of a literary<BR>work, e. g. क्षीर-तरङ्गिणी, राज-त्˚.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण|तरणं|तरणः
तरण, अस्, m. a raft, a boat; Svarga or paradise<BR>(the final landing-place); (अम्), n. crossing over,<BR>passing, going across, carrying over, transporting;<BR>conquering, overcoming; an oar; (for तरणी see<BR>under तरणि below; cf. also सु-तरण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणि|तरणिः
तरणि, इस्, इस् or ई, इ, Ved. passing through, per-<BR>vading (space &c., said of the sun); moving forwards,<BR>quick, untired, energetic; bringing or carrying over,<BR>saving, helping, benevolent; (इस्), m. the sun; the<BR>plant Calotropis Gigantea [cf. अर्क]; a ray of light;<BR>(इस् or ई), f. a float, a raft, a boat, ferry-boat; the<BR>plant Aloe Perfoliata or Hibiscus Mutabilis; (accord-<BR>ing to others = तरणी-वल्ली), a kind of rose, Rosa<BR>Glandulifera; [cf. गो-तरणि.]<BR>—तरणि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. quickness, eagerness, zeal.<BR>—तरणि-धन्य,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—तरणि-पेटक, अस्, m.<BR>an oval bowl or bason of wood for baling a boat.<BR>—तरणि-रत्न, अम्, n. a ruby (‘a sun-jewel’).<BR>—तरणी-वल्ली, f. a kind of rose, Rosa Glandu-<BR>lifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणीय
तरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be crossed or passed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्ड|तरंड|तरंडं|तरंडः|तरण्डः
तरण्ड, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, m. f. n. a boat, a vessel;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a raft or float made of bamboos &c.<BR>tied together and sometimes floated upon jars or<BR>hollow gourds inverted; the float of a fishing line;<BR>an oar; (अस्), m., N. of a country; [cf. the following.]<BR>—तरण्ड-पादा, f. a boat, a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्डक
तरण्डक, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्य
तरण्य (fr. तरण), nom. P. तरण्यति, &c.,<BR>to cross over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्
तरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, crossing, passing over.<BR>—त-<BR>रद्-द्वेषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. conquering or over-<BR>powering enemies, an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्समन्दीय
तरत्समन्दीय, अम्, n., scil. सूक्तम्, the Sūkta<BR>beginning with the words तरत् स मन्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरद्
तरद्, त्, f. a raft, a float; a kind of duck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरन्त|तरंत|तरंतः|तरन्तः
तरन्त, अस्, m. the ocean; a hard shower, a<BR>torrent of rain; a frog; N. of a man with the patro-<BR>nymic Vaidadaśvi; (ई), f. a boat, ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरन्तुक
तरन्तुक, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha; [cf. त-<BR>रण्डक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरल|तरलः
तरल, अस्, आ, अम्, moving to and fro, trembling,<BR>tremulous; fickle, splendid, glittering, sparkling, lu-<BR>minous; unsteady, vain; liquid, liquefied; libidinous,<BR>lecherous, wanton; hollow; (अस्), m. the central<BR>gem of a necklace; a necklace; iron; a level sur-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">Page0365-b+ 81</a>]<BR>face (= तल); bottom, depth, lower or under part;<BR>the thorn-apple; N. of a poet; (आ), f. rice-gruel;<BR>wine, vinous or spirituous liquor; a bee; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a race.<BR>—तरल-ता, f. or तरल-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. tremulousness, unsteadiness, sprightliness.<BR>—तरल-नयनी, f. a woman having tremulous or<BR>rolling eyes; N. of a metre consisting of four lines of<BR>twelve short syllables each.<BR>—तरल-लेखा, f., N. of<BR>a woman.<BR>—तरल-लोचना, f. a woman with tremu-<BR>lous eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलय
तरलय, nom. P. तरलयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to tremble, impart a tremulous motion; to wave,<BR>flutter, move to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलाय
तरलाय, nom. A. तरलायते, &c., to tremble,<BR>move to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलायित|तरलायितः
तरलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to tremble, made<BR>tremulous, agitated, waving to and fro, undulating;<BR>(अस्), m. a large wave, surf; (अस् or अम्), m. or n. (?),<BR>fickleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलिका
तरलिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलित|तरलितं
तरलित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, dangling, moving<BR>to and fro, undulating, trembling, tremulous.<BR>—त-<BR>रलित-हार, अस्, आ, अम्, having a tremulous garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्
तरस्, अस्, n. rapid progress, speed, velocity;<BR>strength, energy, efficacy; a bank; a float, a raft;<BR>a ferry, a place of crossing: a symbolical N. of<BR>Stoma; (आस्, आस्, अस्), Ved. pervading, quick, ener-<BR>getic; तरसा, ind. speedily, quickly, directly,<BR>energetically.<BR>—तरस्-मत्, आन्, m., N. of a son of<BR>the fourteenth Manu.<BR>—तरस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>quick, swift (e. g. तरस्-वत्यस्, ‘the swift ones,’<BR>i. e. the rivers); valiant, energetic, an epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—तरस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. quick, swift,<BR>strong, violent, energetic, courageous, bold; (ई), m.<BR>a courier, an express, a runner; a hero; air, wind;<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस|तरसं
तरस, अम्, n. meat, flesh.<BR>—तरस-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, consisting of meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरसान|तरसानः
तरसान, अस्, m. a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरान्धु|तरांधु|तरांधुः|तरान्धुः
तरान्धु or तरालु, उस्, m. a large flat-bottomed<BR>boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरि|तरिः
तरि, इस्, f. a boat, ship; a clothes-basket; the<BR>end of a cloth; (ई, ईस् or ई), f. a boat; a clothes-<BR>basket; the hem of a garment; a small wooden<BR>baling-vessel; a club; smoke.<BR>—तरि-रथ, अस्, m.<BR>an oar, a paddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिक|तरिकः
तरिक, अस्, m. a ferry-man; a float, a raft, a<BR>boat; (आ), f. a boat; cream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिकिन्
तरिकिन्, ई, m. a ferry-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरितव्य
तरितव्य or तरीतव्य or तर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be crossed or passed over, to be carried over or<BR>across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरितृ
तरितृ or तरीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what<BR>crosses, passes or carries over; (त्री), f. a boat, a raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरित्र|तरित्रं
तरित्र, अम्, n. a boat, a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिन्
तरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, who or what crosses; crossing;<BR>(इणी), f. a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीयस्
तरीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. easily passing through<BR>or pervading; (Sāy.) easy to be passed through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीष|तरीषः
तरीष, अस्, m. a raft, a float, a boat; the ocean;<BR>a fit or competent person; a fine shape or form; deco-<BR>rating, ornamenting; practice, business, profession;<BR>heaven or paradise; (ई), f., N. of a daughter of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीषन्
तरीषन् (occurring only as a loc. or Vedic inf.<BR>तरीषणि), Ved. passing through, going across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरु|तरुः
1. तरु, उस्, उस्, उ, = तरणि, Ved. passing through;<BR>(Sāy.) rapid motion, velocity; a wooden ladle for<BR>taking up the Soma; [cf. 2. तरु next col.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुतृ
तरुतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. overcoming, conquer-<BR>ing, a conqueror; impelling, causing to be quick;<BR>[cf. तरितृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुत्र
तरुत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. carrying across; over-<BR>coming, conquering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुष|तरुषः
तरुष, अस्, m., Ved. a conqueror, overcomer;<BR>(ई), f. victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुष्य
तरुष्य (fr. the next), nom. P. तरुष्यति,<BR>&c., Ved. to attack, overcome, conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुस्
तरुस्, उस्, n., Ved. battle; superiority; (Sāy.)<BR>overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरूषस्
तरूषस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. (Sāy.) overcoming,<BR>conquering, saving, protecting; (अस्), n. rescue (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरक्ष|तरक्षः
तरक्ष तरक्ष, अस्, m. or तरक्षु, उस्, m.<BR>or तरक्षुक, अस्, m. a hyena, or perhaps a<BR>tiger (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरंगः|तरङ्गः
तरङ्ग तरङ्ग. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरट
तरट तरट, a kind of medicinal plant,<BR>commonly ṭāmMMkalā; [cf. तरदी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्सल
तरत्सल तरत्सल, अस्, m. conflagration of<BR>chaff; (perhaps a wrong reading.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरदी
तरदी तरदी, f., N. of a thorny plant<BR>(= तारदी, तीव्रा, खर्वुरा, रक्त-वीजका; some<BR>read also तरटी and तारटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरन्तुक
तरन्तुक तरन्तुक. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरबालिका
तरबालिका तरबालिका, f. a kind of sword,<BR>= करबालिका; [cf. तरवारि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरम्बुज|तरम्बुजं
तरम्बुज तरम्बुज, अम्, n. a water-melon,<BR>(most probably borrowed from the Persian تربز);<BR>[cf. also खर्वूज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरल|तरलः
तरल तरल. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरवट
तरवट तरवट, the plant Cassia Auri-<BR>culata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरवारि|तरवारिः
तरवारि तरवारि, इस्, m. a sword, a scymi-<BR>tar; [cf. तरबालिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरवी
तरवी तरवी, in astrology = تربيع quadra-<BR>ture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्
तरस् तरस्, तरसा, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरसन्ती
तरसन्ती तरसन्ती, f. (fr. rt. त्रस्), Ved. the<BR>female of a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तराम्
तराम् तराम्, an adverbial form of 1. तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिता
तरिता तरिता, f. (perhaps fr. rt. तॄ), the<BR>fore-finger; garlic, or perhaps hemp; a form of<BR>Durgā; [cf. तारिणी.]<BR>—तरिता-धारणा-यन्त्र<BR>and तरिता-पूजा-यन्त्र, अम्, n. mystic diagrams<BR>given in the Tantra-sāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरु|तरुः
तरु 2. तरु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. तॄ;<BR>for 1. तरु see col. 2), a tree; N. of a son of Manu<BR>Cākṣuṣa; (तरु in the sense of ‘tree’ does not<BR>appear to occur in the Veda or Manu; it is perhaps<BR>a modern derivation fr. द्रु; but according to Sāy.<BR>it is used in Ṛg-veda V. 44, 5, in the sense of<BR>‘wooden ladle;’ cf. 1. तरु, col. 2); [cf. Lat. termes.]<BR>—तरु-खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. an assemblage of<BR>trees; (also तरु-षण्ड.)<BR>—तरु-च्छाया, f. the<BR>shade of a tree.<BR>—तरु-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by<BR>a tree (as a flower, fruit, &c.).<BR>—तरु-जीवन, अम्,<BR>n. the root of a tree, i. e. the vital organ of a<BR>tree.<BR>—तरु-तल, अस्, m. the part under the<BR>branches of a tree, the ground about its root, the<BR>foot of a tree.<BR>—तरु-ता, f. the state of a tree, the<BR>being a tree.<BR>—तरु-तूलिका or (according to another<BR>reading) तरु-दूलिका, f. the flying fox (suspended<BR>like a balance from the branches of a tree); [cf. वा-<BR>तुलि.]<BR>—तरु-नख, अस्, m. a thorn, (‘a tree-nail.’)<BR>—तरु-पङ्क्ति, इस्, f. a row of trees, an avenue.<BR>—तरु-भुज्, क्, m. a kind of parasitical plant, Vanda<BR>Roxburghii; [cf. तरु-रुहा, तरु-रोहिणी, तरु-<BR>स्था.]<BR>—तरु-महिमन्, आ, m. a section in the<BR>Vṛkṣāyur-veda which treats of the future rewards<BR>of those who plant trees.<BR>—तरु-मृग, अस्, m. ‘a<BR>tree-animal,’ a monkey, an ape.<BR>—तरु-राग, अस् or<BR>अम्, m. or n. (?), a sprout; a bud, a blossom.<BR>—तरु-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘the king of trees,’ the palmyra-<BR>tree; [cf. तृण-राज.]<BR>—तरु-राजन्, आ, m. ‘the<BR>king of the trees,’ an epithet of the Pārijāta.<BR>—तरु-रुहा, f. and तरु-रोहिणी, f. ‘growing<BR>on trees,’ a parasitical plant, = तरु-भुज्.<BR>—तरु-<BR>वर, अस्, m. an excellent tree, the best of trees, an<BR>epithet of the Pārijāta.<BR>—तरु-वल्ली, f. a kind of<BR>plant; [cf. पर्पटी.]<BR>—तरु-विटप, अस्, m. a<BR>branch or sprout.<BR>—तरु-शायिन्, ई, m. a bird (‘sleep-<BR>ing on trees’).<BR>—तरु-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. the best of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">Page0366-a+ 77</a>]<BR>trees.<BR>—तरु-षण्ड, अस्, m. a group of trees.<BR>—तरु-सार, अस्, m. ‘essence of trees,’ camphor.<BR>—तरु-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, staying or being in a tree;<BR>(आ), f. a parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुश
तरुश, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुकूणि|तरुकूणिः
तरुकूणि तरुकूणि, इस्, m. a sort of bird,<BR>= वाग्गुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुक्ष
तरुक्ष तरुक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf.<BR>तारुक्षायणि, तारुक्ष्य, तलुक्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुण|तरुणं|तरुणः
तरुण तरुण, अस्, ई, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तॄ), young, tender, juvenile; new, fresh; a young<BR>man, one of the virile age; fresh, lively, vivid;<BR>risen only a short time ago (as the sun), not yet<BR>high in the sky; (अस्), m. the castor-oil plant, Ricinus<BR>Communis; large cumin seed, = कुब्ज-पुष्प, the<BR>blossom of Achyranthes Aspera; N. of one of the<BR>Saptarṣayas in the eleventh Manv-antara; N. of a<BR>Gandharva; N. of a particular section in a mystical<BR>Tantra work treating of various stages in the life of the<BR>Tāntrika; (ई), f. a young woman, a girl from about<BR>sixteen years of age; N. of several plants; a kind of<BR>pot-herb, Aloe Perfoliata; also = तरणी, Rosa Glan-<BR>dulifera; also = दन्ती, a kind of flower, = सहा,<BR>कुमारी, गन्धाढ्या, चारु-केशरा, &c.; a kind<BR>of perfume, commonly चीडा; (अम्), n. cartilage [cf.<BR>तरुणास्थि below]; a sprout; [cf. तलुन; cf. also<BR>Gr. τέρην, τέρεινα; Old Germ. diorna, ‘maiden;’<BR>Old Island. therna.]<BR>—तरुण-ज्वर, अस्, m. a fever<BR>that lasts a week.<BR>—तरुण-दधि, इ, n. coagulated<BR>milk five days old.<BR>—तरुण-पीतिका, f. red arsenic.<BR>—तरुणाभास (˚ण-आभ्˚), अस्, m. a kind of cu-<BR>cumber.<BR>—तरुणास्थि (˚ण-अस्˚), इ, n. ‘soft-bone;’<BR>cartilage, gristle.<BR>—तरुणी-कटाक्ष-माल, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a plant, = तिलक.<BR>—तरुणी-गण, अस्, m. a<BR>number of young women.<BR>—तरुणी-जन, अस्, m. a<BR>young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणक|तरुणकं
तरुणक, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-demon; (अम्),<BR>n. a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणाय
तरुणाय, nom. P. -यति, &c., to bring forth; A. त-<BR>रुणायते, &c., to become or remain young or fresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणिमन्
तरुणिमन्, आ, m. youth, juvenility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरूट|तरूटः
तरूट तरूट, अस्, m. the root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरूणक
तरूणक तरूणक, अम्, n. (probably a wrong<BR>reading for तरुणक), Ved. a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्
तर्क् तर्क्, cl. 10. P. (ep. also A.) तर्कयति,<BR>-ते, तर्कयामास, तर्कयितुम्, to sup-<BR>pose, conjecture, guess, suspect, make a guess, infer,<BR>express an opinion, try to discover or ascertain,<BR>reason, speculate about; to consider or regard as<BR>(with two acc.); to reflect, think of, recollect, have<BR>in one's mind, intend; to ascertain; to shine, to<BR>speak; [cf. Lat. torqueo, torques, torcular, torvus;<BR>Goth. threihan; Angl. Sax. thringan; Old Germ.<BR>drayan; Mod. Germ. drehen; Goth. thagkyan;<BR>Lith. tikiu?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क|तर्कः
तर्क, अस्, m. supposition, conjecture; reasoning,<BR>speculation, inquiry, meditation, discussion; doubt;<BR>the science of logic, logic; a system of doctrine<BR>founded on speculation or free thinking, a philoso-<BR>phical system (especially one of the six, viz. Pūrva-<BR>mīmāṃsā, Uttara-mīmāṃsā, Nyāya, Vaiśeṣika, Sāṅ-<BR>khya, and Yoga); a name of the number six; (in<BR>logic) confutation, reduction to absurdity, a conclusion<BR>opposed to or disproving the premises; wish, desire;<BR>supplying an ellipsis; cause, motive; (आ), f. specu-<BR>lation, reasoning.<BR>—तर्क-कारिका, f., N. of a work<BR>setting forth the principles of the Vaiśeṣika phil.<BR>by Jīva-rāja Dīkṣita.<BR>—तर्क-कौमुदी, f., N. of<BR>an elementary work on the Vaiśeṣika system.<BR>—तर्क-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. a treatise on reasoning,<BR>manual of logic.<BR>—तर्क-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of an ele-<BR>mentary exposition of the Nyāya philosophy.<BR>—तर्क-<BR>ज्वाला, f. ‘the flame of speculation,’ N. of a Buddhist<BR>work.<BR>—तर्क-दीपिका, f., N. of a commentary<BR>on the Tarka-saṅgraha.<BR>—तर्क-प्रकाश, अस्, m.<BR>= तर्क-भाषा-प्रकाश.<BR>—तर्क-प्रदीप, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a manual of Vaiśeṣika principles by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">Page0366-b+ 78</a>]<BR>Koṇḍa-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—तर्क-भाषा or तर्कानुभाषा<BR>(˚क-अन्˚) or तर्क-परिभाषा, f., N. of a manual-<BR>of the Nyāya phil.<BR>—तर्कभाषा-प्रकाश, अस्, m.<BR>or तर्कभाषा-प्रकासिका, f. or तर्कभाषा-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. or तर्कभाषा-सार-मञ्जरी, f.,<BR>N. of certain commentaries on this work.<BR>—तर्क-<BR>मञ्जरी, f., N. of a commentary on the Tarka-<BR>kārikā by the author of the original work.<BR>—तर्क-<BR>मुद्रा, f. a particular position of the hand.<BR>—तर्क-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, conjectured, suspected.<BR>—तर्क-<BR>रत्न, अम्, n., N. of a Vaiśeṣika disquisition<BR>by Koṇḍa-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—तर्क-वाग्-ईश, अस्, m., N. of<BR>several writers on the Nyāya phil.<BR>—तर्क-विद्या,<BR>f. the science of reasoning or logic, a logical treatise.<BR>—तर्क-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the science of reasoning,<BR>logic; a philosophical work.<BR>—तर्क-सङ्ग्रह, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a manual of the Vaiśeṣika branch of the<BR>Nyāya phil. by Annam-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—तर्कसङ्ग्रह-<BR>दीपिका, f., N. of a commentary on the preceding<BR>by the same author.<BR>—तर्काभास (˚क-आभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. apparent reasoning, fallacy in drawing conclusions,<BR>incompatibility of conclusion and premises.<BR>—तर्का-<BR>मृत (˚क-अम्˚), अम्, n., N. of an elementary<BR>work on the Vaiśeṣika doctrine by Jagad-īśa Tar-<BR>kālaṅkāra Bhaṭṭācārya.<BR>—तर्कामृत-चषक, N.<BR>of a commentary on the preceding work by Gaṅ-<BR>gārāma Jaḍī.<BR>—तर्कामृत-तरङ्गिणी, f., N. of<BR>a commentary on the Tarkāmṛta by Mukunda<BR>Bhaṭṭa Gāḍegila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कक|तर्ककः
तर्कक, अस्, आ, अम्, inquiring, inquisitive, investi-<BR>gating; (अस्), m. a suppliant, a petitioner, an asker,<BR>an inquirer; a logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कण|तर्कणं
तर्कण, अम्, n. conjecturing, reasoning, specu-<BR>lating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कणीय
तर्कणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be suspected, to be an<BR>object of the suspicion of others (with gen.); causing<BR>suspicion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कयत्
तर्कयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, conjecturing, expecting,<BR>anticipating, doubting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कारी
तर्कारी, f. the tree Sesbania Ægyptiaca, a kind of<BR>gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किण|तर्किणः
तर्किण or तर्किल, अस्, m. the tree Cassia Tora,<BR>= चक्र-मर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कित
तर्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, investigated, examined, doubted,<BR>discussed, &c.; (अम्), n. conjecture, supposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किन्
तर्किन्, ई, इणी, इ, conjecturing, supposing; reason-<BR>ing, skilled in speculation or philosophy; (ई), m. a<BR>logician, disputant, reasoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुक|तर्कुकः
तर्कुक, अस्, m. a suppliant, beggar; [cf. तर्कक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्य
तर्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be imagined or supposed,<BR>capable of investigation or reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कु|तर्कुः
तर्कु तर्कु, उस्, उस्, m. f. (said to be fr. rt. कृत्,<BR>with transposition of the consonants), a spindle, an<BR>iron pin upon which the cotton is first drawn out and<BR>which serves as the distaff, the cotton being next<BR>transferred from it to the wheel; [cf. Gr. ἄ-τρακτος.]<BR>—तर्कु-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a ball of clay &c. at the<BR>lower end of a spindle to assist in giving it a rotatory<BR>motion.<BR>—तर्कु-पीठ, अस्, ई, m. f. or तर्कु-पाठी,<BR>f. a ball at the lower end of a spindle.<BR>—तर्कु-<BR>लासक, अस्, m. a concave shell or saucer which serves<BR>to hold the lower end of the spindle when whirled<BR>round.<BR>—तर्कु-शाण, अस्, m. a small whetstone for<BR>sharpening spindles, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुट|तर्कुटं
तर्कुट, अम्, n. drawing out the cotton upon the<BR>distaff or upon the wheel; spinning; (ई), f. a spindle,<BR>a distaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्षु|तर्क्षुः
तर्क्षु तर्क्षु, उस्, m. = तरक्षु, a hyena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्ष्य|तर्क्ष्यः
तर्क्ष्य तर्क्ष्य, अस्, m. nitre, saltpetre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज्
तर्ज् तर्ज्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) तर्जति,<BR>-ते, ततर्ज, तर्जितुम्, to threaten, me-<BR>nace; to blame, censure, reprove; Caus. P. (ep. also<BR>A.) तर्जयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to threaten; to scold,<BR>censure; to frighten, terrify; to deride, mock; [cf.<BR>Old Germ. trug, druk, triugu, driuku, ‘to cheat:’<BR>Angl. Sax. threagan, ‘to chide;’ thracian, thraec:<BR>Old Germ. dravyan: Mod. Germ. drohen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जन|तर्जनं|तर्ज्जन|तर्ज्जनं
तर्जन, अम्, n. threatening, blaming, censuring;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">Page0366-c+ 73</a>]<BR>pointing at in ridicule or contempt; putting to shame,<BR>surpassing; wrath, anger; (आ), f. threatening, censur-<BR>ing; (ई), f. the fore-finger (as used for threatening).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जनीय
तर्जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be threatened, repre-<BR>hensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जित|तर्ज्जित
तर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, threatened, blamed, reviled;<BR>shamed, disgraced; (अम्), n. threatening, menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जिक|तर्ज्जिक|तर्ज्जिकः
तर्जिक तर्जिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a country<BR>or people, perhaps to the north-west of India or<BR>Bokhara, the country of the Tājiks; (also तायिक<BR>or ताजिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ण|तर्णः
तर्ण तर्ण or तर्णक, अस्, m. (perhaps cor-<BR>rupted fr. तरुण), a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णि|तर्णिः
तर्णि तर्णि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. तॄ), a float, a<BR>raft; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्तरीक|तर्त्तरीक|तर्त्तरीकं
तर्तरीक तर्तरीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. तॄ), being in the habit of passing or crossing over,<BR>a passenger; (अम्), n. a boat, a raft, a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्तव्य
तर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्. See तरितव्य, p. 365, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द्
तर्द् तर्द् (connected with rt. तृद्) , cl. 1.<BR>P. तर्दति, &c., to kill, injure, hurt; cut<BR>through; [cf. rt. तृद्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द|तर्द्द
तर्द, अस्, m., Ved. a species of bird; [cf. Lat.<BR>turdus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्दू
तर्दू, ऊस्, m. f. ? (fr. rt. तृद्, but said to be fr.<BR>rt. तॄ), a wooden ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द्मन्
तर्द्मन्, अ, n., Ved. a hole, an opening, a cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पण|तर्पणं
तर्पण तर्पण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. तृप्), satis-<BR>fying, satiating, pleasing, refreshing [cf. घ्राण-<BR>तर्पण]; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a kind of plant; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of a plant, = गुरु-स्कन्ध, श्लेष्मणा; (अम्),<BR>n. the becoming satisfied or satiated, the act of sati-<BR>ating, refreshing, pleasing; satisfaction given or re-<BR>ceived; the state of being pleased; satiety, fulness;<BR>pleasure; a religious rite, libation, presenting libations<BR>of water to the manes of the deceased or to the<BR>Pitṛs collectively, also to the gods, either generally or<BR>individually; gladdening; satiating the eyes, i. e. filling<BR>them with oil &c.; food; fuel used on sacrificial<BR>occasions or for lighting a sacrificial fire; a kind of<BR>sweetmeat (?).<BR>—तर्पण-विधि, इस्, m. a chapter of<BR>the Smṛty-artha-sāra by Śrīdhara-svāmin on funeral<BR>ceremonies &c.<BR>—तर्पणेच्छु (˚ण-इच्˚), उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, desirous of satisfaction or of receiving after death<BR>the presentation of water called Tarpaṇa; (उस्), m.<BR>an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पणीय
तर्पणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be satiated or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पयितव्य
तर्पयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be satiated or re-<BR>freshed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पयित्वा
तर्पयित्वा, ind. having satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पित
तर्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, gratified, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पिन्
तर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, gratifying, giving pleasure or<BR>satisfaction; offering oblations to the manes, one<BR>who does so; (इणी), f. the plant Hibiscus Mutabilis<BR>(पद्म-चारिणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्फितृ
तर्फितृ तर्फितृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. rt. तृफ्),<BR>a killer, injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ब्
तर्ब् तर्ब्, cl. 1. P. तर्बति, &c., to go<BR>or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्बट|तर्बटः|तर्ब्बट
तर्बट तर्बट, अस्, m. a year; the plant<BR>Cassia Tora, = चक्र-मर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्मन्|तर्म्मन्
तर्मन् तर्मन्, अ, n. (perhaps fr. rt. तॄ),<BR>the top or end of the sacrificial post; [cf. सु-तर्मन्;<BR>cf. also Gr. τέρμα; Lat. terminus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्य
तर्य तर्य, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तॄ), Ved. (Sāy.)<BR>N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ष|तर्षः
1. तर्ष, अस्, m. a raft or float; the ocean; the<BR>sun; [cf. तरणि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ष|तर्षः
तर्ष 2. तर्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तृष्), thirst;<BR>wish, desire; Desire personified as a son of Arka<BR>(the sun) and Vāsanā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षण|तर्षणं
तर्षण, अम्, n. thirsting, thirst; desiring, wish,<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षम्
तर्षम्, ind. thirsting, being thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षित|तर्षितः
तर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, thirsting, athirst, thirsty;<BR>desiring, wishing for; [cf. तृषित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षुल
तर्षुल, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing, desiring; in अ-तर्-<BR>षुल, without desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ष्यावत्|तर्ष्यावन्त्
तर्ष्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हण|तर्हणं
तर्हण तर्हण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. तृह्), Ved.<BR>injuring, crushing, bruising; [cf. दस्यु-तर्हण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हि
तर्हि तर्हि, ind. (fr. the pronom. base 2. त),<BR>at that time, then, at that moment, in that case; in<BR>the mean time; (this word occurs in the Veda, but<BR>is rarely found in the earlier epic poetry); यदा —<BR>तर्हि, when — then; यदि — तर्हि, यत्र — तर्हि,<BR>चेद् — तर्हि, if — then; [cf. एतर्हि, कर्हि, यर्हि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्
तल् तल्, cl. 1. 10. P. तलति, तालयति, &c.,<BR>to be full or complete; to fix, found; to<BR>establish; to be fixed; to accomplish a vow; (ac-<BR>cording to others a Sautra root.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल|तलं|तलः
तल तल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (perhaps fr. rt.<BR>स्तृ), surface, a level surface, the flat roof of a house;<BR>(often used in composition with only a slight altera-<BR>tion of the sense of the word to which it is added,<BR>but explained by lexicographers to mean ‘essential<BR>nature,’ e. g. मही-तल, the very earth, the surface<BR>of the earth, earth itself; नभस्-तल, the sky,<BR>heaven); the inner side or palm of the hand with<BR>extended fingers (in पाणि-तल, &c.); the sole of the<BR>foot (in पाद-तल); the fore-arm; a span; a slap or<BR>clap with the hand, (अन्योन्यस्य तलान् ददुः, they<BR>slapped each other with the palms of the hands);<BR>depth, lowness, inferiority of position, the under<BR>part, the part underneath, lower part, base, bottom;<BR>a hole, a pit, a chasm; तले, ind. at the bottom,<BR>under, beneath; (अम्, आ), n. f. a leathern fence worn<BR>by archers on the left arm [cf. तल-त्र and तल-<BR>त्राण]; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva [cf. ताल and<BR>अ-तल]; the palmyra-tree, = ताल; the hilt or haft<BR>or handle of a sword &c.; pressing the strings of a<BR>lute with the left hand; a division of hell; (अम्), n.<BR>a wood; a pond; cause, origin, motive, the root or<BR>seed of events; [cf. अ-तल, जिह्वा-त्˚, धरणी-त्˚,<BR>नि-त्˚, प्र-त्˚, महा-त्˚, रसा-त्˚, वि-त्˚, सु-त्˚; cf. also<BR>Hib. talamh, ‘the world, earth;’ Lat. tellus.]<BR>—त-<BR>ल-घात, अस्, m. a slap with the palm of the hand.<BR>—तल-तस्, ind. from the bottom.<BR>—तल-ताल, अस्,<BR>m. clapping the hands; [cf. ताल-शब्द.]<BR>—तल-<BR>त्र or तल-त्राण, अम्, n. (hand or arm-guard), the<BR>leathern glove of an archer.<BR>—तलत्र-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, wearing a leathern glove (as an archer).<BR>—तल-<BR>प्रहार, अस्, m. a slap or blow with the palm of<BR>the hand or with a claw.<BR>—तल-मुख-हस्त, अस्,<BR>m. a particular position of the hand with the palm<BR>expanded.<BR>—तल-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with a<BR>handle or haft.<BR>—तल-युद्ध, अम्, n. a fight carried<BR>on with the palms of the hands, a fight.<BR>—तल-<BR>लोक, अस्, m. the lower regions, nether world; [cf.<BR>तलातल, रसातल, अ-तल.]<BR>—तल-सारक, अम्,<BR>n. a martingale, a strap passing between the fore-<BR>legs of a horse; a kind of trough or vessel from<BR>which horses are fed (?).<BR>—तल-स्थ or तल-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, remaining beneath.<BR>—तल-हृदय,<BR>अम्, n. the centre of the sole of the foot.<BR>—तलाङ्-<BR>गुलि (˚ल-अङ्˚), इस्, f. a toe.<BR>—तलाची, f. (fr. तल<BR>and rt. अञ्च्), a mat, one made of reeds or bamboos.<BR>—तलातल (˚ल-अत्˚), अम्, n. the fourth of the<BR>seven divisions of the infernal regions; [cf. अ-तल,<BR>महा-त्˚, रसा-त्˚, वि-त्˚, सु-त्˚.]<BR>—तलेक्षण (˚ल-<BR>ईक्˚), अस्, m. a hog (‘looking downwards’).<BR>—त-<BR>लोत्तम (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), cover, site (?).<BR>—तलोदर (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having a<BR>protuberant belly or one that hangs down (?); (ई),<BR>f. a mistress or wife.<BR>—तलोदा (˚ल-उद्), f. a river<BR>(‘whose water flows downwards’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलक|तलकं|तलकः
तलक, अम्, n. a large pond; [cf. तल्ल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलकोट
तलकोट, a kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिका
तलिका, f. a martingale; [cf. तल-सारक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित|तलितं
1. तलित, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed, placed, having a bottom;<BR>[cf. 2. तलित next col.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन्
तलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing the leathern fence called<BR>Tala (as an archer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलमीन
तलमीन तल-मीन, a various reading for<BR>नल-मीन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलव|तलवः
तलव तलव, अम्, n., Ved. a musician.<BR>—तलव-कार, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school of the<BR>Sāma-veda.<BR>—तलवकारोपनिषद् (˚र-उप्˚), त्, f.<BR>= केनोपनिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवारण|तलवारणं
तलवारण तलवारण, अम्, n. a sword; [cf.<BR>तरवारि; Beng. talvār; Hind. تلوار]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलाशा
तलाशा तलाशा, f., Ved. a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित|तलितं
तलित 2. तलित, अम्, n. fried meat. (For<BR>1. तलित see col. 1, under तल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन|तलिनं|तलिनः
तलिन तलिन, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तल्), thin, spare, meagre, delicate; small, little;<BR>clear, clean; separate, having spaces or interstices;<BR>below, situated under or beneath [cf. तल]; (अम्),<BR>n. a bed, a couch or cot; (a various reading for त-<BR>लिम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिम|तलिमं
तलिम तलिम, अम्, n. ground prepared for<BR>the site of a dwelling &c. (कुट्टिम); a bed, a couch<BR>or cot [cf. तलिन and तल्प]; an awning; a scymitar,<BR>a large sacrificial sword or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलीड्य
तलीड्य तलीड्य, Ved. a particular part of<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुक्ष
तलुक्ष तलुक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf.<BR>तरुक्ष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुन|तलुनः
तलुन तलुन, अस्, ई, अम् (for तरुण, q. v.),<BR>young; (अस्), m. a youth; air, wind; (ई), f. a girl,<BR>a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्क|तल्कं
तल्क तल्क, अम्, n. a wood, a forest; [cf.<BR>तल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्प|तल्पं|तल्पः
तल्प तल्प, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in the earlier<BR>language m., in the later n.; perhaps fr. rt. स्तृ, but<BR>according to others fr. rt. तल् or fr. rt. तृप्), a couch,<BR>bed, sofa; a wife; the seat of a carriage; an upper<BR>story, a room on the top of a house, a turret, a tower or<BR>keep; (in the Atharva-veda XIII. 1, 17, तल्पा occurs.)<BR>—तल्प-कीट, अस्, m. ‘a bed-insect,’ a bug.<BR>—तल्प-<BR>ग, see under गुरु.<BR>—तल्प-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—तल्प-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, brought forth in<BR>or on a marriage-bed; born of a wife (as a son by<BR>an appointed substitute).<BR>—तल्प-शीवन्, आ, अरी, अ,<BR>or तल्पे-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. resting on a couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पक|तल्पकः
तल्पक, अस्, m. a maker of beds or sofas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पन|तल्पनं
तल्पन, अम्, n. (fr. a nom. formed fr. तल्प),<BR>an elephant's back, the exterior muscles of the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पीकृत
तल्पी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made into a bed or couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्प्य
तल्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to a bed;<BR>worthy of a couch or sofa; born in a marriage-bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्ल|तल्लं|तल्लः
तल्ल तल्ल, अस्, m. a reservoir, a large pond,<BR>a tank or Talao; (ई), f. a young woman; N. of the<BR>wife of Varuṇa; a boat; (अम्), n. a pit, a hole; [cf.<BR>तल and तलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लक्षण
तल्लक्षण तल्-लक्षण. See under तद्, p. 361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लज|तल्लजः
तल्लज तल्लज, अस्, m. excellence, happiness;<BR>(also attributively) excellent, happy; used in apposition<BR>as an epithet (e. g. कुमारी-तल्लज, an excellent<BR>maiden; गो-तल्लज, the best of cows.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लह
तल्लह तल्लह (?), अस्, m. a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लिका
तल्लिका तल्लिका, f. a key; [cf. ताली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्व|तल्वं
तल्व तल्व, अम्, n. scent arising from the<BR>rubbing of fragrant substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक|तवकः
तवक तवक, अस्, आ, अम्, thine; (perhaps an<BR>incorrect form for तावक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक्षीर|तवक्षीरं
तवक्षीर तवक्षीर (a corruption of त्वक्-<BR>क्षीर), अम्, n. manna of bamboo (commonly Ta-<BR>bāṣīr); a N. applied to a kind of extract of wheat,<BR>barley, rice, &c., (or, according to some, a kind<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">Page0367-c+ 74</a>]<BR>of milk and water), = पयः-क्षीर, यव-ज,<BR>यवजोद्भव (commonly Toṣākṣīra); (ई), f. a<BR>kind of Curcuma (गन्ध-पत्त्रा).<BR>—तवक्षीर्य्-<BR>एकपत्त्रिका, the single-leaved Tavakṣīrī, turmeric,<BR>Curcuma Zedoaria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवर
तवर तवर, a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवराज|तवराजः
तवराज तवराज, अस्, m. a sort of sugar<BR>prepared from a species of Hedysarum (यवास-<BR>शर्करा).<BR>—तवराजोद्भव-खण्ड (˚ज-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a sort of hard sugar prepared from the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्
तवस् तवस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (fr. rt. 2. तु), Ved.<BR>strong, powerful, courageous, efficacious, energetic;<BR>an epithet of Rudra, the Maruts, Indra, Parjanya,<BR>Agni, Pūṣan; (आस्), m. power, strength, courage;<BR>[cf. प्र-तवस्.]<BR>—तवस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>powerful, strong, an epithet of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्य
तवस्य, अम्, n., Ved. strength, efficacy; courage;<BR>(Sāy.) an oblation which increases the strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवागा
तवागा (fr. तवा, a derivative of rt. 2. तु, and गो?),<BR>an epithet of a bull; (but in the Pada-pāṭha this<BR>word is not considered as a compound, and by Sāy.<BR>it is said to mean) of great strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष|तविषः
तविष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. powerful, strong, ener-<BR>getic, efficacious; courageous; (अस्), m. the ocean,<BR>sea; heaven, paradise; (ई), f. power, strength, violence,<BR>courage, (inst. plur. तविषीभिस्, powerfully, violently);<BR>the earth; a river; N. of a daughter of Indra; (अम्),<BR>n. power, strength.<BR>—तविषी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>powerful, violent, epithet of the winds.<BR>—तविषी-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. powerful, strong, an epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविषीय
तविषीय, nom. P., Ved. तविषीयति, &c., to be<BR>strong or violent or courageous, to make effort;<BR>(Sāy.) to wish for power or strength; [cf. तविष्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविषीयु
तविषीयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. spirited (as a horse);<BR>violent, epithet of the Maruts; (Sāy.) evincing<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष्य
तविष्य, nom. A., Ved. तविष्यते, &c., to be<BR>strong or violent, have courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष्या
तविष्या, f., Ved. violence, force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवीयस्
तवीयस् or तव्यस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of त-<BR>वस्), stronger, very strong, powerful, rich; (generally<BR>found in the phrase तवसस् तवीयान्, stronger than<BR>the strong.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवीष|तवीषः
तवीष, अस्, m. the ocean; heaven; gold; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Indra; [cf. तविष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तव्य
1. तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. powerful, strong, grown<BR>strong. (For 2. तव्य see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवारिसाण
तवारिसाण तवारिसाण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविपुला
तविपुला त-विपुला, f. a particular metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तव्य
तव्य 2. तव्य, a कृत् affix by means of which<BR>the future passive participle is formed from roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तश्ली
तश्ली तश्ली, f. in astron., trigon. = تثليث<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्ट|तष्टः
तष्ट तष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तक्ष्), pared,<BR>hewn, cut, chiseled, split, made thin; fashioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्टृ
तष्टृ, टा, m. a carpenter, a builder, a builder<BR>of chariots; a N. of Viśva-karman, the architect of<BR>the gods; N. of one of the twelve Ādityas; [cf.<BR>त्वष्टृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्
तस् तस्, cl. 4. P. तस्यति, &c., to fade<BR>away, become exhausted, perish, wane;<BR>to throw down; to cast upwards, reject, cast; [cf.<BR>rt. तंस् and Eng. toss.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तसर|तसरः
तसर तसर, अम्, अस्, n. m. (?), (fr. rt.<BR>तंस् ?), Ved. a shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तसीर
तसीर तसीर, in astron. = तासीर, = تسيير<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्कर|तस्करः
तस्कर तस्कर, अस्, m. (said to be derived<BR>fr. अतस् and rt. कृ; according to others fr. तद् and<BR>rt. कृ), a thief, a robber; (at the end of a comp.)<BR>anything bad or contemptible [cf. चौर]; (in astron.)<BR>N. of certain Ketus; a kind of pot-herb, Trigonella<BR>Corniculata; a tree, Vangueria Spinosa [cf. मदन];<BR>the ear; (ई), f. a passionate woman; N. of several<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">Page0368-a+ 72</a>]<BR>plants, a sort of Mimosa, = तस्कर-स्नायु, Leea<BR>Hirta, &c.<BR>—तस्कर-ता, f. or तस्कर-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>thievishness, thieving, theft; catching by means of<BR>the ear, hearing.<BR>—तस्कर-वत्, ind. like a thief.<BR>—तस्कर-स्नायु, उस्, m. the plant Leea Hirta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0367-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्तुव
तस्तुव तस्तुव, अम्, n., Ved. an antidote<BR>against poison (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्थु
तस्थु तस्थु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the weakest<BR>cases of तस्थिवस्, perf. part. of rt. स्था), stationary,<BR>immovable, motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्दी
तस्दी तस्दी, in astron., hexagon, = تسْديس<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्मात्
तस्मात् तस्मात्, ind. (abl. of the pronom.<BR>base 2. त), from that, on that account, therefore,<BR>(correlative to यस्मात् and यद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्षक
ताक्षक ताक्षक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तक्षकीया),<BR>relating or belonging to Takṣakīyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्षण्य|ताक्षण्यः
ताक्षण्य, अस्, m. (fr. तक्षन्), the son of a<BR>woodcutter or carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्षशिल
ताक्षशिल, अस्, ई, अम्, coming or produced from<BR>Takṣaśilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्ष्ण|ताक्ष्णः
ताक्ष्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तक्षन्), fit for a car-<BR>penter; (अस्), m. the son of a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छब्द्य
ताच्छब्द्य ताच्छब्द्य, अम्, n. (fr. तच्छब्द<BR>[तद्+शब्द], having that name or the name of that),<BR>the being called or named after that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छीलिक|ताच्छीलिकः
ताच्छीलिक ताच्छीलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तच्-<BR>छील or ताच्छील्य), a N. given to an affix when it<BR>denotes ‘having a particular inclination or custom.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छील्य|ताच्छील्यं
ताच्छील्य, अम्, n. the being accustomed to that,<BR>doing anything regularly, consuetude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजक्
ताजक् ताजक्. See ताजत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजक
ताजक ताजक and ताजिक, अम्, n., N. of<BR>certain astronomical books translated from the Arabic<BR>and Persian (e. g. ताजिक-ज्योतिर्-मणि, ताजक-पद्-<BR>धति, ताजक-शास्त्र, ताजक-सार-सुधा-निधि,<BR>विश्वनाथ-ताजक, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजत्
ताजत् ताजत् or sometimes ताजक्, ind., Ved.<BR>suddenly, abruptly, (opposed to चिरम्.)<BR>—ताजद्-<BR>भङ्ग, अस्, m., Ved. a species of very fragile wood;<BR>[cf. कोविदार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजिक|ताजिकः
ताजिक ताजिक or ताजीक, N. of a district;<BR>also = ताजक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटङ्क|ताटंक|ताटंकः|ताटङ्कः
ताटङ्क ताटङ्क, अस्, m. an ornament for<BR>the ear, a large sort of ear-ring; [cf. ताडङ्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटस्थ्य|ताटस्थ्यं
ताटस्थ्य ताटस्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. तट-स्थ, a<BR>by-stander), proximity; indifference, disregard, ex-<BR>emption from attachment or aversion, neutrality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड ताड, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तड्), beating,<BR>striking; (अस्), m. a blow, thump, knock, beating,<BR>whipping, chastisement; sound, noise; a handful of<BR>grass, corn, &c., a sheaf; a mountain; a kind of grass,<BR>Andropogon Serratus, = देवताड; [cf. ताडि next col.]<BR>—ताड-घ, अस्, आ, अम्, beating with a whip or<BR>strokes of any kind; (अस्), m. a blacksmith (?).<BR>—ताड-घात, अस्, m. an artificer who beats or<BR>hammers, a smith.<BR>—ताड-वक्र, N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडका
ताडका, f., N. of a Yakṣiṇī or female fiend,<BR>daughter of Su-ketu, wife of Sunda, and mother of<BR>Mārīca, (she was changed into a Rākṣasī by Agastya,<BR>whose devotions she had disturbed, and was afterwards<BR>killed by Rāma, see Rāmāyaṇa I. 28); the large<BR>dark-green pumpkin.<BR>—ताडका-फल, अम्, n. large<BR>cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडकायन
ताडकायन, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडन|ताडनं
ताडन, अस्, आ, अम्, beating, whipping, striking,<BR>hitting, hurting; (अम्), n. the act of striking, beating,<BR>thumping, whipping, chastising, a stroke, blow; (in<BR>astron.) touching, partial eclipse; (आ), f. striking;<BR>(ई), f. a whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडनीय
ताडनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be beaten, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयितृ
ताडयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a striker, beater, thumper,<BR>who or what beats or strikes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयित्वा
ताडयित्वा, ind. having beaten or struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडित
ताडित, अस्, आ, अम्, struck, beaten, chastised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडुल|ताडुलः
ताडुल, अस्, आ, अम्, beating, who or what beats<BR>or strikes, punishing with blows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्य
ताड्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be beaten or chastised or<BR>punished, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्यमान|ताड्यमानः
ताड्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being beaten or struck;<BR>suffering blows, undergoing a beating; (अस्), m. a<BR>musical instrument which is struck (as a drum &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडङ्क|ताडंक|ताडंकः|ताडङ्कः
ताडङ्क ताडङ्क, अस्, m. or ताडपत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of ear-ring or ornament of the ear; [cf.<BR>ताटङ्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडाग
ताडाग ताडाग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तडाग), being<BR>in tanks, coming from ponds (as water &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडि|ताडिः
ताडि ताडि, इस् or ई f. (for ताली), a kind of<BR>palm, Corypha Taliera; (ई), f. a kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्ड
ताण्ड ताण्ड, अस्, m. (fr. तण्ड or तण्डा),<BR>N. of an old sage; (अम्), n., N. of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डक
ताण्डक, अम्, n., N. of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डव|तांडव|तांडवं|ताण्डवं|तांडवः|ताण्डवः
ताण्डव ताण्डव, अस्, अम्, m. n. dancing,<BR>especially with violent gesticulation, and particularly<BR>applied to the frantic dance of the god Śiva and his<BR>votaries; (in prosody) a tribrach or foot of three<BR>short syllables; a sort of grass, Saccharum Procerum.<BR>—ताण्डव-तालिक, अस्, m. an epithet of Nandin<BR>the door-keeper of Śiva.<BR>—ताण्डव-प्रिय, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva (‘fond of the Tāṇḍava dance’).<BR>—ताण्डव-ब्राह्मण, perhaps a wrong reading<BR>for ताण्डक-ब्राह्मण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवित|तांडवित
ताण्डवित, अस्, आ, अम्, moving round in a wild<BR>dance; dancing; fluttering; frowning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डि|तांडिः|ताण्डिः
ताण्डि, इ, n., N. of a manual of the art of dancing;<BR>the science of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डिन्
ताण्डिन्, ई, m., N. of a writer on prosody; (इनस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a Vedic school founded by a pupil of<BR>Vaiśampāyana.<BR>—ताण्डि-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Brāhmaṇa belonging to this school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्ड्य
ताण्ड्य, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a Brāhmaṇa belonging to the Sāma-veda, to which<BR>there is a commentary by Sāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्ड्यायनी
ताण्ड्यायनी, f. a patronymic from Tāṇḍya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्
तात् तात्, ind. (an obsolete abl. fr. the<BR>pronom. base 2. त), Ved. thus, in this way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात|तातः
तात तात, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. 3. तन्),<BR>venerable, reverend, respectable, dear; (अस्), m. a<BR>father; a term of affection or endearment addressed<BR>to any person, but especially to a junior or inferior,<BR>as to a child or pupil (e. g. हे तात, O child!); any<BR>person for whom one feels pity; [cf. Lat. tata: Gr.<BR>τἐττα; Boh. tata, ‘father:’ Lith. téta, tétis,<BR>‘daddy;’ teta, ‘aunt:’ Old Germ. toto: Low<BR>Germ. teite, ‘daddy, dad.’]<BR>—तात-गु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>agreeable to a father, paternal, fatherly, relating or<BR>belonging to a father; (उस्), m. a paternal uncle.<BR>—तात-जनयित्री, त्र्यौ, f. du. father and mother,<BR>parents.<BR>—तात-तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, like a father,<BR>paternal; (अस्), m. a paternal uncle or the most<BR>respectable of a man's male relations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातल|तातलः
तातल, अस्, m. a fatherly relative, one who may<BR>be considered as a father; an iron club or spike;<BR>sickness, disease; cooking or maturing; heat, physical<BR>or morbid; (अस्, आ, अम्), hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताति|तातिः
ताति, इस्, m. offspring, a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्य
तात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. paternal, fatherly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातन|तातनः
तातन तातन, अस्, m. a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातृपि
तातृपि तातृपि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. Intens. of rt.<BR>तृप्), Ved. satisfying, delighting much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातृषाण
तातृषाण तातृषाण, अस्, आ, अम् (perf. part.<BR>fr. rt. 1. तृष्), Ved. thirsting, very thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कर्म्य
तात्कर्म्य तात्कर्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. तत्-कर्मन्),<BR>sameness of occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कालिक|तात्कालिकः
तात्कालिक तात्कालिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr.<BR>तत्-काल), ‘lasting that time,’ lasting equally long,<BR>happening at that time, simultaneous, contemporary,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">Page0368-c+ 71</a>]<BR>instantly appearing; happening immediately or with-<BR>out delay; relating to any particular moment of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्काल्य|तात्काल्यं
तात्काल्य, अम्, n. simultaneousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्तलि
तात्तलि तात्तलि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्त्विक
तात्त्विक तात्त्विक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तत्त्व),<BR>accordant with reality, real, true, essential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्य|तात्पर्यं|तात्पर्य्य|तात्पर्य्यं
तात्पर्य तात्पर्य, अम्, n. (fr. तत्-पर),<BR>aim, reference to any object (with loc.), object,<BR>purpose, intent, design; meaning, scope, purport;<BR>explanation; तात्पर्यतस् or तात्पर्येण, ind. with<BR>this intention, with this aim or object.<BR>—तात्पर्य-<BR>परिशुद्धि, इस्, f., N. of a work by Udayana.<BR>—तात्पर्य-बोधिनी, f., N. of a commentary on<BR>a philosophical work called Citra-dīpa.<BR>—तात्पर्-<BR>यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. the meaning or purpose<BR>of a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यक
तात्पर्यक, अस्, इका, अम्, aiming at, intending,<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्य
तात्य तात्य. See under तात, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्स्तोम्य
तात्स्तोम्य तात्स्तोम्य, अम्, n. (fr. तत्-स्तोम),<BR>sameness of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्स्थ्य
तात्स्थ्य तात्स्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. तत्-स्थ), the<BR>residing in that, the being contained in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताथाभाव्य
ताथाभाव्य ताथाभाव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. तथा-<BR>भाव), a N. for the Svarita accent at the end of the<BR>first member of a compound when an Udātta syllable<BR>immediately follows, (the low-sounding vowel in such<BR>a position cannot strictly be called either Svarita or<BR>Anudātta-tara, and a new name is therefore given<BR>to it; this may often happen in the case of two<BR>separate words, but the vowel is then called An-<BR>udātta-tara.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थिक
तादर्थिक तादर्थिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तद्-अर्-<BR>थ or तादर्थ्य), destined or intended for that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थ्य|तादर्थ्यं
तादर्थ्य, अम्, n. the being destined or intended<BR>for that, the having that or the same object, identity<BR>of aim, object; relation to; sameness or precision of<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्म्य|तादात्म्यं
तादात्म्य तादात्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. तद्-आत्मन्),<BR>sameness of nature or character, identity, unity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादीत्ना
तादीत्ना तादीत्ना, ind. (fr. तदी = तदि, a cor-<BR>relative of यदि, and affix त्न?), Ved. at that time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादुरी
तादुरी तादुरी, f., Ved. epithet of a frog<BR>(explained by Durga as either तरण-शीला, able to<BR>swim, or तावद् उदरम्, consisting only of a belly;<BR>perhaps a wrong reading for ताडुरी, as if fr. rt. तड्;<BR>cf. also दर्दुर, ‘a frog’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृक्ष|तादृक्षः
तादृक्ष ता-दृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the pronom.<BR>base 2. त and दृक्ष fr. rt. दृश्), such like, such<BR>a one, like that, like him, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृशि
ता-दृशि, क्, क्, क् (Ved. nom. m. f. तादृङ्), like<BR>that, such like, like him or it, &c.; (क्), ind. in<BR>such a manner.<BR>—तादृग्-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, of such<BR>qualities.<BR>—तादृग्-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, of such a shape<BR>or form.<BR>—तादृग्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of such a<BR>kind, of such qualities, being in this situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश|तादृशः
ता-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, such like, such a one; या-<BR>दृशस् तादृशस्, anybody whosoever; [cf. Prāk.<BR>tārisa; Gr. τηλίκος; Dor. ταλίκος Slav. tolik;<BR>Lat. talis.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताद्धर्म्य
ताद्धर्म्य ताद्धर्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. तद्-धर्-<BR>मन्), sameness of law, analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताद्धित
ताद्धित ताद्धित, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तद्-धित),<BR>formed with a Taddhita affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताद्रूप्य
ताद्रूप्य ताद्रूप्य, अम्, n. (fr. तद्-रूप),<BR>oneness or sameness of form, figure, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान|तानं|तानः
तान तान, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. तन्), a thread,<BR>a fibre; a tone, a protracted tone, the key-note (in<BR>music); a monotonous tone (in reciting, also called<BR>Eka-śruti); (अम्), n. expanse, extension; an object<BR>of sense; [cf. Gr. τόνος.]<BR>—तान-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">Page0369-a+ 74</a>]<BR>tuning the voice previously to singing; running over<BR>the notes to catch the key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0368-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानव|तानवं
तानव तानव, अम्, n. (fr. तनु), thinness,<BR>spareness, meagreness, smallness.<BR>—तानव-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, diminishing, causing thinness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानव्य
तानव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tanu; (the<BR>fem. is तानव्यायनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूनपात
तानूनपात तानूनपात, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तनू-<BR>नपात्), relating to Tanū-napāt, addressed to that<BR>form of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूनप्त्र
तानूनप्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. तनू-नप्तृ), a cere-<BR>mony in which Tanū-napāt is invoked and the<BR>oblation touched by the sacrificer and the priests as<BR>a form of adjuration; (अस्, ई, अम्), used or employed<BR>in this ceremony, (as clarified butter &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूर|तानूरः
तानूर तानूर, अस्, m. a whirlpool; [cf.<BR>तालूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त|तांत|तान्तः
तान्त तान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तम्), wearied,<BR>fatigued, distressed; languid, languishing; faded,<BR>withered, blighted; a mystical N. of the letter द्.<BR>—तान्त-नयन, अस्, आ, अम्, having languid or<BR>languishing eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तव|तांतव
तान्तव तान्तव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तन्तु), made<BR>of thread; (अम्), n. spinning, weaving; a web; a<BR>woven cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तव्य
तान्तव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tantu; (the<BR>fem. is तान्तव्यायनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तुवाय्य|तान्तुवाय्यः
तान्तुवाय्य, अस्, m. (fr. तन्तु-वाय), the son of<BR>a weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्र
तान्त्र तान्त्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तन्त्र; rt. 3.<BR>तन्), stringed, having wires or strings (as a musical<BR>instrument); relating to the Tantras &c.; (अम्), n.<BR>the music of a stringed instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्रिक|तांत्रिक|तान्त्रिकः
तान्त्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, completely versed in any<BR>science or system, a scholar; a philosopher; relating<BR>to the Tantras, taught or contained in them, fol-<BR>lowing them, &c.; तान्त्रिकी सञ्ज्ञा, a technical<BR>name; (अस्), m. a follower of the Tantra doctrine<BR>or mystical system of the Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्दन
तान्दन तान्दन (?), अस्, m. wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्व
तान्व तान्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तनू), Ved. be-<BR>longing to one's own body or person, personal;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic from Tanva; (अम्), n., N. of<BR>a Sāman called after Tanva; (अस्, आ, अम्), forming<BR>the warp of a web, woven, spun; (Sāy.) a cloth for<BR>filtering the Soma; (perhaps for तन्व by a metrical<BR>lengthening of the first syllable.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्वङ्ग
तान्वङ्ग, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tanv-aṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप ताप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. तप्), heat,<BR>glow, burning, torment, pain (mental or physical);<BR>fever; sorrow, affliction, distress; (ई), f., N. of the<BR>Taptī or Surat river; N. of the Yamunā or Jumnā<BR>river; [cf. पश्चात्-ताप.]<BR>—ताप-हर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>removing heat; cooling; consoling, alleviating distress;<BR>(ई), f. a dish, a sort of soup of pulse and grain, first<BR>fried with ghee and turmeric and afterwards boiled<BR>with salt and sugar.<BR>—तापी-ज or तापी-समुद्भव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, produced near or occurring near the<BR>river Taptī; pyrites or another kind of mineral<BR>substance; a kind of gem.<BR>—तापेश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚प-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—ताप्य्-उत्थ-<BR>सञ्ज्ञक, अम्, n. = ताप्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापक|तापकः
तापक, अस्, आ, अम्, heating, burning, inflaming;<BR>(अस्), m. fever, morbid heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्य|तापत्यः
तापत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Tapatī (q. v.),<BR>treating of her; a metronymic from Tapatī, epithet<BR>of Kuru, also of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन, अस्, ई, अम्, burning, inflaming, heating,<BR>distressing [cf. इन्द्र-त्˚ and चन्द्र-त्˚]; (अस्), m.<BR>the sun; the hot season; the sun-stone [cf. सूर्य-<BR>कान्त]; N. of one of the arrows of the god of<BR>love; (अम्), n. burning; distressing, chastising; a<BR>division of hell; gold; [cf. तपन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीय
तापनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. तपनीय), golden,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">Page0369-b+ 74</a>]<BR>made of gold; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a school of the<BR>Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā or White Yajur-veda.<BR>—तापनी-<BR>योपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापयान
तापयान, अस्, आ, अम्, warming, burning, illu-<BR>minating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापयिष्णु
तापयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. heating, burning,<BR>causing pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापश्चित
तापश्चित, अम्, n. (fr. तपश्-चित्), N. of a sacri-<BR>ficial ceremony of long continuance; (अस्, ई, अम्), an<BR>epithet of the sacrificial fire used at this ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस|तापसं|तापसः
तापस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तपस्), performing pe-<BR>nance, a practiser of austerities; devout; a hermit;<BR>a devotee, an ascetic; relating to religious penance<BR>or to an ascetic; (अस्), m., N. or epithet of a Hotṛ;<BR>a kind of crane, Ardea Nivea, = वक; a kind of<BR>sugar-cane; a kind of plant, = दमनक; (ई), f., N.<BR>of two plants, viz. Curcuma Zedoaria and Jaṭāmāṃsī;<BR>(अम्), n. the leaf of the Laurus Cassia, = तमाल-<BR>पत्त्र; [cf. तापस-ज.]<BR>—तापस-ज, अम्, n. the<BR>leaf of the Laurus Cassia.<BR>—तापस-तरु, उस्, m. or<BR>तापस-द्रुम, अस्, m. the tree of the ascetics,<BR>Terminalia Catappa [cf. इङ्गुद] or Putranjiva<BR>Roxburghii.<BR>—तापसद्रुम-सन्निभा, f. a kind<BR>of plant, = गर्भ-दात्री.<BR>—तापस-पत्त्री, f. the<BR>plant Artemisia Indica.<BR>—तापस-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dear to ascetics; (अस्), m. the tree Buchanania Lati-<BR>folia, = प्रियाल; (आ), f. a kind of sugar-cane; a<BR>grape; Ganitrus Sphærica; Chironia Sapida, = रुद्रा-<BR>क्ष.<BR>—तापस-वृक्ष, अस्, m. = तापस-तरु.<BR>—तापसाध्युषित (˚स-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>habited by hermits.<BR>—तापसारण्य (˚स-अर्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a wood of hermits.<BR>—तापसेष्ट (˚स-इष्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the tree Buchanania Latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस्य|तापस्यं
तापस्य, अम्, n. asceticism, the condition of a<BR>devotee, penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापायन
तापायन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school of the<BR>Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā or White Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिक
तापिक in जल-तापिक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापित
तापित, अस्, आ, अम्, heated, inflamed, distressed,<BR>pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिन्
तापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, oppressed by heat, morbid, suf-<BR>fering from disease (moral or physical); anything<BR>heated or glowing; (ई), m. one of the deified saints<BR>of the Buddhists; (इनी), f. a N. of the letter व्;<BR>[cf. जल-तापिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप्य|ताप्यं
ताप्य, अस्, अम्, m. n. or ताप्यक, अम्, n. a<BR>mineral substance, sulphuret of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिच्छ|तापिच्छः
तापिच्छ तापिच्छ or तापिञ्छ, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Xanthochymus Pictorius; [cf. तमाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिञ्ज|तापिञ्जं|तापिञ्जः
तापिञ्ज, अस्, m. the plant Xanthochymus Pictorius;<BR>(अम्), n. = तापीज, ताप्य, sulphuret of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापितट
तापितट तापितट or तीपीतट or तापीतट-<BR>देश, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापीमाहात्म्य
तापीमाहात्म्य तापी-माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a part of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताबरिसाणु
ताबरिसाणु ताबरिसाणु, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताबुव
ताबुव ताबुव, अम्, n., Ved. an antidote<BR>against poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम|तामः
ताम ताम, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तम्), an object of<BR>terror; fault, defect, vice; anxiety, distress, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामर|तामरं
तामर तामर, अम्, n. water; ghee or<BR>oiled butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरस|तामरसं
तामरस तामरस, अम्, n. a red-coloured<BR>lotus; gold; copper [cf. ताम्र]; a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of twelve syllables each; (अस्), m. a<BR>kind of crane, Ardea Sibirica; (ई), f. a lotus pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामलकी
तामलकी तामलकी, f. the tree Flacourtia<BR>Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामलिप्त|तामलिप्तं
तामलिप्त तामलिप्त, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people in the south of Bengal; (अम्, ई), n. f., N. of<BR>the city and district inhabited by this people, the<BR>modern Tumlook or Tamoluk in the district of<BR>Midnapore; (also called तमोलिप्ती, ताम्रलिप्त, दा-<BR>मलिप्त; cf. also तमालिका and तमालिनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामस|तामसं|तामसः
तामस तामस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तमस्), dark,<BR>of or belonging to darkness; affected by or apper-<BR>taining to the third quality or that of darkness (vice,<BR>ignorance, &c.); ignorant, vicious, malignant; relating<BR>to Manu Tāmasa; (अस्), m. a malignant or mis-<BR>chievous person, a villain, an incendiary; a snake;<BR>an owl; N. of the fourth Manu; N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Śiva; (ई), f. night; sleep; an epithet<BR>of Durgā; N. of a river, = जटामांसी (in this sense<BR>a wrong reading for तापसी); (अम्), n. darkness<BR>[cf. अन्ध-तामस]; तामसी तनूस्, the form as-<BR>sumed by the Deity for the destruction of the world;<BR>तामसी शक्तिस्, the faculty of Tamas.<BR>—तामस-<BR>कीलक, अस्, m., N. of certain astronomical Ketus.<BR>—तामस-गुण, अस्, m. the quality of darkness;<BR>see गुण.<BR>—तामस-लीन, अस्, आ, अम्, (in the<BR>Sāṅkhya phil.) one of the forms of अ-तुष्टि, dissatis-<BR>faction.<BR>—तामस-वन, अम्, n. ‘the dark wood,’<BR>N. of a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसिक|तामसिकं
तामसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, dark, obscure, of or be-<BR>longing to the quality of darkness, derived from it,<BR>teaching lessons so characterized, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामि|तामिः
तामि तामि, इस् or ई, f. (fr. rt. तम्), restrain-<BR>ing or keeping in the breath until it produces ex-<BR>haustion; (also said to = तमी, night.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिस्र|तामिस्रं|तामिस्रः
तामिस्र तामिस्र (fr. तमिस्र), scil. पक्ष,<BR>the dark half of the month, the time from full moon<BR>to new moon; (अस्), m. a Rākṣasa (as going about<BR>in the dark); indignation at being disappointed or<BR>slighted, anger, one of the five forms of Avidyā in<BR>the Sāṅkhya system; a division of hell, that of<BR>deep gloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामु
तामु तामु, उस्, m., Ved. a praiser; (a various<BR>reading has स्तामु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बली
ताम्बली ताम्बली, f., N. of a kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूल|तांबूल|तांबूलं|ताम्बूलं
ताम्बूल ताम्बूल, अम्, ई, n. f. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. तम्), betel, Piper Betel, or rather its pungent<BR>and aromatic leaf, which together with the areca-nut<BR>and catechu and sometimes caustic lime and spices<BR>is eaten or chewed very generally by the natives of<BR>the east, acting as a carminative and antacid tonic.<BR>It is called Pān (fr. पर्ण, ‘a leaf,’ the name<BR>betel being connected with वीटिका, q. v.), and is pre-<BR>sented to guests and visitors, and sometimes sent to<BR>relations and friends at family festivals, inclosed in<BR>gold or silver paper; (अम्), n. the areca-nut; (अस्),<BR>m. Bengal Śaṇa or Crotolaria Juncea.<BR>—ताम्बूल-<BR>करङ्क, अस्, m. the Pān-dān or betel-box, (this box<BR>generally resembling a Karaṅka or hollowed cocoa-<BR>nut.)<BR>—ताम्बूल-द or ताम्बूल-दायक or ताम्-<BR>बूल-धर, अस्, m. the betel-bearer (who attended<BR>on kings and great men).<BR>—ताम्बूल-पत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. betel-leaf; (अस्), m. the Dioscorea Globosa; [cf.<BR>पिण्डालु.]<BR>—ताम्बूल-पेटिका, f. a betel-box.<BR>—ताम्-<BR>बूल-भक्षण, अम्, n. the eating of betel-leaf.<BR>—ताम्बूल-राग, अस्, m. a kind of pulse, Ervum<BR>lens.<BR>—ताम्बूल-वल्लिका or ताम्बूल-वल्ली, f. the<BR>betel plant (Piper Betel) bearing a pungent leaf;<BR>see above.<BR>—ताम्बूल-वाहक, अस्, m. or ताम्बूल-<BR>वाहिन्, ई, m. a betel-bearer, a servant attached to<BR>men of rank to prepare the Pān and carry the betel-<BR>box.<BR>—ताम्बूलाक्त (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, smeared<BR>with the juice of chewed betel.<BR>—ताम्बूलाधिकार<BR>(˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, m. the office of carrying the betel-<BR>box for persons of rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|तांबूलिकः|ताम्बूलिकः
ताम्बूलिक, अस्, m. a seller of betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिन्|तांबूलिन्
ताम्बूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, relating or belonging to betel,<BR>having betel, giving it, &c.; (ई), m. the Pān-bearer,<BR>a servant who prepares and furnishes the Pān; a<BR>seller of betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्य
ताम्य ताम्य, अम्, n. (?) = क्लोमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्यत्
ताम्यत् ताम्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. rt. तम्),<BR>distressing, afflicting, annoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र ताम्र, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तम्), of a coppery red colour, (ताम्रा त्वच्, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-a" target="_blank">Page0370-a+ 81</a>]<BR>fourth of the seven skins or membranes with which an<BR>embryo is covered); (अस्), m. a kind of leprosy with<BR>large red spots; N. of a man [cf. ताम्रायण]; N.<BR>of an island [cf. ताम्र-द्वीप]; (आ), f., N. of several<BR>plants, viz. = मञ्जिष्ठा, Rubia Munjista, = रक्त-<BR>गुञ्जा, Abrus Precatorius, = सैंहली; N. of a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa, one of the wives of Kaśyapa,<BR>and mother of various birds; N. of a river; (अम्),<BR>n. a dark or coppery red; copper; a kind of sandal,<BR>represented as of a dark-red colour and smelling like<BR>a lotus; Ved. form, figure; (अस्, ई, अम्), made of<BR>copper; (ई), f. a copper or metallic cup of prescribed<BR>capacity and perforated by a small hole at the bottom,<BR>(when placed in a vessel of water it answers the<BR>purpose of a clepsydra, and the water gradually filling<BR>it marks the time that has elapsed); [cf. Hib. umha,<BR>‘copper.’]<BR>—ताम्र-कण्टक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a kind of Acacia.<BR>—ताम्र-कर्णी, f., N. of the<BR>female of one of the elephants of the quarters called<BR>Añjana; also of the elephant Śeṣa.<BR>—ताम्र-कार,<BR>अस्, m. a brazier, a copper-smith.<BR>—ताम्र-किलि, इस्,<BR>m. a small worm of a red colour; [cf. ताम्र-कृमि.]<BR>—ताम्र-कुट्ट, अस्, ई, m. f. a brazier or copper-<BR>smith.<BR>—ताम्र-कुट्टक, अस्, m. = the last; tobacco (?).<BR>—ताम्र-कुण्ड, अम्, n. a copper bason or other<BR>vessel; probably N. of a place.<BR>—ताम्र-कूट, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a kind of plant, tobacco (?).<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>कृमि, इस्, m. the lady-bird; cochineal.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>गर्भ, अम्, n. blue vitriol or sulphate of copper.<BR>—ताम्र-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. a kind of pigeon.<BR>—ताम्र-चूड, अस्, आ, अम्, red-crested; (अस्),<BR>m. a cock [cf. ताम्र-शिखिन्]; a kind of plant<BR>(कुक्कुर-द्रु); a particular position of the hand<BR>[cf. ताम्रचूडक]; N. of a Pari-vrājaka; (आ),<BR>f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—ताम्रचूडक, अस्, m. (scil. हस्त), a kind of<BR>theatrical gesticulation or motion of the hands.<BR>—ताम्रचूड-भैरव, अस्, m. a peculiar form of<BR>Bhairava.<BR>—ताम्रचूडादि-कथन (˚ड-आद्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘explanation of the Tāmra-cūḍa gesticulation<BR>&c.,’ N. of a section of the Mantra-mahodadhi by<BR>Mahī-dhara.<BR>—ताम्रजाक्ष (˚ज-अक्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a son of Kṛṣṇa and Satya-bhāmā.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>तनु, उस्, उस्, उ, having a ruddy or fair complexion,<BR>copper-coloured.<BR>—ताम्र-तुण्ड, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>monkey.<BR>—ताम्र-त्रपुज, brass.<BR>—ताम्र-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. dark-red or copper colour, redness.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>दुग्धा, f. a species of plant, = गोरक्ष-दुग्धा.<BR>—ताम्र-द्रु, उस्, m. red sandal-wood.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>द्वीप, अस्, m. the island Ceylon.<BR>—ताम्र-धातु,<BR>उस्, m. red chalk.<BR>—ताम्र-धूम्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. dark-red, coppery red.<BR>—ताम्र-ध्वज, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—ताम्र-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, red-<BR>eyed.<BR>—ताम्र-पक्षा, f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—ताम्र-पक्षिन्, ई, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—ताम्र-पट्ट, अस्, m. a copper plate on<BR>which Hindū grants of land &c. are frequently in-<BR>scribed; [cf. ताम्र-शासन.]<BR>—ताम्र-पत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. a copper plate; (अस्), m. a kind of pot-herb,<BR>= जीव-शाक.<BR>—ताम्र-पत्त्रक, N. of the two<BR>plants Bauhinia Tomentosa and Capparis Aphylla.<BR>—ताम्र-पर्ण, अम्, n., N. of a district renowned<BR>for a temple of Śiva, the ancient Taprobane; Ceylon;<BR>(ई), f. the plant Rubia Munjista (मञ्जिष्ठा);<BR>a kind of pond or lake; N. of a river rising in<BR>Malaya and of the district in its vicinity, (the river is<BR>celebrated for its pearls); N. of a town in Ceylon,<BR>after which the whole island is by some called<BR>Tāmra-parṇī; [cf. ताम्र-द्वीप.]<BR>—ताम्रपर्-<BR>णीय, अस्, m. (fr. the last), an inhabitant of Ceylon,<BR>especially a Buddhist.<BR>—ताम्र-पल्लव, अस्, m. the<BR>Aśoka tree.<BR>—ताम्र-पाकिन्, ई, m. the tree Thes-<BR>pesia Populneoides and Hibiscus Populneoides.<BR>—ता-<BR>म्र-पात्र, अम्, n. a copper vessel.<BR>—ताम्र-पादी,<BR>f. a kind of plant related to the Mimosa Pudica,<BR>= हंस-पदी.<BR>—ताम्र-पुष्प, अम्, n. a copper-<BR>coloured or red flower; (अस्), m. the plant Bauhinia<BR>Variegata or a kind of ebony (रक्त-काञ्चन);<BR>another plant, Kæmpferia Rotunda (भूमि-चम्-<BR>पक); (ई), f., N. of several plants having red<BR>flowers, viz. Bignonia Suaveolens, Grislea Tomentosa,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">Page0370-b+ 79</a>]<BR>Ipomœa Turpethum (त्रि-वृत्); [cf. ताम्र-पुष्-<BR>पिका.]<BR>—ताम्र-पुष्पक, अस्, m. Bauhinia Varie-<BR>gata or a kind of ebony; (इका), f., N. of several<BR>plants, viz. = Bignonia Suaveolens, Grislea Tomentosa,<BR>also = Marāthī रक्त-निशोत्तरा.<BR>—ताम्र-फल,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Alangium Hexapetalum.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>फलक, अम्, n. a copper plate.<BR>—ताम्र-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of copper, coppery.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>मारण, अम्, n. the decomposition of copper and<BR>its application as a remedy.<BR>—ताम्र-मुख, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, copper-faced, fair-complexioned; (अस्), m. a<BR>European.<BR>—ताम्र-मूला and ई, f., N. of several<BR>plants, Rubia Munjista, Alhagi Maurorum, Mimosa<BR>Pudica.<BR>—ताम्र-मृग, अस्, m. the red deer.<BR>—ताम्र-रसायनी, f. a species of plant with a<BR>milky juice, = ताम्र-दुग्धा.<BR>—ताम्र-लिप्त, आस्,<BR>m. pl., N. of a people near the western mouth of<BR>the Ganges; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi; (आ or ई), f.,<BR>N. of the capital of the Tāmra-liptas; [cf. ताम-<BR>लिप्ती.]<BR>—ताम्रलिप्तक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>near the western mouth of the Ganges; (इका), f.,<BR>N. of the capital of this people, = ताम्र-लिप्ता.<BR>—ताम्र-वर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, copper-coloured, dark-<BR>red; (अस्), m. a kind of grass, = पल्लिवाह; N. of<BR>one of the nine divisions of Bhārata-varṣa; (आ), f.<BR>the China rose; (ई), f. the blossom of sesamum.<BR>—ताम्र-वर्णक, अस्, m. = ताम्र-वर्ण.<BR>—ता-<BR>म्र-वल्ली, f. the plant Rubia Munjista; a medi-<BR>cinal plant used as an emollient in affections of<BR>the mouth and fauces; also called तमाली, ताली,<BR>सूक्ष्म-वल्ली, &c.<BR>—ताम्र-वीज, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of vetch, Dolichos Uniflorus (कुलत्थ).<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. the plant Dolichos Uniflorus; a red<BR>sort of sandal-wood.<BR>—ताम्र-वृन्त, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Dolichos Uniflorus; (आ), f. another kind of Dolichos.<BR>—ताम्र-शाटीय, आस्, m. pl. ‘having red vestments,’<BR>N. of a Buddhist school.<BR>—ताम्र-शासन, अम्, n.<BR>an edict or grant &c. inscribed on copper; [cf. ताम्र-<BR>पट्ट.]<BR>—ताम्र-शिखिन्, ई, m. ‘having a red crest,’<BR>a cock; [cf. ताम्र-चूड.]<BR>—ताम्र-सागर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an ocean.<BR>—ताम्र-सार, अम्, n. a red kind<BR>of sandal, Pterospermum Santolinum.<BR>—ताम्र-<BR>सारक, अस्, m. a sort of Khadira with red flowers;<BR>(अम्), n. red sandal-wood.<BR>—ताम्र-सेन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—ताम्राख (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>red-eyed; (अस्), m. a crow; the Indian cuckoo.<BR>—ताम्राख्य (˚र-आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, N. of a kind<BR>of pearl, so called either because reddish in colour or<BR>because found in the river Tāmra-parṇī.<BR>—ताम्राभ<BR>(˚र-आभ्˚), अम्, n. red saunders.<BR>—ताम्रारि (˚र-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. ‘the copper-coloured enemy,’ N. of a<BR>hostile people.<BR>—ताम्रारुण (˚र-अर्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>coppery red dawn; (आ), f., N. of a river; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—ताम्रार्ध (˚र-अर्˚), अम्, n.<BR>mixed or bell-metal.<BR>—ताम्रा-वती, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—ताम्रोपजीविन् (˚र-उप्˚), ई, m. a copper-<BR>smith.<BR>—ताम्रोष्ठ and ताम्रौष्ठ (˚र-ओष्˚),<BR>औ, m. du. red lips; (अस्, आ, अम्), having red lips;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Yakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0369-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रक|ताम्रकं
ताम्रक, अम्, n. copper; (इका), f. = ताम्री, the<BR>plant Abrus Precatorius, = गुञ्जा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रायण
ताम्रायण, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Yājñavalkya;<BR>(also read ताम्रायणि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिक|ताम्रिकः
ताम्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, coppery, made of copper,<BR>&c.; (अस्), m. a brazier, a copper-smith; (for ता-<BR>म्रिका see ताम्रक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिमन्
ताम्रिमन्, आ, m. redness, dark-red, copper colour,<BR>the colour of copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रीकृ
ताम्री-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to die red or a dark-red or coppery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र्य
ताम्र्य, अम्, n. a dark-red colour, redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राकु|ताम्राकुः
ताम्राकु ताम्राकु, उस्, m., N. of an Upa-<BR>dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताय्
ताय् ताय् [cf. rt. 3. तन्, त्रै, तय्], cl. 1.<BR>A. तायते, तताये, तायिष्यते, अतायि<BR>and अतायिष्ट, तायितुम्, to spread, extend, proceed<BR>in a continuous stream or line; to cherish, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायन|तायनं
तायन, अम्, n. proceeding or succeeding well;<BR>increase, growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताय
ताय ताय, ? in Gaṇa to Pāṇ. VI. 1, 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायादर
तायादर तायादर, ? Atharva-veda VI. 72, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायिक|तायिकः
तायिक तायिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a country;<BR>the inhabitants of this country, = तर्जिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायु|तायुः
तायु तायु, उस्, m. [cf. स्तायु; Gr. τητάω],<BR>Ved. a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार|तारं|तारः
तार तार, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तॄ, or in the<BR>senses ‘shining,’ ‘star,’ &c., for स्तार fr. rt. स्तृ,<BR>to scatter rays of light, or according to others fr. rt.<BR>2. अस्, cf. अस्त्र), all-pervading, all-conquering, a<BR>protector; an epithet of Rudra and Viṣṇu; high<BR>(as a note in music), soprano; loud, shrill; a loud<BR>or shrill note, a high tone or note (in music); shin-<BR>ing, radiant, radiating; clean, clear; good, excellent,<BR>well flavoured, &c.; (अस्), m. descent to a river, a<BR>bank [cf. तीर and तीर्थ]; crossing, passing over,<BR>&c.; the clearness or transparency of a pearl, a clear<BR>or beautiful pearl; the (saving) mystical syllable ॐ<BR>(प्रणव); a mystical monosyllable in the Tantras;<BR>N. of a Daitya slain by Viṣṇu; N. of one of Rāma's<BR>monkey generals, who was a son of Bṛhas-pati, and<BR>whose wife is called Tārā; N. of Maṇi-rāma, a<BR>commentator on the Bhāminī-vilāsa; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>m. f. n. a star in general, a fixed star, asterism, &c.<BR>[cf. तृ and स्तृ]; (आ), f. a star, planet, a kind of meteor,<BR>perhaps a falling star; the pupil of the eye, (according<BR>to some also m. and n.); N. of one of the eight<BR>Siddhis in the Sāṅkhya phil.; a kind of perfume;<BR>N. of the wife of Bṛhas-pati who was carried off by<BR>Soma; of a form of Dākṣāyaṇī worshipped on the<BR>mountain Kiṣkindha, protectress of the Gṛtsa-madas;<BR>of the wife of Buddha Amogha-siddha; of one<BR>of the Jaina Śaktis; of a female monkey in the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa, daughter of Su-ṣeṇa, wife of Bālin and<BR>mother of Aṅgada; N. of the wife of Tāra; (अम्),<BR>n. silver; (अस्, अम्), m. n. camphor; (अम्, आ),<BR>n. f. a pearl; [cf. Zend śtārĕ; Gr. ἀστήρ, ἄστρον;<BR>Goth. stairno; Lat. aster, astrum, stella for ste-<BR>rula.]<BR>—तार-ज, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a kind of<BR>mineral substance.<BR>—तार-तण्डुल, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Sorghum (धवल-यावनाल).<BR>—तार-तम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very loud.<BR>—तार-तार, अम्, n., N. of one of the<BR>eight Siddhis in the Sāṅkhya phil.; [cf. तार and<BR>तारा.]<BR>—तार-नाथ, अस्, m. (for तारा-न्˚), N. of a<BR>renowned Tibetian who lived in the beginning of the<BR>seventeenth century and wrote a history of Buddhism.<BR>—तार-नाद, अस्, m. a loud or shrill sound or cry.<BR>—तार-पतन, अम्, n. the falling of a meteor, a<BR>falling star.<BR>—तार-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a lexico-<BR>grapher.<BR>—तार-पुष्प, अस्, m. jasmine.<BR>—तार-<BR>माक्षिक, अम्, n. a kind of mineral substance, =<BR>तार-ज.<BR>—तार-मूल and तार-मूलक, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—तार-विमला, f. a sort of mineral<BR>said to be of the colour of silver.<BR>—तार-शुद्धि-<BR>कर, अम्, n. (‘what refines silver’), lead.<BR>—तार-<BR>सार, अस्, m., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—तार-स्वर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a loud or shrill sound.<BR>—तारा-<BR>कवच, अम्, n., N. of a chapter in the Tantra-sāra<BR>by Kṛṣṇānanda; see कवच.<BR>—तारा-कारुण्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the compassion of Tārā,’ N. of a chapter in<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—ताराक्ष (˚रा-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>star-eyed, one whose eyes are stars; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a Daitya, = तारकाक्ष, uncle of Dhūmrākṣa and<BR>king of the Niṣadhas.<BR>—तारा-ग्रह, ‘star-planet,’<BR>i. e. one of the five lesser planets exclusive of the<BR>sun and moon.<BR>—तारा-चक्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>mystical circle.<BR>—तारा-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>scholiast and of a king.<BR>—तारा-च्छाय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>reflecting the stars.<BR>—ताराधिप, अस्, m. or तारा-<BR>धिपति (˚रा-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘ruler of the stars,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—ताराधीश (˚रा-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a prince.<BR>—तारा-पज्झटिका, f., N. of a hymn<BR>written by Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—तारा-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the stars,’ the moon; a N. of Bṛhas-pati as<BR>husband of Tārā; N. of Śiva; of the monkey Bālin;<BR>of a prince.<BR>—तारा-पथ, अस्, m. the path of the<BR>stars, the atmosphere, the firmament, heaven or<BR>sky; N. of a country.<BR>—तारापहरण (˚रा-अप्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-a" target="_blank">Page0371-a+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n., N. of a chapter in the Brahmavaivarta-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—तारापीड (˚रा-आप्˚), अस्, m. the moon<BR>(‘having a chaplet of stars’); N. of several princes.<BR>—तारा-प्रमाण, अम्, n. sidereal measure,<BR>sidereal time.<BR>—ताराभ (˚र or ˚रा-आभ), अस्,<BR>m. quicksilver, (‘looking like silver or bright as the<BR>stars.’)<BR>—तारा-भूषा, f. ‘decorated with stars,’ an<BR>epithet of the night.<BR>—ताराभ्र (˚रा-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. camphor.<BR>—तारा-मण्डल, अम्, n. the starry<BR>region, the sphere of the stars, the zodiac; the<BR>pupil of the eye; (अस्), m. a Śiva temple of a par-<BR>ticular form or decorated in a peculiar manner.<BR>—तारा-मन्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a chapter in the<BR>Mantra-mahodadhi.<BR>—तारा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of stars.<BR>—तारा-मृग, अस्, m. the star-<BR>antelope, the Nakṣatra Mṛga-śīrṣa.<BR>—तारारि (˚र-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. a pyritic ore of iron; see विड्-माक्षिक.<BR>—तारा-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, star-shaped, star-like.<BR>—तारा-वती, f., N. of a form of Durgā; of a<BR>daughter of Kakut-stha and Mano-māthinī, wife of<BR>king Candra-śekhara; of the wife of Dharma-dhvaja,<BR>who was a king of Kāñcana-pura.<BR>—तारा-वर्ष,<BR>अम्, n. ‘star-rain,’ falling stars.<BR>—तारावली (˚रा-<BR>आव्˚), f., N. of a daughter of the Yakṣa prince<BR>Maṇi-bhadra.<BR>—तारा-वाक्य, अम्, n. ‘the speech of<BR>Tārā,’ N. of a chapter in the fourth book of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—तारा-विलाप, अस्, m. ‘the lamentation<BR>of Tārā,’ N. of a chapter in the fourth book of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—तारा-स्थान, अम्, n. the place in the<BR>gamut for the treble notes, those of the higher<BR>octave.<BR>—तारेन्द्र (˚रा-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘the prince<BR>of the stars,’ N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0370-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारक|तारकं|तारकः
तारक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who causes or enables<BR>to pass or go over, carrying over; rescuing; one<BR>who helps another through a difficulty &c.; a pro-<BR>tector, a preserver (e. g. तारकम् ब्रह्म, ‘the<BR>saving prayer,’ N. of a particular prayer which saves<BR>or liberates); belonging to the stars; (अस्), m. a pilot,<BR>a helmsman or steersman; a N. of Śiva; N. of<BR>a Daitya conquered by Indra with the assistance of<BR>Kārttikeya or Skanda; (Tāraka is also enumerated<BR>among the nine enemies of Viṣṇu); N. of a friend<BR>of Sīmanta; (आस्), m. pl. the children of Tāraka; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. a float, a raft; (अका), f. a star; a meteor,<BR>a falling star. &c., (with Jainas constituting one of<BR>the five divisions of the Jyotiṣkas); a sort of colo-<BR>quintida; N. of a daughter of Sunda; of the wife of<BR>Bṛhas-pati, usually called Tārā; also = लघु-वृन्-<BR>दावन; (इका), f. the juice of palms, = ताल-रस,<BR>commonly ताडी; (आ, अम्), f. n. the pupil of the<BR>eye; the eye; (अम्), n., N. of a metre of four lines<BR>of thirteen syllables each.<BR>—तारक-जय, अस्, m.<BR>‘conquest of Tāraka,’ N. of a chapter in the Padma-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—तारक-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of Tāraka,’<BR>epithet of Skanda.<BR>—तारक-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR>—तारक-वध, अस्, m. ‘the killing of<BR>Tāraka,’ N. of a chapter in the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—ता-<BR>रकाक्ष (˚का-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having stars for<BR>eyes; (अस्), m., N. of a Daitya, a son of Tāraka.<BR>—तारकाख्य (˚क-आख्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Daitya,<BR>a son of Tāraka.<BR>—तारकान्तक (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘destroying Tāraka,’ an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—ता-<BR>रका-मय, अस्, ई, अम् (तारका = तारा), on account<BR>of Tārā, by reason of Tārā, (generally used as an<BR>epithet of either Saṅgrāma or Yuddha or Samara,<BR>i. e. the war waged by gods and demons for the<BR>rescue of Tārā, the wife of Bṛhas-pati, who had<BR>been carried off by Soma); a N. of Śiva, as taking<BR>part in that fight.<BR>—तारका-मान, अम्, n. sidereal<BR>measure, sidereal time.<BR>—तारकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. ‘the enemy of Tāraka,’ an epithet of Skanda.<BR>—तारकोपनिषद् (˚क-उप्˚), त्, f. ‘the saving or<BR>liberating Upaniṣad,’ N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकायण
तारकायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tāraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकित|तारकितं
तारकित, अस्, आ, अम्, starry, star-spangled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकिन्
तारकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, starry; (इणी), f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारण|तारणः
तारण, अस्, ई, अम्, who or what causes or enables<BR>to cross; helping over a difficulty &c.; liberating,<BR>saving; (अस्), m. a N. of Śiva and of Viṣṇu; a<BR>raft, a float; (अम्), n. crossing, reaching the opposite<BR>shore, safe passage; conquering; carrying or con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">Page0371-b+ 74</a>]<BR>veying across, the act of saving or liberating; a sort<BR>of sacrificial vessel (?); N. of a Sāman; N. of the<BR>third year of the fourth Jupiter cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारणि|तारणिः
तारणि, इस्, f. = तरणि, a boat, ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारणेय|तारणेयः
तारणेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of Yāja and<BR>Upa-yāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारयितृ
तारयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a liberator, promoter,<BR>promoting, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारायण|तारायणः
तारायण, अस्, m. the tree of salvation, the holy<BR>fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिक|तारिकं
तारिक, अम्, n. fare, freight, toll for passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिका
तारिका, f. See under तारक, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारित
तारित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to cross, conveyed<BR>across, saved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिन्
तारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, enabling or causing to get over<BR>or across, saving; (इणी), f. a form of Durgā, =<BR>द्वितीया शक्तिः; N. of a kind of goddess with<BR>Buddhists.<BR>—तारिणी-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a section<BR>of the Śakti-ratnākara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारेय|तारेयः
तारेय, अस्, m. a metronymic of the monkey<BR>Aṅgada; [cf. तारा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्य|तार्य्य
तार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be crossed, passable, to be<BR>carried across, to be ferried over, to be conquered or<BR>defeated; (अम्), n. fare, freight, toll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारक्षति
तारक्षति तारक्षति, तारक्षिति, and तिरि-<BR>क्षति, N. of a district to the west of Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारतम्य|तारतम्यं
तारतम्य तारतम्य, अम्, n. (an abstract<BR>noun from तर+तम, the affixes of the compara-<BR>tive and superlative degrees), gradation, proportion,<BR>the state or condition of more or less; dependance<BR>of larger numbers on smaller in a progressive series;<BR>(एन), ind. in different degrees, in various gradations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारदी
तारदी तारदी, f. a kind of plant, = तरदी;<BR>also read तारटी (तरटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारल|तारलः
तारल तारल, अस्, ई, अम् (= तरल), un-<BR>steady; libidinous, dissipated, a lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारल्य|तारल्यं
तारल्य, अम्, n. tremulousness, unsteadiness, libi-<BR>dinousness, wantonness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराज्
ताराज् ता-राज्, ट्, f., N. of a kind of Virāj<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिक|तारिकं
तारिक तारिक, तारिन्. See under तार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारीष
तारीष तारीष, an incorrect form for ता-<BR>वीष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुक्षायणि
तारुक्षायणि तारुक्षायणि, a patronymic<BR>from Tarukṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुक्ष्य
तारुक्ष्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tarukṣa;<BR>(the fem. is तारुक्ष्यायणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण
तारुण तारुण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तरुण), youth-<BR>ful, young, adolescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण्य|तारुण्यं
तारुण्य, अम्, n. youth, youthfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्कव|तार्क्कव
तार्कव तार्कव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तर्कु), spun,<BR>woven, made with a spindle, belonging to a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्किक|तार्किकः|तार्क्किक
तार्किक तार्किक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तर्क), re-<BR>lated or belonging to the science of reasoning or<BR>logic, belonging to philosophy; (अस्), m. a dialecti-<BR>cian, a logician, a philosopher, a sophist, a follower<BR>of one of the six schools of Hindū philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष|तार्क्षः
तार्क्ष तार्क्ष, अस्, m. a kind of bird; a<BR>kind of plant; a N. of Kaśyapa; a wrong reading<BR>for तार्क्ष्य, i. e. Garuḍa; (ई), f. a sort of creeping<BR>plant, = पाताल-गरुडी.<BR>—तार्क्ष-ज = तार्क्ष्य-<BR>ज, q. v.<BR>—तार्क्ष-पुत्र or तार्क्ष-सुत, अस्, m.<BR>‘the son of Tārkṣa or Kaśyapa,’ i. e. Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्षाक
तार्क्षाक, a patronymic from Tṛkṣāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्य|तार्क्ष्यं|तार्क्ष्यः
तार्क्ष्य, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. तृक्ष), N.<BR>of a mythical being, described either as a horse or<BR>bird, and originally one of the personifications of the<BR>sun, which was represented under these forms; (the<BR>most ancient representation seems to have been that<BR>of the horse: in Mahā-bh. 1. 2548, Tārkṣya,<BR>Ariṣṭa-nemi, Garuḍa, Aruṇa, and Āruṇī are described<BR>as children of Kaśyapa and Vinatā; Tārkṣya is also<BR>called Garuḍāgra-ja, the elder brother of Garuḍa: in<BR>Mahā-bh. III. 12660, mention is made of a Muni<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">Page0371-c+ 77</a>]<BR>called Ariṣṭa-nemi Tārkṣya, but in the epic and<BR>later literature Tārkṣya is generally identified with<BR>Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of Viṣṇu and destroyer<BR>of the race of snakes); a N. of Garuḍa; a N. of<BR>Śiva; a Vedic hymn supposed to be composed by<BR>Ariṣṭa-nemi Tārkṣya; a horse in general; a car,<BR>a chariot; a bird in general; N. of a race; a snake;<BR>the tree Vatica Robusta [cf. तार्क्ष्य-प्रसव]; a<BR>sort of antidote; gold; (ई), f. a wild creeper; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of drug; a sort of collyrium.<BR>—तार्क्ष्य-<BR>ज and तार्क्ष-ज, अम्, n. a sort of collyrium.<BR>—तार्क्ष्य-ध्वज, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>(whose symbol is Garuḍa).<BR>—तार्क्ष्य-नायक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the leader or chief of the birds,’ an epithet<BR>of Garuḍa.<BR>—तार्क्ष्य-नाशक, अस्, m. ‘destroyer<BR>of birds,’ the bird Falco Calidus.<BR>—तार्क्ष्य-प्र-<BR>सव, अस्, m. the tree Vatica Robusta; [cf. अश्व-<BR>कर्ण and तार्क्ष्य.]<BR>—तार्क्ष्य-शैल, अम्, n.<BR>a substance prepared from the calx of brass or from<BR>the Amomum Anthorrhiza, and used as a medical<BR>application to the eyes; [cf. रसाञ्जन.]<BR>—तार्-<BR>क्ष्य-सामन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यायण
तार्क्ष्यायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tār-<BR>kṣya.<BR>—तार्क्ष्यायण-भक्त, अम्, n. the district<BR>inhabited by the Tārkṣyāyaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्ण|तार्णः
तार्ण तार्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तृण), made of<BR>grass; levied from grass (as a tax); (अस्, ई), m. f. a<BR>patronymic from Tṛṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्णक
तार्णक, अस्, ई, अम्, an adjective derived from<BR>Tṛṇakīyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्णकर्ण
तार्णकर्ण, a patronymic from Tṛṇa-karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्णविन्दवीय
तार्णविन्दवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, sacred to Tṛṇa-<BR>vindu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्णायन
तार्णायन, a patronymic from Tṛṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्तीय|तार्त्तीय
तार्तीय तार्तीय, अस्, आ or ई (?), अम् (fr. तृतीय),<BR>belonging to the third; the third; (अम्), n. a third<BR>part.<BR>—तार्तीयसवन or तार्तीयसवनिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. तृतीय-सवन), belonging to the third<BR>Savana; [cf. त्रि-षवण.]<BR>—तार्तीयाह्निक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. तृतीय+अहन्), belonging to the third day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्तीयक
तार्तीयक, belonging to the third, third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्तीयीक|तार्त्तीयीक
तार्तीयीक, अस्, आ, अम्, the third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्प्य
तार्प्य तार्प्य, अम्, n., Ved. a garment made<BR>of a particular vegetable substance; (according to<BR>Sāy. derived fr. तृपा, a kind of plant.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्य|तार्य्य
तार्य तार्य. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्ष्टाघ
तार्ष्टाघ तार्ष्टाघ, अस्, m. (fr. तृष्टाघ ?),<BR>a kind of tree; (अस्, ई, अम्), coming from or be-<BR>longing to this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताल|तालं|तालः
ताल ताल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तड् or तल्), the<BR>palmyra-tree or fan-palm, Borassus Flabelliformis,<BR>from the juice of which a sort of sugar or by fer-<BR>mentation a spirituous liquor is prepared; a measure<BR>of height (i. e. the palm-tree so considered, e. g.<BR>प्रासादो बहु-ताल-समुत्सेधः, a palace many<BR>palm-trees in height); a banner formed of the palm<BR>[cf. ताल-केतु, ताल-ध्वज, ताल-भृत्, ताल-लक्ष्-<BR>मन्, तालाङ्क]; slapping or clapping the hands<BR>together or against the opposite arm; clapping or<BR>flapping in general; the flapping of the ears of an<BR>elephant; beating time in music, musical time or<BR>measure; a musical instrument of bell-metal or brass,<BR>a sort of cymbal played with a stick; (in prosody) a<BR>trochee; an epithet of Śiva [cf. तल]; a short span,<BR>one measured by the thumb and middle finger; the<BR>open hand with the fingers extended, the palm; the<BR>hilt of a sword or sacrificial knife; a lock, a bolt;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people [cf. अपर-ताल and<BR>ताल-वन]; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a division of hell [cf.<BR>तल]; = हरिताल, yellow orpiment; (ई), f. the tree<BR>Corypha Taliera; a species of the mountain-palm;<BR>Corypha Umbraculifera; Flacourtia Cataphracta; Cur-<BR>culigo Orchioides; the spirituous juice of the palm,<BR>the common toddy; a fragrant earth, = तुवरी; a<BR>sort of key or instrument for opening a door, =<BR>प्रति-ताली; a sort of metre consisting of four lines of<BR>three long syllables each; (अम्), n. the fruit or nut of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-a" target="_blank">Page0372-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the palmyra-palm; orpiment; the throne of Durgā<BR>[cf. मनस्-ताल]; (अस्, ई, अम्), made of the palmyra-<BR>tree or of the palm-wood; [cf. उच्च-ताल, उत्-त्˚, एक-त्˚,<BR>कर-त्˚, काम-त्˚, क्रोश-त्˚, &c.]<BR>—ताल-केतु, उस्, m.<BR>‘having the palm-tree as a banner,’ an epithet of<BR>Bhīṣma; N. of an adversary of Kṛṣṇa, slain by the<BR>latter; N. of a Dānava who was a younger brother of<BR>Pātāla-ketu.<BR>—ताल-क्षीर, अम्, n. an extract, =<BR>तवक्षीर.<BR>—ताल-क्षीरक, अम्, n. the exuda-<BR>tion of the palm.<BR>—ताल-गर्भ, अस् or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?), the fermented exudation of the palm-tree.<BR>—ताल-चर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—ताल-<BR>जङ्घ, अस्, आ, अम्, having legs as long as a palm-<BR>tree; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe; (अस्), m.<BR>the prince of this tribe; N. of the ancestor of the<BR>Tāla-jaṅghas who was a descendant of Śaryāti; N.<BR>of a son of Jaya-dhvaja; of a Rakṣas; of a<BR>Daitya.<BR>—ताल-जटा, f. the fibres of the palm-tree<BR>under the outer bark.<BR>—ताल-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing the palm-tree as a banner,’ a N. of Bala-rāma<BR>[cf. ताल-भृत्, ताल-लक्ष्मन्, तालाङ्क]; N. of a<BR>mountain; (आ), f., N. of a town; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—ताल-नवमी, f. the ninth day of the light<BR>half of the month Bhādra, sacred to Durgā.<BR>—ताल-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. the palm-leaf, an oblong piece of<BR>the leaf used to write on with an iron stile; Trigonella<BR>Fœnum Græcum; a hollow cylinder of gold (or a<BR>palm-leaf used as a substitute) with or without a ring<BR>attached and thrust through the lobe of the ear as<BR>an ornament; (ई), f., N. of several plants, = रण्डा,<BR>Salvinia Cucullata; Anethum Graveolens; Curculigo<BR>Orchioides.<BR>—ताल-पर्ण, अम्, ई, n. f. a kind of<BR>vegetable perfume, see मुरा; (ई), f. a sort of anise,<BR>Anethum Graveolens (मधुरिका).<BR>—ताल-पुष्-<BR>पक, अम्, n. a medicinal application to the eyes<BR>(= प्र-पौण्डरीक).<BR>—ताल-प्रलम्ब, अम्, n.<BR>the fibres growing on the cocoa-nut and other palms<BR>under the outer rind, and from which a sort of<BR>cordage called coir is prepared, = ताल-जटा.<BR>—ताल-<BR>बद्ध or ताल-शुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, measured,<BR>rhythmical, regulated by measure or musical time.<BR>—ताल-भट, अस्, m., N. of a warrior.<BR>—ताल-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘bearer of the palm-tree,’ a N. of<BR>Bala-rāma; [cf. ताल-ध्वज.]<BR>—ताल-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, made of the palm.<BR>—ताल-मर्दक, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of musical instrument.<BR>—ताल-मर्दल, अस्,<BR>m. a cymbal.<BR>—ताल-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, of the<BR>measure of a palm-tree, as big as a palm; (अम्), ind.<BR>only a moment, i. e. one beat.<BR>—ताल-मूलिका or<BR>ताल-मूली, f. Curculigo Orchioides.<BR>—ताल-यन्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. a particular surgical instrument, a small pair of<BR>pincers; a lock, a lock and key.<BR>—ताल-रेचनक,<BR>अस्, m. a dancer, actor; (a various reading has ताल-<BR>वेचनक.)<BR>—ताल-लक्ष्मन्, आ, m. a N. of Bala-<BR>rāma; [cf. ताल-ध्वज.]<BR>—ताल-वन, अम्, n. a<BR>grove of palmyra-trees; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—ताल-वृन्त, अम्, n. a palm-leaf used as a fan,<BR>a fan in general; (अस्), m. a kind of Soma plant.<BR>—ताल-वृन्तक, अम्, n. a fan.<BR>—तालवृन्त-<BR>निवासिन्, ई, m., N. of a scholiast.<BR>—ताल-वेचनक,<BR>see ताल-रेचनक.<BR>—ताल-शब्द, अस्, m. the noise<BR>caused by the falling of the fruit of the palm; clap-<BR>ping the hands; [cf. तल-ताल.]<BR>—तालाख्या (˚ल-<BR>आख्˚), f. = ताल-पर्णी, a sort of vegetable perfume<BR>(मुरा).<BR>—तालाङ्क (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a N. of<BR>Bala-rāma [cf. ताल-ध्वज]; a N. of Śiva [cf.<BR>तालिन्]; a man marked with every fortunate spot or<BR>sign &c.; the leaf of a palm used for writing, the<BR>leaf of a book; a book; a saw; a sort of vegetable.<BR>—तालाध्याय (˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of the sixth<BR>book of the Saṅgīta-darpaṇa, treating of musical in-<BR>struments.<BR>—तालावचर (˚ल-अव्˚), अस्, m. a dancer,<BR>an actor; (also read तालावचरण and, less correctly,<BR>तालार्ध-चरण.)<BR>—ताली-पत्त्र, अम्, n. = तालीश-<BR>पत्त्र.<BR>—तालीश (˚ली-ईश), अम्, n. or तालीश-पत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. the tree Flacourtia Cataphracta, the leaves of<BR>which are used in medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0371-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालक|तालकं
तालक, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous insect; N. of<BR>a teacher; of a prince; (इका), f. the open palm of<BR>the hand [cf. तालिक]; N. of two plants, = ताल-<BR>मूली and ताम्र-वल्ली; (ई), f. toddy or the fer-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">Page0372-b+ 74</a>]<BR>mented exudation of the palm; (अम्), n. = ताल,<BR>हरि-ताल, yellow orpiment; a fragrant earth; a<BR>bolt, a latch, a kind of lock for fastening a door;<BR>a kind of ornament.<BR>—तालकाभ (˚क-आभ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (‘like orpiment’), green; (अस्), m. green,<BR>the colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालि|तालिः
तालि, इस्, f. Corypha Taliera; Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta; [cf. ताडि, and ताली under ताल, p. 371.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिक|तालिकः
तालिक, अस्, m. the open palm of the hand; clap-<BR>ping the hands; a tie, seal, string or cover for binding<BR>a letter, or parcel of papers, or the leaves of a manu-<BR>script; N. of a preceptor; [cf. तालिका under तालक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालित|तालितं
तालित, अम्, n. dyed or coloured cloth; a string,<BR>a tie; any musical instrument.<BR>—तालित-नगर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिन्
तालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘furnished with cymbals,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva; (इनस्), m. pl. the pupils of Tala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताली
ताली, compounded as a गति (q. v.) with the roots<BR>अस्, भू, and कृ; see also ताली under ताल, p. 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीयक
तालीयक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a cymbal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालकट
तालकट तालकट or तालिकट or तालाकट,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालव्य|तालव्यं
तालव्य तालव्य. See under तालु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालित|तालितं
तालित तालित. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिश|तालिशः
तालिश तालिश, अस्, m. a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीश|तालीशं
तालीश तालीश, अम्, n., N. of a tree or its<BR>leaf.<BR>—तालीश-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the leaf of this tree;<BR>Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालु
तालु तालु, उ, n. (rarely used as masc.; said<BR>to be fr. rt. तॄ), the palate.<BR>—तालु-कण्टक, अस्,<BR>or अम्, m. or n. (?) , a disease of the palate with<BR>children.<BR>—तालु-जिह्व, अस्, m. a crocodile; the<BR>uvula.<BR>—तालु-पाक, अस्, m. suppuration or abscess<BR>in the palate.<BR>—तालु-पात or तालु-पीडक, अस्, m.<BR>a particular disease of the palate with children.<BR>—तालु-पुप्पुट, अस्, m. an indolent swelling of<BR>the palate.<BR>—तालु-मूल, अम्, n. the root or back<BR>part of the palate.<BR>—तालु-विशोषण, अम्, n. the<BR>drying of the palate (through much talking &c.).<BR>—तालु-शोष, अस्, m. morbid dryness of the palate.<BR>—तालु-स्थान, अस्, आ, अम्, palatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालव्य|तालव्यं
तालव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the palate, palatal;<BR>(the palatal letters are formed by the contact of the<BR>tongue and the palate; they are इ, ए, ऐ, च्, छ्, ज्,<BR>झ्, ञ्, य्, and श्.<BR>—तालव्य-वर्ण, अस्, m. a palatal<BR>letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुक|तालुकं
तालुक, अम्, n. the palate; a disease of the palate;<BR>तालुका, ए, f. du. the two arteries of the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुकिन्
तालुकिन्. See काक-तालुकिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालूषक|तालूषकं
तालूषक = तालु, the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुक्ष्य
तालुक्ष्य तालुक्ष्य, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Talukṣa; (the fem. is तालुक्ष्यायणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुन
तालुन तालुन, adj. formed fr. तलुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालूर|तालूरः
तालूर तालूर, अस्, m. a whirlpool, an eddy;<BR>(also written तालुर; cf. तानूर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताल्प
ताल्प ताल्प, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तल्प), = तल्प्य,<BR>offspring of the marriage-bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावक
तावक तावक (fr. तव), अस्, ई, अम्, thy, thine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावकीन|तावकीनं
तावकीन, अस्, आ or ई (?), अम्, thine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्|तावन्त्
तावत् तावत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. the pronom.<BR>base 2. त; correlative of यावत्), so great, so large,<BR>so much, so far, so long, so many, such (e. g. ता-<BR>वन्तस् तण्डुलाः, so many rice-grains; यावता<BR>क्षणेन तावता, after what time, in that time;<BR>यावन्ति तस्य द्वीपस्य वस्तूनि तावन्त्य् उपने-<BR>तव्यानि, whatever are the commodities of that<BR>island, so many are to be brought); तावता, ind. in<BR>the mean time, during that time; to that extent;<BR>तावत्, ind. so much, so greatly, to such an extent,<BR>in such a number, so far, so long, in that time<BR>(correlatively to यावत्, e. g. यावत् — तावत्, as long<BR>as — so long; when — then; यावत् त्रयस् ते जीवेयुस्<BR>तावन् नान्यं समाचरेत्, as long as those three<BR>live, so long he must perform no other duty), mean-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">Page0372-c+ 74</a>]<BR>while, in the mean time, (often connected with या-<BR>वत् and a negative, e. g. तावच् छोभते^1 मूर्खो<BR>यावत् किञ्चिन् न भाषते, so long a fool shines as<BR>long as he says nothing; or with omission of the<BR>negative, e. g. शोषयिष्याम्य् आत्मानं तावद्<BR>यावन् मे प्राप्तम् ब्राह्मण्यम्, so long I will<BR>emaciate myself as long as, i. e. until I have obtained<BR>the state of a Brāhman); at once, now, just, (often<BR>connected rather redundantly with an imperative or<BR>with a potential or the verb अर्ह्, e. g. गच्छ तावत्<BR>or गच्छेस् तावत्, go now; तत् तावद् वाक्यं<BR>क्षन्तुम् अर्हसि, deign now to pardon that speech);<BR>indeed, really, truly, well, (as an emphatic particle,<BR>or to express assent, e. g. दृढस् तावद् बन्धः,<BR>the knot is tight I must admit; गता तावत्, she<BR>is indeed gone; sometimes connected in this sense<BR>with the particle एव, e. g. विक्रयस् तावद् एव सः,<BR>it is really a sale.) न तावत्, not at all; not yet<BR>(e. g. न तावद् दृश्यते सूर्यः, the sun is not<BR>yet visible); इतस् तावत्, away then! just come hither;<BR>मा तावत्, by no means, God forbid! यावत् — द्विस्-<BR>तावत्, as long — twice so long. According to the<BR>lexicographers तावत् may imply measure, limitation,<BR>totality, restriction, surprise, emphasis, &c.; [cf. Lat.<BR>tantus fr. tavantus; Gr. τόσος, τῆμος.]<BR>—तावच्-<BR>छत (˚वत्-श˚), अस्, ई, अम्, a measure containing<BR>so many hundreds.<BR>—तावच्-छस् (तावत्-शस्), ind.,<BR>Ved. in so many ways, so manifoldly.<BR>—तावत्-कालम्,<BR>ind. for so long a period, for such a time.<BR>—तावत्-<BR>कृत्वस्, ind. so many times.<BR>—तावत्-फल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having such results.<BR>—तावद्-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having so many qualities.<BR>—तावद्-द्वयस, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, measuring so much, so long, &c.<BR>—तावद्-धा,<BR>ind. in that number, in such a number; so many<BR>times, so often.<BR>—तावद्-वर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, so<BR>many years old.<BR>—तावद्-व्यक्त, (in alg.) a known<BR>number annexed to an unknown quantity.<BR>—तावन्-<BR>मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, just so much, just so many.<BR>—तावन्-मान, अस्, आ, अम्, measuring so much.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161201. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावतिक
तावतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, bought for so much, worth<BR>so much, of so great value; [cf. तावत्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावतिथ
तावतिथ, अस्, ई, अम्, the so manieth, such a one<BR>(of a number).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्क
तावत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, bought for so much, worth<BR>so much, of so much value, &c.; [cf. तावतिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावर|तावरं
तावर तावर, अम्, n. a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताविष|ताविषः
ताविष ताविष, अस्, ई, m. f. the ocean;<BR>heaven or paradise; gold; [cf. तविष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावीष|तावीषः
तावीष, अस्, m. the ocean; heaven or paradise;<BR>gold; (ई), f. a river; the earth; N. of a daughter<BR>of Indra; N. of a daughter of the moon (?); [cf.<BR>तवीष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावुरि|तावुरिः
तावुरि तावुरि, इस्, m. (borrowed fr. the<BR>Gr. ταῦρος), the sign of the Zodiac Taurus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तासीर
तासीर तासीर = तसीर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तास्कर्य|तास्कर्यं|तास्कर्य्य
तास्कर्य तास्कर्य, अम्, n. (fr. तस्कर),<BR>theft, robbery, larceny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तास्यन्द्र
तास्यन्द्र तास्यन्द्र or तास्विन्द्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ति|तिः
ति ति = इति in the Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्
तिक् तिक्, cl. 1. A. तेकते, &c., to go or<BR>move [cf. rt. तीक्]; cl. 5. P. तिक्नोति, &c.,<BR>to go or move; to assail, assault; to wound; to seek to<BR>injure or kill; to challenge; [cf. rt. तिग् and स्तिघ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक
तिक तिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—तिक-<BR>कितव, आस्, m. pl. the descendants of Tika and<BR>Kitava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिकीय
तिकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, an adj. derived from Tika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्त|तिक्तं|तिक्तः
तिक्त तिक्त. See rt. तिज्, p. 373, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्
तिग् तिग्, cl. 5. P. तिग्नोति, &c., to go or<BR>move; to assail, assault; to seek to<BR>injure or kill; [cf. rt. तिक्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिगल
तिगल तिगल (?), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्म|तिग्मं
तिग्म तिग्म. See next page, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0372-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिघ्
तिघ् तिघ्, cl. 5. P. तिघ्नोति, &c., to<BR>strike; to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिङ्गुद
तिङ्गुद तिङ्गुद, अस्, m. (a wrong reading<BR>for तिन्दुक), N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिज्
तिज् तिज्, cl. 1. P. A., Ved. तेजति, -ते,<BR>Ved. Inf. तेजसे, to be or become sharp;<BR>to sharpen: Caus. P. तेजयति, -यितुम्, to sharpen,<BR>whet; to stir up, excite, incite, urge on: Desid. A.<BR>तितिक्षते, to desire to become sharp or firm, to<BR>resist, oppose, to bear with firmness, suffer with<BR>courage or patience, endure, bear: Intens. Ved.<BR>तेतिक्ते; [cf. Zend tigh-ra, ‘pointed, peaked;’<BR>tigh-ri, ‘an arrow:’ Gr. στίζ-ω, στίγ-μα, στιγ-μή,<BR>στικ-τό-ς: Lat. di-sting-u-o (δια-στίζω), in-stinc-<BR>tu-s, in-stīga-re, stĭ-mulu-s for stig-mulu-s, stĭ-<BR>lu-s for stig-lu-s: Goth. us-stiggan, ‘to sting;’<BR>tēka, ‘to touch;’ stiggqvan, stik-s, stak-s: Old<BR>Germ. sting-u, stihhu, ‘I sting;’ stachila, ‘a<BR>prickle;’ stihhil, ‘a stile:’ Angl. Sax. stician,<BR>‘to sting:’ Lith. tékinu, ‘I whet;’ tékélis, ‘a large<BR>whetstone:’ Russ. tocù, ‘I whet;’ tocílo, ‘a whet-<BR>stone:’ Cambro-Brit. teg, ‘clear, fair, beautiful, pretty,<BR>bland.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्त|तिक्तं|तिक्तः
तिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bitter (as sharpening the appe-<BR>tite), pungent; fragrant; (अस्), m. a bitter taste;<BR>one of the six modifications of flavour (रस); bit-<BR>terness, pungency; fragrance, perfume; N. of several<BR>plants, viz. Wrightia Antidysenterica (= कुटज);<BR>Capparis Trifoliata (= वरुण); Agathotes Chirayta<BR>(= किरात-तिक्त); Melia Azadirachta; Terminalia<BR>Catappa (= इङ्गुदी); a bitter sort of cucumber,<BR>Trichosanthes Cucumerina (?); a kind of salt; (आ),<BR>f., N. of several plants, viz. Helleborus Niger (=<BR>कटु-रोहिणी); Clypea Hernandifolia (= पाठा);<BR>Artemisia Sternutatoria; (अम्), n. a medicinal plant,<BR>Mollugo Pentaphylla.<BR>—तिक्त-कन्दका, f. Curcuma<BR>Zedoaria.<BR>—तिक्त-गन्धा or तिक्त-गन्धिका, f.<BR>mustard, Lycopodium Imbricatum.<BR>—तिक्त-गुञ्जा,<BR>f. Pongamia Glabra, = करञ्ज.<BR>—तिक्त-घृत, अम्,<BR>n. a mixture of Ghṛta with bitter herbs &c.<BR>—तिक्त-<BR>तण्डुला, f. long pepper.<BR>—तिक्त-तुण्डी, f. = कटु-<BR>तुण्डी.<BR>—तिक्त-तुम्बी, f. = कटु-तुम्बी, a bitter<BR>gourd.<BR>—तिक्त-दुग्धा, f., N. of several plants, =<BR>क्षीरिणी, अज-शृङ्गी, स्वर्ण-क्षीरी.<BR>—तिक्त-<BR>धातु, उस्, m. bile.<BR>—तिक्त-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a cu-<BR>curbitaceous plant, Momordica Mixta.<BR>—तिक्त-पर्-<BR>वन्, आ, f., N. of several plants, viz. Cocculus Cor-<BR>difolius; Hingcha (= हिलमोची) Repens; Panicum<BR>Dactylon, = मधु-यष्टि; liquorice.<BR>—तिक्त-<BR>पुष्पा, f. Clypea Hernandifolia; Bignonia Suaveo-<BR>lens.<BR>—तिक्त-फल, अस्, m. Strychnos Potatorum<BR>[cf. कतक]; (आ), f., N. of several plants, = यव-<BR>तिक्ता, वार्ताकी, षड्-भुजा.<BR>—तिक्त-भद्रक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of cucumber, Trichosanthes Dioica.<BR>—तिक्त-मरिच, अस्, m. Strychnos Potatorum; [cf.<BR>कतक.]<BR>—तिक्त-यवा, f., N. of a plant, = शङ्-<BR>खिनी.<BR>—तिक्त-रोहिणिका or तिक्त-रोहिणी, f. a medi-<BR>cinal plant, = कटु-रोहिणी.<BR>—तिक्त-वल्ली, f. the plant<BR>Sanseviera Roxburghiana.<BR>—तिक्त-वीजा, f. a kind of<BR>cucumber, = कटु-तुम्बी.<BR>—तिक्त-शाक, अस्, m.<BR>‘bitter herbs or greens,’ N. of several plants, viz.<BR>Capparis Trifoliata; Acacia Catechu, a kind of Mi-<BR>mosa [cf. खदिर]; = पत्त्र-सुन्दर.<BR>—तिक्त-<BR>सार, अस्, m. the plant Acacia Catechu; (अम्), n. a<BR>kind of fragrant grass.<BR>—तिक्ताख्या (˚त-आख्˚), f.<BR>the plant Tikta-tuṇḍī.<BR>—तिक्ताङ्गा (˚त-अङ्˚), f. a<BR>kind of creeper, = पाताल-गरुडी.<BR>—तिक्तामृता<BR>(˚त-अम्˚), f. Menispermum Glabrum.<BR>—तिक्तायन<BR>(˚त-अय्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. possessing the heat or<BR>radiance of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तक|तिक्तकः
तिक्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, bitter; anything having a<BR>bitter flavour; (अस्), m., N. of several plants, viz.<BR>Trichosanthes Dioica; Agathotes Chirayta; a sort<BR>of Acacia Catechu; Terminalia Catappa [cf. किरात-<BR>तिक्तक]; (आ), f. a kind of gourd (कटु-तुम्बी);<BR>Cardiospermum Halicacabum, = करञ्ज-वल्ली;<BR>(इका), f. a kind of gourd (कटु-तुम्बी); [cf. जल-<BR>तिक्तिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिगित
तिगित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sharp, pointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्म|तिग्मं
तिग्म, अस्, आ, अम्, sharp, pointed (as a weapon<BR>or as flame or a ray of light); violent; hot;<BR>pungent, acrid; scorching; fiery, passionate, hasty;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a prince; (अम्), n. heat; a pungent<BR>or hot flavour, the heat of spices, pungency;<BR>[cf. तीक्ष्ण; cf. also Hib. time, ‘heat, warmth.’]<BR>—तिग्म-कर, अस्, m. ‘hot-rayed,’ the sun; [cf.<BR>तिग्म-दीधिति, तिग्म-रश्मि, तिग्मांशु.]<BR>—तिग्-<BR>म-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Svar-vīthi and<BR>Vatsara.<BR>—तिग्म-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going or flying<BR>swiftly.<BR>—तिग्म-जम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>sharp teeth, an epithet of Agni.<BR>—तिग्म-ता, f. or<BR>तिग्म-त्व, अम्, n. sharpness, pungency; heat;<BR>passion, petulance.<BR>—तिग्म-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved.<BR>sharp-edged, sharp-pointed; penetrating, pervading;<BR>of a violent character.<BR>—तिग्म-दीधिति, इस्, m. the<BR>sun; [cf. तिग्म-कर.]<BR>—तिग्म-भृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. sharp-pointed, a N. of Agni.<BR>—तिग्म-यातना,<BR>f. acute pain, agony, torment.<BR>—तिग्म-रश्मि, इस्,<BR>m. the sun; [cf. तिग्म-कर.]<BR>—तिग्म-रुच्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>shining brightly, hot; (क्), m. the sun.<BR>—तिग्म-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing the word तिग्म.<BR>—तिग्म-शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having sharp<BR>horns.<BR>—तिग्म-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having sharp<BR>rays, epithet of Agni.<BR>—तिग्म-हेति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>having sharp weapons (or flames); forming a sharp<BR>weapon (as the horns of Agni).<BR>—तिग्मांशु (˚म-<BR>अं˚), उस्, उस्, उ, having sharp rays or warm beams;<BR>(उस्), m. the sun; fire; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—तिग्मा-<BR>त्मन् (˚म-आत्˚), आ, m., N. of a prince, son of Urva.<BR>—तिग्मानीक (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sharp-<BR>pointed; (Sāy.) sharp-mouthed.<BR>—तिग्मायुध<BR>(˚म-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having or casting or<BR>forming sharp weapons.<BR>—तिग्मेषु (˚म-इषु),<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having sharp arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्ष
तितिक्ष, अस्, m. (fr. Desid. of rt. तिज्), N. of a man;<BR>(आ), f. endurance, patience, resignation, suffering,<BR>forbearance; Patience personified as a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and wife of Dharma and mother of Kṣema.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षित|तितिक्षितः
तितिक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, borne, endured, suffered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षु|तितिक्षुः
तितिक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, bearing, enduring patiently,<BR>patient, resigned, forbearing; (उस्), m., N. of a son<BR>of Mahā-manas and descendant of Janam-ejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिजिल|तिजिलः
तिजिल तिजिल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तिज्), the moon; a Rakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिटिभ
तिटिभ तिटिभ, a particular high number;<BR>(also read तिटिलम्भ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिणिस
तिणिस तिणिस, अस्, m. = तिनिश, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिण्टी
तिण्टी तिण्टी, f. a plant, commonly Teori,<BR>Convolvulus Turpethum (= त्रि-वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितउ|तितउः
तितउ तित-उ, उस्, उ, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>3. तन् by a kind of reduplication, cf. τιταίνω but<BR>perhaps fr. rt. तंस्), a sieve, a cribble; a parasol; [cf.<BR>चालनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितनिषु
तितनिषु तितनिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. 3. तन्), desirous of extending or enlarging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्ष
तितिक्ष तितिक्ष. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिभ|तितिभः
तितिभ तितिभ, अस्, m. an insect, cochineal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिरि
तितिरि तितिरि, इस्, m. = तित्तिरि, a partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिल|तितिलं
तितिल तितिल, अम्, n. a sort of sweetmeat<BR>made of sesamum ground and baked with sugar; one<BR>of the seven Karaṇas or astronomical periods; a<BR>bowl or bucket, = नन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षा
तितीर्षा तितीर्षा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. तॄ),<BR>desire of crossing over, wish to pass, wish to be freed<BR>from mundane existence, desire of final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षु
तितीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of crossing; wishing<BR>to attain; desirous of emancipation from existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिड
तित्तिड तित्तिड and तित्तिडीक, incorrect forms<BR>for तिन्तिड and तिन्तिडीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिर|तित्तिरः
तित्तिर तित्तिर, अस्, m. = तित्तिरि, col. 3; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरि|तित्तिरिः
तित्तिरि तित्तिरि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. तॄ,<BR>but perhaps an onomatopoetic word fr. the cry<BR>तित्ति), the francoline partridge; N. of a Muni, pupil<BR>of Yāska, and said to be the first teacher of the<BR>Taittirīya or Black Yajur-veda; (according to a<BR>legend the pupils of Vaiśampāyana became par-<BR>tridges in order to pick up the Veda which was<BR>vomited forth in a tangible shape by Yājñavalkya;<BR>cf. तैत्तिरीय); N. of a Nāga; [cf. Gr. τέτριξ,<BR>τέτραξ, τετράων, τετράζω; Old Island. thid-r, ‘a<BR>kind of hen;’ Lith. tetèrva, ‘black grouse;’ Boh.<BR>tetrev.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरिक|तित्तिरिकः
तित्तिरिक, अस्, m. the francoline partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरीक
तित्तिरीक, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated like a partridge<BR>(तित्तिरि) or made of Croton Tiglium (तित्तिरी-फल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरीफल
तित्तिरी-फल (तित्तिरी = तित्तिरि?), Croton Tiglium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथ|तिथः
तिथ तिथ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. तिज्),<BR>fire; love; time; autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथि|तिथिः
तिथि तिथि, इस्, ई, m. f. (said to be fr. rt. अत्),<BR>a lunar day, the thirtieth part of a whole lunation,<BR>(the auspicious Tithis are Nandā, Bhadrā, Vi-jayā,<BR>Pūrṇā); the number 15; [cf. जन्म-तिथि.]<BR>—ति-<BR>थि-क्षय, अस्, m. the day of new moon; the<BR>day or space in which a Tithi begins or ends without<BR>one sunrising; the difference between the solar and<BR>lunar days in a Yuga.<BR>—तिथि-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of<BR>the seventh section of the Smṛti-tattva, treating of<BR>lunar holidays, by Raghu-nandana.<BR>—तिथितत्त्व-<BR>टीका, f., N. of the commentary on the preceding<BR>work by Kāśī-rāma.<BR>—तिथि-दान, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter of the second part of the Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa,<BR>treating of the observance of various ceremonies.<BR>—तिथि-द्वैत, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva by Halāyudha.<BR>—तिथि-नियम,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Tantra-sāra, or com-<BR>pendium of Tantra doctrine, by Kṛṣṇānanda.<BR>—तिथि-निर्णय and तिथिनिर्णय-सङ्क्षेप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of two astronomical works.<BR>—तिथि-पति,<BR>इस्, m. = तिथीश.<BR>—तिथि-पत्त्री, f. an almanack.<BR>—तिथि-पालन, अम्, n. observance of the rites<BR>appointed for the several lunar days.<BR>—तिथि-प्र-<BR>करण, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Cintā-maṇiḥ<BR>Sāraṇikā or Tithi-sāraṇikā, treating of astronomical<BR>periods and constellations, by Daśa-bala; N. of a<BR>chapter of the Jyotiṣa-ratna-mālā, an astronomical<BR>work by Śrī-pati.<BR>—तिथि-प्रणी, ईस्, m. ‘the leader of<BR>the lunar days,’ the moon; [cf. दिन-प्रणी.]<BR>—तिथि-<BR>वार-योग, आस्, m. pl., N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-<BR>sarva-sva.<BR>—तिथि-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of<BR>the Saṃskāra-tattva by Raghu-nandana, treating of<BR>the Indian sacraments.<BR>—तिथि-वृद्धि, इस्, f. that<BR>day or space in which a Tithi commences before or<BR>with one sunrise and ends after or at the next, thus<BR>completed under two suns.<BR>—तिथीश (˚थि-ईश), अस्,<BR>m. the regent of a lunar day.<BR>—तिथ्य्-अन्त-निर्-<BR>णय, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Smṛty-artha-<BR>sāra by Śrī-dhara-svāmin, treating of the Indian<BR>ceremonies.<BR>—तिथ्य्-अर्ध, अस्, अम्, m. n. half a<BR>Tithi, = करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनाशक|तिनाशकः
तिनाशक तिनाशक, अस्, m. a tree, = तिनिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनिका
तिनिका तिनिका, f. Holcus Sorghum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनिश|तिनिशः
तिनिश तिनिश, अस्, m. the tree Dalbergia<BR>Ougeinensis; [cf. तिणिस and तिमिश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिड|तिंतिड|तिंतिडः|तिन्तिडः
तिन्तिड तिन्तिड, अस्, m. the tamarind tree,<BR>Tamarindus Indica; acid seasoning, sour sauce,<BR>especially a sauce made of the fruit of the tamarind<BR>tree; an inauspicious period, the evil aspect of<BR>planets (?); (ई), f. the Indian tamarind tree; a sour<BR>sauce, especially one made of the fruit of the tamarind<BR>tree; Emblic Myrobalan.<BR>—तिन्तिडी-द्यूत, अम्, n.<BR>a kind of game, a sort of odd or even played with<BR>tamarind seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडिका|तिंतिडिका
तिन्तिडिका, f. the tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडीक|तिंतिडीक|तिन्तिडीकं|तिंतिडीकः|तिन्तिडीकः
तिन्तिडीक, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. the tamarind tree;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of the tamarind; a sour sauce,<BR>especially one made of the fruit of the tamarind<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0373-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिली|तिंतिली
तिन्तिली or तिन्तिलिका or तिन्तिलीका, f. the tamarind<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दिश|तिन्दिशः
तिन्दिश तिन्दिश, अस्, m. a kind of plant,<BR>= टिण्डिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दु|तिंदु|तिंदुः|तिन्दुः
तिन्दु तिन्दु, उस्, m. a species of ebony,<BR>from the fruit of which is obtained a kind of resin<BR>used in India as pitch for caulking vessels &c.,<BR>Diospyros Glutinosa; also Strychnos Nux Vomica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुक|तिंदुक|तिंदुकं|तिन्दुकं|तिंदुकः|तिन्दुकः
तिन्दुक, अस्, m. the tree Diospyros Embryopteris<BR>or Diospyros Glutinosa; (ई), f. the resinous fruit<BR>of this tree; (अम्), n. the fruit of this tree; a<BR>Karṣa, a kind of measure or weight (= the weight<BR>of the Tinduka fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुकि|तिन्दुकिः
तिन्दुकि, इस्, f. or तिन्दुल, अस्, m. the tree Dios-<BR>pyros Embryopteris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुकिनी
तिन्दुकिनी, f. the senna plant, = आवर्तकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुविल्व
तिन्दुविल्व तिन्दुविल्व, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>birthplace of the Lyric poet Jaya-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिप्
तिप् तिप्, cl. 1. P. तेपति, &c., to sprinkle,<BR>to distil or drop, to ooze or leak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिम्
तिम् तिम्, cl. 4. P. तिम्यति, तितेम, &c.,<BR>to be or become wet or damp &c.; to<BR>become pacified or quiet: Intens. तेतिम्यते; [cf.<BR>rt. तीम् and स्तिम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमित|तिमितः
तिमित, अस्, आ, अम्, moistened, moist, wet, damp;<BR>quiet; unmoved, unshaken; steady, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमि|तिमिः
तिमि तिमि, इस्, or sometimes तिम, अस्, m.<BR>(said to be fr. rt. तम्), a kind of whale or fabulous<BR>fish of an enormous size, said to be 100 Yojanas<BR>long; a fish in general; the figure of a fish produced<BR>by drawing two lines, one intersecting the other at<BR>right angles; the ocean; N. of a son of Dūrva and<BR>father of Bṛhad-ratha; (इस्, ई), f. a fish; N. of a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa who was the wife of Kaśyapa<BR>and mother of the sea-monsters.<BR>—तिमि-कोष or<BR>तिमि-कोषक, अस्, m. the ocean (‘the receptacle of<BR>great fish’).<BR>—तिमिङ्-गिल, अस्, m. ‘swallowing even<BR>the Timi,’ a large fabulous fish; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people in Dakṣiṇā-patha; (अस्), m. a prince of<BR>this people.<BR>—तिमिङ्गिल-गिल, अस्, m. a large<BR>fabulous fish (‘swallowing even the Timiṅ-gila’).<BR>—तिमि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, coming or derived from the<BR>Timi, a sort of pearl.<BR>—तिमि-तिमिङ्-गिल, अस्, m.<BR>a large fabulous fish.<BR>—तिमि-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘having a Timi depicted in his banner,’ epithet of<BR>the Asura Śambara, prince of Vaijayanta; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमित|तिमितः
तिमित तिमित. See under rt. तिम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिर|तिमिरं|तिमिरः
तिमिर तिमिर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तिम्, but rather related to तमस् fr. rt. तम्), dark,<BR>gloomy; (अम्), n. darkness; darkness of the eyes,<BR>blindness; a class of morbid affections of the eyes<BR>seated in the पटल or coats of the eye; gutta<BR>serena, total blindness from affection of the optic<BR>nerve; iron-rust; a sort of aquatic plant [cf. तिमीर<BR>and तिमिष]; (अम्, आ), n. f., N. of two towns.<BR>—तिमिर-नुद्, त्, त्, त्, dispelling darkness; (त्), m.<BR>the sun; the moon.<BR>—तिमिर-प्रतिषेध, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Uttara-tantra or sixth book<BR>of the Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya-saṃhitā by Vāg-bhaṭa,<BR>treating of medicine.<BR>—तिमिर-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of darkness; (अस्), m. an epithet of Rāhu<BR>(who creates darkness), or an eclipse in general.<BR>—तिमिर-रिपु, उस्, m. ‘the enemy of darkness,’ the<BR>sun.<BR>—तिमिरारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m. ‘the enemy of<BR>darkness,’ the sun.<BR>—तिमिरोद्घाट (˚र-उद्˚), N.<BR>of a treatise in verse connected with the Śaiva<BR>dogmas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिरय
तिमिरय, nom. P. तिमिरयति, -यितुम्, to ob-<BR>scure, darken, eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिराय
तिमिराय, nom. A. तिमिरायते, &c., to appear<BR>dark, to darken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिरिन्
तिमिरिन्, ई, m. the cochineal insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिरि
तिमिरि तिमिरि, a kind of fish (not the<BR>तिमि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिर्घ
तिमिर्घ तिमिर्घ, अस्, m., N. of a man with<BR>the patronymic Daureśruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिश
तिमिश तिमिश, probably a wrong reading<BR>for तिनिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिष|तिमिषः
तिमिष तिमिष, अस्, m. a kind of pumpkin-<BR>gourd, Benincasa Cerifera; a water-melon (ना-<BR>टाम्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमीर
तिमीर तिमीर, अस्, m. a kind of tree; [cf.<BR>तिमिर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरय
तिरय तिरय. See next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्च्
तिरश्च् तिरश्च्, &c. See under तिर्यञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्
तिरस् तिरस्, ind. (fr. rt. तॄ, the अस् being<BR>probably the ablative termination), through (with acc.<BR>in Ved., e. g. तिरः पवित्रम्, through the strainer;<BR>तिरस् तमांसि दर्शतः, discernible through the<BR>darkness); across, beyond, over (e. g. नदीं तिरस्,<BR>across the river; रजांसि तिरस्, over the world; ते<BR>नस् तिरो विश्वानि दुरिता नयन्ति, they lead us<BR>over all difficulties); without (i. e. in such a manner<BR>as to pass by or leave on one side); apart from, on<BR>one side of, aside, secretly from, ‘clam’ (with acc.,<BR>e. g. तिरश् चित्तानि, without the knowledge; तिरो<BR>वशम्, against the will; or sometimes with abl.,<BR>e. g. मनुष्येभ्यस् तिरस्, on one side of the men);<BR>crookedly, obliquely, awry; transversely, indirectly,<BR>badly, secretly, covertly; [cf. Lat. trans: Goth.<BR>thairh: Germ. durch: Hib. tar, tair, ‘beyond,<BR>over, across, through; bad;’ tri, ‘through, by:’<BR>Lith. tiês: Zend tarō.]<BR>—तिरस्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>leaving on one side, passing by, surpassing, excelling.<BR>—तिरस्-करिन्, ई, इणी, m. f. a curtain, veil; an<BR>outer tent, kanāt, wall, or screen of cloth surrounding<BR>the principal tent; a kind of magical veil rendering<BR>the wearer invisible.<BR>—तिरस्-कार, अस्, m. placing<BR>aside, concealment, disappearance; disrespect, abuse,<BR>reproach, censure, disgrace, disdain.<BR>—तिरस्-कारिणी,<BR>f. a curtain, = तिरस्-करिणी.<BR>—तिरस्-कुड्य or ति-<BR>रस्-प्राकार, अस्, आ, अम्, looking through a wall.<BR>—तिरस्-कृ or तिरः कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to put on one side, set aside, remove, cover, conceal;<BR>to pass by, surpass, excel, conquer; to blame, re-<BR>proach, abuse, treat disrespectfully, contemn, despise;<BR>[according to Pāṇini I. IV. 71, 72, तिरस् must be<BR>a गति (q. v.), in the sense of ‘covering,’ ‘concealing,’<BR>but an option is allowed in its connection with<BR>rt. 1. कृ.]<BR>—तिरस्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, concealed,<BR>hidden, veiled, vanished, disappeared; censured, re-<BR>viled, abused, reproached, scorned.<BR>—तिरस्-कृत्य<BR>(or तिरः कृत्वा), ind. having concealed.<BR>—तिरस्-<BR>क्रिया, f. concealment, disappearance; disrespect,<BR>reproach, contempt.<BR>—तिरो-अह्न्य or तिरो-ऽह्न्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (the former form occurring in the Veda,<BR>the latter in the Brāhmaṇas and later writings), more<BR>than one day old, prepared the day before yesterday.<BR>—तिरो-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, disappeared, vanished, out<BR>of sight.<BR>—तिरो-जनम्, ind., Ved. apart from men.<BR> — 1. तिरो-धा or तिरो धा, cl. 3. P. A. दधाति,<BR>धत्ते, धातुम्, to place on one side, set aside,<BR>remove out of the way, cover, conceal, hide; to<BR>hide one's self from (with abl.), disappear; to over-<BR>power, conquer: Pass. तिरो-धीयते or तिरो धीयते,<BR>to be hidden, to vanish, disappear.<BR>—२. तिरो-धा, f.,<BR>Ved. concealment, secrecy.<BR>—तिरो-धातव्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, to be covered or concealed, to be closed.<BR>—तिरो-धान, अम्, n. disappearance, vanishing, the<BR>being hidden or the act of hiding, concealing, &c.; a<BR>covering, a sheath, a veil, a cloth or cloak, anything<BR>which conceals from sight.<BR>—तिरो-भवितृ, ता, त्री,<BR>तृ, disappearing.<BR>—तिरो-भाव, अस्, m. disappear-<BR>ance, (opposed to आविर्-भाव and प्रादुर्-भाव.)<BR>—तिरो-भू, cl. 1. P. तिरो-भवति, -वितुम्, to be<BR>set on one side, disappear, vanish, hide one's self:<BR>Caus. तिरो-भावयति or तिरो भावयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to disappear, dispel.<BR>—तिरो-वर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>protected from rain.<BR>—तिरो-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered,<BR>concealed, hidden, removed or withdrawn from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">Page0374-c+ 70</a>]<BR>sight.<BR>—तिरोहित-ता, f. disappearance, the becoming<BR>invisible; तिरोहिततां गम्, to disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरय
तिरय, nom. P. तिरयति, -यितुम्, to keep<BR>hidden or concealed, to prevent from appearing,<BR>hinder, stop, restrain; to conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्य
तिरस्य, nom. P. तिरस्यति, &c., to disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोहय
तिरोहय, nom. P. तिरोहयति, -यितुम्, to hide,<BR>conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोह्न्य
तिरो-ऽह्न्य. See तिरो-अह्न्य, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कर
तिरस्कर तिरस्-कर, तिरस्-कृ, &c. See<BR>under तिरस्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिजिह्विक
तिरिजिह्विक तिरिजिह्विक, अस्, or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), Erythrina Crista Galli (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिटि|तिरिटिः
तिरिटि तिरिटि, इस्, or तिरिट, अस् (?), m. the<BR>joint of the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिणीकण्ट
तिरिणीकण्ट तिरिणीकण्ट = तिरिजिह्विक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिन्दिर
तिरिन्दिर तिरिन्दिर, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिम|तिरिमः
तिरिम तिरिम or तिरिय, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>rice; [cf. तिर्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीट|तिरीटं|तिरीटः
तिरीट तिरीट, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. तॄ,<BR>perhaps for तिरी-त्र, or a wrong form for किरीट),<BR>a kind of head-dress, a tiara, a diadem; gold; (अस्),<BR>m. the tree Symplocos Racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीटक
तिरीटक, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीटिन्
तिरीटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. furnished with a head-<BR>dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरो
तिरो तिरो for तिरस्. See under तिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोहित|तिरोहितः
तिरोहित तिरो-हित. See under तिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्पिरिक
तिर्पिरिक तिर्पिरिक, अम्, n. = तिल्पिलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्पिलि
तिर्पिलि तिर्पिलि, इस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य
तिर्य तिर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = तिल्य, Ved. prepared<BR>from the seeds of sesamum (?); [cf. तिरिय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यग
तिर्यग तिर्यग for तिर्यग्-ग. See तिर्यञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्यञ्च्|तिर्य्यञ्च्
तिर्यञ्च् तिर्यञ्च् or तिर्यच्, अङ्, तिरश्ची, or<BR>according to Vopa-deva also तिर्यञ्ची, अक् (fr. तिरस् and<BR>rt. अञ्च्), going or lying crosswise or transversely or<BR>obliquely, oblique, transverse (opposed to अन्व्-अञ्च्),<BR>horizontal (opposed to ऊर्ध्व, vertical); going<BR>across; crossing over, traversing; moving tortuously,<BR>going crookedly or awry; curved, crooked; mean-<BR>dering; lying in the middle or between; (अङ्, अक्),<BR>m. n. an animal (going horizontally, as opposed to<BR>man who walks erect), a brute, an amphibious<BR>animal; a bird; (with Jainas) plants, the organic<BR>world; (तिरश्ची or तिर्यञ्ची), f. the female of an<BR>animal or of any beast or bird; (अक्), ind., Ved. across,<BR>obliquely, transversely, horizontally, sideways; तिरश्चा,<BR>ind. across, obliquely.<BR>—तिरश्चि-राजि, इस्, इस्, इ (तिरश्चि<BR>loc. case of तिर्यञ्च्), Ved. striped across (as a ser-<BR>pent).<BR>—तिर्यक्-कारम् or तिर्यक्-कृत्य, ind. having<BR>laid aside (after the completion of any work), having<BR>placed on one side.<BR>—तिर्यक्-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>placed obliquely or across; a form of dislocation<BR>when a part of the joint is forced outwards.<BR>—तिर्-<BR>यक्-ता, f. or तिर्यक्-त्व, अम्, n. the state of going<BR>across or obliquely; the state of a beast or animal,<BR>animal nature; measurement across, breadth.<BR>—तिर्-<BR>यक्-पातन, अम्, n., N. of a part of the Ānanda-<BR>kanda, treating of medicine.<BR>—तिर्यक्-प्रमाण,<BR>अम्, n. measurement across, breadth; पुरस्तात्-<BR>तिर्यक्प्रमाण, breadth in front; पश्चात्-त्˚, breadth<BR>behind.<BR>—तिर्यक्-प्रेक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking<BR>obliquely or askance; (अम्), n. a squint, oblique<BR>glance, side look.<BR>—तिर्यक्-प्रेक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>looking obliquely or sideways.<BR>—तिर्यक्-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n. a cross-line.<BR>—तिर्यक्-स्रोतस्, अस्, n. ‘the hori-<BR>zontal stream of life,’ the animal creation; (आस्), m.<BR>‘hurrying the stream of life horizontal,’ i. e. the<BR>animal world; an animal, a beast or bird; [cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">Page0375-a+ 79</a>]<BR>अर्वाक्-स्रोतस्, अवाक्-स्रोतस्, ऊर्ध्व-स्रोतस्.]<BR>—तिर्-<BR>यग्-अन्तर, अम्, n. intermediate space measured<BR>across, breadth.<BR>—तिर्यग्-अयन, अम्, n. the hori-<BR>zontal course, the annual revolution of the sun,<BR>(opposed to its diurnal revolution, in which it rises<BR>and sets vertically.)<BR>—तिर्यग्-आगत, अस्, आ, अम्, lying<BR>across (a particular position of the child at birth).<BR>—तिर्यग्-ईक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, looking obliquely; [cf.<BR>तिर्यक्-प्रेक्षण.]<BR>—तिर्यग्-ईश, अस्, m. ‘the lord<BR>of the animals,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—तिर्यग्-ग<BR>(or sometimes तिर्य-ग), अस्, आ, अम्, going obliquely,<BR>going across or horizontally [cf. प्रतीप-ग, अधो-<BR>मुख, ऊर्ध्व-ग]; an animal; going towards the<BR>north or south, (opposed to पूर्व-मुखी and<BR>पश्चान्-मुखी.)<BR>—तिर्यग्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>horizontally, (opposed to man who walks erect.)<BR>—तिर्यग्-गति, इस्, f. the course of an animal, trans-<BR>migration of animals.<BR>—तिर्यग्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>going sideways or obliquely.<BR>—तिर्यग्-गमन, अम्,<BR>n. motion sideways or across, (opposed to ऊर्ध्व-ग्˚<BR>and अधो-ग्˚.)<BR>—तिर्यग्-गुणन, अम्, n. oblique<BR>multiplication.<BR>—तिर्यग्-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born from<BR>an animal, having an animal as father or mother.<BR>—तिर्यग्-जन, अस्, m. an animal.<BR>—तिर्यग्-जाति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, belonging to the race of animals or to the<BR>brute creation, born as an animal; (इस्), f. the brute<BR>kind.<BR>—तिर्यग्-ज्या, f. an oblique chord.<BR>—तिर्यग्-<BR>दिश्, क्, f. the region or part of the universe which<BR>lies horizontally, (opposed to ऊर्ध्व and अधस्.)<BR>—तिर्यग्-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, having curved or oblique<BR>edges.<BR>—तिर्यग्-नास or तिर्यङ्-नास, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>crooked-nosed, wry-nosed.<BR>—तिर्यग्-यवोदर (˚व-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. a barleycorn.<BR>—तिर्यग्-यान, अस्, m.<BR>‘going crookedly,’ a crab.<BR>—तिर्यग्-योन, अस्, m. an<BR>animal (as a bird &c.); [cf. तैर्यग्योन.]<BR>—तिर्यग्-<BR>योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, born of or as an animal; (इस्), f. the<BR>womb of an animal, the animal creation or race, organic<BR>nature (including plants).<BR>—तिर्यग्योन्य्-अन्वय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of the animal race; (अस्), m. the race of<BR>animals, birds, &c.<BR>—तिर्यग्-विद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pierced obliquely (as a vein in bleeding by an unskilful<BR>operator).<BR>—तिर्यङ्-निरय, अस्, m. the hell of animals<BR>or animal nature as a punishment for evil deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0374-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्च
तिरश्च, अम्, n., Ved. the cross-board of a bed-<BR>stead.<BR>—तिरश्चाङ्गिरस (˚च-आङ्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>Āṅgirasa Tiraśca; [cf. तिरश्ची.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्चता
तिरश्चता, ind., Ved. across, transversely, through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्चथा
तिरश्चथा, ind., Ved. aside, secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्ची
तिरश्ची, m., Ved., N. of a Ṛṣi, descendant of<BR>Aṅgiras.<BR>—तिरश्ची-निधन, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्चीन
तिरश्चीन, अस्, आ, अम्, lying across, oblique, trans-<BR>verse, sideways, awry, horizontal; irregular; आ-तिर-<BR>श्चीनम्, a little across.<BR>—तिरश्चीन-निधन, अम्,<BR>n., Ved., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—तिरश्चीन-पृश्नि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. spotted across.<BR>—तिरश्चीन-वंश, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. a bee-hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्
तिल् 1. तिल्, cl. 1. P. तेलति, &c., to go<BR>or move; [cf. rt. तिल्ल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्
तिल् 2. तिल् (probably an artificial rt. fr.<BR>तिल below), cl. 6. 10. P. तिलति, तेलयति,<BR>&c., to be unctuous or greasy; to oil or anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल|तिलः
तिल, अस्, m. the sesamum plant (Sesamum Indi-<BR>cum) which bears an oily seed; the seed of this<BR>plant (much used in Oriental cookery); a mole or<BR>spot compared to a seed of sesamum; a small particle<BR>or portion as much as a sesamum-seed [cf. कृष्ण-<BR>तिल and चर्म-तिल]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a chapter<BR>of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—तिल-कट, अम्, n. the farina<BR>of sesamum.<BR>—तिल-कल्क, अस्, m. dough made of<BR>ground sesamum.<BR>—तिलकल्क-ज, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), oil-cake made of the sediment of ground<BR>sesamum.<BR>—तिल-कालक, अस्, m. a mole, a dark spot<BR>under the skin; a disease of the penis in which the<BR>fleshy parts become black and die off; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having a mole or mark.<BR>—तिल-किट्ट, अम्, n. the<BR>caky sediment of sesamum after the oil is pressed out.<BR>—तिल-खलि, इस् or ई f. oil-cake made from sesa-<BR>mum.<BR>—तिल-गञ्जि-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place<BR>mentioned in the Rasika-ramaṇa by Raghu-nātha.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-b" target="_blank">Page0375-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—तिल-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a Grāma or township.<BR>—तिल-चित्र-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. a kind of bulbous<BR>plant.<BR>—तिल-चूर्ण, अम्, n. sesamum ground and<BR>pounded.<BR>—तिल-तण्डुलक, अम्, n. an embrace<BR>(as agreeable as rice mixed with sesamum).<BR>—तिल-<BR>तेजा, f. a kind of plant.<BR>—तिल-तैल, अम्, n. sesa-<BR>mum-oil.<BR>—तिलदेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚द-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha; [cf. तिलकेश्वर-तीर्थ.]<BR>—तिल-<BR>द्वादशी, f. a festival occurring on the twelfth day of<BR>a particular month.<BR>—तिल-धेनु, उस्, f. sesamum<BR>made up in the shape of a cow for the purpose of<BR>being presented to Brāhmans &c.<BR>—तिलधेनु-<BR>दान, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Vārāha-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—तिलन्-तुद, अस्, आ, अम्, bruising sesamum-<BR>seed, a sesamum-grinder, one who extracts oil out of<BR>sesamum-seed; [cf. तिल-पीड.]<BR>—तिल-पर्ण, अस्, m.<BR>turpentine; (ई), f. the sandal tree, Pterocarpus Santa-<BR>linus; frankincense; turpentine; (अम्), n. the leaf of<BR>the Tila tree; sandal-wood.<BR>—तिल-पर्णिका, f. or तिल-<BR>पर्णिक or तिल-पर्णक, अम्, n. red sanders, sandal-<BR>wood.<BR>—तिल-पिच्चट, अम्, n. (पिच्चट = पिष्टक),<BR>a sort of sweetmeat made chiefly of ground sesamum.<BR>—तिल-पिञ्ज, अस्, m. barren sesamum, bearing no<BR>blossom or yielding a seed which gives no oil; white<BR>sesamum; [cf. तिल-पेज, तिल्पिञ्ज, तैल-पिञ्ज.]<BR>—तिल-पीड, अस्, m. = तिलन्-तुद; [cf. तैल-<BR>पीड.]<BR>—तिल-पुष्पक, Terminalia Bellerica (वि-<BR>भीतक).<BR>—तिल-पेज, अस्, m. barren sesamum;<BR>[cf. तिल-पिञ्ज.]<BR>—तिल-भार, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>race.<BR>—तिल-भाविनी, f. jasmine.<BR>—तिल-भृष्ट,<BR>अम्, n. fried sesamum-seed.<BR>—तिल-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of or prepared from sesamum, abounding with<BR>sesamum.<BR>—तिल-मयूर, अस्, m. a species of pea-<BR>cock.<BR>—तिल-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed with sesamum.<BR>—तिल-रस, अस्, m. sesamum-oil.<BR>—तिल-वत्स, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having sesamum-seed (as it were) for<BR>children.<BR>—तिल-व्रतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, eating only sesa-<BR>mum-seeds in consequence of a vow.<BR>—तिल-शस्, ind.<BR>in pieces as small as sesamum-seeds.<BR>—तिल-सम्-<BR>बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed with sesamum-oil.<BR>—तिल-<BR>स्नेह, अस्, m. oil, especially of sesamum.<BR>—तिल-<BR>होम, अम्, n. burnt-offering of sesamum.<BR>—तिलाङ्-<BR>कित-दल (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a kind of bulbous<BR>plant, = तैल-कन्द.<BR>—तिलाढक? (˚ल-आढ्˚), N.<BR>of a monastery; (also read तिलटक, तिलढाक,<BR>तिल-शाक्य.) — तिलान्न (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. rice with<BR>sesamum-seeds.<BR>—तिलापत्या (˚ल-अप्˚), f. a plant<BR>bearing a small pungent seed, Nigella Indica.<BR>—तिलाम्बु (˚ल-अम्˚), उ, n. water with sesamum.<BR>—तिलोत्तमा (˚ल-उत्˚), f., N. of an Apsaras; a<BR>form of Dākṣāyaṇī; N. of a woman.<BR>—तिलोदक<BR>(˚ल-उद्˚), अम्, n. sesamum-seeds and water (as an<BR>oblation).<BR>—तिलौदन (˚ल-ओद्˚), अम्, n. a dish of<BR>milk, rice, and sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलक|तिलकं|तिलकः
तिलक, अस्, m. a species of tree with beautiful<BR>flowers, (so called either because it is similar in some<BR>way to the sesamum plant, or because it is used as an<BR>ornament like the mark on the forehead); a plant<BR>growing near water; a freckle, a natural mark under<BR>the skin (compared to a seed of sesamum); a kind of<BR>eruption of the skin; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a mark or marks<BR>made with coloured earths, sandal-wood, or unguents,<BR>upon the forehead and between the eyebrows, either as<BR>an ornament or a sectarial distinction; the ornament<BR>of anything (used in comp. to express greatness or<BR>distinction, e. g. त्रैलोक्य-तिलक, the ornament of<BR>the three worlds, i. e. a distinguished personage);<BR>(अस्), m. the burden of a song, = ध्रुवक; a<BR>species of horse; N. of a son of Pra-dyota; N. of a<BR>prince of Kampanā; (आ), f. a kind of necklace;<BR>(अम्), n. the bladder; the lungs; black sochal salt,<BR>a factitious salt containing sulphur and iron &c.; a<BR>disease, the appearance of dark spots on the skin,<BR>unattended with inflammation; alliteration; a kind<BR>of metre consisting of four lines of six syllables each;<BR>[cf. ऊर्ध्व-तिलकिन्, एण-तिलक, ख-त्˚, वसन्त-<BR>त्˚.]<BR>—तिलक-राज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—तिलक-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the second part<BR>of the Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa, treating of ceremonies.<BR>—तिलक-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—तिलका-<BR>श्रय (˚क-आश्˚), अस्, m. the forehead (‘the receptacle<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">Page0375-c+ 71</a>]<BR>of the Tilaka’).<BR>—तिलकेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha; [cf. तिलदेश्वर-तीर्थ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकक
तिलकक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकाय
तिलकाय, nom. A. तिलकायते, &c., to form the<BR>Tilaka mark on the forehead, to ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकित
तिलकित, अस्, आ, अम्, marked with the Tilaka, or-<BR>namented; freckled, spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकिन्
तिलकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, marked with the Tilaka; freckled,<BR>spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलु
तिलु, an adj. derived by Sāy. fr. तिल, and meaning<BR>‘fertile,’ ‘rich;’ [cf. तिल्विल below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्पिञ्ज
तिल्पिञ्ज, अस्, m., Ved. = तिल-पिञ्ज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्य|तिल्यं
तिल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, suited for the cultivation of<BR>sesamum, grown with sesamum; (अम्), n. a field of<BR>sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्व|तिल्वः
तिल्व or तिल्वक, अस्, m. the tree Symplocus<BR>Racemosa, = इङ्गुदी, Terminalia Catappa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्विल
तिल्विल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a fertile soil,<BR>prolific, rich; [cf. इभ्य-तिल्विल and धान्य-त्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्विलाय
तिल्विलाय, nom. A. तिल्विलायते, &c., Ved. to be<BR>fertile or rich, to cause fertility of soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकनिज
तिलकनिज तिलकनिज, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलिङ्ग
तिलिङ्ग तिलिङ्ग, N. of a place mentioned<BR>in the Kāka-rudra-saṃvāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलिङ्गिल
तिलिङ्गिल तिलिङ्गिल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (also तिमिङ्गिल, तिलेङ्गल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलित्स|तिलित्सः
तिलित्स तिलित्स or तिलिच्छ, अस्, m. a large<BR>snake; (according to some = Gokhura; according<BR>to others = the Boa or Boa Constrictor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्पिलिक
तिल्पिलिक तिल्पिलिक, अम्, n. = तिर्पिरिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्ल्
तिल्ल् तिल्ल्, cl. 1. P. तिल्लति, &c., to go or<BR>move; (a various reading for 1. तिल्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिव्य
तिव्य तिव्य, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठत्|तिष्ठन्त्
तिष्ठत् तिष्ठत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (pres. part. fr.<BR>rt. स्था), staying, remaining, abiding, standing,<BR>being, &c.<BR>—तिष्ठद्-गु, ind. (गु fr. गो), at<BR>milking-time (when the cows stand to be milked),<BR>after sunset.<BR>—तिष्ठद्-धोम (˚अत्-हो˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. (a sacrifice) at which the oblation is offered<BR>standing, (opposed to उपविष्ट-होम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्य|तिष्यः
तिष्य तिष्य, अस्, m., N. of a mythical<BR>being who like Kṛśānu is a kind of heavenly<BR>archer; an asterism regarded as shaped like an<BR>arrow and containing three stars, of which δ Cancri<BR>is one, (it is the sixth Nakṣatra of the old or eighth<BR>of the new order, and is also called Puṣya and<BR>Sidhya); the month Pauṣa (December-January);<BR>a common N. of men, ‘born under the asterism<BR>Tishya’ [cf. उप-तिष्य]; (आ), f. Terminalia To-<BR>mentosa; Emblica Officinalis; Emblic Myrobalan;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. the Kali-yuga, the fourth or present<BR>age; (अस्, आ, अम्), auspicious, fortunate, lucky (?).<BR>—तिष्य-केतु, उस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—तिष्य-<BR>पुनर्वसीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the asterisms<BR>Tiṣya and Punar-vasu.<BR>—तिष्य-पुष्पा, f. Emblic<BR>Myrobalan (आमलकी).<BR>—तिष्य-फला, f. Emblic<BR>Myrobalan.<BR>—तिष्य-रक्षिता, f., N. of the first<BR>wife of Aśoka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यक|तिष्यकः
तिष्यक, अस्, m. the month Pauṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिसृ
तिसृ तिसृ, तिस्रस्, f. pl. three; see त्रि,<BR>—तिसृ-धन्व, अम्, n., Ved. a bow with three<BR>arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिसृका
तिसृका, f., N. of a Grāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिस्रा
तिस्रा, f. the grass Andropogon Aciculatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिहन्
तिहन् तिहन्, आ, m. sickness; a good dis-<BR>position; rice; a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्
तीक् तीक्, cl. 1. A. तीकते, &c., to go or<BR>move; [cf. rt. तिक्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं|तीक्ष्णः
तीक्ष्ण तीक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तिज्; cf.<BR>the similar word तिग्म, which is more used than<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-a" target="_blank">Page0376-a+ 81</a>]<BR>तीक्ष्ण in the older literature), sharp (in all senses),<BR>hot, pungent, warm, fiery; acid (= खर-उष्ण);<BR>virulent, harsh, rough, rude, cross; injurious, noxious,<BR>unfriendly, unpropitious, inauspicious (e. g. तीक्ष्-<BR>णानि नक्षत्राणि, the inauspicious Nakṣatras,<BR>viz. Mūla, Ārdrā, Jyeṣṭhā, Ā-śleṣā); sharp, keen;<BR>intelligent; zealous, vehement, active, eager, energetic,<BR>quick; devoted, self-abandoning; devout, ascetic, a de-<BR>votee, zealot; (अस्), m. nitre; the resin of Boswellia<BR>Thurifera, = श्वेत-कुश or श्वेत-दर्भ; long<BR>pepper; black pepper; black mustard; Moringa<BR>Pterygosperma, horse-radish tree; Dalbergia Sissoo<BR>(शिंशपा), marjoram; Asa Fœtida; Galmei; N. of<BR>a Nāga; N. of a man; (आ), f., N. of several plants,<BR>= वचा, = सर्प-कङ्कालिका (wrongly translated<BR>‘the cast skin of a snake’); Mucuna Pruritus, =<BR>महा-ज्योतिष्मती, = अत्यम्ल-पर्णी; Cardiosper-<BR>mum Halicacabum; black mustard; a mystical name<BR>of the letter प्; (अम्), n. iron; steel; any weapon;<BR>anything sharp (as sharp language, &c.); heat, pun-<BR>gency; haste; sea-salt, nitre; poison, = मुष्कक;<BR>the tree Bignonia Suaveolens or (according to others)<BR>the scrotum or testicles; Piper Chaba; war, battle;<BR>plague, pestilence, epidemic destruction; death, dying;<BR>[cf. अ-तीक्ष्ण and सु-तीक्ष्ण.]<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-कण्-<BR>टक, अस्, m., N. of several plants, viz. thorn-apple;<BR>Capparis Aphylla; Terminalia Catappa; Acacia Ara-<BR>bica; Euphorbia Tortilis; (आ), f. a kind of plant, =<BR>कन्थारी.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-कन्द, अस्, m. ‘pungent root,’<BR>the onion.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-कर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, acting<BR>in a sharp or clever manner, active, energetic.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, ‘sharp in action,’ active,<BR>energetic, zealous, brisk; (अ), n. a clever work.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-कल्क, अस्, m. coriander.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-<BR>कान्ता, f. a form of Caṇḍikā.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-गन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a pungent smell,’ N. of two plants,<BR>= शोभाञ्जन and फणिज्झक; the resin of the<BR>Boswellia Thurifera; (आ), f., N. of several plants, =<BR>शोभाञ्जन, राजिका, वचा, श्वेत-वचा, कन्थारी,<BR>जीवन्ती; small cardamoms.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-गन्धक,<BR>अस्, m. = शोभाञ्जन.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-तण्डुला, f. long<BR>pepper.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, sharper, &c.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-ता, f. or तीक्ष्ण-त्व, अम्, n. warmth,<BR>heat, sharpness, pungency.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-तुण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a sharp beak (as a bird).<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-<BR>तैल, अम्, n. ‘pungent oil,’ the resin of the Shorea<BR>Robusta; the milky juice of the Euphorbia Lactea;<BR>spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-दंष्ट्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having sharp teeth or tusks; (अस्), m.<BR>a tiger.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-दंष्ट्रक, अस्, m. a leopard.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, sharp-edged, sharp; (अस्),<BR>m. a sword.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘having pun-<BR>gent leaves,’ coriander; the plant Terminalia Catappa;<BR>a species of sugar-cane.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-पुष्प, अम्,<BR>n. ‘pungent flower,’ cloves; (आ), f. Pandanus Odora-<BR>tissimus; the clove tree.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-प्रिय = तीक्ष्-<BR>ण-शूक, barley.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-फल, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>pungent fruit,’ coriander; black mustard.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-<BR>बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, sharp-witted, sagacious, acute.<BR>—ती-<BR>क्ष्ण-मञ्जरी, f. the betel plant.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-मुख,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, sharp-mouthed.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-मूल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having a pungent root,’ Moringa Pterygosperma;<BR>Alpinia Galanga.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, having<BR>hot rays (as the sun).<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-रस, अस्, m. ‘pun-<BR>gent liquid,’ saltpetre.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-लोह, अस्, m. ‘sharp<BR>iron,’ steel.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-विष, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>virulent poison.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-वृषण, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>strong testicles,’ N. of a bull.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-वेग, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, possessing great velocity; (अस्), m., N. of a Rak-<BR>shas.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-शूक, अस्, m. ‘having sharp awns,’<BR>barley.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-शृङ्ग, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having<BR>sharp horns.<BR>—तीक्ष्ण-सार, अस्, m. Dalbergia<BR>Sissoo (= शिंशपा); Bassia Latifolia; iron.<BR>—तीक्ष्-<BR>णांशु (˚ण-अं˚), उस्, उस्, उ, having hot rays; (उस्),<BR>m. the sun; fire.<BR>—तीक्ष्णांशु-तनय, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>son of the sun,’ the planet Saturn.<BR>—तीक्ष्णाग्नि<BR>(˚ण-अग्˚), इस्, m. ‘acid gastric juice,’ heartburn,<BR>dyspepsia.<BR>—तीक्ष्णाग्र (˚ण-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sharp-pointed; (अस्), m. Zingiber Zerumbet.<BR>—तीक्ष्-<BR>णायस (˚ण + अयस for अयस्, q. v.), अम्, n.<BR>‘sharp iron,’ steel; (अस्, ई, अम्), made of steel,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">Page0376-b+ 74</a>]<BR>sharp.<BR>—तीक्ष्णेषु (˚ण-इषु), उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>sharp arrows.<BR>—तीक्ष्णोपाय (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>forcible means, a strong measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0375-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णक|तीक्ष्णकः
तीक्ष्णक, अस्, m. = मुष्कक, Bignonia Suave-<BR>olens or (according to others) the scrotum or testicles;<BR>black mustard; long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णिष्ठ
तीक्ष्णिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णीयस्
तीक्ष्णीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, sharper, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीम्
तीम् तीम्, cl. 4. P. तीम्यति, &c., to be<BR>wet or moist; [cf. rt. तिम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्
तीर् तीर्, cl. 10. P., to accomplish, (better<BR>regarded as a nominal verb; see under<BR>तीर below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर|तीरं|तीरः
तीर तीर, अम्, n. (fr. rt. तॄ), a shore, a<BR>bank; margin, brink, edge; the brim of a vessel;<BR>a sort of arrow [cf. the Pers. تير]; (अस्), m. tin<BR>[cf. तीव्र]; (ई), f. a kind of arrow, three-fourths of<BR>which consists of reed and a fourth part of iron.<BR>—तीर-ग्रह, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—तीर-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, growing or standing near a shore;<BR>(अस्), m. a tree near a shore.<BR>—तीर-भुक्ति, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a country, the modern Tirhut, a province in<BR>the east of central Hindūstan, lying to the north of<BR>Bahar (fr. तीर, a bank, and भुक्ति, here signifying<BR>a limit; being bounded on the east by Bhaugulpore,<BR>on the west by Sarum, on the south by the Ganges,<BR>and on the north by the skirts of the Himā-<BR>laya mountains); [cf. त्रि-भुक्ति.]<BR>—तीर-रुह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, growing on a bank; (अस्), m. a tree<BR>growing on a bank.<BR>—तीर-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated<BR>on a bank or shore.<BR>—तीरान्तर (˚र-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the opposite bank or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरय
तीरय, nom. P. तीरयति, -यितुम्, to get through,<BR>cross over, to finish, accomplish, complete success-<BR>fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरित|तीरितं
तीरित, अस्, आ, अम्, finished, settled, completed,<BR>adjudged, decided according to evidence; (अम्), n.<BR>completion of any act or affair; corrupt or improper<BR>non-infliction of a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरण
तीरण तीरण, a kind of plant, = करञ्जिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीराट
तीराट तीराट, अस्, m. = तिरीट, Symplocos<BR>Racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरु|तीरुः
तीरु तीरु, perhaps a wrong reading for<BR>भीरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्ण|तीर्णः
तीर्ण तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्. See under rt. तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्त्वा
तीर्त्वा तीर्त्वा, ind. See under rt. तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ|तीर्थं|तीर्थः
तीर्थ तीर्थ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. तॄ, the<BR>masc. is only exceptionally used in epic poetry), a<BR>passage, way, road, ford; especially a Ghāt or the<BR>stairs of a landing-place, a descent into a river, a<BR>bathing-place, a holy place, a shrine or sacred place<BR>of pilgrimage, as Benares &c., especially particular<BR>spots along the course of sacred streams, as the<BR>Ganges &c., or in the vicinity of sacred springs;<BR>any piece of water; (in sacrificial language) the path<BR>to the altar between the Cātvāla and Utkara; a<BR>channel, a canal, watercourse; the usual way, the<BR>usual or right manner (e. g. तीर्थेन or तीर्थतस्,<BR>in right order, in the usual way; अ-तीर्थेन, in a<BR>wrong way); the right place, the right moment;<BR>a sacred place, a sacred moment, opportunity; a<BR>sacrifice; advice, instruction, counsel; a counsellor,<BR>an adviser; a sacred preceptor, a Guru; an oppor-<BR>tunity, a means, an expedient; certain lines or parts<BR>of the hand sacred to the deities &c. (as the root<BR>of the two smaller fingers, to Prajāpati; the tops of<BR>the fingers, to the gods; the space between the<BR>thumb and finger, to the manes; the root of the<BR>thumb, to Brahma or to the Veda; सौम्यन् तीर्-<BR>थम् = the middle of the hand); an object of<BR>veneration, a sacred object; a worthy object or<BR>person, a fit recipient, (sometimes at the end of<BR>names, e. g. आनन्द-तीर्थ, जय-त्˚, &c.); a Brāh-<BR>man; a minister; a N. given to certain officers<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">Page0376-c+ 79</a>]<BR>(eighteen or fifteen in number) who are in close<BR>attendance on a king; pudendum muliebre; menstrual<BR>courses of a woman; a school of philosophy (= दर्-<BR>शन), a sect; ascertainment of disease; fire.<BR>—तीर्-<BR>थ-कमण्डलु, उस्, उ, m. n. a pot with water<BR>from a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—तीर्थ-कर, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, ‘creating a passage (through life, or through the<BR>circuit of life);’ (अस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; one<BR>of the synonyms of an Arhat or sanctified teacher of<BR>the Jaina sect; (with Buddhists) an ascetic (‘bathing<BR>in holy waters’).<BR>—तीर्थ-काक, अस्, m. a crow at<BR>a sacred bathing-place, i. e. one not in his own<BR>proper place.<BR>—तीर्थ-काशिका, f., N. of a work by<BR>Gaṅgā-dhara.<BR>—तीर्थ-कीर्त्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, one whose<BR>mere fame makes holy.<BR>—तीर्थ-कृत्, त्, m. =<BR>तीर्थ-कर, a Jaina Arhat.<BR>—तीर्थ-गोपाल, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—तीर्थङ्-कर,<BR>अस्, m. = तीर्थ-कर, a Jaina Arhat.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>चिन्ता-मणि, इस्, m. f., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Saṃskāra-tattva by Raghu-nandana, treating of the<BR>Indian sacraments.<BR>—तीर्थ-तम, अम्, n. (fr. तीर्-<BR>थ with the affix of the superl.), a more sacred<BR>place of pilgrimage; an object of the highest sanctity.<BR>—तीर्थ-देव, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—तीर्-<BR>थ-ध्वाङ्क्ष^1, अस्, m. ‘a crow at a place of pil-<BR>grimage,’ a contemptuous epithet; [cf. तीर्थ-काक.]<BR>—तीर्थ-पति, इस्, m., N. of the chief of a sect.<BR>—तीर्थ-पाद्, पात्, पदी, पत्, ‘one whose feet are<BR>sacred or sanctify,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>पादीय, अस्, m. an adherent of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, rendered holy, sacred.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>महा-ह्रद, अस्, m., N. of a shrine or place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—तीर्थ-महिमन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Śūdra-dharma-tattva, treating of the<BR>duties of the Śūdras.<BR>—तीर्थ-माहात्म्य, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva by Halā-<BR>yudha.<BR>—तीर्थ-यात्रा, f. a visit to any sacred<BR>shrine or bathing-place, a pilgrimage; N. of a<BR>chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—तीर्थयात्रा-तत्त्व,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a part of the Smṛti-tattva by Raghu-<BR>nandana.<BR>—तीर्थयात्रा-पर्वन्, अ, n., N. of a sec-<BR>tion of the third book of the Mahā-bhārata (ch. 80-<BR>156).<BR>—तीर्थ-यात्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going to a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—तीर्थ-राजी, f. ‘a line of sacred bathing-<BR>places,’ epithet of Benares.<BR>—तीर्थ-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having descents to the water, abounding in<BR>sacred bathing-places; (अती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—तीर्-<BR>थ-वाक, अस्, m. the hair of the head.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>वायस, अस्, m. a crow at a Tīrtha; see तीर्थ-<BR>काक.<BR>—तीर्थ-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling at a place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—तीर्थ-विधि, इस्, m. the rites ob-<BR>served at a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—तीर्थ-शिला, f. the<BR>stone steps leading to a bathing-place.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>श्रवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one whose mere fame is sacred<BR>or sanctifies.<BR>—तीर्थ-श्राद्ध-प्रयोग, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Śrāddha-cintā-maṇi by Śiva-<BR>rāma, treating of funeral ceremonies.<BR>—तीर्थ-<BR>सेनि, इस्, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda.<BR>—तीर्थ-सेविन्, ई, इनी, इ, visiting shrines,<BR>a pilgrim; (ई), m. a kind of crane, Ardea Nivea.<BR>—तीर्थ-सौख्य, अम्, n. title of a particular work<BR>or of a part of a work.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161202. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 308-310. note: guttural nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थक|तीर्थकः
तीर्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, holy, sacred, venerable;<BR>(अस्), m. an ascetic Brāhman; N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थिक|तीर्थिकः
तीर्थिक, अस्, m. an ascetic Brāhman (visiting<BR>holy shrines or bathing-places), a pilgrim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थीकृ
तीर्थी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make sacred.<BR>—तीर्थी-करण, अम्, n. the<BR>act of rendering sacred; (अस्, ई, अम्), sanctifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थीभूत
तीर्थी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become sacred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ्य|तीर्थ्यः
तीर्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a ford or to a<BR>sacred bathing-place, &c.; (अस्), m. an ascetic; [cf.<BR>तैर्थ्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्
तीव् तीव्, cl. 1. P. तीवति, &c., to be<BR>large or strong, to be fat or corpulent;<BR>[cf. rt. नीव्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीवर|तीवरः
तीवर तीवर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. तीर्),<BR>the ocean; a hunter, the adulterine offspring of a<BR>Rājaputrī by a Kṣatriya; one who lives by killing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">Page0377-a+ 77</a>]<BR>and selling game; a fisherman (?); (ई), f. the wife<BR>of a hunter or of a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्र|तीव्रं|तीव्रः
तीव्र तीव्र, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt. तिज्;<BR>probably connected with rt. तीव् and rt. 2. तु), strong,<BR>severe, violent, intense, fierce, ardent, impetuous,<BR>sharp, keen, acute, poignant, pungent, sour; hot,<BR>warm; flashing, pervading; much, exceeding, ex-<BR>cessive, endless, unbounded, unlimited; horrible,<BR>dreadful; (अस्), m. sharpness, &c.; a hunter (?); an<BR>epithet of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of several plants, viz.<BR>Helleborus Niger; black mustard; a sort of Dūrvā<BR>or bent grass, = गण्ड-दूर्वा; basil, = तरदी, =<BR>महा-ज्योतिष्मती; N. of a river, the Padma-vatī,<BR>in the east of Bengal; (अम्), n. heat, pungency; a<BR>shore [cf. तीर]; tin [cf. तीर]; iron, steel [cf.<BR>तीक्ष्ण]; (अम्), ind. violently, impetuously, sharply,<BR>fiercely; much, excessively.<BR>—तीव्र-कन्द or (ac-<BR>cording to a various reading) तीव्र-कण्ठ, अस्, m.<BR>a pungent kind of Arum.<BR>—तीव्र-गति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>moving rapidly, quick, swift.<BR>—तीव्र-गन्धा, f.<BR>cumin-seed or Ptychotis Ajowan.<BR>—तीव्र-ज्वाला, f.<BR>Grislea Tomentosa; [cf. अग्नि-ज्वाला and वह्नि-<BR>शिखा.]<BR>—तीव्र-ता, f. violence, sharpness, heat,<BR>pungency.<BR>—तीव्र-दारु, उस्, m. a species of tree.<BR>—तीव्र-पौरुष, अम्, n. daring heroism, such as<BR>the storming of a fortress.<BR>—तीव्र-रोष-समाविष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filled with fierce anger.<BR>—तीव्र-वेदना,<BR>f. excessive pain, agony, the pain of damnation.<BR>—तीव्र-शोक-समाविष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, filled with<BR>excessive sorrow.<BR>—तीव्र-शोकार्त (˚क-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, afflicted with poignant grief.<BR>—तीव्र-सव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an Ekāha sacrifice.<BR>—तीव्र-सुत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. pressed out of a sour or fermenting substance;<BR>(Sāy. तीव्र-सुत, अस्, आ, अम्), whose expressed juice<BR>is sharp or pungent; (त्), m., N. of an Ekāha sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>—तीव्रानन्द (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘having intense<BR>joy,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—तीव्रान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. becoming strong or sharp at the close<BR>(i. e. by a process of fermentation); having a sure or<BR>excessive result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रय
तीव्रय, nom. P. -यति, -यितुम्, to make sharp,<BR>strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीसट
तीसट तीसट, अस्, m., N. of a writer on<BR>medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु 1. तु, the base of some of the cases of<BR>the 2nd personal pronoun; [cf. त्व.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु 2. तु, cl. 2. P., Ved. तवीति and तौति,<BR>तूताव, तोतुम् and तवितुम्, to have authority<BR>or power, to be strong; to attain; to thrive or increase,<BR>to fill, become full; to go or move; to injure, hurt,<BR>kill: Caus., Ved. (only used in aor. तूतोत्), to make<BR>strong or efficient, make valid, accomplish; [cf. Zend<BR>tav, ‘to be able;’ tavan, ‘powerful:’ Pers. توان tuvân,<BR>‘power;’ توانم tuvânam, ‘I can:’ Gr. τύλος, τύλη,<BR>τυλόω, ταΰς: Lat. tumor, tumere, tumidus, tu-<BR>mulus (?), tuber, tueri, totus: Umbr. Osc. tauta,<BR>tota, touta, ‘town;’ tut-icus, ‘townish:’ Goth.<BR>thiuda, thiuth, thiuthyan: Angl. Sax. thū-ma,<BR>‘the thumb;’ theod, ‘people:’ Old Germ. dū-mo,<BR>‘the thumb:’ Slav. ty-ti, ‘to grow fat;’ tu-kŭ, ‘fat:’<BR>Lith. tau-ka-i, ‘fat;’ tunk-u, ‘I become fat:’ Old<BR>Pruss. tau-ta, ‘land, country:’ Cambro-Brit. tyv-u,<BR>‘to increase.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु 3. तु, ind. (a particle, perhaps connected<BR>with the pronom. base 2. त, or with the Vedic pro-<BR>noun त्व; never found at the beginning of a sentence<BR>or verse, and causing the verb with which it is con-<BR>structed to retain its accent). As a particle implying<BR>‘earnest entreaty’ or ‘urgent request’ it is often used in<BR>the Veda, like Lat. dum, with an imperative, and may<BR>be translated by ‘pray!’ ‘I beg,’ ‘do’ (e. g. आ त्वेत,<BR>come here, do); or it may be rendered by ‘well,’<BR>‘now then,’ ‘now,’ ‘just.’ As an adversative particle<BR>it is equivalent to ‘but,’ ‘on the contrary,’ ‘on the<BR>other hand’ (e. g. न च्छिनति जनयति तु, he<BR>does not destroy but he produces). The sense ‘but’<BR>is most common in later Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु is sometimes, however, used for च, ‘and’<BR>(e. g. आ समुद्रात् पूर्वाद् आ समुद्रात् तु पश्चि-<BR>मात्, to the eastern sea and to the western sea); and<BR>even for वा, ‘or’ (e. g. उष्ट्र-यानं समारुह्य<BR>खर-यानं तु, having ascended a camel-carriage<BR>or one drawn by donkeys). Sometimes it appears to<BR>be incorrectly written for नु (e. g. किन् तु for किन्<BR>नु). Occasionally it seems to be used for तदा after<BR>चेत् (e. g. तां चेद् न दित्सेयम् प्रमथ्यैनां<BR>हरेयुस् तु, if I were not willing to give her then<BR>they would take her by force). Not unfrequently तु<BR>is used as an expletive to fill out a verse or prevent<BR>the blending of vowels (e. g. ईर्ष्यी घृणी त्व्<BR>अ-सन्तुष्टः, &c., an envious man, one over-com-<BR>passionate, a discontented man, &c.). तु — तु,<BR>although — yet; अपि-तु, moreover; किन् तु, but,<BR>nevertheless, notwithstanding; परन् तु, more-<BR>over, but, nevertheless; न त्व् एव तु, but by no<BR>means. According to lexicographers तु implies dis-<BR>junction, mutual opposition, alternative, asseveration,<BR>emphasis, conjunction, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुःखार
तुःखार तुःखार, आस्, m. pl. (probably =<BR>तुखार), N. of a race of people; (अस्), m. a man<BR>of this race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुक्
तुक् तुक्. See 1. तुच् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुकज्योतिर्विद्
तुकज्योतिर्विद् तुक-ज्योतिर्-विद्, त्, m., N. of<BR>an astronomer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुकाक्षीरी
तुकाक्षीरी तुकाक्षीरी, f. = तुगाक्षीरी, the<BR>manna of bamboos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुक्क
तुक्क तुक्क, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुखार|तुखारः
तुखार तुखार, आस्, m. pl., N. of a non-<BR>Hindū people to the north-west of Madhya-deśa;<BR>(often written तुषार); [cf. तुःखार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुगा
तुगा तुगा, f. the so-called Tabāṣīr (fr.<BR>त्वक्-क्षीरा), a white secretion found sometimes in<BR>the joints of bamboos, the manna of bamboos.<BR>—तु-<BR>गा-क्षीरी, f. a peculiar kind of bamboo manna; [cf.<BR>तुका-क्षीरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुग्र
तुग्र तुग्र, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Bhujyu who was protected by the Aśvins; N. of an<BR>enemy of Indra, conquered by the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुग्रिय
तुग्रिय, Ved. = तुग्र्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुग्र्य
तुग्र्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic of Bhujyu; N.<BR>of a man or of a race; (आ), f. water.<BR>—तुग्र्या-<BR>वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. delighting in the Tugryas; epi-<BR>thet of Indra and of Soma; (Sāy.) increasing water,<BR>increasing with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुग्वन्
तुग्वन् तुग्वन्, अ, n., Ved. = तीर्थ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्ग|तुंग|तुङ्गः
तुङ्ग तुङ्ग. See under rt. 2. तुज् next col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्
तुच् 1. तुच् or 1. तुज्, क्, f., Ved. offspring,<BR>children, propagation; [cf. तोक and तोक्मन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुजि
तुजि, इस्, f., Ved. propagation, begetting children;<BR>(इस्), m., Ved., N. of a man protected by Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्
तुच् 2. तुच् in आ-तुच् (q. v.), growing dusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छ|तुच्छं|तुच्छः
तुच्छ तुच्छ, अस्, आ, अम् (probably for तुष),<BR>empty, void, vain, light; small, little, trifling; aban-<BR>doned, deserted; low, mean, insignificant, contemptible;<BR>miserable, poor; worthless; (आ), f. the Indigo plant,<BR>= तुत्था; (अम्), n. chaff; [cf. Lith. tuszcias,<BR>‘empty.’]<BR>—तुच्छ-त्व, अम्, n. emptiness, mean-<BR>ness, inanity, vanity.<BR>—तुच्छ-द्रु, उस्, m. (‘the<BR>sapless tree’), the castor-oil tree, Ricinus Communis.<BR>—तुच्छ-धान्य or तुच्छ-धान्यक, अम्, n.<BR>straw, chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छक
तुच्छक, अस्, आ, अम्, void, empty, &c., = तुच्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छय
तुच्छय, nom. P. तुच्छयति, &c., to make<BR>empty or poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छीकृ
तुच्छी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to consider as vain or idle, to despise, contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छ्य|तुछ्य
तुच्छ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. void, empty, vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्
तुज् 1. तुज्. See 1. तुच् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्
तुज् 2. तुज् or तुञ्ज्, cl. 1. 6. P., Ved. तो-<BR>जति, तुजति, तुतोज, तोजितुम्, or cl. 1. P.<BR>तुञ्जति, तुतुञ्ज, तुञ्जितुम्, Ved. Inf. तुजसे, to<BR>strike, hit; impel, push; to press out, emit; to stir<BR>up, urge on, instigate, incite; wave to and fro; to<BR>hasten; Ved. reach, extend, project; to kill or hurt;<BR>to guard, protect, to be strong; to clothe; to live:<BR>Pass. तुज्यते, &c., to be struck, to be vexed, &c.: Caus.<BR>तुजयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to promote, instigate; to<BR>move quickly, spring, run [cf. तूतुजान]; तुञ्जयति<BR>or तोजयति, -यितुम्, to hurt, to injure or kill; to be<BR>strong or vigorous; to give or take; to dwell, abide;<BR>to shine, speak; [cf. तूतुजि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्ग|तुंग|तुङ्गः
तुङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, high, elevated, prominent, erect,<BR>lofty; long; vaulted; chief, principal; strong, passionate<BR>[cf. उत्-तुङ्ग]; (अस्), m. an elevation, height, culmina-<BR>tion, altitude; a mountain; top, highest point, peak,<BR>vertex; the superior apsis or aphelion of a planet; (meta-<BR>phorically) a throne; a wise man; a rhinoceros; the<BR>planet Mercury; the tree Rottleria Tinctoria; the<BR>cocoa-nut; N. of a man; (आ), f., N. of a tree [cf.<BR>शमी]; also = तुगा, bamboo manna; N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of eight syllables each; N. of<BR>a river in the Mysore territory; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>Ocimum (वर्वरा); turmeric; night; (अम्), n.<BR>the stamina of the lotus blossom; [cf. Lith. tunkù,<BR>‘to grow fat:’ Russ. tucnyĭ, ‘fat:’ Hib. tonngo, ‘a<BR>billowy sea;’ tonnghail, tonnta, ‘waved.’]<BR>—तुङ्ग-<BR>कूट, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—तुङ्ग-ता, f. or तुङ्ग-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>altitude, loftiness, height, passionateness.<BR>—तुङ्ग-<BR>धन्वन्, आ, m., N. of a king of Suhma.<BR>—तुङ्ग-<BR>नाभ, अस्, m. a particular species of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR>—तुङ्ग-नासिका or ई, f. a woman having a<BR>prominent nose.<BR>—तुङ्ग-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—तुङ्ग-बल, अस्, m., N. of a warrior.<BR>—तुङ्ग-भ, अम्, n. the lunar mansion in which<BR>a planet reaches its apsis, the apsis of a planet.<BR>—तुङ्ग-भद्र, अस्, m. a restive elephant or one<BR>in rut; (आ), f., N. of a river in the Mysore territory,<BR>commonly called Tumbudra, formed by the junction<BR>of the Tuṅga and Bhadra rivers.<BR>—तुङ्ग-मुख,<BR>अस्, m. a rhinoceros, (‘having a prominent snout.’)<BR>—तुङ्ग-वीज, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), quick-<BR>silver, (‘forming long seed-like balls.’)<BR>—तुङ्ग-वेणा,<BR>f., N. of a river in the Dekha.<BR>—तुङ्ग-शेखर,<BR>अस्, m. the top of a mountain.<BR>—तुङ्ग-शैल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the high mountain,’ N. of a mountain with a<BR>temple of Śiva.<BR>—तुङ्गी-नास, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>poisonous insect.<BR>—तुङ्गी-पति, इस्, m. the moon,<BR>(‘lord of night.’)<BR>—तुङ्गीश (˚गी-ईश), अस्, m. the<BR>moon; the sun; an epithet of Śiva; N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—तुङ्गेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>mountains,’ an epithet of Śiva; a temple of Śiva;<BR>[cf. गिरिश and गिरीश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गक|तुङ्गकः
तुङ्गक, अस्, m. the tree Rottleria Tinctoria;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a sacred forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गिन्|तुंगिन्
तुङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, high, lofty; (ई), m. a planet<BR>at the apex of its orbit or of its position with regard<BR>to others considered astrologically; (इनी), f., N. of a<BR>plant, = महा-शतावरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्
3. तुज्, क् (?), f., Ved. shock, impulse; pressure;<BR>assault; (क्, क्, क्), pressing, urging on, impelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्य
तुज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be struck or pushed, to<BR>be impelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुञ्ज|तुंज
तुञ्ज, अस्, m., Ved. shock, assault; a Daitya, a<BR>demon; a thunderbolt; giving; (अस्, आ, अम्), noxious,<BR>mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुजि
तुजि तुजि. See under 1. तुच्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुञ्जीन
तुञ्जीन तुञ्जीन, अस्, m., N. of several kings<BR>of Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुट्
तुट् तुट्, cl. 6. P. तुटति, तुतोट, तुटितुम्,<BR>to dispute, quarrel, wrangle; to hurt or<BR>injure: Caus. P. तोटयति, &c., a wrong reading for<BR>त्रोटयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुटितुट|तुटितुटः
तुटितुट तुटितुट, अस्, m. a N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुटुम|तुटुमः
तुटुम तुटुम, अस्, m. a mouse or rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड्
तुड् तुड्, cl. 1. 6. P. तोडति, तुडति, तुतोड,<BR>तोडितुम् or तुडितुम्, to tear, split, break,<BR>cut, pull to pieces; to push; to injure, hurt or kill;<BR>to bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड्ड्
तुड्ड् तुड्ड्, cl. 1. P. तुड्डति, &c., to dis-<BR>respect, disregard, contemn; [cf. rt. तूड्<BR>and तोड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्
तुण् तुण्, cl. 6. P. तुणति, तुतोण, तोणि-<BR>तुम्, to curve, bend or make crooked; to<BR>be crooked or curved; to act fraudulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुणि|तुणिः
तुणि तुणि, इस्, m. = कुणि = तुन्न, the tree<BR>Cedula Toona.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुणिक
तुणिक तुणिक (तूणिक ?), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>tree, = नन्दी-वृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्ड्|तुंड्
तुण्ड् तुण्ड्, cl. 1. A. तुण्डते, &c., = तुड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्ड|तुंड|तुंडं|तुण्डं|तुण्डः
तुण्ड, अम्, n. (according to some also अस्, m.),<BR>a beak, snout (of a hog &c.), trunk (of an elephant),<BR>mouth, face; the point of an instrument; (अस्), m.<BR>a N. of Śiva; of a Rakṣas or demon; [cf. अस्थि-त्˚,<BR>कङ्क-त्˚, काक-त्˚, &c.]<BR>—तुण्ड-देव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a race or of a particular class of men.<BR>—तुण्ड-<BR>देव-भक्त, अम्, n. the district inhabited by the<BR>Tuṇḍa-devas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डक
तुण्डक = तुण्ड above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डकेरिका|तुंडकेरिका
तुण्डकेरिका, f. = तुण्डिकेरी, the cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डकेरी
तुण्डकेरी, f. a cucurbitaceous plant, Momordica<BR>Monadelpha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डि|तुंडि|तुंडिः|तुण्डिः
तुण्डि, इस्, m. a beak, the mouth, the face; (इस्),<BR>f. the navel, a prominent navel [cf. तुन्दि]; em-<BR>physema or distention of the navel (in infants); a<BR>kind of gourd or cucumber, = ईर्वारु, कुष्माण्ड;<BR>[cf. तुण्डी in कटु-तुण्डी, तिक्त-त्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिक|तुंडिक
तुण्डिक, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with a trunk or<BR>snout; (आ), f. the navel [cf. तुन्दिका]; the plant<BR>Momordica Monadelpha; [cf. कटु-तुण्डिका and<BR>काक-त्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेर
तुण्डिकेर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race; (अस्), m. the<BR>prince of this race; (ई), f. the cotton plant; a kind<BR>of cucumber, Momordica Monadelpha; a large boil<BR>or swelling on the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेरिका
तुण्डिकेरिका, f. Momordica Monadelpha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेरिन्
तुण्डिकेरिन्, ई, m. a species of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेशी
तुण्डिकेशी, f. a sort of gourd, Momordica Mona-<BR>delpha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिचेल
तुण्डिचेल, अम्, n. a particular kind of costly<BR>garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिभ|तुंडिभ|तुण्डिभः
तुण्डिभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having a prominent or<BR>elevated navel; [cf. तुन्दिभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिल|तुंडिल|तुण्डिलः
तुण्डिल, अस्, आ, अम्, talkative; speaking harshly<BR>or severely; loquacious; having a prominent or<BR>elevated navel; [cf. तुन्दिल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डेल
तुण्डेल तुण्डेल, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a kind<BR>of evil spirit or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुतात
तुतात तुतात, अस्, m., N. of the founder of<BR>a philosophical system; [cf. तौतातिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुतुर्वणि
तुतुर्वणि तुतुर्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. 1. तुर्),<BR>Ved. striving to bring near or obtain; (Sāy.) acting<BR>with alacrity, acting speedily; [cf. जुगुर्वणि and<BR>शुशुक्वनि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ|तुत्थं|तुत्थः
तुत्थ तुत्थ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. तुद्),<BR>fire; (आ), f. the Indigo plant; small cardamoms;<BR>(अम्), n. blue vitriol, sulphate of copper, especially<BR>considered as an ointment or medical application to<BR>the eyes; a collyrium extracted from the Amomum<BR>Zanthorrhiza; a stone, a rock.<BR>—तुत्थाञ्जन<BR>(˚थ-अञ्˚), अम्, n. blue vitriol as an ointment or<BR>medicinal application to the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थक|तुत्थकं
तुत्थक, अम्, n. blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थय
तुत्थय (originally ‘to cover with blue vitriol ?’),<BR>nom. P. तुत्थयति, -यितुम्, to screen, veil, cover;<BR>to spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुथ
तुथ तुथ, Ved. occurring in certain<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">Page0378-b+ 74</a>]<BR>formularies, (explained in commentaries by ब्रह्म-<BR>रूप, ‘having the shape or form of Brahma.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुद्
तुद् 1. तुद्, cl. 6. P. A. तुदति, -ते, तुतोद,<BR>तुतुदे, तोत्स्यति, -ते, अतौत्सीत्, अतुत्त,<BR>तोत्तुम्, to strike, hit, push; to goad, prick; to<BR>bruise; to pain, wound, sting, vex, harass, tease,<BR>torture, torment: Caus. तोदयति, -यितुम्, अतूतु-<BR>दत्, to push &c.: Desid. तुतुत्सति, -ते: Intens.<BR>तोतुद्यते, तोतोत्ति; [cf. rt. तुन्द्, तोत्त्र, तोद;<BR>Gr. Τυδ-εύ-ς, Τύδ-α-ς, Τυνδ-άρη-ς, Τυνδ-άρεο-ς,<BR>Τυνδ-άρεω-ς, Τυνδάρ-ιχο-ς; Lat. tund-o, tud-es,<BR>tud-i-tare, dea Pertunda, tussis; Goth. staut-<BR>an; Old Germ. stoz-an; Mod. Germ. stoss-en;<BR>Angl. Sax. a-stintan, ‘to blunt:’ the initial s is<BR>original, and dropped in Sanskrit.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुद्
2. तुद्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of a comp.) striking,<BR>pricking, goading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुद
तुद, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) striking,<BR>pricking, stinging, paining, tormenting [cf. तिलन्-<BR>तुद and अरुन्-तुद, ‘striking a wound’]; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—तुद्-आदि, the grammatical<BR>designation of the sixth class of roots or those of<BR>which तुद् is the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्न|तुन्नः
तुन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, struck, hit; pricked; goaded,<BR>tormented, hurt, vexed, injured; cut, broken, cut<BR>down &c.; (अस्), m. the Toon or Tuna tree, the<BR>wood of which bears some resemblance to mahogany<BR>and is used for furniture &c.; Cedrela Toona.<BR>—तुन्न-वाय, अस्, m. a tailor.<BR>—तुन्न-सेवनी,<BR>f. the suture of a wound (in surgery); a suture of<BR>the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन
तुन तुन, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), Ved. a various<BR>reading (in the Sāma-veda) for तन, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्द्
तुन्द् तुन्द्, cl. 1. P. तुन्दति, &c., to be<BR>busy, active; to search, seek; [cf. rt.<BR>त्रन्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्द|तुंद|तुंदं|तुन्दं|तुन्दः
तुन्द तुन्द, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1. तुद्),<BR>a protuberant belly, the belly, abdomen; (अस्, ई), m. f.<BR>the navel.<BR>—तुन्द-कूपिका or तुन्द-कूपी, f. the<BR>cavity of the navel.<BR>—तुन्द-परिमार्ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who is in the habit of stroking his belly (in the<BR>literal sense).<BR>—तुन्द-परिमृज, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who is in the habit of rubbing his belly (meta-<BR>phorically), a lazy man, a sloth, a sluggard.<BR>—तुन्द-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दि|तुंदि|तुन्दिः
तुन्दि, इस्, इ, f. n. the belly; (इस्), f. the navel;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिक|तुंदिक|तुन्दिकः
तुन्दिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a large or prominent<BR>navel or belly, fat, corpulent; (आ), f. the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिकर|तुंदिकरः|तुन्दिकरः
तुन्दिकर, अस्, m. the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दित|तुंदित|तुन्दितः
तुन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, or तुन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or<BR>तुन्दिभ or तुन्दिल, अस्, आ, अम्, having a large or<BR>prominent belly or navel; gorbellied, corpulent.<BR>—तुन्दिल-फला, f. Cucumis Utilissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्न|तुन्नः
तुन्न तुन्न. See under rt. 1. तुद् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुप्
तुप् तुप् or तुफ् or तुम्प् or तुम्फ्, cl. 1.<BR>6. P. तोपति, तुपति, तोफति, तुफति,<BR>तुम्पति, तुम्फति, &c., (in the last two the form<BR>in cl. 1. will only differ from that in cl. 6. by the<BR>accent), to injure, hurt, wound; kill; तुम्प्, cl. 10.<BR>P. तुम्पयति, &c., a various reading for तुम्ब्, q. v.;<BR>[cf. Gr. τύπ-τ-ω, τύπο-ς, τυπή, τύμ-μα, τυπά(δ)ς,<BR>τύμπ-ανο-ν; Lat. stupeo; Old Germ. stumpf,<BR>stumb-alon, stumph; Old Island. stūf-r.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुबरी
तुबरी तुबरी, f. = तुम्बरी, coriander; a<BR>bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुभ्
तुभ् तुभ्, cl. 1. A., 4. 9. P. तोभते,<BR>तुभ्यति, तुभ्नाति, तुतोभ, तुतुभे,<BR>तोभितुम्, to push, to kill, hurt, injure in any man-<BR>ner; [cf. स्तुभ्; Goth. thiubs; Angl. Sax. theof.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुभ
तुभ तुभ, अस्, m. = स्तुभ, a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमल
तुमल तुमल, a various reading for तु-<BR>मुल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमिञ्ज
तुमिञ्ज तुमिञ्ज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुर|तुमुरः
तुमुर तुमुर, अस्, अम्, m. n. mingled com-<BR>bat; [cf. तुमुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुल|तुमुलं|तुमुलः
तुमुल तुमुल, अस्, आ, अम्, tumultuous,<BR>noisy; excited, perplexed, confused; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>uproar, tumult, tumultuous sound, clang, clatter,<BR>tumultuous or confused combat, melée, confusion;<BR>(अस्), m. Beleric Myrobalan, Terminalia Bellerica;<BR>(sometimes read तुमल and तुमूल); [cf. Lat.<BR>tumultus.]<BR>—तुमुल-युद्ध, अम्, n. a tumultuous<BR>conflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्प्|तुंप्
तुम्प् तुम्प् and तुम्फ्. See rt. तुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब्|तुंब्
तुम्ब् तुम्ब्, cl. 1. P. तुम्बति, &c., to<BR>distress, trouble, torment; to hurt, kill;<BR>cl. 10. P. तुम्बयति, &c., to trouble; or (according<BR>to a various reading) to be invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब|तुंब|तुंबः|तुम्बः
तुम्ब तुम्ब, अस्, m. a kind of long gourd,<BR>Lagenaria Vulgaris; (आ), f. Lagenaria Vulgaris; a<BR>milk-pail or vessel used in milking; a milch-cow;<BR>(ई), f. Lagenaria Vulgaris; Asteracantha Longifolia;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of Lagenaria Vulgaris; [cf. कटु-<BR>तुम्बी, कुम्भ-त्˚, गोरक्ष-त्˚.]<BR>—तुम्ब-वन,<BR>अस् or अम्, m. n. (?), N. of a country.<BR>—तुम्ब-<BR>वीण, अस्, m. ‘having a Tumba or gourd for a lute,’ a<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>—तुम्बी-पुष्प, अम्, n. the flower of<BR>the Lagenaria Vulgaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बक|तुम्बकः
तुम्बक, अस्, m. the gourd Lagenaria Vulgaris;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of this gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बि|तुंबि|तुंबिः|तुम्बिः
तुम्बि, इस्, or तुम्बिका, f. a long white gourd,<BR>Lagenaria Vulgaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बिनी
तुम्बिनी, f. = कटु-तुम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुक|तुम्बुकं|तुम्बुकः
तुम्बुक, अस्, m. the plant, and (अम्), n. the<BR>fruit, of Lagenaria Vulgaris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बर|तुंबर|तुंबरः|तुम्बरः
तुम्बर तुम्बर, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a<BR>kind of plant; (ई), f. = तुवरी, a sort of earth, =<BR>तुबरी, a bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बरु|तुंबरुः|तुम्बरुः
तुम्बरु तुम्बरु, उस्, m., N. of a Gandharva;<BR>(perhaps a wrong reading for तुम्बुरु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुम
तुम्बुम तुम्बुम, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race or<BR>people; [cf. तुम्बुर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुर
तुम्बुर तुम्बुर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race;<BR>(ई), f. coriander; a bitch; [cf. तुम्बरी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरु|तुंबुरु|तुंबुरुः|तुम्बुरुः
तुम्बुरु तुम्बुरु, उस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Kalāpin; N. of a Gandharva; N. of the attendant<BR>of the fifth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; (उ), n.<BR>the fruit of Diospyros Embryopteris; coriander;<BR>(according to others उस्, उ), m. n. the plant and seed<BR>of Diospyros Embryopteris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्र
तुम्र तुम्र, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. तुमुर above],<BR>Ved. big, strong, powerful; wild; (Sāy.) energetic (=<BR>प्रेरक); destroying or defeating adversaries; see<BR>तूतुम; [cf. Lat. tumidus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्
तुर् 1. तुर् (connected with rts. तॄ, त्वर्,<BR>and तूर्), cl. 6. P. A., Ved. तुरति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to hurry, hasten, press forwards, run; overcome; in-<BR>jure; cl. 3. P., Ved. तुतोर्ति: Caus. तुरयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to run: Desid., Ved. तूतूर्षति: Intens. A., Ved.<BR>in the part. तर्तुराण, running forwards; [cf. rt.<BR>त्वर्; Gr. τύρ-βη, τύρ-βα, τυρβάζω, τυρβασία,<BR>Τυρ-μ-ίδαι; Lat. turba, turbare, turb-idu-s, turma;<BR>Angl. Sax. thrym, ‘multitude, mass, troop;’ Goth.<BR>thaurp; Old Germ. dorf, ‘conference, assembly,<BR>meeting;’ Old Island. thyrpaz, ‘to congregate.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्
2. तुर्, तूर्, तूर्, तूर्, Ved. running a race, hasten-<BR>ing, fighting, conquering, a warrior; [cf. अप्-तुर्,<BR>आजि-तुर्, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
1. तुर, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. 3. तुर see p. 379, col. 1),<BR>Ved. furthering, promoting, a promoter; quick, will-<BR>ing, prompt; (अम्), ind. quickly.<BR>—तुर-ग, अस्, m.<BR>‘going quickly,’ a horse; the mind, thought; (ई), f.<BR>a mare, = अश्व-गन्धा, the plant Physalis Flexuosa;<BR>[cf. तुरङ्-ग and तुरङ्-गम.]<BR>—तुरग-गन्धा,<BR>f. = तुर-गी, Physalis Flexuosa; [cf. तुरङ्ग-गन्धा.]<BR>—तुरग-दानव or तुरग-दैत्य, अस्, m. ‘horse-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">Page0379-a+ 79</a>]<BR>titan’ or ‘Dānava in the shape of a horse,’ an epithet<BR>of Keśin.<BR>—तुरग-नील-ताल, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>gesture with the hand.<BR>—तुरग-प्रिय, अस् or अम्,<BR>m. or n. (?), barley, ‘liked by horses;’ [cf. तुरङ्ग-<BR>प्रिय.]<BR>—तुरग-ब्रह्म-चर्यक, अम्, n. the<BR>sexual restraint of horses, i. e. compulsory celibacy,<BR>leading a life of continence, in consequence merely<BR>of being without female society.<BR>—तुरग-मेध,<BR>अस्, m. a horse-sacrifice, = अश्व-मेध.<BR>—तुरग-<BR>रक्ष, अस्, m. ‘horse-guardian,’ a groom, an equery.<BR>—तुरग-लीलक, अस्, m. a particular time in music.<BR>—तुरग-वदन or तुरगानन (˚ग-आन्˚), आस्,<BR>m. pl. ‘horse-faced,’ N. of a race in the north of<BR>Madhya-deśa.<BR>—तुर-गातु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. going<BR>quickly.<BR>—तुरगारोह (˚ग-आर्˚), अस्, m. ‘one<BR>mounted on a horse,’ a horseman.<BR>—तुरगिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, equestrian, riding, mounted or carried on a<BR>horse; (ई), m. a horseman, a cavalier.<BR>—तुरगीय,<BR>an adj. derived fr. तुर-ग in खर-तुरगीय-सम्-<BR>पर्क, अस्, m. sexual intercourse between asses<BR>and horses.<BR>—तुरगोपचारक (˚ग-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘attending to horses,’ a groom, an equery.<BR>—तुरङ्-<BR>ग, अस्, m. ‘going quickly,’ a horse; a N. of the<BR>number seven (because of the seven horses of the<BR>sun); the mind considered as the seat of feeling as<BR>well as of intellect, the heart; (ई), f. a mare, =<BR>तुर-गी, Physalis Flexuosa, = घोटिका, Cucumis Uti-<BR>lissimus; [cf. तुर-ग and तुरङ्-गम.]<BR>—तुरङ्-<BR>गक, अस्, m. the plant Luffa Fœtida; (इका), f. a<BR>kind of cucurbitaceous plant, = देव-दाली, the large<BR>dark-green pumpkin.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-गन्धा, f. = तु-<BR>रग-गन्धा.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-द्विषणी, f. (for -द्वे-<BR>षणि), a she-buffalo.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-नाथ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the chief of a sect.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-प्रिय, अस्, m.<BR>= तुरग-प्रिय, barley.<BR>—तुरङ्-गम, अस्, m. a<BR>horse; (ई), f. a mare; [cf. तुर-ग and तुरङ्-ग.]<BR>—तुरङ्गम-शाला, f. a horse-stable.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-<BR>मेध, अस्, m. a horse-sacrifice, = अश्व-मेध.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going on horseback.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-वक्त्र or तुरङ्ग-वदन, अस्, m.<BR>‘horse-faced,’ a Kinnara or chorister of Indra's heaven.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-सादिन्, ई, m. a horseman, a horse-soldier.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a troop of horses.<BR>—तुरङ्ग-स्थान, अम्, n. a horse-stable.<BR>—तु-<BR>रङ्गारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of the horse,’ a<BR>buffalo; fragrant oleander (करवीर).<BR>—तुरङ्गा-<BR>रूढ (˚ग-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, mounted on horseback;<BR>(अस्), m. a horseman.<BR>—तुरङ्गिन्, ई, m. a horse-<BR>man, a rider, a groom; [cf. तुरगिन्.]<BR>—तुर-या,<BR>आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरण
तुरण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. quick, swift, energetic;<BR>(अम्), n. haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरण्य
तुरण्य, nom. P., Ved. तुरण्यति, &c., to be<BR>quick or swift; to make haste, to accelerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरण्यसद्
तुरण्य-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. dwelling among the<BR>quick or active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरण्यु
तुरण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. quick, swift, energetic,<BR>zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरस्पेय
तुरस्-पेय, अम्, n., Ved. anything drunk quickly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरी
1. तुरी, f., Ved. overpowering strength, superior<BR>power. (For 2. तुरी see col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्या
तुर्या, f., Ved. overpowering or superior strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर 2. तुर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. तु; for 1. तुर<BR>see p. 378, col. 3), Ved. strong, powerful, excelling,<BR>surpassing, overpowering; an epithet of Indra, of the<BR>Maruts, Ādityas, &c.; possessed of property; rich;<BR>abundant, abounding; (अस्), m., N. of a preceptor<BR>and priest with the patronymic Kāvaṣeya.<BR>—तुरा-<BR>षाह्, -षाट्, ट्, ट्, overpowering the mighty or over-<BR>powering quickly, epithet of Indra and of Viṣṇu;<BR>(ट्), m. a N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरायण|तुरायणं|तुरायणः
तुरायण, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. 2. तुर), N.<BR>of a man; (अम्), n., N. of a particular sacrifice or<BR>vow, = पौर्णमास-विकार, a modification of the<BR>full moon sacrifice; N. of a Sattra; (अस्, आ, अम्), m.<BR>f. n. attachment to any object or pursuit; attached<BR>to any object or pursuit (?); [cf. परायण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर 3. तुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hurt, wounded;<BR>(according to Sāy. = आ-तुर, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरकिन्
तुरकिन् तुरकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Turkish; [cf.<BR>तुरुष्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरक्व|तुरक्वः
तुरक्व तुरक्व, N. of a people, ‘the Turks;’<BR>[cf. तुरुष्क.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरग|तुरगः
तुरग तुर-ग, तुरङ्ग. See 1. तुर, p. 378.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरष्क
तुरष्क तुरष्क, N. of a country and people<BR>mentioned in the Śrī-ṣavāyaṇa or part of the Ro-<BR>maka-siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुराषाह्
तुराषाह् तुरा-षाह्. See 2. तुर, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरी
तुरी 2. तुरी, f. (or तुरि, इस्, in the first<BR>sense; cf. तुलि), the fibrous stick used by weavers to<BR>clean and separate the threads of the woof; a painter's<BR>brush; a shuttle; N. of a wife of Kṛṣṇa (or Vasu-<BR>deva) and mother of Jaras. (For 1. तुरी see col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीप
तुरीप तुरीप, अम्, n., Ved. seminal fluid;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Tvaṣṭṛ, ‘spermatic.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीय|तुरीयं|तुरीयः
तुरीय 1. तुरीय, P., Ved. तुरीयति, &c., to<BR>go or move; [cf. rt. 1. तुर् and तुरण्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीय|तुरीयं|तुरीयः
तुरीय 2. तुरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fourth, a<BR>fourth; consisting of four parts; whose power ex-<BR>tends on all four sides, mighty; (अम्), n. the fourth<BR>state of the soul (according to the Vedānta phil.),<BR>that state in which it has become one with Brahma<BR>or the universal spirit; (अस्, आ, अम्), (with a different<BR>accent), a fourth, constituting the fourth part; (अम्),<BR>n. a fourth part, a quarter; [cf. तुर्य and चतुर्थ.]<BR>—तुरीय-भाग, अस्, m. a fourth part or share.<BR>—तुरीय-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, a sharer of a fourth<BR>—तुरीय-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>fourth caste; (अस्), m. the fourth caste or tribe, a<BR>Śūdra.<BR>—तुरीयांश (˚य-अं˚), अस्, m. a fourth<BR>part or share, a quarter.<BR>—तुरीयातीत (˚य-अत्˚), N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—तुरीयार्ध (˚य-अर्˚), अम्, n.<BR>one half of a fourth, an eighth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयक
तुरीयक, अस्, आ, अम्, a fourth (part).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्य|तुर्य्य|तुर्य्यः
तुर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = 2. तुरीय, fourth, a fourth;<BR>(अम्), n. the fourth state of the soul, in which it be-<BR>comes one with Brahma, a quarter; (अस्, आ, अम्), being<BR>in the above state; the fourth (part).<BR>—तुर्य-वह् or<BR>-वाह्, ट्, f. तुर्यौही, Ved. an ox or cow four years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरुष्क|तुरुष्कः
तुरुष्क तुरुष्क, आस्, m. pl., N. of a race,<BR>the Indo-Scythian race or Turks; (अस्), m. the country<BR>of this race, Turan or Turkestan; a prince of this<BR>race; (अस्, अम्), m. n. olibanum, Indian incense,<BR>the resin of the Boswellia Serrata; the resin of the<BR>Pinus Longifolia; [cf. यावन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्फरि
तुर्फरि तुर्फरि, Ved. (fr. rt. तृफ्), accord-<BR>ing to Yāska = क्षिप्र-हन्तृ, striking quickly; (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy., तुर्फरी, du. = killers of the enemy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्फरीतु
तुर्फरीतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. according to Yāska<BR>= हन्तृ, striking; (according to Sāy., तुर्फरीतू,<BR>du. = तर्फितारौ = शत्रूणां हन्तारौ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्य|तुर्य्य|तुर्य्यः
तुर्य तुर्य. See above under 2. तुरीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्या
तुर्या तुर्या, f. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व्
तुर्व् तुर्व् [cf. rt. 1. तुर्], cl. 1. P., Ved. तूर्-<BR>वति, तुतूर्व, तूर्वितुम्, to overpower,<BR>overcome, excel; to cause to overpower or conquer,<BR>help to victory; to save; to strike, to hurt, kill,<BR>injure; [cf. तूर्वयाण and तूर्वि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वणि
तुर्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. 1. तुर्), Ved. overpowering,<BR>excelling, victorious; (Sāy.) acting quickly, serving<BR>quickly, moving quickly; injuring or destroying<BR>enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वन्
तुर्वन्, अ, n., Ved. (only used in the dat. तुर्-<BR>वणे), conquering, defeating, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वश
तुर्वश तुर्वश, अस्, m. (also written तुर्वसु),<BR>Ved., N. of a hero and ancestor of the Āryan race,<BR>often mentioned in the Ṛg-veda and probably re-<BR>lated to the Kaṇvas; he is generally mentioned<BR>together with his brother Yadu; N. of a whole<BR>race; [cf. तुर्वसु and तौर्वश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वसु|तुर्व्वसु|तुर्व्वसुः
तुर्वसु तुर्वसु, उस्, m. (a later form of<BR>तुर्वश), N. of a son of Yayāti and Devayāni and<BR>brother of Yadu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्वीति
तुर्वीति तुर्वीति, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a man<BR>or of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्
तुल् तुल् [cf. rt. तूल्], cl. 10. P. A. (accord-<BR>ing to Vopa-deva also cl. 1. P.) तोलयति or<BR>तुलयति, -ते, (the form तोलयति is rarely used in<BR>the metaphorical sense), तोलति, अतूतुलत्, -यितुम्, to<BR>lift up, raise; to determine the weight of anything by<BR>lifting it; to weigh, poise, measure; to compare by<BR>weighing and examining; to ponder, weigh in the<BR>mind, consider; to examine with distrust, suspect;<BR>to make equal in weight, to equal, compare one<BR>thing with another (with inst., e. g. न ब्राह्मणैस्<BR>तुलये भूतम् अन्यत्, I do not compare any other<BR>being with Brāhmans); to counterpoise, counter-<BR>balance, outweigh, weigh against, equal in weight,<BR>match, be equal to (with acc.); to possess in the same<BR>degree, to attain, reach; [cf. rt. दुल्: Old Lat. tul-o,<BR>te-tul-i: Lat. tul-i, lātus; (for tlātus), tollere, toll-o,<BR>tolleno, tolerare, tolūtim: Gr. τλῆ-ναι, τάλα-ς,<BR>πολύ-τλᾱ-ς, ταλα-ό-ς, τλή-μων, τάλ-αντο-ν, ἀ-τά-<BR>λαντο-ς, τάλ-αρο-ς, τελα-μών, τόλ-μα, τολμά-ω,<BR>Τάν-ταλο-ς: Goth. thul-an, ‘to tolerate;’ us-<BR>thul-ain-s, ‘patience:’ Angl. Sax. tholian, thyl-<BR>dian, athylgian: Old Germ. dol-an: Germ.<BR>duld-en: Slav. tul-ŭ, ‘a quiver.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलन|तुलनं
तुलन, अम्, n. lifting, raising; weighing, mea-<BR>suring; rating, assessing, taxing; a particular high<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलयित्वा
तुलयित्वा, ind. having weighed, having counter-<BR>poised, having made equal or like, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुला
तुला, f. a balance, especially a fine balance, the<BR>beam of a balance, goldsmith's or assay scales; a<BR>measure, a weight, (तुलया धृ, to hold in a<BR>balance, to weigh); the balance as an ordeal; weigh-<BR>ing; resemblance, likeness, equality, similarity; the<BR>sign of the zodiac Libra; the seventh sign in a circle<BR>divided like a zodiac; a measure or weight of gold<BR>and silver = 100 Palas or about 145 ounces troy; a<BR>kind of vessel; sloping beams or timbers in the roof<BR>of a house; [cf. भार-तुला and तुलोपतुला.]<BR>—तुला-<BR>कोटि, इस्, ई, m. f. an ornament on the feet or toes<BR>of women; a particular weight; a hundred millions,<BR>= अर्बुद.<BR>—तुला-कोश or तुला-कोष, अस्, m. a<BR>place where a balance or pair of scales is kept; ordeal<BR>by weighing; see तुला-परीक्षा.<BR>—तुलाकोश-र-<BR>हस्य, अम्, n. a mystical rite which consists in<BR>weighing seeds and thence calculating the fertility<BR>of the soil.<BR>—तुला-दान, अम्, n. the gift to a<BR>Brāhman of as much gold, silver, &c., as equals the<BR>weight of the body.<BR>—तुला-धट, अस्, m. the scale<BR>or cup of a balance; an oar, a paddle.<BR>—तुला-<BR>धर, अस्, m. ‘holding a pair of scales,’ the sign of<BR>the zodiac Libra, the sun.<BR>—तुला-धार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘holding a pair of scales;’ trading, trafficking, a<BR>trader, a dealer; (अस्), m. the string of a balance;<BR>the beam; the sign of the zodiac Libra; N. of a<BR>merchant.<BR>—तुला-पद्धति, N. of a book by Ka-<BR>malākara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—तुला-परीक्षा, f. ordeal by the<BR>balance, (the weight of the accused being first taken,<BR>certain prayers and ceremonies are performed, after<BR>which he is weighed again; if lighter, he is innocent; if<BR>heavier, or as at first, guilty.)<BR>—तुला-पुरुष, अस्, m.<BR>‘a weighed man,’ or gold, jewels, and other ornaments<BR>equal to a man's weight, an offering of such extent<BR>constituting one of the sixteen pious gifts; a kind<BR>of penance.<BR>—तुलापुरुष-दान, अम्, n. gift of<BR>gold or valuables to an amount equivalent to the<BR>weight of the donor.<BR>—तुला-प्रग्रह or तुला-<BR>प्रग्राह, अस्, m. the string of a balance.<BR>—तुला-<BR>मान, अम्, n. measure by weight.<BR>—तुला-यष्टि,<BR>इस्, m. or f. (?), the beam of a balance.<BR>—तुला-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with or possessed of a balance.<BR>—तुला-वीज, अम्, n. the Guñjā or berry of the<BR>Abrus Precatorius, from which the goldsmith's or<BR>jeweller's weight in India is taken; the berry weighs<BR>about 1(5/16) grain troy, the factitious weight about 2(3/16).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">Page0380-a+ 75</a>]<BR>—तुला-सूत्र, अम्, n. the string of a balance.<BR>—तुलोपतुला (˚ला-उप्˚), f. a supporting beam or<BR>prop in the roof of a house (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलित
तुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, made equal or like, equalled,<BR>compared (with inst., e. g. शशाङ्केन तुलित, com-<BR>pared with the moon); weighed, counterpoised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्य|तुल्यः
तुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, equal to, of the same kind or<BR>class, well matched, similar, comparable, equally<BR>valuable or precious, like, resembling (with gen. or<BR>inst., e. g. तुल्य एतस्य, equal to him; प्राणैस्<BR>तुल्या, a woman as dear as life; or with the crude form<BR>in comp., e. g. अमृत-तुल्य, similar to the immor-<BR>tals or to nectar; एतत्-तुल्य, equal to this man); fit<BR>for (with inst.); even, same; indifferent; (अम्), ind.<BR>equally, similarly, in like manner; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a Gandharva.<BR>—तुल्य-ता, f. or तुल्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>equality, likeness, sameness, resemblance (with inst.,<BR>e. g. वयसा तुल्यता, equality in age); equality of<BR>place, conjunction (in astronomy); दृक्-तुल्यता,<BR>conformity with any observed place.<BR>—तुल्य-तेजस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, equal in splendor.<BR>—तुल्य-दर्शन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, regarding with equal or indifferent eyes.<BR>—तुल्य-पान, अम्, n. drinking together, compota-<BR>tion.<BR>—तुल्य-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, of equal strength.<BR>—तु-<BR>ल्य-भावना, f. (in arithm. or algebra) combination of<BR>like or analogous sets of magnitude.<BR>—तुल्य-मूल्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of equal value.<BR>—तुल्य-योगिता, f. ‘com-<BR>bination of equal actions or qualities,’ a figure in<BR>rhetoric.<BR>—तुल्य-रूप, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, of like or<BR>equal form; like, similar, analogous.<BR>—तुल्य-लक्-<BR>षणा, f. a particular figure in rhetoric.<BR>—तुल्य-<BR>वंश, अस्, आ, अम्, equal in race, of equal race.<BR>—तु-<BR>ल्य-विक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, of equal prowess.<BR>—तुल्य-<BR>वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, of equal strength.<BR>—तुल्य-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, following the same or similar occupation.<BR>—तुल्य-शस्, ind. in equal parts.<BR>—तुल्य-शुद्धि,<BR>इस्, f. equal subtraction, transposition (in arithmetic).<BR>—तुल्य-शोधन, अम्, n. reducing an equation by<BR>removing the like magnitudes on both sides.<BR>—तु-<BR>ल्याकृति (˚य-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, of the same form,<BR>alike.<BR>—तुल्यातुल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, similar and dis-<BR>similar, like and unlike.<BR>—तुल्यानुमान (˚य-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. like inference, a parallel case.<BR>—तुल्योद्योग<BR>(˚य-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, equal in labours or exertions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलकुचि
तुलकुचि तुलकुचि, इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलभ
तुलभ तुलभ, आस्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-<BR>tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलभीय
तुलभीय, अस्, m. a prince of the above tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसारिणी
तुलसारिणी तुलसारिणी, f. = तूण, a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसी
तुलसी तुलसी or तुलसिका, f. holy basil, a<BR>small shrub said to have been produced from the<BR>hair of the goddess Tulasī and held in veneration by<BR>the worshippers of Viṣṇu (Ocymum Sanctum); N.<BR>of a deity.<BR>—तुलसी-द्वेषा, f. a kind of plant, =<BR>वर्वरी.<BR>—तुलसी-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a Tulasī leaf,<BR>hence a very small gift.<BR>—तुलसी-विवाह, अस्, m.<BR>the marriage of an image of Viṣṇu with the holy<BR>basil, a festival on the twelfth day in the first half of<BR>the month Kārttika.<BR>—तुलसी-वृन्दावन, अस्, m.<BR>a small altar, a square pedestal before the gate of a<BR>Hindū house on which the sacred basil is planted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलि|तुलिः
तुलि तुलि, इस्, or तुली, f. a fibrous stick or<BR>brush used by weavers for cleaning the threads of<BR>the woof; a painter's brush used for that purpose; [cf.<BR>तूली, तूलि, तूलिका, तुरि.]<BR>—तुलि-फला, f. the Simul<BR>or silk-cotton tree; [cf. तूलि-फला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिनी
तुलिनी (= तूलिनी), f. the Simul or silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिका
तुलिका तुलिका, f. a small bird said to re-<BR>semble the wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्य|तुल्यः
तुल्य तुल्य. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवर|तुवरः
तुवर तुवर, अस्, आ, अम्, astringent; beard-<BR>less; (अस्, अम्), m. n. an astringent taste; (अस्),<BR>m. a sort of grain, = तुवर-यावनाल; (ई), f. =<BR>आढकी, a kind of lentil, Cajanus Indicus; a fragrant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-b" target="_blank">Page0380-b+ 79</a>]<BR>earth; alum; [cf. तूवर.]<BR>—तुवर-यावनाल,<BR>अस्, m. a sort of grain, = कषाय-यावनाल, &c.<BR>—तुवरी-शिम्ब, अस्, m. a kind of plant, Cassia<BR>Tora, = चक्र-मर्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवरक
तुवरक, अस्, m. a sort of grain (?); N. of a tree<BR>growing in the countries bordering on the western<BR>ocean; (इका), f. Cajanus Indicus; a sort of earth;<BR>alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवि|तुविः
तुवि तुवि (fr. rt. 2. तु), = बहु, much, many,<BR>great, strong, excessive, very, (only used in the Ved.<BR>compounds enumerated below); (इस्), f. = तुम्बी, a<BR>long gourd.<BR>—तुवि-कूर्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, or तुवि-कूर्मिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, Ved. powerful in working, efficacious; (Sāy.)<BR>doing many and various deeds; epithet of Indra.<BR>—तु-<BR>वि-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. of a strong will; (Sāy.) doing<BR>many deeds; having much knowledge; epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—तुवि-क्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. epithet of Indra's<BR>bow, (according to Sāy. and the Nirukta = बहु-वि-<BR>क्षेप or महा-विक्षेप), ‘throwing far,’ perhaps<BR>‘very destructive,’ (क्ष being then fr. rt. 4. क्षि.)<BR>—तुवि-क्षत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ruling powerfully,<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara) preserving from many inju-<BR>ries, epithet of Aditi.<BR>—तुवि-ग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>swallowing much; (Sāy.) sounding loudly; going<BR>quickly.<BR>—तुवि-ग्राभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. seizing<BR>powerfully.<BR>—तुवि-ग्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. swallowing<BR>much or greedily; (Sāy.) having a full throat or to<BR>be praised by many.<BR>—तुवि-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having a powerful or firm or erect neck, having<BR>many throats, swallowing or consuming much, all-<BR>embracing.<BR>—तुवि-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of strong<BR>or powerful nature, powerful; born for many,<BR>born for the protection of many; (Sāy.) born<BR>with many (qualities), from whom many are<BR>born; epithet of the gods Indra, Varuṇa, Varuṇa-<BR>Mitra, &c.<BR>—तुवि-देष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting<BR>excellent gifts, epithet of Indra; (Sāy.) giving much.<BR>—तुवि-द्युम्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very glorious,<BR>powerful, wealthy; epithet of Indra, and of the<BR>Maruts.<BR>—तुवि-नृम्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very<BR>manly or valiant or courageous; epithet of Indra.<BR>—तुवि-प्रति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (Sāy.) visiting many,<BR>approaching many; withstanding many, (perhaps<BR>rather) resisting powerfully; [cf. अ-प्रति.]<BR>—तुवि-<BR>बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. killing many.<BR>—तुवि-<BR>ब्रह्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. very devoted or pious.<BR>—तुवि-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. very zealous, very<BR>furious.<BR>—तुवि-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. making or<BR>creating much, very efficacious, measuring many (?).<BR>—तुवि-म्रक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. injuring greatly,<BR>destructive; (Sāy.) destroying much (timber).<BR>—तुवि-<BR>राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. granting in abundance;<BR>(Sāy.) opulent, having great wealth.<BR>—तुवि-वाज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having much food or strength,<BR>strengthening, abounding with food.<BR>—तुवि-शग्म,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. able to do much; (Sāy.) having<BR>much enjoyment or pleasure.<BR>—तुवि-शुष्म, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. high-spirited; (Sāy.) of great power,<BR>very strong, epithet of Indra and of Indra-Varuṇa.<BR>—तुवि-श्रवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. highly renowned,<BR>having great fame.<BR>—तुविश्रवस्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having very great fame, an epithet of Agni.<BR>—तुविष्-<BR>टम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. strongest, most powerful,<BR>most valid.<BR>—तुविष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. power-<BR>ful, mighty, efficacious.<BR>—तुवि-ष्वणस् (˚वि-स्व्˚),<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, or तुवि-ष्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ, or तुवि-ष्वन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. loud-sounding, roaring.<BR>—तुवी-मघ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving abundantly; (Sāy.) having<BR>great riches, epithet of Indra, and of the Maruts.<BR>—तुवी-रव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. making a terrible<BR>noise (in battle &c.).<BR>—तुवी-रवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>making a great noise (?); (Sāy.) possessed of many<BR>praisers, (either for तुवीरव-वत्, or रवान् may be<BR>an irregular nom. case of the part. रवत्.)<BR>—तुव्य्-<BR>ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. very strong or powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुश्
तुश् 1. तुश्, cl. 1. A., Ved. तोशते, &c., to drip,<BR>trickle; sprinkle; (Sāy.) to be struck; to<BR>be pressed out or extracted; to be drunk; [cf. तोश<BR>and तोशस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुश्
तुश् 2. तुश् (for तुष् ?), cl. 1. A., Ved. तो-<BR>सते, &c., to quiet, pacify, appease, satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्
तुष् तुष् [cf. rt. 1. जुष्], cl. 4. P. (ep.<BR>also A.) तुष्यति, -ते, तुतोष, तोक्ष्यति,<BR>अतुषत्, तोष्टुम्, to become tranquil or calm or<BR>quiet; to be contented or satisfied, to be pleased or<BR>delighted with anything or any person (with inst.,<BR>gen., loc. or प्रति after the acc., e. g. दत्तेन<BR>तुष्यति, he is satisfied with the gift; तस्य or<BR>तेन or तस्मिन् or तम् प्रति तुष्यामि, I am<BR>pleased with him); to satisfy, please (with acc.,<BR>e. g. सा पतिं न तुतोष, she did not please her<BR>husband): Caus. P. तोषयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>satisfied, satisfy, please, gratify, gladden, quiet, calm,<BR>appease, pacify; to gratify any one with anything<BR>(with acc. of the person and inst. of the thing,<BR>e. g. तोषय हरं तपसा, gratify Śiva with<BR>penance; आत्मानम् तोषयति, he satisfies himself,<BR>he becomes satisfied): Desid. तुतुक्षति: Intens.<BR>तोतुष्यते, तोतोष्टि; [cf. तूष्णीम्; cf. also Lith.<BR>têsziju, ‘to recreate, to refresh;’ Lat. taceo; Goth.<BR>thahan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषित|तुषितः
तुषित, आस्, m. pl. a class of subordinate deities,<BR>thirty-six in number (sometimes reckoned as twelve<BR>in number and identified with the twelve Ādityas);<BR>N. of twelve sons of Bhaga-vat; (अस्), m. a N. of<BR>Viṣṇu (one of the Ādityas); (आ), f., N. of the<BR>wife of Veda-śiras and mother of the god Vibhu.<BR>—तुषित-कायिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the<BR>body or class of the Tuṣitas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्ट|तुष्टः
तुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied, contented, pleased,<BR>glad, &c.<BR>—तुष्ट-धी, धीस्, धीस्, धि, pleased in<BR>mind, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टि|तुष्टिः
तुष्टि, इस्, f. satisfaction, gratification, content-<BR>ment, pleasure; acquiescence, indifference to every-<BR>thing but that possessed, (the Sāṅkhya phil. reckons<BR>nine kinds of Tuṣṭi); Contentment personified as<BR>a daughter of Dakṣa and mother of Santoṣa or<BR>Muda; N. of a daughter of Kaśyapa; of a deity<BR>sprung from the Kalās of Prakṛti and wife of<BR>Ananta; of a Mātṛkā; of one of the Kalās of the<BR>moon.<BR>—तुष्टि-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing satis-<BR>faction, pleasing, gratifying, satisfying.<BR>—तुष्टि-ज-<BR>नन, अस्, ई, अम्, or तुष्टि-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving<BR>or producing satisfaction, affording pleasure, gratify-<BR>ing.<BR>—तुष्टि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pleased, gratified;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a prince, a son of Ugra-sena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्ट्वा
तुष्ट्वा, ind. having pleased or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्य|तुष्यः
तुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be satisfied or gratified,<BR>easily satisfied; an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोष|तोषः
तोष, तोषित, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष|तुषः
तुष तुष, अस्, m. (perhaps connected with<BR>त्वच्), the husk or chaff of grain, of corn, rice, &c.<BR>[cf. अ-तुष, उत्-तुष, निस्-तुष, तुच्छ]; Beleric<BR>Myrobalan, Terminalia Bellerica.<BR>—तुष-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. Agni or fire (‘seizing the husk’).<BR>—तुष-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from husk or chaff.<BR>—तुषज-क, अस्, m., N. of a Śūdra.<BR>—तुष-<BR>धान्य, अम्, n. a leguminous plant; N. of a place.<BR>—तुष-वन, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>place; (a various reading has तुंव-वन.)<BR>—तु-<BR>ष-सार, अस्, m. (= तुष-ग्रह), Agni or fire.<BR>—तुषाग्नि (˚ष-अग्˚), इस्, m. or तुषानल (˚ष-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. a conflagration of chaff or of the husk<BR>of corn; a capital punishment which consists in<BR>twisting dry straw &c. round the limbs of a criminal<BR>and setting it on fire.<BR>—तुषाम्बु (˚ष-अम्˚), उ,<BR>n. sour rice or barley-gruel.<BR>—तुषोत्थ (˚ष-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. or तुषोदक (˚ष-उद्˚), अम्, n. sour rice-<BR>gruel or barley-gruel, (‘made from husk.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषस्प
तुषस्प तुषस्प, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषार|तुषारः
तुषार तुषार, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तुष्), cold, frigid, frosty, dewy; (अस्), m. frost,<BR>cold; ice, snow, mist, dew, thin rain; N. of a place<BR>mentioned in the Śrī-ṣavāyaṇa or part of the<BR>Romaka-siddhānta; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a race; [cf.<BR>तुहिन; cf. also Angl. Sax. thystre, thystrian,<BR>theostre, theosterlic.]<BR>—तुषार-कण, अस्, m. a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">Page0381-a+ 69</a>]<BR>dew-drop, an icicle, hoar frost.<BR>—तुषार-काल, अस्,<BR>m. winter, the cold season.<BR>—तुषार-किरण, अस्,<BR>m. the moon (‘having cold rays’).<BR>—तुषार-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. the snowy mountain, the Himālaya.<BR>—तुषा-<BR>र-गौर, अस्, ई, अम्, white as snow, white with<BR>snow; camphor.<BR>—तुषार-रश्मि, इस्, m. the moon;<BR>[cf. तुषार-किरण.]<BR>—तुषाराद्रि (˚र-अद्˚), इस्,<BR>m. or तुषार-पर्वत or तुषार-शैल, अस्, m.<BR>the Himālaya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषित|तुषितः
तुषित तुषित, तुष्टि, &c. See under rt. तुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टु|तुष्टुः
तुष्टु तुष्टु, उस्, m. a jewel worn in the ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस्
तुस् तुस्, cl. 1. P. तोसति, &c., to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस|तुसः
तुस तुस, अस्, m. the husk of corn or rice,<BR>= तुष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस्त|तुस्तं
तुस्त तुस्त, अस्, अम्, m. n. dust; husk; (a<BR>various reading for बुस्त); [cf. तूस्त; Angl. Sax.<BR>and Eng. dust.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुह्
तुह् तुह्, cl. 1. P. तोहति, &c., to hurt,<BR>pain, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहर
तुहर तुहर, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Skanda; (also written तुहार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिन|तुहिनं
तुहिन तुहिन, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तुह्), cold, frigid, frosty; (अम्), n. mist, dew, snow,<BR>frost, cold; moonlight, moonshine; camphor; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a tree, = शुक-नास; [cf. तुषार; Hib.<BR>deigh, ‘ice.’]<BR>—तुहिन-कण, अस्, m. a dew-drop;<BR>snow-flake.<BR>—तुहिन-किरण, अस्, m. ‘cold-rayed,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—तुहिनकिरण-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son<BR>of the moon, the planet Mercury.<BR>—तुहिन-गु, उस्,<BR>m. ‘having cold rays,’ the moon.<BR>—तुहिन-द्युति,<BR>इस्, m. or तुहिन-रश्मि, इस्, m. ‘cold-rayed,’ the<BR>moon.<BR>—तुहिन-शर्करा, f. a piece of ice, ice.<BR>—तुहिन-शैल, अस्, m. a snowy mountain, a snowy<BR>peak, the Himālaya.<BR>—तुहिनांशु (˚न-अं˚), उस्,<BR>m. ‘cold-rayed,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—तुहिनांशु-<BR>तैल, अम्, n. oil of camphor.<BR>—तुहिनाचल (˚न-<BR>अच्˚), अस्, m. or तुहिनाद्रि (˚न-अद्˚), इस्, m. a snow<BR>mountain, a snowy peak, the Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहुण्ड
तुहुण्ड तुहुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava;<BR>of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूख
तूख तूख, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूड्
तूड् तूड् (= तुड्), cl. 1. P. तूडति, &c., to<BR>split; to slight, disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण्
तूण् तूण् [cf. कूण् and चूण्], cl. 10. P.<BR>तूणयति, -यितुम्, to shrink, contract, close<BR>as the eyelids, wink; A. तूणयते, to fill, fill up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण|तूणः
तूण तूण, अस्, ई, m. f. (this word appears<BR>to be connected with the preceding root, which may<BR>perhaps be formed from it), a quiver; (ई), f. an in-<BR>ternal disease by which the anus and the bladder<BR>become painfully affected; the Indigo plant; [cf.<BR>Slav. tūl, ‘quiver.’]<BR>—तूण-धार, अस्, m. a quiver-<BR>bearer (a kind of officer).<BR>—तूण-मुख, अम्, n.<BR>the mouth or opening of a quiver.<BR>—तूण-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, furnished with a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणि|तूणिः
तूणि, इस्, m. a quiver [cf. तूण and तूणी]; N. of<BR>a prince, father of Yugan-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणिक
तूणिक or तूणीक, अस्, m., N. of a tree, =<BR>नन्दी-वृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणिन्
तूणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a quiver, quivered; (ई),<BR>m., N. of a tree, = नन्दी-वृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणीर|तूणीरं|तूणीरः
तूणीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. a quiver.<BR>—तूणीर-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, provided with a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणक|तूणकं
तूणक तूणक, अस्, m. a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines of fifteen syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणव
तूणव तूणव, अस्, m., Ved. a wind instru-<BR>ment, a flute (?).<BR>—तूणव-ध्म, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>flute-player (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणिक
तूणिक तूणिक, तूणीक. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूतक|तूतकं
तूतक तूतक, अम्, n. = तुत्थ, blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूतुजान
तूतुजान तूतुजान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. तुज्),<BR>Ved. hastening, quick, eager, ardent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूतुजि
तूतुजि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. quick, swift; (a various<BR>reading has तूतुजित्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूतुम
तूतुम तूतुम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting<BR>much (?); (Sāy.) quick, active; [cf. तुम्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूद|तूदः
तूद तूद, अस्, m. = तूल-वृक्ष, the cotton<BR>tree; also توت the mulberry tree; Thespesia<BR>Populneoides; (ई), f., N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूपर|तूपरः
तूपर तूपर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hornless,<BR>(often applied to a goat, and sometimes used alone<BR>to denote ‘a hornless goat.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूबर|तूबरः
तूबर तूबर, see तूवर; तूबरिका, तुबरी,<BR>and तूबरीका, f. = तुबरिका, a kind of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूय
तूय तूय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. तु), Ved. strong,<BR>powerful; (Sāy.) quick, not delaying; (अम्), n.<BR>water; (अम्), ind. quickly, swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्
तूर् 1. तूर् [cf. rt. 1. तुर् and त्वर्], cl. 4. A.<BR>तूर्यते, &c., to go quickly, make haste;<BR>to kill, hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्
तूर् 2. तूर्, र्, र्, र् (fr. त्वर्), hastening; a<BR>courier; (र्), f. speed, swift motion, swiftness; [cf.<BR>2. तुर्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर|तूरं
तूर तूर, अम्, n. = 1. तूर्य, any musical in-<BR>strument; (ई), f. a thorn-apple; [cf. अर्ध-तूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्घ्न
तूर्घ्न तूर्घ्न, अम्, n., N. of the northern<BR>part of Kuru-kṣetra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्ण|तूर्णं|तूर्ण्ण
तूर्ण तूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तुर्व् and त्वर्),<BR>quick, expeditious; fleet; (अम्), n. rapidity, quickness;<BR>(अम्), ind. quick, swift, quickly, speedily, in haste;<BR>[cf. Hib. tonn, ‘quick.’]<BR>—तूर्ण-वनि, quickly<BR>honouring or serving, (a word made by Yāska to<BR>explain the etymology of तुर्वणि, q. v.)<BR>—तूर्णो-<BR>दित (˚ण-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, spoken quickly, uttered<BR>rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्णक
तूर्णक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a sort of rice<BR>which ripens quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्णि|तूर्णिः
तूर्णि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. quick, swift, expeditious;<BR>clever, zealous; (इस्), m. f. speed, velocity, expedi-<BR>tion; (इस्), m. the mind; a Śloka; dirt, excrement.<BR>—तूर्ण्य्-अर्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. pursuing an object<BR>with zeal, eager to accomplish a purpose; (Sāy.)<BR>going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्त
तूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. quick, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्णाश|तूर्ण्णाश
तूर्णाश तूर्णाश, अम्, n., Ved. water; a<BR>waterfall (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य|तूर्यं|तूर्यः|तूर्य्य|तूर्य्यं
तूर्य 1. तूर्य, अम्, n., Ved. an abstract noun<BR>of 2. तुर्, occurring at the end of comp. [cf. अप्-<BR>तूर्य under अप्त, &c.]; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a musical<BR>instrument, of which four kinds are sometimes<BR>reckoned, (wind instruments, stringed instruments,<BR>&c.); स-तूर्य, accompanied by music; स-तूर्यम्,<BR>with music; [cf. मङ्गल-त्˚, मृत्यु-त्˚, याम-त्˚,<BR>तौर्य.]<BR>—तूर्य-खण्ड, अस्, m. a musical instru-<BR>ment, a sort of tabor.<BR>—तूर्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>representing music, musical.<BR>—तूर्यौघ (˚य-<BR>ओघ), अस्, m. a band of instruments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य|तूर्यं|तूर्यः|तूर्य्य|तूर्य्यं
तूर्य 2. तूर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for तुर्य), a fourth,<BR>a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्वयाण
तूर्वयाण तूर्वयाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तुर्व्),<BR>Ved. overpowering; (Sāy.) going quickly, having a<BR>rapid course (as if तूर्व-यान); (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्वि
तूर्वि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. excelling, superior; (Sāy.)<BR>quick, rapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूल्
तूल् तूल् [cf. तुल्], cl. 1. P. and according<BR>to some cl. 10. P. A. तूलति, तूलयति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">Page0381-c+ 73</a>]<BR>ते, &c., to ascertain quantity or weight; to weigh,<BR>measure; to fill; [cf. rt. तूण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूल|तूलं|तूलः
तूल तूल, अम्, n. a tuft of grass or reeds<BR>&c.; the panicle of a flower or plant; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. cotton; (अम्), n. the mulberry, Morus Indica;<BR>the thorn-apple; the sky, air, atmosphere; (आ), f.<BR>the cotton tree; the wick of a lamp, cotton twisted<BR>into that form for applying unguents &c.; (ई), f.<BR>cotton; the wick of a lamp; a weaver's fibrous stick<BR>or brush, a painter's brush &c.; the Indigo plant;<BR>[cf. इन्द्र-तूल &c.]<BR>—तूल-कार्मुक or तूल-<BR>चाप, अम्, n. or तूल-धनुस्, उस्, n. ‘cotton-bow,’<BR>i. e. a bow or similarly shaped instrument used for<BR>cleaning cotton.<BR>—तूल-नाली or तूल-नालिका, f.<BR>‘cotton-tube,’ i. e. a thick roll of cotton which is<BR>drawn out in spinning.<BR>—तूल-पिचु, उस्, m. = तूल<BR>or पिचु, cotton.<BR>—तूल-मूल, N. of a district on<BR>the Candra-bhāgā.<BR>—तूल-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the<BR>cotton tree.<BR>—तूल-शर्करा, f. a pod or seed of<BR>the cotton plant, any seed yielding a similar sub-<BR>stance.<BR>—तूल-सेचन, अम्, n. the act of spinning<BR>(‘sprinkling or moistening the cotton’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलक|तूलकं
तूलक, अम्, n. cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलि|तूलिः
तूलि, इस्, f. a painter's brush or pencil or a fibrous<BR>stick so used and for other purposes; [cf. तूली under<BR>तूल.]<BR>—तूलि-फला, f. the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलिका
तूलिका, f. a pencil, a brush, a painter's brush or<BR>stick with a fibrous extremity used as one; a wick<BR>or twist of cotton either for a lamp or for applying<BR>unguents, a whisk of any soft substance, &c.; a kind<BR>of probing-rod; a mattress or quilt filled with cotton,<BR>a bed, a down or cotton bed; an ingot mould.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलिनी
तूलिनी, f. the silk-cotton tree; a kind of bulbous<BR>plant, = लक्ष्मणा-कन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूवर|तूवरः
तूवर तूवर, अस्, आ, अम्, = तुवर, astrin-<BR>gent; (अस्), m. an astringent taste; a bull without<BR>horns [cf. तूपर] though of an age to have them;<BR>a beardless man; a eunuch; (ई), f. a fragrant earth,<BR>= तुवरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूवरक
तूवरक, अस्, आ, अम्, unmanly; a eunuch; (used<BR>as a taunt or abusive epithet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूवरिका
तूवरिका, f. = तुवरिका, a kind of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्
तूष् तूष् (= तुष्), cl. 1. P. तूषति, &c.,<BR>to be satisfied or pleased; to satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष|तूषः
तूष तूष, अस्, अम्, m. n., Ved. a lappet,<BR>the border or fringe of a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीम्
तूष्णीम् तूष्णीम्, ind. (fr. rt. तुष् with the<BR>termination नीम्, as in इदानीम्, तदानीम्, &c.; cf.<BR>जोषम् fr. rt. 1. जुष्), silent, in silence, silently,<BR>quietly, still, softly, without speaking, without noise.<BR>—तूष्णीं-शंस, अस्, m., Ved. silent recitation,<BR>certain formulas or verses to be recited; [cf. Russ.<BR>tishina, ‘silence, tranquillity:’ Lith. tylà, ‘silence;’<BR>tylù, ‘to be silent:’ Hib. tosd, ‘silence, taciturnity;’<BR>tosdadh, ‘silencing, confutation.’]<BR>—तूष्णीं-शील,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, silent, taciturn.<BR>—तूष्णीङ्-गङ्गम्, ind.<BR>(a place) where the Ganges flows silently.<BR>—तूष्णीम्-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the being silent, silence, taciturnity;<BR>(rarely spelt तुष्णी-भाव.)<BR>—तूष्णीम्-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being silent, silent.<BR>—तूष्णीम्-भूय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, become silent.<BR>—तूष्णी-शील = तूष्णीं-<BR>शील, (perhaps a wrong reading.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीक|तूष्णीकः
तूष्णीक, अस्, आ, अम्, silent, taciturn; (अम् or<BR>आम्), ind. silently, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूस्त|तूस्तं
तूस्त तूस्त, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. तुस्),<BR>a braid of hair, matted or clotted hair; dust; sin;<BR>an atom, any very minute or delicate substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृ
तृ तृ, ता, m. (for स्तृ), Ved. a star; [cf.<BR>तार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृंह्
तृंह् तृंह्. See rt. तृह्, p. 383, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृंहण|तृंहणं
तृंहण, अम्, n. crushing, bruising, hurting,<BR>killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृंहणीय
तृंहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be crushed, killed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृढ
तृढ, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed, bruised, hurt, injured,<BR>&c. See under rt. तृह्, p. 383.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्वन्
तृक्वन् तृक्वन्, आ, m., Ved. a thief; (also<BR>read त्रिक्वन् and रिक्वन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्ष्
तृक्ष् तृक्ष्, cl. 1. P. तृक्षति, &c., to<BR>go, move or approach; [cf. rt. स्तृक्ष्:<BR>Gr. τρέχω: Goth. thragjan, ‘to run;’ treihan, ‘to<BR>urge:’ Hib. teilg, ‘to go;’ teilgin, ‘a shock.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्ष|तृक्षः
तृक्ष तृक्ष, अस्, m. or तृक्षस्, अस्, n., Ved.<BR>strength (?), [cf. त्वक्षस्]; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>tree (?); N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्षाक
तृक्षाक तृक्षाक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्षि
तृक्षि तृक्षि, इस्, m., N. of a man with the<BR>patronymic Trāsadasyava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृख|तृखं
तृख तृख, अम्, n. nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृच|तृचः
तृच तृच or त्रिच, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. त्रि-<BR>ऋच्), a strophe consisting of three verses; [cf. त्र्य्-<BR>ऋच्.]<BR>—तृच-कॢप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. arranged in<BR>strophes of three verses each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृढ
तृढ तृढ. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्
तृण् तृण् (according to some, a rt.<BR>formed from the conjugational base of rt.<BR>तृद्), cl. 8. P. A. तृणोति, -णुते, or तर्णोति, -णुते,<BR>&c., to eat (especially grass), to graze; [cf. तृण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण|तृणं
तृण तृण, अम्, n. (according to the lexi-<BR>cographers also अस्, m.; perhaps connected with the<BR>preceding rt. or fr. rt. स्तृ, to spread, or rt. तॄ, to<BR>pierce, cf. तरु; but according to native authorities<BR>fr. rt. तृह्; according to the conjecture of others,<BR>तृण is for तृण्ण fr. rt. तृद्), grass, a herb or<BR>any gramineous plant, a blade of grass, a bamboo,<BR>a reed, (often a symbol of minuteness and worthless-<BR>ness); straw, grass or reeds for roofing a house [cf.<BR>rt. ज्वल्]; (अस्), m., N. of a man; N. of a prince,<BR>a son of Uśīnara; [cf. Goth. thaurnus; Angl. Sax.<BR>thorn; Germ. dorn; Russ. tern, ‘thorn;’ Hib.<BR>dreas, dris, ‘a briar, bramble.’]<BR>—तृण-कर्ण,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants<BR>of this man.<BR>—तृण-काण्ड, अम्, n. a heap or<BR>quantity of grass.<BR>—तृण-कुङ्कुम, अम्, n. a sort<BR>of perfume.<BR>—तृण-कुटी, f. or तृण-कुटीरक,<BR>अम्, n. a hut of grass or straw.<BR>—तृण-कूट, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a heap of grass.<BR>—तृण-कूर्म, अस्, m.<BR>a long gourd, Cucurbita Lagenaria (= तुम्बी).<BR>—तृण-केतकी, f. a kind of Tabāṣīr (तवक्षीर).<BR>—तृण-केतु, उस्, or तृण-केतुक, अस्, m. a bam-<BR>boo; [cf. तृण-ध्वज.]<BR>—तृण-गड, अस्, m. a<BR>sort of sea crab, = उच्-चिङ्गट.<BR>—तृण-गन्धा, f.<BR>Batatas Paniculata, = विदारी; [cf. इक्षु-गन्धा.]<BR>—तृण-गोधा, f. a kind of newt, a chameleon,<BR>a worm, = चित्र-कोल and कृकलास.<BR>—तृण-<BR>गौर, अम्, n. a sort of perfume, = तृण-<BR>कुङ्कुम.<BR>—तृण-ग्रन्थि, इस्, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= स्वर्ण-जीवन्ती.<BR>—तृण-ग्राहिनि, ई, m. sapphire,<BR>= नील-मणि; another gem, commonly काफुर-<BR>दाना, amber, &c., or any gem which being<BR>rubbed becomes electrically attractive.<BR>—तृण-<BR>चर, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a kind of gem, =<BR>गो-मेद.<BR>—तृण-जम्भन्, आ, आ, अ, grass-toothed,<BR>having teeth like grass, &c., graminivorous, feeding<BR>on grass.<BR>—तृण-जलायुका or तृण-जलूका, f.<BR>a caterpillar.<BR>—तृण-जाति, इस्, m. the vegetable<BR>kingdom.<BR>—तृण-ज्योतिस्, a particular kind of<BR>shining plant.<BR>—१. तृण-ता, f. or तृण-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the aggregate properties of grass or herbage, the<BR>state or condition of grass, gramineousness; (for<BR>2. तृणता see col. 3.)<BR>—तृण-दुह्, -धुक्, m. =<BR>बडवाग्नि.<BR>—तृण-द्रुम, अस्, m. a palm-tree,<BR>any of the various species, as the palmyra, cocoa-nut,<BR>date, &c.; [cf. तृण-वृक्ष.]<BR>—तृण-धान्य,<BR>अम्, n. grain growing wild or without cultivation;<BR>[cf. तृणान्न.]<BR>—तृण-ध्वज, अस्, m. a bamboo;<BR>[cf. तृण-केतु.]<BR>—तृण-निम्ब, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Nimba growing in Nepal (नेपाल-निम्ब); Aga-<BR>thotes Chirayta (किरात-तिक्त) — तृण-प, अस्, m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-b" target="_blank">Page0382-b+ 81</a>]<BR>N. of a Gandharva.<BR>—तृण-पञ्च-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>an aggregate of five roots of gramineous plants, viz.<BR>of rice, sugar-cane, Darbha, Scirpus Kysoor (क-<BR>शेरु), and a cane similar to Saccharum Sara (=<BR>शर).<BR>—तृण-पत्त्रिका, f. a kind of sugar-cane<BR>(इक्षु-दर्भा).<BR>—तृण-पत्त्री, f. a kind of grass,<BR>= गुण्डाशिनी.<BR>—तृण-पदी, f. having legs as thin<BR>as blades of grass.<BR>—तृण-पाणि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>Ṛṣi.<BR>—तृण-पीड, अम्, n. pressing as close as<BR>grass, hand to hand fighting, close quarters.<BR>—तृण-<BR>पुष्प, अम्, n. a kind of perfume, = तृण-कुङ्-<BR>कुम; (ई), f. a kind of plant, = सिन्दूर-पुष्पी.<BR>—तृण-पूलक = तृण-पूली (?) .<BR>—तृण-पूली,<BR>f. a mat, a seat made of reeds or basket-work.<BR>—तृण-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, worth a straw, worth-<BR>less.<BR>—तृण-मणि, इस्, m. ‘straw-attracting gem,’<BR>a sort of gem, apparently amber; [cf. तृण-ग्रा-<BR>हिन्.]<BR>—तृण-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting or made<BR>of grass, grassy.<BR>—तृण-मुष्टि, इस्, f. a handful of<BR>grass.<BR>—तृण-राज्, ट्, m. ‘the king of the grasses,’<BR>the vine-palm.<BR>—तृण-राज, अस्, m. ‘the king of<BR>the grasses,’ the palm or the palmyra-tree, Borassus<BR>Flabelliformis; the cocoa-nut tree; bamboo; sugar-<BR>cane.<BR>—तृण-राजन्, आ, m. ‘the king of the grasses,’<BR>the vine-palm.<BR>—तृण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding<BR>in grass, grassy.<BR>—तृण-वल्व-ज, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), Saccharum Cylindricum; (आ), f. = वल्व-जा.<BR>—तृण-विन्दु, उस्, m., N. of an ancient sage and<BR>prince; [cf. तार्णविन्दवीय.]<BR>—तृणविन्दु-सरस्,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a lake.<BR>—तृण-विस्तर, अस्, m. a<BR>heap of grass.<BR>—तृण-वीज or तृण-वीजक or तृ-<BR>णवीजोत्तम (˚ज-उत्˚), अस्, m. a kind of grain, =<BR>श्यामाक.<BR>—तृण-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the fan-palm;<BR>the date tree; the cocoa-nut tree; the areca-nut<BR>tree; Pandanus Odoratissimus; [cf. तृण-द्रुम.]<BR>—तृण-शीत, अम्, n. a kind of fragrant grass, An-<BR>dropogon Serratus; (आ), f. a kind of aquatic plant,<BR>= जल-पिप्पली.<BR>—तृण-शून्य, अस्, m. Jasmi-<BR>num Sambac; the fruit of Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR>—तृण-शूली, f. a kind of plant.<BR>—तृण-शोणित,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of perfume, = तृण-कुङ्कुम; [cf.<BR>तृणासृज्.]<BR>—तृण-शोषक, अस्, m. a kind of ser-<BR>pent.<BR>—तृण-शौण्डिका, f. a kind of Achyranthes.<BR>—तृण-षट्पद, अस्, m. a wasp (‘an insect with<BR>six feet infesting grass’).<BR>—तृण-सारा, f. the plan-<BR>tain or banana, Musa Sapientum.<BR>—तृण-सिंह,<BR>अस्, m. an axe (‘a reed lion’).<BR>—तृण-सोमाङ्गिरस्<BR>(˚म-अङ्˚), आस्, m., N. of one of the seven sacrificial<BR>priests of Yama.<BR>—तृण-स्कन्द, अस्, m., Ved., N.<BR>of a man; (Sāy.) trembling or fading away like<BR>grass.<BR>—तृण-हर्म्य, अस्, m. a house or upper<BR>room of grass or straw.<BR>—तृणांह्रिप (˚ण-अं˚),<BR>अस्, m. a kind of grass, = मन्थानक-तृण; (also<BR>read तृणाङ्घ्रिप.)<BR>—तृणाग्नि (˚ण-अग्˚), इस्, m.<BR>a grass fire, i. e. one quickly extinguished; confla-<BR>gration of straw or chaff; burning a criminal wrapped<BR>up in straw.<BR>—तृणाञ्जन (˚ण-अञ्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>chameleon, a lizard.<BR>—तृणाटवी (˚ण-अट्˚), f. a<BR>forest abounding in grass.<BR>—तृणाढ्य (˚ण-आढ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a kind of grass, = पर्वत-तृण; [cf. पत्-<BR>त्राढ्य.]<BR>—तृणान्न (˚ण-अन्˚), अम्, n. rice grow-<BR>ing wild; [cf. तृण-धान्य.]<BR>—तृणाम्ल (˚ण-<BR>अम्˚), अम्, n. a kind of grass, = लवण-तृण.<BR>—तृणारि (˚ण-अरि), इस्, m. a kind of Mollugo, (a<BR>common weed.)<BR>—तृणावर्त (˚ण-आव्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—तृणावर्त-वध, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a chapter of the Gaṇeśa-khaṇḍa or third part of the<BR>Brahmavaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—तृणा-वल्ली-तीर्थ, N.<BR>of a place mentioned in the Rasika-ramaṇa by<BR>Raghu-nātha.<BR>—तृणासृज् (˚ण-अस्˚), क्, n. a kind<BR>of perfume, = तृण-कुङ्कुम, तृण-शोणित.<BR>—तृ-<BR>णेक्षु (˚ण-इक्˚), उस्, m. a kind of long grass,<BR>Saccharum Cylindricum.<BR>—तृणेन्द्र (˚ण-इन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘prince of the grasses,’ the palmyra-palm (=<BR>ताल); [cf. तृण-राज.]<BR>—तृणोत्तम (˚ण-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘best of grasses,’ a kind of Andropogon (उखर्-<BR>वल).<BR>—तृणोत्थ (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>perfume, = तृण-कुङ्कुम.<BR>—तृणोदक (˚ण-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. grass and water.<BR>—तृणोद्भव (˚ण-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. rice &c. growing wild or without culti-<BR>vation; a kind of perfume, = तृणोत्थ.<BR>—तृणोलप<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">Page0382-c+ 75</a>]<BR>(˚ण-उल्˚), अम्, n. grass and shrubs.<BR>—तृणोल्का<BR>(˚ण-उल्˚), f. a torch of hay; a fire-brand made of a<BR>wisp of straw.<BR>—तृणौकस् (˚ण-ओक्˚), अस्, n. a hut,<BR>a house of straw or mats.<BR>—तृणौषध (˚ण-<BR>ओष्˚), अम्, n. the fragrant bark of Feronia Elephan-<BR>tum (= एलवालुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणक|तृणकं
तृणक, अम्, n. grass, a worthless blade of grass;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकीया
तृणकीया, f. a grassy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणस
तृणस, अस्, आ, अम्, grassy, abounding in grass, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणीकृ
तृणी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make straw<BR>of, to make light of.<BR>—तृणी-कृत्य, having esteemed<BR>as lightly as straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणीय
तृणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to grass (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्या
तृण्या, f. a heap or quantity of grass or straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणता
तृणता 2. तृणता, f. (for 1. see under तृण,<BR>col. 1), a bow, = त्रिणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणमत्कृण
तृणमत्कृण तृणमत्कृण or तृणमत्कुण,<BR>अस्, m. a bail or surety, security, warranty; (the right<BR>reading may be ऋणमत्कुण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणाङ्कु
तृणाङ्कु तृणाङ्कु, उस्, m., N. of an ancient<BR>sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणामल्ल
तृणामल्ल तृणामल्ल, N. of a temple; (also<BR>read त्रिणामल्ल and त्रिमल्ल and तृणावल्ली-<BR>तीर्थ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्ण
तृण्ण तृण्ण. See under rt. तृद् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृत
तृत तृत = त्रित, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीय|तृतीयः
तृतीय तृतीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. त्रि), the third;<BR>forming or constituting the third part; (अस्), m.,<BR>scil. वर्ण, the third consonant of a Varga (i. e.<BR>ग्, ज्, ड्, द्, ब्); (आ), f., scil. तिथि, the third day in<BR>a half month; scil. विभक्ति, the terminations of<BR>the third case, the third case, the instrumental;<BR>(अम्), n. a third part; (अम् or एन), ind. at or<BR>for the third time, thirdly; [cf. Zend thri-tya;<BR>Lith. tré-cia-s of trétias; Lat. ter-tius; Gr. τρίτος;<BR>Goth. thri-dya; Slav. tre-tiĭ; Scot. tri-teamh;<BR>Hib. triugha.]<BR>—तृतीय-ता, f. ‘thirdness,’ the con-<BR>dition of the third consonant of a Varga.<BR>—तृतीय-<BR>प्रकृति, इस्, f. (‘the third nature’), a eunuch; the<BR>neuter gender.<BR>—तृतीय-सवन, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>third Soma offering (in the evening).<BR>—तृतीय-<BR>सवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the third Soma<BR>offering.<BR>—तृतीय-स्वर, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—तृतीयांश (˚य-अं˚), अस्, m. a third part; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), receiving a third as one's share.<BR>—तृतीया-<BR>प्रकृति, इस्, f. a eunuch; a hermaphrodite; the<BR>neuter gender, = तृतीय-प्रकृति.<BR>—तृतीया-स-<BR>मास, अस्, m. a compound word (Tat-puruṣa), the<BR>former member of which would stand in the instru-<BR>mental case, if separated from the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयक
तृतीयक, अस्, इका, अम्, recurring every third day,<BR>tertian (as fever &c.); occurring for the third time;<BR>the third; (इका), f. = तृतीया, the third day in a half<BR>month.<BR>—तृतीयक-ज्वर, अस्, m. tertian ague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाकृ
तृतीया-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to plough for the third time.<BR>—तृतीया-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, thrice ploughed (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयिन्
तृतीयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, holding the third place or<BR>rank; having or receiving a third as one's share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृत्सु
तृत्सु तृत्सु, उस्, m., अवस्, m. pl., Ved., N. of<BR>a Vedic race or family; (Sāy.) injurious, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृद्
तृद् तृद् [cf. rt. तर्द्], cl. 7. P. A. तृ-<BR>णत्ति, तृन्त्ते or तृन्ते, ततर्द, ततृदे,<BR>तर्दिष्यति, -ते, and तर्त्स्यति, -ते, अतृदत् and<BR>अतर्दीत्, अतृत्त, तर्दितुम्, to cleave; to split<BR>open; to pierce, cut through; to let out, set free;<BR>to kill, destroy, injure; to disregard; to eat (?); to<BR>give; cl. 1. P. तर्दति, to kill, injure: Caus. तर्-<BR>दयति, -यितुम्, अततर्दत् and अतीतृदत्: Desid.<BR>तितर्दिषति, -ते, and तितृत्सति, -ते: Intens. तरी-<BR>तृद्यते, तरीतर्त्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्ण
तृण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, split, pierced, cut, injured, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृदिल
तृदिल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having holes, porous;<BR>(Sāy.) splitting, cleaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0382-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्
तृप् 1. तृप्, cl. 4. 5. 6. P. तृप्यति, तृप्-<BR>नोति (Ved. तृप्णोति), तृपति or तृम्पति,<BR>ततर्प; तर्पिष्यति, तर्प्स्यति, त्रप्स्यति; अतृ-<BR>पत्, अतर्पीत्, अतार्प्सीत्, अत्राप्सीत्; तर्प्तुम्, त्रप्-<BR>तुम्, तर्पितुम्; to satisfy one's self, to become<BR>satiated or satisfied, to be pleased or satisfied or con-<BR>tented (with gen., inst., or loc., e. g. नाग्निस् तृप्-<BR>यति काष्ठानाम्, fire is not satisfied with wood;<BR>तृप्यति फलैः, he is satisfied with fruits); to<BR>enjoy; to satisfy, satiate, please; cl. 1. P. तर्पति,<BR>&c., to light up, kindle (i. e. satiate a fire with fuel):<BR>Caus. P. A. तर्पयति, -ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अतीतृपत्<BR>and अततर्पत्, to gladden, exhilarate; to satiate,<BR>refresh, satisfy; A. to become satiated or satisfied;<BR>P. to light, kindle: Desid. तितृप्सति, तितर्पिषति,<BR>to wish to satiate one's self, to desire to satisfy:<BR>Desid. of the Caus. तितर्पयिषति, to wish to<BR>satiate or refresh or satisfy: Intens. तरीतृप्यते, त-<BR>रीतर्प्ति and तरीत्रप्ति; [cf. तृम्प्, तृफ्, तृम्फ्:<BR>Gr. τέρτω, τρέφω (?) Old Pruss. en-terpo, ‘to be<BR>useful:’ Lith. tarpstu, ‘to increase, to prosper;’<BR>tarpà, ‘increase:’ Goth. tharf, ‘to satisfy, to be<BR>useful:’ Old Germ. trôstyan: Angl. Sax. thearf:<BR>Hib. tropadh, ‘heavy, grave;’ tromaighim = tar-<BR>payāmi; tormach, ‘increase, augmentation;’ torp,<BR>‘bulk;’ tormad, ‘pregnant, big.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्
2. तृप्, at the end of a comp. in अ-सुतृप् and<BR>पशु-तृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप
तृप. See अ-तृप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपत्
तृपत्, ind., Ved. with pleasure or enjoyment, to<BR>one's satisfaction; (त्), m. a parasol; the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपल|तृपलः
तृपल, अस्, आ, अम् (said by some to be fr. rt.<BR>त्रप्), Ved. quick, restless, hasty, anxious; pleased,<BR>glad; (आ), f. a creeper or creeping plant; [cf.<BR>तृप्र.]<BR>—तृपल-प्रभर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>pressing quickly forwards, acting quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपा
तृपा, f. a kind of plant; [cf. तार्प्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपाय
तृपाय (fr. तृपत्), nom. A. तृपायते, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्त|तृप्तः
तृप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, satiated, satisfied, contented;<BR>(अम्), n. the becoming satiated, satisfaction.<BR>—तृप्-<BR>तांशु (˚त-अं˚), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having well nou-<BR>rished shoots or members, epithet of the Soma<BR>plant.<BR>—तृप्तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, having a<BR>contented mind, contented, satisfied, tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ताय
तृप्ताय, nom. A. तृप्तायते, &c., to be or<BR>become satiated or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ति|तृप्तिः
तृप्ति, इस्, f. satisfaction, contentment; satiety,<BR>disgust; hilarity, pleasure, gratification; Ved. water;<BR>[cf. अति-तृप्ति.]<BR>—तृप्ति-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving satis-<BR>faction, pleasing.<BR>—तृप्ति-दीप, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—तृप्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, satisfied, feeling<BR>satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्तिन्
तृप्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, satiated, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्र|तृप्रः
तृप्र, अस्, आ, अम्, restless, hasty, anxious; pleased,<BR>contented, (compar. त्रपीयस्, superl. त्रपिष्ठ);<BR>(अस्), m. an oblation of ghee or boiled butter.<BR>—तृप्र-दंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. biting hastily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्रालु
तृप्रालु, उस्, उस्, उ, having ghee, but not liking<BR>it or not blending with it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपु|तृपुः
तृपु तृपु, उस्, m., Ved. a thief; [cf. त्रिपु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफ्
तृफ् तृफ्, cl. 6. P. तृफति, &c., = 1. तृप्,<BR>to satisfy, gratify, please; to be contented<BR>or pleased; to kill, hurt. See तर्फितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफला
तृफला तृफला, f. = त्रि-फला, the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफू
तृफू तृफू, ऊस्, f. a serpent in general,<BR>the serpent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृमदण्डिक
तृमदण्डिक तृमदण्डिक (?), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्प्|तृंप्
तृम्प् तृम्प् or तृम्फ्, cl. 6. P. तृम्पति<BR>or तृम्फति, &c., = 1. तृप्, to be pleased<BR>or satisfied; to content, please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्फण
तृम्फण, अम्, n. pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्फणीय
तृम्फणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pleased, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
तृष् 1. तृष्, cl. 4. P. तृष्यति, ततर्ष<BR>(Ved. 3rd pl. तातृषुस्, part. तातृषाण),<BR>अतर्षत्, तर्षितुम्, to be thirsty, to thirst; to<BR>thirst for (metaphorically), desire, long for: Caus.<BR>तर्षयति, -यितुम्, to cause to thirst; [cf. Zend<BR>tarṣṇa, ‘thirst;’ Goth. thars, ‘to become dry;’<BR>thairsa, thars, thaursum; thaursus, ‘dry;’ thaurs-<BR>tei, ‘thirst;’ thaursyan, ‘to thirst;’ ga-thaurs-<BR>an-s, ‘dry:’ Angl. Sax. thurst, thyrr: Old Germ.<BR>darran, ‘to become dry:’ Germ. durst: Gr. τέρσ-<BR>ο-μαι, τερσαίνω, ταρσός, ταρσ-ιά, τρασ-ιά: Lat.<BR>torreo for torseo, tos-tum from tors-tum, torris,<BR>torrens: Lith. tróksztu, ‘to thirst;’ trószkulis,<BR>‘thirst:’ Hib. tart (tar-t), ‘thirst, drought;’ tart-<BR>mhar, ‘thirsty, dry.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
2. तृष्, ट्, f. thirst; thirst after (metaphorically),<BR>wish, strong desire; Desire personified as a daughter<BR>of the god of Love (Kāma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषा
तृषा, f. thirst; strong desire or wish; Desire<BR>personified as a daughter of Kāma; a poisonous<BR>plant, Methonica Superba (लाङ्गलिकी).<BR>—तृषा-<BR>भू, ऊस्, f. the bladder (whence thirst exists or<BR>arises).<BR>—तृषा-रोग, अस्, m. ‘morbid thirst,’ N. of<BR>a particular disease.<BR>—तृषार्त (˚षा-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, suffering from thirst, thirsty; affected by desire.<BR>—तृषा-ह, अम्, n. water (destroying or quenching<BR>thirst); (आ), f. a kind of anise, = मधुरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषाण
तृषाण, अस्, आ, अम्, (Ved. part.) being thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषित|तृषितः
तृषित, अस्, आ, अम्, thirsty, thirsting (physically<BR>or metaphorically); (अम्), n. thirst, desire.<BR>—तृ-<BR>षितोत्तरा (˚त-उत्˚), f., N. of a plant, = अशन-<BR>पर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषित्वा
तृषित्वा or तर्षित्वा, ind. having become thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषु
तृषु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. greedy, libidinous, thirst-<BR>ing for, eagerly desirous; rushing violently, quick.<BR>—तृषु-च्यवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. moving rapidly<BR>or quickly.<BR>—तृषु-च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. quickly<BR>issuing, rapidly moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णक
तृष्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, said to = तृष्णज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णज्
तृष्णज्, क्, क्, क्, thirsty (physically or meta-<BR>phorically), desiring, longing for, cupidinous; [cf.<BR>अ-तृष्णज्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णा
तृष्णा, f. (in the Veda the accent is on the first<BR>syllable, in later Sanskrit on the last), thirst, strong<BR>wish, desire, avidity; (Tṛṣṇā and Lobha are some-<BR>times personified as the parents of Dambha; or<BR>Tṛṣṇā is variously regarded as a daughter of Death,<BR>or of Pāpīyas, or as generated by Vedanā and gene-<BR>rating Upādāna); [cf. अति-तृष्ण.]<BR>—तृष्णा-<BR>क्षय, अस्, m. cessation of desire, tranquillity of<BR>mind, resignation, patience, content.<BR>—तृष्णा-घ्न,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, quenching the thirst.<BR>—तृष्णामय<BR>(˚णा-आम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ill with thirst.<BR>—तृष्णा-<BR>मार, अस्, m., Ved. dying of thirst.<BR>—तृष्णारि<BR>(˚णा-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of thirst,’ a kind of plant<BR>(= पर्पट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णालु
तृष्णालु, उस्, उस्, उ, thirsting much, very thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्यत्
तृष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, thirsting, athirst; desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्या
तृष्या, f., Ved. thirst.<BR>—तृष्या-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. thirsty; [cf. तर्ष्या-वत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषम
तृषम तृषम = त्रिषम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्ट
तृष्ट तृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rough, harsh;<BR>pungent; rugged; hoarse.<BR>—तृष्ट-जम्भ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having rough or uneven teeth.<BR>—तृष्ट-<BR>दंश्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. biting roughly.<BR>—तृष्ट-<BR>धूम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having pungent breath,<BR>epithet of a snake.<BR>—तृष्ट-वन्दन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. one whose praise is distasteful.<BR>—तृष्टामा<BR>(˚ट-अम्˚), f., Ved. N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्टिका
तृष्टिका, f., Ved. rough, disagreeable, epithet of<BR>a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृह्
तृह् तृह् or तृंह्, cl. 6. 7. P. तृहति or<BR>तृंहति, तृणेढि, ततर्ह, तर्हिष्यति<BR>and तर्क्ष्यति, अतर्हीत् and अतृक्षत्, तर्हितुम्<BR>and तर्ढुम्, to dash to pieces, crush, bruise; to<BR>hurt, injure, strike, kill: Caus. तर्हयति: Desid.<BR>तितर्हिषति, तितृक्षति, तितृंहिषति: Intens.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">Page0383-c+ 78</a>]<BR>तरीतृह्यते, तरीतर्ढि: [cf. perhaps Goth. thras-<BR>can; Angl. Sax. therscan old desid.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृढ
तृढ, अस्, आ, अम् (Ved. तृऌह), crushed, bruised,<BR>hurt, injured, wounded, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृढ्वा
तृढ्वा or तर्हित्वा, ind. having killed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तॄ
तॄ तॄ, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A., Ved. also<BR>cl. 6.) तरति, -ते, ततार (2nd sing. तेरिथ,<BR>3rd du. तेरतुस्, 3rd pl. तेरुस्), तरिष्यति or त-<BR>रीष्यति, अतारीत्, तरितुम् or तरीतुम् or तर्तुम्;<BR>[the following are Vedic forms, some of them<BR>occurring also in epic poetry; तिरति when preceded<BR>by prep.; तितर्ति, part. तित्रत्; तीर्यति, -ते; तुर्यात्,<BR>तुतुर्यात्; Aor. तारिषत्, अतारिम, तरीत्; तरु-<BR>षेम in Ṛg-veda VII. 48, 2, Pāṇ. III. 1, 85,<BR>तरुषन्त, तरुषन्ते; तितिरुस्, part. तितिर्वस्;<BR>gen. ततरुषस्; inf. तरध्यै]; to pass across<BR>or over, cross over (a river), sail across, navigate; to<BR>float, swim; to move on rapidly; to get through,<BR>attain an end or aim; to pervade; to come to the<BR>end of; to live through (a definite period); to fulfil,<BR>accomplish, perform; to surpass, overcome, over-<BR>power, subdue, destroy, become master of; to ac-<BR>quire, gain; to escape (with acc.); to be saved or<BR>rescued; to escape from a danger (with abl.); to<BR>carry through or over, transport, save, liberate from;<BR>to strive or contend together, to compete: Caus. P.<BR>तारयति, -यितुम्, to carry or lead over or across;<BR>to cause to arrive at; to rescue, save, liberate [cf. rt.<BR>त्रै]: Desid. तितीर्षति, तितरिषति, तितरीषति,<BR>to wish to cross: Intens. तेतीर्यते, तातरीति or ता-<BR>तर्ति (Ved. pres. part. तरित्रत्), to pass completely<BR>through, make a way through, pervade; [cf. 1. तुर्, तुल्,<BR>तुर्व्; तर at p. 365: Zend tarō, ‘over:’ Gr. τερ-<BR>έ-ω, τέρ-ε-τρο-ν, τέρ-θρο-ν, τέρ-μα, τέρμων, τέρμ-<BR>ιο-ς, τερμιό-ει-ς, τείρ-ω, τρύ-ω, τρί-βω, τρύ-χ-ω,<BR>τέρ-ην, τι-τρά-ω, τι-τραίν-ω, τέρ-α-ς, τορ-ό-ς, τόρ-<BR>ο-ς, τόρ-νο-ς, τορ-ύνη, τορ-εύ-ω, τρῦ-μα, τρῶ-μα,<BR>τρῆ-μα, τέλος, τέλλω (‘to rise’), τηρέω (caus.),<BR>τρῡτάνη; perhaps also Τάρᾱς, Τρο-ία, Τροιζήν,<BR>τελέω, τέλειος, τελευτή, τᾶλις, θραύ-ω, τραῦ-μα<BR>θλά-ω, θλίβ-ω: Lat. ter-mo, ter-men, ter-minu-s,<BR>ter-o, ter-e(t)-s, ter-e-bra, trib-ula, tribulare, trī-<BR>ti-cu-m, in-tra-re, peni-tra-re, ex-tra-re, trans:<BR>Umbr. termnu, traf = trans: Osc. teremenniu§:<BR>Sabin. terentum, Terentius, tur-unda, tru-a,<BR>‘a ladle;’ trāme(t)-s, Tras-im-enu-s, ‘the opposite,<BR>ulterior:’ Goth. thair-ko, ‘a hole;’ thairh: Old<BR>Germ. durh: Eng. through: Old Island. thrö-m,<BR>‘margin:’ Old Germ. dru-m, ‘limit, border:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. thrā-v-an: Old Germ. drā-y-an, ‘to turn,<BR>whirl;’ thearl, thearm, thirel, thirlian, thole,<BR>tholian, thaelian, for-thyldian: Slav. tre†-ti, try-<BR>ti, ‘to rub:’ Lith. trī1n-ti, ‘to rub, file, polish,<BR>bore;’ til-tas, ‘a bridge;’ tolùs, ‘long, distant:’<BR>Hib. toir, ‘a pursuit;’ tor, ‘a pursuer;’ toramh,<BR>‘pursuit;’ toras, ‘a journey;’ teirin, ‘a descent;’<BR>tearnadh, ‘descending;’ tarradh, ‘protection;’<BR>tarthadoir, ‘a saviour.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरूतृ
तरूतृ = तरुतृ, at p. 365, by Pāṇ. VII. 2, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्ण|तीर्णः
तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, crossed, passed over; spread,<BR>expanded; surpassed, excelled; (आ), f., N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of four long syllables each.<BR>—तीर्ण-पदी, f. a species of plant, = ताल-मूली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्त्वा
तीर्त्वा, ind. having passed, crossed over, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेग
तेग तेग, अस्, m., Ved. only occurring in<BR>Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā XXV. 1, where the sense is<BR>doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज्
तेज् तेज् (probably connected with rt.<BR>तिज्), cl. 1. P. तेजति, &c., to guard, cherish,<BR>defend, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज|तेजः
तेज तेज, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तिज्), sharpness,<BR>pungency; sharpness (of a weapon); brilliancy;<BR>spirit; N. of a man.<BR>—तेज-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the leaf<BR>of Laurus Cassia.<BR>—तेज-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, sharp,<BR>&c.; see तेजो-वत्.<BR>—तेज-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king, a descendant of Paramāra, mentioned in the<BR>Rāja-taraṅgiṇī by Kalhaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजन|तेजनं|तेजनः
तेजन, अम्, n. sharpening; kindling, inflammation;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-a" target="_blank">Page0384-a+ 81</a>]<BR>enlightening, rendering bright, making splendid or<BR>polished; whetting; a point, the point of an arrow;<BR>a reed, a bamboo, the shaft of an arrow; the reed<BR>Saccharum Sara; (ई), f. a number of reeds, straw,<BR>&c., twisted or matted together, a mat; a tuft; a<BR>tuft of hair on the head (of a horse); N. of a plant,<BR>= मूर्वा, Sanseviera Roxburghiana; also = ज्योतिष्-<BR>मती, Cardiospermum Halicacabum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजनक|तेजनकः
तेजनक, अस्, m. a kind of reed, Saccharum Sara<BR>(= शर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजल|तेजलः
तेजल, अस्, m. the francoline partridge (= क-<BR>पिञ्जल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्
तेजस्, अस्, n. sharpness; the sharp edge (of a<BR>knife &c.); the point or top of a flame or of a ray<BR>&c.; glow, glare, fierce or scorching heat, radiance,<BR>splendor, brilliance, lustre, light, fire; clearness of<BR>the eyes; the clear or bright appearance of the<BR>human body (in health), beauty; the heating and<BR>strengthening faculty of the human frame seated in<BR>the पित्त; the bile; bilious humor &c.; fiery<BR>energy, ardour, power, might, spirit, strength,<BR>efficacy, male energy, semen virile, vital power;<BR>the brain; marrow; the essential nature or value<BR>of anything, essence; violence, mettle, fierceness,<BR>severity, energetic opposition; impatience, inability<BR>to bear or put up with; spiritual or moral or magical<BR>power; virtue; influence, effect, consequence, ma-<BR>jesty, fame, dignity, glory, authority; a brave man;<BR>a venerable or dignified person, a splendid object, a<BR>renowned person, a person of consequence; fresh<BR>butter; gold; [cf. अ-तेजस्, अग्नि-त्˚, उग्र-त्˚, तिग्म-<BR>त्˚, &c.; cf. also Hib. teas, ‘warmth, fervour.’]<BR>—तेजः-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, gleaming with lustre,<BR>flashing with brilliance (as a weapon).<BR>—तेजः-फल,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of plant, = बहु-फल, &c.<BR>—तेजः-<BR>सम्भव, अस्, m. = रस, lymph; [cf. अग्नि-सम्-<BR>भव.]<BR>—तेजः-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer.<BR>—तेजः-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—तेजस्-क, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, splendid, radiant, glorious, famous.<BR>—तेजस्-<BR>कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, irradiating, illuminating, granting<BR>strength or vital power.<BR>—तेजस्-काम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>longing for manly strength or vital power, desiring<BR>influence or authority or dignity.<BR>—तेजस्-तिमिर, ए,<BR>n. du. light and darkness.<BR>—तेजस्-तेजस्, आस्, m.<BR>whose essence is light, who is light of lights.<BR>—ते-<BR>जस्-त्व, अम्, n. the nature or essence of light,<BR>brightness, &c.<BR>—तेजस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a<BR>sharp edge (as a weapon); sharp, pungent; splendid,<BR>bright; energetic, spirited; (ती), f., N. of a princess;<BR>[cf. तेजो-वत्.]<BR>—तेजस्वि-ता, f. or तेजस्वि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. energetic behaviour or nature, energy, brilliancy,<BR>splendor.<BR>—तेजस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, brilliant, splendid,<BR>bright; powerful, energetic, strong, sound, inspiring<BR>respect, dignified, noble; famous, glorious, illustri-<BR>ous, celebrated; violent; lawful; haughty; granting<BR>strength &c.; (ई), m., N. of a son of Indra; (इनी),<BR>f. = ज्योतिष्-मती, Cardiospermum Halicacabum.<BR>—तेजस्वि-प्रशंसा, f., N. of a chapter of Śārṅga-<BR>dhara's anthology called Śārṅga-dhara-paddhati.<BR>—तेजो-नाथ-तीर्थ, अम्, n. the Tīrtha of the<BR>lord of light (the Sun?).<BR>—तेजो-निधि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘a<BR>treasury of glory,’ abounding in glory.<BR>—तेजो-बल-<BR>समन्वित or तेजो-बल-समायुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>endowed with spirit and strength.<BR>—तेजो-भङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. destruction of dignity, disgrace.<BR>—तेजो-मण्-<BR>डल, अम्, n. a disk or halo of light.<BR>—तेजो-मन्थ,<BR>अस्, m. the tree Premna Spinosa, (the friction of the<BR>wood engendering flame); [cf. अग्नि-मन्थ.]<BR>—तेजो-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of splendor or<BR>light, shining, brilliant, luminous, glorious; full of<BR>energy or ardour.<BR>—तेजो-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, whose<BR>form is light, consisting totally of light.<BR>—तेजो-राशि,<BR>इस्, m. a heap or mass of splendor, i. e. all splendor.<BR>—तेजो-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, whose form is light, con-<BR>sisting wholly of splendor; (अम्), n. Brahma, the<BR>supreme spirit; the nature of light.<BR>—तेजो-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, sharp, pungent; bright, splendid; energetic;<BR>(ती), f. = चव्य, Piper Chaba; Scindapsus Officinalis,<BR>= गज-पिप्पली, = महा-ज्योतिष्मती; a kind of<BR>medicinal root, commonly called Tejo-bala; N. of a<BR>princess; [cf. तेजस्-वत्.]<BR>—तेजो-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">Page0384-b+ 70</a>]<BR>possessing splendor or light.<BR>—तेजो-विन्दूपनिषद्<BR>(˚दु-उप्˚), त्, f. ‘a drop or particle of light,’ N. of<BR>an Upaniṣad.<BR>—तेजो-वीज, अम्, n. marrow.<BR>—तेजो-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. = क्षुद्राग्नि-मन्थ.<BR>—तेजो-<BR>वृत्त, अम्, n. noble or dignified behaviour; superior<BR>brilliancy or power.<BR>—तेजो-वृद्धि, इस्, f. increase<BR>of glory or dignity.<BR>—तेजो-ह्रास, अस्, m. loss of<BR>dignity or lustre.<BR>—तेजोह्वा (˚जस्-आह्˚), f. = तेजस्-<BR>विनी, = तेजिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस
तेजस, अम्, n. = तेजस्, power &c. (at the end of a<BR>compound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्य
तेजस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. splendid, conspicuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजित|तेजितः
तेजित, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened, whetted, polished,<BR>burnished; excited, invigorated, stimulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजिनी
तेजिनी, f. a sort of medicinal plant, commonly<BR>called Tejo-bala; Sanseviera Zeylanica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजिष्ठ
तेजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of तिग्म or<BR>तीक्ष्ण), Ved. very sharp or pointed, very bright,<BR>splendid, shining; vigorous, powerful, violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजीयस्
तेजीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. very bright, radiant,<BR>splendid; very powerful or vigorous; a man of high<BR>dignity or influence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजेयु
तेजेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजाउर
तेजाउर तेजाüर, N. of a place mentioned<BR>in the poem Rasika-ramaṇa by Raghu-nātha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेदनी
तेदनी तेदनी, f., Ved. blood or clotted<BR>blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेन|तेनः
तेन 1. तेन, अस्, m. a note or cadence in-<BR>troductory to a song &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेन|तेनः
तेन 2. तेन, ind. (Inst. sing. of the pronom.<BR>base 2. त), in that direction, there (correlative to<BR>येन, in which direction, where); in that manner,<BR>thus, so (correlative to येन, in what manner); on<BR>that account, for that reason, therefore, in conse-<BR>quence of; so with regard to (with acc.); तेन हि,<BR>therefore, now then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेप्
तेप् तेप्, cl. 1. A. तेपते, &c., to sprinkle,<BR>distil, ooze, drop; to shake, tremble; to<BR>shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेम|तेमः
तेम तेम, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तिम्), the becoming<BR>wet, wet, damp, moisture; [cf. स्तेम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेमन|तेमनं
तेमन, अम्, n. wetting, moistening, moisture;<BR>a sauce, condiment; (ई), f. a sort of chimney, a fire-<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेर
तेर तेर (?), अम्, n. the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेल
तेल तेल, अस्, m. a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेलु
तेलु तेलु, उस्, m., N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेव्
तेव् तेव्, cl. 1. A. तेवते, &c., to play,<BR>sport; to weep, lament; [cf. दिव् and देव्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेवन|तेवनं
तेवन, अम्, n. play, sport, pastime; a garden, a<BR>pleasure-garden or play-ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैकायन
तैकायन तैकायन, अस्, m. and तैकायनि,<BR>इस्, m. two patronymics from Tika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैकायनीय
तैकायनीय, अस्, m. a descendant or a pupil of<BR>Taikāyani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैक्ष्णायन
तैक्ष्णायन तैक्ष्णायन, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Tīkṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैक्ष्ण्य|तैक्ष्ण्यं
तैक्ष्ण्य तैक्ष्ण्य, अम्, n. (fr. तीक्ष्ण), sharp-<BR>ness (of a knife &c.), acuteness, heat, pungency,<BR>acerbity, fierceness, severity, vehemence, violence,<BR>cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैग्म्य
तैग्म्य तैग्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. तिग्म), sharp-<BR>ness, pungency, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैजनित्वच्
तैजनित्वच् तैजनित्वच्, क्, f. (?), a sort of<BR>Vīṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैजस|तैजसं|तैजसः
तैजस तैजस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तेजस्), bright,<BR>luminous, brilliant, consisting of light or fire, fiery,<BR>splendid; consisting of any shining substance such<BR>as metal, metallic; the gastric juice as coloured by<BR>digested food; passionate, energetic, vigorous, power-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">Page0384-c+ 75</a>]<BR>ful, intense; (अस्), m. ‘the bright one,’ i. e. the highly<BR>refined or subtle essence (in the Vedānta phil.); (ई),<BR>f. Scindapsus Officinalis; (अम्), n. any metal; ghee<BR>or oiled butter; intensity; vigour, energy; N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—तैजसावर्तनी or तैजसावर्तिनी (˚स-<BR>आव्˚), f. a crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतल
तैतल तैतल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतलायनि
तैतलायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Taitala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिक्ष
तैतिक्ष तैतिक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तितिक्षा),<BR>patient; (this word is also an adj. fr. तैतिक्ष्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिक्षव
तैतिक्षव, अस्, m. a patronymic from Titi-<BR>kṣu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिक्ष्य
तैतिक्ष्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Titikṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिर|तैतिरः
तैतिर तैतिर, अस्, m. = तित्तिरि, a partridge;<BR>(probably a wrong reading for तैत्तिर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिल|तैतिलं|तैतिलः
तैतिल तैतिल, अस्, m. a rhinoceros; a god;<BR>= कलिङ्ग; (अम्), n., N. of the fourth astronomical<BR>period called Karaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिलि
तैतिलि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिर|तैत्तिरं|तैत्तिरः
तैत्तिर तैत्तिर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तित्तिरि), pro-<BR>duced or coming from a partridge; sprung from the<BR>sage Tittiri; (अस्), m. = तित्तिरि, a partridge; a rhino-<BR>ceros; (अम्), n. a flock of partridges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरि|तैत्तिरिः
तैत्तिरि, इस्, m., N. of an ancient sage who was<BR>an elder brother of Vaiśampāyana; N. of a son of<BR>Kapota-roman and father of Punar-vasu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरिक|तैत्तिरिकः
तैत्तिरिक, अस्, m. one who catches partridges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरीय|तैत्तिरीयः
तैत्तिरीय, आस्, m. pl. the pupils of Tittiri, the<BR>followers of the Taittirīya school of the Yajur-veda;<BR>or the Yajur-veda itself, according to the version of<BR>this school; see तैत्तिरीय-संहिता.<BR>—तैत्तिरीय-<BR>चरण, अस्, अम्, m. n. the school or sect of the<BR>Taittirīyas.<BR>—तैत्तिरीय-प्रातिशाख्य, अम्, n. the<BR>Prātiśākhya of the Taittirīyas.<BR>—तैत्तिरीय-ब्राह्-<BR>मण, अम्, n. a Brāhmaṇa of the Taittirīya Yajur-<BR>veda.<BR>—तैत्तिरीय-शिक्षा, f. the pronunciation of<BR>letters, accents, &c., according to the Taittirīyas.<BR>—तैत्तिरीय-संहिता, f. the collection of the<BR>hymns &c. of the dark or black Yajur-veda; (this,<BR>the more ancient version of the Yajur-veda, was<BR>called Taittirīya, as, handed, down by Tittiri, the<BR>pupil of Yāska, the pupil of Vaiśampāyana; the more<BR>modern or bright Yajur-veda being attributed to<BR>Yājñavalkya, of the family of the Vājasaneyins: the<BR>legend relates that the Yajus in its original form<BR>was first taught by the sage Vaiśampāyana to twenty-<BR>seven pupils, Yājñavalkya being deputed by him to<BR>teach it to others; subsequently the sage being<BR>offended with Yājñavalkya, bade him relinquish the<BR>Veda committed to him, which he instantly disgorged<BR>in a tangible form; whereupon the other disciples of<BR>Vaiśampāyana receiving his command to pick it up,<BR>assumed the form of partridges for that purpose, and<BR>swallowed the texts, which were soiled, and hence<BR>named ‘black,’ the other name तैत्तिरीय having<BR>reference to the partridges. Yājñavalkya then had<BR>recourse to the Sun, and from that deity received a<BR>new revelation of the Yajus, which is sometimes<BR>called ‘white,’ and sometimes from the patronymic<BR>of Yājñavalkya, Vājasaneyin.)<BR>—तैत्तिरीयारण्यक<BR>(˚य-आर्˚), अम्, n. the Āraṇyaka of the Taittirīyas.<BR>—तैत्तिरीयोपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚), त्, f. the Upani-<BR>shad of the Taittirīyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरीयक|तैत्तिरीयकः
तैत्तिरीयक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Taitti-<BR>rīya version of the Yajur-veda; (आस्), m. pl. = तैत्ति-<BR>रीयास्, i. e. the followers of the Taittirīya school of<BR>the Yajur-veda.<BR>—तैत्तिरीयकोपनिषद् (˚क-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f. the Upaniṣad of the Taittirīyas mentioned in<BR>the Sarva-darśana-saṅgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैन्तिडीक|तैंतिडीक
तैन्तिडीक तैन्तिडीक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तिन्तिडीक),<BR>prepared with a sour sauce of tamarinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैन्दुक
तैन्दुक तैन्दुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तिन्दुक),<BR>derived from or belonging to the tree Diospyros<BR>Embryopteris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैभ
तैभ तैभ, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैमात
तैमात तैमात, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैमिर|तैमिरः
तैमिर तैमिर, अस्, m. (fr. तिमिर), scil.<BR>रोग, darkness or dimness of the eyes, a disease of<BR>the eyes; [cf. तिमिर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैमिरिक
तैमिरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, affected by this disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर
तैर तैर, अस्, m. or तैरण, अस्, m. or<BR>तैरणी, f., N. of a plant, = कु-नीली, राग-द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैरभुक्त
तैरभुक्त तैरभुक्त, अस्, ई, अम्, derived from<BR>or a native of Tīra-bhukti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैरश्च
तैरश्च तैरश्च, अस्, ई, अम्, derived from or<BR>composed by Tiraścī (as a Sāman or Sūkta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैरश्च्य
तैरश्च्य, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैरोविराम
तैरोविराम तैरोविराम, अस्, m. (fr. तिरस्+<BR>विराम), ‘extending beyond a pause’ or ‘having a<BR>pause between,’ i. e. the dependent Svarita in a com-<BR>pound when the Udātta upon which it depends<BR>stands on the last syllable of the first member of the<BR>compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैरोव्यञ्जन
तैरोव्यञ्जन तैरोव्यञ्जन, अस्, m. (fr. तिरस्<BR>+व्य्˚), ‘extending beyond the consonant’ or<BR>‘having a consonant between,’ the dependent Sva-<BR>rita when separated from the Udātta syllable of<BR>the same word by one or more consonants, i. e. a<BR>circumflex accent between which and the preceding<BR>acute vowel one or more consonants intervene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैरोह्न्य
तैरोऽह्न्य तैरोऽह्न्य = तिरो-ऽह्न्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर्थ
तैर्थ तैर्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तीर्थ), relating<BR>to a sacred bathing-place or shrine, coming from<BR>it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर्थक
तैर्थक, अस्, &c., an adj. fr. तीर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर्थिक|तैर्थिकः
तैर्थिक, अस्, ई, अम्, coming or derived from a<BR>holy place of pilgrimage; visiting the holy shrines or<BR>bathing-places; sacred, holy; (अम्), n. water from<BR>a sacred bathing-place, holy water; (अस्), m. an<BR>ascetic; [cf. तीर्थिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर्थ्य
तैर्थ्य, अम्, n. abstract noun fr. तीर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर्यगयनिक|तैर्य्यगयनिक
तैर्यगयनिक तैर्यगयनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>तिर्यग्-अयन), measured by the revolution of the<BR>sun, as a year, (opposed to सावनः संवत्-<BR>सरः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैर्यग्योन|तैर्य्यग्योन
तैर्यग्योन तैर्यग्योन, अस्, ई, अम्, or तैर्-<BR>यग्योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, or तैर्यग्योन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>तिर्यग्-योनि), of animal origin, relating to the<BR>animals, an animal, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैल|तैलं
तैल तैल, अम्, n. (fr. तिल), oil expressed<BR>from sesamum, mustard, &c.; oil in general, (often<BR>compounded with the name of the plant from which<BR>the oil is extracted); storax, gum benzoin, incense;<BR>[cf. तीक्ष्ण-तैल.]<BR>—तैल-कन्द, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of bulbous plant.<BR>—तैल-कल्क-ज, अस्, m. oil-cake;<BR>[cf. तिलकल्क-ज.]<BR>—तैल-कल्पना, f., N. of a<BR>chapter in the Śārṅga-dhara-saṃhitā or medical<BR>work by Śārṅga-dhara, son of Dāmodara.<BR>—तैल-<BR>कार, अस्, m. an oil manufacturer.<BR>—तैल-किट्ट,<BR>अम्, n. oil-cake, a cake made of oily seed; [cf. तिल-<BR>किट्ट.]<BR>—तैल-कीट, अस्, m. a kind of insect, =<BR>तैलिनी, दर्द्रु-नाशिनी, &c.<BR>—तैल-चौरिका, f.<BR>a cock-roach (‘stealing oil’).<BR>—तैल-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>oiliness, oily state.<BR>—तैल-द्रोणी, f. a tub or bath<BR>filled with oil.<BR>—तैल-पक, अस्, m. (पक fr. प,<BR>drinking), a kind of bird; an ‘oil-drinking’ beetle,<BR>a cock-roach; [cf. तैल-पा.]<BR>—तैल-पर्णक, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of fragrant grass, = ग्रन्थि-पर्ण; sandal-<BR>wood.<BR>—तैलपर्णिक, अस्, m. a kind of sandal-<BR>wood.<BR>—तैल-पर्णी, f. sandal; turpentine; incense;<BR>[cf. तिल-पर्ण and तिल-पर्णी.]<BR>—तैल-पा or<BR>तैल-पायिका, f. a kind of beetle or cock-roach; [cf.<BR>तैल-पक.]<BR>—तैल-पायिन्, ई, m. a kind of cock-<BR>roach; a sword (‘drinking oil,’ i. e. anointed with<BR>oil ?); (इनी), f. a kind of cock-roach.<BR>—तैल-पिञ्ज<BR>= तिल-पिञ्ज, white sesamum.<BR>—तैल-पिपीलिका, f.<BR>the small red ant.<BR>—तैल-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, = पीत-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">Page0385-b+ 73</a>]<BR>तैल, one who has drunk oil.<BR>—तैल-फल, अस्,<BR>m. the sesamum plant; Terminalia Catappa (=<BR>इङ्गुदी); Terminalia Bellerica.<BR>—तैल-भाविनी, f.<BR>= तिल-भाविनी, jasmine.<BR>—तैल-माली, f. a wick,<BR>the cotton of a lamp.<BR>—तैलम्-पाता, f. the pouring<BR>of sesamum-seeds into fire [cf. श्यैनम्-पाता];<BR>oblation to fire; (अस्, आ, अम्), mixed with oil &c.<BR>—तैल-यन्त्र, अम्, n. an oil-mill.<BR>—तैल-वल्ली,<BR>f. a kind of plant, = लघु-शतावरी (Asparagus).<BR>—तैल-वीज, Semecarpus Anacardium.<BR>—तैल-<BR>साधन, अम्, n. a fragrant substance or perfume,<BR>civet? (= कक्कोलक).<BR>—तैल-स्पन्दा, f., N. of<BR>several plants, = श्वेत-गोकर्णी; काकोली; Cucurbita<BR>Pepo.<BR>—तैल-स्फटिक, अस्, m. a sort of gem,<BR>amber (?).<BR>—तैलाकर (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्, m. seeds &c.<BR>from which oil is expressed.<BR>—तैलागुरु (˚ल-अग्˚),<BR>उ, n. a sort of Agallochum.<BR>—तैलाटी (˚ल-अटी), f.<BR>a wasp.<BR>—तैलाभ्यङ्ग (˚ल-अभ्˚), अस्, m. anoint-<BR>ing the body with oil.<BR>—तैलाम्बुका (˚ल-अम्˚), f.<BR>= तैल-पायिका, a sort of cock-roach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलक|तैलकं
तैलक, अम्, n. a small quantity of oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिक|तैलिकः
तैलिक, अस्, m. an oilman, an oil manufacturer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिन्
तैलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, relating or belonging to oil, oily,<BR>&c.; (ई), m. an oilman, an oil-grinder or preparer;<BR>(इनी), f. the wick or cotton of a lamp; a kind of<BR>insect found in oil (= तैल-कीट).<BR>—तैलि-शाला, f.<BR>an oil-mill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलीन|तैलीनं
तैलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, grown with sesamum; (अम्),<BR>n. a field of sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलक्य
तैलक्य तैलक्य, अम्, n. (fr. तिलक), putting<BR>the Tilaka-mark on the forehead (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलङ्ग|तैलंग|तैलंगः|तैलङ्गः
तैलङ्ग तैलङ्ग, अस्, m. the country along<BR>the coast south of Orissa as far as Madras, the<BR>modern Carnatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलवक
तैलवक तैलवक, अस्, &c., inhabited by<BR>the Telus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैल्वक
तैल्वक तैल्वक, अस्, &c. (fr. तिल्वक), com-<BR>ing from or made of the Tilvaka tree, the plant<BR>Symplocos Racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैव्रक
तैव्रक तैव्रक, अस्, &c., inhabited by the<BR>Tīvras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैव्रदारव
तैव्रदारव तैव्रदारव, अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>or coming from the tree Tīvra-dāru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैष|तैषः
तैष तैष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तिष्य), relating<BR>to the asterism Tiṣya; (अस्), m., N. of a month<BR>(December-January), the month in which the full<BR>moon stands in the asterism Tiṣya, = पौष and<BR>सहस्य; (ई), f., scil. तिथि or रात्रि, the day of full<BR>moon in month Taiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोक|तोकं
तोक तोक, अम्, n. (connected with 1. तुच् and<BR>1. तुज्, and said by some to be fr. rt. 2. तु), offspring,<BR>children, race, male or female offspring, a child,<BR>(in the Ṛg-veda तोक is never used in pl.; it is<BR>often joined with तनय); a new-born child; the<BR>offspring of any animal (in comp., e. g. वराह-<BR>तोक, a young boar); [cf. त्वक्ष्, स्तोक, तक्ष्; Gr.<BR>τέκνον, τίκτω, ἔτεκον, τοκάς; Angl. Sax. thegn,<BR>thegen; Old Germ. degan, ‘servant.’]<BR>—तोक-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. connected with offspring, having<BR>children.<BR>—तोक-साति, इस्, f., Ved. the acquisition of<BR>offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोक्म|तोक्मं|तोक्मः
तोक्म, अस्, m. and (in the earlier language) तोक्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. a young green blade of corn, especially<BR>of barley, green or unripe barley; (अस्), m. green<BR>colour; (अम्), n. the wax of the ear; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोटक|तोटकं|तोटकः
तोटक तोटक, अस्, m. a kind of poisonous<BR>insect; N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya; (अम्), n. a<BR>particular metre (each line of the stanza containing<BR>twelve syllables); according to some also a kind of<BR>drama, (probably a Prākṛt form for त्रोटक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोड्
तोड् तोड्, cl. 1. A. तोडते, &c., to treat<BR>with disrespect; to despise; [cf. तुड्ड्,<BR>तूड्, रौड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोडन|तोडनं
तोडन तोडन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. तुड्), split-<BR>ting (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोडलतन्त्र
तोडलतन्त्र तोडल-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोतल
तोतल तोतल, अस्, m., N. of a writer on<BR>medicine; (आ), f., N. of a goddess; [cf. त्रोतल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोतस्
तोतस् तोतस्, ind., Ved. (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara), a wife; or = त्वयि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोत्तायन
तोत्तायन तोत्तायन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>branch of the Atharva-veda, (also read तोत्तायनीय,<BR>तौत, and तौत्तायन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोत्त्र
तोत्त्र तोत्त्र or तोत्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. तुद्),<BR>a stick or bamboo with a sharp iron head used for<BR>guiding an elephant; a goad or pike for driving<BR>cattle.<BR>—तोत्र-वेत्र, अम्, n. a rod or wand borne<BR>by Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोद|तोदः
तोद, अस्, m. guiding or driving (horses &c.);<BR>‘the instigator and exciter’ (of all nature), an epi-<BR>thet of the Sun; sharp, shooting or pricking pain;<BR>pain, anguish, vexation, torture, disease, uneasiness<BR>either of body or mind; (अस्), m., Ved. a sacrificer;<BR>गोतमस्य तोदः, N. of a Sāman.<BR>—तोद-पर्णी,<BR>f. ‘prick-leaf,’ N. of a plant enumerated among the<BR>Ku-dhānyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोदन|तोदनं
तोदन, अम्, n. a stick used for guiding or driving<BR>cattle &c., a goad; stinging; pain, affliction from<BR>disease &c.; (अस्, अम्), m. n., N. of a tree and its<BR>fruit, (in Marāṭhī लघुकाङ्कड.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमर|तोमरं|तोमरः
तोमर तोमर, अस्, अम्, m. n. an iron club<BR>or crow; a lance, a javelin; a kind of metre con-<BR>sisting of four lines of nine syllables each; N. of a<BR>man; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a race.<BR>—तोमर-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. a warrior armed with a club or lance; throw-<BR>ing a lance.<BR>—तोमर-धर, अस्, m. a warrior<BR>armed with a club or lance; fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमराण
तोमराण तोमराण, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>[cf. तोरमाण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरिका
तोमरिका तोमरिका, f. = तुवरिका, a fra-<BR>grant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोय|तोयं
तोय तोय, अम्, n. (perhaps fr. rt. 2. तु),<BR>water; the regent of the Nakṣatra Āṣāḍhā;<BR>(तोयं कृ, to make an offering of water to a<BR>deceased person, with gen.); (आ), f., N. of a river;<BR>[cf. Slav. tayati, ‘to melt.’]<BR>—तोय-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>a religious ceremony performed with water, ablutions<BR>of various parts of the body, oblations of water<BR>offered to a deceased person.<BR>—तोय-काम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fond of water; (अस्), m. a sort of cane growing<BR>in or near water, Calamus Fasciculatus.<BR>—तोय-<BR>कुम्भ, Blyxa Saivala.<BR>—तोय-कृच्छ्र, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. a sort of penance, drinking nothing but water<BR>for a fixed period.<BR>—तोय-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing water<BR>or rain.<BR>—तोय-क्रीडा, f. sport or pastime in water,<BR>splashing about in water or besprinkling one another;<BR>[cf. जल-क्रीडा.]<BR>—तोय-गर्भ, the cocoa-nut<BR>(‘containing water’).<BR>—तोय-चर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>moving in water; (अस्), m. an aquatic animal.<BR>—तोय-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or living in water.<BR>—तोय-डिम्ब or -डिम्भ or -डिम्भक, अस्, m.<BR>hail.<BR>—तोय-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving water; (अस्), m.<BR>a cloud; a kind of Cyperus, = मुस्तक; (अम्), n.<BR>ghee or oiled butter.<BR>—तोयदात्यय (˚द-अत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the departure of the clouds, the autumn.<BR>—तोय-<BR>दान, अम्, n. a kind of gesticulation mentioned in<BR>the Purāṇa-sarva-sva by Halāyudha.<BR>—तोय-धर,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, bearing or containing water; (अस्), m.<BR>a cloud; a kind of medicinal plant, = सु-निषण्ण;<BR>a kind of Cyperus, = मुस्ता.<BR>—तोय-धार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, bearing or containing water; (अस्), m. a stream<BR>of water.<BR>—तोय-धि, इस्, m. ‘the receptacle of<BR>waters,’ the ocean.<BR>—तोयधि-प्रिय, अम्, n. cloves,<BR>(‘fond of the sea,’ i. e. produced in maritime<BR>countries.)<BR>—तोय-निधि, इस्, m. ‘a treasure-house<BR>of water,’ the ocean.<BR>—तोय-नीवी, f. ‘girdled by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">Page0386-a+ 77</a>]<BR>the ocean,’ an epithet of the earth.<BR>—तोय-पाषाण-<BR>ज-मल, अम्, n. calamine, oxide of zinc.<BR>—तोय-<BR>पिप्पली, f. the plant Jussiæa Repens.<BR>—तोय-<BR>पुष्पी or तोय-प्रष्ठा, f. trumpet-flower, Big-<BR>nonia Suaveolens.<BR>—तोय-प्रसादन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>purifying water; (अम्), n. the tree or the nut of the<BR>tree Strychnos Potatorum, the clearing-nut, (this nut<BR>being rubbed upon the inside of a water-jar occasions<BR>the precipitation of the impurities of the water<BR>poured into it.)<BR>—तोयप्रसादन-फल, अम्, n.<BR>the nut of the tree Strychnos Potatorum; [cf. the<BR>preceding.]<BR>—तोय-फला, f. Cucumis Utilissimus<BR>(= इर्वारु).<BR>—तोय-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed or<BR>consisting of water.<BR>—तोय-मल, अम्, n. sea foam.<BR>—तोय-मुच्, क्, m. a cloud (‘discharging water’).<BR>—तोय-यन्त्र, अम्, n. a water-clock, a clepsydra;<BR>[cf. जल-यन्त्र.]<BR>—तोय-रस, अस्, m. water,<BR>moisture.<BR>—तोय-राज्, ट्, m. ‘the king of the waters,’<BR>an epithet of the ocean.<BR>—तोय-राशि, इस्, m. ‘a heap<BR>of water,’ a pond, a lake.<BR>—तोय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>‘having water,’ surrounded by water; (अती), f., N.<BR>of a plant, = अमृत-वल्ली, Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—तोय-वल्लिका, f. Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—तोय-<BR>वल्ली, f. a kind of gourd, Momordica Charantia; [cf.<BR>कारवेल्ल.]<BR>—तोय-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the plant Blyxa<BR>Saivala.<BR>—तोय-वृत्ति = तोयापामार्ग.<BR>—तोय-<BR>वेला, f. the margin of the water, the water's edge,<BR>the shore.<BR>—तोय-व्यतिकर, अस्, m. blending or<BR>union of the waters (of two rivers).<BR>—तोय-शुक्तिका,<BR>f. a bivalve shell, an oyster.<BR>—तोय-शूक, Blyxa Sai-<BR>vala.<BR>—तोय-सर्पिका, f. a frog.<BR>—तोय-सुचक, अस्,<BR>m. a frog.<BR>—तोयाधार (˚य-आध्˚), अस्, m. a water<BR>reservoir, a lake.<BR>—तोयाधि-वासिनी (˚य-अध्˚), f.<BR>trumpet-flower, Bignonia Suaveolens; [cf. अम्बु-<BR>वासिनी and अम्बु-वासी.]<BR>—तोयापामार्ग (˚य-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. Achyranthes Aquatica.<BR>—तोयालय (˚य-आल्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ocean, sea; N. of a constellation.<BR>—तोयाशय<BR>(˚य-आश्˚), अस्, m. a water reservoir, a cistern, a lake,<BR>a river.<BR>—तोयोत्सर्ग (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, m. the pouring<BR>out or discharge of water, raining.<BR>—तोयोत्सर्ग-<BR>स्तनित-मुखर, अस्, आ, अम्, noisy with rain and<BR>thunder.<BR>—तोयोद्भवा (˚य-उद्˚), f. Achyranthes<BR>Aquatica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोरण|तोरणं|तोरणः
तोरण तोरण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (perhaps fr.<BR>rt. 1. तुर्, to press forwards, i. e. through a passage),<BR>an arch, a gate, an arched doorway, a portal, the<BR>ornamented arch of a door or gateway; any tempo-<BR>rary and ornamental arch; decoration of the gate-post<BR>(with boughs of trees, garlands, &c.); an outer door;<BR>a mound or elevated place near a bathing-place; a<BR>triangle supporting a large balance; (अम्), n. the<BR>neck, the throat; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—तोरण-माल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a<BR>place of pilgrimage.<BR>—तोरण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>arched, having ornamental arches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोरमाण
तोरमाण तोरमाण, अस्, m., N. of a prince;<BR>[cf. तोमराण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोरश्रवस्
तोरश्रवस् तोर-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N. of a<BR>Ṛṣi with the patronymic Āṅgirasa; [cf. तौर-<BR>श्रवस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोल|तोलं|तोलः
तोल तोल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तुल्), poising<BR>one's self, e. g. घन-तोल, (a bird) poising itself in<BR>the clouds; (अस्, अम्), m. n. weighing, weight or<BR>quantity measured by the balance; a Tola, a weight<BR>of gold or silver, (reckoned in books at 16 Māṣas<BR>or 5 Rettis or 6(1/2) grains each, and weighing there-<BR>fore 105 grains troy: in practice it is calculated at<BR>12 Māṣas, jeweller's weight, and weighs nearly<BR>double or 210 grains; but actually it is of the same<BR>weight as the Sicca or 179(2/3) grains.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलक|तोलकं
तोलक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of weight, = तोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलन|तोलनं
तोलन, अम्, n. raising, lifting up, weighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलयित्वा
तोलयित्वा, ind. having lifted up, having weighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोल्य
तोल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be raised, to be weighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोश
तोश तोश, अस्, आ, अम्, or तोशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्<BR>(fr. rt. 1. तुश्), Ved. distilling, trickling, granting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोष|तोषः
तोष तोष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तुष्), satisfaction,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">Page0386-b+ 65</a>]<BR>gratification, contentment, pleasure, joy, happiness;<BR>Contentment personified as a son of Bhaga-vat and<BR>one of the twelve Tuṣitas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषक
तोषक, अस्, इका, अम्, gratifying, causing pleasure<BR>or happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषण
तोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, satisfying, gratifying, making<BR>contented, appeasing, pleasing; (अम्), n. the act<BR>of satisfying, satisfaction, gratification, pleasing, de-<BR>lighting; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषणीय
तोषणीय or तोषयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>satisfied or gratified or made contented, to be<BR>pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषित
तोषित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, satisfied, gratified,<BR>appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषिन्
तोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) satisfied<BR>or contented with, pleased with, liking; gladdening,<BR>satisfying, making contented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोष्य
तोष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made satisfied or con-<BR>tented, to be pleased or delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषल|तोषलं
तोषल तोषल or तोसल, आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a race (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौक्षायण
तौक्षायण तौक्षायण, adj. from Tukṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौक्षिक|तौक्षिकः
तौक्षिक तौक्षिक, अस्, m. (a word borrowed<BR>fr. the Gr. τοξότης), the sign of the zodiac Sagit-<BR>tarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौग्र्य
तौग्र्य तौग्र्य, अस्, m., Ved. the son of<BR>Tugra, a patronymic of Bhujyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौच्छ्य
तौच्छ्य तौच्छ्य, अम्, n. (abstract noun fr.<BR>तुच्छ), emptiness, meanness, worthlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौण्डिकेर
तौण्डिकेर तौण्डिकेर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>race; [cf. तुण्डिकेर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौत
तौत तौत, another form for तोत्तायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौतातिक|तौतातिकं
तौतातिक तौतातिक, अस्, ई, अम्, composed<BR>by Tutāta, (according to a scholiast) = Kaumārilaṃ<BR>Śāstram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौतिक|तौतिकं|तौतिकः
तौतिक तौतिक, अस्, m. the pearl-oyster;<BR>(अम्), n. a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौत्तायन
तौत्तायन तौत्तायन, another form for<BR>तोत्तायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौद
तौद तौद, अम्, n. (fr. तुद or तोद), N. of<BR>a Sāman; (ई), f., Ved., N. of a plant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौदादिक
तौदादिक तौदादिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तुद् + आदि),<BR>belonging to the class of roots which begins with<BR>तुद्, i. e. to the sixth class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौदेय
1. तौदेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tuda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौदिय
तौदिय तौदिय, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौदेय
तौदेय 2. तौदेय, अस्, ई, अम्, produced in or<BR>coming from the district called Tūdī, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौम्बुरविन्
तौम्बुरविन् तौम्बुरविन्, इणस्, m. pl. the<BR>pupils of Tumburu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर
तौर तौर, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Tura;<BR>(अम्), n., scil. अयन, N. of a Sat-tra ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौरयाण
तौरयाण तौरयाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. =<BR>तूर्णयान, hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौरश्रवस
तौरश्रवस तौरश्रवस, अम्, n. (fr. तोर-<BR>श्रवस्), N. of two Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौरायणिक
तौरायणिक तौरायणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, per-<BR>forming the sacrifice or vow Turāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्य|तौर्यं|तौर्य्य|तौर्य्यं
तौर्य तौर्य, अम्, n. (fr. तूर्य), the sound<BR>of musical instruments, music, harmony, &c.<BR>—तौर्-<BR>य-त्रिक, अम्, n. triple symphony or harmony, i. e.<BR>union of song, dance, and instrumental music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्वश
तौर्वश तौर्वश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तुर्वश),<BR>epithet of a peculiar species of horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौल|तौलं
तौल तौल, अम्, n. a balance, = तुला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिक|तौलिकः
1. तौलिक in दश-तौलिक, having the weight of<BR>10 Tulās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिन्
तौलिन्, ई, m. (fr. तुला), one who holds a balance,<BR>a weigher; the sign of the zodiac Libra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौल्य|तौल्यं
तौल्य, अम्, n. weight; equality, similarity,<BR>likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिक|तौलिकः
तौलिक 2. तौलिक, अस्, m. (fr. तूलिका), a<BR>painter; [cf. the next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिकिक|तौलिकिकः
तौलिकिक, अस्, m. a painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौल्वलि
तौल्वलि तौल्वलि, इस्, m. (fr. तुल्वल?), N.<BR>of a preceptor; अजा-तौल्वलि, Taulvali fond of<BR>goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौल्वलायन
तौल्वलायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Taulvali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौवरक
तौवरक तौवरक, अस्, ई, अम्, derived or<BR>coming from the plant Tuvaraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौविलिका
तौविलिका तौविलिका, f., Ved. a kind of<BR>animal (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौषार|तौषारं
तौषार तौषार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. तुषार),<BR>snowy, dewy; (अम्), n. snow, cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्मन्
त्मन् त्मन्, आ, m. = आत्मन् (acc. त्मनम्<BR>and त्मानम्, dat. त्मने, loc. त्मनि; the initial<BR>आ is also rarely dropped in epic poetry after ए<BR>or ओ), Ved. the vital breath; one's own person, self.<BR>त्मन् is also used in Ved. for त्मना at the end of<BR>a Pāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्मना
त्मना, ind., Ved. Although according to the<BR>unanimous interpretation of the native scholiasts<BR>and grammarians (cf. Pāṇ. VI. 4, 141) this word<BR>stands for आत्मना, ‘by itself, myself, himself, one's<BR>self,’ &c., yet it has evidently in many cases lost its<BR>original meaning and is used as an emphatic particle<BR>in the same way as the Greek μέν and μήν; it may<BR>then be translated by ‘yet,’ ‘really,’ ‘indeed,’ ‘even,’<BR>‘at least,’ ‘certainly,’ ‘also;’ (त्मना usually lays<BR>stress on a preceding and more rarely on a following<BR>word); उत त्मना, त्मना च, and also, and cer-<BR>tainly; इव त्मना or न त्मना, just as; अध<BR>त्मना, then certainly, even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्मन्या
त्मन्या, ind., Ved. (in certain Āprī hymns) =<BR>त्मना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्मूत
त्मूत त्मूत, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps for त्यूत fr.<BR>rt. तीव्), Ved. soaked with fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्य
त्य त्य. See त्यद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यगल
त्यगल त्यगल, अस्, m., N. of an author;<BR>(also read तिगल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यग्नायि
त्यग्नायि त्यग्नायि, Ved., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यज्
त्यज् 1. त्यज्, cl. 1. P. त्यजति, तत्याज<BR>(Ved. तित्याज), त्यक्ष्यति (rarely त्यजि-<BR>ष्यति), अत्याक्षीत्, त्यक्तुम्, to leave, abandon,<BR>quit; to leave a place, go away from; to let go, dis-<BR>miss, discharge; to shoot off; to give up, surrender,<BR>resign, part from, renounce (e. g. तनुं or देहं<BR>or कलेवरं त्यज्, to abandon the body, die; प्रा-<BR>णान् or श्वासं or जीवितं त्यज्, to give up breath or<BR>life, die, risk one's life); to shun, avoid; to get rid<BR>of, free one's self from, lose; to distribute, give away,<BR>give, offer (as a sacrifice or oblation to a deity);<BR>to set aside, leave unnoticed, disregard; to except:<BR>Pass. त्यज्यते, to be abandoned by, to become<BR>deprived of, lose, get rid of (with inst., e. g. ध-<BR>नेन त्यज्यते, he loses his riches): Caus. त्याज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अतित्यजत्, to cause to leave or<BR>abandon or quit, to deprive a person of anything<BR>(with two acc., e. g. त्याजयति मां गृहम्, he<BR>causes me to quit the house; or with acc. and inst.,<BR>e. g. अतित्यजत् तम् प्राणैः, he caused him to lose his<BR>life); to expel, turn out; to quit; to cause anything<BR>not to be noticed: Desid. तित्यक्षति: Intens.<BR>तात्यज्यते, तात्यक्ति; [cf. Hib. treigim, ‘I leave,<BR>forsake;’ treigthe, ‘forsaken,’ = त्यक्त; treigean,<BR>‘leaving, forsaking, abandonment,’ = त्यजन;<BR>treigtheoir, ‘a deserter, forsaker,’ = त्यक्तृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्त|त्यक्तं
त्यक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, left, resigned, forsaken, aban-<BR>doned, deserted, left alone, &c.<BR>—त्यक्त-जीवित or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">Page0387-a+ 80</a>]<BR>त्यक्त-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, ready to abandon life;<BR>willing to run all hazards, having relinquished all<BR>expectation of life as men on the forlorn hope.<BR>—त्यक्त-लज्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoning shame,<BR>shameless.<BR>—त्यक्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having left,<BR>leaving, abandoning, &c.<BR>—त्यक्त-विधि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>transgressing rules.<BR>—त्यक्त-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, abandoned<BR>by fortune.<BR>—त्यक्ताग्नि (˚त-अग्˚), इस्, m. a Brāh-<BR>man who has given up his household fire, one who<BR>neglects essential ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तव्य
त्यक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be left or abandoned or<BR>released, to be left to one's fate; to be removed or<BR>kept back; to be given up or sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तुकाम
त्यक्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तृ
त्यक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, resigning, leaving, abandon-<BR>ing, giving up, sacrificing; an abandoner, forsaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्त्वा
त्यक्त्वा, ind. having left, abandoned, surrendered,<BR>&c.; leaving aside, disregarding, with exception of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यज्
2. त्यज्, क्, क्, क्, (at the end of a comp.) leaving,<BR>abandoning, giving up, dying, risking one's life; [cf.<BR>तनु-त्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजन|त्यजनं
त्यजन, अम्, n. leaving, quitting, abandoning;<BR>giving; excepting, exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजनीय
त्यजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be left or abandoned, to<BR>be avoided, to be excepted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजस्
त्यजस्, अस्, n., Ved. abandonment; difficulty,<BR>danger; alienation, estrangement, dislike, anger,<BR>aversion, envy; (Sāy.) a weapon or instrument<BR>causing abandonment; (आस्, आस्, अस्), m. f. n., Ved.<BR>offspring, a descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याग|त्यागः
त्याग, अस्, m. leaving, letting go, abandoning,<BR>forsaking, parting from, deserting, renouncing, separa-<BR>tion; discharging; dismissing; giving up, resigning;<BR>gift, donation, distribution; sacrificing one's life;<BR>liberality, generosity, prodigality; secretion, excretion;<BR>a sage, one who separates himself from the world;<BR>[cf. आत्म-त्˚, तनु-त्˚, देह-त्˚.]<BR>—त्याग-पत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. a bill of divorcement.<BR>—त्याग-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, consisting only in giving or in donation.<BR>—त्याग-युत, अस्, आ, अम्, liberal.<BR>—त्याग-शील,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, disposed to give away, generous, liberal.<BR>—त्यागशील-ता, f. or त्यागशील-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>generosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिन्
त्यागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, leaving, abandoning, renouncing;<BR>giving up, resigning; sacrificing; liberal; (ई), m. an<BR>abandoner, (often applied to the religious ascetic who<BR>abandons terrestrial objects, thoughts, &c.); a giver,<BR>a donor; a hero.<BR>—त्यागि-ता, f. or त्यागि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. liberality, generosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिम|त्यागिमः
त्यागिम, अस्, आ, अम्, left, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याजक
त्याजक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who leaves, abandons,<BR>expels; leaving, abandoning, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याजित
त्याजित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to quit or abandon;<BR>caused to be disregarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याज्य|त्याज्यः
त्याज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be left or abandoned or<BR>quitted, to be avoided or shunned, to be expelled, to<BR>be removed; to be given up or relinquished or<BR>abstained from; to be sacrificed; to be excepted;<BR>(अम्), n. part of an asterism or its duration con-<BR>sidered as unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यद्
त्यद् त्यद्, स्यस्, स्या, त्यद् (a pronoun com-<BR>posed of the base of the demonstrative pron. त and<BR>the relative य, and not found in the later language),<BR>Ved. that, that person or thing, (often used like the<BR>article in other languages, e. g. त्यद् वसु पणीनां<BR>विदस्, thou didst find that wealth, i. e. the wealth of<BR>the Paṇis); it is sometimes strengthened by चिद् and<BR>often occurs in connection with other demonstratives;<BR>(त्यद्), ind., Ved. indeed, namely, as it is known,<BR>(always preceded by the particle ह, e. g. त्वम् ह<BR>त्यद् इन्द्र कुत्सम् आवस्, thou indeed, O Indra,<BR>didst help Kutsa); [cf. Old Germ. dër fr. diar, f. diu,<BR>acc. dia = त्याम्, nom. pl. m. die = त्ये, f. dio = त्यास्,<BR>n. diu = त्यानि: to syā belongs Old Germ. siu, acc.<BR>sia: Lith. and Slav. szis, sy, = syas; szi, si, = syā.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यत्र
त्यत्र, ind., Ved. at that place, there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यत्रत्य
त्यत्रत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. existing or being there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यद
त्यद, अस्, m. a son of that person; (अम्), ind.<BR>(at the end of an adv. comp.) = त्यद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यदायनि
त्यदायनि, इस्, m. a son of that person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यादृश्
त्या-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, and त्या-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, such<BR>a one as that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र
त्र 1. त्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. त्रै), protecting<BR>(in comp.; see अंस-त्˚, अङ्गुलि-त्˚, आतप-त्˚, कटि-<BR>त्˚, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र
त्र 2. त्र = त्रि, three, in द्वि-त्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रंस्
त्रंस् त्रंस्, cl. 1. 10. P. त्रंसति, त्रंस-<BR>यति, &c., to speak or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रख्
त्रख् त्रख्, cl. 1. P. त्रखति, &c., to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रङ्क्|त्रंक्
त्रङ्क् त्रङ्क्, cl. 1. A. त्रङ्कते, &c., to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रङ्ख्
त्रङ्ख् त्रङ्ख् or त्रङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. त्रङ्खति<BR>or त्रङ्गति, &c., to go or move, (a various<BR>reading for त्वङ्ग्); [cf. Hib. tairgim, ‘I escape;’<BR>tairgeadh, ‘going, passing.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रङ्ग|त्रङ्गः
त्रङ्ग त्रङ्ग, अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of town<BR>or N. of a town; the city of Hari-ścandra supposed to<BR>be suspended in the air; [cf. द्रङ्क, द्रङ्ग, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रद
त्रद त्रद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. तृद्), Ved. split-<BR>ting, one who cleaves or opens; a creator; (Sāy.) =<BR>तर्दयितृ, a killer or injurer (of enemies).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रन्द्|त्रंद्
त्रन्द् त्रन्द्, cl. 1. P. त्रन्दति, &c., to<BR>act, perform functions; to endeavour,<BR>strive; to be busy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप्
त्रप् त्रप्, cl. 1. A. त्रपते, त्रेपे, त्र-<BR>पिष्यते and त्रप्स्यते, अत्रपिष्ट and<BR>अत्रप्त, त्रपितुम् and त्रप्तुम्, to become per-<BR>plexed or embarrassed, to be ashamed, be modest:<BR>Caus. त्रपयति and त्रापयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>perplexed or ashamed: Desid. तित्रपिषते and ति-<BR>त्रप्सते: Intens. तात्रप्यते, तात्रप्ति; [cf. Gr.<BR>τρέπω, έν-τρέπω; Lat. turpis, probably also trepi-<BR>dus, = Ved. तृप्र, ‘hastening;’ Lith. trópiyu, ‘to<BR>throw;’ Slav. trepet, ‘trembling;’ probably Goth.<BR>dreiban; Angl. Sax. drif-an, dref-an.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप
त्रप, अस्, आ, m. f. (more commonly आ, f.), per-<BR>plexity, embarrassment, bashfulness, shame, modesty;<BR>(आ), f. an unchaste woman (a shame to her family);<BR>family, race; fame, celebrity; [cf. Gr. ἐν-τροπή.]<BR>—त्रपा-निरस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless, impudent.<BR>—त्रपान्वित (˚पा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, modest, bash-<BR>ful, ashamed.<BR>—त्रपा-भर, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome<BR>with shame.<BR>—त्रपा-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bashful,<BR>modest.<BR>—त्रपा-रण्डा, f. a harlot.<BR>—त्रपा-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, modest, ashamed.<BR>—त्रपा-हीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, shameless, immodest, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपमाण
त्रपमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपित
त्रपित, अस्, आ, अम्, modest, bashful, ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपु|त्रपुः
त्रपु, उ, n. tin; lead; (tin is said to be called<BR>त्रपु from its contracting just before melting; cf.<BR>लज्जालु, as a N. of the sensitive plant.)<BR>—त्रपु-<BR>कर्कटी, f. a kind of cucumber, = त्रपुसी.<BR>—त्रपु-<BR>कर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having tin ear-ornaments; (ई),<BR>m. an epithet of Bhava-nandin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुल|त्रपुलं
त्रपुल, अम्, n. tin, lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुष|त्रपुषं
त्रपुष, अस्, m., N. of a merchant; a cucumber<BR>or melon; (ई), f. = त्रपुसी; (अम्), n. cucumber,<BR>the fruit of the Trapuṣī; tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुस्
त्रपुस्, उस्, n. tin; [cf. त्रापुष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुस|त्रपुसं
त्रपुस, अम्, n. cucumber, the fruit of the<BR>Trapusī; tin; (ई), f. coloquintida and other sorts<BR>of cucumber, = महेन्द्र-वारुणी, कर्कटी, पीत-<BR>पुष्पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाक|त्रपाकः
त्रपाक त्रपाक, अस्, m., N. of a barbarous<BR>tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपिष्ठ|त्रपिष्ठः
त्रपिष्ठ त्रपिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of तृ-<BR>प्र), highly satisfied, much pleased or contented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपीयस्
त्रपीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of तृप्र), more<BR>satisfied, highly pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुटी
त्रपुटी त्रपुटी, f. small cardamoms; [cf.<BR>also त्रि-पुटा and त्रि-पुटी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुस्
त्रपुस् त्रपुस्. See under rt. त्रप् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप्र
त्रप्र त्रप्र, अम्, n. (a various reading for<BR>वप्र), lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप्स्य|त्रप्स्यं
त्रप्स्य त्रप्स्य, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तृप्), thin or diluted curds; (according to some<BR>authorities written द्रप्स्य and द्रप्स.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रय|त्रयं|त्रयः
त्रय त्रय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि), triple, three-<BR>fold, consisting of three, divided into three parts, of<BR>three kinds, treble; (ई), f., scil. विद्या, the threefold<BR>knowledge, the triple science (i. e. sacred revelation<BR>in its threefold form of hymn, sacrificial formula,<BR>and song, afterwards represented by the Ṛg, Yajur,<BR>and Sāma Vedas), the three Vedas collectively<BR>(omitting the Atharvan, which is not of equal au-<BR>thority); a triad, three collectively, a triplet, three,<BR>(e. g. शत-त्रयी, 300); a matron, a married woman<BR>whose husband and children are living; intellect,<BR>understanding; N. of a plant (Conyza Serratula), =<BR>सोम-राजिन्; (अम्), n. a triad, three collectively,<BR>three, τριάς.<BR>—त्रयी-तनु, उस्, m. an epithet of<BR>the Sun (having the three Vedas for a body, either as<BR>celebrated in the Vedas or because the Sāma-veda<BR>and portions of the other Vedas are said to have<BR>proceeded from the Sun); an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्रयी-धर्म, अस्, m. the duty enjoined by the<BR>Vedas (i. e. the forms of sacrifice &c. prescribed by<BR>them).<BR>—त्रयी-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of the<BR>three Vedas, containing them, resting on them, &c.<BR>—त्रयी-मुख, अस्, m. a Brāhman (‘having the<BR>three Vedas in his mouth’).<BR>—त्रयी-विद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. knowing the triple science; [cf. त्रयी and<BR>त्रैविद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयस्
त्रयस्, nom. pl. of त्रि, three, (used in comp. with<BR>a following decad, except असीति which takes त्रि. The<BR>other decads, except ten, twenty, and thirty, may also<BR>take त्रि for + 3.)<BR>—त्रयः-पञ्चाशत्, त्, f. fifty-<BR>three; [cf. त्रि-पञ्चाशत्.]<BR>—त्रयः-षष्टि, इस्, f.<BR>sixty-three; [cf. त्रि-षष्टि.]<BR>—त्रयः-सप्तति, इस्,<BR>f. seventy-three; [cf. त्रि-सप्तति.]<BR>—त्रयश्-चत्वा-<BR>रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the forty-third.<BR>—त्रयश्-चत्वा-<BR>रिंशत्, त्, f. forty-three; [cf. त्रि-चत्वारिंशत्.]<BR>—त्रयस्-त्रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the thirty-third; joined<BR>with thirty-three (e. g. त्रयस्त्रिंशं शतम्, 133);<BR>consisting of thirty-three; celebrated with the Stoma<BR>which consists of thirty-three parts or syllables, con-<BR>taining that Stoma, &c.<BR>—त्रयस्-त्रिंशत्, त्, f. thirty-<BR>three.<BR>—त्रयस्-त्रिंशति, इस्, f., Ved. thirty-three.<BR>—त्रयस्त्रिंश-पति, इस्, m. the chief of the thirty-<BR>three gods, an epithet of Indra.<BR>—त्रयस्त्रिंश-<BR>स्तोम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing the Trayastriṃśa-<BR>stoma.<BR>—त्रयस्-त्रिंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, containing thirty-<BR>three.<BR>—त्रयो-दश, अस्, ई, अम्, the thirteenth; joined<BR>with thirteen or having thirteen added (e. g. त्र-<BR>योदशं शतम्, 113); consisting of thirteen; (ई),<BR>f. the thirteenth day of the lunar fortnight; a kind<BR>of gesticulation mentioned in the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—त्रयोदशक, consisting of thirteen; (अम्), n. the<BR>number thirteen.<BR>—त्रयोदश-धा, ind. into or in<BR>thirteen parts.<BR>—त्रयो-दशन्, अ, m. f. n. pl. thirteen;<BR>[Gr. τρις-καί-δεκα for τρεῖς-˚ cf. Lat. tredecim for<BR>tres-decem; Lith. trylika fr. trydika.]<BR>—त्रयो-<BR>दशम, अस्, ई, अम्, the thirteenth.<BR>—त्रयोदश-<BR>विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of thirteen kinds.<BR>—त्रयो-<BR>दशिक, happening on the thirteenth day of the<BR>half-moon.<BR>—त्रयो-दशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. containing<BR>thirteen.<BR>—त्रयो-नवति, इस्, f. ninety-three; [cf.<BR>त्रि-नवति.]<BR>—त्रयोविंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the twenty-<BR>third; consisting of twenty-three.<BR>—त्रयो-विंशति,<BR>इस्, f. twenty-three.<BR>—त्रयो-विंशतिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, consisting of twenty-three.<BR>—त्रयोविंशति-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the twenty-third.<BR>—त्रयोविंशति-<BR>धा, ind. in twenty-three parts, in twenty-three<BR>ways, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रययाय्य
त्रययाय्य त्रययाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy.) = त्रातव्य, to be protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयोदशन्
त्रयोदशन् त्रयो-दशन्. See त्रयस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रय्यारुण
त्रय्यारुण त्रय्यारुण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince, a son of Tri-dhanvan; a son of Uru-kṣaya;<BR>N. of the Vyāsa in the fifteenth Dvāpara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रवाडिलघु
त्रवाडिलघु त्रवाडि-लघु, उस्, m., N. of the<BR>father of Mahī-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्
त्रस् 1. त्रस्, cl. 10. P. त्रासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to take, seize; to hold; to oppose, pre-<BR>vent, forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्
त्रस् 2. त्रस्, cl. 1. and 4. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>त्रसति, त्रस्यति, तत्रास (3rd pl. त-<BR>त्रसुस् and त्रेसुस्), त्रसिष्यति, अत्रासीत् and अत्र-<BR>सीत्, त्रसितुम्, to tremble, quiver, quake, or start<BR>with fear; to be agitated, be afraid of; to fear, dread<BR>(with abl. or gen. and more rarely with inst., e. g.<BR>तस्मात् or तस्य त्रस्यति, he fears that or is afraid<BR>of him); to run away, run: Caus. त्रासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to tremble, terrify, to frighten, scare,<BR>agitate, set in motion: Desid. तित्रसिषति: Intens.<BR>तात्रस्यते, तात्रस्ति; [cf. Zend tareś, tars-ti: Gr.<BR>τρέω for τρεσιyω, ταρταρίζω, τρήπων for τρεσ-<BR>πων, τρέ-μ, τάρβος, ταράσσω, θάλασσα, ὀ-τρηρός,<BR>ὀ-τραλέος: Lat. tristis = trasta; tremo; terreo fr.<BR>terseo for treseo = Caus. त्रासयामि: Goth. thlahs-<BR>yan: Russ. tryasu, ‘to shake;’ tryasu-sy, ‘I<BR>tremble:’ Lett. trīsseht, ‘to tremble:’ Hib. tor,<BR>‘fear, dread.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस|त्रसं|त्रसः
त्रस, अस्, आ, अम्, movable, moving, locomotive;<BR>(अम्), n. the collective body of moving or living<BR>beings; animals; animals and men, (opposed to<BR>स्थावर, cf. जगत्; under त्रस are sometimes<BR>reckoned gods, men, and the inhabitants of the<BR>lower regions); (अस्), m. the heart (‘the quivering<BR>one’); (अम्), n. a forest, a wood.<BR>—त्रस-दस्यु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘before whom evil beings tremble,’ N. of a<BR>prince, (celebrated for his liberality and favoured by the<BR>gods; he bears the patronymic Paurukutsya or Pauru-<BR>kutsi or Paurukutsa, and is supposed to be the author<BR>of certain Ṛg-veda hymns; in the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa<BR>त्रसद्-दस्यु, which is probably the original form,<BR>is identified with Māṃ-dhātṛ and regarded as the<BR>father of Puru-kutsa; the meaning of the name may<BR>be ‘frightening evil beings;’ cf. जमद्-अग्नि, तरद्-<BR>द्वेषस्, भरद्-वाज, &c.)<BR>—त्रस-रेणु, उस्, m. f.<BR>an atom, the mote or atom of dust which is seen<BR>moving in a sun-beam, especially considered as an<BR>ideal weight either of the lowest denomination or<BR>equal to three or (according to some) thirty invisible<BR>atoms; (उस्), f., N. of one of the wives of the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसन|त्रसनं
त्रसन, अम्, n. in हस्ति-त्रसनानि, the moving<BR>ornaments of an elephant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसर|त्रसरः
त्रसर, अस्, m. a shuttle; weaving; = तसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसुर|त्रसुरः
त्रसुर, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, timid, fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्त|त्रस्तः
त्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, frighted, alarmed; timid,<BR>trembling, fearful; quick.<BR>—त्रस्त-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>terrified, fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्नु|त्रस्नुः
त्रस्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, fearful, timid, timorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्यत्
त्रस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, fearing, apprehending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रास|त्रासः
त्रास, अस्, आ, अम्, moving, movable, locomotive;<BR>frightening; (अस्), m. fear, terror, anxiety; terrifying,<BR>frightening, causing alarm, (often in comp., e. g.<BR>त्रासार्थम्, ind. in order to frighten); a flaw or<BR>defect in a jewel.<BR>—त्रास-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing<BR>fear, fearful, alarming.<BR>—त्रास-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>causing alarm, fear-exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासदस्यव
त्रासदस्यव, अस्, m. a patronymic from Tra-<BR>sad-dasyu; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासन
त्रासन, अस्, ई, अम्, terrifying, alarming, frighten-<BR>ing (with gen.), making anxious; (अस्), m. epithet of<BR>Śiva; (अम्), n. the act of frightening or alarming; a<BR>means of frightening, cause of alarm, fright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासनीय
त्रासनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dreaded, frightened, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासित
त्रासित, अस्, आ, अम्, frightened, scared, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासिन्
त्रासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fearful, timid, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रा
त्रा 1. त्रा (by native authorities written<BR>त्रै, q. v.), cl. 1. A. त्रायते, &c., to pro-<BR>tect, &c. See rt. त्रै, p. 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रा
2. त्रा, आस्, m., Ved. a protector, a defender; [cf.<BR>1. त्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राण|त्राणं
त्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, preserved, saved, guarded, pro-<BR>tected; (अम्), n. protecting, preserving; protection,<BR>a preservative, defence; shelter, help, (often in<BR>comp., e. g. आर्त-त्राणाय, for the protection of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">Page0388-b+ 77</a>]<BR>distressed; आत्म-त्राण, self-defence); protection for<BR>the body, armour; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = त्राय-<BR>माणा; [cf. Hib. troiath, ‘a helmet.’]<BR>—त्राण-<BR>कर्तृ, ता, or त्राण-कारिन्, ई, m. a preserver, pro-<BR>tector, saviour, deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रात|त्रातं
त्रात, अस्, आ, अम्, preserved, rescued, guarded,<BR>protected; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (अम्), n. pre-<BR>serving, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रातव्य
त्रातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be guarded or protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रातृ
त्रातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a protector, saviour, guardian,<BR>defender; protecting, defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रात्र
त्रात्र, अम्, n. defence, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रात्वा
त्रात्वा, ind. having preserved or rescued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रामन्
त्रामन्, अ, n., Ved. protection; [cf. सु-त्रामन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायत्
त्रायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, preserving, defending, pro-<BR>tecting; (अन्ती), f. a protectress; a medicinal plant;<BR>[cf. त्रायमाणा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायन्तिका
त्रायन्तिका, f. a medicinal plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायमाण|त्रायमाणं
त्रायमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, preserving, defending, a<BR>preserver; (आ), f., N. of a medicinal plant; also<BR>त्रायमाणिका, f.; [cf. कृत-त्रा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राहि
त्राहि (2nd sing. impv. of rt. त्रै), save! deliver!<BR>to the rescue!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रापुष|त्रापुषं
त्रापुष त्रापुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रपु), made<BR>of tin [cf. जातुष]; silver (produced from tin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रापुस
त्रापुस त्रापुस, अस्, ई, अम्, sprung or coming<BR>from the plant Trapusī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायोदश
त्रायोदश त्रायोदश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रयो-<BR>दशी), relating &c. to the thirteenth day of a half-<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रि|त्रिः
त्रि त्रि, त्रयस् m. pl., तिस्रस् f. pl., त्रीणि<BR>n. pl. (said to be fr. rt. तॄ; in Ved. त्री occurs for<BR>त्रीणि and त्रीणाम् for त्रयाणाम्), three; [cf. Gr.<BR>τρεῖς, τρί-α, τρί-το-ς, τρί-ς, τρισσό-ς: Zend thri,<BR>thri-tya, thris: Lat. tres, tri-a, ter-tiu-s, ter:<BR>Goth. threis, thriya, thri-dya: Angl. Sax. threo,<BR>thry, thri: Slav. triye, tre-tii, ‘third:’ Lith. trýs,<BR>‘three;’ tré-cza-s, ‘third:’ to tisras belong Old<BR>Hib. teora, Cambro-Brit. f. tair, Armor. teir.]<BR>—त्रि-ककुद्, त्, त्, त्, having three peaks or points<BR>or horns &c.; (त्), m., N. of a mountain in the<BR>Himālaya [cf. त्रि-कूट and सु-वेल]; an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; N. of a son of Śuci and father<BR>of Dharma-sārathi; a kind of ritual observance; the<BR>highest, chief.<BR>—त्रि-ककुद, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>three peaks or humps &c.<BR>—त्रि-ककुभ्, प्, प्, प्,<BR>Ved. having three peaks or points; an epithet of<BR>Indra's thunderbolt or of Indra himself; (प्), m., N.<BR>of a mountain; a kind of ritual observance; [cf. त्रि-<BR>ककुद्.]<BR>—त्रि-कट, अस्, m., N. of a plant (Ruellia<BR>Longifolia), = गो-क्षुरक; [cf. त्रि-कण्ट.]<BR>—त्रि-<BR>कटु, उ, n. or त्रि-कटुक, अम्, n. the aggregate of<BR>three spices, viz. black and long pepper and dry<BR>ginger; [cf. कटु-त्रय.]<BR>—त्रि-कण्ट, अम्, n. the<BR>three thorny plants, a collective N. of three kinds of<BR>Solanum, viz. बृहती, अग्नि-दमनी, and दुः-<BR>स्पर्शा; (अस्, आ, अम्), having three thorns; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a plant, = गो-क्षुरक or पत्त्र-गुप्त;<BR>a kind of fish.<BR>—त्रि-कण्टक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>plant, = गो-क्षुरक; a kind of poisonous insect;<BR>a kind of fish (Silurus); a kind of weapon.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>कद्रुक, आस्, m. pl., Ved. probably a N. of three<BR>peculiar Soma-vessels [cf. कद्रु], or perhaps a N.<BR>of an oblation consisting of three offerings of the<BR>Soma (which is of a dark-brown colour); the first<BR>three days of the Abhi-plava festival which lasts six<BR>days, (respectively called Jyotis, Go, and Āyus.)<BR>—त्रिकद्रुकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, containing the word<BR>त्रि-कद्रुक.<BR>—त्रि-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>three ears.<BR>—त्रि-कर्मन्, (at the beginning of a<BR>comp.) the three chief duties of a Brāhman, viz.<BR>sacrifice, study of the Vedas, and liberality (e. g. त्रि-<BR>कर्म-कृत्, performing these three duties); (आ, आ,<BR>अ), engaging in these three actions.<BR>—त्रि-कर्ष,<BR>अम्, n. = त्रि-कार्षिक.<BR>—त्रि-कला, f., N. of a female<BR>deity produced by the union of three gods for<BR>the destruction of Andhaka.<BR>—त्रि-काण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-c" target="_blank">Page0388-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, consisting of three parts or divisions; forty-<BR>eight cubits long; (अस् or अम्), m. or n. (?), a work<BR>consisting of three parts, especially the dictionary of<BR>Amara-siṃha, also called Amara-koṣa.<BR>—त्रिकाण्ड-<BR>चिन्ता-मणि, इस्, m. or त्रिकाण्ड-विवेक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of commentaries on this work.<BR>—त्रिकाण्ड-मन्-<BR>दन, N. of a work.<BR>—त्रिकाण्ड-शेष, अस्, m. a<BR>vocabulary in three chapters supplementary to the<BR>Amara-koṣa by Puruṣottama.<BR>—त्रि-काय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having three bodies; (अस्), m., N. of Buddha or of<BR>a Buddha.<BR>—त्रि-कार्षिक, अम्, n. the three contracting<BR>(कार्षिक fr. rt. कृष्) substances, dry ginger, Ati-<BR>viṣā, and Mustā; [cf. त्रि-कर्ष, दन्त-कर्षण.]<BR>—त्रि-काल, अम्, n. the three times, viz. past,<BR>present, and future time; morning, noon, and<BR>evening; the present, past, and future tenses of a<BR>verb; (अम्), ind. three times, thrice; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>connected with or relating to the three times (past,<BR>present, and future).<BR>—त्रिकाल-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>knowing the three times, omniscient; (अस्), m. a<BR>divine sage; a deity; a N. of Buddha, the founder of<BR>the Buddhist religion.<BR>—त्रिकाल-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, see-<BR>ing (or knowing) the past, present, and future, omni-<BR>scient; (ई), m. a Ṛṣi or divine sage; N. of Buddha.<BR>—त्रिकाल-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing the three times; (त्),<BR>m. a Buddha; (with Jainas) an Arhat.<BR>—त्रि-कुण्डी-<BR>श्वर (˚ड-ईश्˚?), अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>कूट, अस्, आ, अम्, having three peaks or humps or<BR>elevations &c.; (अस्), m., N. of several mountains,<BR>= त्रि-ककुद् and सु-वेल; a mountain in Ceylon<BR>on the top of which Laṅkā, the capital of Rāvaṇa,<BR>was situated; (अम्), n. sea-salt prepared by evapo-<BR>ration.<BR>—त्रिकूट-लवण, अम्, n. a peculiar kind<BR>of salt (= द्रोणी-लवण).<BR>—त्रिकूट-वत्, आन्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—त्रि-कूर्चक, अम्, n. a sort of<BR>knife with three edges.<BR>—त्रिकैक (˚क-एक), Ved.,<BR>N. of an Ekāha; [cf. एक-त्रिक.]<BR>—त्रि-कोण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (borrowed fr. the Gr. τρίγωνον), triangular,<BR>forming a triangle; (अस्, आ), m. f. Trapa Bispinosa;<BR>(अम्), n. (in astron.) N. of the fifth and ninth<BR>mansion [cf. त्रि-कोन-भवन and त्रि-त्रिकोण];<BR>the vulva; [cf. त्रि-भुज्.]<BR>—त्रिकोण-कुण्ड, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a mystical vessel in the form of a diagram.<BR>—त्रिकोण-फल, अम्, n. Trapa Bispinosa.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>कोण-भवन, अम्, n. (in astron.) N. of the fifth<BR>and ninth mansion.<BR>—त्रि-क्रम, अस्, m. (according<BR>to the Prātiśākhyas) a Krama word composed of three<BR>words or members, the middle one of which is a single<BR>vowel.<BR>—त्रि-क्षार, अम्, n. the three burning or<BR>acrid substances, viz. natron, saltpetre, and borax.<BR>—त्रि-क्षुर, N. of a plant, = कोकिलाक्ष.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>ख, अम्, n. a cucumber (‘having three cavities’).<BR>—त्रि-खट्व, अम्, ई, n. f. three beds collectively.<BR>—त्रि-खण्ड, the earth as divided into three por-<BR>tions.<BR>—त्रि-खर्व, आस्, m. pl., Ved., N. of a particu-<BR>lar school of theologians.<BR>—त्रि-गङ्ग, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha; [cf. सप्त-गङ्ग.]<BR>—त्रि-गण, अस्,<BR>m. the aggregate of the three objects of existence,<BR>viz. virtue (धर्म), pleasure or the ‘dulce’ (काम),<BR>and wealth or the ‘utile’ (अर्थ); [cf. त्रि-वर्ग.]<BR>—त्रि-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, tripled; gone or done in three<BR>ways; (अम्), n. the expression of different senses by the<BR>same word.<BR>—त्रि-गन्धक, अम्, n. = त्रि-जातक,<BR>—त्रि-गम्भीर, see under गभीर.<BR>—त्रि-गर्त,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people inhabiting the modern<BR>Lahore; (अस्), m. a prince of the Tri-gartas; the<BR>country of the Tri-gartas; a particular method of<BR>calculation; (आ), f. a lascivious woman, a wanton;<BR>a woman in general; a kind of cricket (= घुर्-<BR>गुरी, घुर्गुरिका); a pearl.<BR>—त्रिगर्तक, आस्,<BR>m. pl. = त्रि-गर्त.<BR>—त्रिगर्त-राज, अस्, and त्रि-<BR>गर्त-राजन्, आ, m. king of Tri-garta.<BR>—त्रि-गर्-<BR>तिक, अस्, m. the country of the Tri-gartas.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>गुण, आस्, m. pl. the three qualities or constituents<BR>of nature and every existing thing, i. e. सत्-त्व,<BR>रजस्, and तमस्; (अस्, आ, अम्), consisting of three<BR>threads or strings; threefold, three times repeated,<BR>thrice, triple, treble (e. g. सप्त त्रिगुणानि दिनानि,<BR>three times seven days); containing the three Guṇas<BR>or properties; (अम्), ind. in three ways, three times,<BR>thrice.<BR>—त्रिगुणा-कर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, whose ears<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0389-a" target="_blank">Page0389-a+ 81</a>]<BR>have two slits dividing them into three parts (as a<BR>mark of distinction).<BR>—त्रिगुणा-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>thrice ploughed (a field &c.).<BR>—त्रि-ग्रामी, f. an<BR>assemblage of three villages, N. of a place.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, extending to the length of three<BR>(padyās).<BR>—त्रि-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. ‘triocular,’ ‘three-<BR>eyed,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa (more properly of Śiva).<BR>—त्रि-चतुः-कर्ण, the third and fourth hypo-<BR>tenuses.<BR>—त्रि-चतुर, आस्, आस्, आणि, pl. three or<BR>four.<BR>—त्रि-चतुर्दश, औ, &c., du. the thir-<BR>teenth and fourteenth.<BR>—त्रिचत्वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. the next), the forty-third.<BR>—त्रि-चत्वारिंशत्,<BR>त्, f. forty-three.<BR>—त्रि-चरित्र (?), अम्, n. three<BR>kinds of characters, (perhaps a wrong reading for<BR>स्त्री-चरित्र; cf. त्रि-गूढ.)<BR>—त्रि-चित्, त्, त्, त्, con-<BR>sisting of three layers or seats of sacrificial grass.<BR>—त्रि-चीवर, अम्, n. the three vestments of the<BR>Buddhist ascetic.<BR>—त्रिजगज्-जननी, f. the mother of<BR>the three worlds, an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR>—त्रि-जगत्,<BR>त्, n. or त्रि-जगती, f. the triple world, i. e. heaven,<BR>the intermediate region, and earth, or heaven, earth,<BR>and the lower world.<BR>—त्रिजगन्-मोहिनी, f. confound-<BR>ing the minds of the (inhabitants of the) three worlds,<BR>a form of Durgā (?).<BR>—त्रि-जट, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing<BR>three braids of hair; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva;<BR>N. of a Brāhman; (आ), f., N. of a Rākṣasī who<BR>was friendly to Sītā; N. of a tree, = विल्व, Ægle<BR>Marmelos.<BR>—त्रिजटा-स्वप्न-दर्शन, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>dream of Tri-jaṭā,’ N. of a chapter in the fifth book<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—त्रि-जात or त्रि-जातक, अम्, n.<BR>three spices collectively, viz. mace, cardamoms, and<BR>Laurus Cassia (cinnamon).<BR>—त्रि-जीवा, f. the sine<BR>of three signs or ninety degrees, a radius.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>ज्या, f. = the preceding.<BR>—त्रि-णत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>त्रि-नत), bent in three places, epithet of a bow;<BR>(आ), f. a bow; [cf. तृणता.]<BR>—त्रि-णयन, अस्, m.<BR>[cf. त्रि-नयन], ‘three-eyed,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्रि-णवन् or त्रि-णव (fr. त्रि+नवन्), consisting<BR>of three times nine or twenty-seven parts, connected<BR>with the Tri-ṇava Stoma; three times nine, i. e. twenty-<BR>seven; त्रिणव-साहस्र, twenty-seven thousand; [cf.<BR>त्रि-सप्तन्.]<BR>—त्रि-णाचिकेत, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has thrice kindled the fire called Nāciketa; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Nārāyaṇa (perhaps as worshipped<BR>with this fire); (according to Kullūka Bhaṭṭa on<BR>Manu III. 185, त्रि-णाचिकेत means either ‘a part<BR>of the Adhvaryu or Yajur-veda,’ or ‘a vow connected<BR>with it,’ or ‘one who performs this vow.’)<BR>—त्रि-<BR>णामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. having three names, epithet<BR>of a deity, perhaps of Agni.<BR>—त्रि-णीता, f. a wife,<BR>(‘thrice married,’ according to the belief that a girl<BR>belongs to Soma, Gandharva and Agni, before she<BR>obtains a human husband.)<BR>—त्रि-तक्ष, अम्, ई, n. f.<BR>(fr. त्रि-तक्षन्), an association of three carpenters.<BR>—त्रि-तस्, ind. on three sides, from every side.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>ता, f. or त्रि-त्व, अम्, n. a triad, a trinity, an assemblage<BR>of three.<BR>—त्रि-त्रिकोण, अम्, n. (in astronomy) N. of<BR>the ninth mansion; [cf. त्रि-कोण and त्रिकोण-भ-<BR>वन.]<BR>—त्रि-दण्ड, अम्, n. the three staves of a<BR>mendicant Brāhman who has resigned the world,<BR>(these staves are tied together so as to form one);<BR>triple subjection of words, thoughts, and acts; the<BR>state of a religious ascetic; (ई), f., N. of a literary<BR>work.<BR>—त्रि-दण्डक, अम्, n. the three staves of a<BR>mendicant Brāhman described above.<BR>—त्रिदण्ड-<BR>धारण, अम्, n. carrying three staves tied together.<BR>—त्रि-दण्डिन्, ई, m. a wandering mendicant or<BR>devotee who has resigned worldly pursuits and carries<BR>three long bamboo staves tied together in his right<BR>hand; the religious man who has obtained a com-<BR>mand over his words, thoughts, and actions, or mind,<BR>body, and speech; [cf. एक-दण्डिन्.]<BR>—त्रि-दत्, अन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having three teeth.<BR>—त्रि-दला, f. a creeping<BR>plant, Cissus Pedata.<BR>—त्रि-दलिका or (according to<BR>some) त्रि-दालिका, f., N. of a plant, = चर्म-कषा.<BR>—त्रि-दश, आस्, m. pl. (fr. त्रि-दशन्), three times<BR>ten, i. e. thirty; the three times ten or thirty<BR>deities, i. e. in round numbers a N. for the thirty-<BR>three deities, not including Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and<BR>Śiva, viz. the twelve Ādityas, eight Vasus, eleven<BR>Rudras, and two Aśvins; (अस्, आ, अम्), divine; (अस्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0389-b" target="_blank">Page0389-b+ 81</a>]<BR>m. a god, a deity, an immortal; (अम्), n. the<BR>residence of the thirty-three deities, i. e. heaven.<BR>—त्रिदश-गुरु, उस्, m. ‘the preceptor of the gods,’<BR>i. e. Bṛhas-pati, regent of the planet Jupiter.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>दश-गोप or त्रिदश-गोपक, अस्, m. a fire-fly, =<BR>इन्द्र-गोप, q. v.<BR>—त्रिदश-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>or condition of a god, divinity, divine nature.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>दश-दीर्घिका, f. ‘the heavenly lake,’ epithet of<BR>the Gaṅgā.<BR>—त्रिदश-नदी, f. the heavenly river,<BR>the Gaṅgā.<BR>—त्रिदश-पति, इस्, m. the chief of<BR>the gods, Indra.<BR>—त्रिदशपति-शस्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>Indra's weapon, the thunderbolt.<BR>—त्रिदश-प्रति-<BR>पक्ष, अस्, m. an adversary of the gods.<BR>—त्रिदश-<BR>मञ्जरी, f. = तुलसी, basil.<BR>—त्रिदश-वधू, ऊस्,<BR>f. or त्रिदश-वनिता, f. a nymph of Indra's heaven,<BR>an Apsaras, a goddess.<BR>—त्रिदश-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m.<BR>‘the best of the thirty-three deities,’ a N. of Agni; of<BR>Brahmā.<BR>—त्रिदश-सर्षप, अस्, m. = देव-सर्-<BR>षप.<BR>—त्रिदशाङ्कुश (˚श-अङ्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>thunderbolt (‘divine goad’).<BR>—त्रिदशाचार्य (˚श-<BR>आच्˚), अस्, m. = त्रिदश-गुरु above.<BR>—त्रिदशाधि-<BR>पति (˚श-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘lord of the thirty-three<BR>deities,’ a N. of Śiva.<BR>—त्रिदशायन (˚श-अय्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘the refuge of the deities,’ i. e. to whom the<BR>deities resort, an epithet of Nārāyaṇa; [cf. ब्रह्मा-<BR>यण and लोकायन.]<BR>—त्रिदशायुध (˚श-आय्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘the divine bow,’ the rainbow; a thunder-<BR>bolt.<BR>—त्रिदशारि (˚श-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of the<BR>gods,’ an Asura, a demon, a Titan.<BR>—त्रिदशारि-<BR>राजन्, आ, m. ‘king of the demons,’ a N. of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—त्रिदशालय (˚श-आल्˚), अस्, m. the residence of<BR>the gods, Svarga, Indra's heaven or paradise, the<BR>mountain Su-meru; an inhabitant of the divine world,<BR>a god.<BR>—त्रिदशावास (˚श-आव्˚), अस्, m. the resi-<BR>dence of the gods, heaven.<BR>—त्रिदशाहार (˚श-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, m. the food of the gods, i. e. Amṛta or<BR>ambrosia.<BR>—त्रिदशी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become<BR>divine or immortal.<BR>—त्रिदशेन्द्र (˚श-इन्˚) or<BR>त्रिदशेश (˚श-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘the chief of the thirty-<BR>three deities,’ epithet of Indra; of Śiva; of Brahmā,<BR>&c.<BR>—त्रिदशेश-द्विष्, ट्, m. epithet of Rāvaṇa<BR>or any demon.<BR>—त्रिदशेश्वर (˚श-ईश्˚) = त्रि-<BR>दशेन्द्र; (ई), f., N. of Durgā.<BR>—त्रिदशेश्वर-<BR>द्विष् = त्रिदशेश-द्विष्.<BR>—त्रि-दालिका, f. for त्रि-<BR>दलिका, q. v.<BR>—त्रि-दिन, अम्, n. three days col-<BR>lectively.<BR>—त्रिदिन-स्पृश्, क्, m. conjunction or con-<BR>currence of three lunations with one solar day.<BR>—त्रि-दिव, अम्, n. the space within the third sky,<BR>i. e. the innermost or most sacred part of the sky,<BR>heaven; the sky, atmosphere; paradise; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a river; cardamoms.<BR>—त्रिदिवाधीश (˚व-अध्˚)<BR>or त्रिदिवेश (˚व-ईश्˚) or त्रिदिवेश्वर (˚व-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘the lord of Tri-diva or heaven,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra; a god, a deity.<BR>—त्रिदिवोद्भवा (˚व-उद्˚),<BR>f. small cardamoms.<BR>—त्रिदिवौकस् (˚व-ओक्˚), आस्,<BR>m. an inhabitant of Tri-diva, a celestial, a god.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>दृश्, क्, m. ‘triocular,’ ‘three-eyed,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—त्रि-दोष, अम्, n. disorder of the three<BR>humors of the body, vitiation of the bile, blood,<BR>and phlegm.<BR>—त्रिदोष-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, correcting<BR>the vitiated state of the three humors.<BR>—त्रिदोष-<BR>ज, अस्, m. disease &c. proceeding from disorder of<BR>the three humors of the body.<BR>—त्रि-धन्वन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a prince or father of Trayyāruṇa.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>धा, ind. adv. in three ways, in three parts, in three<BR>places, triply, trebly; त्रिधा-कृ, to do in three<BR>ways, to make threefold.<BR>—त्रि-धातु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>consisting of three elements or ingredients, triple,<BR>threefold, thrice repeated (used like triplex in Lat.<BR>to denote excessive), tripartite; (Sāy.) causing the<BR>well-being of the three humors; (उस्), m. a N. of<BR>Gaṇeśa; (उ), n. the aggregate of three minerals or<BR>of the three humors; the triple world.<BR>—त्रिधातु-<BR>शृङ्ग, अस्, m., Ved. having a tripartite horn, having<BR>horns or flames of three colours, red, white, and<BR>black (with smoke), an epithet of Agni.<BR>—त्रिधा-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of being threefold or in three<BR>parts, tripartition.<BR>—त्रि-धामन्, अ, n. probably =<BR>त्रि-दिव; (आ, आ, अ), belonging or relating to the<BR>three worlds or regions; having three residences,<BR>&c.; (आ), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of Vyāsa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0389-c" target="_blank">Page0389-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(= Viṣṇu) in the tenth Dvāpara; an epithet of<BR>Śiva; Agni or fire; death.<BR>—त्रिधा-मूर्ति, इस्, f. a<BR>girl three years of age representing the deity Durgā<BR>at her festivals.<BR>—त्रि-धारक, अस्, m. ‘having three<BR>edges,’ the plants Scirpus Kysoor and Euphorbia<BR>Antiquorum.<BR>—त्रि-धार-स्नुही, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= धारा-स्नुही, त्र्य्-अश्र.<BR>—त्रि-नगरी, f. the three<BR>cities.<BR>—त्रि-नयन, अस्, आ, अम्, triocular, three-<BR>eyed; (अस्), m. an epithet of Rudra-Śiva; (आ), f.<BR>epithet of Durgā; [cf. त्रि-णयन.]<BR>—त्रि-नवत,<BR>अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-नवति), the ninety-third.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>नवति, इस्, f. ninety-three.<BR>—त्रिनवति-तम, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, the ninety-third.<BR>—त्रि-नाक, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>= त्रि-दिव.<BR>—त्रि-नाभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having three<BR>navels or centres or central points; whose navel sup-<BR>ports the three worlds.<BR>—त्रि-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ, =<BR>त्रि-नाभ.<BR>—त्रि-निधन, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman<BR>(generally in connection with the names आग्नेयम्,<BR>आयस्यम्, and त्वाष्ट्री-साम).<BR>—त्रि-निष्क, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = त्रि-नैष्किक, worth three Niṣkas.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>नेत्र, अस्, ई, अम्, triocular; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Rudra-Śiva; N. of a prince; (ई), f. = वाराही-<BR>कन्द, the root of Yam (Dioscorea).<BR>—त्रिनेत्र-<BR>चूडा-मणि, इस्, m. ‘the crest of the three-eyed,’<BR>i. e. the moon (worn by Śiva as his crest).<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पक्ष, अम्, n. a period of three fortnights or six<BR>weeks.<BR>—त्रि-पच्छस्, ind. adv. (त्रि+पद्+शस्),<BR>by three Pādas.<BR>—त्रिपञ्चाश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-<BR>पञ्चाशत्), the fifty-third; containing or consisting<BR>of fifty-three.<BR>—त्रि-पञ्चाशत्, त्, f. fifty-three; [cf.<BR>त्रयः-पञ्चाशत् under त्रयस्.]<BR>—त्रिपञ्चाशत्-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the fifty-third.<BR>—त्रि-पटु, उ, n.<BR>the three saline substances, stone-salt (= सैन्धव),<BR>Viḍ-lavaṇa, and black salt (= काच).<BR>—त्रि-पताक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, (with हस्त) the hand with three fingers<BR>stretched out or erect; (with ललाट) the forehead<BR>marked naturally with three horizontal lines or<BR>wrinkles.<BR>—त्रि-पती, f., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—त्रि-पत्त्र, अस्, m. three-leaved, trifoliate, the<BR>plant Ægle Marmelos (= विल्व); (अम्), n. = चण्-<BR>डाल-कन्द, a kind of bulbous plant.<BR>—त्रि-पत्-<BR>त्रक, अस्, m. the Kiṃśuka tree, Butea Frondosa.<BR>—त्रि-पथ, अम्, n. the three paths or ways, viz.<BR>the sky, atmosphere, and earth, or the sky, earth,<BR>and lower world; a place where three roads meet;<BR>(आ), f. epithet of Mathurā.<BR>—त्रिपथ-गा or त्रि-<BR>पथ-गामिनी, f. ‘flowing through heaven, earth,<BR>and the lower regions,’ an epithet of the Gaṅgā.<BR>—त्रि-पद् or त्रि-पाद्, -पात्, -पात् or -पदी, -पत्,<BR>Ved. ‘three-footed,’ ‘tripod,’ epithet of Viṣṇu (as<BR>pacing the universe in three steps; cf. त्रि-विक्रम);<BR>epithet of Fever personified as a demon or evil<BR>spirit and represented with three feet and three<BR>hands, (probably symbolizing the cold, hot, and<BR>sweating stages of fever); having three steps; con-<BR>taining three Pādas; trinomial; (त्), m., N. of a<BR>Daitya; (-पदी), f. the girth of an elephant; the<BR>plant Cissus Pedata (= गोधा-पधी); a kind of<BR>metre in Prākṛt; (according to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 9, the<BR>f. must be त्रि-पदा when agreeing with ऋच्, e. g.<BR>त्रीपदा ऋक्, a verse containing three Pādas, cf. the<BR>next.)<BR>—त्रि-पद, अस्, आ, अम्, three-footed; having<BR>three divisions (as a stanza); containing a measure<BR>of three feet; containing three words; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a plant, = हंस-पदी; (अम्), n. a tripod; three<BR>words.<BR>—त्रि-पदिका, f. a stand with three feet.<BR>—त्रि-पन्न, अस्, m., N. of one of the ten horses<BR>of the moon.<BR>—त्रि-परिक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who walks thrice round the sacred fire or who cir-<BR>cumambulates the three sacred fires.<BR>—त्रि-पर्ण,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, three-leaved, trefoil; (अस्), m. Butea<BR>Frondosa; (आ), f. wild hemp; (ई), f., N. of several<BR>plants, Desmodium Gangeticum, = शाल-पर्णी, wild<BR>cotton, wild hemp, = पृश्नि-पर्णी-भेद and वन-<BR>कार्पासी, Sanseviera Ceylanica; a kind of bulbous<BR>plant, = त्रि-पर्णिका.<BR>—त्रि-पर्णिका, f., N. of<BR>several plants, a kind of bulbous plant (= बृहत्-<BR>पत्त्रा, &c.); Carpopogon Pruriens; Alhagi Mau-<BR>rorum.<BR>—त्रि-पर्याय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>three folds or plaits.<BR>—त्रि-पशु, उस्, उस्, उ, having<BR>three victims.<BR>—त्रि-पस्त्य, अस्, m., Ved. ‘having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0390-a" target="_blank">Page0390-a+ 81</a>]<BR>three dwellings,’ an epithet of Agni.<BR>—त्रि-पाजस्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having three flanks or sides; (Sāy.)<BR>having three breasts (or seasons).<BR>—त्रि-पाट, अस्,<BR>m. intersection of a prolonged side and perpendicular<BR>(in a quadrangular figure); the figure formed by such<BR>intersection.<BR>—त्रिपाठिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. त्रि-पाठ),<BR>familiar with the three Pāṭhas, (probably with the<BR>संहिता, पद, and क्रम-पाठ, q. v.)<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पाण, अस्, ई, अम् (probably a Prākṛt form for त्रि-<BR>पर्ण or त्रैपर्ण), made of the plant Tri-parṇī.<BR>—त्रि-पाद्, see त्रि-पद्.<BR>—त्रि-पाद, अस्, m. a<BR>constellation or asterism of which three-fourths are<BR>included under one sign of the zodiac; a stand with<BR>three feet?; (ई), f. a kind of Mimosa.<BR>—त्रि-पादक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, three-footed; (इका), f., N. of a plant,<BR>= हंस-पदी, a kind of Mimosa.<BR>—त्रि-पिटक,<BR>अम्, n. the three baskets or collections of writings,<BR>a collective N. for the three classes of Buddhist<BR>writings, viz. Sūtra-piṭaka, Vinaya-piṭaka, and Abhi-<BR>dharma-piṭaka.<BR>—त्रि-पिण्डी, f. the three sacrificial<BR>cakes (mentioned in Manu III. 215).<BR>—त्रि-पिब,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, drinking with three members of the body<BR>(as with the two pendent ears and tongue); (अस्), m.<BR>along-eared goat.<BR>—त्रि-पिष्टप, अम्, n. = त्रि-दिव,<BR>the residence of the thirty-three gods, Indra's heaven;<BR>paradise; the sky, ether; [cf. त्रि-विष्टप.]<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पिष्टप-सद्, त्, m. an inhabitant of heaven, a<BR>deity.<BR>—त्रि-पुट, अस्, ई, अम्, triangular; (अस्), m.<BR>pulse, pease of three kinds; a kind of vetch, Cicer<BR>Arietinum; the palm of the hand; a measure, =<BR>हस्त-भेद, a cubit; a bank or shore; (आ), f.<BR>Convolvulus Turpethum; Arabian jasmine; small<BR>cardamoms; a form of Durgā; (ई), f. Convolvulus<BR>Turpethum; small cardamoms; [cf. कराल-त्रि-<BR>पुटा.]<BR>—त्रिपुटक, अस्, आ, अम्, triangular; (अस्),<BR>m. a triangle; a species of pulse.<BR>—त्रिपुटा-पूजा-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a kind of mystical diagram<BR>described in the Tantra-sāra by Kṛṣṇānanda.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पुटा-मन्त्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of a chapter of the Tan-<BR>tra-sāra.<BR>—त्रिपुटा-स्तोत्र, अम्, n., N. of a chapter<BR>of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—त्रिपुटिन्, ई, m. or त्रिपुटी-<BR>फल, अस्, m. the castor-oil plant, Ricinus Com-<BR>munis.<BR>—त्रि-पुण्ड्र or त्रि-पुण्ढ्र or त्रि-<BR>पुण्ड्रक, अम्, n. a mark consisting of three lines<BR>on the forehead, the back, heart, and shoulders, or<BR>three curved horizontal marks made across the fore-<BR>head with cow-dung, ashes, &c., which are worn<BR>especially by the followers of Śiva or Śakti, and are<BR>indispensable in proceeding to worship the former;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having three horizontal marks.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पुर्, f. (in pl. त्रि-पुरस्) = त्रि-पुर.<BR>—त्रि-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. three strong cities collectively, a triple forti-<BR>fication; (in epic poetry) three strong cities of gold,<BR>silver, and iron, in the sky, air, and earth, built by<BR>Maya for a celebrated Asura or demon, and burnt by<BR>Śiva; (अस्), m., N. of the above Asura and king of<BR>Tri-pura; a form of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of a town; a<BR>form of Durgā (= त्रि-पुटा ?); (ई), f., N. of a town,<BR>= चेदि-नगरी; N. of a country to the south-east<BR>of Madhya-deśa, the modern Tipparah; (आ or ई?),<BR>N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—त्रिपुर-कुमार, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya mentioned in the<BR>Śaṅkara-vijaya by Anantānanda-giri.<BR>—त्रिपुर-<BR>घ्न, अस्, or त्रिपुर-जित्, त्, or त्रिपुर-दहन, or<BR>त्रिपुर-दाह, अस्, m., N. of Śiva as destroyer<BR>of Tri-pura.<BR>—त्रिपुर-दाह, अस्, m. ‘burning of<BR>Tri-pura,’ N. of the 3rd chapter of the Pātāla-<BR>khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—त्रिपुर-भैरवी,<BR>f. a form of Durgā.<BR>—त्रिपुर-मल्लिका, f. a medicinal<BR>plant, apparently a kind of jasmine; [cf. त्रि-पुटा.]<BR>—त्रिपुर-वध, अस्, m. ‘slaughter of Tri-pura,’<BR>N. of the 7th chapter of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—त्रिपुर-विजय, अस्, m. ‘conquest<BR>of Tri-pura,’ N. of the 70th chapter of the Liṅga-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—त्रिपुर-हर, अस्, m., N. of the 71st<BR>chapter of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—त्रिपुराधारण-<BR>यन्त्र (˚न-आध्˚), अम्, n., N. of a mystical dia-<BR>gram given in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—त्रिपुराधिपति<BR>(˚र-अध्˚), इस्, m., N. of Maya, builder of the city of<BR>Tri-pura.<BR>—त्रिपुरान्तक or त्रिपुरान्त-कर (˚र-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of Śiva as destroyer of Tri-pura.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0390-b" target="_blank">Page0390-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—त्रिपुरा-न्यास, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Tantra-sāra.<BR>—त्रिपुरा-भैरवी, f. a form of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—त्रिपुराभैरवी-पूजा-यन्त्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a mystical diagram given in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—त्रिपुरारि (˚र-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘the enemy of Tri-<BR>pura,’ a N. of Śiva.<BR>—त्रिपुरार्णव (˚र-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a literary work.<BR>—त्रिपुरार्दन (˚र-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. = त्रिपुरान्तक.<BR>—त्रिपुरी-प्रकरण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work, probably by Saṅkara, con-<BR>taining the elements of the Vedānta phil.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पुरुष, अस्, आ, अम्, having the length of three<BR>men; having three assistants; (अम्), ind. through<BR>three males, i. e. through three generations of men,<BR>or father, grandfather, and great-grandfather.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पुरुषागत (˚ष-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, inherited through<BR>three generations.<BR>—त्रिपुरेश (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of Tri-pura,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—त्रिपुरेशाद्रि (˚श-<BR>अद्˚), इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—त्रिपुरेश्वर<BR>(˚र-ईश्˚), N. of a town or district, or of a sacred<BR>place.<BR>—त्रिपुरोपाख्यान (˚रा-उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘the<BR>story of Tri-pura,’ N. of the 52-54th chapters of the<BR>Jñāna-khaṇḍa or second part of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—त्रि-पुषा, f. Convolvulus Turpethum, = कृष्ण-<BR>त्रि-वृत्; [cf. त्रि-पुटा.]<BR>—त्रि-पुष्कर, आस्, m. pl.<BR>‘the three lakes,’ N. of certain holy bathing-places;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), decorated with three lotus flowers.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>पृष्ठ, अस्, m. (with Jainas) N. of the first of the<BR>black Vāsu-devas; a N. of Viṣṇu, as ‘living above<BR>the three worlds,’ or as ‘existing independently of the<BR>three qualities of nature;’ epithet of the Soma, as hav-<BR>ing three elevations or surfaces, found in three places (?),<BR>having three hymns (?), having three vessels (?), hav-<BR>ing three waters (used in its preparation ?), having<BR>three oblations (?), having three filtering cloths (?),<BR>or press, filter, and vessel for holding the Soma (?).<BR>(The above are the conjectures of various scholars, but<BR>according to Sāy. the word means) ‘mixed with<BR>cream, thickened with milk,’ &c.; (अम्), n. the<BR>highest part of the three heavens, the highest heaven.<BR>—त्रि-पौरुष, अस्, ई, अम्, extending or be-<BR>longing to three persons or three generations of<BR>men; offered to three (as the funeral cake &c.),<BR>inherited from three (as an estate &c.); [cf. त्रै-<BR>पुरुष.]<BR>—त्रि-प्रस्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, epithet of a<BR>rutting elephant, i. e. ‘having three streams of fluid<BR>flowing from the forehead.’<BR>—त्रि-प्लक्ष, आस्, m.<BR>pl. ‘the three fig-trees,’ a place near the Yamunā in<BR>the neighbourhood of which the Dṛṣad-vatī dis-<BR>appears.<BR>—त्रि-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, having three fruits;<BR>(आ), f. the three myrobalans, the fruits of Terminalia<BR>Chebula, T. Bellerica, and Phyllanthus Emblica;<BR>the three fragrant fruits, nutmeg, areca-nut, and<BR>cloves; the three sweet fruits, grape, pomegranate,<BR>and date.<BR>—त्रिफलादि-वर्ग (˚ल-आद्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Śabda-candrikā or medical<BR>lexicon by Cakra-pāṇi-datta.<BR>—त्रि-बन्धन, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the son of Aruṇa and father of Tri-śaṅku.<BR>—त्रि-बन्धु, उस्, m. the friend of the three<BR>worlds or regions; (Sāy.) binding together or sup-<BR>porting the three worlds, (said of Indra.)<BR>—त्रि-<BR>बन्धुर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having three uneven<BR>poles or seats, (said of the chariot of the Aśvins.)<BR>—त्रि-बर्हिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved. having three seats of<BR>sacrificial grass.<BR>—त्रि-बली, f. three folds of skin or<BR>corrugations over the navel (of a woman; this<BR>peculiarity is regarded as a beauty); the anus.<BR>—त्रि-बलीक, अस्, m., N. of Rāma, ‘having three<BR>folds in the neck;’ (अम्), n. the anus.<BR>—त्रि-बाहु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, ‘three-armed,’ epithet of a kind of<BR>spirit or demon; (उस्), m. a technical term in<BR>fighting.<BR>—त्रि-बुलीक, अम्, n. the anus.<BR>—त्रि-भ,<BR>अम्, n. three signs of the zodiac, the quadrant of a<BR>circle, ninety degrees; (अस्, आ, अम्), containing three<BR>signs of the zodiac.<BR>—त्रि-भङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having three curves or bends (as have many images<BR>of Kṛṣṇa); (ई), f., N. of a metre consisting of<BR>4 × 32 syllabic instants.<BR>—त्रिभ-जीवा, f. and त्रि-<BR>भ-ज्या, f. = त्रि-जीवा and त्रि-ज्या.<BR>—त्रि-भण्डी,<BR>f. Convolvulus Turpethum.<BR>—त्रि-भद्र, अम्, n.<BR>copulation, cohabitation.<BR>—त्रिभ-मौर्विका, f. =<BR>त्रि-ज्या.<BR>—त्रि-भाग, अस्, m. the third part; the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0390-c" target="_blank">Page0390-c+ 81</a>]<BR>third part of a sign of the zodiac.<BR>—त्रि-भानु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of a descendant of Yayāti and father of<BR>Karan-dhama.<BR>—त्रि-भाष्य-रत्न, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a commentary on the Taittirīya-Prātiśākhya.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>भुक्ति = तीर-भुक्ति (?) .<BR>—त्रि-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>threefold.<BR>—त्रि-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, having three arms,<BR>triangular; (अस्), m. a triangle.<BR>—त्रि-भुवन, अम्,<BR>n. the three worlds, i. e. sky, atmosphere, and earth,<BR>or heaven, earth, and the lower region; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—त्रिभुवन-गुरु, उस्, m. ‘master<BR>of the three worlds,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्रिभुव-<BR>न-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the three worlds,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—त्रिभुवनेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the three worlds,’ epithet of Indra.<BR>—त्रिभु-<BR>वनेश्वर-लिङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga temple.<BR>—त्रिभोन-लग्न (˚भ-ऊन्˚), अम्, n. that part of<BR>the ecliptic which does not reach the eastern point<BR>by three signs or ninety degrees, i. e. the highest<BR>point of the ecliptic above the horizon.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>मण्डला, f., scil. लूता, a kind of poisonous spider.<BR>—त्रि-मद, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?) the three narcotic<BR>plants, Mustā, Citraka, Viḍaṅga; the threefold illusion.<BR>—त्रि-मधु, उ, n. the three sweet substances,<BR>sugar, honey, and ghee; (उस्), m. one who knows or<BR>recites the three verses of Ṛg-veda 1. 90, 6-8, which<BR>begin with मधु.<BR>—त्रि-मधुर, अम्, n. the<BR>three sweet substances, sugar, honey, and ghee.<BR>—त्रि-मल्ल, N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>मातृ, ता, m., Ved. ‘having three mothers;’ (Sāy.) the<BR>maker or creator of the three worlds.<BR>—त्रि-मार्ग,<BR>(at the beginning of a comp.) the three paths;<BR>(ई), f. three ways or paths; the meeting of three<BR>roads; [cf. त्रि-पथ.]<BR>—त्रिमार्ग-गा, f. flowing<BR>by three ways; [cf. त्रिपथ-गा.]<BR>—त्रि-मुकुट,<BR>अस्, m. a mountain with three peaks; N. of a<BR>mountain, = त्रि-कूट.<BR>—त्रि-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>three-faced, having three faces, having three mouths;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the third Arhat of the present Ava-<BR>sarpiṇī; (आ), f. an epithet of Māyā or the mother of<BR>Śākya-muni.<BR>—त्रि-मुनि, ind. produced by the<BR>three Munis or sages, (as the grammar of Pāṇini,<BR>Kātyāyana, and Patañjali.)<BR>—त्रि-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>having or assuming three forms or shapes, (as Brahmā,<BR>Viṣṇu, and Śiva); (इस्), m. a Buddha, a Jina; (इस्),<BR>f. (?) the Hindū triad, the united form of the above<BR>three gods.<BR>—त्रि-मूर्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, three-headed.<BR>—त्रि-मूर्धन्, आ, m. ‘three-headed,’ N. of a<BR>Rākṣasa.<BR>—त्रिय्-अम्बक, अस्, m. = त्र्य्-अम्बक,<BR>‘triocular,’ ‘three-eyed,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—त्रि-यव, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, containing or weighing three barleycorns; (अम्),<BR>n. a retti (= रक्तिक) or weight of three barley-<BR>corns, = कृष्णल.<BR>—त्रिय्-अवि = त्र्य्-अवि.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>यष्टि, इस्, m. a species of plant, = क्षेत्र-पर्पटी.<BR>—त्रि-यान, अम्, n. (with Buddhists) the three<BR>vehicles (leading to welfare).<BR>—त्रि-याम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>containing (as the night) three Yāmas or watches,<BR>i. e. about nine hours; (आ), f. night, (अहस्-त्रिया-<BR>मम्, day and night); turmeric; a convolvulus with<BR>dark flowers; the Indigo plant; the river Yamunā.<BR>—त्रि-यामक, अम्, n. sin (‘the impeder of the<BR>three objects of life?’).<BR>—त्रि-युग, अम्, n. a space<BR>of time containing three periods or ages; (अस्), m.<BR>‘appearing in the three Yugas,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—त्रि-योनि, इस्, f. a lawsuit in which a person<BR>engages from anger, covetousness, or infatuation.<BR>—त्रिय्यृच = त्र्य्-ऋच = तृच, a strophe consist-<BR>ing of three verses.<BR>—त्रि-रत्न, अम्, n. the three<BR>gems, viz. Buddha, the law, and the congregation.<BR>—त्रि-रसक, अम्, n. a spirituous liquor (‘having<BR>a triple flavour’).<BR>—त्रि-रात्र, अम्, n. three nights<BR>collectively, or the duration of three nights or days;<BR>(अम्), ind. for three nights or days, during three<BR>days; (आत् or एण), ind. after three days; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>lasting three days; (अस्), m. a festival which lasts<BR>three days; [cf. त्र्य्-अह.]<BR>—त्रि-राशि-प, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>governing three signs of the zodiac.<BR>—त्रि-रूप,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of three colours.<BR>—त्रि-रेख, अस्, m.<BR>‘having three lines,’ a conch, a muscle-shell, a shell<BR>marked with three lines.<BR>—त्रि-लवण, अम्, n. the<BR>three salts, = त्रि-पटु, q. v.<BR>—त्रि-लिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing the three Guṇas; having three genders,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0391-a" target="_blank">Page0391-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(often = ‘an adjective’); the Sanskrit form for Telinga<BR>(called so fr. three Liṅgas).<BR>—त्रि-लिङ्गक, अस्, &c.,<BR>having three genders, an adjective.<BR>—त्रि-लिङ्गी,<BR>f. the three grammatical genders.<BR>—त्रि-लोक, अम्, n.<BR>the three worlds, i. e. sky, atmosphere, and earth, or<BR>heaven, earth, and the lower region; (अस्), m. an<BR>inhabitant of the three worlds; (ई), f. the universe,<BR>the aggregate of the three worlds.<BR>—त्रिलोक-नाथ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of the three worlds,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—त्रिलोक-रक्षिन्, ई, m. guardian of the<BR>three worlds.<BR>—त्रिलोकात्मन् (˚क-आत्˚), आ, m. ‘soul<BR>of the three worlds,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्रिलोकी-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—त्रिलोकेश<BR>(˚क-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the three worlds,’ an<BR>epithet of the Sun.<BR>—त्रि-लोचन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, ‘tri-<BR>ocular,’ ‘three-eyed,’ epithet of Śiva; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a poet; of a grammarian; of a prince &c.; (आ), f.<BR>a disloyal wife, unchaste woman; (with Buddhists)<BR>N. of a deity; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>लोचन-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—त्रिलोचन-<BR>दास, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR>—त्रिलोचने-<BR>श्वर-तीर्थ (˚न-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—त्रि-लोहक, अम्, n. the three metals, i. e. gold,<BR>silver, and copper.<BR>—त्रि-लौह, अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>the above three metals.<BR>—त्रि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, con-<BR>taining the word त्रि.<BR>—त्रि-वत्स, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>three years old (as an ox or cow).<BR>—त्रि-वन्धुर,<BR>see त्रि-बन्धुर.<BR>—त्रि-वर्ग, अस्, m. an aggreagate<BR>of three things or substances &c.; the three objects<BR>or pursuits of life, viz. religion or virtue (धर्म),<BR>pleasure (काम), and wealth (अर्थ); the three<BR>conditions of a king or kingdom, viz. progress<BR>(वृद्धि), remaining stationary (स्थान), and de-<BR>cline (क्षय); the three qualities of nature, viz.<BR>सत्-त्व, रजस्, and तमस्, see under गुण; the<BR>three higher castes or tribes; the three myrobalans;<BR>the three spices &c.; propriety, good behaviour.<BR>—त्रिवर्ग-चिन्तन, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of<BR>the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—त्रिवर्ग-पारीण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having passed through the three conditions or<BR>attained the three objects of life.<BR>—त्रि-वर्ण, अम्, n.<BR>three colours; (अस्, आ, अम्), three-coloured (Ved.).<BR>—त्रि-वर्णक, अम्, n. a kind of plant, = गो-क्षु-<BR>रक; the three myrobalans [cf. त्रि-फला]; the three<BR>spices; [cf. त्रि-कटु.]<BR>—त्रिवर्ण-कृत्, त्, m. the<BR>chameleon.<BR>—त्रि-वर्तु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. threefold;<BR>[cf. त्रि-वृत्.]<BR>—त्रिवर्त्म-गा, f. ‘flowing by three<BR>paths,’ an epithet of the Gaṅgā; [cf. त्रिपथ-गा.]<BR>—त्रि-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. three paths; (आ, आ, अ), going<BR>by three paths (Ved.).<BR>—त्रि-वर्ष, अम्, n. a period<BR>of three years; (अस्, आ, अम्), three years old.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>वर्षिका, f. a three-year-old heifer.<BR>—त्रि-वर्षीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, triennial, lasting for three years, used for<BR>three years.<BR>—त्रि-वलि, ई, n. f. the three folds or<BR>wrinkles across the belly; [cf. त्रि-बली.]<BR>—त्रि-<BR>वार, अस्, m., N. of a son of Garuḍa; (अम्), ind.<BR>three times, thrice.<BR>—त्रि-विक्रम, अम्, n. the<BR>three steps (of Viṣṇu), three strides; (अस्), m.<BR>‘one who makes three steps or strides,’ an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu, who paced the three worlds in three<BR>steps in his Vāmana or dwarf Avatār, see बलि; N.<BR>of a Brāhman; of an astronomer; of a jurist; of a<BR>medical author.<BR>—त्रिविक्रम-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha.<BR>—त्रिविक्रम-देव, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—त्रिविक्रम-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Damayantī-kathā.<BR>—त्रिविक्रमाचार्य<BR>(˚म-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an astronomer.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>विद्य, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva, ‘familiar with or<BR>containing the three Vedas;’ (आ), f. three branches<BR>of knowledge, especially that of the three Vedas.<BR>—त्रि-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of three kinds, threefold,<BR>triple, in three ways.<BR>—त्रि-विधा, ind. (?), in three<BR>parts, triply (?).<BR>—त्रि-विनत, अस्, आ, अम्, bowing<BR>in the presence of three, viz. gods, Brāhmans, and<BR>preceptors; bent in three places, curved in three<BR>parts of the body (?).<BR>—त्रि-विष्टप, अम्, n. = त्रि-<BR>पिष्टप, the world of Indra, i. e. heaven or paradise;<BR>the three worlds.<BR>—त्रिविष्टप-सद्, त्, m. an in-<BR>habitant of heaven, a deity.<BR>—त्रि-विस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>= त्रि-वैस्तिक, worth three Vistas.<BR>—त्रि-वीज, अस्,<BR>m. a kind of grain; [cf. श्यामाक.]<BR>—त्रि-वृत्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0391-b" target="_blank">Page0391-b+ 81</a>]<BR>त्, त्, त्, threefold, triple, tri-form; consisting of three<BR>parts or folds &c.; (with स्तोम) a threefold hymn<BR>of praise, (i. e. a particular recitation, in which first<BR>the first three Ṛks of each Tṛca of the eleventh<BR>hymn of the ninth Maṇḍala of the Ṛg-veda are sung<BR>together, then the second Ṛks, and lastly the third;<BR>hence this Stoma consists of 3 × 3 or 9 verses);<BR>connected with the Trivṛt-stoma; (त्), m. a triple<BR>cord consisting of three strings; a girdle &c. of<BR>three strings; an amulet of three strings; (त्), f. a<BR>plant of valuable purgative properties, commonly<BR>called Tëori, and distinguished into two species,<BR>white and black (Convolvulus Turpethum); also<BR>called त्रि-वृता; [cf. त्र्य्-आवृत्.]<BR>—त्रि-वृत, f.; see<BR>the preceding.<BR>—त्रिवृत्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, com-<BR>bining three things; (अम्), n. making a com-<BR>bination of three things; combining earth, water,<BR>and fire, in the proportion of half of one with a<BR>quarter of each of the others.<BR>—त्रि-वृत्ति, इस्, f.<BR>truth (?); [cf. त्र्य्-अक्षर.]<BR>—त्रिवृत्-पर्णी, f.,<BR>N. of a pot-herb, Hincha Repens; [cf. हिल-मोचि.]<BR>—त्रि-वृन्त, अस्, m. (?) the plant Butea Frondosa.<BR>—त्रिवृन्तिका, f. the plant Ipomœa Turpethum.<BR>—त्रि-वृष, अस्, m., N. of a Muni; [cf. the next.]<BR>—त्रि-वृषन्, आ, m., N. of the father of Try-aruṇa<BR>[cf. त्रै-वृष्ण]; N. of the Vyāsa of the twelfth<BR>Dvāpara.<BR>—त्रि-वेणी, f. ‘triple-braid,’ the place (now<BR>called Allahabad) where the Gaṅgā joins with the<BR>Yamunā or Jumnā and is supposed to receive under-<BR>ground the Sarasvatī; N. of the Gaṅgā.<BR>—त्रि-वेणु,<BR>उस्, m. a particular part of a carriage; (उस्, उस्, उ),<BR>epithet of a carriage, (according to some) furnished<BR>with three banners.<BR>—त्रि-वेद, (at the beginning of<BR>a comp.) the three Vedas, viz. Ṛg, Yajus, and<BR>Sāman; (अस्, आ, अम्), familiar with the three Vedas.<BR>—त्रि-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, familiar or acquainted with<BR>the three Vedas.<BR>—त्रि-वेदी, f. the three Vedas<BR>collectively.<BR>—त्रि-वेला, f. the plant Ipomœa Tur-<BR>pethum.<BR>—त्रि-शक्ति, इस्, f., N. of a female deity,<BR>= त्रि-कला.<BR>—त्रि-शङ्कु, उस्, m., N. of a sage; N.<BR>of a prince of the solar race, king of Ayodhyā,<BR>(according to the Rāmāyaṇa he was a son of Pṛthu,<BR>and was a pious prince who aspired to celebrate a<BR>great sacrifice whereby to ascend to heaven in his<BR>mortal body; he first requested the sage Vasiṣṭha<BR>to officiate for him, but being refused he then<BR>applied to the sage's hundred sons, by whom he was<BR>cursed and degraded to the condition of a Cāṇḍāla;<BR>in this emergency he had recourse to Viśvā-mitra,<BR>who undertook the sacrifice and invited all the gods<BR>to be present; they, however, declined, upon which<BR>the enraged Viśvā-mitra, by his own power, trans-<BR>ported Tri-śaṅku to the skies, whither he had no<BR>sooner arrived than he was hurled down again head-<BR>foremost by the gods; but, being arrested in his<BR>downward course by Viśvā-mitra, remained suspended<BR>with his head towards the earth, forming a constella-<BR>tion in the southern hemisphere: according to the<BR>Hari-vaṃśa and Vāyu-Purāṇa he was a son of Tray-<BR>yāruṇa: according to the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa, a son<BR>of Tri-bandhana: and he is sometimes described as<BR>a wicked prince, guilty of three Śaṅkus or heinous<BR>crimes); a cat, the civet-cat; a bird, the Cātaka,<BR>Cuculus Melanoleucos; a grasshopper; a fire-fly.<BR>—त्रिशङ्कु-ज, अस्, m. ‘the son of Tri-śaṅku,’ epithet<BR>of Hari-ścandra.<BR>—त्रिशङ्कु-याजिन्, ई, m. ‘sacrificing<BR>for Tri-śaṅku,’ epithet of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—त्रि-शत,<BR>अम्, n., 103, 300; (अस्, ई, अम्), the 300th; con-<BR>sisting of 300; (आस्), m. pl., 300.<BR>—त्रि-शतक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, consisting of 300.<BR>—त्रिशत-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 300th; the 103rd.<BR>—त्रि-शती, f. the<BR>aggregate of 300 (e. g. पशूनां त्रि-शती, 300<BR>cattle).<BR>—त्रि-शरण, अम्, n. (with Buddhists) the<BR>three places of refuge, Buddha, the Law, and the<BR>Assembly; (अस्), m. a Buddha.<BR>—त्रि-शर्करा, f.<BR>three kinds of sugar, viz. गुडोत्पन्ना, हिमोत्था,<BR>and मधुरा; [cf. त्रि-सिता.]<BR>—त्रि-शला, f., N. of the<BR>mother of the twenty-fourth Arhat of the present Ava-<BR>sarpiṇī.<BR>—त्रिशलाका-पुरुष-चरित, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a work by Hema-candra.<BR>—त्रि-शस्, ind. by threes,<BR>by three at a time.<BR>—त्रि-शाख, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0391-c" target="_blank">Page0391-c+ 81</a>]<BR>three branches.<BR>—त्रिशाख-पत्त्र, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Ægle Marmelos.<BR>—त्रि-शाण, अस्, ई, अम्, worth<BR>three Śāṇas.<BR>—त्रि-शानु, उस्, m. a various reading<BR>for त्रि-भानु.<BR>—त्रि-शाल, अस्, आ, अम्, or त्रि-<BR>शालक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of three halls or<BR>rooms; (अम्), n. a house with three halls.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शिख, अस्, आ, अम्, three-crested, three-headed, having<BR>the shape of a trident; (अस्), m. the plant Ægle<BR>Marmelos; the son of Rāvaṇa, a demon with three<BR>heads; N. of Indra in the Manv-antara of Tāmasa;<BR>(ई), f., N. of an Upaniṣad; (अम्), n. a trident, a<BR>three-pronged spear; a crest, a tiara with three<BR>points.<BR>—त्रि-शिखर, अस्, आ, अम्, having three tops<BR>or peaks; (अस्), m. (with शैल) N. of a mountain.<BR>—त्रिशिखि-दला, f. a kind of bulbous plant.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शिखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, three-crested, three-headed.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शिर, अस्, आ, अम्, having three points; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a Rākṣasa; (आ), f. the root of Bignonia Suave-<BR>olens.<BR>—त्रि-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, three-headed, having<BR>three points or tops; (आस्), m. epithet of Tvāṣṭra<BR>Viśva-rūpa; Fever personified as a demon with three<BR>heads [cf. त्रि-पद् and त्रि-पाद्]; N. of an Asura<BR>killed by Viṣṇu; N. of a Rākṣasa killed by<BR>Rāma; an epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—त्रि-शीर्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘three-headed,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्रि-शीर्-<BR>षक, अस्, आ, अम्, three-headed; (अम्), n. a tri-<BR>dent, a three-pointed or three-pronged spear.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शीर्षन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. three-headed.<BR>—त्रि-शुक्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. white or bright in three places.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शुक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. triply illuminated.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शुच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. triply shining or splendid, shining in<BR>three ways.<BR>—त्रि-शूल, अम्, n. a trident, a three-<BR>pointed pike or spear, especially the weapon of Śiva;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), ‘bearing the trident,’ epithet of Śiva;<BR>N. of a mountain.<BR>—त्रिशूल-खात, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Tīrtha, (‘digged with the trident.’)<BR>—त्रिशूल-<BR>गङ्गा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—त्रिशूलाङ्क (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘trident-marked,’ a N. of Śiva; of a teacher.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘armed with the trident;’ (ई), m.<BR>epithet of Śiva; (इनी), f. epithet of Durgā.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having three horns or peaks;<BR>(अस्), m. a hill with three peaks; N. of a mountain;<BR>a triangle.<BR>—त्रिशृङ्गिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having three<BR>horns; (ई), m. a sort of fish, commonly Rohi,<BR>Cyprinus Rohita.<BR>—त्रि-शोक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. =<BR>त्रि-शुच् (?) ; (अस्), m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—त्रि-षं-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for त्रि-सम्˚), triply connected.<BR>—त्रि-षंवत्सर, अस्, आ, अम् (for त्रि-सम्˚),<BR>lasting three years.<BR>—त्रि-षत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for त्रि-<BR>सत्य), Ved. trebly true (in thought, word, and deed).<BR>—त्रि-षधस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in three<BR>places.<BR>—त्रि-षन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ (for त्रि-सन्˚), Ved.<BR>composed of three parts or members; (इस्), m., N.<BR>of a demon in the Atharva-veda, generally associated<BR>with Arbudi; (ई), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—त्रि-षप्त<BR>or त्रि-सप्त (fr. त्रि+सप्तन्), Ved. three times<BR>seven, twenty-one; an indefinite number.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>षप्तीय, अस्, m. adj., N. of the first verse of the<BR>Atharva-veda, beginning with the words ये त्रि-<BR>षप्तास्, &c.<BR>—त्रि-षवण or त्रि-सवन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, containing three oblations; (अस्), m., N. of an<BR>ancient sage; त्रि-षवणम् or त्रिषवण-स्नानम्,<BR>the three ablutions to be performed daily, i. e. at dawn,<BR>noon, and sunset.<BR>—त्रिषवण-स्नायिन्, ई, m. a<BR>man performing regularly the prescribed ablutions<BR>morning, noon, and evening.<BR>—त्रिषष्ट, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the sixty-third.<BR>—त्रि-षष्टि, इस्, m. sixty-<BR>three; [cf. त्रयः-षष्टि.]<BR>—त्रिषष्टि-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the sixty-third.<BR>—त्रिषष्टि-धा, ind.<BR>in sixty-three parts, sixty-three-fold.<BR>—त्रिषष्टि-<BR>शलाकापुरुष-चरित, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—त्रिष्टुप्-छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having the<BR>metre Tri-ṣṭubh.<BR>—त्रि-ष्टुभ्, प्, f. (for त्रि-स्तुभ्<BR>fr. त्रि+स्तुभ्, to praise; or possibly the word may<BR>come fr. स्तुभ्, to stop, because the voice is obliged<BR>to pause three times; according to Yāska, the prefix<BR>त्रि may be fr. rt. तॄ, to denote the rapidity of<BR>the metre, cf. जगती; or fr. त्रि, three, +स्तुभ्, to<BR>praise, because the metre is in praise of the वज्र<BR>or thunderbolt, which has three edges); N. of a<BR>Vedic metre consisting of four Pādas of eleven<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-a" target="_blank">Page0392-a+ 81</a>]<BR>syllables each; (in the later metrical system) N. of<BR>every metre consisting of four times eleven syllables<BR>(e. g. the Indra-vajrā and Upendra-vajrā metres); [cf.<BR>त्रैष्टुभ.]<BR>—त्रि-ष्टोम, अस्, आ, अम् (for त्रि-<BR>स्तोम), Ved. containing three Stomas; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>an Ekāha.<BR>—त्रि-ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (for त्रि-स्थ), Ved.<BR>standing on three (wheels), situated in three places;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—त्रि-ष्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ (for त्रि-<BR>स्थिन्), Ved. standing on triply divided ground.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>संवत्सर, see under त्रि-षंवत्सर.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सत्य, see under त्रि-षत्य.<BR>—त्रि-सन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>see त्रि-षन्धि; (इस्), f. a kind of mallow.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सन्धिक, अस्, आ, अम्, occurring or happening at the<BR>three periods or divisions of the day, (probably a<BR>wrong reading for त्रिसन्ध्यिक.)<BR>—त्रि-सन्ध्य,<BR>अम्, n. the three periods or divisions of the day, viz.<BR>dawn, noon, and evening or sunset; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>goddess; a form of Durgā; a kind of mallow; (आ<BR>or ई), f. the three periods of the day; (अम्), ind.<BR>at the time of the three Sandhyās; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>relating to the three periods of the day.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सन्ध्य-कुसुमा, f. a kind of mallow.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सप्तत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the following), the seventy-<BR>third.<BR>—त्रि-सप्तति, इस्, f. seventy-three; [cf. त्रयः-<BR>सप्तति.]<BR>—त्रिसप्तति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the seventy-<BR>third.<BR>—त्रि-सप्तन् or त्रि-सप्त, three times seven,<BR>twenty-one [cf. त्रि-षप्त]; त्रिसप्त-कृत्वस्,<BR>ind. twenty-one times.<BR>—त्रि-सम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(in geom.) having three equal sides; (अम्), n. an<BR>aggregate of equal parts of three substances, viz.<BR>yellow myrobalan, ginger, and molasses; त्रिसम-<BR>चतुरश्र, अम्, n. a quadrangle having three equal<BR>sides.<BR>—त्रि-सर, अस्, अम्, m. n. a dish of<BR>sesamum, rice, &c., = कृशर or कृसर.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सर्ग, अस्, m. the triple product of the three<BR>qualities of nature.<BR>—त्रि-सवन = त्रि-षवण, q. v.<BR>—त्रि-साधन, अस्, आ, अम्, triply composed, having<BR>three component parts.<BR>—त्रि-सामन्, आ, आ, अ, sing-<BR>ing three Sāmans or the Sāman called Triḥ-sāman.<BR>—त्रि-सामा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—त्रि-साम्य, अम्, n.<BR>equilibrium of the three (qualities).<BR>—त्रि-साहस्र,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. consisting of 3000.<BR>—त्रि-सिता, f. = त्रि-<BR>शर्करा, three kinds of white sugar, viz. गुडोत्-<BR>पन्ना, मधु-जा, and हिमोत्था.<BR>—त्रि-सीत्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, thrice ploughed (as a field &c.).<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सुगन्धि or त्रि-सुगन्धिक, अम्, n. = त्रि-जात, the<BR>three fragrant substances or spices.<BR>—त्रि-सुपर्ण, अस्,<BR>m. a N. of certain hymns of the Ṛg and Yajur<BR>Vedas; (अस्, आ, अम्), or त्रि-सुपर्णक, अस्, इका,<BR>अम्, familiar or conversant with the above hymns of<BR>the Veda; [cf. त्रि-सौपर्ण.]<BR>—त्रि-सुवर्चक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a threefold excellent splendor.<BR>—त्रि-सौगन्ध्य, अम्, n. = त्रि-सुगन्धि.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>सौपर्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the part of the<BR>Vedas called Tri-suparṇa; N. of a particular religious<BR>vow or observance.<BR>—त्रि-सौवर्ण, अम्, n. perhaps<BR>a wrong reading for त्रि-सुपर्ण.<BR>—त्रि-स्कन्धक,<BR>N. of a Sūtra work.<BR>—त्रि-स्तन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, milked<BR>from three nipples (Ved.); having three breasts.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>स्तोभ-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having three pauses or<BR>three rhythms or three divisions (?).<BR>—त्रि-स्थली, f.<BR>the three (sacred) places.<BR>—त्रिस्थली-सेतु, N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—त्रि-स्थान, अम्, n. a sacred spot celebrated<BR>for a junction of three streams of the Ganges; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), reaching through the three worlds.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>स्रोतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, having three streams; (आस्), f. an<BR>epithet of the Ganges [cf. त्रि-पथ-गा, त्रि-मार्ग-<BR>गा, त्रि-वर्त्म-गा]; N. of another river.<BR>—त्रि-<BR>स्रोतसी, f., N. of a river.<BR>—त्रि-हल्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>thrice ploughed (as a field &c.).<BR>—त्रि-हायण, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, three years old; appearing in three ages of<BR>the world; (ई), f. a three-year-old heifer.<BR>—त्रीषु<BR>(त्रि-इष्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, or त्रीषुक, अस्, आ, अम्, fur-<BR>nished with three arrows.<BR>—त्रीष्टक (त्रि-इष्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. furnished with three Iṣṭakās or sacri-<BR>ficial bricks.<BR>—त्र्य्-अंश, अस्, अम्, m. or n. (?), three<BR>shares or portions, three-fourths; a third part, the third<BR>part of a sign of the zodiac (= दृक्काण, q. v.).<BR>—त्र्यंश-नाथ, अस्, m. the regent of a Dṛkkāṇa.<BR>—त्र्य्-अक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, triocular; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Rudra-Śiva; also of a Daitya or Dānava.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-b" target="_blank">Page0392-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—त्र्यक्षक, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्र्य्-<BR>अक्षन्, आ, आ, अ, triocular; (आ), m. epithet of Rudra.<BR>—त्र्यक्ष-पत्नी, f. an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR>—त्र्य्-<BR>अक्षर, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of three sounds or<BR>letters or syllables, triliteral; (अम्), n. a word or<BR>song consisting of three letters or syllables (e. g.<BR>सत्यम् or स + ति + अम्); (अस्), m. a genealogist;<BR>the Ghaṭaka or matchmaker; [cf. घटक and<BR>खटक.]<BR>—त्र्य्-अङ्कट, अम्, n. or त्र्य्-अङ्गट,<BR>अस्, m. a sling or three strings like those of a balance<BR>suspended to either end of a pole for carrying bur-<BR>dens; a sort of collyrium; (अस्), m. a N. of Śiva.<BR>—त्र्य्-अङ्ग, आणि, n. pl., Ved. three portions of the<BR>sacrificial victim supposed to belong to the Sv-iṣṭa-<BR>kṛt, q. v., viz. the upper part of the right fore-foot,<BR>a part of the left thigh, and a part of the bowels.<BR>—त्र्य्-अङ्गुल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. three fingers long<BR>or broad or deep &c.<BR>—त्र्यङ्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>belonging to the Try-aṅgas.<BR>—त्र्य्-अञ्जन, अम्, n.<BR>the three kinds of collyrium, or Kālāñjana, Push-<BR>pāñjana, and Rasāñjana.<BR>—त्र्य्-अञ्जल, अम्, n. and<BR>त्र्य्-अञ्जलि, इ, n. three handfuls.<BR>—त्र्य्-अधिपति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘the lord of the three qualities,’ (i. e. सत्-त्व,<BR>रजस्, and तमस्; cf. गुण), an epithet of Kṛṣṇa<BR>or Viṣṇu.<BR>—त्र्य्-अधिष्ठान, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>three stations, situated in three places.<BR>—त्र्य्-अधीश,<BR>अस्, m. = त्र्य्-अधिपति, q. v.<BR>—त्र्य्-अध्व-गा, f. a<BR>N. of the Ganges, ‘going or flowing through the<BR>three worlds.’<BR>—त्र्य्-अनीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>three faces, followed by three hosts; (Sāy.) having<BR>the three properties of heat, rain, and cold.<BR>—त्र्य्-<BR>अन्त, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—त्र्य्-अब्द, अम्, n.<BR>a period of three years; (अम्), ind. during three<BR>years; (अस्, आ, अम्), three years old.<BR>—त्र्य्-अम्बक,<BR>अस्, m. a N. of Śiva (Rudra) as triocular or uttering<BR>the three (Vedas) or uttering the three mystical<BR>letters (?), or as having three wives or sisters (as<BR>if fr. त्रि-अम्बा); N. of one of the eleven Rudras;<BR>the sacrificial ceremony in which the Try-ambakās<BR>or cakes sacred to Rudra Try-ambaka are offered;<BR>N. of a mountain; (आ), f. an epithet of Pārvatī;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—त्र्यम्बक-माहात्म्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the glory of Try-ambaka,’ N. of a part of<BR>the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—त्र्यम्बक-सख, अस्, m.<BR>‘the friend of Try-ambaka,’ an epithet of Kuvera,<BR>the god of wealth.<BR>—त्र्य्-अरुण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man with the patronymic Traivṛṣṇa.<BR>—त्र्य्-अरुष,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. marked red in three places.<BR>—त्र्य्-<BR>अवर, अस्, आ, अम्, having three who are inferior,<BR>three at the least; (अम्), ind. at least three times,<BR>(see Manu XI. 80.)<BR>—त्र्य्-अवि, इस्, ई, m. f., Ved. a<BR>calf eighteen months old.<BR>—त्र्यशीत, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. त्र्य्-अशीति), the eighty-third.<BR>—त्र्य्-अशीति, इस्, f.<BR>eighty-three.<BR>—त्र्यशीति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>eighty-third.<BR>—त्र्य्-अश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, triangular; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a plant, = त्रिधार-स्नुही; (अम्), n. a<BR>triangle.<BR>—त्र्यश्र-कुण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a mystical<BR>diagram.<BR>—त्र्य्-अष्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, containing three<BR>Aṣṭakās; (अम्), n. a kind of vessel.<BR>—त्र्य्-अष्टन्<BR>or त्र्य्-अष्ट, three times eight, twenty-four; त्र्य्-<BR>अष्ट-वर्ष, twenty-four years old.<BR>—त्र्य्-अस्र,<BR>see त्र्य्-अश्र.<BR>—त्र्य्-अह, अम्, n. a period of<BR>three days; त्र्य्-अहम्, ind. during three days; त्र्य्-<BR>अहात् or त्र्य्-अहेन, ind. after three days; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), lasting three days; (अस्), m., Ved. a festival lasting<BR>three days.<BR>—त्र्यह-स्पर्श, अस्, m. or त्र्यह-<BR>स्पृश, अम्, n. the meeting of part of three lunar<BR>days in one solar day, (the first lunar day ending just<BR>after midnight and the third beginning a little before<BR>the next midnight.)<BR>—त्र्यहीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. last-<BR>ing three days.<BR>—त्र्यहैहिक (˚ह-ऐह्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having provision sufficient for three days, providing<BR>for three days.<BR>—त्र्य्-अह्न, अस्, आ, अम्, happening<BR>or occurring after three days.<BR>—त्र्याक्षायण, अस्,<BR>m. (fr. त्र्य्-अक्ष), a worshipper of Śiva (?).<BR>—त्र्या-<BR>क्षायण-भक्त, अम्, n. a district inhabited by<BR>worshippers of Śiva.<BR>—त्र्य्-आयुष, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>threefold vital power or period of life; (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara) the threefold period of life, consisting of<BR>childhood, youth, and old age.<BR>—त्र्यारुणि, इस्, m.<BR>(fr. त्र्य्-अरुण), N. of the Vyāsa in the fifteenth<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">Page0392-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Dvāpara; N. of a mountain.<BR>—त्र्य्-आर्षेय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, containing three lines or families of Ṛṣis;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. an aggregate of three persons, viz. blind,<BR>deaf, and dumb.<BR>—त्र्य्-आलिखित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>scratched or marked in three places.<BR>—त्र्यालिखित-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, consisting of bricks marked in<BR>three places.<BR>—त्र्य्-आवृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. carried on in<BR>three periods, consisting of three series.<BR>—त्र्य्-आशिर्,<BR>ईर्, m., Ved. mixed with three products of milk;<BR>(according to Sāy.) mixed with Dadhi, Saktu, and<BR>Payas, (said of the Soma.)<BR>—त्र्याहिक, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. त्र्य्-अह), produced or performed &c. in three<BR>days; tertian; returning after the third day, quartan<BR>(as a fever); having provisions for three days.<BR>—त्र्य्-उत्तरी-भाव, अस्, m. progression by three.<BR>—त्र्य्-उदाय, अम्, n., Ved. the threefold going to<BR>the altar, i. e. in the three daily oblations; (Sāy.)<BR>having three goings to the altar (as the Soma).<BR>—त्र्य्-उधन्, आ, m., Ved. three-uddered, (according<BR>to Sāy.) said of the year as having three seasons.<BR>—त्र्य्-उषण or त्र्य्-ऊषण, अम्, n. the three<BR>spices collectively, i. e. black pepper, long pepper,<BR>and dry ginger.<BR>—त्र्य्-ऋच, अम्, n. = तृच, a<BR>strophe consisting of three verses.<BR>—त्र्य्-एत, अस्, m.,<BR>त्र्येणी or त्र्येनी, f., अम्, n., Ved. variegated or<BR>spotted in three places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंश|त्रिंशः
त्रिंश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रिंशत्), the thirtieth, con-<BR>stituting the thirtieth part; joined with thirty (e. g.<BR>त्रिंशं शतम्, 130); consisting of thirty (as a<BR>Stoma); connected with the Triṃśa-stoma; (1/30) of<BR>a sign of the zodiac, a degree.<BR>—त्रिंशांश or<BR>त्रिंशांशक (˚श-अं˚), अस्, m. a thirtieth part,<BR>(1/30) of a sign of the zodiac, a degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशक|त्रिंशकः
त्रिंशक, अस्, आ, अम्, = त्रिंश, consisting of thirty<BR>parts, divided into thirty; bought for thirty, worth<BR>thirty; (अम्), n. a collection or aggregate of thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्
त्रिंशत्, त्, f. (fr. त्रि and शत् = दशत्), thirty,<BR>the number thirty.<BR>—त्रिंशच्-छत, अम्, n., 130.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशति|त्रिंशतिः
त्रिंशति, इस्, f. = त्रिंशत्, thirty; [cf. त्रयस्-<BR>त्रिंशति, पञ्च-त्˚, सप्त-त्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्क|त्रिंशत्कं
त्रिंशत्क, अम्, n. an aggregate or collection of<BR>thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्तम
त्रिंशत्-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the thirtieth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्पत्त्र
त्रिंशत्-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the white esculent water-<BR>lily, Nymphæa Esculenta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशद्विंश
त्रिंशद्-विंश, आस्, m. pl. about twenty or thirty,<BR>between twenty and thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशिन्
त्रिंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, containing thirty, consisting of<BR>thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिक|त्रिकं
त्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, triple, threefold; trine, forming<BR>a triad; trebly repeated, happening the third time;<BR>(with or without शत) three out of every hundred,<BR>three per cent; (अस्), m., N. of two plants, = गो-<BR>क्षुरक and Trapa Bispinosa [cf. त्रि-कण्टक];<BR>(आ), f. a triangular frame or bar across the mouth of<BR>a well over which passes the rope of the bucket; a<BR>wooden frame at the mouth of a well, or the upper<BR>part of the well; a frame at the bottom of a well on<BR>which the masonry rests; the cover or lid of a well;<BR>(अम्), n. the aggregate of three, a triad [cf. तौर्य-<BR>त्रिक]; a place where three roads meet; the lower<BR>part of the spine or regio sacra; the part about the<BR>hips; the part between the shoulder-blades; the<BR>three mystical words pronounced before the Gāyatrī<BR>[cf. व्याहृति]; the three spices, three myrobalans<BR>&c. collectively.<BR>—त्रिक-स्थान, अम्, n. the region<BR>at the lower part of the spine.<BR>—त्रिकाग्नि-काल<BR>(˚क-अग्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रित
त्रित, अस्, m., Ved. (in the Atharva-veda also<BR>तृत), N. of a Vedic deity; (he is generally asso-<BR>ciated with the Maruts, Vāyu, and Indra; and fights<BR>like the latter with Tvāṣṭra, Vṛtra, and other<BR>demons: he is also called Āptya, q. v., either as<BR>produced in water by Agni, whence he is sometimes<BR>called ‘a son of the water,’ or as son of the Ṛṣi<BR>Āpta. In some passages of the Taittirīya-Saṃhitā he<BR>is regarded as bestowing long life; while elsewhere<BR>he is supposed to reside in the remotest regions of<BR>the world, whence the idea of wishing to remove<BR>calamity to Trita or to the remotest place possible;<BR>cf. Ṛg-veda VIII. 47, 14. In some passages of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">Page0393-a+ 72</a>]<BR>Veda, Indian commentators explain Trita by त्रि-<BR>स्थान, ‘reaching through the triple world,’ as an<BR>epithet of Indra or Vāyu. In later myths Trita is<BR>described as a Ṛṣi, by whom several hymns of the<BR>Ṛg-veda were-composed. Sāyaṇa in his introduction<BR>to Ṛg-veda I. 105, relates that there were three Ṛṣis,<BR>named Ekata, Dvita, and Trita, who lived in a desert<BR>country; being parched with thirst, they looked<BR>about for a well, and having found one, Trita entered<BR>it to draw water, when the other two, desirous of<BR>obtaining his property, threw him into the well and<BR>closed up the mouth with a wheel; shut up in the<BR>well, Trita composed a hymn to the gods, and<BR>managed, in a marvellous manner, to perform the<BR>Soma sacrifice, that he might drink the Soma himself<BR>before death, or offer it to the deities in the hope of<BR>being extricated by them: his preparation of the<BR>Soma is described in the Mahā-bh. Śalya-parva 2095,<BR>and he is elsewhere celebrated as an offerer of the<BR>Soma. In various other epic legends, Ekata, Dvita,<BR>and Trita are described as three brothers, sons of<BR>Gautama or of Prajā-pati, = Brahmā. According to<BR>the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa, Trita is one of the twelve<BR>sons of Manu and Naḍvalā. Some identify the Vedic<BR>त्रित with the Vedic त्रैतन, and with Thraetana<BR>the Zend form of Feridun. His connection with<BR>water points to a comparison with the Gr. Τρίτων,<BR>τριτο-γενής, Τριτωνίς, Τριτο-πάτορες, &c.) (त्रित<BR>seems also to mean) a class of deities, ‘the third<BR>ones,’ i. e. those who live in the sky (?); the priest<BR>who prepares the Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0392-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितय|त्रितयं
त्रितय, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of three parts;<BR>(अम्), n. a collection of three, τριάς.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्
त्रिस्, ind. thrice, three times, at three places;<BR>(followed by gutturals and palatals there may be the<BR>optional substitution of ष् for Visarga, e. g. त्रिष्<BR>करोति or त्रिः करोति, he does thrice.)<BR>—त्रिः-<BR>प्लक्ष = त्रि-प्लक्ष, q. v.<BR>—त्रिः-सामन्, अ, n.,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR>—त्रिः-स्नान, अम्, n. bathing<BR>thrice every day.<BR>—त्रिर्-अश्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having<BR>three edges, three-cornered.<BR>—त्रिस्-तावा, f. (fr. त्रिस्-<BR>तावत्), three times the usual size, (only used with<BR>वेदि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगूढ
त्रिगूढ त्रिगूढ, अम्, n. the dancing or<BR>acting of a man in female attire, (evidently a wrong<BR>form for स्त्री-गूढ); [cf. त्रि-चरित्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिङ्ख्
त्रिङ्ख् त्रिङ्ख्, cl. 1. P. त्रिङ्खति, &c., to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचरित्र
त्रिचरित्र त्रिचरित्र, a wrong reading for<BR>स्त्री-चरित्र; [cf. त्रिगूढ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिण|त्रिणं
त्रिण त्रिण, अम्, n. = तृण, grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणाक|त्रिणाकः
त्रिणाक त्रि-णाक = त्रि-नाक, p. 389, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपु
त्रिपु त्रिपु, उस्, m., Ved. a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुक्ति
त्रिभुक्ति त्रिभुक्ति (?) for तीर-भुक्ति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियूह|त्रियूहः
त्रियूह त्रियूह, अस्, m. (probably a foreign<BR>word), a chesnut-coloured horse; [cf. उकनाह,<BR>उराह, कियाह, कोकाह, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिल्लक
त्रिल्लक त्रिल्लक and त्रिल्लसेन, अस्, m., N.<BR>of two men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषम
त्रिषम त्रिषम, Ved. = ह्रस्व, short (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्
त्रिस् त्रिस्. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रीणि
त्रीणि त्रीणि, n. pl. three. See त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रीशट
त्रीशट त्रीशट, अस्, m. [cf. तीसट], N. of<BR>the author of a medical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुट्
त्रुट् त्रुट्, cl. 6. 4. P. त्रुटति, त्रुट्यति,<BR>तुत्रोट, त्रुटितुम्, to be torn or split, to<BR>tear, break, burst, snap, fall asunder: Caus. P. A.<BR>त्रोटयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to tear, break, cut, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटि|त्रुटिः
त्रुटि, इस्, f. (or त्रुटी, f. ?), cutting, breaking,<BR>a tear, split; a small part, an atom or a visible atom<BR>composed of three subtler elementary particles; a<BR>very minute space of time, a moment, equal to (1/2)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">Page0393-b+ 77</a>]<BR>Lava, = (1/4) Kṣaṇa, = (1/40) Kāṣṭhā, = (1/400) Kalā, =<BR>(1/4000) Nālikā, = (1/8000) Muhūrta, (or = (1/100) Vedha, =<BR>(1/300) Lava, = (1/900) Nimeṣa, = (1/2700) Kṣaṇa, = (1/13500)<BR>Kāṣṭhā, = (1/202500) Laghu, = (1/3037500) Nāḍikā, =<BR>(1/6075000) Muhūrta); small cardamoms (Alpinia Car-<BR>damomum), cardamoms from Guzerat; a sort of<BR>tree; doubt, uncertainty; breaking (a promise); loss,<BR>destruction; N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda.<BR>—त्रुटि-वीज, अस्, m. Arum Colocasia (=<BR>कचु), an esculent root.<BR>—त्रुटि-शस्, ind. in short<BR>spaces of time.<BR>—त्रुट्य्-अवयव, अस्, m. one half<BR>of a Truṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटित
त्रुटित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, broken, divided, hurt,<BR>wounded, chapped, chafed.<BR>—त्रुटित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having cut or broken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटि|त्रोटिः
त्रोटि, इस्, f. the beak or bill of a bird; the mouth<BR>of a fish; a kind of bird; a kind of pike (Esox<BR>Kankila); a medicinal plant.<BR>—त्रोटि-हस्त, अस्, m. a<BR>bird (‘having a beak for hands’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुड्
त्रुड् त्रुड्, Ved. = त्रुट्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुप्
त्रुप् त्रुप् or त्रुफ् or त्रुम्प् or त्रुम्फ्, cl.<BR>1. P. त्रोपति or त्रोफति or त्रुम्पति or<BR>त्रुम्फति, &c., to hurt, injure, kill; [cf. Gr. θρύπτω,<BR>τρύφος: Lith. truppù, ‘to be worn away by friction;’<BR>trumpas, ‘short;’ trumpinu, ‘to shorten.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेता
त्रेता त्रेता, f. (fr. त्रय, which is fr. त्रि,<BR>p. 388), a triad, a collection or assemblage of three,<BR>a triplet; the three sacred fires collectively (i. e. the<BR>southern, household, and sacrificial fires; often called<BR>अग्नि-त्रेता, see अग्नि-त्रय); trey, i. e. a throw at<BR>dice or the side of a die marked with three spots or<BR>points; (with or without युग) the second Yuga or<BR>silver age of the Hindūs which consists of 1, 296, 000<BR>years.<BR>—त्रेताग्नि (˚ता-अग्˚), इस्, m. one who has<BR>preserved the three sacred fires; the three fires<BR>collectively (= अग्नि-त्रेता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेतिनी
त्रेतिनी, f., Ved. the threefold flame of the three<BR>fires of the altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेधा
त्रे-धा, ind. = त्रि-धा, triply, in three parts, in<BR>three ways, in three places.<BR>—त्रेधा-विहित, divided<BR>into three parts.<BR>—त्रेधा-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, existing<BR>in three states.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैंश
त्रैंश, अम्, n. (fr. त्रिंशत्), scil. ब्राह्मण, the<BR>Brāhmaṇa consisting of thirty Adhyāyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैंशिक
त्रैंशिक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैककुद
त्रैककुद, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. coming from the<BR>mountain Tri-kakud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैककुभ
त्रैककुभ, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-ककुभ्), N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकण्टक
त्रैकण्टक, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from or made<BR>of the plant Tri-kaṇṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकालज्ञ
त्रैकाल-ज्ञ, probably a wrong reading for त्रै-<BR>काल्य-ज्ञ; [cf. त्रि-काल-ज्ञ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकालिक
त्रैकालिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-काल), relating to<BR>the three times, i. e. past, present, and future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकाल्य|त्रैकाल्यं
त्रैकाल्य, अम्, n. the three times; past, present,<BR>and future time; sunrise, noon, and sunset; tripar-<BR>tition; an aggregate of three, a triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैकुन्तक
त्रैकुन्तक, अम्, n. ? (fr. त्रि-कुन्त), a kind of<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगर्त
त्रैगर्त, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the Trigartas;<BR>(अस्), m. a prince of the Trigartas; (ई), f. a princess<BR>of the Trigartas; (आस्), m. pl. the Trigartas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगर्तक|त्रैगर्त्तक
त्रैगर्तक, belonging to the Trigartas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुणिक
त्रैगुणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-गुण), relating or<BR>belonging to three qualities, repeated three times,<BR>triple, relating to thrice, threefold, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुण्य|त्रैगुण्यं
त्रैगुण्य, अम्, n. the state of consisting of<BR>three threads, qualities, &c.; triplicity, tripleness,<BR>a triad, the triad of qualities, the three Guṇas or<BR>properties collectively (i. e. Sat-tva, Rajas, and Tamas;<BR>cf. गुण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैचीवरिक
त्रैचीवरिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-चीवर), possessing<BR>three mendicant garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैत|त्रैतं
त्रैत, अम्, n. (fr. त्रेता), Ved. a triad, a collec-<BR>tion of three, the aggregate of three, triplicity; (fr.<BR>त्रित), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैतन
त्रैतन, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a Vedic deity or<BR>supernatural being, thought by some to be connected<BR>with Trita, q. v.; (according to Sāy.) N. of a Dāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैदशिक
त्रैदशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रिदश), relating to<BR>the thirty-three gods; sacred to the gods, belonging<BR>to them, divine; (अम्), n. the part of the hand<BR>sacred to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैध|त्रैधं
त्रैध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-धा or त्रे-धा), three-<BR>fold, triple; (अम्), ind. = त्रि-धा or त्रे-धा, triply,<BR>in a triple manner, in three ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधातवी
त्रैधातवी, f. (scil. इष्टि), N. of a particular<BR>closing ceremony, (fr. त्रि-धातु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधातवीय
त्रैधातवीय, अम्, n. (scil. कर्मन्), N. of a<BR>particular closing rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधातुक
त्रैधातुक, अम्, n. the three worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधात्व
त्रैधात्व, अस्, m. a patronymic of Try-aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैनिष्किक
त्रैनिष्किक, अस्, ई, अम्, three Niṣkas worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपथ
त्रैपथ, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-पथ), a peculiar<BR>manner of sitting (generally with आसन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपद
त्रैपद, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-पद), three quarters<BR>(of a Yojana).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपारायणिक
त्रैपारायणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, performing the<BR>Pārāyaṇa three times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपिष्टप
त्रैपिष्टप, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Tri-pish-<BR>ṭapa, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुर|त्रैपुरः
त्रैपुर, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Tri-pura; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the inhabitants of the three cities of the Asura<BR>named Tri-pura, q. v.; the inhabitants of Tri-purā or<BR>Tri-purī or the Cedis; (अस्), m. a prince of Tri-pura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुरीय
त्रैपुरीय, N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुरुष
त्रैपुरुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-पुरुष), ex-<BR>tending through three male generations, or father,<BR>grandfather, and great-grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैफल
त्रैफल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-फला), coming from<BR>or belonging to the three myrobalans &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैबलि
त्रैबलि, इस्, m. (fr. त्रि-बलि or त्रि-बली), N. of<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैभाव्य
त्रैभाव्य, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-भाव), threefold<BR>nature or manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैमातुर|त्रैमातुरः
त्रैमातुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-मातृ), having<BR>three-mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैमासिक
त्रैमासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-मास), three<BR>months old, lasting three months, occurring every<BR>three months, quarterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैमास्य|त्रैमास्यं
त्रैमास्य, अम्, n. a period of three months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैयम्बक
त्रैयम्बक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging<BR>to Try-ambaka (e. g. अपूप, cake sacred to Try-<BR>ambaka).<BR>—त्रैयम्बक-मन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of<BR>the twenty-third chapter of the Śāradā-tilaka by<BR>Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैयारुण
त्रैयारुण, अस्, m., N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैराशिक|त्रैराशिकं
त्रैराशिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-राशि), relating<BR>to three numbers or to the three signs of the zodiac;<BR>त्रैराशिकम् or त्रैराशिक-गणितम्, the rule of<BR>three in arithmetic, (this is of two kinds, viz. क्रम-<BR>त्रैराशिक, rule of three direct; व्यस्त- or विलोम-<BR>त्रैराशिक, rule of three inverse.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैरूप्य
त्रैरूप्य, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-रूप), tripleness of<BR>form, threefold change of form; three forms or ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलाट
त्रैलाट (fr. त्रि-लाट ?), a sort of horse-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलिङ्ग
त्रैलिङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-लिङ्ग), having three<BR>genders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलोक|त्रैलोकः
त्रैलोक, अस्, m. (fr. त्रि-लोक), ‘the ruler of the<BR>three worlds,’ epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलोक्य|त्रैलोक्यं
त्रैलोक्य, अम्, n. the three worlds, see त्रि-<BR>लोक; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-कर्तृ,<BR>ता, m. ‘creator of the three worlds,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-डम्बर, N. of a medical work.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-दीपिका, f., N. of a Jaina work.<BR>—त्रै-<BR>लोक्य-देवी, f., N. of the wife of king Yaśas-kara.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of the three<BR>worlds,’ epithet of Rāma as an incarnation of Viṣṇu.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of an astrono-<BR>mical work.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-प्रभव, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-भय-कारक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing fear to the three worlds.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-राज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘king of the three worlds,’ N. of a powerful<BR>man.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-राज्य, अम्, n. the sovereignty<BR>of the three worlds.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-विक्रमिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva (striding through the three<BR>worlds).<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-विजया, f. a sort of hemp from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">Page0394-a+ 78</a>]<BR>which an intoxicating infusion &c. is prepared.<BR>—त्रैलोक्य-सागर, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—त्रै-<BR>लोक्य-सार, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—त्रैलोचन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-लोचन), relating to Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0393-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवणि
त्रैवणि, इस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्गिक
त्रैवर्गिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-वर्ग), relating<BR>to the three objects of life [cf. त्रि-वर्ग], directed<BR>towards or devoted to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्ग्य
त्रैवर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Tri-<BR>varga. See त्रैवर्गिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्णिक
त्रैवर्णिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-वर्ण), relating<BR>or belonging to the first three castes; (अस्), m. a<BR>member of the first three castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्षिक
त्रैवर्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-वर्ष), tri-<BR>ennial, three years old, lasting three years, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवार्षिक
त्रैवार्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, sufficient for three<BR>years, lasting three years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविक्रम
त्रैविक्रम, अस्, &c. (fr. त्रि-विक्रम), be-<BR>longing to Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. the three strides or<BR>steps (of Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविद
त्रैविद, a various reading for त्रयी-विद, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविद्य|त्रैविद्यं|त्रैविद्यः
त्रैविद्य, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-विद्या and त्रि-विद्य),<BR>the three sciences; the three Vedas (Ṛg, Yajus, and<BR>Sāman); study or knowledge of the three Vedas;<BR>the three duties of teaching the Veda, sacrificing, and<BR>donation; a particular Vrata or religious observance;<BR>a collection or assembly of Brāhmans who are<BR>familiar with the three Vedas; (अस्, आ, अम्), familiar<BR>with the three Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविध्य|त्रैविध्यं
त्रैविध्य, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-विध), the state of<BR>being of three kinds, threefoldness, triplicity, triple-<BR>ness, three ways or kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविष्टप|त्रैविष्टपः
त्रैविष्टप or त्रैविष्टपेय, अस्, m. an inha-<BR>bitant of Tri-viṣṭapa, a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवृत
त्रैवृत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-वृत्), coming from<BR>the plant Ipomœa Turpethum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवृष्ण
त्रैवृष्ण, अस्, m. a patronymic of Try-aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवेदिक
त्रैवेदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-वेद), relating to<BR>the three Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैशङ्कव|त्रैशंकव|त्रैशंकवः|त्रैशङ्कवः
त्रैशङ्कव, अस्, m. (fr. त्रि-शङ्कु), a patro-<BR>nymic of Hari-ścandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैशाण
त्रैशाण, अस्, ई, अम्, = त्रिशाण, worth three Śāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैशाम्ब
त्रैशाम्ब, अस्, m., N. of the father of Karan-<BR>dhama; (various readings have त्रिभानु, त्रिशानु,<BR>त्रिशारि, त्रैसानु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैशीर्ष
त्रैशीर्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. त्रि-शीर्षन्), relating<BR>to the three-headed Viśva-rūpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैशोक
त्रैशोक, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-शोक), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैष्टुभ
त्रैष्टुभ, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or written<BR>in the metre Tri-ṣṭubh; (अम्), n. the Tri-ṣṭubh<BR>stanza or metre; (Sāy.) the atmosphere or inter-<BR>mediate region consisting of rain, clouds, and light-<BR>ning. (In the Brāhmaṇas the three chief metres<BR>Gāyatrī, Tri-ṣṭubh, and Jagatī are often identified<BR>with the sky, atmosphere, and earth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैसानु
त्रैसानु, उस्, m., N. of the father of Karan-<BR>dhama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैस्रोतस
त्रैस्रोतस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. त्रि-स्रोतस्), belonging<BR>to the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैस्वर्य|त्रैस्वर्य्य
त्रैस्वर्य, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-स्वर), the three<BR>accents collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैहायण
त्रैहायण, अम्, n. (fr. त्रि-हायण), Ved. a<BR>period or age of three years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रै
त्रै त्रै (by some modern scholars written<BR>त्रा, q. v.), cl. 1. A. त्रायते (3rd sing. Pres. ep.<BR>त्राति; 2nd sing. Impv. Ved. त्रास्व, ep. त्राहि, त्रातु),<BR>तत्रे, त्रास्यते (ep. त्रास्यति), अत्रास्त, त्रातुम्, to<BR>protect, preserve, cherish, defend, rescue from, (in<BR>the earlier language with abl. and gen., in the later<BR>only with abl.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राण|त्राणं
त्राण, त्रात, &c. For these and other deriva-<BR>tives of the rt. त्रै see 1. त्रा, p. 388, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुण्य|त्रैगुण्यं
त्रैगुण्य त्रैगुण्य, अम्, n. See p. 393, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटक|त्रोटकं|त्रोटकः
त्रोटक त्रोटक, अस्, m. [cf. तोटक], a kind<BR>of poisonous insect; N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya;<BR>(ई), f. a Rāgiṇī or one of the female personifications<BR>of music; (अम्), n. a minor drama, such as the<BR>Vikramorvaśī; angry speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटि|त्रोटिः
त्रोटि त्रोटि. See p. 393, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोतल
त्रोतल त्रोतल, अम्, n. f., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—त्रोतलोत्तर (˚ल-उत्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोत्र|त्रोत्रं
त्रोत्र त्रोत्र, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. त्रै<BR>above), a weapon, a goad; a kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रौक्
त्रौक् त्रौक्, cl. 1. A. त्रौकते, &c., to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यंश|त्र्यंशः
त्र्यंश त्र्य्-अंश. For compounds with त्र्य्<BR>for त्रि see under त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्व|त्वं|त्वः
त्व 1. त्व, base of some cases of the second<BR>personal pronoun (in some of the cases the base is<BR>तु, Nom. sing. त्वम्, Acc. त्वा and त्वाम्, Abl.<BR>त्वत् or त्वद्; in Ved. त्वा occurs for त्वया,<BR>तुभ्य for तुभ्यम्, त्वे for त्वयि; at the be-<BR>ginning of a compound त्वत् or त्वद्, and in the<BR>Vedas त्वा is used), thou, you; [cf. Lat. tu; Lith.<BR>tù; Hib. tu; Goth. thu; Slav. ty; Gr. τούν, τύ,<BR>σύ.]<BR>—त्वङ्-कार, अस्, m. the expression ‘thou,’<BR>addressing with ‘thou’ (disrespectfully).<BR>—त्वङ्-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to address with<BR>‘thou.’<BR>—त्वत्-क, अस्, आ, अम् (a familiar diminu-<BR>tive), thine, your.<BR>—त्वत्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>or composed by thee; made like you.<BR>—त्वत्-तन,<BR>‘your sphere or department,’ you.<BR>—त्वत्-सङ्गम,<BR>अस्, m. union with thee.<BR>—त्वद्-अन्य, अस्, आ, अत्,<BR>other than thee.<BR>—त्वद्-अर्थम् or त्वद्-अर्थे,<BR>ind. on thy account, about thee, respecting thee.<BR>—त्वद्-गृह, अम्, n. thy house.<BR>—त्वद्-भ-<BR>य, अम्, n. dread of thee.<BR>—त्वद्-भू, cl. 1. P.<BR>-भवति, -वितुम्, to become thou, to become like<BR>you.<BR>—त्वद्-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. produced or pro-<BR>ceeding from thee.<BR>—त्वद्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, similar<BR>to thee, like thee, of thy kind.<BR>—त्वद्-वियोग, अस्,<BR>m. separation from thee.<BR>—त्वन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>produced from thee, consisting of thee.<BR>—त्व-यत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. given by thee.<BR>—त्वाङ्-काम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. longing for thee.<BR>—त्वा-दत्त or त्वा-<BR>दात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. given by thee; (Sāy. त्वा-<BR>दात, purified by thee.)<BR>—त्वा-दूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having thee as a messenger.<BR>—त्वा-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, or<BR>त्वा-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, similar to thee, one of thy kind.<BR>—त्वा-निद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. blaming thee.<BR>—त्वा-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. similar to thee; as rich, mighty,<BR>great, &c., as you; worthy of thee.<BR>—त्वा-वसु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. having thee as a possession; (Sāy.)<BR>having thee as a pervading attribute.<BR>—त्वा-वृध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having thee as patron, favoured by<BR>thee.<BR>—त्वेषित, अस्, आ, अम् (त्व or त्वा+इषित),<BR>Ved. sent by thee.<BR>—त्वोत, अस्, आ, अम् (त्व or त्वा<BR>+ ऊत), Ved. helped or protected or loved by thee.<BR>—त्वोति, इस्, इस्, इ (त्व or त्वा + ऊति), Ved. enjoying<BR>thy protection or help or love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्व|त्वं|त्वः
2. त्व, अस्, आ, m. f. thy, your, yours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वकत्
त्वकत्, a familiar diminutive from त्वद्, e. g. in<BR>त्वकत्-पितृक; [cf. त्वत्-क above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वदीय|त्वदीयं
त्वदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, thine, your, yours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वद्रिक्
त्वद्रिक्, ind. towards thee, directed towards thee;<BR>(Sāy. = त्वद्-अभिमुख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वायत्|त्वायन्त्
त्वायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (part. fr. a nom. derived fr. 1.<BR>त्व), Ved. longing for thee, seeking thee, loving thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाया
त्वाया (fr. the same nom.; used as an inst.), Ved.,<BR>out of love towards thee, for thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वायु
त्वायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. longing for thee, loving thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्व|त्वं|त्वः
त्व 3. त्व, अस्, आ, अत्, Ved. pron. one, several,<BR>other, different; त्व — त्व, one — the other; त्वद्,<BR>ind. partly; त्वद् — त्वद्, partly — partly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्ष्
त्वक्ष् त्वक्ष्, cl. 1. P. त्वक्षति, तत्व-<BR>क्ष, त्वक्षितुम् and त्वष्टुम्, to<BR>create, produce, generate, effect, to work (Ved.); to<BR>pare, make thin, peel, skin; to cover; [cf. rt. तक्ष्,<BR>तक्मन्, तोक: Zend thwakhsh, tash, ‘to cut;’<BR>tasha, ‘a hatchet;’ tas-ta, ‘a cup, bowl;’ tuc, ‘to<BR>produce, create:’ Gr. τεκ, ἔ-τεκ-ον, τίκ-τ-ω, τοκ-<BR>εύ-ς, τόκ-ος, τέκ-μαρ, τεκμήρ-ιο-ν, Τέκμησσα,<BR>τόξο-ν, τόσσαις, τέχ-νη, τέκ-τ-ων, τυκ, τυχ,<BR>τυγχάν-ω, ἔ-τυχ-ο-ν, τύχ-η, τεύχ-ω, τε-τύκ-οντο,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">Page0394-c+ 79</a>]<BR>τύκ-ο-ς, Τεῦκ-ρο-ς: Lat. tig-nu-m, tē-lu-m, tē-mo,<BR>tex-o, tex-tor, tex-tura, tē-la: Goth. theik-an,<BR>‘to thrive:’ Old Sax. thigg-yu: Old Germ. dig-yu,<BR>‘I obtain;’ deh-s-a, ‘a mattock, trowel;’ deh-<BR>sen, ‘to break flax;’ dihsel, ‘a shaft:’ Lith. tek-<BR>ý-s, ‘a ram;’ tenk-ù, ‘to fall to one's share;’ tink-ù,<BR>‘to be fit;’ tinka-s, ‘it happens;’ tik-ra-s, ‘right,<BR>orderly;’ tiký-ti, ‘to take aim;’ taszý-ti, ‘to cut<BR>timber;’ taisy-ti, ‘to prepare:’ Slav. tŭk-ña-ti, ‘to<BR>fix;’ tŭk-a-ti, ‘to weave;’ tes-a-ti, ‘to cut;’ te†z-<BR>a-ti, ‘to obtain:’ Boh. tesar, ‘a smith.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्षस्
त्वक्षस्, अस्, n., Ved. efficiency, energy, vigour;<BR>(Sāy.) foe-destroying might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्षीयस्
त्वक्षीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. very vigorous, very<BR>invigorating; [cf. Zend thwakhshista.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्ट|त्वष्टः
त्वष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, pared, peeled, made thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टि|त्वष्टिः
त्वष्टि, इस्, f. carpentry, the profession of a<BR>carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टृ
त्वष्टृ, टा, m. a carpenter, builder, workman,<BR>maker of carriages, &c. [cf. तष्टृ]; N. of a god,<BR>sometimes identified with the later deity Viśva-<BR>karman, (he is the builder and architect κατ᾽ ἐξοχήν<BR>and the Vulcan of the Hindūs; hence in the Veda he<BR>has the epithets सु-पाणि, सु-गभस्ति, स्व्-अपस्, सु-<BR>कृत्, विश्व-रूप, पुरु-रूप, &c.: he makes the<BR>various implements of the gods, especially the<BR>thunderbolt of Indra, and is said to have taught the<BR>Ṛbhus who are also skilful workmen: he is some-<BR>times regarded as the creator himself, and as forming<BR>the bodies of men and animals is invoked for the<BR>sake of offspring, especially in the Āprī hymns;<BR>elsewhere he is associated with other similar deities,<BR>e. g. Dhātṛ, Savitṛ, Prajā-pati, and Pūṣan; as<BR>Indra is accompanied by the Vasus, Rudra by the<BR>Rudras, so Tvaṣṭṛ is surrounded by the divine<BR>females called Gnās, Janayas, Devānām Patnyaḥ, who<BR>may be regarded as the recipients of his generative<BR>energy; he has a son Viśva-rūpa or Tri-śiras, a<BR>daughter Saraṇyū (or Sureṇu, Svareṇu, Sañjñā), wife<BR>of Vivasvat, the children of whom are the Aśvins,<BR>and Vāyu is called his son-in-law: Indra overpowers<BR>Tvaṣṭṛ and recovers the Soma, which, according to<BR>the Brāhmaṇas, was concealed by the latter because<BR>Indra had killed his son Viśva-rūpa: Tvaṣṭṛ is<BR>the deity of the Nakṣatra Citrā, regent of the fifth<BR>Yuga or of the fifth cycle of Jupiter; and is also a<BR>form of the sun, the N. being derived by Yāska in<BR>Nirukta VIII. 13. fr. the rt. त्विष्, ‘to shine,’ and<BR>being applied in Ṛg-veda 1. 84, 15, to one of<BR>the Ādityas; it is also in the sense ‘shining,’<BR>‘brilliant,’ applied to Agni and to Vāyu as well as to<BR>the Rudras); N. of a prince, a son of Manasyu<BR>(Bhauvana).<BR>—त्वष्टृ-मत् or त्वष्टी-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. connected with or accompanied by Tvaṣṭṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाष्टी
त्वाष्टी, f. (? for त्वाष्टॄ), N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाष्ट्र|त्वाष्ट्रः
त्वाष्ट्र, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or coming<BR>from Tvaṣṭṛ; (with युग) the fifth Jupiter cycle,<BR>the regent of which is Tvaṣṭṛ; (with पुत्र) the<BR>son of Tvaṣṭṛ; (अस्), m. the son of Tvaṣṭṛ, i. e.<BR>Viśva-rūpa (also identified with Vṛtra), and Ābhūti;<BR>(ई), f. the daughter of Tvaṣṭṛ, patronymic of<BR>Saraṇyū (or Sureṇu, Svareṇu, Sañjñā), who was wife<BR>of Vivasvat; the asterism Citrā, the regent of which<BR>is Tvaṣṭṛ; a small car; त्वाष्ट्र्यस्, f. pl. the<BR>daughters of Tvaṣṭṝ, certain divine female beings;<BR>(अम्), n. the power or energy of Tvaṣṭṛ, creative<BR>power; (with भ or नक्षत्र) the asterism<BR>Citrā [cf. त्वष्टृ]; a kind of eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगेल
त्वगेल त्वगेल, अम्, n. probably = एलवालु,<BR>the bark of Feronia Elephantum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वङ्ग्|त्वंग्
त्वङ्ग् त्वङ्ग्, cl. 1. P. त्वङ्गति, &c., to<BR>go, move, tremble, wave; to jump, leap,<BR>gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच्
त्वच् 1. त्वच्, cl. 6. P. त्वचति, &c., to<BR>cover, (a root artificially formed to furnish<BR>an etymology for 2. त्वच्); [cf. Lat. tego; Old Germ.<BR>dekiu, ‘to cover;’ Lith. dengiù.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्क
त्वक्क at end of adj. comp., e. g. सान्द्र-त्वक्क,<BR>covered with thick armour-like skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0394-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच्
2. त्वच्, क्, f. skin (as of men, serpents, &c.); hide<BR>(as of a goat, cow, &c.); a cow's hide (used in<BR>pressing out the Soma); bark, rind, peel; any<BR>surface or covering (as turf of the earth); a cover,<BR>horse-cloth; (Ved.) the black cover, = darkness; a<BR>protecting cover or guard, mail, a shield; a leather<BR>bag; Cassia bark; cinnamon, the cinnamon tree;<BR>mystical N. of the letter य.<BR>—त्वक्-कण्डुर, अस्,<BR>m. skin-wound, a sore.<BR>—त्वक्-क्षीरा, ई, f. manna<BR>of bamboo (commonly Tabāṣīr); [cf. तवक्षीर.]<BR>—त्वक्-छद, अस्, m. the grass Lipeocercis Serrata.<BR>—त्वक्-छेद, अस्, m. a skin-wound, flesh-wound,<BR>cut, scratch; circumcision.<BR>—त्वक्-छेदन, अम्, n.<BR>cutting the skin; see त्वक्-छेद.<BR>—त्वक्-तरङ्-<BR>गक, अस्, m. ‘skin-wave,’ a wrinkle.<BR>—त्वक्-त्र,<BR>अम्, n. ‘protection for the skin,’ armour.<BR>—त्वक्-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. Cassia (the plant and bark); (ई), f. =<BR>कारवी, हिङ्गु-पत्त्री, the leaf of the Asa Fœtida (?),<BR>= तमाल-पत्त्र, the leaf of the Laurus Cassia,<BR>Malabathron.<BR>—त्वक्-परिपुटन, अम्, n. peeling<BR>of the skin, desquamation.<BR>—त्वक्-पाक, अस्, m.<BR>inflammation of the skin, N. of a particular disease.<BR>—त्वक्-पारुष्य, अम्, n. roughness of the skin.<BR>—त्वक्-पुष्प, अम्, n. ‘skin-sprout,’ erection of<BR>the hairs of the skin, horripilation; (अम्, ई), n. f.<BR>blotch, scab, cutaneous eruption, &c.<BR>—त्वक्-पुष्-<BR>पिका, f. scab, blotch.<BR>—त्वक्-सार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having an excellent or sound skin; (अस्), m. a<BR>bamboo; Cassia (the plant and the bark); Bignonia<BR>Indica; (आ), f. Tabāṣīr; [cf. त्वक्-क्षीरा.]<BR>—त्वक्-<BR>सार-भेदिनी, f. a kind of plant, = क्षुद्र-चञ्चु.<BR>—त्वक्-सुगन्ध, अस्, m. an orange (‘having<BR>fragrant peel’); (आ), f. the fragrant bark of Fe-<BR>ronia Elephantum (= एलवालुक).<BR>—त्वक्-स्वाद्वी,<BR>f. a kind of cinnamon (‘having sweet bark’).<BR>—त्वग्-अङ्कुर, अस्, m. = त्वक्-पुष्प above.<BR>—त्वग्-अस्थि-मात्र-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, with mere<BR>skin and bone left, reduced to a skeleton.<BR>—त्वगा-<BR>क्षीरी, f. = तुगा-क्षीरी, = त्वक्-क्षीरा, ई.<BR>—त्वग्-<BR>इन्द्रिय, अम्, n. the sense or organ of touch.<BR>—त्वग्-गन्ध, अस्, m. an orange; [cf. त्वक्-<BR>सुगन्ध.]<BR>—त्वग्-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced on or<BR>issuing from the skin; (अम्), n. the hairs on the<BR>body; blood.<BR>—त्वग्-दोष, अस्, m. disease of the<BR>skin, leprosy.<BR>—त्वग्-दोषापहा (˚ष-अपहा),<BR>f. Vernonia Anthelminthica (‘destroying leprosy’).<BR>—त्वग्-दोषारि (˚ष-अरि), इस्, m. a kind of<BR>bulbous plant (‘the enemy of leprosy’), = हस्ति-<BR>कन्द.<BR>—त्वग्दोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, affected with skin<BR>disease or with leprosy.<BR>—त्वग्-भेद, अस्, m.<BR>‘breaking of the skin,’ a flesh-wound, a scratch.<BR>—त्वग्-भेदक, अस्, m. one who cuts the skin, a<BR>stabber, scratcher, one who draws blood from the<BR>skin.<BR>—त्वग्-रोग, अस्, m. any cutaneous disease;<BR>leprosy &c.<BR>—त्वग्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with<BR>skin or bark.<BR>—त्वङ्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>bark or skin.<BR>—त्वङ्-मल, अम्, n. the hairs of the<BR>body.<BR>—त्वचि-सार, अस्, m. (त्वचि loc. of 2. त्वच्), =<BR>त्वक्-सार, a bamboo.<BR>—त्वचि-सुगन्धा, f. small<BR>cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच|त्वचं
त्वच at the end of a comp. = 2. त्वच्; cf. स-त्˚,<BR>सूर्य-त्˚, हिरन्य-त्˚; (अम्), n. skin; bark, rind;<BR>cinnamon, the cinnamon tree, Cassia bark; (आ), f.<BR>skin; [cf. गुड-त्वच and तनु-त्वचा.]<BR>—त्वचा-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. = त्वक्-पत्त्र, Cassia bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचन|त्वचनं
त्वचन, अम्, n. covering with a skin or hide;<BR>skinning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचय
त्वचय, nom. P. त्वचयति, &c., to cover with a<BR>skin or hide; to tear off the skin, to skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचस्य
त्वचस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिष्ठ|त्वचिष्ठः
त्वचिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of त्वग्-वत्, Pāṇ.<BR>V. 3, 65), having the best skin, having an excellent<BR>skin; bark &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिसार|त्वचिसारः
त्वचि-सार. See under 2. त्वच् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचीयस्
त्वचीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of त्वग्-वत्, Pāṇ.<BR>V. 3, 65), having a more excellent or an excellent<BR>skin; bark &c.; [cf. त्वचिष्ठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच्य
त्वच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, conducive to the healthiness<BR>of the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाच
त्वाच, अस्, ई, अम्, cuticular, relating to the skin,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">Page0395-b+ 76</a>]<BR>contagious, derived from touch.<BR>—त्वाच-प्रत्य-<BR>क्ष, अम्, n. ascertainment of objects by contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वञ्च्
त्वञ्च् त्वञ्च् = तञ्च्, cl. 1. P. त्वञ्चति, &c.,<BR>to go, move; cl. 7. P. त्वनक्ति, &c., to<BR>contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वत्
त्वत् त्वत् or (according to the proper form<BR>of the base) त्वद्. See 1. त्व, p. 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वर्
त्वर् त्वर्, cl. 1. A. त्वरते (ep. also P.<BR>त्वरति), तत्वरे, त्वरितुम्, to hurry, make<BR>haste, go or move with speed, do anything quickly or<BR>precipitately: Caus. त्वरयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अतत्व-<BR>रत्, to cause to hasten, quicken, urge forward,<BR>accelerate: Desid. तित्वरिषति: Intens. तात्वर्यते,<BR>तोतूर्ति; [cf. तुर्, तॄ: Gr. θόρνυμι, θοῦρος, θρύσκω;<BR>perhaps ἀ-θύρω, τύρβη, θόρυβος: Lat. turba: per-<BR>haps Angl. Sax. a-thwerian, ‘to move, shake:’ Hib.<BR>tuairim, ‘to go round, move in a circle.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्ण|तूर्णं|तूर्ण्ण
तूर्ण = त्वरित. See p. 381, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरण|त्वरणं
त्वरण, अस्, आ, अम्, making haste; (अम्), n.<BR>making haste, speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरणीय
त्वरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be hastened or acce-<BR>lerated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरा
त्वरा, f. haste, speed, velocity.<BR>—त्वरान्वित<BR>(˚रा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of haste, swift, quick.<BR>—त्वरा-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, hasty, impetuous, quick,<BR>expeditious.<BR>—त्वरारोह (˚रा-आर्˚), अस्, m. a pigeon<BR>(‘ascending quickly’).<BR>—त्वरा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>quick, expeditious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरायस्य
त्वरायस्य, nom. P. त्वरायस्यति, &c., to make<BR>haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरि|त्वरिः
त्वरि, इस्, f. haste, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरित|त्वरितं
त्वरित, अस्, आ, अम्, hastening, quick, swift,<BR>speedy, expeditious; (अम्), n. despatch, haste;<BR>(अम्), ind. quickly, swiftly; hastily, in haste, fast,<BR>speedily; (आ), f. a form of Durgā; a magical formula<BR>called after her.<BR>—त्वरित-गति, इस्, f. swift motion;<BR>a species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>—त्वरित-प्रयोग,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—त्वरिता-<BR>मन्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Śāradā-<BR>tilaka.<BR>—त्वरिता-यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a mystical<BR>diagram.<BR>—त्वरितोदित (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, spoken<BR>quickly, uttered rapidly, hurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरितक
त्वरितक, अस्, आ, m. f. a sort of rice ripening<BR>before the usual time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरायण
त्वरायण त्वरायण, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. (a<BR>various reading for परायण), adherence, attach-<BR>ment; (according to some only अम्, n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्ट|त्वष्टः
त्वष्ट त्वष्ट, त्वष्टृ, &c. See under rt.<BR>त्वक्ष्, p. 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाच
त्वाच त्वाच. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वादृश्
त्वादृश् त्वा-दृश्. See 1. त्व, p. 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वायत्|त्वायन्त्
त्वायत् त्वायत्. See under 1. त्व, p. 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
त्विष् 1. त्विष्, cl. 1. P. A. त्वेषति, -ते,<BR>तित्वेष, तित्विषे (part. तित्विषाण),<BR>त्वेक्ष्यति, -ते, अत्विक्षत्, अत्विक्षत (Ved. forms<BR>अत्विषुस्, अत्विषन्त, अतित्विषन्त), त्वेष्टुम्,<BR>Ved. inf. त्विषे, to be violently agitated or moved;<BR>to be excited; to be troubled or perplexed; to ex-<BR>cite, instigate; to shine, glitter, sparkle; to be<BR>brilliant, to blaze: Caus. त्वेषयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अतित्विषत्: Desid. तित्विक्षति, -ते: Intens. तेत्वि-<BR>ष्यते, तेत्वेष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
2. त्विष्, ट्, f. violent agitation or quivering motion<BR>of any kind, vehemence, violence, fury, perplexity;<BR>light, brilliance, glitter, any shining colour, splendor,<BR>beauty; authority, weight, consideration; speech;<BR>wish, desire; custom, practice, usage; [cf. अचल-त्˚<BR>and वात-त्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषा
त्विषा, f. light, splendor; N. of a daughter of<BR>Kaśyapa.<BR>—त्विषाम्-ईश, अस्, or त्विषाम्-पति, इस्,<BR>m. ‘the lord of rays,’ the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषि|त्विषिः
त्विषि, इस्, f., Ved. vehemence, impetuousity,<BR>energy, internal power; (Sāy.) splendor, light, ray,<BR>brilliancy, beauty.<BR>—त्विषि-मत् and (Ved.) त्विषी-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, vehemently excited, vehement,<BR>energetic; brilliant, beautiful, N. of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेष
त्वेष, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. vehement, impetuous;<BR>inspiring awe, causing fear, awful; (Sāy.) brilliant,<BR>bright, glittering, epithet of Rudra and the Maruts,<BR>shining.<BR>—त्वेष-द्युम्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>vehement energy, impetuous; (Sāy.) possessed of<BR>brilliant reputation.<BR>—त्वेष-नृम्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having impetuous energy or courage; (Sāy.)<BR>of brilliant power.<BR>—त्वेष-प्रतीक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having a brilliant appearance, having an awful aspect,<BR>having the aspect of great power; (Sāy.) bright-<BR>pointed (as a shaft).<BR>—त्वेष-याम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. impetuous in course, rushing impetuously;<BR>(Sāy.) ‘having a brilliant course,’ epithet of the<BR>Maruts.<BR>—त्वेष-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>rushing chariots; (Sāy.) having brilliant chariots.<BR>—त्वेष-सन्दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. of a splendid<BR>aspect, similar to flame; ‘looking awful,’ epithet of<BR>the Maruts, of Indra, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषथ
त्वेषथ, अस्, m., Ved. fury, violence; (Sāy.)<BR>radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषस्
त्वेषस्, अस्, n., Ved. force, energy, impulse;<BR>(Sāy.) brilliant energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेष्य
त्वेष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, agitating, terrifying, awful,<BR>inspiring awe, any terrible object; (Sāy.) shining,<BR>brilliant, epithet of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वैषीरथि
त्वैषीरथि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Kuśika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वोत
त्वोत त्वोत, त्वोति. See 1. त्व, p. 394.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सर्
त्सर् त्सर्, cl. 1. P. त्सरति, तत्सार, त्सरि-<BR>ष्यति, अत्सारीत् and अत्सार्, त्सरितुम्, Ved.<BR>to go or approach stealthily, to creep, crawl, creep<BR>on, steal upon, sneak, to obtain by sneaking; to<BR>proceed crookedly or fraudulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरु|त्सरुः
त्सरु, उस्, m. any creeping or crawling animal or<BR>a particular animal of this kind; the stalk of a leaf<BR>&c.; the hilt or handle of a sword and similar<BR>weapons.<BR>—त्सरु-मार्ग, अस्, m. sword-exercise,<BR>sword-fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सारिन्
त्सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. creeping, sneaking, ap-<BR>proaching stealthily or secretly; crooked; (Sāy.)<BR>very fearful, very much alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सारुक
त्सारुक, अस्, आ, अम्, skilful in handling a sword,<BR>skilled in sword-exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ 1. थ, the second consonant of the<BR>dental class and the aspirate of the preceding letter,<BR>having much the sound of थ् in अन्त्-हिल्ल्, but more<BR>dental.<BR>—थ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
2. थ, अस्, m. a mountain; a protector, preserver;<BR>a sign of danger; a kind of disease; eating; (अम्),<BR>n. preserving, preservation; fear, terror; auspicious-<BR>ness; a prayer for the welfare of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थक्कन
थक्कन थक्कन, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(also read ढक्कन and ढक्कम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थक्कियक
थक्कियक थक्कियक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थक्रिय
थक्रिय थक्रिय, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थर्व्
थर्व् थर्व् (said to be = rt. चर्), cl. 1. P.<BR>थर्वति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थल्योरक
थल्योरक थल्योरक, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुड्
थुड् थुड्, cl. 6. P. थुडति, &c., to cover,<BR>screen; to clothe; to hide; [cf. rt. स्थुड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थोडन|थोडनं
थोडन, अम्, n. covering, clothing, wrapping up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुत्कार|थुत्कारः
थुत्कार थुत्-कार, अस्, m. the making of<BR>the sound थुत्, the sound made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुत्थु
थुत्थु थुत्थु (an onomatopoetic word),<BR>the sound heard in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुथुकृत्
थुथु-कृत्, त्, m. the making the imitative<BR>sound थुथु; a kind of bird (= Marāṭhī होला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुर्व्
थुर्व् थुर्व्, cl. 1. P. थूर्वति, तुथूर्व,<BR>&c., to hurt, injure; [cf. rt. तुर्व्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थूत्कार|थूत्कारः
थूत्कार थूत्-कार, अस्, m. the making of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">Page0396-a+ 73</a>]<BR>the sound थूत्, the sound made in spitting; [cf.<BR>थुत्-कार.]<BR>—थूत्-कृत, अम्, n. the sound थूत्<BR>made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0395-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थूथू
थूथू थूथू, imitative sound of spitting;<BR>(according to others थुथु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थैथै
थैथै थैथै, imitative sound of a musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द 1. द, the eighteenth consonant of the<BR>alphabet and the third letter of the fourth or dental<BR>class, the sound of which is more dental than the<BR>English द्.<BR>—द-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द 2. द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. दा, to give),<BR>giving, a giver, donor; presenting, favouring with,<BR>granting, a granter; causing, (often at the end of<BR>comp., e. g. वारि-द, giving water; अन्न-द,<BR>granting food &c.; exceptionally compounded with<BR>the receiver of the gift, e. g. पितृ-द, giving to the<BR>father); (अस्), m. a gift, anything given; (अम्, आ),<BR>n. f. a gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द 3. द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. दा for दो, to<BR>cut), cutting off, destroying, breaking, &c., (generally<BR>at the end of comp.); (अस्, आ), m. f. the act of cutting<BR>off, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द 4. द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 4. दा, to bind),<BR>binding, (generally at the end of comp.; cf. ऋश्य-<BR>द.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द 5. द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 7. दा, to purify),<BR>cleaning, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द 6. द, अस्, m. a mountain; (आ), f. heat,<BR>pain, repentance; (अम्), n. a wife; [cf. दम्-पती.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
दंश् 1. दंश्, cl. 1. 10. P. दंशति, दंश-<BR>यति, &c., to speak or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
दंश् 2. दंश्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) द-<BR>शति, -ते, ददंश, दङ्क्ष्यति (ep. also<BR>दंशिष्यति), अदाङ्क्षीत्, दंष्टुम्, to bite, sting;<BR>to see [? cf. rt. दंस्]: Caus. P. दंशयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अददङ्क्षत्, to cause to bite; to bite: Desid.<BR>दिदङ्क्षति: Intens. दन्दश्यते, दन्दंष्टि,<BR>दन्दष्टि: Caus. of Intens. दन्दशयति, to cause<BR>to bite violently; [cf. Gr. δάκνω, δάκος, ὀδαγμός,<BR>ὀδάζω, ὀδακτάζω, ὀδαξέω, &c., δάκρυ; Lat. la-<BR>cruma, perhaps lacero; Goth. tahyan, ‘dilacerate,’<BR>tagr; Angl. Sax. taeher, tux, tusk, tang; Old Germ.<BR>zanga, zangar; Cambro-Brit. danhezu, ‘to bite;’<BR>Hib. dan-t, ‘a morsel, portion, share;’ Russ. desnà,<BR>‘ginger.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश, अस्, m. biting, stinging; cutting, dividing,<BR>tearing; the sting of a snake; a bite, the spot bitten;<BR>pungency; fault, defect (in a jewel &c.); a tooth; a<BR>gad-fly; armour, a coat of mail; a joint, limb; N. of<BR>an Asura; (ई), f. a small gad-fly; [cf. क्षमा-द्˚ and वृ-<BR>ष-द्˚.]<BR>—दंश-नाशिनी, f. (‘healing irritation of the<BR>skin ?’), a kind of insect, = तैल-कीट; [cf. दर्द्रु-<BR>नाशिनी.]<BR>—दंश-भीरु, उस्, m. or दंश-भीरुक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘afraid of the gad-fly,’ a buffalo.<BR>—दंश-मूल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a pungent root,’ the plant Hyperanthera<BR>Moringa or a sort of horse-radish, = शिग्रु.<BR>—दंश-<BR>वदन, अस्, m. ‘having a sharp beak,’ a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशक|दंशकः
दंशक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, biting, stinging;<BR>(अस्), m. a dog; gad-fly, common fly; N. of a<BR>prince of Kampana; (इका), f. a kind of gad-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन, अम्, n. the act of biting, stinging;<BR>armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित, अस्, आ, अम्, bitten, stung; (fr. दंश),<BR>armed, mailed; protected; fitting closely (like armour),<BR>standing closely together, crowded; (अम्), n. a bite;<BR>[cf. परि-दंशित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशिन्
दंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, biting, stinging [cf. तृप्र-<BR>दंशिन्]; (ई), m. a dog; a gad-fly, a wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशुक
दंशुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. biting, stinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशेर
दंशेर, अस्, आ, अम् (more correctly दशेर,<BR>q. v.), biting, mordacious; noxious, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्मन्
दंश्मन्, अ, n., Ved. a bite; the place bitten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्टृ
दंष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, Ved. a biter, biting, stinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्र
दंष्ट्र, अस्, आ, m. f. (in the later language<BR>usually f.), a large tooth, tusk, fang, (often at the<BR>end of comp.; cf. अयो-द्˚, अष्ट-द्˚, तीक्ष्ण-द्˚,<BR>&c.)<BR>—दंष्ट्रा-कराल, अस्, आ, अम्, having terrible<BR>tusks.<BR>—दंष्ट्रा-निवासिन्, ई, m., N. of a Yakṣas.<BR>—दंष्ट्रायुध (˚रा-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, using<BR>tusks as weapons; (अस्), m. a wild boar.<BR>—दंष्-<BR>ट्रा-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्राल
दंष्ट्राल, अस्, आ, अम्, tusked, having large<BR>tusks; (अस्), m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिक
दंष्ट्रिक, अस्, आ, अम्, tusked, having tusks;<BR>(आ), f. = दाढिका, a beard (?); a kind of plant; [cf.<BR>नकुलेष्टा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, tusked, having tusks or<BR>large teeth; biting or wounding with the teeth;<BR>carnivorous; (ई), m. any animal with tusks; a wild<BR>boar; a hyena; a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्वा
दंष्ट्वा, ind. having bitten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दष्ट
दष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, bitten, &c. See p. 406, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंस्
दंस् दंस् (connected with rt. दस्, q. v.;<BR>perhaps only a various reading for rt. 1. and<BR>2. दंश्, col. 1, or a Prākṛt form of rt. 1. दृश्), cl.<BR>1. P. 10. A. दंसति, दंसयते or दासयते, &c.,<BR>to bite; to destroy, overpower; to see, (दंसति ?);<BR>cl. 10. P. दंसयति, &c., to speak or to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसन|दंसनं
दंसन, अम्, आ, n. f. (Ved. inst. दंसना),<BR>a surprising or wonderful deed or operation, mar-<BR>vellous power; an action, work, deed; armour,<BR>mail, (in the latter meaning only a various reading<BR>for दंशन); [cf. दस्म and दस्र.]<BR>—दं-<BR>सना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having wonderful power;<BR>(Sāy.) abounding in marvellous deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसयितृ
दंसयितृ, ता, m. a destroyer, (a word formed<BR>to explain दस्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसस्
दंसस्, अस्, n., Ved. = दंसन, a surprising<BR>action or deed (applied especially to the wonderful<BR>actions of the Aśvins, by which these deities pro-<BR>tected their human friends); [cf. पुरु-द्˚ and सु-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसि|दंसिः
दंसि, इस्, m. f. (?), Ved. = कर्मन्, act, deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसिष्ठ
दंसिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of दंसु or द-<BR>स्र), Ved. of very wonderful strength, performing<BR>marvellous deeds, eminent in action, epithet of the<BR>Aśvins and of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसु
दंसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. of wonderful strength;<BR>(according to Sāy., loc. of दम् = दंसेषु or कर्-<BR>म-वत्सु); (उ), ind. in a wonderful way, wonder-<BR>fully.<BR>—दंसु-जूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wonderfully<BR>quick; (Sāy.) borne along by well-trained horses (as<BR>if fr. rt. 1. दम्).<BR>—दंसु-पत्नी, f., Ved. having a<BR>powerful lord or master; (Sāy.) having the Asuras<BR>as good masters (as if fr. दम् + सु + पत्नी, सु =<BR>सुष्ठु); in Ṛg-veda VI. 3, 7, दम् is regarded<BR>as a separate word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंह्
दंह् दंह्, cl. 10. P. दंहयति, &c., to<BR>shine, burn; [cf. rt. 1. दह्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक|दकं
दक दक, अम्, n. = उदक (the initial vowel<BR>being dropped), water.<BR>—दक-लावणिक, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. दक+लवण), prepared with water and salt.<BR>—दकोदर (˚क-उद्˚), अम्, n. (instead of उद-<BR>कोदर, cf. उदकोदरिन्), a watery or dropsical belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष्
दक्ष् दक्ष्, cl. 1. P. A. दक्षति, -ते,<BR>ददक्ष, दक्षितुम्, Ved. to act to the<BR>satisfaction of another (with dat. in P.); to be<BR>competent, be able, be strong or powerful (A.); to<BR>grow, increase; to do or act quickly, go, move;<BR>to hurt, kill: Caus. P. दक्षयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अददक्षत्, to make able or strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, able, fit, competent, suitable,<BR>adroit, expert, clever, judicious, dexterous [cf. Gr.<BR>δεξιός]; intelligent, upright, honest; (अस्), m. epi-<BR>thet of Soma (as heightening or strengthening the<BR>intellectual faculties; according to Sāy. = वृद्ध);<BR>epithet of Śiva; epithet of the Ganges (as satisfying<BR>or suiting all); ability, power, fitness; capacity,<BR>intellectual ability, mental power, talent; strength of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-c" target="_blank">Page0396-c+ 81</a>]<BR>will, energy, will, disposition; (in the Veda दक्ष<BR>and क्रतु, i. e. energy and intelligence, are often<BR>joined together as the chief two faculties of the<BR>mind, cf. क्रतु); bad disposition, evil design; N.<BR>of an Āditya; a creative power associated with<BR>Aditi, and therefore sometimes identified with Prajā-<BR>pati; (his daughter is called Kṛttikā: in the Post-<BR>vedic literature Dakṣa is the subject of numerous<BR>legends, which relate his history differently; he is<BR>there generally called the son of Brahmā, and placed<BR>among the Prajā-patis or at their head as ‘the lord<BR>of all creatures,’ being born from Brahmā's right<BR>thumb, as his wife was from the left, see Manu IX.<BR>128: in other legends he is said to be the son of<BR>the ten Pra-cetasas or of Pra-cetas alone, whence his<BR>patronymic Prācetasa; he is variously stated to have<BR>had fifty, sixty, forty-four, and a less number of<BR>daughters, of whom twenty-seven became the wives<BR>of the Moon, forming the lunar asterisms, and thir-<BR>teen or, according to others, seventeen or only eight<BR>the wives of Kaśyapa, becoming by this latter the<BR>mothers of gods, demons, men, and animals: Dakṣa<BR>on one occasion celebrated a great sacrifice to obtain<BR>a son, but omitted to invite Śiva who, according to<BR>one legend, was his son-in-law, (Śiva's wife being Satī,<BR>a form of Durgā, daughter of Dakṣa); this irritated<BR>the god, who interrupted the sacrifice and decapitated<BR>his father-in-law, see दक्षाध्वर-ध्वंश-कृत्:<BR>Dakṣa is sometimes regarded as an Avatār of<BR>Brahmā himself, and is even in one legend identified<BR>with Viṣṇu); N. of a son of Garuḍa; N. of a man<BR>with the patronymic Pārvati; of a Muni and legis-<BR>lator; of a prince or a son of Uśīnara; of one of the<BR>five Brāhmans of Kānya-kubja, from whom the<BR>Brāhmans of Bengal are said to have sprung; (ac-<BR>cording to the lexicographers also) the bull of Śiva;<BR>a cock; a kind of plant; a name of Agni or fire;<BR>a general lover, one attached to many mistresses; (आ),<BR>f. the earth; [cf. अतूर्त-दक्ष, दीन-द्˚, &c.: cf. also<BR>दक्षिण; Gr. δεξιός, δεξιτερός; Lat. dex-ter, dex-<BR>timus; Goth. taihsvs; Angl. Sax. teso; Old Germ.<BR>zeso; Hib. deas, ‘right, southern.’]<BR>—दक्ष-कन्या,<BR>f. ‘daughter of Dakṣa,’ (especially) epithet of Durgā,<BR>the wife of Śiva.<BR>—दक्ष-क्रतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>having a strong will or intelligence, having a clear<BR>understanding.<BR>—दक्ष-जा, f. ‘daughter of Dakṣa,’<BR>the goddess Durgā; a lunar asterism; [cf. दक्ष.]<BR>—दक्षजा-पति, इस्, m. ‘the husband of the<BR>daughters of Dakṣa,’ an epithet of the Moon; also<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—दक्ष-ता, f. or दक्ष-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>dexterity, cleverness, ability.<BR>—दक्ष-ताति, इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. mental power or capacity.<BR>—दक्ष-निधन,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—दक्ष-पति, इस्, m., Ved.<BR>lord of the faculties, lord of power or might; pro-<BR>tector of the sacrifice.<BR>—दक्ष-पितृ, ता, त्री, तृ,<BR>Ved. having Dakṣa as father or progenitor, (the m.<BR>pl. may be either दक्ष-पितरस् or -पितारस्); pre-<BR>serving, possessing or granting abilities.<BR>—दक्ष-<BR>मख-मथन, अम्, n. ‘destruction of Dakṣa's<BR>sacrifice,’ N. of the ninety-seventh and ninety-eighth<BR>chapters of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—दक्ष-यज्ञ, अस्,<BR>m. the sacrifice celebrated by Dakṣa.<BR>—दक्ष-<BR>यज्ञ-भङ्ग, अस्, m. the interruption of Dakṣa's<BR>sacrifice.<BR>—दक्षयज्ञ-विध्वंस, अस्, m. ‘de-<BR>struction of Dakṣa's sacrifice,’ N. of the fifteenth<BR>chapter of the Kūrma-Purāṇa.<BR>—दक्षयज्ञ-वि-<BR>ध्वंसन, अम्, n., N. of the fifth chapter of the<BR>Śṛṣṭi-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—दक्षय-<BR>ज्ञ-विनाशिनी, f. ‘destroyer of the sacrifice of Dakṣa,’<BR>an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—दक्ष-विहिता, f. (scil. गा-<BR>था), a hymn or song arranged by Dakṣa.<BR>—द-<BR>क्ष-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. rejoicing in power or<BR>energy &c.<BR>—दक्ष-शाप, अस्, m. ‘the curse of<BR>Dakṣa,’ N. of the thirty-third chapter of the<BR>Svarga-khaṇḍa or third part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—दक्ष-साधन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. effective<BR>of energy, inspiring courage.<BR>—दक्ष-सावर्णि,<BR>इस्, m., N. of the ninth Manu.<BR>—दक्ष-सुत,<BR>अस्, m. the son of Dakṣa (?); (आ), f. a daughter<BR>of Dakṣa, a lunar asterism or one of the wives<BR>of the Moon.<BR>—दक्षाध्वर-ध्वंश-कृत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-a" target="_blank">Page0397-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(˚क्ष-अध्˚), त्, m. ‘disturber of the sacrifice of<BR>Dakṣa,’ a N. of Śiva; (Dakṣa having instituted<BR>a sacrifice to which he invited all the gods except<BR>his son-in-law Śiva and his wife Satī, the latter went<BR>unbid, and being received contemptuously, threw<BR>herself into the fire; upon which an emanation or<BR>incarnation of Śiva was produced, named Vīra-bha-<BR>dra, who attacked Dakṣa, and a general affray<BR>ensued in which the gods and Ṛṣis took the part<BR>of Dakṣa, but were wounded and dispersed: Dakṣa<BR>himself was decapitated, but was restored to life by<BR>Śiva at the prayer of the gods; the decapitated head,<BR>however, was not to be found, and the head of a ram<BR>had therefore to be substituted for the one lost.)<BR>—द-<BR>क्षेश्वर-लिङ्ग (˚क्ष-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0396-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षस्
दक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. = दक्ष, able, strong,<BR>dexterous, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाय्य|दक्षाय्यः
दक्षाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be satisfied or<BR>pleased; (Sāy.) increaser of all; to be honoured, to<BR>be augmented (by oblations); (अस्), m. a vulture;<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa or the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Pāṇ. I. 1,<BR>34, and VII. 1, 16, can only be declined as a<BR>pronominal when it denotes relative position, i. e.<BR>‘situated on the right hand’ or ‘southern,’ and<BR>even in this sense can be optionally declined like<BR>शिव in abl. loc. sing. m. n. and nom. voc. pl. m.;<BR>but दक्षिणायां दिशि, for the loc. f. in Hari-vaṃśa<BR>12390, is against the rule), able, competent, clever,<BR>skilful, dexterous [cf. दक्ष]; right (not left;<BR>probably applied to the right hand, foot, &c., as the<BR>cleverest or most skilful), situated on the right side,<BR>(opposed to सव्य, वाम; दक्षिणम् परी, to<BR>walk round a person with the right side towards<BR>him; दक्षिणं कृ, to place on the right side,<BR>to turn the right side towards a person as a mark of<BR>respect); south, southern (as being on the right side<BR>of a person looking towards the east), situated to<BR>the south, turned or directed southward, (दक्षिणा<BR>दिश्, the south, the southern quarter or point of the<BR>compass; दक्षिणस्यां दिशि, in the southern<BR>quarter; दक्षिण आम्नायस्, the southern sacred<BR>text, one of the holy texts of the Tāntrikas); straight-<BR>forward, candid, sincere, upright, honest, impartial;<BR>pleasing, amiable, compliant; submissive, dependent,<BR>subject; (अस्), m. the right (hand or arm); the<BR>right hand horse, the horse on the right side of the<BR>pole of a carriage; an epithet of Śiva; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. the right side; सव्यं दक्षिणम् एव च,<BR>to the left and to the right; the south, the country<BR>of the south, the Dekhan; (आ), f., scil. गो, a prolific<BR>cow, ‘able to calve and give milk,’ a good milch-<BR>cow; a present to Brāhmans or young virgins (con-<BR>sisting originally of a cow, and given upon solemn<BR>or sacrificial occasions); property so acquired [cf.<BR>Manu VIII. 349]; Donation to Brāhmans personified<BR>as a goddess, (generally mentioned together with<BR>Brahmaṇas-pati, Soma, Indra, &c., and said to be<BR>the authoress of Ṛg-veda X. 107; sometimes re-<BR>garded as a daughter of Prajā-pati, or as the wife of<BR>Sacrifice personified, or as born from Kṛṣṇa's right<BR>side, or as the wife of Ruci); wages or remunera-<BR>tion in general; a fee, gift, donation (e. g. प्राण-<BR>दक्षिणा, the gift of life); offering, oblation in<BR>general; completion of any rite, fixing or establish-<BR>ing any act or place; scil. दिश्, the south; the<BR>southern quarter, the southern point of the compass,<BR>the Dekhan; a form or figure of Durgā, in which<BR>the right side is said to be advanced; (अम्), n. the<BR>right hand or highest doctrine of the Śāktas; द-<BR>क्षिणा or दक्षिणेन, ind. on the right, on the<BR>right side of (with acc. and gen.); on the south,<BR>southward; दक्षिणेन कृ, to place on the right,<BR>to leave on the right; दक्षिणात्, ind. on the<BR>right, from the south, southward; दक्षिणे, ind.<BR>on the right, on the south, southward; [cf. Lith.<BR>dészinê, f. ‘the right hand,’ = perhaps Russ. yug,<BR>‘south;’ yuṣnyĭ, ‘southern.’]<BR>—दक्षिण-कालिका,<BR>f. a form of Durgā worshipped by the Tāntrikas.<BR>—दक्षिण-तस्, ind. from the right, to the right<BR>hand; from the south, southward, southerly; द-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-b" target="_blank">Page0397-b+ 81</a>]<BR>क्षिणतः कृ, to turn the right side towards a<BR>person (as a mark of respect); to stand on the<BR>right side of any one and so assist him; दक्षिण-<BR>तः पुरस्तात् or दक्षिणतः पुरः, to the south-<BR>east, on the south-east.<BR>—दक्षिणतस्-कपर्द or<BR>दक्षिणा-कपर्द, आस्, m. pl., Ved. ‘wearing the<BR>hair knotted or braided on the right side of the<BR>head,’ epithet of the Vasiṣṭhas.<BR>—दक्षिण-त्रा,<BR>ind., Ved. on the right side.<BR>—दक्षिण-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. uprightness, honesty.<BR>—दक्षिण-धुरीण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, harnessed on the right side of the pole of a<BR>carriage.<BR>—दक्षिण-पथ, a wrong reading for<BR>दक्षिणा-पथ, q. v.<BR>—दक्षिण-पश्चात्, ind. to<BR>the south-west, on the south-west.<BR>—दक्षिण-<BR>पश्चार्ध (˚च-अर्˚), अस्, m. the south-western side.<BR>—दक्षिण-पश्चिम, अस्, आ, अम्, south-western.<BR>—दक्षिण-पाञ्चालक, अस्, इका, अम्, relating to<BR>the southern Pañcālas.<BR>—दक्षिण-पूर्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, south-eastern; (आ), f., scil. दिश्, the south-east<BR>quarter; (एण), ind. to the south-east of (with acc.).<BR>—दक्षिण-प्राञ्च्, आङ्, आची, आक्, south-eastern; द-<BR>क्षिण-प्राची, f. the south-east quarter.<BR>—दक्षिण-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. the southern hemisphere.<BR>—दक्षि-<BR>ण-मानस, N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—दक्षि-<BR>ण-मारुत, अस्, m. the south wind.<BR>—दक्षिण-<BR>सद् or दक्षिणा-सद्, त्, त्, त्, sitting or remaining<BR>seated on the right or southern side.<BR>—दक्षिण-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing upon the right, to the<BR>south, &c.; (अस्), m. a charioteer (as standing<BR>on the right of his master; cf. सव्ये-ष्ठ).<BR>—दक्षिणा-कपर्द, see दक्षिणतस्-कपर्द.<BR>—दक्षिणा-काल, अस्, m. the time of (receiving)<BR>the sacrificial gift or fee.<BR>—दक्षिणाग्नि (˚ण-अग्˚),<BR>इस्, m. the southern fire of the altar, a sacred fire<BR>placed towards the south, (in the Brāhmaṇas generally<BR>called Anvāhārya-pacana.)<BR>—दक्षिणाग्र (˚णा-<BR>अग्र), अस्, आ, अम्, pointing to the south, having<BR>the head or point turned towards the south.<BR>—द-<BR>क्षिणाचल (˚ण-अच्˚), अस्, m. the southern moun-<BR>tain, the Malaya range.<BR>—दक्षिणाचार (˚ण-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, honest or upright in conduct, well-<BR>behaved; a worshipper of Śakti according to the<BR>purer or right hand ritual.<BR>—दक्षिणाचारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, a worshipper of Śakti according to the purer or<BR>right hand ritual; a follower of the right hand<BR>Śākta system.<BR>—दक्षिणा-ज्योतिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, Ved.<BR>brilliant by the sacrificial gift.<BR>—दक्षिणाञ्च् (˚ण-<BR>अञ्च्), आङ्, आची, आक्, turned to the south, southward.<BR>—दक्षिणात्यय (˚ण-अत्˚), अस्, m. one who<BR>goes beyond the south, a dweller in the south.<BR>—दक्षिणा-द्वार, अस्, आ, अम्, having the door<BR>on the south.<BR>—दक्षिणान्तिका (˚ण-अन्˚), f. a<BR>kind of metre.<BR>—दक्षिणा-पथ, अस्, m. the path<BR>or road of the Dakṣiṇā, i. e. of the cow constituting<BR>the sacrificial fee (situated between the Śālā and the<BR>Sadas); the southern region or country, the De-<BR>khan.<BR>—दक्षिणापथ-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going to<BR>the south, living in the south.<BR>—दक्षिणापथ-जन्-<BR>मन्, आ, m. born in the south, a southern; (-जन्मा-<BR>नस्), m. pl., N. of the Andhakas, Guhas, Pulindas, Sava-<BR>ras, Cucukas, and Madrapas, all outcast or barbarous<BR>tribes.<BR>—दक्षिणा-पथिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging<BR>to the southern region.<BR>—दक्षिणापर (˚ण-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, south-western.<BR>—दक्षिणा-प्रवण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, shelving or inclining to the south.<BR>—द-<BR>क्षिणा-प्रष्टि, इस्, m., Ved. the horse harnessed on<BR>the right side of the yoke-horses (युग्य); [cf. Gr.<BR>δεξιόσειρος.]<BR>—दक्षिणा-बन्ध, अस्, m. (in the<BR>Sāṅkhya phil.) N. of one of the three states of bondage,<BR>the bondage of ritual observance; [cf. दाक्षिण and<BR>दाक्षिणिक.]<BR>—दक्षिणाभिमुख (˚णा-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, facing southwards, directed southwards,<BR>flowing southwards.<BR>—दक्षिणाभिमुख-स्थित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, standing with the face southwards.<BR>—द-<BR>क्षिणा-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, turning the face to the<BR>right or to the south, facing south.<BR>—दक्षिणा-<BR>मूर्ति, इस्, m. one of the forms of Śiva with the<BR>Tāntrikas; N. of an author.<BR>—दक्षिणामूर्ति-<BR>प्रयोग, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Tantra-<BR>sāra.<BR>—दक्षिणामूर्ति-मन्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Śāradātilaka by Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—द-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">Page0397-c+ 79</a>]<BR>क्षिणामूर्ति-संहिता, f., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Tantra-sāra.<BR>—दक्षिणामूर्त्य्-उपनिषद्, त्, f., N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—दक्षिणायन (˚ण-अय्˚), अम्,<BR>n. the sun's progress south of the equator, the winter's<BR>solstice, the half-year in which the sun moves from<BR>north to south; दक्षिणायनम् अनुया, to follow<BR>the southward way, to go to Yama's quarter, i. e. to<BR>die; (अस्, आ, अम्), situated in the sun's course from<BR>north to south (said of certain asterisms).<BR>—द-<BR>क्षिणा-युग्य, अस्, m. the right yoke-horse.<BR>—द-<BR>क्षिणारण्य (˚ण-अर्˚), अम्, n. the southern forest,<BR>N. of a particular forest (probably in the Dekhan).<BR>—दक्षिणारुस् (˚ण-अर्˚), उस्, उस्, उस्, wounded on<BR>the right side.<BR>—दक्षिणार्ध (˚ण-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the right side, the southern side.<BR>—दक्षिणार्ध्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the preceding), Ved. situated on the<BR>right, being on the southern side.<BR>—दक्षिणार्ह<BR>(˚णा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, deserving a fee, meriting a<BR>reward, worthy of a gift.<BR>—दक्षिणा-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत् (fr. दक्षिण with lengthening of the final), Ved.<BR>able, competent, strong, fit, effective; (fr. दक्षि-<BR>णा), giving sacrificial presents, offering large remu-<BR>neration, abounding in presents, possessed of a gift,<BR>having ample rewards, piously disposed.<BR>—दक्षिणा-<BR>वर्त (˚णा-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, turning to the right,<BR>turned towards the south; दक्षिणावर्त आदित्यस्,<BR>the sun in his course from the north to the south;<BR>(अस्), m. the southern country, the Dekhan, a conch-<BR>shell with the valve opening to the right.<BR>—दक्षि-<BR>णावर्तक (˚णा-आव्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, turning to the<BR>right, turned towards the south; (अकी), f., N. of a<BR>plant or shrub (= वृश्चि-कालि); a line of bees.<BR>—दक्षिणा-वह्, -वाट्, Ved. ‘being borne to the right<BR>or to the south of the (Āhavanīya) fire,’ epithet of the<BR>sacrificial ladle.<BR>—दक्षिणावृत् (˚णा-आव्˚), त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>turned towards the right, going round on the right.<BR>—दक्षिणाशा (˚ण-आशा), f. the southern quarter,<BR>the south.<BR>—दक्षिणाशा-पति, इस्, m. ‘the lord of<BR>the south,’ epithet of Yama.<BR>—दक्षिणाशा-रति, इस्,<BR>m. (? रति for पति), an epithet of Agastya.<BR>—द-<BR>क्षिणा-सद्, see दक्षिण-सद्.<BR>—दक्षिणेतर<BR>(˚ण-इत्˚), different from the right, other than the<BR>right, the left.<BR>—दक्षिणेर्मन् (˚ण-ईर्मन् = 2.<BR>ईर्म), आ, आ, अ, wounded on the right side or right fore<BR>leg (as a deer). (In any other sense this compound<BR>takes the form दक्षिणेर्म, अस्, आ, अम्, e. g. द-<BR>क्षिणेर्मं शकटम्, a cart broken on the right<BR>side.)<BR>—दक्षिणोत्तर (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, situ-<BR>ated on the right and left, lying to the south and<BR>north, turned to the south and north.<BR>—दक्षि-<BR>णोत्तर-वृत्त, the meridian line.<BR>—दक्षिणोत्त-<BR>रिन् (˚ण-उत्˚), ई, इणी, इ, Ved. being above on the<BR>right side, overhanging on the right side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा, दक्षिणेन, दक्षिणे. See col. 1,<BR>under दक्षिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाहि
दक्षिणाहि, ind. far on the right, far in the<BR>south (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणित्
दक्षिणित्, त्, ind., Ved. on the right hand, to the<BR>right; [cf. प्र-दक्षिणित्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीकृ
दक्षिणी-कृ, cl. 5. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to place on the right hand, to turn the right<BR>side towards any one (acc.), to walk round a person<BR>with the right side turned towards him (as a mark<BR>of respect).<BR>—दक्षिणी-कृत्य, ind. having walked<BR>round in the above manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of the sacrificial<BR>fee, meriting a reward, fit for a sacrificial donation,<BR>worthy to be honoured with presents; [cf. आ-दक्षि-<BR>णीय and दक्षिण्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण्य|दक्षिण्यः
दक्षिण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = दक्षिणीय, merit-<BR>ing a sacrificial reward &c.; [cf. दाक्षिण्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षि
दक्षि दक्षि or दक्षिन् (fr. 1. दह्), Ved.<BR>burning, blazing; (according to Sāy. = धक्षि),<BR>thou burnest. (In Ṛg-veda I. 141, 8, दक्षि =<BR>दहति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण दक्षिण. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दगार्गल|दगार्गलं
दगार्गल दगार्गल, अम्, n. (fr. द = उद +<BR>2. ग + अर्गल), examining the soil in searching for<BR>wells or rules for doing so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0397-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दगु
दगु दगु, उस्, m., N. of a man; [cf. दाग-<BR>व्यायनि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. दह्), burnt,<BR>scorched, consumed by fire; (metaphorically) tor-<BR>mented, tortured, pained, consumed by grief, dis-<BR>tressed; burnt by the fire of the gastric juice (as the<BR>stomach; cf. जठराग्नि), famished; dry; tasteless,<BR>insipid; inauspicious; cunning (= वि-दग्ध); (आ),<BR>f. the quarter where the sun remains overhead (?);<BR>a lunar day or Tithi on which it is unlucky to do<BR>anything and religious rites are prohibited; a species<BR>of plant, = दग्धिका, दग्ध-रुहा; (अम्), n.<BR>burning, cauterizing (e. g. अग्नि-दग्ध, actual cau-<BR>tery; क्षार-दग्ध, potential cautery, in surgery;<BR>त्वग्-दग्ध, cauterizing of the skin); a species of<BR>fragrant grass, = रोहिष.<BR>—दग्ध-काक, अस्, m.<BR>‘a black or inauspicious crow,’ a raven, or perhaps<BR>the carrion crow.<BR>—दग्ध-तिथि, N. of a chapter<BR>of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—दग्ध-मन्दिर-सार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has burned the best of mansions.<BR>—दग्ध-मरण, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—दग्ध-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, having its source or<BR>origin destroyed.<BR>—दग्ध-रथ, अस्, m. = चित्र-<BR>रथ, N. of the chief of the Gandharvas.<BR>—दग्ध-<BR>रुह, अस्, m. ‘growing in ashes,’ N. of a tree, =<BR>तिलक; (आ), f., N. of a plant, = दग्धा, दग्धिका,<BR>भस्म-रोहा, &c.<BR>—दग्ध-वर्णक, ‘black-<BR>coloured (?),’ a species of grass, = दग्ध, रोहिष.<BR>—दग्धाक्षर (˚ध-अक्˚), N. of certain letters<BR>regarded as inauspicious in poems.<BR>—दग्धेष्टका<BR>(˚ध-इष्˚), f. a burnt or vitrified brick.<BR>—दग्धो-<BR>दर (˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having a burnt or<BR>starving stomach,’ starving; (अम्), n. ‘a burnt stomach,’<BR>i. e. an empty or craving stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धव्य
दग्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be burnt or consumed<BR>by fire, inflammable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धिका
दग्धिका, f. scorched rice; N. of a plant, =<BR>दग्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धृ
दग्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, a burner, consuming<BR>by fire, one who burns, a consumer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध्वा
दग्ध्वा, ind. having burnt, having consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्
दघ् दघ्, cl. 4. P. दघ्यति, &c., Ved.<BR>to move, go, flow, reach, attain; to go<BR>away; (with पश्चा or पश्चात्) to lag behind, fall<BR>short of [cf. अ-पश्चा-दघ्वन्]; cl. 5. P. दघ्-<BR>नोति, &c., to hurt, kill; to go, to leap; to protect;<BR>[cf. rt. दङ्घ् below; cf. also Gr. ταχύς, δέχομαι;<BR>Goth. tekan, ‘to take;’ Angl. Sax. taengan, ‘to<BR>hasten;’ Lat. tango.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्न
दघ्न, अस्, ई, अम् (at the end of a comp.; re-<BR>garded by native grammarians as an affix), reaching<BR>to, as high as; [cf. आ-दघ्न, उपस्थ-दघ्न,<BR>ऊरु-दघ्न, जानु-दघ्न, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्वन्
दघ्-वन् in अपश्चा-दघ्वन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंक्ष्णु
दंक्ष्णु दङ्क्ष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. 2. दंश्),<BR>Ved. biting, mordaceous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दङ्घ्|दंघ्
दङ्घ् दङ्घ्, cl. 1. P. दङ्घति, &c., to<BR>quit, abandon; to cherish, protect; [cf. rt.<BR>दघ् above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दच्छद|दच्छदः
दच्छद दच्-छद. See under दत्, p. 399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड्|दंड्
दण्ड् दण्ड्, cl. 10. P. दण्डयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to punish, &c. (rather to be regarded as<BR>a nom. fr. दण्ड below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. 1. दम्, but connected<BR>with the preceding; the neut. is rare), a stick, staff, rod,<BR>pole, cudgel, mace, club or club-shaped weapon; a<BR>sceptre; a blow with a stick, &c.; the staff given to a<BR>twice-born man at initiation or at investiture with the<BR>sacred thread, (this staff was of different lengths, the<BR>longest belonging to the Brāhmans, see Manu II.<BR>45-47); the penis; the trunk of an elephant; an<BR>arm or leg (generally in comp. with a word signifying<BR>‘arm,’ &c.; see दोर्-दण्ड, बाहु-दण्ड); a stalk,<BR>the stem of a tree [cf. उद्-द्˚ and खर-द्˚];<BR>the handle of anything (as of a ladle, sauce-pan, fly-<BR>flap, parasol, &c.), the staff or pole of a banner or of<BR>a tent; the beam of a plough; the oar of a boat; the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-b" target="_blank">Page0398-b+ 81</a>]<BR>cross-bar or bridge of a lute or other stringed instrument<BR>which holds the strings; a churning-stick (said to be<BR>neut. only, cf. दण्डाहत); a pole as a measure of<BR>length, = 4 Hastas, = 96 finger-breadths; a particular<BR>measure of time, = 60 Vi-kalās, = 360 breaths, = (1/60)<BR>part of the day and night, = 24 minutes [cf. नाडिका];<BR>the stick with which an instrument is played; a<BR>particular appearance in the sky similar to a staff or<BR>rod; a particular planet, = ग्रह-भेद; a particular<BR>constellation; a form of military array, a long line<BR>or column of troops [cf. दण्ड-व्यूह]; an uninter-<BR>rupted row or series, a line [cf. दण्ड-पात and<BR>दण्डक]; a staff or sceptre as a symbol of power<BR>and sovereignty; application of power or physical<BR>force (e. g. राजा नित्यम् उद्यत-दण्डः स्यात्, a king<BR>should always hold his sceptre erect, i. e. prepared to<BR>use his power; दण्डोद्यम, raising the sceptre,<BR>exertion of power; न्यस्त-दण्ड, laying aside the<BR>sceptre, resigning power); assault, attack, violence,<BR>(in this sense दण्ड is one of the four Upāyas;<BR>सामन्, ‘negotiation,’ दान, ‘bribery,’ and भेद,<BR>‘sowing dissension,’ constituting the other three,<BR>see उपाय); power over, control, restraint (e. g.<BR>मनो-द्˚, वाग्-द्˚, काय-द्˚, restraint of thoughts,<BR>words, and bodily actions, see Manu XII. 10; cf. त्रि-<BR>दण्डिन्); power or physical force embodied, an<BR>army (e. g. कोष-दण्डौ, du. treasure and army);<BR>the rod as a symbol of judicial authority and punish-<BR>ment; punishment in general; corporal chastisement;<BR>fine, mulct, amercement; imprisonment; capital<BR>punishment, putting to death; reprimand; (Punish-<BR>ment personified is a son of Dharma and Kriyā;<BR>sometimes = Yama or = Śiva); standing upright or<BR>erect; N. of one of the attendants of the sun; N.<BR>of a man; N. of a prince slain by Arjuna (brother of<BR>Daṇḍa-dhara and identified with the Asura Krodha-<BR>hantṛ); N. of a son of Ikṣvāku; (according to<BR>lexicographers दण्ड also means) pride; a horse, a<BR>corner, an angle (?); (आ), f. Hedysarum Lagopodi-<BR>oides, = नाग-बला; [cf. चर्म-द्˚, जाल-द्˚, &c.]<BR>—दण्ड-कन्दक, अस्, m. a species of bulbous<BR>plant, = धरणी-कन्द.<BR>—दण्ड-कर्तृ, ता, m. a<BR>punisher, chastiser.<BR>—दण्ड-कर्मन्, अ, n. ‘appli-<BR>cation of the rod,’ infliction of punishment, chastise-<BR>ment.<BR>—दण्ड-कल, a kind of metre.<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>काक, अस्, m. a raven; (perhaps for दग्ध-काक,<BR>q. v.)<BR>—दण्ड-काष्ठ, अम्, n. a wooden staff or<BR>pole.<BR>—दण्ड-कुश, आस्, m. pl. a various reading for<BR>the next.<BR>—दण्ड-कूल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—दण्ड-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>गौरी, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—दण्ड-ग्रहण,<BR>अम्, n. assumption of the (pilgrim's) staff, becoming<BR>a mendicant or ascetic.<BR>—दण्ड-ग्राह, अस्, m. a<BR>staff-bearer, (probably) N. of a man.<BR>—दण्ड-घ्न,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, striking with a stick, one who commits<BR>an assault.<BR>—दण्ड-चक्र, अस्, m. ‘the discus of<BR>punishment,’ N. of a mythical weapon; a division of<BR>an army; [cf. दण्डानीक.]<BR>—दण्ड-च्छदन,<BR>अम्, n. a room in which utensils of various kinds are<BR>kept.<BR>—दण्ड-जित, अस्, आ, अम्, subdued by punish-<BR>ment.<BR>—दण्ड-ढक्का, f. a sort of kettle-drum,<BR>upon which the hours are struck.<BR>—दण्ड-ताम्री,<BR>f. = ताम्री, p. 370, col. 1.<BR>—दण्ड-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of a staff, stick, &c.<BR>—दण्ड-दास, अस्, m.<BR>‘a slave from a fine not paid,’ i. e. one who has be-<BR>come a slave from non-payment of a debt.<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>देव-कुल, अम्, n. ‘temple of punishment,’ a court<BR>of justice.<BR>—दण्ड-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, a staff-<BR>bearer, having or carrying a staff or sceptre, hav-<BR>ing oars (as a ship); exercising judicial power,<BR>chastising, punishing, having authority to punish;<BR>(अस्), m. a king; a magistrate, judge, the supreme<BR>judge; a N. of Yama; a mendicant carrying a staff;<BR>a potter.<BR>—दण्डधराधिप (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘the prince of sceptre-bearers,’ a plenipotentiary, a<BR>king.<BR>—दण्ड-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing the<BR>sceptre, exercising judicial power; (अस्), m. a king;<BR>a judge; an epithet of Yama; N. of a prince slain<BR>by Arjuna (brother of Daṇḍa and identified with the<BR>Asura Krodha-vardhana, enumerated among the sons<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra in Mahā-bh. I. 2738); (आस्), m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-c" target="_blank">Page0398-c+ 81</a>]<BR>pl., N. of a barbarous people.<BR>—दण्ड-धारण,<BR>अम्, n. the carrying a staff (as by the Brahma-cārin);<BR>following the order of a mendicant; chastising,<BR>punishment.<BR>—दण्ड-धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, carrying<BR>the rod, chastening, punishing.<BR>—दण्ड-धृष्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, carrying the staff or rod, exercising authority.<BR>—दण्ड-नायक, अस्, m. ‘one who applies the<BR>rod,’ a judge, magistrate, a head police-officer; a<BR>leader of a column, leader of an army, general, com-<BR>mander-in-chief; N. of one of the attendants of the<BR>sun.<BR>—दण्डनायक-पुरुष, अस्, m. a policeman,<BR>police-officer, constable, beadle.<BR>—दण्ड-निपातन,<BR>अम्, n. applying the rod, chastising, punishing; [cf.<BR>दण्ड-पातन.]<BR>—दण्ड-नीति, इस्, f. application of<BR>the rod, administration of justice, judicature, the<BR>doctrine of the right administration of justice; the<BR>rule of inflicting punishment, the system of civil and<BR>military administration taught by Cāṇakya and others,<BR>polity, ethics, system of morals; an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—दण्डनीति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, familiar with<BR>the administration of justice.<BR>—दण्ड-नेतृ, ता, m.<BR>‘one who applies the rod,’ a punisher, an inflicter of<BR>punishment, a judge; अधि-दण्डनेतृ, the supreme<BR>chastiser, i. e. Yama.<BR>—दण्डनेतृ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the office of a judge, administration of justice.<BR>—दण्ड-प, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>पक्षक, अस्, m. a particular gesture or motion of<BR>the hands.<BR>—दण्ड-पांशुल (?), अस्, m. a porter, a<BR>warder or door-keeper.<BR>—दण्ड-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>staff-handed, bearing a staff or rod; (इस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Yama; N. of a leader of two of the<BR>troops of the god Śiva in Kāśī (identified with<BR>the Yakṣa Hari-keśa); N. of the father of Go-pā,<BR>the wife of Śākya-muni; N. of a prince, grand-<BR>father of Kṣemaka; [cf. खण्ड-पाणि.]<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>पाणि-वर-प्रदान, अम्, n., N. of the forty-<BR>fourth chapter of the Jñāna-khaṇḍa or second part<BR>of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—दण्ड-पात, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>falling of the stick’ [cf. दाण्ड-पाता]; dropping one<BR>line in a manuscript.<BR>—दण्ड-पातन, अम्, n. ap-<BR>plying the rod, punishing, punishment; [cf. दण्ड-<BR>निपातन.]<BR>—दण्ड-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘letting fall the<BR>stick or rod,’ punishing, chastising, fining, mulcting.<BR>—दण्ड-पारुष्य, अम्, n. ‘stick-assault, actual<BR>violence, assault and battery (as a title of jurispru-<BR>dence); cruel or harsh infliction of punishment, (one<BR>of the seven vices of kings and rulers.)<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>पाल or दण्ड-पालक, अस्, m. ‘superintendent of<BR>punishment or of the administration of justice,’ a<BR>head magistrate or judge; a door-keeper, a porter;<BR>a kind of fish (= अर्ध-शफर, शकुल; com-<BR>monly दाण्डिका).<BR>—दण्डपाल-ता, f. the adminis-<BR>tration of justice.<BR>—दण्ड-पाशक or दण्ड-पा-<BR>शिक, अस्, m. ‘holding the fetters or noose of punish-<BR>ment,’ a head police-officer, policeman; a hangman,<BR>an executioner.<BR>—दण्ड-पासिक (?) = पौरिक,<BR>q. v.<BR>—दण्ड-पिङ्गलक, आस्, m., N. of a people<BR>to the north of Madhya-deśa.<BR>—दण्ड-पोण, अम्,<BR>n. (पोण = पवन), a strainer or filtering machine<BR>with a handle.<BR>—दण्ड-प्रणयन, अम्, n. ‘in-<BR>fliction of punishment,’ N. of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva by Halāyudha.<BR>—दण्ड-प्रणाम,<BR>अस्, m. a stiff bow, bowing without bending the<BR>body like a stick.<BR>—दण्ड-बध, अस्, m. ‘death<BR>by punishment,’ capital punishment.<BR>—दण्ड-बा-<BR>लधि, इस्, m. an elephant (‘having a tail like a<BR>stick’).<BR>—दण्ड-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, ‘stick-armed,’<BR>carrying a stick or staff; (उस्), m., N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Skanda.<BR>—दण्ड-भङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>‘omission of punishment,’ non-execution of a sen-<BR>tence, reprieve, escape.<BR>—दण्ड-भय, अम्, n. fear<BR>of the rod.<BR>—दण्ड-भीति, इस्, f. dread of punish-<BR>ment.<BR>—दण्ड-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, carrying a staff or<BR>stick; (त्), m. a potter.<BR>—दण्ड-माणव or दण्ड-<BR>मानव, अस्, m. ‘a staff-man,’ a staff-bearer, an<BR>ascetic, one who bears a staff; a chief or leader.<BR>—दण्ड-मातङ्ग, Tabernæmontana Coronaria<BR>(= पिण्ड-तगर).<BR>—दण्ड-मुख, अस्, m. the<BR>leader of an army, a general, a commander-in-chief;<BR>[cf. दण्ड-नायक.]<BR>—दण्ड-यात्रा, f. a solemn<BR>or festive procession, moving in state or with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-a" target="_blank">Page0399-a+ 81</a>]<BR>attendants, especially a bridal procession; warlike<BR>expedition, subjection or conquest of a region or<BR>quarter (= दिग्-विजय).<BR>—दण्ड-याम, अस्, m. a<BR>day; an epithet of Yama; of Agastya; (also written<BR>दण्डा-याम.)<BR>—दण्ड-योग, अस्, m. infliction of<BR>punishment.<BR>—दण्ड-लेश, अम्, n. a small fine.<BR> — 1. दण्ड-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a stick, carrying<BR>a staff; furnished with a handle; having a large<BR>army.<BR>—२. दण्ड-वत्, ind. like a stick, erect or up-<BR>right as a stick; prostrate, falling or lying prostrate;<BR>दण्ड-वत् प्रणम्य, bowing like a stick; [cf.<BR>दण्ड-प्रणाम.]<BR>—दण्ड-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, utter-<BR>ing a reprimand, rebuking, censuring, threatening<BR>with punishment or castigation; (ई), m. a door-<BR>keeper, warder; [cf. दण्ड-वासिन्.]<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>वार्क्ष, अम्, n. a particular posture, a mode of<BR>sitting.<BR>—दण्ड-वासिक, अस्, m. a door-keeper.<BR>—दण्ड-वासिन्, ई, m. a door-keeper, warder,<BR>chamberlain; the magistrate or head of a village.<BR>—दण्ड-वाहिन्, ई, m. a police-officer.<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>विकल्प, अस्, m. ‘alternative of punishment,’ discre-<BR>tionary punishment or fine.<BR>—दण्ड-विधि, इस्, m.<BR>criminal law; rule or mode of punishment.<BR>—दण्ड-<BR>विशेष, अस्, m. kind or degree of punishment.<BR>—दण्ड-विष्कम्भ, अस्, m. a post or a stake to<BR>which is fastened the string that works the churning-<BR>stick.<BR>—दण्ड-वीर्य, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—दण्ड-वृक्षक, अस्, m. the plant Tithymalus<BR>Antiquorum (= स्नुही).<BR>—दण्ड-व्यूह, अस्, m.<BR>drawing up or arraying an army in long lines or<BR>columns.<BR>—दण्ड-व्रत-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, exer-<BR>cising judicial power, decreeing punishment, punish-<BR>ing.<BR>—दण्ड-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a prince; (also<BR>read दत्त-शर्मन्.)<BR>—दण्ड-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the<BR>criminal law.<BR>—दण्ड-सङ्ख्या, f., N. of a chapter<BR>of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—दण्ड-सेन, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince, son of Viṣvak-sena.<BR>—दण्ड-हस्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘staff-handed,’ ‘a staff-bearer;’ epithet of<BR>the god of death; a door-keeper, warder; (अस्, आ<BR>or ई), m. f. the plant Tabernæmontana Coronaria;<BR>(अम्), n. the flower of this plant.<BR>—दण्डाख्य<BR>(˚ड-आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, called after a staff; having<BR>the name Daṇḍa; (अम्), n., N. of a place of pilgrim-<BR>age; a hall with two wings, one of which faces<BR>towards the north, the other towards the east.<BR>—दण्डाघात (˚ड-आघ्˚), अस्, m. a blow with a<BR>stick or staff.<BR>—दण्डाजिन (˚ड-अज्˚), अम्, n. ‘staff<BR>and skin’ (as mere outer signs of devotion); hypo-<BR>crisy, deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery; [cf. दाण्डा-<BR>जिनिक.]<BR>—दण्डाज्ञा (˚ड-आज्˚), f. judicial sentence.<BR>—दण्डा-दण्डि, ind. ‘stick against stick’ in fight-<BR>ing, single-stick, cudgelling, fighting with sticks and<BR>staves.<BR>—दण्डाधिप, अस्, or दण्डाधिपति (˚ड-<BR>अध्˚), इस्, m. a superior judge, supreme magistrate.<BR>—दण्डानीक (˚ड-अन्˚), अम्, n. a division of an<BR>army, a detachment; [cf. दण्ड-चक्र.]<BR>—दण्डा-<BR>पतानक (˚ड-अप्˚), अस्, m. tetanus, lock-jaw,<BR>spasm.<BR>—दण्डामित्रा (˚ड-अम्˚), f., N. of a place;<BR>[cf. दत्तामित्र or दत्तामित्रा.]<BR>—दण्डा-याम<BR>= दण्ड-याम.<BR>—दण्डार्त (˚ड-आर्˚), N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place.<BR>—दण्डार्ह (˚ड-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deserving punishment.<BR>—दण्डालसिका (˚ड-<BR>अल्˚), f. the cholera.<BR>—दण्डाश्रम (˚ड-आश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the order of the staff, condition of a pilgrim.<BR>—दण्डा-<BR>श्रमिन् (˚ड-आश्˚), ई, m. assuming the pilgrim's staff,<BR>a devotee.<BR>—दण्डासन (˚ड-अस्˚ or -आस्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>sort of arrow.<BR>—दण्डास्त्र (˚ड-अस्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>stick-weapon or ‘the weapon of punishment,’ N. of<BR>a fabulous weapon.<BR>—दण्डाहत (˚ड-आह्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘struck with the churning-stick,’ buttermilk.<BR>—दण्डोत्पल (˚ड-उत्˚), अम्, n. a species of plant<BR>(commonly Ḍānipolā and Ḍānakuni) with yellow,<BR>red, and white flowers; (according to some, the one<BR>with white flowers is called Daṇḍotpalā.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0398-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डक|दंडक|दंडकः|दण्डकः
दण्डक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a stick, staff, handle,<BR>staff of a banner &c., see दण्ड; a species of<BR>plant; a line, row, uninterrupted series; a sort of<BR>metre the stanza of which may extend from 27 × 4<BR>to 999 × 4 syllables; N. of a work; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>m. f. n., N. of a district in the Dekhan between the<BR>Nermadā and Godavarī rivers, which in the time of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">Page0399-b+ 78</a>]<BR>Rāma-candra was a forest and celebrated as a place<BR>of pilgrimage; (आस्), m. pl. the above district and its<BR>inhabitants; (अस्), m., N. of a prince who was son<BR>of Īkṣvāku and connected with the Daṇḍaka<BR>district; N. of a man; (इका), f. a stick, a staff; a<BR>row, line, series; a rope; a string of pearls; [cf.<BR>यष्टि.]<BR>—दण्डकारण्य (˚क-अर्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>Daṇḍaka forest, see above; N. of a part of the<BR>Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—दण्डकारण्य-प्रस्थान, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a part of the Abhirāma-maṇi-nāṭaka.<BR>—दण्-<BR>डकालसक (˚क-अल्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डन|दंडन|दंडनं
दण्डन, अस्, m., Ved. a cane?; (अम्), n.<BR>beating, punishing, chastising, inflicting punishment<BR>(e. g. अधर्म-दण्डन, unjust punishment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीय|दंडनीय
दण्डनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, punishable, to be chas-<BR>tised, deserving punishment, liable to a fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डय
दण्डय, nom. P. दण्डयति, -यितुम्, to punish,<BR>chastise, to fine, amerce (with acc. of the person<BR>and of the punishment inflicted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डाय
दण्डाय, nom. A. दण्डायते, &c., (common in<BR>Bengālī for) to stand erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डायमान
दण्डायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, (common in Bengālī<BR>for) standing erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिक|दंडिक|दंडिकः|दण्डिकः
दण्डिक, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying a stick, punishing,<BR>one who chastises; (अस्), m. a staff-bearer, mace-<BR>bearer [cf. दाण्डिक]; a fish, Cyprinus Dankena,<BR>commonly called Ḍānikaṇā Māca; (आ), f., see<BR>दण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डित|दंडित|दण्डितः
दण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, punished, chastised, amerced,<BR>sentenced, mulcted, fined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिन्|दंडिन्
दण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having or bearing a staff or<BR>stick [cf. त्रि-दण्डिन्]; (ई), m. a Brāhman of the<BR>fourth order or in the fourth stage of his life; a<BR>religious mendicant or Bhikṣu carrying a staff; N.<BR>of a particular order of mendicants deriving their<BR>origin from Śaṅkarācārya; a Jaina ascetic; a door-<BR>keeper, warder, porter; an oarsman, boatman; a N. of<BR>Yama; of Mañju-śrī; of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of the<BR>author of the Kāvyādarśa; of the author of the Daśa-<BR>kumāra-carita; a species of plant; [cf. दमनक.]<BR>—दण्डि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing staff-bearers,<BR>having club-bearers.<BR>—दण्डि-मुण्ड, अस्, m. ‘carry-<BR>ing a staff and having the head shaved,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—दण्डिमुण्डीश्वर (? for दण्डिमुण्डे-<BR>श्वर), a form of Śiva; N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिमन्
दण्डिमन्, आ, m. (abstract noun fr. दण्ड), the<BR>state or condition of a staff, rod, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड्य|दंड्य|दण्ड्यः
दण्ड्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be punished, punishable,<BR>deserving punishment, to be fined (with acc. of<BR>the punishment inflicted, or in comp., e. g. सर्व-<BR>स्व-दण्ड्य, to be fined in all one's property).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डरी
दण्डरी दण्डरी, f. = डङ्गरी, a species of<BR>cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डार|दंडार|दंडारः|दण्डारः
दण्डार दण्डार, अस्, m. a carriage, vehicle;<BR>a raft, boat; a potter's wheel; a bow or any other<BR>instrument for shooting arrows or darts; an elephant<BR>in rut, a furious or intoxicated elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्|दन्त्
दत् दत् (perhaps fr. rt. अद्, to eat, the initial<BR>being dropped, as in खादन, a tooth, fr. rt. खाद् and<BR>φαγόνες fr. φαγ; or according to others fr. rt. 3. दा,<BR>to cut), optionally substituted for दन्त, a tooth, in<BR>the acc. pl. and remaining weak and middle cases (Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 1, 63; Vopa-deva III. 39); the form दत् occurs<BR>frequently at the end of compounds, the nom. case<BR>ending in अन् as in pres. participles; [cf. उभ-<BR>यतो-दत्, सु-दत्, अ-दत्, &c.]<BR>—दच्-छद, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the covering of the teeth,’ the lip, (chiefly in<BR>comp., see दष्ट-दच्छद); [cf. दन्त-च्छद.]<BR>—दत्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. furnished with teeth,<BR>biting; दत्-वती रज्जुः, ‘a rope with teeth,’ = a<BR>serpent or snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्क
दत्क in अदत्क, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त 1. दत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. दा, to give;<BR>cf. 1. दद्), given, granted, presented, made over,<BR>assigned; placed, extended, stretched forth; (अस्),<BR>m. a given son, i. e. a son given away by his natural<BR>parents to persons engaging to adopt him [cf. दत्तक<BR>and दत्रिम]; a common N. or title of a man of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">Page0399-c+ 78</a>]<BR>the Vaiśya or third tribe, (generally in comp. with a<BR>preceding word, e. g. वसु-दत्त, देव-दत्त, &c.,<BR>but दत्त sometimes stands alone, at present the<BR>title is common to the Kāyastha or writer class);<BR>N. of a man, brother of Dur-vāsas; of a son of Atri,<BR>= दत्तात्रेय; (with Jainas) N. of a son of Agni-<BR>siṃha and the seventh black Vāsu-deva; of a son of<BR>Rājādhideya Śūra; one of the seven sages in the<BR>second Manv-antara; (आ), f., N. of several women;<BR>(अम्), n. a gift, a donation.<BR>—दत्त-तीर्थ-कृत्, त्,<BR>m., N. of the eighth Arhat of the past Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR>—दत्त-नृत्योपहार (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, com-<BR>plimented with a dance.<BR>—दत्त-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has given up or sacrificed life.<BR>—दत्त-<BR>भुजङ्ग-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. and दत्त-महिमन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of two works of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—दत्त-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, given way to, having the road<BR>ceded.<BR>—दत्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has given.<BR>—दत्त-वर, अस्, आ, अम्, allowed to choose a boon;<BR>granted as a boon.<BR>—दत्त-शत्रु, उस्, or दत्त-<BR>शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a son of Rājādhideya Śūra.<BR>—दत्त-शुल्का, f. a bride for whom a sum of money<BR>or dowry has been paid.<BR>—दत्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a hand given for support, supported.<BR>—दत्ता-<BR>त्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one who has given himself,<BR>self-given; (with पुत्र) an orphan or a son deserted<BR>by his parents who gives himself to persons disposed<BR>to adopt him as their child; (आ), m., N. of one of<BR>the Viśve Devās.<BR>—दत्तात्रेय (˚त-आत्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a sage, son of Atri and Anasūyā, who favoured<BR>Arjuna Kārtavīrya, (see Mahā-bh. Śānti-parva 1751;<BR>according to one legend, Atri performed a very severe<BR>penance by which the three gods Brahmā, Viṣṇu,<BR>and Śiva were propitiated and became in portions<BR>of themselves severally his sons Soma, Datta, and<BR>Dur-vāsas); N. of an author mentioned in the<BR>Ānanda-laharī or Saundarya-laharī by Śaṅkara.<BR>—दत्तात्रेयाष्टोत्तर-शत-नाम-स्तोत्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Brahmāṇḍa-Purāṇa.<BR>—दत्ता-<BR>त्रेयीय, अम्, n. the story of Dattātreya.<BR>—दत्ता-<BR>दत्त (˚त-आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, given and received.<BR>—दत्तादर (˚त-आद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, showing re-<BR>spect, respectful; treated with respect.<BR>—दत्तानप-<BR>कर्मन् (˚त-अन्˚), अ, n. non-resumption of gifts.<BR>—दत्तापहृत (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, given and<BR>taken again.<BR>—दत्ताप्रदानिक (˚त-अ-प्र्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, relating to the non-delivery of a gift; (अम्),<BR>n. non-delivery or resumption of gifts, one of the<BR>eighteen titles of law.<BR>—दत्तामित्र (˚त-अम्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a prince of the Sauvīras; (अस्, आ), m. f.,<BR>N. of a district; [cf. दण्डामित्रा.]<BR>—दत्ताव-<BR>धान (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attentive.<BR>—दत्ता-<BR>सन (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a seat given,<BR>requested to sit.<BR>—दत्तैरण्ड-पल्लक (˚त-एर्˚),<BR>N. of a district in the Dekhan.<BR>—दत्तोपनिषद्<BR>(˚त-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad; (also written<BR>श्रीमद्-दत्तोपनिषद्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक|दत्तकः
दत्तक, अस्, m. (scil. पुत्र), a son given away by<BR>his natural parents to persons engaging to adopt him;<BR>one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by the old<BR>Hindū law; N. of the father of Māgha; N. of the<BR>author of the Vaiśikādhikaraṇa; a familiar diminu-<BR>tive of the names of persons ending with दत्त.<BR>—दत्तक-चन्द्रिका and दत्तक-मीमांसा, f.,<BR>N. of two legal works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ति|दत्तिः
दत्ति, इस्, f. a gift, donation, offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तिक
दत्तिक, दत्तिय, and दत्तिल, अस्, m. familiar<BR>diminutives of the names of persons ending in<BR>दत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तेय|दत्तेयः
दत्तेय, अस्, m., N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त 2. दत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 5. दा), pre-<BR>served, guarded, protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तोलि
दत्तोलि दत्तोलि, इस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Pulastya, one of the seven sages in the second<BR>Manv-antara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्र|दत्रं
दत्र दत्र. See below under rt. 1. दद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्
दद् 1. दद्, a reduplicated form substituted<BR>for rt. 1. दा, to give, before certain affixes and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">Page0400-a+ 76</a>]<BR>terminations (Pāṇ. VI. 4, 126; VII. 4, 46; VIII. 2,<BR>38), and by some grammarians given as a separate<BR>rt.: cl. 1. A. ददते, &c., to give, (see rt. 1. दा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0399-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्र|दत्रं
दत्र, अम्, n. (perhaps more correctly दत्त्र),<BR>Ved. gift, donation; [cf. अ-दत्रया and गो-दत्र.]<BR>—दत्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. rich in gifts, giving<BR>abundantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्रिम|दत्त्रिमः
दत्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, received by gift, produced<BR>or effected by gifts; (अस्), m. a slave or a son re-<BR>ceived by gift; (see Manu VII. 415; IX. 141.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्
2. दद्, giving, in आयुर्-दद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद
दद, अस्, आ, अम्, giving; [cf. अभयन्-दद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददत्
ददत्, अत्, अती, अत् (pres. part. of rt. 1. दा),<BR>giving, presenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददन|ददनं
ददन, अम्, n. gift, giving, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददि
ददि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. giving, bestowing, distributing<BR>(with acc.); [cf. Pāṇ. II. 3, 69.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददितृ
ददितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. a giver, giving;<BR>(according to others) a preserver, preserving; a<BR>possessor; [cf. 5. दा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददिवस्
ददिवस्, वान्, दुषी, वस्, who or what has<BR>given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददद
ददद ददद, an onomatopoetic word for<BR>the roaring of thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददरि
ददरि ददरि, N. of a river.<BR>—ददरि-<BR>सङ्गम, N. of a place mentioned in the Rasika-<BR>ramaṇa by Raghu-nātha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददाश्वस्
ददाश्वस् ददाश्वस्, वान्, उषी, वस् (perf. part.<BR>fr. rt. 1. दाश्), worshipping, serving the gods, giving,<BR>having given or bestowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृक्षेण्य
ददृक्षेण्य ददृक्षेण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1.<BR>दृश्), Ved. worth seeing, worthy to be seen, (Pāṇ.<BR>III. 4, 14; according to some दिदृक्षेण्य, q. v.,<BR>is the only correct form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृशानपवि
ददृशान-पवि, इस्, m., Ved. having the track<BR>of the wheels visible; epithet of Agni; (Sāy.) having<BR>a thunderbolt or weapon visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृशिवस्
ददृशिवस् or ददृश्वस्, वान्, उषी, वस्, having<BR>seen, having looked at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृत्
ददृत् ददृत्, त्, त्, त् (reduplicated form fr.<BR>rt. दॄ), tearing, splitting, bursting out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रु|दद्रुः
दद्रु, उस्, or ऊ, ऊस्, m. f. [cf. दर्द्रु], a cuta-<BR>neous eruption or rash, herpes; a kind of leprosy,<BR>(or according to others) a ringworm; a tortoise.<BR>—दद्रु-घ्न or दद्रू-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, de-<BR>stroying or removing cutaneous eruptions; (अस्), m.<BR>ringworm-shrub, Cassia Tora or Alata; Psoralea<BR>Corylifolia, (commonly Hākuc; the seeds are used<BR>as a remedy for cutaneous diseases.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुक|दद्रुकः
दद्रुक, अस्, m. cutaneous eruption or scab,<BR>leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुण|दद्रुणः
दद्रुण or दद्रूण, अस्, आ, अम्, or दद्रु-<BR>रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, herpetic, afflicted with cutaneous<BR>diseases or ringworm; [cf. दर्द्रु-रोगिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्
दध् दध् (reduplicated form substituted<BR>for rt. 1. धा before certain affixes and ter-<BR>minations; also given as a distinct rt.), cl. 1. A.<BR>दधते, &c., to hold, possess, retain; to give,<BR>present, assign, make over; (see rt. 1. धा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध
दध, अस्, आ, अम्, holding, having, possessing,<BR>giving; [cf. इला-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधत्
दधत्, अत्, अती, अत् (pres. part. of rt. 1. धा),<BR>having, holding, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधान
दधान, अस्, आ, अम् (pres. part.), having, hold-<BR>ing, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधि
1. दधि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. presenting, giving; pre-<BR>serving, keeping (with acc.); holding, having, pos-<BR>sessing, bearing; (इ), n. a house, an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधन्
दधन् दधन्, substituted for 2. दधि<BR>below, in the weakest cases (e. g. inst. दध्ना, dat.<BR>दध्ने, abl. gen. दध्नस्, loc. दध्नि or द-<BR>धनि).<BR>—दधन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing<BR>coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधि
दधि 2. दधि, इ, n. (perhaps a reduplicated<BR>form fr. rt. धे, to drink; cf. दधन् above),<BR>milk thickened or coagulated spontaneously by heat,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-b" target="_blank">Page0400-b+ 81</a>]<BR>thick sour milk, commonly called दही, (it is a<BR>general article of food in high estimation among the<BR>Hindūs, and regarded as a remedy or preventive of<BR>many disorders; it differs from curds in not having<BR>the whey separated from it); turpentine, the resin<BR>of the Shorea Robusta; [cf. Goth. daddyan, ‘to<BR>suckle.’]<BR>—दधि-कर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga;<BR>N. of a cat in the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—दधि-कुल्या, f.<BR>a stream of coagulated milk.<BR>—दधि-कूर्चिका, f. a<BR>mixture of boiled and coagulated milk; see कूर्चक.<BR>—दधि-क्र, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf. the fol-<BR>lowing.]<BR>—दधि-क्रा, आस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>mythical being often mentioned in the Veda, and<BR>the actual subject of Ṛg-veda IV. 38, 39, 40;<BR>VII. 44; (he is described as a kind of divine horse,<BR>and probably, like Tārkṣya, is a personification of<BR>the morning Sun; sometimes he is considered as a<BR>creation of heaven and earth, sometimes of Mitra-<BR>Varuṇa, and is invoked in the morning, together<BR>with Agni, Uṣas, and the Aśvins; the N. is pro-<BR>bably derived fr. 2. दधि and rt. 1. कॄ, to scatter,<BR>in allusion to the rising sun spreading dew and hoar<BR>frost like milk, but Mahī-dhara and Yāska explain it<BR>as if fr. 1. दधि and rt. क्रम्, i. e. one who bears<BR>his rider and advances, see Nirukta II. 27: in Nigh.<BR>I. 14, दधि-क्रा is given as one of the synonyms<BR>of अश्व, a horse.)<BR>—दधि-क्रावन्, आ, m., Ved. =<BR>दधि-क्रा.<BR>—दधि-घर्म, अस्, m., Ved. a warm<BR>beverage made of inspissated milk.<BR>—दधि-चार,<BR>अस्, m. the churning-stick.<BR>—दधि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>produced from thickened or coagulated milk; (अम्),<BR>n. fresh butter.<BR>—दधि-द्रप्स, अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>drop or globule of thickened milk.<BR>—दधि-धेनु,<BR>उस्, f. a quantity of thickened milk representing or<BR>equivalent to a cow given as an offering to the priests<BR>at a sacrifice; N. of the 105th chapter of the<BR>Vārāha-Purāṇa.<BR>—दधिधेनु-विधि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of the 168th chapter of the second part of the<BR>Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa.<BR>—दधि-नदी, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—दधि-पर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a saint.<BR>—दधि-पुच्छ, अस्, m., N. of a jackal.<BR>—दधि-पुष्पिका, f. the plant Clitoria Ternatea,<BR>= अपराजिता.<BR>—दधि-पुष्पी, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= कोलशिम्बी.<BR>—दधि-पूरण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Nāga.<BR>—दधि-पूर्व-मुख, अस्, m. = दधि-<BR>मुख, N. of a monkey, (‘in whose name the<BR>word मुख is preceded by दधि.’)<BR>—दधि-<BR>फल, अस्, m. the elephant or wood-apple, Feronia<BR>Elephantum, (the fruit having the acid taste of<BR>coagulated milk.)<BR>—दधि-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a vessel<BR>for holding coagulated milk, a pail.<BR>—दधि-मण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. the liquid part of curdled milk, whey.<BR>—द-<BR>धि-मण्डोद (˚ड-उद), अस्, m. the sea of whey.<BR>—दधि-मन्थन, अम्, n. the churning of co-<BR>agulated milk.<BR>—दधि-मुख, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>serpent, N. of a Nāga; N. of a monkey, brother-<BR>in-law of Su-grīva; N. of a Yaska.<BR>—दधिमुख-<BR>श्राव, अस्, m., N. of the fifty-seventh chapter of<BR>the Sundara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—दधि-<BR>वक्त्र, अस्, m., N. of a monkey, brother-in-law<BR>of Su-grīva.<BR>—दधि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. hav-<BR>ing coagulated milk, prepared with thick sour<BR>milk.<BR>—दधि-वर्ग, अस्, m., N. of a chapter in<BR>the medical work called Bhāva-prakāśa.<BR>—दधि-<BR>वामन-प्रयोग, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Tantra-sāra.<BR>—दधिवामन-मन्त्र, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—दधि-वारि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, containing coagulated milk for water (as<BR>a sea).<BR>—दधि-वाहन, अस्, m., N. of a prince,<BR>son of Aṅga and father of Divi-ratha.<BR>—दधि-<BR>विदर्भ, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (various<BR>reading for दशी-विदर्भ.)<BR>—दधि-शोण, अस्, m.<BR>a monkey.<BR>—दधि-सक्तु, अवस्, m. pl. barley-<BR>meal mixed with thickened milk.<BR>—दधि-सम्-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared or produced from thickened<BR>milk.<BR>—दधि-सर, अस्, m. the skim of coagulated<BR>milk.<BR>—दधि-सार, अस्, m. fresh butter.<BR>—दधि-<BR>स्कन्द, अस्, m., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—दधि-स्नेह,<BR>अस्, m. the oily skim of coagulated milk.<BR>—दधि-<BR>स्वेद, अस्, m. buttermilk.<BR>—दध्य्-अञ्च्, अङ्, m.<BR>(acc. दध्यञ्चम्, inst. दधीचा, &c.), Ved., N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">Page0400-c+ 76</a>]<BR>of a Ṛṣi or of a mythical being, called in Ṛg-veda<BR>I. 80, 16, and 117, 22, son of Atharvan; (the N.<BR>properly denotes ‘sprinkling or bestowing thick<BR>milk’ [cf. घृताची]; and the legends concerning<BR>him were probably originally connected with those<BR>of Dadhi-krā; he is described as having the head<BR>of a horse given to him by the Aśvins, with which he<BR>taught them the Madhu-vidyā and revealed to them<BR>where the Soma of Tvaṣṭṛ was concealed; accord-<BR>ing to Ṛg-veda I. 84, 13, Indra slew ninety times<BR>nine Vṛtras with his bones converted into a thunder-<BR>bolt; a portion of the latter part of the Yajur-veda<BR>is ascribed to Dadhy-añca, and he and his father are<BR>regarded as the first founders of sacrifice.)<BR>—दध्य्-<BR>अन्न, अम्, n. rice prepared with दधि.<BR>—दध्य्-<BR>आकर, अस्, m. the sea of inspissated milk.<BR>—दध्य्-<BR>आशिर्, ईर्, ईर्, ईर्, Ved. mixed with coagulated milk<BR>(as Soma).<BR>—दध्य्-आह्व or दध्य्-आह्वय, अस्,<BR>m. the resin of the Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—दध्य्-<BR>उत्तर or दध्युत्तरक, अम्, n. the skim of<BR>curdled milk, whey.<BR>—दध्य्-उद, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>दधि-वारि above.<BR>—दध्य्-ओदन, अस्, m. boiled<BR>rice mixed with coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिक
दधिक (at the end of adj. comp.) = दधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधित्थ|दधित्थः
दधित्थ, अस्, m. the wood-apple, Feronia Ele-<BR>phantum, the wood of which is not allowed to be<BR>used in sacrifices; [cf. दधि-फल, कपित्थ,<BR>दादित्थ.]<BR>—दधित्थ-रस, अस्, m. or दधित्था-<BR>ख्य (˚थ-आख्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. the resin of the<BR>above tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिषाय्य|दधिषाय्यः
दधिषाय्य, अस्, m. clarified butter; [cf. दिधि-<BR>षाय्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिस्य
दधिस्य, nom. P. दधिस्यति, &c., to wish for<BR>thick milk; [cf. दधीय and दध्यस्य below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीच|दधीचः
दधीच, अस्, m. (a later and corrupt form of<BR>दध्य्-अञ्च्, col. 2), the N. of a Ṛṣi or sage cele-<BR>brated for having devoted himself to death that the<BR>gods might be armed with his bones, (his story is<BR>told in Mahā-bh. III. 8695; the gods being op-<BR>pressed by the Kālakeya Asuras, solicited from the<BR>sage his bones, and with them Tvaṣṭṛ fabricated<BR>the thunderbolt with which Indra slew Vṛtra and<BR>routed the Asuras; the Saras-vatī receives his gene-<BR>rative energy, from which springs Sāras-vata.)<BR>—द-<BR>धीच-क्षुप-संवाद, अस्, m., N. of the thirty-<BR>fifth chapter of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीचि|दधीचिः
दधीचि, इस्, m. = दधीच.<BR>—दधीच्य्-अस्थि,<BR>n. Dadhīci's bones, the thunderbolt; the diamond,<BR>(the latter being regarded as similar in nature to<BR>the thunderbolt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीय
दधीय, nom. P. दधीयति, &c., to like sour-<BR>curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्यस्य
दध्यस्य, nom. P. दध्यस्यति, &c., to long<BR>for thick or coagulated milk; [cf. दधिस्य and<BR>दधीय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्यानी
दध्यानी, f., N. of a medicinal plant, = सु-<BR>दर्शना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधृष्
दधृष् दधृष्, क्, क्, क्, m. f. n. (reduplicated<BR>form of rt. धृष्), Ved. firm, strong, bold.<BR>—द-<BR>धृक्, ind. firmly, strongly, boldly; (according to<BR>some, this word is to be referred to rt. दृंह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधृष
दधृष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. courageous, bold,<BR>fighting bravely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधृष्वणि
दधृष्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ, = दधृष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्न|दध्नः
दध्न दध्न, अस्, m. an epithet of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्यञ्च्
दध्यञ्च् दध्य्-अञ्च्, &c. See bottom of col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्
दन् 1. दन्, Ved., explained by Sāyaṇa as<BR>a participle fr. rt. 1. दा = ददत् or दातृ, giving,<BR>bestowing; modern scholars connect this word with<BR>पति and explain पतिर्-दम् as a transposition of<BR>दम्-पति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्
दन् 2. दन्, considered by some as a Vedic<BR>root, from which they derive the Desid. दीदांसते<BR>(referred by Pāṇ. III. 1, 6, to rt. दान्, q. v.) and<BR>other forms; the meaning is said to be straight, to<BR>straighten; to correct. (In Ṛg-veda I. 174, 2,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-a" target="_blank">Page0401-a+ 78</a>]<BR>दनस् is said by Yāska to = दान-मनसस्, liberal-<BR>minded, disposed to give, see Nirukta VI. 31; but<BR>according to Sāy., दनस् = अदमयस्, thou hast<BR>humbled, or by transposition of the letters अन-<BR>दस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0400-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनायुस्
दनायुस् दनायुस्, उस्, f., N. of one of the<BR>daughters of Dakṣa, married to Kaśyapa; (ऊस्),<BR>m. (?), N. of the supposed father (?) of the Dānavas;<BR>[cf. दनु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनीध्वंस
दनीध्वंस दनीध्वंस, an adj. formed fr.<BR>Intens. of rt. ध्वंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनु|दनुः
दनु दनु, उस्, f., N. of one of the daughters<BR>of Dakṣa, wife of Kaśyapa, and mother of the<BR>demons called Dānavas, the Titans of Hindū mytho-<BR>logy; the number of these Dānavas is stated to be<BR>40 in Mahā-bh. 1. 252, but 100 &c. are reckoned<BR>in other places; (उस्), m., N. of a son of Śrī, also<BR>called Dānava; (he was originally very handsome,<BR>but having offended Indra, was changed by him into<BR>a deformed monster; see कबन्ध.)<BR>—दनु-ज,<BR>अस्, or दनु-सम्भव, अस्, or दनु-सूनु, उस्, m.<BR>a son of Danu, a Dānava.<BR>—दनुज-द्विष्, ट्, or<BR>दनुजारि (˚ज-अरि), इस्, m. an enemy of the Dānavas,<BR>a god, a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुष
दनुष, अस्, m. (?) a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त|दंत|दंतः|दन्तः
दन्त दन्त, अस्, m. (for etym. see दत्, p. 399,<BR>col. 2), a tooth, tusk, fang; an elephant's tusk, ivory;<BR>the point of an arrow; the peak of a mountain, the<BR>side or ridge of a mountain; (ई), f. a medicinal plant<BR>yielding a pungent oil, commonly Danti, Croton<BR>Polyandrum or Croton Tiglium [cf. दन्त-मूलिका<BR>and दन्तिनी]; at the end of an adj. comp. the fem.<BR>of दन्त may end in आ or ई; [cf. इभ-दन्ता,<BR>कुड्मल-दन्ती, क्रूर-दन्ती, &c.: cf. also Zend<BR>dañt-an, ‘tooth;’ Gr. ἀ-δούς, ὀ-δοντ Æol. pl.<BR>ἔδοντες; Lat. dens; Lith. dant-i-s; Goth. tunth-<BR>u-s; Angl. Sax. todh; Old Germ. zant, zand, zan;<BR>Cambro-Brit. dant; Hib. déad.]<BR>—दन्त-कर्-<BR>षण, अस्, ई, अम्, contracting the teeth, i. e. setting<BR>them on edge; (अस्), m. the common lime, Citrus<BR>Acida.<BR>—दन्त-कार, अस्, m. an artist who works<BR>in ivory.<BR>—दन्त-काष्ठ, अम्, n. a piece of stick<BR>or small twig of particular trees used as a tooth-brush<BR>or chewed to cleanse the teeth; cleaning the teeth<BR>in this manner; (अस्), m., N. of various trees, the<BR>wood of which is used for cleaning the teeth; Fla-<BR>courtia Sapida (= वि-कङ्कत); Asclepias Gigantea;<BR>Ficus Indica (= वट); Acacia Catechu; Pongamia<BR>Glabra; Terminalia Alata; [cf. दन्त-धावन.]<BR>—दन्त-काष्ठक, अस्, m. the shrub Tabernæ-<BR>montana Coronaria (= आहुल्य).<BR>—दन्तकाष्ठा-<BR>भक्षण (˚ठ-अ-भ्˚), अम्, n., N. of the 128th<BR>chapter of the Vārāha-Purāṇa.<BR>—दन्त-कुमार,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दन्त-क्रूरम्, ind. cruelly<BR>or fearfully on the teeth, fearfully with or by the<BR>teeth (e. g. to seize or strike a person in this man-<BR>ner).<BR>—दन्तग्राहि-ता, f. the state of causing injury<BR>to the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, injuring<BR>the teeth, causing them to decay &c.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>घर्ष, अस्, m. chattering or grinding of the teeth;<BR>[cf. दन्त-सङ्घर्ष and दन्त-हर्ष.]<BR>—दन्-<BR>त-घात, अस्, m. ‘a blow with the teeth,’ a bite<BR>[cf. दन्त-विघात]; N. of a man.<BR>—दन्त-चाल,<BR>अस्, m. looseness of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-च्छद,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the covering of the teeth,’ a lip [cf. दच्-<BR>छद and दशन-च्छद]; (आ), f. Momordica<BR>Monadelpha.<BR>—दन्तच्छदोपमा (˚द-उप्˚), f.<BR>Momordica Monadelpha, (to the red fruit of which<BR>the lips are often compared.)<BR>—दन्त-जात = जात-<BR>दन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having teeth,’ a child who is teeth-<BR>ing or whose teeth are just appearing; (अ-दन्तजात,<BR>having no teeth.)<BR>—दन्त-जाह, अम्, n. the root<BR>of a tooth.<BR>—दन्त-दर्शन, अम्, n. showing the<BR>teeth (as a dog does).<BR>—दन्त-धावन, अम्, n.<BR>cleaning or washing the teeth; a tooth-brush or<BR>fibrous stick for cleaning the teeth, or a piece of<BR>wood chewed for that purpose [cf. दन्त-काष्ठ];<BR>(अस्), m., N. of various trees, the wood of which is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-b" target="_blank">Page0401-b+ 81</a>]<BR>used for cleaning the teeth, Acacia Catechu, Mimu-<BR>sops Elengi (= वकुल); N. of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva by Halāyudha.<BR>—दन्तधाव-<BR>नक, अस्, m. a species of tree.<BR>—दन्तधावन-<BR>प्रकरण, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Parā-<BR>śara-smṛti-vyākhyā by Mādhava.<BR>—दन्तधावन-<BR>विधि, इस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Smṛti-kau-<BR>mudī.<BR>—दन्त-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a kind of ear-ring.<BR>—दन्त-पत्त्रक, अम्, n. a kind of jasmine (=<BR>कुन्द), Jasminum Pubescens, (the petals or leaves<BR>of the flower resembling teeth in colour and shape,<BR>and are often so compared in poetry.)<BR>—दन्त-<BR>पवन, अम्, n. a dentifrice, or a small piece of<BR>wood taken to clean the teeth; [cf. दन्त-काष्ठ<BR>and दन्त-धावन.]<BR>—दन्त-पात, अस्, m. the<BR>falling out of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-पाली, f. the gum.<BR>—दन्त-पुप्पुट or दन्त-पुप्पुटक, अस्, m.<BR>gum-boil.<BR>—दन्त-पुर, अम्, n. ‘the town of Bud-<BR>dha's tooth,’ N. of the capital of the Kaliṅgas.<BR>—दन्त-पुष्प, अस्, m. the plant Strychnos Po-<BR>tatorum, the flower of which is compared to a tooth;<BR>(अम्), n. the fruit of the above plant.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>प्रक्षालन, अम्, n. cleaning the teeth; any in-<BR>strument or means for cleaning the teeth; [cf. दन्-<BR>त-काष्ठ, दन्त-धावन, दन्त-पवन.]<BR>—दन्त-फल, अस्, m. Feronia Elephantum, =<BR>कपित्थ [cf. दधि-फल]; (आ), f. long pepper;<BR>(अम्), n. = दन्त-पुष्प, q. v.<BR>—दन्त-भङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. fracture of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-भाग, अस्,<BR>m. the fore part of an elephant's head (where the<BR>tusks appear); part of a tooth.<BR>—दन्त-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, made of ivory.<BR>—दन्त-मल, अम्, n. the<BR>tartar of the teeth, any impurity of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-मांस, अम्, n. the gums.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. the root of a tooth, the gums; a gum-<BR>boil.<BR>—दन्त-मूलिका, f. = दन्ती, Croton Polyan-<BR>drum or Croton Tiglium.<BR>—दन्तमूलीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, belonging to the root of the teeth, as the dental<BR>letters; दन्तमूलीयस् त-कार-वर्गस्, the class of<BR>letters beginning with त which are uttered from the<BR>root of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-रजस्, अस्, n. the tartar of<BR>the teeth, impurity of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-रोग, अस्,<BR>m. disease of the teeth, tooth-ache.<BR>—दन्तरोगिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, affected with tooth-ache.<BR>—दन्त-लेख-<BR>क, अस्, m. one who makes a livelihood by painting<BR>or marking the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-लोक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain in Gāndhāra.<BR>—दन्त-वक्त्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince of the Karūṣas (described as a Dānava or<BR>Asura; more correctly दन्त-वक्र).<BR>—दन्त-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having teeth, toothed.<BR>—दन्त-वल्क,<BR>अम्, n. the enamel of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-वस्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. (according to some also अस्, m.), ‘teeth-<BR>covering,’ i. e. the lip.<BR>—दन्त-वासस्, आस् (?), अस्, m. (?)<BR>n. the lip; see the preceding.<BR>—दन्त-विघात,<BR>अस्, m. = दन्त-घात, a bite.<BR>—दन्त-वीज, अस्,<BR>आ, m. f. and दन्त-वीजक, अस्, m. pomegranate;<BR>(आ), f. a kind of cucumber.<BR>—दन्त-वीणा, f. ‘a<BR>tooth-guitar,’ a kind of jew's-harp; (दन्त-वीणां<BR>वादयत्, playing this instrument; in Pañca-tantra<BR>94, 4, = making a chattering with the teeth.)<BR>—दन्-<BR>त-वेष्ट, अस्, m. the gums; (औ), m. du. the<BR>gums of the upper and lower jaw; a ring round<BR>the tusk of an elephant (?) ; tumor of the gums;<BR>see the next.<BR>—दन्त-वेष्टक, अस्, m. tumor of<BR>the gums (internal abscess accompanied with loosening<BR>of the teeth), gum-boil.<BR>—दन्त-वैदर्भ, अस्, m.<BR>loosening of the teeth through external injury.<BR>—दन्त-व्यसन, अम्, n. fracture or decay of the<BR>teeth or of a tusk.<BR>—दन्त-शङ्कु, उ, n. a pair of<BR>forceps or pincers for drawing teeth.<BR>—दन्त-शट,<BR>अस्, m. a wrong form for दन्त-शठ.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>शठ, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘bad for the teeth,’ acid; (अस्),<BR>m. sourness, acidity; N. of several trees with acid<BR>fruits; common lime (Citrus Acida), elephant or<BR>wood-apple, Feronia Elephantum, Averrhoa Caram-<BR>bola (Acida), Citrus Aurantium; (आ), f. wood-sorrel,<BR>Oxalis Pusilla, = क्षुद्राम्लिका; (अम्), n. the fruits<BR>of the above trees.<BR>—दन्त-शर्करा, f. tartar or<BR>concretion of the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-शाण, अम्, n. a<BR>dentifrice composed chiefly of the powdered fruit of<BR>the myrobalan and green sulphate of iron.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">Page0401-c+ 79</a>]<BR>शिरा, f. a back or double tooth (= माढी); the<BR>gum.<BR>—दन्त-शुद्धि, इस्, f. cleaning the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-शूल, अस्, अम्, m. n. tooth-ache.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>शोधनी, f. ‘tooth-cleanser,’ a tooth-pick.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>शोफ, अस्, m. swelling of the gum.<BR>—दन्त-श्लि-<BR>ष्ट or दन्त-सक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, entangled in or<BR>between the teeth.<BR>—दन्त-सङ्घर्ष, अस्, m.<BR>rubbing the teeth together, gnashing the teeth;<BR>[cf. दन्त-घर्ष and दन्त-हर्ष.]<BR>—दन्त-<BR>हर्ष, अस्, m. morbid sensitiveness of the teeth,<BR>intolerance of any rough or acid substances; chat-<BR>tering of the teeth; [cf. दन्त-घर्ष and दन्त-<BR>सङ्घर्ष.]<BR>—दन्त-हर्षक or दन्त-हर्-<BR>षण, अस्, m. ‘making the teeth sensitive, setting<BR>them on edge,’ the lime tree, Citrus Acida.<BR>—दन्त-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, toothless.<BR>—दन्ताग्र (˚त-अग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the top or point of a tooth.<BR>—दन्ताघात<BR>(˚त-आघ्˚), अस्, m. ‘tooth-blow’ or ‘tooth-wound,’<BR>a bite; the citron or lime tree.<BR>—दन्ताघातिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, struck with the teeth, bitten, remaining<BR>between the teeth.<BR>—दन्ताद (˚त-अद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, corroding the teeth.<BR>—दन्ता-दन्ति, ind. tooth<BR>against tooth, i. e. biting one another.<BR>—दन्तान्तर<BR>(˚त-अन्˚), अम्, n. the space between the teeth.<BR>—दन्तान्तराधिष्ठित (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sticking between the teeth.<BR>—दन्तायुध (˚त-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, m. a wild boar, a hog (‘having tusks for<BR>weapons’).<BR>—दन्तार्बुद (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>gum-boil, ulceration of the gums.<BR>—दन्तालय (˚त-<BR>आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘the abode of the teeth,’ i. e. the<BR>mouth.<BR>—दन्तालिका or दन्ताली (˚त-आल्˚), f. a<BR>horse's bridle or bit; [cf. 1. आलि.]<BR>—दन्तोच्-<BR>छिष्ट (˚त-उच्˚), अम्, n. the remains of food<BR>lodged between the teeth.<BR>—दन्तोद्भेद (˚त-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. appearance of the teeth, dentition.<BR>—दन्तो-<BR>लूखलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, or दन्तोलूखलिन् (˚त-उल्˚),<BR>ई, इनी, इ, ‘one who uses his teeth as a mortar,’ one<BR>who grinds his grain between the teeth, i. e. eats it<BR>before being ground, an anchorite.<BR>—दन्तोष्ठक<BR>(˚त-ओष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who attends to or takes<BR>care of his teeth and lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तक|दंतक|दन्तकः
दन्तक = दन्त, a tooth &c. (at the end of a<BR>comp., cf. अ-दन्तक, कृमि-द्˚, श्याव-द्˚); (अस्),<BR>m. a jagged peak or projection in a rock or moun-<BR>tain; a bracket, a pin or shelf projecting from a<BR>wall; (अस्, आ, अम्), paying attention to one's teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तावल|दंतावल|दंतावलः|दन्तावलः
दन्तावल or दन्ताबल, अस्, m. an elephant<BR>(? for दन्त-वल = दन्तिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्ति
दन्ति, इस्, m. (probably) an epithet of Gaṇeśa;<BR>[cf. एक-दन्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिका
दन्तिका or दन्तिजा = दन्ती below; [cf. गुच्छ-<BR>दन्तिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिन्|दंतिन्
दन्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having teeth, toothed, tusked;<BR>(ई), m. an elephant; a mountain; (इनी), f. = दन्ती<BR>below.<BR>—दन्ति-दन्त, अस्, m. an elephant's tusk,<BR>ivory.<BR>—दन्तिदन्त-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>ivory.<BR>—दन्ति-मद, अस्, m. the juice flowing from<BR>the temples of a rutting elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिल
दन्तिल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्ती
दन्ती, f. the plant Croton Polyandrum; see above<BR>under दन्त; [cf. दन्तिका and दन्तिजा.]<BR>—दन्ती-<BR>वीज, अम्, n. a strongly purgative nut, the fruit of<BR>the Croton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुर|दंतुर|दन्तुरः
दन्तुर, अस्, आ, अम्, having long or projecting<BR>teeth; jagged, notched, serrated, uneven; waving,<BR>undulatory; rising (as hair), bristling.<BR>—दन्तुर-<BR>च्छद, अस्, m. the lime tree (‘having prickly leaves’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुरक
दन्तुरक, अस्, आ, अम्, having prominent teeth;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people living to the east of<BR>Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुरित|दंतुरित
दन्तुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, having prominent teeth,<BR>toothed, notched, bristling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तूल
दन्तूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having teeth, furnished with<BR>teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त्य|दंत्य|दन्त्यः
दन्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, dental, of or belonging to<BR>the teeth, produced on the teeth; suitable to the<BR>teeth; [cf. अ-द्˚.]<BR>—दन्त्योष्ठ्य or दन्त्यौ-<BR>ष्ठ्य (˚य-ओष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, denti-labial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकूर|दंतकूर|दन्तकूरः
दन्तकूर दन्तकूर, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0401-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दश|दंदश|दंदशः|दन्दशः
दन्दश दन्दश, अस्, m. (fr. Intens. of rt.<BR>2. दंश्), a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दशूक|दंदशूक|दन्दशूकः
दन्दशूक, अस्, आ, अम्, mordacious, biting, mis-<BR>chievous, malignant, venomous; (अस्), m. a snake,<BR>serpent; a particular kind of serpent; N. of a hell<BR>infested by serpents; a Rākṣasa, a demon or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्द्रम
दन्द्रम दन्द्रम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. द्रम्), going tortuously or slowly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्द्रमण
दन्द्रमण, अम्, n. the act of going tortu-<BR>ously; (अस्, आ, अम्), who or what goes tortuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्व्
दन्व् दन्व्, cl. 1. P. दन्वति, &c., to go<BR>or move; [cf. 1. दु, धन्व्, धाव्;<BR>Gr. δονέω = Caus. दन्वयामि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दफारबाह्लीक
दफारबाह्लीक दफारबाह्लीक, N. of a place<BR>mentioned in the Romaka-siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्
दभ् दभ् (connected with rt. दम्भ्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. 5. P. दभति, दभ्नोति,<BR>&c., to hurt, injure, destroy; to go; cl. 10. P.<BR>दाभयति or दम्भयति, &c., to send, impel, order,<BR>command; [cf. Gr. θάμβος, ἔταφον, τέθηπα; Old<BR>Germ. tepyan or depyan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दब्धि|दब्धिः
दब्धि, इस्, f., Ved. injury, hurt, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ|दभः
दभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. injuring, hurting; (अस्),<BR>m. deception, deceiving, (only occurring in dat. case,<BR>दभाय used for inf.; cf. अ-दभ, दम्भ,<BR>दूडभ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभीति
दभीति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. injuring, an enemy;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a being protected by the Aśvins<BR>and especially by Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्य
दभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be hurt or injured,<BR>to be deceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, little, small, deficient; (अस्), m.<BR>the sea, ocean; (अम्), ind. a little, slightly.<BR>—द-<BR>भ्र-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or दभ्र-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, little-minded, weak-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
दम् 1. दम्, cl. 4. P. दाम्यति, ददाम,<BR>दमितुम्, to be tamed or subdued; to be<BR>tranquillized; to tame, subdue, conquer, subject, con-<BR>trol, restrain; to quiet, pacify: Pass. दम्यते (Aor.<BR>अदमि): Caus. P. A. दमयति, -ते, &c., to subdue,<BR>overpower, conquer; [cf. Gr. δάμνημι, δαμνάω, δαμνάζω<BR>δάμ-αρ, δαμάλη-ς, δμώς, δαμάω = Caus. द-<BR>मयामि; Lat. domare, damnum, damnare; Goth.<BR>tamyan, ‘to tame,’ ga-timan; Angl. Sax. tam, tam-<BR>yan; Old Germ. zami, zam; Mod. Germ. zahm,<BR>ziemen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
2. दम् (in comp.) = दम, a house.<BR>—दम्-<BR>पति, इस्, m., Ved. the master or lord of the house,<BR>a master or lord in general; (ई), du. wife and hus-<BR>band; (in this case the compound is by modern<BR>scholars explained as = ‘the two masters;’ but accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. and others दम् is here = जाया, a wife;<BR>cf. Gr. δεσπότης.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम, अस्, अम्, m. n., Ved. house, home, (pro-<BR>perly ‘domain,’ the place of the husband's do-<BR>minion); the inmates of a house [cf. Gr. δόμος,<BR>δέμω; Lat. domus; Goth. timryan; Angl. Sax.<BR>timber, timbrian]; (अस्, आ, अम्), (at the end of<BR>comp.) taming, subduing, see अरिन्-दम; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of several men; of a Maharṣi; of one of the<BR>three sons of Bhīma, king of Vidarbha; taming,<BR>subduing; self-command, self-restraint, self-control,<BR>endurance of painful austerities, temperance, sub-<BR>duing the passions; punishing, punishment, chastise-<BR>ment, fine, mulct, a N. of Prajā-pati (?); mud,<BR>mire (?) .<BR>—दम-कर्तृ, ता, m. a ruler.<BR>—दम-<BR>घोष, अस्, m. a prince of the lunar race, king of<BR>Cedi, father of Śiśu-pāla.<BR>—दमघोष-सुत, अस्,<BR>m., N. of Śiśu-pāla, the enemy of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—दम-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of self-control.<BR>—दम-<BR>स्वसृ, आ, f. ‘the sister of Dama,’ a N. of Dama-<BR>yantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमक|दमकः
दमक, अस्, आ, अम्, taming, a tamer, subduer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथ|दमथः
दमथ, अस्, अम्, m. n. self-restraint, self-con-<BR>trol, taming, subduing, endurance of rigorous aus-<BR>terities, subduing the senses, suppressing the passions;<BR>punishment, punishing, chastising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथु|दमथुः
दमथु, उस्, m. self-restraint, self-subjugation;<BR>self-denial, subjection; punishment, punishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन, अस्, ई, अम्, taming, subduing, over-<BR>powering, (at the end of a comp., e. g. शत्रु-द्˚);<BR>tranquil, passionless, a philosopher; (अस्), m. a sub-<BR>duer, a tamer of horses, a charioteer; N. of a son<BR>of Vasu-deva and Rohiṇī; of a Brahmarṣi; of a<BR>son of Bharad-vāja; of an old king; of a son of<BR>Bhīma, king of Vidarbha; the flower Artemisia<BR>Indica, commonly called Donā; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>plant, = अग्नि-दमनी, Solanum Jacquini; (अम्), n.<BR>taming, subduing, subjugation, restraining, chastising,<BR>punishing, self-restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनक|दमनकः
दमनक, अस्, m., N. of a man; N. of a<BR>jackal; Artemisia Indica, = दमन; N. of a metre<BR>consisting of four lines of six short syllables each;<BR>N. of another metre of four lines of ten short sylla-<BR>bles and one long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनीय
दमनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, tamable, to be restrained<BR>or subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन्य
दमन्य, Nom. P. दमन्यति, &c., Ved. to<BR>subdue, overpower, conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयत्
दमयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, subduing, taming, re-<BR>straining, chastising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयन्तिका
दमयन्तिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयन्ती|दमयंती
दमयन्ती, f. (‘subduing men’), N. of a beauti-<BR>ful woman who was the daughter of Bhīma, king of<BR>Vidarbha, and wife of Nala, whose story forms the<BR>subject of a celebrated episode of the Mahā-bhārata;<BR>(according to some) = Śākya-muni in a former birth;<BR>a kind of cucumber, see भद्र-मल्लिका.<BR>—दम-<BR>यन्ती-कथा, f. ‘the story of Damayantī,’ N. of a<BR>song.<BR>—दमयन्ती-काव्य, अम्, n. ‘poem of Da-<BR>mayantī,’ N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयितृ
दमयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a tamer, subduer, sub-<BR>duing; a punisher, chastiser; epithet of Viṣṇu and<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमाय
दमाय, Nom. P. दमायति, &c., Ved. to restrain<BR>or control one's self; to subdue, overpower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमित|दमितः
दमित, अस्, आ, अम् (or दान्त, q. v.), tamed,<BR>subdued, patient of every suffering or exaction or<BR>privation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमितृ
दमितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. a tamer, subduer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमित्वा
दमित्वा or दान्त्वा, ind. having subdued or<BR>tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमिन्
दमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, tamed, subdued, subduing the<BR>passions; taming, subduing, a tamer; (इ), n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमुनस्
दमुनस्, आस्, m., N. of Agni, the god of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमूनस्
दमूनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. belonging to the<BR>house or family, devoted to the house or family;<BR>a friend of the house; epithet of Agni, Savitṛ, Indra,<BR>&c.; (Sāy.) of subdued mind, docile. In Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 42, 12, the pl. is regarded by Sāy. as an epithet<BR>of the Ṛbhus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
1. दम्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fut. pass. part.), to be<BR>tamed, tamable, to be subjected or controlled; to be<BR>punished, punishable; (अस्), m. a young bullock; a<BR>steer that has to be tamed.<BR>—दम्य-सारथि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘the guide of those who have to be restrained,’<BR>an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
2. दम्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. दम), Ved. being in<BR>a house, being at home, homely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमावन्दु
दमावन्दु दमावन्दु, N. of a place men-<BR>tioned in the Romaka-siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्पति|दंपति
दम्पति दम्-पति. See under 2. दम्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ्|दंभ्
दम्भ् दम्भ् (connected with rt. दभ्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. 5. P. दभति, दभ्नोति,<BR>ददम्भ or ददाभ or देभ (pl. ददम्भुस्<BR>or देभुस्), दम्भिष्यति, अदम्भीत्, दम्भितुम्,<BR>Ved. inf. आ-दभे, to seek to injure, to hurt, injure,<BR>cause damage; to act deceitfully, cheat, impose upon,<BR>trick, deceive: Caus. P. A. दम्भयति, -ते, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अददम्भत्, to destroy, strike down; A. to<BR>collect, gather, arrange, string: Desid. दिदम्भि-<BR>षति, धिप्सति, धीप्सति, Ved. दिप्सति or दीप्सति,<BR>to wish to hurt or injure, desire to destroy; to have<BR>the power to deceive or destroy: Intens. दादभ्-<BR>यते, दादम्ब्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः|दम्भः
दम्भ, अस्, m. deceit, fraud, cheating, trickery,<BR>feigning hypocrisy, sanctimony; arrogance, osten-<BR>tation, pride; sin, wickedness; Deceit personified<BR>as a son of A-dharma and Mṛṣā; an epithet of<BR>Śiva; Indra's thunderbolt.<BR>—दम्भ-चर्या, f. de-<BR>ceit, hypocrisy.<BR>—दम्भोद्भव (˚भ-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king whose story is told in Mahā-bh.<BR>Udyoga-parva 3473, (he fought with two hermits<BR>but was worsted.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भक|दंभक
दम्भक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of comp.)<BR>cheating, deceiving, deluding; [cf. काम-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भन|दंभन|दंभनं
दम्भन, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comp.)<BR>injuring, damaging, subduing [cf. अमित्र-दम्-<BR>भन, सपत्न-द्˚]; (अस्), m. cheating, deceiving,<BR>deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भिन्|दंभिन्
दम्भिन्, ई, इनी, इ, acting deceitfully, hypocritical,<BR>wicked, proud; (ई), m. a hypocrite, a deceiver, an<BR>impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भोलि|दंभोलि|दंभोलिः|दम्भोलिः
दम्भोलि, इस्, m. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
दम्य दम्य. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय्
दय् दय् [cf. rt. 3. दा], cl. 1. A. दयते,<BR>दयाञ्-चक्रे, दयितुम्, to divide, impart,<BR>allot, grant, give, (according to Pāṇ. II. 3, 52, re-<BR>quiring the gen. case); to partake, possess; to divide<BR>asunder, destroy, kill, hurt; to take part in, be in-<BR>terested in, sympathise with, have pity on, love,<BR>protect (with acc. or gen.); to repent; to go, move:<BR>Intens. दन्दय्यते and दादय्यते; [cf. Gr. δαίομαι<BR>δαίνυμι, δαῖς: Hib. deidh, f. ‘desire, longing;’<BR>deidh, m. ‘a protector, defender;’ deide, ‘obedi-<BR>ence, submission.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयमान
दयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, dividing, having pity on,<BR>preserving, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दया
दया, f. taking interest in, sympathy, compas-<BR>sion, pity, mercy, tenderness, love, clemency, pity<BR>for (with loc. or gen., e. g. मयि or मम द-<BR>यां कुरु, take pity on me); Pity personified as a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa, wife of Dharma, and mother<BR>of Abhaya. (According to some, the form दय,<BR>अस्, m. occurs; and according to others, दय may<BR>be used as an adj. meaning ‘compassionate;’ cf.<BR>अ-दय, निर्-द्˚, स-द्˚.)<BR>—दया-कर, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, showing pity or compassion, sympathis-<BR>ing, kind; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—दया-<BR>कूर्च, अस्, m. a Buddha or a form of Buddha,<BR>the founder of the Buddhist religion.<BR>—दया-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, pitiful, compassionate.<BR>—दया-निधि,<BR>इस्, m. a treasure of mercy, a very compassion-<BR>ate person.<BR>—दयान्वित (˚या-अन्˚) or दया-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, full of pity, pitiful, compassionate,<BR>benevolent.<BR>—दया-राम, अस्, m., N. of several<BR>men.<BR>—दया-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pitiful, merciful,<BR>tender, compassionate, taking pity on (with loc. or<BR>gen.).<BR>—दया-वीर, अस्, m. a hero in compassion,<BR>a very merciful man.<BR>—दया-शङ्कर, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—दया-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, tender-hearted,<BR>compassionate.<BR>—दयोर्मि (˚या-ऊर्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having<BR>compassion for (its) waves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालु|दयालुः
दयालु, उस्, उस्, उ, or दयालुक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pitiful, merciful, compassionate, kind, tender, taking<BR>pity on (with loc.).<BR>—दयालु-ता, f. or दयालु-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. pitifulness, tenderness, compassionateness,<BR>pity for (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयित|दयितं|दयितः
दयित, अस्, आ, अम्, desired, cherished, beloved,<BR>dear; (अस्), m. ‘the loved one,’ a husband, a lover;<BR>(आ), f. a wife or mistress, a woman.<BR>—दयिताधीन<BR>(˚ता-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, subject to a wife, hen-pecked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयित्नु
दयित्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. pitiful, compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर|दरं|दरः
दर दर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. दॄ; at the end<BR>of comp.) cleaving, rending, splitting, cutting open,<BR>opening, breaking [cf. पुरन्-द्˚]; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>f. n. a hole in the ground, a cave, cavity; a conch-<BR>shell; (ई), f. a natural or artificial excavation in a<BR>mountain, a cave, a cavern, a grotto, &c.; a valley;<BR>(अस्), m. a stream [cf. असृग्-द्˚]; fear, terror, dread,<BR>despair; (अस्, आ, अम्), little, small; (अम्), ind. a<BR>little.<BR>—दर-कण्टिका, f. the plant Asparagus Race-<BR>mosa (= शतावरी).<BR>—दर-तिमिर, अम्, n. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">Page0403-a+ 79</a>]<BR>darkness of fear.<BR>—दर-मन्थर, अस्, आ, अम्, a<BR>little slow.<BR>—दर-मुकुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, a little<BR>budded.<BR>—दर-विदलित, अस्, आ, अम्, slightly burst<BR>or opened.<BR>—दर-व्रीडा, f. slight shame.<BR>—दर-<BR>श्लथ, अस्, आ, अम्, a little loose.<BR>—दरी-भू, ऊस्, f.<BR>a cavern, a hollow.<BR>—दरी-भृत्, त्, m. ‘having<BR>caves,’ a mountain.<BR>—दरी-मुख, अम्, n. a mouth<BR>like a cave; a cave like a mouth; the opening of<BR>a cave; (अस्, ई, अम्), having a mouth as large as a<BR>cave; (अस्), m., N. of a monkey.<BR>—दरी-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, containing caves, cavernous, abounding in<BR>caves.<BR>—दरेन्द्र (˚र-इन्˚), अस्, m. Viṣṇu's conch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0402-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरण|दरणं
दरण, अम्, n. the act of cleaving, rending,<BR>splitting, tearing, breaking; breaking off, falling<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरणि|दरणिः
दरणि, इस्, इस्, m. f. breaking; an eddy; a cur-<BR>rent; breakers, surf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरथ|दरथः
दरथ, अस्, m. a cavity, cave; running away,<BR>taking flight; spreading over the country for forage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद्
दरद्, त्, m., N. of a people; (त्), f. the heart;<BR>a bank, mound; a mountain; a precipice; terror,<BR>fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद|दरदं|दरदः
दरद, आस्, m. pl. a country bordering on<BR>Kaśmīr, the mountains about Kaśmīr and above<BR>Peshāwar; the inhabitants of this country; (अस्), m.<BR>the king or chief of the Daradas; (अस्), m. fear,<BR>terror; (अम्), n. red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरि|दरिः
दरि, इस्, इस्, इ, splitting, rending, opening [cf.<BR>गो-द्˚]; (इस्), m., N. of a Nāga; (इस्), f. a cave.<BR>(For दरी see under दर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरित|दरितः
दरित, अस्, आ, अम्, frightened, terrified, timid;<BR>torn, rent, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्तृ|दर्त्तृ
दर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or दर्त्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>a breaker, render, splitting, breaking, one who splits,<BR>breaks, or opens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दर|दर्दरः|दर्द्दरः
दर्दर, अस्, आ, अम्, cracked, broken, burst,<BR>flawed, slightly broken; (अस्), m. a mountain (‘con-<BR>taining caves’); N. of a mountain (also दर्दुर);<BR>a kind of drum.<BR>—दर्दराम्र (˚र-आम्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a sort of sauce or condiment (= मीनाम्रीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दरीक|दर्दरीकः|दर्द्दरीकं|दर्द्दरीकः
दर्दरीक, अस्, m. a frog; a cloud; a kind of<BR>musical instrument; (अम्), n. any musical instru-<BR>ment; [cf. दर्वरीक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुर|दर्दुरः|दर्द्दुर|दर्द्दुरं|दर्द्दुरः
दर्दुर, अस्, m. (perhaps an onomatopoetic<BR>word), a frog [cf. दार्दुर and दार्दुरिक]; a sort<BR>of musical instrument, a pipe or flute; the sound of<BR>a drum; a cloud; a sort of rice; a mountain; N.<BR>of a mountain in the south (sometimes associated with<BR>the mountain Malaya); N. of a man; of a gamester;<BR>(आ or ई), f. a N. of Durgā; (अम्), n. an assem-<BR>blage of villages, a district, a province.<BR>—दर्दुर-<BR>च्छदा, f. or दर्दुर-पर्णी, f., N. of a plant, =<BR>ब्राह्मी.<BR>—दर्दुर-पुट, अस्, m. the mouth or<BR>extremity of a pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुरक|दर्दुरकं
दर्दुरक, अस्, m., N. of a gamester; [cf. द-<BR>रोदर and दुरोदर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दू
दर्दू, ऊस्, or दर्द्रु, उस्, or दर्द्रू, ऊस्, m.<BR>(according to some fr. दरिद्रा), = दद्रु, cutaneous<BR>and herpetic eruptions, especially a kind of leprosy.<BR>—दर्द्रु-घ्न, अस्, m. = दद्रु-घ्न, the shrub<BR>Cassia Tora; Psoralea Corylifolia.<BR>—दर्द्रु-नाशिनी,<BR>f. a kind of insect, = तैलिनी.<BR>—दर्द्रु-रोगिन् or<BR>दर्द्रू-रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, afflicted with cutaneous<BR>eruptions, herpetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रुण|दर्द्रुणः
दर्द्रुण or दर्द्रूण, अस्, आ, अम्, having cu-<BR>taneous eruptions, herpetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रा
दरिद्रा दरिद्रा (reduplicated form of<BR>rt. 1. द्रा; according to some, an old<BR>Intens. form; perhaps connected with rt. दॄ), cl. 2.<BR>P. दरिद्राति (दरिद्रिवस्, दरिद्रितस्, 3rd pl. द-<BR>रिद्रति), दरिद्राञ्-चकार or ददरिद्रौ, दरि-<BR>द्रिष्यति, अदरिद्रीत् and अदरिद्रासीत्, दरिद्रि-<BR>तुम्, to be poor or needy, to be in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्र|दरिद्रः
दरिद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, poor, needy, indigent, dis-<BR>tressed, a poor person, beggar; (Ved.) unsteady,<BR>roving, strolling.<BR>—दरिद्र-ता, f. or दरिद्र-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. poverty, indigence, penury.<BR>—दरिद्र-<BR>निन्दा, f., N. of the twenty-fifth chapter of the<BR>Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्राण|दरिद्राणं
दरिद्राण, अम्, n. the state of being poor,<BR>poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रायक|दरिद्रायकः
दरिद्रायक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, poor, needy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रित|दरिद्रितः
दरिद्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, impoverished, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रितृ
दरिद्रितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, poor, distressed, needy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरोदर|दरोदरं|दरोदरः
दरोदर दरोदर, अस्, m. = दुरोदर, a<BR>gamester [cf. दर्दुर and दर्दुरक]; a stake<BR>at play; (अम्), n. gambling, playing at dice; a<BR>die, dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दर|दर्दरः|दर्द्दरः
दर्दर दर्दर, दर्दरीक, दर्दुर. See<BR>last col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्प|दर्पः
दर्प दर्प, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. दृप् or 2. दृप्;<BR>according to some, also अम्, n.), pride, arrogance,<BR>haughtiness, insolence, rashness, temerity; vanity, con-<BR>ceit; sullenness, sulkiness; Pride &c. personified as a<BR>son of Śrī, or of A-dharma and Śrī, or of Dharma and<BR>Lakṣmī, or of Unnati; heat; musk; [cf. अति-द्˚<BR>and स-द्˚.]<BR>—दर्प-च्छिद्, त्, त्, त्, destroying pride,<BR>humbling.<BR>—दर्प-द, अस्, m., N. of Śiva.<BR>—दर्-<BR>प-ध्मात, अस्, आ, अम्, puffed up or swelling with<BR>pride.<BR>—दर्प-नारायण, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—दर्प-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. a kind of grass; [cf. दर्-<BR>भ-पत्त्र.]<BR>—दर्प-पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, full of<BR>pride.<BR>—दर्प-सार, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दर्-<BR>प-ह or दर्प-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, pride-destroying,<BR>humbling, humiliating.<BR>—दर्प-हन्, आ, m., N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—दर्पारम्भ (˚प-आर्˚), अस्, m. beginning<BR>of pride, incipient pride, conceit.<BR>—दर्पोपशान्ति<BR>(˚प-उप्˚), इस्, f. allaying pride, conciliating or sub-<BR>duing arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पक|दर्पकः
दर्पक, अस्, आ, अम्, making proud, inflaming,<BR>exciting, an inflamer; (अस्), m. a N. of Kāma-deva,<BR>god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पण|दर्पणं|दर्पणः
दर्पण, अस्, m. ‘causing vanity or pride,’ a<BR>looking-glass, mirror, (sometimes occurring at the<BR>end of comp. or titles of books, e. g. कर्ण-द्˚,<BR>ज्ञान-द्˚, साहित्य-द्˚, q. v.); a N. of Śiva [cf.<BR>दर्प-द]; N. of a mountain inhabited by Kuvera<BR>and of a river rising there; (अम्), n. the eye;<BR>kindling, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पित
दर्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, made proud, arrogant; in-<BR>flamed.<BR>—दर्पित-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पिन्
दर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, proud, arrogant, insolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भ|दर्भः
दर्भ दर्भ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. दृभ्; said<BR>to be fr. rt. दॄ), a bundle of grass, tuft or bunch<BR>of grass; N. of various kinds of grass used at sacri-<BR>ficial ceremonies, especially of the Kuśa grass, Poa<BR>Cynosuroides; Saccharum Spontaneum; Saccharum<BR>Cylindricum; (the first kind or Kuśa grass was held<BR>very sacred; it was used to strew the ground in<BR>preparing for a sacrifice, the officiating Brāhmans<BR>being purified by sitting on it; under the name Darbha<BR>it was even addressed as a deity; its various sancti-<BR>fying qualities are described in Manu II. 43, III.<BR>208, IV. 36, &c.; cf. कुश, काश, मुञ्ज, वल्व-ज,<BR>शर); N. of a man; [cf. Old Germ. zurba, zurft;<BR>Mod. Germ. torf; Eng. turf.]<BR>—दर्भ-कुसुम,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of insect (= दर्भ-पुष्प).<BR>—दर्-<BR>भ-चीर, अम्, n. a dress of Kuśa grass.<BR>—दर्भ-त-<BR>रुणक, अम्, n., Ved. a young shoot of Kuśa grass.<BR>—दर्भ-पत्त्र, अस्, m. a kind of grass, Saccha-<BR>rum Spontaneum (= काश).<BR>—दर्भ-पुञ्जील =<BR>दर्भ-पिञ्जूल, अम्, n., Ved. a bunch or bundle<BR>of Kuśa grass.<BR>—दर्भ-पुष्प, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>serpent; a kind of insect, ‘similar to the Darbha<BR>flower;’ [cf. दर्भ-कुसुम.]<BR>—दर्भ-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, made of Kuśa or Darbha grass.<BR>—दर्भ-<BR>मुष्टि, इस्, m. f. a handful of Kuśa grass.<BR>—दर्भ-<BR>संस्तर, अस्, m. a bed of Darbha grass.<BR>—दर्भ-<BR>स्तम्ब, अस्, m. a cluster or bunch of Kuśa grass.<BR>—दर्भाह्वय (˚भ-आह्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>grass; [cf. मुञ्ज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भर
दर्भर, अस्, m. (?), a kind of bird, = लावा,<BR>Perdix Chinensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भि
दर्भि, इस्, m. or दर्भिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भट|दर्भटं
दर्भट दर्भट, अम्, n. a private apartment<BR>or house, a retired room; [cf. दार्वट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वट|दर्वटः|दर्व्वट|दर्व्वटः
दर्वट, अस्, m. a door-keeper, warder, village<BR>constable, police officer; [cf. गर्वाट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्म|दर्म्म
दर्म दर्म, अस्, or दर्मन्, आ, m. (fr. rt.<BR>दॄ), Ved. a destroyer, demolisher; a tearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्यक
दर्यक दर्यक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्व|दर्वः|दर्व्वः
दर्व दर्व, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. दॄ), a<BR>ladle, spoon (at the end of comp., e. g. पूर्ण-द्˚, q. v.);<BR>the hood of a snake [cf. दर्वि below]; a Rākṣasa,<BR>an imp, goblin; a mischievous man, a rapacious<BR>animal, &c.; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people [cf. दार्व];<BR>(आ), f., N. of a wife of Uśīnara; (sometimes written<BR>दर्बा; cf. दार्वन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वि|दर्विः|दर्व्विः
दर्वि or दर्बि, इस्, f. (in later Sanskrit also दर्वी<BR>or दर्बी, f.; acc. in Ved. दर्व्यम् or दर्वीम्), a<BR>ladle, spoon; the expanded hood of a snake; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a country.<BR>—दर्वि-होम or दर्वी-होम,<BR>अस्, m. an oblation made with a ladle; [cf. दार्वी-<BR>हौमिक.]<BR>—दर्विहोमिन्, relating to the preceding<BR>oblation.<BR>—दर्वी-कर, अस्, m. (scil. सर्प), a class<BR>of snakes with expanded hoods, of which twenty-six<BR>species are enumerated.<BR>—दर्वी-सङ्क्रमण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्विक|दर्विकः|दर्व्विकः
दर्विक or दर्बिक, अस्, आ, m. f. a ladle, a spoon;<BR>(आ), f. a pot-herb; a kind of collyrium; [cf. दार्-<BR>विका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वट|दर्वटः|दर्व्वट|दर्व्वटः
दर्वट दर्वट. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वरीक|दर्वरीकः|दर्व्वरीकः
दर्वरीक दर्वरीक, अस्, m. a kind of musical<BR>instrument; air, wind; an epithet of Indra; [cf.<BR>दर्दरीक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्वि|दर्विः|दर्व्विः
दर्वि दर्वि or दर्वी. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्विदा
दर्विदा दर्विदा, f., Ved. a species of bird,<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara) = काष्ठ-कुट्ट, a sort<BR>of woodpecker; (perhaps corrupted fr. दारु-विध;<BR>cf. दार्वाघाट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श|दर्शः
दर्श दर्श, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. दृश्), looking<BR>at, viewing, seeing, perceiving, showing, having a<BR>view, (generally at the end of comp., see अवसान-<BR>द्˚, आदिनव-द्˚, आत्म-द्˚, तत्त्व-द्˚); (अस्), m.<BR>sight, view, seeing, appearance, (generally at the<BR>end of comp., see प्रिय-द्˚, दुर्-द्˚); the moon<BR>when only just becoming visible, the new moon;<BR>day of new moon; the festival of new moon; half<BR>monthly sacrifice (performed at the change of the<BR>moon by persons maintaining a perpetual fire); New<BR>Moon or Day of New Moon, personified as a son<BR>of Dhātṛ and Sinīvalī.<BR>—दर्श-प, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>drinking the new moon oblation.<BR>—दर्श-पूर्ण-<BR>मासौ, m. du. new and full moon, the days and the<BR>ceremonies which precede all other ceremonies.<BR>—दर्-<BR>श-याग, अस्, m. a sacrifice or ceremony on the day<BR>of new moon.<BR>—दर्श-यामिनी, f. the night of new<BR>moon on which it rises hardly visible.<BR>—दर्श-<BR>विपद्, त्, m. the moon (‘as having the misfortune to<BR>be hardly visible when new’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शक|दर्शकः
दर्शक, अस्, आ or इका, अम्, seeing, looking at,<BR>a spectator; examining, searching; who or what<BR>shows or displays or explains or makes clear; (अस्),<BR>m. a door-keeper, a warder; a shower, exhibiter,<BR>discoverer, one who points out; a skilful man, one<BR>conversant with any science or art; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शत|दर्शतः
दर्शत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. visible, striking the<BR>eye, beautiful; conspicuous; (अस्), m. the sun; the<BR>moon.<BR>—दर्शत-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. of conspicuous<BR>beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शन|दर्शनं
दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, seeing, looking, (at the end of<BR>comp., e. g. तुल्य-द्˚, देव-द्˚, धर्म-द्˚); show-<BR>ing, exhibiting, demonstrating, teaching; (ई), f. epithet<BR>of Durgā, ‘as showing the way or leading;’ (अम्),<BR>n. seeing, observing, looking; sight, vision, observa-<BR>tion; inspection, examination; perception; the being<BR>or becoming visible; the act of showing [cf. दन्-<BR>त-द्˚]; exhibition; appearance, aspect, semblance,<BR>colour; visiting, visiting a sacred shrine, worshipping<BR>in the presence of an image; going into the presence<BR>of (e. g. दर्शनं कृ, to visit, to go into any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">Page0404-a+ 80</a>]<BR>one's presence; cf. पुण्य-दर्शन); a view or<BR>theory prescribed in a system or book (e. g. शास्त्र-<BR>दर्शनात्, in the manner prescribed in the Śāstras);<BR>experiencing; seeing in the mind, mental or spiritual<BR>vision, foreseeing, divining; contemplating; a vision,<BR>a dream; apprehension, judgment; discernment,<BR>understanding, intellect; knowledge, religious know-<BR>ledge; opinion; intention; doctrine, demonstration,<BR>a Śāstra, a N. applied to the six recognized systems<BR>of philosophy (viz. 1. Pūrva-mīmāṃsā, usually called<BR>Mīmāṃsā by Jaimini; 2. Uttara-mīmāṃsā, usually<BR>called Vedānta by Vyāsa or Bādarāyaṇa; 3. Nyāya<BR>by Gotama; 4. Vaiśeṣika by Kaṇāda; 5. Sāṅkhya<BR>by Kapila; 6. Yoga by Patañjali; cf. तर्क); virtue,<BR>moral merit; the eye; a mirror [cf. आ-द्˚]; a sacri-<BR>fice, oblation [cf. दन्त-द्˚]; (ई), f. a kind of insect<BR>(= तैल-कीट).<BR>—दर्शन-पथ, अस्, m. ‘the path<BR>of the sight,’ the range of sight or view, horizon.<BR>—दर्शन-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दर्-<BR>शन-प्रतिभू, ऊस्, m. bail or surety for appearance.<BR>—दर्शन-प्रातिभाव्य, अम्, n. surety for appear-<BR>ance, bail.<BR>—दर्शन-भूमि, इस्, f. the region or<BR>range of perception; (with Buddhists) one of the<BR>periods in the life of a Śrāvaka.<BR>—दर्शन-लालस,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, longing to see, ardently desirous of<BR>beholding.<BR>—दर्शनेप्सु (˚न-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>anxious to see.<BR>—दर्शनोज्ज्वला (˚न-उज्˚), f. ‘of<BR>brilliant aspect,’ great white jasmine.<BR>—दर्शनोप-<BR>निषद् (˚न-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0403-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीय|दर्शनीयः
दर्शनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, visible, to beseen; observable,<BR>perceptible, conspicuous; worthy of being seen, good-<BR>looking, beautiful, agreeable, handsome; to be made<BR>to appear before a court of justice, to be produced<BR>in court; (अस्), m. Asclepias Gigantea.<BR>—दर्श-<BR>नीय-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most worthy of being seen,<BR>very beautiful.<BR>—दर्शनीय-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, think-<BR>ing one's self good-looking, vain, conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितुकाम
दर्शयितु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितृ
दर्शयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, showing, exhibiting, dis-<BR>playing, a shower, exhibiter, director, instructor, show-<BR>man, guide; (ता), m. a warder, usher, door-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयित्वा
दर्शयित्वा, ind. having shown or exhibited, hav-<BR>ing made manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयिष्यत्
दर्शयिष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, intending or pro-<BR>posing to show or explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शित|दर्शितः
दर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, shown, displayed, exhibited,<BR>exposed to view; explained; seen, understood;<BR>visible, apparent.<BR>—दर्शित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>shown or explained or taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शिन्
दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of comp.) seeing,<BR>a spectator, looking, looking at, inspecting, observ-<BR>ing, examining, perceiving, apprehending; knowing,<BR>understanding; seeing or knowing (the hymns of<BR>the Veda); experiencing, looking, appearing, having<BR>an aspect; causing to see, showing, exhibiting, teach-<BR>ing, causing to experience or suffer; [cf. अनीचि-द्˚,<BR>अमोघ-द्˚, क्षेम-द्˚, पाप-द्˚, &c.]<BR>—दर्शि-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of seeing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शिवस्
दर्शिवस्, आन्, m. (perf. part. fr. rt. 1. दृश् without<BR>reduplication; always at the end of comp., and usually<BR>at the end of a verse), a seer, one who has seen, one<BR>who sees or knows or understands (e. g. अर्जुन-<BR>दर्शिवान्, one who has seen Arjuna; cf. दीर्घ-द्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श्य
दर्श्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of being shown<BR>or exhibited; worthy of being seen, conspicuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्
दल् दल् (connected with rt. दॄ), cl. 1.<BR>P. दलति, ददाल, अदालीत्, दलितुम्, to<BR>burst open, split, crack, to be divided, to fly open,<BR>open in chinks, open (as a bud or blossom), expand,<BR>blossom: Caus. दलयति and दालयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to burst, to split or tear or open, tear asunder; to<BR>cut, divide, split, pierce; to wither; [cf. Lith. dalis,<BR>‘a part;’ dallykas, ‘a fragment;’ daliyu, ‘to<BR>divide:’ Goth. dails, ‘a part:’ Old Germ. tail,<BR>teil; tīlōn, tīligōn = Caus. दलयामि: Lat. dolo:<BR>Hib. dail, ‘a share;’ dailim, ‘I deal out;’ duil,<BR>‘partition;’ duillean, ‘a spear.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल|दलं|दलः
दल, अम्, n. (according to lexicographers also<BR>अस्, m.), a piece torn or split off; a part, a portion,<BR>a fragment, a rent, side [cf. अष्ट-दल]; a degree;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">Page0404-b+ 80</a>]<BR>a half, the half (e. g. अहर्-दल, mid-day); a sheath,<BR>scabbard; a small shoot, blade, petal, leaf (i. e. what<BR>unfolds itself; often occurring at the end of names<BR>of plants, the fem. being दला; cf. उदुम्बर-द्˚,<BR>कर्कश-द्˚, काम-खड्ग-द्˚, क्षार-द्˚); the blade<BR>of anything (as of a knife &c.); a clump, lump, heap,<BR>quantity; a detachment, body of men; dividing,<BR>tearing, cutting, splitting, &c.; an adulteration or<BR>alloy; (अस्), m., N. of a prince; (ई), f., see दलि<BR>below; [cf. Hib. duille, ‘a leaf.’]<BR>—दल-कपाट, अस्,<BR>m. a folded petal or leaf.<BR>—दल-कोमल = कमल,<BR>the lotus (Nelumbium).<BR>—दल-कोष, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing young shoots incased in sheaths,’ a sort of jasmine<BR>(J. Pubescens).<BR>—दल-ज, अम्, n. ‘produced by<BR>small bees’ or ‘produced from young shoots,’ a kind<BR>of honey; [cf. दाल.]<BR>—दल-तरु, उस्, m. = ताडी,<BR>a kind of palm, Corypha Taliera.<BR>—दल-निर्मोक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of birch (lit. ‘leaf-shedding’), the<BR>bark of which is used for hookahs &c. (= भूर्ज-<BR>पत्त्र).<BR>—दल-पति, इस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—दल-<BR>पुष्पा, ई, f. a fragrant plant, the leaves of which<BR>surround the flower, Pandanus Odoratissimus (= के-<BR>तकी).<BR>—दल-मालिनी, f. a kind of cabbage.<BR>—दल-<BR>शस्, ind. in pieces or fragments (e. g. दलशो या, to<BR>go or fall to pieces).<BR>—दल-शालिनी, f. a species of<BR>pot-herb (= कञ्चुक-शाक).<BR>—दल-सायसी (?), f.<BR>white basil.<BR>—दल-सारिणी, f. = केमुक, a species<BR>of pot-herb, (probably) = दल-शालिनी.<BR>—दल-सूचि,<BR>इस्, m. a thorn.<BR>—दल-स्नसा, f. the fibre or vein of a<BR>leaf.<BR>—दलाख्य (˚ल-आख्˚), अस्, m., N. of a parti-<BR>cular constellation (subdivisions of which are Ahi and<BR>Mālā).<BR>—दलाग्र-लोहित, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a sort of spinage.<BR>—दलाढक (˚ल-आढ्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of several plants, Pistia Stratiotes (= पृश्नी);<BR>a kind of jasmine (= कुन्द); wild sesamum;<BR>Mesua Ferrea (commonly Nageśar); Acacia Sirissa<BR>(= शिरीष); red chalk (= गौरिक); foam (=<BR>फेन); cuttle-fish bone; a moat, a ditch; a Śūdra;<BR>the head man of a village (?), the driver of an ele-<BR>phant (?); an elephant's ear; a hurricane, a high<BR>wind.<BR>—दलाढ्य (˚ल-आढ्˚), अस्, m. mud, espe-<BR>cially on the banks of a river; [cf. दलाढक.]<BR>—दलामल (˚ल-अम्˚), अम्, n., N. of several<BR>plants, = दमनक and मरुवक; Vangueria<BR>Spinosa and Artemisia.<BR>—दलाम्ल (˚ल-अम्˚), अम्,<BR>n. sorrel.<BR>—दली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, divided, bisected,<BR>halved.<BR>—दले-गन्धि, इस्, m. (‘fragrance in the<BR>leaf’), N. of a plant, Echites Scholaris; [cf. सप्त-<BR>पर्ण.]<BR>—दलोद्भव (˚ल-उद्˚), अम्, n. a kind<BR>of honey; [cf. दल-ज and दाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलत्
दलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, splitting, bursting open,<BR>rending; being torn or cut.<BR>—दलद्-धृदय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम् (दलत् + हृदय), broken-hearted, cut to the<BR>heart, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलन|दलनं
दलन, अस्, ई, अम्, splitting, tearing asunder or<BR>in two, breaking to pieces, cutting, dividing; (ई), f.<BR>a clod of earth [cf. दलि]; (अम्), n. bursting; tear-<BR>ing, rending, breaking, crushing, cutting to pieces,<BR>grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलनीय
दलनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken or destroyed<BR>or trodden down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलि|दलिः
दलि, इस्, f. (according to some also दली), a clod<BR>of clay or earth; [cf. दलनी and दलन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलिक|दलिकं
दलिक, अम्, n. timber, a piece of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलित|दलितं
दलित, अस्, आ, अम्, burst, split, broken, torn,<BR>rent; torn asunder, cut to pieces, wounded; opened,<BR>unfolded, expanded, blown, full blown; divided in<BR>two, bisected, halved; divided into degrees, distri-<BR>buted; driven asunder, scattered; trodden down;<BR>crushed; destroyed; manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलिन्
दलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having pieces, leaves, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्मि|दल्मिः
दल्मि, इस्, m. Indra's thunderbolt; an epithet of<BR>Indra; [cf. दर्म, दर्मिन्, दाल्मि.]<BR>—दल्मि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलप|दलपः
दलप दलप, अस्, m. a weapon; a sacred<BR>or religious book (= शास्त्र for शस्त्र); gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्भ|दल्भः
दल्भ दल्भ, अस्, m. a wheel; fraud, dis-<BR>honesty, sin; N. of a Ṛṣi; [cf. Hib. dalbh,<BR>‘falsehood.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्भ्य
दल्भ्य, अस्, m., N. of an ancient preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दव|दवः
दव दव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. दु), fire, burn-<BR>ing, heat; fever, pain; a wood on fire, a forest con-<BR>flagration; a wood, a forest; [cf. दाव; cf. also<BR>Cambro-Brit. daiv, ‘burning.’]<BR>—दव-दग्धक,<BR>अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a kind of grass (= रो-<BR>हिष).<BR>—दव-दहन, अस्, m. the fire in a<BR>burning forest.<BR>—दवाग्नि (˚व-अग्˚), इस्, or दवा-<BR>नल (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. a wood on fire, a forest<BR>conflagration; [cf. दावाग्नि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवथु|दवथुः
दवथु, उस्, m. fire, heat; pain, anxiety, vex-<BR>ation, distress; inflammation of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवय
दवय दवय (fr. दव, substituted for दूर<BR>in the same manner as in दवीयस्, दविष्ठ), Nom.<BR>P. दवयति, -यितुम्, to make distant, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवयत्
दवयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, removing, making distant,<BR>distancing, placing at a distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दविष्ठ|दविष्ठः
दविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. fr. दूर), very<BR>remote, very distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवीयस्
दवीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. fr. दूर), more<BR>or very remote, more distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दश्
दश् दश्. See 2. दंश्, p. 396, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन्
दशन् दशन्, अ, m. f. n. pl. (said to be fr. rt. 2.<BR>दंश्), ten; [cf. Gr. δέκα Lat. decem; Goth. taihun<BR>for tihun; Armor. dek; Hib. déagh, deich; Lith.<BR>deszimtis, deszim-ts, deszim-t; Slav. desya-ty.]<BR>—दश-कण्ठ or दश-कन्धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ten-necked; (अस्), m. an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—दश-<BR>कण्ठ-जित्, त्, m. or दशकण्ठारि (˚ठ-अरि), इस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Rāma.<BR>—दश-कन्या-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the Tīrtha of the ten virgins,’ N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—दश-कर्मन्, आणि, n. pl. the ten ceremonies<BR>prescribed to the three twice-born classes.<BR>—दश-<BR>कर्म-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work on the ten cere-<BR>monies.<BR>—दश-काम-ज-व्यसन, अम्, n. ten vices<BR>(see Manu VII. 47) arising from love of pleasure, viz.<BR>hunting, gambling, sleeping by day, fault-finding, lust,<BR>drunkenness, dancing, singing, playing, and useless<BR>travel.<BR>—दश-कुमार-चरित, अम्, n. ‘the adven-<BR>tures of the ten princes,’ N. of a book of stories by<BR>Daṇḍin.<BR>—दश-क्षिति-गर्भ, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), N. of a Buddhist Sūtra work.<BR>—दश-क्षीर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, mixed with ten parts of milk; (अम्), n. a<BR>compound of ten parts of milk mixed with one part<BR>of some other substance.<BR>—दश-गणी, f. ten classes<BR>collectively.<BR>—दश-गीतिका, f., N. of an astronomical<BR>work, i. e. ‘the ten poems of Ārya-bhaṭṭa.’<BR>—दश-<BR>गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, ten-fold, ten times larger, ten<BR>times more; (अम्), ind. ten times, ten-fold.<BR>—दश-<BR>ग्राम, अम्, n. a district or collection of ten villages.<BR>—दशग्राम-पति, इस्, m. a magistrate or chief of<BR>ten villages.<BR>—दशग्रामिन्, ई, m. the head man of<BR>ten villages.<BR>—दश-ग्रामी, f. a collection of ten<BR>villages; a municipality or corporation of ten villages.<BR>—दश-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्, ten-necked; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a demon; of an enemy of Vṛṣa, who is the Indra<BR>of the eleventh Manv-antara; an epithet of Rāvaṇa;<BR>N. of a son of Dama-ghoṣa.<BR>—दश-ग्व, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. going in ten ways, one who observes a ten-<BR>days rite or conducts sacrifices for ten months; going<BR>to completion in ten months; a N. applied to the<BR>Maruts; also to the family of the Aṅgirasas.<BR>—दश-<BR>ग्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, ten-fold, going ten ways; (Sāy.)<BR>going for ten (leagues).<BR>—दश-ज्योति and दश-<BR>ज्योतिस्, इस्, m., N. of a son of Su-bhrāj.<BR>—दश-दशिन्<BR>or दशन्-दशिन् or दशा-दशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. con-<BR>sisting of repeated decads.<BR>—दश-दिश्, क्, f. the ten<BR>quarters of the heavens (including that overhead and<BR>underneath).<BR>—दश-द्यु, उस्, m., Ved. (according<BR>to Sāy.) N. of a person.<BR>—दश-धनुस्, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of the ancestors of Śākya-muni.<BR>—दश-<BR>धा, ind. in ten parts, into ten parts, ten-fold, in<BR>ten ways.<BR>—दश-प, अस्, m. a chief of ten villages;<BR>[cf. दशग्राम-पति.]<BR>—दश-पशु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. prepared or intended for ten oxen.<BR>—दश-<BR>पादी, f., N. of a grammatical work.<BR>—दश-पार-<BR>मिता-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing the ten Pāra-<BR>mitās or perfections; (अस्), m. a Buddha or Buddhist<BR>saint.<BR>—दश-पार्श्व, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-a" target="_blank">Page0405-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—दश-पिण्ड-श्राद्ध, अम्, n. a funereal cere-<BR>mony in which a Piṇḍa or ball of rice is offered<BR>by the next of kin to a person deceased, increasing<BR>the number daily for ten successive days until they<BR>amount to ten.<BR>—दश-पुर, अम्, n. a district or<BR>part of Malwa or Bandelkhand; (perhaps) N. of a<BR>town, Decapolis; a fragrant grass, a species of Cyperus<BR>Rotundus.<BR>—दश-पुरुषम्, ind. for ten persons<BR>or male progenitors, i. e. through a series of ten<BR>ancestors.<BR>—दशपुरुषं-राज्य, अम्, n. a king-<BR>dom inherited through a series of ten ances-<BR>tors.<BR>—दश-पूर, अम्, n. a fragrant grass (= द-<BR>श-पुर).<BR>—दश-पूरुषम् = दश-पुरुषम्<BR>above.<BR>—दश-पूर्व-रथ, अस्, m. a periphrasis<BR>for the name Daśa-ratha (‘रथ preceded by दश’).<BR>—दश-पूर्विन्, ई, m., N. of seven saints of the<BR>Jainas.<BR>—दश-पेय, अस्, m., Ved. ‘to be quaffed by<BR>ten,’ N. of a Soma oblation forming part of the<BR>Rāja-sūya.<BR>—दश-प्रमति, इस्, इस्, इ (?), Ved. re-<BR>ceiving excessive honour in the ten regions or spread-<BR>ing over the ten regions.<BR>—दश-बन्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>tenth part, a fine equivalent to the tenth part.<BR>—दश-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing ten powers;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Buddha.<BR>—दशबल-काश्-<BR>यप, अस्, m., N. of one of the first five pupils of<BR>Śākya-muni.<BR>—दश-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, ten-armed;<BR>(उस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—दशभक्ति-पञ्च-<BR>स्तुति, इस्, f., N. of a collection of Jaina prayers.<BR>—दश-भुजा, f. ‘the ten-armed,’ a form of Durgā.<BR>—दश-भूमि-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, traversing the ten<BR>worlds; (अस्), m. Buddha, the founder of the Bud-<BR>dhist religion, a Buddha or the generic name of<BR>the sanctified teachers of that religion.<BR>—दश-भू-<BR>मीश (˚मि-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the ten worlds,’ a<BR>N. of Buddha or a Buddha.<BR>—दशभूमीश्वर (˚मि-<BR>ईश्˚), N. of a Buddhist Sūtra work.<BR>—दश-महा-<BR>विद्या, f. an epithet of Durgā (‘possessing the ten<BR>great sciences’).<BR>—दश-माल, अम्, ई, n. f. a collec-<BR>tion of ten garlands.<BR>—दश-मालिक, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people.<BR>—दश-मास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ten<BR>months old, as the child in the womb just before<BR>birth; (with अश्व), a horse let loose for ten months.<BR>—दश-मुख, आनि, n. pl. ten mouths or faces;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), having ten faces; (अस्), m. an epithet of Rā-<BR>vaṇa.<BR>—दशमुख-रिपु, उस्, or दशमुखान्-<BR>तक (˚ख-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘the enemy of Rāvaṇa,’<BR>an epithet of Rāma.<BR>—दश-मूत्रक, अम्, n. the<BR>urine of ten (i. e. of the elephant, buffalo, camel,<BR>cow, goat, sheep, horse, donkey, man, and woman).<BR>—दश-मूल, अम्, n. a tonic medicine prepared<BR>from the roots of ten plants, viz. Tri-kaṇṭaka, the<BR>two Vṛhatīs, Pṛthak-parṇī, Vidāri-gandhā, Vilva,<BR>Agni-mantha, Ṭuṇṭuka, Pāṭalā, and Kāśmarī; [cf.<BR>द्विपञ्च-मूल.]<BR>—दश-योजन-विस्तीर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ten Yojanas broad.<BR>—दश-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having ten chariots; (अस्), m., N. of several princes,<BR>among whom the most renowned is the father of<BR>Rāma, (he was a descendant of Ikṣvāku and sove-<BR>reign of Ayodhyā or Oude); N. of an older Daśa-<BR>ratha, son of Mūlaka, and ancestor of the above,<BR>(also written शत-रथ); N. of a son of Nava-<BR>ratha and father of Śakuni; N. of a son of Su-yaśas<BR>and father of Saṅgata; N. of an ancestor of Buddha;<BR>(अम्), n. the body (?).<BR>—दशरथ-तत्त्व, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—दशरथ-यज्ञारम्भ (˚ञ-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, m., N. of the fourteenth chapter of the Pātāla-<BR>khaṇḍa or fourth part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—दश-<BR>रथ-विजय, अस्, m., N. of the twelfth chapter of the<BR>Pātāla-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—दश-रश्मि-<BR>शत, अस्, m. ‘possessed of a thousand rays,’ an epi-<BR>thet of the sun; [cf. दशशत-रश्मि.]<BR>—दश-<BR>रात्र, अस्, m. a period of ten days and nights; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), Ved. lasting ten days; (अस्), m., Ved. any<BR>ceremony that lasts ten days; a particular ceremony<BR>lasting ten days (forming the chief part of the Dvā-<BR>daśāha).<BR>—दशरात्र-पर्वन्, अ, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—दश-रूपक, अम्, n., N. of a rhetorical work.<BR>—दशरूपक-टीका, f., N. of a commentary on<BR>the preceding work by Pāṇi.<BR>—दश-रूप-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, taking ten forms, appearing in ten shapes; (त्),<BR>m. an epithet of Viṣṇu (with reference to his ten<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-b" target="_blank">Page0405-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Avatāras).<BR>—दशर्च (˚श-ऋच), अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>strophe of ten verses.<BR>—दशर्षभ (˚श-ऋष्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. consisting of ten bulls.<BR>—दश-<BR>लक्षण, अम्, n. ten marks or attributes.<BR>—दश-<BR>लक्षणक, अस्, इका, अम्, having ten forms or<BR>characteristics, ten-fold.<BR>—दश-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having ten mouths; (अस्), m. a particular magical<BR>formula against the evil spirits supposed to possess<BR>certain weapons.<BR>—दश-वदन, अस्, m. ‘the ten-<BR>faced,’ an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—दश-वर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—दश-वर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, ten<BR>years old.<BR>—दश-वाजिन्, ई, m. the moon ‘whose<BR>car is drawn by ten horses.’<BR>—दश-वार्षिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, happening after ten years.<BR>—दश-विध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of ten kinds, ten-fold.<BR>—दश-वीर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. granting ten men.<BR>—दश-वृक्ष, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. a species of tree.<BR>—दश-व्रज, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—दश-शत, अम्, n. ten hundred, a<BR>thousand; one hundred and ten; (ई), f. a thousand;<BR>(अस्, ई, अम्), Ved. containing ten hundred.<BR>—दश-<BR>शत-कर-धारिन्, ई, m. ‘having a thousand rays,’<BR>the sun.<BR>—दशशत-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the one<BR>hundred and tenth.<BR>—दशशत-नयन, अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, having a thousand eyes; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>—दशशत-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a<BR>thousand rays; (इस्), m. the sun; [cf. दश-रश्मि-<BR>शत.]<BR>—दशशताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>a thousand eyes; (अस्), m. an epithet of Indra.<BR>—दशशताङ्घ्रि (˚त-अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having a<BR>thousand feet; (इस्), f. a species of plant, = शतावरी.<BR>—दश-शिप्र, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दश-<BR>शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, ten-headed; (आस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Rāvaṇa; N. of a mountain.<BR>—दश-शीर्ष, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ten-headed; (अस्), m. an epithet of Rāvaṇa;<BR>a kind of magical formula against the evil spirits<BR>supposed to possess weapons.<BR>—दश-श्लोकी, f. ‘a col-<BR>lection of ten Ślokas,’ N. of a summary of the Vedānta<BR>system by Śaṅkarācārya; also of another similar<BR>summary by Nimbārka.<BR>—दश-सप्ता, f., Ved., N.<BR>of a Viṣṭuti of the Saptadaśa-stoma (in which the<BR>verses of a Tṛca are repeated in the following order,<BR>11123, 12223, 1222333).<BR>—दश-साहस्र, अम्,<BR>n., 10,000; (अस्, ई, अम्), consisting of 10,000, form-<BR>ing 10,000.<BR>—दश-साहस्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>of 10, 000.<BR>—दश-स्तोभ, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—दश-हरा, f. an epithet of Gaṅgā or the Ganges,<BR>‘as taking away ten sins;’ a festival in honour of<BR>Gaṅgā (vulgarly called Dusrah) on the tenth day of<BR>the month Jyaiṣṭha, but now held in honour of Durgā<BR>in the month Aśvin.<BR>—दश-होतृ, ता, m., Ved. a<BR>particular Mantra in which the ten sacrificial vessels are<BR>mentioned; (ता, त्री, तृ), connected with the Mantra<BR>Daśa-hotṛ.<BR>—दशांश (˚श-अंश), अस् or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?), ten parts, the tenth part, ten-fold amount<BR>of anything (?) .<BR>—दशाक्ष (˚श-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>ten-eyed; (अस्), m. a kind of magical formula against<BR>the evil spirits supposed to possess weapons.<BR>—द-<BR>शाक्षर (˚श-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing ten<BR>syllables.<BR>—दशाङ्गुल (˚श-अङ्˚), अस्, &c., ten<BR>fingers long; (अम्), n. a water-melon.<BR>—दशाधि-<BR>पति (˚श-अध्˚), इस्, m. a decurion or commander<BR>of ten men.<BR>—दशानन (˚श-आन्˚), अस्, आ or ई,<BR>अम्, ten-faced; (अस्), m. an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—द-<BR>शानुगान (˚श-अन्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—द-<BR>शार्ध (˚श-अर्˚), आस्, आस्, आनि, pl. half of ten, five.<BR>—दशार्ध-सङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, five in number.<BR>—दशार्ह (˚श-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘worthy of ten (?),’ an<BR>epithet applied to a Buddha; an epithet of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>(आस्), or दशार्हकास्, m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe<BR>descended from Daśārha of the family of Yadu; (ई),<BR>f. a princess of the Daśārhas.<BR>—दशावतार (˚श-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu (the deity, of whom there<BR>are ten descents from heaven); N. of the fifty-sixth<BR>chapter of the Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa.<BR>—दशावर (˚श-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of ten at least; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of an evil spirit.<BR>—दशाश्व (˚श-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing ten horses, driving ten horses; (अस्), m. the<BR>moon; N. of a son of Ikṣvāku.<BR>—दशाश्वमेध<BR>(˚श-अश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha, the Tīrtha of the<BR>ten horse-sacrifices.<BR>—दशास्य (˚श-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having ten mouths, ten-faced; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">Page0405-c+ 80</a>]<BR>of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—दशास्य-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of the<BR>ten-faced,’ an epithet of Rāma.<BR>—दशाह (˚श-अह),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, lasting ten days; (अस्), m. a period of ten<BR>days; a kind of ceremonial observance; [cf. दश-<BR>रात्र.]<BR>—दशेन्द्र (˚श-इन्˚), अस्, &c., having the<BR>ten Indrāṇīs as a deity (schol. to Pāṇ. 1. 2, 49).<BR>—द-<BR>शेन्द्रिय (˚श-इन्˚), आणि, n. pl. the ten organs of per-<BR>ception and action, viz. the skin, eye, tongue, nose, ear,<BR>larynx, hand, foot, anus, and pudendum; see इन्द्रिय.<BR>—दशेश (˚श-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a superintendent of ten<BR>villages.<BR>—दशैकादशिक (˚श-एक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, one<BR>who lends ten and receives eleven in return, i. e. one<BR>who lends money for ten per cent.<BR>—दशोणि (˚श-<BR>ओणि), इस्, m., N. of a person protected by Indra;<BR>of an Asura; (Sāy.) offering many oblations; (ac-<BR>cording to some) an oblation giving ten-fold reward.<BR>—दशोण्य, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दशोपनिषद्-<BR>भाष्य (˚श-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of a commentary<BR>by Ānanda Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0404-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दश
दश (at the end of comp.) = दशन् above; [cf.<BR>त्रि-दश, द्वि-दश, निर्-दश.] दश (at the end<BR>of comp.) may also stand for दशा, p. 406, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशक
दशक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of ten, having ten,<BR>having ten parts, ten-fold; (with शत), ten in a hun-<BR>dred, ten from a hundred, ten per cent; (अम्), n.<BR>an aggregate of ten, a decad.<BR>—दशक-मासिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, hired for ten months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशत्
दशत्, त्, f. a collection or aggregate of ten, a<BR>decad; (m. f. n. ?), consisting of ten, divided into ten<BR>parts; [cf. दाशत् and पञ्चत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशतय
दशतय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of ten parts,<BR>ten-fold; (य्यस्), f. pl., scil. शाखास् or ऋचस्, the<BR>texts of the ten-fold Ṛg-veda, i. e. of the Ṛg-veda<BR>divided into ten Maṇḍalas; (ई), f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary; [cf. दाशतय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशति|दशतिः
दशति, इस्, f. (probably for original दशती), a<BR>collection or aggregate of ten, a decad; N. of the<BR>subdivisions of a Prapāṭhaka of the first part of the<BR>Sāma-veda, usually containing ten verses, (in this<BR>sense the crude form दशति without Visarga is used,<BR>probably as a weakened form of दशती); = a hun-<BR>dred in connection with दशन् (e. g. दशतीर् दश<BR>in Mahā-bh. 1. 1081).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशम|दशमः
दशम, अस्, ई, अम्, the tenth, the tenth part,<BR>the tenth day, N. of an Ekāha, the last day of the<BR>Daśa-rātra belonging to the Dvādaśāha; (ई), f., scil.<BR>तिथि, the tenth day of the half moon; the tenth<BR>decad or last stage of human life, the last ten years<BR>of a century; (अम्), n. a tenth part; (अम्), ind. at or<BR>for the tenth time; [cf. Lat. decimus; Scot. dei-<BR>cheamh; Hib. deachmad.]<BR>—दशम-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the culminating point, or that point in which<BR>the meridian crosses a given circle.<BR>—दशमीङ्-गत<BR>or दशमी-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, arrived at the tenth<BR>decad of life, above ninety years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमिन्
दशमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, between ninety and one hun-<BR>dred years, very old or aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशिन्
दशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having ten, divided into ten parts;<BR>(इनी), f. a decad; (ई), m. a superintendent of ten<BR>villages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन|दशनं|दशनः
दशन दशन, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. दश् or<BR>2. दंश्), a tooth; biting; (अस्), m. the peak of a<BR>mountain; (अम्), n. armour, mail; [cf. दंशन.]<BR>—दशन-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘teeth-covering,’ the<BR>lip.<BR>—दशन-पद, अम्, n. ‘teeth-mark,’ a bite.<BR>—दशन-वासस्, अस्, n. ‘the covering of the teeth,’<BR>the lip.<BR>—दशन-वीज, अम्, n. (?) the pomegranate.<BR>—दशनांशु (˚न-अं˚), उस्, m. whiteness or bright-<BR>ness of the teeth.<BR>—दशनाङ्क (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘teeth-mark,’ a bite.<BR>—दशनाढ्या (˚न-आढ्˚), f.<BR>a kind of sorrel (= चुक्रिका).<BR>—दशनोच्छिष्ट<BR>(˚न-उच्˚), अस्, m. ‘remainder or leavings of the teeth,’<BR>a kiss; a sigh; a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेर|दशेरः
दशेर, अस्, आ, अम्, biting, mordacious, injuring;<BR>hurtful, attacking or killing any one when asleep;<BR>(अस्), m. a mischievous or venomous animal, a beast<BR>of prey, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेरक|दशेरकः
दशेरक or दसेरक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people, = मरु; a young camel; [cf. दाशेर, दा-<BR>शेरक, दासेर, दासेरक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दष्ट
दष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, bitten, stung; pressed together.<BR>—दष्ट-दच्छद, अस्, आ, अम्, biting the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमान
दशमान दशमान or दशमानिक, आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a people; (also written देशमानिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशस्य
दशस्य दशस्य (fr. दशस्, probably an old<BR>form for यशस्, = Lat. decus; cf. rt. 1. दाश्), Nom. P.<BR>दशस्यति, &c., Ved. to render service, serve, wor-<BR>ship, favour, oblige, aid (with acc.); to do service<BR>or favour to any one (with dat.); to grant, accord;<BR>[cf. नमस्य; दाशस्पत्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशस्या
दशस्या, f. occurring only in Ved. inst. दशस्या,<BR>at the pleasure of, according to the liking, in order to<BR>please; (Sāy.) by desire of giving or granting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशा
दशा दशा, f. (said to be fr. rt. दश् or 2. दंश्),<BR>the threads or fringe projecting at the end of a piece<BR>of woven cloth, the fringe of a garment (e. g. अप-<BR>दशं वासस्, a fringeless garment), the loose ends<BR>of any piece of cloth or garment, the skirt or edge<BR>or hem of a garment, (according to some in these<BR>senses also m. pl., but in most passages where the pl.<BR>दशास् occurs the gender may be f.); the wick of a<BR>lamp; ‘the wick of life,’ state or condition of life;<BR>age, period or time of life (as youth, manhood, &c.);<BR>period in general; state, condition, circumstances;<BR>state or condition of mind; the result of actions,<BR>fate; (in astrology) the aspect or position of the<BR>planets (at birth &c.), the fate of men as depending<BR>on the position of the planets; the mind, under-<BR>standing.<BR>—दशाकर्ष, अस्, or दशाकर्षिन् (˚शा-<BR>आक्˚ or ˚शा-क˚), ई, m. ‘wick-drawing,’ a lamp.<BR>—द-<BR>शान्त (˚शा-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of a wick, the end<BR>of life.<BR>—दशापन्न (˚शा-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being in<BR>a particular state or condition.<BR>—दशा-पवित्र, अम्,<BR>n. a fringed filtering cloth for straining the Soma.<BR>—दशा-पाक, अस्, m. the fulfilment of fate.<BR>—दशा-<BR>फल, अम्, n. result of circumstances or of condition<BR>of life.<BR>—दशारुहा (˚शा-आर्˚), f, N. of a particular<BR>species of plant, = कैवर्तिका, (probably so called<BR>as sticking or attaching itself to clothes.)<BR>—दशा-<BR>लक्षण, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-<BR>sarva-sva.<BR>—दशा-विशेष, अस्, m. any particular<BR>state or condition, existing circumstances.<BR>—दशेन्-<BR>धन (˚शा-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘wick-kindling,’ a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशानिक|दशानिकः
दशानिक दशानिक, अस्, m. = दन्ती, Croton<BR>Polyandrum or Croton Tiglium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशामय|दशामयः
दशामय दशामय, अस्, m. (fr. दशा or द-<BR>शन् + आमय ?), an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ण|दशार्णः
दशार्ण दशार्ण, आस्, m. pl. (said to be fr.<BR>दशन् + ऋण, ‘having ten forts’), N. of a people<BR>living south-east of Madhya-deśa in the centre of<BR>Hindūstān; (अस्), m. the king of the Daśārṇas; the<BR>region of the Daśārṇas; (आ), f., N. of a river rising<BR>in the Vindhya hills, the ancient Dosarence (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्णक
दशार्णक, a wrong form for दाशार्णक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्णेयु
दशार्णेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ह|दशार्हः
दशार्ह दशार्ह. See p. 405, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशीविदर्भ
दशीविदर्भ दशीविदर्भ, आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a people; [cf. दधि-विदर्भ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेर|दशेरः
दशेर दशेर. See दशन, p. 405, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशोनसि
दशोनसि दशोनसि, इस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दष्ट
दष्ट दष्ट. See above at top of this col.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्
दस् दस् (connected with rt. दंस्, p. 396,<BR>col. 2), cl. 4. P. दस्यति, ददास, &c.,<BR>Ved. to suffer want, to waste away, perish, become ex-<BR>hausted, to be ruined; to throw up, toss [cf. rt. तस्;<BR>Eng. toss]; cl. 1. 10. P. दंसति, दंसयति, &c. (see<BR>rt. दंस्), to bite, destroy, overpower; to see; to<BR>shine: Caus. P. दसयति, दासयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to waste away, exhaust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस
दस, अस्, m., Ved. = दस्यु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसन|दसनं
दसन, अम्, n. wasting, perishing, destroying;<BR>throwing, tossing; dismissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसमान
दसमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wasting away, be-<BR>coming exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्त
दस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, wasted, lost, destroyed; thrown,<BR>tossed; sent away, dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्म|दस्मः
दस्म, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, destructive, over-<BR>coming enemies, worthy to be seen, beautiful, ac-<BR>complishing wonderful deeds, wonderful, extraordi-<BR>nary; (अस्), m. an epithet of Agni; of Indra; of<BR>Pūṣan; of Varuṇa; (आस्), m. pl. an epithet of the<BR>Maruts; of the horses of Agni. According to the<BR>lexicographers दस्म, अस्, m., may also mean ‘a<BR>sacrificer’ or ‘institutor of a sacrifice;’ ‘fire;’ ‘a thief,’<BR>‘a rogue;’ [cf. दंसन.]<BR>—दस्म-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. of wonderful appearance; (Sāy.) whose<BR>glory is worthy of being seen or whose power is<BR>destructive; (आस्), m. an epithet of Indra; of Pūṣan;<BR>(असस्), m. pl. an epithet of the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्मत्|दस्मन्त्
दस्मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. wonderful, extraordi-<BR>nary; (Sāy.) worthy of being seen, desirable, accept-<BR>able. According to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 74, 4, the<BR>form दस्मत् is for दस्मम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्म्य
दस्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wonderful, extraordi-<BR>nary; (Sāy.) beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्यु|दस्युः
दस्यु, उस्, m. (probably connected with दास),<BR>‘destroyer (of the good),’ N. of a class of evil beings<BR>or demons, enemies of god and men, and especially<BR>of Indra and Agni; (many of the demons defeated<BR>by Indra have the general name Dasyu, e. g. Vṛtra,<BR>Śambara, Śuṣṇa, Cumuri, &c.; and these Dasyus<BR>are not only spirits of darkness like the Rākṣasas,<BR>but have other characteristics which bring them into<BR>closer relationship to men living in the world: some-<BR>times a general distinction is drawn between man,<BR>i. e. मनु, आयु, नृ, and the Dasyus, the latter<BR>being called अ-मानुष, or the Dasyu is contrasted<BR>as an अन्-आर्य with the pious and respectable man<BR>or आर्य; or rarely दस्यु means ‘a barbarian or<BR>savage,’ as contrasted with ‘a civilized man’); any<BR>cruel or mischievous man, an enemy, thief, robber,<BR>oppressor, bandit, ruffian, violator, perpetrator of in-<BR>justice; (according to Manu) a barbarian, an out-<BR>cast or a Hindū who has become so by neglect of<BR>the essential rites.<BR>—दस्यु-जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living<BR>the life of a robber or barbarian.<BR>—दस्यु-जूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. instigated by Dasyus or by wicked men.<BR>—दस्यु-तर्हण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. crushing the<BR>Dasyus; killing or injuring the Dasyus.<BR>—दस्यु-<BR>सात्, ind. into the hands of the Dasyus, a prey to<BR>robbers.<BR>—दस्यु-हत्य, अम्, n., Ved. a fight with<BR>the Dasyus or with wicked men.<BR>—दस्यु-हन्, आ,<BR>घ्नी, अ, Ved. destroying the Dasyus or the wicked;<BR>(आ), m. an epithet of Indra; of Agni; of Manyu.<BR>—दस्युहन्-तम, अस्, m. (superl. of the preced-<BR>ing), an epithet of Budha, who was son of Tārā<BR>and Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्र|दस्रं|दस्रः
दस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. destroying, destructive,<BR>overcoming enemies, accomplishing wonderful deeds,<BR>giving marvellous aid; worthy to be seen, handsome,<BR>beautiful; (अस्), m., N. of Pūṣan; N. of one of<BR>the two Aśvins (the other being called Nāsatya); an<BR>ass; a robber, thief, &c., see दस्यु; (औ, Ved. आ), m.<BR>du., N. or epithet of the Aśvins, said to be so called<BR>as ‘destroying diseases or enemies,’ (occurring usually<BR>in the nom. and voc.); a N. of Indra-Viṣṇu; the<BR>numeral two; (आस्), m. pl. an epithet of the Maruts;<BR>(अम्), n. the cold season, hoar frost. In Sūrya-sid-<BR>dhānta VIII. 9, दस्रादीनाम् must be translated ‘of<BR>the Nakṣatra Aśvinī, &c.,’ see दस्र-देवता; [cf.<BR>दंसन, दंसस्, दंस, दंसिष्ठ.]<BR>—दस्र-<BR>देवता, f. the lunar constellation Aśvinī.<BR>—दस्र-<BR>सू, ऊस्, f. ‘the mother of the Aśvins,’ N. of Sañjñā<BR>or the wife of the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासित
दासित, अस्, आ, अम्, = दस्त above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसाराम
दसाराम दसाराम, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्
दह् 1. दह् (the original form of this rt.<BR>was probably दघ्), cl. 1. P. दहति (ep.<BR>दहते), ददाह, धक्ष्यति (ep. दहिष्यति),<BR>धक्ष्यते, दग्धुम् (Ved. inf. दग्धोस्; other<BR>Vedic forms are दक्षि, अधाक्, धाक्; part. ध-<BR>क्षत् or दक्षत्), to burn, consume by fire, scorch,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">Page0406-c+ 79</a>]<BR>roast; (in surgery) to cauterize; to consume, de-<BR>stroy completely; to torment, torture, pain, distress,<BR>disturb, grieve: Pass. दह्यते (ep. also दह्यति),<BR>to be burnt, to burn, to be in flames; to be consumed<BR>by fire; to be inflamed; to be consumed by internal<BR>heat or by grief, to suffer pain, be distressed, be<BR>vexed; to be destroyed &c.; (also transitive) to<BR>burn: Caus. दाहयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अदीदहत्, to<BR>cause to burn or to be burned &c.; to cause to<BR>roast or to be cooked: Desid. दिधक्षति (ep. -ते),<BR>to wish to burn, to be about to consume or destroy,<BR>&c. [cf. दिधक्षा and दिधक्षु]: Caus. of<BR>Desid. दिधक्षयति, -यितुम्, to cause to desire<BR>to burn or to be about to burn: Intens. दन्दहीति,<BR>दन्दह्यते, दन्दग्धि (also 2nd sing. impv.),<BR>to burn completely, destroy completely; (A.) to be<BR>burnt completely, be entirely consumed by fire or<BR>grief; [cf. Hib. daghaim; daighim, daghte, ‘burnt,’<BR>= दग्ध; dvighir, ‘flame:’ Lith. degù, ‘I am<BR>hot;’ deginù, ‘I burn:’ Old Germ. tāh-t or dāh-t,<BR>‘a wick,’ fr. Caus.: Goth. dag-s, ‘the day:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. daeg: Mod. Germ. tag: Eng. day: perhaps<BR>Gr. τήγανον: Lat. lig-nu-m for dig-nu-m.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्
2. दह्, धक्, क्, क्, burning (at the end of comp.;<BR>cf. उश-धक्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहत्
दहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, burning, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहति
दहति, इस्, m., N. of one of the attendants on<BR>Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहदहा
दहदहा, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहन|दहनं|दहनः
दहन, अस्, ई, अम्, burning, consuming by fire,<BR>scorching, destroying [cf. त्रिपुर-द्˚]; destructive,<BR>injurious, mischievous; (अस्), m. fire, a N. of Agni<BR>the god of fire; the numeral three; one of the five<BR>forms of fire in the Svāhā-kāra; N. of one of the<BR>eleven Rudras; of one of the attendants of Skanda;<BR>a bad man; a pigeon; lead-wort, Plumbago Zeyla-<BR>nica (= चित्रक); the marking-nut, Anacardium<BR>Officinarum (= भल्लातक); (ई), f. fire; (अम्), n.<BR>burning, cauterizing, consuming by fire; sour gruel.<BR>—दहन-केतन, अस्, m. ‘the mark of burning,’<BR>smoke.<BR>—दहन-प्रिया, f. ‘the beloved of fire,’<BR>N. of Svāhā or the wife of Agni.<BR>—दहनर्क्ष<BR>(˚न-ऋक्ष), अम्, n. ‘the burning constellation,’<BR>the constellation Kṛttikā.<BR>—दहनागुरु (˚न-अग्˚),<BR>उस्, m., N. of a species of the plant Agallochum.<BR>—दहनाराति (˚न-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘enemy of fire,’<BR>water.<BR>—दहनोपकरण (˚न-उप्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>means for cauterizing.<BR>—दहनोपल (˚न-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘fire-stone,’ the sun-gem, a crystal lens; (also<BR>read दहनोपम; cf. सूर्य-कान्त.)<BR>—दह-<BR>नोल्का (˚न-उल्˚), f. a firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनीय|दहनीयः
दहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be burnt, burnable,<BR>combustible.<BR>—दहनीय-ता, f. or दहनीय-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. combustibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्यमान
दह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहर|दहरं|दहरः
दहर दहर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. दह्, probably another form of दह्र, which is<BR>for दभ्र; see दह्र below), small, fine, thin,<BR>subtile, short; young in age, (opposed to वृद्ध);<BR>the cavity of the heart, the heart; (अस्), m. a child,<BR>infant; a younger brother; a young animal; a rat,<BR>mouse.<BR>—दहर-पृष्ठ, अम्, n., N. of a section<BR>of the Taittirīya-saṃhitā; [cf. महा-पृष्ठ.]<BR>—दहर-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist Sūtra<BR>work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहरक
दहरक = दहर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्र|दह्रः
दह्र, अस्, आ, अम्, small, fine, thin; the cavity of<BR>the heart; the heart itself; (अस्), m. fire; a forest<BR>conflagration, a wood on fire.<BR>—दह्र-तस्, ind. from<BR>the cavity of the heart.<BR>—दह्राग्नि (˚र-अग्˚), इस्,<BR>m., N. of Agastya in a former birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहियक
दहियक दहियक, अस्, m. (?) , N. of a par-<BR>ticular kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्र|दह्रः
दह्र दह्र. See above under दहर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा 1. दा (many of the forms of this rt.<BR>are to be referred to the base दद्, which is<BR>sometimes regarded as a separate rt.; cf. 1. दद्), cl. 3.<BR>P. A. ददाति, दत्ते, 1st pl. दद्मस्, 2nd pl. दत्थ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-a" target="_blank">Page0407-a+ 81</a>]<BR>3rd pl. ददति (3rd pl. A. ददते); Impf. अददात्,<BR>अदत्त (3rd du. अदत्ताम्, 3rd pl. अददुस्, A.<BR>अददत); Pot. दद्यात्, ददीत (1st pl. A. ददी-<BR>महि, 3rd pl. ददीरन्); Impv. ददातु, दत्ताम्<BR>(2nd sing. देहि, A. दत्स्व, 3rd du. दत्ताम्, 2nd<BR>pl. दत्त, 3rd pl. ददतु); Perf. ददौ, ददे<BR>(2nd sing. ददिथ or ददाथ, 2nd du. ददथुस्,<BR>2nd pl. दद, 3rd pl. ददुस्, 3rd du. A. ददाते,<BR>part. ददिवस्, gen. ददुषस्); Fut. दाता, दास्यति,<BR>-ते; Aor. अदात्, अदित (3rd pl. P. अदुस्, 1st sing. A.<BR>अदिषि, 3rd pl. अदिषत); Prec. देयात्, दासीष्ट;<BR>(Ved. forms are Pres. 3rd sing. दाति, 1st pl. दद्-<BR>मसि; Impf. 2nd pl. अददात, अदत्तन, 2nd sing.<BR>ददास्, 3rd sing. ददात्, 2nd pl. ददात; Impv.<BR>दातु, 2nd sing. दद्धि; Perf. 3rd pl. A. with<BR>प्र, दद्रिरे, part. ददावत्, दद्वत्; Aor. दात्,<BR>3rd du. दाताम्, 2nd pl. दात, 3rd pl. दुस्, 3rd sing.<BR>A. अददिष्ट, अदेदिष्ट, 2nd sing. Let ददस्.<BR>Ep. forms fr. 1. दद् are 1st sing. Pres. दद्मि, 3rd<BR>sing. ददति, -ते, 3rd pl. ददन्ति, -ते; Impf. 3rd<BR>sing. अददत्; Impv. 2nd sing. दद, A. ददस्व;<BR>Perf. 3rd sing. दददे, 3rd du. दददाते, 3rd pl.<BR>दददिरे); दातुम्, Ved. inf. दातवे, दातवै, दा-<BR>तोस्, दै in परा-दै; to give, bestow, grant,<BR>yield, impart, present, offer (usually with acc. of the<BR>thing and dat. gen. or loc. of the person, e. g. तत्<BR>तस्मै or तस्य or तस्मिन् देहि, give that to him);<BR>to deliver over, hand over; to give back, restore,<BR>return; to pay (e. g. ऋणं दा, to pay a debt;<BR>दण्डं दा, to pay a fine); to give away, give up,<BR>cede, sacrifice, devote, surrender (e. g. प्राणान् or<BR>जीवितं दा, to give one's life; आत्मानं दा, to<BR>sacrifice one's self; आत्मानं खेदाय दा, to give<BR>one's self up to grief); to give in marriage (with or<BR>without भार्याम्, e. g. ददौ कन्यां तस्मै<BR>भार्याम्, he gave the maiden to him as wife;<BR>यस्मै पिता तां दद्यात्, to whomsoever a father<BR>may marry her); to communicate knowledge or<BR>advice, to teach (e. g. विद्यां दा, to impart know-<BR>ledge); to sell (with inst. of the price, e. g. गवां<BR>सहस्रेण दा, to sell for a thousand cows); to<BR>permit, allow (e. g. वाष्पो न ददाति तां द्रष्-<BR>टुम्, tears do not allow her to see); to place, put,<BR>apply (e. g. पदम् भस्म-चये ददौ, he placed<BR>his foot on a heap of ashes). The root दा may<BR>sometimes yield senses equivalent to ‘to do,’ ‘make,’<BR>‘cause,’ ‘perform,’ ‘bring about,’ ‘accomplish;’ and<BR>the meanings of this root may be variously modified<BR>according to the nouns with which it is connected,<BR>as in the following examples: शोकं दा, to cause<BR>grief; व्रतं दा, to accomplish a vow; श्राद्धं<BR>दा, to perform the Śrāddha; सञ्ज्ञां दा, to make<BR>a sign; पन्थानं or मार्गं दा, to give up<BR>the road, stand out of the way, allow to pass; अव-<BR>काशं दा, to give room or space, allow to enter;<BR>युद्धं or सङ्ग्रामं दा, to give battle, fight<BR>with; आज्ञां or आदेशं दा, to give an order, to<BR>command; सन्देशं दा, to give information;<BR>वरं दा, to grant a boon; आशिषो दा, to grant<BR>or utter blessings; प्रति-वचस् or प्रति-वचनं<BR>or प्रत्य्-उत्तरं दा, to give an answer; शब्दं<BR>दा, to make a noise, call out; वाचं दा (with<BR>dat.), to address a speech to; सत्यं वचो दा, to<BR>speak the truth; समयं दा, to propose an agree-<BR>ment; शापं दा, to utter a curse or oath; आलिङ्ग-<BR>नं दा, to embrace; झम्पं दा, to give a<BR>spring, to jump; अनुयात्रां दा, to accompany;<BR>तलं or तलान् दा, to slap with the palms of the<BR>hands, to shake hands; तल-प्रहारं दा, to strike<BR>with the palm &c.; तालं दा, to beat time with<BR>the hands; सङ्केतकं दा, to make an appoint-<BR>ment with any one; प्रयोगं दा, to give a dramatic<BR>representation; वृतिं दा, to inclose or fence in;<BR>दर्शनं or दृष्टिं दा, to show one's self, be-<BR>come visible, appear; दृष्टिं or दृशं or अक्षि<BR>or चक्षुर् दा (with loc.), to fix the eyes on, look<BR>at; निगडानि दा, to put on fetters; पावकं दा, to<BR>set on fire; शारं दा, to move a chess-man; अर्-<BR>गलं दा, to draw a bolt, to bar; पदं दा, to<BR>direct the steps; कर्णं दा, to give ear, listen;<BR>मनो दा, to direct the mind to anything, think<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">Page0407-b+ 81</a>]<BR>upon. In some passages of the Veda the base दद्<BR>(A. ददते) yields senses equivalent to ‘to receive,’<BR>‘carry,’ ‘convey,’ ‘bear,’ ‘hold,’ ‘keep,’ ‘preserve,’<BR>to which some refer the part. दत्त, preserved; [cf.<BR>5. दा.] Caus. P. दापयति, -यितुम्, अदीदपत्,<BR>to cause to give or to be given, to cause to bestow,<BR>present, &c. (with two acc.); to cause to be offered;<BR>to oblige to pay, make pay; to force to restore or<BR>return, to make surrender or deliver; to procure;<BR>to cause to do or perform or accomplish; to cause to<BR>put or apply, cause to be put on; to cause to speak<BR>or utter: Desid. P. A. दित्सति, -ते, (Ved.) दिदासति,<BR>to wish to give &c., to be ready to bestow &c.:<BR>Intens. देदीयते, दादाति; [cf. rts. दास्, रा, ला:<BR>Zend dā, ‘to give;’ dā-tar, dā-ta, ‘giver;’ dā-na, dā-<BR>thra, ‘present:’ Gr. δίδομι = ददामि, δο-τήρ, δω-τήρ,<BR>δῶ-τι-ς, δό-τι-ς, δῶ-ρο-ν, δάνος, δαπάνη from<BR>the Caus. दापयति: Lat. dă-re, dă-tor, dō-s, dō-<BR>nu-m: Slav. da-mĭ = dad-mi; da-rŭ, ‘present;’<BR>da-nĭ, ‘tax:’ Lith. du§-mi = dad-mi, du§-ti-s, du§-<BR>ni-s, ‘a gift:’ Hib. daighim or dailim fr. daidim,<BR>‘I give:’ Cambro-Brit. dodi, ‘to give:’ Angl. Sax.<BR>tidhe, tidhian.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
2. दा, आस्, m., Ved. a giver; (at the end of comp.)<BR>giving, granting; [cf. अन्-अश्व-दा, अश्व-दा, आयुर्-<BR>दा, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक|दाकः
दाक, अस्, m. a giver, donor, one who makes<BR>presents, especially to Brāhmans; the institutor of<BR>a sacrifice who employs and pays the officiating<BR>priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
1. दात, Ved., said by some to = दत्त, ‘given,’ in<BR>त्वा-दात, q. v.; but the form दात according to<BR>native authorities can only belong to 3. दा or 7. दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातव्य
दातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be given or bestowed;<BR>to be paid, payable; to be restored or returned; to<BR>be communicated or taught; to be given in marriage;<BR>to be placed upon or applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाति|दातिः
1. दाति, इस्, f. giving. See दाति-वार under 2.<BR>दाति, p. 408, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातुकाम
दातु-काम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. दातुम् inf. of 1. दा<BR>+ काम), wishing to bestow, desirous of giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
1. दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, giving, bestowing, imparting,<BR>communicating, liberal; a giver, donor, imparter,<BR>lender, creditor, payer; teacher; [cf. कन्या-द्˚,<BR>ब्रह्म-द्˚, ऋन-द्˚; Gr. δωτήρ, δοτήρ; Lat.<BR>dator.]<BR>—दातृ-ता, f. or दातृ-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being a giver, liberality.<BR>—दातृ-निरूपण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—दातृ-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्व|दात्वः
दात्व, अस्, m. a giver, donor; (अम्), n. a sacri-<BR>ficial ceremony; the performance of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाद|दादः
दाद, अस्, m. (fr. base दद्), a gift, donation,<BR>oblation, giving.<BR>—दाद-द, अस्, m. a donor, giver<BR>of a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दादिन्
दादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, giving, a giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
1. दान, अस्, m., Ved. a giver, giving; an offering,<BR>(according to Sāy. = दत्त or देय-भूत, but<BR>thought by modern scholars to be the epithet of a<BR>horse); (अम्), n. giving, presenting; giving in<BR>marriage (e. g. कन्या-द्˚, q. v.); giving up, sacri-<BR>ficing (e. g. प्राण-द्˚, q. v.); delivering, distributing;<BR>communicating, imparting, teaching, giving instruc-<BR>tion (e. g. ब्रह्म-द्˚, q. v.); a gift, present, donation<BR>(e. g. दानं दा, to offer a gift; cf. Lat. donum);<BR>special gift, oblation (e. g. उदक-द्˚, q. v.); adding,<BR>addition; liberality; bribery (one of the four means<BR>by which a king overpowers his enemies; cf. उपाय);<BR>the fragrant fluid that flows from the temples of an<BR>elephant in rut (more probably connected with rt. 3. दा;<BR>see 2. दान, p. 408, col. 1); a kind of honey, (per-<BR>haps for दाल.)<BR>—दान-कल्प-तरु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>work mentioned in the Saṃskāra-tattva by Raghu-<BR>nandana.<BR>—दान-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fond of<BR>giving, liberal.<BR>—दान-कुल्या, f. the flow of fluid from<BR>an elephant's temples.<BR>—दान-कुसुमाञ्जलि (˚म-<BR>अञ्˚), N. of a poem.<BR>—दान-कौमुदी, f., N. of the<BR>second part of the Kriyā-kaumudī.<BR>—दान-च्युत, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—दान-तस्, ind. through gifts, by<BR>liberality.<BR>—दान-दर्पण, N. of a work mentioned<BR>in the Saṃskāra-tattva.<BR>—दान-धर्म, अस्, m. alms-<BR>giving, charitable acts, charity; the rules or practice<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">Page0407-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of alms-giving.<BR>—दानधर्म-विधि, इस्, m. ‘the<BR>rules for alms-giving &c.,’ N. of a chapter of the<BR>Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—दान-पति, इस्, m. ‘a master of<BR>liberality,’ an exceedingly liberal or munificent man;<BR>an epithet of A-krūra, who was kinsman of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>N. of a Daitya.<BR>—दान-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a deed of<BR>gift or conveyance.<BR>—दान-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>a work on the sixteen chief oblations.<BR>—दान-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. ‘an object of charity, one who deserves a gift,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—दान-<BR>प्रतिभाव्य, अम्, n. security for payment of a debt<BR>&c.<BR>—दान-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, divided or made<BR>hostile by bribes.<BR>—दान-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy<BR>of a gift, meriting a donation.<BR>—दान-वज्र, अस्,<BR>&c., ‘whose thunderbolt is liberality,’ an epithet of<BR>the Vaiśyas or men of the third tribe.<BR>—दान-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having gifts, presenting gifts, liberal.<BR>—दान-विधि, इस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—दान-वीर, अस्, m. ‘a hero in<BR>liberality,’ an exceedingly liberal man.<BR>—दान-व्य-<BR>त्यास, अस्, m. ‘perversion of gifts,’ gift under error,<BR>giving to the wrong person.<BR>—दान-व्रत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, devoted to liberality or benevolence; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the inhabitants of Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—दान-शील, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, liberally disposed, liberal, generous, charitable,<BR>munificent; (अस्), m., N. of one of the translators<BR>of the Lalita-vistara in Tibetian.<BR>—दान-शूर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘a hero in liberality,’ N. of a Bodhi-sattva (=<BR>Śākya-muni in a former birth; cf. दान-वीर).<BR>—दा-<BR>न-शौण्ड, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘intoxicated with giving,’ ex-<BR>ceedingly liberal.<BR>—दान-सागर, अस्, m. ‘the ocean<BR>of gifts,’ N. of a work by Malamāsa mentioned<BR>in the Saṃskāra-tattva by Raghu-nandana.<BR>—दा-<BR>न-स्तुति, इस्, f. ‘praise of liberality,’ N. of a kind of<BR>hymn.<BR>—दान-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of gifts.<BR>—दान-हेमाद्रि (˚म-अद्˚), N. of a work on<BR>oblations written under the patronage of Hemādri.<BR>—दानाधिकार (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of a short<BR>Buddhist work on alms-giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानक|दानकं
दानक, अम्, n. a mean, paltry, or miserable gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिक
दानिक, (at the end of comp.) relating or referring<BR>to a gift, liberality, giving instruction, &c. (e. g.<BR>अध्ययन-द्˚, consisting in the giving of instruction<BR>or in reading; cf. वर-द्˚ and उदक-द्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिन्
दानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, giving, liberal, benevolent; hav-<BR>ing gifts; [cf. अग्र-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानीय|दानीयः
दानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, due, bestowable, worthy or<BR>fit to be given; receiving gifts or oblations; (अम्),<BR>n. a thing to be given, gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानु|दानुः
1. दानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. liberal; a donor, giver;<BR>prosperity, contentment; air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापन|दापनं
दापन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), forcing or obliging<BR>to give or pay, causing to restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापनीय
दापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made to give or pay,<BR>liable to be amerced, subject to the payment of a<BR>fine (with acc. of the sum paid); to be caused to<BR>be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापयितव्य
दापयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be forced or obliged<BR>to give or pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापयित्वा
दापयित्वा, ind. having caused or compelled to<BR>give or pay, having fined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापित|दापितः
1. दापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be given, con-<BR>demned to pay, fined; adjudged, to be paid by way<BR>of fine; assigned, awarded, entitled to receive a fine,<BR>any one to whom a fine is to be paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाप्य
दाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = दापनीय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
1. दामन्, आ, m. (for 2. and 3. दामन् see<BR>p. 408, col. 2), Ved. a giver, donor; (अ), n. giving,<BR>a gift; [cf. अ-द्˚ and सु-द्˚.] — 1. दामन्-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, furnished with gifts; [cf. 2. दामन्-वत्<BR>under 3. दामन्, p. 408, col. 2.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
1. दाय, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. 2. दाय, p. 408, col. 2], giv-<BR>ing, presenting [cf. शत-द्˚]; (अस्), m. a gift, present,<BR>donation; a special gift, a nuptial present, that which<BR>a bride and bridegroom receive on their marriage;<BR>alms to a student at his initiation &c.; delivering,<BR>delivery, handing over; (for other meanings given by<BR>some under 1. दाय see 2. दाय, p. 408, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायक|दायकः
1. दायक, अस्, इका, अम्, giving, bestowing, pre-<BR>senting, granting; effecting; a giver, donor (e. g.<BR>विष-द्˚, उत्तर-द्˚, मनोरथ-द्˚, कान्ति-द्˚,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">Page0408-a+ 80</a>]<BR>जीव-द्˚, q. v.); placing upon, arranging.<BR>—दायक-<BR>ता, f. the state of a giver, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0407-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायित|दायितः
दायित, अस्, आ, अम्, probably a wrong reading for<BR>दापित, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायितृ
1. दायितृ, incorrect form for 1. दातृ, p. 407, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायिन्
दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of comp.) giving,<BR>presenting, granting, paying, owing; communicat-<BR>ing; causing, effecting; [cf. अ-द्˚, उदक-द्˚, ऋ-<BR>षभ-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारु|दारुः
1. दारु, उस्, उस्, उ (for 2. दारु see p. 410, col. 1),<BR>liberal, munificent, giving, communicating, compas-<BR>sionate; a giver, donor; an artist (in this sense<BR>perhaps to be referred to rt. दॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दावन्
दावन्, Ved., occurring only in dat. दावने, for<BR>the giving, in order to give or present; in order to<BR>receive; (आ, आ, अ), giving, granting, (usually at the<BR>end of comp.; cf. अश्व-द्˚ and शत-द्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा 3. दा, cl. 2. 4. P. दाति, द्यति, दातुम्, to<BR>cut, divide; [according to native authorities the<BR>proper form of this rt. is दो, q. v.; cf. rts. दाय्, दल्:<BR>Gr. δαί-ο-μαι, δαί(τ)-ς, δαιτύ-ς, δαί-τη, δαι-τρό-ς,<BR>δαί-νυ-μι, δαί-νυ-μαι, δαι-τυ-μών, δαΐζω, δατέ-ο-μαι,<BR>δα-σ-μό-ς, δάπτω (Caus.), δεῖπνον: Lat. daps:<BR>Cambro-Brit. de, ‘to part;’ dead, ‘a parting.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
2. दात, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, divided; reaped; (see<BR>Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 46.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाति|दातिः
2. दाति, इस्, f. cutting, destroying; distribution.<BR>—दाति-वार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (Sāy.) splitting the<BR>clouds or yielding water or giving strength or giving<BR>riches, (as if fr. 1. दा; see 1. दाति, p. 407, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातु
दातु, उ, n., Ved. a part, division, allotted portion<BR>or task; (at the end of an adj. comp. after a nume-<BR>ral = fold, e. g. सहस्र-दातु, thousand-fold.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
2. दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ (for 1. दातृ see p. 407, col. 2),<BR>Ved. cutting off, mowing; cropping (grass); a cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्र|दात्रं
दात्र, अम्, n., Ved. anything allotted or fallen<BR>to one's share, share, possession; an instrument for<BR>cutting or chopping wood &c., a sort of sickle or<BR>large knife, a bill-hook or hatchet with a curved<BR>point, commonly called a Dā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
2. दान, अस्, m. (for 1. दान see p. 407, col. 2),<BR>Ved. distribution (especially of food); a meal; a sacri-<BR>ficial meal; distributing, communicating, liberality;<BR>part, share, possession; a distributer; (अम्), n. cut-<BR>ting off, dividing; pasture; the fluid flowing from<BR>an elephant's temples when in rut; [cf. 1. दान.]<BR>—दानाप्नस् (˚न-अप्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having<BR>abundant shares (or gifts, fr. 1. दान).<BR>—दानौकस्<BR>(˚न-ओक्˚), आस्, m., Ved. delighting in the sacrificial<BR>meal; (Sāy.) ‘the abode of liberality, munificent,’<BR>epithet of Indra, (as if fr. 1. दान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव|दानवः
दानव, अस्, ई, m. f. a class of demons, a giant,<BR>a Titan; (according to a later conception the Dānavas,<BR>who are implacable enemies of the Devas, are children<BR>of Danu and Kaśyapa, see दनु, p. 401; the Daityas<BR>and Dānavas are often identified, and both of them<BR>are called Asuras); (अस्, ई, अम्), belonging to the<BR>Dānavas, peculiar to the Dānavas, &c.<BR>—दानव-<BR>गुरु, उस्, m. ‘the preceptor of the Dānavas,’ N. of<BR>the regent of the planet Venus.<BR>—दानव-पति, इस्,<BR>m. the king of the Dānavas.<BR>—दानव-पूजित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, worshipped by the Dānavas; (अस्), m. the<BR>regent of the planet Venus.<BR>—दानव-प्रिया, f. the<BR>betel plant.<BR>—दानव-सूदन, अस्, आ, अम्, destroy-<BR>ing the Dānavas.<BR>—दानवारि (˚व-अरि), इस्, m. an<BR>enemy of the Dānavas; an epithet of Indra; of<BR>Śiva; (अयस्), m. pl. the gods.<BR>—दानवेन्द्र (˚व-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, m. the chief of the Dānavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवेय|दानवेयः
दानवेय, अस्, m. a Dānava or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानु|दानुः
2. दानु, उस्, उस्, उ (for 1. see p. 407, col. 3), valiant;<BR>a victor, conqueror, destroyer; (उस्), m. a class of<BR>demons; (उ), n. a fluid, a drop, dew; [cf. आर्द्र-द्˚,<BR>जीर-द्˚.]<BR>—दानु-चित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining<BR>with dew, brilliant with moisture; (Sāy.) wonderfully<BR>destructive, wonderfully liberal, marvellous by gifts,<BR>(as if fr. 1. दा.)<BR>—दानु-द, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving<BR>drops, trickling.<BR>—दानुनस्-पती, m. du. (fr. the<BR>gen. sing. of 2. दानु), Ved. ‘the lords of dew,’ epithet<BR>of Mitra-varuṇa and of the Aśvins; (Sāy.) lords of<BR>munificence, (as if fr. 1. दा.)<BR>—दानु-पिन्व, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">Page0408-b+ 80</a>]<BR>&c., Ved. swelling with drops.<BR>—दानु-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. having many oblations; liquid, fluid,<BR>trickling; (Sāy.) malignant, injurious; having gifts,<BR>liberal, suited to a giver, (as if fr. 1. दा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
2. दामन्, आ, आ, m. f. (for 1. दामन् see p. 407,<BR>col. 3; for 3. दामन् see below), an allotment, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
2. दाय, अस्, m. [cf. 1. दाय, p. 407, col. 3], share,<BR>portion, separate property, inheritance, patrimony<BR>(e. g. दायाद् उपागत, fallen to one's share by in-<BR>heritance); a part (in शत-द्˚, q. v.); distributing,<BR>dividing, breaking; loss, destruction; irony; place,<BR>site, (some of the meanings here given as connected<BR>with rt. 3. दा may perhaps be referred to rt. 1. दा;<BR>cf. 1. दाय.)<BR>—दाय-काल, अस्, m. the time of<BR>dividing an inheritance.<BR>—दाय-क्रम-सङ्ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a work on the law of inheritance.<BR>—दाय-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a part of the Smṛti-<BR>tattva.<BR>—दायतत्त्व-कृत्, त्, m., N. of an author<BR>mentioned in the Mitrodaya by Mitra-miśra.<BR>—दाय-<BR>बन्धु, उस्, m. ‘a friend or partner in the inherit-<BR>ance,’ a brother.<BR>—दाय-भाग, अस्, m. partition or<BR>portioning of inheritance, division of property among<BR>heirs, apportioning, inheritance; N. of a work on<BR>the law of inheritance.<BR>—दायभाग-टीका, f., N. of<BR>a commentary on the Dāya-bhāga by Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—दायभाग-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a work by<BR>Raghu-nandana.<BR>—दाय-विभाग, अस्, m. portion-<BR>ing of inheritance, division of property amongst<BR>heirs, portion.<BR>—दायाद (˚य-आद), अस्, m. ‘the<BR>receiver of a portion or heritage,’ an heir, claimant,<BR>candidate, pretender (with gen. or loc. of thing); a<BR>son, a kinsman near or remote, a distant descendant;<BR>(आ, ई), f. an heiress, daughter.<BR>—दायाद-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having an heir.<BR>—दायाद्य, अम्, n. inherit-<BR>ance.<BR>—दायाद्य-ता, f. the state of being an inheritor<BR>or near relation, near relationship, affinity.<BR>—दाया-<BR>पवर्तन (˚य-अप्˚), अम्, n. forfeiture of property,<BR>privation.<BR>—दायार्ह (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, claim-<BR>able or claiming inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायक|दायकः
2. दायक, अस्, m. a heir, inheritor, kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायादव
दायादव, अस्, m. an inheritor, heir, kinsman (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित|दितं
1. दित, अस्, आ, अम्, cut, torn, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन|दिनं|दिनः
1. दिन, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. दिन see p. 412, col. 3),<BR>cut, split, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा 4. दा, cl. 4. P. द्यति, दातुम्, to bind;<BR>(this root does not occur separately, and is<BR>not given in the Dhātu-pāṭha); [cf. Gr. δέ-ω, δί-δη-μι,<BR>δέ-σι-ς, δε-τἠ, δε-σ-μό-ς, διά-δη-μα; Angl.<BR>Sax. ti-an, ‘to tie.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाम
दाम (at the end of comp.) = 3. दामन् below;<BR>[cf. उद्-द्˚ and स्रग्-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
3. दामन्, अ, n. (said to be also आ, f.), a string,<BR>cord, thread, rope, fetter, fillet; a girdle; a chaplet,<BR>wreath or garland for the forehead; a large bandage;<BR>a particular constellation. The word दामन् may<BR>be used at the end of an adj. comp., e. g. उरु-<BR>दामन्, having a large garland; and according to<BR>Pāṇini IV. 1, 27, when a numeral precedes, the fem.<BR>must end in ई, e. g. द्वि-दाम्नी, having two cords:<BR>it also occurs at the end of proper names, e. g.<BR>आशा-द्˚, q. v.; [cf. Gr. κρή-δεμνον.]<BR>—दाम-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having a rope round the<BR>neck; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>descendants of this man.<BR>—दाम-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. a<BR>name assumed by Nakula; [cf. ग्रन्थिक.]<BR>—दा-<BR>म-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दाम-जात-<BR>श्री, ईस्, m., N. of a prince (occurring only on coins).<BR> — 2. दामन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (for 1. see p. 407, col. 3),<BR>furnished with cords &c.<BR>—दाम-सिंह, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—दामाञ्चन (˚म-अञ्˚), अम्, n. a foot-<BR>rope for horses &c.; (also दामाञ्चल, अम्, n.)<BR>—दा-<BR>माद्य्-उपाख्यान (˚म-आद्˚), अम्, n., N. of the<BR>fourteenth chapter of the Vāsiṣṭha-rāmāyaṇa, com-<BR>monly called Yoga-vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—दामोदर (˚म-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu (‘having a<BR>cord round the belly,’ Yaśodā his foster-mother<BR>having in vain passed a rope round his body, whilst<BR>a child, to keep him in confinement); N. of the<BR>twelfth month; of the ninth Arhat of the past<BR>Ut-sarpiṇī; of two kings of Kaśmīra; of a poet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">Page0408-c+ 79</a>]<BR>in the Bhoja-prabandha by Ballāla; of the editor of<BR>the drama called Mahā-nāṭaka; of the author of a<BR>medical work; of the father of Malhaṇa and of<BR>several other men; of a river.<BR>—दामोदर-गुप्त,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—दामोदर-दत्त, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the father of Padma-nātha-datta.<BR>—दामोदर-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—दामोदर-पद्-<BR>धति, इस्, f., N. of an astronomical work.<BR>—दामो-<BR>दरारण्य (˚र-अर्˚), अम्, n. ‘Kṛṣṇa's wood,’ N.<BR>of a forest.<BR>—दामोष्णीष (˚म-उष्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of an old sage; (also read दामोष्णीव and दामोष्-<BR>णीश.)<BR>—दामोष्णीषि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Dāmoṣṇīṣa.<BR>—दामोष्णीष्य, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Dāmoṣṇīṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनी
दामनी, f. [cf. दामन, p. 409, col. 3], a mul-<BR>titude of ropes or strings for tying cattle (especially<BR>calves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनीक
दामनीक, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of an adj.<BR>comp. = दामनी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामा
दामा, f. a string, cord, &c., = 3. दामन्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित|दितं
2. दित, अस्, आ, अम्, bound; [cf. सं-दित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा 5. दा, cl. 1. A. दयते, दातुम्, to pro-<BR>tect, defend, guard; (according to native<BR>authorities the proper form of this rt. is दे, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, protected, defended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
6. दा, आस्, f. protection, defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा 7. दा, cl. 1. P. दायति, दातुम्, to<BR>clean, purify; (according to native authori-<BR>ties the proper form of this rt. is दै, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
8. दा, आस्, f. cleansing, purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
3. दात, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. अव-दात], cleansed, cleaned,<BR>washed, purified; (see Pāṇ. VII. 4, 46.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
3. दान, अम्, n. purification; [cf. 1. अव-दान.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक|दाकः
दाक दाक. See under. rt. 1. दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष
दाक्ष दाक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दक्ष), relat-<BR>ing to Dakṣa; relating to Dākṣi; (अस्), m. or<BR>(अम्), n. the south; दाक्षस्यायनम् (˚य-अय्˚)<BR>= दक्षिणायनम्, the progress of the sun towards<BR>the south; the winter solstice; the sacrifice per-<BR>formed at this time; (आस्), m. pl., N. of the disciples<BR>of a particular school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षक|दाक्षकं
दाक्षक, अस्, &c., inhabited by the Dākṣis;<BR>(अम्), n. a multitude of the descendants of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण|दाक्षायणः
दाक्षायण, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from the<BR>Dakṣa family, of or relating to Dakṣa; (अस्), m.<BR>a son or distant descendant of Dakṣa; a particular<BR>kind of sacrifice [cf. दाक्षायण-यज्ञ]; (ई), f., N. of<BR>any of the daughters of Dakṣa; of Aditi; of Diti; of<BR>Kadrū; of Vi-natā; of the nymph and asterism<BR>Rohiṇī; of Su-rasā, mother of the Nāgas; of Jayā<BR>and Vi-jayā; of Svadhā; of Durgā, wife of Śiva; of<BR>the wife of Dharma, mentioned in the Vāmana-<BR>Purāṇa; N. of the plant Croton Polyandrum, =<BR>दन्ती; (ण्यस्), f. pl. the twenty-seven lunar man-<BR>sions considered mythologically as the daughters of<BR>Dakṣa and wives of the Moon; (अम्), n. the pos-<BR>terity of Dakṣa; gold or a gold ornament (as an<BR>ear-ring &c.); = दाक्षस्यायनम्, the winter sol-<BR>stice; the sacrifice performed at this time.<BR>—दा-<BR>क्षायण-भक्त, अम्, n. the district inhabited by<BR>the Dākṣas.<BR>—दाक्षायण-यज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a kind of sacrifice said to be a modification of the<BR>Darśapaurṇamāsa (extending through fifteen instead<BR>of thirty years).<BR>—दाक्षायणयज्ञिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or दाक्षायणयज्ञिन्, ई, इनी, इ, belonging to the<BR>Dākṣāyaṇa sacrifice.<BR>—दाक्षायणी-प, अस्, or दा-<BR>क्षायणी-पति, इस्, m. ‘husband of Dākṣāyaṇī,’<BR>epithet of the Moon; of Śiva.<BR>—दाक्षायणी-र-<BR>मण, अस्, m. ‘delighting in Dākṣāyaṇī,’ epithet<BR>of the Moon.<BR>—दाक्षायण्य्-अग्नि-प्रवेश, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the tenth chapter of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणिन्
दाक्षायणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having gold, wearing<BR>golden ornaments; (ई), m. a Brāhman student wear-<BR>ing golden ear-rings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण्य|दाक्षायण्यः
दाक्षायण्य, अस्, m. the son of the Dākṣā<BR>yaṇī Aditi, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणी
दाक्षायिणी, f. wrong form for दाक्षायणी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षि|दाक्षिः
दाक्षि, इस्, m. a son of Dakṣa; (ई), f. a daughter<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">Page0409-a+ 76</a>]<BR>of Dakṣa.<BR>—दाक्षि-कन्था, f., N. of a village in<BR>the north of India in the country of the Vāhlikas<BR>or Balkh.<BR>—दाक्षिकन्थीय, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>or born in Dākṣi-kanthā, relating to Dākṣi-kanthā.<BR>—दाक्षि-कर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR>—दा-<BR>क्षिकार्षुक, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from or relating<BR>to Dākṣi-karṣa.<BR>—दाक्षि-कूल, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>village.<BR>—दाक्षि-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR>—दाक्षिग्रामीय, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or<BR>relating to Dākṣi-grāma.<BR>—दाक्षि-नगर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town.<BR>—दाक्षि-पलद and दाक्षि-<BR>प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of places.<BR>—दाक्षि-ह्रद,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a lake.<BR>—दाक्षिह्रदीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to the above lake.<BR>—दाक्षी-पुत्र, अस्, m.<BR>‘the son of Dākṣī,’ Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षेय|दाक्षेयः
दाक्षेय, अस्, m. ‘the son of Dākṣī,’ a metro-<BR>nymic of Pāṇini; (ई), f. ‘the daughter of Dākṣī (?).’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष्य|दाक्ष्यं
दाक्ष्य, अम्, n. cleverness, dexterity, skill, abi-<BR>lity, capability, fitness; probity, integrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षाय्य|दाक्षाय्यः
दाक्षाय्य दाक्षाय्य, अस्, m. a vulture; [cf.<BR>दक्षाय्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण
दाक्षिण दाक्षिण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दक्षिणा),<BR>belonging or relating to a sacrificial gift or to a gift<BR>in general; relating or belonging to the south;<BR>(अम्), n. a collection of sacrificial gifts; (आनि), n.<BR>pl., N. of a Kāṇḍa in the Taittirīya-saṃhitā.<BR>—दा-<BR>क्षिणशाल, अस्, &c. (fr. दक्षिण + शाला), relating<BR>to a hall or room situated to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणात्य|दाक्षिणात्यः
दाक्षिणात्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. दक्षिणा, ind.),<BR>southerly, southern, belonging to or produced in<BR>the south; belonging to or living in the Dekhan,<BR>situated in the Dekhan; दाक्षिणात्या भाषा, the<BR>language spoken in the south; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>preceptor mentioned in the Ānanda-laharī; the cocoa-<BR>nut; (अस्, अम्), m. or n. (?), the south; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the inhabitants of the Dekhan; N. of several precep-<BR>tors mentioned in the Kāma-sūtra by Vātsyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणिक
दाक्षिणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दक्षिणा), connected<BR>with a sacrificial gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणीय
दाक्षिणीय = दक्षिणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्य|दाक्षिण्यं
1. दाक्षिण्य, अस्, &c. (fr. दक्षिणा), belonging<BR>or relating to a sacrificial gift; meriting a sacrificial<BR>gift or reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्य|दाक्षिण्यं
2. दाक्षिण्य, अम्, n. (fr. दक्षिण), civility, cour-<BR>tesy, politeness, conciliatory conduct, propitiation,<BR>kindness, obsequiousness, concord, harmony, agree-<BR>ment; honesty, sincerity, candour; cleverness, talent;<BR>(probably) the ritual of the right-hand Sāktas (?);<BR>N. of a Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दागव्यायनि
दागव्यायनि दागव्यायनि, a patronymic<BR>from Dagu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडक|दाडकः
दाडक दाडक, अस्, m. a tooth, tusk; [cf.<BR>दाढा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम|दाडिमः
दाडिम दाडिम, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. दल्), the pomegranate tree, (according to<BR>some the m. f. applies to the tree, and the n. to the<BR>fruit); small cardamoms; (अस्, ई, अम्), being on the<BR>pomegranate tree.<BR>—दाडिम-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. or<BR>दाडिम-पुष्प or दाडिम-पुष्पक, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Soymida Febrifuga or Amoora Rohitaka (=<BR>रोहितक).<BR>—दाडिम-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond of<BR>pomegranates,’ a parrot.<BR>—दाडिम-भक्षण, अस्,<BR>m. ‘eating pomegranates,’ a parrot.<BR>—दाडिमी-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, planted with pomegranate trees.<BR>—दा-<BR>डिमी-सार, अस्, m. = दाडिम, the pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम्ब|दाडिंब|दाडिंबः|दाडिम्बः
दाडिम्ब, अस्, m. = दाडिम, the pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडी
दाडी दाडी, f. a kind of plant and its fruit;<BR>[cf. दोडी and दालि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढा
दाढा दाढा, f. = दंष्ट्रा, a large tooth,<BR>tusk; wish, desire; a number, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढिका
दाढिका, f. = दंष्ट्रिका, the beard, the whiskers;<BR>(Manu VIII. 283.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्ड|दांड
दाण्ड दाण्ड, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a stick<BR>or staff, relating to punishment, &c.; (आ), f. a par-<BR>ticular game with sticks.<BR>—दाण्डग्राहिक, अस्, m.<BR>a patronymic from Daṇḍa-graha.<BR>—दाण्डपाता, f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">Page0409-b+ 73</a>]<BR>(fr. दण्ड-पात), scil. तिथि, a particular festival,<BR>the day of full moon in the month Phālguna, on<BR>which sticks are thrown; [cf. तैलम्पाता and श्यै-<BR>नम्पाता.]<BR>—दाण्डपायन, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Daṇḍa-pa.<BR>—दाण्डमाथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>दण्ड-माथ), churning with a straight stick or<BR>staff.<BR>—दाण्डाजिनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दण्डाजिन),<BR>carrying a staff and hide as mere outward signs of<BR>religion; (अस्), m. a cheat, rogue, an hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डकि
दाण्डकि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Daṇḍaka;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl., N. of a race belonging to the<BR>Tri-gartas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डकीय
दाण्डकीय, अस्, m. a prince of the Dāṇḍakis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डायन
दाण्डायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Daṇḍa (?).<BR>—दाण्डायनस्थलक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>or coming from Dāṇḍāyana-sthalī.<BR>—दाण्डायन-<BR>स्थली, f., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डिक|दांडिक|दांडिकः|दाण्डिकः
दाण्डिक, अस्, ई, अम्, inflicting punishment,<BR>punishing; (अस्), m. a chastiser, punisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डिक्य
दाण्डिक्य, अम्, n. punishing, the state of being<BR>a punisher (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डिन्
दाण्डिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of the disciples of the<BR>school of Daṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डिनायन
दाण्डिनायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Daṇḍin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
दात दात, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school of the<BR>Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
दातृ दातृ. See p. 407, col. 2; p. 408, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्तामित्रीय
दात्तामित्रीय दात्तामित्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relat-<BR>ing to or coming from Dattāmitra or Dattāmitrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्तेय
दात्तेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Dattā, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यूह|दात्यूहः
दात्यूह दात्यूह, अस्, m. a gallinule; the<BR>Cātaka, a sort of cuckoo, Cuculus Melanoleucus;<BR>a cloud (the water of which the Cātaka is said to<BR>drink).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यूहक
दात्यूहक, अस्, m. a familiar diminutive of दा-<BR>त्यूह, a little gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यौह|दात्यौहः
दात्यौह, अस्, m. (according to Pāṇ. VII. 3, 1, fr.<BR>दित्य-वाह्), a gallinule; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to or<BR>produced in the vehicle of a demon (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाद|दादः
दाद दाद, दादिन्, &c. See p. 407, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दादाभाई
दादाभाई दादाभाई, N. of the author of<BR>the Kiraṇāvalī (a commentary on the Indian astro-<BR>nomical work Sūrya-siddhānta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधिक|दाधिकं
दाधिक दाधिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दधि), made<BR>of or from Dadhi or coagulated milk; mixed with<BR>it, sprinkled with it; carrying about or selling coagu-<BR>lated milk; eating anything with coagulated milk;<BR>(अम्), n. a kind of broth or gruel made of coagu-<BR>lated milk mixed with other substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधिक्र
दाधिक्र, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. relating to Dadhi-krā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधित्थ
दाधित्थ दाधित्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दधित्थ),<BR>coming from or belonging to the Feronia Elephan-<BR>tum; (अम्), n. the resin of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधीच
दाधीच दाधीच, अस्, m. (fr. दध्यञ्च्),<BR>Ved. a patronymic of Cyavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधृवि
दाधृवि दाधृवि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. धृ), Ved.<BR>holding, bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधृषि
दाधृषि दाधृषि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. the Intens.<BR>of rt. धृष्), Ved. courageous, bold; overbearing,<BR>overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्
दान् दान्, cl. 1. P. A. or cl. 10. P. दान-<BR>यति, &c., to cut off: Desid. P. A. दीदं-<BR>सति, -ते, to straighten, make straight; to be straight;<BR>(this verb is by some regarded as a nominal fr. 2.<BR>दान; cf. 2. दन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
दान दान, &c. See under rts. 1. and 3. दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव|दानवः
दानव दानव. See दानु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त|दांत|दान्तः
दान्त 1. दान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. दम्),<BR>tamed, broken in, subdued, daunted, bridled, re-<BR>strained; tame, mild; patient of privations or aus-<BR>terity, &c.; resigned; liberal (fr. rt. 1. दा?); (अस्),<BR>m. a tamed ox or steer; a donor, giver (fr. rt. 1. दा);<BR>N. of a plant, = दमनक, = वड, = वट, Ficus<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">Page0409-c+ 75</a>]<BR>Indica; N. of a son of Bhīma, king of Vidarbha;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a school of the Atharva-veda;<BR>(आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्ति|दांति|दांतिः|दान्तिः
दान्ति, इस्, f. self-restraint; the patient endurance<BR>of religious austerities or privations; subjection, hu-<BR>miliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त्वा
दान्त्वा, ind. having subdued, tamed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त|दांत|दान्तः
दान्त 2. दान्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दन्त), dental,<BR>made of ivory; ‘completed by Danta (?),’ epithet of a<BR>well situated on the northern or southern bank of the<BR>river Vipāśā; (see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 74, Schol.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्तिक|दांतिक
दान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, made of ivory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाभी
दाभी दाभी, f. (fr. rt. दभ्?), Ved. hurt-<BR>ing, injuring (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाभ्य
दाभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be disturbed or obstructed;<BR>to be governed or ruled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामचरित
दामचरित दाम-चरित or श्री-दाम-चरित<BR>or -चरित्र, अम्, n. ‘the adventures of Śrī-dāman’<BR>(or Śrī-dāma ?), N. of a drama in five acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन
दामन दामन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दमन), re-<BR>lating to the Dona or Artemisia flower.<BR>—दामन-<BR>पर्वन्, अ, n. the fourteenth of the light half of the<BR>month Caitra, a festival on which Artemisia flowers<BR>are gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनि
दामनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Damana;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl., N. of a warrior-tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनीय
दामनीय, अस्, m. (fr. दामनि), a prince of the<BR>Dāmanis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामलिप्त|दामलिप्तं
दामलिप्त दामलिप्त, अम्, n., N. of a town<BR>or country, the modern district of Tumlook, =<BR>तामलिप्त; [cf. ताम्रलिप्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामोद
दामोद दामोद, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school<BR>of the Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाम्पत्य|दांपत्य|दांपत्यं
दाम्पत्य दाम्पत्य, अम्, n. (fr. दम्-पती),<BR>matrimony, the marriage-state, the matrimonial or<BR>conjugal relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाम्भिक|दांभिक|दाम्भिकः
दाम्भिक दाम्भिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दम्भ,<BR>q. v.), deceitful, hypocritical; proud, imperious, os-<BR>tentatious; sanctimonious; (अस्), m. a cheat; a<BR>hypocrite; a kind of crane, Ardea Nivea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय्
दाय् दाय् (a form of rt. 1. दा, given by<BR>some grammarians; cf. आ-दायमान<BR>under 1. आ-दा), cl. 1. A. दायते, &c., to give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
दाय दाय. See under rts. 1. दा at p. 407,<BR>col. 3, and 3. दा at p. 408, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार|दारः
दार दार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. दॄ), a rent, cleft,<BR>gap, hole; a ploughed field; a wife, (usually occurring<BR>in the m. pl. आस् or in comp.: an exceptional form दारा,<BR>f. sing., occurs in one or two passages; and in Pañca-<BR>tantra I. 450, the neut. pl. दाराणि); दारान् कृ, to<BR>take a wife, marry; [cf. कृत-द्˚.]<BR>—दार-कर्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. or दार-क्रिया, f. taking a wife, marry-<BR>ing, marriage; [cf. दार-परिग्रह.]<BR>—दार-<BR>गव, अम्, n. wife and cows.<BR>—दार-ग्रहण, अम्,<BR>n. ‘taking a wife,’ marriage.<BR>—दार-परिग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘taking a wife,’ marriage.<BR>—दारपरिग्र-<BR>हिन्, ई, इणी, इ, ‘taking a wife,’ marrying.<BR>—दार-<BR>लक्षण, अम्, n. a characteristic sign or decisive<BR>mark of wife-hood.<BR>—दार-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘taking<BR>a wife,’ marrying, marriage.<BR>—दाराणुक्रमण<BR>(˚र-अण्˚), अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-<BR>sarva-sva.<BR>—दाराधीन (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dependent on a wife, in the power of a wife.<BR>—दा-<BR>रोपसङ्ग्रह (˚र-उप्˚), अस्, m. ‘taking a wife,’<BR>marrying, marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारक|दारकः
दारक, अस्, इका, अम्, breaking, tearing, splitting;<BR>(अस्), m. a boy, son, child, infant; a young animal;<BR>a village hog; the charioteer of Kṛṣṇa; (इका), f. a<BR>rent, cleft, gap, chap; a daughter; a harlot; (औ), m.<BR>du. a boy and a girl.<BR>—दारकाचार्य (˚क-आच्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘a preceptor of boys,’ a schoolmaster.<BR>—दारिका-<BR>दान, अम्, n. the gift of a daughter in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारण|दारणं
दारण, अस्, ई, अम्, tearing, splitting, tearing<BR>asunder; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of tearing, rending, dividing; opening, bursting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">Page0410-a+ 81</a>]<BR>flying open; a means of opening; the clearing-nut<BR>plant, Strychnos Potatorum; [cf. कतक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारव
दारव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. दारु below), wooden,<BR>made of wood, coming from or relating to wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारि|दारिः
दारि, इस्, इस्, इ, tearing, causing to burst, splitting<BR>[cf. वेणु-द्˚]; (इस्), f. cutting, tearing, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारित|दारितः
दारित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn, rent, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिन्
दारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, tearing, splitting; (ई), m. (fr.<BR>दार), a husband; a polygamist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारी
दारी, f. a cleft, gap; a chap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारु|दारुः
2. दारु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ (for 1. दारु see p. 408,<BR>col. 1), tearing, rending; a tearer, breaker, destroyer;<BR>(उस्), m., Ved. ‘the destroyer of cities,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra; (उस्, उ), m. n. (usually n.), a piece of wood,<BR>wood, timber; a block; a lever; a bolt; (उ), n. a<BR>sort of pine, Pinus Devadāru; ore, metal in its<BR>natural state; [cf. तरु, द्रु; Zend dāuru, ‘wood;’<BR>Gr. δόρυ, δούρατα for δόρϝατα, δορήϊος, δουρ-ειο-ς,<BR>δουράτ-εο-ς; Goth. triu, ‘tree;’ Old Sax. trio,<BR>‘timber;’ Eng. tree; Slav. dre†vo, ‘tree;’ Russ.<BR>dérevo, drova; Lith. dervà; Hib. doireach,<BR>‘woody.’]<BR>—दारु-कच्छ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), N. of<BR>a district.<BR>—दारुकच्छक, relating to the above<BR>district.<BR>—दारु-कदली, f. a wild uneatable plantain<BR>(= वन-कदली).<BR>—दारु-कर्णिन्, ई, m. ‘having<BR>wooden ear-rings,’ a N. of Bhavila.<BR>—दारु-गन्धा,<BR>f. a kind of perfume (commonly चीडा).<BR>—दारु-<BR>गर्भा, f. a wooden puppet, a doll.<BR>—दारु-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced from wood, made of wood, wooden;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of drum.<BR>—दारु-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—दारु-निशा, f. Curcuma Zanthor-<BR>rhizon (= दार्वी).<BR>—दारु-पत्त्री, f. a plant, =<BR>हिङ्गु-पत्त्री.<BR>—दारु-पात्र, अम्, n. a wooden<BR>vessel.<BR>—दारु-पीता, f. a plant, = दार्वी.<BR>—दारु-<BR>पुत्रिका or दारु-पुत्री, f. a wooden doll or puppet.<BR>—दारु-फल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), Pistachio (tree<BR>and nut).<BR>—दारु-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, wooden, made<BR>of wood (e. g. दारु-मयी योषा or स्त्री or नारी,<BR>‘a wooden woman,’ a doll).<BR>—दारु-मुख्याह्वया<BR>or दारु-मुख्याह्वा (˚य-आह्˚), f. a lizard.<BR>—दारु-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a wooden puppet moved by strings.<BR>—दारु-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दारु-<BR>वह, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing or carrying timber.<BR>—दारु-<BR>सिता, f. cinnamon in sticks.<BR>—दारु-स्त्री, f. a wooden<BR>doll; [cf. दारु-मय.]<BR>—दारु-हरिद्रा, f. a species<BR>of Curcuma, = दार्वी.<BR>—दारु-हस्तक, अस्, m. a<BR>wooden spoon or ladle.<BR>—दारु-आघाट, अस्, m. or<BR>दार्व्-आघात, अस्, m. the woodpecker.<BR>—दार्व्-<BR>आहार, अस्, m. a collector of wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुक|दारुकं|दारुकः
दारुक, अस्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa's charioteer, who<BR>was son of Satyaka; N. of an incarnation of Śiva;<BR>(आ), f. a wooden figure; a doll, puppet; (अम्), n.<BR>a sort of pine, Pinus Devadāru.<BR>—दारुका-वन,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a wood containing a famous Liṅga.<BR>—दारुकेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क or ˚का-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुकि
दारुकि, इस्, m., N. of Pra-dyumna's charioteer,<BR>who was son of Dāruka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण|दारुणः
दारुण, अस्, आ or rarely ई, अम् (perhaps not<BR>directly fr. rt. दॄ, but rather fr. 2. दारु above),<BR>hard, harsh (opposed to मृदु), rough, sharp,<BR>severe (as speech); cruel, pitiless, heart-rending; ter-<BR>rible, terrific, frightful, dreadful, fearful, grievous;<BR>shocking, atrocious, dire; agonising, painful; intense,<BR>violent, severe, great; (अस्, अम्), m. n. harshness,<BR>severity, hard-heartedness, cruelty, horror, horrible-<BR>ness; (अस्), m., N. of the plant Plumbago Zeylanica<BR>(= चित्रक). दारुण at the beginning of comp.<BR>or before a verb expresses excellence or superiority;<BR>[cf. काष्ठ and see दारुणाध्यापक below.]<BR>—दारुण-कर्मन्, अ, n. violent treatment (as of<BR>diseases).<BR>—दारुण-ता, f. harshness, roughness,<BR>frightfulness, direness, severity, intensity.<BR>—दारुण-<BR>वपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, of frightful shape.<BR>—दारुणा-<BR>कृति (˚ण-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, of terrible or dreadful<BR>form.<BR>—दारुणात्मन् (˚ण-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, hard-<BR>hearted, cruel.<BR>—दारुणाध्यापक (˚ण-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. an energetic or indefatigable teacher; [cf.<BR>दारुण above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुणक|दारुणकं
दारुणक, अम्, n. ‘harshness,’ N. of a particular<BR>disease affecting the roots of the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुणाय
दारुणाय, Nom. A. दारुणायते, &c., to act<BR>harshly or cruelly, to be unmerciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण्य|दारुण्यं
दारुण्य, अम्, n. harshness (as of a sound &c.);<BR>cruelty, dreadfulness, direness, severity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व|दार्वं
दार्व, अस्, ई, अम्, wooden, made of wood; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people to the north-east of Madhya-<BR>deśa, generally associated with the Abhi-sāras; (ई),<BR>f., N. of several plants, = दारु-हरिद्रा, दारु-<BR>निशा, Curcuma Aromatica or Curcuma Xanthorrhiza;<BR>a particular species of collyrium extracted from an<BR>infusion of the Curcuma Xanthorrhiza; a species<BR>of pine, = देव-दारु; turmerick; a species of pot-<BR>herb, Go-jihvā.<BR>—दार्वि-पत्त्रिका, f., N. of a plant,<BR>= गो-जिह्वा.<BR>—दार्वी-क्वाथोद्भव (˚थ-उद्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a particular kind of collyrium prepared from<BR>an infusion of Curcuma Aromatica or Curcuma<BR>Xanthorrhiza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वक
दार्वक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or coming from<BR>Dārva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्विका|दार्व्विका
दार्विका, f. a sort of collyrium prepared from<BR>an infusion of Curcuma Aromatica; N. of a plant, =<BR>गो-जिह्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारक|दारकः
दारक दारक, दारण, &c. See p. 409, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारद|दारदः
दारद दारद, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from<BR>the country of the Darads, (a various reading has<BR>दरद); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people, (probably<BR>only a wrong form for दरद); (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>poison brought from the above country; quicksilver;<BR>the ocean; (अस्, अम्), m. n. vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारबलिभुज्
दारबलिभुज् दार-बलि-भुज्, incorrect form<BR>for द्वार-बलि-भुज्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारित|दारितः
दारित दारित, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र|दारिद्रं
दारिद्र दारिद्र, अम्, n. (fr. दरिद्र), poverty,<BR>indigence, (perhaps a wrong form for दारिद्र्य<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र्य|दारिद्र्यं
दारिद्र्य, अम्, n. poverty, indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारु|दारुः
दारु दारु. See col. 1. and p. 408, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण|दारुणः
दारुण दारुण. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारोदर
दारोदर दारोदर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दरोदर),<BR>connected with gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्घसत्त्र
दार्घसत्त्र दार्घसत्त्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दीर्घ-<BR>सत्त्र), connected with a long continued sacrifice,<BR>performing such a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ढच्युत
दार्ढच्युत दार्ढच्युत, अस्, m. (fr. दृढ-<BR>च्युत), a patronymic, (also read दौर्याच्युत);<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ढ्य|दार्ढ्यं
दार्ढ्य दार्ढ्य, अम्, n. (fr. दृढ), hard-<BR>ness, fixedness, tightness, stability; strength, energy;<BR>confirmation, corroboration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्तेय
दार्तेय दार्तेय, अस्, ई, अम्, leathern, made<BR>of leather; (अस्), m. a patronymic from Dṛti, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्दुर|दार्दुरं|दार्दुरः|दार्द्दुर|दार्द्दुरं
दार्दुर दार्दुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दर्दुर), re-<BR>lating to a cloud, frog, &c.; (अम्), n. a conch-shell<BR>or muscle, the valve of which opens to the right;<BR>lac; water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्दुरिक
दार्दुरिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a frog, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्भ
दार्भ दार्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दर्भ), made<BR>of Darbha grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्भायण
दार्भायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Darbha;<BR>(see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 102.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्भि
दार्भि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Darbha; (see<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 1, 102.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्भ्य
दार्भ्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from Darbha,<BR>applied to Śyāvāśva; [cf. दाल्भ्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व|दार्वं
दार्व दार्व. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वट|दार्वटं|दार्व्वट|दार्व्वटं
दार्वट दार्वट, अम्, n. (fr. the Pers. دربار),<BR>a court or council-house; [cf. दर्भट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वण्ड|दार्वंड|दार्वण्डः|दार्व्वण्ड|दार्व्वण्डः
दार्वण्ड दार्वण्ड, अस्, m. a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वन्
दार्वन् दार्वन्, आ, m., N. of a son of Uśī-<BR>nara; [cf. दर्वा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वाघाट|दार्वाघाटः|दार्व्वाघाट|दार्व्वाघाटः
दार्वाघाट दार्व्-आघाट. See 2. दारु, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्वीहौमिक
दार्वीहौमिक दार्वीहौमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>दर्वी-होम), relating to an oblation made with<BR>a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्श
दार्श दार्श, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दर्श), relating<BR>to the new moon or the new moon sacrifice; (अस्),<BR>m., scil. यज्ञ, the new moon sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्शनिक|दार्शनिकः
दार्शनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दर्शन), seeing far;<BR>familiar with the Darśanas or philosophical systems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्शपौर्णमासिक
दार्शपौर्णमासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दर्श-<BR>पूर्ण-मास), belonging to the Darśa-pūrṇa-māsa<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्शिक
दार्शिक, अस्, ई, अम्, or दार्श्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relat-<BR>ing to the new moon or the new moon sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्षद|दार्षदः
दार्षद दार्षद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दृषद्),<BR>ground on a flat stone (as meal &c.); stony, of<BR>stone, mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्षद्वत
दार्षद्वत दार्षद्वत, अम्, n. (fr. दृषद्-<BR>वती), N. of a Sattra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ष्टान्त|दार्ष्टांत
दार्ष्टान्त दार्ष्टान्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दृष्टान्त),<BR>explained by an example or simile or case in point;<BR>illustrated by metaphor or figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ष्टान्तिक|दार्ष्टांतिक
दार्ष्टान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, explained by an illus-<BR>tration or simile; illustrated, any thing which is the<BR>subject of an illustration or simile; suitable to be<BR>used in illustration; one who uses an example or<BR>simile as a proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल|दालं|दालः
दाल दाल, अम्, n. a sort of wild or unpre-<BR>pared honey, (according to some produced by a pecu-<BR>liar kind of small bee; see दल-ज); (आ), f. = दालिका,<BR>देव-दालिका, colocynth; (ई), f. a kind of plant, =<BR>देव-दाली; (अस्), m. a sort of grain, = Paspalum<BR>Frumentaceum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालकि
दालकि दालकि, इस्, m., N. of a pupil of<BR>Śaka-pūrṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालन|दालनं
दालन दालन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. दल्), crum-<BR>bling or decay (of the teeth), tooth-ache.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालभ्य
दालभ्य दालभ्य, a wrong form for Dāl-<BR>bhya, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालव|दालवः
दालव दालव, अस्, m. a sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालिका
दालिका दालिका, f. = दाला, देव-दालिका,<BR>colocynth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालिम|दालिमः
दालिम दालिम, अस्, m. the pomegranate;<BR>[cf. दाडिम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्भ
दाल्भ दाल्भ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दाल्भ्य below),<BR>relating to or coming from Dālbhya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्भि
दाल्भि, इस्, m. (fr. दल्भ), a patronymic of Vaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्भ्य|दाल्भ्यः
दाल्भ्य, अस्, m. (fr. दल्भ), a patronymic of<BR>Keśin; of Caikitāyana; N. of a grammarian.<BR>—दाल्-<BR>भ्य-घोष, अस्, m., N. of an ancient sage.<BR>—दाल्-<BR>भ्य-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n., N. of a poetical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्भ्यक
दाल्भ्यक, अस्, m., N. of an ancient sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्मायणि
दाल्मायणि दाल्मायणि, probably a wrong<BR>form for दाल्भायनि or दार्भायणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्मि|दाल्मिः
दाल्मि दाल्मि, इस्, m., N. of Indra; [cf.<BR>दल्मि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाव|दावः
दाव दाव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. दु), a forest<BR>conflagration, a forest on fire; fire in general, heat;<BR>a forest; [cf. अन्तर्-द्˚ and दव.]<BR>—दाव-दहन-<BR>ज्वाला-कलाप, the mass or sheet of flame arising from<BR>the conflagration of a forest.<BR>—दावदहनज्वाला-<BR>कलापाय, Nom. A. -यते, &c., to resemble the<BR>sheet of flame of a burning forest.<BR>—दाव-प,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. one who keeps watch over a forest on<BR>fire.<BR>—दाव-लता, f. a creeper in a burning wood.<BR>—दाव-विवर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from fire.<BR>—दाव-सु, उस्, m., N. of an Āṅgirasa.<BR>—दावसु-<BR>निधन, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—दावाग्नि (˚व-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, or दावानल (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. a forest on<BR>fire, a forest conflagration, fire in a wood; [cf.<BR>दवाग्नि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0410-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाविक|दाविकः
दाविक दाविक, अस्, &c. (fr. देविका), coming<BR>from the river Devikā; (Pāṇ. VII. 3, 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाविककूल
दाविककूल (fr. देविका-कूल), see Pāṇ. VII. 3, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्
दाश् 1. दाश् (apparently occurring only<BR>in Ṛg-veda), cl. 1. P. A. दाशति, -ते,<BR>(rarely cl. 2. 5. P.) दाष्टि, दाश्नोति, (according to<BR>Vopa-deva also) cl. 10. A. दाशयते, ददाश, (Ved.<BR>forms are ददाशति, ददाशत्, part. दाशिवस् and<BR>दाश्वस्, dat. sing. दाशुषे or ददाशुषे), दाशितुम्,<BR>Ved. to honour or serve a god (dat. or acc.) with<BR>any offering (inst.); to offer any thing (acc.), make<BR>an oblation; to grant, give, bestow [cf. rt. दास्];<BR>cl. 5. दाश्नोति, &c., to hurt, injure, kill [cf. rts.<BR>दास् and दस्]: Caus. P. दाशयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अददासत्, to offer: Desid. दिदाशिषति, -ते: Intens.<BR>दादाश्यते, दादाष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्
2. दाश्, worshipping, making oblations (?); [cf.<BR>दू-डाश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश|दाशः
दाश, अस्, m. [cf. दास with which दश is inter-<BR>changed], Ved. presenting oblations, honouring the<BR>gods with offerings [cf. पुरो-डाश]; a fisherman,<BR>ferryman, boatman, mariner; the son of a Niṣāda by<BR>a woman of the Āyogava caste; a servant, = 1. दास,<BR>col. 2; (ई), f. a fisherwoman; a female slave.<BR>—दा-<BR>श-नन्दिनी or दास-नन्दिनी, f. ‘the fisherman's<BR>daughter,’ epithet of Satya-vatī, who was the mother<BR>of the poet Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशक
दाशक, (probably) a fisherman, (occurring only<BR>in दाशक-पुत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशु
दाशु, उस्, उस्, उ, giving, &c.; see अ-द्˚.<BR>—दाश्व्-<BR>अध्वर, Ved. presenting oblations, honouring the<BR>gods with sacrifices; (Sāy.) the oblation of the<BR>giver of the sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशुरि
दाशुरि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. making oblations or offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेय|दाशेयः
दाशेय or दासेय, अस्, m. (fr. दाशी), the son of<BR>a fisherman's wife; (ई), f. ‘the daughter of a fisher-<BR>man's wife,’ epithet of Satya-vatī, mother of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेर|दाशेरः
दाशेर, अस्, m. a fisherman; a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेरक|दाशेरकः
दाशेरक, अस्, m. a fisherman; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a people, = मरु-भू; [cf. दशेरक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्व|दाश्वः
दाश्व, अस्, आ, अम् (corrupted fr. दाश्वस्), liberal,<BR>giving, a giver, donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्वस्
दाश्वस् (rarely दाशिवस्), वान्, उषी, वस्, Ved.<BR>honouring or serving the gods with offerings, bestow-<BR>ing, offering, giving, granting (with acc. or compounded<BR>with the thing given). In the Ṛg-veda दाश्वस् is<BR>often a general expression for a faithful worshipper<BR>of the gods or a religious and pious man, especially<BR>when connected with मर्त, मर्त्य, and जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशत्
दाशत् दाशत्, wrong form for दशत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशतय
दाशतय दाशतय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दशतय),<BR>belonging to the Ṛg-veda which consists of ten<BR>divisions or Maṇḍalas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशपुर|दाशपुरं
दाशपुर दाशपुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दश-पुर),<BR>coming from Daśa-pura; (अम्), n. a fragrant grass<BR>related to the Cyperus Rotundus; (also दाशपूर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशफली
दाशफली, f. (fr. दश-फल), N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथ|दाशरथः
दाशरथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दश-रथ), belonging<BR>to Daśa-ratha, coming from Daśa-ratha, a descendant<BR>of Daśa-ratha; (अस्), m. a patronymic of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथि|दाशरथिः
दाशरथि, इस्, m. ‘descendant of Daśa-ratha,’ a<BR>patronymic of Rāma; of Lakṣmaṇa, the younger<BR>brother of Rāma; of Catur-aṅga; (with Jainas) N.<BR>of the eighth Black Vāsu-deva; (ई), m. du. Rāma<BR>and Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशराज्ञ
दाशराज्ञ, अम्, n. (fr. दशन् + राजन्), Ved.<BR>‘the fight with ten kings,’ a famous battle fought by<BR>Su-dās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरूप्य
दाशरूप्य (fr. दशन् + रूप), N. of a Grāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशवाज
दाशवाज, अम्, n. (fr. दशन् + वाज); in कौत्-<BR>सं दाशवाजम्, N. of a Sāman; [cf. पाञ्चवाज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशशिरस्
दाशशिरस्, n. (perhaps for दाशशिरस fr. दश-<BR>शिरस्), N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्ण
दाशार्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दशार्ण), containing<BR>the word Daśārṇa, treating of it (as an अनु-वाक<BR>or अध्याय); (अस्), m. a prince of the Daśārṇas;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. = दशार्ण, N. of a people.<BR>—दा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">Page0411-b+ 77</a>]<BR>शार्ण-राज, अस्, m. or दाशार्णेश (˚ण-ईश), अस्,<BR>m. a king of the Daśārṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्णक
दाशार्णक, अस्, इका, अम्, coming from or relat-<BR>ing to or belonging to the Daśārṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्ह|दाशार्हः
दाशार्ह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दशार्ह, q. v.), contain-<BR>ing the word Daśārha, treating of it (as an अध्याय<BR>or अनु-वाक); belonging to Daśārha, i. e. to Kṛṣṇa;<BR>(अस्), m. a prince of the Daśārhas; an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; a Daśārha king of Mathurā; (ई), f. a<BR>princess of the Daśārhas; (आस्), m. pl. = the Da-<BR>śārhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्हक
दाशार्हक, आस्, m. pl. = दशार्हास् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशाश्वमेध
दाशाश्वमेध, आस्, m. pl. (perhaps a wrong<BR>reading for दशाश्वमेधास्), ten horse-sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशौदनिक
दाशौदनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. दशन् + ओदन), N.<BR>of a particular sacrificial rite; (ई), f. the offering made<BR>to the priests at this rite; [cf. पञ्चौदनिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशमेय
दाशमेय दाशमेय. See दासमेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशर्म
दाशर्म दाशर्म, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशस्पत्य
दाशस्पत्य दाशस्पत्य, अम्, n. (fr. दशस् or<BR>दाशस् ? + पति; cf. दशस्य and rt. 1. दाश्), N. of<BR>a Sāman, (perhaps ‘the lord of pious oblations.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशिवस्
दाशिवस् दाशिवस्, दाश्वस्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशुर
दाशुर दाशुर or दाशूर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेय|दाशेयः
दाशेय दाशेय, दाशेर. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्
दास् दास् (generally occurring in con-<BR>nection with the prep. अभि, connected<BR>with rts. 1. दाश्, दस्, दंश्, दंस्), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>दासति, -ते, ददास, -से, दासिता, &c., to give; cl.<BR>5. P. दास्नोति, &c., Ved. to hurt, injure, wound,<BR>kill; [cf. perhaps Gr. ληΐη, ληΐς, λεΐζομαι, ληϊστής,<BR>the द् being changed into ल्, as in rt. ला fr. rt. दा;<BR>probably also Gr. λά-τρο-ν, λά-τρις; Lat. la-tro.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
1. दास, अस्, m. a general N. applied in the Veda<BR>to certain evil beings or demons, hostile to the<BR>human race and to Indra, (those defeated by Indra<BR>have also special names, e. g. Namuci, Pipru, Śambara,<BR>Varcin, &c.); a savage, a barbarian, (opposed in the<BR>Veda to आर्य, &c.; cf. दस्यु); a slave, servant, (in<BR>this sense occurring at the end of the names of<BR>Sūdras and Kāya-sthas; cf. also कालि-दास); one to<BR>whom gifts may be made; = दाश, a fisherman,<BR>boatman; (ई), f. a female servant or slave, servant-<BR>maid; whore, harlot, (in this sense having the<BR>accent on the first syllable); N. of a plant, =<BR>नीलाझिण्टी, = काक-जङ्घा, = नीलाम्लान; an altar;<BR>N. of a river; (अस्, ई, अम्), belonging to the<BR>Dāsas, i. e. to demons, barbarians, &c.; consisting<BR>of the Dāsas, &c.; [cf. Gr. δοῦλος derived in a<BR>similar manner from δοῦν, ‘to give or serve.’]<BR>—दा-<BR>स-जन, अस्, m. a slave; = दासी, a female servant.<BR>—दास-जीवन, अम्, n. ‘slave-life,’ the work or<BR>business of a slave.<BR>—दास-ता, f. or दास-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the condition of a slave, slavery, servitude.<BR>—दा-<BR>स-दासी, f. the female slave of a slave.<BR>—दास-<BR>नन्दिनी = दाश-नन्दिनी, q. v.<BR>—दास-पत्नी, f.,<BR>Ved. having the demons as masters, being in the<BR>power of the demons; (Sāy.) having Dāsa, i. e. the<BR>destroyer, or Vṛtra as husband; [cf. Gr. δέσποινα.]<BR>—दास-प्रवर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to<BR>Sāy.) having a multitude of servants, having a large<BR>number of slaves; [cf. प्र-वर्ग.]<BR>—दास-भार्य,<BR>अम्, n. servants and wives.<BR>—दास-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>the condition of a slave, slavery, servitude.<BR>—दास-<BR>मित्र, अस्, m. ‘friend of a slave,’ N. of a man.<BR>—दासमित्रायण, अस्, or दासमित्रि, इस्, m. a<BR>patronymic from Dāsa-mitra.<BR>—दासमित्रायण-<BR>भक्त or दासमित्रि-भक्त, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>district inhabited by the Dāsamitrāyaṇas or Dāsa-<BR>mitris.<BR>—दासमित्रिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, relating to<BR>or coming from Dāsa-mitra.<BR>—दास-मिथुन, अम्,<BR>n., Ved. a couple of slaves or servants.<BR>—दास-वर्ग,<BR>अस्, m. the whole collection of slaves, all the servants.<BR>—दास-वेश, अस्, m., Ved. (according to Sāy.) the<BR>destruction of the demons.<BR>—दास-शर्मन्, आ, m.,<BR>N. of a scholiast on the Śrauta-sūtras of Śāṅkhāyana.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">Page0411-c+ 75</a>]<BR>—दासस्य-कुल, अम्, n. (see Pāṇ. VI. 3, 21), the<BR>common people, low people, the mob.<BR>—दासानु-<BR>दास (˚स-अन्˚), अस्, m. a slave of a slave, a servant<BR>of servants; (sometimes applied by a humble speaker<BR>to himself.)<BR>—दासी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A.<BR>—करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to make any one a slave or a female slave;<BR>to enslave.<BR>—दासी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made a slave.<BR>—दासी-त्व, अम्, n. the state of a female slave.<BR>—दासी-दान-विधि, इस्, m. ‘the rules for giving<BR>female slaves,’ N. of the 146th chapter of the<BR>Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa or second part of the Bha-<BR>viṣya-Purāṇa.<BR>—दासी-दास, अम्, n. female slaves<BR>and slaves, female servants and servants.<BR>—दासी-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘the son of a female slave’ (used as<BR>an abusive expression), = a low wretch, a miscreant.<BR>—दासी-माणवक, अम्, n. female slaves and boys.<BR>—दासी-श्रोत्रिय, अस्, m. a Brāhman (conversant<BR>with the Vedas) who goes after a female slave.<BR>—दा-<BR>सी-सभ, अम्, n. an assembly of female slaves or<BR>servants.<BR>—दासी-सुत, अस्, m. the son of a female<BR>slave.<BR>—दास्याः-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a female<BR>slave; (ई), f. the daughter of a female slave; [cf.<BR>दासी-पुत्र.]<BR>—दास्याः-सदृशी, f. behaving like a<BR>female slave.<BR>—दास्याः-सुत, अस्, m. = दासी-सुत, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासक
दासक, अस्, m., N. of a man; of a son of Bha-<BR>jamāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासकायन
दासकायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Dāsaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासनु
दासनु, उस्, m., Ved., N. of a semi-divine being<BR>associated with Kṛśānu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासाय
दासाय, Nom. P. A. दासायति, -ते, &c., to be-<BR>come a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासायन
दासायन, अस्, m. the son of a slave or of a man<BR>called Dāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासिका
दासिका, f. a female slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासी
दासी, f. See under 1. दास, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीक
दासीक for दासी, at the end of comp. (e. g. त्रिं-<BR>शद्-दासीक, having thirty female slaves).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेय|दासेयः
1. दासेय, अस्, m. (fr. दासी), the son of a female<BR>slave, a slave, servant, = दाशेय, q. v.; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>born of a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेर|दासेरः
दासेर, अस्, m. (fr. दासी), the son of a female<BR>slave, a slave, servant, = दाशेर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेरक|दासेरकः
दासेरक, अस्, m. = दासेर; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people to the north of Madhya-deśa, = दशे-<BR>रक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्य|दास्यं
दास्य, अम्, n. servitude, slavery, service.<BR>—दास्य-<BR>योग, अस्, m. servitude, slavery.<BR>—दास्य-वृत्ति, इस्,<BR>f. the business of a slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्वत्|दास्वन्त्
दास्वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. disposed to give, giv-<BR>ing, liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास 2. दास, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. दंस्,<BR>q. v.), a knowing man; a knower of the universal<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास 3. दास, अस्, m. = दाश, a fisherman, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासनीय
दासनीय दासनीय for दासमीय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासपूर|दासपूरं
दासपूर दासपूर, अम्, n. = दाशपूर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासमीय
दासमीय दासमीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; [cf. दासमेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासमेय
दासमेय दासमेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people to the north of Madhya-deśa; (also written<BR>दाशमेय; cf. दासमीय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाससरस्
दाससरस् दाससरस्, अस्, n., N. of a Sāman;<BR>(also read दाशशिरस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासित
दासित दासित. See under rt. दस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह|दाहः
दाह दाह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. दह्), burning,<BR>combustion, conflagration; glowing redness (as of<BR>the sky; cf. दिग्-दाह); cauterizing, cautery (in<BR>surgery); the sensation of burning, internal heat; the<BR>heat of a fever, feverish or morbid heat [cf. अन्तर्-द्˚,<BR>गृह-द्˚, गेह-द्˚]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(a various reading for वैदेह, q. v.)<BR>—दाह-<BR>काष्ठ, अम्, n. a kind of Agallochum used as a<BR>perfume; [cf. दाहागुर.]<BR>—दाह-ज्वर, अस्, m.<BR>inflammatory fever.<BR>—दाह-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting in burning or heat.<BR>—दाहमय-त्व, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">Page0412-a+ 74</a>]<BR>n. the state of consisting in burning, &c.<BR>—दाह-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, burning, heated, on fire.<BR>—दाह-<BR>सर, अस्, m. or दाह-सरस्, अस्, n. or दाह-स्थल,<BR>अम्, n. a place where dead bodies are burnt.<BR>—दाह-<BR>हरण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, removing heat; (अम्), n.<BR>the root of Andropogon Muricatus, (a fragrant grass,<BR>the root of which when woven into screens and kept<BR>wet tempers the hot winds, = वीरण-मूल.)<BR>—दा-<BR>हागुरु (˚ह-अग्˚), उ, n. = दाह-काष्ठ, q. v.<BR>—दाहात्मक (˚ह-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, of an in-<BR>flammable nature, easily kindled or burning, com-<BR>bustible.<BR>—दाहाधिकार (˚ह-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a chapter of a medical work by Vṛnda on cauter-<BR>izing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0411-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहक|दाहकः
दाहक, अस्, इका, अम्, burning, kindling, setting<BR>on fire; causing heat or combustion; incendiary,<BR>inflammatory; cauterizing, caustic; (अस्), m. the<BR>plant Plumbago Zeylanica (= चित्रक = रक्त-चि-<BR>त्रक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहन|दाहनं
दाहन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), causing to burn,<BR>burning, inflaming, reducing to ashes; cauterizing.<BR>—दाहनागुरु for दहनागुरु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहनीय
दाहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be burnt, combustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहिन्
दाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, burning, setting on fire, burning<BR>hot; tormenting, paining; [cf. गेहे-द्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहुक
दाहुक, अस्, आ, अम्, burning, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह्य
दाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be burnt, inflammable,<BR>combustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिकम्
दिकम् दिकम्, ind. given by some as an<BR>indeclinable under the Gaṇa चादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्क|दिक्कः
दिक्क दिक्क, अस्, m. = करभ, a young<BR>elephant ?; (also read धिक्क and विक्क.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

