दित दित. See under rt. 3. दा at p. 408,<BR>col. 2, and 4. दा at p. 408, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिति|दितिः
दिति दिति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 3. दा or दो), cut-<BR>ting, splitting, dividing; distributing, liberality, (in<BR>this sense also fr. rt. 1. दा); Liberality personified;<BR>(इस्), f., N. of a divine female, (probably a N. formed<BR>to answer to A-diti, as Sura to A-sura, and without<BR>any distinct character: in epic poetry Diti is a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa; the race<BR>of Daityas or implacable enemies of the gods are<BR>described as her progeny or derived from her through<BR>her son Hiraṇya-kaśipu; but the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa I.<BR>21, describes Indra as dividing the embryo in the<BR>womb of Diti, through fear of his future enemies,<BR>and forming the forty-nine Maruts from the divided<BR>pieces); (इस्), m., N. of a king; a king.<BR>—दिति-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘a son of Diti,’ a Daitya, an enemy of the<BR>gods.<BR>—दितिजाराति (˚ज-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘the enemy of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">Page0412-b+ 72</a>]<BR>the Daityas,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—दिति-तनय<BR>or दिति-नन्दन or दिति-सुत, अस्, m. ‘a son of<BR>Diti,’ a Daitya.<BR>—दिति-रूप-राक्षसी-वध, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the twenty-first chapter of the Krīḍā-<BR>khaṇḍa or second part of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—दिति-<BR>शोक-प्रशम, अस्, m., N. of the sixth chapter of<BR>the Bhūmi-khaṇḍa or second part of the Padma-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—दिति-सम्बोधन, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>ninth chapter of the Bhūmi-khaṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्य|दित्यः
दित्य, अस्, m. ‘a son of Diti,’ a Daitya; (a wrong<BR>form for दैत्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्यवह्
दित्यवह् दित्य-वह् or दित्य-वाह्, -वाट्, m.<BR>(inst. दित्यौहा), दित्यौही, f. (दित्य probably a<BR>corruption of द्वितीय), Ved. a two-year-old steer or<BR>cow; [cf. तुर्य-वह् and दात्यौह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्यौही
दित्यौही. See above under दित्य-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सा
दित्सा दित्सा, f. (fr. the Desid. of rt. 1. दा),<BR>desire or intention of giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सु
दित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, ready or wishing to give, willing<BR>to grant (with acc.); ready to perform (e. g. श्राद्-<BR>धम्, the funeral ceremony; cf. अ-दित्सु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्स्य
दित्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, what one is willing to give or<BR>ready to grant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदित्सु
दिदित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, = दित्सु, ready or wishing to<BR>give away; (an irregular form with double redupli-<BR>cation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदम्भिषु
दिदम्भिषु दिदम्भिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the<BR>Desid. of rt. दम्भ्), intending or wishing to de-<BR>ceive; [cf. धिप्सु and दिप्सु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदिवि
दिदिवि दिदिवि, इस्, इ, m. n. heaven, the sky.<BR>See दीदिवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदीवि
दिदीवि दिदीवि, इस्, m. boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षमाण
दिदृक्षमाण दिदृक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>the Desid. of rt. 1. दृश्), wishing to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षा
दिदृक्षा, f. desire of seeing, wish to see.<BR>—दि-<BR>दृक्षा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a desire to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षु
दिदृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of seeing (with<BR>acc.); wishing or desiring to examine, desirous of<BR>inspecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षेण्य
दिदृक्षेण्य or दिदृक्षेय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>what one likes or wishes to see, conspicuous, at-<BR>tracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदेविषत्
दिदेविषत् दिदेविषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the<BR>Desid. of rt. 2. दिव्), wishing to play or sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्दा
दिद्दा दिद्दा, f., N. of a princess of Kaś-<BR>mīra.<BR>—दिद्दा-क्षेम, अस्, m. ‘having affection for<BR>Diddā,’ an epithet of Kṣema-gupta.<BR>—दिद्दा-पाल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—दिद्दा-पुर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a town built by Diddā.<BR>—दिद्दा-स्वामिन्, ई, m.,<BR>N. of a temple built by Diddā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्यु|दिद्युः
दिद्यु दिद्यु, उस्, m. (fr. 2. दिव् or 2. दी or<BR>1. द्यु ?), Ved. a missile weapon, arrow; (Sāy.) a<BR>shining weapon; the sky, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्युत्
दिद्युत्, त्, f., Ved. an arrow, a missile (especially<BR>the missiles of the gods and the thunderbolt of Indra);<BR>N. of an Apsaras; (त्, त्, त्), shining, blazing, bright,<BR>(in this last sense derived by some fr. rt. 3. द्युत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्योतिषु
दिद्योतिषु दिद्योतिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the<BR>Desid. of rt. 3. द्युत्), wishing to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्ष्
दिधक्ष् दिधक्ष्, क्, क्, क् (fr. the Desid. of<BR>rt. 1. दह्), wishing or intending to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षमाण
दिधक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षयत्
दिधक्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desiring to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षा
दिधक्षा, f. desire or wish to burn or consume<BR>by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षु
दिधक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, intending to burn or<BR>destroy, desirous of burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधि|दिधिः
दिधि दिधि, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 1. धा), firmness,<BR>stability, fixed state of mind or being; (probably a<BR>wrong form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिक्ष्
दिधिक्ष् दिधिक्ष्, क्, क्, क् (fr. the Desid. of<BR>rt. 1. दिह्), intending to smear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषाय्य|दिधिषाय्यः
दिधिषाय्य दिधिषाय्य, अस्, m. (fr. the<BR>Desid. of rt. 1. धा), ‘to be tried to be gained,’ an<BR>epithet of Agni; (Sāy.) a supporter; (अस्), m. a<BR>pretended friend (?); [cf. दधिषाय्य, which is<BR>by some considered as another reading.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषु|दिधिषुः
दिधिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. wishing or trying to<BR>gain or obtain; (उस्), m. a suitor; a husband; the<BR>second husband of a woman twice married; (उस् or<BR>दिधिषू, ऊस्), f. a virgin widow remarried; an<BR>elder sister unmarried having a younger married<BR>sister; [cf. अग्रे-द्˚ and एदिधिषुः-पति.]<BR>—दि-<BR>धिषू-पति, इस्, m. the husband of a woman re-<BR>married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधीषू
दिधीषू, f. = दिधिषू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन|दिनं|दिनः
दिन 1. दिन. See rt. 3. दा, p. 408, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन|दिनं|दिनः
दिन 2. दिन, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably for<BR>दिवन and related to 3. दिव् fr. rt. 2. दिव्, said to<BR>be fr. rt. दो), a day; [cf. दुर्-द्˚, पुरु-द्˚, मध्-<BR>यन्-द्˚, सु-द्˚; cf. also Lith. die†na, f. ‘a day;’<BR>Slav. deny, ‘a day;’ Lat. peren-dinus, peren-dina-<BR>tio, peren = para; perhaps Goth. sin-teins, ‘daily,’<BR>sin = sam.]<BR>—दिन-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, making day<BR>or light; (ई), f., scil. टीका, N. of a commentary on<BR>the Bhāṣā-pariccheda; (अस्), m. the sun; N. of<BR>the author of the work Candrārkī.<BR>—दिनकर-<BR>तनय, अस्, m. ‘the son of the Sun,’ the planet<BR>Saturn.<BR>—दिनकर-देव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—दिनकरात्मजा (˚र-आत्˚), f. ‘the daughter of<BR>the Sun,’ an epithet of the Yamunā or Jumnā river.<BR>—दिन-कर्तृ, ता, m. or दिन-कृत्, त्, m. ‘the<BR>day-maker,’ the sun.<BR>—दिन-केशर or दिन-केसर<BR>or दिन-केशव, अस्, m. ‘the hair of the day,’ the<BR>darkness.<BR>—दिन-क्षय, अस्, m. ‘the decline of<BR>day,’ the evening, = तिथि-क्षय; N. of a chapter<BR>in the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—दिन-ज्योतिस्, इस्, n. ‘day-<BR>light,’ sunshine.<BR>—दिन-दुःखित, अस्, आ, अम्, af-<BR>flicted by day, sorrowing by day; (अस्), m. the bird<BR>Cakra-vāka, the ruddy goose.<BR>—दिन-नक्त, अम्,<BR>n. day and night.<BR>—दिन-पति, इस्, m. ‘the lord of<BR>the day,’ the sun.<BR>—दिन-प्रणी, ईस्, m. ‘the bringer<BR>of day,’ the sun; [cf. तिथि-प्रणी.]<BR>—दिन-बन्-<BR>धु, उस्, m. ‘the friend of the day,’ the sun.<BR>—दिन-<BR>बल, अस्, m. ‘the strength of the day,’ N. of the<BR>fifth, sixth, seventh, eighth, eleventh, and twelfth<BR>signs of the zodiac collectively.<BR>—दिन-मणि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘the jewel of day,’ the sun.<BR>—दिन-मल, अम्, n.<BR>‘day-refuse (?),’ a month.<BR>—दिन-मूर्धन्, आ, m.<BR>‘the head of the day,’ the eastern mountain behind<BR>which the sun is supposed to rise; [cf. उदय.]<BR>—दिन-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘the jewel of the day,’ the<BR>sun.<BR>—दिन-राशि, इस्, m. ‘the sum or collective<BR>amount of days,’ i. e. the number of solar days<BR>which have elapsed from one given point of time to<BR>another.<BR>—दिन-व्यास-दल, अम्, n. ‘half-diameter<BR>or radius of the sky,’ i. e. the radius of a circle made<BR>by an asterism in its daily revolution.<BR>—दिनांश<BR>(˚न-अंश), अस्, m. ‘any portion of a day,’ i. e. a<BR>watch, an hour, morning, forenoon, afternoon, &c.<BR>—दिनागम (˚न-आग्˚), अस्, m. day-break.<BR>—दि-<BR>नाण्ड (˚न-अण्ड?), अम्, n. ‘day-egg,’ i. e. dark-<BR>ness, (the egg or embryo whence day proceeds.)<BR>—दिनात्यय (˚न-अत्˚), अस्, m. ‘the decline of<BR>day,’ evening.<BR>—दिनादि (˚न-आदि), इस्, m. ‘day-<BR>break,’ dawn.<BR>—दिनाधीश (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘the lord of day,’ the sun.<BR>—दिनान्त (˚न-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘end of day,’ sun-set, evening.<BR>—दिनान्तक<BR>(˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘day-destroyer,’ darkness.<BR>—दि-<BR>नारम्भ (˚न-आर्˚), अस्, m. ‘day-break,’ morning.<BR>—दिनार्ध (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘the half of the<BR>day,’ noon.<BR>—दिनावसान (˚न-अव्˚), अम्, n. ‘close<BR>of day,’ evening.<BR>—दिनास्त्र (˚न-अस्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘day-missile,’ N. of a magical formula.<BR>—दिनी-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to reduce<BR>to days.<BR>—दिनेश (˚न-ईश), अस्, m. ‘the lord of<BR>day,’ the sun; the regent of a day.<BR>—दिनेशात्मज<BR>(˚श-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘the son of the Sun,’ the planet<BR>Mercury.<BR>—दिनेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘the lord<BR>of the day,’ the sun.<BR>—दिनैक (˚न-एक), अस्, m.<BR>one day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0412-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनिका
दिनिका, f. a day's wages, hire for a day or by<BR>the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन्नाग्राम
दिन्नाग्राम दिन्ना-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>village of the Khāśakas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन्व्
दिन्व् दिन्व्, cl. 1. P. दिन्वति, &c., to be<BR>glad, to gladden; to please, to be pleased;<BR>[cf. धिन्व् and जिन्व्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिप्
दिप् दिप्, cl. 1. A. देपते, &c., to drop;<BR>(various reading for तिप्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिप्सु
दिप्सु दिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid. of rt.<BR>दभ्), Ved. intending to hurt or injure; [cf. धिप्सु<BR>and दिदम्भिषु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिम्प्|दिंप्
दिम्प् दिम्प्, cl. 10. A. दिम्पयते, &c.,<BR>to accumulate, order, direct; [cf. डिप्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिम्भ्
दिम्भ् दिम्भ्, cl. 10. A. दिम्भयते, &c.,<BR>to accumulate; P. दिम्भयति, &c., to<BR>order, command, direct; to incite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिय
दिय दिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be given,<BR>deserving of a gift, (according to Durga on Nirukta<BR>III. 15 = देय or दानार्ह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0413-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिर्
