द्विषा
द्विषा द्विषा, f. cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0445-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्ट|द्विष्टं
द्विष्ट 2. द्विष्ट, अम्, n. (for द्व्य्-अष्ट),<BR>copper. (For 1. द्विष्ट see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0445-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीप|द्वीपं|द्वीपः
द्वीप द्वीप, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. द्वि + अप्,<BR>water), an island, peninsula, any land surrounded by<BR>water, a sandbank; a place of refuge, shelter, protec-<BR>tion, a protector; a division of the terrestrial world<BR>(of which according to different authorities there are<BR>seven or four or nine or thirteen and which are<BR>situated round the mountain Meru like the leaves<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">Page0446-a+ 76</a>]<BR>encircling a lotus flower; each Dvīpa is separated from<BR>the next by a distinct circumambient ocean: the seven<BR>Dvīpas, reckoning from the central one, are Jambu,<BR>Plaksha or Go-medaka, Śālmalī, Kuśa, Krauñca,<BR>Śāka, and Puṣkara: according to Mahā-bhārata,<BR>Bhīṣma-parva 208, there are four Dvīpas, viz.<BR>Bhadrāśva, Ketu-māla, Jambu-dvīpa, and Uttarāḥ<BR>kuravas. In Viṣṇu-Purāṇa II. 3. nine Dvīpas are<BR>enumerated, which are sometimes joined with the<BR>above-named four, so as to make thirteen in all);<BR>a tiger's skin?; (according to some) cubebs; [cf.<BR>द्वीप-सम्भव.]<BR>—द्वीप-कर्पूरक or द्वीप-<BR>कर्पूरज (?), अस्, m. camphor from China.<BR>—द्वी-<BR>प-कुमार, आस्, m. pl. (with Jainas) N. of a class<BR>of deities belonging to the Bhavana-patis.<BR>—द्वीप-<BR>खर्जूर or द्वीप-ज, अम्, n. a kind of fruit tree,<BR>= महा-पारेवत.<BR>—द्वीप-छन्दिर, N. of a place<BR>mentioned in the Tarka-bhāṣā-prakāśikā by Cinna-<BR>bhaṭṭa.<BR>—द्वीप-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in<BR>islands; (आन्), m. the ocean; a river; (ती), f. a river;<BR>the earth.<BR>—द्वीप-शत्रु, उस्, m. Asparagus Race-<BR>mosus (= शतावरी; cf. the right form द्वीपि-शत्रु<BR>and द्वीपिका).<BR>—द्वीप-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>best of islands.<BR>—द्वीप-सम्भव, अस्, m. the<BR>largest sort of raisin [cf. द्वीप्य]; Vernonia Anthel-<BR>minthica; (आ), f. a kind of date.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0445-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपिका
द्वीपिका, f. Asparagus Racemosus; [cf. द्वीप-<BR>शत्रु and द्वीप्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपिन्
द्वीपिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having islands; having spots<BR>like islands; (ई), m. a tiger, an ounce or panther,<BR>leopard; (इनी), f. a kind of plant, = वट-पत्त्री.<BR>—द्वीपि-कर्णि, इस्, m. ‘having the ear of a tiger,’<BR>N. of a king; [cf. मन्द-कर्णि.]<BR>—द्वीपि-नख,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of perfume; [cf. व्याघ्र-नख and<BR>व्याल-नख.]<BR>—द्वीपि-शत्रु, उस्, m. the plant<BR>Asparagus Racemosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीप्य|द्वीप्यः
द्वीप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, living on an island, an islander;<BR>(अस्), m. the largest sort of raisin, cubebs; a sort of<BR>crow; N. of Vyāsa [cf. द्वैपायन]; (आ), f. Aspa-<BR>ragus Racemosus; [cf. द्वीपिका and द्वीपि-शत्रु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वृ
द्वृ द्वृ, cl. 1. P. द्वरति, &c., to obstruct;<BR>to cover; to disregard; to appropriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेधा
द्वेधा द्वे-धा. See p. 445, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष|द्वेषः
द्वेष द्वेष. See p. 445, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेसत
द्वेसत द्वेसत, अस्, आ, अम्, having the same<BR>length above and below the navel; (also read द्व-<BR>यसत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगत
द्वैगत द्वैगत, अम्, n. (fr. द्वि-गत्), Ved.,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगुणिक|द्वैगुणिकः
द्वैगुणिक द्वैगुणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वि-<BR>गुण), one who requires the double or cent per cent<BR>interest; (अस्), m. an usurer, money-lender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगुण्य|द्वैगुण्यं
द्वैगुण्य, अम्, n. the double, double amount,<BR>double value or measure, double the amount; duality;<BR>doubling; the possession of two out of the three<BR>qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैजात
द्वैजात द्वैजात, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वि-जाति), be-<BR>longing to the twice-born, consisting of twice-born<BR>men, belonging to one of the three higher classes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैत|द्वैतं
द्वैत द्वैत, अम्, n. (fr. 1. द्वि-ता), duality,<BR>the state of being doubled, duplicity, dualism in philo-<BR>sophy, the assertion of two principles (as of spirit<BR>and matter, God and the universe, &c.); doubt.<BR>—द्वैत-निर्णय, अस्, m. ‘the decision or discus-<BR>sion of duality,’ N. of a philosophical work by Vācas-<BR>pati-miśra.<BR>—द्वैत-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n. ‘the re-<BR>mainder of discussions on duality,’ N. of a work by<BR>Keśava.<BR>—द्वैत-भृत, आस्, m. pl., N. of a philo-<BR>sophical school.<BR>—द्वैत-वादिन्, ई, m. ‘an assertor<BR>of dualism,’ a philosopher who asserts the two prin-<BR>ciples or the existence of the soul as separate from<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR>—द्वैत-विवेक, अस्, m. ‘dis-<BR>crimination of duality,’ N. of a part of the Pañca-<BR>daśī by Bhāratī-tīrtha.<BR>—द्वैत-वैतथ्योपनिषद्<BR>(˚य-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतवन
द्वैतवन, अस्, m. (fr. द्वित-वन), Ved. a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">Page0446-b+ 73</a>]<BR>patronymic of the king Dhvasan; (अस्, ई, अम्), be-<BR>longing or relating to Dhvasan Dvaitavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतीयक
द्वैतीयक, अस्, ई, अम्, returning every second<BR>day, second; [cf. द्वितीयक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध|द्वैधं
द्वैध द्वैध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वि-धा), two-<BR>fold, double; (अम्), n. duality, duplicity, double exist-<BR>ence or nature, twofold form or state, a double re-<BR>source, secondary array or reserve; division or sepa-<BR>ration into two parts; disunion, diversity, difference,<BR>variance, contest, conflict, a duel; doubt, uncertainty;<BR>a dilemma; contradiction, dispute; (अम्), ind. in<BR>two parts, into two portions; in two ways, doubly.<BR>—द्वैधा-करण, अम्, n. making into two, sepa-<BR>rating into two parts, disuniting.<BR>—द्वैधी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, separated, made twofold, divided into<BR>two, sundered; brought into a dilemma.<BR>—द्वैधी-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. twofold form or state, a double state,<BR>duality, duplicity, double nature, the nature or pro-<BR>perty of being two or distinct; separation into two,<BR>difference; contest, dispute, doubt, dilemma, uncer-<BR>tainty; sowing dissension or causing the separation<BR>of allies, dividing an army into two detachments,<BR>making peace with one and waging war with another<BR>(one of the six kinds of military tactics); falsehood.<BR>—द्वैधी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become separated or divided into two parts, to be<BR>disunited.<BR>—द्वैधी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, separated<BR>into two, divided, disunited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध्य|द्वैध्यं
द्वैध्य, अम्, n. ‘the state of being twofold,’<BR>double nature, duplicity; diversity, variance, discre-<BR>pancy; falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप|द्वैपः
द्वैप द्वैप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वीप), being or<BR>living on an island, an islander; occurring on an<BR>island; (fr. द्वीपिन्), belonging to a tiger or panther,<BR>made of a tiger's skin, covered with it; (अस्), m. a<BR>car covered or hung with a tiger's skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपक
द्वैपक, अस्, ई, अम्, living on an island, an<BR>islander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपायन|द्वैपायनः
द्वैपायन, अस्, m. (fr. द्वीप), ‘the island-<BR>born,’ N. of Vyāsa, author or compiler of the Vedas<BR>and Purāṇas, (the place of his nativity being a small<BR>island in the Ganges); (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to<BR>Dvaipāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप्य|द्वैप्यं
द्वैप्य, अस्, आ or -पी, अम् (fr. द्वीप), of or<BR>relating to an island or peninsula, the inhabitant of<BR>an island or of the coast, an islander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपक्ष|द्वैपक्षं
द्वैपक्ष द्वैपक्ष, अम्, n. (fr. द्वि-पक्ष),<BR>two factions or parties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपद
द्वैपद द्वैपद, अस्, m. (fr. द्वि-पद), a<BR>combination or compound of two words.<BR>—द्वै-<BR>पद-शस्, ind. in a compound or combination of<BR>two words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपदिक
द्वैपदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वि-पदा), familiar<BR>with the Dvi-padā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपराक
