द्वैवर्षिक
द्वैवर्षिक द्वैवर्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वि-<BR>वर्ष), biennial, happening after two years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैविध्य|द्वैविध्यं
द्वैविध्य द्वैविध्य, अम्, n. (fr. द्वि-विध),<BR>the state of being twofold, duality, twofold manner<BR>or character, duplicity, diversity, variance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैशाण
द्वैशाण द्वैशाण, अस्, ई, अम्, worth two<BR>Śāṇas; [cf. द्वि-शाण and द्विशाण्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैषणीया
द्वैषणीया द्वैषणीया, f. (fr. द्वेषणीय), a<BR>sort of betel pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैसमिक
द्वैसमिक द्वैसमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. द्वि-समा),<BR>two years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैहायन|द्वैहायनं
द्वैहायन द्वैहायन, अम्, n. (fr. द्वि-हा-<BR>यन), the age of two years, the state of being two<BR>years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यंश
द्व्यंश द्व्य्-अंश, for this and other comps.<BR>beginning with द्व्य् see under द्वि, p. 445, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध 1. ध, the nineteenth consonant of the<BR>alphabet and the fourth of the fourth or dental class,<BR>being the aspirate of द् and pronounced like dh in<BR>madhouse.<BR>—ध-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध 2. ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. धा), placing,<BR>putting; holding, containing, possessing, having; caus-<BR>ing, &c.; (अस्), m. an epithet of Brahmā; epithet<BR>of Kuvera; virtue, moral merit; (आ), f., N. of the<BR>residence of Kṛṣṇa; (अम्), n. wealth, property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्
धक् 1. धक्, ind. (probably fr. rt. 1. दह्),<BR>an exclamation of wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्
धक् 2. धक्, see उश-धक्; cf. 2. दह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धकित्
धकित् धकित्, ind. = धिक्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्क्
धक्क् धक्क्, cl. 10. P. धक्कयति, &c.,<BR>to destroy or annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धट|धटः
धट धट, अस्, m. (probably a Prākṛt form<BR>of धर्तृ, derived from the nom. sing. धर्ता and<BR>rt. धृ, like भट्, भाट, भाटक, भाटि fr. rt.<BR>भृ; cf. तुला-धट and तुलया धृ under तुला),<BR>a balance, the scale of a balance, a pair of scales;<BR>the sign of the zodiac Libra; ordeal by the balance;<BR>(ई), f. old cloth or raiment; a piece of cloth worn<BR>over the privities.<BR>—धटी-दान, अम्, n. giving old<BR>cloth to a woman after impregnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटक|धटकः
धटक धटक, अस्, m. a kind of weight<BR>equal to 14 Vallas or 42 Raktikās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिन्
धटिन् धटिन्, ई, m. an epithet of Śiva,<BR>(perhaps a wrong reading for घटिन्; cf. घण्ट,<BR>घण्टिन्, घटिघट); (इनी), f. a cotton cloth or<BR>string fastened round the loins; [cf. धटी under<BR>धट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटोत्कच
धटोत्कच धटोत्कच, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(probably for घटोत्कच.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धडि
धडि धडि, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धण्
धण् धण्, cl. 1. P. धणति, &c., to<BR>sound; [cf. rt. 1. धन्, ध्वण्, 2. ध्वन्,<BR>ध्रण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0446-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धत्तूर|धत्तूरः
धत्तूर धत्तूर, अस्, m. or धत्तूरक, अस्,<BR>आ, m. f. the white thorn-apple, Datura Alba; [cf.<BR>धुस्तूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्
धन् 1. धन्, cl. 1. P. धनति, &c., to<BR>sound; [cf. rt. 2. ध्वन् and धण्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्
धन् 2. धन् (related to rt. धन्व्), cl.<BR>3. P. दधन्ति, &c., Ved. to cause to<BR>move or run, to put in motion; to bear fruit,<BR>produce crops of grain, &c.: Caus. P. A. धन-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, to cause to move or run, to put in<BR>motion; to move, run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन|धनं
धन, अम्, n. (connected with 2. धन्, but said to<BR>be fr. rt. 1. धा), the reward given to a victor in a com-<BR>bat, spoil taken from an enemy, booty, prey; a gift;<BR>the prize or thing won in a game, (धनम् भृ, to<BR>carry off the prize, to carry off booty); a contest or<BR>struggle for any prize, a match; anything valuable;<BR>property of any description, wealth, treasure, riches,<BR>money, gold, chattels, wealth in cattle or herds, abound-<BR>ing in anything, possessions in general [cf. स्त्री-<BR>ध्˚, धान्य-ध्˚, विद्या-ध्˚]; a valued object, an<BR>object of affection or endearment, capital (opposed<BR>to वृद्धि, interest); surplus, residue, the affirma-<BR>tive quantity or plus (in arithmetic, opposed to<BR>ऋण, क्षय, व्यय, हानि); (in astrology) N. of<BR>the second mansion; [cf. probably Gr. εὐ-θενής.]<BR>—धन-काम or धन-काम्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>desirous of money, avaricious, covetous.<BR>—धन-<BR>केलि, इस्, इस्, इ, sporting with riches or treasures; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—धन-क्रीती (according<BR>to some also धन-क्रीता), f. a woman bought with<BR>money.<BR>—धन-क्षय, अस्, m. loss of money or<BR>property; ‘one who has lost his money,’ N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—धन-गर्व, अस्, m. ‘one who has pride<BR>in riches, purse-proud,’ N. of a man.<BR>—धन-गर्-<BR>वित, अस्, आ, अम्, proud of riches, purse-proud.<BR>—धन-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for गुप्त-धन),<BR>one who guards his property carefully; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a merchant's son.<BR>—धनगुप्त-ता, f. careful<BR>guarding of property.<BR>—धन-च्छू, ऊस्, m. the<BR>numidian crane (said to = करेटव्या, but the name<BR>suggests an analogy to the Dhaneśa of the spoken<BR>dialects or the Indian Buceros).<BR>—धन-च्युत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, fallen from affluence, reduced to poverty,<BR>poor.<BR>—धन-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, arising from wealth,<BR>produced by wealth; (आनि), n. pl. all kinds of valu-<BR>able objects or possessions.<BR>—धन-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>conquering booty, victorious in a fight; acquiring<BR>treasures; (त्), m., N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—धनञ्-<BR>जय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. conquering booty, victorious<BR>in battle; wealth-acquiring; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Soma; a N. of fire; a particular vital air which is<BR>supposed to nourish the body; the plant Plumbago<BR>Zeylanica; N. of a Brāhman; an epithet of Arjuna,<BR>third son of Pāṇḍu; the plant Terminalia Arjuna;<BR>N. of a serpent-demon; of a Vyāsa; of a king of<BR>Kaliṅga; of a king of Kausthala-pura; of a merchant;<BR>of a lexicographer; of the author of the Dharma-<BR>pradīpa; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of the Brāhman<BR>Dhanañ-jaya.<BR>—धनञ्जय-निघण्टु, उस्, m. ‘the<BR>vocabulary of Dhanañ-jaya,’ N. of a dictionary men-<BR>tioned in the commentary Prauḍha-manoramā by<BR>Bhaṭṭojī-dīkṣita.<BR>—धनञ्जय-विजय, अस्, m.<BR>‘the victory of Dhanañ-jaya (or Arjuna),’ N. of a<BR>drama.<BR>—धनञ्जय-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work mentioned in the Saṃskāra-tattva by Raghu-<BR>nandana.<BR>—धन-तम, अम्, n., scil. दायम्, an<BR>exceedingly rich donation.<BR>—धन-तृष्णा, f.<BR>thirst for riches, covetousness.<BR>—धन-त्यज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>resigning wealth.<BR>—धन-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving<BR>money or property, granting wealth, munificent, wealth-<BR>yielding, liberal, tributary; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Kuvera, god of riches; N. of a Guhyaka or a being<BR>attending on Kuvera; N. of a mountain; the plant<BR>Barringtonia Acutangula (= हिज्जल); (आ), f., N. of<BR>one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; of a Tantra<BR>deity; [cf. धन-दा.]<BR>—धन-दण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>fine, amercement.<BR>—धनद-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha mentioned in the Revā-māhātmya.<BR>—ध-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-b" target="_blank">Page0447-b+ 81</a>]<BR>न-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘wealth-given,’ N. of several<BR>persons.<BR>—धनद-देव, अस्, m. = धन-देव,<BR>N. of a poet.<BR>—धन-दर्प, अस्, m. pride of<BR>wealth.<BR>—धनद-स्तोत्र, अम्, n. ‘praise of the<BR>liberal,’ N. of a small work.<BR>—धन-दा, आस्, आस्,<BR>अम्, Ved. giving rewards, granting spoil; granting<BR>riches or treasures; [cf. धन-द.]<BR>—धनदाक्षी<BR>(˚द-अक्षि), f. a kind of tree, = कुवेराक्षी, लता-<BR>करञ्ज.<BR>—धनदानुज (˚द-अन्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>younger brother of Kuvera, an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR>—धनदा-पूजा-यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a mystical<BR>diagram given in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—धनदा-मन्-<BR>त्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of a particular prayer mentioned<BR>in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—धन-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, grant-<BR>ing treasures; (ई), m. an epithet of Agni.<BR>—ध-<BR>नदावास (˚द-आव्˚), अस्, m. the residence of Kuvera,<BR>epithet of the mountain Kailāsa.<BR>—धन-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man, = धनद-देव, N. of a poet.<BR>—धनदेश्वर (˚द-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of wealth-<BR>givers,’ an epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—धनदेश्वर-तीर्-<BR>थ, अम्, n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—धन-<BR>धानी, f. a receptacle for valuable articles, a treasury,<BR>storehouse.<BR>—धन-धान्य, अम्, n., N. of a spell<BR>for restraining certain magical weapons.<BR>—धनधा-<BR>न्याधिक (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, rich in money and<BR>grain.<BR>—धनन्-ददा, f. ‘granting treasures,’ one<BR>of the Śaktis or female personifications of divine<BR>power peculiar to the Buddhas.<BR>—धन-पति, इस्,<BR>m. ‘the lord of riches or treasures,’ epithet of Indra,<BR>and especially of Kuvera.<BR>—धन-पाल, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a guardian of treasure, a treasurer; N. of a<BR>merchant; of a poet; of a lexicographer.<BR>—धन-<BR>पिशाचिका or धन-पिशाची, f. avarice, thirst for<BR>wealth.<BR>—धन-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of wealth;<BR>(आ), f. the plant Ardisia Solanacea (= काक-जम्बू).<BR>—धन-भक्ष, अस्, m., Ved. enjoying a reward,<BR>enjoyment of booty or wealth; (Sāy.) desirous of<BR>distributing wealth or possessing wealth (in cattle &c.).<BR>—धन-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, proud, inflated with<BR>the pride of wealth, purse-proud; (अस्), m. pride or<BR>intoxication of wealth.<BR>—धन-मित्र, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing wealth as a friend,’ N. of a merchant.<BR>—धन-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. principal, capital; (अस्, आ, अम्), pro-<BR>ceeding from wealth, founded on wealth.<BR>—धन-<BR>मोहन, अस्, m., N. of a merchant's son.<BR>—धनर्च<BR>(˚न-ऋच?), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. perhaps incorrectly for<BR>धनर्ज (˚न-ऋज), striving after a reward (?).<BR>—धनर्ण (˚न-ऋण), अम्, n. positive and<BR>negative quantities (in mathematics).<BR>—धन-लुब्-<BR>ध, अस्, आ, अम्, or धन-लोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘greedy<BR>of wealth,’ avaricious, covetous, miserly, mercenary.<BR>—धन-लोभ, अस्, m. ‘desire of wealth,’ covet-<BR>ousness, avarice.<BR>—धन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, wealthy,<BR>opulent, rich; (अती), f. the constellation Dhaniṣṭhā;<BR>N. of a merchant's daughter; [cf. probably Lat.<BR>dives.]<BR>—धन-विभाग, अस्, m. distribution of<BR>property.<BR>—धन-वृद्धि, इस्, f. increase of pro-<BR>perty.<BR>—धन-व्यय, अस्, m. ‘the spending of<BR>money,’ expenditure, extravagance.<BR>—धन-सञ्-<BR>चय, अस्, m. collection of riches.<BR>—धनसञ्चयिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, rich; one who has amassed wealth; (ई),<BR>m. a rich man.<BR>—धन-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. grant-<BR>ing a reward, giving riches.<BR>—धन-सम्पत्ति, इस्,<BR>f. accumulation of wealth.<BR>—धन-सा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. granting a reward, distributing gifts or treasures;<BR>acquiring or conquering booty.<BR>—धन-साति, इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. acquisition of wealth or treasure.<BR>—धन-सू,<BR>ऊस्, m. ‘producing wealth,’ the fork-tailed shrike.<BR>—धन-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘living in wealth,’<BR>rich, wealthy.<BR>—धन-स्थान, अम्, n. a recepta-<BR>cle for riches, a treasury.<BR>—धनस्थानाधिकारिन्<BR>(˚न-अध्˚), ई, m. the superintendant of a treasury,<BR>a treasurer.<BR>—धन-स्पृत्, त्, m., Ved. carrying away<BR>or conquering booty; (Sāy.) gratifying with wealth;<BR>epithet of Agni; of Indra.<BR>—धन-हर, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, carrying off wealth, stealing property, a thief;<BR>receiving property, inheriting, an heir; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of perfume commonly called Chora.<BR>—धन-हरिन्<BR>or धन-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, stealing property, a thief;<BR>inheriting property, an heir.<BR>—धन-हीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deprived of wealth; reduced to poverty, poor.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">Page0447-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—धन-हृत्, त्, त्, त्, a stealer of property, a thief;<BR>(त्), m. f. n. (?), a kind of bulbous plant (= चण्डाल-<BR>कन्द).<BR>—धनागम (˚न-आग्˚), अस्, m. accession<BR>of wealth, gain.<BR>—धनाढ्य (˚न-आढ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, opulent, wealthy.<BR>—धनादान (˚न-आद्˚),<BR>अम्, n. acceptance of money.<BR>—धनाधन-नि-<BR>बन्धन (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, contingent on<BR>the possession or non-possession of wealth.<BR>—धना-<BR>धार (˚न-आध्˚), अस्, m. a treasury, storehouse.<BR>—धनाधिकार (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. title or right<BR>to property.<BR>—धनाधिकारिन् (˚न-अध्˚), ई, इणी,<BR>m. f. an heir, an heiress, one who has a right or title<BR>to property; (ई), m. a treasurer; a collector.<BR>—ध-<BR>नाधिकृत (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘any one placed<BR>over treasures,’ a treasurer.<BR>—धनाधिगोप्तृ (˚न-<BR>अध्˚), ता, m. ‘the guardian of treasure,’ an epithet<BR>of Kuvera.<BR>—धनाधिप, अस्, or धनाधिपति<BR>(˚न-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘the lord of treasure,’ an epithet of<BR>Kuvera; a treasurer.<BR>—धनाधिपत्य (˚न-अध्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the dominion or superintendance over<BR>treasure.<BR>—धनाध्यक्ष (˚न-अध्˚), अस्, m. an<BR>overseer of treasure, a treasurer; an epithet of<BR>Kuvera; of Śiva; [cf. कोषाध्यक्ष.]<BR>—ध-<BR>नान्ध (˚न-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blinded by riches.<BR>—धनापहार (˚न-अप्˚), अस्, m. ‘taking away<BR>of property,’ fine, amercement; plunder.<BR>—ध-<BR>नायुस् (˚न-आय्˚), उस्, m., N. of a son of Dṛḍhāyus.<BR>—धनार्घ (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. deserving<BR>a reward, worthy of wealth.<BR>—धनार्चित (˚न-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wealthy, opulent.<BR>—धनार्जन<BR>(˚न-अर्˚), अम्, n. acquisition of property or of wealth.<BR>—धनार्थिन् (˚न-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, desiring wealth,<BR>wealth-seeking, a seeker of riches, covetous, miserly.<BR>—धनाशा (˚न-आशा), f. longing after wealth, de-<BR>sire of riches.<BR>—धनेश (˚न-ईश), अस्, m. the lord<BR>of treasure, a rich man; an epithet of Kuvera; N.<BR>of the teacher of Vopa-deva.<BR>—धनेश्वर (˚न-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of treasure,’ an epithet of Kuvera;<BR>N. of a Brāhman; of a teacher of Vopa-deva; (ई),<BR>f. a female possessor of riches; the wife of Kuvera.<BR>—धनैश्वर्य (˚न-ऐश्˚), अम्, n. the dominion<BR>over treasure.<BR>—धनैषिन् (˚न-एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ,<BR>longing for riches, wishing or claiming property;<BR>(ई), m. a creditor who claims his money.<BR>—धनो-<BR>पचय (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, m. accumulation of wealth.<BR>—धनोष्मन् (˚न-उष्˚ or -ऊष्˚), आ, m. burning<BR>desire for wealth or treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनक|धनकः
धनक, अस्, m. avarice, covetousness, desire for<BR>riches; N. of a Yādava, son of Dur-dama or Dur-<BR>mada; of another man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाय
धनाय, Nom. P. धनायति, &c., to wish for<BR>wealth, long for riches, be desirous of anything<BR>(with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाया
धनाया, f. the desire of obtaining riches, covet-<BR>ousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिक|धनिकः
धनिक, अस्, आ, अम्, rich, wealthy, opulent;<BR>pious, virtuous, excellent; (अस्), m. a wealthy man;<BR>a money-lender, a creditor, owner; a husband;<BR>coriander; N. of a poet; (इका), f. a virtuous or<BR>excellent woman; a wife, young woman; a tree,<BR>see प्रियङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिन्
धनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing wealth or treasures,<BR>opulent, wealthy, rich, well off; (ई), m. a rich man;<BR>a creditor; the possessor of anything; N. of a<BR>messenger of the Kapas, Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p.<BR>7333.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिष्ठ
धनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, very rich; (superl. of<BR>2. धन्), Ved. very swift; (आ), f. the more modern<BR>N. of the Nakṣatra Śraviṣṭhā or twenty-third<BR>lunar mansion, (it comprises four stars, apparently<BR>α, β, γ, and δ Delphini, and is figured by a drum<BR>or tabor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीका
धनीका, f. = धनिका, f. a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीय
धनीय, Nom. P. धनीयति, &c., to wish for<BR>riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीयक|धनीयकं
धनीयक or धनेयक, अम्, n. coriander<BR>seed, = धन्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनू
1. धनू, ऊस्, m. a store of grain. (For 2. धनू<BR>see p. 448, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेयु
धनेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्य|धन्यः
धन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, bringing wealth, bestowing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">Page0448-a+ 79</a>]<BR>opulence (Ved.); opulent, wealthy, rich; fortunate,<BR>happy, blest, lucky, auspicious; good; virtuous;<BR>(अस्), m. a fortunate or virtuous man; an infidel,<BR>atheist; N. of a spell for using or restraining magi-<BR>cal weapons; N. of a man; (आ), f. a nurse; Emblic<BR>Myrobalan; coriander; (अम्), n. treasure, wealth;<BR>coriander.<BR>—धन्य-ता, f. or धन्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>good fortune, fortunate condition, good luck; opu-<BR>lence.<BR>—धन्यम्-मन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, considering<BR>one's self happy, thinking one's self fortunate.<BR>—धन्य-वाद, अस्, m. thanksgiving, thankful-<BR>ness, thanks, praise, applause.<BR>—धन्य-स्तोत्र, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the praise of the blessed,’ N. of a short philo-<BR>sophical poem ascribed to Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0447-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यक
धन्यक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्याक|धन्याकं
धन्याक, अम्, n. a plant bearing a small pun-<BR>gent seed used by the Hindūs as a condiment,<BR>Coriandrum Sativum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्यक|धनस्यकः
धनस्यक धनस्यक, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Asteracantha Longifolia (= गो-क्षुर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाश्री
धनाश्री धनाश्री, ईस् (?), f., N. of a Rāgiṇī;<BR>(according to Hanu-mat, the third wife of Śrī-rāga.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनु|धनुः
धनु धनु, उस्, m. or 2. धनू, ऊस्, f. (fr.<BR>धन् = rt. हन्, to kill, or according to some fr.<BR>rt. तन्, to stretch; the full form is धनुस् below),<BR>a bow; a measure of four Hastas or cubits; the<BR>sign of the zodiac Sagittarius; a kind of tree, =<BR>पियाल, Semecarpus Anacardium; (उस्), f. a dry<BR>sandbank, a sandy shore; [cf. धनुस्, धन्वन्;<BR>Gr. θίς; θινός.]<BR>—धनु-केतकी, f. a kind of flower.<BR>—धनु-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a tree.<BR>—धनु-<BR>राज, अस्, m., N. of one of the ancestors of Śākya-<BR>muni.<BR>—१. धन्व्-अन्तर, अम्, n. (for 2. see under<BR>धन्वन्, col. 2), an extent or distance of a Dhanu<BR>or four Hastas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष
धनुष, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्क
धनुष्क (at the end of an adj. comp.) =<BR>धनुस्, a bow [cf. स-ध्˚]; (अम्), n. a small bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुस्
धनुस्, उस्, m. n. (generally n.), a bow; a measure<BR>of length equal to four Hastas or = (1/2000) Gavyūti;<BR>(उस्), n. an arc or part of a circle; an arc or<BR>quadrant for obtaining by observation the altitude<BR>of the sun and the zenith-distance; the sign of<BR>the zodiac Sagittarius; a kind of tree, = पियाल; a<BR>desert, arid land; (उस्, उस्, उस्), armed with a bow;<BR>(उस्), m. a N. of Śiva.<BR>—धनुः-काण्ड, अम्, n. a<BR>bow and arrow.<BR>—धनुः-खण्ड, अम्, n. a portion<BR>of a bow; the stick or any other part of a bow.<BR>—धनुः-पट, अस्, m. the Piyal tree, Bucha-<BR>nania Latifolia; (also read धनुष्-पट.)<BR>—ध-<BR>नुः-शत, अम्, n., 100 Dhanus or 400 Hastas or<BR>cubits.<BR>—धनुः-शाखा, f. = धनुर्-गुण, q. v.<BR>—धनुः-शाला, f. the place where bows are kept,<BR>bow-room.<BR>—धनुः-श्रेणी, f., N. of two plants, =<BR>धनुर्-गुणा or धनु-श्रेणी and महेन्द्र-<BR>वारुणी.<BR>—धनुः-स्तम्भ, अस्, m. (?), a kind of<BR>spasmodic contraction of the body.<BR>—धनुर्-आकार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or धनुर्-आकृति, इस्, इस्, इ, bow-shaped,<BR>formed like a bow, curved, bent.<BR>—धनुर्-गुण,<BR>अस्, m. a bow-string; (आ), f. a plant from the leaves<BR>of which a tough thread is extracted of which bow-<BR>strings were formerly made; Sanseviera Zeylanica,<BR>S. Roxburghiana.<BR>—धनुर्-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bearing a bow, an archer; (अस्), m., N. of one of<BR>the 100 sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra [cf. धनुर्-धर];<BR>the art of managing a bow.<BR>—धनुर्-ग्राह, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘bearing a bow,’ an archer.<BR>—धनुर्-ज्या, f.<BR>a bow-string.<BR>—धनुर्ज्या-तल-शब्द, अस्, m. the<BR>mere twanging noise of the bow-string.<BR>—धनुर्-<BR>दुर्ग = धन्व-दुर्ग under धन्वन्, col. 2.<BR>—धनुर्-द्रुम, अस्, m. the bamboo used for<BR>bows.<BR>—धनुर्-द्वितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, furnished with<BR>a bow.<BR>—धनुर्-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing a bow,<BR>armed with a bow, an archer, a bowyer; (अस्), m.<BR>the sign of the zodiac Sagittarius; N. of one of the<BR>100 sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—धनुर्-धारिन्, ई,<BR>m. or धनुर्-भृत्, त्, m. an archer, a bowyer.<BR>—धनुर्-मध्य, अम्, n. the middle part of a<BR>bow (= लस्तक).<BR>—धनुर्-मह, अस्, m. a fes-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-b" target="_blank">Page0448-b+ 79</a>]<BR>tival or ceremony performed at the consecration of<BR>a bow; (a various reading has धनुर्-मख.)<BR>—धनुर्-मार्ग, अस्, m. a line curved like a bow,<BR>a curve.<BR>—धनुर्-माला, f. a plant from the leaves<BR>of which bow-strings were made; [cf. धनुर्-गुणा.]<BR>—धनुर्-यास, अस्, m. the plant Hedysarum Alhagi<BR>(= धन्वयास).<BR>—धनुर्-लता, f. the moon-plant<BR>(= सोम-वल्ली).<BR>—धनुर्-वक्त्र, अस्, m., N. of<BR>one of Skanda's attendants; (probably a wrong form<BR>for धनुर्-वक्र.)<BR>—धनुर्-वात, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of disease.<BR>—धनुर्-विद्या, f. the science of archery,<BR>skill in archery.<BR>—धनुर्-वृक्ष, अस्, m., N. of<BR>several plants used for making bows, as the bam-<BR>boo, Ficus Religiosa, Semecarpus Anacardium; a<BR>measure of four cubits; an arc, a portion of the cir-<BR>cumference of a circle; [cf. धनु and धनुस्.]<BR>—धनुर्-वेद, अस्, m. ‘knowledge of archery,<BR>the science of archery,’ N. of a treatise on archery<BR>(regarded as an Upa-veda connected with the Yajur-<BR>veda and ascribed to Viśvā-mitra or according to others<BR>to Bhṛgu).<BR>—धनुर्वेद-पर or धनुर्वेद-<BR>परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to the science of<BR>archery.<BR>—धनुर्-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, versed in the<BR>Dhanur-veda; (ई), m. epithet of Śiva.<BR>—धनुर्-<BR>हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, bow in hand, bearing a bow.<BR>—धनुषाक्ष (˚षा-अक्˚), अस्, m. (धनुषा<BR>probably inst. c. of धनुस्), N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—ध-<BR>नुष्-कर, अस्, m. a bow-maker; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>carrying a bow in the hand, armed with a bow, an<BR>archer, bowyer; (ई), f. a kind of plant; (also read<BR>धानुष्-करि.)<BR>—धनुष्-कार, अस्, or धनुष्-<BR>कृत्, त्, m. a bow-maker.<BR>—धनुष्-पट, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of tree, = पियाल.<BR>—धनुष्-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>‘bow-handed,’ armed with a bow, an archer.<BR>—ध-<BR>नुष्-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished or armed with a bow,<BR>bearing a bow, an archer, bowman, bowyer; (आन्),<BR>m., N. of a mountain to the north of Madhya-deśa;<BR>(अती), f., N. of the tutelary deity in the family of<BR>Vyāghra-pād.<BR>—धनुष्मत्-ता, f. archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्य|धन्यः
धन्य धन्य. See p. 447, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्व्
धन्व् धन्व्, cl. 1. P. A. (allied to rts.<BR>धव् and धाव् and 2. धन्), Ved. धन्-<BR>वति, -ते, दधन्वे, &c., to run; to flow; to cause<BR>to run or flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुतृ
धनुतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. rt. धन्व् or 2. धन्),<BR>Ved. running, flowing, flowing quickly; (Sāy.) en-<BR>riching by crops of grain; causing to flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्व|धन्वं|धन्वः
धन्व धन्व, अम्, n. (a curtailed form of<BR>धन्वन् below; said to be fr. rt. धन्व्), a bow,<BR>(in the classical language almost always at the end<BR>of an adj. comp.; cf. प्रिय-ध्˚); (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—धन्व-धि, इस्, m. a bow-case, anything<BR>in which a bow is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन्, अ, n. a bow, (in the later language<BR>generally at the end of a comp.; cf. अवतत-ध्˚,<BR>अस्थि-ध्˚, उग्र-ध्˚, कृत-ध्˚, क्षिप्र-ध्˚,<BR>क्षेम-ध्˚, &c.); (आ, अ), m. n. (in the earlier<BR>language n. only), a dry soil, a country scantily sup-<BR>plied with water, a desert, a waste; a firm spot, land,<BR>ground, shore; the plant Alhagi Maurorum which<BR>grows in a dry soil; (Sāy.) the sky, rain-water; [cf.<BR>Gr. θέναρ: Old Germ. ten-ar: Angl. Sax. denu,<BR>‘valley:’ Mod. Germ. tenne, ‘thrashing-floor;’ duene,<BR>‘down.’]<BR>—धन्व-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. going<BR>in a desert land; (Sāy.) going like an archer or<BR>warrior armed with a bow.<BR>—धन्व-च्युत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. agitating or moving the soil; (Sāy.) flowing<BR>with rain-water.<BR>—धन्व-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, growing<BR>on dry soil, produced on waste or barren land.<BR>—धन्व-तरु, उस्, m. a kind of Soma plant.<BR>—धन्व-दुर्ग, अम्, n. inaccessible by reason<BR>of a surrounding desert.<BR>—२. धन्वन्-तर, अस्,<BR>m. (for 1. see col. 1) = धन्वन्-तरि, a N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—धन्वन्-तरि, इस्, m. (for धन्वनि-<BR>तरि), ‘moving in a curve,’ N. of a form of the<BR>Sun; of a deity to whom oblations were offered in<BR>the north-east quarter, (the deity Dhanvantari was<BR>honoured with morning and evening oblations along<BR>with Soma, Vanas-pati, Agni-Soma, Indra-Agni,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">Page0448-c+ 78</a>]<BR>Heaven and Earth, Indra, the Viśve-devās, and<BR>Brahmā); the physician of the gods (who was pro-<BR>duced at the churning of the ocean, holding a cup<BR>of Amṛta in his hands; author of the Āyur-veda);<BR>a celebrated physician also called Divo-dāsa, king of<BR>Kāśi, (said to be the same as the preceding in<BR>another existence, and considered to be the founder<BR>of the Hindū school of medicine; also read धान्-<BR>वन्तरि); N. of the author of a medical dictionary<BR>(perhaps the same as the Dhanvantari mentioned<BR>among the nine gems of the court of Vikramāditya).<BR>—धन्वन्तरि-ग्रस्ता, f. ‘the plant eaten by<BR>Dhanvantari,’ Helleborus Niger, a medicinal plant;<BR>[cf. कटुकी.]<BR>—धन्वन्तरि-दर्प-भङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the breaking of Dhanvantari's pride,’ N. of the<BR>fifty-second chapter of the Kṛṣṇa-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—धन्वन्तरि-निघण्टु,<BR>उस्, m. the vocabulary of Dhanvantari.<BR>—धन्वन्-<BR>तरि-यज्ञ, अस्, m. the sacrifice of Dhanvantari.<BR>—धन्वन्तरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, composed by Dhan-<BR>vantari; (also read धान्वन्तरीय.)<BR>—धन्व-<BR>यवास or धन्वयवासक or धन्व-यास, अस्,<BR>m. Alhagi Maurorum.<BR>—धन्वा-सह् or धन्वा-<BR>साह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्य
धन्वन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in dry soil or<BR>barren land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वायन
धन्वायन, bearing bows (?), in भीम-धन्-<BR>वायनी. See भीम-धन्वायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वायिन्
धन्वायिन् or धन्वाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. carrying<BR>or bearing a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन्
धन्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, armed with a bow, an archer,<BR>a bowman, (at the end of comp., e. g. इषु-ध्˚,<BR>furnished with arrow and bow); cunning, shrewd, a<BR>wag, wit, sharp or shrewd fellow; (ई), m. the sign of<BR>the zodiac Sagittarius; an epithet of Śiva; of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Arjuna; N. of a son of Manu Tāmasa; N. of a<BR>commentator on the Drāhyāyaṇa-sūtras; several<BR>plants, Terminalia Arjuna, Mimusops Elengi (=<BR>वकुल); Alhagi Maurorum.<BR>—धन्वि-भाष्य,<BR>अम्, n. the commentary of Dhanvin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वङ्ग|धन्वङ्गः
धन्वङ्ग धन्वङ्ग or धन्वन, अस्, m. a<BR>fruit tree called in the modern languages of India<BR>‘Dhāmani, Dhāmana, Dhāminī, and Dhunin;’ (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of this tree.<BR>—धन्वन-च्छद, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Grewia Asiatica; (also read धन्वग;<BR>cf. धान्वन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरि|धन्वंतरि|धन्वंतरिः|धन्वन्तरिः
धन्वन्तरि धन्वन्-तरि. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन|धन्विनः
धन्विन धन्विन, अस्, m. a kind of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम|धमः
धम धम, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. ध्मा),<BR>blowing (fire, a trumpet, tube, &c.); smelting, fusing,<BR>melting, (generally at the end of a comp.; cf. करन्-<BR>ध्˚, जलन्-ध्˚, घटिन्-ध्˚); (अस्), m. the moon;<BR>an epithet of Kṛṣṇa; of Yama; of Brahma, the<BR>supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमक|धमकः
धमक, अस्, m. ‘a blower,’ a blacksmith (as<BR>blowing the forge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमधम
धमधम, अस्, m. (fr. ध्मा with redupli-<BR>cation), ‘the blower,’ N. of a demon that causes<BR>disease; N. of one of the attendants of Śiva; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; (आ),<BR>ind. blowing repeatedly or the sort of sound made by<BR>blowing with a bellows or a trumpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमन|धमनः
धमन, अस्, आ, अम्, blowing (a bellows or wind<BR>instrument, trumpet, &c.); cruel; (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of reed, Arundo Tibialis or Karka (= नड, नल);<BR>a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनि|धमनिः
धमनि, इस्, and in the later language also ध-<BR>मनी, f. a reed, a pipe, (perhaps also) the act of<BR>blowing (a wind instrument); a tube or canal of the<BR>human body; any tubular vessel, as a vein, nerve, &c.,<BR>(in the Hindū medical system there are twenty-four<BR>chief tubular vessels, which starting from the heart<BR>carry the रस or chyle through the body; according<BR>to another system the starting-point of these vessels<BR>is the navel, whence they branch out and perform<BR>various functions); the throat, neck; (ई), f. a sort<BR>of perfume (= हट्ट-विलासिनी and नलिका); tur-<BR>meric (= हरिद्रा); another plant, = पृश्नि-पर्णी;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">Page0449-a+ 77</a>]<BR>(इस्), f., N. of the mother of Vātāpi and Ilvala, and<BR>wife of Hrāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0448-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमनील
धमनील, अस्, आ, अम्, full-veined, large-veined,<BR>having prominent veins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमर
धमर or धमात्र (also read धेमात्र),<BR>a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमि|धमिः
धमि, इस्, इस्, इ, blowing, puffing; (इस्), f. the<BR>act of blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमित
धमित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. blown, kindled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्यत्
धम्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or धम्यमान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being blown; being melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मट
धम्मट धम्मट, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मल|धम्मलः
धम्मल धम्मल, अस्, m. the breast orna-<BR>mented with gold or jewels; [cf. धम्मिल्ल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिका
धम्मिका धम्मिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिल्ल|धम्मिल्लः
धम्मिल्ल धम्मिल्ल, अस्, m. the braided and<BR>ornamented hair of a woman tied round the head<BR>and intermixed with flowers, pearls, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिल्लक
धम्मिल्लक = धम्मिल्ल at end of comp.<BR>(e. g. स्रस्त-धम्मिल्लका वधूस्, a woman with<BR>loosened braided hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धय
धय धय, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. धे),<BR>drinking, sipping, sucking, (often at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. आस्यन्-धय, घटिन्-ध्˚, स्तनन्-ध्˚,<BR>&c.); (आ), f. a little girl (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर|धरः
धर धर, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. धृ),<BR>holding, bearing, carrying; wearing; possessing, hav-<BR>ing, possessed of, containing, keeping, sustaining,<BR>preserving, observing, (often compounded with its<BR>object; cf. अंशु-ध्˚, अक्ष-ध्˚, अश्रुति-ध्˚, असृग्-<BR>ध्˚, कक्ष-ध्˚, &c.); (अस्), m. a mountain [cf.<BR>क्षिति-ध्˚, भू-ध्˚, मही-ध्˚]; a flock of cotton;<BR>a frivolous or dissolute man (= विट), N. of one of<BR>the Vasus; of a hero on the side of the Pāṇḍavas;<BR>of the king of the tortoises; of the father of Padma-<BR>prabha, the sixth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī;<BR>(आ), f. ‘the bearer, supporter,’ the earth, the ground;<BR>the uterus or womb; a vein or tubular vessel of the<BR>body; marrow; a mass of gold or heap of valuables<BR>(representing the earth and given to Brāhmans); N.<BR>of one of the wives of Kaśyapa, mother of the land and<BR>water-birds, (probably = the Earth.)<BR>—धर-पट्ट<BR>or धर-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a prince of the Ballabhī<BR>or Vallabhī dynasty.<BR>—धर-संस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>equal to a mountain, huge as a mountain, &c.<BR>—ध-<BR>रा-कदम्ब, अस्, m. the Kadamba tree, Nauclea<BR>Cadamba; [cf. धारा-कदम्ब.]<BR>—धरात्मज<BR>(˚रा-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘son of the earth,’ the planet Mars<BR>or its regent.<BR>—धरा-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘bearing<BR>or sustaining the earth, prop of the earth,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; (अस्), m. a mountain.<BR>—धराधारा (˚रा-आध्˚?), f. the earth.<BR>—ध-<BR>राधिप (˚रा-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘sovereign of the earth,’<BR>a king.<BR>—धरान्तर-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, walking<BR>in the interior of the earth; (probably a wrong read-<BR>ing for धारान्तर-चर, q. v.)<BR>—धरा-पति, इस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of the earth,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—ध-<BR>रा-पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son of the earth,’ the planet<BR>Mars.<BR>—धरा-भुज्, क्, m. ‘enjoying or possessing<BR>the earth,’ a king.<BR>—धरा-भृत्, त्, m. ‘sustaining<BR>the earth,’ a mountain.<BR>—धरामर (˚रा-अम्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘a god or immortal on the earth,’ a Brāhman.<BR>—धरा-शय, अस्, ई, अम्, sleeping on the earth,<BR>lying on the ground.<BR>—धरा-सूनु, उस्, m. ‘son of<BR>the earth,’ the planet Mars.<BR>—धरोद्धार (˚रा-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. deliverance of the world.<BR>—धरो-<BR>पस्थ (˚रा-उप्˚), अस्, m. surface of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरण|धरणं|धरणः
धरण, अस्, ई, अम्, bearing, holding; preserving;<BR>(अस्), m. a dike, a bank, a ridge of land answering<BR>the purpose of a bridge &c., the side of a mountain;<BR>the world; the sun; the female breast; rice, corn;<BR>the Himālaya considered as king of mountains; N.<BR>of a king of the Nāgas; (ई or धरणि, इस्), f. the<BR>earth, the soil, the ground, the Earth personified as<BR>the wife of Dhruva; a tubular vessel of the body, a<BR>vein; a kind of bulbous plant, an esculent root, =<BR>धारणीया, धीर-पत्त्री, कन्दालु, कन्दाढ्य,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">Page0449-b+ 81</a>]<BR>दण्ड-कन्दक, वन-कन्द, सु-कन्दक; the<BR>silk-cotton tree, = शाल्मलि; a beam or rafter for a<BR>roof; N. of a dictionary (generally called धरणि<BR>or धरणि-कोश); (अम्), n. the act of holding,<BR>seizing, possessing, keeping, bearing, supporting, sup-<BR>port; bringing, procuring; a support, fastening,<BR>prop, stay; security; a sort of weight variously<BR>reckoned as = 10 Palas, = 16 silver Māṣakas, =<BR>1 silver Purāṇa, = (1/10) Śatamāna, = 19 Niṣpāvas, =<BR>(2/5) Karṣa, = (1/10) Pala, = 24 Raktikās; a particular<BR>high number.<BR>—धरण-प्रिया, f., N. of the<BR>goddess executing the commands of the nineteenth<BR>Arhat.<BR>—धरणि-गोणिग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—धरणि-ज, अस्, m. ‘the son of the earth,’ an<BR>epithet of Aṅgiras or the planet Mars.<BR>—धरणि-<BR>धर, अस्, m. ‘the bearer of the earth,’ an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; [cf. धरणी-धर.]<BR>—धरणि-<BR>मण्ड, N. of a place.<BR>—धरणि-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being or staying on earth.<BR>—धरणी-कन्द, अस्,<BR>m. an esculent root or bulb (= धरणी).<BR>—ध-<BR>रणी-कीलक, अस्, m. a mountain.<BR>—धरणी-तल,<BR>अम्, n. the surface of the earth.<BR>—धरणी-तलश्री,<BR>ईस्, m., N. of a king of the Kin-naras.<BR>—धरणी-<BR>धर, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘bearing or sustaining the earth,’<BR>epithet of the mythical elephants which are fabled<BR>to support the earth; (अस्), m. epithet of Śeṣa; of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; of Śiva; a mountain; a tor-<BR>toise; a king; N. of several persons; of a man of<BR>the family of Maunin and son of Maheśvara; of the<BR>father of Śaśi-dhara; of the father of Vāsu-deva and<BR>grandfather of the author Hari-nātha; of the father<BR>of Dayā-śaṅkara; of a scholiast on Manu; of a<BR>Bodhi-sattva; (sometimes read धरणि-धर or<BR>धरणीन्-धर.)<BR>—धरणी-धृत्, त्, m. ‘sup-<BR>porting the earth,’ an epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>—धरणी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the earth,’ a king.<BR>—धरणी-<BR>पूर, अस्, m. the ocean (as ‘surrounding the earth’).<BR>—धरणी-प्लव, अस्, m. the ocean (‘in which<BR>the earth floats’).<BR>—धरणी-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, bearing or<BR>supporting the earth; (त्), m. a mountain; a king;<BR>(also read धरणि-भृत्.)<BR>—धरणी-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the sphere of the earth,’ the globe.<BR>—ध-<BR>रणी-रुह, अस्, m. ‘growing on the earth,’ a tree;<BR>[cf. क्षिति-रुह् and क्षिति-रुह.]<BR>—धरणीश्वर<BR>(˚णि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the earth,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—धरणीश्वर-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of the<BR>lords of the earth,’ N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ध-<BR>रणी-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the earth,’ an epithet of<BR>Aṅgiras or the planet Mars; (आ), f. ‘the daughter<BR>of the earth,’ an epithet of Sītā, wife of Rāma (as<BR>produced from the soil by Janaka when he was<BR>ploughing a spot to prepare it for a sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणि|धरणिः
धरणि, इस्. See above under धरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीय
धरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be held or kept, to be<BR>borne or carried; supportable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिणि
धरिणि, इस्, m. (?), N. of an Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरित्री
धरित्री, f. a female bearer, supporter; the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिमन्
धरिमन्, आ, m. a balance, a pair of scales, a<BR>weight; form, figure, semblance; [cf. धरीमन्.]<BR>—धरिम-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, measurable by weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरीमन्
धरीमन् = धर्मन् (only occurring in the<BR>loc. धरीमणि), Ved. according to custom or law<BR>or precept; (Sāy.) containing the essence of the<BR>earth (as an altar); a vessel for holding anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरुण|धरुणः
1. धरुण, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 451, col. 3), Ved.<BR>carrying, holding, supporting, one who supports or<BR>keeps; (अस्), m. the supposed author of a hymn of the<BR>Ṛg-veda; an epithet of Brahmā; heaven, paradise;<BR>water; opinion, conception; (अस्, ई, अम्), containing<BR>in one's self, spacious; a place where anything is<BR>preserved or kept; (अम्), n. a basis, foundation,<BR>support, prop, stay; the firm soil of the earth; any-<BR>thing that is undermost or innermost; a receptacle,<BR>reservoir; water.<BR>—धरुण-ह्वर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. trembling in its innermost foundations ?; (Sāy.)<BR>obstructing the flow of waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्णस
धर्णस, अस्, आ, अम्, or धर्णसि or धर्णि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. bearing, supporting, sustaining; a<BR>supporter; strong, energetic, powerful, able; full of<BR>spirit (as Soma); firm, durable; (धर्णसि in Naigh.<BR>II. 9. is one of the synonyms of बल, strength.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्तव्य|धर्त्तव्य|धर्त्तव्यं
धर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be upheld or supported;<BR>to be held, had or possessed; to be placed or fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्तृ|धर्त्तृ
धर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, holding, bearing, supporting;<BR>(ता), m. a bearer, supporter, preserver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्र|धर्त्रं
धर्त्र, अम्, n. a prop, a stay; a house; a sacri-<BR>fice; virtue, moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म|धर्मः|धर्म्म|धर्म्मः
1. धर्म, अस्, अम्, m. n. (rarely n.; the older<BR>form which occurs in the Ṛg-veda is धर्मन्, q. v.;<BR>for 2. धर्म see p. 451, col. 3), that which is to be<BR>held fast or kept, ordinance, statute, law, usage, practice,<BR>custom, the customary observances of caste, sect, &c.;<BR>religion, piety; prescribed course of conduct, duty,<BR>(thus ‘giving alms’ &c. is the धर्म of the house-<BR>holder, ‘administering justice’ of a king, ‘piety’ of a<BR>Brāhman, ‘courage’ of a Kṣatriya); right, justice,<BR>equity, anything right, proper, or just; virtue, mora-<BR>lity, morals, merit, good works; nature, character,<BR>the peculiar state or condition of anything; an<BR>essential or characteristic quality, mark, peculiarity;<BR>manner, resemblance; any sacrifice; a peculiar kind<BR>of sacrifice; an Upaniṣad; religious abstraction,<BR>devotion (= योग); associating with the virtuous;<BR>a bow; a drinker of Soma juice; Right, Justice,<BR>Law, or Virtue personified (as born from the right<BR>breast of Brahmā, and having Śama, Kāma, and<BR>Harṣa as his offspring); or personified as a Bull;<BR>or personified as a Dove; a N. of Yama (the Hindū<BR>Pluto, ruler of the lower regions, god of justice, and<BR>judge of the dead); one of the attendants of the god<BR>of the Sun; Justice or Virtue identified with Viṣṇu;<BR>also identified with Prajā-pati, and said to be son-in-<BR>law of Dakṣa; N. of the fifteenth Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī, descended from Ikṣvāku, son of<BR>Bhānu and Su-vratā; N. of a son of Anu and father<BR>of Ghṛta; of a son of Gāndhāra and father of<BR>Dhṛta; of a son of Haihaya and father of Netra;<BR>of a son of Pṛthu-śravas and father of Uśanas; of a<BR>son of Su-vrata; of a son of Dīrgha-tapas; of a<BR>prince of Kaśmīra; of a lexicographer; (in astrology)<BR>N. of the ninth mansion; धर्मात् or धर्मेण,<BR>ind. according to right, rightly, justly, according to<BR>rule, according to the nature of anything.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-कथक, अस्, m. a propounder of the law.<BR>—धर्म-कथा, f. a discourse upon law, &c.<BR>—धर्म-कर्मन्, अ, n. a work of duty or piety;<BR>any virtuous or pious action.<BR>—धर्म-काम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, loving justice, observing right or duty; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of the demon Pāpīyas; of a god of<BR>the Bodhi tree.<BR>—धर्म-कामार्थ-सम्बद्ध<BR>(˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, joined with or containing<BR>virtue, pleasure, and wealth.<BR>—धर्म-काय, अस्, m.<BR>‘the body of law or of abstract existence,’ epithet of one<BR>of the three bodies of a Buddha; (अस्), m. a Buddha;<BR>a Jina or Jaina saint; an epithet of Avalokiteśvara.<BR>—धर्म-कार, अस्, m. a doer or observer of the<BR>law; N. of a person.<BR>—धर्म-कारण, अम्, n.<BR>cause of virtue.<BR>—धर्म-कार्य, अम्, n. any act of<BR>duty or religion (as digging a well, building a temple,<BR>&c.); pious act, good work, virtuous conduct.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m. ‘glory of religion,’ N. of a poet; of<BR>a logician; of a king mentioned in the twenty-first<BR>chapter of the Vṛhan-nāradīya-Purāṇa.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>कील, अस्, m. royal edict or order, decree, grant.<BR>—धर्म-कीलक, अस्, m. the command of a<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—धर्म-कूप, अस्, m. ‘the holy well,’<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—१. धर्म-कृत्, त्, त्, त् (for 2.<BR>see under धर्मन्), fulfilling duty, one who acts<BR>justly or practises virtue.<BR>—धर्म-कृत्य, अम्, n.<BR>fulfilment of duty, virtue; any moral or religious<BR>observance.<BR>—धर्म-केतु, उस्, m. ‘having justice<BR>for a banner or symbol,’ N. of a son of Su-ketu and<BR>father of Satya-ketu; N. of a Buddha; of a Jaina<BR>deified saint.<BR>—धर्म-कोश or धर्म-कोष, अस्,<BR>m. the treasury of law or duties; the collective body<BR>of laws or duties.<BR>—धर्मकोश-व्याख्या, f. ‘the<BR>explanation of the treasury of law,’ N. of a Buddhist<BR>work.<BR>—धर्म-क्रिया, f. observance of duties,<BR>acting according to law, righteous conduct, any reli-<BR>gious act or pious work.<BR>—धर्म-क्षेत्र, अम्, n.<BR>the department or province of the law; a plain in<BR>the north-west of India near Delhi (the scene of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0450-a" target="_blank">Page0450-a+ 81</a>]<BR>great battle between the Kurus and Pāṇḍus, com-<BR>monly called Kuru-kṣetra); (अस्), m. a man of piety<BR>and virtue.<BR>—धर्म-गञ्ज, अस्, m. ‘treasury of<BR>law or religion,’ N. of a library.<BR>—धर्म-गवेष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘seeking virtue &c.,’ N. of a man.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-गहनाभ्युद्गत-राज (˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘a prince who has threaded the labyrinth of the<BR>law,’ N. of a Buddha.<BR>—धर्म-गुप्त, अस्, m.<BR>‘protected by the law,’ N. of several persons; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a Buddhist school.<BR>—धर्मगुप्त-मिश्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author mentioned in the Saṅkṣepa-<BR>śaṅkara-jaya by Mādhava.<BR>—धर्म-ग्रन्थ, अस्,<BR>m. book of the law, sacred scriptures.<BR>—धर्म-ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. observance of moral or religious precepts,<BR>accepting or following the law.<BR>—धर्म-घट, अस्,<BR>m. a jar of fragrant water offered daily in the month<BR>Vaiśākha.<BR>—धर्म-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘destroying<BR>law or right,’ contrary to law or duty, immoral,<BR>unlawful; (अस्), m. (?), the plant Terminalia Belle-<BR>rica (so called because the seeds are used as dice).<BR>—धर्म-चक्र, अम्, n. ‘the wheel or circle of<BR>religion or law,’ (an expression used to denote the<BR>vast range of Dharma); a kind of mythical weapon;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘having the wheel of Dharma,’ a Buddha.<BR>—धर्मचक्र-भृत्, त्, m. ‘holding the wheel<BR>of Dharma,’ a Buddha or Jaina.<BR>—धर्म-चरण,<BR>अम्, n. or धर्म-चर्या, f. observance of the law,<BR>performance of duty.<BR>—धर्म-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>observing the law, fulfilling one's duties, practising<BR>virtue, virtuous, dutiful, moral; (ई), m., N. of a<BR>Buddhist deity; epithet of Śiva; (इणी), f. a female<BR>helpmate in the fulfilment of duties, especially a<BR>wife, an honest wife, a virtuous woman.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>चिन्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, reflecting on the law, studying<BR>duty, familiar with it.<BR>—धर्म-चिन्तन, अम्, n.<BR>or धर्म-चिन्ता, f. pondering on the law or duty,<BR>study of virtue, consideration of moral duties, virtuous<BR>reflection.<BR>—धर्म-चिन्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, reflecting on<BR>the law or duty; an epithet of Śākya-muni; (perhaps<BR>wrongly for धर्म-चिन्तिन्.)<BR>—धर्म-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, produced by a sense of duty; (अस्), m. ‘son<BR>of Dharma, judge of the dead,’ an epithet of Yudhi-<BR>ṣṭhira.<BR>—धर्म-जिज्ञासा, f. ‘inquiry into the law,’<BR>N. of a Pariśiṣṭa ascribed to Kātyāyana.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>जीवन, अस्, आ, अम्, living by fulfilment of prescribed<BR>duties, a Brāhman who lives according to the rules<BR>of his class, one who practises the outward acts of the<BR>law.<BR>—धर्म-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing the law<BR>or what is right, knowing one's duty, conversant with<BR>virtue.<BR>—धर्म-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of<BR>moral, legal, and religious duty.<BR>—धर्म-तत्त्व,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Mīmāṃsā work by Kamalākara.<BR>—धर्मतत्त्व-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing the truths<BR>of law or religion.<BR>—धर्म-तस्, ind. according to<BR>law or to rule, rightly, justly, religiously, righteously,<BR>virtuously; from a virtuous motive.<BR>—धर्म-तीर्-<BR>थ, अम्, n. ‘the holy Tīrtha,’ N. of a sacred place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—धर्म-त्याग, अस्, m. abandon-<BR>ment of religion, apostacy.<BR>—धर्म-त्रात, अस्, m.<BR>‘protected by the law,’ N. of a Buddhist author.<BR>—धर्म-त्व, अम्, n. religion, virtue, righteous-<BR>ness, morality, piety; inherent nature, peculiar pro-<BR>perty.<BR>—धर्म-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving or granting<BR>virtue; (अस्), m., N. of one of the attendants of<BR>Skanda.<BR>—धर्म-दत्त, अस्, m. ‘given by religion,’<BR>N. of a writer on rhetoric.<BR>—धर्म-दर्शन,<BR>अम्, n. seeing or knowing duty or the law.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-दान, अम्, n. a gift made from a sense of duty<BR>(without regard to self-interest).<BR>—धर्म-दार,<BR>आस्, m. pl. a lawful wife; [cf. धर्म-पत्नी.]<BR>—धर्म-दास, अस्, m. ‘the slave of duty,’ N. of<BR>a poet, author of the Vidagdha-mukha-maṇḍana.<BR>—धर्म-दिन्ना, f. ‘given by religion,’ (दिन्न<BR>in Pāli = दत्त), N. of a female.<BR>—धर्म-दीपिका,<BR>f., N. of a work.<BR>—धर्म-दुघा, f. a cow<BR>milked for the fulfilment of religious duty.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-दृढाभेद्य-सुनिलम्भ (˚ढ-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of the Garuḍas.<BR>—धर्म-दृश्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, seeing the right, regarding piety.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>द्रवी, f. ‘having law or virtue for its waters,’ the<BR>Ganges.<BR>—धर्म-द्रोहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, violating the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0450-b" target="_blank">Page0450-b+ 81</a>]<BR>law or right; (ई), m. a Rākṣasa.<BR>—धर्म-द्वे-<BR>षिन्, ई, m. the plant Terminalia Bellerica; see<BR>धर्म-घ्न.<BR>—धर्म-धर, अस्, m. ‘sup-<BR>porter of the law,’ N. of a king of the Kin-naras.<BR>—धर्म-धातु, उस्, m. ‘the element of law or<BR>of existence,’ one of the eighteen Dhātus of the<BR>Buddhists; a Buddha (‘whose Dhātu is Dharma’).<BR>—धर्मधातु-वाग्-ईश्वर, अस्, m., N. of a deity.<BR>—धर्म-धृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. observing the law.<BR>—धर्म-धृष्, क्, m. (धृक् is also referred to<BR>rt. धृ or to rt. दृह्), ‘supporter of the law or<BR>right,’ N. of a son of Śva-phalka; [cf. धर्म-भृत्.]<BR>—धर्म-ध्वज, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘whose banner is<BR>virtue,’ one who hangs out the flag of religion for<BR>selfish purposes, one who makes a livelihood by<BR>assumed devotion, a religious hypocrite or impostor;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the Sun; of a king of Mithilā, son<BR>of Kuśa-dhvaja and father of Amita-dhvaja and<BR>Kṛta-dhvaja; N. of a brother of Kuśa-dhvaja; of a<BR>king of Kāṅkana-pura.<BR>—धर्म-ध्वजिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, ‘hoisting the flag or colours of religion,’ a religious<BR>hypocrite or impostor, one who makes a livelihood<BR>by assumed devotion.<BR>—धर्म-नद, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a sacred lake; (according to a legend, a meta-<BR>morphosis of the god Dharma.)<BR>—धर्म-नन्-<BR>दन, अस्, m. ‘Dharma's joy, a son of the god<BR>Dharma,’ properly an epithet of Yudhi-ṣṭhira, but<BR>applied in Bhāg.-Purāṇa I. 9, 12, to all the sons of<BR>Pāṇḍu; [cf. धर्म-ज, धर्म-पुत्र, धर्म-<BR>सुत.]<BR>—धर्म-नन्दिन्, ई, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>who translated certain sacred writings into Chinese.<BR>—धर्म-नाथ, अस्, m. legal protector, rightful<BR>lord.<BR>—धर्म-नाभ, अस्, m. ‘the centre of the<BR>law,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of a king.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-निबन्ध, अस्, m. attachment to virtue or re-<BR>ligion, piety, virtue.<BR>—धर्म-निबन्धिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, pious, attached to virtue, engaged in religious<BR>duties, holy.<BR>—धर्म-निवेश, अस्, m. religious<BR>devotion.<BR>—धर्म-निष्पत्ति, इस्, f. fulfilment or<BR>discharge of duty, moral or religious observance.<BR>—धर्म-नेत्र, अस्, m. ‘law-eyed,’ N. of a grand-<BR>son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a son of Taṃsu and father<BR>of Dush-manta (Dushyanta).<BR>—धर्म-पट्ट, अस्,<BR>m. the band of law or duty.<BR>—धर्म-पति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. the lord or guardian of order and law.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-पत्तन, अम्, n. ‘the city of the law,’ epithet<BR>of the city of Śrāvantī [cf. धर्म-पट्टन];<BR>pepper.<BR>—धर्म-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the plant Ficus<BR>Glomerata.<BR>—धर्म-पत्नी, f. a lawful wife, a<BR>man's first wife, a wife of the same caste with her<BR>husband and married conformably to the established<BR>law.<BR>—धर्म-पथ, अस्, m. the way of duty or<BR>virtue, virtuous course; N. of a merchant.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-पथिन्, -पन्थास्, m. the way of duty or virtue.<BR>—धर्म-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, intent on virtue,<BR>devoted to duty; pious, righteous.<BR>—धर्म-पा-<BR>ठक, अस्, m. a teacher of law, a lawyer.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. ‘protector or guardian of the law,’<BR>metaphorical expression for ‘punishment’ or for ‘a<BR>sword;’ N. of a minister of king Daśa-ratha; of a<BR>learned Buddhist; of a prince.<BR>—धर्म-पालक,<BR>अस्, इका, अम्, observing the law, dutiful.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>पाश, अस्, m. ‘the noose of the god of justice,’ N. of<BR>a mythical weapon.<BR>—धर्म-पीठ, ‘the seat of<BR>law,’ N. of a place in Vārāṇasī.<BR>—धर्म-पीडा, f.<BR>an offence against the law, transgressing the law or<BR>right.<BR>—धर्म-पुत्र, अस्, m. a lawful son, a son<BR>begot from a sense of duty (not from sensual pleasure);<BR>‘son of the god Dharma,’ epithet of Yudhi-ṣṭhira;<BR>(औ), m. du. epithet of the Ṛṣis Nara and Nārā-<BR>yaṇa.<BR>—धर्म-पुर, अम्, n. ‘the city of the<BR>law,’ N. of a town situated on the Narmadā river.<BR>—धर्म-पुराण, अम्, n. ‘the Purāṇa of law,’<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—धर्म-प्रचार, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>course of law or right,’ metaphorical expression for<BR>‘a sword.’<BR>—धर्म-प्रदीप, अस्, m. ‘light of the<BR>law,’ N. of a work composed by Dhanañ-jaya.<BR>—धर्मप्रदीप-व्याख्यान, अम्, n. ‘the ex-<BR>planation of the lamp of law,’ N. of a commentary<BR>to the preceding work.<BR>—धर्म-प्रधान, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, eminent in piety.<BR>—धर्म-प्रभास, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0450-c" target="_blank">Page0450-c+ 81</a>]<BR>m. ‘illuminator of the law,’ N. of a Buddha.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-प्रवक्तृ, ता, m. a teacher or expounder of<BR>the law.<BR>—धर्म-प्रवचन, अम्, n. enuncia-<BR>tion of the law, the act of propounding the law.<BR>—धर्म-प्रस्थ, अस्, m. ‘the table-land of the<BR>god Dharma,’ N. of a place.<BR>—धर्म-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>m. ‘a friend of the law,’ N. of a Buddhist scholar.<BR>—धर्म-बल, अस्, m. ‘the strength of law,’ N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—धर्म-बाणिजिक, अस्, m. one who tries<BR>to make a profit out of his virtue like a merchant.<BR>—धर्म-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, virtuously-minded,<BR>virtuous; (इस्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—धर्म-भ-<BR>गिनी, f. a lawful sister, a female that has the rights of<BR>a sister; ‘a sister in respect of religion,’ i. e. as be-<BR>longing to the same religion; [cf. धर्म-भ्रातृ.]<BR>—धर्म-भागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessed of religion<BR>or virtue; (इनी), f. a virtuous wife.<BR>—धर्म-भा-<BR>णक, अस्, m. ‘an expounder of the law;’ a lecturer,<BR>a public reader of the Mahā-bhārata and other sacred<BR>works which are read aloud and explained to large<BR>assemblies of Hindūs at particular seasons.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-भिक्षुक, अस्, m. a mendicant from virtuous<BR>motives.<BR>—धर्म-भीरुक, अस्, आ, अम्, tremblingly<BR>alive to duty.<BR>—धर्म-भृत्, त्, m. ‘a supporter<BR>of law, a maintainer of justice,’ (often an epithet of<BR>a king); a virtuous person; N. of a son of Śva-phalka.<BR>—धर्म-भृत, अस्, m., N. of one of the sons<BR>of the thirteenth Manu.<BR>—धर्म-भ्रातृ, ता,<BR>m. ‘a brother in respect of religion,’ a fellow religious<BR>student, any one regarded as a brother from discharg-<BR>ing the same religious duties; [cf. धर्म-भगिनी.]<BR>—धर्म-मति, इस्, m. ‘virtuous-minded,’ N. of a<BR>prince; of a god; of the Bodhi tree.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of law or virtue, made<BR>up or replete with virtue, moral, righteous.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-महामात्र, अस्, m. a minister in matters of<BR>religion.<BR>—धर्म-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, depending<BR>only on custom.<BR>—धर्म-मार्ग, अस्, m. the path<BR>of virtue.<BR>—धर्म-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a Bud-<BR>dhist.<BR>—धर्म-मीमांसा-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘an<BR>abridgment of the inquiry into Dharma,’ N. of a<BR>Mīmāṃsā work by Kṛṣṇa-deva.<BR>—धर्म-मूल,<BR>अम्, n. the foundation of Hindū law and religion,<BR>the Vedas.<BR>—धर्म-मेघा, f., N. of one of the<BR>ten Bhūmis with Buddhists.<BR>—धर्म-युग, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the age of religion,’ the Kṛta-yuga.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>युज्, क्, क्, क्, righteous, pious, just.<BR>—धर्म-रक्-<BR>षिता, f., N. of a female.<BR>—धर्म-रति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>‘delighting in justice or virtue,’ N. of one of the sons<BR>of the demon Pāpīyas.<BR>—धर्म-रत्न, अम्, n.<BR>‘gem of the law,’ N. of a work.<BR>—धर्म-रथ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘whose chariot is dharma,’ N. of a son of Sagara;<BR>of Divi-ratha.<BR>—धर्म-राज्, ट्, m. ‘the king of<BR>justice,’ epithet of Yama; of Yudhi-ṣṭhira; of a<BR>king of the herons, son of Kaśyapa and an Apsaras.<BR>—धर्म-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of justice,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Yama; an epithet of Yudhi-ṣṭhira; a king<BR>in general; a Buddha.<BR>—धर्मराज-ता, f. the rank<BR>or title of Dharma-rāja.<BR>—धर्मराज-दीक्षित,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Vedānta-paribhāṣā.<BR>—धर्म-राजन्, आ, m. ‘king of justice,’ epithet<BR>of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—धर्मराज-पुरोगम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having Yudhi-ṣṭhira for a leader; headed<BR>by Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—धर्म-राजिका, f. a Stūpa.<BR>—धर्म-रुचि, इस्, m., N. of a god of the Bodhi<BR>tree; N. of a man.<BR>—धर्म-रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>opposed to law or virtue, illegal, immoral.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-लक्षण, अम्, n. an essential mark or character-<BR>istic of ethics or law, as place, time, &c.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>लोप, अस्, m. irreligion.<BR>—धर्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>endowed with virtue, virtuous, pious, upright, just,<BR>lawful; accompanied by Dharma; (अती), f., N. of a<BR>Mudrā; N. of a queen.<BR>—धर्म-वत्सल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, tenderly alive to duty, loving piety.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘abiding in duty,’ righteous.<BR>—धर्म-वर्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘increasing right<BR>or virtue,’ an epithet of Śiva; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>king of Śrāvastī; of a poet; (अम्), n., N. of a town.<BR>—धर्म-वर्मन्, अ, n. ‘shield or armour of jus-<BR>tice or virtue,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—धर्म-वाद,<BR>अस्, m. discussion or argument about law or duty.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-a" target="_blank">Page0451-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—धर्म-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, discussing the law or<BR>duty.<BR>—धर्म-वासर, अस्, m. ‘day of religious<BR>duties,’ the day of full moon, peculiar sacrifices being<BR>performed on this day.<BR>—धर्म-वाहन, अस्, m.<BR>‘whose vehicle is the bull, considered as a personi-<BR>fication of virtue,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘outside the law,’ contrary to<BR>what is right.<BR>—धर्म-विचार-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an abridgment of the Mīmāṃsā-sūtras by the<BR>Muni Jaimini.<BR>—धर्म-विद्, त्, त्, त्, acquainted with<BR>the law, duty-knowing, endued with a sense of<BR>justice, virtuous, pious, moral.<BR>—धर्म-विद्या, f.<BR>knowledge of the law or right; [cf. धार्मविद्य.]<BR>—धर्म-विधि, इस्, m. legal precept or injunction.<BR>—धर्म-विप्लव, अस्, m. ‘confusion or violation<BR>of duty,’ immorality, wickedness.<BR>—धर्म-विवर्-<BR>धन, अस्, m. ‘promoter of law or right,’ epithet<BR>of a son of Aśoka, = कुनाल.<BR>—धर्म-विवेक,<BR>अस्, m. investigation of right or virtue.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>विवेक-वाक्य, अम्, n., N. of a short poem ascribed<BR>to Halāyudha.<BR>—धर्म-विवेचन, अम्, n. judicial<BR>investigation.<BR>—धर्म-वृत्ति, इस्, f. ‘explanation<BR>of the law,’ N. of a chapter of the Śārṅgadhara-<BR>paddhati.<BR>—धर्म-वृद्ध, अस्, m. ‘advanced<BR>in virtue,’ N. of a son of Śva-phalka; [cf. धर्म-<BR>धृष् and धर्म-भृत्.]<BR>—धर्म-वैतंसिक,<BR>अस्, m. one who gives away money unlawfully ac-<BR>quired in the hope of appearing generous.<BR>—धर्-<BR>म-व्याध, अस्, m. ‘the hunter versed in law,’ N.<BR>of a Brāhman changed into a hunter in consequence<BR>of a curse; of a Brāhman-killer (born as a hunter<BR>from the body of Vasu, king of Kaśmīra).<BR>—धर्म-<BR>शरीर, अम्, n. ‘religious or sacred relic,’ a term<BR>applied to certain small Buddhist Stūpas.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—धर्म-शाला,<BR>f. a court of justice, a tribunal; a charitable insti-<BR>tution, a hospital.<BR>—धर्म-शासन or धर्म-<BR>शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘a law-book,’ a code of laws, the<BR>body or code of Hindū law, jurisprudence, any work<BR>on the subject.<BR>—धर्म-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a<BR>virtuous disposition, virtuous, just, pious; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a female.<BR>—धर्म-श्रेष्ठिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>Buddhist Arhat.<BR>—धर्म-संश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘following or seeking virtue,’ virtuous, just, pious.<BR>—धर्म-संहिता, f. a code or collection of law,<BR>especially the work of some saint or divine person<BR>(as Manu, Yājñavalkya, &c.).<BR>—धर्म-सङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. addiction to justice or virtue; hypocrisy.<BR>—धर्म-सङ्गीति, इस्, f. a discussion about the<BR>law; (with Buddhists) a council; N. of a work.<BR>—धर्म-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘collection of laws,<BR>legal compilation,’ N. of a Buddhist work on law.<BR>—धर्म-सन्तान-सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, producing vir-<BR>tuous offspring or actions.<BR>—धर्म-सभा, f. a<BR>court of justice, tribunal.<BR>—धर्म-सहाय, अस्,<BR>m. a companion in the fulfilment of religious duties.<BR>—धर्म-साधन, अम्, n. ‘means of performing<BR>duty,’ any act or virtue essential to a system of<BR>duties.<BR>—धर्म-सारथि, इस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Tri-kakud.<BR>—धर्म-सावर्णि, इस्, m., N. of the<BR>eleventh Manu.<BR>—धर्म-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—धर्म-सुत, अस्, m. ‘the son of the god<BR>Dharma,’ an epithet of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—धर्म-<BR>सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. promoting order or justice; (ऊस्),<BR>m. the fork-tailed shrike.<BR>—धर्म-सूत्र, अम्, n.<BR>a Sūtra work treating on law and custom; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Su-vrata.<BR>—धर्म-सेतु, उस्, m.<BR>‘barrier of justice,’ epithet of Śiva; N. of a son of<BR>Āryaka.<BR>—धर्म-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—धर्म-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. ‘collection of laws,’<BR>N. of a work by Śāriputra and Maudgalyāyana.<BR>—धर्म-स्थ, अस्, m. ‘abiding in the law,’ a<BR>judge.<BR>—धर्म-स्थल, अम्, n. ‘the place of<BR>justice,’ N. of a town.<BR>—धर्म-स्थविर, अस्, m.<BR>‘firm in law,’ N. of a man.<BR>—धर्म-स्वामिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘the lord of law and right,’ epithet of Buddha;<BR>N. of a sanctuary built by Dharma, king of Kaś-<BR>mīra.<BR>—धर्म-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, transgress-<BR>ing the law or justice.<BR>—धर्माकर (˚म-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘mine of virtue or law,’ N. of a disciple of<BR>Buddha Lokeśvara-rāja; of the ninety-ninth Buddha;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-b" target="_blank">Page0451-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of a Buddhist translator.<BR>—धर्मागम (˚म-आग्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a law-book.<BR>—धर्माङ्गद (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man; of a prince, son of Priyaṅ-kara.<BR>—धर्माङ्गा (˚म-अङ्˚), f. a heron.<BR>—धर्मा-<BR>चार्य (˚म-आच्˚), अस्, m. a teacher of law or of<BR>customs.<BR>—धर्माचार्य-स्तुति, इस्, f. ‘praise of the<BR>teacher of the law,’ N. of a work.<BR>—धर्मात्मज<BR>(˚म-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘the son of Dharma,’ an epithet<BR>of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR>—धर्मात्म-ता, f. pious-minded-<BR>ness, justice, virtue.<BR>—धर्मात्मन् (˚म-आत्˚), आ,<BR>आ, अ, just, virtuous, pious-minded, virtuously-minded,<BR>of a virtuous disposition, pious, fulfilling duties;<BR>(आ), m. a saint, a pious or virtuous person; an<BR>epithet of Kumāra-pāla.<BR>—धर्मादित्य (˚म-आद्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist king.<BR>—धर्माधर्म<BR>(˚म-अध्˚), औ, m. du. right and wrong, justice<BR>and injustice.<BR>—धर्माधर्म-परीक्षा, f. or<BR>-परीक्षण, अम्, n. ‘test of right and wrong,’ a kind<BR>of ordeal by drawing lots or slips of black and white<BR>paper.<BR>—धर्माधर्म-सेना-हनन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of the 120th chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—धर्माधिकरण (˚म-अध्˚),<BR>अम्, n. administration of the laws; a court of justice;<BR>(अस्), m. a judge, magistrate.<BR>—धर्माधिकरण-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. a court of justice.<BR>—धर्माधिक-<BR>रणिक, अस्, m. or धर्माधिकरणिन्, ई, m. ‘pre-<BR>siding over justice,’ a judge, an administrator of the<BR>law.<BR>—धर्माधिकार (˚म-अध्˚), अस्, m. admin-<BR>istration of justice, the office of a judge; N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—धर्माधिकारिन्, ई, m. or धर्माधि-<BR>कृत, अस्, m. a chief officer of justice, an adminis-<BR>trator of the law, lord-chief-justice, magistrate, a<BR>judge.<BR>—धर्माधिष्ठान (˚म-अध्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a court of justice.<BR>—धर्माध्यक्ष (˚म-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘overseer of justice,’ minister of justice, a<BR>magistrate, a judge.<BR>—धर्माध्वन् (˚म-अध्˚),<BR>आ, m. the way of justice or virtue.<BR>—धर्मानुष्-<BR>ठान (˚म-अन्˚), अम्, n. virtuous or moral conduct,<BR>acting according to law.<BR>—धर्मानुसार (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. conformity to law or virtue, course or<BR>practice of duty.<BR>—धर्मानुस्मृत्य्-उपस्थान,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist Āgama.<BR>—धर्मान्धु<BR>(˚म-अन्˚), उस्, m. ‘the well of Dharma, the holy<BR>well,’ N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—धर्मापेत (˚म-अप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, departing from virtue, wicked, immoral,<BR>unrighteous; (अम्), n. injustice, immorality, vice.<BR>—धर्माभिमनस् (˚म-अभ्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, di-<BR>recting the mind to virtue or religion, virtuous.<BR>—धर्माभिषेक-क्रिया (˚म-अभ्˚), f. any ab-<BR>lution prescribed as a religious duty.<BR>—धर्माम्-<BR>भोधि (˚म-अम्˚), इस्, m. ‘the ocean of laws,’ N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—धर्मायतन (˚म-आय्˚), अम्, n.<BR>knowledge of धर्म by means of मनस् (?).<BR>—धर्मारण्य (˚म-अर्˚), अम्, n. ‘grove of<BR>religion,’ a sacred grove, a wood inhabited by her-<BR>mits or ascetics; N. of a sacred forest in Madhya-<BR>deśa, into which Dharma is said to have retired; N.<BR>of a town founded by Amūrta-rajas.<BR>—धर्मार्थ-<BR>काम-मोक्ष (˚म-अर्˚), आस्, m. pl. religious merit,<BR>wealth, pleasure, and final emancipation, (the four<BR>ends or objects of existence.)<BR>—धर्मार्थ-दर्-<BR>शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having an eye to duty and interest<BR>or to religion and wealth.<BR>—धर्मार्थ-प्रति-<BR>बद्ध-ता, f. attachment to duty and interest or to<BR>religion and wealth.<BR>—धर्मार्थम्, ind. for reli-<BR>gious purposes; according to right or duty, in a just<BR>manner, according to prescript.<BR>—धर्मार्थीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (fr. धर्म-अर्थ), relating to law or<BR>duty.<BR>—धर्मालीक (˚म-अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>a false character.<BR>—धर्मालोक-मुख (˚म-आल्˚),<BR>अम्, n. introduction to the understanding of the<BR>धर्म of Śākya-muni.<BR>—धर्माशोक (˚म-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the Aśoka of justice,’ epithet of king Aśoka,<BR>grandson of Candra-gupta, (after he had adopted the<BR>Buddhist faith.)<BR>—धर्माश्रित (˚म-आश्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, seeking virtue, just, virtuous.<BR>—धर्मासन<BR>(˚म-आस्˚), अम्, n. the throne of justice, judgment-<BR>seat, the bench.<BR>—धर्मासन-गत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>seated on the judgment-seat.<BR>—धर्मास्तिकाय<BR>(˚म-अस्˚), अस्, m. (with Jainas) the category or<BR>predicament of virtue.<BR>—धर्मेन्द्र (˚म-इन्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">Page0451-c+ 78</a>]<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of justice,’ epithet of Yama.<BR>—धर्-<BR>मेप्सु (˚म-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to acquire<BR>religious merit.<BR>—धर्मेश (˚म-ईश), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of justice,’ epithet of Yama.<BR>—धर्मेश्वर<BR>(˚म-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of justice,’ epithet of Yama;<BR>N. of a Buddhist deity; of a commentator on Yājña-<BR>valkya.<BR>—धर्मेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n. ‘the Tīrtha<BR>of the lord of justice,’ N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—धर्मेश्वर-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘the Liṅga of the<BR>lord of justice,’ N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—धर्-<BR>मोच्चय (˚म-उच्˚), अस्, m. ‘collection of law,’ N.<BR>of a place (in which Śākya-muni is said to have<BR>instructed the deities called Tuṣitas).<BR>—धर्मोत्-<BR>तर (˚म-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘chiefly characterized by<BR>virtue,’ N. of a Buddhist teacher.<BR>—धर्मोत्तरीय,<BR>आस्, m. pl. the disciples of Dharmottara.<BR>—धर्मो-<BR>पदेश (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m. instruction in law or duty,<BR>a discourse on religion, moral or religious instruction;<BR>the laws, the collective body of laws.<BR>—धर्मोप-<BR>देशक (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, m. a teacher of the law, a<BR>Guru or spiritual preceptor.<BR>—धर्मोपदेशना<BR>(˚म-उप्˚), f. instruction in the law, advice relating<BR>to it.<BR>—धर्मोपध (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>making a pretence of religion, hypocritical.<BR>—धर्-<BR>मोपेत (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, endowed with vir-<BR>tues, virtuous, moral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0449-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म|धर्मः|धर्म्म|धर्म्मः
2. धर्म, Nom. P. धर्मति, &c., to become<BR>law. (For 1. धर्म see p. 449, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मक
धर्मक (at the end of an adj. comp.) =<BR>1. धर्म; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मन्|धर्म्मन्
धर्मन्, आ, m., Ved. bearer, maintainer, sup-<BR>porter, arranger; N. of a son of Bṛhad-rāja and<BR>father of Kṛtañ-jaya; (अ), n. (the older form for the<BR>later धर्म; and even in the later language used<BR>as a substitute for धर्म at the end of adj.<BR>comps.), support, prop; (Sāy.) religious rite (Ved.);<BR>law, order, custom; religion, duty; mode, manner;<BR>quality, characteristic mark, natural order [cf. क्ष-<BR>त्र-ध्˚, क्षेम-ध्˚, जय-ध्˚, &c.]; धर्मणा,<BR>inst. sing. or धर्मभिस्, inst. pl., Ved. in order,<BR>according to rule, regularly, naturally.<BR>—२. धर्म-<BR>कृत्, त्, m., Ved. ‘a maintainer of order or a per-<BR>former of religious rites,’ epithet of Indra; (for 1.<BR>see p. 449, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयु|धर्म्मयु|धर्म्मयुः
धर्मयु, उस्, उस्, उ, righteous, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माय
धर्माय, Nom. P. A. धर्मायति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to become law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिन्|धर्म्मिन्
धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, virtuous, religious, pious, just;<BR>obeying the law, knowing one's duties, having duties;<BR>endowed with any peculiar property or faculty; (often<BR>at the end of comp.) subject to particular laws (e. g.<BR>विनाश-ध्˚, q. v.); having the peculiar qualities or<BR>properties or nature of anything, having anything as<BR>a characteristic mark [cf. एक-ध्˚]; following the<BR>habits of any person; (ई), m., N. of the fourteenth<BR>Vyāsa; (इणी), f. a kind of perfume; [cf. धार्मि-<BR>णेय.]<BR>—धर्मि-त्व, अम्, n. virtuousness, justice,<BR>devotion to one's duties, virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मिष्ठ|धर्मिष्ठः|धर्म्मिष्ठ
धर्मिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of धर्मिन्),<BR>very pious or virtuous; completely according to law,<BR>completely harmonizing or agreeing with law or<BR>virtue, lawful.<BR>—धर्मिष्ठ-ता, f. great virtuous-<BR>ness, righteousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मीयस्|धर्म्मीयस्
धर्मीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of धर्मिन्),<BR>more virtuous &c.; very pious or moral &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मेयु
धर्मेयु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Raudrāśva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्य|धर्म्म्यः
धर्म्य, अस्, आ, अम्, lawful, legal, conformable<BR>to justice or law or custom or morality, consistent<BR>with duty; usual; just, righteous; legitimate; en-<BR>dowed with particular qualities (e. g. तद्-धर्म्य,<BR>endowed with those qualities); suitable to any person<BR>or thing (with gen.).<BR>—धर्म्य-विवाह, अस्, m.<BR>legal marriage (of which there are various kinds<BR>described in Manu III. 22).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरुण|धरुणः
धरुण 2. धरुण, अस्, m. (fr. rt. धे?),<BR>Ved. a sucking calf; (for 1. धरुण see p. 449,<BR>col. 2; cf. धारु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्कट
धर्कट धर्कट, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0451-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्बक
धर्बक धर्बक, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Ajāta-śatru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म|धर्मः|धर्म्म|धर्म्मः
धर्म धर्म. See p. 449, col. 3; p. 451, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मण|धर्म्मण|धर्म्मणः
धर्मण धर्मण, अस्, m. a kind of snake;<BR>a kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मीपुत्र|धर्मीपुत्रः
धर्मीपुत्र धर्मीपुत्र, अस्, m. an actor, a<BR>player; (also read धात्री-पुत्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ष|धर्षः
धर्ष धर्ष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. धृष्), bold-<BR>ness, insolence, overbearing conduct, daringness, im-<BR>pudence, licentiousness, pride, arrogance; impatience;<BR>violation (of a woman); injury, wrong, insult; re-<BR>straint; a eunuch; [cf. धर्ष-वर.]<BR>—धर्ष-<BR>कारिणी, f. a violated virgin.<BR>—धर्ष-वर, अस्,<BR>m. a eunuch superintending the women's apartments;<BR>(probably wrong reading for वर्ष-धर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षक|धर्षकः
धर्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, attacking, assailing, assault-<BR>ing, violating, overbearing; seducing; (अस्), m. a se-<BR>ducer, adulterer; a dancer, actor; mime, mummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षण|धर्षणं
धर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, offending, hurting, injur-<BR>ing, assaulting; (अम्, आ), n. f. assault, affront, insult,<BR>outrage; offence; violation, rape, seduction; bad<BR>treatment; overbearingness; contempt, disrespect,<BR>contumely, abuse; arrogance; copulation; (ई), f. or<BR>(इस्), f. a wanton or unchaste woman, a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षणीय
धर्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to be attacked or<BR>assaulted, easily assailable or conquerable, violable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षित|धर्षितं
धर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, violated; overpowered,<BR>overcome, smitten, ill-treated; (अम्), n. contumely,<BR>pride, insolence; copulation, cohabitation; (आ), f. an<BR>unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिन्
धर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, attacking, assaulting, ill-treat-<BR>ing, treating badly; audacious, overbearing; proud,<BR>arrogant; cohabiting; (इणी), f. a disloyal or unchaste<BR>woman, a harlot; [cf. धर्षणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धलण्ड|धलण्डः
धलण्ड धलण्ड, अस्, m. a kind of small<BR>thorny tree, commonly called Dhala-āṅkaḍā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धलिल
धलिल धलिल, N. of a valley in which<BR>the capital of Udyāna is said to have been situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव्
धव् धव् (connected with rts. 1. धाव्<BR>and धन्व्), cl. 1. A. धवते, &c., Ved.<BR>to run, flow; [cf. Gr. θέ-ω, θεύσομαι, θοός, βοη-θέ-ω,<BR>νω-θής.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव 1. धव, अस्, m. the plant Grislea<BR>Tomentosa (= मधुर-त्वच).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव 2. धव, अस्, m. (said by some to be<BR>fr. rt. 1. धू?), a man; a husband [cf. स-धवा<BR>and वि-धवा]; a possessor, master, lord; a rogue,<BR>a cheat; N. of a Vasu (probably incorrect for<BR>धर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवनी
धवनी धवनी, f. a kind of plant, Desmo-<BR>dium Gangeticum or a similar species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवर
धवर धवर, अम्, n. a particular high<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवल|धवलः
धवल धवल, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>2. धाव्), white, dazzling white, of a shining white<BR>colour; handsome, beautiful; (अस्), m. white (the<BR>colour); an old bull, an excellent ox; a kind of<BR>camphor (= चीन-कर्पूर); the plant Grislea To-<BR>mentosa (= धव); N. of one of the elephants of<BR>the quarters; N. of a Rāga or mode of music,<BR>(according to Bharata, the eighth son of Hindola-<BR>rāga); (आ or ई), f. a white cow; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>disease (perhaps only whiteness of the hair); N. of<BR>a river; (अम्), n. white pepper; a kind of metre<BR>consisting of 4 × 18 short syllables and 1 long (=<BR>धवलाङ्क; cf. उदय-ध्˚).<BR>—धवल-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘the white or snowy mountain’ (commonly<BR>dhoula-giri or dola-gir), N. of one of the highest<BR>peaks of the great snowy range of the Himālayas,<BR>lat. 29. 11, long. 82. 59.<BR>—धवल-गृह, अम्, n.<BR>a house whitened with chunam or stucco, a palace.<BR>—धवल-त्व, अम्, n. whiteness.<BR>—धवल-<BR>पक्ष, अस्, m. ‘white-winged,’ a goose; the light<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">Page0452-b+ 80</a>]<BR>half of the month, the fortnight of the moon's in-<BR>crease.<BR>—धवल-पुराण-समुच्चय, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—धवल-मृत्तिका, f. ‘white earth,’<BR>chalk.<BR>—धवल-यावनाल, अस्, m. white Yāvanāla.<BR>—धवलाङ्क (˚ल-अङ्˚), अम्, n. = धवल, a<BR>species of the Ati-dhṛti metre.<BR>—धवली-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made white, whitened, whited.<BR>—धवली-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become white.<BR>—धवलोत्पल<BR>(˚ल-उत्˚), अम्, n. the white esculent water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलित
धवलित, अस्, आ, अम्, made dazzling white,<BR>whitened, white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलिमन्
धवलिमन्, आ, m. whiteness, white colour, white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवाणक|धवाणकः
धवाणक धवाणक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. धू),<BR>air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवितव्य
धवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be fanned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवित्र|धवित्रं
धवित्र, अम्, n. a Paṅkhā or fan (made of ante-<BR>lope's skin or leather, and used especially for blowing<BR>a sacrificial fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा 1. धा, cl. 3. P. A. दधाति, धत्ते<BR>(1st pl. दध्मस्, 2nd धत्थ, 3rd द-<BR>धति; 1st sing. A. दधे, 2nd धत्से, 3rd धत्ते,<BR>2nd du. दधाथे, 3rd du. दधाते, 3rd pl. दध-<BR>ते); Impf. अदधात्, अधत्त (2nd du. P. अधत्-<BR>तम्, 2nd pl. अधत्त, 3rd pl. अदधुस्; 2nd sing.<BR>A. अधत्थास्, 3rd pl. अदधत); Pot. दध्यात्,<BR>दधीत; Impv. दधातु, धत्ताम् (2nd sing.<BR>धेहि, 2nd du. धत्तम्, 3rd du. धत्ताम्, 2nd pl.<BR>धत्त, 3rd pl. दधतु; 2nd sing. A. धत्स्व,<BR>2nd pl. धद्ध्वम्, 3rd pl. दधताम्); Perf.<BR>दधौ, दधे (2nd sing. दधिथ or दधाथ,<BR>1st pl. दधिम, 2nd pl. दध, 3rd pl. दधुस्;<BR>3rd pl. A. दधिरे); Fut. धाता; धास्यति, -ते;<BR>Aor. अधात्, अधित (3rd pl. A. अधिषत); Prec.<BR>धेयात्, धासीष्ट; (Ved. forms are, Pres. 1st pl.<BR>P. दध्मसि, 3rd pl. दधन्ति, 2nd sing. A. द-<BR>धसे, 3rd sing. दधे or दधते, 3rd du. दधेते,<BR>2nd pl. दधिध्वे; Impf. 2nd sing. P. दधस्,<BR>3rd sing. दधत्, दधात्, 1st pl. दधाम, 3rd<BR>pl. दधन्; Leṭ, Impf. 2nd du. P. दधथस्;<BR>Pot. 1st sing. धेयाम्, 2nd sing. धायीस्, 1st pl.<BR>धेम, 2nd pl. धेतन; Impv. 3rd sing. धातु,<BR>2nd pl. धात, धत्तन, दधात, दधातन,<BR>3rd pl. धान्तु, दधन्तु, 2nd sing. A. धिष्व;<BR>Perf. 2nd sing. A. धिषे, 3rd pl. दध्रे, धिरे;<BR>Aor. 1st sing. P. धाम्, 2nd sing. धास्, 3rd sing.<BR>धात्, with प्रति also धत्, 3rd pl. धुस्; 1st pl.<BR>A. अधीमहि, धीमहि, see under 1. धी; Leṭ,<BR>Aor. 3rd sing. P. धाति, 2nd du. P. धासथस्, A.<BR>धेथे, धैथे, 1st pl. A. धामहे, 2nd pl. P.<BR>धासथ, 3rd pl. धासुस्); धातुम् (Ved. inf.<BR>धातवे, धातवै, धातोस्, धै in वयो-धै,<BR>धाम् in प्रति-धाम्, धियध्यै), to put, place,<BR>set, lay; put in, lay on or upon (with loc., e. g.<BR>तेषु दण्डं दधाति, he lays the stick on them,<BR>i. e. punishes them); to place in any state or con-<BR>dition; to bring, convey, lead towards (Ved.); to<BR>cause to obtain, cause (Ved.); to fix upon, direct<BR>towards (with dat. or loc.), fix or direct the mind<BR>(मनस् or मतिम्), fix the thoughts or attention<BR>(समाधिम्) on (dat., or loc.), make up the mind<BR>to do anything (dat., loc., or inf.), to resolve upon; to<BR>bestow anything (acc.) upon a person (loc., dat., gen.),<BR>grant, confer, present, give; to put in possession; to<BR>appoint, fix, constitute; to make, render, produce,<BR>generate; to cause, create; to perform, do, under-<BR>take; to hold, take hold of, seize; to keep, pre-<BR>serve; to bear, wear, put on (clothes); to sustain,<BR>support, maintain; to accept, take, receive, obtain,<BR>get; to conceive (in the womb); to take possession<BR>of, assume, have, possess; to show, exhibit (A.); to<BR>incur, undergo: Pass. धीयते, to be put or placed<BR>or laid; to be arranged; to be contained in; to be<BR>fixed (as the thoughts), to resolve (e. g. मे धीयते<BR>मतिस्, my opinion or resolution is): Caus. धाप-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अदीधिपत्, generally with pre-<BR>positions [cf. अन्तर्-धा, अपि-धा, अभि-धा, अव-<BR>धा, &c.]: Desid. धित्सति, -ते (Ved. दिधिषति),<BR>to wish to give or present (Ved.); to wish to place<BR>or put; to wish to obtain, strive to gain, &c.:<BR>Intens. देधीयते, दाधाति; [cf. Zend dā, ‘to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-c" target="_blank">Page0452-c+ 81</a>]<BR>put, make;’ dā-ta-m, ‘law;’ dā-man, ‘creature:’<BR>Gr. τί-θη-μι, θέ-μα, θέ-σι-ς, θε-σ-μός, θέ-μι-ς<BR>θεμός, θε-μέ-λιο-ν, θέ-με-θλο-ν, θής, θῆσσα, θή-κη,<BR>θῶκος, θᾶκος: Lat. fămulus, familia, -do in<BR>ab-do, con-do, per-do, ven-do, pessum-do, cre-do<BR>= श्रद्-दधामि: Osc. faa-ma, ‘house (?),’ fam-<BR>el = familia: Goth. ga-dêd-s, dê-ths, ‘deed,’ in<BR>missa-dêths, ‘a crime;’ dôm-s, ‘judgment:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. don, ‘to do;’ dema, ‘a judge;’ dom, ‘judg-<BR>ment:’ Old Sax. dō-m, ‘I do,’ = दधामि: Old<BR>Germ. tō-m, ‘I do:’ Old Eng. -de in ask-e-de = ‘ask-<BR>did:’ Mod. Germ. -te in such-te: Lith. de-mi, de-<BR>du, ‘I put:’ Slav. de-yun, ‘I do;’ de-lo, ‘work:’<BR>Hib. deanaim, ‘I do;’ dan, ‘work.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
2. धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR>placing; holding; containing, having; causing, &c.,<BR>see किये-धा, चनो-धा, धाम-धा, धियन्-धा,<BR>&c.; (आस्), m. a placer; a holder, container, possessor,<BR>&c.; a N. of Brahmā; of Bṛhas-pati; (आस्), f. the<BR>act of placing or holding, &c., (at the end of comp.,<BR>cf. तिरो-धा and दुर्-धा.) The affix धा after<BR>numerals is thought by some to be an old inst. from<BR>this धा; [cf. the use of 1. धातु after numerals.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाक|धाकः
धाक, अस्, m. an ox; a receptacle, reservoir (=<BR>आ-धार or according to another reading आ-हार);<BR>food, boiled rice; a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातु|धातुः
1. धातु, उस्, m. (for 2. धातु see p. 453, col. 3),<BR>that which is placed or laid, a deposit, layer (Ved.);<BR>a constituent or essential part, an ingredient, (thus<BR>गुण, string, is the धातु of a rope made of several<BR>strings); part, portion, (sometimes used at the end of<BR>an adj. comp. like the English ‘fold,’ see त्रि-धातु,<BR>सप्त-ध्˚); an element, primary or elementary<BR>substance, primitive matter (of which five are usually<BR>reckoned or with Brahma six, thus enumerated by<BR>Yājñavalkya III. 145: 1. ब्रह्म, the eternal spirit;<BR>2. ख or आकाश, ether; 3. अनिल, air; 4. तेजस्,<BR>fire; 5. जल, water; 6. भू, earth: the Buddhists<BR>substitute विज्ञान for ब्रह्म: the eighteen ele-<BR>ments or धातु-लोकस् of the southern Buddhists are<BR>the five organs of sense with मनस्, the six qualities<BR>observed by these, and six ideas produced by these<BR>six qualities); constituent element or essential ingre-<BR>dient of the body, primary or essential fluid or juice,<BR>a secretion, (the number of which is variously given<BR>as seven or ten; these Dhātus are distinct from the<BR>five elements of which the body also consists, and<BR>are sometimes regarded as Rasas, i. e. secretions or<BR>fluids; they are chyle, blood, flesh, fat, bone, marrow,<BR>and semen, to which must be added hair, skin, and<BR>sinews, if ten are reckoned); a humor or affection of<BR>the body (viz. phlegm, wind, and bile); a bone;<BR>(according to some) any one of the five organs of<BR>sense; any one of the five properties or qualities of<BR>the elements observed by the organs of sense (viz.<BR>sound, tangibility, colour, flavour, smell, see under<BR>गुण); a primary element of the earth or of moun-<BR>tains, a mineral, fossil, metal, ore; a fluid mineral<BR>of a red colour; the primary element of words, a<BR>verbal root; [cf. उप-ध्˚, काम-ध्˚, गिरि-ध्˚,<BR>&c.]<BR>—धातु-काय, अस्, m. ‘body of elements,’ N.<BR>of a Buddhist work by Pūrṇa.<BR>—धातु-काशीश or<BR>धातु-कासीस, अम्, n. red sulphate of iron.<BR>—धातु-<BR>कुशल, अस्, आ, अम्, skilled in metals, a metallurgist,<BR>mineralogist.<BR>—धातु-क्रिया, f. metallurgy, minera-<BR>logy.<BR>—धातु-क्षय, अस्, m. waste of the bodily<BR>humors, any mortal disease.<BR>—धातुक्षय-कास,<BR>अस्, m. a consumptive cough.<BR>—धातु-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a receptacle for Buddhist relics, a dagop, (according<BR>to some द-गोप् = धातु-गोप.)<BR>—धातु-ग्राहिन्,<BR>ई, m. calamine.<BR>—धातु-घोषा, f., N. of a work<BR>on the verbal roots.<BR>—धातु-घ्न, अम्, n. sour<BR>gruel prepared from the fermentation of rice-water.<BR>—धातु-चन्द्रिका, f. ‘elucidation of roots,’ N. of<BR>a grammatical work by Kavi-candra.<BR>—धातु-ज =<BR>धातुक, bitumen.<BR>—धातु-दीपिका, f. ‘elucidation<BR>of roots,’ N. of a commentary by Durgā-dāsa on<BR>Vopa-deva's collection of roots.<BR>—धातु-द्रावक,<BR>‘dissolving metals,’ borax, tinkal.<BR>—धातु-नाशन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘destroying the humors,’ sour gruel; [cf.<BR>धातु-घ्न.]<BR>—धातु-न्याय-मञ्जाषा, f., N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-a" target="_blank">Page0453-a+ 81</a>]<BR>a work on the radicals.<BR>—धातु-प, अस्, m. the<BR>alimentary juice or chyle, the chief of the seven<BR>elementary ingredients of the body.<BR>—धातु-पा-<BR>ठ, अस्, m. ‘recital of roots,’ a list or collection of<BR>roots compiled and arranged according to Pāṇini's<BR>system, (the most important and well-known Dhātu-<BR>pāṭha is ascribed to Pāṇini himself.)<BR>—धातु-पारा-<BR>यण or धातु-पारायणीय, अम्, n., N. of a work<BR>on verbal roots.<BR>—धातु-पुष्टि, इस्, f. nutrition of<BR>the bodily humors.<BR>—धातु-पुष्पी and धातु-पु-<BR>ष्पिका, f. a plant, = धातृ-पुष्पी.<BR>—धातु-प्र-<BR>दीप, अस्, m., N. of a commentary by Maitreya-<BR>rakṣita on the Dhātu-pāṭha.<BR>—धातुप्रदीप-दी-<BR>पिका or धातुप्रदीप-टीका, f., N. of a commentary<BR>on the preceding work.<BR>—धातु-भृत्, त्, m. ‘bear-<BR>ing metals,’ a mountain; (त्, त्, त्), promoting the<BR>elementary juices or secretions, robust.<BR>—धातु-<BR>मञ्जरी, f., N. of a commentary by Kāśī-nātha on<BR>the Dhātu-pāṭha.<BR>—धातु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, con-<BR>taining or possessing elements or elementary sub-<BR>stances, abounding in minerals or metals.<BR>—धातु-<BR>मत्-ता, f. richness in metals &c.<BR>—धातु-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of or abounding in metals,<BR>metallic.<BR>—धातु-मल, अम्, n. impure excretion<BR>from the essential fluids of the body; lead (the most<BR>impure of metals).<BR>—धातु-माक्षिक, अम्, n. a<BR>mineral substance, sulphuret of iron.<BR>—धातु-मारिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘dissolving metals,’ sulphur; (इणी), f. borax.<BR>—धातु-रत्न-माला, f., N. of a medical work by<BR>Deva-datta.<BR>—धातु-रत्नावली, f. ‘a necklace or<BR>string of roots,’ N. of a metrical collection of roots<BR>by Rādhā-kṛṣṇa.<BR>—धातु-राजक, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>chief of the essential fluids of the body,’ semen, the<BR>seminal fluid.<BR>—धातु-लक्षण, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—धातु-वल्लभ, अम्, n. ‘friend of metals,’<BR>borax (used as a flux).<BR>—धातु-वाद, अस्, m. metal-<BR>lurgy, mineralogy.<BR>—धातुवादिन्, ई, m. an assayer,<BR>miner, mineralogist, metallurgist.<BR>—धातु-विकार,<BR>अस्, m. = धातु-क्षय.<BR>—धातु-विष्, ट्, f. = धातु-<BR>मल, lead.<BR>—धातु-वृत्ति, इस्, f. a commentary on<BR>the roots.<BR>—धातु-वैरिन्, ई, m. ‘enemy of metals,’<BR>sulphur.<BR>—धातु-शेखर, अम्, n. ‘chief of mine-<BR>rals,’ green sulphate of iron or green vitriol.<BR>—धातु-<BR>शोधन or धातु-सम्भव, lead.<BR>—धातु-सा-<BR>म्य, अम्, n. equilibrium of the bodily humors, good<BR>health.<BR>—धातु-हन्, ‘killing metals,’ sulphur.<BR>—धातूपल (˚तु-उप्˚), अस्, m. ‘the stone among<BR>metals,’ chalk.<BR>—धात्व्-अर्थ, अस्, m. ‘having the<BR>sense of a root,’ i. e. a verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0452-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुक|धातुकः
धातुक (at the end of comp.) = धातु; bitumen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृ
धातृ, ता, m. one who places or lays, a founder<BR>[cf. Lat. con-ditor], maker, creator, originator,<BR>author; orderer, arranger; bearer, supporter, main-<BR>tainer, preserver; N. of a divine being who is the<BR>creator, arranger, maintainer, and manager of all<BR>things, (strictly perhaps without any distinct and<BR>definite place in the Hindū mythological system, but<BR>rather the personification of the various ideas and<BR>functions inherent in the rt. 1. धा; he is not<BR>mentioned in the older hymns of the Ṛg-veda, but<BR>is invoked in the tenth Maṇḍala, and agrees in many<BR>points with Tvaṣṭṛ and Prajā-pati; he is described<BR>as promoting generation, presiding over matri-<BR>mony and domestic life, preserving health, curing<BR>diseases and broken limbs, granting riches, ordering<BR>times and seasons, &c.; not only is he associated<BR>with Tvaṣṭṛ and Prajā-pati, but with Savitṛ and<BR>Bṛhas-pati; sometimes with Mitra, Viṣṇu, and<BR>Aryaman, and occasionally identified with Prajā-pati:<BR>in one Brāhmaṇa Dhātṛ and Aryaman are declared<BR>to be the first-born children of Aditi: in epic poetry<BR>Dhātṛ is one of the twelve Ādityas, and in post-vedic<BR>mythology the name Dhātṛ is applicable to Prajā-pati<BR>and to Brahmā as ‘creator and maintainer of the<BR>world;’ in the Bhagavad-gītā it is applied to Kṛṣṇa<BR>in the same sense; elsewhere Dhātṛ and Vidhātṛ<BR>are associated as sons of Brahmā, the goddess<BR>Lakṣmī being then their sister, and in another<BR>place as children of Bhṛgu and Khyāti); one of the<BR>seven sages of the fourth Manv-antara; one of the<BR>forty-nine winds; the paramour of a married woman,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">Page0453-b+ 81</a>]<BR>an adulterer; N. of the forty-fourth year in the cycle<BR>of Jupiter.<BR>—धातृ-पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘Brahmā's son,’<BR>especially an epithet of Sanat-kumāra.<BR>—धातृ-<BR>पुष्पिका or धातृ-पुष्पी, f. Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—धातृ-भवन, अम्, n. Brahmā's heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्र|धात्रं
धात्र, अम्, n. a vessel for holding anything, a<BR>receptacle; (अस्, ई, अम्), belonging to Dhātṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्री
धात्री, f. See under 2. धातु, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान|धानं
धान, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of comp.), con-<BR>taining [cf. उद-ध्˚]; (अम्), n. a receptacle, reser-<BR>voir, seat, (at the end of comp., see अग्नि-ध्˚, ऐल-<BR>ध्˚, &c.); (ई), f. a receptacle, anything which holds<BR>or contains, a place where anything is kept, seat, (at<BR>the end of comp., see अङ्गार-ध्˚, खले-ध्˚,<BR>जीव-ध्˚, मत्स्य-ध्˚, &c.); the site of a habit-<BR>ation, N. of a tree (= पीलु); coriander; N. of a<BR>river; (आस्), f. pl. corn, grain; fried barley or rice;<BR>grain fried and reduced to powder; coriander, Cori-<BR>andrum Sativum (= धन्याक); a bud, shoot.<BR>—धाना-चूर्ण, अम्, n. the meal or flour of fried<BR>barley or rice &c.<BR>—धानान्तर्वत् (˚ना-अन्˚), आन्,<BR>m., N. of a Gandharva.<BR>—धाना-पूप, अस्, m. a<BR>cake of fried barley &c.<BR>—धाना-भर्जन, अम्, n.<BR>the frying or parching of grain.<BR>—धाना-मुष्टि,<BR>इस्, f. a handful of grain.<BR>—धाना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. accompanied by grain (as the Soma).<BR>—धाना-<BR>सोम, अस्, m., Ved. Soma with grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानक|धानकं|धानकः
धानक, अम्, n. = धन्याक, coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानाका
धानाका, आस्, f. pl. grain, corn; fried barley or<BR>parched rice; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानी
धानी, f. See under धान above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानेय|धानेयं
धानेय or धानेयक, अम्, n. = धन्याक,<BR>धान्याक, coriander; Coriandrum Sativum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्य|धान्यं
धान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of grain or corn,<BR>made of grain, &c.; (अम्), n. grain, corn in general,<BR>rice (Oryza Sativa); a measure equal to four sesamum-<BR>seeds; coriander; Cyperus Rotundus (= परिपेल);<BR>(आ), f. coriander.<BR>—धान्य-कर्तन, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>cutting of corn,’ N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-<BR>sarva-sva.<BR>—धान्य-कल्क, अम्, n. bran; chaff; straw.<BR>—धान्य-कोष, अस्, m. a granary, storehouse of corn<BR>or rice.<BR>—धान्य-कोष्ठक, अम्, n. a granary, a<BR>basket or cupboard or small shed of matting &c. for<BR>keeping rice, &c.<BR>—धान्य-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>corn-field, rice-field.<BR>—धान्य-चमस, अस्, m. rice<BR>flattened by threshing after it has been steeped and<BR>fried in the husk.<BR>—धान्य-तिल्विल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. abounding in corn.<BR>—धान्य-त्वच्, क्, f. the<BR>husk of corn or rice.<BR>—धान्य-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>giving or distributing rice.<BR>—धान्य-धन, अम्,<BR>n. property in grain; धान्य-धनतस्, on account<BR>of possessing grain &c.<BR>—धान्य-धेनु, उस्, f. a<BR>heap of rice (like a cow) to be presented to Brāh-<BR>mans.<BR>—धान्य-पर्वत-दान-विधि, इस्, m. ‘rules<BR>for giving heaps of grain,’ N. of the 156th chapter<BR>of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR>—धान्य-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, abounding with rice, made of grain.<BR>—धान्य-<BR>मातृ, ता, m. a measurer of corn.<BR>—धान्य-माय,<BR>अस्, m. a corn-chandler, corn-dealer, &c.<BR>—धान्य-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘the prince of grains,’ barley.<BR>—धा-<BR>न्य-रोपण, अम्, n. ‘the planting of corn or rice,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—धान्य-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in grain, rich in corn.<BR>—धान्य-वनि (?), a heap of grain.<BR>—धान्य-<BR>वपन, अम्, n. ‘the sowing of corn or rice,’ N. of<BR>a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—धान्य-वर्-<BR>धन, अम्, n. lending grain at interest, usury with<BR>grain, receiving an usurious return for a load of seed-<BR>corn supplied to peasants.<BR>—धान्य-वीज, अम्, n.<BR>coriander.<BR>—धान्य-वीर, अस्, m. ‘the chief of<BR>grain,’ a sort of pulse, Phaseolus Max. (= माष).<BR>—धान्य-शीर्षक, अम्, n. the ear or spike of<BR>corn.<BR>—धान्य-शूक, अम्, n. the awn or beard of<BR>corn.<BR>—धान्य-शैल-दान, अम्, n. ‘the giving of<BR>a heap of corn or rice,’ N. of the eighty-second<BR>chapter of the Matsya-Purāṇa.<BR>—धान्य-सङ्ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. a store or magazine of grain.<BR>—धान्य-सार,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the essence of grain,’ threshed corn.<BR>—धा-<BR>न्या-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. preparing corn; (Sāy.) a culti-<BR>vator of grain.<BR>—धान्याचल (˚य-अच्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>pile of grain for presentation to Brāhmans.<BR>—धा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">Page0453-c+ 79</a>]<BR>न्याद (˚य-अद), अस्, आ, अम्, eating corn, feeding on<BR>corn.<BR>—धान्याम्ल (˚य-अम्˚), अम्, n. sour gruel<BR>made of the fermentation of rice-water.<BR>—धान्यारि<BR>(˚य-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of corn,’ a mouse, rat.<BR>—धान्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. wealth in rice or<BR>grain.<BR>—धान्यास्थि (˚य-अस्˚), इ, n. ‘the kernel of<BR>grain,’ threshed corn.<BR>—धान्योत्तम (˚य-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the best of grain, rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यक|धान्यकं|धान्यकः
धान्यक (at the end of an adj. comp. for धा-<BR>न्य), grain, corn; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (अम्), n.<BR>= धान्य, धान्याक, धन्याक, coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याक|धान्याकं
धान्याक, अम्, n. = धान्यक, coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाम
धाम, अम्, n. = धामन्, abode, &c.; (आस्), m.,<BR>N. of a class of superhuman beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन्, अ, n. a dwelling-place, house, abode,<BR>home, residence; domain; site, especially the site of<BR>the sacred fire and the Soma; (in the sacrificial<BR>formulas and in the Brāhmaṇas generally with प्रिय,<BR>e. g. प्रियं धाम, favourite residence, also = any<BR>favourite thing or person); the inmates of a house,<BR>the members of a family, domestics; a class; a troop,<BR>host, race; the body; law, rule (Ved.); state or con-<BR>dition; manner, fashion, mode, form, tone (Ved.);<BR>effect, power, strength, ability, faculty; majesty,<BR>dignity, glory, light, splendor, radiance, brilliancy<BR>[cf. ध्यामन्]; (Sāy.) property, wealth; a band,<BR>fetter, (wrong reading for 3. दामन्); (आ), m., N.<BR>of one of the Saptarṣis in the fourth Manv-antara;<BR>[cf. Gr. θέ-μα; Lat. do-mu-s; Osc. faa-ma; Hib.<BR>dai-m, ‘a house, church, people;’ Old Germ. do-m;<BR>Angl. Sax. and Eng. dom = Mod. Germ. thum as<BR>affix of abstract nouns; Slav. do-mŭ.]<BR>—धाम-<BR>केशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘having rays for hair,’ epithet of the<BR>Sun.<BR>—धाम-च्छद्, त्, m., Ved. ‘covering his<BR>residence or changing his abode,’ epithet of Agni as<BR>giver of rain, (also applied to the Vashat-kāra); N.<BR>of a verse in the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā containing the<BR>word धाम-च्छद् (18. 76).<BR>—धाम-धा, आस्,<BR>m., Ved. the causer of order, a creator; (Sāy.) a<BR>bearer, supporter.<BR>—धाम-निधि, इस्, m. ‘treasure<BR>of splendor,’ the sun.<BR>—धाम-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>possessing sites or seats.<BR>—धाम-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, splendid, luminous, eminent, exalted, illustrious,<BR>heroic.<BR>—धाम-शस्, ind., Ved. according to (their)<BR>several abodes, in (their) several places, according to<BR>order.<BR>—धाम-साच्, क्, क्, क्, attached to or keeping a<BR>particular place; (Sāy.) possessing splendor or riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय|धायः
धाय, अस्, आ, अम्, or धायक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>having, possessing, holding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायस्
1. धायस्, अस्, n. sustaining, supporting, bearing.<BR>(For 2. धायस् see p. 454, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायु
1. धायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. liberal; (Sāy.) possessing<BR>power, supporting. (For 2. धायु see p. 454, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय्य|धाय्यः
धाय्य, अस्, m., Ved. a Puro-hita or family<BR>priest?; (आ), f., scil. ऋच्, an additional verse inserted<BR>in certain hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासि|धासिः
1. धासि, इस्, f., Ved. a dwelling-place, seat, home;<BR>(Sāy.) a holder, bearer, maintainer; food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाटी
धाटी धाटी, f. assault, assaulting or con-<BR>fronting an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाणक|धाणकः
धाणक धाणक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. धा), a weight of gold, a gold coin, part of a<BR>Dīnāra [cf. धानक]; (इका), f., Ved. pudendum<BR>muliebre (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातकि
धातकि धातकि, इस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>two sons of Vītihotra Praiyavrata, king of a Varṣa of<BR>Puṣkara-dvīpa; (ई), f. the plant Grislea Tomentosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातु|धातुः
धातु 2. धातु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. धे; for 1.<BR>धातु see p. 452, col. 3), Ved. to be drunk or<BR>sucked in?; (Sāy.) sustainer, supporter, (fr. rt. 1.<BR>धा); (उस्), m. anything to be drunk or sucked,<BR>milk, &c.; (उस्), f. a milch cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रिका
धात्रिका, f. the plant Emblica Officinalis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्री
धात्री, f. a wet-nurse, foster-mother, nurse,<BR>mother; the earth; Emblica Myrobalan, Emblica<BR>Officinalis.<BR>—धात्री-पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of a<BR>nurse, a foster-brother; an actor; (a various reading<BR>for धर्मी-पुत्र.)<BR>—धात्री-फल, अम्, n. the<BR>fruit of the Emblic Myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0453-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रेयिका
धात्रेयिका, f. a foster-sister, (sometimes employed<BR>as a sort of confidante); a nurse, foster-mother, wet-<BR>nurse (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रेयी
धात्रेयी, f. the daughter of a nurse, a foster-<BR>sister, (sometimes employed as a sort of confidante);<BR>a wet-nurse (according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायस्
2. धायस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (for 1. धायस् see p. 453,<BR>col. 3), Ved. nourishing, fostering, sustaining, (often in<BR>comp., e. g. अरि-ध्˚, कारु-ध्˚, गो-ध्˚, भूरि-ध्˚,<BR>&c.); drinking, sipping; the act of fostering, nourish-<BR>ing, satiating, (used only in dat. धायसे in the sense<BR>of an infinitive.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायु
2. धायु, उस्, उस्, उ (for 1. धायु see p. 453,<BR>col. 3), Ved. feeding, eating, fond of eating; (Sāy.)<BR>holding, supporting, (as if fr. rt. 1. धा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारु|धारुः
धारु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. drinking, sucking, a<BR>drinker, sucker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासि|धासिः
2. धासि, इस्, m. (for 1. धासि see p. 453, col. 3), Ved.<BR>a milk-beverage, a drink; nourishment in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धास्यु
धास्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. desirous of drinking or<BR>of eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृ
धातृ धातृ. See p. 453, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्री
धात्री धात्री. See 2. धातु, p. 453, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानक|धानकं|धानकः
धानक धानक, a copper coin worth about<BR>twopence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानद
धानद धानद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धन-द),<BR>relating to Dhana-da, i. e. Kuvera, ‘giver of riches.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुर्दण्डिक|धानुर्दंडिक|धानुर्दंडिकः|धानुर्दण्डिकः
धानुर्दण्डिक धानुर्दण्डिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>धनुस् and दण्ड), living by bow and club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्क|धानुष्कः
धानुष्क धानुष्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धनुस्),<BR>armed with a bow, one who carries a bow, a bowyer,<BR>bowman, archer; (आ), f. the plant Achyranthes Aspera<BR>(= अपामार्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्करि
धानुष्करि, N. of a plant; (probably a wrong<BR>reading for धनुष्करी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्य|धानुष्यः
धानुष्य, अस्, m. ‘suitable for bows,’ a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्त
धान्त धान्त (or ध्वान्त?), a mystical<BR>name of the letter न्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्धा|धांधा
धान्धा धान्धा, f. small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्व
धान्व धान्व, अस्, m. (probably fr. धन्वन्),<BR>a patronymic of Asita, chief of the Asuras; (also read<BR>धान्वन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन
धान्वन 1. धान्वन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धन्-<BR>वन्), situated in a desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन
धान्वन 2. धान्वन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धन्-<BR>वन), made of the wood of the tree Dhanvana<BR>(as bows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन्तर
धान्वन्तर धान्वन्तर, अस्, ई, अम्, or धान्-<BR>वन्तरीय, or धान्वन्तर्य, &c. (fr. धन्वन्-<BR>तरि), relating to or proceeding from Dhanvantari;<BR>sacred to the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वपत
धान्वपत धान्वपत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धन्व-<BR>पति), relating to or proceeding from Dhanva-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामक|धामकः
धामक धामक, अस्, m. a sort of weight<BR>(= माषक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन् धामन्. See p. 453, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनिका
धामनिका धामनिका, f. (fr. धमनी), the<BR>plant Solanum Jacquini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनी
धामनी धामनी, f. the plant Hemionitis<BR>Cordifolia; any tubular vessel of the body; [cf.<BR>धमनी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामार्गव|धामार्गवः|धामार्ग्गव
धामार्गव धामार्गव, अस्, m. a sort of<BR>plant (= घोषक) with white flowers, Luffa Fœtida<BR>or a similar plant; Achyranthes Aspera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार|धारं|धारः
धार धार, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. धृ, but in<BR>some of its senses apparently connected with rt. 1.<BR>धाव्), holding, bearing, supporting, containing, (at<BR>the end of a comp., see असृग्-ध्˚, कर्ण-ध्˚,<BR>जल-ध्˚, तुला-ध्˚); continuing, streaming down in<BR>a continuous line, raining hard, flowing, dripping, (in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-b" target="_blank">Page0454-b+ 81</a>]<BR>these senses said to be connected with rt. 1. धाव्);<BR>(अस्), m. ‘a supporter, holder,’ epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>a sudden and violent shower of rain; snow, hail;<BR>frost (?); a deep place, depth; debt; a boundary,<BR>limit, line; a sort of stone; (आ), f. the flowing or<BR>dropping of any fluid, (said to be connected with rt.<BR>1. धाव्); a stream or current of water, a line of<BR>descending fluid; a water-course, a torrent, a flood, a<BR>hard shower falling in large drops or in hail, a shower,<BR>the dripping of any liquid, a drop, (often at the end<BR>of a comp., cf. असृग्-ध्˚); a leak, a hole in a<BR>pitcher &c. letting out the water; the pace of a<BR>horse (of which five are enumerated, cf. धोरित,<BR>वल्गित, प्लुत, उत्-तेजित, उत्-तेरित); the margin<BR>or border of anything, the sharp edge of a sword or<BR>any cutting instrument, the edge of anything, (often<BR>at the end of a comp.; cf. अर्ध-ध्˚, असि-ध्˚,<BR>क्षुर-ध्˚, खण्ड-ध्˚, खर-ध्˚); the edge of<BR>a mountain or precipice; the circumference or peri-<BR>phery of a wheel; a garden-wall, fence, hedge; any<BR>continuous line or series, the line of a family; the<BR>van or front line of an army [cf. धाराङ्कुर];<BR>the tip of the ear, ear-lap; the highest point, excel-<BR>lence, pre-eminence; a multitude; fame; night; tur-<BR>meric; likeness; custom, usage (?); N. of a town;<BR>of a sacred bathing-place; (अम्), n. rain-water (?).<BR>—धार-पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. purified with streams<BR>of water; clear as water (?).<BR>—धार-वाक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. (Sāy.) sustaining or reciting praises.<BR>—धारा-कदम्ब or धारा-कदम्बक, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of Kadamba tree; N. of a poet.<BR>—धारा-<BR>गृह, अम्, n. a bath-room with flowing water, shower-<BR>bath.<BR>—धाराग्र (˚रा-अग्˚), अम्, n. the broad-<BR>edged head of an arrow.<BR>—धाराङ्कुर (˚रा-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a drop of rain; hail; advancing before the<BR>line of an army to defy the enemy.<BR>—धाराङ्ग (˚रा-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. a sacred bathing-place; a sword, scimitar.<BR>—धाराट (˚रा-अट), अस्, m. the Cātaka bird; a<BR>horse; a cloud; a furious elephant or one in rut<BR>(when juice exudes from his temples).<BR>—धारा-<BR>धर, अस्, m. ‘containing showers,’ a cloud; ‘hav-<BR>ing an edge,’ a sword.<BR>—धाराधिरूढ (˚रा-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, elevated to the highest point,<BR>raised to the highest pitch.<BR>—धारा-ध्वनि, इस्, m.<BR>the sound of falling rain or flowing water.<BR>—धारा-<BR>निपात or धारा-पात, अस्, m. a fall of rain, pelting<BR>shower; a stream of water.<BR>—धारान्तर-चर (˚रा-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, moving among the showers; flying<BR>amid the clouds (as the Cātaka bird).<BR>—धारा-फल,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a tree with prickly fruits (= मदन).<BR>—धारा-यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘machine for sprinkling<BR>water,’ a fountain; a watering-can, a sprinkling vase<BR>or ewer, a sort of censer.<BR>—धारा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having an edge, edged; (अती), f., N. of a town.<BR>—धारा-वनि, इस्, m. wind, air.<BR>—धारा-वर,<BR>आस्, m. pl. ‘fond of showers,’ epithet of the Maruts;<BR>(Sāy.) covering (the sky) with showers or preventing<BR>the stability of stationary objects, i. e. moving them.<BR>—धारा-वर्ष, अस्, अम्, m. n. a stream or torrent<BR>of rain, a hard shower.<BR>—धारा-विष, अस्, m.<BR>‘having a poisoned edge,’ a crooked sword, a scimitar,<BR>sabre.<BR>—धाराश्रु (˚रा-अश्˚), उ, n. a flood of tears.<BR>—धारा-सम्पात, अस्, m. a hard shower, a heavy<BR>fall of rain.<BR>—धारासार (˚रा-आस्˚), अस्, m. a heavy<BR>downfall of rain, a hard shower.<BR>—धारा-स्नुही, f.,<BR>N. of a plant (= त्रिधार-स्नुही).<BR>—धारोष्ण<BR>(˚रा-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, warm from the cow (as milk).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारक|धारकः
धारक, अस्, आ, अम्, holding, containing, pos-<BR>sessing, bearing, carrying, (at the end of a comp.,<BR>see कुल-ध्˚, देह-ध्˚, नाम-ध्˚); (अस्), m. a<BR>receptacle or vessel of any kind, a trunk or box (for<BR>holding clothes &c.), a water-pot; (आ), f. the vulva<BR>of a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारण|धारणं
धारण, अस्, ई, अम्, holding, bearing, carrying.<BR>keeping, sustaining, preserving, maintaining, protect-<BR>ing; possessing, having, assuming; keeping in re-<BR>membrance; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Kaśyapa; of<BR>a prince of the Candra-vatsas; (औ), m. du. the two<BR>female breasts; (आ), f. the act of holding, supporting,<BR>bearing, maintaining, preserving, keeping, holding<BR>fast, keeping back; keeping in remembrance, retain-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">Page0454-c+ 81</a>]<BR>ing in the mind, a good memory; memory; keeping<BR>the mind collected, holding the breath suspended<BR>and all the natural wants restrained; steady or im-<BR>movable abstraction of mind; fortitude, firmness,<BR>steadiness, resolution; continuance in rectitude, keep-<BR>ing in the right way; fixed precept or injunction, a<BR>settled rule, certainty, conclusion; understanding, in-<BR>tellect; conviction; (आस्), f. pl. the four days fol-<BR>lowing the eighth day in the light half of month<BR>Jyaiṣṭha; (ई), f. any tubular vessel of the body; a<BR>mystical verse or charm or collection of such verses<BR>among the Buddhists; a row or line, (wrong reading<BR>for धोरणी); N. of a daughter of Svadhā [cf. धा-<BR>रिणी]; (अम्), n. the act of holding, bearing, uphold-<BR>ing, supporting, sustaining; possessing, possession;<BR>containing; keeping, maintaining; observing, hold-<BR>ing fast; keeping in the memory; immovable ab-<BR>straction of the mind; restraining; (in grammar)<BR>keeping back, i. e. pronouncing imperfectly; [cf.<BR>अङ्क-ध्˚, असु-ध्˚, गर्भ-ध्˚, छत्त्र-ध्˚,<BR>दण्ड-ध्˚, देह-ध्˚, &c.]<BR>—धारण-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. a receptacle for the sieve (?) of a Buddhist<BR>mendicant; a vessel for holding anything.<BR>—धा-<BR>रण-यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of certain amulets.<BR>—धा-<BR>रणा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, depending on or connected<BR>with abstraction of the mind.<BR>—धारणा-योग, अस्,<BR>m. deep devotion.<BR>—धारणा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessing memory, connected with memory.<BR>—धा-<BR>रणी-मति, इस्, m. (?), N. of a Samādhi.<BR>—धारणी-<BR>मुख-सर्व-जगत्-प्रणिधि-सन्धारण-गर्-<BR>भ, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—धारणी-<BR>राज, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणक|धारणकः
धारणक, अस्, आ, अम्, holding, containing; (अस्),<BR>m. a debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणीय
धारणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be held or retained,<BR>to be maintained, borne, sustained, possessed, &c.;<BR>to be adhered to; (आ), f. = धरणी-कन्द, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारय|धारयः
धारय, अस्, आ, अम्, holding, possessing, having,<BR>keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयत्
धारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, having, possessing; hold-<BR>ing as doctrine, believing, maintaining, asserting, pro-<BR>fessing; acquainted with, versed in.<BR>—धारयत्-<BR>कवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. supporting or cherishing sages;<BR>(Sāy.) supporting or bearing water.<BR>—धारयत्-<BR>क्षिति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. bearing or sustaining creatures;<BR>(Sāy.) one who has prepared ground (for an altar).<BR>—धारयद्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. ‘possessing the<BR>quality of sustaining or supporting,’ an epithet of<BR>the Ādityas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयाण
धारयाण, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing, holding, sup-<BR>porting, containing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयितव्य
धारयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne, to be<BR>kept or retained; to be perceived or understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयितृ
धारयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a holder, bearer; holding,<BR>keeping, keeping back, restraining; (ई), f. = धरि-<BR>त्री, the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयिष्णु
धारयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, capable of holding,<BR>bearing, maintaining, sustaining.<BR>—धारयिष्णु-ता,<BR>f. capability of bearing or supporting, patience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयु
धारयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. flowing, streaming,<BR>dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारा
धारा, f. See under धार, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारि
धारि, इस्, इस्, इ, holding, maintaining, carrying,<BR>bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिका
धारिका, f. a division of time, = 6 Kṣaṇas, =<BR>(1/2) Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारित
धारित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), borne, sup-<BR>ported, maintained; (अम्), n. a horse's trot; (wrong<BR>reading for धोरित, धौरितक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, carrying, bearing, wearing, hav-<BR>ing, holding, keeping, possessing; sustaining, main-<BR>taining, preserving, keeping in one's memory, ob-<BR>serving [cf. जटा-ध्˚, दण्ड-ध्˚, धनुर्-ध्˚];<BR>having an edge, edged; (ई), m., N. of a tree [cf.<BR>पीलु]; (इणी), f. the earth; Bombax Heptaphyllum<BR>(= शाल्मली); N. of a daughter of Svadhā [cf. धा-<BR>रणी]; (इण्यस्), f. pl. a collective N. of the seventy-four<BR>wives of the gods; (with Jainas) N. of a deity who<BR>executes the commands of the eighteenth Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī; N. of the wife of Agni-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य|धार्य्य|धार्य्यं
धार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be held or maintained,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">Page0455-a+ 77</a>]<BR>to be borne or carried, bearable; to be imposed (as<BR>a punishment); to be worn; to be suffered, support-<BR>able; to be upheld or preserved; to be contained;<BR>to be kept or detained; to be kept in the memory;<BR>to be directed steadily towards; to be kept back or<BR>restrained [cf. अ-धार्य and दुर्-ध्˚]; (अस् or अम्),<BR>m. or n. (?), Ved. water; (अम्), n. clothes, garments.<BR>—धार्य-त्व, अम्, n. the being held or borne or<BR>worn; capability or fitness for the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0454-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्यमाण|धार्य्यमाण
धार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being held, borne,<BR>maintained, &c.<BR>—धार्यमाण-त्व, अम्, n. pos-<BR>sessions, property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्तराष्ट्र धार्तराष्ट्र, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging<BR>to Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; (अस्), m. a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra,<BR>especially a patronymic of Dur-yodhana who was his<BR>eldest son; a kind of snake [cf. धृत-राष्ट्र];<BR>(fr. धृत-राष्ट्री), a sort of goose with black legs<BR>and bill.<BR>—धार्तराष्ट्र-पदी, f., N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तराष्ट्रि
धार्तराष्ट्रि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तेय
धार्तेय धार्तेय, आस्, m. pl. (perhaps fr.<BR>धृत), N. of a warlike tribe; (अस्), m. a prince of<BR>this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म|धार्म्म
धार्म धार्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धर्म), relat-<BR>ing to justice or virtue, belonging to Dharma or the<BR>god of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मपत|धार्म्मपत
धार्मपत, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Dharma-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मपत्तन|धार्म्मपत्तन
धार्मपत्तन, अम्, n. (fr. धर्म-पत्तन),<BR>black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मविद्य
धार्मविद्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. धर्म-विद्या),<BR>knowing the law, familiar with it, a lawyer, a jurist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिक|धार्म्मिकः
धार्मिक, अस्, ई, अम्, righteous, just, fulfilling<BR>or performing duties, virtuous, religious, pious; rest-<BR>ing on right, conformable to justice.<BR>—धार्मिक-ता,<BR>f. or धार्मिक-त्व or धार्मिक्य, अम्, n. righteous-<BR>ness, justice, virtuousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिण|धार्मिणं
धार्मिण, अम्, n. an assemblage of virtuous men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिणेय
धार्मिणेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Dhar-<BR>miṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म्यायण
धार्म्यायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Dharmya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट
धार्ष्ट धार्ष्ट, अस्, ई, अम्, or धार्ष्टिक, अस्,<BR>ई, अम् (fr. धृष्ट, rt. धृष्), proceeding or<BR>descended from Dhṛṣṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्टद्युम्न
धार्ष्टद्युम्न, अस्, m. or धार्ष्टद्युम्नि,<BR>इस्, m. a patronymic from Dhṛṣṭa-dyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट्य|धार्ष्ट्यं
धार्ष्ट्य, अम्, n. violence, boldness, daringness,<BR>audacity, arrogance, impudence, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्णक
धार्ष्णक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धृष्णु), descended<BR>from Dhṛṣṇu; (the more correct form would be<BR>धार्ष्णव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
धाव् 1. धाव् (connected with rts. धव्<BR>and धन्व्), cl. 1. P. and sometimes<BR>A. धावति, -ते, दधाव, -ए, धाविष्यति, -ते,<BR>अधावीत्, अधाविष्ट, धावितुम्, to flow, stream or<BR>flow forth, flow towards; to give milk (as a cow);<BR>to run, proceed quickly, advance, run away, run<BR>towards, advance against; to rush against, assault;<BR>run a race; run away, flee; to go, move, glide:<BR>Caus. धावयति, &c., Aor. अदीधवत्, to cause to<BR>run, make run, drive, impel, push on; धावयति<BR>रथेन, he drives in a chariot: Desid. दिधावि-<BR>षति, -ते: Intens. दाधाव्यते: [cf. Gr. θέ-ω, θεύ-σομαι,<BR>θο-ό-ς, θοάζ-ω, βοη-θό-ος; Hib. deifir, ‘haste.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
1. धावक, अस्, आ, अम्, running, flowing, going<BR>quickly, running in advance, expeditious; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of an author in the pay of king Śrī-harṣa; (also<BR>read भासक; he is said to have composed the<BR>Ratnāvalī for Śrī-harṣa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावत्|धावन्त्
धावत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, running, going quickly,<BR>running away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावन|धावनं
1. धावन, अम्, n. running, galloping, flowing,<BR>moving; attack, assault; (अस्), m., N. of a spell for<BR>using or restraining magical weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावमान
धावमान, अस्, आ, अम्, running, going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावित|धावितः
1. धावित, अस्, आ, अम्, running, running off or<BR>away; running towards, advanced against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावितृ
धावितृ, ता, m. a runner; running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाविन्
धाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, running, going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
धाव् 2. धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. धावति, -ते,<BR>दधाव, -ए, धाविष्यति, -ते, अधावीत्,<BR>अधाविष्ट, धावितुम्, to rub, rub off, cleanse,<BR>clean, wash, purify, polish, brighten, make pure or<BR>bright; A. to rub one's self with anything, to rub into<BR>one's person: Caus. धावयति, &c., Aor. अदी-<BR>धवत्, to cleanse, wash: Desid. दिधाविषति, -ते:<BR>Intens. दाधाव्यते; [cf. probably Goth. daupya<BR>= Old Sax. dopyu = Mod. Germ. taufe, ‘I baptize,’<BR>= Caus. धावयामि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव
धाव, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansing, washing, making<BR>bright, polishing, (at the end of an adj. comp.; cf.<BR>चैल-ध्˚ and असि-ध्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक, अस्, आ, अम्, washing, cleansing; (अस्),<BR>m. a washerman, a dhobī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावन|धावनं
2. धावन, अम्, n. rubbing off, washing off, cleans-<BR>ing, purifying; rubbing with anything, (in comp.,<BR>e. g. मीन-धावन-तोय, मनःशिला-चन्दन-<BR>ध्˚, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावनि|धावनिः
धावनि, इस्, ई, f. a sort of creeping plant, Hedy-<BR>sarum Lagopodioides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावनिका
धावनिका, f. a kind of prickly nightshade, =<BR>कण्ट-कारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावित|धावितः
2. धावित, अस्, आ, अम्, purified, cleansed, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed, &c. See p. 460,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावल्य|धावल्यं
धावल्य धावल्य, अम्, n. (fr. धवल),<BR>whiteness, white (the colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासस्
धासस् धासस्, आस्, m., Ved. a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि 1. धि (allied to rt. 1. धा), cl. 6. P.<BR>धियति, दिधाय, धेष्यति, अधैषीत्,<BR>धेतुम्, to have, hold, keep, possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
2. धि, इस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. धा), what holds, con-<BR>tains or preserves; any receptacle, (only at the end<BR>of a comp., e. g. अम्बु-धि, अम्भो-धि, इषु-धि,<BR>उत्स-धि, उद-धि, जल-धि, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धित
1. धित, अस्, आ, अम् (earlier form of हित fr. rt.<BR>1. धा), put, placed, arranged, given, caused; re-<BR>solved; [cf. दुर्-ध्˚ and नेम-ध्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धितावन्
धितावन्, आ, m., Ved. abounding in gifts (?).<BR>(According to Sāy. Ṛg-veda III. 27, 2, धितावा-<BR>नम् = धित-वानम् = निहित-धनम्, laying up<BR>or granting wealth; III. 40, 3, = निहित-हविष्कम्,<BR>[a sacrifice] in which oblations are offered.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिति
धिति in नेम-ध्˚, मित्र-ध्˚, &c., q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि 3. धि or धिन्व्, cl. 5. P. धिनोति, दि-<BR>धिन्व, धिन्वितुम्, to satisfy (Ved.); to<BR>delight, please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धित
2. धित, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि 4. धि sometimes = 2. अधि, as पि = अपि<BR>and व = अव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् धिक्, ind. (said to be connected with<BR>rt. 1. दिह्), an interjection of reproach, menace or<BR>displeasure, = fie! shame! out upon! what a pity!<BR>&c.; (generally followed by the acc., sometimes by<BR>the nom. or voc., and rarely by the gen., e. g. धिक्<BR>त्वाम्, shame upon thee! धिग् इयम् दरिद्रता,<BR>shame upon this poverty!)<BR>—धिक्-पारुष्य, अम्,<BR>n. abuse, reproach, excessive reviling.<BR>—धिग्-दण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. reprimand, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृ
धिक्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to reproach,<BR>censure, reprimand, curse (with acc.).<BR>—धिक्-कार,<BR>अस्, m. or धिक्-क्रिया, f. reproach, contempt, cen-<BR>sure, disrespect.<BR>—धिक्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, reproached,<BR>reviled, censured, condemned, cursed; (अम्), n. a<BR>reproach, contempt, curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष्
धिक्ष् धिक्ष् (perhaps a Desid. form of<BR>rt. 1. दह्, cf. rt. धुक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>धिक्षते, &c., to kindle; to live; to be weary or<BR>harassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वण|धिग्वणः
धिग्वण धिग्वण, अस्, m. (perhaps a Prā-<BR>kṛt form of धिक्-वर्ण), a man of a low or mixed<BR>caste, sprung from a Brāhman and a female of the<BR>tribe called Āyogava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धित्स्य
धित्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be wished to be placed,<BR>&c.; desirable to be given or created, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धित
धित 1. and 2. धित. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिन्व्
धिन्व् धिन्व्. See rt. 3. धि, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु धिप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>दम्भ्), wishing to trick or deceive, deceptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियञ्जिन्व|धियंजिन्व
धियञ्जिन्व धियञ्-जिन्व, धियाय, धिया-<BR>वसु. See p. 456, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
धिष् 1. धिष् (thought by some to be<BR>an abbreviated form of a Vedic Desid.<BR>दिधिष् derived fr. rt. 1. धा; connected with rt. 1.<BR>धी), cl. 3. P. दिधेष्टि, &c., to sound, emit a<BR>sound; to praise, celebrate by hymns (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
2. धिष्, f. (only occurring in inst. धिषा and<BR>probably connected with rt. 1. धी), fixing the mind,<BR>attention (?), intelligence (?), devotion; (Sāy.) = धि-<BR>षणा, knowledge, understanding; action; praise,<BR>hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
धिषण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. धिष् substi-<BR>tuted for rt. धृष्), ‘the intelligent one,’ N. of<BR>Bṛhas-pati, preceptor of the gods and regent of the<BR>planet Jupiter, the planet Jupiter itself [cf. धिष-<BR>णाधिप and धी-मत्]; any Guru or spiritual pre-<BR>ceptor; epithet of a Nārāyaṇa; N. of an astronomer;<BR>of an evil spirit or demon; (आ), f. a sort of Soma-<BR>vessel, a cup, goblet, bowl; a Soma press; (accord-<BR>ing to some commentators) the Soma juice itself and<BR>its effects; (metaphorically धिषणे, f. du. the two<BR>cups or bowls, i. e. the two worlds or heaven and<BR>earth; and धिषणास्, f. pl. the three worlds or<BR>heaven, earth, and the intermediate atmosphere); a<BR>female divinity presiding over prosperity and gain,<BR>(sometimes reckoned among the wives of the gods);<BR>= वाच्, speech, praise, hymn; = 2. धी, intelligence,<BR>intellect, understanding, knowledge; N. of the wife<BR>of Havir-dhāna, daughter of Agni; of the wife of<BR>Kṛśāśva and mother of Veda-śira, Devala, Vayuna,<BR>and Manu; (अम्), n. a dwelling-place, abode, seat,<BR>site, resting-place [cf. धिष्ण्य]; understanding,<BR>intellect.<BR>—धिषणाधिप, अस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>planet Jupiter,’ epithet of Bṛhas-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण्य
धिषण्य, an adj. formed by Yāska (Nir. VIII.<BR>3) to explain धिष्ण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण्यत्
धिषण्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. a Nom. धिषण्य<BR>which only occurs in the part.), attentive, devout (?);<BR>(Sāy.) desiring to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ट्य|धिष्ट्यं|धिष्ट्यः
धिष्ट्य, अस्, आ, अम्, placed on a fire-altar (?);<BR>(wrong reading for धिष्ण्य, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठ्य
धिष्ठ्य, अम्, n. site, seat, place, (wrong reading<BR>for धिष्ण्य, q. v.); (अस्), m. fire; the planet<BR>Venus (?).<BR>—धिष्ठ्य-प, अस्, m. world-protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्णिय
धिष्णिय for धिष्ण्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्णीय
धिष्णीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. intended for or<BR>belonging to the Dhiṣṇyas, i. e. certain receptacles<BR>or places for fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. only perceptible by<BR>the mind; (Sāy. = धार्ष्ट्य-युक्त), endowed with<BR>fortitude; intelligent, thoughtful, devout, pious;<BR>(Sāy.) to be praised or meditated upon; worthy of a<BR>high station; placed upon the heaps of earth used<BR>for side-altars; see below. In Ṛg-veda III. 22, 3,<BR>Sāy. explains धिष्ण्या by प्राणास् = the divinities<BR>presiding over the vital airs; (अस्), m. a place for<BR>the sacrificial fire, a sort of inferior or side-altar,<BR>(generally a heap of earth covered with sand on which<BR>the fire is placed, and of which eight are enumerated,<BR>cf. आग्नीध्रीय, मार्जालीय, &c.); an epithet of<BR>Uśanas, the planet Venus; power, strength; (अम्),<BR>n. a site, seat, place, abode, spot, region, house; a<BR>star, asterism, (looking like the fire on the side-altars);<BR>a meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी 1. धी (sometimes given in the redu-<BR>plicated form दीधी; the later forms of धी<BR>are 1. धा, ध्या, ध्यै, q. v., with which such<BR>Vedic forms as धीमहि are connected by native<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">Page0456-a+ 79</a>]<BR>commentators), cl. 2. A. दीधीते, &c., to shine,<BR>appear (see दीधी); cl. 1. P. (fr. rt. ध्यै), ध्या-<BR>यति, &c. (see ध्यै), to perceive, think, reflect;<BR>to wish, desire. (A root धी, cl. 4. A. धीयते,<BR>&c., which is properly Pass. of rt. 1. धा, is given<BR>in the Dhātu-pāṭha and is said to have the following<BR>senses, — to contain, hold; to slight, disregard; to<BR>accomplish; to propitiate.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0455-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियसान
धियसान, अस्, आ, अम्, reflecting, meditating<BR>upon, fixing the mind upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियाय
धियाय (fr. 2. धी), Nom. A. धियायते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to fix the mind upon; to be devout, practise<BR>devotion; (Sāy.) to wish for praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियाय
धियाय, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the preceding), Ved. reflect-<BR>ing, devout, pious; (Sāy.) wishing to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
2. धी, ईस्, f. thought, idea, notion, intention;<BR>understanding, wisdom, intellect, intelligence, intel-<BR>lectual power, mind; knowledge, science, art; reli-<BR>gious reflection, devotion, prayer; a religious rite,<BR>sacrifice; Intelligence personified (as the wife of Rudra<BR>in the form Manyu); (in astrology) the fifth house<BR>from the Lagna; (इयस्), f. pl. Holy Thoughts per-<BR>sonified; [cf. इत्था-धी, उदार-धी, दुर्-धी, दू-<BR>ढी, सु-धी, &c.]<BR>—धियञ्-जिन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>exciting pious reflection or promoting devotion;<BR>(Sāy.) to be propitiated by pious rites; (आ), m. du.<BR>epithet of the Aśvins.<BR>—धियन्-धा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. reflecting, devout, pious, wise; (Sāy.) celebrating<BR>sacred rites.<BR>—धिया-जुर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, Ved. worn<BR>out or grown old in the performance of religious<BR>duties.<BR>—धियाम्-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the thoughts,’<BR>the soul; an epithet of Mañju-ghoṣa.<BR>—धिया-<BR>वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. abounding in devotion, very<BR>devout; (Sāy.) recompensing religious rites by wealth.<BR>—धी-जवन, अस्, आ, अम्, or धी-जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ,<BR>Ved. infusing spirit, inspiring; (Sāy.) rapid as thought.<BR>—धीन्द्रिय (धी-इन्˚), अस्, m. an organ of per-<BR>ception (= बुद्धीन्द्रिय and opposed to कर्मेन्-<BR>द्रिय, see इन्द्रिय).<BR>—धी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessed of understanding, endowed with intelligence,<BR>intellectual, intelligent, wise, learned, sensible; (आन्),<BR>m. an epithet of Bṛhas-pati, preceptor of the gods;<BR>N. of a son of Virāj; of a son of Purū-ravas.<BR>—धी-<BR>मन्त्रिन्, ई, m. a minister for counsel (as distinguished<BR>fr. कर्म-मन्त्रिन्, a minister for action).<BR>—धी-<BR>मरण, अस्, m. (with preceding मिश्र), N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—धी-रण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. delighting in<BR>devotion; (Sāy.) whose speech is with praise, a<BR>devout worshipper.<BR>—धी-राज, अस्, m., N. of one of<BR>the attendants of Śiva.<BR>—धी-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>intelligent, pious, religious.<BR>—धी-शक्ति, इस्, f. power<BR>of the mind, mental or intellectual faculty (as atten-<BR>tion, comprehension, &c.).<BR>—धी-सख, अस्, m. a<BR>wise counsellor, an adviser, mentor, minister; a tutor<BR>or friendly adviser.<BR>—धी-सचिव, अस्, m. a minister<BR>for counsel, a counsellor, minister; a wise or prudent<BR>adviser.<BR>—धी-हरा, f. a kind of sweet gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
1. धीत, अस्, आ, अम्, reflected on, thought about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीति|धीतिः
1. धीति, इस्, f. (for 2. धीति see col. 2), Ved.<BR>thought, notion, reflection, idea; devotion, prayer;<BR>(अयस्), f. pl. understanding, wisdom; (Sāy.) the<BR>fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीतिक
धीतिक, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist patriarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
1. धीदा, f. (for 2. धीदा see col. 2), understand-<BR>ing, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवन्
धीवन्, आ, वरी, अ, Ved. clever, skilful; (आ),<BR>m. an artizan, artificer, a worker in brass; a fisher-<BR>man; [cf. the next.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर, अस्, m. a fisherman, fisher; (ई), f. a<BR>fisherman's wife; a sort of harpoon for catching fish;<BR>a receptacle for fish, a fish-basket; (अम्), n. iron;<BR>[cf. तीव्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरक|धीवरकः
धीवरक, अस्, m. a fisherman, fisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीक्ष्
धीक्ष् धीक्ष् (perhaps Desid. of rt. 1.<BR>दिह्), cl. 1. A. धीक्षते, &c., Ved. to<BR>wish to anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत 2. धीत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. धे), drunk,<BR>sucked, sucked in, sucked out.<BR>—धीत-रस, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the juice sucked out or extracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीति|धीतिः
2. धीति, इस्, f. (for 1. धीति see col. 1), drink-<BR>ing; (according to the commentators), thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
धीदा 2. धीदा, f. (probably a Prākṛt form<BR>for दुहिता), a daughter, a virgin, a maiden. (For<BR>1. धीदा see col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीन
धीन धीन, अम्, n. iron (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर धीर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. धृ, but said<BR>to be fr. rt. 1. धा and certainly connected with<BR>this latter rt.), steady, holding firmly, steadfast, en-<BR>during, durable, lasting, constant, continual; firm,<BR>determined, resolute, persevering, persistent; strong,<BR>energetic, courageous; brave, bold, daring, head-<BR>strong, self-controlled, strong-minded, self-possessed,<BR>composed, calm, collected; sedate, grave, solemn,<BR>sober; deep, grave, hollow, low, dull (as sound);<BR>emitting a long or prolonged sound; lazy, dull,<BR>slow; gentle, soft (as a breeze); well-conducted,<BR>well-behaved, well-bred; (fr. 1. धा = 1. धी), in-<BR>telligent, wise, prudent; sensible, learned, skilful,<BR>clever, shrewd; (अस्), m. the ocean, sea; ‘the wise<BR>one,’ epithet of a Buddha; of Bali; of several men;<BR>a species of medicinal plant, = ऋषभ; (आ), f. a<BR>woman who, although jealous of a husband or lover,<BR>suppresses all expression of resentment in his pre-<BR>sence; an intoxicating beverage; N. of several medi-<BR>cinal plants, = काकोली, = महा-ज्योतिष्मती, = क्षी-<BR>र-काकोली, श्वेत-वचा, मेदा, Rosa Glandulifera;<BR>(अम्), n. saffron; (अम्), ind. firmly, steadily,<BR>resolutely, steadfastly.<BR>—धीर-गोविन्द-शर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of the author of the modern work Āthar-<BR>vaṇa-rahasya.<BR>—धीर-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, strong-<BR>minded, self-possessed, courageous.<BR>—धीर-ता, f. or<BR>धीर-त्व, अम्, n. firmness, fortitude, energy, courage;<BR>suppression; the female property of suppressing<BR>violent expression of jealousy; refusal.<BR>—धीर-<BR>ध्वनि, इस्, m. a deep sound.<BR>—धीर-पत्त्री, f. a<BR>kind of bulbous plant (= धरणी-कन्द).<BR>—धीर-<BR>प्रशंसा, f. ‘the praise of the firm or of the wise,’<BR>N. of the thirteenth chapter of the Śārṅgadhara-<BR>paddhati.<BR>—धीर-प्रशान्त, अस्, m. the hero of a<BR>poem or play who is both brave and calm or mild (?).<BR>—धीर-ललित, अस्, m. the hero of a poem or play<BR>who is firm and brave but reckless and sportive at<BR>the same time; (आ), f., N. of a metre consisting of<BR>four lines of sixteen syllables each.<BR>—धीर-स्कन्-<BR>ध, अस्, m. ‘strong-shouldered,’ a buffalo.<BR>—धीरा-<BR>धीरा (˚र-अध्˚), f. a mistress or wife who having<BR>cause for jealousy pursues a middle course between<BR>suppression and expression of resentment, a jealous<BR>woman who alternately expresses and conceals her<BR>jealousy.<BR>—धीरेश-मिश्र (˚र-ईश-म्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—धीरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of the<BR>father of Jyotir-īśvara, author of the Dhūrta-samā-<BR>gama.<BR>—धीरोदात्त (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m. the hero of<BR>a poem or play who is brave and noble-minded.<BR>—धीरोद्धत (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m. the hero of a<BR>poem or play who is brave but haughty.<BR>—धीरोष्-<BR>णिन् (˚र-उष्˚), ई, m., N. of one of the Viśve-devās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरावी
धीरावी, f., N. of a plant (= पीतशिंशपा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर्य|धीर्य्य
धीर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. धा = 1. धी), Ved.<BR>intelligent, wise, clever; (अम्), n. intelligence, pru-<BR>dence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटी
धीलटी धीलटी, f. (probably a Prākṛt<BR>form for दुहितृ), a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर धीवर. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु 1. धु = rt. 1. धू, to shake, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
2. धु, उस्, f. shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, agitated, moved<BR>quickly to and fro; abandoned, deserted, left.<BR>—धुत-पाप, अस्, आ, अम्, purified from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन
धुन, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनन
धुनन, अम्, n. shaking, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनान
धुनान, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनि, इस्, इस्, इ. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वत्|धुन्वन्त्
धुन्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वान
धुन्वान, अस्, आ, अम्, shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवन|धुवनः
धुवन, अस्, m., Ved. fire; (अम्), n. shaking,<BR>agitation; place of execution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवित्र|धुवित्रं
धुवित्र, अम्, n. a sort of fan (made of deer-skin<BR>and especially used to kindle or excite a sacrificial<BR>fire); [cf. धवित्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक
धुक धुक, अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of plant<BR>(commonly Bhuyabora or Rānabora, बोर = बदर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष्
धुक्ष् धुक्ष्, cl. 1. A. धुक्षते, &c., to<BR>kindle; to be weary; to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुङ्क्षा
धुङ्क्षा धुङ्क्षा, f., Ved. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन
धुन धुन, अस्, आ, अम् (variously derived fr.<BR>rt. 2. ध्वन् or rt. 1. धु), Ved. sounding, roaring;<BR>shaking, agitating, (only in comp.)<BR>—धुनेति (˚न-<BR>इति), इस्, इस्, इ, having a roaring or blustering course;<BR>having an agitating or destructive course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनय
धुनय (fr. धुनि below), Nom. P. A. धुन-<BR>यति, -ते, &c., Ved. to sound, roar, to flow with a<BR>roaring noise; to flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. sounding, roaring, blustering;<BR>(Sāy.) shaking, agitating, causing to tremble, (fr. rt.<BR>1. धु); (इस्), m. epithet of the Soma; N. of a<BR>demon slain by Indra; (इस् or धुनी), f. a river [cf.<BR>नदी]; (अयस्), m. pl. ‘the agitators,’ an epithet of<BR>the Maruts.<BR>—धुनि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. roaring,<BR>sounding; (Sāy.) agitated, trembling.<BR>—धुनि-<BR>व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. habitually roaring or bluster-<BR>ing; (Sāy.) whose function is the agitation or shaking<BR>(of trees &c.).<BR>—धुनी-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>rivers,’ the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धु
धुन्धु धुन्धु, उस्, m., N. of an Asura slain<BR>by Kuvalāśva (or Kuvalayāśva), father of Sunda; (a<BR>various reading for चुञ्चु who was a descendant of<BR>Tri-śaṅku.)<BR>—धुन्धु-मार, अस्, m. ‘the slayer<BR>of Dhundhu,’ epithet of Kuvalāśva (Kuvalayāśva), a<BR>son of Tri-śaṅku and father of Yuvanāśva; a house-<BR>lizard (? = गृहालिक); an insect, coccinella (=<BR>इन्द्र-गोप, शक्र-गोप); a kind of plant (=<BR>गृह-धूम); the smoke of a house (?), cf.<BR>दुन्दु-मार.<BR>—धुन्धुमारोपाख्यान (˚र-<BR>उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘the episode of Dhundhu-māra,’ N. of<BR>the seventeenth chapter of the Svarga-khaṇḍa or<BR>third part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् धुर्, ऊर्, f. (fr. rt. धृ?, in Mahā-bh.<BR>Anuśāsana-p. 2876. धुर् is masc.), that part of a<BR>yoke which rests on the shoulder; a yoke; a bur-<BR>den, load (literally and metaphorically); the peg or<BR>pin at both ends of an axle for fastening the nave<BR>of the wheel; the foremost part of the pole, where<BR>the yoke is fixed; the pole itself, the shaft, the fore-<BR>most or highest place, the top, the place of honour;<BR>a finger; N. of six verses of the Bahish-pavamāna<BR>which are to be sung in a peculiar manner; (some<BR>lexicographers add the following meanings) agitation,<BR>trembling; reflection, recollection; a spark of fire; a<BR>part, a portion; wealth; a N. of the Ganges; धुरि,<BR>ind. at the head of, = अग्रे; [cf. धूर्, दुर्-धुर्,<BR>दृढ-धुर्.]<BR>—धुरन्-धर, अस्, ई, अम्, bear-<BR>ing the yoke, bearing a burden, fit to be harnessed;<BR>bearing a burden with patience, (figuratively) laden<BR>with good qualities or with weighty duties, &c.; (अस्),<BR>m. a beast of burden; a man of business; a chief,<BR>leader; an epithet of Śiva; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; N. of a Rakṣas; the tree Grislea Tomen-<BR>tosa.<BR>—धुर्-गत, धुर्-वह, धुर्-वोढृ, incor-<BR>rect forms for धूर्-गत, धूर्-वह, धूर्-वोढृ;<BR>see under 2. धूर्, p. 458, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर|धुरः
धुर, अस्, m. at end of comp. = धुर्, a yoke,<BR>pole; burden; pin at the end of an axle &c.; (1.<BR>धुरा), f. a burden, load.<BR>—धुरा-वह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, bearing a burden (= धूर्-वह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be harnessed; bearing<BR>a burden or able to bear one, laden with, abounding<BR>with (qualities, duties, &c.); (अस्), m. a beast of<BR>burden; a man of business; a leader, chief; [cf.<BR>उत्तर-ध्˚, एक-ध्˚, दक्षिण-ध्˚, सर्व-ध्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीय|धुरीयः
धुरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, able to bear a burden, fit<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">Page0457-a+ 77</a>]<BR>for a load, suited to a burden; charged with important<BR>duties; (अस्), m. a beast of burden; a man of business<BR>or one entrusted with weighty affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0456-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य or (sometimes wrongly spelt) धूर्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fit to be harnessed, fit for a burden, able<BR>to bear one, &c.; standing at the head, holding the<BR>first place, foremost, best; a leader; (अस्), m. a<BR>beast of burden, a horse or bullock attached to the<BR>shaft, shafter; a leader, chief (e. g. कुल-धुर्य, the<BR>chief or leader of a family); a minister, a chargé<BR>d'affaires; a kind of medicinal plant, = ऋषभ;<BR>(अम्), n. the fore-part of the pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा 2. धुरा, ind. (for 1. see धुर, p. 456,<BR>col. 3), violently, hurtfully, (perhaps fr. rt. धुर्व् or<BR>धूर्व्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्
धुर्व् धुर्व् [cf. rt. धूर्व्], cl. 1. P. धुर्-<BR>वति, &c., to hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवका
धुवका धुवका, f. the introductory stanza<BR>of a song, forming afterwards the burden of each<BR>verse; [cf. ध्रुवका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुशुल्या
धुशुल्या धुशुल्या (?), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तुर|धुस्तुरः
धुस्तुर धुस्तुर or धुस्तूर, अस्, m. the<BR>thorn-apple, Datura Fastuosa; [cf. धत्तूर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू 1. धू, cl. 5. P. A. धूनोति, धूनुते,<BR>(in the later language also) धुनोति, धु-<BR>नुते; cl. 6. P. धुवति; cl. 9. P. A. धुनाति, धु-<BR>नीते, दुधाव, दुधुवे, धोष्यति and धविष्-<BR>यति, -ते, अधावीत् and अधौषीत्, (cl. 6. Aor.<BR>अधुवीत्), अधोष्ट and अधविष्ट, धोतुम् and<BR>धवितुम्, to shake, shake off, remove; to agitate,<BR>cause to tremble; to treat (a person) roughly, hurt,<BR>injure; to blow away, destroy; to kindle, excite,<BR>fan (a fire &c.); to shake off from one's self,<BR>liberate one's self from (A.); to strive against, re-<BR>sist: Pass. धूयते: Caus. धावयति and धून-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to shake: Desid. दुधूषति, -ते:<BR>Intens. दोधूयते, दोधोति, दोधवीति, to shake or<BR>agitate violently, shake in a threatening manner, shake<BR>out, shake down from; to be shaken violently, totter<BR>exceedingly (A.); [cf. Zend dun-man, ‘mist, fog:’<BR>Gr. θύ-ω, θύ-ν-ω, θυά-ω, θυά-ζω, θῦ-νο-ς, θύ-ελλα,<BR>θυά-(δ)-ς, θυι-ά-ς, θυ-μό-ς, θῦ-μα, θυ-σία, θύ-ος,<BR>θυή-εις, θύ-μο-ν: Lat. fū-mu-s, sub-fī-o, sub-fī-<BR>men: Goth. daun-s, ‘smell:’ Old Iceland. du-s-t<BR>= Eng. dust: Old Germ. tun-s-t, ‘storm;’ tou-m,<BR>‘smoke:’ Slav. du-na-ti, ‘to breathe;’ dy-mŭ,<BR>‘smoke;’ du-chŭ, ‘breath;’ du-sha, ‘soul:’ Lith. dú-<BR>mai, ‘smoke;’ du-ma-s, dū-mà, ‘thought, mind.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
2. धू, ऊस्, f. shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूक|धूकः
धूक, अस्, m. air or wind; a rogue, cheat; time;<BR>a kind of plant (= वकुल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत|धूतः
धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, shaken off, removed,<BR>agitated; fanned, rinsed, cleansed (in this sense said<BR>to be an old form for धौत, q. v.); deserted, aban-<BR>doned; reproached, reviled; judged, discriminated;<BR>(अम्), n. (?), good behaviour; (आ), f. a wife.<BR>—धूत-<BR>कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose sins are shaken<BR>off, free from sin, pure.<BR>—धूत-पाप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has shaken off his sins; removing or<BR>destroying sin; (आ), f., N. of a river; of the daughter<BR>of the ascetic Veda-śiras.<BR>—धूतपाप-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—धूतपापेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚प-<BR>ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—धूत-<BR>पाप्मन्, आ, आ, अ, = धूत-पाप, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूति|धूतिः
धूति, इस्, m., Ved. ‘a shaker, agitator,’ N. of an<BR>Āditya; (इस्), f. shaking, moving to and fro, fanning;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl. epithet of the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत्वा
धूत्वा, ind. having shaken or shaken off; having<BR>agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धून|धूनः
धून, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken, agitated; distressed<BR>by heat or thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनन|धूननं|धूननः
धूनन, अस्, m. wind; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>shaking, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनय
धूनय (fr. धून), Nom. P. A. धूनयति,<BR>-ते, &c. (generally considered as the Caus. of rt. 1.<BR>धू), to shake, agitate, move to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनि|धूनिः
धूनि, इस्, f. shaking agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप, अस्, m. (by native authorities derived fr.<BR>a rt. धूप्, q. v.), incense, frankincense, perfume,<BR>aromatic vapour or smoke, the vapour proceeding<BR>from fragrant gum or resin, (often in pl. धूपास्);<BR>fragrant powder; [cf. कृत्रिम-ध्˚, कॢप्त^1-ध्˚,<BR>ख-ध्˚, &c.]<BR>—धूप-दान, अम्, n. ‘the giving<BR>of incense,’ N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva<BR>by Halāyudha.<BR>—धूप-धूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>fragrant or fumigated with incense.<BR>—धूप-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. a vessel for incense, censer; a perfume box.<BR>—धूप-वृक्ष or धूपवृक्षक, अस्, m.<BR>‘incense-tree,’ a species of pine, Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—धूपागुरु (˚प-अग्˚), उ, n. a kind of Agallo-<BR>chum used for incense.<BR>—धूपाङ्ग (˚प-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. turpentine.<BR>—धूपार्ह (˚प-अर्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>black kind of Agallochum used or fit for incense.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk. on 20161122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/320. note: lṛi is mw72 coding of vocalic 'l'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपक|धूपकः
धूपक, अस्, m. = धूप in कृत्रिम-ध्˚ and<BR>other adj. comp.; a preparer of perfumes or incense,<BR>a perfumer [cf. धूपिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपन|धूपनं|धूपनः
धूपन, अम्, n. (fr. धूपय), incensing, fumi-<BR>gation, perfuming; perfume, incense, the aromatic<BR>vapour produced from gums or resins.<BR>—धूपनाङ्ग<BR>(˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, m. = धूपाङ्ग, turpentine (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपय
धूपय (fr. धूप, but native authorities recog-<BR>nise a rt. धूप्, q. v.), Nom. P. धूपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to fumigate, perfume, incense, make fragrant; (in<BR>astron.) to obscure with mist, to be about to eclipse;<BR>to speak; to shine; [cf. Gr. τύφ-ω, τῦφ-ο-ς, τυφ-ών,<BR>τυφώς, τυφεδών, Τυμφρηστός (?), τυφλό-ς,<BR>τυφεδανός, τυφεδών: Old Germ. dimpf-en, ‘to<BR>smoke:’ Lith. dump-iù, ‘I fan or blow a fire;’<BR>dùmp-les, ‘bellows.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपाय
धूपाय (fr. धूप, but native authorities give<BR>a rt. धूप्, q. v.), Nom. P. धूपायति, -यितुम्, to<BR>fumigate, perfume with incense; [cf. धूपय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपायित|धूपायितः
धूपायित, अस्, आ, अम्, incensed, perfumed, fumi-<BR>gated, scented with incense; vexed, pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपि
धूपि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a class of divine beings<BR>presiding over rain (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपिक|धूपिकः
धूपिक, अस्, m. a preparer of perfumes or in-<BR>cense, a perfumer; [cf. धूपक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपित|धूपितः
धूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, scented, perfumed, incensed;<BR>suffering pain or fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्य
धूप्य, अम्, n. (?), the claw of a particular ani-<BR>mal which when burned emits a fragrant perfume;<BR>[cf. Pers. nāḳhuni ḳhwuṣ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम|धूमः
धूम, अस्, m. (connected by some with rt. 1. ध्मा),<BR>smoke, vapour, incense; mist, haze; breath (Ved.); a<BR>cloud; (in medic.) smoke as a sternutatory in five<BR>forms; = गो-धूम, = शिलारस, a kind of incense; a<BR>place prepared for the building of a house; N. of a<BR>man; (आ), f. a kind of plant (= धीरावी); [cf. गो-ध्˚,<BR>चरिष्णु-ध्˚, तृष्ट-ध्˚: cf. also rt. 1. ध्मा; Gr.<BR>θῡ-μό-ς; Lat. fū-mu-s; Old Germ. daum, toum,<BR>‘fume;’ Lith. dū-mai, ‘smoke;’ Slav. dü-mŭ,<BR>‘smoke;’ Hib. dluimh, ‘cloud, darkness.’]<BR>—धू-<BR>म-केतन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘smoke-marked,’ whose ensign<BR>or mark is smoke; (अस्), m. fire or its deity; a<BR>meteor, a comet; Ketu or the personified descending<BR>node.<BR>—धूम-केतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. ‘whose sign<BR>is smoke,’ known or to be known from smoke;<BR>(उस्), m. fire; a comet or falling star, the personi-<BR>fied descending node; N. of a son of Kṛśāśva by<BR>Arcis; of Tṛṇa-vindu by Alambuṣā.<BR>—धूम-<BR>गन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. smelling of smoke.<BR>—धूम-<BR>गन्धिक, अम्, n. a kind of grass (= रोहिष-<BR>तृण).<BR>—धूम-जाङ्गज (धूम-ज-अङ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ammoniac.<BR>—धूम-जाल, अम्, n. a multitude or<BR>mass of clouds or smoke.<BR>—धूम-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, Ved. seeing smoke or vapour (as a person affected<BR>with a peculiar disease of the eye).<BR>—धूम-ध्वज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘whose banner or symbol is smoke,’ fire.<BR>—धूम-प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking or inhaling<BR>only smoke; [cf. धूम-प्राश.]<BR>—धूम-प-<BR>थ, अस्, m. ‘the way of smoke,’ sacrifice; seeking<BR>salvation by works; [cf. धूम-वर्त्मन्.]<BR>—धू-<BR>म-पान, अम्, n. inhaling smoke or vapour; smoking<BR>tobacco.<BR>—धूमपान-विधि, इस्, m. ‘the rule of<BR>inhaling smoke,’ N. of the twenty-eighth chapter of<BR>the Śārṅgadhara-saṃhitā.<BR>—धूम-प्रभा, f., N.<BR>of one of the seventeen divisions of hell where smoke<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">Page0457-c+ 81</a>]<BR>takes the place of light.<BR>—धूम-प्राश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘smoke-eating,’ feeding only on smoke, as a hermit;<BR>[cf. धूम-प.]<BR>—धूम-मङ्गज, various reading<BR>for धूम-जाङ्गज, q. v.<BR>—धूम-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, consisting of smoke or vapour, smoky.<BR>—धू-<BR>म-महिषी, f. fog, mist.<BR>—धूम-योनि, इस्, m.<BR>‘engendered from smoke or vapour,’ a cloud.<BR>—धू-<BR>म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, smoky; smoking, steaming;<BR>containing the word धूम.<BR>—धूमवत्-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. smokiness.<BR>—धूम-वर्चस्, आस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—धूम-वर्ण, अस्, m. ‘smoke-coloured,’ N.<BR>of a king of the serpents.<BR>—धूम-वर्त्मन्, अ,<BR>n. ‘the path of smoke,’ sacrifice; seeking salvation<BR>by works.<BR>—धूम-शिख, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘smoke-<BR>crested’ (said of flame or a tongue of fire).<BR>—धूम-<BR>संहति, इस्, f. a quantity of smoke, a mass or cloud<BR>of smoke.<BR>—धूमाकार (˚म-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the form or appearance of smoke.<BR>—धू-<BR>माक्ष (˚म-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. having dim,<BR>dark or troubled (?) eyes.<BR>—धूमाङ्ग (˚म-अङ्˚)<BR>= शिंशपा.<BR>—धूमाभ (˚म-आभ), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of a smoky appearance or colour, of a purple colour;<BR>(अस्), m. purple.<BR>—धूमा-वती, f., N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—धूमावती-मन्त्र, अस्, m. or धू-<BR>मावती-मनु, उस्, m., N. of certain magical for-<BR>mulas.<BR>—धूमावलि (˚म-आव्˚), इस्, f. a wreath or<BR>cloud of smoke.<BR>—धूमोत्थ (˚म-उत्˚), अम्, n.<BR>= वज्र-क्षार, ammoniac; [cf. धूम-जाङ्गज.]<BR>—धूमोद्गार (˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘the issuing of<BR>smoke or vapour,’ N. of a kind of disease.<BR>—धू-<BR>मोपहत (˚म-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘smoke-struck,’<BR>suffocated with smoke.<BR>—धूमोर्णा (˚म-ऊर्˚), f.,<BR>N. of the wife of Yama; of the wife of Mārkaṇ-<BR>ḍeya; [cf. धूम्रोर्णा.]<BR>—धूमोर्णा-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘husband of Dhūmorṇā,’ epithet of Yama, ruler of<BR>the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमक
धूमक, अस्, आ, अम्, = धूम at the end of<BR>a comp.; (इका), f. smoke, vapour, fog.<BR>—धू-<BR>मक-पुष्पा, f. a species of plant (compared to<BR>smoke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमय
धूमय (fr. धूम), Nom. P. धूमयति,<BR>&c., to cover with smoke, obscure with mist: Pass.<BR>धूम्यते, &c., to be obscured with vapour or mist;<BR>to be about to be eclipsed, to be darkened; [cf.<BR>धूमाय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमल|धूमलः
धूमल, अस्, आ, अम्, smoke-coloured, of a<BR>smoky hue, brownish red, of a purple colour; (अस्),<BR>m. a colour compounded of black and red, purple;<BR>a kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमस
धूमस, अस्, m. the plant Tectona Grandis;<BR>(ई), f. a sort of cake made of pulse steeped in water<BR>and dried in the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाय
धूमाय (fr. धूम), Nom. P. A. धूमायति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to smoke, be covered or obscured with<BR>smoke, to steam: Caus. P. धूमाययति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to smoke or to be covered with smoke,<BR>mist, vapour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायन|धूमायनं
धूमायन, अम्, n. smoking, steaming; (in<BR>medic.) heat, fever, feverishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायित
धूमायित, अम्, n. the act of smoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिका
धूमिका. See धूमक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमित
धूमित, अस्, आ, अम्, obscured with smoke, mist,<BR>&c., darkened; (आ), f., scil. दिश्, that quarter towards<BR>which the sun turns first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिन्
धूमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, smoking, steaming; (इनी), f.,<BR>N. of one of the seven tongues of Agni; of the<BR>wife of Aja-mīḍha; of another woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्यमान
धूम्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being obscured with<BR>mist &c., being obscured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्या
धूम्या, f. thick smoke, a volume or cloud of<BR>smoke.<BR>—धूम्याट (˚या-अट), अस्, m. the fork-<BR>tailed shrike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्र|धूम्रः
धूम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, smoky, smoke-coloured,<BR>grey; (according to the lexicographers) dark-red or<BR>the colour of fire seen through smoke; of a deep<BR>purple colour, purple; (metaphorically) dark, lurid,<BR>obscured; (अस्), m. a mixture of red and black;<BR>purple (the colour); incense. (= तुरुष्क); N. of<BR>one of Skanda's attendants; of a Dānava; of a Muni;<BR>of a monkey or bear [cf. धूम्रायण and धौ-<BR>म्रायण]; an epithet of Śiva; of Parāśara; (in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">Page0458-a+ 79</a>]<BR>astrology) N. of the twenty-eighth Yoga; (आ), f. a<BR>kind of gourd (= शशाण्डुली); epithet of Durgā; of<BR>the mother of Vasu-dhara; (अम्), n. sin, vice,<BR>wickedness; [cf. ताम्र-ध्˚.]<BR>—धूम्र-केतु, उस्,<BR>m. ‘grey-bannered,’ N. of a son of Bharata; of<BR>Tṛṇa-vindu.<BR>—धूम्र-केश, अस्, m. ‘dark-haired,’<BR>N. of a son of Pṛthu and Arcis; of a son of<BR>Kṛśāśva and Arcis [cf. धूम-केतु]; of a son of<BR>Danu.<BR>—धूम्र-गिरि, इस्, m. ‘the smoky moun-<BR>tain,’ N. of a mountain.<BR>—धूम्र-धी, ईस्, ईस्,<BR>इ, ‘whose intellect is dim’ or ‘whose devotion is<BR>obscured,’ devoted to works.<BR>—धूम्र-नीकाश, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. of a deep dark-red colour.<BR>—धूम्र-<BR>पत्त्रा, f. ‘having grey or dark-red leaves,’ N. of a<BR>shrub (= धूम्राह्वा, सु-लभा, स्वयम्-भुवा,<BR>गृध्र-पत्त्रा, गृध्राणी, कृमि-घ्नी, श्रीम-<BR>लापहा).<BR>—धूम्र-मूलिका, f. ‘having a grey or<BR>dark-red root,’ a kind of grass (= शूली).<BR>—धूम्र-<BR>रुच्, क्, क्, क्, of a purple hue, of a deep-red colour.<BR>—धूम्र-रोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. dark-red, deep<BR>purple.<BR>—धूम्र-लोचन, अस्, m. ‘dark-eyed,’ a<BR>pigeon; N. of a general of the Asura Śumbha.<BR>—धूम्र-लोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-red, deep purple.<BR>—धूम्र-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, smoky-coloured,<BR>dark-red, deep purple; (अस्), m. incense; N. of a<BR>son of Aja-mīḍha and Dhūminī; N. of a mountain;<BR>(आ), f., N. of one of the seven tongues of Fire;<BR>flame.<BR>—धूम्र-वर्णक, अस्, m. ‘the dark-<BR>coloured one,’ a kind of animal living in caves, a<BR>fox; [cf. कोकड.]<BR>—धूम्रवर्णा-मनु, N. of<BR>a magical formula.<BR>—धूम्र-शूक, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>grey bristles,’ a camel; (also read धूम्र-शूल.)<BR>—धूम्र-संरक्त-लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>dark-red or greyish-red eyes.<BR>—धूम्राक्ष (˚र-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, grey-eyed; (अस्), m., N. of a Ra-<BR>kṣas; of a son of Hema-candra, grandson of Tṛṇa-<BR>vindu [cf. धूम्राश्व]; of a king of the Niṣadhas.<BR>—धूम्राक्षि (˚र-अक्˚), इस्, m. a pearl of a bad<BR>colour.<BR>—धूम्राट (˚र-अट), अस्, m. the fork-<BR>tailed shrike; [cf. धूम्याट.]<BR>—धूम्रानीक (˚र-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of one of the seven sons of Medhā-<BR>tithi and a Varṣa called after him.<BR>—धूम्राभ-<BR>(˚र-आभ), अस्, m. air, wind, atmosphere (some-<BR>times of a smoky or dark-red hue?).<BR>—धूम्राश्व<BR>(˚र-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘having dark horses,’ N. of a son<BR>of Su-candra (son of Hema-candra) and father of<BR>Sṛñjaya; [cf. धूम्राक्ष.]<BR>—धूम्राह्वा (˚र-<BR>आह्˚), f. = धूम्र-पत्त्रा.<BR>—धूम्रोर्णा (˚र-ऊर्˚),<BR>f. = धूमोर्णा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0457-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रक|धूम्रकः
धूम्रक, अस्, m. ‘the grey animal,’ a camel;<BR>(इका), f. the plant Dalbergia Sissoo (= शिंशपा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रायण
धूम्रायण, अस्, m. (fr. धूम्र), a patronymic<BR>from Dhūmra; [cf. धौम्रायण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रिमन्
धूम्रिमन्, आ, m., Ved. dark-red (the colour),<BR>darkness of colour; obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूयमान
धूयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being shaken or agitated<BR>or fanned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलि|धूलिः
धूलि, इस्, m. f. or धूली, f. (perhaps connected<BR>with rt. ध्वस् or ध्वंस्, cf. धूसर), dust; powder;<BR>[cf. गन्ध-ध्˚, गो-ध्˚]; a particular number.<BR>—धूलि-कुट्टिम, अम्, n. or धूलि-केदार, अस्,<BR>m. a mound, rampart of earth.<BR>—धूलि-गुच्छक,<BR>अस्, m. the red fragrant vegetable powder thrown<BR>about at the spring festival called the Holi.<BR>—धूलि-<BR>धूम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-red or dark with dust.<BR>—धूलि-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘dust-marked,’ ‘whose<BR>sign is dust,’ air or wind.<BR>—धूलि-पुष्पिका, f. the<BR>plant Pandanus Odoratissimus; [cf. केतकी.]<BR>—धूलि-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, covered with dust.<BR>—धूलि-मुष्टि,<BR>इस्, m. f. a handful of dust.<BR>—धूलिमुष्टि-प्र-<BR>क्षेप, अस्, m. the throwing of handfuls of dust.<BR>—धूली-कदम्ब or धूली-कदम्बक or धूलि-<BR>कदम्ब or धूलि-कदम्बक, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Dalbergia Ougeinensis (= तिनिश); a species of the<BR>Kadamba tree, Nauclea Cordifolia (= नीप); Cap-<BR>paris Trifoliata (= वरुण).<BR>—धूली-पटल, अस्, m.<BR>a cloud of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिका
धूलिका, f. fog, mist, (from its dust-like appearance.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूण
धूण धूण, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the resin<BR>of the Shorea Robusta; [cf. धूनक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनक|धूनकः
धूनक, अस्, m. the resin of the Shorea Robusta<BR>or resin in general; [cf. धूर्ण and धूण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्
धूप् धूप्, cl. 1. P. धूपायति, &c., cl.<BR>10. P. धूपयति, &c. See धूपय<BR>and धूपाय, p. 457, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप. See p. 457, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम|धूमः
धूम धूम, धूम्र. See p. 457, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्
धूर् 1. धूर् (connected with rt. धूर्व्),<BR>cl. 4. A. धूर्यते, &c., to hurt or kill;<BR>to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्
धूर् 2. धूर् for धुर् (q. v.) at the begin-<BR>ning of a comp.<BR>—धूर्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, standing<BR>on or going along the pole or fore-part of a chariot;<BR>standing at the head, taking the first place, preceding,<BR>foremost.<BR>—धूर्-जटि, इस्, m., in one place also धूर्-<BR>जटिन्, ई, m. (fr. धुर् and जटि = जटा), ‘whose matted<BR>locks are like a burden,’ an epithet of Rudra-Śiva;<BR>N. of a medical author.<BR>—धूर्-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bearing a load or burden, managing affairs; (अस्),<BR>m. a beast of burden; [cf. धुरन्-धर.]<BR>—धूर्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a load, laden.<BR>—धूर्-वह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bearing a load, carrying a burden;<BR>managing affairs; (अस्), m. a beast of burden.<BR>—धूर्-वोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ, bearing a load,<BR>the carrier of a burden.<BR>—धूर्-षद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>standing under the yoke, drawing a load; resting on<BR>the yoke; moving, promoting.<BR>—धूर्-षाह्, ट्, ट्,<BR>ट्, Ved. bearing the yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्य
धूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, for धुर्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्ण
धूर्ण धूर्ण = धूण = धूनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त|धूर्तः|धूर्त्त|धूर्त्तं|धूर्त्तः
धूर्त धूर्त. See under rt. धूर्व् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्व्
धूर्व् धूर्व् (connected with rts. धुर्व्,<BR>ध्वृ, धूर्, ह्वृ), cl. 1. P. धूर्वति, दु-<BR>धूर्व, धूर्विष्यति, अधूर्वीत्, धूर्वितुम्, Ved.<BR>to bend, cause to fall, hurt, injure: Desid. दुधूर्-<BR>षति, to wish to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त|धूर्तः|धूर्त्त|धूर्त्तं|धूर्त्तः
धूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cunning, crafty, dishonest,<BR>knavish, fraudulent, subtle; mischievous, injurious;<BR>(अस्), m. a rogue, cheat, swindler; a gamester; (in<BR>amatory language) a gay deceiver, a lover or<BR>gallant; the thorn-apple, Datura [cf. कितव and<BR>क्रूर-धूर्त]; a kind of perfume [cf. चोरक];<BR>(आ), f. a sort of nightshade; (अम्), n. rust<BR>or iron-filings; black salt (= खण्ड-लवण;<BR>cf. क्षेम-धूर्त).<BR>—धूर्त-कितव, अस्, m. a<BR>gamester.<BR>—धूर्त-कृत्, त्, m. = धूर्त, dishonest,<BR>a knave, rogue, cheat; (त्), m. thorn-apple.<BR>—धूर्त-<BR>चरित, अम्, n. ‘the actions of rogues,’ N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—धूर्त-जन्तु, उस्, m. ‘the cunning creature,’<BR>man.<BR>—धूर्त-ता, f. or धूर्त-त्व, अम्, n. knavery,<BR>craftiness, roguery, knavishness, shrewdness.<BR>—धूर्-<BR>त-त्रय, अम्, n. three rogues, a trio of swindlers.<BR>—धूर्त-नर्तक, अम्, n. ‘rogues as actors,’ N.<BR>of a comedy by Sāma-rāja.<BR>—धूर्त-प्रलाप, अस्,<BR>m. the talk or confabulation of rogues.<BR>—धूर्त-<BR>मण्डल, अस्, m. a party of rogues or gamblers.<BR>—धूर्त-मानुषा, f., N. of a plant (= रास्ना).<BR>—धूर्त-रचना, f. a cunning plot, roguery.<BR>—धूर्त-राज, अस्, m. the chief of rogues.<BR>—धूर्-<BR>त-समागम, अम्, n. ‘assemblage of rogues,’ N. of<BR>a comedy by Jyotir-īśvara.<BR>—धूर्त-स्वामिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘lord of the rogues,’ N. of a commentator on<BR>Āpastamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्तक|धूर्तकः|धूर्त्तक|धूर्त्तकः
धूर्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, cunning, a cheat, a rogue;<BR>(अस्), m. a jackal; N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्ति|धूर्त्ति
धूर्ति, इस्, f., Ved. injury, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्तिल
धूर्तिल in अक्ष-ध्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वन्
धूर्वन्, अ, n., Ved. causing to fall, bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वा
धूर्वा धूर्वा, f., Ved. = दूर्वा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वी|धूर्व्वी
धूर्वी धूर्वी, f. the fore-part or pole of a<BR>carriage, = धुर्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलक|धूलकं
धूलक धूलक, अम्, n. poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलि|धूलिः
धूलि धूलि. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूश्
धूश् धूश् or धूष् or धूस् (perhaps a<BR>Prākṛt form of धृष् for हृष्), cl. 10.<BR>P. धूशयति, धूषयति, धूसयति, &c., to<BR>make splendid or elegant; to embellish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूषर
धूषर धूषर, a wrong spelling for धू-<BR>सर below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसर|धूसरः
धूसर धूसर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. ध्वस् for<BR>ध्वंस्, cf. ध्वसिर; but said to be fr. rt. 1. धू<BR>and connected with धूलि, q. v.), of a dusty or<BR>greyish or dusty-white colour, grey; (अस्), m. grey<BR>(the colour); a jackass, a donkey; a camel; a pigeon;<BR>an oilman; anything of a grey tint; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>small shrub, = पाण्डुर-फली; (ई), f., N. of a Kin-<BR>narī or female chorister of heaven.<BR>—धूसर-च्छ-<BR>दा, f. a kind of plant, = श्वेत-वुह्ना.<BR>—धूसर-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. grey colour, paleness; (also read धू-<BR>षर-त्व.)<BR>—धूसर-पत्त्रिका, f. the plant Tragia<BR>Involucrata [cf. उष्ट्र-धूसर, पुच्छिका]; a kind<BR>of Heliotropium (= हस्ति-शुण्डी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरक
धूसरक, अस्, m., N. of a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरित
धूसरित, अस्, आ, अम्, made grey, greyish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस्तूर|धूस्तूरः
धूस्तूर धूस्तूर, अस्, m. = धुस्तूर, the<BR>thorn-apple, Datura Metel and Fastuosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृ
धृ धृ (allied to rt. भृ, which is pro-<BR>bably the more ancient form), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>धरति, -ते, दधार (Ved. दाधार), दध्रे<BR>(part. दध्राण), धरिष्यति, -ते, अधार्षीत्,<BR>अधृत, धर्तुम्, and more commonly cl. 10.<BR>(identical with Caus. but with the same senses as<BR>cl. 1.) धारयति, -ते, Pot. धारयेत्, -त (Mahā-<BR>bh. Anuśāsana-p. 5007. धारयीत), धारयामास,<BR>धरयिष्यति, -ते, अदीधरत्, -त (Vedic forms<BR>दीधरत्, दिधृतम्, दिधृत, नि-दीधर्), धा-<BR>रयितुम्, to hold, bear, carry; hold up, support,<BR>sustain, maintain; carry on; to hold in, hold back,<BR>keep back, restrain, stop, detain, curb, resist; to hold<BR>in one's possession, keep, possess, have; to keep, retain<BR>(in one's service); to hold fast, preserve; to hold, con-<BR>tain; to lay hold of, seize, recover; to hold, observe,<BR>practise; to wear, use (as clothes &c.); to bear,<BR>undergo, suffer; to hold out, hold on, endure, con-<BR>tinue, continue to live; (A.) to hold one's place, stand<BR>firm, remain; to fix, place, deposit; to destine for,<BR>assign or present anything (acc.) to any person (dat.);<BR>to allot, assign, confer; (A.) to destine a person (acc.)<BR>to anything (dat.); (cl. 10.) to owe anything (acc.)<BR>to any person (dat. or gen.); to weigh in a balance;<BR>to prolong (in pronunciation); to cite, quote. The<BR>above meanings of धृ (cl. 1. or more frequently<BR>cl. 10. identified with Caus.) may be variously ex-<BR>tended by connecting it with various nouns, e. g.<BR>गर्भं धृ, to conceive, to become pregnant,<BR>(in this sense the older language uses rt. भृ);<BR>दण्डं धृ, to carry a stick, use force, chastise<BR>(with loc. of the pers.); दमं धृ, to punish<BR>(with loc. of the pers.); आत्मानं or जीवितं or<BR>प्राणान् or शरीरं or गात्रं or देहं धृ, to<BR>maintain the soul, preserve the vital spirits, body,<BR>&c., to continue to live, survive; मनो or मान-<BR>सं or मतिं or चित्तं or बुद्धिं धृ, to fix<BR>the mind, direct the thoughts or attention upon,<BR>resolve; व्रतं धृ, to observe or keep a vow,<BR>&c. [cf. धृत-व्रत]; तपो धृ, to undergo or<BR>perform penance; धारणां धृ, to practise self-<BR>control; तुलया धृ (or without तुलया), to hold<BR>in a balance, weigh, measure; शिरसा or मूर्ध्नि<BR>धृ, to bear on the head, honour highly; मनसा<BR>धृ (or without मनसा), to bear in mind, recollect,<BR>remember; समये धृ, to bring to an agreement,<BR>cause to make a compact; अन्तरे धृ, to deposit<BR>anything as surety, to give bail, to pledge: Pass. or<BR>cl. 6. A. धृयते (ep. also धृयति), to be firm or<BR>fixed, to be supported or maintained, to be preserved;<BR>to exist, live, continue to live, remain alive, survive;<BR>to remain, continue; to undertake, resolve upon<BR>(with dat. or acc. of the thing or with inf.): Caus.<BR>धारयति, -ते (with the meanings of cl. 1. and<BR>cl. 10.): Pass. of Caus. धार्यते, to be held or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-a" target="_blank">Page0459-a+ 81</a>]<BR>supported, to be maintained or preserved; to con-<BR>tinue to live (with inst., e. g. तेन न धार्यते, it<BR>is not lived by him): Desid. दिधीर्षति, -ते,<BR>दिधरिषते, दिधारयिषति, to wish to hold or<BR>keep, to try to support or maintain, &c.: Intens.<BR>देध्रीयते, दर्धर्ति (Ved. दाधर्ति), to hold<BR>very fast, lay hold of firmly, bear firmly, &c.; [cf.<BR>1. धर्म, धीर, ध्रुव, धुर्, धुर्य;<BR>Zend dar, ‘to hold;’ Gr. θρή-σα-σθαι, θρᾶ-ν-ος,<BR>θρῆν-υ-ς, θρόνο-ς, θέρ-μα, θέλ-ω, ἐ-θέλ-ω; Lat.<BR>frē-tu-s, frē-nu-m, fir-mu-s, for-ma; Angl. Sax.<BR>drag-an, dreog-an; Old Germ. trag-an; Mod.<BR>Germ. trag-en.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0458-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृक्
धृक् (at end of comp., and only occurring in<BR>nom. sing. धृक्, and more probably to be referred<BR>to rt. धृष् or to rt. दृह्), bearing, carrying, sup-<BR>porting, sustaining, suffering, wearing, possessing,<BR>having, &c.; [cf. काल-रूप-ध्˚, शक्ति-ध्˚, श-<BR>रीर-ध्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्
धृत्, त्, त्, त् (at end of comp.), a holder, bearer,<BR>possessor; bearing, carrying, possessing, having, ob-<BR>serving, &c.; [cf. चर्षणी-ध्˚, धरणी-ध्˚,<BR>धर्म-ध्˚, नित्य-ध्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत|धृतः
धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, held, borne, carried, main-<BR>tained, supported; contained; possessed; kept, re-<BR>tained, detained; laid hold of, seized, grasped, griped;<BR>worn, used; observed, practised; weighed; placed,<BR>deposited; holding, bearing, continuing, enduring,<BR>existing, standing; intent upon, i. e. resolved or<BR>determined to do anything (with dat. or loc., e. g.<BR>जये धृतस्, resolved on victory); firm, prepared,<BR>ready; (अस्), m., N. of a son of the thirteenth Manu;<BR>of a descendant of Druhyu and son of Dharma [cf.<BR>धार्तेय]; (अम्), n. a peculiar manner of fighting;<BR>(अम्), ind. firmly, slowly, solemnly.<BR>—धृत-क-<BR>नक-माल, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a golden collar or<BR>wreath.<BR>—धृत-कार्मुकेषु (˚क-इषु), उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, armed with bow and arrows.<BR>—धृत-दक्ष,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of enduring intelligence; (Sāy.) of<BR>enduring strength, possessing vigour.<BR>—धृत-<BR>दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying the stick, inflicting<BR>punishment; one on whom punishment has been<BR>inflicted.<BR>—धृत-दीधिति, इस्, m. ‘constant in<BR>splendor,’ fire; [cf. घृत-दीधिति.]<BR>—धृत-देवा,<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Devaka.<BR>—धृत-पट, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, covered or overspread with a cloth &c.<BR>—धृत-मती, f., N. of a river; (wrong form for<BR>धृति-मती.)<BR>—धृत-राजन्, आ, m., N. of a man;<BR>[cf. धार्तरज्ञ.]<BR>—धृत-राष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose empire is firm or who holds the kingdom;<BR>(अस्), m. a good king; N. of a Nāga, also called<BR>Airāvata; of a Deva-gandharva, sometimes identified<BR>with king Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a son of the Daitya Bali;<BR>of a king of Kāśī; (according to the Mahā-bhārata)<BR>N. of the eldest son of Vyāsa by the widow of Vicitra-<BR>vīrya, (he was brother of Pāṇḍu and Vidura, and as<BR>the first-born was entitled to the throne of Hāstina-<BR>pura, but being born blind, he at first renounced the<BR>sovereignty in favour of Pāṇḍu; afterwards, on the<BR>retirement of Pāṇḍu to the woods, Dhṛta-rāṣṭra<BR>was called to undertake the government, which he<BR>did with the assistance of Bhīṣma as his regent; he<BR>was husband of Gāndhārī and father of 100 sons, the<BR>eldest of whom was named Dur-yodhana; he is some-<BR>times identified with Dhṛta-rāṣṭra and with Haṃsa,<BR>two chiefs of the Gandharvas); N. of a son of<BR>Janam-ejaya; a kind of bird, perhaps a sort of goose;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra, whose names<BR>are enumerated in Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 4540; (ई), f.,<BR>N. of a daughter of Tāmrā, mother of the geese and<BR>other water-birds, = हंस-पत्नी, = हंस-पदी;<BR>[cf. धार्तराष्ट्र and धार्तराष्ट्रि.]<BR>—धृत-<BR>राष्ट्र-ज, अस्, m. ‘sprung from Dhṛta-rāṣṭra,’ epi-<BR>thet of any son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—धृत-वर्मन्,<BR>आ, m. ‘bearing armour or mail, mailed,’ N. of a<BR>warrior on the side of the Kurus.<BR>—धृत-व्रत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. of fixed law or order; keeping<BR>vows or engagements, devoted, attached, faithful;<BR>(Sāy.) accepting pious acts, performing religious<BR>rites; (अस्), m. epithet of Varuṇa; of Indra; of<BR>Rudra; of Savitṛ; of Agni; of a son of Dhṛti;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">Page0459-b+ 80</a>]<BR>(आस्), m. pl. epithet of the Ādityas.<BR>—धृत-श-<BR>रीर, अस्, आ, अम्, continuing to live or exist, existing.<BR>—धृत-श्री, ईस्, f., N. of a metre consisting of<BR>four lines of twenty-one syllables each.<BR>—धृत-<BR>सन्धि, इस्, m. ‘keeping agreements or compacts,’<BR>N. of a son of Su-sandhi and father of Bharata.<BR>—धृत-सिंह, अस्, m. a various reading for धृति-<BR>सिंह, q. v.<BR>—धृत-हेति, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘bearing weapons,’<BR>armed.<BR>—धृतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, firm-<BR>minded, self-possessed, steady, calm, collected.<BR>—धृ-<BR>ताम्भस् (˚त-अम्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्, containing water.<BR>—धृतेषुधि (˚त-इष्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, carrying a<BR>quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतक
धृतक, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist patriarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतवत्|धृतवन्त्
धृत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having taken or con-<BR>veyed or held or resolved; (अती), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृति|धृतिः
धृति, इस्, f. holding, holding fast, laying hold of,<BR>seizing, having, possessing; supporting, maintaining;<BR>firmness (e. g. धृतिं कृ, to show firmness, stand<BR>firm); constancy, steadiness, steadfastness, fortitude,<BR>energy, resolution; strong will, self-command; will,<BR>command (Ved.); satisfaction, happiness, pleasure,<BR>contentment; N. of certain evening oblations offered<BR>at the Aśva-medha; a sacrifice, offering; N. of a<BR>Vedic metre of seventy-two syllables; (in the later<BR>language) any metre consisting of 4×18 syllables;<BR>a metre composed of the Upendra-vajrā and Indra-<BR>vajrā; N. of one of the astrological Yogas; Reso-<BR>lution or Satisfaction personified as a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and wife of Dharma, (regarded as one of the<BR>Vasu-patnīs or as a form of Dākṣāyaṇī in Piṇḍā-<BR>raka); N. of one of the sixteen Kalās of the Moon;<BR>N. of a goddess, daughter of a Kalās of Prakṛti and<BR>wife of Kapila; N. of the wife of Rudra-manu; N.<BR>of the thirteenth of the sixteen Mātṛkās; (इस्), m.,<BR>N. of one of the Viśve-Devās; of a preceptor,<BR>Dhṛti Aindrota; of a son of Vi-jaya and father of<BR>Dhṛta-vrata; of a son of Vīta-havya and father of<BR>Bahulāśva; of a son of Babhru; [cf. अ-ध्˚ and<BR>क्ष्मा-ध्˚.]<BR>—धृति-परिपूर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—धृति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, steadfast,<BR>firm, steady, calm, determined, resolute; satisfied,<BR>content; (आन्), m., N. of a form of Agni; of a son<BR>of Manu Raivata; of Manu Sāvarṇa; of one of the<BR>Saptarṣis in the thirteenth Manv-antara; of a son<BR>of Kīrtti-mat, son of Aṅgiras; of a son of Yavīnara;<BR>of a Brāhman; (अती), f., N. of a river, also read<BR>धृत-वती; (अत्), n., N. of a Varṣa in Kuśa-<BR>dvīpa.<BR>—धृतिमत्-ता, f. steadfastness, steadiness,<BR>calmness, &c.<BR>—धृति-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>of steadfastness or constancy; consisting of content-<BR>ment.<BR>—धृति-मुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, ‘fortitude-stealing,’<BR>who or what robs one of one's steadfastness, dis-<BR>composing, agitating.<BR>—धृति-सिंह, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man said to have assisted Puruṣottama in com-<BR>posing the Hārāvalī; (also read धृत-सिंह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वन्
धृत्वन्, आ, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; of Brahmā;<BR>a clever man; virtue, morality; the sea; the sky<BR>[cf. क्षेम-ध्˚]; (अरी), f. the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वा
धृत्वा, ind. having held, having laid hold of or<BR>seized; having taken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज्
धृज् धृज् or धृञ्ज् (connected with rts.<BR>ध्रज् and ध्रिज्), cl. 1. P. धर्जति,<BR>धृञ्जति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् धृष्, cl. 1. 5. P. धर्षति, धृष्-<BR>णोति, दधर्ष (part. दधृष्वस्),<BR>धर्षिष्यति, अधर्षीत् (Vedic forms दधर्-<BR>षीत्, दधर्षत्, दधर्षति), धर्षितुम्, to<BR>be bold or courageous; to be confident or presump-<BR>tuous, to be proud or overbearing; to be impudent<BR>or impatient; to have courage to do anything, to<BR>dare, venture (with inf., e. g. धृष्णुमः प्रष्-<BR>टुम्, we dare to ask); to dare to attack, &c. (with<BR>acc. of the person); to insult, overbear, treat with<BR>indignity: Pass. धृष्यते, to be attacked or in-<BR>sulted, to be subdued or overpowered: Caus. धर्-<BR>षयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अदधर्षत् or अदीधृषत्,<BR>to dare to attack, to overbear, insult, treat with indig-<BR>nity, violate (a woman); offend, injure; assail, over-<BR>power, overcome, conquer, destroy; (A.) to surpass (?):<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">Page0459-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Desid. दिधर्षिषति: Intens. दरीधृष्यते,<BR>दरीधर्ष्टि; [cf. Zend daresh, ‘to dare;’ darshi,<BR>‘strong:’ Gr. θρασ-ύ-ς, θράσ-ος, θάρσ-ος, θαρσ-έ-ω,<BR>θαῤῥέω, θαρσ-ύνω, Θερσ-ίτη-ς: Lat. fortis: Goth.<BR>ga-daurs-an, ‘to dare:’ Slav. drĭz-a-ti, drĭz-na-ti,<BR>‘to dare:’ Lith. dras-ù-s, ‘courageous;’ dras-à,<BR>‘courage:’ Hib. das-ached, ‘fierceness.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषज्
धृषज्, क्, क्, क् (?) , Ved. assailing, attacking,<BR>destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषत्|धृषन्त्
धृषत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, pres. part., Ved. bold,<BR>daring, courageous, confident; (अता), ind. boldly,<BR>courageously.<BR>—धृषद्-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>of a brave race, heroic.<BR>—धृषद्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>Ved. bold, courageous.<BR>—धृषन्-मनस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. brave-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषित
धृषित, अस्, आ, अम्, bold, courageous, brave, daring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषु|धृषुः
धृषु, उस्, उस्, उ, bold, proud; clever; (उस्),<BR>m. a heap, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, bold, daring, courageous,<BR>confident; insolent, impudent, rude, saucy, shame-<BR>less; forward, intrusive, presumptuous; profligate,<BR>abandoned; obtained?; (अस्), m. a faithless hus-<BR>band; N. of a son of Manu Vaivasvata, (also read<BR>धृष्णु; cf. धार्ष्ट); of a son of Kunti; of a<BR>son of Bhajamāna; (अस्), m., N. of a spell for using<BR>or restraining magical weapons; (आ), f. a disloyal or<BR>unchaste woman; (अम्), ind. boldly, courageously,<BR>fearlessly; (it is said that धृष्ट may be used at the<BR>end of a comp. to give a bad sense to the word with<BR>which it is compounded); [cf. Angl. Sax. thriste;<BR>Swed. dristig; Old Iceland. dreiss; Mod. Germ.<BR>dreist.]<BR>—धृष्ट-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Cedi; of a king of Videhā or Mithilā, son of Su-<BR>dhṛti; of a son of Satya-dhṛti; of a son of Su-<BR>kumāra; of the father of Su-kumāra; of a son of<BR>Dhṛṣṭa-dyumna; of a king of the Kaikayas; of a<BR>son of Manu.<BR>—धृष्ट-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>bold or daring, most confident or courageous.<BR>—धृष्ट-ता, f. or धृष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. bold-<BR>ness, courage, impudence.<BR>—धृष्ट-द्युम्न, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Dru-pada (killed by Aśvatthāman<BR>while asleep).<BR>—धृष्ट-धी, ईस्, or धृष्ट-<BR>बुद्धि, इस्, m. ‘bold-minded,’ N. of a man.<BR>—धृष्ट-पराक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, of daring<BR>valour.<BR>—धृष्ट-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a high<BR>opinion of one's self.<BR>—धृष्ट-रथ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—धृष्ट-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>son of Śvaphalka.<BR>—धृष्टोक्त (˚ट-उक्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Arjuna Kārttavīrya; (also read<BR>धृष्णोक्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टक
धृष्टक, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टि
धृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (according to Mahī-<BR>dhara) bold; (इस्), m. a pair of tongs; N. of a son<BR>of Hiraṇya-kaśipu; of a minister of king Daśa-ratha;<BR>(इस्), f. boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ण
धृष्ण, अस्, &c., a wrong reading for धृष्ट,<BR>q. v.<BR>—धृष्णोक्त (˚ण-उक्˚), अस्, &c., a wrong<BR>reading for धृष्टोक्त, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णज्
धृष्णज्, क्, क्, क्, bold, confident; impudent,<BR>shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णि|धृष्णिः
धृष्णि, इस्, m. a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, courageous, bold, confident,<BR>valiant; impudent, shameless; strong, powerful,<BR>(applied in the Veda to Indra, Soma, the Maruts,<BR>and the horses of Indra); (उ), ind. in a bold or<BR>confident or powerful way; firmly, strongly; with<BR>force [cf. दधृक्]; (उस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Manu Vaivasvata [cf. धृष्ट]; of a son of Manu<BR>Sāvarṇa; of a son of Kavi; of a son of Ku-<BR>kura; कश्यपस्य धृष्णु, N. of a Sāman.<BR>—धृष्णु-त्व, अम्, n. boldness, confidence.<BR>—धृष्णु-षेण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having an<BR>overpowering weapon; (Sāy.) having a conquering<BR>or overpowering host, leading a valiant army (as a<BR>drum).<BR>—धृष्ण्व्-ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. of over-<BR>powering strength, endowed with resistless might,<BR>(applied to Indra and the Maruts.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णुक
धृष्णुक, अस्, m., N. of a prince; [cf. धृष्-<BR>टक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णुया
धृष्णुया, ind., Ved. in a bold or powerful<BR>manner, firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0459-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्य
धृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, assailable, to be attacked;<BR>conquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषद्
धृषद् धृषद्, Ved. = दृषद्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धॄ
धॄ धॄ, cl. 9. P. धृणाति, &c., to be old,<BR>grow old; (various reading for rt. 1. जॄ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे धे, cl. 1. P. धयति, दधौ, धास्-<BR>यति, अधात्, अधासीत्, अदधत्, Prec. धे-<BR>यात्, धातुम्, to suck, drink, to suck in, drink in,<BR>absorb; appropriate; to suck out, draw away, take<BR>away: Caus. धापयति, -यितुम्, to give suck,<BR>suckle, nourish: Desid. धित्सति, to wish to suck;<BR>[cf. दधि, धात्री, 2. धायस्, धारु, 2. धासि:<BR>Zend daēnu, ‘female:’ Gr. θῆ-σθαι, θη-λή, θη-λώ,<BR>θηλα-μών, τήθη, τι-θή-νη, τί-τθο-ς, θῆ-λυ-ς,<BR>γαλα-θη-νό-ς, Τη-θύ-ς, ϴέ-τι-ς: Lat. fī-liu-s, fī-<BR>li-a, fē-lā-re, fē-mina: Umbr. fe-liu = filius:<BR>Goth. dadd-ya = Old Germ. tā-u, ‘I suck;’ tila,<BR>‘female breast;’ tuta, tutta = Eng. teat: Slav. do-<BR>ya, ‘to suck;’ doilica, ‘nurse;’ de†-te, ‘child;’<BR>de†-va, ‘virgin:’ Hib. daif, ‘drink.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेन|धेनः
धेन, अस्, m. the ocean, a male river; (आ), f.,<BR>Ved. a milch cow; a mare (?); a river; speech;<BR>voice; N. of the wife of Bṛhas-pati; (आस्), f. pl.<BR>any beverage made of milk; [cf. धेनु, गो.] (In<BR>Ṛg-veda I. 2, 3, धेना may possibly be an epithet<BR>of the horses of Vāyu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनु|धेनुः
धेनु, उस्, f. a milch cow, a cow that has lately<BR>calved, (sometimes compounded with the names of<BR>other animals to denote the female of a species,<BR>see खड्ग-ध्˚, गो-ध्˚, वडव-ध्˚); the earth<BR>[cf. गो]; a gift, offering, present to Brāhmans, (pro-<BR>perly a milch cow so presented, but applied also to)<BR>any gift supposed to be formed in the shape of a cow<BR>or to be offered in its stead, (in this sense धेनु is<BR>generally at the end of a compound, e. g. घृत-ध्˚,<BR>an offering of ghee; जल-ध्˚, an oblation of water;<BR>cf. लवण-ध्˚, रत्न-ध्˚, सुवर्ण-ध्˚: occasion-<BR>ally it is uncompounded, e. g. तिलानाम् धेनुः, an<BR>offering of sesamum-seeds); (अवस्), f. pl. any<BR>beverage made of milk; (उ), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>(धेनु at the end of a comp. may form a diminutive,<BR>the female being weaker than the male; cf. असि-<BR>ध्˚, खड्ग-ध्˚, पुत्री, पुत्रिका.)<BR>—धेनु-गो-<BR>दुह, अम्, n. cow and milker.<BR>—धेनु-दुग्ध,<BR>अम्, n. cow's milk; a kind of gourd, = चिर्भिट.<BR>—धेनुदुग्ध-कर, अस्, m. carrot, Daucus Ca-<BR>rota.<BR>—धेनु-मक्षिका, f. a horse-fly, gad-fly.<BR>—धेनु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessing cows,<BR>rich in cattle; containing or giving nourishing beve-<BR>rage; containing the word धेनु; (अती), f., N. of<BR>the wife of Deva-dyumna.<BR>—धेनुम्-भव्या, f.<BR>(probably) about to become a milch cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुक|धेनुकः
धेनुक, अस्, m., N. of an Asura or demon in the<BR>shape of a donkey (killed by Kṛṣṇa or according to<BR>other authorities by Rāma); a kind of coitus [cf. धै-<BR>नुक]; (आ), f. a milch cow; a gift, offering, see<BR>धेनु above; a female animal in general (as a she-<BR>elephant, a woman, &c., see धेनु above); also<BR>used like धेनु at the end of comps. to form dimi-<BR>nutives (e. g. असि-ध्˚, a knife, from असि, a sword); a<BR>vein which when cut bleeds only at intervals; N. of<BR>the wife of Kīrtti-mat who was a son of Aṅgiras;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—धेनुक-<BR>वध, अस्, m. ‘the killing of Dhenuka,’ N. of<BR>the twenty-third chapter of the Kṛṣṇa-khaṇḍa or<BR>fourth part of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—धे-<BR>नुक-सूदन, अस्, m. ‘the slayer of Dhenuka,’ an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—धेनुका-दुग्ध, अम्, n.<BR>cow's milk; N. of a plant, = धेनु-दुग्ध.<BR>—धे-<BR>नुकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of Dhenuka,’ an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa; a kind of small tree, = Nagesar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्टरी
धेनुष्टरी, f. (fr. धेनुस्, nom. case of धेनु,<BR>with the comparative affix), a milch cow ceasing to<BR>give milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्या
धेनुष्या, f. a cow whose milk has been<BR>pledged; a cow tied up to be milked (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्यित
धेनुष्यित, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) one who has<BR>pledged the milk of his cows and therefore cannot<BR>make use of it himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनूक
धेनूक in बहु-ध्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैनुक|धैनुकं
धैनुक, अम्, n. a herd of cows; a kind of<BR>coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेमात्र
धेमात्र धेमात्र, a particular high number;<BR>(a various reading for धमात्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेय
धेय धेय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. धा), to be<BR>held or taken &c.; to be created; what is created or<BR>produced; (at the end of comps. the neut. is con-<BR>sidered as an affix, Pān. V. 4, 36, vārt.; cf. नाम-<BR>धेय, भाग-ध्˚, मित्र-ध्˚, रूप-ध्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेष्ठ
धेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving the most;<BR>(Sāy.) the best supporter, firmest stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य|धैर्यं|धैर्य्य|धैर्य्यं
धैर्य 1. धैर्य, अम्, n. (fr. धीर), firmness,<BR>durability, steadiness, stability, strength, consistency,<BR>constancy; calmness; gravity; patience; fortitude,<BR>courage; inflexibility; precision of diction; (Ved.)<BR>intelligence, forethought.<BR>—धैर्य-कलित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, assuming firmness or composure, endowed with<BR>calmness.<BR>—धैर्य-ध्वंस, अस्, m. failure of<BR>courage.<BR>—धैर्य-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—धैर्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of firmness or<BR>patience, firm, steady.<BR>—धैर्य-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, of<BR>steady conduct, steadily behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत|धैवतः
धैवत धैवत, अस्, m. the sixth note of<BR>the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत्य|धैवत्यं
धैवत्य धैवत्य, अम्, n. (fr. धीवन्, Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 4, 174), cleverness, skilfulness (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवर
धैवर धैवर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. धीवर),<BR>belonging or relating to a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोईकवि
धोईकवि धोई-कवि, इस्, m., N. of a poet men-<BR>tioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati; [cf. धोयिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोड|धोडः
धोड धोड, अस्, m. a sort of snake, com-<BR>monly Dhora, a kind of water-snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोयिन्
धोयिन् धोयिन्, ई, m. or धोयी, ईस्, m., N.<BR>of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर्
धोर् धोर्, cl. 1. P. धोरति, दुधोर,<BR>धोरितुम्, to run well, to trot, to be<BR>quick or alert, to have good paces: Caus. धोरयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अदुधोरत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरण|धोरणं
धोरण, अम्, n. a vehicle in general, any means<BR>of conveyance (as a horse, an elephant, a car, &c.);<BR>a horse's trot; going well or quickly; (ई), f. or<BR>(धोरणि, इस्), f. an uninterrupted series; tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरित|धोरितं
धोरित or धोरितक, अम्, n. a horse's trot;<BR>[cf. धौरितक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत धौत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. धाव्),<BR>washed, cleansed, cleaned, purified, washed off;<BR>polished, brightened, whetted; white, bright, silvered,<BR>shining; (अम्), n. silver.<BR>—धौत-कट, अस्, m. a<BR>bag of coarse cloth, a sack made of kind of mat-<BR>ting.<BR>—धौत-कोषज or धौत-कौषेय or<BR>धौत-कौशेय, अम्, n. bleached or purified silk<BR>(= पत्त्रोर्ण).<BR>—धौत-खण्डी, f. sugar-candy.<BR>—धौत-बली, f. = धौताञ्जली, (probably rather<BR>धौताञ्जनी, q. v.)<BR>—धौत-मूलक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince of the Cīnas.<BR>—धौत-शिल, अम्, n.<BR>‘bright stone,’ crystal, rock-crystal.<BR>—धौताञ्जनी,<BR>f. a sort of collyrium, = त्र्यङ्कट or त्र्यङ्गट.<BR>—धौतापाङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having the corners of<BR>the eyes brightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतय
धौतय धौतय, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a<BR>kind of salt (= सैन्धव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतरी
धौतरी धौतरी, f. (fr. rt. 1. धू), Ved.<BR>(according to Sāy.) shaking, agitating, causing to<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौति
धौति धौति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 1. धाव्), Ved. a<BR>spring, well; river, rivulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौन्धुमार
धौन्धुमार धौन्धुमार, अस्, ई, अम्, treating<BR>of Dhundhu-māra (as an episode).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौन्धुमारि
धौन्धुमारि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Dhundhu-māra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमक|धौमकः
धौमक धौमक, अस्, m. (fr. धूम), N. of<BR>a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमत
धौमत, myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमतायन
धौमतायन, अस्, m. a patronymic (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमतायनक
धौमतायनक, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Dhaumatāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमायन
धौमायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Dhūma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमीय
धौमीय, अस्, ई, अम्, smoky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौम्य|धौम्यः
धौम्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Dhūma;<BR>N. of an ancient Ṛṣi; a son of Vyāghra-pāda;<BR>a younger brother of Devala and family priest of the<BR>Pāṇḍavas; a pupil of Vālmīki.<BR>—धौम्य-शिक्षा,<BR>f. ‘the science of Dhaumya,’ N. of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौम्र|धौम्रः
धौम्र, अस्, m., N. of an ancient Ṛṣi; N. of<BR>a class of demons; (अम्), n. grey (the colour), grey-<BR>ness; a place for building prepared in a peculiar<BR>way; [cf. धूम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौम्रायण
धौम्रायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Dhūmra;<BR>[cf. धूम्रायण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर|धौरः
धौर धौर, अस्, m. Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—धौरादित्य-तीर्थ (˚र-आद्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरितक|धौरितकं
धौरितक धौरितक, अम्, n. a horse's trot;<BR>[cf. धोरित and धोरितक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरेय|धौरेयः
धौरेय धौरेय or धौरेयक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>(fr. धुर्), fit to be harnessed, fit for a burden,<BR>capable of drawing or bearing a load (either a<BR>vehicle or beast, &c.); (अस्), m. a beast of burden;<BR>a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तक|धौर्तकं|धौर्त्तक
धौर्तक धौर्तक, अम्, n. (fr. धूर्त),<BR>roguery, knavery, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तिक|धौर्तिकं|धौर्त्तिक|धौर्त्तिकं
धौर्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, cheating, dishonest, roguish,<BR>knavish, fraudulent, &c.; (अम्), n. fraud, dishonesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तेय|धौर्त्तेय
धौर्तेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a warlike tribe;<BR>(अस्), m. a prince of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्त्य|धौर्त्यं
धौर्त्य, अम्, n. fraud, dishonesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्य|धौर्यं|धौर्य्य|धौर्य्यं
धौर्य धौर्य, अम्, n. a horse's trot, =<BR>धोरित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौवकि
धौवकि धौवकि, इस्, m. (fr. धुवका), a<BR>metronymic from Dhuvakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
ध्मा 1. ध्मा, cl. 1. P. धमति, दध्मौ,<BR>ध्मास्यति (ep. धमिष्यति), अध्मासीत्,<BR>ध्मातुम्, to blow (as wind or breath), breathe out,<BR>exhale; to blow (a conch-shell, trumpet, or any wind<BR>instrument), to produce sound by blowing; to blow<BR>a fire, excite fire by blowing; to excite sparks; to<BR>manufacture by blowing, melt, smelt; to blow away<BR>from one's self, cast, throw: Pass. ध्मायते, ep.<BR>and Ved. धम्यते, ध्मायति, to be blown, to be<BR>melted, &c.: Caus. ध्मापयति, &c., to cause to<BR>blow or melt, to consume by fire, burn: Desid.<BR>दिध्मासति: Intens. देध्मीयते, दाध्माति (दा-<BR>ध्मायते), to be blown violently; [cf. Lat. flā-<BR>re; Old Germ. blayan, blāhan, blāsan, ‘blow;’<BR>Gr. σμώ-νη, σμώ-ς ?].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्म
ध्म, अस्, आ, अम्, blowing; [cf. तूणव-ध्˚ and<BR>शङ्ख-ध्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
2. ध्मा, आस्, m. (?), blowing.<BR>—ध्मा-कार, अस्,<BR>m. a blacksmith, a smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मात
ध्मात, अस्, आ, अम्, blown (as a wind instru-<BR>ment), blown into, blown up, inflated, blown by a<BR>bellows (a fire &c.), inflamed, puffed, excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मातव्य
ध्मातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be blown, to be ex-<BR>cited or kindled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमातृ
धमातृ, ता, m., Ved. a blower, smelter (of<BR>metal); (तृ), n. a contrivance for blowing or<BR>melting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मान|ध्मानं
ध्मान, अम्, n. blowing, puffing, swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मापित
ध्मापित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), reduced to<BR>ashes, burnt to cinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मायत्
ध्मायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or ध्मायमान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being blown; being melted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माङ्क्ष्|ध्मांक्ष्
ध्माङ्क्ष् ध्माङ्क्ष् (various reading for<BR>ध्वाङ्क्ष्), cl. 1. P. ध्माङ्क्षति,<BR>&c., to crow or caw; to desire; [cf. ध्राक्ष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0460-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माङ्क्ष|ध्मांक्ष|ध्माङ्क्षः
ध्माङ्क्ष, अस्, m. a crow, &c.; (wrong form<BR>for ध्वाङ्क्ष, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मामन्
ध्मामन् ध्मामन्, आ, m. wrong reading for<BR>ध्यामन्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्या
ध्या ध्या, ध्यात, ध्यान. See under rt.<BR>ध्यै below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याम|ध्यामं
ध्याम ध्याम, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-coloured,<BR>black; (अम्), n. a fragrant grass in general or a<BR>particular kind of it; the plant Artemisia Indica<BR>(= दमनक).<BR>—ध्यामी-करण, अम्, n. mak-<BR>ing dark-coloured, blackening.<BR>—ध्यामी-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made dark-coloured, blackened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामक|ध्यामकं
ध्यामक, अम्, n. a particular kind of grass<BR>(= रोहिष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्युषिताश्व
ध्युषिताश्व ध्युषिताश्व, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince; (a various reading for व्युषिताश्व.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यै
ध्यै ध्यै [cf. the older form 1. धी], cl.<BR>1. P. (ep. also A.) ध्यायति (ep. also ध्याति,<BR>2nd sing. Impv. ध्याहि), Pot. ध्यायेत्, दध्यौ,<BR>ध्याता, ध्यास्यति, अध्यासीत्, ध्यातुम्, to think<BR>of, have in mind, imagine, contemplate, ponder,<BR>meditate, think on, meditate on, reflect upon (with<BR>or without मनसा or मनसि or चेतसा or धिया),<BR>to call to mind, recollect: Caus. ध्यापयति, -यितुम्:<BR>Desid. दिध्यासति: Intens. दाध्यायते, दाध्याति,<BR>दाध्येति; [cf. Gr. θέα, θεά-ο-μαι, related to ध्यै,<BR>as Lat. vid-ere to Sanskrit विद्, ‘to know;’ or as<BR>Zend बुध्, ‘to see,’ to Sanskrit बुध्, ‘to know.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्या
ध्या, आस्, f. thinking, thought, meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, thought of, meditated on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातव्य
ध्यातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thought of or re-<BR>flected upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातृ
ध्यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who reflects upon or<BR>meditates; a thinker, reflector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात्व
ध्यात्व, अम्, n. thought, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात्वा
ध्यात्वा, ind. having thought of or reflected,<BR>having pondered or recollected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यान, अम्, n. meditation, thought, reflection,<BR>especially profound and abstract religious contem-<BR>plation; divine intuition or discernment; mental<BR>representation of the personal attributes of a deity;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of the eleventh day in the light half in<BR>Brahmā's month.<BR>—ध्यान-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>attainable by meditation or reflection.<BR>—ध्यान-<BR>गोचर, अस्, m., N. of a class of Buddhist deities;<BR>[cf. ध्यानावचर.]<BR>—ध्यान-जप्य, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a race.<BR>—ध्यान-तत्पर, अस्, आ, अम्, lost in<BR>thought, absorbed in meditation, reflecting, medi-<BR>tative.<BR>—ध्यान-दीप, अस्, m. ‘the lamp of medi-<BR>tation,’ N. of a work.<BR>—ध्यान-द्युति, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—ध्यान-निष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged<BR>in meditation, contemplative, lost in thought.<BR>—ध्या-<BR>न-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, = ध्यान-तत्पर.<BR>—ध्यान-<BR>पारमिता, f., see पारमिता.<BR>—ध्यान-फल, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the fruit of meditation,’ N. of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva by Halāyudha.<BR>—ध्यान-भङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. interruption of thought or meditation.<BR>—ध्यान-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of reflection<BR>or meditation.<BR>—ध्यान-मात्र, अम्, n. mere re-<BR>flection, thought alone.<BR>—ध्यान-मुद्रा, f. the<BR>prescribed attitude in which to meditate on the deity.<BR>—ध्यान-योग, अस्, m. profound meditation, the<BR>performance of religious abstraction, (also explained<BR>as a Dvandva, meditation and abstraction); N. of a<BR>kind of magic mentioned in the Yoga-ratna-mālā,<BR>‘destroying one's enemies by images formed in the<BR>mind.’<BR>—ध्यान-लक्षण, अम्, n. ‘the mark of<BR>meditation,’ N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—ध्यान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, occupied in or intent<BR>on religious meditation.<BR>—ध्यान-विन्दूपनिषद्<BR>(˚दु-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad belonging to<BR>the Atharva-veda.<BR>—ध्यान-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, ab-<BR>sorbed in meditation; lost in thought.<BR>—ध्याना-<BR>वचर (˚न-अव्˚), आस्, m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>Buddhist deities; [cf. ध्यान-गोचर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिक
ध्यानिक, अस्, आ, अम्, proceeding from religious<BR>meditation, sought or obtained by pious contemplation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिन्
ध्यानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, contemplative, engaged in<BR>religious meditation, meditating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिबुद्ध|ध्यानिबुद्धः
ध्यानि-बुद्ध, अस्, m. (probably fr. ध्यानि,<BR>patronymic fr. ध्यान; cf. मानुषि-बुद्ध),<BR>a spiritual or mental Buddha, an incorporeal Buddha<BR>resulting from meditation, (their number is given as<BR>five or six or ten or more.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिबोधिसत्त्व|ध्यानिबोधिसत्त्वः
ध्यानि-बोधि-सत्त्व, अस्, m. (with Buddhists) an<BR>incorporeal son of a Dhyāni-buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानीय
ध्यानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to Vopa-deva<BR>26. 25, fut. pass. part.), to be meditated upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामन्
ध्यामन्, आ, m. measure; light; (अ), n. medi-<BR>tation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यायत्
ध्यायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, thinking of, considering,<BR>reflecting, meditating upon; supposing, imagining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यायमान
ध्यायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being reflected on,<BR>being meditated upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्येय|ध्येयः
ध्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be meditated upon, to be<BR>pondered or contemplated; fit for meditation; to be<BR>imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्र
ध्र ध्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. धृ), = धर<BR>(at the end of some comps., e. g. अंस-ध्री, मही-<BR>ध्र, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रज्
ध्रज् ध्रज् or ध्रञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. ध्रजति<BR>or ध्रञ्जति or धृञ्जति, &c., Ved. to<BR>move, go, glide (as a bird &c.); [cf. rt. धृज्,<BR>ध्रिज्, ध्वज्, ध्वञ्ज्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रजस्
ध्रजस्, अस्, n. (?), Ved. = ध्रजि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रजि
ध्रजि, इस्, f., Ved. the gliding course or motion<BR>of the wind, &c.<BR>—ध्रजी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>gliding, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राजि|ध्राजिः
ध्राजि, इस्, f., Ved. the gliding course of the<BR>wind, &c.; impulse; whirlwind, gale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रण्
ध्रण् ध्रण्, cl. 1. P. ध्रणति, &c., to<BR>sound (as a drum or other instrument);<BR>[cf. rt. धण्, 2. ध्वन्, 3. धारा; Gr. θρέ-ο-μαι,<BR>θρό-ο-ς, θρῆ-νο-ς, θρῦ-λο-ς, θρύλλος, θόρυ-βο-ς, τεν-θρη-δών,<BR>ἀν-θρη-δών, τον-θρύ-ς, τον-θορύζω; Goth.<BR>drun-yu-s, ‘voice;’ Angl. Sax. dran, ‘a drone;’<BR>Mod. Germ. drönen.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रस्
ध्रस् ध्रस्, cl. 9. and 10. P. ध्रस्नाति,<BR>ध्रासयति, -यितुम्, to glean; to throw<BR>or toss up, cast upward; [cf. उध्रस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रा
ध्रा ध्रा, cl. 2. and 1. P. ध्राति or ध्रति,<BR>ध्रयति, &c., Ved. to go, (Naigh. II. 14.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राख्
ध्राख् ध्राख्, cl. 1. P. ध्राखति, &c.,<BR>to be dry or arid, &c., = rt. द्राख्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राघ्
ध्राघ् ध्राघ्, cl. 1. A. ध्राघते, &c., to<BR>be able or competent, &c., = rt. द्राघ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राङ्क्ष्|ध्रांक्ष्
ध्राङ्क्ष् ध्राङ्क्ष् [cf. rt. ध्माङ्क्ष्,<BR>धवाङ्क्ष्, द्राङ्क्ष्], cl. 1. P. ध्राङ्-<BR>क्षति, &c., to utter the sound of birds, to crow,<BR>caw, &c.; to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राड्
ध्राड् ध्राड्, cl. 1. A. ध्राडते, &c., to<BR>divide, split, &c., = rt. द्राड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राडि|ध्राडिः
ध्राडि, इस्, m. gathering or plucking flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रि
ध्रि ध्रि (fr. rt. धृ) in अ-ध्रि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रियमाण
ध्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being held or sustained;<BR>being withheld or checked or suppressed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रिज्
ध्रिज् ध्रिज्, cl. 1. P. ध्रेजति, &c., to go<BR>or move, &c., = rt. ध्रज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रिज
ध्रिज in अ-ध्रिज, अस्, आ, अम्, unrestrainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु 1. ध्रु (connected with rt. धृ), cl. 1.<BR>6. P. ध्रवति, ध्रुवति, दुध्राव, &c., to<BR>be firm or fixed, to stand firm; to go, move; to ascer-<BR>tain, know with certainty; to kill: Caus. ध्राव-<BR>यति: Desid. दुध्रूषति, दुध्रुविषति: Intens.<BR>दोध्रूयते; [cf. Lith. drūtas, ‘firm;’ Goth. traua,<BR>‘I trust,’ = Caus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुति|ध्रुतिः
ध्रुति, इस्, f., Ved. (Sāy.) fixed destiny, settled course<BR>of fate; (according to modern scholars) misleading,<BR>leading astray, corrupting, seduction, (fr. rt. ध्वृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed, firm, remaining fixed<BR>in one place, firmly fixed, fast, immovable, stable,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-c" target="_blank">Page0461-c+ 81</a>]<BR>enduring, constant, lasting, permanent, continual, per-<BR>petual, eternal, invariable, unchangeable, inevitable;<BR>certain, sure, well-ascertained; firm, strong, fixed,<BR>settle (as a day); fixed (in astrology, as a करण,<BR>q. v.; the fixed Karaṇas are four, viz. Śakuni, Nāga,<BR>Catuṣpada, and Kiṃstughna or Kintu-ghna (?): the<BR>seven A-dhruvāṇi are given under करण: some of<BR>the Nakṣatras are also called Dhruvāṇi, see नक्ष-<BR>त्र); fixed (in anatomy, as certain members or<BR>organs of the body which cannot be severed without<BR>causing death, those which are separable being called<BR>अ-ध्रुव, q. v.); tenacious, retentive (e. g. ध्रुवा<BR>स्मृतिः, a retentive memory); (अस्), m. the polar<BR>star or the north pole itself (personified in mythology<BR>as son of Uttāna-pāda and grandson of the first<BR>Manu); the pole of any great circle (especially either<BR>of the celestial poles); polar longitude, the distance<BR>of a planet from the beginning of the sidereal zodiac;<BR>a constant arc; N. of one of the twenty-seven<BR>astronomical Yogas or the Yoga star of the twelfth<BR>lunar asterism (supposed to = ß Leonis?); a knot (?);<BR>the trunk of a lopped tree or pollard, a post, stake;<BR>the Indian fig-tree; the tip or point of the nose (?); a<BR>sort of bird, = शरारि, (perhaps incorrectly for स्म-<BR>रारि, meaning Śiva); the introductory stanza of a<BR>poem or song (‘the constantly recurring verse,’ which<BR>is repeated as a kind of burden or chorus); time,<BR>epoch, era, any fixed period from which dates are<BR>computed; an epithet of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu [cf.<BR>ध्रुवाक्षर]; of Śiva; N. of one of the serpents<BR>supporting the earth; N. of one of the Vasus; of a<BR>son of Vasu-deva and Rohiṇī; of an Āṅgirasa, sup-<BR>posed to be the author of a Ṛg-veda hymn (Ṛg-<BR>veda X. 173); of a son of Nahuṣa; of a hero on<BR>the side of the Pāṇḍus; of a son of Ranti-nāra (or<BR>Ranti-bhāra); (आ), f. the largest of the three sacri-<BR>ficial ladles (made in the shape of the Indian fig-leaf<BR>and of the wood of the Flacourtia Sapida?); the plant<BR>Desmodium Gangeticum; the plant Sanseviera Zey-<BR>lanica, a small tree from the fibres of which bow-<BR>strings are made (= मूर्वा); a virtuous woman; a<BR>cow which stands quiet when milked; scil. दिश्, the<BR>point of the heavens directly under the feet, the<BR>point of the lower hemisphere directly opposite to<BR>the zenith; (अम्), n. ‘the enduring sound,’ a sound<BR>heard or supposed to be heard after the Abhinidhāna,<BR>probably the mere prolongation of the preceding<BR>sound; heaven, sky, atmosphere; (अम्), ind. cer-<BR>tainly, surely, assuredly; eternally; (आय), ind. for<BR>ever. (According to grammarians, ध्रुव at the<BR>end of a comp. may give a bad sense to the word<BR>with which it is compounded, Pāṇ. II. 1, 53); [cf.<BR>Hib. dearbh, ‘sure, true;’ Goth. triggvs; Angl.<BR>Sax. treowe, for-truwyan; Old Germ. triu, triuwi,<BR>ga-triu, ga-triuwi, ga-triwi, = Mod. Germ. treu,<BR>treue, ge-treu, = Eng. true, trusty.]<BR>—ध्रुव-केतु,<BR>उस्, m. a kind of meteor.<BR>—ध्रुव-क्षित्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. resting firmly, abiding fixedly; abiding in the<BR>fixed (sacrifice).<BR>—ध्रुव-क्षिति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>having a firm position or abode.<BR>—ध्रुव-क्षेम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abiding in fixed habitations, having<BR>enduring mansions; firmly fixed.<BR>—ध्रुव-गति,<BR>इस्, f. a firm position; (इस्, इस्, इ), going firmly.<BR>—ध्रुव-चरित, अम्, n., N. of the twelfth and<BR>thirteenth chapters of the Svarga-khaṇḍa or third<BR>part of the Padma-Purāṇa; N. of the sixty-second<BR>chapter of the Liṅga-Purāṇa; of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—ध्रुव-च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. caus-<BR>ing to fall or shaking the immovable (mountains).<BR>—ध्रुव-तारा, f. or ध्रुव-तारक, अम्, n. the<BR>polar star.<BR>—ध्रुव-पटु, उस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Vallabhī or Ballabhī; [cf. ध्रुव-सेन.]<BR>—ध्रुव-<BR>योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a firm resting-place.<BR>—ध्रुव-रत्ना, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—ध्रुव-लक्षण, अम्, n.<BR>‘the mark of recurring stanzas,’ N. of a chapter<BR>of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—ध्रुव-सद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>Ved. resting on firm ground, abiding in a firm<BR>place.<BR>—ध्रुव-सन्धि, इस्, m., N. of a prince, son<BR>of Su-sandhi or Su-ṣandhi and father of Bharata.<BR>—ध्रुव-सिद्धि, इस्, m. ‘through whom conva-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">Page0462-a+ 77</a>]<BR>lescence is sure,’ N. of a physician at the court of<BR>Agni-mitra.<BR>—ध्रुव-सेन, अस्, m., N. of two Bal-<BR>labhī princes; [cf. ध्रुव-पटु.]<BR>—ध्रुवाक्षर<BR>(˚व-अक्ष्˚), अस्, m. ‘fixed and eternal,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—ध्रुवावर्त (˚व-आव्˚), अस्, m. the point<BR>on the crown of the head from which the hairs radiate.<BR>—ध्रुवाश्व (˚व-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0461-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवक|ध्रुवकः
ध्रुवक, अस्, m. polar longitude; the trunk of<BR>a lopped tree; a post, pale, stake; the introductory<BR>or recurring stanza of a song, see ध्रुव; N. of<BR>one of the attendants of Skanda; (आ), f. the intro-<BR>ductory stanza and burden of a song [cf. धुवका];<BR>N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवसे
ध्रुवसे (an infinitive form from ध्रुवस् which<BR>may be derived from ध्रुव), Ved. in order to rest;<BR>(Sāy.) for a firm seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवि
ध्रुवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. firmly fixed, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रौव
ध्रौव, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to Dhruva or the<BR>polar star; being in the ladle called Dhruvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रौव्य|ध्रौव्यं
ध्रौव्य, अम्, n. fixedness, firmness, immovable-<BR>ness, uninterrupted rest; duration; certainty, necessity;<BR>(अस्, &c.), conferring duration or fixedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु 2. ध्रु (said to be fr. rt. ध्वृ) in<BR>अ-स्मृत-ध्रु, not disappointing desire; (Sāy.) not<BR>remembering injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुत्
ध्रुत् in वरुण-ध्रुत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव्
ध्रुव् ध्रुव्, cl. 6. P. ध्रुवति, &c., to<BR>stand firm; to go, move; (various reading<BR>for rt. 1. ध्रु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रू
ध्रू ध्रू, cl. 6. P. ध्रुवति, &c., = rt. 1.<BR>ध्रु and ध्रुव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रेक्
ध्रेक् ध्रेक्, cl. 1. A. ध्रेकते, &c., to<BR>sound; to grow or increase; to be exhi-<BR>larated or elevated with joy; to manifest elevation<BR>or hilarity by noise; [cf. द्रेक्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रै
ध्रै ध्रै, cl. 1. P. ध्रायति, &c., to be<BR>satisfied or pleased; [cf. probably Gr. τρέφ-ω<BR>= Caus. ध्रापयामि, θρέψις, τρόφις, ταρφύς.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस्
ध्वंस् ध्वंस् (sometimes written ध्वस्),<BR>cl. 1. A. ध्वंसते (ep. also -ति), द-<BR>ध्वंसे, ध्वंसिष्यते, अध्वंसिष्ट, अध्वसत्,<BR>ध्वंसितुम्, to fall down, fall to pieces, fall to dust,<BR>be reduced to powder, decay, to be ruined; perish;<BR>to become eclipsed; to scatter or sprinkle over, cover<BR>with; to be covered or sprinkled with dust; (the<BR>imperative ध्वंस, ध्वंसत, = ‘be gone,’ ‘away<BR>with you,’ ‘vanish’): Pass. ध्वस्यते, to be destroyed,<BR>perish, &c.: Caus. ध्वंसयति, to cause to fall,<BR>fell, throw down, cause to perish, destroy; to inter-<BR>rupt; ध्वसयति, &c., Ved. to scatter, disperse<BR>(darkness &c.): Desid. दिध्वंसिषते: Intens. द-<BR>नीध्वस्यते and दनीध्वंस्ति, दनीध्वंसीति;<BR>[cf. Goth. drus, ‘to fall;’ drausya = ‘I fall,’ = Caus.<BR>ध्वंसयामि: Old Germ. troryu, ‘I gush.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस|ध्वंसः
ध्वंस, अस्, m. falling down, perishing, destruc-<BR>tion, demolition; vanishing, ceasing to exist, loss, ruin;<BR>(ई), f. a mote in a sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसक|ध्वंसकः
ध्वंसक, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of a comp.),<BR>destroying, causing to fall or perish, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसन|ध्वंसनं
ध्वंसन, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to fall, destroying,<BR>demolishing, ruining; scattering, dispersing; sprinkling;<BR>(अम्), n. perishing, dying; loss, destruction, ruin;<BR>falling; going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसनीय
ध्वंसनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to destruction,<BR>capable of being ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसयित्वा
ध्वंसयित्वा, ind. having destroyed; having<BR>interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसि|ध्वंसिः
ध्वंसि, इस्, m. (1/100) part of a Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसित
ध्वंसित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to fall, destroyed,<BR>demolished, ruined, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिन्
ध्वंसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling, perishing, being<BR>destroyed, decaying; causing to fall, destroying,<BR>destructive; (ई), m. a Pīlu tree (said to grow in<BR>mountainous districts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज्
ध्वज् 1. ध्वज् or ध्वञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. ध्वजति,<BR>ध्वञ्जति, &c., to go, move; [cf. perhaps<BR>Lat. vagus, vagari.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज्
2. ध्वज् = ध्वज in कृत-ध्˚, Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>83, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज|ध्वजः
ध्वज, अस्, rarely अम्, n. (connected with rt.<BR>1. ध्वज् and perhaps with rt. 1. धू), a banner,<BR>standard, flag-staff, flag, ensign, pennon; (meta-<BR>phorically) a distinguished or eminent personage<BR>(e. g. कुल-ध्वज, the head or ornament of a<BR>family); a mark, emblem, sign, symbol, character-<BR>istic mark [cf. कज्जल-ध्˚, धर्म-ध्˚, धूम-<BR>ध्˚, धूलि-ध्˚, वृषभ-ध्˚, &c.]; the attribute<BR>of a deity; the sign of any trade; the sign of<BR>a distillery or of a tavern [cf. सुरा-ध्˚]; the<BR>business there carried on; the penis &c., the organ<BR>of generation (of any animal, male or female); a<BR>skull carried on a staff as a mark of ascetics and<BR>Yogis; a house situated to the east of any object;<BR>a place prepared in a peculiar way for building; (in<BR>prosody) an iambic; (in Vedic grammar) N. of a<BR>peculiar kind of Krama-pāṭha; (in astronomy) N.<BR>of a Yoga; N. of a Grāma situated towards the<BR>north; (अस्), m. one who prepares or sells spirituous<BR>liquors; (according to some) pride, hypocrisy.<BR>—ध्वज-गृह, अम्, n. a room in which banners<BR>are kept or from which flags wave.<BR>—ध्वज-ग्रीव,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a neck erect as a banner,’ N. of a<BR>Rakṣas.<BR>—ध्वज-द्रुम, अस्, m. the palm tree<BR>(used for making flag-staffs, = ताल).<BR>—ध्वज-न-<BR>वमी, f., N. of a particular festival.<BR>—ध्वज-पट,<BR>अस्, m. ‘banner-cloth,’ the cloth of the flag, a flag.<BR>—ध्वज-प्रहरण, अस्, m. ‘striking banners or<BR>flags,’ air, wind, gale.<BR>—ध्वज-भङ्ग or ध्वज-<BR>पात, अस्, m. ‘fall or impotence of the male organ,’<BR>inability to procreate children; fracture or fall of a<BR>banner.<BR>—ध्वज-यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘banner-instru-<BR>ment,’ any contrivance to which a flag-staff is fastened.<BR>—ध्वज-यष्टि, इस्, f. a flag-staff.<BR>—ध्वज-राजिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, displaying flags or ensigns.<BR>—ध्वज-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, decorated or adorned with flags; having<BR>a mark or sign, bearing the mark of a criminal,<BR>branded; (आन्), m. an ensign, a standard-bearer; a<BR>distiller, a vendor of spirituous liquors; a Brāhman<BR>who having slain another carries the skull of the<BR>murdered man with him to places of pilgrimage by<BR>way of penance; (अती), f., N. of a divine female;<BR>N. of a divine attendant of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—ध्वज-<BR>स्तम्भ, अस्, m. a flag-staff.<BR>—ध्वजांशुक (˚ज-<BR>अं˚), अम्, n. ‘banner-cloth,’ a flag.<BR>—ध्वजाग्र-<BR>केयूर (˚ज-अग्˚), अम्, n. ‘the ring on the top of a<BR>standard,’ N. of a kind of abstract contemplation<BR>(among Buddhists).<BR>—ध्वजाग्र-निशा-मणि (˚ज-<BR>अग्˚), इस्, m. ‘the moon (night-jewel) of the standard-<BR>top,’ N. for a peculiar method of numeration.<BR>—ध्वजाग्र-वती (˚ज-अग्˚), f. ‘furnished with a<BR>standard-top,’ N. for a mode of reckoning.<BR>—ध्व-<BR>जारोह, probably a wrong reading for गजारोह,<BR>q. v.<BR>—ध्वजाहृत (˚ज-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, robbed<BR>or taken possession of at the standard, i. e. on the<BR>battle-field.<BR>—ध्वजी-करण, अम्, n. raising a<BR>standard, hoisting a flag; making anything a plea,<BR>setting up as a claim or right.<BR>—ध्वजी-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to set up a standard,<BR>hoist a flag; to use as a mark, sign, or pretext.<BR>—ध्वजी-कृत्य, ind. having raised a standard;<BR>having made a plea or pretext.<BR>—ध्वजोच्छ्राय<BR>(˚ज-उच्˚), अस्, m. erecting a banner; erection of the<BR>male organ.<BR>—ध्वजोत्थान (˚ज-उत्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘erection of a flag,’ a festival in honour of Indra,<BR>the twelfth day of the light half of the month<BR>Bhādra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिक|ध्वजिकः
ध्वजिक in धर्म-ध्वजिक, a hypocrite who<BR>only makes a pretence of religion; [cf. धर्म-<BR>ध्वज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिन्
ध्वजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with or bearing a<BR>flag, carrying a flag or standard, hoisting an ensign;<BR>(at end of comp.) having as a mark or sign; (ई), m.<BR>a standard-bearer; one having an emblem or sign;<BR>a distiller or vendor of spirituous liquors; a car,<BR>chariot, carriage; a mountain; a snake; a peacock;<BR>a horse; a Brāhman; (इनी), f. ‘a bannered host,’<BR>an army.<BR>—ध्वजिनी-पति, इस्, m. the leader of<BR>an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वञ्ज्
ध्वञ्ज् ध्वञ्ज्. See rt. 1. ध्वज्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वण्
ध्वण् ध्वण् (connected with rt. 2. ध्वन्),<BR>cl. 1. P. ध्वणति, &c., to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्
ध्वन् 1. ध्वन् (related to rt. ध्वंस्),<BR>Ved. to become covered or shut up, cover<BR>one's self, &c.: Caus. ध्वनयति, -यितुम्, to en-<BR>velope, wrap up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वांतं|ध्वान्तं
1. ध्वान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under 2. ध्वन्<BR>below), covered, enveloped, dark; (अम्), n. darkness,<BR>night.<BR>—ध्वान्त-चित्त, अस्, m. ‘perceived in the<BR>dark (?),’ a fire-fly; (also read ध्वान्त-वित्त.)<BR>—ध्वान्-<BR>त-जाल, अम्, n. ‘the net of darkness or the cover of<BR>night,’ a veil (?).<BR>—ध्वान्त-शात्रव, अस्, m. ‘enemy<BR>of darkness,’ N. of the tree Cassia Fistula; the sun<BR>or any luminary.<BR>—ध्वान्ताराति (˚त-अर्˚), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of darkness,’ the sun or any luminary.<BR>—ध्वान्तोन्मेष (˚त-उन्˚), अस्, m. ‘flashing or<BR>twinkling in the darkness,’ a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्
ध्वन् 2. ध्वन् (connected with rts. ध्वण्<BR>and ध्रण्), cl. 1. P. ध्वनति, द-<BR>ध्वान, ध्वनितुम्, to sound, produce a sound,<BR>utter sounds, buzz, roar, echo, reverberate: Caus. P.<BR>ध्वनयति and ध्वानयति, &c., to sound, cause<BR>to sound; [cf. Goth. drun-yu-s, ‘sound;’ Angl.<BR>Sax. dyn-an, dyne.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन|ध्वनः
ध्वन, अस्, m., N. of a wind; sound, tune; N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—ध्वन-मोदिन्, ई, m. ‘delighting by its<BR>sound,’ the humble-bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनत्
ध्वनत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sounding, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनन|ध्वननं
ध्वनन, अम्, n. sounding; hinting at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनयत्|ध्वनयन्त्
ध्वनयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to sound or<BR>resound, resounding, echoing with; (अन्), m., N. of<BR>a wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनि|ध्वनिः
ध्वनि, इस्, m. sound, echo, noise; tone, tune;<BR>thunder; the sound of a drum; an inarticulate sound,<BR>a mere empty sound without reality; a word; allu-<BR>sion, hint, figurative allusion, implied meaning,<BR>poetical style; N. of a work.<BR>—ध्वनि-कार, अस्,<BR>or ध्वनि-कृत्, त्, m. the author of the work called<BR>Dhvani.<BR>—ध्वनि-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘apprehending<BR>sounds,’ the ear; hearing.<BR>—ध्वनि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>figurative allusion, poetical style.<BR>—ध्वनि-नाथ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—ध्वनि-नाला, f., N. of<BR>several musical instruments, = काहला, a sort of<BR>trumpet; the Vīṇā or lute; a pipe, fife.<BR>—ध्वनि-<BR>बोधक or ध्वनि-बोधन, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of the grass Rohisha.<BR>—ध्वनि-विकार, अस्, m.<BR>a change of voice (caused by fright or grief, &c.).<BR>—ध्वन्य्-अर्थ, अस्, m. the meaning or truth<BR>implied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनित|ध्वनितः
ध्वनित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, making a noise<BR>(as a drum); alluded to, implied, figuratively or<BR>rhetorically expressed; (अम्), n. sound, thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्य
ध्वन्य, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान|ध्वानः
ध्वान, अस्, m. humming, murmuring, one of the<BR>seven kinds of speech or वाचः स्थानानि, (a degree<BR>louder than उपांशु, q. v.); sound or tone in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वानित
ध्वानित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to sound, made<BR>resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वांतं|ध्वान्तं
2. ध्वान्त, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a wind. (For 1.<BR>ध्वान्त see under 1. ध्वन् above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्
ध्वस् ध्वस्. See rt. ध्वंस्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्
ध्वस्, ध्वत् (fr. rt. ध्वंस्), (at the end of<BR>certain comps.) causing to fall, throwing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसन्
ध्वसन्, आ, m., Ved., N. of a king of the Matsyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसनि
ध्वसनि, इस्, m., Ved. the sprinkler; sprinkling,<BR>scattering (as a cloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसन्ति
ध्वसन्ति, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसिर
ध्वसिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sprinkled, spattered,<BR>covered; (Sāy.) destroyed; [cf. धूसर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen; destroyed, perished,<BR>hurt, lost; covered, eclipsed, disappeared.<BR>—ध्वस्-<BR>ताक्ष (˚त-अक्ष), अस्, ई, अम्, having the eyes<BR>sunk (as in death).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्ति|ध्वस्तिः
ध्वस्ति, इस्, f. ceasing, destruction, cessation (of<BR>all the consequences of actions), one of the four states<BR>to which the Yogin attains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्मन्
ध्वस्मन्, आ, m., Ved. polluting, darkening;<BR>(Sāy.) destroying, destructive; causing destruction.<BR>—ध्वस्मन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. covered?;<BR>(Sāy.) whose faults or imperfections are destroyed;<BR>(अत्), n. (according to Yāska) water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्र
ध्वस्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sprinkling, spattering;<BR>scattering, liberal; (Sāy.) destructive; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाक्षा
ध्वाक्षा ध्वाक्षा, f., N. of a plant and its<BR>fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष्|ध्वांक्ष्
ध्वाङ्क्ष् ध्वाङ्क्ष् [cf. rts. ध्माङ्क्ष् and<BR>ध्राङ्क्ष्], cl. 1. P. ध्वाङ्क्षति,<BR>&c., to utter the cry of birds, to caw, croak, crow,<BR>&c.; to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष|ध्वांक्ष|ध्वांक्षः|ध्वाङ्क्षः
ध्वाङ्क्ष, अस्, m. a crow; (according to some)<BR>any aquatic bird, as a crane, gull, &c., feeding on fish,<BR>= Ardea Nivea; (sometimes used at the end of a<BR>comp. to express contempt, e. g. तीर्थ-ध्वाङ्क्ष,<BR>a crow at a sacred bathing-place, i. e. a man in the<BR>wrong place); a beggar (on account of his insatia-<BR>bleness); an impudent fellow; N. of one of the Nāgas<BR>(= तक्षक); a house?; (in astronomy) N. of<BR>a Yoga; (ई), f. a kind of plant, = काकोली, कक्को-<BR>लिका, लघु-कावऌई; [cf. Hib. duis, ‘a crow.’]<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-जङ्घा, f., N. of a plant, = काक-<BR>जङ्घा.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-जम्बू, ऊस्, f. = काक-जम्बू.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-तुण्ड-फल, a kind of plant the<BR>fruit of which resembles the beak of a crow, (com-<BR>monly called Thora-śvetakāvaḷī.)<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-<BR>तुण्डा, ई, f. = ध्वाङ्क्ष-तुण्ड-फल; (ई), f. =<BR>काक-नासा.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-दन्ती or ध्वाङ्क्ष-<BR>नखी, f. = काक-तुण्डी.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-नामन्, आ<BR>or अ, m. or n. (?), a dark species of Uḍumbara;<BR>(नाम्नी), f. = काकोदुम्बरिका.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-ना-<BR>शिनी, f. = हपुषा (?).<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-नासा, f. and<BR>ध्वाङ्क्ष-नासिका, f. = काक-नासा.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-<BR>पुष्ट, अस्, m. the Kokila or Indian cuckoo, =<BR>काक-पुष्ट.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-माची, f. = काक-माची,<BR>= लघु-कावऌई.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-राविन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>cawing like a crow, having a voice like a crow.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्ष-वल्ली, f. = काक-नासा, = ध्वाङ्क्ष-<BR>दन्ती, = करञ्ज.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्षादनी (˚ष-अद्˚),<BR>f. = ध्वाङ्क्ष-दन्ती.<BR>—ध्वाङ्क्षाराति (˚ष-<BR>अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘enemy of crows,’ an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षिका
ध्वाङ्क्षिका, f. = काकोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षोलिका
ध्वाङ्क्षोलिका or ध्वाङ्क्षोली, f. a medicinal<BR>plant, = काकोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वांतं|ध्वान्तं
ध्वान्त ध्वान्त. For 1. and 2. ध्वान्त<BR>see p. 462, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृ
ध्वृ ध्वृ (connected with rts. ह्वृ and<BR>धूर्व्), cl. 1. P. ध्वरति, दध्वार, ध्व-<BR>रिष्यति, अध्वार्षीत् (3rd du. Aor. A. अध्वरि-<BR>षाताम् or अध्वृषाताम्); Prec. ध्वरिषीष्ट<BR>or ध्वृषीष्ट, ध्वर्तुम्, to bend, make crooked,<BR>cause to fall, fell; to kill: Caus. ध्वारयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्: Desid. दुध्वूर्षति, दिध्वरिषति: Intens.<BR>दाध्वर्यते; [cf. अ-ध्वर, 2. ध्रु; probably<BR>Angl. Sax. thwer, thweorh, thwir, thwur, dwelian,<BR>dol, dweorg, for-dwilman; Old Germ. dwer-an,<BR>ga-dwor, twar-ōn, dwerh; Goth. dvals; Gr. θόλ-ο-ς,<BR>θάλ-α-μο-ς.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वरस्
ध्वरस्, आस्, m. f., Ved. ‘destructive, hurtful,<BR>injurious,’ N. of certain female demons or noxious<BR>beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वर्य
ध्वर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bent, made crooked, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृत्
ध्वृत्, त्, त्, त् (at the end of a comp.), causing to<BR>fall, felling, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्व्रण्
ध्व्रण् ध्व्रण्, cl. 1. P. ध्व्रणति, &c., to<BR>sound; (a various reading for ध्रण्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न 1. न, the twentieth consonant of the<BR>alphabet, and the fifth letter of the fourth or dental<BR>class, having much the sound of the English n in<BR>tenth.<BR>—न-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न 2. न, ind. a particle of negation equi-<BR>valent to ‘not,’ ‘no,’ ‘nor,’ ‘neither’ [cf. नो, न-<BR>नु, न-हि, न-तराम्], and in the Veda a particle of<BR>comparison; it is used as a negative particle in wishing,<BR>requesting, and commanding (e. g. न मा गरन्<BR>नद्यः, let not the waters swallow me; नावमन्-<BR>येत कञ्चन, let him not despise any one), but not<BR>in prohibition before an imperative, and not before<BR>the aorist when it has lost its augment and stands for<BR>an imperative (in both which cases मा, q. v., is used).<BR>When joined with the potential, न may often have<BR>the sense of ‘that not,’ ‘lest,’ ‘for fear lest’ (e. g.<BR>न त्वां शपेत्, lest he should curse thee). In<BR>argumentative writings न often comes at the end of<BR>a hypothetical argument in the sense ‘not so’ (e. g.<BR>ननु न किञ्चिन् मानम् इति चेन् न, now if it be<BR>said that there is no proof, not so). Two नस् are<BR>not unfrequently used in the same sentence to intensify<BR>an affirmation (e. g. न खलु न तत् करिष्यामि,<BR>I will most certainly do that; न तु जातु न, most<BR>assuredly), or any other negative particle may be<BR>joined with न with the same effect (e. g. नादण्ड्यो<BR>ऽस्ति, he is not to go unpunished, i. e. he must cer-<BR>tainly be punished). When a negation has to be<BR>repeated in successive clauses of a sentence or in<BR>successive sentences, न may be simply repeated or<BR>may be strengthened by one of the particles उत, च,<BR>अपि, चापि, वा, अथवा (e. g. नाहम् अस्यारण्यस्य<BR>देवता न चाप्य् अस्य गिरेः, I am not the deity of<BR>this forest nor of this mountain), or the negative is<BR>not expressed in the second clause but represented<BR>by वा or अपि वा or च standing alone (e. g. न हृष्-<BR>यति ग्लायति वा, he neither rejoices nor desponds),<BR>or two clauses may have the negative particle and<BR>not a third (e. g. न देवेषु न यक्षेषु मानु-<BR>षेष्व् अपि चान्येषु तादृग् रूपवती दृष्ट-<BR>पूर्वा, neither among gods nor Yakṣas nor other<BR>mortals has so beautiful a female been before seen).<BR>न is sometimes placed before round or collective<BR>numbers to denote a deficiency, the deficient number<BR>being prefixed in the inst. or abl. case (e. g. एकया<BR>or एकेन न विंशतिः, not twenty by one, i. e. nine-<BR>teen; पञ्चभिर् न चत्वारि शतानि, 395). When<BR>न is the negative of the simple idea expressed by a<BR>word, it may be regarded as compounded with it,<BR>and is then identical with 3. अ, q. v. (e. g. न-विद्वस्,<BR>unwise; नाधीत, unread; न-किञ्चन, q. v.) न<BR>is often joined with other particles, e. g. न च, न<BR>चापि, नापि, नोत, न वा, नैव, न चैव, नापि<BR>च, न तु, न त्वेव, न त्वेव तु, न चेत् (see<BR>चेद्), न खलु, न ह (after this last a verb is<BR>said to retain its accent if used in the future with an<BR>imperative sense, Pāṇ. VIII. 1, 31). न is frequently<BR>used in early Vedic composition as a particle of com-<BR>parison = ‘like,’ ‘as,’ ‘as it were’ (e. g. त्वा नावं<BR>न धीमहि, we meditate on thee like a boat; cf.<BR>3. अ, which also in a few instances = ‘like’); it is also<BR>found in this sense in the later artificial poems; [cf.<BR>Lat. ne, non; Gr. νη in νη-κηδής;<BR>Lith. ne; Slav. ne; Goth. ni, ne, nei; Angl. Sax.<BR>na; Old Germ. ni; Hib. ni.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न 3. न, अस्, m. a N. of Buddha; binding,<BR>tying, a band; one who is praised; a N. of Gaṇeśa<BR>(= द्वि-रण्ड?); a jewel, pearl; war; giving, a<BR>gift; welfare, prosperity; (आ), f. the navel; a musical<BR>instrument; knowledge; (अस्, आ, अम्), thin, spare;<BR>vacant, empty; identical, same, like; unvexed, un-<BR>wearied; undivided, unbroken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न 4. न, (in prosody) a tribrach or foot<BR>of three short syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंश्
नंश् नंश्, the base of many forms of rt.<BR>2. नश्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंश
नंश, अस्, m. (?), Ved. (according to Sāy.) =<BR>नाशन, removal, removing, destruction; (but per-<BR>haps fr. rt. 1. नश्), acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंशन
नंशन, अम्, n. (?), destruction, in स्वप्न-न्˚,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंशुक|नंशुकः
नंशुक, अस्, ई, अम्, injurious, destructive; going<BR>astray, being lost; small, minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंष्टव्य
नंष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, destructible, to be injured<BR>or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंष्टृ
नंष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, a destroyer, destructive;<BR>perishing, being lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नःक्षुद्र|नःक्षुद्रः
नःक्षुद्र नः-क्षुद्र. See under 3. नस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्
नक् नक्, ind. (probably fr. rt. 2. नश्),<BR>Ved. night; [cf. 1. नक्त, 2. निश्, निशा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
1. नक्त, अम्, n., आ, f. (in the Veda नक्ता is regarded<BR>as f. du.), night; eating only at night as a sort of<BR>penance; a species of poisonous plant, = कलिकारु;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Pṛthu; of Pṛthu-ṣeṇa and<BR>Ākūtī; (अम्), ind. by night, at night; [cf. 2. निश्,<BR>निशा; Zend nakhturu or nakhtru, ‘nocturnal;’<BR>Gr. νύξ, νύκτωρ, νύκτερο-ς, νυκτερ-ινό-ς, νύχιο-ς,<BR>νυκτερί-ς; Lat. nox, noctu, nocturnu-s, noctua;<BR>Goth. nahts; Angl. Sax. naht, niht; Mod. Germ.<BR>nacht; Eng. night; Slav. noṣtĭ; Russ. nocyi;<BR>Lith. nakti-s; Hib. nochd.]<BR>—नक्त-चारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, going or moving about at night; (ई), m. an<BR>owl; a cat; a thief; a goblin, a Rakṣas; (also read<BR>नक्तञ्-चारिन्, which is the better form.)<BR>—नक्तञ्-<BR>चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going or walking about at night;<BR>(अस्), m. any creature or animal that goes about<BR>at night; a nocturnal fiend, a goblin, demon, evil<BR>spirit, Rakṣas; a thief; the bdellium tree, see<BR>गुग्गुल; (ई), f. a female demon.<BR>—नक्तञ्चरे-<BR>श्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord of the night-rovers<BR>or goblins.<BR>—नक्तञ्-चर्या, f. walking or moving<BR>about at night, wandering by night.<BR>—नक्तञ्-चारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, walking about at night, (opposed to दिवा-<BR>चारिन्, दिवा-चर); (ई), m. a cat; [cf. नक्त-<BR>चारिन्.]<BR>—नक्तञ्-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. grown or<BR>produced at night.<BR>—नक्तन्-दिन, अम्, n. night<BR>and day; (अम्), ind. by night and day.<BR>—नक्तन्-<BR>दिवम्, ind. by night and day.<BR>—नक्त-भोजन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘eating at night,’ supper.<BR>—नक्त-मुखा,<BR>f. evening, night; (a wrong reading for नक्त-<BR>मुषा.)<BR>—नक्तम्-प्रभव, अस्, आ, अम्, pro-<BR>duced at night; (also read नक्त-प्रभव.)<BR>—नक्त-व्रत, अम्, n. fasting by day and eating<BR>at night; any religious rite or obligation observed<BR>at night.<BR>—नक्तान्ध (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blind<BR>at night.<BR>—नक्तान्ध्य (˚त-अन्˚), अम्, n. blind-<BR>ness at night.<BR>—नक्तोषासा (˚त-उष्˚), f. du., Ved.<BR>night and morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तन्
नक्तन्, अ, n., Ved. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तम्
नक्तम्, ind. by night, at night. See under<BR>1. नक्त above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तया
नक्तया, ind., Ved. at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्ति|नक्तिः
नक्ति, इस्, f., Ved. night; [cf. Lith. nakti-s,<BR>‘night.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक
नक नक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Dāruka;<BR>(अम्), n. in भरद्-वाजस्य नकम्, N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकिञ्चन
नकिञ्चन न-किञ्चन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>nothing, very poor, beggarly; [cf. अ-किञ्चन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकिम्
न-किम्, ind. not, not at all; [cf. न-कीम् and<BR>मा-कीम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकिस्
न-किस्, ind. (किस् is said to be an old nom. sing.<BR>m. of कि, see किम् and cf. Lat. quis), Ved. not, not<BR>at all, never, (a little stronger than in the simple न);<BR>no one, nobody; (also written न-किर्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकीम्
न-कीम्, ind., Ved. not, not at all, never; [cf.<BR>न-किम् and मा-कीम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुच
नकुच नकुच, अस्, m. a various reading for<BR>लकुच, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुट|नकुटं
नकुट नकुट, अम्, n. the nose; [cf. नर्-<BR>कुटक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुल|नकुलः
नकुल नकुल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. न-कुल, without<BR>a family?), rejected from a family or race (?), disgraced (?),<BR>coloured like the ichneumon?; (अस्), m. the Bengal<BR>mungoose or Viverra Ichneumon (similar to the pole-<BR>cat and hostile to mice and serpents, from the poison<BR>of which it protects itself by a medicinal plant, cf.<BR>गन्ध-न्˚ and जल-न्˚); a son; N. of a Vedic<BR>poet with the patronymic Vāma-deva or Vāma-devya<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">Page0464-a+ 76</a>]<BR>or Vaiśvāmitra; N. of a Sāman (नकुलस्य वाम-<BR>देवस्य प्रेङ्खस्); N. of a son of Pāṇḍu or<BR>rather of the Aśvins by Pāṇḍu's wife Mādrī, he was<BR>twin-brother of Saha-deva, and fourth of the five<BR>Pāṇḍu princes; N. of a physician mentioned in the<BR>Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa, author of a work on horses;<BR>an epithet of Śiva; (ई), f. a female ichneumon;<BR>several plants, Salmalia Malabarica, = कुक्कुटी; Nar-<BR>dostachys Jatamansi, = जटामांसी; saffron, = शङ्-<BR>खिनी; a mystical N. of the letter ह् [cf. नकुलीश];<BR>(आ), f. an epithet of the wife of Śiva; (also read<BR>अ-कुला, q. v.)<BR>—नकुल-त्व, अम्, n. the state or<BR>condition of an ichneumon.<BR>—नकुलाढ्या (˚ल-<BR>आढ्˚), f. a plant (= गन्ध-नाकुली).<BR>—नकु-<BR>लान्ध-ता (˚ल-अन्˚), f. or नकुलान्ध्य, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of disease of the eye in which the eye becomes<BR>like that of an ichneumon and all objects have a<BR>variegated appearance; [cf. नाकुलान्ध्य.]<BR>—न-<BR>कुलीश (˚ली-ईश), अस्, or (according to others) न-<BR>कुलेश (˚ल-ईश), अस्, m. a form of Bhairava re-<BR>garded as an attendant on or emanation from Śiva;<BR>the letter ह् used mystically in the Tantras; [cf.<BR>नकुली.]<BR>—नकुलीश-योग-पारायण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Yoga work.<BR>—नकुलेष्टा or नकुलेष्टका<BR>(˚ल-इष्˚), f. ‘liked by the ichneumon,’ a plant, =<BR>नाकुली, गन्ध-नाकुली, (the mungoose if wounded<BR>in a conflict with a poisonous snake is supposed to<BR>prevent the effects of the venom by the use of<BR>this plant.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलक
नकुलक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), an ornament<BR>shaped like an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्क्
नक्क् नक्क्, cl. 10. P. नक्कयति, &c., to<BR>destroy, kill, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
नक्त 2. नक्त or नक्ल (?), अम्, n. (for 1.<BR>नक्त see p. 463, col. 3), = نقل N. of the fifth<BR>Yoga (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तक|नक्तकः
नक्तक नक्तक, अस्, m. dirty or ragged<BR>cloth; a rag, wiper, handkerchief, &c.; (a various<BR>reading for लक्तक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमाल|नक्तमालः
नक्तमाल नक्तमाल or नक्तमालक, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Pongamia Glabra or Dalbergia Arborea<BR>or Galeduba Arborea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्र|नक्रं|नक्रः
नक्र नक्र, अस्, m. (derived in Pāṇ. VI. 3,<BR>75, fr. न-क्र), a crocodile, an alligator [cf. नाक्र];<BR>the sign of the zodiac Scorpio; (अम्, आ), n. f. the<BR>nose; (according to others) a peculiar disease of the<BR>nose (= नासा-ज्वर, आहक-ज्वर); (अम्), n. the<BR>upper timber of a door-frame; (आ), f. a swarm of<BR>bees or wasps.<BR>—नक्र-राज्, ट्, or नक्र-राज, अस्,<BR>or नक्र-हारक, अस्, m. ‘king of the Nakras,<BR>seizer of the Nakras,’ a shark or any other large sea<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्ष्
नक्ष् नक्ष् (connected with rt. 1. नश्,<BR>cf. इनक्ष्), cl. 1. P. A. नक्षति, -ते,<BR>&c., Ved. to come near, come to, approach, visit,<BR>meet with, attain, gain, obtain; [cf. Lat. nanciscor,<BR>nactum.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्
नक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, approaching.<BR>—नक्षद्-<BR>दाभ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. striking down any one that<BR>approaches; (अस्), m. an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्र|नक्षत्रं
नक्षत्र, अम्, n. (fr. the above rt. in the sense<BR>of ‘coming or ascending;’ derived by some fr.<BR>नक्ष = नक्त + त्र, i. e. guarding the night, but<BR>this would not apply to the sun; also by some fr.<BR>न + क्षत्र, decaying ?), a star in general (also<BR>applied to the sun), a constellation, an asterism in the<BR>moon's path, a lunar mansion, of which, according<BR>to the earlier reckoning, twenty-seven are enume-<BR>rated, but in the later astrology more usually twenty-<BR>eight, distinct in name, figure, and number of stars,<BR>(the usual names are as follow: 1. Śraviṣṭhā or<BR>Dhaniṣṭhā; 2. Śata-bhiṣaj; 3. Pūrva-Bhādra-<BR>padā; 4. Uttara-Bhādrapadā; 5. Revatī; 6. Aśvinī;<BR>7. Bharaṇī; 8. Kṛttikā; 9. Rohiṇī or Brāhmī;<BR>10. Mṛga-śiras or Āgrahāyaṇī; 11. Ārdrā; 12.<BR>Punar-vasū or Yāmakau; 13. Puṣya or Sidhya;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-b" target="_blank">Page0464-b+ 81</a>]<BR>14. Āśleṣā; 15. Maghā; 16. Pūrva-Phalgunī;<BR>17. Uttara-Phalgunī; 18. Hasta; 19. Citrā; 20.<BR>Svātī; 21. Viśākhā or Rādhā; 22. Anurādhā; 23.<BR>Jyeṣṭhā; 24. Mūla; 25. Pūrvā Aṣāḍhā; 26.<BR>Uttarā Aṣāḍhā; 27. Abhijit; 28. Śravaṇa. In the<BR>Taittirīya-Brāhmaṇa, Śraviṣṭhās is given for 1;<BR>Pūrve Proṣṭha-padās for 3; Uttare Proṣṭha-padās<BR>for 4; Aśva-yujau for 6; Apabharaṇīs or Bharaṇīs<BR>for 7; Kṛttikās for 8; Invakās or Mṛga-śīrṣam<BR>for 10; Bāhū and Ārdrā for 11; Tiṣyas for<BR>13; Āśleṣās or Āśreṣās for 14; Maghās for<BR>15; Pūrve Phalgunī or Phalgunīs for 16; Uttare<BR>Phalgunī for 17; Niṣṭyā or in the Taittirīya-<BR>Saṃhitā also Svātī for 20; Viśākhe for 21; Anu-<BR>rādhās for 22; Rohiṇī or Jyeṣṭha-ghnī or Jyeṣṭhā<BR>for 23; Mūla-barhaṇī or in the Taittirīya-Saṃhitā<BR>also Vicṛtau for 24; Pūrvā Aṣāḍhās for 25;<BR>Uttarā Aṣāḍhās or Abhijit for 26; Śroṇā for 27:<BR>the names of the months Māgha, Phālguna, Caitra,<BR>Vaiśākha, Jyeṣṭha, Āṣāḍha, Śrāvaṇa, Bhādra,<BR>Āśvina, Kārttika, Mārgaśīrṣa, and Pauṣa were<BR>derived from the names of the corresponding twelve<BR>lunar mansions; according to some, certain Nakṣatras<BR>are called ध्रुवाणि, fixed, viz. Rohiṇī and the three<BR>double asterisms Uttara-Phalgunī, Uttarā Aṣāḍhā,<BR>and Uttara-Bhādrapadā. In the Vedas the asterisms<BR>are considered to be the abodes of the gods or the<BR>visible forms of pious persons after death, see Sāyaṇa<BR>on Ṛg-veda I. 50, 2; in the later mythology the<BR>lunar mansions are regarded as the wives of the<BR>moon and daughters of Dakṣa; according to the<BR>Jainas, the sun, moon, Grahas or planets, Nakṣatras,<BR>and Tārās or stars form the Jyotiṣkas); a pearl;<BR>[cf. देव-न्˚ and यम-न्˚.]<BR>—नक्षत्र-कल्प,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Pari-śiṣṭa belonging to the Atharva-<BR>veda and treating of the lunar mansions.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-कान्ति-विस्तार, अस्, m. ‘spreading brilliance (like<BR>that) of the Nakṣatras or constellations,’ the white<BR>Yāvanāla flower.<BR>—नक्षत्र-कूर्म-चार, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of Bhaṭṭotpala's commentary to Varā-<BR>ha-mihira's Bṛhat-Saṃhitā.<BR>—नक्षत्रकूर्म-वि-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. distribution of countries supposed to<BR>be under the dominion of the different lunar man-<BR>sions.<BR>—नक्षत्र-ग्रह-युत्य्-अधिकार, अस्, m.<BR>‘the chapter of the conjunction of asterisms and<BR>planets,’ N. of a chapter of the Sūrya-siddhānta.<BR>—नक्षत्र-चक्र, अम्, n. a particular diagram<BR>for astrological calculations; the sphere of the fixed<BR>stars; the lunar asterisms collectively.<BR>—नक्षत्र-<BR>चिन्तामणि, इस्, m. ‘Nakṣatra gem’ (see चिन्ता-<BR>मणि), N. of a work on lunar mansions.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-जा, आस्, m., Ved. ‘star-born,’ son of the stars.<BR>—नक्षत्र-तारा-राजादित्य (˚ज-आद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the sun as king of the stars and lunar asterisms;<BR>(with Buddhists) N. of a particular kind of religious<BR>meditation.<BR>—नक्षत्र-दर्श, अस्, m., Ved. ‘star-<BR>gazer,’ one who looks at the stars.<BR>—नक्षत्र-<BR>दान-विधि, इस्, m. ‘rules about the Nakṣatra<BR>offering,’ N. of the 153rd chapter of the Bhaviṣ-<BR>yottara-Purāṇa.<BR>—नक्षत्र-दोहद-शान्तिक, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of the lunar mansions,’ the<BR>moon.<BR>—नक्षत्र-निर्णय, अस्, m. ‘determin-<BR>ation of the Nakṣatras,’ N. of a chapter of the<BR>Tantra-sāra; N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नक्षत्र-नेमि, इस्, m. the pole star; the<BR>moon; an epithet of Viṣṇu; (इस्), f. the last of<BR>the asterisms, Revatī, containing thirty-two stars.<BR>—नक्षत्र-न्यास, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नक्षत्र-प, अस्, m. ‘protector<BR>or lord of the lunar asterisms,’ the moon.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-पथ, अस्, m. ‘the path of the Nakṣatras or<BR>stars,’ the starry sky.<BR>—नक्षत्र-पाठक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘reader of the stars,’ an astrologer.<BR>—नक्षत्र-<BR>पुरुष, अस्, m. (in astrology) the figure of a man's<BR>body on the limbs of which the various lunar aste-<BR>risms are distributed (e. g. Mūla on the feet, Jyeṣṭhā<BR>on the neck, &c., cf. काल-पुरुष; in this sense<BR>also written नक्षत्र-पुरुषक); a ceremony<BR>in which such a figure is worshipped; N. of the<BR>eightieth chapter of the Vāmana-Purāṇa.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-c" target="_blank">Page0464-c+ 80</a>]<BR>त्रपुरुष-व्रत, अम्, n. ‘the vow Nakṣatra-<BR>puruṣa,’ N. of the fifty-third chapter of the Matsya-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नक्षत्र-पूजित, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘star-<BR>honoured,’ favoured by the constellations.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-प्रकरण, अम्, n. ‘the Nakṣatra chapter,’ N.<BR>of the second chapter of the Cintā-maṇi Śāraṇikā<BR>by Daśa-bala.<BR>—नक्षत्र-फल, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>result obtained from the observation or influence of<BR>the lunar mansions,’ N. of a work on the lunar<BR>mansions.<BR>—नक्षत्र-भक्ति, इस्, f. ‘distribution<BR>of the Nakṣatras or explanation of the relation in<BR>which they stand to each other,’ N. of the fifteenth<BR>Adhyāya of Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-Saṃhitā; [cf.<BR>नक्षत्र-व्यूह.]<BR>—नक्षत्र-मार्ग, अस्, m.<BR>the path of the Nakṣatras.<BR>—नक्षत्र-माला, f. a<BR>ring or group of stars; the table of the asterisms in<BR>the moon's path, the asterisms collectively; a necklace<BR>containing twenty-seven pearls; a kind of dance.<BR>—नक्षत्र-याजक, अस्, आ, अम्, offering oblations<BR>to the lunar mansions; [cf. ग्रह-यज्ञ.]<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-योग, अस्, m. the conjunction of the moon with<BR>the lunar mansions.<BR>—नक्षत्र-योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>connected with the lunar mansions; (इन्यस्), f. pl.<BR>the chief stars in the lunar asterisms.<BR>—नक्षत्र-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘the king of the asterisms,’ the moon;<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—नक्षत्रराज-विक्रीडित,<BR>अम्, n. ‘moon-sport,’ N. of a particular kind of<BR>abstract contemplation.<BR>—नक्षत्र-लोक, अस्, m.<BR>the starry region, the firmament; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>world of the Nakṣatras.<BR>—नक्षत्र-वर्त्मन्, अ,<BR>n. ‘the path of the Nakṣatras,’ the sky.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-विद्या, f. ‘star-knowledge,’ astronomy.<BR>—नक्ष-<BR>त्र-वीथी, f. the path of the Nakṣatras.<BR>—नक्षत्र-<BR>वृष्टि, इस्, f. ‘star-shower,’ falling or shooting stars.<BR>—नक्षत्र-व्यूह, अस्, m. = नक्षत्र-भक्ति,<BR>q. v.<BR>—नक्षत्र-शवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. equal to<BR>the Nakṣatras in number?; (Sāy.) going to the<BR>gods.<BR>—नक्षत्र-शुद्धि-प्रकरण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of the first chapter of the Vivāha-vṛndāvana by Keśa-<BR>vārka, a work on the different lunar mansions re-<BR>garded as favourable or unfavourable to marriage.<BR>—नक्षत्र-समुच्चय, अस्, m. ‘the assemblage<BR>of the Nakṣatras,’ N. of an astrological work by Lalla-<BR>vārāha-suta.<BR>—नक्षत्र-सूचक, अस्, m. ‘star-indi-<BR>cator,’ an astrologer.<BR>—नक्षत्रेश (˚र-ईश), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of the Nakṣatras,’ the moon.<BR>—नक्षत्रे-<BR>ष्टका (˚र-इष्˚), f., Ved., N. of certain sacrificial<BR>bricks.<BR>—नक्षत्रेष्टि (˚र-इष्˚), इस्, f. a sacrifice<BR>or oblation to the asterisms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रिन्
नक्षत्रिन्, ई, m. ‘bearing the stars (?),’ an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रिय
नक्षत्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the Nakṣatras or to the stars in general, containing<BR>a number equal to that of the Nakṣatras, i. e. twenty-<BR>seven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्ष्य
नक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be approached or attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख्
नख् नख् or नङ्ख्, cl. 4. and 1. P.<BR>नख्यति, नखति and नङ्खति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to move, go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख|नखं|नखः
नख नख, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. नह्, perhaps fr. नघ् for rt. अङ्घ् = अङ्क्, to<BR>move in a curve; in Pāṇ. VI. 3, 75, derived fr. न +<BR>ख), a nail of a finger or of a toe, a claw, talon, the<BR>spur of a cock; an expression for the number twenty;<BR>(अस्), m. a part, portion; (अम्, ई), n. f. a particular<BR>perfume, a dried substance of a brown colour and of<BR>the shape of a nail, apparently a dried shell-fish (=<BR>शुक्ति) used as a perfume, see धूप्य; (ई), f. a vege-<BR>table perfume different from the above though known<BR>by the same name, नखी; [cf. Lith. naga-s,<BR>‘nail;’ Slav. nogŭ-tĭ = Russ. nogotĭ; Gr. ἔ-νυξ;<BR>Lat. unguis, ungula; Old Germ. nagal; Angl.<BR>Sax. naegel; Hib. ionga, perhaps for nionga.]<BR>—नख-कुट्ट, अस्, m. ‘a nail-cutter,’ a barber.<BR>—नख-खादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘eating the nails,’<BR>biting the nails.<BR>—नख-गुच्छ-फला, f. = नख-<BR>निष्पाव.<BR>—नख-छेद, अस्, m. nail-paring, nail-<BR>cutting.<BR>—नख-जाह, अम्, n. the root of a nail.<BR>—नख-दारण, अस्, m. ‘tearing with the nails,’<BR>a falcon, a hawk.<BR>—नख-निकृन्तन, अस् or अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-a" target="_blank">Page0465-a+ 80</a>]<BR>m. or n. (?), a pair of nail-scissors.<BR>—नख-निष्-<BR>पाव, अस्, m. or नख-निष्पाविका or नख-<BR>निष्पावी, f. a kind of pulse.<BR>—नख-पद, अम्,<BR>n. the mark of a finger-nail, a scratch.<BR>—नख-<BR>पर्णी, f. a species of plant (= वृश्चिका).<BR>—नख-<BR>पुञ्ज-फला, f. = नख-निष्पाव.<BR>—नख-<BR>पुष्पी, f. a species of grass (= पृक्का).<BR>—नख-<BR>पूर्विका or नख-फलिनी, f. = नख-निष्पाव.<BR>—नख-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘nail-divided,’ scratched<BR>or torn off with a nail.<BR>—नख-मुच, अस्, m. ‘nail-<BR>looser,’ a bow.<BR>—नखम्-पच, अस्, आ, अम्, nail-<BR>scalding, nail-scorching.<BR>—नख-रजनी, f. a species<BR>of plant and its fruit.<BR>—नख-रञ्जनी, f. a nail-<BR>parer.<BR>—नख-लेखक, अस्, m. a nail-painter.<BR>—नख-लेखा, f. a scratch; nail-painting.<BR>—न-<BR>ख-विलेख, अस्, m. a scratch; nail-painting (?).<BR>—नख-विष, अस्, आ, अम्, having venom in the<BR>nails or claws.<BR>—नख-विष्किर, अस्, आ, अम्, tearing<BR>or rending with the claws; (अस्), m. a bird of prey.<BR>—नख-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a species of plant (=<BR>नील-वृक्ष).<BR>—नख-व्रण, अम्, n. ‘nail-wound,’<BR>a scratch.<BR>—नख-शङ्ख, अस्, m. a small shell.<BR>—नखांशु (˚ख-अं˚), उस्, m. elegance or bright-<BR>ness of the finger-nails.<BR>—नखाङ्क (˚ख-अङ्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘nail-mark,’ a scratch; a sort of perfume (=<BR>व्याघ्र-नखी).<BR>—नखाङ्ग (˚ख-अङ्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a kind of perfume (= नली).<BR>—नखा-नखि, ind.<BR>nail against nail, (a fight with) mutual scratching,<BR>scratching one another.<BR>—नखायुध (˚ख-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘claw-armed,’ using the nails or claws as<BR>weapons; (अस्), m. an animal which uses its claws<BR>as weapons, any beast or bird having talons; a tiger;<BR>a lion; a cock; a monkey, &c.<BR>—नखायुध-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the state of being claw-armed or of using claws<BR>as weapons.<BR>—नखारि (˚ख-अरि), इस्, m., N. of<BR>one of the attendants of Śiva.<BR>—नखालि, इस्, m. or<BR>नखालिका (˚ख-आल्˚), f. a small shell; [cf. नख-<BR>शङ्ख.]<BR>—नखाशिन् (˚ख-आश्˚), ई, m. ‘eating<BR>with claws,’ an owl (as using its claws in feeding).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखक
नखक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga-rāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखर|नखरं|नखरः
नखर, अस्, आ, अम्, shaped like a claw, any<BR>pointed and curved instrument (as a knife, sword,<BR>&c.); (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. a finger-nail, claw; (ई),<BR>f. a kind of perfume (= नखी, = क्षुद्र-नखी).<BR>—नखरायुध (˚र-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘claw-<BR>armed,’ using claws as weapons; (अस्), m. a lion,<BR>tiger, any beast of prey; a cock.<BR>—नखराह्व<BR>(˚र-अह्˚), अस्, m. fragrant oleander (= कर-<BR>वीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखालु|नखालुः
नखालु, उस्, m. = नख-वृक्ष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखिन्
नखिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having nails, armed with claws<BR>or talons, clawed; thorny, prickly; (ई), m. an<BR>animal or a beast with claws, especially the lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग|नगः
नग न-ग, अस्, m. (fr. न-ग, not moving,<BR>or said to be fr. rt. 1. दह् through change of द् into<BR>न्, Uṇādi-s. V. 61), a mountain; a symbolical ex-<BR>pression for the number seven (because of the seven<BR>principal mountains; cf. कुल-पर्वत); a tree; a<BR>plant in general; a serpent; the sun; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>not moving, immovable; [cf. अ-ग.]<BR>—नग-ज, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, mountain, mountaineer; (अस्), m. ‘mountain-<BR>born,’ an elephant; (आ), f. a species of plant (=<BR>क्षुद्र-पाषाण-भेदा).<BR>—नग-नदी, f. ‘moun-<BR>tain-river,’ N. of a river.<BR>—नग-नन्दिनी, f. an<BR>epithet of the goddess Durgā (‘daughter of the<BR>mountain,’ Durgā being in one of her characters<BR>the daughter of the personified Himālaya).<BR>—नग-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘chief of mountains,’ the Himālaya range<BR>of mountains.<BR>—नग-भिद्, त्, m. ‘rock-splitter’ or<BR>‘tree-splitter,’ a species of plant (= पाषाण-भेद-<BR>न), Plectanthrus Scutellaroides; an axe; a crow; Indra.<BR>—नग-भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, ‘mountain-born,’ mountain,<BR>mountaineer; (ऊस्), m. a species of plant, = क्षुद्र-<BR>पाषाण-भेदा, (more probably fem. like नग-जा.)<BR>—नग-मूर्धन्, आ, m. the crest or brow of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—नग-रन्ध्र-कर, अस्, m. ‘rending<BR>the mountains,’ an epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—नग-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing mountains, abounding in<BR>trees.<BR>—नग-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘whose vehicle is<BR>a mountain, mountain-borne,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-b" target="_blank">Page0465-b+ 80</a>]<BR>—नग-स्वरूपिणी, f. a kind of metre consisting<BR>of four lines of eight syllables each.<BR>—नगाग्र<BR>(˚ग-अग्˚), अम्, n. the summit or top of a mountain.<BR>—नगाटन (˚ग-अट्˚), अस्, m. ‘moving about on<BR>trees,’ a monkey.<BR>—नगाधिप (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘chief of mountains,’ the Himālaya.<BR>—नगाधिराज<BR>(˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m. = the preceding.<BR>—नगारि (˚ग-<BR>अरि), इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नगावास (˚ग-आव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘living on trees,’ a peacock.<BR>—नगाश्रय<BR>(˚ग-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, living in or frequenting moun-<BR>tains; (अस्), m. a species of bulbous plant growing<BR>on mountains (= हस्ति-कन्द).<BR>—नगाह्वय (˚ग-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नगेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘chief of mountains,’ the Himālaya, Kailāsa.<BR>—नगेश (˚ग-ईश), अस्, m. ‘chief of mountains,’<BR>N. of a particular mountain.<BR>—नगोच्छ्राय (˚ग-<BR>उच्˚), अस्, m. heighth or elevation of a mountain.<BR>—नगौकस् (˚ग-ओक्˚), आस्, m. ‘inhabiting a moun-<BR>tain or tree;’ a lion; the fabulous animal Śarabha;<BR>a bird in general; a crow; [cf. अगौकस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगणा
नगणा नगणा, f. a plant, Cardiospermum<BR>Halicacabum; (also read नग्ना.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगर|नगरं
नगर नगर, अम्, ई (fr. न-ग?), n. f. a<BR>town, city, (often appended to the names of cities in<BR>India or standing alone as a name.) According to<BR>Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 39, the initial न् cannot be cerebralized<BR>[cf. गिरि-नगर]; at the end of adj. comps. the<BR>fem. may end in आ (e. g. स-ग्राम-नगरा मेदिनी,<BR>the earth with its villages and cities).<BR>—नगर-<BR>काक, अस्, m. ‘a crow in a town,’ an expression of<BR>contempt; [cf. नगर-वायस.]<BR>—नगर-कोटि,<BR>N. of a place; N. of a town at the foot of the Himā-<BR>laya, Nagar-kot.<BR>—नगर-घात, अस्, आ, अम्, town-<BR>destroying; (अस्), m. an elephant.<BR>—नगर-घा-<BR>तक, अस्, m. the destroyer of a city.<BR>—नगर-जन,<BR>अस्, m. towns-folk; a citizen.<BR>—नगर-द्वार, अम्,<BR>n. the gate of a town, city-gate.<BR>—नगर-धन-वि-<BR>हार, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist monastery.<BR>—नगर-<BR>पति, इस्, m. the chief of a town.<BR>—नगर-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—नगर-प्रदक्षिणा, f.<BR>carrying an idol round a city in procession; [cf. प्र-<BR>दक्षिणा.]<BR>—नगर-प्रान्त, अस्, m. the outskirts<BR>of a town.<BR>—नगर-मर्दिन्, ई, m. ‘town-crusher,’<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—नगर-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, garlanded<BR>with cities.<BR>—नगर-मुस्ता, f. = नगरोत्था; [cf.<BR>नागर-मुस्ता.]<BR>—नगर-रक्षा, f. superintend-<BR>ence or government of a town.<BR>—नगररक्षा-<BR>धिकृत (˚क्षा-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, appointed to<BR>the government of a town.<BR>—नगर-रक्षिन्,<BR>ई, m. the governor or superintendent of a town,<BR>civic-guard, town-watchman.<BR>—नगर-वायस, अस्,<BR>m. = नगर-काक.<BR>—नगर-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, in-<BR>habiting towns, dwelling in cities, citizen.<BR>—नगर-<BR>वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, situated without the town.<BR>—नग-<BR>र-सम्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, equal to a town.<BR>—नगर-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, city-dwelling; a resident in a city,<BR>a townsman, citizen, burgess.<BR>—नगर-स्वरूपिणी,<BR>f. a species of the Anu-ṣṭubh metre.<BR>—नगर-<BR>हार, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), ‘town-taking,’ N. of<BR>a kingdom.<BR>—नगराधिकृत (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the superintendent or governor of a town.<BR>—नगरा-<BR>धिप (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m. or नगराधिपति, इस्,<BR>m. the chief magistrate of a town, head police-officer.<BR>—नगराध्यक्ष (˚र-अध्˚), अस्, m. the over-<BR>seer or superintendent of a town.<BR>—नगराभ्याश<BR>(˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the neighbourhood of a city.<BR>—नगरी-निरोध, अस्, m., N. of the sixty-third<BR>chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa or second part of the<BR>Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—नगरी-युक्ति, इस्, f., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Yukti-kalpa-taru ascribed to king<BR>Bhoja.<BR>—नगरी-रक्षिन्, ई, m. = नगर-रक्षिन्.<BR>—नगरी-वक, अस्, m. ‘town-crane,’ a crow.<BR>—नगरोत्था (˚र-उत्था), f. a species of plant, =<BR>नगर-मुस्ता; [cf. नागरोत्था.]<BR>—नगरोपान्त<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n. suburb, skirts of a town.<BR>—नग-<BR>रौकस् (˚र-ओक्˚), आस्, m. the inhabitant of a town,<BR>townsman.<BR>—नगरौषधि (˚र-ओष्˚), इस्, f. the<BR>plantain, Musa Sapientum (= कदली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगराय
नगराय, Nom. P. नगरायते, &c., to have<BR>the appearance of a town, look like a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरिन्
नगरिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरीय
नगरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a town, civic,<BR>city, urban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न नग्न. See under rt. नज् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नहु
नग्नहु नग्नहु, उस्, m. or नग्नहू, ऊस्, m.<BR>ferment, a drug used for fermenting spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्ना
नग्ना 1. नग्ना, f. (for 2. नग्ना see नग्न<BR>below), Ved. speech; (a various reading for नना, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नघमार
नघमार नघ-मार, अस्, m. (fr. नघ, a<BR>disease? and मार), Ved. an expression for the<BR>plant कुष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नघारिष
नघा-रिष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. an epithet of<BR>plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नघुष
नघुष नघुष, अस्, m. = नहुष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नङ्ख्
नङ्ख् नङ्ख्. See rt. नख्, p. 464, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नङ्ग|नंग|नंगः|नङ्गः
नङ्ग नङ्ग, अस्, m. a lover, paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नचिकेतस्
नचिकेतस् न-चिकेतस्, आस्, or न-चिकेत, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Vājaśravasa; [cf. नाचिकेत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नचिर
नचिर न-चिर, अस्, आ, अम्, not long (in time),<BR>not of long duration; (अम्), ind. not long, for<BR>a short time; (एण or आत् or आय), ind. in no long<BR>time, in a short time, quickly, speedily, shortly, soon;<BR>[cf. अ-चिर and माचिरम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नच्युत
नच्युत न-च्युत = अ-च्युत, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नज्
नज् नज् (allied to rt. लज् = लज्ज्, of which<BR>it appears to be another form only found in<BR>the past pass. part. नग्न below), cl. 1. A. नजते,<BR>&c., to be ashamed, be modest or bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, naked, nude, bare; uncultivated,<BR>uninhabited, desolate; (अस्), m. a naked mendicant;<BR>a N. of Śiva; a hypocrite (whose nakedness is a<BR>mere pretence); a Buddhist mendicant, = क्षप-<BR>णक; a bard accompanying an army; (2. नग्ना),<BR>f. a naked, wanton woman; a girl before menstru-<BR>ation (and therefore allowed to go naked; cf. नग्-<BR>निका); the plant Cardiospermum Halicacabum; [cf.<BR>नगणा, 1. नग्ना above; Lith. nōga-s, ‘naked;’<BR>Russ. nagiĭ; Slav. nago-ta, ‘nakedness;’ Goth.<BR>naqvaths; Old Iceland. nakt-r; Angl. Sax. nacud,<BR>nacod, genacyan; Old Germ. nachat; Mod. Germ.<BR>nackt; Hib. nochd; Lat. nudus.]<BR>—नग्नङ्-<BR>करण, अस्, ई, अम्, making naked.<BR>—नग्न-जित्, त्,<BR>m., N. of a prince of the Gandhāras, father of one<BR>of Kṛṣṇa's wives; N. of an author of a work on<BR>architecture; of a poet.<BR>—नग्न-ता, f. or नग्न-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. nakedness, nudity.<BR>—नग्नम्-भ-<BR>विष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, or नग्नम्-भावुक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, becoming naked, uncovering one's self in a<BR>shameless manner.<BR>—नग्न-वृत्ति, इस्, f. ‘the men-<BR>dicant's commentary,’ N. of a commentary on the<BR>Uṇādi-sūtras.<BR>—नग्न-व्रत-धर, अस्, m. ‘observ-<BR>ing the vow of a naked mendicant,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—नग्नाट or नग्नाटक (˚न-अट्˚), अस्, m. a man<BR>who wanders about naked, especially a Buddhist or<BR>Jaina religious mendicant.<BR>—नग्नी-करण, अम्, n.<BR>making naked, undressing, stripping.<BR>—नग्नी-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to render<BR>naked, to convert into a naked mendicant.<BR>—नग्नी-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made naked, undressed, stripped;<BR>converted into a naked mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नक|नग्नकः
नग्नक, अस्, इका, अम्, naked, wanton; (अस्),<BR>m. a naked mendicant, especially a Buddhist or Jaina<BR>ascetic; a bard; (इका), f. a naked or wanton woman;<BR>a girl before menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्निका
नग्निका, f. a naked woman; a girl before men-<BR>struation or about ten years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नञ्
नञ् नञ्, ind. (in grammar) the technical<BR>term for the negative particle न, q. v., negation.<BR>—नञ्-अर्थ-निर्णय, अस्, m. ‘inquiry into the<BR>meaning of the negative particle,’ N. of a chapter of<BR>the grammatical work Vaiyākarṇa-bhūṣaṇa-sāra by<BR>Koṇḍa-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—नञ्-वाद-टिप्पणी, f. ‘commentary<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">Page0466-a+ 78</a>]<BR>to the chapter of negation,’ N. of a grammatical work<BR>by Raghu-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0465-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट्
नट् नट् (a corrupted form of the original<BR>rt. नृत्), cl. 1. P. नटति, ननाट, नटिष्-<BR>यति, &c., to dance, to dance or perform as an actor,<BR>to act; to injure by any deceptive trick; cl. 10. P.<BR>नाटयति, &c., to represent anything (acc.) drama-<BR>tically or by pantomime; to act; to drop or fall; to<BR>injure; to speak or shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट|नटः
नट, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. नम्, Uṇādi-s.<BR>IV. 104), a dancer, mime, actor, &c.; (in modern<BR>times) N. for a particular caste, the son of a degraded<BR>Kṣatriya by a woman of the second caste; the tree<BR>Calosanthes Indica [cf. कुटन्नट]; Jonesia Asoka<BR>(= अशोक); a sort of reed, Arundo Tibialis, or latterly<BR>called Arundo Karka (= किष्कु-पर्वन्); a subor-<BR>dinate mode of music; N. of a man who with his<BR>brother Bhaṭa built a Vihāra; (आ), f. a species of<BR>shrub, Cæsalpina Banducella; (ई), f. an actress, a<BR>dancer, a Nauch girl; a courtezan, harlot; a species<BR>of fragrant plant (= नली); red arsenic; N. of a<BR>Rāgiṇī.<BR>—नट-गति, इस्, f. a kind of metre con-<BR>sisting of four times fourteen syllables.<BR>—नट-<BR>चर्या, f. the performance of an actor.<BR>—नट-ता,<BR>f. the office or state of a player, condition of an<BR>actor.<BR>—नट-नारायण, अस्, m. a Rāga or mode<BR>of music, (according to some) the sixth, (or according<BR>to others) a subdivision of that called Dīpaka or of<BR>Megha.<BR>—नट-पत्त्रिका, f. Solanum Melongena.<BR>—नट-पर्ण, अम्, n. the skin (?).<BR>—नट-भ-<BR>टिक-विहार, अस्, m. ‘the temple of Naṭa and<BR>Bhaṭa,’ N. of a temple on the mountain Uru-muṇḍa.<BR>—नट-भूषण, अम्, n. ‘actor's ornament or<BR>pigment,’ orpiment.<BR>—नट-मण्डन, अम्, n.<BR>‘actor's ornament,’ yellow orpiment.<BR>—नट-रङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘actor's’ stage, a theatrical stage,’ a meta-<BR>phorical N. for anything illusory.<BR>—नट-वटु, उस्,<BR>m. (वटु said to be fr. rt. वट्), the son of an actor,<BR>a young actor.<BR>—नट-वर, अस्, m. a chief dancer<BR>or actor.<BR>—नट-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. a chief or excel-<BR>lent dancer or actor.<BR>—नट-सञ्ज्ञक, अस्, m. yellow<BR>orpiment; an actor, a dancer, &c.; [cf. नट-भू-<BR>षण and नट-मण्डन.]<BR>—नट-सूत्र, अम्, n.<BR>rules or directions for actors.<BR>—नटान्तिका (˚ट-अन्˚),<BR>f. shame, modesty; (also read नटान्धिका.)<BR>—नटी-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. the son of a dancing girl.<BR>—नटेश्वर<BR>(˚ट-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘the lord of dancers,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटक|नटकः
नटक, अस्, m. an actor.<BR>—नटक-मेलक, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the company of actors,’ N. of a comedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटन|नटनं
नटन, अम्, n. (derived fr. नर्तन), the act of<BR>dancing or representing dramatically, pantomime,<BR>&c.; a dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटित|नटितं
नटित, अम्, n. acting, representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटी
नटी, f. an actress, &c. See under नट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट्या
नट्या, f. a company of actors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट्टपट्टग्राम
नट्टपट्टग्राम नट्ट-पट्ट-ग्राम, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्
नड् नड् (connected with rt. नट् = नृत्),<BR>cl. 10. P. नाडयति, &c., to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (the n. does not seem to<BR>occur), a species of reed, Arundo Tibialis or Karka;<BR>(Ved. written नऌअ; cf. नल); (अस्), m. a particular<BR>tribe whose employment is making a sort of glass<BR>bracelets; N. of a prince with the patronymic<BR>Naiṣidha; (according to the commentator) = Nala<BR>Naiṣadha; N. of a Nāga; [cf. Lith. néndre†, ‘a<BR>reed.’]<BR>—नड-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in<BR>reeds.<BR>—नड-भक्त, अम्, n. a place abounding in<BR>reeds.<BR>—नड-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of reeds,<BR>made of reeds.<BR>—नड-मीन, अस्, m. a small fish, a<BR>species of sprat frequenting reedy places (= नल-<BR>मीन).<BR>—नड-वन, अम्, n. a thicket of reeds; N.<BR>of a place.<BR>—नड-संहति, इस्, f. a collection or<BR>quantity of reeds.<BR>—नडागार (˚ड-आग्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a hut of reeds.<BR>—नडा-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडक|नडकं
नडक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), the hollow of a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडकीय|नडकीयः
नडकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, abounding in reeds (as a<BR>field &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडस
नडस, अस्, ई, अम्, covered with reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडिनी
नडिनी, f. a quantity of reeds, a reed bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडिल
नडिल, अस्, आ, अम्, reedy, covered with reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्या
नड्या, f. a quantity of reeds, a bed of reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वत्|नड्वन्त्
नड्वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (नड् for नड), covered<BR>with reeds, abounding in reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वल|नड्वलः
नड्वल, अस्, आ, अम् (नड् for नड), abounding<BR>in reeds, reedy; (अम्), n. a quantity of reeds, a<BR>reed bed; (आ), f. a quantity of reeds; N. of the wife<BR>of Manu Cākṣuṣa; (also written नवला; cf. नाड्-<BR>वलेय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वाभू
नड्वा-भू, ऊस्, f. a house or hut of reeds (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडह|नडहः
नडह नडह, अस्, आ, अम्, lovely, beautiful,<BR>desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत्
नत् नत्, त्, त्, त् (fr. rt. नम्), bowing, bowing<BR>one's self, (at the end of comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत|नतं|नतः
नत, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, bowed, inclined, inclining;<BR>depressed, sunk; crooked, curved; (अम्), n. the<BR>zenith-distance at meridian transit; hour-angle or<BR>the distance of any planet from the meridian; (अस्),<BR>m. the plant Tabernæmontana Coronaria (= तगर,<BR>तगर-पादी).<BR>—नत-कन्धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘bowing the neck,’ bowing.<BR>—नत-ज्या, f. the sign<BR>of the hour-angle.<BR>—नत-द्रुम, अस्, m. = लता-<BR>शाल (?).<BR>—नत-नाडी or नत-नाडिका, f. hour-<BR>angle or the distance in time of any planet from the<BR>meridian; any hour of birth after noon or before<BR>midnight.<BR>—नत-नासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>depressed or flattened nose, flat-nosed.<BR>—नत-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. (in astronomy) zenith-distance.<BR>—नत-भ्रू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, bending the brow, frown-<BR>ing.<BR>—नत-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, bending down the<BR>face, looking down.<BR>—नत-मूर्धन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>bending or hanging down the head.<BR>—नतांश<BR>(˚त-अं˚), अस्, m. (in astronomy) zenith-distance.<BR>—नताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, bowing the<BR>limbs, bending the body, bent, curved, bowed,<BR>stooping; (ई), f. a woman.<BR>—नतोन्नत-भ्रू (˚त-<BR>उन्˚), ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, depressing and elevating the eye-<BR>brows, frowning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नति|नतिः
नति, इस्, f. bending, bowing, stooping; curvature,<BR>crookedness; a bow, a courtesy, modest behaviour;<BR>(in grammar) the change of a dental letter to a<BR>cerebral; parallax in latitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतमंहस्
नतमंहस् न-तम्-अंहस्, the beginning of<BR>a particular holy text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतराम्
नतराम् नतराम्, ind. (fr. न with the affix<BR>of the compar.), Ved. a strong negative particle<BR>equivalent to ‘not at all,’ ‘never.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्
नद् नद् (allied to rt. नर्द्), cl. 1. P.<BR>(ep. rarely A.) नदति (-ते), ननाद,<BR>नदिष्यति, अनदीत् and अनादीत्, नदितुम्, to vi-<BR>brate; to sound, resound, thunder (as a cloud); to<BR>roar, shout, cry, speak (often with the acc. of words<BR>denoting sound, e. g. शब्दम्, स्वनम्, नादम्,<BR>नादान्, रवान्, &c., thus नदन्तो भैरवान् ना-<BR>दान्, uttering frightful cries): Caus. P. नदयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to vibrate or shake (Ved.); नाद-<BR>यति, -ते, &c., to cause to sound or resound, fill with<BR>noise, make resonant: Intens. नानदीति, नानद्यते,<BR>to vibrate or shake violently (Ved.); to make a<BR>tremulous sound, to cry, roar (especially used of the<BR>lion), howl; to sound violently; [cf. rts. वद्,<BR>नर्द्; Cambro-Brit. nadu, ‘to cry.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद|नदः
नद, अस्, m., Ved. who or what sounds or makes<BR>a noise; a horse; a cloud (which thunders); a praiser;<BR>N. of a verse of the Ṛg-veda beginning with<BR>नदम् (Ṛg-veda VIII. 58, 2); a river (the per-<BR>sonification of which is male, as the Brahma-putra,<BR>Sone, Indus, &c.); any flowing water; (ई), f. a<BR>torrent, a river (the common personification of rivers<BR>being female); a kind of metre consisting of four<BR>lines of fourteen syllables each; (in grammar) a N.<BR>for crude bases ending in ई or ऊ, if like नदी they<BR>are invariably feminine (and not like ग्राम-णी<BR>which is both masc. and fem., see Pāṇini I. 4, 3).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">Page0466-c+ 80</a>]<BR>At the end of an adverbial compound नद becomes<BR>नदम् and नदी becomes नदि [cf. उप-नदम्,<BR>उप-नदि, and see Pāṇini V. 4, 110].<BR>—नद-<BR>नदी-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the male and female<BR>(personified) rivers,’ the ocean, sea.<BR>—नद-राज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘king of the rivers,’ the Sindhu, father of Śrī.<BR>—नदी-कदम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a plant.<BR>—नदी-<BR>कान्त, अस्, m. ‘lover of the rivers,’ the ocean; a small<BR>tree, Vitex Negundo; another sort of tree, Baring-<BR>tonia Acutangula; (आ), f. ‘beloved by rivers,’ the<BR>rose-apple, Eugenia Jambolana; a shrub, Leea Hirta;<BR>a species of creeper.<BR>—नदी-काश्यप, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a contemporary of Śākya-muni.<BR>—नदी-कूल,<BR>अम्, n. the bank or shore of a river.<BR>—नदीकूल-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond of river-banks,’ a species of<BR>reed, Calamus Rotang.<BR>—नदी-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, river-<BR>born, water-born, aquatic; (अस्), m. ‘son of the<BR>river,’ an epithet of Bhīṣma; several plants, Ter-<BR>minalia Arjuna; a species of reed (= यावनाल-शर);<BR>Baringtonia Acutangula; a species of grain (= नदी-<BR>निष्पाव); antimony; (आ), f. Premna Spinosa or<BR>Longifolia; (अम्), n. a lotus.<BR>—नदी-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, knowing the course of rivers.<BR>—नदी-तर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, crossing a river.<BR>—नदीतर-स्थान or<BR>नदीतर-स्थल, अम्, n. ‘a place for crossing a<BR>river,’ a landing-place, ferry, Ghāt.<BR>—नदी-तीर, अम्,<BR>n. the bank of a river.<BR>—नदी-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—नदी-दोह, अस्, m. a river-toll or<BR>tribute.<BR>—नदी-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘bearing the<BR>river Ganges,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—नदीन (˚दी-<BR>इन), अस्, m. ‘lord of the rivers,’ the ocean; Varuṇa,<BR>the god of the ocean; N. of a son of Saha-deva and<BR>father of Jagat-sena.<BR>—नदी-निष्पाव, अस्, m. a<BR>species of grain (= कटु-निष्पाव).<BR>—नदी-पङ्क,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘river-mud,’ the marshy bank of a<BR>river.<BR>—नदी-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the rivers,’ an<BR>epithet of the ocean; (metaphorically) the water of<BR>the ocean, sea-water (Ved.).<BR>—नदी-पूर, अस्, m.<BR>a river which has overflown its banks.<BR>—नदी-<BR>भव, अम्, n. river-salt.<BR>—नदी-मातृक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, nourished or watered by rivers (as land, rice,<BR>&c.); well-irrigated, possessing rivers.<BR>—नदी-मु-<BR>ख, अम्, n. the mouth of a river; a kind of grain;<BR>[cf. नन्दी-मुख.]<BR>—नदी-रय, अस्, m. the<BR>stream or current of a river.<BR>—नदी-वङ्क, अस्, m.<BR>the bend or arm of a river.<BR>—नदी-वट, अस्, m. a<BR>species of tree (= वटि).<BR>—नदी-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>stream-obstructing.<BR>—नदी-वेग, अस्, m. the stream<BR>or flow of a river.<BR>—नदी-वेला, f. the current or<BR>tide of a river.<BR>—नदीश (˚दी-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>the rivers,’ the ocean.<BR>—नदी-ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>नदी + स्न), bathing &c. in rivers; knowing the<BR>dangerous spots in rivers or their depth, course, &c.;<BR>(hence) versed in, experienced, clever in general.<BR>—नदी-सर्ज, अस्, m. the tree Terminalia Arjuna.<BR>—नद्य्-अम्बु-जीवन, अस्, आ, अम्, deriving its<BR>sustenance from river-water.<BR>—नद्य्-आम्र, अस्, m.<BR>a species of plant (= समष्ठिला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदत्|नदन्त्
नदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sounding, resounding, mak-<BR>ing a noise or cry, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदथु|नदथुः
नदथु, उस्, m. noise, sound; roaring; crying;<BR>din.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदन
नदन, अस्, आ, अम् (formed by Yāska to explain<BR>नद), sounding (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनिमन्
नदनिमन्, आ (?), m., Ved. sounding, humming,<BR>murmuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनु|नदनुः
नदनु, उस्, m., Ved. noise, roaring, sounding;<BR>the sound of approbation; thunder (?); a cloud;<BR>a lion; (according to the Naighaṇṭuka) = सङ्-<BR>ग्राम, war, battle; (Sāy.) = न-दनु, not giving.<BR>—नदनु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of<BR>sound, loud-sounding, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदि|नदिः
नदि, इस्, m., Ved. a crier, caller, one who calls<BR>out; (Sāy.) praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदिका
नदिका, f. in कु-नदिका, an insignificant rivulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदेयी
नदेयी, f. the plant Premna Herbacea; (wrong<BR>form for नादेयी?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्य
नद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, connected with a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदाल
नदाल नदाल, अम्, n. a potsherd, the<BR>fragment of a broken pitcher, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0466-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदी
नदी नदी. See rt. नद्, p. 466, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदृश्य
नदृश्य न-दृश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be<BR>seen, invisible.<BR>—नदृश्य-त्व, अम्, n. invisibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध|नद्धः
नद्ध नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 1. नह्),<BR>bound, tied, bound on, bound round, put on, fastened,<BR>joined, connected; covered, inlaid, embroidered, inter-<BR>woven; (अम्), n. a tie, fastening, band, bond, knot.<BR>—नद्ध-विमोक्ष, अस्, m. deliverance from<BR>fastenings or fetters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्धि|नद्धिः
नद्धि, इस्, f. binding, fastening; [cf. बर्स-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध्री
नद्ध्री, f. a strip of leather, a leather thong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननन्दृ|ननंदृ
ननन्दृ ननन्दृ or ननान्दृ, आ, f. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. नन्द्), a husband's sister, a sister-in-law.<BR>—ननान्दृ-पति or ननान्दुः-पति, इस्, m. the<BR>husband of a husband's sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नना
नना नना, f., Ved. a familiar expression<BR>for ‘mother,’ corresponding to तत, q. v.; (according<BR>to the Naighaṇṭuka I. 11) = वाच्, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु न-नु, ind. (fr. 2. न + नु), a strong<BR>negative particle = ‘not at all’ (Ved.); a particle of<BR>interrogation = the Latin नोन्ने, ‘not?’ ‘is not?’<BR>‘are not?’ ‘does he not?’ often a particle of affir-<BR>mation = ‘is it not so?’ i. e. ‘it certainly must be<BR>so,’ hence = ‘certainly,’ ‘assuredly,’ or with an impe-<BR>rative = ‘pray,’ ‘do,’ ‘just,’ ‘well,’ ‘do now,’ &c., or<BR>sometimes with an interrogative pronoun (e. g. ननु<BR>को भवान्, pray who art thou?); in argumentative<BR>writings often a mere inceptive particle = ‘now then,’<BR>‘but then,’ ‘but’ (e. g. ननु न किञ्चिन् मानम्<BR>इति चेन् न, now if it be said that there is no proof,<BR>not so); नन्व् अस्तु तथापि, ‘well, be it so, never-<BR>theless;’ ननु च, ‘and (is it) not so?’ ‘is not then?’<BR>‘there can be no doubt.’ According to native lexi-<BR>cographers ननु is also a vocative particle = ‘ho,’<BR>‘hallo;’ a particle implying kindness, conciliation, &c.,<BR>= ‘pray,’ ‘good friend;’ a responsive particle; a parti-<BR>cle of reproach, perplexity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्तृ
नन्तृ नन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. rt. नम्), bend-<BR>ing, bowing, stooping; (in grammar) Ved. changing<BR>a dental to a cerebral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्तव्य
नन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bent or bowed, to<BR>be saluted, to be revered or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्त्व
नन्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be bent or bowed,<BR>to be humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्|नंद्
नन्द् नन्द् (thought by some to be for<BR>ननद्, a reduplicated form of rt. नद्, to<BR>utter sounds of approbation; the intial न् is never<BR>cerebralized), cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) नन्दति (-ते),<BR>ननन्द, नन्दिष्यति, अनन्दीत्, नन्दितुम्, to<BR>be pleased or satisfied with, to be contented with, be<BR>glad of anything (with inst., rarely abl.): Caus. नन्-<BR>दयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अननन्दत्, to make glad,<BR>gladden: Desid. निनन्दिषति: Intens. नानन्द्-<BR>यते, नानन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द|नंद|नंदः|नन्दः
नन्द, अस्, m. happiness, pleasure, joy, felicity,<BR>prosperity; a flute eleven inches long; N. of one<BR>of the two drums of Yudhi-ṣṭhira; of one of the<BR>nine inestimable gems or treasures of Kuvera; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a Buddhist deity, (also read नन्दन); of a<BR>Nāga [cf. नन्दक]; of a Nāga-rāja; of an attend-<BR>ant on Dakṣa; of a son of king Dhṛta-rāṣṭra [cf.<BR>नन्दक]; of a brother of Śākya-muni [cf. नन्-<BR>दक]; of a son of Vasu-deva; of a cowherd who<BR>was the foster-father of Kṛṣṇa and apparently also<BR>of Durgā; of a leader of the Sātvatas; of a king of<BR>Pāṭali-putra, cut off by the machinations of Candra-<BR>gupta's minister Cāṇakya, and founder of the Nanda<BR>dynasty; of a Buddhist writer on law [cf. नन्द-<BR>पण्डित]; of a mountain [cf. नन्दि-गिरि]; (आ),<BR>f. Delight, Felicity (personified as the wife of Har-<BR>sha, cf. नन्दि), prosperity, happiness, joy; a small<BR>earthen water-jar [cf. नन्दिका]; a husband's sister<BR>[cf. ननान्दृ]; N. of one of the seven or five small<BR>Kumārīs or staffs of Indra's standard, (according to<BR>a commentator नन्दा and उप-नन्दा); the first,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-b" target="_blank">Page0467-b+ 81</a>]<BR>sixth, or eleventh day of the fortnight, considered as<BR>three auspicious Tithis [cf. नन्दिका]; an epithet of<BR>Gaurī; a form of Dākṣāyaṇī; N. of an Apsaras,<BR>(also read काम्या); of the eldest daughter of Vi-<BR>bhīṣaṇa; N. of a girl connected with Śākya-muni,<BR>(also read नन्दी); of the mother of the tenth Arhat<BR>of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; N. of a wife of Gopāla-<BR>varman; of a river flowing near Kuvera's city Alakā,<BR>(often mentioned with अपर-नन्दा; cf. नन्दा-<BR>तीर्थ); (ई), f. the tree Cedrela Toona [cf. नन्दी-<BR>वृक्ष]; an epithet of Durgā; N. of Indra's resi-<BR>dence, = अमरा-वती; [cf. आ-न्˚, अलक-न्˚, गो-न्˚.]<BR>—नन्द-किशोर, अस्, m., N. of the author of a<BR>supplement to Vopa-deva's Mugdha-bodha.<BR>—नन्द-<BR>गोप, अस्, m. the cowherd Nanda.<BR>—नन्दगोप-<BR>कुमार, अस्, m. ‘son of the cowherd Nanda,’ epi-<BR>thet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—नन्द-गोपिता, f., N. of a plant,<BR>see रास्ना.<BR>—नन्द-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘the foster-<BR>son of the cowherd Nanda,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—नन्द-नन्दनी, f. ‘daughter of the cowherd<BR>Nanda,’ epithet of Durgā.<BR>—नन्द-पण्डित, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a writer on jurisprudence.<BR>—नन्द-पद्र,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—नन्द-पाल, अस्, m. ‘guardian of<BR>the treasure Nanda,’ epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—नन्द-<BR>पुत्री, f. ‘daughter of the cowherd Nanda,’ epithet<BR>of Durgā.<BR>—नन्द-पुत्रोत्सव (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the ninth chapter of the Kṛṣṇa-khaṇḍa or<BR>fourth part of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्द-<BR>प्रयाग, अस्, m., N. of a place mentioned in the<BR>Rasika-ramaṇa by Raghu-nātha (at the confluence<BR>of two rivers containing the word नन्द in their<BR>names).<BR>—नन्द-बला, f., N. of a girl connected<BR>with Śākya-muni.<BR>—नन्द-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—नन्द-वर्धन, अस्, m. ‘joy-increaser,’<BR>N. of a poet mentioned in the Śārṅgadhara-pad-<BR>dhati.<BR>—नन्द-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नन्दा-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha (the river<BR>Nandā?).<BR>—नन्दात्मज (˚द-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘son of<BR>the cowherd Nanda,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa; (आ), f.<BR>‘daughter of the cowherd Nanda,’ epithet of Durgā.<BR>—नन्दा-पुराण, अम्, n. ‘the Purāṇa treating of<BR>Nandā,’ N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दा-प्राची-<BR>माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of the eighteenth chapter<BR>of the Sṛṣṭi-khaṇḍa or first part of the Padma-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दाश्रम (˚द-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>hermitage.<BR>—नन्दा-ह्रद-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place.<BR>—नन्दी-पुर, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a town mentioned in the Kathārṇava.<BR>—नन्दी-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m., N. of several plants, = नन्दि-<BR>वृक्ष, Cedrela Toona; = मेष-श्रिङ्गी, Thespe-<BR>sia Populneoides; = स्थाली.<BR>—नन्दी-सरस्, अस्, n.,<BR>N. of Indra's lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दक|नंदक|नन्दकः
नन्दक, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoicing, making happy or<BR>glad, causing pleasure, gladdening; rejoicing or de-<BR>lighting in; rejoicing a family; joyful; (अस्), m.<BR>a frog (= नन्दन); N. of Kṛṣṇa's sword; of a<BR>Nāga [cf. नन्द]; of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a son of king Dhṛta-rāṣṭra [cf. नन्द]; of a<BR>Śākya [cf. नन्द]; of a bull; of a village; (ac-<BR>cording to some also) happiness, pleasure (= आनन्द);<BR>N. of the foster-father of Kṛṣṇa, = नन्द; (इका),<BR>f. a small water-jar [cf. नन्दा]; N. of three auspi-<BR>cious Tithis, the first, sixth, and eleventh, (according<BR>to the Tithi-tattva) the sixth Tithi [cf. नन्दा]; N.<BR>of Indra's pleasure-ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकि|नंदकिः|नन्दकिः
नन्दकि, इस्, m. (fr. नन्द्?), long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकिन्|नंदकिन्
नन्दकिन्, ई, m. ‘the possessor of Nandaka,’<BR>an epithet of Kṛṣṇa-Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दथु|नंदथु|नंदथुः|नन्दथुः
नन्दथु, उस्, m. happiness, joy, felicity, pros-<BR>perity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन|नंदन|नन्दनं|नन्दनः
नन्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, delighting, rejoicing, glad-<BR>dening, pleasing, making glad or happy; (अस्), m.<BR>‘rejoicing (a father),’ a son; ‘the rejoicer,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu; an epithet of Śiva; a frog [cf. नन्-<BR>दक]; a species of plant with a poisonous fruit,<BR>(according to commentators also f.); N. of one of<BR>Skanda's attendants; of a Siddha; of a Buddhist<BR>deity, (also read नन्द); of the seventh of the nine<BR>white Jaina Balas; of a mountain; of the twenty-<BR>sixth year in a Jupiter cycle of sixty years; of a par-<BR>ticular form of temple; (आ), f. ‘rejoicing (a mother),’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">Page0467-c+ 81</a>]<BR>a daughter; (अम्), n. a grove or garden frequented<BR>by the gods, especially Indra's pleasure-ground or<BR>elysium [cf. नान्दन]; N. of a sword (= असि-<BR>रत्न, cf. नन्दक); N. of a species of the Dhṛti<BR>metre (four times eighteen syllables); rejoicing,<BR>gladdening; joy, felicity; [cf. Hib. naoidhin, ‘an<BR>infant.’]<BR>—नन्दन-कानन, अम्, n. ‘the divine<BR>pleasure-grove,’ N. of a wood mentioned in the<BR>Rasika-ramaṇa by Raghu-nātha.<BR>—नन्दन-ज,<BR>अम्, n. ‘produced in elysium,’ yellow sandal-wood.<BR>—नन्दन-माला, f. ‘joy-causing garland,’ N. of a<BR>garland worn by Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—नन्दन-वन, अम्, n.<BR>the pleasure-grove of the gods; [cf. नन्दन, n.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनक|नंदनकः|नन्दनकः
नन्दनक, अस्, m. (at the end of a comp.)<BR>a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन्त|नंदंत|नन्दन्तः
नन्दन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, delighting, making happy;<BR>(अस्), m. a son; a friend; a king, a prince; (ई), f. a<BR>daughter; [cf. नन्दयन्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दयत्
नन्दयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, rejoicing, delighting,<BR>making glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दयन्त|नंदयंत|नन्दयन्तः
नन्दयन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, making happy, rejoicing,<BR>delighting; (also read नन्दन्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दायनीय
नन्दायनीय, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Bāṣkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दि|नंदि|नंदिः|नन्दिः
नन्दि, इस्, m. (for नन्दी see under नन्द),<BR>‘the happy one,’ epithet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; N. of<BR>an attendant of Śiva [cf. नन्दिन् and नन्दिकेश्वर];<BR>N. of a man; of a Gandharva; (according to some<BR>also) the speaker of the prologue or prelude to a<BR>drama or one who pronounces the benediction, see<BR>नान्दी, नान्दिन्; (इस्, इ), m. n. gambling, gaming;<BR>(इस्), f. joy, delight, pleasure, happiness, prosperity,<BR>welfare, (in these senses said to be also m. n.); Joy<BR>personified as a daughter of Heaven or as the wife of<BR>Kāma and mother of Harṣa.<BR>—नन्दि-कुण्ड, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>क्षेत्र, अम्, n., N. of a district frequented by the<BR>gods.<BR>—नन्दि-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain; [cf.<BR>नन्दि-देवी.]<BR>—नन्दिगिरि-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>glory of Nandi-giri,’ N. of a work.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a prince of Kaśmīra.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a village (near the modern<BR>Daulatābād, where Bharata resided during Rāma's<BR>banishment).<BR>—नन्दिग्राम-दर्शन, अम्, n.<BR>‘description of the village Nandi-grāma,’ the twenty-<BR>ninth chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa of the Padma-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दि-घोष, अस्, m. cry of joy (=<BR>वन्दि-घोष); the proclamation of a panegyrist<BR>or herald; the chariot of Arjuna.<BR>—नन्दि-तरु, उस्,<BR>m. = धव, the tree Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>तूर्य, अम्, n. a musical instrument played on joyful<BR>occasions.<BR>—नन्दि-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man; (ई), ? the<BR>common N. of one of the loftiest Himalayan peaks.<BR>—नन्दि-पुराण, अम्, n. ‘the Purāṇa of Nandi,’<BR>N. of part of the Kedāra-kalpa.<BR>—नन्दि-मुख =<BR>नन्दी-मुख, a species of rice [cf. नदी-मुख];<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—नन्दिमुख-सुघोष, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—नन्दिमुखसुघोषावदान (˚ष-<BR>अव्˚), N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—नन्दि-रुद्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of Śiva in a joyful or serene form.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, increasing pleasure, promoting<BR>happiness; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; a son [cf.<BR>नन्दन]; a friend; the end of a half month,<BR>i. e. the day of full moon or new moon; N. of a<BR>particular form of temple (= नन्दिन्); N. of a<BR>prince, son of Udāvasu or of Janaka, (in this sense<BR>also read नन्दि-वर्ध); N. of a place.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>वारलक, अस्, m. a species of fish.<BR>—नन्दि-वृक्ष<BR>or नन्दि-वृक्षक, अस्, m. the tree Cedrela Toona;<BR>[cf. नन्दी-वृक्ष.]<BR>—नन्दि-वेग, आस्, m. pl., N.<BR>of a people.<BR>—नन्दि-षेण or नन्दि-सेन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of one of Skanda's attendants.<BR>—नन्दिषेणेश्वर<BR>(˚ण-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—नन्दी-मुख,<BR>अस्, m. (नन्दी for नन्दि?), ‘having joy on the<BR>face,’ an epithet of Śiva; a species of aquatic bird;<BR>a species of rice [cf. नन्दि-मुख, नदी-मुख,<BR>नान्दी-मुखी]; (आस्), m. pl. a class of manes or<BR>deceased ancestors who are worshipped on festival<BR>occasions [cf. नान्दी-मुख]; (ई), f. sleep (in which<BR>the face shows joy), drowsiness; a species of the<BR>Ati-śakvarī metre; (more correctly नान्दी-मुख.)<BR>—नन्दीश (˚दि-ईश), अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">Page0468-a+ 79</a>]<BR>attendants [cf. नन्दि, नन्दिन्]; N. of Śiva; a kind<BR>of time in music (= नन्दीश्वर).<BR>—नन्दीश्वर<BR>(˚दि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of joy,’ an epithet of Śiva;<BR>N. of Nandin, the leader of Śiva's attendants; N. of<BR>one of Kuvera's attendants; N. of a place held sacred<BR>by the Jainas; a kind of time in music (= नन्दीश).<BR>—नन्दीश्वर-पुराण = नन्दि-पुराण.<BR>—नन्-<BR>दीश्वर-योगोपाख्यान (˚ग-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>the thirty-first and thirty-second chapters of the<BR>Uttara-khaṇḍa of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दीश्वरोत्-<BR>पत्ति (˚दि-ईश्˚, ˚र-उत्˚), इस्, f. ‘the birth of Śiva,’<BR>N. of the forty-second chapter of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्द्य्-आवर्त, अस्, m. a particular kind of<BR>diagram [cf. नन्दिकावर्त]; a sort of palace or<BR>temple built in the shape of the above diagram or in<BR>the form of a quadrangle without a western gate, (in<BR>this sense also अम्, n.); a species of large fish; a<BR>kind of tree; the shrub Tabernæmontana Corona-<BR>ria (= तगर, = भगवद्-द्रुम), probably the<BR>sacred fig-tree; a species of shell called so because<BR>of its convolutions (आवर्त).<BR>—नन्द्य्-उपपुराण,<BR>अम्, n. = नन्दि-पुराण.<BR>—नन्द्य्-उपाख्यान,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the episode of Nandi,’ N. of the forty-fifth<BR>to the fiftieth chapter of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0467-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिक|नंदिक|नंदिकः|नन्दिकः
नन्दिक, अस्, m. the Tūn tree (Cedrela Toona),<BR>the wood of which resembles mahogany and is used<BR>for furniture &c. [cf. नन्दी, नन्दी-वृक्ष]; N.<BR>of one of Śiva's attendants; N. of a pupil of Śākya-<BR>muni, chief of the village Uru-vilvā.<BR>—नन्दिका-<BR>चार्य-तन्त्र (˚क-आच्˚), N. of a medical work.<BR>—नन्दिकावर्त (˚क-आव्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>diagram (= नन्द्य्-आवर्त); a species of plant.<BR>—नन्दिकेश (˚क-ईश), अस्, m., N. of a temple or<BR>holy place.<BR>—नन्दिकेश-लिङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>thirty-ninth chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दि-<BR>केश्वर (˚क-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's chief<BR>attendants [cf. नन्दिन्, नन्दि]; N. of an author.<BR>—नन्दिकेश्वर-काशिका, f., N. of a Vedānta work<BR>by Nandikeśvara treating of the first of Pāṇini's gram-<BR>matical aphorisms as containing the dogmas of the Ve-<BR>dānta belief.<BR>—नन्दिकेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a sacred bathing-place mentioned in the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दिकेश्वर-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of an Upa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दिकेश्वर-संहिता, f., N. of a work<BR>mentioned in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—नन्दिकेश्वरा-<BR>भिषेक (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N. of the forty-third<BR>and forty-fourth chapters of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—नन्दिकेश्वरोत्पत्ति (˚र-उत्˚), इस्, f., N. of the<BR>twenty-first chapter of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिन्|नंदिन्
नन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ (at the end of a comp.), rejoic-<BR>ing, gladdening; happy, delighted; delighting in,<BR>liking; making happy, gladdening; (ई), m. ‘rejoicing<BR>(a father),’ a son; the speaker of the prelude or bene-<BR>diction at the opening of a drama [cf. नान्दिन्]; N.<BR>of several plants, the Indian fig-tree, Thespesia Popul-<BR>neoides, Phaseolus Radiatus; N. of a particular form<BR>of temple [cf. नन्दि-वर्धन]; N. of a being<BR>attending on Śiva and (commonly) of the bull on<BR>which he rides [cf. नन्दि, नन्दीश, नन्दिकेश्-<BR>वर]; N. of a Buddhist saint and teacher; (इनी),<BR>f. ‘rejoicing (a mother),’ a daughter; a husband's<BR>sister (= ननान्दृ); holy basil (= तुलसी); Nar-<BR>dostachys Jatamansi (= जटामांसि); a kind of per-<BR>fume (= रेणुका); a fabulous cow, daughter of<BR>Surabhi, related to the cow of plenty, and the property<BR>of the sage Vasiṣṭha; an epithet or a form of Durgā;<BR>an epithet of Gaṅgā or the Ganges; N. of one of<BR>the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; of a place; of a<BR>river (also called Vala-jā).<BR>—नन्दिनी-तनय or<BR>नन्दिनी-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of Nandinī,’ epithet of<BR>Vyāḍi.<BR>—नन्दिनी-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred<BR>bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दी
नन्दी, f. See under नन्द and नन्दि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्य
नन्द्य (fr. नन्द), Nom. P. नन्द्यति, &c., to<BR>be glad, to rejoice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दलाल
नन्दलाल नन्दलाल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीक
नन्दीक नन्दीक, अस्, m. (?), a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीट
नन्दीट नन्दीट, अस्, m. a bald-headed man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्नम
नन्नम नन्नम (fr. rt. नम्) in कु-न्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्नम्यमान
नन्नम्यमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Intens.),<BR>bending or bowing very low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपराजित्
नपराजित् न-पराजित्, त्, m. ‘having no<BR>conquerer,’ ‘not overpowered (?),’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपात्
नपात् नपात् and नप्तृ, ता, m. (in Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 96. derived fr. न + rt. पत्, ‘to fall;’ in Pāṇini<BR>VI. 3, 75, fr. न + पात् fr. rt. 3. पा, ‘to protect,’<BR>according to which latter derivation नपात्, नप्तृ<BR>are for न-पातृ, ‘not the protector,’ allied to न-<BR>पितृ, ‘not the father;’ but a more probable deriva-<BR>tion is fr. rt. 1. नभ्, an older form of rt. 1. नह्, ‘to<BR>connect,’ a descendant being ‘the connecting relative;’<BR>in the earlier Vedic language the strong cases are<BR>formed fr. नपात्, the weak fr. नप्तृ, e. g. acc.<BR>sing. नपातम्, dat. sing. नप्त्रे; in the later<BR>Sanskrit all the cases come fr. नप्तृ), a descendant,<BR>offspring in general, a son, &c. (Ved.); a grandson,<BR>a son's son, (in the later language restricted to this<BR>meaning); N. of one of the Viśve-devās; (according<BR>to Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā XIX. 56. न-<BR>पातः = देव-यान-पथः, the path of the gods;<BR>according to Sāyaṇa on Ṛg-veda X. 15, 3, नपातः<BR>= विनाशाभावः); (ती), f., Ved. a daughter; a<BR>granddaughter, (in Atharva-veda IX. 1, 3, नप्ति);<BR>नप्ती and नप्त्या, f. du. = (in Sāma-veda) ‘the two<BR>pieces of wood for pressing out the Soma,’ or =<BR>‘heaven and earth;’ or in Ṛg-veda IX. 9, 1, = ‘the<BR>hands;’ नप्त्यः, f. pl. in Ṛg-veda I. 50, 9, = ‘the<BR>female horses of the chariot,’ i. e. ‘the daughters of<BR>the chariot,’ (according to Sāy. so called ‘because<BR>with them the chariot does not fall’); in Ṛg-veda<BR>IX. 14, 5, नप्त्यः is said to = ‘rays’ or ‘fingers;’<BR>horses as ‘granddaughters of the chariot;’ the fingers,<BR>the hands; (त्री), f. a granddaughter, (नप्त्री, f., and<BR>not नप्ती, is the only form used in classical Sanskrit);<BR>[cf. तनू-नपात्, प्र-नपात्: Zend नप्तर्, नपत्,<BR>‘descendant;’ नप्त्-इ, ‘kindred;’ नप्त्य, ‘a family:’<BR>Gr. ἀ-νεψιό-ς for ἁ-νεπτιό-ς, quasi चोन्-नेपोत्-इउ-स्,<BR>νέπ-ο-δες: Lat. nepō(t)-s, f. nept-i-s: Old Iceland.<BR>nefi, ‘brother;’ nift, ‘sister:’ Old Germ. nefo,<BR>‘grandson, cousin;’ niftila, ‘female cousin:’ Goth.<BR>nithyi-s, m. ‘cousin;’ nith-yō, f. ‘a female cousin:’<BR>Slav. netii, ‘a brother's son:’ Boh. neti, base neter,<BR>‘a female cousin.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपात्क
नपात्क, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to a<BR>grandson; (applied to a particular sacrificial fire, =<BR>तृतीयो ऽग्निस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्तृका
नप्तृका, f. a species of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंस्
नपुंस् न-पुंस्, -पुमान्, m. not a man, a<BR>eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंस|नपुंसः
न-पुंस, अस्, m. not a male, a eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसक|नपुंसकं|नपुंसकः
न-पुंसक, अस्, अम्, m. n. neither man nor<BR>woman, a hermaphrodite; a eunuch, an impotent or<BR>imbecile man, a coward; (अम्), n. a word in the<BR>neuter gender; the neuter gender.<BR>—नपुंसक-<BR>पाद, अस्, m., N. of the eighth chapter of Durgā-<BR>dāsa's commentary on Vopa-deva's Mugdha-bodha,<BR>called Su-bodhā.<BR>—नपुंसक-लिङ्ग-सङ्ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the grammatical work<BR>Nāma-liṅgānuśāsana by Amara-siṃha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्तृ
नप्तृ नप्तृ, नप्ती, नप्त्री. See नपात् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
नभ् 1. नभ्, cl. 1. A. नभते, &c., Ved.<BR>to burst, to be torn or rent asunder; to<BR>hurt, injure, destroy, (नेभे occurs in Bhaṭṭi-kāvya<BR>XIV. 33); cl. 4. 9. P. नभ्यति, नभ्नाति, &c., to<BR>hurt, injure: Caus. P. नभयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to burst, tear open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
2. नभ्, प्, f., Ved. (according to Sāy.) hurt,<BR>injury, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभनु
नभनु, उस्, m. and ऊ, ऊस्, f., Ved. a spring,<BR>river, (water which bursts forth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभन्य
1. नभन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नभन), Ved. burst-<BR>ing out, breaking or coming forth (as a hymn or as<BR>a horse). According to Sāy. = ‘being in the sky,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-c" target="_blank">Page0468-c+ 80</a>]<BR>‘ethereal;’ ‘injuring,’ ‘destroying;’ ‘a hymn.’ (For<BR>2. नभन्य see under नभ below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभन्व
नभन्व, अस्, m., Ved. a river; (according to<BR>modern scholars the form is नभनु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ|नभः
नभ नभ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. नह्<BR>with affix भ, but rather fr. नभ् an older form of<BR>1. नह्, ‘to bind,’ ‘connect,’ as ‘connecting heaven<BR>and earth;’ according to others fr. rt. 1. नभ्, ‘to<BR>rend asunder or be broken up into clouds’), = नभस्,<BR>the sky, atmosphere; the month Śrāvaṇa (July —<BR>August); N. of a son of Manu Svārociṣa or of the<BR>third Manu (mentioned together with Nabhasya);<BR>N. of one of the seven sages of the sixth Manv-<BR>antara; N. of a demon, son of Vipra-citti by Siṃhikā;<BR>N. of a son of Nala (Niṣadha) and father of Puṇ-<BR>ḍarīka [cf. नभस्]; (आ), f. a spitting-pot (for<BR>नभास्?); N. of the city of the Sun; [cf. Zend<BR>nap-ta, ‘moist, wet;’ Gr. νέφ-ος, νεφ-έλη, ξυν-νέ-νοφε,<BR>νεφό-ω, probably δνόφος, ἰο-δνέφής,<BR>γνό-φος; Lat. nūb-ē-s, nūbilu-s, nēbula, probably Nep-<BR>tū-nu-s, nimbu-s for nembu-s; Old Iceland. nifl-<BR>heim-r; Old Germ. nib-ul; Mod. Germ. neb-el;<BR>Angl. Sax. ge-nip, ‘a cloud;’ Slav. neb-o, base neb-<BR>es, ‘sky;’ Lith. debes-i-s, ‘a cloud,’ through change<BR>of n into d, as in dewyni, ‘nine;’ Hib. neamh,<BR>‘heaven;’ Cambro-Brit. nev, ‘heaven.’]<BR>—नभ-<BR>ग, अस्, m. ‘going on the sky,’ N. of a son of Manu<BR>Vaivasvata; [cf. नभाग, नाभाग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभन्य
2. नभन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to Sāy.)<BR>being in the sky, ethereal, heavenly; (see col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्
नभस्, अस्, n. fog, vapour; a cloud; sky, atmo-<BR>sphere, ether or heaven; ether as one of the five ele-<BR>ments; N. of a month in the rainy season (= श्रा-<BR>वण) or July-August, (according to lexicographers in<BR>this sense m.); period of life, age; the vapour or<BR>fluidity of the Soma (Ved.); water (Ved.); the sun<BR>(according to Nir. II. 14); (आस्), m. a cloud, the<BR>rains or the rainy season; the nose, smell; the fibres<BR>in the root of a lotus or a rope made of lotus fibres;<BR>a spitting-pot; N. of a prince, son of Nala and father<BR>of Puṇḍarīka; (असी), n. du. both worlds, heaven and<BR>earth.<BR>—नभः-केतन, अम्, n. ‘sky-banner,’ the<BR>sun.<BR>—नभः-क्रान्त, अस्, or नभः-क्रान्तिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘going in the sky’ (from the lion-like shape<BR>of certain clouds), a lion.<BR>—नभः-पान्थ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘sky-traveller,’ the sun.<BR>—नभः-प्रभेद,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a descendant of Vi-rūpa and author of<BR>a Ṛg-veda hymn (X. 112).<BR>—नभः-प्राण, अस्,<BR>m. ‘sky-breath,’ air, wind; [cf. ख-श्वास, नभः-<BR>श्वास.]<BR>—नभः-श्रित्, त्, त्, त्, reaching to the sky,<BR>attaining heaven.<BR>—नभः-श्वास, अस्, m. ‘sky-<BR>breath,’ air, wind; [cf. नभः-प्राण.]<BR>—नभः-<BR>सद्, त्, m. ‘inhabiting the sky,’ a god; a star.<BR>—नभः-सरस्, अस्, n. ‘sky-lake,’ the clouds.<BR>—नभः-सरित्, f. ‘sky-river,’ the milky-way (=<BR>देव-पथ); the celestial Ganges.<BR>—नभः-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘situated in heaven,’ celestial, aerial,<BR>heavenly, ethereal.<BR>—नभः-स्थल, अस्, m. ‘whose<BR>residence is the sky,’ an epithet of Śiva; (ई), f. the<BR>sky.<BR>—नभः-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, abiding in heaven<BR>or in the sky; (अस्), m. a division of the infernal<BR>regions, a hell.<BR>—नभः-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, or नभः-<BR>स्पृश, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘sky-touching,’ reaching to<BR>the sky.<BR>—नभश्-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. ‘eye of the<BR>sky,’ the sun.<BR>—नभश्-चमस, अस्, m. ‘drinking<BR>vessel of heaven,’ the moon; a variegated cake (=<BR>चित्र-पूप); magic, conjuring.<BR>—नभश्-चर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, ‘sky-going,’ going in the air; (अस्), m. an<BR>inhabitant of heaven, a god; a Vidyā-dhara or demi-<BR>god so called.<BR>—नभस्-तल, अम्, n. ‘the bottom<BR>of the clouds,’ the lower region of the sky, nether<BR>sky; the sky, atmosphere; (in astronomy) N. of the<BR>tenth solar mansion.<BR>—नभस्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. vaporous, vapory, filled with vapour, exhaling<BR>vapour, misty, hazy; (Sāy.) bright as the sun.<BR> — 1. नभस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, vaporous, filled with<BR>vapour, misty, cloudy; young; (आन्), m. air, wind;<BR>(अती), f., N. of the wife of Antar-dhāna and mother<BR>of Havir-dhāna.<BR>—२. नभस्-वत्, ind. like vapour.<BR>—नभो-ग, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), a star; (अस्), m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">Page0469-a+ 77</a>]<BR>N. of one of the seven sages of the tenth Manv-<BR>antara.<BR>—नभो-गज, अस्, m. ‘an elephant in the<BR>sky,’ a cloud.<BR>—नभो-गति, इस्, f. going through<BR>the sky, going in the air, soaring, flying.<BR>—नभो-<BR>जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. produced from vapour.<BR>—नभो-<BR>जू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. impelling the clouds; (Sāy.)<BR>pervading or traversing the sky.<BR>—नभो-द, अस्,<BR>m., N. of one of the Viśve-devās.<BR>—नभो-दुह,<BR>‘milking the sky;’ or नभो-द्वीप, ‘sky-island;’ or<BR>नभो-धूम, ‘sky-smoke;’ or नभो-ध्वज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘sky-banner,’ a cloud.<BR>—नभो-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, blind; looking up to heaven.<BR>—नभो-नदी, f.<BR>‘sky-river,’ the celestial Ganges.<BR>—नभो-मणि, इस्,<BR>m. ‘sky-jewel,’ the sun.<BR>—नभो-मण्डल, अम्,<BR>n. ‘sky-circle,’ the firmament; the atmosphere.<BR>—नभोमण्डल-दीप, अस्, m. ‘light of the sky,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—नभो ऽम्बु-प, अस्, m. ‘drinking the<BR>water of the sky or rain-water,’ the bird Cātaka,<BR>Cuculus Melanoleucus.<BR>—नभो-योनि, इस्, m. ‘whose<BR>birthplace is the sky,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—नभो-<BR>रजस्, अस्, n. ‘sky-dust (?),’ darkness.<BR>—नभो-रूप,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the form or colour of the<BR>clouds, dark-coloured.<BR>—नभो-रेणु, उस्, f. fog,<BR>mist, vapour.<BR>—नभो-लय, अस्, m. ‘having its<BR>abode in the sky,’ smoke.<BR>—नभो-लिह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, ‘sky-<BR>licking,’ lofty, towering, rising to the clouds.<BR>—नभो-<BR>वट, अस्, m. ‘the expanse of the sky,’ the atmo-<BR>sphere.<BR>—नभो-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing or possessing<BR>heaven or the sky.<BR>—नभो-वीथी, f. ‘sky-road,’ the<BR>path of the sun.<BR>—नभौकस् (नभ for नभस्<BR>+ ओकस्), inhabiting the atmosphere or heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0468-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस|नभसं|नभसः
नभस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. vapourish, vapoury,<BR>filled with vapour, misty; (अस्), m. heaven, air,<BR>atmosphere; the rainy season; the ocean; N. of<BR>one of the seven sages in the tenth Manv-antara; of<BR>a Dānava; (also read रभस.)<BR>—नभसङ्-<BR>गम, अस्, m. ‘sky-goer,’ a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्य|नभस्यः
नभस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, vapoury, filled with vapour,<BR>misty, foggy; (अस्), m., N. of a month of the rainy<BR>season (= Bhādra, August-September); N. of a son<BR>of Manu Svārociṣa or of the third Manu [cf. नभ];<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभाक|नभाकं|नभाकः
नभाक, अस्, m., N. of a Vedic Ṛṣi by whom<BR>three hymns of the Ṛg-veda (VIII. 39-41) are<BR>supposed to have been composed, see नाभाक;<BR>(अम्), n. (said to be = नभस् and to be derived<BR>fr. 2. न + rt. 1. भा + aff. आक), darkness; a cloud;<BR>the sky.<BR>—नभाक-वत् in Ṛg-veda VIII. 40 = the<BR>hymn of Nabhāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्य|नभ्यं
1. नभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, foggy, misty, cloudy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभाग
नभाग नभाग, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Manu Vaivasvata; [cf. नभ-ग, नाभाग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभि|नभिः
नभि नभि, इस्, m. (?), a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभीत
नभीत न-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, not afraid, un-<BR>daunted, dauntless.<BR>—नभीत-वत्, ind. in a fearless<BR>manner, fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्य|नभ्यं
नभ्य 2. नभ्य, अम्, n. (said to be fr. नभ<BR>for नाभि), Ved. the centre part of a wheel, the<BR>nave; the middle.<BR>—नभ्य-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>standing in the middle; belonging to the nave of<BR>a wheel, fit for a nave; नभ्यं तैलम्, oil for<BR>greasing the nave of a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्राज्
नभ्राज् न-भ्राज्, ट्, m. ‘not shining,’ a<BR>dark cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्
नम् नम्, cl. 1. P. A. नमति, -ते (the<BR>Ātmane-pada being generally used in the<BR>intransitive sense), ननाम, नेमे (2nd sing. ने-<BR>मिथ or ननन्थ, ep. 3rd pl. A. अव-ननामिरे,<BR>Ved. 1st sing. P. नानाम), नन्ता, नंस्यति, न-<BR>मिष्यति, अनंसीत्, अनंस्त (Ved., Aor. 3rd sing.<BR>अनान्; Leṭ, 1st sing. नंसै, Ṛg-veda III. 33, 10),<BR>नन्तुम् (Ved. inf. नि-नमे), to bow to, make or<BR>pay obeisance to (with dat., gen., and acc.); to bow,<BR>bow down, subject or submit one's self; to bend;<BR>to be bent or curved; to sink; (in grammar) to<BR>change a dental letter into a cerebral; to sound;<BR>Pass. नम्यते: Caus. नमयति and (with prep.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">Page0469-b+ 81</a>]<BR>नामयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अनीनमत्, to cause to<BR>bow, bend, curve, make curved, (with धनुस् or<BR>चापम्) to bend a bow; to cause to sink or de-<BR>cline; to ward off; to turn away from; (in grammar)<BR>to change a dental into a cerebral: Desid. निनं-<BR>सति: Intens. नन्नमीति, नन्नन्ति, नन्नम्यते,<BR>to bow, be bent, bend very low; [cf. Zend nemanh<BR>= नमस्, निम्-अत, ‘grass:’ Gr. νέμ-ω, νέμ-ο-μαι,<BR>νωμά-ω, νομ-ή, νέμ-η-σι-ς, νεμ-έ-τωρ, νομ-εύ-ς,<BR>νέμ-ε-σι-ς, νόμο-ς, νομίζ-ω, νόμισ-μα, νέμ-ος, Νε-μέα,<BR>νομ-ό-ς: Lat. Nŭma, Nŭm-i-tor, nŭm-e-ru-s,<BR>Numerius, nĕm-us: Goth. and Angl. Sax. nim-an,<BR>‘to take,’ originally ‘to subdue:’ Old Germ. nām-a,<BR>‘prey:’ Lith. náma-s, ‘a house;’ nú§m-a-s, ‘gain:’<BR>Lett. nom-a, ‘interest:’ probably Hib. naomh, ‘a<BR>saint, sacred;’ naomhachd, ‘holiness.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत्
नमत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bending, bowing, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत|नमतः
नमत, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, bowed, crooked, curved;<BR>(अस्), m. a master, lord (?); an actor, mime; smoke;<BR>a cloud; (अम्), n. felt, woollen stuff; [cf. नामतिक,<BR>1. नवत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमन|नमनं|नमनः
नमन, अस्, m. one who causes to bend or bow;<BR>(अम्), n. bowing down, sinking; [cf. गृह-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमनीय
नमनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bowed down to,<BR>one to whom one must pay obeisance, venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमयत्
नमयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bending, causing to bow<BR>down, inclining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमयिष्णु
नमयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. bowing, bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्
नमस्, अस्, n. (often treated as an indeclinable<BR>interjection or exclamation), bowing, bending, making<BR>a bow, a bow, salutation, reverential salutation, paying<BR>honour (in gesture or words); adoration, obeisance<BR>(performed by joining the palms and inclining the<BR>head; often used in connection with the N. of a<BR>deity in the dat., e. g. रामाय नमस्, salutation<BR>or glory or reverence to Rāma); food (Ved.); giving,<BR>presenting, a gift, present; a thunderbolt (Ved.);<BR>an inarticulate cry (said to be m. ?).<BR>—नम-उक्ति,<BR>इस्, f., Ved. uttering a salutation, paying homage or<BR>obeisance.<BR>—नमस्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, worshipping<BR>or adoring (the gods); a worshipper, pious.<BR>—न-<BR>मस्-कार, अस्, m. uttering the interjection or excla-<BR>mation नमस्, bowing, respectful or reverential<BR>address or salutation, adoration, obeisance; a sort of<BR>poison; (ई), f. a sensitive plant.<BR>—नमस्कार-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing the Namas-kāra.<BR>—न-<BR>मस्-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bowed down to, one<BR>to whom one must pay obeisance, before whom one<BR>must say नमस्; to be worshipped.<BR>—नमस्-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to utter the exclamation<BR>नमस् (sometimes with dat., loc., and acc.).<BR>—न-<BR>मस्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, worshipped, reverenced,<BR>adored.<BR>—नमस्-कृत्य or नमस्-कृत्वा, ind. hav-<BR>ing saluted reverentially.<BR>—नमस्-क्रिया, f. reve-<BR>rential salutation, bowing, worshipping, adoration.<BR>—नमस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. paying adoration<BR>or homage, worshipping, adoring; inspiring vene-<BR>ration; (Sāy.) abounding in food.<BR>—नमस्-विन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, paying homage, worshipping, reverential,<BR>respectful.<BR>—नमो-गुरु, उस्, m. a spiritual teacher.<BR>—नमो-वाक, अस्, m., Ved. uttering the नमस्<BR>or obeisance in general.<BR>—नमो-वृक्ति, इस्, f., Ved.<BR>reverential cleansing (of the Barhis).<BR>—नमो-वृध्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. honoured by adoration; (Sāy.) food-<BR>augmenting, increasing food; (आ), m. du. ‘delighting<BR>in adoration,’ epithet of Mitra-Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस|नमसः
नमस, अस्, आ, अम्, favourable, kindly disposed;<BR>(अस्), m. agreement (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमसान
नमसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. paying obeisance,<BR>worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमसित|नमसितः
नमसित, अस्, आ, अम् (probably corrupted from<BR>नमस्यित), reverenced, respected, worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
1. नमस्य (fr. नमस्), Nom. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>नमस्यति (-ते), &c., to pay homage, make obei-<BR>sance, worship (with acc.); to act humbly or defe-<BR>rentially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
2. नमस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be worshipped or<BR>adored, one to whom obeisance must be made,<BR>venerable, respectable, entitled to salutation or civility;<BR>reverential, respectful, humble; (आ), f. reverence,<BR>respect, worship, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
3. नमस्य, ind. having paid homage, having<BR>worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यत्
नमस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, saluting reverentially,<BR>making obeisance, bowing to, paying adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यित|नमस्यितः
नमस्यित, अस्, आ, अम्, reverenced, respected,<BR>worshipped; [cf. नमसित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यु
नमस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. paying homage, making<BR>obeisance, worshipping; (उस्), m., N. of a son of<BR>Pravīra, descendant of Puru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमित|नमितः
नमित, अस्, आ, अम्, bowed, bent down, making<BR>salutation or obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्य
नम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bowed down to, vene-<BR>rable; changeable to a cerebral letter; (आ), f. the<BR>night (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, bowing, bowing down, in-<BR>clining, (मूर्ध्ना नम्रः, bowing the head, lit.<BR>with the head); bent, bowed, inclined; curved,<BR>crooked; hanging down; sunk; making obeisance;<BR>lowly, submissive, reverential, humble; worshipping,<BR>adoring; devoted to; (आ), m. du., Ved. epithet of<BR>two verses addressed to Agni.<BR>—नम्र-ता, f. or<BR>नम्र-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being bowed or<BR>bent, bowing, bowing or hanging down, obeisance,<BR>adoration, respect, devotion; submissiveness, humble-<BR>ness, humility, meekness; condescension.<BR>—नम्र-<BR>प्रकृति, इस्, इस्, इ, of a gentle or submissive dispo-<BR>sition.<BR>—नम्र-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having the face<BR>bent down, looking down.<BR>—नम्र-मूर्ति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, having the form bent, stooping, bowed.<BR>—नम्-<BR>राङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, bowing or bending the<BR>body, bowed, bent, stooping.<BR>—नम्री-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, bowed down, bent down, humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रक|नम्रकः
नम्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, bowed down, bent, stoop-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. a species of reed (= वेतस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रित
नम्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, bent down, bowed down,<BR>made to sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमात्र
नमात्र न-मात्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), a par-<BR>ticular high number; [cf. नहि-मात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमि
नमि नमि = नेमि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमी
नमी नमी, m., Ved., N. of a Ṛṣi; (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 53, 7), foe-prostrating<BR>(applied to the thunderbolt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुच
नमुच नमुच, अस्, m., N. of an ancient<BR>sage; (also read उन्मुचु, प्रमुचु, मुचु, उन्-<BR>मुच, विमुच.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचि|नमुचिः
नमुचि न-मुचि, इस्, m. ‘not loosing the<BR>heavenly waters’ (i. e. confining the clouds and pre-<BR>venting the flow of rain), N. of a demon vanquished<BR>and slain by Indra and the Aśvins; N. of the god<BR>of love.<BR>—नमुचि-द्विष्, ट्, ‘enemy of Namuci;’ or<BR>नमुचि-सूदन, अस्, ‘destroyer of Namuci;’ or न-<BR>मुचि-हन्, आ, m. ‘killer of Namuci,’ epithets of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुर
नमुर न-मुर, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), Ved. not<BR>dying (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमेरु|नमेरुः
नमेरु नमेरु, उस्, m. the tree Eleocarpus<BR>Ganitrus (= रुद्राक्ष, = सुर-पुन्नाग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमैय
नमैय नमैय, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्ब्
नम्ब् नम्ब्, cl. 1. P. नम्बति, &c., to<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र नम्र. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय 1. नय्, cl. 1. A. नयते, नेये, नयि-<BR>तुम्, to go, move; to protect; [cf. rt.<BR>1. नी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय नय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. नी), guiding,<BR>leading, directing, managing; manner of conducting<BR>one's self, behaviour, conduct, course of conduct, way<BR>of life, management; prudent conduct or behaviour,<BR>good management; prudence, reason; polity, policy,<BR>political wisdom, state-policy, political economy,<BR>statesmanship, civil administration, government; any<BR>work on policy or political economy; Prudence or<BR>Policy personified as a son of Dharma and Kriyā;<BR>plan, design; leading thought, maxim, principle;<BR>opinion, system, course, method; philosophical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">Page0470-a+ 79</a>]<BR>system; the philosophical part of the Veda (?); a<BR>kind of game; a sort of dice or men for playing this<BR>game [cf. नय-पीठी]; a move in this game (?);<BR>N. of a son of the thirteenth Manu; (अस्, आ, अम्), =<BR>नेतृ, leading, guiding, conducting; a leader, guide;<BR>= न्याय, fit, right, proper.<BR>—नय-कोविद, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, skilled in policy, prudent.<BR>—नय-ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, following a system.<BR>—नय-चक्षुस्, उस्,<BR>उस्, उस्, having political foresight, wise, prudent.<BR>—नय-जा, f., N. of the wife of king Brahma-dāsa,<BR>father of Nārāyaṇa, who composed the Praśnārṇava.<BR>—नय-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing polity, prudent;<BR>knowing any system, a follower of any system.<BR>—नय-नेतृ, ता, m. a master in policy or politics.<BR>—नय-पाल, अस्, m. ‘protector of policy,’ N. of a<BR>man; of a king.<BR>—नय-पीठी, f. the board or cloth<BR>on which dice or men are moved in play.<BR>—नय-<BR>प्रयोग, अस्, m. policy, political wisdom or address.<BR>—नय-लोचन, अम्, n. ‘the eye of policy,’ N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—नय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, familiar with<BR>policy, versed in polity, prudent; containing any<BR>form of rt. 1. नी (as a Ṛk).<BR>—नय-विद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>or नय-विशारद, अस्, आ, अम्, m. knowing polity,<BR>skilled in policy, a politician, statesman.<BR>—नय-<BR>शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing political wisdom, endowed<BR>with prudence.<BR>—नय-शास्त्र, अम्, n. any work on<BR>policy or political economy, the doctrine of polity.<BR>—नय-सार, अस्, m. ‘essence of polity,’ N. of a<BR>treatise.<BR>—नय-सिद्धि, इस्, f. political success, ac-<BR>complishing anything by good management.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0469-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयक|नयकः
नयक, अस्, आ, अम्, a skilful manager, clever in<BR>policy or political administration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयत्
नयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, leading, guiding; tending<BR>or conducing to; informing, certifying, giving evi-<BR>dence, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयन|नयनं
नयन, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आ or ई), f. the<BR>pupil of the eye; (अम्), n. leading, guiding, con-<BR>ducting, managing; governing, directing, ruling;<BR>leading or bringing to, drawing; (with कालस्य),<BR>passing or spending (time); attaining, obtaining;<BR>‘the guiding or leading organ,’ the eye.<BR>—नयन-<BR>गोचर, अस्, आ, अम्, perceptible by the eye, within<BR>the range of vision, visible, apparent.<BR>—नयन-<BR>च्छद, अस्, m. ‘eye-covering,’ an eyelid.<BR>—न-<BR>यन-जल, अम्, n. ‘eye-water,’ tears.<BR>—नयन-<BR>पथ, अस्, m. range or field of sight.<BR>—नयन-<BR>पुट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), the eyelid.<BR>—नयन-वारि,<BR>इ, n. ‘eye-water,’ tears.<BR>—नयन-विषय, अस्, m.<BR>‘field of vision, range of sight,’ the horizon.<BR>—न-<BR>यन-सलिल, अम्, n. ‘eye-water,’ tears.<BR>—नय-<BR>नाञ्जन (˚न-अञ्˚), अम्, n. any ointment for the<BR>eye.<BR>—नयनानन्द (˚न-आन्˚) or नयनानन्द-<BR>शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a commentator on the Amara-<BR>koṣa.<BR>—नयनामोषिन् (˚न-आम्˚), ई, इणी, इ, ‘sight-<BR>stealing,’ blinding.<BR>—नयनोत्सव (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘eye-festival,’ any lovely or desired object; a<BR>lamp.<BR>—नयनोद (˚न-उद), अम्, n. eye-water;<BR>[cf. नयन-सलिल.]<BR>—नयनोपान्त (˚न-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the outer angle or corner of the eye, the<BR>canthus.<BR>—नयनौषध (˚न-ओष्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘eye-medicament,’ green sulphate of iron or that<BR>salt in a state of partial decomposition by exposure<BR>to the atmosphere (used as a collyrium).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयितव्य
नयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be conducted or brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयिष्ठ
नयिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. leading in the best<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयुत
नयुत नयुत, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), 100,000<BR>millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय्यग्रोध
नय्यग्रोध नय्यग्रोध, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. न्य-<BR>ग्रोध), Ved. relating to or produced from the<BR>sacred fig-tree; (also read नैयग्रोध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर|नरं|नरः
नर नर, अस्, m. (for etymology see the<BR>simple form नृ), a man, a male, a person; a man<BR>or piece at chess, draughts, &c.; the pin or gnomon<BR>of a sun-dial; (in grammar) person, personal ter-<BR>mination [cf. पुरुष]; a sort of measure, a man's<BR>length; the original or eternal Man, the divine<BR>imperishable spirit pervading the universe (always<BR>associated with Nārāyaṇa which as a patronymic from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-b" target="_blank">Page0470-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Nara = ‘son of the original Man;’ in Manu Nara<BR>is apparently identified with Nārāyaṇa, see 1. 10, where<BR>the waters are called Nārā as produced from Nara or the<BR>eternal spirit [according to Kullūka = Paramātman,<BR>Brahman], which spirit is thence also called Nārāyaṇa<BR>as ‘having his first place of motion on the waters;’ but<BR>in the more systematic mythology Nara and Nārāyaṇa<BR>are distinct, the former being regarded as a sage or<BR>patriarch, ‘the best of men’ or ‘chief man,’ while the<BR>latter is a god; in epic poetry they are the sons of<BR>Dharma by Mūrti or A-hiṃsā and are emanations<BR>of Viṣṇu, Arjuna being identified with Nara, and<BR>Kṛṣṇa with Nārāyaṇa; in some places Nara and<BR>Nārāyaṇa are called देवौ, ‘the two gods,’ or<BR>पूर्व-देवौ, ‘the two original gods,’ or ऋषी,<BR>‘the two sages,’ or पुराणाव् ऋषि-सत्तमौ, ‘the<BR>two most ancient and best of sages,’ or तापसौ, ‘the<BR>two ascetics,’ or महा-मुनी, ‘the two great Munis’);<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of certain mythical beings allied to the<BR>Gandharvas and Kin-naras, qq. vv. (thought by some<BR>to be a kind of centaur, half horse, half man); N.<BR>of one of the ten horses of the moon; N. of a son<BR>of Manu Tāmasa; of a son of Viśvā-mitra; N. of a<BR>son of Gaya and father of Virāj; of a son of Su-<BR>dhṛti and father of Kevala; N. of a son of Bhavan-<BR>manyu (Manyu) and father of Saṅkṛti; N. of two<BR>kings of Kaśmīra; (ई), f. a woman, = नारी; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of fragrant grass, = राम-कर्पूर; [cf.<BR>Gr. ἀνήρ; Lat. Nero, Neriene; probably Hib.<BR>naoi, ‘a man,’ but see नृ.]<BR>—नर-कपाल, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a man's skull.<BR>—नर-कीलक, अस्, m. the<BR>murderer of his spiritual preceptor.<BR>—नर-केशरिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘man-lion,’ ‘half man, half lion,’ Viṣṇu in his<BR>fourth Ava-tāra; [cf. नर-सिंह.]<BR>—नर-ग्राह,<BR>अस्, m. ‘man-crocodile,’ ‘half man, half crocodile,’<BR>N. of a kind of Kirāta.<BR>—नर-ता, f. or नर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. humanity, manhood, human condition.<BR>—न-<BR>र-त्रोटकाचार्य (˚क-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नर-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman, a nephew<BR>of the Ṛṣi Asita; (आ), f., N. of a goddess executing<BR>the commands of the twentieth Arhat of the present<BR>Ava-sarpiṇī; one of the sixteen Vidyā-devīs.<BR>—नर-<BR>देव, अस्, m. ‘a god among men,’ a sovereign, king.<BR>—नरदेव-त्व, अम्, n. kingship, royalty, kingly<BR>rank.<BR>—नरदेव-देव, अस्, m. a god among the<BR>gods of men or kings.<BR>—नरदेव-पुत्र, अस्, m.<BR>the son of a man and a god.<BR>—नर-द्विष्, ट्, m.<BR>‘enemy of men,’ a Rakṣas.<BR>—नर-नगर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town.<BR>—नर-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘protector<BR>of men,’ a king, a prince.<BR>—नरनाथ-मार्ग, अस्,<BR>m. ‘king's road, royal road,’ the chief road, high<BR>street.<BR>—नरनाथासन (˚थ-आस्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>throne or dignity of a king.<BR>—नर-नायक, अस्,<BR>m. ‘leader of men,’ a king, a prince.<BR>—नर-नारा-<BR>यण, अस्, m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa; (औ), m. du.<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Arjuna, see नर above.<BR>—नरन्-धि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘man-containing,’ the world, (a word given<BR>by Mahī-dhara to explain the etymology of नरन्-<BR>धिष below.)<BR>—नरन्-धिष, अस्, m., Ved. ‘ob-<BR>serving men (?),’ an epithet of Viṣṇu; of Pūṣan;<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-s. VIII. 55.<BR>this comp. is either नरन्धि-ष, ‘destroying the<BR>world,’ see नरन्-धि above, or न-रन्धिष,<BR>‘not injuring,’ i. e. ‘a protector;’ in XXII. 20. he<BR>explains नरन्-धिष by ‘man-praising.’)<BR>—नर-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of men,’ a king, sovereign; N. of<BR>one of the four mythical kings of Jambu-dvīpa.<BR>—नरपति-जय-चर्या, f., N. of a work.<BR>—नर-<BR>पति-पथ, अस्, m. ‘king's road,’ the chief road,<BR>high street.<BR>—नरपति-विजय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—नर-पशु, उस्, m. ‘man-beast,’ a brute in<BR>human form, a beast-like man.<BR>—नर-पाल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘protector of men,’ a king, a prince.<BR>—नर-<BR>पुङ्गव, अस्, m. an excellent hero.<BR>—नर-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, favourable or friendly to manking; (अस्),<BR>m. a species of tree (= नील-वृक्ष).<BR>—नर-बलि,<BR>इस्, m. a human sacrifice; [cf. नर-मेध, पुरु-<BR>ष-मेध.]<BR>—नर-ब्रह्म-देव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—नर-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, man-eating. can-<BR>nibal.<BR>—नर-भू, ऊस्, f. or नर-भूमि, इस्, f. ‘the<BR>land of men, birthplace of men,’ Bhārata-varṣa,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-c" target="_blank">Page0470-c+ 81</a>]<BR>i. e. India or the central part of the known con-<BR>tinent.<BR>—नर-मानिका or नर-मानिनी, f. a man-<BR>like woman, a woman with a beard; [cf. नर-<BR>मालिनी.]<BR>—नर-माला, f. a string or girdle of skulls.<BR>—नर-मालिनी, f. = नर-मानिनी (of which it is<BR>probably a corruption).<BR>—नर-मूर्छन, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of the eighty-ninth chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa<BR>of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—नर-मेध, अस्, m. a<BR>human sacrifice, the sacrifice of a man; [cf. नृ-<BR>बलि, पुरुष-मेध.]<BR>—नरम्-मन्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, considered as a man, passing for a man.<BR>—नर-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘instrument with a gnomon,’ a sun-<BR>dial.<BR>—नर-यान, अम्, n. a carriage drawn by<BR>men; (in Pañca-tantra III. 248. नर-याण with<BR>cerebral ण् = ‘a man-vehicle, a man serving as a<BR>vehicle for carrying another.’)<BR>—नर-रथ, अस्, m.<BR>a wrong form for नव-रथ.<BR>—नर-राज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘king of men,’ a king.<BR>—नरराज्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘empire over men,’ kingship, royalty, kingdom.<BR>—नर-रूप, अस्, ई, अम्, formed like a man, man-<BR>like; (अम्), n. the form of a man, human form.<BR>—नर-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having the human form.<BR>—नरर्षभ (˚र-ऋष्˚), अस्, m. ‘man-bull,’<BR>chief of men, a prince.<BR>—नर-लोक, अस्, m. the<BR>world of men, the earth; mortals, men.<BR>—नरलोक-<BR>पाल, अस्, m. ‘protector of men,’ a king.<BR>—नरलोक-<BR>वीर, अस्, m. ‘a hero among men,’ a human hero.<BR>—नर-वत्, ind. like a man.<BR>—नर-वर, अस्,<BR>m. an excellent or illustrious man.<BR>—नरवर-<BR>वृषभ, अस्, m. an excellent hero (like a bull).<BR>—नरवरोत्तम (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m. the best of<BR>excellent men.<BR>—नर-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>prince of Mālava in the twelfth century.<BR>—नर-<BR>वाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, borne or carried by men, drawn<BR>by men; (अस्), m. an epithet of Kuvera; N. of a<BR>prince, successor of Śāli-vāhana; of a prince of the<BR>Dārvābhisāras; of a minister of king Kṣema-gupta.<BR>—नरवाहन-जनन, अम्, n., N. of the fourth<BR>section of the Kathā-sarit-sāgara by Soma-deva.<BR>—नरवाहन-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of king<BR>Udayana.<BR>—नर-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, carried or drawn<BR>by men (as a vehicle).<BR>—नर-विष्वण, अस्, m.<BR>‘man-devourer,’ a Rakṣas, an imp or goblin.<BR>—नर-वीर, अस्, m. ‘a hero of a man,’ an heroic<BR>man, a hero or brave man.<BR>—नरवीर-लोक, अस्,<BR>m. the bravest of men; mankind in general.<BR>—नर-<BR>व्याघ्र or नर-शार्दूल, अस्, m. ‘man-tiger,’ an<BR>eminent man; the most illustrious of men.<BR>—नर-<BR>शृङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘man's horn,’ i. e. anything chime-<BR>rical or impossible.<BR>—नर-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. the<BR>best of men.<BR>—नर-संसर्ग, अस्, m. intercourse<BR>of men, human society.<BR>—नर-सख, अस्, m.<BR>‘friend of Nara,’ an epithet of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—नर-<BR>सङ्घाराम (˚घ-आर्˚), अस्, m. (?), N. of a Buddhist<BR>monastery.<BR>—नर-सार, अस्, m. a particular sub-<BR>stance or article of commerce, sal ammoniac (?).<BR>—नर-सिंह, अस्, m. ‘man-lion,’ a lion among<BR>men, a great warrior, a man of eminence or power,<BR>a chief; ‘the lion-headed man’ or Viṣṇu in his<BR>fourth Ava-tāra when he descended to fight with<BR>Hiraṇya-kaśipu; N. of the father of king Bhairava;<BR>of several authors and princes; [cf. नार-सिंह, नृ-<BR>सिंह, नर-हरि.]<BR>—नरसिंह-देव, अस्, m. ‘a<BR>god among the men-lions,’ N. of several princes.<BR>—नरसिंह-द्वादशी-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a par-<BR>ticular ceremony performed in the month Phālguna;<BR>N. of the forty-second chapter of the Vārāha-Purāṇa.<BR>—नरसिंह-पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नरसिंह-पारिजात, N. of a work by Nara-<BR>siṃha.<BR>—नरसिंह-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नरसिंह-मनु, N. of the sixteenth<BR>chapter of the Śāradā-tilaka by Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>—नर-<BR>सिंह-यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a mystical diagram<BR>described in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—नरसिंह-सरस्-<BR>वती, m., N. of a commentator on the Vedānta-<BR>sāra.<BR>—नरसिंह-सहस्र-नामानि, n. pl. ‘the<BR>thousand names of the man-lion,’ i. e. of Viṣṇu,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—नर-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. a multitude<BR>or body of men.<BR>—नर-हय, अम्, n. (with युद्-<BR>ध), a fight between man and horse; [cf. देवा-<BR>सुर.]<BR>—नर-हरि, इस्, m. Viṣṇu as ‘the man-lion’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-a" target="_blank">Page0471-a+ 80</a>]<BR>in his fourth Ava-tāra [cf. नर-सिंह]; N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—नरहरि-देव, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—नराङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘male-<BR>member,’ the penis; (अस्), m. eruption on the face.<BR>—नराची (˚र + आची fr. अञ्च्), f., Ved. a species of<BR>plant (?); N. of a wife of Kṛṣṇa; a kind of metre,<BR>(see under नाराच.)<BR>—नराधम (˚र-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a low or vile man, a wretch.<BR>—नराधार (˚र-<BR>आध्˚), अस्, m. ‘asylum or receptacle of men,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva; (आ), f. the earth.<BR>—नराधिप (˚र-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of men,’ a prince, king, monarch;<BR>the tree Cathartocarpus Fistula; [cf. राज-वृक्ष.]<BR>—नराधिपति (˚र-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘lord of men,’<BR>a king, a prince.<BR>—नरान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a son of Hṛdīka.<BR>—नरान्तक (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘man-destroyer,’ death; N. of a Rākṣasa, son of<BR>Rāvaṇa.<BR>—नरान्तक-निग्रह-वर्णन, अम्, n.<BR>‘description of the subjugation of Narāntaka,’ N. of<BR>the fifty-ninth chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—नरान्तक-निर्गम, अस्, m.<BR>‘the coming forth of Narāntaka,’ N. of the fifty-<BR>seventh chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नरायण (˚र-अय्˚), अस्, m. = नारायण,<BR>a N. of Viṣṇu, &c.<BR>—नराश (˚र-आश), अस्, m.<BR>‘man-eater,’ a Rakṣas, an imp or demon.<BR>—नरा-<BR>शंस (˚र-आश्˚), अस्, m., Ved. ‘the desire of men,<BR>desired of men (?),’ a mystical N. of Agni (invoked<BR>in the Āprī hymns with Tanū-napāt, another mystical<BR>epithet of Fire, or taking the place of Tanū-napāt in<BR>these hymns, see आ-प्री).<BR>—नराशन (˚र-अश्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘man-eater,’ a Rakṣas or demon.<BR>—नरेतर<BR>(˚र-इत्˚), अस्, m. a being differing from men; a higher<BR>being than a man; a lower being, an animal, a<BR>beast-like man.<BR>—नरेन्द्र (˚र-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of men,’ a king, a prince, an anointed sovereign; a<BR>physician, a dealer in antidotes; a juggler (?); a con-<BR>veyer of news or intelligence (?); N. of a man; a<BR>species of tree (= नराधिप); a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines of twenty-one syllables each.<BR>—नरेन्द्र-त्व, अम्, n. kingship, royalty.<BR>—न-<BR>रेन्द्र-द्रुम, अस्, m. the tree Narendra.<BR>—न-<BR>रेन्द्र-पुत्र, अस्, m. a prince.<BR>—नरेन्द्र-मार्ग,<BR>अस्, m. the king's high-road, a royal or main road,<BR>high street.<BR>—नरेन्द्र-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>temple or holy place built by and called after Naren-<BR>drāditya.<BR>—नरेन्द्राचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a grammarian.<BR>—नरेन्द्रादित्य (˚र-आद्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of two princes of Kaśmīra.<BR>—नरेन्द्राह्व (˚र-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), a kind of Aloë (= काष्ठा-<BR>गुरु).<BR>—नरेश or नरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of men,’ a king, a prince.<BR>—नरेश्वर-विवेक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Śaiva work by Parameṣṭhin.<BR>—नरे-<BR>ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. serving as a standing-place<BR>for men?; (Sāy.) resting on conducting (wheels).<BR>—नरोत्तम (˚र-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘best of men,’ an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; of Buddha; N. of a scholiast of<BR>the Adhyātma-rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्य|नर्यः|नर्य्य
नर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. manly, human, (often<BR>with अपस्, a manly deed, a heroic deed); strong,<BR>powerful; suitable or agreeable to men (as food);<BR>(अस्), m. a man, a person; an epithet of Indra; of<BR>Agni Gārhapatya; N. of a man; (आ), m. du., scil.<BR>उभा शंसा, the two objects of desire, i. e. heaven<BR>and earth [cf. नराशंस]; (आस्), m. pl. epithet of<BR>the Maruts; (अम्), n. a manly act, manly deed; a<BR>gift for men.<BR>—नर्यापस् (˚य-अप्˚), आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. performing manly deeds; (Sāy.) performing<BR>deeds agreeable or suitable to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरक|नरकं|नरकः
नरक नरक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. नॄ), hell, the place of torment (distinguished fr.<BR>पाताल, the lower regions, q. v.), including a num-<BR>ber of places of torture of various descriptions, gene-<BR>rally said to be twenty-one in number [cf. नारक];<BR>(Hell is sometimes personified as a son of Anṛta and<BR>Nirṛti or Nikṛti); (अस्), m., N. of a demon, a son of<BR>Bhūmi or Earth (therefore called Bhauma, haunting<BR>Prāg-jyotiṣa and slain there by Kṛṣṇa); N. of a<BR>man; N. of a district; of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—न-<BR>रक-कुण्ड, अम्, n. a pit or abyss in hell wherein<BR>the wicked are tormented, (eighty-six such are enume-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">Page0471-b+ 74</a>]<BR>rated).<BR>—नरक-जित्, त्, m. ‘vanquisher of the demon<BR>Naraka,’ epithet of Viṣṇu-Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—नरक-दे-<BR>वता, f. ‘the deity of hell,’ Nirṛti; Misfortune per-<BR>sonified as a goddess.<BR>—नरक-भूमि, इस्, f. a<BR>division of hell, (of which seven are enumerated.)<BR>—नरक-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, ‘hell-formed,’ hellish.<BR>—नरक-वर्ग, अस्, m. ‘the hell chapter,’ N.<BR>of a chapter of Amara-siṃha's Nāma-liṅgānuśāsana.<BR>—नरक-वर्णन, अम्, n. ‘description of hell,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Revā-māhātmya.<BR>—नरक-<BR>स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, living or being in hell; (आ), f. the<BR>river of hell, Vaitaraṇī.<BR>—नरक-स्वर्ग-प्राप्ति-<BR>प्रकार-वर्णन, अम्, n. ‘description of the mode<BR>of obtaining heaven and hell,’ N. of the eighth<BR>chapter of the Māgha-māhātmya.<BR>—नरकान्तक<BR>(˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘destroyer of the demon Naraka,’<BR>an epithet of Kṛṣṇa-Viṣṇu.<BR>—नरकामय (˚क-<BR>आम्˚), अस्, m. the soul after death; a ghost or spirit.<BR>—नरकारि (˚क-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of the<BR>demon Naraka,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa-Viṣṇu.<BR>—नरकावास (˚क-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘one whose abode<BR>is hell,’ an inhabitant of hell.<BR>—नरकौकस् (˚क-<BR>ओक्˚), आस्, m. an inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकाय
नरकाय, Nom. A. नरकायते, &c., to repre-<BR>sent a hell; to resemble or be similar to hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरङ्ग|नरंग|नरंगं|नरङ्गः
नरङ्ग नरङ्ग, अस्, m. pimples on the face<BR>(= वरण्डक); (अम्), n. the penis; (wrong form<BR>for नराङ्ग, see col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरद
नरद नरद, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a par-<BR>ticular substance or article of commerce, a kind of<BR>perfume ? [cf. नलद]; (अस्), m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरदिक
नरदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, dealing in the substance<BR>called Narada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरायण|नरायणः
नरायण नरायण, नरेन्द्र. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरिष्टा
नरिष्टा नरिष्टा, f., Ved. joking, chatter-<BR>ing; sport, pastime; [cf. नर्म, नर्मन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरिष्यत्|नरिष्यन्त्
नरिष्यत् न-रिष्यत्, अन्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Manu Vaivasvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरिष्यन्त|नरिष्यन्तः
नरिष्यन्त, अस्, m., N. of a son of Marutta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरीय
नरीय नरीय, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Bhaṅga-kāra; (also read नारेय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरुण
नरुण नरुण, अस्, m. (fr. rt. नॄ), Ved.<BR>(according to a commentator) a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्कुटक|नर्कुटकं
नर्कुटक नर्कुटक, अम्, n. a nose [cf. न-<BR>कुट]; a kind of metre consisting of four lines of<BR>seventeen syllables each; [cf. नर्दटक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त|नर्तः|नर्त्त
नर्त नर्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. नृत्, the initial<BR>न् of which is not liable to become ण्), dancing;<BR>(अस्), m. dancing, dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तक|नर्तकः|नर्त्तक|नर्त्तकः
नर्तक, अस्, m. a dancer, a player of any de-<BR>scription; an actor, gesticulator, mime, mummer;<BR>a bard, herald; an elephant; a peacock; a species<BR>of reed [cf. पोटगल]; (ई), f. a female dancer,<BR>actress, singing girl; a female elephant; a peahen;<BR>a kind of perfume (= नलिका; cf. नटी); (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fr. the Caus.), causing to dance; (अस्), m. a<BR>dancing-master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तन|नर्तनः|नर्त्तन|नर्त्तनं
नर्तन, अस्, m. a dancer; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>dancing, gesticulating, acting, performing on the<BR>stage; [cf. नर्तना-गृह.]<BR>—नर्तन-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, fond of dancing; (अस्), m. a peacock.<BR>—नर्-<BR>तन-शाला, f. or नर्तनागार (˚न-अग्˚ or -आग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. or नर्तना-गृह, अम्, n. a dancing-room.<BR>—नरतन-स्थान, अम्, n. a dancing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तयितृ
नर्तयितृ, ता, m. ‘one who causes to dance,’ a<BR>dancing-master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तित|नर्त्तित
नर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, danced; made to dance;<BR>dandled; dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तिन्
नर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dancing; [cf. वंश-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तू
नर्तू, ऊस्, f. a female dancer or actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्
नर्द् नर्द् (connected with rt. नद्), cl.<BR>1. P. (ep. also A.) नर्दति (-ते), ननर्द,<BR>नर्दिता, नर्दिष्यति, अनर्दीत्, नर्दितुम्, to<BR>bellow, roar, shriek, sound; to go, move; [cf. pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">Page0471-c+ 77</a>]<BR>bably Hib. nuail-im, ‘I roar, howl;’ nuail, ‘roar-<BR>ing, howling.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द|नर्द्द
नर्द, अस्, आ, अम्, bellowing, roaring, sounding;<BR>[cf. गो-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दत्|नर्द्दत्
नर्दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, roaring, sounding; praising<BR>aloud; proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दन|नर्दनं|नर्द्दन
नर्दन, अस्, m. ‘one who roars,’ N. of a Nāga-<BR>rāja; (अम्), n. sounding, roaring, making a noise;<BR>celebrating, praising aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दनीय|नर्द्दनीय
नर्दनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sounded; to be<BR>celebrated or praised aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दमान
नर्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shouting, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दित|नर्दितः|नर्द्दित
नर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, roared, sounded, bellowed;<BR>celebrated, loudly praised; (अम्), n. sound, roar,<BR>bellow, bellowing; (अस्), m. a kind of die or a throw<BR>at dice, the chief die, (commonly नादी or नान्दी,<BR>perhaps ‘an ace,’ cf. वृष, a N. for the chief die<BR>in Nala VII. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दिन्|नर्द्दिन्
नर्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding, roaring, making a<BR>noise; [cf. गेहे-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दटक|नर्दटकः|नर्द्दटक|नर्द्दटकं
नर्दटक नर्दटक, अम्, n. a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines of seventeen syllables each;<BR>(wrongly written नर्धटक; cf. नर्कुटक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दबुद
नर्दबुद नर्दबुद or नर्दवुद, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्धटक
नर्धटक नर्धटक, wrong form for नर्-<BR>दटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्ब्
नर्ब् नर्ब्, cl. 1. P. नर्बति, &c., to go,<BR>move; [cf. rt. नम्ब्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म|नर्मः|नर्म्म
नर्म नर्म, अस्, m., Ved. sport, pastime;<BR>[cf. नरिष्टा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मठ|नर्मठः|नर्म्मठ|नर्म्मठः
नर्मठ, अस्, m. a jester; a rake, lecher, liber-<BR>tine; sport, amusement; coition; the nipple; the<BR>chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मन्|नर्म्मन्
नर्मन्, अ, n. sport, play, amusement, pastime;<BR>diversion; jest, joke, (नर्माणि कृ, to joke); wit,<BR>humour; (अणा), ind. in jest, by way of jest.<BR>—नर्-<BR>म-कील, अस्, m. a husband.<BR>—नर्म-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a secret lover.<BR>—नर्म-द, अस्, आ, अम्, delight-<BR>ing, making happy, giving or causing pleasure; (अस्),<BR>m. a jester; the associate or companion of a person's<BR>sports or amusements; N. of the son of Lāḍana;<BR>(आ), f. the Narma-dā or modern Nerbudda river,<BR>which, rising in the Vindhya mountains, runs west-<BR>ward to the gulf of Cambay, (personified as the wife<BR>of Puru-kutsa and mother of Trasa-dasyu); a sister<BR>of the Uragas or serpents; a daughter of the Soma-<BR>pas; a species of plant (see पृक्का).<BR>—नर्मदा-<BR>तट-देश, अस्, m., N. of a district mentioned in<BR>the Ratna-koṣa.<BR>—नर्मदा-तीर-गमन, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the seventeenth chapter of the Uttara-<BR>kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—नर्मदा-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n. a sacred bathing-place on the Narma-dā; [cf.<BR>नार्मद.]<BR>—नर्मदा-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>glory of Narma-dā,’ N. of the 173rd-181st chapter<BR>of the Matsya-Purāṇa.<BR>—नर्मदेश्वर (˚दा-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a form of Śiva.<BR>—नर्मदेश्वर-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of several sacred bathing-places.<BR>—नर्-<BR>मदेश्वर-माहात्म्य, अम्, n. ‘the glory of Śiva,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नर्मदेश्व-<BR>र-लिङ्ग, अम्, n., N. of the ninety-second chapter<BR>of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—नर्म-द्युति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, bright with joy, cheerful, happy, merry; (इस्),<BR>f. enjoyment of a joke or any amusement.<BR>—नर्म-<BR>वती, f., N. of a comedy.<BR>—नर्म-सचिव, अस्, m.<BR>‘amusement-companion,’ an associate or promoter of<BR>the amusements of a prince or man of rank.<BR>—नर्-<BR>म-साचिव्य, अम्, n. superintendence of a prince's<BR>amusements.<BR>—नर्म-सुहृद्, त्, m. = नर्म-स-<BR>चिव.<BR>—नर्म-स्फूर्ज, अस्, m. happiness or amuse-<BR>ment ending in alarm (?).<BR>—नर्म-स्फोट, अस्, m.<BR>slight or inferior amusement (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मय
नर्मय, Nom. P. नर्मयति, &c., to make<BR>happy or gladden by jests or sports, exhilarate by<BR>jesting and wit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मट|नर्मटः|नर्म्मट|नर्म्मटः
नर्मट नर्मट, अस्, m. a potsherd; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मरा
नर्मरा नर्मरा, f. a cavity, a valley; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">Page0472-a+ 79</a>]<BR>bellows; an old woman past menstruation; a species<BR>of plant (= सरला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0471-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्य|नर्यः|नर्य्य
नर्य नर्य. See p. 471, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्
नल् नल्, cl. 1. P. नलति, &c., to smell;<BR>to pain (?); to bind (?); cl. 10. P. नाल-<BR>यति, &c., to speak or shine; to bind or confine,<BR>(the two meanings ‘smelling’ and ‘binding’ have<BR>probably arisen from a confusion between गन्धे<BR>and बन्धे in the Dhātu-pāṭha.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल|नलं|नलः
नल नल, अस्, m. (for नड, q. v.), a species<BR>of reed, Amphidonax Karka, eight to twelve feet<BR>high [cf. नड, नाल, देव-नल]; N. of a king of<BR>the Niṣadhas or of the country called Niṣadha, son<BR>of Vīra-sena and husband of Damayantī and hero of<BR>the celebrated tale called Nala and Damayantī; a son<BR>of Niṣadha and father of Nabha or Nabhas; a<BR>descendant of the latter Nala, son of Su-dhanvan and<BR>father of Uktha [cf. नड]; N. of a son of Yadu;<BR>N. of a monkey-chief, son of Tvaṣṭṛ or Viśva-<BR>karman, who made a bridge for Rāma from the<BR>continent to Laṅkā; N. of a Daitya; N. of a<BR>medical author; (in astrology) N. of a particular<BR>form of constellation in which all the planets or stars<BR>are grouped in double mansions; a deified proge-<BR>nitor, wrongly written for नल्व; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>fragrant substance, a perfume (= नटी); red arsenic,<BR>= मनः-सिला, कुनटी; (अम्), n. the blossom of<BR>Nelumbium Speciosum (?); smell, odour; [cf. rt. नल्.]<BR>—नल-कानन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people, (this<BR>word may perhaps be separated into नलक-आनन;<BR>also read नल-कालक, नभ-कानन.)<BR>—नल-<BR>कील, अस्, m. the knee.<BR>—नल-कूबर and नल-<BR>कूवर, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kuvera.<BR>—नल-<BR>चम्पू, ऊस्, f., N. of a work by Tri-vikrama-bhaṭṭa,<BR>also called Damayantī-kathā, describing the fortunes<BR>of Nala and Damayantī in a highly artificial mixed<BR>style, half prose, half verse; [cf. चम्पू.]<BR>—नल-<BR>द, अम्, आ, n. f. Indian spikenard, Nardostachys Ja-<BR>tamansi (= जटामांसी); (अम्), n. the root of Andro-<BR>pogon Muricatus (= उशीर); the honey or nectar<BR>of a flower; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of Raudrāśva.<BR>—नल-पट्टिका, f. a sort of mat made with reeds,<BR>a coarse mat.<BR>—नल-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—नल-मीन, अस्, m. a species of sprat or (according<BR>to some) a shrimp or prawn; (also read तल-मीन.)<BR>—नल-सेतु, उस्, m. ‘Nala's bridge,’ the causeway<BR>constructed by the monkey Nala, (a name given to<BR>the rocks between Ramisseram and Ceylon, com-<BR>monly called Adam's bridge.)<BR>—नलेश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚ल-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—न-<BR>लोत्तम (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, m. a species of reed (= देव-<BR>नल).<BR>—नलोदय (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘Nala's rise,’<BR>N. of an artificial poem ascribed to Kāli-dāsa and<BR>describing the restoration of the fallen Nala to pros-<BR>perity and power.<BR>—नलोपख्यान (˚ल-उप्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘the story of Nala (and Damayantī),’ N. of a<BR>celebrated episode of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलक|नलकं
नलक, अम्, n. a bone (hollow like a reed),<BR>any long bone of the body; the tibia; the radius of<BR>the arm; (इका), f. a kind of fragrant substance (=<BR>नली, commonly पवारी or पन्ठारी); the legu-<BR>minous plant Dolichos Lablab; the plant Polianthes<BR>Tuberosa; Dæmia Extensa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकिनी
नलकिनी, f. (fr. an unused नलकिन्), the knee-cap<BR>or knee-pan; the leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलदिक
नलदिक, अस्, ई, अम्, dealing in Indian spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलित|नलितः
नलित, अस्, m. a species of vegetable, (commonly<BR>नालिता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिन|नलिनं|नलिनः
नलिन, अम्, n. (connected with नल, its stalk<BR>being hollow like that of a reed), a lotus flower or<BR>water-lily, Nelumbium Speciosum or Nymphæa Ne-<BR>lumbo; the indigo plant; water; (ई), f. a lotus,<BR>Nelumbium Speciosum, the flexible stalk of the water-<BR>lily; an assemblage of the Nelumbium Speciosum or<BR>of lotus flowers; a pond in which the lotus grows or<BR>may grow, a place abounding in lotuses, (नलिनी is<BR>to नलिन as अब्जिनी to अब्ज, पङ्कजिनी to पङ्क-<BR>ज, and पद्मिनी to पद्म); the Ganges of heaven<BR>or rather an arm of it; a mystical N. of one of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-b" target="_blank">Page0472-b+ 79</a>]<BR>nostrils (= नलिका); a kind of fragrant substance;<BR>the fermented and intoxicating juice of the cocoa-nut;<BR>N. of the wife of Aja-mīḍha and mother of Nīla;<BR>(अस्), m. the Indian crane (as a synonym of पुष्-<BR>कर); a species of shrub (= कृष्ण-पाक-फल).<BR>—नलिन-दल, अम्, n. a leaf of the lotus flower;<BR>[cf. नलिनी-दल, नव-नलिन-दलाय.]<BR>—नलिनी-<BR>खण्ड, अम्, n. an assemblage of the Nelumbium<BR>Speciosum.<BR>—नलिनी-दल, अम्, n. a leaf of the<BR>lotus plant; [cf. नलिन-दल.]<BR>—नलिनी-नन्दन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the divine garden near the Nalinī (?),’ N. of<BR>a garden of Kuvera.<BR>—नलिनी-पद्म-कोष, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular position of the hands in<BR>dancing.<BR>—नलिनी-रुह, अस्, आ, अम्, what comes<BR>forth or has come forth from a Nelumbium Speci-<BR>osum; (अस्), m. an epithet of Brahmā; (अम्), n.<BR>the fibres of the stalk of Nelumbium Speciosum.<BR>—नलिने-शय, अस्, m. (नलिने, loc. sing.), ‘reclin-<BR>ing on a lotus,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीक
नलिनीक at the end of comp. = नलिनी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्ल
नल्ल नल्ल, wrongly for नल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्व|नल्वः
नल्व नल्व, अस्, m. a furlong, a measure<BR>of distance = 400 or 104 (?) cubits; (wrongly read<BR>नल्ल, नल.)<BR>—नल्व-वर्त्मग, अस्, आ, अम्, going<BR>the distance of a Nalva; (आ), f. a spreading plant; the<BR>orange tree (= काकाङ्गी for नारङ्ग?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव 1. नव, अस्, आ, अम् (probably connected<BR>with the particle 1. नु, q. v., or less probably with<BR>नु for prep. अनु, or by some derived fr. rt. 4. नु,<BR>to praise), new, fresh, recent, young, modern; (अस्),<BR>m. a crow; a species of plant (= रक्त-पुनर्-नवा);<BR>N. of a son of Uśīnara and Navā; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a wife of Uśīnara and mother of Nava; (अम्), ind.<BR>recently, newly, lately, a short time ago, not long<BR>since, just, (the crude नव is prefixed to a past pass.<BR>part. in this sense, see नव-बद्ध); [for 2. नव<BR>see p. 473, col. 1: cf. Zend नव: Gr. νέο-ς,<BR>for νέϝο-ς, νεός, νειός, νε-αρό-ς, νε-ᾱν, νεᾱν-ία-ς,<BR>νέ-ᾱξ, νε-οσσό-ς, νε-οττ-ία, νε-οχ-μό-ς, νε-βρό-ς,<BR>νέ-ατο-ς, νεί-αιρα, νει-ρό-ν: Lat. novu-s, Noviu-s,<BR>nov-īciu-s, nov-āli-s, nov-ellu-s, nov-āre, nov-er-ca,<BR>nū-nt-iu-s, de-nuo, nū-per: Osk. Nuv-la, Nuceria:<BR>Goth. niu-yi-s, ‘new;’ niuyi-tha, ‘newness:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. niwe, neow, niwa: Lith. naú-ye-s, ‘new;’<BR>nauyó-ka-s, ‘a novice:’ Slav. nov-ŭ, ‘new:’ Hib.<BR>nua, nuadh.]<BR>—नव-कारिका, f. a bride, a woman<BR>newly married, (probably wrong reading for नव-<BR>वरिका); a new Kārikā or comment.<BR>—नव-कालिका,<BR>f. (fem. of नव-कालक), a young woman, either<BR>one recently married or one in whom menstruation<BR>has lately commenced.<BR>—नव-कृत्, wrongly for नव-<BR>गत्.<BR>—नव-गत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. first-born (?).<BR>—१. न-<BR>व-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under नवन्),<BR>lately caught; [cf. नव-बद्ध.]<BR>—नव-च्छात्त्र,<BR>अस्, m. a new scholar, a student, novice.<BR>—नव-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, recently born, lately produced, new, young<BR>(e. g. नव-जः शशी, the new moon or the moon<BR>just becoming visible).<BR>—नव-जा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved.<BR>lately produced, new, young.<BR>—नव-जात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. born anew, new-born, fresh, new.<BR>—नव-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम् (compar.), newer, younger, fresher,<BR>&c.; [cf. नवीयस्.]<BR>—नव-ता, f. or नव-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. freshness, novelty.<BR>—नव-दल, अम्, n. the fresh<BR>leaf of a lotus flower, any young leaf.<BR>—नव-द्वीप,<BR>अस्, m. ‘the new island,’ N. of a place now called<BR>Nuddea, sixty miles from Calcutta, in the district of<BR>Burdwan on the right bank of the Bhāgīrathī or<BR>great western branch of the Ganges at the point where<BR>it is joined by the Jellinghee.<BR>—नव-नगर, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the new town,’ N. of a town.<BR>—नव-नलिन-<BR>दलाय (fr. नव-नलिन-दल), Nom. A. नव-<BR>नलिन-दलायते, &c., to resemble the leaf of a<BR>fresh lotus blossom.<BR>—नवनलिनदलायमान,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, resembling the leaf of a fresh lotus<BR>flower.<BR>—नव-नी, ईस्, f. or नव-नीत, अम्, n. fresh<BR>butter.<BR>—नवनीतक, अम्, n. clarified butter.<BR>—न-<BR>वनीत-धेनु, उस्, f. a quantity of butter presented<BR>to Brāhmans, see धेनु.<BR>—नव-पर्णादि-भक्-<BR>षण, अम्, n. ‘eating of new leaves &c.,’ N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-c" target="_blank">Page0472-c+ 81</a>]<BR>chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नव-पल्लव,<BR>अम्, n. a new shoot, young sprout.<BR>—नव-प्रसूता,<BR>f. a woman who has lately brought forth (a child).<BR>—नव-प्राशन, अस्, m. eating of new rice or new<BR>barley.<BR>—नव-फलिका, f. a bride, a newly-married<BR>woman; a girl in whom menstruation has recently<BR>begun.<BR>—नव-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, lately caught,<BR>recently bound.<BR>—नव-मल्लिका, f. Arabian jasmine,<BR>Jasminum Sambac; (also read नव-मालिका.)<BR>—न-<BR>व-मालिका, f. many-flowered Nykanthes, Jasminum<BR>Sambac (= नव-मल्लिका); N. of a daughter of<BR>Dharma-vardhana, king of Śrāvasti.<BR>—नव-मालिनी,<BR>f. a kind of metre consisting of four lines of twelve<BR>syllables each.<BR>—नव-मेघ, अस्, m. a new cloud<BR>or one just appearing.<BR>—नव-यज्ञ, अस्, m. sacrifice<BR>or oblation of the first-fruits of the harvest; [cf. ना-<BR>वयज्ञिक, नवशस्येष्टि, नव-शस्य.]<BR>—नव-<BR>यौवन, अम्, n. fresh or incipient youth, bloom of<BR>youth, prime; (अस्, आ, अम्), being in the bloom of<BR>youth; (आ), f. a young woman.<BR>—नवयौवन-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, blooming with the freshness of<BR>youth.<BR>—नव-रक्तक, अम्, n. a newly-dyed gar-<BR>ment.<BR>—नव-रजस्, आस्, f. a girl who has only recently<BR>menstruated.<BR>—नव-वधू, ऊस्, f. a bride, a newly-<BR>married woman; a daughter-in-law.<BR>—नव-वरिका,<BR>f. a newly-married woman; [cf. नव-कारिका.]<BR>—नव-वस्त्र, अम्, n. new cloth.<BR>—नव-वास्त्व,<BR>अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man or of an evil spirit.<BR>—नव-शशि-भृत्, त्, m. ‘bearing the new moon<BR>(on his brow),’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—नव-शस्य,<BR>अम्, n. the first-fruits of the year's harvest, the grain<BR>first matured.<BR>—नवशस्येष्टि (˚य-इष्˚), इस्, f.<BR>‘sacrifice of first-fruits,’ a sacrifice performed on<BR>eating the first matured rice or grain of the year;<BR>(wrongly written नवसस्येष्टि; cf. नव-यज्ञ.)<BR>—नव-श्राद्ध, अम्, n. the first series of Śrāddhas<BR>collectively, or funeral offerings on the first, third,<BR>fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh days after a person's<BR>demise.<BR>—नव-सङ्घाराम (˚घ-आर्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a monastery.<BR>—नव-सू, ऊस्, f., Ved. a cow that has<BR>recently calved.<BR>—नव-सूतिका, f. a milch cow; a<BR>woman recently delivered.<BR>—नवाङ्कुर (˚व-अङ्˚),<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—नवान्न (˚व-अन्˚), अम्, n. new<BR>rice, new grain, the first-fruits; the grain first<BR>ripened, rice or grain recently matured; a cere-<BR>mony observed on first eating the new rice, &c.<BR>—नवान्न-भक्षण, अम्, n. ‘eating of new<BR>grain,’ N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नवान्न-स्थाली-पाकामन्त्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—नवान्नेष्टि (˚न-इष्˚), इस्, f. sacrifice<BR>of the first-fruits, see नवशस्येष्टि.<BR>—नवाम्बर<BR>(˚व-अम्˚), अम्, n. new and unbleached cloth.<BR>—नवाम्बु (˚व-अम्˚), n. fresh water.<BR>—नवार्म<BR>(˚व-अर्˚), अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—नवाह (˚व-<BR>अह), अस्, m. a new day, the first day of a fortnight.<BR>—नवी-करण, अम्, n. making new, doing anew,<BR>renewing.<BR>—नवी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to make new, renew, restaurate, revive.<BR>—नवी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done or made anew,<BR>renewed, revived.<BR>—नवी-भाव, अस्, m. becoming<BR>young or new, renovation.<BR>—नवी-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, become new, renewed, revived.<BR>—नवेतर<BR>(˚व-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘other than new,’ old.<BR>—न-<BR>वोढा (˚व-ऊढा), f. a newly-married woman, a<BR>bride.<BR>—नवोद्धृत (˚व-उद्˚), अम्, n. fresh<BR>butter; [cf. नव-नीत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवक
1. नवक, अस्, इका, अम्, = 1. नव, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नविष्ठ
नविष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. the newest, youngest,<BR>last; (अम्), ind. (?), at last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीन|नवीनं
नवीन, अस्, आ, अम्, = 1. नव, new, fresh, recent,<BR>modern.<BR>—नवीन-चन्द्र, अस्, m. the new moon.<BR>—नवीन-मत-विचार, अस्, m. ‘inquiring into<BR>new opinions,’ N. of a philosophical work by Hari-<BR>rāma.<BR>—नवीन-वेदन्तिन्, ई, m. a modern Vedānta<BR>philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीयस्
नवीयस् or नव्यस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of<BR>1. नव), Ved. new, fresh, young, recent, who has<BR>done anything or shown himself recently; very new;<BR>(अस्), ind. recently, lately; (असे or असा), ind. anew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
1. नव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. new, fresh, young;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of plant, = रक्त-पुनर्-नवा;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">Page0473-a+ 79</a>]<BR>[cf. Lith. nauya-s; Goth. niuyi-s.]<BR>—नव्य-मत-<BR>विचार, अस्, m. = नवीन-मत-विचार.<BR>—नव्य-<BR>वत्, ind. like new, ever new (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0472-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्यस्
नव्यस्. See नवीयस्, p. 472, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव 2. नव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 4. नु), praise;<BR>panegyric, celebration. (For 1. नव see p. 472,<BR>col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवन|नवनं
नवन, अम्, n. the act of praising, laudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नविष्टि
नविष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. a song of praise, hymn;<BR>(Sāy.) a new sacrifice or oblation, (as if fr. 1. नव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
2. नव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be praised, praise-<BR>worthy, laudable, deserving of praise.<BR>—नव्य-वर्-<BR>धमान, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत|नवतः
नवत 1. नवत, अस्, m. (for 2. see col. 2),<BR>an elephant's painted or variegated housings; woollen<BR>cloth; a cover, blanket, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवन्
नवन् नवन्, m. f. n. pl. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>4. नु), nine; [cf. Zend navan, ‘nine:’ Gr. ἐννέα,<BR>ἔνα-το-ς, ἔννα-το-ς, εἴνατο-ς, ἐννά-κις, ἐνάκις,<BR>εἰνάκις, ἐνα-κόσιοι, ἐννα-κόσιοι, ἐνενή-κοντα,<BR>ἐννή-κοντα: Lat. novem, nōnu-s, nov-iens, nōnā-ginta,<BR>non-genti: Goth. niun, ‘nine;’ niun-da, ‘the<BR>ninth:’ Angl. Sax. nigan, ‘nine:’ Old Germ. niun:<BR>Mod. Germ. neun: Old Pruss. nevīn-ts, ‘the ninth:’<BR>Slav. devan-tĭ, ‘nine:’ Lith. devyn-i, ‘nine,’ n<BR>changed into d as in debes-i-s, ‘a cloud,’ from Sanskrit<BR>नभस्; devī1n-ta-s, ‘the ninth:’ Hib. naoi, ‘nine:’<BR>Cambro-Brit. naw, ‘nine.’]<BR>—नवकाण्डिका-भा-<BR>ष्य, अम्, n. ‘commentary of nine sections,’ N. of a<BR>commentary on Kātyāyana's Śrāddha-sūtras by Nīlā-<BR>sura.<BR>—नव-कृत्वस्, ind., 9 times.<BR>—२. नव-<BR>ग्रह, आस्, m. pl. the 9 planets, or sun, moon,<BR>five planets, and the ascending and descending nodes.<BR>—नवग्रह-मन्त्र, आस्, m. pl. ‘hymns or prayers<BR>to the 9 planets (?),’ N. of a work.<BR>—नवग्रह-<BR>शान्ति, इस्, f. propitiation of the 9 planets.<BR>—नव-<BR>ग्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ninefold, consisting of 9;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a mythological family often<BR>associated with that of Aṅgiras and described as<BR>sharing in Indra's battles, regulating the worship of<BR>the gods, &c.; (अस्), m. one of the family called<BR>Nava-gvas; [cf. दश-ग्व, दशग्विन्.]<BR>—नवचत्-<BR>वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the following), the 49th.<BR>—नव-चत्वारिंशत्, त्, f., 49.<BR>—नव-तन्तु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—नवत्रिंश, अस्,<BR>ई, अम् (fr. the following), the 39th.<BR>—नव-त्रिंशत्,<BR>त्, f., 39.<BR>—नव-दश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the follow-<BR>ing), the 19th; consisting of 19.<BR>—नव-दशन्, अ,<BR>m. f. n. pl., 19.<BR>—नव-दीधिति, इस्, m. ‘nine-rayed,’<BR>Mars, the planet or its deified regent; [cf. नवार्चिस्.]<BR>—नव-दुर्गा, f. Durgā in her 9 forms (viz.<BR>कुमारिका, त्रि-मूर्ति, कल्याणी, रोहिणी, काली, चण्-<BR>डिका, शाम्भवी, दुर्गा, भद्रा).<BR>—नव-दोला,<BR>f. a litter borne by 9 men.<BR>—नव-द्वार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘nine-doored,’ having 9 gates; an epithet of<BR>the body, which has 9 apertures or outlets, as the<BR>nostrils, ears, mouth, &c.; [cf. नव-मुख.]<BR>—न-<BR>व-धा, ind. divided into 9 parts, ninefold, in 9<BR>ways, 9 times.<BR>—नव-नवति, इस्, f., 99; (in the<BR>Veda the number 99 is used for any large number.)<BR>—नवनवति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 99th.<BR>—नव-<BR>पञ्चाश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the following), the 59th.<BR>—न-<BR>व-पञ्चाशत्, त्, f., 59.<BR>—नव-पद्, -पात्, -पदी,<BR>पत्, Ved. having 9 feet, consisting of 9 feet.<BR>—नव-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. the 9th part, especially of an asterism<BR>or of a lunar mansion; [cf. नवांश.]<BR>—नव-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having 9 apertures or openings;<BR>[cf. नव-द्वार.]<BR>—नव-रङ्ग, अम्, n. gift to five<BR>and acceptance by four persons of the best Kāyastha<BR>families (?).<BR>—नवरङ्ग-कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the privilege of marrying into 9 distinct families (?).<BR>—नव-रत्न, अम्, n., 9 precious gems, viz. a<BR>pearl, ruby, topaz, diamond, emerald, lapis lazuli, coral,<BR>sapphire, and one called Go-meda, (these 9 jewels are<BR>supposed to be related to the 9 planets); the 9 jewels,<BR>i. e. the 9 men of letters at the court of Vikramā-<BR>ditya were Dhanvantari, Kṣapaṇaka, Amara-siṃha,<BR>Śaṅku, Vetāla-bhaṭṭa, Ghaṭa-karpara, Kāli-dāsa, Vara-<BR>ruci, and Varāha-mihira; N. of a collection of 9 verses.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">Page0473-b+ 77</a>]<BR>—नव-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Bhīma-ratha<BR>and father of Daśa-ratha.<BR>—नव-रात्र, अस्, m. or<BR>नवरात्रिक, अम्, n. a period of 9 days; a Soma<BR>sacrifice with 9 Sutyā days; 9 days in the middle of<BR>the Gavām-ayana; (अम्), n. the period of 9 days<BR>from the first of the light half of month Āśvina to<BR>the 9th, devoted to the worship of Durgā.<BR>—नव-<BR>राशिक, the rule of proportion with 9 terms com-<BR>prising four proportions.<BR>—नवर्च (˚व-ऋच), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. consisting of 9 verses.<BR>—नवविंश,<BR>अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the following), the 29th.<BR>—नव-<BR>विंशति, इस्, f., 29.<BR>—नव-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, nine-<BR>fold, consisting of 9 parts.<BR>—नव-व्यूह, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; [cf. चतुर्-व्यूह.]<BR>—नव-<BR>शक्ति, इस्, m. ‘having 9 faculties,’ an epithet of Śiva<BR>or Viṣṇu.<BR>—नव-शत, अम्, n., 109.<BR>—नवशत-<BR>तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 109th.<BR>—नव-शस्, ind., 9 by<BR>9, by nines.<BR>—नव-शायक, अस्, m. a N. given to any<BR>of 9 inferior classes, viz. cowherd, gardener, oilman,<BR>weaver, confectioner, water-carrier, potter, blacksmith,<BR>and barber.<BR>—नव-षट्क, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting<BR>of 9 × 6 (strings &c.).<BR>—नव-षष्टि, इस्, f., 69.<BR>—नवषष्टि-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 69th.<BR>—न-<BR>व-सप्तति, इस्, f., 79.<BR>—नवसप्तति-तम, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the 79th.<BR>—नव-सप्तदश, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>Atirātra (‘containing 9 Saptadaśa-stotras’).<BR>—नव-<BR>साहसाङ्क-चरित, अम्, n. ‘the 9 or the new (fr.<BR>1. नव) deeds of king Sāhasāṅka,’ N. of a Campū<BR>composed by Śrī-harṣa.<BR>—नवांश or नवांशक<BR>(˚व-आं˚), अस्, m. a 9th, a 9th part, especially of an<BR>asterism or lunar mansion; [cf. नव-भाग.]<BR>—न-<BR>वांशक-प, अस्, m. the regent of a Navāṃśaka.<BR>—नवांश-नाथ, अस्, m. the regent of a Navāṃśa.<BR>—नवाङ्गा (˚व-अङ्˚), f. a species of plant (=<BR>कर्कट-शृङ्गी).<BR>—नवायस (˚व-आय्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>medicinal preparation of iron, containing 9 parts of<BR>iron.<BR>—नवार्चिस् (˚व-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘nine-rayed,’ the<BR>planet Mars or its deified personification.<BR>—नवाशीति<BR>(˚व-अश्˚), इस्, f., 89.<BR>—नवाशीति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>the 89th.<BR>—नवाह (˚व-अह), अस्, m. a period of<BR>9 days; a Soma sacrifice with 9 Sutyā days; 9 days<BR>in the middle of the Gavām-ayana; [cf. नव-<BR>रात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
3. नव = नवन्, nine, in त्रि-णव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवक
2. नवक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of 9; (अम्), n.<BR>the aggreagate of nine, nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत|नवतः
2. नवत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 90th; [cf. एक-न्˚, चतुर्-<BR>ण्˚, चतुर्-न्˚, त्रि-न्˚, द्वा-न्˚, द्वि-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवति|नवतिः
नवति, इस् (according to lexicographers also न-<BR>वती), f., 90.<BR>—नवति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 90th.<BR>—नवति-धनुस्, उस्, m., N. of an ancestor of<BR>Śākya-muni.<BR>—नवति-धा, ind. ninetyfold.<BR>—न-<BR>वति-रथ, अस्, m., N. of an ancestor of Śākya-<BR>muni.<BR>—नवति-शस्, ind. by nineties, ninety by<BR>ninety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिक
नवतिक, f. (fr. नवति), a paint-brush containing<BR>90 hairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवम|नवमः
नवम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 9th; (आ), f., scil. तिथि,<BR>the 9th day of a lunar half month.<BR>—नवमांश<BR>(˚म-अं˚), अस्, m. = नवांश, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमक
नवमक, अस्, इका, अम्, the 9th.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नविन्
नविन्, ई, इनी, इ, consisting of 9, composed of 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवपत्त्रिका
नवपत्त्रिका नव-पत्त्रिका, f. (fr. 1. or 2.<BR>नव?), a particular sport described in the Kāma-sūtra<BR>by Vātsyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवर
नवर नवर, a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरम्
नवरम् नवरम्, ind. only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नविपुला
नविपुला न-विपुला, f. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवेदस्
नवेदस् नवेदस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. cognizant,<BR>observing, perceiving; appreciating; an observer; ap-<BR>preciator (with gen. of the object); [cf. को-विद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
नव्य 1. and 2. नव्य, See p. 472, col. 3;<BR>and col. 1. of this page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
नश् 1. नश् (related to rt. नक्ष्; cf. rt.<BR>1. अश्), cl. 1. P. A. नशति, -ते, Aor.<BR>आनट् or आनक्, &c. (Pāṇ. VI. 4, 73, but these forms<BR>may be referred to rt. 1. अश्), Ved. to reach, attain,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">Page0473-c+ 80</a>]<BR>obtain; to meet with, find; Caus. नशयति, &c., to<BR>cause to obtain or meet with; [cf. Lat. nanciscor.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश|नशः
1. नश in दू-णश, दुर्-णश, q. v.; [cf. 1.<BR>नाश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
नश् 2. नश्, cl. 1. 4. (more usually cl.<BR>4.) P. नशति, नश्यति (ep. also -ते),<BR>ननाश (3rd pl. नेशुस्), नशिता, नंष्टा (accord-<BR>ing to Vopa-deva also नङ्ग्धा), नशिष्यति, नङ्क्-<BR>ष्यति, अनशत्, अनेशत्, नशितुम्, नंष्टुम्, to be<BR>lost, disappear, to become invisible, to vanish; to<BR>perish, be destroyed, wane; to escape, run away;<BR>to come to nothing, be frustrated, be unsuccessful:<BR>Caus. नाशयति (ep. also A. नाशयते), -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अनीनशत्, to cause to disappear, make invisible;<BR>to cause to perish, suffer to perish, destroy, efface;<BR>to violate, deflower; to cause to be lost, to lose; to<BR>forget; to extinguish (as a fire); to drive away, cause<BR>to fly away; to disappear (in मा व्याघ्रा नीनशुर्<BR>वनात्, let not the tigers disappear from the forest,<BR>Mahā-bh. Udyoga-p. 862): Desid. निनशिषति, नि-<BR>नङ्क्षति: Intens. नानश्यते, नानंष्टि; [cf.<BR>Zend naśu, ‘a corpse;’ naś-ista, ‘very destructive:’<BR>Gr. νέκ-υ-ς, νέκυ-ια, νεκ-ρό-ς, probably νόσο-ς,<BR>νοῦσο-ς for νοξο-ς, like συν for ξυν: Lat. nex, nec-<BR>are, noc-ēre, noxa, per-nicies, ve-ne-nu-m for ve-<BR>nec-nu-m: Goth. nau-s, navi-s, ‘a corpse,’ for nag-<BR>u-s or nah-u-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
3. नश्, क्, क्, क्, or ट्, ट्, ट्, disappearing; perishing;<BR>[cf. जीव-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश|नशः
2. नश, अस्, m. destruction; perishing; [cf. 2.<BR>नाश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशन
नशन, अम्, n. disappearing, vanishing; perishing;<BR>escaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशितृ
नशितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who disappears; perishing,<BR>being lost; destroying, a destroyer; [cf. नंष्टृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्
नश्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, perishing, decaying, being<BR>destroyed; waning, wasting.<BR>—नश्यत्-प्रसूति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, whose offspring perishes; (इस्), f. a woman<BR>who brings forth a dead child.<BR>—नश्यत्प्रसूतिका,<BR>f. a female bearing a dead child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर, अस्, ई, अम्, perishing, perishable; de-<BR>structible; transitory, evanescent, subject to decay;<BR>destructive, mischievous.<BR>—नश्वर-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>perishableness, transitoriness; destructiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, lost, disappeared, disappearing;<BR>vanished, invisible, lost sight of; perished, destroyed,<BR>ruined, spoiled, wasted, annihilated, dead; run away,<BR>fled; depraved, debauched; deprived of (at the<BR>beginning of a comp.).<BR>—नष्ट-चन्द्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the fourth day in both halves of the<BR>month Bhādra.<BR>—नष्ट-चेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has lost consciousness, unconscious, fainted, in-<BR>sensible, swooning away, losing one's senses.<BR>—नष्-<BR>ट-चेष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost the power<BR>of motion; unconscious, fainted, insensible.<BR>—नष्-<BR>टचेष्ट-ता, f. unconsciousness, insensibility, faint-<BR>ing, swooning.<BR>—नष्ट-जन्मन्, अ, n. ‘the lost<BR>nativity,’ subsequent calculation or casting of a lost<BR>nativity.<BR>—नष्ट-जातक, अम्, n. = नष्ट-जन्-<BR>मन्; N. of the thirteenth Adhyāya in Varāha-<BR>mihira's Laghu-jātaka.<BR>—नष्ट-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>one who has lost his sight, blind.<BR>—नष्ट-मति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, one who has lost his intellects.<BR>—नष्ट-<BR>मार्गण, अम्, n. seeking any lost object.<BR>—नष्ट-<BR>राज्य, अम्, n., N. of a district to the north-east of<BR>Madhya-deśa.<BR>—नष्ट-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>form is lost or no more seen; (आ), f., scil. अनु-<BR>ष्टुभ्, a variety of the Anu-ṣṭubh.<BR>—नष्ट-<BR>विष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (a snake &c.) that has lost<BR>(its) venom.<BR>—नष्ट-वीज, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute<BR>of the seminal secretion, without the power of pro-<BR>creating, impotent.<BR>—नष्ट-वेदन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>finding a lost object.<BR>—नष्ट-संस्मृति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>one who has lost his memory, unmindful, forgetful.<BR>—नष्ट-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost<BR>his consciousness.<BR>—नष्ट-स्मृति, इस्, इस्, इ, one<BR>who has lost his memory, forgetful.<BR>—नष्टाग्नि<BR>(˚ट-अग्˚), इस्, m. a Brāhman or householder whose<BR>fire has been extinguished or who has lost his conse-<BR>crated fire.<BR>—नष्टातङ्कम् (˚ट-आत्˚), ind. without<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">Page0474-a+ 76</a>]<BR>anxiety or fear.<BR>—नष्टात्मन् (˚ट-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ,<BR>deprived of mind or sense.<BR>—नष्टाप्ति-सूत्र (˚ट-<BR>आप्˚), अम्, n. booty, plunder.<BR>—नष्टार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost his property, reduced<BR>to poverty.<BR>—नष्टाशङ्क (˚ट-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>destitute of fear, fearless, dauntless.<BR>—नष्टासु<BR>(˚ट-असु), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. one whose vital spirits<BR>have disappeared.<BR>—नष्टेन्दु-कला (˚ट-इन्˚), f. the<BR>day of new moon when it rises invisible.<BR>—नष्टेन्-<BR>द्रिय (˚ट-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has lost his<BR>organs of sense, deprived of one's senses.<BR>—नष्-<BR>टैषिन् (˚ट-एष्˚), ई, इणी, इ, seeking any lost object.<BR>—नष्टैष्य, अम्, n. the act of seeking what<BR>has been lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0473-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टि|नष्टिः
नष्टि, इस्, f. loss, destruction, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशाक|नशाकः
नशाक नशाक, अस्, m. a species of crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट नष्ट. See p. 473, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् 1. नस् (the alternative form for अस्मान्<BR>acc. pl., for अस्मभ्यम् dat. pl., and for अस्माकम्<BR>gen. pl. of the first personal pronoun अस्मद्, q. v.),<BR>us, to us, of us; (नस् is an enclitic and has no<BR>accent.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् 2. नस्, cl. 1. A. नसते, नेसे, नसिता,<BR>&c., Ved. to approach, to go towards, to<BR>join; to copulate (especially as husband and wife);<BR>(said to mean also) to be crooked or curved; to bend;<BR>to be fraudulent; [cf. Gr. νέ-ο-μαι, νίσ-σ-ο-μαι,<BR>νόσ-το-ς, probably also ναίω for νασ-_y_-ω, ἔ-νασ-σα,<BR>ἐ-νάσ-θη-ν.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् 3. नस्, f. (probably fr. rt. स्ना, to<BR>bathe, or स्नु, to flow, the initial स् being dropped;<BR>cf. नौ; नस् is defective in nom. voc. sing. du. and<BR>pl., acc. sing. du., but may be optionally substituted for<BR>नासिका, q. v., in the acc. pl. and remaining cases, e. g.<BR>नसस् or नासिकास्, नसा or नासिकया, नोभ्याम् or<BR>नासिकाभ्याम्; only the weak cases नसा, नसि, न-<BR>सोस्, however, appear to occur), the nose; [cf. नासा,<BR>नासिका; Lat. nasus, naris.]<BR>—नः-क्षुद्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, small-nosed.<BR>—नस्तः-कर्मन्, अ, n. ‘the put-<BR>ting into the nose,’ taking snuff.<BR>—नस्-तस्, ind. from<BR>the nose, into the nose.<BR>—नस्य्-ओत, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr.<BR>नसि loc. sing. + ओत), led by a string through the<BR>septum of the nose, fastened by the nose, furnished<BR>with a nose-ring; an ox or other animal led by a<BR>string through the septum of the nose.<BR>—नस्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस
नस (at the end of an adj. comp.) = 3. नस्, the<BR>nose, see उन्-न्˚, उरू-ण्˚, कुम्भी-न्˚, खर-ण्˚,<BR>गो-न्˚, द्रु-ण्˚, &c.; (आ), f. the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसि
नसि, the nose (?), in कुम्भी-न्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्त|नस्तः
नस्त, अस्, m. the nose; (आ), f. a hole bored<BR>in the septum of the nose, cf. नस्तक, नस्-<BR>तित; (अम्), n. a sternutatory, snuff.<BR>—नस्त-<BR>करण, अम्, n. a kind of instrument used by the<BR>Bhikṣus for injecting the nose.<BR>—नस्त-तस्, ind.<BR>(perhaps only = नस्-तस् with reduplicated affix तस्),<BR>from the nose, out of the nose.<BR>—नस्तोत (˚त-<BR>ओत), अस्, m. an ox led by a string through his nose;<BR>(also read नस्य्-ओत; see under 3. नस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तक|नस्तकं
नस्तक, अस्, m. a hole bored in the septum or<BR>bridge of the nose of cattle for draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तित|नस्तितः
नस्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, nozzled, having a hole bored<BR>in the septum of the nose, an ox or any other<BR>draught animal with a string through its nose, (the<BR>sort of rein usually employed in India.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्य|नस्यं
नस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to the<BR>nose, nasal, in the nose; (आ), f. the nose; the string<BR>through the nose of an animal [cf. नास्य]; (अम्),<BR>n. the hairs in the nose; a sternutatory, snuff.<BR>—नस्य-विधि, इस्, m. ‘rules about sternutatories,’<BR>N. of the twenty-seventh chapter of the medical<BR>work Śārṅgadhara-saṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसंविद्
नसंविद् न-संविद्, त्, f. unconsciousness;<BR>forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसुकर
नसुकर न-सुकर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, not easy<BR>to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह्
नह् 1. नह्, cl. 4. P. A. नह्यति, -ते, न-<BR>नाह, नेहे, नद्धा, नत्स्यति, -ते, अनात्-<BR>सीत्, अनद्ध, नद्धुम्, to bind, tie, bind on, bind<BR>round, put on, gird round, bind together; A. to put<BR>on one's self, dress, put on armour, arm one's self:<BR>Caus. नाहयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अनीनहत्, to cause<BR>to bind or tie together, to cause to put on: Desid.<BR>निनत्सति, -ते: Intens. नानह्यते, नानद्धि; [cf.<BR>Gr. νέ-ω, νή-θ-ω, νῆ-μα, νῆ-σι-ς, νῆ-τρο-ν, νέ-ω,<BR>Intens. νη-νέ-ω, νη-έ-ω: Lat. ne-o, ne-men, ne-<BR>tu-s, nec-t-o, nexu-s: Old Germ. nā-an, nāw-an,<BR>nāh-an, ‘to sew;’ nā-dal, ‘needle;’ nah, ‘near:’<BR>Goth. nethla, ‘a needle;’ nēhva, ‘near:’ Angl. Sax.<BR>naedl, ‘needle;’ neah, neh-st, nearra: Eng. nigh:<BR>Mod. Germ. näh-en, nad-el, nah, nach, ge-nug:<BR>Hib. nasgaim, ‘I bind;’ nas, ‘a tie.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह्
2. नह्, त्, f., Ved. a bond, tie; [cf. अक्षा-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह
नह in द्रु-णह, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहन
नहन, अम्, n., Ved. a bolt, a nail or connecting<BR>beam in a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह्यमान
नह्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being bound, tied, or<BR>fettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहि
नहि न-हि, ind. for not, surely not, cer-<BR>tainly not, by no means, not at all; न-नहि, cer-<BR>tainly not; (नहि is sometimes strengthened in the<BR>Veda by other particles, e. g. नह्य् अङ्ग, नहि नु,<BR>नहि स्म.)<BR>—नहि-मात्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a particular high number; [cf. न-मात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुस्
नहुस् नहुस्, उस्, m. a man, one who does<BR>not belong to one's own immediate community, a<BR>neighbour [cf. नाभि; Mod. Germ. nahe]; (collec-<BR>tively) the neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष|नहुषः
नहुष, अस्, m., Ved. = नहुस्, a man; N. of a<BR>son of Manu and author of a Ṛg-veda hymn; N. of<BR>an ancient king, one of the lunar race, son of Āyus<BR>and grandson of Purū-ravas, father of Yayāti, who<BR>took possession of Indra's throne in heaven for a<BR>time, but was afterwards deposed and changed into a<BR>serpent; (according to others) a son of Ambarīṣa,<BR>father of Nābhāga; N. of a serpent-demon; N. of a<BR>Marut; an epithet of Kṛṣṇa-Viṣṇu; [cf. नघु-<BR>ष, नाहुष, नाहुषि.]<BR>—नहुष-चरित, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the life of Nahuṣa,’ N. of the 112th chapter<BR>of the Bhūmi-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—न-<BR>हुषाख्य (˚ष-आख्˚), अम्, n. the plant Taber-<BR>næmontana Coronaria (= तगर-पुष्प).<BR>—न-<BR>हुषात्मज (˚ष-आत्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king, the<BR>son of Nahuṣa, also called Yayāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष्टर
नहुष्टर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. nearer (?), nearer<BR>than a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष्य|नहुष्यः
नहुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to a de-<BR>scendant of Nahus, belonging to a man in general,<BR>human; (अस्), m. a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ना
ना ना, ind. = न, no, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक|नाकः
नाक नाक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. न + अ-<BR>क, where there is no unhappiness), heaven, the<BR>vault or ceiling of heaven, the upper sky, the firma-<BR>ment, sky, atmosphere, ether, paradise, (often in the<BR>Veda with दिवो, gen. of 3. दिव्, or with उत्तम or<BR>तृतीय; cf. त्रि-नाक, त्रि-दिव: in Vājasaneyi-<BR>saṃhitā XVII. 67, the scale upwards is given as<BR>follows, 1. पृथिवी, earth; 2. अन्तरीक्ष, atmo-<BR>sphere; 3. दिव्, sky; 4. दिवो-नाक, upper sky;<BR>5. स्वर्-ज्योतिस्, heaven of light or sphere of the<BR>luminaries); the sun (?) ; N. of a Maudgalya; N. of<BR>a mythical weapon of Arjuna; (अस्, आ, अम्), ‘pain-<BR>less (?),’ N. of a dynasty.<BR>—नाक-चर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>walking in the sky (as the Pitṛs).<BR>—नाक-नाथ,<BR>अस्, m. or नाक-नाथक, अस्, m. ‘guardian of the<BR>sky,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—नाक-नायक, अस्, m.<BR>‘chief of the sky,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—नाकना-<BR>यक-पुरोहित, अस्, m. ‘Indra's chief priest,’ an<BR>epithet of Bṛhas-pati.<BR>—नाक-पाल, अस्, m. guardian<BR>or lord of the sky.<BR>—नाक-पृष्ठ, अम्, n. ‘sky-<BR>ceiling,’ the upper sky, the uppermost heaven.<BR>—ना-<BR>क-पृष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the highest<BR>heaven.<BR>—नाक-लोक, अस्, m. the heavenly world.<BR>—नाक-वनिता, f. ‘a nymph of heaven,’ an Apsaras.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">Page0474-c+ 78</a>]<BR>—नाक-सद्, त्, त्, त्, resting in the firmament, in-<BR>habiting the sky; (त्), m. an inhabitant of heaven,<BR>a deity; (अस्), m. pl., N. of nine Ekāhas; (त्), f., N.<BR>of an Iṣṭakā.<BR>—नाकापगा (˚क-आप्˚), f. the river<BR>of heaven, the heavenly Gaṅgā.<BR>—नाकेश (˚क-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. ‘the lord of the sky,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—नाकेश्वर (˚क-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘the lord of heaven,’<BR>a god.<BR>—नाकौकस् (˚क-ओक्˚), आस्, m. ‘whose dwell-<BR>ing is the sky,’ an inhabitant of heaven, a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिन्
नाकिन्, ई, m. a deity, god (as dwelling in Nāka).<BR>—नाकि-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘chief of the gods,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकु|नाकुः
नाकु नाकु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. नम्),<BR>an ant-hill or mole-hill, a burrow; a mountain; N.<BR>of a Muni or saint.<BR>—नाकु-सद्मन्, आ, m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुल|नाकुलः
नाकुल नाकुल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नकुल), re-<BR>lating or belonging to an ichneumon, ichneumon-like,<BR>similar to an ichneumon; (अस्), m. a patronymic from<BR>Nakula [cf. नाकुलि]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(ई), f. the ichneumon plant, a particular plant sup-<BR>posed to furnish the ichneumon or mungoose with<BR>an antidote when bitten in a conflict with a snake<BR>[cf. गन्ध-नाकुली, नकुलेष्टा]; a sort of pepper,<BR>Piper Chaba (= चव्य); the root of the Seemul tree<BR>(= कुक्कुटी-कन्द) and several other plants, as य-<BR>व-तिक्ता, श्वेत-कण्ट-कारी, सर्प-गन्धा.<BR>—ना-<BR>कुलान्ध्य (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘ichneumon blindness,’<BR>a kind of weakness of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुलि
नाकुलि, इस्, m. a descendant of Nakula, a patro-<BR>nymic of Śatānīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्र
नाक्र नाक्र, अस्, m., Ved. an aquatic animal;<BR>[cf. नक्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्र|नाक्षत्रं|नाक्षत्रः
नाक्षत्र नाक्षत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नक्षत्र),<BR>belonging to the constellations or lunar asterisms,<BR>starry, sidereal; (अम्), n. a month computed by the<BR>moon's passage through the twenty-seven mansions,<BR>or one of thirty days of sixty Ghaṭis each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्रिक|नाक्षत्रिकः
नाक्षत्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>the lunar asterisms, sidereal; (अस्), m. a month of<BR>twenty-seven days, each day being the period of the<BR>moon's passage through a lunar asterism; (ई), f. the<BR>state or condition to which a person is subjected<BR>agreeably to the asterism presiding over his nativity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग|नागं|नागः
नाग नाग, अस्, m. (perhaps for original<BR>स्नाग; Angl. Sax. snaca; Eng. snake; or connected<BR>with नग, a mountain, or नग्न, naked; said to be<BR>fr. rt. 1. दह् through change of द् into न्), a snake in<BR>general, especially the spectacle-snake or cobra capella,<BR>Coluber; a Nāga or fabulous serpent-demon so<BR>called, having a human face with the tail of a ser-<BR>pent, (the race of these beings is said to have sprung<BR>from Kadrū, wife of Kaśyapa [or from Su-rasā], in<BR>order to people Pātāla, one of the regions below the<BR>earth, their city is called Bhoga-vatī); an elephant;<BR>a shark (= तन्तु-नाग); a cruel or tyrannical<BR>person; (at the end of a comp.) ‘an elephant of a<BR>man,’ any great or pre-eminent person; N. of several<BR>plants, the small tree with fragrant blossoms, Mesua<BR>Roxburghii [cf. नाग-केशर]; Rottlera Tinctoria<BR>(= पुन्-नाग); a Cyperus (= मुस्तक); Piper<BR>Betel; a poisonous plant (see नाग-स्तोकक); a<BR>cloud; a peg or nail projecting from a wall to hang<BR>anything upon; one of the five airs of the body,<BR>that which is expelled by eructation; N. of the<BR>number seven, (probably to be referred to seven<BR>mythical serpents, but eight principal Nāgas are<BR>mentioned); N. of a Sādhya; of a Buddhist teacher;<BR>of a king of Āryāvarta, contemporary of Samudra-<BR>gupta; N. of a dynasty consisting of nine or seven<BR>princes; N. of several men; N. of a mountain; of<BR>a district; (ई), f. a female Nāga; a female elephant;<BR>(अम्), n. tin; lead; one of the astronomical periods<BR>called Karaṇas, (it is one of those termed ध्रुव,<BR>q. v., or invariable, and corresponds to the last half of<BR>Amāvāsya or new moon); the effects of that period<BR>on anything done or happening during it; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), formed or consisting of snakes, serpentine,<BR>snaky; relating to serpents or serpent-demons;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-a" target="_blank">Page0475-a+ 81</a>]<BR>elephantine, belonging to or resembling an elephant;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a woman; [cf. क्षिति-न्˚.]<BR>—नाग-<BR>कन्द, अस्, m. a kind of bulbous plant (= हस्ति-<BR>कन्द).<BR>—नाग-कन्यका, f. a serpent-virgin.<BR>—नाग-कर्ण, अस्, m. a kind of Ricinus (= रक्-<BR>तैरण्ड, हस्ति-कर्ण).<BR>—नाग-किञ्जल्क, अम्, n.<BR>the blossom of Mesua Roxburghii.<BR>—नाग-कुमार,<BR>अस्, m. a prince of the serpent-demons; N. of a class<BR>of deities among the Bhavanādhīśas guarding the<BR>treasures of Kuvera.<BR>—नाग-केश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>minister of king Nageśa.<BR>—नाग-केशर or नाग-<BR>केसर, अस्, m. a small tree with fragrant blossoms<BR>(commonly Nageśar), Mesua Roxburghii or Ferrea;<BR>(अम्), n. the blossom of this tree.<BR>—नाग-खण्ड,<BR>N. of one of the nine divisions of Bhārata-varṣa.<BR>—नाग-गन्धा, f. a species of bulbous plant (=<BR>नाकुली or सर्प-गन्धा).<BR>—नाग-गर्भ, अम्,<BR>n. red lead.<BR>—नाग-चूड, अस्, m. ‘snake-crested’ or<BR>‘whose top-knot consists of snakes,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—नाग-च्छत्त्रा, f. a kind of plant, Tiaridium<BR>Indicum.<BR>—नाग-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by or born<BR>from a Nāga, &c.; (अम्), n. red lead; tin.<BR>—नाग-<BR>जिह्वा, f. ‘snake-tongue,’ a species of plant, Asclepias<BR>Pseudosarsa; (see शारिवा.)<BR>—नाग-जिह्विका, f. red<BR>arsenic.<BR>—नाग-जीवन, अम्, n. tin.<BR>—नागजीवन-<BR>शत्रु, उस्, m. ‘enemy of tin,’ orpiment.<BR>—नाग-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—नाग-दत्त, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, given by Nāgas or serpents; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>one of the 100 sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; N. of a man<BR>related to Śākya-muni; of a king of Āryāvarta,<BR>contemporary of Samudra-gupta.<BR>—नाग-दन्त, अस्,<BR>m. elephant's tusk or ivory, the tooth or tusk of an<BR>elephant; a shelf, peg, or bracket projecting from<BR>a wall and used to hang things upon; (आ), f., N. of<BR>an Apsaras; (ई), f. a species of sun-flower, Helio-<BR>tropium Indicum; a harlot.<BR>—नागदन्तक, अस्,<BR>m. ivory; a wooden peg or bracket projecting from<BR>a wall, a shelf; (इका), f. a plant, commonly called<BR>Rāma-dūti, Tragia Involucrata.<BR>—नाग-दमनी, f.<BR>a particular plant (= जम्बू, जाम्बवती, वृक्का).<BR>—नाग-दलोपम (˚ल-उप्˚), अम्, n. the tree<BR>Xylocarpus Granatum.<BR>—नाग-दाशक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a prince.<BR>—नाग-देण्टिका, f. the betel plant.<BR>—नाग-देव, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नाग-<BR>द्रु, उस्, m. a species of Euphorbia used in offerings<BR>to the snake-goddess Manasā (= समन्त-दुग्ध).<BR>—नाग-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of a Dvīpa in Jambū-<BR>khaṇḍa or Bhārata-varṣa.<BR>—नाग-नक्षत्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the three asterisms forming the Nāga-<BR>vīthi (?).<BR>—नाग-नाथ, अस्, m. the king of the ser-<BR>pents, a serpent-chief; (अम्), n., N. of a Liṅga sacred<BR>to Śiva; (also called नागनाथेश-लिङ्ग.)<BR>—नाग-<BR>नाभ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नाग-नामक, अम्,<BR>n. tin.<BR>—नाग-नामन्, आ, m. holy basil (= तुलसी).<BR>—नाग-नायक, अस्, m. the leader or chief of the<BR>Nāgas or snakes.<BR>—नाग-नासा, f. the trunk or pro-<BR>boscis of an elephant.<BR>—नागनासोरू (˚सा-ऊरू), ऊस्,<BR>f. a woman whose thighs taper like the trunk of an<BR>elephant; [cf. करभोरू, p. 205, col. 2.]<BR>—नाग-<BR>निर्यूह, अस्, m. = निर्यूह and नाग-दन्त, a<BR>large pin or bracket projecting from a wall like a<BR>shelf.<BR>—नाग-पञ्चमी, f. a particular festival, the<BR>fifth day in the light half of month Śrāvaṇa;<BR>the fifth day in the dark half of month Āṣāḍhā.<BR>—नाग-पति, इस्, m. a serpent-chief.<BR>—नाग-पत्-<BR>त्रा, f. = नाग-दमनी.<BR>—नाग-पत्त्री, f. a species<BR>of plant (= लक्ष्मणा).<BR>—नाग-पद, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of coitus.<BR>—नाग-पर्णी, f. the betel plant.<BR>—नाग-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a man; a prince of<BR>Sāśikya.<BR>—नाग-पाश, अस्, m. a sort of magical noose<BR>or lasso used in battle to entangle an enemy; ‘the<BR>serpent-noose,’ an epithet of the weapon of Varuṇa,<BR>regent of the waters; a kind of coitus.<BR>—नाग-<BR>पाशक, अस्, m. a kind of coitus.<BR>—नाग-पुर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘elephant's town,’ ancient Delhi (= गज-<BR>पुर, हास्तिन-पुर).<BR>—नाग-पुष्प, अस्, m.<BR>several plants, = Rottlera Tinctoria (= पुन्-नाग);<BR>Mesua Roxburghii (= नाग-केसर); Michelia<BR>Champaka (= चम्पक); (अम्), n. the blossom of<BR>this plant; (ई), f. = नाग-दमनी.<BR>—नागपुष्प-<BR>फला, f. the plant Benincasa Cerifera (= कुष्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-b" target="_blank">Page0475-b+ 81</a>]<BR>माण्डी).<BR>—नाग-पुष्पिका, f. yellow jasmine (=<BR>स्वर्ण-यूथी).<BR>—नाग-फल, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Trichosanthes Diœca; (आ), f. a various reading for<BR>नाग-बला.<BR>—नाग-बधू, ऊस्, f. a female ele-<BR>phant.<BR>—नाग-बन्धक, अस्, m. an elephant-<BR>catcher.<BR>—नाग-बन्धु, उस्, m. ‘elephant-friend,<BR>liked by elephants,’ the holy fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa<BR>(= अश्वत्थ).<BR>—नाग-बल, अस्, m. ‘having the<BR>strength of an elephant,’ an epithet of Bhīma; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Uraria Lagopodioides; (अम्), n. a par-<BR>ticular high number.<BR>—नाग-बुद्ध, अस्, m. or<BR>नाग-बोधि, इस्, m., N. of a Buddhist teacher.<BR>—नाग-बुद्धि, इस्, m., N. of a medical author.<BR>—नाग-बोध, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नाग-<BR>भगिनी, f. ‘serpent's sister,’ N. of the goddess Manasā;<BR>[cf. नाग-मातृ.]<BR>—नाग-भिद्, त्, m. ‘elephant-<BR>destroyer,’ a species of snake, Amphisbæna; (also<BR>written नाग-भृत्, = डुण्डु.)<BR>—नाग-भूषण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘decorated with serpents,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva; [cf. नाग-चूड.]<BR>—नाग-भोग, अस्, m. a<BR>species of serpent.<BR>—नाग-मण्डलिक, अस्, m. a<BR>snake-keeper; a snake-catcher.<BR>—नाग-मती, f. the<BR>plant Ocimum Sanctum.<BR>—नाग-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of or in elephants.<BR>—नाग-मल्ल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘an athlete among the elephants,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra's elephant Airāvata.<BR>—नाग-मातृ, ता, f.<BR>‘mother of serpent-demons,’ an epithet of Su-rasā; an<BR>epithet of the goddess Manasā (supposed to preside<BR>over snakes); red arsenic.<BR>—नाग-मार, अस्, m. a<BR>species of pot-herb, also Keśa-rāja.<BR>—नाग-मुद्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist Sthavira (= नाग-सेन).<BR>—नाग-यष्टि, इस्, f. or नाग-यष्टिका, f. a gradu-<BR>ated pole or post for showing the depth of water in<BR>a newly dug pond, a boring-rod or stick driven into<BR>the earth.<BR>—नाग-रक्त, अम्, n. red lead.<BR>—नाग-<BR>रङ्ग, अस्, m. the orange, (usually applied to the<BR>Silhet orange, Citrus Aurantium.)<BR>—नाग-रट्ट, अस्,<BR>m. a various reading for नाग-वट्ट, q. v.<BR>—नाग-<BR>राज्, ट्, m. a serpent-king, a chief of the Nāgas.<BR>—नाग-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of the serpents,’ an epithet<BR>of Ananta or of Vāsuki, chief of the serpents; a king<BR>among the elephants, a large elephant.<BR>—नागराज-<BR>कर, अस्, m. the trunk of the king of elephants.<BR>—नाग-राजन्, आ, m. a serpent-king.<BR>—नाग-रुक,<BR>अस्, m. = नाग-रङ्ग, the orange-tree.<BR>—नाग-रेणु,<BR>उस्, m. red lead.<BR>—नाग-लता, f. the penis; N. of a<BR>woman.<BR>—नाग-लेखा, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—नाग-<BR>लोक, अस्, m. the Nāga world or one of the regions<BR>below the earth, otherwise called Pātāla, the world of<BR>the serpent-demons, the abode of serpents or the<BR>race of serpents collectively.<BR>—नाग-वट्ट, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man; [cf. नाग-रट्ट.]<BR>—नाग-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, consisting of snakes; possessed of elephants.<BR>—ना-<BR>ग-वधू, see नाग-बधू.<BR>—नाग-वन, अम्, n.<BR>‘serpent-wood,’ N. of a place.<BR>—नाग-वर्त्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—नाग-वल्लरी or नाग-<BR>वल्लि, इस्, ई, or नाग-वल्लिका, f. Piper Betel, the<BR>betel plant.<BR>—नाग-वारिक, अस्, m. a royal elephant;<BR>an elephant-driver or keeper; a peacock; an epithet<BR>of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu; the chief person in a<BR>court or assembly.<BR>—नाग-वास, अस्, m. ‘abode of<BR>snakes,’ N. of a lake supposed to have been formed<BR>originally by the valley of Nepal.<BR>—नाग-वीथी, f. a<BR>row of serpents; the serpents' path, that part of the<BR>moon's path which contains the asterisms Svāti or<BR>(according to others) Aśvinī, Bharaṇī, and Kṛttikā;<BR>N. of a daughter of Yāmī who was the daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and wife of Dharma; of a daughter of Kaś-<BR>yapa by Yāminī.<BR>—नाग-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a species<BR>of tree.<BR>—नाग-शत, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—नाग-श्री, ईस्, f., N. of a queen.<BR>—नाग-सम्-<BR>भव, अम्, n. minium or red lead.<BR>—नाग-सम्-<BR>भूत, ‘produced from serpents,’ epithet of a sort of<BR>pearl.<BR>—नाग-साह्वय, अस्, आ, अम्, called after<BR>elephants, (generally with नगर = ‘elephant's town,’<BR>i. e. Hāstina-pura.)<BR>—नाग-सुगन्धा, f. the ich-<BR>neumon plant (= सु-गन्धा, सर्प-सुगन्धा,<BR>भुजङ्गाक्षी; cf. नाकुली).<BR>—नाग-सेन, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Buddhist Sthavira; a king of Āryāvarta and<BR>contemporary of Samudra-gupta.<BR>—नाग-स्तोकक,<BR>अम्, n. a species of poisonous plant.<BR>—नाग-स्थल,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">Page0475-c+ 79</a>]<BR>N. of a village near Mathurā.<BR>—नाग-स्फोता or<BR>rather नाग-स्फोटा, f. two plants (= दन्ती and नाग-<BR>दन्ती).<BR>—नाग-स्वरूपिणी, f. a kind of metre con-<BR>sisting of four lines of eight syllables each.<BR>—नाग-<BR>हनु, उस्, m. a kind of perfume (= नख).<BR>—नाग-<BR>हन्त्री, f. a species of plant (= बन्ध्या-कर्को-<BR>टकी; cf. नागाराति).<BR>—नाग-ह्रद, अम्, n. a<BR>lake inhabited by snakes or serpent-demons.<BR>—ना-<BR>गाख्य (˚ग-आख्˚), अस्, m. = नाग-केसर, Mesua<BR>Roxburghii.<BR>—नागाङ्ग, अम्, n. Hāstina-pura.<BR>—ना-<BR>गाङ्गना (˚ग-अङ्˚), f. a female elephant; the pro-<BR>boscis of an elephant; [cf. नागाञ्जना.]<BR>—नागाञ्-<BR>चला (˚ग-अञ्˚), f. = नाग-यष्टि, q. v.<BR>—नागाञ्-<BR>जना, f. the female of an elephant (= नाग-यष्टि,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—नागाधिप (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘the ser-<BR>pent-prince,’ an epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>—नागाधिपति<BR>(˚ग-अध्˚), इस्, m. ‘serpent-chief,’ an epithet of<BR>Virūḍhaka.<BR>—नागाधिराज (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>king or chief of the elephants.<BR>—नागानन्द<BR>(˚ग-आन्˚), अस् or अम्, m. n. (?), or नागानन्द-ना-<BR>टक, अम्, n., N. of a play ascribed to king Harṣa.<BR>—नागान्तक (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘destroyer of<BR>serpents,’ an epithet of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu.<BR>—नागाभिभु, उस्, or -भू (˚ग-अभ्˚), ऊस्, m., N.<BR>of a Buddha.<BR>—नागाराति (˚ग-अर्˚), इस्, m. a species<BR>of plant (= बन्ध्या-कर्कोटकी; cf. नाग-हन्त्री).<BR>—नागारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of serpents,’<BR>epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—नागारूढ (˚ग-आर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, mounted or riding upon an elephant.<BR>—नागार्-<BR>जुन (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of an ancient Buddhist<BR>teacher of the rank of a Bodhi-sattva, said to be<BR>the author of the Yoga-ratna-mālā or Āścarya-ratna-<BR>mālā; (ई), f., N. of a rock-cavern.<BR>—नागालाबु<BR>(˚ग-अल्˚), उस्, f. a species of gourd (= कुम्भ-<BR>तुम्बि).<BR>—नागाशन (˚ग-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘snake-<BR>eater,’ a peacock; an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—ना-<BR>गाह्व (˚ग-आह्˚), अम्, n. ‘the town called after<BR>elephants,’ Hāstina-pura; (आ), f. a species of bulbous<BR>plant (= लक्ष्मणा; cf. नाग-पत्त्री).<BR>—नागाह्-<BR>वय (˚ग-आह्˚), अस्, m. a species of plant; an epithet<BR>of Tathāgata-bhadra.<BR>—नागेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a serpent-prince, serpent-chief; (ई), f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—नागेश (˚ग-ईश), अस्, m., N. of a prince;<BR>an epithet of Patañjali; नागेश or नागेश-भट्ट,<BR>N. of a grammarian, see नागोजी; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>Liṅga in Dārukā-vana.<BR>—नागेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man; (ई), f., N. of the deity Manasā;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—नागेश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of several sacred bathing-places.<BR>—नागोदर<BR>(˚ग-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a medical author; (अम्),<BR>n. a medical term for a peculiar disease of preg-<BR>nancy, dissolution of the fetus in the womb; a<BR>breast-plate, a cuirass.<BR>—नागोद्भेद (˚ग-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a sacred spot where the river Saras-vatī<BR>re-appears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0474-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागक
नागक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागिन्
नागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having serpents, covered with<BR>or surrounded by serpents; snaky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोद|नागोदं
नागोद, अम्, n. armour for the front of the body;<BR>[cf. नागोदर above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपैय
नागपैय नागपैय, अस्, m., N. of a poet<BR>mentioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागम्मा
नागम्मा नागम्मा, f., N. of a female poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर नागर, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. नगर), town-<BR>born, town-bred, city, citizen; relating or belonging to<BR>a town, civic; spoken in a town or city; polite, civil;<BR>clever, sharp, knowing; bad, vile; nameless; (अस्), m. a<BR>citizen; = पौर, a term for a prince engaged in war<BR>under certain circumstances and (in astrology) applied<BR>to a planet in a state of opposition to other planets; a<BR>husband's brother; an orange; a lecturer; denial of<BR>knowledge; hardship, toil, fatigue; desire of final<BR>beatitude; (ई), f. the Nāgarī or Deva-nāgarī (q. v.)<BR>character in which Sanskrit is commonly written; a<BR>species of Euphorbia (= स्नुही); a clever or crafty<BR>or intriguing woman; (अम्), n. dry ginger; the root<BR>of Cyperus Pertenuis; a sort of coitus.<BR>—नागर-<BR>खण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a section of the Skanda-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—नागर-घन, अस्, m. or नागर-मुस्ता,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">Page0476-a+ 74</a>]<BR>f. a species of grass, Cyperus.<BR>—नागराह्व (˚र-<BR>आह्˚), अम्, n. dry ginger.<BR>—नागरोत्था (˚र-उत्˚),<BR>f. = नागर-मुस्ता, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0475-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक, अस्, ई, अम्, living in a town, (op-<BR>posed to आरण्यक); clever, cunning; (अस्), m. a<BR>citizen; the chief of the police or of a town; an<BR>artist; a thief, (a various reading for नागरिक);<BR>(अम्), n. dry ginger; [cf. नागर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरिक
नागरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, town-born, town-bred;<BR>living in or inhabiting a town; produced from a<BR>town; polite; clever, cunning; (अस्), m. a citizen,<BR>the chief of a town, superintendant of police; (अम्),<BR>n. the toll raised from a town.<BR>—नागरिक-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—नागरिक-बल, अम्, n.<BR>the guard of a police-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेयक|नागरेयकः
नागरेयक, अस्, ई, अम्, city, citizen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर्य|नागर्यं|नागर्य्य
नागर्य, अम्, n. town-life, shrewdness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरमर्दि
नागरमर्दि नागरमर्दि, इस्, m. (fr. नगर-<BR>मर्दिन्), a patronymic from Nagara-mardin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरीट|नागरीटः
नागरीट नागरीट, अस्, m. a libertine, rake,<BR>blackguard; (probably for नागवीट below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीट|नागवीटः
नागवीट, अस्, m. a rake; intriguer, match-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागशुण्डी
नागशुण्डी नागशुण्डी, f. a species of gourd;<BR>(also read नामशुण्डी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागुली
नागुली नागुली, f., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोजी
नागोजी नागोजी or नागोजि or नागोजि-भट्ट,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a modern grammarian, also called<BR>नागेश-भट्ट, author of a Vivaraṇa or interpreta-<BR>tion of Kaiyaṭa's commentary on Patañjali, of a<BR>grammar called Paribhāṣendu-śekhara, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग्नजित
नाग्नजित नाग्नजित, अस्, m. (fr. नग्न-जित्),<BR>a descendant of Nagna-jit; (ई), f., N. of one of the<BR>wives of Kṛṣṇa; (wrongly spelt नग्नजिती.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिक
नाचिक नाचिक, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिकेत|नाचिकेतः
नाचिकेत नाचिकेत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. न-चिकेत,<BR>q. v.), relating to Na-ciketa or Na-ciketas; (अस्), m.<BR>a synonym of fire, (wrongly written नाचिकेतु); N.<BR>of an ancient sage, son of Uddālaki; [cf. न-चिकेत,<BR>त्रि-णाचिकेत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचीन
नाचीन नाचीन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाज्जक
नाज्जक नाज्जक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट|नाटः
नाट नाट, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. नट्),<BR>dancing, acting, a dance; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga-<BR>rāja; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people, = कर्णाटक,<BR>the Carnatic; (ई), f., scil. भाषा, the language<BR>spoken by the Nāṭas.<BR>—नाटाम्र (˚ट-अम्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the water-melon, Cucurbita Citrullus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटक|नाटकं|नाटकः
नाटक, अस्, ई, अम्, dancing, acting; (अम्), n. a<BR>play, drama; the first of the ten pieces of dramatic<BR>compositions of the first order; (अस्), m. an actor,<BR>dancer, mime; N. of a mountain in Kāmākhyā;<BR>(इका), f. a kind of play, see below; (अकी), f. the<BR>court of Indra.<BR>—नाटक-प्रपञ्च, अस्, m. course<BR>or arrangement of a drama.<BR>—नाटक-रत्न-कोष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘treasure of jewels of plays,’ N. of a work.<BR>—नाटक-विधि, इस्, m. mimic art, dramatic action.<BR>—नाटकावतार (˚क-अव्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकीय
नाटकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, dramatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकेय
नाटकेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटार|नाटारः
नाटार, अस्, m. (fr. नटी), the son of an actress;<BR>[cf. नाटेर, नाटेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटिका
नाटिका, f. a short or light comedy, the first of the<BR>Upa-rūpakas or dramas of the second order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटितक|नाटितकं
नाटितक, अम्, n. a mimic representation, a gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेय|नाटेयः
नाटेय, अस्, m. the son of an actress or dancing-<BR>girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेर|नाटेरः
नाटेर, अस्, m. = नाटेय; [cf. नाटार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्य|नाट्यं|नाट्यः
नाट्य, अम्, n. dancing, mimic or dramatic repre-<BR>sentation, a play; action on the stage, the science or<BR>art of dancing or acting, scenic art, the union of song,<BR>pantomime dance and instrumental music; the cos-<BR>tume of an actor; (अस्), m. an actor, mime.<BR>—नाट्य-<BR>दर्पण, अम्, n. ‘mirror of acting,’ N. of a work.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">Page0476-b+ 78</a>]<BR>—नाट्य-धर्मिका or नाट्य-धर्मी, f. the rules<BR>of dramatic representation.<BR>—नाट्य-प्रिय, अस्, m.<BR>‘fond of dancing,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—नाट्य-<BR>लोचन-कार, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Nāma-liṅgānuśāsana by Amara-siṃha.<BR>—नाट्य-शाला,<BR>f. a room or building for dramatic exhibitions, a<BR>theatre, a dancing-room, (according to some it should<BR>be built near the gate of a palace.)<BR>—नाट्य-शास्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. any book on dancing or dramatic repre-<BR>sentation.<BR>—नाट्याचार्य (˚य-आच्˚), अस्, m. a danc-<BR>ing-master.<BR>—नाट्योक्ति (˚य-उक्˚), इस्, f. dramatic<BR>phraseology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाड
नाड नाड, अम्, n. = नाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडपित्
नाडपित् नाडपित्, Ved., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडायन
नाडायन नाडायन, अस्, m. (fr. नड), a<BR>patronymic from Naḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडायनक
नाडायनक, relating to Nāḍāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडि|नाडिः
नाडि नाडि, इस्, or नाडी, f. (fr. नड, q. v.),<BR>the tubular stalk or culm of any plant; the hollow<BR>stalk of a lotus, &c.; any tubular organ of the body<BR>(as an artery, vein, intestine, &c.); any pipe or tube,<BR>a flute; a fistulous sore, fistula, sinus [cf. नाडी-<BR>व्रण]; the pulse either at the hand or feet, &c.;<BR>a measure of time = (1/60) of a sidereal day or (1/2) Mu-<BR>hūrta; a period or hour of twenty-four minutes; the<BR>box of a wheel (Ved.); a sort of bent grass; a juggling<BR>trick, deception.<BR>—नाडि-चीर, अम्, n. a small reed<BR>or tube round which the woof is wound, (it is then<BR>used as a shuttle.)<BR>—नाडिन्-धम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing movement of the intestines (as fright), terri-<BR>fying; (अस्), m. a goldsmith; (also read नाडीन्-<BR>धम.)<BR>—नाडिन्-धय, अस्, ई, अम्, drinking or<BR>sucking through a tube.<BR>—नाडि-पत्त्र, अम्, n. an<BR>esculent root, Arum Colocasia.<BR>—नाडि-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. the celestial equator.<BR>—नाडी-कलापक, अस्,<BR>m. a species of plant (= गण्डिनी in Hindī).<BR>—नाडी-<BR>चरण, अस्, m. ‘whose feet or legs are like stalks,’<BR>a bird.<BR>—नाडी-जङ्घ, अस्, m. ‘having stalk-like<BR>legs,’ a crow; N. of a fabulous crane; N. of a holy<BR>teacher or saint; [cf. नालि-जङ्घ.]<BR>—नाडी-त-<BR>रङ्ग, अस्, m. = काकोल; a sort of poison; an astro-<BR>loger; a ravisher, debaucher (= रत-हिण्डक; cf.<BR>नारी-तरङ्गक).<BR>—नाडी-तिक्त, अस्, m. a species<BR>of Nimba growing in Nepal (= नेपाल-निम्ब).<BR>—नाडी-दत्त, अस्, m. = नाडिका-दत्त, q. v.<BR>—ना-<BR>डी-देह, अस्, m. ‘thin-bodied like a tube or stalk,’<BR>N. of one of the attendants of Śiva (= भृङ्गिन्;<BR>cf. नाडी-विग्रह).<BR>—नाडी-नक्षत्र, अम्, n. the<BR>planet of a person's nativity (= जन्म-नक्षत्र).<BR>—नाडीन्-धम = नाडिन्-धम, q. v.<BR>—नाडी-<BR>परीक्षा, f. feeling the pulse; N. of a medical work.<BR>—नाडी-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a pharmaceutical<BR>work commented on by Śaṅkara-sena.<BR>—नाडी-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, abounding with blood-vessels.<BR>—नाडी-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. any tubular instrument.<BR>—नाडी-<BR>विग्रह, अस्, m., N. of Bhṛṅgin, one of Śiva's chief<BR>attendants; [cf. नाडी-देह.]<BR>—नाडी-व्रण, अस्,<BR>m. an ulcer, a fistula, fistulous sore, sinus.<BR>—नाडी-<BR>शाक, अस्, m. a species of vegetable (= नाडीक).<BR>—नाडी-शुद्धि, इस्, f., N. of a Yoga work.<BR>—नाडी-<BR>सङ्ख्या, f., N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नाडी-सञ्चार, अस्, m., N. of the forty-second<BR>chapter of the Jñāna-khaṇḍa of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नाडी-स्नेह, अस्, m. a N. of Bhṛṅgin; see नाडी-<BR>विग्रह.<BR>—नाडी-हिङ्गु, उ, n. = हिङ्गु-नाडिका, the<BR>resin of the plant Gardenia Gummifera?; (उस्), m.<BR>a plant (= वंश-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिक|नाडिकं
नाडिक, अम्, n. the plant Ocimum Sanctum (=<BR>काल-शाक); (आ), f. a hollow stalk or stalk in<BR>general; any tubular organ of the body (as an artery,<BR>vein, intestine, &c.); a fistulous sore; a ray of the<BR>sun (supposed to be hollow); an Indian hour or twenty-<BR>four minutes = (1/60) of a sidereal day = (1/2) Muhūrta; a<BR>measure of length = (1/2) Daṇḍa, (also read नारिका);<BR>a piece of metal on which the hours are struck, an<BR>Indian clock, a gong.<BR>—नाडिका-दत्त, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author mentioned in the Saṃskāra-tattva by<BR>Raghu-nandana; [cf. नाडी-दत्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीक|नाडीकः
नाडीक, अस्, m. a species of pot-herb (= com-<BR>monly पाट्शाक्); Corchorus Olitorius; (आ), f. the<BR>wind-pipe or throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिकेल|नाडिकेलः
नाडिकेल नाडिकेल or नाडीकेल, अस्, m. =<BR>नारिकेल, the cocoa-nut palm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीच|नाडीचः
नाडीच नाडीच, अस्, m. an esculent root,<BR>Colocasia Antiquorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाड्वलेय
नाड्वलेय नाड्वलेय, अस्, m. a metronymic<BR>from Naḍvalā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणक|नाणकं
नाणक नाणक, अम्, n. a coin or anything<BR>stamped with an impression.<BR>—नाणक-परीक्षा, f.<BR>‘the testing of coin,’ assaying.<BR>—नाणक-परीक्षिन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘coin-tester,’ an assayer, assay-master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिचिर
नातिचिर नाति-चिर, अस्, आ, अम्, not very<BR>long (in time), of no long duration; (आत् or ए), ind.<BR>in no very long time, soon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिदूर
नातिदूर नाति-दूर (न-अति-द्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not very distant; (ए), ind. not far from (with abl. or<BR>gen.); (अम्), ind. not very far, no great distance,<BR>not far away.<BR>—नातिदूर-निरीक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, not<BR>seeing very far, not far-sighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिभिन्न
नातिभिन्न नाति-भिन्न (न-अति-भ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, not very different from (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिवाद|नातिवादः
नातिवाद नातिवाद (न-अत्˚), अस्, m. avoid-<BR>ing opprobrious or abusive language, abstaining from<BR>reproof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नात्र|नात्रं|नात्रः
नात्र नात्र, अम्, n. (for नान्त्र), praise,<BR>eulogium; surprise, wonder; (अस्), m. Śiva; a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ्
नाथ् नाथ् (allied to rt. नाध् and gene-<BR>rally identified with it), cl. 1. P. नाथति,<BR>ननाथ, नाथिता, नाथिष्यति, अनाथीत्, नाथितुम्,<BR>to ask, solicit, beg for anything (with dat. or gen. of<BR>the object or with two acc.); to have power; to be<BR>master; to harass, destroy (?); to be sick or ill (?);<BR>(in the Veda only the part. नाथित and नाध-<BR>मान fr. नाध् appear to occur); [cf. rt. नाध्;<BR>Old Germ. nōt, ‘necessity;’ Mod. Germ. noth;<BR>Angl. Sax. nead, neod = Eng. need; Goth. nauth-<BR>yan, ‘to force.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ, अम्, n. refuge, help; (अस्), m. a protector,<BR>patron, master, leader, ruler, lord, (often at the end<BR>of a comp., see जीवित-न्˚, पर्जन्य-न्˚, कु-न्˚; and<BR>often used at the end of names of gods and men,<BR>see गोविन्द-न्˚, जगन्-न्˚, त्रैलोक्य-न्˚); a hus-<BR>band [cf. अ-न्˚]; a possessor [cf. स-नाथ, possessed<BR>of]; a rope passed through the nose of a draft ox<BR>[cf. नाथ-हरि]; N. of an author; [cf. अ-न्˚, कु-<BR>न्˚, गोविन्द-न्˚.]<BR>—नाथ-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>seeking for help or protection, seeking a refuge.<BR>—नाथ-कुमार, अस्, m., N. of a poet mentioned<BR>in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR>—नाथ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the office or dignity of a protector or patron, pro-<BR>tectorship, patronage.<BR>—नाथ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having a patron or protector, having a master, de-<BR>pendant, subservient, subject; (अती), f. having a<BR>husband.<BR>—नाथ-विद्, त्, त्, त्, or नाथ-विन्दु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. possessing or granting protection.<BR>—ना-<BR>थ-हरि, इस्, इस्, इ, carrying a master, any animal<BR>bridled by the nose.<BR>—नाथ-हार, अस्, ई, अम्, taking<BR>or carrying a master, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथमान
नाथमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. seeking help.<BR>asking, begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथाय
नाथाय, Nom. P. नाथायति, -यितुम्, to be-<BR>come a protector or patron, to grant a request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथित
नाथित, अस्, आ, अम्, one who needs help, needy,<BR>oppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथिन्
नाथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a protector or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद|नादः
नाद नाद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. नद्), a loud<BR>sound, cry, sounding, roaring, bellowing, crying, a<BR>sound or tone in general, (sometimes at the end of<BR>an adj. comp., e. g. दारुण-नाद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>sounding dreadfully); (in the Yoga) the nasal sound<BR>represented by a semicircle and used as an abbre-<BR>viation or hieroglyphic in mystical words; one who<BR>praises.<BR>—नाद-ता, f. the quality of sounding.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">Page0477-a+ 73</a>]<BR>—नाद-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa treating<BR>of musical sounds.<BR>—नाद-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pro-<BR>nounced with sound (as letters), sonant.<BR>—नाद-<BR>विन्दूपनिषद् (˚दु-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upa-<BR>niṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0476-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादि
नादि, इस्, इस्, इ, sounding, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिन्
नादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who or what sounds, sounding,<BR>resonant, sounding aloud, pronounced with sound (as<BR>a letter); roaring, bellowing, braying, (often at the<BR>end of a comp.; cf. खर-न्˚, गर्दभ-न्˚); (ई),<BR>m., N. of a Dānava; of a Brāhman metamorphosed<BR>into an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादर|नादरः
नादर नादर (न-आद्˚), अस्, m. disrespect,<BR>disregard, inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिक
नादिक नादिक, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिग
नादिग नादिग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय 1. नादेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नदी), com-<BR>ing from or belonging to a river, river-born, fluvial,<BR>fluviatic, aquatic, marine; (अस्), m. the reed Saccha-<BR>rum Spontaneum (= काश); Calamus Rotang (=<BR>वानीर); (ई), f. several plants, a species of reed<BR>growing usually near water, Calamus Fasciculatus (=<BR>अम्बु-वेतस, = जल-वानीर); the orange-tree (=<BR>भूमि-जम्बूक, भूमि-जम्बू, or भू-जम्बू);<BR>Sesbania Ægyptiaca (= जया); the China rose (=<BR>जपा, जवा, = व्यङ्गुष्ठ, = अग्नि-मन्थ, का-<BR>क-जम्बू); (अम्), n. rock-salt (= सैन्धव);<BR>antimony (= सौवीराञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद्य
नाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from a river, fluvial,<BR>river-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय 2. नादेय (for न आदेय), not to be<BR>taken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाध्
नाध् नाध् (= नाथ्, q. v.), cl. 1. A. ना-<BR>धते, ननाधे, नाधिष्यते, नाधि-<BR>तुम्, to ask, beg for, crave, &c. See rt. नाथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाधमान
नाधमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. seeking help,<BR>asking, begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाधस्
नाधस्, अस्, n. (probably = नाथ), Ved. refuge,<BR>help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान
नान नान, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानद
नानद नानद, अम्, n. (fr. rt. नद्), N. of a<BR>Sāman; [cf. नानन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानन्द
नानन्द नानन्द, अम्, n. (fr. rt. नन्द्), scil.<BR>इन्द्रस्य, N. of a Sāman; [cf. नानद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानर्दमान
नानर्दमान नानर्दमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the<BR>Intens. of rt. नर्द्), sounding loudly, roaring lustily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाना
नाना नाना, ind. (probably a reduplication<BR>of the negative particle न or of the pronominal<BR>affix न in अ-न &c.), in different or various ways,<BR>in different places, manifoldly, differently, variously;<BR>distinctly, separately; (when used as an adj. at the<BR>beginning of a comp. = ) of different kinds, of dif-<BR>ferent classes, various, sundry, different, manifold,<BR>diverse; (according to Pāṇ. II. 3, 32) = विना, without<BR>(with gen., abl., inst.).<BR>—नाना-कन्द, अस्, m. a<BR>species of bulbous plant (= पिण्डालु).<BR>—नानाकार<BR>(˚ना-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of different forms or manifold<BR>kinds, multiform, various.<BR>—नाना-कारम्, ind. hav-<BR>ing done variously.<BR>—नाना-ग्रह, अस्, m. taking<BR>separately, (used to explain अव-ग्रह.)<BR>—नाना-<BR>जातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, of various kinds or sorts, belonging<BR>to different classes, &c.<BR>—नानात्म-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>maintaining the Sāṅkhya doctrine that each individual<BR>being has a soul distinct from the universal spirit.<BR>—नानात्यय (˚ना-अत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of different<BR>kinds, manifold.<BR>—नाना-त्व, अम्, n. variety, diver-<BR>sity, difference, manifoldness, (opposed to एक-त्व,<BR>ऐक्य.)<BR>—नाना-दानानि, n. pl. ‘various presents,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—नाना-<BR>देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or coming from<BR>different districts or countries.<BR>—नाना-धर्मन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. having different customs or character-<BR>istics.<BR>—नाना-धातु-शत, अम्, n. a hundred various<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">Page0477-b+ 75</a>]<BR>minerals.<BR>—नानाधातु-समाकीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>filled with various minerals.<BR>—नाना-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ,<BR>Ved. having different intentions.<BR>—नाना-ध्वनि,<BR>इस्, m. a musical instrument of more than one tone.<BR>—नाना-नाम-निरूपण, अम्, n., N. of the tenth<BR>chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—नाना-पक्षि-गणाकीर्ण (˚ण-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>filled with flocks of various birds.<BR>—नानापक्षि-<BR>निषेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, frequented by various birds.<BR>—नाना-पद, अम्, n., Ved. a different or separate<BR>or independent word.<BR>—नानापद-स्थ, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. (an accent) standing on distinct words or on a<BR>separate word (?).<BR>—नाना-प्रभृति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>beginning differently, (opposed to नानोदर्क.)<BR>—नाना-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the great-grandfather<BR>of Raṅga-nātha, a commentator on Kāli-dāsa's Vikra-<BR>morvaśī.<BR>—नाना-मृग-गण, आस्, m. pl. flocks of<BR>various animals.<BR>—नाना-रथम्, ind., Ved. in<BR>many chariots, in various cars.<BR>—नाना-रस, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of different flavours, variously flavoured.<BR>—नाना-<BR>राग, अस्, आ, अम्, variegated, of many colours.<BR>—नाना-रूप, आणि, n. pl. various forms, different<BR>shapes; (अस्, आ, अम्), of different forms or shapes,<BR>of various kinds, multiform, various.<BR>—नानारूप-<BR>ता, f., Ved. multiformity, diversity of form, various-<BR>ness.<BR>—नानार्थ (˚ना-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>different aim or object, containing something else<BR>(as a new sentence or thing); having different mean-<BR>ings (as a word).<BR>—नानार्थ-कोष, अस्, m. a<BR>dictionary which contains words with different mean-<BR>ings.<BR>—नानार्थ-ध्वनि-मञ्जरी, f. ‘a cluster or<BR>nosegay of words with different meanings,’ N. of a<BR>dictionary by an anonymous author.<BR>—नानार्थ-रत्-<BR>न-तिलक, N. of a dictionary, = अनेकार्थ-तिलक.<BR>—नानार्थरत्न-माला, f. ‘necklace of words of<BR>different meanings,’ N. of a glossary.<BR>—नानार्थ-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘collection of words with dif-<BR>ferent meanings,’ N. of a dictionary by Ajaya-pāla.<BR>—नाना-वर्ण, आस्, m. pl. different colours; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), many-coloured, variegated.<BR>—नाना-विध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of various sorts, of sundry kinds, in<BR>various ways, multiform, manifold.<BR>—नाना-वीर्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having different effects, having manifold<BR>efficacy.<BR>—नानावीर्य-ता, f., Ved. the state of having<BR>manifold efficacy.<BR>—नाना-सूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>illuminated by different suns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानानम्
नानानम्, ind., Ved. = नाना, differently, sepa-<BR>rately, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानान्द्र|नानांद्र|नानांद्रः|नानान्द्रः
नानान्द्र नानान्द्र, अस्, m. (fr. ननान्दृ),<BR>a husband's sister's son, a sister-in-law's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानुष्ठेय|नानुष्ठेयं
नानुष्ठेय नानुष्ठेय (न-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not to be performed, improper, unusual, not right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानू
नानू नानू, ऊस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्त|नांत
नान्त नान्त (न-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, = अन्-अन्त,<BR>endless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्तरीयक|नांतरीयक
नान्तरीयक नान्तरीयक (न-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>inseparable, invariably connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्त्र|नांत्र|नांत्रं|नान्त्रं
नान्त्र नान्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. नम्), praise,<BR>eulogy; [cf. नात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्द
नान्द नान्द, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नन्द), relating<BR>to Nanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दन
नान्दन नान्दन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. नन्द् or<BR>नन्दन), Ved. a pleasure-garden, a paradise,<BR>elysium; [cf. नन्दन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दिन्|नांदिन्
नान्दिन् नान्दिन्, ई, m. the speaker of the<BR>benediction before the commencement of a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दी|नांदी
नान्दी नान्दी, f. (fr. rt. नन्द्), joy, satis-<BR>faction; prosperity; eulogium or praise of a deity,<BR>or a prayer recited in benedictory verses at the open-<BR>ing of a religious ceremony or of a drama, (generally<BR>a kind of blessing pronounced as a prologue to a<BR>Nāṭaka or play; cf. नन्दी.)<BR>—नान्दी-कर, अस्,<BR>m. the speaker of the benediction at the opening of<BR>a drama; (also with the vowel ई made short, नान्दि-<BR>कर.)<BR>—नान्दी-निनाद, अस्, m. a shout of joy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">Page0477-c+ 75</a>]<BR>—नान्दी-पट, अस्, m. = नान्दी-मुख, the lid or<BR>cover of a well.<BR>—नान्दी-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>town in the East.<BR>—नान्दीपुरक, अस्, &c., coming<BR>from or relating to the town Nāndī-pura.<BR>—नान्दी-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, (with पितरस् or पितृ-गणस्)<BR>the class of manes of deceased progenitors to whom<BR>the Nāndī-mukha Śrāddha is offered; (अम्), n. (with<BR>or without श्राद्ध) a Śrāddha or commemorative<BR>offering to the manes preliminary to any joyous<BR>occasion, as initiation, marriage, &c., in which nine<BR>balls of meat are offered to the deceased father,<BR>paternal grandfather, and great-grandfather; to the<BR>maternal grandfather, great-grandfather, and great-<BR>great-grandfather; and to the mother, paternal grand-<BR>mother, and paternal great-grandmother; (अस्), m. =<BR>नान्दी-पट, the lid or cover of a well; (ई), f. a female<BR>ancestor sharing in the above Śrāddha; a kind of grain<BR>reckoned among the Ku-dhānyas; a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines of fourteen syllables each;<BR>[cf. नन्दी-मुख.]<BR>—नान्दी-रव, अस्, m. a cry<BR>of joy.<BR>—नान्दी-वादिन्, ई, m. the speaker of the<BR>prologue or introduction to a drama; a drummer,<BR>one who beats a drum at festivals.<BR>—नान्दी-श्राद्ध,<BR>अम्, n. = नान्दी-मुखं श्राद्धम्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीक|नांदीकः|नान्दीकः
नान्दीक, अस्, m. a post in a door-way set up for<BR>good luck; (also read as du. नान्दीकौ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दुक
नान्दुक नान्दुक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापि
नापि नापि (न-अपि), ind. not even. See न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित|नापितः
नापित नापित, अस्, m. (according to some<BR>a corruption of स्नापितृ, one who bathes), a barber,<BR>a shaver; (ई), f. the wife of a barber; [cf. वप्तृ.]<BR>—नापित-वास्तु, उ, n. a barber's dwelling.<BR>—ना-<BR>पितवास्तुक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or coming<BR>from the dwelling of a barber.<BR>—नापित-शाला or<BR>नापित-शालिका, f. a barber's shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितायनि|नापितायनिः
नापितायनि, इस्, m. the son or offspring of a<BR>barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित्य|नापित्यं|नापित्यः
नापित्य, अस्, m. the son of a barber; (अम्), n.<BR>the trade or business of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्
नाभ् नाभ्, प्, f. (fr. rt. 1. नभ्), Ved.<BR>an opening, aperture, mouth (?); a rent (?); (Sāy.)<BR>destructive, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ
नाभ नाभ. See p. 478, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभक|नाभकः
नाभक नाभक, अस्, m. a myrobalan, Ter-<BR>minalia Chebula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभस
नाभस नाभस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नभस्),<BR>celestial, heavenly, appearing in the sky; (with<BR>योग) N. of certain constellations, (according to<BR>Bhaṭṭotpala there are thirty-two, divided into four<BR>classes, viz. three Āśraya-yogas, two Dala-yogas,<BR>twenty Ākṛti-yogas, and seven Saṅkhyā-yogas.)<BR>—नाभस-योगाध्याय (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of the twelfth chapter of the Bṛhaj-jātaka, an astro-<BR>logical work by Varāha-mihira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभाक
नाभाक नाभाक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नभाक),<BR>belonging to or composed by Nabhāka; (अस्), m. (like<BR>नभाक), Ved., N. of a Ṛṣi of the Kaṇva family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभाग|नाभागः
नाभाग नाभाग, अस्, m. (fr. नभ-ग), N.<BR>of a son of Manu Vaivasvata; a patronymic of Am-<BR>barīṣa [cf. नाभागि]; a son of Manu and father of<BR>Ambarīṣa, &c.; a son of Nabha-ga or Nabhāga and<BR>father of Ambarīṣa; a son of Śruta and father of<BR>Ambarīṣa; of a son of Nediṣṭha or Ariṣṭa or<BR>Diṣṭa and father of Bhalandana; of a son of Yayāti,<BR>grandson of Ambarīṣa, and father of Aja; [cf.<BR>नभाग, नाभा-नेदिष्ठ.]<BR>—नाभाग-दिष्ट,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Manu Vaivasvata; [cf. ना-<BR>भा-नेदिष्ठ, नाभाग, दिष्ट.]<BR>—नाभाग-<BR>धेय, perhaps = नाभाग-भागधेय, one who<BR>has the same lot or destiny as Nābhāga.<BR>—नाभाग-<BR>नेदिष्ठ, अस्, m. and नाभागारिष्ट (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Manu Vaivasvata; [cf. नाभाग,<BR>अरिष्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभागि
नाभागि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Ambarīṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभि|नाभिः
नाभि नाभि, इस्, or नाभी, f. (according to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">Page0478-a+ 80</a>]<BR>lexicographers also m.; probably fr. नभ्, an older<BR>form of rt. 1. नह्, to bind, connect), the navel;<BR>any navel-like cavity; the nave of a wheel (e. g.<BR>त्रि-नाभि चक्रम्, a three-naved wheel, a wheel<BR>with a triple nave or centre, Ṛg-veda I. 164, 2);<BR>the centre, focus, central point, middle, point of<BR>junction or that which holds the parts of anything<BR>together, point of concentration, chief point, chief,<BR>head, (hence नाभिर् नृप-मण्डलस्य in Raghu-v.<BR>XVIII. 19 = the chief of the circle of kings); the<BR>close connection of relations, near relationship, com-<BR>munity of race or family; home; a near relation;<BR>musk (= मृग-नाभि); (इस्), m. a sovereign, a<BR>lord paramount; a chief; a Kṣatriya or Hindū of<BR>the regal and military tribe; N. of a grandson of<BR>Priya-vrata [cf. नाभि-गुप्त, नाभि-वर्ष], son<BR>of Agnīdhra and father of Ṛṣabha; of the father of<BR>Ṛṣabha, first Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; [cf.<BR>नाभ, 2. नभ्य, अन्य-न्˚, घन-न्˚, &c.: cf.<BR>also Gr. ὀμφ-αλό-ς, ὅμφαξ: Lat. umb-il-īcu-s,<BR>umbo: Old Germ. nab-a, ‘nave;’ nabulo, ‘navel:’<BR>Angl. Sax. nafu, nafela: Mod. Germ. nabe, na-<BR>bel: Lett. nabba, ‘navel:’ Lith. namba, ‘navel.’]<BR>—नाभा-नेदिष्ठ, अस्, m. (नाभा loc. sing. for<BR>नाभौ), N. of a son of Manu Vaivasvata and<BR>author of two Ṛg-veda hymns, (Ṛg-veda X. 61,<BR>62.)<BR>—नाभानेदिष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम्, or नाभाने-<BR>धिष्ठीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or composed by<BR>Nābhā-nediṣṭha; (अम्), n., scil. सूक्तम्, N. of a<BR>Vedic hymn.<BR>—नाभि-कण्टक, अस्, m. ruptured or<BR>protruded navel (= commonly गोण्ड).<BR>—नाभि-गु-<BR>डक, अस्, m. a protruding or ruptured navel.<BR>—ना-<BR>भि-गुप्त, अस्, m. (?), ‘protected by Nābhi,’ N. of<BR>a Varṣa in Kuśa-dvīpa, (the king of Kuśa-dvīpa was<BR>Hiraṇya-retas, a son of Priya-vrata, who divided the<BR>seven Varṣas of his Dvīpa among his seven sons;<BR>Nābhi was probably the N. of one of these seven<BR>sons; cf. नाभि-वर्ष.)<BR>—नाभि-गोलक, अस्, m.<BR>a protruding or ruptured navel (= नाभि-गुडक).<BR>—नाभि-च्छेदन, अम्, n. cutting or separating<BR>the umbilical cord.<BR>—नाभि-ज, अस्, m. or नाभि-<BR>जन्मन्, आ, m. an epithet of Brahmā, (this deity<BR>appearing on the lotus which sprang from the navel<BR>of Viṣṇu.)<BR>—नाभि-द्वार, अम्, n. the aperture<BR>of the navel.<BR>—नाभि-नाडी, f. or नाभि-नाला, f. or<BR>नाभि-नाल, अम्, n. the umbilical cord; [cf. गर्-<BR>भ-नाडी.]<BR>—नाभि-भू, ऊस्, m. ‘born from the<BR>navel,’ an epithet of Brahmā; [cf. नाभि-ज.]<BR>—ना-<BR>भि-मूल, अम्, n. the part of the body immediately<BR>under the navel.<BR>—नाभि-वर्धन, अम्, n. division<BR>of the umbilical cord; rupture of the navel, umbilical<BR>hernia; corpulency.<BR>—नाभि-वर्ष, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>the Varṣa governed by Nābhi, son of Āgnīdhra (=<BR>भारत-वर्ष).<BR>—नाभ्य्-आवर्त, अस्, m. the cavity<BR>of the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0477-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ
नाभ (substituted for नाभि at the end of an<BR>adj. comp.), the navel (e. g. अब्ज-नाभ, अस्, m.<BR>‘lotus-naveled,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu; cf. उन्-न्˚,<BR>ऊर्ण-न्˚, कञ्ज-न्˚, काल-न्˚); the nave of a<BR>wheel; the centre or central point of anything;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; N. of a son of Śruta<BR>and father of Sindhu-dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिक
नाभिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR>= नाभि (e. g. षण्-णाभिक, having six naves);<BR>(आ), f. a cavity shaped like a navel; a species of<BR>plant, Achyranthes Atropurpurea (= कटभी).<BR>—ना-<BR>भिक-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town of the Uttara-<BR>kurus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिल
नाभिल, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or coming from<BR>a navel; [cf. नाभील.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभील|नाभीलं
नाभील, अम्, n. the groin of a woman; a promi-<BR>nent or ruptured navel; the cavity of the navel; pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभेय
नाभेय, अस्, m. a patronymic of Ṛṣabha, first<BR>Arhat of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्य|नाभ्यं|नाभ्यः
नाभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proceeding from the navel,<BR>being in the navel, umbilical, of or relating to<BR>the navel; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; [cf.<BR>नाभ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिजात
नाभिजात नाभिजात (न-अभिजात), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, not well-born, not noble, low-bred, ignoble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिमान
नाभिमान नाभिमान (न-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ab-<BR>sence of pride, humbleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम
नाम नाम, ind. See under नामन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामतिक
नामतिक नामतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नमत),<BR>dressed in woollen cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधेय|नामधेयं
नामधेय नाम-धेय. See under नामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामन्
नामन् नामन्, अ, n. (fr. rt. 1. ज्ञा, the initial<BR>ज् being lost; said to be fr. rt. म्ना), a mark by<BR>which anything is known, sign, token (Ved.); form,<BR>manner, mode, character, personal character, nature,<BR>species (Ved.); name, appellation, (especially a per-<BR>sonal name, as opposed to गोत्र, a family name);<BR>merely the name (as opposed to the reality); (in<BR>grammar) appellative, common name for a class of<BR>objects, noun, word (e. g. मेघ-नामन्, [every]<BR>noun or word denoting cloud); substance, essence,<BR>(in the Mīmāṃsā phil. opposed to गुण, accidental<BR>quality); water (according to Naigh. 1. 11); नाम्ना<BR>वच् or नाम ग्रह्, to address by name, mention or<BR>call upon by name; नाम कृ or नाम दा or<BR>नाम धा or नाम्ना कृ or नाम्ना वि-धा, to give<BR>a name, to name, call (e. g. सावित्रीति नामास्याश्<BR>चक्रुः, they called her name Sāvitrī; लक्ष्मणम्<BR>इति नाम कृतवान्, he named him Lakṣmaṇa;<BR>तां दुःख-लब्धिकां नाम्ना चकार, he called<BR>her Duḥkha-labdhikā). नामन् often occurs at<BR>the end of an adj. comp., in which case the fem. is<BR>generally नाम्नी (e. g. विष्णु-शर्म-नामा पण्-<BR>डितः, a sage named Viṣṇu-śarman; नदी-नाम्नी<BR>कन्या, a girl with the name of a river); but the<BR>fem. may be also नामा from नामन् and नामा<BR>from a base नाम, which is rarely substituted for<BR>नामन् at the end of a comp. (नाम, acc. sing.<BR>used as an adverb =) namely, by name (e. g. मा-<BR>धवो नाम ब्राह्मणः, a Brāhman, Mādhava by<BR>name); indeed, certainly, forsooth, really, of course,<BR>even, probably, possibly, perhaps, agreed, granted,<BR>granting (e. g. अस्तु नाम स धनी मे किञ्चिद्<BR>दधाति, granting [which I doubt] that this rich man<BR>will offer me something). नाम as an emphatic<BR>particle may have some of the above senses, but is<BR>often untranslatable by any single equivalent English<BR>word. It is frequently placed after interrogative<BR>pronouns (e. g. किं नाम, कथं नाम, कदा<BR>नाम, को नाम), when it may be translated by<BR>‘then,’ ‘indeed,’ &c.; अपि नाम at the beginning<BR>of a sentence = perhaps, probably, would that! oh<BR>that! of course; मा नाम = may it not be that,<BR>perhaps, but I hope not; ननु नाम, certainly,<BR>evidently; after an imperative नाम = I care not,<BR>no matter, if you like, &c. According to native<BR>lexicographers नाम implies certainty, possibility,<BR>anger, reproach, consent, promise, recollection, sur-<BR>prise, pretence, &c.; [cf. Zend nāman: Gr. ὄνο-μα(τ),<BR>ἀν-ώνυ-μο-ς, νώνυμν-ο-ς, ὀνομαίνω,<BR>ὀνο-μάζω: Lat. co-gnō-men, i-gnō-min-ia, nō-men,<BR>nōmin-ā-re, nam, quis-nam, quem-nam = Sanskrit<BR>कं नाम, nem-pe = Sanskrit नाम अपि: Umbr.<BR>nume, nome, dat. sing. nomn-e: Goth. namō,<BR>gen. sing. namin-s, namn-yan, ga-namn-yan,<BR>‘to name:’ Mod. Germ. nāmen, nāme: Angl.<BR>Sax. nāma, nemn-an: Eng. name: Slav. i-man,<BR>‘name;’ imen-ova-ti, ‘to name:’ Scot. ainm,<BR>‘name:’ Cambro-Brit. env, ‘name.’]<BR>—नाम-<BR>करण, अस्, m. a nominal affix; (अम्), n. giving<BR>a name, naming a child after birth.<BR>—नाम-कर्-<BR>मन्, अ, n. the ceremony of naming a child after<BR>birth.<BR>—नाम-ग्रह, अस्, m. or नाम-ग्रहण,<BR>अम्, n. or (Ved.) नाम-ग्राह, अस्, m. addressing or<BR>mentioning by name.<BR>—नाम-ग्राहम्, ind., Ved.<BR>by mentioning the name, by naming.<BR>—नाम-तस्,<BR>ind., see col. 3.<BR>—नाम-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नाम-द्वादशी, f. a religious ceremony, wor-<BR>shipping Durgā daily under one of her twelve appel-<BR>lations (Gaurī, Kālī, Umā, Bhadrā, Durgā, Kānti,<BR>Sarasvatī, Maṅgalā, Vaiṣṇavī, Lakṣmī, Śivā, and<BR>Nārāyaṇī).<BR>—नाम-ध, अस्, or नाम-धा, आस्, m.,<BR>Ved. one who gives a name, a name-giver.<BR>—नाम-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">Page0478-c+ 80</a>]<BR>धातु, उस्, m. a verbal base derived from a noun, a<BR>nominal verb.<BR>—नाम-धारक, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing<BR>only the name, being anything only by name (e. g.<BR>पुरुषो नाम-धारकः, one who is a man only<BR>in name).<BR>—नाम-धेय, अम्, n. a name, a title,<BR>an appellation, (sometimes at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. किन्-न्˚, see under किम्; पुन्-न्˚, see under<BR>पुंस्); the ceremony of giving a name to a child.<BR>—नामधेय-करण, अम्, n. giving a name,<BR>naming.<BR>—नामधेय-तस्, ind. by name.<BR>—नाम-<BR>नामिक, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—नाम-नि-<BR>धान, अम्, n. ‘a collection of nouns,’ N. of a<BR>glossary.<BR>—नाम-नियत-प्रवेश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Samādhi.<BR>—नाम-निर्देश, अस्, m. pointing out by<BR>name.<BR>—नाम-पारायण, अम्, n. ‘a complete col-<BR>lection of nouns,’ N. of a glossary.<BR>—नाम-मात्र,<BR>अम्, n. the mere name, a mere name; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>having only the name; (एण), ind. by the mere<BR>name, merely, nominally.<BR>—नाममात्रावशेषित<BR>(˚र-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having only the name left.<BR>—नाम-माला, f. a vocabulary, nomenclature; N. of<BR>a Prākṛt glossary of synonyms.<BR>—नाम-मुद्रा, f.<BR>a seal-ring, signet-ring with a name (engraved on it).<BR>—नाम-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a sacrifice only in name.<BR>—नाम-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘the gender of nouns,’ N.<BR>of a work treating thereof.<BR>—नामलिङ्गानुशासन<BR>(˚ग-अन्˚), अम्, n. the rules of gender or lessons on<BR>the gender of nouns.<BR>—नाम-वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, desti-<BR>tute of name, nameless, stupid.<BR>—नाम-वाचक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, expressing a name; (in grammar) a pro-<BR>per name.<BR>—नाम-विधि, इस्, m. ‘name-rule,’ N. of<BR>the twenty-third chapter of the Jñāna-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नाम-विस्मृति, इस्, f. forgetting the<BR>name (of any one).<BR>—नाम-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing only the name left, deceased, dead; (अस्), m.<BR>name as the only thing left, dying, death; [cf.<BR>आलेख्य-शेष, कीर्त्ति-शेष.]<BR>—नाम-सङ्कीर्तन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘name-glorification,’ N. of the fourteenth<BR>chapter of the Jñāna-khaṇḍa of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नाम-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. a collection of words<BR>(exclusive of verbs).<BR>—नाम-सारोद्धार (˚र-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentary on Hema-candra's<BR>Abhidhāna-cintā-maṇi.<BR>—नामाख्यातिक (˚म-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, relating to nouns and verbs.<BR>—नामाङ्क (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, marked with<BR>a name.<BR>—नामाङ्क-शोभित (˚म-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>adorned with the mark of the name or with name<BR>and cipher.<BR>—नामादेशम् (˚म-आद्˚), ind. by<BR>announcing one's name.<BR>—नामानुशासन (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘the rules about nouns,’ N. of a lexi-<BR>cographical work.<BR>—नामापराध (˚म-अप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. abusing (a respectable person) by name, calling<BR>names.<BR>—नामार्थ-निर्णय (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘inquiry into the bases of nouns,’ N. of a chapter of<BR>the Vaiyākaraṇa-bhūṣaṇa-sāra by Koṇḍa-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—नामावलि (˚म-आव्˚), इस्, f. a list of names<BR>(especially of a god).<BR>—नामाष्टमी-विधान<BR>(˚म-अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of the twenty-fourth chap-<BR>ter of the Jñāna-khaṇḍa of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामक
नामक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.) = नामन्, e. g. कृत-नामक, one to whom<BR>a name has been given, having a name, named;<BR>[cf. अ-न्˚, अञ्जन-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामतस्
नाम-तस्, ind. by name, namely, with the name,<BR>with respect to the name; (in Bhāgavata-Purāṇa<BR>V. 12, 8, used for the abl. c. of नामन्); नामतस्<BR>is sometimes redundantly joined with नाम (e. g.<BR>बाहुको नाम नामतः, namely Bāhuka by name);<BR>नामतः कृ, to give a name, to name, call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामथा
नाम-था, ind., Ved. by name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामिक
नामिक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a name or to<BR>a noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामि|नामिः
नामि नामि, इस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामित
नामित नामित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. नम्),<BR>bent, bent down, bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामिन्
नामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bending; (in grammar) changing<BR>a dental to a cerebral, a N. given to all the vowels<BR>except अ and आ; [cf. भाविन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम्य
नाम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be bent (as a bow &c.),<BR>bendable, pliable, pliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0478-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम्ब
नाम्ब नाम्ब, अस्, m., Ved. a species of<BR>grain, (also read आम्ब); (अस्, ई, अम्), consisting of<BR>Nāmba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाय|नायः
नाय नाय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. नी), a leader,<BR>guide, driver (e. g. in अश्व-न्˚, गो-न्˚); perhaps N.<BR>of a man; = नय, guiding, directing (morally or<BR>physically); policy; means, expedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक, अस्, इका, अम्, guiding, leading, con-<BR>ducting; (अस्), m. a guide, leader, conductor [cf.<BR>कु-न्˚]; a chief, lord, head; pre-eminent, principal;<BR>(with or without सैन्यस्य) a general, a com-<BR>mander; (in erotic or dramatic poetry) the lover or<BR>hero in a drama &c., a husband; the central gem of<BR>a necklace; a paradigm or example (in grammar);<BR>an epithet of Śākya-muni; N. of a Brāhman; (इका),<BR>f. a mistress; a wife; the heroine in a drama &c., a<BR>noble lady; an inferior form or Śakti of Durgā, (of<BR>which there are eight, viz. Ugra-caṇḍā, Pra-caṇḍā,<BR>Caṇḍogrā, Caṇḍa-nāyikā, Ati-caṇḍā, Cāmuṇḍā,<BR>Caṇḍā, and Caṇḍā-vatī; cf. कुल-न्˚.)<BR>—नायक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. leadership, headship, chieftainship.<BR>—नायक-रत्न, अम्, n., N. of a commentary<BR>on Pārtha-sārathi's Nyāya-ratna-mālā by Rāmānuja.<BR>—नायकाधिप (˚क-अध्˚), अस्, m. the chief of<BR>leaders, a king, sovereign, prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायिन्
नायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, leading, conducting; [cf. अयु-<BR>त-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार|नारं|नारः
नार नार, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. नर), proceeding<BR>from men, relating or belonging to men, human,<BR>mortal; spiritual (?); (अस्), m. a man (?); a calf;<BR>(अस् or, according to some, अम्, आ), m. n. f. water,<BR>(probably only a form invented to explain नारा-<BR>यण; cf. नीर, νάω, νηρός, Νηρεύς); (अम्), n. a<BR>multitude or assemblage of men; dry ginger; (ई),<BR>f. a woman, a wife, (in the older language also<BR>with short इ, नारि); a female or any object regarded<BR>as feminine; a kind of metre consisting of four<BR>lines of three long syllables each; N. of a daughter<BR>of Meru; (यस्), f. pl. a sacrifice, oblation (Ved.).<BR>—नार-कीट, अस्, m. a species of worm (= अश्म-<BR>कीट); a deceiver, one who disappoints expectations<BR>excited by himself.<BR>—नार-जीवन, अम्, n. gold.<BR>—नारी-कवच, अस्, m. ‘having women for armour,’<BR>an epithet of Mūlaka, king of the solar line and son<BR>of Aśmaka.<BR>—नारी-तीर्थ, आनि, n. pl. ‘bathing-<BR>places of women,’ N. of five sacred bathing-places.<BR>—नारी-दूषण, अम्, n. a woman's vice, any great<BR>fault in women, (six are usually reckoned, viz.<BR>drinking spirits, keeping bad company, quitting a<BR>husband, rambling abroad, sleeping and dwelling<BR>in a strange house.)<BR>—नारी-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing a woman for possessor or owner (e. g. नारी-<BR>नाथं गृहम्, a house having a woman for its<BR>possessor).<BR>—नारी-परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to<BR>women.<BR>—नारी-प्रसङ्ग, अस्, m. libertinism,<BR>lechery.<BR>—नारी-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of<BR>women.<BR>—नारी-मुख, अस्, m., N. of a people to<BR>the south-east of Madhya-deśa.<BR>—नारी-यान, अम्,<BR>n. a woman's conveyance, a litter, &c.<BR>—नारी-रत्न,<BR>अम्, n. a jewel of a woman, an excellent woman.<BR>—नारी-वाक्य, अम्, n. the word of a wife.<BR>—नारीष्टा (˚री-इष्˚), f. ‘dear to women,’ Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR>—नारी-ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanying<BR>women (?), fond of them (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायण|नारायणः
नारायण, अस्, m. (fr. नर, q. v.; sometimes de-<BR>rived fr. नार + अयन), ‘son of Nara or the original<BR>man,’ patronymic of the personfied Puruṣa or first<BR>living being, author of the Puruṣa hymn; he is often<BR>associated with Nara or the original man, and identified<BR>with Brahmā (in Manu I. 9, 11) and with Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa; in Hari-vaṃśa 4601 Urvaśī is described as<BR>springing from his thigh; elsewhere he is regarded<BR>as a Kāśyapa or Āṅgirasa [cf. महा-न्˚, अर्ध-न्˚];<BR>chief of the Sādhyas; the eighth of the nine black<BR>Vāsu-devas (with Jainas); the Puruṣa hymn, com-<BR>posed by Nārāyaṇa (Ṛg-veda X. 90); N. of the<BR>second month, reckoning from Mārgaśīrṣa; N. of<BR>a son of Ajāmila; of Bhūmi-mitra; of Nara-hari;<BR>N. of several men, authors and commentators; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">Page0479-b+ 79</a>]<BR>mystical N. of the letter आ; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating or<BR>belonging to Nārāyaṇa or Kṛṣṇa, (the warriors in<BR>Kṛṣṇa's army are called Nārāyaṇāḥ in Udyoga-<BR>parva 147); (with क्षेत्र) a term applied to the<BR>ground on the banks of the Ganges for a distance of<BR>four Hastas or cubits from the water; (with तैल)<BR>a sort of oil to which efficacy is ascribed in medicine;<BR>(ई), f. epithet of Lakṣmī, the goddess of prosperity<BR>and wife of Viṣṇu; epithet of Durgā; epithet and<BR>patronymic of Indra-senā, wife of Mudgala; epithet<BR>of the Ganges or of the Gaṇḍakī (?); the plant Aspa-<BR>ragus Racemosus.<BR>—नारायण-कण्ठ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR>—नारायण-कल्प, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—नारायण-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. four cubits on<BR>either side of the Ganges; see above.<BR>—नारायण-<BR>गीता, f., N. of a work containing the principles of the<BR>sect founded by Rāmānanda.<BR>—नारायण-गुप्त, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Gupta prince.<BR>—नारायण-चक्रवर्तिन्,<BR>ई, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR>—नारायण-तार, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author; (also read नारायण-तारा.)<BR>—नारा-<BR>यण-तीर्थ, अस्, m., N. of an author; (अम्), n.,<BR>N. of a bathing-place.<BR>—नारायण-तैल, अम्, n.<BR>an oil expressed from various plants of great reputed<BR>efficacy in many complaints.<BR>—नारायण-दास-<BR>सिद्ध, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नारायण-देव,<BR>अस्, m. the god Nārāyaṇa; N. of an author.<BR>—नारा-<BR>यण-दैव-विद्, त्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नारायण-<BR>पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of a learned man.<BR>—नारायण-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘the friend of Nārāyaṇa,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva; yellow sandal-wood (= पीत-चन्दन).<BR>—नारायण-बलि, इस्, m. ‘an oblation to Nārāyaṇa,’<BR>N. of a peculiar funeral ceremony.<BR>—नारायण-<BR>भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नारायण-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of or in Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—नारायण-वर्मन्, अ, n. ‘armour of Nārā-<BR>yaṇa,’ N. of a poem in praise of Kṛṣṇa, forming<BR>part of the sixth book of the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa.<BR>—नारायण-श्री-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—नारायण-सरस्, अस्, n. Nārāyaṇa's lake.<BR>—नारायण-सरस्वती, ईस्, m., N. of a commen-<BR>tator.<BR>—नारायण-सूरि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नारायणाश्रम (˚ण-आश्˚), अस्, m. Nārāyaṇa's<BR>hermitage; N. of the author of the commentary<BR>Bheda-dhikkāra-satkriyā.<BR>—नारायणास्त्र (˚ण-<BR>अस्˚), अम्, n. ‘weapon of Nārāyaṇa,’ a mystical<BR>weapon.<BR>—नारायणेन्द्र (˚ण-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a commentator.<BR>—नारायणोपनिषद् (˚ण-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f. the Upaniṣad treating of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—नाराय-<BR>णोपाध्याय (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणि
नारायणि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणीय
नारायणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, referring or relating to<BR>Nārāyaṇa, treating of him; (आ), f., scil. उपनिषद्,<BR>N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—नारायणीय-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिक
नारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, watery, aqueous; spiritual;<BR>(नारिका wrong reading for नाडिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीक
नारीक at the end of an adj. comp. = नारी;<BR>(अम्), n. (in the Sāṅkhya phil.) one of the nine<BR>kinds of Tuṣṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारेय
नारेय, अस्, m. (fr. नारी), N. of a son of<BR>Bhaṅga-kāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारक|नारकः
नारक नारक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. नरक), re-<BR>lating to hell, happening in hell, being or abiding<BR>in hell, hellish, infernal, (नारकी निर्वृतिः, the<BR>death suffered in hell); (अस्), m. an inhabitant of<BR>the infernal regions; hell or the infernal regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिक
नारकिक, अस्, ई, अम्, hellish, infernal; (अस्), m.<BR>an inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिन्
नारकिन्, ई, इणी, इ, hellish, infernal, being in<BR>hell, condemned to or deserving hell; (ई), m. an<BR>inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकीय
नारकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, hellish; (अस्), m. an in-<BR>habitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारङ्ग|नारंग|नारङ्गं|नारंगः|नारङ्गः
नारङ्ग नारङ्ग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>नॄ, but probably a corruption of नाग-रङ्ग, q. v.),<BR>the orange-tree; the juice of the pepper plant; a liber-<BR>tine, a catamite; a living being, an animal; a twin,<BR>one of twins; (अम्), n. a carrot, Daucus Carota (= गर्-<BR>जर).<BR>—नारङ्ग-पत्त्रक, अस्, m. yellow carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारद|नारदः
नारद नारद, अस्, m. (etymology uncer-<BR>tain), N. of a Ṛṣi or rather Devarṣi (i. e. Ṛṣi<BR>among the gods) regarded in the Veda as a descendant<BR>of Kaṇva and author of certain hymns of the Ṛg-<BR>veda (VIII. 13, IX. 104, 105), often associated in<BR>the later mythology with Parvata, (he appears on the<BR>earth, like Mercury, as a messenger from the gods to<BR>men or vice versâ, and is reckoned among the ten<BR>Prajā-patis as a son of Brahmā (Manu I. 35), from whose<BR>forehead he is said to have been produced; in the<BR>modern mythology he is a friend of Kṛṣṇa and is<BR>regarded as inventor of the Vīṇā or lute; in epic<BR>poetry he is occasionally called a Deva-gandharva,<BR>‘divine Gandharva,’ or a Gandharva-rājan, ‘king of<BR>the Gandharvas,’ or simply Gandharva); N. of a<BR>son of Viśvā-mitra; of an author; of a mountain;<BR>(आ), f. a species of sugar-cane, = इक्षु-मूल; (अस्,<BR>ई, अम्), relating to Nārada, composed by him, &c.<BR>—नारद-पञ्च-रात्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—नारद-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—नारदपुराण-सूचन, अम्, n., N. of the sixty-<BR>fifth chapter of the Vārāha-Purāṇa.<BR>—नारद-प्र-<BR>करण, अम्, n. ‘Nārada chapter,’ N. of the 129th<BR>chapter of the Kṛṣṇa-khaṇḍa or fourth section of<BR>the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—नारद-वाक्य, अम्,<BR>n. ‘speech of Nārada,’ N. of the sixty-seventh chapter<BR>of the Uttara-kāṇḍa or seventh section of the Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa.<BR>—नारद-संहिता, f., N. of a musical work.<BR>—नारद-सनत्कुमार-वाद, अस्, m. ‘discourse<BR>of Nārada and Sanatkumāra,’ N. of the 103rd chapter<BR>of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—ना-<BR>रद-समागम, अस्, m. ‘arrival of Nārada,’ N. of<BR>the twenty-first chapter of the Uttara-kāṇḍa of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—नारदेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚द-ईश्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—नारदोपदेश<BR>(˚द-उप्˚), अस्, m. ‘the advice of Nārada,’ N. of the<BR>first chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारदिन्
नारदिन्, ई, m., N. of a son of Viśvā-mitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारदीय
नारदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Nārada, com-<BR>posed by Nārada, &c.; (अम्), n. (with or without<BR>पुराण), N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—नारदीय-महा-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR>—नारदीयोपपु-<BR>राण (˚य-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारदीयक
नारदीयक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or proceeding<BR>from Nārada; (अम्), n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारद्वसव
नारद्वसव नारद्वसव (?), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारसिंह|नारसिंहः
नारसिंह नारसिंह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नर-<BR>सिंह), referring or belonging to Viṣṇu in his man-<BR>lion Ava-tāra or incarnation; (अस्), m., N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>of a man; of a town.<BR>—नारसिंह-तन्त्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tantra.<BR>—नारसिंह-पुराण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Purāṇa.<BR>—नारसिंहोपपुराण (˚ह-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराच|नाराचः
नाराच नाराच, अस्, m. an iron arrow, an<BR>arrow in general; a water-elephant (= जलेभ,<BR>अम्बु-हस्तिन्); a bad or cloudy day (?); a species<BR>of the Dhṛti metre, also called Narāca, consisting of<BR>4 times 8 iambics; (नाराची or नाराचिका), f. a gold-<BR>smith's scales, a fine or assay balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायण|नारायणः
नारायण नारायण. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराशंस
नाराशंस नाराशंस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नरा-<BR>शंस), Ved. laudatory or eulogistic praise of a man<BR>or men, (hence a tale or legend which eulogizes a<BR>liberal patron is called Nārāśaṃsī or Nārāśaṃsam);<BR>sacred to or belonging to Agni-narāśaṃsa, relating to<BR>him, containing him, (applied to certain Soma liba-<BR>tions, at which Narāśaṃsa's name is mentioned;<BR>applied also to the Pitṛs because reference is made<BR>to them at these libations.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराशर्य
नाराशर्य नाराशर्य, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(also read पाराशर्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेर|नारिकेरः
नारिकेर नारिकेर or नारिकेल, अस्, m. or<BR>नारिकेलि, इस् and ई, f. the cocoa-nut tree, the cocoa-<BR>nut.<BR>—नारिकेल-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0479-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिङ्गकन्द
नारिङ्गकन्द नारिङ्ग-कन्द, अस्, or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?), the yellow carrot; [cf. नारङ्ग-पत्-<BR>त्रक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारी
नारी नारी, f. See नार, p. 479, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकेल|नारीकेलः
नारीकेल नारीकेल, अस्, ई, m. f. the cocoa-<BR>nut; (ई), f. fermented liquor made from the water<BR>or milk of the cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीच|नारीचं
नारीच नारीच, अम्, n. an esculent root<BR>(= commonly नालिता), Corchorus Capsularis; [cf.<BR>नाडीका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीतरङ्गक|नारीतरंगक|नारीतरङ्गकः
नारीतरङ्गक नारी-तरङ्गक, अस्, m. a liber-<BR>tine, a catamite; [cf. नाडी-तरङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारुन्तुद|नारुंतुद
नारुन्तुद नारुन्तुद (न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>not causing wounds, not hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्तिक
नार्तिक नार्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नर्त), re-<BR>lating to or connected with dancing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्पत्य
नार्पत्य नार्पत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नृ-पति),<BR>kingly, relating to royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्मत
नार्मत नार्मत, अस्, m. (fr. नृ-मत्), a<BR>patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्मद
नार्मद नार्मद, अस्, m. (fr. नर्म-दा), a<BR>metronymic from Narma-dā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्मर
नार्मर नार्मर, अस्, m. (fr. नृ-मर), Ved.<BR>‘man-slayer,’ N. of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्मिण
नार्मिण नार्मिण, अस्, ई, अम् (perhaps fr.<BR>नर्मिन् or नर्मिण, which may be a N. derived<BR>fr. नर्म or नर्मन्), Ved. (Sāy.) delightful, joy-<BR>ful (= नर्म-वत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्मेध
नार्मेध नार्मेध, अम्, n. (fr. नृ-मेध),<BR>Ved., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्य|नार्य्य
नार्य नार्य, अस्, m. (fr. नर्य), Ved. pro-<BR>bably N. of a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्यङ्ग|नार्यंग|नार्यंगः|नार्यङ्गः|नार्य्यङ्ग|नार्य्यङ्गः
नार्यङ्ग नार्यङ्ग, अस्, m. = नारङ्ग, the<BR>orange-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्यतिक्त|नार्य्यतिक्त
नार्यतिक्त नार्य-तिक्त = अनार्य-तिक्त, Aga-<BR>thotes Chirayta (= किरात-तिक्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्षद
नार्षद नार्षद, अस्, m. (fr. नृ-षद्), Ved.<BR>a patronymic of Kaṇva; N. of a demon (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाल|नालं|नालः
नाल नाल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नल), consisting<BR>of reeds, made of a reed or reeds; (आ or ई, अम्), f. n.<BR>a hollow or tubular stalk, especially the stalk of the<BR>lotus [cf. खर-न्˚], of a pot-herb, &c.; (अम्), n.<BR>any pipe or tube or tubular vessel of the body, the<BR>windpipe, urethra, &c.; a handle; = ताल, आल,<BR>yellow orpiment; (आ), f., N. of a river; (ई), f. an<BR>instrument for perforating an elephant's ear; a piece<BR>of metal on which the hours are struck (= घटी);<BR>a period of twenty-four minutes; a lotus flower.<BR>—नाल-वंश, अस्, m. = नल, a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालक
नालक for नाल in चारु-नालक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालकिनी
नालकिनी = नालीकिनी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालायित
नालायित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. an unused Nom. ना-<BR>लाय), representing the handle (of an axe).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालि|नालिः
नालि, इस्, f. = नाडी, any tubular vessel of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिक|नालिकः
नालिक, अस्, m. a buffalo; (आ), f. a stalk, the stalk<BR>of a lotus, a tube, see गन्ध-न्˚, कपाल-न्˚; a<BR>species of pot-herb (= नालिता); a species of plant<BR>(= चर्म-कषा); an instrument for piercing an<BR>elephant's ear; = नाडी, a period of twenty-four<BR>minutes; (अम्), n. a lotus flower [cf. नालीक];<BR>myrrh; a kind of wind instrument, (perhaps) a flute;<BR>a peculiar manner of sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिनी
नालिनी, f. (fr. an unused form नालिन्, which is de-<BR>rived fr. नाल), a mystical N. of one nostril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीक|नालीकः
नालीक, अस्, m. an arrow (= नाराच, but in the<BR>epic poetry different from it); a dart, a javelin, a<BR>pike; body, limb (?); a lotus; the fibrous stalk of<BR>the lotus; (अम्), n. an assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीकिनी
नालीकिनी, f. (fr. an unused form नालीकिन्, which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">Page0480-b+ 73</a>]<BR>is derived fr. नालीक), a multitude or assemblage<BR>of lotus flowers, a lotus lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालन्द|नालन्दः
नालन्द नालन्द, N. of a village near Rāja-<BR>gṛha containing a celebrated Buddhist monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालन्दर
नालन्दर, N. of a Buddhist monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेर|नालिकेरः
नालिकेर नालिकेर, अस्, m. the cocoa-nut<BR>tree, the cocoa-nut; N. of a district to the south-east<BR>of Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेल
नालिकेल, अम्, n. the cocoa-nut; (various reading<BR>for नालिकेर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिजङ्घ|नालिजङ्घः
नालिजङ्घ नालि-जङ्घ, अस्, m. a raven or<BR>the carrion-crow; [cf. नाडी-जङ्घ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिता
नालिता नालिता, f. an esculent root, Arum<BR>Colocasia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीप|नालीपः
नालीप नालीप, अस्, m. = कदम्बक; per-<BR>haps for कडम्बक, the stalk of a pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीव्रण|नालीव्रणः
नालीव्रण नाली-व्रण, अस्, m. a fistulous or<BR>sinus^1 sore (= नाडी-व्रण).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव|नावः
नाव 1. नाव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 4. नु), Ved. a<BR>shout of joy or triumph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव|नावः
नाव 2. नाव = 2. नौ, q. v., a boat, a ship,<BR>in Dvigu comps. after numerals and अर्ध (e. g.<BR>द्वि-नावम्, two boats; अर्ध-न्˚, q. v., Pāṇ. V.<BR>4, 99, 100).<BR>—नावाज (˚व-अज), अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>steerer of a boat, a sailor.<BR>—नावोपजीवन (˚व-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. a sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविक|नाविकः
नाविक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to a vessel, ship,<BR>boat, &c.; (अस्), m. (said to be fr. rt. नुद्), the<BR>helmsman of a vessel, the steersman, pilot; a pas-<BR>senger on board ship, a navigator, a sailor; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविन्
नाविन्, ई, m. a boatman, shipman, sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
1. नाव्य, Nom. P. नाव्यति, &c., to wish for a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
2. नाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, navigable; belonging to a<BR>boat; attainable or accessible by a boat or ship; (आ),<BR>f., Ved. a navigable river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावनीत
नावनीत नावनीत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नव-नीत),<BR>mild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावमिक
नावमिक नावमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नवम),<BR>the ninth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावयज्ञिक
नावयज्ञिक नावयज्ञिक (fr. नव-यज्ञ),<BR>with काल, the time of offering the first-fruits &c.<BR>of the harvest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावाकार
नावाकार नावाकार, नावारोह. See 2. नौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
नाव्य 3. नाव्य, अम्, n. (fr. 1. नव), new-<BR>ness, novelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश|नाशः
नाश 1. नाश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. नश्), Ved.<BR>attainment, obtaining; [cf. दू-णाश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश|नाशः
नाश 2. नाश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. नश्), dis-<BR>appearance; destruction, annihilation, ruin, loss;<BR>death; misfortune; abandonment, desertion; flight,<BR>retreat; (in arithmetic) elimination; [cf. कर्म-न्˚,<BR>ग्रह-न्˚, चित्त-न्˚, दू-णाश.]<BR>—नाश-तस्, ind. =<BR>नाशात्, from death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशक
नाशक, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, destructive, anni-<BR>hilating, causing to perish; [cf. कु-न्˚, कृत-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशन
नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying, annihilating,<BR>causing to be lost, causing to perish, removing,<BR>(commonly in comp. with the object; cf. दुःस्वप्-<BR>न-न्˚); (अम्), n. destruction, removing, removal,<BR>expulsion; ruin, perishing; forgetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशनीय
नाशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to be destroyed,<BR>destructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशयत्
नाशयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, destroying, annihilating,<BR>removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशयितृ
नाशयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. a destroyer, remov-<BR>ing, a remover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशित
नाशित, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed, ruined, suffered to<BR>perish, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशिन्
नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destructive, destroying, a de-<BR>stroyer; removing; perishing, perishable, being lost<BR>or destroyed; [cf. अनर्थ-न्˚, कुष्ठ-न्˚, क्ष-<BR>य-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशी
नाशी, f., N. of a river near Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशुक
नाशुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. disappearing, perishing,<BR>being lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश्य
नाश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, liable to be destroyed, de-<BR>structible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्टिक|नाष्टिकः
नाष्टिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नष्ट), belonging or<BR>relating to anything lost; (अस्), m. the owner of<BR>anything lost, the former owner of a lost chattel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्ट्रा
नाष्ट्रा, f., Ved. danger, destruction; an evil<BR>spirit, a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्
नास् 1. नास्, cl. 1. A. नासते, ननासे,<BR>नासितुम्, to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्
नास् 2. नास्, Ved. the nose, in नासा, du.<BR>(Ṛg-veda II. 39, 6); [cf. 3. नस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासा
नासा, f. (said by some to be fr. rt. स्ना = rt. स्नु),<BR>the nose, (originally perhaps नासा, sing. = a nostril;<BR>नासे, du. = the two nostrils or the nose); a pro-<BR>boscis, the trunk of an elephant [cf. गज-न्˚]; a<BR>piece of wood over a door projecting like a nose,<BR>the upper timber of a door [cf. नक्र]; the plant<BR>Gendarussa Vulgaris (= वासक); [cf. Lat. nāsus,<BR>nāris for nāsis; Old Germ. nāsa; Angl. Sax. nāse;<BR>Mod. Germ. nāse; Slav. nōsŭ; Lith. nōsis; Gr. νῆ-<BR>σος; Hib. neas, ‘a promontory,’ ness in Dunge-ness.]<BR>—नासाग्र (˚सा-अग्˚), अस्, m. the point or tip of<BR>the nose.<BR>—नासा-छिद्र, अम्, n. a nostril.<BR>—नासा-<BR>छिन्नी, f. a species of bird with a divided beak (=<BR>पूर्णिका).<BR>—नासा-ज्वर, अस्, m. a kind of disease<BR>of the nose (= नक्र).<BR>—नासा-दक्षिणावर्त<BR>(˚ण-आव्˚), अस्, m. wearing the nose-ring in the right<BR>nostril by rich women who have children (?).<BR>—नासा-<BR>दारु, n. = नासा, a piece of wood over a door pro-<BR>jecting like a nose; the upper timber of a door-frame.<BR>—नासा-नाह, अस्, m. thickening of the membrane<BR>of the nose, stoppage of the nostrils.<BR>—नासान्तिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नासा-अन्त), reaching to the nose; [cf.<BR>केशान्तिक.]<BR>—नासा-परिशोष, अस्, m. heat and<BR>dryness of the nose.<BR>—नासा-परिस्राव, अस्, m. ‘nose-<BR>flow,’ running at the nose, a running cold.<BR>—नासा-<BR>पाक, अस्, m. a kind of disease of the nose attended<BR>with inflammation.<BR>—नासा-पुट, अस्, m. ‘nose-cup,’<BR>the outside of the nostril, the nostril.<BR>—नासापुट-<BR>मर्यादा, f. the septum of the nose.<BR>—नासा-प्र-<BR>तीनाह, अस्, m. = नासा-नाह, thickening of the<BR>membrane of the nose, stoppage of the nostrils.<BR>—नासा-रक्त-पित्त, अम्, n. bleeding of the nose.<BR>—नासा-रन्ध्र, अम्, n. ‘nose-aperture,’ the<BR>nostril.<BR>—नासार्शस् (˚सा-अर्˚), आस्, m. polypus of the<BR>nose.<BR>—नासा-वंश, अस्, m. the bridge of the nose.<BR>—नासा-वामावर्त (˚म-आव्˚), अस्, m. wearing the<BR>nose-ring in the left nostril, a mark of sorrow or<BR>distress.<BR>—नासा-विवर, अस्, m. ‘nose-cavity,’ a<BR>nostril.<BR>—नासा-शोष, अस्, m. dryness of the nostrils.<BR>—नासा-संवेदन, अस्, m. Momordica Charantia<BR>(= काण्डीर-लता).<BR>—नासा-स्राव, अस्, m. = नासा-<BR>परिस्राव, ‘nose-flow,’ running at the nose, a<BR>running cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासालु|नासालुः
नासालु, उस्, m. a tree, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>See कट्फल, p. 196, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिका
नासिका, f. the nose, (originally नासिका, sing. = a<BR>nostril; नासिके, du. = the two nostrils or the nose);<BR>the trunk of an elephant; a proboscis; any nose-<BR>shaped object [cf. चर्म-न्˚]; a projection, the<BR>upper timber of a door; an epithet of the nymph<BR>Aśvinī; [cf. अ-नासिक, काक-नासिका, चर्म-न्˚.]<BR>—नासिक-त्र्यम्बक-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sa-<BR>cred bathing-place mentioned in the Rasika-ramaṇa.<BR>—नासिकन्-धम, अस्, आ, अम् (नासिकम् for acc.<BR>sing. नासिकाम्), blowing or breathing through the<BR>nose, snoring, &c.<BR>—नासिकन्-धय, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(नासिकम् for acc. sing. नासिकाम्), drinking through<BR>the nose.<BR>—नासिक-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (for नासिका-<BR>वत्), Ved. having a nose.<BR>—नासिकाग्र (˚क-अग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the tip of the nose.<BR>—नासिका-पाक, अस्, m.<BR>= नासा-पाक, a kind of disease or inflammation of<BR>the nose.<BR>—नासिका-पुट, अस्, m. = नासा-पुट,<BR>‘nose-cup,’ the outside of the nostril, the nostril.<BR>—नासिका-मल, अम्, n. the mucus of the nose,<BR>snot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0480-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्य|नासिक्यं|नासिक्यः
नासिक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the nose; uttered<BR>through the nose, nasal; (अस्), m. any nasal sound; a<BR>peculiar nasal sound related to the so-called Yamas;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people in Dakṣiṇā-patha;<BR>(औ), du. = नासत्यौ, the two sons of Aśvinī, the<BR>Aśvins; (अम्), n. the nose; N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्यक|नासिक्यकं
नासिक्यक, अम्, n. the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्य|नास्यं
नास्य, अम्, n. a nose-cord, the rein of a draught-ox<BR>passed through the septum of the nostrils; (perhaps<BR>collectively) noses, a multitude of noses (?); [cf.<BR>नस्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासत्य
नासत्य नासत्य, अस्, m. (derived by native<BR>commentators fr. न + अ-सत्य, ‘not untrue,’ or fr.<BR>नासा + affix त्य, or still more improbably fr. ना,<BR>nom. of नृ = नेतृ + सत्य), N. of one of the<BR>Aśvins, the other being then called Dasra; (औ), m.<BR>du. the common N. of the two Aśvins, see अश्विनौ;<BR>(आ), f. the constellation Aśvinī; (अस्, आ, अम्), re-<BR>ferring or relating to the Nāsatyas; [cf. Zend nā-<BR>onhaitya.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासमौजस
नासमौजस नासमौजस (न-अस्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the brother of Asamaujas and son of Kambala-<BR>barhiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिका
नासिका नासिका. See p. 480, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासीर|नासीरं
नासीर नासीर, अम्, n. advancing or skir-<BR>mishing in front of an army, leaving the line and<BR>defying or challenging the enemy by shouts and<BR>gestures; (अस्), m. the van or a champion who<BR>advances before the line; (also read नासिर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्ति
नास्ति नास्ति (न-अस्ति), ind. non-existence,<BR>not so, it is not.<BR>—नास्ति-ता, f. or नास्ति-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>non-existence.<BR>—नास्ति-वाद, अस्, m. “assertion of ‘it<BR>is not’ or of non-existence,” infidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक|नास्तिकः
नास्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, atheistical, unbelieving, infidel,<BR>an unbeliever, applied by the orthodox Hindūs to<BR>any one who denies the divine authority of the<BR>Vedas and a future life, or doubts the legends of the<BR>Purāṇas; [cf. आस्तिक.]<BR>—नास्तिक-ता, f. or नास्तिक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. or नास्तिक्य, अम्, n. infidelity, disbelief,<BR>atheism, denial of the deity, of a future state, of the<BR>authority of the Vedas, &c.; Buddhism, heresy, &c.<BR>—नास्तिक-मत, अम्, n. an atheistical opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिद|नास्तिदः
नास्तिद नास्तिद or (according to others)<BR>नास्तितद, अस्, m. the mango tree (= आम्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाह|नाहः
नाह नाह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. नह्), binding,<BR>confinement; a trap, a snare for catching deer &c.;<BR>obstruction in any organ or secretion of the body, as<BR>costiveness &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहल|नाहलः
नाहल नाहल, अस्, m. a man of a bar-<BR>barous or outcast tribe; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a non-<BR>Āryan people (= म्लेच्छ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुष|नाहुषः
नाहुष 1. नाहुष, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. नहुस्), Ved.<BR>neighbouring, being in the vicinity, neighbourly?;<BR>(Sāy.) human, belonging to men; (अस्), m. a<BR>neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुष|नाहुषः
नाहुष 2. नाहुष, अस्, m. (fr. नहुष), a<BR>patronymic of Yayāti; N. of a serpent-demon; [cf.<BR>नहुष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुषि|नाहुषिः
नाहुषि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Yayāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि नि (an indeclinable prefix to verbs and<BR>nouns, used as a preposition except in one passage<BR>in Atharva-veda X. 8, 7, where it stands alone as an<BR>adverb), in, into, within; down, under, back; on,<BR>upon. As a prefix to nouns नि appears sometimes to<BR>be a curtailed form of निस् in its sense of ‘without,’<BR>‘deprived of’ (e. g. in नि-किल्विष, नि-खिल, q. v.),<BR>but the idea of negation in such compounds may pos-<BR>sibly be derived from the meanings ‘down,’ ‘down-<BR>wards,’ ‘back,’ which properly belong to नि; occasion-<BR>ally, however, नि is inaccurately written for निः (=<BR>निस्), as in नि-शब्द for निः-शब्द; according to<BR>native lexicographers the senses in which नि may be<BR>used are expressed by the following Sanskrit words,<BR>क्षेप, भृशार्थ, नित्यार्थ, दान, सन्-नि-<BR>धान, उप-रम, सं-श्रय, आ-श्रय, राशि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">Page0481-b+ 70</a>]<BR>मोक्ष, अन्तर्-भाव, अधो-भाव, बन्धन,<BR>कौशल, नि-वेश, वि-न्य्-आस; [नि is thought by<BR>some to be for primitive अनि; cf. अन्-तर्, अन्-तरा;<BR>Gr. ἐν, ἐνί, εἰν, εἰς, ἐς for ἐν-ς, ἐν-τό-ς, ἔν-δο-ν,<BR>ἔσ-ω, ἔνεροι, ἔνερ-θε, ὑπ-ένερ-θε, ἐνέρ-τερο-ς,<BR>ἔντερο-ν; Lat. en-do, in-du, in, in-ter, in-trā, in-<BR>ter-ior, in-tumu-s, in-tus; Umbr. en, an-der;<BR>Osk. an-ter; Goth. in, inna, innuma, inna-<BR>thrō, un-dar; Mod. Germ. nieder; Angl. Sax. in,<BR>nidhan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निंस्
निंस् निंस् (thought by some to be a con-<BR>traction of निनंस्, old Desid. of rt. नम्),<BR>cl. 2. A. निंस्ते (2nd sing. निंस्से, 2nd sing. Impv.<BR>निंस्स्व), निनिंसे, निंसितुम्, &c., Ved. to touch,<BR>kiss, salute. (After प्र the initial न् is optionally<BR>cerebralized, cf. प्र-णिंसितव्य, प्र-निंसितव्य,<BR>परि-णिंसक; cf. also rt. निक्ष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निः|नि
निः निः, euphonically substituted for निस्,<BR>q. v., before श्, ष्, स्, and rarely before क्, ख्, प्, फ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक
निःक˚ निः-क˚, निः-का˚, &c. See under<BR>निष्-क˚, निष्-का˚, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षत्र
निःक्षत्र निः-क्षत्र or निः-क्षत्रिय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, destitute of the military tribe, having no<BR>warrior-caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्
निःक्षिप् निः-क्षिप्, probably for नि-क्षिप्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्त
निः-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or sent away;<BR>spent (as time), passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्य
निः-क्षिप्य, ind. having thrown or sent away;<BR>having spent (as time); having wiped away (as tears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षेप|निःक्षेपः
निः-क्षेप, अस्, m. throwing, sending, putting<BR>away; spending, passing (time); wiping away (as<BR>tears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःप
निःप˚ निः-प˚ and निः-फ˚. See under<BR>निष्-प˚ and निष्-फ˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशंसय
निःशंसय निः-शंसय, wrongly spelt for<BR>निः-संशय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशङ्क
निःशङ्क निः-शङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>fear, fearless, without misgiving or apprehension,<BR>having no cares, free from risk; (अम्), ind. fearlessly,<BR>without fear or care, without anxiety.<BR>—निःशङ्क-<BR>सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping without care, sleeping<BR>calmly and securely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशङ्कित
निः-शङ्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, free from fear or care,<BR>free from risk, secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्द|निःशब्दः
निःशब्द निः-शब्द, अस्, आ, अम्, noiseless,<BR>soundless, not making a noise; (अस्, अम्), m. n. (?),<BR>soundlessness, silence, a calm; (अम्), ind. without<BR>noise, noiselessly; [cf. नि-शब्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशम|निःशमः
निःशम निः-शम, अस्, m. uneasiness, dis-<BR>composure, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशयान
निःशयान निः-शयान, अस्, आ, अम्, not sleep-<BR>ing, not lying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशरण
निःशरण निः-शरण, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>protection or refuge, defenceless, unprotected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशर्कर
निःशर्कर निः-शर्कर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>stones or pebbles (as a bathing-place).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशलाक|निःशलाकः
निःशलाक निः-शलाक, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>talking birds (as parrots, jays, or crows); solitary, private.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशल्य
निःशल्य निः-शल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>an arrow; free from spikes or thorns; (अम्), ind.<BR>without an arrow; unthorny; without pain or diffi-<BR>culty; without reluctance, willingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशस्
निःशस् निः-शस्, f., Ved. refusing, declin-<BR>ing; (Sāy.) disinclination, absence of wish or desire,<BR>dislike (= निः-शंसन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशस्त्र
निःशस्त्र निः-शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>arms, unarmed, weaponless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशास्
निःशास् निः-शास् (निस्-श्˚), cl. 2. P. -शास्ति,<BR>-शासितुम्, Ved. to order off or away; to expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशिष्
निःशिष् निः-शिष् (निस्-श्˚), Caus. -शेषयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to take away or destroy completely, con-<BR>sume entirely, annihilate; (also regarded as a Nom.<BR>fr. निः-शेष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निः-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्, having no remainder, with-<BR>out remainder, completely spent, complete, entire,<BR>whole, (often in the sense of an adverb at the be-<BR>ginning of a comp. before a participle, e. g. निः-<BR>शेष-भग्न, completely broken); (अम् or एण),<BR>ind. completely, totally; निःशेषं कृ, to destroy<BR>or consume completely; [cf. अ-शेष.]<BR>—निःशेष-<BR>तस्, ind. without remainder, completely, totally.<BR>—निःशेष-ता, f. complete destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेषण
निः-शेषण, अस्, आ, अम्, = निः-शेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेषित
निः-शेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, having nothing left, com-<BR>pletely consumed or finished, destroyed, annihilated;<BR>(wrongly read नि-शेषित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशुक्र
निःशुक्र निः-शुक्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. without<BR>brilliancy; without virile energy, impotent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशूक|निःशूकः
निःशूक निः-शूक, अस्, m. beardless rice<BR>without any awn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निःशेष निः-शेष. See निः-शिष् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशोक
निःशोक निः-शोक, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>sorrow or care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशोध्य|निःशोध्यं
निःशोध्य निः-शोध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be<BR>purified, not requiring cleansing; clean, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्मश्रु
निःश्मश्रु निः-श्मश्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, beardless;<BR>(wrongly read नि-श्मश्रु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रम
निःश्रम निः-श्रम. See नि-श्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रयणी
निःश्रयणी निः-श्रयणी or निः-श्रयिणी, f. a<BR>ladder, a staircase, steps, &c.; [cf. नि-श्रयणी, नि-<BR>श्रयिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेणि|निःश्रेणिः
निः-श्रेणि, इस्, ई, f. a ladder or staircase, a flight of<BR>stairs or steps; the wild date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेणिका
निःश्रेणिका, f. a species of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्री
निःश्री निः-श्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, deprived of happi-<BR>ness or prosperity, unfortunate.<BR>—निःश्री-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made unfortunate, rendered unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रीक
निःश्रीक, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of beauty (as a<BR>dead body), deprived of happiness, &c.; one whose<BR>happiness is destroyed, unhappy, inglorious; (also<BR>read नि-श्रीक.)<BR>—निःश्रीक-ता, f. absence of good<BR>fortune, want of good luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेणि|निःश्रेणिः
निःश्रेणि निः-श्रेणि. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेयस|निःश्रेयसं|निःश्रेयसः
निःश्रेयस निः-श्रेयस, अस्, ई, अम्, having<BR>nothing better or superior, the best, most excellent;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; (अम्), n. final beatitude,<BR>ultimate bliss or supreme felicity in the life to come,<BR>happiness, welfare; knowledge which brings deliver-<BR>ance, learning; belief, faith, devotedness; appre-<BR>hension, conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वस्
निःश्वस् निः-श्वस्, cl. 2. P. -श्वसिति, -श्वसि-<BR>तुम्, to breathe out, expire, sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसन|निःश्वसनं
निः-श्वसन, अम्, n. breathing out, sighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसित
निः-श्वसित, अस्, आ, अम्, breathed out, sighed;<BR>sighing, breathing out; (अम्), n. sighing, expiration,<BR>a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वस्य
निः-श्वस्य, ind. having sighed, sighing, breath-<BR>ing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वास|निःश्वासः
निः-श्वास, अस्, m. breathing out, expiration;<BR>breath, sighing, a sigh; (often read नि-श्वास.)<BR>—निः-<BR>श्वास-परम, अस्, आ, अम्, chiefly engaged in sigh-<BR>ing, melancholy, sorrowful.<BR>—निःश्वास-संहिता, f.,<BR>N. of a code of laws supposed to have been revealed<BR>by Rudra-Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःषमम्
निःषमम् निः-षमम्, ind. (fr. निस् + स-<BR>मम्), at the wrong time, unseasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःषिध्
निःषिध् निः-षिध्, त्, f. (fr. निस् + सिध् =<BR>साध्), granting, bestowing; grant, oblation, gift,<BR>donation; (Sāy.) hindrance, obstruction; destroying,<BR>destructive, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःषिध्वन्
निः-षिध्वन्, आ, अरी, अ (fr. निस् + सिध्वन्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">Page0482-a+ 69</a>]<BR>Ved. granting, presenting; (Sāy.) coming to com-<BR>plete perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0481-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंशय
निःसंशय निः-संशय, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>doubted, infallible, unerring, certain; not doubting,<BR>not doubtful; (अम्), ind. without doubt, doubtless,<BR>infallibly, certainly, surely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसङ्कक्ष|निःसंकक्ष
निःसङ्कक्ष निः-सङ्कक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, not per-<BR>plexed, not confused; (also written नि-सङ्कक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसङ्ख्य|निःसंख्य
निःसङ्ख्य निः-सङ्ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, innu-<BR>merable, numberless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसङ्ग|निःसंग|निःसंगः|निःसङ्गः
निःसङ्ग निः-सङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, unattached,<BR>unobstructed; not attached, not devoted, regardless,<BR>indifferent to (with loc.); free from worldly attach-<BR>ment or selfish desires, unselfish, disinterested; un-<BR>connected, separated; (एन or अम्), ind. without<BR>attachment, without interest, unselfishly, without<BR>further reflection; (also written निः-षङ्ग; cf.<BR>अ-सङ्ग.)<BR>—निःसङ्ग-ता, f. or निःसङ्ग-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. absence of attachment, unselfishness, disinterested-<BR>ness, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसञ्चार|निःसंचार|निःसंचारः
निःसञ्चार निः-सञ्चार, अस्, आ, अम्, not mov-<BR>ing, not walking about, not leaving one's home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसञ्ज्ञ
निःसञ्ज्ञ निः-सञ्ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, senseless,<BR>insensible, unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्त्व
निःसत्त्व निः-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>courage or strength, unenergetic, weak, impotent;<BR>insignificant, low, mean; non-existent, unsubstantial;<BR>deprived of living beings; (अम्), n. absence of power,<BR>want of energy; insignificance; non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्य
निःसत्य निः-सत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, untrue, false.<BR>—निःसत्य-ता, f. insincerity, falsehood, untruth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसन्तति|निःसंतति
निःसन्तति निः-सन्तति, इस्, इस्, इ, destitute<BR>of offspring, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसन्तान|निःसंतान
निः-सन्तान, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of posterity,<BR>childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसन्दिग्ध|निःसंदिग्ध
निःसन्दिग्ध निः-सन्दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>doubted, not doubtful, certain; (अम्), ind. without<BR>any doubt, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसन्देह|निःसंदेह
निः-सन्देह, अस्, आ, अम्, free from uncertainty,<BR>doubtless, undoubted, certain; (अम्), ind. without<BR>any doubt, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसन्धि|निःसंधि|निःसन्धिः
निःसन्धि निः-सन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, having no<BR>joints, having no joints perceptible, well knit, com-<BR>pact, close, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसपत्न
निःसपत्न निः-सपत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no rival, not sharing the possession of anything with<BR>another; not claimed by another, belonging exclu-<BR>sively to one possessor; having no enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसम्पात|निःसंपात|निःसंपातः|निःसम्पातः
निःसम्पात निः-सम्पात, अस्, आ, अम्, afford-<BR>ing no passage, blocked up; (अस्), m. thick dark-<BR>ness, midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसम्बन्ध
निःसम्बन्ध निः-सम्बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, with-<BR>out relatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसम्बाध|निःसंबाध
निःसम्बाध निः-सम्बाध, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>contracted, large, spacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसम्भ्रम|निःसंभ्रम
निःसम्भ्रम निः-सम्भ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>perplexed or flurried, unembarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरण|निःसरणं
निःसरण निः-सरण. See under निः-सृ,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसलिल
निःसलिल निः-सलिल, अस्, आ, अम्, waterless,<BR>having no water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसह
निःसह निः-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, unable to bear<BR>or support or resist, impatient; powerless, weak;<BR>intolerable, unbearable, irresistible.<BR>—निःसह-ता, f.<BR>or निःसह-त्व, अम्, n. inability to bear or support;<BR>impatience, unendurance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसहाय
निःसहाय निः-सहाय, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>helpers or associates, unassisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसाध्वस
निःसाध्वस निः-साध्वस, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">Page0482-b+ 70</a>]<BR>bold; (अम्), ind. fearlessly, boldly.<BR>—निःसाध्वस-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. fearlessness, boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसामर्थ्य
निःसामर्थ्य निः-सामर्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unfit,<BR>unsuitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसामान्य
निःसामान्य निः-सामान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, extra-<BR>ordinary, uncommon, unusual, special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार|निःसारः
निःसार 1. निः-सार, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. निः-<BR>सार see under निः-सृ below), sapless, pithless,<BR>worthless, vain, vapid, unsubstantial; (अस्), m. the plant<BR>Trophis Aspera; a kind of time in music; (आ), f.<BR>the pisang, Musa Sapientum (= कदली).<BR>—निःसार-<BR>ता, f. saplessness, worthlessness, vanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसाल
निःसाल निः-साल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being<BR>out of the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसीमन्
निःसीमन् निः-सीमन्, आ, आ, अ, immeasurable,<BR>having no boundaries or limits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसुख
निःसुख निः-सुख, अस्, आ, अम्, joyless, sad,<BR>unhappy; disagreeable, distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसृ
निःसृ निः-सृ (निस्-स्˚), cl. 1. P. -सरति,<BR>-सर्तुम्, to go out, come forth, issue, slip out,<BR>depart, withdraw: Caus. -सारयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to go out or away, turn out, expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसर
निः-सर, अस्, आ, अम्, issuing out.<BR>—निःसर-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. = पित्त-रोग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरण|निःसरणं
निः-सरण, अम्, n. going forth or out, coming<BR>forth, exit; the egress or outlet from a house,<BR>market-place, town, &c., the gate, the gate-way;<BR>a means or expedient, a remedy; departure, dying,<BR>death; final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार|निःसारः
2. निः-सार, अस्, m. (for 1. निः-सार see above),<BR>going forth or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारण|निःसारणं
निः-सारण, अम्, n. driving out, expelling, turn-<BR>ing out; the egress or outlet from a building, town,<BR>&c., a passage, road of ingress or egress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारित|निःसारितः
निः-सारित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned out, made to come<BR>out, expelled, dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार्य
निः-सार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be turned out, to be<BR>excluded or expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसृत
निः-सृत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone forth or out, broken<BR>forth; having departed (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्तम्भ
निःस्तम्भ निः-स्तम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>posts or columns, having no pillars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्तुति
निःस्तुति निः-स्तुति, इस्, इस्, इ (also read नि-<BR>स्तुति), praising nothing, without praising (anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्नेह|निःस्नेहः
निःस्नेह निः-स्नेह, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>unction, not greasy or unctuous, dry; without love<BR>or affection, insensible, cold, unfeeling; not longing<BR>for, indifferent; not loved, uncared for, hated; (आ),<BR>f. linseed, Linum Usitatissimum.<BR>—निःस्नेह-फला,<BR>f. a species of Solanum with white flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पन्द|निःस्पंद
निःस्पन्द निः-स्पन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पृह
निःस्पृह निः-स्पृह, अस्, आ, अम् (often written<BR>नि-स्पृह), free from desire; disregarding, indiffer-<BR>ent to (with abl.); content, unenvious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्यन्द
निःस्यन्द निः-स्यन्द. See नि-स्यन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्रु
निःस्रु निः-स्रु (निस्-स्˚), Caus. -स्रावयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to flow out or off, to empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्रव|निःस्रवः
निः-स्रव, अस्, m. remainder, surplus, overplus<BR>(with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्राव|निःस्रावः
निः-स्राव, अस्, m. causing to flow out, expending,<BR>expense; the moisture or water of boiled rice; [cf.<BR>नि-स्राव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्व|निःस्वः
निःस्व निः-स्व, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of one's<BR>own, having no property, indigent, poor.<BR>—निःस्व-<BR>ता, f. poverty.<BR>—निःस्वी-कृत or निःस्वी-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, deprived of one's property, impoverished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वन|निःस्वनः
निःस्वन निः-स्वन, अस्, m. (fr. स्वन् with<BR>निस्), sound, noise, voice; [cf. नि-स्वन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वभाव|निःस्वभावः
निःस्वभाव निः-स्वभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, void of<BR>peculiarities, without peculiar properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वादु
निःस्वादु निः-स्वादु, उस्, उस् or द्वी, उ, taste-<BR>less, void of flavour, insipid, unsavoury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वाध्याय
निःस्वाध्याय निः-स्वाध्याय, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>muttering prayers, not repeating texts.<BR>—निःस्वा-<BR>ध्याय-वषट्कार, अस्, आ, अम्, neither repeating<BR>holy texts nor sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकक्ष
निकक्ष नि-कक्ष, अस्, m., Ved. the armpit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकट|निकटं|निकटः
निकट नि-कट, अस्, आ, अम्, situated at the<BR>side, near, proximate, close by; without neighbours,<BR>kinless?; (अस्, अम्), m. n. proximity; (ए), ind. in<BR>the neighbourhood, at hand.<BR>—निकटी-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकथित
निकथित नि-कथित, अस्, आ, अम्, told, re-<BR>lated (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकथितिन्
निकथितिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has told.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकम्
निकम् नि-कम्, cl. 10. A. -कामयते, -च-<BR>कमे, &c., to long for, wish for, have a desire for,<BR>lust after (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाम|निकामं|निकामः
नि-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desirous of, longing<BR>for, vehemently desiring, (often at the beginning of<BR>a comp. in the sense of नि-कामम्, ind.); (अस्), m.<BR>desire, wish; (अम्), ind. according to wish or desire,<BR>willingly, according to pleasure or to one's satisfaction,<BR>to one's heart's content; यदा निकामम्, if you<BR>please, if you like.<BR>—निकाम-काम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>covetous.<BR>—निकाम-वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, raining ac-<BR>cording to wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकामन्
नि-कामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. desirous of, longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकामन|निकामनं
नि-कामन, अम्, n. desire, longing after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकामयमान
नि-कामयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, longing for, wish-<BR>ing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर|निकरः
निकर नि-कर, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. कॄ with नि),<BR>a heap, pile; a flock or multitude; a bundle; pith,<BR>sap, essence; suitable gift, a honorarium; a treasure,<BR>the best of anything, a treasure belonging to Kuvera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
1. नि-कार, अस्, m. piling up or winnowing corn;<BR>tossing or lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकष|निकषः
निकष नि-कष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कष् for<BR>कर्ष् = कृष् with नि), the touchstone, the streak<BR>of gold or test made on it [cf. नि-काष]; (आ), f., N.<BR>of the mother of Rāvaṇa or of the mother of the<BR>Piśitāśana fiends or imps in general.<BR>—निकषात्-<BR>मज (˚षा-आत्˚), अस्, m. a Rākṣasa, a sort of<BR>demon; [cf. कषा-पुत्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषण|निकषणः
नि-कषण, अम्, n. (?), the touchstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषा
नि-कषा, ind. near to (with acc.), proximate;<BR>in the middle, betwixt, between (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषाय
निकषाय, Nom. A. निकषायते, &c., to be<BR>used or serve as a touchstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकस|निकसः
निकस नि-कस, निकसात्मज = नि-कष and<BR>निकषात्मज, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाणम्
निकाणम् नि-काणम्, ind. (fr. rt. कण् with<BR>नि), having closed the eyes; निकाणम् अक्षि जल्-<BR>पति or अक्षि-निकाणं जल्पति, he speaks with<BR>closed eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय|निकायः
निकाय नि-काय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. चि with नि),<BR>a heap, an assemblage, a group, class, association or<BR>set of persons who perform like duties; a congre-<BR>gation, a school; a flock, multitude in general; a<BR>house, dwelling-place, habitation, hiding-place; the<BR>body; (according to Mahī-dhara) the air, wind<BR>(Ved.); a butt, aim, mark; the universal Soul,<BR>Supreme Being.<BR>—निकायान्तरीय (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, belonging to another assemblage or school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकायिन्
नि-कायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, an epithet of particular oblations<BR>or sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय्य|निकाय्यः
नि-काय्य, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), a dwelling, house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
निकार 1. and 2. नि-कार. For 1. see above;<BR>for 2. see under नि-कृ, p. 483, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारिन्
निकारिन् नि-कारिन्. See p. 483, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकावल्गा
निकावल्गा निकावल्गा, f., N. of a woman,<BR>(perhaps rather two names, निका and वल्गा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाश|निकाशः
निकाश नि-काश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. काश् with नि),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">Page0483-a+ 73</a>]<BR>the horizon; appearance, sight; (at the end of an<BR>adj. comp.) having the appearance of, similar, like;<BR>[cf. नी-काश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0482-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाषम्
निकाषम् नि-काषम्, ind. having pounded<BR>or mixed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकास|निकासः
निकास नि-कास = नि-काश, नी-काश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकिल्बिष
निकिल्बिष नि-किल्बिष, अम्, n., Ved. freeing<BR>from sin, deliverance from evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुचिति
निकुचिति नि-कुचिति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. कुञ्च् with<BR>नि), contraction ?; [cf. Pāṇ. I. 2, 18.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुच्यकर्णि
निकुच्य-कर्णि, ind. with the ears hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चक|निकुञ्चकः
नि-कुञ्चक, अस्, m. a measure of capacity equal<BR>to (1/4) of a Kuḍava; a species of reed (= वानीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चित|निकुञ्चितं
नि-कुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्ज|निकुंज|निकुंजं|निकुञ्जं|निकुंजः|निकुञ्जः
निकुञ्ज नि-कुञ्ज, अस्, अम्, m. n. = कुञ्ज, an<BR>arbour, a bower, a place overgrown with shrubs and<BR>creepers, a thicket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्जिकाम्ला
निकुञ्जिकाम्ला (˚का-अम्˚), f. a species of plant<BR>(= कुञ्जिका, कुञ्ज-वल्लरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भ|निकुंभ|निकुंभः|निकुम्भः
निकुम्भ नि-कुम्भ, अस्, m. the plant Croton<BR>Polyandrum; N. of a Dānava who, like Kumbha,<BR>was son of Pra-hlāda, (he was father of Sunda and<BR>Upa-sunda); N. of a Rakṣas; of a son of Kumbha-<BR>karṇa; of an attendant of Śiva; of one of Skanda's<BR>attendants; N. of one of the Viśve Devāḥ, (also<BR>read विस्कुम्भु); N. of a hero on the side of the<BR>Kurus; N. of a king of Ayodhyā, son of Hary-aśva<BR>and father of Saṃhatāśva; (ई), f. the plant Croton<BR>Polyandrum.<BR>—निकुम्भाख्य-जीव (˚भ-आख्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a plant, Croton Jamalgota (= जय-पाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भित|निकुम्भितं
नि-कुम्भित, अम्, n. a kind of time in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भिला|निकुंभिला
नि-कुम्भिला, f. (fr. कुम्भ, a jar?), a place<BR>where oblations are offered; a grove at the western<BR>gate of Laṅkā for the performance of sacrificial rites;<BR>(according to another commentator) an image of<BR>Bhadra-kālī on the west side of Laṅkā; (also,<BR>according to some, नि-कुम्भिलस्, m., and नि-कुम्-<BR>भिलम्, n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरुम्ब|निकुरुंब|निकुरुंबं
निकुरुम्ब नि-कुरुम्ब or नि-कुरुम्बक, अम्,<BR>n. a flock, mass, multitude; (also read नि-कुरम्ब,<BR>-नि-कुरूम्ब, नि-कुरुम्भ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुलीनिका
निकुलीनिका नि-कुलीनिका, f. a family art or<BR>one inherited by birth, any skill or skilful act pecu-<BR>liar to a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकूल
निकूल नि-कूल, अस्, आ, अम्, going down<BR>hill, (opposed to उत्-कूल); standing on a declivity<BR>or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृ
निकृ नि-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, Ved. to put down, bring down, lower,<BR>humiliate, subdue, overcome, overpower, depreciate,<BR>debase; to act in a low or base manner, to treat ill;<BR>(in the post-Vedic literature only occurring in the<BR>past part. नि-कृत, q. v.): Desid. नि-चिकीर्षति, to<BR>wish to subdue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्तव्य
नि-कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be acted badly or<BR>basely, to be injured; (अस्माकं तैर् निकर्तव्यम्,<BR>a wrong is to be done us by them.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
2. नि-कार, अस्, m. putting down, bringing down,<BR>humiliation, subjugation; injury, insult, wrong, offence;<BR>wickedness, malice, abuse, reproach, disrespect; op-<BR>position, contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारण|निकारणं
नि-कारण, अम्, n. killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारिन्
नि-कारिन्, ई, m., Ved. an injurer, oppressor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत|निकृतः
नि-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought down, lowered,<BR>cast down, humbled, humiliated; insulted, offended;<BR>afflicted; injured; tricked, cheated, deceived; re-<BR>moved, set aside, dismissed; dishonest, wicked, per-<BR>verse; low, base, vile; (अम्), n. lowering, humbling,<BR>humiliation; (also read नि-कृति.)<BR>—निकृत-प्रज्ञ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, evil-minded.<BR>—निकृत-मति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>depraved in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृति|निकृतिः
नि-कृति, इस्, f. low conduct, baseness, wicked-<BR>ness, dishonest practice, dishonesty, fraud, deception,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">Page0483-b+ 73</a>]<BR>deceit, cheating; offence, insult; abuse, reproach;<BR>rejection, removal; poverty, indigence; wickedness,<BR>a wicked person (personified as a daughter of<BR>A-dharma and Hiṃsā, or Nirṛti); (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>base, low, dishonest, wicked; (इस्), m., N. of one<BR>of the eight Vasus.<BR>—निकृति-प्रज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>versed in dishonesty, well acquainted with vice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतिन्
निकृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. नि-कृत), = नि-कृति, dis-<BR>honest, low, base, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत्या
नि-कृत्या, f. wickedness, dishonesty, fraud, &c.,<BR>= नि-कृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत्वन्
नि-कृत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. acting basely, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत्
निकृत् नि-कृत्, cl. 6. P. -कृन्तति, -कर्तितुम्,<BR>to cut down, hew down, cut away, cut or chop off,<BR>cut through, cut asunder, cut to pieces, massacre;<BR>tear off, tear away, wear away; A. (-ते), to cut one-<BR>self (or one's nails &c.); to cut down &c.: Caus.<BR>-कर्तयति, &c., to cause to cut or cut down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्तन|निकर्तनं
नि-कर्तन, अम्, n. cutting down, cutting to<BR>pieces, cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत्त
नि-कृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cut off, cut up.<BR>—निकृत्त-<BR>मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, cut up by the roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृन्तन|निकृंतन
नि-कृन्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, cutting down, cutting<BR>off, destroying; (अस्), m., N. of a hell; (अम्), n.<BR>massacring, cutting, cutting off, destruction; an in-<BR>strument for cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्
निकृष् नि-कृष्, cl. 1. 6. P. -कर्षति, -कृ-<BR>षति, -कर्ष्टुम् or -क्रष्टुम्, to draw down,<BR>drag down; to tear asunder (?). In Mahā-bh. 1.<BR>3616. नि-कृष्यते may mean ‘is drawn down by<BR>the stream of a river.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षण|निकर्षणं
नि-कर्षण, अम्, n. an open space for recreation,<BR>a sort of play-ground in or near a town; a court at<BR>the entrance of a house; a neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्ट|निकृष्टः
नि-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, debased, low, base, vile,<BR>vulgar; despised, outcast; near; (अम्), n. vicinity,<BR>proximity.<BR>—निकृष्टाशय (˚ट-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having base intentions.<BR>—निकृष्टाशय-ता, f. the<BR>state of one who has base intentions, base disposition<BR>of mind; jealousy.<BR>—निकृष्टोपाधि-ता (˚ट-उप्˚),<BR>f. a state of base or low deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेचाय|निकेचायः
निकेचाय नि-केचाय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. चि with<BR>नि), piling or collecting repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेत|निकेतः
निकेत नि-केत or नि-केतक, अस्, m. = केतन,<BR>a house, mansion, habitation; a mark, countersign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतन|निकेतनं|निकेतनः
निकेतन नि-केतन, अस्, m. an onion; (अम्),<BR>n. = नि-केत, a house, mansion, abode, habitation,<BR>temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोचक|निकोचकः
निकोचक नि-कोचक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कुञ्च्<BR>with नि), the tree Alangium Decapetalum; (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोचन|निकोचनं
नि-कोचन, अम्, n. contracting, contraction, com-<BR>pression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोठक|निकोठकः
निकोठक नि-कोठक, अस्, m. = नि-कोचक<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोथक
निकोथक नि-कोथक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कुथ् with<BR>नि), N. of a teacher with the epithet Bhāyajātya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोश्य
निकोश्य नि-कोश्य, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>Ved. a particular part of the entrails of sacrificial<BR>animals; [cf. कोश्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्तहस्त
निक्तहस्त निक्त-हस्त. See rt. निज्, p. 485.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रन्द्
निक्रन्द् नि-क्रन्द्, cl. 1. P. -क्रन्दति, -क्रन्-<BR>दितुम्, Ved. to utter a cry in a direction downwards<BR>(as a bird on a tree): Caus. -क्रन्दयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to cause to roar &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रम्
निक्रम् नि-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. -क्रामति, -क्र-<BR>मितुम्, to set the foot on the ground, put down the<BR>feet; to enter; to tread down (with acc.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रमण|निक्रमणं
नि-क्रमण, अम्, n., Ved. putting down the feet,<BR>treading down; the place where the foot is put,<BR>foot-step, foot-fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रीड्
निक्रीड् नि-क्रीड्, Caus. -क्रीडयति, &c., to<BR>play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रीड
नि-क्रीड, अस्, m. play, sport; मरुतां निक्रीडः,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वण|निक्वणः
निक्वण नि-क्वण or नि-क्वाण, अस्, m. a<BR>musical tone or sound; any sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्ष्
निक्ष् निक्ष्, cl. 1. P. निक्षति, &c., to<BR>pierce (Ved.); to kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षण|निक्षणं
निक्षण, अम्, n. kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षा
निक्षा निक्षा, f. a nit; (a wrong form for<BR>लिक्षा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्
निक्षिप् नि-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -क्षिपति, -ते,<BR>-क्षेप्तुम्, to throw down, cast or put down, throw<BR>upon, put or lay down; put in, pour in; to deliver<BR>anything (acc.) to a person (loc.); to give or hand<BR>over, grant; to deposit, commit, deliver to any one's<BR>charge, intrust; to install, appoint, establish; to lay<BR>aside, give up, leave off, cast off, repel; to encamp:<BR>Caus. -क्षेपयति, &c., to cause to put down, to<BR>cause to be set down in writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिपत्
नि-क्षिपत्, अन्, अन्ती or अती, अत्, throwing down<BR>or on, placing in or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्त|निक्षिप्तं
नि-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown down or upon,<BR>put down, laid down or on, placed into, thrust into;<BR>deposited, pawned, pledged; rejected, abandoned,<BR>foregone, given or thrown away; sent, sent off or<BR>away.<BR>—निक्षिप्त-वाद, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>ceased talking or left off boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्य
नि-क्षिप्य, ind. having placed or laid down or<BR>upon; having given in charge, having intrusted or<BR>deposited in a place of safety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप|निक्षेपः
नि-क्षेप, अस्, m. throwing upon, casting on<BR>(with loc.); a deposit, pledge, trust, anything de-<BR>posited without a seal in trust or as a compensation,<BR>anything pawned; abandoning, parting with, throw-<BR>ing away; sending or putting away; wiping, drying;<BR>in निक्षेप-लिपि probably N. of a country; [cf.<BR>उत्-क्षेप, प्र-क्षेप, वि-क्षेप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपण|निक्षेपणं
नि-क्षेपण, अम्, n. putting down (the feet); a<BR>means by which or place in which anything is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपित
नि-क्षेपित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be put down<BR>or set down in writing, committed to writing, in-<BR>scribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप्तृ
नि-क्षेप्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what places or<BR>deposits, delivers to one's care; (ता), m. a depositor,<BR>a pawner or pledger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप्य
नि-क्षेप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be deposited, to be<BR>thrust into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षुभा
निक्षुभा नि-क्षुभा, f. (fr. rt. क्षुभ् with<BR>नि), N. of the mother of Maga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखन्
निखन् नि-खन्, cl. 1. P. A. -खनति, -ते,<BR>-खनितुम्, to dig into (the ground), bury; to dig<BR>in or up, root up; to infix, pierce (with an arrow<BR>&c.), to fix, implant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखनन|निखननं
नि-खनन, अम्, n. digging in, burying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखात
नि-खात, अस्, आ, अम्, dug in, buried; dug up,<BR>excavated; fixed in the ground as a stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखानित
नि-खानित, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the Caus.), infixed,<BR>dug in, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्ब|निखर्ब्ब|निखर्ब्बं|निखर्ब्बः
निखर्ब नि-खर्ब or नि-खर्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>dwarfish, a dwarf; (अम्), n. a billion; [cf. खर्व.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्वक
नि-खर्वक, अम्, n., 1000 millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्वट
नि-खर्वट, अस्, m., N. of a Rakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिद्
निखिद् नि-खिद्, cl. 6. P., Ved. -खिदति,<BR>-खेत्तुम्, to press down; (Sāy.) to cut off, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिल|निखिलं
निखिल नि-खिल, अस्, आ, अम् (probably for<BR>निः-खिल), complete, all, whole, entire; (एन), ind.<BR>completely, totally; [cf. खिल, अ-ख्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखुर्यप
निखुर्यप निखुर्य-प (?), अस्, m., Ved. an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगड|निगडः
निगड नि-गड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably fr.<BR>rt. गड् = rt. गल्; cf. नि-गल), an iron chain for<BR>the feet, a fetter, especially the chain used to secure<BR>the hind feet of an elephant or a noose for catching<BR>the feet and throwing an animal down, a fetter or<BR>shackle in general, gyves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0483-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडन|निगडनं
नि-गडन, अम्, n. putting in irons or fetters,<BR>binding, fettering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडय
निगडय, Nom. P. निगडयति, &c., to put in<BR>irons or fetters, to bind, fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडयित्वा
निगडयित्वा, ind. having fettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडित|निगडितः
नि-गडित, अस्, आ, अम्, chained, bound, tied, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगण|निगणः
निगण नि-गण, अस्, m. the smoke of a burnt<BR>offering or sacrificial fire; [cf. नि-गरण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद्
निगद् नि-गद्, cl. 1. P. -गदति, &c., to<BR>recite, proclaim, declare, communicate, tell, speak,<BR>say, shout out; to speak to, address any one (with<BR>acc.), to tell anything to any one (with two acc.); to<BR>enumerate; to call: Pass. -गद्यते, &c., to be re-<BR>cited, to be named or called: Caus. -गादयति, &c.,<BR>to cause to recite, tell, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद|निगदः
नि-गद or नि-गाद, अस्, m. reciting, audible<BR>recitation of prayers or charms; a prayer or sacrificial<BR>formula recited aloud; mention, mentioning; speech,<BR>speaking, discourse; N. of a teacher with the epithet<BR>Pārṇavalki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदत्
नि-गदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, reciting, addressing,<BR>speaking, saying, speaking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदित
नि-गदित, अस्, आ, अम्, recited, told, said, spoken;<BR>(अम्), n. speech.<BR>—निगदित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one<BR>who has spoken, having spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद्य
नि-गद्य, ind. having told, having declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगाद|निगादः
नि-गाद, अस्, m. speech, discourse, recitation, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगादिन्
नि-गादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, reciting, telling, speaking, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगम्
निगम् नि-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्तुम्,<BR>to settle down upon (Ved.); to enter (acc. or loc.);<BR>inire feminam (Ved.); to go to any place or state,<BR>to undergo, become (e. g. शान्तिं नि-गम्, to be-<BR>come pacified); to be inserted: Caus. -गमयति,<BR>to cause to go in, to insert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगम|निगमः
नि-गम, अस्, m. insertion, especially of the name<BR>of a deity into a liturgical formula; the place or<BR>passage in a book where a word occurs, especially<BR>a passage of the Vedas or the actual word quoted<BR>from such a passage; the Veda or the Vedic text;<BR>the root (as the source from which a word comes);<BR>a sacred precept, the words of a god or holy man;<BR>certainty, assurance; a town, a city; a market, a<BR>fair; a road, a market road; trade, traffic; a camp<BR>or caravan of itinerant merchants, a merchant; =<BR>लुण्डी; (अम्), n. a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमन|निगमनं
नि-गमन, अम्, n. insertion, quotation of words<BR>(from the Veda &c.) or the word &c. quoted; the<BR>conclusion in a syllogism, the deduction; going in<BR>or into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमिन्
निगमिन्, ई, इनी, इ, familiar with or versed in the<BR>Vedas or in holy writ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगर|निगरः
निगर नि-गर, नि-गरण, &c. See नि-गॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगर्ह्
निगर्ह् नि-गर्ह्, cl. 10. P. -गर्हयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to disdain, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगल्
निगल् नि-गल्, cl. 1. P. -गलति, &c., to<BR>fall down (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगल|निगलः
नि-गल, अस्, अम्, m. n. = नि-गड, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगा
निगा नि-गा, cl. 3. P. -जिगाति, &c., to go<BR>into, enter, attach one's self to; to come or get into<BR>any state &c.; to nestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगु|निगुः
निगु नि-गु, उस्, m. = मनस्, the mind, the<BR>faculty of feeling and reasoning; (according to others)<BR>dirt, excrement [cf. rt. 4. गु]; a root; painting;<BR>(उस्, उस्, उ), pleasing, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगुत्
निगुत् नि-गुत्, त्, m. (probably fr. rt. 3. गु<BR>with नि), Ved. (according to Sāy.) an enemy; [cf.<BR>नैगुत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगुह्
निगुह् नि-गुह्, cl. 1. P. A. -गूहति, -ते,<BR>गूहितुम्, to cover, conceal, hide: Caus. -गूहयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to cover or hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढ|निगूढः
नि-गूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, hidden, concealed; profound,<BR>recondite, mysterious, obscure; (अम्), ind. privately,<BR>secretly.<BR>—निगूढ-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, secret in<BR>operation.<BR>—निगूढ-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, well con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">Page0484-b+ 77</a>]<BR>cealed or hidden.<BR>—निगूढ-निश्चय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose resolve or determination is concealed.<BR>—नि-<BR>गूढ-रोमन्, आ, आ, अ, having concealed hair.<BR>—निगूढार्थ (˚ढ-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>hidden sense or purpose, difficult to be understood,<BR>abstruse, occult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढक
नि-गूढक, अस्, m. a species of wild bean; [cf.<BR>वन-मुद्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहक
नि-गूहक, अस्, आ, अम्, hiding, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहन|निगूहनं
नि-गूहन, अम्, n. hiding, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहनीय
नि-गूहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be hidden or con-<BR>cealed; to be covered or protected or defended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
निगृहीत नि-गृहीत. See नि-ग्रह् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगॄ
निगॄ नि-गॄ, cl. 6. P. -गिरति and -गिलति,<BR>&c., to swallow, swallow up, swallow down, ingur-<BR>gitate, devour: Caus. Pass. -गार्यते and -गाल्यते:<BR>Intens., Ved. -जेगिल्यते, -गल्गलीति, to swallow with<BR>a gurgling sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगर|निगरः
नि-गर, अस्, m. swallowing, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरण|निगरणं|निगरणः
नि-गरण, अम्, n. swallowing, devouring, deglu-<BR>tition; (अस्), m. the throat, the gullet, esophagus;<BR>the smoke of a burnt offering; [cf. नि-गण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगलन
नि-गलन = नि-गरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगार|निगारः
नि-गार, अस्, m. swallowing, swallowing down,<BR>devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगारक
नि-गारक, अस्, इका, अम्, = नि-गालक, swallowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगाल|निगालः
नि-गाल, अस्, m. the throat or neck of a horse;<BR>[cf. गल, नि-गरण.]<BR>—निगाल-वत्, आन्, m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालक
नि-गालक, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowing, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीर्ण
नि-गीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, swallowed; (metaphorically)<BR>left out, omitted, not expressed; (अ-निगीर्ण, ex-<BR>pressed.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीर्यमाण
नि-गीर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being swallowed down;<BR>(with act. sense?), swallowing, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगै
निगै नि-गै, cl. 1. P. -गायति, -गातुम्, to<BR>accompany with song; to sing, chant; to proclaim,<BR>announce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीत
नि-गीत, अस्, आ, अम्, sung, chanted; said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रन्थ्
निग्रन्थ् नि-ग्रन्थ्, cl. 9. P. -ग्रथ्नाति, &c.,<BR>to intertwine, interweave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रन्थन|निग्रंथन|निग्रंथनं
नि-ग्रन्थन, अम्, n. (probably a corruption of<BR>नि-क्रन्थन; cf. क्रथ्, क्रथन), killing, de-<BR>stroying, slaughter; [cf. निर्-ग्रन्थन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रह्
निग्रह् नि-ग्रह्, in the older language नि-<BR>ग्रभ्, cl. 9. P. A. -गृभ्णाति, -णीते, -गृह्णाति,<BR>-णीते, -ग्रहीतुम्, to hold down, keep down, de-<BR>press, keep under, keep in check; to keep back,<BR>hold back, stop, obstruct, restrain, suppress, con-<BR>fine; to seize, catch, apprehend, hold, hold fast; to<BR>oppress, overpower, subdue, conquer; to chastise,<BR>punish, tame; to draw together, contract, close (as the<BR>eyes): Caus. -ग्राहयति, to cause to be apprehended<BR>or seized: Caus. of the Desid. -जिघृक्षयति, to<BR>cause any one to desire to keep under or suppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
नि-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, seized, arrested; held<BR>back, restrained, confined, subdued, checked; harassed,<BR>assailed, attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीति|निगृहीतिः
नि-गृहीति, इस्, f. restraint, check; overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीतृ
नि-गृहीतृ, wrong form for नि-ग्रहीतृ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्णत्
नि-गृह्णत्, अन्, अती, अत्, seizing, taking; keeping,<BR>suppressing, restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्य
1. नि-गृह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be held back; to<BR>be punished, punishable; deserving chastisement or<BR>reproof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्य
2. नि-गृह्य, ind. having taken; having arrested<BR>or confined; having restrained or suppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रह|निग्रहः
नि-ग्रह, अस्, m. keeping down, holding down,<BR>keeping under, keeping back, keeping in check,<BR>coercion, restraining, binding, restraint, subjugation,<BR>subduing, restraint of the appetite &c., abstinence;<BR>obstruction, suppression, putting down; seizing,<BR>catching, confinement, capture, arrest; the arresting<BR>or suppressing of disease, cure; taking down, hum-<BR>bling, punishing, punishment, chastisement, rebuke,<BR>rebuff, reprimand, blame; aversion, dislike, disgust;<BR>(in the Nyāya phil.) putting down in argument, fault<BR>in a syllogism, flaw in an argument, failure in proof;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">Page0484-c+ 76</a>]<BR>any place for catching hold of, a handle; a boundary,<BR>a limit; N. of Śiva and of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—निग्रह-स्थान, अम्, n. the predicament of<BR>rebuke for failure in argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहण
नि-ग्रहण, अस्, आ, अम्, holding down, holding<BR>back, suppressing; (अम्), n. subduing, suppression;<BR>capture, confinement, prison; defeat, punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहीतव्य
नि-ग्रहीतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be chastised or<BR>punished, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहीतृ
नि-ग्रहीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who seizes or lays<BR>hold of; one who keeps back or prevents; seizing,<BR>restraining, binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राभ|निग्राभः
नि-ग्राभ, अस्, m., Ved. pressing down; N. of a<BR>verse recited when the Soma plants are pressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राभ्य
नि-ग्राभ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., with आपस्, the water<BR>with which the Soma plants are sprinkled before they<BR>are pressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राह|निग्राहः
नि-ग्राह, अस्, m. punishment, chastisement, (used<BR>in imprecations, e. g. निग्राहस् ते भूयात्, confusion<BR>seize thee, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राह्य
नि-ग्राह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be suppressed or<BR>punished, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ|निघः
निघ नि-घ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. हन् with नि),<BR>as high as broad; (anything) whose height and cir-<BR>cumference are equal; a round or circle, a ball; sin.<BR>—निघानिघ (˚घ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of different<BR>forms or sizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्ट|निघण्टः
निघण्ट नि-घण्ट (said to be fr. rt. गम्<BR>or हन् or हृ with नि; gender doubtful), a word;<BR>a glossary or collection of words or names, (in this<BR>sense properly pl.); often the collection of Vedic words<BR>explained in the Nirukta, see नि-घण्टु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टि
नि-घण्टि, probably only a wrong form for नि-<BR>घण्ट or नि-घण्टु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टिका
नि-घण्टिका, f. a species of bulbous plant (=<BR>गुलञ्च-कन्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टु|निघंटु|निघंटुः|निघण्टुः
नि-घण्टु, उस्, m. (or नि-घण्टुक), any vocabu-<BR>lary or collection of words or names, but especially a<BR>N. of the Vedic glossary explained by Yāska in his<BR>Nirukta, (in this sense usually pl. निघण्टवस् as<BR>embracing five chapters.)<BR>—निघण्टु-भाष्य, अम्,<BR>n. ‘commentary on part of the Nighaṇṭus,’ N. of a<BR>work by Deva-rāja on the three chapters of synonyms<BR>incompletely treated by Yāska.<BR>—निघण्टु-राज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘king of glossaries,’ N. of a medical lexicon<BR>commonly called Abhidhāna-cūḍā-maṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्ष|निघर्षः
निघर्ष नि-घर्ष. See नि-घृष् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघस|निघसः
निघस नि-घस, अस्, m. (fr. rt. घस् with<BR>नि), eating; food, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघात|निघातः
निघात नि-घात, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus. of<BR>rt. हन् with नि), a blow, stroke; suppression of<BR>accent, absence of accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघातम्
नि-घातम्, ind. having struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघाति|निघातिः
नि-घाति, इस्, f. an iron club or mace or hammer (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघातिन्
नि-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, striking down, killing, de-<BR>stroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघुष्
निघुष् नि-घुष् (rt. 2. घुष् = घृष् with<BR>नि), Caus. P. -घोषयति, -यितुम्, to tread down,<BR>trample under foot, crush, pound, grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघुष्ट|निघुष्टं
निघुष्ट नि-घुष्ट, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. घुष्<BR>with नि), sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्
निघृष् नि-घृष्, cl. 1. P. -घर्षति, &c.,<BR>to rub into, rub down, rub, pound, grind, triturate;<BR>graze, chafe, abrade, wear away by rubbing, excoriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्ष|निघर्षः
नि-घर्ष, अस्, m. rubbing, friction, pounding,<BR>crushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षण|निघर्षणं
नि-घर्षण, अम्, n. rubbing, friction, grinding,<BR>trituration; [cf. निर्-घर्षण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्ट
नि-घृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed, ground; chafed,<BR>worn, grazed, abraded, excoriated; subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्व|निघृष्वः
नि-घृष्व, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed off, abraded,<BR>excoriated; small, insignificant; (अस्), m. a hoof;<BR>wind; an ass or a mule; a boar; a road; (अम्), n.<BR>the mark of a hoof (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्न|निघ्नः
निघ्न नि-घ्न, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. नि-हन्), depend-<BR>ant, subservient, docile; dependant on a substantive<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">Page0485-a+ 72</a>]<BR>(as an adjective); (after a numeral) multiplied with;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of An-araṇya and father of An-<BR>amitra; of a son of An-amitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0484-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नक
निघ्न-क, अस्, आ, अम्, = नि-घ्न, dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नत्|निघ्नन्त्
नि-घ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, smiting, slaying, killing,<BR>destroying, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नान
नि-घ्नान, अस्, आ, अम्, slaying, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचक्र
निचक्र नि-चक्र, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचङ्कुण
निचङ्कुण नि-चङ्कुण for नि-चुङ्कुण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचन्द्र
निचन्द्र नि-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचमन
निचमन नि-चमन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. चम् with<BR>नि), sipping, taking liquid into the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचय|निचयः
निचय नि-चय. See under 1. नि-चि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचङ्कुण
निचङ्कुण नि-चङ्कुण for नि-चुङ्कुण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचाय्
निचाय् नि-चाय्, cl. 1. P. -चायति, &c. (oc-<BR>curring only in the form नि-चाय्य), Ved. to regard with<BR>reverence, honour, worship; to see; [cf. rt. 4. चि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचाय्य
नि-चाय्य, ind. having seen, having observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचि
निचि 1. नि-चि, cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति, -चिनुते,<BR>-चेतुम्, to pile up, heap up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचय|निचयः
नि-चय, अस्, m. piling up, heaping up; collection,<BR>heap, multitude, quantity, store, stock, provisions (e. g.<BR>षण्-मास-निचय, provisioned for six months);<BR>assemblage, assemblage or collection of parts con-<BR>stituting a whole (e. g. शरीर-निचय, the assem-<BR>blage of parts of which the body consists; वधू-<BR>निचय, a collection of women); certainty, ascertain-<BR>ment (in this sense for निश्-चय, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयिन्
नि-चयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, heaped up, containing a<BR>quantity, full of, abounding in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचाय|निचायः
नि-चाय, अस्, m. a heap (as a measure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचित|निचितं
नि-चित, अस्, आ, अम्, piled up, heaped up, full of,<BR>filled; covered, overspread; raised up; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a warrior-tribe [cf. नैचित्य]; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचेकाय
नि-चेकाय, अस्, m. (fr. the Intens.), continual or<BR>repeated piling up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचेय
नि-चेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be piled or heaped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचि
निचि 2. नि-चि, cl. 3. P. -चिकेति, -चिकाय,<BR>&c., Ved. to observe, perceive, recognise: Desid.,<BR>Ved. -चिकीषते, to observe, watch, guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिर
नि-चिर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. attentive, observant,<BR>vigilant; (आ), m. du. epithet of Mitra-Varuṇa; (Sāy.)<BR>excessively ancient (= नितरां चिरन्तनौ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचेतृ
नि-चेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. an observer; observing,<BR>paying attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिकी
निचिकी निचिकी, f. an excellent cow (=<BR>नैचिकी, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिर
निचिर नि-चिर. See under 2. नि-चि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुङ्कुण
निचुङ्कुण नि-चुङ्कुण, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. Intens.<BR>of rt. कुण्?), Ved. roaring, murmuring; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a Vāruṇi; (often read नि-चङ्कुण or नि-<BR>चाङ्कुण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुम्पुण|निचुंपुणः|निचुम्पुणः
निचुम्पुण नि-चुम्पुण, अस्, आ, अम्, (rt. चुप्?),<BR>Ved. an epithet of Soma (because, according to Yāska,<BR>निचमनेन प्रीणाति); of the Ava-bhṛtha; of the sea<BR>(because, according to Yāska, निचमनेन पूर्यते);<BR>moving about?; (अस्), m., N. of a Śaunaḥśepha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुल|निचुलः
निचुल नि-चुल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. चुल् with नि),<BR>the tree Barringtonia Acutangula, commonly called<BR>Hijjal, = वेतस; = नि-चोल, an upper garment, over-<BR>coat; (also read नि-चूल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलक|निचुलकं
नि-चुलक, अम्, n. an outer garment; a breast-<BR>plate, a cuirass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोल|निचोलः
नि-चोल, अस्, m. a cover, wrapper, veil, surtout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलक|निचोलकः
नि-चोलक, अस्, m. a sort of jacket, bodice, mantle,<BR>but especially a soldier's jacket serving as a cuirass or<BR>breast-plate; (अम्), n. = नि-चुलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचृत्
निचृत् 1. नि-चृत्, cl. 6. P. -चृतति, -चर्ति-<BR>तुम्, to insert, infix, fix into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचृत्
2. नि-चृत्, त्, f. a defective metre; [cf. अति-न्˚,<BR>नि-वृत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचेरु
निचेरु नि-चेरु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. चर् with नि),<BR>Ved. gliding; creeping; an epithet of the Ava-bhṛtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छवि|निच्छविः|निछवि
निच्छवि निच्छवि, इस्, f., N. of a district (=<BR>तीर-भुक्ति), the modern Tirhut; [cf. लिच्छवि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिद्र
निच्छिद्र नि-च्छिद्र for निश्-छिद्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिवि|निच्छिविः|निछिवि
निच्छिवि निच्छिवि, इस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>degraded castes sprung from the outcast or Vrātya<BR>Kṣatriyas (see Manu X. 22; their occupation appears<BR>to have been the public exhibition of gymnastic<BR>performances &c., as they are classed with the<BR>Jhallas, Mallas, and others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छेद|निच्छेदः
निच्छेद नि-च्छेद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. छिद् with<BR>नि), cutting off; (in arithmetic) leaving no common<BR>measure, reduced by the common divisor to the least<BR>term so as not to allow of further reduction (in<BR>this sense for निश्-छेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज्
निज् निज्, cl. 3. P. A. नेनेक्ति (3rd pl.<BR>नेनिजति), नेनिक्ते, निनेज, निनिजे,<BR>नेक्ता, नेक्ष्यति, -ते, अनिजत्, अनैक्षीत्, अनिक्त,<BR>नेक्तुम्, to wash, clean, cleanse, purify; A. to wash<BR>or clean one's self; to nourish: Pass. निज्यते, &c.,<BR>to be washed: Caus. नेजयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अनीनि-<BR>जत्: Desid. निनिक्षति, -ते: Intens. नेनिज्यते,<BR>नेनिजीति, नेनेक्ति; [cf. rt. निञ्ज्: Zend śnizh, ‘to<BR>snow:’ Gr. νίζ-ω, νίπ-τ-ω, χέρ-νιβ-α (acc.) νίπ-<BR>τρο-ν, νῐ́φ-α (acc.), νιφ-ά(δ)-ς, νῐφ-ετό-ς, νῑ́φει:<BR>Lat. Nep-tūnu-s = νιπτόμενο-ς, ‘bathing;’ ning-<BR>i-t, ningu-i-t, ningu-i-s, nix, base niv for nigv:<BR>Goth. snaivs, ‘snow:’ Old Germ. sneo, ‘snow;’<BR>sniwit, ‘it snows:’ Lith. snig-ti, sning-ti, ‘to<BR>snow;’ snḗg-a-s, ‘snow;’ snaig-alà, ‘a flake of<BR>snow:’ Slav. sne†g-ŭ, ‘snow:’ Hib. nigh-im, ‘I<BR>wash;’ nigh-te, ‘washed,’ = Sanskrit निक्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्त
निक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, washed, cleaned, cleansed,<BR>rinsed; sprinkled.<BR>—निक्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>clean-handed, having clean hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज|निजं
निज नि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. जन् with नि),<BR>innate, native, congenital, indigenous; own, of one's<BR>own party or country; proper, peculiar; continual, per-<BR>petual; (आस्), m. pl. one's own people. नि-ज is used<BR>in later Sanskrit as a reflexive possessive pronoun, like<BR>स्व, for ‘my own,’ ‘his own,’ ‘our own,’ &c.; and<BR>frequently for simple ‘my,’ ‘his,’ ‘our,’ &c.<BR>—निज-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. one's own work, any duty pertaining<BR>to one's self.<BR>—निज-कर्म-बन्धन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, fettered by one's own works.<BR>—निज-घास,<BR>अस्, m. ‘devouring his own,’ N. of a demon.<BR>—निज-<BR>धृति, इस्, f., N. of a river in Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—निज-<BR>मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (according to the commentators)<BR>= स्वभाव-मुक्त, liberated in own nature, essen-<BR>tially liberated (?).<BR>—निज-लाभ-पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>engrossed in self-interest, self-satisfied.<BR>—निज-स्व,<BR>अम्, n. own property.<BR>—निजार्थम् (˚ज-अर्˚), ind.<BR>for one's own sake, for one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजघ्नि
निजघ्नि नि-जघ्नि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. नि-हन्), Ved.<BR>striking down, overpowering; [cf. जघ्नि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजानुका
निजानुका नि-जानुका, f. (fr. नि-जानु), Ved.<BR>shaking or trembling of the knees (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजिघृक्षयत्
निजिघृक्षयत् नि-जिघृक्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्<BR>(Caus. of Desid. of rt. ग्रह् with नि), causing to be<BR>desirous of overpowering or excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजुर्व्
निजुर्व् नि-जुर्व् or नि-जूर्व्, cl. 1. P. -जूर्वति,<BR>&c., to consume by fire; (Sāy.) to destroy, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजुर्
नि-जुर्, ऊर्, f., Ved. killing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजुह्नूषु
निजुह्नूषु नि-जुह्नूषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid.<BR>of rt. ह्नु with नि), wishing to conceal or deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निञ्ज्|निंज्
निञ्ज् निञ्ज्, cl. 2. A. निक्ते, &c., = rt.<BR>निज्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटल|निटलं
निटल नि-टल or नि-टाल, अम्, n. the fore-<BR>head.<BR>—निटलाक्ष (˚ल-अक्ष), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>an eye on the forehead,’ an epithet of Śiva; (incor-<BR>rectly spelt निटिलाक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निडी
निडी नि-डी, cl. 1. 4. A. -डयते and -डीयते,<BR>&c., to fly down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निडीन|निडीनं
नि-डीन, अम्, n. the downward flight or swoop of<BR>a bird or a peculiar mode of flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निणिज्
निणिज् नि-णिज्, क् (according to Sāy. fr. नि-<BR>निज्, to purify), milk; (according to modern scholars<BR>this word may be an adverb related to नि-ण्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्डिका
निण्डिका निण्डिका, f. a species of convol-<BR>vulus, = तिण्डी; (probably wrongly for तिण्डिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्य
निण्य नि-ण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि), Ved. in-<BR>terior, hidden, concealed, secret, mysterious, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda 1. 32, 10, = निर्-नामधेय, nameless,<BR>according to Sāy.); (अम्), n. a secret, a mystery;<BR>(अम्), ind. secretly, mysteriously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितततपम्
नितततपम् नितततपम्, ind., Ved. an ono-<BR>matopoetic word to denote the speech of a stutterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितन्
नितन् नि-तन्, cl. 8. P. A. -तनोति, -नुते,<BR>-तनितुम्, Ved. to pervade, penetrate, pierce; to<BR>cause to grow downwards (as a shoot, root, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितत्नी
नि-तत्नी, f., Ved. a species of plant; N. of an<BR>Iṣṭakā; N. of one of the seven stars of the asterism<BR>Kṛttikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान
नि-तान, अस्, m., Ved. the shoot of a plant which<BR>grows downwards; N. of a man with the patronymic<BR>Māruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितप्
नितप् नि-तप्, cl. 1. P. -तपति, -तप्तुम्,<BR>Ved. to emit heat downwards; to consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्
नितम् नि-तम्, Caus. P. -तमयति, &c., Ved.<BR>to choke, suffocate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्त|नितांत|नितान्तं
नि-तान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, extraordinary, excessive,<BR>exceeding, much, considerable; (अम्), ind. exceed-<BR>ingly, excessively, very, much, in a high degree.<BR>—नितान्तावृक्ष (˚त-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, excessively<BR>treeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्ब|नितंब|नितंबः|नितम्बः
नितम्ब नि-तम्ब, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>तम्ब्, probably connected with rt. स्तम्भ्), the<BR>buttocks or posteriors, especially of a woman, (in<BR>this sense generally नितम्बौ, m. du.); the cir-<BR>cumference of the hip and loins; the ridge or side<BR>or protuberant flank or swell of a mountain [cf. गिरि-<BR>नितम्ब]; a precipice; the sloping bank or shore<BR>of a river; the shoulder; a particular position of the<BR>hands in dancing; (आ), f. a form of Durgā.<BR>—नि-<BR>तम्ब-ता, f. the state of having large hips.<BR>—नि-<BR>तम्ब-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having beautiful buttocks or<BR>hips, καλλίπυγος; (ती), f. a woman.<BR>—नितम्ब-<BR>विम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, having Vimba-like hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बिन्|नितंबिन्
नितम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ (at the end of a comp.),<BR>having buttocks; having beautiful hips; having<BR>graceful slopes, having beautiful sides (as a moun-<BR>tain); (इनी), f. a woman with large and handsome<BR>hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्भू
नितम्भू नितम्भू, ऊस्, m., N. of a person<BR>mentioned in Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 1765; (per-<BR>haps for नित्यम्-भू.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितराम्
नितराम् नि-तराम्, ind. (fr. नि with the<BR>comparative affix), downwards, towards the lower<BR>part (Ved.); in a low tone (Ved.); completely,<BR>wholly, entirely; much, extremely, excessively, in a<BR>high degree; in an especial manner, always, con-<BR>tinually, eternally; at all events; certainly; [cf. Angl.<BR>Sax. nidher; Old Germ. nidar.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितल|नितलं
नितल नि-तल, अम्, n. one of the seven<BR>divisions of the lower regions. See पाताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्त|नितांत|नितान्तं
नितान्त नि-तान्त. See नि-तम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितिक्त
नितिक्त नि-तिक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. तिज् with<BR>नि), Ved. excited, roused up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितिक्ति
नि-तिक्ति, इस्, f., Ved. excitement, haste, speed;<BR>(इ), ind. quickly, speedily; (Sāy.) = 3rd sing. Pres.<BR>of rt. तिज् = तीक्ष्णी-करोति, he sharpens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0485-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितुद्
नितुद् नि-तुद्, cl. 6. P. A. -तुदति, -ते, -तोत्-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to pierce, penetrate, pierce into; to goad;<BR>(Sāy.) to incite or pain vehemently, or to issue forth<BR>(= नितरां व्यथयति or निर्-गच्छति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितोद
नि-तोद, अस्, m. piercing, a prick, puncture, hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितोदिन्
नि-तोदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. piercing, penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितृद्
नितृद् नि-तृद्, cl. 7. P. A. -तृणत्ति, -तृन्त्ते,<BR>-तर्दितुम्, Ved. to pierce, penetrate, cleave in two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितॄ
नितॄ नि-तॄ, cl. 6. P. -तिरति, -तरितुम्, -त-<BR>रीतुम्, Ved. to dispel, subdue, overpower, obstruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितोशन
नितोशन नि-तोशन, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. तुश्<BR>with नि), Ved. sprinkling, distributing, granting;<BR>(अस्), m. a distributer, granter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य नित्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि), own (Ved.);<BR>continual, perpetual, regularly repeated, constant,<BR>uninterrupted, endless, eternal, everlasting; invariable,<BR>regular, fixed, regularly prescribed, inevitable, not op-<BR>tional, (opposed to काम्य &c.); necessary, obligatory,<BR>essential; ordinary, usual, (opposed to नैमित्तिक,<BR>unusual, produced by an unusual cause); constantly<BR>dwelling in, perpetually engaged in, (often at the end<BR>of a comp., e. g. अरण्य-नित्य, constantly dwelling<BR>in a forest; तपो-नित्य, engaged in constant penance);<BR>(with समास) a necessary compound which cannot<BR>be resolved without losing its meaning, because the<BR>separate ideas have merged in one, as in जमद्-अग्नि;<BR>(with स्वरित) = जात्य, the primary or independent<BR>Svarita, as opposed to the secondary or dependent;<BR>(अस्), m. the ocean; (आ), f. an epithet of Durgā; a<BR>Śakti or form of Durgā; an epithet of the goddess Ma-<BR>nasā; (अम्), n. constant and indispensable rite or act;<BR>(अम्), ind. always, ever, daily, constantly, continually,<BR>perpetually, everlastingly, eternally; न नित्यम्, not<BR>always, never, (in Manu VI. 8. नित्यम् अन्-आदाता =<BR>never a receiver.)<BR>—नित्य-कर्मन्, अ, n. or नित्य-<BR>क्रिया, f. constant act or duty, as observance of the<BR>five great sacrifices or any daily and necessary rite.<BR>—नित्य-कृत्य, अम्, n. regular and necessary act<BR>or ceremony; daily or regular act or routine.<BR>—नित्य-<BR>गति, इस्, इस्, इ, moving continually; (इस्), m. air or<BR>wind, the god of wind.<BR>—नित्य-जात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>constantly born.<BR>—नित्य-ता, f. perpetuity, eternity,<BR>continuance, continual repetition, (as मैथुन-<BR>नित्यता, continually repeated coitus); perseverance;<BR>necessity.<BR>—नित्य-त्व, अम्, n. invariableness, per-<BR>petuity, eternity; endurance; inevitableness, neces-<BR>sity.<BR>—नित्य-दा, ind. always, ever, perpetually, con-<BR>stantly, eternally, at all times.<BR>—नित्य-दान, अम्, n.<BR>daily alms-giving.<BR>—नित्य-धृत्, त्, त्, त्, constantly<BR>bearing or maintaining, observing daily duties (?).<BR>—नित्य-धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, constantly maintained<BR>or kept up.<BR>—नित्य-नाथ-सिद्ध, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an author.<BR>—नित्य-नियम, अस्, m. fixed rule,<BR>constant observance.<BR>—नित्य-नैमित्तिक, अम्, or<BR>नित्य-नैमित्तिकं कर्म, n. any regularly re-<BR>curring occasional act or ceremony or any rite con-<BR>stantly performed to accomplish some object, as<BR>Śrāddhas at fixed lunar periods.<BR>—नित्य-परिवृत,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—नित्य-परीक्षण, अम्,<BR>n. constant investigation or inspection.<BR>—नित्य-पूजा-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a kind of amulet.<BR>—नित्य-प्रलय,<BR>अस्, m. the constant dissolution of living beings.<BR>—नित्य-भाव, अस्, m. the state of being eternal,<BR>eternity.<BR>—नित्य-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed of or<BR>consisting of anything eternal, eternal.<BR>—नित्य-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, always busy, ever engaged in.<BR>—नित्य-यौवन, अम्, n. perpetual youth; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), ever or always young; (आ), f. an epithet of<BR>Draupadī.<BR>—नित्यर्तु (˚य-ऋ), उस्, उस्, उ, regularly<BR>recurring at the seasons, annual.<BR>—नित्य-वत्स, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. always possessing a calf; (आ), f. a par-<BR>ticular form of Sāma supplication; (अम्), n., N. of<BR>several Sāmans.<BR>—नित्य-वित्रस्त, अस्, m. ‘constantly<BR>scared,’ N. of an antelope.<BR>—नित्य-वैकुण्ठ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular residence of Viṣṇu, the<BR>heaven of Viṣṇu.<BR>—नित्य-व्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, always<BR>expending, constantly disbursing; (आ), f. always ex-<BR>pending, ever laying out.<BR>—नित्य-शङ्कित, अस्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">Page0486-b+ 75</a>]<BR>अम्, perpetually alarmed, always suspicious.<BR>—नित्य-<BR>शय, अस्, आ, अम्, always sleeping or reclining.<BR>—नित्य-<BR>शस्, ind. always, continually, constantly, eternally.<BR>—नित्य-संहृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, always exulting<BR>or triumphant; always rivalling one another, (in this<BR>sense संहृष्ट = सङ्घृष्ट.)<BR>—नित्य-सम,<BR>अस्, m. the assertion that all things remain the same (?).<BR>—नित्य-समास, see नित्य.<BR>—नित्य-सिद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘ever perfect,’ a Jaina predicate of the soul.<BR>—नित्य-स्तोत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. receiving perpetual<BR>praise, constantly lauded.<BR>—नित्य-स्नायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>constantly bathing or making ablutions.<BR>—नित्यान-<BR>ध्याय (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, m. invariable suspension of<BR>repetition of the Vedas, (a term applied to periods<BR>when the perusal of the Vedas is invariably prohibited,<BR>as the day of full moon, new moon, the eighth and<BR>fourteenth days of the half month.)<BR>—नित्यानन्द<BR>(˚य-आन्˚), अस्, m. eternal happiness.<BR>—नित्यानन्द-<BR>रसोदधि (˚स-उद्˚), इस्, m. ‘ocean of the essence of<BR>eternal joy,’ God.<BR>—नित्यानन्दाश्रम (˚द-आश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentator.<BR>—नित्यानित्य (˚य-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, eternal and perishable, permanent and<BR>temporary.<BR>—नित्यायुक्त (˚य-आय्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Bodhi-sattva; (also read नित्योयुक्त; cf. नित्यो-<BR>द्युक्त.)<BR>—नित्यारित्र (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having (its) own oars, ever fitted with oars (i. e.<BR>according to Sāy. with priests).<BR>—नित्योत्क्षिप्त-<BR>हस्त (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, m. ‘who always raises his hand,’<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—नित्योदित (˚य-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—नित्योद्युक्त (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva; [cf. नित्यायुक्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यज्
नित्यज् नि-त्यज्, cl. 1. P. -त्यजति, -त्यक्तुम्,<BR>Ved. to scare or drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
निद् 1. निद्, cl. 1. P. A. नेदति, नेदते,<BR>निनेद, निनिदे or निनेदे, नेदिता, &c.,<BR>to be near [cf. rt. नेद्, नेदीयस्, नेदिष्ठ]; to<BR>ridicule, blame, reproach, censure, &c., (in this sense<BR>properly a separate rt., the form of which is usually<BR>निन्द्, q. v.): Desid., Ved. निनित्सति, to wish to<BR>reproach or depreciate; [cf. rt. निन्द्; Gr. ὄ-νειδ-<BR>ο-ς, probably λοίδ-ο-ρο-ς; Goth. ga-nait-yan, nai-<BR>teins, probably neith; Old Germ. neiz-yan; Angl.<BR>Sax. naet-an, naet-ing, nidh, ge-nidhe, ‘hatred;’<BR>Mod. Germ. neid, ‘envy.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
2. निद्, त्, f., Ved. mocking, ridiculing, despising,<BR>censure, contempt; (त्), m. one who ridicules or con-<BR>temns, a blamer, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदा
1. निदा, f., Ved. blame, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदान|निदानं
1. निदान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (= निद्यमान),<BR>reproached, ridiculed. (For 2. see 3. नि-दा, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्यमान
निद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being reproached, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद नि-द, अम्, n. (said to be fr. नि-दो),<BR>poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदण्ड
निदण्ड नि-दण्ड, अस्, m., according to a<BR>commentator = निहित-दण्ड, a stick put aside or laid<BR>down; (अस्, आ, अम्), one who has put down a stick<BR>(i. e. not using force), one who has laid down a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदत्त
निदत्त नि-दत्त. See 2. नि-दा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदद्रु|निदद्रुः
निदद्रु निद-द्रु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. निद<BR>+ द्रु), a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
निदर्शन नि-दर्शन. See नि-दृश्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदह्
निदह् नि-दह्, cl. 1. P. -दहति, -दग्धुम्,<BR>to burn down, consume by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघ|निदाघः
नि-दाघ, अस्, m. (according to native lexicogra-<BR>phers also अम्, n.), heat, warmth; the hot season<BR>(May and June), summer; internal heat, sweat,<BR>perspiration; N. of a man; N. of a son of Pulastya;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the descendants of the former person.<BR>—निदाघ-कर, अस्, m. ‘heat causer’ or ‘hot-<BR>rayed,’ the sun.<BR>—निदाघ-काल, अस्, m. ‘the time<BR>of heat,’ the hot season, two months previous to the<BR>rains, about May and June.<BR>—निदाघ-सिन्धु, उस्,<BR>m. a river in hot weather, one nearly dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदा
निदा 2. नि-दा (rt. 1. दा), cl. 3. P. -ददाति,<BR>&c., Ved. to give. (For 1. निदा see above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदत्त
नि-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, given, given absolutely; [cf.<BR>नीत्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदा
निदा 3. नि-दा (rt. 4. दा, to bind), cl. 4. P.<BR>-द्यति, &c., Ved. to fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदातृ
नि-दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who fastens or ties<BR>up; (Sāy.) a restrainer, obstructer, (as if fr. rt. 3. दा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदान|निदानं
2. नि-दान, अम्, n. (for 1. निदान see col. 2),<BR>a band, a rope, a halter; a rope for tying up a calf<BR>&c.; a first or original cause, a primary or remote<BR>cause [cf. नि-बन्धन]; original form, essence,<BR>(निदानेन, ind. originally, essentially, properly);<BR>the cause of a disease, inquiry into the causes of<BR>disease, pathology, i. e. study of the symptoms with<BR>a view to trace the remote or proximate causes, (re-<BR>garded as a department of medical science; the six-<BR>teen Nidānas being the title of the sixteen divisions<BR>into which it is divided; cf. निदान-स्थान); N.<BR>of a work on metres and Vedic Stomas (see निदान-<BR>सूत्र); end, termination, cessation; purification,<BR>purity, correctness; claiming the reward of peni-<BR>tential acts.<BR>—निदान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. founded<BR>on a cause, essential.<BR>—निदान-सूत्र, अम्, n. a work<BR>in ten Prapāṭhakas on metres and Vedic Stomas.<BR>—निदान-स्थान, अम्, n. one of the five depart-<BR>ments of medical science, inquiry into the causes of<BR>diseases, pathology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदित
नि-दित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. preserved, concealed;<BR>(Sāy.) completely bound or fettered (= नितराम्<BR>बद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघ|निदाघः
निदाघ नि-दाघ. See नि-दह्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्ध|निदिग्धं
निदिग्ध नि-दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. दिह्<BR>with नि), smeared, anointed, plastered; clinging to;<BR>(आ), f. small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्धिका
निदिग्धिका, f. = कण्ट-कारिका, a species of prickly<BR>nightshade, Solanum Jacquini [cf. निर्-दिग्धिका, निर्-<BR>दग्धिका]; cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासन|निदिध्यासनं
निदिध्यासन नि-दिध्यासन, अम्, n. (fr. the<BR>Desid. of rt. ध्यै), profound and repeated medi-<BR>tation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासु
नि-दिध्यासु, उस्, उस्, उ, desiring to meditate upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्येय
नि-दिध्येय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be deeply meditated<BR>upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिश्
निदिश् नि-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति, -देष्टुम्,<BR>to order, point out, &c.; (perhaps for निर्-दिश् and<BR>apparently only used in the derivatives below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिष्ट
नि-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, ordered, directed; advised,<BR>enjoined; explained, pointed out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेश|निदेशः
नि-देश, अस्, m. order, command, direction, in-<BR>struction; speech, speaking, narration, conversation;<BR>vicinity, proximity, neighbourhood; = भाजन, a<BR>vessel, vase; (ए), ind. in the vicinity, near.<BR>—निदेश-<BR>कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, executing orders, obedient, servile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशिन्
नि-देशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, showing, directing, ordering,<BR>pointing out; (इनी), f. a region, quarter, point of<BR>the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेश्य
नि-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ordered, to be told.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेष्टृ
नि-देष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, who or what points out<BR>or orders; explaining, advising, commanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदी
निदी नि-दी, cl. 3. P. (see rt. 2. दी), Ved.<BR>to shine down upon; (Sāy. = नितराम् प्र-काश्, to<BR>shine exceedingly.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदुश
निदुश निदुश, अस्, m. a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदृश्
निदृश् नि-दृश्, Caus. -दर्शयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to see, to show, point, to point out; to<BR>introduce, cause to enter; to impart knowledge,<BR>communicate, teach; advise; to appear (in a vision)<BR>to any person (acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शक
नि-दर्शक, अस्, आ, अम्, seeing into, perceiving;<BR>seeing; pointing out, proclaiming, announcing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
नि-दर्शन, अस्, ई, अम्, pointing to, showing,<BR>foreshowing, prognosticating, indicating; proclaim-<BR>ing, announcing, teaching; suiting, pleasing?; (आ),<BR>f. a simile, a comparison; (अम्), n. seeing, look-<BR>ing into, view, insight, sight, vision (e. g. स्वप्न-<BR>निदर्शन, a vision in sleep); pointing to; showing;<BR>evidence; an example or illustration; a designation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">Page0487-a+ 78</a>]<BR>of the third member of a complete syllogism (usually<BR>called उद्-आहरण, q. v.); a foreboding, prognostic,<BR>sign, mark, omen; a scheme, system; injunction, pre-<BR>cept, ordinance, scriptural authority; authority, text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शित
नि-दर्शित, अस्, आ, अम्, illustrated, exemplified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शिन्
नि-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, seeing, viewing, having an<BR>insight into, familiar with, knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेश|निदेशः
निदेश नि-देश. See नि-दिश्, p. 486, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा 1. नि-द्रा or नि-द्रै, cl. 1. 2. P. A.<BR>-द्रायति, -ते, -द्राति, &c., to fall asleep, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
2. नि-द्रा, f. (said to be fr. rt. निन्द् + affix र),<BR>sleep, slumber, sleepiness, sloth; (in flowers the<BR>budding state is considered as sleep. hence निद्रां<BR>त्यज् = to bloom); a mystical N. of the letter भ्.<BR>—निद्रा-दरिद्र, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—निद्रान्-<BR>ध (˚रा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blind with sleep.<BR>—नि-<BR>द्रा-भङ्ग, अस्, m. rousing from sleep, awaking;<BR>[cf. भग्न-निद्र.]<BR>—निद्रा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting in sleep.<BR>—निद्रा-योग, अस्, m. sleep<BR>and deep meditation; [cf. योग-निद्रा.]<BR>—निद्रा-<BR>लस (˚रा-अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, slothful from drowsi-<BR>ness, fast asleep, sleepy.<BR>—निद्रा-वृक्ष, अस्, m.<BR>darkness.<BR>—निद्रा-सञ्जनन, अम्, n. ‘producing<BR>drowsiness,’ phlegm, the phlegmatic humor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राण|निद्राणः
नि-द्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping, asleep, sleepy,<BR>drowsy; shut up, closed (as a bud or blossom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रात्
नि-द्रात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत्, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रायमाण
नि-द्रायमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping, asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालु|निद्रालुः
नि-द्रालु, उस्, उस्, उ, sleeping, sleepy, drowsy,<BR>slothful; (उस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; (उस्), f. the<BR>plant Solanum Melongena; another plant (= वन-<BR>वर्वरिका); a kind of perfume (= नली).<BR>—नि-<BR>द्रालु-त्व, अम्, n. sleepiness, drowsiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रित
निद्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping, asleep.<BR>—निद्रित-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधन|निधनं|निधनः
निधन नि-धन, अम्, n. (in some senses<BR>apparently fr. 1. नि-धा below, but in others more<BR>probably fr. धन् = rt. हन्, to kill, with नि; cf.<BR>प्र-धन), settling down in a residence, residence,<BR>place of residence, domicile, resting-place, receptacle<BR>(Ved.); race, family; conclusion, end; dying, death,<BR>destruction, loss, disappearance, annihilation, (in<BR>these senses also rarely नि-धनस्, m., see Hari-<BR>vaṃśa 4846); the concluding passage or words at<BR>the end of a Sāman which is sung in chorus, (several<BR>words are used for this purpose, e. g. स्वर्-ज्योतिः,<BR>वषट्, व्रतम्, ईम्, नाम्, &c.); the finale in music;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of the eighth mansion; (अस्), m. the<BR>head of a family; (अस्, आ, अम्), without money,<BR>poor, (in this sense for निर्-धन); [cf. rt. हन्;<BR>Gr. θάν-α-το-ς; Hib. nidh, nith, ‘manslaughter,<BR>battle.’]<BR>—निधन-काम, अम्, n., Ved., N. of several<BR>Sāmans.<BR>—निधन-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, causing death,<BR>destroying, destructive.<BR>—निधन-क्रिया, f. a funeral<BR>ceremony.<BR>—निधन-ता, f. poverty, indigence.<BR>—निधन-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the end or<BR>of destruction.<BR>—निधन-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>become final or like a finale in music.<BR>—निधन-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a finale in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधा
निधा 1. नि-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, -धातुम्, to put down, lay down, put or<BR>lay into, fix in, deposit, lodge, bury; (with मनस्)<BR>to fix or direct the thoughts upon or towards<BR>(dat.); resolve, determine; (with क्रियाम्) to direct<BR>one's labours, use efforts; to appoint; to lay aside,<BR>put away, remove, relinquish; lay up, treasure up,<BR>put into a safe place; to preserve for one's self (A.);<BR>to deliver, intrust, commit, present; (with हृदये<BR>or मनसि) to keep in mind, bear in mind, re-<BR>member, lay to heart, keep close; to keep down,<BR>keep back, restrain; to end, close; to place in any<BR>state, render: Pass. -धीयते, to be place on or in,<BR>to be deposited, be situated in or on, be absorbed<BR>into, to rest in: Caus. -धापयति, &c., to cause to<BR>be put or laid on or into, to cause to be deposited<BR>or preserved; to appoint: Intens. (?), Ved. 3rd sing.<BR>-देध्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधा
2. नि-धा, f., Ved. laying snares; a net; a collection<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">Page0487-b+ 79</a>]<BR>of snares, a snare.<BR>—निधा-पति, इस्, m. the possessor<BR>or bearer of snares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधातव्य
नि-धातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be put down or de-<BR>posited; to be delivered; to be directed towards; to<BR>be concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधातृ
नि-धातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. a depositor, one who<BR>deposits, keeps, conceals, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधान|निधानं
नि-धान, अम्, n. putting down, laying down,<BR>depositing, (दण्ड-निधान, putting down or laying<BR>aside the stick, i. e. not using force, = mildness,<BR>clemency); keeping, preserving; a place where any-<BR>thing is laid, a vessel in which anything is deposited,<BR>a receptacle; a place of cessation or rest; anything<BR>laid up, a treasure, a divine treasure (especially be-<BR>longing to Kuvera, god of wealth); store, hoard,<BR>property, possessions, wealth.<BR>—निधानेश (˚न-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of treasure,’ a Yakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधान्य
नि-धान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fit for being laid<BR>or put down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधापक
नि-धापक, अस्, m. one who causes to be put<BR>down or deposited; a weapon (?); burnt timber (?),<BR>charcoal (?); the castor-oil plant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधाप्य
नि-धाप्य, ind. having caused to be placed or<BR>fixed in, having installed or appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधाय
नि-धाय, ind. having fixed or placed in or on,<BR>(मनसि निधाय, fixing or laying up in the mind,<BR>reflecting.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधि|निधिः
नि-धि, इस्, m. setting down or serving up food<BR>&c. (Ved.); the lower part or bottom of the Ukhā<BR>(Ved.); a place where anything is laid or deposited,<BR>a receptacle, (अपां निधिः, the receptacle of waters,<BR>the ocean, sea; also N. of a Sāman; sometimes<BR>निधि alone stands for ‘the ocean’); a place for<BR>storing up, a storehouse, treasury, granary, a nest, &c.;<BR>(figuratively) a treasure-house of good qualities, a<BR>man endowed with many good qualities; a treasure,<BR>store, hoard, any collection of wealth or valuables;<BR>a divine treasure belonging to Kuvera, (nine of which<BR>are enumerated, viz. the Padma, Mahā-padma,<BR>Śaṅkha, Makara, Kacchapa, Mukunda, Nanda, Nīla,<BR>and Kharba; their nature is not exactly defined,<BR>though some of them appear to be precious gems;<BR>according to the Tāntrika system they are personified<BR>and worshipped as demi-gods, attendant either upon<BR>Kuvera who is sometimes called निधीनम् अधि-<BR>पः, ‘lord of the Nidhis,’ or upon Lakṣmī, the<BR>goddess of prosperity); N. of a particular medicinal<BR>plant, commonly Jīvikā; a kind of perfume (=<BR>नलिका); दैवो निधिः, ‘the divine treasure,’ N. of<BR>a particular philosophical doctrine.<BR>—निधि-गोप,<BR>अस्, m. guardian of treasure.<BR>—निधि-नाथ, अस्, m.<BR>or निधि-प्रभु, उस्, m. or निधीश्वर (˚धि-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of treasures,’ an epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—निधि-प, अस्, m. guardian of treasure; [cf.<BR>निधि-पा.]<BR>—निधि-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of treasures,’<BR>an epithet of Kuvera; N. of a rich merchant.<BR>—निधिपति-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—निधि-पा, आस्, Ved., or निधि-पाल, अस्, m.<BR>guardian of treasure.<BR>—निधि-पालित, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a merchant.<BR>—निधि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. pos-<BR>sessing treasure, forming a store.<BR>—निधीश or नि-<BR>धीश्वर (˚धि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of treasures,’ an<BR>epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—निध्य्-अर्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, treasure<BR>seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधीयमान
नि-धीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being laid down or<BR>deposited, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधेय
नि-धेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be placed in or on, to<BR>be deposited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहित|निहितं
नि-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, put down, deposited, &c.<BR>See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधि|निधिः
निधि नि-धि. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधू
निधू नि-धू, cl. 5. 6. P. A. -धूनोति, -धू-<BR>नुते (in the later language also -धुनोति, -धुनुते),<BR>-धुवति, -धोतुम्, -धवितुम्, to throw down, give<BR>or deliver over (Ved.); shake to and fro, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधुवन|निधुवनं
नि-धुवन, अम्, n. shaking about, agitation,<BR>trembling; coition, sexual intercourse; pleasure, en-<BR>joyment; sport, play, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधृ
निधृ नि-धृ, cl. 10. P. -धारयति, -यितुम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">Page0487-c+ 73</a>]<BR>(Ved. -दीधर्), to place down or in, deposit in;<BR>determine; establish; render (Ved.); to keep, pre-<BR>serve; (Sāy.) to establish firmly; to conceive in the<BR>womb: Pass. -धार्यते (Ved. -दध्रे), to be placed<BR>in or deposited; to bend down, to stoop (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधारय
नि-धारय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. placing in or on,<BR>depositing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधारयत्
नि-धारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, (Sāy.) abiding in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधृति
नि-धृति, इस्, m., N. of a prince, a son of Vṛṣṇi;<BR>[cf. निर्-वृति, नि-वृत्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यै
निध्यै नि-ध्यै, cl. 1. P. -ध्यायति, -ध्या-<BR>तुम्, to observe, perceive (Ved.); to meditate on,<BR>be absorbed in meditation; to think of, reflect on;<BR>remember: Desid. -दिध्यासति, -ते, to wish to<BR>meditate on; think of attentively (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासन|निदिध्यासनं
नि-दिध्यासन, अम्, n. profound meditation,<BR>deep and repeated consideration, thinking of or re-<BR>calling repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासितव्य
नि-दिध्यासितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be reflected or<BR>meditated upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासु
नि-दिध्यासु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of meditating on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यात
नि-ध्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, meditated on, thought on,<BR>imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यान|निध्यानं
नि-ध्यान, अम्, n. intuition, looking at, seeing,<BR>beholding, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्रुव
निध्रुव नि-ध्रुव, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. his descendants; [cf. नैध्रुव, नै-<BR>ध्रुवि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्रुवि
निध्रुवि नि-ध्रुवि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. constant,<BR>persevering, faithful; (इस्), m., N. of a Kāśyapa and<BR>author of a Ṛg-veda hymn (IX. 63).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्वान|निध्वानः
निध्वान नि-ध्वान, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. ध्वन्<BR>with नि), sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनङ्क्षु|निनंक्षु
निनङ्क्षु निनङ्क्षु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. 2. नश्), wishing or expecting to perish or die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनद्
निनद् नि-नद्, cl. 1. P. -नदति, &c., to<BR>sound, make a sound, cry out; to resound: Caus.<BR>P. -नादयति, -यितुम्, to cause to sound or resound,<BR>fill with noise, cries, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनद|निनदः
नि-नद or नि-नाद, अस्, m. sound, noise, cry,<BR>buzzing, humming, crying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादित
नि-नादित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to sound, filled with<BR>noise or cries; (अम्), n. a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादिन्
नि-नादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding, resounding, ringing,<BR>crying; causing to sound, playing (as a musical<BR>instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनयन|निनयनं
निनयन नि-नयन. See नि-नी below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनर्तशत्रु|निनर्त्तशत्रु
निनर्तशत्रु निनर्त-शत्रु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of An-ādhṛṣṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनर्द्
निनर्द् नि-नर्द्, cl. 1. P. -नर्दति, -नर्दि-<BR>तुम्, to sound; prolong a note in chanting; [cf.<BR>अव-नर्द्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनर्द|निनर्दः
नि-नर्द, अस्, m. prolonging a note in chanting,<BR>trilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनर्दत्
नि-नर्दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sounding; prolonging<BR>a cadence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनह्
निनह् नि-नह्, cl. 4. P. A. -नह्यति, -ते,<BR>-नद्धुम्, Ved. to fasten, tie; [cf. नीनाह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनद्ध
नि-नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened, tied fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनाह्य|निनाह्यः
नि-नाह्य, अस्, m., Ved. a water-jar; (according to<BR>the commentaries) a water-jar put into the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनित्सु
निनित्सु निनित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>निद्), Ved. wishing to censure or blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनी
निनी नि-नी, cl. 1. P. A. -नयति, -ते, -ने-<BR>तुम्, to lead to, carry or bring towards, bring near,<BR>bring, fetch; to incline, bend; to pour on or into<BR>(Ved.); to carry out, perform, accomplish, cause; to<BR>spend (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनयन|निनयनं
नि-नयन, अम्, n. carrying out, performing,<BR>accomplishing; performance; pouring down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनीषा
निनीषा निनीषा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. 1. नी),<BR>wishing to bring, desire or intention of carrying or<BR>taking or leading away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनीषु
निनीषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous to take or lead, wishing<BR>to bring; wishing to spend (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनृत्त
निनृत्त नि-नृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, repeated (as a<BR>portion of a verse or syllable; lit. danced again).<BR>—निनृत्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having repetition (as<BR>above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनृत्ति|निनृत्तिः
नि-नृत्ति, इस्, f. repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द्|निंद्
निन्द् निन्द् (sometimes written निद्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 1. P. निन्दति (rarely A. -ते), निनिन्द,<BR>निन्दिष्यति, अनिन्दीत्, निन्दितुम्, to blame, censure,<BR>reprimand, contemn, despise, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द
निन्द in निन्द-तल, अस्, ई, अम्, = निन्दित-<BR>हस्त, having a maimed or defective hand; (some-<BR>times read निम्न-तल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दक|निंदक|निन्दकः
निन्दक, अस्, आ, अम्, blaming, defaming, re-<BR>proachful, abusive, scurrilous, censorious; one who<BR>ridicules or blames, a scorner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दत्
निन्दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, blaming, censuring, abusing,<BR>ridiculing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दन|निंदन|निंदनं|निन्दनं
निन्दन, अम्, n. reproach, censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दनीय
निन्दनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, blamable, liable to reproof<BR>or censure or blame, reprehensible; [cf. अ-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दा|निंदा
निन्दा, f. blame, censure, reproach, reproof, abuse,<BR>defamation, scorn, reviling; injury, injuring, wicked-<BR>ness; [cf. निदा.]<BR>—निन्दा-स्तुति, इस्, f. praise which<BR>involves reproof, ironical praise, irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दित|निंदित|निन्दितः
निन्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, blamed, abused, reviled,<BR>reproved, despised, rejected; low, despicable, worthy<BR>of being reviled; prohibited, forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दितृ
निन्दितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who ridicules or<BR>blames or despises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दिन्
निन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, blaming, censuring, reproaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दु|निंदु|निंदुः|निन्दुः
निन्दु, उस्, f. a woman bearing a dead child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द्य|निंद्य
निन्द्य, अस्, आ, अम्, blamable, to be censured or<BR>reproached, despicable, reprehensible, bad, vile; for-<BR>bidden, prohibited; [cf. अ-न्.]<BR>—निन्द्य-ता, f. or<BR>निन्द्य-त्व, अम्, n. blamableness, infamy, con-<BR>temptibleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्व्
निन्व् निन्व् (or according to some सिन्व्),<BR>cl. 1. P. निन्वति, &c., to wet or sprinkle;<BR>or to attend, wait on, worship ?; (the two mean-<BR>ings have probably arisen from a confusion between<BR>सेचने and सेवने.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप|निपं|निपः
निप नि-प. See under 2. नि-पा, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपक्षति
निपक्षति नि-पक्षति, इस्, f., Ved. the<BR>second rib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठ|निपठः
निपठ नि-पठ, अस्, m. or निपठन, अम्, n.<BR>(fr. rt. पठ् with नि), reading, recitation, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठित
नि-पठित, अस्, आ, अम्, read, recited, studied,<BR>(hence निपठितिन्, Pāṇ. V. 2, 88.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठिति|निपठितिः
नि-पठिति, इस्, f. reading, recitation, study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाठ|निपाठः
नि-पाठ, अस्, m. = नि-पठ, reading, study of the<BR>sacred books or public perusal of popular poems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्
निपत् नि-पत्, cl. 1. P. -पतति, -पतितुम्, to<BR>fly down, fall down, tumble down, settle down, fall,<BR>descend, alight, throw one's self down; to fall upon,<BR>throw one's self upon, assault, assail, fall into, rush<BR>into, rush in, flow in, disembogue into, discharge<BR>into; fall into ruin; to fall into (any state or con-<BR>dition); to fall into (a place), enter, insert one's self,<BR>become fixed in; to befall, happen, take place; to<BR>fall to the share of (with loc.): Caus. -पातयति,<BR>-अपीपतत्, -यितुम्, to cause to fall down, throw<BR>down, fell, cast down, cause to fall on (e. g. to cause<BR>a stick to fall on any one = strike with a stick); to<BR>hurl down; to cast, throw, hurl, throw into; to let in,<BR>inlay, emboss; to direct (the eyes &c.) upon; to spit<BR>on, spit out; to ruin, kill, destroy (with abl.); to<BR>raise or levy a tribute from (with करान् and abl. c.,<BR>in Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 3313); (in grammar) to put<BR>down as a special or irregular form, to give as an<BR>irregularity, consider as anomalous or irregular; (नि-<BR>पात्यते is put down or mentioned as a special rule<BR>or irregular form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतत्
नि-पतत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, flying down, falling down,<BR>falling, descending, alighting, prostrating one's self, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतन|निपतनं
नि-पतन, अम्, n. flying down, falling down,<BR>falling, descending; alighting, flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतित
नि-पतित, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen down, fallen; de-<BR>scended, alighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्य
नि-पत्य, ind. having fallen down, having pros-<BR>trated one's self, having descended or alighted.<BR>—नि-<BR>पत्य-रोहिणी, f. falling and ascending (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्या
नि-पत्या, f. any slippery ground; a field of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपात|निपातः
नि-पात, अस्, m. falling down, falling, descending,<BR>coming down, alighting; falling upon, attacking;<BR>casting, hurling; death, dying; accidental occurrence<BR>or mention; putting down as irregular or exceptional,<BR>irregular form, irregularity (e. g. पूर्व-निपात,<BR>irregular occurrence of a word at the beginning<BR>instead of at the end of a compound; पर-निपात,<BR>irregular placing of a word at the end instead of<BR>beginning); the opposite extremity, the lower end;<BR>(in grammar) a particle, the term for all adverbs in-<BR>cluding conjunctions and interjections, (called निपात<BR>as falling into the sentence in various senses, i. e.<BR>taking their place after other words to modify the<BR>sense in various ways.)<BR>—निपात-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being a particle.<BR>—निपात-प्रतीकार, अस्,<BR>m. the repelling of assaults.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातक|निपातकः
नि-पातक, अस्, अम्, m. n. = पातक, a bad deed,<BR>a sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातन|निपातनं
नि-पातन, अस्, आ, अम्, throwing down, overthrow-<BR>ing, killing, destroying; (अम्), n. causing to descend<BR>or fall, throwing down, overthrowing; beating,<BR>knocking down; putting on; touching with; killing,<BR>destroying; (in grammar) putting down as an irre-<BR>gularity, accidental mention or use of a word; a form<BR>which by its rare occurrence shows itself to be irre-<BR>gular; irregularity, exception; falling down, hurrying<BR>down, flying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातनीय
नि-पातनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cast down or over-<BR>thrown, caused to fall (e. g. दण्डो निपातनीयस्,<BR>the stick must be caused to fall, punishment must<BR>be inflicted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातित
नि-पातित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to fall or descend;<BR>beaten down; killed; irregular, excepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातिन्
नि-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling down, flying down or on,<BR>alighting; striking down, destroying, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपात्य
नि-पात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cast down or over-<BR>thrown; to be put down or mentioned as an irregu-<BR>larity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपात्यमान
नि-पात्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being thrown down,<BR>being precipitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपलाशम्
निपलाशम् नि-पलाशम्, ind., Ved. (Sāy.)<BR>without speaking, i. e. like a tree without foliage (or<BR>as a leafless tree moves without rustling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपा
निपा 1. नि-पा, cl. 2. P. -पाति, -पातुम्, &c.,<BR>to guard, protect, defend; observe, watch over: Caus.<BR>-पालयति, -यितुम्, to protect, guard, govern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपा
निपा 2. नि-पा, cl. 1. and 2. P. -पिबति or<BR>-पिवति, -पातुम्, to drink in, imbibe, suck in; to<BR>absorb, dry up: Caus. P. -पाययति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to imbibe or suck in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप|निपं|निपः
नि-प, अस्, अम्, m. n. a water-jar; (अस्), m. the<BR>Kadamba tree, Nauclea Cadamba (= कदम्ब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपान|निपानं
नि-पान or निपानक, अम्, n. drinking, im-<BR>bibing; any reservoir of water, any place or trough<BR>near a well for watering cattle; a well, pool; a<BR>milk-pail.<BR>—निपान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having reser-<BR>voirs or ponds, abounding in pools, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीत
नि-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, drunk in, drunk up, absorbed,<BR>imbibed, dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीति|निपीतिः
नि-पीति, इस्, f. drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीयमान
नि-पीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being drunk in or<BR>imbibed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाक|निपाकः
निपाक नि-पाक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पच् with नि),<BR>cooking, maturing, ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाठ|निपाठः
निपाठ नि-पाठ. See नि-पठ, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपात|निपातः
निपात नि-पात. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाद|निपादः
निपाद नि-पाद, अस्, m., Ved. low ground,<BR>a valley; (Sāy.) high and low ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपिष्
निपिष् नि-पिष्, cl. 7. P., Ved. -पिनष्टि,<BR>-पेष्टुम्, to crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीड्
निपीड् नि-पीड्, cl. 10. P. -पीडयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to press close to or against, press together, squeeze;<BR>to embrace; to impress; to cause pain, afflict,<BR>plague, trouble; (in astronomy) to eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडन|निपीडनं
नि-पीडन, अम्, n. squeezing, pressing; hurting,<BR>giving pain; (आ), f. oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडयत्
नि-पीडयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, pressing, pressing to-<BR>gether; (दन्तान् दन्तैर् निपीडयन्, gnashing<BR>the teeth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडित
नि-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, squeezed, pressed, embraced;<BR>pained, hurt.<BR>—निपीडितालक्तक-वत् (˚त-अल्˚), ind.<BR>like pressed lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीड्य
नि-पीड्य, ind. having pressed; having pressed<BR>against or upon; having embraced; having hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीय्
निपीय् नि-पीय्, cl. 1. P., Ved. -पीयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to revile, abuse, treat with contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपु
निपु निपु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुण|निपुणः
निपुण नि-पुण, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>पुण् with नि; perhaps fr. rt. पुष् + affix न, through<BR>which dialectically पुण्ण = पुण), clever, adroit,<BR>skilful, skilled in, conversant with (loc. and gen.);<BR>experienced; kind or friendly towards (with loc. or<BR>with प्रति); sharp, acute, fine, delicate; complete,<BR>perfect, accurate; (अम् or एन), ind. skilfully, cleverly,<BR>sharply; completely, perfectly, totally, exactly, care-<BR>fully; in a delicate manner.<BR>—निपुण-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, more clever, perfect, &c.; (अम्), ind. cleverly;<BR>perfectly.<BR>—निपुण-तस्, ind. cleverly, skilfully;<BR>completely.<BR>—निपुण-ता, f. skilfulness, cleverness,<BR>conversancy, adroitness, versatility; carefulness, accu-<BR>racy.<BR>—निपुण-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, sharp-sighted, clever,<BR>knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुणिका
निपुणिका, f. ‘the clever one,’ N. of a waiting-<BR>maid in the Vikramorvaśī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुथ्
निपुथ् नि-पुथ्, Caus. -पोथयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to dash down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुर्
निपुर् नि-पुर्, ऊर्, f., Ved. (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara) = सूक्ष्म-देह, the subtle body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपूत
निपूत नि-पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. strained,<BR>filtered, purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप्रहन्
निप्रहन् नि-प्र-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -हन्-<BR>तुम्, to kill (with gen. of the object).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप्रियाय
निप्रियाय निप्रियाय (fr. नि-प्रिय), Nom.<BR>A. निप्रियायते, &c., Ved. to keep in one's pos-<BR>session, not to be willing to give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफला
निफला नि-फला, f. the plant Cardiosper-<BR>mum Halicacabum (= ज्योतिष्मती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफालन
निफालन नि-फालन, अम्, n. (probably<BR>incorrect for नि-भालन), seeing, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफेन|निफेनं
निफेन नि-फेन, अम्, n. = अ-फेन, opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबद्ध
निबद्ध नि-बद्ध. See under नि-बन्ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्ध्|निबंध्
निबन्ध् नि-बन्ध्, cl. 9. P. -बध्नाति, -बन्द्-<BR>धुम्, to bind on, bind, tie, fasten, tie together; to<BR>fetter, enchain, imprison, ensnare; to attach, to join,<BR>unite, connect; compose (in writing), record, write;<BR>to construct; to draw together, contract (e. g. भ्रु-<BR>कुटीम्, the brow); to fix, hold fast, confine, restrain,<BR>obstruct, stop, close up, restrict; to fix on, place or<BR>put upon, impose; to put together, form, acquire;<BR>(with पदम्) to put the foot upon, i. e. to under-<BR>take anything; to fix or direct upon; to appoint,<BR>commission, charge; to place, locate; to destroy,<BR>(Mahā-bh. Virāṭa-p. 982; cf. rt. वध्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबद्ध
नि-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound in or on, bound;<BR>fastened, tied, connected, bound or sewed together,<BR>fastened to; caught (as in a net), fettered, enchained,<BR>chained to, dependant on; connected, coherent; shut<BR>up, closed, stopped, obstructed; confined, costive;<BR>checked, restrained, restricted to; bound over or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">Page0489-a+ 75</a>]<BR>called as a witness (Manu VIII. 76); composed, written;<BR>fixed in, inlaid (as with gold or jewels), enchased, set,<BR>inserted; committed, intrusted; enveloped, enclosed,<BR>involved, covered with; constructed of, formed of,<BR>consisting of; accompanied by, furnished or endowed<BR>with; relating to, contained or involved in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्द्धृ|निबंद्धृ
नि-बन्द्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, who or what<BR>ties or binds, a binder, fastener; (धा), m. a com-<BR>poser, writer, author; a commentator; (also written<BR>नि-बन्धृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्ध|निबंध|निबन्धं|निबंधः|निबन्धः
नि-बन्ध, अस्, m. binding on, binding, fastening,<BR>tying, attachment, attachment to, intentness on; com-<BR>posing, writing down, recording; restraint, obstruc-<BR>tion, confinement, constipation, suppression of urine,<BR>strangury; a band, bond, fetter; fixed property, not<BR>movable or fluctuating; a grant of property, an assign-<BR>ment of cattle or money for support; foundation,<BR>origin, root, cause, reason; any literary composition<BR>or treatise; a commentary or explanation of technical<BR>rules [cf. ग्रन्थ]; N. of a particular work; the<BR>plant Azadirachta Indica; (अम्), n. song, singing.<BR>—निबन्ध-दान, अम्, n. grant of property, as-<BR>signment or gift of a corrody.<BR>—निबन्ध-सङ्-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a commentary on Su-śruta's<BR>medical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धन|निबंधन|निबंधनं|निबन्धनं
नि-बन्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, binding, fastening,<BR>fettering; (ई), f. band, bond, fetter; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of fastening to, binding together, ligation; con-<BR>structing, building (as a bridge &c.); checking, re-<BR>straining, confining; band, fetter; that to which<BR>anything is fastened or on which it rests; a receptacle;<BR>the part of a lute where the strings are fastened, the<BR>tie or peg of a lute; cause, origin, reason, motive,<BR>condition; (in grammar) syntax; a composition; a<BR>commentary; a grant, an assignment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धिक
नि-बन्धिक. See अश्व-न्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धित|निबन्धितः
नि-बन्धित, अस्, आ, अम्, bound, fastened, con-<BR>fined, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धिन्|निबंधिन्
नि-बन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, binding, confining; joined<BR>or connected by or with, hanging together, cohering;<BR>causing, being a cause or having a reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबर्हण|निबर्हणं
निबर्हण नि-बर्हण. See नि-बृह् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबल
निबल निबल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a<BR>particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबाध्
निबाध् नि-बाध्, cl. 1. A. -बाधते, -बाधि-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to press down or together, force in; to<BR>cramp, contract, confine, obstruct; to oppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबाध
नि-बाध, अस्, m. obstruction, in अ-न्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबाळ्ह
निबाळ्ह नि-बाऌह, अस्, आ, अम् (according<BR>to some fr. rt. बंह्, according to Sāy. fr. rt. बाह् =<BR>वाह्, to endeavour), Ved. forced down, thrown into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबुध्
निबुध् नि-बुध्, cl. 1. P. A. -बोधति, -ते,<BR>-बोधितुम्, to learn or hear anything (acc.) from<BR>any one (gen. or with सकाशात्); to attend to, listen<BR>to, (often occurring in the impv. नि-बोध); to<BR>know, consider: Caus. -बोधयति, &c., to cause to<BR>know or learn, to inform, give to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबोद्धव्य
नि-बोद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be learnt; to be<BR>considered or regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबृह्
निबृह् नि-बृह् (also written नि-वृह्, q. v.),<BR>cl. 1. P. -बर्हति, -बर्हितुम्, -बर्हयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to throw down, destroy, annihilate, extirpate,<BR>eradicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबर्हण|निबर्हणं
नि-बर्हण, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, &c.; (अम्),<BR>n. destruction, annihilation, &c. See नि-वर्हण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभ|निभः
निभ नि-भ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. भा with<BR>नि), like, resembling, similar, (only at the end of a<BR>comp.; sometimes pleonastically after adjectives, e. g.<BR>चारु-निभानन, handsome-faced; and occasionally<BR>with another word meaning ‘like,’ e. g. नग-निभो-<BR>पम, like a mountain); (अस्, अम्), m. n. appear-<BR>ance, light, manifestation; pretence, pretext, fraud,<BR>sham, trick, disguise.<BR>—निभ-ता, f. similarity, likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभञ्ज्
निभञ्ज् नि-भञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. -भनक्ति, -भङ्क्-<BR>तुम्, to break or dash to pieces, break asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभर्त्सन
निभर्त्सन नि-भर्त्सन, wrong reading for<BR>निर्-भर्त्सन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभल्
निभल् नि-भल्, cl. 10. P. A. -भालयति,<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, to perceive, see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभालन|निभालनं
नि-भालन, अम्, n. seeing, sight, perception;<BR>[cf. नि-फालन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभसद्
निभसद् नि-भसद् (?), having the hinder<BR>parts directed downwards (?). See भसद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभिद्
निभिद् नि-भिद्, cl. 7. P. A. -भिनत्ति,<BR>-भिन्त्ते, -भेत्तुम्, to break or divide asunder: Pass.<BR>-भिद्यते, to be opened, to open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभीम
निभीम नि-भीम, अस्, आ, अम्, terrible, fright-<BR>ful.<BR>—निभीम-विक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, of terrible<BR>valour, of formidable prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभूत|निभूतं
निभूत नि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, past, gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभूयप
निभूयप निभूयप, अस्, m., Ved. epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu, (meaning unknown.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृ
निभृ नि-भृ, cl. 1. P. -भरति, -भर्तुम्,<BR>&c., to bear or put down, (apparently only used in<BR>the part. नि-भृत below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृत|निभृतः
नि-भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, borne or placed down, deposited<BR>in a low place, lowered; concealed, hidden, secret,<BR>occult, unperceived, imperceptible; modest, humble,<BR>unassuming; mild, gentle; lonely, solitary; still, silent;<BR>firm, unmoved, immovable; resolute, decided, firmly<BR>attached, faithful; filled with, full of, (Bhāgavata-Purāṇa<BR>X. 32, 20, = पूर्ण, व्याप्त); (अम्), n. humility,<BR>modesty, meekness [cf. नैभृत्य]; (अम्), ind.<BR>covertly, secretly, privately, apart, unobservedly, im-<BR>perceptibly, in a corner, out of sight.<BR>—निभृतागत<BR>(˚त-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, secretly arrived.<BR>—निभृतात्-<BR>मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, resolute-minded, resolute.<BR>—निभृतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>secret meaning, occult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभ्रंश्
निभ्रंश् नि-भ्रंश्, Caus. -भ्राशयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Ved. to cause to fall off, to strike or break off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम|निमः
निम निम, अस्, m. a pin, stake (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्ज्
निमज्ज् नि-मज्ज्, cl. 6. P. -मज्जति, -मङ्क्-<BR>तुम्, to sink into, sink down, dive, plunge into,<BR>immerse one's self, bathe, be immersed or submerged<BR>(e. g. अक्षि निमज्जति, the eye sinks; चिरं नि-<BR>ममज्ज, he remained long under the water); to be<BR>drowned; to penetrate into; to disappear, perish; to<BR>immerse or submerge in water, cause to sink (e. g. into<BR>hell, Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 4156): Caus. P. -मज्जयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to dive, immerse, dip, plunge (any-<BR>thing) into water, submerge, drown; (figuratively)<BR>to cause to plunge or penetrate into a battle, lead<BR>into the thick of a fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्न
नि-मग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, plunged or immersed in,<BR>dipped into, fallen into (water &c.), submerged,<BR>sunk; gone down, set (as the sun); forcibly entered<BR>into or penetrated; (with पर-लोकाय) entered<BR>into the other world; sunk in, depressed, not<BR>prominent; overwhelmed, covered.<BR>—निमग्न-ना-<BR>भि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a depressed navel.<BR>—निमग्न-<BR>मध्या, f. a woman having a depressed (and there-<BR>fore slender) waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्नक
नि-मग्नक, अस्, आ, अम्, hiding one's self, lurking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जत्
नि-मज्जत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, bathing, diving,<BR>plunging in, sinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जथु|निमज्जथुः
नि-मज्जथु, उस्, m. the act of diving or entering<BR>into, plunging; (with तल्पे) going to bed, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जन|निमज्जनं
नि-मज्जन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to enter or plunge<BR>into (with gen.), immersing, absorbing; (अम्), n.<BR>bathing, diving, immersion, sinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जमान
नि-मज्जमान, अस्, आ, अम्, sinking, plunging<BR>into; immersed; being drowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जित
नि-मज्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, plunged into the water,<BR>drowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमद्
निमद् नि-मद्, Caus. P. -मादयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to pronounce distinctly but slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमद|निमदः
नि-मद, अस्, m. pronunciation which is distinct<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">Page0489-c+ 77</a>]<BR>but slow, one of the seven degrees of pronunciation<BR>(वाचः स्थानानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्र्|निमंत्र्
निमन्त्र् नि-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्रयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to invite, summon, call (to a feast), entertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रक
नि-मन्त्रक, अस्, m. one who summons or<BR>invites, an inviter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रण|निमंत्रण|निमंत्रणं|निमन्त्रणं
नि-मन्त्रण, अम्, n. inviting, invitation; sum-<BR>moning, calling; a summons.<BR>—निमन्त्रण-पत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. a written summons, a note of invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रित
नि-मन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, invited, summoned,<BR>convoked; bidden to a feast, entertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्र्य
नि-मन्त्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be invited, to be called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्यु
निमन्यु नि-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. not angry,<BR>unresentful, appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमय|निमयः
निमय नि-मय. See नि-मे, p. 490, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमा
निमा नि-मा [cf. नि-मे], cl. 2. 3. P. A.<BR>-माति, -मिमीते, -मातुम्, to measure; to adjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमातव्य
1. नि-मातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be measured, &c.;<BR>[the नि-मातव्य which occurs in Manu X. 94. is to<BR>be referred to नि-मे, q. v.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमान|निमानं
नि-मान, अम्, n. measure. See अ-न्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित
1. नि-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, measured out. See दुर्-न्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेय|निमेयः
1. नि-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see नि-मे), to be<BR>measured, measurable, anything the measure or value<BR>of which can be fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमि|निमिः
निमि 1. निमि, इस्, m., N. of several kings of<BR>Videha; of a son of Dattātreya; of a son of Ikṣvāku,<BR>(this Nimi lost his body through the curse of<BR>Vaśiṣṭha, and when the gods were willing to restore<BR>it, requested that instead of receiving his former<BR>shape he might occupy the eyes of all living creatures;<BR>the request was granted, and in consequence of the<BR>presence of Nimi, men's eyelids are ever opening<BR>and shutting; cf. नि-मिष, and see Viṣṇu-Purāṇa<BR>IV. 5); N. of the twenty-first Jaina Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī; of a son of Bhajamāna; of<BR>Daṇḍa-pāṇi; of a Dānava; closing or winking of<BR>the eyes, twinkling.<BR>—निमिन्-धर, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>निमिम् acc. sing. + धर), N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमि|निमिः
निमि 2. नि-मि, cl. 5. P. A. -मिनोति, -मिनुते,<BR>&c., to fix in, dig in; to fix, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित
2. नि-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed in, fixed, erected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्त|निमित्तं
निमित्त नि-मित्त, अम्, n. (probably con-<BR>nected with नि-मा above), a mark, an aim; an<BR>archer's butt, target; sign, token; prognostic, pre-<BR>sage, omen [cf. दुर्-न्˚]; cause, motive, reason,<BR>instrumental or efficient cause, (opposed to उपा-दान,<BR>the material cause); निमित्त is used at the end of<BR>a comp. in the sense ‘having as a motive or cause,’<BR>‘caused or produced by,’ ‘occasioned by,’ e. g. विष-<BR>निमित्ता पीडा, pain caused by poison; (अम् acc.,<BR>एन inst., आय dat., आत् abl., अस्य gen., ए loc.),<BR>because of, on account of, for the sake of, for the<BR>purpose of, through.<BR>—निमित्त-कारण, अम्, n. an<BR>instrumental or efficient cause, (especially the Deity<BR>considered as the agent in creation.)<BR>—निमित्त-<BR>कारण-ता, f. the state of being the efficient cause.<BR>—निमित्त-काल, अस्, m. the period or moment of<BR>time which may be regarded as causing any event;<BR>any given or specific time.<BR>—निमित्त-कृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘omen-maker,’ a crow, raven.<BR>—निमित्त-ज्ञ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, acquainted with omens.<BR>—निमित्त-ज्ञान,<BR>अम्, n. ‘knowledge of causes or signs,’ N. of the fifty-<BR>eighth chapter of the Kāma-sūtra by Vātsyāyana.<BR>—निमित्त-तस्, ind. by or from a special cause or<BR>reason.<BR>—निमित्त-ता, f. or निमित्त-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being a cause, causality, instrumentality.<BR>—निमित्त-धर्म, अस्, m. expiation; any occa-<BR>sional or special penance, rite, or obligation.<BR>—नि-<BR>मित्त-निदान, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—निमित्त-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become a cause or reason, being<BR>a cause or means.<BR>—निमित्त-मात्र, अम्, n. the<BR>mere efficient cause or instrument.<BR>—निमित्त-विद्,<BR>त्, m. ‘omen-knower,’ an astrologer.<BR>—निमित्त-<BR>वेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hitting an aim, piercing the mark.<BR>—निमित्त-हेतु, उस्, m. an efficient cause.<BR>—नि-<BR>मित्तहेतु-त्व, अम्, n. the being an instrumental<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">Page0490-a+ 77</a>]<BR>or efficient cause.<BR>—निमित्तार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the infinitive mood (in grammar).<BR>—निमित्तावृत्ति<BR>(˚त-आव्˚), इस्, f. dependance upon a special cause or<BR>occasion.<BR>—निमित्ती-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to make anything a cause, to use as<BR>a cause or means.<BR>—निमित्ती-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति,<BR>-वितुम्, to become a cause or reason for (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तक|निमित्तकं
नि-मित्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.), caused or occasioned or produced by; (अम्),<BR>n. kissing, a kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तायमान
निमित्तायमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. an unused Nominal<BR>verb निमित्ताय), causing, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तिन्
निमित्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, operated on or influenced by<BR>a cause, having a cause or reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिश्ल
निमिश्ल नि-मिश्ल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. devoted<BR>to, attached to (with loc.); (Sāy.) commixed, com-<BR>mingling, mixing with, being mixed.<BR>—निमिश्ल-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most attached to (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिष्
निमिष् 1. नि-मिष्, cl. 6. P. -मिषति, -मे-<BR>षितुम्, to shut the eyelids, wink, twinkle, blink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिष्
2. नि-मिष्, ट्, f., Ved. winking or twinkling of the<BR>eye; shutting the eyes, falling asleep [cf. निमि];<BR>अ-निमिष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, never closing or winking the eyes;<BR>(ट्), m. a god; [cf. Nala V. 24.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिष|निमिषः
नि-मिष, अस्, m. twinkling, winking, shutting<BR>the eye; the twinkling of an eye considered as a<BR>measure of time, a moment; morbid twinkling of the<BR>eyes; N. of a son of Garuḍa (Mahā-bh. Udyoga-parva<BR>3595); an epithet of Viṣṇu, (also अ-निमिष.)<BR>—निमिषान्तर (˚ष-अन्˚), अम्, n. the interval<BR>of a moment; (एण), ind. in a twinkling, in the<BR>interval of a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिषत्
नि-मिषत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, winking, blinking,<BR>closing the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेष|निमेषः
नि-मेष, अस्, अम्, m. n. twinkling of the eyes,<BR>(opposed to उन्-मेष); a momentary space of<BR>time, a moment, a twinkling of the eye considered<BR>as a measure of time; morbid twinkling of the eye,<BR>morbid closing of the eyelid; N. of a mythical<BR>being; निमेषं निमेषम्, every moment.<BR>—नि-<BR>मेष-कृत्, त्, f. ‘twinkler,’ lightning.<BR>—निमेष-<BR>तस्, ind., Ved. with regard to the shutting of the<BR>eyes, (according to Mahī-dhara gen. sing. of the<BR>pres. part.)<BR>—निमेष-द्युत्, त्, or निमेष-रुच्, क्,<BR>m. a fire-fly.<BR>—निमेष-मात्र, अम्, n. only a twink-<BR>ling, merely an instant; (एण), ind. in a twinkling,<BR>in an instant of time, in barely a moment.<BR>—निमे-<BR>षार्धात् (˚ष-अर्˚), ind. in half a twinkling of the<BR>eye, i. e. in less than an instant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषक|निमेषकः
नि-मेषक, अस्, m. twinkling of the eye; a fire-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषण
नि-मेषण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing twinkling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिह्
निमिह् नि-मिह्, cl. 1. P. -मेहति, &c., to<BR>urine, sprinkle down urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमील्
निमील् नि-मील्, cl. 1. P. -मीलति, -मीलितुम्,<BR>to shut or close the eyes, fall asleep, sleep; to close (as<BR>flowers); to die, disappear; Caus. -मीलयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause (one) to shut the eyes, to close; to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलत्
नि-मीलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, closing the eyes, winking<BR>the eyelids, twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलन|निमीलनं
नि-मीलन, अम्, n. shutting the eyelids, winking<BR>or twinkling of the eyes, winking; closing the eyes<BR>in death; (figuratively) dying, death; (in astronomy)<BR>immersion, complete obscuration, a total eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीला
नि-मीला, f. shutting the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलिका
नि-मीलिका, f. shutting the eyes, winking, twink-<BR>ling, blinking, conniving at anything; fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलित
नि-मीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, closed, shut (as the eye),<BR>winked, blinked; blinded, darkened, obscured; [cf.<BR>रजो-निमीलित.]<BR>—निमीलिताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, having the eyes closed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलिन्
नि-मीलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, closing the eyes, having the<BR>eyelids shut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीव्
निमीव् नि-मीव्, cl. 1. P. -मीवति, &c., to<BR>press on, press down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीश्वर|निमीश्वरः
निमीश्वर निमीश्वर, अस्, m. (with Jainas)<BR>N. of the sixteenth Arhat of the present Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमूलम्
निमूलम् नि-मूलम्, ind. down to the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमृज्
निमृज् नि-मृज्, cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि (cl. 6. Ved.<BR>-मृजति, -ते), -मार्जितुम्, -मार्ष्टुम्, to rub in,<BR>rub upon, wipe, wipe off, wipe away, to cleanse<BR>one's self (A.); to lead to, attach to: Intens., Ved.<BR>-मामृजे, to wipe away, cleanse; to destroy:<BR>Desid., Ved. -मिमृक्षति, (in Ṛg-veda I. 64, 4,<BR>Sāy. considers नि-मिमृक्षुः as a Vedic redupli-<BR>cated perf. = नि-मृष्टाः स्थिता बभूवुः; accord-<BR>ing to some the meaning is ‘to flash down.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमृग्र
नि-मृग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. devoted, attached to;<BR>(Sāy.) excessively purifying or cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमृण्
निमृण् नि-मृण्, cl. 6. P. -मृणति, &c., to<BR>dash down, strike down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमृद्
निमृद् नि-मृद्, cl. 9. P. -मृद्नाति, -मर्दि-<BR>तुम्, to crush, dash to pieces; to rub off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमे
निमे नि-मे [cf. नि-मा], cl. 1. A. -मयते,<BR>मातुम्, to change, exchange for (with inst.), barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमय|निमयः
नि-मय, अस्, m. barter, change, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमातव्य
2. नि-मातव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see नि-मा),<BR>to be exchanged or bartered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेय|निमेयः
2. नि-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see नि-मा), to be ex-<BR>changed; (अस्), m. barter, exchange; [cf. नैमेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेष|निमेषः
निमेष नि-मेष. See under 1. नि-मिष्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्न|निम्नं
निम्न निम्न, अम्, n. (fr. नि or perhaps<BR>rather fr. rt. नम् with नि or according to others fr.<BR>rt. मन् or rt. म्ना with नि), depth, low ground, low-<BR>land; a slope, declivity; gap, chasm or cavity in the<BR>ground; a depression, deepening; (अस्, आ, अम्), deep,<BR>profound (literally or figuratively); low (as ground),<BR>depressed, sunk; (अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—निम्न-<BR>ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going low or deep, going downwards,<BR>descending; (आ), f. a river, mountain-stream; [cf.<BR>गिरि-न्˚.]<BR>—निम्न-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, going in deep<BR>or low places; (अम्), n. a low place.<BR>—निम्न-तल,<BR>see under निन्द-तल.<BR>—निम्न-ता, f. or निम्न-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. depth, lowness, profundity.<BR>—निम्न-<BR>देश, अस्, m. or निम्न-भाग, अस्, m. a low or deep<BR>place.<BR>—निम्नोन्नत (˚न-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, low<BR>and high, depressed and elevated, up and down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नैस्
निम्नैस्, ind., Ved. in deep places, low, down-<BR>wards; [cf. उच्चैस्, नीचैस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्ब|निंब|निंबः|निम्बः
निम्ब निम्ब or निम्बक, अस्, m. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. नी), a tree with bitter fruits, Azadirachta<BR>Indica, the Nimb or Neemb tree, (the leaves of this<BR>tree are chewed at funeral ceremonies); [cf. गिरि-न्˚,<BR>तृण-न्˚.]<BR>—निम्ब-तरु, उस्, m. the tree Erythrina<BR>Fulgens or (according to others) Melia Sempervirens,<BR>(it is considered as one of the trees of paradise.)<BR>—निम्ब-रजस्, अस्, n. a particular high number;<BR>[cf. महा-न्˚.]<BR>—निम्ब-वती, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—निम्ब-वीज, अस्, m. a tree (= राजादनी).<BR>—निम्-<BR>बार्क-करवीरार्चन-व्रत (˚ब-अर्˚, ˚र-अर्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a particular vow; N. of the seventy-seventh<BR>chapter of the Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्बूक|निम्बूकं|निंबूकः|निम्बूकः
निम्बूक निम्बूक, अस्, m. the common lime,<BR>Citrus Acida; (also read निस्बू.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्लुच्
निम्लुच् नि-म्लुच् (Ved. नि-म्रुच्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-म्लोचति, &c., to set, disappear (as the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्रुक्ति
नि-म्रुक्ति, Ved., or in later Sanskrit नि-म्लुक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. sunset, setting of the sun, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्रुच्
नि-म्रुच्, क्, f., Ved. sunset, setting of the sun,<BR>evening; (क्, क्, क्), slack, loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्लोच|निम्लोचः
नि-म्लोच, अस्, m. setting of the sun, sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्लोचनी
नि-म्लोचनी, f. (fr. an unused form नि-म्लोचन),<BR>N. of the city of Varuṇa situated on the mountain<BR>Mānasottara towards the west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्लोचि
नि-म्लोचि, इस्, m., N. of a prince, son of Bhajamāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियत|नियतः
नियत नि-यत. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्र्
नियन्त्र् नि-यन्त्र्, cl. 10. P. -यन्त्रयति, &c.,<BR>to restrain, [apparently only used in the derivatives.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्रण|नियंत्रण|नियंत्रणं
नि-यन्त्रण, अम्, n. the act of restraining, restraint,<BR>checking; governing, guiding; defining, definition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्रित|नियंत्रित|नियन्त्रितः
नि-यन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, restrained, curbed, checked;<BR>governed, guided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम्
नियम् नि-यम्, cl. 1. P. -यच्छति, -यन्तुम्,<BR>to check, curb, restrain, hold back, suppress, stop;<BR>to hold in (as the breath &c.); govern, control, rule,<BR>direct, regulate; to punish; to restrict; to bind,<BR>confine, fasten; to conceal; to attain, obtain; to<BR>assume; to present, offer; to place or fix upon:<BR>Caus. -यमयति, -यितुम्, to restrain, curb, check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियत|नियतः
नि-यत, अस्, आ, अम्, checked, curbed, restrained,<BR>held in; governed, controlled, subdued, submissive,<BR>self-governed; abstemious, self-denying, temperate;<BR>attentive, intent upon; fixed, constant, steady, per-<BR>manent, incessant; ascertained, certain, destined,<BR>settled, sure; inevitable; positive, definite; perme-<BR>able, what may be spread through or over?; (अम्),<BR>n. elementary or crude matter, the recipient of attri-<BR>butes or properties; (अम्), ind. always, constantly,<BR>decidedly, positively, surely, certainly, inevitably; for-<BR>cibly.<BR>—नियत-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, of subdued<BR>mind or spirit.<BR>—नियत-विषय-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>steadily abiding in one's own sphere.<BR>—नियतात्मन्<BR>(˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, self-regulated, self-controlled, self-<BR>restrained.<BR>—नियताहार (˚त-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abstemious in food, temperate.<BR>—नियतेन्द्रिय (˚त-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the passions subdued or<BR>restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियति|नियतिः
नि-यति, इस्, f. restraint, restriction; the fixed<BR>order of things, necessity, destiny, fate, luck, good or<BR>bad fortune; a religious duty or obligation; self-<BR>command, self-restraint; (नियति is sometimes per-<BR>sonified as a goddess, she and Āyati being regarded<BR>as daughters of Meru and wives of Dhātṛ and Vi-<BR>dhātṛ); (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तवय
नि-यन्तवय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be restrained, checked,<BR>controlled, tamed; to be forced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तु
नि-यन्तु in दुर्-न्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तृ|नियंतृ
नि-यन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what holds in,<BR>restrains, curbs, governs, guides, tames, &c.; re-<BR>straining; (ता), m. a restrainer, charioteer, driver,<BR>coachman; a ruler, governor, master; a punisher.<BR>—नियन्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. restraint, government, abi-<BR>lity to rule, power of restraining, controlling faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम|नियमः
नि-यम, अस्, m. restraining, holding back, check-<BR>ing, keeping back; taming, subduing, preventing,<BR>confining; restraint, restriction, restriction to (with<BR>loc.); limitation; fixing, defining, definition; keeping<BR>down, lowering (as the tone of the voice); fixed<BR>rule or law, necessity, obligation; rule, precept (e. g.<BR>स्त्रीणाम् प्राकृत-भाषणम् एव नियमः, the<BR>usage of women is to speak only Prākṛt); certainty,<BR>ascertainment; agreement, contract, engagement,<BR>assent, promise, vow; any self-imposed restraint or<BR>religious observance voluntarily practised, as fast-<BR>ing, watching, pilgrimage, praying, &c.; voluntary<BR>penance, meritorious or supererogatory piety; a lesser<BR>vow, minor observance (as opposed to यम, a greater<BR>vow which must always be observed); (in rhetoric)<BR>a common-place in poetry, any conventional expres-<BR>sion or usual comparison (as notice of the birch in<BR>describing the Himālaya, of the sandal tree in de-<BR>scribing the Malaya mountains, of the peacock's cry<BR>in the rains, of the koïl in spring, &c.); Necessity<BR>or Fixed Law personified as a son of Dharma by<BR>Dhṛti; (एन or आत्), ind. by a fixed rule, necessarily,<BR>surely, certainly.<BR>—नियम-निष्ठा, f. rigid ob-<BR>servance of prescribed rites.<BR>—नियम-पत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a written agreement or stipulation.<BR>—नियम-<BR>पर, अस्, आ, अम्, observing fixed rules; relating to<BR>or corroborative of a rule.<BR>—नियम-पाल, अस्, m.<BR>‘observer of vows,’ N. of a sage from whom the<BR>Nepalese derive the name of their country, (properly<BR>Nipāl.)<BR>—नियम-भङ्ग, अस्, m. breach of a<BR>stipulation or contract.<BR>—नियम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>practising or observing religious observances; (अती), f.<BR>(a woman) having the monthly courses.<BR>—नियम-<BR>स्थिति, इस्, f. a state of self-restraint, steady observance<BR>of religious obligations, asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमन|नियमनं
नि-यमन, अस्, ई, अम्, regulating, controlling,<BR>subduing, taming, overpowering; (अम्), n. subduing,<BR>checking, restraining; humiliation, coercion; binding;<BR>restriction, limitation; precept, fixed practice or rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमित|नियमितः
नि-यमित, अस्, आ, अम्, checked, restrained, sup-<BR>pressed, bound, confined; governed, guided; fixed,<BR>regulated, prescribed, stipulated, agreed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम्य
1. नि-यम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be checked or re-<BR>strained, restrainable, tamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम्य
2. नि-यम्य, ind. having restrained, having<BR>guided, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियाम|नियामः
नि-याम, अस्, m. = नि-यम, restraint; religious<BR>vow, penance, fasting, &c., especially if an act of<BR>supererogation; = नि-यामक, a boatman, sailor; [cf.<BR>निर्-याम.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामक|नियामकः
नि-यामक, अस्, आ, अम्, restraining, checking, con-<BR>trolling, subduing, suppressing, overpowering; re-<BR>strictive, limiting; defining more closely; guiding,<BR>governing, who or what regulates or restrains; a re-<BR>strainer, ruler, master; (अस्), m. a charioteer; a boat-<BR>man, a sailor, but variously applied to one who rows<BR>or steers, a pilot, a helmsman; [cf. निर्-याम.]<BR>—नि-<BR>यामक-ता, f. controllership, power of restraining,<BR>restraint; exact definition, explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामन
नि-यामन, अम्, n. taming, checking, restraining;<BR>(probably incorrectly for नि-यमन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निययिन्
निययिन् नि-ययिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. rt. या with<BR>नि), Ved. driving over, passing over (as a carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियान|नियानं
नि-यान, अम्, n., Ved. way, access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियव|नियवः
नियव नि-यव. See under 2. नि-यु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियातन|नियातनं
नियातन नि-यातन, अम्, n. causing to fall<BR>or descend; (wrong reading for नि-पातन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियु
नियु 1. नि-यु, cl. 3. P. -युयोति, &c., Ved.<BR>to repel, keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियु
नियु 2. नि-यु, cl. 2. P. -यौति, cl. 9. P. A.<BR>-युनाति, -नीते, -यवितुम्, to join, yoke, harness;<BR>to mix; to bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियव|नियवः
नि-यव, अस्, m. compact order, continuous line or<BR>series; (Sāy.) mixing, mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत्
नि-युत्, त्, f., Ved. series, line, row; (Sāy.) a<BR>horse, steed (as harnessed to a car), especially one of<BR>the horses of Vāyu called Niyuts; praise, a praiser;<BR>(अस्), f. pl. series of words [cf. ग्रन्थ, नि-बन्-<BR>धन], verses, a poem; (Sāy.) a team of horses,<BR>especially the Niyuts or horses of Vāyu; N. of a<BR>wife of Rudra in one of his different forms.<BR>—नियुत्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. forming a series; flowing<BR>continuously, as the Soma; drawn by a line of horses,<BR>as Vāyu or Indra, or the Maruts; (Sāy.) possessing<BR>the Niyut steeds, possessing horses; containing the<BR>word नियुत् or नियुत्-वत् (as a verse or hymn).<BR>—नियुद्-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one whose car is<BR>drawn by a line or team of horses; (Sāy.) having a<BR>harnessed chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत|नियुतं
नि-युत, अम्, n. (according to some lexicographers<BR>also m.), a million; a hundred thousand; 100 Ayutas<BR>= 10, 000 Koṭis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत्वतीय
नि-युत्वतीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to<BR>Niyut-vat (Vāyu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुज्
नियुज् नि-युज्, cl. 7. P. A. -युनक्ति, -युङ्क्ते,<BR>-योक्तुम्, to join to, attach or fasten to; to put to<BR>(horses), yoke, harness; to place over, appoint, elect<BR>or depute any one to any office or duty (with acc.<BR>of the person and loc. of the thing or business); to<BR>give authority, authorize; to assign, employ, engage;<BR>to commit, intrust, commission; to enjoin, order,<BR>command; to constrain, urge, coerce, compel; to<BR>harass: Caus. (or cl. 10.) -योजयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to be attached, cause to be placed or put, to fasten;<BR>to appoint, commission, charge, employ; to order,<BR>command, direct, prescribe; to urge, instigate, coerce;<BR>to perform, make, place in any state (e. g. सन्देहे,<BR>in jeopardy); to offer, present with, endow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्त|नियुक्तः
नि-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened to; engaged in,<BR>attached to; directed, enjoined, commanded; autho-<BR>rized, appointed; ascertained; (अस्), m. a functionary,<BR>official.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्तक
नि-युक्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, appointed, elected, placed<BR>in authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्ति|नियुक्तिः
नि-युक्ति, इस्, f. injunction, order, command; ap-<BR>pointment, commission, charge, office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुज्य
नि-युज्य, ind. having joined or attached; having<BR>put to or harnessed; having appointed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुज्यमान
नि-युज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being appointed,<BR>being engaged or employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुञ्जान
नि-युञ्जान, अस्, आ, अम्, appointing, authorizing,<BR>enjoining, constituting, appointing to an office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोक्तव्य
नि-योक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be appointed or autho-<BR>rized, to be employed, ordered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोक्तृ
नि-योक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who joins or fastens<BR>or attaches; (ता), m. a ruler, lord master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग|नियोगः
नि-योग, अस्, m. attaching or fastening to; appli-<BR>cation, use, employment, appointment, injunction,<BR>direction, order, command, commission, charge,<BR>precept; any trust or appointed task or duty, any<BR>business or function committed to one's charge;<BR>effort, exertion; certainty, ascertainment; necessity;<BR>(आत् or एन), ind. according to order or command,<BR>necessarily, certainly, surely.<BR>—नियोग-करण, अम्,<BR>n. making a command, commanding.<BR>—नियोग-तस्,<BR>ind. according to order or command.<BR>—नियोग-<BR>पाश, अस्, m. a fastening, (probably) a halter.<BR>—नि-<BR>योग-प्रयोजन, अम्, n. the object or business of<BR>any appointment, authorized act or duty.<BR>—नियोग-<BR>विधि, इस्, m. the form or rule of appointing to any<BR>act or duty.<BR>—नियोगार्थ (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>object of an authorized act or appointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगिन्
नि-योगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, appointed, authorized, invested<BR>with authority, employed, engaged in any duty,<BR>attached to any business; (ई), m. a functionary, an<BR>official, officer, man in office, a minister, a deputy,<BR>an agent, &c.<BR>—नियोग्य्-अर्थ-ग्रहोपाय (˚ह-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. the resource of confiscating the property<BR>of men in office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग्य|नियोग्यः
नि-योग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be enjoined or prescribed;<BR>fit to be appointed or authorized, able or qualified<BR>for a duty [cf. नि-योज्य]; (अस्), m. (according to Vopa-<BR>deva) a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजन|नियोजनं
नि-योजन, अम्, n. tying or fastening (as an<BR>animal to the Yūpa or sacrificial post); uniting,<BR>attaching to; that with which anything is fastened<BR>or tied (Ved.); ordering, prescribing, commanding,<BR>directing; urging, impelling; appointing (e. g. क्रि-<BR>यासु, to affairs); (ई), f. a halter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजनीय
नि-योजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attached or joined<BR>to, to be appointed or authorized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजयितव्य
नि-योजयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), to be<BR>appointed, to be commanded or urged or directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजित
नि-योजित, अस्, आ, अम्, joined or attached to, con-<BR>nected with, adapted to; appointed, authorized,<BR>commissioned; directed, ordered; impelled, urged,<BR>instigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोज्य|नियोज्यः
नि-योज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fastened or attached<BR>to; fit to be appointed or employed in; to be ordered,<BR>commanded, directed, instigated; proper to be en-<BR>joined; (अस्), m. a functionary, official, employé,<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत|नियुतं
नियुत नि-युत. See under 2. नि-यु, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत्सा
नियुत्सा नि-युत्सा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. युध्<BR>with नि without reduplication), N. of the wife of<BR>Pra-stāva and mother of Vi-bhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुद्ध|नियुद्धं
नि-युद्ध, अम्, n. (fr. rt. युध् with नि), fight-<BR>ing, especially fighting on foot, close fight or combat,<BR>personal struggle.<BR>—नियुद्ध-भू, ऊस्, f. a battle-<BR>field, a place where close fighting has taken place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोद्धृ
नि-योद्धृ, धा, m. a combatant, a wrestler, a<BR>boxer; a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोधक|नियोधकः
नि-योधक, अस्, m. a fighter, combatant, wrestler,<BR>pugilist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग|नियोगः
नियोग नि-योग. See under नि-युज् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्
निर् निर् euphonically substituted for निस्,<BR>q. v., before vowels and soft consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंश
निरंश निर्-अंश, अस्, आ, अम्, having no part<BR>or fraction remaining, whole.<BR>—निरंश-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of having no part or fraction over,<BR>wholeness, completeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंशु
निरंशु निर्-अंशु, उस्, उस्, उ, having no rays,<BR>rayless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरक्ष|निरक्षः
निरक्ष निर्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having no dice;<BR>having no latitude; (अस्), m. (in astronomy) the<BR>place of no latitude, i. e. the terrestrial equator.<BR>—निरक्ष-देश, अस्, m. a first meridian, as Laṅkā;<BR>a place where the sun is always vertical and the days<BR>and nights are equal; the equatorial region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरग्नि
निरग्नि निर्-अग्नि, इस्, इस्, इ, or निरग्निक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having no fire, having lost or neglected the<BR>consecrated fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरघ
निरघ निर्-अघ, अस्, आ, अम्, sinless, blame-<BR>less, free from fault or imperfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरङ्कुश|निरंकुश|निरङ्कुशः
निरङ्कुश निर्-अङ्कुश, अस्, आ, अम्, unchecked<BR>(lit. not held by a hook), uncontrolled, unruly, self-<BR>willed, unfettered, independant, completely free;<BR>(अम्), ind. freely.<BR>—निरङ्कुश-ता, f. or निरङ्कुश-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. unruliness, independance, self-will, wil-<BR>fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरङ्ग|निरंग
निरङ्ग निर्-अङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having no re-<BR>sources, deprived of expedients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरज्
निरज् निर्-अज्, cl. 1. P. -अजति, -अजितुम् (Ved.<BR>inf. -अजे), Ved. to drive or bring out, extricate, re-<BR>move; to issue out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरजिन
निरजिन निर्-अजिन, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>skin or hide, skinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरञ्छन
निरञ्छन नि-रञ्छन, अम्, n. (fr. रञ्छ् =<BR>लञ्छ् with नि), a mark or knot in a measuring line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरञ्जन|निरंजन|निरञ्जनः
निरञ्जन 1. निर्-अञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>collyrium or ointment, unstained, untinged, unblack-<BR>ened, unpainted; free from falsehood; artless; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva; N. of one of the attendants<BR>of Śiva; (आ), f. an epithet of Durgā; the day of<BR>full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरञ्जन|निरंजन|निरञ्जनः
निरञ्जन 2. नि-रञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, void of<BR>passion or emotion, (applied to the Supreme Being.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरण्
निरण् नि-रण्, cl. 1. P. -रणति, -रणितुम्,<BR>Ved. to rejoice, delight in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत|निरतं
निरत नि-रत. See नि-रम्, p. 492, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरतिशय|निरतिशयः
निरतिशय निर्-अतिशय, अस्, आ, अम्, unsur-<BR>passed.<BR>—निरतिशय-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being<BR>unsurpassed, unsurpassedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत्यय
निरत्यय निर्-अत्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>danger, dangerless, secure, infallible, completely<BR>successful, faultless, unblamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरधिष्ठान
निरधिष्ठान निर्-अधिष्ठान, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing no fixed resting-place, having no solid basis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरध्व
निरध्व निर्-अध्व, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably)<BR>one who has lost his way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोश|निरनुक्रोशः
निरनुक्रोश निर्-अनुक्रोश, अस्, m. absence of<BR>compassion, hard-heartedness, unmercifulness; (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), uncompassionate, without pity, pitiless, merci-<BR>less; hard-hearted towards any person or thing (with<BR>loc.).<BR>—निरनुक्रोश-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting without<BR>compassion or pitilessly.<BR>—निरनुक्रोश-ता, f. piti-<BR>lessness, unmercifulness; hard-heartedness, cruelty.<BR>—निरनुक्रोश-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, uncompassionate,<BR>ruthless, hard-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुग
निरनुग निर्-अनुग, अस्, आ, अम्, unattended,<BR>without retinue or followers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुग्रह
निरनुग्रह निर्-अनुग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, unfa-<BR>vourable, unkind, ungracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुनासिक
निरनुनासिक निर्-अनुनासिक, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>marked with the nasal symbol called Anunāsika<BR>(Gram. 7), not nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुमान
निरनुमान निर्-अनुमान, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>inference, not binding one's self to conclusions or<BR>consequences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुरोध
निरनुरोध निर्-अनुरोध, अस्, आ, अम्, unfa-<BR>vourable, unfriendly, unkind, ungracious, unamiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तर|निरंतर|निरन्तरं
निरन्तर निर्-अन्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, without any<BR>intermediate space, having no intervening space,<BR>granting no room or free space, having no interval,<BR>closely contiguous, close; closely connected, conti-<BR>nuous; uninterrupted, continual, constant; without<BR>interstices, completely filled, compact, dense, coarse,<BR>gross; persevering, faithful, true (as a friend); un-<BR>concealed, not hidden from view; not other or dif-<BR>ferent, similar, identical; (अम्), ind. without inter-<BR>vening space, without interval, without interruption,<BR>constantly, incessantly, continually; closely, tightly,<BR>firmly; immediately.<BR>—निरन्तराभ्यास (˚र-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. constant repetition or study, continual reading<BR>to one's self; diligent and uninterrupted exercise or<BR>practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तराल|निरंतराल
निरन्तराल निर्-अन्तराल, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>an intervening space, without intervals or interstices;<BR>close, contracted, narrow.<BR>—निरन्तराल-ता, f. close<BR>contiguity, closeness, compactness, narrowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्धस्
निरन्धस् निर्-अन्धस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, foodless,<BR>without food, hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्न
निरन्न निर्-अन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, foodless, want-<BR>ing food, hungry, starving; giving no food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्वय
निरन्वय निर्-अन्वय, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>offspring or descendants, childless; unconnected with,<BR>unrelated; not agreeing with the context (of a sen-<BR>tence); without logical connection, without regular<BR>order or sequence, unmethodical; without being seen<BR>or observed, out of sight, not visibly committed<BR>(Manu VIII. 332).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरप
निरप निर्-अप, अस्, आ, अम्, waterless, desti-<BR>tute of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपत्रप|निरपत्रपः
निरपत्रप निर्-अपत्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, shame-<BR>less, impudent; bold, confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपराध|निरपराधः
निरपराध निर्-अपराध, अस्, m. faultless-<BR>ness, innocence; (अस्, आ, अम्), unoffending, inoffen-<BR>sive, innocent, faultless, guiltless, blameless.<BR>—निर्-<BR>अपराध-ता, f. faultlessness, innocence.<BR>—निरप-<BR>राध-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, faultless, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपवर्त|निरपवर्त्त
निरपवर्त निर्-अपवर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, not re-<BR>turning or turning back; (in arithmetic) leaving no<BR>common measure, not to be divided by a common<BR>divisor, reduced to the lowest terms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपवाद
निरपवाद निर्-अपवाद, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>censure, without reproof, blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपाय
निरपाय निर्-अपाय, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>destruction or decay, imperishable, eternal, free from<BR>detriment or loss, free from harm or evil; infallible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्ष|निरपेक्षः
निरपेक्ष निर्-अपेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, disregard-<BR>ing, not taking notice of (with loc.); careless, negli-<BR>gent, without desire, indifferent; not expecting any-<BR>thing from another; independant of, unconnected or<BR>unconcerned with; (often without any object) re-<BR>gardless, indifferent (to praise or blame); without<BR>purpose or hope; (आ), f. indifference; disregard,<BR>the absence of expectation; (अम्), n. without regard,<BR>regardlessly, accidentally.<BR>—निरपेक्ष-ता, f. or<BR>निरपेक्ष-त्व, अम्, n. disregard, indifference;<BR>independance; relationlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्षित
निर्-अपेक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, disregarded; regardless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्षिन्
निर्-अपेक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, disregarding, indifferent,<BR>not expecting anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्ष्य
निर्-अपेक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिभव
निरभिभव निर्-अभिभव, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>subject to defeat or humiliation, not disgraced; not to<BR>be surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिमान
निरभिमान निर्-अभिमान or निर्-अभीमान,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, exempt from pride, free from self-con-<BR>ceit, devoid of egotism; unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिलाष
निरभिलाष निर्-अभिलाष, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no desire for, not intent upon, indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभ्र
निरभ्र निर्-अभ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, cloudless; (ए),<BR>ind. in a cloudless sky, when the sky is unclouded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरम्
निरम् नि-रम्, cl. 1. A. -रमते, -रन्तुम्,<BR>Ved. to delight in, be delighted; to rest, repose,<BR>desist: Caus. -रामयति, -यितुम्, Aor. -अरीरमत्,<BR>Ved. to gladden; to cause to rest or abide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत|निरतं
नि-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged or interested in;<BR>attached or devoted to; pleased, delighted; rested,<BR>ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरति|निरतिः
नि-रति, इस्, f. delighting in; attachment to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरमण
नि-रमण, अम्, n. delighting in; resting; (in<BR>Śata-patha-Brāhmaṇa XIII. 4, 2, 5, नि-रमण is<BR>by some separated into निर्-अमण and explained to<BR>mean ‘exhausted,’ ‘worn out.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरमर्ष
निरमर्ष निर्-अमर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, not im-<BR>patient; patient, apathetic, devoid of energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरमित्र
निरमित्र निर्-अमित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>foes, free from enemies; (अस्), m., N. of several<BR>persons; of a son of Nakula; of a king of Tri-garta;<BR>of a son of Khaṇḍa-pāṇi or Daṇḍa-pāṇi, (also निर्-<BR>आमित्र); of a son of Ayutāyus; of a sage, con-<BR>sidered as a son of Śiva, (also निर्-आमित्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरम्बर
निरम्बर निर्-अम्बर, अस्, आ, अम्, undressed,<BR>naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरम्बु|निरंबु
निरम्बु निर्-अम्बु, उस्, उस्, उ, abstaining from<BR>water, not drinking; waterless, destitute of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरय|निरयः
निरय निर्-अय, अस्, m. ‘without happiness,’<BR>hell [cf. तिर्यन्-निरय]; Niraya or Hell personified<BR>as a child of fear and death; (according to some<BR>निर्-अय, in the sense of ‘hell,’ is fr. निर्-इ and means<BR>‘exit,’ ‘egress from life.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरयण
निर्-अयण, अम्, n., Ved. egression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्गल|निरर्गलः
निरर्गल निर्-अर्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, unbarred,<BR>without a bolt or hindrance, unobstructed, unrestrained,<BR>unimpeded; irresistible; (अम्), ind. without bolt or<BR>bar; without restraint or constraint, freely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थ|निरर्थः
निरर्थ निर्-अर्थ, अस्, m. loss, detriment;<BR>nonsense; (अस्, आ, अम्), destitute of wealth, poor;<BR>useless; meaningless, unmeaning, nonsensical, pur-<BR>poseless, vain; (a consonant is called निर्-अर्थ, not<BR>fulfilling its purpose if it is not followed by a vowel.)<BR>—निरर्थ-ता, f. senselessness, nonsense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थक|निरर्थकं
निर्-अर्थक, अस्, आ or इका or अकी (?), अम्, not<BR>fulfilling one's aim or object, purposeless, useless, vain,<BR>unprofitable; having no reasonable sense, unmeaning,<BR>nonsensical; a consonant which is not followed by a<BR>vowel; (अम्), ind. without a purpose, uselessly, in<BR>vain.<BR>—निरर्थक-त्व, अम्, n. uselessness, vanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्द्
निरर्द् निर्-अर्द्, cl. 1. P. -अर्दति, -अर्दितुम्,<BR>Ved. to stream forth, flow out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्बुद
निरर्बुद निर्-अर्बुद, अस्, m.? (with Bud-<BR>dhists) N. of a hell in which the wicked are punished<BR>by excessive cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरव|निरवः
निरव निर्-अव, अस्, आ, अम्? (occurring only<BR>in the gen. sing. निर्-अवस्य, which might be the<BR>ind. part. of rt. सो with preps. निर् and अव; said by<BR>others to be = नि = निस् + रव, अस्, m. loss of voice;<BR>but according to Sāy.) Ved. having no protector or<BR>uttering praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवकाश
निरवकाश निर्-अवकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>free space; having no room for moving freely,<BR>wanting an opportunity, without leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवग्रह|निरवग्रहः
निरवग्रह निर्-अवग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>obstruction or obstacle, unrestrained, unchecked, un-<BR>controlled; irresistible; free, independant; self-willed,<BR>unmanageable, headstrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवत्त
निरवत्त निर्-अव-त्त, निर्-अव-त्ति. See un-<BR>der निर्-अव-दो, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवदय्
निरवदय् निर्-अव-दय्, cl. 1. A. -दयते,<BR>Ved. to distribute, allot a share or shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवदो
निरवदो निर्-अव-दो [cf. 3. दा], cl. 2. 4. P.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">Page0492-c+ 72</a>]<BR>Ved. -दाति and -द्यति, -दातुम्, to distribute, allot<BR>a share, give any one his share, to satisfy a claim; to<BR>divide completely among.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवत्त
निर्-अव-त्त, अस्, आ, अम्, distributed, completely<BR>divided or allotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवत्ति
निर्-अव-त्ति, इस्, f., Ved. allotment or distribution<BR>of shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवद्य
निरवद्य निर्-अवद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unblamable,<BR>blameless, faultless, unobjectionable, unexceptionable;<BR>(अम्), n. (or आ?), f. unblamableness, blamelessness,<BR>faultlessness; (अस् or अम्), m. or n. (?), a particular high<BR>number.<BR>—निरवद्य-त्व, अम्, n. blamelessness,<BR>unblamableness, excellence.<BR>—निरवद्य-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, unblamable, blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवधि
निरवधि निर्-अवधि, इस्, इस्, इ, without bounds<BR>or boundaries, unlimited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवयव
निरवयव निर्-अवयव, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>limbs or members, without component parts, not<BR>consisting of parts, indivisible.<BR>—निरवयव-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. indivisibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवरोध
निरवरोध निर्-अवरोध, अस्, आ, अम्, unre-<BR>strained, unobstructed, unopposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवलम्ब|निरवलंब
निरवलम्ब निर्-अवलम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no prop or stay; unsupported; not affording support;<BR>not depending or relying on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवलम्बन
निर्-अवलम्बन, अम्, n. want of a prop, want<BR>of reliance, want of a person or thing to depend<BR>upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवशेष
निरवशेष निर्-अवशेष, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>a residue, complete, whole; (एण), ind. completely,<BR>totally, fully, particularly, circumstantially.<BR>—निर्-<BR>अवशेष-तस्, ind. completely, &c. (= निरवशे-<BR>षेण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवसाद
निरवसाद निर्-अवसाद, अस्, आ, अम्, not cast<BR>down, cheerful, good-humoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवस्कृत
निरवस्कृत निर्-अवस्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed,<BR>clean?; [cf. अवस्-कर, अन्-अवस्कर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवस्तार
निरवस्तार निर्-अवस्तार, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>a bed or coverlet; not strewn (with leaves &c.), bare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवहालिका
निरवहालिका निर्-अवहालिका, f. a fence, a<BR>hedge, an outer wall; [cf. अवहालिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरविन्द
निरविन्द निरविन्द, अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवेक्ष्
निरवेक्ष् निर्-अवेक्ष् (-अव-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-ईक्षते, -ईक्षितुम्, to perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवेक्ष्य
निर्-अवेक्ष्य, ind. having perceived or observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरव्यय
निरव्यय निर्-अव्यय, अस्, आ, अम्, undecaying,<BR>eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरश्
निरश् निर्-अश्, cl. 9. P. -अश्नाति, &c., Ved.<BR>to eat up, consume entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशित
निर्-अशित, अस्, आ, अम्, eaten up, completely con-<BR>sumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशन|निरशनं
निरशन निर्-अशन, अस्, आ, अम्, abstaining<BR>from food; (अम्), n. going without food, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरष्ट|निरष्टः
निरष्ट निर्-अष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. अश् or<BR>अक्ष् with निस्), Ved. deprived of vigour, exhausted;<BR>(Sāy.) = निर्-आकृत, driven away, scattered, dispersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्
निरस् निर्-अस्, cl. 4. P. -अस्यति, -असितुम्, to<BR>cast out, throw away, drive away, banish, expel, evict,<BR>drive back, send back; to keep off; to turn out (of<BR>doors); to reject, repudiate, decline, refuse; to re-<BR>move; to tear out, strip off; to stretch out (e. g.<BR>हस्तौ निरस्यति or -ते, he stretches out the hands);<BR>to annihilate, destroy, subdue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरसन|निरसनं
निर्-असन, अस्, ई, अम्, expelling, removing, re-<BR>jecting; vomiting, spitting out; (अम्), n. expelling,<BR>ejecting; expulsion, removal, rejection, denial, con-<BR>tradiction, refusal, disallowance; vomiting forth,<BR>spitting out; suppressing, checking; killing, destroy-<BR>ing, destruction, extermination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरसनीय
निर्-असनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown out, to be<BR>driven away or expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्त|निरस्तः
निर्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, cast out or away, expelled;<BR>thrown out or away, cast off; thrown off (as from a<BR>horse); driven away, expelled, banished; rejected,<BR>repudiated, abandoned, deserted; disallowed; re-<BR>futed; sent forth, sent away; deprived of, removed;<BR>shot off, discharged (as an arrow); spit out; uttered<BR>hurriedly or rapidly (as a speech or word); torn out<BR>or away; destroyed; broken (as an agreement);<BR>suppressed, checked; (अम्), n. rejecting; dropping<BR>or leaving out, not pronouncing (regarded as a fault<BR>in pronunciation).<BR>—निरस्त-भेद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having all difference removed, identical.<BR>—निरस्त-<BR>राग, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has abandoned worldly<BR>desires or has devoted himself to religious penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्य
1. निर्-अस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be expelled or driven<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्य
2. निरस्य, ind. having cast out, thrown out or<BR>ejected, having expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्यत्
निर्-अस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, ejecting, throwing out;<BR>expelling; abandoning, neglecting, scattering, de-<BR>stroying, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्यमान
निर्-अस्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being thrown out or<BR>expelled; being abandoned; being suppressed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास|निरासः
निर्-आस, अस्, m. throwing out, casting out, ejection,<BR>expulsion, removal, abandonment; dropping (a sound<BR>or letter &c.); vomiting; opposing, contradiction,<BR>refutation.<BR>—निरास-गुटिका, f. a pill to produce<BR>vomiting; (also written निराश-गुटिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरासन|निरासनं
निर्-आसन, अम्, n. = निर्-असन, p. 492, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस|निरसः
निरस नि-रस, अस्, आ, अम्, = नी-रस, without<BR>flavour, tasteless, insipid, dry; (अस्), m. want of<BR>flavour, insipidity; want of juice, dryness; want of<BR>passion or feeling; (आ), f. a species of grass (= निः-<BR>श्रेणिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्त्र
निरस्त्र निर्-अस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, weaponless,<BR>unarmed; (fought) without weapons (as a battle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्थि
निरस्थि निर्-अस्थि, इस्, इस्, इ, having no bones,<BR>boneless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरह्
निरह् निर्-अह्, only in perf. निर्-आह, Ved.<BR>to utter, pronounce, express.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्कार|निरहंकार
निरहङ्कार निर्-अहङ्कार, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from egotism, devoid of selfishness, free from pride,<BR>humble, lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्कृत|निरहंकृत
निर्-अहङ्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, having no self-con-<BR>sciousness, without individuality or personality; un-<BR>selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्कृति|निरहंकृति
निर्-अहङ्कृति, इस्, इस्, इ, free from egotism or<BR>selfishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्क्रिय|निरहंक्रिय
निर्-अहङ्क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, having no individu-<BR>ality or personality, without self-consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्क्रिया|निरहंक्रिया
निर्-अहङ्क्रिया, f. absence of egotism or selfishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहम्
निरहम् निर्-अहम् or निर्-अहम्मति, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, devoid of self-conceit, free from selfishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक|निराकः
निराक निराक, अस्, m. cooking; sweat; the<BR>recompense of a bad action; (wrong reading for<BR>नि-पाक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरण|निराकरणं
निराकरण निर्-आकरण. See under निर्-<BR>आ-कृ, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकाङ्क्ष|निराकांक्ष
निराकाङ्क्ष निर्-आकाङ्क्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, expect-<BR>ing nothing, wishing nothing, free from desire;<BR>wanting nothing to fill up or make complete (as the<BR>sense of a sentence or word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकाङ्क्षिन्
निराकाङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, expecting nothing, wish-<BR>ing or wanting nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
निराकार 1. निर्-आकार, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see<BR>निर्-आ-कृ, col. 2), devoid of form, deprived of one's<BR>natural form; without external appearance; formless,<BR>shapeless, deformed; disguised; unassuming; not<BR>claiming anything for one's self, modest; (अस्), m.<BR>heaven, Viṣṇu; Śiva; the universal Spirit, God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
1. निर्-आकृति, इस्, इस्, इ, formless, shapeless, de-<BR>formed, ugly; (इस्), m. a person who has not duly<BR>gone through a course of study, (especially applied<BR>however to the religious student who has not duly<BR>read the Vedas); one who neglects the five great<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">Page0493-b+ 73</a>]<BR>religious obligations, who does not worship the gods,<BR>&c.; a Brāhman who neglects the duties of his caste<BR>(आकृति) by not going through a regular course of<BR>study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकाश
निराकाश निर्-आकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>free space, leaving no room, completely filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकुल
निराकुल निर्-आकुल, अस्, आ, अम्, unconfused,<BR>not disordered; unperplexed; unbewildered; clear;<BR>steady, calm; perspicuous; (अम्), n. calmness, per-<BR>spicuity, clearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृ
निराकृ निर्-आ-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to separate or divide off (Ved.); to<BR>push away, turn or drive away, repudiate, keep away,<BR>keep off, banish, expel, eject, remove, reject; to<BR>refuse; to oppose, obstruct, contradict; to disallow;<BR>to omit, intermit; to frustrate; to contemn, spurn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरण|निराकरणं
निर्-आकरण, अम्, n. repudiating, expelling, turn-<BR>ing out, turning away, throwing off; removing,<BR>banishing; repudiation, obstruction, opposition, con-<BR>tradiction, rejection; refutation, reply; contempt,<BR>disesteem; forgetting; neglecting the chief sacrificial<BR>or religious duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरिष्णु|निराकरिष्णुः
निर्-आकरिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, expelling, repudiating,<BR>a repudiator; obstructive, obstructing, hindering from<BR>(with abl.); spurning, disdaining, despising; seeking<BR>to remove from (with abl.), envying any person<BR>anything (abl.); forgetful.<BR>—निराकरिष्णु-ता, f.<BR>the state of being a repudiator; envy, malevolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकर्तृ
निर्-आकर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a repudiator, repudi-<BR>ating; a despiser, contemner (as of the gods).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
2. निर्-आकार, अस्, m. rebuke, reproach, censure,<BR>blame. (For 1. निर्-आकार see col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृत|निराकृतः
निर्-आकृत, अस्, आ, अम्, pushed away, driven away,<BR>repudiated, expelled, banished, ejected, rejected, re-<BR>moved, set aside, turned away, turned out; thrown<BR>off; divorced; refused, denied; refuted, replied to;<BR>contemned, despised, spurned, made light of; de-<BR>prived of.<BR>—निराकृतान्योत्तर (˚त-अन्य-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, refuting every answer, irrefutable, irrefragable.<BR>—निराकृतान्योत्तर-त्व, अम्, n. irrefutableness,<BR>irrefragableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
2. निर्-आकृति, इस्, f. repudiation, rejection; refusal,<BR>disallowance; obstruction, obstacle, impediment, in-<BR>terruption; contradiction, opposition; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>impeding, obstructing; annihilating, destroying; (इस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of the first Manu Sāvarṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृतिन्
निर्-आकृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (probably) repudiating,<BR>impeding, obstructing; avoiding; making no exertion<BR>either to do or avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रिया
निर्-आक्रिया, f. repudiation, expulsion, removal;<BR>contradiction, denial, refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
निराकृति 1. and 2. निर्-आकृति. See under<BR>1. निर्-आकार, col. 1, and under निर्-आ-कृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रन्द|निराक्रन्दः
निराक्रन्द निर्-आक्रन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, not com-<BR>plaining; a place where no sound can be heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रम्
निराक्रम् निर्-आ-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रामति,<BR>-क्रमते, -क्रान्तुम् and -क्रमितुम्, to come<BR>forth, to go out of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रिया
निराक्रिया निर्-आक्रिया. See निर्-आ-कृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रोश
निराक्रोश निर्-आक्रोश, अस्, आ, अम्, unaccused,<BR>unreviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराग
निराग नि-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, passionless, dis-<BR>passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरागम
निरागम निर्-आगम, अस्, आ, अम्, not founded<BR>on revelation, not resting on scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरागस्
निरागस् निर्-आगस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, sinless, fault-<BR>less, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराग्रह
निराग्रह निर्-आग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, not insist-<BR>ing upon, not peremptory or obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराचार|निराचारः
निराचार निर्-आचार, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>approved usages or customs, lawless, barbarian, (espe-<BR>cially applied to those people who have not the ordi-<BR>nances of the Vedas or distinction of castes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराजीव्य
निराजीव्य निर्-आजीव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not yield-<BR>ing subsistence, not granting a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराडम्बर|निराडंबर
निराडम्बर निर्-आडम्बर, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>drums.<BR>—निराडम्बर-सुन्दर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>(perhaps) beautiful in itself, not requiring a drum to<BR>attract attention or not requiring ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरातङ्क|निरातंक|निरातङ्कः
निरातङ्क निर्-आतङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, not feeling<BR>pain or uneasiness, without ailment, well, comfort-<BR>able; not causing pain or ailment or disagreeable<BR>feelings; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरातप
निरातप निर्-आतप, अस्, आ, अम्, not pene-<BR>trated by the sun's rays, shady; (आ), f. the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरात्मक
निरात्मक निर्-आत्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, or निर्-<BR>आत्मन्, आ, आ, अ, or निरात्म-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>no separate soul or no individual existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादर
निरादर निर्-आदर, अस्, आ, अम्, showing no<BR>respect, disrespectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादान
निरादान निर्-आदान, अस्, आ, अम्, taking<BR>nothing, not taking, one from whom nothing is<BR>taken; an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादिष्ट
निरादिष्ट निर्-आदिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, paid off<BR>(as a debt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादेश|निरादेशः
निर्-आदेश, अस्, m. complete payment or discharge<BR>of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराधा
निराधा निर्-आ-धा, cl. 3. P. A. -दधाति,<BR>-धत्ते, &c., Ved. to take out of, take away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराधान
निराधान निर्-आधान, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराधार
निराधार निर्-आधार, अस्, आ, अम्, without a<BR>receptacle; without a fulcrum or support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराधि
निराधि निर्-आधि, इस्, इस्, इ, free from anxiety,<BR>undisturbed by care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरानन्द
निरानन्द निर्-आनन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, joyless,<BR>sad, sorrowful; not delighting.<BR>—निर्-आनन्द-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, causing no pleasure, causing care or<BR>sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरान्त्र
निरान्त्र निर्-आन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. evisce-<BR>rated, disembowelled; having the entrails hanging<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरापद्
निरापद् निर्-आपद्, त्, f. freedom from mis-<BR>fortune or calamity, a prosperous condition, security;<BR>(त्, त्, त्), free from calamity or misfortune, prosperous,<BR>fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराबाध|निराबाधः
निराबाध निर्-आबाध, अस्, आ, अम्, undis-<BR>turbed, unmolested, unvexed, secure from disturb-<BR>ance; unobstructed; not disturbing, not molesting,<BR>not injuring, not paining; frivolously or not really<BR>vexatious.<BR>—निर्-आबाध-कर, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>causing injury or pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामय|निरामयः
निरामय निर्-आमय, अस्, अम्, m. n. freedom<BR>from illness, health, happiness, welfare; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>free from illness, healthy, well, hale, recovered from<BR>sickness, free from disease; free from taint, pure;<BR>guileless; free from defects or failings; infallible;<BR>not liable to failure or miscarriage; complete, full;<BR>(अस्), m. a wild goat; a hog, a boar; N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामर्द
निरामर्द निर्-आमर्द, अस्, m. ‘not oppress-<BR>ing,’ N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामालु|निरामालुः
निरामालु निर्-आमालु, उस्, m. (fr. निराम-<BR>आलु?), the wood apple, Feronia Elephantum; [cf.<BR>कपित्थ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामित्र
निरामित्र निर्-आमित्र. See निर्-अमित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामिन्
निरामिन् नि-रामिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. remain-<BR>ing, staying in; (Sāy.) delighting in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामिष
निरामिष निर्-आमिष, अस्, आ, अम्, fleshless,<BR>without meat or prey; not receiving wages; having<BR>no sensual desires, free from covetousness.<BR>—निरा-<BR>मिषाशिन् (˚ष-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, not feeding on<BR>meat; living without meat; free from sensual desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0493-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराय|निरायः
निराय निर्-आय, अस्, आ, अम्, having no in-<BR>come or revenue, profitless, yielding no income or<BR>profit.<BR>—निर्-आय-व्यय-वत्, आन्, m. having neither<BR>income nor expenditure, an idler who lives by clan-<BR>destine means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायत
निरायत 1. निर्-आयत, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. यम्<BR>with आ and निस्), stretched out, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायत
निरायत 2. निर्-आयत, अस्, आ, अम्, unex-<BR>tended, contracted, compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायास
निरायास निर्-आयास, अस्, आ, अम्, not causing<BR>trouble, not requiring efforts, not fatiguing; easily<BR>attainable, easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायुध
निरायुध निर्-आयुध, अस्, आ, अम्, weapon-<BR>less, disarmed, unarmed, defenceless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरारम्भ
निरारम्भ निर्-आरम्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, not un-<BR>dertaking enterprises, not enterprising, abstaining<BR>from all work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालक
निरालक निरालक, अस्, m. a species of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालम्ब|निरालंब
निरालम्ब निर्-आलम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>prop or support, not resting or depending on another,<BR>independent, self-supported, not relying on another,<BR>standing alone, friendless; (अस्), m., N. of a man<BR>mentioned in the Śaṅkara-vijaya; (आ), f. spikenard,<BR>= आकाश-मांसी; (अम्), ind. without support, in-<BR>dependently.<BR>—निरालम्बोपनिषद् (˚ब-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालम्बन
निर्-आलम्बन, अस्, आ, अम्, having no prop,<BR>without support, not resting on another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालस्य
निरालस्य निर्-आलस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालोक|निरालोकः
निरालोक निर्-आलोक, अस्, आ, अम्, not looking<BR>about, not moving the eye, without moving the eyes;<BR>deprived of light, dark; invisible, uninvestigable (?);<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरावर्ष
निरावर्ष निर्-आवर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, unpene-<BR>trated by rain, protecting from rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश|निराशः
निराश निर्-आश, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + 1. आ-शा;<BR>cf. आ-शंस्), without hope, hopeless, despairing of<BR>(with loc., dat., or with प्रति and acc., e. g. स्व-<BR>जीविते or स्व-जीविताय or स्व-जीवितम् प्रति निर्-<BR>आशः, despairing of one's own life); depriving of all<BR>hope; [cf. नैराश्य.]<BR>—निराश-त्व, अम्, n. hope-<BR>lessness, despair.<BR>—निराशी-भाव, अस्, m. hopeless-<BR>ness, despair.<BR>—निराशी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become<BR>hopeless; despairing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराशक
निर्-आशक, अस्, आ, अम्, desponding, despairing of<BR>(with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराशिन्
निर्-आशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, hopeless.<BR>—निराशि-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. = निराश-त्व, hopelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराशङ्क|निराशंक
निराशङ्क निर्-आशङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless;<BR>(अम्), ind. fearlessly, without fear or hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराशिस्
निराशिस् निर्-आशिस्, ईस्, ईस्, इस् (see आ-शास्),<BR>having no wishes or hopes; without a blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश्रम
निराश्रम निर्-आश्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, or निर्-<BR>आश्रमिन्; ई, इणी, इ, not being in one of the four<BR>periods or orders of a Brāhman's life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश्रय
निराश्रय निर्-आश्रय, अस्, आ, अम्, supportless,<BR>without prop or stay, not resting or depending on,<BR>unsupported, self-supported, without shelter or refuge,<BR>unprotected, destitute; not deep (as a wound?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास|निरासः
निरास निर्-आस, अस्, m. See under निर्-अस्<BR>at p. 493, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरासित्व
निरासित्व निरासि-त्व incorrect reading for<BR>निराशि-त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास्पद
निरास्पद निर्-आस्पद, अस्, आ, अम्, restless,<BR>having no place of rest, homeless; portionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास्वाद
निरास्वाद निर्-आस्वाद, अस्, आ, अम्, tasteless,<BR>flavourless, unsavoury, yielding no enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास्वाद्य
निर्-आस्वाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unsavoury, giving no<BR>enjoyment.<BR>—निरास्वाद्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most<BR>unsavoury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराहार|निराहारः
निराहार निर्-आहार, अस्, m. want of food,<BR>not eating, fasting; (अस्, आ, अम्), foodless, fasting,<BR>abstaining from food, without food, having nothing<BR>to eat.<BR>—निराहार-ता, f. foodlessness, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराहावत्|निराहावन्त्
निराहावत् निर्-आहा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, for निर्-<BR>आहाव-वत्, without invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरि
निरि निर्-इ, cl. 2. P. -एति, &c., -एतुम्, to go<BR>out, come forth, go off, depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिङ्ग
निरिङ्ग निर्-इङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, immovable,<BR>not moving to and fro, not flickering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिङ्गिनी|निरिंगिनी
निरिङ्गिनी निरिङ्गिनी, f. a veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिच्छ
निरिच्छ निर्-इच्छ, अस्, आ, अम्, without wish<BR>or desire, indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिन्द्रिय|निरिंद्रिय|निरिन्द्रियः
निरिन्द्रिय निर्-इन्द्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. im-<BR>potent, destitute of manly vigour or of strength (in<BR>general); barren; having lost the use of a limb;<BR>imperfect, mutilated, maimed, infirm, weak, frail;<BR>(in Manu IX. 18) without evidence or means of<BR>certain knowledge (according to Kullūka = प्रमाण-<BR>रहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिन्धन|निरिंधन
निरिन्धन निर्-इन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute<BR>of fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरी
निरी नि-री, cl. 9. P. -रिणाति, -रेतुम्, Ved.<BR>to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्ष्
निरीक्ष् निर्-ईक्ष्, cl. 1. A. -ईक्षते, -ईक्षि-<BR>तुम्, to look at, look towards, behold, gaze at, look<BR>about, regard, observe, view, contemplate, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षक
निर्-ईक्षक, अस्, आ, अम्, looking at, seeing, view-<BR>ing, observing, visiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षण|निरीक्षणं
निर्-ईक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking at, regarding;<BR>(अम्), ṇ. look; looking at, regarding, seeing; ex-<BR>pecting; the aspect of the planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षत्
निर्-ईक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, or निर्-ईक्षमाण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, looking at, regarding, expecting, hoping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षा
निर्-ईक्षा, f. looking at, regarding; considera-<BR>tion; hope, expectation; (अया), ind. in respect of,<BR>in relation to, as to (e. g. बलाबल-निरीक्षया, in<BR>respect of strength and weakness; cf. दुर्-निरीक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षिन्
निर्-ईक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, seeing, looking, viewing;<BR>[cf. नातिदूर-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्ष्य
1. निर्-ईक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked at or<BR>regarded; to be considered; [cf. दुर्-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्ष्य
2. निर्-ईक्ष्य, ind. having looked at or viewed<BR>or scanned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्ष्यमाण
निर्-ईक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being looked at or<BR>regarded; looking, (Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 7694.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीति
निरीति निर्-ईति, इस्, इस्, इ, free from calami-<BR>ties or afflictions, painless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीतिक
निर्-ईतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, not inauspicious, not prog-<BR>nosticating calamity, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीश|निरीशं
निरीश निर्-ईश = निर्-ईष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीश्वर
निरीश्वर निर्-ईश्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, godless,<BR>atheistic.<BR>—निरीश्वर-वाद, अस्, m. godlessness,<BR>atheism.<BR>—निरीश्वर-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, atheistical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीष|निरीषं
निरीष निर्-ईष, अम्, n. the body of a<BR>plough (without the pole and ploughshare; also<BR>read निर्-ईश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीह|निरीहः
निरीह निर्-ईह, अस्, आ, अम्, inactive, effort-<BR>less; desireless, not wishful, indifferent, unanxious.<BR>—निरीह-ता, f. or निरीह-त्व, अम्, n. or निर्-ईहा,<BR>f. indifference, absence of desire or effort.<BR>—निरीहा-<BR>वस्था (˚हा-अव्˚), f. a state of indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्त|निरुक्तं
निरुक्त निर्-उक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वच् with<BR>निस्), uttered, pronounced, expressed, explained, de-<BR>fined; loud, distinct; (अम्), n. explanation or ety-<BR>mological interpretation of a word; N. of one of the<BR>six Vedāṅgas or works considered as connected with<BR>the Vedas; glossarial explanation of obscure terms,<BR>(especially those occurring in the Vedas); N. of a<BR>well-known commentary on the Nighaṇṭus by Yāska;<BR>[cf. नैरुक्त, नैरुक्तिक.]<BR>—निरुक्त-कार, अस्,<BR>m. ‘Nirukta-composer,’ N. or epithet of a com-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">Page0494-c+ 73</a>]<BR>mentator on Kāli-dāsa's Megha-dūta.<BR>—निरुक्त-<BR>कृत्, त्, m. epithet of a pupil of Śāka-pūrṇi.<BR>—नि-<BR>रुक्त-ज, अस्, m., N. of a class of sons enumerated<BR>in Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 2615.<BR>—निरुक्त-परि-<BR>शिष्ट, अम्, n., N. of a work supplementary to the<BR>Nirukta.<BR>—निरुक्त-वत्, आन्, m. ‘possessing the Ni-<BR>rukta, author of the Nirukta,’ an epithet of Yāska.<BR>—निरुक्त-वृत्ति, इस्, f. ‘commentary on the Ni-<BR>rukta,’ N. of a commentary on Yāska's Nirukta by<BR>Durgācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्ति|निरुक्तिः
निर्-उक्ति, इस्, f. explanation, etymological inter-<BR>pretation of words; (in rhetoric) an artificial or<BR>poetical explanation of the derivation of a word (e. g.<BR>deriving दोषा-कर, ‘the moon,’ from दोषा +<BR>आकर instead of दोषा + कर); = निर्-उक्त, Yāska's<BR>commentary on the Nighaṇṭus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुच्यमान
निर्-उच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being uttered or<BR>expressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्ष्
निरुक्ष् निर्-उक्ष्, cl. 6. P. -उक्षति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to remove by sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुच्छ्वास|निरुच्छ्वासः
निरुच्छ्वास निर्-उच्छ्वास, अस्, m. absence of<BR>breath, not breathing; (अस्, आ, अम्), without breath-<BR>ing, not breathing, breathless; narrow, contracted,<BR>crowded; (अम्), n. (?) a particular hell where the<BR>wicked cannot breathe.<BR>—निरुच्छ्वास-निपीडित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, pained by not breathing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुज
निरुज नि-रुज, अस्, आ, अम्, for नी-रुज,<BR>healthy, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्तर
निरुत्तर निर्-उत्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>superior; answerless, without a reply, unable to<BR>answer, silenced, posed; (अम्), n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—निरुत्तर-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्पात
निरुत्पात निर्-उत्पात, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>portents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्सव
निरुत्सव निर्-उत्सव, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>festivals, having no festivities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्साह|निरुत्साहः
निरुत्साह निर्-उत्साह, अस्, m. absence of<BR>exertion, want of energy, indolence, pusillanimity;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), without energy, devoid of energy, un-<BR>dertaking nothing, without courage, indolent, indif-<BR>ferent.<BR>—निरुत्साह-ता, f. want of energy, cowardice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्सुक
निरुत्सुक निर्-उत्सुक, अस्, आ, अम्, careless,<BR>indifferent, unconcerned; calm, tranquil, unanxious,<BR>unregretful, having no vehement desire for; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Manu Raivata; one of the<BR>Saptarṣis under the thirteenth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुदक
निरुदक निर्-उदक, अस्, आ, अम्, waterless,<BR>devoid of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्यम
निरुद्यम निर्-उद्यम, अस्, आ, अम्, effortless,<BR>inactive, lazy, at rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्योग|निरुद्योगः
निरुद्योग निर्-उद्योग, अस्, आ, अम्, making<BR>no efforts, lazy, listless, idle; disheartened; cause-<BR>less (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्विग्न
निरुद्विग्न निर्-उद्विग्न or निर्-उद्वेग, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unexcited, undisturbed, free from perturbation,<BR>fearless, sedate, calm.<BR>—निरुद्विग्न-मनस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, undisturbed in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुध्
निरुध् नि-रुध्, cl. 7. P. A. -रुणद्धि,<BR>-रुन्द्धे, -रोद्धुम्, to shut in, shut, obstruct,<BR>stop, hinder, prevent, restrain, check; to confine; to<BR>keep off, remove; to accomplish (?): Caus. -रोध-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to be shut or obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्ध|निरुद्धः
नि-रुद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, stopped, obstructed, re-<BR>strained, checked, hindered, opposed; confined, im-<BR>prisoned; (अस्), m., N. of a prince.<BR>—निरुद्ध-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having the breath obstructed,<BR>suffocated.<BR>—निरुद्ध-गुद, अस्, m. contraction or<BR>obstruction of the rectum.<BR>—निरुद्ध-प्रकश,<BR>अस्, m. stricture of the urethra.<BR>—निरुद्ध-शम-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘whose state of repose is interrupted,’<BR>wearied, tired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुन्धत्
नि-रुन्धत्, अन्, अती, अत्, checking, hindering,<BR>suppressing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुन्धान
नि-रुन्धान, अस्, आ, अम्, obstructing, opposing,<BR>hindering, preventing; depriving of, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोद्धव्य|निरोद्धव्यं
नि-रोद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be shut in or confined,<BR>to be fenced, to be enclosed with a fence or hedge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोध|निरोधः
नि-रोध, अस्, m. shutting in, confinement, locking<BR>up, imprisonment; enclosing, covering up; check,<BR>restraint, coercion, suppression, hindrance, prevention,<BR>obstruction, opposition; annihilation, destruction;<BR>(in dramatic language) disappointment, frustration of<BR>hope; hurting, injuring (= नि-ग्रह); aversion,<BR>disfavour, dislike; (with Buddhists) suppression or<BR>annihilation of pain (one of the four principles); N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोधक
नि-रोधक, अस्, आ, अम्, obstructive, obstructing,<BR>confining, hindering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोधन|निरोधनं
नि-रोधन, अस्, ई, अम्, confining, obstructing;<BR>(अस्), m. (with अवट) N. of a hell; (अम्), n. con-<BR>finement, imprisonment; keeping back, restraining,<BR>keeping down, coercion; denying; (in dramatic<BR>language) disappointment, frustration of hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोधिन्
नि-रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, obstructing, hindering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपक्रम
निरुपक्रम निर्-उपक्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no beginning, without a commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपद्रव|निरुपद्रवः
निरुपद्रव निर्-उपद्रव, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from hostile attacks, free from ravages, not visited<BR>by calamity or affliction, free from adversity or<BR>danger, lucky, happy, undisturbed, unharmed, un-<BR>molested; free from national distress, free from<BR>tyranny; causing no affliction or adversity; peaceful,<BR>secure; not inauspicious (as a star).<BR>—निरुपद्रव-<BR>ता, f. absence of calamity or danger, security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपद्रुत
निर्-उपद्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, not visited by calamities;<BR>not boding evil (as a star).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपधि
निरुपधि निर्-उपधि, इस्, इस्, इ, without guile,<BR>guileless, honest, secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपपत्ति
निरुपपत्ति निर्-उपपत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, unfit, un-<BR>suitable.<BR>—निरुपपत्ति-त्व, अम्, n. unfitness, un-<BR>suitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपपद
निरुपपद निर्-उपपद, अस्, आ, अम्, not con-<BR>nected with a subordinate word; [cf. उप-पद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपप्लव
निरुपप्लव निर्-उपप्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from calamity or disturbance, free from trouble or<BR>alarm; unharmed; not causing adversity; an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपभोग
निरुपभोग निर्-उपभोग, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>enjoying, destitute of enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपम|निरुपमः
निरुपम निर्-उपम, अस्, आ, अम्, peerless,<BR>matchless, without a compeer or equal, unequalled,<BR>incomparable; (अस्), m. a species of poisonous animal<BR>(= गौधेरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपल
निरुपल निर्-उपल, अस्, आ, अम्, stoneless,<BR>free from stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपलेप
निरुपलेप निर्-उपलेप, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>smeared, free from ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपसर्ग
निरुपसर्ग निर्-उपसर्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from portents, not portentous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपस्कृत
निरुपस्कृत निर्-उपस्कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, uncor-<BR>rupted, inartificial, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपहत
निरुपहत निर्-उपहत, अस्, आ, अम्, unhurt,<BR>uninjured, not afflicted; auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपाख्य
निरुपाख्य निर्-उपाख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>perceptible by the eyes, invisible, immaterial; unreal,<BR>false, non-existent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपाधिक
निरुपाधिक निर्-उपाधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>attributes or qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपाय
निरुपाय निर्-उपाय, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>expedients, remediless, helpless; unsuccessful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपेक्ष|निरुपेक्षः
निरुपेक्ष निर्-उपेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, not neg-<BR>lectful; free from trick or fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुप्ति
निरुप्ति निर्-उप्ति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. वप् with निस्),<BR>= 1. निर्-वाप, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुप्य
निर्-उप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be scattered or sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुब्ज्
निरुब्ज् निर्-उब्ज्, cl. 6. P. -उब्जति, &c., Ved.<BR>to press down, cause to flow down, send down, let<BR>loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुष्णीष
निरुष्णीष निर्-उष्णीष, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>a turban or head-dress, bare-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुष्मन्
निरुष्मन् निर्-उष्मन्, आ, आ, अ, devoid of<BR>heat, cold.<BR>—निरुष्म-त्व, अम्, n. absence of heat,<BR>coldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूढ|निरूढः
निरूढ 1. नि-रूढ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि-रुह्),<BR>inherent, conventional, accepted (as the familiar<BR>meaning of words in opposition to their etymological<BR>sense); (अस्), m. (in rhetoric) the force or application<BR>of words according to their natural or received<BR>meanings; (in logic) the inherence of any property<BR>in the term implying it (as of redness in the word<BR>red &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूढ|निरूढः
निरूढ 2. निर्-ऊढ, आ, f. (fr. rt. वह् with<BR>निस्), unmarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्
निरूप् नि-रूप्, cl. 10. P. -रूपयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to perform; to represent, enact, act dramatically; to<BR>see, perceive, look at, look into; to observe, con-<BR>sider, reflect upon; to investigate, examine, look<BR>out for, discover, search; to ascertain; to select,<BR>choose, appoint; to resolve, determine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपण|निरूपणं
नि-रूपण, अस्, ई, अम्, defining, determining;<BR>(अम्), n. form, shape; sight, seeing; looking for,<BR>searching; looking into, investigation, determination,<BR>definition; ascertaining, defining, (in these senses<BR>also नि-रूपणा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपणीय
नि-रूपणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked for; to be<BR>searched into or examined, to be investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपयत्
नि-रूपयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, looking for, investi-<BR>gating, considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपित|निरूपितः
नि-रूपित, अस्, आ, अम्, seen, beheld; discovered,<BR>found; appointed, elected, chosen, deputed; consi-<BR>dered, weighed; ascertained, determined, resolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपिति|निरूपितिः
नि-रूपिति, इस्, f. definition (of an idea), ascertain-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्य
1. नि-रूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be seen or defined or<BR>ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्य
2. नि-रूप्य, ind. having seen or considered.<BR>—निरूप्य-ता, f. or निरूप्य-त्व, अम्, n. ascer-<BR>taining, determining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूष्मन्
निरूष्मन् निर्-ऊष्मन्. See निर्-उष्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूह्
निरूह् निर्-ऊह् [cf. rt. 1. ऊह्], cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-ऊहति, -ते, &c., Ved. inf. निर्-ऊहितवै, to push<BR>out, draw out, remove: Caus. -ऊहयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to draw out or purge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूढ|निरूढः
3. निर्-ऊढ, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn out, purged,<BR>eviscerated; (for 2. निर्-ऊढ see above.)<BR>—निर्-<BR>ऊढ-पशु-प्रयोग, अस्, m., N. of a treatise on<BR>particular sacrifices, (see the next.)<BR>—निरूढ-<BR>पशु-बन्ध, अस्, m. ‘the offering or oblation of an<BR>eviscerated animal,’ N. of one of the regular Havir-<BR>yajñas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूढि|निरूढिः
निर्-ऊढि, इस्, f. (also to be referred to rt. वह्<BR>with निस्), fame, celebrity, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूह|निरूहः
1. निर्-ऊह, अस्, m. a purging clyster; an enema<BR>not of an oily kind, = नि-ग्रह?; (for 2. निर्-<BR>ऊह see below.)<BR>—निरूह-वस्ति-विधि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of the twenty-fifth chapter of the Śārṅga-dhara-saṃ-<BR>hitā, a medical work by Śārṅga-dhara.<BR>—निरूहा-<BR>धिकार (˚ह-अध्˚), अस्, m., N. of a chapter of a<BR>medical work by Vṛnda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूहण|निरूहणं
1. निर्-ऊहण, अम्, n. causing to purge with a<BR>clyster; administering enemas not of an oily kind.<BR>(For 2. निर्-ऊहण see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूहित
निर्-ऊहित, अस्, आ, अम्, purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूह|निरूहः
निरूह 2. निर्-ऊह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. ऊह् with<BR>निस्), logic, disputation; certainty, ascertainment.<BR>(For 1. निर्-ऊह see above; for 3. see next col.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूहण|निरूहणं
2. निर्-ऊहण, अम्, n. ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूह|निरूहः
निरूह 3. निर्-ऊह, अस्, m. (for 1. and 2.<BR>see col. 2), a sentence having no ellipsis, a complete<BR>sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृ
निरृ निर्-ऋ, cl. 3. P. -इयर्ति, &c., Ved. to<BR>go out from, depart from, liberate one's self from<BR>(with abl.); to be excluded, to become deprived of<BR>(with abl.); Caus. निर्-अर्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to go to pieces or decay, to dissolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृत
निर्-ऋत, अस्, आ, अम्, dissolved, decaying; debili-<BR>tated; (अस्), m., N. of a Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृति|निरृतिः
निर्-ऋति, इस्, f. decay, dissolution, destruction, anni-<BR>hilation, calamity, evil, adversity; imprecation, curse;<BR>Decay or Destruction personified (goddess of death<BR>and corruption; she is described as binding mortals<BR>with her cords, and is often associated with Mṛtyu,<BR>A-rāti, and similar beings; she is variously regarded<BR>as the wife of A-dharma, mother of Bhaya, Mahā-<BR>bhaya, and Mṛtyu, or as a daughter of A-dharma and<BR>Hiṃsā and mother of Naraka and Bhaya; she is<BR>regent of the south-west or south-western quarter<BR>and of the asterism Mūla); (इस्), f. the bottom or<BR>lower depths of the earth (perhaps regarded as the<BR>seat of putrefaction; cf. नैरृत); (इस्, इस्, इ), free<BR>from adversity, (in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृथ|निरृथः
निर्-ऋथ, अस्, m. destruction, the Destroyer (i. e.<BR>Nirṛtha personified); an epithet of a particular Agni;<BR>(according to some) the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृछ्
निरृछ् निर्-ऋछ्, cl. 6. P. -ऋच्छति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to go out from, fall from, be excluded from<BR>(with abl.); to go or cleave asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरे
निरे निर्-ए (निर्-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. निर्-ऐति, Ved.<BR>to come forth from, to go off, depart, make way for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरेक
निरेक नि-रेक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. रिच् with नि),<BR>Ved. a lasting possession (?), wealth, property; (ए),<BR>ind. lastingly, for ever; (Sāy.) in poverty or want; in<BR>donation or gifts; (according to Mahī-dhara) not<BR>empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरेभ
निरेभ नि-रेभ, अस्, आ, अम्, soundless, noise-<BR>less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोद्धव्य|निरोद्धव्यं
निरोद्धव्य नि-रोद्धव्य, नि-रोध, &c. See<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गत|निर्गतः
निर्गत निर्-गत. See निर्-गम् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्ध|निर्गंध|निर्गन्धं
निर्गन्ध निर्-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, inodorous,<BR>scentless, unfragrant, void of smell.<BR>—निर्गन्ध-ता,<BR>f. absence of smell, want of fragrance, scentlessness.<BR>—निर्गन्ध-पुष्पी, f. the silk-cotton tree (=<BR>शाल्मलि), Bombax Heptaphyllum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्धन|निर्गंधन|निर्गंधनं|निर्गन्धनं
निर्गन्धन निर्गन्धन, अम्, n. = निर्ग्रन्-<BR>थन, killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गम्
निर्गम् निर्-गम्, cl. 1. P. -गच्छति, -गन्-<BR>तुम्, to go out, come forth, depart from (with abl.),<BR>set out; to come out or appear (as a bud); to go<BR>away, disappear; to be freed from (with abl.); to enter<BR>into any state, undergo (with acc.): Desid. -जिगमि-<BR>षति, to wish to go out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग|निर्गः
निर्-ग, अस्, m. country, region; place or province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गत|निर्गतः
निर्-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone out, come forth, come<BR>out, appeared; gone away, departed; disappeared,<BR>extinct; freed from.<BR>—निर्गत-विशङ्क, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, freed from fear, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गम|निर्गमः
निर्-गम, अस्, m. going forth or out, setting out,<BR>going away, receding; departure, vanishing; exit,<BR>issue, outlet; a door; [cf. जल-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गमन|निर्गमनं
निर्-गमन, अम्, n. going out or forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गर्व
निर्गर्व निर्-गर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>pride, humble, lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गल्
निर्गल् निर्-गल्, cl. 1. P. -गलति, &c., to<BR>trickle or flow out; to dissolve, melt.<BR>—निर्-गलित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, flowed out, poured forth; dissolved,<BR>melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गवाक्ष
निर्गवाक्ष निर्-गवाक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, window-<BR>less, without windows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गा
निर्गा निर्-गा, cl. 3. P. -जिगाति (or -जगाति),<BR>-गातुम्, Ved. to go out, come forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुण|निर्गुणः
निर्गुण निर्-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, stringless (as<BR>a bow); devoid of all qualities or properties; without<BR>attributes; having no epithet; devoid of good<BR>qualities or virtues, bad, worthless, vicious; (अस्), m.<BR>the Supreme Being (as without qualities of any kind).<BR>—निर्गुण-ता, f. or निर्गुण-त्व, अम्, n. absence<BR>of qualities, want of properties, freedom from all<BR>qualities (as an attribute of the Supreme Being);<BR>absence or want of good qualities, wickedness, vicious-<BR>ness, baseness.<BR>—निर्गुणात्मक (˚ण-आत्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having no qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुण्टी
निर्गुण्टी निर्गुण्टी or निर्गुण्डी or निर्गुण्डि,<BR>इस्, f. the shrub Vitex Negundo; another plant (=<BR>नील-शेफालिका); the root of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुप्
निर्गुप् निर्-गुप्, cl. 1. P. -गोपायति, &c., to<BR>guard, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुल्म
निर्गुल्म निर्-गुल्म, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>bushes, destitute of shrubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गूढ|निर्गूढः
निर्गूढ निर्-गूढ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. गुह् with<BR>निस्), the hollow of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गृह
निर्गृह निर्-गृह, अस्, आ, अम्, houseless,<BR>homeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गॄ
निर्गॄ निर्-गॄ, cl. 6. P. -गिरति or -गिलति, &c.,<BR>to vomit forth.<BR>—निर्-गीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, vomited<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गौरव
निर्गौरव निर्-गौरव, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute<BR>of respect; without dignity, undignified, affable; (अम्),<BR>ind. without pride, condescendingly, affably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थ|निर्ग्रंथ|निर्ग्रन्थः
निर्ग्रन्थ निर्-ग्रन्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>all ties or hindrances; a saint, a devotee who has<BR>withdrawn from the world and lives either as a<BR>hermit or a beggar wandering about naked; pos-<BR>sessionless, poor, a pauper, beggar [cf. ग्रन्थ, said<BR>to mean ‘riches’]; (अस्), m. an idiot; a fool; a<BR>gambler; N. of a man, son of Jñāti.<BR>—निर्ग्रन्थ-<BR>शास्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थक|निर्ग्रन्थकः
निर्-ग्रन्थक, अस्, आ, अम्, unattended, unac-<BR>companied; abandoned, deserted; fruitless; clever,<BR>expert, conversant; (अस्), m. a religious mendicant;<BR>a naked devotee; a gambler; (अस्, अम्), m. n. (?),<BR>Buddhism (because the Buddhists appeared as religious<BR>mendicants, especially as ascetics).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थि
निर्-ग्रन्थि, इस्, इस्, इ, free from knots, knotless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थिक|निर्ग्रंथिक|निर्ग्रन्थिकः
निर्-ग्रन्थिक, अस्, m. a naked mendicant, an<BR>ascetic; (अस्, आ, अम्), clever, conversant; = हीन,<BR>destitute (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थन|निर्ग्रंथनं|निर्ग्रन्थनं
निर्ग्रन्थन निर्-ग्रन्थन, अम्, n. killing,<BR>slaughter; [cf. नि-ग्रन्थन, नि-गन्धन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्राह्य
निर्ग्राह्य निर्-ग्राह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be traced<BR>or found out, perceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घट|निर्घटं
निर्घट निर्-घट, अम्, n. a fair or crowded<BR>market, a free market, a wharf or ghaut where no<BR>toll is levied, a place where there is no quay or stairs,<BR>(in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घण्ट|निर्घंट|निर्घंटं|निर्घंटः|निर्घण्टः
निर्घण्ट निर्-घण्ट or निर्-घण्टक, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. a vocabulary, a collection of words, =<BR>नि-घण्टु, (perhaps for निर्-ग्रन्थक, ‘singling<BR>out the words of a sentence and writing them down<BR>in their independent form.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घात|निर्घातः
निर्घात निर्-घात, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हन् with<BR>निस्), destruction; a violent gust of wind, hurricane,<BR>whirlwind; the noise of contending vapours in the<BR>sky; an earthquake; a thunder-stroke; any severe<BR>stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घातन|निर्घातनं
निर्-घातन, अम्, n. forcing out, bringing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घात्य
निर्-घात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be forced or brought<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घुष्ट
निर्घुष्ट निर्-घुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. घुष्<BR>with निस्), sounded, resounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घोष|निर्घोषः
निर्-घोष, अस्, m. sound in general, noise, a<BR>loud noise, rattling, trampling; (अस्, आ, अम्), sound-<BR>less, noiseless, (in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR>—निर्घोषाक्षर-विमुक्त (˚ष-अक्ष्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Samādhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घूरिणी
निर्घूरिणी निर्-घूरिणी, f. a river, (perhaps<BR>a wrong reading for निर्-झरिणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घृण
निर्घृण निर्-घृण, अस्, आ, अम्, unmerciful,<BR>pitiless, cruel; shameless, immodest; (अम्), ind.<BR>without pity, pitilessly.<BR>—निर्घृण-ता, f. or निर्-<BR>घृण-त्व, अम्, n. pitilessness, unmercifulness, hard-<BR>heartedness, cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घृणा
निर्-घृणा, f. unmercifulness, cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घृष्
निर्घृष् निर्-घृष्, cl. 1. P. -घर्षति, &c.,<BR>to rub against or on (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घर्षण|निर्घर्षणं
निर्-घर्षण, अम्, n. rubbing, friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घर्षणक
निर्घर्षणक, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what rubs,<BR>a rubber, rubbing, a rubbing, a dentifrice fit for<BR>cleaning the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घृष्य
निर्-घृष्य, ind. having rubbed, having rubbed<BR>on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घोष|निर्घोषः
निर्घोष निर्-घोष. See निर्-घुष्ट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जन|निर्ज्जन|निर्ज्जनः
निर्जन निर्-जन, अस्, आ, अम्, unpeopled, de-<BR>populated, uninhabited, unfrequented, lonely, de-<BR>serted, desolate; (अम्), n. a solitude, desert.<BR>—निर्-<BR>जन-ता, f. or निर्जन-त्व, अम्, n. depopulation,<BR>the state of being unpeopled or deserted.<BR>—निर्जन-<BR>वन, अम्, n. a lonely or unfrequented forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जर|निर्जरं|निर्जरः|निर्ज्जर|निर्ज्जरः
निर्जर 1. निर्-जर, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see<BR>निर्-जॄ, col. 3), not becoming old, young, fresh;<BR>imperishable, immortal, undecaying; (अस्), m. an<BR>immortal, a deity, god; (आ), f. the plant Cocculus<BR>Cordifolius; Anethum Graveloens, = तत्त्व-भिद्;<BR>(अम्), n. ambrosia, the food of the gods.<BR>—निर्-<BR>जर-सर्षप, अस्, m. a species of mustard (=<BR>देव-सर्षप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जरस्
निर्-जरस्, optionally substituted for 1. निर्-जर<BR>in certain cases. (See Pāṇ. VII. 2, 101.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जरायु
निर्जरायु निर्-जरायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. skin-<BR>less (as a snake which has cast its skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जर्जल्प
निर्जर्जल्प निर्-जर्जल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (ac-<BR>cording to Mahī-dhara, probably because of its simi-<BR>larity to जर्जर, =) ragged, tattered; (another read-<BR>ing has निर्-जाल्मक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जल|निर्जलः|निर्ज्जलः
निर्जल निर्-जल, अस्, आ, अम्, waterless, desti-<BR>tute of water, dry, desert; not mixed with water<BR>(as buttermilk); (अस्), m. a desert, waste.<BR>—निर्जल-<BR>तोयदाभ (˚द-आभा), अस्, आ, अम्, of the colour of<BR>a waterless cloud, i. e. white, of a fair complexion.<BR>—निर्जलैकादशी (˚ल-एक्˚), f., N. of the eleventh<BR>day in the light half of month Jyaiṣṭha, on which<BR>even the drinking of water is forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जात
निर्जात निर्-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, come forth,<BR>appeared, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जाल्मक
निर्जाल्मक निर्-जाल्मक. See निर्-जर्जल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जि
निर्जि निर्-जि, cl. 1. P. A. -जयति, -ते, -जेतुम्,<BR>to conquer, win, gain, acquire, subdue, vanquish;<BR>to overcome in play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जय|निर्जयः
निर्-जय, अस्, m. conquest, complete victory, van-<BR>quishing, subduing; [cf. मन्यु-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जित|निर्ज्जितः
निर्-जित, अस्, आ, अम्, conquered, completely van-<BR>quished, thoroughly subdued, overcome; won, ac-<BR>quired, gained; claimed; unconquered.<BR>—निर्जित-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a man.<BR>—निर्जितारि-गणस्<BR>(˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has conquered hosts<BR>of enemies.<BR>—निर्जितेन्द्रिय (˚त-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of subdued passions or feelings.<BR>—निर्जितेन्द्रिय-<BR>ग्राम, अस्, m. ‘one who has subdued the whole<BR>assemblage of his organs,’ a Muni, a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जिति|निर्जितिः
निर्-जिति, इस्, f. conquest, complete victory, sub-<BR>duing, subjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जित्य
निर्-जित्य, ind. having conquered or won or gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जेतृ
निर्-जेतृ, ता, m. a conquerer, vanquisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जिह्व|निर्जिह्वः
निर्जिह्व निर्-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, tongueless,<BR>without a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जीव|निर्ज्जीवः
निर्जीव निर्-जीव, अस्, m. lifelessness, death;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), lifeless, inanimate, dead.<BR>—निर्जीव-<BR>कारण, अम्, n. a cause of death, a fatal blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जीवित
निर्-जीवित, अस्, आ, अम्, lifeless, dead, inanimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जुष्ट
निर्जुष्ट निर्-जुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. जुष्<BR>with prep. निस्), frequented, inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जॄ
निर्जॄ निर्-जॄ, Caus. -जरयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>wear down, wear away, rub to pieces, crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जर|निर्जरं|निर्जरः|निर्ज्जर|निर्ज्जरः
2. निर्-जर, अस्, आ, अम्, completely wearing down<BR>or destroying. (For 1. निर्-जर see col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ज्ञाति
निर्ज्ञाति निर्-ज्ञाति, इस्, इस्, इ, destitute of<BR>relations; having no kinsfolk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ज्वर
निर्ज्वर निर्-ज्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, feverless,<BR>healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्झर|निर्झरं|निर्झरः
निर्झर निर्-झर, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. (perhaps<BR>fr. झर् for rt. क्षर् with निस्), a waterfall, cataract,<BR>cascade, mountain-torrent, the precipitous descent of<BR>water from mountains, &c. [cf. झर]; (अस्), m.<BR>burning chaff; an elephant; a horse of the Sun<BR>[cf. निर्-णर]; (ई), f. a river [cf. निर्-झरिणी; cf.<BR>also निलिम्प-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्झरिन्
निर्-झरिन्, ई, m. a mountain; (इणी), f. a torrent,<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णय|निर्णयः
निर्णय निर्-णय. See under निर्-णी below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णर|निर्णरः
निर्णर निर्-णर, अस्, m. one of the horses<BR>of the Sun; [cf. निर्-झर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णाम|निर्णामः|निर्ण्णाम
निर्णाम निर्णाम, अस्, m., Ved. the joint of<BR>a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिज्
निर्णिज् 1. निर्-णिज्, cl. 3. P. A. -णेनेक्ति, -णे-<BR>निक्ते, Ved. inf. निर्-णिजे, निर्-णिजम्, &c., to wash<BR>off, wash, cleanse (A.); to wash one's self; to dress<BR>one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिक्त|निर्णिक्तं
निर्-णिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, washed, purified, cleaned,<BR>cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिज्
2. निर्-णिज्, क्, f., Ved. a shining dress or ornament,<BR>any bright garment [cf. अधि-न्˚, अश्व-न्˚, घृत-<BR>न्˚]; purification, cleansing; (Sāy.) a form, shape;<BR>well nourished (m. f. n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेक|निर्णेकः
निर्-णेक, अस्, m. washing, cleansing, cleaning;<BR>ablution; expiation, atonement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेजक|निर्णेजकः
निर्-णेजक, अस्, m. a washerman, washer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेजन|निर्णेजनं
निर्-णेजन, अम्, n. ablution; expiation, atonement<BR>for an offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णी
निर्णी निर्-णी, cl. 1. P. A. -णयति, -ते, -णे-<BR>तुम्, to lead or take away, carry away, carry off;<BR>to trace out, investigate, find out, ascertain, educe,<BR>elicit, to settle, come to a decision, decide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णय|निर्णयः
निर्-णय, अस्, m. removing, removal; deciding,<BR>rendering certain, complete ascertainment, decision,<BR>certainty, determination, proof, affirmation, precise<BR>definition, settlement; (in logic) deduction, inference,<BR>conclusion, demonstration; application of a conclu-<BR>sive argument; (in law) sentence, verdict; (in rhe-<BR>toric) narration of events; discussion, consideration,<BR>investigation.<BR>—निर्णय-कमलाकर (˚ल-आक्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘a lotus-bed of conclusions,’ N. of a Mīmāṃsā work.<BR>—निर्णय-दर्पण, अम्, n. ‘mirror of certainty,’<BR>N. of a Vedānta work.<BR>—निर्णय-दीप, ‘lamp of<BR>certainty,’ N. of a work mentioned in the Śūdra-<BR>dharma-tattva by Kamalākara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—निर्णय-<BR>दीपिका, f., N. of a work written about the middle<BR>of the seventeenth century.<BR>—निर्णय-पाद, अस्,<BR>m. a sentence, decree, verdict in law.<BR>—निर्णय-<BR>सिन्धु, N. of a Mīmāṃsā work by Kamalākara-<BR>bhaṭṭa; (also read निर्णेय-सिन्धु.)<BR>—निर्णया-<BR>मृत (˚य-अम्˚), अम्, n. ‘nectar of certainty,’ N.<BR>of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयत्
निर्-णयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, concluding, deciding,<BR>ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयन|निर्णयनं
निर्-णयन, अम्, n. ascertainment, certainty;<BR>positive conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायक
निर्-णायक, अस्, आ, अम्, causing or leading to<BR>certainty, conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायन|निर्णायनं|निर्ण्णायन
निर्-णायन, अम्, n. rendering certain; the outer<BR>angle of the elephant's eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णीत|निर्णीतं
निर्-णीत, अस्, आ, अम्, deduced, traced out, brought to<BR>a conclusion, ascertained, settled, decided, proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेतृ
निर्-णेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, decisive, certifying, veri-<BR>fying, leading to certainty, demonstrating, proving;<BR>(ता), m. one who pronounces a sentence, a judge;<BR>a voucher; a guide.<BR>—निर्णेतृ-त्व, अम्, n. proof,<BR>verification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेय
निर्-णेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ascertained, to be<BR>decided or determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णुद्
निर्णुद् निर्-णुद्, cl. 6. P. A. (sometimes<BR>wrongly निर्-नुद्), -णुदति, -ते, -णोत्तुम्, to push<BR>or drive out; to drive away, expel, reject, remove;<BR>to repudiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णोद|निर्णोदः
निर्-णोद, अस्, m. removal, banishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दंश्
निर्दंश् निर्-दंश्, cl. 1. P. -दशति or -दं-<BR>शति, -दंष्टुम्, to bite through, bite; (with दन्-<BR>तान्) to gnash the teeth, grind the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दंशिन्
निर्-दंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, biting through; not biting,<BR>(Ved., in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दशत्|निर्द्दशत्
निर्-दशत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, biting, biting through;<BR>consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दशमान
निर्-दशमान, अस्, आ, अम्, biting through, biting;<BR>gnashing or grinding (the teeth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दश्य
निर्-दश्य, ind. having bitten, biting through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दग्ध|निर्द्दग्ध
निर्दग्ध निर्-दग्ध. See निर्-दह् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दड
निर्दड निर्-दड, अस्, आ, अम्, unkind, un-<BR>feeling, unmerciful; devoid of pity or charity, re-<BR>joicing over the faults of others; envious, slanderous,<BR>abusive; useless, unnecessary; mad, intoxicated; vio-<BR>lent; (sometimes spelt निर्-दट; cf. निर्-दय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दण्ड|निर्दंड|निर्दण्डः
निर्दण्ड निर्-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, not punishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दय|निर्द्दयः
निर्दय निर्-दय, अस्, आ, अम्, pitiless, un-<BR>merciful, unkind, cruel, hard-hearted; passionate;<BR>excessive, violent; unpitied by any; (अम्), n. without<BR>pity, unmercifully; passionately, violently, exces-<BR>sively, much.<BR>—निर्दय-त्व, अम्, n. unmercifulness,<BR>cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दर|निर्दरः|निर्द्दर|निर्द्दरं
निर्दर निर्-दर, अस्, or निर्-दरि, इस्, m. =<BR>दर or दरि, a cave, cavern; [according to some<BR>निर्-दर, अस्, आ, अम्, = निर्-दय, pitiless, hard;<BR>shameless; also निर्-दरम्, ind. = excessively, and<BR>निर्-दर, अम्, n. = pith, essence.]<BR>—निर्दरि-वासिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, inhabiting a cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दलन|निर्दलनं
निर्दलन निर्-दलन, अम्, n. splitting,<BR>cleaving asunder, breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दश
निर्दश निर्-दश, अस्, आ, अम्, more than ten<BR>days old, what happened more than ten days ago;<BR>[cf. अ-न्˚, नैर्दश्य.]<BR>—निर्दशाह (˚श-अह),<BR>see अ-न्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दशत्|निर्द्दशत्
निर्दशत् निर्-दशत्, &c. See निर्-दंश् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दशन
निर्दशन निर्-दशन, अस्, आ, अम्, toothless.<BR>—निर्दशनाक्षि-जिह्व (˚न-अक्ष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>deprived of teeth, eyes, and tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दस्यु
निर्दस्यु निर्-दस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, free from<BR>robbers or bandits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दह्
निर्दह् निर्-दह्, cl. 1. P. -दहति, -दग्धुम्,<BR>to burn out, burn up, consume by fire, destroy com-<BR>pletely: Caus. -दाहयति, -यितुम्, to cause to burn<BR>up or set on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दग्ध|निर्द्दग्ध
निर्-दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt, burnt up; un-<BR>burnt, (in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दग्धिका
निर्-दग्धिका, f. = नि-दिग्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दहन|निर्द्दहनः
निर्-दहन, अस्, ई, अम्, burning, burning up,<BR>consuming; (अस्), m. the plant Semecarpus Ana-<BR>cardium; (ई), f. the plant Sanseviera Roxburghiana;<BR>(अम्), n. burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दाह
निर्-दाह, अस्, आ, अम्, or निर्-दाहुक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. burning, consuming by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दातृ|निर्द्दातृ
निर्दातृ निर्-दातृ, ता, m. (fr. rt. 3. दा or दो<BR>with निस्), a weeder, digger up of weeds; a reaper,<BR>husbandman; [cf. निर्-यातृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दारित|निर्द्दारित
निर्दारित निर्-दारित. See निर्-दॄ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिग्ध|निर्द्दिग्धः
निर्दिग्ध निर्-दिग्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. दिह्<BR>with निस्), anointed, smeared; well fed, corpulent,<BR>stout, lusty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिग्धिका
निर्-दिग्धिका, f. a various reading for निर्-दग्-<BR>धिका or नि-दिग्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिश्
निर्दिश् निर्-दिश्, cl. 6. P. -दिशति, -देष्टुम्,<BR>to point to, point out, show, direct, declare, announce,<BR>tell, enjoin, order; to denote, indicate, mark; to<BR>assign, destine; to enumerate, specify, particularize,<BR>name; to foretel; to define, determine; to describe;<BR>to recommend, advise, suggest; to denounce: Desid.<BR>-दिदिक्षति, to wish to point out or to define<BR>more closely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिश्य
निर्-दिश्य, ind. having pointed out, having shown,<BR>explained, enjoined, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिष्ट|निर्द्दिष्टः
निर्-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, pointed out, shown,<BR>specified, particularized; described, depicted; assigned;<BR>ordered, directed; asserted, declared; ascertained,<BR>determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देश|निर्देशः|निर्द्देशः
निर्-देश, अस्, m. pointing out, directing, ordering,<BR>order, command, direction; instruction; saying, tell-<BR>ing, declaring; description, designation; depicting,<BR>specifying, particularizing, giving particulars or details,<BR>specification, special mention; certainty, ascertain-<BR>ment; vicinity, proximity; a particular number;<BR>[cf. नि-देश.]<BR>—निर्देश-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, executing<BR>orders, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देशक
निर्-देशक, अस्, इका, अम्, pointing out, showing,<BR>describing; ordering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देशनीय
निर्-देशनीय or निर्-देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>pointed out; assignable; to be determined; to be<BR>arranged; to be described, to be defined or particu-<BR>larized; to be proclaimed or foretold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देष्टृ
निर्-देष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, who or what shows,<BR>explains, points out, defines, &c.; (टा), m. an<BR>authority, a guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दी
निर्दी निर्-दी, cl. 4. P. -दीयति, &c., Ved. to<BR>fly away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दुःख
निर्दुःख निर्-दुःख, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>pain, painless, not suffering pain; not causing pain.<BR>—निर्दुःख-त्व, अम्, n. absence of pain; pain-<BR>lessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दुह्
निर्दुह् निर्-दुह्, cl. 2. P. A. -दोग्धि, -दुग्-<BR>धे, -दोग्धुम्, to milk out, extract, draw out,<BR>produce; to withdraw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दुग्ध
निर्-दुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, milked out, drawn out,<BR>extracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दॄ
निर्दॄ निर्-दॄ, cl. 9. P. -दृणाति, -दरितुम्, -द-<BR>रीतुम्, to tear or rend asunder, tear in pieces, split<BR>asunder: Caus. -दारयति, -यितुम्, to tear or split<BR>asunder; to root up, cause to be dug up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दारित|निर्द्दारित
निर्-दारित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn asunder, rent; split<BR>open, opened, unclosed; starting open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देव
निर्देव निर्-देव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. abandoned<BR>by the gods, without the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दैन्य
निर्दैन्य निर्-दैन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>misery or wretchedness, happy, comfortable, at ease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दोष|निर्द्दोषः
निर्दोष निर्-दोष, अस्, आ, अम्, faultless, with-<BR>out defect or blemish; guiltless, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दोषीकृत
निर्दोषी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, cleared from guilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्रव्य
निर्द्रव्य निर्-द्रव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, immaterial;<BR>without property, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्रु
निर्द्रु निर्-द्रु, cl. 1. P. -द्रवति, -द्रोतुम्,<BR>Ved. to run out, run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्रोह
निर्द्रोह निर्-द्रोह, अस्, आ, अम्, not malevo-<BR>lent, not hostile, friendly; well-disposed; innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्वन्द्व|निर्द्वंद्व
निर्द्वन्द्व निर्-द्वन्द्व, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>either of two alternatives or indifferent in regard to<BR>opposite pairs of feelings (as pleasure and pain),<BR>neither glad nor sorry, &c.; not standing in mutual<BR>relation, not dependant upon another, independant;<BR>not striving together, free from envy or jealousy;<BR>not causing disputes, uncontested, undisputed; not<BR>double; not acknowledging two principles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धन|निर्धनः
निर्धन निर्-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, without pro-<BR>perty or money; poor, indigent; (अस्), m. an<BR>old ox.<BR>—निर्धन-ता, f. or निर्धन-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. absence of property, poverty, indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धर्म|निर्धर्म्म|निर्धर्म्मः
निर्धर्म निर्-धर्म, अस्, m. unrighteous-<BR>ness; (अस्, आ, अम्), unjust, unrighteous, impious,<BR>immoral, void of law, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धा
निर्धा निर्-धा, cl. 3. P. -दधाति, -धातुम्,<BR>Ved. to free from; to find out (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार|निर्धारः
निर्धार निर्-धार, &c. See निर्-धृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार्तराष्ट्र
निर्धार्तराष्ट्र निर्-धार्तराष्ट्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having no descendants of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra, free from<BR>them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धाव्
निर्धाव् 1. निर्-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,<BR>-ते, -धावितुम्, to stream forth from, spring from;<BR>to run out, escape from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धाव्
निर्धाव् 2. निर्-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,<BR>-ते, -धावितुम्, to wash off, wash away, cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धौत|निर्धौतं
निर्-धौत, अस्, आ, अम्, washed off, cleansed,<BR>polished, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धू
निर्धू निर्-धू, cl. 5. P. A. -धूनोति, -धू-<BR>नुते (in later language also -धुनोति, -धुनुते),<BR>-धोतुम् and -धवितुम्, to shake out, shake off,<BR>remove; to drive away, expel, banish, repudiate,<BR>disown; to shake, agitate, brandish, move about;<BR>to harass, distress, torment, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धूत|निर्धूतं|निर्धूतः
निर्-धूत or निर्-धुत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken off,<BR>shaken out, thrown out or off; removed; avoided;<BR>departed; deserted, rejected; broken, divided; re-<BR>futed, destroyed; deprived of, bereft; suffered, un-<BR>dergone; (अस्), m. a man abandoned by his relatives<BR>or friends.<BR>—निर्धूत-पाप, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose sins are wholly shaken off or removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धूम
निर्धूम निर्-धूम, अस्, आ, अम्, smokeless.<BR>—निर्धूम-त्व, अम्, n. smokelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धृ
निर्धृ निर्-धृ, cl. 1. P. A. -धरति, -ते, cl.<BR>10. or Caus. -धारयति, -यितुम्, to take out from;<BR>to separate one out of many, particularize; to de-<BR>termine, define, state accurately; to ascertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार|निर्धारः
निर्-धार, अस्, m. or निर्-धारण, अम्, n. taking<BR>out from, separating or specifying one out of many,<BR>particularizing individuals according to their degree<BR>of merit; determining, defining, settling; certainty,<BR>ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारणीय
निर्-धारणीय or निर्-धारितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be ascertained; irresistible, (in this sense निर् is<BR>a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारित|निर्धारितं
निर्-धारित, अस्, आ, अम्, determined, ascertained,<BR>settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार्य|निर्धार्य्य|निर्धार्य्यं
निर्-धार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ascertained or<BR>determined, ascertainable; not to be restrained, act-<BR>ing resolutely or fearlessly, active, energetic, (in this<BR>sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार्यमाण
निर्-धार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being particular-<BR>ized; being determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धे
निर्धे निर्-धे, cl. 1. P. -धयति, -धातुम्,<BR>Ved. to drink up, suck up, absorb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धौत|निर्धौतं
निर्धौत निर्-धौत. See 2. निर्-धाव् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध्मा
निर्ध्मा निर्-ध्मा, cl. 1. P. -धमति, -ध्मा-<BR>तुम्, to blow away, blow out of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध्मापन
निर्-ध्मापन, अम्, n. blowing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध्यै
निर्ध्यै निर्-ध्यै, cl. 1. P. -ध्यायति, -ध्या-<BR>तुम्, to think of, reflect upon, meditate about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध्यात
निर्-ध्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, thought of, reflected<BR>upon, meditated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ध्याय
निर्-ध्याय, ind. having thought of, having re-<BR>flected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नमस्कार
निर्नमस्कार निर्-नमस्कार, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>respecting any one, uncourteous; unrespected, re-<BR>spected by no one, despised by all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नर
निर्नर निर्-नर, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned by<BR>men, deserted, desolate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाथ
निर्नाथ निर्-नाथ, अस्, आ, अम्, protectorless,<BR>without a guardian or master or superior.<BR>—निर्नाथ-<BR>ता, f. the being without a master or guardian or pro-<BR>tector, want of protection; widowhood; orphanage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाभि
निर्नाभि निर्-नाभि, इस्, इस्, इ, without the<BR>navel, not reaching to the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाशन
निर्नाशन निर्-नाशन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. नश्<BR>with निस्), removing, expelling, banishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाशिन्
निर्-नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ (from an unused निर्-नाश),<BR>removing, expelling, banishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्निद्र
निर्निद्र निर्-निद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, sleepless.<BR>—निर्निद्र-ता, f. sleeplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्निमित्त
निर्निमित्त निर्-निमित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>reason or motive, causeless, groundless; (अम्), n.<BR>causelessly, without cause.<BR>—निर्निमित्त-कृत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, produced without a cause, whose cause is<BR>invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्निमेष
निर्निमेष निर्-निमेष, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्निरोध
निर्निरोध निर्-निरोध, अस्, आ, अम्, unob-<BR>structed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नीड
निर्नीड निर्-नीड, अस्, आ, अम्, having no nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बद्ध
निर्बद्ध निर्-बद्ध. See निर्-बन्ध् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बन्ध्|निर्बंध्
निर्बन्ध् निर्-बन्ध्, cl. 9. P. -बध्नाति,<BR>-बन्द्धुम्, to fix or fasten upon, attach one's self<BR>to, cling to, to insist upon, persist in; press upon;<BR>to urge, importune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बद्ध
निर्-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed upon, fastened<BR>upon; directed on; clung to; pressed hard, urged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बन्ध|निर्बंध|निर्बंधः|निर्बन्धः|निर्ब्बन्ध
निर्-बन्ध, अस्, m. insisting upon (with loc.),<BR>persistence, perseverance, pertinacity, intentness; ob-<BR>stinacy; importunity, urgency, pressing or urging<BR>anything, (निर्बन्धं कृ, to urge); accusing,<BR>accusation; contest, dispute; caprice, fancy?; [cf.<BR>णि-बन्ध.]<BR>—निर्बन्ध-पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>urgently asked, importuned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बन्धनीय
निर्-बन्धनीय, अम्, n. (perhaps) contest, dis-<BR>pute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बन्धिन्
निर्-बन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, insisting upon (with loc.),<BR>urgent, persisting in, intent upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बन्धु|निर्बंधु
निर्बन्धु निर्-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, without re-<BR>lations, without kindred, friendless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बर्हण|निर्ब्बर्हण|निर्ब्बर्हणं
निर्बर्हण निर्-बर्हण, अम्, n. = नि-वर्हण,<BR>slaughter, killing, destroying, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बल|निर्ब्बल
निर्बल निर्-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, powerless, with-<BR>out strength, impotent, weak, feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बाध्
निर्बाध् निर्-बाध्, cl. 1. A. -बाधते, -बा-<BR>धितुम्, Ved. to keep off, ward off, hold back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बाध|निर्बाधः
निर्-बाध, अस्, m., Ved. a knob, prominence;<BR>(निर्बाधे कृ is perhaps a proverbial expression<BR>meaning ‘to put on one side, set aside, remove.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बाधिन्
निर्बाधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. furnished with knobs or<BR>prominences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बुद्धि|निर्ब्बुद्धि
निर्बुद्धि निर्-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, senseless,<BR>witless, unwise, ignorant, stupid, out of one's wits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बुसीकृत
निर्बुसीकृत निर्बुसी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, freed<BR>from chaff, husked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्रू
निर्ब्रू निर्-ब्रू, cl. 2. P. -ब्रवीति, &c., Ved.<BR>to speak out, pronounce (loud or clearly); to inter-<BR>pret, explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भक्त
निर्भक्त निर्-भक्त. See निर्-भज् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भग्न
निर्भग्न निर्-भग्न. See निर्-भञ्ज् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भज्
निर्भज् निर्-भज्, cl. 1. P. A. -भजति, -ते,<BR>-भक्तुम्, Ved. to exclude from participation or<BR>coparceny (with abl.): Caus. -भाजयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>exclude from sharing in, to disinherit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भक्त
निर्-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, excluded from partici-<BR>pation in; taken without eating (as medicine; in<BR>this sense निर् is a privative).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भाज्य
निर्-भाज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be excluded from<BR>participation in, to be debarred from sharing in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भञ्ज्
निर्भञ्ज् निर्-भञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. -भनक्ति,<BR>-भङ्क्तुम्, to break asunder, split asunder; to<BR>defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भग्न
निर्-भग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken in pieces; broken<BR>down; bent.<BR>—निर्-भज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>broken in pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भट|निर्भटः
निर्भट निर्-भट, अस्, आ, अम्, hard, firm,<BR>compact; (perhaps a wrong reading.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भय|निर्भयः
निर्भय निर्-भय, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless, un-<BR>daunted; free from danger, secure; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a son of the thirteenth Manu; (अम्), ind. fearlessly,<BR>without danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर|निर्भरं|निर्भरः
निर्भर निर्-भर, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. भर],<BR>excessive, exceeding, vehement, violent; deep, sound<BR>(as sleep); ardent; beyond measure, much; (at the<BR>end of a comp.) full of, filled with; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. essence?; (अम्), ind. excessively, exceed-<BR>ingly, very much; soundly, deeply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्स्
निर्भर्त्स् निर्-भर्त्स्, cl. 10. P. A. -भर्त्स-<BR>यति, -ते, -यितुम्, to threaten, menace, abuse, re-<BR>buke, reprimand, chide, blame, deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सन|निर्भर्त्सनं
निर्-भर्त्सन, अम्, आ, n. f. threatening, threat,<BR>menace; abuse, reviling, reproach, blame; malignity;<BR>red paint, lac.<BR>—निर्भर्त्सन-दण्ड-मोहित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, bewildered by the threat of punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सित|निर्भर्त्सितं
निर्-भर्त्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, threatened, menaced;<BR>reviled, abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्स्य
निर्-भर्त्स्य, ind. having threatened; having<BR>reviled or reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भस्
निर्भस् निर्-भस्, cl. 3. P. -बभस्ति, -बप्-<BR>सति, &c., Ved. to bite off, chew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भा
निर्भा निर्-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति, -भातुम्,<BR>to shine forth, appear, arise, proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भात
निर्-भात, अस्, आ, अम्, shone forth, shining forth,<BR>appeared, arisen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भाग्य|निर्भाग्यः
निर्भाग्य निर्-भाग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unlucky,<BR>unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भाज्य
निर्भाज्य निर्-भाज्य. See निर्-भज् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भास्
निर्भास् निर्-भास्, Caus. -भासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भासित
निर्-भासित, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminated, illumined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिद्
निर्भिद् निर्-भिद्, cl. 7. P. A. -भिनत्ति,<BR>-भिन्त्ते, -भेत्तुम्, to cleave or split asunder, break<BR>in two, rend, divide, separate, open; to break through,<BR>pierce, penetrate, wound; to put out (the eyes); to<BR>break down, destroy; to divulge, betray; to find<BR>out, detect, discover; to excavate: Pass. -भिद्यते,<BR>to be broken asunder, to cleave or split open (intrans.);<BR>to burst asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिद्य
निर्-भिद्य, ind. having broken through, having<BR>pierced or penetrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिन्न
निर्-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken asunder, pierced,<BR>divided.<BR>—निर्भिन्न-तनु, उस्, उस्, उ, having the<BR>body pierced through or transfixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भेद|निर्भेदः
निर्-भेद, अस्, m. breaking or splitting asunder,<BR>bursting, dividing, a split, rent; the bed or channel<BR>of a river; the issue or termination of an affair,<BR>event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भेदिन्
निर्-भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, splitting asunder, piercing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भेद्य
निर्-भेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be split asunder; having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">Page0498-c+ 66</a>]<BR>no rent; missing an aim; disappointed; (in the last<BR>three senses निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भीत
निर्भीत निर्-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless, not<BR>afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भुज्
निर्भुज् निर्-भुज्, cl. 6. P. -भुजति, -भोक्-<BR>तुम्, to bend on one side, bend awry, distort;<BR>(ओष्ठौ निर्भुजति, he distorts his lips, makes a<BR>wry face.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भुग्न
निर्-भुग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, bent awry, distorted;<BR>not bent, straight, (in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भुज
निर्-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, a term applied to a kind<BR>of Sandhi (or Saṃhitā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भू
निर्भू निर्-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्,<BR>Ved. to come out, move out, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भूति
निर्-भूति, इस्, f., Ved. disappearing, passing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भृ
निर्भृ निर्-भृ, cl. 1. 3. P. -भरति, -बि-<BR>भर्ति, -भर्तुम्, to take out, draw out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भृत
निर्-भृत, probably a wrong reading for नि-<BR>भृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भृति
निर्भृति निर्-भृति, इस्, इस्, इ, without wages,<BR>hireless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भेद|निर्भेदः
निर्भेद निर्-भेद, निर्-भेद्य. See निर्-भिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भोग
निर्भोग निर्-भोग, अस्, आ, अम्, not devoted<BR>to pleasure or enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मक्षिक
निर्मक्षिक निर्-मक्षिक, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from flies, free from tormentors, untroubled; (अम्),<BR>n. the being free from flies; (अम्), ind. without flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मज्
निर्मज् निर्-मज्, Ved. (according to Sāy.)<BR>completely pure (as cows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मज्ज्
निर्मज्ज् निर्-मज्ज्, cl. 1. P. -मज्जति, &c.,<BR>to sink under, sink into; to inundate, deluge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मग्न
निर्-मग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk, sunk into, sunk<BR>under, (opposed to उन्-मग्न.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मज्ज
निर्मज्ज निर्-मज्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, fatless, mar-<BR>rowless, meagre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मण्डूक
निर्मण्डूक निर्-मण्डूक, अस्, आ, अम्, frogless,<BR>destitute of frogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मत्सर
निर्मत्सर निर्-मत्सर, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>envy, unenvious, free from envy or passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मत्स्य
निर्मत्स्य निर्-मत्स्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fishless,<BR>destitute of fish.<BR>—निर्मत्स्य-ता, f. absence of fish,<BR>the having no fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथ|निर्मथः
निर्मथ निर्-मथ, निर्-मथन. See under<BR>निर्-मन्थ् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मद|निर्म्मद|निर्म्मदः
निर्मद निर्-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, unintoxicated,<BR>sober, quiet; not proud, humble; not in rut (as an<BR>elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मध्य
निर्मध्य निर्-मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>middle; (आ), f. = नलिका, a fragrant substance; [cf.<BR>निर्-मथ्या below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मनस्क
निर्मनस्क निर्-मनस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, mindless,<BR>having no Manas.<BR>—निर्मनस्क-ता, f. the having<BR>no Manas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मनुज
निर्मनुज निर्-मनुज, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned<BR>by men (as a forest), desolate, uninhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मनुष्य|निर्म्मनुष्य
निर्मनुष्य निर्-मनुष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, un-<BR>peopled, uninhabited, deserted by men, without a<BR>man; (मातङ्गो निर्मनुष्यस्, an elephant with-<BR>out riders.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्त्र
निर्मन्त्र निर्-मन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, unaccom-<BR>panied by holy texts or the recitation of sacred verses<BR>(as the Gandharva marriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्थ्|निर्मंथ्
निर्मन्थ् निर्-मन्थ् or निर्-मथ्, cl. 1. 9. P.<BR>-मथति, -मन्थति, -मथ्नाति, &c., to stir about,<BR>agitate, churn, shake about, toss about roughly or<BR>violently; to rub, elicit fire by rubbing; to strike,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">Page0499-a+ 76</a>]<BR>beat violently, thresh, bruise, crush, stamp to pieces,<BR>grind, break in pieces, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथ|निर्मथः
निर्-मथ, अस्, m. stirring, rubbing.<BR>—निर्मथ-<BR>दारु = निर्मन्थ-दारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथन|निर्मथनं
निर्-मथन, अम्, n. stirring, churning, rubbing,<BR>rubbing two pieces of wood together to light a fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथित
निर्-मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, stirred about, agitated,<BR>churned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथ्य|निर्म्मथ्य
1. निर्-मथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stirred about or<BR>rubbed; (आ), f. a kind of fragrant substance, =<BR>नलिका; [cf. निर्-मध्या above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथ्य|निर्म्मथ्य
2. निर्-मथ्य, ind. having churned; having ground;<BR>having discriminated or particularized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथ्यमान
निर्-मथ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being shaken or<BR>tossed about roughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्थ|निर्मंथ|निर्मंथः|निर्मन्थः
निर्-मन्थ, अस्, m. rubbing.<BR>—निर्मन्थ-दारु,<BR>उस्, उ, m. n. or निर्मन्थ-काष्ठ, अम्, n. the<BR>wood used for kindling fire by friction; a churning-<BR>stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्थन|निर्मंथन|निर्मंथनं|निर्म्मन्थन
निर्-मन्थन, अम्, n. rubbing, churning; sepa-<BR>rating, distinguishing, discriminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्थ्य|निर्मंथ्य|निर्म्मन्थ्य
निर्-मन्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stirred, to be<BR>churned; to be excited by friction (as fire); to be<BR>distinguished or discriminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माथिन्
निर्-माथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crushing or stamping to<BR>pieces, churning, rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मन्यु
निर्मन्यु निर्-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, free from<BR>anger or resentment; (उस्), m., N. of a hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मम|निर्म्मम
निर्मम निर्-मम, अस्, आ, अम्, unselfish, dis-<BR>interested; regardless, indifferent to (with loc.); free<BR>from all connection with the outer world; an epithet<BR>of Śiva; (अस्), m. (with Jainas) N. of the fifteenth<BR>Arhat of the future Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR>—निर्मम-ता, f. or<BR>1. निर्मम-त्व, अम्, n. unselfishness, disregard of<BR>worldly interests, indifference towards (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ममत्व|निर्म्ममत्व
2. निर्-ममत्व, अस्, आ, अम्, free from selfishness,<BR>indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मर्याद|निर्मर्य्याद
निर्मर्याद निर्-मर्याद, अस्, आ, अम्, boundless,<BR>having no limits, immeasurable, innumerable; trans-<BR>gressing the boundaries of right, unrestrained, unruly,<BR>wicked, criminal, sinful, impious; confused; (अम्),<BR>n. confusion, disturbance of boundaries or rules;<BR>N. of a kind of fight; (अम्), ind. confusedly,<BR>topsy-turvy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मल|निर्म्मल|निर्म्मलं
निर्मल निर्-मल, अस्, आ, अम्, spotless, free<BR>from spots or dirt or impurities, stainless, unsullied,<BR>clear, clean, pure, limpid; shining, splendent, bright;<BR>virtuous; (अम्), n. talc; the remains of an offering<BR>made to a deity.<BR>—निर्मल-गद, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a bright mace.<BR>—निर्मल-ता, f. or निर्मल-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. stainlessness, purity, cleanness (physical<BR>or moral).<BR>—निर्मली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>impurity, cleansed, cleared.<BR>—निर्मलोपल (˚ल-<BR>उप्˚), अस्, m. crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माल्य|निर्म्माल्य|निर्म्माल्यं
निर्-माल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, stainless, clean, &c., =<BR>निर्-मल; (आ), f. a species of medicinal plant, see<BR>पृक्का; (अम्), n. stainlessness, purity, cleanness, clear-<BR>ness; the remains of an offering to a deity, flowers<BR>left at a sacrificial ceremony; remains in general.<BR>—निर्माल्य-ता, f. = निर्मल-ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मशक
निर्मशक निर्-मशक, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>gnats or musquitoes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मा|निर्म्मा
निर्मा 1. निर्-मा, cl. 2. P., 3. and 4. A., -माति,<BR>-मिमीते, -मायते, -मातुम्, to build, make, form,<BR>fabricate; to produce, create; to compose; to cause:<BR>Caus. -मापयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be made or<BR>built.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मा|निर्म्मा
2. निर्-मा, f. value, measure, equivalent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माण|निर्माणं|निर्म्माण|निर्म्माणं
निर्-माण, अम्, n. measuring or meting out,<BR>measure; reach, extent, (एक-निर्माण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of the same measure; ककुदोदग्र-निर्माण, as<BR>high as the top of a mountain; अव्यक्त-निर्माणो<BR>बालस्, a boy who has not yet reached his full<BR>growth, not yet full grown); forming, making, pro-<BR>ducing, creating, production, fabrication, manufacture,<BR>formation, creation, building; composing, composi-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">Page0499-b+ 72</a>]<BR>tion, work; a building; a part; (with Buddhists) trans-<BR>formation; the best of anything, pith, marrow,<BR>essence; (आ), f. propriety, decorum, fitness.<BR>—निर्-<BR>माण-रत, आस्, m. pl. ‘delighting in creating or<BR>building,’ N. of a particular class of gods.<BR>—निर्-<BR>माण-रति, इस्, इस्, इ, delighting in creating; (अयस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a class of deities in the eleventh Manv-<BR>antara; (with Buddhists) delighting in transforma-<BR>tion; [cf. निर्वाण-रुचि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मातृ
निर्-मातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a maker, builder, creator,<BR>former, producer; building, fabricating, forming, &c.<BR>—निर्मातृ-त्व, अम्, n. creatorship, the condition<BR>of a maker or builder or producer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मित|निर्म्मित|निर्म्मितं
निर्-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, constructed, manufactured,<BR>produced, built, fashioned, fabricated, formed, made;<BR>artificial; meted out; (आस्), m. pl. (with Buddhists) N.<BR>of a class of deities, ‘the transformed.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मिति|निर्मितिः|निर्म्मिति|निर्म्मितिः
निर्-मिति, इस्, f. formation, production, creation,<BR>fabrication, manufacture, artificial production; making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मांस
निर्मांस निर्-मांस, अस्, आ, अम्, fleshless,<BR>emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माख्य
निर्माख्य निर्-माख्य, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(probably a wrong form, also read तिग्मात्मन् and<BR>निर्माद्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माथिन्
निर्माथिन् निर्-माथिन्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मान
निर्मान निर्-मान, अस्, आ, अम्, without self-<BR>confidence, free from pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मानुष
निर्मानुष निर्-मानुष, अस्, आ, अम्, unpeopled,<BR>uninhabited, abandoned by men, desolate; (ए), ind.<BR>in a solitary place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मार्ग
निर्मार्ग 1. निर्-मार्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, roadless,<BR>pathless. (For 2. निर्-मार्ग see under निर्-मृज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माली
निर्माली निर्-माली, f. = निर्-माल्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माल्य|निर्म्माल्य|निर्म्माल्यं
निर्माल्य निर्-माल्य. See under निर्-मल,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुच्
निर्मुच् निर्-मुच्, cl. 6. P. A. -मुञ्चति, -ते,<BR>-मोक्तुम्, to loosen, free from, liberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुक्त|निर्मुक्तः|निर्म्मुक्त
निर्-मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed, set free, liberated,<BR>disjoined, sundered, separated, &c.; (अस्), m. a snake<BR>which has lately cast his skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुक्ति|निर्मुक्तिः
निर्-मुक्ति, इस्, f. liberation, deliverance; [cf.<BR>शाप-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोक|निर्मोकः|निर्म्मोक|निर्म्मोकः
निर्-मोक, अस्, m. setting loose or free, liberat-<BR>ing; a hide or skin, especially the cast off skin or<BR>slough of a snake [cf. सर्प-न्˚]; armour, mail;<BR>sky, heaven, atmosphere; N. of a son of the eighth<BR>Manu; of one of the Saptarṣis under the thirteenth<BR>Manu; [cf. निर्-मोह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोक्तृ
निर्-मोक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who solves or<BR>liberates, a liberator, looser, solver (of doubts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोचन|निर्मोचनं
निर्-मोचन, अम्, n. liberation, deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुट|निर्मुटं|निर्मुटः|निर्म्मुट
निर्मुट निर्-मुट, अस्, m. a tree bearing<BR>large blossoms (= वनस्-पति); the sun; a rogue;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a large and free market or fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मूल|निर्म्मूल
निर्मूल निर्-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, rootless, de-<BR>prived of roots (as a tree); baseless, without origin,<BR>unfounded; eradicated.<BR>—निर्मूल-ता, f. rootless-<BR>ness, baselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मूलन|निर्मूलनं
निर्-मूलन, अम्, n. uprooting, eradicating, ex-<BR>tirpating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मूलय
निर्-मूलय, Nom. P. निर्मूलयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>uproot, eradicate, extirpate, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मृज्
निर्मृज् निर्-मृज्, cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि, -मार्-<BR>जितुम् and -मार्ष्टुम्, to wipe off, wipe out, rub<BR>out, sweep out, strip off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मार्ग
2. निर्-मार्ग, अस्, m. (for 1. see above), rubbing<BR>or stripping off, wiping off; that which is stripped<BR>or wiped off, refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मार्गुक
निर्-मार्गुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. drawing off,<BR>withdrawing, separating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मार्जन|निर्मार्जनं
निर्-मार्जन, अम्, n. wiping off, sweeping,<BR>cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मृष्ट
निर्-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, rubbed out, wiped off<BR>or out, swept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मेघ
निर्मेघ निर्-मेघ, अस्, आ, अम्, cloudless.<BR>—निर्मेघाश्रम (˚घ-आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मेध
निर्मेध निर्-मेध, अस्, आ, अम्, without un-<BR>derstanding, stupid, dull.<BR>—निर्मेधाश्रम (˚ध-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोक|निर्मोकः|निर्म्मोक|निर्म्मोकः
निर्मोक निर्-मोक, निर्-मोक्तृ, &c. See<BR>under निर्-मुच्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोक्ष|निर्मोक्षः|निर्म्मोक्षः
निर्मोक्ष निर्-मोक्ष, अस्, m. (rt. मोक्ष्),<BR>liberation from, deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोह|निर्मोहः
निर्मोह निर्-मोह, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘free from<BR>illusion,’ an epithet of Śiva; (अस्), m., N. of a son<BR>of the fifth Manu; of one of the Saptarṣis under<BR>the thirteenth Manu; [cf. निर्-मोक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्रेतुक
निर्म्रेतुक निर्-म्रेतुक, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps<BR>fr. म्रै = म्लै with निस्), Ved. fading away,<BR>withering; (also read निर्-मेतुक, निर्-मॄतुक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्लुक्ति
निर्म्लुक्ति निर्-म्लुक्ति. See नि-म्लुक्ति, p. 490.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यत्
निर्यत् 1. निर्-यत्, अन्, अती, अत् (fr. निर्-इ),<BR>going forth, coming out, issuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यत्
निर्यत् 2. निर्-यत्, cl. 10. P. -यातयति, &c.,<BR>to give back, restore, make restitution; to forgive,<BR>pardon, set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातक
निर्-यातक, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing away, carrying<BR>away, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातन|निर्यातनं|निर्य्यातन
निर्-यातन, अम्, n. giving back, returning, de-<BR>livering, restitution, delivery of a deposit, replacing<BR>anything lost; gift, donation; payment of a debt;<BR>requital, revenge; killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातित|निर्य्यातित
निर्-यातित, अस्, आ, अम्, restored, given back,<BR>retaliated, requited; taken away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यात्य
निर्-यात्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be given back or<BR>restored or delivered (as a deposit &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यत्न
निर्यत्न निर्-यत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, inactive, lazy,<BR>listless.<BR>—निर्यत्न-ता, f. inactivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यन्त्रण|निर्यंत्रण|निर्यन्त्रणं|निर्य्यन्त्रण
निर्यन्त्रण निर्-यन्त्रण, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>restraint, unrestrained, unobstructed, uncontrolled,<BR>unconfined, unrestricted, self-willed, independant;<BR>(अम्), n. absence of restraint, independance; (अम्),<BR>ind. without restraint, unrestrainedly.<BR>—निर्यन्त्रण-<BR>प्रदेशावस्थित (˚श-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being at a<BR>place where no restraint is needed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यन्त्रित|निर्य्यन्त्रित
निर्-यन्त्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, uncontrolled, unre-<BR>strained, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यशस्क
निर्यशस्क निर्-यशस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>fame or reputation, inglorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्या
निर्या 1. निर्-या, f., Ved. any disturbance<BR>of the regular course of a rite, any defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्या
निर्या 2. निर्-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्,<BR>to go out, issue, set out: Caus. -यापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to go out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याण|निर्याणं|निर्य्याण
निर्-याण, अम्, n. going forth or out, exit, issue,<BR>setting out, departure; vanishing, disappearance;<BR>departure from life, dying, death; eternal emanci-<BR>pation, final beatitude, (probably confounded with<BR>1. निर्-वाण, q. v.); the outer corner of an elephant's<BR>eye [cf. निर्-णायन]; iron; a rope for tying cattle<BR>or for binding a calf's feet, a foot-rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यात|निर्य्यात
निर्-यात, अस्, आ, अम्, gone out, gone forth, issued,<BR>departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याति|निर्यातिः
निर्-याति, इस्, f. going out, exit, departing, dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यापण|निर्यापणं
निर्-यापण, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), expelling,<BR>expulsion, banishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याय|निर्य्याय
निर्-याय, ind. having gone out or departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यियासु
निर्-यियासु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid.), trying or<BR>wishing to go out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातृ
निर्यातृ निर्-यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a husband-<BR>man, reaper, weeder; (wrong reading for निर्-<BR>दातृ, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यादव
निर्यादव निर्-यादव, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>the Yādavas, without the Yādavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याम|निर्यामः|निर्य्याम
निर्याम निर्याम, अस्, m. a sailor, pilot,<BR>boatman (= नियामक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यास|निर्यासं|निर्यासः|निर्य्यास
निर्यास निर्-यास, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. यस्<BR>with निस्), exudation of trees or plants, juice, gum,<BR>resin, milk, &c.; extract, decoction, infusion; any<BR>thick fluid substance; [cf. अग्नि-न्˚, तन्तु-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्युक्ति|निर्य्युक्ति
निर्युक्ति निर्-युक्ति, इस्, f. disunion; want of<BR>connection or government (in grammar); unfitness,<BR>inappropriateness, impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्युक्तिक|निर्युक्तिकं|निर्य्युक्तिक
निर्-युक्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, detached, disunited;<BR>unconnected, unmeaning, illogical, not founded on<BR>sound reasoning; inappropriate, improper.<BR>—निर्-<BR>युक्तिक-त्व, अम्, n. inappropriateness; illogicalness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यूथ
निर्यूथ निर्-यूथ, अस्, आ, अम्, separated from<BR>the herd (as an elephant &c.), strayed from the flock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यूष|निर्यूषः
निर्यूष निर्-यूष, अस्, m. extract, juice, &c.,<BR>= निर्-यास = निर्-यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यूह|निर्यूहः|निर्य्यूह
निर्यूह निर्-यूह, अस्, m. (probably for निर्-<BR>व्यूह), a prominence, projection (also अम्, n.), perhaps<BR>a kind of turret-like ornament on columns or gates,<BR>a pinnacle, turret; a chaplet, crest, head-ornament,<BR>the crest of a helmet; a peg or bracket projecting<BR>from a wall to hang or place anything upon [cf.<BR>नाग-निर्यूह]; wood placed in a wall for doves to<BR>build their nests upon; a door, gate (also n.); extract,<BR>juice, decoction, &c.; [cf. निर्-यास, निर्-यूष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्योग|निर्योगः
निर्योग निर्-योग, अस्, m. (perhaps) a deco-<BR>ration, ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्योगक्षेम|निर्य्योगक्षेम
निर्योगक्षेम निर्-योगक्षेम, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from care or anxiety about property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लक्षण|निर्लक्षणः
निर्लक्षण निर्-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no special marks, undistinguished, unimportant, insig-<BR>nificant; unmarked, unspotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लक्ष्य
निर्लक्ष्य निर्-लक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, not to be<BR>observed or perceived, unobservable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लज्ज
निर्लज्ज निर्-लज्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless, im-<BR>modest, impudent, brazen.<BR>—निर्लज्ज-ता, f. shame-<BR>lessness, impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लिङ्ग|निर्लिंग
निर्लिङ्ग निर्-लिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>characteristic or distinguishing marks, not to be de-<BR>fined (as आत्मन्, ब्रह्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लिप्त|निर्लिप्तः
निर्लिप्त निर्-लिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. लिप्<BR>with निस्), unsmeared, unanointed; undefiled, uncon-<BR>taminated; (अस्), m., N. of Kṛṣṇa; a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लेप|निर्लेपः
निर्-लेप, अस्, आ, अम्, unanointed, unsmeared,<BR>free from fatty substances; stainless, spotless, sinless;<BR>(अस्), m. a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लुञ्चन|निर्लुंचन|निर्लुंचनं
निर्लुञ्चन निर्-लुञ्चन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. लुञ्च्<BR>with निस्), pulling out or off, tearing off, peeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लुण्ठन|निर्लुंठन|निर्लुंठनं
निर्लुण्ठन निर्-लुण्ठन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. लुण्ठ्<BR>with निस्), robbing, plundering; pulling out, tearing<BR>off, (in the latter sense a wrong reading for निर्-<BR>लुञ्चन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लेखन|निर्लेखनं
निर्लेखन निर्-लेखन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. लिख्<BR>with निस्), a scraper, instrument for scraping; [cf.<BR>जिह्वा-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लोभ
निर्लोभ निर्-लोभ, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>desire, unavaricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लोम
निर्लोम निर्-लोम, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of<BR>hair, hairless, smooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ल्वयनी
निर्ल्वयनी निर्-ल्वयनी, f. the cast off skin<BR>of a snake; (wrong reading for निर्-व्लयनी, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वंश
निर्वंश निर्-वंश, अस्, आ, अम्, without lineage<BR>or posterity, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वक्तव्य
निर्वक्तव्य निर्-वक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>वच् with निस्), to be interpreted or explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वचन|निर्वचनं|निर्व्वचन
1. निर्-वचन, अम्, n. (for 2. see below), pro-<BR>nunciation; a proverbial expression, proverb; inter-<BR>pretation, etymological explanation, etymology; vo-<BR>cabulary, index; [cf. 1. नि-वचन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वचनीय
निर्-वचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be defined more<BR>closely, to be interpreted or explained, to be described<BR>or related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाच्य|निर्व्वाच्य
1. निर्-वाच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = निर्-वचनीय. (For<BR>2. see under निर्-वाक्य, p. 501, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वचन|निर्वचनं|निर्व्वचन
निर्वचन 2. निर्-वचन, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1.<BR>see above), not speaking, silent; unobjectionable,<BR>unblamable, blameless; (अम्), ind. silently; [cf. 2.<BR>नि-वचन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वण|निर्व्वण
निर्वण निर्-वण or निर्-वन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being out of a wood, ranging in the open country;<BR>free from woods; bare, open, (in this sense निर् is<BR>a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वत्सशिशुपुङ्गव|निर्वत्सशिशुपुंगव
निर्वत्सशिशुपुङ्गव निर्-वत्स-शिशुपुङ्गव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, deprived of calves and young bulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वद्
निर्वद् निर्-वद्, cl. 1. P. A. -वदति, -ते,<BR>-वदितुम्, to speak out, to blame; to deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाद|निर्वादः|निर्व्वाद|निर्व्वादः
1. निर्-वाद, अस्, m. (for 2. निर्-वाद see p. 501, col.<BR>1), obloquy, censure, blame, reproach; rumour, report;<BR>asseveration, affirmation, decision of a controversy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वन|निर्व्वन
निर्वन निर्-वन. See निर्-वण above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वप्
निर्वप् निर्-वप्, cl. 1. P. A. -वपति, -ते,<BR>-वप्तुम्, to pour out, sprinkle, drop, scatter; to<BR>offer sacrifical food, present funeral oblations or<BR>libations to the Manes of deceased ancestors; to<BR>present, deliver; to perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वपण|निर्व्वपण|निर्व्वपणं
निर्-वपण, अम्, n. pouring out, sprinkling,<BR>offering, especially the presentation of funeral offer-<BR>ings to the Manes, libation, oblation; spending,<BR>bestowing presents; gift, donation, alms; a ladle or<BR>vessel for pouring; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to libations;<BR>scattering, pouring out, bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाप|निर्वापः|निर्व्वाप|निर्व्वापः
1. निर्-वाप, अस्, m. (for 2. see p. 501, col. 1),<BR>scattering, strewing, pouring out; offering, giving,<BR>bestowing; offering oblations, especially funeral obla-<BR>tions in honour of a deceased ancestor; gift, alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापण|निर्वापणं|निर्व्वापणं
1. निर्-वापण, अम्, n. (for 2. see p. 501, col. 1),<BR>scattering, throwing or pouring out, casting in, sow-<BR>ing; offering, presenting funeral oblations; gift, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापित|निर्व्वापित
1. निर्-वापित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 501, col. 1),<BR>offered in oblation, scattered, poured out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाप्य|निर्व्वाप्य
1. निर्-वाप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 3. see p. 501, col. 1),<BR>to be scattered or offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाप्य|निर्व्वाप्य
2. निर्-वाप्य, ind. having offered funeral cakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वयनी|निर्व्वयनी
निर्वयनी निर्-वयनी, f. the cast off skin<BR>of a snake; (a various reading for निर्-व्लयनी;<BR>cf. निर्-ल्वयनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर
निर्वर निर्-वर, a various reading for निर्-<BR>दर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वरुणता
निर्वरुणता निर्वरुण-ता, f. or निर्वरुण-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. deliverance from Varuṇa's power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्ण्
निर्वर्ण् निर्-वर्ण्, cl. 10. P. -वर्णयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to look at, contemplate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्णन|निर्वर्णनं|निर्व्वर्णनं
निर्-वर्णन, अम्, n. looking at, regarding,<BR>sight, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्णनीय
निर्-वर्णनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked at or<BR>regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्ण्य
निर्-वर्ण्य, ind. having looked at, having re-<BR>garded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तक
निर्वर्तक निर्-वर्तक, निर्-वर्तन, &c. See<BR>under निर्-वृत्, p. 502, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वस्
निर्वस् निर्-वस्, cl. 1. P. -वसति, -वस्तुम्,<BR>to dwell, finish dwelling; to dwell abroad: Caus.<BR>-वासयति, -यितुम्, to expel from home, banish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वास|निर्वासः
निर्-वास, अस्, m. leaving or abandoning one's<BR>home, residing far from one's native place; expulsion,<BR>banishment; killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासन|निर्वासनं|निर्व्वासन|निर्व्वासनं
1. निर्-वासन, अम्, n. (for 2. निर्-वासन see<BR>p. 501, col. 1), expelling or driving from home,<BR>banishing, banishment, expulsion; hurting, injuring,<BR>killing, slaughter, annihilation; [cf. उद्-वासन,<BR>-प्र-वासन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासनीय
निर्-वासनीय or निर्-वास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>expelled or banished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासित|निर्व्वासित
निर्-वासित, अस्, आ, अम्, expelled, banished, driven<BR>from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वसु
निर्वसु निर्-वसु, उस्, उस्, उ, destitute of<BR>wealth or property, poor.<BR>—निर्वसु-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>poverty, destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वह्
निर्वह् निर्-वह्, cl. 1. P. A. -वहति, -ते,<BR>-वोढुम्, to bring or carry out, bring one's self out<BR>of, extricate one's self: Caus. P. -वाहयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to carry out, carry on, perform, accomplish, effect,<BR>fulfil, settle; to pass, spend (time &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वहण|निर्वहणं|निर्व्वहण|निर्व्वहणं
निर्-वहण, अम्, n. end, issue, completion; the<BR>closing scene or catastrophe of a drama, the con-<BR>clusion; carrying on, (for निर्-वाहण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वहितृ
निर्-वहितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, separating, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाह|निर्वाहः|निर्व्वाह|निर्व्वाहः
निर्-वाह, अस्, m. carrying on, accomplishing, per-<BR>forming, managing, accomplishment, management;<BR>completion, end; narrating, describing; supporting,<BR>maintaining; subsisting on; sufficiency, adequacy,<BR>competent provision or means of living; steadfastness;<BR>[cf. नैर्वाहिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहक|निर्व्वाहक
निर्-वाहक, अस्, इका, अम्, accomplishing, per-<BR>forming, effecting; (अम्), n. application or connec-<BR>tion of cause and effect (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहण|निर्व्वाहण|निर्व्वाहणं
निर्-वाहण, अस्, आ, अम्, carrying out, effecting;<BR>carrying away, removing; (अम्), n. accomplishment,<BR>completion; the catastrophe or closing scene of a<BR>drama (= निर्-वहण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहिन्
निर्-वाहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, leading out, carrying out;<BR>discharging (as a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाह्य
निर्-वाह्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be carried on or<BR>accomplished or performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वा|निर्व्वा
निर्वा निर्-वा, cl. 2. P. -वाति, -वातुम्, to<BR>cease to blow; (cl. 4. -वायति, &c.), to be extin-<BR>guished; to be refreshed: Caus. -वापयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to extinguish, put out; to refresh, cool, allay, make<BR>happy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाण|निर्व्वाण|निर्व्वाणं|निर्व्वाणः
1. निर्-वाण, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. निर्-वाण see p. 501,<BR>col. 1), blown out, gone out, put out, extinguished<BR>(as a fire); lost, disappeared; liberated from exist-<BR>ence (lit. having the fire of life extinguished); dead,<BR>deceased, defunct; set (as a planet); calmed, quieted,<BR>(अ-निर्वाण, an elephant not yet tamed or one<BR>just caught and wild); immersed, plunged; (अम्), n.<BR>blowing out, extinguishing, extinction, (in this and<BR>some of the following senses निर्-वाणम् is not the<BR>neut. of the pass. part. but formed fr. निर्-वा with<BR>affix अन), becoming extinguished, disappearance,<BR>setting, vanishing from sight, (निर्वाणं कृ, to<BR>act as if nothing had happened, not to keep one's<BR>promise); extinction of the flame of life, dissolution,<BR>liberation, eternal bliss, final emancipation from<BR>matter and reunion with the deity, union with the<BR>Supreme Spirit; (with Buddhists and Jainas) absolute<BR>extinction or annihilation, complete extinction of<BR>individual existence; perfect and perpetual calm,<BR>repose; complete satisfaction or pleasure, highest<BR>felicity; desisting, leaving off, cessation; vacuity,<BR>vacuum; union, association, blending, confluence; of-<BR>fering oblations, (perhaps wrongly for 1. निर्-वापण);<BR>bathing of an elephant (because he draws in water<BR>with his trunk and then blows it out over his body);<BR>instructing in sciences; ‘Deliverance,’ N. of an Upa-<BR>niṣad; [cf. अप-न्˚, परि-न्˚.]<BR>—निर्वाण-पुराण,<BR>अम्, n. offering oblations to the dead.<BR>—निर्वाण-<BR>प्रकरण, अम्, n., N. of the fourth chapter of<BR>the Vāsiṣṭha-rāmāyaṇa, commonly called Yoga-<BR>vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—निर्वाण-भूयिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, almost<BR>all vanished or departed.<BR>—निर्वाण-मण्डप, N.<BR>of a temple.<BR>—निर्वाण-मन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>mystical formula.<BR>—निर्वाण-मस्तक, अस्, m. libe-<BR>ration, deliverance.<BR>—निर्वाण-रुचि, अयस्, m. pl.<BR>‘delighting in final beatitude,’ N. of a class of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">Page0501-a+ 73</a>]<BR>deities under the eleventh Manu; [cf. निर्माण-रति.]<BR>—निर्वाण-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having complete<BR>felicity as its characteristic mark.<BR>—निर्वाण-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of certain Buddhist Sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणिन्
निर्-वाणिन्, ई, m. (with Jainas) N. of the second<BR>Arhat of the past Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वात|निर्वातः|निर्व्वात|निर्व्वातः
1. निर्-वात, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see below), ceased<BR>to blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाप|निर्वापः|निर्व्वाप|निर्व्वापः
2. निर्-वाप, अस्, m. (for 1. see under निर्-वप्,<BR>p. 500, col. 2), putting out, extinguishing (as a fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापण|निर्वापणं|निर्व्वापणं
2. निर्-वापण, अम्, n. (for 1. see under निर्-वप्,<BR>p. 500, col. 2), putting out (as a fire or light),<BR>extinguishing, quenching; extinction, annihilation;<BR>slaughter, killing; (in medicine) refrigerant; cooling,<BR>refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापयितृ
निर्-वापयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, extinguishing, refri-<BR>gerant, one who allays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापित|निर्व्वापित
2. निर्-वापित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see under निर्-<BR>वप्, p. 500, col. 2), extinguished, put out, quenched;<BR>allayed, cooled; killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाप्य|निर्व्वाप्य
3. निर्-वाप्य, ind. (for 1. and 2. see under निर्-<BR>वप्, p. 500, col. 2), having extinguished or quenched;<BR>having refreshed or delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाक
निर्वाक निर्वाक, अस्, m. in कर्ण-निर्वाक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाक्य
निर्वाक्य निर्-वाक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, speechless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाच्
निर्-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, silent, mute, dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाच्य|निर्व्वाच्य
2. निर्-वाच्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see under निर्-<BR>वक्तव्य, p. 500, col. 2), improper to be said;<BR>unobjectionable, blameless, not to be found fault with<BR>or censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाञ्च्
निर्वाञ्च् निर्वाञ्च्, आङ्, आची, आक् (according to<BR>the commentator fr. निर्-अव-अञ्च्), outward, exterior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाण|निर्व्वाण|निर्व्वाणं|निर्व्वाणः
निर्वाण 2. निर्-वाण, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see<BR>under निर्-वा, p. 500, col. 3), having no arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाणी
निर्वाणी निर्-वाणी, f. (with Jainas) N. of a<BR>deity who executes the commands of the sixteenth<BR>Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वात|निर्वातः|निर्व्वात|निर्व्वातः
निर्वात 2. निर्-वात, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see<BR>above), free from wind, sheltered from wind, not<BR>windy, calm, still; (अस्), m. a calm, a place sheltered<BR>from wind.<BR>—निर्वात-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing<BR>sheltered from the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाद|निर्वादः|निर्व्वाद|निर्व्वादः
निर्वाद 2. निर्-वाद, अस्, m. (for 1. निर्-वाद<BR>see under निर्-वद्, p. 500, col. 2), absence of<BR>dispute or railing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वानर
निर्वानर निर्-वानर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>monkeys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाप|निर्वापः|निर्व्वाप|निर्व्वापः
निर्वाप 1. and 2. निर्-वाप. See p. 500,<BR>col. 2, and above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वायस
निर्वायस निर्-वायस, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>crows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वार्य|निर्वार्य्य|निर्व्वार्य्य|निर्व्वार्य्यः
निर्वार्य निर्-वार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, irresistible,<BR>not to be opposed or resisted; acting fearlessly or<BR>determinedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासन|निर्वासनं|निर्व्वासन|निर्व्वासनं
निर्वासन 2. निर्-वासन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस्<BR>+ वासना; for 1. निर्-वासन see under निर्-वस्,<BR>p. 500, col. 2), without fancy or imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाह|निर्वाहः|निर्व्वाह|निर्व्वाहः
निर्वाह निर्-वाह, निर्-वाहण. See निर्-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विकल्प|निर्व्विकल्प
निर्विकल्प निर्-विकल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, not ad-<BR>mitting an alternative; recognising no such distinc-<BR>tions as that of subject and object; being without<BR>determination; (अम्), ind. without hesitation or<BR>vacillation, without wavering, without reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विकल्पक|निर्व्विकल्पक|निर्व्विकल्पकं
निर्-विकल्पक or निर्-विकल्पन, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>admitting an alternative, free from differences, having<BR>no mutual dependence; not capable of mutual relation;<BR>undeliberative; conditioned; (अम्), n. knowledge not<BR>depending upon or derived from the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विकार|निर्विकारः|निर्व्विकार|निर्व्विकारः
निर्विकार निर्-विकार, अस्, आ, अम्, or निर्-<BR>विकार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, unchanged, unaltered, un-<BR>changeable, immutable, uniform.<BR>—निर्विकार-ता, f.<BR>unchangeableness, uniformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विकास
निर्विकास निर्-विकास, अस्, आ, अम्, not yet<BR>opened or expanded (as a blossom), unblown.<BR>—निर्-<BR>विकास-त्व, अम्, n. the being not yet opened or<BR>expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विक्रम्
निर्विक्रम् निर्-वि-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रामति,<BR>-क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to go out of, come out of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विघ्न|निर्व्विघ्न
निर्विघ्न निर्-विघ्न, अस्, आ, अम्, unobstructed,<BR>uninterrupted, untroubled, secure from impediments;<BR>(अम्), n. absence of obstruction or impediment;<BR>(अम् or एन), ind. unobstructedly, freely, securely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विचार
निर्विचार निर्-विचार, अस्, आ, अम्, not re-<BR>flecting or considering; (अम्), ind. without reflection,<BR>without consideration, inconsiderately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विचिकित्स
निर्विचिकित्स निर्-विचिकित्स, अस्, आ, अम्, with-<BR>out reflecting much; (अम्), ind. without much or<BR>long reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विचेष्ट
निर्विचेष्ट निर्-विचेष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, motion-<BR>less, insensible, unresisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वितर्क
निर्वितर्क निर्-वितर्क, अस्, आ, अम्, unreflect-<BR>ing, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विद्|निर्व्विद्
निर्विद् निर्-विद्, cl. 4. A. -विद्यते, &c., to<BR>be disgusted with one's self, to disparage or despise<BR>one's self, be ashamed of one's self, to be disgusted,<BR>to be despondent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्णः
निर्-विण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, despondent, depressed;<BR>disgusted with anything (gen.); loathing; self-dis-<BR>paraged, overcome with fear or sorrow; emaciated<BR>with grief; decayed, impaired; abused, degraded;<BR>humble; known, certain.<BR>—निर्विण्ण-चेतस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, depressed in mind, broken in spirit, humble-<BR>minded, meek, resigned, desponding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेद|निर्वेदः|निर्व्वेदः
1. निर्-वेद, अस्, m. disgust, loathing, feeling dis-<BR>gust for (with gen. or loc., e. g. जीविते निर्वेदः,<BR>disgust for life); satiety, loathsomeness; despondency,<BR>self-disparagement; humility; grief; complete indif-<BR>ference, disregard of worldly objects; despair, despera-<BR>tion; shame.<BR>—निर्वेद-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, disgusted<BR>(with worldly concerns); full of despondency; in-<BR>different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विद्य
निर्विद्य निर्-विद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unlearned,<BR>destitute of knowledge, uneducated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विधित्स
निर्विधित्स निर्-विधित्स, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>wishing to do, having no designs, free from desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विनोद
निर्विनोद निर्-विनोद, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>amusement, without pastime, void of solace or<BR>diversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विन्ध्य
निर्विन्ध्य निर्-विन्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, living on<BR>the outside or other side of the Vindhyas; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a river rising in the Vindhya hills or of one<BR>rising in the Ṛkṣa mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विभास्
निर्विभास् निर्-वि-भास्, Caus. -भासयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to illuminate, enlighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विमर्श
निर्विमर्श निर्-विमर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, not con-<BR>sidering, unreflecting, devoid of reflection; (also<BR>written निर्-विमर्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवर|निर्व्विवर
निर्विवर निर्-विवर, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>opening or rent, without interval or interstice, close,<BR>contiguous.<BR>—निर्विवर-ता, f. want of interstice,<BR>contiguousness (as of the female breasts); want of<BR>enmity; agreement, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवह्
निर्विवह् निर्-वि-वह्, cl. 1. P. A. -वहति,<BR>-ते, -वोढुम्, to carry out, export; to expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवाद
निर्विवाद निर्-विवाद, अस्, आ, अम्, not con-<BR>tending or disagreeing, agreeing with each other;<BR>(अम्), n. absence of contention or controversy.<BR>—निर्-<BR>विवादी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made to agree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवित्सु
निर्विवित्सु निर्-विवित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the<BR>Desid. of rt. विद् with निस्), desirous to find (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवेक|निर्व्विवेक
निर्विवेक निर्-विवेक, अस्, आ, अम्, indiscreet,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">Page0501-c+ 72</a>]<BR>undiscriminating, wanting discrimination or judg-<BR>ment, foolish.<BR>—निर्विवेक-त्व, अम्, n. want of<BR>discrimination or judgment, indiscretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विश्
निर्विश् निर्-विश्, cl. 6. P. -विशति, -वेष्टुम्,<BR>to enter into, to meet with, enjoy (with acc., e. g.<BR>मधुं निर्विविशुः, they enjoyed wine); to ex-<BR>perience; to embellish; to reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशत्|निर्व्विशत्
निर्-विशत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, entering in or into;<BR>attaining, obtaining; engaging in; marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्टः
निर्-विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, attained, arrived at, met<BR>with; obtained, gained, experienced, earned, received;<BR>engaged in, occupied by, staying in; married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेश|निर्वेशः|निर्व्वेशः
निर्-वेश, अस्, m. entering into, gaining, obtaining;<BR>wages, hire, employment; payment, returning pay-<BR>ment [cf. नि-वेश्य]; expiation, atonement, (अ-निर्-<BR>वेश, one who has not expiated his sins); enjoyment,<BR>eating; fainting, swooning, syncope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेशनीय
निर्-वेशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gained or enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेष्टव्य
निर्-वेष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be entered into; to<BR>be rewarded, to be paid; to be embellished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशङ्क|निर्विशंक|निर्व्विशङ्क
निर्विशङ्क निर्-विशङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, or निर्-<BR>विशङ्कित, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless, undaunted, confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशेष|निर्विशेषः|निर्व्विशेष
निर्विशेष निर्-विशेष, अस्, m. absence of<BR>difference, no difference; (अस्, आ, अम्), showing no<BR>difference, making no difference, not differing, with-<BR>out distinction; undiscriminating; indiscriminate;<BR>same, like, (at the end of an adj. comp.; cf. नीलोत्-<BR>पल-न्˚); (अम् or एण), ind. without difference,<BR>indifferently, indiscriminately, without distinction,<BR>equally, (स्व-गृह-निर्विशेषेण, just the same as in<BR>one's own house.)<BR>—निर्विशेष-त्व, अम्, n. absence<BR>of difference, want of distinction, indiscriminateness.<BR>—निर्विशेष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, showing no differ-<BR>ence, undistinguished, indiscriminate.<BR>—निर्विशेषा-<BR>कृति (˚ष-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, whose forms are pre-<BR>cisely alike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशेषण
निर्-विशेषण, अस्, आ, अम्, having no attributes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष
निर्विष निर्-विष, अस्, आ, अम्, without venom,<BR>poisonless (as serpents); (आ and ई), f. a species of<BR>grass, Kyllingia Monocephala, used as an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषङ्ग
निर्विषङ्ग निर्-विषङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>attached to anything, indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषय|निर्व्विषय
निर्विषय निर्-विषय, अस्, m. no residence;<BR>any place not deserving the name of a residence;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), expelled or driven away from one's<BR>residence or home, banished; having no sphere of<BR>action, not attached to any object, objectless; sepa-<BR>rated from sensual objects, not attached to them (as<BR>mind).<BR>—निर्विषय-त्व, अम्, n. non-attachment<BR>to any object.<BR>—निर्विषयाकार (˚य-आक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, not deserving the name of a dwelling-place.<BR>—निर्विषयी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, expelled from one's<BR>place of residence.<BR>—निर्विषयोपराग (˚य-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, unharmed by objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषाण
निर्विषाण निर्-विषाण, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute<BR>of horns or tusks, tuskless (as an elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विहङ्ग|निर्विहंग
निर्विहङ्ग निर्-विहङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>birds, free from birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विहार
निर्विहार निर्-विहार, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>pleasure, deprived of pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीज|निर्व्वीज
निर्वीज निर्-वीज, अस्, आ, अम्, seedless; im-<BR>potent; (आ), f. a sort of grape without seeds or stones<BR>(= काकली-द्राक्षा, commonly called किष्मिष्).<BR>—निर्वीज-त्व, अम्, n. seedlessness, impotence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर|निर्व्वीर|निर्व्वीरं
निर्वीर निर्-वीर, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of<BR>men or heroes; unheroic, cowardly; (आ), f. a woman<BR>whose husband and children are dead, a childless<BR>widow; N. of a river; (अम्), n., N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीरुध्
निर्वीरुध् निर्-वीरुध्, त्, त्, त्, deprived of<BR>plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर्य|निर्वीर्य्य|निर्व्वीर्य्य
निर्वीर्य निर्-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, powerless,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">Page0502-a+ 72</a>]<BR>unmanly, without manly courage, spiritless, tame,<BR>feeble, impotent.<BR>—निर्वीर्य-ता, f. unmanliness,<BR>powerlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृ
निर्वृ निर्-वृ, apparently only occurring in<BR>the derivatives below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied, contented, happy,<BR>pleased, enraptured, tranquil, at ease, secure, free<BR>from cares, free from anxiety and troubles, free from<BR>occupation or interest, emancipated; ended, termi-<BR>nated, ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृति|निर्वृतिः
निर्-वृति, इस्, f. complete satisfaction, contentment,<BR>tranquillity, bliss, happiness, gladness, pleasure; final<BR>emancipation or liberation from existence; freedom;<BR>rest, repose; setting, disappearance, death, destruc-<BR>tion; completion, accomplishment (for निर्-वृत्ति);<BR>ceasing, abstaining from (for नि-वृत्ति); incivility,<BR>impropriety (for निर्-वृत्ति); (इस्), m., N. of a man;<BR>of a son of Vṛṣṇi; (the forms निर्-वृति, निर्-<BR>वृत्ति, and नि-वृत्ति are often incorrectly confounded<BR>together.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृक्ष
निर्वृक्ष निर्-वृक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, treeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्
निर्वृत् निर्-वृत्, cl. 1. A. (also P. in Fut.<BR>Cond. and Aor.) -वर्तते, -वर्तितुम्, to be completed<BR>or accomplished, to be effected; to draw back, recede,<BR>desist, cease, not to be done, not to take place, (in<BR>these senses probably for नि-वृत्, q. v.): Caus.<BR>-वर्तयति, -यितुम्, to complete, accomplish, finish,<BR>perform, produce, create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तक
निर्-वर्तक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), com-<BR>pleting, accomplishing, performing, finishing, ending,<BR>executing; desisting; [cf. नि-वर्तक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तन|निर्वर्तनं|निर्वर्त्तन|निर्व्वर्त्तन
निर्-वर्तन, अम्, n. accomplishment, completion,<BR>execution; desisting (for नि-वर्तन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तनीय
निर्-वर्तनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be completed or<BR>accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तिन्
निर्-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, accomplishing, performing,<BR>executing; behaving rudely or uncivilly, uncivil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्त्य|निर्व्वर्त्य
1. निर्-वर्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be accomplished, per-<BR>formable, to be pronounced or uttered, pronounceable.<BR>—निर्वर्त्य-त्व, अम्, n. performableness; pro-<BR>nounceableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्त्य|निर्व्वर्त्य
2. निर्-वर्त्य, ind. having accomplished, having<BR>performed or finished; having ceased, (for नि-वर्त्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्त|निर्वृत्तः
निर्-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, finished, completely done,<BR>accomplished.<BR>—निर्वृत्त-शत्रु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince of the Kaliṅgas; (probably wrongly for नि-<BR>वृत्त-शत्रु; cf. निनर्त-शत्रु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्ति|निर्वृत्तिः
निर्-वृत्ति, इस्, f. completion, termination, con-<BR>clusion; (in grammar) cessation of the influence of<BR>one rule over another; result, fruit, reward; impro-<BR>priety, incivility [cf. निर्-वर्तिन् above]; final beati-<BR>tude (for निर्-वृति); abstaining from action, inac-<BR>tivity (for नि-वृत्ति); (इस्, इस्, इ), having no occu-<BR>pation, destitute, (in this sense निर् is a privative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्वृत निर्-वृत, निर्-वृति. See under निर्-<BR>वृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृष्
निर्वृष् निर्-वृष्, cl. 1. P. -वर्षति, -वर्-<BR>षितुम्, to cease to rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृष्टि
निर्-वृष्टि, इस्, f. cessation of rain, want of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृष
निर्वृष निर्-वृष, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of<BR>bulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेग
निर्वेग निर्-वेग, अस्, आ, अम्, without violent<BR>motion or impetuosity, not waving, quiet, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेतन
निर्वेतन निर्-वेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, not receiv-<BR>ing wages, unsalaried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेद|निर्वेदः|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेद 2. निर्-वेद, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. निर्-<BR>वेद see under निर्-विद्, p. 501, col. 2), not having<BR>the Vedas, infidel, unscriptural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेधिम
निर्वेधिम निर्-वेधिम (fr. व्यध् with निस्),<BR>with कर्ण, a peculiar deformity of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेपन
निर्वेपन निर्-वेपन, अस्, आ, अम्, not trem-<BR>bling, not flickering (as the flame of a lamp).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेश|निर्वेशः|निर्व्वेशः
निर्वेश निर्-वेश. See under निर्-विश्, p. 501,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेष्टन|निर्वेष्टनं|निर्व्वेष्टनं
निर्वेष्टन निर्-वेष्टन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. वेष्ट्<BR>with निस्), a small reed used as a shuttle, a weaver's<BR>shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वैर
निर्वैर निर्-वैर, अम्, n. absence of enmity;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), free from enmity, without enmity,<BR>living in peace, peaceable; (अस्), m., N. of a hunter;<BR>(अम्), ind. peaceably, without enmity.<BR>—निर्वैर-ता,<BR>f. freedom from enmity, peaceableness, concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वैरिण
निर्-वैरिण, अम्, n. absence of enmity, concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वोढृ
निर्वोढृ निर्-वोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ, car-<BR>rying or leading away, who or what carries away;<BR>separating, dividing; [cf. निर्-वहितृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यञ्जन|निर्व्यंजन
निर्व्यञ्जन निर्-व्यञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>condiment; straightforward; (ए), ind. in a straight-<BR>forward or downright manner; plainly, without<BR>verbosity; silently (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथ
निर्व्यथ निर्-व्यथ, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>pain; quiet, unmoved, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथन|निर्व्यथनं
निर्-व्यथन, अम्, n. a hole, chasm (a place of<BR>rest); freedom from pain; paining, afflicting, (in<BR>this sense निर् is a prep.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यपेक्ष
निर्व्यपेक्ष निर्-व्यपेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, disre-<BR>garding, indifferent to (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यलीक
निर्व्यलीक निर्-व्यलीक, अस्, आ, अम्, not caus-<BR>ing pain, not hurting, not offending; not feeling<BR>pain, without pain, pleased, doing willingly or sin-<BR>cerely, sincere, genuine, undissembling; (अम्), ind.<BR>sincerely, readily.<BR>—निर्व्यलीक-तस्, ind. sincerely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याकुल
निर्व्याकुल निर्-व्याकुल, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>troubled or disquieted, not excited, calm.<BR>—निर्-<BR>व्याकुल-ता, f. freedom from trouble, calmness;<BR>(तया), ind. with complete calmness, quite calmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याघ्र
निर्व्याघ्र निर्-व्याघ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>tigers, not infested by tigers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याज
निर्व्याज निर्-व्याज, अस्, आ, अम्, without de-<BR>ceit, candid, upright, straightforward, honest, plain,<BR>exact; (अम्), ind. honestly, exactly, plainly.<BR>—निर्व्याज-<BR>ता, f. honesty, plainness, candour.<BR>—निर्व्याजी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, made plain, freed from deceit or illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याधि
निर्व्याधि निर्-व्याधि, इस्, इस्, इ, free from<BR>sickness, healthy, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यापार
निर्व्यापार निर्-व्यापार, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>employment or business, free from occupation, un-<BR>occupied, not busy, at leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूह्
निर्व्यूह् निर्-व्य्-ऊह्, cl. 1. P. A. -ऊहति, -ते,<BR>&c., to push out, carry out, lead or bring away, re-<BR>move; to arrange, put in order, perform, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढ|निर्व्यूढं
निर्-व्यूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, finished, completed;<BR>abandoned, left, deserted; (अम्), n. various reading<BR>for निर्-वाह, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढि|निर्व्यूढिः
निर्-व्यूढि, इस्, f. end, completion; the top,<BR>highest point or degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूह|निर्व्यूहः
निर्-व्यूह, अस्, m. a turret; a helmet or its<BR>ornament, a crest; a pinnacle (?); a door, gate; a<BR>pin or peg in a wall to hang things upon; decoction;<BR>[cf. निर्-यूह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्रण
निर्व्रण निर्-व्रण, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>wounds, unhurt; undamaged; without notches or<BR>rents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्रत
निर्व्रत निर्-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, neglecting<BR>religious observances, not observing vows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्रस्क
निर्व्रस्क निर्-व्रस्क, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. व्रश्च्<BR>with निस्), uprooted, extirpated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्लयनी
निर्व्लयनी निर्-व्लयनी, f. (fr. rt. व्ली with<BR>निस्). See निर्-ल्वयनी, p. 500, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हन्
निर्हन् निर्-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -हन्तुम्,<BR>Ved. to strike out, expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हस्त
निर्हस्त निर्-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. handless,<BR>without hands; [cf. नैर्हस्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हाद|निर्हादः
निर्हाद निर्-हाद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हद् with<BR>निस्), evacuation, voiding excrement; [cf. निर्-हार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हार|निर्हारः
निर्हार निर्-हार. See under निर्-हृ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हिम
निर्हिम निर्-हिम, अम्, n. cessation of winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृ
निर्हृ निर्-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते, -हर्-<BR>तुम्, to draw out from, extract, tear out, pull out,<BR>root up; to carry out (a dead body), to carry or<BR>take away; to export (goods); to change or mix<BR>together (clothes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरण|निर्हरणं
निर्-हरण, अम्, n. taking forth or out, drawing<BR>out, extracting, rooting up, taking away, removing,<BR>removal; setting aside, carrying away, carrying out<BR>dead bodies to be burnt, carrying a corpse to the<BR>funeral pyre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरणीय
निर्-हरणीय or निर्-हर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to<BR>be taken away or removed; to be drawn out, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हार|निर्हारः
निर्-हार, अस्, m. extracting, drawing out, rooting<BR>up, destroying, destruction; putting forth or out;<BR>carrying away, carrying out a corpse or dead body<BR>to the funeral pile to be burnt; taking away, re-<BR>moving, abstracting; setting aside; accumulation of<BR>a private store of wealth, a hoard; evacuation of any<BR>of the natural excrements of the body, (opposed to<BR>आ-हार; cf. निर्-हाद, नी-हार); giving away (?);<BR>diffusive fragrance; completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारक
निर्-हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, carrying out (a dead<BR>body to the funeral pile), one who carries out or<BR>extracts or removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारण
निर्-हारण, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), causing (a<BR>dead body) to be carried out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिन्
निर्-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking forth or out, carrying<BR>out; diffusively fragrant, spreading wide (as odour);<BR>having wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत
निर्-हृत, अस्, आ, अम्, extracted, drawn out, taken<BR>or carried forth or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृति|निर्हृतिः
निर्-हृति, इस्, f. bringing away, taking out of<BR>one's way, removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत्य
1. निर्-हृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be taken out;<BR>to be left out or omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत्य
2. निर्-हृत्य, ind. having taken forth or out, having<BR>extracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हेति
निर्हेति निर्-हेति, इस्, इस्, इ, weaponless, un-<BR>armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हेतु
निर्हेतु निर्-हेतु, उस्, उस्, उ, causeless, reason-<BR>less, having no cause or reason.<BR>—निर्हेतु-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. causelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्राद|निर्ह्रादः
निर्ह्राद निर्-ह्राद or नि-ह्राद, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>rt. ह्राद् with निस्), a sound in general.<BR>—निर्ह्राद-<BR>भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, terrified by a sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रादिन्
निर्-ह्रादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding, resounding, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रास|निर्ह्रासः
निर्ह्रास निर्-ह्रास, अस्, m. abbreviation,<BR>shortening (of a vowel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रीक
निर्ह्रीक निर्-ह्रीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + ह्री),<BR>not shy, without shame, bold, daring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निल्
निल् निल्, cl. 6. P. निलति, &c., to un-<BR>derstand with difficulty, to be impassable<BR>or impenetrable; [cf. नि-ली below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलय्
निलय् निल्-अय् (= निर्-अय्), cl. 1. A. -अयते,<BR>-यितुम्, to go out; [cf. rt. इ and rt. अय्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयन|निलयनं
1. निल्-अयन, अम्, n. (for 2. see under नि-ली<BR>below), the act of going out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्प|निलिंप|निलिंपः|निलिम्पः
निलिम्प नि-लिम्प, अस्, m. (fr. rt. लिप् with<BR>नि), Ved., N. of a particular class of supernatural<BR>beings; a troop of Maruts; a god in general; (आ),<BR>f. a cow.<BR>—निलिम्प-निर्झरी, f. the river of the<BR>gods, the Gaṅgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पिका|निलिंपिका
निलिम्पिका, f. a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निली
निली नि-ली, cl. 4. A. -लीयते, -लेतुम् and<BR>-लातुम्, to lie down, settle down, alight; to hide<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">Page0503-a+ 75</a>]<BR>one's self, disappear, conceal one's self from (with<BR>abl.); to sink down, perish, (नि-लिल्यिरे, they perished,<BR>Mahā-bh. Sauptika-p. 399.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलय|निलयः
नि-लय, अस्, m. hiding one's self; a hiding-place;<BR>the lair or den of animals, a nest; dwelling, abode,<BR>residence, house, habitation; (often at the end of a<BR>comp. in the sense of) having one's residence,<BR>living, residing in (e. g. कैलास-निलय, residing<BR>in Kailāsa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयन|निलयनं
2. नि-लयन, अम्, n. (for 1. see p. 502, col. 3),<BR>settling in a place, alighting; place of refuge, dwelling-<BR>place, dwelling, habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायिता
निलायि-ता, f. dwelling, residing in, the being<BR>domesticated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायिन्
नि-लायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in, inhabiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीन|निलीनं
नि-लीन, अस्, आ, अम्, fused in or into; involved, en-<BR>compassed, surrounded, shut or wrapt up, embraced,<BR>destroyed, perished; transformed, changed; full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीनक
निलीनक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), N. of a village in<BR>the north country; [cf. नैलीनक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीयमान
नि-लीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, hiding, lying concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवक्षस्
निवक्षस् नि-वक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. (pro-<BR>bably) an epithet of the sacrificial animal (implying<BR>some peculiarity of colour &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवचन
निवचन 1. नि-वचन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. वच्<BR>with नि), Ved. expression, address; a proverbial<BR>expression; [cf. 1. निर्-वचन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवचन
निवचन 2. नि-वचन, अस्, आ, अम् (नि = निस्),<BR>(Pāṇ. 1. 4, 76), not speaking; [cf. 2. निर्-वचन.]<BR>—निवचने-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>obstruct the speech, to cease to speak.<BR>—निवचने-<BR>कृत्य or निवचने-कृत्वा, ind. having ceased to<BR>speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवत्
निवत् नि-वत्, त्, f. (fr. नि), Ved. a steep<BR>place, a valley; (ता), ind. downhill, downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवध्
निवध् नि-वध्, a defective verb (see वध्),<BR>to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवना
निवना नि-वना, ind., Ved. downwards,<BR>downhill; [cf. नि-वता.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवप्
निवप् नि-वप्, cl. 1. P. A. -वपति, -ते,<BR>-वप्तुम्, to scatter seed, sow; to offer, make offer-<BR>ings of cakes &c. to the Manes; to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवपन|निवपनं
नि-वपन, अम्, n. pouring out, scattering or<BR>throwing down; sowing; oblations or gifts in<BR>honour of deceased ancestors, an offering to the<BR>Manes; [cf. निर्-वपण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाप|निवापः
नि-वाप, अस्, m. seed, grain, seed corn; an oblation<BR>or offering to the Manes of deceased parents or<BR>relatives, a libation or offering of water &c. at the<BR>Śrāddha; gift, offering in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापक|निवापकः
नि-वापक, अस्, m. a sower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापिन्
निवापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pouring out, throwing or scat-<BR>tering down, sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युप्त
न्य्-उप्त, न्य्-उप्य. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर|निवरः
निवर नि-वर. See नि-वृ, p. 504, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त
निवर्त नि-वर्त, नि-वर्तन, &c. See नि-<BR>वृत्, p. 504, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हण
निवर्हण नि-वर्हण. See नि-वृह्, p. 504.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवस्
निवस् 1. नि-वस्, cl. 1. P. -वसति, -वस्तुम्,<BR>to dwell, inhabit, reside, lodge, live in (with loc.);<BR>to sojourn, pass time, pass the night; to roost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसत्
नि-वसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, dwelling in, inhabiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसति|निवसतिः
नि-वसति, इस्, f. a habitation, abiding, abode,<BR>house, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसथ|निवसथः
नि-वसथ, अस्, f. a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसन|निवसनं
1. नि-वसन, अम्, n. a dwelling, house, a habita-<BR>tion. (For 2. see under 2. नि-वस्, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवस्तव्य
नि-वस्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be lived; to be spent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवास|निवासः
1. नि-वास, अस्, m. (for 2. see under 2. नि-वस्,<BR>col. 2), living, dwelling, residing; passing the night;<BR>a place of residence, dwelling-place, abode, house;<BR>night-quarters.<BR>—निवास-भूमि, इस्, f. place of<BR>residence.<BR>—निवास-भूय, अम्, n. habitation; in-<BR>habiting.<BR>—निवास-राजन्, आ, m. the king of the<BR>country in which one dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासन|निवासनं
1. नि-वासन, अम्, n. (for 2. see under 2. नि-वस्<BR>below), living, residing [cf. जगन्-न्˚]; sojourn;<BR>passing or spending time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासिन्
1. नि-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dwelling, abiding in, inhabit-<BR>ing, an inhabitant, resident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवस्
निवस् 2. नि-वस्, cl. 2. A. -वस्ते, -वसितुम्,<BR>to put on or wear (clothes), dress; to change one's<BR>clothes: Caus. or cl. 10. P. -वासयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>put on (a garment?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसन|निवसनं
2. नि-वसन, अम्, n. (for 1. see under 1. नि-वस्,<BR>col. 1), putting on (a garment), cloth, clothes, raiment;<BR>an under garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवास|निवासः
2. नि-वास, अस्, m. (for 1. see under 1. नि-वस्,<BR>col. 1), dress (e. g. in चर्म-निवास, dressed in a<BR>skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासन|निवासनं
2. नि-वासन, अम्, n. (for 1. see under 1. नि-वस्,<BR>above), (with Buddhists) a kind of raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासय
नि-वासय (fr. 2. नि-वास), Nom. P. निवासयति,<BR>&c., to put on (a garment), to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासिन्
2. नि-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ (at the end of a comp.),<BR>dressed in, wearing, clothed, covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवह्
निवह् नि-वह्, cl. 1. P. A. -वहति, -ते,<BR>-वोढुम्, to bring or lead near; to carry, to support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवह|निवहः
नि-वह, अस्, m. a multitude, quantity, heap, (in<BR>this sense also आस्, m. pl.); N. of one of the seven<BR>winds; one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाह
नि-वाह, अस्, m., Ved. leading down, (opposed to<BR>अभ्य्-अवरोह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवात|निवातः
निवात 1. नि-वात, अस्, आ, अम् (नि = निस्),<BR>protected against or sheltered from the wind, not<BR>reached by the wind, not windy, calm [cf. 2. निर्-<BR>वात]; (अम्), n. a place sheltered from or inac-<BR>cessible to the wind, a sheltered spot, (sometimes<BR>used at the end of a comp. of which the first member<BR>expresses the sheltering object, see Pāṇ. VI. 2, 8);<BR>a calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवात|निवातः
निवात 2. नि-वात, अस्, आ, अम् (नि + वात fr.<BR>वन्), unimpeded, unhurt, uninjured; secure, safe<BR>(as in an asylum); well armed, accoutred in strong<BR>mail; (अस्), m. an asylum, a refuge, a dwelling, &c.;<BR>an impenetrable coat of mail; (अम्), n. security, a<BR>secure spot; strong armour.<BR>—निवात-कवच, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, whose armour or mail is impenetrable, wear-<BR>ing an impenetrable coat of mail; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>demon, the grandson of Hiraṇya-kaśipu; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a class of Dānavas or Daityas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाप|निवापः
निवाप नि-वाप, &c. See नि-वप्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार|निवारः
निवार नि-वार. See नि-वृ, p. 504, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाश
निवाश नि-वाश, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वाश् with<BR>नि), Ved. bellowing, roaring, sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविड|निविडं
निविड नि-विड, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. विड = विल,<BR>a hole, with नि = निस्), without spaces or interstices,<BR>close, contiguous, coarse, large, bulky; gross, thick,<BR>impervious, impenetrable, dense, firm; crooked-<BR>nosed; (अस्), m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविडय
निविडय, Nom. P. निविडयति, &c., to make<BR>tight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविडीस
नि-विडीस, अस्, आ, अम्, compact, close; coarse,<BR>gross; crooked-nosed (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीस|निविरीसं
नि-विरीस or नि-विरीश = नि-विड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविद्
निविद् 1. नि-विद्, cl. 2. P. -वेत्ति, -वेद, -वे-<BR>दितुम्, to tell, communicate, proclaim: Caus. -वेद-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to make known, tell, communicate,<BR>report, represent, betray, relate (with dat., loc., or gen.<BR>of the person); to present, offer, give, deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविद्
2. नि-विद्, त्, f., Ved. instruction, information, direc-<BR>tion, communication, precept, doctrine; invocation;<BR>N. of certain sentences or short formularies inserted<BR>in a liturgy and containing epithets or short invoca-<BR>tions of the gods (e. g. अग्निः सुषमित्, होता देव-<BR>वृतः); (Sāy.) speech, a short text of the Veda.<BR>—निविद्-धान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing the<BR>Nivids; (अम्), n. (according to Sāy.) inserting the<BR>Nivids.<BR>—निविद्धानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing<BR>the Nivids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदक
नि-वेदक, अस्, आ, अम्, communicating, relating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदन|निवेदनं|निवेदनः
नि-वेदन, अस्, आ, अम्, proclaiming, announcing;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; (अम्), n. making<BR>known, proclaiming, apprizing, publishing, relating,<BR>communicating, announcement, communication; in-<BR>formation; representation; delivering, giving, en-<BR>trusting; an offering, oblation; dedication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदयिषु
नि-वेदयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid. of the<BR>Caus. without reduplication), wishing to make known<BR>or report, intending to relate about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदित|निवेदितं
नि-वेदित, अस्, आ, अम्, made known, announced,<BR>reported, communicated, stated, told; represented;<BR>delivered, addressed, entrusted, presented, given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदिन्
नि-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, communicating, reporting,<BR>relating, proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेद्य|निवेद्यं
1. नि-वेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be communicated or<BR>related; fit to be reported; (अम्), n. an oblation,<BR>offering food to an idol, (probably for नैवेद्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेद्य|निवेद्यं
2. नि-वेद्य, ind. having respectfully announced<BR>or made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीस|निविरीसं
निविरीस नि-विरीस. See नि-विड, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविवृत्सत्
निविवृत्सत् नि-विवृत्सत्, नि-विवृत्सु. See<BR>p. 504, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविश्
निविश् नि-विश्, cl. 6. A. -विशते (ep. also<BR>P. -विशति), -वेष्टुम्, to enter; to alight, descend;<BR>to sit down, take a seat; to lie down; to settle<BR>down, to encamp; to settle, take a wife; to be fixed<BR>or intent on (with loc.): Caus. -वेशयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to enter, introduce, place in or on; to cause<BR>to sit down; to cause to settle or dwell, cause to lie<BR>down or encamp; to cause to marry; to put or<BR>place down; to found (a city); to enter (in writing),<BR>mark down (letters, lines, &c.), inscribe (on a tablet),<BR>depict; (with मनस्) to apply the mind to, fix the<BR>mind on (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्ट|निविष्टं|निविष्टः
नि-विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, entered, gone in or into;<BR>seated, sitting upon; situated or placed in or on,<BR>fixed on, intent upon; arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्टि|निविष्टिः
नि-विष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. entering (a female), copu-<BR>lation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेश|निवेशः
नि-वेश, अस्, m. entering, entrance; settling in a<BR>place, encamping, halting; dwelling-place, habita-<BR>tion; halting-place, place of lying, camp, palace, the<BR>residence of a king or general, (निवेशं कृ, to take<BR>up one's residence, settle, encamp); depositing, de-<BR>livering; founding (a household), settling, marrying,<BR>marriage; founding (a town); impression, mark,<BR>copy; military array; ornament, dress, decoration.<BR>—निवेश-देश, अस्, m. a dwelling-place.<BR>—निवेश-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (at the end of a comp.), lying in or<BR>on, resting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशन|निवेशनं
नि-वेशन, अस्, ई, अम्, entering; placing or laying<BR>down, lodging, providing with a resting-place; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a Vṛṣṇi; (अम्), n. entering, entrance;<BR>sitting down, encamping, settling, putting or laying<BR>down, (निवेशनं कृ, to settle, encamp); entering<BR>(in writing), inscribing; founding (a household), mar-<BR>rying, marriage; resting-place, habitation, dwelling-<BR>place, abode, dwelling, house; a nest; a camp; a<BR>town or city; [cf. अ-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशनीय|निवेशनीयः
नि-वेशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be entered; to be<BR>fixed; to be engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशयत्
नि-वेशयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to enter, intro-<BR>ducing, sending in or into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशित
नि-वेशित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to enter, introduced;<BR>placed in or upon; turned to or towards, fixed upon,<BR>directed on; sent into, entered into, engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशिन्
नि-वेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, resting in, being in, situated<BR>on, lying near; resting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेश्य|निवेश्यः
1. नि-वेश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be founded (as a town);<BR>to be married (as a man); to be returned or paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेश्य|निवेश्यः
2. नि-वेश्य, ind. having placed in or on, having<BR>made to remain or dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्टव्य
नि-वेष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be married (applied<BR>to a man); (अम्), n. to be married, (used impersonally,<BR>e. g. महाकुले निवेष्टव्यं सदृशे वा, one<BR>should marry into a high family or an equal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविशेष|निविशेषः
निविशेष नि-विशेष, अस्, आ, अम्, not differ-<BR>ent, alike; (अस्), m. want of difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीत|निवीतं|निवीतः
निवीत नि-वीत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. व्ये with<BR>नि), having the sacred Brāhmanical thread suspended<BR>round the neck; (अम्), n. wearing the Brāhmanical<BR>thread round the neck; the Brāhmanical thread so<BR>worn; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. a veil, mantle, a<BR>wrapper (= नि-वृत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतिन्
निवीतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing the sacred thread sus-<BR>pended round the neck; (ई), m. a Brāhman with<BR>the cord so suspended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीर्य
निवीर्य नि-वीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, impotent (=<BR>निर्-वीर्य, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृ
निवृ नि-वृ, cl. 5. 9. 1. P. A. -वृणोति,<BR>-णुते, -वृणाति, -णीते, -वरति, -ते, -वरितुम्, -व-<BR>रीतुम्, to surround, defend, restrain: Caus. -वार-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to surround, protect; to keep off,<BR>ward off, prohibit, hinder, prevent, hold back from,<BR>stop, withhold, forbid, interdict, exclude, obstruct,<BR>oppose: Caus. Pass. -वार्यते, to be interdicted,<BR>to be withheld.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर|निवरः
नि-वर, अस्, m., Ved. covering, protection, a<BR>protector; (Sāy.) a preventer, obstructer; (आ), f. a<BR>virgin, an unmarried girl, (in this sense probably fr.<BR>नि, ‘not,’ + वर, ‘a husband.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार|निवारः
नि-वार, अस्, m. keeping off, warding off, defend-<BR>ing, preventing, hindering, opposition, impediment;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारक|निवारकः
नि-वारक, अस्, आ, अम्, keeping off, defending,<BR>able to keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारण|निवारणं
नि-वारण, अस्, आ, अम्, keeping off, preventing,<BR>defending; (अम्), n. keeping back or off, preventing,<BR>defending, hindering, opposing; prohibition, an im-<BR>pediment; contemning (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारणीय
नि-वारणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be kept off or de-<BR>fended, to be checked or hindered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारयत्
नि-वारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, preventing, opposing,<BR>hindering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारित|निवारितः
नि-वारित, अस्, आ, अम्, hindered, forbidden, pre-<BR>vented, checked, opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार्य
1. नि-वार्य = नि-वारणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार्य
2. नि-वार्य, ind. having suppressed, having for-<BR>bidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार्यमाण|निवार्य्यमाण
नि-वार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being prevented or<BR>hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत|निवृतं|निवृतः
नि-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, surrounded, enclosed, en-<BR>compassed; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. (= नि-वीत), a<BR>veil, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृति|निवृतिः
नि-वृति, इस्, f. covering, enclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृज्
निवृज् नि-वृज्, cl. 7. 1. P. -वृणक्ति, -वर्-<BR>जति, -वर्जितुम्, Ved. to immerse, drown; to over-<BR>throw; to pour out; to extirpate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्
निवृत् 1. नि-वृत्, cl. 1. A. (also P. in Fut.<BR>Cond. and Aor.) -वर्तते, -वर्तितुम्, to turn back,<BR>return, retreat, retire, go back, turn back or away<BR>from (with abl.); to recoil; to escape from (with<BR>abl.), run away; to cease from, desist from, abstain<BR>or refrain from (with abl.); to refuse, decline; to<BR>cease; to come to an end, be accomplished; to be<BR>finished, stop, set (as the sun); not to occur; to be<BR>withheld; to be forbidden; to be reversed; to be<BR>occupied or engaged in: Caus. -वर्तयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to return; to bring back; to turn away,<BR>keep back from, restrain; to cause to desist; to drive<BR>back, repel; to accomplish, perform, bring to an<BR>end, (for निर्-वृत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त
नि-वर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing to return or<BR>turn back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तक
नि-वर्तक, अस्, इका, अम्, returning, turning or<BR>coming back, flying; desisting from, stopping, ceasing;<BR>bringing back, causing to cease, abolishing, expelling,<BR>removing.<BR>—निवर्तक-त्व, अम्, n. the state of one<BR>who turns back, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तन|निवर्त्तन
नि-वर्तन, अस्, आ, अम्, turning back, ceasing, ceas-<BR>ing to exist, disappearing; causing to return; (अम्), n.<BR>returning, turning or coming back, return; ceasing,<BR>not happening, not occurring; desisting or abstaining<BR>from (with abl.); desisting from work, inactivity,<BR>(opposed to प्र-वर्तन); repenting, reforming;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">Page0504-b+ 79</a>]<BR>causing to come back, bringing back; turning back<BR>(the hair); a means of returning (Ved.); keeping<BR>back from (with abl.); a measure of land, 20 rods<BR>or 200 cubits or 40,000 Hastas square.<BR>—निवर्तन-<BR>स्तूप, अस्, m., N. of a Stūpa erected at the spot<BR>where the charioteer of Buddha returned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तनीय
नि-वर्तनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought back;<BR>to be made to turn back, to be kept back or diverted<BR>or hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तमान
नि-वर्तमान, अस्, आ, अम्, turning back, re-<BR>turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तयितव्य|निवर्त्तयितव्य
नि-वर्तयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be kept back,<BR>to be restrained, to be diverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तित
नि-वर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned back or away,<BR>brought back, made to desist.<BR>—निवर्तित-पूर्व,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has turned away before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तितव्य
नि-वर्तितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be brought back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तिन्
नि-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, turning back, returning, flying,<BR>(सङ्ग्रामाद् अ-निवर्तिन्, not turning back from the<BR>fight, i. e. not flying); leaving off, abstaining from;<BR>allowing to return, causing to turn back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्य
नि-वर्त्य, ind. having turned or brought back,<BR>having induced to desist; having desisted or refrained<BR>from; having repented; having repaid; [cf. दुर्-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविवृत्सत्
नि-विवृत्सत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the Desid.), wishing<BR>to return or desist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविवृत्सु
नि-विवृत्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of turning back,<BR>wishing to desist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्
2. नि-वृत्, f. = नि-चृत्, q. v.; [cf. अति-न्˚, पाद-न्˚,<BR>अतिपाद-न्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्त|निवृत्तः
नि-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, returned, returning, turned<BR>back; gone, departed; vanished; ceased, refrained<BR>from, abstained, stopped, desisted, prohibited; abstain-<BR>ing from worldly acts, &c.; abstaining, abstracted or<BR>abstained from or independent of worldly acts or<BR>motives, abstracted from this world, quiet; desisting<BR>from or repenting of any improper conduct; finished,<BR>completed, whole; (अम्), n. return; [cf. दुर्-न्˚.]<BR>—निवृत्त-कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, without further<BR>cause or motive; (अस्), m. a virtuous man, one<BR>uninfluenced by worldly desires.<BR>—निवृत्त-कृषि-<BR>गोरक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, ceasing from agriculture and the<BR>tending of cattle.<BR>—निवृत्त-देव-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>ceasing from sacrificial rites or offerings to the gods.<BR>—निवृत्त-मांस, अस्, आ, अम्, one who abstains<BR>from eating meat.<BR>—निवृत्त-यज्ञ-स्वाध्याय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ceasing from sacrifices and the repetition of<BR>prayers.<BR>—निवृत्त-राग, अस्, आ, अम्, of subdued<BR>appetites or passions.<BR>—निवृत्त-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>quitting any practice or occupation.<BR>—निवृत्त-<BR>हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, with relenting heart.<BR>—निवृत्-<BR>तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. ‘one whose spirit is ab-<BR>stracted,’ a sage; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्ति|निवृत्तिः
नि-वृत्ति, इस्, f. returning, return; disappearing,<BR>disappearance, ceasing, cessation, suspension, abstain-<BR>ing from action, inactivity, (opposed to प्र-वृत्ति);<BR>ceasing to be active, ceasing to be valid or binding<BR>(as a rule); leaving off, desisting from (with abl.);<BR>resigning, discontinuance of worldly acts, cessation of<BR>emotions, separation from the world, abstinence;<BR>repose, rest; felicity, bliss, beatitude, (wrongly for<BR>निर्-वृत्ति); denial, refusal; abolition, prevention;<BR>completion; (इस्), m., N. of a son of Vṛṣṇi; of a<BR>son of Dharma, king of Magadha; [cf. निर्-वृत्ति,<BR>नि-धृति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृह्
निवृह् नि-वृह् [cf. नि-बृह्], Caus. -वर्ह-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to throw down; to annihilate; to<BR>extirpate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हण
नि-वर्हण, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying, extirpating,<BR>annihilating, removing; (अम्), n. destruction, eradi-<BR>cation, annihilation, killing, removing; [cf. नि-बर्-<BR>हण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हित
नि-वर्हित, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed, annihilated,<BR>eradicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदक
निवेदक नि-वेदक, नि-वेदन, &c. See<BR>under 1. नि-विद्, p. 503, cols. 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्ट|निवेष्टः
निवेष्ट नि-वेष्ट, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वेष्ट् with<BR>नि), a cover, envelope; वसिष्ठस्य निवेष्टस्,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्टन|निवेष्टनं
नि-वेष्टन, अम्, n. covering, enveloping, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्य|निवेष्यः
निवेष्य नि-वेष्य, अस्, m. (fr. rt. विष् with<BR>नि), Ved. a whirlpool, a water-spout; a whirlwind<BR>or any similar phenomenon [cf. स्तनयित्नु]; a part<BR>of the upper or fore-part of an animal, the vertebra?;<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara) eddy or hoar-frost; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), whirling, belonging to a whirlpool or eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्याध
निव्याध नि-व्याध, अस्, m. (fr. rt. व्यध्<BR>with नि), Ved. an opening, aperture, a window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्याधिन्
नि-व्याधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. piercing, opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्यूढ|निव्यूढं
निव्यूढ नि-व्यूढ, अम्, n. perseverance,<BR>resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् 1. निश्, euphonically substituted for<BR>निस् before च्, छ्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् 2. निश्, cl. 1. P. -नेशति, &c., to<BR>meditate upon, meditate profoundly, to<BR>be absorbed in meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् 3. निश्, f. (perhaps connected with<BR>नक् fr. rt. 2. नश्, or merely a curtailed form of निशा<BR>below, which may be connected with नि-शीथ and<BR>so derived fr. rt. शी with नि; the form निश् is<BR>defective in nom. voc. sing. du. and pl., acc. sing.<BR>du., but may be optionally substituted for निशा in<BR>acc. pl. and remaining cases, e. g. निशस् or निशास्,<BR>निशा or निशया, निड्भ्याम् [according to some also<BR>निज्भ्याम्] or निशाभ्याम्, &c.), night; निशि निशि,<BR>every night; महा-निशि, at midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश
निश, अम्, n. (at the end of a comp.) = निशा,<BR>night (e. g. अहर्-निशम्, ind. day and night; दिवा-<BR>निशम्, ind. day and night; cf. also अ-निश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशा
निशा, f. night; a vision, dream; turmeric, Cur-<BR>cuma (of two species, = हरिद्रा and दारु-हरिद्रा,<BR>probably C. Zedoaria and C. Longa; a collective N.<BR>of the asterisms Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer,<BR>Sagittarius, and Capricorn; cf. निशा-बल.)<BR>—निशा-<BR>कर, अस्, m. ‘the night-maker,’ the moon, (regarded<BR>with दिवा-कर as a son of Garuḍa); a symbolical<BR>expression for the numeral one; a cock.<BR>—निशा-<BR>कर-कला-मौलि, इस्, m. ‘bearing a crescent as<BR>diadem,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—निशा-काल, अस्, m.<BR>the time of night.<BR>—निशा-केतु, उस्, m. ‘night-sign,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—निशा-क्षय, अस्, m. the close of night.<BR>—निशा-गण, अस्, m. a number of nights.<BR>—निशा-<BR>गम (˚शा-आग्˚), अस्, m. the coming on or com-<BR>mencement of night.<BR>—निशा-गृह, अस्, m. a bed-<BR>room, sleeping-room.<BR>—निशा-चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>going or moving about by night, nocturnal, night-<BR>walking; (अस्), m. a Rākṣasa, a fiend, an imp or<BR>goblin; an epithet of Śiva [cf. निशाचर-पति]; a<BR>jackal; an owl; a snake; the ruddy goose, Cakra-<BR>vāka; a thief; a ghost, an evil spirit; (ई), f. a she-<BR>devil, a female fiend; a woman who goes to an as-<BR>signation, a harlot, whore; a sort of perfume, (see<BR>केशिनी.)<BR>—निशाचर-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of night-<BR>walkers,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—निशाचरेश (˚र-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the Rākṣasas,’ an epithet of<BR>Rāvaṇa.<BR>—निशा-चर्मन्, अ, n. ‘the skin of night,’<BR>darkness.<BR>—निशा-छद, अस्, m. a species of plant.<BR>—निशा-जल, अम्, n. ‘the water of night,’ hoar-<BR>frost, frost, dew.<BR>—निशाट (˚शा-अट), अस्, m. ‘roving<BR>by night,’ an owl; a demon, a ghost.<BR>—निशाटक,<BR>अस्, m. bdellium (= गुग्गुलु, connected with नि-<BR>शाट, an owl; cf. कौशिक, = owl and bdellium,<BR>उलूखल, उलूखलक).<BR>—निशाटन (˚शा-अट्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘night-rover,’ an owl; (ई), f. a species of moth.<BR>—निशातिक्रम (˚शा-अत्˚), अस्, m. the passing away<BR>of night.<BR>—निशात्यय (˚शा-अत्˚), अस्, m. the close of<BR>night, day-break.<BR>—निशा-दर्शिन्, ई, m. ‘seeing at<BR>night,’ an owl.<BR>—निशादि (˚शा-आदि), इस्, f. the begin-<BR>ning of night, evening, twilight.<BR>—निशाधीश (˚शा-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of night,’ the moon.<BR>—निशा-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of night,’ the moon.<BR>—निशा-<BR>नारायण, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—निशा-निशम्,<BR>ind. night by night, every night, always.<BR>—१. नि-<BR>शान्त (˚शा-अन्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. (for 2. नि-शान्त<BR>see under नि-शम्, p. 505, col. 1), the end of<BR>night, break of day.<BR>—निशान्ध (˚शा-अन्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">Page0505-a+ 75</a>]<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, blind at night; (आ), f. a species of<BR>creeper (= जतुका).<BR>—निशा-पति, इस्, m. ‘husband<BR>of the night,’ the moon; camphor.<BR>—निशा-पुत्र,<BR>आस्, m. pl. ‘the sons of night,’ N. of certain demons.<BR>—निशा-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘the flower of night,’ the<BR>white water-lily; hoar-frost, dew.<BR>—निशा-प्राणे-<BR>श्वर, अस्, m. ‘husband of night,’ the moon.<BR>—निशा-बल, अस्, m. a collective N. of the signs of<BR>the zodiac Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer, Sagit-<BR>tarius, and Capricorn.<BR>—निशा-भङ्गा, f. a species<BR>of plant (= दुग्ध-पुच्छी).<BR>—निशा-मणि, इस्, m.<BR>‘jewel of the night,’ the moon; [cf. ध्वजाग्र-<BR>निशामणि.]<BR>—निशा-मुख, अम्, n. the beginning<BR>of night.<BR>—निशा-मृग, अस्, m. ‘night-animal,’ a<BR>jackal.<BR>—१. निशा-रण, अम्, n. a nocturnal battle; (for<BR>2. see नि-शरण below.)<BR>—निशा-रत्न, अम्, n. (or,<BR>according to some, अस् m.), ‘the jewel of the night,’<BR>the moon.<BR>—निशार्धकाल (˚शा-अर्ध-क्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the first part of the night (opposed to the following).<BR>—निशावसान (˚शा-अव्˚), अम्, n. the close or end<BR>of night, the second part of the night (opposed to<BR>the preceding).<BR>—निशा-विहार, अस्, m. a night-<BR>walker, a nocturnal imp or goblin, a Rākṣasa.<BR>—निशा-वृन्द, अम्, n. a number of nights.<BR>—निशा-<BR>वेदिन्, ई, m. ‘knowing the night,’ a cock.<BR>—निशा-<BR>हस, अस्, m. ‘night-smiler,’ the white water-lily<BR>which opens its petals at night.<BR>—निशाह्वा (˚शा-<BR>आह्˚), f. turmeric.<BR>—निशि-पाल, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>metre consisting of four lines of fifteen syllables<BR>each.<BR>—निशि-पुष्पा or निशि-पुष्पी or निशिपुष्-<BR>पिका, f. the tree Nyctanthes Arbor Tristis.<BR>—निशेश<BR>(˚श-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of night,’ the moon.<BR>—नि-<BR>शैत (˚श-एत), अस्, m. ‘shining at night,’ the crane,<BR>Ardea Nivea.<BR>—निशोत्सर्ग (˚शा-उत्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>end of night, day-break.<BR>—निशोपशाय (˚शा-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. resting at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशठ|निशठः
निशठ नि-शठ, अस्, आ, अम्, not false,<BR>candid, honest; (अस्), m., N. of a Vṛṣṇi, a son of<BR>Bala-rāma by Revatī; (also written नि-षठ, नि-<BR>सठ, नि-सथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशद्
निशद् नि-शद्, Caus. -शातयति, -यितुम्, Ved.<BR>to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशब्द
निशब्द नि-शब्द, अस्, आ, अम्, speechless,<BR>silent; [cf. निः-शब्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशम्
निशम् नि-शम्, cl. 4. P. -शाम्यति, -शमितुम्,<BR>to observe, see; to hear, listen: Caus. -शामयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to observe, perceive, see; to hear, listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमन|निशमनं
नि-शमन, अम्, n. looking at; seeing, sight;<BR>hearing; becoming aware of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशम्य
नि-शम्य, ind. having perceived, having heard,<BR>hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्त|निशांत|निशान्तं|निशान्तः
2. नि-शान्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. निशान्त see under<BR>निशा, p. 504, col. 3), tranquillized, quiet, tranquil,<BR>patient; (अम्), n. a house, dwelling, habitation.<BR>—निशान्त-नारी, f. a house-wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्तीय
निशान्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>a house (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाम|निशामः
नि-शाम, अस्, m. observing, perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामन|निशामनं
नि-शामन, अम्, n. sight, seeing; looking at,<BR>beholding; looking at repeatedly; observing, hearing;<BR>a shadow, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामयत्
नि-शामयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, perceiving, hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाम्य
नि-शाम्य, ind. having seen; having heard; having<BR>tranquillized; having put out (as a light).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशरण|निशरणं
निशरण नि-शरण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. शॄ with<BR>नि), killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारण|निशारणं
2. नि-शारण, अम्, n. (fr. शॄ with नि), killing,<BR>slaughter, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारुक|निशारुकः
नि-शारुक, अस्, m. a kind of Rūpaka (see under<BR>दृढ); (अम्), n. an air, a sort of musical compo-<BR>sition played as an accompaniment to dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात|निशातः
निशात नि-शात. See under नि-शो, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाद|निशादः
निशाद नि-शाद, अस्, m. a man of low caste;<BR>(see निषाद.)<BR>—निशाद-त्व, अम्, n. the state or<BR>condition of a man of low caste.<BR>—निशादा-पुत्र,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">Page0505-b+ 69</a>]<BR>अस्, m. (?), a pestle.<BR>—निशादा-शिला, f. a mortar, a<BR>slab for grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामय
निशामय नि-शामय = शृणु, listen, (impv.<BR>of Caus. of नि-शम्, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशायिन्
निशायिन् नि-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. rt. शी with<BR>नि), lying down in, sleeping in (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावन|निशावनः
निशावन निशावन, अस्, m. hemp. See<BR>शण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशि
निशि नि-शि [cf. नि-शो], cl. 5. P. A. -शिनोति,<BR>-नुते, -शेतुम्, to sharpen; to stimulate, excite;<BR>to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशित|निशितं|निशितः
नि-शित, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened, whetted, pointed,<BR>stimulated; (अम्), n. iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिति|निशितिः
नि-शिति, इस्, f., Ved. excitement, stimulation, en-<BR>couragement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिता
निशिता नि-शिता, f., Ved. night; [cf. नि-<BR>शीथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिथ
निशिथ नि-शिथ, अस्, m. (for नि-शीथ), N. of<BR>one of the three sons of Doṣā (Night); (some read<BR>this word in Bhāgavata-Purāṇa IV. 13, 14, नि-शीथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ|निशीथः
निशीथ नि-शीथ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शी with नि),<BR>midnight, the time of sleep, night in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनी
नि-शीथिनी, f. night.<BR>—निशीथिनी-नाथ, अस्, m.<BR>‘husband of night,’ the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ्या
नि-शीथ्या, f. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भ|निशुंभ|निशुंभः|निशुम्भः
निशुम्भ नि-शुम्भ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. शुम्भ्<BR>with नि), killing, slaughter; N. of a Dānava, brother<BR>of Śumbha, slain by Durgā; (also written नि-<BR>सुम्भ.)<BR>—निशुम्भ-मथनी, f. or निशुम्भ-<BR>मर्दिनी, f. ‘destroyer of Niśumbha,’ an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भन|निशुंभन|निशुंभनं|निशुम्भनं
नि-शुम्भन, अम्, n. killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भिन्
नि-शुम्भिन्, ई, m. an epithet of Vajra-ṭīka; an<BR>inferior deity of the Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुष्म
निशुष्म नि-शुष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. not<BR>sparkling (as fire), not coruscating, (opposed to उच्-<BR>छुष्म.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशृम्भ
निशृम्भ नि-शृम्भ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्रम्भ्<BR>with नि), Ved. stepping firmly?; (Sāy.) fastened to<BR>(a car), harnessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशैत|निशैतः
निशैत निशैत. See under निशा, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशो
निशो नि-शो [cf. नि-शि], cl. 4. P. -श्यति,<BR>-शातुम्, to sharpen, whet, polish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात|निशातः
नि-शात, अस्, आ, अम्, sharpened, whetted, sharp;<BR>polished, burnished, varnished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान|निशानं
नि-शान, अम्, n. sharpening; (also read नि-शाण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चक्षुस्
निश्चक्षुस् निश्-चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, eyeless,<BR>blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चत्
निश्चत् निश्-चत् (निस्-चत्), Caus. A. -चात-<BR>यते, -यितुम्, Ved. to scare or drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चत्वारिंश|निश्चत्वारिंशः
निश्चत्वारिंश निश्-चत्वारिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, with-<BR>out forty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चप्रच
निश्चप्रच निश्च-प्रच, (perhaps) backwards<BR>and forwards; [cf. आच-पराच under 2. आच.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चर्
निश्चर् निश्-चर् (निस्-चर्), cl. 1. P. -चरति,<BR>-चरितुम्, to come forth, issue, go out, arise, pro-<BR>ceed, appear, be produced; to rise (as sounds): Caus.<BR>-चारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to issue or come forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चर
निश्-चर, अस्, m., N. of one of the Saptarṣis in<BR>the eleventh Manv-antara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चारक|निश्चारकं|निश्चारकः
निश्-चारक, अम्, n. evacuation by stool; air,<BR>wind; obstinacy, wilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चल
निश्चल निश्-चल, अस्, आ, अम्, immovable,<BR>not moving, stock-still, still, fixed, steady; not<BR>subject to motion or fluctuation, invariable, un-<BR>changeable; (आ), f. the earth; Desmodium Gange-<BR>ticum (= शाल-पर्णी).<BR>—निश्चल-मति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>steady-minded, of unshaken mind.<BR>—निश्चलाङ्ग<BR>(˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having immovable limbs,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">Page0505-c+ 73</a>]<BR>firm-bodied, firm; (अस्), m. a species of crane,<BR>Ardea Nivea; a rock, mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चि
निश्चि निश्-चि (निस्-चि, see rt. 2. चि), cl. 3. P.<BR>-चिकेति, cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति, -नुते, -चेतुम्, Ved. to<BR>ascertain, investigate, know thoroughly, arrive at a<BR>certain decision, decide, regard as decided, to fix<BR>upon, determine, resolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चय|निश्चयः
निश्-चय, अस्, m. ascertainment, investigation,<BR>inquiry, a fixed opinion, a firm conviction, accurate<BR>or certain knowledge, certainty, positiveness, positive<BR>conclusion, determination, resolution, resolve, decision;<BR>settled purpose, fixed intention, design, purpose, aim,<BR>(इति निश्चयः, this is a fixed opinion or established<BR>conclusion; निश्चयं ज्ञातुम्, to ascertain the cer-<BR>tainty; निश्चयं कृ, to decide, come to a deter-<BR>mination; cf. पाप-न्˚, मरण-न्˚, एक-न्˚); ‘re-<BR>moval of fallacy or deception,’ N. of a figure in<BR>rhetoric; (एन or आत्), ind. certainly.<BR>—निश्चय-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—निश्चय-रूप,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having (only) the appearance of cer-<BR>tainty, uncertain, wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चयिन्
निश्-चयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, decided, determined, resolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चायक|निश्चायकः
निश्-चायक, अस्, आ, अम्, who or what ascertains<BR>or determines, one who is certain about anything,<BR>determining, decisive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित
निश्-चित, अस्, आ, अम्, ascertained, determined,<BR>settled, concluded, decided, established, certain, one<BR>who has come to a conclusion or formed a fixed<BR>opinion; sentenced, pronounced; (अम्), n. certainty,<BR>decision, conclusion; (अम्), ind. decidedly, positively;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चिति|निश्चितिः
निश्-चिति, इस्, f. ascertainment, fixing, determining,<BR>settling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित्य
निश्-चित्य, ind. having ascertained, having con-<BR>cluded or decided, having made out for certain, having<BR>settled or come to a final decision, feeling assured or<BR>convinced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चीयमान|निश्चीयमानः
निश्-चीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the course of<BR>ascertainment, being under investigation, being con-<BR>cluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित्त
निश्चित्त निश्-चित्त, अस्, m., N. of a Samādhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चिन्त|निश्चिंत|निश्चिन्तः
निश्चिन्त निश्-चिन्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unthinking,<BR>thoughtless, inconsiderate, void of reflection, careless,<BR>unconcerned; [cf. नैश्चिन्त्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चुक्कण|निश्चुक्कणं
निश्चुक्कण निश्-चुक्कण, अम्, n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. चुक्क्), a sort of tooth-powder prepared from<BR>sulphate of iron &c. which destroys the tartar but<BR>blackens the teeth; (also written निश्-चुक्वण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चृत्
निश्चृत् निश्-चृत्, cl. 6. P. -चृतति, -चर्तितुम्,<BR>Ved. to loosen, untie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेतन
निश्चेतन निश्-चेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>consciousness, unconscious, unreasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेतस्
निश्चेतस् निश्-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, out of one's<BR>mind, not in one's right senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्ट|निश्चेष्टः
निश्चेष्ट निश्-चेष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, motionless,<BR>powerless, helpless; incapable of motion or effort;<BR>(अम्), ind. without motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्टा
निश्-चेष्टा, f. motionlessness.<BR>—निश्चेष्टा-क-<BR>रण, अस्, आ, अम्, causing motionlessness; epithet of<BR>one of the arrows of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चौर
निश्चौर निश्-चौर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>robbers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्च्यवन
निश्च्यवन निश्-च्यवन, अस्, m. ‘unperish-<BR>ing,’ a form of fire; N. of one of the Saptarṣis in<BR>the second Manv-antara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छन्दस्|निश्छंदस्
निश्छन्दस् निश्-छन्दस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, not<BR>studying holy writ; निश्छन्दः कुलम्, a family in<BR>which the Vedas are not studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छिद्र
निश्छिद्र निश्-छिद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>rent or openings, without holes, having no holes,<BR>without weak points or defects, having no weak side;<BR>unhurt, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्छेद
निश्-छेद, अस्, आ, अम्, indivisible, without division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रथ्य
निश्रथ्य नि-श्रथ्य, ind. having fastened<BR>or harnessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रम|निश्रमः
निश्रम नि-श्रम, अस्, m. (fr. rt. श्रम् with<BR>नि), labour bestowed upon anything, continued<BR>practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रयणी
निश्रयणी नि-श्रयणी, f. (fr. rt. श्रि with नि),<BR>a ladder, staircase; (also written निः-श्रयणी, निः-<BR>श्रयिणी, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रेणी
नि-श्रेणी, f. a ladder, staircase; (other forms of the<BR>word are नि-श्रेणि, f., निः-श्रेणी, and निः-श्रेणि, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रीक
निश्रीक नि-श्रीक for निः-श्रीक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वस्
निश्वस् नि-श्वस्, cl. 2. P. -श्वसिति, -श्वसितुम्,<BR>to draw in the breath, inspire; to sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वस्य
नि-श्वस्य, ind. having drawn in the breath,<BR>having sighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वास|निश्वासः
नि-श्वास, अस्, m. inspiration, inhaling, sighing.<BR>—निश्वास-प्रश्वास, औ, m. du. inspiration and<BR>expiration, respiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्
निष् 1. निष्, euphonically substituted for<BR>निस् before क्, ख्, ट्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्
निष् 2. निष् [cf. rt. निक्ष्], cl. 1. P.<BR>नेषति, &c., to moisten, sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्ग|निषंग|निषंगः|निषङ्गः
निषङ्ग नि-षङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सञ्ज् with<BR>नि), clinging to, attachment; union, meeting, associ-<BR>ation; a quiver; a sword (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गथि|निषंगथि|निषंगथिः|निषङ्गथिः
नि-षङ्गथि, इस्, इस्, इ, embracing; (इस्), m.<BR>embracing, an embrace [cf. स्वञ्ज्]; a bowman; a<BR>charioteer; a car; grass; the shoulder.<BR>—निषङ्ग-<BR>धि, इस्, m., Ved. (according to commentators) the<BR>sheath of a sword, a scabbard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गिन्|निषंगिन्
निषङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a quiver; (ई), m. an<BR>archer, bowman; N. of one of the hundred sons of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषञ्ज
निषञ्ज नि-षञ्ज in कु-न्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषठ
निषठ नि-षठ. See नि-शठ, p. 505.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्
निषद् 1. नि-षद् (नि-सद्), cl. 1. 6. P. -षी-^1<BR>दति, -षत्तुम्, to sit down, lie down, recline; to<BR>settle down, sink down; to dwell; to be afflicted,<BR>suffer pain: Caus. -षादयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>sit down.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161213. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 316-318.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्ण|निषण्णः
नि-षण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, seated, sitting, perched,<BR>placed in or on, rested, reclined, resting or leaning<BR>on, reclining; supported; sunk down, afflicted, dis-<BR>tressed; gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्णक|निषण्णकं
नि-षण्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, sitting, seated; (अम्),<BR>n. a seat; a species of pot-herb, Marsilea Dentata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषत्ति|निषत्तिः
नि-षत्ति, इस्, f., Ved. sitting down idly, remaining<BR>inactive or indifferent, indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषत्स्नु
नि-षत्स्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. sitting fast, firmly<BR>settled or fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्
2. नि-षद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sitting inactive; (त्), f.<BR>sitting, especially near the altar at a sacrificial rite;<BR>N. of a kind of composition mentioned with Upa-<BR>niṣad in Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 1613.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद|निषदः
नि-षद, अस्, m., N. of an ancient king, (probably<BR>a wrong reading for निषध); = नि-षाद, a musical<BR>note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषदन|निषदनं|निषदनः
नि-षदन, अम्, n., Ved. sitting down, reclining;<BR>dwelling, residing; a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्या
नि-षद्या, f. a small bed or couch; the hall of<BR>a merchant; a market-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वर|निषद्वरः
नि-षद्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. seated (near the<BR>altar), sitting lazily; (अस्), m. mud, mire (in which<BR>one sinks); the god of love; (ई), f. ‘the time of<BR>rest,’ night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषाद|निषादः
नि-षाद, अस्, m., N. of certain wild aboriginal<BR>tribes in India not belonging to the Āryan race, and<BR>described as hunters, fishermen, robbers, &c.; (ac-<BR>cording to Mahī-dhara) a N. of the Bhillas (a wild<BR>mountain tribe whose progenitor is said by a legend<BR>to have sprung from the thigh of Vena); a man of<BR>a degraded tribe in general, an outcast (especially<BR>the son of a Brāhman by a Śūdra woman); the first<BR>of the seven musical notes or more properly the last<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">Page0506-b+ 76</a>]<BR>or highest of the scale, corresponding to B of our<BR>scale; N. of a Kalpa; [cf. नैषाद, नैषादक,<BR>नैषादिका, नैषादि.]<BR>—निषाद-कर्षु, उस्,<BR>m., N. of a district; [cf. नैषाद-कर्षुक.]<BR>—निषाद-वत्, n., N. of a musical note, = B of<BR>our scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादित
नि-षादित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made to<BR>sit down; afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादिन्
नि-षादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sitting down, lying down, re-<BR>clining, resting; (ई), m. an elephant-keeper or driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषीदत्
नि-षीदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sitting down, sitting<BR>on; settling or sinking down; resting in or on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेदिवस्
नि-षेदिवस्, वान्, दुषी, वत्, seated in or upon,<BR>reclined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषध|निषधः
निषध निषध, अस्, m., N. of a mountain<BR>or chain of mountains forming one of the principal<BR>ranges of the earth, and described as lying immedi-<BR>ately south of Ilāvṛta and north of the Himālaya;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people and their country<BR>governed by Nala; the sovereign of the Niṣadhas;<BR>N. of a son of Janam-ejaya; of Kuśa the father of<BR>Nala; a peculiar position of the closed hand; a<BR>musical note [cf. नि-षाद]; (अस्, आ, अम्), hard,<BR>solid; (आ), f., N. of Nala's capital, the city of the<BR>Niṣadhas; N. of a river rising in the Vindhya<BR>mountains.<BR>—निषध-वंश, अस्, m. the race of<BR>Niṣadha.<BR>—निषधाधिप (˚ध-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>or निषधाधिपति (˚ध-अध्˚), इस्, m. or निष-<BR>धेश्वर (˚ध-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of Niṣadha,’<BR>epithet of Nala; [cf. नैषध, नैषध्य.]<BR>—निषधाश्व (˚ध-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Kuru.<BR>—निषधेन्द्र-काव्य, अम्, n. ‘the poem<BR>of the prince of the Niṣadhas,’ N. of a poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषमम्
निषमम् नि-षमम्, ind. (fr. नि + सम),<BR>see Pāṇ. VI. 2, 121, Schol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषर्ग
निषर्ग नि-षर्ग, अस्, m. a various reading<BR>for नि-षङ्ग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषाद|निषादः
निषाद नि-षाद. See 1. नि-षद्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिच्
निषिच् नि-षिच् (नि-सिच्), cl. 6. P. A. -षिञ्चति,<BR>-ते, -षेक्तुम्, to sprinkle, pour upon or into, infuse,<BR>instil, irrigate: Caus. -षेचयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to sprinkle or irrigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिक्त
नि-षिक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled upon, poured<BR>into, infused, instilled, irrigated.<BR>—निषिक्त-पा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. protecting the infused (semen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेक|निषेकः
नि-षेक, अस्, m. sprinkling, infusion, aspersion;<BR>distilling; effusion; seminal infusion, impregnation;<BR>the ceremony performed upon impregnation; irriga-<BR>tion; water for washing, (but according to others)<BR>seminal impurity; what is poured upon the ground,<BR>dirty water, swill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेक्तव्य
नि-षेक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled or<BR>poured into, to be watered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेचन|निषेचनं
नि-षेचन, अम्, n., Ved. pouring out, sprinkling,<BR>watering, irrigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेचितृ
नि-षेचितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who sprinkles or<BR>pours into, an instiller, infuser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिध्
निषिध् नि-षिध् (नि-सिध्), cl. 1. P. -षे-<BR>धति, -षेद्धुम्, -षेधितुम्, to prohibit, forbid,<BR>restrain, keep off, ward off, keep back, prevent,<BR>remove: Caus. -षेधयति, -यितुम्, to prohibit,<BR>keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्ध|निषिद्धं
नि-षिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, prohibited, forbidden,<BR>kept back, restrained, warded off, prevented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्धि|निषिद्धिः
नि-षिद्धि, इस्, f. prohibition, warding off, keep-<BR>ing off, defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेद्धव्य
नि-षेद्धव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be kept back or<BR>obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेद्धृ
नि-षेद्धृ, धा, ध्री, धृ, keeping back,<BR>obstructing, who or what restrains or prevents or<BR>prohibits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेद्ध्र
नि-षेद्ध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, in अ-निषेद्ध्र, having<BR>no impeder or subduer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेध|निषेधः
नि-षेध, अस्, m. warding off, keeping off, hin-<BR>dering, stopping, obstructing, prevention, prohibition;<BR>negation, denial; discontinuance, contrariety to or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">Page0506-c+ 74</a>]<BR>deviation from rule, exception; N. of several<BR>Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेधक
नि-षेधक, अस्, आ, अम्, keeping back, obstruct-<BR>ing, preventing, prohibiting, forbidding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेधन
नि-षेधन, अम्, n. the act of warding off or<BR>defending, prevention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेधिन्
नि-षेधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, defending, keeping back;<BR>excelling, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेध्य
नि-षेध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be kept back or pro-<BR>hibited or hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिध
निषिध नि-षिध, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (various reading for निषध; cf. नै-<BR>षिध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूद्
निषूद् नि-षूद् (नि-सूद्), Caus. -षूदयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to kill, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूदन|निषूदनं|निषूदनः
नि-षूदन, अम्, n. killing, slaughter; [cf. नि-<BR>सूदन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेव्
निषेव् नि-षेव् (नि-सेव्), cl. 1. A. -षेवते,<BR>-षेवितुम्, to wait upon, serve, attend, follow;<BR>attach or devote one's self to; to honour, worship,<BR>adore; to pursue, practise, perform, observe, cultivate;<BR>to frequent, inhabit, visit; to enjoy; to employ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेव
नि-षेव, अस्, आ, अम्, practising, exercising, fol-<BR>lowing, devoted to [cf. ह्री-न्˚]; (आ), f. exercising,<BR>practice, service; worship, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवक
नि-षेवक, अस्, आ, अम्, practising, following,<BR>devoted to; frequenting, inhabiting; enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवण|निषेवणं
नि-षेवण, अम्, n. waiting on, serving, service,<BR>attaching one's self to, worshipping, worship, adora-<BR>tion; practice, performance, adherence to; living in,<BR>inhabiting, enjoying, using, use, familiarity with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवणीय
नि-षेवणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be served or attended<BR>to, to be followed or observed; to be obeyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवित
नि-षेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, visited, frequented; ob-<BR>served, practised; served, honoured, obeyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवितव्य
नि-षेवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be practised or<BR>observed; to be used or enjoyed; (also read नि-<BR>सेवितव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवितृ
नि-षेवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who attaches or<BR>devotes himself to anything, an observer, practiser,<BR>cultivator, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेविन्
नि-षेविन्, ई, इणी, इ, practising, observing, enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेव्य|निषेव्यः
नि-षेव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be observed, to be<BR>honoured, to be visited or frequented; to be enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्
निष्क् निष्क् (probably a Nominal verb<BR>artificially formed fr. निष्क below),<BR>cl. 10. A. निष्कयते, &c., to measure, weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क|निष्कं|निष्कः
निष्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt. सद् with<BR>preposition नि and affix क), a golden ornament for<BR>the neck or breast; a golden ornament of a certain<BR>weight, used as money; a weight of gold varying in<BR>value at different times, = 1 Dīnāra of 32 small or<BR>16 large Rettis, = 1 Karṣa or Su-varṇa of 16<BR>Māṣas, = 1 Pāla of 4 or 5 Su-varṇas, = 1 larger<BR>Pāla or Dīnāra variously reckoned at 108 or 150<BR>Su-varṇas, = 4 Māṣas, = 16 Drammas; a weight of<BR>silver of 4 Su-varṇas; gold in general, a golden<BR>vessel; (अस्), m. a Cāṇḍāla; (आ), f. a measure of<BR>length; [cf. नैष्किक, नैष्कशतिक, नैष्क-<BR>सहस्रिक.]<BR>—निष्क-कण्ठ, अस्, ई, अम्, wearing<BR>a golden ornament round the neck; (अम्), n. a<BR>golden ornament of the neck.<BR>—निष्क-ग्रीव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. wearing a gold ornament round the<BR>neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्किन्
निष्किन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. having an ornament<BR>round the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्टक|निष्कंटक|निष्कण्टकः
निष्कण्टक निष्-कण्टक, अस्, आ, अम्, =<BR>अ-कण्टक, thornless, free from thorns or enemies;<BR>free from danger or trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्ठ|निष्कण्ठः
निष्कण्ठ निष्-कण्ठ, अस्, m. a species of<BR>tree, Capparis Trifoliata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कनिष्ठ
निष्कनिष्ठ निष्-कनिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>निष्कनिष्ठक, अस्, आ, अम्, having the little finger<BR>stretched out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0506-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कन्द|निष्कंद
निष्कन्द निष्-कन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>edible or esculent roots, having no bulbous roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कपट
निष्कपट निष्-कपट, अस्, आ, अम्, guileless,<BR>free from deceit or fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कम्प|निष्कंप
निष्कम्प निष्-कम्प, अस्, आ, अम्, not shaking,<BR>not tremulous, motionless, immovable.<BR>—निष्कम्-<BR>प-ता, f. motionlessness, immovableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कम्भ
निष्कम्भ नि-ष्कम्भ in वज्र-निष्कम्भ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the sons of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कम्भु
नि-ष्कम्भु, उस्, m., N. of a particular divine<BR>being (= Viśva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्करुण
निष्करुण निष्-करुण, अस्, आ, अम्, pitiless,<BR>unmerciful, merciless, cruel.<BR>—निष्करुणी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, rendered pitiless, made or become heart-<BR>less or cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्करूष
निष्करूष निष्-करूष, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>dirty, free from dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्तृ
निष्कर्तृ निष्-कर्तृ, ता, m., Ved. = इष्-<BR>कर्तृ, p. 143, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्मन्|निष्कर्म्मन्
निष्कर्मन् निष्-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, inactive;<BR>exempt from or neglecting religious or worldly<BR>acts, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्ष|निष्कर्षः
निष्कर्ष निष्-कर्ष, &c. See under निष्-<BR>कृष्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल|निष्कलं|निष्कलः
निष्कल निष्-कल, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>parts, undivided, indivisible; waned, diminished,<BR>decayed; impotent, seedless, barren; maimed, in-<BR>firm; (अस्), m. a receptacle; pudendum muliebre; N.<BR>of Brahmā; a fancied personification of Brahmā for<BR>religious ceremonies; (आ or ई), f. an elderly woman<BR>past childbearing or in whom menstruation has<BR>ceased.<BR>—निष्कल-त्व, अम्, n. undividedness, indi-<BR>visibility, the state of the absolute Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कलङ्क|निष्कलंक
निष्कलङ्क निष्-कलङ्क, अस्, आ, अम्, stainless,<BR>spotless, sinless, immaculate, unblemished.<BR>—निष्क-<BR>लङ्क-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल्मष
निष्कल्मष निष्-कल्मष, अस्, आ, अम्, spot-<BR>less, sinless.<BR>—निष्कल्मषी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>become spotless or sinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कषाय
निष्कषाय निष्-कषाय, अस्, आ, अम्, free<BR>from dirt or impure passions; (अस्), m., N. of the<BR>thirteenth Arhat of the future Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कस्
निष्कस् निष्-कस् (निस्-कस्; sometimes in-<BR>correctly spelt निष्-कश्), Caus. -कासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to drive out, expel, turn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कास|निष्कासः
निष्-कास, अस्, m. exit, egress; a portico, veranda,<BR>(wrongly spelt निष्-काश); the day-break; waning,<BR>disappearance; (also a wrong reading for निष्-<BR>काष, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासित|निष्कासितः
निष्-कासित, अस्, आ, अम्, expelled, dismissed,<BR>turned out; gone forth or out, issued; placed, de-<BR>posited; placed over, appointed, stationed; reviled,<BR>reproached; opened out, blown, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासिन्
निष्-कासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who or what expels; (इनी),<BR>f. a female slave not restrained by her master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काम
निष्काम निष्-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desireless,<BR>free from wish or desire, disinterested, unselfish;<BR>(अम्), ind. without wish or desire; unwillingly.<BR>—निष्काम-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting disinterestedly<BR>or without desire, unselfish in one's conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारण|निष्कारणं
निष्कारण निष्-कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, cause-<BR>less, needless, unnecessary; free from motive, disinter-<BR>ested, groundless, without a reason, not proceeding<BR>from any cause; (अम्), ind. without any special<BR>motive, without a reason, causelessly, without any<BR>secondary view; [cf. नि-कारण.]<BR>—निष्कारण-<BR>वैरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, groundlessly hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारुष
निष्कारुष निष्-कारुष, अस्, आ, अम्, of a<BR>noble race, not degraded (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालक|निष्कालकः
निष्कालक निष्-कालक, अस्, m. a penitent<BR>shaven and smeared with ghee or clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालन|निष्कालनं
निष्कालन निष्-कालन, अस्, m. (fr. कल्<BR>with निस्), driving away (cattle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालिक
निष्कालिक निष्-कालिक, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has no more time (to live), one whose time is<BR>over or whose term of life is elapsed; (अम्), ind.<BR>without delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काश|निष्काशः
निष्काश निष्-काश, अस्, m. issue, egress;<BR>a portico, veranda; [cf. निष्-कास.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काशित|निष्काशितः
निष्-काशित, अस्, आ, अम्. See निष्-कासित, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काष
निष्काष निष्-काष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. कष्<BR>with निस्), Ved. the scrapings from a caldron or<BR>pan; (also written निष्-कास.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्किञ्चन|निष्किंचन
निष्किञ्चन निष्-किञ्चन, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>nothing, very poor.<BR>—निष्किञ्चन-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>poverty, indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्किरीय
निष्किरीय निष्-किरीय, आस्, m. pl. (fr. निष्-<BR>किर, which is fr. rt. 1. कॄ with निस्), N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्किल्विष
निष्किल्विष निष्-किल्विष, अस्, आ, अम्, sin-<BR>less, faultless; [cf. नि-किल्बिष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुट|निष्कुटः
निष्कुट निष्-कुट, अस्, m. a pleasure-grove<BR>near a house, (in this sense also अम्, n.); a field;<BR>the hollow of a tree [cf. निष्-कुह]; a door; the<BR>female apartments, Zenana; N. of a country (?);<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a hole of a peculiar form in the<BR>frame of a bedstead; (also read निः-कुह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटि|निष्कुटिः
निष्-कुटि, इस्, ई, f. large cardamoms; [cf. निस्-<BR>त्रुटी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटिका
निष्कुटिका, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>on Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुतूहल
निष्कुतूहल निष्-कुतूहल, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing no curiosity, incurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुम्भ|निष्कुम्भः
निष्कुम्भ निष्-कुम्भ, अस्, m. = नि-कुम्भ,<BR>Croton Polyandrum; (आ), f., N. of the mother of<BR>the Magas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुल
निष्कुल निष्-कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, having no<BR>family or kindred, left alone in the world; निष्-<BR>कुलं कृ, to make (any one) without family, cut<BR>off entirely, exterminate.<BR>—निष्कुल-ता, f. loss of<BR>family, dying out, perishing.<BR>—निष्कुला-कृ or<BR>निष्कुली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to extir-<BR>minate one's family; to strip off the husk, to husk,<BR>shell.<BR>—निष्कुला-कृत्य, ind. having stripped off<BR>the husk; (also read निःकुला-कृत्य.)<BR>—निष्कुली-<BR>कृत्य, ind. having husked or shelled; (also read<BR>निःकुली-कृत्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुलीन
निष्-कुलीन, अस्, आ, अम्, of low family, plebeian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुष्
निष्कुष् निष्-कुष् (निस्-कुष्), cl. 9. P.<BR>-कुष्णाति, -कोषितुम् and -कोष्टुम्, to pull off or<BR>out, strip off, tear off or out, extract; to injure or<BR>hurt by tearing; to husk, shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुषित
निष्-कुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn off, stripped off,<BR>extracted, forced or drawn out, torn, lacerated; ex-<BR>pelled; (अस्), m., N. of a Marut; (also read निष्-<BR>कर्षिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोष|निष्कोषः
निष्-कोष, अस्, m. tearing out, stripping off the<BR>husk, shelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषण|निष्कोषणं
निष्-कोषण, अम्, n. tearing off or out, strip-<BR>ping off, drawing out, extracting, extirpating; taking<BR>away, husking, shelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषणक|निष्कोषणकं
निष्-कोषणक, अस्, आ, अम्, fit for picking, used<BR>as a picker, serving for a tooth-pick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषितव्य
निष्-कोषितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be stripped off or<BR>extracted, to be forced or drawn out; to be taken<BR>away; to be expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुह|निष्कुहः
निष्कुह निष्-कुह, अस्, m. = निष्-कुट, the<BR>hollow of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कूज
निष्कूज निष्-कूज, अस्, आ, अम्, noiseless,<BR>soundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कूट
निष्कूट निष्-कूट, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>deceit or fraud, guileless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृ
निष्कृ निष्-कृ (निस्-कृ), cl. 8. P. A. -क-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">Page0507-c+ 75</a>]<BR>रोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to bring out, extract (Ved.);<BR>to take away, do away, remove, expel, exclude, drive<BR>away; to break in pieces, destroy; to prepare,<BR>equip, arrange, accomplish, finish; to absolve, acquit;<BR>to restore, cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारण|निष्कारणं
निष्-कारण, अम्, n. removing, taking away,<BR>doing away; killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत
निष्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done away, taken away,<BR>removed, expelled; absolved, pardoned, acquitted;<BR>disregarded; (अम्), n. expiation, atonement; a fixed<BR>place, place of rendezvous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृति|निष्कृतिः
निष्-कृति, इस्, f. expiation, atonement; absolution,<BR>pardon; acquittance, compensation, discharge of a<BR>debt or obligation; removal, doing away; restoration,<BR>cure; escaping from, avoiding; disregarding, neglect-<BR>ing; (Niṣkṛti personified is a sister of Lobha and<BR>daughter of Dambha by Māyā); bad conduct, roguery,<BR>(various reading for नि-कृति); (इस्), m. a form of<BR>Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत्
निष्कृत् निष्-कृत् (निस्-कृत्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-कृन्तति, -कर्तितुम्, to cut off, to cut out; to<BR>divide, separate; to cut through, hew asunder,<BR>massacre; to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृप
निष्कृप निष्-कृप, अस्, आ, अम्, pitiless, mer-<BR>ciless, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृष्
निष्कृष् निष्-कृष् (निस्-कृष्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-कर्षति, -कर्ष्टुम् and -क्रष्टुम्, to draw out,<BR>extract; to tear out, tear in pieces, rend asunder;<BR>Caus. -कर्षयति, -यितुम्, to tear in pieces, destroy,<BR>annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्ष|निष्कर्षः
निष्-कर्ष, अस्, m. drawing out, extracting; the<BR>essence of anything, chief point, main point; measur-<BR>ing; certainty, ascertainment; (आत्), ind. succinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षण|निष्कर्षणं
निष्-कर्षण, अम्, n. drawing out, extracting;<BR>pulling off, drawing off, taking off; deducting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षिन्
निष्-कर्षिन्, ई, m., N. of one of the Maruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृष्ट
निष्-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn forth, pulled<BR>out, extracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्केवल
निष्केवल निष्-केवल, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging<BR>exclusively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्केवल्य
निष्-केवल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging exclusively;<BR>N. of a particular Uktha (q. v.) connected with the<BR>midday oblation and belonging to Indra exclusively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कैवल्य
निष्कैवल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, mere, pure, absolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0507-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कौरव
