निष्पुत्र
निष्पुत्र निष्-पुत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, sonless,<BR>childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुराण
निष्पुराण निष्-पुराण, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>existing before, new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुरुष|निष्पुरुषः
निष्पुरुष निष्-पुरुष, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived<BR>of men, without males, unpeopled, desolate; not<BR>having produced male children; not male, feminine,<BR>neuter; (अस्), m. a eunuch or impotent man; a<BR>coward; [cf. नैष्पुरुष्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुलाक
निष्पुलाक निष्-पुलाक, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>chaff or rather from bad or useless grain; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of the fourteenth Arhat of the future Ut-<BR>sarpiṇī.<BR>—निष्पुलाकी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पू
निष्पू निष्-पू (निस्-पू), cl. 9. P. A. -पुनाति,<BR>-पुनीते, -पवितुम्, to cleanse, purify; to winnow, fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पवण
निष्-पवण, अम्, n. winnowing, fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाव|निष्पावः
निष्-पाव, अस्, m. fanning, winnowing, cleaning<BR>corn, &c.; the wind caused by the winnowing sieve<BR>or basket; wind, air; straw, chaff (?) = कडङ्गक<BR>or कडङ्ग; a legume, a pod; a species of pulse,<BR>Phaseolus Radiatus; Dolichos Sinensis or a similar<BR>kind, = राज-माष, = वल्ल, = सितशिम्बिक, = शिम्-<BR>बिका, = श्वेत-शिम्बी, = बोल, = शिमी, i. e. शिम्बी; (ई<BR>or इस्), f. a species of pulse, commonly वाडा, of which<BR>there are two kinds, a green and a white one; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), indubitable, certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पावक|निष्पावकः
निष्-पावक, अस्, m. a species of pulse, = वल्ल or<BR>श्वेत-शिम्बी; (इका), f., cf. नख-न्˚, वृत्त-न्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पावल
निष्-पावल, an adj. formed fr. निष्-पाव, Pāṇini<BR>V. 2, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पॄ
निष्पॄ निष्-पॄ or निष्-पृ (निस्-पॄ), cl. 3. 9.<BR>P. -पिपर्ति, -पृणाति, -परितुम् or -परीतुम्, to<BR>bring out, help out, extricate; to fill: Caus. -पार-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to lead or bring out, help out, extricate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पूर्त
निष्-पूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, poured out; filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पौरुष
निष्पौरुष निष्-पौरुष, अस्, आ, अम्, devoid<BR>of manhood, unmanly; (also written निः-पौरुष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रकम्प|निष्प्रकंप
निष्प्रकम्प निष्-प्रकम्प, अस्, आ, अम्, im-<BR>movable, motionless; (अस्), m., N. of one of the<BR>Saptarṣis in the thirteenth Manv-antara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रकारक
निष्प्रकारक निष्-प्रकारक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>without distinction of species or kind, without speci-<BR>fication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रकाश
निष्प्रकाश निष्-प्रकाश, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>transparent, not clear, lightless, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रचार
निष्प्रचार निष्-प्रचार, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>going or moving away, remaining in one's place;<BR>concentrated or fixed upon one point (as mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रणय
निष्प्रणय निष्-प्रणय, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>affection, cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रताप
निष्प्रताप निष्-प्रताप, अस्, आ, अम्, void of<BR>dignity, mean, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिकार
निष्प्रतिकार निष्-प्रतिकार. See निष्-प्र-<BR>तीकार below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिक्रिय
निष्प्रतिक्रिय निष्-प्रतिक्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>curable, irremediable, what cannot be remedied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिग्रह
निष्प्रतिग्रह निष्-प्रतिग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>accepting gifts.<BR>—निष्प्रतिग्रह-ता, f. the state of<BR>not accepting gifts, not taking presents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिघ
निष्प्रतिघ निष्-प्रतिघ, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>impeded by obstacles, unhindered, unimpeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिद्वन्द्व|निष्प्रतिद्वंद्व
निष्प्रतिद्वन्द्व निष्-प्रतिद्वन्द्व, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>without adversaries or enemies, unopposed; having<BR>no match, matchless, unequalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिपक्ष
निष्प्रतिपक्ष निष्-प्रतिपक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having no adversary, without an opponent.<BR>—निष्-<BR>प्रतिपक्ष-ता, f. the state of having no adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभ|निष्प्रतिभः
निष्प्रतिभ निष्-प्रतिभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>no splendor, deprived of splendor; stupid, frigid,<BR>dull, apathetic, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभान
निष्प्रतिभान निष्-प्रतिभान, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>bold, cowardly, pusillanimous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतीकार
निष्प्रतीकार निष्-प्रतीकार, अस्, आ, अम्, with-<BR>out obstacles, unobstructed, uninterrupted; (अम्), ind.<BR>unobstructedly, uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतीप
निष्प्रतीप निष्-प्रतीप, अस्, आ, अम्, not<BR>turned backwards, directed forwards, looking straight-<BR>forwards; निष्प्रतीपं दर्शनम्, an untroubled<BR>or unconcerned look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रत्यूह|निष्प्रत्यूहः
निष्प्रत्यूह निष्-प्रत्यूह, अस्, आ, अम्, unob-<BR>structed, unimpeded, irremediable; (अम्), ind. with-<BR>out hindrance or obstacle, freely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रधान
निष्प्रधान निष्-प्रधान, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived<BR>of a chief, destitute of leaders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रपञ्च|निष्प्रपंच
निष्प्रपञ्च निष्-प्रपञ्च, अस्, आ, अम्, without<BR>extension or diffusion; without deceit, pure, honest.<BR>—निष्प्रपञ्चात्मन् (˚च-आत्˚), आ, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रपतन
निष्प्रपतन निष्-प्रपतन in दुर्-न्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रभ|निष्प्रभः
निष्प्रभ निष्-प्रभ, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived of<BR>light or radiance, lustreless; gloomy, dark, obscure;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—निष्प्रभ-ता, f.<BR>or निष्प्रभ-त्व, अम्, n. obscurity, gloominess,<BR>darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रभाव
निष्प्रभाव निष्-प्रभाव, अस्, आ, अम्, power-<BR>less.<BR>—निष्प्रभाव-ता, f. or निष्प्रभाव-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. powerlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रमाणक
निष्प्रमाणक निष्-प्रमाणक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>wanting authority, without authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयत्न
निष्प्रयत्न निष्-प्रयत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, abstain-<BR>ing from exertion or effort, inactive, inert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयोजन|निष्प्रयोजनं
निष्प्रयोजन निष्-प्रयोजन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>without motives, not influenced by any motive;<BR>causeless, groundless, reasonless; useless, without an<BR>object; needless, unnecessary, uncalled for; (अम्),<BR>ind. causelessly, unnecessarily, without reason; (also<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">Page0509-c+ 68</a>]<BR>written निः-प्रयोजन.)<BR>—निष्प्रयोजन-ता, f. or<BR>निष्प्रयोजन-त्व, अम्, n. uselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवणि
निष्प्रवणि निष्-प्रवणि, इस्, इस्, इ, or निष्-<BR>प्रवाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, or निष्-प्रवाण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>fresh from the loom, quite new and unbleached (as<BR>cloth or linen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्राण
निष्प्राण निष्-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose<BR>breath has departed, breathless, lifeless, dead, quite<BR>exhausted.<BR>—निष्प्राण-ता, f. lifelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रीति
निष्प्रीति निष्-प्रीति, इस्, इस्, इ, joyless, feeling<BR>no pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्लाव
निष्प्लाव निष्-प्लाव in कटु-न्˚, incorrectly<BR>for निष्-पाव under निष्-पू, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फल|निष्फलः
निष्फल निष्-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing no<BR>fruit, fruitless, unfruitful, barren, useless, unprofitable,<BR>vain; meaningless; unproductive, seedless, impotent;<BR>(आ or ई), f. a woman past childbearing or in whom<BR>menstruation has ceased, (also read निष्कला); (आ),<BR>f. a species of Momordica.<BR>—निष्फल-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. unfruitfulness, unproductiveness.<BR>—निष्फली-<BR>कृत्य, ind. having made unfruitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फलय
निष्-फलय, Nom. P. निष्फलयति, &c., to<BR>make unfruitful, to render fruitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फेन
निष्फेन निष्-फेन, अस्, आ, अम्, foamless,<BR>without foam; (also written निः-फेन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्यन्द|निष्यंद|निष्यंदः|निष्यन्दः
निष्यन्द नि-ष्यन्द, नि-ष्यन्दिन्. See नि-<BR>स्यन्द, नि-स्यन्दिन्, p. 510, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्यूत
निष्यूत नि-ष्यूत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. सिव् with<BR>नि), sewn on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्षपिन्
निष्षपिन् निष्षपिन्, ई, इणी, इ (according to<BR>the Nirukta fr. निस् + सप = पस), Ved. libidinous,<BR>lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्षह्
निष्षह् निष्-षह् or निष्-षाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved.<BR>overpowering, expelling; (Sāy. = निःसारयितृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्
निस् निस्, ind. (as a preposition or prefix<BR>to verbs and their derivative nouns, expressing) out,<BR>forth, outward, out of, out from, away, away from;<BR>(निस् is used as an independent and separable adverb in<BR>Atharva-veda VI. 18, 3; VII. 115, 3; XVI. 2, 1.)<BR>निस् is also prefixed to nouns, not immediately con-<BR>nected with verbs, in the sense ‘out of,’ ‘away<BR>from’ [cf. निर्-वन], but more commonly in the<BR>sense of a privative or negative adverb = 3. अ, ‘no,’<BR>‘not,’ ‘without.’ In this latter signification it may<BR>form either negative substantives (e. g. fr. अर्थ, ad-<BR>vantage, निर्-अर्थ, disadvantage) or more frequently<BR>adjectives (e. g. fr. मल, a stain, निर्-मल, stain-<BR>less). निस् is liable to be euphonically changed to<BR>निर्, निः, निश्, निष् or नी [cf. नी-रस, &c.] accord-<BR>ing to the letter which follows it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसङ्कक्ष|निसंकक्ष
निसङ्कक्ष नि-सङ्कक्ष. See निः-सङ्कक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसञ्ज्ञ|निसंज्ञ
निसञ्ज्ञ नि-सञ्ज्ञ for निः-सञ्ज्ञ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसम्पात|निसंपात|निसम्पातः
निसम्पात नि-सम्पात, अस्, m. midnight;<BR>(also निः-सम्पात.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर
निसर नि-सर, अस्, m., Ved. (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara) a noun of agency fr. rt. सृ with नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्ग|निसर्गः
निसर्ग नि-सर्ग. See under नि-सृज्, p. 510.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्प
निसर्प नि-सर्प, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सृप् with<BR>नि). See नैसर्प, p. 518, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसिन्धु|निसिन्धुः
निसिन्धु नि-सिन्धु, उस्, or निसिन्धुक, अस्,<BR>m. a species of shrub, Vitex Negundo (= निर्गुण्डी);<BR>[cf. सिन्धु, सिन्धुक, सिन्धु-वार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसुन्द
निसुन्द नि-सुन्द, अस्, m., N. of an Asura<BR>slain by Kṛṣṇa; [cf. सुन्द, उप-सुन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसुम्भ
निसुम्भ नि-सुम्भ. See नि-शुम्भ, p. 505.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसुसूष्
निसुसूष् नि-सुसूष्, ऊस्, ऊस्, ऊस् (fr. the Desid.<BR>of rt. सु with नि). See Pāṇini VIII. 3, 117, and<BR>cf. अभि-सुसूष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसूदक
निसूदक नि-सूदक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. सूद्<BR>with नि), one who kills, a killer, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसूदन|निसूदनं
नि-सूदन, अस्, आ, अम्, killing, destroying, a<BR>destroyer, (at the end of a comp.); (अम्), n. killing,<BR>destroying, slaughter; (often incorrectly नि-षूदन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृ
निसृ नि-सृ, cl. 1. P. -सरति, -सर्तुम्, to<BR>go forth, (apparently only occurring in the derivative<BR>below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृत
नि-सृत, अस्, आ, अम्, = निः-सृत, q. v., gone<BR>forth, gone away, disappeared; (आ), f. the plant<BR>Ipomœa Turpethum (= त्रि-वृता); N. of a river;<BR>(a various reading for निश्-चिता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृज्
निसृज् नि-सृज्, cl. 6. P. -सृजति, -स्रष्टुम्,<BR>to let go, set free, dismiss, (apparently only used in<BR>the derivatives below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्ग|निसर्गः
नि-सर्ग, अस्, m. evacuation, voiding excrement;<BR>giving away, presenting, bestowing, granting, showing<BR>a favour; a grant; relinquishment, abandoning, set-<BR>ting free; creation; the natural state, nature, natural<BR>character, natural condition or form; exchange,<BR>barter; निसर्गेण or निसर्गात् or निसर्ग-तस्, by<BR>nature, naturally, from one's natural state or condition.<BR>—निसर्ग-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, innate; inborn, produced<BR>at creation, natural.<BR>—निसर्ग-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>naturally distinct.<BR>—निसर्ग-विनीत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>naturally discreet.<BR>—निसर्ग-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>effected by nature, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्ट|निसृष्टं
नि-सृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, dismissed, delivered, de-<BR>posited, given, bestowed, emancipated; allowed, per-<BR>mitted; central, middle.<BR>—निसृष्टार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, any one to whom the management of<BR>an affair is intrusted; (अस्), m. a chargé d'affaires,<BR>envoy, ambassador; messenger, agent, manager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसेवितव्य
निसेवितव्य नि-सेवितव्य for नि-षेवितव्य,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तक्ष्
निस्तक्ष् निस्-तक्ष्, cl. 1. P. -तक्षति, &c.,<BR>to form, create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तत्त्व
निस्तत्त्व निस्-तत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, not com-<BR>prehended in the twenty-four Tattvas or principles,<BR>(see तत्त्व.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तनी
निस्तनी नि-स्तनी, f. (according to some<BR>fr. नि + स्तनी, a small breast), a pill, bolus, a sort<BR>of force-meat ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तन्तु|निस्तंतु
निस्तन्तु निस्-तन्तु, उस्, उस्, उ, having no off-<BR>spring, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तन्द्र|निस्तंद्र
निस्तन्द्र निस्-तन्द्र, अस्, आ, अम्, or निस्-<BR>तन्द्रि, इस्, इस्, इ, not lazy or listless, fresh, healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तब्ध
निस्तब्ध नि-स्तब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, paralyzed,<BR>numbed, stiffened; stopped, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तम्भ
नि-स्तम्भ. See निः-स्तम्भ, p. 482, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तमस्क
निस्तमस्क निस्-तमस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>darkness, not gloomy, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तरण|निस्तरणं
निस्तरण निस्-तरण, निस्-तार, &c. See<BR>under निस्-तॄ, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्क्य
निस्तर्क्य निस्-तर्क्य, अस्, आ, अम्, unimagin-<BR>able, inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्हण|निस्तर्हणं
निस्तर्हण निस्-तर्हण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. तृह्<BR>with निस्), crushing, destroying, killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तल|निस्तलं
निस्तल निस्-तल, अस्, आ, अम्, not flat, round,<BR>globular; trembling, shaking, moving; down, below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तिमिर
निस्तिमिर निस्-तिमिर, अस्, आ, अम्, free from<BR>darkness, clear, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुति
निस्तुति नि-स्तुति. See under निः-स्तुति, p. 482.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुद्
निस्तुद् निस्-तुद्, cl. 6. P. A. -तुदति, -ते,<BR>-तोत्तुम्, to pierce, prick, sting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तोद|निस्तोदः
निस्-तोद, अस्, m. or निस्तोदन, अम्, n. pricking,<BR>piercing, stinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुष
निस्तुष निस्-तुष, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">Page0510-b+ 72</a>]<BR>chaff or husk; (metaphorically) purified, cleansed;<BR>simplified.<BR>—निस्तुष-क्षीर, अस्, m. wheat.<BR>—निस्-<BR>तुष-रत्न, अम्, n. crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषित|निस्तुषितं
निस्-तुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, skinned, peeled, shelled,<BR>husked, made thin, pared; left, abandoned, deserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तृणकण्टक
निस्तृणकण्टक निस्-तृण-कण्टक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>cleared or freed from grass and thorns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तॄ
निस्तॄ निस्-तॄ, cl. 1. P. -तरति, -तरितुम्,<BR>-तरीतुम्, to come forth from, to rescue or free<BR>one's self from, get out of, get clear of, escape,<BR>be saved; to pass over, pass, cross; to pass through;<BR>to pass or spend time; to accomplish, perform,<BR>fulfil, settle; to overcome, overpower, master;<BR>to expiate; अभियोगं निस्-तॄ, to clear one's self<BR>from an accusation: Caus. -तारयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to pass over; to rescue, save, release, deliver,<BR>liberate; to overcome, overpower: Desid. -तितीर्-<BR>षति, -तितरिषति, -तितरीषति, to wish to cross<BR>or pass over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तरण|निस्तरणं
निस्-तरण, अम्, n. going out or forth, coming<BR>out (of danger); crossing over or passing; rescue,<BR>releasing, deliverance, getting rid of or free from;<BR>means of success or rescue, an expedient, a plan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्तव्य
निस्-तर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be overcome or<BR>conquered or overpowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तार|निस्तारः
निस्-तार, अस्, m. crossing or passing over or<BR>across, getting rid of or away from, release, escape,<BR>rescue, preservation; final emancipation, salvation;<BR>means, expedient; payment, discharge of a debt,<BR>acquittance, requital.<BR>—निस्तार-वीज, अम्, n. a<BR>means of crossing (the ocean of life), a cause of<BR>final liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तारक
निस्-तारक, अस्, इका, अम्, rescuing, delivering; a<BR>saviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तारण|निस्तारणं
निस्-तारण, अम्, n. passing or transporting over<BR>or across, overcoming, conquering; liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तितीर्षत्
निस्-तितीर्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desirous or anxious<BR>to cross (the ocean of life); wishing for salvation or<BR>liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तीर्ण
निस्-तीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, rescued, delivered, saved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तेजस्
निस्तेजस् निस्-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, deprived of<BR>strength or energy, destitute of fire or heat, powerless,<BR>impotent; spiritless, dull; obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तोय
निस्तोय निस्-तोय, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived or<BR>destitute of water, waterless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्यज्
निस्त्यज् निस्-त्यज्, cl. 1. P. -त्यजति, -त्यक्-<BR>तुम्, to drive away, expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रंश
निस्त्रंश निस्-त्रंश, अस्, आ, अम्, fearless;<BR>(probably incorrect for निस्-त्रिंश below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रप
निस्त्रप निस्-त्रप, अस्, आ, अम्, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंश|निस्त्रिंशः
निस्त्रिंश निस्-त्रिंश, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् +<BR>त्रिंशत्), more than thirty; merciless, unfeeling,<BR>unpitying, cruel (as a sword); (अस्), m. a sword, a<BR>scimitar, falchion, a sacrificial knife, (so called because<BR>more than thirty fingers in length.)<BR>—निस्त्रिंश-<BR>धारिन्, ई, m. a sword-bearer, a swordsman or<BR>soldier armed with a sword.<BR>—निस्त्रिंश-पत्त्रक,<BR>अस्, इका, m. f. a thorny species of Euphorbia, (An-<BR>tiquorum or Tortilis).<BR>—निस्त्रिंश-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, a<BR>sword-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंशिन्
निस्त्रिंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing a sword, armed with<BR>a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रुटी
निस्त्रुटी निस्-त्रुटी, f. cardamoms; [cf. त्रुटि,<BR>निष्-कुटि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रैगुण्य
निस्त्रैगुण्य निस्-त्रैगुण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, desti-<BR>tute of the three qualities (viz. सत्त्व, रजस्, and<BR>तमस्; see गुण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रैणपुष्पक
निस्त्रैणपुष्पक निस्त्रैणपुष्पक, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. निस् + स्त्रैण + पुष्प?), a species of thorn-<BR>apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्नाव|निस्नावः
निस्नाव नि-स्नाव, अस्, m. (fr. नि-स्नु?),<BR>residue of articles &c. after a sale or market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्नेहफला
निस्नेहफला निस्नेह-फला. See निःस्नेह-<BR>फला under निः-स्नेह, p. 482, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पन्द|निस्पंद|निस्पन्दः
निस्पन्द 1. नि-स्पन्द, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्पन्द्<BR>with नि), throbbing, trembling motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पन्द|निस्पंद|निस्पन्दः
निस्पन्द 2. नि-स्पन्द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि for<BR>निस् + स्पन्द), immovable, still, steady; [cf. नि-<BR>ष्पन्द.]<BR>—निस्पन्द-त्व, अम्, n. immovableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पृश्
निस्पृश् नि-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. confiding;<BR>caressing, fondling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पृह
निस्पृह नि-स्पृह. See निः-स्पृह, p. 482.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्द|निस्यंदः|निस्यन्दः
निस्यन्द नि-स्यन्द or नि-ष्यन्द, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (fr. rt. स्यन्द् with नि, or नि for निस्), flowing<BR>or trickling down, dripping, dropping; (अस्), m. a<BR>trickling or flowing down, oozing, issuing, streaming,<BR>dropping, distilling; a discharge (of any fluid), a<BR>flux; a stream, any fluid that trickles down or drops;<BR>trickling forth from, flowing out, flowing from;<BR>necessary consequence or result; uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्दमान
नि-स्यन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trickling, flowing,<BR>oozing, issuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्दिन्|निस्यंदिन्
नि-स्यन्दिन्, ई, इनी, इ, flowing or streaming or<BR>trickling down or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्रव|निस्रवः
निस्रव नि-स्रव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्रु with<BR>नि), flowing down, a stream, torrent; (perhaps for<BR>निः-स्रव, flowing forth, streaming out.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्राव|निस्रावः
नि-स्राव, अस्, m. flowing down, a stream, torrent;<BR>the scum of boiled rice; [cf. निः-स्राव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्राविन्
नि-स्राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, flowing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वन|निस्वनः
निस्वन 1. नि-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., various<BR>reading for नि-स्वर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वन|निस्वनः
निस्वन 2. नि-स्वन, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्वन्<BR>with नि), noise, sound, voice, (often at the end of<BR>comps. when the fem. is निस्वना; cf. रथ-न्˚,<BR>उद्धतार्णव-न्˚); (अम्), ind. with noise or<BR>sound; [cf. निः-स्वन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वनित|निस्वनितं
नि-स्वनित, अम्, n. a noise, sound, crying, a cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वान|निस्वानः
नि-स्वान, अस्, m. noise, sound; the whistling<BR>sound of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वर
निस्वर नि-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. soundless,<BR>noiseless; (अस्), m. an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्
निह् निह्, Ved. = नि-हन्तृ (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्
निहन् 1. नि-हन्, cl. 2. P. -हन्ति, -हन्तुम्,<BR>to strike down, strike, kill, destroy; to strike in,<BR>fix in, infix; to disregard, neglect: Caus. -घात-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to kill, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहत
नि-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, struck down, stricken,<BR>smitten, killed, slain, overcome; struck into, infixed;<BR>attached, devoted.<BR>—निहत-भूयिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the greater number killed.<BR>—निहत-सेन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having (their) armies smitten or destroyed.<BR>—निहतोष्ट्र (˚त-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>camels killed, whose camels have been slain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्
2. नि-हन्, आ, m. a killer, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहनन|निहननं
नि-हनन, अम्, n. killing, slaughter, murder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्तव्य
नि-हन्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be struck down, to<BR>be killed or destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्तृ|निहंतृ
नि-हन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what kills or<BR>destroys, a killer; destructive, murderous; one who<BR>removes or dispels or hinders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्यमान
नि-हन्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being struck down<BR>or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहव|निहवः
निहव नि-हव. See नि-ह्वे, p. 511, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहा
निहा नि-हा, Pass. -हीयते, &c., to be de-<BR>prived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहाका
निहाका, f., Ved. a storm, whirlwind, &c.; (Sāy.)<BR>an iguana, the Gangetic alligator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीन|निहीनः
नि-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, low, vile, of low origin;<BR>(अस्), m. a low man, an outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहिंसन|निहिंसनं
निहिंसन नि-हिंसन, अम्, n. killing,<BR>slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहित|निहितं
निहित नि-हित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. नि-धा),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">Page0511-a+ 77</a>]<BR>placed, laid, fixed, lodged, situated, deposited, de-<BR>livered, given, intrusted; inserted, infixed, attached;<BR>applied to; bestowed upon; treasured up; held;<BR>laid (as dust by rain); uttered in a deep tone.<BR>—निहित-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, one who lays aside the<BR>rod, one who shows clemency.<BR>—निहित-नयन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the eyes fixed or directed upon<BR>(with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीन|निहीनः
निहीन नि-हीन. See under नि-हा, p. 510,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहृ
निहृ नि-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति, -ते, -हर्-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to offer, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहार|निहारः
नि-हार, अस्, m. = नी-हार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहारिन्
नि-हारिन्. See निर्-हारिन् under निर्-हृ, p. 502,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नु
निह्नु नि-ह्नु, cl. 2. A. -ह्नुते, -ह्नोतुम्, to<BR>disown, deny, dissimulate, conceal, evade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नव|निह्नवः
नि-ह्नव, अस्, m. denial, concealment, hushing<BR>up, dissimulation; concealment in general, secrecy;<BR>mistrust, doubt, suspicion; a secret; wickedness;<BR>atonement, expiation; excuse, exculpation, depre-<BR>cation; N. of a ceremony; N. of a Sāman.<BR>—नि-<BR>ह्नव-वादिन्, ई, m. a defendant or witness who<BR>prevaricates or tries to hide the truth.<BR>—निह्नवोत्-<BR>तर (˚व-उत्˚), अम्, n. an evasive reply or defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुत
नि-ह्नुत, अस्, आ, अम्, denied, disowned, evaded;<BR>concealed, secreted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुति|निह्नुतिः
नि-ह्नुति, इस्, f. denial or concealment of know-<BR>ledge; dissimulation, reserve, secrecy; hiding, con-<BR>cealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुवन
नि-ह्नुवन, अम्, n. denial or concealment of<BR>knowledge; excuse, exculpation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुवान
नि-ह्नुवान, अस्, आ, अम्, dissimulating, prevari-<BR>cating, insinuating, using double entendre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्राद|निह्रादः
निह्राद नि-ह्राद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. ह्राद् with<BR>नि), sound; (also read निर्-ह्राद.)<BR>—निह्राद-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, sounding, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्रादिन्
नि-ह्रादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding, pealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्वे
निह्वे नि-ह्वे, cl. 1. P. A. -ह्वयति, -ते,<BR>-ह्वातुम्, to invoke, call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहव|निहवः
नि-हव, अस्, m. invocation, calling, summoning,<BR>calling near; N. of a Sāman, (वसिष्ठस्य नि-<BR>हवस् or वसिष्ठ-निहवस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी 1. नी, cl. 1. P. A. नयति, -ते, अनयत् (ep.<BR>also अनयीत्), नयेत (ep. also नयीत), निनाय<BR>(3rd pl. निन्युस्, anomalous form of Perf. नयाम्-<BR>आस), निन्ये, नेता (ep. also नयिता), नेष्यति, -ते<BR>(ep. also नयिष्यति), अनैषीत्, अनेष्ट (Ved. forms<BR>नेषत्, नेषति, नेषि, नैष्ट, नेष्ट), नेतुम्<BR>(ep. also नयितुम्), to lead, guide, conduct, (व्यव-<BR>हारं नी, to conduct a process); to direct, govern;<BR>to lead or bring away, carry away, to lead or bring<BR>away to (with acc., dat., or loc.); to carry off for<BR>one's self (A.); to marry; to bring a person (acc.)<BR>into any state or condition (acc. or loc., e. g. नृ-<BR>पतीन् वशम् अनयत्, he brought the kings into<BR>subjection; तां दुहितृत्वे नयति, he brings her<BR>into the state of a daughter: sometimes used with<BR>a substantive in the same way as 1. कृ, q. v., e. g.<BR>विनाशं नी, to destroy; परितोषं नी, to gratify;<BR>विक्रयं नी, to sell; दुःखं नी, to pain;<BR>साक्ष्यं नी, to admit as a witness; आधानं नी,<BR>to give in pledge; शूद्रतां नी, to reduce to a<BR>Śūdra: or with an adverb ending in सात्, e. g. भस्-<BR>मसाद् नी, to reduce to ashes); to lead away from,<BR>exclude from; to draw (a line &c.); to trace, track;<BR>to ascertain, investigate; to settle; to pass or spend<BR>(time); to carry, bear; (with दण्डम्) to bear<BR>the rod, inflict punishment; to guide in learning,<BR>instruct (A.): Pass. नीयते, to be led, &c.: Caus.<BR>नाययति, &c., to cause to lead, &c.; to cause to<BR>be carried away: Desid. निनीषति, -ते (Ved. निने-<BR>षति), to wish to lead, &c.; to wish to take away;<BR>to wish to bring to a state; to wish to exclude from<BR>(with abl.); to wish to trace or ascertain, investigate<BR>[cf. निनीषा, निनीषु]: Intens. नेनीयते, to lead<BR>as a captive, have in one's power, rule; [cf. Gr.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">Page0511-b+ 81</a>]<BR>νέ-ο-μαι, νίσσομαι, νῑσομαι; Lith. neṣù; Slav. ne-<BR>sun, ‘I bear.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
2. नी, ईस्, m. a leader, a guide, (used at the end<BR>of a comp.; cf. अग्र-णी, अग्रे-णी, ऋत-नी, गाथा-<BR>नी, ग्राम-णी, पद-नी, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीक|नीकः
नीक, अस्, m. a species of tree; (आ), f. a channel<BR>for irrigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
1. नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, led, guided, conducted; brought,<BR>reduced; gained, obtained; well-behaved, correct,<BR>modest; (अम्), n. wealth; corn, grain; [cf. असु-न्˚,<BR>दुर्-न्˚, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीति|नीतिः
नीति, इस्, f. guiding, guidance, directing, direction,<BR>management; manner of conducting one's self, con-<BR>duct, propriety; right or moral or prudent behaviour,<BR>prudent counsel, policy, political wisdom or science,<BR>political economy, state policy, statesmanship, the<BR>administration of government; moral philosophy,<BR>ethics, precepts for prudent and moral behaviour,<BR>prudence, Prudence or Polity personified [cf. नय];<BR>leading or bringing to, obtaining, acquirement, acqui-<BR>sition; presenting, offering; relation, support; [cf.<BR>अग्र-णीति, अदब्ध-न्˚, असु-न्˚, ऋजु-न्˚, &c.]<BR>—नीति-<BR>कथा, f. any work on moral or political science, a<BR>discourse on political economy.<BR>—नीति-कुशल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, conversant with political science, skilful in<BR>human affairs, a good statesman.<BR>—नीति-घोष, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the car of Bṛhas-pati.<BR>—नीति-ज्ञ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, knowing what is right especially in government,<BR>sagacious, politic, prudent; (अस्), m. a prudent<BR>statesman or soldier, a politician.<BR>—नीति-दोष, अस्,<BR>m. error of conduct, mistake in policy.<BR>—नीति-<BR>निष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, versed in political or moral<BR>science.<BR>—नीति-प्रदीप, अस्, m. ‘the light of pru-<BR>dent behaviour,’ N. of a collection of verses attributed<BR>to Vetāla-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—नीति-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a work<BR>on morality or right behaviour.<BR>—नीति-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, knowing the rules of moral or prudent<BR>behaviour, moral, prudent, eminent for political<BR>wisdom.<BR>—नीति-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘the jewel of mora-<BR>lity,’ N. of a collection of verses attributed to Vara-<BR>ruci.<BR>—नीति-वाक्यामृत (˚य-अम्˚), अम्, n. ‘nectar<BR>of discourse on morality or prudent behaviour,’ N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—नीति-विद्, त्, m. a politician, any one<BR>versed in political science, a statesman.<BR>—नीति-विद्या,<BR>f. moral or political science, political economy; [cf.<BR>नीति-शास्त्र.]<BR>—नीति-विषय, अस्, m. the sphere of<BR>morality or prudent conduct.<BR>—नीति-वीज, अम्, n. a<BR>germ or source of intrigue.<BR>—नीति-वेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>knowing policy, a politician.<BR>—नीति-व्यतिक्रम, अस्,<BR>m. error of conduct, transgression of the rules of<BR>moral or political science.<BR>—नीति-शतक, अम्, n. the<BR>hundred verses on morality by Bhartṛ-hari.<BR>—नीति-<BR>शास्त्र, अम्, n. the science of ethics or politics, any<BR>work on political ethics or morals.<BR>—नीति-सङ्क-<BR>लन, अम्, n. ‘collection of rules for moral conduct<BR>or prudent behaviour,’ N. of a modern work.<BR>—नीति-<BR>सार, अस्, m. or अम्, n. the essence of political or<BR>moral science; (अम्), n. a special work on this<BR>subject by Ghaṭa-karpara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत्वा
नीत्वा, ind. having led or conducted or guided;<BR>having taken; having passed or spent (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीथ|नीथः
नीथ, अस्, m. (Ved. also n.) leading, guiding;<BR>a leader, a guider; N. of a man; (आ), f., Ved. way,<BR>trick; evasion, subterfuge; a mode in music; water;<BR>[cf. दीर्घ-न्˚, देव-न्˚.]<BR>—नीथा-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>knowing ways, knowing the musical modes, skilled<BR>in sacred song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीथ्य
नीथ्य. See ग्रामणीथ्य, p. 304, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीयमान|नीयमानं
नीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being led or conducted or<BR>conveyed, being carried or brought, being taken or<BR>taken away; being traced or sought or obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतव्य
नेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be led or guided or con-<BR>ducted, to be led away, to be taken, to be carried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतृ
नेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, leading, conducting, guiding,<BR>one who brings or leads to; (ता), m. a leader, guide,<BR>conductor; a chief, master, owner; (with दण्डस्य)<BR>an inflicter of punishment [cf. दण्ड-न्˚]; the hero<BR>of a drama or play; the plant Azadirachta Indica<BR>(= निम्ब); the numeral two; (त्री), f. a female<BR>leader; a river; a vein; an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—नेतृ-त्व, अम्, n. the office or business of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">Page0511-c+ 78</a>]<BR>leader &c., leadership.<BR>—नेतृ-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>containing the word नेतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्र|नेत्रं
नेत्र, अस्, ई, अम्, one who guides or leads, a<BR>leader, guide; a substitute for नेतृ at the end of a<BR>comp. (e. g. भवन्-नेत्र, having thee as com-<BR>mander); (अस्), m., N. of a son of Dharma and<BR>father of Kunti; also a son of Su-mati; (अम्), n.<BR>leading, conducting; the eye (as the instrument of<BR>leading or guiding); symbolic expression for the<BR>number two; the string with which a churning-stick<BR>is whirled round; an enema-pipe; the root of a tree;<BR>bleached or wove silk; a carriage.<BR>—नेत्र-कनी-<BR>निका, f. the pupil of the eye.<BR>—नेत्र-कोष, अस्,<BR>m. the eyeball; the bud of a flower.<BR>—नेत्र-गो-<BR>चर, अस्, आ, अम्, within the range of the sight,<BR>visible.<BR>—नेत्र-च्छद, अस्, m. the eyelid.<BR>—नेत्र-<BR>ज, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘eye-born,’ coming from the eyes; (अम्),<BR>n. a tear.<BR>—नेत्र-जल, अम्, n. ‘eye-water,’ tears.<BR>—नेत्र-ता, f. the state of being an eye; नेत्रतां<BR>या, to become an eye.<BR>—नेत्र-त्रिभाग-ब्रह्म-<BR>यशस्विन्, ई, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नेत्र-पर्यन्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, as far as to the eye, up to the eye; (अस्),<BR>m. the outer angle of the eye.<BR>—नेत्र-पिण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. a cat (‘having full eyes’); the eyeball.<BR>—नेत्र-<BR>पुष्करा, f. a species of plant; [cf. रुद्र-जटा.]<BR>—नेत्र-मनः-स्वभावास्, m. pl. eyes, mind,<BR>and soul.<BR>—नेत्र-मीना, f. a species of plant (=<BR>यव-तिक्ता).<BR>—नेत्र-मुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, stealing or cap-<BR>tivating the eye.<BR>—नेत्र-योनि, इस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Indra (as covered with marks resembling the female<BR>organ, through the curse of Gautama, whose wife<BR>Ahalyā he had attempted to seduce; the sage after-<BR>wards relenting, changed these disgraceful marks on<BR>the body of the deity to as many eyes); the moon<BR>(as produced from the eye of Atri).<BR>—नेत्र-रञ्जन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘eye-colouring,’ collyrium.<BR>—नेत्र-रुज्, क्,<BR>f. disease of the eyes.<BR>—नेत्र-रोग, अस्, m. disease<BR>of the eyes, ophthalmia; (अस्, आ, अम्), afflicted with<BR>disease of the eyes.<BR>—नेत्ररोग-ता, f. disease of the<BR>eyes.<BR>—नेत्ररोग-हन्, आ, m. a particular plant used<BR>for diseases of the eyes, Tragia Involucrata.<BR>—नेत्र-<BR>रोमन्, अ, n. the eyelash.<BR>—नेत्र-वस्ति, इस्, m. f.<BR>a clyster-pipe with a bag.<BR>—नेत्र-वस्त्र, अम्, n. a<BR>veil over the eye.<BR>—नेत्र-वारि, n. ‘eye-water,’<BR>tears.<BR>—नेत्र-विष्, ट्, f. excretion of the eyes.<BR>—नेत्र-विष, अस्, आ, अम्, having poison in the<BR>eyes.<BR>—नेत्र-स्तम्भ, अस्, m. rigidity of the eyes.<BR>—नेत्राञ्जन (˚र-अञ्˚), अम्, n. ‘eye-ointment,’<BR>collyrium.<BR>—नेत्रान्त (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, m. the outer<BR>corner of the eye.<BR>—नेत्राभिष्यन्द (˚र-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. running of the eyes.<BR>—नेत्रामय (˚र-<BR>आम्˚), अस्, m. ophthalmia.<BR>—नेत्राम्बु (˚र-अम्˚)<BR>or नेत्राम्भस् (˚र-अम्˚), अस्, n. ‘eye-water,’<BR>tears.<BR>—नेत्रारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m. a species of plant<BR>(= सीहुण्ड).<BR>—नेत्रोत्सव (˚र-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘eye-<BR>feast,’ any pleasing or beautiful object.<BR>—नेत्रोपम<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n. the almond fruit (as resembling<BR>eyes).<BR>—नेत्रोपम-फल, अस्, m. the almond<BR>tree.<BR>—नेत्रौषध (˚र-औष्˚), अम्, n. medi-<BR>cine for the eyes, collyrium, green sulphate of iron<BR>used as collyrium; (ई), f. Odina Pinnata (= अज-<BR>शृङ्गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रिक|नेत्रिकं
नेत्रिक, अम्, n. a pipe, a clyster-pipe; a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेय
नेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be guided or led; to be<BR>governed; to be passed or spent (as time); to be<BR>led away; to be inflicted (e. g. नेयो दण्डस्,<BR>punishment must be inflicted).<BR>—नेय-पाल, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी 3. नी (नि इ), cl. 2. P. न्य्-एति, न्य्-एतुम्,<BR>Ved. to go into, enter, come or fall into, change to;<BR>[cf. न्य्-आय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
2. नीत, अस्, आ, अम्, entered, gone to; (Sāy.) =<BR>नितराम् प्राप्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकर्षिन्
नीकर्षिन् नी-कर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. rt. कृष्<BR>with नि), spreading the tail (as a peacock ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकार|नीकारः
नीकार नी-कार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. कृ with<BR>नि), disrespect, contempt, vilifying, degrading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकाश|नीकाशः
नीकाश नी-काश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. काश् with नि),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">Page0512-a+ 78</a>]<BR>appearance, look, air, mien; certainty, ascertainment;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), like, resembling, (at the end of comps.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकुलक
नीकुलक नीकुलक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीक्लेद
नीक्लेद नी-क्लेद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. क्लिद् with नि),<BR>moistening, bedewing (?), Pāṇ. VI. 3, 122, Schol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीक्षण|नीक्षणं
नीक्षण नीक्षण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. ईक्ष् with नि<BR>or rt. निक्ष्?), Ved. a stick for stirring up a caldron,<BR>a kind of ladle, (Sāy. = पाक-परीक्षा-साधनं<BR>काष्ठम्); [cf. नेक्षण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीच|नीचः
नीच नीच, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि + अञ्च्, cf. उच्च;<BR>said to be fr. rt. चि with नि), low, not high, short,<BR>little, small, dwarfish; deep, lowered (as the voice),<BR>pronounced without an accent; situated below, being<BR>in a low position; low, vile, insignificant, inferior,<BR>base, mean (as a man or action); (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of perfume (= चोरक); (अम्), n. (in astrology) the<BR>lowest point of a planet (= ταπείνωμα), the seventh<BR>house from the highest point; (आत्), ind. from below,<BR>from beneath; [cf. नीचैस्, उच्च-नीच, न्य्-अञ्च्.]<BR>—नी-<BR>च-कदम्ब, अस्, m., N. of a plant (= मण्डीरी).<BR>—नीच-कुल, अम्, n. a low family.<BR>—नीच-ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, going low or downwards, descending (as a<BR>river); being in or belonging to a low man or<BR>to a low class of men; low, vile, base; (आ), f. a<BR>river; (अम्), n. water.<BR>—नीच-गत, अस्, आ, अम्<BR>being at the lowest point (as a planet).<BR>—नीच-<BR>गृह, अम्, n. (in astrology) the house or station of<BR>the heavens in which a planet stands at its lowest<BR>point.<BR>—नीच-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, of low birth.<BR>—निच-ता,<BR>f. or नीच-त्व, अम्, n. (opposed to उच्च-ता), lowness,<BR>meanness, vileness, baseness, humbleness, inferiority,<BR>a low situation.<BR>—नीच-भोज्य, अस्, m. ‘the food of<BR>low men,’ an onion.<BR>—नीच-मेढ्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. one whose penis hangs low.<BR>—नीच-योनिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, being of low origin, low-born.<BR>—नीच-रत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, delighting in mean things.<BR>—नीचर्क्ष<BR>(˚च-ऋक्˚), अम्, n. (?) = नीच-गृह, q. v.<BR>—नीच-<BR>वज्र, अम्, n. an inferior diamond, a sort of gem (=<BR>वैक्रान्त).<BR>—नीचा-वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one<BR>whose strength has failed; (Sāy.) bending down the<BR>body.<BR>—नीचोक्ति (˚च-उक्˚), इस्, f. a low or vulgar<BR>expression.<BR>—नीचोच्च-वृत्त (˚च-उच्˚), अम्, n. an<BR>epicycle.<BR>—नीचोपगत (˚च-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, situ-<BR>ated low in the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचक|नीचकः
नीचक, अस्, इका, अम्, low, short, dwarfish; (low<BR>as the voice), soft; vile, mean; (अका), f. an excel-<BR>lent cow; (अकी), f. the head of an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकिन्
नीचकिन्, ई, m. the head or top of anything, the head<BR>of an ox; the owner of a good cow; [cf. नैचिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकैस्
नीचकैस्, ind. (diminutive of नीचैस्), low, below,<BR>little, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचा
नीचा, ind. low, below, down, downwards, (this word<BR>may be regarded as the inst. c. of न्य्-अञ्च्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचात्
नीचात्, ind. from below. See नीच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचायमान
नीचायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. descending, flying<BR>down (as a falcon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचीकृ
नीची-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to lower, to pronounce without an accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचीन
नीचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being low or below,<BR>low, directed downwards or underneath, hanging<BR>down, flowing down, cast down.<BR>—नीचीन-बार, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having its opening below (as a cloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचैस्
नीचैस्, ind. low, below, down, downwards, under-<BR>neath, beneath, deeply, deep, in the depths, in a<BR>bent or inclined position, bowing low, humbly,<BR>modestly; with a low or depressed or deep tone of<BR>voice, in a low tone (i. e. अन्-उदात्त, q. v.), softly;<BR>short, small, little, dwarfish; N. of a mountain, also<BR>called वामन-गिरि and खर्व (Dwarfish); [cf.<BR>उच्चैस्, निम्नैस्, शनैस्.]<BR>—नीचैः-कर, अस्, आ<BR>or ई, अम्, causing a low or deep tone, giving depth<BR>of voice.<BR>—नीचैर्-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, with down-<BR>cast countenance.<BR>—नीचैस्-तराम्, ind. in a low<BR>tone, softly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीच्य
1. नीच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, living below; Ved. an epithet<BR>of some nations in the West.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीच्य
2. नीच्य, Nom. P. नीच्यति, &c., to be in a low<BR>situation, be a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीड|नीडं|नीडः
नीड नीड (Ved. नीऌअ), अस्, अम्, m. n. (per-<BR>haps fr. rt. सद् with नि, whence नि-षद = निष्ड<BR>= निड्ड = नीड, or fr. rt. इल् with नि), a resting-place,<BR>a place for lying down, a bird's nest; a bed, couch;<BR>a lair, den; the interior or seat of a carriage or<BR>chariot; a place, abode in general; [cf. Lat. nīdus;<BR>Hib. nead; Cambro-Brit. nyth; Germ. and Angl.<BR>Sax. nest.]<BR>—नीड-ज, अस्, m. ‘nest-born,’ a bird.<BR>—नीडजेन्द्र (˚ज-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘chief of the birds,’<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—नीडोद्भव (˚ड-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘nest-born,’ a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडक|नीडकः
नीडक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the nest of a<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडय
नीडय or नीऌअय, Nom. P. नीडयति or नीऌअ-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Ved. (according to Sāy.) to bring<BR>together, join together, cause to come to close fight-<BR>ing; to bring to rest (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडि
नीडि or नीऌइ, इस्, m., Ved. one who lives in the<BR>same house (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
नीत नीत, नीति, &c. See p. 511, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतमिश्र
नीतमिश्र नीत-मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम् (नीत =<BR>नव-नीत), Ved. not yet become butter, (said of<BR>दधि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत्त
नीत्त नी-त्त, अस्, आ, अम् (for नि-दत्त fr. rt.<BR>1. दा with नि), Ved. given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीध्र|नीध्रं
नीध्र नीध्र, अम्, n. the edge of thatch,<BR>edge of a roof; a wood; the circumference of a<BR>wheel; the moon; the constellation Revatī; (consi-<BR>dered by some as a various reading for नीव्र, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीनाह
नीनाह नीनाह, अस्, m., Ved. anything<BR>which encircles another (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीप|नीपः
नीप नीप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि-अप्, but said to<BR>be fr. rt. 1. नी), situated low, deep; (अस्), m. the<BR>foot of a mountain; N. of a son of Kṛtin; the<BR>tree Nauclea Cadamba (= कदम्ब = धारा-क-<BR>दम्बक = धरा-कदम्ब = धूली-कदम्ब);<BR>the plant Ixora Bandhuca (= बन्धूक); a species<BR>of Aśoka (= नीलाशोक); (अम्), n. the fruit of the<BR>above plants; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a regal family<BR>descended from Nīpa, son of Pāra.<BR>—नीप-राज,<BR>अम्, n. (?), the fruit (?) of the Nīpa.<BR>—नीपातिथि<BR>(˚प-अत्˚), इस्, m., N. of a descendant of Kaṇva and<BR>author of a hymn of the Ṛg-veda (VIII. 34).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीप्य
नीप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being low or on the<BR>ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीमानुय
नीमानुय नीमानुय, अस्, m., N. of a Vaiṣ-<BR>ṇava teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीयमान|नीयमानं
नीयमान नीयमान. See p. 511, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीर्
नीर् नीर् (नि-ईर्), Caus. P. नीरयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to drive or impel into, urge forwards (to an aim);<BR>to send forth, appoint (to a business).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीर|नीरं
नीर नीर, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1. नी),<BR>water; juice, liquor, (sometimes written for नीड,<BR>नीऌअ, q. v.); (अस्), m., N. of a prince; [cf. क्षीर-<BR>नीर, नार; Gr. νηπός, Νηρεύς.]<BR>—नीर-ग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. taking up water in a ladle; see under<BR>ग्रह. — 1. नीर-ज, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see below),<BR>‘water-born,’ being in water, aquatic; (अस्), m. an<BR>otter; a species of grass, = उशीरी; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>(according to the lexicographers only n.), a lotus<BR>in general, the water-lily; (अम्), n. a species of<BR>Costus, Costus Speciosus (= कुष्ठ); a pearl.<BR>—नीर-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘water-born,’ produced<BR>from water, aquatic.<BR>—१. नीर-द, अस्, m. (for 2.<BR>see col. 3), ‘giving water,’ a cloud; a species of<BR>Cyperus.<BR>—नीरदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, cloudy.<BR>—नीर-धि<BR>or नीर-निधि, इस्, m. ‘the receptacle of waters,’ the<BR>ocean; [cf. अब्-धि, तोय-धि, &c.]<BR>—नीर-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, m. a species of reed (जल-वेतस).<BR>—नीर-<BR>रुह, अम्, n. the water-lily, lotus.<BR>—नीराखु (˚र-<BR>आखु), उस्, m. ‘water-rat,’ an otter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरक्त
नीरक्त नी-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रक्त),<BR>colourless, faded, having the colour gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरज|नीरजं|नीरजः
नीरज 2. नी-रज, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रज<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">Page0512-c+ 72</a>]<BR>for रजस्), free from dust; devoid of passion; (with<BR>वि-रज) an epithet of Śiva. (For 1. नीर-ज see<BR>under नीर, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्
नी-रजस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (fr. निस् + रजस्), free from<BR>dust, having no pollen (as a flower); free from<BR>passion; (आस्), f. a woman not menstruating.<BR>—नी-<BR>रजस्-तमसा, f. absence of passion and darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्क
नी-रजस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, free from dust, not<BR>accompanied by dust (as wind); free from passion,<BR>pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्व
नी-रजस्व, अस्, आ, अम्, free from dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजीकृ
नीरजी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make free from dust.<BR>—नीरजी-कारित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, made free from dust, cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरत|नीरतः
नीरत नी-रत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रत),<BR>not delighting in, not attached to, indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरद|नीरदः
नीरद 2. नी-रद, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रद),<BR>toothless. (For 1. नीर-द see under नीर, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरन्ध्र|नीरंध्र|नीरन्ध्रं
नीरन्ध्र नी-रन्ध्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् +<BR>रन्ध्र), having no holes or openings, without<BR>apertures or interstices, imperforate, close, uninter-<BR>rupted; coarse, thick, gross.<BR>—नीरन्ध्र-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. closeness, close connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरव
नीरव नी-रव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रव),<BR>soundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरस|नीरसः
नीरस नी-रस, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रस),<BR>without juice, sapless, dried up, withered; flavourless,<BR>unsavoury, tasteless, devoid of taste, flat, dry; insipid;<BR>vain; (अस्), m. the pomegranate.<BR>—नीरस-ता, f. the<BR>state of being devoid of taste, tastelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरसन
नीरसन नी-रसन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + र-<BR>सना), having no girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराजन|नीराजनं
नीराजन नी-राजन, अम्, आ, n. f. (fr. rt. राज्<BR>with नि), lustration of arms (lustratio exercitus),<BR>a military and religious ceremony held by kings or<BR>generals on the nineteenth of Aśvin before taking the<BR>field, (it consists in purifying the Puro-hita or chaplain,<BR>the king's ministers, and various component parts of<BR>the army during the recitation of sacred texts);<BR>waving lights before an idol as an act of adoration,<BR>(this may also be performed with a lotus, clean<BR>cloth, or the leaves of various sacred plants; pros-<BR>tration is considered as a fifth kind of adoration.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरिन्दु|नीरिन्दुः
नीरिन्दु नीरिन्दु, उस्, m. a species of plant<BR>(= अश्व-शाखोट), Trophis Aspera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुच्
नीरुच् नी-रुच्, क्, क्, क् (fr. निस् + रुच्), lustre-<BR>less, dull, dim, faded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज्
नीरुज् नी-रुज्, क्, क्, क् (fr. निस् + रुज्), free<BR>from sickness; convalescent, well, in health; painless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज|नीरुजं|नीरुजः
नी-रुज, अस्, आ, अम्, = नी-रुज्, healthy, in health,<BR>well, (sometimes written नि-रुज); (अम्), n. a<BR>species of Costus, Costus Speciosus (= कुष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरूप|नीरूपं|नीरूपः
नीरूप नी-रूप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रूप),<BR>formless, shapeless, mis-shapen; (अस्), m. air, wind;<BR>a god; (अम्), n. heaven, ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरेणुक|नीरेणुकः
नीरेणुक नी-रेणुक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् +<BR>रेणु), dustless, free from dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरोग
नीरोग नी-रोग, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रोग),<BR>free from sickness, healthy, well.<BR>—नीरोग-ता, f.<BR>health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरोग्यता
नीरोग्य-ता, f. health, freedom from sickness,<BR>(perhaps an error for नीरोग-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरोह
नीरोह नी-रोह, अस्, m. (fr. निस् + रुह्), Ved.<BR>shooting out, growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नील्
नील् नील् (rather a Nom. derived fr.<BR>नील below), cl. 1. P. नीलति, &c., to be<BR>of a dark colour; to dye dark, make or dye blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नील|नीलं|नीलः
नील, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (probably fr. निश् + ल =<BR>निश्ल = निल्ल = नील; according to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 42,<BR>the fem. form नीला is used in relation to clothes &c.,<BR>and नीली in relation to plants, animals, &c.; in proper<BR>names either form is allowed), of a dark colour,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0513-a" target="_blank">Page0513-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(especially dark-blue or black); dyed with indigo;<BR>(अस्), m. dark-blue or black (the colour); a gem,<BR>the sapphire; the Indian fig-tree (= वट); a species<BR>of bird, the blue or hill Maina; an ox or bull of<BR>a dark colour; one of the nine Nidhis or divine<BR>treasures of Kuvera; N. of a man, the prince of<BR>Māhiṣmatī; of a son of Yadu; of a historian of<BR>Kaśmīra; an epithet of Mañju-śrī; N. of a Nāga;<BR>of one of the monkey-chiefs attending on Rāma,<BR>(said to be a son of Agni); the blue mountain, one<BR>of the principal ranges of mountains dividing the<BR>world into nine portions and lying immediately north<BR>of Ilāvṛta or the central division [cf. नीलाद्रि]; (आ),<BR>f. the indigo plant, Indigofera Tinctoria [cf. नीली];<BR>a species of Boerhavia with blue blossoms (= नील-<BR>पुनर्-नवा); a species of blue fly [cf. नीली]; the<BR>two arteries in front of the neck, (in this sense नीले,<BR>f. du.); a black and blue mark on the skin (either<BR>from a bruise or a disease?); a Rāgiṇī or mode of<BR>music, personified as the wife of Rāga Mallāra; (ई),<BR>f. the indigo plant; another plant, Blyxa Saivala (=<BR>शैवल; cf. जल-नीली); a species of blue fly; a<BR>kind of disease (= नीली-रोग, नीलिका); N. of the<BR>wife of Aja-mīḍha [cf. नीलिनी, नलिनी]; (अम्), n.<BR>darkness (Ved.); indigo, the dye; black salt (=<BR>काच-लवण); blue vitriol (= तुत्थ); antimony<BR>(= सौवीराञ्जन); poison (= तालीश-पत्त्र); a<BR>peculiar position in dancing; a kind of metre con-<BR>sisting of four times sixteen syllables; [cf. Lat.<BR>niger for nigro = निश्-र.]<BR>—नील-कणा, f. a species<BR>of cumin.<BR>—नील-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, blue-necked;<BR>(अस्), m. a peacock; a species of gallinule or water-<BR>hen (= दात्यूह); a wag-tail; a sparrow; a blue-<BR>necked jay; the plant Hyperanthera Moringa (=<BR>पीत-सार); an epithet of Śiva (as having a black<BR>throat, so stained by the acrimony of the poison<BR>which he swallowed on its production at the churn-<BR>ing of the ocean); N. of several authors and com-<BR>mentators; (अम्), n. a radish; [cf. काल-कण्ठ.]<BR>—नीलकण्ठ-चम्पू, ऊस्, f., N. of a work by<BR>Nīlakaṇṭha Dīkṣita.<BR>—नीलकण्ठ-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the bathing-place of Śiva,’ N. of a sacred Tīrtha.<BR>—नीलकण्ठ-भारती, m., N. of an author men-<BR>tioned in the Sarva-darśana-saṅgraha of Mādhavā-<BR>cārya.<BR>—नीलकण्ठ-स्तव, अस्, m. ‘the praise of<BR>Śiva,’ N. of the fifty-first chapter of the Jñāna-<BR>khaṇḍa of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—नीलकण्ठाक्ष<BR>(˚ठ-अक्˚), अम्, n. the berry or seed of Elæocarpus<BR>Ganitrus.<BR>—नील-कन्द, अस्, m. a species of bulbous<BR>plant (= महिष-कन्द-भेद).<BR>—नील-कमल,<BR>अम्, n. the blue water-lily.<BR>—नील-कायिक, आस्, m.<BR>pl. (with Buddhists) ‘blue-bodied’ or ‘dark-bodied,’<BR>epithet of a class of deities.<BR>—नील-कुन्तला, f., N.<BR>of a female friend of Durgā.<BR>—नील-कुरण्टक,<BR>अस्, m. or नील-कुसुमा, f. or नील-कुरुण्टक, a<BR>species of Barleria with blue blossoms (B. Cœrulea,<BR>= नील-झिण्टी).<BR>—नील-केशी, f. the indigo plant.<BR>—नील-क्रान्ता, f. a species of plant (= विष्णु-<BR>क्रान्ता).<BR>—नील-क्रौञ्च, अस्, m. a species of curlew<BR>or heron.<BR>—नील-गङ्गा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—नील-<BR>गणेश, अस्, m. the blue Gaṇeśa.<BR>—नील-गर्भ,<BR>a young blue water-lily (?).<BR>—नील-गिरि-कर्णिका, f.<BR>a blue variety of Clitoria Ternatea.<BR>—नील-ग्रीव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, blue-necked; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Rudra-Śiva or Mahā-deva, (see नील-कण्ठ); N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—नील-घोर, a various reading for नील-<BR>पोर, q. v.<BR>—नील-चर्मन्, अ, n. the tree Xylo-<BR>carpus Granatum.<BR>—नील-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘dark-<BR>leaved,’ the date tree; ‘blue-winged,’ an epithet<BR>of Garuḍa.<BR>—नील-च्छवी, a species of bird (=<BR>कुकु; the right form is probably नील-च्छविन्, ई,<BR>m.).<BR>—नील-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced in the blue<BR>mountains; (अम्), n. blue steel; (आ), f. the river<BR>Vitastā.<BR>—नील-झिण्टी, f. blue Barleria (= नील-<BR>कुरण्टक).<BR>—नील-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—नील-तरु, उस्, m. the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>—नील-ता,<BR>f. blueness, blackness, a blue or dark colour.<BR>—नील-<BR>ताल, अस्, m. Xanthochymus Pictorius; Phœnix<BR>Paludosa.<BR>—नील-दूर्वा, f. a species of plant (=<BR>हरिता).<BR>—नील-द्रुम, अस्, m. a species of tree (=<BR>नीलासन).<BR>—नील-ध्वज, अस्, m. Xanthochymus<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0513-b" target="_blank">Page0513-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Pictorius; N. of a prince of Māhiṣmatī.<BR>—नील-<BR>नख, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. black-clawed, having black<BR>claws.<BR>—नील-निर्गुण्डी, f. a species of Nirguṇḍī<BR>with blue blossoms.<BR>—नील-निर्यासक, अस्, m. a<BR>species of tree (= नीलासन).<BR>—नील-नीरज, अम्, n.<BR>the blue water-lily.<BR>—नील-पक्ष्मन्, आ, आ, अ, having<BR>black eyelashes.<BR>—नील-पङ्क, अम्, n. darkness;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. black mud.<BR>—नील-पटल, अम्, n. a<BR>sort of dark film or membrane over the eye of a blind<BR>person; a dark mass, a black coating or covering.<BR>—नील-पत्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-leaved, having black<BR>or dark-blue leaves; (अस्), m., N. of several plants, Scir-<BR>pus Kysoor; the pomegranate tree; (आ), f. Premna<BR>Herbacea; (अम्), n. the blue water-lily.<BR>—नील-<BR>पद्म, अम्, n. the blue water-lily.<BR>—नील-पर्ण,<BR>अस्, m. Grevia Orientalis; (ई), f. Vanda (= वन्दा)<BR>Roxburghii.<BR>—नील-पाचन, अम्, n. steeping or<BR>maceration of indigo.<BR>—नीलपाचन-भाण्ड, अम्,<BR>n. a vessel for steeping indigo, an indigo vat.<BR>—नील-<BR>पिङ्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, of a dark-brown colour.<BR>—नील-पिच्छ, अस्, m. ‘black-tailed,’ a falcon.<BR>—नील-पिट, अस्, m. (with Buddhists) a collection<BR>of annals and royal edicts.<BR>—नील-पिष्टोडी, f. a<BR>species of shrub (= नीलाम्ली).<BR>—नील-पुनर्-नवा,<BR>f. a species of Punar-navā with blue blossoms.<BR>—नील-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—नील-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—नील-पुष्प,<BR>अस्, m. a species of Verbesina with blue flowers;<BR>(आ), f. a plant (= विष्णु-क्रान्ता); (ई), f. a plant<BR>(= नील-वुह्ना); (अम्), n. a species of fragrant plant<BR>(= ग्रन्थि-पर्ण).<BR>—नील-पुष्पिका, f. the indigo<BR>plant; linseed, Linum Usitatissimum.<BR>—नील-पृष्-<BR>ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘black-backed,’ epithet of<BR>Agni; (अस्), m. a species of fish, commonly called<BR>Rohi, Cyprinus Denticulatus.<BR>—नील-पोर, अस्, m.<BR>a species of sugar-cane.<BR>—नील-भ, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>a bluish or dark appearance,’ the moon; a cloud;<BR>a bee; [cf. नीलाभ.]<BR>—नील-भू, ऊस्, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—नील-भृङ्गराज, अस्, m. a species of<BR>Verbesina with blue blossoms.<BR>—नील-मक्षा, f. a<BR>species of blue fly or bee.<BR>—नील-मणि, इस्, m. a<BR>blue gem, the sapphire.<BR>—नील-मत, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a poem in the Pauranic style, celebrating the sacred<BR>places of Kaśmīra, and said to have been inspired<BR>by Nīla the serpent-king.<BR>—नील-मल्लिका, f. Ægle<BR>Marmelos.<BR>—नील-माधव, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (as being of a dark colour).<BR>—नील-माष, अस्, m. Dolichos Catjang.<BR>—नील-<BR>मीलिक, अस्, m. a fire-fly.<BR>—नील-मृत्तिका, f. iron<BR>pyrites; black earth or mould.<BR>—नील-मेहिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, voiding dark or bluish urine.<BR>—नील-यष्-<BR>टिका, f. a species of dark sugar-cane.<BR>—नील-रत्न,<BR>अम्, n. the sapphire.<BR>—नील-राजि, इस्, f. a dark line,<BR>dark row, dark mass.<BR>—नील-रुद्रोपनिषद् (˚र-<BR>उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—नील-रूपक,<BR>अस्, m. Thespesia Populneoides.<BR>—नील-लोह, अम्,<BR>n. blue steel.<BR>—नील-लोहित, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-blue<BR>mixed with red, purple, of a purple colour, dark-red;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Rudra-Śiva; N. of a Kalpa; a<BR>mixture of blue and red, a purple colour; (आ), f. a<BR>species of vegetable (= भूमि-जम्बु); N. of a<BR>goddess, the wife of Śiva.<BR>—नील-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. blackish, dark; (आन्), m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—नील-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, blue-coloured, blue, of a<BR>blue colour; (अस् or अम्), m. n. Grevia Orientalis;<BR>radish.<BR>—नीलवर्ण-शृगाल-वत्, ind. like the blue<BR>jackal.<BR>—नील-वल्ली, f. Vanda Roxburghii.<BR>—नील-<BR>वसन, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing dark-blue or black<BR>garments; (अस्), m. the planet Saturn.<BR>—नील-<BR>वस्त्र, अम्, n. a blue or dark garment, dark-<BR>coloured cloth; (अस्, आ, अम्), dressed in dark or blue<BR>garments; (अस्), m. an epithet of Bala-rāma; (आ),<BR>f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—नील-वानर, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>blue monkey,’ a species of monkey.<BR>—नील-वासस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, dressed in dark-blue clothes; (आस्), m.<BR>the planet Saturn.<BR>—नील-वीज, अस्, m. a species of<BR>tree (= नीलासन).<BR>—नील-वुह्ना, f. Convolvulus<BR>Argenteus.<BR>—नील-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a species of<BR>plant (= वातारि).<BR>—नील-वृन्त, अस्, m. (?), a fan.<BR>—नीलवृन्तक, अम्, n. cotton.<BR>—नील-वृष, अस्,<BR>m. a dark-coloured bull; (आ), f. Solanum Melongena.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0513-c" target="_blank">Page0513-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—नील-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a kind of religious<BR>ceremony.<BR>—नील-शिखण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>black tufts or locks of hair.<BR>—नील-शिग्रु, उस्, m.<BR>Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR>—नील-षण्ड, अस्, m. a<BR>dark-coloured bull at liberty.<BR>—नील-सन्ध्या, f. =<BR>नील-गिरि-कर्णिका, q. v.<BR>—नील-सरस्वती, f., N.<BR>of a goddess (= तारा).<BR>—नीलसरस्वती-मनु, N. of<BR>an incantation or magical formula.<BR>—नील-सिन्दु-<BR>वार, अस्, m. Vitex Negundo.<BR>—नील-स्कन्दा or<BR>नील-स्कन्धा or नील-स्पन्दा, f. the dark Go-<BR>karṇī.<BR>—नील-स्वरूप, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N.<BR>of a metre consisting of four lines of eleven syllables<BR>each.<BR>—नीलाक्ष (˚ल-अक्ष), अस्, m. ‘blue-eyed,’<BR>a goose.<BR>—नीलाङ्कित-दल (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस् or अम्,<BR>m. or n. (?), a species of bulbous plant (= तैल-<BR>कन्द).<BR>—नीलाङ्ग (˚ल-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dark-<BR>bodied, having a dark-coloured or dark-blue body;<BR>(अस्), m. the Indian crane; the blue jay, Coracias<BR>Indica.<BR>—नीलाञ्जन (˚ल-अञ्˚), अम्, n. antimony;<BR>blue vitriol; (आ), f. lightning; (ई), f. a species of<BR>shrub (= कालाञ्जनी).<BR>—नीलाञ्जसा (˚ल-अञ्˚), f.<BR>lightning [cf. नीलाञ्जना]; N. of an Apsaras or<BR>courtezan of Svarga; N. of a river.<BR>—नीलाद्रि (˚ल-<BR>अद्˚), इस्, m. the mountain Nīla.<BR>—नीलाद्रि-कर्-<BR>णिका, f. or नीलापराजिता (˚ल-अप्˚), f. = नील-गिरि-<BR>कर्णिका.<BR>—नीलाब्ज (˚ल-अब्˚), अम्, n. the blue<BR>water-lily, a blue lotus.<BR>—नीलाभ (˚ल-आभा), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, blue-looking, blue; (अस्), m. a cloud; [cf.<BR>नील-भ.]<BR>—नीलाभ्र (˚ल-अभ्˚), अस्, m. a dark<BR>cloud.<BR>—नीलाभ्र-संवृत (˚ल-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>obscured or concealed by dark clouds.<BR>—नीलाम्बर<BR>(˚ल-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dressed in dark-blue cloth,<BR>wearing a blue garment; (अस्), m. a demon, a<BR>goblin; the planet Saturn; an epithet of Bala-rāma;<BR>(अम्), n. black or dark-blue raiment.<BR>—नीलाम्बु-<BR>जन्मन् (˚ल-अम्˚), अ, n. the blue lotus.<BR>—नीलाम्-<BR>लान (˚ल-अम्˚), अस्, m. a species of plant (in Hindī<BR>कालाकोराठा) = दासी = छादन.<BR>—नीलाम्ली (˚ल-<BR>अम्˚), f. a species of shrub.<BR>—नीलारुण (˚ल-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘the dark-red’ or first dawn of day.<BR>—नी-<BR>लालि-कुल-सङ्कुल (˚ल-अल्˚), ‘full of swarms of<BR>blue bees,’ the plant Rosa Glandulifera.<BR>—नीलालु<BR>(˚ल-आलु), उस्, m. a species of bulbous plant (= असि-<BR>तालु).<BR>—नीलाशी, f. the plant Vitex Negundo.<BR>—नी-<BR>लाशोक (˚ल-अश्˚), अस्, m. an Aśoka with blue blos-<BR>soms.<BR>—नीलाश्मन् (˚ल-अश्˚), आ, m. a blue stone, a<BR>sapphire.<BR>—नीलाश्व (˚ल-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a dis-<BR>trict.<BR>—नीलासन (˚ल-अस्˚), अस्, m. a species of tree<BR>(= नील-द्रुम, नील-निर्यासक, &c.).<BR>—नीलासुर<BR>(˚ल-अस्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of the commen-<BR>tary Nava-kaṇḍikā-bhāṣya on Kātyāyana's Śrāddha-<BR>sūtras.<BR>—नीली-राग, अस्, m. an affection which is<BR>unchangeable as the colour of indigo, unalterable<BR>attachment; (अस्, आ, अम्), having the colour of the<BR>indigo plant; ‘as unchangeable as the indigo colour,’<BR>constant in affection; (अस्), m. a firm and constant<BR>friend.<BR>—नीली-सन्धान, अम्, n. fermentation or<BR>maceration of indigo.<BR>—नीलीसन्धान-भाण्ड,<BR>अम्, n. a vessel for steeping indigo, an indigo vat.<BR>—नीलेश्वर (˚ल-ईश्˚), N. of a town on the Mala-<BR>bar shore (Νελκύνδα).<BR>—नीलोत्पल (˚ल-उत्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a blue lotus, the blue water-lily, Nymphæa Cyanea.<BR>—नीलोत्पल-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed or consisting<BR>of blue lotuses.<BR>—नीलोत्पलिन्, ई, m. an epithet of<BR>Mañju-śrī, one of the Jaina saints or teachers.<BR>—नी-<BR>लोद (˚ल-उद), अस्, m., N. of an ocean or river with<BR>blue water.<BR>—नीलोपल (˚ल-उप्˚), अम्, n. a blue<BR>stone, lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलक|नीलकं|नीलकः
नीलक, अस्, आ, अम्, blue, especially an epithet of the<BR>third unknown quantity or of its square; (अस्), m.<BR>the tree Terminalia Tomentosa (= अशन); a species<BR>of bee (?); a species of antelope, A. Picta; a dark-<BR>coloured horse; (इका), f. a species of rank-grow-<BR>ing aquatic plant; = शेफालिका, Nyctanthes Arbor<BR>Tristis; = नीली, the indigo plant; = नील-सिन्दुवार,<BR>a species of medicinal plant; a slight malady, black<BR>and blue marks on the body from bruises &c.; =<BR>नीलिका-काच; N. of a river; (अम्), n. black salt<BR>(= काच-लवण); blue steel; blue vitriol; [cf.<BR>कण्ठ-न्˚, जीन-नीलिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलङ्गु|नीलंगु|नीलंगुः|नीलङ्गुः
नीलङ्गु, उस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. लग्, to go,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">Page0514-a+ 74</a>]<BR>with नि), = नीलाङ्गु, a species of worm growing in<BR>the inside of animals; an insect in general; a large<BR>bee; a species of fly (= भ्रमराली or भम्भ-<BR>राली); a jackal; = प्र-सून or प्र-सूत, a bud (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाङ्गु|नीलांगु|नीलांगुः|नीलाङ्गुः
नीलाङ्गु, उस्, m. = नीलङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाय
नीलाय, Nom. P. A. नीलायति, -ते, &c., to be-<BR>come blue or dark-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिका
नीलिका, see under नीलक, p. 513, col. 3.<BR>—नीलिका-<BR>काच, अस्, m. a disease of the lens or crystalline<BR>humor of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिनी
नीलिनी, f. the indigo plant, Indigofera Tinctoria;<BR>a species with blue blossoms; N. of the wife of<BR>Aja-mīḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिमन्
नीलिमन्, आ, m. blueness, blackness, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव्
नीव् नीव् [cf. rts. तीव्, पीव्, मीव्], cl. 1. P.<BR>नीवति, नीवितुम्, to become fat or cor-<BR>pulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव|नीवः
नीव नीव, अस्, m. a species of tree; [cf.<BR>नीप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवन्
नीवन् नीवन्, आ, m., N. of one of the ten<BR>horses of the Moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवर|नीवरः
नीवर नीवर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>नी), trade, traffic; a trader; a religious mendicant;<BR>a place suitable for the site of a habitation; mud;<BR>(अम्), n. water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवाक|नीवाकः
नीवाक नीवाक, अस्, m. (fr. नि-वच्), the<BR>increased demand for grain in times of dearth;<BR>dearth, scarcity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवार|नीवारः
नीवार नीवार, अस्, m. rice growing wild or<BR>without cultivation; (आस्), m. pl. grains of wild rice;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवारक
नीवारक, अस्, m. rice growing wild or without<BR>cultivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवि|नीविः
नीवि नीवि, इस् and ई, f. (probably fr. rt. व्ये<BR>with नि), a cloth worn round a woman's waist or the<BR>ends of the cloth passed round the loins so as to<BR>hold the whole together; a petticoat; the tie or<BR>encircling band of a woman's drawers; the outer tie<BR>of a packet in which the offerings of a Śūdra at<BR>funeral obsequies are presented; capital, principal,<BR>stock; a stake at play, stake, wager.<BR>—नीवि-भार्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be worn in an apron, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवृत्
नीवृत् नी-वृत्, त्, त्, त्, m. f. n. (fr. वृत् with<BR>नि), any inhabited country, a realm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव्र|नीव्रं
नीव्र नीव्र, अम्, n. the edge of a thatch,<BR>the edge or side of a sloping roof; a thatch, a roof;<BR>a wood; the circumference of a wheel; the constel-<BR>lation Revatī; the moon; [cf. नीध्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीशार|नीशारः
नीशार नी-शार, अस्, m. (fr. शॄ with नि),<BR>a warm cloth or outer garment, a blanket; curtains,<BR>musquito curtains; an outer tent or screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीषह्
नीषह् नी-षह्, आट्, आट्, आट् (fr. सह् with नि),<BR>Ved. overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीहार|नीहारः
नीहार नी-हार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. हृ with नि?),<BR>fog, mist; frost, hoar-frost, heavy dew; evacuation.<BR>—नीहार-कर, अस्, m. ‘dew-maker’ or ‘cold-<BR>rayed,’ the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीहाराय
नीहाराय, Nom. A. नीहारायते, &c., to make<BR>frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु 1. नु, ind. (perhaps related to 1. नव;<BR>cf. नूतन), written नू in Ved. at the beginning of<BR>a verse and frequently in other places. (As an adverb<BR>of time in Ved.), now, still (e. g. नू-च पुरा-च,<BR>both now and heretofore; अस्ति स्विन् नु वीर्यं तत्<BR>-ते, hast thou still that power?). (As an inferential<BR>particle in Ved. often beginning the last sentence of<BR>a hymn), now therefore, now then, therefore, then<BR>(e. g. नू नो रास्व, do thou therefore give us):<BR>(as an introductory particle, or in encouraging, in-<BR>voking, inviting, summoning), now, then, pray,<BR>come then (e. g. अभि नु मा चक्षमीथाः, pray<BR>now [Sāy. quickly] have compassion upon me).<BR>नु is often employed in questions, both in Vedic and<BR>classical Sanskrit, to strengthen an interrogative pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">Page0514-b+ 78</a>]<BR>noun or adverb (e. g. कदा नु, when indeed?<BR>कथं नु, how indeed? क्व नु, where indeed?<BR>कं नु पृच्छामि, whom can I possibly ask?<BR>किं नु स्यात्, what can that possibly be? किं नु<BR>खलु, why in the world?). नु is also used inter-<BR>rogatively in classical Sanskrit, without an interro-<BR>gative pronoun, in sentences of two or more clauses<BR>(e. g. स्वप्नो नु माया नु मति-भ्रमो नु, was<BR>it a dream? or an illusion of magic? or a mental<BR>delusion?). नु also serves as a particle of affirma-<BR>tion, to express ‘indeed,’ ‘certainly,’ ‘surely’ (e. g.<BR>अहं नु अकार्षम्, Yes, I certainly did so), and<BR>often gives emphasis to the word it follows without<BR>being itself translateable, in which way it is frequently<BR>connected in the Veda with other particles (e. g. with<BR>चिद् in चिन् नु; with इद् in इन् नु; with अध in<BR>अध नु; with घ in घा नु, &c.); but in the<BR>Veda नु sometimes means ‘never’ (especially in<BR>the construction नू चित् = never, nevermore; in other<BR>passages it is said to = ‘from this time forward,’ ‘for<BR>ever’). In classical Sanskrit नु is sometimes found<BR>in connection with वा, ‘or;’ and in Rāmāyaṇa II.<BR>72, 27, नु — नु may be translated ‘either’ — ‘or.’<BR>According to native commentators on the Veda नु<BR>often = क्षिप्रम्, quickly. According to native<BR>lexicographers नु is used in the following senses:<BR>पृच्छा, विकल्प, वितर्क, अनुनय, अतीत, अप-<BR>मान, हेतु, अपदेश; [cf. नू-नम्, नू-तन;<BR>Zend नू, ‘just now;’ Gr. νύ, νῡ-νί, νῦν; Lat. num,<BR>nun-c; Goth. nu-h; Old Germ. nu; Slav. nyne,<BR>‘at present.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु 2. नु, उस्, m. a weapon; time; a boat;<BR>(probably only at the end of a comp.; cf. नौ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु 3. नु, cl. 1. A. नवते, &c., to go:<BR>Caus. नावयति, &c., (probably) to move<BR>from a place, remove; (according to a Schol.) to<BR>make new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु 4. नु, cl. 2, or नू, cl. 6. P. नौति, नु-<BR>वति, नुनाव, नविष्यति, नुविष्यति, अना-<BR>वीत्, अनुवीत्, नवितुम्, नुवितुम्, to roar, cry, low,<BR>bray, &c.; to sound; to shout; to exult; to praise,<BR>commend (with acc.): Caus. नावयति, अनूनवत्:<BR>Desid. नुनूषति: Intens. नोनूयते, नोनोति, to<BR>sound loudly, roar, be tumultuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
5. नु, उस्, f. praise, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत|नुतं
नुत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised, commended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुति|नुतिः
नुति, इस्, f. praise, laudation, eulogium, panegyric;<BR>worship, reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत|नूतः
1. नूत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised, eulogized, lauded,<BR>hymned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुड्
नुड् नुड्, cl. 6. P. नुडति, &c., to hurt,<BR>strike, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुद्
नुद् 1. नुद्, cl. 6. P. A. नुदति, -ते, नुनोद,<BR>नुनुदे, नोत्स्यति, -ते, अनौत्सीत्, अनुत्त,<BR>नोत्तुम्, to push, push on, impel, incite, propel, urge<BR>on, push away, drive away, repel, banish; to move,<BR>remove; to throw, shoot, cast, send; to raise, lift up<BR>(Ved.): Caus. नोदयति, -यितुम्, to push on, incite,<BR>excite: Intens. नोनुद्यते, नोनोत्ति, to push or impel<BR>or drive away repeatedly; [cf. Angl. Sax. nyd-ian,<BR>‘to compel;’ a-nydan, ‘to repel;’ niot-an: Goth.<BR>niut-an: perhaps Gr. νύσσα.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत्त|नुत्तः
नुत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, pushed away, despatched, sent,<BR>ordered; (अस्), m. a plant, see लकुच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुद्
2. नुद्, त्, त्, त् (at the end of a comp.), driving<BR>away, removing, rejecting, repelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुद
नुद, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of a comp.), pushing,<BR>impelling, driving away, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुदत्
नुदत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, urging forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुदित
नुदित, अस्, आ, अम्, (ep.) = नुत्त, नुन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुनुत्सु
नुनुत्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of impelling or<BR>inciting or removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुन्न|नुन्नः
नुन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, pushed, propelled; pushed<BR>away; thrown, cast; dismissed, sent, despatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत|नूतः
2. नूत, अस्, आ, अम्, = नुत्त or नुन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतन|नूतनः
नूतन नूतन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. नु and con-<BR>nected with 1. नव, q. v.), new, novel, recent, modern,<BR>fresh, young, (opposed to पूर्व, पुराण, &c.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">Page0514-c+ 78</a>]<BR>present; instantaneous, sudden; curious, strange.<BR>—नूतन-ता, f. or नूतन-त्व, अम्, n. newness,<BR>novelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतनय
नूतनय, Nom. P. नूतनयति, &c., to make<BR>new, renew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत्न|नूत्नः
नूत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, new, fresh, young, recent.<BR>—नूत्न-वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, in the bloom of youth,<BR>in the spring of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूद|नूदः
नूद नूद, अस्, m. the mulberry tree,<BR>Morus Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूनम्
नूनम् नूनम्, ind. (fr. 1. नु), now, at<BR>present (Ved.); just now, just, exactly (Ved.); im-<BR>mediately (Ved.); from this time forward, for<BR>the future (Ved.); now then, therefore (Ved.);<BR>probably, in all probability, perhaps; without doubt,<BR>certainly, assuredly, surely, indeed.<BR>—नून-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. probability; (आत्), ind. in all probability,<BR>probably, indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूपुर|नूपुरं|नूपुरः
नूपुर नूपुर, अस्, अम्, m. n. an ornament<BR>for the toes or ancles or feet, an anklet; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a descendant of Ikṣvāku.<BR>—नूपुर-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, adorned with anklets or foot-ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृ
नृ नृ, ना, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. नी, cf. rt.<BR>नॄ, see Gram. 128. b; the gen. pl. may be नराम्<BR>or नृणाम् in Ved., but generally नॄणाम् in classical<BR>Sanskrit), a leader (said of gods), a man, person, mankind,<BR>people (generally pl.); a piece at chess, &c.; the pin<BR>or gnomon of a sun-dial; (in grammar) a masculine<BR>word; a horse (Ved.); [cf. नर: Zend नर्, नर,<BR>‘a man;’ नैर्य, ‘manly:’ Gr. ἀνήρ, ἠνορ-έη,<BR>ἀγ-ήνωρ, ἄνθρ-ωπο-ς, ‘man's face:’ Sabin. nero,<BR>‘brave;’ ner-io, ‘fortitude:’ Hib. nearth = Welsh<BR>nerth, ‘virtue.’]<BR>—नृ-कुक्कुर, अस्, m. ‘man-dog,’<BR>a dog of a man.<BR>—नृ-केशरिन् or नृ-केसरिन्, ई,<BR>m. a being, half man and half lion; Viṣṇu in his<BR>fourth Ava-tāra as man-lion.<BR>—नृ-ग, अस्, m., N.<BR>of several persons; an old king; a grandson of Ogha-<BR>vat; a son of Uśīnara by Nṛgā (he was ancestor of<BR>the Yaudheyas); a son of Manu; the father of Su-<BR>mati; (आ), f., N. of the wife of Uśīnara and mother<BR>of Nṛga.<BR>—नृग-शाप, अस्, m. ‘the curse of<BR>Nṛga,’ N. of the fiftieth chapter of the Uttara-kāṇḍa<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—नृगाख्यान (˚ग-आख्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘the tale of Nṛga,’ an episode of the Mahā-bh.<BR>Anuśāsana-p. 3452; N. of the twenty-fourth chapter<BR>of the Pārtha Itihāsa-samuccaya.<BR>—नृगोपाख्यान<BR>(˚ग-उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘the episode of Nṛga,’ N. of the<BR>forty-ninth chapter of the Uttara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa.<BR>—नृ-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. seeing or<BR>observing men, (an epithet of the Sun, Savitṛ, Soma,<BR>Agni, &c.); leading or guiding men; living among<BR>men; (Sāy.) seeing men or injuring men; (आस्), m.<BR>‘waiting for men,’ a demon, a Rākṣasa, a goblin.<BR>—नृ-चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, seeing with human eyes;<BR>(उस्), m., N. of a prince, a grandson or son of<BR>Su-nītha.<BR>—नृ-चन्द्र, अस्, m. ‘man-moon,’ N. of<BR>a prince, son of Rantināra.<BR>—नृ-जग्ध, अस्, m.<BR>‘man-eater,’ a cannibal, a Rākṣasa.<BR>—नृ-जल, अम्,<BR>n. human urine.<BR>—नृ-जाति, इस्, f. the human race.<BR>—नृ-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. conquering men; (Sāy.)<BR>conquering leaders; (त्), m., N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—नृ-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most manly.<BR>—नृ-देव, अस्,<BR>m. ‘man-god,’ a god among men, a king.<BR>—नृ-<BR>धर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, acting as a man, doing a man's<BR>duty; (आ), m. a N. of Kuvera; (अ), n. manly<BR>quality or duty.<BR>—नृ-धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>shaken about or stirred by men (as the Soma).<BR>—नृ-नमन, अम्, n. the bending or bowing of<BR>men (?).<BR>—नृ-प, अस्, m. a protector of men, a<BR>warrior, a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—नृप-कन्द,<BR>अस्, m. a species of onion (= राज-पलाण्डु).<BR>—नृ-<BR>प-क्रिया, f. ‘king's act,’ government, dominion.<BR>—नृप-गृह, अम्, n. ‘king's house,’ the habita-<BR>tion of a prince, a palace.<BR>—नृपञ्-जय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of two princes, a son of Su-vīra and a son of<BR>Medhāvin.<BR>—नृ-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of men,’ a<BR>king, prince, sovereign, (also applied to gods); an<BR>epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—नृपति-पथ, अस्, m. (?),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-a" target="_blank">Page0515-a+ 81</a>]<BR>‘king's road,’ royal road, chief street.<BR>—नृपति-वल्-<BR>लभ, अस्, m. ‘king's favourite,’ a species of medi-<BR>cinal plant.<BR>—नृपति-शासन, अम्, n. a king's order,<BR>edict.<BR>—नृ-पत्नी, f., Ved. a king's wife, queen.<BR>—नृप-त्व, अम्, n. royalty, sovereignty, dominion;<BR>नृपत्वं कृ, to reign.<BR>—नृप-दीप, अस्, m.<BR>‘king-lamp,’ a king who is like a lamp.<BR>—नृप-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. the plant Cathartocarpus (Cassia)<BR>Fistula; a species of tree (= राजादनी).<BR>—नृप-<BR>द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, king-hating.<BR>—नृप-नीति, इस्, f. royal<BR>policy, king-craft.<BR>—नृप-प्रिय, अस्, m. a thorny<BR>species of bamboo, Bambusa Spinosa; a variety of Sac-<BR>charum Sara; rice; a species of onion; the mango tree;<BR>(आ), f. the tree Pandanus Odoratissimus; a species of<BR>date tree.<BR>—नृपप्रिय-फला, f. Solanum Melon-<BR>gena.<BR>—नृप-बदर, अस्, m. a species of jujube;<BR>(अम्), n. its fruit.<BR>—नृप-मन्दिर, अम्, n. a<BR>king's residence, a royal palace.<BR>—नृप-माङ्गल्-<BR>यक, अम्, n. Tabernæmontana Coronaria.<BR>—नृप-<BR>मान, अस्, m. (?), music played before kings when<BR>eating or feasting; [cf. नृपाभीर.]<BR>—नृप-<BR>लक्ष्मन्, अ, n. a mark or symbol of a king, any<BR>one of the royal insignia, especially the white<BR>umbrella.<BR>—नृप-लिङ्ग, अम्, n. an emblem or<BR>mark of royalty.<BR>—नृपलिङ्ग-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>assuming the insignia of sovereignty; taking (frau-<BR>dulently) the emblem or marks of the royal or<BR>military caste.<BR>—नृप-वल्लभ, अस्, आ, अम्, dear<BR>to a king; (अस्), m. the friend or favourite of a<BR>king; a species of mango; (आ), f. a king's wife, a<BR>queen; a species of plant.<BR>—नृप-वृक्ष, अस्,<BR>m. = राज-वृक्ष.<BR>—नृप-शासन, अम्, n. a<BR>royal edict.<BR>—नृ-पशु, उस्, m. ‘man-beast,’ a brute<BR>of a man; a man serving as a sacrificial victim.<BR>—नृप-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. the best of kings.<BR>—नृप-संश्रय, अस्, m. seeking the protection<BR>of kings, service of princes.<BR>—नृप-सभ, अम्, n.<BR>an assembly of princes; a royal palace.<BR>—नृप-<BR>सुत, अस्, m. a king's son, a prince; (आ), f. ‘a king's<BR>daughter,’ the musk-rat.<BR>—नृप-स्नुषा, f. the<BR>daughter-in-law of a king.<BR>—नृपांश (˚प-अं˚),<BR>अस्, m. king's share, royal portion (i. e. a sixth, eighth,<BR>or twelfth of grain, a sixth of fruit, a fiftieth of<BR>merchandise &c.), royal revenue.<BR>—नृपाकृष्ट<BR>(˚प-आक्˚), a particular favourable position of the<BR>pieces in the game Catur-aṅga (a kind of chess).<BR>—नृपाङ्गण and नृपाङ्गन (˚प-अङ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a royal court.<BR>—नृ-पाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. giving<BR>drink to men.<BR>—नृ-पातृ, ता, m., Ved. the pro-<BR>tector of men.<BR>—नृपात्मज (˚प-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of royal birth; (अस्), m. a king's son, a prince; (आ),<BR>f. a king's daughter, a princess; a bitter gourd.<BR>—नृपाधम (˚प-अध्˚), अस्, m. a bad king.<BR>—नृपाध्वर (˚प-अध्˚), अस्, m. a sort of<BR>sacrifice (the Rāja-sūya) held by a lord paramount<BR>in which all the offices are performed by tributary<BR>princes.<BR>—नृपानुचर (˚प-अन्˚), अस्, m. a king's<BR>attendant, a minister.<BR>—नृपान्न (˚प-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘royal rice,’ a sort of rice.<BR>—नृपान्यत्व (˚प-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. change of government.<BR>—नृपाभीर<BR>(˚प-आभ्˚), अम्, n. music played at the royal meals.<BR>—नृपामय (˚प-आम्˚), अस्, m. ‘king's disease or<BR>evil,’ consumption.<BR>—नृ-पाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>protecting men; (Sāy.) to be drunk by the leaders or<BR>gods, or to be protected by the leaders of the sacrifice.<BR>—नृ-पाल, अस्, m. ‘protector of men,’ a king.<BR>—नृपालय (˚प-आल्˚), अस्, m. a king's residence,<BR>a palace.<BR>—नृपावर्त (˚प-आव्˚), अम्, n. a kind<BR>of gem (= राजावर्त).<BR>—नृपासन (˚प-आस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the seat of a king, a throne, a chair of state.<BR>—नृपास्पद (˚प-आस्˚), अम्, n. a king's resi-<BR>dence, a palace.<BR>—नृपाह्वय (˚प-आह्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a species of onion (= राज-पलाण्डु).<BR>—नृ-पीति,<BR>इस्, f., Ved. the protection of men.<BR>—नृपेच्छा<BR>(˚प-इच्˚), f. the royal pleasure.<BR>—नृ-पेशस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. (according to Sāy. f.), ‘man-shaped,’ having<BR>the form of men; (probably) formed or decorated<BR>by men.<BR>—नृपोचित (˚प-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, suited<BR>to a king, kingly, princely; (अस्), m. a species of<BR>bean (= राज-माष).<BR>—नृ-बाहु, उस्, m., Ved.<BR>a man's arm.<BR>—नृ-भर्तृ, ता, m. ‘lord of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-b" target="_blank">Page0515-b+ 81</a>]<BR>men,’ a prince, sovereign.<BR>—नृ-मणस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. propitious or well-disposed towards men,<BR>honoured by men; epithet of Indra; (Sāy.) having<BR>the mind turned towards men.<BR>—नृमणस्य,<BR>Nom. A. नृमणस्यते, Ved. to be friendly or<BR>propitious to men.<BR>—नृ-मणि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>demon said to seize on children; [cf. ग्रह.]<BR>—नृ-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in men; (आन्),<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—नृ-मर, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘man-<BR>destroying,’ killing men.<BR>—नृ-मांस, अम्, n. the<BR>flesh of men.<BR>—नृ-मादन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>exhilarating or gladdening men.<BR>—नृ-मिथुन,<BR>अम्, n. the sign of the zodiac Gemini.<BR>—नृ-मेघ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘man-cloud,’ a man compared to a cloud or<BR>who has qualities like that of a cloud yielding rain.<BR>—नृ-मेध, अस्, m. ‘man-sacrifice’ [cf. नृ-यज्ञ],<BR>N. of a man, an Āṅgirasa and author of two hymns<BR>of the Ṛg-veda.<BR>—नृ-यज्ञ, अस्, m. ‘man-offer-<BR>ing,’ the sacrifice to be offered to men, i. e. hospi-<BR>tality.<BR>—नृ-युग्म, अम्, n. the sign of the zodiac<BR>Gemini.<BR>—नृ-लोक, अस्, m. the world of men, the<BR>earth.<BR>—१. नृ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having men,<BR>manly, belonging to men, fit for men, consisting of<BR>men, accompanied by men.<BR>—२. नृ-वत्, ind., Ved.<BR>like a man, in a manly way, strongly, powerfully,<BR>bravely; in abundance.<BR>—नृवत्-सखि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>having manly companions.<BR>—नृ-वराह, अस्, m.<BR>‘man-boar,’ Viṣṇu in his boar incarnation (with<BR>the figure of a man and the head of the wild boar).<BR>—नृ-वाहण, अस्, आ, अम्, or नृ-वाहस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. carrying or bearing men; (Sāy.) conveying<BR>leaders or chiefs (i. e. the Aśvins).<BR>—नृ-वीर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘man-hero,’ a hero of a man, a hero among<BR>men.<BR>—नृ-वेष्टन, अस्, आ, अम्, encircled with<BR>(the bones of) men; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—नृ-शंस, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or praised<BR>by men (Ved.); hurting or injuring men, malicious,<BR>noxious, cruel, wicked, hurtful, injurious to mankind,<BR>mischievous, base, destructive; [cf. Zend nairya<BR>śaṅgho.]<BR>—नृशंस-ता, f. mischievousness, mali-<BR>ciousness, vileness, baseness.<BR>—नृशंस-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, malicious, vile.<BR>—नृशंस-वृत्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, practising mischief.<BR>—नृशंस्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>malicious, mischievous, vile; (अम्), n. injury to<BR>man, maliciousness, mischievousness, vileness.<BR>—नृ-<BR>शृङ्ग, अम्, n. ‘man's horn,’ any chimerical or<BR>impossible thing.<BR>—नृ-षद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. dwelling<BR>among men, (in some passages applied to चैतन्य,<BR>consciousness, or बुद्धि, understanding); (त्), m.,<BR>N. of the father of Kaṇva; [cf. नार्षद.]<BR>—नृ-<BR>षदन, अम्, n., Ved. an assemblage of men,<BR>residence of men; (Sāy.) the hall of sacrifice, the<BR>receptacle of oblations, the house of the sacrificing<BR>priest.<BR>—नृ-षद्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, or नृ-षद्मन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, Ved. sitting or living among men.<BR>—नृ-<BR>षह् or नृ-षाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. overpowering or<BR>overcoming men.<BR>—नृ-षह्य or नृ-षाह्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. overpowering men; (Sāy.) to be borne<BR>by men; (अम्), n. the overpowering of men; battle<BR>(as to be borne by men).<BR>—नृ-षा, आस्, आस्, अम्<BR>(fr. नृ + सा = सन्), Ved. granting or procuring<BR>men.<BR>—नृ-षाच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. serving men,<BR>friendly or benevolent to men; an epithet of the<BR>Maruts.<BR>—नृ-षाति, इस्, f., Ved. ‘capturing or<BR>making spoil of men,’ i. e. battle, (in Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>27, 1, नृ-षाता is Ved. loc., but according to Sāy.<BR>it is nom. c. of नृ-षातृ, benefactor of men.)<BR>—नृ-षूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. impelled or incited<BR>by men.<BR>—नृ-सिंह, अस्, m. ‘man-lion,’ a lion<BR>among men, a chief, a noble, a great or illustrious<BR>man; Viṣṇu in his fourth Ava-tāra or incarnation<BR>in the shape of a man with the head and claws of a<BR>lion [cf. नर-सिंह]; a kind of coitus; N. of<BR>several men.<BR>—नृसिंह-कवच, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—नृसिंह-चतुर्दशी,<BR>f. the fourteenth day in the light half of the month<BR>Vaiśākha (a festival).<BR>—नृसिंह-चम्पू, ऊस्, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—नृसिंह-तापनीय, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—नृसिंहतापनीयो-<BR>पनिषद्-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a commentary on<BR>the preceding Upaniṣad by Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—नृ-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">Page0515-c+ 74</a>]<BR>सिंह-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—नृसिंह-प्रसाद, अस्, m., N. of an author<BR>mentioned in the Śūdra-dharma-tattva.<BR>—नृसिंह-<BR>प्रादुर्भाव, अस्, m. ‘the manifestation of the<BR>man-lion,’ N. of the thirty-ninth to the forty-third<BR>chapter of the Narasiṃha-Purāṇa.<BR>—नृसिंह-भट्ट,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नृसिंह-वन, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a district in the north-west of Madhya-deśa.<BR>—नृसिंह-सरस्वती, m., N. of a commentator<BR>on the Vedānta-sāra.<BR>—नृसिंहाचार्य (˚ह-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—नृसिंहाश्रम (˚ह-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m., N. of the author of the Prayoga-ratna.<BR>—नृसिंहीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Nṛ-siṃha;<BR>N. of a book.<BR>—नृ-सेन, अम्, आ, n. f. an army<BR>of men.<BR>—नृ-सोम, अस्, m. ‘man-moon,’ any<BR>illustrious or great man, a prince or chief.<BR>—नृ-हन्,<BR>आ, घ्नी, अ, Ved. killing men.<BR>—नृ-हरि, इस्, m.<BR>Viṣṇu in his fourth Ava-tāra as the man-lion [cf.<BR>नर-सिंह]; N. of a man.<BR>—न्र्-अस्थि-मालिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, decorated with a garland of human bones;<BR>(ई), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृम्ण|नृम्णः
नृम्ण, अम्, n., Ved. manhood (विर्तुस्), power,<BR>strength, wealth, ability, courage; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>making happy; (अस्), m. ‘giving happiness,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—नृम्ण-वर्धन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. enhancing courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्
नृत् 1. नृत्, cl. 4. P. नृत्यति (ep. also -ते),<BR>ननर्त, नर्त्स्यति and नर्तिष्यति,<BR>अनर्तीत्, नर्तितुम्, to dance; to act on the stage;<BR>represent (as an actor), gesticulate, play: Caus. नर्-<BR>तयति, -यितुम्, to cause to dance: Desid. निनृत्-<BR>सति and निनर्तिषति: Intens. नर्नर्त्ति, नर्-<BR>नृतीति, नरिनर्त्ति, नरिनृतीति, नरीनर्त्ति, नरी-<BR>नृतीति, नरीनृत्यते, to dance about, dance with<BR>vehement gesticulations; (P.) to cause to dance<BR>about or to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्
2. नृत्, त्, f., Ved. dancing, gesticulation, gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृति|नृतिः
नृति, इस्, f. dancing, acting, playing; (perhaps in<BR>Ved.) lovely or grand appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृतु|नृतुः
नृतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. dancing, gesticulating,<BR>lively, active, (generally as an epithet of Indra);<BR>(नृतू, ऊस्), m. a dancer, an actor, a mime; the<BR>earth; a worm; length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्त|नृत्तं
नृत्त, अम्, n. dancing, acting, gesticulation.<BR>—नृत्त-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting in dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्य|नृत्यं
नृत्य, अम्, n. dancing, acting, dance, gesticula-<BR>tion, pantomime.<BR>—नृत्य-गीत-वाद्य, आनि, n. pl.<BR>dancing, singing, and instrumental music.<BR>—नृत्य-<BR>प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of dancing; (अस्), m. a<BR>peacock; (आ), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>on Skanda.<BR>—नृत्य-शाला, f. a dancing-room.<BR>—नृत्य-सर्वस्व, अम्, n. ‘the whole essence of<BR>dancing,’ N. of a work.<BR>—नृत्य-स्थान, अम्, n. a<BR>place for dancing, a dancing-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्यत्
नृत्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपीट
नृपीट नृपीट, अम्, n., Ved. a various<BR>reading (in the Nighaṇṭus) for कृपीट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृमणा
नृमणा नृमणा, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नॄ
नॄ नॄ, cl. 9. P. नृणाति, ननार, &c., to<BR>lead: Caus. नरयति, नारयति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेक्षण
नेक्षण नेक्षण, अम्, n., Ved. a sharp<BR>stick, a spear, a fork or similar cooking implement;<BR>[cf. नीक्षण, मेक्षण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेग
नेग नेग, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school of the<BR>Sāma-veda; [cf. नैगेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजक|नेजकः
नेजक नेजक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. निज्), a<BR>washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजन|नेजनं
नेजन, अम्, n. washing, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजमेष
नेजमेष नेजमेष, अस्, m., N. of a demon<BR>hurtful to children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतव्य
नेतव्य नेतव्य, नेतृ, &c. See p. 511, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्र|नेत्रं
नेत्र नेत्र, नेत्रिक, &c. See p. 511, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेद्
नेद् 1. नेद् or नेत्, ind. (fr. न + इद्, and<BR>regarded in the Pada-pāṭha as two words), Ved. not,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">Page0516-a+ 77</a>]<BR>not indeed (Sāy. = नैव); that not; (see Pāṇ.<BR>VIII. 1, 30; cf. Zend noiḍ, ‘not.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेद्
नेद् 2. नेद् [cf. rt. 1. निद्], cl. 1. P. नेदति,<BR>&c., to censure, blame; to be near; to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदय
नेदय (fr. नेद, see नेदिष्ठ), Nom. P.<BR>नेदयति, &c., to bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदयत्
नेदयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bringing near, approxi-<BR>mating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदिष्ठ|नेदिष्ठं
नेदिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of नेद which is<BR>substituted for अन्तिक, near; probably allied to नद्-<BR>ध fr. rt. 1. नह्), the nearest, next, very near;<BR>(अम्), ind. very nearly, next, in the first place; (आत्),<BR>ind. from the neighbourhood; (अस्), m. Alangium<BR>Hexapetalum; N. of a son of Manu; [cf. Zend<BR>nazdista.]<BR>—नेदिष्ठ-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. the<BR>nearest of all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदिष्ठिन्
नेदिष्ठिन्, ई, इनी, इ, very near, very nearly<BR>related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदीयस्
नेदीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of नेद which<BR>is substituted for अन्तिक), nearer, very near, as<BR>near as possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेन्य
नेन्य नेन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of rt.<BR>1. नी), taking or obtaining frequently (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेप|नेपः
नेप नेप, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. नी),<BR>a family priest; (अम्), n. water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपथ्य|नेपथ्यं
नेपथ्य नेपथ्य, अम्, n. (for नर्-पथ्य, i. e.<BR>नृ-पथ्य?; cf. वेतन for वर्तन), an ornament,<BR>embellishment, decoration, the costume of an actor,<BR>attire, (in this sense said to be also m.); the part<BR>of a stage behind the scenes (or rather behind the<BR>curtain which was stretched across the stage and<BR>served for scenes), the space behind the curtain or<BR>scenes where the decorations were kept and where<BR>the actors attired themselves; the postscenium; the<BR>tiring-room; नेपथ्ये, loc. sing. (a voice) in the<BR>postscenium or behind the scenes, (used in the plays<BR>as a stage-direction, where anything is to be said by<BR>an actor behind the scenes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपाल|नेपालः
नेपाल नेपाल, अस्, m. (said to be con-<BR>tracted fr. नियम-पाल, q. v., the N. of a sage);<BR>N. of a country, Nepal; a species of sugar-cane;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of the people inhabiting Nepal;<BR>(ई), f. red arsenic; the wild date tree or its fruit;<BR>(अम्), n. copper.<BR>—नेपाल-जा, f. or नेपाल-जाता,<BR>f. red arsenic.<BR>—नेपाल-निम्ब, अस्, m. ‘the Nepal<BR>Nimba,’ a species of tree.<BR>—नेपाल-मूलक, अम्,<BR>n. a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपालक|नेपालकं
नेपालक, अम्, n. copper; (इका), f. red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपाल|नैपालः
नैपाल, अस्, ई, अम्, produced &c. in Nepal;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of sugar-cane; the Nepal Nimba,<BR>a species of tree; (ई), f. red arsenic; a species of<BR>plant, Arabian jasmine, Jasminum Zambac and Nyc-<BR>tanthes Arbor Tristis; the indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपालिक|नैपालिकं
नैपालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, produced in or brought<BR>from Nepal; (अम्), n. copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपालीय
नैपालीय, अस्, ई, अम्, produced in or brought<BR>from Nepal.<BR>—नैपालीय-देवता-कल्याण-पञ्च-<BR>विंशतिका, f., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेम|नेमः
नेम नेम, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. नम् with ए<BR>instead of reduplication, but said to be fr. rt. 1. नी;<BR>नेम is one of the सर्वादि or pronominals accord-<BR>ing to Pāṇ. I. 1, 27, but the nom. pl. m. is either<BR>नेमे or नेमास्), Ved. some, a few, several, (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy. नेम = अल्प, कतिपय; नेमे = के-<BR>चने, also = एते, these); the one, the other; half;<BR>(अस्), m. a part, portion; time, period, season; term,<BR>boundary, limit; a fence, enclosure, a boundary wall<BR>or hedge; the foundation of a wall; a hole, a chasm;<BR>fraud, deceit; acting, dancing; evening; a root; food<BR>(Ved.); upper part, above; (अम्), n. a particular<BR>number; [cf. Zend naima.]<BR>—नेम-चन्द्र, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the half moon,’ N. of a prince of Bengal.<BR>—ने-<BR>म-धित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. divided, set at variance;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., scil. सङ्ग्रामाः, battles in which only<BR>some are engaged; (अस्), m., scil. इन्द्रः, the sharer of<BR>half the oblation, the other half going to all the gods;<BR>(see Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 72, 4.)<BR>—नेम-धिति, इस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">Page0516-b+ 75</a>]<BR>f., Ved. battle, conflict, dispute.<BR>—नेम-नाथ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man who is also called Nitya-nātha.<BR>—नेम-साह, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—नेमादित्य<BR>(˚म-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man, father of Trivi-<BR>krama-bhaṭṭa, the author of the Damayantī-kathā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमि|नेमिः
नेमि, इस्, ई, f. the circumference or ring or felly or<BR>outer rim of a wheel; edge, rim; a windlass or frame-<BR>work for the rope of a well; a thunderbolt, a circle or<BR>circumference in general, the earth; (इस्), m. the<BR>plant Dalbergia Ougeinensis; N. of a Daitya; (with<BR>Jainas) N. of the twenty-second Arhat of the present<BR>Ut-sarpiṇī; N. of a Cakra-vartin; a sacred place, as<BR>Mathurā (?).<BR>—नेमि-चक्र, अस्, m. a prince de-<BR>scended from Parīkṣit, who is said to have removed<BR>the capital of India to Kauśāmbi after the inunda-<BR>tion of Hāstina-pura.<BR>—नेमिन्-धर, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमिन्
नेमिन्, ई, m. the tree Dalbergia Ougeinensis;<BR>(with Jainas) N. of the twenty-second Arhat of the<BR>present Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमन्निष्
नेमन्निष् नेमन्न्-इष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. (perhaps)<BR>following guidance?; (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 56, 2), moving reverentially or bearing oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेय
नेय नेय. See p. 511, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेल
नेल नेल, अस्, or नेलु, उस्, or नेवल, अस्, m.<BR>a particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्
नेष् नेष्, cl. 1. A. नेषते, निनेषे, &c.,<BR>to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष
नेष नेष (fr. rt. 1. नी), forming a super-<BR>lative नेष-तम, occurring in the inst. pl. नेष-<BR>तमैस्, used adverbially in Ṛg-veda I. 141, 12, =<BR>with the best guidance, by the most effective means;<BR>(Sāy.) most conducive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेषन्
नेषन्, आ or अ, m. or n. (?), Ved. leading, con-<BR>ducting; (Sāy.) नेषणि = नेतव्ये विषये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्टृ
नेष्टृ, टा, m. one of the chief officiating priests<BR>at a Soma sacrifice, he who leads forward the wife of<BR>the sacrificer and prepares the Surā. In Ṛg-veda I.<BR>15, 3, Neṣṭṛ is said to be another name of Tvaṣṭṛ<BR>from his having assumed upon some occasion the<BR>function of the Neṣṭṛ priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्ट्र
नेष्ट्र, अम्, n. the Soma vessel of the Neṣṭṛ;<BR>the office of the Neṣṭṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्ट्रीय
नेष्ट्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the Neṣṭṛ<BR>priest, relating to him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्ट
नेष्ट नेष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. न + इष्ट), not<BR>wished for, undesired, disagreeable, unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयस
नैःश्रेयस नैःश्रेयस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निः-<BR>श्रेयस), leading to happiness or future beatitude;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a wood in the world of Viṣṇu; N.<BR>of a fabulous forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयसिक
नैःश्रेयसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, leading to happiness,<BR>conducive to future beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःस्नेह्य
नैःस्नेह्य नैःस्नेह्य, अम्, n. (fr. निः-स्नेह),<BR>absence of love, want of affection, coldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःस्व्य|नैःस्व्यं
नैःस्व्य नैःस्व्य, अम्, n. (fr. निः-स्व), ab-<BR>sence of property, destitution, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैक|नैकः
नैक नैक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. न + एक), not<BR>one, more than one, several, manifold, various, nu-<BR>merous, many.<BR>—नैक-चर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, going<BR>about in troops or flocks, gregarious, living in society,<BR>not living alone.<BR>—नैक-दुःख-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>causing many sorrows.<BR>—नैक-दृश्, क्, m., N. of<BR>one of the sons of Viśvā-mitra.<BR>—नैक-पृष्ठ,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—नैक-भावाश्रय<BR>(˚व-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘not abiding in one condition,’<BR>changeable, fickle, unsteady.<BR>—नैक-भेद, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of many kinds, various, multiform, manifold.<BR>—नैक-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, multiform, of various<BR>kinds, various.<BR>—नैक-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, many<BR>coloured, of various colours.<BR>—नैक-शस्त्र-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of a multitude of arrows or of<BR>various missiles.<BR>—नैकात्मन् (˚क-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, of<BR>manifold nature; (आ), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकधा
नैकधा, ind. in many ways, in various ways,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">Page0516-c+ 70</a>]<BR>manifoldly, in many parts, in many directions, on<BR>various sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकशस्
नैकशस्, ind. in great numbers, repeatedly, several<BR>times, often.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकटिक|नैकटिकः
नैकटिक नैकटिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-कट),<BR>near, contiguous, neighbouring, living in the neigh-<BR>bourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकट्य|नैकट्यं
नैकट्य, अम्, n. nearness, proximity, neighbour-<BR>hood, vicinage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकती
नैकती नैकती, f., N. of a village in the<BR>North of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकषेय|नैकषेयः
नैकषेय नैकषेय, अस्, m. a child of<BR>Nikaṣā, a Rākṣasa, fiend, goblin; N. of a race of<BR>Rākṣasas; (also read नैकसेय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकृतिक
नैकृतिक नैकृतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-कृति),<BR>dishonest, wicked, low, vile, morose, harsh spoken;<BR>fallacious, (Manu IV. 196.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैखान्य
नैखान्य नैखान्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि-खान,<BR>see नि-खन्), liable to be buried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगम|नैगमः
नैगम नैगम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-गम), re-<BR>lating to Vedic quotations or Vedic words, relating<BR>or belonging to the Veda or holy writ, occurring in<BR>it, Vedic; (अस्), m. an interpreter of the sacred<BR>writings; an Upaniṣad or portion of the Vedas; a<BR>way, road (?); a means, an expedient; prudent con-<BR>duct; a citizen, a townsman; a trader, a merchant;<BR>N. of an ancient teacher.<BR>—नैगम-काण्ड, N. of<BR>the second part of the Nirukta, or of the fourth, fifth,<BR>and sixth books of that work, where Yāska explains<BR>the Nigamas or Vedic words collected in the fourth<BR>Adhyāya of the Nighaṇṭus, (also called ऐकपदिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगमिक
नैगमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, connected with or peculiar<BR>to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगमेय
नैगमेय नैगमेय, अस्, m. a form of Skanda,<BR>(considered also as his son and play-fellow; cf. नै-<BR>गमेष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगमेष
नैगमेष नैगमेष, अस्, m., N. of a demon<BR>with the head of a ram, (supposed to seize or injure<BR>children.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगुत
नैगुत नैगुत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निगुत्), Ved.<BR>destroying enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगेय
नैगेय नैगेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school<BR>of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैघण्टुक|नैघंटुक|नैघंटुकं
नैघण्टुक नैघण्टुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-<BR>घण्टु, q. v.), mentioned by the way; (अम्), n. ‘a<BR>collection of words,’ N. of the whole five chapters of<BR>the Vedic glossary commented upon by Yāska, but<BR>especially of the first three chapters treating of<BR>synonyms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचाशाख
नैचाशाख नैचाशाख, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नीचा +<BR>शाखा), Ved. belonging to the low branches of the<BR>community, i. e. belonging to the lower orders or<BR>common people; (अम्), n. (perhaps) low or common<BR>people; (Sāy.) N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचिक|नैचिकं
नैचिक नैचिक, अम्, n. the head of an ox;<BR>(ई), f. an excellent cow, a cow exhibiting excellent<BR>marks on her head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचित्य
नैचित्य नैचित्य, अस्, m. a prince of the<BR>Nicitas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचुल
नैचुल नैचुल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-चुल), belong-<BR>ing to or produced by the Barringtonia Acutangula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैज|नैजं
नैज नैज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-ज), own,<BR>one's own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैतन्धव
नैतन्धव नैतन्धव, अस्, m., N. of a place<BR>on the Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैतोश
नैतोश नैतोश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-तोश), Ved.<BR>(perhaps) granting, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्य|नैत्यं
नैत्य नैत्य, अस्, आ (?), अम् (fr. नित्य), con-<BR>tinual, perpetual, constant, regularly repeated; (अम्),<BR>n. eternity, perpetuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यक
नैत्यक, अस्, ई, अम्, to be done always or regu-<BR>larly and not only on certain occasions, (opposed to<BR>नैमित्तिक); regularly recurring, constantly re-<BR>peated; constant, indispensable, obligatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यिक
नैत्यिक, अस्, ई, अम्, invariable, constant, per-<BR>petual, indispensable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदाघ|नैदाघः
नैदाघ नैदाघ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-दाघ),<BR>Ved. peculiar or belonging to the hot season, summer-<BR>like, scorching; (अस्), m. summer time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदाघिक
नैदाघिक or नैदाघीय, अस्, ई, अम्, peculiar<BR>to the summer, summer-like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदान|नैदानः
नैदान नैदान, अस्, m. (fr. नि-दान), an<BR>etymologist (who investigates the sources of words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदानिक|नैदानिकः
नैदानिक, अस्, m. a pathologist (who inquires<BR>into the causes of diseases).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैदेशिक|नैदेशिकः
नैदेशिक नैदेशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-देश),<BR>executing orders, a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैद्र
नैद्र नैद्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-द्रा), sleepy,<BR>soporific, somniferous, relating to or occurring in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैधन
नैधन नैधन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-धन),<BR>subject to death, liable to decay, perishable, relating<BR>to death, causing death; (in astrology with or with-<BR>out गृह) the eighth house, the house of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैधान
नैधान नैधान, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to a<BR>treasure, to a nest, &c.; (ई), f. a boundary where<BR>articles of value are buried and dug up (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैध्रुवि
नैध्रुवि नैध्रुवि, इस्, m. (patronymic fr.<BR>नि-ध्रुव), an epithet of Kāśyapa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैप
नैप नैप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नीप), belonging<BR>or relating &c. to the Nauclea Cadamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपातिक
नैपातिक नैपातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-पात),<BR>only mentioned incidentally or by the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपातिथ
नैपातिथ नैपातिथ, अम्, n. (fr. नीपातिथि),<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपाल|नैपालः
नैपाल नैपाल. See under नेपाल, p. 516.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण|नैपुणं
नैपुण नैपुण or नैपुण्य, अम्, n. (fr. नि-<BR>पुण), dexterity, cleverness, skill; artfulness; expe-<BR>rience, exactness, strictness; anything which requires<BR>skill, a delicate matter; totality, completeness, com-<BR>pletion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैबुक
नैबुक नैबुक, N. of certain rites to be<BR>performed at full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैभृत्य|नैभृत्यं
नैभृत्य नैभृत्य, अम्, n. (fr. नि-भृत),<BR>modesty, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमन्त्रणक|नैमंत्रणक|नैमंत्रणकं
नैमन्त्रणक नैमन्त्रणक, अम्, n. (fr. नि-<BR>मन्त्रण), a banquet, feast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमय|नैमयः
नैमय नैमय, अस्, m. (fr. नि-मय), a<BR>trader, a merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्त|नैमित्तः
नैमित्त नैमित्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-मित्त),<BR>relating to or explanatory of signs, tokens, marks,<BR>prognostics, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिक|नैमित्तिकं|नैमित्तिकः
नैमित्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, produced by any cause;<BR>connected with any particular cause, dependent on an<BR>external cause; (opposed to नित्य), produced by some<BR>cause or by particular and unusual circumstances,<BR>unusual, occasional, accidental; (अस्), m. an astro-<BR>loger, a prophet; (अम्), n. an effect; occasional or<BR>periodical act or rite.<BR>—नैमित्तिक-कर्मन्, अ, n.<BR>or नैमित्तिक-क्रिया, f. an occasional ceremony (as<BR>observed on the birth of a child &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिष
नैमिष नैमिष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-मिष),<BR>momentary, transient, lasting for a twinkling; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a forest and sacred Tīrtha celebrated as the<BR>residence of certain Ṛṣis to whom Sauti related<BR>the Mahā-bhārata (Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 7275, Vana-p.<BR>6079; the district was so called because in it the<BR>sage Gaura-mukha destroyed an army of Asuras in<BR>a twinkling); (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of the<BR>Naimiṣa wood.<BR>—नैमिष-कानन, अम्, n. the<BR>Naimiṣa wood.<BR>—नैमिषारण्य (˚ष-अर्˚), अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">Page0517-b+ 69</a>]<BR>n. the Naimiṣa forest.<BR>—नैमिषारण्य-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषायन
नैमिषायन, अस्, ई, अम्, living in the Naimiṣa<BR>forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषीय|नैमिषीयः
नैमिषीय, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of the<BR>Naimiṣa forest; (अस्, आ, अम्), relating to the Nai-<BR>misha forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषेय|नैमिषेयः
नैमिषेय, अस्, ई, अम्, living in the Naimiṣa<BR>forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमेय|नैमेयः
नैमेय नैमेय, अस्, m. barter, exchange<BR>(= नि-मय under नि-मे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैम्ब
नैम्ब नैम्ब, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निम्ब), relating<BR>to the Azadirachta Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयग्रोध|नैयग्रोधं
नैयग्रोध नैयग्रोध or नैय्यग्रोध, अस्,<BR>ई, अम् (fr. न्यग्-रोध), belonging to or made of<BR>the Ficus Indica or Indian fig-tree; (अम्), n. the<BR>fruit of the Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयङ्कव|नैयङ्कवं
नैयङ्कव नैयङ्कव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. न्य्-अङ्कु),<BR>belonging to or coming from the antelope called<BR>Nyaṅku, made of its skin, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयत्य|नैयत्यं
नैयत्य नैयत्य, अम्, n. (fr. नि-यत), re-<BR>straint, self-command, self-government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयमिक
नैयमिक नैयमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-यम),<BR>according to rule, conformable to precept, regular,<BR>enjoined; (अम्), n. regularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयाय
नैयाय नैयाय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. न्य्-आय),<BR>treating of the Nyāya philosophy (q. v.), explaining<BR>it, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयायिक|नैयायिकः
नैयायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, knowing the Nyāya<BR>philosophy, knowing the laws of logic; (अस्), m. a<BR>dialectician, logician (especially a follower of the<BR>Nyāya philosophy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरञ्जना
नैरञ्जना नैरञ्जना, f. (fr. निर्-अञ्जन), N.<BR>of a river falling into the Gaṅgā in Magadha (now<BR>called Niladyan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरन्तर्य|नैरंतर्य|नैरंतर्यं|नैरन्तर्य्य|नैरन्तर्य्यं
नैरन्तर्य नैरन्तर्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-अन्तर),<BR>absence of interruption or interval, uninterruptedness,<BR>close succession, continuousness, contiguity, closeness,<BR>compactness; (एण), ind. without interval or inter-<BR>ruption, constantly, incessantly, uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरपेक्ष्य|नैरपेक्ष्यं
नैरपेक्ष्य नैरपेक्ष्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-<BR>अपेक्ष), disregard, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरयिक|नैरयिकः
नैरयिक नैरयिक, अस्, m. (fr. निर्-अय), an<BR>inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरर्थ्य|नैरर्थ्यं
नैरर्थ्य नैरर्थ्य, अम्, n. meaninglessness,<BR>senselessness, nonsense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैराश्य|नैराश्यं
नैराश्य नैराश्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-आश),<BR>hopelessness, despair; the absence of wish or expect-<BR>ation, non-expectancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरास्य
नैरास्य नैरास्य, अस्, m. (fr. निर्-आस), N.<BR>of a magical formula pronounced over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्त|नैरुक्तं|नैरुक्तः
नैरुक्त नैरुक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निर्-उक्त),<BR>relating to the Nirukta (q. v.), explaining it; resting<BR>on etymology, explained etymologically; (अस्), m.<BR>one who knows the etymology or true derivation<BR>of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्तिक|नैरुक्तिकः
नैरुक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who knows the<BR>etymology or radical meaning of words, an etymo-<BR>logist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुज्य|नैरुज्यं
नैरुज्य नैरुज्य, अम्, n. (fr. नी-रुज), health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरूहिक
नैरूहिक नैरूहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. निर्-<BR>ऊह), purging, cleaning out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृत|नैरृतः
नैरृत नैरृत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निर्-ऋति), be-<BR>longing &c. to Nir-ṛti; south-western; belonging to<BR>the Rākṣasas; relating to the lunar mansion Nairṛta<BR>(Mūla); (अस्), m., N. of the ruler of the south-west<BR>quarter; a child or offspring of Nir-ṛti, a demon,<BR>imp, goblin, Rākṣasa; N. of a Rudra; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā; (with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">Page0517-c+ 69</a>]<BR>or without दिश्) the south-west quarter; (अम्), n.<BR>the lunar mansion Mūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृति
नैरृति, इस्, m., N. of a demon, a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृतेय
नैरृतेय, अस्, ई, अम्, descended from Nir-ṛti,<BR>belonging to or connected with Nir-ṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृत्य
नैरृत्य, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Nir-ṛti; south-<BR>western; a sacrifice offered to Nir-ṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्गन्ध्य
नैर्गन्ध्य नैर्गन्ध्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-गन्-<BR>ध), absence of smell or odour, inodorousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्गुण्य|नैर्गुण्यं
नैर्गुण्य नैर्गुण्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-गुण),<BR>absence of qualities or properties; freedom from<BR>qualities; want of excellencies; absence of good<BR>qualities; (अस्, ई, अम्), having no connection with<BR>qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्घृण्य|नैर्घृण्यं
नैर्घृण्य नैर्घृण्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-घृण),<BR>pitilessness, unmercifulness, cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्दश्य
नैर्दश्य नैर्दश्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-दश),<BR>getting over the critical period of the first ten days<BR>(of a new-born child), surmounting any dangerous<BR>time or bad influence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्देशिक|नैर्देशिकः
नैर्देशिक नैर्देशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, servant,<BR>servile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्बाध्य
नैर्बाध्य नैर्बाध्य (fr. निर्-बाध), Ved.<BR>(with हविस्) a sort of oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्मल्य|नैर्मल्यं|नैर्म्मल्यं
नैर्मल्य नैर्मल्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-मल),<BR>stainlessness, spotlessness (physical and moral), clean-<BR>ness, purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्लज्ज्य|नैर्लज्ज्यं
नैर्लज्ज्य नैर्लज्ज्य, अम्, n. (fr. निर्-लज्ज),<BR>shamelessness, impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्वाहिक
नैर्वाहिक नैर्वाहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निर्-<BR>वाह), conducting or leading out, carrying (water<BR>&c.) out; (with द्वार) a sluice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्हस्त
नैर्हस्त नैर्हस्त (fr. निर्-हस्त), Ved. ‘in-<BR>tended for handless demons,’ N. of a particular<BR>magical missile weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैल्य|नैल्यं
नैल्य नैल्य, अम्, n. (fr. नील), blueness,<BR>darkness of colour, blackness, dark-blue (the colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवसंज्ञानासंज्ञायतन
नैवसंज्ञानासंज्ञायतन नैवसञ्ज्ञानासञ्ज्ञा-<BR>यतन, अम्, n. a place (आयतन) where there is<BR>no (न-एव) thinking (सञ्ज्ञान) and no (न) not-<BR>thinking (अ-सञ्ज्ञा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवसञ्ज्ञासमाधि|नैवसंज्ञासमाधि
नैव-सञ्ज्ञा-समाधि, इस्, m. meditation in<BR>which there is no reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवार
नैवार नैवार, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नीवार), con-<BR>sisting in or made of wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैविड्य|नैविड्यं
नैविड्य नैविड्य, अम्, n. (fr. नि-विड), close-<BR>ness, denseness, compactness, thickness; substance;<BR>a prolonged note or continuous sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैविद
नैविद नैविद, अस्, ई, अम्, having a Ni-<BR>vid (q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेद्य|नैवेद्यं
नैवेद्य नैवेद्य, अम्, n. (fr. नि-वेद्य), an<BR>offering of eatables presented to a deity or idol<BR>(which may afterwards be distributed to his ministers<BR>or worshippers, especially if presented to any form<BR>of Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेशिक|नैवेशिकं
नैवेशिक नैवेशिक, अम्, n. (fr. नि-वेश),<BR>any vessel or implement belonging to the furniture<BR>of a house; a present to a Brāhman householder, a<BR>girl so given, or ornaments with her, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश|नैशं
नैश नैश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निशा), nocturnal,<BR>nightly, relating to the night; a person &c. doing<BR>anything by night; done at night; to be observed<BR>by night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशाकर
नैशाकर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निशा-कर), caused by<BR>or belonging to the moon, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैशिक|नैशिकं
नैशिक, अस्, ई, अम्, nocturnal, happening at night,<BR>obtained in one night, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चल्य|नैश्चल्यं
नैश्चल्य नैश्चल्य, अम्, n. fixedness, fixity,<BR>immovableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चित्य|नैश्चित्यं
नैश्चित्य नैश्चित्य, अम्, n. (fr. निश्-चित), de-<BR>termination, certainty; a fixed ceremony or festival<BR>(as a birth, investiture, marriage, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चिन्त्य
नैश्चिन्त्य नैश्चिन्त्य, अम्, n. (fr. निश्-चिन्त),<BR>freedom from anxiety, absence of care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषदिक
नैषदिक नैषदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-षद्),<BR>sitting, (not lying down.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषध|नैषधः
नैषध नैषध, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>Niṣadha; (अस्), m. a prince of the Niṣadhas,<BR>especially an epithet of Nala; (आस्), m. pl., N. of the<BR>people of Niṣadha; a species of plant used as food;<BR>(अम्), n. or नैषध-चरित, अम्, n., N. of an<BR>artificial epic poem by Śrī-harṣa, treating of Nala's<BR>adventures.<BR>—नैषधचरित-भाव-द्योतनिका,<BR>f. ‘an explanation of the meaning of the Naiṣadha-<BR>carita,’ N. of a commentary on the preceding poem.<BR>—नैषधान्वेषण (˚ध-अन्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>seeking or searching for Naiṣadha, i. e. Nala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषधीय
नैषधीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Nala Nai-<BR>ṣadha; (अम्), n. (with or without चरित) N. of<BR>an artificial epic poem on Nala's adventures by<BR>Śrī-harṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषध्य
नैषध्य, अस्, ई, अम्, peculiar or belonging<BR>to the Niṣadhas; (अस्), m. a prince of the Ni-<BR>ṣadhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषिध
नैषिध, अस्, m. an epithet of Naḍa, (an earlier<BR>form of नैषध above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषाद
नैषाद नैषाद, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to<BR>the Niṣādas; (अस्), m. a Niṣāda; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>Niṣāda people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषादि
नैषादि, इस्, m. a prince of the Niṣādas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कर्म्य|नैष्कर्म्यं
नैष्कर्म्य नैष्कर्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. निष्-कर्-<BR>मन्), idleness, inactivity; abstinence or exemption<BR>from acts or their consequences; the salvation obtained<BR>by abstraction in opposition to that obtained by<BR>works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कशतिक
नैष्कशतिक नैष्कशतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>निष्क-शत), worth a hundred Niṣkas, bought<BR>with them, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कसहस्रिक
नैष्कसहस्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निष्क-स-<BR>हस्र), worth a thousand Niṣkas, bought with<BR>them, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किक|नैष्किकः
नैष्किक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निष्क), bought with a<BR>Niṣka, made of a Niṣka, &c.; (अस्), m. a Mint-<BR>master, superintendent of a Mint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किञ्चन्य|नैष्किंचन्य|नैष्किंचन्यं
नैष्किञ्चन्य नैष्किञ्चन्य, अम्, n. (fr. निष्-<BR>किञ्चन), absence of property, poverty, destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कृतिक
नैष्कृतिक नैष्कृतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, acting<BR>wickedly, wicked, malignant, (probably incorrect for<BR>नैकृतिक); free from occupation, disengaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्क्रमण|नैष्क्रमणं
नैष्क्रमण नैष्क्रमण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. निष्-<BR>क्रमण), any oblation offered or rite performed<BR>when a new-born child is taken out of the house for<BR>the first time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक नैष्ठिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-ष्ठा),<BR>forming the end or conclusion, final, last; conclusive,<BR>definitive, decided, accomplished, fixed, firm, con-<BR>stant; highest, perfect, complete; completely versed<BR>in or familiar with conversant; vowing perpetual<BR>abstinence and chastity; belonging to the character<BR>or office of a perpetual student; (अस्), m. a perpetual<BR>religious student or Brāhman who continues with his<BR>spiritual preceptor even after the prescribed term of<BR>study is expired and observes the vow of chastity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठ्य|नैष्ठ्यं
नैष्ठ्य, अम्, n. constancy, steady adherence to<BR>rule, firm belief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठुर्य|नैष्ठुर्यं|नैष्ठुर्य्य
नैष्ठुर्य नैष्ठुर्य, अम्, n. (fr. नि-ष्ठुर),<BR>severity, cruelty, coarseness, harshness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्णिह्य
नैष्णिह्य नैष्णिह्य, अम्, n. (apparently fr.<BR>a form नि-ष्णिह् = निः-स्निह्), getting rid of, freeing<BR>one's self from anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्फल्य
नैष्फल्य नैष्फल्य, अम्, n. (fr. निष्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">Page0518-b+ 73</a>]<BR>फल), unfruitfulness, fruitlessness, absence of fruit<BR>or effect, barrenness, unprofitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैसर्गिक|नैसर्गिकः
नैसर्गिक नैसर्गिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. नि-सर्ग),<BR>natural, innate, inherent, constitutional, original;<BR>(with Buddhists) cast off, put off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैसर्प
नैसर्प नैसर्प, अस्, m. (fr. an unused form<BR>नि-सर्प), N. of one of the nine treasures (with Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैस्त्रिंशिक|नैस्त्रिंशिकः
नैस्त्रिंशिक नैस्त्रिंशिक, अस्, m. (fr. निस्-<BR>त्रिंश), a swordsman, a soldier armed with a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नो
नो नो, ind. (fr. न-उ), and not (Ved.); not,<BR>no (for न, but in epic poetry and later literature<BR>नो is generally only used for न to suit the verse).<BR>नो चेत्, if not; otherwise, else, unless; नो वा, or not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोत्
नोत् नोत् or नोद्, ind., Ved. almost, nearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोदन|नोदनं
नोदन नोदन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. नुद्), push-<BR>ing, impelling, driving away, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोदिन्
नोदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, impelling, driving away, re-<BR>moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोद्य
नोद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be impelled or driven away<BR>or removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधस्
नोधस् नोधस्, आस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 4.<BR>नु), N. of a Ṛṣi with the epithet Gautama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधा
नोधा नोधा, ind. (contracted fr. नव-<BR>धा), ninefold, in nine parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोपस्थातृ
नोपस्थातृ नोपस्थातृ (न-उप्˚), ता, त्री, तृ,<BR>not at hand, absent, remote, far off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ 1. नौ, the alternative form for the<BR>acc., dat., and gen. of the 1st pers. pron., see अस्मद्.<BR>नौ is an enclitic in the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ 2. नौ, नौस्, f. (fr. rt. 4. नु), Ved.<BR>speech; [cf. नविष्टि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ 3. नौ, नौस्, f. (probably fr. rt. स्नु,<BR>but said to be fr. rt. 1. नुद्; in Ṛg-veda 1. 97, 8,<BR>नावया is Vedic inst. for नावा), a ship, a boat, a<BR>vessel; (in astrology) N. of a peculiar appearance on<BR>the moon; N. of a constellation; [cf. Gr. ναῦς,<BR>ναύ-τη-ς, ναυ-τίλο-ς, ναυ-τίλλο-μαι, ναῦ-λο-ν,<BR>ναῦ-σθ-λο-ν, ναυ-τία, ναυ-σία, ναυ-τιά-ω, ναυ-σιά-ω;<BR>Lat. nāvis, nau-ta, nāvita, nāv-igare, nav-ig-<BR>iu-m; Old Germ. nacho; Angl. Sax. naca; Bavarian<BR>naue, ‘a ship;’ Old Iceland. nau-st, ‘a ship station,’<BR>Nōa-tūn; Hib. naoi, noi.]<BR>—नाव्-आकार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, boat-shaped, cymbiform.<BR>—नाव्-आरोह, अस्, m. a<BR>passenger on board ship, a sailor.<BR>—नौ-कर्णधार,<BR>अस्, m. the steersman of a ship, a helmsman, pilot.<BR>—नौ-कर्णी, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—नौ-कर्मन्, अ, n. ‘boat-<BR>business,’ the occupation or business of a sailor.<BR>—नौ-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going in a ship, a<BR>sailor.<BR>—नौ-जीविक, अस्, m. ‘living in ships or<BR>boats,’ a sailor, boatman.<BR>—नौ-तार्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘passable in a boat,’ navigable, to be traversed<BR>in a vessel.<BR>—नौ-दण्ड, अस्, m. ‘boat-pole,’ an<BR>oar.<BR>—नौ-बन्धन, अम्, n. ‘ship-binding,’ N.<BR>of the highest peak of the Himālayas to which in the<BR>great flood Manu fastened his ship.<BR>—नौ-भू, cl. 1.<BR>P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to be a ship, to have been<BR>made a ship.<BR>—नौ-यान, अम्, n. going in a ship,<BR>navigation.<BR>—नौ-यायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going in a boat<BR>or vessel, a passenger; freight.<BR>—नौ-वाह, अस्, m.<BR>‘ship-conductor,’ a steersman, pilot, captain.<BR>—नौ-<BR>व्यसन, अम्, n. ship-wreck, naufrage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौक
नौक (at the end of an adj. comp.) = 3. नौ; (आ),<BR>f. a small boat or ship; N. of a commentary on the<BR>Mantra-mahodadhi by Mahī-dhara.<BR>—नौकाकृष्ट<BR>(˚का-आक्˚), अम्, n., N. of a favourable position of<BR>the pieces in the game Catur-aṅga; [cf. नृपा-<BR>कृष्ट.]<BR>—नौका-दण्ड, अस्, m. ‘boat-pole,’ an<BR>oar, a paddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौधस
नौधस नौधस, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्
न्यक् न्यक्, न्य्-अक्ष. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोध|न्यग्रोधः
न्यग्रोध न्यग्-रोध. See under 2. न्य्-अञ्च्,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यच्छ|न्यच्छं
न्यच्छ न्यच्छ, अम्, n. a mole or spot upon<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च्|न्यंच्
न्यञ्च् 1. न्य्-अञ्च्, cl. 1. P. A. -अचति or -अञ्-<BR>चति, -अञ्चितुम्, Ved. to bend down, curve down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कृ
न्यक्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make low,<BR>lower, humble, humiliate, degrade, treat with dis-<BR>respect or contempt, slight.<BR>—न्यक्-करण, अम्,<BR>n. the act of lowering or degrading, treating with<BR>disrespect or contempt.<BR>—न्यक्-कार, अस्, m. making<BR>low, humiliation, humbling, contempt, disregard, dis-<BR>respect.<BR>—न्यक्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, humbled, treated<BR>with contempt or contumely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्न
न्य्-अक्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bent down.<BR>—न्यक्-<BR>नाङ्गुलि (˚न-अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having the<BR>fingers bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्ष|न्यक्षं|न्यक्षः
न्य्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. rt. अक्ष्, which may be<BR>connected with rt. अच् = अञ्च्], low, inferior; whole,<BR>entire; (अस्), m. a buffalo; an epithet of Paraśu-<BR>rāma; (अम्), n. the whole; grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भू
न्यग्-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become low<BR>or humble, to humble one's self: Caus. न्यग्-भाव-<BR>यति, to cause to become low, humiliate, treat with<BR>disrespect.<BR>—न्यग्-भाव, अस्, m. humiliation, degra-<BR>dation, debasement, contempt.<BR>—न्यग्-भावन,<BR>अम्, n. humbling, degrading, treating with contempt,<BR>defiling.<BR>—न्यग्-भावयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who<BR>lowers or humbles; humbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्क
न्य्-अङ्क, अस्, m. a particular part of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कु|न्यंकु|न्यंकुः|न्यङ्कुः
न्य्-अङ्कु, उस्, m. a deer, an antelope; N. of a<BR>Muni; of a Cakra-vartin.<BR>—न्यङ्कु-भूरुह, अस्,<BR>m. the tree Calosanthes Indica.<BR>—न्यङ्कु-शिरस्,<BR>scil. ककुभ्, a sort of metre consisting of 11 + 12<BR>+ 4 syllables.<BR>—न्यङ्कु-सारिणी, f., scil. बृहती, f. a<BR>sort of metre, also called उरो-बृहती, consisting of<BR>8 + 12 + 8 + 8 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च्|न्यंच्
2. न्य्-अञ्च्, न्यङ्, नीची, न्यक् [cf. नीच, p. 512],<BR>going downwards, turned or directed downwards, bent<BR>down; lying on the face; low, vile, contemptible,<BR>base; whole, entire; slow, lazy; नीचा, inst. c. on the<BR>ground, (see p. 512, col. 1); (न्यक्), ind. downwards,<BR>down, humbly.<BR>—न्यग्-जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, of a low or<BR>inferior race, low born.<BR>—न्यग्-रोध, अस्, m. (=<BR>न्यक्-रोह, growing downwards), the Indian fig-tree,<BR>Ficus Indica; another tree [cf. शमी]; a fathom,<BR>measured by the arms extended; N. of a son of<BR>Ugra-sena; of a Brāhman, of a monastery, of a village;<BR>(ई or आ), f. Salvinia Cucculata; a medicinal plant<BR>(commonly Mohānā).<BR>—न्यग्रोध-परिमण्डल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being a fathom in circumference; (आ), f.<BR>an elegant woman.<BR>—न्यग्रोध-पाद, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चन|न्यंचन|न्यंचनं
न्य्-अञ्चन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. taking on one's lap;<BR>(ई), f. the lap; (अम्), n. a curve; a hollow, recess;<BR>a hiding-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चित|न्यंचित|न्यञ्चितं
न्य्-अञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or cast down,<BR>bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्ज्|न्यंज्
न्यञ्ज् न्य्-अञ्ज्, cl. 7. P. -अनक्ति (Ved. also<BR>A. -अङ्क्ते), -अञ्जितुम् or -अङ्क्तुम्, to anoint, be-<BR>smear; (A.) to creep in, to conceal or hide one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्त
न्य्-अक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, anointed, smeared; mixed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्ग|न्यंगः|न्यङ्गः
न्य्-अङ्ग, अस्, m. a mark, sign; sort, kind (e. g.<BR>अवभृथ-न्यङ्ग, a sort of Avabhṛtha); (अम्),<BR>n. low abuse (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्जलिका
न्यञ्जलिका न्य्-अञ्जलिका, f. an Añjali which<BR>is directed downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यन्त|न्यन्तः
न्यन्त न्य्-अन्त, m. n. (?), proximity; (एन),<BR>ind., Ved. near, near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यय|न्ययः
न्यय न्य्-अय, अस्, m. (fr. 3. नी, i. e. rt. 5. इ<BR>with नि), destruction, loss, waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्ययन
न्य्-अयन, अम्, n., Ved. entrance or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्ण|न्यर्ण्ण
न्यर्ण न्य्-अर्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. अर्द् or rt.<BR>4. ऋ with नि), dissolved (Ved.); injured; asked,<BR>solicited (?); gone (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्थ
न्यर्थ न्य्-अर्थ, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 4. ऋ with नि),<BR>Ved. destruction, annihilation; (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>VII. 18, 9) not going in the usual course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0518-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्पय
न्यर्पय न्य्-अर्पय, Caus. of न्य्-ऋ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्बुद|न्यर्बुदं
न्यर्बुद न्य्-अर्बुद, अम्, n., Ved. one hundred<BR>millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्बुदि
न्यर्बुदि न्य्-अर्बुदि, इस्, m., N. of a divine<BR>being described as taking an active part in war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यवग्रह|न्यवग्रहः
न्यवग्रह न्य्-अवग्रह, अस्, m. the accentless<BR>vowel at the end of a Pūrva-pada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यवचर्
न्यवचर् न्य्-अव-चर्, cl. 1. P. -चरति, -च-<BR>रितुम्, to enter into, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्
न्यस् न्य्-अस्, cl. 4. P. -अस्यति, -असितुम्, to<BR>throw down, cast down, lay down, set or put down<BR>(with loc., e. g. भूमौ, on the ground); to lay<BR>down, resign, give up (e. g. जीवितं न्य्-अस्, to lay<BR>down one's life); to bring forward, adduce, pro-<BR>pound (as an argument &c.); to lay or put down or<BR>place upon anything (with loc., e. g. चित्रे न्य्-अस्, to<BR>place in a picture, paint, depict; पथि न्य्-अस्, to lay<BR>down on the road, give up an occupation, &c.; शिरस्य्<BR>आज्ञां न्य्-अस्, to place a command on one's head,<BR>i. e. receive a command with due reverence; शापम्<BR>मयि न्यस्यति, he lays a curse upon me); to put<BR>in, place within (with loc.), to deposit with any one<BR>(loc.); to give into any one's keeping, make a de-<BR>posit, intrust, deliver, consign, commit; to settle, fix,<BR>appoint; to support: Caus. न्य्-आसयति, to cause to<BR>put or lay down, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यसन|न्यसनं
न्य्-असन, अम्, n. casting or laying down, de-<BR>positing; delivering, giving up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्त|न्यस्तं
न्य्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or cast down, laid<BR>down, placed in or upon, put in, inserted, applied;<BR>delivered, deposited, consigned; depicted (e. g. चित्र-<BR>न्यस्त, committed to a picture, painted); rested<BR>on, leaning, resting; given up, resigned, set aside.<BR>—न्यस्त-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘laying down the<BR>rod,’ giving up all means of punishment.<BR>—न्यस्त-<BR>देह, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has laid down the body,<BR>dead.<BR>—न्यस्त-शस्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>laid down or resigned his weapons, laying down<BR>arms; unarmed, defenceless; harmless; epithet of<BR>the Manes or deified progenitors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्य
1. न्य्-अस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be deposited; to be ap-<BR>pointed to any office (with loc.); to be delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्य
2. न्य्-अस्य, ind. having put down, having laid<BR>down, having deposited, having given up, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यास|न्यासः
न्य्-आस, अस्, m. putting down, placing, settling,<BR>planting or putting down (the feet), stepping, a<BR>step; depositing; a deposit, pledge; delivering,<BR>intrusting, committing, delivery; putting on colour<BR>&c., painting; writing down, writing, impress, stamp,<BR>mark; giving up, putting off or away, laying aside;<BR>deserting, abandoning; lowering the tone of the<BR>voice; bringing forward, adducing; striking or digging<BR>in (the claws &c.), seizing (with the claws); con-<BR>signing or intrusting anything to the mind; mental<BR>appropriation or assignment of various parts of the<BR>body to tutelary divinities (accompanied with certain<BR>prayers and gesticulations); N. of a commentary on<BR>the Kāśikā-vṛtti by Jinendra.<BR>—न्यास-धारिन्, ई,<BR>m. the holder of a deposit, a mortgagee.<BR>—न्यासा-<BR>पह्नव (˚स-अप्˚), अस्, m. repudiation of a deposit.<BR>—न्यासी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make a deposit, deposit anything with a<BR>person.<BR>—न्यासोद्द्योत (˚स-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>grammatical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासिन्
न्य्-आसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has abandoned all<BR>worldly concerns; (ई), m. a Sannyāsī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यह्न
न्यह्न न्य्-अह्न (?), Ved. the closing day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याकृ
न्याकृ न्य्-आ-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>Ved. to keep back, hold back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याक्य|न्याक्यं
न्याक्य न्याक्य, अम्, n. fried rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याग्रोधमूल
न्याग्रोधमूल न्याग्रोधमूल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>न्यग्रोध-मूल), being or situated at the roots of<BR>the Ficus Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याद|न्यादः
न्याद न्याद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अद् with नि),<BR>eating, feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याधा
न्याधा न्य्-आ-धा, cl. 3. P. -दधाति, -धा-<BR>तुम्, to fix in, place in, appoint; to put down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय|न्यायः
न्याय न्य्-आय, अस्, m. (fr. 3. नी, i. e. rt. 5. इ<BR>with नि), method, way, rule (lit. that to which any-<BR>thing goes back or in which anything goes), model,<BR>manner, system, plan, doctrine, right or fit or suitable<BR>manner, that which is fitting, fitness, propriety,<BR>right, justice, virtue, equity, law, a lawful act; (in<BR>gram.) a general or universal rule, an axiom which<BR>precedes and must be kept in view in the explanation<BR>of special rules; a lawsuit, policy, good government;<BR>decision in a lawsuit, judicial sentence, judgment; a<BR>celebrated system of Hindū philosophy delivered by<BR>Gautama or Gotama in a set of aphorisms divided<BR>into five lectures; the proper way of stating an argu-<BR>ment, logic, logical philosophy; a logical argument,<BR>a complete argument or syllogism (consisting of five<BR>members with the Naiyāyikas, viz. प्रतिज्ञा, हेतु,<BR>उदाहरण, उपनय, निगमन, and of three<BR>members with the Vedāntins); likeness, analogy,<BR>apposite illustration; न्यायेन, in the way of, after<BR>the manner of (e. g. लीला-न्यायेन, by way of sport, as<BR>if in sport; cf. न्याय-तस् below). Placed after a<BR>finite verb न्यायम् is said by Pāṇini (VIII. 1, 27,<BR>57) to express either censure or repetition.<BR>—न्याय-<BR>कल्पलतिका, f., N. of a commentary.<BR>—न्याय-कुसु-<BR>माञ्जलि, इस्, m., N. of the aphorisms of Udayana;<BR>[cf. कुसुमाञ्जलि.]<BR>—न्याय-कोकिल (?), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Buddhist teacher.<BR>—न्याय-कौस्तुभ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a general work on the Nyāya<BR>philosophy.<BR>—न्याय-चूडा-मणि, N. of a confuta-<BR>tion of the Nyāya system of philosophy in favour<BR>of the Vedānta by Mādhava Sarasvatī.<BR>—न्याय-<BR>चूडामणि-प्रभा, f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>preceding work by Caṇḍīśvara.<BR>—न्याय-तस्, ind.<BR>in a fitting manner, as is fitting; suitably, justly, fitly,<BR>according to right or justice.<BR>—न्याय-ता, f. or न्याय-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. fitness, propriety.<BR>—न्याय-द्वार-तार-<BR>क-शास्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—न्याय-<BR>पञ्चानन, अस्, m. an epithet of Jaya-rāma; [cf.<BR>पञ्चानन.]<BR>—न्याय-बिन्दु, N. of a commentary<BR>on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtras by Vaidya-nātha.<BR>—न्याय-<BR>बोधिनी, f., N. of a commentary on the Tarka-<BR>saṅgraha by Go-vardhana Miśra.<BR>—न्याय-भाष्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a commentary on the Nyāya-sūtras<BR>by the Ṛṣi Vātsyāyana.<BR>—न्याय-भास्कर, N. of<BR>a philosophical work.<BR>—न्याय-भूषण, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—न्याय-मकरन्द, N. of a work<BR>on the Nyāya system controverted from the stand-<BR>point of the Vedānta.<BR>—न्याय-माला-विस्तर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an introduction to the study of the<BR>Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR>—न्याय-रत्नमाला, f., N.<BR>of a work on the Mīmāṃsā.<BR>—न्याय-लीलावती, N.<BR>of an elementary treatise on the Nyāya philosophy.<BR>—न्याय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, acting rightly, behaving<BR>properly.<BR>—न्याय-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, well behaved,<BR>acting with propriety.<BR>—न्याय-वागीश, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of Śrī-kṛṣṇa; of Dīkṣita-śrī-kaṇṭha-śarman.<BR>—न्याय-विहित, अस्, आ, अम्, prescribed by rule.<BR>—न्याय-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the philosophical system<BR>of the Nyāya school; logic (as connected with this<BR>school).<BR>—न्याय-सङ्क्षेप, अस्, m. or न्याय-<BR>सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m. or न्याय-सार, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n., N. of certain compendious works on the Nyāya<BR>philosophy.<BR>—न्याय-सारिणी, f. right or fit behaviour;<BR>a woman acting or judging rightly.<BR>—न्याय-सिद्-<BR>धान्त-पञ्चानन, अस्, m. an epithet of Viśva-<BR>nātha.<BR>—न्यायसिद्धान्त-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—न्याय-सूत्र, अम्, n. the aphorisms of the<BR>Nyāya philosophy by Gautama.<BR>—न्यायाचार (˚य-<BR>आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, acting justly, virtuous.<BR>—न्याया-<BR>धार (˚य-आध्˚), अस्, m. ‘receptacle of justice,’ a<BR>term applied to any one who is a model of virtue or<BR>propriety.<BR>—न्यायानुसार-शास्त्र (˚य-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—न्यायामृत (˚य-<BR>अम्˚), अम्, n. ‘nectar of Nyāya,’ N. of a Vedānta<BR>work by Vyāsa Tīrtha Bindu.<BR>—न्यायामृत-त-<BR>रङ्गिनी, f., N. of a commentary on the Nyāyāmṛta<BR>by Rāma Ācārya.<BR>—न्यायार्जित (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, obtained in a regular way.<BR>—न्यायालङ्कार-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">Page0519-c+ 75</a>]<BR>भट्ट (˚य-अल्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Śrī-<BR>govinda; also of Śrī-maheśvara.<BR>—न्यायावली-दी-<BR>धिति (˚य-आव्˚), इस्, f., N. of a commentary on<BR>Jaimini.<BR>—न्यायोपेत (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, accord-<BR>ing to rule, right, admitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायिन्
न्यायिन्, ई, इनी, ई, right, fit; logical, rational.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय्य|न्याय्यं
न्याय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, regular, proper, just, right,<BR>equitable, fit, suitable, adapted, (sometimes giving a<BR>passive sense to the infin.); usual, customary.<BR>—न्याय्-<BR>य-त्व, अम्, n. fitness, suitableness, propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याव्यध्
न्याव्यध् न्य्-आ-व्यध्, cl. 4. P. -विध्यति,<BR>-व्यद्धुम्, to cause to burst forth, let loose, set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यास|न्यासः
न्यास न्य्-आस. See under न्य्-अस्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युङ्ख|न्युंख|न्युङ्खः
न्युङ्ख न्युङ्ख, अस्, m. a kind of Sāman, the<BR>sixfold repetition of the triliteral name of God or<BR>ॐ, [cf. न्यूङ्ख]; (अस्, आ, अम्), proper, right;<BR>pleasing, agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युच्
न्युच् न्य्-उच्, cl. 4. P. -उच्यति, &c., Ved. to<BR>rejoice in, delight in, take pleasure in; (Sāy.) to<BR>assent to, agree to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योचनी
न्य्-ओचनी, f., Ved. (probably) a kind of woman's<BR>ornament; (Sāy.) a female servant or slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योचर
न्य्-ओचर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) belonging<BR>to or fit for a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युत्त
न्युत्त न्य्-उत्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 2. उद् or उन्द्<BR>with नि), dipped in, sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युप्त
न्युप्त न्य्-उप्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. नि-वप्, q. v.),<BR>offered, presented (to the Manes of deceased ancestors).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युप्य
न्य्-उप्य, ind. having offered, having presented<BR>(cakes &c. to the Manes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज्
न्युब्ज् न्य्-उब्ज्, cl. 6. P. -उब्जति, &c., to<BR>bend down, press down, throw down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज|न्युब्जं|न्युब्जः
न्य्-उब्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, turned or bent downwards,<BR>lying on the face or with the face downwards;<BR>looking downwards; bent, crooked; hump-backed,<BR>crooked-backed (as the result of disease); convex;<BR>(अस्), m. the Nyag-rodha tree; a sort of ladle made<BR>of Kuśa grass; (अम्), n. the fruit of the Averrhoa<BR>Carambola; a vessel used at Śrāddhas.<BR>—न्युब्ज-<BR>खड्ग, अस्, m. a crooked sword, a sabre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युष्
न्युष् न्य्-उष् [cf. rt. 1. उष्], cl. 1. P. -ओषति,<BR>&c., Ved. to burn down; (Sāy.) to consume utterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूङ्ख|न्यूंख
न्यूङ्ख न्यूङ्ख, अस्, m. the insertion of the<BR>sound ओ in different places with variety of prosodial<BR>length and accentuation in the recitation of hymns,<BR>(this sound may be repeated any number of times in<BR>the recitation of Mantras, or may be made long,<BR>short, or prolated, or may have different accents.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूङ्खय
न्यूङ्खय, Nom. P. न्यूङ्खयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>insert the Nyūṅkha, (occurring in fut. pass. part.<BR>न्यूङ्खनीय and न्यूङ्ख्य); (A. -ते), to make<BR>a peculiar sound, to growl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यून|न्यूनं
न्यून न्य्-ऊन, अस्, आ, अम् (see ऊन), lessened,<BR>diminished, shortened, made smaller, less, inferior,<BR>deficient, defective, wanting, destitute, deprived of<BR>(e. g. अर्थ-न्यून, deprived of property, destitute<BR>of wealth); imperfect or defective in some organ (e. g.<BR>पाद-न्यून, having a defect in the feet); low, vile,<BR>wicked, despicable, blamable; (अम्), ind. less; (अम्),<BR>n. an euphemistic expression for the vulva.<BR>—न्यून-<BR>ता, f. or न्यून-त्व, अम्, n. inferiority, deficiency,<BR>incompleteness.<BR>—न्यून-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, deficient<BR>in intellect, ignorant, foolish.<BR>—न्यून-पञ्चाशद्-<BR>भाव, अस्, n. ‘having but forty-nine properties of<BR>human nature,’ an idiot.<BR>—न्यूनाक्षर (˚न-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, defective in letters or syllables.<BR>—न्यू-<BR>नाङ्ग (˚न-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, defective in a limb or<BR>organ, maimed, mutilated, imperfect.<BR>—न्यूनाधिक<BR>(˚न-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, less or more, unequal.<BR>—न्यू-<BR>नाधिक-विभाग, अस्, m. unequal partition.<BR>—न्यू-<BR>नेन्द्रिय (˚न-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wanting some organ<BR>or sense, deficient, imperfect (as blind, deaf, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनय
न्यूनय, Nom. P. न्यूनयति, -यितुम्, or<BR>न्यूनी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to lessen, diminish, make less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूह्
न्यूह् न्य्-ऊह् [cf. rt. 2. ऊह्], cl. 1. A. -ओहते<BR>or -ऊहते, Ved. to attend to, observe; (Sāy.) to bear<BR>up or support completely, (as if fr. rt. 1. ऊह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यृ
न्यृ न्य्-ऋ [cf. rt. 4. ऋ], cl. 5. P. -ऋणोति or<BR>-ऋण्वति, &c., Ved. to put or place in; to infuse:<BR>Caus. न्य्-अर्पयति, -यितुम्, to throw down, cast<BR>down, overthrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यृञ्ज्
न्यृञ्ज् न्य्-ऋञ्ज् [cf. rt. 2. ऋञ्ज्], cl. 6. A.<BR>-ऋञ्जते, &c., Ved. to reach, attain, gain, obtain,<BR>win; (Sāy.) to propitiate, befriend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यृष्
न्यृष् न्य्-ऋष् [cf. rt. 2. ऋष्], cl. 6. P.<BR>-ऋषति, &c., Ved. to press down or under, suppress,<BR>hide, cover; to put in; (Sāy.) to attain to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यृष्ट
न्य्-ऋष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, pressed under; (Sāy.)<BR>attained to, gained, endowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्ये
न्ये न्य्-ए (= न्य्-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. न्य्-ऐति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to come or fall into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योकस्
न्योकस् न्य्-ओकस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. belonging<BR>to home or one's native country, domestic, home-<BR>bred; (Sāy.) dwelling in an eternal mansion, having<BR>an eternal abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योचनी
न्योचनी न्य्-ओचनी, न्य्-ओचर. See न्य्-उच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्योजस्
न्योजस् न्य्-ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्रस्थिमालिन्
न्रस्थिमालिन् न्र्-अस्थि-मालिन्. See p. 515,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्वै
न्वै न्वै for नु-वै, ind., Ved. indeed,<BR>really, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प 1. प, the twenty-first consonant of<BR>the Nāgarī alphabet and the first letter of the fifth<BR>or labial class, having the sound of the English प्.<BR>—प-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound प.<BR>—प-<BR>वर्ग, अस्, m. ‘the प् series,’ the labial series of<BR>consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प 2. प, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. पा), (at the<BR>end of a comp.), drinking; [cf. अनेक-प, आज्य-प,<BR>क्षीर-प, &c.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प 3. प, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. पा), (at the<BR>end of a comp.), guarding, protecting, ruling; (आ),<BR>f. guarding, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प 4. प, अस्, m. air, wind; a leaf; an egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंश्
पंश् पंश् or पंस्, cl. 1. and 10. P.<BR>पंशति, पंसति, पंशयति, पंसयति,<BR>&c., to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पकथ
पकथ पकथ, अस्, m., N. of a man with<BR>the patronymic Saubhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्कटी
पक्कटी पक्कटी, f. the tree Thespesia Po-<BR>pulnea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्कण|पक्कणः
पक्कण पक्कण, अस्, m. the hut of a<BR>Cāṇḍāla or of any outcast, the abode of a savage or<BR>barbarian; (incorrectly read पक्वण; cf. पक्वश.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तपौड|पक्तपौडः
पक्तपौड पक्तपौड, अस्, m. a species of<BR>plant (= पञ्च-कृत्य, पञ्च-रक्षक, वर्-<BR>धन; in Hindī = pakhauḍā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तव्य
पक्तव्य पक्तव्य. See rt. 2. पच्, p. 521.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ति|पक्तिः
पक्ति पक्ति, पक्व. See rt. 2. पच्, p. 521.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वश|पक्वशः
पक्वश पक्वश, अस्, m., N. of a barbarous<BR>tribe; a Cāṇḍāla; [cf. पुक्कश, पुक्वस, पक्कण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वापक्वा
पक्वापक्वा पक्वापक्वा, an onomatopoetic<BR>word imitative of the cry of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्
पक्ष् पक्ष् [cf. rt. 2. पश्], cl. 1. 10. P.<BR>पक्षति, पक्षयति, &c., to take, seize,<BR>accept; to take a part or side; [cf. Zend paś, ‘to<BR>bind:’ Gr. πήγ-νυ-μι, ἐ-πάγ-η-ν, πῆγ-μα, πηγ-ό-ς,<BR>πάγ-ο-ς, πάχ-νη, πάγ-η, πάσσ-αλο-ς: Lat. pac-i-<BR>sc-or, pāx, pac-i-o, pang-o, pig-nus, pā-lu-s: Goth.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-b" target="_blank">Page0520-b+ 81</a>]<BR>fah-an, ‘to catch:’ Mod. Germ. fang-en: Old<BR>Germ. fuog-a, ga-fuogi, ‘apt;’ gafag-yan, ‘to<BR>satisfy;’ fah, ‘a shelf:’ Bohem. pás, ‘a girdle;’<BR>pas-mo, ‘yarn.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष|पक्षः
पक्ष, अस्, m. (probably connected with the pre-<BR>ceding, but by some regarded as an unreduplicated<BR>Desid. form of an unused rt. पज्, fr. which पाजस्,<BR>‘strength,’ may be derived; in Uṇādi-s. III. 69. पक्-<BR>ष is derived fr. rt. 1. पण्), a wing, pinion, (in this<BR>sense also अम्, n.); symbolical expression for the<BR>number two; a feather, the feathers on both sides of<BR>an arrow; the flank or side (of a man &c.), the<BR>shoulder; the side of anything (as of a house, car-<BR>riage, the head, hair, &c.); the wing or flank of an<BR>army, &c.; the half of anything; the half of a lunar<BR>month, a fortnight comprising fifteen days, (the half<BR>from new moon to full moon was called पूर्व or<BR>आपूर्यमाण, later शुक्ल or शुद्ध; the other half<BR>was called अपर or अप-क्षीयमाण, later कृष्ण<BR>or तामिस्र; and every half month is divided into<BR>fifteen Tithis, named प्रथमा, द्वितीया, &c.); a<BR>side, party, faction, a partisan, adherent, follower; a<BR>class, multitude, host, set, troop, number of adherents<BR>or friends (e. g. शत्रु-पक्ष, the enemy's side or<BR>[as an adj.] being on the enemy's side; महा-<BR>पक्ष, one who has many adherents; देव-<BR>पक्ष-वराः, the most distinguished adherents of<BR>the gods; पक्ष-सम्मत, approved by a certain<BR>set of people); one of two cases, one side of an<BR>argument, an alternative, (पक्षे, on the other<BR>alternative, on the other hand); a case in general,<BR>a supposition, (पक्षान्तरे, in the other case, on<BR>the other supposition); a thesis, a point under investi-<BR>gation or discussion, a position advanced or argument<BR>to be maintained; (in logic) the subject of a syl-<BR>logism or conclusion or inference; place, position;<BR>supposition, view, notion, idea, opinion (e. g. मु-<BR>ख्यः पक्षः, an excellent idea); state, condition;<BR>(in algebra) a primary division or the side of an<BR>equation in a primary division. According to the<BR>lexicographers the word has also the following mean-<BR>ings: the wall of a house; a wall; an army; favour;<BR>contradiction, opposition, rejoinder, reply; the ash-<BR>pit of a fire-place, a royal elephant; a limb or<BR>member of the body; the feathers of the tail of a<BR>peacock, a tail; proximity, neighbourhood; a brace-<BR>let; purity, perfection. In composition with words<BR>signifying ‘hair,’ पक्ष is said to mean ‘quantity;’<BR>see केश-पक्ष; [cf. पूर्व-प्˚, उत्तर-प्˚, एक-प्˚,<BR>काक-प्˚, कृष्ण-प्˚, &c.: cf. probably Gr. παξ in<BR>ἅπαξ; Goth. fug-ls, ‘a bird;’ Mod. Germ. Vogel;<BR>Lith. panksh-tis; perhaps Lat. passer for paxer.]<BR>—पक्ष-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, moving with or by<BR>means of wings, flying.<BR>—पक्ष-गुप्त, अस्, m.<BR>‘wing-protected,’ a species of bird.<BR>—पक्ष-ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. choosing a party.<BR>—पक्ष-ग्राह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, or पक्ष-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who<BR>chooses a party.<BR>—पक्ष-घात = पक्षाघात,<BR>q. v.<BR>—पक्ष-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, a Tri-śālaka having<BR>no hall towards the west.<BR>—पक्षङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>moving by means of wings, flying.<BR>—पक्ष-चर, अस्,<BR>m. an elephant strayed from the herd; the moon; an<BR>attendant, a constant companion.<BR>—पक्ष-च्छिद्,<BR>त्, m. ‘cutter of the wings’ (of the mountains), an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>—पक्ष-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, or पक्ष-<BR>जन्मन्, आ, आ, अ, produced in a fortnight; (अस् or<BR>आ), m. the moon.<BR>—पक्ष-ता, f. or पक्ष-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. partisanship, alliance; adherence to a party;<BR>the being a part of; the taking up a side or argu-<BR>ment; maintaining or defending a thesis; the essential<BR>nature of a proposition; the being the subject of<BR>a syllogism.<BR>—पक्ष-द्वय, अम्, n. both sides of<BR>an argument, &c.; a month (two fortnights).<BR>—पक्-<BR>ष-द्वार, अम्, n. a side door, an inner or back<BR>door, a private entrance.<BR>—पक्ष-धर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having a side or wing, winged; taking the side<BR>or adhering to the party of any one (gen.); belonging<BR>to any party or faction, siding with any one (gen.);<BR>(अस्), m. a bird; a partisan, adherent; the moon; an<BR>elephant that has strayed from the herd.<BR>—पक्ष-<BR>नाडी, f. a quill.<BR>—पक्ष-पात, अस्, m. ‘falling of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">Page0520-c+ 81</a>]<BR>the feathers,’ the moulting of birds (considered to<BR>proceed from fever); the act of taking the side or<BR>adhering to the party of any one (gen.); siding with<BR>any one (gen.); adopting a side or argument<BR>whether right or wrong, attachment to a party,<BR>partisanship, partiality for (with loc. or gen.); a<BR>partisan, adherent.<BR>—पक्षपात-कृत-स्नेह, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, manifesting party attachment, sympathising.<BR>—पक्षपाति-ता, f. or पक्षपाति-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>partisanship, adherence to a side or party, partiality,<BR>friendship, fellowship, faction, factiousness.<BR>—पक्ष-<BR>पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, taking the side or adhering to the<BR>party (of any one), siding with, favouring a party;<BR>(ई), m. a partisan, friend, adherent, follower.<BR>—पक्-<BR>ष-पालि, इस्, m. a private or back door.<BR>—पक्ष-<BR>पुट, अस्, m. a wing.<BR>—पक्ष-पोषण, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, fostering or favouring a party, factious.<BR>—पक्-<BR>ष-प्रद्योत, अम्, n., N. of a peculiar position of<BR>the hands in dancing.<BR>—पक्ष-बल, अम्, n. strength<BR>of wing.<BR>—पक्ष-भाग, अस्, m. the side or flank,<BR>especially the flank of an elephant.<BR>—पक्ष-भुक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. the course traversed by the sun in a fortnight.<BR>—पक्ष-भेद, अस्, m. distinction between two<BR>sides of an argument; the difference between the two<BR>halves of a lunar month.<BR>—पक्ष-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>the root or articulation of a wing.<BR>—पक्ष-रचना,<BR>f. forming a party or faction.<BR>—पक्ष-वञ्चितक,<BR>अस्, m. a peculiar position of the hands in dancing.<BR>—पक्ष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, winged; having flanks;<BR>having a side or party, firmly adhering to or having<BR>a predilection for any one; belonging to a good<BR>family, of good extraction (?).<BR>—पक्ष-वाद, अस्,<BR>m. expression of opinion, stating a case; ex parte<BR>statement.<BR>—पक्ष-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘whose vehicles<BR>are wings,’ a bird.<BR>—पक्ष-विन्दु, उस्, m., ‘wing-<BR>spot,’ a heron.<BR>—पक्ष-व्यापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, em-<BR>bracing the whole of an argument or thesis.<BR>—पक्-<BR>ष-शस्, ind. by or for half months or fortnights.<BR>—पक्ष-सुन्दर, अस्, m. a species of tree; [cf.<BR>लोध्र.]<BR>—पक्ष-हत, अस्, आ, अम्, paralysed on<BR>one side.<BR>—पक्ष-हर, अस्, m. a bird; (perhaps<BR>a wrong reading for पक्ष-धर, ‘possessing<BR>wings.’)<BR>—पक्ष-होम, अस्, m. (probably) an obla-<BR>tion to be offered every half month.<BR>—पक्षाकार<BR>(˚ष-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wing-shaped.<BR>—पक्षा-<BR>घात (˚ष-आघ्˚), अस्, m. ‘side-stroke,’ paralysis or<BR>palsy of one side, hemiplegia; refutation of an argument<BR>or view.<BR>—पक्षान्त (˚ष-अन्˚), अस्, m. the fifteenth<BR>and last day of either half month, new or full moon;<BR>the end of the wings of an army arranged in the<BR>shape of a bird.<BR>—पक्षान्तर (˚ष-अन्˚), अम्,<BR>n. another side or part, another or different view of<BR>an argument, another supposition.<BR>—पक्षाभास<BR>(˚ष-आभ्˚), अस्, m. a seeming or fallacious argu-<BR>ment, a fallacy, a false plaint.<BR>—पक्षावसर<BR>(˚ष-अव्˚), अस्, m. the last day of either half<BR>month, day of new or full moon.<BR>—पक्षाहति<BR>(˚ष-आह्˚), इस्, f. a stroke with the wings.<BR>—पक्-<BR>षाहार (˚ष-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who eats food<BR>only once in a half month.<BR>—पक्षी-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to make anything<BR>the subject of an argument or syllogism.<BR>—पक्षोद्-<BR>ग्राहिन् (˚ष-उद्˚), ई, इणी, इ, showing partiality,<BR>taking a side or adopting a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षक|पक्षकः
पक्षक, अस्, m. a side door, a private or back<BR>door; a side; a sidesman; an associate, a confederate<BR>or partisan, (at the end of comps. used for पक्ष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षति|पक्षतिः
पक्षति, इस्, f. the root or insertion of a wing, the<BR>pit of a bird's wing; the first day of the half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षस्
पक्षस्, अस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1. पच्), a wing;<BR>the side part of a carriage; the leaf of a door; the<BR>wing of an army; a half, a division; a half month;<BR>the side or shore of a river; a side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षालिका
पक्षालिका, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षालु|पक्षालुः
पक्षालु, उस्, m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षि
पक्षि, इस्, m. (curtailed form for पक्षिन्), a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिन्
पक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, winged, (figuratively) furnished<BR>with wings; taking the side or adhering to the<BR>party (of any one); siding with; (ई), m. a day<BR>with the two nights enclosing it; the bird Garuḍa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">Page0521-a+ 79</a>]<BR>as one of the eighteen attendants of the Sun;<BR>an arrow; an epithet of Śiva; (ई, इणी), m. f. a<BR>bird; (इणी), f. (with or without रात्रि) a night with<BR>the two days enclosing it; the day of full moon;<BR>N. of a Śākinī; [cf. Lith. pauksh-tis, ‘a bird;’<BR>Goth. fug-ls, ‘a bird;’ Angl. Sax. fug-ul; Mod.<BR>Germ. Vogel; probably Lat. passer for paxer.]<BR>—पक्षि-कीट, अस्, m. ‘bird-insect,’ an insect-<BR>like bird, an insignificant species of bird.<BR>—पक्षि-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—पक्षि-पति, इस्, m. ‘the prince of birds,’ an<BR>epithet of Sampāti.<BR>—पक्षिपानीय-शालिका, f. a<BR>trough or reservoir for watering birds, cattle, &c.<BR>—पक्षि-पुङ्गव, अस्, m. ‘a bull among the<BR>birds,’ an epithet of Jaṭāyu.<BR>—पक्षि-प्रवर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the most excellent among the birds,’ an epithet<BR>of Garuḍa.<BR>—पक्षि-बालक, अस्, m. a young bird.<BR>—पक्षि-मृग-ता, f. (fr. पक्षिन् and मृग),<BR>the form or condition of a bird or of a beast.<BR>—पक्षि-राज्, ट्, or पक्षि-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of<BR>the birds,’ an epithet of Garuḍa or of Jaṭāyu.<BR>—पक्-<BR>षि-राज्य, अम्, n. the sovereignty of the feathered<BR>tribes.<BR>—पक्षि-शाला, f. ‘bird-house,’ an aviary, a nest.<BR>—पक्षि-शावक, अस्, m. a young bird.<BR>—पक्षि-<BR>सिंह, अस्, m. ‘lion among the birds,’ an epithet<BR>of Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of Viṣṇu.<BR>—पक्षि-<BR>स्वामिन्, ई, m. ‘lord or master of the birds,’ an<BR>epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—पक्षीन्द्र (˚षि-इन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘prince of the birds,’ an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिल|पक्षिलः
पक्षिल, अस्, m. (with स्वामिन्) an epithet of<BR>the saint Vātsyāyana.<BR>—पक्षिल-स्वामिन्, ई, m. an<BR>epithet of Vātsyāyana who is identified with Cāṇakya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षीय
पक्षीय, अस्, आ, अम् (at the end of a comp.),<BR>belonging to a side, siding with, taking the side<BR>or adhering to the party of any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मन्
पक्ष्मन्, अ, n. an eyelash; the filament of a<BR>flower; the point of a thread, a thin thread; the<BR>leaf of a flower; a wing; a whisker.<BR>—पक्ष्म-<BR>कोप or पक्ष्म-प्रकोप, अस्, m. irritation pro-<BR>duced in the eye by the eyelashes turning inwards<BR>(Entropium).<BR>—पक्ष्माक्ष (˚म-अक्ष), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, having an eyelash or eyelashes in the eye<BR>(suffering from Entropium).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मल
पक्ष्मल, अस्, आ, अम्, having strong or long<BR>eyelashes; having long or thick hair, hairy, shaggy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्य|पक्ष्यः
पक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. descended from Pakṣa<BR>(i. e. according to Sāy. the Sun); changing every half<BR>month; produced or occurring in a fortnight; be-<BR>longing to a side, siding with, taking part with;<BR>lateral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्णु|पक्ष्णुः
पक्ष्णु पक्ष्णु. See p. 522, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मन्
पक्ष्मन् पक्ष्मन्. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क|पंक|पंकं|पंकः|पङ्कः
पङ्क पङ्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. 1. पच् or पञ्च्), mud, mire, dirt, clay; a slough, a<BR>quagmire; ointment, unguent; moral impurity, sin;<BR>[cf. निष्-पङ्क, नील-प्˚.]<BR>—पङ्क-कर्वट, अस्,<BR>m. soft mud, especially such as is left by the retiring<BR>of floods or on the banks of a river, alluvium, a marsh,<BR>a quagmire.<BR>—पङ्क-कीर, अस्, m. an aquatic bird, a<BR>lap-wing.<BR>—पङ्क-क्रीड, अस्, आ, अम्, wallowing or<BR>sporting in mud; (अस्), m. a pig; (also पङ्क-<BR>क्रीडनक, अस्, m.)<BR>—पङ्क-गडक, अस्, m. or<BR>पङ्क-गति, इस्, f. a small fish, Macrognathus Pan-<BR>calus.<BR>—पङ्क-ग्राह, अस्, m. the marine monster<BR>Makara, q. v.<BR>—पङ्क-च्छिद्, त्, m. ‘mud-destroyer,’<BR>Strychnos Potatorum (the fruit of which is used for<BR>purifying foul water).<BR>—पङ्क-ज, अम्, n. ‘mud-<BR>born,’ a species of lotus, Nelumbium Speciosum (or<BR>rather its flower which closes in the evening); (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Brahmā, (incorrect for पङ्कज-<BR>ज, ‘lotus-born’); (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—पङ्कज-जन्मन्, आ, m. ‘sprung from a lotus,’<BR>an epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—पङ्कज-नाभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘having a lotus springing from his navel,’ an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—पङ्क-जन्मन्, अ, n. = पङ्क-<BR>ज.<BR>—पङ्कज-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the leaf of a lotus.<BR>—पङ्कजपत्त्र-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>eyes like lotus-leaves.<BR>—पङ्कजावली (˚ज-आव्˚), f. a<BR>particular metre; [cf. पङ्कावली.]<BR>—पङ्क-जित्, त्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">Page0521-b+ 79</a>]<BR>m., N. of a son of Garuḍa.<BR>—पङ्कजिनी, f. (fr.<BR>पङ्कजिन् which is fr. पङ्क-ज), Nelumbium Spe-<BR>ciosum (the plant itself), a group of such lotuses, a<BR>lotus pool, a pool or pond where the lotus grows or<BR>a place abounding with that flower; the flexible<BR>stalk of a water-lily.<BR>—पङ्क-ता, f. the nature or<BR>property of mud, muddiness.<BR>—पङ्क-दिग्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, besmeared with mud, soiled with dirt.<BR>—पङ्कदिग्ध-शरीर, अस्, m. ‘having a mud-<BR>smeared body,’ N. of a Dānava; (also read as if two<BR>names, पङ्क-दिग्ध and शरीर.)<BR>—पङ्कदिग्-<BR>धाङ्ग (˚ध-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘having mud-smeared<BR>limbs,’ N. of a being attending on Skanda.<BR>—पङ्क-<BR>प्रभा, f. (with Jainas) N. of one of the seven<BR>divisions of hell (where mud or mire takes the place<BR>of light).<BR>—पङ्क-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, sunk in the mire.<BR>—पङ्क-भारक, अस्, आ, अम्, laden with mud,<BR>muddy.<BR>—पङ्क-मज्जन, अम्, n. immersion in<BR>mud.<BR>—पङ्क-मण्डूक, अस्, m. a bivalve conch;<BR>(also wrongly read -मण्डूक.)<BR>—पङ्क-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, full of mud or mire, muddy.<BR>—पङ्क-रुह्,<BR>ट्, or पङ्क-रुह, अम्, n. ‘mud-growing,’ a lotus.<BR>—पङ्क-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, muddy, covered with<BR>mud.<BR>—पङ्क-वास, अस्, m. ‘dwelling in mud,’<BR>a crab.<BR>—पङ्क-शुक्ति, इस्, f. ‘mud-shell,’ a par-<BR>ticular species of muscle or cockle (the stair-case<BR>shell, spinnet shell).<BR>—पङ्क-सूरण, अस्, m. ‘mud-<BR>root,’ the fibrous edible root of a lotus; (also written<BR>पङ्क-शूरण, पङ्क-षूरण.)<BR>—पङ्के-ज,<BR>अम्, n. ‘born in the mud,’ a lotus.<BR>—पङ्के-रुह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘growing in mud,’ a lotus; (अस्), m. the<BR>Indian crane (as a synonym of पुष्कर).<BR>—पङ्के-<BR>शय, अस्, आ, अम्, resting or dwelling in mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कार|पंकार|पंकारः|पङ्कारः
पङ्कार, अस्, m. the aquatic plant Blyxa Oc-<BR>tandra or Vallisneria (= शैवल); the aquatic plant<BR>Trapa Bispinosa (= जल-कुब्जक); a dam, dike,<BR>or raised bank forming a path amidst inundated fields;<BR>stairs, steps, a ladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कावली
पङ्कावली, f. = पङ्कजावली (of which it may<BR>be a contraction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्किन्|पंकिन्
पङ्किन्, ई, इनी, इ (at the end of a comp.), muddy,<BR>filled or covered with mud; [cf. मल-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्किल|पंकिल|पङ्किलः
पङ्किल, अस्, आ, अम्, muddy, dirty, clayey; (अस्),<BR>m. a boat, canoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कण|पंकण|पंकणः|पङ्कणः
पङ्कण पङ्कण, wrong form for पक्कण,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कवारि
पङ्कवारि पङ्क-वारि. See पक्व-वारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्ति|पंक्ति|पंक्तिः|पङ्क्तिः
पङ्क्ति पङ्क्ति, इस्, ई, f. (connected with पञ्-<BR>चन्), a row or line or set of five, a collection of<BR>five, the number five; a sort of fivefold metre con-<BR>sisting of five Pādas of eight syllables each; (in the<BR>later literature) any stanza of four times ten syllables<BR>(or of four lines, each line consisting of ten syllables);<BR>the number ten, (sometimes in comp., cf. रावण-<BR>शिरः-प्˚, पङ्क्ति-ग्रीव, पङ्क्ति-रथ); a line,<BR>range, row, series; a group, flock, troop; a heap;<BR>a row of people sitting down to a meal, a company,<BR>society, assembly, party; a company of persons of<BR>the same caste; the living generation; the earth;<BR>cooking, maturing, (incorrectly for पक्ति); fame,<BR>celebrity (for पक्ति); [cf. अक्षर-प्˚, आस्तार-प्˚,<BR>पद-प्˚, प्रस्तार-प्˚.]<BR>—पङ्क्ति-कण्टक, ‘having<BR>rows of thorns (?),’ a white-flowering Achyranthes.<BR>—पङ्क्ति-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘ten-necked,’ an epithet of<BR>Rāvaṇa; [cf. पङ्क्ति-रथ.]<BR>—पङ्क्ति-चर, अस्,<BR>m. ‘going in lines,’ an osprey.<BR>—पङ्क्ति-दूष or<BR>-दूषक, अस्, आ, अम्, defiling or contaminating any<BR>society or company of persons; (अस्), m. an improper<BR>person with whom to associate, (opposed to पङ्क्ति-<BR>पावन.)<BR>—पङ्क्ति-दोष, अस्, m. a bane of society,<BR>anything which defiles or contaminates a company,<BR>what spoils a society.<BR>—पङ्क्ति-पावन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>purifying a society or company of persons, (opposed<BR>to पङ्क्ति-दूष); (अस्), m. a respectable or emi-<BR>nent person.<BR>—पङ्क्ति-रथ, अस्, m. ‘having ten<BR>chariots,’ a N. of Daśa-ratha, the father of Rāma-<BR>candra.<BR>—पङ्क्ति-राधस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. (a sacri-<BR>fice) containing fivefold gifts; (Sāy.) abounding in<BR>properly presented oblations.<BR>—पङ्क्ति-वीज, अस्, m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">Page0521-c+ 79</a>]<BR>a species of plant (= वर्वूर).<BR>—पङ्क्ती-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, associated in groups.<BR>—पङ्क्त्य्-उत्तर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a Paṅkti at the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिका|पंक्तिका
पङ्क्तिका, f. a row, line, (in अक्षर-पङ्क्तिका,<BR>a row of letters.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गु|पंगु|पङ्गुः
पङ्गु पङ्गु, उस्, ऊस् or वी, उ (perhaps fr.<BR>अप-अङ्ग, said to be connected with rt. 1. खञ्ज्),<BR>lame, crippled, halt, one who has lost his legs, &c.;<BR>(उस्), m. the planet Saturn (as moving slowly); an<BR>epithet of Nirjita-varman.<BR>—पङ्गु-ग्राह, अस्, m.<BR>the sea-monster Makara, q. v. [cf. पङ्क-ग्राह, अस्,]; one<BR>of the signs of the zodiac, see मकर.<BR>—पङ्गु-<BR>ता, f. or पङ्गु-त्व, अम्, n. lameness, deformity,<BR>mutilation.<BR>—पङ्गुत्व-हारिणी, f. a species of shrub<BR>(= शिमृडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुक|पंगुक
पङ्गुक, अस्, आ, अम्, = पङ्गु, lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुल|पंगुल|पङ्गुलः
पङ्गुल, अस्, आ, अम्, lame, crippled; (अस्), m. a<BR>horse of a glassy or silvery white colour; (अम्?),<BR>n. lameness (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्
पच् 1. पच् or पञ्च्, cl. 1. P. A. पचति,<BR>-ते, पञ्चति, -ते, &c., to make clear or<BR>evident: Caus. पञ्चयति, &c., to explain or state<BR>fully, amplify; to spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चा
पञ्चा, f. spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्
पच् 2. पच्, cl. 1. P. A. पचति, -ते, प-<BR>पाच (पपक्थ or पेचिथ), पेचे (perf.<BR>part. पेचिवस्, f. पेचुषी), पक्ष्यति, -ते, अपाक्षीत्,<BR>अपक्त (Vedic forms पक्षत्, अपेचिरन्, पेचिरन्),<BR>पक्तुम् (Ved. पक्तवे), to cook, dress food, bake,<BR>roast, boil; to melt (metals &c.); to bake or burn<BR>(bricks); to digest; to ripen, mature, bring to<BR>maturity; (figuratively) to bring to perfection or<BR>completion; to develop anything (acc.) into another<BR>state (acc.); to cook for one's self (A.): Pass. पच्-<BR>यते, to be cooked; to become ripe or mature, to<BR>ripen; to arrive at completion or perfection (Mahā-<BR>bh. Anuśāsana-p. 6205); to be developed; to be<BR>inflamed: Caus. पाचयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अपीपचत्,<BR>to cause to be cooked, to have cooked, have dressed<BR>(as food), to cook; to cause to ripen, to bring to<BR>maturity or perfection, bring to completion, bring to<BR>an end; to cure, heal; (A. -ते), to cause to cook<BR>for one's self: Pass. of Caus. पाच्यते, to be cooked:<BR>Desid. पिपक्षति: Intens. पापच्यते, पापचीति,<BR>to be much cooked, to cook very much, burn exces-<BR>sively; (figuratively) to be much afflicted: Desid. of<BR>the Intens. पापचिषति, -ते; [cf. Zend pac, ‘to<BR>cook:’ Gr. πέπ-ων, πεπ-τό-ς, πέψι-ς, πέπ-τω, πέμ-μα,<BR>πόπ-ανο-ν, ἕψ-ω for πέψ-ω, ὄψ-ο-ν, ὀπ-τό-ς for<BR>ποπ-τό-ς, ὀπτάω, ἀρτο-κόπος, ἀρτο-πόπος,<BR>δρυ-πεπής, δρύ-πεψ: Lat. coqu-o, coquu-s, cŭ-līna,<BR>co-quina = pop-īna: Slav. pek-a, ‘I cook;’ pesh-ti,<BR>‘a stove:’ Lith. kep-ti, ‘to bake.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तव्य
पक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cooked or dressed,<BR>to be baked; to be matured; to be digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ति|पक्तिः
पक्ति, इस्, f. cooking, preparing food; food or<BR>any dish of cooked food (Ved.); digesting, digestion;<BR>the place of digestion; becoming ripe, ripening;<BR>development; respectability, dignity, fame.<BR>—पक्ति-<BR>शूल, अम्, n. violent pain or inflammation of the<BR>bowels proceeding from indigestion, colic.<BR>—पक्ति-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. the place of digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तृ
पक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, who or what cooks, cooking,<BR>a cook; digestive, promoting digestion; who or what<BR>ripens, ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्र|पक्त्रं
पक्त्र, अम्, n. the state of a householder who<BR>possesses a sacred fire; the sacred fire perpetually<BR>maintained by the householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्रिम|पक्त्रिमं
पक्त्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared by cooking,<BR>cooked; obtained by boiling (as salt); ripe, ripened,<BR>matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्वा
पक्त्वा, ind. having cooked or dressed; having<BR>matured, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्थ
पक्थ, अस्, m., Ved. (according to Sāy.) one who<BR>cooks the oblation; N. of a man protected by the<BR>Aśvins; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्थिन्
पक्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. (according to Sāy.)<BR>cooking the oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्व|पक्वं
पक्व, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part.), cooked,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">Page0522-a+ 81</a>]<BR>roasted, boiled, prepared on the fire, (opposed to<BR>आम); warmed, (द्वि-पक्व, warmed up again);<BR>baked or burnt (as bricks, porcelain, &c.); digested;<BR>mature, ripe, ripened, matured (as fruits or corn or<BR>as the milk in an udder); ready to discharge matter<BR>or suppurate; ripe (as a boil); grey (as the hair);<BR>come to perfection, accomplished, perfect, fully de-<BR>veloped (as the understanding, character, &c.), shrewd,<BR>experienced; ripe for destruction; on the eve of<BR>decay, near to death, perishing, decaying; (अम्), n.<BR>cooked food; [cf. निष्-प्˚, परि-प्˚, &c.; cf. also Gr.<BR>πέπ-ων, πεπ-ανό-ς, πέπ-ειρο-ς.]<BR>—पक्व-कषाय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having passion destroyed.<BR>—पक्व-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, cooking, maturing, dressing food; (त्), m. the tree<BR>Azadirachta Indica (= निम्ब), the leaves of which<BR>are applied to certain swellings to induce suppuration.<BR>—पक्व-केश, अस्, ई, अम्, grey-haired.<BR>—पक्व-<BR>ता, f. ripeness, maturity, greyness (of the hair).<BR>—पक्व-रस, अस्, m. wine or any intoxicating<BR>liquor.<BR>—पक्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has<BR>cooked, &c.<BR>—पक्व-वारि, n. sour rice-gruel, the<BR>water of boiled rice (= काञ्जिक); boiling water;<BR>distilled water; (also read पङ्क-वारि.)<BR>—पक्व-<BR>सस्योपमोन्नति (˚स्य-उपम-उन्˚) = राज-क-<BR>दम्ब.<BR>—पक्वातिसार (˚व-अत्˚), अस्, m. chronic<BR>dysentery.<BR>—पक्वाधान (˚व-आध्˚), अम्, n. or<BR>पक्वाशय (˚व-आश्˚), अस्, m. the receptacle for<BR>digested food, the place of digestion, the stomach,<BR>belly, abdomen; [cf. आमाशय.]<BR>—पक्वान्न (˚व-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. cooked or dressed food.<BR>—पक्वेष्-<BR>टक-चित, अम्, n. (a building) constructed with burnt<BR>bricks, (Pāṇ. VI. 3, 65.)<BR>—पक्वेष्टका (˚व-इष्˚),<BR>f. a burnt or baked brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0521-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्णु|पक्ष्णुः
पक्ष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, who or what cooks or<BR>matures, cooking, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्
3. पच्, क्, क्, क् (at the end of a comp.), cooking,<BR>baking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच|पचः
पच, अस्, आ, अम्, cooking, baking, roasting;<BR>digesting [cf. अल्पम्-पच, इष्टि-प्˚, किम्-प्˚, दुष्-<BR>प्˚, &c.]; (अस्, आ), m. f. cooking, maturing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचक|पचकः
पचक, अस्, m. a cook, cooking, baking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत्
पचत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, cooking, boiling, roasting,<BR>ripening, &c.<BR>—पचत्-पुट, अस्, m. the tree Hibiscus<BR>Phœniceus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत|पचतः
पचत, अस्, आ, अम्, cooked, dressed, boiled, ripe,<BR>mature; (अस्), m. the sun; fire; a N. of Indra;<BR>(अम्), n. cooked food.<BR>—पचत-भृज्जता, f. con-<BR>tinual baking and roasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचतिकल्प|पचतिकल्पं
पचति-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, or (अम्), ind. almost<BR>cooked or ripened, (also in a similar sense पचति-<BR>देश्य and पचति-देशीय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत्य
पचत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. cooked, dressed (as<BR>food), ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचन|पचनं|पचनः
पचन, अस्, आ, अम्, cooking, roasting, maturing<BR>[cf. एणी-प्˚]; (अस्), m. fire; (आ), f. becoming ripe,<BR>ripening; (ई), f. the wild citron tree, = वन-वीज-<BR>पूरक; (अम्), n. the act of cooking, a means or<BR>instrument for cooking, fuel, a cooking utensil, a<BR>vessel, a frying-pan, &c.; cooking, dressing, boiling;<BR>ripening, maturing; becoming cooked, becoming ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचनिक
पचनिक (gender doubtful), a pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचपच|पचपचः
पच-पच, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) ‘continually<BR>bringing to maturity,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचप्रकूटा
पच-प्रकूटा, see Gaṇa Mayūra-vyaṃsakādi to<BR>Pāṇ. II. 1, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचमान|पचमानः
पचमान, अस्, आ, अम्, cooking, in the act of<BR>cooking or ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचम्पचा|पचंपचा
पचम्-पचा, f. (reduplicated form fr. rt. 2. पच्), a<BR>species of Curcuma, C. Aromatica or C. Xanthorrhiza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचलवणा
पच-लवणा, f. constant boiling of salt, (पच is<BR>2nd sing. impv., and the comp. belongs to the Gaṇa<BR>Mayūra-vyaṃsakādi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचान
पचान, अस्, आ, अम् (anomalous form of the pres.<BR>part. A.), cooking, preparing food, (see Mahā-bh.<BR>Vana-p. 13239, and cf. किम्-प्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचि|पचिः
पचि, इस्, m. fire; cooking, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलिम|पचेलिमः
पचेलिम, अस्, आ, अम्, being soon cooked, cook-<BR>ing or ripening quickly; fit to cook or ripen, fit to<BR>be matured; (अस्), m. Phaseolus Mungo or a similar<BR>species of bean; fire; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलुक|पचेलुकः
पचेलुक, अस्, m. a cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्य
पच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming ripe, ripening, (see<BR>कृष्ट-प्˚ and cf. पाक्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्यमान|पच्यमानः
पच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being cooked, being in<BR>the act of ripening, being baked, being melted,<BR>being under digestion, being matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाच्यमान
पाच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्छब्द|पच्छब्दः
पच्छब्द पच्-छब्द, पज्-ज, &c. See under<BR>3. पद्, p. 529, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पज्झटिका
पज्झटिका पज्झटिका, f. a kind of metre;<BR>a small bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पज्र|पज्रः
पज्र पज्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) stout,<BR>fat, corpulent, in good condition, in good plight;<BR>wealthy, rich; (Sāy.) powerful, strong, rich in food;<BR>पज्राया गर्भः, ‘the son or child of the fat one,’<BR>= the Soma; (आस्), m. pl. (according to Sāy.) an epi-<BR>thet of the Aṅgirasas or of the family of Kakṣīvat;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—पज्र-होषिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>Ved. (perhaps) having rich oblations; (Sāy.) for whom<BR>the acclamation of praise (घोष) is prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पज्रिय
पज्रिय, अस्, m. an epithet of Kakṣīvat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्च्|पंच्
पञ्च् पञ्च्. See rt. 1. पच्, p. 521, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चन्|पंचन्
पञ्चन् पञ्चन्, अ, m. f. n. pl. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>पञ्च्; originally the spreading out of the hand to re-<BR>present the number by the five fingers), five. In the<BR>Veda पञ्च स्वसारः, the five sisters = the fingers;<BR>द्विः पञ्च स्वसारः = the ten fingers; पञ्च क्षि-<BR>तीनाम्, the five classes of dwellers on the earth = the<BR>four castes and the Niṣādas, Ṛg-veda 1. 7, 9;<BR>[cf. 1. क्षिति, चर्षणि, कृष्टि, जन; cf. also<BR>Ved. पञ्च-थ = Zend pukh-dha = Gr. πέμπ-<BR>το-ς; Zend pañcan; Gr. πέντε, Æol. πέμπε; Lat.<BR>quinque, quinc-tu-s or quin-tu-s, Quinct-īli-s;<BR>Goth. fimf; Mod. Germ. fünf; Lith. pan-ti;<BR>Hib. cuig; Cambro-Brit. pump.]<BR>—पञ्च-कपाल,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. prepared or offered in five cups or<BR>bowls, a particular ceremony in which ghee is offered<BR>in five cups.<BR>—पञ्च-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, (perhaps)<BR>branded in the ear with the number five (as cattle),<BR>see Pāṇ. VI. 3, 115.<BR>—पञ्च-कर्पट, आस्, m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people.<BR>—पञ्च-कर्मन्, अ, n. (in medi-<BR>cine) five kinds of treatment, viz. giving emetics,<BR>purging, giving sternutatories, and administering<BR>enemas of two kinds, oily and not oily.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>कषाय, अस्, m. (?), a decoction from the fruits of<BR>five plants, the Jambu, Śālmali, Vāṭyāla, Vakula,<BR>and Badara; (for the five Kaṣāyas of the Buddhists<BR>see under कषाय.)<BR>—पञ्चकषाय-ज or पञ्च-<BR>कषायोत्थ (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, produced from<BR>the above decoction.<BR>—पञ्च-कापित्थ, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>prepared with the five products of the Kapittha tree<BR>or Feronia Elephantum, (perhaps leaves, blossom,<BR>fruit, gum, and bark.)<BR>—पञ्च-कृत्य, अस्, m. a<BR>species of plant (= पक्त-पौड).<BR>—पञ्च-कृत्-<BR>वस्, ind. five times.<BR>—पञ्च-कृष्ण, अस्, m.<BR>‘having five black spots,’ a species of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR>—पञ्च-कृष्णलक, अस्, आ, अम्, compris-<BR>ing five Kṛṣṇalas.<BR>—पञ्च-कोण, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>five angles,’ a pentagon.<BR>—पञ्च-कोल, अम्, n. the<BR>five spices, viz. long pepper (कणा), its root (कणा-<BR>मूल), Chai or Piper Chaba (चव्य), plumbago<BR>(अग्नि), and dry ginger (नागर).<BR>—पञ्च-कोष,<BR>आस्, m. pl. the five sheaths or cases supposed to invest<BR>the soul; see under कोश.<BR>—पञ्च-क्रम, N. of a<BR>work ascribed to Nāgārjuna.<BR>—पञ्च-क्रोश-मा-<BR>हात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a poem.<BR>—पञ्च-क्रोशी, f.<BR>(probably) a distance of five Krośas.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>क्षार, अम्, n. = पञ्च-लवण.<BR>—पञ्च-खट्व,<BR>अम्, ई, n. f. a collection of five bedsteads.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>गङ्ग, आस्, m. pl., N. of a place (Mahā-bh. Droṇa-<BR>p. 2095).<BR>—पञ्च-गण-योग, अस्, m. a collective<BR>name of the five plants Vidārī-gandhā, Bṛhatī,<BR>Pṛśni-parṇī, Nidigdhikā, and Śva-daṃṣṭrā.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, (in algebra) raised to the fifth<BR>power, (lit. arrived at five.)<BR>—पञ्च-गव, अम्, ई,<BR>n. f. a collection of five cows.<BR>—पञ्चगव-धन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, whose property consists of five cows.<BR>—पञ्च-गव्य, अम्, n. five products of the cow,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-c" target="_blank">Page0522-c+ 81</a>]<BR>viz. milk, coagulated or sour milk, butter, urine, and<BR>cow-dung.<BR>—पञ्च-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, bought with five<BR>cows.<BR>—पञ्च-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, five times, fivefold.<BR>—पञ्च-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, covered or protected<BR>in a fivefold manner, having five members covered<BR>or concealed; (अस्), m. a tortoise, turtle (as drawing<BR>in its four feet and head under its shell; cf. पञ्-<BR>चाङ्ग-गुप्त); the materialistic system of the Cār-<BR>vākas.<BR>—पञ्च-गुप्ति-रसा, f. a species of vegetable,<BR>Medicago Esculenta (Trigonella Corniculata).<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. taken or taken up five<BR>times.<BR>—पञ्च-गोणि, इस्, इस्, इ, containing five<BR>Droṇas (?), see Pāṇ. I. 2, 50.<BR>—पञ्च-ग्रामी, f.<BR>a collection of five villages.<BR>—पञ्च-चत्वारिंश,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 45th.<BR>—पञ्च-चत्वारिंशत्, त्,<BR>f., 45.<BR>—पञ्च-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—पञ्च-चामर, अम्, n., N. of a metre consisting<BR>of four lines of sixteen syllables each; of another<BR>metre of four lines each containing nineteen syllables.<BR>—पञ्च-चितिक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. piled up in five<BR>tiers or layers.<BR>—पञ्च-चीर, अस्, m. a Buddhist<BR>saint and legislator, also named Mañju-śrī, appa-<BR>rently the teacher of Buddhism in Nepal.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>चूड, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘five-crested,’ having five tufts of<BR>hair; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras or nymph of heaven.<BR>—पञ्च-चोल, N. of a part of the Himālaya range.<BR>—पञ्च-जन, आस्, m. pl. the five kinds or classes<BR>of beings, viz. gods, men, Gandharvas and Apsarasas,<BR>serpents, and Pitṛs; man, mankind; N. of a demon<BR>who lived in the sea in the form of a conch shell<BR>which was formed of his bones, (he was slain by<BR>Kṛṣṇa, who took the conch shell, thence called<BR>Pāñcajanya, and used it as his horn, see Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa V. 21); N. of a son of Saṃhrāda by Kṛti;<BR>of a Prajā-pati; of a son of Sagara by Keśinī; of a<BR>son of Sṛñjaya and father of Soma-datta; (ई), f. an<BR>assemblage or aggregate of five persons; N. of a<BR>daughter of Viśva-rūpa and wife of Bharata.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>चजनालय (˚न-आल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, an epithet of the<BR>Ābhīras, (perhaps so called as living where the<BR>demon Pañca-jana lived.)<BR>—पञ्चजनीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, devoted to the five races; (अस्), m. an actor, a<BR>mimic, a buffoon; the chief of five men.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, consecrated to or intended for<BR>the five classes of beings.<BR>—पञ्च-ज्ञान, अस्, m.<BR>‘possessing the five kinds of knowledge,’ a Buddha<BR>or Buddhist sanctified teacher.<BR>—पञ्च-तक्ष, अम्,<BR>ई, n. f. a collection of five carpenters.<BR>—पञ्च-तत्त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the five elements collectively, see under<BR>तत्त्व; (in the Tantras) the five essentials (all<BR>beginning with म, cf. पञ्च-म-कार), viz. wine<BR>(मद्य), meat (मांस), fish (मत्स्य), mystic<BR>intertwining of the fingers (मुद्रा), and sexual<BR>intercourse (मैथुन).<BR>—पञ्च-तन्त्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a well-known collection of moral stories and<BR>fables in five books or chapters (तन्त्र) from which<BR>the author of the Hitopadeśa drew a large portion of<BR>his materials.<BR>—पञ्चतन्त्रक, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work consisting of five sections, (see the preceding.)<BR>—पञ्च-तन्मात्र, अम्, n. the five subtile rudi-<BR>ments of the five elements; see तन्-मात्र.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-तपस्, आस्, m. an ascetic who in the hot weather<BR>sits between four fires placed towards the four quarters<BR>with the burning sun above (Manu VI. 23).<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-ता, f. or पञ्च-त्व, अम्, n. fivefoldness, fivefold<BR>state; the aggregate of five, a collection of five<BR>things; the five elements collectively (viz. earth, air,<BR>fire, water, and ākāśa); separation into the five ele-<BR>ments of which the body consists, death, dissolu-<BR>tion.<BR>—पञ्च-तार, अस्, आ, अम्, five-starred.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-तिक्त, अम्, n. five bitter things (viz. Nimba,<BR>Amṛtā, Vṛṣa, Paṭola, and Nidigdhikā).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>तीर्थी, f. any five principal places of pilgrimage<BR>(especially Viśrānti, Śaukara, Naimiṣa, Prayāga,<BR>and Puṣkara); N. of a sacred bathing-place;<BR>bathing on the day of the equinox (?).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>त्रिंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 35th.<BR>—पञ्च-त्रिंशत्, त्,<BR>f. or पञ्च-त्रिंशति, इस्, f., 35.<BR>—पञ्च-त्व, see<BR>पञ्च-ता above.<BR>—पञ्च-दक, आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a people.<BR>—पञ्च-दश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 15th; con-<BR>sisting of 15; joined with or increased by 15 (e. g.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0523-a" target="_blank">Page0523-a+ 81</a>]<BR>पञ्च-दशं सहस्रम्, 1015); containing or<BR>representing the Pañca-daśa Stoma or connected<BR>with it; (ई), f., scil. तिथि, the 15th day of a half<BR>month, the day of full or new moon; N. of a<BR>book (belonging to the Uttara-mīmāṃsā) consist-<BR>ing of 15 chapters.<BR>—पञ्चदश-कृत्वस्, ind.,<BR>15 times.<BR>—पञ्चदश-धा, ind. in or into 15<BR>parts or ways.<BR>—पञ्च-दशन्, अ, m. f. n. pl.,<BR>15.<BR>—पञ्चदशम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 15th.<BR>—पञ्चदश-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing the<BR>Pañca-daśa Stoma.<BR>—पञ्चदशाह (˚श-अह), अस्,<BR>m. a period of 15 days.<BR>—पञ्चदशाहिक, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, lasting 15 days.<BR>—पञ्चदशिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>consisting of 15, or of 15 parts.<BR>—पञ्चदशी-<BR>समास, अस्, m., N. of a work by Rāma-kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पञ्च-दामन्, आ, म्नी, अ, Ved. having five<BR>cords.<BR>—पञ्च-दीर्घ, अम्, n. the five long parts<BR>of the body (viz. the arms, eyes, belly [according to<BR>the Buddhists, the knees], nose, and breast).<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-धा, ind. in five ways, in five parts, fivefold.<BR>—पञ्च-नख, अस्, आ, अम्, five-clawed, having<BR>five nails; (अस्), m. any animal having five claws or<BR>toes; an elephant; a tiger; a tortoise.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>नद, अम्, n. (according to Pāṇ. II. 1, 20, an<BR>Avyayī-bhāva comp.), the Pañjāb or country of five<BR>rivers, viz. the Śata-dru (Sutluj), Vipāśā (Beas),<BR>Irā-vatī (Ravee), Candra-bhāgā (Chenab), and<BR>Vitastā (Jhelum or Behut); N. of a river produced<BR>by the junction of the five rivers of the Pañjāb and<BR>which falls into the Sindhu; N. of a Tīrtha near<BR>the spot where the Kiraṇā and Dhūta-pāpa fall into<BR>the Ganges after the union of the latter river with<BR>the Yamunā and Sarasvatī; (अस्), m. a prince of<BR>Pañca-nada; N. of an Asura; N. of a preceptor;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of Pañca-nada.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>नद-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—पञ्चनवत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 95th.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>नवति, इस्, f., 95.<BR>—पञ्चनवति-तम, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the 95th.<BR>—पञ्च-नामन्, आ, म्नी, अ, having<BR>five names.<BR>—पञ्च-निधन, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR>—पञ्च-निम्ब, अम्, n. the five products<BR>of the Azadirachta Indica (viz. the flowers, fruit,<BR>leaves, bark, and root).<BR>—पञ्च-नीराजन, अम्, n.<BR>waving four things (viz. a lamp, lotus, cloth, mango<BR>or betel leaf) before an idol and then falling pros-<BR>trate.<BR>—पञ्च-पक्षिन्, ई, m., N. of a small book<BR>ascribed to Śiva containing prophecies, in which the<BR>five vowels अ, इ, उ, ए, ओ are connected with five birds;<BR>(also ˚पक्षि or ˚पक्षिन्, n.)<BR>—पञ्च-पञ्च-<BR>नख, अस्, m. five species of animals allowed to be<BR>killed and eaten, the hare, porcupine, alligator,<BR>rhinoceros, and tortoise.<BR>—पञ्च-पञ्चाश, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the 55th.<BR>—पञ्च-पञ्चाशत्, त्, f., 55.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-पञ्चिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. having five parts, fivefold.<BR>—पञ्च-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘five-leaved,’ a species of<BR>Caṇḍāla-kanda.<BR>—पञ्च-पद् or पञ्च-पाद्, पात्,<BR>पात् or पदी, पात्, consisting of five feet, steps, or<BR>parts; (पदी), f., N. of a river in Śāka-dvīpa.<BR>—पञ्च-पद, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. containing five<BR>Padas; (ई), f. ‘only five steps,’ a term expressive of<BR>a cold unfriendly relationship, (opposed to साप्त-<BR>पदीन, q. v.); the five strong cases (viz. the nom.<BR>voc. and acc. sing., the nom. voc. and acc. du., and<BR>the nom. and voc. pl.).<BR>—पञ्च-पर्णिका or पञ्च-<BR>पर्णी, f. a species of small shrub (= गो-रक्षी).<BR>—पञ्च-पर्वत, अम्, n. ‘the five mountains,’ N.<BR>of five peaks of the Himālayas.<BR>—पञ्च-पल्लव,<BR>अम्, n. the aggregate of five sprigs or young shoots<BR>of the Āmra, Jambū, Kapittha, Vīja-pūraka, and<BR>Vilva; (according to others, of the Āmra, Aśvattha,<BR>Vaṭa, Parkaṭī, and Yajñodumbara; or of the Panasa,<BR>Āmra, Aśvattha, Vaṭa, and Vakula); Bél or Mar-<BR>melos, citron, and wood-apple.<BR>—पञ्च-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. five cups or vessels collectively; a Śrāddha in<BR>which offerings are made in five vessels.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>पाद, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of or containing five<BR>feet.<BR>—पञ्च-पादिका or पञ्च-पादी, f., N. of<BR>a treatise on the Uṇādi affixes consisting of five<BR>sections; N. of a philosophical work by Sa-nan-<BR>dana treating of the first four Brahma-sūtras.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>चपादिका-विवरण, अम्, n. a commentary by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0523-b" target="_blank">Page0523-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Prakāśātman on Sa-nandana's Pañca-pādī.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-पित्त, अम्, n. the gall or bile of five animals (viz.<BR>the boar, goat, buffalo, fish, and peacock).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a city.<BR>—पञ्चपुष्प-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, formed of five flowers.<BR>—पञ्च-प्रस्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having five elevations or rising grounds<BR>(as a forest; perhaps N. of a forest).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>प्राण, आस्, m. pl. the five vital airs, the five airs<BR>supposed to be in the body.<BR>—पञ्च-प्रासाद, अस्,<BR>m. a temple with four pinnacles and a steeple.<BR>—पञ्च-बन्ध, अस्, m. a fine equal to the fifth<BR>part of anything lost or stolen.<BR>—पञ्च-बला, f. the<BR>five plants called Balā (viz. Balā, Nāga-b˚, Mahā-b˚,<BR>Ati-b˚, and Rāja-b˚).<BR>—पञ्च-बाण or पञ्च-वाण,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having five arrows,’ epithet of the god of<BR>love.<BR>—पञ्च-बाहु, उस्, m. ‘five-armed,’ N. of one<BR>of the attendants of Śiva.<BR>—पञ्च-ब्रह्म, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—पञ्च-भद्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having five good qualities; consisting of five good<BR>ingredients (as a sauce or a decoction); having five<BR>auspicious marks or spotted on the chest, back, face,<BR>and flanks (as a horse); vicious.<BR>—पञ्च-भुज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, five-armed, pentagonal; (अस्), m. a<BR>pentagon.<BR>—पञ्च-भूत, अम्, n. the five ele-<BR>ments, earth, air, fire, water, and ākāśa.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>भूत-परित्यक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, deserted by the five<BR>elements (as a dead body).<BR>—पञ्चभूतात्मन्<BR>(˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, consisting of the five elements,<BR>formed of the five primary elements (as the body).<BR>—पञ्च-भृङ्ग, epithet of the five plants Deva-<BR>dālī, Śamī, Bhaṅgā, Nirguṇḍī, and Tamāla-pattra.<BR>—पञ्च-भौतिक incorrect reading for पाञ्च-<BR>भौतिक, q. v.<BR>—पञ्च-म-कार, अम्, n. the five<BR>essentials of the left-hand Tantra ritual, the words<BR>for which begin with the letter म्; see पञ्च-<BR>तत्त्व.<BR>—पञ्च-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting or<BR>formed of five, made up or consisting of the five<BR>(elements).<BR>—पञ्च-महापातकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, guilty<BR>of the five great sins; see महा-पातक.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>महायज्ञ, आस्, m. pl. the five great sacrifices of<BR>the Hindūs; (see महा-यज्ञ.)<BR>—पञ्च-महिष,<BR>अम्, n. the five products of the buffalo cow; [cf.<BR>पञ्च-गव्य.]<BR>—पञ्च-माषिक or पञ्च-मा-<BR>षक, अस्, &c., consisting of five Māṣas, amounting<BR>to five Māṣas (as a fine &c.).<BR>—१. पञ्च-मास्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under पञ्चम), happening<BR>every five months, containing five months; (अस्), m.<BR>the Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>—पञ्च-मुख, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, five-faced or five-headed, (sometimes applied in<BR>the Upaniṣads to Prajā-pati); (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva; a lion; an arrow with five points; (ई), f.<BR>a species of plant, Gendarussa Vulgaris; [cf. पञ्च-<BR>शिख, पञ्च-वक्त्र, पञ्चानन, पञ्चास्य.]<BR>—पञ्च-मुद्रा, f. five gestures to be made in<BR>presenting offerings to an idol.<BR>—पञ्च-मुष्टि, इस्,<BR>ई, f. the plant Trigonella Corniculata.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>मूत्र, अम्, n. the urine of five female animals<BR>(viz. the cow, goat, sheep, buffalo, and ass).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. or पञ्च-मूली, f. a collection or<BR>group of five roots or plants with tuberous roots<BR>(e. g. Vilva, Agni-mantha, Ṭuṇṭuka, Pāṭala, and<BR>Kāśmarī; or Tri-kaṇṭaka, the two Bṛhatīs, Pṛthak-<BR>parṇī, and Vidāri-gandha; the first is considered the<BR>larger collection, the second the smaller; other<BR>groups are also enumerated).<BR>—पञ्च-यक्षा, f.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पञ्च-यज्ञ, आस्, m. pl. the five<BR>rites or sacrifices of a house-keeper; [cf. पञ्च-<BR>महायज्ञ.]<BR>—पञ्चयज्ञ-परिभ्रष्ट, अस्, m.<BR>a Brahman who omits to perform the five great sacri-<BR>fices.<BR>—पञ्च-याम, अस्, m., N. of a son of Ātapa<BR>(Sun-shine).<BR>—पञ्च-युग, अम्, n. a cycle of five<BR>years, a lustrum.<BR>—पञ्च-रक्ष, N. of two Prajñā-<BR>pāramitās (q. v.) connected with each other.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>च-रक्षक, अस्, m. a species of plant (= पक्त-<BR>पौड).<BR>—पञ्च-रत्न, अम्, n. a collection of<BR>five jewels or precious things, viz. gold, the diamond,<BR>sapphire, ruby, and pearl, or (according to Gauḍa)<BR>gold, silver, coral, pearl, and Rāga-paṭṭa; N. of a<BR>collection of five verses on ethical subjects; (आनि), n.<BR>pl. the five gems or five most admired episodes of<BR>the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—पञ्च-रसा, f. the Emblic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0523-c" target="_blank">Page0523-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Myrobalan tree (= आमलकी).<BR>—पञ्च-रात्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, lasting five nights or days; (अम्), n. a period<BR>of five nights, N. of an Ahīna (q. v.) which lasts five<BR>days; a general term for the sacred books of various<BR>Vaiṣṇava sects; see पाञ्चरात्र.<BR>—पञ्च-रा-<BR>त्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, lasting five nights (i. e. days).<BR>—पञ्चरात्र-दीपिका, f. (probably) N. of a treatise<BR>on the fabrication and right dimensions and deco-<BR>ration of idols.<BR>—पञ्च-राशिक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating<BR>to the five ratios or proportions of numbers; (अम्),<BR>n. the rule of five, the rule of proportion with five<BR>terms, double rule of three (?).<BR>—पञ्चर्च (˚च-<BR>ऋच), अम्, n., Ved. a stanza consisting of five<BR>verses.<BR>—पञ्च-लक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing<BR>five characteristics (said of the Purāṇas, which ought<BR>strictly to comprehend five topics, viz. the creation<BR>of the universe, its destruction and renovation, the<BR>genealogy of gods and patriarchs, the reigns of the<BR>Manus, and the history of the solar and lunar races;<BR>but few Purāṇas, except the Viṣṇu, conform to<BR>this description, and even the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa di-<BR>verges into other topics).<BR>—पञ्च-लम्बक, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the fourteenth Lambaka in the Kathā-<BR>sarit-sāgara.<BR>—पञ्च-लवण, अम्, n. five kinds of<BR>salt (viz. Kāca, Saindhava, Sāmudra, Viḍa, and Sau-<BR>varcala).<BR>—पञ्च-लाङ्गलक, अम्, n. a gift of as<BR>much land as can be cultivated with five ploughs.<BR>—पञ्च-लोह, अम्, n. a metallic alloy containing<BR>five metals (viz. copper, brass, tin, lead, and iron).<BR>—पञ्च-लोहक, अम्, n. the five metals (viz. gold,<BR>silver, copper, tin, and lead).<BR>—पञ्च-वक्त्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, five-faced; (अस्), m. epithet of Śiva; N. of one<BR>of the attendants of Skanda; a lion; (आ), f. epithet<BR>of Durgā; [cf. पञ्च-मुख.]<BR>—पञ्च-वट, अस्,<BR>m. ‘five-threaded,’ the Brāhmanical or sacrificial<BR>cord worn across the breast or over the shoulder [cf.<BR>पञ्चा-वट]; N. of a man; (ई), f. the five fig-trees<BR>(viz. Aśvattha, Vilva, Vaṭa, Dhātrī, and Aśoka); N. of<BR>a part of the great southern forest where the Godā-<BR>varī rises and where Rāma resided for a long period<BR>of his banishment; (in Rāmāyaṇa 1. 3, 18, पञ्च-<BR>वट, अम्, n. occurs.)<BR>—पञ्च-वर्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>class or group or series of five; the five essential<BR>ingredients or constituent elements of the body, (see<BR>1. धातु); the five organs of sense; the five<BR>sacrifices, &c., (according to some also पञ्च-वर्गी,<BR>which may mean ‘five classes’); (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved.<BR>proceeding in five lines or at five times.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, five-coloured; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>mountain; (अम्), n., N. of a forest.<BR>—पञ्च-वर्-<BR>धन, अस्, m. = पञ्च-रक्षक.<BR>—पञ्च-वर्-<BR>षक-देशीय, अस्, आ, अम्, nearly five years old.<BR>—पञ्च-वर्षीय, अस्, आ, अम्, five years old.<BR>—पञ्च-वल्कल, अम्, n. a collection of the bark<BR>of five kinds of trees, viz. the Indian, glomerous,<BR>holy and waved-leaf fig-tree, and Calamus Rotang, a<BR>sort of reed, (i. e. Nyag-rodha, Udumbara, Aśvattha,<BR>Plaksha, and Vetasa; but other trees are sometimes<BR>substituted.)<BR>—पञ्च-वाण, अस्, m. ‘five-arrowed,’<BR>a N. of Kāma-deva, the Indian Cupid.<BR>—पञ्च-वा-<BR>तीय, अम्, n., N. of an oblation offered to the five winds<BR>at the Rāja-sūya.<BR>—पञ्च-वार्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, re-<BR>curring every five years.<BR>—पञ्च-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>yoked with five, drawn by five (as a carriage &c.).<BR>—पञ्च-विंश, अस्, ई, अम्, the 25th; consisting of<BR>25, containing 25; presenting the Pañca-viṃśa Stoma,<BR>belonging to it, celebrated with it; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu regarded as the 25th Tattva.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>विंशक, अस्, ई, अम्, the 25th; 25 years old (वयसा<BR>पञ्च-विंशकः); consisting of 25.<BR>—पञ्च-विंशति,<BR>इस्, f., 25.<BR>—पञ्चविंशतिका, f. a collection of 25<BR>stanzas or tales, &c.; [cf. वेताल-प्˚.]<BR>—पञ्चविं-<BR>शति-तम or पञ्चविंशतिम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 25th.<BR>—पञ्च-विध or पञ्चविधेय, अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>five kinds, fivefold.<BR>—पञ्च-विधान-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work belonging to the Sāma-veda.<BR>—पञ्च-विन्दु-प्रसृत, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>movement in dancing.<BR>—पञ्च-वीज, अम्, n. a col-<BR>lection of five kinds of seeds (viz. of Cardiospermum<BR>Halicacabum, Trigonella Fœnum Græcum, Astera-<BR>cantha Longifolia, Ligusticum Ajowan, and cumin-seed;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-a" target="_blank">Page0524-a+ 81</a>]<BR>or of Trapusa, Karkaṭī, Dāḍima, Padma, and Vānarī;<BR>or of Sinapis Racemosa, Ligusticum Ajowan, cumin-<BR>seed, sesamum from Chorasan, and poppy).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>वीर-गोष्ठ, अम्, n. (perhaps) an assembly-room<BR>named ‘The Five Heroes,’ i. e. the five sons of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—पञ्च-वृत् or पञ्च-वृतम्, ind. fivefold, five<BR>times.<BR>—पञ्च-शत, अम्, n., 105; 500; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), amounting to 500 (as a fine); fined 500<BR>(paṇas).<BR>—पञ्चशत-तम, अस्, ई, अम्, the 105th.<BR>—पञ्च-शर, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘five-arrowed,’ armed<BR>with five arrows; (अस्), m., N. of Kāma-deva, the<BR>god of love.<BR>—पञ्च-शस्, ind. by fives, five by five.<BR>—पञ्च-शस्य, अम्, n. (or more correctly पञ्च-<BR>सस्य), five species of grain, viz. Dhānya, Mudga,<BR>Tila, Yava, and Śveta-sarṣapa (or Māṣa).<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>शाख, अस्, m. ‘five-branched,’ the hand (πέντοζον).<BR>—पञ्च-शारदीय, अस्, m., N. of a Pañcāha<BR>representing five years.<BR>—पञ्च-शिख, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘five-crested,’ having five tufts of hair on the head;<BR>(अस्), m. a lion; N. of a Sāṅkhya teacher (a pupil<BR>of Āsuri); N. of an attendant of Śiva; N. of a<BR>Gandharva.<BR>—पञ्च-शीर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, five-headed;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—पञ्च-शुक्ल, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having five white (spots); (अस्), m. a species of<BR>venomous insect.<BR>—पञ्च-शूरण, अम्, n. the five<BR>Śūraṇas (Śūraṇa = the bulbous root of Amorpho-<BR>phallus Campanulatus), a collective name of five<BR>bulbous plants; (this word may also be used as an<BR>adj.)<BR>—पञ्च-शैरीषक, अम्, n. the five products<BR>of the Acacia Śirīṣa, leaf, flower, fruit, bark, root.<BR>—पञ्च-शैल, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>ष, आस्, आस्, आणि, pl. (fr. पञ्चन् + षष्), five or<BR>six.<BR>—पञ्च-षष्ट, अस्, ई, अम्, the 65th.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>षष्टि, इस्, f., 65.<BR>—पञ्चषष्टि-तम, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, the 65th.<BR>—पञ्च-सट, अस्, आ, अम्, five-<BR>tailed (as a badge of slavery?).<BR>—पञ्च-सत्त्र, N. of<BR>a place.<BR>—पञ्च-सप्तत, अस्, ई, अम्, the 75th.<BR>—पञ्च-सप्तति, इस्, f., 75.<BR>—पञ्चसप्तति-तम,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, the 75th.<BR>—पञ्च-सप्तन्, अ, m. f. n. pl.<BR>five times seven or 35.<BR>—पञ्च-सायक, N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—पञ्च-सिद्धान्तिका, f., N. of an astrono-<BR>mical work by Varāha-mihira, founded on the five<BR>older astronomical works, and called by Varāha-mihira<BR>himself Karaṇa.<BR>—पञ्च-सिद्धौषधिक (˚ध-<BR>ओष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of five kinds of medi-<BR>cinal plants.<BR>—पञ्च-सुगन्धक, अम्, n. a col-<BR>lection of five kinds of aromatic vegetable substances,<BR>cloves (लवङ्ग), nutmeg (जाती-फल), camphor<BR>(कर्पूर), aloe wood (अ-गुरु), and kakkola (q. v.).<BR>—पञ्च-सूत्री, f. the five Sūtras.<BR>—पञ्च-सूना,<BR>आस्, m. pl. the five things in a house by which<BR>animal life may be accidentally destroyed, the fire-<BR>place, the slab on which condiments are ground, the<BR>broom, the pestle and mortar, and the water-pot.<BR>—पञ्च-स्कन्धक, N. of a work.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>स्रोतस्, five streams (probably = पञ्च-नद).<BR>—पञ्च-स्वरा, f., N. of an astrological work in<BR>seven chapters on fortune-telling and the averting of<BR>good or bad luck by Prajāpati-dāsa-vaidya.<BR>—पञ्च-<BR>स्वरोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of an astronomical<BR>work ascribed to Rudra.<BR>—पञ्च-स्वस्त्ययन, N.<BR>of a Vedic work accentuated in an unusual manner<BR>and resembling a Brāhmaṇa in its subject-matter.<BR>—पञ्च-हस्त, N. of a place.<BR>—पञ्च-हायन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, five years old.<BR>—पञ्च-होत्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a son of Manu Rohita.<BR>—पञ्च-ह्रद-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>चांश (˚च-अं˚), अस्, m. the fifth part, a fifth.<BR>—पञ्चाक्षर (˚च-अक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting<BR>of five syllables, five-syllabled.<BR>—पञ्चाख्यान (˚च-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of five tales; (अम्), n.<BR>another name of the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—पञ्चाग्नि (˚च-<BR>अग्˚), इ, n. a collection of five fires, the five sacred<BR>fires (viz. Anvāhārya-pacana, Gārhapatya, Āhava-<BR>nīya, Sabhya, and Āvasathya, generally in comp.);<BR>five mystic fires supposed to be present in the body;<BR>(इस्), m. a householder who maintains the five sacred<BR>fires, one who keeps the five fires constantly burning<BR>(= अग्नि-होत्री, see Manu III. 185); one who is ac-<BR>quainted with the doctrine of the five mystic fires.<BR>—पञ्चाग्नि-त्व, अम्, n. a collection or aggregate<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-b" target="_blank">Page0524-b+ 81</a>]<BR>of five fires or of five passions (which inflame men's<BR>minds), &c.<BR>—पञ्चाग्नि-विद्या-प्रकरण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a sacred work of the Vājasaneyins.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>चाङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम्, five-limbed, five-membered, having<BR>five parts or subdivisions, consisting of five members<BR>or parts, &c.; पञ्चाङ्गः प्रणामः, obeisance<BR>made with the arms, knees, head, voice, and look;<BR>(अस्), m. a tortoise or turtle [cf. पञ्चाङ्ग-गुप्त];<BR>a horse with five spots in various parts of his body<BR>(= पञ्च-भद्र); (ई), f. a bit for horses; a kind<BR>of bandage; (अम्), n. five parts of a tree (viz. root,<BR>bark, leaf, flower, and fruit); five limbs or members<BR>of the body (in comp.); five modes of devotion,<BR>(said to be silent prayer, burnt offerings, libations,<BR>bathing idols, and feeding Brāhmans); any aggregate<BR>of five parts; a calendar or almanac treating of five<BR>things, viz. solar days, lunar days, asterisms, Yogas,<BR>and Karaṇas.<BR>—पञ्चाङ्ग-गुप्त, अस्, m. a tortoise<BR>or turtle (= पञ्च-गुप्त, q. v.).<BR>—पञ्चाङ्ग-<BR>पत्त्र, अम्, n. a calendar or almanac, (see above.)<BR>—पञ्चाङ्ग-शुद्धि, इस्, f. the propitious or<BR>favourable state of five important points, the solar<BR>day, lunar day, Nakṣatra, Yoga, and Karaṇa.<BR>—पञ्चाङ्गिक (˚च-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, five-limbed,<BR>five-membered.<BR>—पञ्चाङ्गुरि (˚च-अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>Ved. five-fingered, having five fingers.<BR>—पञ्चाङ्गुल<BR>(˚च-अङ्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, five fingers long, measuring<BR>five fingers; (अस्), m. the castor-oil plant, Ricinus<BR>Communis; (ई), f. a species of shrub.<BR>—पञ्चाङ्गुलि<BR>(˚च-अङ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, five-fingered, having five fingers<BR>or finger-like divisions.<BR>—पञ्चाज (˚च-आज), अम्,<BR>n. the five products of the goat; [cf. पञ्च-गव्य.]<BR>—पञ्चातपा (˚च-आत्˚), f. doing penance with five<BR>fires or with four fires and the sun, (see under तपस्.)<BR>—पञ्चात्मक (˚च-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of<BR>the five elements, (said of the body.)<BR>—पञ्चाधिका<BR>(according to the Ṛg-veda Anukramaṇī) = 25 (i. e.<BR>20 + 5).<BR>—पञ्चानन (˚च-आन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, five-<BR>faced, (hence = अत्य्-उग्र, very fierce, very passionate,<BR>&c.); (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; a lion; (often at<BR>the end of names of learned men to express respect,<BR>e. g. न्याय-पञ्चानन, न्याय-सिद्धान्त-प्˚,<BR>&c.); (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—पञ्चानन्द-<BR>माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—पञ्चानु-<BR>गान (˚च-अन्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—पञ्चाप्-<BR>सरस् (˚च-अप्˚), अस्, n., N. of a lake or pool sup-<BR>posed to have been produced by an ascetic named<BR>Mandakarṇi (Śātakarṇi) through the power of his<BR>penance, (so called because under it Mandakarṇi<BR>formed a secret chamber for five Apsarasas who had<BR>seduced him from his devotions, see Rāmāyaṇa III.<BR>15, 11; Raghu-v. XIII. 38.)<BR>—पञ्चाब्ज-मण्डल<BR>(˚च-अब्˚), अम्, n., N. of a mystical circle.<BR>—पञ्चा-<BR>मृत (˚च-अम्˚), अम्, n. the five kinds of divine<BR>food (viz. milk, coagulated or sour milk, butter,<BR>honey, and sugar); the aggregate of any five drugs<BR>of supposed efficacy; (अस्, आ, अम्), consisting of five<BR>ingredients (as a medicine); (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>Tantra.<BR>—पञ्चाम्नाय (˚च-आम्˚), आस्, m. pl. five<BR>Śāstras supposed to have proceeded from the five<BR>mouths of Śiva, constituting the basis of the Tantra<BR>ritual.<BR>—पञ्चाम्ल (˚च-आम्˚), अम्, n. the aggregate<BR>of five acid plants, the jujube, pomegranate, sorrel,<BR>spondias, and citron.<BR>—पञ्चार्चिस् (˚च-अर्˚), इस्,<BR>m. the planet Mercury.<BR>—पञ्चार्थ-भाष्य-<BR>दीपिका, f., N. of a chapter of the Sarva-darśana-<BR>saṅgraha by Mādhavācārya.<BR>—पञ्चा-वट, अस्, m.<BR>the sacrificial cord as worn crossed upon the breast with<BR>the ends hanging over the shoulders; [cf. पञ्च-<BR>वट.]<BR>—पञ्चावत्त (˚च-अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>divided into five parts.<BR>—पञ्चावत्त-ता, f. or पञ्-<BR>चावत्त-त्व, अम्, n. fivefold division.<BR>—पञ्चा-<BR>वत्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. that which is divided into five<BR>parts or has a fivefold division; that which divides<BR>into five parts.<BR>—पञ्चावत्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>divided into five portions, offered in five portions.<BR>—पञ्चावयव, अस्, आ, अम्, five-limbed, five-<BR>membered; पञ्चावयवं वाक्यम्, a five-mem-<BR>bered argument, a syllogism.<BR>—पञ्चावस्थ (˚च-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. a corpse (resolved into the five ele-<BR>ments).<BR>—पञ्चावि (˚च-अवि), इस्, ई, इ, Ved. reckoning<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-c" target="_blank">Page0524-c+ 81</a>]<BR>five lambing times, i. e. five times six months.<BR>—पञ्चाविक (˚च-आव्˚), अम्, n. the five products<BR>of the sheep; [cf. पञ्च-गव्य, पञ्चाज.]<BR>—पञ्-<BR>चाशीत (˚च-अश्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, the 85th.<BR>—पञ्चाशीति<BR>(˚च-अश्˚), इस्, f., 85.<BR>—पञ्चाशीति-तम, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>the 85th.<BR>—पञ्चास्य (˚च-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, five-<BR>faced, five-headed; five-pointed (as an arrow); (अस्),<BR>m. a lion.<BR>—पञ्चाह (˚च-अह), अस्, m. a period<BR>of five days; (अस्, आ, अम्), lasting five days; (अस्),<BR>m. a Soma oblation with five Sutyā days.<BR>—पञ्चा-<BR>हिक, अस्, आ, अम्, containing five feast days or fes-<BR>tivals.<BR>—पञ्ची-करण-वार्त्तिक, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>philosophical work by Sureśvara.<BR>—पञ्ची-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to render fivefold<BR>&c., cause anything to contain all the five elements.<BR>—पञ्चेध्मीय (˚च-इध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, (a nocturnal<BR>rite) in which five torches &c. are used.<BR>—पञ्चेन्-<BR>द्र (˚च-इन्˚), अस्, m. one who has the five Indrāṇīs<BR>as his deity.<BR>—पञ्चेन्द्र-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, like<BR>five Indras.<BR>—पञ्चेन्द्रिय (˚च-इन्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>five organs of sense (viz. the eye, ear, nose, tongue,<BR>and skin) or the five organs of action (viz. hands,<BR>feet, larynx, and organs of generation and excretion);<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), having five organs of sense.<BR>—पञ्चेषु<BR>(˚च-इष्˚), उस्, m. ‘five-arrowed,’ N. of Kāma-deva,<BR>the Hindū Cupid.<BR>—पञ्चोना (according to the Ṛg-<BR>veda Anukramaṇī) = 15 (i. e. 20 — 5).<BR>—पञ्चोष्मन्<BR>(˚च-उष्˚), आणस्, m. pl. the five digestive fires<BR>supposed to be in the body.<BR>—पञ्चौदन (˚च-<BR>ओद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. prepared with fivefold pulp<BR>of mashed grain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चक|पंचक|पञ्चकं|पञ्चकः
पञ्चक, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of five, relating<BR>to five, made of five, bought with five &c., taking<BR>five per cent; (अस्), m. any collection or aggregate<BR>of five; N. of one of the attendants of Skanda;<BR>(इका), f., N. of each book of the Aitareya-Brāhmaṇa<BR>(as consisting of five Adhyāyas); N. of a game<BR>played with five shells; (अम्), n. an aggregate of five,<BR>πεντάς; a field of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्|पंचत्
पञ्चत्, त्, f. an aggregate of five,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतय|पंचतय|पञ्चतयं|पञ्चतयः
पञ्चतय, अस्, ई, अम्, fivefold, having five parts<BR>or limbs, five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

