पञ्चम|पंचम|पञ्चमं|पञ्चमः
पञ्चम, अस्, ई, अम्, the fifth; forming the fifth<BR>part, constituting a fifth part, beautiful, brilliant,<BR>pleasing; dexterous, clever; (अस्), m. the fifth or in<BR>later times the seventh note of the Hindū musical<BR>scale, (so called because, according to the Hindūs, its<BR>tone is produced by air drawn from five parts of the<BR>body, the navel, breast, throat, heart, and forehead);<BR>one of the Rāgas or musical modes; N. of the<BR>twenty-first Kalpa (called after the musical note);<BR>the fifth consonant of a Varga, i. e. a nasal; (ई), f.,<BR>scil. तिथि, the fifth day of the half month; the<BR>termination of the fifth or ablative case, a word in<BR>the ablative; an epithet of Draupadī, the wife of<BR>the five Pāṇḍu princes [cf. पाञ्चाली]; a chequered<BR>cloth for playing at draughts &c., a chess-board (=<BR>शारि-शृङ्खला); N. of a river; (अम्), n. a fifth,<BR>the fifth part; copulation as the fifth of the Tattvas<BR>of the Tāntrikas, see under पञ्च-तत्त्व; (अम्),<BR>ind. for the fifth time, fifthly.<BR>—पञ्चम-भागीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the fifth part.<BR>—पञ्चम-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having the fifth (of anything).<BR>—पञ्चम-सार-संहिता, f., N. of a musical<BR>work.<BR>—पञ्चमार (˚म-अर), अस्, m. the fifth<BR>spoke in the wheel of time (with Jainas); N. of<BR>a son of Bala-deva.<BR>—२. पञ्चमास्य (˚म-आस्˚),<BR>अस्, m. (for 1. see p. 523, col. 2), the Indian cuckoo<BR>or Koïl (as producing the fifth note of the scale with<BR>its mouth or throat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमक
पञ्चमक, अस्, आ or ई (?), अम्, fifth, the fifth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0524-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमिन्|पंचमिन्
