पञ्चाशक
पञ्चाशक, अस्, इका, अम्, 50; (इका), f. a collec-<BR>tion or aggregate of 50; [cf. श्लोक-पञ्चाशिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशत्|पंचाशत्
पञ्चाशत्, त्, f., 50; (अर्ध-पञ्चाशत्, 25;<BR>एकोन-पञ्चाशत्, 49; cf. Gr. πεντήκοντα; Lat.<BR>quinquaginta; Hib. caogat.)<BR>—पञ्चाशच्-छस्,<BR>ind. (पञ्चाशत् + शस्), by fifties, fifty by fifty.<BR>—पञ्-<BR>चाशद्-भाग, अस्, m. the 50th part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

