पर्यश्
पर्यश् 2. पर्य्-अश्, cl. 9. P. -अश्नाति, -अशितुम्,<BR>to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0554-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यश्रु|पर्य्यश्रु
पर्यश्रु पर्य्-अश्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, bathed in or<BR>suffused with tears, shedding tears, tearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0554-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यस्
पर्यस् 1. पर्य्-अस्, cl. 2. P. -अस्ति, Ved. to<BR>be in the way; to surpass; to pass or spend (time);<BR>(Sāy.) = परितो भू, to be everywhere about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0554-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यस्
पर्यस् 2. पर्य्-अस्, cl. 4. P. A. -अस्यति, -ते,<BR>-असितुम्, to throw or cast round, put or place round,<BR>put on, spread round, diffuse; to surround, encircle,<BR>encompass; to enchase; to entrap, ensnare; to turn<BR>round, turn over; to turn away; to throw down,<BR>overturn, upset: Pass. -अस्यते, to fall down, drop,<BR>sink down: Caus. to cause to drop, to cause to roll<BR>down or shed (as tears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0554-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यसन|पर्यसनं|पर्य्यसन
पर्य्-असन, अम्, n. throwing about, moving to<BR>and fro, wagging; casting, sending; putting off or<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0554-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यस्त|पर्य्यस्त|पर्य्यस्तः
पर्य्-अस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or cast round,<BR>placed round, put on, diffused; surrounded, encom-<BR>passed, ensnared; thrown off, thrown down; thrown<BR>or tossed up; overturned, upset; dismissed, laid aside;<BR>struck, killed; bound.<BR>—पर्यस्त-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. containing the notion expressed by the word<BR>पर्य्-अस्त.<BR>—पर्यस्त-विलोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>पर्यस्ताक्ष (˚त-अक्ष), अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. having<BR>the eyes cast or directed round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0554-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यस्ति|पर्यस्तिः|पर्य्यस्ति
