पर्युप्ति|पर्युप्तिः
पर्य्-उप्ति, इस्, f. scattering seed, sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्युषण|पर्युषणं
पर्युषण पर्य्-उषण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 6. वस्<BR>with परि or incorrectly for पर्य्-एषण), service,<BR>worship, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्युषित|पर्य्युषित|पर्य्युषितं
पर्य्-उषित, अस्, आ, अम्, having passed the night;<BR>stale, not fresh; insipid; stupid, vain.<BR>—पर्युषित-<BR>भोजिन्, ई, m. the eater of stale food (said to become<BR>a maggot or worm in the next birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यूह्
पर्यूह् पर्य्-ऊह् [cf. rt. 1. ऊह्], cl. 1. P. A.<BR>-ऊहति, -ते, -ऊहितुम्, Ved. to heap or pile round; to<BR>surround or fortify with mounds or embankments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यूहण
पर्य्-ऊहण, अम्, n., Ved. sweeping or heaping<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यृष्
पर्यृष् 1. पर्य्-ऋष्, cl. 1. P. -अर्षति, -अर्-<BR>षितुम्, Ved. to flow round, flow into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यृष्
पर्यृष् 2. पर्य्-ऋष्, cl. 6. P. -ऋषति, -अर्षि-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to embrace, clasp round, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्यर्षण
पर्य्-अर्षण, अम्, n., Ved. clasping round, sup-<BR>porting, making firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ये
पर्ये पर्य्-ए (परि-आ-इ), cl. 2. P. -एति, -एतुम्,<BR>Ved. to roam about; to come back, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्येतृ
पर्येतृ पर्य्-एतृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. परी), Ved.<BR>overpowering, mastering; (Sāy.) = नाशक, a de-<BR>spoiler; = परि-गमयितृ, a promoter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्येष्
पर्येष् पर्य्-एष्, cl. 1. P. -एषति, -एषितुम्,<BR>to seek about for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्येषण|पर्येषणं
पर्य्-एषण, अम्, n. search, inquiry, investigation;<BR>(आ), f. search, inquiry, research, investigation of duty<BR>by reasoning; serving, waiting upon, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्येषत्
पर्य्-एषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, seeking about for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्येष्टव्य
पर्य्-एष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sought after, to<BR>be sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्येष्टि|पर्येष्टिः|पर्य्येष्टि
पर्य्-एष्टि, इस्, f. searching for, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्
पर्व् पर्व्, cl. 1. P. पर्वति, पर्वितुम्, to<BR>fill; [cf. rts. पॄ, पूर्व्, मर्व्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व|पर्व्व
पर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) =<BR>पर्वन्, p. 556, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वक|पर्वकं|पर्व्वक|पर्व्वकं
पर्वक, अम्, n. the knee-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वण
पर्वण, अस्, m., N. of a demon; (ई), m. the<BR>period of a change of the moon; a festival; (also<BR>पर्वणिका and पर्वणीका), a particular disease of<BR>the so-called juncture (सन्धि) of the eye; (at the<BR>end of a comp.) = पर्वन्, a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वत|पर्वतः|पर्व्वत|पर्व्वतः
पर्वत, अस्, m. (probably connected with पर्वन्,<BR>p. 556, col. 1, as ‘having crags or elevations’), a moun-<BR>tain, mountain-range, height, hill, elevation, rock, (in<BR>Ṛg-veda 1. 37, 7, V. 56, 4, पर्वत is joined as an<BR>adj. with गिरि; and according to Sāy. = जगत्-पूर-<BR>कोदक-वत्, laden with water filling the world, or<BR>बहुविध-पर्व-युक्त, shelving, rugged); an<BR>artificial mountain or heap (of grain, salt, saffron,<BR>sugar, silver or gold presented to the Brāhmans); N. of<BR>the presiding genius of the mountains (personified in<BR>the Veda with Āptya, Rudra, and Ṛbhu as ruler of<BR>the clouds, and associated with Indra, Savitṛ, the<BR>Maruts, and other deities; in later times enumerated<BR>among the eight Vasus); a fragment of rock, bowl-<BR>der, stone, (अद्रयः पर्वताः, the stones with<BR>which the Soma plant is pressed); a cloud (Ved.; in<BR>some passages of the Ṛg-veda where पर्वत is<BR>interpreted by अद्रि, the sense ‘cloud’ seems equally<BR>applicable, especially when the battles of Indra or<BR>the deeds of the Maruts are described); a N. of the<BR>number 7 (from the 7 principal mountains); a tree;<BR>a kind of vegetable; a kind of fish (commonly<BR>called Pāvdā, the Silurus Pabda); N. of a divine<BR>Ṛṣi mentioned in several passages of the Mahā-bh.<BR>(regarded as a companion of Nārada and messenger<BR>of the gods, cf. Nala II. 14; he is the author of<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 12, IX. 104, 105, where he has the<BR>patronymics Kāṇva and Kāśyapa); N. of a son of<BR>Paurṇamāsa (a son of Marīci and Sam-bhūti); of a<BR>minister of king Purū-ravas; of a grammarian (?);<BR>of an ape; (ई), f. (Ved.) a rock, stone; [cf. Serv.<BR>brdo, ‘a mountain;’ perhaps Goth. fairguni.]<BR>—पर्वत-काक, अस्, m. a raven.<BR>—पर्वत-च्युत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, Ved. ‘causing mountains (clouds) to totter or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-a" target="_blank">Page0556-a+ 81</a>]<BR>fall,’ an epithet of the Maruts.<BR>—पर्वत-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, mountain-born; (आ), f. a river.<BR>—पर्वत-<BR>तृण, अम्, n. ‘mountain-grass,’ a species of grass<BR>(= तृणाढ्य).<BR>—पर्वत-पति, इस्, m. ‘moun-<BR>tain-prince,’ lord of the mountains.<BR>—पर्वत-<BR>मोचा, f. a species of plant (= गिरि-कदली).<BR>—पर्-<BR>वत-राज्, ट्, m. ‘mountain-king,’ a lofty mountain,<BR>‘the highest mountain-range,’ the Himālaya.<BR>—पर्-<BR>वत-राज, अस्, m. ‘mountain-king,’ the Himālaya.<BR>—पर्वतराज-कन्या, f. ‘daughter of the moun-<BR>tain-king,’ N. of Pārvatī or Durgā (daughter of<BR>Hima-vat, sovereign of the snowy mountains).<BR>—पर्-<BR>वतराज-पुत्री, f. ‘daughter of the mountain-king,’<BR>an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—पर्वत-वासिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>living in the mountains; (ई), m. a mountaineer;<BR>(इनी), f. nard, spikenard; a designation of Durgā; of<BR>the Gāyatrī.<BR>—पर्वत-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. the best of<BR>mountains.<BR>—पर्वत-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, situated on<BR>a mountain or hill.<BR>—पर्वताकार (˚त-आक्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, mountain-shaped, formed like a mountain.<BR>—पर्वतात्मजा (˚त-आत्˚), f. ‘daughter of the<BR>mountain,’ an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—पर्वताधारा<BR>(˚त-आध्˚), f. ‘receptacle of mountains,’ the earth.<BR>—पर्वतारि (˚त-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of the moun-<BR>tains,’ epithet of Indra (who clipped their wings).<BR>—पर्वता-वृध्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. delighting in moun-<BR>tains; (Sāy.) ‘delighting in the stones used to press the<BR>Soma plant’ or ‘produced in the mountains,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Soma.<BR>—पर्वताशय (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘rest-<BR>ing on the mountains,’ a cloud.<BR>—पर्वताश्रय (˚त-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, living on the mountains, a moun-<BR>taineer; (अस्), m. a fabulous animal, the Śarabha.<BR>—पर्वताश्रयिन् (˚त-आश्˚), ई, m. a dweller on the<BR>mountains, mountaineer.<BR>—पर्वती-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>-करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make into a mountain.<BR>—पर्-<BR>वतेश्वर (˚त-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a lord of the mountains.<BR>—पर्वते-ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. ‘dwelling in<BR>the heights,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0555-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वतक
पर्वतक in एक-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वतीय|पर्व्वतीय|पर्व्वतीयः
पर्वतीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to a<BR>mountain, mountainous, hilly; a mountaineer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वत्य
पर्वत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging to a moun-<BR>tain or rock; produced in mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वन्|पर्व्वन्
पर्वन्, अ, n. (said to be fr. rt. पॄ, but con-<BR>nected with पर्वत above), a knot or joint, espe-<BR>cially of a cane or other plant; a joint of the body,<BR>knuckle, limb, member; a break, pause, division,<BR>section; book, chapter; (in Vedic grammar) a mem-<BR>ber of a compound; a division of time, period,<BR>fixed time (especially the Cāturmāsya festival), the<BR>days of the four changes of the moon, i. e. the<BR>full and change of the moon and the eighth and<BR>fourteenth of each half month; the days of conjunction<BR>and opposition or eclipse of the sun or moon; a sacrifice<BR>performed on the occasion of a change of the moon; a<BR>particular period of the year (as the equinox, solstice,<BR>&c.); the moment of the sun's entering a new sign;<BR>a festival, holiday; opportunity, occasion; a moment,<BR>instant; [cf. परुस्.]<BR>—पर्व-कार, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>पर्व-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who works on holidays;<BR>(according to others) a Brāhman who for the sake of<BR>gain performs on common days such ceremonies as<BR>should be performed only on festivals.<BR>—पर्व-काल,<BR>अस्, m. a periodic change of the moon; the time at<BR>which the moon at its conjunction or opposition<BR>passes through the node.<BR>—पर्व-गामिन्, ई, m. one<BR>who has intercourse with his wife on festivals or holi-<BR>days.<BR>—पर्व-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—पर्-<BR>व-धि, इस्, m. ‘period-holder,’ the moon.<BR>—पर्व-<BR>नाडी, f. ‘moment of the Parvan,’ moment of opposi-<BR>tion or conjunction.<BR>—पर्व-पुष्पी or पर्व-पुष्-<BR>पिका, f. a plant, = राम-दूती, Tiaridium Indicum (=<BR>नाग-दन्ती).<BR>—पर्व-पूर्ण-ता, f. preparations for<BR>an assembly or festival; completion of a festival;<BR>joining, uniting.<BR>—पर्व-भेद, अस्, m. the fracture<BR>of a joint.<BR>—पर्व-मूल, अम्, n. the moment at<BR>which the fourteenth day passes into the fifteenth<BR>day of a month; (आ), f. a species of plant (= श्वेता).<BR>—पर्व-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, growing from joints or<BR>knots; (इस्), m. a cane or reed, the sugar-cane, &c.<BR>—पर्व-रुह्, ट्, m. a pomegranate tree.<BR>—पर्व-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">Page0556-b+ 75</a>]<BR>वर्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, except the forbidden days of<BR>a month.<BR>—पर्व-वल्ली, f. a species of Dūrvā<BR>(= ग्रन्थि-दूर्वा, मूल-दूर्वा).<BR>—पर्व-शर्क-<BR>रक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—पर्व-शस्, ind.,<BR>Ved. limb by limb, limb from limb, piece by<BR>piece; पर्वशः कृत्, to cut to pieces.<BR>—पर्-<BR>व-सन्धि, इस्, m. a joint; the full and change<BR>of the moon, the junction of the fifteenth and<BR>first of a lunar fortnight or the precise moment of<BR>the full and change of the moon.<BR>—पर्वावधि<BR>(˚व-अव्˚), इस्, m. a particular period, the end of a<BR>Parvan, &c.<BR>—पर्वास्फोट (˚व-आस्˚), अस्, m. a par-<BR>ticular movement of the fingers (regarded as inde-<BR>corous).<BR>—पर्वेश (˚व-ईश), अस्, m., Ved. the regent<BR>of an astronomical node.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वरीण|पर्व्वरीण|पर्व्वरीणं|पर्व्वरीणः
पर्वरीण, अस्, m. = पर्ण-वृन्त-रस; =<BR>गर्व; = मारुत; = पर्ण-शिरा; = मृतक; =<BR>द्यूत-कम्बल; = पत्त्र-चूर्ण-रस; = पर्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वत|पर्वतः|पर्व्वत|पर्व्वतः
पर्वत पर्वत, पर्वन्. See under rt. पर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्वित|पर्वितः|पर्व्वित|पर्व्वितः
पर्वित पर्वित, अस्, m. a species of fish,<BR>Silurus Pabda (= पर्वत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शान
पर्शान पर्शान, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rts. पर्ष् and पृष्), Ved. a precipice, chasm;<BR>a well; (Sāy.) = पार्श्व-स्थान, the side; = पीड्य-<BR>मान, being oppressed; = स्पृश्यमान; = विमर्-<BR>शन-क्षम; (according to the Naighaṇṭuka I.<BR>10) a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शु|पर्शुः
1. पर्शु, उस्, m., Ved. a rib; a curved knife,<BR>pruning-hook, sickle; N. of a man; (अवस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a warrior-tribe; (उस्), f. (according to the<BR>Nirukta IV. 6) the supporting or side wall of a well<BR>(Ṛg-veda I. 105, 8, but according to Sāy. = पार्-<BR>श्वास्थि); N. of a woman.<BR>—पर्शु-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, shaped like a curved knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुका
पर्शुका, f. a rib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शु|पर्शुः
पर्शु 2. पर्शु, उस्, m. (fr. पृ, substituted<BR>for rt. स्पृश्), = परशु, an axe, hatchet.<BR>—पर्शु-<BR>पाणि, इस्, m. ‘axe in hand, ’ an epithet of Gaṇeśa;<BR>[cf. परशु-धर.]<BR>—पर्शु-राम = परशु-रा-<BR>म, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्श्वध|पर्श्वधः
पर्श्वध, अस्, m. = परश्वध, an axe, hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ष्
पर्ष् पर्ष् [cf. rts. पृष्, वर्ष्, स्पर्ष्],<BR>cl. 1. A. पर्षते, &c., to grow wet, be-<BR>come moist; to delight in, accept (Sāy. = स्वी-कृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ष|पर्षः
पर्ष पर्ष, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with rt. पृष्), a bundle, sheaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षिन्
पर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. in इषु-प्˚, (probably)<BR>carrying bundles (of arrows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षणि
पर्षणि पर्षणि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. rt. 1. पृ),<BR>Ved. carrying over or across, ferrying across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षन्
पर्षन्, अ, n. (?), Ved. leading out, delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षिष्ठ
पर्षिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most mighty in<BR>delivering or rescuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षद्
पर्षद् पर्षद्, त्, f. = परिषद्, an assem-<BR>bly, audience.<BR>—पर्षद्-भीरु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>shy in society.<BR>—पर्षद्-वल, अस्, आ, अम्, = परि-<BR>षद्-वल, surrounded by an assembly; (अस्), m. an<BR>assistant at an assembly, a spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्
पल् पल्, cl. 1. P. पलति, पलितुम्, to<BR>go, move; cl. 10. पालयति, -यितुम्, see<BR>rt. 3. पा; [cf. Gr. πάλλω, παλμό-ς, πάλο-ς,<BR>πα-λάσσω, παλ-ύν-ω; Lat. pello, poll-en, pul-vi-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल, अस्, m. = पाल (Gaṇa Jvalādi to Pāṇ. III.<BR>1, 140); = पलाल, straw; (अम्), n. a particular<BR>weight (= 4 Karṣas = (1/100) of a Tulā); a particular<BR>measure of fluids; a particular measure of time (=<BR>विघटिका); flesh, meat; [cf. Lat. palea; Angl.<BR>Sax. flesc, flœsc, flec; Old Germ. fleisk; French<BR>paille; Hib. feol, feoile, ‘flesh.’]<BR>—पल-क्षार,<BR>अस्, m. ‘flesh-fluid,’ blood.<BR>—पल-गण्ड, अस्, m. a<BR>mason, bricklayer, plasterer.<BR>—पलङ्-कर, अस्, m.<BR>‘flesh-maker,’ gall, bile.<BR>—पलङ्-कष, अस्, m.<BR>‘flesh-hurter,’ a Rākṣasa, imp, goblin; bdellium;<BR>a species of bdellium (= कण-गुग्गुलु); (आ), f.,<BR>N. of various plants (= गो-क्षुरक, Asteracantha<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">Page0556-c+ 73</a>]<BR>Longifolia; = क्षुद्र-गोक्षुरक; = किंशुक,<BR>Butea Frondosa; = मुण्डीरी, a species of climbing<BR>plant; = रास्न; = महा-श्रावणी, bdellium); = लाक्-<BR>षा, cochineal; a fly.<BR>—पल-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond<BR>of meat,’ a Rākṣasa; a raven.<BR>—पल-भा or पल-<BR>विभा, f. the equinoctial shadow at midday, the<BR>midday shadow of a gnomon when the sun is in the<BR>equinoctial points (= विष्णुवत्-प्रभा).<BR>—पलाग्नि<BR>(˚ल-अग्˚), इस्, m. ‘flesh-fire,’ bile, the bilious humor.<BR>—पलाद (˚ल-अद), अस्, m. ‘flesh-eater,’ a Rāk-<BR>ṣasa; (आ), f. a Rākṣasī.<BR>—पलादन (˚ल-अद्˚),<BR>अस्, or 1. पलाश (˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, or 1. पलाशिन्<BR>(˚ल-आश्˚), ई, m. ‘flesh-eater,’ a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलद
पलद, अस्, m., Ved. a particular material for<BR>building, (perhaps) bundles of straw or reeds used<BR>for roofing and wainscoting; (ई), f., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलल|पललं|पललः
पलल, अस्, m. a Rākṣasa; ground sesamum<BR>seeds, a kind of sweetmeat made of ground sesamum<BR>and sugar; mud, mire, clay; = पल, flesh, meat;<BR>[cf. पल्वल; Gr. πηλό-ς, πήλ-ινο-ς,<BR>προ-πηλακ-ίζω; Lat. păl-ū(d)s, palus-tri-s; Hib. poll, ‘mire,<BR>dirt.’]<BR>—पलल-ज्वर, अस्, m. gall, bile; [cf. प-<BR>लाग्नि, पलङ्-कर.]<BR>—पलल-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond<BR>of flesh,’ a raven (= पल-प्रिय).<BR>—पललाशय<BR>(˚ल-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘flesh-receptacle,’ swelled neck,<BR>goitre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिक
पलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp. after<BR>a numeral), weighing or containing so many Palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलक्या
पलक्या पलक्या, f. a kind of vegetable<BR>(= पालङ्क्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलक्ष
पलक्ष पलक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, (a secondary<BR>form of बलक्ष), Ved. white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कट|पलंकट|पलङ्कटः
पलङ्कट पलङ्कट, अस्, आ, अम्, shy, bashful,<BR>timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलव|पलवः
पलव पलव, अस्, m. (said to be connected<BR>with rt. पल्, probably for प्लव fr. rt. प्लु), a snare<BR>or basket of wicker-work for catching fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलस
पलस पलस, अस्, m. = पनस, the bread<BR>fruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलस्ति
पलस्ति पलस्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (according<BR>to Sāy.) = पलित, grey-haired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाङ्ग|पलांग|पलाङ्गः
पलाङ्ग पलाङ्ग, अस्, m. Delphinus Gange-<BR>ticus; (perhaps an error for चपलाङ्ग.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाण्डु|पलांडु|पलाण्डुः
पलाण्डु पलाण्डु, उस्, उ, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. पल्), an onion.<BR>—पलाण्डु-भक्षित, अस्,<BR>आ or ई, अम्, one who has eaten onions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाप|पलापः
पलाप पलाप, अस्, m. a halter; an ele-<BR>phant's temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलापहा
पलापहा पलापहा, f. a kind of collyrium<BR>(= कुलत्था; perhaps only an error for प्र-<BR>लाप-हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाय
पलाय पलाय (fr. अय् = rt. 5. इ with पला =<BR>परा), cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.) पलायते (-ति), -यितुम्,<BR>to flee, run away, make off, take to one's heels,<BR>scamper off; to escape; to cease, die away, sink<BR>into oblivion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायक
पलायक, अस्, आ, or इका (?), अम्, fleeing, flying,<BR>taking to flight; a fugitive, runaway, deserter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायत्
पलायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, fleeing, running away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायन|पलायनं
पलायन, अम्, n. fleeing, running away, flight,<BR>escape; a saddle (= पल्ययन, पर्याण).<BR>—प-<BR>लायन-परायण, अस्, आ, अम्, occupied in flight,<BR>fugitive.<BR>—पलायन-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, thinking<BR>of flight.<BR>—पलायन-विषय, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>flight for an object, bent on flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायमान
पलायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, fleeing, flying away,<BR>taking to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायित|पलायितः
पलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, flown, run away, fled,<BR>retreated; defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायिन्
पलायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fleeing, flying, running away,<BR>taking to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाल|पलालं|पलालः
पलाल पलाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. पल्), straw; the stalk of the Sorghum,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">Page0557-a+ 73</a>]<BR>Indian millet; (अस्), m., Ved., N. of a demon (asso-<BR>ciated with Anu-palāla and considered dangerous to<BR>children); (आ), f., N. of one of the seven Mātṛs<BR>of Skanda; (ई), f. straw.<BR>—पलाल-दोहद, अस्, m.<BR>‘longing for straw,’ the mango tree (the fruit of<BR>which is sometimes ripened in straw).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0556-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाव|पलावः
पलाव पलाव, अस्, m., Ved. chaff, husks;<BR>[cf. Lat. palea.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाश|पलाशं|पलाशः
पलाश 2. पलाश, अम्, n. (for 1. see under<BR>पल, rt. पल्, p. 556, col. 2), a leaf, petal, foliage;<BR>the blossom of the tree Butea Frondosa; (अस्),<BR>m. Butea Frondosa; Curcuma Zedoaria; a N. of<BR>ancient Behar or Magadha; (ई), f. cochineal; a<BR>species of climbing plant (= पत्त्र-वल्ली, पर्ण-<BR>वल्ली, पलाशिका); (अस्, आ, अम्), green; unfeeling,<BR>unmerciful, cruel; (at the end of a comp.) see Gaṇa<BR>to Pāṇ. II. 1, 56.<BR>—पलाश-पत्त्र, अम्, n. the leaf<BR>of the Butea Frondosa; a single leaf; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a Nāga.<BR>—पलाश-पर्णी, f. Physalis Flexuosa<BR>(= अश्व-गन्धा).<BR>—पलाश-शातन, अस्, m. an<BR>instrument for lopping foliage.<BR>—पलाशाख्य (˚श-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, m. = नाडी-हिङ्गु, q. v.; Asa Fœtida.<BR>—पलाशान्ता (˚श-अन्˚) or पलाशाम्भा, f. =<BR>गन्ध-पत्त्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशक|पलाशकः
पलाशक, अस्, m. Butea Frondosa; Curcuma<BR>Zedoaria (= शटी); N. of a place; (इका), f. a species<BR>of climbing plant (= पलाशी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशिन्
2. पलाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ (for 1. see under पल, rt.<BR>पल्), leafy, covered with foliage, having luxuriant<BR>foliage; (ई), m. a tree; a species of plant (= क्षीर-<BR>वृक्ष); N. of a city or a village (said to be the<BR>modern Plassey); (इनी), f., N. of a river issuing from<BR>the Śukti-mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिक्नी
पलिक्नी पलिक्नी, f. See पलित below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिघ|पलिघः
पलिघ पलिघ, अस्, m. a water-pot, pitcher,<BR>glass water-vessel; a wall, rampart; the gate-way of<BR>a building; an iron club or one studded with iron<BR>(= परिघ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलित|पलितं|पलितः
पलित पलित, अस्, पलिक्नी, अम् (said to be<BR>fr. rt. फल् with substitution of प् for फ्; a doubtful<BR>fem. form पलिता is also given), grey, grey-haired,<BR>hoary, old, aged; (अस्), m., N. of a mouse in Mahā-<BR>bh. Śānti-p. 4933; (पलिक्नी), f. a cow for the first<BR>time with calf; (अम्), n. grey hair; a tuft of hair<BR>(= केश-पाश); much or ornamented hair; mud,<BR>mire; heat, burning; benzoin; [cf. Gr. πελ-ὀ-ς,<BR>πελ-ιό-ς, πελ-λό-ς, πελιδνό-ς, παλ-ιό-ς: Lat. pall-<BR>e-o, pall-idu-s, pallu-s: Old Germ. falo (fal-w-<BR>er): Angl. Sax. fealo, falu, fealwe, falewe: Slav.<BR>plavŭ, ‘white:’ Lith. pàl-va-s, ‘fallow;’ pī1l-ka-s,<BR>‘ash-coloured.’]<BR>—पलितङ्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, ren-<BR>dering grey.<BR>—पलितम्-भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, or<BR>पलितम्-भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming grey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलितिन्
पलितिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having grey hair, grey-haired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलियोग
पलियोग पलि-योग, अस्, m. = परि-योग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलीजक
पलीजक पलीजक, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्पूल्
पल्पूल् पल्पूल् (considered by some as<BR>a reduplicated form of rt. पल्), cl.<BR>10. P. पल्पूलयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to wash in lye<BR>or water impregnated with alkaline salt; to wash,<BR>cleanse; to tan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्पूलन
पल्पूलन, अम्, n., Ved. lye, water impregnated<BR>with alkaline salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्पूलित
पल्पूलित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. curried, tanned;<BR>washed (in lye).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्य|पल्यं
पल्य पल्य, अम्, n. (perhaps fr. पल), a<BR>sack for corn (probably containing a certain measure,<BR>Ved.); a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यङ्क|पल्यंक|पल्यंकः|पल्यङ्कः
पल्यङ्क पल्य्-अङ्क, अस्, m. = पर्य्-अङ्क, a<BR>bed, couch, bedstead; a cloth thrown round the loins<BR>while sitting (= पर्य्-अस्ति, पर्यस्तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यङ्ग्
पल्यङ्ग् पल्य्-अङ्ग् (for पर्य्-अङ्ग्), Caus. P.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">Page0557-b+ 77</a>]<BR>-अङ्गयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to cause to go round, stir<BR>round: Pass. -अङ्ग्यते, to turn round, revolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यय्
पल्यय् पल्य्-अय् (fr. अय् = rt. 5. इ with पलि<BR>= परि), cl. 1. A. -अयते, &c., Ved. to go round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ययन|पल्ययनं
पल्य्-अयन, अम्, n. = पर्याण, a saddle, pack-<BR>saddle; a rein, bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्युल्
पल्युल् पल्युल् and पल्यूल् (various<BR>readings for पल्पूल्, q. v.), cl. 10.<BR>P. पल्युलयति, पल्यूलयति, -यितुम्, to wash,<BR>&c.; to cut, cut off (in this sense perhaps for<BR>परि-लू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल्
पल्ल् पल्ल् [cf. rt. पल्], cl. 1. P. पल्लति,<BR>पल्लितुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल|पल्लः
पल्ल, अस्, m. a large granary, barn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लव|पल्लवं|पल्लवः
1. पल्लव, अस्, अम्, m. n. a sprout, shoot, twig,<BR>sprig, spray, (literally and as a metaphorical expression<BR>for the fingers, toes, and lips; cf. कर-प्˚, ओष्ठ-<BR>प्˚); a bud, blossom; a blade of grass; the extre-<BR>mity of a robe, the loose end of a garment or scarf;<BR>spreading, expansion; epithet of a particular position<BR>of the hands in dancing; the red dye called अ-लक्त;<BR>love, affection; a bracelet, armlet; unsteadiness<BR>moral or physical (?); strength, power (?); a wood (?);<BR>(अस्), m. a libertine, catamite; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—पल्लवग्राहि-ता, f. the picking up of<BR>twigs or straws, the dealing with trifles; superficial<BR>or diffusive knowledge.<BR>—पल्लव-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>putting forth young shoots, sprouting in all directions;<BR>twig-picking, straw-gathering; laying hold of trifles;<BR>diffusive; superficial; (ई), m., scil. दोष, the fault<BR>of prolixity or diffusiveness or of mere superficial<BR>knowledge.<BR>—पल्लव-द्रु, उस्, m. the Aśoka tree.<BR>—पल्लव-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of young<BR>shoots or twigs.<BR>—पल्लवाङ्कुर (˚व-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a leaf-bud.<BR>—पल्लवाद (˚व-अद), अस्, m. ‘eating<BR>young shoots,’ a deer.<BR>—पल्लवाधार (˚व-आध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘receptacle or support of twigs,’ a branch.<BR>—पल्लवापीडित (˚व-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bud-laden,<BR>loaded with buds.<BR>—पल्लवास्त्र (˚व-अस्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘having blossoms for missiles,’ an epithet of the<BR>god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लव|पल्लवं|पल्लवः
2. पल्लव, Nom. P. पल्लवति, पल्लवितुम्, to<BR>put forth young shoots, sprout, bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवक|पल्लवकः
पल्लवक, अस्, m. a libertine, gallant, the paramour<BR>of a harlot; a catamite; a species of fish, Cyprinus<BR>Denticulatus; (इका), f., N. of a female attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवय
पल्लवय, Nom. P. पल्लवयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>put forth young shoots, sprout; to cause to sprout,<BR>to make diffuse or prolix (according to a Scholiast<BR>= विस्तारय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविक|पल्लविकः
पल्लविक, अस्, m. a libertine, gallant; a catamite;<BR>a species of fish, Cyprinus Denticulatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवित|पल्लवितं|पल्लवितः
पल्लवित, अस्, आ, अम्, sprouting, having young<BR>shoots; spread, extended; dyed red with lac, pos-<BR>sessing the red dye; (अस्), m. the red dye of the<BR>lac insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविन्
पल्लविन्, ई, इनी, इ, sprouting, having young shoots;<BR>(ई), m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लि|पल्लिः
पल्लि, इस्, or ई, f. a small village, especially a settle-<BR>ment of wild tribes; a hut, house; any number of<BR>houses, a station; a city (or rather an affix to words<BR>forming the name of towns; it is especially used in<BR>the Dekhan as in Trichinopoly = Triśira-pallī, &c.);<BR>a small house-lizard; a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लिका
पल्लिका, f. a village, station [cf. आभीर-प्˚]; a<BR>small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लि|पल्लिः
पल्लि पल्लि. See under rt. पल्ल् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लिवाह|पल्लिवाहः
पल्लिवाह पल्लिवाह, अस्, m. a species of<BR>grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वल|पल्वलं
पल्वल पल्वल, अस्, m. (connected with प-<BR>लित; said to be fr. rt. पल्), a small tank, pond, pool;<BR>[cf. Gr. πηλό-ς, πήλ-ινο-ς, προ-πηλακ-ίζω; Lat. pal-<BR>u(d)-s, palus-tri-s; perhaps Angl. Sax. pol, ‘a pool.’]<BR>—पल्वल-तीर, अम्, n. the bank or margin of a<BR>pool.<BR>—पल्वल-पङ्क, अस्, m. the mud of a<BR>pool.<BR>—पल्वलावास (˚ल-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘living in<BR>ponds,’ a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वल्य
पल्वल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. marshy, boggy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव्
पव् पव्, cl. 1. A. पवते, पवितुम्, to<BR>go; (a various reading for प्लव्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव|पवं|पवः
पव पव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. पू), purification,<BR>purity; winnowing corn; air, wind; a marsh; (आ),<BR>f. purification; (अम्), n. cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवत्
पवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, purifying; pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवन|पवनं|पवनः
पवन, अम्, n. the act of purifying, purification;<BR>winnowing; an instrument for purifying, sieve,<BR>strainer, &c.; water; (अस्), m. ‘the purifier,’ wind,<BR>air, the wind of the body; Wind personified (as<BR>regent of the Nakṣatra Svāti and of the North-west<BR>region); a N. of the number five (Ved.); a house-<BR>holder's sacred fire; N. of a son of Manu Uttama;<BR>of the author of a Gāndharva-veda; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. a potter's kiln; (ई), f. a broom; N. of a river;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), clean, pure.<BR>—पवन-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, tempest-tossed.<BR>—पवन-तनय, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of the Wind,’ an epithet of Hanu-mat.<BR>—पवन-वा-<BR>हन, अस्, m. ‘having wind as a vehicle,’ fire.<BR>—प-<BR>वन-विजय, अस्, m. ‘victory over the wind or<BR>breath,’ N. of a mystic work.<BR>—पवन-व्याधि,<BR>इस्, m. an epithet of Ud-dhava, the friend and<BR>counsellor of Kṛṣṇa; morbid condition of wind,<BR>rheumatism, &c.<BR>—पवनात्मज (˚न-आत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘son of the Wind;’ fire; an epithet of Hanu-<BR>mat the monkey-hero.<BR>—पवनाश (˚न-आश),<BR>or पवनाशन (˚न-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘feeding on<BR>air,’ a serpent, snake.<BR>—पवनाश-नाश, अस्, m.<BR>‘snake-destroyer,’ a peacock; Garuḍa the bird and<BR>vehicle of Viṣṇu.<BR>—पवनाशिन् (˚न-आश्˚), ई, m.<BR>‘feeding on air,’ a serpent.<BR>—पवनाहत (˚न-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, struck or shaken by the wind;<BR>rheumatic.<BR>—पवनोद्भ्रान्त-कारिन् (˚न-उद्˚), ई,<BR>इणी, इ, ‘agitating the air,’ epithet of a particular mode<BR>of fighting.<BR>—पवनोद्भ्रान्त-वीचि, इस्, इस्, m. f.<BR>a wave tossed up by the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमान|पवमानः
पवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being purified, being<BR>strained (usually said of the Soma, Ved.); (अस्), m.<BR>wind; N. of a particular Fire (associated with<BR>Pāvaka and Śuci, and also regarded as a son of<BR>Agni by Svāhā); epithet of the moon; epithet of<BR>particular Stotras sung by the Sāma-ga at the Jyo-<BR>tiṣṭoma (Ved.).<BR>—पवमान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. having the Pavamāna-stotra.<BR>—पवमान-<BR>हविस्, इस्, n. or पवमानेष्टि (˚न-इष्˚), इस्, f.,<BR>Ved. offerings to Agni invoked under the title of<BR>Pavamāna or Pāvaka or Śuci.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवयितृ
पवयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who purifies or<BR>cleans, a purifier, cleanser, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवाका
पवाका, f. a storm, whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवि|पविः
पवि, इस्, m., Ved. the tire of a wheel; the<BR>metallic point of a spear or arrow; a thunderbolt;<BR>an arrow; speech; fire; [cf. आर्द्र-प्˚, कृष्ण-प्˚,<BR>क्षुर-प्˚.]<BR>—पवी-नस, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘having a<BR>nose like a spear-head,’ epithet of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित|पवितः
पवित, अस्, आ, अम्, purified, cleansed; (अम्), n.<BR>black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवितृ
पवितृ or Ved. पवीतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who<BR>purifies or cleanses, a purifier, cleanser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्र|पवित्रं|पवित्रः
पवित्र, अम्, n. a means of purification, instru-<BR>ment for cleansing, filter, strainer, straining-cloth,<BR>colander (made of thread or hair or straw plaited<BR>or woven, for clarifying fluids, especially the Soma);<BR>Kuśa grass (especially a couple of Kuśa leaves a<BR>span long used at sacrifices to present offerings<BR>upon or to sprinkle and purify ghee, &c.); a ring<BR>of Kuśa grass worn on the fourth finger on par-<BR>ticular occasions; a purifying prayer or Mantra;<BR>water, rain; rubbing, cleansing; the vessel in<BR>which the Argha is presented; copper; the<BR>sacred thread, Brāhmanical cord; melted butter;<BR>honey; any divinity as Agni &c.?; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a Soma-yāga belonging to the Rāja-sūya; the<BR>sesame plant, Nageia Putranjiva; N. of a man (of<BR>the family of Aṅgiras and the reputed author of<BR>Ṛg-veda IX. 67, 73, 83, 107); (आस्), m. pl. epithet<BR>of a class of deities in the fourteenth Manv-antara;<BR>(आ), f., N. of various plants; basil; Indian saffron,<BR>turmeric; = अश्वत्थी, q. v.; N. of a river (the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">Page0558-a+ 75</a>]<BR>Pabar, a little to the north-west of Hari-dwār); the<BR>twelfth day of the light half of Śrāvaṇa (a festival in<BR>honour of Viṣṇu); (अस्, आ, अम्), purifying, cleans-<BR>ing; pure, clean; holy, sinless; averting evil; [cf.<BR>Hib. beathra, ‘water;’ fothragaim, ‘I bathe,<BR>cleanse;’ fothragadh, ‘a bath, well of purification.’]<BR>—पवित्र-ता, f. or पवित्र-त्व, अम्, n. purity,<BR>cleanness.<BR>—पवित्र-धान्य, अम्, n. ‘pure grain,’<BR>barley.<BR>—पवित्र-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the<BR>Pavitra.<BR>—पवित्र-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘pure-handed,’<BR>having clean hands or holding Darbha grass in the<BR>hand; (इस्), m., N. of an ancient sage.<BR>—पवित्र-<BR>पूत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. clarified with a strainer or co-<BR>lander.<BR>—पवित्र-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the<BR>colander as a chariot (said of the Soma).<BR>—पवित्र-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having an instrument for<BR>purifying (as a strainer or Darbha grass); purifying,<BR>cleansing; being in the colander; holding Darbha<BR>grass; an epithet of Agni; (अती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—पवित्रारोपण (˚र-आर्˚), अम्, n. ‘putting on<BR>the Pavitra,’ investiture with the Brāhmanical cord;<BR>investing the image of Kṛṣṇa with the sacred<BR>thread; N. of a festival on the twelfth day of the<BR>light half of Śrāvaṇa.<BR>—पवित्रारोहण (˚र-आर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘putting on the Pavitra,’ investing with the<BR>sacred thread, N. of a festival in honour of Durgā<BR>on the eighth day of the light half of the month<BR>Śrāvaṇa or Āṣāḍha.<BR>—पवित्री-करण, अम्, n.<BR>purification, cleansing; the instrument or means of<BR>purifying.<BR>—पवित्री-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to purify, cleanse.<BR>—पवित्री-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, purified, cleansed, cleaned, sanctified.<BR>—पवित्री-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become pure or clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0557-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रक|पवित्रकं|पवित्रकः
पवित्रक, अम्, n. a small strainer or colander,<BR>the vessel in which an Argha or oblation is pre-<BR>sented (?); pack-thread or a rope or net made of<BR>pack-thread; (अस्), m., N. of several sacred plants,<BR>Poa Cynosuroides (= कुश); Artemisia Indica (=<BR>दमनक); Ficus Religisa; Ficus Glomerata;<BR>(at the end of a comp.) = पवित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रय
पवित्रय, Nom. P. पवित्रयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cleanse, purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रित|पवित्रितः
पवित्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed, purified, clean, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रिन्
पवित्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, purifying, cleansing; pure,<BR>clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीर|पवीरं
पवीर, अम्, n., Ved. a weapon with a metallic<BR>point, a lance, spear.<BR>—पवीर-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. armed with a lance or spear; having a goad;<BR>having a metallic share (said of a plough).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीरव
पवीरव, अस्, m., Ved. having a metallic share<BR>(said of a plough); (Sāy.) = कुलिश or कुलिश-शब्द,<BR>a thunderbolt or the noise of a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीरु
पवीरु, उस्, m., Ved. (probably) a flash of light-<BR>ning, a thunderbolt; N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव्या
पव्या, f., Ved. purification, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाल|पवनालः
पवनाल पवनाल, अस्, m. a species of grain,<BR>Andropogon Saccharatus (= देव-धान्य; incor-<BR>rectly for यवनाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनेष्ट|पवनेष्टः
पवनेष्ट पवनेष्ट, अस्, m. a large species<BR>of Nimba tree; (probably incorrectly for यव-<BR>नेष्ट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनोम्बुज|पवनोम्बुजं
पवनोम्बुज पवनोम्बुज, अम्, n. = परूष,<BR>the Parush tree; (probably an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पविन्द
पविन्द पविन्द, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीतृ
पवीतृ पवीतृ. See पवितृ, p. 557, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीनस
पवीनस पवी-नस. See under पवि, p. 557.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीर|पवीरं
पवीर पवीर, अम्, n. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्
पश् 1. पश्, for original स्पश् substituted<BR>for rt. 1. दृश्, q. v., ‘to see,’ in certain<BR>tenses; [cf. rt. स्पश्, स्पश: Zend श्पश्, ‘to see,<BR>guard;’ śpaś, ‘a spy:’ Gr. σκεπ by metathesis for<BR>σπεκ in σκέπ-τ-ο-μαι, σκοπ-ή, σκοπιά, σκόπ-ελο-ς,<BR>σκοπ-ό-ς, σκώψ: Lat. spec-i-o, con-spici-o, specula,<BR>speculum, specu-s, spec-to: Old Germ. speh-ō-m,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">Page0558-b+ 80</a>]<BR>spāh-i: Mod. Germ. späh-en: Lith. spega-s, ‘a<BR>spy:’ Hib. faic-im, ‘I see;’ feach-aim, ‘I look,<BR>view;’ faoch-og, ‘an eye.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्
2. पश्, according to some the form पड्भिस् in<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 2, 12, may be connected with a base<BR>पश् derived fr. rt. 1. पश् in the sense of ‘sight,’<BR>‘look,’ ‘eye.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशु|पशुः
1. पशु, ind. see! behold!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
1. पश्य, Ved. or पश्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, seeing,<BR>beholding, surveying, rightly understanding; [cf.<BR>अ-प्˚, अ-सूर्यम्-पश्या.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
2. पश्य (2nd sing. imperative of rt. 1. दृश्), lo!<BR>behold! see! (an exclamation of wonder or admi-<BR>ration.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यत्
पश्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, seeing, beholding, looking,<BR>viewing, observing, remarking; regarding, consider-<BR>ing; (अन्ती), f. a courtezan, harlot; epithet of a<BR>particular sound.<BR>—पश्यतो-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, steal-<BR>ing before a person's eyes or in the very sight of the<BR>possessor; (अस्), m. a thief, pilferer (a term of re-<BR>proach proverbially applied to the goldsmith &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यत
पश्यत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. visible, conspicuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यना
पश्यना, f., in अ-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्
पश् 3. पश्, cl. 10. P. पाशयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to bind; [cf. Zend paś, ‘to bind;’ Gr.<BR>πήγ-νυ-μι, ἐ-πάγ-ην, πῆγ-μα, πηγ-ό-ς, πάγ-ο-ς,<BR>πάχ-νη, πάγ-η, πάσσ-αλα-ς: Lat. pac-i-sc-or, pâx,<BR>pac-i-o(n), pang-o, pig-nus, pâ-lu-s, com-pe-sc-o,<BR>dis-pe-sc-o: Goth. fah-an, ‘to catch;’ fulla-fah-<BR>jan, ‘to fulfil;’ fagr-s: Old Germ. fuog-a, ga-<BR>fuogi, gafag-jan, fah: Cambro-Brit. fasgu, ‘to<BR>bind or tie in a bundle;’ fasgiad, ‘a ligation, a<BR>tying in a bundle.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशव्य|पशव्यं
पशव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>cattle, fit or suitable for cattle (as a meadow, pas-<BR>turage, &c.); relating to a herd or drove; possessed<BR>of cattle; brutish; (with काम) sexual love, sexual<BR>intercourse; (अम्), n. a herd or drove of cattle; a<BR>stall for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशु|पशुः
2. पशु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. पश्, ‘to bind,’ like<BR>Lat. bestia fr. rt. बन्ध्; also said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>पश्; Vedic forms are du. पश्वा, acc. pl. पश्वस्,<BR>inst. पश्वा, dat. पश्वे, gen. पश्वस्), cattle (both<BR>singly and collectively), a herd, drove; any smaller<BR>animal used as a sacrificial victim, a goat; an animal<BR>in general, any domestic animal, (ग्राम्याः पशवः,<BR>domestic animals, of which five kinds are enumerated,<BR>men, kine, horses, goats, and sheep, to which are<BR>sometimes added mules and asses or camels and<BR>dogs); a brute, beast, (आरण्याः or वन्याः पशवः,<BR>wild beasts, beasts of the forest; sometimes said con-<BR>temptuously of a man; cf. पुरुष-प्˚); a mere<BR>animal in sacred things, an uninitiated person; a<BR>victim [cf. नृ-प्˚]; an oblation; a subordinate deity<BR>and one of Śiva's followers; (with Māheśvaras and<BR>Pāśupatas) soul, the Supreme Spirit, the divine soul of<BR>the universe; Ficus Glomerata; (उ), n., Ved. cattle; an<BR>animal, beast; [cf. Lat. pecu; Old Pruss. pecku; Goth.<BR>faih-u; Old Germ. fih-u; Mod. Germ. vieh, ‘cat-<BR>tle;’ perhaps Gr. πῶῑ.]<BR>—पशु-कर्मन्, अ, n., Ved.<BR>the act of offering the victim; sacrifice; copulation.<BR>—पशु-कल्प, अस्, m., Ved. the ritual of animal sa-<BR>crifice.<BR>—पशु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desirous of<BR>possessing cattle.<BR>—पशु-क्रिया, f. the act of animal<BR>sacrifice; acting like cattle, copulation.<BR>—पशु-गा-<BR>यत्री, f. a parody of the holy verse of the Vedas<BR>whispered into the ear of an animal about to be<BR>sacrificed (पशु-पाशाय विद्महे शिरश्-छेदाय<BR>धीमहि तन् नः पशुः प्रचोदयात्).<BR>—पशु-<BR>घात, अम्, n. slaughter of animals for sacrifice.<BR>—पशु-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, slaughtering cattle.<BR>—प-<BR>शु-चर्या, f. acting like cattle; copulation.<BR>—पशु-<BR>चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. piled up with cattle (as a sacrificial<BR>fire).<BR>—पशु-जातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, pertaining to the<BR>animal kingdom.<BR>—पशु-तन्त्र, अस्, m. = पशु-<BR>कल्प, q. v.<BR>—पशु-ता, f. or पशु-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>condition or nature of an animal, bestiality, brutality;<BR>the condition of a sacrificial animal, the being a sa-<BR>crificial animal; the sacrifice of an animal.<BR>—पशु-<BR>तृप्, प्, प्, प्, Ved. gratifying one's self with cattle,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-c" target="_blank">Page0558-c+ 81</a>]<BR>i. e. stealing cattle; (Sāy.) = पशूनां तर्पयितृ,<BR>feeding cattle.<BR>—पशु-द, अस्, आ, अम्, making a<BR>grant of cattle; (आ), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—पशु-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, mak-<BR>ing a grant of cattle.<BR>—पशु-देवत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. invoking cattle as a deity (said of a for-<BR>mula or ceremony); (आ), f. the deity of the<BR>victim, i. e. the deity to whom the sacrifice is<BR>offered.<BR>—पशु-धर्म, अस्, m. the characteristics<BR>of cattle, conduct of cattle, treatment of cattle;<BR>promiscuous cohabitation; the marrying of widows;<BR>(एण), ind. like a beast.<BR>—पशु-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of cattle,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पशु-प, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, guarding or keeping cattle; (अस्), m. a herds-<BR>man.<BR>—पशु-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the animals’ (or<BR>according to others ‘lord of a servant named Paśu’),<BR>an epithet of the later Rudra (Rudra-Śiva) or of a<BR>similar deity (often associated in the Veda with<BR>Bhava, Śarva, Ugra, Rudra, Mahā-deva, Īśāna, and<BR>others, who together with Bhīma are in later times<BR>regarded as manifestations of the one deity Rudra);<BR>= Śiva; N. of a scholiast; of a lexicographer; of Agni;<BR>(according to one legend every deity acknowledged<BR>himself to be a mere पशु or animal before his lord<BR>and master Śiva, when they solicited him to destroy the<BR>Asura Tri-pura.)<BR>—पशुपति-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—पशुपति-शास्त्र, अम्, n. the sacred book<BR>of the Pāśupatas revealed by Śiva.<BR>—पशु-पल्वल,<BR>अम्, n. a fragrant grass, Cyperus Rotundus (which<BR>grows in pools frequented by cattle).<BR>—पशु-पा, आस्,<BR>m., Ved. a keeper of herds, herdsman; an epithet of<BR>Pūṣan; (आ), m. du. epithet of Pūṣan and Revatī.<BR>—पशु-पाल, अस्, m. a keeper of herds, herdsman;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people to the N. E. of Madhya-<BR>deśa; (अम्), n. the country or kingdom of the Paśu-<BR>pālas; (अस्), m., N. of a king (or perhaps a king of the<BR>Paśu-pālas).<BR>—पशु-पालक, अस्, m. a herdsman;<BR>(इका), f. a herdsman's wife.<BR>—पशु-पालन, अम्,<BR>n. tending or rearing cattle.<BR>—पशु-पाल्य, अम्, n.<BR>breeding cattle.<BR>—पशु-पाश, अस्, m. the cord with<BR>which the victim is bound, binding the victim at a<BR>sacrifice; an animal sacrifice; the chains which fetter<BR>the individual soul, the world of sense.<BR>—पशु-<BR>पाशक, अस्, m. a kind of coitus.<BR>—पशु-प्रेरण,<BR>अम्, n. the driving of cattle.<BR>—पशु-बन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. an animal sacrifice; N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—पशु-<BR>बन्धक, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?), a rope for<BR>tethering cattle.<BR>—पशु-भर्तृ, ता, m. ‘lord of<BR>cattle,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पशु-भेद, अस्, m. a<BR>class or species of animals.<BR>—पशु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>connected with cattle or animals, relating to cattle or<BR>animals; rich in cattle, rich in herds; connected<BR>with animal sacrifices; containing the word पशु;<BR>(अत्), n. possession of cattle.<BR>—पशु-मार, अस्, m.<BR>the manner of slaughtering cattle; (अम्, एण), ind.<BR>according to the manner of slaughtering cattle.<BR>—पशु-मारक, अस्, आ, अम्, attended with the<BR>sacrifice of animals, accompanied by immolation of<BR>animals.<BR>—पशु-मोहनिका, f. ‘stupefying animals,’<BR>a species of plant (= कट्वी).<BR>—पशु-यज्ञ, अस्, m.<BR>an animal sacrifice.<BR>—पशु-याग, अस्, m. the sa-<BR>crifice of animals.<BR>—पशु-रक्षण, अम्, n. the<BR>tending of cattle.<BR>—पशु-रक्षि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>keeping or tending cattle; (इस्), m. a herdsman.<BR>—पशु-रक्षिन्, ई, m. ‘tending cattle,’ a herdsman,<BR>shepherd.<BR>—पशु-रज्जु, उस्, f. a cord for tethering<BR>cattle, a tether for animals.<BR>—पशु-राज, अस्, m.<BR>‘monarch of the beasts,’ a lion.<BR>—पशु-रोमन्, अ,<BR>n. the hair of an animal.<BR>—पशु-वत्, ind. like an<BR>animal, brutally; (Ved.) as in an animal (sacrifice).<BR>—पशु-वर्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. increasing<BR>cattle, causing cattle to thrive; (अम्), n. the thriving<BR>of cattle.<BR>—पशु-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. providing cattle.<BR>—पशु-शीर्ष, अम्, n. the head of an animal.<BR>—पशु-श्रपण, अम्, n., Ved. cooking a sacrificial<BR>animal; (अस्), m., scil. अग्नि, the fire on which the<BR>victim's flesh is cooked.<BR>—पशु-ष, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>पशु-षा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. bestowing cattle.<BR>—पशु-<BR>ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. existing or found in cattle.<BR>—पशु-सख, अस्, m. ‘friend of cattle,’ N. of a<BR>Śūdra.<BR>—पशु-सनि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. bestowing cattle.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-a" target="_blank">Page0559-a+ 79</a>]<BR>—पशु-समाम्नाय, अस्, m. ‘enumeration of sa-<BR>crificial animals,’ N. of a section of the Vājasaneyi-<BR>saṃhitā.<BR>—पशुसमाम्नायिक, अस्, ई, अम्, men-<BR>tioned in books on animal sacrifices.<BR>—पशु-सम्-<BR>भव, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by animals (as flesh,<BR>honey, butter, &c.).<BR>—पशु-साधन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. leading or guiding cattle.<BR>—पशु-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—पशु-हरीतकी, f. the fruit of<BR>the Spondias Mangifera<BR>—पशु-हव्य, अम्, n.<BR>sacrifice of animals.<BR>—पशु-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -क-<BR>रोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to transform into an animal;<BR>to offer as a victim.<BR>—पश्व-इष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr.<BR>पश्वस्, acc. pl. of पशु and इष्टि), Ved. wishing<BR>for herds; (इस्), f. desire of cattle; (Sāy.) = अग्नेर्<BR>इष्टिः, a fire offering, offering by fire.<BR>—पश्व्-<BR>अयन, अम्, n., Ved. a festival attended with animal<BR>sacrifices.<BR>—पश्व-यन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. पश्व<BR>for पश्वस् + यन्त्र), Ved. being within the cattle-<BR>fold; (Sāy.) provided with the means of letting out<BR>or extricating cattle.<BR>—पश्व्-अवदान, अम्, n. sa-<BR>crifice or offering of animals.<BR>—पश्व्-आचार, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a particular form of the worship of Devī.<BR>—पश्व्-इज्या, f., Ved. animal sacrifice.<BR>—पश्व्-इष्,<BR>ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. wishing for cattle; (Sāy.) driving cattle,<BR>a cattle-driver.<BR>—पश्व्-इष्टका, f., Ved. bricks in the<BR>shape of animals.<BR>—पश्व्-एकादशिनी, f. an aggregate<BR>of eleven sacrificial animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुका
पशुका, f. any small animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्च
पश्च पश्च, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पस् = अपस् = अप<BR>+ च fr. rt. अञ्च्; cf. उच्च, नीच, तिरश्चीन), being<BR>behind; posterior, later; western, westerly; (अ),<BR>ind., Ved. afterwards; (आ), ind., Ved. behind, at the<BR>back, abaft, after; afterwards, later; westward; (आत्),<BR>ind. from behind, from the back, behind (पश्चात्-<BR>कृ, to leave behind, surpass, excel), to or towards<BR>the back, backwards (e. g. पश्चाद् अपसरद् यानम्,<BR>a carriage moving backwards); after, afterwards,<BR>subsequently, at a later time, in later times, at last;<BR>from the west, westward, to the west of; ततः<BR>पश्चात्, thereupon, after that; उत्तरतः-पश्चात्,<BR>from the north-west. As a prep. पश्चात् governs<BR>the gen. or abl., e. g. रथस्य पश्चात्, behind the<BR>chariot; [cf. probably Lat. post, pone for pos-ne,<BR>postid-ea: Gr. ὀπίσσω: Lith. paskuy, ‘afterwards;’<BR>paskuttinis, paskiausas, ‘last:’ Old Pruss. pans-<BR>dan, ‘afterwards:’ Hib. feasd, feasda, ‘hereafter,<BR>henceforward, forthwith.’]<BR>—पश्चाच्-चर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, coming or approaching behind.<BR>—पश्चाच्-छ्र-<BR>मण, अस्, m. a Buddhist priest who walks behind<BR>another Buddhist priest in visiting the laity.<BR>—पश्-<BR>चात्-कर्णम्, ind., Ved. behind the ear.<BR>—पश्चात्-<BR>काल, अस्, m. subsequent time; (ए), ind. in later<BR>times, afterwards.<BR>—पश्चात्-तप्, cl. 1. P. A. -तपति,<BR>-ते, -तप्तुम्, to feel pain after, regret, repent, feel<BR>remorse.<BR>—पश्चात्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. later, pos-<BR>terior.<BR>—पश्चात्-ताप, अस्, m. ‘after-pain,’ sorrow,<BR>regret, repentance, remorse; पश्चात्तापं कृ, to<BR>feel regret, repent.<BR>—पश्चात्-तापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, re-<BR>gretting, repenting.<BR>—पश्चात्-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. sitting<BR>behind or towards the west.<BR>—पश्चाद्-अक्षम्, ind.,<BR>Ved. behind the axle-tree.<BR>—पश्चाद्-अपवर्ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. closed or completed behind.<BR>—पश्चाद्-<BR>आगत्य, ind. having returned.<BR>—पश्चाद्-आयात्, आन्,<BR>आती or आन्ती, आत्, coming behind, following.<BR>—पश्चा-<BR>दोष, अस्, m., Ved. the later part of the evening.<BR>—पश्चाद्-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, remaining behind,<BR>following after.<BR>—पश्चाद्-वात, अस्, m., Ved. a wind<BR>from behind, a west wind.<BR>—पश्चानुताप (˚च-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. regret, repentance.<BR>—पश्चानुपूर्वी<BR>(˚च-अन्˚), f. a repeated or recurring series.<BR>—पश्-<BR>चान्-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk or depressed behind.<BR>—पश्चान्-मारुत, अस्, m. a wind blowing from<BR>behind.<BR>—पश्चार्ध (˚च-अर्˚), अस्, m. the hinder<BR>side or part; the remaining half or part; the west<BR>side.<BR>—पश्चार्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being on the<BR>hinder side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चातात्
पश्चातात्, ind., Ved. from behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिम|पश्चिमं
पश्चिम, अस्, आ, अम्, being behind, hinder, hind-<BR>most; latter, last (e. g. पश्चिमा सन्ध्या, the<BR>latter, i. e. the evening twilight; पश्चिमा क्रिया,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">Page0559-b+ 75</a>]<BR>the last rite, burning the dead); west, western,<BR>westerly; (आ), f., scil. दिश्, the west; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a Tantra; (एन), ind. behind (with acc.), after;<BR>in the west; (ए), ind. in the west; [cf. उत्तर-प्˚,<BR>दक्षिण-प्˚.]<BR>—पश्चिम-जन, आस्, m. pl., Ved.<BR>the people in the west, the inhabitants of the western<BR>districts of India.<BR>—पश्चिम-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tantra.<BR>—पश्चिम-तस्, ind. from behind.<BR>—पश्-<BR>चिम-दर्शन, अम्, n. a last look; पश्चिम-दर्-<BR>शनं द्रष्टुम्, to see for the last time.<BR>—पश्-<BR>चिम-देश, अस्, m., N. of a district mentioned in<BR>the Romaka-Siddhānta.<BR>—पश्चिमानूपक (˚म-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—पश्चिमाभिमुख<BR>(˚म-अभ्˚), अस्, आ or ई, अम्, directed towards the<BR>west.<BR>—पश्चिमार्ध (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, m. the latter<BR>half, the hinder part.<BR>—पश्चिमोत्तर (˚म-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, north-westerly, north-western; (अस्याम्),<BR>loc. sing. f., scil. दिशि, Ved. in the north-west; (ए), ind.<BR>in the north-west.<BR>—पश्चिमोत्तर-दिक्पति, इस्, m.<BR>the regent of the north-west, the god of wind, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
पश्य पश्य, पश्यत्, पश्यत. See under<BR>rt. 1. पश्, p. 558.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पष्
पष् पष्, cl. 1. P. A. पषति, -ते, प-<BR>षितुम्, a various reading for rt. स्पश्,<BR>q. v.; cl. 10. P. पषयति, -यितुम्, to bind; to<BR>hinder; to touch; to go; पाषयति, -यितुम्, a<BR>various reading for rt. 3. पश्, p. 558, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पष्ठवाह्
पष्ठवाह् पष्ठ-वाह्, ट्, m. (said to be fr.<BR>पष्ठ = पृष्ठ + वाह्), Ved. a bull four years<BR>old; (पष्ठौही), f. a heifer four years old,<BR>(probably) a young cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्
पस् 1. पस्, cl. 1. P. A. पसति, -ते, प-<BR>सितुम्, a various reading for rt. स्पश्,<BR>q. v.; cl. 10. P. पासयति, -यितुम्, a various reading<BR>for rt. 3. पश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्
पस् 2. पस्, the pudenda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पसस्
पसस्, अस्, n., Ved. membrum virile; [cf. Gr.<BR>πέος, πόσ-θη: Lat. pên-is: Old Germ. visellin,<BR>‘penis:’ Lith. pis-á, ‘cunnus;’ pís-ti, ‘coire cum<BR>muliere.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्त्य|पस्त्यं
पस्त्य पस्त्य, अम्, n., Ved. habitation, abode,<BR>stall, stable; (आस्), m. pl. a house, dwelling, residence;<BR>household, family; (Sāy.) = दैव्यः प्रजाः, divine<BR>progeny; = मनुष्य, a man; = ऋत्व्-इज्, a priest;<BR>(आ), f. the goddess of domestic affairs; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>to be approached by all, venerated (Sāy. = सर्वैर्<BR>गन्तव्यः).<BR>—पस्त्य-सद्, त्, m., Ved. a member<BR>of a family; (Sāy.) = देव-यजन-लक्षणे गृहे<BR>निषण्णः, seated in the chamber of divine worship.<BR>—पस्त्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a fixed<BR>habitation; filled with habitations, abounding in<BR>dwellings or sacrificial halls (Sāy. = गृह-वत्, यज्ञ-<BR>गृहोपेत); belonging to the Soma press; (आन्),<BR>m. a householder, a wealthy man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्पृश्
पस्पृश् पस्पृश्, Ved. in अ-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लव
पह्लव पह्लव, आस्, m., N. of a people, the<BR>Persians, (also spelt पह्नव; in the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa<BR>they are said to be a degraded Kṣatriya race con-<BR>quered by Sagara and sentenced by him to wear<BR>beards, see Wilson's Viṣṇu-Purāṇa, p. 375.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लिका
पह्लिका पह्लिका, f. Pistia Stratiotes (=<BR>वारि-प्रश्नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा 1. पा, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.) पिबति<BR>(in later works generally written पिवति),<BR>-ते (Ved. पाति), पपौ, पास्यति, अपात्, पातुम्<BR>(Ved. पातवे, पिबध्यै), to drink, quaff (some-<BR>times with gen. in Ved., e. g. मध्वः पिबन्ति<BR>गौर्यः, the white cows drink of the sweet Soma<BR>juice); to inhale, swallow (dust); to drink in,<BR>imbibe (metaphorically, e. g. पिबन् यशो मूर्तम्<BR>इव, drinking in as it were embodied glory); to<BR>feast on (with the eyes or ears, e. g. तं सा पपौ<BR>लोचनाभ्याम्, she feasted on him with her eyes);<BR>to drink up, absorb, swallow up; to drink intoxi-<BR>cating liquors: Caus. पाययति, -ते, -यितुम् (Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">Page0559-c+ 81</a>]<BR>-यितवै), to cause to drink, give to drink; to water<BR>(horses or cattle): Desid. पिपासति (Ved. पिपीषति),<BR>to wish to drink, thirst, thirst for, thirst after: Desid.<BR>of Caus. पिपाययिषति, to wish or intend to give<BR>to drink: Intens. पेपीयते, to drink greedily or<BR>with avidity, drink repeatedly; [cf. Gr. πί-ν-ω, Fut.<BR>πί-ομαι, Aor. ἔ-πι-ο-ν, πῖθι, Perf. πέ-πω-κα,<BR>πό-το-ς, πό-μα, πῶ-μα, πό-σι-ς, πό-τη-ς, πο-τήρ-ιο-ν,<BR>πῖ-νο-ν, πι-πί-σκ-ω, πῖ-σ-ος, Πῖσα, πίσ-τρα, Æol.<BR>πώ-ν-ω: Lat. po-tu-s, po-ti-o(n), po-tor, po-c-<BR>ulu-m, pô-tare, bi-b-o, vini-bu-a for vini-bib-a,<BR>ex-bu-res, im-bu-o: Slav. pi-ti, ‘to drink:’ Old<BR>Pruss. pou-ton, ‘to drink:’ Lith. po-ta, ‘tippling;’<BR>pḗ-na-s, ‘milk;’ pý-va-s, ‘beer:’ Angl. Sax. beor:<BR>Old and Mod. Germ. bier.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
2. पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) drink-<BR>ing, quaffing; [cf. अग्रे-पा, अञ्जस्-पा, ऋतु-पा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातव्य
1. पातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be drunk, drinkable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातृ
1. पातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who drinks, a drinker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
1. पात्र, अम्, n. a drinking-vessel, goblet, bowl,<BR>cup, plate, dish, jar, pot; a vessel in general; a<BR>utensil; any kind of sacrificial vase or vessel (com-<BR>prising various forms of cups, plates, spoons, ladles,<BR>&c. so used); the channel or bed of a river; a<BR>receptacle of any kind, anything which holds or<BR>supports; (metaphorically) a receptacle, a recipient<BR>or a person in whom any quality is contained [cf.<BR>विश्वास-प्˚]; a fit or competent or worthy person,<BR>a person worthy to receive gifts, worthy of, fit for<BR>(with gen. or loc. or inf., e. g. पात्रं ह्य् एषाम्<BR>असि, for thou art worthy or these); a king's coun-<BR>sellor or minister; an actor, dramatis persona; a<BR>part in a play; propriety, fitness; an order, com-<BR>mand; a leaf; (अस्), m. a vessel &c.; a measure of<BR>capacity = 1 Āḍhaka; (ई), f. a vessel, plate, dish;<BR>pot, barrel; a small or portable furnace; an epithet<BR>of Durgā; [cf. perhaps Lat. patera; Goth. fōdr;<BR>Hib. putraice, ‘a vessel, pot.’]<BR>—पात्र-कटक, अस्<BR>or अम्, m. or n. (?), the ring on which a beggar's<BR>alms-dish is carried.<BR>—पात्र-ता, f. or पात्र-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the property or capacity of a cup or vessel;<BR>the being a receptacle for anything; capacity, fitness;<BR>worthiness, merit, desert; dignity, honour; appro-<BR>priate state or circumstance.<BR>—पात्र-पाणि, इस्, m.<BR>‘cup-handed,’ N. of a demon hurtful to children.<BR>—पात्र-पाल, अस्, m. ‘vessel-guiding,’ a large<BR>paddle used as a rudder (commonly called पाततु-<BR>यार).<BR>—पात्र-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘become a re-<BR>cipient,’ worthy of receiving anything from any one<BR>(gen.); the object of a present or of respectful treat-<BR>ment.<BR>—पात्र-भृत्, त्, m. ‘taking care of utensils,’<BR>a servant, scullion.<BR>—पात्र-भेद, अस्, m. breaking<BR>a drinking-vessel or cup.<BR>—पात्र-मेलन, अम्, n.<BR>the bringing together of the characters of a play.<BR>—पात्र-वर्ग, अस्, m. a company of actors.<BR>—पात्र-<BR>संस्कार, अस्, m. the current of a river; the cleaning of<BR>a vessel or dish.<BR>—पात्र-सञ्चार, अस्, m. (perhaps)<BR>removing the dishes or arranging them after dinner<BR>(or incorrect for पात्र-संस्कार).<BR>—पात्र-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being in a dish.<BR>—पात्र-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘cup-handed,’ holding a vessel in the hand.<BR>—पात्री-<BR>निर्णेजन, अम्, n., Ved. water for rinsing a vessel.<BR>—पात्रे-बहुल, अस्, आ, अम्, constant at meals; a<BR>parasite.<BR>—पात्रे-समित, अस्, आ, अम्, constant at<BR>meals, a parasite; a treacherous or hypocritical person.<BR>—पात्रोपकरण (˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n. decorations<BR>of an inferior class, as bells, chowries, vases, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रक|पात्रकं
पात्रक, अम्, n. a vessel, bowl, bason, dish;<BR>(इका), f. a cup, a beggar's bowl or alms-dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रटीर|पात्रटीरः
पात्रटीर, अस्, m. an ex-minister; (according to<BR>others) an able or competent minister; a vessel of<BR>metal; mucus running from the nose; rust of iron;<BR>fire; a heron; a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रय
पात्रय, Nom. P. पात्रयति, -यितुम्, to use as<BR>a drinking-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसात्कृ
पात्रसात्-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to pre-<BR>sent a worthy person with anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिक
पात्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, measured out with any vessel<BR>or with the measure Pātra; sown with as much as<BR>will fill a Pātra; containing it, possessing it; fit, ade-<BR>quate, appropriate; (अम्, ई), n. f. a vessel, cup, dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0559-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिन्
पात्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having a drinking-vessel or pro-<BR>vided with a dish; having fit or worthy persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिय
पात्रिय or पात्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, worthy to partake<BR>of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीकृ
पात्री-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make a<BR>fitting receptacle or recipient, to make a worthy<BR>object; to dignify, promote to honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीण
पात्रीण, अस्, आ, अम्, measured or sown or cooked<BR>with a Pātra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीभू
पात्री-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to be-<BR>come a fitting recipient or worthy object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीय|पात्रीयं
पात्रीय, अम्, n. a sacrificial vessel or utensil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीर|पात्रीरं|पात्रीरः
पात्रीर, अस्, m. an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीव
पात्रीव, अस्, अम्, m. n. a kind of sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
1. पान, अम्, n. (for 2. see col. 2), drinking,<BR>drinking spirituous liquors; enjoying; a drink,<BR>beverage; a drinking-vessel, cup; a canal; (अस्),<BR>m. a distiller, one who sells spirituous liquors,<BR>a publican, inn-keeper; [cf. Lith. péna-s, ‘milk.’]<BR>—पान-कुम्भ, अस्, m. a drinking-vessel.<BR>—पान-<BR>गोष्ठिका or पान-गोष्ठी, f. a drinking-party,<BR>drinking-bout; a dram-shop, tavern, place where<BR>people drink together.<BR>—पान-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, caused<BR>by drinking (as a disease).<BR>—पान-दोष, अस्, m.<BR>the vice of drinking, drunkenness.<BR>—पान-प, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, a dram-drinker, drinker of spirituous liquors.<BR>—पान-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to drinking.<BR>—पान-पात्र, अम्, n. a drinking-vessel, glass, cup,<BR>goblet.<BR>—पान-बणिज्, क्, m. a vender of spirits, a<BR>distiller.<BR>—पान-भाजन, अम्, n. a drinking-vessel,<BR>glass, goblet.<BR>—पान-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a drinking-<BR>vessel.<BR>—पान-भू, ऊस्, or पान-भूमि, इस् or ई, f.<BR>a drinking-place, drinking-room, refreshment-room.<BR>—पान-मङ्गल, अम्, n. a drinking-party, drink-<BR>ing-bout.<BR>—पान-मद, अस्, m. intoxication.<BR>—पा-<BR>न-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to drink, drinking,<BR>drunken, a toper.<BR>—पान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. abound-<BR>ing in drink, rich in beverages.<BR>—पान-विभ्रम, अस्,<BR>m. ‘drink-giddiness,’ intoxication.<BR>—पान-शौण्ड,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to intoxication; (अस्), m. a hard<BR>drinker.<BR>—पानागार (˚न-अग्˚ or -आग्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>drinking-house, tavern.<BR>—पानात्यय (˚न-अत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. hard drinking, drinking; morbid state after in-<BR>toxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानक|पानकं
पानक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a draught, drink, beverage,<BR>potion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानिक|पानिकः
पानिक, अस्, m. a vender of spirituous liquors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानिल|पानिलं
पानिल, अम्, n. a drinking-vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीय|पानीयं
1. पानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see col. 2), to<BR>be drunk, drinkable; (अम्), n. a beverage, drink;<BR>water.<BR>—पानीय-काकिका, f. ‘sea-crow,’ the cormo-<BR>rant.<BR>—पानीय-नकुल, अस्, m. ‘water-ichneumon,’<BR>an otter.<BR>—पानीय-पृष्ठ-ज, अस्, m. ‘born on<BR>the surface of the water,’ an aquatic plant, Pistia<BR>Stratiotes.<BR>—पानीय-फल, अम्, n. the seed of<BR>Euryala Ferox.<BR>—पानीय-मूलक, अम्, n. the plant<BR>Vernonia Anthelminthica.<BR>—पानीय-वर्णिका, f.<BR>sand (= बालुका).<BR>—पानीय-शाला or पानीय-शा-<BR>लिका, f. a place where water is distributed, a shed on<BR>the road-side for providing passengers with water.<BR>—पानीय-शीत, अस्, आ, अम्, too cold to drink.<BR>—पा-<BR>नीयाध्यक्ष (˚य-अध्˚), अस्, m. a superintendent<BR>of the water.<BR>—पानीयामलक (˚य-आम्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a kind of fruit, Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR>—पानीयार्-<BR>थम् (˚य-अर्˚), ind. for the sake of water.<BR>—पानी-<BR>यालु (˚य-आलु), उस्, m. a species of tuberous plant<BR>(= जलालु, क्षुपालु).<BR>—पानीयाश्रा (˚य-अश्˚), f.<BR>a species of grass (= वल्वजा, दृढ-क्षुरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्त
पान्त, अस्, m., Ved. = 1. पानीय, a drink, beverage;<BR>(Sāy.) = पालन-स्वभाव, nutritious (as if fr. rt.<BR>3. पा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा 3. पा, cl. 2. P. पाति, पपौ, पास्यति,<BR>अपासीत् (Ved. forms पीपाय [Sāy. fr. प्यै],<BR>पासति), पातुम्, to watch, keep, preserve, protect,<BR>screen, shelter, defend against (with abl.); to rule,<BR>govern; to beware of (with abl); to observe, notice,<BR>attend to (Ved.); to oversee, take care of, tend<BR>(Ved.); to keep, observe (in this sense also A., Ved.):<BR>Caus. (or rt. पल् or पाल्, cl. 10; or Nom. fr. पाल)<BR>P. (ep. also A.) पालयति (-ते), -यितुम्, to watch,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">Page0560-b+ 80</a>]<BR>keep, protect, screen, defend, be a guardian to; to<BR>cherish; to rule, govern; to maintain, keep, observe<BR>(as a promise or vow): Desid. पिपासति: Intens.<BR>पापायते, पापेति, पापाति; [cf. Gr. πατ-έομαι,<BR>ἐ-πᾱσάμην, πέ-πᾱμαι, ἄ-πασ-τος perhaps Πάν,<BR>πάτνη, πάθην, φάτνη, δεσ-πό-της, perhaps ἄνθρωπος<BR>for ἄνδρο-πος = नृ-प (?): Lat. pa in pâ-vi,<BR>pa-bulum, pa-sc-or, pas-tor, Pă-le-s, pā-nis, pe-<BR>n-us, penātes, penes, pene-tro: Slav. pit-a-ti, ‘to<BR>nourish:’ Russ. pitáyu, ‘I feed:’ Lith. pō-nas, ‘a<BR>lord;’ pé-nas, ‘fodder, food;’ pénù, ‘I feed;’ pë-<BR>mú§, ‘a shepherd;’ pḗ-tu-s, ‘midday:’ Goth. fod-<BR>yan, ‘to feed;’ fôd-ein-s, ‘food:’ Angl. Sax. fod-a:<BR>Mod. Germ. futter: Eng. food.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
4. पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) keep-<BR>ing, protecting, guarding, screening; [cf. अपान-पा,<BR>आप्रीत-पा, गो-पा, तपुष्-पा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
1. पात्, आन्, आती or आन्ती, आत् (for 2. see p. 563), guard-<BR>ing, defending, preserving; a guardian, protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
1. पात, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. पात see under 2. पात्),<BR>watched, protected, preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातव्य
2. पातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see p. 559, col. 3),<BR>to be guarded or protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातृ
2. पातृ, ता, त्री, तृ (for 1. see p. 559, col. 3),<BR>a defender, protector, defending (with gen. or acc.);<BR>(ता), m. a species of Ocymum (= गन्ध-पत्त्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
2. पात्र, अम्, n. a preservative from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
2. पान, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see col. 1) Ved.<BR>observing, keeping; (अम्), n. protection, defence;<BR>[cf. तनू-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीय|पानीयं
2. पानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. see col. 1), to be<BR>cherished or protected, to be preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशु|पांशुः
पांशु पांशु, पांशन, &c., = पांसु, पां-<BR>सन, &c. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसु|पांसुः
पांसु पांसु, उस्, m. (in later writings mostly<BR>spelt पांशु; probably fr. rt. पंस् or पंश्, to<BR>destroy), crumbling soil, dust, sand; a particle of<BR>dust, grain of sand; dung, manure; a species of<BR>plant (= पर्पट); a kind of camphor; landed<BR>property; [cf. Lat. pulvis for pulcvis; Cambro-<BR>Brit. pain, ‘pollen, fine powder or dust.’]<BR>—पांसु-<BR>कासीस, अम्, n. sulphate of iron.<BR>—पांसु-कुली, f.<BR>‘multitude of dust,’ a high road, highway.<BR>—पांसु-<BR>कूल, अम्, n. a dust-heap, particularly a collection of<BR>rubbish and rags out of which the Buddhist priests<BR>make up their clothing; a legal document not made<BR>out in any particular person's name.<BR>—पांसुकूल-<BR>सीवन, अम्, n. ‘the sewing together of rags from a<BR>dust-heap,’ N. of the place where Śākya-muni assumed<BR>his priestly dress.<BR>—पांसुकूलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who wears clothes made of rags from a dust-heap.<BR>—पांसु-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with dust,<BR>dusty.<BR>—पांसु-क्षार = पांसु-ज, q. v.<BR>—पांसु-<BR>गुण्ठित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with dust.<BR>—पांसु-<BR>चत्वर, अम्, n. hail.<BR>—पांसु-चन्दन, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पांसु-चामर, अस्, m. a heap<BR>of dust; a tent; a bank covered with Dūrvā grass;<BR>praise; a small cucumber.<BR>—पांसु-ज, अम्, n. ‘earth-<BR>born,’ a kind of salt extracted from soil, rock or fossil<BR>salt.<BR>—पांसु-जालिक, अस्, m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—पांसु-धूम्र, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-red or dark<BR>with dust; [cf. धूलि-धूम्र.]<BR>—पांसु-ध्वस्त-<BR>शिरोरुह, अस्, आ, अम्, having the hair soiled with<BR>dust.<BR>—पांसु-निपात, अस्, m. a fall of dust.<BR>—पां-<BR>सु-पटल, अम्, n. a coating or mass of dust.<BR>—पांसु-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a kind of vegetable, Che-<BR>nopodium Album.<BR>—पांसु-भव, अस् or अम्, m.<BR>or n. (?) = पांसु-ज, q. v.<BR>—पांसु-मर्दन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘dust-destroying,’ an excavation for water round<BR>the root of a tree.<BR>—पांसु-रागिणी, f. a species of<BR>plant (= महा-मदा).<BR>—पांसु-राष्ट्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a country; (आस्), m. pl., N. of its inhabitants.<BR>—पांसु-वर्ष, अस्, m. a shower of dust, falling<BR>dust.<BR>—पांसु-समूहन, अस्, ई, अम्, collecting or<BR>raising dust (as the wind).<BR>—पांसुत्कर (˚सु-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, m., Ved. = पांसु-वर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसक
पांसक, अस्, आ, अम्, vitiating, spoiling; con-<BR>temptible, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसन|पांसनः
पांसन, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>defiling, disgracing, dishonouring; vitiating, spoiling,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">Page0560-c+ 80</a>]<BR>destructive; contemptible, wicked, bad, infamous;<BR>(अम्), n. contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसव
पांसव, अस्, आ, अम्, formed or consisting of dust;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic (Ved.); a kind of salt (in<BR>this sense spelt पांशव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्सिन्
पान्सिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = पांसन (for which it is<BR>probably only a wrong reading).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुक
पांसुक, आस्, m. pl. dust; (आ), f. a menstruous<BR>woman; a fragrant plant, Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुर|पांसुरः
पांसुर, अस्, आ, अम्, dusty (Ved.); a gad-fly; a<BR>cripple carried or moving about in a chair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुल|पांसुलः
पांसुल or पांशुल, अस्, आ, अम्, dusty, covered with<BR>dust; sullied, defiled, disgraced; defiling, disgracing<BR>(e. g. कुल-पांसुल, disgracing a family, a disgrace to<BR>the family); (अस्), m. a wicked or profligate man, a<BR>libertine, paramour, gallant; one of Śiva's weapons<BR>(a sort of pole armed at the upper end with transverse<BR>pieces representing the breast-bone and adjoining ribs<BR>and surmounted by a skull); an epithet of Śiva; a<BR>species of tree, Cæsalpinia Bonducella; (आ), f. a<BR>menstruous woman; a licentious woman, (अ-पां-<BR>शुला, a chaste woman); the earth; Pandanus Odo-<BR>ratissimus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक 1. पाक, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>1. पा, to drink), Ved. very young; sincere, simple,<BR>genuine, inartificial, honest; ignorant; (अस्), m. the<BR>young of animals, a child, an infant; N. of a Daitya<BR>slain by Indra; an owl.<BR>—पाक-त्रा, ind., Ved. in a<BR>simple or honest way, in simplicity; (Sāy.) = विपक्व-<BR>प्रज्ञेषु, towards the sincere-minded.<BR>—पाक-<BR>दूर्वा, f., Ved. a species of plant.<BR>—पाक-द्विष्, ट्,<BR>m. ‘the enemy of the Daitya Pāka,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>—पाक-यज्ञ, अस्, m. a simple or domestic<BR>sacrifice (an oblation offered on building a house,<BR>liberating a bull, &c.; according to Āpastamba this<BR>term comprise the Aupāsana-homa, Vaiśvadeva, Pār-<BR>vaṇa, Aṣṭakā, Śrāddha, Sarpa-bali, Īśāna-bali;<BR>according to Baudhāyana, the Huta, Pra-huta,<BR>Ā-huta, Śūla-gava, Bali-haraṇa, Praty-avarohaṇa, Ash-<BR>ṭakā-homa; according to Gautama, the Aṣṭakā,<BR>Pārvaṇa, Śrāddha, Śrāvaṇī, Āgrahāyaṇī, Caitrī,<BR>Aśva-yujī); N. of a man.<BR>—पाकयज्ञिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, relating to the Pāka-yajña; (अस्), m. a per-<BR>former of the Pāka-yajña ceremony.<BR>—पाकयज्ञिय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the Pāka-yajña.<BR>—पाक-वत्,<BR>ind., Ved. simply, honestly.<BR>—पाक-शंस, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. honest-minded; (Sāy.) = परिपक्व-व-<BR>चन, सत्य-भाषिन्, speaking sincerely.<BR>—पाक-<BR>शाला, f. ‘cook-house,’ a kitchen.<BR>—पाक-शासन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘punisher of the Daitya Pāka or instructor of the<BR>ignorant,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—पाकशासनि, इस्,<BR>m. (a patronymic fr. the preceding), an epithet of<BR>Jayanta; of Arjuna.<BR>—पाक-संस्था, f. = पाक-<BR>यज्ञ, q. v.<BR>—पाक-सुत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. offering<BR>Soma with a simple or sincere mind (Sāy. = वि-<BR>पक्वेन मनसा सोमस्याभिषोतृ).<BR>—पाक-<BR>स्थामन्, आ, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR>—पाक-हन्-<BR>तृ, ता, m. ‘slayer of the Daitya Pāka,’ an epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य, अम्, n., Ved. honesty, simplicity; (आ),<BR>ind. in simplicity, in ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक 2. पाक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. पच्), cook-<BR>ing, baking, roasting, boiling, dressing food; burning<BR>(bricks or earthenware); digestion, assimilation of<BR>food; ripening, becoming ripe, ripeness; maturity,<BR>perfect development (e. g. धियस्, of the intellect),<BR>development of consequences (as of an act done in a<BR>former life or of any act); completion, perfection,<BR>fulfilment, accomplishment [cf. फल-प्˚]; greyness<BR>of the hair, old age; inflammation, suppuration,<BR>ripeness of a boil; an abscess, ulcer; a vessel in which<BR>anything is cooked or dressed, cooking utensil (a<BR>saucepan, boiler, &c.); the domestic fire; general<BR>fear and panic resulting in national disaster or revo-<BR>lution; the subversion of a country; [cf. अ-प्˚,<BR>इक्षु-प्˚, कृष्ण-प्˚.]<BR>—पाक-कृष्ण, अस्, m.<BR>the Caronda tree, Carissa Carondas (‘bearing a black<BR>fruit when ripe,’ also other similar compounds, as<BR>पाककृष्ण-फल, कृष्ण-पाक).<BR>—पाक-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, caused by cooking or roasting, produced<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">Page0561-a+ 80</a>]<BR>by maturing; (अम्), n. ‘obtained by boiling,’ black<BR>salt; flatulence.<BR>—पाकज-त्व, अम्, n. production by<BR>warmth, capability of being affected by contact with<BR>fire.<BR>—पाक-पात्र, अम्, n. a cooking utensil, a<BR>boiler, &c.<BR>—पाक-पुटी, f. a potter's kiln, pottery.<BR>—पाक-फल, अस्, m. the Caronda tree (= कृष्ण-<BR>पाक-फल).<BR>—पाक-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a cooking<BR>utensil.<BR>—पाक-मत्स्य, अस्, m. a species of fish; a<BR>kind of fish-sauce; a species of venomous insect.<BR>—पाक-रञ्जन, अम्, n. the leaf of the Laurus<BR>Cassia.<BR>—पाक-राजेश्वर (˚ज-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a writer on the art of cookery.<BR>—पाक-शाला, f. ‘hall<BR>for cooking,’ a kitchen.<BR>—पाक-शुक्ला, f. chalk.<BR>—पाक-स्थान, अम्, n. ‘place for cooking,’ a<BR>kitchen; (scil. कुलालस्य) a potter's kiln.<BR>—पाका-<BR>गार (˚क-अग्˚ or -आग्˚), अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>‘cooking-room,’ a kitchen.<BR>—पाकातीसार (˚क-अत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. chronic dysentery; [cf. आमातीसार.]<BR>—पा-<BR>काध्याय (˚क-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘chapter on cooking,’<BR>N. of a chapter of the Sannipāta-kalikā treating of<BR>particular medical decoctions.<BR>—पाकारु (˚क-अरु),<BR>उस्, m., Ved., N. of a particular disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0560-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकल|पाकलं|पाकलः
पाकल, अस्, आ, अम्, bringing to maturity; sup-<BR>purative, causing suppuration in a boil; (अस्), m.<BR>fever in an elephant; fire; wind; = वोधन-<BR>द्रव्य (probably an error for राधन-द्रव्य);<BR>(आ), f. Bignonia Suaveolens; (ई), f. Cucumis Utilis-<BR>simus; (अम्), n. Costus Speciosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकलि|पाकलिः
पाकलि, इस्, f. a species of plant (= रोहिणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिन्
पाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) becoming<BR>mature, ripening; being digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिम|पाकिमं
पाकिम, अस्, आ, अम्, cooked, dressed, ripened<BR>(naturally or artificially); obtained by boiling or<BR>evaporation (as salt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुक|पाकुकः
पाकुक, अस्, m. a cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cooked or matured;<BR>fit to cook, eatable; obtained by cooking or evapo-<BR>ration; (अम्), n. a kind of salt; (अस्), m. saltpetre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक, अस्, इका, अम्, cooking, roasting, baking;<BR>causing digestion, digestive, peptic, tonic; maturing,<BR>bringing to maturity; (अस्, इका), m. f. a cook; (अस्),<BR>m. fire; (अम्), n. the bile which assists in digestion.<BR>—पाचक-स्त्री, f. a female cook.<BR>—पाचिका-भार्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a cook for a wife, married to a<BR>cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचन|पाचनं|पाचनः
पाचन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to cook or boil,<BR>cooking, ripening; softening, relaxing, digestive;<BR>suppurative; (अस्), m. fire; acidity, sourness; a<BR>species of plant (= रक्तैरण्ड); (ई), f. a species<BR>of Myrobalan, Terminalia Chebula; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of cooking or baking; ripening; causing a wound<BR>to close; a styptic for closing wounds; a medicinal<BR>preparation, infusion, decoction (of various drugs,<BR>chiefly carminatives or gentle stimulants given to<BR>bring the vitiated humors in fever &c. to maturity);<BR>‘extraction by boiling,’ eliciting extraneous sub-<BR>stances from a wound or ulcer by means of cata-<BR>plasms &c.; a cataplasm; a sort of diet-drink;<BR>dissolving; a dissolvent, digestive; penance, expi-<BR>ation; (इका), f. cooking, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनक|पाचनकः
पाचनक, अस्, m. borax; (अम्), n. a sort of<BR>diet-drink; causing a wound to close (by means of<BR>styptics &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनीय
पाचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cooked or digested;<BR>dissolving, digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचल|पाचलं|पाचलः
पाचल, अस्, m. whatever cooks, ripens, causes<BR>digestion, &c.; a cook; fire; wind; a thing dressed<BR>or matured without the aid of fire; (अम्), n. cook-<BR>ing, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचा
पाचा or पाचि, इस्, f. cooking, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाच्य
पाच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cooked; capable of<BR>being matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्ष
पाक्ष पाक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पक्ष), be-<BR>longing to a half month, fortnightly, relating to a<BR>side or party, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षपातिक
पाक्षपातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पक्ष-पात),<BR>favouring a party or faction, partial, factious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षायण|पाक्षायणः
पाक्षायण, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or occurring<BR>in a Pakṣa or fortnight, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिक|पाक्षिकः
पाक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पक्ष or पक्षिन्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">Page0561-b+ 75</a>]<BR>belonging to a bird; belonging to a fortnight, fort-<BR>nightly; belonging to an argument, &c.; favouring a<BR>party or faction; subject to an alternative, that which<BR>may or may not take place, possible but not necessary,<BR>contingent, allowed but not prescribed; (अस्), m. a<BR>fowler, bird-catcher; an alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाखण्ड|पाखंड|पाखंडः|पाखण्डः
पाखण्ड पाखण्ड, अस्, m. a heretic, hete-<BR>rodox Hindū (adopting the exterior marks of the<BR>classes, but not respecting the ordinances of the<BR>Vedas; also पाषण्ड, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पागल|पागलः
पागल पागल, अस्, आ, अम्, mad, deranged,<BR>demented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्त
पाङ्क्त पाङ्क्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पङ्क्ति), con-<BR>sisting of five parts, fivefold (Ved.); relating to or<BR>composed in the Paṅkti metre; an epithet of a kind<BR>of Soma; (अम्), n., scil. सामन्, N. of a Sāman.<BR>—पाङ्क्त-ता, f. or पाङ्क्त-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. five-<BR>foldness, fivefold nature or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्तकाकुभ
पाङ्क्तकाकुभ, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. पङ्क्ति-ककुभ्),<BR>Ved. an epithet of a Pra-gātha consisting of the Paṅkti<BR>and Kakubh metres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्तेय|पांक्तेय
पाङ्क्तेय or पाङ्क्त्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fit to sit in<BR>the general row at meals, fit to be associated with,<BR>admissible into society, fit for respectable society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्त्र
पाङ्क्त्र पाङ्क्त्र, अस्, m., Ved. (according to<BR>Mahī-dhara) a kind of mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्गुल्य|पांगुल्यं
पाङ्गुल्य पाङ्गुल्य, अम्, n. (fr. पङ्गुल),<BR>limping, halting, hobbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक पाचक. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाची
पाची पाची, f. a species of climbing plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्
पाजस् पाजस्, अस्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 3.<BR>पा), Ved. brightness, shining, glimmer, gleam, glit-<BR>ter, sheen [cf. सहस्र-प्˚]; cheerfulness, freshness,<BR>activity, strength, vigour, impetuosity; a shining sur-<BR>face (said of the sky); (असी), n. du. ‘the two shining<BR>surfaces,’ heaven and earth; (Sāy.) = बलवत्यौ,<BR>powerful (as an epithet of Dyāvā-kṣāmā); (आंसि), n.<BR>pl. glittering hues, glowing colours; (Sāy.) = बलानि.<BR>—पाजस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. brilliant, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्य
पाजस्य पाजस्य, अम्, n., Ved. the region<BR>of the belly (of an animal); the flanks, side; [cf.<BR>त्रि-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चकपाल|पांचकपाल|पाञ्चकपालः
पाञ्चकपाल पाञ्चकपाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>पञ्च-कपाल), relating to or forming part of an<BR>oblation offered in five cups.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चगतिक
पाञ्चगतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-गति), con-<BR>sisting of five forms of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजनी
पाञ्चजनी, f. a patronymic of Asiknī the daughter<BR>of the Prajā-pati Pañca-jana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्य|पांचजन्य|पांचजन्यः|पाञ्चजन्यः
पाञ्चजन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पञ्च-जन, q. v.),<BR>containing or relating to the five classes or races of<BR>men, extending over the five races (Ved.); (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of the conch of Kṛṣṇa which was taken by him<BR>from the demon Pañca-jana, see पञ्च-जन, p. 522;<BR>fire; a species of fish (= पोट-गल); N. of one of<BR>the eight Upa-dvīpas in Jambu-dvīpa; (आ), f. a<BR>patronymic of Asiknī; (अम्), n. (?), N. of a forest.<BR>—पाञ्चजन्य-धर, अस्, m. ‘bearing the conch<BR>Pāñcajanya,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश|पांचदश
पाञ्चदश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-दशी), relating<BR>to the fifteenth day of a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चदश्य|पांचदश्यं
पाञ्चदश्य, अस्, शी, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>the fifteenth day of a month, used on the fifteenth day<BR>of a half month; (अम्), n. the aggregate of fifteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चनख
पाञ्चनख, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-नख), made<BR>of the skin of an animal with five claws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चनद|पांचनद|पाञ्चनदः
पाञ्चनद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-नद), pre-<BR>vailing in the land of the five rivers, observed in<BR>Pañca-nada or the Pañjāb; (अस्), m. a prince of the<BR>Pañjāb; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of the Pañjāb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चभौतिक|पांचभौतिक
पाञ्चभौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-भूत),<BR>composed of or containing the five elements; (with<BR>आ-दान) the assumption of the five elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चमाह्निक
पाञ्चमाह्निक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्चम + अहन्),<BR>Ved. belonging to the fifth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चमिक
पाञ्चमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, treated of in the fifth<BR>(book).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चयाज्ञिक
पाञ्चयाज्ञिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-यज्ञ), re-<BR>lating or belonging to or included in the five great<BR>sacrifices or ceremonies; (अम्), n. any one of the<BR>five great sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चरात्र
पाञ्चरात्र, आस्, m. pl. (fr. पञ्च-रात्र), N. of a<BR>Vaiṣṇava sect following the doctrine of their sacred<BR>book called Pañca-rātra.<BR>—पाञ्चरात्र-रहस्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work mentioned in the Sarva-<BR>darśana-saṅgraha by Mādhavācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चरात्र्यनिबर्हण
पाञ्चरात्र्य-निबर्हण, अम्, n., N. of the eighth<BR>chapter of the Śaṅkara-vijaya by Anantānanda-giri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चवर्षिक|पांचवर्षिक
पाञ्चवर्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-वर्ष),<BR>five years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चवाज
पाञ्चवाज, अम्, n. (fr. पञ्च-वाज), N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चविध्य
पाञ्चविध्य, अम्, n. (fr. पञ्च-विधि), N. of a<BR>Sūtra treating of the five Vidhis of the Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चशब्दिक|पांचशब्दिक|पांचशब्दिकं|पाञ्चशब्दिकं
पाञ्चशब्दिक, अम्, n. (fr. पञ्च-शब्द), music<BR>of five kinds; musical instruments in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चशर
पाञ्चशर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पञ्च-शर), belonging<BR>to ‘the five-arrowed’ or the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चार्थिक|पांचार्थिकः|पाञ्चार्थिकः
पाञ्चार्थिक, अस्, m. (fr. पञ्चन् + अर्थ), a<BR>follower or votary of Paśu-pati or Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल|पांचाल|पाञ्चालं|पाञ्चालः
पाञ्चाल पाञ्चाल, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or be-<BR>longing to the Pañcālas, dwelling in or ruling over<BR>the country of the Pañcālas; (अस्), m. a prince of<BR>the Pañcālas; the country of the Pañcālas; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the people of the Pañcālas; an association of<BR>five guilds (viz. those of the carpenter, weaver, barber,<BR>washerman, and shoe-maker); (ई), f. a princess of<BR>the Pañcālas; a N. of Draupadī the wife of the<BR>five Pāṇḍu princes; a doll, puppet; scil. रीति, epithet<BR>of a particular poetical style; the melodious combina-<BR>tion of five or six words.<BR>—पाञ्चाल-देश, अस्, m. the<BR>country of the Pañcālas.<BR>—पाञ्चाल-राज, अस्, m. the<BR>king of the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालक|पांचालक|पाञ्चालकः
पाञ्चालक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to the people<BR>of the Pañcālas; (अस्), m. a sovereign of the Pañ-<BR>cālas; (इका), f. a princess of the Pañcālas; a doll,<BR>puppet (sometimes written पाञ्चलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालेय|पाञ्चालेयः
पाञ्चालेय or पाञ्चाल्य, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to<BR>the Pañcālas; (अस्), m. a prince of the Pañcālas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चि
पाञ्चि पाञ्चि, इस्, m. (fr. पञ्चन्), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR>—पाञ्चि-ग्राम, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चिक
पाञ्चिक, अस्, m., N. of the leader of the Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्
पाट् पाट्, ind. an interjection used in call-<BR>ing (सम्बोधने).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट|पाटः
पाट पाट, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पट्), breadth,<BR>expanse, extension; (in geometry) the intersection of<BR>a prolonged side and perpendicular or the figure<BR>formed by such intersection; (आ), f. regular or suc-<BR>cessive order, series, succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटक|पाटकः
पाटक, अस्, m. a splitter, divider, one who cleaves<BR>or tears asunder; the half of a village, part of a<BR>village, a kind of village; a shore, bank; a flight of<BR>steps leading to the water; a kind of musical instru-<BR>ment; a long span (= महा-किष्कु); expense or<BR>loss of capital or stock; throwing dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटन|पाटनं
पाटन, अम्, n. splitting, cleaving, slitting up,<BR>tearing up, breaking, cutting to pieces, destroying.<BR>—पाटन-क्रिया, f. lancing an abscess or ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल, अस्, आ, अम् (said by some to be connected<BR>with पाट above), pale-red, of a pink or pale-red<BR>colour; rose colour; pallid; (अस्, ई, अम्), made of<BR>the Pāṭalī or forming a part of it; (अस्), m. a pale-<BR>red hue, rose colour, redness; the trumpet-flower,<BR>Bignonia Suaveolens (a tree with sweet-scented blos-<BR>soms); a species of rice ripening in the rains; N. of<BR>a man; (आ), f. Bignonia Suaveolens (both the tree<BR>and its blossom); red Lodhra; a kind of fresh-water<BR>fish; an epithet of Durgā; a form of Dākṣāyaṇī;<BR>(अम्, आ), n. f. the flower of the Bignonia Suaveolens;<BR>saffron.<BR>—पाटल-गण्ड-लेख, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the complexion of the cheek reddened.<BR>—पाटल-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. a species of tree, Rottleria Tinctoria<BR>(= पुन्-नाग).<BR>—पाटल-पुष्प-सन्निभ, अम्,<BR>n. a species of medicinal plant (= पद्म-काष्ठ).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">Page0562-a+ 75</a>]<BR>—पाटला-वती, f., N. of a river; an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—पाटलोपल (˚ल-उप्˚), अम्, n. a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0561-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलक
पाटलक, अस्, आ, अम्, of a pale-red colour, pink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलि|पाटलिः
पाटलि, इस्, ई, m. f. the trumpet-flower, Bignonia<BR>Suaveolens; a species of rice; (ई), f., N. of a city;<BR>of a daughter of king Mahendra-varman.<BR>—पाटलि-<BR>पुत्र or पाटलि-पुत्रक, अम्, n., N. of the capital<BR>of Magadha near the confluence of the Śoṇa and the<BR>Ganges, supposed to be the ancient Palibothra and<BR>the modern Patna.<BR>—पाटलिपुत्र-नामधेय, अम्,<BR>n., scil. नगर, a city called Pāṭali-putra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिक|पाटलिकः
पाटलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing the secrets of<BR>others; one who knows time and place; (अस्), m. a<BR>pupil; (अम्), n., N. of a town (= पाटलि-पुत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिमन्
पाटलिमन्, आ, m. a pale-red or rose colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल्या
पाटल्या, f. a multitude of Pāṭalā flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटित|पाटितं
पाटित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn, split, broken, divided;<BR>epithet of a form of fracture of the leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटी
पाटी, f. arithmetic; a species of shrub (= बला).<BR>—पाटी-गणित, अम्, n. arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीर|पाटीरः
पाटीर, अस्, m. a field; a pungent root, a kind<BR>of radish; the pith or manna of the bamboo; a cloud;<BR>a sieve, searce, cribble; tin; disease arising from<BR>wind, catarrh; sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटच्चर|पाटच्चरः
पाटच्चर पाटच्चर, अस्, m. (fr. पटच्चर),<BR>a thief, robber, shop-lifter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल पाटल. See p. 561, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटव|पाटवं
पाटव पाटव, अस्, m. (fr. पटु), a son or<BR>descendant of Paṭu; a pupil of Paṭu; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>clever, sharp, dexterous; (अम्), n. sharpness, acute-<BR>ness, intensity, energy; cleverness, skill, dexterity,<BR>talent, eloquence; quickness, rashness, precipitation;<BR>health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविक|पाटविकः
पाटविक, अस्, ई, अम्, clever, adroit, dexterous;<BR>cunning, crafty, fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटहिका
पाटहिका पाटहिका, f. a small shrub, Abrus<BR>Precatorius; [cf. गुञ्ज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटा
पाटा पाटा, f., Ved. a species of plant<BR>(= पाठा ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटिकावाडि
पाटिकावाडि पाटिकावाडि, N. of a village<BR>(probably Putcabarry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटिन्
पाटिन् पाटिन्, ई, m. a species of fish de-<BR>scribed as having many teeth; [cf. पाठीन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटूर
पाटूर पाटूर, अस्, m., Ved. a particular<BR>part of an animal near the ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्य|पाट्यं
पाट्य पाट्य, अम्, n. a kind of vegetable<BR>(= पट्ट-शाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ|पाठः
पाठ पाठ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पठ्), recitation,<BR>recital; reading, perusal, study; reading sacred texts,<BR>studying the Vedas or scriptures; the text of a book.<BR>—पाठ-च्छेद, अस्, m. a break in recitation or in<BR>a text; a pause, cæsura.<BR>—पाठ-दोष, अस्, m. an<BR>error in a text, a false reading.<BR>—पाठ-निश्चिति, इस्,<BR>f. determining or settling the text (of a passage).<BR>—पाठ-भू, ऊस्, f. ‘reading-place,’ a place where<BR>the Vedas are read or studied.<BR>—पाठ-मञ्जरी, f.<BR>a particular small bird, Graculus Religiosa.<BR>—पाठ-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. well-read, learned.<BR>—पाठ-<BR>विच्छेद, अस्, m. = पाठ-च्छेद.<BR>—पाठ-शाला, f.<BR>‘lecture-room,’ ‘hall of study,’ a college, school.<BR>—पा-<BR>ठ-शालिन्, ई, इनी, m. f. a scholar, pupil; (इनी), f. =<BR>पाठ-मञ्जरी.<BR>—पाठान्तर (˚ठ-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>a variation of reading in a book or manuscript.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठक|पाठकः
पाठक, अस्, m. a reciter, reader, one who recites<BR>or delivers; a student, pupil; a scholar, a scientific<BR>person; a teacher, preceptor, lecturer, public reader<BR>(of the Purāṇas or other sacred works), a Paṇḍit who<BR>declares what is the law or custom according to the<BR>scriptures; a spiritual teacher; the text of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठन|पाठनं
1. पाठन, अम्, n. lecturing, teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिक
पाठिक, अस्, आ, अम्, conformable to the text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठित
पाठित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused or taught to read or<BR>recite; instructed, taught, lectured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिन्
पाठिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has read or studied<BR>(any subject), a student; knowing, conversant with;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">Page0562-b+ 78</a>]<BR>(ई), m. a Brāhman, especially one who has finished<BR>his studies; Plumbago Zeylanica (also पाठी-कुट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठीन|पाठीनः
पाठीन, अस्, m. a public reader or lecturer (on<BR>the Purāṇas &c.); a kind of sheat-fish, Silurus<BR>Pelorius or Boalis; a species of Moringa with red<BR>blossoms (= गुग्गलु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ्य|पाठ्यं
पाठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be taught, needing in-<BR>struction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठन|पाठनं
पाठन 2. पाठन, पाठनी, various read-<BR>ings for पानठ, पानठी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठा
पाठा पाठा, f. a climbing plant possessing<BR>various medicinal properties, Clypea Hernandifolia<BR>(commonly called आकनादि); (according to others)<BR>= पहाड-मूल, the root of Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाडिनी
पाडिनी पाडिनी, f. an earthen pot; a boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण|पाणः
पाण 1. पाण, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. पण्), a stake<BR>at play, a game; trade, traffic; a trader; praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण|पाणः
पाण 2. पाण. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणि|पाणिः
पाणि पाणि, इस्, m. (perhaps akin to पर्ण;<BR>said to be fr. rt. 2. पण्), the hand (in this sense<BR>frequently at the end of a comp. describing that<BR>which is carried in the hand, e. g. दर्भ-पाणि,<BR>with Kuśa grass in the hand, carrying Kuśa grass;<BR>cf. दण्ड-प्˚, शस्त्र-प्˚, समित्-प्˚); a hoof (Ved.);<BR>a place of sale, shop, market; पाणिं ग्रह्, to take<BR>the hand of a girl in the marriage ceremony, to<BR>marry.<BR>—पाणि-कच्छपिका, f. ‘hand-tortoise,’ a<BR>particular position of the fingers.<BR>—पाणि-कर्ण, अस्,<BR>m. ‘hand-eared,’ ‘having hands for ears,’ one of the<BR>epithets of Śiva.<BR>—पाणिकूर्चन्, आ, m., N. of one<BR>of the attendants of Skanda.<BR>—पाणि-खात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘dug with the hand,’ N. of a sacred bathing-<BR>place.<BR>—पाणि-गृहीत, अस्, आ, अम्, taken by the<BR>hand, seized; (ई), f. married according to the ritual,<BR>a bride, wife.<BR>—पाणि-ग्रह, अस्, m. or पाणि-ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. taking by the hand, taking the hand,<BR>marrying, marriage (the joining of the bride and<BR>bridegroom's hands forming part of the ceremony).<BR>—पाणिग्रह-कर, अस्, m. one who performs (the<BR>ceremony of) taking the hand; a lawful husband.<BR>—पाणिग्रहणिक or पाणिग्रहणीय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>relating to marriage, matrimonial, nuptial; (अम्), n.<BR>a wedding present.<BR>—पाणि-ग्रहीतृ, ता, m. ‘hand-<BR>taker,’ one who has married, a bridegroom, husband.<BR>—पाणि-ग्राह, अस्, m. taking the hand, marriage;<BR>one who has married, a bridegroom, husband.<BR>—पाणि-घ, अस्, m. ‘striking with the hand,’ a<BR>drummer, one who plays on a tabor or other hand-<BR>instrument; a workman, handicraftsman.<BR>—पाणि-<BR>घात, अस्, m. a blow with the hand; striking with<BR>the hand, boxing; one who strikes with his hand, a<BR>boxer.<BR>—पाणि-घ्न, अस्, m., Ved. clapping the<BR>hands.<BR>—पाणि-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—पाणि-चापल्य, अम्, n. fidgeting with the hands,<BR>snapping the fingers, &c.<BR>—पाणि-ज, अस्, m. a finger-<BR>nail.<BR>—पाणि-तल, अम्, n. the palm or flat of the<BR>hand; a particular weight (= 2 Tolakas); (ए), n. du.<BR>the two palms.<BR>—पाणि-धर्म, अस्, m. form of<BR>marriage, manner of marrying.<BR>—पाणिन्-धम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, blowing through the hands; with<BR>अध्वन्, a journey in which a person blows into his<BR>hands, (perhaps) cold, chilly; obscure, dark (as a<BR>path, where a noise is made with the hands to<BR>frighten away snakes &c.).<BR>—पाणिन्-धय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, drinking out of the hands.<BR>—पाणिन्-पल्लव, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. ‘hand-twig,’ the fingers.<BR>—पाणि-पात्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘hand-cupped,’ using the hand as a drinking-<BR>vessel, drinking out of the hand.<BR>—पाणि-पाद, अम्,<BR>n. the hands and feet.<BR>—पाणि-पीडन, अम्, n. press-<BR>ing the hand (of a bride), marriage.<BR>—पाणि-पूर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filling the hand.<BR>—पाणिप्रणयि-ता, f.<BR>the state of being taken as a wife, wife-hood.<BR>—पाणि-<BR>प्रणयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, loved by the hand, being or<BR>resting in the hand; (इनी), f. ‘beloved of the<BR>hand,’ a wife.<BR>—पाणि-प्रदान, अम्, n. giving<BR>the hand (in confirmation of a promise).<BR>—पाणि-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. union or junction of the hands (in<BR>marrying).<BR>—पाणि-भुज्, क्, m. the glomerous fig-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">Page0562-c+ 78</a>]<BR>tree, Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—पाणि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessed of hands.<BR>—पाणि-मर्द, अस्, m. Carissa<BR>Carandas (= कर-मर्द).<BR>—पाणि-मुक्त, अम्, n.,<BR>scil. अस्त्र, a missile weapon, one thrown with the<BR>hand, as a dart, spear.<BR>—पाणि-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>‘hand-mouthed,’ having the hand for a mouth.<BR>—पाणि-<BR>मूल, अम्, n. the root of the hand, the extremity<BR>of the arm.<BR>—पाणि-रुह्, ट्, or पाणि-रुह, अस्, m. a<BR>finger-nail.<BR>—पाणि-वाद, अस्, m. ‘playing with the<BR>hand,’ one who plays a drum or tabour, a drummer;<BR>(अम्), n. clapping the hands together.<BR>—पाणि-<BR>वादक, अस्, m. ‘playing with the hand,’ one who<BR>plays a drum or tabour, a drummer.<BR>—पाणि-सङ्-<BR>ग्रहण, अम्, n. clasping the hand (in confirmation<BR>of a promise), shaking hands.<BR>—पाणि-सर्ग्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, unwound and let out of the hand (as a rope).<BR>—पाणि-सर्या (?), f. a rope or cord.<BR>—पाणि-स्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being in the hand, held in the hand.<BR>—पाणि-स्वनिक, अस्, m. one who plays musical<BR>instruments with the hands.<BR>—पाणि-हता, f., scil.<BR>पुष्करिणी, N. of a lake (which the gods created<BR>for Śākya-muni with a stroke of the hand).<BR>—पाणौ-<BR>करण, अम्, n. marriage.<BR>—पाण्य्-आस्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘hand-mouthed,’ having the hand for a mouth; (अस्),<BR>m. a Brāhman who reads the Vedas upon receiving<BR>a gift at a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण|पाणः
2. पाण, अस्, m. = पाणि, the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिक|पाणिकः
पाणिक, अस्, m. a merchant; N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Skanda; (आ), f. a kind of song or<BR>singing; a sort of spoon or ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन्
पाणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, at the end of an adj. comp. for<BR>पाणि [cf. शस्त्र-प्˚, शूल-प्˚]; (इनस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a family reckoned among the Kauśikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणीतल|पाणीतलं
पाणीतल, अम्, n. a particular measure (= 2 To-<BR>lakas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्य|पाण्यः
1. पाण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 563), belonging<BR>to the hand (Ved.); a patronymic (= कौण्डिन्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन|पाणिनः
पाणिन पाणिन, अस्, m. said to = पाणिनि,<BR>and according to some a patronymic from Paṇin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनि|पाणिनिः
पाणिनि, इस्, m. (probably fr. पाणिन above), N.<BR>of the most eminent Hindū grammarian (regarded<BR>as an inspired Muni; according to one legend his<BR>grandfather was an inspired legislator called Devala,<BR>and his mother's name was Dākṣī, see दाक्षेय;<BR>the date at which he lived is a subject of controversy,<BR>but he is generally placed in the middle of the<BR>fourth century B. C.; from Śalātura, thought to<BR>have been the dwelling-place of his ancestors, he is<BR>said by some to have been called Śālāturīya; cf.<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 3, 94).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीय|पाणिनीयं|पाणिनीयः
पाणिनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Pāṇini, written<BR>or composed by Pāṇini; (अस्), m. a disciple or fol-<BR>lower of Pāṇini, one who follows the system of<BR>Pāṇini; an adherent or admirer of Pāṇini; (अम्),<BR>n. (with or without व्य्-आकरण) the grammar of<BR>Pāṇini.<BR>—पाणिनीय-दर्शन, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Sarva-darśana-saṅgraha.<BR>—पाणिनीय-<BR>मत-दर्पण, अम्, n. ‘mirror of the system of<BR>Pāṇini,’ N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणीतक
पाणीतक पाणीतक, अस्, m., N. of a being<BR>attendant upon Skanda; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>(a various reading for करीति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डक
पाण्डक पाण्डक, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डर|पांडर|पाण्डरं|पाण्डरः
पाण्डर पाण्डर, पाण्डव. See p. 563,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डित्य|पांडित्य|पांडित्यं|पाण्डित्यं
पाण्डित्य पाण्डित्य, अम्, n. (fr. पण्डित),<BR>scholarship, erudition, learning; cleverness, skill,<BR>dexterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डु|पांडु|पाण्डुः
पाण्डु पाण्डु, उस्, उस्, उ (said to be fr. rt.<BR>पण्ड्), yellowish white, white, pale; (उस्), m. pale<BR>or yellowish white colour; jaundice; N. of two<BR>plants, Trichosanthes Diœca (= पाण्डुर-फली);<BR>a white elephant; N. of a prince, a son of Vyāsa by<BR>the wife of Vicitra-vīrya and brother of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra and Vidura; of a son of Janam-ejaya and<BR>brother of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a son of Dhātṛ by<BR>Āyatī (according to others he is called Prāṇa); of an<BR>attendant of Śiva; of a Nāga-rāja; of a people in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-a" target="_blank">Page0563-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Madhya-deśa; (उस्), f. a species of plant, Glycine<BR>Debilis (commonly called Maṣāṇi); [cf. Hib.<BR>buidhe, ‘yellow.’]<BR>—पाण्डु-कण्टक, अस्, m. Achy-<BR>ranthes Aspera (= अपा-मार्ग).<BR>—पाण्डु-कम्बल,<BR>अस्, m. a white woollen covering or blanket; a warm<BR>upper garment; the housings of a royal elephant; a<BR>kind of stone (limestone or marble ?).<BR>—पाण्डु-<BR>कम्बलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, covered with a white woollen<BR>blanket; (ई), m. a carriage covered with a sort of<BR>blanket; the housings of a royal elephant.<BR>—पाण्-<BR>डु-करण, अम्, or पाण्डु-कर्मन्, अ, n. (in<BR>medicine) making or rendering white.<BR>—पाण्डु-<BR>तरु, उस्, m. Grislea Tomentosa (= धव).<BR>—पाण्-<BR>डु-ता, f. or पाण्डु-त्व, अम्, n. whitish-yellow<BR>colour, paleness.<BR>—पाण्डु-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—पाण्डु-दुकूल, अम्, n. a white winding-<BR>sheet.<BR>—पाण्डुदुकूल-सीवन, अम्, n. ‘sewing of<BR>the white winding-sheet,’ N. of a place where<BR>Śākya-muni made a white winding-sheet.<BR>—पाण्डु-<BR>नाग, अस्, m. a white elephant; the plant Rottleria<BR>Tinctoria.<BR>—पाण्डु-पत्त्र-ता, f., Ved. the growing<BR>yellow of leaves.<BR>—पाण्डु-पत्त्री, f. = रेणुका, a<BR>species of fragrant substance.<BR>—पाण्डु-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m. a son of Pāṇḍu, any one of the Pāṇḍava princes;<BR>(there are many similar compounds, as पाण्डु-<BR>नन्दन, &c.)<BR>—पाण्डु-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>white-backed, having no distinguished or auspicious<BR>mark on the body, one from whom nothing great<BR>is to be expected.<BR>—पाण्डु-फल, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>yellow fruit,’ Trichosanthes Diœca; (आ), f. a species<BR>of gourd (= चिर्भिटा); (ई), f. = पाण्डुर-फली.<BR>—पाण्डु-भाव, अस्, m. becoming yellowish-white.<BR>—पाण्डु-भूम, अस्, आ, अम्, having a white, chalky<BR>soil; (अस्), m. a country with a light-coloured soil.<BR>—पाण्डु-मृत्तिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a white,<BR>chalky soil, consisting of chalk; (आ), f. a pale soil;<BR>the opal.<BR>—पाण्डु-मृद्, त्, f. chalk, a chalky soil,<BR>a country in which the soil is of a whitish colour.<BR>—पाण्डु-रङ्ग, अस्, m. a kind of vegetable (com-<BR>monly called पाटराङ्गा).<BR>—पाण्डु-राग, अस्, m.<BR>Artemisia Indica; whiteness, pallor.<BR>—पाण्डु-रोग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘yellow disease,’ jaundice.<BR>—पाण्डुरोगिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, suffering from jaundice, jaundiced.<BR>—पाण्डु-<BR>लेख, अम्, n. an outline or sketch made with a style<BR>or with chalk.<BR>—पाण्डु-लोमशा or पाण्डु-लोमा, f.<BR>Glycine Debilis.<BR>—पाण्डु-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, pale-<BR>coloured, white; (अस्), m. whiteness.<BR>—पाण्डु-वर्म-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—पाण्डु-शर्करा,<BR>f. light-coloured gravel (the disease).<BR>—पाण्डु-शर्-<BR>मिला, f. an epithet of Draupadī the wife of the<BR>sons of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—पाण्डु-सोपाक, अस्, m. a particular<BR>mixed caste, the offspring of a Caṇḍāla by a Vaidehī<BR>mother (whose occupation, according to Manu X.<BR>37, is working with bamboos and reeds, making<BR>baskets, mats, &c.).<BR>—पाण्ड्व्-आमय, अस्, m. ‘yellow<BR>disease,’ jaundice.<BR>—पाण्ड्वामयिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffer-<BR>ing from jaundice, jaundiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0562-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डर|पांडर|पाण्डरं|पाण्डरः
पाण्डर, अस्, आ, अम्, whitish-yellow, whitish,<BR>white; (अस्), m. a species of plant (= मरु-वक);<BR>N. of a mountain; of a Nāga; of a sect; (अम्), n.<BR>the blossom of the jasmine; red chalk, ruddle.<BR>—पाण्डर-द्वार-गो-पुर, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>white doors and city gates.<BR>—पाण्डर-पुष्पिका, f.<BR>a species of plant (= शीतला).<BR>—पाण्डर-भिक्षु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘a white-robed mendicant,’ epithet of a par-<BR>ticular sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डरक
पाण्डरक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga-rāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डव|पांडव|पांडवः|पाण्डवः
पाण्डव, अस्, m. a patronymic, a son or descendant<BR>of Pāṇḍu; a partisan of the sons of Pāṇḍu; N. of a<BR>mountain; (आस्), m. pl. the five reputed sons of<BR>Pāṇḍu (Yudhi-ṣṭhira, Bhīma, Arjuna, Nakula, and<BR>Saha-deva; cf. कुन्ती and माद्री); the party or<BR>adherents of the sons of Pāṇḍu; (अस्, ई, अम्), be-<BR>longing to the sons of Pāṇḍu, connected with the<BR>five Pāṇḍavas.<BR>—पाण्डव-नकुल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>poet.<BR>—पाण्डव-वह्नि, अयस्, m. pl. ‘the Pāṇḍava<BR>fires,’ a N. applied to the three elder sons of Pāṇḍu<BR>(‘kindled on the Araṇi, Pṛthā or Kuntī;’ cf. पृथा-<BR>रणि).<BR>—पाण्डव-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘best of the<BR>sons of Pāṇḍu,’ an epithet of Yudhi-ṣṭhria.<BR>—पाण्-<BR>डवाभील (˚व-आभ्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवायन|पांडवायनः|पाण्डवायनः
पाण्डवायन, आस्, m. pl. the children of Pāṇḍu;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa the friend and ally of<BR>the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवीय|पांडवीय
पाण्डवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the children of<BR>Pāṇḍu, happening to the Pāṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवेय|पांडवेय|पांडवेयः|पाण्डवेयः
पाण्डवेय = पाण्डव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुक|पांडुकः|पाण्डुकः
पाण्डुक, अस्, आ, अम्, = पाण्डु; (अस्), m. a pale or<BR>yellowish-white colour; the jaundice; N. of a prince<BR>(= पाण्डु); a species of rice; N. of one of the<BR>nine treasures of the Jainas; (अम्), n., N. of a par-<BR>ticular forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकिन्|पांडुकिन्
पाण्डुकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from jaundice,<BR>jaundiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुर|पांडुर
पाण्डुर, अस्, आ, अम्, whitish, white, pale, yel-<BR>lowish-white; (अस्), m. a form of jaundice; a species<BR>of plant (= मरु-वक); N. of a being attendant<BR>upon Skanda; (आ), f. Glycine Debilis (= माष-<BR>पर्णी); (अम्), n. the white leprosy, vitiligo.<BR>—पाण्-<BR>डुर-ता, f. whiteness, white colour.<BR>—पाण्डुर-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘the pale tree,’ Wrightia Antidy-<BR>senterica.<BR>—पाण्डुर-पृष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, = पाण्डु-<BR>पृष्ठ, q. v.<BR>—पाण्डुर-फली, f. a species of shrub<BR>(= पाण्डु-फली, पाण्डु, धूसरा, &c.).<BR>—पाण्-<BR>डुरेक्षु (˚र-इक्˚), उस्, m. ‘pale sugar-cane,’ a<BR>species of sugar-cane (= श्वेतेक्षु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरिमन्|पांडुरिमन्
पाण्डुरिमन्, आ, m. pale or white colour, paleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डूक
पाण्डूक, अस्, m., Ved. a species of rice; [cf.<BR>पाण्डुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्य|पांड्य|पाण्ड्यः
पाण्ड्य, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people and of the<BR>country in the Dekhan inhabited by them; (अस्), m.<BR>a prince of the Pāṇḍyas; N. of a son of Ā-krīḍa;<BR>N. of the mountain-range in the Pāṇḍya country.<BR>—पाण्ड्य-देश, अस्, m. the country of the Pāṇḍyas.<BR>—पाण्ड्य-वाट, Ved., N. of a district in which<BR>pearls are found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्ड्व|पांड्वं
पाण्ड्व, अम्, n. an uncoloured woollen garment;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people in Madhya-deśa; (a<BR>various reading for पाण्डु and पाण्ड्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्य|पाण्यः
पाण्य 2. पाण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. पण्),<BR>praiseworthy, excellent. (For. 1. पाण्य see p. 562,<BR>col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात् 2. पात्, m. (fr. rt. 2. पत्), falling;<BR>sin, wickedness. (For 1. see under rt. 3. पा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
2. पात, अस्, m. (for 1. see under rt. 3. पा), flying,<BR>mode of flying, flight; throwing one's self into or<BR>down, falling, fall, downfall; alighting, descending;<BR>a cast, throw, shot; a stroke (e. g. खड्ग-पात, a<BR>sword-stroke); shedding, discharging, emitting, pour-<BR>ing out; destruction, dissolution; an attack, inroad,<BR>incursion; falling out, happening, coming to pass;<BR>defect, failing, fault, transgression; (in astrology) a<BR>malignant aspect; the node in a planet's orbit; an<BR>epithet of Rāhu; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a school of<BR>the Yajur-veda.<BR>—पाताधिकार (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘chapter on malignant aspects,’ N. of the eleventh<BR>chapter of the Sūrya-Siddhānta and of the thirteenth<BR>of the Ārya-Siddhānta<BR>—पातोत्पात (˚त-उत्˚), आस्,<BR>m. pl. falls and rises, depressions and elevations,<BR>ups and downs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातक|पातकं|पातकः
पातक, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to fall; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>‘that which causes to fall or sink,’ sin, crime.<BR>—पा-<BR>तक-योग, अस्, m. incurring guilt, acting sinfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकिन्
पातकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, guilty of a crime, criminal,<BR>wicked, sinful, a sinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातन|पातनं
पातन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to fall, felling, laying<BR>low, cutting down; (अम्), n. causing to fall, felling,<BR>bringing down, throwing down, knocking down,<BR>laying low; throwing (as dice); lowering, humbling;<BR>removing, bringing away; causing to fall asunder,<BR>dividing; nodding (?); (with दण्डस्य) causing the<BR>rod to fall, chastising, punishing; (with जलौकसाम्)<BR>application of leeches; (with गर्भस्य) destroying<BR>the fetus, causing an abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातनीय
पातनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caused to fall or<BR>alight, to be discharged or shot off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातयितृ
पातयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who causes to fall,<BR>one who throws (dice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातयित्वा
पातयित्वा, ind. having made to fall; having<BR>thrown or put down or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाताल|पातालं|पातालः
पाताल, अम्, n. (probably connected with 2. पात,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">Page0563-c+ 78</a>]<BR>the termination is compared with आल = आलय in<BR>अन्तर्-आल; the names of the other hells point to<BR>some connection with तल), one of the seven<BR>regions under the earth and the abode of the Nāgas<BR>or serpents and demons (seven such regions are<BR>enumerated, viz. A-tala, Vi-tala, Su-tala, Rasā-tala,<BR>Talātala, Mahā-tala, and Pātāla; but Pātāla is some-<BR>times used as a general name for all: according to<BR>the Mahā-bhārata, Pātāla is also a town in the<BR>world of the serpent-race); an excavation, hole,<BR>chasm; submarine fire; (in astrology) the fourth<BR>sign from that in which the sun is present, the fourth<BR>house; (अस्), m. a sort of apparatus for distillation<BR>or for calcining and subliming metals (formed of two<BR>earthen pots, the upper one inverted over the lower,<BR>and the two joined together by their necks with<BR>cement and placed in a hole containing fire); an<BR>epithet of Jupiter's year of 361 days; N. of the<BR>attendant of the fourteenth Arhat of the present<BR>Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—पाताल-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a Daitya<BR>prince.<BR>—पाताल-खण्ड, अस्, m., N. of the fourth<BR>part of the Padma-Purāṇa and of a part of the<BR>Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—पाताल-गङ्गा, f. the Ganges of<BR>the lower regions.<BR>—पाताल-गरुडी, f. or पाताल-<BR>गरुडाह्वय (˚ड-आह्˚), अस्, m. a species of creeper<BR>(= गारुडी).<BR>—पाताल-निलय, अस्, or पाताल-वासिन्,<BR>ई, or पातालौकस् (˚ल-ओक्˚), आस्, m. an inhabitant<BR>of the nether world, a demon, Daitya, Asura; a<BR>Nāga or serpent-demon.<BR>—पाताल-भोगि-वर्ग, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a part of the Nāma-liṅgānuśāsana by<BR>Amara-siṃha.<BR>—पाताल-वर्णन, अम्, n. ‘description<BR>of hell,’ N. of the first chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa<BR>of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—पाताल-विजय, अस्, m.<BR>‘victory over hell,’ N. of the twenty-fourth and<BR>twenty-fifth chapters of the Uttara-kāṇḍa of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिक|पातिकः
पातिक, अस्, m. the Gangetic porpoise, Delphinus<BR>Gangeticus (= शिशु-मार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित
पातित, अस्, आ, अम्, made to fall, felled, thrown<BR>down, cast down, struck down; lowered, depressed,<BR>humbled, overthrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित्य|पातित्यं
पातित्य, अम्, n. (fr. पतित), the state of one<BR>who is fallen or sunk, loss of position or caste,<BR>degraded condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिन्
पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, flying, going to, going, alighting<BR>on; falling, sinking; being included or contained<BR>in; causing to fall, felling, throwing down; pouring<BR>forth, discharging, emitting; [cf. अन्तः-प्˚, एक-प्˚,<BR>गर्भ-प्˚, दण्ड-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिली
पातिली, f. a trap or snare for catching deer; a small<BR>earthen vessel or pot, especially used by religious<BR>mendicants; a woman of a particular class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुक|पातुकः
पातुक, अस्, ई, अम्, falling frequently or habitually,<BR>apt or disposed to fall; falling, losing caste; going<BR>to hell; (अस्), m. the declivity of a mountain, a<BR>precipice; an aquatic animal of a large size; (figura-<BR>tively) the water-elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
1. पात्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 564, col. 1),<BR>to be felled, to be caused to fall, to be precipitated;<BR>to be inflicted or imposed (as a penalty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्यमान
पात्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being caused to fall,<BR>being precipitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्ग|पातंग
पातङ्ग पातङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पतङ्-ग),<BR>belonging or peculiar to a grasshopper or moth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्गि|पातंगि|पातंगिः|पातङ्गिः
पातङ्गि, इस्, m. the son of the Sun, Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातञ्जल|पातंजल|पातञ्जलं
पातञ्जल पातञ्जल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पतञ्जलि),<BR>composed by Patañjali; (अम्), n., scil. शास्त्र, the<BR>Yoga system of philosophy (first taught by Patañjali).<BR>—पातञ्जल-दर्शन, अम्, n. ‘the system of Pa-<BR>tañjali,’ N. of a chapter of the Sarva-darśana-saṅgraha<BR>ascribed to Mādhavācārya.<BR>—पातञ्जल-भाष्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a philosophical work on the Yoga-<BR>sūtras by Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातञ्जलि
पातञ्जलि, इस्, m. a various reading for पतञ्-<BR>जलि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातत्रिण
पातत्रिण पातत्रिण, अस्, ई, अम्, containing<BR>the word पतत्रिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातल्य
पातल्य पातल्य, अम्, n., Ved. a particular<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">Page0564-a+ 72</a>]<BR>part of a carriage; (according to Sāy.) = कीलक, a<BR>yoke-pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातव्य
पातव्य 1. and 2. पातव्य. See under rts.<BR>1. and 3. पा, pp. 559, 560.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातसाह
पातसाह पातसाह, अस्, m. = پادشاه a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाताण्डिनीय
पाताण्डिनीय पाताण्डिनीय, आस्, m. pl., N.<BR>of a school of the Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाति|पातिः
पाति पाति, इस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. पा; but con-<BR>nected with rt. 1. पत्), a master, lord, owner, pos-<BR>sessor; a husband (= पति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिव्रत्य|पातिव्रत्यं
पातिव्रत्य, अम्, n. (fr. पति-व्रता), devotedness<BR>or loyalty to a husband, conjugal fidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्नीवत
पात्नीवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पत्नी-वत्), Ved. be-<BR>longing to Agni-patnīvat, i. e. to Agni together with<BR>the wives of the gods; containing the word पत्नीवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्नीशाल
पात्नीशाल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पत्नी-शाला), Ved. being<BR>or contained in the पत्नी-शाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
2. पात्य, अम्, n. dominion. (For 1. पात्य see<BR>p. 563, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातृ
पातृ पातृ. See under rts. 1. and 3. पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्यमान
पात्यमान पात्यमान. See p. 563, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
पात्र 1. and 2. पात्र. See under rts. 1.<BR>and 3. पा, pp. 559, 560.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रट|पात्रटः
पात्रट पात्रट, अस्, आ, अम्, spare, emaciate,<BR>thin; (अस्), m. a cup, pot; ragged garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रपाक
पात्रपाक पात्र-पाक, अस्, m. decoction of<BR>medicinal herbs; (incorrectly for पत्त्र-पाक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथ|पाथं|पाथः
पाथ पाथ, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. पा),<BR>fire; the sun; (अम्), n. water [cf. पीथ]; N. of a<BR>Sāman; = पथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथस्
पाथस्, अस्, n., Ved. a spot, place; food; air;<BR>water.<BR>—पाथो-ज, अम्, n. ‘water-born,’ a lotus.<BR>—पाथो-द, अस्, m. ‘water-giver,’ a cloud.<BR>—पा-<BR>थो-धर, अस्, m. ‘water-bearer,’ a cloud.<BR>—पा-<BR>थो-धि, इस्, m. ‘receptacle of waters,’ the ocean.<BR>—पाथो-निधि, इस्, m. ‘treasure-house of waters,’<BR>the ocean.<BR>—पाथो-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. possessing<BR>room or space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथिस्
पाथिस्, इस्, m. the sea; the eye; (इस्), n. a blotch,<BR>scab; water (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथ्य
पाथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a spot or place;<BR>(Sāy.) N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथेय|पाथेयं
पाथेय पाथेय, अम्, n. (fr. पथिन्), pro-<BR>vender or provisions &c. for a journey, viaticum; the<BR>sign of the zodiac Virgo (= पाथोन).<BR>—पाथेय-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with provisions for a<BR>journey, provisioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोन
पाथोन पाथोन (corrupted fr. the Gr.<BR>παρθένος), Ved. the sign of the zodiac Virgo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथ्न्य
पाथ्न्य पाथ्न्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic<BR>of Dadhīca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्
पाद् पाद् (fr. rt. 2. पद्), see 3. पद्, p. 529;<BR>used at the end of comps., cf. द्वि-पाद्, त्रि-पाद्,<BR>and see Gram. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद|पादः
पाद, अस्, m. the foot (of men and animals;<BR>sometimes added in token of respect to proper names<BR>or titles of address, e. g. आकर्णयन्तु देव-पादाः,<BR>let your Majesty listen; कुमारिल-पादाः, the<BR>venerable Kumārila); the foot or leg of an inanimate<BR>object (as of a bedstead); a column, pillar; a foot as<BR>a measure (= 12 Aṅgulis); the foot or root of a<BR>tree; the foot of a mountain, a hill at the foot of<BR>a mountain; the bottom (of a bag); a ray or beam<BR>of light (rays being considered as the feet or hands<BR>of the heavenly bodies); a quarter, a fourth part<BR>(this sense is perhaps derived from the foot of a<BR>quadruped being one out of four); a quarter of<BR>a weight of gold (= 1(1/4) Paṇa); the fourth part of a<BR>book, (the Adhyāyas in the Śaunakīyā Catur-adhyā-<BR>yikā, in the Śārīraka-mīmāṃsā, and in Pāṇini's<BR>grammar are divided severally into four Pādas, as<BR>also the Dhanur-veda and the Vāyu-Purāṇa; while,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-b" target="_blank">Page0564-b+ 81</a>]<BR>on the other hand, the Adhyāyas in Vopa-deva's<BR>grammar contain more than four Pādas); the fourth<BR>part of a Śloka or of any verse; the line of a hymn<BR>or stanza of the Ṛg-veda or of any stanza; the<BR>quadrant of a circle; a part in general; [cf. Goth.<BR>fōtu-s, ‘a foot:’ Lith. páda-s, ‘the sole of the<BR>foot;’ pénda-s, ‘a vestige:’ probably Hib. fadadh,<BR>‘kindling, lighting;’ fadaidhim, ‘I kindle, excite,<BR>provoke.’]<BR>—पाद-कटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. or पाद-<BR>कीलिका, f. an ornament for the feet or ankles, an<BR>anklet.<BR>—पाद-कृच्छ्र, अस्, m. ‘quarter-penance,’<BR>a sort of penance (eating and fasting on alternate<BR>nights).<BR>—पाद-क्षेप, अस्, m. a footstep.<BR>—पाद-<BR>गण्डिर, अस्, m. morbid enlargement of the legs<BR>and feet.<BR>—पाद-गृह्य or पादे-गृह्य, ind., Ved.,<BR>see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. II. 1, 72.<BR>—पाद-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m.<BR>‘foot-knot,’ the ankle.<BR>—पाद-ग्रहण, अम्, n.<BR>laying hold of or clasping the feet (of a Brāhman or<BR>superior as a mark of respectful salutation).<BR>—पाद-<BR>घृत, अम्, n. melted butter for anointing the feet.<BR>—पाद-चतुर or पाद-चत्वर, अस्, m. a slan-<BR>derer, calumniator; a goat; a sand-bank; hail; the<BR>religious fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa.<BR>—पाद-चापल्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘foot-unsteadiness,’ fidgeting or shuffling with<BR>the feet.<BR>—पाद-चार, अस्, m. going on foot, walk-<BR>ing; the daily position of the planets; (एण), ind. on<BR>foot.<BR>—पाद-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, going or walking on<BR>foot, having feet for locomotion; fighting on foot;<BR>(ई), m. a footman, pedestrian, a foot-soldier.<BR>—पाद-<BR>चिह्न, अम्, n. foot-mark, foot-print.<BR>—पाद-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘born from the foot (of Brahmā),’ a Śūdra,<BR>man of the fourth and servile tribe.<BR>—पाद-जल,<BR>अम्, n. water for the feet; water in which the feet<BR>have been washed; (अस्, आ, अम्), that of which a<BR>fourth part is water, mixed with one fourth of water.<BR>—पाद-जाह, अम्, n. = पाद-मूल, that part of<BR>the foot to which the leg is articulated, the tarsus.<BR>—पाद-तल, अम्, n. the sole or lower part of the<BR>foot; (ए), ind. under the feet.<BR>—पाद-तस्, ind. out<BR>of the feet, from the feet, at or near the feet,<BR>(पादतः कृ, to put down at the feet); at the<BR>foot (of a bed); in the south-west (Manu III. 89,<BR>according to Kullūka, this may also mean ‘at the<BR>foot of the bed’); by or with a quarter; after a<BR>quarter of a verse (Ved.); step by step, by degrees.<BR>—पाद-त्र, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?), or पाद-त्रा,<BR>f. ‘foot-covering,’ a shoe.<BR>—पाद-त्राण, अम्, n.<BR>‘foot-protecting,’ a boot, shoe.<BR>—पाद-दारी or<BR>पाद-दारिका, f. ‘foot-rending,’ a chap in the feet,<BR>a chilblain.<BR>—पाद-दाह, अस्, m. a burning sensation<BR>in the feet (said to be in India an excruciating pain<BR>difficult to remedy).<BR>—पाद-धावन, अम्, n.<BR>washing the feet.<BR>—पाद-धावनिका, f. sand used<BR>for rubbing the feet.<BR>—पाद-नख, अस्, m. a toe-<BR>nail.<BR>—पाद-नालिका, f. an ornament for the feet,<BR>an anklet.<BR>—पाद-निचृत्, त्, f., scil. गायत्री, a<BR>defective metre, in which one syllable is wanting in<BR>each Pāda; (also wrongly spelt पाद-निवृत्.)<BR>—पा-<BR>द-निष्क, अस्, m. = पन्-निष्क, p. 529.<BR>—पाद-<BR>न्यास, अस्, m. placing the feet, a dance or measured<BR>step.<BR>—पाद-प, अस्, m. ‘imbibing nourishment<BR>with the foot or root,’ a plant, tree; ‘protecting<BR>the feet,’ (fr. rt. 3. पा) a foot-stool, cushion for the<BR>feet; (आ), f. a shoe, slipper.<BR>—पादप-खण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. a group or clump of trees.<BR>—पाद-पद्धति,<BR>इस्, f. a line of footsteps, a track, trail.<BR>—पाद-<BR>पद्म, अस्, m. ‘foot-lotus,’ a foot beautiful as a lotus.<BR>—पाद-परिघट्टन, अम्, n. trampling with the<BR>feet, treading upon.<BR>—पादप-रुहा, f. a climbing<BR>plant, parasitical plant.<BR>—पाद-पालिका, f. an orna-<BR>ment for the feet, an anklet.<BR>—पाद-पाश, अस्, m.<BR>a foot-rope for cattle or horses; an anklet of small<BR>bells, &c.; (ई), f. a chain for the feet, a fetter; a<BR>foot-carpet or mat.<BR>—पाद-पीठ, अम्, n. a foot-<BR>stool.<BR>—पादपीठिका, f. any common or vulgar<BR>trade, as that of a barber, &c.; white stone.<BR>—पाद-<BR>पीवी, f. a shoe; (incorrectly for पाद-पीठी?).<BR>—पाद-पूरण, अस्, आ, अम्, (Ved.) filling out a<BR>part or line of a verse (as a particle), expletive; (अम्),<BR>n. the filling out a line or the measure of a verse.<BR>—पाद-प्रक्षालन, अम्, n. ‘washing the feet,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-c" target="_blank">Page0564-c+ 81</a>]<BR>N. of a chapter of the Purāṇa-sarva-sva.<BR>—पाद-<BR>प्रणाम, अस्, m. bowing to the feet, prostration.<BR>—पाद-प्रतिष्ठान, अम्, n. a foot-stool.<BR>—पा-<BR>द-प्रधारण, अम्, n. ‘foot-covering,’ a shoe.<BR>—पाद-प्रहार, अस्, m. ‘foot-blow,’ a kick.<BR>—पाद-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound or held toge-<BR>ther by quarters of verses (as a metre).<BR>—पाद-बन्-<BR>ध, अस्, m. any tie for the foot, a chain or fetter for<BR>the feet.<BR>—पाद-बन्धन, अम्, n. a fetter for the<BR>feet; a stock of cattle (so called from the foot-ropes<BR>with which cattle are tied).<BR>—पाद-भाग, अस्, m. a<BR>fourth part, quarter.<BR>—पाद-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, possessing<BR>a quarter, being only a quarter.<BR>—पाद-मिश्र, see<BR>Pāṇ. VI. 3, 56.<BR>—पाद-मुद्रा, f. the impression<BR>of a footstep, foot-print, trace.<BR>—पाद-मूल, अम्, n.<BR>‘root of the foot,’ the part of the foot to which the<BR>leg is articulated, tarsus; the sole of the foot; the<BR>heel; a polite designation of a person; the foot of<BR>a mountain.<BR>—पाद-युद्ध, अम्, n. ‘foot-fight,’<BR>fighting on foot.<BR>—पाद-रक्ष, अस्, m. a foot-<BR>protector, foot-guard; (आस्), m. pl. armed men who<BR>run by the side of an elephant in battle to protect its<BR>feet from wounds.<BR>—पाद-रक्षण, अम्, n. a cover<BR>for the feet; a leather boot or shoe, a stocking.<BR>—पाद-रजस्, अस्, n. the dust of the feet.<BR>—पाद-<BR>रज्जु, उस्, f. a tether or rope for the foot of an<BR>elephant.<BR>—पाद-रथी, f. ‘foot-vehicle,’ a shoe,<BR>boot, slipper.<BR>—पाद-रोहण, अस्, m. ‘growing<BR>from roots,’ the Indian fig-tree.<BR>—पाद-लग्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, sticking to the foot.<BR>—पाद-लेप, अस्, m.<BR>an unguent for the feet.<BR>—पाद-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having feet, possessed of feet.<BR>—पाद-वन्दन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘saluting the feet,’ respectful salutation.<BR>—पा-<BR>द-वल्मीक, अस्, m. morbid enlargement of the legs<BR>and feet, elephantiasis.<BR>—पाद-विग्रह, अस्, m.<BR>(probably) a mode of reading in which the divisions<BR>in verses are carefully marked; (अस्, आ, अम्), hav-<BR>ing a quarter of the compass or extent.<BR>—पाद-<BR>विधान, अम्, n. ‘the arrangement of the parts of a<BR>verse,’ N. of a work ascribed to Śaunaka.<BR>—पाद-<BR>विरजस्, आस्, f. a shoe, slipper, stocking (as keeping<BR>रजस् or dust from the feet?).<BR>—पाद-वीथी, f.<BR>a shoe; (probably an incorrect form, cf. पाद-<BR>पीवी.)<BR>—पाद-वृत्त, औ, m. du., Ved. the two<BR>component elements of the quarter of a verse, i. e.<BR>the long and short syllable; (अस्), m. epithet of a<BR>Svarita separated from the preceding Ud-ātta by a<BR>hiatus.<BR>—पाद-वेष्टनिक, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a stocking.<BR>—पाद-शब्द, अस्, m. the sound or<BR>noise of footsteps (= पच्-छब्द).<BR>—पाद-शस्, ind.<BR>foot by foot; verse by verse, stanza by stanza; by a<BR>fourth part.<BR>—पाद-शाखा, f. ‘branch of the foot,’<BR>a toe.<BR>—पाद-शीली, f. an ornament for the feet, an<BR>anklet; (probably an incorrect form.)<BR>—पाद-शु-<BR>श्रूषा, f. obedience towards the feet (a respectful<BR>expression for शुश्रूषा).<BR>—पाद-शेष, अम्, n. a<BR>quarter, fourth part.<BR>—पाद-शैल, अस्, m. a hill at<BR>the foot of or near a mountain.<BR>—पाद-शोथ, अस्,<BR>m. swelling of the feet, gout.<BR>—पाद-शौच, अम्, n.<BR>cleaning the feet (= पच्-छौच).<BR>—पाद-सं-<BR>हिता. f. the union of words in a quarter of a verse.<BR>—पाद-सेवन, अम्, n. or पाद-सेवा, f. ‘foot-<BR>salutation,’ showing respect by touching the feet,<BR>service, duty.<BR>—पाद-स्तम्भ, अस्, m. a supporting<BR>beam, pillar, post.<BR>—पाद-स्फोट, अस्, m. ‘cracking<BR>of the feet,’ chilblain, a sore or ulcer on the foot.<BR>—पाद-स्वेदन, अम्, n. perspiration of the feet,<BR>causing perspiration in the feet.<BR>—पाद-हत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, struck with the feet, kicked, trodden on,<BR>touched with the feet.<BR>—पाद-हर्ष, अस्, m. numb-<BR>ness of the feet after pressure upon the crural nerves.<BR>—पाद-हारक, अस्, आ, अम्, taken away with the<BR>feet; (अस्), m. one who takes away or steals any-<BR>thing with the feet (?).<BR>—पाद-हीनात्, ind. without<BR>division or transition; on a sudden, all at once.<BR>—पादा-<BR>कुलक (˚द-आक्˚), अस्, अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of two<BR>kinds of metres.<BR>—पादाग्र (˚द-अग्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>point or extremity of the foot.<BR>—पादाघात (˚द-<BR>आघ्˚), अस्, m. ‘a blow with the foot,’ a kick.<BR>—पा-<BR>दाङ्क (˚द-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a foot-mark, footstep, foot-<BR>print, vestige.<BR>—पादाङ्गद (˚द-अङ्˚), अम्, ई, n. f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">Page0565-a+ 81</a>]<BR>an ornament for the feet or toes, an anklet.<BR>—पा-<BR>दाङ्गुलि (˚द-अङ्˚), इस्, ई, f. ‘foot-finger,’ a toe.<BR>—पादाङ्गुलीयक (˚द-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a ring worn<BR>on one of the toes.<BR>—पादाङ्गुष्ठ (˚द-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the great toe.<BR>—पादाङ्गुष्ठाश्रितावनि (˚ठ-<BR>आश्˚, ˚त-अव्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, ‘touching the ground with the<BR>toes,’ on tiptoe.<BR>—पादाङ्गुष्ठिका, f. a ring worn<BR>on the great toe.<BR>—पादाध्यास (˚द-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>treading upon, kicking.<BR>—पादानत (˚द-आन्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, bowed or bent down to the feet, prostrate.<BR>—पादानुध्यात (˚द-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, thought<BR>of by the feet of such an one (a respectful expression<BR>in inscriptions for ‘thought of by such an one’);<BR>the son and successor of any one, rightful successor<BR>of any one (‘thought of by his predecessor’).<BR>—पा-<BR>दान्त (˚द-अन्˚), अस्, m. the extremity of the feet;<BR>proximity to the feet; (ए), ind. near the feet.<BR>—पा-<BR>दान्तर (˚द-अन्˚), अम्, n. the interval of a step,<BR>the distance of a foot; (ए), ind. in immediate prox-<BR>imity to, close to (with gen.); after the interval of a<BR>step.<BR>—पादान्तिक (˚द-अन्˚), अम्, n. proximity to<BR>the feet, the neighbourhood of the feet.<BR>—पादाम्बु<BR>(˚द-अम्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, containing a fourth part of<BR>water.<BR>—पादाम्भस् (˚द-अम्˚), अस्, n. ‘foot-water,’<BR>water in which the feet have been washed.<BR>—पादा-<BR>रविन्द (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m. ‘foot-lotus,’ the foot of<BR>a deity, lover, &c.<BR>—पादार्घ्य (˚द-अर्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘offering to the feet,’ a donation to Brāhmans or<BR>venerable persons.<BR>—पादार्ध (˚द-अर्˚), अम्, n.<BR>half a quarter, an eighth; half a line of a stanza.<BR>—पादार्पण (˚द-अर्˚), अम्, n. setting down the<BR>feet.<BR>—पादावनेजन (˚द-अव्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, used<BR>for washing the feet (Ved.); washing the feet.<BR>—पादावर्त (˚द-आव्˚), अस्, m. a wheel worked by<BR>the feet for raising water from a well; a square foot.<BR>—पादावसेचन (˚द-अव्˚), अम्, n. washing the<BR>feet; water for washing the feet, water in which the<BR>feet have been washed.<BR>—पादाष्ठील (˚द-अष्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the ankle; contusion of the feet (?).<BR>—पा-<BR>दासन (˚द-आस्˚), अम्, n. a footstool.<BR>—पादास्-<BR>फालन (˚द-आस्˚), अम्, n. trampling or shuffling<BR>of the feet, motion of the feet (as in wrestling or<BR>struggling), floundering.<BR>—पादाहत (˚द-आह्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘struck with the foot,’ kicked, trodden,<BR>touched by the foot.<BR>—पादाहति (˚द-आह्˚), इस्, f.<BR>a blow with the foot, kick; treading, trampling.<BR>—पादे-गृह्य = पाद-गृह्य.<BR>—पादोत्फाल<BR>(˚द-उत्˚), अस्, m. shuffling or moving the feet.<BR>—पादोदक (˚द-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘foot-water,’ water<BR>for washing the feet, water in which the feet of a<BR>Brāhman have been washed, water hallowed by the<BR>washing of sacred feet.<BR>—पादोदक-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a sacred bathing-place at Benares.<BR>—पादो-<BR>दर (˚द-उद्˚), अस्, m. a serpent (‘using the belly<BR>in place of feet’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादक
पादक, अस्, m. a little foot (Ved.); (अस्, इका,<BR>अम्), making a quarter of anything (Ved.); at the<BR>end of a comp. = पाद; [cf. त्रि-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादय
पादय, Nom. A. पादयते, -यितुम्, to stretch<BR>out the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविक|पादविकः
पादविक, अस्, m. a traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात्
पादात्, त्, m. (properly पाद + अत्), a foot-soldier,<BR>footman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात|पादातं|पादातः
पादात, अस्, m. (properly पाद + आत), a foot-<BR>soldier, footman; (अम्), n. infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाति|पादातिः
पादाति, इस्, or पादातिक, or पादाविक, अस्, m. =<BR>पदाति, a foot-soldier, man on foot, footman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिक
पादिक, अस्, ई, अम्, lasting for a quarter of the<BR>time, amounting to a quarter or fourth, a fourth;<BR>पादिकं शतम्, one quarter of a hundred, 25 per<BR>cent; [cf. अर्ध-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन्
पादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, footed, having feet; having a<BR>fourth part or share, claiming or receiving a fourth<BR>part; having four parts, as a stanza &c.; (ई), m. a<BR>footed aquatic animal, an amphibious animal; the<BR>heir to a fourth part of an estate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन|पादिनः
पादिन, अस्, m. a fourth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादु
पादु, उस्, m., Ved. course, path (Sāy. = पादेना-<BR>गमन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुका
पादुका, f. a wooden shoe, shoe, slipper [cf.<BR>चर्म-प्˚], (अस्, आ, or ई, अम्), going on foot, going<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">Page0565-b+ 74</a>]<BR>with feet.<BR>—पादुका-कार, अस्, or पादुका-कृत्, त्,<BR>m. a shoemaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादू
पादू, ऊस्, f. a shoe.<BR>—पादू-कृत्, त्, m. a shoe-<BR>maker; (also spelt पादु-कृत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्य|पाद्यं
पाद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to the<BR>foot; (अम्), n. (with or without उदक) water for<BR>washing the feet.<BR>—पाद्य-पात्र, अम्, n. a metal<BR>vessel for washing the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादक्रमिक|पादक्रमिकः
पादक्रमिक पादक्रमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पद-<BR>क्रम), one who reads or knows the Pada-krama,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप|पादपः
पादप पाद-प. See p. 564, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादारक|पादारकः
पादारक पादारक, अस्, m. the knees or<BR>ribs of a boat (supporting the deck on each side ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्द|पादालिंदः|पादालिन्दः
पादालिन्द पादालिन्द, अस्, आ or ई, m. f. a<BR>boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्म|पाद्मः
पाद्म पाद्म, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पद्म), relating<BR>to the lotus, referring to or treating of the lotus;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic of Brahmā [cf. पद्म-<BR>गर्भ, पद्म-योनि]; N. of a Mahā-kalpa.<BR>—पाद्म-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
पान 1. पान, पानीय, पान्त. See p. 560,<BR>cols. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
पान 2. पान, अस्, m. = अपान, breath,<BR>breathing out, expiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानस|पानसं
पानस पानस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पनस), pre-<BR>pared from the fruit of the Jaka or bread-fruit tree;<BR>(अम्), n. a spirituous liquor so prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्थ|पांथ|पांथः|पान्थः
पान्थ पान्थ, अस्, m. (fr. पथिन्), a wan-<BR>derer, traveller; ‘the wanderer in the sky,’ the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्नग
पान्नग पान्नग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पन्न-ग),<BR>formed or consisting of snakes, having serpents, snaky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्नेजन
पान्नेजन पान्नेजन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. पद् +<BR>नेजन), Ved. used for washing the feet; (अम्), n.<BR>a vessel in which the feet are washed, foot-bath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप|पापं|पापः
पाप पाप, अस्, आ (or in the earlier language<BR>ई), अम् (said to be fr. rt. 3. पा; according to some for<BR>अपाप fr. rt. आप् with अप), bad, wicked, vicious, sinful,<BR>evil, mischievous, destructive; vile, low, abandoned;<BR>(in astrology) boding evil, malignant, inauspicious;<BR>(अस्), m. a wicked man, wretch, profligate; N. of<BR>a hell; (अम्), n. bad fortune, bad state, unhappiness;<BR>evil, sin, vice, crime, wickedness, transgression, guilt<BR>(e. g. पापम् अवाप्स्यसि, thou wilt incur guilt); (अम्),<BR>ind. badly, miserably, wrongly; (अया), ind., Ved.<BR>badly, wrongly, wickedly; [cf. Gr. κάκο-ς: Lat.<BR>peccare: Lith. pykiù, ‘I am angry;’ paika-s,<BR>pikta-s, ‘angry.’]<BR>—पाप-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्,<BR>or पाप-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or पाप-कर्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, or पाप-कर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or पाप-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, or पाप-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, ‘wrong-doing,’ wicked,<BR>sinful, criminal, an evil-doer, malefactor, villain.<BR>—पाप-कृत, अम्, n. or पाप-कृत्या, f. an evil<BR>deed, bad action, sin, crime.<BR>—पाप-क्षय, अस्,<BR>m. the destruction of sin.<BR>—पापक्षय-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पापक्षय-मात्र,<BR>अम्, n. entire destruction (or expiation) of sins.<BR>—पाप-गुम्प, अस्, m. epithet of Bāla-kṛṣṇa;<BR>(perhaps incorrectly for पाय-गुण्ड.)<BR>—पाप-गो-<BR>चर, अस्, आ, अम्, evidently involved in (the con-<BR>sequences of) sin.<BR>—पाप-ग्रह, अस्, m. a planet of<BR>evil or malignant aspect (as Mars, Saturn, Rāhu,<BR>Ketu); any ill-omened or inauspicious aspect of the<BR>stars as the conjunction of the sun or Budha with<BR>the moon in its last quarter; calamitous or fatal<BR>destiny.<BR>—पाप-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying or<BR>removing sin or evil deeds, expiating guilt; (अस्), m.<BR>the sesamum plant; (ई), f., N. of a river.<BR>—पाप-<BR>चर, अस्, m. ‘walking in sin,’ N. of a king.<BR>—पाप-<BR>चर्य, अस्, m. a sinner; a fiend, Rākṣasa.<BR>—पाप-<BR>चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, doing evil, sinful, wicked, criminal.<BR>—पाप-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, evil-minded, being of an<BR>evil disposition, wicked, vile.<BR>—पाप-चेली or पाप-<BR>चेलिका, f. the plant Clypea Hernandifolia, a species<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-c" target="_blank">Page0565-c+ 81</a>]<BR>of creeper (commonly called आकनादि).<BR>—पाप-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. springing from evil.<BR>—पाप-जीव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, leading an evil life, wicked, criminal.<BR>—पाप-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, worse, more wicked, very<BR>evil.<BR>—पाप-तिमिर, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘sin-bedarkened,’<BR>blinded by sin.<BR>—पाप-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. evil con-<BR>dition, misery, poverty.<BR>—पाप-द, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>bringing misfortune, inauspicious.<BR>—पाप-दर्शिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, looking at faults, malevolent.<BR>—पाप-<BR>दृश्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, seeing guilt, knowing an<BR>act to be wicked.<BR>—पाप-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, evil-<BR>eyed.<BR>—पाप-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, evil-minded.<BR>—पाप-<BR>नक्षत्र, अम्, n., Ved. an inauspicious constella-<BR>tion.<BR>—पाप-नापित, अस्, m. a vile or bad barber.<BR>—पाप-नामन्, आ, म्नी, अ, Ved. having a bad name.<BR>—पाप-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying the wicked;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; N. of a temple of<BR>Viṣṇu; (अम्), n., N. of a part of the Brahmāṇḍa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—पाप-नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sin-destroying,<BR>purifying.<BR>—पाप-निरति, इस्, इस्, इ, wicked, vil-<BR>lainous; a wretch; (इस्), f. attachment to evil, wicked-<BR>ness.<BR>—पाप-निश्चय, अस्, आ, अम्, having evil designs,<BR>malevolent.<BR>—पाप-निष्कृति, इस्, f. atonement for<BR>sin.<BR>—पाप-पति, इस्, m. ‘sinful master,’ a para-<BR>mour.<BR>—पाप-पराजित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ignomi-<BR>niously defeated.<BR>—पाप-पुण्य, आनि, n. pl. vicious<BR>or virtuous (deeds).<BR>—पाप-पुरुष, अस्, m. a vil-<BR>lainous man (a personification of all sin or archetype<BR>of a sinner, whose head is Brāhmaṇicide, whose arms<BR>are theft, and whose heart is wine-drinking, &c.; also<BR>spelt पाप-पूरुष).<BR>—पाप-फल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having evil consequences, inauspicious.<BR>—पाप-बुद्-<BR>धि, इस्, इस्, इ, evil-minded, wicked; (इस्), m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—पाप-भक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, devouring<BR>the wicked; (अस्), m. an epithet of Kāla-bhairava, a<BR>son of Śiva.<BR>—पाप-भञ्जन, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking<BR>or destroying the wicked; (अस्), m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—पाप-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, being of an evil dispo-<BR>sition, evil-minded.<BR>—पाप-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, evil-<BR>minded, of a corrupt mind, sinful, graceless, ungodly,<BR>depraved.<BR>—पाप-मित्र, अम्, n. friend or com-<BR>panion of sin, bad counsellor, seducer.<BR>—पापमित्र-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. friendship with the wicked.<BR>—पाप-<BR>मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from sin, liberated from all<BR>crime.<BR>—पाप-मोचन, अम्, n. liberating form sin,<BR>remission of guilt.<BR>—पाप-यक्ष्म, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>‘the evil disease,’ consumption.<BR>—पाप-योनि, इस्, f. a<BR>bad or low birthplace, birth in an inferior condition (as<BR>in that of an animal; considered as the punishment<BR>of sin).<BR>—पाप-रहित, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from sin.<BR>sinless.<BR>—पाप-रोग, अस्, m. any bad disease con-<BR>sidered as the penalty of sin in a former life (as<BR>leprosy, elephantiasis); small pox.<BR>—पापरोगिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, suffering from a bad disease as a penalty for<BR>sin (committed in a former life).<BR>—पापर्द्धि<BR>(˚प-ऋद्˚), इस्, f. ‘sin-prosperity,’ getting a living by<BR>hunting, the chase.<BR>—पाप-लोक, अस्, m., Ved. the<BR>evil world, the place of suffering, place of the wicked.<BR>—पापलोक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to hell or the<BR>world of the wicked, fiendish, infernal; belonging to<BR>the wicked.<BR>—पाप-वसीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, inverted;<BR>confused; (अस्), n. inversion, confusion.<BR>—पाप-व-<BR>सीयस or पाप-वस्यस, अम्, n., Ved. inversion, in-<BR>verted order, confusion.<BR>—पाप-वाद, अस्, m., Ved. an<BR>inauspicious cry.<BR>—पाप-विनाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, sin-<BR>destroying, destroying transgressions.<BR>—पापविना-<BR>शन-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पाप-<BR>विनिग्रह, अस्, m. restraining or punishing wicked-<BR>ness.<BR>—पाप-विनिश्चय, अस्, आ, अम्, intending evil,<BR>resolved on wickedness or crime.<BR>—पाप-शमन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, palliating or removing crime; (अम्), n.<BR>a sin offering; (ई), f. a species of tree; [cf. शमी.]<BR>—पाप-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, ill-disposed, prone to<BR>evil, of bad character, wicked.<BR>—पाप-शोधन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, cleansing or washing away sins; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पाप-संशमन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>removing sin.<BR>—पाप-सङ्कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, evil-<BR>minded, ill-intentioned.<BR>—पाप-सम, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>a bad year.<BR>—पाप-सम्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, equal in<BR>sin, of like guilt.<BR>—पाप-सूदन, अस्, आ, अम्, sin-<BR>destroying.<BR>—पापसूदन-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">Page0566-a+ 78</a>]<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—पाप-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, sin-destroying,<BR>destroying the wicked.<BR>—पाप-हर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>removing evil, destroying sin; (अम्), n. a means of<BR>removing evil; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR>—पापाख्या<BR>(˚प-आख्˚), f., scil. गति, epithet of one of the seven<BR>divisions of the planetary courses (according to the<BR>Parāśara-tantra extending over the constellations<BR>Hasta, Maitra, and Vi-śākhā).<BR>—पापाङ्कुशा (˚प-<BR>अङ्˚), f., N. of the eleventh day in the light half<BR>of the month Āśvina.<BR>—पापाचार (˚प-आच्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ill-conducted, following evil courses, practising<BR>evil, living an evil life, vicious.<BR>—पापात्मन् (˚प-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, evil-minded, wicked; (आ), m. a sinner,<BR>reprobate, wretch; (opposed to धर्मात्मन्.)<BR>—पापाधम (˚प-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, the lowest of<BR>the wicked, exceedingly low or wicked.<BR>—पापानुव-<BR>सित (˚प-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to sin, sinful.<BR>—पापान्त (˚प-अन्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha<BR>(‘where sins come to an end’).<BR>—पापापनुत्ति<BR>(˚प-अप्˚), इस्, f. ‘removal of sins,’ expiation.<BR>—पा-<BR>पावहीयम् (˚प-अव्˚), ind., Ved. wrongfully staying<BR>away or remaining behind.<BR>—पापाशय (˚प-आश्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, evil-intentioned, wicked, sinful.<BR>—पापाह<BR>(˚प-अह˚), अम्, n., Ved. an unlucky day.<BR>—पापाहि<BR>(˚प-अहि), इस्, m. a snake, serpent.<BR>—पापोक्त (˚प-<BR>उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. addressed in ill-omened words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापक|पापकं|पापकः
पापक, अस्, इका or अकी, अम्, bad, evil, wicked;<BR>(अम्), n. evil, wrong, wickedness, sin; (अस्), m. a<BR>wicked person, rascal; an evil or malignant planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापल|पापलं
पापल, अस्, आ, अम्, imparting or incurring guilt;<BR>(अम्), n. a particular measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिन्
पापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wicked, sinful, bad; a sinner,<BR>criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिष्ठ
पापिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, worst, lowest, most wicked;<BR>exceedingly bad, very wicked.<BR>—पापिष्ठ-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, worst, most wicked; worse, more wicked.<BR>—पापिष्ठ-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, worse, more wicked;<BR>the very worst; exceedingly wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीय
पापीय, अस्, आ, अम्, worse, &c.; (a contracted<BR>form of पापीयस् below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीयस्
पापीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, worse, worse off, more<BR>wretched or miserable; lower, poorer; more wicked;<BR>very bad or wicked, very criminal; मारः पापीयान्,<BR>(with Buddhists) the evil spirit, the devil; (अस्), m.<BR>a wicked man, wretch, villain.<BR>—पापीयस्-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = पापीयस्.<BR>—पापीयस्-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of being very wicked, great wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप्मन्
पाप्मन्, आ, m. evil, unhappiness, evil plight,<BR>suffering; crime, evil, sin, wickedness; (आ, आ, अ),<BR>injurious, hurtful, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापापुरी
पापापुरी पापापुरी, f. = पावापुरी, f., N.<BR>of a town near Rāja-gṛha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन्
पामन् पामन्, आ, m. (fr. rt. पै), a kind<BR>of skin disease, cutaneous eruption, herpes, scab.<BR>—पाम-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying the scab;<BR>(अस्), m. sulphur; (ई), f. a species of plant (= क-<BR>टुका).<BR>—पाम-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, diseased with<BR>herpes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन|पामनः
पामन, अस्, आ, अम्, diseased with herpes.<BR>—पा-<BR>मनम्-भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. becoming dis-<BR>eased with herpes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामर|पामरः
पामर, अस्, आ, अम्, diseased with herpes, scabby;<BR>wicked, vile; low, vulgar, base; stupid; (अस्), m. a<BR>man of the lowest extraction, a man engaged in<BR>any degrading occupation; an idiot, fool; a wicked<BR>man; (अम्), n. evil, bad character, wickedness.<BR>—पामरोद्धारा (˚र-उद्˚), f. ‘removing herpes,’<BR>a species of plant (= गुडूची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामा
पामा, f. herpes, scab (enumerated among the<BR>forms of so-called mild leprosy).<BR>—पामारि (˚मा-<BR>अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of the scab,’ sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाम्प
पाम्प पाम्प, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to or<BR>situated on the river Pampā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाम्पन
पाम्पन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to the<BR>river Pampā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय|पायं
पाय पाय, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. पा), water.<BR>—पाय-गुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of the author of a com-<BR>mentary on the Laghu-śabdendu-śekhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायक
पायक, अस्, इका, अम्, drinking; [cf. तैल-<BR>पायिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायन|पायनं
पायन, अम्, n. the causing or giving to drink;<BR>(Sāy.) = 1. पान, a beverage; (आ), f. causing to drink;<BR>watering, moistening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायिन्
पायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) drinking;<BR>[cf. कुण्ड-प्˚, क्षीर-प्˚, चन्द्रिका-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायु|पायुः
1. पायु, उस्, m. the anus.<BR>—पायु-क्षालन-<BR>भूमि, इस्, f. or पायु-क्षालन-वेश्मन्, अ, n. a<BR>water-closet, privy.<BR>—पायु-भेद, अस्, m., Ved. (in<BR>astrol.) N. of two ways in which an eclipse terminates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय्य|पाय्यं
1. पाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be drunk, to be caused<BR>to drink; (अम्), n. water; drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायस|पायसः
पायस पायस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पयस्), pre-<BR>pared with or made of milk or water; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. food prepared with milk, rice boiled in milk; an<BR>oblation of milk, rice, and sugar; the resin of Pinus<BR>Longifolia; turpentine; (अम्), n. milk; a kind of<BR>divine beverage, nectar (Rām. I. 15, 8).<BR>—पायस-<BR>दग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, scalded by milk-porridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायसिक
पायसिक, अस्, ई, अम्, fond of boiled milk, re-<BR>lating to any mixture of milk, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायिक|पायिकः
पायिक पायिक, अस्, m. a foot-soldier, foot-<BR>man; (probably a corruption of पादातिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायु|पायुः
पायु 2. पायु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. पा; for 1.<BR>see above), Ved. a guard, protector; N. of a man;<BR>(अवस्), m. pl. protecting powers or actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय्य|पाय्यं
2. पाय्य (for 1. see above), protection (at the<BR>end of a comp.; cf. नृ-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय्य|पाय्यं
पाय्य 3. पाय्य, अम्, n. measure; practice,<BR>profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय्य|पाय्यं
पाय्य 4. पाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, low, vile, repre-<BR>hensible, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार|पारं|पारः
पार पार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. पृ or rt. पॄ), cross-<BR>ing [cf. दुष्-प्˚]; the further shore or opposite bank of<BR>a river; the further side, concluding bound; the end<BR>or limit of anything, the utmost reach or extent;<BR>quicksilver; N. of a sage, a son of Pṛthu-ṣeṇa and<BR>father of Nīpa; of a son of Samara and father of<BR>Pṛthu; of a son of Aṅga and father of Divi-ratha;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of deities under the ninth<BR>Manu; (आ), f., N. of a river (said to flow from the<BR>Pāriyātra mountains or the central and western<BR>portion of the Vindhya chain); (ई), f. a quantity of<BR>water; a small water-jar, drinking-vessel, glass, cup;<BR>a milk-pail; a rope for tying an elephant's feet;<BR>pollen; (अम्), n. (according to some also अस्, m.),<BR>the further or opposite end or bank of a river; the<BR>totality of an object, the fullest extent (with gen.,<BR>e. g. तमसस्, of darkness; कारणानाम्, of tor-<BR>tures); extremity, end, aim (in this sense also m.);<BR>पारं गम्, to cross over; to fulfil (e. g. प्रतिज्ञा-<BR>याः पारं स गतः, he fulfilled his promise);<BR>to become proficient in; पारं नी, to bring to<BR>a close; [cf. पर, परम्; Gr. πόρο-ς, πέρα<BR>πέρᾱν, περαίνω, πείρω, περαῖο-ς, περά-τη, Πειραιεύ-ς,<BR>πέρας, πεῖραρ, ἀπειρέσ-ιο-ς; Lat. per; Lith. per,<BR>‘across;’ Slav. polŭ, ‘the opposite bank.’]<BR>—पार-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of reaching the opposite<BR>bank.<BR>—पार-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going to the opposite<BR>shore, crossing over, going through or over or across<BR>or to the end, ferrying across, intending to cross; one<BR>who has arrived at the end, accomplishing, one who<BR>has accomplished or completely mastered, completely<BR>familiar or conversant with, knowing thoroughly,<BR>well versed in (with gen. or loc. or in a comp.,<BR>e. g. वेदानाम् पारगः, well versed in the Vedas;<BR>प्रतिज्ञा-प्˚, fulfilling or keeping a promise); pro-<BR>foundly learned; going over or beyond the world;<BR>(अम्), n. keeping, fulfilling.<BR>—पार-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or पार-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who has reached<BR>the opposite shore, passed over in safety, crossed;<BR>passed beyond the world, pure, holy; (अस्), m. (with<BR>Jainas) an Arhat or deified saint and teacher.<BR>—पार-<BR>गति, इस्, f. going through, reading, studying through.<BR>—पार-गमन, अम्, n. reaching the opposite<BR>shore, crossing, going to the end.<BR>—पार-चर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, arriving at the opposite shore, crossing over.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">Page0566-c+ 81</a>]<BR>—पार-तस्, ind., Ved. on the opposite bank, on<BR>the further side.<BR>—पार-दण्डक, अस्, m. (perhaps<BR>a Vṛddhied form fr. पर + दण्डक), N. of a<BR>country (part of Orissa).<BR>—पार-दर्शक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, showing the opposite bank.<BR>—पार-दर्शन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, beholding the opposite bank or shore,<BR>able to survey all things.<BR>—पार-दृश्वन्, आ, अरी,<BR>अ, one who has seen the opposite bank, completely<BR>familiar with, knowing thoroughly; long-sighted,<BR>far-seeing, wise.<BR>—पार-ध्वज, आस्, m. pl. ‘banners<BR>of the further shore,’ N. of certain banners brought<BR>from beyond the sea (from Ceylon) and borne in<BR>procession by the kings of Kaśmīra.<BR>—पार-नेतृ,<BR>ता, त्री, तृ, bringing to the further shore.<BR>—पारम्-<BR>इत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to the opposite bank; crossed,<BR>traversed; transcendant (as spiritual knowledge);<BR>(आ), f. (probably a contracted form for पारमित-<BR>ता), coming to the opposite bank, complete attainment,<BR>perfection (the Buddhists enumerate six or sometimes<BR>ten Pāramitās or perfections as belonging to a Bodhi-<BR>sattva).<BR>—पारापार (˚र-अप्˚), अम्, n. = पारावार,<BR>the nearer and further bank, both banks, (a various<BR>reading for पारावार, q. v.); (अस्), m. the sea,<BR>ocean.<BR>—पारायण (˚र-अय्˚), अम्, n. going over,<BR>going across; reading from one end to the other,<BR>reading through, perusing, studying, study; reading<BR>a Purāṇa or causing it to be read; the whole, totality,<BR>entireness, completeness [cf. धातु-प्˚, नाम-प्˚];<BR>N. of a grammatical work; (ई), f. a N. of the<BR>goddess Sarasvatī; an act, action; considering, medi-<BR>tating; light.<BR>—पारायण-माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a section. of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa of the Pādma-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—पारायणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, reading to (any<BR>one), teaching how to pronounce; (अस्), m. a lec-<BR>turer, reader of the Purāṇas; a pupil, scholar; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. epithet of a particular school of grammarians.<BR>—पारायणीय, अम्, n., N. of a grammar.<BR>—पा-<BR>रावार (˚र-अव्˚), अम्, n. the further and the<BR>nearer bank or shore, the opposite banks (e. g.<BR>पारावारस्य नौः, a boat which plies from one<BR>side to the other); (अस्), m. the sea, ocean; [cf.<BR>पारापार.]<BR>—पारावारीण, अस्, आ, अम्, on both<BR>sides of a river, &c., one who goes to both sides.<BR>—पारे-गङ्गम्, ind. on the other side of the<BR>Gaṅgā, beyond the Ganges.<BR>—पारे-विशोक, N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—पारे-सिन्धु, ind. on the other side of the<BR>Sindhu, beyond the Indus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक|पारकः
1. पारक, अस्, ई, अम् (for 2. see p. 567, col. 1),<BR>carrying over, bearing across, saving, delivering (in<BR>उग्र-प्˚, q. v.); enabling to cross (a river or the<BR>world).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारण|पारणं|पारणः
1. पारण, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 2. see p. 567, col.<BR>1), bringing over, carrying across, saving, deli-<BR>vering; (अम्), n. fulfilling, accomplishing; reading<BR>through, reading, studying; the complete text (of a<BR>book); (अम्, आ), n. f., also व्रत-पारण, concluding<BR>a fast, eating or drinking after a fast, breakfast; [cf.<BR>शोणित-प्˚.]<BR>—पारण-कर्मन्, अ, n. exercise in<BR>reading, mode of reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारणीय
पारणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, having an attainable end,<BR>capable of being completed or brought to an end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
1. पारय, Nom. P. A. पारयति, -ते, &c., to<BR>bring over, lead over; to be able; (this is also<BR>regarded as the Caus. of rt. 1. पृ, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
2. पारय, अस्, आ, अम्, able, adequate, fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयत्
1. पारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being able, competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयिष्णु
1. पारयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ (for 2. see s. v.), Ved.<BR>bringing to a successful issue, causing to succeed,<BR>victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीण|पारीणः
पारीण, अस्, आ, अम्, being on the other or opposite<BR>side; crossing to the other or opposite side; (at the<BR>end of a comp.) completely familiar with, well<BR>acquainted with [cf. त्रिवर्ग-प्˚]; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a man (= पारिण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीय
पारीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) com-<BR>pletely familiar with, well acquainted with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्य|पार्य्य
पार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being on the opposite<BR>side or bank; upper; last, final; giving the last<BR>stroke, decisive (e. g. पार्ये धने, Ved. in a decisive<BR>battle); causing to succeed, helping through; effec-<BR>tual, efficient; (अम्), n. end; decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0566-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक|पारकः
पारक 2. पारक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. पॄ; for<BR>1. see p. 566, col. 3), satisfying, pleasing; cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारण|पारणं|पारणः
2. पारण, अस्, m. (for 1. see p. 566, col. 3), satis-<BR>fying, satisfaction; a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
3. पारय, अस्, आ, अम्, (for 1. and 2. see p. 566,<BR>col. 3), satisfying, filling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयत्
2. पारयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, satisfying, filling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयिष्णु
2. पारयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, gratifying, pleasing,<BR>satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्य|पारक्यं|पारक्यः
पारक्य पारक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = परकीय, be-<BR>longing to another or a stranger, alien (opposed to<BR>स्व); intended for others, serving others; belonging<BR>to an enemy, hostile, inimical; (अस्), m. an enemy;<BR>(अम्), n. doing anything for the sake of future hap-<BR>piness, pious conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग्रामिक
पारग्रामिक पारग्रामिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>पर + ग्राम), ‘belonging to another village,’ hos-<BR>tile, inimical, (पारग्रामिकं विधिम् आचिकीर्षति,<BR>he is about to perform hostile action, i. e. prepares<BR>for hostilities.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारज्
पारज् पारज्, क्, m. (said to be fr. पार),<BR>gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारजायिक|पारजायिकः
पारजायिक पारजायिक, अस्, m. (fr. पर +<BR>जाया), one who intrigues with another's wife, an<BR>adulterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारटीट|पारटीटः
पारटीट पारटीट, अस्, m. (connected with<BR>पार?), a stone, rock; [cf. पारारुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारणीय
पारणीय पारणीय. See p. 566, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत|पारतः
पारत 1. पारत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर-तस्),<BR>see Vārttikā to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 104; (Ved.) N. of a<BR>people or country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत|पारतः
पारत 2. पारत, अस्, m. quicksilver; [cf.<BR>पारद.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतक
पारतक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्रिक|पारतंत्रिक
पारतन्त्रिक पारतन्त्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर-<BR>तन्त्र), belonging to or enjoined by the religious<BR>treatises of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्र्य|पारतंत्र्य|पारतंत्र्यं|पारतन्त्र्यं
पारतन्त्र्य, अम्, n. the being subject to another,<BR>dependence, subservience, slavery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्रिक|पारत्रिकं
पारत्रिक पारत्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर-त्र),<BR>relating to another world, belonging to the next<BR>world, advantageous in the future life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्र्य|पारत्र्यं
पारत्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the next world;<BR>rewarded in a future state (according to Kullūka =<BR>परलोक-फल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारद|पारदः
पारद पारद, अस्, m. quicksilver; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a barbarous people (described in Manu<BR>X. 44. as a Kṣatriya tribe degraded to Śūdras by<BR>neglect of duties; cf. 2. पारत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदण्डक|पारदण्डकः
पारदण्डक पार-दण्डक. See पार, p. 566.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदारिक|पारदारिकः
पारदारिक पारदारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर-<BR>दार), intriguing with another's wife; relating to<BR>another's wife; (अस्), m. an adulterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदारिन्
पारदारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, intriguing with another's<BR>wife; (perhaps incorrectly for पर-दारिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदार्य|पारदार्यं|पारदार्य्य
पारदार्य, अम्, n. intriguing with another's<BR>wife, adultery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेशिक|पारदेशिकः
पारदेशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर-देश), outlandish,<BR>foreign, abroad; (अस्), m. a traveller; a foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेश्य|पारदेश्यः
पारदेश्य, अस्, शी, अम्, belonging to or coming<BR>from a foreign country, foreign; (अस्), m. a traveller,<BR>one who has gone to a foreign country; a foreigner;<BR>[cf. Lat. per-egrinus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारधेनु|पारधेनुः
पारधेनु, उस्, or पारधेनुक, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a low mixed caste, an Āyogava (q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्परीण|पारंपरीण
पारम्परीण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परम्-परा),<BR>passing from one to another, handed down from<BR>father to son, hereditary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्परीय|पारंपरीय
पारम्परीय, अस्, ई, अम्, handed down, tra-<BR>ditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्पर्य|पारंपर्य|पारंपर्यं|पारम्पर्य्य|पारम्पर्य्यं
पारम्पर्य, अस्, ई, अम्, one following the other;<BR>(अम्), n. uninterrupted series, continuous order or<BR>hereditary succession; traditional instruction, tradition;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">Page0567-b+ 75</a>]<BR>intercession, intermediation; (एण), ind. successively.<BR>—पारम्पर्य-क्रमागत (˚म-आग्˚), or पारम्-<BR>पर्यागत (˚य-आग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, derived from<BR>tradition.<BR>—पारम्पर्योपदेश (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>traditional instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलोक्य
पारलोक्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पर-लोक), relating<BR>to the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलौकिक
पारलौकिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the next<BR>world (e. g. सहायः पारलौकिकः, a companion<BR>on the way to the next world); epithet of a place<BR>where pearls are found and of the pearls found<BR>there (Ved.); (अम्), n. things or circumstances relat-<BR>ing to the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवर्ग्य
पारवर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. पर + वर्ग), be-<BR>longing to another party, siding with the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवश्य|पारवश्यं
पारवश्य, अम्, n. (fr. पर-वश), dependence,<BR>dependency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्त्रैणेय|पारस्त्रैणेयः
पारस्त्रैणेय, अस्, m. (fr. पर-स्त्री), a son by<BR>another's wife, an adulterine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारहंस्य
पारहंस्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पर-हंस), re-<BR>lating to an ascetic who has subdued all his senses;<BR>[cf. पारमहंस्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावर्य
पारावर्य, एण, ind. (fr. परावर), on all<BR>sides, completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृत|पारभृतं
पारभृत पारभृत, अम्, n. a present, offer-<BR>ing (incorrectly for प्राभृत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृतीय
पारभृतीय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>a present (incorrectly for प्राभृतीय); belonging<BR>to a cuckoo (fr. पर-भृत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस
पारमहंस पारमहंस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प-<BR>रम-हंस), relating to Parama-haṃsa (Brahmā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमहंस्य|पारमहंस्यं
पारमहंस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the Parama-<BR>haṃsas or religious men who have subdued all their<BR>senses by abstract meditation; (अम्), n. most sublime<BR>ascetism or meditation.<BR>—पारमहंस्य-परि, ind.<BR>relating to the most sublime meditation or speculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमार्थिक|पारमार्थिकः
पारमार्थिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परमार्थ),<BR>relating to a high or spiritual object, relating to<BR>supreme truth; real, essential, true; one who cares<BR>for truth, loving right; supremely good, excellent,<BR>superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमिक
पारमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परम), supreme,<BR>chief, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेश्वर
पारमेश्वर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परमेश्वर), re-<BR>lating or belonging to the supreme lord (Śiva),<BR>coming from the supreme lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेष्ठ
पारमेष्ठ, अस्, m. a patronymic from Para-<BR>meṣṭhin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमेष्ठ्य|पारमेष्ठ्यं
पारमेष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. परमेष्ठिन्),<BR>relating or belonging to the highest or supreme god<BR>(Brahman), coming from the supreme deity; relating<BR>to a king; (अम्), n. highest position, supremacy;<BR>royal insignia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमित
पारमित पारम्-इत. See under पार, p. 566.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
पारय 1. and 2. पारय, पारयत्, पार-<BR>यिष्णु. See p. 566, col. 3, and col. 1. of this p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवत|पारवतः
पारवत पारवत, अस्, m. = पारावत, a<BR>pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवश्य|पारवश्यं
पारवश्य पारवश्य. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव|पारशवः
पारशव पारशव, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. प-<BR>रशु), iron (used for axes), an iron weapon; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a mixed caste, the son of a Brāhman by a<BR>Śūdrā woman; a son by another's wife, an adulterine,<BR>bastard; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people in the south-<BR>west of Madhya-deśa; (अस्, ई, अम्), made of iron;<BR>made or derived from an axe; (sometimes written<BR>पारसव.)<BR>—पारशव-त्व, अम्, n. the state of<BR>being born of a Śūdrā woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव्य
पारशव्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic of Tirindira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशीक|पारशीकः
पारशीक पारशीक = पारसीक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वध|पारश्वधः
पारश्वध पारश्वध or पारश्वधिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. परश्वध), armed with an axe; (अस्), m.<BR>a man armed with an axe, halbert-man, hatchet-man,<BR>pioneer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वय
पारश्वय पारश्वय, अस्, m. gold (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस
पारस पारस, अस्, ई, अम्, Persian; (ई), f.<BR>(with or without भाषा) the Persian language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसिक|पारसिकः
पारसिक, आस्, m. pl. the Persians; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>Persian; (अस्), m. Persia (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीक|पारसीकः
पारसीक, आस्, m. pl. the Persians; (अस्), m.<BR>Persia; a Persian horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीकेय
पारसीकेय, अस्, ई, अम्, Persian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसव
पारसव पारसव. See पारशव, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्कर|पारस्करः
पारस्कर पारस्कर, अस्, m. (fr. पार + कर,<BR>स् being inserted; or fr. परस्-कर), N. of the author<BR>of certain Gṛhya-sūtras forming a supplement to Kā-<BR>tyāyana's Śrauta-sūtras and of a Dharma-śāstra; N. of<BR>a district; (अस्, ई, अम्), composed by Pāraskara.<BR>—पा-<BR>रस्कर-गृह्य-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work on<BR>domestic customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्त्रैणेय|पारस्त्रैणेयः
पारस्त्रैणेय पारस्त्रैणेय, पारहंस्य. See<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापत|पारापतः
पारापत पारापत, अस्, m. = पारावत, a<BR>pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापतक
पारापतक पारापतक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायण|पारायणं
पारायण पारायण. See पार, p. 566.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारारुक|पारारुकः
पारारुक पारारुक, अस्, m. a rock; [cf.<BR>पारटीट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावत|पारावतः
पारावत पारावत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परा-वत्),<BR>remote, coming or brought from a distance, of foreign<BR>extraction (Ved.); (अस्), m., N. of a tribe on the<BR>Yamunā; a turtle-dove, turtle-pigeon, dove, pigeon; a<BR>kind of snake; N. of a Nāga of the race of Airāvata;<BR>a monkey; a species of tree, Diospyros Embryopteris;<BR>a mountain; N. of a class of deities under Manu<BR>Svārociṣa; (ई), f. the fruit of the Lavalī plant<BR>(Annona Reticulata ?); a form of song peculiar to<BR>cowherds; N. of a river in the peninsula; (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of the tree Diospyros Embryopteris.<BR>—पारावत-घ्नी, f., Ved. (according to the Nirukta)<BR>destroying both banks (an epithet of the Sarasvatī;<BR>Sāy. = पारावार-घातिनी or = दूर-देशे विद्यमा-<BR>नस्यापि वृक्षादेर् हन्त्री; but the right meaning<BR>probably is), hitting the remote (demon), slaying from<BR>afar.<BR>—पारावत-देश, अस्, m., N. of a district men-<BR>tioned in the Ratna-koṣa.<BR>—पारावत-पदी, f. or<BR>पारावताङ्घ्रि (˚त-अङ्˚), ‘pigeon's foot,’ Cardios-<BR>permum Halicacabum (so called from the form of the<BR>leaf).<BR>—पारावताङ्घ्रि-पिच्छ, अस्, m. a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावति
पारावति, इस्, m. a patronymic of Vasu-rocis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावदघ्नी
पारावदघ्नी पारावद-घ्नी, a wrong reading<BR>for पारावत-घ्नी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावर
पारावर पारावर. See p. 566, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावर्य
पारावर्य पारावर्य. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर|पाराशरं|पाराशरः
पाराशर पाराशर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पराशर),<BR>proceeding or derived from Parāśara or from Pārā-<BR>śarya; (अस्), m. a patronymic from Parāśara and<BR>N. of the poet Vyāsa; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>school; (ई), f. a daughter of Parāśara; (अम्), n. the<BR>rules of Pārāśara for the conduct of the mendicant<BR>order.<BR>—पाराशरी-पुत्र, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR>—पाराशरोपपुराण (˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरकल्पिक|पाराशरकल्पिकः
पाराशरकल्पिक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who studies<BR>the Parāśara-kalpa; (अस्), m. a follower of Parāśara<BR>the institutor of rules for the mendicant order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरि|पाराशरिः
पाराशरि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरिन्
पाराशरिन्, ई, m. a mendicant of the school of Parā-<BR>śara or of Pārāśarya; a religious mendicant in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर्य|पाराशर्यः|पाराशर्य्य|पाराशर्य्यः
पाराशर्य, अस्, m. a patronymic of the poet<BR>Vyāsa; N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिकर्मिक|पारिकर्मिकः|पारिकर्म्मिक
पारिकर्मिक पारिकर्मिक, अस्, m. (fr. परि-<BR>कर्मन्), one who takes charge of the lesser vessels<BR>or utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिकाङ्क्षिन्|पारिकांक्षिन्
पारिकाङ्क्षिन् पारिकाङ्क्षिन्, ई, m. an ascetic<BR>(who devotes himself to devout contemplation), a<BR>contemplative saint, a Brāhman in the fourth period<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">Page0568-a+ 70</a>]<BR>of life, a religious mendicant; (also पारिकाङ्क्षक;<BR>cf. परि-काङ्क्षित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0567-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिकुट|पारिकुटः
पारिकुट पारिकुट, अस्, m., Ved. an at-<BR>tendant, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिक्षित|पारिक्षितः
पारिक्षित पारिक्षित, अस्, ई, अम्, epithet of<BR>the verses of the Atharva-veda XX. 127, 7-10;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic of Janam-ejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिक्षितीय
पारिक्षितीय, अस्, m., Ved. (according to the<BR>commentator) the brother of Pari-kṣit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिखेय
पारिखेय पारिखेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परि-खा),<BR>surrounded by a ditch or fosse, belonging to a ditch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिग्रामिक
पारिग्रामिक पारिग्रामिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परि-<BR>ग्रामम्), situated round a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजात|पारिजातः
पारिजात पारिजात, अस्, m. (fr. परि + जात),<BR>the coral tree, Erythrina Indica (a splendid tree<BR>losing its leaves in June and then covered with large<BR>crimson flowers, sometimes identified with the Man-<BR>dāra); the wood of this tree; N. of one of the five<BR>trees of paradise (which was produced at the churning<BR>of the ocean and came into the possession of Indra<BR>from whom it was afterwards taken by Kṛṣṇa);<BR>fragrance; N. of a Ṛṣi; N. of a Nāga of the race<BR>of Airāvata.<BR>—पारिजात-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of<BR>flowers of the celestial Pārijāta.<BR>—पारिजात-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, possessing the celestial Pārijāta.<BR>—पारिजात-<BR>सरस्वती-मन्त्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of certain magical<BR>formulas.<BR>—पारिजात-हरण, अम्, n. ‘carrying off<BR>of the Pārijāta tree,’ N. of sections of the Hari-vaṃśa<BR>and Viṣṇu-Purāṇa (describing the taking of the<BR>Pārijāta tree by Kṛṣṇa from Indra); N. of a<BR>comedy by Gopāla-dāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजातक|पारिजातकः
पारिजातक, अस्, m. the coral tree, Erythrina Indica;<BR>one of the five trees of paradise; N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिण
पारिण पारिण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाय्य|पारिणाय्यं
पारिणाय्य पारिणाय्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. परि-<BR>णाय = परि-णय), relating to marriage, obtained<BR>on the occasion of marriage; (अम्), n. property or<BR>paraphernalia received by a woman at the time of<BR>marriage; marriage settlement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाह्य|पारिणाह्यं
पारिणाह्य पारिणाह्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-णाह),<BR>household furniture and utensils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितथ्या
पारितथ्या पारितथ्या, f. (fr. परि + तथ्य?),<BR>a string of pearls for binding the hair, a trinket worn<BR>on the forehead where the hair is parted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितवत्|पारितवन्त्
पारितवत् पारित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing<BR>the word पारित or other forms of the Caus. of<BR>rt. 1. पृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितोषिक|पारितोषिकं
पारितोषिक पारितोषिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परि-<BR>तोष), gratifying, delighting, pleasing, making happy,<BR>satisfactory, consolatory; (अम्), n. a reward, gratuity<BR>(given as a token of satisfaction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिध्वजिक|पारिध्वजिकः
पारिध्वजिक पारिध्वजिक, अस्, m. (fr. परि<BR>+ ध्वज), a standard-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिन्द्र|पारिंद्र|पारिंद्रः|पारिन्द्रः
पारिन्द्र पारिन्द्र, अस्, m. a lion (= पा-<BR>रीन्द्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपन्थिक|पारिपंथिक|पारिपंथिकः|पारिपन्थिकः
पारिपन्थिक पारिपन्थिक, अस्, m. (fr. परि-<BR>पन्थम्), a highwayman, robber, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपाट्य|पारिपाट्यं
पारिपाट्य पारिपाट्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-पाटी),<BR>regularity, methodicalness, successiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्र|पारिपात्रं|पारिपात्रः
पारिपात्र पारिपात्र, अस्, m. (fr. परि +<BR>पात्र?), N. of one of the seven principal mountain<BR>ranges of India (the central or western portion of<BR>the Vindhya chain which skirts the province of<BR>Malwa); N. of a son of Ahīna-gu; (also read पा-<BR>रियात्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्रक
पारिपात्रक or पारियात्रक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>mountain range, the central or western portion of<BR>the Vindhya chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्रिक|पारिपात्रिकः
पारिपात्रिक or पारियात्रिक, अस्, m. an inhabitant<BR>of the Pāripātra or Pāriyātra mountain range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपान्थिक
पारिपान्थिक पारिपान्थिक, अस्, m. probably<BR>only a wrong reading for पारिपन्थिक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपार्श्व|पारिपार्श्वं
पारिपार्श्व पारिपार्श्व, अम्, n. (fr. परि-<BR>पार्श्व), retinue, attendants, followers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपार्श्वक|पारिपार्श्वकः
पारिपार्श्वक, अस्, इका, अम्, standing at the side,<BR>attending on; (अस्), m. an attendant; an assistant of<BR>the manager of a play; an actor who serves in place<BR>of a chorus in the drama and is one of the inter-<BR>locutors in the prologue; (इका), f. a female attendant,<BR>a chamber-maid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपार्श्विक|पारिपार्श्विकः
पारिपार्श्विक, अस्, ई, अम्, standing at the side,<BR>belonging to a retinue; attending on; (अस्), m. an<BR>attendant; an assistant of the manager of a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपेल
पारिपेल पारिपेल, अम्, n. = परिपेलव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लव|पारिप्लवं|पारिप्लवः
पारिप्लव पारिप्लव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. परि-<BR>प्लव), swimming; moving to and fro, shaking,<BR>unsteady, tremulous, trembling; perturbed, troubled<BR>in mind; ‘moving in a circle,’ epithet of a particular<BR>legend recited at the Aśva-medha and repeated at<BR>certain intervals throughout the year (Ved.); (अस्),<BR>m. a boat; N. of a sage (?) in the fifth Manv-antara;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पारिप्लव-गत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being in a boat.<BR>—पारिप्लव-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having tremulous or swimming eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लवीय
पारिप्लवीय, अम्, n., Ved. an oblation accom-<BR>panying the recitation of the Pāriplava legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लाव्य|पारिप्लाव्यः
पारिप्लाव्य, अस्, m. a goose; (अम्), n. perplexity,<BR>agitation; tremulousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिबर्ह|पारिबर्हः
पारिबर्ह पारिबर्ह and पारिवर्ह, अस्, m.<BR>= परि-बर्ह or परि-वर्ह, q. v.; a wedding<BR>present; N. of one of the sons of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभद्र|पारिभद्रः
पारिभद्र पारिभद्र, अस्, m. (fr. परि +<BR>भद्र), the coral tree, Erythrina Indica; the Nimb<BR>tree, Azadirachta Indica; a species of pine, Pinus<BR>Devadāru; the Saral, Pinus Longifolia; N. of a son<BR>of Yajña-bāhu; (अम्), n., N. of a Varṣa in Śālmala-<BR>dvīpa named after Pāribhadra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभद्रक|पारिभद्रकः
पारिभद्रक, अस्, m. the tree Erythrina Fulgens;<BR>the Nimb tree, Azadirachta Indica; (अम्), n. Costus<BR>Speciosus or Arabicus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाव्य|पारिभाव्यं
पारिभाव्य पारिभाव्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-भू),<BR>surety, security, bail (= प्रातिभाव्य); a drug, a<BR>species of Costus, Costus Speciosus or Arabicus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाषिक|पारिभाषिकं
पारिभाषिक पारिभाषिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>परि-भाषा), universally received, generally current,<BR>usual, common; technical (as a term).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमाण्डल्य|पारिमांडल्य|पारिमांडल्यं|पारिमाण्डल्यं
पारिमाण्डल्य पारिमाण्डल्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>परि-मण्डल), having the measure or being of the<BR>size of an atom; (अम्), n. an atom (as a measure of<BR>space), a mote in a sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमाण्य|पारिमाण्यं
पारिमाण्य पारिमाण्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-<BR>माण), circumference, compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमित्य|पारिमित्यं
पारिमित्य पारिमित्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-मित),<BR>the being confined or limited, limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुखिक|पारिमुखिकः
पारिमुखिक पारिमुखिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परि-<BR>मुखम्), being before or round the face, being<BR>near or present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुख्य|पारिमुख्यं
पारिमुख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being before or round<BR>the face, being near or present; (अम्), n. the being<BR>before the face, presence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्र|पारियात्रः
पारियात्र पारियात्र, अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain; of a country; [cf. पारिपात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्रक
पारियात्रक, N. of a place mentioned in the<BR>Romaka-Siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियानिक|पारियानिकः
पारियानिक पारियानिक, अस्, m. (fr. परि +<BR>यान), a travelling carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिरक्षिक
पारिरक्षिक पारिरक्षिक, अस्, m. (fr. परि-<BR>रक्षा), a Brāhman in the fourth period of life, an<BR>ascetic or religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिवत्स
पारिवत्स पारिवत्स, अस्, m. (fr. परि +<BR>वत्स), a calf belonging (to the cows mentioned in<BR>Hari-vaṃśa 11877).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिवित्त्य|पारिवित्त्यं
पारिवित्त्य पारिवित्त्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-<BR>वित्त), the being unmarried while a younger brother<BR>is married, the condition of an elder brother who is<BR>unmarried while the younger is married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिवेत्त्र्य
पारिवेत्त्र्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-वेत्तृ), the marry-<BR>ing of a younger brother before the elder; the being<BR>unmarried while a younger brother is married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिव्राजक|पारिव्राजकं
पारिव्राजक पारिव्राजक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परि-<BR>व्राजक), intended for a religious mendicant; (अम्),<BR>n. the wandering life of a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिव्राज्य|पारिव्राज्यं
पारिव्राज्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-व्राज्), the wandering<BR>life of a religious mendicant; (also incorrectly written<BR>पारिव्रज्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिश|पारिशः
पारिश पारिश, अस्, m. a species of tree<BR>(= फलीश, commonly called पलाश-पिपुल and<BR>गज-हण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिशील|पारिशीलः
पारिशील पारिशील, अस्, m. a cake (= अपूप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिशेष्य|पारिशेष्यं
पारिशेष्य पारिशेष्य, अम्, n. (fr. परि-<BR>शेष), that which is left over, a remainder; (आत्), ind.<BR>this alone remaining, there being no alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद्
पारिषद् पारिषद्, त्, त्, त् (fr. परि-षद्),<BR>one who is present at an assembly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषत्क
पारिषत्क, अस्, आ, अम्, one who studies or knows<BR>what has been settled in an assembly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद|पारिषदः
पारिषद, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to an assembly<BR>or council, one who belongs to an assembly or council;<BR>(अस्), m. a person present at an assembly or congre-<BR>gation, a spectator; an assessor at a council; a king's<BR>companion; (आस्), m. pl. the retinue or attendants of<BR>a god; (अम्), n. taking part in an assembly; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. or n. (?), N. of a village in the North.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषदक
पारिषदक, अस्, ई, अम्, done by an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद्य|पारिषद्यः
पारिषद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, = परिषदं सम-<BR>वैति, = परिषदि साधुः, one who is present at<BR>an assembly, a spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0568-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिसारक
