पारुषेय
पारुषेय पारुषेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. परुष),<BR>Ved. spotted, freckled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुष्य|पारुष्यं|पारुष्यः
पारुष्य, अम्, n. roughness [cf. त्वक्-प्˚], harsh-<BR>ness; harshness of language, abuse, reproach, con-<BR>tumelious or scurrilous language, opprobrious or<BR>unfriendly speech, insult; violence (in word or deed,<BR>cf. दण्ड-प्˚, वाक्-प्˚); squalor; the forest or grove<BR>of Indra; aloe wood or Agallochum; (अस्), m. a N.<BR>of Bṛhas-pati, the planet Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुष्ण
पारुष्ण पारुष्ण, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारेगङ्गम्|पारेगंगम्
