पार्घट|पार्घटं
पार्घट पार्घट, अम्, n. ashes, = अर्घट;<BR>[cf. पार्पर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्जन्य
पार्जन्य पार्जन्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पर्जन्य),<BR>belonging to Parjanya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ण|पार्णः
पार्ण पार्ण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर्ण), made<BR>or consisting of leaves, leafy; raised from leaves (as<BR>a tax); made of the wood of the Butea Frondosa;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्णवल्कि
पार्णवल्कि, इस्, m. (fr. पर्ण-वल्क), a patro-<BR>nymic of Ni-gada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थ|पार्थः
पार्थ 1. पार्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पृथि), Ved.<BR>an epithet of twelve sacred texts, ascribed to Pṛthi<BR>Vainya, repeated during the ceremony of unction in<BR>the Rāja-sūya sacrifice; (अस्), m. a patronymic of<BR>Tānva; (अम्), n., N. of several Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थ्य
पार्थ्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from Pṛthi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थ|पार्थः
पार्थ 2. पार्थ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पृथ् for<BR>प्रथ् and connected with पृथु, wide), a prince,<BR>king (= पार्थिव); (fr. पृथा), a metronymic<BR>of Yudhi-ṣṭhira, Bhīma-sena, and Arjuna, especially<BR>of the last; N. of a son of Paṅgu and king of<BR>Kaśmīra; N. of a man; the plant Terminalia<BR>Arjuna; (आस्), m. pl. an epithet of the five sons<BR>of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—पार्थ-ज, अस्, m. the son of Pārtha.<BR>—पार्थ-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a city near the con-<BR>fluence of the Go-dāvarī and Vi-darbhā.<BR>—पार्थ-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of sons of Pṛthā.<BR>—पार्थ-सारथि, इस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Tantra-ratna.<BR>—पार्थसारथि-मिश्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a commentator on Jaimini's Nyāya-sūtras.<BR>—पार्-<BR>थानुग (˚थ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, followed by<BR>(Pārtha, i. e.) Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थव|पार्थवं
पार्थव, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or peculiar to<BR>Pṛthu; (अम्), n. width, greatness, immensity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थवि
पार्थवि, an earthy substance, rotten wood; (pro-<BR>bably a wrong reading for पार्थिव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिव|पार्थिवं|पार्थिवः
पार्थिव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पृथिवी for पृथ्वी, f.<BR>of पृथु), earthen, earthly, terrestrial, relating to<BR>the earth, springing or derived from the earth, made<BR>of earth, earthy; ruling or possessing the earth; fit<BR>for kings or princes, royal, princely; अ-पार्थिव,<BR>unearthly, i. e. heavenly, celestial; (अस्), m. a dweller<BR>on the earth, inhabitant of the earth; a lord of the<BR>earth, king, prince, sovereign, warrior; an earthen<BR>vessel; the 19th (or 53rd) year in Jupiter's cycle of<BR>60 years; (आस्), m. pl. a patronymic; (ई), f. ‘earth-<BR>born,’ an epithet of Sītā; of Lakṣmī; (अम्), n. an<BR>earthy substance; (आनि), n. pl., Ved. the regions of<BR>the earth (Sāy. = पृथिव्याम् भवानि स्थानानि).<BR>—पार्थिव-ता, f. or पार्थिव-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>dignity or rank of king, royalty.<BR>—पार्थिव-नन्-<BR>दिनी, f. the daughter of a king.<BR>—पार्थिवर्षभ<BR>(˚व-ऋ˚), अस्, m. ‘king-bull,’ an excellent king.<BR>—पार्थिव-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. best of kings, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">Page0569-b+ 77</a>]<BR>excellent sovereign.<BR>—पार्थिव-सुता or पार्थिवात्-<BR>मजा (˚व-आत्˚), f. the daughter of a king.<BR>—पार्-<BR>थिवाधम (˚व-अध्˚), अस्, m. the lowest or<BR>meanest of kings.<BR>—पार्थिवेन्द्र (˚व-इन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the chief or greatest of princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थक्य|पार्थक्यं
पार्थक्य पार्थक्य, अम्, n. (fr. पृथक्),<BR>severalty, individuality, separation, separateness, sin-<BR>gleness, difference, variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थुरश्म
पार्थुरश्म पार्थुरश्म, अम्, n. (fr. पृथु-<BR>रश्मि), Ved. epithet of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्पर|पार्परः
पार्पर पार्पर, अस्, m. a handful of rice;<BR>consumption (= क्षय-रोग); a filament of the<BR>Nauclea Cadamba; ashes; = कीनाश; = गदान्तर<BR>(a kind of disease ?); a N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्य|पार्य्य
पार्य पार्य. See p. 566, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्यन्तिक|पार्यंतिक|पार्य्यन्तिक
पार्यन्तिक पार्यन्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर्य्-<BR>अन्त), final, concluding, last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व|पार्व्व
पार्व पार्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर्वन्), = पार्-<BR>वण; (probably an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वण|पार्व्वण|पार्व्वणः
पार्वण, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>division of time or of the month; increasing, waxing<BR>full (as the moon); (अस्), m. a kind of deer; the<BR>general funeral ceremony to be offered to all the<BR>Manes at the Parvan (or conjunction of the sun and<BR>moon, at which double oblations are offered, three<BR>cakes to the father, paternal grandfather and great-<BR>grandfather, and three to the maternal grandfather,<BR>his father and grandfather; and the crumbs of each<BR>set to the remoter ancestors in each line).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वायनान्तीय|पार्व्वायनान्तीय
पार्वायनान्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. पर्वन् + अय-<BR>नान्त), occurring at the end of a Parvan or solstice<BR>(as a sacrifice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वत|पार्व्वत|पार्व्वतः
पार्वत पार्वत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पर्वत),<BR>being or living in the mountains, growing on or<BR>coming from the mountains, consisting of moun-<BR>tains, mountainous; (अस्), m. the tree Melia Sem-<BR>pervirens (= महा-निम्ब); (ई), f. a mountain<BR>stream; a female cowherd or Gopī; a N. of Durgā<BR>(as being the daughter of Hima-vat the king of the<BR>snowy mountains); N. of a cave in mount Meru;<BR>of various women (named after the goddess); an<BR>epithet of Draupadī (incorrectly for पार्षती); a<BR>kind of fragrant earth; a red clay commonly called<BR>Saurāṣṭrī or Surat earth; N. of various plants; the<BR>olibanum tree, Boswellia Thurifera; Grislea To-<BR>mentosa; = Celtis Orientalis; = क्षुद्र-पाषाण-<BR>भेदा; = जीवनी.<BR>—पार्वती-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. ‘dis-<BR>trict of Pārvatī (Durgā),’ N. of one of the four<BR>especially sacred districts of Orissa.<BR>—पार्वती-नन्-<BR>दन, अस्, m. ‘son of Pārvatī,’ an epithet of Kārtti-<BR>keya.<BR>—पार्वती-पश्चात्ताप-वर्णन, अम्, n., N.<BR>of the sixth chapter of the Gīta-gaṅgādhara, a poem<BR>by Kalyāṇa.<BR>—पार्वती-प्रवर्तन, अम्, n., N. of<BR>the ninth chapter of the Gīta-girīśa, a poem by<BR>Rāma.<BR>—पार्वती-प्रसादन, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>fifth chapter of the Gīta-gaṅgādhara.<BR>—पार्वती-<BR>मोक्षण, अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Gaṇeśa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—पार्वतीश्वर-लिङ्ग (˚ती-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—पार्वती-सम्प्रदान, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतायन
पार्वतायन, अस्, m. a patronymic; N. of a<BR>chamberlain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वति
पार्वति, इस्, m. a patronymic of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतिक|पार्वतिकं
पार्वतिक, अम्, n. a multitude of mountains,<BR>mountain-range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतीय|पार्वतीयः|पार्व्वतीय
पार्वतीय, अस्, ई, अम्, living or dwelling in the<BR>mountains, mountainous; (अस्), m. a mountaineer;<BR>epithet of a particular sovereign ruling in the moun-<BR>tains; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a mountain tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतेय|पार्व्वतेय|पार्व्वतेयं|पार्व्वतेयः
पार्वतेय, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the mountains, mountain-born; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>prince of mountaineers; a species of culinary plant<BR>bearing a pungent fruit; (ई), f. the smaller or upper<BR>mill-stone; (अम्), n. antimony (= सौवीराञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शव|पार्शवः
पार्शव 1. पार्शव, अस्, m. (fr. 1. पर्शु),<BR>a prince of the Parśus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शुका
पार्शुका, f. = पर्शुका, a rib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व|पार्श्वं|पार्श्वः
पार्श्व, अस्, अम्, m. n. the region of the ribs or<BR>the part of the body below the armpit; the side,<BR>flank (either of animate or inanimate objects); a<BR>side of any square figure; a curved knife (Ved.);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of an ancient Buddhist teacher; (with<BR>Jainas) N. of the twenty-third Arhat of the present<BR>Ava-sarpiṇī; (औ), m. du. heaven and earth; (अम्),<BR>n. a multitude of ribs, the thorax; the extremity of<BR>the fore-axle nearest the wheel to which the outside<BR>horses of a four-horse chariot are attached; a fraudu-<BR>lent or crooked expedient, dishonourable means;<BR>(आनि), n. pl. the ribs (Ved.); (ए), ind. at the side,<BR>near, on, upon, (opposed to दूर-तस्, दूरे);<BR>aside; (अयोस्), ind. on both sides; (आत्), ind. away<BR>from; (अम्), ind. near to, to, towards; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>near, proximate, by the side of.<BR>—पार्श्व-ग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, going at the side (of any one), accompanying,<BR>being in close proximity to, an attendant; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. attendants, retinue.<BR>—पार्श्व-गत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being at the side, attending, accompanying, being<BR>close to or beside; sheltered, screening.<BR>—पार्श्व-<BR>गमन, अम्, n. the act of going by the side,<BR>accompanying.<BR>—पार्श्व-चर, अस्, m. an attendant;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. attendants, retinue.<BR>—पार्श्व-तस्, ind.<BR>by or from the side, at the side, near, sideways,<BR>aside.<BR>—पार्श्व-द, अस्, m. ‘turning the side towards<BR>another,’ an attendant; (आस्), m. pl. attendants,<BR>retinue.<BR>—पार्श्व-दाह, अस्, m. a burning pain in<BR>the side.<BR>—पार्श्व-देश, अस्, m. the region of the<BR>ribs, the side.<BR>—पार्श्व-द्रुम, आस्, m. pl. the<BR>trees at the side, the trees on every side.<BR>—पार्श्व-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. (with Jainas) N. of an Arhat; the<BR>Jaina pontiff.<BR>—पार्श्वनाथ-काव्य, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a poem by Padma-sundara celebrating the preceding<BR>Arhat.<BR>—पार्श्व-परिवर्तन, अम्, n. ‘the turning<BR>round on the other side or from one side to the<BR>other,’ epithet of a festival on the eleventh day of the<BR>light half of the month Bhādra (Viṣṇu being sup-<BR>posed to turn upon the other side in his sleep on<BR>this day).<BR>—पार्श्व-परिवर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being or<BR>going by the side (of any one).<BR>—पार्श्व-पिप्पल,<BR>अम्, n. a species of Harītakī (= Hindī गजहड्).<BR>—पार्श्व-भाग, अस्, m. ‘side-portion,’ the side,<BR>flank (of an elephant).<BR>—पार्श्व-रुज्, क्, f. pain in<BR>the side.<BR>—पार्श्व-वक्त्र, अस्, m. whose face is in<BR>his side,’ N. of a being attendant upon Śiva (Hari-<BR>vaṃśa 14851).<BR>—पार्श्व-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, standing<BR>by the side, an attendant; situated at the side,<BR>adjacent; (इनस्), m. pl. attendants, retinue.<BR>—पार्-<BR>श्व-विवर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being by the side of, living<BR>with.<BR>—पार्श्व-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, lying or sleeping<BR>on the side; sleeping at the side.<BR>—पार्श्व-शायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, ‘lying on the side,’ epithet of a particular<BR>position of the moon.<BR>—पार्श्व-शूल, अस्, m. a<BR>shooting pain in the side, spasm of the chest, stitch;<BR>pleurisy.<BR>—पार्श्व-संस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, lying on<BR>the side.<BR>—पार्श्व-सूत्रक, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a kind of ornament.<BR>—पार्श्व-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>standing at the side or next to, being near or close<BR>to, adjacent, proximate; (अस्), m. an associate, com-<BR>panion; a stage manager's assistant (said to serve as<BR>a sort of chorus to the Indian drama, being some-<BR>times an actor in the prelude and interpreter of the<BR>plot).<BR>—पार्श्व-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, standing at the<BR>side, being near or close to.<BR>—पार्श्वानुचर (˚व-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘attending at the side,’ an attendant,<BR>body-servant, lackey.<BR>—पार्श्वायात (˚व-आय्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one who has approached close to.<BR>—पार्श्वा-<BR>सन्न (˚व-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, standing by the side,<BR>standing next, present.<BR>—पार्श्वासीन (˚व-आस्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, sitting by the side.<BR>—पार्श्वास्थि (˚व-अस्˚),<BR>इ, n. ‘side-bone,’ a rib.<BR>—पार्श्वैकादशी (˚व-एक्˚),<BR>f., N. of a particular festival (= पार्श्व-परिवर्-<BR>तन).<BR>—पार्श्वोदर-प्रिय (˚व-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘fond of (moving) sideways on the belly,’ a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वक|पार्श्वकः
पार्श्वक, अस्, m. a rib; (अस्, आ, अम्), one who<BR>seeks wealth or other objects by dishonest or indirect<BR>or side means; a pilferer, swindler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतीय|पार्श्वतीयः
पार्श्वतीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. पार्श्व-तस्), being<BR>on or belonging to the side, situated at the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्विक|पार्श्विकं|पार्श्विकः
पार्श्विक, अस्, ई, अम्, lateral, belonging to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">Page0570-a+ 72</a>]<BR>side; (अस्), m. a sidesman, partisan; an associate,<BR>companion; a juggler; one who seeks money by<BR>dishonest means; N. of an ancient Buddhist teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0569-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व्य
पार्श्व्य, औ, m. du. heaven and earth (a various<BR>reading for पार्श्वौ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शव|पार्शवः
पार्शव 2. पार्शव, अस्, m. a warrior armed<BR>with an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व|पार्श्वं|पार्श्वः
पार्श्व पार्श्व. See p. 569, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षकि
पार्षकि पार्षकि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षत|पार्षतः
पार्षत पार्षत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पृषत),<BR>belonging to the spotted antelope, made of the skin<BR>of the spotted antelope; (अस्), m. a patronymic of<BR>Dru-pada and his son Dhṛṣṭa-dyumna; (ई), f. a<BR>patronymic of Draupadī; an epithet of Durgā (in<BR>this sense a wrong reading for पार्वती); N. of<BR>two plants, Boswellia Thurifera; = जीवनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्
पार्षद् पार्षद्, त्, f. (for परि-षद?), an<BR>assembly; (दस्), m. pl. the attendants or retinue of<BR>a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद|पार्षदः
पार्षद, अस्, m. (fr. पर्षद्), an associate,<BR>companion, attendant; a train, retinue (especially of<BR>a god); a person present in a congregation or<BR>assembly, a spectator; (perhaps) a councillor, dis-<BR>tinguished personage; (अम्), n. a text-book received<BR>by any particular grammatical school, a N. given to<BR>the Prātiśākhyas; N. of a work on ceremonies.<BR>—पार्षद-ता, f. the office of an attendant (espe-<BR>cially of the attendant of a deity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षदीय
पार्षदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, conformable to the<BR>received text-book of any particular grammatical<BR>school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्य|पार्षद्यः
पार्षद्य, अस्, m. = पारिषद्य, a member of<BR>an assembly or council, assessor; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>attendants or retinue of a god (especially of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्वाण
पार्षद्वाण पार्षद्वाण, अस्, m. (fr. पृषद्-<BR>वाण), N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षिका
पार्षिका पार्षिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षी
पार्षी पार्षी (?), f. dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्टेय
पार्ष्टेय पार्ष्टेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पृष्टि),<BR>being within the ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्ठिक
पार्ष्ठिक पार्ष्ठिक, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. being<BR>after the manner of the Pṛṣṭhya (Ṣaḍ-aha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णि|पार्ष्णिः
पार्ष्णि पार्ष्णि, इस्, m. f., rarely पार्ष्णी, f.<BR>(said to be fr. rt. पृष्), the heel; the extremity of<BR>the fore-axle to which the outside horses of a four-<BR>horse chariot are attached (the two inner horses being<BR>harnessed to the धुर् or chariot-pole); the rear of<BR>an army; the back; a kick; enquiry, asking (?);<BR>(इस्), f. a foolish or licentious woman; a N. of<BR>Kuntī the wife of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—पार्ष्णि-क्षेम, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a divinity.<BR>—पार्ष्णि-ग्रह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, seizing from behind, threatening from behind;<BR>(अस्), m. a follower.<BR>—पार्ष्णि-ग्रहण, अम्, n.<BR>attacking or threatening (an enemy) in the rear.<BR>—पार्ष्णि-ग्राह, अस्, आ, अम्, attacking or menac-<BR>ing (an enemy) in the rear; (अस्), m. an enemy in<BR>the rear; a commander in the rear of an army;<BR>an ally who supports a prince (Manu VII. 207).<BR>—पार्ष्णि-त्र, अम्, n. ‘rear-protecting,’ a rear-<BR>guard, reserve, a body of forces in the rear.<BR>—पार्ष्-<BR>णि-वाह्, ट्, ऊही, ट्, or पार्ष्णि-वाह, अस्, आ, अम्, draw-<BR>ing (i. e. harnessed to) the extremities of the axle-<BR>tree; (अस्), m. an outside horse.<BR>—पार्ष्णि-सारथि,<BR>इस्, m. a charioteer who drives one of the outside<BR>horses; (ई), m. du. the two charioteers who drive<BR>the outer horses attached to the extremities of the<BR>axle-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्
पाल् पाल्. See Caus. of rt. 3. पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल|पालः
पाल, अस्, m. a guard, guardian, protector,<BR>nourisher, keeper; a herdsman; a protector of the<BR>earth, a prince; a spitting-pot, spittoon; N. of a<BR>Nāga of the race of Vāsuki; of a prince; (ई), f. a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">Page0570-b+ 72</a>]<BR>herdsman's wife; [cf. पालि.]<BR>—पाल-कवि-राज, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a poet (also called Śrī-pāla-kavi-rāja).<BR>—पाल-काव्य, अम्, n. ‘the poem of Pāla,’ N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—पाल-घ्न, अस्, m. a mushroom.<BR>—पाल-<BR>बणिज्, क्, m. = कन्या-पाल; (a wrong form for<BR>पान-बणिज्.)<BR>—पाली-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a par-<BR>ticular religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक|पालकः
पालक, अस्, इका, अम्, guarding, protecting, nourish-<BR>ing; (अस्), m. a guardian, protector, cherisher,<BR>nourisher; a foster-father; a prince, ruler, sovereign;<BR>a horse-keeper, a groom; one who maintains or<BR>observes; N. of several princes; a species of plant<BR>with a poisonous bulb, Plumbago Zeylanica; a<BR>horse.<BR>—पालक-गोत्र, अम्, n. the family or tribe<BR>of one's adoptive parents.<BR>—पालकाख्या (˚क-<BR>आख्˚), f., N. of the mother of Dhanvantari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालन|पालनं
पालन, अस्, ई, अम्, the act of protecting, guarding,<BR>fostering, nourishing, cherishing; (अम्), n. guarding,<BR>providing with a guardian, protecting, protection,<BR>preserving, cherishing, fostering, nourishing; main-<BR>taining, keeping, observing; the milk of a cow that<BR>has recently calved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालनीय
पालनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be guarded or protected,<BR>to be cherished or nourished; fit to be preserved or<BR>maintained; to be observed or respected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयत्
पालयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, guarding, protecting,<BR>cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयितृ
पालयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, protecting, cherishing; a<BR>protector, guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित|पालितः
पालित, अस्, आ, अम्, guarded, protected, cherished,<BR>nourished; (अस्), m. a species of tree (= शाखोट);<BR>N. of a son of Parā-jit (or Parā-vṛt); (आ), f., N. of<BR>one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्
पालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, protecting, guarding, cherishing,<BR>nourishing; (ई), m., N. of a son of Pṛthu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्य
पाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be protected or guarded, to<BR>be cherished; being under (any one's) protection or<BR>guardianship; to be observed or kept, to be main-<BR>tained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकाप्य|पालकाप्यः
पालकाप्य पालकाप्य, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>ancient sage or Muni; a form of the divine physician<BR>Dhanvantari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक्क
पालक्क पालक्क, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N.<BR>of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक्या
पालक्या पालक्या, f. the plant Beta Ben-<BR>galensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्क|पालंकः|पालङ्कः
पालङ्क पालङ्क, अस्, m. the olibanum tree,<BR>Boswellia Thurifera; a species of beet-root, Beta<BR>Bengalensis; a hawk; (ई), f. the resin of the<BR>olibanum tree, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्क्य|पालंक्य|पालङ्क्यं
पालङ्क्य, अस्, आ, m. f. gum olibanum, incense;<BR>(अम्, आ), n. f. the plant Beta Bengalensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्गिन्
पालङ्गिन् पालङ्गिन्, इनस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>school called after a disciple of Vaiśampāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालल
पालल पालल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पलल), made<BR>of powdered sesamum seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालवी
पालवी पालवी, f. a kind of vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालहरि
पालहरि पालहरि, इस्, m. (probably a patro-<BR>nymic fr. पलहर), N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालागल
पालागल पालागल, अस्, m., Ved. a runner,<BR>messenger; (according to others) a bearer of false<BR>tidings; (ई), f. the fourth and least respected wife<BR>of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाल
पालाल पालाल, अस्, ई, अम् (probably incor-<BR>rectly for पाल्वल), living in a marsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाश|पालाशं|पालाशः
पालाश पालाश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पलाश), com-<BR>ing from or belonging to the tree Butea Frondosa,<BR>made of the wood of the Butea Frondosa; green;<BR>(अस्), m. green (the colour).<BR>—पालाश-खण्ड and<BR>पालाश-षण्ड, अस्, m. an epithet of Magadha (a<BR>country in India, the western part of Behar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालि|पालिः
पालि पालि, इस्, f. (fr. Caus. of rt. 3. पा?;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">Page0570-c+ 77</a>]<BR>said to be fr. rt. पल्), the tip of the ear; an edge,<BR>margin; a boundary, limit; the sharp side of any-<BR>thing, the sharp edge or point of a sword or any<BR>cutting instrument; a line, row, range; a raised<BR>bank, dike, causeway, bridge; the lap, bosom; the<BR>hip, haunch; a mark, spot, stain; a particular mea-<BR>sure of capacity (= प्रस्थ); a louse; a woman<BR>with a beard; prescribed food, maintenance of a<BR>scholar during the period of his studies by his teacher;<BR>praise, eulogium; a circumference; (ई), f. an edge,<BR>margin; the sharp edge of a sword; a line, row,<BR>range; a woman with a beard; a louse; a pot,<BR>boiler; an oblong pond; a causeway, bridge.<BR>—पा-<BR>लिं-हिर, अस्, m. a kind of snake, (perhaps a<BR>wrong reading for पालिं-हर, seizing by the tip<BR>of the ear.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिका
पालिका, f. the tip of the ear; the sharp edge of<BR>a cutting instrument; a sort of ladle or knife for<BR>skimming milk, curds, &c.; a cheese or butter<BR>knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित्य|पालित्यं
पालित्य पालित्य, अम्, n. (fr. पलित), grey-<BR>ness (of age), hoariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्द|पालिंदः|पालिन्दः
पालिन्द पालिन्द, अस्, m. incense; a species<BR>of jasmine, Jasminum Pubescens; (ई), f. a species of<BR>creeper, Ichnocarpus Frutescens; = पालिन्धी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्धी
पालिन्धी पालिन्धी, f. a species of Ipomœa<BR>with dark blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालीवत
पालीवत पालीवत, अस्, m. a species of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्लवा
पाल्लवा पाल्लवा, f. (fr. पल्लव), scil. क्रीडा,<BR>a game played with twigs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्वल
पाल्वल पाल्वल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पल्वल),<BR>coming from a tank or pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावक|पावकः
पावक पावक, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 1. पू),<BR>(Ved.) pure, clear, bright, shining; (Sāy.) = शोधक,<BR>cleansing, purifying (said of Agni, Āditya, Sūrya, and<BR>the Maruts; of water, of the dawn, of day and night,<BR>&c.); (अस्), m. epithet of a particular Agni (in the<BR>Purāṇas said to be a son of Agni Abhi-mānin and<BR>Svāhā or of Antar-dhāna and Śikhaṇḍinī; cf. पव-<BR>मान, शुचि); fire in general; Agni or the god of<BR>fire; social fire, a fire lighted in common; a fire<BR>lighted on taking possession of a house; a species of<BR>tree, Premna Integrifolia or Spinosa (see अरणि); a<BR>species of plant, Plumbago Zeylanica (= चित्रक);<BR>Semecarpus Anacardium; a plant used as a vermifuge,<BR>Carthamus Tinctorius (= विडङ्ग); a symbolical<BR>expression for the number three (like all other words<BR>for ‘fire’); epithet of a kind of Ṛṣi, a saint, a<BR>person purified by religious abstraction, one who<BR>purifies from sin; (ई), f. the wife of Agni.<BR>—पावक-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. ‘having the name Pāvaka,’<BR>an epithet of Agni; containing the word पावक.<BR>—पावक-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. brightly resplen-<BR>dent (as Agni).<BR>—पावक-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>being of pure or brilliant aspect; (Sāy.) = अग्नि-<BR>समान-तेजस्क, resembling the brilliance of fire.<BR>—पावक-शोचिस्, इस्, इस्, इस्, (voc. anomalously -चे),<BR>Ved. shining brightly.<BR>—पावकारणि (˚क-अर्˚), इस्,<BR>m. the tree Premna Integrifolia or Spinosa (see<BR>अरणि).<BR>—पावकेश्वर (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकि|पावकिः
पावकि, इस्, m. ‘son of Fire,’ an epithet of Skanda<BR>or Kārttikeya; of Su-darśana; of Hari (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन|पावनं|पावनः
पावन, अस्, ई, अम्, purifying, purificatory, expur-<BR>gatory, freeing from sin, sanctifying; purified, pure,<BR>holy; (अस्), m. fire (generally or for various cere-<BR>monial purposes); incense; a species of Verbesina with<BR>yellow flowers; a kind of demigod otherwise called<BR>a Siddha; N. of one of the Viśve Devāḥ; an epithet<BR>of the inspired poet Vyāsa; (ई), f. the plant Termi-<BR>nalia Chebula; holy basil; a cow; N. of a river;<BR>the Ganges or the goddess Gaṅgā; (अम्), n. the act<BR>of cleansing, purifying, sanctifying, expiation, puri-<BR>fication (by acts of austerity and devotion); a means<BR>of purification; penance; water; cow-dung; the<BR>seed of the plant Elæocarpus Ganitrus (of which<BR>rosaries are made); a species of grass, Costus Speci-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">Page0571-a+ 78</a>]<BR>osus; a sectarial mark (= चित्रक).<BR>—पावन-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the property of cleansing or purifying.<BR>—पा-<BR>वन-ध्वनि, इस्, m. a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0570-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमान
पावमान, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पवमान), relating<BR>to Soma juice while being purified or while pass-<BR>ing through the strainer (Ved.); (ई), f., scil. ऋच्, an<BR>epithet of particular Vedic hymns (especially of Ṛg-<BR>veda IX, Atharva-veda XIX. 71, 1); purificatory<BR>water (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावित
पावित, अस्, आ, अम्, cleansed, purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावित्र
पावित्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. ? (fr. पवित्र), N.<BR>of a metre, four times ¯¯¯¯˘˘˘˘¯ (perhaps<BR>incorrectly for पवित्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाविन्
पाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, cleansing, purifying (Mahā-bh.<BR>Vana-p. 10543; perhaps only a wrong reading for<BR>पावनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाव्य
पाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleansed or purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन्
पावन् 1. पावन्, आ, अरी, अ (fr. rt. 1. पा),<BR>Ved. (at the end of a comp.) drinking; [cf. असृक्-<BR>प्˚, घर्म-प्˚, घृत-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन्
पावन् 2. पावन्, आ, अरी, अ (fr. rt. 3. पा),<BR>Ved. (at the end of a comp.) protecting; [cf.<BR>तनू-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावर|पावरः
पावर पावर, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the<BR>die or side of a die which is marked with two points<BR>(= द्वा-पर, of which it is a corruption).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावा
पावा पावा or पावा-पुरी (also पापा-पुरी),<BR>f., N. of a city near Rāja-gṛha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावीरव
पावीरव पावीरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पवीरु),<BR>Ved. proceeding from or belonging to the thunder-<BR>bolt; (Sāy.) = पावयितृ, शोधयितृ, purifying;<BR>(ई), f. ‘daughter of lightning,’ the noise of thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश|पाशः
पाश पाश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. पश्), a snare,<BR>trap, noose, tie, fastening, cord, chain, fetter (कवच-<BR>प्˚, ज्या-प्˚); a net or snare for catching birds and<BR>beasts; a string or cord for fastening tame animals<BR>[cf. पशू-प्˚]; a noose or lasso employed as a<BR>weapon [cf. धर्म-प्˚]; a die, dice (= पाशक,<BR>Raghu-v. VI. 18); selvage, edge, border (of anything<BR>woven); (in astrology) epithet of a particular con-<BR>stellation; (at the end of a comp.) expressive of<BR>contempt or depreciation (e. g. छत्त्र-पाश, अस्,<BR>m. a bad or shabby umbrella; cf. भिषक्-प्˚, रक्-<BR>षस्-प्˚, वैयाकरण-प्˚); abundance, quantity<BR>(after a word signifying ‘hair;’ cf. केश-प्˚); expres-<BR>sive of admiration [cf. कर्ण-प्˚].<BR>—पाश-क्रीडा,<BR>f. play with dice, gambling.<BR>—पाश-द्युम्न, अस्,<BR>m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR>—पाश-धर, अस्, m.<BR>‘holding a noose,’ an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—पाश-<BR>पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, noose in hand; (इस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Varuṇa (regent of the waters represented as holding<BR>in one hand a cord shaped like a sling or noose).<BR>—पाश-बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, noosed, snared, en-<BR>trapped, caught in a net, bound.<BR>—पाश-बन्ध, अस्,<BR>m. a noose, snare, halter, net.<BR>—पाश-बन्धक,<BR>अस्, m. one who snares birds, a bird-catcher.<BR>—पाश-<BR>बन्धन, अम्, n. a snare, fetter; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>hanging in a snare.<BR>—पाश-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, noose-<BR>bearing, bearing a noose; (त्), m. any one armed with<BR>a noose; an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—पाश-रज्जु, उस्, f.<BR>a fetter, rope.<BR>—पाश-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having or<BR>possessing a noose.<BR>—पाश-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘snare in hand,’ holding a snare in the hand; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Yama.<BR>—पाशान्त (˚श-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the back of a garment, (opposed to दशा.)<BR>—पाशी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, tied, fettered; snared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशक|पाशकः
पाशक, अस्, m. (at the end of a comp.) = पाश,<BR>a snare, trap, &c. [cf. कण्ठ-प्˚, दण्ड-प्˚];<BR>a die (particularly the long sort used in playing<BR>Chaupai).<BR>—पाशक-केवली, f., N. of a work.<BR>—पा-<BR>शक-पीठ, अम्, n. a gaming-table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशन|पाशनं
पाशन, अम्, n. a noose, lasso, sling; a cord, lash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशय
पाशय, Nom. P. पाशयति, -यितुम्, to bind;<BR>[cf. rt. 3. पश्, to which पाशयति is referred by<BR>native grammarians.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिक|पाशिकः
पाशिक, अस्, m. one who snares animals, a bird-<BR>catcher (Ved.); N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशित|पाशितः
पाशित, अस्, आ, अम्, tied, fettered, bound, snared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिन्
पाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a net or noose, armed<BR>with a net or noose, laying snares; a deer-catcher,<BR>fowler, trapper; (ई), m. an epithet of Varuṇa; of<BR>Yama; N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—पाशि-वाट,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्या
पाश्या, f. a number or multitude of nooses, a<BR>collection of ropes; a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशव
पाशव पाशव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पशु), derived<BR>from or belonging to cattle, relating or belonging to<BR>animals (e. g. पाशवम् मांसम्, animal food);<BR>(अम्), n. a flock, herd.<BR>—पाशव-पालन, अम्, n.<BR>‘nourishing flocks,’ pasturage or meadow grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुक
पाशुक, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. relating or belonging to<BR>cattle, relating or belonging to the sacrificial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपत|पाशुपतः
पाशुपत, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from or belonging<BR>to Śiva Paśu-pati, relating or sacred to Śiva Paśu-<BR>pati; (अस्), m. a follower and worshipper of Śiva in<BR>one of his forms as the supreme deity of the Hindū<BR>triad; the tree Æschynomene Grandiflora; a species<BR>of plant (= वक); N. of a place sacred to Śiva<BR>Paśu-pati.<BR>—पाशुपत-योग-प्रकरण, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of the eighth chapter of the first part of the<BR>Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—पाशुपत-व्रत-विवरण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the eighteenth chapter of the second part<BR>of the Liṅga-Purāṇa.<BR>—पाशुपतास्त्र (˚त-अस्˚),<BR>अम्, n. Śiva's trident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपाल्य|पाशुपाल्यं
पाशुपाल्य, अम्, n. (fr. पशु-पाल), the occu-<BR>pation of a grazier or keeper of cattle, the breeding<BR>and rearing of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुबन्धक|पाशुबंधकः|पाशुबन्धकः
पाशुबन्धक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. पशु-बन्ध),<BR>Ved. belonging to the slaughter of a sacrificial<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशी
पाशी पाशी, f. a stone (perhaps incorrectly<BR>for पाषी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्त्य
पाश्चात्त्य पाश्चात्त्य and पाश्चात्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(fr. पश्चात्), hinder, behind; western; subsequent;<BR>posterior, last; (अम्), n. the hinder part.<BR>—पाश्-<BR>चात्त्य-निर्णयामृत (˚य-अम्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>book on ritual, mentioned in the Saṃskāra-tattva<BR>by Raghu-nandana.<BR>—पाश्चात्त्याकर-सम्भव<BR>(˚य-आक्˚), अम्, n., N. of a species of salt coming<BR>from the West (= रोमक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषक|पाषकः
पाषक पाषक, अस्, m. an ornament for<BR>the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्ड|पाषंड|पाषण्डः
पाषण्ड पाषण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, (sometimes<BR>incorrectly spelt पाखण्ड), heretical, impious;<BR>(अस्), m. a heretic, a hypocrite, impostor, any one<BR>who not conforming to the orthodox tenets of Hindū<BR>faith assumes the external characteristics of tribe or<BR>sect, a Jaina, Buddhist; (अस्, अम्), m. n. false<BR>doctrine, heresy.<BR>—पाषण्ड-ता, f. heresy, hetero-<BR>doxy, hypocrisy.<BR>—पाषण्ड-पथ, अस्, m. the way<BR>of heretics, false doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डक|पाषंडक|पाषंडकः|पाषण्डकः
पाषण्डक or पाषण्डिक, अस्, m. a heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डिन्|पाषंडिन्
पाषण्डिन्, ई, m. a heretic, hypocrite; (also read<BR>पाषाण्डिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाण्ड
पाषाण्ड, अस्, m., Ved. a heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाण|पाषाणः
पाषाण पाषाण, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>पष्), a stone; (ई), f. a small stone used as a weight;<BR>[cf. Gr. βάσανος; Heb. bāshān, ‘basalt-land.’]<BR>—पाषाण-गर्दभ, अस्, m. a hard swelling on<BR>the maxillary joint.<BR>—पाषाण-चतुर्दशी, f. the<BR>fourteenth day in the light half of the month Mārga-<BR>śīrṣa (on which a festival of Gaurī is celebrated,<BR>when cakes made of rice and shaped like large<BR>pebbles are eaten).<BR>—पाषाण-चय-निबद्ध, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, surrounded with a coping of stone (as a<BR>well).<BR>—पाषाण-दारक or पाषाण-दारण, अस्,<BR>m. a sort of hatchet or instrument for cutting stones,<BR>a stone-cutter's chisel.<BR>—पाषाण-भेद or पाषा-<BR>ण-भेदन, अस्, or पाषाण-भेदिन्, ई, m. the plant<BR>Plectranthus Scutellarioides, used as a remedy for<BR>stone in the bladder.<BR>—पाषाण-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of or made of stone.<BR>—पाषाण-सन्धि,<BR>इस्, m. a cave or chasm in a rock.<BR>—पाषाण-सेतु-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. a barrier or dam of stone.<BR>—पा-<BR>षाण-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, stone-hearted, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषी
पाषी, f., Ved. (Sāy.) = शिला, a stone; = शक्ति, a<BR>spear; [cf. पाशी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाष्य
पाष्य, आणि, n. pl., Ved. stones, a rampart of<BR>stones; (ए), n. du. the two stones for pressing the<BR>Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाष्ठौह
