पिंस्
पिंस् पिंस्, cl. 1. 10. P. पिंसति, पिं-<BR>सितुम्, पिंसयति, -यितुम्, to speak; to<BR>shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक|पिकः
पिक पिक, अस्, ई, m. f. (probably for स्पिक,<BR>cf. Gr. σπίζ-ω), the Indian cuckoo, Cuculus Indicus;<BR>[cf. Gr. σίττη for σπίττη or ψίττη, σίττακος,<BR>ψίττακος, ψιττάκη, βίττακος; Lat. pîcus, pîca; Old<BR>Germ. speh, speht.]<BR>—पिक-बन्धु, उस्, m. ‘friend<BR>of the cuckoo,’ the mango tree.<BR>—पिक-बान्धव,<BR>अस्, m. ‘friend of the cuckoo,’ the spring.<BR>—पिक-<BR>राग or पिक-वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘cuckoo's favourite,’<BR>the mango tree.<BR>—पिक-वर, अस्, m. an excellent<BR>cuckoo.<BR>—पिकाक्ष (˚क-अक्ष), अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), ‘cuckoo's eye,’ a vegetable and perfume (com-<BR>monly called रोचनी).<BR>—पिकाङ्ग (˚क-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>small bird, commonly called Cātakīya.<BR>—पिकानन्द<BR>(˚क-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘cuckoo's joy,’ the spring.<BR>—पिके-<BR>क्षणा (˚क-ईक्˚), f. ‘having eyes like the cuckoo's,’<BR>the plant Asteracantha Longifolia or Capparis Spinosa<BR>(= कोकिलाक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक्क|पिक्कः
पिक्क पिक्क, अस्, m. an elephant twenty<BR>years old (= विक्क); a young elephant in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक्का
पिक्का पिक्का, f., Ved. a collection or string<BR>of thirteen pearls weighing a Dharaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0571-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

