पिछ्|पिच्छ्
पिछ् पिछ्, cl. 10. P. पिच्छयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to split, cut, divide; cl. 6. P. पिच्छति,<BR>पिच्छितुम्, to inflict pain; to obstruct, hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छ|पिच्छं|पिच्छः
पिच्छ, अम्, n. a feather of a tail (especially of a<BR>peacock); the tail of a peacock; the feathers of an<BR>arrow; a wing; a crest; (अस्), m. a tail in general;<BR>(आ), f. the scum of boiled rice and of other grain;<BR>the gum of the silk-cotton tree; the venomous<BR>saliva of a snake; a multitude, heap; the calf of the<BR>leg; a sheath, a coat or cover; the areca-nut, betel-<BR>nut; a line, row, range; a diseased affection of a<BR>horse's feet; a plantain, Musa Sapientum; the Śiśu<BR>tree, Dalbergia Sissoo; armour, a sort of cuirass or<BR>jacket; = पिच्छिल.<BR>—पिच्छ-बाण or पिच्छ-वाण,<BR>अस्, m. ‘whose feathers are like arrows,’ a hawk.<BR>—पिच्छ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a tail, tailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छक|पिच्छकः
पिच्छक, अम्, n. a feather of a tail (at the<BR>end of a comp.; cf. चित्र-प्˚); (इका), f. the feathers<BR>of a peacock's tail tied in a bunch (used by conjurors).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छल
पिच्छल, अस्, आ, अम्, slimy, slippery, smeary;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Nāga of the race of Vāsuki; (आ),<BR>f., N. of various plants, Dalbergia Sissoo, Bombax<BR>Heptaphyllum, Basella Lucida or Rubra; N. of a<BR>river; (perhaps an incorrect form for पिच्छिल, q. v.)<BR>—पिच्छल-दला, f. the jujube, Zizyphus Jujuba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छितिका
पिच्छितिका, f. = पिच्छिला, the Śiśu tree, Dalbergia<BR>Sissoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिल|पिच्छिलं|पिच्छिलः
पिच्छिल, अस्, आ, अम्, slimy, lubricous, slippery,<BR>smeary; having a tail; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. sauce<BR>mixed with rice-gruel; sauce, gravy or condiments<BR>with water or ghee; broth, soup; moist and split<BR>pulse; (अस्), m. the plant Cordia Latifolia and Myxa;<BR>the tamarisk, Tamarix Indica; (आ), f., N. of various<BR>plants, Dalbergia Sissoo; Bombax Heptaphyllum,<BR>the silk-cotton tree; a pot-herb, Basella Lucida or<BR>Rubra; linseed, Linum Usitatissimum; Asteracantha<BR>Longifolia; an esculent root, Arum Indicum; N. of<BR>a river.<BR>—पिच्छिल-च्छदा, f. Basella Cordifolia.<BR>—पिच्छिल-त्वच्, क्, m. an orange-tree; orange-peel;<BR>a species of fruit tree (= धन्वन).<BR>—पिच्छिल-<BR>सार, अस्, m. the gum of Bombax Heptaphyllum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिलक|पिच्छिलकः
पिच्छिलक, अस्, m. a species of fruit tree (=<BR>धन्वन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्छ
पिञ्छ, अम्, n. a wing (= पिच्छ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिजवन
पिजवन पिजवन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिजूल
पिजूल पिजूल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्चदेव
पिञ्चदेव पिञ्च-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज्|पिंज्
पिञ्ज् पिञ्ज्, cl. 2. A. पिङ्क्ते, पिपिञ्जे,<BR>पिञ्जिता, पिङ्क्तुम्, to tinge, dye, colour<BR>[cf. rt. 1. पिश्]; to sound; to touch; to join [cf. rt.<BR>1. पृच्]; to adore; cl. 10. P. पिञ्जयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to kill, injure; to be strong; to give; to take; to<BR>dwell; to shine; to speak; to emit a sound; [cf.<BR>Lat. ping-ere.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्ग|पिंग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, reddish-brown, tawny, bright<BR>red, red, yellow; (अस्), m. tawny colour; (probably)<BR>N. of a herb (Ved.); a buffalo; a rat, mouse; N.<BR>of a man (Ved., cf. पैङ्गि, पैङ्गिन्); N. of one<BR>of the attendants of the Sun; (आ), f. a bow-string<BR>(Sāy. = पिङ्ग-वर्णा ज्या); a kind of yellow pig-<BR>ment [cf. गो-रोचना]; the stalk of Ferula Asa Fœ-<BR>tida; bamboo manna; turmeric, Indian saffron; an<BR>epithet of Durgā (?); a tubular vessel of the human<BR>body which according to the Yoga system is the<BR>channel of respiration and circulation for one side;<BR>(ई), f. a species of Mimosa, Mimosa Suma; (अम्),<BR>n. a young animal.<BR>—पिङ्ग-कपिशा, f. ‘tawny-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">Page0572-b+ 81</a>]<BR>brown,’ a species of cockroach.<BR>—पिङ्ग-चक्षुस्,<BR>उस्, m. ‘tawny-eyed,’ a crab.<BR>—पिङ्ग-जट, अस्, m.<BR>‘having tawny braided hair,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पिङ्ग-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पिङ्ग-<BR>लोचन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘tawny-eyed,’ having brown eyes.<BR>—पिङ्ग-सार, अस्, m. yellow orpiment.<BR>—पिङ्ग-<BR>स्फटिक, अस्, m. ‘yellow-crystal,’ a kind of gem (=<BR>गो-मेद).<BR>—पिङ्गाक्ष (˚ग-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>‘tawny-eyed,’ having reddish-brown eyes, red-eyed;<BR>(अस्), m. an ape; N. of Śiva; of a Rakṣas; of a wild<BR>man; of a bird; of one of the four sons of Droṇa;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a divinity; of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—पिङ्गास्य (˚ग-आस्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘tawny-faced,’ a species of fish, Pimelodius Pan-<BR>gasius.<BR>—पिङ्गेक्षण (˚ग-ईक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, ‘tawny-<BR>eyed,’ having reddish-brown eyes; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पिङ्गेश (˚ग-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the yellow hue,’ an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गर
पिङ्गर, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गल|पिंगल|पिङ्गलं|पिङ्गलः
पिङ्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, reddish-brown, tawny, brown,<BR>yellowish; (अस्), m. tawny colour, a dull brown or<BR>yellow hue; fire; a monkey; an ichneumon; a<BR>small kind of owl; a species of snake; a particular<BR>vegetable poison; (with Jainas) N. of a treasure;<BR>N. of one of Kuvera's divine treasures; of an<BR>attendant of the Sun; the sun (?); an epithet of<BR>Śiva or of a kindred being; N. of a Rudra; of a<BR>Yakṣa; of an attendant of Śiva; of a Dānava; of<BR>a fabulous being in the form of a Nāga (or serpent<BR>of the lower regions, the reputed author of the Chaṇḍas<BR>or treatise on prosody, regarded as one of the Vedāṅgas,<BR>and describing Prākṛt as well as Sanskrit metres;<BR>he is identified by some with Patañjali, the author<BR>of the celebrated commentary on Pāṇini called the<BR>Mahā-bhāṣya; by the Hindūs he is considered as a<BR>Muni or inspired and divine personage); N. of<BR>various ancient sages; N. of the fifty-first (or twenty-<BR>fifth) year in a sixty years' cycle of Jupiter; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. a species of bird, a kind<BR>of owl; the Śiśu tree, Dalbergia Sissoo; a kind of<BR>metal; a particular vessel of the body (the right of<BR>three canals running from the os coccygis to the<BR>head, which according to the anatomy of the Yoga<BR>school of philosophy are the chief passages of breath<BR>and air); the female elephant of the South quarter;<BR>N. of a courtezan who became remarkable for her<BR>piety; of an astrological house or period; heart-pea;<BR>(अम्), n. a particular metal (= राज-रीति), brass; yellow<BR>orpiment.<BR>—पिङ्गल-छन्दो-ग्रन्थ-टीका, f., N.<BR>of a commentary by Citra-sena on Piṅgala's Chandaḥ-<BR>śāstra.<BR>—पिङ्गल-नाग, अस्, m. the serpent-demon<BR>Piṅgala.<BR>—पिङ्गल-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary on Piṅgala's Chandaḥ-śāstra.<BR>—पिङ्गल-सार-<BR>विकाशिनी, f. ‘explaining the substance of Piṅgala,’<BR>N. of a commentary by Ravi-kara on Piṅgala's<BR>Chandaḥ-śāstra.<BR>—पिङ्गलाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘tawny-eyed,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पिङ्गला-तन्त्र<BR>and पिङ्गलामृत (˚ल-अम्˚), अम्, n., N. of two<BR>Tantras.<BR>—पिङ्गलेश्वर (˚ल-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Liṅga; (ई), f. a form of Dākṣāyaṇī.<BR>—पिङ्गलेश्-<BR>वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गलक
पिङ्गलक, अस्, इका, अम्, (Ved.) reddish-brown,<BR>tawny; (अस्), m., N. of a Yakṣa; N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of his descendants; (इका), f. a kind<BR>of bee; a variety of the owl; a sort of crane; N. of<BR>a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गलित|पिंगलित
पिङ्गलित, अस्, आ, अम्, made reddish-brown,<BR>become tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गाश|पिंगाश|पिंगाशः|पिङ्गाशः
पिङ्गाश, अस्, m. the chief of a community of<BR>wild tribes; the head man or proprietor of a village;<BR>a kind of fish, Pimelodius Pangasius (= पिङ्गास्य);<BR>(ई), f. the indigo plant; (अम्), n. virgin gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज|पिंज|पिञ्जं|पिञ्जः
पिञ्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, confused, confounded, disturbed<BR>in mind; (अस्), m. the moon; a species of camphor;<BR>killing, slaughter; (आ), f. hurting, injuring, injury;<BR>turmeric; cotton; a species of tree resembling the<BR>vine-palm; a switch; (अम्), n. strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जट|पिंजट|पिंजटः|पिञ्जटः
पिञ्जट, अस्, m. the concrete rheum of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जन|पिंजन|पिंजनं|पिञ्जनं
पिञ्जन, अम्, n. a bow or bow-shaped instrument<BR>used for cleaning cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जर|पिंजर|पिञ्जरं|पिञ्जरः
पिञ्जर, अस्, आ, अम्, reddish-yellow, yellow or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">Page0572-c+ 74</a>]<BR>tawny, of the colour of gold; (अस्), m. tawny-brown<BR>or reddish-yellow colour, a mixture of red and<BR>yellow; a horse (probably a bay or chesnut); N.<BR>of a mountain; (अम्), n. gold; yellow orpiment;<BR>the flower of Mesua Roxburghii; a cage; the ribs<BR>or the cavity formed by them, the thorax; a<BR>skeleton; [cf. पञ्जर.]<BR>—पिञ्जर-ता, f. yellowish-<BR>red (the colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जरक|पिंजरक|पिंजरकं|पिञ्जरकं
पिञ्जरक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga; (अम्), n.<BR>orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जरित|पिंजरित
पिञ्जरित, अस्, आ, अम्, coloured reddish-yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जल|पिंजल|पिञ्जलं|पिञ्जलः
पिञ्जल, अस्, आ, अम्, extremely perplexed or con-<BR>founded, disturbed, overcome with terror or grief;<BR>panic-struck, being in great disorder; (आ), f., N. of<BR>a river; (ई), f. two blades of Kuśa grass serving as<BR>an implement to hold certain articles at a sacrifice;<BR>(अम्), n. the leaf of the Kuśa grass; the plant Cur-<BR>cuma Zerumbet (हरिद्राभ); yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जलक
पिञ्जलक, अस्, आ, अम्, in उत्-पिञ्जलक, extremely<BR>confounded or disturbed, being in great disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जान|पिञ्जानं
पिञ्जान, अम्, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जिका|पिंजिका
पिञ्जिका, f. a roll of cotton from which threads<BR>are spun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूल|पिञ्जूलं
पिञ्जूल, अम्, n., Ved. a bundle of stalks, a bundle<BR>of grass, &c.; the wick of a lamp; (sometimes spelt<BR>पिञ्जुल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूलक
पिञ्जूलक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूष|पिंजूष|पिंजूषः|पिञ्जूषः
पिञ्जूष, अस्, m. the wax of the ear (= पेञ्जूष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जेट|पिंजेट|पिंजेटः|पिञ्जेटः
पिञ्जेट, अस्, m. the excretion or concrete rheum<BR>of the eyes; [cf. पिञ्जट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जोला|पिंजोला
पिञ्जोला पिञ्जोला, f. the noise or rustling<BR>of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्
पिट् पिट्, cl. 1. P. पेटति, पेटितुम्, to<BR>sound; to assemble or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट|पिटं|पिटः
पिट, अस्, m. a basket for holding grain, a sort of<BR>cupboard or granary made of bamboos or canes; a<BR>basket, box; (अम्), n. a house, a hovel; a roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटक|पिटकं|पिटकः
पिटक, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. (usually n.), a basket,<BR>box; a large basket or receptacle of basket-work for<BR>keeping grain &c., a granary; a collection of writings<BR>[cf. त्रि-प्˚]; a boil, blister, ulcer; a kind of orna-<BR>ment on Indra's banner; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटक्या
पिटक्या, f. a multitude of baskets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटाक|पिटाकः
पिटाक, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 49; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a man; N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटङ्काकी
पिटङ्काकी पिटङ्काकी or पिटङ्कोकी, f. the<BR>plant Cucumis Colocynthis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटङ्काश|पिटङ्काशः
पिटङ्काश पिटङ्काश, अस्, m. a kind of fish,<BR>a species of pike, Esax Scolopax, Silurus Pabda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्टक|पिट्टकं
पिट्टक पिट्टक, अम्, n. the tartar or excre-<BR>tion of the teeth; [cf. किट्ट, किट्टक, पिप्पिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्टय
पिट्टय पिट्टय (fr. पिट्ट = पिष्ट?), Nom.<BR>P. पिट्टयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to stamp or press into a<BR>solid mass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्टित
पिट्टित, अस्, आ, अम्, stamped into a solid mass,<BR>pressed flat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ्
पिठ् पिठ्, cl. 1. P. पेठति, पेठितुम्, to<BR>injure, hurt, kill; to feel pain or affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ|पिठः
पिठ, अस्, m. pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठर|पिठरं|पिठरः
पिठर, अस्, ई, अम्, m. f. n. a pot, pan; (अस्),<BR>m. an addition to a building shaped like a hollow<BR>vessel, a hut made of bamboos and mats, or accord-<BR>ing to some a kind of store-room or scullery; N.<BR>of a particular Agni; N. of a Dānava; (अम्), n. a<BR>churning-stick; the root of Cyperus Rotundus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठरक|पिठरकं|पिठरकः
पिठरक, अस्, m. (?), a pot, pan; N. of a Nāga.<BR>—पिठरक-कपाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a fragment of<BR>a pot, potsherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठीनस्
पिठीनस् पिठीनस्, आस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिडक|पिडकः
पिडक पिडक, अस्, m. or पिडका, f. a small<BR>boil, pimple, papula, pustule.<BR>—पिडका-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having boils, pimples, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिडकिन्
पिडकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having boils, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0572-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्ड्|पिंड्
पिण्ड् पिण्ड् (probably akin to rt. पिष्;<BR>considered by some as a Nom. fr. पिण्ड<BR>below), cl. 1. A., 10. P. पिण्डते, पिण्डितुम्, पिण्-<BR>डयति, -यितुम्, to roll into a lump or ball, to put<BR>together, join, unite; to accumulate; to assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्ड|पिंड|पिण्डं|पिण्डः
पिण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in most senses usually m.),<BR>a round mass, ball, globe, lump, knob, clod (e. g.<BR>अयः-पिण्ड, a ball or lump of iron; अग्नि-पिण्डौ,<BR>the knobs at the end of a pair of tongs; cf. नेत्र-प्˚,<BR>मृत्-प्˚); a roundish lump of food, a bite, morsel,<BR>mouthful; a cake or ball of meal offered to the<BR>Manes, a ball or lump of meat or rice mixed up with<BR>milk, curds, flowers, &c., and offered at the several<BR>Śrāddhas to the Manes by the nearest surviving<BR>relations (= नि-वाप); food; sustenance, means of<BR>living, livelihood, subsistence [cf. पर-पिण्डाद];<BR>alms; flesh, meat; the embryo or fetus in an early<BR>stage of gestation; the body; the projection of an<BR>elephant's frontal sinus; a round button; anything<BR>roundish, thick, gross, or solid; thickness (one of<BR>the three dimensions in geometry); a heap, cluster,<BR>quantity, collection; an object; a particular part of<BR>a house; a sort of portico or shed in front of the<BR>door; myrrh, incense, frankincense; the side imme-<BR>diately below the armpit (?); Vangueria Spinosa; the<BR>flower of the China rose; (in arithmetic) sum, total<BR>amount; (in astronomy) a sine expressed in numbers<BR>[cf. ज्या-प्˚]; the twenty-fourth part of the quadrant<BR>of a circle, or 3° 45; N. of a man; (औ), m. du. the<BR>fleshy parts of the shoulder situated above the collar-<BR>bone; (अम्), n. power, might; an army; iron;<BR>fresh butter; (ई), f. a round mass, &c. (= पिण्ड, m.);<BR>a long gourd, Cucurbita Lagenaria (= अ-लाबु); a<BR>species of date tree; the flowering shrub Tabernæ-<BR>montana Coronaria (= तगर); the plant Jonesia<BR>Aśoka; a species of palm, Phœnix Dactylifera; the<BR>nave of a wheel; performance of certain gesticulations<BR>during the silent repetition of prayers while medi-<BR>tating on real or divine knowledge; a house; N. of<BR>a woman.<BR>—पिण्ड-कन्द, अस्, m. a species of<BR>bulbous plant (= पिण्डालु).<BR>—पिण्ड-खर्जूर, अस्,<BR>m. or पिण्ड-खर्जूरिका or पिण्ड-खर्जूरी, f. a<BR>species of date tree.<BR>—पिण्ड-गोस, अस्, m. gum<BR>myrrh.<BR>—पिण्ड-तर्कुक, आस्, m. pl., Ved. the<BR>ancestors preceding the great-grandfather (who eat<BR>the remnants of the oblations made to the Manes).<BR>—पिण्ड-तस्, ind. from a ball or lump.<BR>—पिण्ड-<BR>तैल, अम्, n. or पिण्ड-तैलक, अस्, m. incense,<BR>olibanum.<BR>—पिण्ड-त्व, अम्, n. the being a lump or<BR>ball; पिण्डत्वं गम्, to attain the condition of a<BR>lump.<BR>—पिण्ड-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving or qualified to<BR>give the funeral cake to deceased ancestors; supplying<BR>with bread or with the means of subsistence; (अस्),<BR>m. the nearest male relation who offers the funeral<BR>cake; a patron, master.<BR>—पिण्ड-दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ,<BR>one who gives or is qualified to give the funeral<BR>cake to deceased ancestors.<BR>—पिण्ड-दान, अम्, n.<BR>offering a cake of meal (especially in the oblation to<BR>the Manes); presentation of the obsequial cake; the<BR>funeral oblation made to deceased ancestors on the<BR>evening of new moon.<BR>—पिण्ड-निर्वपण, अम्,<BR>n. presenting obsequial cakes to the Manes, the<BR>sacrifice to the Manes.<BR>—पिण्ड-पद, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of arithmetical calculation.<BR>—पिण्ड-पात, अस्,<BR>m. giving alms.<BR>—पिण्डपातिक, अस्, m. one who<BR>lives on alms.<BR>—पिण्ड-पात्र, अम्, n. the vessel in<BR>which the obsequial cakes are offered to the Manes;<BR>alms (lit. an alms-dish).<BR>—पिण्ड-पाद or पिण्ड-<BR>पाद्य, अस्, m. ‘thick-footed,’ an elephant.<BR>—पिण्ड-<BR>पितृ-यज्ञ, अम्, n., Ved. the oblation of obsequial<BR>cakes to deceased ancestors on the evening of new<BR>moon.<BR>—पिण्ड-पुष्प, अस्, m. the tree Jonesia<BR>Aśoka; the China rose; the pomegranate tree;<BR>(अम्), n. the blossom of the Aśoka tree; the flower<BR>of the China rose; a lotus; the flower of the plant<BR>Tabernæmontana Coronaria.<BR>—पिण्डपुष्पक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of vegetable, Chenopodium Album.<BR>—पिण्ड-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing (long) round<BR>fruits; (आ), f. a bitter gourd.<BR>—पिण्ड-बीज or पिण्ड-<BR>वीज, अस्, m. a flowering shrub, Nerium (or Oleander)<BR>Odorum.<BR>—पिण्डबीजक, अस्, m. Pterospermum<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">Page0573-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Acerifolium (= कर्णिकार).<BR>—पिण्ड-भाज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>partaking of a funeral oblation, entitled to a share<BR>in the funeral cake, eating or receiving the cakes<BR>offered at a funeral ceremony; (जस्), m. pl. de-<BR>ceased ancestors, the Manes.<BR>—पिण्ड-भृति, इस्,<BR>f. means of subsistence, livelihood.<BR>—पिण्ड-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of a lump (of clay).<BR>—पिण्ड-<BR>मात्रोपजीविन् (˚र-उप्˚), ई, इनी, इ, subsisting on a<BR>mere morsel.<BR>—पिण्ड-मुस्ता, f. a species of grass,<BR>Cyperus Pertenuis.<BR>—पिण्ड-मूल or पिण्ड-मू-<BR>लक, अम्, n. a carrot, Daucus Carota (= गर्जर).<BR>—पिण्ड-यज्ञ, अस्, m. the oblation of obsequial<BR>cakes to deceased ancestors.<BR>—पिण्ड-लेप, अस्, m.<BR>the particles or fragments of the obsequial cakes<BR>which cling to the hands, (these are offered to the<BR>three ancestors preceding the great-grandfather.)<BR>—पिण्ड-लोप, अस्, m. an interruption in offering<BR>the funeral cake; a neglect of the solemn obsequies<BR>in honour of deceased ancestors.<BR>—पिण्ड-वत्, ind.<BR>like a lump or ball.<BR>—पिण्ड-सम्बन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>relationship between a living person and one deceased<BR>sufficiently near to qualify the former to offer the<BR>obsequial cake to the latter; [cf. स-पिण्ड.]<BR>—पिण्ड-<BR>सम्बन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, qualified by near relationship<BR>to a living person to receive the obsequial cake from<BR>him at the oblation to the Manes.<BR>—पिण्ड-सेक्तृ,<BR>ता, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—पिण्ड-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. ‘mingled in a lump,’ mixed or intermingled<BR>together.<BR>—पिण्डान्वाहार्य (˚ड-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>to be eaten after the funeral cake has been offered<BR>(Manu III. 123).<BR>—पिण्डान्वाहार्यक, अम्, n.<BR>(with श्राद्ध) a meal in honour of the Manes<BR>after offering the funeral cakes.<BR>—पिण्डाभ्र (˚ड-<BR>अभ्˚), अम्, n. hail.<BR>—पिण्डायस (˚ड-अय्˚), अम्,<BR>n. steel.<BR>—पिण्डालु (˚ड-आलु), उस्, m., N. of<BR>two bulbous plants; = कन्द-गुडूची; an esculent<BR>medicinal root described as sweet, cooling, and<BR>diuretic (= Hindī peḍālu Bengālī cuvaḍiālu; in<BR>this sense also पिण्डालुक, अम्, n.).<BR>—पिण्डाश or<BR>पिण्डाशक (˚ड-आश्˚), or पिण्डाशन (˚ड-अश्˚), अस्,<BR>or पिण्डाशिन् (˚ड-आश्˚), ई, m. ‘eating morsels,’ a beg-<BR>gar.<BR>—पिण्डाह्वा (˚ड-आह्˚), f. the resin of Gardenia<BR>Gummifera (= नाडी-हिङ्गु).<BR>—पिण्डी-खण्ड, अस्,<BR>or अम्, m. or n. (?), a small wood of Tabernæmontana<BR>Coronaria trees (or of Aśoka trees).<BR>—पिण्डी-जङ्घ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man or of his descendants.<BR>—पिण्डी-<BR>तगर, अस्, m. a species of Tabernæmontana Coro-<BR>naria (= कफ-वर्धन).<BR>—पिण्डीतगरक, अस्,<BR>m. Tabernæmontana Coronaria.<BR>—पिण्डी-तरु, उस्,<BR>m. a species of tree (= महा-प्˚).<BR>—पिण्डी-पुष्प,<BR>अम्, n. Jonesia Aśoka.<BR>—पिण्डी-लेप, अस्, m. a kind<BR>of unguent.<BR>—पिण्डी-शूर, अस्, m. ‘a cake-hero,’ a<BR>cowardly boaster, cotquean, braggart.<BR>—पिण्डोदक-<BR>क्रिया (˚ड-उद्˚), f. an oblation of obsequial cakes<BR>and water.<BR>—पिण्डोद्धरण (˚ड-उद्˚), अम्, n.<BR>participating in funeral offerings, presenting them to<BR>common ancestors.<BR>—पिण्डोपनिषद् (˚ड-उप्˚), त्,<BR>f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डक|पिंडक|पिंडकं|पिण्डकं|पिंडकः|पिण्डकः
पिण्डक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a lump, lump of food; a<BR>round swelling or protuberance [cf. मस्तक-प्˚];<BR>the calf of the leg; incense, myrrh; a species of<BR>bulbous plant (= पिण्डालु); a carrot, Daucus Carota;<BR>(in astronomy) a sine expressed in numbers; (अस्),<BR>m. a Piśāca, goblin, demon; (इका), f. a globular<BR>swelling or protuberance, a fleshy swelling (in the<BR>shoulders, arms, legs, &c.), a wen (?); the calf of<BR>the leg; the instep; the nave of a wheel; a stool<BR>or seat of various shapes and dimensions; a base<BR>or pedestal for the image of a deity or for a Liṅga<BR>(Ved.); a kind of shrub (= श्वेताम्लि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डन|पिंडन|पिंडनं|पिण्डनः
पिण्डन, अम्, n. forming globes, taking a globular<BR>form (as water); (अस्), m. a mound or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डरक
पिण्डरक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), a bridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डल|पिंडल|पिंडलः|पिण्डलः
पिण्डल, अस्, m. a bridge, causeway, passage over a<BR>stream or ravine, a mound, ridge, balk raised to form a<BR>path across inundated fields; [cf. पिण्डन, पिण्डिल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डस|पिंडस|पिंडसः|पिण्डसः
पिण्डस, अस्, m. a beggar, mendicant living upon<BR>alms; [cf. पिण्डाश under पिण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डात|पिंडात|पिंडातः|पिण्डातः
पिण्डात, अस्, m. incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डार|पिंडार|पिण्डारं|पिंडारः|पिण्डारः
पिण्डार, अस्, m. a beggar, religious mendicant;<BR>a buffalo-herdsman, neatherd, cowherd; a species<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">Page0573-c+ 76</a>]<BR>of tree, Flacourtia Sapida; Trewia Nudiflora; an<BR>expression of censure; N. of a Nāga; (अम्), n.<BR>a kind of vegetable (= Hindī पिण्डारा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डारक
पिण्डारक, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga; N. of a<BR>Vṛṣṇi; of a son of Vasu-deva and Rohiṇī; of a<BR>river considered holy by the Hindūs; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a place of pilgrimage in Guzerat.<BR>—पिण्डारक-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डि|पिंडि|पिंडिः|पिण्डिः
पिण्डि, इस्, f. the nave of a wheel (= पिण्डी,<BR>पिण्डिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिक
पिण्डिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having large calves (?). See<BR>पिण्डिका under पिण्डक, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डित|पिंडित|पिण्डितं|पिण्डितः
पिण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, rolled into a ball or lump,<BR>pressed into a solid mass; thick, massy, lumpish;<BR>formed into a mass, heaped together, collected;<BR>mixed, intermingled with; united; added, multiplied;<BR>counted, numbered; (अस्), m. incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिन्|पिंडिन्
पिण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing a body (= शरीरिन्);<BR>receiving cakes of meal (as ancestors &c.); possessing<BR>the पिण्ड or funeral oblation; (ई), m. a beggar; an<BR>offerer of obsequial oblations or cakes of meal to<BR>the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिल|पिंडिल|पिण्डिलः
पिण्डिल, अस्, आ, अम्, having large calves (=<BR>स्थूल-जङ्घ); skilled in calculations; (अस्), m. a<BR>skilful calculator or arithmetician, a calculator of nati-<BR>vities, astrologer, astronomer; a bridge, mound, balk,<BR>causeway; (आ), f. a species of cucumber, Cucumis<BR>Maderaspatanus (= गोडुम्बा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीकृ|पिंडीकृ
पिण्डी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make into a lump or ball, press together,<BR>unite, join together, mix or intermingle; to con-<BR>centrate; to identify with (with सह).<BR>—पिण्डी-क-<BR>रण, अम्, n. making into a lump or ball, heaping.<BR>—पिण्डी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made into a lump or<BR>ball.<BR>—पिण्डी-कृत्य, ind. having made into a lump<BR>or ball; having concentrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीतक|पिण्डीतकः
पिण्डीतक, अस्, m. the tree Vangueria Spinosa;<BR>a kind of shrub, Tabernæmontana Coronaria; a<BR>species of basil (= फणिज्झक); (अम्), n. the<BR>fruit of the tree Vangueria Spinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीभू|पिंडीभू
पिण्डी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to be<BR>made into a lump or ball, to become a solid body.<BR>—पिण्डी-भाव, अस्, m. the being rolled together<BR>into a ball.<BR>—पिण्डी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, formed into<BR>a lump or ball, lumped, heaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीर|पिंडीर|पिण्डीरः
पिण्डीर, अस्, आ, अम्, sapless, juiceless, arid, dry;<BR>(अस्), m. the pomegranate tree [cf. कृष्ण-प्˚];<BR>cuttle-fish bone; sea foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोल
पिण्डोल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोलि|पिंडोलि|पिंडोलिः|पिण्डोलिः
पिण्डोलि, इस्, f. leavings of a meal, fragments<BR>dropped from the mouth, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिपाल
पिण्डिपाल पिण्डिपाल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a weapon with a single point; [cf. भिन्दि-<BR>पाल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्या
पिण्या पिण्या, f. heart-pea, Cardiosper-<BR>mum Halicacabum (= पण्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्याक|पिण्याकं|पिण्याकः
पिण्याक पिण्याक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. पिष्), the residue of seeds which have been<BR>ground for oil; oil-cake; incense; saffron; Asa<BR>Fœtida; (आ), f. a species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितामह|पितामहः
पितामह पिता-मह. See p. 574, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितु|पितुः
पितु पितु, उस्, m., Ved. (fr. rt. प्यै),<BR>juice, drink; nourishment; (Sāy.) = पालकम् अन्-<BR>नम्, nourishing food.<BR>—पितु-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>bestowing or providing food.<BR>—पितु-भाज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>Ved. enjoying or partaking of food; (Sāy.) = अन्-<BR>नार्थिन्, seeking or earning food.<BR>—पितु-भृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, Ved. bringing food.<BR>—पितु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>Ved. accompanied by food, abounding in food, nou-<BR>rishing.<BR>—पितु-षणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. bestowing or<BR>granting food.<BR>—पितु-स्तोम, अस्, m. ‘praise of<BR>food,’ N. of the hymn Ṛg-veda I. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितूय
पितूय, Nom. P. पितूयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to long<BR>for food, desire food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृ
पितृ पितृ, ता, m. (fr. rt. 3. पा), a father;<BR>(in the Veda पितृ is an epithet of Bṛhas-pati,<BR>Varuṇa, Prajā-pati, and especially of heaven or the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0574-a" target="_blank">Page0574-a+ 81</a>]<BR>sky; अन्तरा पितरम् मातरञ्-च, between heaven<BR>and earth; according to Sāy. पितृ = पालक, a<BR>protector); (तरौ), m. du. father and mother,<BR>parents, (in the Veda an epithet of the Araṇis or<BR>two pieces of wood regarded as the parents of Fire,<BR>and of heaven and earth regarded as the parents of<BR>all beings); (तरस्), m. pl. fathers, forefathers,<BR>ancestors; a father and his brothers, father and<BR>uncles, paternal ancestors; the spirits of departed an-<BR>cestors, the Manes or spirits of the dead (they are of<BR>two kinds, viz. either the spirits of the father, grand-<BR>fathers, and great-grandfathers of an individual or the<BR>progenitors of mankind generally, to both classes of<BR>whom Śrāddhas or obsequial worship is paid and<BR>oblations of food called Piṇḍas presented; they in-<BR>habit a peculiar region, which, according to some, is<BR>the Bhuvas or region of the air, according to others,<BR>the orbit of the moon, and are considered as the<BR>regents of the Nakṣatras Maghā and Mūla); [cf.<BR>Zend pita, base pa-tar: Gr. πα-τήρ, πάτρω-ς:<BR>Lat. pa-ter, Jup-piter: Goth. fa-dar: Old<BR>Germ. fa-tar, fa-ter, ‘father;’ fataro, ‘uncle:’<BR>Angl. Sax. faeder, ‘father;’ fadhu, ‘aunt,<BR>father's sister:’ Hib. athair, ‘father,’ for pathair.],<BR>—पितरि-शूर, अस्, m. ‘a hero against his father,’<BR>a cowardly boaster.<BR>—पिता-पुत्र, औ, m. du. father<BR>and son.<BR>—पितापुत्र-विरोध, अस्, m. a contest<BR>between father and son.<BR>—पितापुत्र-समागम,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist Sūtra.<BR>—पितापुत्रीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, relating to father and son; containing the<BR>words पितृ and पुत्र; (with सम्प्रदान) the<BR>transmission (of bodily capacities and powers) from<BR>father to son.<BR>—पिता-मह, अस्, m. a paternal<BR>grandfather; a N. of Brahmā the great father of all;<BR>N. of the author of a Dharma-śāstra; of the author<BR>of an astronomical work; (आस्), m. pl. the ancestors,<BR>Manes; (ई), f. a paternal grandmother.<BR>—पितामह-<BR>सरस्, अस्, n. or पितामहस्य सरस्, N. of a place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—पिता-सुमति-संवाद, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a part of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—पितुः-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. a father's son.<BR>—पितुः-ष्वसृ or<BR>पितुः-स्वसृ, सा, f. a father's sister.<BR>—पितृ-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, or पितृ-कार्य, अम्, n. obsequial rites, sacrifice<BR>offered to deceased ancestors.<BR>—पितृ-कल्प, अस्, m.<BR>(perhaps) legends relating to ancestors; N. of a long<BR>period of time, Brahmā's day of new moon.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>कानन, अम्, n. ‘grove of ancestors,’ a cemetery.<BR>—पितृ-कुल्या, f. ‘rivulet of the Pitṛs,’ N. of a<BR>river rising in the Malaya mountains.<BR>—पितृ-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. committed against parents or an-<BR>cestors (as sin).<BR>—पितृ-कृत्य, अम्, n. or पितृ-<BR>क्रिया, f. obsequial rites, oblations offered to the<BR>spirits of deceased ancestors.<BR>—पितृ-गण, अस्, m.<BR>the whole body of ancestors collectively, a group or<BR>class of Manes or deceased progenitors who were<BR>sons of the Ṛṣis or Prajā-patis, (the principal classes,<BR>according to Manu III. 194-199, are the Soma-sads,<BR>descended from Vi-rāj, the Agni-ṣvāttas from Marīci,<BR>Barhi-shads from Atri, Soma-pās from Bhṛgu, Haviṣ-<BR>mats from Aṅgiras, Ājya-pas from Pulastya, and<BR>Su-kālins from Vasiṣṭha; there are also the Agni-<BR>dagdhas and An-agnidagdhas, Kāvyas and Saumyas.)<BR>—पितृ-गणा, f. an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>गाथा, आस्, f. pl. ‘songs of the ancestors,’ an epithet<BR>of particular songs.<BR>—पितृ-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, be-<BR>longing or pertaining to a father.<BR>—पितृ-गृणा, f.<BR>probably a wrong reading for पितृ-गणा, q. v.<BR>—पितृ-गृह, अम्, n. a father's house, paternal<BR>mansion; ‘house of ancestors,’ a burial ground, ceme-<BR>tery.<BR>—पितृ-ग्रह, अस्, m. ‘the genius of the<BR>Manes,’ N. of a demon causing disease.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>घातक, अस्, or पितृ-घातिन्, ई, m. ‘slaying a<BR>father,’ a parricide.<BR>—पितृ-चेट, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—पितृ-तम, अस्, m., Ved., in पितृतमः<BR>पित्रीणां, best of the ancestors (Sāy. = पाल-<BR>कानाम् मध्ये अतिशयेन पालकः, a defender in<BR>the highest degree among defenders).<BR>—पितृ-तर्-<BR>पण, अम्, n. ‘refreshing the Manes,’ gifts in<BR>honour of deceased progenitors, distributed at the<BR>Śrāddhas or funeral ceremonies; an oblation to the<BR>Manes; the act of throwing water out of the right<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0574-b" target="_blank">Page0574-b+ 80</a>]<BR>hand at seasons of ablution as an offering to the<BR>Manes or deceased ancestors in general; the part of<BR>the hand between the thumb and fore-finger sacred<BR>to the Manes; sesamum (= तिल).<BR>—पितृ-तस्, ind.,<BR>Ved. from the father, on the father's side.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>तिथि, इस्, f. day of new moon, a day sacred to the<BR>Manes of either deceased parent, the day appointed<BR>for obsequial rites to deceased ancestors.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n. ‘the place of pilgrimage for proge-<BR>nitors,’ epithet of the city called Gayā (where the<BR>performance of funeral sacrifices is peculiarly meri-<BR>torious and efficacious); the part of the hand be-<BR>tween the fore-finger and thumb sacred to the<BR>Manes.<BR>—पितृतीर्थ-माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>chapter of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—पितृ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>fatherhood, paternity; the state or condition of a<BR>Pitṛ or deified progenitor.<BR>—पितृ-दत्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, given by a father (a term applied to a woman's<BR>peculiar property); (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>दयिता, f., N. of a work.<BR>—पितृ-दान or पितृ-<BR>दानक, अम्, n. a gift in honour of deceased an-<BR>cestors, an offering to the Manes.<BR>—पितृ-दाय,<BR>अस्, m. property inherited from a father, patrimony.<BR>—पितृ-देव, आस्, m. pl. the Manes and the gods;<BR>the divine Manes; (अस्, आ, अम्), worshipping a<BR>father; relating to the worship of the Manes or<BR>deceased ancestors.<BR>—पितृ-देवत or पितृ-देवत्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the Manes for deities,<BR>sacred to the Manes.<BR>—पितृ-दैवत, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>relating to the worship of the Manes; governed or<BR>presided over by the Manes; (अम्), n. epithet of the<BR>tenth lunar asterism or Maghā.<BR>—पितृ-दैवत्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the worship of the Manes;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a sacrifice offered to the Manes on<BR>the day called Aṣṭakā.<BR>—पितृ-द्रव्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘father's substance,’ patrimony.<BR>—पितृ-नामन्, आ,<BR>म्नी, अ, called after the father's name; [cf. मातृ-<BR>नामन्.]<BR>—पितृ-पक्ष, अस्, m. paternal side,<BR>paternal relationship; the half month of the Manes,<BR>N. of the dark half in the Gauṇa Āśvina, so termed<BR>as peculiarly appointed for the celebration of obse-<BR>quial rites to the Pitṛs or Manes; a father's relations,<BR>relatives by the father's side; (अस्, आ, अम्), being on<BR>the father's side.<BR>—पितृ-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>Manes,’ an epithet of Yama, regent of the dead;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl. the Manes and the lords of creatures<BR>(Prajā-patis).<BR>—पितृ-पद, अम्, n. the world or<BR>state of the Manes.<BR>—पितृ-पात्र, अम्, n. a cup or<BR>other vessel used at obsequial rites.<BR>—पितृ-पितृ, ता,<BR>m. a father's father, paternal grandfather.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. drunk by ancestors or deceased<BR>progenitors.<BR>—पितृ-पूजन, अम्, n. worship of the<BR>Manes.<BR>—पितृ-पैतामह, अस्, ई, अम्, inherited or<BR>derived from father and grandfather; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>fathers and grandfathers, ancestors.<BR>—पितृपैता-<BR>महिक, अस्, ई, अम्, inherited or derived from father<BR>and grandfather.<BR>—पितृ-प्रसू, ऊस्, f. a father's<BR>mother; ‘mother of the Manes,’ twilight (the time<BR>when the Manes of departed ancestors are abroad).<BR>—पितृ-प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, received from a father;<BR>inherited patrimonially.<BR>—पितृ-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘dear<BR>to the Pitṛs,’ a species of plant (= भृङ्ग-राज).<BR>—पितृ-बन्धु, उस्, m. a kinsman by the father's<BR>side, as the son of the paternal grandfather's sister,<BR>of the paternal grandmother's sister, and of the<BR>father's maternal uncle; (उ), n. relationship by the<BR>father's side.<BR>—पितृ-बान्धव, अस्, m. a kins-<BR>man in the paternal line.<BR>—पितृ-भक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dutifully attached to a father.<BR>—पितृ-भक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. filial duty to a father.<BR>—पितृभक्ति-तरङ्-<BR>गिणी, f., N. of a work.<BR>—पितृ-भूति, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>commentator on Kātyāyana's Śrauta-sūtras.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>भोजन, अम्, n. a father's food; food offered to the<BR>Manes; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the plant Phaseolus Radi-<BR>atus (a species of pulse = माष).<BR>—पितृ-भ्रातृ,<BR>ता, m. a father's brother, paternal uncle.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a father, having an illus-<BR>trious father; accompanied by the Manes, connected<BR>with the Manes (as Soma or Yama); mentioning<BR>the Manes or deceased ancestors.<BR>—पितृ-मन्दिर,<BR>अम्, n. a father's house, paternal mansion; ‘dwelling-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0574-c" target="_blank">Page0574-c+ 81</a>]<BR>place of ancestors,’ a cemetery.<BR>—पितृ-मातृ-हीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of father and mother, orphan.<BR>—पितृ-मेध or पितृ-यज्ञ, अस्, m. sacrifice<BR>offered to the Manes, obsequial offerings.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>याण, Ved. or पितृ-यान, अस्, आ, अम्, trodden by<BR>the Manes; (अम्), n. the path trodden by the<BR>Manes, the way leading to the Manes; the vehicle<BR>of the Manes, a car to convey holy persons after their<BR>decease to heaven.<BR>—पितृ-राज्, ट्, or पितृ-राज, अस्,<BR>or पितृ-राजन्, आ, m. ‘king of the Manes,’ an<BR>epithet of Yama.<BR>—पितृ-रूप, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Rudra.<BR>—पितृ-लोक, अस्, m. a father's house, paternal<BR>mansion; the world or sphere of the Manes (to<BR>which various situations are ascribed, but principally<BR>the Bhuvas region or mid-heaven).<BR>—पितृ-वंश,<BR>अस्, m. the paternal family.<BR>—१. पितृ-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having a father, whose father is living.<BR>—२. पितृ-<BR>वत्, ind. like a father; like the Manes; as if for the<BR>Manes; as in the sacrifice offered to the Manes.<BR>—पि-<BR>तृ-वन, अम्, n. ‘grove of ancestors,’ a cemetery, a<BR>place where dead bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>—पि-<BR>तृवने-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, haunting a cemetery; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva; a goblin.<BR>—पितृ-वर्तिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘staying or abiding with ancestors,’ N. of a<BR>Brāhman (= king Brahma-datta).<BR>—पितृ-वसति,<BR>इस्, f. ‘abode of departed ancestors,’ a cemetery.<BR>—पितृ-वाक्-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, attentive to the<BR>voice of parents, obedient to parents.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>वित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. acquired by ancestors; (Sāy.)<BR>= पितुः सकाशाल् लब्ध, derived from a father,<BR>patrimonial.<BR>—पितृ-व्रत, अस्, m. a worshipper of<BR>the Manes; (अम्), n. worship of ancestors, obsequial<BR>rites.<BR>—पितृ-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—पितृ-श्रवण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bringing honour<BR>to a father; (Sāy. = पिता प्रख्यायते येन पु-<BR>त्रेण तादृशः.)<BR>—पितृ-श्राद्ध, अम्, n. a<BR>funeral ceremony or obsequial rites in honour of<BR>a father or deceased ancestor.<BR>—पितृ-षद्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, Ved. living unmarried with a father or with<BR>parents; ‘dwelling with the Manes,’ an epithet of<BR>Rudra.<BR>—पितृ-षदन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. inhabited<BR>by the Manes.<BR>—पितृ-ष्वसृ, सा, f. a father's<BR>sister, paternal aunt (= पितुः-ष्वसृ).<BR>—पितृ-<BR>ष्वस्रीय, अस्, आ, m. f. a father's sister's son or<BR>daughter, a paternal aunt's son or daughter.<BR>—पितृ-<BR>सन्निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like a father, fatherly, paternal.<BR>—पितृ-सामान्य, अम्, n. ancestors collectively.<BR>—पितृ-सू, ऊस्, f. a father's mother; ‘mother of the<BR>Manes,’ twilight; [cf. पितृ-प्रसू.]<BR>—पितृ-सूक्त,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Vedic hymn.<BR>—पितृ-स्थान, अस्,<BR>m. a guardian; (अम्), n. the sphere of the Manes.<BR>—पितृस्थानीय, अस्, m. a guardian (who takes the<BR>place of a parent).<BR>—पितृ-स्वसृ, सा, f. an incorrect<BR>form for पितृ-ष्वसृ.<BR>—पितृस्वस्रीय, अस्, आ, m.<BR>f., see पितृष्वस्रीय.<BR>—पितृ-हत्या, f. the murder<BR>of a father, parricide.<BR>—पितृ-हन्, आ, m. a parricide.<BR>—पितृ-हू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, invoking or dedicated to the<BR>Pitṛs; (ऊस्), f., scil. द्वार्, N. of the southern aper-<BR>ture of the human body, i. e. of the right ear; [cf.<BR>देव-हू.]<BR>—पितृ-हूय, अम्, n., Ved. invoking or<BR>summoning deceased ancestors.<BR>—पित्रर्जित (˚तृ-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, derived from a father; property<BR>originally acquired by a father.<BR>—पित्रर्थम् (˚तृ-<BR>अर्˚), ind. for a father's sake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0573-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक|पितृकं
पितृक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>paternal, parental, ancestral, relating or belonging to<BR>parents or progenitors, obsequial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0574-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृव्य|पितृव्यः
पितृव्य, अस्, m. a father's brother, paternal uncle;<BR>any elderly male relation; [cf. Gr. πάτρω-ς; Lat.<BR>patruus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0574-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्र्य|पित्र्यं|पित्र्यः
पित्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, derived from a father, relating<BR>to a father, paternal, patrimonial, ancestral, belonging<BR>to a father or to progenitors, usual or customary with<BR>a father; relating to deceased ancestors, consecrated<BR>to the Manes, referring or devoted to the Manes,<BR>obsequial; in Manu II. 59. पित्र्यं तीर्थम् = the<BR>part of the hand sacred to deified progenitors, i. e.<BR>the part between the fore-finger and thumb; (अस्),<BR>m. the eldest brother (who takes the place of a<BR>father); the month Māgha; (आ), f. the Nakṣatra<BR>Maghā (presided over by the Manes); the day of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">Page0575-a+ 78</a>]<BR>full moon, the worship of the Manes on the day<BR>of full moon; (अम्), n., scil. कर्म, the worship<BR>of the Manes; the Nakṣatra Maghā; the part of<BR>the hand between the fore-finger and thumb.<BR>—पित्र्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. (perhaps) possess-<BR>ing property inherited from a father; (Sāy.) =<BR>पितृ-मत्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0574-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्त|पित्तं
पित्त पित्त, अम्, n. (etymology doubtful),<BR>bile, the bilious humor, one of the three humors of<BR>the body (the other two being वात and कफ; it<BR>is especially secreted between the stomach and<BR>bowels, and thence flows through the liver, and<BR>distributes itself in the spleen, heart, eyes, and skin;<BR>its chief quality is heat); [cf. कूर्म-प्˚, गो-प्˚,<BR>रक्त-प्˚, पैत्तिक.]<BR>—पित्त-कोष, अस्, m. the<BR>gall-bladder.<BR>—पित्त-क्षोभ, अस्, m. excess and<BR>disturbance of the bilious humor.<BR>—पित्त-गदिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, suffering from bilious complaints, bilious.<BR>—पित्त-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘bile-destroying,’ anti-<BR>bilious; (अम्), n. an antidote to bilious com-<BR>plaints; ghee ?; (ई), f. a plant, Cocculus Cordifolius.<BR>—पित्त-ज्वर, अस्, m. bilious fever.<BR>—पित्त-द्रा-<BR>विन्, ई, इणी, इ, ‘bile-dispersing,’ removing bile; (ई),<BR>m. the sweet citron (= मधुर-जम्बीर).<BR>—पित्त-<BR>धर, अस्, आ, अम्, containing bile, bilious.<BR>—पित्त-<BR>निवर्हण, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying bile.<BR>—पित्त-<BR>प्रकृति, इस्, इस्, इ, being of a bilious temperament.<BR>—पित्त-प्रकोप, अस्, m. excess and vitiation of<BR>the bilious humor.<BR>—पित्त-रक्त, अम्, n. plethora;<BR>[cf. रक्त-पित्त.]<BR>—पित्त-रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, suffering<BR>from bilious complaints, bilious.<BR>—पित्त-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having bile, bilious.<BR>—पित्त-वायु, उस्, m.<BR>flatulence arising from excess and vitiation of the<BR>bilious humor.<BR>—पित्त-विदग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt<BR>up by bile, impaired or destroyed by bile.<BR>—पित्त-<BR>विनाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘bile-destroying,’ antibilious.<BR>—पित्त-शमन, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘bile-alleviating,’<BR>antibilious.<BR>—पित्त-स्यन्द, अस्, m. a bilious form<BR>of ophthalmia; [cf. पित्ताभिष्यन्द.]<BR>—पित्त-<BR>हर, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘bile-removing,’ antibilious.<BR>—पित्-<BR>तातीसार (˚त-अत्˚), अस्, m. ‘bile-dysentery,’ a bilious<BR>form of diarrhœa.<BR>—पित्तातीसारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, suffering<BR>from a bilious form of dysentery.<BR>—पित्ताभिष्यन्द<BR>(˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, m. a bilious form of ophthalmia;<BR>[cf. पित्त-स्यन्द.]<BR>—पित्तारि (˚त-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of bile,’ i. e. anything antibilious; N. of<BR>various plants and vegetable substances used to coun-<BR>teract biliousness (= पर्पट, लाक्षा, and वर्वर).<BR>—पित्तोपहत (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, impaired or<BR>destroyed by bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तल|पित्तलं
पित्तल, अस्, आ, अम्, bilious, relating to the bilious<BR>humor, secreting bile; (आ), f. the plant Jussiæa<BR>Repens; (ई), f., N. of a plant, = मूर्वा; (अम्), n.<BR>brass, bell-metal; a species of birch tree (the bark of<BR>which is used for writing upon; cf. भूर्ज-पत्त्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्थ
पित्थ पित्थ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सत्|पित्सन्त्
पित्सत् पित्सत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. 2. पत्), being about to fly or fall, habitually<BR>falling or coming down; (अन्), m. a bird; [cf. Gr.<BR>ψίττακος; Lat. psittacus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सल|पित्सलं|पित्सलः
पित्सल, अम्, n. a road, path, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सु
पित्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, being about to fly or fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषत्|पिपतिषन्त्
पिपतिषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, about to fly or fall,<BR>inclined or addicted to falling repeatedly; (अन्), m.<BR>a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषा
पिपतिषा, f. wish or inclination to come down<BR>or fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषु|पिपतिषुः
पिपतिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, being about to fall; (उस्),<BR>m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिद्व
पिद्व पिद्व, अस्, m., Ved. a species of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधा
पिधा पि-धा = अपि-धा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिदधत्
पि-दधत्, अत्, अती, अत्, covering, veiling, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधातव्य
पि-धातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be covered or hidden;<BR>to be stopped up, to be shut or closed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधान|पिधानं
पि-धान, अम्, n. covering, stopping up, shut-<BR>ting; (अस् or अम्), m. or n. (?), a covering, cover,<BR>concealment; a lid, top, cover; a sheath; a wrap-<BR>per, cloak; [cf. Cambro-Brit. fedon, ‘a screen.’]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">Page0575-b+ 75</a>]<BR>—पिधान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, provided with a cover,<BR>covered with a lid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधानक|पिधानकं
पिधानक, अस्, m. a cover, lid; a sheath, scab-<BR>bard [cf. खड्ग-प्˚].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधाय
पि-धाय, ind. having covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधायक
पि-धायक, अस्, इका, अम्, covering, hiding, con-<BR>cealing.<BR>—पिधायक-ता, f. the state or act of<BR>covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिहित|पिहितं
पि-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, shut, covered, hidden, con-<BR>cealed; filled with; (अम्), n. a particular figure of<BR>speech, showing any person by insinuation that one<BR>knows his secrets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनस
पिनस पिनस, अस्, m. = पीनस, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनह्
पिनह् पि-नह् = अपि-नह्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनद्ध|पिनद्धः
पि-नद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, tied on, put on, fastened,<BR>bound; dressed, accoutred; wrapped, covered, con-<BR>cealed; pierced, penetrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनद्धक
पिनद्धक, अस्, इका, अम्, dressed, clothed,<BR>covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनह्य
पि-नह्य, ind. having put on or dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाक|पिनाकं|पिनाकः
पिनाक पिनाक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. rt. 3. पा), a staff, stick; a bow; the club or bow<BR>of Rudra-Śiva; a trident or three-pronged spear;<BR>the trident of Śiva; a shower or fall of dust, falling<BR>dust; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (ई), f. a kind of<BR>stringed instrument, a sort of violin.<BR>—पिनाक-<BR>गोप्तृ, ता, m. ‘preserver of the Pināka,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—पिनाक-धृक् (see धृक्), or पिनाक-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. ‘bearer of the Pināka,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—पिनाक-पाणि, इस्, m. ‘Pināka in hand,’ an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकि
पिनाकि, इस्, इस्, इ (occurring only in acc. sing.),<BR>substituted for पिनाकिन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकिन्
पिनाकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, armed with a Pināka; (ई), m.<BR>an epithet of Rudra-Śiva; N. of one of the eleven<BR>Rudras; (इनी), f., N. of two rivers.<BR>—पिनाकिनी-<BR>माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a part of the Brahmāṇḍa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्यास|पिन्यासं|पिन्यासः
पिन्यास पिन्यास, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>2. अस् with पि-नि), Asa Fœtida; [cf. पिण्याक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्व्
पिन्व् पिन्व्, cl. 1. P. A. पिन्वति, -ते,<BR>पिपिन्व, पिपिन्वे, पिन्विष्यति, -ते,<BR>पिन्वितुम्, Ved. to cause to swell, to distend, to cause<BR>to overflow or run over, to cause to abound; to cause<BR>to abound in milk (Ṛg-veda I. 112, 3, where,<BR>according to Sāy., पिन्वथः = पयसा पूरित-<BR>वन्तौ); to sprinkle, wet, moisten, water; to dis-<BR>charge, pour forth; to grant, bestow; (A.) to swell,<BR>to be distended, to overflow; [cf. rt. प्यै.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्व
पिन्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing to swell or flow;<BR>[cf. दानु-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्वन
पिन्वन, अम्, n., Ved. a particular vessel used in<BR>religious ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्वन्त्यपीया
पिन्वन्त्यपीया, f., Ved., scil. ऋच्, an epithet of<BR>the verse beginning पिन्वन्त्य् अपो (Ṛg-veda I.<BR>64, 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्वमान
पिन्वमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being swollen,<BR>swelling, being full or filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषत्|पिपतिषन्त्
पिपतिषत् पिपतिषत्, पिपतिषा, पिपतिषु.<BR>See under पित्सत्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपविषु
पिपविषु पिपविषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. 1. पू), wishing to purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपाठक
पिपाठक पिपाठक, अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासत्|पिपासन्त्
पिपासत् पिपासत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. Desid.<BR>of rt. 1. पा), thirsting, thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासा
पिपासा, f. thirst, desire to drink.<BR>—पिपासा-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, thirsting, thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासित|पिपासितः
पिपासित, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to drink, thirsty,<BR>athirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासिन्
पिपासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wishing to drink, thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासु|पिपासुः
पिपासु, उस्, उस्, उ, thirsty, athirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपिली
पिपिली पिपिली, f. = पिपीलि, an ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपिष्वत्|पिपिष्वन्त्
पिपिष्वत् पिपिष्वत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. a rt.<BR>पि for पी), Ved. (perhaps) swollen, overfull, super-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">Page0575-c+ 74</a>]<BR>abundant; (according to Sāy.) favourable to the hus-<BR>bandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीतक|पिपीतकः
पिपीतक पिपीतक, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman<BR>who was the first to perform a particular ceremony<BR>in honour of Viṣṇu on the twelfth day of the light<BR>half of the month Vaiśākha; (ई), f. the twelfth day<BR>of the light half of the month Vaiśākha (when giving<BR>away water is an act of merit, so called after the<BR>Brāhman Pipītaka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपील|पिपीलः
पिपील पिपील, अस्, ई, m. f. (perhaps a re-<BR>duplicated form fr. rt. पीड्), an ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलक|पिपीलकः
पिपीलक, अस्, m. a large black ant; (इका), f. the<BR>common small red ant; a female ant.<BR>—पिपीलिका-<BR>परिसर्पण, अम्, n. the running about of ants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलिक|पिपीलिकः
पिपीलिक, अस्, m. an ant; (अम्), n. a kind of gold<BR>supposed to be collected by ants.<BR>—पिपीलिक-<BR>मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘thin in the middle like an<BR>ant,’ N. of any metre the middle Pāda of which is<BR>shorter than the preceding and following.<BR>—पिपी-<BR>लिक-मध्यमा, f., N. of a species of the Anuṣṭubh<BR>metre.<BR>—पिपीलिका-मध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, a kind of<BR>fasting (beginning on the day of full moon with<BR>fifteen mouthfuls, decreasing by one daily until the<BR>day of new moon, and after that increasing by one<BR>daily until the next day of full moon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपृच्छिषु
पिपृच्छिषु पिपृच्छिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid.<BR>of rt. प्रछ्), about to ask or inquire, wishing to ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पका
पिप्पका पिप्पका, f., Ved. a species of bird;<BR>[cf. पिप्पीक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पटा
पिप्पटा पिप्पटा, f. a kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पल|पिप्पलं|पिप्पलः
पिप्पल पिप्पल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>3. पा), the holy fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa [cf. अश्वत्-<BR>थ]; a kind of bird; a nipple (so called from its<BR>similarity to a berry); the sleeve of a jacket or coat;<BR>N. of a son of Mitra and Revatī; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of a school of the Atharva-veda; (आस्), f., N. of a<BR>river; (ई), f. a berry; long pepper, Piper Longum<BR>(both plant and berry; cf. कपि-प्˚, जल-प्˚, तोय-प्˚);<BR>(अम्), n. a berry in general, the berry of the tree<BR>Ficus Religiosa; sensual enjoyment; water; the<BR>sleeve of a coat; [cf. Gr. πίπερι, πέπερι; Lat.<BR>piper.]<BR>—पिप्पलाद (˚ल-अद˚), अस्, m. ‘eater<BR>of berries,’ N. of an ancient teacher of the<BR>Atharva-veda; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a school of the<BR>Atharva-veda (also पिप्पलादकास्).<BR>—पिप्पलाद-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—पिप्-<BR>पलाद-श्रुति, इस्, f., N. of a work mentioned in<BR>the Parāśara-smṛti.<BR>—पिप्पला-वती, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—पिप्पली-मूल, अम्, n. the root of long<BR>pepper.<BR>—पिप्पली-लवण, ए, n. du. pepper and salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलक|पिप्पलकं
पिप्पलक, अम्, n. a nipple; sewing thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलायन
पिप्पलायन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलि|पिप्पलिः
पिप्पलि, इस्, f. long pepper; वसिष्ठस्य पिप्पलि,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR>—पिप्पलि-श्रोणि, इस्, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलीका
पिप्पलीका, f. a species of plant (= अश्वत्थी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलू
पिप्पलू पिप्पलू, ऊस्, m. or f. (?), N. of a<BR>man (or woman ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पिका
पिप्पिका पिप्पिका, f. the tartar of the teeth;<BR>[cf. पिट्टक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पीक
पिप्पीक पिप्पीक, अस्, m., Ved. a species of<BR>animal, probably a bird; [cf. पिप्पका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्रीषा
पिप्रीषा पिप्रीषा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. 1.<BR>प्री), Ved. desire of pleasing or showing kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्रीषु
पिप्रीषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of pleasing, wishing<BR>to give pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्रु
पिप्रु पिप्रु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. पॄ?), Ved., N.<BR>of a demon (who was conquered and whose strong-<BR>holds were destroyed by Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्लु|पिप्लुः
पिप्लु पिप्लु, उस्, m. (perhaps for अपि-प्लु;<BR>said to be fr. rt. प्लुष् with अपि), a freckle, mark,<BR>mole.<BR>—पिप्लु-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, having a mark on<BR>the ear.<BR>—पिप्लु-प्रच्छादन, अस्, ई, अम्, covering<BR>or concealing a mole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिब
पिब पिब or पिव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. पा),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">Page0576-a+ 76</a>]<BR>drinking, who or what drinks; [cf. त्रि-प्˚.]<BR>—पिब-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing a form of the<BR>verb पिबति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0575-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिबत्
पिबत् or पिवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, drinking, who or<BR>what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिब्दमान
पिब्दमान पिब्दमान, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps<BR>fr. a reduplicated form of rt. 2. पद्), Ved. becoming<BR>or being firm or solid, becoming or being hard or<BR>compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिब्दन
पिब्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. firm, hard, solid,<BR>compact; (अम्), n. (according to Sāy.) a Rakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पियारु
पियारु पियारु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Sautra rt.<BR>1. पीय्), Ved. censuring, blaming, deriding, mis-<BR>chievous (Sāy. = हिंसक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पियाल|पियालः
पियाल पियाल, अस्, m. (= प्रियाल, q. v.,<BR>but said to be fr. the Sautra rt. 1. पीय्), the tree<BR>Buchanania Latifolia (called in Hindī also Chironji,<BR>whence it has been named Chironjia Sapida; in<BR>Bengal it is commonly called Piya or Piyal); (अम्),<BR>n. the fruit of Buchanania Latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्
पिल् पिल्, cl. 10. P. पेलयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>throw, cast; to send; to incite; [cf.<BR>rts. पेल्, विल्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलु|पिलुः
पिलु, उस्, or पिलुक, अस्, m. a species of tree<BR>(= पीलु; cf. पैलव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलुनी
पिलुनी, f. a species of plant (= मूर्वा; a wrong<BR>form for पिलु-पर्णी; cf. पीलु-पर्णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलि
पिलि पिलि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलिन्दवत्स
पिलिन्दवत्स पिलिन्द-वत्स, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>disciple of Śākya-muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलिप्पिल
पिलिप्पिल पिलिप्पिल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. slip-<BR>pery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्ल|पिल्लः
पिल्ल पिल्ल, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be a substi-<BR>tute for क्लिन्न), blear-eyed; (अस्), m. a bleared eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्लका
पिल्लका, f. a female elephant, (the elephant's eye<BR>being usually moist.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश्
पिश् 1. पिश्, cl. 6. P. A. पिंशति, -ते,<BR>पिपेश, पिपिशे, पेशिष्यति, -ते, अपेशीत्,<BR>पेशितुम्, Ved. to adorn, deck, decorate, embellish;<BR>to prepare, make ready (especially meat, by cutting<BR>it up and carving it); to shape, fashion, mould,<BR>form; to be decomposed, to be reduced to consti-<BR>tuent parts; to be organized; to light, enlighten:<BR>Caus. पेशयति, Aor. अपीपिशत्: Desid. पिपिशिषति,<BR>पिपेशिषति; Intens. पेपिश्यते, पेपेष्टि, to be<BR>richly adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश्
2. पिश्, f. an ornament, decoration; (Sāy.) =<BR>रूपं हिरण्यादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश
पिश, अस्, m., Ved. (according to Sāy.) = रुरु, a<BR>sort of deer (probably so called from its colour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्ग|पिशंग|पिशङ्गः
पिशङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम्, reddish, reddish-brown, of a<BR>tawny or brown colour; (अस्), m. tawny colour; N.<BR>of a serpent-demon.<BR>—पिशङ्ग-ता, f. or पिशङ्ग-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the being of a tawny colour, tawniness.<BR>—पिशङ्ग-भृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. (perhaps) having<BR>red fangs; (Sāy.) = ईषद्-रक्त-वर्ण, being of a<BR>pale-red hue, tawny-coloured.<BR>—पिशङ्ग-राति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, Ved. giving reddish (i. e. golden) gifts (said of<BR>Indra); (Sāy.) = बहुरूप-धनेन्द्र, lord of<BR>manifold wealth.<BR>—पिशङ्ग-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>being of a reddish or yellow appearance; (Sāy.) =<BR>हिरण्य-रूप, golden-coloured.<BR>—पिशङ्ग-सन्-<BR>दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. (according to Mahī-dhara) being<BR>of a red or yellow colour; (according to Sāy.) =<BR>नाना-रूप, of various kinds.<BR>—पिशङ्गाश्व (˚ग-<BR>अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having reddish or tawny<BR>horses (said of the Maruts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गक|पिशंगक|पिशंगकः|पिशङ्गकः
पिशङ्गक, अस्, m., N. of an attendant of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गिन्|पिशंगिन्
पिशङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, brown, tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गिल
पिशङ्गिल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., N. of a colour (?);<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara) = पिशं + गिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाच|पिशाचः
पिशाच, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. पिश for पिशित,<BR>‘flesh,’ and rt. 1. अञ्च्), N. of a class of demons<BR>(perhaps originally a personification of the ignis<BR>fatuus; in the Veda they are enumerated after gods,<BR>men, Manes, Asuras, and Rākṣasas; in later times<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">Page0576-b+ 80</a>]<BR>they are described as the children of Krodhā); a<BR>sprite, fiend, goblin, ogre, malevolent being (some-<BR>thing between an infernal imp and a ghost, always<BR>described as fierce and malignant); N. of a Rakṣas;<BR>(ई), f. a female imp, a she-demon [cf. स्त्री-प्˚]; N.<BR>of a daughter of Dakṣa and mother of the Piśācas;<BR>a species of Valeriana (= गन्ध-मांसी).<BR>—पिशाच-<BR>ता, f. or पिशाच-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition<BR>of a Piśāca.<BR>—पिशाच-द्रु, उस्, m. a species of tree,<BR>Trophis Aspera (the favourite haunt of the Piśācas).<BR>—पिशाच-बाधा, f. demoniacal possession.<BR>—पि-<BR>शाच-भाषा, f. ‘Piśāca language,’ a gibberish or cor-<BR>ruption of Sanskrit used in plays.<BR>—पिशाच-मोचन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘release of the Piśāca,’ N. of a place of pilgrim-<BR>age.<BR>—पिशाचमोचन-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR>—पिशाच-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a species of<BR>tree, Trophis Aspera (= शाखोट).<BR>—पिशाच-सञ्-<BR>चार, अस्, m. demoniacal possession.<BR>—पिशाच-सभ,<BR>अम्, n. an assemblage of goblins or fiends; the place<BR>or hall of their assembly, pandemonium.<BR>—पिशाचा-<BR>लय (˚च-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of Piśācas,’ N. of a<BR>particular luminous phenomenon, phosphorescence.<BR>—पिशाची-करण, अम्, n. transforming into a<BR>Piśāca.<BR>—पिशाचोरग-राक्षस (˚च-उर्˚), आस्, m.<BR>pl. Piśācas, serpents, and Rākṣasas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचक
पिशाचक, अस्, m. a Piśāca; (इका), f. = पिशाची<BR>(at the end of comps., e. g. गन्ध-प्˚, धन-प्˚);<BR>N. of a river; scil. भाषा, the language of the Piśā-<BR>cas.<BR>—पिशाचक-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचकिन्
पिशाचकिन्, ई, m. an epithet of Kuvera the god<BR>of wealth (the treasures of this deity being guarded<BR>by Piśācas and other malignant beings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचि|पिशाचिः
पिशाचि, इस्, m., Ved. a Piśāca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशित|पिशितं
पिशित, अम्, n. flesh which has been cut up or<BR>prepared, flesh, meat; a small piece; (आ), f. spikenard,<BR>Nardostachys Jatamansi (= जटा-मांसी).<BR>—पिशित-<BR>भुज्, क्, क्, क्, eating flesh; (क्), m. one who eats<BR>flesh.<BR>—पिशिताश (˚त-आश), अस्, आ, अम्, eating flesh;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of flesh-eating demons, as Rāk-<BR>ṣasas or Piśācas; a fiend; a cannibal.<BR>—पिशिताशन<BR>(˚त-अश्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, flesh-eating, meat-eating; (अस्),<BR>m. a demon, fiend, cannibal, Rakṣas, Piśāca (de-<BR>scribed as a child of Ni-kaṣā); epithet of a wolf.<BR>—पिशिताशिन् (˚त-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating flesh or<BR>meat, carnivorous; (ई), m. a demon, goblin, can-<BR>nibal; N. of an attendant of Śiva.<BR>—पिशितेप्सु<BR>(˚त-ईप्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of flesh, eager for or<BR>greedy after meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशी
पिशी, f. spikenard, Nardostachys Jatamansi (=<BR>पिशिता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुन|पिशुनं|पिशुनः
पिशुन, अस्, आ, अम्, informing against, betraying,<BR>treacherous; disparaging, calumniating, backbiting,<BR>calumnious, slanderous; cruel, wicked, malignant,<BR>mischievous, harsh, unkind; exciting hopes and dis-<BR>appointing them; vile, low, contemptible, infamous;<BR>stupid, a fool; making known, indicating, evincing,<BR>displaying, reminding, commemorating, memorable<BR>for (at the end of comps., e. g. तुल्यानुराग-प्˚,<BR>manifesting an equal attachment; क्षत्र-प्रध-<BR>न-प्˚, memorable for the conflict of Kṣatriyas);<BR>(अस्), m. a betrayer, traitor, informer, spy, tale-<BR>bearer, backbiter, calumniator, slanderer; epithet of<BR>a goblin dangerous to pregnant women; cotton<BR>(which betrays by hanging to the clothes); an epi-<BR>thet of Nārada (the messenger and informant of the<BR>gods); a crow; N. of a Brāhman; N. of a minister<BR>of Dushyanta; (आ), f. a species of plant, Medicago<BR>Esculenta; (अम्), n. informing against, betraying,<BR>sycophancy; saffron (which betrays an unfaithful<BR>lover); [cf. Gr. πικ῏πό-ς, πευκεδανό-ς, πευκάλιμο-ς,<BR>ἐχε-πευκές: Lith. pī1k-ta-s, ‘bad;’ pýk-ti, ‘to be<BR>angry;’ peīk-ti, ‘to despise, to blame.’]<BR>—पिशुन-<BR>ता, f. slander, scandal, backbiting, betrayal, syco-<BR>phancy.<BR>—पिशुन-वचन or पिशुन-वाक्य, अम्,<BR>n. evil speech, bad report, detraction, slander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनय
पिशुनय, Nom. P. पिशुनयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>betray, make known, indicate, make manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिक
पिशिक पिशिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>in the South.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशील|पिशीलं
पिशील पिशील or पिशीलक, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">Page0576-c+ 77</a>]<BR>(a wooden) vessel or dish.<BR>—पिशील-वीणा, f. a kind<BR>of stringed instrument or guitar, the strings of which<BR>are stretched across a frame (= शूर्प-वीणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुन|पिशुनं|पिशुनः
पिशुन पिशुन. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्
पिष् पिष्, cl. 7. P. (ep. also A.) पिनष्टि,<BR>पिंष्टे (Impv. 2nd sing. पिण्ढि), पि-<BR>पेष, पेक्ष्यति, अपिषत्, पेष्टुम् (ep. Impf.<BR>अपिंषत्, Pot. पिषेत्), to grind, pound, crush; to<BR>bruise, hurt, injure, destroy; cl. 10. P. or Caus. पेष-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अपीपिषत्, to grind, pound; to<BR>injure; to give; to be strong; to dwell; cl. 1. 10.<BR>P. पेषति, पेषयति, to go, move; [cf. Gr. πτίσσ-ω<BR>for πίσσ-ω, πίτυρον, πτίσ-μα, πίσ-ο-ς, πίσ-ινο-ς,<BR>πίσσο-; Lat. pins-o, pīs-o, pis-tor, pis-tillu-m,<BR>pistrīnum, pis-tura, pis-u-m, Piso, pī-lu-m,<BR>pī-la, pī-lu-s; Lith. pes-tà, ‘a mill.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्ट|पिष्टं
पिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, ground, pounded, crushed,<BR>bruised; rubbed together, squeezed, clasped (as the<BR>hands); kneaded; (अम्), n. anything ground, any<BR>finely ground substance, flour, meal, (न पिष्टम्<BR>पिनष्टि, he does not grind flour, i. e. he does<BR>no useless work or vain repetition); lead; (अस्),<BR>m. pastry; N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl., N. of his<BR>descendants.<BR>—पिष्ट-पचन, अम्, n. a pan for<BR>parching flower; a boiler, seether, sauce-pan.<BR>—पिष्ट-पशु, उस्, m. an effigy of a beast or<BR>sacrificial victim made with flour or dough.<BR>—पिष्ट-<BR>पाक, अस्, m. food prepared by baking flour.<BR>—पिष्-<BR>टपाक-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, containing food prepared by<BR>baking flour; (त्), m. a boiler.<BR>—पिष्ट-पाचक,<BR>अम्, n. a boiler.<BR>—पिष्ट-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a cake of<BR>meal.<BR>—पिष्ट-पूर, अस्, m. meal made up into a<BR>sort of cake with clarified butter; [cf. घृत-पूर.]<BR>—पिष्ट-पेष, अस्, m. or पिष्ट-पेषण, अम्,<BR>n. ‘grinding flour,’ useless labour, vain repetition.<BR>—पिष्ट-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of meal or flour,<BR>mixed with flour; जलम् पिष्ट-मयम्, water<BR>sprinkled with meal.<BR>—पिष्ट-मेह, अस्, m. flour-<BR>like diabetes.<BR>—पिष्टमेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering<BR>from flour-like diabetes.<BR>—पिष्ट-रस, अस्, m. water<BR>mixed with flour.<BR>—पिष्ट-वर्ति, a small cake made<BR>of the meal of barley, rice, or pulse.<BR>—पिष्ट-<BR>सौरभ, अम्, n. (pulverized) sandal-wood.<BR>—पिष्-<BR>टाद (˚ट-अद), अस्, आ, अम्, feeding on meal.<BR>—पिष्टोदक (˚ट-उद्˚), अम्, n. water mixed with<BR>flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टक|पिष्टकं|पिष्टकः
पिष्टक, अस्, m. a cake made of the flour or<BR>meal of any grain, any baked cake, bread; a disease<BR>of the eyes, opacity of the cornea; (इका), f. a kind<BR>of grits, the meal of pulse steeped in water and<BR>peeled and ground; (अम्), n. pounded sesamum<BR>seeds, oil-cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टात|पिष्टातः
पिष्टात, अस्, m. perfumed powder (for scenting<BR>rooms, garments, &c.); scented dust which the<BR>Hindūs sprinkle over each other at the Holi or<BR>spring festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टिक|पिष्टिकं
पिष्टिक, अम्, n. a cake made of rice flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टोडी
पिष्टोडी, f. a species of shrub (= श्वेताम्लि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टप|पिष्टपं|पिष्टपः
पिष्टप पिष्टप, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>fr. पिश्, substituted for rt. विश्), a world, a division of<BR>the universe; [cf. विष्टप.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस्
पिस् पिस्, cl. 4. P. पिस्यति, पेसितुम्, Ved.<BR>to go; (perhaps) to extend; cl. 1. P.<BR>पेसति, पेसितुम्, to go, move; cl. 10. P. पेसयति,<BR>यितुम्, to go; to hurt, injure; to be strong; to<BR>give; to take; to dwell; [cf. rts. पेस्, विस्, वेस्,<BR>बिश्, बेश्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस्पृक्षु
पिस्पृक्षु पिस्पृक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. स्पृश्), being about to touch; (with जलम्) being<BR>about to enter the water, being about to perform<BR>ablutions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिहित|पिहितं
पिहित पि-हित. See p. 575, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पी
पी 1. पी (probably originally Pass. of rt.<BR>1. पा, q. v.), cl. 4. A. पीयते, पिप्ये, पेष्-<BR>यति, अपेष्ट, पेतुम्, to drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पी
पी 2. पी, ईस्, ईस्, इ (fr. rt. प्यै, q. v.; at the<BR>end of a comp.) becoming fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0576-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीच|पीचं
पीच पीच, अम्, n. the lower jaw, the chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीटिका
पीटिका पीटिका, a various reading for<BR>पीठिका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठ|पीठं
पीठ पीठ, अम्, n. (thought by some to be<BR>a Prākṛt form fr. पि-सद = पि-षद = पि-ष्ड or<BR>connected with rt. पिठ्), a stool, seat, chair, bench; a<BR>religious student's seat made properly of Kuśa grass;<BR>the seat of a deity, an altar (according to some<BR>native authorities in this and the preceding senses<BR>also अस्, ई, m. f.); a basis, basement, pedestal; an<BR>epithet of various temples (erected on the fifty-<BR>one spots on which, according to tradition, the<BR>various members of Pārvatī fell after she had been<BR>cut to pieces by the discus of Viṣṇu); a kind of orna-<BR>ment; a particular posture in sitting; (in geometry)<BR>the complement of a segment; N. of an Asura the<BR>minister of Kaṃsa.<BR>—पीठ-केलि, इस्, m. a particular<BR>dramatic character, a male confidant, a parasite.<BR>—पीठ-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, moving about in a wheel-<BR>chair, lame.<BR>—पीठ-गर्भ or पीठ-विवर, अस्,<BR>m. the cavity in the pedestal of an idol.<BR>—पीठ-<BR>चक्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), Ved. a chariot with<BR>a seat.<BR>—पीठ-नायिका, f. a girl of fourteen (before<BR>menstruation) who impersonates Durgā at the festival<BR>of that goddess.<BR>—पीठ-न्यास, अस्, m. epithet of a<BR>particular mystical ceremony.<BR>—पीठ-भू, ऊस्, f. a<BR>basis, basement.<BR>—पीठ-मर्द, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘rub-<BR>bing the seat,’ (perhaps) riding on horseback, a rider;<BR>exceedingly impudent; (अस्), m. the companion of a<BR>hero in great undertakings; a companion, parasite;<BR>a dancing-master who teaches courtezans.<BR>—पीठ-<BR>सर्प, अस्, आ, अम्, or पीठ-सर्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>moving about on a wheel-chair, lame, crippled, a<BR>cripple.<BR>—पीठ-स्थान, अम्, n. a place where one<BR>of the limbs of Pārvatī is supposed to have fallen and<BR>therefore consecrated to her worship; [cf. पीठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठक|पीठकं|पीठकः
पीठक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a seat, chair, bench; a<BR>saddle ?; (इका), f. a bench; a base, pedestal; a sec-<BR>tion, chapter (sometimes wrongly spelt पीटिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड्
पीड् पीड् (perhaps connected with rt.<BR>पिष्), cl. 1. A. पीडते, पीडितुम्, Ved. to<BR>be squeezed or pressed out (as Soma): Caus. or<BR>cl. 10. P. (ep. also A.) पीडयति (-ते), -यितुम्, to<BR>squeeze, pinch, press, oppress, compress, suppress<BR>(e. g. कालं कालेन पीडयन्, Manu. I. 51, pressing<BR>time against time, or suppressing one period by<BR>means of another, according to Kullūka = सृष्टि-<BR>कालम् प्रलय-कालेन नाशयन्); to overpower;<BR>to hurt, harm, injure, pain, vex, harass, annoy, tor-<BR>ment; to break, violate (an oath); to beleaguer (a<BR>city); to neglect, cause suffering by neglect; to<BR>remove; to cover; (in augury) to cover with any-<BR>thing inauspicious; (in astrology) to eclipse; to<BR>oppose, resist; to stir, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड
पीड, अस्, अम्, m. n., in तिल-प्˚, तृण-प्˚, q. v.<BR>—पीड-यन्त्र-गृह, अस्, m. a workhouse for<BR>criminals, house of correction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडक|पीडकः
पीडक, अस्, m. an oppressor; [cf. तालु-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडन|पीडनं
पीडन, अस्, आ, अम्, molesting, paining, disagree-<BR>able; (अम्), n. the act of pressing, squeezing, rub-<BR>bing; an instrument for pressing, press; oppressing,<BR>inflicting pain, paining, distressing; laying a country<BR>waste, devastation; (in astrology) the oppression or<BR>suppression of a planet &c., i. e. eclipse [cf. ग्रह-<BR>प्˚]; suppressing sounds, a fault in the pronunciation<BR>of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडनीय
पीडनीय or पीडयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be<BR>oppressed or molested, to be pained or harassed;<BR>used for pressing, serving for a press.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडयत्
पीडयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, squeezing, pressing; op-<BR>pressing, suppressing, harassing, paining; breaking,<BR>violating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडा
पीडा, f. pain, suffering, anguish, annoyance;<BR>damage, injury, wrong; infraction, violation [cf.<BR>धर्म-प्˚]; devastation, laying waste; restriction,<BR>limitation; the ‘pain or calamity’ of a planet,<BR>eclipse, occultation [cf. ग्रह-प्˚]; compassion, pity,<BR>charity; a chaplet, garland for the head; the Saral<BR>tree, Pinus Longifolia; a basket (= पिटक, पेटा,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">Page0577-b+ 80</a>]<BR>पेडा).<BR>—पीडा-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, pain-causing, giving<BR>pain, afflicting, tormenting.<BR>—पीडा-करण, अम्, n.<BR>the causing of pain, torturing, tormenting.<BR>—पीडा-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, (according to Malli-nātha) = विमर्द-<BR>भाज् = भङ्ग-वत्.<BR>—पीडा-स्थान, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>(in astrology) an unlucky position, inauspicious dis-<BR>tance (of a planet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाय
पीडाय, Nom. A. पीडायते, -यितुम्, to feel pain,<BR>experience a sense of uneasiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडित|पीडितं
पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, squeezed, pressed; rubbed,<BR>chafed; griped, wrung; oppressed, harassed, dis-<BR>tressed, pained, afflicted, suffering pain or distress,<BR>injured, impaired; violated, transgressed; destroyed,<BR>laid waste, devastated; eclipsed; bound, tied; (अम्),<BR>n. injuring, harming, harassing; a kind of coitus;<BR>(अम्), ind. closely.<BR>—पीडित-ता, f. or पीडित-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the being squeezed or pressed; the being<BR>afflicted or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड्यमान
पीड्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being squeezed or pressed;<BR>being pained or afflicted, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत|पीतं|पीतः
पीत 1. पीत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. पा), drunk,<BR>quaffed; drunk in, imbibed; soaked, steeped, satu-<BR>rated, filled with; (अम्), n. drinking.<BR>—पीत-तैल,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has drunk oil, filled with oil,<BR>= तैल-पीत; (आ), f. a species of creeper; a kind<BR>of heart-pea, Cardiospermum Halicacabum (= ज्यो-<BR>तिष्-मती, = महा-ज्योतिष्मती).<BR>—पीत-दुग्धा,<BR>f. a cow whose milk has been pledged (lit. already<BR>drunk); a cow tied up to be milked [cf. धे-<BR>नुष्या]; any milch cow.<BR>—पीत-निद्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>immersed in slumber.<BR>—पीत-प्रतिबद्ध-वत्स,<BR>आ, f. (a cow) whose calf has drunk milk and been<BR>tied up.<BR>—पीत-मद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>drunk wine or any other intoxicating liquor.<BR>—पीत-<BR>रस, अस्, आ, अम्, whose juice is drunk or quaffed.<BR>—पीत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having drunk or quaffed; con-<BR>taining the verb 1. पा (Ved.).<BR>—पीत-सोम, अस्, m.<BR>a Brāhman by whom the juice of the acid Asclepias<BR>is drunk at a ceremony.<BR>—पीताब्धि (˚त-अब्˚), इस्,<BR>m. an epithet of the Muni Agastya (‘by whom the<BR>ocean was drunk,’ this saint having on one occasion<BR>swallowed up the sea).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीति|पीतिः
1. पीति, इस्, f. (for 2. and 3. see p. 578, col. 1),<BR>drinking, a draught; a tavern, dram-shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतिन्
1. पीतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of comps.) drinking,<BR>having drunk. (For 2. पीतिन् see p. 578, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत्वा
पीत्वा, ind. having drunk or quaffed.<BR>—पीत्वा-<BR>स्थिरक, अस्, आ, अम्, somewhat refreshed by a<BR>draught (Gaṇa to Pāṇ. II. 1, 72).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथ|पीथं|पीथः
1. पीथ, अस्, m. (for 2. and 3. see p. 578, col. 1), a<BR>drink, draught [cf. गो-प्˚]; (अम्), n. water; melted<BR>butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथिन्
पीथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) drinking;<BR>कोश-प्˚, squandering away the treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयमान
पीयमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being drunk or quaffed,<BR>being drunk or sucked in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत|पीतं|पीतः
पीत 2. पीत, अस्, आ, अम् (probably connected<BR>with rt. प्यै, the colour of butter and oil being<BR>yellowish), of a yellow colour, yellow (the colour of<BR>the Vaiśyas, white being that of the Brāhmans, red<BR>that of the Kṣatriyas, and black that of the Śūdras);<BR>(अस्), m. yellow colour; a yellow gem, topaz; a<BR>yellow pigment prepared from the urine of kine;<BR>N. of several plants, Alangium Hexapetalum (=<BR>अङ्कोठ); safflower, Carthamus Tinctorius; Trophis<BR>Aspera (= शाखोट); (आ), f., N. of various plants,<BR>turmeric (= हरिद्रा); a medical plant, Betula,<BR>commonly called Atais; a kind of yellow pigment<BR>(= गो-रोचना); a mystical designation of the letter<BR>ष; (अम्), n. gold; yellow orpiment.<BR>—पीत-<BR>कदली, f. a species of banana (= स्वर्ण-कदली).<BR>—पीत-कन्द, अम्, n. the carrot, Daucus Carota.<BR>—पीत-करवीरक, अस्, m. oleander with yellow<BR>flowers.<BR>—पीत-कावेर, अम्, n. saffron; bell-metal.<BR>—पीत-काष्ठ, अम्, n. yellow sanders.<BR>—पीत-<BR>कीला, f. a species of plant (= आ-वर्तकी).<BR>—पीत-<BR>कौशेय-वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, dressed in yellow silk;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पीत-गन्ध,<BR>अम्, n. yellow sandal.<BR>—पीत-घोषा, f. yellow Gho-<BR>ṣā, a species of creeper with yellow flowers.<BR>—पीत-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-c" target="_blank">Page0577-c+ 81</a>]<BR>चन्दन, अम्, n. a yellow fragrant wood considered<BR>as a yellow species of sandal-wood; saffron; turmeric.<BR>—पीत-चम्पक, अस्, m. a lamp (‘yellow as the<BR>Campa’).<BR>—पीत-तण्डुला, f. millet, Panicum Itali-<BR>cum; a species of Solanum.<BR>—पीत-ता, f. or पीत-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. yellowness, yellow (the colour).<BR>—पीत-<BR>तुण्ड, अस्, m. ‘yellow-beak,’ N. of the Sylvia Sutoria<BR>(the whole bird being of a light yellow colour).<BR>—पी-<BR>त-दारु, उस्, m. a species of pine, Pinus Deodora (=<BR>देव-दारु); Pinus Longifolia; Curcuma Aromatica<BR>or Curcuma Xanthorrhiza (= हरिद्रु).<BR>—पीत-द्रु,<BR>उस्, m. a species of pine, Pinus Longifolia; Cur-<BR>cuma Aromatica or C. Xanthorrhiza.<BR>—पीत-नील,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘yellow-blue,’ green.<BR>—पीत-पर्णी, f.<BR>‘yellow-leaved,’ a plant commonly called Bichati;<BR>a N. of the nettle or a plant of the same<BR>class, Tragia Involucrata.<BR>—पीत-पादा, f. ‘yellow-<BR>footed,’ a small bird, the Maina (Turdus Salica).<BR>—पी-<BR>त-पुष्प, अस्, m., N. of several plants (= कर्णि-<BR>कार), Pterospermum Acerifolium, or a species of<BR>Karṇikāra; Michelia Champaka; a species of Taber-<BR>næmontana Coronaria; a species of Barleria with<BR>yellow flowers; (आ), f. a species of Coloquintida<BR>(= इन्द्र-वारुणी, = झिञ्झरिष्टा), Cajanus Indicus<BR>(= आढकी); a species of yellow Barleria; (ई), f.<BR>Andropogon Acicularis (= शङ्ख-पुष्पी, सह-<BR>देवी, महा-कोषातकी, and त्रपुषी); a species<BR>of Barleria with yellow flowers; (अम्), n. Tabernæ-<BR>montana Coronaria (= आहुल्य).<BR>—पीत-प्रसव,<BR>अस्, m. = पीत-करवीरक, q. v.<BR>—पीत-फल, अस्,<BR>m. a tree, Trophis Aspera; Averrhoa Carambola.<BR>—पीतफलक, अस्, m. Trophis Aspera.<BR>—पीत-<BR>बालुका, f. turmeric; yellow sand.<BR>—पीत-बीजा, f.<BR>Trigonella Fœnum Græcum (= मेथिका).<BR>—पीत-<BR>भृङ्ग-राज, अस्, m. a species of Verbesina with<BR>yellow flowers.<BR>—पीत-मणि, इस्, m. a yellow gem,<BR>a topaz.<BR>—पीत-मस्तक, अस्, m. ‘yellow-head,’ a<BR>small bird, Loxia Philippensis (= कलि-कार; cf.<BR>पीत-मुण्ड).<BR>—पीत-माक्षिक, अम्, n. = मा-<BR>क्षिक, a species of mineral substance.<BR>—पीत-माञ्-<BR>जिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, yellowish-red.<BR>—पीत-मुण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. ‘yellow-head,’ a bird (= कलि-कार), Loxia<BR>Philippensis; a kind of gallinule.<BR>—पीत-मुद्ग,<BR>अस्, m. a species of bean, a yellow variety of the<BR>Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>—पीत-मूलक, अम्, n. the carrot,<BR>Daucus Carota.<BR>—पीत-यूथी, f. yellow jasmine.<BR>—पीत-रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, yellowish-red, orange;<BR>(अम्), n. (or according to some अस् m.), a yellow-<BR>coloured gem, perhaps the topaz.<BR>—पीत-राग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, of a yellow colour; (अम्), n. (or according<BR>to some अस्, m.), a yellow colour; the fibres of the<BR>lotus; wax.<BR>—पीत-रोहिणी, f. the plant Gmelina<BR>Arborea.<BR>—पीत-लोह, अस्, m. yellow metal, queen's<BR>metal or a mixed metal resembling gold.<BR>—पीत-<BR>वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, dressed in yellow; (आस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—पीत-वृक्ष, अस्,<BR>m. a species of Śyonāka and Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—पीत-शाल or पीत-साल or पीत-सालक, अस्, m.<BR>the plant Terminalia Tomentosa.<BR>—पीत-सार, अस्,<BR>m. a yellow gem, a topaz; the sandal tree; the<BR>tree Alangium Hexapetalum; Citrus Medica; East-<BR>Indian incense, = तुरुष्क; (अम्), n. a yellow sandal-<BR>wood.<BR>—पीत-सारक, अस्, m. Alangium Hexapeta-<BR>lum; Azadirachta Indica.<BR>—पीत-सारि, इ, n. anti-<BR>mony.<BR>—पीत-स्कन्ध, अस्, m. ‘fat-shouldered,’ a<BR>hog.<BR>—पीत-स्फटिक, अस्, m. ‘yellow crystal,’ the<BR>topaz.<BR>—पीत-हरित, अस्, आ, अम्, yellowish-green.<BR>—पीताङ्ग (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a species of Śyonāka.<BR>—पीताम्बर (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dressed in<BR>yellow clothes, clad in yellow; (अस्), m. a N. of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; a dancer or actor; a religious<BR>mendicant wearing yellow garments; N. of a man.<BR>—पीतारुण (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, yellowish-red;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of the middle of day-break; [cf.<BR>ताम्रारुण, नीलारुण.]<BR>—पीताशमन् (˚त-अश्˚), आ,<BR>m. ‘yellow-stone,’ a topaz or any yellow gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतक|पीतकं|पीतकः
पीतक, अस्, इका, अम्, of a yellow colour, yellow;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of gentian, Gentiana Cherayta; the<BR>Tūn tree, Cedrela Toona; (इका), f. saffron; turmeric;<BR>yellow jasmine; (अम्), n. yellow orpiment; brass;<BR>honey; saffron; yellow sandal; aloe wood, Amyris<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">Page0578-a+ 74</a>]<BR>Agallocha; a species of Śyonāka; = पीत-शाल.<BR>—पीतक-द्रुम, अस्, m. Curcuma Xanthorrhiza<BR>(= हरि-द्रु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0577-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतन|पीतनं|पीतनः
पीतन, अस्, m. the hog-plum, Spondias Mangifera;<BR>a tree, Pentaptera Tomentosa; the waved-leaf fig-<BR>tree, Ficus Infectoria; (अम्), n. yellow orpiment;<BR>saffron; a species of pine (= देव-दारु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतनक|पीतनकः
पीतनक, अस्, m. the hog-plum, Spondias Man-<BR>gifera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतल|पीतलः
पीतल, अस्, आ, अम्, of a yellow colour; (अस्), m.<BR>yellow colour; (अम्), n. brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतलक|पीतलकं
पीतलक, अम्, n. brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीति|पीतिः
पीति 2. पीति, इस्, f. (fr. rt. 3. पा; for 1. see<BR>p. 577, col. 2), Ved. protection; [cf. नृ-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथ|पीथं|पीथः
2. पीथ, अस्, m. protection; [cf. गो-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथ्य
