पुर्य
पुर्य पुर्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 3. पुर्), Ved.<BR>being in a stronghold or fastness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्यष्ट
पुर्यष्ट पुर्य्-अष्ट or पुर्य्-अष्टक, अम्, n.<BR>the eight constituent parts of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्व्
पुर्व् पुर्व् [cf. rt. पॄ], cl. 1. P. पूर्वति,<BR>पूर्वितुम्, to fill; cl. 10. P. पूर्वयति<BR>or पूर्बयति, -यितुम्, to dwell or inhabit; to<BR>invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्
पुल् पुल् [cf. rt. पॄ], cl. 1. 6. 10. P.<BR>पोलति, पुलति, पोलयति, &c., to be<BR>great or large; to be lofty or high; to be piled or<BR>heaped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल, अस्, आ, अम्, extended, wide, vast, great,<BR>extensive; (अस्), m. erection of the hairs of the<BR>body (considered as a proof of exquisite delight);<BR>horripilation; N. of one of the attendants of Śiva;<BR>(आ), f. the soft palate or uvula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलक|पुलकं|पुलकः
पुलक, अस्, m. erection or bristling of the hairs<BR>of the body (considered by the Hindūs to be<BR>occasioned by delight or desire rather than by fear),<BR>a thrill of joy or of fear, horripilation; a species of<BR>edible plant; a kind of stone or gem; flaw or defect<BR>in a gem; any kind of insect or vermin infesting<BR>animals; a ball of bread and sweetmeats with which<BR>elephants are fed; yellow orpiment; a Gandharva or<BR>heavenly chorister; a wine-goblet or glass; a species<BR>of mustard; (अम्), n. a species of earth (= कङ्कु-<BR>ष्ठ).<BR>—पुलकाकुलाकृति (˚क-आक्˚, ˚ल-आक्˚), इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, ‘having the frame excited by horripilation,’<BR>thrilled with joy.<BR>—पुलकाङ्ग (˚क-अङ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the noose or cord of Varuṇa.<BR>—पुलकालय (˚क-<BR>आल्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of Kuvera.<BR>—पुलकी-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the hairs or down of the body<BR>erect, thrilled with delight.<BR>—पुलकीकृताङ्ग (˚त-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, whose body has its hairs erect,<BR>having the body thrilled with joy.<BR>—पुलकोद्गम<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">Page0586-c+ 77</a>]<BR>(˚क-उद्˚), अस्, m. erection of the hairs of the body<BR>(through rapture), horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकय
पुलकय, Nom. P. पुलकयति, -यितुम्, to have<BR>or feel the hairs of the body erect (with rapture or<BR>desire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकित
पुलकित, अस्, आ, अम्, having the hairs or down<BR>of the body erect or bristling up with joy, thrilled<BR>with joy, delighted, rejoiced, enraptured, joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकिन्
पुलकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the hairs or down of<BR>the body erect, thrilled, enraptured; (ई), m. a species<BR>of Kadamba tree (= धारा-कदम्ब).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्ति|पुलस्तिः
पुलस्ति, इस्, इस्, इ (perhaps fr. पुलस् for पुरस्,<BR>cf. पलस्ति fr. परस्, but said to be fr. पुल and rt.<BR>3. अस्), wearing the hair straight or plain; (gender<BR>doubtful), the hair of the head; (इस्), m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्त्य|पुलस्त्यः
पुलस्त्य, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. पुल्; per-<BR>haps fr. पुलस् for पुरस्), N. of an ancient<BR>Ṛṣi, one of the mind-born sons of Brahmā (Manu<BR>1. 35; also enumerated among the Prajā-patis and<BR>seven sages, and described as a lawgiver); an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—पुलस्त्य-स्मृति, इस्, f., N. of a work<BR>mentioned in the Śūdra-dharma-tattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलह|पुलहः
पुलह, अस्, m., N. of an ancient Ṛṣi, one of<BR>the mind-born sons of Brahmā enumerated among<BR>the Prajā-patis and the seven sages (Manu I. 35);<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाक|पुलाकं|पुलाकः
पुलाक, अस्, अम्, m. n. shrivelled or blighted or<BR>empty grain, bad grain; a small lump of rice rolled<BR>into a ball, a lump of boiled rice; (according to par-<BR>ticular medical authorities) rice-water; brevity, abbre-<BR>viation, abridgement, compendium; smallness, a<BR>little; celerity, dispatch.<BR>—पुलाक-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>making haste, hastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाकिन्
पुलाकिन्, ई, m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलानिका
पुलानिका, f. (perhaps) induration of the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलायित|पुलायितं
पुलायित, अम्, n. a horse's gallop; (a wrong<BR>reading for पलायित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन|पुलिनं|पुलिनः
पुलिन, अस्, अम्, m. n. a sandbank, land deposited<BR>by alluvium on the bank of a river; an island of<BR>alluvial formation or one from which the water has<BR>recently withdrawn, a small island or bank left in<BR>the middle of a river by the subsiding of its waters,<BR>an islet; a sandy beach; (according to a Scholiast)<BR>= तीर, the bank of a river; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>mythical being conquered by Garuḍa.<BR>—पुलिन-<BR>जघना, f. having sandbanks for hips (said of the<BR>Gambhīrā river personified as a female).<BR>—पुलिन-<BR>द्वीप-शोभित, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned with shoals and<BR>islands.<BR>—पुलिन-प्रदेश, अस्, m. island-site, situa-<BR>tion on an island.<BR>—पुलिन-मण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>adorned with sandbanks or islets.<BR>—पुलिन-वती, f.<BR>‘possessing sandbanks,’ (probably) N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन्द|पुलिंद|पुलिंदः|पुलिन्दः
पुलिन्द, आस्, m. pl., N. of a barbarous tribe;<BR>(अस्), m. a man of this tribe, a king of the Pulindas;<BR>a barbarian, savage, Mleccha, mountaineer, one who<BR>uses an uncultivated and unintelligible dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन्दक|पुलिंदक|पुलिंदकः|पुलिन्दकः
पुलिन्दक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a barbarous tribe;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a king of the Pulindas, Śavaras, and<BR>Bhillas; of a son of Ārdraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिक
पुलिक पुलिक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आ), f.<BR>yellowish alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिमत्|पुलिमन्त्
पुलिमत् पुलिमत्, आन्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिरिक|पुलिरिकः
पुलिरिक पुलिरिक, अस्, m. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिश|पुलिशः
पुलिश पुलिश, अस्, m. = Paulus (Alexan-<BR>drinus), N. of the author of a Siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलु
पुलु पुलु = पुरु (in particular comps.).<BR>—पुलु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having many de-<BR>sires, covetous (Sāy.) = बहुकामना-वत्.<BR>—पुल्व्-<BR>अघ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. doing much evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलुष
पुलुष पुलुष, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोम
पुलोम पुलोम, अस्, m. = पुलोमन्, q. v.;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a daughter of the demon Vaiśvānara,<BR>(she was loved by the demon Puloman, but became<BR>the wife of Bhṛgu or Kaśyapa); the plant Acorus<BR>Calamus (= वचा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमन्
पुलोमन्, आ, m., N. of a demon (the father-in-law<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">Page0587-a+ 76</a>]<BR>of Indra by whom he was destroyed).<BR>—पुलोम-जा,<BR>f. ‘daughter of Puloman,’ an epithet of the wife of<BR>Indra.<BR>—पुलोम-जित्, त्, or पुलोम-भिद्, त्, m.<BR>‘conquerer or destroyer of Puloman,’ an epithet of<BR>Indra (who destroyed his father-in-law Puloman in<BR>order to avert his imprecation consequent on the<BR>violation of his daughter).<BR>—पुलोम-द्विष्, ट्, or<BR>पुलोमारि (˚म-अरि), इस्, m. ‘foe of Puloman,’ an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>—पुलोमार्चिस् (˚म-अर्˚), इस्, m.<BR>‘having the lustre of Puloman,’ N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0586-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमत्|पुलोमन्त्
पुलोमत् पुलोमत्, आन्, m., N. of a prince;<BR>[cf. पुलिमत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमही
पुलोमही पुलोमही, f. opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्कस|पुल्कसः
पुल्कस पुल्कस, अस्, m., Ved. (according<BR>to the commentators) = पौल्कस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्ल
पुल्ल पुल्ल wrongly for फुल्ल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्लक
पुल्लक पुल्लक, अम् (?), n. = आश्चर्य, wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्
पुष् 1. पुष् (various reading for व्युष्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 4. P. पुष्यति, &c., to divide,<BR>distribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्
पुष् 2. पुष्, cl. 1. P. पोषति, पुपोष,<BR>पोषिष्यति, अपोषीत्, पोषितुम्, cl. 4. P.<BR>पुष्यति, &c., to be nourished, thrive, prosper, in-<BR>crease (intrans.); to share, divide; cl. 4. P. later also<BR>9. P. पुष्यति, पुष्णाति, &c., to nourish, nurture,<BR>cherish, foster, rear, bring up; to support, maintain,<BR>bear; to cause to thrive or prosper, cause to grow,<BR>unfold, develop; to increase (trans.), augment; to<BR>further, advance, promote, enhance, aggrandize; to<BR>magnify, exalt, extol; to increase in (with acc.),<BR>receive, get, possess, have, enjoy; to manage; to<BR>exhibit, show, display, evince, make to appear:<BR>Caus. पोषयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अपूपुषत्, to<BR>nourish, cherish, foster, rear, bring up; to cause to<BR>thrive or pros per, take care of, provide for; to cause<BR>to be fostered or brought up; to wear, put on:<BR>Desid. पुपोषिषति, पुपुषिषति, पुपुक्षति:<BR>Intens. पोपुष्यते, पोपोष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्
3. पुष् in विश्व-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष
पुष, अस्, आ, अम्, nourishing (in ग्रह-प्˚, q. v.);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a teacher of the Veda; (आ), f. a<BR>species of plant (= लाङ्गलिकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुषर्य
पुषर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. well-nourished, thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुषित|पुषितं
पुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, nourished, nurtured (=<BR>पुष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्क|पुष्कं
पुष्क, a word formed for the explanation of<BR>पुष्कल in Gaṇa to Pāṇ. V. 2, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कर|पुष्करं|पुष्करः
पुष्कर, अम्, n. (probably an anomalous form-<BR>ation fr. an unused पुष + कर), a blue lotus-<BR>flower; a lotus, Nelumbium Speciosum or Nymphæa<BR>Nelumbo, (in Mahā-bh. Udyoga-p. 1790, a meta-<BR>phorical expression for ‘the heart,’ or according to<BR>others for ‘error’); a species of medicinal plant,<BR>Costus Speciosus or Arabicus; the bowl of a spoon;<BR>the tip or extremity of an elephant's trunk; the skin<BR>of a drum or place where any musical instrument is<BR>struck; the blade of a sword; the sheath of a sword;<BR>an arrow; air, atmosphere, sky, heaven; water;<BR>N. of a celebrated place of pilgrimage (now called<BR>Pokur in the district of Ajmere, about five miles<BR>from the city of Ajmere, consisting of a small town<BR>on the bank of a lake, said to be one of the most<BR>sacred in India; in this sense also पुष्कराणि, n.<BR>pl.); a cage; union; a part; war, battle; intoxi-<BR>cation; the art of dancing; (अस्), m. a pond, tank,<BR>lake [cf. त्रि-प्˚]; a kind of drum, a kettle-drum; a<BR>kind of serpent; a species of crane, Ardea Sibirica;<BR>a kind of disease; the sun; (in astrology) an in-<BR>auspicious Yoga, an ill-omened combination of a<BR>lucky lunation with an unlucky day, three-fourths of<BR>a lunar mansion; the regent of Puṣkara-dvīpa; an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa; of Śiva; N. of a son of Varuṇa;<BR>of an Asura; of a Buddha; of a prince the brother<BR>of Nala; of a son of Bharata; of Su-nakṣatra; of a<BR>son of Vṛka and Dūrvākṣī; N. of a mountain in<BR>Puṣkara-dvīpa; (आस्), m. pl. epithet of a class of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-b" target="_blank">Page0587-b+ 81</a>]<BR>clouds said to occasion dearth or famine; of the<BR>inhabitants of Kuśa-dvīpa corresponding to Brāh-<BR>mans; (अस्, अम्), m. n., N. of one of the seven<BR>great Dvīpas or divisions of the universe; (with<BR>Jainas) N. of one of the five Bharatas; (ई), f., N.<BR>of one of the eight wives of Śiva.<BR>—पुष्कर-चूड,<BR>अस्, m. ‘lotus-crested,’ N. of one of the four elephants<BR>that support the earth.<BR>—पुष्कर-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—पुष्कर-द्वीप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Dvīpa or great division of the<BR>universe.<BR>—पुष्कर-नाभ, अस्, m. ‘lotus-naveled,’<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; [cf. पद्म-नाभ.]<BR>—पुष्-<BR>कर-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a lotus-leaf, leaf of a lotus.<BR>—पुष्करपत्त्र-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having eyes<BR>like lotus-leaves.<BR>—पुष्कर-पर्ण, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>a lotus-petal; an epithet of a kind of brick; (ई or<BR>इका), f. the plant Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>—पुष्कर-<BR>पुराण, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—पुष्कर-प्रिय,<BR>अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), wax.<BR>—पुष्कर-बीज, अम्,<BR>n. lotus-seed.<BR>—पुष्कर-मालिन्, ई, m. ‘wearing a<BR>lotus-wreath,’ N. of a man.<BR>—पुष्कर-माहात्म्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a chapter of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—पुष्कर-मूल, अम्, n. the plant Costus Speci-<BR>osus or Arabicus.<BR>—पुष्करमूलक, अम्, n. the<BR>root of Costus Speciosus or Arabicus.<BR>—पुष्कर-<BR>व्याघ्र, अस्, m. ‘water-tiger,’ an alligator.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>कर-शायिका, f. a species of aquatic bird.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>कर-शिका or (according to others) पुष्कर-शिफा,<BR>f. the root of the lotus.<BR>—पुष्कर-सद्, त्, m., N.<BR>of a man; (दस्), m. pl., N. of his descendants;<BR>(in derivatives both members of this comp. are<BR>Vṛddhied; cf. पौष्करसादि.)<BR>—पुष्कर-सा-<BR>गर, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the plant Costus<BR>Speciosus or Arabicus.<BR>—पुष्कर-साद, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a species of bird.<BR>—पुष्कर-सारिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a Brāhman.<BR>—पुष्कर-सारी, f. ‘having the<BR>essence of the lotus,’ a kind of writing (लिपि).<BR>—पुष्कर-स्थपति, इस्, m. ‘architect of the<BR>lotus,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पुष्कर-स्रज्, क्, f. a<BR>lotus-wreath, chaplet of lotuses; (जौ), m. du. an<BR>epithet of the two sons of Aśvinī and physicians of<BR>Svarga or paradise; (क्, क्, क्), wearing a garland of<BR>lotuses, crowned with lotuses.<BR>—पुष्कराक्ष (˚र-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, lotus-eyed; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; N. of a man; of a prince.<BR>—पुष्क-<BR>राख्य (˚र-आख्˚), अस्, m. the Indian crane, Ardea<BR>Sibirica.<BR>—पुष्कराङ्घ्रिज (˚र-अङ्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>plant Costus Speciosus or C. Arabicus.<BR>—पुष्करा-<BR>रण्य (˚र-अर्˚), अम्, n., N. of a forest in the east<BR>of Viśālā.<BR>—पुष्करारुणि (˚र-आर्˚), इस्, m., N. of<BR>a king.<BR>—पुष्करा-वती, f. ‘abounding in lotuses,’<BR>N. of a town (= the Πευκελαῶτις of the ancients<BR>and the Pousekielofati of Hiouen-Thsang); a form of<BR>Dākṣāyaṇī.<BR>—पुष्करावर्तक (˚र-आव्˚), आस्, m.<BR>pl. epithet of a particular class of clouds (also called<BR>पुष्कलावर्तकास्).<BR>—पुष्कराह्व (˚र-आह्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the Indian crane, Ardea Sibirica; the plant<BR>Costus Speciosus or Arabicus (also पुष्कराह्वय).<BR> — 1. पुष्करेक्षण (˚र-ईक्ष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘lotus-eyed,’ having eyes like the blue lotus.<BR>—२. पु-<BR>ष्करे-क्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, being for a moment in<BR>the sky.<BR>—पुष्करोद्धृत (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>raised with the extremity of the trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कराय
पुष्कराय, Nom. A. पुष्करायते, -यितुम्,<BR>to act as or represent a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करिका
पुष्करिका, f. a kind of disease, formation of<BR>abscesses on the penis; N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करिन्
पुष्करिन्, ई, इणी, इ, abounding in lotuses; (ई),<BR>m. an elephant; N. of a prince; (इणी), f. a female<BR>elephant; a lotus-pool, pool in general, piece of<BR>water, lake, artificial pond, square or large pond;<BR>the plant Costus Speciosus or Arabicus; the plant<BR>Hibiscus Mutabilis; N. of a river; of the wife of<BR>Bhumanyu; of the wife of Cākṣuṣa and mother<BR>of Manu; of the mother of Manu Cākṣuṣa; of<BR>the wife of Vyuṣṭa and mother of Cakṣus and<BR>grandmother of Manu; of the wife of Ulmuka; of<BR>a Buddhist temple in Maru or Marwar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कल|पुष्कलं|पुष्कलः
पुष्कल, अस्, आ, अम्, much, many, abundant;<BR>full, filled, complete; rich, sumptuous, splendid, mag-<BR>nificent; good, salutary, eminent, excellent, best;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">Page0587-c+ 81</a>]<BR>resonant, resounding, loud; near, approached; (अस्),<BR>m. a kind of drum; N. of a son of Varuṇa; epithet<BR>of Śiva; of an Asura; N. of a son of Bharata; of a<BR>Ṛṣi; of a Buddha; epithet of mount Meru; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of a people; N. of the military caste in<BR>Kuśa-dvīpa corresponding to the ancient Kṣatriyas;<BR>(ई), f., see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 41; (अम्), n. a<BR>particular measure of capacity (= 8 Kuñcis = 64<BR>handfuls; sometimes = four times a double handful);<BR>a particular weight of gold; alms to the extent of<BR>four mouthfuls of food; N. of a celebrated place of<BR>pilgrimage (= पुष्कर).<BR>—पुष्कल-मोचन,<BR>अम्, n., N. of the 78th chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa<BR>of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—पुष्कल-विजय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the 68th and 69th chapters of the Pātāla-<BR>khaṇḍa of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—पुष्कला-वती, f.<BR>= पुष्करा-वती, q. v.<BR>—पुष्कलावर्तक (˚ल-<BR>आव्˚), आस्, m. pl. epithet of a particular class of clouds<BR>(= पुष्करावर्तक, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कलक|पुष्कलकः
पुष्कलक, अस्, m. the musk-deer; a post,<BR>wedge, pin, bolt; a Buddhist mendicant; (sometimes<BR>wrongly spelt पुष्यलक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कलावत
पुष्कलावत, अस्, m. (probably a wrong form<BR>for पौष्कलावत), an inhabitant of Puṣkalā-<BR>vatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्ट|पुष्टं|पुष्टः
पुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, nourished, cherished, fed, well-<BR>fed; thriving, strong; tended, cared for; incubated,<BR>brooded over; abounding, abundant; rich, well-sup-<BR>plied, amply provided; eminent; full-sounding, loud;<BR>complete, perfect; burnt (for प्लुष्ट?); (अम्), n.,<BR>Ved. increase, acquisition, gain, wealth, property.<BR>—पुष्ट-ता, f. or पुष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>well-fed, a prosperous or thriving condition.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>ट-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the lord of prosperity or<BR>welfare.<BR>—पुष्ट-विपुष्टौ, m. du. the well-fed<BR>and the ill-fed.<BR>—पुष्टाङ्ग (˚ट-अङ्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>fat-limbed, fat in body, fattened, well-fed, fat.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>टार्थ (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a complete<BR>sense.<BR>—पुष्टा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. breeding or<BR>rearing (cattle; Sāy. = सम्भृत-घास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टि|पुष्टिः
पुष्टि, इस्, f. a well-nourished condition, fatness,<BR>plumpness; growth, increase, vegetation, advance,<BR>prosperity, thriving; comfort, wealth, means, pro-<BR>perty; cherishing, nourishing, nourishment, main-<BR>tenance, support; breeding, rearing (of cattle);<BR>Nourishment personified as a daughter of Dakṣa<BR>and wife of Dharma (also mother of Lobha, and one<BR>of the 16 Mātṛkās or divine mothers); a form of<BR>Dākṣāyaṇī; N. of a Kalā of Prakṛti and wife<BR>of Gaṇeśa; of a Kalā of the moon; of a daughter of<BR>Paurṇamāsa; of a plant, Physalis Flexuosa (= अश्व-<BR>गन्धा).<BR>—पुष्टि-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, nourish-<BR>ing, causing to thrive or grow.<BR>—पुष्टि-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. a religious ceremony performed for the attain-<BR>ment of prosperity.<BR>—पुष्टि-कान्त, अस्, m. ‘be-<BR>loved of Puṣṭi,’ an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—पुष्टि-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing for or desirous of pros-<BR>perity or welfare.<BR>—पुष्टि-गु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>man, said to be a Kāṇva and the reputed author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII. 51, 1.<BR>—पुष्टि-द, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, yielding or causing prosperity or welfare,<BR>nourishing, cherishing; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>Manes or deceased ancestors; (आ), f., N. of a plant<BR>(= वृद्धि); the plant Physalis Flexuosa.<BR>—पुष्टि-<BR>दावन्, आ, अरी, अ, yielding or causing prosperity or<BR>welfare, nourishing.<BR>—पुष्टि-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the<BR>lord of welfare or prosperity.<BR>—पुष्टि-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. thriving, abundant, prosperous, well off; con-<BR>taining the word पुष्टि or any other derivative of<BR>rt. 2. पुष्.<BR>—पुष्टि-मति, इस्, m. a N. of Agni;<BR>(incorrectly for पुष्टि-पति.)<BR>—पुष्टिम्-भर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. bringing prosperity, conveying<BR>nutriment; an epithet of Pūṣan.<BR>—पुष्टि-वर्-<BR>धन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. augmenting nourishment,<BR>causing to prosper, promoting welfare; (अस्), m.<BR>a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिक
पुष्टिक, अस्, m., N. of a poet; (आ), f. a bivalve<BR>shell, an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प, अम्, n. a flower, blossom; the menstrual<BR>flux; a disease of the eyes, specks on the eye, albugo;<BR>a topaz; (in dramatic language) gallantry, politeness,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0588-a" target="_blank">Page0588-a+ 81</a>]<BR>declaration of love; blossoming, blooming, expanding,<BR>expansion; the vehicle or car of Kuvera [cf. पुष्-<BR>पक]; a kind of perfume; N. of a Sāman; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a serpent-demon; of a son of Śliṣṭi; of<BR>a son of Śaṅkha; of a Bodhi-sattva (?); of a moun-<BR>tain; (आ), f. a N. of the town Campā (or the capital<BR>of Karṇa; it was in Aṅga and is identified with the<BR>modern Bhāgalpur).<BR>—पुष्प-करण्डक, अम्, n.<BR>‘flower-basket,’ N. of a grove in the vicinity of<BR>Avantī or Oujein sacred to Mahā-deva.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>करण्डिनी, f. a N. of Oujein.<BR>—पुष्प-कर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a flower (i. e. a flower-<BR>shaped mole or mark) in the ear (said of an animal).<BR>—पुष्प-कार, अस्, m. the author of the Puṣpa-<BR>sūtras.<BR>—पुष्प-काल, अस्, m. ‘flower-time,’ the<BR>spring; the time of the menses.<BR>—पुष्प-कासीस,<BR>अम्, n. green or black sulphate of iron.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>कीट, अस्, m. ‘flower-insect, a large black bee; an<BR>insect living in flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-केतन, अस्, m.<BR>‘characterized by flowers,’ the god of love.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>प-केतु, उस्, m. ‘characterized by flowers,’ an epithet<BR>of the god of love; N. of a Buddha; of a prince;<BR>calx of brass; vitriol used for collyrium.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>गण्डिका, f. contrary purpose or effort of man and<BR>woman.<BR>—पुष्प-गिरि, इस्, m. ‘flower-mountain,’<BR>N. of a fabulous mountain (the favourite resort of<BR>Varuṇa).<BR>—पुष्प-गृह, अम्, n. ‘flower-house,’<BR>a conservatory.<BR>—पुष्प-ग्रन्थन, अम्, n. weav-<BR>ing a wreath or garland of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-घा-<BR>तक, अस्, m. ‘having flowers for its destroyer,’ the<BR>bamboo (the stem of which is said to decay after the<BR>plant has flowered).<BR>—पुष्प-चय, अस्, m. a quan-<BR>tity of flowers; gathering flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-चाप,<BR>अस्, m. a bow of flowers, the bow of the god of<BR>love; ‘having a bow of flowers,’ an epithet of Kāma-<BR>deva the god of love.<BR>—पुष्प-चामर, अस्, m.<BR>‘having flowers for a chowrie,’ the plant Artemisia<BR>Indica; a fragrant plant, Pandanus Odoratissimus.<BR>—पुष्प-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, derived or coming from<BR>flowers (e. g. पुष्पजं रजः, dust derived from<BR>flowers, pollen); (अस्), m. the juice of flowers; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a river rising in the Vindhya mountains.<BR>—पुष्प-जाति, इस्, f. ‘flower-born,’ N. of a river<BR>rising in the Malaya mountains.<BR>—पुष्प-द, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, giving blossoms or flowers; (अस्), m. a tree.<BR>—पुष्प-दंष्ट्र, अस्, m. ‘having flowers for<BR>fangs,’ N. of a serpent-demon.<BR>—पुष्प-दन्त,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having flowers for teeth,’ N. of one of<BR>Śiva's attendants; of a Gandharva and author of the<BR>Mahimnaḥ Stavaḥ; of an attendant of Viṣṇu (who<BR>is described as fighting against the Asuras); (with<BR>Jainas) the ninth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī;<BR>N. of a Vidyā-dhara; of the elephant of the north-<BR>west quarter; of a serpent-demon; of the mountain<BR>Śatruñ-jaya; (औ), m. du. the sun and moon; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a Rākṣasī; (अम्), n., N. of a temple; of a<BR>palace; of a city gate (Hari-vaṃśa 6510).<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>दन्तक, अस्, m., N. of a Gandharva and author of the<BR>Mahimnaḥ Stavaḥ.<BR>—पुष्पदन्त-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—पुष्पदन्त-भिद्,<BR>त्, m. an epithet of Śiva; (perhaps wrongly for पूष-<BR>दन्त-भिद्, cf. पूष-दन्त-हर.)<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>दामन्, अ, n. a garland or chaplet of flowers; a kind of<BR>metre, four times ¯¯¯¯¯,˘˘˘˘˘˘¯,¯˘¯¯˘¯¯.<BR>—पुष्प-द्रव, अस्, m. the exudation or saccharine<BR>matter of flowers; an infusion of flowers, as rose-<BR>water &c.<BR>—पुष्प-द्रुम, अस्, m. a flowering<BR>tree, tree which bears flowers.<BR>—पुष्पद्रुम-<BR>कुसुमित-मुकुट, अस्, m. ‘having a flowery dia-<BR>dem like a tree in blossom,’ N. of a Gandharva-rāja.<BR>—पुष्प-ध, अस्, m. the offspring of an outcast<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—पुष्प-धनुस्, उस्, or पुष्प-धन्-<BR>वन्, आ, m. ‘arming his bow with flowers,’ an epithet<BR>of Kāma-deva the god of love.<BR>—पुष्प-धर,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bearing flowers or blossoms, flowering.<BR>—पुष्प-धारण, अस्, m. ‘flower-bearer,’ an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पुष्प-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘cha-<BR>racterized by flowers,’ the god of love.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>नाटक, a various reading for पुष्प-वटुक, q. v.<BR>—पुष्प-निकर, अस्, m. scattering or throwing<BR>flowers; a multitude of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-निक्ष,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0588-b" target="_blank">Page0588-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. ‘flower-kissing,’ a bee.<BR>—पुष्प-निर्यास<BR>or पुष्पनिर्यासक, अस्, m. exudation or juice of<BR>flowers, nectar of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-नेत्र, अम्, n.<BR>the tube of a flower; a kind of cane or bamboo (?).<BR>—पुष्पन्-धय, अस्, m. ‘flower-sucking,’ a bee.<BR>—पुष्प-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘feathered with flowers,’<BR>a kind of arrow.<BR>—पुष्प-पत्त्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, having<BR>flowers for arrows (an epithet of the bow of Kāma-<BR>deva).<BR>—पुष्प-पथ, अस्, m. ‘course of the<BR>menses,’ the vulva.<BR>—पुष्प-पाण्डु, उस्, m. a<BR>species of serpent.<BR>—पुष्प-पुट, अस्, m. the<BR>sheath or calyx of a flower; the hands arranged in<BR>the shape of the calyx of a flower.<BR>—पुष्प-पुर,<BR>अम्, n. the city Pāṭali-putra or Palibothra.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>प्रचय, अस्, m. plucking or gathering flowers;<BR>stealing flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-प्रचाय, अस्, m. pluck-<BR>ing or gathering flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-प्रचायिका, f.<BR>plucking or gathering flowers; तव पुष्पप्रचा-<BR>यिका, it is thy turn to gather flowers, Schol. to Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 2, 74.<BR>—पुष्प-प्रस्तार, अस्, m. a couch of<BR>flowers, flowery couch.<BR>—पुष्पप्रस्तार-शायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, reposing on a flowery couch.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>फल, अम्, n. flowers and fruits; (अस्), m. the<BR>elephant or wood-apple tree, Feronia Elephantum<BR>(= कपित्थ); a pumpkin-gourd, Benincasa Cerifera<BR>(= कुष्माण्ड).<BR>—पुष्पफल-द्रुम, आस्, m.<BR>pl. trees bearing blossom and fruit.<BR>—पुष्प-बलि,<BR>इस्, m. an offering or oblation of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>भङ्ग, अस्, m. a festoon of flowers; (according to<BR>a Scholiast) treading on flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-भ-<BR>द्रक, अम्, n. ‘beautiful with flowers,’ N. of a<BR>particular wood.<BR>—पुष्प-भद्रा, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—पुष्प-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, being or con-<BR>tained in flowers; (अस्), m. the nectar of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-भूषित, अम्, n. ‘adorned with flowers,’<BR>N. of a kind of Prakaraṇa, q. v.<BR>—पुष्प-भेरोत्स,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—पुष्प-मञ्जरिका, f. a<BR>blue lotus.<BR>—पुष्प-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or<BR>consisting of flowers, abounding in flowers, flowery.<BR>—पुष्प-माला, f. a garland of flowers; N. of a<BR>work by Candra-śekhara.<BR>—पुष्प-मास्, आस्, or<BR>पुष्प-मास, अस्, m. ‘flower-month,’ the spring.<BR>—पुष्प-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a king, (according<BR>to the Brāhmanical account, a general of the last<BR>Maurya dynasty and father of prince Agni-mitra;<BR>or according to Buddhists, a king, the successor of<BR>Puṣya-dharman); N. of another king.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>रक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, red as a flower; dyed red with<BR>vegetable colour, as safflower &c.; (अस्), m. the<BR>shrub Hibiscus Phœniceus (= सूर्यमणि-वृक्ष).<BR>—पुष्प-रजस्, अस्, n. ‘flower-dust,’ pollen, espe-<BR>cially saffron.<BR>—पुष्प-रथ, अस्, m. ‘flower-<BR>chariot,’ a car or carriage for travelling or for pleasure<BR>or any purpose except war.<BR>—पुष्प-रस, अस्, m.<BR>‘flower-juice,’ the nectar or honey of flowers.<BR>—पुष्परसाह्वय (˚स-आह्˚), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>the name flower-juice,’ honey, nectar.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>राग or पुष्प-राज, अस्, m. a topaz.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>रेणु, उस्, m. ‘flower-dust,’ the dust or farina of<BR>flowers, pollen.<BR>—पुष्प-रोचन, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Mesua Roxburghii.<BR>—पुष्प-लाव, अस्, m. a flower-<BR>gatherer, flower-seller, garland-maker; (ई), f. a<BR>female flower-gatherer.<BR>—पुष्प-लाविन्, ई, m. a<BR>flower-gatherer, garland-maker.<BR>—पुष्प-लिक्ष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘flower-licker,’ a bee.<BR>—पुष्प-लिपि, इस्, f.<BR>‘flower-writing,’ N. of a particular style of writing.<BR>—पुष्प-लिह्, ट्, m. ‘flower-licker,’ a large black<BR>bee.<BR>—पुष्प-वटुक, अस्, m. a courtier, gallant;<BR>(also read पुष्प-नाटक.) — 1. पुष्प-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having flowers, flowery, blooming, decorated<BR>with flowers; (आन्), m., N. of a Daitya; of a man;<BR>of a prince; of a mountain in Kuśa-dvīpa; (अन्तौ),<BR>m. du. the sun and moon [cf. पुष्प-दन्त];<BR>(अती), f. a menstruous woman; N. of a sacred<BR>bathing-place.<BR>—२. पुष्प-वत्, ind. like a flower.<BR>—पुष्प-वन, अम्, n. ‘flower-forest,’ N. of a<BR>forest.<BR>—पुष्प-वर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a mountain;<BR>(अम्), n. or पुष्प-वर्षण, अम्, n. ‘flower-rain,’<BR>a shower of flowers, flowers showered from heaven<BR>upon a hero or demigod or on any great occasion.<BR>—पुष्प-वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, raining or showering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0588-c" target="_blank">Page0588-c+ 81</a>]<BR>flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-वाटी or पुष्प-वाटिका, f. a<BR>flower garden.<BR>—पुष्प-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘having a<BR>flowery car,’ N. of a king of Puṣkara.<BR>—पुष्प-वा-<BR>हिनी, f. ‘carrying flowers,’ N. of a river.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>वृक्ष, अस्, m. a tree bearing blossoms.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>वृष्टि, इस्, f. ‘flower-rain,’ a shower of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-वेणी, f. a chaplet or garland of flowers;<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—पुष्प-शकटी, f. a heavenly voice,<BR>voice from heaven; raining flowers (?).<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>शकलिन्, ई, m. ‘having flower-like scales,’ a kind of<BR>serpent.<BR>—पुष्प-शय्या, f. a couch of flowers,<BR>flowery couch.<BR>—पुष्प-शर, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>flowers for arrows,’ Kāma-deva the god of love.<BR>—पुष्प-शरासन, अस्, m. ‘arming his bow with<BR>flowers,’ the god of love.<BR>—पुष्प-शून्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, destitute of blossoms, not bearing flowers,<BR>flowerless; (अस्), m. the tree Ficus Glomerata.<BR>—पुष्प-श्री, ईस्, f. abundance or beauty of flow-<BR>ers.<BR>—पुष्पश्री-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘filled with the<BR>beauty of flowers,’ N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—पुष्प-<BR>समय, अस्, m. ‘flower-season,’ the spring.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>प-साधारण, अस्, m. the common time for flowers,<BR>spring.<BR>—पुष्प-सायक, अस्, m. ‘having flowers<BR>for arrows,’ the god of love.<BR>—पुष्प-सार, अस्, m.<BR>the nectar or honey of flowers; (आ), f. basil (=<BR>तुलसी).<BR>—पुष्प-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra<BR>work ascribed to Gobhila.<BR>—पुष्प-सौरभा, f.<BR>the plant Methonica Superba (= कलि-कारी).<BR>—पुष्-<BR>प-स्नान, अम्, n. ‘bathing with flowers,’ a kind of<BR>inauguration.<BR>—पुष्प-स्वेद, अस्, m. the nectar or<BR>honey of flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, stealing<BR>or taking away flowers.<BR>—पुष्प-हास, अस्, m.<BR>‘smiling with flowers,’ a flower garden (?); an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; N. of a man; (आ), f. a woman during<BR>menstruation.<BR>—पुष्प-हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute<BR>of flowers or blossoms, flowerless, not flowering;<BR>(आ), f. the glomerous fig-tree, Ficus Glomerata; a<BR>woman past child-bearing, barren woman.<BR>—पुष्पा-<BR>कर (˚प-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, rich or abounding in<BR>flowers, flowery; पुष्पाकरो मासः, the flowery<BR>month, spring.<BR>—पुष्पाकर-देव, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a poet.<BR>—पुष्पागम (˚प-आग्˚), अस्, m. ‘flower-<BR>advent,’ the spring.<BR>—पुष्पाजीव (˚प-आज्˚), अस्, or<BR>पुष्पाजीविन् (˚प-आज्˚), ई, m. ‘living by flowers,’ a<BR>gardener, florist, garland-maker.<BR>—पुष्पाञ्जन<BR>(˚प-अञ्˚), अम्, n. calx of brass employed as a colly-<BR>rium.<BR>—पुष्पाञ्जलि (˚प-अञ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, presenting<BR>flowers or a nosegay in both hands opened and<BR>hollowed (= प्रसूनाञ्जलि).<BR>—पुष्पानन (˚प-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘flower-faced,’ N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>पापीड (˚प-आप्˚), अस्, m. a chaplet of flowers; N.<BR>of a Gandharva.<BR>—पुष्पाभिकीर्ण (˚प-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, strewed with flowers; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>serpent (‘having spots like flowers’).<BR>—पुष्पाभि-<BR>षेक (˚प-अभ्˚), अस्, m. = पुष्प-स्नान, q. v.<BR>—पुष्पाम्बुज (˚प-अम्˚), अस्, m. the sap of<BR>flowers.<BR>—पुष्पाम्भस् (˚प-अम्˚), अस्, n., N.<BR>of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—पुष्पायुध (˚प-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘flower-armed,’ the god of love.<BR>—पुष्पार्ण (˚प-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Vatsara and Svar-vīthi.<BR>—पुष्पावचय (˚प-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, m. gathering flowers.<BR>—पुष्पावचायिन् (˚प-<BR>अव्˚), ई, इनी, इ, gathering flowers, a flower-gatherer.<BR>—पुष्पा-वती, f., N. of a town.<BR>—पुष्पावलि-<BR>वनराजि-कुसुमिताभिज्ञ (˚प-आव्˚, ˚त-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘knowing the season of the flowering of the<BR>rows of flowers and of the paths of the forest,’ N. of<BR>a Buddha.<BR>—पुष्पासव (˚प-आस्˚), अस्, m. a de-<BR>coction of flowers; (अम्), n. honey.<BR>—पुष्पासार<BR>(˚प-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘flower-rain,’ a shower of flowers.<BR>—पुष्पास्त्र (˚प-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘having flowers<BR>for missiles,’ Kandarpa or Kāma-deva the god of<BR>love.<BR>—पुष्पाहर (˚प-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taking<BR>or plucking flowers.<BR>—पुष्पाह्वा (˚प-आह्˚), f. the<BR>plant Anethum Sowa (= शत-पुष्पा).<BR>—पुष्-<BR>पेषु (˚प-इषु), उस्, m. ‘flower-arrowed,’ the god<BR>of love.<BR>—पुष्पोत्कटा (˚प-उत्˚), f., N. of a Rā-<BR>kṣasī, the mother of Rāvaṇa and Kumbha-karṇa.<BR>—पुष्पोदका (˚प-उद्˚), f. ‘having flowers for<BR>water,’ N. of a river in the lower world.<BR>—पुष्-<BR>पोद्गम (˚प-उद्˚), अस्, m. the coming forth or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">Page0589-a+ 76</a>]<BR>appearance of flowers.<BR>—पुष्पोद्भव (˚प-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘flower-sprung,’ N. of a man.<BR>—पुष्पोद्यान<BR>(˚प-उद्˚), अम्, n. a flower garden.<BR>—पुष्पोप-<BR>जीविन् (˚प-उप्˚), ई, m. ‘living by flowers,’ a gar-<BR>dener, garland-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0587-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पक|पुष्पकं
पुष्पक, अस्, m. a kind of serpent; N. of a<BR>mountain; (इका), f. the tartar of the teeth; the<BR>mucus of the glans penis or urethra; (अम्), n. calx<BR>of brass, green vitriol; a sort of collyrium; a cup or<BR>vessel of iron; a bracelet; a bracelet of diamonds or<BR>jewels; a small earthen fire-place or furnace on<BR>wheels; a disease of the eyes, albugo, specks on the<BR>eye; N. of the self-moving aerial car of Kuvera<BR>(carried off by the demon Rāvaṇa and constantly<BR>used by him till he was slain by Rāma-candra, who<BR>then employed the car, which was of enormous<BR>dimensions, to transport himself and Sītā along with<BR>Lakṣmaṇa and all his allies back to Ayodhyā, see<BR>Rāmāyaṇa VI. 108, Raghu-vaṃśa XIII); N. of a<BR>forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पित|पुष्पितः
पुष्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, flowered, in flower or<BR>blossom, full of flowers, bearing flowers, blooming,<BR>in bloom; flowery, florid (e. g. पुष्पिता वाक्, a<BR>flowery speech, fine words without much sense);<BR>having marks that look like flowers, spotted, varie-<BR>gated; abounding, abounding in, rich in [cf. सु-<BR>वर्ण-प्˚]; completely manifested, fully developed;<BR>(आ), f. a menstruous woman; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>Buddha.<BR>—पुष्पित-पलाश-प्रतिम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>resembling a Butea Frondosa in flower.<BR>—पुष्पि-<BR>ताग्र (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, covered at the extre-<BR>mities with flowers or blossoms; (आ), f. a form of<BR>metre, a variety of the Aupacchandasika, consist-<BR>ing of four lines, alternately ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯¯,<BR>and ˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिन्
पुष्पिन्, ई, इणी, इ, flowery, bearing flowers,<BR>flowering, blossoming; abounding in flowers; (इणी),<BR>f. a woman during menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प्य
पुष्प्य, Nom. P. A. पुष्प्यति, -ते, &c., to<BR>bear flowers, flower, blossom, bloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्य|पुष्यः
पुष्य, अम्, n., Ved. the blossom (i. e. that<BR>which rises to the surface or the best part of any-<BR>thing; cf. Gr. ἄνθος; Lat. flos); the uppermost<BR>part, the foam or froth of a fluid, scum; (अस्), m. the<BR>Kali-yuga or fourth age; N. of the sixth (or in later<BR>times the eighth) Nakṣatra or lunar mansion, also<BR>called Tiṣya; the month Pauṣa; N. of a prince;<BR>of a Buddha; (आ), f. a species of plant; the asterism<BR>Puṣya.<BR>—पुष्य-धर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—पुष्य-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having Puṣya for a<BR>leader.<BR>—पुष्य-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a prince; (a<BR>various reading for पुष्प-मित्र.)<BR>—पुष्य-<BR>यशस्, आस्, m., N. of a man with the patronymic<BR>Audavraji.<BR>—पुष्य-योग, अस्, m. the conjunction<BR>of the moon with the asterism Puṣya, the time of<BR>the moon's entering the lunar mansion Puṣya.<BR>—पुष्य-रथ, अस्, m. a carriage for pleasure,<BR>any sort of car or carriage except a war-chariot;<BR>[cf. पुष्प-रथ.]<BR>—पुष्य-स्नान, अम्, n. or<BR>पुष्याभिषेक (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m. a ceremony of<BR>purification performed while the moon stands in<BR>the asterism Puṣya; [cf. पुष्प-स्नान, पुष्पा-<BR>भिषेक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कर|पुष्करं|पुष्करः
पुष्कर पुष्कर, पुष्कल. See under rt.<BR>2. पुष्, p. 587, cols. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कलेत्र
पुष्कलेत्र पुष्कलेत्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कश
पुष्कश पुष्कश and पुष्कस, various<BR>readings for पुक्कश, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलक|पुष्पलकः
पुष्पलक पुष्पलक, अस्, m. a post, pin,<BR>stake, peg, wedge; [cf. पुष्कलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पस
पुष्पस पुष्पस, अस्, m. the lungs; [cf.<BR>पुप्फुस, फुप्फुस.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाणनाड
पुष्पाणनाड पुष्पाणनाड, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Grāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यलक|पुष्यलकः
पुष्यलक पुष्यलक, अस्, m. the musk-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">Page0589-b+ 78</a>]<BR>deer; a post, pin, bolt, stake, peg, wedge; a naked<BR>mendicant; [cf. पुष्पलक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्
पुस् पुस्, cl. 10. P. पोसयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>discharge, emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त्
पुस्त् पुस्त् [cf. rt. बुस्त्], cl. 10. P. पुस्त-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to honour, respect; to dis-<BR>regard, to treat with disrespect; to bind; to smear (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त|पुस्तं
पुस्त पुस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, filled, covered (?);<BR>(अम्), n. smearing, anointing, plastering, painting;<BR>working in clay, modelling, anything made of metal<BR>or wood or clay; a book, manuscript (in this latter<BR>sense, according to some, also पुस्ती, f.).<BR>—पुस्त-<BR>कर्मन्, अ, n. using a mixture of earth with lime<BR>and cow-dung and water as a mortar or plaster,<BR>plastering, painting.<BR>—पुस्त-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>formed of metal or wood, wrought in clay, modelled.<BR>—पुस्त-वार्त्त, अस्, m., Ved. one who lives by<BR>books, one who makes books.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तक|पुस्तकं|पुस्तकः
पुस्तक, अस्, इका, अम्, m. f. n. (usually m. or n.),<BR>a manuscript, a book.<BR>—पुस्तकागार (˚क-आग्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘book-room,’ a library.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्फुस
पुस्फुस पुस्फुस, अस्, m. the lungs (=<BR>पुप्फुस, फुप्फुस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू 1. पू, cl. 9. P. A., 1. A. पुनाति, पुनीते,<BR>पवते (in Bhagaved-gītā X. 31, P.), पु-<BR>पाव, पुपुवे, पविष्यति, -ते, अपावीत्, अपविष्ट,<BR>पवितुम्, to make clean or pure, cleanse, purify,<BR>clarify, refine; to purge or cleanse from chaff,<BR>winnow; to expiate, atone for; to make clear or<BR>bright; to purify in passing or by pervading, to<BR>ventilate (as the wind); (metaphorically applied to<BR>mental operations), to sift, discriminate, discern,<BR>distinguish; to think out, contrive, invent, compose;<BR>= अभि-गम् (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>28, 4, where however, according to some, it may<BR>have the sense of ‘to scheme or plot’); (A.) to<BR>become clean or pure, to become clear, to flow or<BR>drop clearly (as Soma); to form a clear conception<BR>or distinct notion; cl. 4. A. (properly Pass.) पूयते,<BR>to grow or become pure, to be pure: Caus. पव-<BR>यति or पावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अपीपवत्, to cleanse,<BR>purify: Desid. पुपूषति, -ते, पिपविषते: Desid.<BR>of Caus. पिपावयिषति; [cf. Gr. ποινή, ἄ-ποινα,<BR>πῦρ, πυρ-ε-τό-ς, πυρ-ά, πυρ-σός, πυῤῥό-ς: Lat. pū-<BR>ru-s, pu-tu-s, puta-re, pœna, pûnio, pœnitet,<BR>perhaps pi-u-s, ex-pia-re, pia-culu-m, prū-na:<BR>Umbr. pir, ‘fire:’ Goth. fon = Old Germ. fuir =<BR>Angl. Sax. fyr = Mod. Germ. feuer = Eng. fire:<BR>Old Germ. bar, ‘pure:’ Lith. pûs-tas, ‘desert;’<BR>pus-tau, ‘I sharpen:’ Bohem. púr, ‘glowing<BR>ashes.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
2. पू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, cleansing, purifying, clarifying<BR>(at the end of comps.; cf. अन्न-पू, उद-पू, केत-<BR>पू, घृत-पू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत|पूतं|पूतः
1. पूत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see rt. पूय्, p. 590),<BR>made clean or pure, purified, pure, cleaned, cleansed,<BR>clean, washed; threshed, winnowed; expiated,<BR>atoned for; bright; contrived, invented, composed;<BR>guarded, defended ?; (अम्), n. truth, speaking truth;<BR>(अस्), m. a conch-shell; white Kuśa grass; the plant<BR>Flacourtia Sapida; (औ), m. du. the buttocks, (in<BR>this sense a wrong reading for पुत); (आ), f. an<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>—पूत-क्रता, f., N. of a woman;<BR>[cf. the two following words.]<BR>—पूतक्रतायी, f.<BR>the wife of Pūta-kratu; the wife of Indra.<BR>—पूत-<BR>क्रतु, उस्, m. ‘of clear intellect,’ N. of a man; an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>—पूत-गन्ध, अस्, m. a species<BR>of plant (= वर्वर).<BR>—पूत-तृण, अम्, n. white<BR>Kuśa grass; [cf. पुण्य-तृण.]<BR>—पूत-दक्ष,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘pure-willed, pure-minded,’ an<BR>epithet of the Ādityas and other gods; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a descendant of Aṅgiras, author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 83.<BR>—पूत-दक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्,<BR>Ved. ‘pure-minded,’ an epithet of the Ādityas.<BR>—पूत-द्रु, उस्, m. ‘pure tree,’ the tree Butea<BR>Frondosa (= पलाश, but possibly fr. 2. पूत).<BR>—पूत-धान्य, अम्, n. ‘winnowed grain,’ sesa-<BR>mum.<BR>—पूत-पाप, अस्, आ, अम्, or पूत-पाप्मन्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">Page0589-c+ 79</a>]<BR>आ, आ, अ, purified or freed from sin.<BR>—पूत-फल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘pure-fruited,’ the Jaka or bread-fruit tree,<BR>Artocarpus Integrifolia (= पनस).<BR>—पूत-बन्-<BR>धन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. attached to that which is<BR>pure (Sāy. = पूतं सूर्यम् अनुबध्नत्).<BR>—पूत-<BR>बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, of pure descent, of noble race;<BR>(Sāy. = पूत-स्तोत्र, accepting pious praise.)<BR>—पूत-<BR>भृत्, त्, m., Ved. a kind of vessel which receives<BR>the Soma juice after it has been strained.<BR>—पूत-<BR>मति, इस्, m. ‘pure-minded,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पूत-यवम्, ind. at the time of winnowing<BR>barley; [cf. पूयमान-यवम्.]<BR>—पूतात्म-ता, f.<BR>personal purity, purity of soul.<BR>—पूतात्मन् (˚त-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, pure-minded, personally pure; (आ),<BR>m. a pure or purified person, saint, ascetic; a man<BR>of a cleanly person, a man purified by ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूति|पूतिः
1. पूति, इस्, f. (for 2. see rt. पूय्, p. 590), purity,<BR>purification.<BR>—पूति-धान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. con-<BR>taining winnowed corn; (probably a wrong reading<BR>for पूत-धान्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्रिम
पूत्रिम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. purified, pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्वा
पूत्वा, ind. having purified, having bathed or<BR>washed one's self (= स्नात्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पून|पूनः
पून, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed (= वि-नष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूनि|पूनिः
पूनि, इस्, f. purifying, cleansing (?); [cf. 1. पूति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयमानयवम्
पूयमान-यवम्, ind. at the time of winnowing<BR>barley; [cf. पूत-यवम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू 3. पू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (fr. rt. 1. पा), drinking<BR>(in अग्रे-पू, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूग|पूगं|पूगः
पूग पूग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. पू;<BR>but cf. पुञ्ज), an association, union, assembly, cor-<BR>poration; a heap, quantity, multitude; disposition,<BR>property, nature; the Areca or betel-nut tree, Areca<BR>Catechu [cf. ताम्बूल]; the Jaka tree, Artocarpus<BR>Integrifolia; = छन्द or छन्दस्; (आस्), m. pl. a<BR>number of persons; (अम्), n. the Areca-nut, com-<BR>monly called betel-nut.<BR>—पूग-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>made into a heap or collection, assembled, collected,<BR>heaped.<BR>—पूग-पात्र, अम्, n. a betel-box (=<BR>फरुवक); a spitting-pot, spittoon (commonly<BR>called पिकादिनी).<BR>—पूग-पीठ, अम्, n. ‘betel-<BR>stool,’ a spitting-pot, spittoon (chewing the Pān<BR>producing an increased excretion of saliva).<BR>—पूग-<BR>पुष्पिका, f. betel-nut and flowers (presented to the<BR>principal guests at a marriage festival).<BR>—पूग-फल,<BR>अम्, n. the fruit of the Areca Catechu, the Areca-nut.<BR>—पूग-रोट, अस्, m. or पूग-रोटक, अस् or अम्,<BR>m. or n. (?), ‘resembling the Areca Catechu,’ the<BR>marshy date tree, Phœnix or Elate Paludosa (=<BR>हिन्ताल; also read पूग-वोट).<BR>—पूग-वैर,<BR>अम्, n. enmity against many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगतिथ
पूगतिथ, अस्, ई, अम्, see Pāṇ. V. 2, 52; [cf.<BR>गणतिथ, बहुतिथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूग्य
पूग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) be-<BR>longing to a multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्
पूज् पूज्, cl. 10. P. पूजयति (ep. also<BR>cl. 10. A. पूजयते, and cl. 1. P. पूजति),<BR>अपूपुजत्, पूजयितुम्, to adore, honour, revere,<BR>reverence, worship, respect, receive with honour, re-<BR>ceive hospitably; to take notice of, regard; to honour<BR>with, present with (e. g. रत्नैः पूजयेद् एनम्,<BR>he should honour him with a present of gems).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजक|पूजकः
पूजक, अस्, इका, अम्, honouring, worshipping,<BR>respecting, a worshipper (often used in comps.; cf.<BR>देव-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजत्
पूजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, reverencing, honouring; wor-<BR>shipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजन|पूजनं
पूजन, अम्, n. reverencing, honouring; wor-<BR>shipping, worship, respect; showing attention (to a<BR>visitor), treating with respect or hospitality; an object<BR>of reverence; (ई), f., N. of a female bird a friend of<BR>king Brahma-datta; a hen-sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजनीय
पूजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be revered or honoured,<BR>entitled to homage; venerable, honourable; to be<BR>worshipped, adorable; (आ), f., N. of a female bird<BR>a friend of king Brahma-datta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयान
पूजयान, अस्, आ, अम्, honouring, reverencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितव्य
पूजयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured or wor-<BR>shipped, deserving honour or worship, venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0589-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितृ
पूजयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, honouring, worshipping,<BR>a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयित्वा
पूजयित्वा, ind. having honoured or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजा
पूजा, f. honour, worship, respect, culture, rever-<BR>ence, veneration, homage to superiors or adoration<BR>of the gods.<BR>—पूजा-खण्ड, N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—पूजा-प्रदीप, अस्, m. ‘lamp of worship,’ N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—पूजार्ह (˚जा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy<BR>of reverence or honour, worshipful, venerable, re-<BR>spectable, sacred.<BR>—पूजा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, enjoying<BR>honour or distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजित|पूजितः
पूजित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured, respected, rever-<BR>enced; worshipped, adored; frequented; recom-<BR>mended; acknowledged; endowed.<BR>—पूजित-पू-<BR>जक, अस्, इका, अम्, honouring the honoured or what<BR>is honoured (by others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजिल|पूजिलः
पूजिल, अस्, आ, अम्, venerable, respectable, wor-<BR>shipful; (अस्), m. a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्य|पूज्यः
पूज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured, honourable,<BR>respectable, venerable; fit for or deserving adoration,<BR>worshipful; (अस्), m. a father-in-law.<BR>—पूज्य-ता, f.<BR>or पूज्य-त्व, अम्, n. venerableness, honourableness,<BR>the being entitled to honour.<BR>—पूज्य-पूजा, f.<BR>honouring those worthy of honour.<BR>—पूज्यपूजा-<BR>व्यतिक्रम, अस्, m. neglecting to honour those<BR>worthy of honour,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्यमान
पूज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being honoured or re-<BR>spected; being adored or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूण्
पूण् पूण् [cf. rt. पूल्], cl. 10. P. पूण-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to collect or heap together,<BR>accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्
पूत् पूत्, ind. an onomatopoetic word ex-<BR>pressive of blowing or hard breathing, a puff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्कृ
पूत्-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>blow, puff, breathe hard; to recover breath.<BR>—पूत्-<BR>कर्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to blow or breathe.<BR>—पूत्-कारी, f. a N. of Sarasvatī; of the capital of<BR>the Nāgas or serpent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत|पूतं|पूतः
पूत पूत, पूति. See p. 589 and col. 2. of this p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतना
पूतना पूतना, f., N. of a female demon<BR>(said to cause a particular disease in children; she<BR>was sent by Kaṃsa to destroy the infant Kṛṣṇa,<BR>and having assumed a pleasing form [according to<BR>Hari-vaṃśa 3423, Śakunī-veśa-dhāriṇī] appeared to<BR>the child and offered him her poisoned breast to<BR>suck, which he seized and held till he had sucked<BR>away her life; she is enumerated among the Mātṛs<BR>attending upon Skanda, and associated with Śakuni<BR>as a daughter of Bali; cf. अन्ध-प्˚, अहि-प्˚, कट-<BR>प्˚, गन्ध-प्˚); a kind of disease, atrophy and<BR>wasting in a child (ascribed to the demon Pūtanā);<BR>yellow myrobalan, Terminalia Chebula or Citrina<BR>(= हरीतकी); a species of Valeriana (= गन्ध-<BR>मांसी).<BR>—पूतना-मोक्षण-प्रस्ताव, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—पूतनारि (˚ना-अरि˚), इस्, m. ‘enemy of Pūtanā,’<BR>an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पूतना-सूदन, अस्, m.<BR>‘destroyer of Pūtanā,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पू-<BR>तना-हन्, आ, m. ‘slayer of Pūtanā,’ an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनिका
पूतनिका, f., N. of a female demon (= पूतना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतुदारु
पूतुदारु पूतु-दारु, उस्, m. the tree Butea<BR>Frondosa (= पलाश; cf. पूत-द्रु, p. 589).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतुद्रु
पूतुद्रु पूतु-द्रु, उस्, m. a species of tree, =<BR>पीतु-दारु = खदिर or according to others देव-<BR>दारु; (उ), n. the fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूथिका
पूथिका पूथिका, f. a species of culinary<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूप|पूपः
पूप पूप, अस्, m. a cake, a sort of bread;<BR>[cf. अपूप.]<BR>—पूप-शाला, f. a cake room, baker's<BR>shop (according to Kullūka = अपूप-विक्रय-वेश्-<BR>मन्).<BR>—पूपाष्टका (˚प-अष्˚), f. the eighth day<BR>of the wane of the moon after the day Āgrahāyaṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपला
पूपला or पूपलिका or पूपली, f. a kind of<BR>sweet cake fried with ghee or oil, a rich cake of<BR>wheaten flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपालिक
पूपालिक, अस्, आ, m. f. a cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपाली
पूपाली, f. a sort of cake or biscuit made of meal<BR>or barley half baked or fried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपिका
पूपिका, f. a sort of cake half baked or fried in<BR>oil or ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपीय
पूपीय or पूप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ.<BR>V. 1, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय्
पूय् पूय्, cl. 1. P. A. पूयति, -ते, पुपूय,<BR>-ये, पूयिष्यति, -ते, पूयितुम्, Ved. to<BR>become foul or putrid, to putrefy, stink; to be dis-<BR>solved; to split or cleave (?); [cf. Zend pū, ‘to<BR>stink;’ pui-ti, ‘putridness:’ Gr. πύ-θ-ω, πΰθ-ο-μαι,<BR>πυθ-ε-δών, Πυθ-ώ, Πύθων, πύ-ο-ν, πυέ-ω, πῦος:<BR>Lat. pūs, pus-cīnu-s, pur-u-lentu-s, put-eo, puter,<BR>put-i-du-s, pud-ere: Goth. ful-s, ‘foul:’ Old Norse<BR>fūi, ‘putridness;’ fūk-i, ‘a stench:’ Angl. Sax.<BR>fūl = Eng. foul = Mod. Germ. faul: Lith. pú-ti,<BR>‘to putrefy;’ pú-d-au, ‘I cause to putrefy;’ pú-lei,<BR>‘pus:’ Hib. putar, ‘putrid, stinking.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत|पूतं|पूतः
2. पूत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see rt. 1. पू, p. 589),<BR>putrid, foul-smelling, ill-smelling, fetid, stinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूति|पूतिः
2. पूति, इस्, इस्, इ (for 1. see rt. 1. पू, p. 589),<BR>putrid, foul-smelling, stinking, fetid, ill-smelling;<BR>(इस्), f. a stench, stink, fetor; putrefaction; (इ), n.<BR>filthy water, suds; ichor, pus, matter; the substance<BR>called civet; a species of grass, = रोहिष; (इ), ind.<BR>an expression of censure or blame (after a verb, see<BR>Scholiast on Pāṇ. VIII. 1, 69).<BR>—पूति-करज or<BR>पूति-करञ्ज, अस्, m. a species of shrub, Guilandina<BR>Bonducella.<BR>—पूति-कर्ण or पूतिकर्णक, अस्, m.<BR>or पूतिकर्ण-ता, f. a disease of the ear accompanied<BR>with a discharge of putrid matter.<BR>—पूति-काष्ठ<BR>or पूतिकाष्ठक, अम्, n. a species of pine, Pinus<BR>Deodora (= देव-दारु); Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—पूति-<BR>कीट, अस्, m. ‘stinking insect,’ a species of insect.<BR>—पूति-गन्ध, अस्, m. a fetid odour, stench, fetor;<BR>sulphur; the plant Terminalia Catappa, = इङ्गुदी;<BR>(अम्), n. tin; sulphur; (अस्, आ, अम्), having an<BR>offensive smell, fetid, foul-smelling, stinking.<BR>—पूति-<BR>गन्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, ill-smelling, having an offensive<BR>smell, fetid, stinking.<BR>—पूति-गन्धिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having an offensive smell, stinking, fetid; (आ), f. the<BR>plant Serratula Anthelminthica (= वाकुची).<BR>—पूति-<BR>घास, अस्, m. ‘eating putrid food,’ a species of<BR>animal living in trees.<BR>—पूति-तैला, f. ‘containing<BR>ill-scented oil,’ heart-pea, Cardiospermum Halica-<BR>cabum.<BR>—पूति-त्व, अम्, n. putrid state, stinking.<BR>—पूति-नस्य, अम्, n. ‘fetid exhalation from the<BR>nostrils,’ a kind of disease of the nose attended with<BR>offensive breath; (sometimes wrongly spelt पूत-<BR>नस्य.)<BR>—पूति-नासा-गद, अस्, m. ‘fetid disease of<BR>the nose,’ a kind of disease in the nose attended<BR>with offensive breath.<BR>—पूति-नासिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a fetid nose.<BR>—पूति-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>ill-smelling leaves,’ a species of plant, a variety of the<BR>Śyonāka.<BR>—पूति-पुष्पिका, f. ‘having ill-smelling<BR>blossoms,’ a variety of the common citron (Citrus<BR>Medica).<BR>—पूति-फल, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing ill-<BR>smelling fruit; (आ or ई), f. a species of medicinal<BR>plant, Serratula Anthelminthica.<BR>—पूति-मयूरिका,<BR>f. a species of plant (= अज-गन्धा).<BR>—पूति-मांस,<BR>अम्, n. dead or decayed flesh.<BR>—पूति-माष, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—पूति-मुक्त, अस् or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), evacuation by stool.<BR>—पूति-मृत्तिक, अस्, m.<BR>‘having fetid or stinking soil,’ N. of a hell.<BR>—पूति-<BR>मेद, अस्, m. Vachellia Farnesiana (= अरि-मेद).<BR>—पूति-रज्जु, उस्, f., Ved. (probably) a species of<BR>plant.<BR>—पूति-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘fetid-mouthed,’<BR>having offensive breath.<BR>—पूतिवक्त्र-ता, f. the hav-<BR>ing a fetid mouth or offensive breath.<BR>—पूति-वात,<BR>अस्, m. foul air, a fart; the plant Ægle Marmelos.<BR>—पूति-वृक्ष, अस्, m. ‘ill-scented tree,’ Calosan-<BR>thes Indica.<BR>—पूति-व्रण, अम्, n. a foul ulcer.<BR>—पूति-शारिजा, f. a polecat, civet-cat.<BR>—पूति-सृञ्-<BR>जय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (incorrectly spelt<BR>पुती-सृञ्जय.)<BR>—पूती-करज and पूती-करञ्ज<BR>= पूति-करज, q. v.<BR>—पूत्य्-अण्ड, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>stinking eggs,’ an insect with a fetid smell, the flying<BR>bug; the musk-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिक|पूतिकं|पूतिकः
पूतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, foul, stinking, putrid; (अस्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">Page0590-c+ 80</a>]<BR>m. a species of plant serving as a substitute for the<BR>Soma plant, grey bonduc, Guilandina Bonducella,<BR>= पूति-करज; (आ), f. a species of pot-herb,<BR>Basella Lucida (= उपोदिका, पोतिका, पोतकी); a<BR>polecat, civet-cat, = मार्जारी; (अम्), n. ordure,<BR>excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतीक|पूतीकः
पूतीक, अस्, m. a species of plant serving as a<BR>substitute for the Soma plant, Guilandina Bonducella;<BR>the polecat, civet-cat; (आ), f. a pot-herb, Basella<BR>Rubra and Lucida.<BR>—पूतिका-मुख, अस्, m. a<BR>bivalve shell.<BR>—पूतिकेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚क-ईश्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha on the banks of the Revā or<BR>Narmadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय|पूयं|पूयः
पूय, अस्, अम्, m. n. pus, purulent matter, sup-<BR>puration, discharge from an ulcer or wound.<BR>—पूय-<BR>भुज्, क्, क्, क्, eating purulent carcasses.<BR>—पूय-<BR>रक्त, अस्, m., scil. रोग, ‘having purulent blood,’<BR>a kind of disease of the nose with discharge of puru-<BR>lent blood or sanies; (अम्), n. discharge of sanies<BR>from the nostrils; ichor, sanies.<BR>—पूय-वाह, अस्,<BR>m. ‘filthy-streamed,’ N. of a hell (in which filthy<BR>water flows).<BR>—पूय-शोणित, अम्, n. purulent blood,<BR>ichor, sanies.<BR>—पूयारि (˚य-अरि˚), इस्, m. ‘hostile<BR>to suppuration,’ the Nimb tree, Azadirachta Indica<BR>(the leaves of which are used to produce dis-<BR>persion or absorption of purulent matter).<BR>—पूया-<BR>लस (˚य-अल्˚), अस्, m. a particular disease of the<BR>juncture of the eye; suppuration at the joints, white<BR>swelling.<BR>—पूयोद (˚य-उद), अस्, m. ‘having<BR>stinking water,’ N. of a hell; [cf. पूय-वाह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयन|पूयनं
पूयन, अम्, n. pus, discharge from a wound<BR>or sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्
पूर् पूर्, cl. 10. P. पूरयति, -यितुम्, more<BR>properly regarded as a Caus. of rt. पॄ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर|पूरं|पूरः
पूर, अस्, आ, अम्, filling, making full (e. g. पाणि-<BR>पूरान्न, food that fills the hand, i. e. a handful of<BR>food); (अस्), m. filling, making full; satisfying,<BR>contenting, making content; the swelling or rising<BR>of a river or of the sea, flood, a large quantity of<BR>water, a piece of water, lake; (metaphorically) a<BR>stream, flood (as of tears or blood, cf. वाष्प-प्˚, रक्-<BR>ताम्बु-प्˚); a cake; drawing in breath slowly through<BR>the nose (as a religious exercise); the cleansing or<BR>healing of ulcers or wounds; the citron tree; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of incense, = दाहागुरु; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>m. f. n. a sort of unleavened cake fried with ghee<BR>or oil; [cf. वृक्षाम्ल, कर्ण-प्˚.]<BR>—पूर-कुम्-<BR>भक-रेचक, आस्, or आनि, m. or n. pl. (?), inhaling,<BR>suspending and exhaling the breath.<BR>—पूर-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filled.<BR>—पूराम्ल (˚र-अम्˚), अम्, n.<BR>= अम्ल-पूर or वृक्षाम्ल.<BR>—पूरोत्पीड (˚र-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, m. excess or superabundance of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरक|पूरकः
पूरक, अस्, आ, अम्, filling, completing, that<BR>which fills or completes; filling up; satisfying, mak-<BR>ing content; (अस्), m. (in arithmetic) the multiplier;<BR>a cake of meal offered at the conclusion of the<BR>funeral rites or oblations to the Manes; closing the<BR>right nostril and drawing up air through the left as<BR>a religious ceremonial; a citron, Citrus Medica (=<BR>वीज-पूर or वीज-पूरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरण|पूरणं|पूरणः
पूरण, अस्, ई, अम्, filling, filling up, completing;<BR>satisfying; drawing (a bow); (in gram.) an epithet<BR>of the ordinal numbers from द्वितीय upwards (so<BR>called as ‘filling out or completing’); (अस्), m. a<BR>dam, dike, causeway, bridge; the ocean; a medi-<BR>cinal oil or embrocation; N. of a man; a man with<BR>the patronymic Vaiśvāmitra, author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 160; (ई), f. an epithet of Durgā; the<BR>silk-cotton tree, Bombax Heptaphyllum; an ordinal<BR>number in the feminine gender; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>filling, filling out, filling up, completing or making<BR>up, supplying a deficiency; puffing or swelling up;<BR>(in medicine) injection of fluids; with धनुषः,<BR>filling out, i. e. drawing or bending a bow; furnishing,<BR>decorating with; fulfilling; multiplication (in arith-<BR>metic); rain, raining; a sort of cake; funeral<BR>cake; a species of fragrant grass, Cyperus Rotundus<BR>(= कुटन्नट); the cross threads in weaving<BR>cloth, warp; [cf. अ-प्˚, कर्ण-प्˚, निर्वाण-प्˚,<BR>&c.].<BR>—पूरण-काश्यप, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">Page0591-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—पूरण-प्रत्यय, अस्, m. (in gram.) an affix<BR>forming an ordinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0590-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरणीय
पूरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be filled up, to be com-<BR>pleted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयितव्य
पूरयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be filled or filled up;<BR>to be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयितृ
पूरयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who fills or fills up;<BR>one who fulfils or satisfies; (ता), m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयित्वा
पूरयित्वा, ind. having filled or completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरिक|पूरिकः
पूरिक, अस्, आ, m. f. a kind of pastry, a sort of<BR>unleavened cake fried with ghee or oil.<BR>—पूरिका-<BR>पूप (˚क-अप्˚), अस्, m. an unleavened cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरित|पूरितं
पूरित, अस्, आ, अम्, filled, full, complete; multi-<BR>plied; overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरिन्
पूरिन्, ई, इणि, इ, (at the end of a comp.) filling,<BR>making full, filling up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ण|पूर्णः
पूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, filled, full, filled with, full of<BR>(e. g. भाण्ड-पूर्णानि यानानि, waggons filled with<BR>goods; sometimes with inst. or with gen., e. g.<BR>वसुना पूर्णः, full of wealth; घट अपाम्<BR>पूर्णः, a pitcher full of water); fulfilled, finished,<BR>ended, accomplished; completed, complete, all, en-<BR>tire (e. g. दश पूर्णं शतानि, full ten hundred);<BR>past, elapsed; satisfied, contented; drawn, bent (as<BR>a bow); uttering the full and natural cry, full-<BR>sounding, sonorous (a term of augury applied to the<BR>cry of birds and sometimes to that of beasts; opposed<BR>to दीप्त, प्र-दीप्त, q. v.); strong, powerful, able;<BR>selfish, self-indulgent; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga; of a<BR>Deva-gandharva; of a Buddhist ascetic frequently<BR>called the son of Maitrāyaṇī; (आ), f. an epithet of<BR>the fifteenth Kalā of the moon; of the fifth, tenth,<BR>and fifteenth Tithis; N. of a woman; of a river;<BR>(अम्), n., Ved. fulness, plenty, abundance; water.<BR>—पूर्ण-कंस, अस्, m. a full cup.<BR>—पूर्ण-ककुद्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, ‘full-humped,’ hump-backed.<BR>—पूर्ण-काम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one whose wishes are fulfilled, satisfied,<BR>satiated.<BR>—पूर्णकाम-ता, f. contentment, satiety.<BR>—पूर्ण-कारण, अस्, आ, अम्, filling, satisfying.<BR>—पूर्ण-कुट or पूर्ण-कूट, अस्, m., Ved. epithet<BR>of a particular class of birds.<BR>—पूर्ण-कुम्भ, अस्,<BR>m. a full cup or jar; a water-vessel, one filled with<BR>holy water used at the consecration of a king; a<BR>particular mode of fighting; N. of a Dānava; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), having a full pitcher.<BR>—पूर्ण-कोशा, f.<BR>‘having a full pod,’ a species of plant.<BR>—पूर्ण-<BR>कोष्ठा, f. a species of Cyperus (= नागर-मुस्ता).<BR>—पूर्ण-गभस्ति, इस्, m., Ved. ‘having the arms<BR>full,’ an epithet of Savitṛ; (Sāy.) = सम्पूर्ण-ध-<BR>न-हस्त, whose hands are full of wealth.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>ण-गर्भा, f. pregnant, gravid, ready to bring<BR>forth.<BR>—पूर्ण-चन्द्र, अस्, m. the full moon; N.<BR>of a Bodhi-sattva; of an author.<BR>—पूर्णचन्द्र-<BR>निभ, अस्, आ, अम्, like or resembling the full moon.<BR>—पूर्णचन्द्रनिभानन (˚भ-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a face or countenance like the full moon.<BR>—पूर्णचन्द्र-प्रभा, f. the lustre of the full<BR>moon.<BR>—पूर्ण-ता, f. or पूर्ण-त्व, अम्, n. fulness.<BR>—पूर्ण-तूण, अस्, आ, अम्, full-quivered, having<BR>the quiver full.<BR>—पूर्ण-दर्व, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>ceremony with the full ladle.<BR>—पूर्ण-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an author.<BR>—पूर्ण-पात्र, अस्, अम्, m.<BR>n. a full vessel or cup; as much as will fill a vessel,<BR>a cupful; a particular measure of capacity (properly<BR>256 handfuls of rice; it may also be composed of as<BR>much as will satisfy one great eater); a vessel full of<BR>rice presented at a sacrifice to the superintending and<BR>officiating priests; a box or basket filled with clothes<BR>and ornaments scrambled for by guests and relations<BR>at a festival or distributed as presents.<BR>—पूर्णपात्र-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of a Pūrṇa-pātra; पूर्-<BR>णपात्र-मयं वचः, talking about full vessels,<BR>i. e. a season of plenty.<BR>—पूर्ण-प्रज्ञ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author.<BR>—पूर्णप्रज्ञ-दर्शन, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a chapter of the Sarva-darśana-saṅgraha.<BR>—पूर्ण-भद्र, अस्, m. ‘completely happy,’ N.<BR>of a serpent-demon; of a man; of the father of the<BR>Yakṣa Hari-keśa.<BR>—पूर्ण-मा, f. (मा contracted<BR>fr. मास), the day or night of full moon; [cf. पूर्-<BR>णिमा.]<BR>—पूर्ण-मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">Page0591-b+ 81</a>]<BR>contented in mind, having the mind satisfied,<BR>satisfied.<BR>—पूर्ण-मास्, आस्, m., Ved. full moon.<BR>—पूर्ण-मास, अस्, m. full moon; a monthly<BR>sacrifice or ceremony performed on the day of full<BR>moon; Full Moon personified as a son of Dhātṛ and<BR>Anu-mati; (ई), f. the day or night of full moon.<BR>—पूर्ण-मुख, अस्, m. ‘full-faced,’ N. of a ser-<BR>pent-demon.<BR>—पूर्ण-योग, अस्, m. a particular<BR>mode of fighting.<BR>—पूर्ण-वन्धुर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having the chariot-seat filled; (Sāy.) = धनैः<BR>पूरितेन रथेन युक्तः.<BR>—पूर्ण-वपुस्, उस्,<BR>उस्, उस्, ‘full-bodied,’ corpulent; (with निशा-कर)<BR>the full moon.<BR>—पूर्ण-वर्मन्, आ, m. ‘completely<BR>mail-clad,’ N. of a man.<BR>—पूर्ण-वीज, अस्, m. ‘full-<BR>kerneled,’ a citron.<BR>—पूर्ण-वैनाशिक, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Buddhists (as maintaining the doc-<BR>trine of absolute annihilation, = सर्व-वैनाशिक).<BR>—पूर्ण-श्रुति, इस्, इस्, इ, having the ears filled.<BR>—पूर्ण-समय, अस्, m., N. of a Kṣapaṇaka<BR>who identified time with the Supreme Being.<BR>—पूर्ण-सौगन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—पूर्ण-होम, अस्, m. = पूर्णाहुति, q. v.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>णाङ्क (˚ण-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘a full figure or number,’<BR>an integer.<BR>—पूर्णाङ्क-गणित, अम्, n. arithmetic<BR>of integers.<BR>—पूर्णाङ्गद (˚ण-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a serpent-demon.<BR>—पूर्णाञ्जलि (˚ण-अञ्˚), इस्, m., Ved.<BR>'full अञ्जलि,’ two handfuls.<BR>—पूर्णानक (˚ण-आन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. ‘full drum,’ a drum; the sound of a drum;<BR>clothes and garlands presented to friends at a feast (in<BR>this sense also spelt पूर्णालक; cf. पूर्ण-पात्र);<BR>a vessel; a moon-beam.<BR>—पूर्णा-नदी, f., N. of<BR>a sacred river.<BR>—पूर्णाभिलाष (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, whose wishes are fulfilled, satisfied, contented.<BR>—पूर्णामृता (˚ण-अम्˚), f. epithet of the six-<BR>teenth Kalā of the moon.<BR>—पूर्णायत (˚ण-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, completely bent (as a bow); a bow<BR>that is completely bent.<BR>—पूर्णायुस् (˚ण-आय्˚), उस्,<BR>m., N. of a Gandharva.<BR>—पूर्णार्थ (˚ण-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has attained his object or whose<BR>wishes have been realized.<BR>—पूर्णाशा (˚ण-आशा˚), f.,<BR>N. of a river.<BR>—पूर्णाहुति (˚ण-आह्˚), इस्, f., Ved.<BR>‘complete oblation,’ an offering made with a full<BR>ladle.<BR>—पूर्णाहुतिक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to<BR>an offering made with a full ladle.<BR>—पूर्णेन्दु<BR>(˚ण-इन्˚), उस्, m. the full moon.<BR>—पूर्णेन्दु-बिम्-<BR>बानन (˚ब-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a face like<BR>the disk of the full moon.<BR>—पूर्णेन्दु-वदन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a face like the full moon.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>णोत्कट (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—पूर्णोत्सङ्ग (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR>—पूर्णोदरा (˚ण-उद्˚), f. ‘full-bellied,’ N. of a<BR>deity.<BR>—पूर्णोपमा (˚ण-उप्˚), f. a complete com-<BR>parison (containing the four requisites, उपमान,<BR>उपमेय, साधारण-धर्म, and उपमा-वा-<BR>चक or सादृश्य-प्रतिपादक; opposed to लुप्-<BR>तोपमा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णक|पूर्णकः
पूर्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, filled, full; (अस्), m. a<BR>species of tree; the blue jay (= स्वर्ण-चूड); a<BR>cock; (इका), f. a species of bird described as having<BR>a double or cleft beak (also called नासा-छिन्नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णालक|पूर्णालकं
पूर्णालक, अम्, n. clothes and ornaments dis-<BR>tributed or scrambled for at a feast; [cf. पूर्णा-<BR>नक, पूर्ण-पात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णिमन्
पूर्णिमन्, आ, m., N. of a brother of Kaśyapa<BR>and son of Marīci and Kalā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णिमा
पूर्णिमा, f. (fr. पूर्णि for पूर्ण and मा a<BR>contraction of मास), the day or night of full moon.<BR>—पूर्णिमा-दिन, अम्, n. the day of full moon.<BR>—पूर्णिमान्त (˚मा-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of the<BR>day of full moon.<BR>—पूर्णिमा-रात्रि, इस्, f. the night<BR>of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णिमासी
पूर्णिमासी, f. (according to some) = पौर्ण-<BR>मासी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णीकृ
पूर्णी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त|पूर्त्त|पूर्त्तं|पूर्त्तः
पूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, filled, full, complete, completed,<BR>perfected; covered, concealed; (अम्), n. fulfilling,<BR>fulfilment; granting; the act of nourishing or<BR>cherishing; rewarding, a reward; merit; a merito-<BR>rious work, an act of pious liberality (as feeding a<BR>Brāhman, digging a well, planting a grove, building<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">Page0591-c+ 78</a>]<BR>a temple); nourishing, cherishing; N. of a work on<BR>the digging of wells &c. by Kamalākara; [cf. इष्टा-<BR>पूर्त.]<BR>—पूर्त-कमलाकर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work mentioned in the Śūdra-dharma-tattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ति|पूर्तिः|पूर्त्ति|पूर्त्तिः
पूर्ति, इस्, f. filling, fulfilling, accomplishing; ful-<BR>ness, completion, accomplishment; satiety, satisfac-<BR>tion; (Ved.) granting, rewarding, reward.<BR>—पूर्ति-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. desirous of a grant or<BR>reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्तिन्|पूर्त्तिन्
पूर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. possessing the merit of<BR>pious liberality [cf. पूर्त]; filling, completing;<BR>effective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्य|पूर्य्य
पूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be filled or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरु
पूरु पूरु, उस्, m., Ved. (connected with<BR>पुरुष, पूरुष), a man, people; N. of a tribe<BR>associated with the Yadus, Turvaśas, Druhyus; epi-<BR>thet of a class of demons; N. of an ancient prince<BR>the son of Yayāti and Śarmiṣṭhā; of a son of<BR>Manu and Naḍvalā; of a son of Jahnu; of a de-<BR>scendant of Atri and author of the hymns Ṛg-veda<BR>V. 16, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरुष|पूरुषः
पूरुष = पुरुष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्द्वार्
पूर्द्वार् पूर्-द्वार्, पूर्-द्वार, &c. See un-<BR>der 3. पुर्, p. 583, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्
पूर्व् पूर्व् or पूर्ब्. See rt. पुर्व्, p. 586.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व|पूर्वः|पूर्व्व|पूर्व्वः
पूर्व पूर्व or पूर्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, (connected<BR>with पुरा, पुरस्, but said to be fr. rt. पूर्व्;<BR>declined like a pronominal when implying relative<BR>position whether in place or time, see Pāṇ. I. 1, 34,<BR>but the nom. pl. may be either पूर्वे or पूर्वास्,<BR>the abl. sing. either पूर्वस्मात् or पूर्वात्, the loc.<BR>sing. either पूर्वस्मिन् or पूर्वे), being before or<BR>in front of, fore, first, foremost; eastern, easterly, to<BR>the east of; previous to, earlier than (with abl.);<BR>former, prior, anterior, preceding, antecedent (in<BR>these senses frequently at the end of a comp. and<BR>then translatable by ‘formerly,’ e. g. आढ्य-पूर्व,<BR>formerly wealthy; दर्शनीय-पूर्व, formerly<BR>handsome; often after a past pass. part., cf. अदृष्-<BR>ट-प्˚, कृत-प्˚, दृष्ट-प्˚); first (in a series),<BR>lowest, initial (opposed to उत्तर); ancient, cus-<BR>tomary, hitherto prevalent; foregoing, aforesaid,<BR>before-mentioned; preceded by, accompanied by,<BR>attended with (at the end of comps., cf. प्रीति-प्˚,<BR>बुद्धि-प्˚, मृदु-प्˚, स्मित-प्˚; often used ad-<BR>verbially with the termination of the neut., e. g.<BR>मति-पूर्वम्, knowingly, intentionally); full, all,<BR>entire (wrongly for पूर्ण); (अस्), m. an ancestor,<BR>forefather; N. of a prince; (आस्), m. pl. the ancients,<BR>ancestors; (आ), f., scil. दिश्, the east; epithet of a<BR>country to the east of Madhya-deśa; a collective<BR>epithet of the Nakṣatras Pūrva-phālgunī, Pūrvā-<BR>ṣāḍha, and Pūrva-bhadra-padā; (अम्), n. the fore<BR>part, a particular high number (applied to a period<BR>of years); N. of the most ancient of the Jaina<BR>writings (of which fourteen are enumerated); N. of<BR>a Tantra; an ancient tradition; (अम्), ind. before<BR>(with abl. or gen.), beforehand, formerly, hitherto,<BR>previously, antecedently (in these senses frequently<BR>at the beginning of a comp., cf. पूर्व-कारिन्,<BR>पूर्वोक्त); immemorially; अद्य पूर्वम्, until<BR>now, hitherto; पूर्वम् — ततस्, first — then; पूर्-<BR>वम् — पश्चात्, previously — afterwards; पूर्वम् —<BR>उपरि, previously — subsequently; पूर्वम् — अधु-<BR>ना or पूर्वम् — अद्य, formerly — now; (एण), ind.<BR>(opposed to अपरेण; with acc., gen., or abl.) in<BR>front, before; to the east, eastward of; ततः पूर्-<BR>वेण, to the east of that; [cf. Zend panurva;<BR>Slav. prŭvüj; Russ. pervyi, ‘first;’ Hib. foirfe,<BR>‘old, ancient, perfect, worthy.’]<BR>—पूर्व-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. a former work; preparation; actions done<BR>in a former state of being.<BR>—पूर्व-कल्प, अस्,<BR>m. the preceding or aforesaid manner; former<BR>times.<BR>—पूर्व-काम-कृत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. ful-<BR>filling former wishes.<BR>—पूर्व-काय, अस्, m. the fore<BR>part of the body (of animals); the upper part of the<BR>body (of men).<BR>—पूर्व-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, active at<BR>first.<BR>—पूर्व-काल, अस्, m. earlier time, former<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0592-a" target="_blank">Page0592-a+ 81</a>]<BR>times; (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to former times,<BR>spoken of or mentioned before.<BR>—पूर्वकाल-ता, f.<BR>priority in time.<BR>—पूर्वकालिक, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>पूर्वकालीन, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to former<BR>times, ancient.<BR>—पूर्व-काष्ठा, f. the eastern<BR>quarter, the east.<BR>—पूर्व-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. active<BR>from ancient times (according to Mahī-dhara = पूर्-<BR>वस्य कर्तृ).<BR>—पूर्व-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done<BR>formerly or in a prior existence, previous; (अम्), n.<BR>an action done in former times or in a former birth.<BR>—पूर्व-कृत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. acting before-<BR>hand.<BR>—पूर्व-कोटि = पूर्वान्त, (perhaps) the start-<BR>ing-point.<BR>—पूर्व-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going before,<BR>preceding; belonging to what precedes.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>गङ्गा, f. ‘eastern Gaṅgā,’ epithet of the Narmadā<BR>or Revā river.<BR>—पूर्व-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone be-<BR>fore, preceding; (अम्), n., N. of a Jaina work<BR>belonging to the Dṛṣṭi-vāda.<BR>—पूर्व-गत्वन्, आ,<BR>अरी, अ, Ved. going to meet; (Sāy.) = पुरतो गन्ता<BR>दूतः.<BR>—पूर्वङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, going before,<BR>preceding.<BR>—पूर्व-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. piling up first,<BR>preceding in piling up; (also incorrectly पूर्व-<BR>चित्त.)<BR>—पूर्व-चित्ति, इस्, f. (in the Ṛg-veda occur-<BR>ring only in the dat. perhaps in the sense of ‘before-<BR>hand, in advance’), Ved. foreboding, presentiment,<BR>(Sāy. = अन्येभ्यः पूर्वं लाभः, a first notion<BR>or conception ?); N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—पूर्व-चोदित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, formerly stated, before-mentioned, afore-<BR>said.<BR>—पूर्व-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, born or produced<BR>before or formerly, former, elder, first-born; ancient,<BR>primeval; produced by something antecedent, caused;<BR>born in the east, eastern; (अस्), m. an elder brother;<BR>the son of the elder wife, even though last born;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the deified progenitors of mankind;<BR>ancestors, forefathers in general.<BR>—पूर्व-जन, आस्,<BR>m. pl., Ved. men of former times.<BR>—पूर्वजन्म-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done in a former birth or previous<BR>state of existence.<BR>—पूर्व-जन्मन्, अ, n. a former<BR>birth, former state of existence or life; (आ), m. an elder<BR>brother.<BR>—पूर्वजन्मार्जित (˚म-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>acquired in some former state of existence (as merit<BR>&c.).<BR>—पूर्व-जाति, इस्, f. former birth, previous life<BR>or existence.<BR>—पूर्व-जावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. born<BR>or produced before.<BR>—पूर्व-जिन, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>ancient Jina,’ an epithet of Mañjū-śrī.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of a former life.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—पूर्व-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, earlier, previous, prior, anterior; (अम्), ind.<BR>before, first, previously.<BR>—पूर्व-तापनीय, अस् or<BR>अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of the first half of the Nṛsiṃha-<BR>tāpanīyopaniṣad; [cf. उत्तर-तापनीय.]<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. precedence, priority, a former state.<BR>—पूर्व-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, south-eastern.<BR>—पूर्व-दिक्-पति, इस्, or पूर्व-दिग्-ईश, अस्, m.<BR>‘regent of the eastern quarter,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—पूर्व-दिन, अम्, n. the earlier part of the day,<BR>forenoon.<BR>—पूर्व-दिश्, क्, f. the eastern region,<BR>east quarter.<BR>—पूर्वदिश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, situ-<BR>ated towards the east, bearing east; eastern.<BR>—पूर्व-दिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, determined by former<BR>actions; (अम्), n. the award of destiny.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>दुष्कृत-भोग, अस्, m. the pain or penalty conse-<BR>quent on sins committed in a former birth.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, formerly seen, seen before.<BR>—पूर्व-दृष्टि, इस्, f. a former view or sight.<BR>—पूर्व-देव, अस्, m. an ancient deity, primeval<BR>divinity; an Asura or demon (offspring of Kaśyapa<BR>the parent of both gods and demons); a Pitṛ or<BR>progenitor.<BR>—पूर्व-देवता, f. a primeval deity, a<BR>Pitṛ or progenitor of gods as well as men.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>देविका, f., N. of a Grāma in the eastern part of<BR>India.<BR>—पूर्व-देश, अस्, m. the eastern country or<BR>eastern part of India.<BR>—पूर्व-देह, अस्, m. a for-<BR>mer body, a former birth.<BR>—पूर्वदेहिक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, done in a former existence.<BR>—पूर्व-नडक,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. a hollow bone in the upper part (of<BR>the thigh).<BR>—पूर्व-निपात, अस्, m. (in gram.) the<BR>irregular priority of a word in a compound.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>निवास-ज्ञान, अम्, n. (with Buddhists) ‘knowledge<BR>of former habitations,’ knowledge of the past lives<BR>of all beings.<BR>—पूर्व-निवासानुस्मृति (˚स-अन्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0592-b" target="_blank">Page0592-b+ 81</a>]<BR>इस्, f. ‘recollection of former habitations,’ reminis-<BR>cence of former existence (one of the ten powers<BR>of a Buddha).<BR>—पूर्व-न्यास, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>grammatical work.<BR>—पूर्व-पक्ष, अस्, m. the fore<BR>part or side; the first half of a lunar month, the<BR>fortnight of the waxing moon; the first half of a year;<BR>an assertion, proposition; the first side or part of an<BR>argument, a primâ facie argument or assertion, the<BR>primâ facie view of a question; the first objection to<BR>an argument; the statement of the plaintiff; an<BR>action or suit at law.<BR>—पूर्वपक्ष-पाद, अस्, m.<BR>the first step of a legal process or lawsuit, the plaint.<BR>—पूर्वपक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who makes an<BR>assertion or proposition.<BR>—पूर्वपक्षीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, situated on the front side.<BR>—पूर्व-पञ्चाल,<BR>आस्, m. pl. the eastern Pañcālas.<BR>—पूर्व-पद, अम्,<BR>n. the first member of a compounded word or of a<BR>sentence or of a verse.<BR>—पूर्वपदिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to the first member of a compound term;<BR>reading or knowing the first member of a compound.<BR>—पूर्वपद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the first<BR>member of a compound term.<BR>—पूर्व-पर्वत,<BR>अस्, m. the eastern mountain from behind which the<BR>sun is supposed to rise.<BR>—पूर्व-पश्चान्-मुख,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, flowing to the east and west (as a<BR>river).<BR>—पूर्व-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. drinking<BR>first or before others.<BR>—पूर्वपाञ्चालक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम् (fr. पूर्व-पञ्चाल), belonging to the eastern<BR>Pāñcālas.<BR>—पूर्व-पाटलिपुत्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>in the eastern Pāṭali-putra (?).<BR>—पूर्व-पाणिनीय,<BR>आस्, m. pl. the disciples of Pāṇini living in the east;<BR>पूर्वपाणिनीयं शास्त्रम्, (probably) the gram-<BR>mar of the eastern disciples of Pāṇini.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>पाद, अस्, m. a forefoot.<BR>—पूर्व-पान or पूर्व-<BR>पाय्य, अम्, n. or पूर्व-पीति, इस्, f., Ved. prece-<BR>dence in drinking.<BR>—पूर्व-पालिन्, ई, m., N. of a<BR>prince.<BR>—पूर्व-पितामह, अस्, m. a forefather,<BR>ancestor.<BR>—पूर्व-पुरुष, अस्, m. ‘the primeval<BR>soul,’ an epithet of Brahmā; a forefather, ancestor.<BR>—पूर्व-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, each previous or pre-<BR>ceding one; (आस्), m. pl. forefathers, ancestors.<BR>—पूर्व-पेय, अम्, n., Ved. precedence in drink-<BR>ing; precedence.<BR>—पूर्व-प्रज्ञा, f., Ved. know-<BR>ledge of the past, remembrance, memory.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>प्रयोग, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—पूर्व-प्रवृत्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, formerly happened, done, fixed.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>प्रस्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone before, set out in<BR>advance.<BR>—पूर्व-फल्गुनी, f. ‘the first Phalgunī,’<BR>the eleventh Nakṣatra (figured by a couch and con-<BR>taining two stars, one of which is δ Leonis; cf.<BR>उत्तर-फल्गुनी).<BR>—पूर्वफल्गुनी-भव, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Bṛhas-pati or the planet Jupiter.<BR>—पूर्व-भद्र-पदा, आस्, f. pl. or पूर्व-भद्र-<BR>पद, अस्, m. = पूर्व-भाद्रपदा, q. v.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>भाग, अस्, m. the fore part; the upper part<BR>(opposed to अधो-भाग); दिन-पूर्वभाग, the<BR>earlier part of the day, forenoon, morning.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. receiving the first share, the<BR>first sharer; preferred, excellent.<BR>—पूर्व-भाद्र-<BR>पदा, f. the twenty-fifth Nakṣatra, the former of<BR>the two called Bhādrapadā, containing two stars.<BR>—पूर्व-भाव, अस्, m. the having existed formerly,<BR>previous existence; (in rhetoric) disclosing an inten-<BR>tion.<BR>—पूर्वभावि-त्व, अम्, n. the being previous<BR>to everything else, priority.<BR>—पूर्व-भाविन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, being anterior, preceding (everything else).<BR>—पूर्-<BR>व-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking first, addressing a<BR>person, condescending to speak first, polite, com-<BR>plaisant.<BR>—पूर्व-भुक्ति, इस्, f. prior possession.<BR>—पूर्व-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, existing previously,<BR>preceding.<BR>—पूर्व-मारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, dying before<BR>or first.<BR>—पूर्व-मीमांसा, f. an inquiry into the<BR>first or ritual portion of the Veda (hence sometimes<BR>also called कर्म-मीमांसा, as opposed to उत्तर-<BR>मीमांसा or ब्रह्म-मीमांसा, q. q. v. v., which is<BR>rather an exposition of the later portion of the Veda<BR>or Upaniṣads; the Pūrva-mīmāṃsā forms one of<BR>the six systems of philosophy and is attributed to<BR>Jaimini; it is really an interpretation of the text of<BR>the Veda, and is generally called the Mīmāṃsā, the<BR>term Vedānta being applied to the Uttara-mīmāṃsā;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0592-c" target="_blank">Page0592-c+ 81</a>]<BR>though scarcely a system of philosophy, yet in the<BR>course of its critical explanation of the Vedic text<BR>the Pūrva-mīmāṃsā discusses various philosophical<BR>questions, one of its speculations being the doctrine<BR>of the eternity of sound or of an eternal sound<BR>underlying all temporary sound and by some iden-<BR>tified with Brahma).<BR>—पूर्व-मीमांसार्थ-सङ्-<BR>ग्रह (˚सा-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of an introduction to<BR>the Mīmāṃsā by Laugākṣi Bhāskara.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>यक्ष, अस्, m. ‘the first Yakṣa,’ an epithet of<BR>Maṇi-bhadra, one of the Jinas or Jaina teachers.<BR>—पूर्व-यायात, अम्, n. the more ancient form of<BR>the legend of Yayāti or that current in the east.<BR>—पूर्व-यावन्, आ, m., Ved. ‘going before,’ a<BR>leader.<BR>—पूर्व-रङ्ग, अस्, m. the commencement<BR>or prelude of a drama, a prologue, an overture.<BR>—पूर्व-राग, अस्, m. earliest or incipient affec-<BR>tion, dawning love; affection arising from some pre-<BR>vious cause (before meeting).<BR>—पूर्व-रात्र, अस्,<BR>m. the first part of the night, the former or earlier<BR>part of the night, the time from dusk to midnight.<BR>—पूर्वरात्र-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done during the<BR>first part of the night.<BR>—पूर्व-रूप, अम्, n. indi-<BR>cation of approaching change; symptom of occurring<BR>disease; the first of two concurrent vowels or con-<BR>sonants; (in rhetoric) a figure of speech which<BR>describes anything as unexpectedly returned to its<BR>former state; (अस्, आ, अम्), having the previous<BR>form or shape.<BR>—पूर्व-लक्षण, अम्, n. indica-<BR>tion of something about to occur (as sickness).<BR> — 1. पूर्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having something<BR>preceding or antecedent, having or characterized by<BR>a cause; (according to others) relating to something<BR>preceding.<BR>—२. पूर्व-वत्, ind. as before, as hitherto,<BR>as heretofore, as aforesaid; [applied in the Nyāya<BR>philosophy to a kind of syllogism, e. g. inferring<BR>from the appearance of a dark cloud that rain<BR>will fall.]<BR>—पूर्व-वयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or पूर्व-<BR>वयस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the first period or stage<BR>of life, young.<BR>—पूर्व-वयस, अम्, n., Ved. the<BR>first period or stage of life, youth.<BR>—पूर्व-वयसिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, Ved. being in the first period of life, young.<BR>—पूर्ववर्ति-ता, f. the having existed before,<BR>former existence, precedence, priority.<BR>—पूर्व-वर्-<BR>तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, existing before, preceding, prior, pre-<BR>vious.<BR>—पूर्व-वह्, -वाट्, m., Ved. drawing in front,<BR>being the first horse or leader, or harnessed for the<BR>first time (applied to a horse).<BR>—पूर्व-वाद, अस्,<BR>m. the first plea or commencement of an action at<BR>law, a former plea or assertion.<BR>—पूर्व-वादिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘speaking first,’ ‘stating his case in the first<BR>instance,’ a complainant, plaintiff, one who makes<BR>the first charge or complaint; the first claimant; one<BR>who has made a former plea or complaint.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>वार्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्व-वर्ष), relating<BR>to the first half of the rainy season.<BR>—पूर्व-विद्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, knowing the things or events of the past.<BR>—पूर्व-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, formerly happened,<BR>relating to a previous occurrence; (अम्), n. a former<BR>event, previous occurrence; former conduct.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>व-वैरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who has first commenced<BR>hostilities, the first to declare war, the aggressor.<BR>—पूर्व-शारद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्व-शरद्),<BR>relating to the first half of the autumn.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>शीर्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, turned with the head or face<BR>towards the east.<BR>—पूर्व-शैल, अस्, m. the eastern<BR>mountain behind which the sun is supposed to rise;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a Buddhist school.<BR>—पूर्वशैल-<BR>सङ्घाराम (˚घ-आर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>monastery.<BR>—पूर्व-सक्थ, अम्, n. (probably) the<BR>upper part of the thigh.<BR>—पूर्व-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>sitting in front.<BR>—पूर्व-सन्ध्या, f. ‘earlier twi-<BR>light,’ dawn, day-break.<BR>—पूर्व-समुद्र, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. the eastern sea.<BR>—पूर्व-सर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>going before, preceding.<BR>—पूर्व-सस्य, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. earliest-sown grain.<BR>—पूर्व-सागर, अस्, m.<BR>the eastern sea.<BR>—पूर्व-सार, अस्, ई, अम्, going<BR>eastwards.<BR>—पूर्व-सारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, preceding,<BR>taking precedence of all others.<BR>—पूर्व-साहस,<BR>अम्, n. the first or heaviest fine or punishment.<BR>—पूर्व-सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, Ved. first bringing forth;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-a" target="_blank">Page0593-a+ 81</a>]<BR>first-born.<BR>—पूर्व-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing first, most<BR>excellent.<BR>—पूर्व-स्थिति, इस्, f. first or former state.<BR>—पूर्व-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, (in grammar) having the<BR>accent of the preceding.<BR>—पूर्व-हूति, इस्, f., Ved.<BR>first or earliest invocation, morning prayer.<BR>—पूर्व-<BR>होम, अस्, m., Ved. an introductory sacrifice.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>वाग्नि (˚व-अग्˚), इस्, m., Ved. ‘original or primeval<BR>fire,’ the householder's sacred fire (= आवसथ्य).<BR>—पूर्वाग्नि-वह्, वाट्, m. carrying the sacred fire.<BR>—पूर्वाग्नि-वहन, अम्, n., Ved. a vehicle for<BR>carrying the sacred fire.<BR>—पूर्वाचरित (˚व-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, formerly done or followed.<BR>—पूर्वाचल<BR>(˚व-आच्˚), अस्, or पूर्वाद्रि (˚व-अद्˚), इस्, m. the<BR>eastern mountain (behind which the sun and moon<BR>are supposed to rise).<BR>—पूर्वातिथि (˚व-अत्˚), इस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—पूर्वादि (˚व-आदि˚), इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>beginning with the word पूर्व.<BR>—पूर्वाधिकारिन्<BR>(˚व-अध्˚), ई, m. prior owner, former proprietor.<BR>—पूर्वाधिराम (˚व-अध्˚), अम्, n. the more<BR>ancient form of the story of Rāma or the form<BR>current in the east of India.<BR>—पूर्वानुयोग (˚व-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Jaina work belonging to the<BR>Dṛṣṭi-vāda.<BR>—पूर्वान्त (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>end of a preceding word; = पूर्व-कोटि, q. v.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>वापर (˚व-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being before and<BR>behind, eastern and western; prior and subsequent,<BR>first and last, preceding and following, following one<BR>another, connected with one another; (अम्), n. that<BR>which is before and behind, east and west; connec-<BR>tion; the proof and thing to be proved.<BR>—पूर्वा-<BR>पर-त्व, अम्, n. the being before and behind.<BR>—पूर्वापर-विरोध, अस्, m. opposition of prior<BR>and subsequent, inconsistency, incongruity.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>वापरी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, following one another,<BR>connected with one another.<BR>—पूर्वा-पुष् (?), ट्,<BR>ट्, ट्, Ved. supporting those who precede.<BR>—पूर्वा-<BR>भिभाषिन् (˚व-अभ्˚), ई, इणी, इ, = पूर्व-भा-<BR>षिन्, q. v.<BR>—पूर्वाभिमुख (˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, turned towards or facing the east.<BR>—पूर्वाभि-<BR>रामा (˚व-अभ्˚), f., N. of a river.<BR>—पूर्वाभिषेक<BR>(˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, m. previous anointing; (according<BR>to Sāy.) a particular Mantra.<BR>—पूर्वाभ्यास (˚व-<BR>अभ्˚), अस्, m. the repetition of what precedes, for-<BR>mer practice, antecedent experience; (एन), ind.<BR>afresh, anew.<BR>—पूर्वाम्बुधि (˚व-अम्˚), इस्, m.<BR>the eastern ocean.<BR>—पूर्वायुस् (˚व-आय्˚), उस्, उस्,<BR>उस्, Ved. (perhaps) ‘of an early age,’ young.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>वाराम (˚व-आर्˚), अस्, m. ‘eastern garden,’ N. of a<BR>Buddhist monastery.<BR>—पूर्वार्चिक (˚व-आर्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of the first half of the Sāma-veda (the second<BR>half of which is called उत्तरार्चिक).<BR>—पूर्वार्जित<BR>(˚व-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attained or gained by former<BR>works.<BR>—पूर्वार्ध (˚व-अर्˚), अस्, m. the first<BR>half, front or upper part, eastern part (opposed to<BR>जघनार्ध, उत्तरार्ध, उत्तमार्ध, परार्-<BR>ध); the first half of a hemistich; दिनस्य पूर्-<BR>वार्धः, forenoon.<BR>—पूर्वार्ध-काय, अस्, m.<BR>the front or upper part of the body.<BR>—पूर्वार्ध-<BR>लम्बिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the foremost half inclined,<BR>leaning forward.<BR>—पूर्वार्ध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>relating to the first or front part, relating to the<BR>upper part, relating to the eastern part.<BR>—पूर्वावे-<BR>दक (˚व-आव्˚), अस्, m. a plaintiff.<BR>—पूर्वाशिन्<BR>(˚व-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating before (another, with<BR>abl. or loc.).<BR>—पूर्वाषाढा (˚व-अष्˚), f. the<BR>first of two constellations called Aṣāḍhā, the eigh-<BR>teenth or twentieth Nakṣatra or lunar asterism con-<BR>taining two stars of which one is δ Sagittarii.<BR>—पूर्-<BR>वासिन् (˚व-आस्˚), ई, इनी, इ, Ved. shooting before<BR>(another).<BR>—पूर्वाह्ण (˚व-अह्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>earlier part of the day, forenoon (mostly occurring<BR>in the loc. case; sometimes incorrectly spelt पूर्-<BR>वाह्न).<BR>—पूर्वाह्णक, अस्, m. ‘born in the fore-<BR>noon,’ N. of a man.<BR>—पूर्वाह्णतन or पूर्वाह्-<BR>णिक or पूर्वाह्णेतन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or<BR>relating to the forenoon.<BR>—पूर्वेतर (˚व-इत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘other than eastern,’ western.<BR>—पूर्वे-<BR>द्युस्, ind. on the day before, yesterday (opposed to<BR>उत्तरे-द्युस्, उत्तरम् अहर्, अपरे-द्युस्); on a for-<BR>mer day; at dawn, during the first part of the day;<BR>early, betimes, in the morning; during that portion<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">Page0593-b+ 78</a>]<BR>of a day on which religious ceremonies are to be per-<BR>formed.<BR>—पूर्वेषुकामशमी (˚व-इष्˚), f., N.<BR>of a Grāma.<BR>—पूर्वोक्त (˚व-उक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, said<BR>before, formerly stated, aforesaid, before-mentioned.<BR>—पूर्वोत्तर (˚व-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, north-eastern;<BR>(ए), n. du. the antecedent and subsequent, the pre-<BR>ceding and following; (अम्, आ), n. f. the north-east.<BR>—पूर्वोत्पन्न (˚व-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, previously<BR>produced, previously existent.<BR>—पूर्वोत्पन्न-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. former existence, condition of prior exist-<BR>ence.<BR>—पूर्वोदित (˚व-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, aforesaid,<BR>before-mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0591-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वक|पूर्वकः|पूर्व्वक
पूर्वक, अस्, इका, अम्, earlier, former, previous,<BR>prior, anterior, preceding, antecedent (often like<BR>पूर्व, q. v., at the end of a comp.; cf. स्त्री-प्˚);<BR>first; preceded by, accompanied by, connected with,<BR>attended with (at the end of comps. = पूर्व, q. v.;<BR>cf. व्याहृति-प्˚); (अस्), m. a forefather, ancestor;<BR>(अम्), ind. preceded by, with, according to, in con-<BR>formity with (at the end of comps.; cf. विधि-प्˚,<BR>प्रीति-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वतन|पूर्व्वतन
पूर्वतन, अस्, ई, अम्, former, earlier, older,<BR>more ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वतस्
पूर्व-तस्, ind. in front of, before (with gen.);<BR>towards the east; first, in the first place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वत्र
पूर्व-त्र, ind. in the former or preceding part<BR>(opposed to उत्तर-त्र, q. v.); पूर्वत्र जन्मनि,<BR>in a former birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वथा
पूर्व-था, ind., Ved. at first, formerly, of old,<BR>aforetime; as of old; in front, towards the east (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वय
पूर्वय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. in उपाधाय्य-प्˚,<BR>having an edge or border (of red braid), trimmed,<BR>edged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वातिथ
पूर्वातिथ, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman (= पौर्-<BR>वातिथ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्विक
पूर्विक, अस्, आ, अम्, formerly or previously done;<BR>formerly invited; पूर्वक, previous; [cf. स्त्री-<BR>पूर्विक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्विणेष्ठा
पूर्विणे-ष्ठा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. standing in the<BR>east (? probably a wrong reading).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्विन्
पूर्विन्, ई, इणी, इ, derived from ancestors or fore-<BR>fathers, observed by ancestors, ancestral; having for-<BR>merly, having formerly been (at the end of a comp.;<BR>cf. कृत-प्˚, भुक्त-प्˚, स्त्री-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वीण
पूर्वीण, अस्, आ, अम्, derived from ancestors or<BR>forefathers, ancestral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्य
पूर्व्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. former, previous,<BR>preceding, ancient, old (opposed to नवीयस्, नू-<BR>तन); first, next, nearest (Sāy. = नेदिष्ठ); ex-<BR>cellent; (according to a Scholiast) young; (अम्),<BR>ind. before, formerly, long since, hitherto, at first.<BR>—पूर्व्य-स्तुति, इस्, f., Ved. principal praise (Sāy. =<BR>मुख्या स्तुतिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूल्
पूल् पूल्, cl. 1. 10. P. पूलति, पूलयति,<BR>यितुम्, to collect, gather, heap up, accu-<BR>mulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूल|पूलः
पूल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), or पूलक, अस्, m.<BR>a bundle, pack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूलिका
पूलिका पूलिका, f. a kind of pastry; [cf.<BR>पूरिका, पोलिका, पौलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूल्य|पूल्यं
पूल्य पूल्य, अम्, n. an empty or shrivelled<BR>grain of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष्
पूष् पूष् (= rt. 2. पुष्), cl. 1. P. पू-<BR>षति, पूषितुम्, to nourish; to increase,<BR>grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष|पूषः
पूष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. पुष्), a kind of mul-<BR>berry tree, Morus Indica; (आ), f. epithet of the<BR>third Kalā of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषक|पूषकः
पूषक, अस्, m. a kind of mulberry tree, Morus<BR>Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषण
पूषण, अस्, m. = पूषन् below; (आ), f., N. of<BR>one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषन्
पूषन्, आ, m. (the अ of अन् is not lengthened in<BR>the nom. du. pl. and acc. sing. du., e. g. nom. du.<BR>पूषणौ, nom. pl. पूषणस्, acc. sing. पूष-<BR>णम्, acc. pl. पूष्णस्, or according to some also<BR>पूषस्, inst. sing. पूष्णा or पूषा, loc. sing.<BR>पूष्णि or पूषणि or पूषि, see Gram. 157), N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">Page0593-c+ 74</a>]<BR>of a Vedic deity (regarded as the guardian of flocks<BR>and herds and of property in general, cf. पुष्टिम्-<BR>भर; in the character of a herdsman he is repre-<BR>sented as carrying an ox-goad and riding in a car<BR>drawn by goats, cf. अजाश्व; in that of a presiding<BR>deity of the sun he is all-seeing, the companion of<BR>travellers, guide of the soul on its way to the next<BR>world, and the lover of his sister Sūryā; he causes<BR>the alternation of day and night, and is associated<BR>with Soma or the Moon as protector of the universe;<BR>he is invoked together with various gods, but most<BR>frequently with Indra and Bhaga; his most remark-<BR>able epithets are आ-घृणि, कपर्दिन्, दस्र, द-<BR>स्म, दस्म-वर्चस्; in the Brāhmaṇas Pūṣan is<BR>represented as having lost his teeth and feeding on a<BR>kind of gruel, whence he is called करम्भाद्; in<BR>later times he is enumerated among the twelve<BR>Ādityas, and regent of the Nakṣatra Revatī or<BR>Pauṣṇa); N. of the sun.<BR>—पूषण्-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, Ved. accompanied by Pūṣan; (Sāy.) = पुष्ट्या<BR>युक्त, filled with nutriment.<BR>—पूष-दन्त-हर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘taking away Pūṣan's teeth,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—पूष-भासा, f. ‘sun-splendor,’ N. of the<BR>capital of Indra; (also spelt पूष-भाषा.)<BR>—पू-<BR>ष-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a man with the surname<BR>Gobhila.<BR>—पूष-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having Pūṣan<BR>as a giver, i. e. probably, among whom Pūṣan is<BR>the especial benefactor.<BR>—पूषात्मज (˚ष-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of Pūṣan,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—पू-<BR>षासुहृद् (˚ष-अस्˚), त्, m. ‘enemy of Pūṣan,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषध्र
पूषध्र पूषध्र, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Manu; (probably a wrong reading for पृषध्र.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष्कर
पूष्कर पूष्कर, a word formed for the ex-<BR>planation of पुष्कर (Śatapatha-b. VII. 4, 1, 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
पृ 1. पृ, cl. 3. P. पिपर्ति, पपार, प-<BR>रिष्यति, अपार्षीत् (mostly Ved.), to bring<BR>over, carry over or across, ferry over; to bring<BR>out of, deliver from (with abl.); to escort; to pro-<BR>tect, uphold, support, sustain, maintain; to bring<BR>forward, promote, advance; cl. 9. P. पृनाति,<BR>to protect: Caus. P. (ep. also A.) पारयति<BR>(-ते), -यितुम्, Aor. अपीपरत्, to ferry over or<BR>across, carry over, conduct through; to bring out,<BR>deliver, extricate, rescue, save, protect; to reach<BR>the other side of anything, to accomplish, achieve,<BR>perform, bring to a conclusion; to keep one's ground,<BR>withstand, oppose; to be able or capable; to live;<BR>[cf. Zend par, ‘to carry across:’ Gr. περά-ω, πόρο-ς,<BR>πορεύς, πορ-θ-μός, πορσύν-ω, πορεύ-ω, πορίζ-ω,<BR>ἄπορος, ἀπορέ-ω, ἔμ-πορο-ς, πεῖρ-α, πειρά-ω, παρών,<BR>πειράτης, πεπαρεῖν, πείρω, περόνη, πόρπη, πειρά,<BR>πηρό-ς: Lat. por-ta, por-tu-s, ex-per-i-o-r, peritus,<BR>perî-culu-m, par-a-re (?), parere, partus, portare:<BR>Goth. far-an, ‘to go;’ far-j-an, ‘to carry:’ Old<BR>Germ. ar-far-an, ‘to perceive;’ furt: Angl. Sax.<BR>fyrd.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
पृ 2. पृ [cf. rt. पृण्], cl. 5. P. पृणोमि,<BR>पपार, परिष्यति, अपार्षीत्, पर्तुम्, to<BR>please, gratify, delight; to be pleased or delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
पृ 3. पृ, cl. 6. A. प्रियते, पप्रे, परिष्-<BR>यते, अपृत, पर्तुम्, to be busy or active<BR>(in व्य्-आ-पृ, q. v.); [cf. Gr. περά-ω, πέρ-νη-μι,<BR>πι-πρά-σκ-ω, πρί-α-μαι, πρά-σι-ς, πρα-τία-ς,<BR>πόρ-νη, ἔμ-πορος, ἔμ-πολά-ω, πωλέω; Lat. prec-iu-m,<BR>prec-ari; Old Germ. feil, feili = Mod. Germ. feil,<BR>‘cheap, venal.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
पृ 4. पृ = rt. पॄ, to fill, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्का
पृक्का पृक्का, f. a species of leguminous<BR>plant, Trigonella Corniculata; [cf. स्पृक्का.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्त|पृक्तं
पृक्त पृक्त, पृक्ति. See under rt. 1. पृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्थ|पृक्थं
पृक्थ पृक्थ, अम्, n. possession, property,<BR>wealth; [cf. रिक्थ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्ष्
पृक्ष् पृक्ष्, f. (the nom. sing. does not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">Page0594-a+ 76</a>]<BR>occur; perhaps connected with rt. 1. पृच्), Ved.<BR>refreshment, food, nourishment, satiation.<BR>—पृक्षु-<BR>धा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. (according to Sāy.) = पशु-<BR>पुरोडाशादिषु दाह-मध्ये धीयमानः, being<BR>placed in the midst of the burnt offerings of animals,<BR>ghee, &c., or = प्र-क्षोध्यः. = प्रकर्षेण<BR>बुभुक्षितः; (perhaps a corruption for प्र-<BR>क्षुध, ‘hungry, eager.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0593-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्ष
पृक्ष पृक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fleet, swift<BR>(? said of a horse); having food, (Sāy.) = घासाद्य्-<BR>अन्न-वत्, possessing grass and other food; (अस्),<BR>m. a swift horse, courser (an epithet especially of<BR>the horses of the Aśvins, Agni, and Indra); N. of a<BR>man; a battle.<BR>—पृक्ष-प्रयज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>(perhaps) hastening with swift horses; (Sāy.) in<BR>which oblations of food begin to be offered (said of<BR>the morning).<BR>—पृक्ष-याम, अस्, आ, अम्, driving<BR>swift horses; (Sāy.) = अन्नानां नियमनं यस्-<BR>मिन्, in which there is the offering of food; (अस्),<BR>m. a proper N. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्
पृच् 1. पृच्, cl. 7. P. पृणक्ति, पपर्च,<BR>पर्चिष्यति, अपर्चीत्, पर्चितुम्; cl. 2.<BR>A. पृक्ते or पृङ्क्ते (sometimes referred to a form<BR>पृञ्च्), पपृचे or पपृञ्चे, पर्चिता or पृञ्चिता,<BR>पर्चिष्यते, अपर्चिष्ट, पर्चितुम्; cl. 1. A.<BR>पर्चति, &c. (?), to mix, mingle; to bring into<BR>contact, connect, unite, join; to be in contact, touch;<BR>to fill, satisfy, sate, satiate; to give lavishly, grant<BR>bountifully, bestow anything (acc. or gen.) richly<BR>upon any one (dat.), lavish upon (Ved.); to increase,<BR>augment, multiply; (A.) to fill one's self (?); cl. 1.<BR>10. P. पर्चति, पर्चयति, &c., to touch; to hin-<BR>der, restrain (?); [cf. Gr. πλέκ-ω, πλέγ-μα, πλοκή,<BR>πλόκαμο-ς, δί-πλαξ, perhaps πόρκο-ς, πόρκη-ς:<BR>Lat. plec-t-o, am-plec-t-or, plic-o, du-plex, Parca,<BR>plăg-a: Umbr. tribricu, ‘triplicity:’ Goth. flah-<BR>t-om, ‘with folds;’ fal-th-a, ‘I fold;’ flaht, flihtu,<BR>fluhtumês: Old Germ. flihtu, flahs = Mod. Germ.<BR>Flachs = Eng. flax; flehtan: Mod. Germ. flech-t-<BR>en: Angl. Sax. folg-ian: Slav. ple-t-a, ‘I plait.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्त|पृक्तं
पृक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed, mingled, combined;<BR>brought into contact, touched, united, being in com-<BR>bination with, touching [cf. मयूख-प्˚]; filled,<BR>full (e. g. घृत-पृक्त, full of ghee); (अम्), n.<BR>possessions, property, wealth (in these senses a wrong<BR>reading for पृक्थ, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्ति|पृक्तिः
पृक्ति, इस्, f. touch, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्
2. पृच्, क्, f., Ved. refreshment; (Sāy.) = प्राप्-<BR>तुं कामयमान, desirous of attaining, or = भुज्,<BR>enjoying; [cf. घृत-प्˚, मधु-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छक|पृच्छकः
पृच्छक पृच्छक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. प्रछ्),<BR>one who asks or inquires after (with gen.); inquiring;<BR>inquiring into the future; (अस्), m. an inquirer,<BR>querist, investigator, inquisitive person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छन|पृच्छनं
पृच्छन, अम्, n. asking, inquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छा
पृच्छा, f. asking, questioning, a question, in-<BR>quiry; an inquiry into the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छ्य
पृच्छ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be asked or inquired<BR>after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृज्
पृज् पृज्, पृञ्ज्, cl. 2. A. पृङ्क्ते, &c.,<BR>various readings for rts. 1. पृच्, पृञ्च्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृञ्च्
पृञ्च् पृञ्च्, cl. 2. A. पृङ्क्ते, &c. See<BR>rt. 1. पृच् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृड्
पृड् पृड्, cl. 6. P. पृडति, &c. [cf. rt.<BR>पृण्], to gladden, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृण्
पृण् पृण् [cf. rts. 2. and 4. पृ], cl. 6.<BR>P. A. पृणति, -ते, &c., Ved. to fill; to<BR>please, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृत्
पृत् पृत्, त्, f., Ved. (usually in loc. pl.<BR>पृत्सु, in Ṛg-veda I. 129, 4. पृत्सुषु, but<BR>according to native grammarians also in other cases,<BR>viz. पृतस्, पृता, पृद्भ्याम्), battle, contest,<BR>strife.<BR>—पृत्-सुति, इस्, f., Ved. a hostile attack;<BR>(Sāy.) a host.<BR>—पृत्सु-तुर्, ऊर्, ऊर्, उर्, Ved. vic-<BR>torious; (Sāy.) = पृतनासु तरण-शील = शूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन|पृतनं
पृतन, अम्, n. a hostile encounter (Ved.); an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">Page0594-b+ 80</a>]<BR>army (Ved.); (आ), f. a battle, encounter, fight, con-<BR>test, (in the earlier language only in acc. and loc.<BR>plur.); a hostile armament, army; a small army or<BR>division consisting of 243 elephants, as many chariots,<BR>729 horse, and 1215 foot, = 3 Vāhinīs; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. men, mankind (?).<BR>—पृतनाज् (˚ना-अज्˚), क्, क्,<BR>क्, Ved. running or rushing in battle.<BR>—पृतनाजि<BR>(˚ना-अजि˚), इस्, इस्, इ, = पृतनाज् (Atharva-veda VII.<BR>85, 1).<BR>—पृतना-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. victorious in<BR>battle; (त्), m., N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—पृतनाज्य<BR>(˚ना-अज्˚), अम्, n., Ved. ‘running-match,’ a fight,<BR>battle.<BR>—पृतना-नी, ईस्, or पृतना-पति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a leader in battle, commander, general.<BR>—पृ-<BR>तना-षह् or पृथना-षाह्, ट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. winning<BR>battles, victorious, (Sāy.) = अ-मर्त्य, immortal; (ट्),<BR>m. an epithet of Indra.<BR>—पृतना-षाह्य, अम्, n.,<BR>Ved. victory in battle (Sāy. = परकीय-सेनाभि-<BR>भव).<BR>—पृतनाहव (˚ना-आह्˚), अस्, m., Ved. a<BR>challenge to fight; a fight, battle; (Sāy.) = सङ्ग्रा-<BR>मेषु रक्षणार्थम् आह्वानम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतनायत्
पृतनायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. fighting together,<BR>engaged in combat, (according to Mahī-dhara =<BR>सङ्ग्राम-काम, eager for battle.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतनायु
पृतनायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन्य
पृतन्य, Nom. P. पृतन्यति, -यितुम्, Ved. to<BR>attack, assail, to fight against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन्या
पृतन्या, f. = पृतना, an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन्यु
पृतन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. attacking, hostile;<BR>(Sāy.) = युद्धम् इच्छत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृत्सुध|पृत्सुधः
पृत्सुध, अस्, m. battle ?; (a various reading<BR>for पृत्सु in Naigh. II. 17.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्
पृथ् पृथ्, cl. 10. P. पर्थयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to extend (= rt. 1. प्रथ्); to throw,<BR>cast; to send, direct; [cf. rt. 2. प्रथ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ|पृथः
पृथ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पृथ् as another form of rt.<BR>1. प्रथ्), Ved. the flat or palm of the hand; a par-<BR>ticular measure, the length of the hand from the tip<BR>of the fingers to the knuckles, or = 13 Aṅgulis; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Śūra and adopted daughter of<BR>Kunti and one of the wives of Pāṇḍu (she was the<BR>mother of Karṇa before her marriage and of Yudhi-<BR>ṣṭhira, Bhīma, and Arjuna after her marriage, see<BR>कुन्ति).<BR>—पृथ-हर, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—पृथा-ज, अस्, m. ‘son of Pṛthā,’ an epithet of<BR>Arjuna; the tree Pentaptera Arjuna.<BR>—पृथा-पति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘the husband of Pṛthā,’ an epithet of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—पृथारणि (˚था-अर्˚), इस्, f. ‘the Araṇi Pṛthā,’<BR>a N. of Kuntī the wife of Pāṇḍu (as the mystical<BR>wood from which the Pāṇḍavas were struck out or<BR>generated; cf. पाण्डव-वह्नि).<BR>—पृथा-सुत,<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of Pṛthā,’ an epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्
पृथक्, ind. separately, singly, severally; apart<BR>from, besides, with exception of, except (with abl.);<BR>without (with abl., inst., or gen.); differently from<BR>(with abl.); पृथक् पृथक्, one by one, separately,<BR>with regular intervals; [cf. perhaps Gr. φάρ-σο-ς;<BR>Lat. par(t)s, prī-vus perhaps for prith-vus, pri-<BR>vare.]<BR>—पृथक्-करण, अम्, n. making separate,<BR>separating, distinguishing, setting apart.<BR>—पृथक्-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having different wishes,<BR>having various desires.<BR>—पृथक्-कार्य, अम्, n.<BR>a separate or private affair, the affair of an individual.<BR>—पृथक्-कुल, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a separate<BR>or different family.<BR>—पृथक्-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -क-<BR>रोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to make separate, sever,<BR>sunder; to keep off, avert.<BR>—पृथक्-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, separated, severed, sundered, cut off; made<BR>distinct.<BR>—पृथक्-क्रिया, f. separation, disunion.<BR>—पृथक्-क्षेत्र, आस्, m. pl. children of one<BR>father by different wives or by wives of different<BR>classes.<BR>—पृथक्-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going separately,<BR>walking alone.<BR>—पृथक्-त्व, अम्, n. separateness,<BR>separation, diversity, severalty; singleness, individu-<BR>ality; (एन), ind. singly, one by one.<BR>—पृथक्-<BR>त्वचा, f. ‘diverse-barked,’ a species of aloe com-<BR>monly called Mūrvā, Sanseviera Zeylanica.<BR>—पृथक्-<BR>पर्णी, f. ‘diverse-leaved,’ a species of plant, Hemio-<BR>nitis Cordifolia.<BR>—पृथक्-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a distant<BR>kinsman who offers the funeral cake by himself and<BR>not together with the other relations; (according to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-c" target="_blank">Page0594-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Kullūka = समानोदक.)<BR>—पृथक्-शब्द, अस्, m.<BR>a separate word, a distinct or independant word.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थक्-शय्या, f. sleeping apart.<BR>—पृथक्-श्रुति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, uttering a distinct sound, distinctly heard.<BR>—पृथक्-स्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, existing separately,<BR>separate.<BR>—पृथक्-स्थिति, इस्, f. separate existence,<BR>separation.<BR>—पृथग्-अभिमति, इस्, इस्, इ, regarding<BR>the world as separate (from God).<BR>—पृथग्-आत्मता,<BR>f. separateness, severalty; discrimination, judgment.<BR>—पृथग्-आत्मन्, आ, आ, अ, ‘having a distinct<BR>nature or essence,’ separate, distinct, individual; (आ),<BR>m. individualized spirit, that of an individual as<BR>detached from universal spirit or the soul of the<BR>universe.<BR>—पृथग्-आत्मिका, f. separate or individual<BR>existence, individuality.<BR>—पृथग्-ईश-मानिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, regarding God as distinct from the universe;<BR>[cf. पृथग्-अभिमति.]<BR>—पृथग्-गण, अस्, m. a<BR>separate company.<BR>—पृथग्-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing distinct properties.<BR>—पृथग्-जन, अस्, m. a<BR>man of the lower classes or of low caste, a man of<BR>low character or profession; (with Buddhists) a man<BR>in his natural state, one not yet illuminated; an<BR>ignorant man, fool, blockhead; a wicked or vicious<BR>man, sinner; the lower orders, low people, the mul-<BR>titude; (आस्), m. pl. children of one father by different<BR>mothers; the lower orders, populace.<BR>—पृथग्-दृश्,<BR>क्, क्, क्, beholding other objects (than those of sense).<BR>—पृथग्-बीज, अस्, m. the plant Semecarpus Ana-<BR>cardium (= भल्लातक).<BR>—पृथग्-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>separate state or existence, separateness, difference,<BR>individuality (= पृथक्-त्व, q. v.).<BR>—पृथग्-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become separate, separated, dif-<BR>ferent.<BR>—पृथग्-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) hav-<BR>ing a different lot.<BR>—पृथग्योग-करण, अम्, n.<BR>disuniting things connected with one another.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थग्-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, variously shaped, diverse,<BR>manifold, various, different, of different kinds.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थग्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, of different kinds, various,<BR>diversified, multiform, different from (with inst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथवी
पृथवी, f. = पृथिवी below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवी
पृथिवी, f. (for पृथ्वी, f. of पृथु below),<BR>‘the wide (world),’ the earth, Earth personified (as<BR>the mother of all beings, and often invoked together<BR>with the Sky; in the Veda there are three earths<BR>enumerated corresponding with the three heavens,<BR>that on which mankind lives being called भूमि;<BR>in the Viṣṇu-Purāṇa said to be the daughter of<BR>Pṛthu); land, ground, soil; earth regarded as one<BR>of the elements; (according to Naigh. I. 3) = अन्त-<BR>रिक्ष, sky; पृथिव्या व्रतम् or पृथिव्याः सं-<BR>सर्पम्, N. of a Sāman. [पृथिवी is sometimes<BR>shortened into पृथिवि, especially in comps.]<BR>—पृ-<BR>थिवि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of the earth.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थिवि-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. earth-giving.<BR>—पृथिवि-<BR>भाग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the earth as a share,<BR>one to whom the earth is allotted, entitled to the<BR>earth.<BR>—पृथिवि-लोक, अस्, m., Ved. the earth re-<BR>garded as a world, the terrestrial world.<BR>—पृथिवि-<BR>षद् or पृथिवि-सद्, त्, त्, त्, sitting on the ground.<BR>—पृथिवि-ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. standing on the<BR>ground, stepping firmly (said of a horse; Sāy. =<BR>पृथिव्यां सु-प्रतिष्ठितः).<BR>—पृथिवी-कम्प,<BR>अस्, m. an earthquake.<BR>—पृथिवी-क्षित्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>dwelling on earth (Ved.); reigning over the earth;<BR>(त्), m. a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—पृथिवी-चन्द्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘earth-moon,’ N. of a prince of the Tri-<BR>gartas.<BR>—पृथिवीञ्-जय, अस्, आ, अम्, conquering<BR>the earth; (अस्), m. a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थिवी-तल, अम्, n. the surface of the earth, ground,<BR>bare ground, the very earth.<BR>—पृथिवी-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—पृथिवी-धरण, अम्, n. a<BR>prop or support of the earth.<BR>—पृथिवी-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘lord of the earth,’ a prince, king, sovereign; an<BR>epithet of Yama the regent of the dead; a kind of<BR>drug (= ऋषभ).<BR>—पृथिवी-परिपालक, अस्, m.<BR>‘guardian of the earth,’ a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—पृथिवी-पार्वतक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>rock-oil, petroleum (?).<BR>—पृथिवी-पाल, अस्, m.<BR>‘guardian of the earth,’ a king, sovereign, ruler.<BR>—पृथिवी-भुज्, क्, m. ‘earth-enjoying,’ a prince,<BR>sovereign.<BR>—पृथिवी-मण्ड, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-a" target="_blank">Page0595-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the scum of the earth.<BR>—पृथिवी-मण्डल, अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n. the circuit of the earth.<BR>—पृथिवी-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of earth, earthen.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थिवी-रस, अस्, m. the sap of the earth.<BR>—पृथिवी-<BR>राज्य, अम्, n. the sovereignty of the earth.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थिवी-रुह, अस्, m. ‘earth-growing,’ a plant, tree.<BR>—पृथिवी-लोक, अस्, m. the earth considered as a<BR>world, the terrestrial world; [cf. पृथिवि-लोक.]<BR>—पृथिवीश (˚वि-ईश˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the earth,’<BR>a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—पृथिवी-शक्र, अस्, m.<BR>‘the Indra of the earth,’ a king.<BR>—पृथिव्य्-आपीड,<BR>अस्, m., N. of two princes of Kaśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0594-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथु|पृथुः
पृथु, उस्, उस्, or वी, उ, broad, wide, expansive,<BR>extensive, spacious; ample, abundant, luxuriant;<BR>large, great, gigantic; detailed; prolix; numerous;<BR>smart, clever; various; important; (उस्), m. a N. of<BR>Agni or fire; a particular measure of length (=<BR>पृथ); N. of a mythical personage (= पृथी, see<BR>col. 3); N. of a son of An-enas; of a Vṛṣṇi and son<BR>of Citraka; of a son of Citra-ratha; of a descendant<BR>of Ikṣvāku (son of An-araṇya and father of Tri-<BR>śaṅku); of a son of Pāra; of a son of Pra-stāra; of<BR>a son of Rucaka; of one of the Saptarṣis; of a son<BR>of one of the Manus; of a Dānava; of a monkey;<BR>(उस्), f. a pungent seed, Nigella Indica; a medicinal<BR>substance (commonly हिङ्गु-पत्त्री); opium; (वी),<BR>f. ‘the wide (world),’ earth; earth as an element;<BR>the pungent seed Nigella Indica; = हिङ्गु-पत्त्री;<BR>the plant Boerhavia Procumbens (= पुनर्-नव,<BR>q. v.); great cardamoms; a kind of metre consisting<BR>of four lines of seventeen syllables each; another<BR>metre containing eleven syllables in each line; N. of<BR>the mother of the seventh Arhat of the present<BR>Ava-sarpiṇī; [cf. rt. प्रथ्; प्रथ्-अस्, ‘breadh:’<BR>Zend frath-anh, ‘breadth:’ Gr. πλατύ-ς, πλάτ-ος,<BR>πλάτ-η, πλάτ-ανο-ς, πλάθ-ανο-ς, πλαθ-άνη, πλάσσω,<BR>πλάσ-μα, πλασ-τό-ς, ἔμ-πλασ-τρο-ν: Lat. lăt-<BR>us for platus; Latium, ‘flat country;’ lat-er: Lith.<BR>platus: Goth. braid-s, ‘broad:’ Angl. Sax. brâd:<BR>Eng. broad: Mod. Germ. breit.]<BR>—पृथु-कर्-<BR>मन्, आ, m., N. of a son of Śaśa-vindu and grandson<BR>of Citra-ratha.<BR>—पृथु-कल्पिनी, f. a various reading<BR>for पथ-कल्पना, q. v.<BR>—पृथु-कीर्त्ति, इस्, m.<BR>‘far-famed,’ N. of a son of Śaśa-vindu; (इस्), f., N.<BR>of a daughter of Śūra.<BR>—पृथु-कोल, अस्, m. a species<BR>of jujube.<BR>—पृथु-ग, आस्, m. pl. ‘far-going,’ N. of<BR>a class of deities under Manu Cākṣuṣa.<BR>—पृथु-<BR>गमन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. ‘broad-pathed,’ having a broad<BR>path; thick-set ?; (Sāy. = पृथु-भावम् प्राप्-<BR>नुवत्.)<BR>—पृथु-ग्रीव, अस्, m. ‘broad-necked,’ N.<BR>of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—पृथु-चार्व्-अञ्चितेक्षण (˚त-<BR>ईक्ष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having large, beautiful, and curved<BR>eyes.<BR>—पृथु-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘broad-leaved,’ a<BR>species of plant (= हरिद्-गर्भ).<BR>—पृथु-ज-<BR>घन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘large-hipped,’ having broad hips.<BR>—पृथु-जय, अस्, m. ‘victorious far and wide,’ N.<BR>of a son of Śaśa-vindu.<BR>—पृथु-जमन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>Ved. ‘broad-pathed,’ having a broad path; [cf.<BR>पृथु-ग्मन्.]<BR>—पृथु-ज्रय, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>पृथु-ज्रयस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, widely extended, spread-<BR>ing widely; of rapid or extended impetus (Sāy.<BR>= पृथु-जव = शीघ्र-गामिन् = प्रथित-वेग).<BR>—पृथु-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, broadest, widest, largest<BR>(= प्रथिष्ठ).<BR>—पृथु-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, broader,<BR>wider, larger, more spacious, very large or important<BR>(= प्रथीयस्).<BR>—पृथु-ता, f. or पृथु-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. breadth, width, largeness, greatness.<BR>—पृथु-<BR>दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, far-seeing, far-sighted (in a meta-<BR>phorical sense).<BR>—पृथु-दान, अस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Śaśa-vindu.<BR>—पृथु-दीर्घ-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>having broad and long arms, broad and long-armed.<BR>—पृथु-धरणि-धर, अस्, m. ‘supporting the<BR>broad earth,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu (Mahā-bh. Śānti-p.<BR>13444).<BR>—पृथु-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘broad-edged,’<BR>having a wide or broad edge.<BR>—पृथु-नितम्ब,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having broad hips, large-hipped.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-पक्षस्, अस्, n. (probably) a broad space at the<BR>side (of a chariot); (according to Sāy. an adj. आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्) = पृथु-पार्श्व-द्वय-युक्त, broad-flanked,<BR>having the two flanks broad (said of a horse).<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-पत्त्र, अस्, m. ‘broad-leaved,’ a kind of garlic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-b" target="_blank">Page0595-b+ 81</a>]<BR>(= रक्त-लशुन).<BR>—पृथु-पर्शु, उस्, उस्, उ,<BR>Ved. armed with large sickles; (Sāy.) = विस्तीर्णाश्व-<BR>पर्शु-हस्त, holding large rib-bones of horses.<BR>—पृथु-पलाशिका, f. Curcuma Zedoaria (= शटी,<BR>पलाशिका).<BR>—पृथु-पाजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. far-<BR>shining, resplendent (said of Agni, of the horses of<BR>Uṣas, of the chariot of the Aśvins, and of Indra-<BR>Vāyu; Sāy. = पृथु-तेजस् or पृथु-वेगस्).<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. broad-handed (said of<BR>Savitṛ; Sāy. = महत्-कर).<BR>—पृथु-प्रगाण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a wide approach or access,<BR>approached by wide avenues; (Sāy.) = पृथु-गीति,<BR>much-lauded.<BR>—पृथु-प्रगामन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved.<BR>wide-striding, taking wide strides; moving fleetly<BR>(Sāy. = पृथु-प्रगमन).<BR>—पृथु-प्रथ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, far-famed, having a wide reputation.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-प्रोथ, अस्, आ, अम्, having broad or wide nostrils<BR>(said of a horse).<BR>—पृथु-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, broad-<BR>armed, having brawny arms.<BR>—पृथु-बुध्न, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, broad-based, having a broad basis or foot,<BR>having a broad sole or under-part (Sāy. = स्थूल-<BR>मूल).<BR>—पृथु-भुवन, अम्, n. the wide world.<BR>—पृथु-मृद्वीका, f. ‘wide grape,’ (probably) a<BR>raisin.<BR>—पृथु-यशस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, far-famed, of<BR>wide renown; (आस्), m., N. of a son of Śaśa-vindu;<BR>of a son of Varāha-mihira.<BR>—पृथु-यामन्, आ, आ,<BR>अ, Ved. ‘broad-pathed,’ having a broad path (said<BR>of Uṣas); (Sāy.) = पृथु-रथ, a spacious chariot.<BR>—पृथु-रश्मि, इस्, m., Ved. ‘broad-rayed,’ N. of<BR>a Yati.<BR>—पृथु-रुक्म, अस्, or पृथु-रुक्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a son of Parā-jit (or Parā-vṛt).<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-रोमन्, आ, m. ‘having broad hairs or scales,’ a<BR>fish.<BR>—पृथुरोम-युग्म, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>the sign of the zodiac Pisces.<BR>—पृथु-लोचन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, large-eyed, having large eyes.<BR>—पृथु-<BR>वक्त्रा, f. ‘wide-mouthed,’ N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—पृथु-वेग, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>excessive force or impetus,’ N. of a prince.<BR>—पृथु-<BR>शिम्ब, अस्, m. a species of Śyonāka.<BR>—पृथु-शिरस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. broad-headed, flat-headed.<BR>—पृथु-<BR>शेखर, अस्, m. ‘broad-crested,’ a mountain.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-श्रव, अस्, m., N. of a being attendant upon<BR>Skanda; (probably a wrong reading for पृथु-<BR>श्रवस्.)<BR>—पृथु-श्रवस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, far-famed, of<BR>wide renown; (आस्), m., N. of a man; of a son of<BR>Śaśa-vindu; of a son of Raghu; of a son of the<BR>ninth Manu; of a serpent-demon.<BR>—पृथु-श्री, ईस्,<BR>ईस्, इ, having great fortune, highly prosperous.<BR>—पृ-<BR>थु-श्रोणि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘broad-hipped,’ having broad<BR>hips, having large buttocks.<BR>—पृथु-षेण (पृथु<BR>+ सेना), अस्, m. ‘having an extensive army,’ N. of<BR>a son of Rucira (or Rucirāśva); of a son of Vibhu;<BR>(also read पृथु-सेन.)<BR>—पृथु-ष्ठु, उस्, उस्,<BR>उ, or पृथु-ष्ठुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according<BR>to Mahī-dhara) = पृथु-केश-भार, abundant-<BR>haired, having a broad plait or tuft of hair; much-<BR>praised, much-desired, desired of many; (according<BR>to the Nirukta and Sāy.) = पृथु-जघन, q. v.<BR>—पृथु-सत्त्व-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, abounding in<BR>great living creatures.<BR>—पृथु-सम्पद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>possessing large property, rich, wealthy.<BR>—पृथु-<BR>स्कन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘broad-shouldered,’ a boar.<BR>—पृथूदक (˚थु-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘having exten-<BR>sive waters,’ N. of a sacred bathing-place on the<BR>northern bank of the Sarasvatī.<BR>—पृथूदक-स्वा-<BR>मिन्, ई, m., N. of the author of a commentary on<BR>the Brahma-gupta.<BR>—पृथूदर (˚थु-उद्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, big-bellied, stout, corpulent; (अस्), m. a ram.<BR>—पृथूपाख्यान (˚थु-उप्˚), अम्, n. ‘episode<BR>of Pṛthu,’ N. of the twenty-ninth and thirtieth<BR>chapters of the second part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—पृथ्वी-कुरवक, अस्, m. a species of tree (=<BR>श्वेत-मन्दारक).<BR>—पृथ्वी-खात, अम्, n. a<BR>hole or pit in the earth, cavern.<BR>—पृथ्वी-गर्भ,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—पृथ्वी-गृह, अम्,<BR>n. a dwelling in the earth, a cave.<BR>—पृथ्वी-चन्-<BR>द्रोदय, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—पृथ्वी-ज, अम्,<BR>n. ‘earth-born,’ a species of salt (= गड-लवण).<BR>—पृथ्वी-दण्ड-पाल-ता, f. the office of chief of<BR>the police, prefecture of police.<BR>—पृथ्वी-धर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of the author of the Bhuvaneśvarī-stotra<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">Page0595-c+ 75</a>]<BR>hymn; of the author of a commentary on the<BR>Mṛc-chakatikā.<BR>—पृथ्वी-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>earth,’ a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—पृथ्वी-पाल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘earth-protector,’ N. of a man.<BR>—पृथ्वी-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town in Magadha.<BR>—पृथ्वी-<BR>भर, अस्, m. (?), a species of the Aty-aṣṭi metre.<BR>—पृथ्वी-भुज्, क्, m. ‘earth-enjoyer,’ a prince,<BR>king.<BR>—पृथ्वी-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of the earth,’<BR>N. of a prince.<BR>—पृथ्वीश (˚वी-ईश˚), अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the earth,’ a prince, king, sovereign.<BR>—पृथ्वी-<BR>हर, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुक|पृथुकं|पृथुकः
पृथुक, अस्, अम्, m. n. rice or grain flattened;<BR>rice scalded with hot water and then dried over a<BR>fire and ground in a mortar; (अस्), m. a child,<BR>boy, the young of any animal; (आ), f. a girl; a<BR>species of plant (= हिङ्गु-पत्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुल|पृथुलं
पृथुल, अस्, आ, अम्, broad, large, great; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a medicinal substance (= हिङ्गु-पत्त्री).<BR>—पृथुलाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘large-eyed,’ N.<BR>of a prince, a son of Catur-aṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीका
पृथ्वीका, f. large cardamoms; small cardamoms;<BR>a small pungent seed, Nigella Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथवान
पृथवान पृथवान, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथाश्व
पृथाश्व पृथाश्व, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथि
पृथि पृथि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a man<BR>(according to Sāy. a Rājarṣi) under the especial<BR>protection of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिका
पृथिका पृथिका, f. (said to be fr. rt. पृथ्),<BR>a centipede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवी
पृथिवी पृथिवी. See p. 594, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथी
पृथी पृथी, ई, m., Ved., N. of a mythical<BR>personage with the patronymic Vainya (said to have<BR>been the first anointed sovereign of men, to have<BR>ruled also the lower animals, and to have introduced<BR>the arts of husbandry into the world; he is enume-<BR>rated among the Ṛṣis and said to be the author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 148).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथु|पृथुः
पृथु पृथु. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृदाकु|पृदाकुः
पृदाकु पृदाकु, उस्, m. or पृदाकू, ऊस्, f. (said<BR>to be fr. rt. पर्द्), an adder, viper, snake, serpent; (उस्),<BR>m. a scorpion; a tiger; a panther (= चित्रक); an<BR>elephant; a tree.<BR>—पृदाकु-सानु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>having a surface like that of a serpent; smooth or<BR>variegated or shining like a serpent; (according to<BR>Sāy.) having the head uplifted like a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृशन
पृशन पृशन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. स्पृश्), Ved.<BR>clinging to, attached to; tender, gentle (only used in<BR>the fem.); (अम्), n. clinging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृशनायु
पृशनायु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. clinging to, attached<BR>to; tender; (Sāy.) = स्पर्शन-काम, desirous of<BR>contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नि|पृश्निः
पृश्नि पृश्नि, इस्, इस्, इ (said to be fr. rt.<BR>स्पृश्, the initial स् being elided, see Uṇādi-s. IV. 52),<BR>variegated, party-coloured, dappled, piebald, speckled,<BR>spotted (used in the Veda as a favourite epithet of<BR>cows); manifold, diverse, various, of many kinds<BR>(Ved.); dwarfish, stunted, short, thin, small; deli-<BR>cate, feeble; (इस्), f. (like all other words for ‘cow’<BR>used in various figurative or mythical senses, viz.)<BR>earth, a cloud, milk, the spangled or starry sky, a<BR>ray of light; a kind of fruit; N. of the mother of<BR>the Maruts; of the wife of Savitṛ; of the wife of<BR>king Su-tapas (who in a former birth under the name<BR>of Devakī was mother of Kṛṣṇa); (ई), f. the plant<BR>Pistia Stratiotes; (इस्), m. a dwarf; N. of a prince<BR>the father of Śvaphalka; (अयस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>race of Ṛṣis; पृश्नि or भरद्वाजस्य पृश्नि,<BR>N. of a Sāman; [cf. rts. पृष् and स्पृश्; पृष्-<BR>अत, पृषत्, पृषटी: Gr. περκ-νό-ς, πέρκο-ς,<BR>περκαίνειν, πρακ-νό-ν, πρεκ-νό-ν, πρόξ, προκά-ς,<BR>πρώξ, πρόκ-νη: Lat. spurc-u-s, sparg-o: Old<BR>Germ. spreng-en: Mod. Germ. be-spreng-en = Eng.<BR>sprinkle.]<BR>—पृश्नि-गर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in<BR>the variegated bosom or in the bosom of the varie-<BR>gated one (Sāy. = आदित्यस्य गर्भ-भूत or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-a" target="_blank">Page0596-a+ 80</a>]<BR>सप्तोज्ज्वल-वर्णाः सूर्य-रश्मयस् तेषां गर्-<BR>भ-भूत); (अस्), m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पृश्नि-गु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. driving piebald horses<BR>(said of the Maruts; Sāy. = पृश्नि-वर्णा अश्वा<BR>येषां ते); (उस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—पृश्नि-त्व,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. the being variegated or party-coloured,<BR>the being speckled or spotted.<BR>—पृश्नि-धर, अस्,<BR>m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पृश्नि-निप्रेषित, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. sent down or hastening down to Pṛśni,<BR>i. e. to the earth (said of the Maruts); (Sāy.) =<BR>पृश्न्या मात्रा नितराम् प्रयताः, sent down<BR>by their mother Pṛśni.<BR>—पृश्नि-पर्णी, f. ‘having<BR>variegated leaves,’ N. of a plant, Hemionitis Cordi-<BR>folia.<BR>—पृश्नि-बाहु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. having speckled<BR>arms, i. e. front legs (said of a frog); (उस्), m., N.<BR>of a mythical being.<BR>—पृश्नि-भद्र, अस्, m. ‘pro-<BR>pitious to Devakī,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—पृश्नि-<BR>मत् or पृश्नि-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing<BR>the word पृश्नि.<BR>—पृश्नि-मातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved.<BR>‘having Pṛśni for a mother,’ an epithet of the<BR>Maruts; ‘having the earth for a mother,’ an epithet<BR>of herbs.<BR>—पृश्नि-शृङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘having a small<BR>or a variegated crest,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu<BR>incarnate as Kṛṣṇa; of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—पृश्नि-सक्थ,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having spotted thighs.<BR>—पृश्नि-<BR>हन्, आ, m., Ved. slaying the speckled (snake).<BR>—पृश्न्य्-आह्वया, f. = पृश्नि-पर्णी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निका
पृश्निका, f. an aquatic plant, Pistia Stratiotes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्
पृष् पृष् (akin to rt. प्रुष्; cf. rts.<BR>स्पृश् and वृष्), cl. 1. P. पर्षति, प-<BR>पर्ष, पर्षिष्यति, अपर्षीत्, पर्षितुम्, to<BR>sprinkle; to weary; to vex; to hurt, injure; to give;<BR>cl. 1. A. पर्षते, पर्षितुम् (a various reading<BR>for rt. वृष्), to become wet: Caus. पर्षयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अपपर्षत्, अपीपृशत्: Desid. पि-<BR>पर्षिषति: Intens. परीपृश्यते, परीपर्ष्टि:<BR>[cf. पृश्नि; Zend परेष्, ‘to sprinkle.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्|पृषन्त्
पृषत्, अन्, अती, अत्, (Ved.) spotted, speckled,<BR>mottled, dappled, piebald, party-coloured, variegated;<BR>sprinkling (in this sense used as a part.); (अन्),<BR>m. the spotted antelope; the hog deer, porcine<BR>deer; पृषताम् पतिः, ‘lord of the spotted ante-<BR>lopes,’ a N. of the Wind; (अती), f. a spotted cow;<BR>epithet of the animals ridden by the Maruts (usually<BR>said by commentators to be spotted antelopes, ac-<BR>cording to Mahī-dhara piebald mares, and often<BR>apparently identified in the Ṛg-veda with the horses<BR>of the Maruts); the female spotted antelope, spotted<BR>doe; = पार्षती, the daughter of Pṛṣata; (अत्), n. a<BR>drop of water or of any other liquid.<BR>—पृषत्-ता, f. or<BR>पृषत्-त्व, अम्, n. the being spotted or variegated.<BR>—पृषद्-अश्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘having piebald<BR>horses,’ an epithet of the Maruts; (according to Sāy.)<BR>riding on spotted antelopes; (अस्), m. air, wind, the<BR>god of air or wind divinely personified; an epithet<BR>of Śiva; N. of a man; of a son of An-araṇya and<BR>father of Hary-aśva; of a son of Vi-rūpa; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of the descendants of Pṛṣad-aśva.<BR>—पृषद्-<BR>आज्य, अम्, n. sprinkled or clotted butter, ghee mixed<BR>with coagulated milk forming an oblation.<BR>—पृषद्-<BR>आज्य-प्रणुत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. driven away from<BR>the oblation of ghee and curds.<BR>—पृषद्-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. party-coloured, variegated.<BR>—पृषद्-<BR>वत्स, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having a spotted calf.<BR>—पृ-<BR>षद्-वरा, f. ‘the best among the variegated ante-<BR>lopes,’ N. of a wife of Ruru and daughter of a Vidhyā-<BR>dhara by Menakā (a sort of antelope).<BR>—पृषद्-<BR>वल, अस्, m. ‘piebald,’ N. of a horse of Vāyu or<BR>Wind; [cf. पृषद्-अश्व.]<BR>—पृषद्-वाण, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having variegated arrows,’ N. of a man.<BR>—पृ-<BR>षोदर, अस्, आ, अम् (पृष for पृषत् + उदर),<BR>Ved. ‘speckled-bellied,’ having the belly speckled,<BR>(see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VI. 3, 109.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत|पृषतः
पृषत, अस्, आ, अम्, spotted, speckled, having<BR>white spots, variegated; (अस्), m. the spotted ante-<BR>lope, the porcine deer; a drop of water; a spot,<BR>mark; N. of the father of Dru-pada.<BR>—पृषताश्व<BR>(˚त-अश्˚), अस्, m. air, wind (= पृषद्-अश्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्क|पृषत्कः
पृषत्क, अस्, m. an arrow (so called as being<BR>variegated or as being as swift as an antelope).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषद्धर
पृषद्धर or पृषध्र, अस्, m. (probably a<BR>comp. fr. पृषत् + ध्र), N. of a man the son<BR>of Manu and author of the hymn Ṛg-veda VIII.<BR>57 (= Vālakhilya 8).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषध्रु
पृषध्रु, उस्, m., N. of a warrior on the side<BR>of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषन्ति|पृषंति|पृषंतिः|पृषन्तिः
पृषन्ति, इस्, m. a drop of water (probably an<BR>error for पृषन्ति, n. pl. of पृषत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषातक|पृषातकं
पृषातक, अम्, n. a mixture of ghee and coagu-<BR>lated milk or some similar compound; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Rudra; (ई), f. a kind of disease or N. of<BR>a female demon causing this disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोद्यान|पृषोद्यानं
पृषोद्यान, अम्, n. (fr. पृष for पृषत् +<BR>उद्यान), a small garden or grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट
1. पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. and 3. see below),<BR>sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषभाषा
पृषभाषा पृष-भाषा, f. = पूष-भासा,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषाकरा
पृषाकरा पृषाकरा, f. a small stone used<BR>as a weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट
पृष्ट 2. पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for स्पृष्ट fr. rt.<BR>स्पृश्), Ved. cleaving or adhering to, in contact<BR>with (Sāy. = सं-स्पृष्ट, or = नि-षिक्त = नि-<BR>हित).<BR>—पृष्ट-बन्धु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. (perhaps)<BR>having devoted relatives or attendants; (Sāy.) = स्तो-<BR>तॄणाम् बन्धुः, a friend to those who praise him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टि|पृष्टिः
पृष्टि, इस्, f., Ved. a rib (= पर्शु); touch; a<BR>ray of light.<BR>—पृष्टि-वह्, वाट्, m., Ved. carrying<BR>on the back (as a horse).<BR>—पृष्ट्य्-आमय, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. a pain in the side.<BR>—पृष्ट्य्-आमयिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, Ved. feeling a pain in the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट
पृष्ट 3. पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. प्रछ्),<BR>asked, inquired, questioned, interrogated, demanded.<BR>—पृष्टाभिधायिन् (˚ट-अभ्˚), ई, इनी, इ, Ved. an-<BR>swering that which is asked, answering an inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट्वा
पृष्ट्वा, ind. having asked or inquired, having<BR>questioned or interrogated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टहायन|पृष्टहायनः
पृष्टहायन पृष्टहायन, अस्, m. an ele-<BR>phant; a species of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ|पृष्ठं
पृष्ठ पृष्ठ, अम्, n. (probably fr. प्र-स्थ<BR>or perhaps fr. परा-स्थ), the back of any animal<BR>(as standing out prominently), the back in general<BR>(e. g. अश्व-पृष्ठे सम्मतः, admired on horse-<BR>back, i. e. a good rider; पृष्ठं दा, to bend<BR>the back, make a low obeisance); the hinder part<BR>of anything, the rear [cf. सेना-प्˚]; the upper side,<BR>uppermost part, surface, superficies (e. g. दिवः<BR>पृष्ठम्, Ved. the surface of the sky, vault of<BR>heaven; cf. घृत-प्˚, तृ-प्˚, नाक-प्˚); the flat<BR>roof of a house; a terrace; a page of a book; N.<BR>of a particular arrangement of Sāmans employed at<BR>the midday oblation, and formed from the Rathan-<BR>tara, Bṛhat, Vairūpa, Vairāja, Śākvara, and Raivata<BR>Sāmans, (in this sense more usually written as a<BR>comp. पृष्ठ-स्तोत्र, q. v.); N. of various Sā-<BR>mans; (एन, ए), ind. at the back, behind, from<BR>behind.<BR>—पृष्ठ-गोप, अस्, m. one who guards<BR>or protects the rear of a warrior while fighting.<BR>—पृष्ठ-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. ‘back-knot,’ a hump<BR>on the back.<BR>—पृष्ठ-घ्न, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—पृष्ठ-चक्षुस्, उस्, m. ‘having eyes in<BR>the back,’ a crab.<BR>—पृष्ठ-ज, अस्, m. a form of<BR>Skanda; (also considered as a son of Skanda.)<BR>—पृष्ठ-जाह, अम्, n. = पृष्ठस्य मूलम्,<BR>‘the root of the back,’ (probably) os coccygis; [cf.<BR>जाह.]<BR>—पृष्ठ-तल्पन, अम्, n. the exterior<BR>muscles on an elephant's back (= तल्पन).<BR>—पृष्-<BR>ठ-दृष्टि, इस्, m. ‘looking backwards,’ a bear.<BR>—पृष्ठ-पातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, being behind the<BR>back of a person, following, observing, controlling.<BR>—पृष्ठ-फल, अम्, n. the superficial contents<BR>of a figure.<BR>—पृष्ठ-भङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘breaking<BR>or bending the back,’ epithet of a mode of fighting.<BR>—पृष्ठ-भाग, अस्, m. the hinder part, back.<BR>—पृष्ठ-मध्य, अस्, m. the middle of the<BR>back.<BR>—पृष्ठ-मांस, अम्, n. the flesh on the<BR>back; पृष्ठमांसं खाद् or भक्ष्, ‘to eat<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">Page0596-c+ 79</a>]<BR>the flesh of a person's back,’ i. e. to speak ill of any<BR>one behind his back.<BR>—पृष्ठमांसाद (˚स-<BR>अद˚) or पृष्ठमांसादन (˚स-अद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘eating the flesh of the back,’ backbiting, speaking<BR>ill of a person behind his back, a backbiter, tale-<BR>bearer, slanderer; (अम्), n. backbiting.<BR>—पृष्ठ-<BR>यज्वन्, आ, m., Ved. one who sacrifices on high<BR>places (Sāy. = रथन्तर-बृहद्-आदिभिर् ईजान).<BR>—पृष्ठ-यान, अम्, n. ‘going on the back (of<BR>a horse &c.), riding; (अस्, आ, अम्), an animal for<BR>riding, riding horse.<BR>—पृष्ठ-रक्ष, अस्, m. one<BR>who covers the rear of a warrior while fighting;<BR>[cf. पृष्ठ-गोप.]<BR>—पृष्ठ-रक्षण, अम्,<BR>n. protection or defence of the back.<BR>—पृष्ठ-<BR>वंश, अस्, m. the back-bone.<BR>—पृष्ठ-वास्तु, उ,<BR>n. an upper story, the upper room of a building.<BR>—पृष्ठ-वाह्, ट्, m. (f. पृष्ठौही, see Gram.<BR>182. c), a draught-ox, an ox employed for draught,<BR>(also read प्रष्ठ-वाह् and पष्ठ-वाह्); ‘borne<BR>on the back,’ riding.<BR>—पृष्ठ-वाह्य, अस्, m. a<BR>draught-ox, an ox carrying burdens.<BR>—पृष्ठ-<BR>शय, अस्, आ, अम्, lying or sleeping on the back.<BR>—पृष्ठ-शृङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘having horns over the<BR>back,’ a wild goat.<BR>—पृष्ठ-शृङ्गिन्, ई, m. a<BR>ram; a buffalo; a eunuch; an epithet of Bhīma-sena.<BR>—पृष्ठ-स्तोत्र, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>arrangement of Sāmans (= पृष्ठ, q. v.).<BR>—पृष्-<BR>ठानुग (˚ठ-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, or पृष्ठानु-<BR>गामिन् (˚ठ-अन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, going behind, following<BR>(opposed to अग्र-ग).<BR>—पृष्ठास्थि (˚ठ-अस्˚),<BR>इ, n. the back-bone.<BR>—पृष्ठे-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having the face in the back.<BR>—पृष्ठोदय (˚ठ-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘rising from behind,’ an epithet of<BR>the signs of the zodiac, Aries, Taurus, Gemini,<BR>Sagittarius, and Capricorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठक|पृष्ठकं
पृष्ठक, अम्, n. the back; पृष्ठके कृ,<BR>to place behind, postpone; to resign, renounce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठतस्
पृष्ठ-तस्, ind. from the back, from behind,<BR>behind the back, at the back, behind (with gen.);<BR>to the back, backwards; on the back; behind the<BR>back, secretly, covertly; पृष्ठतः कृ, to place<BR>on the back (e. g. पर्वतम् पृष्ठतः कृत्वा,<BR>having placed the mountain on his back); to place<BR>behind the back, neglect, forsake, abandon; to re-<BR>sign, renounce, desist from; पृष्ठतो गम्, to go<BR>at the back, follow, pursue; पृष्ठतो भू, to be<BR>behind, i. e. to be disregarded, to be an object of<BR>indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ्य|पृष्ठ्यं|पृष्ठ्यः
पृष्ठ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>the back; belonging to or coming from the heights<BR>(Ved., e. g. पृष्ठ्यम् पयः, ‘milk from the<BR>heights,’ i. e. Soma, or according to Sāy. = धार-<BR>कम् पयः, sustaining milk); forming the Pṛṣṭha<BR>hymns (Ved.); having the Pṛṣṭha hymns (said of<BR>a particular period of six sacrificial days, Ved.); (अस्),<BR>m. with or without अश्व, a horse for riding or for<BR>draught, a pack-horse; (अस्, अम्), m. n. = पृष्ठा-<BR>नां समूहः [cf. Pāṇ. IV. 2, 42] = स्तोत्राणां<BR>समूहः (Ujjvala-datta on Uṇādi-s. II. 12); (आ),<BR>f. with or without अश्वा, a mare for riding or for<BR>draught; an edge or ridge along the back of the<BR>Vedi (Ved.).<BR>—पृष्ठ्य-स्तोम, अस्, m., Ved., N.<BR>of six Ekāhas or of a period of six sacrificial days.<BR>—पृष्ठ्यावलम्ब (˚य-अव्˚), अस्, m., Ved.,<BR>scil. पञ्चाह, a period of five sacrificial days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णि|पृष्णिः
पृष्णि पृष्णि, इस्, इस्, इ, small, short, or thin<BR>(= पृश्नि); (इस्), f. the heel (= पार्ष्णि); a ray of<BR>light (= पृश्नि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णिपर्णी
पृष्णिपर्णी पृष्णि-पर्णी, f. a wrong read-<BR>ing for पृश्नि-पर्णी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्वा
पृष्वा पृष्वा, incorrectly for प्रुष्वा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पॄ
पॄ पॄ [cf. rts. 1. and 2. पृ, पृण्], cl. 9.<BR>and 3. P. (Ved. also A.) पृणाति (-णीते),<BR>पिपर्ति (3rd du. पिपृतस् or पिपूर्तस्, Vopa-deva<BR>X. 5), पपार (3rd du. पपरतुस् or पप्रतुस्,<BR>3rd pl. पपरुस् or पप्रुस्, Pāṇ. VII. 4, 12),<BR>परिष्यति, परीष्यति, अपारीत्, Prec. पूर्यात्, प-<BR>रितुम्, परीतु (Ved. forms, Impf. 3rd sing. A.<BR>अपिप्रत, Impv. 2nd sing. पूर्धि, Aor. पर्षि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">Page0597-a+ 74</a>]<BR>पर्षत्, पारिषत्; irregular Impv. 2nd sing. A.<BR>पिपीपृहि?), to fill, fill up; to fulfil; to sate,<BR>satisfy, refresh (e. g. पितॄन् अपारीत्, he satisfied or<BR>refreshed the Manes); to cherish, nourish, nurture,<BR>foster, rear, bring up; to protect; to bestow bounti-<BR>fully, grant abundantly, give plentifully, lavish (with<BR>acc. of the thing and dat. of the person, Ved.); to<BR>collect, accumulate; (A.) to fill or sate one's self;<BR>cl. 4. A. (properly Pass. but ep. also P.), पूर्यते<BR>(-ति), Aor. अपूरि, अपूरिष्ट, to be filled, become<BR>full, to be fulfilled; to be sated or satisfied; Caus.<BR>पारयति, -यितुम् [cf. Caus. of rt. 1. पृ], to fill,<BR>fulfil (Ved.); पूरयति, -ते, -यितुम् (sometimes<BR>regarded as derived fr. a separate rt. पूर्, q. v.),<BR>to fill, fill up, replenish; to fulfil (a wish, hope,<BR>promise, &c.); to make full, fill out, intensify,<BR>strengthen (a sound); to fill with wind, blow, wind<BR>(a conch-shell or other wind instrument); to draw<BR>(a bow, or an arrow to the ear); to cover completely,<BR>cover up, surround, envelop; to load or enrich (with<BR>gifts); to spend the whole (of a period of time):<BR>Desid. पिपरिषति, पिपरीषति, पुपूर्षति, पु-<BR>पूर्षते: Intens. पोपूर्यते, पापर्ति, पोपूर्ति;<BR>[cf. rt. 1. प्रा, 3. पुर्, पुर, पुरु, पुलु: Zend<BR>par, ‘fill;’ perena, ‘full:’ Gr. πί-μ-πλη-μι, πλή-θ-ω,<BR>πλέ-ω-ς, πλή-ρ-ης, πλη-θ-ύ-ς, πλῆ-θ-ος,<BR>πλοῦ-το-ς: Lat. im-ple-o, plē-nu-s, plē-be-s, pŏ-pul-u-s,<BR>multus said to be for pūrtas, am-plu-s: Goth.<BR>full-s, ‘full;’ fullo, ‘fulness;’ full-yan, ‘to fill:’<BR>Old Germ. fol, folc: Angl. Sax. fyll-an: Mod.<BR>Germ. voll = Eng. full: Slav. plŭ-nŭ, ‘full;’ plŭ-<BR>kŭ, ‘people;’ ple-me, ‘a tribe:’ Lith. pil-ti, ‘to<BR>fill;’ pī1l-na-s, ‘full;’ pùl-ka-s, ‘crowd:’ Hib. pailt,<BR>‘abundant, plentiful, copious.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचक|पेचकः
पेचक पेचक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>पच्), an owl; the tip or the root of an elephant's<BR>tail; a couch, bed; a louse; a cloud; (इका), f. a<BR>kind of owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचकिन्
पेचकिन्, ई, m. an elephant; (also read पिचकिन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचिल|पेचिलः
पेचिल, अस्, m. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचु
पेचु पेचु, उ, n. or पेचुली, f. a species of bul-<BR>bous plant with esculent roots, Colocasia Antiquorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेज
पेज पेज in तिल-पेज, q. v.; (आ), f. = पेया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेञ्जूष|पेंजूष|पेंजूषः|पेञ्जूषः
पेञ्जूष पेञ्जूष, अस्, m. the wax of the ear<BR>(= पिञ्जूष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेट|पेटः
पेट पेट, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, m. f. n. (said to<BR>be fr. rt. पिट्, q. v.), a basket, a large basket, bag; a<BR>chest; a multitude; a retinue; (अस्), m. the open<BR>hand with the fingers expanded (= प्र-हस्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटक|पेटकं|पेटकः
पेटक, अस्, इका, अम्, m. f. n. [cf. पिटक], a<BR>basket for holding clothes, books, &c.; (अम्), n.<BR>multitude, company, quantity; (इका), f. a species of<BR>plant (= कुलिङ्गाक्षी, कुवेराक्षी, कृष्ण-वृन्-<BR>तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटाक|पेटाकः
पेटाक, अस्, m. a basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेडा
पेडा, f. a basket, large basket (= पेटा, for which<BR>it is perhaps only a wrong reading).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेट्टिभट्ट
पेट्टिभट्ट पेट्टि-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a man<BR>the father of the commentator Viśveśvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेढाल
पेढाल पेढाल, अस्, m., N. of the eighth<BR>Arhat of the future Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेण्
पेण् पेण् [cf. rts. पैण्, प्रैण्, लैण्], cl.<BR>1. P. पेणति, &c., to go; to send (?); to<BR>grind (?); to embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेत्व|पेत्वं|पेत्वः
पेत्व पेत्व, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. पा?), a ram,<BR>sheep (Ved.); a small part; (अम्), n. nectar, Amṛta;<BR>ghee or clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेदु
पेदु पेदु, उस्, m., Ved., N. of a man (under<BR>the especial protection of the Aśvins, by whom he was<BR>presented with a white horse that killed serpents).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेपीयमान
पेपीयमान पेपीयमान, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. In-<BR>tens. of rt. 1. पा), drinking repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेब्
पेब् पेब्, cl. 1. A. पेबते, a various<BR>reading for rt. सेव्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेय|पेयं
पेय पेय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. पा), to be<BR>drunk or quaffed, fit to be drunk, drinkable, potable;<BR>tastable, sapid; (अस्), m., scil. यज्ञ-क्रतु, a<BR>drink offering, libation (Ved.); (आ), f. rice gruel;<BR>any drink with a small quantity of boiled rice; the<BR>decoction of anything after straining; a species of<BR>anise, = मिश्रेया; (अम्), n. a drink, beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरु|पेरुः
1. पेरु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. (according to Mahī-dhara)<BR>drinking; (उस्), m. the sun; fire; the ocean; the<BR>golden mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयूष|पेयूषं|पेयूषः
पेयूष पेयूष, अस्, अम्, m. n. (= पीयूष,<BR>q. v), the milk of a cow that has calved within seven<BR>days, biestings; fresh butter; nectar, Amṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरज
पेरज पेरज, or पेरोज, अम्, n. a turquoise<BR>(= Pers. فيروزه).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरा
पेरा पेरा, f. a kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरु|पेरुः
पेरु 2. पेरु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. 1. पृ; for 1.<BR>पेरु see above), Ved. drawing through, carrying<BR>across; leading through, delivering, rescuing; (Sāy.<BR>= पूरक, as if fr. rt. पॄ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरु|पेरुः
पेरु 3. पेरु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. rt. प्यै), Ved.<BR>swelling; causing to ferment; (Sāy. = सर्वस्य<BR>रक्षक, as if fr. rt. 3. पा); (उस्), m. a limb,<BR>member (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरुक
पेरुक पेरुक, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल्
पेल् पेल्, cl. 1. 10. P. पेलति, पेलितुम्,<BR>पेलयति, -यितुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल|पेलं|पेलः
पेल, अस्, m. going; a small part; (अम्), n. a<BR>testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलक|पेलकः
पेलक, अस्, m. a testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलव|पेलवं
पेलव, अस्, आ, अम्, delicate, fine, soft, tender;<BR>thin, slim, slender.<BR>—पेलव-पुष्प, अम्, n. a<BR>tender flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलि|पेलिः
पेलि, (perhaps) = पेलिन्, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. VI. 2, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलिन्
पेलिन्, ई, m. a horse.<BR>—पेलि-शाला, f. a horse-stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलोज
पेलोज पेलोज, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेव्
पेव् पेव् [cf. rt. पेब्], cl. 1. A. पेवते,<BR>पेवितुम्, a various reading for rt. सेव्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेश|पेशः
पेश पेश, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. पिश्), Ved. =<BR>पेशस्, q. v.; [cf. पुरु-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशन
पेशन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. well formed, well made;<BR>decorated, adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशल|पेशलः
पेशल, अस्, आ, अम्, artificially formed, adorned,<BR>decorated; beautiful, charming, lovely, pleasant;<BR>soft, smooth, tender; skilful, dexterous, expert,<BR>clever, ingenious; fraudulent, deceitful, crafty; (अम्),<BR>n. beauty, loveliness; [cf. Gr. ποικ-ίλο-ς, ποικἰλλ-ω:<BR>Lat. ping-o, pic-tor, pic-tura: Old Germ. feh,<BR>‘variegated:’ Slav. pĭstrŭ, ‘variegated;’ pis-ati,<BR>‘to write:’ Lith. pisz-nu-s, ‘splendid.’]<BR>—पेशल-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. dexterity, skill.<BR>—पेशल-मध्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, slender-waisted, having a delicate or slender<BR>waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशस्
पेशस्, अस्, n., Ved. shape, form; an artificial figure,<BR>ornament, decoration, embroidery; variety of colour,<BR>brilliance; gold; [cf. अश्व-प्˚, ऋत-प्˚.]<BR>—पेशस्-<BR>कारी, f., Ved. a woman who weaves artistically or<BR>embroiders.<BR>—पेशस्-कृत्, त्, m. ‘the artist,’ an epi-<BR>thet of the hand; a species of insect, a kind of wasp.<BR>—पेशस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. decorated, adorned,<BR>ornamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशि|पेशिः
पेशि, इस्, m. a thunderbolt (for पेषि); (इस्), f. an<BR>egg; split pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशिका
पेशिका, f. (fr. पेशी), rind, shell (of fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशितृ
पेशितृ, ता, m., Ved. one who cuts in pieces or<BR>carves, a carver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशी
पेशी, f. a piece of flesh or meat [cf. पिशित]; a<BR>ball or mass of flesh; the fetus shortly after con-<BR>ception; a muscle (of which there are said to be five<BR>hundred in the human body); the peel or rind (of<BR>fruit); a kind of drum; a sheath, scabbard; a shoe;<BR>the egg of a bird; spikenard, Valeriana Jatamansi;<BR>a blown bud; N. of a Piśācī; of a Rākṣasī; of a<BR>river.<BR>—पेशी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">Page0597-c+ 74</a>]<BR>-कर्तुम्, to cut into pieces, to carve.<BR>—पेशी-कोश or<BR>पेशी-कोष, अस्, m. a bird's egg.<BR>—पेश्य्-अण्ड, अम्,<BR>n. a bird's egg; a piece of flesh; the fetus shortly<BR>after conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेश्वर
पेश्वर, अस्, आ, अम् (? for पेष्वर fr. rt. पिष्),<BR>who or what grinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष्
पेष् पेष् [cf. rt. येष्], cl. 1. A. पेषते,<BR>पेषितुम्, to exert one's self or strive<BR>diligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष|पेषः
पेष पेष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पिष्), pounding,<BR>grinding; [cf. शिला-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषक
पेषक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who pounds or grinds,<BR>a grinder, grinding, pounding, pulverizing, masti-<BR>cating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषण|पेषणं
पेषण, अम्, n. pounding, grinding, crushing,<BR>triturating, pulverizing by means of a mill, (पेषणं<BR>या, to be ground); a threshing-floor; a hand-mill,<BR>a stone and muller, any apparatus for grinding or<BR>pounding; a plant, a species of Euphorbia with three<BR>lobes, Euphorbia Antiquorum (= शत-गुप्ता, Ben-<BR>gālī तेकाटोसिज).<BR>—पेषण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, a word<BR>formed for the explanation of पिपिष्वत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषणि|पेषणिः
पेषणि, इस्, ई, f. a stone slab on which condi-<BR>ments are ground, a muller, mill-stone, grind-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषणीय
पेषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ground or pounded,<BR>fit to be ground or pulverized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषाक|पेषाकः
पेषाक, अस्, m. a small slab for grinding anything<BR>upon, a grind-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषि|पेषिः
पेषि, इस्, m. a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष्टृ
पेष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, one who pounds or crushes,<BR>one who grinds, a grinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष्य
पेष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pounded or ground, to<BR>be triturated or pulverized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषल|पेषलः
पेषल पेषल, अस्, आ, अम्, = पेशल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषी
पेषी पेषी, f., Ved. (according to Sāy.) =<BR>हिंसिका, पिशाचिका, a malevolent spirit, female Pi-<BR>śāca; (perhaps) a nurse; spikenard (in this sense a<BR>various reading for पेशी, q. v.).<BR>—पेषी-कृ, a various<BR>reading for पेशी-कृ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष्ट्र
पेष्ट्र पेष्ट्र, अम्, n. (perhaps fr. rt. 1. पिश्),<BR>Ved. a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस्
पेस् पेस् (= rt. पिस्), cl. 1. P. पेसति,<BR>पेसितुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेसुक
पेसुक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. पिस्), Ved. spreading,<BR>extending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस्वर
पेस्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, going, moving; destructive;<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेसल|पेसलः
पेसल पेसल = पेशल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पै
पै पै, cl. 1. P. पायति, पायितुम्, to dry,<BR>wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्ग
पैङ्ग पैङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिङ्ग), belong-<BR>ing or relating to a rat or mouse; derived from or<BR>composed by Paiṅgya (as a book); acknowledged<BR>by the Paiṅgins; (अम्), n., N. of a work; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a teacher (in this sense perhaps a wrong<BR>reading for पैङ्ग्य).<BR>—पैङ्ग-राज, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्गि|पैंगि|पैंगिः|पैङ्गिः
पैङ्गि, इस्, m. (fr. पिङ्ग), a patronymic of Yāska.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्गिन्
पैङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, derived from Paiṅgya; (ई),<BR>m. a follower of Paiṅgya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्ग्य
पैङ्ग्य, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. पिङ्ग), N.<BR>of a teacher; (अम्), n. the doctrine or the manual of<BR>Paiṅgya.<BR>—पैङ्गी-पुत्र, अस्, m. (fr. पैङ्गी, f.<BR>of पैङ्ग्य, + पुत्र), Ved., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्गल|पैङ्गलः
पैङ्गल पैङ्गल, आस्, m. pl. a patronymic<BR>from Piṅgala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्गलायन
पैङ्गलायन, अस्, or पैङ्गलायनि, इस्, m. a<BR>patronymic from Piṅgala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्गल्य
पैङ्गल्य, अम्, n. the treatise of Piṅgala; brown<BR>or tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैच्छिल्य
पैच्छिल्य पैच्छिल्य, अम्, n. (fr. पिच्छिल),<BR>sliminess, mucilaginousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैजवन
पैजवन पैजवन, अस्, m. (fr. पिजवन), a<BR>patronymic of Su-dās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैञ्जूष|पैंजूष|पैंजूषः|पैञ्जूषः
पैञ्जूष पैञ्जूष, अस्, m. the ear; [cf. पिञ्-<BR>जूष, पेञ्जूष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैटकिक
पैटकिक पैटकिक or पैटाकिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>= पिटाकेन हरति, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैठर|पैठरं
पैठर पैठर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिठर),<BR>cooked in a saucepan, boiled in a vessel or pot (as<BR>meat &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैठीनसि|पैठीनसिः
पैठीनसि पैठीनसि, इस्, or पैठीनस्, आस्,<BR>m. patronymic of an ancient teacher, a Muni and<BR>author of a system of laws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्
पैण् पैण् [cf. rts. पेण्, लैण्, प्रैण्], cl. 1.<BR>P. पैणति, पैणितुम्, to go, approach;<BR>to command, direct (an act); to send; to touch or<BR>embrace; to pound, grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्डपातिक
पैण्डपातिक पैण्डपातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>पिण्ड-पात), living on alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्डायन
पैण्डायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Piṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्डिन्य|पैंडिन्य|पैंडिन्यं|पैण्डिन्यं
पैण्डिन्य, अम्, n. (fr. पिण्डिन्), living on alms,<BR>mendicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतदारव
पैतदारव पैतदारव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पीत-<BR>दारु), see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. IV. 3, 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतापुत्रीय
पैतापुत्रीय पैतापुत्रीय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिता-<BR>पुत्र), relating to father and son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामह|पैतामहं
पैतामह पैतामह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिता-<BR>मह), belonging or relating to a paternal grand-<BR>father; derived or inherited from a grandfather;<BR>belonging or relating to Brahmā, derived from<BR>Brahmā, governed or presided over by Brahmā;<BR>(अस्), m. a son of Brahmā, a patronymic of Manu;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. forefathers, ancestors.<BR>—पैतामह-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामहिक
पैतामहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिता-मह), be-<BR>longing or relating to a grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृक|पैतृकं
पैतृक पैतृक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पितृ), belong-<BR>ing or relating to a father or to ancestors generally,<BR>coming or derived from a father, paternal, ancestral;<BR>belonging or relating to the Manes, sacred to the<BR>Manes; (अम्), n. a sacred rite or Śrāddha in honour<BR>of the Manes or deceased ancestors.<BR>—पैतृक-<BR>धन, अम्, n. ancestral property, patrimony.<BR>—पै-<BR>तृक-भूमि, इस्, f. the country of one's ancestors,<BR>fatherland; a paternal estate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृमत्य|पैतृमत्यः
पैतृमत्य, अस्, m. (fr. पितृ-मत्), sprung<BR>from one who has an illustrious father, the grandson<BR>of an illustrious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृयज्ञिक
पैतृयज्ञिक, Ved. or पैतृयज्ञीय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. पितृ-यज्ञ), belonging or relating to a<BR>sacrifice to the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृष्वसेय|पैतृष्वसेयः
पैतृष्वसेय or पैतृष्वस्रीय, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. पितृ-ष्वसृ), sprung from a father's sister<BR>or paternal aunt; (अस्), m. a father's sister's son,<BR>the son of a paternal aunt; (ई), f. a father's sister's<BR>daughter, the daughter of a paternal aunt (see Manu<BR>XI. 171).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र|पैत्रं
पैत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पितृ), belonging or re-<BR>lating to a father or to ancestors generally, paternal,<BR>ancestral; belonging or relating to the Manes, sacred<BR>or consecrated to the Manes; (अम्), n. the part of<BR>the hand between the thumb and fore-finger, (ac-<BR>cording to others) the root of the fore-finger [cf.<BR>पितृ-तीर्थ]; a year or month or day of the<BR>Pitṛs.<BR>—पैत्राहोरात्र (˚र-अह्˚), अस्, m. a day and<BR>night of the Pitṛs or progenitors (= one month).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्रिक
पैत्रिक = पैतृक (for which it is probably an<BR>incorrect form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र्य
पैत्र्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पितृ), belonging or re-<BR>lating to the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्त|पैत्तः
पैत्त पैत्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पित्त), relating to<BR>the bilious humor, proceeding from bile, bilious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तिक|पैत्तिकः
पैत्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, bilious, of a bilious tem-<BR>perament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तल
पैत्तल पैत्तल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पित्तल), made<BR>of brass, brazen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैद्व
पैद्व पैद्व, अस्, m., Ved. scil. अश्व, the<BR>horse of Pedu said to be a serpent-killer (Ṛg-<BR>veda IX. 88, 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैनाक
पैनाक पैनाक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिनाकिन्),<BR>belonging to or coming from Rudra-Śiva; (अस्), m.<BR>a patronymic from Pināka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पल
पैप्पल पैप्पल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिप्पल),<BR>made of the wood of the holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पलाद
पैप्पलाद, अस्, ई, अम्, derived from Pippalāda;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पलादक
पैप्पलादक, अस्, ई, अम्, peculiar to or taught<BR>by Pippalāda or Paippalāda; (अम्), n. the treatise or<BR>text of Pippalāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पलादि
पैप्पलादि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Pippa-<BR>lāda; N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैयवन
पैयवन पैयवन, an incorrect form for<BR>पैजवन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैयूष
पैयूष पैयूष, अम्, n. = पीयूष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैल|पैलः
पैल पैल, अस्, m. a metronymic from<BR>Pīlā; N. of a teacher (a sage and promulgator of<BR>the Ṛg-veda).<BR>—पैल-गर्ग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—पैल-गर्भ, अस्, m. ‘offspring of Paila,’ N. of<BR>a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलेय
पैलेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Pīlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलव
पैलव पैलव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पीलु), made of<BR>the wood of the Pīlu tree (as the staff borne by a<BR>Vaiśya, Manu II. 45).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशल्य|पैशल्यं
पैशल्य पैशल्य, अम्, n. (fr. पेशल), kind-<BR>liness, graciousness, affability, mildness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच|पैशाचः
पैशाच पैशाच, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or be-<BR>longing to a Piśāca or kind of demon, infernal,<BR>demoniacal; पैशाचो ग्रहः, demoniacal possession;<BR>(अस्), m. the eighth and lowest from of marriage, one<BR>of the eight forms of marriage according to Manu<BR>(described in Manu III. 34 as taking place when a<BR>lover secretly embraces a damsel either sleeping or<BR>intoxicated or disordered in her intellect); a Piśāca<BR>or kind of demon; (ई), f. a present made at a<BR>religious ceremony to secure friendly regard; a sort<BR>of gibberish spoken by demons on the stage [cf. पि-<BR>शाच-भाषा]; night; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाचिक
पैशाचिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to a<BR>Piśāca or kind of demon, infernal, demoniacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन|पैशुनं
पैशुन पैशुन or पैशुन्य, अम्, n. (fr. पि-<BR>शुन), the act of informing or giving information,<BR>tale-bearing, backbiting, calumny, espionage, report-<BR>ing evil of others, malignity, roguery, depravity,<BR>wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्ट|पैष्टः
पैष्ट पैष्ट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिष्ट), made of<BR>flour, ground or made up into a cake; (ई), f. spirituous<BR>liquor distilled from meal or extracted from bruised<BR>rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिक|पैष्टिकं
पैष्टिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिष्ट), made of meal<BR>or flour; (अम्), n. a quantity of cakes; spirituous<BR>liquor distilled from meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोगण्ड|पोगंड|पोगण्डः
पोगण्ड पोगण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, not full-grown<BR>or adult, young; deformed, deficient in a member;<BR>having a redundant member; (अस्), m. a boy, one<BR>from his fifth to his sixteenth year; [cf. अ-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्ड|पौगंड|पौगण्डं
पौगण्ड, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>boy, boyish; (अम्), n. boyhood (a period lasting<BR>from the fifth to the tenth year).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्डक
पौगण्डक, अम्, n. boyhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट|पोटः
पोट पोट, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. पुट्),<BR>the foundation of a house [cf. पोत]; putting to-<BR>gether, uniting, mixing; (आ), f. a woman with a<BR>beard; a hermaphrodite; a female servant or slave;<BR>(ई), f. the rectum; a large alligator.<BR>—पोट-गल,<BR>अस्, m. a species of reed, Arundo Tibialis; a kind<BR>of grass, Saccharum Spontaneum; a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटक|पोटकः
पोटक, अस्, m. a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटाय
पोटाय, Nom. A. पोटायते, &c., = पोटां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटलक|पोटलकः
पोटलक पोटलक, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>or पोटलिका, f. a bundle or packet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट्टली
पोट्टली, f. a bundle, parcel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटिक|पोटिकः
पोटिक पोटिक, अस्, m. a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट्टिल
पोट्टिल पोट्टिल, अस्, m. (with Jainas) N. of<BR>the ninth Arhat of the future Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोडु|पोडुः
पोडु पोडु, उस्, m. the parietal bone, the<BR>bone forming the upper part of the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत|पोतः
पोत पोत, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. पू,<BR>but probably fr. a lost rt. पु, ‘to beget’), the young<BR>of any animal [cf. मृग-प्˚]; a colt, foal; a young<BR>elephant ten years old; a young plant or tree, the young<BR>shoot of a plant; a fetus which has no enveloping mem-<BR>brane; cloth, a garment; the foundation of a house [cf.<BR>पोट]; the site of a house or dwelling; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. a vessel, ship, boat; [cf. पुत्र, २. पुंस्; Gr. πῶλο-ς<BR>for ποϝ-λο-ς, πωλ-ίο-ν, πά-ϊ(δ)ς for παϝ-ι(δ)ς,<BR>πο-ία, πό-α, perhaps ποιέ-ω fr. a form ποιο as in παιδο-<BR>ποιό-ς; Lat. pullu-s, Marci-por, pu-er for pov-er,<BR>pu-era, pu-su-s, pusa, pū-pu-s, pū-pa, pūpilla,<BR>pu-tu-s, pūbes, pum-ilu-s, pumil-io, prœ-pu-tiu-m,<BR>pō-mu-m for pov-mu-m, pa-pav-er; Goth. fula (n),<BR>fula = Old Germ. folo = Eng. foal; Lith. pauta-s,<BR>‘an egg.’]<BR>—पोत-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced or de-<BR>veloped from a fetus which has no enveloping mem-<BR>brane (said of elephants and certain other quadrupeds,<BR>as opposed to men, cattle, &c., which are called<BR>जरायु-ज).<BR>—पोत-धारिन्, ई, m. a ship-owner,<BR>master of a vessel.<BR>—पोत-प्लव, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>‘floating in a ship,’ a seaman, mariner.<BR>—पोत-<BR>बणिज्, क्, m. ‘ship-merchant,’ a voyaging merchant,<BR>sea-faring trader.<BR>—पोत-भङ्ग, अस्, m. shipwreck.<BR>—पोत-रक्ष, अस्, m. ‘ship-governing,’ a large<BR>paddle used for a rudder, the rudder of a boat.<BR>—पोत-वाह, अस्, m. ‘boat-conductor,’ a rower,<BR>boatman, steersman, one of the crew who keeps<BR>watch at the mast-head.<BR>—पोताच्छादन (˚त-<BR>आच्˚), अम्, n. ‘cloth-covering,’ a tent.<BR>—पोता-<BR>धान (˚त-आध्˚), अम्, n. small fry, a shoal of<BR>young fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतक|पोतकः
पोतक, अस्, m. the young of any animal; a young<BR>plant or tree (e. g. चूत-पोतक, a young mango-<BR>tree); N. of a Nāga; the site or foundation of a<BR>house [cf. गृह-प्˚]; (इका), f. a kind of vegetable,<BR>Basella Lucida or Rubra; Anethum Sowa, = शत-<BR>पुष्पा; (अकी), f. Basella Lucida or Rubra; a kind<BR>of bird, Turdus Macrourus (= श्यामा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतल
पोतल, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a sea-<BR>port on the Indus (the Παράλα of the ancients);<BR>N. of the residence of the Dalai Lama in Lhassa<BR>(also called पोतरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतलक
पोतलक, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a moun-<BR>tain (= पोतल?).<BR>—पोतलक-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘fond<BR>of the mountain Potalaka,’ N. of a Buddha; of a<BR>Jina or deified teacher of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतु
पोतु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. पू), = मानभाण्ड-<BR>शोधक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतृ
पोतृ, ता, m. ‘the purifier,’ an epithet of one of<BR>the sixteen officiating priests (ऋत्व्-इज्) at a sacrifice,<BR>the assistant of the Brahman, (Sāy. = पोतृ-नाम-<BR>कर्त्विज् or यज्ञस्य शोधयितृ); an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्या
पोत्या, f. = पोतानां समूहः, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्र|पोत्रं
पोत्र, अम्, n. the Soma vessel of the Potṛ, the<BR>office of the Potṛ, (Sāy. = पोत्रा कृतं कर्म,<BR>पोतुर् यज्ञः); a ship, boat [cf. पोत]; the<BR>snout of a hog; a ploughshare; a dress, garment (?);<BR>a thunderbolt (?).<BR>—पोत्र-मण्डल, अम्, n. ‘snout-<BR>orb,’ the round snout (of a hog &c.).<BR>—पोत्रा-<BR>युध (˚र-आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘armed with a snout,’ a<BR>hog, boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिन्
पोत्रिन्, ई, m. a hog, boar.<BR>—पोत्रि-दंष्ट्रा-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘produced in the tusk of a boar,’ a kind of<BR>gem supposed to be found in the tusk of a boar.<BR>—पोत्रि-रथा, f. ‘hog-vehicled,’ (with Buddhists)<BR>an epithet of Māyā; (with Jainas) N. of a Śakti or<BR>female divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रीय
पोत्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating or belonging to<BR>the Potṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोपुव
पोपुव, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. Intens. of rt. 1. पू),<BR>purifying or cleansing much or repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिक
पौतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, connected with a boat (as<BR>a cargo &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोताल
पोताल पोताल, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman;<BR>a wrong reading for पोतल, p. 598, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतास|पोतासः
पोतास पोतास, अस्, m. a species of camphor;<BR>[cf. Eng. potash.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतिमत्सक
पोतिमत्सक पोतिमत्सक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोथकी
पोथकी पोथकी, f. a kind of ulcer on the<BR>eyelids, red pimples on the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोथिक
पोथिक पोथिक, अस्, or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>in अव-प्˚, a machine for hurling down stones, fire-<BR>brands, and fiery darts upon the enemy, a kind of<BR>ballista (?); [cf. सोल्कालातावपोथिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोयालदह
पोयालदह पोयालदह, अस्, or अम्, m. or<BR>n. (?), N. of a tank or pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोर
पोर पोर, अस्, m. in नील-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोल|पोलः
पोल पोल, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पुल्), magnitude,<BR>bulk; a heap, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोलिका
पोलिका पोलिका, f. flat cakes made of barley<BR>or wheat, &c.; [cf. पूलिका, पौली, पूपाली.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोली
पोली, f. a kind of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोलिन्द|पोलिंद|पोलिंदः|पोलिन्दः
पोलिन्द पोलिन्द, अस्, m. the mast or the<BR>ribs of a ship or boat; [cf. पदार, पादारक,<BR>पादालिन्द.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोविय
पोविय पोविय, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>the commentator Gaṅga-dāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष|पोषः
पोष पोष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. पुष्), thriving,<BR>growth, increase; welfare, prosperity, plenty, abun-<BR>dance; nourishing, cherishing; maintaining, sup-<BR>porting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषक|पोषकः
पोषक, अस्, m. one who feeds or nourishes; a<BR>nourisher, supporter, breeder, keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषण|पोषणं
पोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, nourishing, cherishing [cf.<BR>पक्ष-प्˚]; bringing up, breeding; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of nourishing, cherishing, fostering, supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषणीय
पोषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cherished or pro-<BR>tected, to be nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषयितृ
पोषयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, nourishing, cherishing,<BR>one who breeds or rears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषयित्नु|पोषयित्नुः
पोषयित्नु, उस्, उस्, उ, causing to grow, nourish-<BR>ing, cherishing (Ved.); (उस्), m. (according to a<BR>Scholiast) the Koïl or Kokila or Indian cuckoo;<BR>(probably) a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषयिष्णु
पोषयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. causing to thrive,<BR>nourishing, causing prosperity or welfare, advan-<BR>tageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषित
पोषित, अस्, आ, अम्, nourished, cherished, fostered,<BR>supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषितव्य
पोषितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cherished or pro-<BR>tected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषितृ
पोषितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, nourishing, feeding; one<BR>who breeds or rears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषिन्
पोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, nourishing, bringing up, rearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषुक
पोषुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. prospering, growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्टृ
पोष्टृ, टा, ट्री, टृ, a nourisher, cherisher, one<BR>who brings up; (टा), m. a protector, nourisher,<BR>cherisher; grey bonduc.<BR>—पोष्टृ-वर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>the best of nourishers, nourishing best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्य|पोष्यः
पोष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, well-fed, thriving; causing<BR>welfare or prosperity, prosperous; to be nourished<BR>or cherished, to be taken care of, to be fed, to be<BR>brought up; copious.<BR>—पोष्य-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>one who is to be cherished; being taken care of.<BR>—पोष्य-पुत्र or पोष्य-पुत्रक, अस्, m. ‘a son<BR>to be brought up,’ an adopted son.<BR>—पोष्यपुत्र-<BR>करण, अम्, n. adoption.<BR>—पोष्य-वर्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>class of persons or objects to be cherished, as parents,<BR>children, guests, and the sacred fire; a family, house-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">Page0599-b+ 72</a>]<BR>hold.<BR>—पोष्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. causing pros-<BR>perity; (Sāy. = बहु-पोष्य-जन-युक्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषध|पोषधः
पोषध पोषध, अस्, m. (with Buddhists)<BR>renewal of religious vows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषधिक
पोषधिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (perhaps) one who renews<BR>religious vows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चलीय
पौंश्चलीय पौंश्चलीय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुंश्-<BR>चली), belonging or relating to harlots, meretricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चलेय|पौंश्चलेयः
पौंश्चलेय, अस्, m., Ved. the son of a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चल्य|पौंश्चल्यं
पौंश्चल्य, अम्, n. female incontinency, harlotry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंसवन|पौंसवनं
पौंसवन पौंसवन, अम्, n. (fr. पुं-स-<BR>वन), one of the Saṃskāras or essential ceremonies<BR>of the Hindū religion; a religious observance held<BR>when signs of a living conception take place (in<BR>order to obtain male offspring).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंस्न|पौंस्नं
पौंस्न पौंस्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. पुंस्), worthy<BR>of or fit for a man; relating to or good for man;<BR>manly, virile; human; (अम्), n. manhood, manly<BR>strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंस्य|पौंस्यं
पौंस्य, अम्, n., Ved. manhood, virility, manly<BR>power; the courage or virtue of a man, a manly<BR>deed (Sāy. = बल); (अस्, &c.), masculine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्ड|पौगंड|पौगण्डं
पौगण्ड पौगण्ड. See पोगण्ड, p. 598.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौञ्जिष्ठ
पौञ्जिष्ठ पौञ्जिष्ठ or पौञ्जिष्ट (?), अस्,<BR>m., Ved. (= पुञ्जिष्ठ), a fisherman; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डरीक|पौंडरीक|पौण्डरीकं|पौण्डरीकः
पौण्डरीक पौण्डरीक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुण्ड-<BR>रीक), consisting of lotus-flowers; (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of Soma sacrifice lasting twelve days (Ved.); a pa-<BR>tronymic of Kṣema-dhṛtvan; (अम्), n., scil. कुष्-<BR>ठ, a kind of leprosy; a species of plant (= प्र-<BR>पौण्डरीक).<BR>—पौण्डरीक-पद्धति, इस्, f., N.<BR>of a ritual work containing the prayers used at the<BR>Pauṇḍarīka sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डर्य|पौंडर्यं|पौण्डर्य्य|पौण्डर्य्यं
पौण्डर्य पौण्डर्य, अम्, n. a kind of drug<BR>used as a remedy for diseased eyes (= पुण्डर्य,<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्र|पौंड्र|पौंड्रः|पौण्ड्रः
पौण्ड्र पौण्ड्र, अस्, m. (fr. पुण्ड्र), a species<BR>of sugar-cane of a pale straw colour; N. of a country<BR>(said to include part of South Behar and Bengal);<BR>N. of a king of this country (regarded as a son of<BR>Vasu-deva); N. of the conch-shell of Bhīṣma; a<BR>mark, sectarial mark; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>the inhabitants of the Pauṇḍra country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रक|पौंड्रक|पौंड्रकः|पौण्ड्रकः
पौण्ड्रक, अस्, ई, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>= पौण्ड्र; (अस्), m. the pale straw-coloured<BR>species of sugar-cane; epithet of a particular mixed<BR>caste of hereditary sugar-boilers, (the son of a Vaiśya<BR>by a woman of the distiller class; regarded as one of<BR>the degraded races of Kṣatriyas, Manu X. 44);<BR>a king of the Pauṇḍras; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people, the Pauṇḍras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रनागर
पौण्ड्रनागर, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VII.<BR>3, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रमात्स्यक
पौण्ड्रमात्स्यक, अस्, m. (probably) a king of<BR>the Puṇḍras and Matsyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रवत्स
पौण्ड्रवत्स, आस्, m. pl. (fr. पुण्ड्र + वत्स),<BR>N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रवर्धन|पौण्ड्रवर्द्धनः|पौण्ड्रवर्धनः
पौण्ड्रवर्धन, अम्, n., N. of a city, =<BR>पुण्ड्र-वर्धन; (अस्), m., N. of a country, one<BR>of the divisions of central India, Behar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रिक|पौंड्रिक|पौंड्रिकः|पौण्ड्रिकः
पौण्ड्रिक, अस्, m. a pale straw-coloured variety<BR>of the sugar-cane; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्य
पौण्य पौण्य, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुण्य), up-<BR>right, righteous, virtuous, deserving good treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतन
पौतन पौतन (perhaps fr. पूतना), N. of<BR>a country or people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतव|पौतवं
पौतव पौतव, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>पू), a measure; (also spelt यौतव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिक
पौतिक पौतिक. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिकी
पौतिकी पौतिकी, f. = पूतिका, a kind of<BR>vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिनासिक्य
पौतिनासिक्य पौतिनासिक्य, अम्, n. (fr. पूति-<BR>नासिका), fetor of the nostrils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिमाषीपुत्र
पौतिमाषीपुत्र पौतिमाषी-पुत्र, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिमाष्य
पौतिमाष्य, अस्, m., Ved. (a patronymic fr.<BR>पूति-माष), N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिमाष्यायण
पौतिमाष्यायण, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic<BR>from Pautimāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्तिक|पौत्तिकं
पौत्तिक पौत्तिक, अम्, n. (fr. पुत्तिका), scil.<BR>मधु, the honey of the small bee called पुत्तिका;<BR>pale-coloured honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्र|पौत्त्रः|पौत्रः
पौत्र 1. पौत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुत्र), de-<BR>rived from a son or from children, belonging or<BR>relating to a son or to children; (अस्), m. a son's<BR>son, grandson; (ई), f. a granddaughter (either in the<BR>male or female line, though more usually implying<BR>a son's daughter); an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रजीविक
पौत्रजीविक, अम्, n. (fr. पुत्र-जीव), an amulet<BR>made of the nuts of the tree Putranjiva Roxburghii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्राघ
पौत्राघ (˚र-अघ˚), अम्, n., Ved. any injury<BR>or evil happening to children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्राद्य
पौत्राद्य, perhaps a wrong reading for the pre-<BR>ceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रायण
पौत्रायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Pautra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिक
पौत्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुत्र or 1. पौत्र),<BR>belonging to a son or grandson; (अस्), m. the son<BR>of a Putrikā (?); a patronymic from Putrika (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिकेय|पौत्रिकेयः
पौत्रिकेय, अस्, m. (fr. पुत्रिका), the son of a<BR>daughter appointed to raise issue for her father.<BR>—पौत्रिकेय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having for a grand-<BR>son the son of a daughter appointed to raise issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिन्
पौत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. 1. पौत्र), having a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्र|पौत्त्रः|पौत्रः
पौत्र 2. पौत्र, अम्, n. (fr. पोतृ, q. v.),<BR>Ved. the office of the Potṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौदन्य
पौदन्य पौदन्य, अम्, n., N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुनिक|पौनःपुनिकः
पौनःपुनिक पौनःपुनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>पुनः-पुनः), frequently reiterated, repeated again<BR>and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुन्य|पौनःपुन्यं
पौनःपुन्य, अम्, n. frequent reiteration, con-<BR>stant repetition; (एन), ind. again and again, re-<BR>peatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनराधेयिक
पौनराधेयिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुनर्-आधेय),<BR>Ved. relating to the rite of replacing or renewing the<BR>sacrificial fire; [cf. पुनर्-आधेयिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्त|पौनरुक्तं
पौनरुक्त, अम्, n. (fr. पुनर्-उक्त), repe-<BR>tition, tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्तिक
पौनरुक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, see Gaṇa Ukthādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्त्य|पौनरुक्त्यं
पौनरुक्त्य, अम्, n. repetition, tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्नव
पौनर्नव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुनर्-नवा), relat-<BR>ing or belonging to the plant Boerhavia Procumbens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भव|पौनर्भवः
पौनर्भव, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पुनर्-भू), re-<BR>peated, additional; relating or belonging to a widow<BR>who has married a second husband; (अस्), m. the<BR>son of a widow remarried, the offspring of a twice-<BR>married woman by her second husband, one of the<BR>sons or heirs admitted by the old Hindū law; पौ-<BR>नर्भवो भर्ता, a woman's second husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भविक
पौनर्भविक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुनर्-भव),<BR>relating to regeneration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौम्पा
पौम्पा पौम्पा, f., N. of a sacred lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर|पौरं|पौरः
पौर 1. पौर, अस्, m. (fr. 1. पुर् or fr. rt.<BR>पॄ?), Ved. ‘filling, sating,’ an epithet of Soma (Sāy.<BR>= उदर-पूरक); ‘filler, increaser,’ an epithet of<BR>the Aśvins; an epithet of Indra (Sāy. = पूरयितृ);<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi the author of the hymns Ṛg-veda V.<BR>73, 74; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर|पौरं|पौरः
पौर 2. पौर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुर, see 3. पुर्),<BR>belonging to a town or city, produced in a town<BR>or city; (अस्), m. a townsman, burgher, citizen (op-<BR>posed to जानपद); = नागर, a term for a prince<BR>engaged in war under certain circumstances and (in<BR>astrology) applied to a planet in a state of opposition<BR>to other planets; (ई), f. the language or conversation<BR>of the servants in a palace; (अम्), n. a species of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">Page0600-a+ 75</a>]<BR>fragrant grass (= रौहिष).<BR>—पौर-जन, अस्, m.<BR>a person belonging to the town, townsman, citizen.<BR>—पौर-जानपद, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to town<BR>and country; (आस्), m. pl. citizens and rustics, towns-<BR>men and country people.<BR>—पौर-योषित्, त्, or<BR>पौर-स्त्री or पौराङ्गना (˚र-अङ्˚), f. a woman<BR>living in a town or city.<BR>—पौर-लोक, आस्, m. pl.<BR>city people, citizens.<BR>—पौर-वृद्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>distinguished or eminent citizen, alderman.<BR>—पौर-<BR>सख्य, अम्, n. fellow-citizenship, connection or<BR>equality with others formed by inhabiting the same<BR>city for ten years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरक|पौरकं|पौरकः
पौरक, अस्, m. a garden in the neighbourhood<BR>of a city; a garden round a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरञ्जन
पौरञ्जन, अस्, ई, अम्, sprung or descended<BR>from Purañ-jana and Purañ-janī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरन्दर
पौरन्दर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरन्-दर), be-<BR>longing or relating to Indra, derived or coming from<BR>Indra, sacred to Indra; (अम्), n. the Nakṣatra<BR>Jyeṣṭhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरिक|पौरिकः
पौरिक, अस्, m. (fr. पुर), a townsman, citizen;<BR>a governor of a city; N. of a prince of the city of<BR>Purikā; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरेय
पौरेय, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to a<BR>town or city, civic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरव|पौरवः
पौरव पौरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूरु), be-<BR>longing to or descended from Pūru, of the race of<BR>Pūru; (अस्), m. a descendant of Pūru; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the descendants or the race of Pūru; N. of a people<BR>in the north or north-east of India; (ई), f., N. of the<BR>wife of Vasu-deva; of the wife of Yudhi-ṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवक
पौरवक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवतन्तव
पौरवतन्तव, अस्, m. (probably fr. पूरु +<BR>तन्तु), in पर-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवीय
पौरवीय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूरु), devoted to<BR>Paurava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्य|पौरस्त्यः
पौरस्त्य पौरस्त्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. पुरस्),<BR>situated in front, foremost; eastern; previous, pre-<BR>ceding, former, prior, first, initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराण
पौराण पौराण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुराण),<BR>belonging or relating to the past, of the past, of<BR>ancient occurrence, derived from or belonging to<BR>past ages, primeval, ancient; belonging to former<BR>times, former, previous; relating to the Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराणिक|पौराणिकः
पौराणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the past or to past ages; familiar with the events<BR>and legends of the past; relating or belonging to<BR>the Purāṇas, Paurānic; worth a Purāṇa, of the<BR>value of one Purāṇa; (अस्), m. a Brāhman well-<BR>read in the Purāṇas or a public expounder of them;<BR>a mythologist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरिक|पौरिकः
पौरिक पौरिक. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुकुत्स
पौरुकुत्स पौरुकुत्स, अस्, or पौरुकुत्सि,<BR>इस्, or पौरुकुत्स्य, अस्, m. (fr. पुरु-कुत्स), a<BR>patronymic of Trasa-dasyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुमद्ग
पौरुमद्ग पौरुमद्ग, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुमह्न
पौरुमह्न पौरुमह्न, अम्, n. (fr. पुरु-<BR>मह्न), N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुमीढ
पौरुमीढ पौरुमीढ or पौरुमीऌह, अम्,<BR>n. (fr. पुरु-मीढ), N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुशिष्टि
पौरुशिष्टि पौरुशिष्टि, इस्, m. (fr. पुरु +<BR>शिष्ट), Ved., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष|पौरुषं|पौरुषः
पौरुष पौरुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरुष),<BR>belonging or relating to a man or to man in general,<BR>manly, virile, human; relating or belonging to Pu-<BR>rusha, sacred to Puruṣa; being of the length of a<BR>man with both arms elevated and the fingers ex-<BR>tended; (अस्), m. (according to Kullūka) = पुरुष-<BR>वाह्य-भार, a weight or load which can be carried<BR>by one man; (ई), f. a woman; (अम्), n. manhood,<BR>manliness, manly strength or courage, heroism,<BR>strength, power, vigour; human action, action of<BR>men, man's work, action; effort, exertion; the<BR>measure of a man, the height to which he reaches<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">Page0600-b+ 75</a>]<BR>with both arms elevated and the fingers extended;<BR>generation; semen virile; the penis; a sun-dial.<BR>—पौरुष-ता, f. or पौरुष-त्व, अम्, n. man-<BR>hood, manly strength or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषमेधिक
पौरुषमेधिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरुष-<BR>मेध), Ved. relating or belonging to a human<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषविधिक
पौरुषविधिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = पुरुष-विध,<BR>man-like, resembling man, human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषांसकिन्
पौरुषांसकिन्, इनस्, m. pl. the school of Pu-<BR>ruṣāṃsaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषाद
पौरुषाद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरुषाद), relating<BR>or belonging to man-eaters or cannibals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषिक|पौरुषिकः
पौरुषिक, अस्, m. a worshipper of Puruṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषेय|पौरुषेयः
पौरुषेय, अस्, ई, अम्, derived from or relating<BR>to man, incidental to man, made by man, human,<BR>manly, male, virile; coming from the soul, spiritual;<BR>(अस्), m. a hireling, day-labourer; a crowd or num-<BR>ber of men (?); manslaughter, murder; law as<BR>affecting persons; (अम्), n. human action, the work<BR>of man.<BR>—पौरुषेय-त्व, अम्, n. humanity, human<BR>origin, the human element (in sacred writings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष्य|पौरुष्यं
पौरुष्य, अस्, -षी, अम्, relating to Puruṣa;<BR>(अम्), n. manliness, manly strength or courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुहन्मन
पौरुहन्मन पौरुहन्मन, अम्, n. (fr. पुरु-<BR>हन्मन्), N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुहूत
पौरुहूत पौरुहूत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरु-<BR>हूत), belonging to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरूरवस
पौरूरवस पौरूरवस, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging<BR>or relating to Purū-ravas; (अस्), m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरेय
पौरेय पौरेय. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोगव|पौरोगवः
पौरोगव पौरोगव, अस्, m. (fr. पुरो-गव),<BR>an overseer or superintendent of a royal household,<BR>especially the inspector of the royal kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाश|पौरोडाशः
पौरोडाश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरो-डाश), see Gaṇa<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 62; (अस्), m. a Mantra recited upon<BR>making an oblation of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाशिक|पौरोडाशिकः
पौरोडाशिक, अस्, m. (fr. पुरो-डाश), a priest<BR>who recites the Mantra used in offering an oblation<BR>of clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोधस|पौरोधसं
पौरोधस, अस्, m. a patronymic from Puro-dhas;<BR>(अम्), n. the office or function of a family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोभाग्य|पौरोभाग्यं
पौरोभाग्य, अम्, n. (fr. पुरो-भागिन्), envy,<BR>jealousy, malevolence, ill-will, censoriousness; ob-<BR>trusiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोहित
पौरोहित, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुरो-हित), belonging<BR>to a Puro-hita, coming or proceeding from a family<BR>priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोहित्य|पौरोहित्यं
पौरोहित्य, अस्, -ती, अम्, belonging to the family<BR>of a Puro-hita; (अम्), n. the character or office of a<BR>family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णदर्व
पौर्णदर्व पौर्णदर्व, अम्, n. = पूर्ण-<BR>दर्व, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास|पौर्णमासः
पौर्णमास, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्ण-मास), re-<BR>lating or belonging to the full moon, usual or cus-<BR>tomary at full moon, having the full moon; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. a ceremony performed at the full moon<BR>by persons maintaining a perpetual fire; a patro-<BR>nymic; N. of a son of Marīci and Sambhūti; of a<BR>prince of the Āndhra dynasty; (अम्), n. a day of<BR>full moon; (ई), f. a day or night of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमासायन
पौर्णमासायन, अम्, n. (fr. the preceding),<BR>Ved. a kind of sacrifice offered at the full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमासिक
पौर्णमासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पौर्णमास),<BR>used for the sacrifice offered at the full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास्य|पौर्णमास्यं
पौर्णमास्य, अम्, n., scil. कर्मन्, a sacrifice<BR>offered at the full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमी
पौर्णमी, f. a day of full moon (= पूर्णिमा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिम|पौर्णिमः
पौर्णिम, अस्, m. (fr. पूर्णिमा), an ascetic;<BR>(आ), f. a day of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्त
पौर्त पौर्त, अम्, n. (fr. पूर्त), scil. कर्-<BR>मन्, a meritorious work (= पूर्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्तिक|पौर्त्तिक
पौर्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to a<BR>meritorious work (as the feeding of a Brāhman<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व|पौर्व्व
पौर्व पौर्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्व), relating<BR>or belonging to the past; relating to the east,<BR>eastern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वदेहिक|पौर्व्वदेहिक
पौर्वदेहिक or पौर्वदैहिक, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. पूर्व-देह), belonging or relating to a former<BR>body, belonging or relating to a former life or<BR>existence; derived from a former existence, done in<BR>a former life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वपञ्चालक
पौर्वपञ्चालक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्व-पञ्-<BR>चाल), = पूर्वः पञ्चालानाम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वपदिक|पौर्व्वपदिक
पौर्वपदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्व-पद),<BR>relating to the first member of a compound; (pro-<BR>bably) pronouncing the first member of a compound<BR>(in teaching).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्ववर्षिक
पौर्ववर्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = पूर्वासु वर्-<BR>षासु भवः, Scholiast on Pāṇ. VII. 3, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वशाल
पौर्वशाल, अस्, ई, अम्, = पूर्वस्यां शालायाम्<BR>भवः, Scholiast on Pāṇ. IV. 2, 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वातिथ
पौर्वातिथ, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from<BR>Pūrvātithi; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वापर्य|पौर्वापर्यं|पौर्वापर्य्य|पौर्व्वापर्य्य
पौर्वापर्य, अम्, n. (fr. पूर्वापर), priority<BR>and posteriority, the relation of prior and posterior,<BR>succession, continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वार्ध
पौर्वार्ध or पौर्वार्धिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>पूर्वार्ध), living or situated on the eastern side<BR>of (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिकः
पौर्वाह्णिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्वाह्ण), be-<BR>longing or relating to the morning, produced in the<BR>forenoon, matutinal; (often wrongly spelt पौर्वाह्-<BR>निक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्विक|पौर्व्विक
पौर्विक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पूर्व), former, pre-<BR>vious, prior, primary; ancient, old; ancestral; (ई),<BR>f. an ancestress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलस्त्य|पौलस्त्यः
पौलस्त्य पौलस्त्य, अस्, -स्ती, अम्, relating to<BR>or descended from Pulasti or Pulastya; (अस्), m. a<BR>patronymic from Pulasti or Pulastya; an epithet of<BR>Kuvera; of Rāvaṇa; of Vibhīṣaṇa; of the moon;<BR>N. of an astronomer; (आस्), m. pl. an epithet of the<BR>brothers of Dur-yodhana; (पौलस्ती), f. a patro-<BR>nymic of Śūrpa-ṇakhā the sister of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलि|पौलिः
पौलि पौलि, इस्, ई, m. f. grain half dressed<BR>or scorched or fried with ghee and made into a<BR>sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलिका
पौलिका, f. a kind of cake (= पौलि; perhaps<BR>an error for पोलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलिश
पौलिश पौलिश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुलिश), de-<BR>rived from or composed by Puliśa.<BR>—पौलिश-सिद्-<BR>धान्त, अस्, m., N. of an astronomical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलुषि
पौलुषि पौलुषि, इस्, m. (fr. पुलुष), Ved.<BR>a patronymic of Satya-yajña.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोम|पौलोमः
पौलोम पौलोम, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or<BR>treating of Pulomā, an epithet of Adhyāyas 4-12 of<BR>the Ādi-parva of the Mahā-bhārata; relating to<BR>Puloman or Pulomā or Paulomī; descended from<BR>Puloman or Pulomā; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>demons; (ई), f. the daughter of Puloman, an epithet<BR>of the wife of Indra; (अस्), m. an epithet of Indra;<BR>a Muni.<BR>—पौलोमी-मङ्गल, अस्, आ, अम्, as for-<BR>tunate or happy as Paulomī.<BR>—पौलोमी-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m. born from Paulomī, son of Paulomī (an<BR>epithet of Jayanta, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौल्कस
पौल्कस पौल्कस, अस्, m., Ved. (= पुल्कस,<BR>said to be) the son of a Niṣāda or of a Śūdra<BR>father and of a Kṣatriyā mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष|पौषः
पौष पौष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुष्य), relating<BR>to or occurring at the time when the moon is in the<BR>asterism Puṣya; (अस्), m., N. of a month, the<BR>month Pauṣa (December-January, when the full<BR>moon is in the asterism Puṣya); N. of the third<BR>year in the twelve years' cycle of Jupiter; (ई), f. the<BR>night or day of full moon in the month Pauṣa;<BR>(अम्), n. a festival or a particular festival; a fight,<BR>combat; N. of various Sāmans; [cf. पौष्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कर|पौष्करं
पौष्कर पौष्कर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुष्कर),<BR>relating to the blue lotus-flower, made or consisting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">Page0601-a+ 71</a>]<BR>of blue lotuses, treating of the blue lotus; (with<BR>प्रादुर्-भाव) the appearance of Viṣṇu in the<BR>form of a lotus-flower; belonging to or derived from<BR>Costus Speciosus or C. Arabicus; (अम्), n. the root or<BR>fruit of the plant Costus Speciosus or C. Arabicus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करक
पौष्करक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the blue<BR>lotus-flower, consisting of blue lotuses; (with प्रा-<BR>दुर्-भाव) the appearance of Viṣṇu in the form<BR>of a lotus-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करसादि
पौष्करसादि, इस्, m. (a patronymic fr. पुष्-<BR>कर-सद्), N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करिणी
पौष्करिणी, f. = पुष्करिणी, a lotus-pool, a<BR>large pond or reservoir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करेयक
पौष्करेयक, अस्, ई, अम्, see Gaṇa to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कल|पौष्कलः
पौष्कल पौष्कल, अस्, m. (fr. पुष्कल),<BR>a species of grain; (अम्), n., N. of various Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कलावति
पौष्कलावति, इस्, m. (fr. पुष्कला-वती), N.<BR>of a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कल्य|पौष्कल्यं
पौष्कल्य, अम्, n. full growth, maturity, com-<BR>plete development.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्टिक|पौष्टिकं
पौष्टिक पौष्टिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुष्टि),<BR>relating to or promoting growth or welfare; nutri-<BR>tious, nourishing, nutritive, fattening, invigorating;<BR>preservative, protective; (अम्), n. a cloth worn dur-<BR>ing the ceremony of tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्टी
पौष्टी, f. (probably fr. पुष्ट), N. of the wife<BR>of Pūru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्ण|पौष्णं
पौष्ण पौष्ण, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or<BR>relating to Pūṣan, sacred to Pūṣan; relating to the<BR>sun; (अम्), n. the last of the twenty-eight lunar<BR>asterisms; the Nakṣatra Revatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्प|पौष्पं
पौष्प पौष्प, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पुष्प), re-<BR>lating or belonging to flowers, coming from flowers,<BR>made of flowers, flowery, floral; (ई), f. the city of<BR>Pāṭali-putra (= पुष्प-पुर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पक|पौष्पकं
पौष्पक, अम्, n. oxide of brass considered as<BR>a collyrium, green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पिञ्जि
पौष्पिञ्जि पौष्पिञ्जि, इस्, m. a patronymic;<BR>N. of a teacher; (also read पौष्यिञ्जि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पिण्ड्य
पौष्पिण्ड्य पौष्पिण्ड्य, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>ancient teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्य|पौष्यः
पौष्य पौष्य, अस्, -षी (?) , अम् (fr. पुष्य),<BR>relating to the asterism Puṣya; (fr. पौष्य), re-<BR>lating to or treating of king Pauṣya, an epithet of<BR>the third Adhyāya of the Ādi-parva of the Mahā-<BR>bhārata; (अस्), m., N. of a prince the son of Pūṣan<BR>and king of Karavīra-pura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ना
प्ना प्ना, f. the braided hair of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याट्
प्याट् प्याट्, ind. a particle used in calling,<BR>ho! holla!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याय्
प्याय् प्याय्. See rt. प्यै below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युक्ष्ण
प्युक्ष्ण प्युक्ष्ण, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>Ved. a covering for a bow (made of sinews or of<BR>the skin of a serpent, see Kātyāyana's Śrauta-s. XV.<BR>3, 31).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युष्
प्युष् प्युष्, cl. 4. 10. P. प्युष्यति, प्यो-<BR>षयति, &c., a various reading for rt.<BR>व्युष्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युस्
प्युस् प्युस्, cl. 4. P. प्युस्यति, &c., a<BR>various reading for rt. व्युष्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यै
प्यै प्यै or प्याय् (developed out of a<BR>Vedic rt. पी; cf. rt. पिन्व्), cl. 1. A. प्या-<BR>यते (Ved. पयते), पिप्ये (Ved. पीपाय), प्यास्-<BR>यते, प्यायिष्यते, अप्यास्त, अप्यायिष्ट, अप्यायि,<BR>प्यातुम्, प्यायितुम्, to swell, become swollen or<BR>distended; to be exuberant; to become full; to<BR>increase, grow; to overflow; to cause to swell,<BR>distend; to fill to excess, overfill, surcharge, cause to<BR>run over or overflow: Caus. प्याययति, -यितुम्,<BR>(with आ, see आ-प्यै.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यान
प्यान, अस्, आ, अम्, fat, swollen, grown fat, =<BR>पीन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यायन
प्यायन, अस्, ई, अम्, promoting growth or in-<BR>crease (according to a Scholiast = वृद्धि-हेतु),<BR>causing to thrive; invigorating; (अम्), n. growth,<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यायित
प्यायित, अस्, आ, अम्, fat, grown fat; increased;<BR>strengthened, refreshed; = पीन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र 1. प्र (as a preposition or prefix to<BR>verbs and their derivative nouns, expressing) before,<BR>forward, in advance, in front, onward, forth, away<BR>(e. g. प्र-गम्, to go forward, proceed; प्र-स्था,<BR>to set out; प्र-स्थान, going away, departure;<BR>प्र-क्रम्, to walk onwards, to begin, commence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र is also used in the Veda as a separable adverb,<BR>and the verb of motion is then sometimes to be<BR>supplied, e. g. प्र चक्रियेव रोदसी मरुद्भ्यः,<BR>heaven and earth (have been caused) by the Maruts<BR>(to roll) onward like two wheels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र is also compounded with nouns not imme-<BR>diately connected with verbs in the sense of ‘forth,’<BR>‘away;’ and before adjectives in the sense of ‘pre-<BR>eminently,’ ‘excessively,’ ‘very,’ ‘much;’ [cf. प्र-<BR>पौत्र.]<BR>According to native lexicographers the senses in<BR>which प्र may be used are expressed by the follow-<BR>ing Sanskrit words, गति, आ-रम्भ, उत्-कर्ष,<BR>सर्वतो-भाव, प्राथम्य, ख्याति, उत्-पत्ति, व्य्-<BR>अवहार; [cf. प्र-तरम्, प्र-नप्तृ, प्रथम,<BR>परा, पूर्व, प्रातर्: Zend fra-, frā, ‘before,<BR>away:’ Gr. πρό, πρό-τερος, πρῶ-το-ς (Dor. πρᾶ-<BR>το-ς), πρό-μο-ς, πρύ-τανι-ς (Æol. πρό-τανι-ς), πρίν<BR> for προ-ιν, πρω-ΐ, πρῴην (Dor. πράν), πρόσσω,<BR>πρό-σω, πόρ-σω, πόῥῥω: Lat. prō-d, prō, prŏ- in<BR>prŏ-nepos, prœ for prai, prīmu-s for pro-imus,<BR>pri-or, pris- = prius for pro-ios, pris-tinu-s, pris-<BR>cu-s, pran-diu-m, porro, perhaps pru-īna for<BR>provīna: Umbr. pru = pro; pre = prœ; perne,<BR>‘in front;’ pernaio, ‘ancient;’ per, ‘for (?):’ Goth.<BR>fru-ma, ‘first;’ frum-ist, ‘at first;’ fairra, ‘far:’<BR>Old Germ. fur-iro, ‘former;’ furisto, ‘a prince;’<BR>fruo, ‘early;’ fer, ‘far:’ Angl. Sax. form: Slav.<BR>pra-, pro-, ‘before;’ prĭ-vy, ‘first:’ Lith. pra-,<BR>‘before;’ pro, ‘through, for;’ pir-ma-s, ‘first;’<BR>pirm, ‘before:’ Hib. fur, ‘for;’ foir, ‘before;’<BR>perhaps fri, ‘with, by, through, on.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र 2. प्र, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. पॄ), filling,<BR>fulfilling (at the end of a comp., cf. आकूति-प्र,<BR>कक्ष्य-प्र, काम-प्र); like, resembling (in<BR>इक्षु-प्र, क्षुर-प्र, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रउग
प्रउग प्र-üग, अम्, n. (according to the<BR>commentators fr. प्र-युग), Ved. the forepart of<BR>the pole or shafts of a chariot (Sāy. = ईषयोर् अग्रं<BR>युग-बन्धन-स्थानम्); उभयतः-प्रüग,<BR>having the foreparts of the shafts on both sides; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n., N. of the second Śastra or hymn at<BR>the morning libation.<BR>—प्रüग-चित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>arranged in the form of the forepart of a chariot-pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकङ्कत
प्रकङ्कत प्र-कङ्कत, अस्, m., Ved. a veno-<BR>mous species of reptile; (Sāy.) = प्रकृष्ट-विषो<BR>(or प्रकृष्ट-गामी) महोरगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकच
प्रकच प्र-कच, अस्, आ, अम्, (perhaps) having<BR>the hair erect; [cf. उत्-क्˚, वि-क्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकट|प्रकटं
प्रकट 1. प्र-कट, अस्, आ, अम्, evident, clear,<BR>manifest, apparent, displayed, unfolded, open; public,<BR>commonly known, undisguised; visible; प्रकटः<BR>सो ऽस्तु, let him show himself; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man; (अम्), ind. evidently, clearly, manifestly,<BR>visibly; openly, undisguisedly, in public; अ-प्र-<BR>कटम्, unobservedly; [cf. अव-कट, उत्-क्˚, नि-क्˚,<BR>वि-क्˚, सङ्-क्˚.]<BR>—प्रकट-प्रीति-वर्धन, अस्, m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—प्रकटी-करण, अम्, n.<BR>making visible or apparent, displaying, manifesting.<BR>—प्रकटी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to manifest, bring to light, unfold, display.<BR>—प्रकटी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, manifested, brought<BR>to light, unfolded, displayed.<BR>—प्रकटी-भू, cl. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">Page0601-c+ 73</a>]<BR>P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to become manifest, appear.<BR>—प्रकटी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, manifested, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकट|प्रकटं
2. प्रकट, Nom. P. प्रकटति, प्रकटितुम्, to<BR>appear, become manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटन|प्रकटनं
प्रकटन, अम्, n. manifesting, bringing to<BR>light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटय
प्रकटय, Nom. P. प्रकटयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>manifest, make manifest, bring to light; to disclose,<BR>evince, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटाय
प्रकटाय, Nom. P. प्रकटायति, -यितुम्, to<BR>manifest, reveal, promulgate, proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटित|प्रकटितं
प्रकटित, अस्, आ, अम्, manifested; evident, ap-<BR>parent; unfolded, displayed, opened, expanded;<BR>publicly proclaimed or exhibited.<BR>—प्रकटित-ह-<BR>ताशेष-तमस् (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, ind. having openly<BR>destroyed utter darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकण्व
प्रकण्व प्र-कण्व, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably)<BR>freed from evil (said of a place, Scholiast on Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 1, 153).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकथ्
प्रकथ् प्र-कथ्, cl. 10. P. -कथयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to announce, proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकथन|प्रकथनं
प्र-कथन, अम्, n. announcing, proclaiming,<BR>relating, communicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्प्|प्रकंप्
प्रकम्प् प्र-कम्प्, cl. 1. A. -कम्पते, -कम्-<BR>पितुम्, to tremble, shake, quake, quiver, shudder;<BR>to become lax or loose, to be loosened; to vibrate<BR>(said of sound): Caus. -कम्पयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to tremble; to swing, wave, brandish, shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्प|प्रकंप|प्रकंपः|प्रकम्पः
प्र-कम्प, अस्, m. trembling, quivering, shaking,<BR>quaking, staggering, violent motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पन|प्रकंपन|प्रकम्पनः
प्र-कम्पन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to tremble;<BR>(अस्), m. wind, air; N. of a hell; of an Asura;<BR>(अम्), n. great trembling, shaking, swaying to and<BR>fro, violent or excessive motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पनीय
प्र-कम्पनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made to<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पमान
प्र-कम्पमान, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling violently,<BR>shaking, quaking, quivering; becoming lax or loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पयत्
प्र-कम्पयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to tremble,<BR>shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पिन्|प्रकंपिन्
प्र-कम्पिन्, ई, इनी, इ, trembling, shaking, mov-<BR>ing to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्प्य
प्र-कम्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be caused to tremble,<BR>to be made to shake; [cf. दुष्-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर|प्रकरं|प्रकरः
प्रकर 1. and 2. प्र-कर. See under प्र-<BR>कृ, p. 602, and प्र-कॄ, p. 603.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरण|प्रकरणं
प्रकरण प्र-करण, प्र-कर्तव्य, प्र-<BR>कर्तृ. See प्र-कृ, p. 602, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरितृ
प्रकरितृ प्र-करितृ. See प्र-कॄ, p. 603.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्ष|प्रकर्षः
प्रकर्ष प्र-कर्ष, प्र-कर्षण, &c. See<BR>प्र-कृष्, p. 603.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्
प्रकल् प्र-कल् (see rt. 2. कल्), cl. 10. P.<BR>-कालयति, -यितुम्, to drive onwards, chase, pursue;<BR>to urge on, incite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकालन|प्रकालनः
प्र-कालन, अस्, आ, अम्, driving, driving on,<BR>chasing, pursuing; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga of the<BR>race of Vāsuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकला
प्रकला प्र-कला, f. part of a part, a minute<BR>portion.<BR>—प्रकल-विद्, त्, m., Ved. (according to<BR>the Nirukta) ‘knowing, i. e. calculating the smallest<BR>particles or sums,’ a merchant; (according to Sāy.) =<BR>अ-जानत्, ‘not knowing,’ knowing very little, desti-<BR>tute of knowledge, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पना
प्रकल्पना प्र-कल्पना. See प्र-कॢप्, p. 604.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्याण
प्रकल्याण प्र-कल्याण, अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकश
प्रकश प्र-कश, अस्, m., Ved. the thong or<BR>lash of a whip; hurting, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकस्
प्रकस् प्र-कस्, Caus. P. -कासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to drive away, repel, repulse; to cause to bloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाङ्क्ष्
प्रकाङ्क्ष् प्र-काङ्क्ष्, cl. 1. P. -काङ्क्षति,<BR>काङ्क्षितुम्, to wish for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्ड|प्रकांड|प्रकांडं|प्रकांडः|प्रकाण्डः
प्रकाण्ड प्र-काण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. the stem<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">Page0602-a+ 79</a>]<BR>or trunk of a tree from the root to the branches; a<BR>branch, a shoot; (अस्), m. the upper part of the<BR>arm [cf. प्र-गण्ड]; (अस्, अम्), m. n. anything<BR>excellent of its kind (at the end of a comp.; cf.<BR>गो-प्˚, मन्त्रि-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्डक|प्रकांडक|प्रकांडकः|प्रकाण्डकः
प्रकाण्डक, अस्, m. = प्र-काण्ड (at the end of<BR>a comp.; cf. रक्षः-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्डर|प्रकांडर|प्रकांडरः|प्रकाण्डरः
प्रकाण्डर, अस्, m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाम|प्रकामं|प्रकामः
प्रकाम प्र-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, amorous; (अस्),<BR>m. desire, delight, pleasure, luxury; (अम्), ind.<BR>according to wish or desire, with great pleasure, to<BR>the heart's content; voluntarily, willingly; sufficiently;<BR>very much; indeed.<BR>—प्रकाम-तस्, ind. willingly,<BR>with great pleasure or delight, to the heart's content;<BR>at will, according to the will.<BR>—प्रकाम-भुज्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, eating till satisfied, eating enough.<BR>—प्रकाम-<BR>विस्तार, अस्, m. great expansiveness (according to<BR>Malli-nātha = अत्यन्त-विशालता).<BR>—प्रकामालोक-<BR>नीय-ता (˚म-आल्˚), f. the being an object that may<BR>be viewed at pleasure.<BR>—प्रकामोद्य (˚म-उद्˚),<BR>अम्, n., Ved. talking to the heart's content, talkative-<BR>ness, garrulity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकार|प्रकारः
प्रकार प्र-कार. See प्र-कृ, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश्
प्रकाश् प्र-काश्, cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.)<BR>-काशते (-ति), -काशितुम्, to become visible, come<BR>to light, come in sight, appear; to shine, gleam,<BR>glitter; to become evident or manifest: Caus. P.<BR>-काशयति, -यितुम्, to make visible, bring to light,<BR>cause to appear; to show, display; to lighten, illu-<BR>mine, irradiate; to discover, disclose, unfold, mani-<BR>fest, reveal; to make known, impart, communicate,<BR>proclaim: Pass. -काश्यते, to be illumined, &c.:<BR>Caus. A. -काशयते, -यितुम्, to cause to appear; to<BR>explain: Intens., Ved. -चाकशीति, to irradiate, illumine;<BR>to survey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश|प्रकाशं|प्रकाशः
प्र-काश, अस्, आ, अम्, visible, manifest, clear,<BR>evident; open, public; generally or universally<BR>known, noted, renowned, famous, celebrated; bright,<BR>shining, brilliant; expanded, blown; (at the end of<BR>a comp.) having the appearance of, looking like,<BR>resembling, like; (अस्), m. clearness, brightness,<BR>brilliance, lustre, splendor, light, elucidation (in this<BR>sense frequently at the end of the titles of explana-<BR>tory works; cf. अर्क-प्˚, तत्त्व-प्˚, तर्क-प्˚);<BR>display, manifestation, expansion, diffusion; publicity,<BR>fame, renown, celebrity; sunshine; the open air, an<BR>open spot or space; (according to Mahī-dhara) =<BR>उपरितन-देह-कान्ति, the gloss on the upper part<BR>of a (horse's) body; a golden mirror (wrongly for<BR>प्राकाश); a chapter, section; laughter (perhaps<BR>wrongly for a form प्र-कास fr. प्र-कस्); N. of a<BR>Brāhman the son of Tamas or Darkness personified;<BR>of a son of Manu Raivata; (आस्), m. pl. an epithet<BR>of the messengers of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. white<BR>metal, bell-metal, brass; (अम्), ind. openly, pub-<BR>licly, undisguisedly, before all eyes (opposed to<BR>अ-प्˚, प्र-च्छन्नम्, रहस्यम्); aloud, audibly<BR>(especially in dramatic language where it is opposed<BR>to आत्म-गतम्, स्व-गतम्, अप-वार्य, जनान्-<BR>तिकम्); (ए), ind. visibly, apparently; before the<BR>world, openly, publicly; in the presence of.<BR>—प्र-<BR>काश-कर्तृ, ता, m. ‘maker of light,’ an epithet of<BR>the sun.<BR>—प्रकाश-कर्मन्, आ, m. ‘whose work is<BR>to give light,’ an epithet of the sun.<BR>—प्रकाश-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. wishing for a splendid ap-<BR>pearance or for distinction.<BR>—प्रकाश-क्रय, अस्,<BR>m. a purchase made publicly.<BR>—प्रकाश-ता, f. or<BR>प्रकाश-त्व, अम्, n. brightness, brilliance, splendor,<BR>luminousness; appearance, manifestation, visibility;<BR>celebrity, renown, fame.<BR>—प्रकाश-देवी, f., N. of a<BR>princess (Rāja-taraṅginī IV. 79).<BR>—प्रकाश-नारी,<BR>f. ‘public woman,’ a prostitute, harlot.<BR>—प्रकाश-<BR>वञ्चक, अस्, m. ‘an open rogue,’ public deceiver or<BR>cheat.<BR>—प्रकाश-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, bright, brilliant,<BR>shining; (आन्), m., N. of one of the feet of Brahmā.<BR>—प्रकाश-वर्ष, अस्, m., N. of a poet men-<BR>tioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR>—प्रकाशा-<BR>काश-कान्ति (˚श-आक्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, bright as a clear<BR>sky.<BR>—प्रकाशात्मक (˚श-आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">Page0602-b+ 76</a>]<BR>brilliant in character or nature, shining, brilliant.<BR>—प्रकाशात्मक-त्व, अम्, n. the possession of a<BR>brilliant nature or character, brilliancy.<BR>—प्रका-<BR>शात्मन् (˚श-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, brilliant in character or<BR>nature, brilliant, shining; (आ), m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; the sun; N. of a man; of a philosophical<BR>writer (pupil of Ananyānubhava-svāmin).<BR>—प्रका-<BR>शात्म-पति, इस्, or प्रकाशात्म-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a philosophical writer (= प्रकाशात्मन्).<BR>—प्र-<BR>काशानन्द (˚श-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a philosophical<BR>writer.<BR>—प्रकाशी-करण, अम्, n. giving light,<BR>illuminating, irradiating.<BR>—प्रकाशी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A.<BR>-करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to give light, illumine;<BR>to publish, make known.<BR>—प्रकाशी-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>the becoming light, morning twilight.<BR>—प्रकाशे-<BR>तर (˚श-इत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘other than visible,’<BR>invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशक|प्रकाशकः
प्र-काशक, अस्, इका, अम्, clear, bright, shining,<BR>brilliant; universally known, noted, renowned; irra-<BR>diating, illuminating, giving light, luminous; making<BR>apparent or manifest, disclosing, discovering, pub-<BR>lishing; evincing, betraying; expressing; explaining;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘the giver of light,’ the sun; an expounder,<BR>illustrator; a publisher; a discoverer; (इका), f., N.<BR>of a commentary on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtra by Rāma-<BR>kṛṣṇa.<BR>—प्रकाशक-ज्ञातृ, ता, m. ‘knowing the<BR>giver of light, i. e. the sun,’ a cock.<BR>—प्रकाशक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. luminousness, radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशन|प्रकाशनः
प्र-काशन, अस्, आ, अम्, illuminating, giving<BR>light; making known; (अस्), m. ‘the giver of light,’<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; (अम्), n. causing to appear,<BR>displaying; illuminating, giving light; bringing to<BR>light, making clear or manifest, making known,<BR>publicly showing or manifesting; (आ), f. propound-<BR>ing, explaining, teaching.<BR>—प्रकाशन-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, irradiating, illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशनीय
प्र-काशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be displayed, to be<BR>shown or manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशमान
प्र-काशमान, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming manifest,<BR>appearing; shining, splendid, brilliant, radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशित|प्रकाशितं
प्र-काशित, अस्, आ, अम्, become visible, brought<BR>to light, visible, manifest, apparent, evident; dis-<BR>played, unfolded, discovered; illumined, enlightened,<BR>irradiated; published, promulgated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशिन्
प्र-काशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, visible, clear, bright, shin-<BR>ing; making visible or manifest.<BR>—प्रकाशि-ता, f. or<BR>प्रकाशि-त्व, अम्, n. clearness, brightness, brilliance,<BR>light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश्य
प्र-काश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be illuminated or en-<BR>lightened; to be brought to light or made manifest;<BR>(अम्), n. light, clearness, distinctness (in this sense<BR>a wrong form for प्राकाश्य, q. v.).<BR>—प्रकाश्य-ता,<BR>f. the being manifest; publicity; the being illu-<BR>minated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकिरण|प्रकिरणं
प्रकिरण प्र-किरण. See प्र-कॄ, p. 603.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्तन|प्रकीर्तनं|प्रकीर्त्तन
प्रकीर्तन प्र-कीर्तन, प्र-कीर्तित, प्र-<BR>कीर्त्ति. See प्र-कॄत्, p. 604, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्य|प्रकीर्यः|प्रकीर्य्य|प्रकीर्य्यः
प्रकीर्य प्र-कीर्य. See प्र-कॄ, p. 603.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुञ्च|प्रकुंच|प्रकुंचः|प्रकुञ्चः
प्रकुञ्च प्रकुञ्च, अस्, m. a particular<BR>measure of capacity (somewhat more or less than<BR>a handful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुट्
प्रकुट् प्र-कुट् or प्र-कुट्ट्, cl. 10. P. -कुट-<BR>यति, -कुट्टयति, -यितुम्, to divide, reduce to small<BR>pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुथ्
प्रकुथ् प्र-कुथ्, cl. 4. P. -कुथ्यति, -कोथि-<BR>तुम्, to become putrid, turn putrid, begin to stink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुथित
प्र-कुथित, अस्, आ, अम्, putrid, putrescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोथ|प्रकोथः
प्र-कोथ, अस्, m. putrefaction, putridity, putres-<BR>cence.<BR>—प्रकोथोदक (˚थ-उद्˚), अम्, n. filthy<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुप्
प्रकुप् प्र-कुप्, cl. 4. P. A. -कुप्यति, -ते,<BR>-कोपितुम्, to be moved or agitated; to become<BR>enraged, fly into a passion: Caus. -कोपयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to provoke to anger, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुपित
प्र-कुपित, अस्, आ, अम्, moved, agitated, moving<BR>to and fro (Sāy. = इतस् ततश् चलित); very angry,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">Page0602-c+ 79</a>]<BR>wroth, enraged, incensed; disordered; अति-प्रकु-<BR>पित, excessively irritated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुप्त
प्र-कुप्त, anomalously for प्र-कुपित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुप्य
प्र-कुप्य, ind. having become angry, being<BR>enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोप|प्रकोपः
प्र-कोप, अस्, m. effervescence, ebullition, excite-<BR>ment, emotion, violent anger, rage, fury, wrath, ire,<BR>anger; irritation, provocation, exasperation; political<BR>disturbance, insurrection, mutiny; an attack; (in medi-<BR>cine) excess, superabundance, vitiation [cf. पित्त-प्˚,<BR>वात-प्˚].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपण
प्र-कोपण or प्र-कोपन, अस्, ई, अम्, exciting,<BR>agitating, irritating, provoking; (अम्), n. irritating,<BR>provoking, irritation, provocation, incensing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपणीय
प्र-कोपणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be irritated or<BR>incensed, to be provoked to anger, irritable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपित
प्र-कोपित, अस्, आ, अम्, irritated, provoked, in-<BR>censed, enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपितृ
प्र-कोपितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, exciting, agitating, dis-<BR>quieting, an exciter, agitator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुल|प्रकुलं
प्रकुल प्र-कुल, अम्, n. a handsome or<BR>excellent body; (also read प्रह्वल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकूर्द्
प्रकूर्द् प्र-कूर्द्, cl. 1. P. A. -कूर्दति, -ते,<BR>कूर्दितुम्, to jump forward, leap about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकूष्माण्डी|प्रकूष्मांडी
प्रकूष्माण्डी प्र-कूष्माण्डी, f. an epithet of<BR>Durgā; [cf. कूष्माण्डी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृ
प्रकृ प्र-कृ, cl. 5. Ved. and cl. 8. P. A.<BR>-कृणोति, -कृणुते, -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>make, accomplish, perform, achieve, effect; to make,<BR>render (with double acc., e. g. अन्धकारं शवलम्<BR>प्रकुर्वन्, rendering the darkness partly illumined);<BR>to bring to light, express, utter; to place before or<BR>in front, cause to precede, mention first; to place<BR>at the head, honour, worship; to appoint (to an<BR>office, with loc.); to gain, win, conquer (Ved.); to<BR>do away with, destroy (Ved.); to induce, move,<BR>incline (Ved.); to cause, enable (with inf., Ved.);<BR>Sāy. = प्रकृष्टं कृ, स्तुतिम् प्रकर्षेण कृ,<BR>to exalt, praise highly; to lay out, expend; (with<BR>बुद्धिम् or मनस्) to set the heart upon, apply<BR>the mind to, direct the thoughts towards anything<BR>(dat. or loc.); to resolve upon anything; (with दारान्)<BR>to marry; (with कन्याम्, &c.) to deflower, violate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर|प्रकरं|प्रकरः
1. प्र-कर, अस्, ई, अम् (for 2. see under प्र-कॄ,<BR>p. 603), doing much, doing well; (अस्), m. aid, assist-<BR>ance, friendship; usage, custom, continuance of a<BR>similar practice; respect; seduction, abduction; (ई),<BR>f. an episodical incident or interlude inserted in a<BR>drama to explain that which follows; theatrical dress<BR>or disguise, as wearing a woman's garb, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरण|प्रकरणं
प्र-करण, अम्, n. treatment, discussion, ex-<BR>pounding, explanation; a subject, topic, province,<BR>department; a section, chapter, book, paragraph;<BR>opportunity, occasion; relation; an introduction,<BR>prologue, prelude; a poetical fiction or poem, in<BR>which the story and principal persons are wholly<BR>imaginary; a drama, a kind of drama with a fic-<BR>titious plot; treating with respect; doing much or<BR>well; (ई), f. a drama of the same character as the<BR>Pra-karaṇa but of less extent.<BR>—प्रकरण-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the being a prelude or introduction.<BR>—प्र-<BR>करण-पञ्चिका, f., N. of a philosophical treatise by<BR>Śālika-nātha; (also called शालिका.)<BR>—प्रकरण-<BR>पाद, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—प्रकरण-<BR>शस्, ind. according to species or kind (opposed to<BR>पृथक्त्वेन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरणिका
प्रकरणिका, f. a kind of minor drama (= प्र-<BR>करणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरिका
प्र-करिका, f. an episodical incident or interlude<BR>inserted in a drama to explain that which follows<BR>(= प्र-करी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्तव्य
प्र-कर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be prepared; to be<BR>manifested or shown; to be appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्तृ
प्र-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who causes or<BR>occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकार|प्रकारः
प्र-कार, अस्, m. sort, kind, species; way, mode,<BR>fashion, manner (in these and the preceding mean-<BR>ings frequently at the end of a comp., e. g. नाना-<BR>प्रकार, of many kinds, manifold; त्रि-प्रकार,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">Page0603-a+ 81</a>]<BR>of three kinds, threefold; cf. बहु-प्रकारम्);<BR>similitude; difference; speciality.<BR>—प्रकार-ता, f.<BR>particularity, speciality.<BR>—प्रकार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>belonging to a species or kind.<BR>—प्रकारान्तर<BR>(˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. another sort or kind, another<BR>manner; (ए), ind. in another way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकारक
प्रकारक, अस्, आ, अम्, = प्र-कार (at the end of<BR>comps., e. g. तत्-प्रकारक, of that kind, belonging<BR>to that).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकार्य
प्र-कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be evinced or mani-<BR>fested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुर्वत्|प्रकुर्व्वत्
प्र-कुर्वत्, अन्, अती, अत्, doing much or well;<BR>behaving respectfully to, waiting upon, serving,<BR>honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुर्वाण|प्रकुर्व्वाण
प्र-कुर्वाण, अस्, आ, अम्, doing much or well;<BR>attending or behaving respectfully to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृत|प्रकृतः
प्र-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made, accomplished, com-<BR>pleted; commenced, begun; one who has begun<BR>anything; original; that which is spoken of or is<BR>the original subject of discussion, that which is<BR>now in hand or under consideration; genuine, real;<BR>appointed, charged; wished, expected; mentioned;<BR>important, interesting; (अम्), n. original subject,<BR>present subject of discussion, present case; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—प्रकृत-ता, f. or प्रकृत-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the being begun or in process of execu-<BR>tion, incipient state or condition; the being the<BR>subject of discussion.<BR>—प्रकृतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the original sense; real, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृति|प्रकृतिः
प्र-कृति, इस्, f. the original or natural form of<BR>anything, natural condition, or state, original, primary<BR>substance (opposed to वि-कृति, change, modification,<BR>anything derived or secondary); cause, original<BR>source; origin, extraction, descent; nature, character,<BR>usual or natural state; constitution, disposition, tem-<BR>per; a rule, scheme, paradigm, pattern, model,<BR>standard (especially in ritual); (in the Sāṅkhya<BR>philosophy) = प्र-धान, the evolver of all material<BR>appearances, the ‘originant’ or original source of (or<BR>rather passive power of creating) the material world,<BR>(generally called Nature as opposed to Puruṣa or<BR>Spirit); (in mythology) a goddess, the personified<BR>will of the Supreme in the creation (identified with<BR>Māyā or Illusion and in an especial manner the<BR>prototype of the female sex; hence the same with<BR>the Śakti or personified energy or bride of a deity,<BR>as Lakṣmī, Durgā, &c.; in some systems Pra-kṛti<BR>is considered the same with the Supreme Being);<BR>(in grammar) the crude or elementary form of a<BR>word, an uninflected word, the radical form of a<BR>word before the case-terminations and other affixes<BR>are subjoined; N. of two classes of metres, consisting<BR>of eight and of eighty-four syllables respectively; (in<BR>arithmetic) a coefficient, multiplier; (in anatomy)<BR>temperament, the predominance of one of the<BR>humors at the time of generation; a woman, woman-<BR>kind; a mother; an animal; the male organ of<BR>generation; the female organ of generation; N. of<BR>a woman; तृतीया प्रकृतिः, the third nature, a<BR>eunuch; (अयस्), f. pl. (in the Sāṅkhya) the ma-<BR>terial archetypes of everything existing; the eight<BR>producers or primary elements out of which every-<BR>thing else is evolved (viz. अ-व्यक्त, बुद्धि or म-<BR>हत्, अहङ्कार, and the five तन्-मात्रस्); the con-<BR>stituent elements of the state (of which five are usually<BR>enumerated, viz. the minister, treasure, territory,<BR>fortresses, and army, to these are sometimes added<BR>the king himself and the sovereign who is his ally,<BR>and sometimes also the corporations of citizens); a<BR>king's ministers generally; the subjects of a king,<BR>the citizens, artizans, &c.; the various sovereigns to<BR>be considered in case of war (according to Manu VII.<BR>155, viz. the मध्यम, वि-जिगीषु, उद्-आसीन,<BR>and शत्रु, to which according to Kullūka should be<BR>added eight remoter princes, viz. the मित्र, अरि-<BR>मित्र, मित्र-मित्र, अरिमित्र-मित्र, पार्ष्णि-<BR>ग्राह, आ-क्रन्द, पार्ष्णिग्राहासार, आक्रन्दा-<BR>सार; each of these twelve kings has the five Prakṛtis<BR>above-mentioned, so that the total number of Pra-<BR>kṛtis may be seventy-two, Manu VII. 157); N. of<BR>a class of divinities under Manu Raibhya; प्र-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">Page0603-b+ 79</a>]<BR>कृत्या, ind. by nature, naturally, by birth or extrac-<BR>tion; in the original state or condition, without<BR>change or alteration; properly.<BR>—प्रकृति-कृपण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, naturally plaintive or disposed to lament,<BR>naturally feeble (in discriminating).<BR>—प्रकृति-<BR>खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘section on nature,’ N. of the<BR>second book of the Brahma-vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—प्र-<BR>कृति-गुण, अस्, m. one of the three constituent quali-<BR>ties of nature (see गुण).<BR>—प्रकृति-ज, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>springing from nature, inborn, innate.<BR>—प्रकृति-<BR>तरल, अस्, आ, अम्, naturally changeful, volatile, fickle,<BR>dissolute, voluptuous.<BR>—प्रकृति-पुरुष, अस्, m. a<BR>minister of state.<BR>—प्रकृति-प्रलय, अस्, m. = प्र-<BR>कृति-लय, q. v.<BR>—प्रकृति-भाव, अस्, m. natural<BR>state, original or unaltered condition; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>natural, usual, common.<BR>—प्रकृति-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being in the original state or condition, original.<BR>—प्रकृतिभूतेकार (˚त-इक्˚), अस्, m. the original<BR>sound or letter इ.<BR>—प्रकृति-मण्डल, अम्, n.<BR>the circle or aggregate of the Prakṛtis or of a<BR>king's subjects, the entire kingdom, whole empire.<BR>—प्रकृति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having the original or<BR>natural form or shape, natural, usual, ordinary; in a<BR>natural or usual frame of mind.<BR>—प्रकृति-लय, अस्,<BR>m. absorption into Prakṛti, the dissolution of the<BR>universe.<BR>—प्रकृति-वत्, ind. as in the original<BR>form.<BR>—प्रकृति-विकृति-स्वभाव, अस्, m. the<BR>relation of (a word in its) radical form to (itself<BR>under the) mutations (of inflection &c.).<BR>—प्र-<BR>कृति-विषम, अस्, आ, अम्, naturally rough.<BR>—प्र-<BR>कृति-सिद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, effected by nature, natural;<BR>(अम्), n. true or real nature.<BR>—प्रकृति-सुभग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, naturally pleasing or agreeable.<BR>—प्र-<BR>कृति-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the original or<BR>natural state, being in the natural condition, natural,<BR>genuine, unmixed; healthy, in good health; reco-<BR>vered; inherent, innate; bare, stripped of everything.<BR>—प्रकृतीश (˚ति-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of subjects,’ a<BR>magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रिया
प्र-क्रिया, f. conduct, manner, way; a ceremony,<BR>rite, observance; elevation, exaltation; a privilege,<BR>prerogative, advantage over others, precedence, high<BR>position; the bearing of royal insignia; insignia (of<BR>rank); a chapter, section; an introductory section<BR>of a work; producing, production; (in grammar)<BR>etymological formation, formation of a word with<BR>the root, affix, &c.; rules for the formation and<BR>inflection of words.<BR>—प्रक्रिया-कौमुदी, f. ‘elu-<BR>cidation of etymological structure,’ N. of a gram-<BR>matical work by Rāma-candra.<BR>—प्रक्रियाकौ-<BR>मुदी-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a commentary by Kṛṣṇa-<BR>paṇḍita on the preceding.<BR>—प्रक्रिया-पाद, अस्,<BR>m. ‘introductory section,’ N. of the first part of the<BR>Vāyu-Purāṇa.<BR>—प्रक्रिया-रत्न, अम्, n. ‘gem of<BR>etymological structure,’ N. of a grammatical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचिकीर्षु
प्र-चिकीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, intending or purposing<BR>to recompense, wishing to requite (= प्रति-चि-<BR>कीर्षु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृत्
प्रकृत् प्र-कृत् (see rt. 2. कृत्), cl. 1. 6. P.<BR>-कर्तति, -कृन्तति, -कर्तितुम्, to cut off; to cut<BR>up, cut to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृशित
प्रकृशित प्र-कृशित, अस्, आ, अम्, attenuated,<BR>thin, emaciate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्
प्रकृष् प्र-कृष्, cl. 1. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>-कर्षति (-ते), -कर्ष्टुम्, -क्रष्टुम्, to draw<BR>forth, stretch forth; to draw forwards, drag away;<BR>to lead (an army); to draw or bend (a bow); to<BR>draw out, stretch out, prolong; to place before or in<BR>front; to harass, distract, disturb, trouble, disquiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्ष|प्रकर्षः
प्र-कर्ष, अस्, m. pre-eminence, excellence,<BR>eminence, distinction, superiority, intensity of good<BR>qualities or merit, high degree (in these senses fre-<BR>quently at the end of comps.; cf. प्रणय-प्˚,<BR>वपुः-प्˚, वर्ण-प्˚); might, strength; speciality;<BR>universality; absoluteness, definitiveness; protracted-<BR>ness, length; (in grammar) the effect of the prefix<BR>प्र upon roots; (आत्, एण), ind. in a high degree,<BR>intensely, eminently, exceedingly, mightily, strongly.<BR>—प्रकर्ष-गमन, अम्, n. going absolutely or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">Page0603-c+ 80</a>]<BR>finally (?).<BR>—प्रकर्ष-तन्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, depend-<BR>ent on excellence or intensity of merit; dependent<BR>on superior strength or power.<BR>—प्रकर्ष-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, pre-eminent, eminent, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षक|प्रकर्षकः
प्र-कर्षक, अस्, m. ‘the harasser, disquieter,’<BR>an epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षण
प्र-कर्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, harassing, distracting,<BR>disquieting, troubling; (अम्), n. the act of drawing<BR>away, drawing, attracting; drawing furrows, plough-<BR>ing; pushing forwards; stretching out, extension,<BR>long duration, length; excellence, superiority; the<BR>act of harassing or disquieting, distraction; realizing<BR>by the use of a pledge more than the interest of the<BR>money lent upon it; a bridle (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षणीय
प्र-कर्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dragged away,<BR>to be moved along the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षत्
प्र-कर्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, dragging forth, drawing<BR>out, drawing along; drawing or bending (a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षित
प्र-कर्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn forth, dragged<BR>forwards; stretched out; exceeded in profit (as the<BR>interest of a loan); (अम्), n. profit on a pledge<BR>beyond the interest of the money lent upon it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षिन्
प्र-कर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, drawing forth; excellent,<BR>pre-eminent, distinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्ट|प्रकृष्टं
प्र-कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, drawn forth, dragged<BR>forwards; drawn out, protracted, lengthy, long; pre-<BR>eminent, superior, distinguished, excellent, exalted;<BR>prominent, chief, principal; well to do; distracted,<BR>harassed, disquieted; violent.<BR>—प्रकृष्ट-ता, f. or<BR>प्रकृष्ट-त्व, अम्, n. transcendent excellence,<BR>eminence, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्य
प्र-कृष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dragged forwards,<BR>to be drawn along on the ground; excessive.<BR>—प्र-<BR>कृष्य-कुत्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, strongly censured;<BR>(also read प्रकृष्ट-कुत्सित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॄ
प्रकॄ प्र-कॄ, cl. 6. P. -किरति, -करितुम्,<BR>-करीतुम्, to scatter forth, scatter, strew, throw about;<BR>to issue forth, spring up: Pass. -कीर्यते (ep. Pot.<BR>-कीर्येत्), to disappear, vanish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर|प्रकरं|प्रकरः
2. प्र-कर, अस्, m. (for 1. see under प्र-कृ,<BR>p. 602), a scattered heap, heap, multitude, quantity,<BR>plenty; a bunch of flowers, a nosegay; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of song; an open piece of ground; a place where four<BR>roads meet; the proper site of any magical opera-<BR>tions; (अम्), n. aloe wood, Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरितृ
प्र-करितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who sprinkles;<BR>one who spices or seasons (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकिरण|प्रकिरणं
प्र-किरण, अम्, n. scattering, strewing, throwing<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकिरत्
प्र-किरत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, scattering, strewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्ण|प्रकीर्णं|प्रकीर्णः
प्र-कीर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, scattered forth, scattered,<BR>strewed, dispersed; squandered; spread abroad, spread,<BR>published, public, promulgated; mixed, containing<BR>various subjects, miscellaneous; disordered, loose,<BR>dishevelled; agitated, excited, wild; confused, in-<BR>coherent; waved, waving, undulating; expanded,<BR>open; standing alone, nowhere mentioned; (अस्),<BR>m. the plant Guilandina Bonduc; (अम्), n. a con-<BR>fused mass, miscellany, miscellanea; a collection of<BR>miscellaneous rules; a chapter, section, division of<BR>a book.<BR>—प्रकीर्ण-केशी, f. ‘having dishevelled<BR>hair,’ an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—प्रकीर्ण-मैथुन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, living in mixed (connubial) intercourse.<BR>—प्रकीर्णाम्बर-मूर्धज (˚ण-अम्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, with disordered garments and dishevelled hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्णक|प्रकीर्णकं|प्रकीर्णकः
प्र-कीर्णक, अस्, आ, अम्, scattered about; occur-<BR>ring singly or in single instances; (अस्, अम्), m. n.<BR>a chowrie, the tail of the Bos Grunniens used as a<BR>fan or fly-flap and as an ornament for horses; a<BR>tuft of hair used as an ornament for horses; (अस्),<BR>m. a horse; (अम्), n. a miscellany, any collection of<BR>heterogeneous objects not arranged under any dis-<BR>tinct classes or heads; a section or division of a<BR>book; (in law) a case not provided for by the<BR>Śāstras and to be decided by the judge or king,<BR>the legal decision of a case not anticipated in the<BR>law-books; a section or chapter of a book; extent,<BR>length (especially of a book or stanza).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्य|प्रकीर्यः|प्रकीर्य्य|प्रकीर्य्यः
प्र-कीर्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be strewed or scattered,<BR>to be spread abroad or about; to be diffused or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">Page0604-a+ 77</a>]<BR>promulgated; to be expanded or extended; (अस्), m.<BR>the plant Guilandina Bonduc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॄत्
प्रकॄत् प्र-कॄत्, cl. 10. P. -कीर्तयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to announce, proclaim; to pronounce, declare, call,<BR>name; to approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्तन|प्रकीर्तनं|प्रकीर्त्तन
प्र-कीर्तन, अम्, n. announcing, proclaiming;<BR>pronouncing aloud; praising aloud, lauding, extolling;<BR>(आ), f. mentioning, naming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्तित|प्रकीर्त्तित|प्रकीर्त्तितं
प्र-कीर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, announced, proclaimed;<BR>pronounced, declared, said, mentioned, stated; called,<BR>named; explained; revealed; renowned, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्त्ति|प्रकीर्ति|प्रकीर्तिः
प्र-कीर्त्ति, इस्, f. celebration, praise; fame, cele-<BR>brity; declaration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्
प्रकॢप् प्र-कॢप्, cl. 1. A. -कल्पते, -कल्पि-<BR>तुम्, -कल्प्तुम्, to proceed prosperously, succeed, be<BR>successful; to be fit or suitable for (with inf. or dat.):<BR>Caus. -कल्पयति, -यितुम्, to prepare, make, de-<BR>sign; to put a person at the head, show honour to;<BR>to accompany (?); to establish, fix, settle; to appoint,<BR>invest, install, elect to, choose or select for (with two<BR>acc., or with acc. and loc. of abstract noun); to fix,<BR>fasten; to further; (with अश्रु) to shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पना
प्र-कल्पना, f. fixing, settlement, allotting, allot-<BR>ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पयितृ
प्र-कल्पयितृ, ता, m., Ved. one who prepares<BR>or arranges, setting in order (= इष्-कर्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पित
प्र-कल्पित, अस्, आ, अम्, done, made, appointed;<BR>formed or shed (as a tear); (आ), f. a kind of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्प्य
प्र-कल्प्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be appointed, to be<BR>fixed or settled, to be determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्त
प्र-कॢप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared, arranged, made<BR>ready; (अम्), ind., Ved. readily, easily.<BR>—प्र-<BR>कॢप्त-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. progress, success, success-<BR>fulness.<BR>—प्रकॢप्त-स्नान-मण्डन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one whose ablutions and toilet have been arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्ति
प्र-कॢप्ति, a various reading for प्र-कृति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकेत|प्रकेतः
प्रकेत प्र-केत, अस्, m. (केत fr. 2. कि = rt. 2.<BR>चि), Ved. appearance; observation, perception, intel-<BR>ligence; one who knows; (Sāy. = अन्धकारावृ-<BR>तस्य सर्वस्य पदार्थस्य प्रज्ञापकः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोष्ठ|प्रकोष्ठः
प्रकोष्ठ प्र-कोष्ठ, अस्, m. the fore-arm;<BR>a room near the gate of a royal palace; a court in a<BR>house, an open space surrounded by buildings; a part<BR>of a door-frame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोष्ठक|प्रकोष्ठकः
प्रकोष्ठक, अस्, m. a room near the gate of<BR>a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्खर|प्रक्खरः
प्रक्खर प्रक्खर, अस्, m. iron armour for<BR>the defence of a horse or elephant; (also written<BR>प्र-खर, प्र-क्षर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रन्द्
प्रक्रन्द् प्र-क्रन्द्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रन्दति,<BR>-ते, -क्रन्दितुम्, Ved. to invoke loudly: Caus. P.<BR>-क्रन्दयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to roar; to move with<BR>a rushing sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रम्
प्रक्रम् प्र-क्रम्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रामति,<BR>-क्रमते, -क्रमितुम्, to step or stride forwards,<BR>go forwards, walk on, advance; to set out, march<BR>forth, march off; to come forth, issue forth, to go,<BR>depart; to step or stride across, pass; (usually A.) to<BR>proceed to do or apply one's self to anything, under-<BR>take, prepare; to take the first step, commence,<BR>begin (with inf.); (A.) to act or behave towards<BR>(with loc.): Caus. -क्रामयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to step or stride forwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रन्तृ|प्रक्रंतृ
प्र-क्रन्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who proceeds or<BR>goes; one who takes the first step or begins, a<BR>beginner; conquering, overpowering, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रम|प्रक्रमः
प्र-क्रम, अस्, m. a step, stride; a particular<BR>measure of distance, a pace (the length of which is<BR>variously stated by commentators on works on ritual<BR>at two or three or three and a half Padas, and some-<BR>times at more or less); striding forwards, stepping,<BR>striding; proceeding, going; commencement, be-<BR>ginning; leisure, opportunity; relation, proportion,<BR>degree, measure; a series of oblations correspond-<BR>ing to the movements of a sacrificial horse (Ved.);<BR>the reading of the Krama, q. v.; speaking about or<BR>discussing the point in question; the case in question.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">Page0604-b+ 76</a>]<BR>—प्रक्रम-तृतीय, अम्, n., Ved. the third of a<BR>square pace.<BR>—प्रक्रम-भङ्ग, अस्, m. want of<BR>method, the breaking of arrangement in composition<BR>(= भग्न-क्रम, भग्न-प्रक्रम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमण|प्रक्रमणं
प्र-क्रमण, अम्, n. stepping forwards, step-<BR>ping, proceeding; issuing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमणीय
प्र-क्रमणीय, or प्र-क्रमितव्य, or प्र-<BR>क्रम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone or proceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रममाण
प्र-क्रममाण, अस्, आ, अम्, proceeding, be-<BR>ginning; overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रान्त|प्रक्रांत|प्रक्रान्तः
प्र-क्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, proceeded; gone<BR>beyond, surpassed; commenced, begun; preceded,<BR>previously mentioned, previously laid down or stated;<BR>(अम्), n. the outset of a journey; the point in<BR>question.<BR>—प्रक्रान्त-त्व, अम्, n. beginning, com-<BR>mencing; the being begun; the being stated or<BR>mentioned previously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रय
प्रक्रय प्र-क्रय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. क्री with<BR>प्र), sale (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्री
प्र-क्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. to be bought, purchasable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रीड्
प्रक्रीड् प्र-क्रीड्, cl. 1. P. A. -क्रीडति, -ते,<BR>-क्रीडितुम्, to play, sport, disport one's self, gambol,<BR>frolic, amuse one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रीड|प्रक्रीडः
प्र-क्रीड, अस्, m. play, pastime; a place of<BR>sports, play-ground (Ved.); मरुताम् प्रक्रीडः,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रीडित
प्र-क्रीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, played, playing, sporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रीडिन्
प्र-क्रीडिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. playing, sporting;<BR>playful, sportive, frolicsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रुश्
प्रक्रुश् प्र-क्रुश्, cl. 1. P. -क्रोशति, -क्रोष्-<BR>टुम्, to raise a cry, cry out; to utter (cries), call;<BR>to invoke, call upon, cry out to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रोश
प्र-क्रोश, अस्, m., Ved. a shriek, scream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लिद्
प्रक्लिद् प्र-क्लिद्, cl. 4. A. -क्लिद्यते, -क्लेदि-<BR>तुम्, -क्लेत्तुम्, to become moist or humid, to be-<BR>come wet: Caus. -क्लेदयति, -यितुम्, to moisten,<BR>wet, make wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लिन्न|प्रक्लिन्नः
प्र-क्लिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, moist, humid, wet,<BR>soaked, saturated; moved with compassion or sym-<BR>pathy.<BR>—प्रक्लिन्न-वर्त्मन्, अ, n. a kind of dis-<BR>ease of the eyelids; [cf. क्लिन्न-वर्त्मन्.]<BR>—प्र-<BR>क्लिन्न-हृदयेक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>heart and eyes moist (with affection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लेद|प्रक्लेदः
प्र-क्लेद, अस्, m. moistness, wetness, humidity.<BR>—प्रक्लेद-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, moistening, wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लेदन
प्र-क्लेदन, अस्, आ, अम्, or प्र-क्लेदिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, moistening, wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वण|प्रक्वणः
प्रक्वण प्र-क्वण or प्र-क्वाण, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>rt. क्वण् with प्र), the sound of a Vīṇā or lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षय|प्रक्षयः
प्रक्षय प्र-क्षय. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षर्
प्रक्षर् प्र-क्षर्, cl. 1. P. -क्षरति, -क्ष-<BR>रितुम्, to stream, trickle forth, ooze; to drop down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षर|प्रक्षरः
प्र-क्षर, अस्, m. iron armour for the defence<BR>of a horse or elephant; [cf. प्र-खर, प्रक्-<BR>खर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षरण|प्रक्षरणं
प्र-क्षरण, अम्, n. flowing forth, trickling<BR>out, oozing, dripping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षल्
प्रक्षल् प्र-क्षल्, cl. 10. P. -क्षालयति,<BR>-यितुम्, to wash off, wash away, rinse; to cleanse,<BR>clean, purify: Caus. to cause to wash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालक
प्र-क्षालक, अस्, आ, अम्, washing, one who<BR>washes; [cf. सद्यः-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालन|प्रक्षालनं
प्र-क्षालन, अस्, आ, अम्, performing frequent<BR>ablutions, one who performs frequent ablutions; (अम्),<BR>n. washing, washing off, cleaning, cleansing, purify-<BR>ing; bathing; a means of cleaning, anything used<BR>for purifying, water for washing.<BR>—प्रक्षालनार्-<BR>थाय (˚न-अर्˚), ind. for the sake of washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालनीय
प्र-क्षालनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be washed away<BR>or cleansed; to be purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालित|प्रक्षालितः
प्र-क्षालित, अस्, आ, अम्, washed, cleansed; ex-<BR>piated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षाल्य
1. प्र-क्षाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be washed or<BR>purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षाल्य
2. प्र-क्षाल्य, ind. having washed, having rinsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षि
प्रक्षि प्र-क्षि, cl. 9. 5. 1. P. -क्षिणाति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">Page0604-c+ 75</a>]<BR>क्षिणोति, -क्षयति, -क्षेतुम्, to spoil, injure,<BR>wear out, exhaust, destroy: Pass. -क्षीयते, to be<BR>destroyed, perish, to be worn out or exhausted; to<BR>be diminished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षय|प्रक्षयः
प्र-क्षय, अस्, m. destruction, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षयण
प्र-क्षयण, अस्, आ, अम्, causing to perish,<BR>destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीण
प्र-क्षीण, अस्, आ, अम्, decayed, wasting; de-<BR>stroyed; atoned; vanished, disappeared; (अम्), n.<BR>the spot where any one has perished (e. g. प्रक्षी-<BR>णम् इडं देव-दत्तस्य, this is the spot where<BR>Deva-datta perished).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्
प्रक्षिप् प्र-क्षिप्, cl. 6. P. A. -क्षिपति,<BR>-ते, -क्षेप्तुम्, to throw or fling at, throw or cast<BR>into; to project; to hurl; to put or lay before; to<BR>insert, interpolate: Caus. -क्षेपयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause or order to cast or put into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्त
प्र-क्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown or cast at,<BR>hurled, flung; thrown forth, projected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्तवत्
प्र-क्षिप्तवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has thrown<BR>at, one who has thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्य
प्र-क्षिप्य, ind. having thrown at, having hurled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेप|प्रक्षेपः
प्र-क्षेप, अस्, m. throwing or casting forth or<BR>forward, projecting; a throw, cast; throwing into or<BR>upon, scattering upon; insertion, interpolation; any-<BR>thing added or thrown into drugs while in course of<BR>decoction, an ingredient; the sum deposited by each<BR>member of a commercial company; the box of a<BR>carriage.<BR>—प्रक्षेप-लिपि, इस्, f. a particular style<BR>of handwriting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपण|प्रक्षेपणं
प्र-क्षेपण, अम्, n. throwing, casting; pouring<BR>upon, throwing on, throwing into; fixing (as a<BR>price).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपणीय
प्र-क्षेपणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown or cast<BR>forth, to be thrown away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपिन्
प्र-क्षेपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, throwing upon, placing<BR>upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेप्तव्य
प्र-क्षेप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown into<BR>or upon, to be scattered upon; to be scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेप्य
प्र-क्षेप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thrown or put on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीवित
प्रक्षीवित प्र-क्षीवित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>क्षीव् with प्र), drunken, intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुद्
प्रक्षुद् प्र-क्षुद्, cl. 7. P. -क्षुणत्ति, -क्षोत्-<BR>तुम्, to pound, crush; to break; to pierce, pierce<BR>through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुण्ण
प्र-क्षुण्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed; pierced through,<BR>lacerated; incited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुभ्
प्रक्षुभ् प्र-क्षुभ्, cl. 1. A., 4. P. -क्षो-<BR>भते, -क्षुभ्यति, -क्षोभितुम्, to be moved, to<BR>be shaken or agitated; to totter, stagger; to be<BR>confused: Caus. -क्षोभयति, -यितुम्, to agitate,<BR>excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षोभण|प्रक्षोभणं
प्र-क्षोभण, अम्, n. agitating, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षै
प्रक्षै प्र-क्षै, cl. 1. P. -क्षायति, -क्षा-<BR>तुम्, to be consumed, to burn (intrans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्णु
प्रक्ष्णु प्र-क्ष्णु, cl. 2. P. -क्ष्णौति, -क्ष्ण-<BR>वितुम्, to sharpen, whet, point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडन|प्रक्ष्वेडनः
प्रक्ष्वेडन प्र-क्ष्वेडन or प्र-क्ष्वेदन,<BR>अस्, आ, m. f. (fr. rt. क्ष्विड् or क्ष्विद् with प्र),<BR>clamour, a loud indistinct noise; an iron arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडा
प्र-क्ष्वेडा, f. humming, grumbling, an inarti-<BR>culate sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडित
प्र-क्ष्वेडित or प्र-क्ष्वेदित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>clamorous, shouting, making a loud indistinct noise;<BR>unctuous.<BR>—प्रक्ष्वेडित-वत् or प्रक्ष्वेदित-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, noisy; unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखर|प्रखरः
प्रखर प्र-खर, अस्, आ, अम्, very hot or<BR>acrid, acrid, biting, pungent; very hard or rough;<BR>(अस्), m. iron armour for the defence of a horse or<BR>elephant [cf. प्रक्खर, प्र-क्षर]; a mule;<BR>a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखल
प्रखल प्र-खल, अस्, m. a great scoundrel,<BR>very wicked person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखाद
प्रखाद प्र-खाद, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. खाद्<BR>with प्र), Ved. devouring, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखिद्
प्रखिद् प्र-खिद्, cl. 6. P. -खिदति, -खेत्-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to thrust away; to harass, afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखिदत्
प्र-खिदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. thrusting away;<BR>harassing, afflicting (according to Mahī-dhara = प्र-<BR>कर्षेण खेदयत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्या
प्रख्या प्र-ख्या, cl. 2. P. -ख्याति, -ख्या-<BR>तुम्, to see (Ved.); to announce, report; to praise,<BR>extol, celebrate: Pass. -ख्यायते, to be recognised<BR>or acknowledged, to be known; to shine: Caus.<BR>-ख्यापयति, -यितुम्, to make generally known,<BR>to be published.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्य|प्रख्यः
प्र-ख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, visible, clear, distinct;<BR>looking or appearing like, resembling, like (at the<BR>end of comps., cf. शशाङ्क-किरण-प्˚); (आ), f.<BR>look, appearance; perceptibility, visibility; making<BR>manifest, disclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यस्
प्र-ख्यस्, आस्, m. = प्रजा-पति, q. v.; the planet<BR>Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यात|प्रख्यातः
प्र-ख्यात, अस्, आ, अम्, celebrated, renowned,<BR>famous, noted, notorious; recognised, acknowledged;<BR>bespoken, forestalled, claimed by right of pre-emp-<BR>tion; pleased, happy.<BR>—प्रख्यात-भाण्ड, अम्, n.<BR>a commodity the pre-emption of which is claimed<BR>by a king.<BR>—प्रख्यात-वप्तृक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a celebrated father.<BR>—प्रख्यात-सद्-भर्-<BR>तृ, ता, m. known as a good husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्याति|प्रख्यातिः
प्र-ख्याति, इस्, f. perceptibility; publicity, no-<BR>toriety, celebrity; praise, eulogium, fame; अ-प्र-<BR>ख्यातिम् इ or गम्, to become imperceptible, vanish,<BR>disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यान|प्रख्यानं
प्र-ख्यान, अम्, n. perception, the being per-<BR>ceived or being known; the making known, report-<BR>ing, communicating; a report, information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यानीय
प्र-ख्यानीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be celebrated or<BR>made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यापन|प्रख्यापनं
प्र-ख्यापन, अम्, n. the making known, pub-<BR>lishing; reporting, communicating; report, inform-<BR>ation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यापनीय
प्र-ख्यापनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be made gene-<BR>rally known, to be published.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यायमान
प्र-ख्यायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being celebrated,<BR>being praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्याल
प्रख्याल प्र-ख्याल, probably a wrong<BR>reading for प्र-ख्यात above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग
प्रग प्र-ग. See under प्र-गम् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगण्
प्रगण् प्र-गण्, cl. 10. P. -गणयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to reckon up, calculate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगण्ड|प्रगंड|प्रगंडः|प्रगण्डः
