प्रगल्भ|प्रगल्भः
प्र-गल्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, bold, confident; resolute,<BR>energetic; prompt, ready; spirited, courageous, brave,<BR>intrepid, daring; audacious, proud, arrogant; impudent,<BR>shameless; strong, able; eminent, illustrious; mature<BR>(as age); (अस्), m. an epithet of the fire employed<BR>at the Jāta-karman; N. of a philosophical writer;<BR>(आ), f. a bold or confident woman, a woman who courts<BR>her husband's caresses, a wanton woman; a scolding<BR>woman, shrew; an epithet of Durgā; (अम्), n. in<BR>a spirited or determined manner, resolutely.<BR>—प्र-<BR>गल्भ-कुलाल, अस्, m. a skilful potter.<BR>—प्रगल्-<BR>भ-ता, f. or प्रगल्भ-त्व, अम्, n. boldness, con-<BR>fidence; energy, resolution, resoluteness; audacity,<BR>arrogance; power, eminence, consequence; per-<BR>verseness, wilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भित
