प्रभा
प्रभा 1. प्र-भा, cl. 2. P. -भाति, -भातुम्,<BR>to shine forth, shine, gleam; to begin to become<BR>light, begin to dawn; to appear, seem; to illuminate,<BR>enlighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
2. प्र-भा, f. light, splendor, radiance, effulgence<BR>[cf. अचिर-प्˚, धूम-प्˚]; a ray of light; the shadow<BR>of the gnomon on a sun-dial; Light variously per-<BR>sonified (as wife of the Sun; or as wife of Kalpa<BR>and mother of Prātar, Madhyan-dina, and Sāya,<BR>i. e. of Morning, Midday, and Evening; or as a<BR>daughter of Svar-bhānu and mother of Nahuṣa);<BR>a N. of Durgā; of an Apsaras; of a herdsman's<BR>wife; of the city of Kuvera; a kind of metre, four<BR>times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯,˘¯¯˘¯; N. of a commentary<BR>by Vaidya-nātha on the Kāvya-pradīpa; of a com-<BR>mentary on the Śabda-kaustubha.<BR>—प्रभा-कर,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, causing light or splendor, radiant, luminous;<BR>(अस्), m. ‘light-maker,’ the sun; the moon; fire;<BR>the ocean; a N. of a Śiva; N. of a deity under the<BR>eighth Manu; of a sage of the race of Atri; of a<BR>teacher of the Mīmāṃsā philosophy associated with<BR>Kumārila-bhaṭṭa; of the author of the Rasa-pradīpa<BR>and of the Laghu-sapta-śatikā-stava; N. of a Samādhi;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">Page0635-a+ 78</a>]<BR>(ई), f. (with Buddhists) N. of one of the ten Bhūmis;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Varṣa.<BR>—प्रभाकर-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a minister in Kaśmīra; of a poet.<BR>—प्र-<BR>भाकर-वर्धन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—प्र-<BR>भाकर-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a minister in Kaś-<BR>mīra.<BR>—प्रभाकरवर्म-स्वामिन्, ई, m. ‘lord of<BR>Prabhākara-varman,’ the statue of the tutelary deity<BR>of Prabhākara-varman.<BR>—प्रभाकर-सिद्धि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a learned man.<BR>—प्रभाकर-स्वामिन्, ई,<BR>m., N. of a temple of Viṣṇu built by Prabhākara-<BR>varman.<BR>—प्रभा-कीट, अस्, m. ‘light-insect,’ a fire-<BR>fly.<BR>—प्रभाञ्जन (˚भा-अञ्˚), अस्, m. the tree<BR>Hyperanthera Moringa; [cf. शोभाञ्जन.]<BR>—प्र-<BR>भा-तरल, अस्, आ, अम्, tremulously radiant; प्र-<BR>भातरलं ज्योतिः, a tremulously radiant flash,<BR>i. e. a flash of lightning.<BR>—प्रभा-तीर्थ, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—प्रभा-पल्लवित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having natural radiance in place of red dye.<BR>—प्र-<BR>भा-पाल, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—प्रभा-<BR>प्ररोह, अस्, m. ‘a shoot of light,’ a flash or ray<BR>of light.<BR>—प्रभा-मण्डल, अम्, n. a circle or<BR>crown of rays.<BR>—प्रभामण्डल-शोभिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>shining with a circle of rays.<BR>—प्रभा-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, consisting of light, shining.<BR>—प्रभा-लेपिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, covered with splendor.<BR>—प्रभा-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having light, luminous, radiant, splendid,<BR>resplendent; (अती), f., N. of a goddess; of the wife<BR>of the Sun; of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda; of an Apsaras; of a sister of the Asura<BR>Indra-damana; of a daughter of king Vajra-nābha<BR>and wife of Pra-dyumna; of the wife of Citra-ratha<BR>king of Aṅga; of a daughter of Su-vīra and wife of<BR>Marutta; of a Tāpasī; of the mother of Malli the<BR>nineteenth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; N. of<BR>the daughter of the Śreṣṭhin Soma-datta and wife of<BR>Madana the son of Vikrama-sena; of the lute of one<BR>of the Gaṇas or demigods attendant on Śiva; N. of a<BR>drama; of a metre, four times ¯¯˘¯˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯;<BR>of another metre, four times ¯¯˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯˘¯.<BR>—प्रभावती-परिणय, अस्, m. ‘the marriage of<BR>Prabhāvatī,’ N. of a drama by Viśva-nātha (= प्र-<BR>भा-वती).<BR>—प्रभा-व्यूह, अस्, m., N. of a god;<BR>(also read प्रभ-व्यूह.)<BR>—प्रभेश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚भा-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

