प्रभाष् प्र-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भाषते, -भा-<BR>षितुम्, to speak to, address, converse with; to de-<BR>clare, proclaim, publish, announce; to divulge, dis-<BR>close, reveal, manifest; to expound, explain; to<BR>prate, prattle: Pass. -भाष्यते, to be called or<BR>named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाष|प्रभाषः
प्र-भाष, अस्, m., N. of a Vasu; (a wrong<BR>reading for प्र-भास.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषण|प्रभाषणं
प्र-भाषण, अम्, n. explanation, interpretation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषणीय
प्रभाषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to explanation<BR>or interpretation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषित
प्र-भाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषिन्
प्र-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, saying, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्
प्रभास् प्र-भास्, cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.)<BR>-भासते (-ति), -भासितुम्, to shine, be brilliant;<BR>to appear: Caus. -भासयति, -यितुम्, to irradiate,<BR>illuminate, enlighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास|प्रभासः
प्र-भास, अस्, m. splendor, beauty; N. of a<BR>Vasu; of a being attendant on Skanda; of a deity<BR>under the eighth Manu; (with Jainas) N. of one of<BR>the eleven Gaṇādhipas; of a minister of Candra-<BR>pāla king of Madra; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a race of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">Page0635-b+ 78</a>]<BR>Ṛṣis; (अस्, अम्), m. n., N. of a celebrated place<BR>of pilgrimage on the west coast of the Dekhan near<BR>Dvārakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासत्
प्र-भासत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shining forth, shining,<BR>effulgent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासन|प्रभासनं
प्र-भासन, अम्, n. irradiating, illumining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्वत्|प्रभास्वन्त्
प्र-भास्वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, shining forth, shining<BR>brightly, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्वर
प्र-भास्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, = प्र-भास्वत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिद्
प्रभिद् 1. प्र-भिद्, cl. 7. P. -भिनत्ति,<BR>-भेत्तुम्, to split asunder, split, cleave; to pierce,<BR>bore, break open, open: Pass. -भिद्यते, to be<BR>broken to pieces, crumble (intrans.); to bud forth,<BR>open, expand (as a flower); to split, divide (intrans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिद्
2. प्र-भिद्, त्, त्, त्, splitting or tearing asunder,<BR>splitting, cleaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्न|प्रभिन्नः
प्र-भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, split asunder, split, cleft,<BR>divided, severed; broken to pieces, broken through;<BR>well cut, cut off, detached; pierced, bored, opened;<BR>budding, expanded; loosened, relaxed; disfigured,<BR>deformed, altered, changed; different, distinct;<BR>(अस्), m. a furious elephant, an elephant in rut or<BR>from whose temples a fragrant fluid exudes; [cf. 2.<BR>दान, p. 408, col. 1.]<BR>—प्रभिन्न-करट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘cloven-cheeked,’ having the cheeks cleft (during<BR>the exuding of a fragrant fluid, as an elephant in<BR>the rutting season).<BR>—प्रभिन्न-विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्,<BR>having the feces divided or relaxed.<BR>—प्रभिन्नाञ्-<BR>जन (˚न-अञ्˚), अम्, n. ‘mixed collyrium,’ an<BR>eye-salve mixed with oil (= भिन्नाञ्जन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेद|प्रभेदः
प्र-भेद, अस्, m. splitting, cutting through;<BR>division, separation, distinction, difference, disparity;<BR>kind, sort; the flowing of a juice or peculiar fluid<BR>from the temples of an elephant; [cf. 2. दान,<BR>p. 408, col. 1.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेदक
प्र-भेदक, अस्, इका, अम्, tearing asunder, cleav-<BR>ing, separating, severing; piercing; distinguishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेदन
प्र-भेदन, अस्, ई, अम्, = प्र-भेदक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभी
प्रभी प्र-भी, cl. 3. P. -बिभेति, -भेतुम्,<BR>to be greatly afraid of, to be terrified at (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभीत
प्र-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, terrified, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्रभु प्र-भु, &c. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुज्
प्रभुज् 1. प्र-भुज् (see rt. 1. भुज्), cl. 6. P.<BR>-भुजति, -भोक्तुम्, to bend forwards, incline, bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुग्न
प्र-भुग्न, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुज्
प्रभुज् 2. प्र-भुज् (see rt. 2. भुज्), cl. 7. P.<BR>A. -भुनक्ति, -भुङ्क्ते, -भोक्तुम्, to begin to eat;<BR>to protect, govern (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभू
प्रभू प्र-भू, cl. 1. P. (rarely also A.)<BR>-भवति (-ते), -भवितुम्, to come into being,<BR>come forth, spring forth, spring up; to proceed, rise,<BR>arise, originate; to be brought forth; to become;<BR>to become manifest, appear; to extend beyond, sur-<BR>pass (Ved.); to become more numerous, become<BR>numerous, multiply, increase, become prevalent; to<BR>be strong or powerful, prevail; to prevail over, have<BR>power or control over (with gen., loc., or dat.); to<BR>be a match for (with dat.); to be able or equal<BR>to (with inf.); to have power for, be competent to<BR>(with dat. or loc.); to be useful, be of use; to profit,<BR>avail; to beseech, intreat, implore: Caus. -भाव-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, to cause to come forth; to increase,<BR>augment, multiply (e. g. to multiply the Soma by<BR>placing it in a greater number of vessels); to provide<BR>more amply, endow more richly; to make powerful,<BR>cause to thrive or prosper, nurture; to gain power<BR>or strength; to recognise, discern: Desid. of Caus.<BR>-बिभावयिषति, to wish to increase, wish to<BR>lengthen or prolong (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव|प्रभवः
प्र-भव, अस्, m. production, birth; origin,<BR>source, cause of existence; generative cause, the basis<BR>or root of being or existence; the operative cause or<BR>immediate origin of being, as the father or mother,<BR>&c.; the place of receiving existence or that where<BR>an object is first perceived, birthplace; the source<BR>of a river [cf. यमुना-प्˚]; the Creator; strength,<BR>might, superiority, power, majesty (= प्र-भाव);<BR>N. of a Sādhya; N. of the first or thirty-fifth year<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">Page0635-c+ 81</a>]<BR>in a sixty years’ cycle of Jupiter; (अस्, आ, अम्), be-<BR>coming prominent, prominent, excelling, excellent,<BR>eminent, distinguished; superior, powerful; (at the<BR>end of a comp.) springing or originating from,<BR>rising from, derived from, belonging to; born, pro-<BR>duced.<BR>—प्रभव-प्रभु, उस्, m. (with Jainas)<BR>N. of one of the six Śruta-kevalins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवत्|प्रभवन्त्
प्र-भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, coming forth, arising;<BR>exceeding; being powerful, prevailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवतितराम्
प्रभवति-तराम्, ind. has greater efficacy, has<BR>more power, has great power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवन|प्रभवनं
प्र-भवन, अम्, n. production, source, origin;<BR>the being born or produced; ruling, presiding (?);<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), produced from, springing from (at the<BR>end of a comp.; cf. मेरु-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवनीय
प्र-भवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, see Scholiast on Pāṇ.<BR>VIII. 4, 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवितृ
प्र-भवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, powerful, potent; (ता),<BR>m. a lord, ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णु|प्रभविष्णुः
प्र-भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, pre-eminent; mighty,<BR>strong, powerful, potent; (उस्), m. a mighty man,<BR>lord, master, lord over (with loc. or gen.).<BR>—प्र-<BR>भविष्णु-ता, f. lordship, supremacy, dominion,<BR>power, might, authority, consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव्य
प्र-भव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be born or produced;<BR>being at the source or origin, original; fit for<BR>rule (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाव|प्रभावः
प्र-भाव, अस्, m. might, power, puissance,<BR>strength, efficacy, virtue; majesty, dignity, glory,<BR>grandeur; superhuman strength or power; effect;<BR>extension, circumference; splendor, brilliance; high<BR>spirit, spirit, magnanimity; tranquillizing, concilia-<BR>tion (?); N. of a chapter of the Rasika-priyā; N.<BR>of a son of Manu Sva-rocis; प्रभावेण, प्रभा-<BR>वात्, प्रभाव-तस्, by or through the power of, by<BR>means of, in consequence of, through, by.<BR>—प्रभा-<BR>व-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, proceeding from conscious majesty<BR>or power.<BR>—प्रभाव-ता, f. power, dignity, su-<BR>periority.<BR>—प्रभाव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>power or strength, powerful, strong, mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावक
प्र-भावक, अस्, आ, अम्, prominent, having<BR>power or influence, influential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावन|प्रभावनः
प्रभावन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Nom. below),<BR>mighty, having power over, ruling, governing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावना
प्र-भावना, f. causing to come forth, disclosing,<BR>revealing, uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावय
प्रभावय, Nom. P. प्रभावयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to have power, exercise power, to have great influ-<BR>ence or power over (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावयितृ
प्र-भावयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, making powerful or<BR>mighty (with acc.); enduing with power, empowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्र-भु, उस्, उस्, or वी, उ, or Ved. प्र-भू, ऊस्, वी,<BR>उ, excelling, surpassing; powerful (e. g. रुद्राद् अपि<BR>प्रभुः, more powerful even than Rudra), mighty,<BR>strong; able, capable, competent, having power to<BR>(e. g. प्रहर्तुम् प्रभुः, having power to wound);<BR>more than sufficient, abundant; a match for (e. g.<BR>प्रभुर् मल्लाय, a match for a wrestler); con-<BR>stant, eternal, everlasting; (उस्), m. a superior, ruler,<BR>governor, master, lord, (किम्-प्रभु, a bad master); an<BR>owner, proprietor; an epithet of Brahma; of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Śiva; of Indra; N. of a deity under the eighth<BR>Manu; N. of a son of Kardama; of a son of Śuka<BR>and Pīvarī; of a son of Bhaga and Siddhi; a sound;<BR>quicksilver.<BR>—प्रभु-ता, f. or प्रभु-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>lordship, supremacy, sovereignty, ascendancy, great-<BR>ness, power; ownership, proprietorship, possession.<BR>—प्रभुत्वाक्षेप (˚त्व-आक्˚), अस्, m. (in rhe-<BR>toric) an allusion to the superiority or supremacy (of<BR>another).<BR>—प्रभु-देव, अस्, m., N. of a teacher<BR>of the Yoga system of philosophy.<BR>—प्रभु-भक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, attached or devoted to a lord, faithful to<BR>a master, loyal; (अस्), m. a good horse.<BR>—प्रभु-<BR>भक्ति, इस्, f. attachment to a lord or master, loyalty,<BR>faithfulness.<BR>—प्रभू-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. the being<BR>sufficient, sufficiency; [cf. प्रभु-त्व.]<BR>—प्रभू-<BR>वसु, उस्, उस्, उ (in the Pada-pāṭha written प्रभु-<BR>वसु), Ved. ‘abundantly wealthy,’ an epithet of Indra;<BR>(उस्), m., N. of a descendant of Aṅgiras and author<BR>of the hymns Ṛg-veda V. 35, 36, IX. 35, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूत|प्रभूतं
प्र-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, produced, sprung from;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">Page0636-a+ 78</a>]<BR>become, been; increased, much, abundant; abound-<BR>ing in; existing in great numbers, numerous, many;<BR>gone up or upwards; high, lofty; long; governed,<BR>presided over; mature, perfect.<BR>—प्रभूत-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, very great or numerous, greatest, highest.<BR>—प्रभूत-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, greater, more nu-<BR>merous, very large.<BR>—प्रभूत-ता, f. or प्रभूत-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. abundance, plenty; multitude, great<BR>number.<BR>—प्रभूत-नागाश्व-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having many elephants and horses and chariots.<BR>—प्रभूत-यवसेन्धन (˚स-इन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abounding in fresh grass and fuel.<BR>—प्रभूत-<BR>रत्न, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—प्रभूत-रूप,<BR>अम्, n. great beauty.<BR>—प्रभूत-वयस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, advanced in age, old.<BR>—प्रभूत-वर्ष, आणि,<BR>n. pl. many years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतक
प्रभूतक, अस्, आ, अम्, containing the word<BR>प्रभूत (as an Adhyāya or an Anuvāka); epithet<BR>of a class of Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूति|प्रभूतिः
प्र-भूति, इस्, f. source, origin; power; imperious<BR>demeanour; sufficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूवन्
प्र-भूवन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. reaching or ex-<BR>tending beyond (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्णु|प्रभूष्णुः
प्र-भूष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, powerful, mighty, strong,<BR>able; [cf. प्र-भविष्णु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्
प्रभूष् प्र-भूष्, cl. 1. P. -भूषति, -भू-<BR>षितुम्, Ved. to set forth in order; to offer, present;<BR>(Sāy.) = प्रकर्षेण स्वी-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृ
प्रभृ प्र-भृ, cl. 1. 3. P. A. -भरति, -ते,<BR>-बिभर्ति, -बिभृते, -भर्तुम्, Ved. to bring or<BR>carry towards, bring before, to lead or bring for-<BR>wards, place before; to offer, present; to stretch forth,<BR>extend; to hurl, cast; to bring in, introduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभरत्
प्र-भरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bringing or leading<BR>towards, bringing nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभर्तव्य
प्र-भर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be supported or<BR>nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभर्तृ
प्र-भर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who brings<BR>or leads near to, bringing near, (Sāy. = सम्यक्<BR>प्रभरन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभर्मन्
प्र-भर्मन्, अ, n., Ved. bringing towards, placing<BR>before; reciting, recitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृति|प्रभृतिः
प्र-भृति, इस्, f. offering, oblation (Ved.); throw-<BR>ing, casting, hurling (Ved.); beginning, commence-<BR>ment, (in this latter sense often used in three genders<BR>at the end of comps. to express ‘having as a begin-<BR>ning or commencement,’ ‘commencing with,’ or =<BR>‘et cætera,’ e. g. मुनयः सोमश्रवः-प्रभृ-<BR>तयः, the Munis beginning with Soma-śravas, i. e. the<BR>Munis, Soma-śravas, &c.; वर्णा ब्राह्मण-प्र-<BR>भृतयः, the Brāhmans and other castes); प्र-<BR>भृति, ind. beginning with, commencing with, be-<BR>ginning with and continuing from, from — forward,<BR>from — upward, from, since (at the end of comps.,<BR>e. g. तत्-प्रभृति, from that time forward; जन्म-<BR>प्रभृति, from birth; or after a word in the abl.,<BR>e. g. बाल्यात् प्रभृति, from boyhood upwards;<BR>स्कन्धात् प्रभृति, from the shoulder; or after<BR>adverbs, e. g. अद्य प्रभृति, beginning from to-day,<BR>from this time forwards, henceforward, henceforth;<BR>अधः प्रभृति, from below, downwards; ततः<BR>प्रभृति or तदा प्रभृति, from that time for-<BR>wards, thenceforth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृथ
प्र-भृथ, अस्, m., Ved. an offering, oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेद|प्रभेदः
प्रभेद प्र-भेद. See 1. प्र-भिद्, p. 635.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंश्
प्रभ्रंश् प्र-भ्रंश्, cl. 4. P., 1. A. -भ्रश्-<BR>यति, -भ्रंशते, -भ्रंशितुम्, to fall off, drop<BR>off, slip off, fall down, fall away; to escape from,<BR>free one's self from (with abl.); to be deprived of<BR>(with inst.): Caus. -भ्रंशयति, -यितुम्, to cause<BR>to fall down, cast down; to cause to fall from, cause<BR>to lose (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंश|प्रभ्रंशः
प्र-भ्रंश, अस्, m. falling off, becoming separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशथु|प्रभ्रंशथुः
प्र-भ्रंशथु, उस्, m. a disease of the nose<BR>accompanied with discharge of mucus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशित
प्र-भ्रंशित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to fall down,<BR>cast down; caused to fall from, deprived of (with<BR>abl.); expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशिन्
प्र-भ्रंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling off, falling down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशुक
प्र-भ्रंशुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. falling off;<BR>vanishing, disappearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रश्यमान
प्र-भ्रश्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, falling down,<BR>being broken off, being broken down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्ट
प्र-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen off, fallen, drop-<BR>ping; broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टक|प्रभ्रष्टकं
प्र-भ्रष्टक, अम्, n. a chaplet or wreath of<BR>flowers suspended from the lock on the crown of<BR>the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रम्
प्रभ्रम् प्र-भ्रम्, cl. 1. 4. P. -भ्रमति,<BR>-भ्राम्यति, -भ्रमितुम्, to roam or wander about;<BR>to roam or wander through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्राज्
प्रभ्राज् प्र-भ्राज्, cl. 1. A. -भ्राजते, -भ्रा-<BR>जितुम्, Ved. to shine forth, gleam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्राजमान
प्र-भ्राजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shining forth,<BR>gleaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्
प्रम् प्रम्, ind. (fr. rt. 1. प्रा), in गोष्पद-<BR>प्रम्, sufficiently to fill the print of a cow's foot; (also<BR>गोष्पद-पूरम्, Scholiast on Pāṇ. III. 4, 32.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमंहिष्ठीय
प्रमंहिष्ठीय प्रमंहिष्ठीय, अम्, n., Ved.,<BR>N. of a Sāman (so called from its beginning with<BR>the words प्र मंहिष्ठाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमगन्द
प्रमगन्द प्र-मगन्द, अस्, m., Ved. the son<BR>of a usurer, (according to Sāy. मगन्द = कुसीदिन्,<BR>तद्-अपत्यम् प्र-मगन्दः); N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमग्न
प्रमग्न प्र-मग्न. See प्र-मज्ज् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गन
प्रमङ्गन प्र-मङ्गन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. मङ्ग्<BR>with प्र), going, proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गनीय
प्र-मङ्गनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be gone or pro-<BR>ceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गित
प्र-मङ्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone, proceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमज्ज्
प्रमज्ज् प्र-मज्ज्, cl. 6. P. -मज्जति, -मङ्क्-<BR>तुम्, Ved. to immerse one's self in, dip into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमग्न
प्र-मग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, immersed, dipped,<BR>drowned. See Scholiast on Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमणस्
प्रमणस् प्र-मणस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, careful, soli-<BR>citous, attentive (Ved.); kind, amiable (Ved.); good-<BR>natured, joyful, cheerful; [cf. प्र-मनस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमण्डल
प्रमण्डल प्र-मण्डल, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>the felly of a wheel (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत
प्रमत प्र-मत, &c. See प्र-मन्, p. 637.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्त|प्रमत्तः
प्रमत्त प्र-मत्त, &c. See 1. प्र-मद्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ्
प्रमथ् प्र-मथ् or प्र-मन्थ्, cl. 1. 9. P.<BR>-मथति, -मन्थति, -मथ्नाति, -मन्थितुम्, to<BR>stir about violently, agitate, churn; to trample down,<BR>strike down, bruise; to rob (Ved.); to assault<BR>violently, handle roughly, harass, annoy; to destroy,<BR>lay waste, devastate; to tear away, tear off, tear out,<BR>cut out: Caus. -माथयति, -यितुम्, to assault vio-<BR>lently, handle roughly, harass, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ|प्रमथः
प्र-मथ, अस्, m. ‘destroyer, tormentor,’ N. of<BR>a class of fiends attending on Śiva; N. of one of<BR>the hundred sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; a horse; (आ), f.<BR>the plant Terminalia Chebula or Citrina (= हरी-<BR>तकी); N. of the wife of Kṣupa and mother of<BR>Vīra; pain, affliction (?).<BR>—प्रमथ-नाथ, अस्,<BR>or प्रमथ-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the Pramathas,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—प्रमथाधिप (˚थ-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘ruler of the Pramathas,’ an epithet of Śiva;<BR>of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—प्रमथालय (˚थ-आल्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘abode of torment (?) ,’ hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथन|प्रमथनं
प्र-मथन, अस्, ई, अम्, harassing, tormenting,<BR>torturing, paining, hurting, injuring; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a magical formula pronounced over weapons; N.<BR>of a Dānava; (अम्), n. hurting, paining, distressing,<BR>injuring; killing, slaughter; agitating, churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथित|प्रमथितं
प्र-मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, well churned; trampled<BR>on, cut down, killed; pained, distressed; (अम्), n. but-<BR>termilk without water.<BR>—प्रमथित-पुरःसर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the leader killed, whose leader is slain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ्य
प्र-मथ्य, ind. having conquered or oppressed;<BR>having used violence, violently, forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ्यमान
प्र-मथ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being churned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्थ|प्रमन्थः
प्र-मन्थ, अस्, m., Ved. a stick used for rubbing<BR>wood to produce fire by friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्थु
प्र-मन्थु, उस्, m., N. of a son of Vīra-vrata<BR>and younger brother of Manthu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथ|प्रमाथः
प्र-माथ, अस्, m. stirring about, agitation; tor-<BR>menting, torturing, afflicting, paining; killing;<BR>tearing; forcible abduction, rape [cf. द्रौपदी-प्˚];<BR>violence; N. of one of the sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;<BR>of one of the attendants of Skanda; of a Dānava;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. epithet of the fiends attendant upon<BR>Śiva (= प्र-मथ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथित
प्र-माथित, अस्, आ, अम्, assaulted violently,<BR>roughly handled; violated, ravished, forcibly carried<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथिन्
प्र-माथिन्, ई, इनी, इ, stirring about, setting in<BR>motion, agitating; striking off, striking down, used<BR>for striking or knocking down; tearing, rending;<BR>breaking, cutting; disquieting, troubling, harassing,<BR>annoying, afflicting, torturing [cf. चित्त-प्˚]; killing,<BR>destroying, a destroyer; (ई), m., N. of a son of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a Rākṣasa; of a monkey; N.<BR>of the thirteenth (of forty-seventh) year of a sixty<BR>years' cycle of Jupiter; (इनी), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्
प्रमद् 1. प्र-मद्, cl. 4. P. -माद्यति, -मदि-<BR>तुम्, to enjoy one's self, be joyous, sport, play,<BR>gambol (Ved.); to be regardless of, be indifferent<BR>to (with abl.); to pay no attention to, give no heed<BR>to, neglect, be heedless about (with loc.); to neglect<BR>duty for, idle away time in (with loc.); Caus. P. A.<BR>-मादयति, -ते, -यितुम्, to make light of, ridicule;<BR>(A.) to enjoy, indulge in (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्त|प्रमत्तः
प्र-मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, excited, wanton, lascivious,<BR>rutting; drunken, intoxicated; mad, insane; careless,<BR>regardless, heedless, inattentive, negligent; unmindful<BR>of duty; blundering, a blunderer.<BR>—प्रमत्त-गीत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, inattentively or carelessly sung.<BR>—प्र-<BR>मत्त-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, careless-minded, heedless,<BR>negligent.<BR>—प्रमत्त-ता, f. inattentiveness, inat-<BR>tention, sleepiness, mental inactivity.<BR>—१. प्रमत्त-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, inattentive, careless.<BR>—२. प्रमत्त-<BR>वत्, ind. as if drunk, like one intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्
2. प्र-मद्, त्, f., Ved. lust, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद|प्रमदः
प्र-मद, अस्, m. joy, joyousness, joyfulness,<BR>pleasure, delight, elation, rapture; the Datura tree or<BR>thorn-apple, D. Metel [cf. उन्-मत्त]; N. of a<BR>Dānava; of a son of Vasiṣṭha and one of the seven<BR>sages under Manu Uttama, = गुल्फ?; (आ), f. a<BR>young and wanton woman, a handsome or beautiful<BR>woman, a woman in general; the sign of the zodiac<BR>Virgo; N. of a metre of 29 + 27 syllables; of another<BR>metre, four times ˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘˘¯; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), wanton, dissolute; mad, intoxicated (literally<BR>or metaphorically); impassioned; violent; careless.<BR>—प्रमद-कण्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—प्र-<BR>मद-कानन or प्रमदा-कानन, अम्, n. a<BR>royal garden or pleasure-ground attached to the<BR>gynæceum.<BR>—प्रमद-रोप्य, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city in the Dekhan; [cf. महिला-रोप्य, मिहिला-<BR>रोप्य.]<BR>—प्रमद-वन = प्रमद-कानन.<BR>—प्रमदा-जन, अस्, m. womankind, the female<BR>sex.<BR>—प्रमदानन (˚दा-आन्˚), अम्, n. a kind of<BR>metre, four times ˘˘¯˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘¯˘¯.<BR>—प्रमदा-वन, अम्, n. a royal garden or<BR>pleasure-ground for the wives of a prince (attached<BR>especially to the private apartments of the palace).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदक
प्र-मदक, अस्, आ, अम्, dissolute, licentious,<BR>sensual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदन|प्रमदनं
प्र-मदन, अम्, n. amorous desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदाय
प्रमदाय, Nom. P. प्रमदायति, -यितुम्,<BR>to behave like a wanton woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदितव्य
प्र-मदितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be neglected or dis-<BR>regarded, to be treated with inattention (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्वर
प्र-मद्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, inattentive, careless; (आ),<BR>f., N. of the wife of Ruru and mother of Śunaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद|प्रमादः
प्र-माद, अस्, m. drunkenness, intoxication; mad-<BR>ness, insanity, distraction, confusion; negligence, inat-<BR>tention, carelessness; inadvertence, error, inaccuracy,<BR>a blunder, mistake; a particular high number.<BR>—प्र-<BR>माद-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, drunken, intoxicated; mad,<BR>insane; incautious, careless, heedless, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिका
प्रमादिका, f. an imprudent or careless woman;<BR>a deflowered girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादित
प्र-मादित, अस्, आ, अम्, made light of, ridiculed,<BR>mocked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिन्
प्रमादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, drunken, intoxicated; in-<BR>sane; negligent, inattentive, inadvertent, careless,<BR>heedless, incautious, indifferent; (ई), m., N. of the<BR>forty-seventh (or twenty-first) year of a sixty years’<BR>cycle of Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद्य
प्रमाद्य (?), अम्, n. insanity, carelessness.<BR>—प्रमाद्य-तस् (?), ind. from carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्
प्रमन् प्र-मन्, cl. 8. A. -मनुते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to think upon, excogitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत
प्र-मत, अस्, आ, अम्, thought out, excogitated;<BR>wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमतक
प्रमतक, अस्, m., N. of an ancient sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमति
प्र-मति, इस्, f. care, providence, protection (Ved.,<BR>cf. अदब्ध-व्रत-प्˚, इन्द्र-प्˚); one who pro-<BR>vides for, a protector (Ved.); (इस्), m., N. of an<BR>ancient sage; of a son of Cyavana and father of<BR>Ruru; of a prince (son of Janam-ejaya); of a son<BR>of Prāṃśu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्र-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस् (fr. प्र + मनस्), cheer-<BR>ful-minded, good-tempered, in good spirits, happy,<BR>delighted; [cf. प्र-मणस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्त्र
प्र-मन्त्र, अस्, or अम्, m. or n.? (fr. प्र +<BR>मन्त्र), a particular high number; [cf. प्र-मात्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्थ्|प्रमंथ्
प्रमन्थ् प्र-मन्थ्. See प्र-मथ्, p. 636.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्द
प्रमन्द प्र-मन्द, अस्, m. or प्र-मन्दनी,<BR>f., Ved. a species of fragrant plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्यु
प्रमन्यु प्र-मन्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, incensed or<BR>enraged against (with loc.); distressed, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमय|प्रमयः
प्रमय प्र-मय, &c. See p. 638, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर
प्रमर प्र-मर, &c. See under प्र-मृ,<BR>p. 638, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर्दक
प्रमर्दक प्र-मर्दक, प्र-मर्दन, &c.<BR>See प्र-मृद्, p. 638, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमहस्
प्रमहस् प्र-महस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. of great<BR>splendor (said of Mitra-Varuṇa, Sāy. = प्रकृष्ट-<BR>तेजस्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा 1. प्र-मा, cl. 2. P., 3. 4. A. -माति,<BR>-मिमीते, -मायते, -मातुम्, to measure; to form,<BR>frame, make; to arrange, set in order; to form a<BR>correct notion of (anything), understand; to con-<BR>jecture: Caus. -मापयति, -यितुम्, to cause correct<BR>knowledge, afford proof or authority, give proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
2. प्र-मा, f. basis, foundation (Ved.); a measure<BR>(Ved.); true perception, correct notion, accurate<BR>conception, true and certain knowledge, knowledge<BR>exempt from all error; consciousness, perception; a<BR>kind of metre.<BR>—प्रमा-त्व, अम्, n. accuracy of<BR>perception, trueness or correctness of knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाण|प्रमाणं|प्रमाणः
प्र-माण, अम्, n. measure, scale, standard;<BR>measure in general (whether of weight, length, or<BR>capacity); magnitude, extent, circumference, length,<BR>duration (of time); weight, quantity; rule, sanction,<BR>ground of assurance, standard, authority, judgment,<BR>warrant; a decider, one whose advice or decision is<BR>an authority (e. g. प्रमाणम् भवती, your lady-<BR>ship is the warrant or you must judge; प्रमाणम्<BR>भवन्तः, your honours are the authority, i. e.<BR>it is yours to decide or I abide by your advice, cf.<BR>also स्त्री-प्˚; in this sense प्रमाण sometimes<BR>follows the number and gender of the word with<BR>which it is placed in apposition, e. g. यदि वेदाः<BR>प्रमाणास् ते, if the Vedas be thy authorities; स्त्री<BR>प्रमाणी येषाम्, they whose authority is a woman);<BR>a means of acquiring प्रमा or certain knowledge,<BR>source of knowledge, means of proof, proof, (the<BR>Vedānta admits six Pramāṇas, viz. 1. प्रत्यक्ष,<BR>perception by the senses; 2. अनुमान, inference;<BR>3. उपमान, analogy or comparison; 4. शब्द or<BR>आप्त-वचन, verbal authority, trustworthy testi-<BR>mony, especially of an inspired person, revelation;<BR>5. अन्-उपलब्धि or अभाव-प्रत्यक्ष, non-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">Page0637-b+ 81</a>]<BR>perception or negative proof; 6. अर्थापत्ति, in-<BR>ference from circumstances. The Nyāya admits<BR>only four, excluding the last two. The Sāṅkhya<BR>only three, viz. Pratyakṣa, Anumāna, and Śabda,<BR>excluding the third or Upamāna as well as the fifth<BR>and sixth: besides the Pramāṇas of the three orthodox<BR>schools, with their branches, other schools increase<BR>the number to nine by adding 1. सम्भव, equi-<BR>valence; 2. ऐतिह्य, tradition or fallible testimony;<BR>3. चेष्टा, gesture); testimony, evidence; a scrip-<BR>ture, a work of sacred authority; a speaker of the<BR>truth; a correct notion, right conception; cause,<BR>motive; a sense of security, freedom from appre-<BR>hension; the prosodial length of a vowel; physical<BR>power or strength; the first term in a rule of three<BR>sum; principal, capital; oneness, unity; constant,<BR>eternal; a title of Viṣṇu; (अस्), m. rule, standard,<BR>authority; N. of a large fig-tree on the bank of<BR>the Ganges (Mahā-bh. Vana-p. 41); (ई), f. rule,<BR>standard, authority; a kind of metre.<BR>—प्रमाण-<BR>कोटी, f., N. of a particular spot or of a Tīrtha near<BR>the above fig-tree on the bank of the Ganges; [cf.<BR>प्र-माण.]<BR>—प्रमाण-ज्ञ, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—प्रमाण-तस्, ind. agreeably to measure or<BR>weight, with respect to measure, &c.; according to<BR>proof or authority.<BR>—प्रमाण-ता, f. or प्रमाण-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. authority, warranty.<BR>—प्रमाण-<BR>दृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, recognised by authority, en-<BR>joined by good authorities.<BR>—प्रमाण-पत्त्र,<BR>अम्, n. a written warrant.<BR>—प्रमाण-पुरुष,<BR>अस्, m. ‘a man who is an authority,’ an umpire,<BR>arbitrator, judge.<BR>—प्रमाण-प्रमोद, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Nyāya work by Hari.<BR>—प्रमाण-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, constituting proof or authority; true, autho-<BR>ritative; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—प्रमाण-<BR>माला or प्रमाण-रत्नमाला, f., N. of a Vedānta<BR>work by Ānanda-bodha Yati.<BR>—प्रमाण-लक्षण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Vedānta work.<BR>—प्रमाण-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, furnished with proofs, established by proofs,<BR>well-founded.<BR>—प्रमाण-वाक्य, अम्, n. authorita-<BR>tive statement, authority.<BR>—प्रमाण-वार्त्तिक, अम्,<BR>n. and प्रमाण-विनिश्चय, अस्, m., N. of two<BR>works by Dharma-kīrtti.<BR>—प्रमाण-शास्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>any work of sacred authority, scripture.<BR>—प्रमाण-<BR>समुच्चय, अस्, m., N. of a work by Diṅ-nāga.<BR>—प्रमाण-सूत्र, अम्, n. a measuring cord.<BR>—प्रमाणाधिक (˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>beyond measure, excessive, unnaturally strong.<BR>—प्रमाणान्तर (˚ण-अन्˚), अम्, n. another means<BR>of proof.<BR>—प्रमाणान्तर-ता, f. the being another<BR>means of proof.<BR>—प्रमाणाभाव (˚ण-अभ्˚), अस्,<BR>m. absence of proof, want of authority.<BR>—प्रमाणी-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being an authority or proof,<BR>proving, establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणक|प्रमाणकः
प्रमाणक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of a<BR>comp.) = प्र-माण, measure, quantity, extent, cir-<BR>cumference; (इका), f. a kind of metre, four times<BR>˘¯˘¯˘¯˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणय
प्रमाणय, Nom. P. प्रमाणयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to make or regard as an authority upon any point<BR>(with acc. of the person and loc. of the object); to<BR>receive as an authority, admit or obey as an authority;<BR>to hold up as a model; to prove, demonstrate, show<BR>clearly, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणयत्
प्रमाणयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, receiving or admit-<BR>ting as an authority, obeying as authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणिक
प्रमाणिक, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. प्रमाणक above],<BR>forming a measure or standard, being a measure,<BR>forming an authority (perhaps a wrong reading for<BR>प्रामाणिक, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणित
प्र-माणित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्रमाणय above),<BR>proved, demonstrated, shown clearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकृ
प्रमाणी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to mete out or apportion to (with gen.);<BR>to take as a rule or authority, regard as an autho-<BR>rity; to conform to, obey (with acc.); to regard as<BR>proof; to prove.<BR>—प्रमाणी-करण, अम्, n. esta-<BR>blishing or admitting as authority, regarding as proof.<BR>—प्रमाणी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, admitted or esta-<BR>blished as proof, regarded as authority; conformed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातृ
प्र-मातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, knowing truly or well,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">Page0637-c+ 74</a>]<BR>having a right notion or idea, competent to judge;<BR>any person who gives evidence or proof, an authority,<BR>a proof; proving, demonstrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापक|प्रमापकः
प्र-मापक, अस्, इका, अम्, affording proof or<BR>certain knowledge, furnishing authority; (अस्), m.<BR>an authority, an author cited or quoted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमित|प्रमितः
1. प्र-मित, अस्, आ, अम्, meted out, measured;<BR>known, understood; established by argument, demon-<BR>strated, proved; measured off, limited, few, little;<BR>(at the end of a comp.) measuring, of such and such<BR>measure or extent, of such and such size.<BR>—प्रमि-<BR>ताक्षरा (˚त-अक्˚), f. ‘having measured syllables,’<BR>a kind of metre, four times ˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिति|प्रमितिः
प्र-मिति, इस्, f. measure, measuring, measurement;<BR>a correct notion, right conception, true knowledge,<BR>knowledge or information established by proof; true<BR>inference or analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेय
प्र-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be measured, measurable,<BR>finite; to be fathomed or penetrated; admitting of<BR>evidence or proof, to be proved, provable, demon-<BR>strable; discernible; (अम्), n. an object of certain<BR>knowledge; the thing to be proved, subject under<BR>discussion, topic to be discussed or established.<BR>—प्र-<BR>मेय-कमल-मार्तण्ड, N. of a work.<BR>—प्र-<BR>मेय-त्व, अम्, n. provableness, capability of being<BR>proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातव्य
प्रमातव्य प्र-मातव्य. See p. 638, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामह|प्रमातामहः
प्रमातामह प्र-मातामह, अस्, m. a maternal<BR>great-grandfather; (ई), f. a maternal great-grand-<BR>mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमात्र
प्रमात्र प्र-मात्र, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथ|प्रमाथः
प्रमाथ प्र-माथ, &c. See p. 636, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद|प्रमादः
प्रमाद प्र-माद, &c. See under 1. प्र-<BR>मद्, p. 636, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापण|प्रमापणं
प्रमापण प्र-मापण, &c. See p. 638,<BR>col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाय
प्रमाय प्र-माय. See under प्र-मि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमार
प्रमार प्र-मार. See प्र-मृ, p. 638.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमार्जक
प्रमार्जक प्र-मार्जक, &c. See under प्र-<BR>मृज्, p. 638, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमि
प्रमि प्र-मि (see rt. 1. मि), cl. 5. P. A.<BR>-मिनोति, -मिनुते, -मातुम्, to erect, build (Ved.);<BR>to judge, observe, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाय
प्र-माय, ind. having perceived or observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमित|प्रमितः
2. प्र-मित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see above), Ved.<BR>erected, built.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिद्
प्रमिद् प्र-मिद्, cl. 1. A., 4. P. -मेदते,<BR>-मेद्यति, -मेदितुम्, to begin to become fat; to<BR>begin to show affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदित
प्र-मेदित, अस्, आ, अम्, having begun to show<BR>affection (according to a Scholiast = स्निग्धी-भवि-<BR>तुम् आरब्धः); being or made unctuous, unctuous,<BR>greasy.<BR>—प्रमेदित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having be-<BR>come unctuous, having been made unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिह्
प्रमिह् प्र-मिह्, cl. 1. P. -मेहति, -मेढुम्,<BR>to make water, pass urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीढ|प्रमीढः
प्र-मीढ, अस्, आ, अम्, passed as urine; thick,<BR>compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेह|प्रमेहः
प्र-मेह, अस्, m. urinary disease (a general term<BR>applied to all diseases characterized by a morbid con-<BR>dition of the urine; twenty-one varieties are enume-<BR>rated, including diabetes, gleet, gonorrhœa, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेहिन्
प्र-मेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from urinary<BR>disease or affections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमी
प्रमी प्र-मी, cl. 9. P. A. -मीणाति, -मीणीते<BR>(Ved. -मिनाति, -मिनीते), -मातुम्, to frustrate,<BR>annul, destroy, annihilate; to diminish; to change,<BR>alter; to neglect, transgress, infringe (Ved.); to<BR>miss, lose (one's way), forget (Ved.); to cause to<BR>disappear, put out of sight, leave behind, outstrip,<BR>surmount, surpass; to come to naught, perish, die:<BR>Caus. -मापयति, -यितुम्, to destroy, annihilate,<BR>kill, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमय|प्रमयः
प्र-मय, अस्, m. ruin, downfall, fall, death;<BR>killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमयु
प्र-मयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. liable to be lost or<BR>destroyed, destructible, perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातव्य
प्र-मातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be slain or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापण|प्रमापणं
प्र-मापण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.), murder-<BR>ing, murderous, a murderer; (अम्), n. killing, slay-<BR>ing, slaughter; (sometimes also spelt प्र-मापन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापयितृ
प्र-मापयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, causing to perish,<BR>destructive, leading to ruin; a murderer.<BR>—प्रमा-<BR>पयितृ-त्व, अम्, n. destructiveness, murderousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापित
प्र-मापित, अस्, आ, अम्, destroyed, killed, slain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापिन्
प्र-मापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying, killing, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमायु
प्र-मायु, उस्, उस्, उ, or प्र-मायुक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. liable to ruin or destruction, perishable,<BR>destructible, dying away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीणत्
प्र-मीणत्, अन्, अती, अत्, injuring, killing; over-<BR>coming, subduing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीत|प्रमीतः
प्र-मीत, अस्, आ, अम्, dead, deceased; immo-<BR>lated, sacrificed.<BR>—प्रमीत-पतिक, आ, f. one whose<BR>husband is dead, a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीति|प्रमीतिः
प्र-मीति, इस्, f. ruin, destruction, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीय
प्र-मीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be destroyed or killed,<BR>destructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीढ|प्रमीढः
प्रमीढ प्र-मीढ. See प्र-मिह्, p. 637.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमील्
प्रमील् प्र-मील्, cl. 1. P. -मीलति, -मीलितुम्,<BR>to close or shut the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीला
प्र-मीला, f. shutting the eyes, sleepiness, lassi-<BR>tude, weariness, enervation, exhaustion from indo-<BR>lence or fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीलित
प्र-मीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, closing the eyes, with<BR>closed eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीलिन्
प्र-मीलिन्, ई, m., N. of a demon (who causes<BR>the eyes to close, or brings on faintness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीव्
