प्रसुत
प्र-सुत, अस्, आ, अम्, brought forth, born; (अस्<BR>or अम्), m. or n. (?) , a particular high number; [cf.<BR>महा-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
1. प्र-सू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ (for 2. see p. 649), bringing<BR>forth, bearing [cf. पितृ-प्˚, पुत्रिका-प्˚, स्त्री-प्˚];<BR>fruitful, productive; (ऊस्), f. a mother; a mare; a<BR>young shoot, tender grass or herbs, sacrificial grass,<BR>(Sāy. = प्रसवित्र्य् ओषधी); a spreading creeper,<BR>the plantain.<BR>—प्रसू-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, or प्रसू-<BR>वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. furnished with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूका
प्र-सूका, f. a mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूत|प्रसूतं|प्रसूतः
प्र-सूत, अस्, आ, अम्, procreated, begotten, en-<BR>gendered; brought forth, born, produced, grown;<BR>begetting, engendering; one who has brought forth,<BR>delivered; (अस्), m., N. of a class of deities under<BR>Manu Cākṣuṣa; (अम्), n. a flower; any productive<BR>source; (आ), f. a woman who has brought forth a<BR>child, a woman recently delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूति|प्रसूतिः
1. प्र-सूति, इस्, f. procreating, procreation, beget-<BR>ting, generating; bringing forth, bearing; calving;<BR>laying eggs; birth, production, generation; coming<BR>forth, growth (of fruits, flowers, leaves; cf. फल-<BR>प्˚); a production, product; a procreator, begetter;<BR>one who brings forth, a mother; offspring, children,<BR>progeny; N. of a daughter of Maru and wife of<BR>Dakṣa.<BR>—प्रसूति-ज, अम्, n. ‘birth-produced,’ pain<BR>or affliction (mental or corporeal) resulting as a ne-<BR>cessary consequence of birth.<BR>—प्रसूति-वायु, उस्,<BR>m. air generated in the womb during the pangs of<BR>travail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिका
प्रसूतिका, f. a woman who has had a child, a<BR>woman recently delivered; = 1. प्र-सूति (at the end<BR>of a comp., cf. नश्यत्-प्˚, सकृत्-प्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसून|प्रसूनं
प्र-सून, अस्, आ, अम्, born, produced; (अम्), n.<BR>a flower; a bud, blossom; fruit.<BR>—प्रसून-बाण<BR>or प्रसून-वाण, अस्, m. ‘having flowers for<BR>arrows,’ the god of love.<BR>—प्रसून-वर्ष, अस्,<BR>m. a shower of flowers (rained from heaven).<BR>—प्रसूनाञ्जलि (˚न-अञ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, presenting<BR>a nosegay of flowers held in both hands opened and<BR>hollowed (= पुष्पाञ्जलि).<BR>—प्रसूनेषु (˚न-<BR>इषु), उस्, m. ‘flower-arrowed,’ an epithet of the<BR>god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनक|प्रसूनकं|प्रसूनकः
प्रसूनक, अम्, n. a flower; a bud, blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

