प्राङ्न्याय|प्राङ्न्यायः
प्राङ्न्याय प्राङ्-न्याय, &c. See p. 654, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचण्ड्य|प्राचंड्य|प्राचंड्यं
प्राचण्ड्य प्राचण्ड्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-चण्ड),<BR>violence, vehemence, passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचार
प्राचार प्राचार (प्र-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, con-<BR>trary to or deviating from ordinary institutions and<BR>observances (?); (अस्), m. a particular insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचार्य|प्राचार्यः|प्राचार्य्य
प्राचार्य (प्र-आच्˚), अस्, m. a pupil, scholar (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचिन्वत्|प्राचिन्वन्त्
प्राचिन्वत् प्राचिन्वत्, अन्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Janam-ejaya (= प्र-चिन्वत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीन|प्राचीनः
प्राचीन प्राचीन. See p. 654, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीर|प्राचीरं
प्राचीर प्राचीर, अम्, n. an enclosure, hedge,<BR>fence, wall; [cf. क्षौणी-प्˚, मही-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचुर्य|प्राचुर्यं
प्राचुर्य प्राचुर्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्रचुर), mul-<BR>titude, quantity; abundance, copiousness, plentiful-<BR>ness, plenty; (एण), ind. in a mass; fully, in detail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचेतस्
प्राचेतस् प्राचेतस्, असस्, m. pl. an epithet<BR>of the ten sons of Prācīna-barhis (= प्र-चेतस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचेतस|प्राचेतसः
प्राचेतस, अस्, m. a patronymic from Pra-cetas;<BR>a patronymic of Manu; of Dakṣa; of Vālmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्य|प्राच्यः
प्राच्य प्राच्य. See p. 654, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राछ्|प्राच्छ्
प्राछ् प्राछ्, ट्, ट्, ट् (fr. rt. प्रछ्), asking,<BR>inquiring, an inquirer, questioner.<BR>—प्राड्-विवाक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘one who interrogates and discriminates,’ a<BR>judge, magistrate, the presiding officer in a court of<BR>judicature (Manu VIII. 79, 181).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजक|प्राजकः
प्राजक प्राजक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. अज् with प्र),<BR>a driver, charioteer, coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजन|प्राजनं|प्राजनः
प्राजन, अस्, अम्, m. n. a whip, goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजिक|प्राजिकः
प्राजिक, अस्, m. a hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजितृ
प्राजितृ, ता, m. a driver, charioteer, coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजिन्
प्राजिन्, ई, m. = प्राजिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजया
प्राजया प्राजया, see Gaṇa Sākṣādādi to<BR>Pāṇ. I. 4, 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजहित|प्राजहितः
प्राजहित प्राजहित, अस्, m., Ved. a Gārha-<BR>patya fire maintained during a longer period of time,<BR>an older Gārhapatya fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत
प्राजापत प्राजापत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रजा-<BR>पति), see Gaṇa Mahiṣyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत्य|प्राजापत्यं|प्राजापत्यः
प्राजापत्य, अस्, आ (or ती), अम्, belonging to<BR>or derived from Prajā-pati, relating to Prajā-pati,<BR>sacred to Prajā-pati; (अस्), m., with or without<BR>विवाह or विधि, the third or according to Manu<BR>the fourth form of marriage (that in which the<BR>father gives his daughter to the bridegroom without<BR>receiving a present from him, but with the convic-<BR>tion that the two will live faithfully together, Manu<BR>III. 30); scil. उपवास, a kind of penance (lasting<BR>twelve days, food being eaten during the first three<BR>once in the morning, during the next three once in<BR>the evening, in the next three only if given as<BR>alms, and a plenary fast being observed during the<BR>three remaining days); scil. तिथि, the eighth day in<BR>the dark half of the month Pauṣa; a patronymic<BR>of Pataṅ-ga; of Prajā-vat; of Yakṣma-nāśana; of<BR>Yajña; of Vimada; of Viṣṇu; of Saṃvaraṇa; of<BR>Hiraṇya-garbha; (with Jainas) N. of the first black<BR>Vāsudeva; a N. of the confluence of the Gaṅgā and<BR>Yamunā, = प्र-याग; (अम्), n. a particular sacrifice<BR>performed before appointing a daughter to raise issue<BR>in default of male heirs; scil. भ or नक्षत्र,<BR>the asterism Rohiṇī; generative energy, procreative<BR>power; (अस् or अम्), m. or n. (?), the heaven or<BR>sphere of the Manes, = पितृ-लोक; (आ), f. giving<BR>away the whole of one's property before entering<BR>upon the life of an ascetic or mendicant; a patro-<BR>nymic of Dakṣiṇā; scil. शकटी, N. of an asterism,<BR>the chariot of Rohiṇī (probably = α β γ δ ε Tauri).<BR>—प्राजापत्य-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition<BR>of belonging or referring to Prajā-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत्यक
प्राजापत्यक, अस्, &c., belonging or referring<BR>or sacred to Prajā-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजावत
प्राजावत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रजा-वत्), see Gaṇa<BR>Mahiṣyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजेश|प्राजेशं
प्राजेश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रजेश), Ved. sacred to<BR>Prajā-pati; (अम्), n. the Nakṣatra Rohiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजेश्वर
प्राजेश्वर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रजेश्वर), sacred to<BR>Prajā-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजिधर
प्राजिधर प्राजिधर, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजिमठिका
प्राजिमठिका प्राजिमठिका, f., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजेश|प्राजेशं
प्राजेश प्राजेश, प्राजेश्वर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञ|प्राज्ञः
प्राज्ञ प्राज्ञ, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. प्र-ज्ञा),<BR>intellectual, (opposed to शारीर, तैजस); intelligent,<BR>wise, clever; patient in investigation; (Ved.) having<BR>no deep insight; (अस्), m. a wise or learned man, a<BR>Paṇḍit, a skilful or clever man; a kind of parrot<BR>with red stripes on the neck and wings; (आ or ई), f.<BR>a clever or intelligent woman; (ई), f. the wife of an<BR>intellectual man, wife of a Paṇḍit; (आ), f. intelligence,<BR>understanding.<BR>—प्राज्ञ-कथा, f. a story of a wise<BR>man, tale about a wise man.<BR>—प्राज्ञ-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>or प्राज्ञ-ता, f. wisdom, learning.<BR>—प्राज्ञ-मान,<BR>अम्, n. respect for learned men.<BR>—प्राज्ञ-मानिन् or<BR>प्राज्ञम्-मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, thinking one's self wise,<BR>fancying one's self a learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्य|प्राज्यं
प्राज्य प्राज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्र with rt. अज्<BR>or fr. प्र + आज्य, clarified butter used for obla-<BR>tions?), abundant, plentiful, much, many, great, im-<BR>portant; lofty.<BR>—प्राज्य-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the Rājāvali-patākā.<BR>—प्राज्य-विक्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing great power.<BR>—प्राज्य-वृष्टि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, sending rain in abundance (said of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्च्|प्रांच्
प्राञ्च् प्राञ्च् (प्र-अञ्च्), प्राङ्, प्राची, प्राक्,<BR>turned towards the front, directed forwards, being<BR>before, in front, foremost; turned towards, inclined<BR>towards, disposed, ready, willing (Ved.); turning<BR>eastward, eastern, easterly; previous, prior, former;<BR>प्राञ्चं कृ, to place in front, bring, offer, provide<BR>(Ved.); to promote, further, advance (Ved., Sāy.<BR>= प्रकर्षेण गच्छन्तं कृ); to spread out,<BR>stretch out (Ved.); प्राञ्चस्, m. pl. the people of<BR>the east, eastern people; eastern grammarians;<BR>प्राचि, f. the east; प्राक्, ind. (with abl. or rarely<BR>with gen. or acc.), before (in place or time or order),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-c" target="_blank">Page0653-c+ 81</a>]<BR>in front; up to, as far as (especially in the technical<BR>language of grammatical Sūtras, e. g. प्राक् कडारात्,<BR>up to the word Kaḍāra); in the east; first, at first,<BR>formerly, previously, in the former part (of a book);<BR>at dawn, at day-break, early in the morning; प्राग्<BR>एव, recently, just; (in Buddhist writings) = किम्<BR>उत, how much more? much more, still more;<BR>प्राचा, ind., Ved. forwards, onwards; (Sāy.) = ऋजुना<BR>मार्गेण, by a straight path; प्राचस्, ind., Ved.<BR>from the front.<BR>—प्राक्-कर्मन्, अ, n. preparatory<BR>or preliminary medical treatment; an action done<BR>in a former life.<BR>—प्राक्-कल्प, अस्, m. a former<BR>age or era.<BR>—प्राक्-काल, अस्, m. a former age or<BR>time, a previous time.<BR>—प्राक्कालीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>belonging to former or ancient times, pertaining to<BR>a previous time, anterior, ancient, previous, former.<BR>—प्राक्-कूल, अस्, आ, अम्, having the points turned<BR>towards the east (said of blades of Kuśa grass; ac-<BR>cording to Kullūka on Manu II. 75 = प्राग्-अग्र);<BR>(अम्), n. the point of a blade of Kuśa grass turned<BR>towards the east; (also written प्राक्-तूल; cf.<BR>प्राचीन-कूल.)<BR>—प्राक्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, done be-<BR>fore; (अम्), n. an action done in a former life.<BR>—प्राक्-केवल, अस्, आ, अम्, manifested from the<BR>first in a distinct form (without preliminary symp-<BR>toms, as a disease).<BR>—प्राक्-चरणा, f. an epithet<BR>of the female organ of generation.<BR>—प्राक्-चिरम्,<BR>ind. before it is too late, in good time.<BR>—प्राक्-<BR>छाय, अम्, n. a shadow's falling eastward.<BR>—प्राक्-<BR>तनय, अस्, m. a former pupil (perhaps a wrong<BR>reading for प्राप्त-नय).<BR>—प्राक्-तूल = प्राक्-<BR>कूल, q. v.<BR>—प्राक्-पद, अम्, n. a preceding word,<BR>the first member of a compound.<BR>—प्राक्-पुण्य-<BR>प्रभव, अस्, आ, अम्, caused by merits accrued in<BR>a former existence, resulting from good works done<BR>in a former state of being.<BR>—प्राक्-पुष्पा, f., see<BR>Vārtt. 1. to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 64.<BR>—प्राक्-फल, अस्, m.<BR>the bread-fruit tree (= पनस).<BR>—प्राक्-फल्गुनी,<BR>f. the eleventh of the lunar mansions (= पूर्व-<BR>फल्गुनी, q. v.).<BR>—प्राक्फल्गुनी-भव, अस्, m.<BR>Bṛhaspati or the planet Jupiter (born when the<BR>moon was in the mansion Prākphalgunī).<BR>—प्राक्-<BR>फाल्गुन or प्राक्फाल्गुनेय, अस्, m. the planet<BR>Jupiter.<BR>—प्राक्-फाल्गुनी = पूर्व-फाल्गुनी, q. v.<BR>—प्राक्-शस्, ind. from the front, from the east.<BR>—प्राक्-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or प्राक्-शिरस or<BR>प्राक्शिरस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having the head turned<BR>forwards or to the east.<BR>—प्राक्-शृङ्ग-वत्, आन्, m.,<BR>N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—प्राक्-श्लिष्ट, a various reading for<BR>प्राश्लिष्ट, q. v.<BR>—प्राक्-संस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, turned<BR>or directed eastwards.<BR>—प्राक्-सन्ध्या, f. morning<BR>twilight.<BR>—प्राक्-सवन, अम्, n. a morning libation.<BR>—प्राक्-सोम, अस्, आ, अम्, or प्राक्-सौमिक, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, preceding the Soma sacrifice.<BR>—प्राक्-स्रोतस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, flowing eastward (sometimes wrongly<BR>spelt प्राक्-श्रोतस्).<BR>—प्राग्-अग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the tip or point turned forwards or towards the<BR>east (as a blade of grass).<BR>—प्राग्-अपम्, ind. (fr.<BR>प्राक् and अपम् fr. अपाक्), Ved. from the front<BR>towards the back, in a backward direction.<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>अपरायत (˚र-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, extending eastward<BR>and westward; [cf. प्राग्-आयत.]<BR>—प्राग्-अभाव,<BR>अस्, m. previous non-existence of anything, antecedent<BR>non-existence or privation, the non-existence of any-<BR>thing which may yet be; non-existence (of an<BR>effect) previous (to production); (in law) the non-<BR>possession of property that may be possessed.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>गभाव-विचार, अस्, m., N. of a Nyāya work.<BR>—प्राग्-अभिहित, अस्, आ, अम्, before-mentioned, pre-<BR>viously mentioned.<BR>—प्राग्-अवस्था, f. a former state,<BR>previous existence.<BR>—प्राग्-आयत, अस्, आ, अम्, extend-<BR>ing towards the east; [cf. प्राग्-अपरायत.]<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>आह्निक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the forenoon (=<BR>पौर्वाह्णिक).<BR>—प्राग्-उक्ति, इस्, f. previous utter-<BR>ance.<BR>—प्राग्-उत्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, north-eastern;<BR>(एण), ind. to the north-east of (with abl.), north-<BR>eastwards.<BR>—प्राग्-उदक्-प्लवन, अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>clining towards the north-east, situated in a north-<BR>easterly direction.<BR>—प्राग्-उदङ्मुख, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having the face turned to the east or north.<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>उदञ्च्, अङ्, ईची, अक्, north-eastern; (ईची), f., scil.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-a" target="_blank">Page0654-a+ 81</a>]<BR>दिश्, the north-east quarter, the north-east; (अक्),<BR>ind. to the north-east.<BR>—प्राग्-गमन-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having a forward motion, going forwards.<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going before, preceding, intending to<BR>go before; a precursor.<BR>—प्राग्-गुण, अस्, आ, अम्, pos-<BR>sessing the previously mentioned quality.<BR>—प्राग्-ग्रीव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the neck turned towards the east.<BR>—प्राग्-जन्मन्, अ, n. a former birth, former life.<BR>—प्राग्-जाति, इस्, f. a former birth (= पूर्व-जन्-<BR>मन्).<BR>—प्राग्-ज्योतिष, अम्, n., N. of a city, the<BR>dwelling-place of the demon Naraka; (अस्), m., with or<BR>without राजा, the king of Prāg-jyotiṣa, an epithet<BR>of Bhaga-datta; N. of a country, = काम-रूप;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people living in the city of Prāg-<BR>jyotiṣa or its environs; (अम्), ind. before day-break (?),<BR>—प्राग्ज्योतिष-ज्येष्ठ, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—प्राग्-दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, south-eastern;<BR>(अम्), ind. to the south-east, south-eastwards.<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>दक्षिणाञ्च् (˚ण-अञ्च्), आङ्, आची, आक्, turned to the<BR>south-east, south-eastward.<BR>—प्राग्-दण्ड, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. having the stem or stalk turned towards<BR>the east.<BR>—प्राग्-दिश्, क्, f. ‘the eastern quarter,’ the<BR>east.<BR>—प्राग्-देश, अस्, m. the eastern country,<BR>country of the eastern people; a former or previous<BR>place.<BR>—प्राग्-द्वार्, र्, f. a door on the east side.<BR>—प्राग्-द्वार, अस्, आ, अम्, having doors towards<BR>the east; an epithet of the seven lunar mansions<BR>beginning with Kṛttikā; (ए), ind. in front of or before<BR>the door.<BR>—प्राग्द्वारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, having the<BR>door on the eastern side.<BR>—प्राग्-बोधि, N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR>—प्राग्-भक्त, अम्, n. taking medicine<BR>before a meal.<BR>—प्राग्-भाग, अस्, m. the fore part.<BR>—प्राग्-भार, अस्, m. the top or peak of a moun-<BR>tain; a multitude, heap; bending, inclining, leaning<BR>[cf. प्राचीन-प्˚]; (अस्, आ, अम्), inclined, bent.<BR>—प्राग्-भाव, अस्, m. prior or previous existence;<BR>superiority, excellence; the top of a mountain (in<BR>this sense a various reading for प्राग्-भार).<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>भाव-तस्, ind. from a prior state of existence.<BR>—प्राग्-<BR>रूप, अम्, n. symptom of disease (= पूर्व-रूप).<BR>—प्राग्-वंश, अस्, आ, अम्, having the supporting<BR>beam turned eastwards (Ved.); (अस्), m. the space<BR>before the Vedi, (perhaps) a kind of sacrificial chamber<BR>having columns or beams towards the east and situ-<BR>ated opposite to the Vedi, (according to Malli-nātha<BR>on Raghu-v. XV. 61 = प्राचीन-स्थूणो यज्ञ-<BR>शाला-विशेषः; according to others, a room in which<BR>the family and friends of the person performing the<BR>sacrifice assemble); a former dynasty or generation; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu (?).<BR>—प्राग्-वचन, अम्, n. a for-<BR>mer decision; anything formerly decided or decreed.<BR>—प्राग्-वट, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of a city.<BR>—प्राग्-वत्, ind. as before, as previously, as for-<BR>merly, as in former times, as in the preceding part<BR>(of a book).<BR>—प्राग्-वृत्त, अम्, n. former behaviour;<BR>(in law) = प्राङ्-न्याय, q. v.<BR>—प्राग्-वृत्तान्त, अम्,<BR>n. a former event, previous adventure, a story of the past.<BR>—प्राग्-वेष or प्राग्-वेश, अस्, m. a former dress.<BR>—प्राग्-हार, a various reading for प्राग्-भार,<BR>q. v.<BR>—प्राङ्-आयत, an incorrect form for प्राग्-<BR>आयत, q. v.<BR>—प्राङ्-नासिका or प्राङ्-नासिकी, f., see<BR>Scholiast on Pāṇ. IV. 1, 60.<BR>—प्राङ्-न्याय, अस्, m.<BR>(in law) a former trial of a cause, the plea of a<BR>former trial, special plea; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. turned<BR>forwards or eastwards according to rule.<BR>—प्राङ्न्या-<BR>योत्तर (˚य-उत्˚), अम्, n. the rejoinder of the<BR>defendant that the charge against him has already<BR>been tried.<BR>—प्राङ्-मुख, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, having<BR>the face turned forward or towards the east, facing<BR>the east (Manu II. 51); inclined towards, desirous<BR>of, wishing.<BR>—प्राचा-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. moving<BR>the tongue forwards (said of Agni; Sāy. = प्राग्-<BR>देश-स्थित-जिह्वा-स्थानीय-ज्वाल).<BR>—प्राचा-मन्-<BR>यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. striving to move forwards (said<BR>of Indra; Sāy. = अप्रतिहत-क्रोध).<BR>—प्राची-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the east,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—प्राची-मूल, अम्, n. the eastern horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तन|प्राक्तनः
प्राक्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, former, prior, previous,<BR>anterior, antecedent, preceding; early, old, ancient,<BR>(opposed to इदानीन्तन); relating to a former state<BR>of existence, resulting from acts done in a former<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">Page0654-b+ 81</a>]<BR>life.<BR>—प्राक्तन-कर्मन्, अ, n. any act formerly<BR>done or done in a former state of existence; fate,<BR>destiny.<BR>—प्राक्तन-जन्मन्, अ, n. a former birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तस्
प्राक्तस् or प्राक्तात्, ind., Ved. from the front,<BR>from the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागिवीय
प्रागिवीय (fr. प्राग् इव), see Pāṇ. V. 3, 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्घितीय
प्राग्घितीय (fr. प्राग्घितात्), see Pāṇ. IV. 4, 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्दिशीय
प्राग्दिशीय (fr. प्राग् दिशः), see Scholiast on<BR>Pāṇ. V. 3, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्दीव्यतीय
प्राग्दीव्यतीय (fr. प्राग् दीव्यतः), see Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्धितीय
प्राग्धितीय, a wrong reading for प्राग्घितीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचा
प्राचा, ind. See p. 653, col. 3, and p. 654, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचिका
प्राचिका, f. a musquito; a female falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीन|प्राचीनः
प्राचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, turned towards the front or<BR>towards the east, belonging to the front or east,<BR>eastern, easterly; former, prior, preceding, ancient,<BR>old; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a hedge, fence, wall; (आ), f.<BR>a species of plant, Clypea Hernandifolia; (अम्), ind.<BR>in front, forwards; eastwards, to the east of (with<BR>abl.); before (with abl.); अतः प्राचीनम्, further<BR>on from that point.<BR>—प्राचीन-आवीतिन् = प्राचीना-<BR>वीतिन्, q. v.<BR>—प्राचीन-कल्प, अस्, m. a former Kalpa<BR>or period of the world's duration.<BR>—प्राचीन-कूल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, = प्राक्-कूल, q. v.<BR>—प्राचीन-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an ancient Ṛṣi also called Apāntara-tamas.<BR>—प्राचीन-गाथा, f. an ancient story or tradition.<BR>—प्राचीन-गौड, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the Saṃvatsara-pradīpa.<BR>—प्राचीन-ग्रीव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. having the neck turned forwards or towards the<BR>east.<BR>—प्राचीन-ता, f. or प्राचीन-त्व, अम्, n. anti-<BR>quity, oldness.<BR>—प्राचीन-तिलक, अस्, m. ‘having a<BR>mark towards the east (?),’ the moon.<BR>—प्राचीन-<BR>पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the feathers turned<BR>forwards (as an arrow).<BR>—प्राचीन-पनस, अस्, m.<BR>‘the eastern Jaka tree,’ the plant Ægle Marmelos.<BR>—प्राचीन-प्रक्रिया, f., N. of a grammatical work<BR>(= प्रक्रिया-कौमुदी).<BR>—प्राचीन-प्राग्भार,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, bending or inclining towards the east.<BR>—प्राचीन-बर्हिस्, इस्, m. ‘eastern light (?),’ N. of<BR>a Prajā-pati of the race of Atri; of a son of Havir-<BR>dhāman (or Havir-dhāna) and father of the ten<BR>Pracetasas; of a son of Manu; an epithet of Indra.<BR>—प्राचीन-मत, अम्, n. an ancient opinion, a<BR>belief sanctioned by antiquity.<BR>—प्राचीन-योग, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man; of an ancient teacher, the father of<BR>Patañjali.<BR>—प्राचीनयोगी-पुत्र, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR>—प्राचीनयोग्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Prācīna-yoga; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a school.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>चीन-रश्मि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having the reins directed<BR>forwards (Sāy. = देवाभिमुख).<BR>—प्राचीन-वंश,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the supporting beam turned<BR>forwards or towards the east; [cf. प्राग्-वंश.]<BR>—प्राचीन-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a commentary on<BR>the Uṇādi-sūtras.<BR>—प्राचीन-शाल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—प्राचीन-शिव-स्तुति, इस्, f. an ancient hymn<BR>in praise of Śiva.<BR>—प्राचीनाग्र (˚न-अग्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the points turned towards the east (said<BR>of sacred grass).<BR>—प्राचीनामलक (˚न-आम्˚), अस्,<BR>m. the plant Flacourtia Cataphracta; (अम्), n. the<BR>fruit of the Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR>—प्राचीनावीत<BR>(˚न-आव्˚), अम्, n. the sacrificial cord worn over the<BR>right shoulder and passed under the left arm (as at a<BR>Śrāddha).<BR>—प्राचीनावीतिन् (˚न-आव्˚), ई, इनी, इ, or<BR>प्राचीनोपवीत (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wearing the<BR>sacrificial cord over the right shoulder and under the<BR>left arm (Manu II. 63).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचैस्
प्राचैस्, ind., Ved. forwards; [cf. उच्चैस्, नीचैस्,<BR>पराचैस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्य|प्राच्यः
प्राच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in front, situated in<BR>front; being in the east, living in the east, belonging<BR>to the east, eastern, easterly; preceding, prior, ante-<BR>rior, previous; ancient, old, (opposed to आधुनिक);<BR>an epithet of particular songs belonging to the Sāma-<BR>veda; (आस्), m. pl. the inhabitants of the east, the<BR>eastern country, the country south or east of the<BR>river Sarasvatī (which flows from the north-east<BR>towards the south-west); (आ), f., scil. भाषा, the<BR>dialect spoken in the east of India.<BR>—प्राच्य-पद-<BR>वृत्ति, इस्, f. (in Ved. gram.) a term applied to the<BR>rule according to which ए remains in particular cases<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">Page0654-c+ 77</a>]<BR>unchanged before अ.<BR>—प्राच्य-भाषा, f. the dialect<BR>of the east of India.<BR>—प्राच्य-वृत्ति, इस्, f. a kind<BR>of metre.<BR>—प्राच्य-सप्तसम, see Scholiast on<BR>Pāṇ. VI. 2, 12.<BR>—प्राच्याध्वर्यु, see Scholiast<BR>on Pāṇ. VI. 2, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्यक
प्राच्यक, अस्, आ, अम्, situated in the east, eastern,<BR>easterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्यायन
प्राच्यायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Prācya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्ज्
प्राञ्ज् प्राञ्ज् (प्र-अञ्ज्), cl. 7. P. प्राणक्ति,<BR>प्राञ्जितुम्, प्राङ्क्तुम्, Ved. (?), to adorn, deco-<BR>rate, embellish, beautify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जन
प्राञ्जन, अम्, n., Ved. paint or cement (on an<BR>arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जल|प्रांजल|प्राञ्जलः
प्राञ्जल प्राञ्जल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्र + अञ्-<BR>जलि?), straight; honest, upright, sincere.<BR>—प्राञ्जल-<BR>ता, f. straightness; honesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलि|प्रांजलि
प्राञ्जलि प्राञ्जलि (प्र-अञ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, hold-<BR>ing out the open hands slightly hollowed and placed<BR>side by side (as if to hold an offering; a common<BR>mark of respect and salutation, cf. अञ्जलि, कृताञ्-<BR>जलि); joining the palms of the hands in a suppli-<BR>cating manner (Manu II. 192).<BR>—प्राञ्जलि-द्वैत-<BR>भृत्, तस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलिक|प्रांजलिक
प्राञ्जलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, = प्राञ्जलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलिन्|प्रांजलिन्
प्राञ्जलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = प्राञ्जलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राडाहति
प्राडाहति प्राडाहति, इस्, m. a patronymic;<BR>see Gaṇa Taulvalyādi to Pāṇ. II. 4, 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राड्विवाक|प्राड्विवाकः
प्राड्विवाक प्राड्-विवाक. See प्राछ्, p. 653.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण्
प्राण् 1. प्राण् or प्रान् (प्र-अण् or प्र-अन्),<BR>cl. 2. P. प्राणिति (according to Vopa-deva IX. 27,<BR>also प्रानिति), &c., to breathe in; inhale, inspire; to<BR>blow (as the wind, Ved.); to live; to smell (intrans.):<BR>Caus. P. A. प्राणयति, -ते, Aor. प्राणिणत्, to cause to<BR>breathe, give life to, animate: Desid. प्राणिणिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण्
2. प्राण् (प्र-अण्), ण्, ण्, ण्, breathing (?); see<BR>Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण|प्राणः
2. प्राण, अस्, m. (for 1. see under rt. 1. प्रा, p. 652),<BR>breathing, breath, respiration, inspiration and expira-<BR>tion, breath of life, spirit, vital action or life generally,<BR>vitality; a vital organ, organ of sense, vital air, (the<BR>vital airs are variously enumerated as three, viz.<BR>प्राण, अपान, and व्य्-आन; or five, viz. प्राण,<BR>अपान, सम्-आन, व्य्-आन, उद्-आन; or with the<BR>other vital organs six or seven, or nine or ten, or<BR>thirteen; the fivefold enumeration being however<BR>the most usual; and the first of the five or प्राण<BR>being used from its seat in the lungs to express<BR>pre-eminently life and vitality); air inhaled, wind;<BR>circulation of nutriment, digestion; the place of<BR>breathing, the mouth and nose (?); any one as dear<BR>as the breath of life, any beloved object (e. g. त्वम्<BR>मे प्राणः, thou art as dear to me as the breath of<BR>life; cf. पति-प्राण); the spirit (as opposed to the<BR>body); the spirit or life of a poem, poetical talent,<BR>inspiration; the soul (= पुरुष); vigorous action,<BR>energy, strength, power, might [cf. यथा-प्राणाम्];<BR>breathing, aspiration (in the pronunciation of letters);<BR>a breath as a measure of time, viz. the time required for<BR>the pronunciation of ten long syllables = (1/6) Vināḍikā;<BR>N. of a Kalpa, the sixth day in the light half of a<BR>month of Brahmā; myrrh; a mystical expression for<BR>the letter य्; an epithet of Brahma the Supreme<BR>Spirit; N. of a son of the Vasu, Dhara; of one of<BR>the eight Vasus; of a Marut; of one of the seven<BR>sages in the second Manv-antara; of a son of Dhātṛ;<BR>of a son of Vi-dhātṛ the brother of Dhātṛ; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. the five vital airs or modes of inspiration and<BR>expiration collectively (see above); life, vitality, the vital<BR>organs or organs of sense, (according to Kullūka, Manu<BR>IV. 143, प्राणाः = चक्षुर्-आदीनीन्द्रियाणि); (प्रा-<BR>णान् मुच्, to resign or lay down one's life; प्राणान्<BR>हा or परि-त्यज्, to quit life; प्राणान् रक्ष्, to<BR>save life; प्राणान् नि-हन्, to destroy life); प्रा-<BR>णैस्, ind. with all the soul, with all the strength,<BR>with might and main; [cf. Gr. φρήν, ὀσ-φραίνομαι;<BR>Cambro-Brit. fion, ‘the breath or respiration, a<BR>puff of breath, a sigh.’]<BR>—प्राण-कर, अस्, ई,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-a" target="_blank">Page0655-a+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, ‘life-making,’ refreshing the spirits; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of the father of the author of the Medinī.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>ण-कर्मन्, अ, n. a vital function.<BR>—प्राण-कृच्-<BR>छ्र, अम्, n. danger to life, peril of life.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>कृष्ण, अस्, m., N. of an author of various works.<BR>—प्राण-ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a particular Soma vessel.<BR>—प्राण-घातक, अस्, ई, अम्, life-destroying, de-<BR>structive to life, killing.<BR>—प्राण-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>life-destroying, deadly, mortal.<BR>—प्राण-च्छिद्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, cutting off life, shortening life, murderous.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>ण-च्छेद, अस्, m. the cutting off of life, murder.<BR>—प्राण-तोषणी, f., N. of a compendium of Tantra<BR>works.<BR>—प्राण-त्याग, अस्, m. abandonment of<BR>life, expiring, death, suicide.<BR>—प्राण-द, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>life-giving, saving life; (अस्), m. a species of plant,<BR>= जीवक; (आ), f. the plant Terminalia Chebula (=<BR>हरीतकी); a species of medicinal plant, = ऋद्धि;<BR>(अम्), n. water; blood.<BR>—प्राण-दक्षिणा, f. the<BR>gift of life; प्राणदक्षिणां दा, to grant any one<BR>his life.<BR>—प्राण-दण्ड, अस्, m. the punishment of<BR>death.<BR>—प्राण-दयित, अस्, आ, अम्, dear as life;<BR>(अस्), m. a husband.<BR>—प्राण-दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a<BR>life-giver, one who saves another's life.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>दान, अम्, n. the gift of life, saving any one's life;<BR>resigning or laying down life; anointing the Havis<BR>with Ghṛta during the recitation of sacred texts<BR>supposed to restore life (Ved.).<BR>—प्राण-दावत्,<BR>आन्, m., Ved. life-giving, conferring life.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>दुरोदर, अम्, n. playing or gambling for life,<BR>staking life.<BR>—प्राण-द्यूत, अम्, n. staking life or<BR>existence, a battle for life, fighting for life.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>द्यूताभिदेवन (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, played or<BR>fought with life as a stake (said of a battle in which<BR>life is as it were gambled with or staked, see Mahā-<BR>bh. Śalya-p. 760).<BR>—प्राण-द्रोह, अस्, m. an attack<BR>or attempt upon (any one's) life.<BR>—प्राण-धर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—प्राण-धार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing life, living, animate; (अस्), m. a living<BR>being.<BR>—प्राण-धारण, अम्, n. the support or<BR>maintenance of life, prolongation of life, suste-<BR>nance; a means of supporting life; retaining life,<BR>vitality.<BR>—प्राण-धृक्, क्, क्, Ved. sustaining the<BR>breath, prolonging the act of inhaling the breath;<BR>[cf. धृक्, p. 459, col. 1.]<BR>—प्राण-नाथ, अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of life,’ a husband, lover; an epithet of Yama;<BR>N. of a heresiarch who held a controversy with<BR>Śaṅkara at Pra-yāga.<BR>—प्राण-नाश, अस्, m. de-<BR>struction or cessation of breath.<BR>—प्राण-निग्रह,<BR>अस्, m. checking or obstructing the breath.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>पत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्राण-पति), see Gaṇa to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 84.<BR>—प्राण-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of life,’ the<BR>soul; a husband; the heart (?).<BR>—प्राण-पत्नी, f.<BR>‘wife of the vital breath,’ the voice.<BR>—प्राण-परि-<BR>क्रय, अस्, m. the price of life, staking one's life or<BR>existence.<BR>—प्राण-परिक्षीण, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose life is drawing to a close.<BR>—प्राण-परि-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m. possession of breath or life, life,<BR>existence.<BR>—प्राण-परित्याग, अस्, m. abandoning<BR>or resigning life.<BR>—प्राण-परीप्सा, f. desire of sav-<BR>ing life, wish to escape.<BR>—प्राण-पा, आस्, आस्, अम्,<BR>Ved. life-protecting, preserving life.<BR>—प्राण-प्रद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, life-bestowing, restoring life, saving life;<BR>(आ), f. a species of medicinal plant (= ऋद्धि).<BR>—प्राण-प्रदायक, अस्, इका, अम्, or प्राण-<BR>प्रदायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, life-bestowing, restoring life,<BR>saving life.<BR>—प्राण-प्रयाण, अम्, n. departure of<BR>the breath of life, end of life.<BR>—प्राण-प्रिय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, dear as life; (अस्), m. a lover.<BR>—प्राण-बाध, अस्,<BR>m. danger to life, fear for life, extreme peril.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>ण-बुद्धि, इस्, f. sing. (?), life and intelligence.<BR>—प्राण-भक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘breath-eating,’<BR>‘air-eating,’ inhaling merely the odour of food or<BR>drink.<BR>—प्राण-भय, अम्, n. fear for one's life,<BR>danger to life.<BR>—प्राण-भास्वत्, वान्, m. the<BR>ocean (‘the light of life?’).<BR>—प्राण-भूत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being the breath of life.<BR>—प्राण-भृत्, त्, त्,<BR>त्, supporting life (Ved.); containing life, possessed<BR>of life, living, sentient; (त्), m. a living being, a<BR>man; an epithet of particular bricks used in the<BR>erection of an altar.<BR>—प्राण-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>consisting of breath, endowed with breath or life,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-b" target="_blank">Page0655-b+ 81</a>]<BR>living, breathing.<BR>—प्राणमय-कोष, अस्, m. one<BR>of the cases or investitures of the soul, the vital case.<BR>—प्राण-मोक्षण, अम्, n. giving up the ghost,<BR>resigning life, suicide.<BR>—प्राण-यम, अस्, m. sus-<BR>pending the breath (= प्राणायाम).<BR>—प्राण-यात्रा,<BR>f. support of life, subsistence.<BR>—प्राणयात्रिक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, necessary for the support of life.<BR>—प्राणयात्रिक-<BR>मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, possessing only the necessaries<BR>of life.<BR>—प्राण-योनि, इस्, f. the source or spring of<BR>life.<BR>—प्राण-रक्षणार्थम् (˚ण-अर्˚), ind. for<BR>the preservation of life.<BR>—प्राण-रक्षा, f. protec-<BR>tion or preservation of life.<BR>—प्राण-रन्ध्र, अम्,<BR>n. ‘breath-aperture,’ the mouth; nostril.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>रोध, अस्, m. checking or suppressing the breath;<BR>danger to life; N. of a particular hell.<BR>—प्राण-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, having breath or life, breathing, living,<BR>animated; possessing power, strong, powerful.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>ण-विद्या, f. the science of the breath or vital airs.<BR>—प्राण-विनाश, अस्, m. destruction or loss of life.<BR>—प्राण-विप्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, depriving of life.<BR>—प्राण-वियोग, अस्, m. ‘the separation of breath<BR>or life,’ the departure of the spirit at the hour of<BR>dissolution, death.<BR>—प्राण-वृत्ति, इस्, f. living, acti-<BR>vity, vital function.<BR>—प्राण-व्यय, अस्, m. ‘expen-<BR>diture of life,’ giving up the ghost, death.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>शक्ति, इस्, f. a particular Śakti of Viṣṇu.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>शरीर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. whose (only) body is the<BR>breath of life or spirit.<BR>—प्राण-संयम, अस्, m.<BR>checking or suspending the breath (as a religious<BR>exercise).<BR>—प्राण-संरोध, अस्, m. checking or<BR>obstructing the breath.<BR>—प्राण-संवाद, अस्, m.<BR>a controversy between the vital airs, dispute between<BR>the organs of sense (an imaginary contest or con-<BR>troversy between the senses supposed to be disputing<BR>for precedence).<BR>—प्राण-संशय, अस्, m. danger<BR>to life.<BR>—प्राण-संहिता, f. a manner of reciting<BR>the Vedic texts, pronouncing as many letters as<BR>possible during one breath.<BR>—प्राण-सङ्कट, अम्,<BR>n. danger to life, great peril.<BR>—प्राण-सद्मन्, अ,<BR>n. the abode of the vital airs, the body.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>सन्त्याग, अस्, m. abandoning or resigning life.<BR>—प्राण-सन्देह, अस्, m. danger to life, risk of<BR>life, great peril.<BR>—प्राण-सन्न्यास, अस्, m. giving<BR>up the ghost, dying.<BR>—प्राण-सम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>equal to or as dear as life; (अस्), m. a lover, a<BR>husband; (आ), f. a wife.<BR>—प्राण-सम्भृत, अस्, m.<BR>wind, air; (perhaps a wrong form for प्राण-सम्-<BR>भूत.)<BR>—प्राण-सम्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. reaching<BR>to the nose; dear as life.<BR>—प्राण-सार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>whose whole essence consists of life, spirited, full of<BR>strength, vigorous.<BR>—प्राण-सूत्र, अम्, n. the thread<BR>of life.<BR>—प्राण-हर, अस्, ई, अम्, taking away life,<BR>threatening life, causing death, destructive.<BR>—प्राण-<BR>हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, taking away life, causing<BR>death; (अम्), n. a kind of poison (= वत्स-नाभ).<BR>—प्राण-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking away life, causing<BR>death, mortal, deadly.<BR>—प्राणाकर्षिन् (˚ण-आक्˚),<BR>ई, इणी, इ, attracting the vital spirit.<BR>—प्राणाग्निहोत्र<BR>(˚ण-अग्˚), अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—प्राणाघात (˚ण-आघ्˚), अस्, m. destruction of<BR>life, killing a living being.<BR>—प्राणाचार्य (˚ण-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a physician to a king.<BR>—प्राणातिपात (˚ण-<BR>अत्˚), अस्, m. an attack upon life, taking away life, kill-<BR>ing a living being.<BR>—प्राणात्मन् (˚ण-आत्˚), आ, m. the<BR>vital or animal soul, the lowest of the three souls of<BR>a human being (the other two are called जीवात्मन्<BR>and परमात्मन्, q. q. v. v.).<BR>—प्राणात्यय (˚ण-<BR>अत्˚), अस्, m. the passing away of life; (ए), ind. at a<BR>time when life is in danger of ceasing.<BR>—प्राणाद<BR>(˚ण-आद), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘eating away life,’ causing<BR>death, fatal.<BR>—प्राणाधिक (˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘more than life,’ dearer than life; superior in vigour.<BR>—प्राणाधिनाथ (˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of life,’<BR>a husband.<BR>—प्राणाधिप (˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘ruler<BR>of the breath of life,’ the soul.<BR>—प्राणान्त (˚ण-<BR>अन्˚), अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), the end of life, death;<BR>प्राणान्तं दण्डम् अर्हति, he deserves death as<BR>a punishment, i. e. he deserves the punishment of<BR>death.<BR>—प्राणान्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, destructive to life,<BR>fatal, mortal, capital (as punishment); dangerous; last-<BR>ing to the end of life, ending with life; (अम्), n. murder,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">Page0655-c+ 78</a>]<BR>assassination; (अम्), ind. until death.<BR>—प्राणाप-<BR>हारिन् (˚ण-अप्˚), ई, इणी, इ, taking away life, fatal,<BR>deadly.<BR>—प्राणापान (˚ण-अप्˚), औ, m. du. two of<BR>the vital airs, air inhaled and exhaled; Inspiration<BR>and Expiration personified and identified with the<BR>Aśvins.<BR>—प्राणाबाध (˚ण-आब्˚), अस्, m. injury or<BR>danger to life, any act injurious to life.<BR>—१. प्राणायन<BR>(˚ण-अय्˚), अम्, n. an organ of sense.<BR>—प्राणायाम<BR>(˚ण-आय्˚), अस्, m. restraining or suspending the<BR>breath or breathing in a peculiar way through the<BR>nostrils during the mental recitation of the names<BR>or attributes of some deity, (it is differently performed,<BR>cf. पूरक, कुम्भक, रेचक.)<BR>—प्राणायामिन्<BR>(˚ण-आय्˚), ई, इनी, इ, checking or suppressing the<BR>breath.<BR>—प्राणार्थ-वत् (˚ण-अर्˚), आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessed of life and riches.<BR>—प्राणेश (˚ण-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of life,’ a lover, husband; ‘lord of<BR>breath,’ N. of a Marut; (आ), f. a wife.<BR>—प्राणेश्-<BR>वर (˚ण-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of (my) life,’ a hus-<BR>band, lover; a particular formula; (ई), f. a wife.<BR>—प्राणोत्क्रमण (˚ण-उत्˚), अम्, n. the departure<BR>of the spirit, flight of the soul, death.<BR>—प्राणोत्-<BR>सर्ग (˚ण-उत्˚), अस्, m. giving up the ghost, dying.<BR>—प्राणोपहार (˚ण-उप्˚), अस्, m. food (regarded<BR>as an oblation to life).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0654-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणक|प्राणकः
प्राणक, अस्, m. a living being, an animal or<BR>sentient being; a species of plant (= जीवक); myrrh;<BR>cloth, clothes (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणत्|प्राणन्त्
प्राणत्, अन्, अती, अत्, breathing, living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणथ|प्राणथः
प्राणथ, अस्, m. breathing; air, wind; the lord<BR>of all created beings (= प्रजा-पति); a sacred<BR>bathing-place; (अस्, आ, अम्), strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन|प्राणनं|प्राणनः
प्राणन, अस्, m. the throat; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>breathing, respiration; living, life; producing life,<BR>calling into life; (अस्, आ, अम्), giving life to, pro-<BR>ducing life.<BR>—प्राणनान्त (˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>end of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन्त|प्राणंत|प्राणंतः|प्राणन्तः
प्राणन्त, अस्, m. air, wind; a kind of collyrium,<BR>= रसाञ्जन; (ई), f. sneezing; sobbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणयत्
प्राणयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, restoring to life, resusci-<BR>tating, reanimating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणायन
2. प्राणायन, अस्, m., Ved. the offspring of the<BR>vital airs (in Vājasaneyi-Saṃhitā XIII. 54; according<BR>to Mahī-dhara प्राणायन = प्राणस्यापत्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिणिषु
प्राणिणिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (see Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 21),<BR>wishing to breathe or live, wishing for life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणित
प्राणित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to breathe, kept alive,<BR>animated, longing to do (anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिन्
प्राणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, breathing, living, alive; (ई), m.<BR>a living or sentient being, living creature, animal;<BR>a man.<BR>—प्राणि-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, killing living<BR>beings.<BR>—प्राणि-जात, अम्, n. a class or species of<BR>animals.<BR>—प्राणि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of a living<BR>being, sentient existence, life.<BR>—प्राणि-द्यूत, अम्,<BR>n. gambling with fighting animals, setting animals<BR>to fight for wagers, a fight of animals exhibited for<BR>sport, cock-fighting, ram-fighting, &c.<BR>—प्राणि-पीडा,<BR>f. giving pain to sentient beings, cruelty to animals.<BR>—प्राणि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of or peopled<BR>with living beings.<BR>—प्राणि-मातृ, ता, f. the mother<BR>of a living being; a kind of shrub (= गर्भ-दात्री).<BR>—प्राणि-योधन, अम्, n. setting animals to fight<BR>(= प्राणि-द्यूत above).<BR>—प्राणि-हिंसा, f. doing<BR>harm to any living creature, injuring or killing an<BR>animal.<BR>—प्राणि-हित, अस्, आ, अम्, favourable or good<BR>for living beings; (आ), f. a shoe, a boot, (in this<BR>sense probably for प्राणहिता, q. v.)<BR>—प्राण्य्-अङ्ग,<BR>अम्, n. a part or limb of an animal or man, any<BR>animal product (as flesh, bone, milk, ghee, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणतज
प्राणतज प्राणतज, आस्, m. pl. (with Jainas)<BR>N. of a subdivision of the Kalpa-bhavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहिता
प्राणहिता प्राणहिता, f. a shoe, a boot;<BR>[cf. प्राणि-हिता; both are probably corruptions.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाय्य
प्राणाय्य प्राणाय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, proper, fit,<BR>suited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणावाय
प्राणावाय प्राणावाय, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>twelfth of the fourteen Pūrvas or ancient writings<BR>of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0655-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाह
प्राणाह प्राणाह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. नह् with<BR>प्रा), Ved. cement (used in building).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणीत्य|प्राणीत्यं
प्राणीत्य प्राणीत्य, अम्, n. (probably incor-<BR>rect for प्रामीत्य), debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात|प्रातं|प्रातः
प्रात प्रात. See under rt. 1. प्रा, p. 652.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्
प्रातर् प्रातर्, ind. (fr. 1. प्र), early in the<BR>morning, at day-break, at dawn [cf. अभि-प्˚]; on<BR>the next morning, to-morrow morning, early on the<BR>morrow, to-morrow; Morning personified as a son<BR>of Puṣpārṇa and Prabhā; प्रातः प्रातः, every<BR>morning; [cf. Gr. πρωΐ; Old Germ. fro, fruo;<BR>Mod. Germ. frühe.]<BR>—प्रातः-कर्मन्, अ, or<BR>प्रातः-कार्य, अम्, n. morning business, a morning<BR>ceremony; [cf. प्रातः-कृत्य below.]<BR>—प्रातः-<BR>काल, अस्, m. morning-time, the early time of day,<BR>early morning, first break of day.<BR>—प्रातः-कृत्य,<BR>अम्, n. matutinal duty, morning ceremonies, a reli-<BR>gious duty performed in the morning (as worship,<BR>ablution, purification, &c.).<BR>—प्रातः-प्रहर, अस्,<BR>m. the morning watch, the first part of the day<BR>(from six to nine o'clock); प्रातः-प्रहरे गते,<BR>the morning watch being past, at nine o'clock in<BR>the morning.<BR>—प्रातः-सन्ध्या, f. morning twi-<BR>light, dawn, the morning devotions of a Brāhman;<BR>morning sacrifice.<BR>—प्रातः-समय, अस्, m. the<BR>morning-time, early morning, day-break.<BR>—प्रातः-<BR>सव, अस्, m. or प्रातः-सवन, अम्, n. the morning<BR>libation of Soma (accompanied with ten ceremonial<BR>observances, viz. the प्रातर्-अनुवाक, अभि-षव,<BR>बहिष्-पवमान-स्तोत्र, सवनीयाः पशवः,<BR>धिष्ण्य्-उपस्थान, सवनीयाः पुरोडाशाः, द्वि-<BR>देवत्य-ग्रहाः, द्वि-देवत्य-भक्ष, ऋतु-या-<BR>जाः, आज्य or प्रüग शस्त्र).<BR>—प्रातःसवनिक<BR>or प्रातःसवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. belonging or<BR>relating to the morning libation of Soma.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>तः-साव, अस्, m., Ved. the morning preparation of<BR>Soma, morning libation.<BR>—प्रातः-स्नान, अम्, n.<BR>bathing at sun-rise, morning ablution.<BR>—प्रातः-<BR>स्नायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bathing early in the morning.<BR>—प्रातर्-अनुवाक, अस्, m., Ved. ‘morning recita-<BR>tion,’ the hymn recited at the commencement of<BR>the Prātaḥ-savana.<BR>—प्रातर्-अभिवाद, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>morning salutation.<BR>—प्रातर्-अह्न, अस्, m. the<BR>early part of the day, forenoon; N. of a man.<BR>—प्रातर्-आश, अस्, m. the morning meal, breakfast,<BR>(अ-प्रातराश, not breakfasting.)<BR>—प्रातराशित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has had the morning meal, one<BR>who has breakfasted.<BR>—प्रातर्-आहुति, इस्, f., Ved.<BR>the morning oblation, the second half of the daily<BR>Agni-hotra sacrifice.<BR>—प्रातर्-इत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved.<BR>going out early in the morning; coming at day-break,<BR>an early guest (Sāy. = प्रातर् आगतः).<BR>—प्रातर्-<BR>गेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sung or chanted in the<BR>morning; (अस्), m. a minstrel employed to wake<BR>the king in the morning.<BR>—प्रातर्-जित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>victorious at day-break; conquering the morning.<BR>—प्रातर्-दिन, अम्, n. the early part of the day,<BR>forenoon.<BR>—प्रातर्-दुग्ध, अम्, n., Ved. morning<BR>milk.<BR>—प्रातर्-दोह, अस्, m. milking in the morn-<BR>ing, morning milk.<BR>—प्रातर्-भोक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ,<BR>one who makes an early meal; (ता), m. a crow.<BR>—प्रातर्-भोजन, अम्, n. the morning meal,<BR>breakfast.<BR>—प्रातर्-यावन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. going<BR>out early in the morning, an early guest [cf. प्रातर्-<BR>इत्वन्]; (आणा), m. du. an epithet of the Aśvins<BR>(Sāy. = प्रातर् एव यज्ञ-गन्तारौ).<BR>—प्रातर्-<BR>युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. yoked or harnessed early in<BR>the morning.<BR>—प्रातर्-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. yoking or<BR>harnessing early in the morning; yoked or harnessed<BR>early in the morning (said of a chariot, Sāy. =<BR>प्रातः-काले ऽश्वैर् युज्यमानः); (जा), m. du. an<BR>epithet of the Aśvins (Sāy. = प्रातः-सवन-ग्र-<BR>हेण संयुक्तौ).<BR>—प्रातर्-वस्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ,<BR>Ved. shining in the morning; [cf. दोषा-वस्तृ.]<BR>—प्रातर्-होम, अस्, m. the morning sacrifice.<BR>—प्रातस्-तराम्, ind. very early in the morn-<BR>ing.<BR>—प्रातस्-त्रिवर्गा, f. an epithet of the river<BR>Gaṅgā (Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 1846).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातस्तन
प्रातस्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">Page0656-b+ 70</a>]<BR>morning, matutinal; (अम्), n., Ved. early morning (the<BR>first of five parts of the day, the other four being सङ्-<BR>गव or morning, midday, afternoon, and evening).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातस्त्य
प्रातस्त्य, अस्, &c., belonging or relating to the<BR>morning, matutinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर
प्रातर प्रातर, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga; (in<BR>Gaṇa Kṛśāsvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80, a various reading<BR>for प्रतर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्दन
प्रातर्दन प्रातर्दन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging<BR>to or derived from Pra-tardana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राति|प्रातिः
प्राति प्राति. See under rt. 1. प्रा, p. 652.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकण्ठिक
प्रातिकण्ठिक प्रातिकण्ठिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>प्रति-कण्ठम्), seizing by the throat (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिका
प्रातिका प्रातिका, f. the China rose, Hibis-<BR>cus Rosa Sinensis (= जवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकामिन्
प्रातिकामिन् प्रातिकामिन्, ई, m. (fr. प्रति-<BR>कामम्), a servant, a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूलिक
प्रातिकूलिक प्रातिकूलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-<BR>कूल), opposed to, opposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूल्य|प्रातिकूल्यं
प्रातिकूल्य, अम्, n. contrariety, adverseness, con-<BR>tradiction, hinderance, opposition, resistance, hostility,<BR>unfriendliness, unpleasantness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिजनीन
प्रातिजनीन प्रातिजनीन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-<BR>जन), suitable against an adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिज्ञ|प्रातिज्ञं
प्रातिज्ञ प्रातिज्ञ, अम्, n. (fr. प्रति-ज्ञा), the<BR>subject under discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिथेयी
प्रातिथेयी प्रातिथेयी, f. (fr. प्र-तिथि), N. of<BR>a female sage; (also read प्रातीथेयी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिदैवसिक
प्रातिदैवसिक प्रातिदैवसिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>प्रति-दिवसम्), happening or occurring daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिनिधिक|प्रातिनिधिकः
प्रातिनिधिक प्रातिनिधिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्रति-<BR>निधि), Ved. a substitute, proxy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपक्ष
प्रातिपक्ष प्रातिपक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-<BR>पक्ष), belonging to an enemy, hostile; adverse,<BR>contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपक्ष्य|प्रातिपक्ष्यं
प्रातिपक्ष्य, अम्, n. hostility, enmity; अस्मा-<BR>कम् प्रातिपक्ष्यम्, enmity against us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपथिक|प्रातिपथिकः
प्रातिपथिक प्रातिपथिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>तिपथिक), going along a road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपद
प्रातिपद प्रातिपद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. प्रति-<BR>पद्), forming the beginning or commencement;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपदिक|प्रातिपदिकः
प्रातिपदिक, अम्, n. the crude form or base of a<BR>noun, a crude word or noun as formed by either Kṛt or<BR>Taddhita affix before receiving a case-termination, a<BR>noun in its uninflected state, (when the case-termina-<BR>tion is added, the प्रातिपदिक becomes a पद or<BR>real word); (अस्), m. an epithet of fire; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>in express terms, express, explicit; [cf. प्रति-प-<BR>दम्.]<BR>—प्रातिपदिकानुरोध (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>conformity with the words or express terms of any<BR>statement; (आत्), ind. in conformity with express<BR>terms, expressly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपीय
प्रातिपीय प्रातिपीय or प्रातिपेय, अस्, m. a<BR>patronymic of Balhika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपौरुषिक
प्रातिपौरुषिक प्रातिपौरुषिक, अस्, ई, अम्<BR>(fr. प्रति + पौरुष), relating or belonging to<BR>manliness or valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिबोध
प्रातिबोध प्रातिबोध, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Prati-bodha; see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिबोधायन
प्रातिबोधायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Prati-<BR>bodha; see Gaṇa to Pāṇ. IV. 1. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभ
प्रातिभ प्रातिभ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-भा),<BR>belonging or relating to divination; (अम्), n., scil.<BR>ज्ञान, divination; quick apprehension or conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभाव्य|प्रातिभाव्यं
प्रातिभाव्य प्रातिभाव्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्रति-<BR>भू), the act of becoming bail or surety, suretiship,<BR>being answerable for the appearance of the debtor<BR>or for his being trustworthy or for the payment of<BR>his debt in case of his failing to do it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभासिक
प्रातिभासिक प्रातिभासिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>प्रति-भास), having only the appearance of, exist-<BR>ing only in appearance; bearing a resemblance, re-<BR>sembling, looking like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिरूप्य
प्रातिरूप्य प्रातिरूप्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्रति-<BR>रूप), similarity of form, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोमिक
प्रातिलोमिक प्रातिलोमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>प्रति-लोम), against the hair or the grain, contrary<BR>to natural course or order, hostile, disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोम्य|प्रातिलोम्यं
प्रातिलोम्य, अम्, n. contrary direction, contrariety,<BR>inverted order, inversion, the being at variance with<BR>the natural or established order of things, reverse-<BR>ness; opposition, hostility, hostile feeling; (आत्), ind.<BR>out of opposition to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेशिक|प्रातिवेशिकः
प्रातिवेशिक प्रातिवेशिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्रति-<BR>वेश), a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्मक|प्रातिवेश्मकः
प्रातिवेश्मक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-वेश्मन्), be-<BR>longing to a neighbour's house, neighbouring; (अस्),<BR>m. a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्य|प्रातिवेश्यः
प्रातिवेश्य, अस्, m. a neighbour who lives opposite,<BR>a next-door neighbour, (according to Kullūka = नि-<BR>रन्तर-गृह-वासिन्); a neighbour in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्यक|प्रातिवेश्यकः
प्रातिवेश्यक, अस्, m. a neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिशाख्य|प्रातिशाख्यं
प्रातिशाख्य प्रातिशाख्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्रति-<BR>शाखम्), a grammatical treatise on the rules regu-<BR>lating the euphonic combination of letters and their<BR>pronunciation peculiar to one of the different Śākhās<BR>or branches of the Vedas, i. e. to one of those<BR>versions of the Vedic texts handed down in different<BR>families in different parts of India, (the Prātiśākhyas<BR>do not undo words in the same way as the Vyākaraṇa,<BR>but take actually formed words as they occur in the<BR>hymns and teach the phonetic changes they undergo,<BR>the mode of pronouncing the accents, &c.; there<BR>exist four Prātiśākhyas, 1. a Prātiśākhya to the<BR>Śākala-śākhā of the Ṛg-veda, called Śākala-prāti-<BR>śākhya and ascribed to Śaunaka; 2. to a Śākhā of<BR>the Taittirīya or Black Yajur-veda; 3. to a Śākhā<BR>of the Mādhyandinas who belong to the family of<BR>the Vājasaneyins or authors of the White Yajur-veda,<BR>whence this is called the Vājasaneyi-prātiśākhya, it<BR>is attributed to Kātyāyana; 4. an Atharva-veda-prā-<BR>tiśākhya, called Śaunakīyā Caturādhyāyikā; but no<BR>Prātiśākhya has yet been found to the Sāma-veda.)<BR>—प्रातिशाख्य-कृत्, त्, m. the author of a Prātiśā-<BR>khya.<BR>—प्रातिशाख्य-भाष्य, अम्, n., N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Ūaṭa on the Ṛg-veda-prātiśākhya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिश्रुत्क
प्रातिश्रुत्क प्रातिश्रुत्क, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-<BR>श्रुत्), Ved. existing in the echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिस्विक|प्रातिस्विकं
प्रातिस्विक प्रातिस्विक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-<BR>स्व), own, peculiar, proper, not common to others;<BR>granting to every one his own due.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहत
प्रातिहत प्रातिहत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रति-<BR>हत), epithet of a particular Svarita (= तैरोवि-<BR>राम, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहन्त्र|प्रातिहंत्र|प्रातिहंत्रं
प्रातिहन्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. प्रति-हन्तृ), the state<BR>or condition of a revenger; vengeance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहर्त्र
प्रातिहर्त्र प्रातिहर्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. प्रति-<BR>हर्तृ, rt. हृ with प्रति), the office or duty of<BR>the Prati-hartṛ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहार|प्रातिहारः
प्रातिहार, अस्, m. (fr. प्रति-हार), a juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारक|प्रातिहारकः
प्रातिहारक, अस्, m. = प्रातिहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारिक|प्रातिहारिकः
प्रातिहारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, containing Prati-hāras (as<BR>a Vedic hymn); (अस्), m. a juggler, conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहार्य|प्रातिहार्यं
प्रातिहार्य, अम्, n. juggling, conjuring, legerde-<BR>main; working miracles; a miracle, miraculous phe-<BR>nomenon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीतिक
प्रातीतिक प्रातीतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रतीति),<BR>existing in the mind or imagination, mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीथेयी
प्रातीथेयी प्रातीथेयी, a various reading for<BR>प्रातिथेयी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीप|प्रातीपः
प्रातीप प्रातीप, अस्, m. (fr. प्रतीप), a<BR>patronymic of Śāntanu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीपिक
प्रातीपिक, अस्, ई, अम्, contrary, reverse, retrograde.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0656-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातृद
प्रातृद प्रातृद, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Pra-tṛd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यक्ष
प्रात्यक्ष प्रात्यक्ष or प्रात्यक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>perceptible to the eyes, &c. (= प्रत्यक्ष, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यग्रथि
प्रात्यग्रथि प्रात्यग्रथि, इस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Pratyag-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यन्तिक|प्रात्यंतिक|प्रात्यंतिकः|प्रात्यन्तिकः
प्रात्यन्तिक प्रात्यन्तिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्रत्य्-<BR>अन्त), a prince of the Pratyantas; a lord of the<BR>marches, keeper of the borders (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्ययिक
प्रात्ययिक प्रात्ययिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रत्य्-<BR>अय), relating to or attended with confidence or trust,<BR>confidential, trusty, having faith in; (अस्), m., scil. प्रति-<BR>भू, a surety for the trustworthiness of a debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यवेक्षा
प्रात्यवेक्षा प्रात्यवेक्षा, wrongly for प्रत्य्-<BR>अवेक्षा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यहिक
प्रात्यहिक प्रात्यहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रत्य्-<BR>अहम्), occurring or happening every day, daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमिक|प्राथमिकः
प्राथमिक प्राथमिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>थम), belonging or relating to the first, primary,<BR>first, initial, initiative, prior, previous; happening or<BR>occurring for the first time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमकल्पिक|प्राथमकल्पिकः
प्राथमकल्पिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्रथम +<BR>कल्प), one who has just commenced the perusal<BR>of the Vedas, a student; a term applied to a Yogi<BR>just commencing his course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथम्य|प्राथम्यं
प्राथम्य, अम्, n. the being first, priority, pre-<BR>cedence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राद्
प्राद् प्राद् (प्र-अद्), cl. 2. P. प्रात्ति, प्रात्-<BR>तुम्, to eat up, consume, devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादक्षिण्य|प्रादक्षिण्यं
प्रादक्षिण्य प्रादक्षिण्य, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-<BR>दक्षिण), keeping the right side towards anything<BR>while moving round it, circumambulation by starting<BR>from the left and coming round to the right (by<BR>way of reverence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादा
प्रादा प्रा-दा (प्र-आ-), cl. 3. P. A. -ददाति,<BR>-दत्ते, -दातुम्, to give, bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादाय
प्रादाय, ind. having given or bestowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादित्य
प्रादित्य प्रादित्य (प्र-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>two princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुराक्षि
प्रादुराक्षि प्रादुराक्षि, इस्, m. a patronymic;<BR>(perhaps an incorrect form for प्रादुर्-अक्षि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुस्
प्रादुस् प्रादुस्, ind. (perhaps fr. प्रा for<BR>1. प्र + 1. दुर्, i. e. before or outside the door, in<BR>open daylight; said to be fr. rt. अद् with प्र; accord-<BR>ing to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 41, the final स् is changed into ष्<BR>before क् and प्; and according to Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 87, the<BR>radical स् of rt. 1. अस्, ‘to be,’ is changed to ष् after<BR>प्रादुस् whenever in the conjugation of this rt. the<BR>initial अ is dropped, e. g. प्रादुः षन्ति, not प्रा-<BR>दुः सन्ति; प्रादुस् appears to occur only in con-<BR>nection with the rts. 1. अस्, 1. भू, and 1. कृ, except<BR>in the comp. प्रादुष्-पीतम् given as an example<BR>by the Scholiast on Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 41); apparently,<BR>evidently, manifestly, visibly, in sight. According<BR>to native lexicographers the senses in which प्रादुस्<BR>is used may be expressed by the following Sanskrit<BR>words, प्राकाश्य, नामन्, सम्-भाव्य, सम्-भव,<BR>प्र-वृत्ति, वृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुरस्
प्रादुर्-अस् (see rt. 1. अस्), cl. 2. P. अस्ति, &c., to<BR>be apparent or evident, to be manifest; to appear,<BR>arise, exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भू
प्रादुर्-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become manifest, become visible; to appear, arise,<BR>come to light, exist; to become audible, be heard.<BR>—प्रादुर्-भाव, अस्, m. the becoming manifest or<BR>visible, arising, coming into existence, appearance,<BR>manifestation; the appearance of a deity on earth;<BR>the being evident; the becoming audible.<BR>—प्रादुर्-<BR>भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become manifest or evident, come<BR>to light, manifested, appeared, revealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्कृ
प्रादुष्-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make visible or manifest, bring to light, reveal,<BR>disclose, exhibit, manifest.<BR>—प्रादुष्-करण, अम्,<BR>n. the making visible, bringing to light, manifesta-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">Page0657-b+ 74</a>]<BR>tion, production.<BR>—प्रादुष्-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>visible, brought to light, manifested, displayed to<BR>view.<BR>—प्रादुष्कृत-वपुस्, उस्, उस्, उस्, one whose<BR>form is manifested, appearing in a visible form (as a<BR>deity).<BR>—प्रादुष्-कृत्य, ind. having brought to<BR>light, having produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्य|प्रादुष्यं
प्रादुष्य, अम्, n. appearance, manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेश|प्रादेशः
प्रादेश प्रादेश, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-देश), the<BR>span of the thumb and forefinger, the space measured<BR>by the span of the thumb and forefinger; place,<BR>country (?).<BR>—प्रादेश-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, only a<BR>span long; प्रादेशमात्रम् भूमेः, a mere span<BR>of land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशन|प्रादेशनं
प्रादेशन, अम्, n. = प्र-देशन, a gift, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिक|प्रादेशिकः
प्रादेशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-देश), authorized<BR>by precedents or examples, precedented; significant,<BR>indicatory of the original meaning; local, limited,<BR>relating to a part; प्रादेशिको गुणः, the property<BR>of a word indicatory of its original or etymological<BR>meaning; (अस्), m. a small landed proprietor, the<BR>owner or chief of a district.<BR>—प्रादेशिकेश्वर (˚क-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. the owner or chief of a district, a small<BR>landed proprietor, (opposed to सार्वभौम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिन्
प्रादेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. प्रादेश), a span long;<BR>(इनी), f. the forefinger, (in this sense probably an<BR>error for प्र-देशिनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादोष|प्रादोषः
प्रादोष प्रादोष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-दोष),<BR>belonging or relating to the evening, vespertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादोषिक|प्रादोषिकः
प्रादोषिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = प्रादोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादोहनि
प्रादोहनि प्रादोहनि, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Pra-dohana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राद्युम्नि
प्राद्युम्नि प्राद्युम्नि, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Pra-dyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राद्योति
प्राद्योति प्राद्योति, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Pra-dyota.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राद्रु
प्राद्रु प्रा-द्रु (प्र-आ-द्रु), cl. 1. P. -द्र-<BR>वति, -द्रोतुम्, to run away from, flee from; to<BR>escape to, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधनिक|प्राधनिकं
प्राधनिक प्राधनिक, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-<BR>धन), an implement of war, a destructive weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधा
प्राधा प्राधा, f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and mother of several Apsarasas and Gan-<BR>dharvas; [cf. प्र-धा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधेय
प्राधेय, अस्, ई, अम्, descended from Prādhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधानिक
प्राधानिक प्राधानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>धान), pre-eminent, most eminent or distinguished,<BR>best, most excellent, superior; predominant; derived<BR>from or relating to Pradhāna or primary matter (in<BR>the Sāṅkhya phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्य|प्राधान्यं
प्राधान्य, अम्, n. predominance, preponder-<BR>ance, prevalence, ascendancy, pre-eminence, superi-<BR>ority, supremacy; the being the highest object; a<BR>principal cause; प्राधान्येन or प्राधान्यात् or<BR>प्राधान्य-तस्, ind. in regard to the highest object,<BR>with reference to the chief purpose; in the highest<BR>degree, chiefly, principally, especially.<BR>—प्राधान्य-<BR>स्तुति, इस्, इस्, इ, receiving especial praise, chiefly praised,<BR>especially celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधीत
प्राधीत प्राधीत, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. 5. इ with<BR>प्र-अधि), well-read, highly educated, learned (said<BR>of Brāhmans).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्ययन|प्राध्ययनं
प्राध्ययन, अम्, n. reciting, reading, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्येषण
प्राध्येषण प्राध्य्-एषण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 3.<BR>इष् with प्र-अधि), Ved. incitement, exhortation<BR>(to study).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्व|प्राध्वं|प्राध्वः
प्राध्व प्राध्व (प्र-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, being<BR>on a road or journey, distant, remote, long, a long<BR>way off; bent, bowed, inclined; favourable, conform-<BR>able; (अस्), m. a car, carriage; (अम्), ind. favourably,<BR>conformably, agreeably; crookedly, in a contrary<BR>way (?).<BR>—प्राध्वं-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to make conformable, to bend conform-<BR>ably, to join together (as the hands) in token of good-<BR>will.<BR>—प्राध्वं-कृत्य, ind. making conformable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्वन
प्राध्वन (प्र-अध्˚), अस्, m., Ved. the bed of<BR>a river or stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्वंसन
प्राध्वंसन प्राध्वंसन, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Pra-dhvaṃsana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्वर
प्राध्वर प्राध्वर, अस्, ई, अम्, an epithet of<BR>a branch of a tree; (probably an incorrect form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्
प्रान् प्रान्. See 1. प्राण्, p. 654, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रानाडी
प्रानाडी प्रानाडी, perhaps incorrectly for<BR>प्र-णाडी = प्र-णाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्त|प्रांत|प्रांतः|प्रान्तः
प्रान्त प्रान्त (प्र-अन्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. edge,<BR>margin, verge, border, (ओष्ठ-प्रान्तौ, the corners<BR>of the mouth); boundary, bound, extremity, extreme<BR>verge, end [cf. यौवन-प्˚]; back part; a point,<BR>tip (of a blade of grass); (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—प्रान्त-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, dwelling near the boun-<BR>daries, living close by.<BR>—प्रान्त-तस्, ind. along the<BR>edge or border (of anything), marginally, along or<BR>upon the extremity.<BR>—प्रान्त-दुर्ग, अम्, n. ‘bor-<BR>der-stronghold,’ a suburb or collection of houses<BR>outside the walls of the town, a Petta or town con-<BR>tiguous to a fort and separately fortified.<BR>—प्रान्त-<BR>पुष्पा, f. a kind of plant (having flowers along the<BR>edge of the stem ?).<BR>—प्रान्त-विरस, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>finally or ultimately insipid, tasteless in the end.<BR>—प्रान्त-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabiting the borders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तायन
प्रान्तायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Prānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तर|प्रांतर|प्रांतरं|प्रान्तरं
प्रान्तर प्रान्तर (प्र-अन्˚), अम्, n. a long<BR>desolate road, a lonesome way or lane, a solitary path;<BR>an intervening long tract of country between two vil-<BR>lages; a forest; the hollow of a tree.<BR>—प्रान्तर-शून्-<BR>य, अम्, n. a long tiresome road (also प्रान्त-शून्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्
प्राप् 1. प्राप् (प्र-आप्), cl. 5. P. A. प्राप्-<BR>नोति, प्राप्नुते, प्राप्तुम्, to attain to, reach,<BR>arrive at; to extend, stretch; to come upon, light<BR>upon, meet with, find; to obtain, get, gain, win;<BR>to obtain as a husband or wife; to bring upon<BR>one's self, contract, incur (e. g. दण्डम् प्राप्, to<BR>incur a fine); to suffer, endure (e. g. वधम् प्राप्,<BR>to suffer capital punishment); to flee to (e. g. दिशः<BR>प्रापन्, they fled to the various quarters, i. e. they<BR>fled in all directions); to pass or be changed into<BR>(in gram.), to follow (a grammatical rule); to be<BR>present, be at hand (Ved.): Caus. प्रापयति, -ते,<BR>-यितुम्, to cause to attain to, cause to reach or<BR>arrive at, cause to occupy; to lead to, bring to;<BR>to promote or advance to, appoint to (an office); to<BR>drive to; to cause to obtain or gain, cause to possess,<BR>give anything to any one (with two acc.); to tell,<BR>announce (Rāmāyaṇa VII. 103, 10): Desid. प्रेप्-<BR>सति, to try to attain or get at, strive to reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्
2. प्राप्, प्, प्, प्, (at the end of a comp.) obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप
1. प्राप, अस्, m. (for 2. see p. 658), arriving at,<BR>reaching, attaining, obtaining; [cf. दुष्-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापक|प्रापकः
प्रापक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing to arrive at, leading<BR>to (with gen.), conveying, bringing; causing to obtain,<BR>providing with, procuring; a procurer; establishing,<BR>making valid; obtaining, one who obtains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापण|प्रापणं
प्रापण, अम्, n. attaining to, attainment, reach-<BR>ing, extending, (बाह्वोः प्रापणान्ते, as far as the<BR>arms reach); obtaining, receiving, acquisition; bring-<BR>ing to, leading to, conveying; procuring [cf. दुष्-<BR>प्रापण]; reference to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणीय|प्रापणीयं
प्रापणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attained to, to be<BR>reached, attainable; to be caused to attain, to be<BR>made to arrive at; to be provided with; to be pro-<BR>cured, procurable, obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापय्य
प्रापय्य, ind. = 2. प्राप्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापित
प्रापित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to attain to, made<BR>to arrive at; caused to occupy, placed upon; led or<BR>conducted to, brought to, conveyed; promoted or<BR>advanced to, appointed to; caused to obtain or gain,<BR>caused to possess; procured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापिन्
प्रापिन्, ई, इणी, इ, attaining to, reaching, coming<BR>to; obtaining, getting, gaining, receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्त|प्राप्तः
प्राप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, attained to, reached, arrived<BR>at [cf. कर-प्˚, हस्त-प्˚]; come upon, lighted<BR>upon, met with, found; obtained, got, gained,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-a" target="_blank">Page0658-a+ 81</a>]<BR>acquired, procured, won; incurred, contracted; suf-<BR>fered, endured; one who has attained to or arrived<BR>at; arrived, come, present; come to a close, com-<BR>pleted, arrived at maturity; (in gram.) obtained<BR>from a rule, following from a rule, valid in conse-<BR>quence of a rule (e. g. इति प्राप्ते, because it so<BR>follows from a preceding rule); (in medicine) de-<BR>scribed (as a symptom); fixed, placed; proper, right;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—प्राप्त-कारिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, doing what is fit or proper.<BR>—प्राप्त-काल,<BR>अस्, m. a time or moment arrived, a favourable<BR>moment, a fit time, proper season; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>one whose time has come (e. g. प्राप्त-कालो देही,<BR>a mortal whose time, i. e. whose last hour, is come);<BR>opportune, seasonable, suitable; arrived at maturity,<BR>marriageable; fated, destined; (अम्), ind. at the<BR>right time, opportunely.<BR>—प्राप्तकाल-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being a favourable moment, timeliness, season-<BR>ableness; (त्वात्), ind. because it is the proper season.<BR>—प्राप्त-जीवन, अस्, आ, अम्, restored to life.<BR>—प्राप्त-दोष, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has incurred<BR>guilt, one who has committed an offence.<BR>—प्राप्त-<BR>पञ्चत्व, अस्, आ, अम्, arrived at dissolution into<BR>the five elements, deceased, dead.<BR>—प्राप्त-बुद्धि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, possessed of understanding, enlightened,<BR>instructed, intelligent; regaining consciousness, be-<BR>coming conscious (after fainting), recovering.<BR>—प्राप्-<BR>त-भार, अस्, m. a draught-ox or beast of burden.<BR>—प्राप्त-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has attained<BR>to any state or condition, of a good disposition; (अस्),<BR>m. a young bullock, an ox, (? for प्राप्त-भार.)<BR>—प्राप्त-मनोरथ, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>obtained his wish.<BR>—प्राप्त-यौवन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has attained the age of puberty, being in<BR>the bloom of youth.<BR>—प्राप्त-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, of<BR>a proper form, fit, proper, suitable; handsome, pleas-<BR>ing, beautiful; learned, wise, educated.<BR>—प्राप्त-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has attained to or arrived<BR>at; one who has obtained or gained.<BR>—प्राप्त-<BR>वर, अस्, आ, अम्, fraught with blessings.<BR>—प्राप्त-<BR>व्यवहार, अस्, m. a young man come of age, an<BR>adult, one able to conduct his own affairs and respon-<BR>sible for his conduct.<BR>—प्राप्त-सूर्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the sun (vertical).<BR>—प्राप्तानुज्ञ (˚त-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one who has received permission to with-<BR>draw, allowed to depart.<BR>—प्राप्तापराध (˚त-<BR>अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has committed an offence,<BR>guilty of an offence.<BR>—प्राप्तार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one whose object is attained, successful; (अस्),<BR>m. an object attained, an advantage gained.<BR>—प्राप्-<BR>तार्थाग्रहण (˚थ-अग्˚), अम्, n. the not securing<BR>of advantages gained.<BR>—प्राप्तावसर (˚त-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, taking or finding occasion, opportune,<BR>seasonable; (अस्), m. a proper time, suitable occasion.<BR>—प्राप्तोदय (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has<BR>attained exaltation, fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0657-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तव्य|प्राप्तव्यं
प्राप्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attained to, to be<BR>reached, attainable; to be met with or found; to be<BR>gained or obtained, obtainable, procurable; a fanciful<BR>name given to a man in the Pañca-tantra (who,<BR>whenever asked his name, replied प्राप्तव्यम् अर्-<BR>थं लभते मनुष्यः, a man takes anything<BR>that is to be got, see Pañca-tantra, p. 128. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्ति|प्राप्तिः
प्राप्ति, इस्, f. attaining to, attainment, reaching,<BR>arriving at, arrival, coming; coming or lighting<BR>upon, meeting with, finding; obtaining, getting,<BR>gaining, acquisition, profit, gain, advantage; reach,<BR>range; the power of obtaining everything, one of<BR>the eight superhuman faculties; obtaining by actions<BR>done in a former existence; discovering by percep-<BR>tion, guessing, conjecture; the being valid, holding<BR>good (of a rule); lot, share, portion, fortune, luck,<BR>good luck; (in dramatic language) happy denoue-<BR>ment, successful termination of a plot; (in astrology)<BR>N. of the eleventh lunar mansion (= आय, लाभ);<BR>Prāpti personified as wife of Śama (associated with<BR>Asti as a daughter of Jarā-sandha); a collection,<BR>assemblage, quantity.<BR>—प्राप्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>one who has attained to or reached.<BR>—प्राप्ति-सम,<BR>अस्, m. a particular जाति (q. v.) in logic.<BR>—प्राप्त्य्-<BR>आशा, f. the hope of obtaining (an object).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्य|प्राप्यं
1. प्राप्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be attained, to be<BR>arrived at, attainable, obtainable, acquirable, pro-<BR>curable [cf. सुख-प्˚]; proper, fitting, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्य|प्राप्यं
2. प्राप्य, ind. having attained to or arrived at;<BR>having come upon or met with; having obtained or<BR>gained; having incurred; having suffered or endured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्यमाण
प्राप्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being attained to or ar-<BR>rived at; taking place (according to a rule in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप
प्राप 2. प्राप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्र + अप्),<BR>abounding with water, watery (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणिक|प्रापणिकः
प्रापणिक प्रापणिक, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. पण्<BR>with प्र; according to Malli-nātha fr. प्र-पण),<BR>a trader, dealer, retail dealer; [cf. आपणिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापेय|प्रापेयः
प्रापेय प्रापेय for प्राधेय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबन्ध
प्राबन्ध प्राबन्ध in केसर-प्राबन्धा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबल्य|प्राबल्यं
प्राबल्य प्राबल्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-बल),<BR>superiority of force, superior force, predominance, as-<BR>cendancy; powerfulness, power, vigour, might, force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबालिक|प्राबालिकः
प्राबालिक प्राबालिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-बाल),<BR>a vender of coral, coral merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबोधक|प्राबोधकः
प्राबोधक प्राबोधक, अस्, m. (= प्र-बो-<BR>धक), a minstrel employed to wake the king in<BR>the morning; (a various reading for प्राबोधिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबोधिक|प्राबोधिकः
प्राबोधिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-बोध), dawn, day-<BR>break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभञ्जन|प्राभंजन|प्राभंजनं
प्राभञ्जन प्राभञ्जन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>भञ्जन), presided over by the god of wind; (अम्),<BR>n., scil. नक्षत्र or भ, the Nakṣatra Svāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभव|प्राभवं
प्राभव प्राभव, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-भु), pre-<BR>eminence, superiority, supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभवत्य|प्राभवत्यं
प्राभवत्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-भवत्), superi-<BR>ority, power, authority, ascendancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभूतिक
प्राभूतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-भूत), see<BR>Vārttika II. to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभाकर|प्राभाकरः
प्राभाकर प्राभाकर, अस्, m. (fr. प्रभा-<BR>कर), a follower of Prabhā-kara, the designation<BR>of a particular philosophical sect (a branch of the<BR>Mīmāṃsā school).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभातिक
प्राभातिक प्राभातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>भात), belonging or relating to the morning, matu-<BR>tinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभासिक
प्राभासिक प्राभासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging<BR>to the place Pra-bhāsa, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृत|प्राभृतं
प्राभृत प्राभृत, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-भृति),<BR>a present, gift, offering of ceremony; an offering to a<BR>deity or sovereign; a bribe; a term applied to the<BR>chapters of the Sūrya-prajñapti.<BR>—प्राभृती-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, given as a present, offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृतक|प्राभृतकं
प्राभृतक, अम्, n. a present, an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामति
प्रामति प्रामति, इस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>seven sages in the tenth Manv-antara; (also read<BR>प्राप्तति; cf. प्र-मति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाणिक|प्रामाणिकः
प्रामाणिक प्रामाणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>माण), forming or being a measure; established<BR>by proof, resting or founded on an authority, pro-<BR>ceeding from evidence or authority, being of authority,<BR>authoritative; authentic, credible; true; (अस्), m.<BR>one who accepts proof or rests his arguments on<BR>authority; a president, the chief or head of a trade.<BR>—प्रामाणिक-त्व, अम्, n. = प्रामाण्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाण्य|प्रामाण्यं
प्रामाण्य, अम्, n. the being established by proof,<BR>the resting upon authority; the being an authority;<BR>the being a rule, the being a proof; proof, evidence,<BR>authority; authenticity, credibility, genuineness (=<BR>प्रमाण-ता).<BR>—प्रामाण्य-वाद, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Nyāya work by Raghu-nātha.<BR>—प्रामाण्य-वादिन्,<BR>ई, m. one who affirms or believes in proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामादिक
प्रामादिक प्रामादिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>माद), arising from carelessness or negligence,<BR>blundering, faulty, erroneous, incorrect, wrong; प्रा-<BR>मादिकः पाठः, a wrong reading.<BR>—प्रामादिक-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. erroneousness, incorrectness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाद्य|प्रामाद्यं|प्रामाद्यः
प्रामाद्य, अस्, m. a species of plant, Gendarussa<BR>(= अटरूष) Adhadota or Vulgaris; (अम्), n.<BR>madness, frenzy, fury; intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामीत्य|प्रामीत्यं
प्रामीत्य प्रामीत्य, अम्, n. debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामोदक
प्रामोदक प्रामोदक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>मोद), charming, transporting, enchanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राय|प्रायः
प्राय प्राय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 5. इ with प्र),<BR>setting out or starting (for a battle, Ved.; Sāy. =<BR>प्र-वेश, entering, or = युद्ध, battle); going<BR>away, departure, departure from life, seeking death<BR>by fasting, sitting down and fasting to death (as a<BR>religious or penitentiary act, or, like the practice of<BR>sitting in Dharnā, to enforce compliance with a de-<BR>mand; often used in connection with rt. 4. आस् or<BR>with उप-विश्, e. g. प्रायम् आस्महे, we sit down<BR>seeking death by fasting; but in such examples<BR>प्रायम् may perhaps be regarded as the indeclinable<BR>participle of rt. 5. इ with प्र; cf. प्रयोपवेश);<BR>principal part, largest portion, plurality, majority,<BR>majority of cases, general rule, abundance, plenty,<BR>excess, (when used at the end of adj. comps. often<BR>translatable by ‘in most cases,’ ‘for the most part,’<BR>‘as a general rule,’ ‘generally,’ ‘well nigh,’ ‘almost,’<BR>‘nearly,’ e. g. दण्ड-प्˚, one who generally inflicts<BR>punishment; जित-प्˚, almost conquered; cf. आर्य-<BR>प्˚, गत-प्˚, दुःख-प्˚, संस्तुत-प्˚, सिद्ध-प्˚:<BR>or translatable by ‘abounding in,’ ‘much,’ ‘exceed-<BR>ing,’ ‘abundant,’ e. g. शालि-प्˚, abounding in rice;<BR>cf. हिंसा-प्˚: or by ‘like,’ ‘resembling,’ e. g. अमृत-<BR>प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, like nectar); a stage or condition<BR>of life (as youth, age, &c.); (अम्), n. sin (?); प्रा-<BR>येण, ind. for the most part, in most cases, mostly,<BR>commonly, as a rule; in all probability, probably,<BR>likely; much more, much rather.<BR>—प्राय-गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, near departure from life, nigh unto death.<BR>—प्राय-चित्त, प्राय-चित्ति, see Scholiast on Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 1, 157, and cf. प्रायश्-चित्त, &c.<BR>—प्राय-<BR>दर्शन, अम्, n. a common or ordinary pheno-<BR>menon.<BR>—प्राय-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, being com-<BR>monly the case, usually met with.<BR>—प्राय-विधा-<BR>यिन्, ई, इनी, इ, resolved to die of starvation.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>यश्-चित्त, अम्, n. (प्राय + चित्त with श् euphonically<BR>inserted), an expiation, expiatory act, atonement,<BR>penance, satisfaction, compensation, indemnification,<BR>amends; (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to or included in<BR>an expiation or atonement, expiatory.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्त-<BR>तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a work by Raghu-nandana.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्त-दीपिका, f., N. of a work on ritual<BR>by Vara-da.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्त-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of<BR>a work by Kāma-deva.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्त-रत्न, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work by Kamalākara-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—प्रायश्-<BR>चित्त-विधि, इस्, m. a prescribed rule of penance or<BR>expiation.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्त-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work by Śūla-pāṇi on expiatory ceremonies.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>यश्-चित्ति, इस्, इस्, इ (प्राय + चित्ति with श् euphoni-<BR>cally inserted), expiating, atoning; (इस्), f. expiation,<BR>atonement, penance.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>expiating, expiatory, performing penance (?); expi-<BR>able.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who does<BR>penance or has to make expiation.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्ति-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, making atonement, expiating,<BR>performing penance.<BR>—१. प्रायश्चित्तीय, Nom. A.<BR>प्रायश्चित्तीयते, -यितुम्, to have to expiate, to be<BR>obliged to perform penance.<BR>—२. प्रायश्चित्तीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating to expiation or penance, expia-<BR>tory.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्तीय-ता, f. obligation to make an<BR>atonement.<BR>—प्रायश्चित्तेन्दु-शेखर (˚त-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a work by Kāśī-nātha on expiatory<BR>ceremonies.<BR>—प्रायोपगमन (˚य-उप्˚), अम्, n.<BR>going to meet death, seeking death (by abstaining<BR>from food).<BR>—प्रायोपविष्ट (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, or प्रायोपवेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who sits<BR>down in expectation of death, one who calmly<BR>awaits the approach of death (by abstaining from<BR>food), one who sits in Dharnā to compel compliance<BR>with a demand; [cf. प्रायोपवेश.]<BR>—प्रायोप-<BR>वेश (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m. or प्रायोपवेशन, अम्, n.<BR>or प्रायोपवेशनिका, f. abstaining from food and<BR>awaiting in a sitting posture the approach of death,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">Page0659-a+ 74</a>]<BR>(this corresponds with the practice prevalent in some<BR>parts of India of sitting in Dharnā at the door of a<BR>house to extort a boon or gain a point which cannot<BR>be accomplished by other means; the person so<BR>sitting observes a strict fast till his object is obtained,<BR>and if he dies in the process the sin falls on the<BR>householder who refuses compliance with his de-<BR>mand.)<BR>—प्रायोपेत (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, prepared<BR>to die, resolved to die (by abstaining from food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0658-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायण|प्रायणं
प्रायण, अस्, आ, अम्, going away, going, going<BR>well (Ved.); (अम्), n. entrance, beginning, com-<BR>mencement; the course or path of life; going for<BR>protection, taking refuge; departure from life, death,<BR>voluntary death, (प्रायणं कृ, to court death);<BR>a kind of food prepared with milk.<BR>—प्रायणान्त<BR>(˚ण-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of life; (अम्), ind. till<BR>death, unto death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायणीय|प्रायणीयः
प्रायणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the entrance or commencement, introductory, ini-<BR>tiatory; (अस्), m., scil. याग or कर्म-विशेष, an<BR>introductory libation at a Soma sacrifice; scil. अति-<BR>रात्र, the first day of a Soma sacrifice lasting for<BR>several days; (अम्), n., scil. अहन्, the first day of a<BR>Soma sacrifice lasting for several days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायशस्
प्राय-शस्, ind. for the most part, mostly, almost, in<BR>all probability, always, commonly, generally, usually;<BR>(sometimes wrongly spelt प्राय-सस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायस्
प्रायस्, ind. for the most part, mostly; commonly,<BR>usually, frequently, oftentimes, generally, nearly; in all<BR>probability, most likely, abundantly, largely.<BR>—प्रायो-<BR>देवता, f. the most usually worshipped deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायिक|प्रायिकं
प्रायिक, अस्, आ, अम्, common, usual, general.<BR>—प्रायिक-त्व, अम्, n. likelihood, probability;<BR>usage, custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायत्य|प्रायत्यं
प्रायत्य प्रायत्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-यत),<BR>purity, cleanliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्त|प्रायश्चित्तं
प्रायश्चित्त प्रायश्-चित्त. See प्राय, p. 658.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायाणिक
प्रायाणिक प्रायाणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>याण), necessary for a march, suitable for a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायात्रिक
प्रायात्रिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-यात्रा), = प्रा-<BR>याणिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायास
प्रायास प्रा-यास, अस्, m., Ved. another<BR>form for प्र-यास, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायिक|प्रायिकं
प्रायिक प्रायिक. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायुद्धेषिन्
प्रायुद्धेषिन् प्रायुद्धेषिन्, ई, m. a horse,<BR>(probably an incorrect form; also spelt प्रायुधे-<BR>षिन्; cf. rt. हेष्, to neigh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायुध्
प्रायुध् प्रा-युध् (प्र-आ-), cl. 4. A. -युध्-<BR>यते, -योद्धुम्, to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायेण
प्रायेण प्रायेण. See under प्राय, p. 658.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोग
प्रायोग प्रायोग, अस्, m., Ved. perhaps a<BR>wrong reading for प्र-योग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोगिक
प्रायोगिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-योग), applied,<BR>used, applicable; a kind of sternutatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोज्य|प्रायोज्यं
प्रायोज्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्र-योज्य), belonging<BR>or relating to things requisite or necessary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्
प्रार् प्रार् (प्र-ऋ), cl. 3. P. प्रेयर्ति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to go forth, go, move; to set in motion, pro-<BR>duce: Caus. प्रार्पयति, -यितुम्, to set in motion,<BR>stir up, animate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्पण
प्रार्पण, अस्, m., Ved. one who stirs up or<BR>animates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारभ्
प्रारभ् प्रा-रभ् (प्र-आ-), cl. 1. A. -रभते,<BR>-रब्धुम्, to begin, commence, undertake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्ध|प्रारब्धं
प्रा-रब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, begun, commenced,<BR>beginning; (अम्), n. an undertaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्धि|प्रारब्धिः
प्रा-रब्धि, इस्, f. beginning, commencement;<BR>the post to which an elephant is fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारम्भ|प्रारंभ|प्रारंभः|प्रारम्भः
प्रा-रम्भ, अस्, m. beginning, commencement;<BR>an undertaking, enterprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारम्भण|प्रारंभण|प्रारंभणं
प्रा-रम्भण, अम्, n. beginning, commencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारुह्
प्रारुह् प्रा-रुह् (प्र-आ-), cl. 1. P. -रोहति,<BR>-रोढुम्, to ascend, rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारोह|प्रारोहः
प्रारोह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-रोह), one who is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">Page0659-b+ 75</a>]<BR>used to rise or ascend; (अस्), m. a shoot, sprout, a<BR>new branch or leaf (= प्र-रोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्क्षीय
प्रार्क्षीय प्रार्क्षीय (fr. प्र + ऋक्ष), Nom.<BR>P. प्रार्क्षीयति = प्रर्क्षीयति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्च्
प्रार्च् प्रार्च् (प्र-अर्च्), cl. 1. P. प्रार्चति,<BR>प्रार्चितुम्, to praise, celebrate in hymns (Sāy. =<BR>स्तुति-रूपाभिर् वाग्भिः पूज्); to honour, worship:<BR>Caus. प्रार्चयति, -यितुम्, to praise, honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्ज्
प्रार्ज् प्रार्ज् (प्र-अर्ज्), Caus. P. प्रार्जयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to acquire; to grant, bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्जयितृ
प्रार्जयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who grants or<BR>bestows; (used to explain पर्जन्य, Nirukta X.<BR>10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्जुन
प्रार्जुन प्रार्जुन (प्र-अर्˚), आस्, m. pl., N.<BR>of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्ण|प्रार्णं
प्रार्ण प्रार्ण (प्र-ऋण), अम्, n. a chief or<BR>principal debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थ्
प्रार्थ् प्रार्थ् (प्र-अर्थ्), cl. 10. A. (rarely<BR>also P. and according to some grammarians regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. अर्थ with प्र), प्रार्थयते (-ति),<BR>-यितुम्, to wish for, desire, require, want; to ask<BR>for, beg for, pray for, request, solicit, ask any one<BR>for anything (with two acc.); to wish or want to do<BR>anything (with inf.); to pray, prefer a suit or peti-<BR>tion, make a request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थ
प्रार्थ (प्र-अर्˚), अस्, m., Ved. (perhaps) fur-<BR>niture, gear, harness, apparatus, equipment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थक|प्रार्थकः
प्रार्थक, अस्, इका, अम्, wishing for, asking,<BR>desiring, soliciting, begging, an asker, solicitor; a<BR>suitor, petitioner, candidate; अ-प्रार्थक-वर, a<BR>bridegroom who has not been a suitor [cf. Kullūka<BR>on Manu III. 27].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थन|प्रार्थनं
प्रार्थन, अम्, आ, n. f. desire, wish; longing<BR>desire for; requesting, asking, begging; supplication,<BR>suit; prayer, entreaty, request, application, petition<BR>(the object may be expressed by the loc., e. g. रुक्-<BR>मिण्याम् अस्य प्रार्थना, his petition or suit for<BR>Rukmiṇī; or precedes प्रार्थन in a comp., cf.<BR>अनुज्ञा-प्˚); प्रार्थनया, ind. at the request or<BR>petition of (any one).<BR>—प्रार्थना-भङ्ग, अस्, m.<BR>refusal of a request, asking in vain.<BR>—प्रार्थना-<BR>भाव (˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, m. absence of solicitation.<BR>—प्रार्थना-सिद्धि, इस्, f. accomplishment of a<BR>desire, fulfilment of wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थनीय|प्रार्थनीयं
प्रार्थनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or wished<BR>for; to be asked or begged; to be prayed for;<BR>worthy of desire, desirable, proper to be solicited;<BR>(अम्), n. the third or Dvāpara age of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थयितव्य
प्रार्थयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or<BR>wished for, worthy of desire, desirable; असुलभ-<BR>प्रार्थयितव्य, one the object of whose desire is<BR>difficult of attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थयितृ
प्रार्थयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who wishes for or<BR>asks or solicits, an asker, inquirer, solicitor, impor-<BR>tuner, beggar; a lover, wooer, suitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थित|प्रार्थितः
प्रार्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, wished for, desired, wished,<BR>required, wanted; requested, solicited, asked for,<BR>prayed for; killed, hurt; obstructed or opposed by<BR>an enemy; attacked.<BR>—प्रार्थित-दुर्लभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, desired but hard to obtain.<BR>—प्रार्थित-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, one who has asked or begged; asking,<BR>begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थिन्
प्रार्थिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wishing, desiring, desirous of,<BR>ambitious for; attacking, assailing, assaulting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थ्य
प्रार्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or wished for<BR>by any one (inst. or gen.); desirable; to be suppli-<BR>cated, implored, petitioned, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्द्
प्रार्द् प्रार्द् (प्र-अर्द्), Caus. P. प्रार्दयति,<BR>-यितुम्, Ved. to exert beyond measure, overwork;<BR>to cause to flow away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्दक
प्रार्दक, अस्, इका, अम्, making efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्ध
प्रार्ध प्रार्ध (प्र-अर्˚) in परि-प्रार्ध, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्पण
प्रार्पण प्रार्पण. See under प्रार्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्ष्
प्रार्ष् प्रार्ष् (प्र-ऋष्), cl. 1. P. प्रार्षति,<BR>प्रार्षितुम्, to flow forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्षभीय
प्रार्षभीय प्रार्षभीय (fr. प्र + ऋषभ),<BR>Nom. P. प्रार्षभीयति, -यितुम्, = प्रर्षभीय,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्ह्
प्रार्ह् प्रार्ह् (प्र-अर्ह्), cl. 1. A. प्रार्हते,<BR>प्रार्हितुम्, Ved. to distinguish or signalize one's<BR>self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्ब|प्रालंब|प्रालम्बं|प्रालम्बः
प्रालम्ब प्रालम्ब, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-लम्ब),<BR>hanging down, suspended, pendent; (अस्), m. a kind<BR>of pearl ornament; the female breast; a species of<BR>gourd; (अम्), n. a garland hanging round the neck<BR>and reaching to the breast; [cf. मुक्ता-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्बक|प्रालंबक|प्रालंबकं
प्रालम्बक, अम्, n. a garland hanging round<BR>the neck and reaching to the breast; (इका), f. a<BR>kind of golden necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेपिक
प्रालेपिक प्रालेपिक, अस्, ई, अम्, an adj. de-<BR>rived from प्र-लेपिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेय|प्रालेयं
प्रालेय 1. प्रालेय, अस्, ई (?), अम् (anoma-<BR>lously fr. प्र-लय), produced by melting; (अम्),<BR>n. (according to some also अस्, m.), hail, snow, frost,<BR>hoar-frost (so called as being easily dissolved), dew.<BR>—प्रालेय-रश्मि, इस्, or प्रालेयांशु (˚य-अं˚), उस्,<BR>m. the moon (said to have cold or frosty rays).<BR>—प्रा-<BR>लेय-लेश, अस्, m. a hailstone.<BR>—प्रालेय-शैल, अस्,<BR>or प्रालेयाद्रि (˚य-अद्˚), इस्, m. the snowy moun-<BR>tain, Hima-vat.<BR>—प्रालेयाश्र (˚य-अश्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>cold or chilly tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेय|प्रालेयं
2. प्रालेय, Nom. P. प्रालेयति, -यितुम्, to re-<BR>semble hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राल्कारीय
प्राल्कारीय प्राल्कारीय (fr. प्र + ऌकार),<BR>Nom. P. प्राल्कारीयति, -यितुम्, = प्रल्कारीय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्
प्राव् प्राव् (प्र-अव्), cl. 1. P. प्रावति, प्रा-<BR>वितुम्, Ved. to attend to, observe; to take interest<BR>in, assist, encourage, animate; to protect, defend,<BR>(Sāy. = प्रकर्षेण रक्ष्, to defend strenuously,<BR>to protect exceedingly); to sate, satisfy, content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावितृ
प्रावितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. a protector, bene-<BR>factor, guardian, (Sāy. = रक्षक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावित्र
प्रावित्र, अम्, n., Ved. protection, guardianship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावी
प्रावी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, Ved. attentive, taking care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावट|प्रावटः
प्रावट प्रावट, अस्, m. barley; [cf. प्र-वट,<BR>प्र-वेट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावण|प्रावणं
प्रावण प्रावण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according<BR>to Sāy.) a spade, shovel; (either a lengthened form<BR>for प्र-वण or a derivative from it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावणि
प्रावणि प्रावणि, see Ujjvala-datta on<BR>Uṇādi-sūtras II. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावन्
प्रावन् प्रावन् (fr. rt. 1. प्रा) in क्रतु-प्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावनिज्
प्रावनिज् प्राव-निज् (प्र-अव-), cl. 3. P. A.<BR>-नेनेक्ति, -नेनिक्ते, -नेक्तुम्, Ved. to wash away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर|प्रावरः
प्रावर प्रा-वर. See under प्रा-वृ, p. 660.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरेय
प्रावरेय प्रावरेय, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Pra-vara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर्ग
प्रावर्ग प्रावर्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-वर्ग),<BR>Ved. distinguished, eminent; (Sāy.) pre-eminently a<BR>scatterer of enemies (= प्रकर्षेण शत्रूणां<BR>वर्जयिता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर्तक
प्रावर्तक प्रा-वर्तक, अस्, इका, अम् (for प्र-<BR>वर्तक), bringing to light, manifesting; stirring<BR>up, inciting; founding, a founder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर्षिन्
प्रावर्षिन् प्रा-वर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. rt. वृष्<BR>with प्र), Ved. raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावहणि
प्रावहणि प्रावहणि for प्रावाहणि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावार|प्रावारः
प्रावार प्रा-वार, &c. See under प्रा-वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावास
प्रावास प्रावास, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-वास),<BR>see Gaṇa Vyuṣṭādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावासिक
प्रावासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, see Gaṇa Guḍādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 3, 103, and Gaṇa Santāpādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावाहणि
प्रावाहणि प्रावाहणि, इस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Pra-vāhaṇa; (also wrongly written प्राहणि,<BR>प्रावहणि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0659-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावाहणेय
प्रावाहणेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Pra-<BR>vāhaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावाहणेयक
प्रावाहणेयक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. प्रावाहणेय),<BR>= प्रवाहणेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावाहणेयि
प्रावाहणेयि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Prāvā-<BR>haṇeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावितृ
प्रावितृ प्रावितृ. See under प्राव्, p. 659.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावीण्य|प्रावीण्यं
प्रावीण्य प्रावीण्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-वीण),<BR>cleverness, dexterity, skilfulness, proficiency, accurate<BR>knowledge, conversancy, skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृ
प्रावृ प्रा-वृ (प्र-आ-), cl. 5. 9. 1. P. A.<BR>-वृणोति, -वृणुते, -वृणाति, -वृणीते, -वरति, -ते,<BR>-वरितुम्, -वरीतुम्, to put on, dress one's self in<BR>(with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर|प्रावरः
प्रा-वर, अस्, m. an inclosure, a fence, hedge;<BR>[cf. मही-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरक
प्रा-वरक, अस्, m., N. of a district (= प्रा-वार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरण|प्रावरणं
प्रा-वरण, अम्, n. a covering, cover, an upper<BR>or outer garment, cloak, mantle [cf. कर्ण-प्˚, कु-<BR>प्˚]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; चीर-प्रावरण,<BR>आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरणीय|प्रावरणीयं
प्रावरणीय, अम्, n. a covering, upper garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावार|प्रावारः
प्रा-वार, अस्, m. an upper or outer garment,<BR>cloak, mantle; (अस्), m. = प्रा-वरक, N. of a<BR>district; (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to, found in outer<BR>garments or cloaks.<BR>—प्रावार-कर्ण, अस्, m.<BR>‘cloak-eared,’ N. of an owl.<BR>—प्रावार-कीट, अस्,<BR>m. ‘clothes-insect,’ a large kind of white ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारक|प्रावारकः
प्रा-वारक, अस्, m. an upper or outer garment,<BR>cloak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारिक|प्रावारिकः
प्रावारिक, अस्, m. a maker of upper garments<BR>or cloaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारीय
प्रावारीय, Nom. P. प्रावारीयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>use as an upper garment or cloak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावुवूर्षु
प्रा-वुवूर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing or intending<BR>to wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत|प्रावृतं|प्रावृतः
प्रा-वृत, अस्, आ, अम्, covered, enclosed, encom-<BR>passed, screened, sheltered; (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n.<BR>a veil, mantle, cloak, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृति|प्रावृतिः
प्रा-वृति, इस्, f. an inclosure, fence, hedge; spiritual<BR>darkness, one of the four consequences of Māyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत्य
प्रा-वृत्य, ind. having put on, having dressed<BR>one's self in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत्तिक|प्रावृत्तिकः
प्रावृत्तिक प्रावृत्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>वृत्ति), secondary, derived, derivative, (opposed to<BR>मुख्य); informed of what is passing, well-informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्
प्रावृष् प्रा-वृष्, ट्, f. (fr. प्र-वृष्), the<BR>rainy season, wet season, rains; the months Āṣāḍha<BR>and Śrāvaṇa (comprising the first half of the rainy<BR>season which lasts in some parts from the middle of<BR>June till the middle of October).<BR>—प्रावृट्-काल,<BR>अस्, m. the period of the rains, rainy season.<BR>—प्रा-<BR>वृट्काल-वह, अस्, आ, अम्, flowing only in the<BR>rainy season; (opposed to सदाकाल-वह.)<BR>—प्रा-<BR>वृड्-अत्यय, अस्, m. the time following the rainy<BR>season, autumn.<BR>—प्रावृषि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced<BR>in the rainy season, occurring during the rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष|प्रावृषः
प्रा-वृष, अस्, आ, m. f. the rainy season, the rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषायणी
प्रावृषायणी, f. (fr. प्रा-वृष्), a kind of<BR>weed which grows most luxuriantly during the rains,<BR>Bœrhavia Procumbens; Mucuna Pruritus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिक|प्रावृषिकः
प्रावृषिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the rainy<BR>season, born or produced in the rainy season; (अस्),<BR>m. a peacock (as delighting in the rains).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषीण
प्रावृषीण, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating<BR>to the rainy season, rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषेण्य|प्रावृषेण्यः
प्रावृषेण्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging or relating<BR>to the rainy season; coming in showers, abundant,<BR>numerous, much; (अस्), m. the Cadamba tree,<BR>Nauclea Cadamba [cf. कदम्ब]; Wrightia Anti-<BR>dysenterica; (आ), f. the plant Mucuna Pruritus; a<BR>species of Punar-navā with red flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषेय
प्रावृषेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्य|प्रावृष्यं|प्रावृष्यः
प्रावृष्य, अस्, m. a species of Cadamba, Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica; Hedysarum Alhagi; (अम्), n. lapis<BR>lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेण्य|प्रावेण्यं
प्रावेण्य प्रावेण्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-वेणि or<BR>प्र-वेणी), a fine woollen covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेप
प्रावेप प्रावेप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-वेप),<BR>Ved. revolving easily, rolling easily, (Sāy. = कम्-<BR>पन-शील.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशन
प्रावेशन प्रावेशन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-वे-<BR>शन), given on entering, to be done on entering,<BR>(see Gaṇa Vyuṣṭādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 97); (अम्), n.<BR>a manufactory, workshop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशिक
प्रावेशिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-वेश), relating to<BR>entrance (into a house or upon the stage); connected<BR>with entry; in the habit of entering; प्रावेशिक्य्<BR>आक्षिप्तिका, a particular air or song called Ā-kṣiptikā<BR>sung by a person on entering the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्रज्य|प्राव्रज्यं
प्राव्रज्य प्राव्रज्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-व्रज्या),<BR>wandering as a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्राज्य|प्राव्राज्यं
प्राव्राज्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-व्राज्), the life of a<BR>wandering religious mendicant; vagrancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
प्राश् 1. प्राश् (प्र-अश्, see rt. 1. अश्), cl. 5.<BR>P. A. प्राश्नोति, प्राश्नुते, प्राशितुम्, Ved. to<BR>arrive at, reach, (Sāy. = प्रकर्षेण व्य्-आप्); to<BR>fall to the lot or share of any one (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राष्ट
प्राष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, arrived at, attained, gained.<BR>—प्राष्ट-वर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, = प्रिश्नि (Nirukta<BR>X. 39).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
प्राश् 2. प्राश् (प्र-अश्, see rt. 2. अश्), cl. 9.<BR>P. A. प्राश्नाति, प्राश्नीते, प्राशितुम्, to begin to<BR>eat, begin eating; to take into the mouth; taste<BR>(Manu II. 62); to eat, consume, devour; (A.) to<BR>drink; to enjoy, sport with, dally with (with inst.):<BR>Pass. प्राश्यते, to be fed: Caus. प्राशयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to cause to eat or devour, give to eat, feed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
3. प्राश्, ट्, f., Ved. food, provisions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश|प्राशः
प्राश, अस्, m. eating, consuming, feeding upon,<BR>tasting [cf. घृत-प्˚, धूम-प्˚]; food, victuals<BR>[cf. चातुष्प्राश्य]; (occasionally incorrect) for प्रा-<BR>स, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशक|प्राशकः
प्राशक, अस्, इका, अम्, one who eats, an eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशन|प्राशनं
प्राशन, अम्, n. the act of eating, feeding upon,<BR>tasting; causing to eat or taste [cf. अन्न-प्˚];<BR>feeding (especially applied in Manu II. 29 to the cere-<BR>mony of making an infant taste, for the first time, a<BR>little honey and clarified butter); food, victuals;<BR>अमृत-प्राशन, अस्, m. having nectar for food,<BR>feeding on ambrosia, an immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशनीय
प्राशनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, eatable, edible, esculent,<BR>serving for food; (अम्), n. food, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशव्य
प्राशव्य, आस्, m. pl. (fr. 3. प्राश् or प्राश), Ved.<BR>food, provisions; (Sāy.) = साध्व्-अन्नादि, हितम्<BR>अन्नादि, good or wholesome food, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित|प्राशितं
प्राशित, अस्, आ, अम्, taken into the mouth, tasted;<BR>eaten, devoured, swallowed, well eaten; (अम्), n. an<BR>offering of rice or water to the Manes of progenitors,<BR>obsequies to deceased ancestors (Manu III. 74, =<BR>पितृ-यज्ञाख्यं नित्य-श्राद्धम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशितव्य
प्राशितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eaten, eatable,<BR>edible, esculent, allowed to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशितृ
प्राशितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who eats, an eater,<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित्र|प्राशित्रं
प्राशित्र, अम्, n., Ved. the portion of Havis eaten<BR>by the Brahman at a sacrifice; the vessel in which<BR>the Brahman's portion of Havis is placed; anything<BR>edible.<BR>—प्राशित्र-हरण, अम्, n., Ved. a vessel in<BR>which the Brahman's portion of Havis is placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित्रिय
प्राशित्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. in अ-प्राशित्रिय, not<BR>fit for the Prāśitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशिन्
प्राशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) eating,<BR>feeding upon; अमृत-प्राशिन्, ई, m. eating nectar,<BR>a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्नत्
प्राश्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, eating, consuming, de-<BR>vouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्य
1. प्राश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eaten, eatable, edible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्य
2. प्राश्य, ind. having eaten, having tasted or<BR>sipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशस्त्य|प्राशस्त्यं
प्राशस्त्य प्राशस्त्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-शस्त),<BR>the being praised, praiseworthiness, celebrity, excel-<BR>lence, pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशास्त्र|प्राशास्त्रं
प्राशास्त्र प्राशास्त्र, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-शास्तृ),<BR>the office of the Pra-śāstṛ, q. v.; government, rule,<BR>dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशु|प्राशुः
प्राशु प्राशु (प्र-आशु), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. (accord-<BR>ing to the Nirukta = क्षिप्र), exceedingly quick or<BR>speedy, swift; (Sāy.) = सोमस्य प्राशकः, an eater<BR>or partaker of Soma; or = वृत्रस्य हिंसकः,<BR>the enemy (or injurer) of Vṛtra.<BR>—प्राशु-षह् or<BR>प्राशु-षाह्, षाट्, ट्, ट्, Ved. leading or curbing swift<BR>horses, having fleet horses; (Sāy.) = शीघ्रम् अभि-<BR>भवितृ, rapidly victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशू
प्राशू प्राशू, ऊस्, m. = परा-क्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशृङ्ग
प्राशृङ्ग प्रा-शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>projecting horns, having the horns bent forward;<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara = प्रकृष्ट-श्रिङ्ग-<BR>युक्त.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्निक|प्राश्निकः
प्राश्निक प्राश्निक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रश्न),<BR>containing questions or inquiries [cf. बहु-प्˚]; (अस्),<BR>m. an inquirer, asker, examiner; one who decides a<BR>dispute or quarrel, an umpire, arbiter, arbitrator; an<BR>assistant at a spectacle or assembly (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्नीपुत्र
प्राश्नी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्य
प्राश्य 1. and 2. प्राश्य. See under 2.<BR>प्राश्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्रवण
प्राश्रवण प्राश्रवण. See प्रास्रवण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्लिष्ट
प्राश्लिष्ट प्राश्लिष्ट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>श्लिष्ट; in Ved. gram.) N. of a kind of Svarita<BR>produced by the combination of two short इस्; (also<BR>wrongly read प्राक्-श्लिष्ट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्वमेध
प्राश्वमेध प्राश्वमेध (प्र-अश्˚), अस्, m. a<BR>preceding horse sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राष्ट
प्राष्ट प्राष्ट. See under 1. प्राश्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्
प्रास् 1. प्रास् (प्र-अस्, see rt. 1. अस्), cl. 2.<BR>P. प्रास्ति, &c., Ved. to be in front of, be in an<BR>especial manner or extraordinary degree; to be pre-<BR>eminent, excel, preponderate, (Sāy. = प्र-भू.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्
प्रास् 2. प्रास् (प्र-अस्, see rt. 2. अस्), cl. 4.<BR>P. प्रास्यति, प्रासितुम्, to throw forth, cast away,<BR>hurl forth, fling forth; to throw, cast, discharge (a<BR>missile); अंशम् प्रास्, to cast lots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास|प्रासः
प्रास, अस्, m. casting, throwing; interspersing,<BR>insertion; a barbed missile or dart; a particular<BR>constellation or a particular position of a planet; N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासक|प्रासकः
प्रासक, अस्, m. a die, dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासन|प्रासनं
प्रासन, अम्, n. throwing forth, casting away;<BR>throwing, casting; throwing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासिक|प्रासिकः
प्रासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, armed with a dart or javelin;<BR>(अस्), m. a spearman, lancer, javelin-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्त
प्रास्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown away, thrown off;<BR>thrown into, thrown, cast, hurled, discharged; ex-<BR>pelled, turned out, banished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग|प्रासंग|प्रासंगः|प्रासङ्गः
प्रासङ्ग प्रासङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-सङ्ग), a<BR>kind of yoke for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्गिक|प्रासंगिक
प्रासङ्गिक, अस्, ई, अम्, resulting from attach-<BR>ment, proceeding from near relation, derived from<BR>close connection; connected with, inseparably con-<BR>nected, inherent, innate; pertaining to, belonging to<BR>any topic, relevant; opportune, seasonable; occasion-<BR>ally connected, occasional, incidental, casual, acci-<BR>dental, (opposed to आधिकारिक); episodical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग्य|प्रासंग्य|प्रासंग्यः|प्रासङ्ग्यः
प्रासङ्ग्य, अस्, गी (?), अम्, harnessed with a<BR>yoke, yoked; (अस्), m. any animal used for draught,<BR>a draught-ox or one yoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासच
प्रासच प्रासच, अस्, m., Ved. a sudden and<BR>violent shower of rain?; (ई), f. a flood of water<BR>produced by sudden and violent showers of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासर्पक
प्रासर्पक प्रासर्पक, अस्, m. = प्र-सर्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासह्
प्रासह् प्रा-सह्, ट्, f., Ved. power, force; प्रा-<BR>सहा, by force, violently, mightily, (Sāy. = बलेन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासह
प्रा-सह, अस्, m., Ved. power, force, (Sāy.) = श-<BR>त्रूणाम् प्रकर्षेणाभिभविता; (आ), f., N. of<BR>the wife of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासाह
प्रा-साह, अस्, आ, अम्, overpowering, subduing; ज-<BR>गत्-प्रासाह, (in which) the Jagatīmetre predominates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0660-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासाद|प्रासादः
प्रासाद प्रासाद, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-सद्), a<BR>lofty seat or platform for spectators; a building<BR>erected on high foundations and approached by<BR>means of steps, a building consecrated to a deity or<BR>inhabited by a prince, a temple, palace; the assembly<BR>room and confessional hall of the Buddhist priest-<BR>hood.<BR>—प्रासाद-कुक्कुट, अस्, m. a domestic<BR>pigeon.<BR>—प्रासाद-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone to (the<BR>roof of) a palace.<BR>—प्रासाद-तल, अम्, n. the flat<BR>roof of a house or palace.<BR>—प्रासाद-परामन्त्र,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a particular magical formula (a com-<BR>bination of the letters ह and स, = परा-प्रासाद-<BR>मन्त्र).<BR>—प्रासाद-पृष्ठ, अस्, m. a terrace or<BR>balcony on the top of a large house.<BR>—प्रासाद-प्र-<BR>तिष्ठा, f. the consecration of a temple.<BR>—प्रासाद-<BR>प्रस्तर, अस्, m. the flat roof of a house.<BR>—प्रासाद-<BR>मण्डना, f. a kind of orpiment.<BR>—प्रासाद-वासिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, dwelling in a palace.<BR>—प्रासाद-शायिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, accustomed to sleep in a palace.<BR>—प्रासाद-<BR>शृङ्ग, अम्, n. the spire or pinnacle of a palace or<BR>temple, a turret.<BR>—प्रासाद-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, stand-<BR>ing on (the roof of) a palace.<BR>—प्रासादाग्र्य (˚द-<BR>अग्˚), आणि, n. pl. the most excellent or beautiful<BR>palaces.<BR>—प्रासादाङ्गना (˚द-अङ्˚), f. the court-<BR>yard of a temple, precincts^1 of a shrine.<BR>—प्रासादा-<BR>रोहण (˚द-आर्˚), अम्, n. the going up into a<BR>palace, entering a palace.<BR>—प्रासादारोहणीय, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, relating to the act of going up into a palace.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादिक
प्रासादिक, अस्, आ (?), अम् (fr. प्र-साद), kind,<BR>amiable, friendly, favourable; given by way of<BR>blessing, given as a favour; beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादीय
1. प्रासादीय, Nom. P. प्रासादीयति, &c., to<BR>imagine one's self to be in a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादीय
2. प्रासादीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to a palace,<BR>palatial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासिक|प्रासिकः
प्रासिक प्रासिक. See under 2. प्रास्, p. 660.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासूतिक
प्रासूतिक प्रासूतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. प्र-<BR>सूति), belonging or relating to childbirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासेनजिती
प्रासेनजिती प्रासेनजिती, f. a patronymic<BR>from Prasena-jit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासेव
प्रासेव प्रा-सेव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. सिव् with प्र),<BR>Ved. a rope (forming part of a horse's harness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्कण्व
प्रास्कण्व प्रास्कण्व, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or<BR>relating to Pra-skaṇva; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्तारिक
प्रास्तारिक प्रास्तारिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>स्तार), see Scholiast on Pāṇ. IV. 4, 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्ताविक
प्रास्ताविक प्रास्ताविक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>स्ताव), forming a commencement or introduction;<BR>having a prelude (as a hymn, Ved.); useful on<BR>occasion, suiting the subject under treatment; op-<BR>portune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्तुत्य|प्रास्तुत्यं
प्रास्तुत्य, अम्, n. (fr. प्र-स्तुत), the being pro-<BR>pounded or discussed, the being under discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थानिक
प्रास्थानिक प्रास्थानिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>स्थान), relating to departure; favourable or auspi-<BR>cious to a departure; [cf. महा-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थिक|प्रास्थिकः
प्रास्थिक प्रास्थिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-स्थ),<BR>containing a Prastha, weighing a Prastha, bought for<BR>a Prastha; (अम्), n., scil. क्षेत्रम्, a field sown<BR>with a Prastha of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्रवण
प्रास्रवण प्रास्रवण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्र-<BR>स्रवण), coming or derived from a spring or<BR>fountain (as water); (अस्), m. a patronymic from<BR>Pra-sravaṇa; प्लक्षः प्रास्रवणः, N. of a<BR>place, the source of the Sarasvatī or the spot where<BR>the Sarasvatī reappears [cf. सरस्-वती]; (also spelt<BR>प्राश्रवण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्
प्राह् प्राह् (प्र-अह्, see 3. अह्), only in<BR>Perf. प्राह, to utter, express; to announce, pro-<BR>claim, declare, state, tell, speak, say (with acc. of<BR>the thing and dat. or acc. of the person); to record,<BR>hand down by tradition; to call, name; to consider<BR>or regard as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह|प्राहः
प्राह प्राह, अस्, m. instruction in the art<BR>of acting or dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहणि
प्राहणि प्राहणि, इस्, m. a wrong reading<BR>for प्रावाहणि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहारिक|प्राहारिकः
प्राहारिक प्राहारिक, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-हार),<BR>a police officer, constable (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहृतायन
प्राहृतायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Pra-<BR>hṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहुण|प्राहुणः
प्राहुण प्राहुण, अस्, ई, m. f. a guest (=<BR>प्राघुण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहुणक
प्राहुणक, अस्, m. = प्राहुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहुणिका
प्राहुणिका, f. a female guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्ण|प्राह्णः
प्राह्ण प्राह्ण (fr. प्र + अह्न), अस्, m. the<BR>early part of the day, forenoon, morning; (अम्, ए),<BR>ind. in the forenoon, in the morning.<BR>—प्राह्णे-<BR>तमाम्, ind. very early in the forenoon.<BR>—प्राह्णे-<BR>तराम्, ind. earlier in the forenoon, very early in<BR>the morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतन|प्राह्णेतनः
प्राह्णेतन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to<BR>the forenoon, happening in the morning, matutinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्राद
प्राह्राद प्राह्राद, अस्, m. (fr. प्र-ह्राद),<BR>a patronymic of Vi-rocana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्रादि
प्राह्रादि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Vi-rocana and<BR>of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रिय|प्रियः
प्रिय प्रिय. See under rt. 1. प्री below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाल|प्रियालः
प्रियाल प्रियाल. See p. 662, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
प्री 1. प्री, cl. 9. (and 1 ?). P. A. प्रीणाति,<BR>प्रीणीते, प्रयति (?), -ते (?), पिप्राय, पि-<BR>प्रिये, प्रेष्यति, -ते, अप्रैषीत्, अप्रेष्ट, प्रेतुम्<BR>(Vedic forms are प्रीणाहि = प्रीणीहि, पिप्रीहि, अपि-<BR>प्रेस्, अपिप्रयत्, पिप्रयस्व), (P.) to please, de-<BR>light, gladden, cheer, regale; to act kindly to, show<BR>kindness to, show grace or favour to any one (with<BR>acc.); to take pleasure in, delight in (with gen. or<BR>loc.); to love; (A.) to be pleased or gratified, be<BR>glad or cheerful: Pass. प्रीयते (by some regarded<BR>as cl. 4. A.; ep. also P. प्रीयति), to be pleased or<BR>gratified, be glad or cheerful; to feel affection for,<BR>regard with affection, love; to be satisfied, assent:<BR>Caus. प्रीणयति (according to Siddhānta-kaum.<BR>p. 150 also प्रापयति, and according to Vopa-deva<BR>XVIII. 12 also प्राययति), -यितुम्, Aor. अपि-<BR>प्रीणत्, to give pleasure to, please, delight, gratify;<BR>to act kindly or graciously to, treat kindly: Desid.<BR>पिप्रीषति, -ते, Ved. to wish to please or propitiate:<BR>Intens. पेप्रीयते, पेप्रयीति, पेप्रेति; [cf. Zend<BR>frī, ‘to love, praise;’ fry-a, ‘beloved, a friend:’<BR>Gr. φίλο-ς, φιλέω fr. a rt. φιλ for φλι, πρᾷο-ς,<BR>πραΰ-ς (Ion. πρη-ΰ-ς), πρᾳ-ό-τη(τ)-ς, πραΰ-ν-ω:<BR>perhaps Lat. pla-ceo, pla-co, pius for prius (?),<BR>lœ-tus for plœ-tus (?), filius = प्रिय (?): Goth.<BR>fri-j-on, ‘to love;’ frijond-s, ‘a friend;’ fria-thva,<BR>‘love,’ = प्रिय-त्व; faihu-freiks, ‘money-lov-<BR>ing, avaricious:’ Old Germ. fra-o, frô, ‘joyful;’<BR>friunt, ‘a friend;’ fri-du, fri-da, ‘peace;’ friu-<BR>dil, fri-del, fre-del, ‘a minion, favourite:’ Old<BR>Slav. pri-ja-ti, ‘to provide;’ pri-ja-telu = Russ.<BR>prijāteli = Lith. prëteliu-s, ‘a friend:’ Cambro-<BR>Brit. prïawd.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रिय|प्रियः
प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, beloved, dear to (with gen.,<BR>loc., or dat.), dear, valued, amiable, agreeable, liked,<BR>desired, desirable, pleasing; customary, familiar,<BR>wonted, own (Ved., cf. φίλος); dear, expensive, high<BR>in price [cf. प्रिय-धान्यक, प्रियान्न-त्व];<BR>(mostly in comps.), loving, liking, kind, favourable,<BR>affectionate, fond of (also with loc.), attached to,<BR>addicted to [cf. अक्ष-प्˚, नर्तन-प्˚, पुरु-प्˚];<BR>(अस्), m. a lover, husband; (according to Kullūka on<BR>Manu III. 19) a son-in-law; a kind of deer [cf.<BR>प्रियक]; a species of medicinal plant, = वृद्धि;<BR>(आ), f. a mistress, wife; a woman; news, tidings,<BR>information; small cardamoms; Arabian jasmine;<BR>vinous or spirituous liquor; N. of various metres,<BR>four times ˘˘¯˘¯; a metre of four lines of which<BR>the first, third, and fourth are ¯¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯,<BR>and the second ˘¯ &c.; another variety of metre;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-c" target="_blank">Page0661-c+ 80</a>]<BR>(अम्), n. love; a service, kindness, favour; a pleasure;<BR>(अम्), ind. in an agreeable manner, in a pleasant<BR>way; (एण), ind. willingly, with pleasure, readily,<BR>gladly, pleasantly, agreeably (= प्रिय-प्रियेण).<BR>—प्रियं-वद, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking kindly or<BR>pleasantly, pleasant speaking, sweet speaking, agree-<BR>able; (अस्), m. a kind of bird; N. of the son of the<BR>chief of the Gandharvas; (आ), f. a kind of metre,<BR>four times ˘˘˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯; N. of a woman.<BR>—प्रिय-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing pleasure or en-<BR>joyment, giving pleasure.<BR>—प्रिय-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>one whose actions are kind, one who acts kindly,<BR>kind; (अ), n. the action of a lover.<BR>—प्रिय-क-<BR>लत्र, अस्, m. a man who is fond of his wife.<BR>—प्रिय-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of showing<BR>kindness to (with gen.), well-wishing, friendly dis-<BR>posed, benevolent.<BR>—प्रिय-काम्य, अस्, m. the<BR>plant Terminalia Tomentosa.<BR>—प्रिय-कार, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, doing a kindness to (with gen.), doing a<BR>favour or acting kindly towards, treating kindly,<BR>pleasing, gratifying; kind, favourable, affectionate;<BR>congenial, suiting.<BR>—प्रिय-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>causing love, causing pleasure or gladness, agreeable.<BR>—प्रिय-कारण, अम्, n. the act of doing a favour;<BR>(आत्), ind. for the sake of doing a favour.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>कारि-त्व, अम्, n. the act of showing kindness, kind<BR>treatment.<BR>—प्रिय-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, showing kind-<BR>ness to, acting kindly towards, doing what is pleasing,<BR>acting kindly.<BR>—प्रिय-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, doing a kind-<BR>ness; (त्), m. a friend, benefactor.<BR>—प्रियकृत्-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, giving the greatest pleasure, doing that<BR>which pleases most.<BR>—प्रिय-क्षत्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. ruling benevolently, governing propitiously<BR>(said of the gods; Sāy. = प्रीणयितृ-बल).<BR>—प्रि-<BR>य-गुड, अस्, आ, अम्, one to whom sugar is agree-<BR>able, fond of sugar.<BR>—प्रियङ्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>acting kindly or affectionately to, showing kindness<BR>to (with gen.); agreeable; exciting or attracting<BR>regard, amiable; (अस्), m., N. of a Dānava; N. of<BR>a man; (ई), f., N. of various plants (= बृहज्-<BR>जीवन्ती, श्वेत-कण्टकारी, अश्व-गन्धा).<BR>—प्रि-<BR>यङ्-करण, अस्, ई, अम्, acting kindly or affection-<BR>ately to; exciting or attracting regard, amiable.<BR>—प्रियङ्-कार, अस्, ई, अम्, = प्रिय-कार, q. v.<BR>—प्रिय-चतुर, अस्, आ, अम्, see Vopa-deva III.<BR>110.<BR>—प्रिय-चिकीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to do<BR>what is pleasing (to any one), desirous of pleasing.<BR>—प्रिय-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. dear when born,<BR>born beloved or desired; an epithet of Agni.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>जानि, इस्, m. a man who is fond of his wife.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>जीव, अस्, आ, अम्, one to whom life is dear, loving<BR>life, living long, long-lived; (अस्), m. the plant<BR>Calosanthes Indica.<BR>—प्रिय-जीवित, अस्, आ, अम्, lov-<BR>ing life.<BR>—प्रियजीवित-ता, f. love of life.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>तनु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. loving the body (?).<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most beloved, dearest; (अस्), m. a<BR>lover, husband; N. of a plant, Celosia Cristata, =<BR>मयूर-शिखा; (आ), f. a mistress, wife.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम्, dearer, more beloved, kinder; more<BR>expensive.<BR>—प्रियतर-त्व, अम्, n. the being dearer<BR>to any one (with loc.).<BR>—प्रिय-ता, f. or प्रिय-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. dearness, the being dear; the being fond of,<BR>affection, love.<BR>—प्रिय-तोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, satisfy-<BR>ing a lover; (अस्), m. a kind of coitus.<BR>—प्रिय-द,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, giving agreeable or desired objects; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Rhinacanthus Communis.<BR>—प्रिय-दत्ता,<BR>f. a mystical name of the earth; N. of a woman.<BR>—प्रिय-दर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasant or agree-<BR>able to look at, (opposed to दुर्-दर्श.)<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasant or grateful to the<BR>sight, good looking, lovely, handsome; (अम्), n.<BR>the look of a friend; (अस्), m. a parrot; a kind of<BR>date tree; Terminalia Tomentosa; Mimusops Kauki;<BR>a plant growing in wet weather on trees and stones,<BR>(in Marāṭhī called dagaḍaphūla, in Hindūstani<BR>پتهركى پهول); N. of a prince of the Gandharvas;<BR>of a son of Vāsuki; N. of a Kalpa; (ई), f. a kind<BR>of bird, Gracula Religiosa; (आ), f., N. of a daughter<BR>of Mahā-vīra.<BR>—प्रिय-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, looking<BR>with kindness (upon everything); an epithet of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-a" target="_blank">Page0662-a+ 81</a>]<BR>king Aśoka.<BR>—प्रिय-दास, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of a commentary on the Bhakta-mālā.<BR>—प्रिय-देवन, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of play or<BR>gambling.<BR>—प्रिय-धन्व, अस्, m. ‘fond of the<BR>bow,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—प्रिय-धा, ind., Ved.<BR>lovingly, kindly, affectionately.<BR>—प्रिय-धान्यक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. causing dearness of provisions,<BR>producing scarcity of corn, (opposed to सुभिक्ष-<BR>कारिन्.)<BR>—प्रिय-धाम, अस्, m., Ved. fond of<BR>home, loving the sacrificial enclosure; an epithet of<BR>Agni; (Sāy. = प्रिय-स्थान, fond of his station.)<BR>—प्रिय-धामन्, आ, m., Ved. = प्रिय-धाम, an<BR>epithet of Indra; (आनस्), m. pl. an epithet of the<BR>Ādityas.<BR>—प्रिय-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of the<BR>beloved or desired; (Mahī-dhara) = प्रियाणाम् पा-<BR>लकः.<BR>—प्रिय-पुत्र, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR>—प्रिय-प्रद, अस्, m., N. of an author of a<BR>Śāktamantra.<BR>—प्रिय-प्रसादन, अम्, n. the<BR>conciliation of a husband, reconciliation with any<BR>object of affection.<BR>—प्रियप्रसादन-व्रत, अम्,<BR>n. a vow for the reconciliation of a husband.<BR>—प्रिय-प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of life (=<BR>प्रियासु).<BR>—प्रिय-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, exceed-<BR>ingly kind or amiable; of pleasing speech, well-<BR>spoken, eloquent; (अम्), n. eloquence in language.<BR>—प्रिय-प्रियेण, ind. with pleasure, willingly,<BR>readily, gladly, pleasantly, agreeably.<BR>—प्रिय-प्रेप्-<BR>सु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of obtaining a beloved object,<BR>lamenting the loss or absence of any beloved object,<BR>grieving for an object of affection.<BR>—प्रिय-भाषण,<BR>अम्, n. speaking kindly, kind or friendly speech.<BR>—प्रिय-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking kindly; (इणी),<BR>f. a kind of bird, Gracula Religiosa.<BR>—प्रिय-मण्-<BR>डन, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of trinkets or ornaments.<BR>—प्रिय-मधु, उस्, m. ‘fond of wine,’ an epithet<BR>of Bala-rāma the half-brother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>मानस, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of the lake Mānasa (the<BR>Rāja-haṃsa or Royal-goose).<BR>—प्रिय-माल्यानुले-<BR>पन (˚य-अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of an attendant of<BR>Skanda.<BR>—प्रिय-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a mythical<BR>Cakra-vartin.<BR>—प्रिय-मेध, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi<BR>(a descendant of Aṅgiras and author of the hymns<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 1-40, 57, 58, 76, IX. 28);<BR>of a descendant of Aja-mīḍha; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>descendants of the Ṛṣi Priya-medha.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>मेध-स्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. praised by those who<BR>are fond of sacrifices, celebrated by pious priests;<BR>(Sāy. = प्रिय-यज्ञैर् ऋषिभिः स्तुतः.)<BR>—प्रि-<BR>यम्-भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, becoming dear, be-<BR>coming an object of affection.<BR>—प्रियम्भविष्णु-<BR>ता, f. or प्रियम्भविष्णु-त्व, अम्, n. the becom-<BR>ing an object of affection, amiability.<BR>—प्रियम्-<BR>भावुक, अस्, ई, अम्, one who has become dear,<BR>become an object of affection.<BR>—प्रियम्भावुक-<BR>ता, f. or प्रियम्भावुक-त्व, अम्, n. the having<BR>become dear or beloved, becoming beloved, amia-<BR>bility.<BR>—प्रिय-यज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of sacrifices,<BR>loving sacrifices.<BR>—प्रिय-रण, अस्, आ, अम्, delighting<BR>in war, warlike, martial.<BR>—प्रिय-रथ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing a favourite chariot, (Sāy. = प्रीयमाण-<BR>रथ-युक्त); (अस्), m., N. of a man (?).<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having an agreeable form.<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>वक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who speaks kindly or<BR>agreeably, flattering, a flatterer.<BR>—प्रिय-वचन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one whose words are kind or friendly,<BR>kindly spoken; (अस्), m. = भक्तिमान् रोगी; (अम्),<BR>n. kind or flattering speech, term of endearment,<BR>endearing expression.<BR>—प्रिय-वचस्, अस्, n. a kind<BR>or friendly speech.<BR>—प्रिय-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, con-<BR>taining the word प्रिय.<BR>—प्रिय-वयस्य, अस्,<BR>m. a dear friend.<BR>—प्रिय-वर्णी, f. = प्रियङ्गु, a<BR>creeping plant, Echites Frutescens.<BR>—प्रिय-वल्ली, f.<BR>a species of plant (= प्रियङ्गु, फलिनी).<BR>—प्रिय-<BR>वस्तु, n. a favourite object or topic.<BR>—प्रिय-वाक्-<BR>सहित, अस्, आ, अम्, accompanied by kind words.<BR>—प्रिय-वाच्, क्, f. kind or agreeable speech; (क्, क्,<BR>क्), one whose words are kind, kind in speech,<BR>affable in address.<BR>—प्रिय-वाद, अस्, m. kind or<BR>agreeable speech.<BR>—प्रिय-वादिका, f. a kind of<BR>musical instrument.<BR>—प्रियवादि-ता, f. speaking<BR>kindly, kindliness of speech.<BR>—प्रिय-वादिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-b" target="_blank">Page0662-b+ 81</a>]<BR>इ, speaking kindly or agreeably, speaking affection-<BR>ately, flattering, a flatterer; (इनी), f. a kind of bird,<BR>Gracula Religiosa.<BR>—प्रिय-विनाकृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>abandoned by a lover, deserted by a husband.<BR>—प्रि-<BR>य-विश्व, अस्, आ, अम्, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. I. 1, 29.<BR>—प्रिय-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. liking pious ob-<BR>servances, fond of obedience (said of the gods; Sāy.<BR>= प्रियाणि कर्माणि येषाम्); (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>king (a son of Manu and Śata-rūpā); N. of a priest.<BR>—प्रिय-शालक, अस्, m. the plant Terminalia To-<BR>mentosa; (also spelt प्रिय-सालक.)<BR>—प्रिय-श्र-<BR>वस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, loving glory; an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—प्रिय-स, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. granting desired ob-<BR>jects; (according to Sāy. प्रियसासः = प्रियतमा<BR>धाराः.)<BR>—प्रिय-संवास, अस्, m. the society of<BR>a beloved object, the society of loved persons.<BR>—प्रि-<BR>य-सख, अस्, आ, अम्, one to whom friends are<BR>dear, loving friends; (अस्), m. a dear friend; the tree<BR>Acacia Catechu, = खदिर; (ई), f. a dear female<BR>friend, a female friend or companion, a confidante.<BR>—प्रिय-सङ्गमन, अम्, n. ‘the meeting of<BR>friends,’ N. of a place in which Indra and Viṣṇu<BR>are said to have met with their parents Aditi and<BR>Kaśyapa.<BR>—प्रिय-सत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasant and<BR>true; (अम्), n. speech at once pleasing and true,<BR>eloquent and truthful discourse.<BR>—प्रिय-सन्तति, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, having a beloved son.<BR>—प्रिय-सन्देश, अस्,<BR>m. a tree with fragrant flowers, Michelia Champaca.<BR>—प्रिय-समागम, अस्, m. reunion with a beloved<BR>object.<BR>—प्रिय-समुचित, अस्, आ, अम्, befitting<BR>or becoming a lover.<BR>—प्रिय-सहचरी, f. a dear<BR>female companion, beloved wife.<BR>—प्रिय-सालक, अस्,<BR>m. = प्रिय-शालक, q. v.<BR>—प्रिय-सुहृद्, त्, m. a<BR>dear friend, kind or good friend.<BR>—प्रिय-स्तोत्र,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fond of praise; (Sāy. = प्रियाणि<BR>स्तोत्राणि यस्य.)<BR>—प्रिय-स्वप्न, अस्, आ, अम्, fond<BR>of sleep, sluggish.<BR>—प्रियाख्य (˚य-आख्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, called ‘dear,’ a lover, mistress; announcing<BR>good tidings<BR>—प्रियाख्यान (˚य-आख्˚), अम्, n.<BR>agreeable news, pleasant tidings.<BR>—प्रियाख्यान-<BR>पुरःसर, अस्, आ, अम्, preceded by agreeable<BR>news, preceded by pleasant tidings.<BR>—प्रिया-जन,<BR>अस्, m. any dear or beloved female.<BR>—प्रियातिथि<BR>(˚य-अत्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, fond of guests, a lover of<BR>guests, hospitable.<BR>—प्रियात्मन् (˚य-आत्˚), आ, आ,<BR>अ, of a pleasant nature, agreeable, pleasant.<BR>—प्रिया-<BR>धान (˚य-आध्˚), अम्, n. a friendly office, good<BR>service.<BR>—प्रियान्न (˚य-अन्˚), अम्, n. expensive<BR>food, dear provisions.<BR>—प्रियान्न-त्व, अम्, n. dear-<BR>ness of provisions, dearth, scarcity.<BR>—प्रियापय<BR>(˚य-अप्˚), अस्, m. the absence of a beloved object.<BR>—प्रियाप्रिय (˚य-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, agreeable and<BR>disagreeable, pleasant and unpleasant.<BR>—प्रियाम्बु<BR>(˚य-अम्˚), उस्, उस्, उ, fond of water; (उस्), m. the<BR>mango tree.<BR>—प्रियार्थम् (˚य-अर्˚), ind. for the<BR>sake of a beloved object.<BR>—प्रियार्ह (˚य-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, deserving love, amiable.<BR>—प्रिया-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. having a mistress, enamoured, being<BR>in love with.<BR>—प्रियासु (˚य-असु), उस्, उस्, उ, fond<BR>of life (= प्रिय-प्राण).<BR>—प्रियासूय-मती (˚य-<BR>अस्˚), f., N. of a woman.<BR>—प्रियैषिन् (˚य-एष्˚),<BR>ई, इणी, इ, wishing to please, friendly, affectionate.<BR>—प्रियोक्ति (˚य-उक्˚), इस्, f. friendly speech.<BR>—प्रियोदित (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, well or kindly<BR>spoken, pleasingly uttered; (अम्), n. kind or gentle<BR>speech.<BR>—प्रियोपपत्ति (˚य-उप्˚), इस्, f. a happy<BR>event or circumstance, pleasant occurrence.<BR>—प्रियो-<BR>पभोग (˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m. the enjoyment of a<BR>lover or of a mistress.<BR>—प्रियोपभोग-बन्ध्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, barren or destitute of the enjoyment of a<BR>lover.<BR>—प्रियोस्रिय (˚य-उस्˚), अस्, m., Ved. loving<BR>cows, amorous (said of a bull).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियक|प्रियकः
प्रियक, अस्, m. a kind of variegated or spotted<BR>deer; a kind of bird; a bee; N. of several plants,<BR>Nauclea Cadamba; Terminalia Tomentosa; saffron;<BR>= प्रियङ्गु, a kind of tree; N. of an attendant on<BR>Skanda; N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्गु|प्रियंगु|प्रियंगुः|प्रियङ्गुः
प्रियङ्गु, उस्, उस्, m. f. panic seed, Panicum<BR>Italicum; a medicinal plant and perfume, commonly<BR>called Priyaṅgu and described in some places as a fra-<BR>grant seed (= फलिनी); Italian millet; long pepper;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">Page0662-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Sinapis Ramosa, = कटुकी; (अम्), n. saffron.<BR>—प्रि-<BR>यङ्गु-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of a country.<BR>—प्रियङ्गु-<BR>श्यामा, f., N. of the wife of Naravāhana-datta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाकृ
प्रिया-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to act kindly towards, treat kindly (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाल|प्रियालः
प्रियाल, अस्, m. the tree Buchanania Latifolia (com-<BR>monly called Piyāl, = पियाल, तापस-प्रिय); (आ), f.<BR>a vine, a bunch of grapes (= द्राक्षा).<BR>—प्रियाल-<BR>ताल-खर्जूर-हरीतकी-विभीतक, आस्, m. pl. piyāl,<BR>palm, date and yellow and beleric myrobalan trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
2. प्री, ईस्, ईस्, इ, in अध-प्री, कध-प्री, घृत-<BR>प्री, &c., q. q. v. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीण|प्रीणः
1. प्रीण, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see s. v.), pleased, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणन|प्रीणनं
प्रीणन, अस्, आ, अम्, pleasing, gratifying, appeas-<BR>ing, allaying, soothing; (अम्), n. the act of pleasing<BR>or delighting, gladdening, satisfying, satisfaction,<BR>satiety; a means of gladdening or satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणयित्वा
प्रीणयित्वा, ind. having pleased or propitiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणित
प्रीणित, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, gratified, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीत|प्रीतः
प्रीत, अस्, आ, अम्, pleased, delighted, gladdened,<BR>satisfied; joyful, content; happy, glad; dear, be-<BR>loved, loved; gracious, kind, affectionate; (अम्), n.<BR>pleasure, delight; jest, mirth.<BR>—प्रित-तर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, more highly pleased, much gratified.<BR>—प्रीत-<BR>मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, pleased in mind, gratified in<BR>mind.<BR>—प्रीतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, pleased in<BR>mind, rejoiced in spirit, pleased, satisfied, content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीति|प्रीतिः
प्रीति, इस्, f. any pleasurable sensation, pleasure,<BR>joy, gladness, happiness; enjoyment, gratification, sa-<BR>tisfaction [cf. आत्म-प्˚]; graciousness, grace, favour,<BR>favourableness, kindness, propitiousness; friendly<BR>disposition, liking, fondness for, delighting in, friend-<BR>liness, amity, regard, harmony, affection, love; con-<BR>ciliation; Joy or Gratification personified as a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa; Love personified as wife of<BR>Kāma-deva; the second of the twenty-seven astro-<BR>nomical Yogas; N. of the thirteenth Kalā of the<BR>moon; a symbolical expression for the letter ध्;<BR>प्रीत्या, ind. in a friendly way, amicably, peaceably.<BR>—प्रीति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing pleasure; inspiring<BR>love or affection; pleasing, agreeable.<BR>—प्रीति-क-<BR>रण, अम्, n. the act of causing pleasure, gratifying.<BR>—प्रीति-कर्मन्, अ, n. an act of friendship or<BR>love; kind action.<BR>—प्रीति-कूट, N. of a village.<BR>—प्रीति-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—प्रीति-<BR>जुषा, f., N. of the wife of A-niruddha.<BR>—प्रीति-<BR>तृष्, ट्, m. a N. of the god of love.<BR>—प्रीति-द,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, giving pleasure; inspiring love or regard,<BR>affectionate; (अस्), m. a jester or buffoon in a play,<BR>the Vidūṣaka.<BR>—प्रीति-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, given<BR>through love or affection; (अम्), n. (?), property or<BR>valuables presented to a female by her relations and<BR>friends at the time of her marriage, and constituting<BR>part of her peculiar property.<BR>—प्रीति-दान, अम्, n.<BR>or प्रीति-दाय, अस्, m. ‘gift of love,’ a present<BR>made from love or affection, a kind or friendly<BR>present, token of affection.<BR>—प्रीति-धन, अम्, n.<BR>money given from love or friendship.<BR>—प्रीति-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. an object of affection, a beloved person or<BR>thing.<BR>—प्रीति-पुरोग, अस्, आ, अम्, preceded by<BR>affection, affectionate, loving.<BR>—प्रीति-पूर्वम् or<BR>प्रीति-पूर्वकम्, ind. with the accompaniment of<BR>kindness, kindly, graciously, affectionately, in an af-<BR>fectionate manner.<BR>—प्रीति-प्रमुख, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>preceded by kindness (= प्रीति-पूर्वक), kind,<BR>friendly.<BR>—प्रीतिप्रमुख-वचन, अम्, n. a speech<BR>preceded by affection, affectionate words, kind speech<BR>(= प्रीति-पूर्वकाणि वचनानि or according to others<BR>= स्नेह-प्रधान-वचनम्, speech principally<BR>characterized by affection).<BR>—प्रीति-भाज्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>enjoying friendship, receiving friendly offices.<BR>—प्री-<BR>ति-भोज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eaten joyfully or cheer-<BR>fully.<BR>—प्रीति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having pleasurable<BR>sensations, pleased, gratified; having love or affection<BR>for (with loc. or gen.), full of affection, loving, fond,<BR>affectionate, kind; favourable; (अती), f. a kind of<BR>metre consisting of four lines, alternately ˘¯˘¯¯<BR>˘˘¯˘¯¯ and ¯¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯.<BR>—प्रीति-म-<BR>नस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, joyous-minded, joyful-hearted,<BR>pleased in mind, content, happy; kind, affectionate.<BR>—प्रीति-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made up of affection,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">Page0663-a+ 79</a>]<BR>arising from affection or joy.<BR>—प्रीति-वचस्, अस्, n.<BR>kind or friendly words, gracious or kindly speech.<BR>—प्रीति-वाद, अस्, m. a friendly discussion.<BR>—प्रीति-<BR>विवाह, अस्, m. a love-marriage, love-match.<BR>—प्री-<BR>ति-विश्रम्भ-भाजन, अम्, n. a repository of<BR>affection and confidence.<BR>—प्रीति-श्राद्ध, अम्, n.<BR>a funeral offering to the Manes of both parents<BR>performed for the eldest surviving son, and to be<BR>re-performed at some other period by this son in<BR>person.<BR>—प्रीति-सङ्गति, इस्, f. a covenant of friend-<BR>ship, friendly alliance.<BR>—प्रीति-स्निग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>moist through love or charming through affection<BR>(said of the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0662-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीयमाण
प्रीयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being pleased or pro-<BR>pitiated; being glad or joyful; being dear or beloved;<BR>kind, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेणा
प्रेणा, a shortened form for प्रेम्णा, inst. of<BR>प्रेमन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेणि
प्रेणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. gladdening, delighting, one<BR>who delights (by praises); (Sāy.) = प्रेरयितृ, in-<BR>citing, instigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतृ
प्रेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who loves or cherishes,<BR>a benefactor; (Sāy.) = तर्पयितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेम
प्रेम, अस्, आ, अम्, = प्रेमन्, love, affection,<BR>(at the end of adj. comps.; cf. स-प्˚); (आ), f. =<BR>प्रेमन् (in प्रेमा-बन्ध); a kind of metre<BR>consisting of four lines (the first, second, and fourth<BR>being ¯¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯ and the third ˘¯˘¯¯<BR>&c.).<BR>—प्रेमा-बन्ध = प्रेम-बन्ध, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमन्
प्रेमन्, आ, अ, m. n. love, affection, kindness,<BR>tender regard, favour; sport, pastime; joy, glad-<BR>ness, pleasure; (आ), m. a jest, joke; wind, air;<BR>an epithet of Indra; N. of various men; प्रेम्णा<BR>(Ved. also प्रेणा), ind. through love or affection.<BR>—प्रेम-तत्त्व-निरूपण, अम्, n., N. of a Bengālī<BR>poem by Kṛṣṇa-dāsa.<BR>—प्रेम-नारायण, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king (= प्रेम-साहि).<BR>—प्रेम-पर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, intent on love, filled with affection, affec-<BR>tionate, loving, constant.<BR>—प्रेम-पातन, अम्, n.<BR>defluxion of rheum or of tears.<BR>—प्रेम-पात्र, अम्,<BR>n. an object of affection, a beloved person or thing.<BR>—प्रेम-बन्ध, अस्, m. or प्रेम-बन्धन,<BR>अम्, n. ‘love-bond,’ the ties of love, love.<BR>—प्रेम-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. state of affection, love.<BR>—प्रेम-राशी-<BR>भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to become (as<BR>it were) one mass of affection.<BR>—प्रेमर्द्धि (˚म-<BR>ऋ˚), इस्, f. increase of affection, ardent love.<BR>—प्रेम-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, full of love, affectionate; (अती), f.<BR>a mistress.<BR>—प्रेम-विश्वास-भूमि, इस्, f. an object<BR>of love and confidence.<BR>—प्रेम-सागर, अस्, m. an<BR>ocean of love.<BR>—प्रेम-साहि, इस्, m. (fr. प्रेमन्<BR>+ साहि = شاه) = प्रेम-नारायण.<BR>—प्रेमामृत<BR>(˚म-अम्˚), अम्, n. ‘love-ambrosia,’ N. of a metrical<BR>list of 112 names of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—प्रेमाश्रु (˚म-<BR>अश्˚), उ, n. a tear of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमिन्
प्रेमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, loving, affectionate, friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयस्
प्रेयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. fr. प्रिय), dearer,<BR>very dear, more agreeable, more desired; dearest,<BR>most beloved; kinder, more affectionate; (आन्), m.<BR>a lover, husband; (असी), f. a mistress, wife; (आन्, अस्),<BR>m. n. (in rhetoric) flattery.<BR>—प्रेयस्-कर, अस्, m. the<BR>hand of a lover.<BR>—प्रेयस्-ता, f. or प्रेयस्-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the being dearer, being very dear.<BR>—प्रेयो-ऽपत्य,<BR>अस्, m. ‘very fond of offspring,’ a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्ठ|प्रेष्ठः
प्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. fr. प्रिय), dearest,<BR>very dear, most beloved, greatly beloved, most<BR>agreeable, most desired; (अस्), m. a lover, husband;<BR>(आ), f. a mistress, wife; a leg.<BR>—प्रेष्ठ-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dearest, most beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीण|प्रीणः
प्रीण 2. प्रीण, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. प्र), old,<BR>ancient, former (= प्रण, पुराण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतु
प्रीतु प्रीतु, उस्, m. a bird (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रु
प्रु प्रु [cf. rt. प्लु], cl. 1. A. प्रवते,<BR>पुप्रुवे, &c., to spring up, jump up; to go,<BR>move: Caus. प्रावयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अपुप्रवत्,<BR>अपिप्रवत्, to reach to, extend as far as (with acc.):<BR>Desid. of Caus. पुप्रावयिषति, पिप्रावयिषति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुत्
प्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, moving, going, (at the end of comps.;<BR>cf. अन्तरिक्ष-प्˚, उद-प्˚, उपरि-प्˚, कृष्ण-प्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुथ्
प्रुथ् प्रुथ्, by some regarded as the<BR>proper form of rt. प्रोथ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्
प्रुष् 1. प्रुष् [cf. rt. प्लुष्], cl. 5. 9. 10.<BR>P. A. प्रुष्णोति, प्रुष्णुते, प्रुष्णाति,<BR>प्रुष्णीते, प्रुषायति, -ते, प्रोषितुम्, Ved. to<BR>scatter or sprinkle down in drops, rain, shower,<BR>wet, moisten (in these senses probably fr. प्र +<BR>उक्ष्; Sāy. = सिच्); cl. 9. P. प्रुष्णाति, to become<BR>moist or wet, become unctuous; to pour out, sprinkle,<BR>shed, discharge; to fill; cl. 1. P. प्रोषति, to burn (in<BR>this sense probably fr. प्र + 1. उष्); [cf. Old Germ.<BR>frus, ‘to be cold;’ Mod. Germ. frieren, Frost.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्
2. प्रुष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, sprinkling, (at the end of comps.;<BR>cf. अभ्र-प्˚, घृत-प्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुषित
प्रुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled, wetted, moist-<BR>ened; burning, consuming; (Sāy.) = दग्धुम् प्र-<BR>वृत्तः.<BR>—प्रुषित-प्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. of a<BR>speckled or dappled aspect, piebald, of a varied hue<BR>(said of the horses of the Aśvins and of Indra; Sāy.<BR>= विचित्र-रूप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्ट|प्रुष्टः
प्रुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, burnt, consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्टाय
प्रुष्टाय, Nom. A. प्रुष्टायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>sprinkle; (probably incorrectly for प्रुष्वाय below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्व|प्रुष्वः
प्रुष्व, अस्, m. the rainy season, the rains; the<BR>sun; (आ), f., Ved. a drop of water, a frozen drop<BR>of water, hoar-frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्वाय
प्रुष्वाय, Nom. A. प्रुष्वायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>fall in drops, trickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष|प्रोषः
प्रोष, अस्, m. burning, combustion; [cf. प्लोष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषक
प्रोषक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रू
प्रू प्रू in कट-प्रू, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रे
प्रे प्रे (प्र-इ, see rt. 5. इ), cl. 2. P. प्रैति,<BR>प्रैतुम् (Ved. प्रेषे), to go forth, come forth,<BR>appear (Ved.); to go on, proceed (especially as a<BR>sacrifice, Ved.); to go forwards, go farther; to go<BR>to, come to, arrive at, attain, reach; to go out; to<BR>depart (this life), die: Intens. प्रेयते, Ved. to drive<BR>or go forth (in a chariot, said of Uṣas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत|प्रेतः
प्रेत, अस्, आ, अम्, departed, deceased, dead, de-<BR>funct, a dead person; (अस्), m. the spirit of a de-<BR>parted person, departed spirit, spirit abiding in the<BR>lower world, the spirit before obsequial rites are<BR>performed; a ghost, an evil being (especially one ani-<BR>mating the carcases of the dead).<BR>—प्रेत-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. an obsequial act or rite, funeral rites.<BR>—प्रेत-<BR>कल्प, अस्, m. ‘obsequial ordinance,’ N. of the<BR>second part of the Garuḍa-Purāṇa.<BR>—प्रेत-कार्य,<BR>अम्, n. or प्रेत-कृत्य, अम्, आ, n. f. an obsequial<BR>or funeral rite, obsequial ceremonies in honour of<BR>the dead or of deceased ancestors.<BR>—प्रेत-गत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, gone to the departed, dead.<BR>—प्रेत-गृह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘house of the dead,’ a burying ground.<BR>—प्रे-<BR>त-गोप, अस्, m. the Keeper of the dead.<BR>—प्रेत-<BR>चारिन्, ई, m. ‘roaming among the dead,’ Śiva.<BR>—प्रे-<BR>त-त्व, अम्, n. the state of a departed spirit, the being<BR>dead.<BR>—प्रेत-दाह, अस्, m. the burning of the<BR>dead.<BR>—प्रेत-धूम, अस्, m. ‘smoke of the dead,’<BR>the smoke of a funeral pile; (according to Kullūka<BR>= दह्यमान-शव-धूम.)<BR>—प्रेत-नदी, f.<BR>the river of the dead (= वैतरणी, q. v.).<BR>—प्रेत-<BR>नर, अस्, m. a dead man, a corpse, a ghost.<BR>—प्रेत-निर्यातक or प्रेत-निर्हारक, अस्, m. a<BR>man employed to carry forth dead bodies; a kinsman<BR>who does so.<BR>—प्रेत-पक्ष or प्रेत-पक्षक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘half-month of the departed, i. e. of the<BR>Manes,’ N. of the dark half in the Gauṇa Āśvina<BR>(so called as peculiarly appointed for the celebration<BR>of obsequial rites to the Pitṛs or Manes; = पितृ-<BR>पक्ष).<BR>—प्रेत-पटह, अस्, m. ‘drum of the<BR>dead,’ a drum beaten at a funeral.<BR>—प्रेत-पति, इस्,<BR>m. ‘lord or ruler of the dead,’ an epithet of Yama.<BR>—प्रेत-पात्र, अम्, n. ‘vessel of the dead,’ a vessel<BR>used in obsequial presentations.<BR>—प्रेत-पुर, अम्,<BR>n. the city of the dead, the abode of Yama.<BR>—प्रेत-<BR>प्रसाधन, अम्, n. the laying out of a corpse.<BR>—प्रेत-भक्षिणी, f., N. of a goddess.<BR>—प्रेत-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the state of the departed, the being<BR>dead; संसिद्धः प्रेत-भावाय, ready to die.<BR>—प्रेतभाव-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the state<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">Page0663-c+ 80</a>]<BR>of the departed, dead.<BR>—प्रेत-भूमि, इस्, f. a place<BR>in which the dead are burned or buried, a cemetery.<BR>—प्रेत-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a section of the Garuḍa-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—प्रेत-मेध, अस्, m. a sacrifice to the<BR>dead, funeral sacrifice.<BR>—प्रेत-मोक्ष, अस्, m., N.<BR>of the twenty-eighth chapter of the Māgha-mā-<BR>hātmya.<BR>—प्रेत-राक्षसी, f. a various reading for<BR>अपेत-राक्षसी, = तुलसी.<BR>—प्रेत-राज, अस्, m.<BR>‘king of the dead,’ an epithet of Yama.<BR>—प्रेत-लोक,<BR>अस्, m. the world of the dead, the region of disem-<BR>bodied spirits (in which they remain for one year<BR>or until the obsequial rites are completed).<BR>—प्रेत-<BR>वत्, ind. as if dead, as in the case of the dead.<BR>—प्रेत-वन, अम्, n. ‘grove of the dead,’ a place<BR>where bodies are burnt or buried, a cemetery.<BR>—प्रे-<BR>त-वाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, impelled or possessed by an<BR>evil spirit.<BR>—प्रेत-शरीर, अम्, n. the body which<BR>accompanies a departed spirit.<BR>—प्रेत-शिला, f. ‘stone<BR>of the dead,’ N. of a stone near Gayā, on which<BR>funeral cakes were offered.<BR>—प्रेत-शुद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>or प्रेत-शौच, अम्, n. purification after the death<BR>of a kinsman.<BR>—प्रेत-श्राद्ध, अम्, n. obsequial<BR>ceremonies offered to a departed relative during the<BR>year of his demise (fifteen are said to be required).<BR>—प्रेत-हार, अस्, m. one who carries out the dead,<BR>a near kinsman.<BR>—प्रेताधिप (˚त-अध्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord or ruler of the dead,’ an epithet of Yama.<BR>—प्रेताधिपति (˚त-अध्˚), इस्, m., Ved. the lord of<BR>the dead, ruler of departed spirits.<BR>—प्रेतान्न (˚त-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. food offered to the Manes or distributed<BR>on a person's death.<BR>—प्रेतावास (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘habitation of the dead,’ a burial ground, cemetery.<BR>—प्रेतास्थि (˚त-अस्˚), इ, n. the bone of a dead<BR>man.<BR>—प्रेतास्थि-धारिन्, ई, m. ‘wearing dead men's<BR>bones,’ an epithet of Rudra (Śiva).<BR>—प्रेतेश (˚त-ईश)<BR>or प्रेतेश्वर (˚त-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the dead,’<BR>an epithet of Yama.<BR>—प्रेतोद्देश (˚त-उद्˚), अस्,<BR>m. an offering to the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेति|प्रेतिः
प्रेति, इस्, f., Ved. departure, flight.<BR>—प्रेति-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing the word प्रेति or a<BR>form of प्रे.<BR>—प्रेतीषणि (˚ति-इष्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>striving to move forwards (an epithet of Agni; Sāy.<BR>= प्राप्त-गमन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतिक|प्रेतिकः
प्रेतिक, अस्, m. the soul of a deceased person, a<BR>spirit, ghost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्य
प्रेत्य, ind. having departed, having died, after<BR>death, in the next world, in the life to come.<BR>—प्रेत्य-जाति, इस्, f. rank or position in the world<BR>to come.<BR>—प्रेत्य-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, obtaining after<BR>death, enjoying the fruits of anything in the next<BR>world.<BR>—प्रेत्य-भाव, अस्, m. the state after death,<BR>condition of the soul after death, future state.<BR>—प्रे-<BR>त्यभाविक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the state after<BR>death, (opposed to ऐहलौकिक; probably an incor-<BR>rect form for प्रैत्यभाविक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्वन्
प्रेत्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, straying about (as cattle); (आ),<BR>m. wind, air; an epithet of Indra; [cf. प्रेर्त्वन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहिकटा
प्रेहि-कटा, f. (प्रेहि, 2nd sing. impv. of प्रे +<BR>कट), a rite in which no mats are allowed (see<BR>Gaṇa Mayūra-vyaṃsakādi to Pāṇ. II. 1, 72).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहिकर्दमा
प्रेहि-कर्दमा, f. a rite in which no impurity<BR>of any kind is allowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहिद्वितीया
प्रेहि-द्वितीया, f. a rite at which no second person<BR>is allowed to be present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहिवाणिजा
प्रेहि-वाणिजा, f. a rite at which no merchants are<BR>allowed to be present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेकीय
प्रेकीय प्रेकीय (fr. प्र + एक), Nom. P. प्रे-<BR>कीयति, -यितुम्, = प्रैकीय; see Vopa-deva II. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्
प्रेक्ष् प्रेक्ष् (प्र-ईक्ष्), cl. 1. A. प्रेक्षते,<BR>प्रेक्षितुम्, to look towards, look at, view, see,<BR>behold, regard, observe; to look on (without inter-<BR>fering), allow, suffer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षक|प्रेक्षकः
प्रेक्षक, अस्, इका, अम्, looking at, viewing,<BR>beholding, seeing, surveying, intending to view;<BR>(अस्), m. a looker, spectator, beholder, surveyor,<BR>member of an audience.<BR>—प्रेक्षकेरित (˚क-ईर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, uttered by a spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षण|प्रेक्षणं
प्रेक्षण, अम्, n. looking at, viewing, seeing,<BR>regarding, being a spectator; visiting; looking wan-<BR>tonly; the eye; any public show or spectacle; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">Page0664-a+ 80</a>]<BR>sight; a place where public exhibitions are held.<BR>—प्रेक्षण-कूट, अस्, अम्, m. n. the eye-ball, the<BR>pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0663-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणक|प्रेक्षणकं
प्रेक्षणक, अस्, इका, अम्, looking at, viewing,<BR>a spectator; (अम्), n. a spectacle, show, a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणिक
प्रेक्षणिक, अस्, ई, अम्, looking at, one who looks<BR>at or views; (आ), f. a woman fond of seeing shows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणीय
प्रेक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be seen or viewed,<BR>to be beheld or gazed at, visible, apparent, conspi-<BR>cuous [cf. दुष्-प्˚]; worth seeing, worthy of being<BR>looked at, beautiful to the view, sightly; to be re-<BR>garded as, resembling, looking or appearing like.<BR>—प्रेक्षणीय-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most worthy of<BR>being seen, most sightly.<BR>—प्रेक्षणीय-तर, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, more worthy of being seen, more sightly,<BR>more conspicuous.<BR>—प्रेक्षणीय-ता, f. sightliness,<BR>conspicuousness, beautifulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणीयक|प्रेक्षणीयकं
प्रेक्षणीयक, अस्, इका, अम्, visible, apparent,<BR>conspicuous; (अम्), n. a play, spectacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षत्
प्रेक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, looking at, beholding,<BR>regarding, observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षमाण
प्रेक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking at, looking on,<BR>viewing, beholding, regarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षा
प्रेक्षा, f. looking at, viewing, beholding, ob-<BR>serving, seeing, regarding, (sometimes at the end of<BR>a comp., e. g. धर्म-प्रेक्ष, regarding or con-<BR>sidering the law; cf. मुख-प्˚); sight, view, look,<BR>aspect, appearance; being a spectator, seeing a play<BR>or dance; any public show or spectacle, a sight; a<BR>play, dancing; conceiving, conception, understand-<BR>ing, intellect; circumspection, consideration; reflec-<BR>tion, deliberation; the branch of a tree.<BR>—प्रेक्षा-<BR>गार (˚षा-अग्˚ or ˚षा-आग्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. or<BR>प्रेक्षा-गृह, अम्, n. ‘spectacle-house,’ any build-<BR>ing erected for a show, temporary structure consisting<BR>of stalls for spectators, a play-house.<BR>—प्रेक्षा-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessed of circumspection, considerate,<BR>wise, prudent.<BR>—प्रेक्षा-समाज, अस्, m. an assembly<BR>at a spectacle, crowd at a theatre; (according to<BR>Kullūka = नृत्यादि-स्थान-जन-समृद्धि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षित
प्रेक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, looked at, viewed, beheld,<BR>seen; (अम्), n. a look, glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षितृ
प्रेक्षितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who looks on, a<BR>spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षिन्
प्रेक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, looking at, viewing, regarding;<BR>watching narrowly, scrutinizing [cf. मुख-प्˚];<BR>having the eyes or glance of [cf. मृग-प्˚, वृक-प्˚];<BR>जिह्म-प्रेक्षिन्, looking aside, looking askance.<BR>—प्रेक्षि-त्व, अम्, n. the act of watching nar-<BR>rowly, scrutinizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्य
1. प्रेक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be looked at, to be<BR>regarded or observed [cf. दुष्-प्˚]; to be seen,<BR>visible, apparent, brilliantly conspicuous; to be looked<BR>at patiently, to be suffered or endured; worthy of being<BR>seen, sightly, conspicuous; N. of a Śabdālaṅkāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्य
2. प्रेक्ष्य, ind. having looked at, having beheld<BR>or observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्यमाण
प्रेक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being looked at or<BR>beheld, being seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्ख्|प्रेंख्
प्रेङ्ख् प्रेङ्ख् (प्र-ईङ्ख्), cl. 1. P. प्रेङ्खति,<BR>प्रेङ्खितुम्, to tremble, shake, quiver, oscillate,<BR>vibrate: Caus. प्रेङ्खयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>oscillate or vibrate, swing (trans.), shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्ख|प्रेंखं|प्रेंखः|प्रेङ्खः
प्रेङ्ख, अस्, आ, अम्, trembling, shaking, vibrating,<BR>oscillating, swinging (Ved.); (अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n.<BR>a swing, a sort of hammock or swinging cot (either<BR>for travelling or diversion); नकुलस्य वामदे-<BR>वस्य प्रेङ्खः and मरुताम् प्रेङ्खः, N. of<BR>two Sāmans; (आ), f. dancing; wandering, travelling<BR>about, roaming (?); a particular pace of a horse.<BR>—प्रेङ्खेङ्खन (˚ख-ईङ्˚), अम्, n. swinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खण|प्रेंखण
प्रेङ्खण, अस्, आ, अम्, wandering, moving or<BR>going towards, entering; (अम्), n. swinging; a swing;<BR>a minor drama in one act; going, wandering (?).<BR>—प्रेङ्खण-कारिका, f. a female swinger or dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खणीय
प्रेङ्खणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be swung or made<BR>to oscillate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खत्
प्रेङ्खत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shaking, moving, oscil-<BR>lating, vibrating; wandering (?); diffusing (?);<BR>touching (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खयत्
प्रेङ्खयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, swinging (trans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खित|प्रेंखित|प्रेङ्खितं
प्रेङ्खित, अस्, आ, अम्, swung, shaken, set in<BR>motion, made to oscillate; being in contact with (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलन|प्रेंखोलनं|प्रेङ्खोलनं
प्रेङ्खोलन, अम्, n. swinging, shaking, oscil-<BR>lating; a swing, swing-cot or hammock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलय
प्रेङ्खोलय, Nom. P. प्रेङ्खोलयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to swing, shake; [cf. अन्दोलय, आन्दोलय, हिन्दो-<BR>लय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्गण
प्रेङ्गण प्रेङ्गण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. इङ्ग् with<BR>प्र), see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेड्
प्रेड् प्रेड् (प्र-ईड्), cl. 2. A. प्रेट्टे, प्रेडितुम्,<BR>Ved. to implore, supplicate; praise, celebrate; (Sāy.<BR>= प्रकर्षेण स्तु, to praise greatly, celebrate ex-<BR>ceedingly.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेडक
प्रेडक प्रेडक, an incorrect form for प्रे-<BR>रक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेणि
प्रेणि प्रेणि. See p. 663, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत|प्रेतः
प्रेत प्रेत, &c. See under प्रे, p. 663, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेद्ध
प्रेद्ध प्रेद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. इन्ध् with<BR>प्र), Ved. kindled, lighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेन्
प्रेन् प्रेन् (प्र-इन्), cl. 8. P. प्रेनोति, &c.,<BR>Ved. to send forth, impel forwards or upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेन्वन
प्रेन्वन प्रेन्वन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. इन्व् with<BR>प्र), see Vārttika II. to Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेन्वनीय
प्रेन्वनीय, see Vārttika II. to Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सा
प्रेप्सा प्रेप्सा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt. आप् with<BR>प्र), the wish to attain, desire of obtaining, desire,<BR>longing for; supposition, assumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सु
प्रेप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to attain, desirous of<BR>obtaining, wishing, seeking, longing for (with acc.);<BR>aiming at, having in view; supposing, assuming;<BR>anxious to rescue or save; तत्-प्रेप्सु, उस्, m. (in<BR>Ved. gram.) epithet of a particular form of the<BR>Desiderative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमन्
प्रेमन् प्रेमन्, &c. See p. 663, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयस्
प्रेयस् प्रेयस्. See p. 663, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्
प्रेर् प्रेर् (प्र-ईर्), cl. 2. A. प्रेर्ते, प्रेरि-<BR>तुम्, to move, come forward, come forth, go forth,<BR>rise, appear (Ved.): Caus. P. प्रेरयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to set in motion, cause to move forwards, move; to<BR>drive forwards, push on, drive onwards, urge or<BR>press forwards; to urge on, force on, hasten, stimu-<BR>late, incite, excite; to send forth, dismiss, dispatch;<BR>to send; to direct towards; to utter; to ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरक
प्रेरक, अस्, इका, अम्, setting in motion, urging<BR>on, impelling, inciting, stimulating, exciting; sending.<BR>—प्रेरक-त्व, अम्, n. the act of setting in motion,<BR>urging on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरण|प्रेरणं
प्रेरण, अम्, n. driving on [cf. पशु-प्˚]; (अम्,<BR>आ), n. f. the act of urging on, inciting, driving,<BR>instigating; impulse, passion; sending, dispatching,<BR>directing, ordering, order, direction, commanding;<BR>activity, action; the sense of the causal verb, [cf.<BR>Vopa-deva XVIII. 1.]<BR>—प्रेरणार्थ (˚ण-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the sense of inciting or of the<BR>causal verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरणीय
प्रेरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be urged on or incited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरयत्
प्रेरयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, setting in motion, mov-<BR>ing, directing (the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरयितृ
प्रेरयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who urges, an insti-<BR>gator, inciting, instigating; one who sends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरित|प्रेरितः
प्रेरित, अस्, आ, अम्, driven forwards, impelled,<BR>influenced, instigated; excited, urged, stimulated;<BR>incited to speak; sent, directed, dispatched; ordered;<BR>touched; (अस्), m. an envoy, a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरितृ
प्रेरितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who urges on or incites,<BR>an inciter; one who sends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्त्वन्
प्रेर्त्वन्, आ, m., Ved. the ocean, the sea; (अरी),<BR>f. a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्यमाण
प्रेर्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being urged on, being<BR>incited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्
प्रेष् 1. प्रेष्, cl. 1. A. प्रेषते, &c., to<BR>go, move; (also read ह्रेष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्
प्रेष् 2. प्रेष् (प्र-इष्, see rt. 1. इष्),<BR>cl. 4. P. A. प्रेष्यति, -ते, प्रेषितुम्, to drive<BR>forth, drive away, drive forwards, drive on; to<BR>send forth, send out, utter; to hurl, fling, cast; (P.)<BR>to call upon, invite, summon (in Vedic ritual said<BR>technically of the presiding priest at a sacrifice calling<BR>upon the assistant priests to commence a recitation<BR>or a ceremony; with acc. of the object, e. g. साम<BR>प्रेष्यति गाय ब्रूहीति वा, he calls upon an<BR>assistant priest with the words ‘Sing’ or ‘Say’ to<BR>commence the recitation of a Sāman; also with gen.<BR>of the object; also with dat. of the deity to whom<BR>the recitation is addressed or the sacrifice offered,<BR>e. g. अग्नये प्रेष्य, call upon an assistant priest<BR>to commence the offering or to commence the<BR>hymn to Agni); Caus. प्रेषयति, -यितुम्, to send<BR>forth, send away, dismiss; to send into exile, banish;<BR>to send, dispatch; to send word to, send a message<BR>to; to hurl, fling, cast, throw; to turn or direct<BR>(the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्
3. प्रेष्, ट्, f., Ved. pressing, pressure; (ट्, ट्, ट्),<BR>pressing, urging on, (Sāy. = प्रेरक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष|प्रेषः
प्रेष, अस्, m. urging on, impelling (Ved. =<BR>प्रैष); pain, affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषक
प्रेषक, अस्, इका, अम्, sending, dispatching; one<BR>who orders or commands, ordering, directing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषण|प्रेषणं
प्रेषण, अम्, n. the act of sending, dispatching<BR>(a messenger); sending on a mission, commissioning,<BR>charging, ordering, directing, commanding; execut-<BR>ing a commission.<BR>—प्रेषण-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, executing<BR>a commission.<BR>—प्रेषणाध्यक्ष (˚ण-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a superintendent of the commands (of a<BR>king), chief of the administration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषणीय
प्रेषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sent or dispatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषयत्
प्रेषयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, sending forth, sending<BR>away; turning, directing (the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषयितृ
प्रेषयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, sending on a commis-<BR>sion, giving orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषित|प्रेषितं
प्रेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, sent forth, sent away; sent<BR>into exile, banished; sent, dispatched (on an errand);<BR>ordered, directed; turned, directed (as the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषितवत्
प्रेषितवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has sent or<BR>dispatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषितव्य
प्रेषितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be called upon<BR>or invited (to commence a ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्य|प्रेष्यः
प्रेष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sent or dispatched,<BR>proper to be sent [cf. कार्य-प्˚]; (अस्), m. a mes-<BR>senger, servant, menial, slave [cf. ग्राम-प्˚]; (आ),<BR>f. a female messenger, female servant; (अम्), n. the<BR>being a servant, servitude; [cf. शूद्र-प्˚.]<BR>—प्रेष्य-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, executing orders.<BR>—प्रेष्य-जन,<BR>अस्, m. servants collectively, domestics, an establishment<BR>of servants.<BR>—प्रेष्य-ता, f. or प्रेष्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the being a servant, servitude.<BR>—प्रेष्य-भाव,<BR>अस्, m. the state or condition of a servant, servitude.<BR>—प्रेष्य-वधू, ऊस्, f. a female servant, hand-<BR>maid; the wife of a slave.<BR>—प्रेष्य-वर्ग, अस्, m.<BR>a train of servants.<BR>—प्रेष्या-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of a female servant, being a handmaid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्यमाण
प्रेष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being sent forth, being<BR>sent or dispatched (on an errand).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष|प्रैषः
प्रैष, अस्, m. an invitation, order, command<BR>(especially in liturgical language, = प्रेष); sending,<BR>directing; sorrow, distress, affliction; phrenzy, in-<BR>toxication, insanity (?).<BR>—प्रैष-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>executing orders or commands, a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैषणिक
प्रैषणिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रेषण), executing<BR>orders or commissions (as a means of livelihood),<BR>fitted for the execution of commands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैषम्
प्रैषम्, ind., Ved. in the formula प्रैषैः<BR>or इष्टिभिः प्रैषम् इच्छति, he strives to start<BR>(the sacrifice compared to an animal in the chase)<BR>with invocations or exclamations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैषिक
प्रैषिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रैष), belonging<BR>to or connected with the invitatory formulas (in<BR>liturgical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष्य|प्रैष्यः
प्रैष्य, अस्, m. a servant, slave; (आ), f. a female<BR>servant; (अम्), n. the being a servant, servitude.<BR>—प्रैष्य-भाव, अस्, m. the state or condition<BR>of a servant, servitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0664-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्ठ|प्रेष्ठः
प्रेष्ठ प्रेष्ठ. See p. 663, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहण
प्रेहण प्रेहण, अम्, n. (fr. rt. ईह् with प्र),<BR>see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहिकटा
प्रेहिकटा प्रेहि-कटा, &c. See p. 663, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैकीय
प्रैकीय प्रैकीय (fr. प्र + एक), Nom. P.<BR>प्रैकीयति, -यितुम्, = प्रेकीय, see Vopa-deva II. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैय|प्रैयं
प्रैय प्रैय, अम्, n. an abstract noun from<BR>प्रिय, see Gaṇa Pṛthv-ādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैयक
प्रैयक, अस्, m. a patronymic from Priyaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैयङ्गव
प्रैयङ्गव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रियङ्गु), Ved.<BR>relating to panic-grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैयमेध
प्रैयमेध, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. an adj. from<BR>प्रिय-मेध; (अस्), m., N. of a Sāman; a patro-<BR>nymic of Sindhu-kṣit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैयरूपक
प्रैयरूपक, अम्, n. an abstract noun from<BR>प्रिय-रूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैयव्रत
प्रैयव्रत, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging to<BR>Priya-vrata; (अस्), m. a patronymic from Priya-vrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैय्यङ्गव
प्रैय्यङ्गव, a wrong form for प्रैयङ्गव,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैय्यमेध
प्रैय्यमेध, अस्, m. a patronymic; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), a wrong form for प्रैयमेध, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्त|प्रोक्तं
प्रोक्त प्रोक्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्र-वच्), spoken<BR>to, addressed; announced, declared, laid down as a<BR>rule or axiom, said, told, uttered.<BR>—प्रोक्त-कारिन्,<BR>ई, इणी, इ, doing what one has been told.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्तवत्
प्रोक्तवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has said or<BR>declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्यमान
प्रोच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being declared or an-<BR>nounced, being uttered or said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्ष्
प्रोक्ष् प्रोक्ष् (प्र-उक्ष्), cl. 6. P. A. प्रोक्-<BR>षति, -ते, प्रोक्षितुम्, to sprinkle upon, besprinkle,<BR>sprinkle; to consecrate (by sprinkling), consecrate as<BR>a sacrificial victim; to sacrifice, kill, slay, slaughter<BR>(a sacrificial victim): Caus. प्रोक्षयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to sprinkle, sprinkle with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षण|प्रोक्षणं
प्रोक्षण, अम्, n. the act of sprinkling with<BR>water (for purification), sprinkling, consecration by<BR>sprinkling (of a sacrifical animal or of a dead body<BR>before burial); immolation of victims, killing animals<BR>in sacrifice; a text to be repeated at an animal sacri-<BR>fice; (ई), f. (generally used in pl.) water for sprinkling,<BR>holy water, water for consecrating (mixed with rice<BR>and barley grains).<BR>—प्रोक्षणी-पात्र, अम्, n. a<BR>vessel for sprinkling water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षणि|प्रोक्षणिः
प्रोक्षणि, इस्, f. = प्रोक्षणी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षणीय|प्रोक्षणीयं
प्रोक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled, fit to be<BR>sprinkled; (अम्), n. water used for consecrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षत्
प्रोक्षत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, Ved. sprinkling,<BR>consecrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षित|प्रोक्षितं
प्रोक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled, purified by<BR>sprinkling; offered in sacrifice; immolated, killed,<BR>slaughtered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षितव्य
प्रोक्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sprinkled, to be<BR>consecrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोघीय
प्रोघीय प्रोघीय (प्र-ओघ), Nom. P. प्रो-<BR>घीयति, -यितुम्, = प्रौघीय, see Vopa-deva II. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चण्ड|प्रोच्चंड
प्रोच्चण्ड प्रोच्चण्ड (प्र-उच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>exceedingly terrible or horrible, very violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चर्
प्रोच्चर् प्रोच्-चर् (प्र-उद्-चर्), cl. 1. P. -च-<BR>रति, -चरितुम्, to utter a sound, utter, pronounce:<BR>Caus. -चारयति, -यितुम्, to cause to sound, utter a<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चरत्
प्रोच्-चरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, uttering a sound,<BR>uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चारित
प्रोच्-चारित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to sound, sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चैस्
प्रोच्चैस् प्रोच्चैस् (प्र-उच्˚), ind. exceedingly<BR>high, in a very high degree; very loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छल्
प्रोच्छल् प्रोच्-छल् (प्र-उद्-शल्), cl. 1. A.<BR>-छलते, -छलितुम्, to spirt out, gush forth, flow<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छलत्|प्रोच्छलन्त्
प्रोच्-छलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, spirting out, gushing<BR>forth, flowing or issuing forth, flowing out or up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छून
प्रोच्छून प्रोच्-छून, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. श्वि<BR>with प्र-उद्), swelled, swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छ्रि
प्रोच्छ्रि प्रोच्-छ्रि (प्र-उद्-श्रि), cl. 1. P.<BR>प्रोच्छ्रयति, -यितुम्, to set up, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छ्रित
प्रोच्-छ्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, high, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्जासन|प्रोज्जासनं
प्रोज्जासन प्रोज्-जासन, अम्, n. (fr. rt. जस्<BR>with प्र-उद्), killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्ज्वल्
प्रोज्ज्वल् प्रोज्-ज्वल् (प्र-उद्-ज्वल्), cl. 1. P.<BR>-ज्वलति, -ज्वलितुम्, to shine brightly, flash, glitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झ्
प्रोज्झ् प्रोज्झ् (प्र-उज्झ्), cl. 6. P. प्रोज्झति,<BR>प्रोज्झितुम्, to abandon, forsake, avoid, shun, leave,<BR>quit, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झन|प्रोज्झनं
प्रोज्झन, अम्, n. abandoning, forsaking, leaving,<BR>quitting, letting go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झित|प्रोज्झितं
प्रोज्झित, अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned, forsaken,<BR>quitted, shunned, avoided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोञ्छ्
प्रोञ्छ् प्रोञ्छ् (प्र-उञ्छ्), cl. 1. 6. P. प्रोञ्-<BR>छति, प्रोञ्छितुम्, to wipe out, efface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोञ्छन|प्रोंछन|प्रोंछनं|प्रोञ्छनं
प्रोञ्छन, अम्, n. wiping out, wiping away,<BR>effacing; picking up the remnants; [cf. उञ्छन,<BR>and cf. also Kullūka on Manu II. 241.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोड्डी
प्रोड्डी प्रोड्-डी (प्र-उद्-डी), cl. 1. 4. A. -ड-<BR>यते, -डीयते, -डयितुम्, to fly up, fly away, fly off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोड्डीन
प्रोड्-डीन, अस्, आ, अम्, flown up, flown away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोड्डीय
प्रोड्-डीय, ind. having flown up, having flown away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढम्
प्रोढम् प्रोढम्, ind., see Gaṇa Tish-<BR>ṭhadgv-ādi to Pāṇ. II. 1, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोण्ठ|प्रोंठः|प्रोण्ठः
प्रोण्ठ प्रोण्ठ, अस्, m. a spitting-pot, spit-<BR>toon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत|प्रोतं
प्रोत प्रोत, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वे with प्र),<BR>sewed, stitched; extended lengthwise or perpendicu-<BR>larly, sewed with the threads lengthwise (as the warp<BR>of ‘a piece of cloth, opposed to ओत, q. v., which<BR>means extended horizontally or sewn with the threads<BR>crosswise as the woof of cloth;’ ओत-प्रोत in Mahā-<BR>bh. Udyoga-p. 1789 probably means ‘who is the<BR>woof and warp of the universe,’ i. e. extended every-<BR>where; according to the Scholiast ओतः प्रोतश्च =<BR>तिर्यग् ऊर्ध्वं च पटे तन्तव इवानुस्यूतः);<BR>tied, strung; joined, connected; set, inlaid; trans-<BR>fixed, pierced, impaled, put on (a spit); (अम्), n.<BR>cloth, clothes.<BR>—प्रोतोत्सादन (˚त-उत्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>parasol, umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोतय
प्रोतय, Nom. P. प्रोतयति, -यितुम्, to infix,<BR>insert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोतयित्वा
प्रोतयित्वा, ind. having infixed or inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोति
प्रोति, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कट
प्रोत्कट प्रोत्कट (प्र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, scil.<BR>भृत्य, a head servant, favourite servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कण्ठ|प्रोत्कंठ
प्रोत्कण्ठ 1. प्रोत्कण्ठ (प्र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>stretching out or lifting up the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कण्ठ|प्रोत्कंठ
2. प्रोत्कण्ठ, Nom. Caus. P. -कण्ठयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to awaken longings, excite desires in (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कर्ष|प्रोत्कर्षः
प्रोत्कर्ष प्रोत्कर्ष (प्र-उत्˚), अस्, m. pre-<BR>eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्क्रुष्ट|प्रोत्क्रुष्टं
प्रोत्क्रुष्ट प्रोत्क्रुष्ट (प्र-उत्˚), अम्, n. a loud<BR>cry or uproar, loud sound (Hari-vaṃśa 13816).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्खन्
प्रोत्खन् प्रोत्-खन् (प्र-उद्-खन्), cl. 1. P.<BR>A. -खनति, -ते, -खनितुम्, to dig up, dig through,<BR>dig out, dig open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्खात
प्रोत्-खात, अस्, आ, अम्, dug up, dug out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्खै
प्रोत्खै प्रोत्-खै (प्र-उद्-खै), cl. 1. P.<BR>-खायति, -खातुम्, to dig up, dig out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्तान
प्रोत्तान प्रोत्तान (प्र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>stretched out widely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्तुङ्ग|प्रोत्तुंग
प्रोत्तुङ्ग प्रोत्तुङ्ग (प्र-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, very<BR>high or lofty, elevated, prominent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्तॄ
प्रोत्तॄ प्रोत्-तॄ (प्र-उद्-तॄ), cl. 1. P. -तरति,<BR>-तरितुम्, -तरीतुम्, to cross over, pass over; to rise<BR>or come out from, emerge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्पत्
