प्रोर्णुवत्
प्रोर्णुवत्, अन्, अती, अत्, covering over, covering,<BR>enveloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोर्णुवितृ
प्रोर्णुवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who covers or<BR>envelops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लस्
प्रोल्लस् प्रोल्-लस् (प्र-उद्-लस्), cl. 1. P. -ल-<BR>सति, -लसितुम्, to shine brightly, glitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लसत्|प्रोल्लसन्त्
प्रोल्-लसत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shining brightly, glit-<BR>tering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लाघित
प्रोल्लाघित प्रोल्-लाघित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">Page0666-b+ 74</a>]<BR>लाघ् with प्र-उद्), recovered from sickness, con-<BR>valescent, strong, robust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लिखत्
प्रोल्लिखत् प्रोल्-लिखत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्<BR>(fr. rt. लिख् with प्र-उद्), making lines or scratches,<BR>marking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लेखन|प्रोल्लेखनं
प्रोल्-लेखन, अम्, n. drawing marks or lines,<BR>scratching, marking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष|प्रोषः
प्रोष प्रोष. See rt. 1. प्रुष्, p. 663.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषक
प्रोषक प्रोषक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people<BR>(Mahā-bh. Bhīṣma-p. 376).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषित|प्रोषितः
प्रोषित प्रोषित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 6. वस्<BR>with प्र), sojourning abroad or in a foreign country,<BR>away from home, absent, abroad.<BR>—प्रोषित-त्रास,<BR>अस्, m. fear of one who is absent.<BR>—प्रोषित-<BR>भर्तृक, अस्, आ, अम्, whose husband is abroad.<BR>—प्रोषित-मरण, अम्, n. dying abroad or in a<BR>foreign country.<BR>—प्रोषित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, sojourn-<BR>ing away from home, strange, a stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्य
प्रोष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. moving to distant<BR>places, flowing onwards (as water; perhaps connected<BR>with rt. 1. प्रुष्).<BR>—प्रोष्य-पापीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्,<BR>become worse by sojourning in a foreign country,<BR>deteriorated by living abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठ|प्रोष्ठः
प्रोष्ठ प्रोष्ठ, अस्, m. (perhaps a contrac-<BR>tion for a form प्राव-स्थ fr. rt. स्था with प्र-<BR>अव), a bench, stool; a bull, an ox; N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (अस्, ई), m. f. a sort of<BR>carp, Cyprinus Pausius (= शफरी).<BR>—प्रोष्ठ-<BR>पद, अस्, आ, m. f. (also ए, f. du., आस्, pl.), ‘the foot of<BR>a stool,’ N. of a double Nakṣatra or of the third<BR>and fourth lunar mansions, the month Bhādra or<BR>August-September; (also called पूर्व-भाद्रपदा<BR>and उत्तर-भाद्रपदा; cf. नक्षत्र, भाद्र-<BR>पदा.)<BR>—प्रोष्ठ-पाद, अस्, ई, अम्, one whose<BR>feet rest on a bench; born under the Nakṣatra<BR>Proṣṭha-padā.<BR>—प्रोष्ठे-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>sleeping on a couch; (Sāy.) = प्राङ्गणे शयानः,<BR>sleeping or lying in a court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठिक
प्रोष्ठिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ण
प्रोष्ण प्रोष्ण (प्र-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ex-<BR>ceedingly hot, burning hot, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्य
प्रोष्य प्रोष्य. See under प्रोषित above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह्
प्रोह् प्रोह् (प्र-ऊह्, see rt. 1. ऊह्), cl. 1. P.<BR>प्रोहति, प्रोहितुम्, Ved. to push forward, push<BR>away, (according to Mahī-dhara = निर्-आकृ); to<BR>throw down; (प्रोहति = पातयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह|प्रोहः
1. प्रोह in प्रोह-करटा, f. (प्रोह, 2nd sing.<BR>Impv. of प्रोह्), a various reading for प्रेहि-कटा,<BR>q. v.<BR>—प्रोह-कर्दमा, f. a ceremony at which<BR>impurity is cleared away (see Gaṇa Mayūra-vyaṃsa-<BR>kādi to Pāṇ. II. 1, 72).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोहण
प्रोहण, अम्, n. the act of pushing away (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह्यपदि
प्रोह्य-पदि, ind. (perhaps) by or in pushing<BR>away the foot (Gaṇa Dvidaṇḍy-ādi to Pāṇ. V. 4,<BR>128).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह|प्रोहः
प्रोह 2. प्रोह, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. ऊह् with प्र),<BR>logical reasoning; an elephant's foot; the ankle of<BR>an elephant; a joint, a knot; (अस्, आ, अम्), skilful,<BR>clever; reasoning logically, a reasoner, disputant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोहणीय
प्रोहणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be reasoned or argued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौह|प्रौहः
प्रौह, अस्, ई, अम्, clever, skilful; (अस्), m. con-<BR>sideration, reflection; a good argument; the foot of<BR>an elephant; a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौक्त
प्रौक्त प्रौक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रोक्त), having<BR>the sense of ‘proclaimed by’ (said of a suffix).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौघीय
प्रौघीय प्रौघीय (fr. प्र + ओघ), Nom.<BR>P. प्रौघीयति, -यितुम्, = प्रोघीय, see Vopa-<BR>deva II. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढ|प्रौढं
प्रौढ प्रौढ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. वह् with<BR>प्र), grown up, full-grown, fully developed, matured,<BR>perfected; mature, adult, old; married; luxuriant<BR>(as a plant); great, grand, mighty, strong; impulsive,<BR>impetuous, violent; thick, dense (as darkness); full<BR>(as the moon); filled with, full of, (at the end of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">Page0666-c+ 77</a>]<BR>comps.; cf. मृदु-प्˚); confident, bold, arrogant,<BR>audacious, impudent; forward; raised up, lifted up;<BR>controverted; an epithet of one of the seven Ullāsas<BR>in the Kulārṇava-tantra; (in music) an epithet of<BR>one of the seven Rūpakas; प्रौढम् ब्राह्म-<BR>णम्, the great Brāhmaṇa; (आ), f. a married woman<BR>from thirty to fifty-five years of age; a violent or<BR>impetuous woman (described as a Nāyikā who<BR>stands in no awe of her lover or husband).<BR>—प्रौ-<BR>ढ-चरित-नामन्, आनि, n. pl., N. of a work by<BR>Vallabha Ācārya on the titles of Kṛṣṇa derived<BR>from one hundred and twenty-eight of his exploits<BR>during adolescence.<BR>—प्रौढ-त्व, अम्, n. confi-<BR>dence, arrogance.<BR>—प्रौढ-पाद, अस्, ई, अम्, one<BR>whose feet are raised on a bench; [cf. प्रोष्ठ-पाद.]<BR>—प्रौढ-पुष्प, अस्, आ, अम्, having blossoms<BR>full-grown (as a tree).<BR>—प्रौढ-प्रताप, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of mighty prowess, renowned in arms.<BR>—प्रौ-<BR>ढप्रताप-मार्तण्ड, N. of a work attributed to<BR>Pratāpa-rudra Gaja-pati on the appropriate seasons<BR>for the worship of Viṣṇu.<BR>—प्रौढ-प्रिया, f. a<BR>bold or confident mistress; (according to Malli-nātha<BR>= प्रगल्भ-कान्ता.)<BR>—प्रौढ-मनोरमा, f.,<BR>N. of a commentary by Bhaṭṭoji-dīkṣita on his own<BR>work the Siddhānta-Kaumudī.<BR>—प्रौढ-यौवन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, in the prime or bloom of youth.<BR>—प्रौ-<BR>ढ-वाद, अस्, m. an arrogant expression.<BR>—प्रौ-<BR>ढाङ्गना (˚ढ-अङ्˚), f. a bold or impulsive<BR>woman.<BR>—प्रौढान्त (˚ढ-अन्˚), N. of one of<BR>the seven Ullāsas in the Kulārṇava-tantra.<BR>—प्रौ-<BR>ढोक्ति (˚ढ-उक्˚), इस्, f. a bold expression or<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढि|प्रौढिः
प्रौढि, इस्, f. growth, increase; maturity, per-<BR>fect state (of body or mind); full development,<BR>elevation, greatness, grandeur; sense of power, self-<BR>confidence, feeling of security, arrogance; audacity,<BR>boldness; zeal, enterprise, exertion; investigation,<BR>controversy, discussion.<BR>—प्रौढि-वाद, अस्, m. a<BR>bold assertion, confident affirmation; a pompous<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढीभू
प्रौढी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>grow up, increase, come to maturity.<BR>—प्रौढी-<BR>भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, growing up, coming to matu-<BR>rity.<BR>—प्रौढी-भविष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्,<BR>about to arrive at maturity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौण|प्रौणः
प्रौण प्रौण, अस्, आ, अम्, clever, learned,<BR>skilful; [cf. प्रौह, प्रोह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठ|प्रौष्ठः
प्रौष्ठ प्रौष्ठ, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Proṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठपद|प्रौष्ठपदः
प्रौष्ठपद, अस्, m. (fr. प्रोष्ठ-पद),<BR>scil. मास, the month Bhādra (August-September);<BR>N. of one of Kuvera's treasure-keepers; N. of a<BR>Pari-śiṣṭa of the Sāma-veda; (ई), f., scil. पौर्ण-<BR>मासी, full moon in the month Bhādra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठपदिक
प्रौष्ठपदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. प्रोष्ठ-<BR>पदा), see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठिक
प्रौष्ठिक, अस्, m. a patronymic from Prosh-<BR>ṭhika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौह|प्रौहः
प्रौह प्रौह. See under 2. प्रोह, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक|प्लकः
प्लक प्लक, अस्, m., Ved. in कश-प्लकौ,<BR>pudenda muliebria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष्
प्लक्ष् प्लक्ष्, cl. 1. P. A. प्लक्षति, -ते,<BR>&c., to eat, consume; (a various reading<BR>for भक्ष्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष|प्लक्षः
प्लक्ष प्लक्ष, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>प्लुष्, to burn), the waved-leaf fig-tree or Ficus Infec-<BR>toria (a large and beautiful tree with small white<BR>fruit); the holy fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa; the tree<BR>Hibiscus Populneoides, Thespesia Populneoides; a<BR>side door, private or back door; the space at the<BR>side of a door; one of the seven Dvīpas or continents<BR>into which the world is divided; N. of a man; (आ),<BR>f. a N. of the river Sarasvatī.<BR>—प्लक्ष-जाता, f.<BR>‘rising near the fig-tree,’ an epithet of the Sarasvatī.<BR>—प्लक्ष-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place of pil-<BR>grimage.<BR>—प्लक्ष-प्रस्रवण, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>fig-tree source,’ N. of the place where the Sarasvatī<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">Page0667-a+ 73</a>]<BR>takes its rise.<BR>—प्लक्ष-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of the<BR>fig-trees,’ N. of the place where the Sarasvatī becomes<BR>visible.<BR>—प्लक्ष-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, surrounded by<BR>fig-trees (Ficus Infectoria); (अती), f., N. of a river<BR>(perhaps the Sarasvatī).<BR>—प्लक्ष-समुद्र-वा-<BR>चका, f. an epithet of the river Sarasvatī.<BR>—प्लक्ष-<BR>स्रवण, अम्, n., N. of the place where the Saras-<BR>vatī becomes visible; [cf. प्लक्ष-प्रस्रवण.]<BR>—प्लक्षावतरण (˚ष-अव्˚), अम्, n., N. of a<BR>place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0666-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्षकीय
प्लक्षकीय, see Gaṇa Naḍādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्ष|प्लाक्षं
प्लाक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating to the<BR>waved-leaf fig-tree (Ficus Infectoria); (अम्), n. the<BR>fruit of the waved-leaf fig-tree and of the various<BR>trees called Plaksha; (अस्), m. a patronymic from<BR>Plākṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्षकि
प्लाक्षकि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Plaksha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्षायण
प्लाक्षायण, अस्, m. a patronymic from Plākṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्षि
प्लाक्षि, इस्, ई, m. f. a patronymic from Plaksha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लति
प्लति प्लति, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लात
प्लात, अस्, m. a patronymic from Plati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लब्
प्लब् प्लब् or प्लव्, cl. 1. A. प्लबते, प्ल-<BR>वते, &c., to float, = rt. प्लु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लयोग
प्लयोग प्लयोग (= प्र-योग?), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लायोगि
प्लायोगि, इस्, m. a patronymic of Āsaṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लव|प्लवं|प्लवः
प्लव प्लव, प्लवक, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्ष|प्लाक्षं
प्लाक्ष प्लाक्ष, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाय
प्लाय प्लाय. See under प्ले, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव|प्लावः
प्लाव प्लाव, &c. See col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाशि
प्लाशि प्लाशि, इस्, m., Ved. a particular part<BR>of the intestines; (according to Mahī-dhara = शिश्न<BR>or शिश्न-मूल-नाड्यः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाशुक
प्लाशुक प्लाशुक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. प्लाशु =<BR>प्राशु), Ved. growing rapidly; (according to the<BR>Scholiasts) growing again, springing up again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाशुचित्
प्लाशुचित्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. quick, speedy; [cf. प्राशु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिह्
प्लिह् प्लिह्, cl. 1. A. प्लेहते, पिप्लिहे, प्ले-<BR>हितुम्, to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिहन्
प्लिहन्, आ, m. the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहन्
प्लीहन्, आ, m. the spleen (which with the liver<BR>is regarded by the Hindūs as the part of the body<BR>from which the blood flows); disease of the spleen<BR>(said to be equally applied to enlargement of the<BR>mesenteric glands, &c.); [cf. Gr. σπλήν, σπλάγχ-<BR>νο-ν; Lat. lien; Bohem. slez-ina; Lith. bluz-ni-s;<BR>Eng. spleen.]<BR>—प्लीह-घ्न, अस्, or प्लीह-शत्रु,<BR>उस्, m. ‘destroying spleen’ or ‘enemy to spleen,’ N.<BR>of a medicinal plant, Amoora Rohitaka (commonly<BR>Rohera or Rohinī).<BR>—प्लीहा-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. (according to Mahī-dhara) suffering from a<BR>particular disease of the ear called प्लीहन्.<BR>—प्लीहारि<BR>(˚ह-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy to spleen,’ the holy fig-<BR>tree, Ficus Religiosa.<BR>—प्लीहोदर (˚ह-उद्˚), अम्,<BR>n. enlargement of the spleen, disease of the spleen.<BR>—प्लीहोदरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, affected with enlargement<BR>or disease of the spleen, splenetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहा
प्लीहा, f. = प्लीहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ली
प्ली प्ली, cl. 9. P. प्लिनाति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लु
प्लु प्लु, cl. 1. A. (in poetry sometimes<BR>also P.) प्लवते (-ति), पुप्लुवे, प्लोष्यते,<BR>अप्लोष्ट (2nd pl. अप्लोढ्वम्), प्लोषीष्ट, प्लो-<BR>तुम्, to float, swim; to go in a boat, cross in a<BR>boat, navigate; to bathe; to sway to and fro,<BR>vibrate, hover, soar, fly; to fly away, haste away;<BR>to blow (as the wind); to fade away, disappear; to<BR>leap, jump, spring, (in these senses originally प्रु);<BR>to hop, skip, dance; to spring over, jump over,<BR>leap across, spring upon, spring down; to be length-<BR>ened or prolated (as a vowel): Caus. P. प्लावयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अपुप्लवत्, अपिप्लवत्, to cause to<BR>float or swim, flood, deluge, inundate, submerge; to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">Page0667-b+ 81</a>]<BR>pour water upon, sprinkle, bathe, wash; to wash<BR>away, remove; to cause to leap; to cause to stagger;<BR>to lengthen, prolate (a vowel): Pass. of Caus. प्लाव्-<BR>यते, to be deluged, to be overflowed, to be inun-<BR>dated: Desid. of Caus. पिप्लावयिषति, पुप्लावयि-<BR>षति: Desid. पुप्लूषते: Intens. पोप्लूयते,<BR>पोप्लोति, to float about, swim about; to swim rapidly;<BR>[cf. Gr. πλέ-ω, πλεύ-σομαι, πλό-ο-ς, πλω-τό-ς,<BR>πλώ-τη-ς, πλύν-ω, πλῦ-μα, πλυ-τό-ς, πλυν-τήρ,<BR>πύελος; perhaps λού-ω for πλού-ω: Lat. plu-i-t,<BR>pluv-ia, flu-o, fle-o, plôra-re, linter; perhaps<BR>fund-o for plund-o; perhaps pluma; probably<BR>lav-o for plav-o: Old Lat. per-plov-ere: Umbr.<BR>pre-plo-tutu, ‘overflowed:’ Goth. flô-du-s, ‘a<BR>river:’ Old Germ. flew-iu, ‘float;’ fliu-z-u, ‘flow;’<BR>fluz, perhaps flug: Angl. Sax. fleot, fleowan, flod,<BR>fleogan, fliogan, fleón, flión, aet-flowan, fleotan;<BR>Iceland. flut: Old Slav. plov-a, plou-ti, ‘to sail;’<BR>plu-ti, ‘to swim:’ Russ. plavaju, ‘I swim:’ Lith.<BR>pláu-j-u, plau-ti, ‘to wash off;’ plaú-t-is; plú-sti,<BR>‘to swim:’ Hib. plod, ‘a fleet;’ plodaim, ‘I float;’<BR>perhaps lua = Gaelic lu, ‘water;’ luathaim, ‘I<BR>hasten, I move;’ falcaim, ‘I bathe;’ luan, ‘a<BR>woman's breast:’ Gaelic plucas, ‘a flux, ventris<BR>fluxio.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लव|प्लवं|प्लवः
प्लव, अस्, आ, अम्, swimming, floating; leaping,<BR>jumping, one who goes by leaps or jumps, a tumbler;<BR>superior, excellent (Ved.); (अस्), m. the act of<BR>swimming, floating, diving, bathing [cf. जल-प्˚,<BR>धरणी-प्˚]; flooding, a flood, the swelling of a<BR>river; suffusion, (नयन-प्˚, suffusion or swimming<BR>of the eyes); jumping, leaping, plunging, going by<BR>leaps or plunges; a float, raft, boat, canoe, small<BR>ship; a snare or basket of wicker-work for catching<BR>fish (= पलव); a kind of aquatic bird, Pelicanus<BR>Fusicollis (= गात्र-सम्प्लव); a kind of duck (=<BR>कारण्डव); = जल-वायस; = जल-काक; = जल-<BR>कुक्कुट; a frog; a monkey; a sheep; a man of<BR>low or degraded tribe, a Cāṇḍāla; an enemy; the<BR>waved-leaf fig-tree, Ficus Infectoria (= प्लक्ष); a<BR>kind of weapon; the thirty-fifth (or ninth) year in a<BR>cycle of Jupiter; N. of various Sāmans; the prolated<BR>utterance of a vowel; protracting a sentence through<BR>three or more Ślokas (= कुलक); a kind of metre;<BR>a declivity, slope, shelving ground; proclivity, incli-<BR>nation; returning, return; urging on, inciting;<BR>(अम्), n. a species of grass, Cyperus Rotundus; a<BR>kind of fragrant grass (= गन्ध-तृण); [cf. Gr.<BR>πλόος, πλοῖον; Hib. falc, ‘a flood.’]<BR>—प्लव-ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘going by leaps,’ a frog; an ape, monkey;<BR>a sort of aquatic bird, the diver; the plant Acacia<BR>Sirissa (= शिरीष); N. of the charioteer of the Sun;<BR>of a son of the Sun; (आ), f. the sign of the zodiac<BR>Virgo.<BR>—प्लव-गति, इस्, f. going by leaps and<BR>jumps; (इस्), m. a frog.<BR>—प्लवङ्-ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘going by leaps,’ an epithet of fire as flickering; (अस्),<BR>m. an ape, baboon, monkey; a deer; the waved-leaf<BR>fig-tree, Ficus Infectoria; N. of the forty-first (or<BR>fifteenth) year in a sixty years' cycle of Jupiter.<BR>—प्लवङ्-गम, अस्, m. ‘going by leaps,’ a frog;<BR>an ape, monkey; (आ), f. a kind of metre.<BR>—प्लवङ्-<BR>गमेन्दु (˚म-इन्˚), उस्, m. ‘moon among the apes,’<BR>an epithet of Hanumat.<BR>—प्लव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>possessing a ship, owner of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवक|प्लवकः
प्लवक, अस्, m. a frog; a tumbler, a dancer, a<BR>man who walks on the edge of a sword, a rope-<BR>dancer, &c.; an outcast, a Cāṇḍāla; the waved-leaf<BR>fig-tree, Ficus Infectoria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवन|प्लवनः
प्लवन, अम्, n. swimming, plunging into,<BR>bathing; a deluge, inundation; jumping, leaping,<BR>plunging; capering, one of a horse's paces; flying;<BR>declivity, inclination; (अस्, आ, अम्), inclined, stooping<BR>down, (at the end of comps.; cf. प्राग्-उदक्-प्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवमान
प्लवमान, अस्, आ, अम्, floating, swimming;<BR>going in a boat, crossing in a boat; bathing; hover-<BR>ing, soaring; blowing (as the wind); fading away,<BR>disappearing; leaping, springing, bounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवाका
प्लवाका, f. a boat, a raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लविक
प्लविक, अस्, आ, अम्, ferrying over in a boat, a<BR>ferryman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवितृ
प्लवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, leaping, springing, a leaper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव|प्लावः
प्लाव, अस्, m. flowing over; filling a vessel till it<BR>overflows; submersion; jumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लावन|प्लावनं
प्लावन, अम्, n. bathing, immersion, ablution;<BR>filling a vessel till it overflows, flooding, deluging;<BR>inundation, flood, deluge; [cf. जल-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लावयत्
प्लावयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to float, flooding,<BR>inundating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लावयितृ
प्लावयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who causes to swim,<BR>causing to cross or go in a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लावित|प्लावितं
प्लावित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to float, made to<BR>swim; made to overflow; overflowed, deluged,<BR>inundated, flooded; moistened, soaked; covered<BR>with; [cf. रुधिर-प्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाविन्
प्लाविन्, ई, m. spreading, promulgating; (ई), m. a<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव्य
1. प्लाव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be submerged or inun-<BR>dated; to be steeped or soaked in anything (with<BR>inst.); to be jumped or leaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव्य
2. प्लाव्य, ind. having caused to float or swim;<BR>having immersed or flooded; having washed away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुत|प्लुतं|प्लुतः
प्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, floated, floating or swimming<BR>in [cf. उद-प्˚]; bathed in; inundated, submerged,<BR>overflowed, wet; covered with, filled with [cf. म-<BR>धु-प्˚, रजः-प्˚]; flown; jumped, leaped, one<BR>who has leaped, gone by leaps or jumps; protracted,<BR>prolated, continuous or lengthened to three Mātrās<BR>or prosodial instants (as a vowel in pronunciation,<BR>cf. मात्रा); (अम्), n. leaping, jumping, tumbling;<BR>bounding, vaulting; capering, one of a horse's paces.<BR>—प्लुत-गति, इस्, f. going by jumps or leaps; a<BR>bounding motion, galloping, a gallop; (इस्), m. a hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुतवत्
प्लुतवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has leaped or<BR>jumped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुति|प्लुतिः
प्लुति, इस्, f. overflowing, a flood; a leap, jump,<BR>skip, hop; bounding, capering, curvet, one of a<BR>horse's paces; prolation (of a vowel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्
प्लुष् प्लुष् [cf. rt. 1. प्रुष्], cl. 1. 4. 9. P.<BR>प्लोषति, प्लुष्यति, प्लुष्णाति, पुप्लो-<BR>ष, प्लोषितुम्, to burn, scorch, singe; cl. 9. P.<BR>to sprinkle; to anoint, embrocate; to fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुक्षि|प्लुक्षिः
प्लुक्षि, इस्, m. fire; the god of fire (?); the<BR>burning of a house; oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष|प्लुषः
प्लुष, अस्, m. burning, combustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुषि|प्लुषिः
प्लुषि, इस्, m., Ved. a species of noxious insect;<BR>(according to Mahī-dhara = पुत्तिका; according to<BR>another Scholiast = वक्र-तुण्ड.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्ट|प्लुष्टः
प्लुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, burned, scorched, singed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्टाय
प्लुष्टाय, Nom. A. प्लुष्टायते, -यितुम्, =<BR>प्लुष्टां कृ; (perhaps an incorrect form for<BR>प्लुष्वाय = प्रुष्वाय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लोष|प्लोषः
प्लोष, अस्, m. burning combustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लोषण
प्लोषण, अस्, ई, अम्, burning, scorching, singeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुस्
प्लुस् प्लुस्, cl. 4. P. प्लुस्यति, &c., to burn,<BR>(a various reading for प्लुष्); to share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ले
प्ले प्ले (rt. 5. इ with प्ल for प्र) = प्रे, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाय
प्लाय, अस्, m., Ved. = प्राय, abundance, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लेङ्ख
प्लेङ्ख प्लेङ्ख, Ved. = प्रेङ्ख, a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लेव्
प्लेव् प्लेव् [cf. rts. पेब्, पेव्, सेव्], cl. 1.<BR>A. प्लेवते, &c., to serve, wait upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लोत|प्लोतः
प्लोत प्लोत, अम्, n. (probably = प्रोत),<BR>cloth, stuff; a bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लोष|प्लोषः
प्लोष प्लोष. See under rt. प्लुष् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सरस्
प्सरस् प्सरस्. See under rt. 1. प्सा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
प्सा 1. प्सा, cl. 2. P. प्साति (3rd pl. Impf.<BR>अप्सुस् or अप्सान्), पप्सौ, प्सास्यति, अप्-<BR>सासीत्, प्सायात् or प्सेयात्, प्सातुम्, Ved. to chew,<BR>masticate, eat, consume; to go; [cf. Old Germ.<BR>spīsa, ‘food;’ Mod. Germ. speise.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सरस्
प्सरस्, अस्, n., Ved. a favourite dish or kind of<BR>food, feast, enjoyment, (occurring in connection with<BR>महि; cf. मधु-प्˚); food, sacrificial food; देव-<BR>प्सरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. being a pleasure for the<BR>gods, delightful to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
2. प्सा, f. eating, food; hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सात|प्सातं
प्सात, अस्, आ, अम्, chewed, eaten; hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सान|प्सानं
प्सान, अम्, n. eating, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0667-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सुर्
प्सुर्, र्, f. or प्सुरस्, अस्, n., Ved. (perhaps) fruit,<BR>(according to Sāy. an epithet of Indra, = रूप-वत् which<BR>would come under प्सु below); [cf. Zend fshu.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्स्न्य
प्स्न्य in विश्व-प्स्न्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सु
प्सु प्सु, Ved. form, aspect, (at the end of<BR>comps.; cf. अरुण-प्सु, ऋत-प्सु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ|फं|फः
फ 1. फ, the twenty-second consonant<BR>of the Nāgarī alphabet and the second letter of the<BR>fifth or labial class, being the aspirate of प्, and<BR>said to be pronounced like फ् in uphill, loophole.<BR>—फ-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound फ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ|फं|फः
फ 2. फ, अस्, आ, अम्, evident, manifest;<BR>(अस्), m. the performance of a mystical rite by which<BR>Kuvera's attendants are propitiated; increasing, swell-<BR>ing, enlarging, expanding; an augmenter, increaser;<BR>fruitfulness, fertility, gain; a high wind, a gale;<BR>yawning with the mouth wide open; (अम्), n.<BR>blowing, panting; bursting with a popping noise (as<BR>air bubbles &c.); bubbling, boiling; angry speech;<BR>unprofitable or idle speech; [cf. फा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्क्
फक्क् फक्क्, cl. 1. P. फक्कति, पफक्क,<BR>फक्किष्यति, अफक्कीत्, फक्कितुम्, to<BR>move slowly, go softly, creep, steal along; to have<BR>a preconceived opinion; to behave ill, act wrongly,<BR>act in a low or unjust manner; to swell: Caus.<BR>फक्कयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अपफक्कत्: Desid.<BR>पिफक्किषति: Intens. पाफक्क्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्क|फक्कः
फक्क, अस्, m. a cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्किका
फक्किका, f. a preconceived opinion, previous<BR>statement; a position, assertion or argument to be<BR>proved, thesis to be maintained; logical exposition<BR>or elucidation; a sophism, a trick, illusion, fraud; N.<BR>of a commentary on the Tarka-saṅgraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फगुल
फगुल फगुल, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(perhaps incorrectly for फल्गुन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जी
फञ्जी फञ्जी, f. the plant Clerodendrum<BR>Siphonanthus; [cf. जीर्ण-फ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जिका
फञ्जिका, f. Clerodendrum Siphonanthus; Li-<BR>peocercis Serrata (= देव-ताड); Alhagi Maurorum<BR>(= दुर्-आलभा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जिपत्त्रिका
फञ्जि-पत्त्रिका, f. a species of plant (= आखु-<BR>पर्णी; also read फञ्जि-पुत्रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट्
फट् फट्, an onomatopoetic word used<BR>mystically in incantations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट|फटः
फट फट, अस्, आ, m. f. (probably fr. rt.<BR>स्फट्; = स्फट), the expanded hood or neck of a<BR>serpent [cf. फण]; a tooth; a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फडिङ्गा|फडिंगा
फडिङ्गा फडिङ्गा, f. a cricket, grasshopper,<BR>locust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण्
फण् फण्, cl. 1. P. फणति, पफाण<BR>(2nd sing. फेणिथ or पफणिथ,<BR>3rd pl. फेणुस् or पफणुस्), फणिष्यति,<BR>अफणीत्, अफाणीत्, फणितुम्, to go, go about,<BR>move: Caus. फणयति, फाणयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to spring or run (Ved.); फाणयति, to scum,<BR>skim, take off (the surface of a fluid); to produce<BR>easily or without exertion: Desid. पिफणिषति:<BR>Intens. पम्फण्यते, पम्फणीति, पम्फण्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण|फणः
फण, अस्, m. (perhaps) scum, froth (Ved.);<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), m. f. n. the expanded side of a nostril;<BR>(अस्, आ), m. f. the expanded hood or neck of the<BR>cobra di capello (= फट); अङ्गुली-फण-हस्तक,<BR>one in whose hands the fingers take the shape of a<BR>hood; [cf. गो-फणा.]<BR>—फण-कर, अस्, m. the<BR>cobra di capello, Coluber Naga; a snake in general.<BR>—फण-गिरि, see फेन-गिरि.<BR>—फण-त्रय,<BR>अम्, n. three hoods (of a snake).<BR>—फण-धर,<BR>अस्, m. = फण-कर; an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—फण-<BR>भृत्, त्, m. = फण-कर; a symbolical expression<BR>for the number nine (or eight).<BR>—फण-मणि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘hood-gem,’ a jewel supposed to be found in<BR>the hood of a snake.<BR>—फण-मण्डल, अम्, n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">Page0668-b+ 77</a>]<BR>‘hood-orb,’ the rounded hood (of a serpent).<BR>—फ-<BR>ण-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a hood, hooded; (आन्),<BR>m. the cobra di capello, a snake in general.<BR>—फ-<BR>ण-श्रेणी, f. a line or row of serpents’ hoods.<BR>—फण-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a serpent's hood<BR>(as a gem).<BR>—फणा-कर, अस्, m. = फण-कर.<BR>—फणाटोप (˚ण-आट्˚ or ˚णा-आट्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>swelling of a serpent's hood.<BR>—फणाटोपिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, having the hood swollen (said of a serpent).<BR>—फणातपत्र (˚ण-आत्˚ or ˚णा-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a hood for a parasol (said of a serpent).<BR>—फणा-धर, अस्, m. = फण-धर.<BR>—फ-<BR>णा-फलक, अम्, n. the flat surface of a serpent's<BR>hood.<BR>—फणा-भर, अस्, m. the cobra di capello.<BR>—फणा-भृत्, त्, m. ‘hood-bearing,’ a snake,<BR>serpent.<BR>—फणा-मणि-सहस्र-रुच्, f. the splendor<BR>of the thousand jewels on the hood (of the serpent-<BR>king, Māgha IX. 25).<BR>—फणा-वत्, आन्, m. ‘pos-<BR>sessing a hood,’ the cobra di capello, a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिका
फणिका, f. the tree Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR>—फ-<BR>णिकेश्वर (˚का-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of one of the eight<BR>Vīta-rāgas of the Buddhists; [cf. फणीन्द्रेश्वर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिकार
फणिकार, अस्, m. an epithet of Piṅgala, (perhaps<BR>incorrectly for फण-कर or फणा-कर, which<BR>would be analogous to his epithets नाग-राज and<BR>भुजङ्गेश); N. of a people, (also read कर्णिकार.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणित|फणितः
फणित, अस्, आ, अम्, gone; diluted (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिन्
फणिन्, ई, m. the hooded serpent, cobra di<BR>capello, a serpent in general; an epithet of Rāhu;<BR>of Patañjali; a species of herb (= सर्पिणी).<BR>—फ-<BR>णि-कन्या, f. the daughter of a serpent-demon.<BR>—फणि-केशर or फणि-केसर, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>Mesua Roxburghii (= नाग-केसर).<BR>—फणि-जा,<BR>f. a species of plant (= Marāṭhī झरसी).<BR>—फणि-<BR>जिह्वा, f. ‘serpent's tongue,’ N. of a plant (= महा-<BR>शतावरी); the plant Sida Cordifolia (= महा-स-<BR>मङ्गा).<BR>—फणि-जिह्विका, f. the plant Emblica<BR>Officinalis; = फणि-जिह्वा.<BR>—फणि-तल्प-ग, अस्,<BR>m. ‘resorting to a serpent as a couch,’ an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—फणि-पति, इस्, m. ‘serpent-king,’ N.<BR>of the serpent Śeṣa; of Patañjali.<BR>—फणि-प्रिय,<BR>अस्, m. ‘serpent's friend,’ wind.<BR>—फणि-फेण, अस्,<BR>m. ‘snake's saliva,’ opium (= अहि-फेण).<BR>—फणि-<BR>भारिका, f. the tree Ficus Oppositifolia (= फ-<BR>णिका).<BR>—फणि-भाष्य, अम्, n. the commentary<BR>of Patañjali (= महा-भाष्य).<BR>—फणि-भुज्, क्,<BR>m. ‘serpent-eater,’ a peacock.<BR>—फणि-मुख,<BR>अम्, n. ‘serpent's mouth,’ a kind of spade used by<BR>housebreakers.<BR>—फणि-लता or फणि-वल्ली, f. betel-<BR>pepper (= नाग-वल्ली).<BR>—फणि-हन्त्री, f. the plant<BR>with which the ichneumon is said to cure itself after<BR>the bite of a snake (= गन्ध-नाकुली).<BR>—फणि-<BR>हृत्, त्, f. a kind of plant (= क्षुद्रा दुर्-आलभा).<BR>—फणीन्द्र (˚णि-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘serpent-chief,’ an<BR>epithet of the serpent-demon Śeṣa; an epithet of<BR>Patañjali (= फणिन्).<BR>—फणीन्द्रेश्वर(˚र-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the eight Vīta-rāgas of the<BR>Buddhists; [cf. फणिकेश्वर.]<BR>—फणीश (˚णि-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. ‘serpent-chief,’ an epithet of Patañjali<BR>(= फणिन्).<BR>—फणीश्वर (˚णि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘ser-<BR>pent-chief,’ an epithet of the serpent-demon Śeṣa;<BR>an epithet of Patañjali (= फणिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणीय
फणीय, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?), Cerasus Puddum<BR>(= पद्म-काष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण्ड|फंडः|फण्डः
फण्ड, अस्, m. the belly (= फाण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिखेल|फणिखेलः
फणिखेल फणिखेल, अस्, m. a quail; (pro-<BR>bably incorrectly for फाल-खेला.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिज्झक|फणिज्झकः
फणिज्झक फणिज्झक, अस्, m. marjoram<BR>and another similar plant; (आ), f. a plant, apparently<BR>a species of basil with small leaves (commonly called<BR>राम-दूति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणी
फणी फणी, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फत्
फत् फत्, ind. an interjection, in फत्-कृ<BR>probably an error for फुत्-कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फत्कारिन्
फत्-कारिन्, ई, m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फतिहशाह
फतिहशाह फतिह-शाह, N. of a king of<BR>Kaśmīra (= شاه فتح).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फतेपुर
