फल्
फल् फल्, cl. 1. P. फलति, पफाल<BR>(3rd pl. फेलुस्), फलिष्यति, अफालीत्,<BR>फलितुम्, to split (intrans.) cleave asunder, burst,<BR>cleave open (intrans.), burst open, burst asunder<BR>(Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 7472); to bear fruit, yield<BR>or produce fruit, (सम्पदः फल्, to bring forth<BR>successes as fruit, have a reward); to be fruitful; to have<BR>results or consequences; to result; to succeed; to be<BR>fruitful in, be fulfilled by (with abl.); to fall to the<BR>share of any one (with loc.), befall; to be useful;<BR>to become ripe, ripen; to produce; to shine back,<BR>be reflected; to go (for पल्): Caus. फालयति, अपी-<BR>फलत्: Desid. पिफलिषति: Intens. पम्फुल्यते,<BR>पम्फुल्ति; [cf. Gr. ἐκ-φλαίν-ω, ἔ-φλαδ-ον, φλα-σ-μό-ς<BR>πα-φλάζ-ω; perhaps ὄφελος, ὀφέλλω: Lat.<BR>fla-re, fla-tu-s, flâ-men, flâ-bru-m, flô-s, flôr-eo,<BR>Flora: Osc. Flusa: Goth. uf-blês-an, bloth, blô-<BR>ma: Old Germ. blâ-an, ‘to blow;’ blus-jan, ‘to<BR>bloom;’ bluot, ‘a blossom;’ blâs, ‘blowing;’ blâsa,<BR>bla-tara, ‘bladder;’ bluot, ‘blood;’ bloz, ‘proud:’<BR>Angl. Sax. blowan, bloma, blostma: Cambro-Brit.<BR>pâl, ‘a spread;’ palad, ‘a shooting or spreading<BR>out;’ paladu, ‘to spread or shoot out.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल|फलं|फलः
फल, अम्, n. a fruit, fruit (especially that of a<BR>tree); produce, crop; a kernel, (दाडिम-फ्˚, the<BR>kernel of a pomegranate); fruit metaphorically,<BR>offspring, progeny, a child (Raghu-v. XIV. 39); a<BR>result, consequence, effect [cf. निष्-फ्˚, पुण्य-फ्˚,<BR>पुरः-फ्˚]; profit, gain, interest on capital, ad-<BR>vantage, benefit, utility; recompense, reward, prize,<BR>meed, retribution (good or bad); detriment, loss,<BR>disadvantage; (in mathematics) the result of a cal-<BR>culation, product or quotient, result (in trigonome-<BR>try); second term in a rule of three sum; corrective<BR>equation; area or superficial contents of a figure;<BR>a nutmeg; the three myrobalans (= त्रि-फला); a<BR>testicle; a blade (of a sword or knife, cf. खड्ग-<BR>फ्˚); a tablet, board [cf. शारि-फ्˚]; a shield; the<BR>point of an arrow, head of a dart or spear; a point<BR>or spot on a die; a ploughshare (= फाल); the<BR>menstrual discharge [cf. नव-फलिका, पुष्प];<BR>a gift, giving; (अस्), m. the plant Wrightia Antidy-<BR>senterica, = कुटज; (आ), f. a species of shrub, =<BR>झिञ्झिरिष्टा; (ई), f. a species of fragrant plant<BR>(= फलिनी, प्रियङ्गु); a kind of fish (= फलि).<BR>—फल-कक्ष, अस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—फल-<BR>कण्टका, f. the plant Asclepias Echinata.<BR>—फल-<BR>कामना, f. desire of a result or consequence.<BR>—फल-काल, अस्, m. the time of fruits, fruit<BR>season.<BR>—फल-कृष्ण, अस्, m. Carissa Carandas<BR>or Flacourtia Cataphracta (= कृष्ण-पाक-फल).<BR>—फल-केशर, अस्, m. ‘having fruit for hair,’<BR>the cocoa-nut tree (the fruit of which is covered<BR>with a fibrous coat resembling hair).<BR>—फल-कोश<BR>or फल-कोषक, अस्, m. the covering of the<BR>testicles, the scrotum.<BR>—फल-खण्डन, अम्, n.<BR>the destruction of fruits, frustration of results, dis-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-a" target="_blank">Page0669-a+ 81</a>]<BR>appointing.<BR>—फल-ग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘receiving<BR>fruits,’ deriving profit or advantage, benefited; (अस्),<BR>m. the deriving profit or advantage, being benefited.<BR>—फल-ग्रहि, इस्, इस्, इ, fruitful, bearing fruit in due<BR>season.<BR>—फल-ग्रहिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, fruit-bearing,<BR>fruitful.<BR>—फल-ग्राहिन्, ई, m. ‘fruit-bearer,’ a tree<BR>(properly a fruit tree).<BR>—फल-घृत, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>‘fruit-ghee,’ N. of an aphrodisiac for men (which<BR>is composed of various ingredients, and said to be<BR>the invention of Bharad-vāja); N. of a powerful me-<BR>dicament used in diseases of the uterus.<BR>—फल-<BR>चमस, अस्, m. ‘fruit-goblet,’ a cup containing<BR>fruit instead of Soma (Ved. the fruit consisting of<BR>pounded figs, young leaves, and sour milk); the bark<BR>of the Indian fig-tree (ground and eaten with curds<BR>by way of penance).<BR>—फल-चारक, अस्, m. ‘fruit-<BR>distributor,’ a particular official in Buddhist monasteries.<BR>—फल-चोरक, अस्, m. a kind of perfume.<BR>—फ-<BR>ल-च्छदन, अम्, n. a house built of wooden boards.<BR>—फल-तस्, ind. consequently, accordingly, virtu-<BR>ally.<BR>—फल-ता, f. or फल-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>fruit, the state of fruit.<BR>—फल-त्रय, अम्, n. ‘fruit-<BR>triad,’ three sorts of fruit collectively (the fruit of the<BR>vine with those of Grewia Asiatica or Xylocarpus Gra-<BR>natum and Gmelina Arborea); the three myrobalans.<BR>—फल-त्रिक, अम्, n. ‘fruit-triad,’ the three myro-<BR>balans.<BR>—फल-द, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘fruit-giving,’ yield-<BR>ing or bearing fruit; bringing profit or gain; giving<BR>a reward, rewarding; (अस्), m. a tree (properly a<BR>fruit tree).<BR>—फल-दातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or फल-<BR>दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘fruit-giving,’ yielding fruit; giving<BR>a result.<BR>—फल-निर्वृत्ति, इस्, f. final consequence<BR>or result.<BR>—फल-निवृत्ति, इस्, f. cessation of con-<BR>sequences.<BR>—फल-निष्पत्ति, इस्, f. production of<BR>fruit, bearing fruit, yielding profit, having the desired<BR>results.<BR>—फल-पञ्चाम्ल, अम्, n. a collection of<BR>five kinds of acid vegetables and fruits; (see फ-<BR>लाम्ल-पञ्चक.)<BR>—फल-परिणति, इस्, f. the ripe-<BR>ness of fruit.<BR>—फल-पाक, अस्, m. the ripening of<BR>fruit; the fulness of consequences; Carissa Carandas<BR>or Flacourtia Cataphracta; [cf. पाक-फल and<BR>कृष्ण-पाकफल.]<BR>—फलपाकान्त (˚क-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ending with the ripening of fruit; (आ),<BR>f. an annual plant.<BR>—फलपाकावसाना (˚क-अव्˚),<BR>f. ‘terminating with ripeness of fruit,’ an annual plant.<BR>—फलपाकिन्, ई, m. the plant Thespesia Popul-<BR>neoides.<BR>—फल-पातन, अम्, n. knocking down<BR>or gathering fruit.<BR>—फल-पादप, अस्, m. a fruit<BR>tree.<BR>—फल-पुच्छ, अस्, m. a particular species<BR>of esculent root or bulb.<BR>—फल-पुर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a city (= फलक-पुर).<BR>—फल-<BR>पुष्प-वृद्धि, इस्, f. increase or growth of fruits<BR>and flowers.<BR>—फल-पुष्पा or फल-पुष्पी, f.<BR>Ipomœa Turpethum (= पिण्ड-खर्जूरी).<BR>—फल-<BR>पुष्पोपशोभित (˚प-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, adorned<BR>with fruits and flowers.<BR>—फल-पूर or फल-<BR>पूरक, अस्, m. ‘full of kernels,’ common citron.<BR>—फल-प्रचयन, अम्, n. fruit-gathering, gather-<BR>ing fruits.<BR>—फल-प्रजनन, अम्, n. the produc-<BR>tion of fruit.<BR>—फल-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, yielding<BR>fruit, productive; bringing a reward.<BR>—फल-प्र-<BR>दान, अम्, n. the giving of fruits; a ceremony at<BR>weddings.<BR>—फल-प्रयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, connected<BR>with or producing consequences, yielding fruit.<BR>—फल-प्रसूति, इस्, f. a growth of fruit, crop of<BR>fruit.<BR>—फल-प्राप्ति, इस्, f. obtaining (the desired)<BR>fruit or result; enjoying the consequences of actions.<BR>—फल-प्रिया, f. a species of fragrant plant (=<BR>प्रियङ्गु).<BR>—फल-प्रेप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to<BR>obtain fruit, desirous of attaining results.<BR>—फल-<BR>बन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, forming or developing fruit,<BR>setting (said of blossom).<BR>—फल-बन्ध्य, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, barren or destitute of fruit, not bearing fruit;<BR>[cf. फलाबन्ध्य.]<BR>—फल-भाग, अस्, m. a<BR>share in any product, share of advantage or profit;<BR>N. of an astrological work.<BR>—फल-भागिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, sharing in the profit or advantage, partaking of a<BR>reward.<BR>—फल-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, receiving or having<BR>fruit, having consequences; sharing in a reward.<BR>—फल-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, enjoying fruit.<BR>—फल-<BR>भूति, इस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—फल-भूमि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-b" target="_blank">Page0669-b+ 81</a>]<BR>इस्, f. ‘the land of retribution,’ a place of reward or<BR>recompense (as heaven, hell, &c.).<BR>—फल-भृत्,<BR>त्, त्, त्, fruit-bearing, fruitful, productive.<BR>—फल-<BR>भोग, अस्, m. enjoyment of consequences; possession<BR>of rent or profit, usufruct.<BR>—फल-भोगिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, enjoying fruits or consequences, receiving profits.<BR>—फल-मत्स्या, f. the aloe plant.<BR>—फल-मु-<BR>ख्या, f. a species of plant (= अज-मोदा).<BR>—फल-<BR>मुद्गरिका, f. a kind of date tree (= पिण्ड-खर्-<BR>जूरी).<BR>—फल-मूल, अम्, n. or ए, n. du. or आनि,<BR>n. pl. fruits and roots.<BR>—फलमूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>having (edible) fruits and roots.<BR>—फल-योग, अस्,<BR>m. the attainment of an object; remuneration, wages.<BR>—फल-राजन्, आ, m. ‘king of the fruits,’ a water-<BR>melon.<BR>—फल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, fruit-bearing, fruc-<BR>tiferous, covered or laden with fruits, fruitful; yielding<BR>results or consequences, successful, profitable, advan-<BR>tageous; containing the result or end of a plot; (अती),<BR>f. a species of plant (= प्रियङ्गु; cf. फलिनी).<BR>—फलवत्-त्व, अम्, n. or फलवत्-ता, f. fruit-<BR>fulness, beneficial results or consequences.<BR>—फल-<BR>वर्ति, इस्, f. (in medicine) a suppository.<BR>—फल-<BR>वर्तुल, अम्, n. a water-melon; (probably अस्, m.),<BR>the plant Gardenia Latifolia.<BR>—फल-वल्ली, f. a<BR>series of quotients in the solution of certain arith-<BR>metical problems.<BR>—फल-विक्रयिन्, ई, इणी, m. f. a<BR>fruit-seller, fruiterer, dealer in fruits.<BR>—फल-वृक्-<BR>ष, अस्, m. a fruit tree.<BR>—फल-वृक्षक, अस्, m.<BR>the bread-fruit tree.<BR>—फल-शाडव, अस्, m. the<BR>pomegranate tree.<BR>—फलशालि-त्व, अम्, n. the bear-<BR>ing of fruit; experience of consequences or results.<BR>—फल-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, bearing or yielding fruit;<BR>experiencing consequences, sharing in results.<BR>—फ-<BR>ल-शैशिर, अस्, m. Zizyphus Jujuba (= बदर).<BR>—फल-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘best of fruits,’ the<BR>mango tree.<BR>—फल-संस्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, bearing<BR>fruit.<BR>—फल-सम्पद्, त्, f. abundance of fruit,<BR>good result, success, prosperity.<BR>—फल-सम्बद्-<BR>ध, अस्, m. ‘fruit-endowed,’ the tree Ficus Glome-<BR>rata.<BR>—फल-सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, or फल-<BR>सम्भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, produced in or by fruit.<BR>—फ-<BR>ल-सम्भारा, f. ‘having an abundance of fruit,’ the<BR>tree Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR>—फल-सहस्र, अम्, n.<BR>a thousand fruits; (ए), n. du. two thousand fruits.<BR>—फल-साधन, अम्, n. a means of effecting any<BR>result.<BR>—फल-सिद्धि, इस्, f. acquiring fruit, reaping<BR>fruit, realising an object; a prosperous issue.<BR>—फल-<BR>स्थान, अम्, n. the stage in which fruits or results<BR>are enjoyed.<BR>—फल-स्नेह, अस्, m. ‘having oil in<BR>the fruit,’ a walnut tree.<BR>—फल-हानि, इस्, f. loss<BR>of fruit or profit.<BR>—फल-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, fruit-<BR>seizing, stealing fruits.<BR>—फल-हारी, f. an epithet<BR>of Kālī (a form of Durgā).<BR>—फल-हीन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, void of fruit, yielding no profit.<BR>—फल-<BR>हेतु, उस्, उस्, उ, one who has results for a motive,<BR>acting with a view to results.<BR>—फलाकाङ्क्षा<BR>(˚ल-आक्˚), f. hope or expectation of favourable con-<BR>sequences.<BR>—फलाकाङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, desirous of<BR>results, wishing for favourable consequences.<BR>—फ-<BR>लागम (˚ल-आग्˚), अस्, m. ‘arrival of fruits,’ the fruit<BR>season, autumn.<BR>—फलाढ्या (˚ल-आढ्˚), f. ‘rich<BR>in fruit,’ a variety of the plantain (= काष्ठ-कदली).<BR>—फलादन (˚ल-अद्˚), अस्, m. ‘fruit-eater,’ a<BR>parrot; [cf. फलाशन.]<BR>—फलाध्यक्ष (˚ल-<BR>अध्˚), अम्, n. ‘superintendant of fruits,’ the tree<BR>Mimusops Kauki.<BR>—फलानुबन्ध (˚ल-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. sequence or succession of results, consequences,<BR>results.<BR>—फलानुमेय (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, in-<BR>ferable from consequences or results.<BR>—फलानुस-<BR>रण (˚ल-अन्˚), अम्, n. rate or aggregate of profits.<BR>—फलान्त (˚ल-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘ending with fruit,’<BR>a bamboo (which dies away after bearing fruit).<BR>—फलान्वेषिन् (˚ल-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, seeking fruits<BR>or results, looking for a reward.<BR>—फलापेक्षा<BR>(˚ल-अप्˚), f. regard to results, expectation of conse-<BR>quences.<BR>—फलापेत (˚ल-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, de-<BR>prived of fruit, unproductive, unfertile.<BR>—फलाफ-<BR>लिका (˚ल-अफ्˚), f., see Gaṇa Śāka-pārthivādi to<BR>Vārttika to Pāṇ. II. 1, 69.<BR>—फलाबन्ध्य (˚ल-<BR>अब्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, not barren of fruit, bearing fruit;<BR>[cf. फल-बन्ध्य.]<BR>—फलाभोग (˚ल-अभ्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-c" target="_blank">Page0669-c+ 81</a>]<BR>अस्, m. non-enjoyment of profits, &c.<BR>—फलाम्ल<BR>(˚ल-अम्˚), अस्, m. a species of sorrel, Rumex Vesi-<BR>carius; (अम्), n. a tamarind.<BR>—फलाम्ल-पञ्चक<BR>(˚ल-अम्˚), अम्, n. the five acid or sour fruits, viz.<BR>bergamot, orange, sorrel, tamarind, and citron; [cf.<BR>अम्ल-पञ्च and फल-पञ्चाम्ल.]<BR>—फलाम्-<BR>लिक, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) accompanied with sauce<BR>prepared from sour tamarind juice.<BR>—फलाराम<BR>(˚ल-आर्˚), अस्, m. a fruit-garden, orchard.<BR>—फला-<BR>शन (˚ल-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘fruit-eater,’ a parrot; [cf.<BR>फलादन.]<BR>—फलाशिन् (˚ल-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, feed-<BR>ing or living on fruits.<BR>—फलासक्त (˚ल-आस्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, attached to fruit or results, acting for the<BR>sake of reward; fond of fruit, seeking to pluck fruit.<BR>—फलासव (˚ल-आस्˚), अस्, m. a decoction of<BR>fruits.<BR>—फलास्थि (˚ल-अस्˚), इ, n. ‘having a hard<BR>kernel for fruit,’ a cocoa-nut.<BR>—फलाहार (˚ल-आह्˚),<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, feeding or living on fruits, gathering<BR>fruits.<BR>—फले-ग्रहि or फले-ग्राहि, इस्, इस्, इ, or<BR>फले-ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bearing fruit in season, fruitful<BR>(= फल-ग्रहि).<BR>—फलेन्द्र (˚ल-इन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘fruit-king,’ a species of Eugenia (= राज-जम्बू).<BR>—फले-पाक, फले-पाका, फले-पाकु, see Gaṇa<BR>to Pāṇ. VII. 3, 53.<BR>—फले-पुष्पा, f. a kind of small<BR>shrub (= द्रोण-पुष्पी).<BR>—फले-रुहा, f. the<BR>trumpet-flower, Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—फलोच्चय<BR>(˚ल-उच्˚), अस्, m. the collecting of fruits, a collection<BR>of fruits.<BR>—फलोत्तमा (˚ल-उत्˚), f. ‘best of fruits,’<BR>a kind of grape without stones (= काकली-द्राक्षा);<BR>a black grape; the three myrobalans (= त्रि-फला);<BR>the benefit arising from sacred study (?); a small<BR>sort of rope (?).<BR>—फलोत्पति (˚ल-उत्˚), इस्, m.<BR>the mango tree; (perhaps incorrectly for फलोत्-<BR>पत्ति.)<BR>—फलोत्पत्ति (˚ल-उत्˚), इस्, f. production<BR>of fruit, profit, gain, advantage.<BR>—फलोदक (˚ल-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa.<BR>—फलोदय (˚ल-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. coming forth or appearance of fruit;<BR>profit, advantage, gain; appearance of consequences<BR>or results, consequence, result, recompense, reward,<BR>retribution, punishment; happiness, joy; heaven,<BR>paradise.<BR>—फलोद्गम (˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. the pro-<BR>duction of fruit, appearance of fruit.<BR>—फलोद्देश<BR>(˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, m. regard to results.<BR>—फलोद्भव<BR>(˚ल-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, obtained or derived from fruits.<BR>—फलोपजीविन् (˚ल-उप्˚), ई, इनी, इ, living by the<BR>cultivation or sale of fruits.<BR>—फलोपेत (˚ल-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, possessing fruits, yielding fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0668-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलक|फलकं|फलकः
फलक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp., f. इका), = फल, fruit, result, consequence,<BR>profit, gain; menstruation [cf. नव-फलिकी]; a<BR>shield; (अस्), m. the plant Mesua Roxburghii;<BR>(अम्), n. a board, lath, plank, a bench; a slab at the<BR>base (of a pedestal; cf. स्फटिक-फ्˚); any flat sur-<BR>face [cf. फणा-फ्˚]; a slab or tablet for writing on<BR>[cf. चित्र-फ्˚, लिपि-फ्˚]; a leaf or page for writing<BR>on; the stand on which a Buddhist priest keeps<BR>his turban; a broad and flat bone, the os frontis or<BR>bone of the forehead; the palm of the hand; the<BR>buttocks; a particular vessel; a kind of cloth; the<BR>top or head of an arrow; the pericarp of a lotus;<BR>(आ), f. a various reading for हलका in Gaṇa Prek-<BR>ṣādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR>—फलक-पाणि, इस्, m. a<BR>soldier armed with a shield.<BR>—फलक-पुर, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a town in the east of India; [cf. फल-<BR>पुर.]<BR>—फलक-यन्त्र, अम्, n. an astronomical<BR>instrument invented by Bhāskara.<BR>—फलक-सक्-<BR>थ, अम्, n. a thigh like a board, (Scholiast on Pāṇ.<BR>V. 4, 98.)<BR>—फलका-वन or फलकी-वन, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a forest sacred to Sarasvatī.<BR>—फलकासा-<BR>दन (˚क-आस्˚), अम्, n. the obtaining or reaching a<BR>plank (said of a drowning person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकिन्
फलकिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having boards, boarded; armed<BR>with a shield; (ई), m. a wooden bench; a kind of fish,<BR>= फलि; (ई, इ), m. n. sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्
फलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bearing or yielding fruit;<BR>producing consequences; bringing gain or profit.<BR>—फलज्-जल-वासुदेव, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलन|फलनं
फलन, अम्, n. bearing fruit, fructifying; pro-<BR>ducing consequences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलस|फलसः
फलस, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed of fruit ?; (अस्),<BR>m. the bread-fruit or Jaka tree (= पनस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0669-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलही
फलही, f. the cotton tree, cotton plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलि|फलिः
फलि, इस्, m. a kind of fish commonly Phalai.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिका
फलिका, f. a kind of bean (= निष्-पावी); Thes-<BR>pesia Populneoides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलित|फलितं|फलितः
फलित, अस्, आ, अम्, that has produced fruit,<BR>bearing fruit, yielding fruit, fruitful; yielding a result,<BR>followed by a consequence, successful; fulfilled, ac-<BR>complished (as a desire); produced as a consequence;<BR>फलितं वृक्षैः, fruit was borne by the trees,<BR>the trees bore fruit; (अस्), m. a tree (properly a<BR>fruit tree); (आ), f. a menstruous woman; (अम्), n.<BR>a kind of perfume (= शैलेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलितव्य
फलितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be accompanied by<BR>fruits or good consequences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिन्
फलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, fruitful, bearing fruit, (at the<BR>end of comps.; cf. सत्-फ्˚); productive of results<BR>or consequences, advantageous, profitable; having<BR>an iron point (as an arrow); (ई), m. a tree, espe-<BR>cially one in fruit; (इनी), f. a medicinal plant (=<BR>प्रियङ्गु); a species of herb, Echites Dichotoma;<BR>a species of flower, Celosia Cristata; फलिनी योनिः,<BR>(in medicine) the vagina injured by too violent<BR>sexual intercourse.<BR>—फलि-ग, अस्, m., Ved. a cloud,<BR>(perhaps ‘a receptacle for water;’ Sāy. फलि =<BR>वृष्टि-जल, rain-water.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिन|फलिनः
फलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, fruitful, bearing or yielding<BR>fruit; (अस्), m. the bread-fruit tree (= पनस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलीकृ
फली-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. फली-करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, Ved. to separate the fruit or grain from<BR>the husks, to winnow, thresh, (according to a Scholiast<BR>फली-करोति = अवहत्य सूक्ष्म-तुषेभ्यो वि-<BR>योजयति.)<BR>—फली-करण, अम्, n. or फली-कार,<BR>अस्, m. separating the grain from the husks, the<BR>grain (of rice &c.) separated from the husks.<BR>—फ-<BR>ली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, threshed, winnowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलीय
फलीय, see Gaṇa Utkarādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्य|फल्यं
फल्य, अम्, n. a flower, a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल|फालं|फालः
फाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. a ploughshare, (Sāy. =<BR>भूमि-विदारक-काष्ठ); a kind of hoe or<BR>shovel; a bundle; the forehead; (अस्), m. a citron<BR>tree; an epithet of Mahā-deva; of Bala-rāma; =<BR>उत्-प्लुति; (अस्, ई, अम्), made of cotton (as a gar-<BR>ment; in this sense perhaps fr. फल).<BR>—फाल-<BR>कृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, tilled with the plough, ploughed,<BR>furrowed; growing on arable land, produced by<BR>cultivation; (अम्), n. ploughed or cultivated soil, a<BR>ploughed field; अ-फालकृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, grow-<BR>ing on uncultivated soil, growing wild.<BR>—फाल-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘ploughshare-defended,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Bala-rāma; [cf. हलायुध.]<BR>—फाल-दती,<BR>f. ‘having teeth like ploughshares,’ N. of a female<BR>demon.<BR>—फालाहत (˚ल-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘struck<BR>with the ploughshare,’ ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फालीकरण
फालीकरण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. फली-करण),<BR>Ved. made of husks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ति|फुल्तिः
फुल्ति, इस्, f. full expansion or perfection (?); see<BR>Vopa-deva XXVI. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल|फुल्लः
फुल्ल, अस्, आ, अम् (past pass. part. of rt. फल्<BR>by Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 55), ‘split or cleft open,’ open,<BR>expanded, blown (as a flower); in full bloom,<BR>flowering, flowery, in blossom, covered with flowers;<BR>opened wide, dilated (as the eyes); smiling, gay;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a saint; (अम्), n. a full-blown<BR>flower; [cf. Gr. φύλλο-ν; Lat. foliu-m.]<BR>—फुल्ल-<BR>तुवरी, f. alum.<BR>—फुल्ल-दामन्, अ, n. ‘flowery<BR>garland,’ a kind of metre, four times ¯¯¯¯¯,<BR>˘˘˘˘˘˘¯, ¯˘¯¯˘¯¯, (also called पुष्प-<BR>दामन्, q. v.)<BR>—फुल्ल-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, or फुल्ल-<BR>नयन, or फुल्ल-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having full<BR>or large eyes, having the eyes dilated (with pleasure),<BR>smiling, happy.<BR>—फुल्ल-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city.<BR>—फुल्ल-फाल, अस्, m. the wind raised in<BR>winnowing corn (= फल्ल-फल).<BR>—फुल्ल-लो-<BR>चन, अस्, आ, अम्, having the eyes dilated, looking<BR>pleased or happy; full-eyed; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>antelope; (अम्), n. a large full eye.<BR>—फुल्ल-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, expanded, blossoming, blowing.<BR>—फुल्-<BR>ल-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘smiling-faced,’ looking<BR>pleased or happy.<BR>—फुल्लाम्बिका (˚ल-अम्˚), f., N.<BR>of a woman, wife of Go-vinda and mother of Nīla-<BR>kaṇṭha Catur-dhara.<BR>—फुल्लारण्य-माहात्म्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">Page0670-b+ 76</a>]<BR>(˚ल-अर्˚), अम्, n., N. of a section of the Agni-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—फुल्लोत्पल (˚ल-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘whose<BR>lotuses are in full bloom,’ N. of a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लि|फुल्लिः
फुल्लि, इस्, f. blossoming, blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलय
फलय फलय (?), अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसतीण
फलसतीण फलसतीण, N. of a country<BR>(Palestine ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलहक|फलहकः
फलहक फलहक, अस्, m. a plank, board<BR>(= फलक); N. of a place (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलायोषित्
फलायोषित् फलायोषित्, त्, f. a cricket;<BR>[cf. फडिङ्गा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलूष|फलूषः
फलूष फलूष, अस्, m. a species of creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोनि
फलोनि फलोनि (?), pudenda muliebria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्क|फल्कः
फल्क फल्क, अस्, आ, अम्, having an expanded<BR>or extended body, = विसारिताङ्ग; = विशोधिताङ्क;<BR>[cf. Gr. φολκός.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गु|फल्गुः
फल्गु फल्गु, उस्, उस् (ऊस्, Vājasaneyi-saṃ-<BR>hitā XXIV. 4), उ (said to be fr. rt. फल्; perhaps<BR>fr. rt. स्फुर्ज्), reddish (this meaning is Vedic and<BR>is doubtful; cf. फल्गुन); small, minute; pithless,<BR>sapless, unsubstantial, (opposed to सार); worthless,<BR>vain, unprofitable, unmeaning, useless; flimsy, weak,<BR>feeble, insignificant; untrue; (उस्), f. the opposite-<BR>leaved fig-tree, Ficus Oppositifolia; a red powder<BR>usually of the root of wild ginger (coloured with<BR>sappan wood and thrown over one another by the<BR>Hindūs at the Holī festival; cf. फल्गूत्सव, हो-<BR>लाका); the spring season; N. of a river flowing past<BR>Gayā; (ऊ), f. du., N. of a Nakṣatra.<BR>—फल्गु-<BR>ता, f. or फल्गु-त्व, अम्, n. worthlessness, vain-<BR>ness, vanity, uselessness, insignificance.<BR>—फल्गु-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place near<BR>Gayā.<BR>—फल्गु-द, अस्, आ, अम्, giving little, nig-<BR>gardly; (आ), f., N. of a river (= फल्गु).<BR>—फल्गु-प्रासह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having little<BR>strength.<BR>—फल्गु-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (?), insignificant,<BR>worthless, weak.<BR>—फल्गु-वाटिका, f. the opposite-<BR>leaved fig-tree, Ficus Oppositifolia.<BR>—फल्गु-वृन्त,<BR>अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?) , a species of Symplocos.<BR>—फल्गु-वृन्ताक, अस्, m. a species of Colosan-<BR>thes.<BR>—फल्गु-हस्तिनी, f., N. of a poetess.<BR>—फल्-<BR>गूत्सव (˚गु-उत्˚), अस्, m. the vernal festival, com-<BR>monly called Holī, in honour of Kṛṣṇa, at which<BR>the people throw a red powder over one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुण
फल्गुण, फल्गुणक, incorrect forms for<BR>फल्गुन, फल्गुनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुन|फल्गुनः
फल्गुन, अस्, ई, अम्, red; born under the Nak-<BR>ṣatra Phalgunī; (अस्), m. the month Phalguna (=<BR>फाल्गुन); an epithet of Arjuna (= फाल्गुन);<BR>N. of a man; (ई), f., N. of a double Nakṣatra (q. v.)<BR>also called अर्जुनी; the opposite-leaved fig-tree, Ficus<BR>Oppositifolia; N. of a woman.<BR>—फल्गुन-स्वामिन्,<BR>ई, m., N. of a temple built by Phalguna.<BR>—फल्-<BR>गुनी-भव, अस्, m. an epithet of the planet Jupiter<BR>(= फाल्गुनी-भव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुनक
फल्गुनक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुनाल|फल्गुनालः
फल्गुनाल, अस्, m. the month Phalguna (=<BR>फाल्गुनाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुलुक
फल्गुलुक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्ग्व
फल्ग्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. insignificant, frivolous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुण
फाल्गुण, an incorrect form for फाल्गुन below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुन|फाल्गुनः
फाल्गुन, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the Nakṣatra<BR>Phalgunī; born under the Nakṣatra Phalgunī;<BR>(अस्), m., scil. मास, the month during which the<BR>full moon stands in the Nakṣatra Phalgunī (February<BR>-March); an epithet of Arjuna [cf. फल्गुन];<BR>the plant Terminalia Arjuna, = नदी-ज; (ई), f., N. of<BR>the sixteenth and seventeenth lunar asterisms (dis-<BR>tinguished as पूर्वा and उत्तरा, ‘the former’ and<BR>‘the latter,’ = फल्गुनी); scil. पौर्णमासी, the<BR>day of full moon in the month Phālguna on which<BR>the Holī or great vernal festival of the Hindūs is<BR>celebrated; (अम्), n. a species of grass used as a<BR>substitute for the Soma plant (and also called अर्जु-<BR>नानी); N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—फाल्गुना-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">Page0670-c+ 69</a>]<BR>नुज (˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘younger brother of the<BR>month Phālguna,’ the vernal month Caitra.<BR>—फाल्-<BR>गुनी-पौर्णमासी, f. the day of full moon in the<BR>month Phālguna.<BR>—फाल्गुनी-भव, अस्, m. an<BR>epithet of the planet Jupiter (= फल्गुनी-भव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनाल|फाल्गुनालः
फाल्गुनाल, अस्, m. the month Phālguna (=<BR>फल्गुनाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनि
फाल्गुनि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Phālguna (=<BR>अर्जुन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनिक|फाल्गुनिकः
फाल्गुनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the Nakṣa-<BR>tra Phalgunī or to the day of full moon in the month<BR>Phālguna; (अस्), m., scil. मास, the month Phālguna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुन्य
फाल्गुन्य, अस्, m. a metronymic from Phalgunī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्लकिन्
फल्लकिन् फल्लकिन्, ई, m. a kind of fish<BR>(= फलकिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्लफल|फल्लफलः
फल्लफल फल्ल-फल, अस्, m. = फुल्ल-<BR>फाल (probably onomatopoetic), the wind raised in<BR>winnowing grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फषाजिग
फषाजिग फषाजिग and फषाजिम, N.<BR>of two places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फा
