फिरङ्ग|फिरंग|फिरंगः|फिरङ्गः
फिरङ्ग फिरङ्ग, अस्, m. the country of the<BR>Franks (i. e. of Europeans); the disease of the Franks,<BR>syphilis.<BR>—फिरङ्ग-रोटी, f. European bread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फिरङ्गिन्|फिरंगिन्
फिरङ्गिन्, ई, m. a Frank, a European.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फिराल
फिराल फिराल, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फिरिण्ड
फिरिण्ड फिरिण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फु|फुः
फु फु, उस्, m. a magical formula; useless<BR>or idle talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0670-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुक|फुकः
फुक फुक, अस्, m. a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुट|फुटः
फुट फुट, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. the hood or<BR>expanded neck of a snake (= फट, फण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुट्टिका
फुट्टिका फुट्टिका, f. a sort of woven texture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्
फुत् फुत् or फूत्, an onomatopoetic word<BR>imitative of the sound made by blowing or puffing<BR>into liquids, or by the boiling or bubbling of water,<BR>&c.; sometimes expressive of disregard or contempt;<BR>(used only in connection with rt. कृ.)<BR>—फुत्-कर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘making a blowing or crackling noise,’ fire.<BR>—फुत्-कर्तु-मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, wishing to make<BR>a derisory noise, intending to cry aloud.<BR>—फुत्-<BR>कार or फूत्-कार, अस्, m. blowing, hissing, whiz-<BR>zing; the hiss of a serpent; shouting loudly, shriek-<BR>ing, screaming.<BR>—फुत्कार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, hissing;<BR>shrieking.<BR>—फुत्-कार्य in अ-फुत्कार्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>requiring no blowing.<BR>—फुत्-कृ or फूत्-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to blow, blow into; to<BR>scream, shriek, screech.<BR>—फुत्-कृत or फूत्-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, blown, blown on, blown into, breathed<BR>in, cooled by blowing into; blown up (as a bubble);<BR>screamed aloud; (अम्), n. the sound of a wind<BR>instrument; a loud scream, shriek.<BR>—फुत्-कृति or<BR>फूत्-कृति, इस्, f. blowing, hissing; screaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुप्फु
फुप्फु फुप्फु, ind. an onomatopoetic word.<BR>—फुप्फु-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, panting, gasping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुप्फुस|फुप्फुसः
फुप्फुस, अस्, अम्, m. n. the lungs; [cf. पुप्-<BR>फुस; Gr. φῦ-σα, φυσά-ω.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुम्फुआ|फुंफुआ
फुम्फुआ फुम्फुआ, ind. imitation of the<BR>sound made by the crackling of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुलिङ्ग|फुलिङ्गः
फुलिङ्ग फुलिङ्ग, अस् or अम्, m. or n. (?),<BR>syphilis; [cf. फिरङ्ग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल्
फुल्ल् फुल्ल् (more properly regarded as<BR>a Nom. fr. फुल्ल), cl. 1. P. फुल्लति,<BR>पुफुल्ल, &c., to open, expand (as a flower),<BR>bloom, blossom, blow, flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लन|फुल्लनं
फुल्लन, अस्, ई, अम्, filling with air, inflating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल|फुल्लः
फुल्ल फुल्ल, फुल्ति, &c. See p. 670, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लरीक|फुल्लरीकः
फुल्लरीक फुल्लरीक, अस्, m. a district, place;<BR>a snake, serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्
फूत् फूत्, फूत्-कार, &c. See फुत् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेञ्चक|फेञ्चकः
फेञ्चक फेञ्चक, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेट्
फेट् फेट्, ind. an onomatopoetic word (=<BR>फेत्).<BR>—फेट्-कार, अस्, m. howling, a howl.<BR>—फेट्-<BR>कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, howling.<BR>—फेट्कारिणी-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work on magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेण|फेणः
फेण फेण = फेन below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेण्ट
फेण्ट फेण्ट, अस्, m. a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेत्
फेत् फेत्, ind. an onomatopoetic word.<BR>—फेत्-कार, अस्, m. howling (of the wind or of<BR>animals).<BR>—फेत्-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, howling; (इणी), f.,<BR>N. of a Tantra.<BR>—फेत्कारीय, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra.<BR>—फेत्-कृत, अम्, n. howling, a howl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेन|फेनः
फेन फेन or फेण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to<BR>be fr. फे, substituted for rt. स्फाय्, Uṇādi-s. III. 3;<BR>by some derived fr. rt. फण्), foam, froth, spume;<BR>scum [cf. दुग्ध-फ्˚, पयः-फेनी]; foam of<BR>the mouth, moisture of the lips, saliva [cf. वृषली-<BR>फेन-पीत, फणि-फ्˚]; (अस्), m. white cuttle-fish<BR>bone, os sepiæ, supposed to be indurated foam of<BR>the sea [cf. अब्धि-कफ, अब्धि-फ्˚, समुद्र-<BR>फ्˚]; N. of a son of Ushad-ratha and father of<BR>Su-tapas; (आ), f. a species of shrub, = सातला;<BR>(ई), f. a kind of food; [cf. Lat. spūma;<BR>Angl. Sax. fam, fœman; Slav. pêna, ‘foam.’]<BR>—फेन-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain near the<BR>mouth of the Indus; (also written फेण-गिरि.)<BR>—फेन-ता, f. frothiness, vapour.<BR>—फेन-दुग्धा,<BR>f. a kind of small shrub (= दुग्ध-फेनी).<BR>—फे-<BR>न-प, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘froth-drinking, foam-quaffing,’<BR>feeding on foam; (according to a Scholiast = स्वयम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">Page0671-b+ 73</a>]<BR>पतितैः फलादिभिर् जीवन्; also spelt फेण-<BR>प.)<BR>—फेन-पिण्ड, अस्, m. ‘a mass of foam,’ a<BR>mere bubble, any mere fancy, empty idea, nonentity,<BR>nonsense.<BR>—फेन-प्रख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, foam-like,<BR>resembling foam.<BR>—फेन-मेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, dis-<BR>charging frothy urine.<BR>—फेन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>frothy, foaming, bubbling.<BR>—फेन-वाहिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘carrying off the scum,’ a filtering cloth; ‘foam-<BR>bearing,’ (perhaps) the thunderbolt of Indra (Indra<BR>having used the foam of the sea for his thunderbolt<BR>to kill the demon Vṛtra); (perhaps rather) an epi-<BR>thet of Indra; [cf. फेनाशनि.]<BR>—फेनाग्र (˚न-<BR>अग्˚), अम्, n. ‘surface of foam,’ a bubble on the<BR>water.<BR>—फेनाशनि (˚न-अश्˚), इस्, m. ‘having foam<BR>for a thunderbolt,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—फेनाहार<BR>(˚न-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, living on foam, feeding on<BR>froth.<BR>—फेनोपम (˚न-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, foam-<BR>like, resembling foam (said of life).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनक|फेनकः
फेनक, अस्, m. white cuttle-fish bone, os sepiæ;<BR>(अस्, आ), m. f. a kind of pastry; ground rice boiled<BR>in water; the soap-berry?; (इका), f. a kind of pre-<BR>pared food; froth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनल|फेनलः
फेनल, अस्, आ, अम्, frothy, foamy; [cf. फेनिल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनाय
फेनाय, Nom. A. फेनायते, -यितुम्, to foam,<BR>froth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनायमान|फेनायमानः
फेनायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, foaming, frothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनिल|फेनिलं|फेनिलः
फेनिल, अस्, आ, अम्, foamy, frothy, spumous;<BR>(अस्), m. the soap plant, Sapindus Detergens; the<BR>plant Zizyphus Jujuba, = बदर; (आ), f. a species of<BR>plant (= बाम्ब, बाम्बी, जल-ब्रह्मी, सर्पाक्षी);<BR>the plant Sapindus Detergens; (अम्), n. (probably)<BR>the fruit of Sapindus Detergens; the fruit of Zizyphus<BR>Jujuba; the fruit of Madana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेन्य
फेन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. existing in foam;<BR>(Mahī-dhara) = डिण्डिरे भवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेर|फेरः
फेर फेर, अस्, m. (an onomatopoetic word;<BR>cf. फेट्, फेत्), a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरण्ड|फेरंड|फेरंडः|फेरण्डः
फेरण्ड, अस्, m. a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरल
फेरल फेरल, N. of a place; (perhaps<BR>wrongly for केरल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरव|फेरवः
फेरव फे-रव, अस्, m. (fr. फे onomato-<BR>poetic + रव), a jackal; a Rākṣasa, a goblin, a<BR>demon; (अस्, आ, अम्), fraudulent, crafty, a rogue, a<BR>cheat; malicious, noxious, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरु|फेरुः
फेरु, उस्, m. a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल्
फेल् फेल्, cl. 1. P. फेलति, &c., to go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल|फेलं
फेल फेल, अम्, आ, n. f. remnants of food,<BR>leavings of a meal, droppings from the mouth, refuse,<BR>orts; a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलि|फेलिः
फेलि, इस्, or फेली, f. remnants of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलिका
फेलिका, f. = फेलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेसल
फेसल फेसल (?), N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फौल्लि
फौल्लि फौल्लि (fr. फुल्ल), see Scholiast on<BR>Vārttika III. to Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब|बः
ब 1. ब, the twenty-third consonant of the<BR>Nāgarī alphabet and the third of the labial class, often<BR>confounded with the semivowel व्, with which some<BR>grammarians consider it optionally interchangeable.<BR>—ब-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब|बः
ब 2. ब, अस्, m. a N. of Varuṇa; water;<BR>a water-jar. According to lexicographers ब also =<BR>भग, गन्धन, वपन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंह्
बंह् बंह्, also written वंह् (related to<BR>2. बृह्), cl. 1. A. बंहते, बबंहे, बं-<BR>हिता, &c., to grow, increase: Caus. P. बंहयति,<BR>यितुम्, to cause to grow, increase, strengthen, fix,<BR>make firm; [cf. बहल, बहु, बहुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिमन्
बंहिमन्, आ, m. muchness, abundance, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिष्ठ|बंहिष्ठः
बंहिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of बहुल), very<BR>much, very many, most abundant, very abundant,<BR>very great, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहीयस्
बंहीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of बहुल), much<BR>more, more abundant, very many, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बक|बकः
बक बक, &c. See वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुर|बकुरः
बकुर बकुर, अस्, m., Ved. (according to<BR>native authorities), a thunderbolt, lightning, anything<BR>shining; perhaps ‘a horn, trumpet, or other wind<BR>instrument used in battle;’ [cf. बाकुर, बेकुरा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बगदाद
बगदाद बगदाद, N. of a city, Bagdad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बगदारु
बगदारु, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बगदाह
बगदाह, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बङ्ग
बङ्ग बङ्ग, अस्, m. the country of Bengal;<BR>(usually written वङ्ग, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बङ्गाल
बङ्गाल, अस्, m. (?), N. of the country Bengal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बज
बज बज, अस्, m., Ved. (probably) N. of a<BR>herb used as a charm against evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बट्
बट् बट्, ind. (perhaps connected with<BR>वाढम्, q. v.), Ved. (a particle of affirmation), in<BR>truth, certainly (Sāy. = सत्यम्); [cf. Zend bāṭ, bā.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बठ्
बठ् बठ् = rt. वठ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडपिला
बडपिला बडपिला, f., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवा
बडवा बडवा, f. a mare; the nymph<BR>Aśvinī or the personification of the asterism repre-<BR>sented by a horse's head; a female slave.<BR>—बड-<BR>वाग्नि (˚वा-अग्˚), इस्, or बडवानल (˚वा-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. submarine fire; (in mythology) a being consisting<BR>of flame but with the head of a mare, fabled to have<BR>sprung from the thighs of Urvā and to have been<BR>received by the ocean.<BR>—बडवा-मुख, अस्, m.<BR>submarine fire; (अम्), n. the infernal regions.<BR>—ब-<BR>डवा-सुत, औ, m. du. the two sons of Aśvinī, (see<BR>अश्विन्, अश्विनी-कुमार.)<BR>—बडवा-हृत (?), अस्,<BR>m. the paramour of a female slave, a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडा
बडा बडा or बऌआ, ind., Ved. = बट्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडाह
बडाह बडाह, अस्, m., N. of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण्
बण् बण् = rt. वण्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्
बणिज् बणिज्, क्, m. (connected with the<BR>Vedic पणि fr. rt. 2. पण्, q. v.; but in Ved. and later<BR>Sanskrit often written वणिज्), a merchant, (कु-बणिज्,<BR>a wicked merchant); a trader; the sixth of the astrono-<BR>mical periods called Karaṇa, corresponding to the half<BR>of a lunar day; (क्), f. trade, traffic.<BR>—बणिक्-पथ,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘a trader's path or line,’ traffic, com-<BR>merce; (अस्), m. a merchant.<BR>—बणिक्-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m. a merchant's son, son of a trader, a young mer-<BR>chant or trader; (ई), f. a merchant's daughter, a<BR>young woman of the merchant class.<BR>—बणिग्-बन्-<BR>धु, उस्, m. ‘trader's friend,’ the indigo plant, Indi-<BR>gofera Tinctoria.<BR>—बणिग्-भाव, अस्, अम्, m. n. the<BR>state of being a merchant, traffic, trade, commerce.<BR>—बणिग्-वह, अस्, m. ‘carrying merchants,’ a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्य|बणिज्यं
बणिज्य, अम्, आ, n. f. (for बाणिज्य), trade, traffic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण्ड|बण्डः
बण्ड बण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्. See वण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बत
बत 1. बत, ind. (in the later language<BR>वत), Ved. an interjection of astonishment, sorrow,<BR>or regret, generally translatable by ah! oh! O! alas!<BR>alack! wo! woe! (the word बत seems originally<BR>to have stood immediately after the idea beginning<BR>the sentence and giving rise to the interjection, e. g.<BR>बतो बतासि यम, alas! thou art a weak person, O<BR>Yama.) According to native lexicographers the<BR>senses in which बत may be used are expressed by<BR>the following Sanskrit words, खेद, अनु-कम्प,<BR>अनु-क्रोश, वि-स्मय, आश्चर्य, सन्-तोष, धृति,<BR>आ-मन्त्रण, निन्दा, सम्-बोधन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बत
बत 2. बत, अस्, m. (probably for वत,<BR>past pass. part. of rt. वन्, q. v.), Ved. (according to<BR>the Nirukta) a weak or feeble person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्
बद् बद् or बन्द्, cl. 1. P. बदति, बन्-<BR>दति, बबाद, बदितुम्, &c., to be steady,<BR>to be firm; [cf. rt. 1. पद्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदर|बदरं|बदरः
बदर बदर, अस्, m. (later also वदर),<BR>the jujube tree, Zizyphus Jujuba or Z. Scandens;<BR>a kind of mustard (= देव-सर्षप); the kernel<BR>of the fruit of the cotton plant; N. of a man [cf.<BR>बादरायण]; (आ), f., N. of various plants; the<BR>cotton shrub; a particular species of bulbous plant<BR>(= गृष्टि, वाराही); Mimosa Octandra (= एला-<BR>पर्णी); Clitoria Ternatea (= विष्णु-क्रान्ता); (ई), f.<BR>the jujube tree; the cotton shrub; Mucuna Pruritus<BR>(= कपि-कच्छु); N. of one of the sources of the<BR>Gaṅgā and of the hermitage of Nara and Nārāyaṇa<BR>situated near it [cf. बदरिका]; (अम्), n. the edible<BR>fruit of the jujube; the berry or pod of the cotton<BR>shrub; the same berry used as a weight.<BR>—बदर-<BR>कुण, अस्, m. the time when the fruit of the jujube<BR>becomes ripe.<BR>—बदर-पाचन, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place (‘where the jujube ripens’).<BR>—ब-<BR>दर-फली, f. a species of jujube tree (= भू-ब-<BR>दरी).<BR>—बदर-यूष, a decoction of the fruit of<BR>the jujube.<BR>—बदरामलक (˚र-आम्˚), अम्, n.<BR>Flacourtia Cataphracta (probably the fruit rather than<BR>the plant itself).<BR>—बदरी-च्छद, अस्, आ, m. f. a<BR>kind of perfume (apparently a dried shell-fish, =<BR>शङ्ख-नखी); (आ), f. a species of jujube tree<BR>(= हस्ति-कोलि).<BR>—बदरी-तपोवन, अम्, n. the<BR>penance grove or hermitage at Badarī.<BR>—बदरी-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a temple at Badarī.<BR>—बदरी-<BR>नारायण, N. of a place.<BR>—बदरी-पत्त्र, अस्, m.<BR>a kind of perfume (= नखी).<BR>—बदरीपत्त्रक,<BR>अम्, n. a kind of perfume, a leaf.<BR>—बदरी-पाचन<BR>= बदर-पाचन, q. v.<BR>—बदरी-प्रस्थ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a city.<BR>—बदरी-फल, अम्, n. the fruit of<BR>the jujube tree; (आ), f., N. of a plant, a variety of<BR>Śephālikā or Nyctanthes with blue flowers.<BR>—ब-<BR>दरी-मूल, अम्, n. the root of the jujube tree.<BR>—बदरी-वण or बदरी-वन, अम्, n. a wood<BR>of jujube trees; N. of a place.<BR>—बदरी-वासा, f.<BR>‘dwelling at Badarī,’ an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—बदरी-<BR>शैल, अस्, m. ‘rock of Badarī,’ N. of a rocky emi-<BR>nence at the source of the Gaṅgā in the Himālaya<BR>range (a celebrated place of pilgrimage, the Bhadri-<BR>nāth of modern travellers; or a town and temple on<BR>the west bank of the Alaka-nandā river, in the<BR>province of Śrī-nagar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरि|बदरिः
बदरि, इस्, f. = बदरी, the jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिका
बदरिका, f. (fr. बदरा), the fruit of the<BR>jujube (?); N. of one of the sources of the Gaṅgā<BR>and of the neighbouring hermitage of Nara and<BR>Nārāyaṇa (= बदरी).<BR>—बदरिकाश्रम (˚का-<BR>आश्˚), N. of a hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध|बद्धं
बद्ध बद्ध. See under rt. बन्ध्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धप्पि
बद्धप्पि बद्ध-प्पि, n. (perhaps a Prākṛt<BR>form for बद्ध-पाणि), the clasped hand, the fist;<BR>(also read बद्धापि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्
बध् 1. बध्, to bind, for बन्ध्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्
बध् 2. बध्, used only in Desid. A. बी-<BR>भत्सते, to abhor, detest, &c. See बीभत्स<BR>(which is by some considered to belong to rt. बाध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्
बध् 3. बध् for वध्, to kill, &c., sub-<BR>stituted in some tenses of rt. हन्. See<BR>वध् and हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध
बध, अस्, m. killing, murder, &c.; see वध.<BR>—बध-काङ्क्षिन्, for this and all other com-<BR>pounds of बध see under वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधक
बधक, बध्य, &c. See वधक, वध्य,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिर|बधिरः
बधिर बधिर. See p. 673, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधू
बधू बधू. See वधू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्योग
बध्योग बध्योग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्द्|बंद्
बन्द् बन्द्. See rt. बद्, p. 671, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दि|बंदि|बंदिः|बन्दिः
बन्दि बन्दि, बन्दिन्, &c. See वन्दि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिआरयु
बन्दिआरयु बन्दिआरयु, N. of a place men-<BR>tioned in the Romaka-siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्|बंध्
बन्ध् बन्ध् [cf. rt. बुन्ध्], cl. 9. P. (ep.<BR>also A.) बध्नाति (बध्नीते), Impv. 2nd<BR>sing. बधान, बबन्ध (Ved. 3rd pl. बेधुस्,<BR>2nd sing. A. बेधिषे), भन्त्स्यति (ep. also बन्-<BR>धिष्यति, -ते), अभान्त्सीत्, बन्द्धुम् (ep. also बन्-<BR>धितुम्), to bind, tie, fix, fasten; to chain, enchain,<BR>fetter; to fasten or tie round, bind round, put on (e. g.<BR>चीरम् बध्नन्ति मुनयः, the ascetics put on<BR>clothing made of strips of bark); (A.) to bind on<BR>one's self, put on; to ensnare; to catch (e. g. मत्-<BR>स्यान् बन्ध्, to catch fish), take captive, take<BR>prisoner; to shut up, confine, imprison; to inflict<BR>punishment, punish, chastise; to bind a sacrificial<BR>victim, offer, sacrifice (with dat. of the deity to whom<BR>the victim is presented, Ved.); to fix, direct, fasten<BR>(the eyes or mind) upon (with loc.); to shut, close,<BR>stop, stop up, preclude; to arrest, hold back, check,<BR>suppress; to overpower, oppress, violate; to bind<BR>together, put together, fasten together, join, com-<BR>bine, connect, conglomerate, unite; to construct,<BR>build; to construct verses, compose; to bring to pass,<BR>effect, produce, evoke, result in, be followed by<BR>(with acc.); to form fruit (as a plant), to set; to<BR>strike (root); to take up (an abode); to manifest,<BR>exhibit, evince, display, show (e. g. धृतिम् ब-<BR>धान, show thy resolution); to entertain, cherish,<BR>foster, possess, have, contract, form; अञ्जलिम् बन्ध्,<BR>to place the two hands hollowed side by side;<BR>मुष्टिम् बन्ध्, to clench the fist; सेतुम् बन्ध्,<BR>to construct a dam, build a bridge, (बन्धिष्ये<BR>सेतुना गङ्गाम्, I will span the Gaṅgā with a<BR>bridge); गोलम् बन्ध्, to form or construct a<BR>globe; भ्रु-कुटिम् बन्ध्, to knit the brows,<BR>frown; सौहृद्यम् or सख्यम् or अजर्यम् बन्ध्<BR>to contract friendship; वैरम् बन्ध्, to contract<BR>enmity: Pass. बध्यते, Aor. अबधि (?), to be<BR>bound; to bind on one's self, put on: Caus. बन्-<BR>धयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबबन्धत्, to cause to<BR>bind, cause to be bound; to order to be imprisoned;<BR>to cause to be joined together or constructed, cause<BR>to be built, cause to be embanked; (according to<BR>the Dhātu-pāṭha) to bind, (in this last sense also<BR>बाधयति): Desid. बिभत्सति, to wish to bind:<BR>Intens. बाबध्यते, बाबन्द्धि, to bind fast, tie<BR>firmly; [cf. Zend band, banda, baś-ta, ‘bound;’ Gr.<BR>πείθω, πεῖσ-μα for πενθ-μα, πενθερός; Lat. pat-<BR>ibulum, pendo, pendeo, fī-lum for fid-lum, fū-<BR>nis for fud-nis, fīd-es, fīd-o for feido = πείθω,<BR>fœd-us; Slav. vjazati, ‘to bind;’ Goth. bind-an,<BR>fastan; Old Germ. fasti; Angl. Sax. bindan,<BR>bonda, bœnd, bœst, fœst; Iceland. fas-t.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध|बद्धं
बद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, bound, tied, fixed, fastened;<BR>chained, enchained, fettered; fastened or tied round,<BR>bound on, put on, girt on, dressed; caught, captured,<BR>confined, imprisoned; shut, stopped, closed, pre-<BR>cluded; arrested, held back, checked, restrained,<BR>suppressed, withheld; joined, connected, combined,<BR>united; formed, constructed, built, embanked; inlaid,<BR>studded [cf. रीति-ब्˚, लोह-ब्˚]; composed (as verses);<BR>effected, produced; directed towards; formed, set (as<BR>fruit); struck (as a root); firmly rooted, firm; placed<BR>side by side (as the hollowed hands); clenched (as<BR>the fist); knit (as the brows); contracted (as friend-<BR>ship or enmity); taken up (as an abode); mani-<BR>fested, evinced, displayed; entertained, cherished,<BR>fostered, possessed, got; entangled, involved, en-<BR>meshed; congealed, clotted (as blood; opposed to<BR>द्रव, q. v.); (at the beginning of adj. comps.<BR>बद्ध has often a vague sense analogous to that of<BR>जात, q. v.; see examples below); (अस् or अम्), m.<BR>or n.?, (with Jainas) that which binds or fetters<BR>the embodied spirit (viz. connection of the soul with<BR>deeds; it consists in a succession of births and deaths<BR>as the result of works).<BR>—बद्ध-कक्ष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has the loins girt, girt about the<BR>loins, having a tightened girdle.<BR>—बद्ध-कक्ष्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the girdle bound or girt up,<BR>prepared, ready.<BR>—बद्ध-कट, अस्, आ, अम्, made<BR>of plaited grass.<BR>—बद्ध-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose desires are restrained.<BR>—बद्ध-केसर, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-c" target="_blank">Page0672-c+ 81</a>]<BR>आ, अम्, having hair formed, forming hair.<BR>—बद्ध-<BR>कोप, अस्, आ, अम्, having anger suppressed, smother-<BR>ing resentment, governing wrath.<BR>—बद्ध-गुद,<BR>अम्, n. a dangerous kind of obstruction of the<BR>bowels.<BR>—बद्धगुदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from<BR>the above obstruction.<BR>—बद्ध-गोधाङ्गुलित्र-<BR>वत् (˚धा-अङ्˚), आन्, अती, अत्, (in archery) having<BR>fastened a leathern guard on the left arm and<BR>fingers; [cf. गो-धा.]<BR>—बद्धगोधाङ्गुलि-त्राण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having fastened on a leathern guard<BR>for the left arm and fingers.<BR>—बद्ध-घण्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having bells bound on.<BR>—बद्ध-चित्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having the thoughts fixed, rivetting the<BR>mind.<BR>—बद्ध-जिह्व, अस्, आ, अम्, tongue-tied,<BR>moving the tongue with difficulty.<BR>—बद्ध-ज्ञ-<BR>ता, f. the state of having acquired knowledge, great<BR>knowledge.<BR>—बद्ध-तल, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has put on a leathern guard (for the left arm).<BR>—बद्ध-तूण, अस्, आ, अम्, having a quiver fas-<BR>tened on, girt with a quiver.<BR>—बद्ध-दृष्टि, इस्,<BR>इस्, इ, having the eyes fixed, fixing the gaze (upon<BR>anything).<BR>—बद्ध-द्विरद-सेतु, उस्, उस्, उस्, hav-<BR>ing elephants bound together for bridges.<BR>—बद्-<BR>ध-द्वेष, अस्, आ, अम्, contracting hatred.<BR>—बद्-<BR>ध-धारा-प्रवाह, अस्, आ, अम्, checking the flow<BR>of (tear) drops.<BR>—बद्ध-निश्चय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a firm conviction, forming a firm resolve,<BR>firmly resolved.<BR>—बद्ध-निस्तृंश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>girt with a falchion.<BR>—बद्ध-नेत्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the eyes fixed, fixing the eyes (upon any-<BR>thing).<BR>—बद्ध-नेपथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, attired in<BR>a theatrical costume.<BR>—बद्ध-पङ्क-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, having the mud dried or hardened.<BR>—बद्-<BR>ध-पुरीष, अस्, आ, अम्, having the bowels ob-<BR>structed or constipated.<BR>—बद्धपुरीष-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of being constipated, obstruction of the<BR>bowels.<BR>—बद्ध-प्रतिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has contracted an engagement, one who has made a<BR>vow or promise.<BR>—बद्ध-प्रतिश्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, in<BR>which echoes are formed, resonant with echoing<BR>sounds.<BR>—बद्ध-फल, अस्, m. the plant Pon-<BR>gamia Glabra (= करञ्ज).<BR>—बद्ध-भाव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the mind or heart fixed.<BR>—बद्ध-<BR>भीमान्धकार (˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, enveloped<BR>in terrible darkness.<BR>—बद्ध-भू, ऊस्, f. the<BR>lowest floor (‘fixed on the ground’); ground pre-<BR>pared for the site of a house.<BR>—बद्ध-भूमिक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having an inlaid floor.<BR>—बद्ध-मुख,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, having the mouth or orifice closed.<BR>—बद्ध-मुष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a closed fist;<BR>close-fisted, griping, penurious, covetous; [cf. दृढ-<BR>मुष्टि.]<BR>—बद्धमुष्टि-कर, अस्, m. the hand<BR>with closed fist.<BR>—बद्धमुष्टि-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of having the fist closed (for holding a bow).<BR>—बद्-<BR>ध-मूत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, stopping or obstructing the<BR>urine.<BR>—बद्ध-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, striking root<BR>firmly, deeply rooted.<BR>—बद्धमूल-ता, f. the state<BR>of being firmly rooted.<BR>—बद्ध-मौन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one by whom silence is observed, keeping silence.<BR>—बद्ध-रभस, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has formed<BR>an ardent attachment, passionately attached (to any<BR>one).<BR>—बद्ध-रसाल, अस्, m. a species of mango<BR>(the most highly prized kind).<BR>—बद्ध-राग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, filled with passion, impassioned.<BR>—बद्ध-<BR>राज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, having attained to royalty.<BR>—बद्-<BR>ध-वत्सा, f., scil. गौस्, a cow whose calf is tied<BR>up (in the stall).<BR>—बद्ध-वन्दन-मालक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, having fastened garlands in token of wel-<BR>come.<BR>—बद्ध-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, constipating<BR>the bowels.<BR>—बद्ध-वसति, इस्, इस्, इ, fixing an<BR>abode.<BR>—बद्ध-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, suppressing the<BR>voice, maintaining silence, taciturn.<BR>—बद्धविट्क,<BR>अस्, आ, अम् (fr. बद्ध + विष्), one whose bowels<BR>are constipated, costive.<BR>—बद्धविट्क-ता, f. con-<BR>stipation of the bowels, costiveness.<BR>—बद्ध-विण्-<BR>मूत्र, अस्, आ, अम्, obstructing the evacuations by<BR>stool and by the bladder.<BR>—बद्ध-वीर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, whose heroes or soldiers are bound.<BR>—बद्ध-<BR>वेपथु, उस्, उस्, उ, seized with tremor, trembling.<BR>—बद्ध-वैर, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has con-<BR>tracted great enmity or confirmed hostility, feeling<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">Page0673-a+ 81</a>]<BR>bitter hatred.<BR>—बद्ध-शस्, an incorrect form for<BR>बद्व-शस्, q. v.<BR>—बद्ध-शिख, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose hair is tied up into a single lock upon the<BR>crown of the head; one who is still in childhood,<BR>young, a child, a pupil (not yet tonsured); (आ), f. a<BR>sort of pungent root, (according to some) a kind of<BR>garlic.<BR>—बद्ध-श्रोत्र-मनश्-चक्षुस्, उस्, उस्,<BR>उस्, having the ears, mind, and eyes fixed; fixing the<BR>ears, mind, and eyes.<BR>—बद्ध-सूत, अस्, m. a par-<BR>ticular preparation of quicksilver.<BR>—बद्ध-स्नेह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, forming an attachment, conceiving affection<BR>for (with loc.).<BR>—बद्धाङ्गुलि-त्र or बद्धाङ्-<BR>गुलि-त्राण (˚ध-अङ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a finger-<BR>guard fastened on, equipped with gauntlets.<BR>—बद्-<BR>धाञ्जलि (˚ध-अञ्˚), इस्, इस्, इ, having the hands<BR>hollowed and placed side by side, with hands or<BR>palms joined in humble entreaty, putting the joined<BR>hands to the forehead, saluting respectfully; with<BR>closed hands.<BR>—बद्धाञ्जलि-पुट, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>forming a cup with the hollowed hands.<BR>—बद्-<BR>धात्मन् (˚ध-आत्˚), आ, m. (with Jainas) a soul<BR>which is bound or fettered by deeds and works<BR>previous to its deliverance.<BR>—बद्धानन्द (˚ध-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, feeling pleasure, joyful.<BR>—बद्धा-<BR>नुराग (˚ध-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, manifesting love,<BR>feeling affection.<BR>—बद्धानुशय (˚ध-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, one whose purpose is fixed, of fixed<BR>intent; taking aim.<BR>—बद्धाम्बरचर-मार्ग<BR>(˚ध-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, obstructing the path of birds<BR>(said of a conflagration).<BR>—बद्धायुध (˚ध-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, accoutred with arms.<BR>—बद्धा-<BR>शङ्क (˚ध-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose suspicions<BR>are raised, apprehensive.<BR>—बद्धोत्सव (˚ध-<BR>उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, observing a festival, enjoying a<BR>holiday.<BR>—बद्धोद्यम (˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>uniting efforts, making united efforts, having the<BR>energies intently fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धक
बद्धक, अस्, m., Ved. one who is bound, a<BR>captive, prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध्वा
बद्ध्वा, ind. having bound or tied; having put<BR>on; having joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्व
बद्व, अम्, n., Ved. a large number, multitude;<BR>a particular high number, (according to Sāy.) 100<BR>Koṭis, (according to others) 10,000 millions; the<BR>number 13084.<BR>—बद्व-शस्, ind. in large numbers,<BR>in multitudes; (also incorrectly written बद्ध-शस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्वन्
बद्वन्, आ, m. a causeway, highway.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिर|बधिरः
बधिर, अस्, आ, अम्, deaf, (sometimes written<BR>वधिर); [cf. Hib. bodhar; Cambro-Brit. byzar;<BR>Armor. byzar.]<BR>—बधिर-ता, f. or बधिर-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. deafness.<BR>—बधिरान्ध (˚र-अन्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deaf and blind; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga, son<BR>of Kaśyapa.<BR>—बधिरी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-<BR>रुते, -कर्तुम्, to make deaf, deafen.<BR>—बधिरी-<BR>कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, made deaf, deafened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरक
बधिरक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of his descendants; (इका), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरय
बधिरय, Nom. P. बधिरयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make deaf, deafen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरित
बधिरित, अस्, आ, अम्, made deaf, deafened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरिमन्
बधिरिमन्, आ, m. deafness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्नत्
बध्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, binding, tying; effecting,<BR>producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

