भट्
भट् भट्, cl. 1. P. भटति, भटितुम्, to<BR>hire; to nourish, foster, cherish, maintain;<BR>cl. 10. P. भटयति, -यितुम्, to speak, converse:<BR>Caus. भाटयति, -यितुम्, to hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट|भटः
भट, अस्, m. (probably connected with भृत,<BR>q. v.), a mercenary, hired soldier, soldier in general,<BR>warrior, combatant; N. of a particular degraded<BR>tribe [cf. भट्ट, भड, भण्ड]; an outcast,<BR>barbarian; a demon; N. of a person (perhaps of<BR>a Nāga-rāja); (आ), f. coloquintida.<BR>—भट-भट-<BR>मातृ-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—भ-<BR>टार्क (˚ट-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of the founder of the<BR>Valabhī dynasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटभटाय
भटभटाय भटभटाय (an onomatopoetic<BR>word), Nom. A. भटभटायते, &c., to make a<BR>gurgling sound, gurgle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटित्र|भटित्रं
भटित्र भटित्र, अस्, आ, अम्, roasted on a spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्कला
भट्कला भट्कला, f., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्ट|भट्टः
भट्ट भट्ट, अस्, m. (probably connected<BR>with भर्तृ, q. v.), lord, my lord (as a title of<BR>respect by which a prince is addressed); a title affixed<BR>to the names of learned Brāhmans (the proper name<BR>being sometimes omitted, e. g. भट्ट = कुमारिल-<BR>भट्ट, a respectful designation of Kumārila; cf.<BR>आर्य-भ्˚, केदार-भ्˚, गोविन्द-भ्˚); any learned<BR>man, doctor or philosopher; a title applied to the<BR>son of a Brāhman; best, excellent; an authority (?);<BR>an enemy (?); N. of a particular mixed caste of<BR>hereditary panegyrists, a bard, encomiast; in Rāmā-<BR>yaṇa I. 12, 11, incorrectly for भट, q. v.; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of an enchantress.<BR>—भट्ट-कारिका, आस्, f. pl.,<BR>N. of particular Kārikās.<BR>—भट्ट-केदार, अस्, m.<BR>= केदार-भट्ट, q. v.<BR>—भट्ट-दिवाकर, N. of<BR>a man; [cf. दिवा-कर.]<BR>—भट्ट-दीपिका, f., N.<BR>of a work (= भाट्ट-दीपिका, q. v.).<BR>—भट्ट-ना-<BR>यक, अस्, m., N. of a poet; of a rhetorician.<BR>—भट्ट-नारायण, अस्, m., N. of various men.<BR>—भट्ट-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—भट्ट-<BR>पाद, आस्, m. pl. ‘the feet of Bhaṭṭa,’ the venerable<BR>Kumārila; [cf. पाद.]<BR>—भट्ट-प्रयाग, अस्, m.<BR>‘the chief place of sacrifice,’ the spot where the Ya-<BR>munā falls into the Gaṅgā.<BR>—भट्ट-फल्गुण, see<BR>फल्गुण.<BR>—भट्ट-बलभद्र, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of a commentary on the Brahma-sid-<BR>dhānta; of the author of a logical treatise; [cf.<BR>बल-भद्र.]<BR>—भट्ट-बीजक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>poet.<BR>—भट्ट-भास्कर-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>commentator.<BR>—भट्ट-मदन, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author; [cf. मदन.]<BR>—भट्ट-मल्ल, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a grammarian.<BR>—भट्ट-यशस्, आस्, m., N. of<BR>a poet.<BR>—भट्ट-वार्त्तिक, N. of a work.<BR>—भट्ट-<BR>विश्वेश्वर (˚व-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भट्ट-<BR>शङ्कर = भट्ट-श्री-शङ्कर, q. v.<BR>—भट्ट-<BR>शिव, अस्, m., N. of a philosopher mentioned in the<BR>Śaṅkara-vijaya.<BR>—भट्ट-श्री-शङ्कर, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an astronomer.<BR>—भट्ट-सोमेश्वर (˚म-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author mentioned in Kamalākara-<BR>bhaṭṭa's Śūdra-dharma-tattva.<BR>—भट्ट-स्वामिन्, ई,<BR>m., N. of a poet mentioned in the Śārṅgadhara-<BR>paddhati.<BR>—भट्टाचार्य (˚ट-आच्˚), अस्, m. a title<BR>given to a learned Brāhman or any great teacher or<BR>celebrated instructor, (especially, according to the<BR>Śabda-kalpa-druma) one versed in the doctrine of<BR>Tutāta and Udayanācārya; a great doctor or philo-<BR>sopher; a frequent designation of Kumārila-bhaṭṭa<BR>[cf. भट्ट]; N. of a pupil of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—भट्टाचार्य-चूडामणि, इस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—भट्टाचार्य-शतावधान, अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Rāghavendra.<BR>—भट्टालङ्कार (˚ट-अल्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a metrical commentary by Ananta-bhaṭṭa<BR>on the Mīmāṃsā-nyāya-prakāśa or Āpadevī.<BR>—भट्-<BR>टोत्पल (˚ट-उत्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Scholiast of the<BR>tenth century who wrote a commentary on the<BR>works of Varāha-mihira.<BR>—भट्टोपम (˚ट-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a learned Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टार|भट्टारः
भट्टार, अस्, m. noble lord (affixed as an honour-<BR>able title or distinction to proper names); (अस्, आ,<BR>अम्), worshipful, reverend, entitled to homage or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">Page0698-a+ 76</a>]<BR>respect; [cf. दिल्ह.]<BR>—भट्टार-हरिचन्द्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारक|भट्टारकः
भट्टारक, अस्, इका, अम्, venerable, respectable,<BR>entitled to reverence or to homage; (अस्), m. a<BR>sage, a Muni or saint; noble lord, an epithet of<BR>gods and of great and learned men (especially applied<BR>to Buddhist teachers); (in dramatic language) a king;<BR>the sun; Ardea Nivea?; (इका), f. a noble lady,<BR>a goddess, tutelary deity; [cf. जया-भट्टारिका.]<BR>—भट्टारक-वार, अस्, m. ‘day of the great lord,<BR>i. e. of the sun,’ Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टि|भट्टिः
भट्टि, इस्, m., N. of the author of the epic poem<BR>described below.<BR>—भट्टि-काव्य, अम्, n. ‘the poem<BR>of Bhaṭṭi,’ N. of an artificial epic poem by Bhaṭṭi<BR>(celebrating the exploits of Rāma and illustrating<BR>Sanskrit grammar by the systematic application of all<BR>possible forms and constructions; cf. भर्तृ-हरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टिक|भट्टिकः
भट्टिक, अस्, m., N. of the mythical progenitor<BR>of copyists (son of Citra-gupta and grandson of<BR>Brahmā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टिनी
भट्टिनी, f. (a Prākṛt feminine fr. भर्तृ, per-<BR>haps adopted into Sanskrit from its resemblance to<BR>पत्नी), a woman of high rank, a queen (but one<BR>not crowned or consecrated like the Devī); the wife<BR>of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टीय
भट्टीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Bhaṭṭa, i. e. to<BR>Ārya-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—भट्टीय-दीपिका, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on Ārya-bhaṭṭa's explanation of the Sūrya-<BR>siddhānta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टोजि|भट्टोजिः
भट्टोजि, इस्, m., N. of a grammarian, author of<BR>the Siddhānta-kaumudī.<BR>—भट्टोजि-दीक्षित or<BR>भट्टोजि-भट्ट, अस्, m. = भट्टोजि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भड|भडः
भड भड, अस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>mixed caste; (also read भण्ड.)<BR>—भड-हरी-<BR>मातृ-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भडित
भडित भडित, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्),<BR>m. pl., N. of his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भडिल|भडिलः
भडिल भडिल, अस्, m. an attendant, ser-<BR>vant; a hero; N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl., N. of his<BR>descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्
भण् भण् (perhaps a Prākṛt form con-<BR>nected with rt. भाष्), cl. 1. P. भणति,<BR>बभाण (2nd sing. बभणिथ), अभाणीत्, भ-<BR>णितुम्, to sound; to utter an articulate sound, speak,<BR>say; to call, name: Caus. भाणयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अबीभणत्, अबभाणत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण
भण in दुर्-भण, अस्, आ, अम्, difficult to be<BR>told or mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणन|भणनं
भणन, अस्, ई, अम्, speaking, announcing, pro-<BR>claiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणनीय
भणनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be told or said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणित|भणितं
भणित, अस्, आ, अम्, sounded, uttered, spoken,<BR>said; (अम्), n. talking, talk, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणिति|भणितिः
भणिति, इस्, f. speech, talking, talk, discourse;<BR>(incorrectly भणति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणितृ
भणितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a speaker, speaking, talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणित्वा
भणित्वा, ind. having spoken, having said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ट्
भण्ट् भण्ट्, cl. 10. P. भण्टयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, to deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्टाकी
भण्टाकी भण्टाकी, f. the plant Solanum<BR>Melongena; (also read भण्डाकी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्टुक|भण्टुकः
भण्टुक भण्टुक, अस्, m. the plant Calo-<BR>santhes Indica; (also read भण्डुक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ड्|भंड्
भण्ड् भण्ड्, cl. 1. A. भण्डते, भण्डि-<BR>तुम्, to chide, upbraid, reprove; to deride,<BR>mimic; to jest; to speak; cl. 10. and 1. P. भण्ड-<BR>यति, भण्डति, to be fortunate; to render fortunate,<BR>prosper (trans.); to do an auspicious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ड|भंड|भंडः|भण्डः
भण्ड, अस्, m. a jester, buffoon, actor, mime,<BR>mimic; N. of a particular mixed caste [cf. भड];<BR>(आ), f. in श्वेत-भ्˚, q. v.<BR>—भण्ड-तपस्विन्, ई,<BR>m. a hypocritical ascetic.<BR>—भण्ड-हासिनी, f. a<BR>harlot, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डक|भंडक|भंडकः|भण्डकः
भण्डक, अस्, m. a water wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डन|भंडन|भंडनं|भण्डनं
भण्डन, अम्, n. armour, mail; war, battle;<BR>evil, wickedness, mischief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डर
भण्डर, अस्, m. a particular kind of combat<BR>(= कलह-विशेष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डाकी
भण्डाकी. See भण्टाकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिका
भण्डिका, f. = भण्डी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिजङ्घ
भण्डि-जङ्घ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डित
भण्डित, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl., N.<BR>of his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिन्
भण्डिन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिर|भण्डिरः
भण्डिर, अस्, m. = भण्डिल, Mimosa Seeressa;<BR>(ई), f. = भण्डी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिल|भंडिल|भण्डिलः
भण्डिल, अस्, आ, अम्, fortunate, happy, prosperous,<BR>auspicious; (अस्), m. fortune, welfare; a messenger;<BR>an artizan, workman; the plant Mimosa Seeressa<BR>(= शिरीष); N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl., N. of his<BR>descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डी|भंडी
भण्डी, f. the plant Rubia Munjista (= मञ्-<BR>जिष्ठा).<BR>—भण्डी-पुष्प-निकाश, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>resembling the flowers of Rubia Munjista.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डीतकी
भण्डीतकी = भण्डी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डीर|भण्डीरः
भण्डीर, अस्, m. Amaranthus Polygonoides;<BR>Mimosa Seeressa; N. of a lofty Nyagrodha tree<BR>upon the Go-vardhana mountain; (ई), f. = भण्डी,<BR>q. v.<BR>—भण्डीर-लतिका, f. = भण्डी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डील|भण्डीलः
भण्डील, अस्, m. = भण्डी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डुक|भण्डुकः
भण्डुक, अस्, m. the plant Calosanthes Indica;<BR>(also written भण्डूक; cf. भण्टुक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डूक|भण्डूकः
भण्डूक, अस्, m. the plant Calosanthes Indica;<BR>a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदन्त|भदंत|भदंतः|भदन्तः
भदन्त भदन्त, भदाक. See under rt.<BR>भन्द् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्र|भद्रं|भद्रः
भद्र भद्र. See under rt. भन्द् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्
भन् भन् (a various reading for rt.<BR>भण्), cl. 1. P. भनति, भनितुम्, Ved.<BR>to sound, resound; to cry aloud, shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भनन्दन
भनन्दन भनन्दन, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(wrongly for भलन्दन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्द्|भंद्
भन्द् भन्द् or भद्, cl. 1. A. भन्दते,<BR>भन्दितुम्, Ved. to be greeted with<BR>praise, be hailed with acclamations, receive applause;<BR>to be fortunate or prosperous; to be excellent; to be<BR>glad; to exhilarate; to shine; to make fortunate, to<BR>honour, worship: Caus. भन्दयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to prosper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदन्त|भदंत|भदंतः|भदन्तः
भदन्त, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. भण्ड्,<BR>col. 1), a term of respect applied to a Buddhist; a<BR>Buddhist mendicant.<BR>—भदन्त-गोप-देव and<BR>भदन्त-गोषक or भदन्त-घोषक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of two Buddhist teachers.<BR>—भदन्त-ज्ञान-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—भदन्त-धर्म-<BR>त्रात and भदन्त-राम, अस्, m., N. of two Bud-<BR>dhist teachers.<BR>—भदन्त-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>poet.<BR>—भदन्त-श्री-लाभ, अस्, m., N. of a Bud-<BR>dhist teacher (also called Śrī-lābha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदाक|भदाकः
भदाक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. भन्द्), for-<BR>tune, prosperity; (अस्, आ, अम्), auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्र|भद्रं|भद्रः
भद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, good, well, prosperous,<BR>happy, auspicious (e. g. भद्रा दिश्, the auspicious<BR>quarter, the south); favourable, propitious, gracious,<BR>kind, friendly, benevolent, pious, excellent, (भद्रो<BR>नृपतिः, a good or gracious king; often used<BR>in voc. sing. m. भद्र as a familiar mode of<BR>address, in the sense of ‘my good sir,’ ‘my dear<BR>fellow;’ and in voc. sing. f. भद्रे, ‘my good<BR>lady,’ ‘my dear madam’); pleasant, enjoyable,<BR>desirable, laudable, commendable; lovely, beauti-<BR>ful; beloved, dear; specious, plausible, hypocritical,<BR>any hypocrite or impostor, (according to Kullūka on<BR>Manu IX. 258 = कल्याणाचार-प्रच्छन्न-पाप);<BR>(अम्), n. prosperity, happiness, welfare, good fortune,<BR>fortune, (भद्राणि, n. pl. = भद्रम्, good for-<BR>tune; भद्रम् अ-व्याहतम्, uninterrupted happi-<BR>ness or prosperity; भद्रं ते, prosperity to thee!<BR>भद्रं वः, happiness to you! may it be well<BR>with you! frequently mere forms politely used in<BR>conversation, and sometimes equivalent to our expres-<BR>sions ‘if you please,’ ‘with all deference or respect<BR>for you,’ &c.); gold; iron, steel; a fragrant grass,<BR>Cyperus Rotundus [cf. भद्र-मुस्त]; a particular<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-c" target="_blank">Page0698-c+ 81</a>]<BR>posture in sitting (= भद्रासन); N. of the<BR>seventh of the eleven astronomical periods called<BR>Karaṇas; of various Sāmans; (अस्), m. a bullock; a<BR>term applied to a particular kind of elephant; N. of<BR>one of the elephants which support the world; a<BR>water wag-tail [cf. भद्र-नामन्]; a heap, multi-<BR>tude (?); Nauclea Cadamba; Tithymalus Antiquorum;<BR>an epithet of Śiva; N. of one of the twelve sons of<BR>Viṣṇu and one of the Tuṣita deities in the Svā-<BR>yambhava Manv-antara; (with Jainas) N. of the<BR>third of the nine white Balas; N. of a son of Vasu-<BR>deva and Pauravī; of a son of Vasu-deva and Devakī;<BR>of a son of Upacāru-mat; of an actor; of a friend<BR>of Bāṇa; of a son of Kṛṣṇa; an epithet of mount<BR>Meru; (with Buddhists) N. of a particular world;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of divinities under the<BR>third Manu; N. of a people; (आ), f. a cow; N.<BR>of various plants (= कृष्णा, अनन्ता, रास्ना,<BR>प्र-सारिणी, जीवन्ती, अपराजिता, नीली, बला,<BR>शमी, वचा, दन्ती, हरिद्रा, श्वेत-दूर्वा, काश्-<BR>मरी, सारिवा-विशेष, काकोडुम्बरिका); Gmelina<BR>Arborea; a kind of metre, the first and third lines<BR>of which are ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯, and the second<BR>and fourth ¯¯˘¯¯ &c.; N. of the second, seventh,<BR>and twelfth days of the lunar fortnight; of a goddess;<BR>of a Buddhist woman; of Dākṣāyaṇī in Bhadre-<BR>śvara; of a Vidyā-dharī; of a daughter of Surabhi;<BR>of a wife of Vasu-deva; of the wife of Vaiśravaṇa;<BR>of a daughter of Soma and wife of Utathya; of a<BR>daughter of Raudrāśva and the Apsaras Ghṛtācī; of<BR>a Kākṣīvatī and wife of Vyuṣitāśva; of a daughter<BR>of Meru and wife of Bhadrāśva; of a daughter of<BR>Sruta-kīrtti and wife of Kṛṣṇa; of various rivers;<BR>of a river described as rising on the northern summit<BR>of Meru and flowing through Uttara-kuru into the<BR>northern ocean; the celestial Ganges; भद्रम्,<BR>भद्रया, भद्रेभिस्, ind., Ved. auspiciously,<BR>favourably, propitiously, happily, well, rightly; [cf.<BR>Lat. fastus for fad-tus, fastigium, fastidium,<BR>festivus: Goth. bats, bat-iza, ‘better;’ bat-ista,<BR>‘best:’ Angl. Sax. bet: Old Germ. baz, ‘better;’<BR>beziro, bezisto, ‘best:’ Goth. ga-bat-non, bot-a,<BR>bot-jan: Angl. Sax. bót: Hib. feodhas, ‘better;’<BR>badhach, ‘famous;’ perhaps maith: Cambro-Brit.<BR>mad, ‘good.’]<BR>—भद्र-कण्ट, अस्, m. the plant<BR>Asteracantha Longifolia.<BR>—भद्र-कन्या, f., N.<BR>of the mother of Maudgalyāyana.<BR>—भद्र-कपिल,<BR>अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva; [cf. भद्र and कपिल.]<BR>—भद्र-कर्णिका, f., N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in Go-<BR>karṇa.<BR>—भद्र-कर्णेश्वर (˚ण-ईश्˚), N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place.<BR>—भद्र-कल्प, अस्, m. (with<BR>Buddhists) ‘the good or beautiful Kalpa,’ N. of the<BR>present age; of a Sūtra work.<BR>—भद्रकल्पिक,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—भद्र-कार, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR>—भद्र-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing<BR>prosperity or welfare, propitious, prosperous.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्र-काली, f., N. of a goddess; (in the later mytho-<BR>logy) a form of Durgā [cf. Manu III. 89]; N. of<BR>one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; a species<BR>of plant (= गन्धोली); N. of a village on the<BR>right bank of the Ganges.<BR>—भद्रकाली-क-<BR>वच, अम्, n., N. of the thirty-seventh chapter of<BR>the Gaṇeśa-khaṇḍa or third part of the Brahma-<BR>vaivarta-Purāṇa.<BR>—भद्रकाली-पूजा-यन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a mystical diagram mentioned in Kṛṣṇā-<BR>nanda's Tantra-sāra.<BR>—भद्रकाली-मनु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of the ninth chapter of the Pheṭ-kāriṇī-tantra.<BR>—भद्रकाली-मन्त्र, आस्, m. pl., N. of a chapter<BR>of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—भद्र-काशी, f. = भद्र-<BR>मुस्ता, q. v.<BR>—भद्र-काष्ठ, अम्, n. the wood<BR>of Pinus Deodora or of Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—भद्र-<BR>कुम्भ, अस्, m. ‘auspicious jar,’ a golden jar filled<BR>with water from a holy place or from the Ganges<BR>(used especially at the consecration of a king).<BR>—भद्र-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. causing prosperity or<BR>welfare; (with Jainas) N. of the twenty-fourth Arhat<BR>of the future Ut-sarpiṇī.<BR>—भद्र-गणित, अम्, n.<BR>the construction of magical squares or diagrams.<BR>—भद्र-गन्धिका, f. the plant Cyperus Rotun-<BR>dus (= मुस्तक); the creeping plant Asclepias Pseu-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-a" target="_blank">Page0699-a+ 81</a>]<BR>dosarsa.<BR>—भद्र-गौर, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—भद्र-घट or भद्र-घटक, अस्, m. a<BR>vessel from which a lottery is drawn.<BR>—भद्रङ्-<BR>कर, अस्, ई, अम्, auspicious, propitious, causing pros-<BR>perity or happiness; (अस्), m., N. of a person;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a town in Vidarbha.<BR>—भद्रङ्-<BR>करण, अस्, ई, अम्, causing prosperity or happiness,<BR>prosperous.<BR>—भद्र-चारु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भद्र-चूड, अस्, m. the plant Euphor-<BR>bia Tirucalli.<BR>—भद्र-ज, अस्, m. the plant Wrightia<BR>Antidysenterica.<BR>—भद्र-जय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—भद्र-जानि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. having a beau-<BR>tiful wife.<BR>—भद्र-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more pros-<BR>perous, happier; better.<BR>—भद्र-तरुणी, f. the<BR>plant Trapa Bispinosa (= कुब्जक).<BR>—भद्र-ता,<BR>f. or भद्र-त्व, अम्, n. honesty, probity; pros-<BR>perity, good fortune.<BR>—भद्र-तुङ्ग, N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place.<BR>—भद्र-तुरग, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a Varṣa.<BR>—भद्र-दन्त, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>elephant.<BR>—भद्र-दन्तिका, f. a species of Croton.<BR>—भद्र-दारु, उस्, उ, m. n. a sort of pine, Pinus<BR>Deodora; Pinus Longifolia.<BR>—भद्रदार्व्-आदिक,<BR>अस्, m. a class of thirty-nine medicinal plants and<BR>substances.<BR>—भद्र-देह, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भद्र-द्वीप, अस्, m., N. of an island.<BR>—भद्र-नामन्, आ, m. the wood-pecker; the<BR>water wag-tail; [cf. भद्र.]<BR>—भद्र-नामिका,<BR>f. a species of plant (= त्रायमाणा).<BR>—भद्र-<BR>निधि, इस्, m. ‘treasure of fortune,’ a term applied<BR>to a costly vessel offered to Viṣṇu.<BR>—भद्र-<BR>पद, अम्, n. a kind of metre; (आ), f., N. of the<BR>third and fourth lunar asterisms (= प्रोष्ठ-पद;<BR>cf. नक्षत्र).<BR>—भद्रपदा-योग, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the twenty-eighth chapter of Bhaṭṭotpala's<BR>commentary on Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-saṃhitā.<BR>—भद्र-पर्णा, f. the shrub Pæderia Fœtida.<BR>—भद्र-पर्णी, f. the tree Gmelina Arborea; the<BR>shrub Pæderia Fœtida.<BR>—भद्रपाद, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>born under the Nakṣatra Bhadra-padā.<BR>—भद्र-<BR>पाल, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—भद्र-पी-<BR>ठ, अम्, n. a beautiful chair, splendid seat, throne;<BR>a kind of winged insect, (perhaps incorrectly for a<BR>form भद्र-कीट.)<BR>—भद्र-पुर, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a city; [cf. भद्रा-नगर.]<BR>—भद्र-बलन,<BR>अस्, m. = बल-भद्र, N. of the elder brother of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भद्र-बला, f. the shrub Pæderia Fœ-<BR>tida; Sida Cordifolia (= बला).<BR>—भद्र-बाहु,<BR>उस्, m., N. of a son of Vasu-deva by Rohiṇī (Pau-<BR>ravī); of a king of Magadha; (with Jainas) N. of<BR>one of the six Śruta-kevalins; of the author of certain<BR>Kalpa-sūtras; of the author of the Jātakāmbho-nidhi;<BR>(ऊस्), f., N. of a woman.<BR>—भद्रबाहु-शास्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work mentioned in Nārāyaṇa's Praśnār-<BR>ṇava.<BR>—भद्रबाहु-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of an author<BR>mentioned in Cāritra-siṃha-gaṇi's Shaḍdarśana-vṛtti.<BR>—भद्र-भुज, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘auspicious-armed,’<BR>whose arms confer prosperity.<BR>—भद्र-भूषणी,<BR>f., N. of a deity.<BR>—भद्र-मनस्, आस्, f., N. of<BR>the mother of the elephant Airāvata; [cf. भद्र-<BR>रेणु.]<BR>—भद्र-मन्द, अस्, m. epithet of a parti-<BR>cular kind of elephant; (also read भद्र-मन्द्र;<BR>cf. भद्र, मन्द, मन्द्र.)<BR>—भद्रमन्द्र-<BR>मृग, अस्, m. epithet of a particular kind of ele-<BR>phant.<BR>—भद्र-मल्लिका, f. a species of plant, Cu-<BR>cumis Madraspatanus (= गवाक्षी).<BR>—भद्र-मा-<BR>तृ, ता, f. a good or beautiful mother.<BR>—भद्र-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, one whose face (i. e. whose<BR>look) confers prosperity; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga.<BR>—भद्र-मुञ्ज, अस्, m. a plant akin to Saccha-<BR>rum Sara.<BR>—भद्र-मुस्त or भद्र-मुस्ता, f. a<BR>variety of Cyperus.<BR>—भद्रमुस्तक, अस्, m. =<BR>भद्र-मुस्त.<BR>—भद्र-मृग, अस्, m. epithet<BR>of a particular kind of elephant.<BR>—भद्र-यव,<BR>अम्, n. the seed of Wrightia Antidysenterica (=<BR>इन्द्र-यव).<BR>—भद्र-यान, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man; (commonly written भद्रायन.)<BR>—भ-<BR>द्रयानीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of the school founded by<BR>Bhadra-yāna; (commonly written भद्रायनीय.)<BR>—भद्र-योग, अस्, m., N. of a subdivision of the<BR>Purāṇa-sarvasva; of an astrological Yoga.<BR>—भद्र-<BR>रथ, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भद्र-रुचि, इस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-b" target="_blank">Page0699-b+ 81</a>]<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—भद्र-रूपा, f., N. of a<BR>woman.<BR>—भद्र-रेणु, उस्, m., N. of Indra's ele-<BR>phant; (also read भद्र-वेणु; cf. भद्र-म-<BR>नस्.)<BR>—भद्र-रोहिणी, f. a species of plant.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्र-वट, अस्, m. ‘the auspicious or beautiful fig-<BR>tree,’ N. of a place.<BR>—भद्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>fraught with good, auspicious; (अती), f. a wanton,<BR>courtezan (?Ved.); the tree Gmelia Arborea; N. of<BR>a daughter of Kṛṣṇa; of a wife of Madhu (with<BR>the patronymic Pauravī); N. of a female elephant;<BR>(अत्), n. the tree Pinus Deodora; N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—भद्र-वर्मन्, आ, m. ‘Double Arabian Jasmine,’<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—भद्र-वल्लिका, f. the plant Hemi-<BR>desmus Indicus.<BR>—भद्र-वल्ली, f. Jasminum Sam-<BR>bac; Gærtnera Racemosa, a large Bengal creeper;<BR>the plant Vallaris Dichotomus.<BR>—भद्र-वसन,<BR>अम्, n. splendid apparel, magnificent array.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्र-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. speaking auspiciously.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्र-वाच्य, अम्, n., Ved. wishing well, congratu-<BR>lation.<BR>—भद्र-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. uttering<BR>auspicious cries (said of a bird).<BR>—भद्र-विन्द,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भद्र-विराज्,<BR>ट्, f. a kind of metre.<BR>—भद्र-विहार, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Buddhist monastery.<BR>—भद्र-वेणु, another<BR>form for भद्र-रेणु, q. v.<BR>—भद्र-व्रात, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having or forming a happy assem-<BR>blage.<BR>—भद्र-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a man with<BR>the patronymic Kauśika; [cf. भाद्रशर्मि.]<BR>—भ-<BR>द्र-शाख, अस्, m., N. of a form of Skanda.<BR>—भद्र-शाल-वन = भद्र-साल-वन, q. v.<BR>—भद्र-शील, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भद्र-<BR>शोचि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. beautifully shining, flashing,<BR>coruscating, glittering.<BR>—भद्र-शौनक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—भद्र-श्रय or भद्र-श्रिय,<BR>अम्, n. sandal-wood.<BR>—भद्र-श्रवस्, आस्, m., N.<BR>of a son of Dharma.<BR>—भद्र-श्री, ईस्, f. the<BR>sandal tree.<BR>—भद्र-श्रुत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. hearing<BR>good, hearing pleasant things.<BR>—भद्र-श्रेण्य, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king.<BR>—भद्र-षष्ठी, f., N. of a<BR>form of Durgā.<BR>—भद्र-सामन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—भद्र-सार, अस्, m., N. of a king; (also<BR>read विन्दु-सार.)<BR>—भद्र-साल-वन, (probably)<BR>अम्, n., N. of a forest (of fine Shorea Robusta trees).<BR>—भद्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a man with the<BR>patronymic Ajātaśatrava; of a son of Vasu-deva and<BR>Devakī; of a son of Ṛṣabha; of a son of Mahiṣ-<BR>mat, (in this sense also भद्रसेनक); N. of a<BR>king of Kaśmīra; (with Buddhists) N. of the leader<BR>of the host of the evil spirit Māra-pāpīyas.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्र-सोमा, f., N. of a river in Uttara-kuru; a N. of<BR>the Ganges.<BR>—भद्र-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>beautiful-handed, auspicious-handed (said of the<BR>Aśvins).<BR>—भद्रा-करण, अम्, n. ‘making beau-<BR>tiful,’ the act of shaving.<BR>—भद्रा-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>-करोति, -कर्तुम्, ‘to make beautiful,’ to shave;<BR>[cf. मद्रा-कृ.]<BR>—भद्राक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘fair-eyed,’ N. of a king [cf. भल्लाक्ष]; a<BR>particular seed of which beads are made (?).<BR>—भ-<BR>द्राङ्ग (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘beauteous-framed,’ having<BR>a handsome person,’ an epithet of Bala-bhadra.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्रात्मज (˚र-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘son of iron,’ a sword.<BR>—भद्रा-नगर, अम्, n., N. of a city; [cf. भ-<BR>द्र-पुर.]<BR>—भद्राभद्र (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, good and bad; (अम्), n. good and evil.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्रायुध (˚र-आय्˚), अस्, m. ‘handsome-weaponed,’<BR>N. of a giant; of a warrior.<BR>—भद्रायुस् (˚र-आय्˚),<BR>उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भद्रावकाशा (˚र-अव्˚),<BR>f., N. of a sacred river.<BR>—भद्रा-व्रत, अम्, n. a<BR>particular religious ceremony; (also called विष्टि-<BR>व्रत.)<BR>—भद्राश्रम (˚र or ˚रा-आश्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a hermitage mentioned in the Śambhala-<BR>māhātmya portion of the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—भद्रा-<BR>श्रय, अम्, n. sandal-wood (= भद्र-श्रय, q. v.).<BR>—भद्राश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Dvīpa said<BR>in the Purāṇas to be named after Bhadrāśva, son of<BR>Āgnīdhra, (some systems describe Bhadrāśva as one<BR>of the four Mahā-dvīpas into which the known world<BR>is divided, while another states it to be one of nine<BR>Khaṇḍas or smaller divisions into which the conti-<BR>nent is distributed; in either case it is the eastern<BR>division); N. of a son of Vasu-deva and Rohiṇī; of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">Page0699-c+ 77</a>]<BR>a son of Dhundhumāra; of a king called Bhadrāśva<BR>Śveta-vāhana; of a son of Āgnīdhra or Agnīdhra;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Varṣa named after the son of<BR>Āgnīdhra.<BR>—भद्रासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. a<BR>splendid seat, chair of state, throne; a particular<BR>posture of a devotee while meditating, (the legs being<BR>crossed and bent underneath the body and turned so<BR>as to bring the ankles into contact with the perinæum<BR>while the soles of the feet are held close to the<BR>sides.)<BR>—भद्राह (˚र-अह), अम्, n., Ved. an<BR>auspicious day, favourable season.<BR>—भद्रेन्द्र<BR>(˚र-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भद्रेश (˚र-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भद्रेश्वर (˚र-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. an epithet of various statues and Liṅgas<BR>of Śiva; N. of a place; of a Kāyastha.<BR>—भ-<BR>द्रैला (˚र-एला), f. large cardamoms.<BR>—भद्रो-<BR>दनी (˚र-ओद्˚), f. Sida Cordifolia; Uraria Lagopodi-<BR>oides.<BR>—भद्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n., N. of a par-<BR>ticular medicinal compound.<BR>—भद्रोपवास-व्रत<BR>(˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n. a particular religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रक|भद्रकं|भद्रकः
भद्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, good; fine, handsome,<BR>beautiful; (अस्), m. (according to a Scholiast) a kind<BR>of bean; (probably) Cyperus Pertenuis; the Deodar<BR>tree, Pinus Deodora; N. of a man, (also called<BR>भद्रिक, q. v.); of a king; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people [cf. भद्र]; (इका), f. an amulet; N. of a<BR>metre, four times ¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯; of a metre, four<BR>times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯; (अका), f., N. of a woman;<BR>(अम्), n. Cyperus Rotundus; a particular posture in<BR>sitting (= भद्रासन, q. v.); a kind of metre, four<BR>times ¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯, ˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रारक|भद्रारकः
भद्रारक, अस्, m., N. of one of the eighteen<BR>lesser Dvīpas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रालपत्त्रिका
भद्रालपत्त्रिका, f. Pæderia Fœtida (= गन्-<BR>धाली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राली
भद्राली, f. = भद्रालपत्त्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रावती
भद्रावती, f. a species of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रिक
भद्रिक, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf. भद्रक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रिण
भद्रिण, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्ददिष्टि
भन्दद्-इष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. भन्दत्, pres. part. P.<BR>of rt. भन्द् + इष्टि), Ved. (perhaps) hastening amidst<BR>shouts of applause; (Sāy.) = स्तुति-रूपेष्टिर् यस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दन
भन्दन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. shouting lustily, ap-<BR>plauding, cheering; (Mahī-dhara), causing to prosper,<BR>(or) beautifying, embellishing; (आ), f. acclamation,<BR>applause, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दनाय
भन्दनाय (fr. भन्दन), Nom. P. भन्-<BR>दनायति, -यितुम्, Ved. to shout loudly, howl, yell,<BR>(used only in the pres. part. below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दनायत्
भन्दनायत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. shouting loudly,<BR>howling, yelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दनीय
भन्दनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. a word formed in<BR>Nirukta XI. 19. to explain भद्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दमान
भन्दमान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. hailed with ac-<BR>clamations, greeted with applause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दिल|भंदिल|भंदिलं|भन्दिलं
भन्दिल, अम्, n. fortune, prosperity [cf. भण्-<BR>डिल]; tremulous motion; a messenger (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दिष्ठ
भन्दिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. भन्द् with the<BR>termination of the superl.), Ved. shouting or yelling<BR>most loudly, applauding or praising most highly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्ध्रुक|भन्ध्रुकः
भन्ध्रुक भन्ध्रुक, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भपञ्जर|भपञ्जरं|भपञ्जरः
भपञ्जर भ-पञ्जर, &c. See under 4. भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भप्पट
भप्पट भप्पट, अस्, m., N. of a man who<BR>built a temple named after him Bhappaṭeśvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भ|भंभ|भंभः|भम्भः
भम्भ भम्भ, अस्, m. smoke; a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भरालिका|भंभरालिका
भम्भरालिका, f. a gnat, musquito, gad-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भराली|भंभराली
भम्भराली, f. a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भारव|भंभारव|भंभारवः
भम्भारव भम्भा-रव, अस्, m. (onomato-<BR>poetic), the lowing of a cow; (also बम्भा-रव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भासार|भम्भासारः
भम्भासार भम्भासार, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king of Magadha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भय|भयं|भयः
भय भय, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. भी), fear,<BR>alarm, dread, apprehension (e. g. आत्म-भ्˚, fear for<BR>one's life; मा भयं कुरु, be not afraid; cf.<BR>दण्ड-भ्˚); dismay, fright, terror (e. g. जगद्-भ्˚,<BR>a terror to the universe); cause for fear, danger,<BR>peril, risk, jeopardy, hazard; the blossom of Trapa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-a" target="_blank">Page0700-a+ 81</a>]<BR>Bispinosa; (अस्), m. Fear personified as a son of<BR>Nir-ṛti, as a prince of the Yavanas and husband of<BR>the daughter of Time; sickness, disease; (आत्), ind.<BR>from fear, for fear; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Kāla and wife of the Rākṣasa Heti.<BR>—भय-<BR>कम्प, अस्, m. tremor from fear, the tremor of<BR>fear, trembling caused by fright.<BR>—भय-कर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, or भय-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or भय-कार-<BR>क, अस्, इका, अम्, or भय-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, fear-causing,<BR>fear-exciting, terrifying, dangerous, perilous; fearful,<BR>formidable, terrible.<BR>—भयङ्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, =<BR>भय-कर; (अस्), m. a small kind of owl (=<BR>डुण्डुल); N. of one of the Viśve Devāḥ; N. of<BR>various persons; (ई), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending upon Skanda.<BR>—भयङ्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री,<BR>तृ, = भय-कर्तृ.<BR>—भय-जात, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—भय-डिण्डिम, अस्, m. ‘terror-drum,’ a<BR>drum used in battle.<BR>—भय-त्रातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a<BR>deliverer from danger, rescuer from peril.<BR>—भय-<BR>द, अस्, आ, अम्, causing danger, inspiring fear;<BR>वह्नि-भ्˚, causing danger from fire; (अस्), m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—भय-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, apprehensive<BR>of danger, fearful.<BR>—भय-दाय, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>भय-दायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, causing danger, inspiring<BR>fear; सलिल-भयदायिन्, causing danger from water.<BR>—भय-द्रुत, अस्, आ, अम्, fleeing for fear, run-<BR>ning away in terror, routed, put to flight.<BR>—भय-<BR>नाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destructive of fear or danger; (इनी),<BR>f. a species of plant.<BR>—भय-निमीलिताक्ष, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, having the eyes closed from fear.<BR>—भय-<BR>प्रतीकार, अस्, m. counteraction or removal of fear.<BR>—भय-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, or भय-प्रदायिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, causing danger, inspiring fear, terrible.<BR>—भय-प्रस्ताव, अस्, m. an occasion of alarm,<BR>season of fear.<BR>—भय-ब्राह्मण, अस्, m. a timid<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—भय-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, scattered<BR>in terror, put to flight.<BR>—भय-विधायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>causing alarm, alarming, fearful.<BR>—भय-विप्लुत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, overwhelmed with fear, panic-struck.<BR>—भय-विह्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, disturbed or agitated<BR>with fear.<BR>—भय-व्यूह, अस्, m. ‘array against<BR>danger,’ a term applied to a particular mode of<BR>marshalling an army when threatened with danger<BR>from all sides.<BR>—भय-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, of a timo-<BR>rous disposition, timid.<BR>—भय-शोक-समाविष्ट,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, affected with fear and grief, filled with<BR>sorrow and dismay.<BR>—भय-संहृष्ट-रोमन्,<BR>आ, आ, अ, having the hair erect with terror, horrified.<BR>—भय-सन्त्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, terrified by danger,<BR>scared with terror.<BR>—भयसन्त्रस्त-मानस, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the mind scared with terror.<BR>—भय-<BR>स्थ, Ved. a perilous position, dangerous situation.<BR>—भय-स्थान, अम्, n. an occasion of alarm, cause<BR>of apprehension or fear.<BR>—भयस्थान-शत, आनि,<BR>n. pl. hundreds of occasions of fear.<BR>—भय-हर्तृ,<BR>ता, त्री, तृ, or भय-हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, re-<BR>moving or dispelling fear, a remover of fear.<BR>—भ-<BR>य-हेतु, उस्, m. a cause for fear or alarm, danger.<BR>—भयातुर (˚य-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, distressed with<BR>fear, agitated with alarm.<BR>—भयान्वित (˚य-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, filled with fear, frightened, alarmed.<BR>—भयापह (˚य-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, warding off<BR>fear or danger; a prince, king.<BR>—भयाबाध<BR>(˚य-अब्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, undisturbed by fear, unex-<BR>posed to danger.<BR>—भयार्त (˚य-आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>distressed with fear, alarmed, terrified, frightened,<BR>afraid.<BR>—भयावह (˚य-आव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, bring-<BR>ing fear or danger, causing alarm, formidable, fearful.<BR>—भयैक-प्रवण (˚य-एक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wholly<BR>inclined to the one (feeling) fear, wholly filled with<BR>alarm, wholly absorbed or engrossed by fear.<BR>—भ-<BR>योत्तर (˚य-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, attended with or<BR>succeeded by fear; [cf. उत्तर.]<BR>—भयोपशम<BR>(˚य-उप्˚), अस्, m. soothing or allaying fear, en-<BR>couraging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयमान
भयमान, अस्, m., Ved., N. of the author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda I. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानक|भयानकः
भयानक, अस्, आ, अम् (probably fr. भयान,<BR>an old anomalous present part. A. of rt. 1. भी),<BR>fearful, frightful, formidable, terrible, terrific, horrible;<BR>(अम्), n. terror; (अस्), m. a tiger; Rāhu or the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">Page0700-b+ 80</a>]<BR>Ascending Node personified; the Rasa or sentiment<BR>of terror as excited by poetical or dramatic compo-<BR>sition.<BR>—भयानक-ता, f. or भयानक-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. fearfulness, formidableness.<BR>—भयानक-रस-<BR>निर्देश, अस्, m., N. of the 144th chapter of the<BR>Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भय्य
भय्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be feared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर|भरः
भर भर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. भृ), bearing,<BR>carrying; bringing, getting; granting; cherishing,<BR>upholding, supporting, (often at the end of comps.,<BR>cf. ऋतम्-भ्˚, कटम्-भ्˚, कुलम्-भ्˚, देहम्-<BR>भ्˚, पुष्टिम्-भ्˚, विश्वम्-भ्˚); (अस्), m. the act of<BR>taking or carrying, getting, gaining, taking away,<BR>theft; a burden, load, weight, mass, (भरं कृ,<BR>to place one's weight, support one's self, cf. दुर्-भ्˚,<BR>सु-भ्˚, भार); a particular weight or measure =<BR>भार = 20 Tulās = 2000 Palas; a large quantity,<BR>great number, mass, multitude, bulk; attacking,<BR>battle, contest (Ved.); raising the voice (Ved.); a<BR>joyful song, a hymn (Ved.); [cf. Gr. βάρος.]<BR>—भ-<BR>र-हूति, इस्, f., Ved. a war-cry, war-hoop; (इस्, इस्, इ),<BR>sounding a battle-cry, raising a war-shout.<BR>—भरे-<BR>षु-जा, आस्, m., Ved. ‘born or produced amidst cries<BR>of joy,’ an epithet of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरट|भरटः
भरट, अस्, m. a potter; a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरटिक
भरटिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = भरटेन हरति, see<BR>Gaṇa Bhastrādi to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण|भरणं|भरणः
भरण, अस्, ई, अम्, bearing, cherishing, main-<BR>taining, nourishing, supporting; (अस्, ई), m. f. the con-<BR>stellation Bharaṇī; (ई), f. the creeper Luffa Fœtida<BR>or a similar plant, = घोषक; (ण्यस्), f. pl., N. of<BR>the seventh lunar asterism or Nakṣatra containing<BR>three stars and figured by the pudendum muliebre;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of bearing, supporting, cherishing,<BR>maintaining, nourishing; nutriment; wages, hire;<BR>the act of carrying; wearing; what is worn, clothes<BR>(Ved.); bringing, procuring.<BR>—भरणी-भू, ऊस्,<BR>m. ‘born from the asterism or nymph Bharaṇī,’ an<BR>epithet of Rāhu or the Ascending Node personified.<BR>—भरण्य्-आह्वा, f. the plant Tiaridium Indicum<BR>(= पर्व-पुष्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणि
भरणि, इस्, m. f. (probably) = भरणी, q. v.<BR>—भरणि-षेण or भरणि-सेन, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man; [cf. रोहिणि-षेण or रोहिणि-सेन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणीय|भरणीयः
भरणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne, to be cherished,<BR>to be supported or maintained; a dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्ड|भरंड|भरंडः|भरण्डः
भरण्ड, अस्, m. a master, owner, lord; a hus-<BR>band; a king; an ox, bull; a worm; the earth (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्य|भरण्यं
1. भरण्य (fr. भरण), Nom. P. भरण्यति,<BR>&c., = सम्-भृ, q. v.; [cf. भुरण्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्य|भरण्यं
2. भरण्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for भरणीय), to be<BR>maintained, to be cherished or protected; (आ), f.<BR>wages, hire; a woman; (अम्), n. = भरण, cherish-<BR>ing, maintaining; wages, hire; the asterism Bharaṇī.<BR>—भरण्य-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, receiving wages, working<BR>for hire; (क्), m. a hireling, servant; a labourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्यु|भरण्युः
भरण्यु, उस्, m. a master; a protector (= शर-<BR>ण्यु); a friend; fire; the moon; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत्|भरन्त्
भरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, bearing, holding; wearing;<BR>possessing, having; nourishing, maintaining, sup-<BR>porting.<BR>—भरद्-वाज, अस्, m. ‘bringing or bearing<BR>food,’ a skylark; N. of a Ṛṣi the author of various<BR>Ṛg-veda hymns, said to be a son of Bṛhas-pati,<BR>(Bharad-vāja Bārhaspatya is the author of Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 1-30, 37-43, 53-74; IX. 67, 1-3; X. 137,<BR>1: he is fabled as the Puro-hita of Divo-dāsa; but<BR>Divo-dāsa and Bharad-vāja may be the same person,<BR>cf. Ṛg-veda I. 116, 18; VI. 16, 5); N. of one of<BR>the seven sages; of an author of a law-book; of a<BR>Buddhist Arhat; N. of a district, (also read भारद्-<BR>वाज); N. of an Agni; (आस्), m. pl. the race or<BR>family of Bharad-vāja; [cf. भारद्वाज.]<BR>—भ-<BR>रद्-वाजक, अस्, m. a skylark.<BR>—भरद्वाज-प्रा-<BR>दुर्-भाव, अस्, m., N. of a division of the Bhāva-<BR>prakāśa treating of medicine.<BR>—भरद्वाज-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra work.<BR>—भरद्वाजिन् in भ-<BR>रद्वाजिनां व्रतम्, N. of a Sāman; [cf. भा-<BR>रद्वाजिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत|भरतः
भरत, अस्, आ, अम्, to be supported, being sup-<BR>ported; (अस्), m. an epithet of Agni who is supposed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-c" target="_blank">Page0700-c+ 81</a>]<BR>to be maintained or kept alive by the care of men<BR>(Ved.); N. of a particular Agni, (he has a son Bha-<BR>rata and a daughter Bharatī, cf. भरथ); a hired<BR>soldier, warrior, (perhaps in particular) the charioteer<BR>of a prince, (hence perhaps the Maruts are called<BR>sons of Bharata, i. e. of ‘the warrior’ Rudra); a<BR>(‘hired’) bard, poet, actor, dancer, mime [cf. भ-<BR>रत-पुत्रक]; a weaver; (according to Naighaṇ-<BR>ṭuka III. 18) = ऋत्व्-इज्; N. of an Āditya; N. of a<BR>celebrated hero and monarch of all India, (he was<BR>the first of a series of twelve Cakra-vartins or Sārva-<BR>bhaumas, i. e. universal emperors; as son of Duḥ-<BR>ṣanta or Dushyanta and Śakuntalā, he has the<BR>patronymic Dauḥṣanti or Dauṣyanti, also read<BR>दौष्मन्ति, दौष्वन्ति, &c.; in Ṛg-veda III.<BR>53, 24, the sons of Bharata are regarded as descend-<BR>ants of Viśvā-mitra); N. of a son of Dhruva-sandhi,<BR>father of Asita; of a son of Daśa-ratha and younger<BR>brother of Rāma; of a son of Ṛṣabha; of a son of<BR>Vīti-hotra; an epithet of a Manu who gave the<BR>name to the country Bhārata (Viṣṇu-Purāṇa II. 1);<BR>N. of a son of Manu Bhautya; of a king of Aśmaka;<BR>of an ancient Muni (the celebrated author of the<BR>Gandharva-veda or Alaṅkāra-śāstra, treating of dra-<BR>matic composition; the term is also applied to his<BR>work, which appears to have been a body of Sūtras<BR>or rules relating to every branch of dramatic writing<BR>and theatrical exhibition; although said to be lost,<BR>it is constantly quoted by the commentators on the<BR>Nāṭakas or Indian dramas); a barbarian, moun-<BR>taineer, savage, = क्षेत्र; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>tribe, ‘the descendants of Bharata;’ (आनि), n. pl., N.<BR>of a particular Varṣa; [cf. भारत.]<BR>—भरत-<BR>खण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a part of Bharata-varṣa<BR>(= कुमारिका).<BR>—भरत-ज्ञ, अस्, m. ‘knowing<BR>the science of Bharata,’ conversant with dramatic<BR>writings and rules.<BR>—भरत-त्व, अम्, n. the name<BR>‘Bharata.’<BR>—भरत-द्वादशाह (˚श-अह), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a particular festival.<BR>—भरत-पुत्रक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of Bharata,’ an actor, a mime.<BR>—भ-<BR>रत-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town (mentioned in<BR>the Bharaṭaka-dvātriṃśikā).<BR>—भरत-प्रसू, ऊस्,<BR>f. ‘the mother of Bharata,’ an epithet of Kaikeyī<BR>(wife of Daśa-ratha).<BR>—भरत-मल्ल, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a grammarian.<BR>—भरत-मल्लिक, अस्, m. =<BR>भरत-सेन, q. v.<BR>—भरत-रोह, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a man.<BR>—भरतर्षभ (˚त-ऋ˚), अस्, m. ‘bull-<BR>like descendant of Bharata,’ the best or most dis-<BR>tinguished of the Bharatas; a prince of the Bharatas.<BR>—भरत-वर्ष, अम्, n. ‘the country of Bha-<BR>rata’ (supposed to have been the first monarch of all<BR>India, cf. भरत, col. 2), a N. of India (= भा-<BR>रत).<BR>—भरत-वाक्य, अम्, n. ‘the speech of<BR>Bharata,’ N. of the seventy-seventh chapter of the<BR>Uttara-kāṇḍa or seventh book of the Rāmāyaṇa;<BR>N. of the eighty-third chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa<BR>or fourth part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—भरत-<BR>शार्दूल, अस्, m. ‘tiger-like descendant of Bharata,’<BR>the most distinguished or excellent of the Bharatas.<BR>—भरत-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, or भरत-सत्-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘best of the Bharatas,’ the most<BR>distinguished of the descendants of Bharata.<BR>—भ-<BR>रत-सेन, अस्, m., N. of an author of commentaries<BR>on the Megha-dūta, Raghu-vaṃśa, Śiśupāla-vadha,<BR>and Bhaṭṭi-kāvya.<BR>—भरत-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of<BR>a commentator on the Vedas; of an astronomer.<BR>—भरताग्रज (˚त-अग्˚), अस्, m. ‘the elder bro-<BR>ther of Bharata,’ an epithet of Rāma.<BR>—भरता-<BR>वास (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of Bharata,’ N. of the<BR>twenty-ninth chapter of the Pātāla-khaṇḍa or fourth<BR>part of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—भरताश्रम (˚त-<BR>आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘the hermitage of Bharata,’ N. of a<BR>hermitage.<BR>—भरतेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚त-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरथ|भरथः
भरथ, अस्, m. = लोक-पाल, a world-protector,<BR>a deity presiding over one of the regions of the<BR>world; a sovereign, king; fire [cf. भरत].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाज|भरद्वाजः
भरद्-वाज. See under भरत्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरम
भरम, अस्, m., N. of a man; [cf. भारमेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरस्
भरस्, अस्, n., Ved. bearing, holding, cherishing;<BR>[cf. विस्व-भ्˚, स-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0700-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरि
भरि, इस्, इस्, इ, bearing, possessing, maintaining,<BR>supporting, nourishing, (often at the end of comps.,<BR>cf. आत्मम्-भ्˚, उदरम्-भ्˚, कुक्षिम्-भ्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिणी
भरिणी, f. of 2. भरित below; [cf. हरिणी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित|भरितः
1. भरित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. भर), nourished,<BR>filled, full of; [cf. वसु-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित|भरितः
2. भरित, अस्, आ, or भरिणी, अम्, = हरित,<BR>green, of a green colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित्र|भरित्रं
भरित्र, अम्, n., Ved. the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिमन्
भरिमन्, आ, m. supporting, nourishing, cherish-<BR>ing; [cf. भरीमन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिष
भरिष, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. rapacious, avaricious,<BR>greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरीमन्
भरीमन्, आ, m., Ved. a household, family;<BR>bearing, supporting, nourishing, cherishing (in this<BR>sense the gender is doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरु|भरुः
भरु, उस्, m. a husband, lord; N. of Śiva; of<BR>Viṣṇu; gold; the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्णस्
भर्णस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. in the comp. सहस्र-<BR>भ्˚, q. v.; (according to Sāy. भर्णस् = भरण,<BR>q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तव्य|भर्त्तव्य|भर्त्तव्यं
भर्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be borne or carried;<BR>to be maintained, to be nourished or supported; to<BR>be engaged or hired, to be retained in service or<BR>kept in pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृ|भर्त्तृ
भर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a bearer, carrier (Ved.); a<BR>cherisher, nourisher, holder, supporter, protector; (ता),<BR>m. a husband, lord; master, landlord; chief, com-<BR>mander; (त्री), f. a female supporter or nourisher;<BR>a mother; [cf. जगती-भ्˚, दिवस-भ्˚, नृ-भ्˚,<BR>पशु-भ्˚, प्रोषित-भर्तृक.]<BR>—भर्तृ-गुण,<BR>अस्, m. the excellence or virtue of a husband<BR>(Manu IX. 24).<BR>—भर्तृ-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, mur-<BR>dering a master or supporter; (ई), f. a woman who<BR>murders her husband.<BR>—भर्तृघ्न-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the killing or injuring a master.<BR>—भर्तृ-ता, f. or<BR>भर्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. the state or relation of a hus-<BR>band, husbandship; manhood.<BR>—भर्तृताङ्-गत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘gone to husbandship,’ married.<BR>—भर्-<BR>तृ-दर्शन-काङ्क्षा, f. the desire of seeing a<BR>husband.<BR>—भर्तृदर्शन-लालसा, f. longing or<BR>eager desire to see a husband.<BR>—बहर्तृ-दारक,<BR>अस्, m. a king's son, a crown prince, prince royal<BR>(especially in the drama), a young prince designated<BR>as heir-apparent; (इका), f. a king's daughter, princess.<BR>—भर्तृ-दृढ-व्रता, f. strictly faithful to a<BR>husband.<BR>—भर्तृ-भक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to<BR>a lord or husband.<BR>—भर्तृ-मती, f. possessing a<BR>husband, a married woman.<BR>—भर्तृ-मेण्ठ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a poet; [cf. मेण्ठ.]<BR>—भर्तृ-यज्ञ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—भर्तृ-राज्यापहरण<BR>(˚य-अप्˚), अम्, n. seizure of a husband's kingdom.<BR>—भर्तृ-लोक, अस्, m. the sphere or abode of a<BR>husband (in a future life).<BR>—भर्तृ-व्यसन-पी-<BR>डित, अस्, आ, अम्, afflicted by a husband's or master's<BR>calamity.<BR>—भर्तृ-व्रत, अम्, n. fidelity or devo-<BR>tion to a husband [cf. पति-व्रत]; (आ), f. faithful<BR>to a husband, a virtuous and devoted wife; [cf. पति-<BR>व्रता.]<BR>—भर्तृव्रता-त्व, अम्, n. the state or<BR>condition of fidelity to a husband.<BR>—भर्तृ-शोक-<BR>पर, अस्, आ, अम्, absorbed in grief for a husband or<BR>lord.<BR>—भर्तृशोक-परीताङ्गिन् (˚त-अङ्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, whose limbs are affected by grief for a husband or<BR>lord.<BR>—भर्तृशोकाभिपीडित (˚क-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, afflicted by a husband's sorrow or by grief for a<BR>husband or lord.<BR>—भर्तृ-सात्, ind. to a husband,<BR>to the power of a husband; (with कृता) a married<BR>woman.<BR>—भर्तृ-स्थान, अम्, n., N. of a sacred<BR>place of pilgrimage.<BR>—भर्तृ-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of<BR>a poet mentioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR>—भर्तृ-हरि, इस्, m., N. of a well-known author<BR>(of 300 moral, political, and religious maxims or<BR>apothegms comprised in three Śatakas called Śṛṅ-<BR>gāra-ś˚, Nīti-ś˚, Vairāgya-ś˚, also of some gramma-<BR>tical Kārikās, and of the Vākya-padīya; and also,<BR>according to some, of the Bhaṭṭi-kāvya: he is often<BR>designated by the one name Hari, and though little<BR>is really ascertained about his history, is said to have<BR>been the brother of king Vikramāditya, who lived<BR>in the first century B. C.; according to a legend, he<BR>wrote his apothegms when leading the life of an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">Page0701-b+ 69</a>]<BR>ascetic, after a licentious youth).<BR>—भर्तृ-हीन,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, abandoned or deserted by a husband or<BR>lord.<BR>—भर्तृ-हेम, अस्, m. = भर्तृ-हरि, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्रिम
भर्त्रिम (?), अस्, आ, अम्, maintained, nourished,<BR>supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म|भर्मं|भर्म्म|भर्म्मं
भर्म, अम्, n. = भर्मन्, wages, hire; gold;<BR>a coin of a particular value; the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्मण्या|भर्म्मण्या
भर्मण्या, f. wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्मन्|भर्म्मन्
भर्मन्, अ, n. support, maintenance, nourish-<BR>ment, care [cf. अरिष्ट-भ्˚, गर्भ-भ्˚, जातू-भ्˚];<BR>a burden, load; hire, wages; gold; a coin, piece of<BR>gold, gold coin, piece of money; the navel; [cf.<BR>भर्म.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्वर
भर्वर, अस्, m., Ved. (according to Sāy.) =<BR>जगद्-भर्तृ or प्रजा-पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरग
भरग भ-र-ग, a word invented to ex-<BR>plain भर्ग (भ standing for भासयति, र for<BR>रञ्जयति, and ग for गच्छन्त्य् अस्माद् इमाः<BR>प्रजाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरट|भरटः
भरट भरट. See p. 700, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरटक
भरटक भरटक or भरडक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a particular class of mendicants.<BR>—भरटक-<BR>द्वात्रिंशिका, f., N. of thirty-two popular stories (writ-<BR>ten to ridicule the ignorance and folly of ascetics).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्ड|भरंड|भरंडः|भरण्डः
भरण्ड भरण्ड. See p. 700, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरु|भरुः
भरु भरु. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुक
भरुक भरुक, अस्, m., N. of a prince;<BR>(also written कुरुक or रुरुक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुकच्छ|भरुकच्छः
भरुकच्छ भरुकच्छ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>country, (also read मरुकच्छ); N. of a people;<BR>of a Nāga.<BR>—भरुकच्छ-निवासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, an<BR>inhabitant of Bharukaccha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुज|भरुजः
भरुज भरुज, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. rt. 1.<BR>भ्रज्ज्), a sort of jackal; [cf. भरूजा, भारुजिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुटक|भरुटकं
भरुटक भरुटक or भरूटक, अम्, n.<BR>(probably fr. rt. भॄ), fried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरूजा
भरूजा भरूजा, f. (according to Yāska fr.<BR>rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्), Ved. a particular colour, being of a<BR>particular colour (used adjectively); भरूजी in the<BR>Atharva-veda may be a N. of some wild animal; [cf.<BR>भरुज, which is variously read भरूजा; cf. भा-<BR>रूजिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरेषुजा
भरेषुजा भरेषु-जा. See भर, p. 700.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरेहनगरी
भरेहनगरी भरेह-नगरी, f., N. of a town<BR>mentioned in Nīla-kaṇṭha's Śrāddha-mayūkha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ग|भर्गः
भर्ग भर्ग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. a rt.<BR>भृज्, which is probably here for rt. भ्राज्, = Gr.<BR>φλέγω) Ved. radiance, splendor, lustre, effulgence<BR>(Ved. = भर्गस् below, cf. φλόξ); N. of Śiva; of<BR>Brahman; of a man with the patronymic Prāgātha,<BR>author of the hymns Ṛg-veda VIII. 49-50; of a<BR>king, the son of Veṇu-hotra; of Vīti-hotra; of Vahni;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a race of warriors; (अम्), n., N.<BR>of a Sāman.<BR>—भर्ग-शिखा, f., N. of a work men-<BR>tioned in the Śiva-sūtra-vivṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्गस्
भर्गस्, अस्, n., Ved. radiance, lustre, effulgence;<BR>N. of Brahman; of a Sāman.<BR>—भर्गस्-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. clear, shrill (said of the voice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ग्य|भर्ग्यः
भर्ग्य, अस्, m., N. of Śiva (= भर्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्गभूमि
भर्गभूमि भर्ग-भूमि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>king; [cf. भार्ग-भूमि, भृगु-भूमि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्गायण
भर्गायण भर्गायण, आस्, m. pl. (probably)<BR>an incorrect form for भार्गायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्छु
भर्छु भर्छु, उस्, m., N. of a poet men-<BR>tioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्जन|भर्जनं|भर्ज्जन
भर्जन भर्जन. See under rt. भृज्, p. 720.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्णस्
भर्णस् भर्णस्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तव्य|भर्त्तव्य|भर्त्तव्यं
भर्तव्य भर्तव्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृ|भर्त्तृ
भर्तृ भर्तृ. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्स्
भर्त्स् भर्त्स्, cl. 10. P. A. भर्त्सयति,<BR>-ते (according to the Dhātu-pāṭha only A.),<BR>-यितुम्, rarely cl. 1. भर्त्सति, (in Atharva-veda III.<BR>9, 5, a form भर्त्स्यामि occurs), to menace, threaten;<BR>to reproach, abuse, blame, reprove, chide, rebuke; to<BR>deride: Pass. भर्त्स्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सक|भर्त्सकः
भर्त्सक, अस्, m. a threatener, abuser, reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सन|भर्त्सनं
भर्त्सन, अम्, आ, n. f. threatening, reviling;<BR>cursing; threat, menace, reproach, abuse; a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सपत्त्रिका
भर्त्स-पत्त्रिका, f. (fr. भर्त्स ? + पत्त्र), N.<BR>of a particular plant (= महा-नीली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सित
भर्त्सित, अस्, आ, अम्, threatened, menaced, reviled,<BR>abused, blamed, upbraided, rebuked; (अम्), n. a<BR>menace, threat, curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्स्यमान
भर्त्स्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being threatened &c.,<BR>being reviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ब्
भर्ब् भर्ब् or भर्भ्. See rt. भर्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म|भर्मं|भर्म्म|भर्म्मं
भर्म भर्म, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्याश्व
भर्म्याश्व भर्म्याश्व, अस्, m., N. of a king,<BR>father of Mudgala; (also read हर्यश्व; cf. भार्-<BR>म्य, भार्म्यश्व, भृम्यश्व.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्व्
भर्व् भर्व् or भर्ब् or भर्भ् (connected<BR>with rt. 1. भस्), cl. 1. P. बर्वति or<BR>भर्बति or भर्भति, &c., Ved. to chew, devour,<BR>eat; to hurt, injure, fight; [cf. Gr. φέρβ-ω, φορβ-ή;<BR>Lat. herb-a; Goth. balvjan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्वर
भर्वर भर्वर. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्श्
भर्श् भर्श्. See under rt. भ्रंश् or<BR>भ्रश्, p. 724, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ष्टव्य
भर्ष्टव्य भर्ष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1.<BR>भ्रज्ज्), to be fried or roasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्
भल् भल् or बल् (connected with rt.<BR>भल्ल्, q. v.), cl. 1. A. भलते, बलते,<BR>&c., to describe, recount, mention; to expound, ex-<BR>plain; to strike, kill; to hurt, injure; to give; cl.<BR>10. A. भालयते, बालयते, &c., Ved. to describe;<BR>to see, behold; to throw up (?); [cf. नि-भ्˚, सम्-<BR>भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल
भल 1. भल, ind., Ved. certainly; [cf.<BR>बल्, बट्, and Marāṭhī भल्ल, ‘well!’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल
भल 2. भल, अस्, m. a term used in ad-<BR>dressing the Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भलता
भलता भ-लता, f. See under 4. भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भलन्दन|भलन्दनः
भलन्दन भलन्दन, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>of the father of Vatsa-prī or Vatsa-prīti; (ās), m.<BR>pl. the descendants of Bhalandana; [cf. भालन्दन,<BR>भालन्दनक, भनन्दन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भलानस्
भलानस् भलानस्, m. pl., Ved., N. of a<BR>particular family or race (Ṛg-veda VII. 18, 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल्
भल्ल् भल्ल् (connected with rt. भल्), cl.<BR>1. A. भल्लते, बभल्ले, &c., to tell,<BR>describe; to wound, kill, to hurt, injure; to give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल|भल्लं|भल्लः
भल्ल, अस्, ई, m. f. a kind of arrow or missile with<BR>a point of a particular shape (perhaps crescent-shaped);<BR>(अम्), n. an arrow-head of a particular shape; (अस्),<BR>m. a bear [cf. अच्छ-भ्˚, भल्लुक, भल्लूक]; an<BR>epithet of Śiva, = भद्र; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>tribe, (also read मल्ल); (ई), f. = भल्लातक, the<BR>marking-nut plant, Semecarpus Anacardium [cf. भाल्ल,<BR>भाल्लेय]; (अस्, आ, अम्), propitious, favourable (=<BR>भद्र, शिव); a term used in addressing the Sun<BR>(= 2. भल, q. v.).<BR>—भल्ल-पुच्छी, f. ‘bear's tail,’<BR>N. of the plant Hedysarum Lagopodioides.<BR>—भल्-<BR>लाक्ष (˚ल-अक्˚), अस्, m., Ved. an expression used<BR>in addressing a flamingo (= भद्राक्ष, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लक|भल्लकः
भल्लक, अस्, m. = भल्ल, a bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातक|भल्लातकः
भल्लातक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), = भल्लातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातक|भल्लातकः
भल्लातक, अस्, m. (in Amara-koṣa II. 4, 2, 23,<BR>also भल्लातकी, f.), the marking-nut plant, Seme-<BR>carpus Anacardium; (अम्), n. the Acajou or cashew-<BR>nut, the marking-nut (from which is extracted an<BR>acid juice, used for medicinal purposes, as well as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">Page0702-a+ 76</a>]<BR>black liquid used for marking linen).<BR>—भल्लातक-<BR>तैल, अम्, n. the oil of the cashew-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0701-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लुक|भल्लुकः
भल्लुक, अस्, m. a bear; [cf. भालुक, भालूक,<BR>भीलुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लूक|भल्लूकः
भल्लूक, अस्, m. a bear; a dog; a particular<BR>kind of shell (= महा-कपर्द); a particular<BR>plant, a species of Śyonāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लट
भल्लट भल्लट, अस्, m., N. of a poet men-<BR>tioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लवि
भल्लवि भल्लवि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a man;<BR>[cf. भालविन्, भाल्लवेय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लाक
भल्लाक भल्लाक, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लाट|भल्लाटं|भल्लाटः
भल्लाट भल्लाट अस्,); m., N. of a king,<BR>(also read भल्लाक); of a mythical being; of a<BR>mountain; of a gate.<BR>—भल्लाट-नगर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of the capital of king Śaśi-dhavaja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लाद
भल्लाद, अस्, m., N. of a king, = भल्लाट above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लात|भल्लातः
भल्लात भल्लात, भल्लातक. See under<BR>rt. भल्ल्, p. 701, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लिक
भल्लिक भल्लिक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आ),<BR>f. the marking-nut plant (= भल्लातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लुक|भल्लुकः
भल्लुक भल्लुक, भल्लूक. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्वाचि
भल्वाचि भल्वाचि (?), इस्, m., N. of a man<BR>mentioned in the Vāyu-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव|भवं|भवः
भव भव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. भू), = भाव,<BR>being, state of being (= सत्-ता), existing, existence;<BR>birth, production, origin; worldly existence, life; place<BR>of being, the world (= सं-सार); means of exist-<BR>ence; a sound state of being, welfare, prosperity, health<BR>(= श्रेयस्); excellence, superiority; (according to<BR>some) = आप्ति, प्राप्ति, obtaining, acquisition; a god,<BR>deity; N. of a deity attending on Rudra and frequently<BR>mentioned in connection with Śarva; (in the later<BR>mythology) a N. of Śiva or a form of Śiva; N. of a<BR>Rudra; (according to some = जल, water); of a son of<BR>Mahā-deva; of Agni (Ved.); N. of the first and fourth<BR>Kalpa; of a king; of a son of Prati-hartṛ; of Vi-<BR>loman; of an author; (औ), m. du. the god Bhava<BR>or Śiva with his wife Bhavānī; (अम्), n. the fruit<BR>of Dillenia Speciosa, = भव्य, भविष्य, 2. भा-<BR>वन; (अस्, आ, अम्), arising, coming, produced or<BR>born from, originating in, relating to, (in these<BR>senses at the end of an adj. comp., e. g. देह-भ्˚,<BR>produced from the body; आकाश-भवा, ‘coming<BR>from heaven,’ said of Sarasvatī; cf. अरण्य-भ्˚.)<BR>—भव-कल्प, अस्, m., N. of a particular Kalpa<BR>mentioned in the Vāyu-Purāṇa.<BR>—भव-कान्तार,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. (?), the wilderness of worldly exist-<BR>ence.<BR>—भव-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a particular phe-<BR>nomenon in the heavens.<BR>—भव-क्षिति, इस्, f. the<BR>place of birth.<BR>—भव-घस्मर, अस्, m. the burn-<BR>ing of a wood, a forest conflagration.<BR>—भव-चन्-<BR>द्र, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भव-च्छिद्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>preventing births or transmigration.<BR>—भव-च्छेद,<BR>अस्, m. the destruction of the world; N. of a Grāma.<BR>—भव-त्रात, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor; of a son<BR>of Bhava.<BR>—भव-दा, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda.<BR>—भव-दारु, उ, n. = देव-<BR>दारु, the tree Pinus Deodora.<BR>—भव-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the Vyavahāra-tilaka, of the<BR>Smṛti-candra, and of the Prāyaścitta-prakaraṇa.<BR>—भवदेव-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the Chandoga-paddhati.<BR>—भवदेव-मिश्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the Bhāva-prakāśa; [cf.<BR>भाव-मिश्र.]<BR>—भव-नन्द, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>actor.<BR>—भव-नन्दिन्, ई, m. ‘son of Bhava,’ N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—भव-नाग, अस्, m., N. of an author<BR>mentioned in the Payo-graha-samarthana-prakāra by<BR>Vasudeua.<BR>—भव-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भव-नाशिनी, f. ‘destroying worldly existence,’<BR>N. of the river Sarayū.<BR>—भव-निगड-निबन्ध-<BR>विनाशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying the chains and fetters<BR>of worldly existence.<BR>—भव-निभन्ध-विनाशिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, destroying the fetters of mundane exist-<BR>ence.<BR>—भव-प्रतिसन्धि, इस्, m. entering into<BR>existence, coming into being.<BR>—भव-बन्धेश<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-b" target="_blank">Page0702-b+ 81</a>]<BR>(˚ध-ईश), अस्, m. ‘the lord of the fetters of the<BR>world or worldly existence,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भव-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, sharing the world; expe-<BR>riencing existence, living.<BR>—भव-भावन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘the author of existence,’ a N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—भ-<BR>व-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, being the origin; that Being<BR>through whom all beings exist, the source of all<BR>being.<BR>—भव-भूति, इस्, m., N. of a poet who<BR>lived in the eighth century A. D., author of the three<BR>well known dramas, Mālatī-mādhava, Mahā-vīra-<BR>carita (sometimes called Vīra-carita), and Uttara-<BR>rāma-carita.<BR>—भव-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting<BR>or made up of Śiva, produced from Śiva.<BR>—भव-<BR>मोचन, अस्, m. ‘the liberator of the world or of<BR>existence,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भव-रुद्, a<BR>drum played at funeral ceremonies.<BR>—भव-वीति,<BR>इस्, f. liberation from the world; cessation from<BR>worldly acts; end of the world.<BR>—भव-समुद्र,<BR>अस्, or भव-सिन्धु, उस्, m. the ocean of existence<BR>or life, ocean of the world.<BR>—भव-स्वामिन्, ई,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—भवाचल (˚व-अच्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a mountain.<BR>—भवातिग (˚व-अत्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, overcoming worldly existence.<BR>—भवात्मजा<BR>(˚व-आत्˚), f., N. of the goddess Manasā.<BR>—भवा-<BR>नन्द (˚व-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a commentator on<BR>the Anumāna-dīdhiti; (ई), f., N. of a commentary<BR>by Bhavānanda-siddhānta-vāg-īśa.<BR>—भवानन्द-<BR>सिद्धान्त-वाग्-ईश, अस्, m., N. of an author; [cf.<BR>सिद्धान्त-वाग्-ईश.]<BR>—भवानन्दी-प्रकाश, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a commentary on the Bhavānandī by<BR>Mahā-deva Pandit.<BR>—भवान्त-कृत् (˚व-अन्˚), त्,<BR>m., N. of Brahman; of Buddha.<BR>—भवान्तर<BR>(˚व-अन्˚), अम्, n. another existence; a former ex-<BR>istence; a future existence.<BR>—भवाब्धि (˚व-अब्˚),<BR>इस्, m. the ocean of worldly existence.<BR>—भवाभ-<BR>वौ (˚व-अभ्˚), m. du. existence and non-existence;<BR>prosperity and adversity.<BR>—भवाभाव (˚व-अभ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. non-existence of the world.<BR>—भवाभिभाविन्<BR>(˚व-अभ्˚), ई, इनी, इ, overcoming the world.<BR>—भवा-<BR>भीष्ट (˚व-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘dear to Śiva,’ bdellium.<BR>—भवाम्बुरशि (˚व-अम्˚), इस्, m. the ocean of<BR>life or of worldly existence.<BR>—भवायना (˚व-अय्˚),<BR>f. ‘coming from Śiva,’ N. of the Ganges.<BR>—भवा-<BR>रण्य (˚व-अर्˚), अम्, n. the forest of worldly ex-<BR>istence.<BR>—भवारि (˚व-अरि), इस्, m. the enemy of<BR>life or existence.<BR>—भवार्णव (˚व-अर्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the ocean of existence or of life.<BR>—भवार्त (˚व-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wearied with the world, sick of<BR>worldly troubles or the vanities of life.<BR>—भवेश<BR>(˚व-ईश), अस्, m. ‘the lord of existence or of the<BR>world or of life,’ an epithet of Śiva; N. of a king,<BR>the father of Hara-siṃha.<BR>—भवोच्छेद (˚व-उच्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the destruction of the world or of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवक|भवकः
भवक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.) = भव, being, existing, existence (e. g.<BR>परार्थ-भ्˚, existing for others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
1. भवत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, being, becoming; present;<BR>(अन्ती), f. time being, present time; (with some<BR>grammarians) the technical term for the present tense;<BR>[cf. भवन्ति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
2. भवत्, आन्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. भा, to shine,<BR>Uṇādi-s. 1. 64), the honorific or respectful pronoun,<BR>generally translatable by your honour, your highness,<BR>your worship, your lordship, you (used respectfully<BR>for the second personal pronoun, but properly with<BR>the third person of the verb, e. g. भवान् ददातु,<BR>let your highness give); भवन्, voc. sing. m. ‘O<BR>sir,’ ‘O my lord,’ or contracted into भोस्, q. v.;<BR>भवद्भिस्, by your honour; (अती), f. lady, your<BR>ladyship; भवत्यस्, your ladyships; भवति, voc.<BR>sing. f. ‘O lady:’ Manu II. 49 assigns a different<BR>position in the sentence to this honorific pronoun<BR>according to the person using it; a Brāhman should<BR>say, भवति भिक्षां देहि, ‘good lady give alms;’<BR>a Kṣatriya, भिक्षाम् भवति देहि; a Vaiśya,<BR>देहि भिक्षाम् भवति: this honorific pronoun<BR>भवत् is sometimes used when त्वम् occurs in<BR>another clause of the same sentence; sometimes the<BR>plural is employed to express greater courtesy (e. g.<BR>भवन्तः प्रमाणम्, your honour is an authority);<BR>भवत् is exceptionally found in construction with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">Page0702-c+ 81</a>]<BR>the 2nd person sing.; [cf. अत्र-भ्˚, ततो-भ्˚, तत्र-<BR>भ्˚.]<BR>—भवत्-पुत्र, अस्, m. your honour's son,<BR>your highness' son, your son.<BR>—भवद्-देव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man mentioned in the Smṛti-kaustubha.<BR>—भवद्-वचन, अम्, n. your honour's speech,<BR>your speech.<BR>—भवद्-विध, अस्, आ, अम्, any one<BR>like your honour or like you.<BR>—भवद्-विधि, इस्,<BR>m. your honour's manner (i. e. the way in which you<BR>are treated).<BR>—भवन्-मन्यु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>king; [cf. भु-मन्यु, भू-मन्यु.]<BR>—भवा-<BR>दृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (भवा for भवत्), or भवा-<BR>दृश्, क्, क्, क्, or भवा-दृश, अस्, ई, अम्, any one<BR>like your honour or like you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवती
1. भवती, f. your ladyship, lady (respectfully,<BR>see under 2. भवत्, col. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवती
2. भवती, f. a particular kind of poisoned arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवतु
भवतु, ind. (3rd sing. Impv.), be it so, let it<BR>be, let it pass, very well; enough! no matter!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीय|भवदीयं
भवदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, your honour's, your, thy,<BR>thine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन|भवनं|भवनः
भवन, अम्, n. being, existing, becoming, pro-<BR>duction, birth; nature; a place of abode, house,<BR>home, dwelling; a mansion, (कमल-भवन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having a lotus for a dwelling,’ a N. of<BR>Brahmā); a palace, residence; an edifice, building,<BR>temple, structure, (often at the end of a comp., cf.<BR>अमृत-भ्˚, गर्भ-भ्˚, चर-भ्˚, देव-भ्˚); a<BR>site, spot; the place where anything grows, a field;<BR>= भुवन, water.<BR>—भवन-पति, अयस्, m. pl.<BR>or भवनाधीश (˚न-अध्˚), आस्, m. pl. (with<BR>Jainas) a particular class of gods having ten inferior<BR>classes.<BR>—भवनोदर (˚न-उद्˚), अम्, n. the in-<BR>terior apartments of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनीय|भवनीयं
भवनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be become, to be about<BR>to take place or happen; impending; (अम्), n. it<BR>is to be become; [cf. भवितव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्त|भवंत|भवंतः|भवन्तः
भवन्त, अस्, m. time, present time; (ई), f. a<BR>virtuous wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्ति|भवंति|भवंतिः|भवन्तिः
भवन्ति, इस्, m. time being, present time; [cf.<BR>भवन्ती under 1. भवत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृक्ष|भवादृक्षः
भवा-दृक्ष, भवा-दृश्, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानी
भवानी, f. (fr. भव), N. of a goddess identified<BR>in later times with Pārvatī, (she is the wife of Śiva<BR>in her pacific and amiable form; according to the<BR>Matsya-Purāṇa, especially adored in Sthāneśvara);<BR>N. of the mother of the commentator Gaṇeśa (wife<BR>of Bhava-nātha); N. of a river.<BR>—भवानी-गुरु, उस्,<BR>m. ‘the father of Bhavānī,’ the Himālaya mountain<BR>personified.<BR>—भवानी-दास, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भवानी-पति, इस्, or भवानी-वल्लभ, अस्, m.<BR>‘the husband of Bhavānī,’ Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविक|भविकं
भविक, अस्, आ, अम्, beneficial, suitable, useful;<BR>prosperous, happy, being or faring well; (अम्), n.<BR>a salutary state, prosperous condition; prosperity,<BR>welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवित|भवितः
भवित, अस्, आ, अम्, = भूत, been, become,<BR>happened, taken place, passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्य|भवितव्यं
भवितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be become, to be<BR>about to become, to be about to take place or happen;<BR>(अम्), n. it is to be become, (used impersonally with<BR>an inst., e. g. भवितव्यं त्वया, it is to be become<BR>by thee, i. e. thou must become; मया तव अनु-<BR>चरेण भवितव्यम्, I must become thy com-<BR>panion; cf. भवनीय.)<BR>—भवितव्य-ता, f. the<BR>being about to be, the state of being necessary to<BR>be, necessary consequence, inevitable necessity, fate,<BR>destiny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितृ
भवितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, = भविष्णु, being, be-<BR>coming [cf. तिरो-भ्˚]; what is or ought to be or to<BR>become, about to be, future [Lat. futurus]; immi-<BR>nent, impending, disposed or inclined to be; being<BR>or faring well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवित्र
भवित्र, अम्, n., Ved. the world, heaven, the<BR>atmosphere; (according to Sāy., Ṛg-veda VII. 35, 9)<BR>= भुवनम् अन्तरिक्षम् उदकं वा; [cf. भा-<BR>वित्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविन्
भविन्, ई, इनी, इ, living, being, having life and<BR>sensation; (ई), m. a living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविनिन्
भविनिन्, ई, m. a poet; (the reading भविन is<BR>probably incorrect.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविल|भविलः
भविल, अस्, आ, अम्, = भव्य, being, existing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">Page0703-a+ 79</a>]<BR>what is or exists; what is to be, future; (अस्), m. =<BR>विट, a catamite, voluptuary, sensualist; N. of a man<BR>(son of a certain Bhava).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0702-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्णु|भविष्णुः
भविष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. = भूष्णु, भवितृ,<BR>being, becoming, disposed or inclined to be, what is<BR>or ought to be or to become; to be about to come<BR>to pass, future; being or faring well, existing hap-<BR>pily or virtuously; (often used at the end of a comp.<BR>after an adv. in अम्, cf. अन्धम्-भ्˚, दूरम्-भ्˚,<BR>नग्नम्-भ्˚, पलितम्-भ्˚, प्रियम्-भ्˚, सुभ-<BR>गम्-भ्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्य|भविष्यः
भविष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be about to become;<BR>to be about to come to pass, future, imminent, im-<BR>pending; (अम्), n. the future; (scil. पुराण), N.<BR>of a Purāṇa; the fruit of Dillenia Speciosa (= भव,<BR>2. भावन).<BR>—भविष्य-काल, अस्, m. the future<BR>tense.<BR>—भविष्य-गङ्गा, f., N. of a river.<BR>—भ-<BR>विष्य-ज्ञान, अम्, n. knowledge of futurity.<BR>—भ-<BR>विष्य-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of one of the eighteen<BR>Purāṇas; [this Purāṇa is supposed to have been<BR>communicated by Sumantu to Śatānīka, a king of<BR>the Pāṇḍu family; the original is said to have been<BR>a revelation of future events by Brahmā; the ex-<BR>tant Purāṇa is not so much a book of prophecies,<BR>as a manual of religious rites and observances; the<BR>commencement however treats of creation and is<BR>little else than a transcript of Manu.]<BR>—भविष्योत्-<BR>तर (˚य-उत्˚), or भविष्योत्तर-पुराण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of the second part of the Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa,<BR>(like that Purāṇa it is a sort of manual of religious<BR>observances.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यत्|भविष्यन्त्
भविष्यत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, about to be or<BR>become, about to come to pass, future; (अत्), n. futu-<BR>rity, the future, future time.<BR>—भविष्यत्-काल, अस्,<BR>m. future time, futurity.<BR>—भविष्यत्-ता, f. or भ-<BR>विष्यत्-त्व, अम्, n. the being about to come to<BR>pass, futurity.<BR>—भविष्यद्-आक्षेप, अस्, m. de-<BR>nying that a possible future event will come to pass.<BR>—भविष्यद्-वक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, or भविष्यद्-<BR>वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, predicting future events, prophe-<BR>cying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवीत्व
भवीत्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवीयस्
भवीयस्. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्य|भव्यं|भव्यः
भव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being, existing, being present;<BR>to be become, (sometimes used impersonally, e. g.<BR>भव्यम् अनेन, it is to be become by him); to<BR>be about to be or become; to be about to come to<BR>pass, future (= भाविन्); likely to be or occur, on<BR>the point of becoming [cf. धेनुम्-भव्या]; what<BR>ought to be, suitable, proper, fit, right (= योग्य);<BR>good, excellent; showy in appearance, handsome,<BR>beautiful, nice, pleasant; happy, auspicious, pros-<BR>perous, fortunate; calm, placid, tranquil in mind;<BR>true; (अस्), m., N. of a small fruit tree commonly<BR>called Kāmaraṅga, Averrhoa Carambola; of a son of<BR>Dhruva or the pole-star; of a son of Priya-vrata; of<BR>a Buddhist teacher; (आस्), m. pl. a particular class<BR>of gods under Manu Cākṣuṣa; (आ), f. an epithet<BR>of Umā (Pārvatī); = करि-पिप्पली; a sort of pepper,<BR>Piper Chaba, (a wrong form for चव्या); (अम्), n.<BR>that which is or exists (= यद् भवति); being,<BR>existence, the being present; future time (e. g. भ-<BR>वद्-भूत-भव्ये, in the present, past, and future);<BR>result, fruit; the fruit of the Averrhoa Carambola;<BR>the fruit of the Dillenia Indica; a bone; (अस्, अम्),<BR>m. n. a division of the poetical Rasas or sentiments.<BR>—भव्य-जीवन, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Niryukti-bhāṣya, a Gujarāṭhī commentary on certain<BR>Jaina doctrines.<BR>—भव्य-ता, f. suitableness, good-<BR>ness, excellence, beauty; futurity.<BR>—भव्य-रूप,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘of a good figure or form,’ good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविपुला
भविपुला भ-विपुला. See under 3. भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवीयस्
भवीयस् भवीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, Ved. (pro-<BR>bably a compar. form fr. भूरि), more abundant,<BR>more plentiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भशिरा
भशिरा भशिरा, f. a sort of beet, Beta<BR>Bengalensis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष्
भष् भष्, cl. 1. P. (in epic poetry also<BR>A.) भषति (-ते), बभाष, भषि-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">Page0703-b+ 80</a>]<BR>तुम्, to bark, growl; to bark at, rail against, re-<BR>proach, revile (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष|भषः
भष, अस्, ई, अम्, barking, yelping; chiding,<BR>Ved.; (अस्), m. a dog; (ई), f. a bitch; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a particular species of plant (= स्वर्ण-क्षीरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषक|भषकः
भषक, अस्, m. a barker, a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषण|भषणं|भषणः
भषण, अस्, m. a barker, a dog; (अम्), n. the<BR>act of barking, the barking of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषत्
1. भषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, barking, howling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषत्
भषत् 2. भषत् (?), m. the heart; the<BR>thigh; wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्
भस् 1. भस्, cl. 3. P. बभस्ति (pl. बप्-<BR>सति, Impv. 3rd du. बब्धाम्, Pāṇ. VI.<BR>4, 100), भसितुम्, Ved. to chew, chew asunder; to<BR>eat, eat up, devour, consume [cf. rt. 1. प्सा]; to crush;<BR>(according to the Dhātu-pāṭha) to blame or abuse<BR>[cf. rt. भर्त्स्]; to shine [cf. rts. 1. भा, भास्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्
2. भस्, अस्, n., Ved. ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसद्
भसद्, द्, m. the hinder parts [cf. भासद];<BR>pudendum muliebre; mons Veneris; the sun; a<BR>month; time [cf. भसन्त, भासन्त]; a sort of<BR>duck; a float, raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसद्य
भसद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being or situated on the<BR>hinder parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन|भसनः
भसन, अस्, m. a bee; (also भसल ?.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन्त|भसंत|भसंतः|भसन्तः
भसन्त, अस्, m. time; [cf. भसद् and भ-<BR>वन्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसित|भसितं
भसित, अस्, आ, अम्, reduced to ashes; (अम्), n.<BR>ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रका
भस्त्रका, f. a diminutive fr. भस्त्रा below;<BR>[cf. भस्त्राका, भस्त्रिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रा
भस्त्रा, f. a bellows or a large hide with valves<BR>and a clay nozzle so used; a leathern bottle or vessel<BR>(used for carrying or holding water); a skin, pouch,<BR>leathern bag [cf. मात्रा-भ्˚]; a particular manner<BR>of recitation; [cf. भास्त्रायण.]<BR>—भस्त्रा-फल,<BR>f. a species of plant; (also written भस्त्र-फला.)<BR>—भस्त्रा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, furnished with a bellows<BR>or sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्राका
भस्त्राका, f. a diminutive fr. भस्त्रा above;<BR>[cf. भस्त्रका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रिक
भस्त्रिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (according to Pāṇ. IV. 4,<BR>16) = भस्त्रया हरति; (आ), f. (diminutive fr.<BR>भस्त्रा), a little bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्री
भस्त्री, f. = भस्त्रा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रीय
भस्त्रीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a bellows or<BR>leathern bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मक|भस्मकं
भस्मक, अस्, आ, अम्, in भस्मकाग्नि = भस्-<BR>माग्नि, q. v.; (अम्), n. a disease of the eyes (thick-<BR>ening of the membrane with indistinctness of vision);<BR>morbid appetite from over-digestion of food [cf.<BR>भस्माग्नि]; gold or silver; a species of plant (=<BR>विडङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मन्
भस्मन्, आ, आ, अ, chewing, consuming, Ved.; (अ),<BR>n. ‘what is crushed or consumed by fire,’ what is<BR>reduced to ashes, ashes; [cf. भास्मन.]<BR>—भस्म-<BR>कार, अस्, m. ‘making ashes,’ i. e. using the ashes<BR>of wood in place of soap or lye, a washerman.<BR>—भस्म-कूट, अस्, m. a heap of ashes; N. of a<BR>mountain in Kāma-rūpa; [cf. भस्माचल.]<BR>—भस्-<BR>म-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, see भस्मी-कृत.<BR>—भस्म-<BR>कौमुदी, f., N. of a work by Prāṇa-kṛṣṇa on<BR>quicksilver and other metals.<BR>—भस्म-गन्धा or<BR>भस्म-गन्धिका or भस्म-गन्धिनी, f. ‘having<BR>the smell of ashes,’ a kind of perfume (= रेणुका).<BR>—भस्म-गर्भ, अम्, n. the tree Dalbergia<BR>Ougeinensis, = तिनिश; (आ), f. a species of plant (=<BR>कपिला); a kind of perfume (= रेणुका).<BR>—भस्म-<BR>गुण्ठन, अम्, n. the act of covering with ashes.<BR>—भस्म-चय, अस्, m. a heap of ashes, an ash-heap.<BR>—भस्म-च्छन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with ashes.<BR>—भस्म-जाबाल, N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—भस्म-<BR>ता, f. the state or condition of ashes; (भस्मतां<BR>या, to go to ashes, become ashes.)<BR>—भस्म-तूल,<BR>अम्, n. frost, snow; a shower of dust (= पांसु-<BR>वर्ष); a number of villages.<BR>—भस्मनि-हुत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘one who has sacrificed in ashes,’ i. e.<BR>done a useless work.<BR>—भस्म-पुञ्ज, अस्, m. a<BR>heap of ashes, quantity or collection of ashes.<BR>—भस्-<BR>म-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘friend of ashes,’ an epithet of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-c" target="_blank">Page0703-c+ 79</a>]<BR>Śiva.<BR>—भस्म-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become ashes,<BR>changed into ashes, dead.<BR>—भस्म-मेह, अस्, m.<BR>a particular disease of the bladder, a sort of gravel.<BR>—भस्म-राजी, f., Ved. a row of ashes, line or<BR>stripe of ashes.<BR>—भस्म-राशी-कृ, cl. 8. P. A.<BR>-करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to turn into a heap of<BR>ashes.<BR>—भस्मराशी-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, turned or<BR>changed into a heap of ashes.<BR>—भस्म-रेणु, उस्,<BR>m. the dust of ashes.<BR>—भस्म-रोग, अस्, m. a<BR>particular disease, a kind of bulimy; [cf. भस्-<BR>माग्नि.]<BR>—भस्म-रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, afflicted with<BR>the disease called bulimy.<BR>—भस्म-रोहा, f. ‘grow-<BR>ing on ashes,’ a species of plant (= दग्धा, दग्-<BR>ध-रुहा).<BR>—भस्म-लेपन, अम्, n. the act of<BR>smearing with ashes.<BR>—भस्म-विधि, इस्, m. any<BR>rite or ceremony performed with ashes.<BR>—भस्म-<BR>वेधक, अस्, m. camphor.<BR>—भस्म-शय्या-श-<BR>यान, अस्, m. ‘lying on a couch of ashes,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—भस्म-शायिन्, ई, m. ‘lying on ashes,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भस्म-शुद्धि-कर, अस्, m.<BR>‘performing purification with ashes,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—भस्म-सात्, ind. to the state of ashes, com-<BR>pletely into ashes; (with rt. कृ or नी, to reduce to<BR>ashes; with rt. गम् or या or अस् or भू, to go to<BR>the state of ashes, become ashes, be reduced to ashes.)<BR>—भस्म-स्नान, अम्, n. purification by ashes.<BR>—भस्मा-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to reduce to ashes.<BR>—भस्माख्य (˚म-<BR>आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, called ashes, nothing but ashes.<BR>—भस्माग्नि (˚म-अग्˚), इस्, m., N. of a disease<BR>in which the food is over-digested or as it were<BR>reduced to ashes, a kind of bulimy (?).<BR>—भस्मा-<BR>चल (˚म-अच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a mountain in<BR>Kāma-rūpa; [cf. भस्म-कूट.]<BR>—भस्मान्त<BR>(˚म-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ending in ashes, finish-<BR>ing with ashes (said of the body when burnt on the<BR>funeral pyre); भस्मान्ते, Ved. in the neighbour-<BR>hood of ashes.<BR>—भस्मान्ति, ind. (= भस्म-स-<BR>मीपे), near ashes, in the neighbourhood of ashes.<BR>—भस्मापस् (˚म-आप्˚), f. pl. water with ashes.<BR>—भस्मावृताङ्ग (˚म-आव्˚, ˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the body covered with ashes.<BR>—भस्-<BR>माह्वय (˚म-आह्˚), अस्, m. camphor.<BR>—भस्मी-<BR>करण, अम्, n. the act of reducing to ashes; com-<BR>pletely consuming or burning; calcining.<BR>—भस्मी-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>into ashes, reduce to ashes.<BR>—भस्मी-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, reduced to ashes; calcined (as a metal).<BR>—भस्-<BR>मी-कृत्य, ind. having reduced to ashes.<BR>—भस्मी-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the state or condition of becoming<BR>ashes.<BR>—भस्मी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्,<BR>to become ashes.<BR>—भस्मी-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>come ashes, reduced to ashes, being mere ashes,<BR>being wholly worthless.<BR>—भस्मोद्धूलित-विग्रह<BR>(˚म-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘whose body is strewed over<BR>with ashes,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भस्मोद्वपन<BR>(˚म-उद्˚), अम्, n., Ved. the act of pouring or<BR>shaking out ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसद्
भसद् भसद्, भसन, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रा
भस्त्रा भस्त्रा, भस्त्रिक, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मन्
भस्मन् भस्मन्, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
भा 1. भा [cf. rts. 1. भस्, भाष्, भास्],<BR>cl. 2. P. भाति, बभौ, भास्यति, अभासीत्,<BR>भायात्, भातुम्, to shine, be bright or luminous,<BR>to be splendid or beautiful; to be conspicuous or<BR>eminent; to appear, seem; to show one's self, mani-<BR>fest any feeling; to be, exist: Pass. भायते: Caus.<BR>भापयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबीभपत्, to cause to<BR>shine or appear: Desid. बिभासति: Intens. बाभा-<BR>यते, बाभेति, बाभाति; [cf. Zend bā-nu, ‘a ray;’<BR>bā-ma, ‘brightness:’ Gr. φη-μί, φά-σκ-ω, φά-τι-ς,<BR>φήμη, φανή, φαίνω, φαν-ε-ρό-ς, φαν-ή, φά-σι-ς,<BR>φά-σ-μα; φά-ε (Homeric), ‘he appeared;’ ὑπό-φαυ-σι-ς,<BR>φά-ος, φαῦ-ος, φῶς, φέγγ-ος, φα-έ-θ-ω, φαε-ίν-ω<BR>φαει-νό-ς, φᾱνό-ς, φαίδιμος, πι-φαύ-σκ-ω:<BR>Lat. fā-rī, fā-ma, fā-tu-m, fā-s, fā-bu-la, fă-t-<BR>eo-r, fa-c-s, fă-c-ie-s, făc-ē-tu-s, fav-illa, focus,<BR>februus (fr. the Caus.): Slav. o-ba-v-a-ti, ‘incan-<BR>tare;’ ba-s-nĭ, ‘a tale.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0703-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
2. भा, भास्, f. [cf. 4. भ], light, brightness, splen-<BR>dor (Ved., cf. 2. भास्); lustre, beauty; the reflection of<BR>any object, shadow; (आस्), m. the sun.<BR>—भा-ऋजीक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. light-shedding, radiating, radiant<BR>(Sāy. = प्रकाशस्य प्रार्जयितृ, said of Agni).<BR>—भा-कूट, अस्, m. ‘having a point or peak of<BR>light,’ a species of fish, (also भा-कुट); N. of a<BR>mountain (apparently the part of the Himālaya<BR>called Bhākūr).<BR>—भा-कोश, अस्, m. ‘repository of<BR>light,’ the sun.<BR>—भा-गण, अस्, m. the whole col-<BR>lection of stars or constellations, (for भ-गण.)<BR>—भा-त्वक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. producing light.<BR>—भा-निकर, अस्, m. a multitude of rays, a mass<BR>of light.<BR>—भा-नेमि, इस्, m. ‘a circle of light or<BR>rays,’ the sun.<BR>—भान्-द, अम्, n. ‘giving light,’<BR>N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—भा-मण्डल, अम्, n. a<BR>circle of light, crown or diadem of light, garland of<BR>rays.<BR>—भामती, f. (fr. भा-मत्), or भामती-नि-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a commentary by Vācaspati-<BR>miśra on Śaṅkarācārya's commentary on the Brahma-<BR>sūtras.<BR>—भामती-कार, अस्, m., N. of Vācaspati-<BR>miśra, the author of the Bhāmatī as well as of several<BR>other treatises on the different systems of philosophy.<BR>—भामती-निबन्ध = भामती, q. v.<BR>—भा-<BR>रुचि, इस्, m., N. of an author mentioned in the<BR>Mitākṣarā to whom a commentary on Yājña-<BR>valkya's Dharma-śāstra is ascribed.<BR>—भा-रूप, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, (perhaps fr. भास् + रूप), Ved. light, shining,<BR>bright, splendid.<BR>—१. भा-वन, अम्, n. (for 2. भा-<BR>वन see p. 708, col. 1), a forest of light, sea of<BR>glory, a mass of rays.<BR>—भा-सर्व-ज्ञ, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भात्
भात्, भान्, भान्ती or भाती, भात्, shining,<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भात|भातं|भातः
भात, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, bright, splendid, re-<BR>splendent; (अस्), m. dawn, morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाति|भातिः
भाति, इस्, f. light, brightness, splendor; the being<BR>clear or evident, perception, knowledge (= प्र-तीति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भातु|भातुः
भातु, उस्, m. the sun; [cf. भानु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भान|भानं
भान, अम्, n. the act of appearing or growing<BR>visible, appearance; being clear or evident, per-<BR>ception.<BR>—भान-तस्, ind. in consequence of the<BR>appearance.<BR>—भान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having the<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानवीय
भानवीय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भानु), Ved. coming<BR>from the sun (as rays); (अम्), n. the right eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानु|भानुः
भानु, उस्, m. appearance, brightness, light [cf.<BR>अहि-भ्˚]; a ray of light; the sun; beauty; N. of<BR>an Āditya; day; a sovereign, king, prince, master;<BR>N. of Śiva (= हर); of a Deva-gandharva; of a<BR>son of Kṛṣṇa; of a Yādava; of the father of the<BR>fifteenth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; of a<BR>prince (son of Prati-vyoma); of a son of Viśva-<BR>dhara and brother of Hari-nātha; of a pupil of<BR>Śaṅkarācārya; of an author; (अवस्), m. pl. the<BR>Ādityas (children of Bhānu); the gods of the<BR>third Manv-antara; (उस्), f. = भानु-मती, a hand-<BR>some woman; N. of a daughter of Dakṣa (wife of<BR>Dharma or Manu and mother of Bhānu or Āditya);<BR>of the mother of Devarṣabha; of a daughter of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; of the mother of the Dānava Śakuni.<BR>—भानु-केसर or भानु-केशर, अस्, m. the sun.<BR>—भानु-ज, अस्, m. ‘son of the Sun,’ the planet<BR>Saturn.<BR>—भानुजी-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Bhaṭṭoji-dīkṣita.<BR>—भानु-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man; of the author of the Rasa-taraṅgiṇī; of the<BR>author of the Rasa-mañjarī.<BR>—भानु-दिन, अम्, n.<BR>Sunday; [cf. भानु-वार.]<BR>—भानु-दीक्षित, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a commentator on the Amara-kośa.<BR>—भानु-देव, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भानु-<BR>पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of a poet with the epithet Śrī-<BR>vaidya.<BR>—भानु-फला, f. the plant Musa Sapien-<BR>tum; [cf. अंशुमत्-फला.]<BR>—भानु-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the preceptor of Nārāyaṇa-dāsa.<BR>—भानु-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, luminous, splendid, resplendent;<BR>beautiful, handsome; containing the word भानु;<BR>(आन्), m. the sun; N. of a man with the patronymic<BR>Aupamanyava; of a warrior on the side of the<BR>Kurus, (according to the commentator) a son of<BR>Kaliṅga; of a son of Kuśa-dhuaja (or Keśi-dhvaja);<BR>of Bṛhad-aśva [cf. भानु-रथ]; of Bharga; of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">Page0704-b+ 76</a>]<BR>son of Kṛṣṇa; (मती), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Aṅgiras; of a daughter of Kṛta-vīrya (wife of Ahaṃ-<BR>yāti); of a daughter of the Yādava Bhānu; of a<BR>daughter of Vikramāditya; of the mother of Śaṅkara<BR>(who wrote a commentary on the Śakuntalā).<BR>—भा-<BR>नुमतिन्, ई, m. (fr. भानु-मत् or भानु + मति),<BR>Ved., N. of a man.<BR>—भानु-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>consisting of rays.<BR>—भानु-मित्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king, a son of Candra-giri [cf. भानु-रथ]; of a<BR>son of Udaya-siṃha.<BR>—भानु-रथ, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a king, a son of Candra-giri, (also written भानू-<BR>रथ); N. of a son of Bṛhad-aśva; [cf. भानु-<BR>मत्.]<BR>—भानु-वन, अम्, n. ‘wood of the sun,’<BR>N. of a wood; (also read भार्ग-वन.)<BR>—भानु-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भानु-वार, अस्,<BR>m. ‘day of the sun,’ Sunday; [cf. भानु-दिन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुसेन
—भानु-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुल
भानुल, अस्, m. a diminutive from Bhānu-datta<BR>(used by way of endearment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
1. भाम, अस्, m. (for 2. see rt. भाम्, p. 706),<BR>light, brightness, splendor; the sun.<BR>—भाम-नी, ईस्,<BR>ईस्, इ, Ved. ‘bearing light,’ an epithet of Puruṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिन्
1. भामिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. 1. भाम; for 2. see<BR>under rt. भाम्), shining, glittering, beautiful, hand-<BR>some; proud; (इनी), f. a handsome woman; N. of<BR>the daughter of a Gandharva.<BR>—भामिनी-विलास, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a poem by Jagan-nātha in four chapters,<BR>(the first book contains allegorical precepts, the<BR>second includes amatory subjects, the third an elegy<BR>[karuṇa] on the death of a wife, the fourth teaches<BR>that consolation is only to be obtained by adoration<BR>of Kṛṣṇa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भांश
भांश भांश. See under 4. भ, p. 694.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाःकर
भाःकर भाः-कर, भाः-करण. See भास्-<BR>कर, &c., p. 709, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाःखर
भाःखर भाः-खर, भाः-पति, भाः-फेरु,<BR>= भास्-खर, &c., see Vopa-deva II. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाकुट|भाकुटः
भाकुट भा-कुट, भा-कूट, भा-कोश. See<BR>under 2. भा, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाकुरि
भाकुरि भाकुरि, a patronymic. See भे-<BR>कुरि, p. 721, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्त|भाक्तं
भाक्त 1. भाक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भक्त),<BR>regularly fed by another; a dependent, retainer; fit<BR>for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्त|भाक्तं
2. भाक्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भक्ति), inferior, secon-<BR>dary, (opposed to मुख्य); (आस्), m. pl. ‘the<BR>faithful ones, the pious ones,’ N. of a Vaiṣṇava sect;<BR>of a Śaiva sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्तिक|भाक्तिकः
भाक्तिक, अस्, ई, अम्, = 1. भाक्त, regularly fed<BR>by another; (अस्), m. one who is fed by another, a<BR>dependent, retainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्ष
भाक्ष भाक्ष. See p. 695, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्षालक
भाक्षालक भाक्षालक, relating to or com-<BR>ing from the place Bhakṣālī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग|भागः
भाग 1. भाग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. भज्), a part,<BR>portion, share, lot, division, allotment, partition,<BR>distribution [cf. दाय-भ्˚]; portioning out; good<BR>portion, fortunate lot, good fortune, luck, destiny<BR>(Ved.); a fraction, part of any whole, a part of a<BR>whole (e. g. शत-भ्˚, the hundredth part); a quarter<BR>(in एक-भ्˚, one fourth; त्रि-भ्˚, three fourth); part<BR>of anything given as interest; the numerator of a<BR>fraction; a division of time, the thirtieth part of a<BR>Rāśi or zodiacal sign; a degree or 360th part of the<BR>circumference of a great circle; a quotient; a half<BR>rupee; place, spot, region, side, border; N. of a<BR>king, (also भागवत); N. of one of the branches<BR>of the river Candra-bhāgā, q. v.; (अस्, आ, अम्), taking<BR>the place of any one, representing, (at the end of<BR>adj. comps., cf. भाजन); (अम्), n., N. of a parti-<BR>cular Sāman.<BR>—भाग-कल्पना, f. the allotment of<BR>shares.<BR>—भाग-जाति, इस्, f. assimilation of fractions,<BR>reduction of fractions to a common denominator;<BR>[cf. अंश-सवर्णन.]<BR>—भागजाति-चतुष्टय,<BR>अम्, n. four modes of assimilation of fractions or of<BR>reducing them to a common denominator.<BR>—भा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">Page0704-c+ 81</a>]<BR>गञ्-जय, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भाग-दा, आस्,<BR>आस्, अम्, Ved. granting or giving a share.<BR>—भाग-<BR>दुघ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. yielding or dealing out<BR>portions, distributing.<BR>—भाग-ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. paying a share, discharging or paying what is<BR>due.<BR>—भाग-धेय, अम्, n. share, portion, part,<BR>lot, portion allotted by destiny, luck, fortune, fate,<BR>destiny; property; happiness; (अस्), m. revenue,<BR>tax, dues, impost; one to whom a share is due, an<BR>heir, co-heir; (अस्, ई, अम्), Ved. due as a share or<BR>part.<BR>—भाग-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, having a share in (any-<BR>thing), interested, a partner.<BR>—भाग-भुज्, क्, m.<BR>‘enjoying taxes,’ a king, sovereign.<BR>—भाग-मातृ,<BR>ता, f. a particular rule of division.<BR>—भाग-मुख,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भाग-लक्षणा, f. (in<BR>rhetoric) insinuation or intimation of a part.<BR>—भा-<BR>ग-विज्ञेय, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भाग-वृत्ति,<BR>इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR>—भागवृत्ति-कार, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an author mentioned in the Prauḍha-mano-ramā.<BR>—भाग-शस्, ind. in parts or portions, according to<BR>a share or portion; one part after another, by turns,<BR>alternately; by and by.<BR>—भाग-हर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>taking a part, sharing; (अस्), m. a co-heir; (in<BR>arithmetic) division.<BR>—भाग-हार, अस्, m. (in<BR>arithmetic) division; [cf. भाजन, छेदन.]<BR>—भाग-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, inheriting; (ई), m. an<BR>heir.<BR>—भागानुबन्ध-जाति (˚ग-अन्˚), इस्, f. assi-<BR>milation of quantities by fractional increase; reduc-<BR>tion of quantities to uniformity by the addition of a<BR>fraction.<BR>—भागापहार-जाति (˚ग-अप्˚), इस्, f. assi-<BR>milation of quantities by fractional decrease, reduction<BR>of quantities to uniformity by the subtraction of a<BR>fraction.<BR>—भागार्थिन् (˚ग-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, desirous<BR>of a share (as of a sacrifice).<BR>—भागार्ह (˚ग-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, entitled to a portion or inheritance; to<BR>be divided according to shares.<BR>—भागासुर (˚ग-<BR>अस्˚), अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—भागी-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>A. -करोति, -कुरुते, -कर्तुम्, to divide, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग|भागः
2. भाग, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. relating to Bhaga (as<BR>a hymn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागक|भागकः
भागक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR>= 1. भाग, q. v., sharing, dividing; (अस्), m. (?),<BR>a divisor (in arithmetic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागन|भागनं
भागन, अम्, n. (? for भा-गण, col. 1), the<BR>period of the sun's passing through the signs of the<BR>zodiac; the zodiac; the circumference of a great circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवत|भागवतं|भागवतः
भागवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भग-वत्), relating<BR>to or coming from Bhaga-vat, i. e. Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa;<BR>worshipping Bhaga-vat; holy, sacred, divine; (अस्),<BR>m. a follower of Bhaga-vat, worshipper of Viṣṇu<BR>or Kṛṣṇa; N. of a king.<BR>—भागवत-तात्पर्य,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work by Ānanda-tīrtha or Madhu.<BR>—भागवत-पुराण, अम्, n., N. of the most<BR>celebrated and popular of the eighteen Purāṇas,<BR>especially dedicated to the glorification of Viṣṇu,<BR>(it was narrated by Śuka, son of Vyāsa, to king<BR>Parīkṣit, grandson of Arjuna, who in consequence<BR>of a hermit's curse had been bitten by as snake, and<BR>desired to die with his thoughts fixed on Viṣṇu;<BR>the tenth book, which is the most characteristic and<BR>best known part of the Purāṇa, is devoted to the<BR>history of Kṛṣṇa.)<BR>—भागवत-भावार्थ-दी-<BR>पिका (˚व-अर्˚), f., N. of a commentary by Śrī-<BR>dhara on the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa.<BR>—भागवत-लीला-<BR>रहस्य, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—भागवत-सन्-<BR>दर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—भागवत-सार-<BR>समुच्चय, अस्, m. (perhaps) N. of a collection of<BR>the works of Vallabha.<BR>—भागवतामृत (˚त-<BR>अम्˚), अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवति
भागवति, इस्, m. (probably) a patronymic from<BR>Bhaga-vat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवित्त
भागवित्त, आस्, m. pl. the pupils or followers of<BR>Bhāgavittika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवित्तायन
भागवित्तायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhā-<BR>gavitti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवित्ति
भागवित्ति, इस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from Bha-<BR>gavitta; N. of a son of Kuthumi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवित्तिक
भागवित्तिक, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhā-<BR>gavitti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवित्तिकीय
भागवित्तिकीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Bhāgavittika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0704-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिक|भागिकं
भागिक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to a part; forming<BR>one part; having a part; fractional; bearing interest,<BR>subject to a fractional deduction for interest, (भागि-<BR>कं शतम्, one part in a hundred, i. e. one per<BR>cent; भागिका विंशतिः, one part in twenty, i. e.<BR>five per cent); (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिन्
भागिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a portion or share, shar-<BR>ing, one who shares, a partner; sharing in, partaking<BR>of, participating in [cf. दुःख-भ्˚]; concerned<BR>in, (अपचय-भागिन्, concerned in a loss); one to<BR>whom a share is due, entitled to; possessing, a pos-<BR>sessor, owner; consisting of parts or shares; having<BR>a good portion, having luck, lucky, fortunate; (ई),<BR>m. a co-heir; (इनी), f. a co-heiress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिनेय|भागिनेयः
भागिनेय, अस्, m. (fr. भगिनी), a sister's son;<BR>(ई), f. a sister's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागीयस्
भागीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of भागिन्), hav-<BR>ing a larger share, entitled to a larger share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागीरथ
भागीरथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भगीरथ), relating<BR>to Bhagīratha; (ई), f. a N. of the Ganges; also of<BR>one of the three main streams or branches of the<BR>Ganges, viz. the great western branch; [cf. नव-<BR>द्वीप.]<BR>—भागीरथ-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्य|भाग्यं
1. भाग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. भग), relating to<BR>Bhaga; (with युग) the twelfth or last lustrum in<BR>Jupiter's cycle of sixty years; (अम्), n., scil. भ or<BR>नक्षत्र, the asterism of Bhaga or = the seven-<BR>teenth asterism or latter Phalgunī (see नक्षत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्य|भाग्यं
2. भाग्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. भाग or fr. rt. भज्),<BR>to be shared, to be divided, divisible (= भज्य);<BR>entitled to a share; = भागिक, forming a part, sub-<BR>ject to a fractional deduction (e. g. भाग्यं शतम्,<BR>one for a hundred, one in a hundred, one per cent);<BR>lucky, fortunate [cf. निर्-भ्˚]; (अम् or आनि), n. sing.<BR>or plur. good or bad fortune (resulting from merit or<BR>demerit in former existences); lot, luck, fate, destiny,<BR>fortune; happiness, welfare; sensual pleasure (?);<BR>(एन), ind. by good fortune, fortunately, happily.<BR>—भाग्य-क्रमेण, ind. in course of fortune.<BR>—भाग्य-भाव, अस्, m. state of fortune.<BR>—भा-<BR>ग्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having good qualities, possess-<BR>ing good fortune, fortunate; happy, prosperous.<BR>—भाग्यवत्-ता, f. fortunateness, good fortune.<BR>—भाग्य-वशात्, ind. from the force or influence<BR>of destiny, through the will of fate, through fortune.<BR>—भाग्य-वृत्ति, इस्, f. course or state of fortune,<BR>destiny.<BR>—भाग्योदय (˚य-उद्˚), अस्, m. rise or<BR>dawn of fortune, commencement of good fortune,<BR>rising prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
भाज्, क्, क्, क्, (usually at the end of comps.)<BR>sharing, a sharer; sharing in, participating in, par-<BR>taking of; entitled to; possessing, a possessor, ob-<BR>taining, having, enjoying [cf. रिक्थ-भ्˚, मोक्ष-<BR>भ्˚, स्वप्न-भ्˚]; perceiving, feeling, being sensible<BR>of, devoting one's self to; forming a part of, be-<BR>longing to (Ved.); joined or connected with; occu-<BR>pying (as a seat, place), inhabiting, living in, dwelling<BR>in or on [cf. विष्टर-भ्˚, हर्म्य-भ्˚, यमुना-<BR>भ्˚]; seeking, resorting to, going to, (अङ्क-भाज्,<BR>going to the side or to close proximity, close at hand,<BR>soon to be accomplished); flowing to; revering,<BR>worshipping (e. g. अनन्य-भाज्, worshipping no<BR>other); honouring [cf. लब्ध-वर्ण-भ्˚]; falling<BR>to the share or lot of; what is due, duty, concern,<BR>business, (Bhaṭṭi-k. III. 21 = कर्तव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजक|भाजकः
भाजक, अस्, m. (fr. Caus. of rt. भज्), dividing;<BR>(in arithmetic) a divisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजन|भाजनं
भाजन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), the act of sharing,<BR>dividing; (in arithmetic) division; a vessel, cup, pot,<BR>dish, plate, (often found at the end of a comp., e. g.<BR>जल-भ्˚, पान-भ्˚); a particular measure = an<BR>Āḍhaka = 64 Palas; a vessel (metaphorically), a re-<BR>ceptacle for anything, repository, recipient, a place or<BR>person in which anything is collected or in whom<BR>any quality is conspicuous [cf. प्रीति-विश्रम्भ-भ्˚];<BR>a fit person in general, a deserving person, clever or<BR>capable person [cf. पात्र]; the act of representing<BR>or taking the place of, representation; (at the end<BR>of comps.) a representative, deputy, anything which<BR>serves for or is equivalent to (Ved.); भाजनेन, in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">Page0705-b+ 75</a>]<BR>place of, in lieu of, instead of; (अस्), m., N. of a man;<BR>the patronymic formed from this N., see Gaṇa Gopa-<BR>vanādi to Pāṇ. II. 4, 67; (अस्, आ, अम्), sharing, par-<BR>ticipating in, entitled to (at the end of comps.); relat-<BR>ing to, belonging to (at the end of comps., Ved.).<BR>—भाजन-ता, f. or भाजन-त्व, अम्, n. the state<BR>of being a vessel or receptacle for anything, the pos-<BR>sessing (of any quality &c.), the being a (fit) vessel,<BR>fitness, worthiness, the being worthy of or entitled<BR>to; a fit object.<BR>—भाजन-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved.<BR>a word used in Nirukta IV. 10, XI. 19, XII. 17,<BR>to explain the word भद्र.<BR>—भाजनी-भूत, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having become a vessel or receptacle for<BR>anything, i. e. having become a participator in or<BR>possessor of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजयु
भाजयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. communicating, sharing<BR>with others, generous, liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजित|भाजितं
भाजित, अस्, आ, अम्, shared, divided, distributed,<BR>apportioned, allotted, portioned; (अम्), n. a share,<BR>portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजिन्
भाजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of comps.) sharing,<BR>participating in; connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजी
भाजी, f. rice gruel (= श्राणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्य|भाज्यं
भाज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be divided, divisible, to be<BR>portioned or distributed; (अम्), n. a portion, share;<BR>an inheritance; (in arithmetic) the dividend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागल
भागल भागल, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Bhagala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागलक
भागलक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Bhagala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागलि
भागलि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Bhagala; N.<BR>of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागलेय
भागलेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhāgali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागीरथ
भागीरथ भागीरथ. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्कार|भांकार
भाङ्कार भाङ्-कार, perhaps = झङ्-कार,<BR>q. v.; [cf. भेरी-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्ग|भांग
भाङ्ग भाङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भङ्गा, hemp),<BR>hempen, of hemp, made or consisting of hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गक|भांगक|भांगकः|भाङ्गकः
भाङ्गक (fr. भङ्ग, a fracture), a tattered or<BR>ragged cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गासुरि
भाङ्गासुरि, इस्, m. (fr. भङ्गासुर), a patro-<BR>nymic of Ṛtu-parṇa.<BR>—भाङ्गासुरि-नृपाज्ञा (˚प-<BR>आज्˚), f. the command of king Bhāṅgāsuri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गीन|भांगीन|भांगीनं|भाङ्गीनं
भाङ्गीन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भङ्गा), bearing or<BR>growing hemp; (अम्), n., scil. क्षेत्र, a field of<BR>hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गिल
भाङ्गिल भाङ्गिल, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गिलेय
भाङ्गिलेय, अस्, m., N. of a man; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>coming from Bhāṅgila (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
भाज् भाज्, भाजन, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजक्
भाजक् भाजक्, ind. quickly, swiftly; (pro-<BR>bably incorrectly for ताजक्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाट|भाटं
भाट भाट (fr. rt. भट्), wages, hire, rent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटक|भाटकं|भाटकः
भाटक, अस्, m. price paid for anything, wages,<BR>hire, rent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटि|भाटिः
भाटि, इस्, f. wages, hire, fee; earnings of prosti-<BR>tutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाट्ट|भाट्टः
भाट्ट भाट्ट, अस्, m. a follower of Bhaṭṭa<BR>(i. e. Kumārila-bhaṭṭa); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—भाट्ट-चिन्ता-मणि, इस्, m., N. of a commentary<BR>by Viśveśvara-bhaṭṭa (better known as Gāgā-bhaṭṭa)<BR>on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtra.<BR>—भाट्ट-तन्त्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—भाट्ट-दिनकर, N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Bhaṭṭa Dinakara on the Mīmāṃsā work<BR>Śāstra-dīpikā.<BR>—भाट्ट-दीपिका, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary by Khaṇḍa-deva on Jaimini's Mīmāṃsā-sūtra.<BR>—भाट्टदीपिका-प्रभावली, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary on the preceding work by Śambhu-bhaṭṭa.<BR>—भाट्ट-भाषा-प्रकाशिका, f. ‘explanation of the<BR>language of the Bhāṭṭas,’ an index to the terminology<BR>of the Bhāṭṭas by Nārāyaṇa-tīrtha or Nārāyaṇa-<BR>muni.<BR>—भाट्ट-भास्कर, N. of a work by Jīva-<BR>deva, being a concise account of the various Mīmāṃsā<BR>schools and their doctrines; [cf. भाट्ट-दिनकर.]<BR>—भाट्ट-रहस्य, अम्, n. ‘the secret or mystic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">Page0705-c+ 77</a>]<BR>doctrine of the Bhāṭṭas,’ N. of an elementary Mī-<BR>māṃsā disquisition by Khaṇḍa-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाडितायन
भाडितायन भाडितायन, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Bhaḍita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाडिलायन
भाडिलायन भाडिलायन, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Bhaḍila, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्
भाण् भाण्, Ved. (onomatopoetic) imitation<BR>of the noise of breathing or hissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण|भाणः
भाण भाण, अस्, m. (fr. rt. भण्, q. v.), N.<BR>of a sort of dramatic entertainment (in which one<BR>only of the interlocutors appears on the scene, or<BR>described as a narrative of some intrigue told either<BR>by the hero or a third person).<BR>—भाण-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाणक|भाणकः
भाणक, अस्, m. a proclaimer, announcer, de-<BR>clarer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाणिका
भाणिका, f. a kind of dramatic performance; [cf.<BR>भाण above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्ड|भांड|भांडं|भाण्डं|भाण्डः
भाण्ड भाण्ड, अस्, m. (fr. rt. भण् or भण्ड्?),<BR>the plant Thespesia Populneoides; (ई), f. (perhaps) =<BR>भण्डी, Rubia Munjista [cf. काक-भ्˚, काल-भाण्-<BR>डिका]; (अम्), n. any vessel, pot, pan, cup, plate,<BR>dish, pail, vat, utensil [cf. पाक-भ्˚, पान-भ्˚];<BR>any chest, box, trunk, case [cf. क्षुर-भ्˚]; any<BR>implement, tool, instrument; any musical instrument<BR>(= वाद्य-भ्˚); a pack or bale (of goods or mer-<BR>chandise); horse-trappings, harness; an ornament in<BR>general; the stock (of a shopkeeper), goods, wares,<BR>merchandise, the capital or principal (of a merchant);<BR>the bed of a river, the space between its banks;<BR>mimicry, buffoonery, the practice of the Bhaṇḍa or<BR>professional jester; (आस्), m. pl. wares, merchandise.<BR>—भाण्ड-गोपक, अस्, m. the keeper of vessels or<BR>utensils (in a Buddhist temple).<BR>—भाण्ड-पति, इस्,<BR>m. a possessor of wares, a merchant.<BR>—भाण्ड-<BR>पुट, अस्, m. ‘sharpener of instruments, i. e. razors,’<BR>a barber.<BR>—भाण्ड-पुष्प, अस्, m. a sort of snake.<BR>—भाण्ड-प्रति-भाण्डक, अम्, n. ‘commodity<BR>for commodity,’ computation of the exchange of<BR>goods, barter (in arithmetic).<BR>—भाण्ड-भजक,<BR>अस्, m. the distributer of vessels or utensils (in a<BR>Buddhist temple).<BR>—भाण्ड-भरक, अस्, m. the<BR>contents of any vessel.<BR>—भाण्ड-मूल्य, अम्, n.<BR>capital consisting of wares.<BR>—भाण्ड-वादन, अम्,<BR>n. playing on a musical instrument.<BR>—भाण्ड-शाला,<BR>f. a store-house, store-room, magazine.<BR>—भाण्डा-<BR>गार (˚ड-आग्˚), अम्, n. a store-room, store-house, place<BR>where household goods and utensils are kept; a<BR>magazine, treasury; a treasure, store.<BR>—भाण्डागा-<BR>रिक, अस्, m. the overseer of a store-house, store-<BR>keeper, keeper of magazine; a steward, treasurer.<BR>—भाण्डानुसारिन् (˚ड-अन्˚), ई, इणी, इ, hanging to<BR>a pot or vessel.<BR>—भाण्डा-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city.<BR>—भाण्डोदर (˚ड-उद्˚), अम्, n. the cavity or<BR>interior of a vessel.<BR>—भाण्डोपपुराण (˚ड-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डक|भांडक|भांडकं|भांडकः|भाण्डकः
भाण्डक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a small vessel, cup,<BR>plate, utensil, box, chest; (इका), f. an implement,<BR>tool, utensil; = भाण्डी, see काल-भ्˚; (अम्), n.<BR>goods, merchandise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डायन
भाण्डायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डायनि
भाण्डायनि, इस्, m. a patronymic (probably)<BR>from Bhāṇḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डार|भांडार|भांडारं
भाण्डार = भाण्डागार (of which it is a corrupt<BR>or contracted form).<BR>—भाण्डार-गृह, अम्, n. a<BR>store-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डारिक|भांडारिक
भाण्डारिक, अस्, m. = भाण्डागारिक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डारिन्|भांडारिन्
भाण्डारिन्, ई, m. the keeper of a store-house,<BR>steward, treasurer (= भाण्डागारिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डी
भाण्डी, a razor-case; [cf. भाण्डि-वाह, भाण्-<BR>डिल, and क्षुर-भाण्ड.]<BR>—भाण्डि-वाह, अस्, m.<BR>a barber.<BR>—भाण्डि-शाला, f. (probably) a barber's<BR>shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिक|भांडिक|भांडिकः|भाण्डिकः
भाण्डिक, अस्, m. a barber; [cf. भाण्डिल,<BR>भाण्डि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिजङ्घि
भाण्डिजङ्घि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Bhaṇḍi-<BR>jaṅgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0705-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डित
भाण्डित, आस्, m. pl. of भाण्डित्य below, see<BR>Gaṇa Kaṇvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डितायन
भाण्डितायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhaṇ-<BR>ḍita; [cf. भाडितायन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डित्य
भाण्डित्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhaṇḍita;<BR>[cf. भाण्डित.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिनी|भांडिनी
भाण्डिनी, f. (fr. भाण्ड), a chest, a basket (=<BR>मञ्जूषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिल|भांडिल|भांडिलः|भाण्डिलः
भाण्डिल, अस्, m. a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिलायन
भाण्डिलायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhaṇ-<BR>ḍila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डीर|भांडीर|भांडीरः|भाण्डीरः
भाण्डीर, अस्, m., N. of a lofty Nyag-rodha tree<BR>on the Govardhana in Vṛndā-vana; = वट, the<BR>Indian fig-tree [cf. भण्डीर]; N. of a Dānava.<BR>—भाण्डीर-वन, अम्, n., N. of a forest.<BR>—भाण्-<BR>डीरवन-वासिन्, ई, m. ‘dwelling in the Bhāṇḍīra<BR>forest,’ N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाति|भातिः
भाति भाति, भातु. See p. 704, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भादिग
भादिग भादिग, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्र|भाद्रः
भाद्र भाद्र, अस्, m. (fr. भद्र), the month<BR>Bhādra, = भाद्रपद below; (ई), f., scil. तिथि,<BR>the day of full moon in the month Bhādra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रदारव
भाद्रदारव, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Bhadra-dāru, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रपद|भाद्रपदः
भाद्रपद, अस्, m. (fr. भद्र-पदा), the<BR>month Bhādra (a rainy month corresponding to a<BR>period in our calendar from about the middle of<BR>August to the middle of September); (आ), f. (also ए,<BR>du., आस्, pl.), = भद्र-पदा, a name common to<BR>the third and fourth lunar asterisms or Nakṣatras<BR>[cf. नक्षत्र]; (ई), f. the day of full moon in the<BR>month Bhādrapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रमातुर|भाद्रमातुरः
भाद्रमातुर, अस्, m. (fr. भद्र-मातृ), the<BR>son of a virtuous or handsome mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रमौञ्ज
भाद्रमौञ्ज, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. made from<BR>Bhadra (a kind of Cyperus grass) and Muñja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रवर्मण
भाद्रवर्मण, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Bhadra-varman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रशर्मि
भाद्रशर्मि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Bhadra-<BR>śarman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रसाम
भाद्रसाम, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhadra-<BR>sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भान|भानं
भान भान, भानु, &c. See p. 704, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भान्त
भान्त भान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. perhaps a<BR>participle of rt. भाम् below; (according to Mahī-<BR>dhara) = वज्र-रूप, having the shape of a thunder-<BR>bolt, or = चन्द्र, the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भान्द
भान्द भान्-द, अम्, n., N. of an Upa-<BR>Purāṇa (see under 2. भा, p. 704, col. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम्
भाम् भाम्, cl. 1. A. भामते, बभामे,<BR>&c., or (by Dhātu-pāṭha XXXV. 20) cl.<BR>10. P. भामयति, &c., Ved. to be angry or wrath-<BR>ful; to be impatient: Intens. बाभाम्यते, to be<BR>very angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
2. भाम, अस्, m. (for 1. see p. 704, col. 2; for<BR>3. see below), passion, wrath, fury, anger; (आ), f. a<BR>passionate woman; = सत्य-भामा, one of the<BR>wives of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामित
भामित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. enraged, angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिन्
2. भामिन्, ई, इनी, इ (for 1. see p. 704, col. 2),<BR>passionate, angry; (इनी), f. an angry or passionate<BR>woman, vixen, (often used as a term of endearment,<BR>in the same sense as मानिनी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
भाम 3. भाम or भामक, अस्, m. a sister's<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामह|भामहः
भामह भामह, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Mano-ramā commentary and of a treatise on<BR>the art of rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भायजात्य
भायजात्य भायजात्य, अस्, m. (fr. भय-<BR>जात), a patronymic of Kapi-vana; of Nikothaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार|भारः
भार भार, अस्, m. (fr. rt. भृ), a burden,<BR>load, weight, gravity [cf. अति-भ्˚, अंस-भ्˚]; heavy<BR>work, labour, toil, trouble; a large quantity, mass,<BR>bulk, (often connected with words meaning ‘hair,’<BR>e. g. जटा-भार-धर, wearing a great quantity of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">Page0706-b+ 79</a>]<BR>matted hair); a particular weight = 20 Tulās = 2000<BR>Palas of gold; a pole or yoke for carrying burdens<BR>[cf. उदक-भ्˚]; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—भार-<BR>जीविन्, ई, m. one who earns his livelihood by carrying<BR>loads.<BR>—भार-भारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. bearing or<BR>carrying a load or weight.<BR>—भार-भूति-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—भार-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>= भार-भारिन्.<BR>—भार-यष्टि, इस्, f. a pole or<BR>yoke (generally laid over the shoulder) for carry-<BR>ing burdens.<BR>—भार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a<BR>weight or load, loaded, burdened, bearing a burden.<BR>—भारवत्-त्व, अम्, n. the state of carrying a<BR>load, weightiness, ponderousness.<BR>—भार-वाह्, वाट्,<BR>भारौही, वाट्, bearing a burden, carrying a load.<BR>—भार-वाह, अस्, m. a bearer of burdens, porter,<BR>carrier; (ई), f. indigo.<BR>—भार-वाहन, अस्, m. a<BR>burden-bearer, beast of burden, pack-bearer; (अम्),<BR>n. a vehicle for loads, a cart, waggon.<BR>—भार-<BR>वाहिक, अस्, ई, अम्, load-bearing, carrying burdens;<BR>(अस्), m. a load-bearer, porter.<BR>—भार-वाहिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, load-bearing, carrying a burden; (ई), m. a<BR>burden-bearer, porter.<BR>—भार-वृक्ष, अस्, m. a<BR>fragrant substance commonly called Kākṣī (con-<BR>sidered variously as a vegetable or a mineral product).<BR>—भार-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, burden-bearing, able to<BR>carry a great weight, very strong or powerful.<BR>—भा-<BR>र-साधन, अस्, ई, अम्, or भार-साहिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>accomplishing difficult feats (said of certain weapons),<BR>effecting great objects.<BR>—भार-हर, अस्, आ, अम्, or<BR>भार-हार, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, load-bearing, carrying<BR>a weight, bearing burdens; (अस्), m. a burden-bearer,<BR>porter.<BR>—भार-हारिक, अस्, ई, अम्, burden-bearing,<BR>carrying a load; relating or referring to the carrying<BR>of loads.<BR>—भार-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, load-bearing,<BR>carrying weights; (ई), m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भाराक्रान्त (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, oppressed<BR>by a burden, overburdened, heavily laden, bearing a<BR>heavy burden; (आ), f. a species of the Atyaṣṭi<BR>metre, four times — — — —, ∪ ∪ ∪ ∪ ∪ —, ∪ — ∪ ∪ — ∪ —;<BR>[cf. मन्दाक्रान्ता.]<BR>—भारावतरण or भारा-<BR>वतारण (˚र-अव्˚), अम्, n. the taking down or<BR>removal of a burden, taking away a burden.<BR>—भा-<BR>रोढि (˚र-ऊढि), इस्, f. the bearing of a burden.<BR>—भारोद्धरण (˚र-उद्˚), अम्, n. the act of<BR>raising up or lifting a burden.<BR>—भारोद्वह (˚र-<BR>उद्˚), अस्, m. a burden-carrier, porter.<BR>—भारोपजी-<BR>वन (˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n. living by burdens, earning<BR>a livelihood by carrying weights.<BR>—भारौही, f.,<BR>see भार-वाह् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारक|भारकः
भारक, अम्, n. a load, burden, weight, a par-<BR>ticular weight; (अस्, इका, अम्), loaded with, (at the<BR>end of comps.; cf. फणि-भारिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाराय
भाराय, Nom. A. भारायते, &c., to become a<BR>burden, form a load; to be like a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिक|भारिकः
भारिक, अस्, आ, अम्, forming a load, heavy;<BR>swollen (said of a particular kind of elephantiasis);<BR>(अस्), m. a burden-bearer, porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिन्
भारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, bearing a load, carrying a<BR>burden, a bearer, porter [cf. भार-भ्˚]; having<BR>weight, heavy, ponderous.<BR>—भारि-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>heaviness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारङ्गी|भारंगी
भारङ्गी भारङ्गी, f., see Gaṇa Kāśyādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारङ्गिक
भारङ्गिक, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, an adj. from the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारण्ड|भारंड|भारंडः|भारण्डः
भारण्ड भारण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a fabulous<BR>bird, (also written भारुण्ड, भेरण्ड, भेरुण्ड);<BR>(ई), f. the female of the above bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारत|भारतं|भारतः
भारत भारत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भरत), de-<BR>scended from Bharata; belonging or relating to the<BR>Bharatas; (with सङ्ग्राम, समिति, युद्ध, स-<BR>मर) the war or battle of the Bharatas; (with<BR>कथा, आख्यान, इतिहास) the story of the Bharatas,<BR>the history or narrative of their war, (in this sense<BR>also भारतम्, n.); (with वर्ष) India (so called<BR>from its king Bharata, son of Dushyanta; in this<BR>sense also भारतम्, n.); an inhabitant of India or<BR>Bhārata-varṣa; भारतं सरस्, N. of a lake;<BR>(अस्), m. a descendant of Bharata; N. of Agni or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">Page0706-c+ 76</a>]<BR>Fire (so called, according to Sāy., either ‘as sprung<BR>from the priests called Bharatas,’ or ‘as bearer of the<BR>oblation’); an actor, a mime [cf. भरत]; N. of<BR>Deva-śravas; of Deva-rāta; an epithet of the sun<BR>shining on the south of Meru; (ई), f., N. of a Vedic<BR>goddess (invoked among the Ā-prī deities together<BR>with Ilā and Sarasvatī [cf. आ-प्री] or sometimes with<BR>Hotrā and Varūtrī; according to Yāska, Nirukta<BR>VIII. 13, she is a daughter of Āditya); the goddess<BR>of speech, Sarasvatī; speech, voice, word, eloquence,<BR>literary composition, the dramatic art, dramatic reci-<BR>tation or declamation; (with वृत्ति) a particular kind<BR>of style; a quail; N. of a river; (ई), m., N. of a<BR>teacher (‘personified speech’); अश्व-मेध भा-<BR>रत, N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda V. 27.<BR>—भारत-तात्पर्य-निर्णय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—भारत-भाव-दीप, अस्, m. ‘light of the<BR>meaning of the Bhārata,’ N. of Nīla-kaṇṭha's com-<BR>mentary on the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—भारत-सङ्ग्र-<BR>ह-दीपिका, f. = भारतार्थ-दीपिका, q. v.<BR>—भा-<BR>रत-सत्तम, अस्, m. the best of the descendants<BR>of Bharata.<BR>—भारताचार्य (˚त-आच्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a preceptor; of Arjuna-miśra (a commentator on<BR>the Mahā-bhārata).<BR>—भारतार्थ-दीपिका (˚त-<BR>अर्˚), f. ‘light of the meaning of the Bhārata,’ N. of<BR>a commentary by Arjuna-miśra on the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—भारतार्थ-प्रकाश, अस्, m. ‘light of the<BR>meaning of the Bhārata,’ N. of Nārāyaṇa's commen-<BR>tary on the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—भारती-कवि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a poet mentioned in the Śārṅgadhara-paddhati.<BR>—भारती-कृष्णाचार्य (˚ण-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a preceptor.<BR>—भारती-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—भारती-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred<BR>bathing-place; (अस्), m., N. of the author of the<BR>philosophical treatise Pañca-daśī, (he was preceptor<BR>of Mādhavācārya.)<BR>—भारती-यति, इस्, m., N. of<BR>the author of the Tattva-kaumudī-vyākhyā.<BR>—भा-<BR>रती-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. accompanied by Bhāratī;<BR>(आन्), m. an epithet of Indra.<BR>—भारती-श्री-नृ-<BR>सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतेय
भारतेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhārata<BR>(or from Bharata).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाज|भारद्वाजं|भारद्वाजः
भारद्वाज भारद्वाज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भरद्-<BR>वाज), coming from or relating to Bharad-vāja; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Śūṣa Vāhneya; of Śaunahotra; of Satya-<BR>vāha; of Sukeśan; of Śauṅga; of Droṇa (who was<BR>son of Bharad-vāja and preceptor of the Kurus and<BR>Pāṇḍus); of one of the seven Ṛṣis; of a son of<BR>Bṛhas-pati; of the Muni Agastya; of a grammarian;<BR>the planet Mars (according to the Graha-yajña-tattva);<BR>a skylark [cf. भरद्-वाज]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people [cf. भरद्-वाज]; (ई), f. a particular species<BR>of bird; the wild cotton shrub; N. of a river; (अम्),<BR>n. a bone; N. of a country; (a various reading for<BR>भरद्-वाज.)<BR>—भारद्वाजी-पुत्र, अस्, m., Ved.,<BR>N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजक
भारद्वाजक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or relating<BR>to Bharad-vāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजायन
भारद्वाजायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Bharad-vāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजिन्
भारद्वाजिन्, इनस्, m. pl. (fr. भरद्-वाज or<BR>भारद्वाज), N. of a school; [cf. भरद्-वाजिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजीय
भारद्वाजीय, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or relat-<BR>ing to Bhāradvāja; (आस्), m. pl., N. of the school of<BR>the grammarian Bhāradvāja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारमेय
भारमेय भारमेय, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Bharama, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारय|भारयः
भारय भारय, अस्, m. = भारद्वाज, a sky-<BR>lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारव|भारवं
भारव भारव, अम्, n. a bow-string; (ई),<BR>f. sacred basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवि|भारविः
भारवि भारवि, इस्, m., N. of the author of<BR>the poem called Kirātārjunīya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाराय
भाराय भाराय. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारि|भारिः
भारि भारि, इस्, m. a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिक|भारिकः
भारिक भारिक, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0706-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारुजिक
भारुजिक भारुजिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भरुज),<BR>relating to or coming from a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारुण्ड
भारुण्ड भारुण्ड, अस्, m. = भारण्ड, q. v.;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of a Sāman; of a wood mentioned<BR>in Rāmāyaṇa II. 71, 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्ग|भार्गः
भार्ग भार्ग, अस्, m. a king of the Bhargas;<BR>N. of a son of Pratardana; of a king also called<BR>Bharga; (ई), f. a queen of the Bhargas; the plant<BR>Clerodendrum Siphonanthus.<BR>—भार्ग-भुमि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of a king; [cf. भर्ग-भूमि and भृगु-<BR>भूमि.]<BR>—भार्ग-वन, अम्, n., N. of a forest;<BR>(a various reading has भानु-वन.)<BR>—भार्ग-<BR>श्री-कान्त-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गायण
भार्गायण, अस्, m. (fr. भर्ग), Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic of Sutvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गि
भार्गि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Bharga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गलेश्वरतीर्थ
भार्गलेश्वरतीर्थ भार्गलेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚ल-<BR>ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गव|भार्गवः
भार्गव भार्गव, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or<BR>coming from Bhṛgu, belonging to Bhṛgu; (अस्), m.<BR>epithet of Cyavana [cf. चण्ड-भ्˚]; of Gṛtsa-mada;<BR>of Dvi-gat; of Dṛśāna; of Iṭala; of Mārkaṇḍeya;<BR>of Śaunaka; of Ṛcīka; of Jamad-agni; of Paraśu-<BR>rāma; of Pramati; of Śiva; the planet Venus (pro-<BR>perly a patronymic of Śukra, regent of the planet<BR>Venus and preceptor of the Daityas); an archer, a<BR>good archer (= धन्विन्, सु-धन्वन्); an ele-<BR>phant; (आस्), m. pl. ‘the descendants of Bhṛgu,’<BR>commonly called Bhṛgavas, N. of a particular tribe;<BR>(ई), f. a female descendant of Bhṛgu; N. of Deva-<BR>yāni; an epithet of Lakṣmī; an epithet of Pārvatī;<BR>= दूर्वा, bent grass, Panicum Dactylon; = नील-<BR>दूर्वा; = श्वेत-दूर्वा.<BR>—भार्गव-दीपिका, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—भार्गव-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘dear to<BR>Śukra or to the planet Venus,’ a diamond.<BR>—भार्ग-<BR>वार्चन-दीपिका (˚व-अर्˚), f., N. of a work; [cf.<BR>भार्गव-दीपिका.]<BR>—भार्गवालाप (˚व-आल्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of the third Act of the Abhirāma-maṇi-nāṭaka.<BR>—भार्गवोपपुराण (˚व-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—भार्गवोपाख्यान (˚व-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of the thirteenth chapter of the Vāsiṣṭha-<BR>rāmāyaṇa, commonly called Yoga-vāsiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवीय
भार्गवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Bhārgava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्द्वाजी
भार्द्वाजी भार्द्वाजी, f. = भारद्वाजी, the<BR>wild cotton shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्मन्
भार्मन् भार्मन् (fr. rt. भृ), Ved. bring-<BR>ing, waiting upon, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्म्य
भार्म्य भार्म्य, अस्, m. a patronymic of<BR>Mudgala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्म्यश्व
भार्म्यश्व, अस्, m. (fr. भृम्यश्व), a patro-<BR>nymic of Mugdala; [cf. भर्म्याश्व.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य|भार्यः|भार्य्य
भार्य भार्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. भृ), to be<BR>borne, to be supported, to be cherished or nourished;<BR>to be maintained, dependent for a livelihood on<BR>another; (अस्), m. a servant, dependent, mercenary;<BR>(आ), f. a wife (espoused according to the ritual of the<BR>Vedas), any wife; the female of an animal.<BR>—भार्-<BR>याट (˚या-आट), अस्, आ, अम्, living by the prostitution<BR>of a wife; [cf. पत्न्य्-आट.]<BR>—भार्याटिक, अस्, m.<BR>a husband under the rule of his wife, a hen-pecked<BR>husband; a species of antelope (= हरिणान्तर);<BR>N. of a Muni.<BR>—भार्या-त्व, अम्, n. wifehood,<BR>the state of being a wife, the condition of a wife.<BR>—भार्याधिकारिक (˚या-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, relat-<BR>ing to the chapter on wives.<BR>—भार्या-पति-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. the being man and wife, conjugal union.<BR>—भार्या-पती, m. du. husband and wife.<BR>—भार्-<BR>यार्थिन् (˚या-अर्˚), ई, m. seeking or desiring a wife.<BR>—भार्या-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a wife.<BR>—भार्-<BR>या-वृक्ष, अस्, m. the tree Cæsalpina Sappan (=<BR>पत्तङ्ग).<BR>—भार्योढ (˚या-ऊढ), अस्, m. =<BR>ऊढ-भार्य, married (said of a man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यक
भार्यक = भार्या, a wife, (at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. स-भ्˚, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यारु|भार्यारुः|भार्य्यारु|भार्य्यारुः
भार्यारु, उस्, m. (fr. भार्या), the father of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">Page0707-b+ 74</a>]<BR>child by another man's wife; a kind of deer or<BR>antelope; N. of a mountain.<BR>भार्वर भार्वर, अस्, m., Ved. (according to<BR>Sāy., Ṛg-veda IV. 21, 7), a N. of Indra as son of<BR>Bharvara, = Jagad-bhartṛ, Prajā-pati, (perhaps to be<BR>referred to the horses of Indra as ‘bearing,’ ‘carry-<BR>ing,’ fr. rt. भृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्श्य|भार्श्यं
भार्श्य भार्श्य, अम्, n. (fr. भृश), vehe-<BR>mence, violence; excessiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल|भालं
भाल भाल, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. 1.<BR>भा; according to some also भालस्, m.), the fore-<BR>head, brow; light, lustre.<BR>—भाल-कृत्, त्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—भाल-चन्द्र, अस्, m. ‘having the<BR>moon on his forehead,’ an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—भा-<BR>लचन्द्राचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—भाल-दर्शन, अम्, n. red lead (‘appearing on<BR>the forehead,’ being used to stain the forehead with<BR>lines &c.).<BR>—भाल-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, watching<BR>the brow or countenance (said of a servant who is<BR>attentive to a master's wishes).<BR>—भाल-दृश्, क्, or<BR>भाल-लोचन, अस्, m. ‘having an eye in the fore-<BR>head,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भालाङ्क (˚ल-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having (auspicious) marks on the fore-<BR>head; (अस्), m. a man born with lucky lines on his<BR>forehead; a sort of fish (known as the Rohi, Cypri-<BR>nus Rohita); a tortoise; an epithet of Śiva; a saw;<BR>a species of leguminous plant or pot-herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालु|भालुः
भालु, उस्, m. the sun; [cf. भानु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालन्दन
भालन्दन भालन्दन, अस्, m., Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic from Bhalandana, N. of Vatsa-prī; (also read<BR>बालन्दन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालन्दनक
भालन्दनक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Bhalandana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालु|भालुः
भालु भालु. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालुक|भालुकः
भालुक भालुक, अस्, m. a bear; [cf. भल्ल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालूक|भालूकः
भालूक, अस्, m. = भालुक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालुकि
भालुकि भालुकि, इस्, m. (probably a patro-<BR>nymic), N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालुकिन्
भालुकिन्, ई, m., N. of a preceptor (= वालुकिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालुकीपुत्र
भालुकी-पुत्र, अस्, m. (fr. भालुकी, f.), Ved.<BR>‘the son of Bhālukī,’ N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्ल
भाल्ल भाल्ल, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or com-<BR>ing from Bhalla, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लवि|भाल्लविः
भाल्लवि भाल्लवि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Bhallavi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लविन्
भाल्लविन्, इनस्, m. pl. the pupils of Bhallavin (?).<BR>—भाल्लवि-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n. and भाल्लवि-<BR>शाखा, f. and भाल्लवि-श्रुति, इस्, f. and भाल्लव्य्-<BR>उपनिषद्, त्, f., N. of certain Vedic works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लवेय
भाल्लवेय, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from<BR>Bhāllavi, of Indra-dyumna; N. of a preceptor.<BR>—भाल्लवेय-श्रुति, इस्, f., N. of a Vedic work.<BR>—भाल्लवेयोपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚), त्, f., N. of an<BR>Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लुक|भाल्लुकः
भाल्लुक भाल्लुक or भाल्लूक, अस्, m. a bear;<BR>[cf. भल्ल, भल्लुक, भल्लूक, भालुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लेय
भाल्लेय भाल्लेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or<BR>coming from Bhalla, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव|भावः
भाव भाव, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. भू), becom-<BR>ing, being, existing, existence, taking place, occurring,<BR>appearing, appearance; state of being, condition of<BR>existence, state, condition, relationship; manner,<BR>mode; true condition or state, truth, (भावेन, in<BR>truth, really, truly); manner of being, nature, natural<BR>state, innate property, temperament, disposition,<BR>temper, (एको भावः, a simple or artless nature);<BR>any state of mind or body, affection, sentiment, feel-<BR>ing, emotion, passion, (in the dramatic system of the<BR>Hindūs, two kinds of Bhāvas are usually enumerated,<BR>see स्थायिन्, व्यभि-चारिन्; but other divisions are<BR>also given, see अनु-भाव, वि-भाव, सात्त्विक-<BR>भाव); feeling of love, inclination, attachment,<BR>(भावं तेषु चक्रे, he felt an affection for them;<BR>सा तस्मिन् भावम् बबन्ध, she fixed her affec-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-c" target="_blank">Page0707-c+ 81</a>]<BR>tions on him); inclination or disposition of mind,<BR>(यादृशेन भावेन, with whatever disposition or<BR>condition of mind); sentiment, idea, thought, opinion,<BR>supposition, conjecture; resolution, intention, pur-<BR>pose, (दृढो भावः, a firm resolution); purport,<BR>tenor, scope, drift; meaning, sense, (इति भावः,<BR>‘such is the sense,’ constantly used by Indian com-<BR>mentators at the end of their interpretations); con-<BR>templation, reflection, abstract meditation; the seat<BR>of the feelings and affections, the heart, soul, mind,<BR>(परितुष्टेन भावेन, with a pleased mind, Manu<BR>IV. 227; यदा मन्येत भावेन, when he believes<BR>in his mind, Manu VII. 171; but according to<BR>Kullūka, भावेन here = तत्त्व-तस्, truly); that<BR>which is or exists, a being, living creature, thing,<BR>matter, object, substance, (सर्व-भावेषु निःस्पृ-<BR>हः, one who is free from attachment to all [earthly]<BR>objects); behaviour, conduct, act, action, movement,<BR>gesture; amorous gesture, corporeal expression of<BR>amorous sentiments, wanton sport, dalliance (= लीला);<BR>passing from one state to another, change or substi-<BR>tution of one nature for another, (दन्त्यानाम् मूर्-<BR>धन्य-भावः, the change of dentals to cerebrals;<BR>भो-भावः, the existence or substitution [for the<BR>name of a person] of the expression भोस्, Manu II.<BR>124); birth; the place of birth, the womb (=<BR>योनि); the place of being, the world, universe; an<BR>organ of sense; superhuman power; the Supreme<BR>Being; advice, instruction: (in theatrical language)<BR>a learned or worthy man, a man of dignity or conse-<BR>quence, gentleman, master, honourable sir [cf. भाव-<BR>मिश्र, 2. भवत्]: (in astronomy) the state or<BR>condition of a planet; an astrological house, mansion,<BR>lunar mansion; N. of the twenty-seventh Kalpa; of<BR>the eighth (forty-second) year in Jupiter's cycle of<BR>sixty years; (in Pāṇini's grammatical system) a term<BR>for an impersonal passive or neuter verb having<BR>neither agent nor object expressed (e. g. पच्यते,<BR>there is cooking, i. e. cooking is going on); the<BR>abstract idea conveyed by a word, the sense of the<BR>abstract noun (as describing the state or condition of<BR>anything; sometimes used at the end of a comp.<BR>instead of the affixes ता, त्व, य, e. g. बाल-भाव<BR>= बाल-ता, &c., the state of a child, childhood; and<BR>even added pleonastically to the abstract noun itself,<BR>e. g. तनुता-भाव, the state of thinness); the sense<BR>of a noun of action (as expressing the idea of the<BR>root, e. g. going, doing, &c.): = मिश्र-भाव, N. of<BR>the author of the Bhāva-prakāśa.<BR>—भाव-कल्प-<BR>लता, f., N. of a commentary by Bhaṭṭa-mudgala on<BR>the Bhāvanā-viveka, q. v.<BR>—भाव-गम्भीरम्, ind.<BR>from the bottom of the heart, (भाव-गम्भीरं<BR>जहसुः, they laughed heartily); deeply; gravely.<BR>—भाव-गम्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be ascertained by<BR>reflection or by meditating in the heart.<BR>—भाव-<BR>ग्राहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, apprehending the sense, appre-<BR>ciating the sentiment.<BR>—भाव-चूडा-मणि, इस्, m.,<BR>N. of a work.<BR>—भाव-ज, अस्, m. ‘produced in<BR>the heart,’ love; the god of love; [cf. मनो-ज.]<BR>—भाव-ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing the heart.<BR>—भाव-तस्, ind. through being, in consequence<BR>of being, (ज्ञाति-भावतस्, through being a relation.)<BR>—भाव-त्व, अम्, n. the state of Bhāva, q. v.<BR>—भाव-दीप, अस्, m., N. of a commentary on<BR>the Tattva-prakāśa; = भारत-भावदीप.<BR>—भा-<BR>व-दीपिका, f., N. of a commentary.<BR>—भाव-नारा-<BR>यण-माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—भाव-<BR>पदार्थ, अस्, m. a thing which has a real or posi-<BR>tive existence.<BR>—भाव-पाद, अस्, m., N. of a lexi-<BR>cographer.<BR>—भाव-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a medical<BR>work by Bhava-deva-miśra.<BR>—भाव-प्रकाशिका, f.,<BR>N. of a grammatical commentary.<BR>—भाव-प्र-<BR>त्यय-वादार्थ (˚द-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work<BR>by Mathurā-nātha Tarka-vāg-īśa Bhaṭṭācārya.<BR>—भा-<BR>व-प्रदीपिका, f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>Mālatī-mādhava.<BR>—भाव-बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘heart-enchaining,’ fettering the heart, joining hearts<BR>(as love).<BR>—भाव-बोधक, अस्, इका, अम्, revealing<BR>or displaying any sentiment, indicating a feeling or<BR>passion.<BR>—भाव-मिश्र, अस्, m. (in dramatic lan-<BR>guage) a gentleman, a man of dignity or consequence,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-a" target="_blank">Page0708-a+ 81</a>]<BR>master, sir; N. of the author of the Bhāva-prakāśa,<BR>(also called Miśra-bhāva and Bhāva-deva-miśra.)<BR>—भाव-राम-कृष्ण, अस्, m., N. of a man men-<BR>tioned in the second part of the Prabodha-candrodaya.<BR>—भाव-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘consisting of reality,’<BR>actually being, really existing, real, actual; (अम्),<BR>n. (?), N. of a work.<BR>—भाव-वचन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(in gram.) signifying a state or action, denoting the<BR>abstract notion of a verb.<BR>—भाव-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>being in a state or condition.<BR>—भाव-वाचक (?),<BR>an abstract noun.<BR>—भाव-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Buddhist teacher.<BR>—भाव-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, relat-<BR>ing to creation, concerned with cosmogony; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of Brahmā.<BR>—भाववृत्तीय, अस्, आ, अम्, an<BR>adj. formed from भाव-वृत्त.<BR>—भाव-शतक,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—भाव-शबल-ता, f. or<BR>भाव-शबला, f. mixture or union of various emo-<BR>tions.<BR>—भाव-शान्ति, इस्, f. the allaying of any<BR>(transitory) emotion.<BR>—भाव-शुद्धि, इस्, f. purity<BR>of mind.<BR>—भाव-शून्य, अस्, आ, अम्, void of affec-<BR>tion or attachment.<BR>—भाव-संशुद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>purification of the natural condition, purity of nature.<BR>—भाव-सन्धि, इस्, m. union of emotions or feel-<BR>ings, co-existence of two emotions, a vacillating frame<BR>of mind between conflicting emotions and feelings.<BR>—भाव-समाहित, अस्, आ, अम्, fixed or collected<BR>in mind, abstracted, devout.<BR>—भाव-सर्ग, अस्, m.<BR>the intellectual creation (comprising the faculties of<BR>the human mind and their affections, as distinguished<BR>from the material creation, see भौतिक).<BR>—भाव-<BR>सार-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a work by Gaṅgā-dhara<BR>Mahāḍakara.<BR>—भाव-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in a<BR>state of love or affection, attached, enamoured.<BR>—भाव-स्निग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, attached in heart or<BR>mind, affectionately disposed.<BR>—भावाकूत (˚व-<BR>आक्˚), अम्, n. the thoughts of the heart or mind.<BR>—भावा-गणेश-दीक्षित, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of several commentaries.<BR>—भावात्मक (˚व-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘consisting of reality,’ real, actual; [cf.<BR>भाव-रूप.]<BR>—भावात्मक-ता, f. reality.<BR>—भा-<BR>वाद्वैत (˚व-अद्˚), अम्, n. natural cause; material<BR>cause (as thread of cloth).<BR>—भावानन्दी (˚व-आन्˚),<BR>f., N. of a commentary by Bhāvānanda Siddhānta-<BR>vāg-īśa on the Dīdhiti or Śiro-maṇi.<BR>—भावाननदी-<BR>प्रकाश, अस्, m., N. of a commentary on the pre-<BR>ceding by Mahā-deva Pandit.<BR>—भावानुग (˚व-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘following the object,’ natural,<BR>simple, not forced or assumed; (आ), f. a shadow;<BR>[cf. भावालीना.]<BR>—भावान्तर (˚व-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>another state, a different state or condition.<BR>—भा-<BR>वाभास (˚व-आभ्˚), अस्, m. simulation of feeling or<BR>emotion.<BR>—भावार्थ (˚व-अर्˚), अस्, m. the simple<BR>or inherent meaning (of words), the obvious purport<BR>(of a phrase &c.), subject-matter.<BR>—भावार्थ-दी-<BR>पिका, f. ‘light of the inherent meaning,’ N. of a<BR>metrical commentary by Gaurī-kānta Sārvabhauma<BR>Bhaṭṭācārya on the Tarka-bhāṣā; on the Vṛtta-<BR>ratnā-kara by Janārdana-vibudha; = भागवत-भ्˚,<BR>q. v.<BR>—भावालीना (˚व-आल्˚), f. ‘cleaving to an<BR>object,’ a shadow; [cf. भावानुगा.]<BR>—भावोदय<BR>(˚व-उद्˚), अस्, m. the rising of emotion or passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावक|भावकः
भावक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>be, effecting; promoting any one's welfare; imagin-<BR>ing, fancying; having a taste for the beautiful; having<BR>a poetical taste; (अस्), m. sentiment, feeling, affec-<BR>tion, emotion; the external expression of amatory<BR>sentiments; [cf. भावाट, col. 2.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावन|भावनं|भावनः
2. भावन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.; for 1. भा-<BR>वन see p. 704, col. 1), causing to be, causing,<BR>forming, creating, framing, manifesting; promoting<BR>or effecting any one's welfare; imagining, fancying;<BR>teaching; (अस्), m. a creator, producer, efficient<BR>cause; N. of Śiva (= ध्यातृ); N. of the twenty-<BR>second Kalpa; (आ, अम्), f. n. the act of causing to<BR>be or creating, manifesting, manifestation; promotion<BR>of any one's interests (= वर्धन); the act of form-<BR>ing in the mind, conceiving, imagination, conception,<BR>fancy, thought, (भावनया, in thought, in imagina-<BR>tion); reflection, meditation, abstract meditation, con-<BR>templation; supposition, hypothesis, mental perception,<BR>recollection; observing, investigating; settling, fixing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">Page0708-b+ 81</a>]<BR>determining; (in law) proof, demonstration, argu-<BR>ment, ascertainment; (in medicine) saturating any<BR>dry powder with fluid, steeping, infusion, drying an<BR>article by day and keeping it moist at night; (in<BR>arithmetic) finding by combination or composition [cf.<BR>समास-भ्˚]; decorating with flowers and perfumes,<BR>scenting, anointing; (at the end of an adj. comp.) =<BR>nature, essence; (आ), f., N. of an Upaniṣad; a crow<BR>(= का-रव); water, = अम्बु; (अम्), n. apprehen-<BR>sion, perception; the fruit of the Dillenia Speciosa<BR>(= भव्य, भविष्य); N. of a wood, (perhaps<BR>for 1. भा-वन, q. v.)<BR>—भावना-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, produced by imagination or fancy, imaginary.<BR>—भावना-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thoughtful, full of<BR>anxiety, anxious.<BR>—भावना-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a commentary on a metrical treatise on the nature<BR>of injunction according to the theory of Madhu.<BR>—भावनाश्रय (˚न-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘the refuge of<BR>thought,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भावना-सार-सङ्-<BR>ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a Vedānta work by Mudgala<BR>Bhaṭṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनिका
भावनिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनीय
भावनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the Caus.) to be<BR>manifested, to be effected or accomplished; to be<BR>conceived or imagined, to be fancied; to be medi-<BR>tated on; to be proved, requiring demonstration; to<BR>be taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयत्
भावयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, fancying, imagining,<BR>calling to mind; reflecting on, meditating on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयव्य
भावयव्य, अस्, m. (fr. भावयु), Ved., N.<BR>of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda I. 126, 6; a<BR>patronymic of Svana-ja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयितव्य
भावयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), Ved.<BR>to be cherished, to be protected or taken care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयितृ
भावयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. causing to be; pro-<BR>moting the welfare (of any one), cherishing, taking<BR>care of, protecting; a cherisher, protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयु
भावयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. cherishing, taking care<BR>of, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाट|भावाटः
भावाट, अस्, m. = भावक, affection, emotion,<BR>passion; the external expression or indication of<BR>amatory feeling; a pious or holy man; an amorous<BR>man; an actor; dress, decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविक|भाविकः
भाविक, अस्, ई, अम्, actually being or existing,<BR>real, natural, innate; full of feeling or sentiment,<BR>expressive, sentimental; future; (अम्), n. a descrip-<BR>tion of an imaginary object so vivid that it actually<BR>appears to be present, describing the past or future<BR>as present; = भावुक, language full of feeling or<BR>passion; (अस्), m. an equation involving products of<BR>unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित|भावितः
भावित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), caused to be,<BR>brought into being, produced, obtained, got; made<BR>to thrive, protected, cherished, fostered; made to<BR>become, transformed into; made to exist or appear,<BR>manifested, exhibited; made to exist in the mind,<BR>presented to the imagination, conceived, imagined,<BR>supposed, thought of; thought about, meditated on;<BR>fixed on (as the mind or thoughts); purified by<BR>meditation; known, recognised, acknowledged;<BR>proved, established; convicted; occupied with, per-<BR>vaded by, filled with; inspired by, animated; mixed<BR>with (as an ingredient); soaked in, saturated with,<BR>steeped, infused; perfumed with, scented; (in arith-<BR>metic and algebra) involving a product of unknown<BR>quantities; (अम्), n. a product obtained by multipli-<BR>cation, a factum.<BR>—भावित-बुद्धी, इस्, इस्, इ, one<BR>who has purified his mind by meditation &c.; see भा-<BR>वितात्मन्.<BR>—भावित-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has<BR>imagined or conceived or infused &c.<BR>—भावितात्मन्<BR>(˚त-आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, one whose soul is purified or who<BR>has purified it by meditating on the universal soul,<BR>one who has perceived or whose thoughts are fixed<BR>on the Supreme Spirit; thoughtful, meditative;<BR>intent upon, engaged in; a sage; (आ), m., N. of<BR>the thirteenth Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितक|भावितकं
भावितक, the product of a multiplication; [cf.<BR>भावित above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित्र|भावित्रं
भावित्र, अम्, n. the three worlds (viz. earth,<BR>heaven, and the lower regions or the atmosphere),<BR>the universe; [cf. भवित्र.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविन्
भाविन्, इ, इनि, इ, becoming, being, existing [cf.<BR>भृत्य-भ्˚, पूर्व-भ्˚]; about to be, about to<BR>come to pass, future; predestined; what ought to<BR>be; what will fall to the share of (any one); attached<BR>to, (हरि-भाविन्, attached to Hari); being pos-<BR>sessed of, (at the end of a comp., e. g. ज्ञान-विज्ञा-<BR>न-भ्˚, possessing sacred and profane knowledge);<BR>beautiful, illustrious; (ई), m. (according to the Vāja-<BR>saneyi-prātiśākhya) every vowel except अ and आ<BR>(perhaps so called as liable to become changed into<BR>the corresponding semivowels); N. of the caste of<BR>Śūdras in Plaksha-dvīpa; (इनी), f. a distinguished<BR>or handsome woman; a lady, noble lady [cf. भ-<BR>व्य]; a wanton woman; N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda; of a daughter of a Gandharva;<BR>[cf. अ-निरुद्ध-भ्˚.]<BR>—भावि-ता, f. the state of<BR>being or becoming, (तद्-भाव-भावि-ता, conform-<BR>ing one's self to the mode of thought of that person);<BR>futurity, predestination.<BR>—भावि-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being or becoming, the being obliged to<BR>take place, inevitableness, unavoidableness, necessity.<BR>—भाव्य्-उपध, अस्, m., scil. विसर्जनीय, a<BR>Visarjanīya following in the Pada-pāṭha after any<BR>vowel except the vowel अ or आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक, अस्, आ, अम्, being, disposed to be, about<BR>to be, becoming, (sometimes used like भविष्णु<BR>at the end of a comp. after an adv. in अम्, cf. आढ्-<BR>यम्-भ्˚, अन्धम्-भ्˚, दूरम्-भ्˚, नग्नम्-भ्˚,<BR>पलितम्-भ्˚, प्रियम्-भ्˚); happy, well, auspicious,<BR>prosperous; having a taste for the beautiful, having<BR>a poetical taste; (अस्), m. (in theatrical language) a<BR>sister's husband; (अम्), n. language full of feeling or<BR>passion; happiness, auspiciousness, welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्य|भाव्यं
भाव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. भू or its Caus.),<BR>being, existing at the present time (Ved., cf. भव्य);<BR>about to be or happen, future, to be become, what<BR>must or ought to be or become, (sometimes used for<BR>the future tense of the verb, e. g. पुलहो भाव्यो<BR>महर्षिः, Pulaha is to be reckoned a great Ṛṣi;<BR>and often impersonally, e. g. भाव्यं तया, it is<BR>to be become by her, i. e. she must become); to be<BR>effected or accomplished, to be performed; to be appre-<BR>hended or perceived; to be imagined or conceived<BR>[cf. दुर्-भ्˚]; to be convinced; to be argued or<BR>proved or demonstrated; to be investigated or de-<BR>termined; (according to Vedic commentators) =<BR>भावयव्य, to be honoured or worshipped?; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a king (= भाव्य-रथ or भानु-<BR>रथ).<BR>—भाव्य-ता, f. or भाव्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the state of being about to happen, futurity.<BR>—भा-<BR>व्य-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a king; [cf. भाव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावड
भावड भावड, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत|भावतः
भावत भावत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 2. भवत्),<BR>your honour's, your, thy (respectfully).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्क|भावत्कः
भावत्क, अस्, ई, अम्, your honour's, your, thy,<BR>thine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावला
भावला भावला, f., N. of the wife of Bhā-<BR>vaḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाट|भावाटः
भावाट भावाट. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाव
भावाव भावाव, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr.<BR>भाव + अव fr. rt. अव्), delicate, tender, compas-<BR>sionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्
भाष् 1. भाष् (connected with rt. 1.<BR>भा as Gr. φη-μί with φαίνω), cl. 1. A.<BR>भाषते (ep. also P. -ति), बभाषे, भाषितुम्,<BR>to speak, talk, say; to speak to, address (with acc.<BR>of the person or sometimes with acc. of the person<BR>and thing); to tell or announce (anything) to (any<BR>one); to speak of or about; to reply, to call or<BR>name; to use or employ in speaking; to describe:<BR>Pass. भाष्यते, to be spoken, to be addressed or<BR>spoken to (sometimes with acc., e. g. स वचो मु-<BR>निना बभाषे, he was addressed by the Muni in a<BR>speech): Caus. भाषयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबभा-<BR>षत् or अबीभषत्, to cause to speak or talk; to<BR>say or speak; to cause disquietude, disturb (?): Desid.<BR>बिभाषिषते: Intens. बाभाष्यते, बाभाष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0708-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषक
भाषक, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, talking about,<BR>(at the end of a comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषण|भाषणं
भाषण, अम्, n. speaking, talking, saying;<BR>speech, talk; kind words, kindness, = साम-दानादि;<BR>(in theatrical language) expression of satisfaction at<BR>the end of a drama, applause (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषत्
भाषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, speaking, saying, talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषमाण
भाषमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, saying, talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषा
भाषा, f. speech, language [cf. देश-भ्˚, पर-<BR>भ्˚, भूत-भ्˚]; common or vernacular speech (in<BR>ancient times as opposed to Vedic, in later as opposed<BR>to Sanskrit), any Prākṛt dialect, (the five Prākṛts<BR>or vernaculars, viz. Mahā-rāṣṭrī, Śaurasenī, Māgadhī,<BR>Prācyā, and Avantī, are called Pañca-vidhā Bhāṣā);<BR>description, definition; (in law) an accusation, charge,<BR>complaint, plaint; N. of Sarasvatī (goddess of speech);<BR>of a Rāgiṇī.<BR>—भाषा-ज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भाषान्तर (˚षा-अन्˚), अम्, n. another dialect<BR>or version, a translation.<BR>—भाषा-परिच्छेद, अस्,<BR>m. ‘definition of (the categories of) speech,’ N. of<BR>a compendium of the Vaiśeṣika branch of the Nyāya<BR>system of philosophy by Viśva-nātha.<BR>—भाषा-<BR>पाद, अम्, n. the plaint or charge, the first of the<BR>four stages of a lawsuit.<BR>—भाषा-मञ्जरी, f., N.<BR>of an elementary work on Sanskrit grammar.<BR>—भा-<BR>षार्णव (˚षा-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a work by<BR>Candra-śekhara.<BR>—भाषा-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a<BR>commentary on Pāṇini's grammar.<BR>—भाषावृत्त्य्-<BR>अर्थ-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>preceding work.<BR>—भाषा-सम, अस्, m. a particular<BR>figure in rhetoric, a sentence so arranged that it may<BR>be either Sanskrit or Prākṛt.<BR>—भाषा-समिति, इस्,<BR>f. (with Jainas) one of the Samitis, moderation in<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिक
भाषिक, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to common or<BR>vernacular speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिका
भाषिका, f. speech, language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषित|भाषितं
भाषित, अस्, आ, अम्, spoken, uttered, said; (अम्),<BR>n. that which is spoken, speech, language, talk,<BR>speaking.<BR>—भाषित-पुंस्क, अस्, अम्, m. n. =<BR>उक्त-पुंस्क, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितव्य
भाषितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be spoken to or<BR>addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितृ
भाषितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a speaker, talker; speak-<BR>ing, talking, telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिन्
भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking, talking, saying, tell-<BR>ing, a speaker, (commonly at the end of a comp., cf.<BR>अल्प-भ्˚, प्राकृत-भ्˚); loquacious, a chatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्य|भाष्यं
भाष्य, अम्, n. speaking, talking; any work in<BR>the common or vernacular speech; an explanatory<BR>work, exposition, explanation, commentary in general<BR>(but especially the explanation of technical Sūtras or<BR>aphorisms); Patañjali's commentary on the Sūtras<BR>of Pāṇini [cf. महा-भाष्य]; a sort of house or<BR>building.<BR>—भाष्य-कर or भाष्य-कार, अस्,<BR>or भाष्य-कृत्, त्, m. ‘commentary-maker,’ the<BR>writer of any explanatory work or commentary, a<BR>commentator, scholiast, an expounder of technical<BR>Sūtras or aphorisms; (especially) an epithet of Patañ-<BR>jali, the author of the Mahā-bhāṣya or great com-<BR>mentary on Pāṇini; epithet of the commentators<BR>Nātha and Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—भाष्य-टीका, f., N.<BR>of a commentary on the Mahā-bhāṣya; of another<BR>commentary better known as Śrīmad-bhāṣya-ṭīkā.<BR>—भाष्य-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of Kaiyaṭa's com-<BR>mentary on the Mahā-bhāṣya.<BR>—भाष्यप्रदीप-<BR>विवरण, अम्, n., N. of Iśvarānanda's explanation<BR>of the Bhāṣya-pradīpa.<BR>—भाष्यप्रदीपोद्द्योत<BR>(˚प-उद्˚), अस्, m., N. of Nāgojī-bhaṭṭa's expla-<BR>nation of Kaiyaṭa's Bhāṣya-pradīpa.<BR>—भाष्य-<BR>रत्न-प्रभा, f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>Śārīraka-mīmāṃsā-bhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यमाण
भाष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being spoken to or<BR>addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्
भाष् 2. भाष् (fr. rt. भष्), Ved. occur-<BR>ring only in the comp. रक्षो-भाष्, barking like<BR>a Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष
भाष भाष. See भास, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषणीक्षौलेम
भाषणीक्षौलेम भाषणीक्षौलेम, आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a race (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् 1. भास् (connected with rt. 1.<BR>भा), cl. 1. A. (in epic poetry also P.)<BR>भासते (-ति), बभासे, भासिष्यते, अभासिष्ट,<BR>भासितुम्, to shine, to be bright; to appear; to<BR>appear or come into the mind, to be conceived or<BR>imagined, to become clear or evident: Caus. भास-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबभासत् and अबीभसत्, to<BR>make shine, illuminate; to cause to appear, show,<BR>make evident: Desid. बिभासिषते: Intens. बाभा-<BR>स्यते, बाभास्ति; [cf. Hib. beosach, ‘bright, glitter-<BR>ing,’ perhaps mais, ‘sparkling;’ probably Lat. fes-<BR>tra, fas-tus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
2. भास्, f. n. (according to some fr. rt. 1. भा,<BR>q. v.; but according to Pāṇini III. 2, 177, fr. rt. 1.<BR>भास्), light, glare, lustre, brightness; a ray or gleam<BR>of light, (भासां निधिः, receptacle of rays of<BR>light, the sun); an image, reflection, shadow; glory,<BR>splendor, power, majesty; wish, desire.<BR>—भासा-<BR>केतु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. भासा inst. c. + केतु), Ved.<BR>perceivable by light, appearing through light; (Sāy.<BR>= ज्वाला-लक्षण-ज्ञापक.)<BR>—भास्-कर, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, ‘light-causing,’ shining, glittering, bright, re-<BR>splendent; (अस्), m. the sun, (if used at the end of<BR>an adj. comp. the fem. will end in आ); N. of Śiva;<BR>fire; a hero; the plant Calotropis Gigantea (=<BR>अर्क); N. of various men; of a famous Hindū<BR>astronomer, (also called Bhāskarācārya, q. v.; भास्-<BR>कर is often found at the end of names, cf. ज्ञान-<BR>भ्˚, ब्रह्मण्य-भ्˚, भगवद्-भ्˚, भगवन्त-<BR>भ्˚, भाट्ट-भ्˚); (अम्), n. gold; N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—भास्कर-नृसिंह, अस्, m., N. of a Scholiast<BR>of the last century.<BR>—भास्कर-प्रिय, अस्, m.<BR>‘fond of the sun,’ a ruby.<BR>—भास्कर-भट्ट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of an author.<BR>—भास्कर-मिश्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of an author; (also called भट्ट-भ्˚.)<BR>—भास्-<BR>कर-लवण, अम्, n. a particular mixture (contain-<BR>ing salt &c.).<BR>—भास्कर-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>king of Kāma-rūpa; of a person mentioned in the<BR>Daśa-kumāra-carita, p. 194, 1. 14.<BR>—भास्कर-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n., N. of a particular religious observ-<BR>ance.<BR>—भास्कर-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a com-<BR>mentator of the seventeenth century; [cf. हरि-<BR>भास्कर.]<BR>—भास्कर-सप्तमी, f., N. of the<BR>seventh day in the light half of the month Māgha.<BR>—भास्कराचार्य (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author; N. of a celebrated astronomer and mathe-<BR>matician who lived in the twelfth century and wrote<BR>the Siddhānta-śiro-maṇi (which contains treatises on<BR>algebra, arithmetic, and geometry, called Vīja-gaṇita<BR>and Līlāvatī).<BR>—भास्करि, इस्, m. (a patronymic fr.<BR>भास्-कर), the planet Saturn; N. of a Muni.<BR>—भास्करीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to or coming<BR>from Bhāskara; (अस्), m. a pupil of Bhāskara.<BR>—भास्करेष्टा (˚र-इष्˚), f. the plant Polanisia<BR>Icosandra.<BR>—भास्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing light,<BR>luminous, splendid, shining; (आन्), m. the sun; light,<BR>lustre, brightness; a hero; (अती), f. the city of the<BR>sun; N. of a work; (according to Naighaṇṭuka 1. 8)<BR>= उषस्, dawn; (यस्), f. pl. (according to Naighaṇ-<BR>ṭuka 1. 13) = नदी, a river.<BR>—भास्वती-करण,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास|भासः
भास, अस्, m. (sometimes written भाष), light,<BR>lustre, brightness; shining, (at the end of a comp.,<BR>e. g. चन्द्र-भास, shining as the moon); im-<BR>pression made on the mind, fancy; a vulture; a<BR>cock; a sort of bird described as a water-fowl; =<BR>शकुन्त; = कुक्कुट; = नील-पक्षः पक्षी; a<BR>cow-shed, cattle-fold (= गोष्ठ); N. of a Sāman<BR>(also अम्, n.); of a man; of a dramatic poet; of a<BR>son of a minister of king Candra-prabha; of a Dā-<BR>nava; of a mountain; (ई), f. the mother of the Bhāsas<BR>or vultures; N. of a daughter of Prādhā.<BR>—भास-<BR>कर्ण, अस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—भास-ता, f.<BR>the being a vulture or bird of prey; vulturous nature,<BR>rapacity.<BR>—भास-विलास-संवाद, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the twenty-fifth chapter of the Vāsisṭha-rāmāyaṇa,<BR>commonly called Yoga-vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—भासा-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासक|भासकः
भासक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>appear, making evident, showing, manifesting; en-<BR>lightening; making intelligible, (usually at the end of<BR>comps.); (अस्), m., N. of a dramatic poet.<BR>—भा-<BR>सक-त्व, अम्, n. enlightenment, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन|भासनं
भासन, अम्, n. shining, glittering, illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्त|भासंत|भासन्तः
भासन्त, अस्, ई, अम्, shining, splendid; beautiful,<BR>handsome; (अस्), m. the sun; the moon; a star, an<BR>asterism; the bird Bhāsa, q. v.; (ई), f. an asterism,<BR>a Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासमान
भासमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, radiant; ap-<BR>pearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासयत्
भासयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, making to shine, illu-<BR>minating; shining, radiant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासस्
भासस्, अस्, n., Ved. brightness, light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासाय
भासाय, Nom. A. भासायते, &c., to act the<BR>part of the bird Bhāsa, to appear like this bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासिन्
भासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of a comp.) shining,<BR>brilliant (e. g. ऊर्ध्व-भ्˚, shining upwards; cf.<BR>ज्योतिर्-भ्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासु|भासुः
भासु, उस्, m. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुर|भासुरं|भासुरः
भासुर, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, splendid; terrible,<BR>(in this sense probably an incorrect form); (अस्), m.<BR>a crystal; a hero; (अम्), n. Costus Speciosus or<BR>Arabicus; [cf. भास्वर.]<BR>—भासुर-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>splendor.<BR>—भासुर-पुषपा, f. the plant Tragia<BR>Involucrata (= वृश्चि-काली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुरक
भासुरक, अस्, m., N. of a lion (in Pañca-tantra,<BR>p. 53, 1. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्य
भास्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), to be made<BR>visible, to be brought to light.<BR>—भास्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state or condition of appearing, visibleness.<BR>—भास्य-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a section in the<BR>Kāktantra treating of the meaning of grammatical<BR>forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वर|भास्वरं|भास्वरः
भास्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, radiant, brilliant,<BR>bright, resplendent; (अस्), m. the sun; a day; N. of<BR>a satellite of the god of the sun; of a Buddhist<BR>deity; (अम्), n. Costus Arabicus or Speciosus (=<BR>कुष्ठ; cf. प्र-भ्˚, भासुर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासद
भासद भासद, अस्, m., औ, m. du. (fr.<BR>भसद्), Ved. (perhaps) the buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासिन्
भासिन् भासिन्, भासुर, &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कर|भास्करं|भास्करः
भास्कर भास्-कर. See under 2. भास्, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्त्रायण
भास्त्रायण भास्त्रायण, भास्त्रायणक (fr.<BR>भस्त्रा), see Gaṇa Arīhaṇādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्मन
भास्मन भास्मन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भस्मन्),<BR>made or consisting of ashes, ashy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्मायन्य
भास्मायन्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhas-<BR>man; भास्मायनास्, m. pl., see Gaṇa Kuñjādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 1, 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिःखराज
भिःखराज भिःख-राज, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्ष्
भिक्ष् भिक्ष् (probably for बिहक्ष्,<BR>Desid. of rt. भज्), cl. 1. A. (ep. also P.)<BR>भिक्षते, बिभिक्षे, भिक्षिष्यते, अभिक्षिष्ट,<BR>भिक्षितुम्, lit. to wish to share or partake; to beg<BR>for, ask for; to desire, implore (Ved. with acc. and<BR>gen., e. g. भिक्षे सुमतिं तुराणाम्, I implore<BR>your favour against eager foes, Ṛg-veda 1. 171, 1);<BR>to solicit, to beg alms (with abl. of person or with a<BR>double acc.); to obtain; to ask for without obtain-<BR>ing; to be weary or distressed (?); to speak (?):<BR>Caus. भिक्षयति, -यितुम्, to cause to beg, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षण|भिक्षणं
भिक्षण, अम्, आ, n. f. the act of begging,<BR>asking alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षमाण
भिक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, asking, begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षा
भिक्षा, f. the act of begging, asking [cf. मांस-<BR>भ्˚]; anything given as alms or obtained by begging,<BR>(sometimes in comp. with the object asked for, e. g.<BR>पुत्र-भिक्षां देहि, grant the boon of a son,<BR>lit. a son as alms); alms, food given as alms [cf.<BR>दुर्-भिक्ष, सु-भ्˚]; hire, wages (= भृति);<BR>service.<BR>—भिक्षा-करण, अम्, n. the act of ask-<BR>ing alms, begging.<BR>—भिक्षा-चर, अस्, ई, अम्, going<BR>about begging; a beggar, mendicant; (अस्), m., N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">Page0710-a+ 79</a>]<BR>of a son of Bhoja, (also called भिक्षु.)<BR>—भिक्षा-<BR>चरण, अम्, n. or भिक्षा-चर्य, अम्, आ, n. f.<BR>the act of going about begging, begging, mendi-<BR>cancy.<BR>—भिक्षा-चार, अस्, ई, अम्, = भिक्षा-चर.<BR>—भिक्षाटन (˚षा-अट्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wandering<BR>about begging or asking for alms, begging, men-<BR>dicity, mendicancy; (अस्), m. a mendicant; N. of a<BR>poet; (अम्), n. the act of begging, mendicancy,<BR>going about asking for alms; N. of a work; भिक्-<BR>षाटनं कृ, to wander about as a mendicant.<BR>—भिक्षान्न (˚षा-अन्˚), अम्, n. food obtained<BR>as alms; [cf. भिक्षाहार.]<BR>—भिक्षा-पात्र, अम्,<BR>n. a mendicant's bowl, vessel for collecting alms,<BR>alms-dish.<BR>—भिक्षा-प्रचार, अस्, m. = भिक्षा-<BR>चरण, q. v.<BR>—भिक्षा-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a mendi-<BR>cant's bowl or vessel.<BR>—भिक्षा-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, living<BR>on alms.<BR>—भिक्षा-माणव, अस्, m. a beggar boy,<BR>young beggar (as a term of contempt).<BR>—भिक्षा-<BR>यण (˚षा-अय्˚), अम्, n. the act of plying for alms.<BR>—भिक्षार्थिन् (˚षा-अर्˚), ई, इनी, इ, asking for<BR>alms, a petitioner for charity; begging; a beggar or<BR>mendicant.<BR>—भिक्षार्ह (˚षा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>worthy of alms.<BR>—भिक्षा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>or receiving alms, begging.<BR>—भिक्षा-वासस्, अस्, n.<BR>the garment of a mendicant, a beggar's dress.<BR>—भिक्-<BR>षा-वृत्ति, इस्, इस्, इ, living or subsisting on alms,<BR>begging.<BR>—भिक्षाशि-त्व (˚षा-आश्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>eating begged food, subsisting on alms; mendi-<BR>cancy; profligacy, roguery.<BR>—भिक्षाशिन् (˚षा-<BR>आश्˚), इ, इनी, इ, eating begged food, living or sub-<BR>sisting on alms; dishonest; [cf. भैक्षाश्य.]<BR>—भिक्षाहार (˚षा-आह्˚), अस्, m. begged food;<BR>[cf. भिक्षान्न.]<BR>—भिक्षोत्कर (˚षा-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. scattering alms.<BR>—भिक्षोपजीविन् (˚षा-उप्˚), ई,<BR>इनी, इ, subsisting by alms, one who lives by begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0709-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाक|भिक्षाकः
भिक्षाक, अस्, ई, m. f. begging, a beggar, men-<BR>dicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षित
भिक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, begged, solicited or ob-<BR>tained as alms; [cf. शूद्र-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षितव्य
भिक्षितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. to be begged or<BR>asked for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षिन्
भिक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, begging, asking for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षु|भिक्षुः
भिक्षु, उस्, m. a beggar, mendicant, religious<BR>mendicant (especially a Brāhman of the fourth or<BR>mendicant order, i. e. one in the fourth āśrama or<BR>last stage of his life when he abandons his house and<BR>family and subsists entirely on alms; cf. आश्रम,<BR>महा-भ्˚); a Buddhist mendicant; a particular<BR>Buddha; N. of an Āṅgīrasa (author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 117); of a son of Bhoja (= भिक्षा-<BR>चर); N. of a particular species of plant, = श्रा-<BR>वणी, = कोकिलाक्ष; (उ), n., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—भिक्षु-चर्या, f. ‘a beggar's course of life,’<BR>begging.<BR>—भिक्षु-तत्त्व, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—भिक्षु-सङ्घ, अस्, m. a society of Buddhist<BR>mendicants.<BR>—भिक्षु-सङ्घाती, f. beggar's clothes,<BR>old or ragged raiment.<BR>—भिक्षु-सूत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>collection of rules or precepts for mendicants.<BR>—भिक्-<BR>षुसूत्र-भाष्य-वार्त्तिक, अम्, n., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुक|भिक्षुकः
भिक्षुक, अस्, m. a beggar, mendicant, a Brāh-<BR>man of the mendicant order [cf. भिक्षु]; (ई), f. a<BR>female mendicant.<BR>—भिक्षुकी-पारक (?), N. of<BR>a building mentioned in Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VI. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुणी
भिक्षुणी, f. a Buddhist female mendicant or<BR>nun, (probably a Pāli form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्ष्य
भिक्ष्य (fr. भिक्षा), Nom. P. भिक्ष्यति,<BR>&c., to beg or ask for alms, (a doubtful form.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिण्ड|भिण्डः
भिण्ड भिण्ड or भिण्डक or भिण्डीतक,<BR>अस्, m. or भिण्डा, f. the plant Abelmoschus Escu-<BR>lentus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्त|भित्तं
भित्त भित्त, भित्ति, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद् 1. भिद्, cl. 7. P. A. भिनत्ति,<BR>भिन्त्ते (Ved. also cl. 1. भेदति), Impf.<BR>अभिनत् (2nd sing. अभिनस् or अभिनत्, 1st sing.<BR>Ved. अभेदम्, 2nd sing. अभेत्, भेत्), Impv. भि-<BR>नत्तु (2nd sing. भिन्द्धि or भिन्धि), बिभेद<BR>(2nd sing. बिभेदिथ), बिभिदे (Part. बिभिद्वस्),<BR>भेत्स्यति, -ते, Aor. अभिदत् and अभैत्सीत्, अभित्त<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">Page0710-b+ 81</a>]<BR>(2nd sing. अभित्थास्), Inf. भेत्तुम् (Ved. भेत्-<BR>तवै), to break, split, cleave, slit, cut asunder, sever,<BR>rend, tear, pierce, penetrate; to break through or<BR>down, burst through (e. g. सेतुम् भिद्, to break<BR>through an embankment; तिमिरम् भिद्, to break<BR>through or disperse darkness); to violate (e. g. सन्-<BR>धिम् भिद्, to violate a compact or alliance); to<BR>interrupt, disturb; to tear up; to destroy; to divide,<BR>separate; to open; to make to open or blossom,<BR>expand; to divide into parts or portions, disjoin,<BR>disunite; to loose, loosen, dissolve; to unravel, extri-<BR>cate; to betray, disclose; to set at variance; to<BR>unsettle, perplex; to alter, change, make to differ;<BR>to distinguish, discriminate: Pass. भिद्यते, to be<BR>split; to burst (e. g. शीतेन, with frost); to be torn<BR>asunder; to be destroyed; to be harassed or afflicted;<BR>to be divided or separated; to open, be opened,<BR>become relaxed; to expand, blossom, bloom; to<BR>become loose, be loosened; to separate one's self<BR>from, keep aloof from (with inst.); to differ or be<BR>different from (with abl.); to alter, change; to be<BR>divulged: Caus. भेदयति, -यितुम्, अबीभिदत्, to<BR>cause to break or split &c., to break, split, cleave,<BR>divide, tear or dash to pieces; to destroy, overcome;<BR>to separate, dissolve, disunite, unsettle (in opinion),<BR>perplex, set at variance, cause dispersion; to seduce:<BR>Desid. of Caus. बिभेदयिषति: Desid. बिभित्-<BR>सति, -ते: Intens. बेभिद्यते, बेभिदीति, बेभेत्ति,<BR>to break or split repeatedly, to divide or cut into<BR>again and again; [cf. Lat. findo, fi-nis fr. fid-<BR>nis (?): Goth. bit, ‘to bite;’ beita, bait, bitum:<BR>Old Germ. biz.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्त|भित्तं
भित्त, अम्, n. a fragment, broken piece, bit; a<BR>part, portion; = भित्ति, a partition, wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्ति|भित्तिः
भित्ति, इस्, f. breaking, splitting, tearing, dividing;<BR>a wall of earth or masonry, a partition; a mat (made<BR>of split reeds); anything broken or divided; a rent,<BR>fissure; a fragment, bit, piece, portion, part; a place,<BR>spot; a flaw, defect, deficiency; an opportunity,<BR>occasion; an asylum (?).<BR>—भित्ति-खातन, अस्, m.<BR>‘wall-digger,’ one who digs into or undermines<BR>walls, a rat; [cf. भित्ति-पातन.]<BR>—भित्ति-चौर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘wall-burglar,’ a house-breaker (the mud wall<BR>of the Hindū cottages being easily cut through by<BR>burglars).<BR>—भित्ति-पातन, अस्, m. ‘wall-overthrower,<BR>wall-destroyer,’ a kind of rat; [cf. भित्ति-खातन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिका
भित्तिका, f. a partition, wall; a small house-<BR>lizard; (अस्, आ, अम्) = भित्ति (at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्त्वा
भित्त्वा, ind. having broken, having split, having<BR>burst through, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
2. भिद्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of a comp.) breaking,<BR>splitting, dividing, piercing; a breaker, &c.; break-<BR>ing to pieces, destroying [cf. अश्म-भ्˚, गिरि-भ्˚,<BR>गोत्र-भ्˚, तमो-भ्˚, पुर-भ्˚]; (त्), f., Ved. a<BR>breaker, destroyer, &c.; breaking, splitting, dividing;<BR>difference; different sort, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदक|भिदकं|भिदकः
भिदक, अस्, m. ‘cutter or wounder,’ a sword;<BR>(अम्), n. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदा
भिदा, f. breaking, splitting, piercing, bursting in<BR>pieces, tearing, rending [cf. दुर्-भिद]; dividing,<BR>separation; difference; sort, kind, species; coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदापन
भिदापन, अम्, n. (fr. an irregular Caus. भि-<BR>दापय), the act of causing to break, causing to<BR>pound or trample on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदि|भिदिः
भिदि, इस्, or भिदु, उस्, m. Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदिर|भिदिरं
भिदिर, अम्, n. a thunderbolt (= भिदि above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुर|भिदुरं|भिदुरः
भिदुर, अस्, आ, अम्, breaking, splitting, piercing,<BR>destroying; easily broken or split, fragile, brittle;<BR>divided, variegated, mingled; (अम्), n. a thunderbolt<BR>[cf. भिदिर].<BR>—भिदुर-स्वन, अस्, m. ‘making a<BR>piercing sound, N. of an Asura; (in Hari-vaṃśa’ 2289<BR>also read मृदुर-स्वन, सृमरः खनः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदेलिम
भिदेलिम, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken or split,<BR>easily broken, brittle, fragile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्य|भिद्यः
भिद्य, अस्, m. a rushing river (‘one bursting its<BR>banks’); N. of a river; [cf. पूर्-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्यमान
भिद्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being broken or split<BR>or pierced; being divided or separated; being dis-<BR>tinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्र|भिद्रं|भिद्रः
भिद्र, अम्, n. a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्वत्|भिद्वन्त्
भिद्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing the root भिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दत्
भिन्दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, breaking, splitting, cleaving,<BR>piercing, destroying, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दु|भिंदु|भिन्दुः
भिन्दु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. breaking, splitting; de-<BR>stroying; a destroyer; (उस्), m. a drop [cf. बिन्दू];<BR>(उस्), f. a woman bringing forth a still-born child, a<BR>woman who bears a dead child; [cf. निन्दु.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्द्धिलवणा
भिन्द्धि-लवणा, f. (fr. 2nd sing. Impv.), con-<BR>stant sprinkling of salt; [cf. पच-ल्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्न|भिन्नः
भिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, broken, fractured, split,<BR>(भिन्ना नौः, a leaky ship, a wrecked vessel);<BR>torn, rent, cloven, pounded, lacerated; opened, ex-<BR>panded, budded, blossoming; divided, separated<BR>into parts, anything less than a whole; detached,<BR>disunited, disjoined; loosened; separated or different<BR>from; distinct, other, different (e. g. आङ्-भिन्नो-<BR>निपातः, any particle other than आङ्); deviated,<BR>deviating or varying from; deprived of, without;<BR>furious (as an elephant, see भिन्न-करट); mingled,<BR>mixed, cleaving to; (अस्), m. a flaw or defect in a<BR>jewel; (अम्), n. a fragment, bit, part, portion; (in<BR>arithmetic) a fraction; a blossom; a wound from a<BR>pointed weapon, a stab; a particular mode of fight-<BR>ing mentioned in Hari-vaṃśa 15978 (also read<BR>मित्र.)<BR>—भिन्न-करट, अस्, m. an elephant in<BR>rut or from whose divided temples the juice exudes.<BR>—भिन्न-कर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, having divided ears<BR>(said of particular animals).<BR>—भिन्न-कूट, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, deprived of a chief or leader (said of an army).<BR>—भिन्न-क्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, having the order<BR>broken, out of order or place, displaced.<BR>—भिन्न-<BR>गति, इस्, इस्, इ, going with great strides, going quickly.<BR>—भिन्न-गर्भ, अस्, आ, अम्, disunited in its<BR>centre (said of an army), broken up, disorganized.<BR>—भिन्न-गात्रिका, f. a kind of cucumber, Cucumis<BR>Usitatissimus (= कर्कटी).<BR>—भिन्न-गुणन, अम्,<BR>n. multiplication of fractions.<BR>—भिन्न-घन, अस्,<BR>m. the cube of a fraction.<BR>—भिन्न-जातीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of a different tribe or caste.<BR>—भिन्न-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of being different, difference, variation.<BR>—भिन्न-दर्शिन्, ई, इनी, इ, or भिन्न-दृश्, क्,<BR>क्, क्, seeing different things, seeing a difference,<BR>making a difference, partial, (opposed to सम-<BR>दर्शिन्.)<BR>—भिन्न-देश, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to<BR>different or various places; occurring or happening<BR>in various places.<BR>—भिन्नदेश-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>condition of being widely distant.<BR>—भिन्न-देह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘whose body is pierced,’ wounded.<BR>—भिन्न-नौ, औस्, औस्, उ, or भिन्न-नौक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘whose ship is broken,’ shipwrecked.<BR>—भिन्न-परिकर्मन्, अ, n. an arithmetical ope-<BR>ration with fractions.<BR>—भिन्न-प्रकार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of a different kind or sort.<BR>—भिन्न-भाग-<BR>हर, अस्, m. division of fractions.<BR>—भिन्न-भाण्ड<BR>or भिन्न-भाजन, अम्, n. a broken pot or vessel,<BR>potsherd.<BR>—भिन्न-भिन्नात्मन् (˚न-आत्˚), आ, m.<BR>chick-pea, Cicer Arietinum.<BR>—भिन्न-मर्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, pierced in the vital organs, mortally wounded.<BR>—भिन्न-मर्याद, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘whose course is<BR>broken or separated from the right way,’ uncontrolled,<BR>unrestrained; unbounded.<BR>—भिन्न-मस्तक-पिण्-<BR>डक or -पिण्डिक, अस्, आ, अम्, whose skull and<BR>forehead is cloven, (an elephant) whose frontal globes<BR>are open.<BR>—भिन्न-योजनी, f. the plant Plectran-<BR>thus Scutellarioides (= पाषाण-भेद).<BR>—भिन्न-<BR>लिङ्ग, अम्, n. incongruity of gender in a comparison.<BR>—भिन्न-वचन, अम्, n. incongruity of number<BR>in a comparison.<BR>—भिन्न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who<BR>has divided.<BR>—भिन्न-वर्ग, अस्, m. the square of a<BR>fraction.<BR>—भिन्न-वर्चस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, or भिन्न-<BR>वर्चस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, voiding excrement, &c.<BR>—भिन्-<BR>वर्चस्क, अस्, आ, अम्, changed in colour, discoloured,<BR>pale; of a different caste or tribe.<BR>—भिन्न-वर्त्-<BR>मन्, आ, आ, अ, separated from the right way; [cf.<BR>भिन्न-मर्याद.]<BR>—भिन्न-विट्क, अस्, आ, अम् (fr.<BR>भिन्न + विष्), = भिन्न-वर्चस्.<BR>—भिन्नविट्क-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state of one who voids excrement,<BR>&c., (according to some commentators) change of<BR>colour in the feces.<BR>—भिन्न-वृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having abandoned the path of duty, leading a bad<BR>life; containing a metrical fault.<BR>—भिन्न-वृत्ति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">Page0711-a+ 74</a>]<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, having different occupations, occupied dif-<BR>ferently; leading a bad life; neglecting prescribed<BR>observances, following bad courses.<BR>—भिन्नवृत्ति-<BR>ता, f. the following of evil courses, neglect of pre-<BR>scribed observances.<BR>—भिन्न-व्यवकलित, अम्, n.<BR>subtraction of fractions.<BR>—भिन्न-संहति, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>whose union is broken, disunited.<BR>—भिन्न-सङ्-<BR>कलन or भिन्न-सङ्कलित, अम्, n. addition of<BR>fractions.<BR>—भिन्न-स्वर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>broken or changed voice, hesitating in speech, fal-<BR>tering; discordant.<BR>—भिन्नस्वर-मुख-वर्ण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a broken or changed voice and<BR>complexion.<BR>—भिन्न-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, pierced<BR>through the heart.<BR>—भिन्नाञ्जन (˚न-अञ्˚), अम्,<BR>n. divided antimony, pounded collyrium, or colly-<BR>rium mixed (with oil and used as an eye-salve), eye-<BR>ointment consisting of various materials pounded and<BR>mixed.<BR>—भिन्नाञ्जद्न-चयोपम (˚य-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, like a quantity of pounded antimony or<BR>mixed collyrium.<BR>—भिन्नाञ्जन-सन्निभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, similar to pounded antimony or mixed pigment.<BR>—भिन्नाञ्जनाकर (˚न-आक्˚), or भिन्नाञ्जना-<BR>भ (˚न-आभ˚), अस्, आ, अम्, appearing like pounded<BR>antimony or mixed collyrium.<BR>—भिन्नाभिन्न<BR>(˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, distinct and not distinct,<BR>separate and not separate.<BR>—भिन्नार्थ (˚न-अर्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a clear or distinct meaning, clear,<BR>evident, intelligible, perspicuous.<BR>—भिन्नार्थ-ता,<BR>f. clearness of meaning, intelligibleness, clearness.<BR>—भिन्नोदर (˚न-उद्˚), अस्, m. a brother by a<BR>different mother, a half brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0710-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नक|भिन्नकः
भिन्नक, अस्, m. ‘a seceder,’ a Buddhist; N. of<BR>a musical mode or Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेत्तव्य
भेत्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken; to be be-<BR>trayed; to be divulged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेत्तृ
भेत्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, breaking, splitting, piercing,<BR>bursting through, dividing, &c.; a breaker, splitter,<BR>piercer, interrupter, disturber, troubler, frustrator; a<BR>divulger (of a secret), betrayer, traitor; a factious or<BR>seditious man; (ता), m., N. of a particular magical<BR>spell recited over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्द्
भिन्द् भिन्द्, a various reading for rt.<BR>बिन्द्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दपाल|भिंदपाल|भिंदपालः|भिन्दपालः
भिन्दपाल भिन्दपाल or भिन्दिपाल, अस्, m.<BR>a short javelin or arrow thrown from the hand or shot<BR>through a tube; a stone fastened to a string; (also<BR>read भिन्दमाल, भिन्दुमाल, भिण्डिमाल, भिण्-<BR>डिमाला.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दु|भिंदु|भिन्दुः
भिन्दु भिन्दु, भिन्न, &c. See p. 710, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भियस्
भियस् भियस्. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिरिण्टिका|भिरिंटिका
भिरिण्टिका भिरिण्टिका, f. a species of plant,<BR>= श्वेत-गुञ्जा; (also read भृण्टिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्
भिल् भिल् = rt. बिल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्म
भिल्म भिल्म, अम्, n. a word used by<BR>Yāska (Nirukta 1. 20) to explain बिल्म, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्ल|भिल्लः
भिल्ल भिल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a wild mountain<BR>race, probably the modern Bheels, (they live in the<BR>Vindhya mountains, in the forests of Malwa, Mewar,<BR>and Kandesh, and in the Dakhin to the north of<BR>Poona; they were formerly notorious for their depre-<BR>dations); a kind of the Bhillas; (ई), f. the plant<BR>Symplocos Racemosa.<BR>—भिल्ल-गवी, f. = गवयी,<BR>the female of the Bos Gavæus.<BR>—भिल्ल-तरु, उस्,<BR>m. Symplocos Racemosa; [cf. भिल्ली.]<BR>—भिल्ल-<BR>भूषणा, f. the seed of the plant Abrus Preca-<BR>torius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्लोट|भिल्लोटः
भिल्लोट or भिल्लोटक, अस्, m., N. of a species<BR>of plant, (perhaps) = भिल्ल-तरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिश्चा
भिश्चा भिश्चा, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्
भिषज् 1. भिषज् (a Vedic verb of which<BR>the 3rd sing. present भिषक्ति occurs in Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 79, 2, where according to Sāy. भिषक्ति =<BR>भिषज्यति), to heal or cure; [cf. भेषज.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्
2. भिषज्, क्, क्, क् (in Uṇādi-s. I. 137 derived<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">Page0711-b+ 78</a>]<BR>fr. rt. 1. भी with vowel shortened and affix अज्, ष्<BR>being inserted), healing, sanative, curative; (क्), m.<BR>a physician; medicine, a remedy (= भेषज); N.<BR>of a man with the patronymic Ātharvaṇa; of a son<BR>of Śata-dhanvan; (औ), m. du. the Aśvins; [cf.<BR>शत-भ्˚.]<BR>—भिषक्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>most healing; (औ), m. du. ‘the best physicians,’ the<BR>Aśvins.<BR>—भिषक्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. more<BR>healing.<BR>—भिषक्-पाश, अस्, m. an inferior phy-<BR>sician, a quack doctor.<BR>—भिषक्-प्रिया, f. ‘dear<BR>to a physician,’ the plant Cocoulus Cordifolius (=<BR>गुडूची).<BR>—भिषग्-जित, अम्, n. ‘subdued by phy-<BR>sicians,’ any drug or medicine.<BR>—भिषग्-भद्रा, f.<BR>a species of the plant Croton; [cf. भद्र-दन्तिका.]<BR>—भिषग्-वर, अस्, m. the best of physicians;<BR>(औ), m. du. the two Aśvins.<BR>—भिषङ्-मातृ, ता,<BR>f. the plant Justicia Adhadota; [cf. वैद्य-मातृ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषजावर्त|भिषजावर्तः|भिषजावर्त्त
भिषजावर्त, अस्, m., N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्य|भिषज्यं
1. भिषज्य, Nom. P. भिषज्यति, &c., Ved. to<BR>heal, cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्य|भिषज्यं
2. भिषज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. sanative, healing,<BR>healthful; (आ), f. the act of healing or curing; a<BR>remedy, cure; [cf. दुर्-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्यित
भिषज्यित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. healed, cured, (also<BR>incorrectly read भिषज्ज्यित, भिषज्जियित, भि-<BR>षज्जयित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिष्णज
भिष्णज, अस्, m., see Gaṇa Gargādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिष्णज्य
भिष्णज्य, Nom. P. भिष्णज्यति, &c., Ved. =<BR>1. भिषज्य, to heal, cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिष्मा
भिष्मा भिष्मा, f. a various reading for<BR>भिस्सा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिष्मिका
भिष्मिका, भिष्मिटा, भिष्मिष्टा, various<BR>readings for भिस्सटा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिस्सटा
भिस्सटा भिस्सटा or भिस्सिटा, f. parched or<BR>fried rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिस्सा
भिस्सा, f. boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिहु
भिहु भिहु (?), उस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
भी 1. भी, cl. 1. A. भयते (Ved.); cl. 3.<BR>P. (Ved. and ep. also A.) बिभेति (3rd du.<BR>बिभीतस् or बिभितस्, 3rd pl. बिभ्यति, Part. बिभ्-<BR>यत्, ep. 1st sing. A. बिभ्ये), Impf. अबिभेत् (3rd pl.<BR>अबिभयुस्), Pot. बिभीयात् or बिभियात् (3rd pl. बि-<BR>भीयुस् or बिभियुस्, बिभ्येयुस् Mahā-bh. Śānti-p.<BR>459), बिभाय or बिभयाञ्-चकार or बिभयाम्-<BR>आस (3rd pl. बिभ्युस्, Part. बिभीवस्, बिभ्युषी, f.),<BR>भेष्यति, Aor. अभैषीत् (2nd sing. अभैषीस्,<BR>ep. मा भैस् for मा भैषीस्, Ved. forms भेस्,<BR>भेम), भेतुम् (Ved. forms भयन्ते, अभयन्त,<BR>Part. भयमान, भियान, Inf. भियसे, cf. भियस्<BR>below; according to the Dhātu-pāṭha even cl. 10. P.<BR>भाययति), to fear, dread, be afraid of (with abl. or<BR>gen., e. g. मृत्योर् बिभेति, he fears death; बिभेमि<BR>-ते, I fear thee; very rarely with inst. or acc.); to fear<BR>for, be anxious or solicitous about (A.): Pass. भी-<BR>यते, Aor. अभायि: Caus. A. भीषयते (ep. also<BR>P. भीषयति), भापयते, Aor. अबिभीषत, &c.,<BR>to terrify, put in a fright, intimidate; भाययति,<BR>Aor. अबीभयत्, &c., to frighten or terrify any one<BR>(acc.) with anything (inst.): Desid. बिभीषति:<BR>Intens. बेभीयते, बेभयीति, बेभेति; [cf. Zend<BR>rt. बी, ‘to be frightened:’ Gr. φέβ-ο-μαι, φόβο-ς,<BR>φοβέ-ω, φοβέ-ο-μαι, φοβ-ερό-ς: Lith. bij-au, ‘I<BR>am afraid;’ baime, ‘fear;’ bai-dau, ‘I terrify;’<BR>baisis, ‘terrible;’ perhaps belonging to the Caus.<BR>भीषय; byaurùs, ‘deformed,’ see भीरु; baj-<BR>us, ‘fear,’ = भय: Slav. boj-a-ti, ‘to be afraid:’<BR>probably Goth. fia for bia, fiangds: Mod. Germ.<BR>feind: Eng. fiend: Old Germ. bi-bê-n: Angl. Sax.<BR>bif-ian, beof-ian: Mod. Germ. beb-en = Intens.<BR>बेभेति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भियस्
भियस्, m., Ved. fear, apprehension, dread, (oc-<BR>curring only in the acc. and inst. sing., the dat.<BR>sing. भियसे being used as Ved. inf. of rt. 1. भी,<BR>above; cf. Zend bienghe.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भियसान
भियसान, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fearful, timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिया
भिया, f. fear, apprehension, dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
2. भी, ईस्, f. fear, apprehension, alarm, dread,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-c" target="_blank">Page0711-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(sometimes at the end of a comp., cf. अवद्य-भी.)<BR>—भी-कर, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, causing or exciting<BR>fear.<BR>—भी-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीत|भीतं
भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, frightened, alarmed, terrified,<BR>afraid, fearful, timid; placed in jeopardy or danger,<BR>imperiled, (often at the end of a comp., e. g. अग्नि-<BR>भ्˚, afraid of fire; मृत्यु-भ्˚); (अम्), n. fear,<BR>alarm, apprehension; (अम्), ind. timidly.<BR>—भीतङ्-<BR>कार, अस्, आ, अम्, making afraid; (अम्), ind. making<BR>a coward, calling a coward, (तम् भीतङ्-कारम्<BR>आक्रुश्य, calling him a coward.)<BR>—भीत-परित्राण-<BR>वस्तूपालम्भ-पण्डित (˚तु-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>clever in finding fault with the means of rescuing<BR>the terrified.<BR>—भीत-भीत, अस्, आ, अम्, very much<BR>frightened, exceedingly afraid.<BR>—१. भीत-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, one who is afraid.<BR>—२. भीत-वत्, ind. like<BR>a frightened person, timidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीति|भीतिः
भीति, इस्, f. fear, alarm, apprehension, dread,<BR>terror, (often at the end of a comp., cf. दोष-भ्˚,<BR>देव-भ्˚); tremor, trembling, shaking; danger.<BR>—भीति-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, causing fear, exciting alarm.<BR>—भीति-नाटितक, अम्, n. mimic representation of<BR>fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीम|भीमं|भीमः
भीम, अस्, आ, अम्, fearful, dreadful, terrible, for-<BR>midable, horrible, horrid, terrific, terrifying; (अम्),<BR>n. horror, terror; (अस्), m. a kind of sorrel (=<BR>अम्ल-वेतस), Rumex Vesicarius; N. of Rudra; of<BR>Śiva; of one of the eight forms of Śiva; of one<BR>of the eleven Rudras; of a Deva-gandharva; of one<BR>of the Devas called Yajña-mush; of a Dānava; of a<BR>Vidyā-dhara; of a son of the Rākṣasa Kumbha-<BR>karṇa; of the second son of Pāṇḍu (also called<BR>Bhīma-sena and Vṛkodara; he was only the reputed<BR>son of Pāṇḍu, being really the son of his wife Pṛthā<BR>or Kuntī by Vāyu, god of the wind; he was remark-<BR>able for his vast size and strength and voracious<BR>appetite; cf. वायु-पुत्र); N. of a Vaidarbha; of<BR>a son of Īlina; of a son of Amāvasu or Āmāvasu<BR>and father of Kāñcana; of a son of Sattvata; of a<BR>king of Dvārakā; of several kings; of an author;<BR>of a poet; of the father of Ananta; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the race of Bhīma; (आ), f. a whip; a sort of perfume<BR>(= रोचना); N. of a form of Durgā; of an Apsaras;<BR>of several rivers; of a district (probably sacred to<BR>Durgā); of a town.<BR>—भीम-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>terrible in act, of terrific prowess; dreadful, destruc-<BR>tive.<BR>—भीम-कार्मुक, अस्, आ, अम्, having for-<BR>midable bows.<BR>—भीम-खण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>work treating of the Liṅga Bhīmeśvara (mentioned<BR>in the Skanda-Purāṇa).<BR>—भीम-गव, अस्, or भी-<BR>म-गु, उस्, m. (गव or गु = गो), N. of a man;<BR>[cf. भैमगव.]<BR>—भीम-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a king.<BR>—भीम-ग्राह-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>terrible sea monsters.<BR>—भीम-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—भीम-जानु, उस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भीम-ता, f. terribleness, fearfulness, formidable-<BR>ness.<BR>—भीम-तिथि, इस्, f. the day of Bhīma (=<BR>भीमैकादशी).<BR>—भीम-दर्शन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>frightful in appearance or aspect, frightful, hideous.<BR>—भीम-द्वादशी, f., N. of the twelfth day of the<BR>light half of the month Māgha (called after Bhīma<BR>the reputed son of Pāṇḍu; cf. भीमैकादशी).<BR>—भीमद्वादशी-व्रत, अम्, n., N. of the sixty-<BR>fifth chapter of the Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR>—भीम-<BR>धन्वन्, आ, m. ‘having a terrific bow,’ N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—भीम-धन्वायन, ‘bearing dreadful<BR>bows,’ in भीम-धन्वायनी सेना, Mahā-bh. Ud-<BR>yoga-p. 7633.<BR>—भीम-नगर, अम्, n. ‘Bhīma's<BR>city,’ N. of a town; [cf. भीम-पुर.]<BR>—भीम-<BR>नाद, अस्, आ, अम्, sending forth a fearful sound,<BR>sounding dreadfully; (अस्), m. a loud or fearful sound;<BR>a lion; N. of one of the seven clouds which will<BR>cover the sky at the destruction of the world.<BR>—भी-<BR>म-नायक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भीम-परा-<BR>क्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing fearful power or<BR>prowess; of terrible strength; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of a man; of a work mentioned in Raghu-<BR>nandana's Saṃskāra-tattva.<BR>—भीम-पाल, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—भीम-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town<BR>situated on the Ganges; [cf. भीम-नगर.]<BR>—भी-<BR>म-बल, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing fearful or tremendous<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">Page0712-a+ 81</a>]<BR>strength; (अस्), m., N. of one of the sons of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra; of one of Devas called Yajña-mush,<BR>see Mahā-bh. Vana-p. 14166.<BR>—भीम-भट, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—भीम-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of<BR>an author.<BR>—भीम-भुज, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भीम-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, of fearful aspect or<BR>appearance; (अस्), m., N. of a monkey.<BR>—भीम-<BR>रथ, अस्, m., N. of a king; of a son of Dhṛta-<BR>rāṣṭra; of Ketu-mat (the father of Divo-dāsa); of<BR>a son of Vikṛti and father of Nava-ratha; of a son<BR>of Kṛṣṇa by Satya-bhāmā; of a Rākṣasa [cf.<BR>भैमरथ]; (आ, ई), f., N. of a river in the<BR>Himālaya mountains; (ई), f. ‘the fearful night,’ N.<BR>of the seventh night in the seventh month of the<BR>seventy-seventh year of life (supposed to be the<BR>ordinary period of human life; a person after this<BR>period is thought to be arrived at dotage and<BR>exempt from all religious observances; भीम-रथी<BR>is probably for भीम-रात्री or for Prākṛt भीम-<BR>रत्ती; cf. काल-रात्री).<BR>—भीम-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>of terrible form, of fearful aspect.<BR>—भीम-विक्रम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of terrible prowess, tremendous in power<BR>or strength; (अस्), m., N. of one of the sons of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—भीम-विक्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fear-<BR>fully powerful or courageous; (अस्), m. a lion.<BR>—भीम-विग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, of fearful form, ter-<BR>rific in appearance, gigantic.<BR>—भीम-वेग, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, of fearful or tremendous speed, terribly swift<BR>or impetuous; (अस्), m., N. of one of the sons of<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; of a Dānava.<BR>—भीम-वेग-रव,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, of dreadful speed and sound, fearful in<BR>velocity and noise; (अस्), m., N. of one of the sons<BR>of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—भीम-शङ्कर, अम्, n., scil.<BR>लिङ्ग, N. of one of the twelve most sacred Liṅgas.<BR>—भीम-शर, अस्, m. ‘having fearful arrows,’ N.<BR>of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR>—भीम-शासन, अस्, m.<BR>‘terrible in rule,’ N. of Yama.<BR>—भीम-शाह, अस्,<BR>m. (शाह = شاه ‘the terrible king,’ N. of a king.<BR>—भीम-शुक्ल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भीम-<BR>सिंह-पण्डित, अस्, m., N. of a learned man and<BR>poet.<BR>—भीम-सेन, अस्, m. ‘having a terrible<BR>army,’ N. of a brother of Janam-ejaya; of a son of<BR>Janam-ejaya; of a son of Ṛkṣa; of the second son<BR>of Pāṇḍu [cf. भीम]; of a Deva-gandharva; of a<BR>Yakṣa; of a king; of a grammarian; of a phy-<BR>sician; a kind of camphor; [cf. भैमसेनि, भै-<BR>मसेन्य.]<BR>—भीमसेन-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of Bhīmasena.<BR>—भीम-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a Brāhman.<BR>—भीमाकर (˚म-आक्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—भीमा-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भीमाद्य्-उपाख्यान, अम्, n., N. of the fifteenth<BR>chapter of the Vāsiṣṭha-rāmāyaṇa, commonly called<BR>Yoga-vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—भीमेश (˚म-ईश˚) or भीमे-<BR>श्वर (˚म-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a place sacred to<BR>Śiva.<BR>—भीमेश्वर-तीर्थ and भीमेश्वर-मा-<BR>कात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of two chapters of the Revā-<BR>māhātmya of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—भीमैकादशी<BR>(˚म-एक्˚), f., N. of the eleventh day in the light<BR>half of the month Māgha; [cf. भीम-द्वादशी.]<BR>—भीमोत्तर (˚म-उत्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Kum-<BR>bhāṇḍa.<BR>—भीमोदरी (˚म-उद्˚), f. an epithet of<BR>Umā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0711-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमक
भीमक, अस्, m., N. of a demon; (also read<BR>भीषक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमयु
भीमयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. fearful, dreadful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमर|भीमरं|भीमरः
भीमर, अम्, n. war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमल
भीमल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = भीम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरक
भीरक, अस्, m. a various reading for भीरुक, a<BR>kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरु|भीरुः
भीरु, उस्, उस्, or ऊस्, उ, fearful, timid, cowardly,<BR>(opposed to शूर); fearing, afraid of (with abl.,<BR>e. g. मरणाद् भीरुः, afraid of death; or at the<BR>end of a comp., e. g. प्रतिज्ञा-भङ्ग-भीरु, afraid<BR>of breaking a promise); (उस्), m. a jackal [cf. फेरु];<BR>a tiger; a kind of sugar-cane; (उस्, ऊस्), f. a timid<BR>woman; a shadow; a goat; a centipede; Solanum<BR>Jacquini or a sort of prickly nightshade; the plant<BR>Asparagus Racemosus, (in some of these last senses<BR>said to be also m.); (उ), n. silver.<BR>—भीरु-चेतस्,<BR>आस्, m. ‘timid-hearted,’ a deer; [cf. भीरु-हृदय.]<BR>—भीरु-जन, अस्, m. one whose servants are<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">Page0712-b+ 81</a>]<BR>cowards.<BR>—भीरु-ता, f. or भीरु-त्व, अम्, n. fear-<BR>fulness, timidity, cautiousness, cowardice; natural<BR>cowardice (as of a tiger, cf. भीरु, col. 1).<BR>—भीरु-<BR>पत्त्री, f. Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>—भीरु-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, fearful, terrible, frightful.<BR>—भीरु-योध,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having cowardly soldiers, possessing a<BR>cowardly garrison.<BR>—भीरु-रन्ध्र, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>a fearful chasm,’ an oven, a furnace.<BR>—भीरु-सत्त्व,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having a timid nature, fearful, timid.<BR>—भीरु-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, timid-hearted, fearful,<BR>timid; (अस्), m. a deer; [cf. भीरु-चेतस्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुक|भीरुकं|भीरुकः
भीरुक, अस्, आ, अम्, fearful, timid, timorous,<BR>cowardly; afraid; shy; formidable; (अस्), m. an<BR>owl; a bear [cf. भीलुक]; a kind of sugar-cane,<BR>(also written भीरक); N. of a man; (अम्), n. a<BR>wood, forest.<BR>—भीरुक-जन, अस्, m. one whose<BR>servants are cowards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुण
भीरुण, अस्, आ, अम्, terrific, &c. See अ-भ्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलु|भीलुः
भीलु = भीरु, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलुक|भीलुकः
भीलुक, अस्, आ, अम्, = भीरुक above; (अस्), m.<BR>a bear; [cf. भल्लूक, भीरुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषक
भीषक, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus.), N. of one of<BR>Śiva's attendants [cf. भीमक]; (इका), f., N. of a<BR>goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषण|भीषणः
भीषण, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the Caus.), terrifying,<BR>frightening, causing alarm, terrific, awful, formidable,<BR>horrible, (often at the end of a comp., e. g. शत्रु-<BR>भ्˚, terrifying an enemy); (अस्), m. the sentiment<BR>of horror (in poetical composition); N. of a form of<BR>Bhairava (= Yama); an epithet of Śiva; the olibanum<BR>tree, Boswellia Thurifera; the plant Phœnix Paludosa<BR>(= हिन्ताल); a pigeon, dove; N. of a Rākṣasa;<BR>(आ), f., N. of a goddess, (probably a form of Durgā);<BR>(अम्), n. the act of terrifying or frightening, causing<BR>alarm or horror; anything which excites terror.<BR>—भीषण-त्व, अम्, n. terribleness, horribleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषणक
भीषणक, अस्, इका, अम्, = भीषण, terrify-<BR>ing, frightening, intimidating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषयमाण
भीषयमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, terrifying, fright-<BR>ening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषा
1. भीषा, f. the act of terrifying, frightening,<BR>intimidation, terror, fright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषा
2. भीषा, ind. (perhaps contracted fr. भियसा,<BR>or inst. c. of भीस् = 2. भी), Ved. from fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषित
भीषित, अस्, आ, अम्, terrified, frightened, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषिदास
भीषि-दास, अस्, m., N. of the man under whose<BR>patronage Nārāyaṇa's commentary on the Gīta-<BR>govinda was composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्म|भीष्मं|भीष्मः
भीष्म, अस्, आ, अम्, = भीम, terrible, horrible,<BR>terrific, fearful; (अस्), m. the sentiment of horror as<BR>the object of poetical composition; an epithet of<BR>Śiva (Rudra); a Rākṣasa, imp, goblin; N. of a<BR>son of Śāntanu and Gaṅgā, (he is an important<BR>personage in the Mahā-bhārata, being the half<BR>brother of both Vicitra-vīrya and Vyāsa, — Śāntanu,<BR>who was a descendant of Bharata, having had his<BR>son Vicitra-vīrya by his legitimate wife Satyavatī,<BR>but Bhīṣma by Gaṅgā before his marriage; when<BR>Vicitra-vīrya died childless, Bhīṣma undertook the<BR>government of Hastinā-pur, and brought up his three<BR>nephews, the sons of his half brother Vyāsa, viz.<BR>Dhṛta-rāṣṭra, Pāṇḍu, and Vidura; whence he is<BR>sometimes called their father; he took the side of<BR>his grand-nephews, the sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra, against<BR>the sons of Pāṇḍu; he was a warrior renowned for<BR>his continence, wisdom, bravery, and fidelity to his<BR>word); (आस्), m. pl. the race or followers of Bhīṣma;<BR>(अम्), n. horror, horribleness, the property of excit-<BR>ing fear or terror.<BR>—भीष्म-गरिजित-घोष-<BR>स्वर-राज, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha; [cf. भीष्म-<BR>स्वर-राज.]<BR>—भीष्म-जननी, f. ‘mother of<BR>Bhīṣma,’ an epithet of the Ganges.<BR>—भीष्म-<BR>पञ्चक, अम्, n. ‘five days sacred to Bhīṣma,’ the<BR>five days from the eleventh to the fifteenth in the light<BR>half of the month Kārttika.<BR>—भीष्मपञ्चक-<BR>व्रत, अम्, n., N. of the sixty-third chapter of the<BR>Bhaviṣyottara-Purāṇa.<BR>—भीष्म-पर्वन्, अ, n.,<BR>N. of the sixth book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—भीष्-<BR>म-मुक्ति-प्रदायक, अस्, m. ‘giving release to<BR>Bhīṣma,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—भीष्म-रत्न-परी-<BR>क्षा, f. trial of the jewel of Bhīṣma.<BR>—भीष्म-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">Page0712-c+ 71</a>]<BR>सू, ऊस्, f. ‘mother of Bhīṣma,’ an epithet of the<BR>Ganges.<BR>—भीष्म-स्तव-राज, अस्, m. ‘Bhīṣma's<BR>hymn to Kṛṣṇa,’ N. of the forty-seventh chapter of<BR>the twelfth book of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—भीष्म-<BR>स्वर-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of terrible sounds,’ N. of<BR>a Buddha; [cf. भीष्म-गर्जित-घोष-स्वर-<BR>राज.]<BR>—भीष्माष्टमी (˚म-अष्˚), f. the eighth<BR>day in the light half of the month Māgha (when<BR>there is a festival sacred to Bhīṣma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मक|भीष्मकः
भीष्मक, अस्, m. Bhīṣma, the son of Śāntanu<BR>(used contemptuously); N. of a king (the father of<BR>Rukmiṇī who was carried off by Kṛṣṇa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेतव्य
भेतव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be feared or dreaded, to<BR>be apprehended, (the neuter is used impersonally,<BR>e. g. न भेतव्यम्, it is not to be feared, i. e. one<BR>need not fear; often with abl. or gen., e. g. न<BR>तस्मात् or तस्य भेतव्यम्, one need not be afraid<BR>of him.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेय
भेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be feared, (the neut. may<BR>be used impersonally, e. g. अरेर् भेयम्, one must<BR>fear an enemy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीणी
भीणी भीणी, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs<BR>attending on Skanda, (in Mahā-bh. Śalya-p. 2645<BR>also read भीती.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमरिका
भीमरिका भीमरिका, f., N. of a daughter<BR>of Kṛṣṇa by Satya-bhāmā; (also read भीमनिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीर
भीर भीर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(incorrectly for आभीर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरक
भीरक भीरक. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुकच्छ
भीरुकच्छ भीरुकच्छ, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (probably for भरुकच्छ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलभूषणा
भीलभूषणा भील-भूषणा. See भिल्ल-<BR>भूषणा, p. 711, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलु|भीलुः
भीलु भीलु. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषक
भीषक भीषक, भीषण, भीषा, भीष्म.<BR>See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषटाचार्य
भीषटाचार्य भीषटाचार्य (?), अस्, m., N. of<BR>an author mentioned in Raghu-nandana's Saṃskāra-<BR>tattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भु
भु भु, उस्, उस्, उ, = भू, existing, being,<BR>becoming, produced, (at the end of some comps.,<BR>cf. अग्नि-भु, प्र-भु, स्वयम्-भु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुःखार
भुःखार भुःखार, N. of a country in<BR>Independent Tartary, Bokhāra; [cf. भूःखार.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्
भुक् भुक्, ind., Ved. an exclamation of<BR>surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्कभूपाल
भुक्कभूपाल भुक्क-भूपाल, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त|भुक्तं
भुक्त भुक्त, भुक्ति. See p. 713, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुग्न|भुग्नः
भुग्न भुग्न. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुङ्
भुङ् भुङ्, a syllable inserted in certain<BR>Sāmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
भुज् 1. भुज्, cl. 6. P. भुजति, बुभोज,<BR>भोक्तुम्, to bend, curve, turn round,<BR>make crooked: Pass. भुज्यते, to be bent, to<BR>incline one's self; [cf. Gr. φεύγ-ω, φυγ-ή, φύζα,<BR>φυγἀ-ς, φύξ-ις, φύξι-μο-ς, probably φυγών from<BR>φυγών: Lat. fug-i-o, fug-a, fug-ax, fugitivu-s,<BR>fugare: Goth. biug-an: Angl. Sax. big-an,<BR>bug-an, beág, beagrian, boga, eln-boga, el-<BR>boga: Old Germ. baug, bogo, elin-bogo, buoc,<BR>būh: Mod. Germ. bieg-en: Eng. bow, elbow:<BR>Slav. be†g-a, ‘I flee;’ be†g-l-ĭ-c-ĭ, ‘a deserter:’ Lith.<BR>be†g-u, ‘I flee, run;’ bug-ti, ‘to be afraid;’ baug-<BR>ù-s, ‘fearful, timid:’ Hib. bog-aim, ‘I put in<BR>motion;’ bogha, ‘bow;’ boghaighim, ‘I bend;’<BR>boghadoir, ‘an archer.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुग्न|भुग्नः
भुग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, bent, crooked, distorted;<BR>curved; bending, stooping, bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
2. भुज्, क्, क्, क्, in त्रि-भ्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज|भुजः
भुज, अस्, आ, m. f. the arm, = 1. बाहु; (often at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-a" target="_blank">Page0713-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the end of an adj. comp., cf. चतुर्-भ्˚, दश-भ्˚,<BR>भद्र-भ्˚); = पाणि, कर, the hand; (अस्), m. a<BR>bending, bend, curve; an arm or branch; the trunk<BR>(of an elephant); a side (of a triangle or of any<BR>mathematical figure; प्रति-भुज, the opposite<BR>side); the base of a triangle; (in astronomy) the<BR>base of a shadow; the supplement of two or four<BR>right angles or the complement of three right angles;<BR>(आ), f. a winding; = 1. भोग, the coil of a snake;<BR>[cf. perhaps Lat. pug-nus for fug-nus, ‘a fist.’]<BR>—भुज-कोटर, अस्, m. the armpit.<BR>—भुज-ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘going crookedly or in a curve,’ = भुजङ्ग,<BR>a snake; (ई), f. a female snake; a species of shrub,<BR>= सर्पिणी; [cf. भुजङ्गी.]<BR>—भुजग-दारण,<BR>अस्, m. ‘snake-destroyer,’ an epithet of Garuḍa;<BR>(this and similar compounds may be applied to any<BR>of the natural enemies of the serpent race, as the<BR>Ardea, peacock, ichneumon, &c.)<BR>—भुजग-पति,<BR>इस्, m. the king of snakes.<BR>—भुजग-पुषप, अस्,<BR>m. = भुजङ्ग-पुष्प, q. v.<BR>—भुजग-भोजिन्, ई,<BR>m. ‘snake-eater,’ a peacock; Garuḍa.<BR>—भुजग-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘snake-king,’ an epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>—भुजगराजय, Nom. A. भुजगराजयते,<BR>&c., to become or act like the king of snakes.<BR>—भुजग-वलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bracelet con-<BR>sisting of a serpent.<BR>—भुजग-शिशु-सृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, going or moving like a young snake; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of a metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯, ˘˘.<BR>—भु-<BR>जगान्तक (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘snake-destroyer,’ an<BR>epithet of Garuḍa; [cf. भुजग-दारण.]<BR>—भु-<BR>जगाभोजिन् (˚ग-आभ्˚), ई, m. ‘feeding on snakes,’<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—भुजगाशन (˚ग-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘snake-eater,’ Garuḍa.<BR>—भुजगेन्द्र (˚ग-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘snake-king,’ any large snake.<BR>—भुज-<BR>गेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘snake-lord,’ an epithet<BR>of Śeṣa.<BR>—भुजङ्-ग, अस्, m. = भुज-ग, a snake,<BR>serpent, (भुजङ्-ग is said by some to be formed<BR>fr. भुजम् as an indec. part. of rt. 1. भुज्); a term<BR>for the number eight; the paramour of a prostitute;<BR>the dissolute friend of a king; a catamite, lecher; a<BR>species of Daṇḍaka metre; N. of a man; (ई), f. a<BR>female snake, a young female snake; a species of<BR>shrub, = सर्पिणी [cf. भुजगी]; (अम्), n., N. of a<BR>particular metal, (perhaps lead; cf. भुजङ्-गम.)<BR>—भुजङ्ग-कन्या, f. a young female snake.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-घात्नी, f. ‘killing snakes,’ a species<BR>of plant, (commonly called Kankālika, considered as<BR>an antidote and said to be a sort of mustard; =<BR>सूक्रि, सर्पाक्षी, क्षुत्-करी, स्पृहा.)<BR>—भुजङ्ग-<BR>जिह्वा, f. ‘snake's tongue,’ a species of plant (=<BR>महा-समङ्गा).<BR>—भुजङ्ग-दमनी, f. a species<BR>of plant (= नकुलेष्टा).<BR>—भुजङ्ग-पर्णिनी, f.<BR>a species of plant (= नाग-दमनी).<BR>—भुजङ्ग-<BR>पिहित, अस्, आ, अम्, covered with serpents.<BR>—भु-<BR>जङ्ग-पुष्प, a species of plant, = नाग-पुष्प;<BR>[cf. भुजग-पुष्प.]<BR>—भुजङ्ग-प्रयात, अम्,<BR>n. ‘snake-like course,’ N. of a metre, four times<BR>˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯¯˘¯¯.<BR>—भुजङ्गप्रयात-स्तोत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a hymn addressed to Śiva, composed<BR>in the Bhujaṅga-prayāta metre, and said to be by<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—भुजङ्गप्रयाताष्टक (˚त-<BR>अष्˚), अम्, n., N. of a piece of poetry in praise of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-भ, अम्, n. ‘snake-asterism,’<BR>N. of the Nakṣatra Āśleṣā.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-भुज्, क्,<BR>m. ‘snake-eater,’ a peacock; an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-भोजिन्, ई, m. ‘feeding on snakes,’ a<BR>particular species of snake, the large Indian serpent<BR>(Boa Constrictor), = राज-सर्प; an epithet of Ga-<BR>ruḍa.<BR>—भुजाङ्-गम, अस्, m. = भुजङ्-ग, a<BR>snake, serpent; a term for the number eight; an<BR>epithet of Rāhu; N. of a Nāga; (आ), f. a female<BR>snake, a female snake-demon; (अम्), n. lead.<BR>—भु-<BR>जङ्ग-लता, f. betel-pepper (= नाग-वल्ली).<BR>—भु-<BR>जङ्ग-विजृम्भित, अम्, n. a species of the Utkṛti<BR>metre.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-शिशु, उस्, m. a species of Vṛhatī<BR>metre.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-सङ्गता, f. a species of metre,<BR>four times ˘˘¯˘¯˘¯˘¯.<BR>—भुजङ्ग-हन्, आ,<BR>m. ‘snake-killer,’ Garuḍa.<BR>—भुजङ्गाक्षी (˚ग-<BR>अक्षि), f. the ichneumon plant, = नकुलेष्टा; =<BR>रास्ना.<BR>—भुजङ्गाख्य (˚ग-आख्˚), अस्, m. the<BR>plant Mesua Roxburghii (= नाग-केशर).<BR>—भु-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-b" target="_blank">Page0713-b+ 80</a>]<BR>जङ्गिका, f., N. of a village.<BR>—भुजङ्गेद्र (˚ग-<BR>इन्˚), अस्, m. the king of snakes.<BR>—भुजङ्गेरित<BR>(˚ग-ईर्˚), अम्, n. a kind of metre.<BR>—भुजङ्गेश<BR>(˚ग-ईश), अस्, m. ‘snake-lord,’ an epithet of Piṅga-<BR>laka.<BR>—भुज-ज्या, f. (in astronomy) the base sine.<BR>—भुजज्या-फल, अम्, n. the result from the<BR>base sine.<BR>—भुज-दण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘arm-<BR>staff,’ an arm like a staff, the arm; [cf. बाहु-<BR>दण्ड.]<BR>—भुज-दल, अस्, m. ‘arm-leaf,’ the<BR>hand; [cf. भुजा-दल.]<BR>—भुज-नगर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a town.<BR>—भुज-प्रतिभुज, अम्, n. opposite<BR>sides in a plane figure.<BR>—भुज-फल, अम्, n. =<BR>बाहु-फल, the result from the base sine.<BR>—भुज-<BR>बल, अम्, n. strength of arm; (अस्), m., N. of an<BR>author, (also called भुज-बल-भीम.)<BR>—भुज-<BR>मध्य, अम्, n. ‘the part between the arms,’ the<BR>breast.<BR>—भुज-मूल, अम्, n. ‘the root of the arm,’<BR>the shoulder.<BR>—भुज-यष्टि, इस्, m. f. = भुज-<BR>दण्ड.<BR>—भुज-वीर्य, अम्, n. vigour of arm.<BR>—भुज-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing strong arms;<BR>[cf. बाहु-शालिन्.]<BR>—भुज-शिखर, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>head of the arm,’ the shoulder.<BR>—भुज-शिरस्, अस्,<BR>n. ‘the head of the arm,’ the shoulder, the shoulder-<BR>blade.<BR>—भुज-संश्रय, अस्, m. going for pro-<BR>tection to the arms, taking refuge in the arms (of<BR>another).<BR>—भुज-सूत्र, अम्, n. the base sine.<BR>—भुजा-कण्ट, अस्, m. (कण्ट = कण्टक), ‘hand-<BR>thorn,’ a finger-nail.<BR>—भुजाग्र (˚ज-अग्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘end of the arm,’ the hand; the shoulder.<BR>—भुजा-<BR>दल, अस्, m. ‘arm-leaf,’ the hand (= भुज-दल).<BR>—भुजान्तर (˚ज-अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘the interval or<BR>part between the arms or between the shoulders,’ the<BR>breast, chest; (अम्), ind. between the arms, in the<BR>embrace.<BR>—भुजान्तराल (˚ज-अन्˚), अम्, n. = भु-<BR>जान्तर.<BR>—भुजापीड (˚ज-आप्˚), अस्, m. clasping or<BR>embracing in the arms.<BR>—भुजा-मध्य, अम्, n.<BR>‘the middle of the arm,’ the elbow.<BR>—भुजा-मूल,<BR>अम्, n. = भुज-मूल, q. v. the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0712-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजि|भुजिः
1. भुजि, इस्, f., Ved. clasping round, enfolding, fold,<BR>(at the end of a comp., e. g. दश-भ्˚, tenfold; cf.<BR>शत-भ्˚, त्रि-भुज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यु|भुज्युः
1. भुज्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. capable of being<BR>bent, pliant, flexible; easily turned or guided (said of<BR>a chariot; according to Sāy. = रक्षक, see rt. 3.<BR>भुज्); (उस्), m., N. of a son of Tugra saved from<BR>shipwreck by the Aśvins; of Bhujyu Lāhyāyani;<BR>(perhaps) a snake or viper; (according to some<BR>भुज्यु also) = भाण्ड, भाजन, a pot, vessel; =<BR>भोजन, food; = अग्नि, fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
भुज् 3. भुज् [cf. rt. भक्ष्], cl. 7. P. A.<BR>भुनक्ति, भुङ्क्ते (3rd pl. भुञ्जते,<BR>ep. also 3rd sing. भुञ्जते, Ved. भोजते), Impf.<BR>अभुनक्, अभुङ्क्त, Pot. भुञ्ज्यात् (ep. भुञ्जीयात्<BR>and भुञ्जेत्), भुञ्जीत, Impv. भुनक्तु, भुङ्क्-<BR>ताम्, Perf. बुभोज, बुभुजे (1st pl. irreg. बुभुज्-<BR>महे, 3rd pl. irreg. बुभुज्रिरे), 2nd Fut. भोक्ष्-<BR>यति, -ते, Aor. अभौक्षीत्, अभुक्त (Ved. forms<BR>are भोजम्, भुजेम, भुक्षिषीय), भोक्तुम्<BR>(Ved. Inf. भुजे, भोजसे), to enjoy, enjoy a meal,<BR>eat and drink, eat, consume, (generally A., especially<BR>if without an object; in Ved. with inst. of the thing<BR>eaten, but in later Sanskrit with acc.); to possess,<BR>have, make use of; to enjoy carnally (with acc.); to<BR>rule, govern; to suffer, experience, endure; to pass<BR>(as time), live through; (in astronomy) to pass<BR>through, fulfil; to be useful to any person (P. with<BR>acc. Ved.): Pass. भुज्यते, to be enjoyed, to be<BR>eaten; to be possessed; to be brought under the<BR>power of: Caus. भोजयति (also भुञ्जापयति),<BR>-ते, -यितुम्, Aor. अबूभुजत्, to cause to enjoy or<BR>eat, to feed (with double acc. or with acc. of the<BR>person and inst. of the thing, e. g. ताम् अन्नम् or<BR>अन्नेन भोजयाम्-आस, he caused her to eat food):<BR>Desid. बुभुक्षति, -ते, to desire to enjoy or eat, to<BR>be hungry [cf. बुभुक्षु]: Intens. बोभुज्यते, to<BR>be eaten frequently; बोभोक्ति, to eat frequently; [cf.<BR>Lat. fung-or, fru-or, fr. frug-or, fruges, fructus,<BR>frustum, frustra, frutex; Goth. bugjan, biuhts,<BR>biuhti, bruks, brūkjan; Angl. Sax. bycgan, brucan,<BR>bryce; Old Germ. brūchan; Old Island. brūka.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त|भुक्तं
भुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, enjoyed, eaten; used, pos-<BR>sessed; experienced, suffered; passed (as time);<BR>(अम्), n. the thing eaten or enjoyed, food [cf. कु-<BR>भ्˚]; the act of eating; the place where any person<BR>has eaten.<BR>—भुक्त-पूर्विन्, ई, इणी, इ, one who<BR>has eaten before.<BR>—भुक्त-भोग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has enjoyed an enjoyment or suffered a<BR>suffering; made use of, used, employed, enjoyed.<BR>—भुक्त-मात्रे, ind. immediately on having eaten.<BR>—भुक्त-वृद्धि, इस्, f. the swelling of food (in<BR>the stomach).<BR>—भुक्त-शेष or भुक्त-शेषक<BR>or भुक्त-समुज्झित, अम्, n. what is left after<BR>eating, the remnants of a meal, leavings, orts.<BR>—भुक्त-सुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, sleeping after a meal.<BR>—भुक्तासव (˚त-अस्˚), अस्, m. (in astronomy) the<BR>equivalent in respirations of the part of the sign<BR>traversed.<BR>—भुक्तोच्छिष्ट (˚त-उच्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>rejected leavings or remnants of food (= फेलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तवत्|भुक्तवन्त्
भुक्तवत्, आन्, अती, अत्, one who has eaten or<BR>possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्ति|भुक्तिः
भुक्ति, इस्, f. the act of enjoying or eating, enjoy-<BR>ment, eating; fruition, possession, usufruct; food; (in<BR>astronomy) the daily motion of a planet [cf. पक्ष-<BR>भ्˚, मास-भ्˚]; a limit [cf. तीर-भ्˚].<BR>—भुक्ति-<BR>पात्र, अम्, n. a dish for food.<BR>—भुक्ति-प्रद, अस्,<BR>m. the plant Phaseolus Mungo (= मुद्ग).<BR>—भुक्-<BR>ति-मती, f., N. of a river; (also read मुक्ति-मती.)<BR>—भुक्ति-वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, excluded from enjoy-<BR>ment, not allowed to be enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त्वा
भुक्त्वा, ind. having enjoyed or eaten; having<BR>possessed.<BR>—भुक्त्वा-सुहित, अस्, आ, अम्, satisfied<BR>after eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
4. भुज्, क्, f. enjoyment; profit, advantage, wel-<BR>fare, usefulness; (क्, क्, क्), enjoying, eating, consum-<BR>ing, an eater, &c., (at the end of comps., cf. अन्न-<BR>भ्˚, अमृत-भ्˚, क्रव्य-भ्˚); possessing, ruling,<BR>(in comp. with words meaning ‘earth,’ e. g. काश्यपी-<BR>भ्˚, a ruler of the earth, i. e. king; cf. क्षिति-भ्˚);<BR>experiencing, enduring, suffering, suffering punish-<BR>ment for (e. g. किल्विष-भ्˚, suffering for a crime);<BR>passing (as time), fulfilling; useful to, serviceable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजि|भुजिः
2. भुजि, इस्, f., Ved. enjoyment, favour, (Sāy.<BR>= भोग, परि-भोग); (इस्, इस्, इ), one who causes<BR>enjoyment or grants favours, one who protects; (ई),<BR>m. du. an epithet of the two Aśvins, (Sāy. = हवि-<BR>षाम् भोक्तारौ, eaters of the oblations); (इस्), m.<BR>fire, (see Uṇādi-s. IV. 141.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजिष्य|भुजिष्यः
भुजिष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, granting food, useful<BR>(Ved.); free, independent; (अस्), m. a slave, servant<BR>[cf. Uṇādi-s. IV. 178]; a companion; a string worn<BR>round the wrist (= हस्त-सूत्रक, which some in-<BR>terpret as a Dvandva comp., ‘the hand’ and ‘a string’);<BR>(आ), f. a female slave or servant, maid-servant, slave-<BR>girl, hand-maid, (perhaps in general) any woman<BR>dependent on or working for others; a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्मन्
भुज्मन्, आ, आ, अ, Ved. producing or giving food;<BR>(Sāy. = सर्वेषाम् भोजयितृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यमान
भुज्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being enjoyed or eaten;<BR>being possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यु|भुज्युः
2. भुज्यु, उस्, m. (for 1. see col. 2), eating;<BR>= भोजन, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुञ्जत्
भुञ्जत्, अन्, अती, अत्, enjoying, eating, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुञ्जान|भुञ्जानः
भुञ्जान, अस्, आ, अम्, enjoying, eating, feeding<BR>on, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तव्य|भोक्तव्यं
भोक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be enjoyed, to be<BR>eaten; to be used or employed, to be made use of;<BR>to be possessed; to be governed or ruled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तुकाम
भोक्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the Inf.), wishing<BR>to enjoy or eat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृ
भोक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, an enjoyer, eater, feeder<BR>[cf. प्रातर्-भ्˚]; enjoying, eating; possessing; one<BR>who employs or makes use of; one who feels or<BR>experiences (joy, sorrow, &c.), feeling, experienc-<BR>ing; (ता), m. a possessor; a king, ruler; a husband;<BR>a lover.<BR>—भोक्तृ-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being and<BR>enjoyer or eater, the being a possessor or feeler;<BR>enjoyment, possession; perception.<BR>—भोक्तृ-शक्ति,<BR>इस्, f. the faculty of the soul as the enjoyer and pos-<BR>sessor of nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्ष्यमाण
भोक्ष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being about to enjoy<BR>or eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0713-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्य|भोग्यं
भोग्य, भोजनीय, भोज्य, &c. See p. 723.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजिङ्ग
भुजिङ्ग भुजिङ्ग, आस्, m. pl,. N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुट्ट
भुट्ट भुट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भुट्ट-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town built by Bhuṭṭa.<BR>—भुट्-<BR>टेश्वर (˚ट-ईश्˚), N. of a temple (?) built by Bhuṭṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुट्व
भुट्व, a various reading for भुट्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुण्ड्|भुंड्
भुण्ड् भुण्ड् [cf. rt. हुण्ड्], cl. 1. A. भुण्-<BR>डते, &c., to support, maintain; to support, maintain; to select;<BR>to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुमन्यु
भुमन्यु भुमन्यु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Bharata; of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुय्य
भुय्य भुय्य, अस्, m., N. of a person men-<BR>tioned in Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VI. 264.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुर्
भुर् भुर् (a Vedic rt. not occurring in<BR>the Dhātu-pāṭha and regarded by Sāy. as a<BR>Vedic form of rt. भृ, to bear), P. A. भुरति, -ते,<BR>&c., to move rapidly, make a short quick move-<BR>ment, be active; to wish for, (Sāy. भुरन्त =<BR>इच्छन्ति). Intens. जर्भुरीति (Pres. part. जर्भु-<BR>राण), to shoot out in flames (as fire); [cf. भूर्णि;<BR>Gr. πορφύρω; Lat. fur-ere.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरण
भुरण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. active, (Sāy. = भर्तृ<BR>or पोषक, as if fr. rt. भृ); (आ), m. du. epithet<BR>of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरण्य
भुरण्य, Nom. P. भुरण्यति, &c., Ved. to<BR>be active, move restlessly; to stir, (Sāy. = गच्छति<BR>or पोषयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरण्यत्
भुरण्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. being active, stirring,<BR>restless; (Sāy. = धारयत्, supporting; पोषयत्,<BR>nourishing; or गन्तुम् इच्छत्, wishing to go.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरण्यु|भुरण्युः
भुरण्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. active, stirring, rest-<BR>less, uneasy; eager; (Sāy. = हविषाम् भर्तृ,<BR>bearer of the oblations, as an epithet of Agni; ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. II. 15 = क्षिप्र, quick); (ऊ),<BR>m. du. epithet of the Aśvins; (Sāy. = सर्वत्र गन्-<BR>तारौ or यज्ञस्य भर्तारौ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरमाण
भुरमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. moving actively,<BR>struggling; (Sāy. = भ्रियमाण, being borne.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुर्वणि
भुर्वणि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. active, stirring, restless,<BR>uneasy, impatient; (according to Sāy. = अत्तृ, eating,<BR>devouring, as if fr. भुर्व् for rt. भर्व्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुर्वन्
भुर्वन्, Ved. restless motion (of water &c.; but<BR>according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 134, 5, भुर्वणि,<BR>loc. sing. = भरणवति, and may here stand either<BR>for ‘the sacrifice’ which bears oblations &c. or for<BR>‘a cloud’ which bears water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरज्
भुरज् भुरज् (a Vedic verb probably con-<BR>nected with rt. भुर्), A. भुरजते, &c., (perhaps)<BR>to bubble, spout up, (but according to Sāy. भुर-<BR>जन्त in Ṛg-veda IV. 43, 5, = प्राप्नुवन्ति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरिज्
भुरिज् भुरिज्, औ, f. du. (said in Uṇādi-s.<BR>II. 72. to be fr. rt. भृ), Ved. the two arms;<BR>heaven and earth; (in Ṛg-veda VIII. 4, 16) a pair<BR>of scissors or shears, (but according to Sāy. भु-<BR>रिजोः here = बाह्वोः, of the two arms); a carpen-<BR>ter's vice or implement consisting of two arms, (but<BR>in Ṛg-veda IV. 2, 14, Sāy. makes भुरिजौ = बा-<BR>हू); (क्), f. the earth; N. of a particular metre in<BR>which a Pāda has one or two superfluous syllables;<BR>N. of certain insertions in liturgical formularies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरुण्ड|भुरुण्डः
भुरुण्ड भुरुण्ड, अस्, m. a species of animal<BR>[cf. भारण्ड, भारुण्ड, भेरुण्ड]; N. of a<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुर्भुरिका
भुर्भुरिका भुर्भुरिका and भुर्भुरी, f. a<BR>sort of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुव|भुवः
भुव भुव, भुवत्, भुवन, भुवन्यु,<BR>भुवस्, &c. See col. 3, and p. 715, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुशुण्ड
भुशुण्ड भुशुण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुशुण्डि|भुशुंडि|भुशुंडिः|भुशुण्डिः
भुशुण्डि भुशुण्डि, इस्, or भुशुण्डी, f. a kind<BR>of weapon, (perhaps a kind of fire-arms; sometimes<BR>incorrectly written भुषुण्डि and भूशुण्डि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
भू 1. भू, cl. 1. P. A. भवति, -ते, Impf.<BR>अभवत्, अभवत, Pot. भवेत्, भवेत,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-b" target="_blank">Page0714-b+ 81</a>]<BR>Impv. भवतु, भवताम् (Ved. 2nd sing. बोधि<BR>[but referred by Sāy. to rt. 1. बुध्], 3rd sing. भूतु;<BR>in Ṛg-veda 1. 94, 12, भवतात्), Perf. बभूव,<BR>बभूवे (according to Vopa-deva VIII. 33, Pass. and<BR>Impers. बभूवे or बुभूवे, 2nd sing. बभूविथ,<BR>Ved. बभूथ, 2nd pl. बभूव, part. बभूवस्,<BR>बभूवुषी, f.; in Ṛg-veda 1. 27, 2, बभूयात् =<BR>भवतु), 1st Fut. भविता, 2nd Fut. भविष्यति,<BR>-ते (ep. 2nd pl. भविष्यध्वम्), Aor. अभूत्,<BR>अभविष्ट (3rd pl. अभूवन्, Ved. forms भुवस्,<BR>भुवत्), Prec. भूयात्, भविषीष्ट, Cond. अभ-<BR>विष्यत्, अभविष्यत, भवितुम् (Ved. भवितोस्.<BR>भुवे), to become, be, (नाभिजानामि भवेद् एवं<BR>न वेति, I do not know whether it may be so or not);<BR>to be in any state or condition, (कथं स भ-<BR>विष्यति, in what state will he be?); to be born<BR>or produced; to exist, live, (अभून् नृपः, there<BR>lived a king); to remain, stay, abide (e. g. पथि<BR>भव, remain thou or stay thou awhile on the<BR>road, Megha-dūta 30); to arise, spring up, happen,<BR>occur, befall, take place, (यदि संशयो भवेत्,<BR>if a doubt should arise, cf. Manu XII. 108); to be<BR>possible, (according to Pāṇ. III. 3, 146, a future<BR>tense may follow भवति in this sense, e. g. भवति<BR>भवान् याजयिष्यति, it is possible or it may happen<BR>that you will cause a sacrifice to be performed); to<BR>turn out, lead to (with dat., e. g. तन् नाशाय भ-<BR>वति, that leads to destruction; तत् सङ्गमाय<BR>भवति, that leads to union); to serve for, tend or<BR>conduce to (with dat., e. g. तद् दातुर् अनर्थाय<BR>भवति, that conduces to the disadvantage of the<BR>giver); to conduct one's self, behave; to become the<BR>property of any one, belong to (with gen., = ‘to<BR>have, to possess,’ e. g. तस्य भ्राता भवति, of<BR>him there is a brother, i. e. he has a brother); to be<BR>on the side of, assist (with gen., e. g. ये मित्राणां<BR>न भवन्ति, those who do not assist their friends;<BR>or with the affix तस्, e. g. देवा अर्जुन-तो ऽभवन्,<BR>the gods were on the side of Arjuna); to be occupied<BR>with or engaged in (with loc., e. g. तपसि भव,<BR>be thou engaged in, i. e. devote thyself to penance);<BR>to be of importance or consequence, become pros-<BR>perous (Ved.); to turn out well, succeed (Ved.); to<BR>obtain, attain to (Ved., cf. Mahā-bh. Ādi-p. 5366).<BR>The senses of the verb may be almost infinitely<BR>extended when भू is compounded with a preceding<BR>adjective or substantive, the final of which if अ, आ, इ,<BR>अन्, or अस् becomes ई; if उस् or उ, becomes ऊ (e. g.<BR>fr. अग्नि, अग्नी-भू, to become fire; fr. अरुस्, अरू-<BR>भू, to become wounded; fr. एक-मति, एकमती-<BR>भू, to become unanimous; fr. कठोर, कठोरी-<BR>भू, to become sharp; fr. कृष्ण, कृष्णी-भू,<BR>to become black; fr. 1. क्षपण, क्षपणी-भू,<BR>to become a Buddhist mendicant; fr. गो-चर, गो-<BR>चरी-भू, to become visible; fr. जर्जर, जर्जरी-<BR>भू, to decay; fr. तरुणी, तरुणी-भू, to become<BR>a marriageable girl; fr. तीव्र, तीव्री-भू, to become<BR>violent or intense; fr. परिखा, परिखी-भू, to<BR>become a ditch or moat; fr. पर्य्-उत्सुक, पर्युत्-<BR>सुकी-भू, to become sorrowful; fr. प्र-णिधि, प्र-<BR>णिधी-भू, to become a spy; fr. प्रत्य्-अनन्तर,<BR>प्रत्यनन्तरी-भू [also read प्रत्यन्तरी-भू],<BR>to be near; fr. बन्धकी, बन्धकी-भू, to become<BR>a harlot; fr. भस्मन्, भस्मी-भू, to become<BR>ashes; fr. रहस्, रही-भू, to become solitary, &c.).<BR>The senses of भू may also be variously modified<BR>when it is connected with adverbs or with the nega-<BR>tive न (e. g. पृथिवी न भविष्यति, the earth<BR>will not exist, i. e. will perish or be destroyed; पुनर्<BR>भू, to marry again, see Manu IX. 175; cf. आविर्-<BR>भू, प्रादुर्-भू, तिरो-भू, मिथ्या-भू, वृथा-<BR>भू; अन्यथा भू, to become otherwise, i. e. to<BR>be changed or be falsified; अग्रे भू, to be in front,<BR>to precede, &c.). The perfect of भू (बभूव,<BR>&c.) is used after the syllable आम् like the perfect of<BR>the rts. 1. अस् and 1. कृ as an auxiliary to form the<BR>perfect of verbs of the 10th class, derivative verbs,<BR>and others mentioned in Gram. r. 385 [cf. Pāṇini<BR>III. 1, 40]: Pass. भूयते, Aor. अभावि (sometimes<BR>used impersonally, e. g. तैर् भविष्यते, by them<BR>it will be existed, i. e. they will exist): Caus. भाव-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-c" target="_blank">Page0714-c+ 81</a>]<BR>यति (rarely A. -ते), -यितुम्, Aor. अबीभवत्, to<BR>cause to be or become or exist; to bring into exist-<BR>ence or being, call into life; to originate, produce,<BR>effect, cause, create; to cherish, support, protect,<BR>preserve, foster, animate, enliven, encourage; to<BR>devote one's self to, addict one's self to; to manifest,<BR>make manifest, exhibit; to change, transform; to<BR>purify; to obtain, attain to, get (P. A.); to cause to<BR>exist in the mind, present to the mind, think about,<BR>reflect upon, consider, know; to convince, convict;<BR>to prove, substantiate, establish; to mingle, mix; to<BR>soak, saturate, steep; to perfume: Pass. of Caus.<BR>भाव्यते, to be caused to be, to be preserved: Desid.<BR>of Caus. बिभावयिषति, to wish to cause to be, &c.:<BR>Desid. बुभूषति, &c., to wish to become or be:<BR>Intens. बोभूयते, बोभवीति, बोभोति, &c. (Impv.<BR>3rd sing. Ved. बोभूतु), to be or become very fre-<BR>quently, to be generally, to take various forms (with<BR>acc., Ved.); [cf. Zend bū, ‘to be, become:’ Gr.<BR>φύ-ω, ἔ-φῡ-ν, ἔ-φῡ-ς, ἔ-φῡ = अभूवम्, अभूस्,<BR>अभूत्, φύ-ο-μαι, φυ-ή, φύ-σι-ς, φῦ-μα, φυ-τό-ς,<BR>φυτεύ-ω, φῦ-λο-ν, φυ-λή, φῖ-τυ, φί-τυ-μα, φι-τύ-ω,<BR>φοι-τά-ω(?), φώς, gen. φωτός, ‘the generating one,’<BR>probably = भवत्: Lat. fu-a-m, fu-i, fu-turu-s,<BR>fo-re, fu-tu-o, -bam (in amabam) = अभवम्, -bo,<BR>bimus = भविष्यामि, भविष्यामस्, fe-tu-s, fe-<BR>cundu-s, fe-nus, fe-nu-m: Osc. Fu-tri-s: Old.<BR>Sax. biu-m: Angl. Sax. beo-m: Old Germ. bi-m,<BR>‘I am:’ Mod. Germ. bin: Goth. bau-an, ‘to<BR>dwell;’ bau-ains = भवन, ‘a dwelling:’ Slav.<BR>by-ti: Lith. bu-ti, ‘to be;’ bù-ta-s, ‘a house:’<BR>Hib. fuilim, ‘I am.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव|भवं|भवः
भव, भवत्, भवतु, भवित, &c. See<BR>p. 702, cols. 1, 2, 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव|भावः
भाव, भावनीय, भावयत्, भावित, भाव्य,<BR>&c. See pp. 707, 708.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुव|भुवः
भुव, अस्, m., Ved. (according to Mahī-dhara)<BR>an epithet of Agni; = भुवस्, atmosphere [cf. भु-<BR>व-भर्तृ, भूर्-भुव-कर]; a fungus, mush-<BR>room (?).<BR>—भुव-पति, इस्, m., Ved. the lord of<BR>the atmosphere (as contrasted with भुवन-पति,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—भुव-भर्तृ, ता, m. (according to a<BR>commentator) the lord of the atmosphere (as con-<BR>trasted with भू-पति, the lord of the earth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवत्
भुवत्, probably an old Pres. part., but occurring<BR>only in the following compounds.<BR>—भुवद्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. ‘giving prosperity;’ (अन्तस्), m.<BR>pl. an epithet of the Ādityas.<BR>—भुवद्-वसु, उस्,<BR>उस्, उ, Ved. (according to the Nirukta) producing<BR>wealth, (but the Pada-pāṭha separates भुवत् from<BR>उअसु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन|भुवनं
भुवन, अम्, n. a being, animated being, living<BR>creature; man, mankind; the world; heaven; earth;<BR>place of being, abode, residence (Ved.); (as a va-<BR>rious reading for भवन), a house; = 2. भावन,<BR>the act of bringing into existence; becoming pros-<BR>perous, prospering (Ved.); water; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a particular month; of a Rudra [cf. भुवनाधीश,<BR>भुवनेश]; of a man; of an Āptya (author of<BR>the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 157).<BR>—भुवन-कोश, अस्,<BR>m. the globe or sphere of the earth, receptacle of<BR>beings.<BR>—भुवन-चन्द्र, अस्, m. ‘moon of the<BR>world,’ N. of a man.<BR>—भुवन-च्यव, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. shaking the world.<BR>—भुवन-ज्ञान, अम्, n.<BR>knowledge of the world.<BR>—भुवन-त्रय, अम्,<BR>n. triad of worlds, the three worlds, viz. heaven,<BR>atmosphere, and earth; [cf. त्रि-भुवन.]<BR>—भु-<BR>वन-द्वय, अम्, n. the two worlds, heaven and<BR>earth.<BR>—भुवन-पति, इस्, m. the lord of beings or<BR>of the world; [cf. भुव-पति.]<BR>—भुवन-पावन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, world-purifying; (ई), f. an epithet of the<BR>Ganges.<BR>—भुवन-प्रतिष्ठा-दान-विधि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of the 152nd chapter of the Bhaviṣyottara-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—भुवन-भर्तृ, ता, m. lord of the<BR>world, supporter of the earth.<BR>—भुवन-मती, f.,<BR>N. of a princess.<BR>—भुवन-मल्ल-वीर, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—भौवन-राज, अस्, m. ‘king of the<BR>world,’ N. of a king.<BR>—भुवन-विन्यास, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of the fortieth chapter of the Kūrma-Purāṇa.<BR>—भुवन-शासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, ruling the world; (ई),<BR>m. a king, prince.<BR>—भुवन-सद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">Page0715-a+ 81</a>]<BR>reposing or situated in the world.<BR>—भुवन-हित,<BR>अम्, n. the welfare of the world.<BR>—भुवनाद्भुत<BR>(˚न-अद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, astonishing the world.<BR>—भु-<BR>वनाधीश or भुवनाधीश्वर (˚न-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of the world,’ N. of a Rudra; [cf. भुव-<BR>नेश.]<BR>—भुवनानन्द (˚न-आन्˚), अस्, m. ‘joy<BR>of the world,’ N. of a man.<BR>—भुवनाभ्युदय<BR>(˚न-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘prosperity of the world,’ N. of<BR>a poem by Śaṅkuka; of the nineteenth chapter of<BR>the Kṛṣṇa-krīḍita.<BR>—भुवनालोकन (˚न-आल्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the act of looking at the earth, the sight of<BR>the world.<BR>—भुवनेश (˚न-ईश˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of<BR>the world,’ N. of a Rudra; of a place; (ई), f., N.<BR>of a goddess.<BR>—भुवनेशानी (˚न-ईश्˚), f. the mis-<BR>tress of the world.<BR>—भुवनेशी-पारिजात, N. of a<BR>work mentioned in Raghu-nandana's Saṃskāra-tattva.<BR>—भुवनेशी-यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a mystical<BR>diagram described in Kṛṣṇānanda's Tantra-sāra.<BR>—भुवनेश्वर (˚न-ईश्˚), अस्, m. a lord of the<BR>earth, king, prince; an epithet of Śiva; (ई), f. ‘mis-<BR>tress of the world,’ N. of several goddesses; (अम्),<BR>n., N. of a temple and city sacred to Śiva.<BR>—भु-<BR>वनेश्वरी-कवच, अम्, n. ‘the armour of the<BR>mistress of the world,’ N. of a chapter in Kṛṣṇā-<BR>nanda's Tantra-sāra.<BR>—भुवनेश्वरी-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—भुवनेश्वरी-पूजा-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a mystical diagram described<BR>in the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—भुवनेश्वरी-रहस्य, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a section of the Rudra-yāmala-tantra.<BR>—भुवने-ष्ठ (भुवने, loc. sing. + स्थ), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. being in the world or in all existing<BR>things.<BR>—भुवनौकस् (˚न-ओक्˚), आ, m. an inha-<BR>bitant of heaven, a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0714-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन्ति
भुवन्ति, इस्, m. a word occurring in Vājasaneyi-<BR>saṃhitā XVI. 19, (according to Mahī-dhara fr. भु-<BR>वं तनोति) = भू-मण्डल-विस्तारकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन्यु|भुवन्युः
भुवन्यु, उस्, m. a master, lord; the sun; the<BR>moon; fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवस्
भुवस्, ind. the atmosphere, ether, sky; a mys-<BR>tical word (being the second of the three Vyāhṛtis<BR>भूर् भुवः स्वर्, uttered by every Brāhman in<BR>commencing his daily prayers, see व्याहृति, and cf.<BR>Manu II. 76; from its being pronounced between<BR>भू, the earth, and स्वर्, heaven, भुवस् is supposed<BR>to mean ‘the atmosphere’ situated between the two;<BR>it was probably originally the pl. of 2. भू, q. v.; in<BR>Hari-vaṃśa 11506, Bhuvas is described as one of the<BR>mind-born sons of Brahmā); the second of the seven<BR>worlds, (according to the system which supposes<BR>seven worlds rising one above the other); N. of the<BR>second and eleventh Kalpa mentioned in the Vāyu-<BR>Purāṇa.<BR>—भुवर्-लोक, अस्, m. one of the divisions<BR>of the universe, the space between the earth and<BR>heaven (frequented by Siddhas and other superhuman<BR>beings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवस्पति
भुवस्-पति, इस्, m. (fr. भुवस्, gen. sing. of 2.<BR>भू), = प्रजा-पति, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुविष्ठ
भुवि-ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. भुवि, loc. sing. of<BR>2. भू + स्थ), standing on the ground (i. e. not<BR>in a chariot), staying or dwelling on the earth, (op-<BR>posed to दिवि-ष्ठ, q. v.)<BR>—भुवि-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्,<BR>touching the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुविस्
भुविस्, m. (?), the sea, ocean; heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
2. भू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, (at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR>being, becoming, springing, taking rise [cf. अग्नि-<BR>भू, अक्षि-भू, अश्लेषा-भू, गाधि-भू, गिरि-<BR>भू, चित्त-भू]; (ऊस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; N.<BR>of an Ekāha; (ऊस्), f. the act of becoming, arising;<BR>the place of being or abiding, the universe; the<BR>earth (as opposed to the other two divisions of the<BR>universe, viz. atmosphere and heaven); ground, floor;<BR>land, landed property; earth (as a substance); space,<BR>site, place [cf. कूल-भू, केश-भू]; a district,<BR>piece or plot of ground, (भुवस्, pl. districts); a<BR>mystical word (being the first of the three Vyāhṛtis<BR>भूर् भुवः स्वर्, uttered by every Brāhman in<BR>commencing his daily prayers; in this sense only in<BR>the nom. sing. भूस्, which is considered indeclinable,<BR>see भूर्, भुवस्, व्याहृति, and cf. Manu 11. 76);<BR>the base of a triangle or of any geometrical figure;<BR>object, matter, subject-matter, subject (see विवाद-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-b" target="_blank">Page0715-b+ 81</a>]<BR>संवाद-भू, cf. स्थान); a sacrificial fire; a sym-<BR>bolical expression for the number one (derived from<BR>the earth considered as one); a term for the letter ब्.<BR>—भू-कदम्ब, अस्, m. a species of plant com-<BR>monly called Kokasima (= अलम्बुष); = भू-<BR>कदम्बक; (आ), f. a plant commonly called Go-<BR>rakṣamuṇḍī, perhaps Sphæranthus Mollis.<BR>—भू-<BR>कदम्बक, अस्, m. the plant Ligusticum Ajowan,<BR>= यवानी; (इका), f. = भू-कदम्बा.<BR>—भू-कन्-<BR>द, अस्, m. a medicinal plant (= महा-श्रावणिका).<BR>—भू-कपित्थ, अस्, m. the plant Feronia Ele-<BR>phantum; (अम्), n. the fruit of this plant.<BR>—भू-<BR>कम्प, अस्, m. an earthquake; N. of a man.<BR>—भूकम्प-लक्षण, अम्, n., N. of the thirty-<BR>third chapter of Bhaṭṭotpala's commentary on Varāha-<BR>mihira's Bṛhat-saṃhitā.<BR>—भू-कर्ण, अस्, m. (in<BR>astronomy) the diameter of the earth, the radius of<BR>the equator.<BR>—भू-कर्णि, इस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भू-कर्बुदारक, अस्, m. the plant Cordia<BR>Myxa.<BR>—भू-कश्यप, अस्, m. an epithet of Vasu-<BR>deva (the father of Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—भू-काक, अस्, m.<BR>‘earth-crow,’ N. of several birds, a species of<BR>heron (= स्वल्प-कङ्क); the curlew (= क्रनुञ्च);<BR>a species of pigeon (= नील-कपोत).<BR>—भू-काण्ड,<BR>अस्, m. ‘chapter of the earth,’ N. of a chapter of the<BR>Bhūri-prayoga.<BR>—भू-कुम्भी, f. a plant (= भू-<BR>पाटली).<BR>—भू-कुष्माण्डी, f. the plant Batatas<BR>Paniculata.<BR>—भू-केश, अस्, m. ‘earth-hair,’ the<BR>Indian fig-tree; the plant Blyxa Saivala; (आ), f. a<BR>Rākṣasī or female demon; (ई), f. the plant Ver-<BR>nonia Anthelminthica.<BR>—भू-क्षित्, त्, m. ‘earth-<BR>destroyer,’ a hog.<BR>—भू-क्षीर-वाटिका, f., N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—भू-खण्ड, अस्, m. ‘earth-section,’ N. of<BR>a section of the Skanda-Purāṇa; of a section of the<BR>Padma-Purāṇa (= भूमि-खण्ड).<BR>—भू-खर्-<BR>जूरी, f. a species of date.<BR>—भूगत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being or existing on the earth.<BR>—भू-गर, अम्, n.<BR>‘earth-poison,’ a particular mineral poison.<BR>—भू-<BR>गर्भ, अस्, m. an epithet of the poet Bhava-bhūti.<BR>—भू-गृह, अम्, n. an underground room or<BR>chamber; a particular part of a diagram.<BR>—भू-<BR>गेह, अम्, n. an underground room.<BR>—भू-गोल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘earth-ball,’ the terrestrial globe, the earth.<BR>—भूगोल-विद्या, f. knowledge of the terrestrial<BR>globe, geography.<BR>—भूगोल-वृत्तान्त and भू-<BR>गोल-सङ्ग्रह and भूगोल-सार, N. of certain<BR>works treating of the earth.<BR>—भू-घन, अस्, m.<BR>the body.<BR>—भू-चक्र, अम्, n. ‘earth-circle,’ the<BR>equator or equinoctial line.<BR>—भू-चर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>going on the earth (opposed to आकाश-गति), mov-<BR>ing on the ground, moving on land, living on land<BR>(opposed to जल-चर), inhabiting the earth, ter-<BR>restrial, any land animal; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>—भू-छाया or भू-च्छाया, f. or (according<BR>to some) अम्, n. ‘earth-shadow,’ darkness.<BR>—भू-<BR>जन्तु, उस्, m. ‘earth-animal,’ a kind of snail, an<BR>earth-worm (= भू-नाग).<BR>—भू-जम्बु, उस्, or<BR>भू-जम्बू, ऊस्, f. wheat (= नादेयी); the plant<BR>Flacourtia Sapida or the fruit of this plant.<BR>—भू-<BR>तल, अम्, n. the face of the earth, the surface of<BR>the ground, the earth.<BR>—भूतल-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>standing or being on the face of the earth.<BR>—भू-<BR>तलिका, f. (probably fr. भू-तल), the plant Trigo-<BR>nella Corniculata (= पृक्का).<BR>—भूतलोन्मथन<BR>(˚ल-उन्˚), अस्, m. ‘earth-shaker,’ N. of a Dānava.<BR>—भू-तृण, अस्, m. [cf. भू-स्-तृण], ‘earth-<BR>grass,’ the plant Andropogon Schœnanthus; a kind<BR>of fragrant grass (= गन्ध-खेड, रोहिष).<BR>—भूत्तम (भू-उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘the best of earths,’<BR>gold.<BR>—भू-दरी-भवा, f. the plant Salvinia Cu-<BR>cullata.<BR>—भू-दार, अस्, m. ‘earth-tearer,’ i. e. root-<BR>ing up the earth, a hog.<BR>—भू-देव, अस्, m. ‘earth-<BR>god,’ a divinity upon earth, a Brāhman [cf. भू-<BR>सुर]; an epithet of Śiva; N. of several persons;<BR>of the author of a commentary on the Kāśikā-tilaka.<BR>—भू-धन, अस्, m. ‘whose property is the<BR>earth,’ a king, prince.<BR>—भू-धर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>‘earth-bearing,’ supporting the earth; dwelling in<BR>the earth; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>of Vaṭuka-bhairava; a mountain; a term for the<BR>number seven [cf. कुल-पर्वत]; a kind of che-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-c" target="_blank">Page0715-c+ 80</a>]<BR>mical or medical apparatus, a sort of sand-bath (?);<BR>N. of a commentator on the Sūrya-siddhānta.<BR>—भू-<BR>धर-गुहान्तर-तस् (˚हा-अन्˚), ind. from within<BR>the caves of the mountains.<BR>—भूधर-ज, अस्, m.<BR>‘mountain-born,’ a tree.<BR>—भूधर-ता, f. the state<BR>or act of supporting the earth.<BR>—भूधरेश्वर<BR>(˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘mountain-lord,’ an epithet of<BR>Hima-vat.<BR>—भू-धात्री, f. ‘earth-mother,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Vaṭuka-bhairava; the plant Flacourtia Cata-<BR>phracta.<BR>—भू-ध्र, अस्, m. = भू-धर, a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—भू-नन्दन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भू-<BR>नाग, अस्, m. ‘earth-snake,’ a kind of snail or earth-<BR>worm.<BR>—भू-निम्ब, अस्, m. the plant Gentiana<BR>Cherayta, commonly called Cherayta.<BR>—भू-नीप,<BR>अस्, m. = भू-कदम्ब.<BR>—भू-नेतृ, ता, m. ‘earth-<BR>leader,’ a sovereign, king, prince.<BR>—भू-प, अस्, m.<BR>‘earth-protector,’ a sovereign, king, prince.<BR>—भूप-<BR>ता, f. the state or rank of a king, sovereignty, king-<BR>ship.<BR>—भू-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of the earth,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Rudra; of Indra; of Vaṭuka-bhairava; of<BR>one of the Viśve-Devāḥ; a king, monarch, prince;<BR>N. of a sacrificer; of a poet (probably Bhoja, cf.<BR>भू-पाल); a kind of medicinal plant (= ऋषभ).<BR>—भू-पद, अस्, m. ‘earth-fixed, earth-rooted,’ a<BR>tree; (ई), f. Arabian jasmine, Jasminum Zambac.<BR>—भूप-पुत्र, अस्, m. a king's son, prince.<BR>—भू-<BR>परिधि, इस्, m. the circumference of the earth; the<BR>equinoctial line.<BR>—भू-पलाश, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>plant commonly called Viśālī.<BR>—भू-पवित्र, अम्,<BR>n. ‘earth-purifying,’ cow-dung.<BR>—भूप-सुत, अस्,<BR>m. a king's son, prince.<BR>—भू-पाटली, f. a kind of<BR>plant (= भू-कुम्भी).<BR>—भू-पाल, अस्, m. ‘earth-<BR>guardian,’ a sovereign, king, prince; an epithet of<BR>Bhoja-rāja; N. of a son of Soma-pāla; of a country;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a particular scale in the Hindū musical<BR>system.<BR>—भू-पालन, अम्, n. protection or govern-<BR>ment of the earth, sovereignty, dominion.<BR>—भू-<BR>पाल-वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘king's favourite,’ N. of an<BR>author; of an astronomer.<BR>—भूपाल-श्री, ईस्, f.<BR>‘king's fortune,’ N. of a temple of Śiva mentioned<BR>in the Skanda-Purāṇa.<BR>—भूपाल-साहि, इस्, m.<BR>(साहि = Persian شاه), N. of a king.<BR>—भू-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. ‘son of the earth,’ the planet Mars.<BR>—भू-<BR>पुत्री, f. ‘daughter of the earth,’ an epithet of Sītā<BR>(wife of Rāma-candra).<BR>—भू-पुर, अम्, n. a par-<BR>ticular part of a diagram; [cf. भू-गृह.]<BR>—भू-<BR>पेष्ट (˚प-इष्˚), अस्, m. ‘liked by kings,’ a kind of<BR>fruit tree (= राजादनी).<BR>—भू-प्रकम्प, अस्, m.<BR>an earthquake.<BR>—भू-प्रदान, अम्, n. a gift of<BR>land.<BR>—भू-फल, अस्, m. a kind of rat.<BR>—भू-<BR>बदरी, f. a species of jujube.<BR>—भू-बिम्ब, अस्, अम्,<BR>m. n. ‘earth-ball,’ the globe.<BR>—भू-भट, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR>—भू-भर्तृ, ता, m. ‘earth-supporter,<BR>earth-lord,’ a sovereign, king, prince.<BR>—भू-भाग,<BR>अस्, m. a portion of ground, a place, spot, station;<BR>[cf. भूमि-भाग.]<BR>—भू-भुज्, क्, m. ‘earth-pos-<BR>sessor,’ a sovereign, king, prince.<BR>—भू-भृत्, त्, m.<BR>‘earth-supporter,’ a mountain [cf. कुल-भ्˚]; an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; a king, prince.<BR>—भू-मण्डल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘earth-circle, earth-ball,’ the terrestrial globe;<BR>the circumference or circuit of the earth.<BR>—भू-मत्,<BR>आन्, m. ‘possessing the earth,’ a king, prince.<BR>—१. भू-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम् (for 2. भूमय see p. 717,<BR>col. 3), made or formed or consisting of earth, pro-<BR>duced from the earth, earthen, earthy, terrene; (ई),<BR>f. an epithet of Chāyā or Shadow (personified as<BR>wife of the Sun).<BR>—भू-मित्र, अस्, m. ‘earth-friend,’<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—भू-युक्ता, f. a kind of palm (=<BR>भूमि-खर्जूरी).<BR>—भू-रति, इस्, m. ‘earth-joy,’<BR>N. of a magical spell recited over weapons (personi-<BR>fied as a son of Kṛśāśva).<BR>—भू-रुण्डी, f. a sort of<BR>sun-flower, Heliotropium Indicum.<BR>—भू-रुह्, ट्, m.<BR>‘earth-grower,’ a plant, tree.<BR>—भू-रुह, अस्, m.<BR>‘earth-growing,’ any plant, tree; the plant Termi-<BR>nalia Arjuna and Glabra.<BR>—भूर्-भुव, अस्, m.<BR>(भुव = भुवस्), one of the mind-born sons of<BR>Brahmā (mentioned with Bhūr and Bhuvas in Hari-<BR>vaṃśa 11509).<BR>—भूर्भुव-कर, अस्, m. a dog.<BR>—भूर्भुव-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage.<BR>—भूर्-लोक, अस्, m. the terrestrial world,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0716-a" target="_blank">Page0716-a+ 81</a>]<BR>habitation of mortals, the earth; the country on the<BR>southern part of the equator; [cf. भू-लोक.]<BR>—भू-<BR>लग्ना, f. ‘clinging to the ground,’ the plant Andro-<BR>pogon Aciculatus.<BR>—भू-लता, f. an earth-worm, a<BR>worm.<BR>—भू-लिङ्ग, N. of a district of Sālua [cf.<BR>भौलिङ्गि]; (आ), f., N. of a town.<BR>—भूलिङ्ग-<BR>शकुन, अस्, or भूलिङ्ग-शकुनी, इस्, m. a species<BR>of bird described in Mahā-bhārata Sabhā-parva,<BR>1. 1546, &c., (it is said to make a sound like मा<BR>साहसम्, no rashness!)<BR>—भू-लोक, अस्, m. the<BR>terrestrial world, earth; [cf. भूर्-लोक.]<BR>—भू-<BR>लोक-सुरनायक, अस्, m. ‘earth-Indra,’ an Indra<BR>of the earth.<BR>—भू-वलय, अस्, अम्, m. n. the cir-<BR>cumference of the earth; the terrestrial globe.<BR>—भू-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘earth's favourite,’ a king, prince.<BR>—भू-वाह् (gen. c. भूहस्, inst. c. भूहा), see<BR>Vopa-deva III. 103.<BR>—भू-वृत्त, अम्, n. ‘earth-<BR>circle,’ the equator.<BR>—भू-शक्र, अस्, m. ‘earth-<BR>Indra,’ a king, prince.<BR>—भू-शमी, f. a kind of<BR>Acacia (= लघु-शमी).<BR>—भू-शय, अस्, m. ‘lying<BR>or dwelling on the earth,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu; any<BR>animal living in the earth; [cf. भूमि-शय.]<BR>—भू-<BR>शय्या, f. a couch on the bare ground, lying on the<BR>ground.<BR>—भू-शर्करा f. a species of bulbous plant<BR>commonly called Kaḍamākaḍa-kanda.<BR>—भू-शुद्-<BR>धि, इस्, f. purification of the ground (by sweeping,<BR>burning, &c.).<BR>—भू-शेलु, उस्, m. the plant Cordia<BR>Myxa.<BR>—भू-श्रवस्, आस्, m. an ant or mole hill.<BR>—भू-संस्कार, अस्, m., Ved. ‘preparation of the<BR>ground,’ a term applied to five methods of preparing<BR>and consecrating the Khara, q. v., at a sacrifice, (these<BR>five methods are called परि-समूह्, उप-लिप्, लेखाः<BR>कृ, पांसु-नुद्धृ, अद्भिर् अभ्युक्ष्; some<BR>enumerate seven.)<BR>—भू-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the<BR>earth,’ the planet Mars; (आ), f. ‘daughter of the<BR>earth,’ an epithet of Sītā (wife of Rāma).<BR>—भू-<BR>सुर, अस्, m. ‘earth-god,’ a Brāhman; [cf. भू-<BR>देव.]<BR>—भू-स्-तृण, अस्, m. = भू-तृण, q. v.<BR>—भू-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing on the earth,<BR>living on the earth.<BR>—भू-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, touching<BR>the ground; (क्), m. a man; man, mankind; a<BR>Vaiśya; [cf. भूमि-स्पृश्.]<BR>—भू-स्वर्ग, अस्, m.<BR>‘heaven on earth,’ an epithet of the mountain Su-<BR>meru.<BR>—भूस्वर्गाय (fr. the preceding), Nom. A.<BR>भूस्वर्गायते, &c., to become a heaven on earth.<BR>—भू-स्वामिन्, ई, m. a landlord, landholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत|भूतं|भूतः
भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, been, become, produced,<BR>formed, being, existing, being or becoming like,<BR>consisting of, (in all these senses often at the end of<BR>comps., cf. आत्म-भ्˚, जीव-भ्˚, चित्र-भ्˚, भव-<BR>भ्˚, इत्थम्-भ्˚, भस्म-भ्˚, शक्तु-भ्˚); being<BR>mixed or joined with [cf. मांस-भूतोदन, भा-<BR>वित]; actually being, really happened, true; right,<BR>proper, fit; past, gone, former; obtained, got; (अस्),<BR>m. a son, child, youth; a great devotee or ascetic<BR>[cf. भूतेन्द्रिय-जयिन्]; an epithet of Śiva; N. of<BR>a priest of the gods; of a son of Vasu-deva and<BR>Pauravī; of a son-in-law of Dakṣa and father of<BR>numerous Rudras; of a Yakṣa; the fourteenth day<BR>of the dark half of the lunar month, (in this sense<BR>also आ, f.; cf. भुतेष्टा); (अम्), n. that which is<BR>or exists, any being (whether human or divine, and<BR>applied also to inanimate objects or plants), a living<BR>being, animal, creature, (in these senses exception-<BR>ally अस्, m.); a spirit (good or evil), the spirit of a<BR>deceased person, a ghost, a particular class of super-<BR>human beings, a demon, imp, goblin, (in these<BR>senses also occasionally अस्, m.); an element, (pro-<BR>perly a gross element, of which, according to the<BR>Hindūs, there are five, viz. earth, water, fire, air,<BR>ether, cf. महा-भ्˚, पाञ्च-भौतिक; but also<BR>exceptionally a subtile element, cf. तन्-मात्र; the<BR>Buddhists reckon only four elements); a symbolical<BR>expression for the number five; the place of being,<BR>the world; that which has actually been or really<BR>happened, an actual occurrence, fact, matter of fact,<BR>the real state of the case; that which is past and<BR>gone, past time, the past; well-being, welfare, pros-<BR>perity; (आस्), m. pl., N. of an heretical sect, the<BR>followers of which rub their bodies with ashes; (with<BR>Jainas) a class of the Vyantaras.<BR>—भूत-करण,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0716-b" target="_blank">Page0716-b+ 81</a>]<BR>अम्, n. ‘maker of past meaning,’ a term for the<BR>augment in Vedic grammar (cf. Atharva-veda Prā-<BR>tiśākhya III. 49).<BR>—भूत-कर्तृ, ता, m. ‘maker<BR>of beings,’ Brahmā, the creator.<BR>—भूत-कर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a man (in Mahā-bh. Droṇa-p. 1085).<BR>—भूत-काल, अस्, m. past time, the preterite tense.<BR>—भूतकालिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to time past.<BR>—भूत-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, forming beings, creative; (त्),<BR>m. the creator.<BR>—भूत-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Manu Dakṣasāvarṇi; of a Vetāla (Kathā-sarit-s.<BR>123, 34).<BR>—भूत-केश, अस्, m. a particular plant,<BR>root of sweet flag (= गो-लोमी); the plant mussænda<BR>Frondosa; (ई), f. Nardostachys Jatmansi (= जटा-<BR>मांसी); Vitex Negundo (= निर्गुण्डी); white basil;<BR>Nyctanthes Arbor Tristis (= शेफालिका).<BR>—भूत-<BR>केसरा, f. the plant Trigonella Fœnum Græcum.<BR>—भूत-कोटि, (with Buddhists) ‘the highest culmi-<BR>nating point for all beings,’ absolute nonentity (=<BR>शून्य-ता).<BR>—भूत-क्रान्ति, इस्, f. possession by<BR>spirits; (perhaps for भूताक्रान्ति.)<BR>—भूत-गण,<BR>अस्, m. the aggregate or whole collection of beings;<BR>the troop or whole class of demons or spirits, any<BR>class of spirits or superhuman beings.<BR>—भूतगणा-<BR>धिप (˚ण-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘lord of the Bhūta-gaṇas,’<BR>an epithet of Nandin, q. v.<BR>—भूत-गन्धा, f. a<BR>particular perfume (used perhaps in the ceremonies<BR>with which the Bhūtas are worshipped, = मुरा).<BR>—भूत-ग्रस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, possessed by an evil<BR>spirit.<BR>—भूत-ग्राम, अस्, m. or आस्, m. pl. the<BR>aggregate or whole collection of living beings; a<BR>multitude of spirits or ghosts; the world; (अस्), m.<BR>any aggregate of elementary matter, the body.<BR>—भूत-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying or removing<BR>spirits or demons; a camel; garlic; a species of<BR>birch; (ई), f. the sacred basil (= मुण्डितिका).<BR>—भूत-चतुर्दशी, f. the fourteenth day in the<BR>dark half of the month Kārttika (consecrated to<BR>Yama).<BR>—भूत-चारिन्, ई, m. ‘going among beings<BR>or among spirits,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूत-चिन्ता,<BR>f. investigation or inquiry into the elements.<BR>—भू-<BR>त-जटा, f. the plant Nardostachys Jatamansi [cf.<BR>भूत-केशी]; a species of Valeriana, Indian spike-<BR>nard (= गन्ध-मांसी).<BR>—भूत-जय, अस्, m.<BR>victory over the elements.<BR>—भूत-ज्योतिस्, इस्, m.<BR>‘light of living beings,’ N. of a king.<BR>—भूत-डा-<BR>मर, N. of a Tantra.<BR>—भूत-तन्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>‘the doctrine of spirits,’ as contained in the Uttara-<BR>tantra or sixth division of the Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya.<BR>—भूत-तृण, अम्, n. a kind of plant (= अति-<BR>गन्ध).<BR>—भूत-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being<BR>an element.<BR>—भूत-दया, f. compassion or ten-<BR>derness towards all beings or creatures, universal be-<BR>nevolence or compassion.<BR>—भूत-द्रुह्, ध्रुक्, क्,<BR>क्, injuring beings, injurious.<BR>—भूत-धरा, f. ‘sup-<BR>porting beings,’ the earth.<BR>—भूत-धात्री, f. ‘nurse<BR>or mother of beings,’ the earth.<BR>—भूत-धामन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a son of Indra.<BR>—भूत-धारिणी, f. =<BR>भूत-धरा, the earth.<BR>—भूत-नन्द, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—भूत-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘lord of beings<BR>or spirits,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूत-नायिका, f.<BR>‘leader of the Bhūtas,’ an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—भू-<BR>त-नाशन, अस्, आ, अम्, destroying evil beings; (अस्),<BR>m. the marking-nut plant, Semicarpus Anacardium<BR>[cf. भल्लातक]; mustard; pepper; (अम्), n. Asa<BR>Fœtida; the berry or seed of the Eleocarpus (used<BR>for rosaries).<BR>—भूत-निचय, अस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of elements,’ the body.<BR>—भूत-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of beings’ (especially of evil beings), an epithet of<BR>Rudra; of Bhava and Śarva; of Śiva; of Agni; the<BR>plant Ocymum Sanctum or sacred basil.<BR>—भूत-<BR>पत्त्री, f. sacred basil.<BR>—भूत-पाल, अस्, m., Ved.<BR>the guardian of living beings.<BR>—भूत-पुर, आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a people; (ई), f., N. of a town.<BR>—भूत-<BR>पुष्प, अस्, m. the plant Calosanthes Indica.<BR>—भू-<BR>त-पूर्णिमा, f. the day of full moon in the month<BR>Āśvina (when the Bhūtas are worshipped).<BR>—भूत-<BR>पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, been before, existed before,<BR>existing formerly or previously, prior; (अम्), ind.<BR>formerly.<BR>—भूतपूर्व-ता, f. the totality of past<BR>events, all that has happened before, all former cir-<BR>cumstances.<BR>—भूत-प्रकृति, इस्, f. the orgin of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0716-c" target="_blank">Page0716-c+ 81</a>]<BR>all beings.<BR>—भूत-प्रतिषेध, अस्, m. the ward-<BR>ing off of evil spirits or demons.<BR>—भूत-बलि, इस्,<BR>f. the offering for all beings, see बलि.<BR>—भूत-<BR>ब्रह्मन्, आ, m. = देवल, q. v.<BR>—भूत-भर्तृ,<BR>ता, त्री, तृ, supporting the elements or living beings;<BR>(ता), m. ‘lord of evil beings,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूत-भाव, अस्, आ, अम्, elementary, consisting<BR>of the elements.<BR>—भूत-भावन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>causing the existence of beings, creating or caus-<BR>ing the welfare of living beings; (अस्), m. the<BR>creator of living beings, Brahmā; Viṣṇu.<BR>—भूत-<BR>भाषा, f. or भूत-भाषित, अम्, n. the lan-<BR>guage of demons or Piśācas.<BR>—भूतभाषा-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, composed in the language of Piśācas.<BR>—भूत-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, sustaining the elements,<BR>supporting living beings.<BR>—भूत-भैरव, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular medical compound (रस);<BR>N. of a Tantra.<BR>—भूतभौतिक, अस्, ई, अम्, con-<BR>sisting of the elements or of anything formed from<BR>them.<BR>—भूत-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed out of<BR>the elements or out of created beings; containing or<BR>including all beings.<BR>—भूत-महेश्वर, अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of the Bhūtas,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूत-<BR>मातृ, ता, f. ‘mother of all beings,’ an epithet of<BR>Gaurī, Brāhmī, &c.<BR>—भूत-मात्र, अम्, आ, n. f.<BR>the rudiment of an element; (आस्), f. pl. the subtile<BR>rudiments of the elements, (see तन्-मात्र); the<BR>coarse and subtile elements, (in this sense a Dvandva<BR>comp.); ten primary perceptions (viz. वाच्, गन्ध,<BR>रूप, शब्द, अन्न-रस, करमन्, सुख-दुःखे,<BR>आनन्द or रति or प्रजाति, इत्या, मनस्).<BR>—भूत-<BR>मारी, f. a particular perfume (= चीडा).<BR>—भूत-<BR>यज्ञ, अस्, m. the oblation of food &c. to all created<BR>beings, (one of the five महा-यज्ञ, see बलि.)<BR>—भूत-योनि, इस्, f. the origin or source of all<BR>beings, (an epithet applied to the Supreme Being.)<BR>—भूत-रय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a class of gods<BR>under the fifth Manu.<BR>—भूत-राज्, ट्, m. ‘king of<BR>the Bhūtas, lord of imps,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूत-रूप, अस्, आ, अम्, having the form of a<BR>Bhūta or evil being, imp-like.<BR>—भूत-लिपि, इस्, f.<BR>‘demon-writing,’ N. of a particular magical formula.<BR> — 1. भूत-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, connected with or con-<BR>taining the word भूत.<BR>—२. भूत-वत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having been, what has been.<BR>—भूत-वर्ग, अस्,<BR>m. the whole class or company of Bhūtas or evil<BR>beings.<BR>—भूत-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, telling the real<BR>fact, speaking the truth.<BR>—भूत-वास, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>abode of evil beings,’ the tree Belleric Myrobalan,<BR>Terminalia Bellerica, (so called because the nuts of<BR>this plant are used as dice; cf. भूतावास.)<BR>—भूत-<BR>वाहन, अस्, m. ‘having the Bhūtas for his vehicle,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूतवाहन-सारथि, इस्, m.<BR>‘charioteer of the Bhūta vehicle,’ an epithet of Śiva.-<BR>—भूत-विक्रिया, f. possession by evil spirits, epi-<BR>lepsy.<BR>—भूत-विज्ञान, अम्, n. the knowledge of<BR>evil spirits or demons.<BR>—भूत-विद्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>knowing all beings.<BR>—भूत-विद्या, f. the know-<BR>ledge of evil beings or demons, demonology.<BR>—भू-<BR>त-विनायक, अस्, m. a leader of evil beings.<BR>—भू-<BR>त-विष्णु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भूत-वीर, आस्,<BR>m. pl., Ved., N. of a race.<BR>—भूत-वृक्ष, अस्,<BR>m. ‘demon-tree,’ the tree Trophis Aspera; Calo-<BR>santhes Indica; Terminalia Bellecrica.<BR>—भूत-वेषी<BR>or भूत-वेशी, f. a white-flowering Vitex Negundo.<BR>—भूत-शुद्धि, इस्, f. purification of the elements<BR>(of the body); N. of a work.<BR>—भूत-संसार, अस्,<BR>m. the world of sentient beings or mortals.<BR>—भूत-<BR>सङ्क्रामिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. going through all<BR>beings (?).<BR>—भूत-सङ्घ, अस्, m. the whole col-<BR>lection or totality of beings, the aggregate of the<BR>elements.<BR>—भूत-सञ्चार, अस्, m. possession by<BR>evil spirits, demoniac possession, madness; (ई), f.<BR>fire in a forest, a forest conflagration (?).<BR>—भूत-<BR>सन्ताप, अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—भूत-सन्ता-<BR>पन, अस्, m. ‘harasser of living beings,’ N. of a<BR>Daitya (son of Hiraṇyākṣa).<BR>—भूत-सम्पृक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, combined with elementary matter.<BR>—भू-<BR>त-सम्प्लव, अस्, m. the flooding or drowning of<BR>all creatures, universal deluge, drowning of the world.<BR>—भूत-सर्ग, अस्, m. a class or order of created<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-a" target="_blank">Page0717-a+ 81</a>]<BR>beings (usually classified into eight species of Deva-<BR>yonis or divine beings, men, and five species of<BR>Tiryag-yonis, viz. cattle, birds, wild animals, creep-<BR>ing things, and plants); elementary creation, crea-<BR>tion of the elements.<BR>—भूत-साक्षिन्, ई, m. an<BR>eye-witness of created beings, all-seeing.<BR>—भूत-<BR>साधन, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. (according to Mahī-dhara)<BR>producing creatures or created beings (as the earth);<BR>effecting (objects) for living beings.<BR>—भूत-सार,<BR>अस्, m. a variety of Colosanthes Indica.<BR>—भूत-<BR>सूक्ष्म, अम्, n. a subtile element (= तन्-मात्र,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—भूत-सृष्टि, इस्, f. the creation of Bhūtas;<BR>the illusions effected by the power of Bhūtas; the<BR>whole class of Bhūtas collectively.<BR>—भूत-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being in living creatures, existing in all<BR>beings, residing in the elements.<BR>—भूत-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. the dwelling-place of beings, abode of living<BR>creatures.<BR>—भूत-हत्या, f. the killing of a being,<BR>destruction of a living creature.<BR>—भूत-हन्तृ, त्री,<BR>f. ‘destroying beings, counteracting evil spirits,’ two<BR>plants (= बन्ध्या-कर्कोटकी and नील-दूर्वा).<BR>—भूत-हर, अस्, m. bdellium.<BR>—भूत-हारिन्, इ,<BR>n. the tree Pinus Deodora.<BR>—भूतांश (˚त-अं˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of the author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 106,<BR>(he was a descendant of Kaśyapa.)<BR>—भूताङ्कुश<BR>(˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a kind of plant (= क्षव, क्ष-<BR>वक, क्षुरक, तीक्ष्ण, क्रूर).<BR>—भूतात्मक<BR>(˚त-आत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessing the essence of the<BR>elements, consisting of the elements, composed of<BR>the elements.<BR>—भूतात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. ‘soul<BR>of all beings,’ epithet of Brahman; of Mahā-puruṣa<BR>(Viṣṇu); of Śiva [cf. सर्व-भूतात्मन्]; the<BR>individual soul; the elementary or vital principle; a<BR>soul or mind which clings to the elements, a carnal<BR>mind (see Yājñavalkya III. 34); war, conflict; (आ,<BR>आ, अ), whose soul is subdued or purified [cf. भावि-<BR>तात्मन्]; whose soul is the elements, consisting or<BR>composed of the [five] elements, epithet of the body<BR>(in this sense masc., and in Manu XII. 12. opposed<BR>to क्षेत्र-ज्ञ).<BR>—भूतादि (˚त-आदि), इस्, m. ‘the<BR>original or originator of all beings,’ an epithet of Ma-<BR>hā-puruṣa or the Supreme Spirit; (in the Sāṅkhya<BR>phil.) an epithet of Ahaṅ-kāra as the principle from<BR>which the five Tan-mātras and elements are evolved.<BR>—भूतादिक, अस्, आ, अम्, beginning with the ele-<BR>ments, the elements, &c.; (अस्), m. a term applied<BR>to Ahaṅ-kāra as the source of the elements; [cf.<BR>भूतादि above.]<BR>—भूताधिपति (˚त-अध्˚), इस्,<BR>m., Ved. the lord of all beings.<BR>—भूतानुकम्पा<BR>(˚त-अन्˚), f. compassion towards all beings.<BR>—भू-<BR>तान्तक (˚त-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘destroyer of beings,’ the<BR>god of death.<BR>—भूतारि (˚त-अरि), इ, n. ‘enemy of<BR>evil beings,’ Asa Fœtida.<BR>—भूतार्त (˚त-आर्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, afflicted by evil beings, possessed by demons.<BR>—भूतार्थ (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, m. anything which has<BR>really happened, anything really existing, real fact, a<BR>matter of fact, fact; an element of life.<BR>—भूतार्-<BR>थ-कथन or भूतार्थ-वर्णन, अम्, n. nar-<BR>ration of a real fact or of a past event, description of<BR>past occurrences.<BR>—भूतार्थानुभव (˚थ-अन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the apprehension of a matter of fact.<BR>—भू-<BR>तार्म (˚त-अर्˚), अम्, n., see Pāṇini VI. 2, 91.<BR>—भूतावास (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of beings,’<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; the plant Terminalia<BR>Bellerica [cf. भूत-वास]; the body (as the abode<BR>of the elements).<BR>—भूताविष्ट (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, occupied by evil spirits, possessed by a devil.<BR>—भूतावेश (˚त-आव्˚), अस्, m. possession by a<BR>devil or evil spirit, demoniac possession.<BR>—भूता-<BR>सन (˚त-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘seat of Bhūtas,’ N. of a<BR>magic chariot.<BR>—भूतेज्य (˚त-इज्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, wor-<BR>shipping evil beings or spirits; making oblations to<BR>the Bhūtas (see भूत-यज्ञ).<BR>—भूतेन्द्रिय-<BR>जयिन् (˚त-इन्˚), ई, इनी, इ, ‘one who has subdued<BR>both the elements (of the body) and the senses,’ a<BR>kind of ascetic or devotee.<BR>—भूतेश (˚त-इश), अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of beings,’ Brahmā; Viṣṇu; Kṛṣṇa;<BR>‘lord of evil beings,’ an epithet of Śiva (or of<BR>an idol representing him).<BR>—भूतेश्वर (˚त-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. lord of beings (said of man); ‘lord of evil<BR>beings,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भूतेष्टका (˚त-इष्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">Page0717-b+ 81</a>]<BR>f., Ved. a particular kind of brick.<BR>—भूतेष्टा<BR>(˚त-इष्˚), f. ‘liked by the Bhūtas,’ the fourteenth<BR>day of a half month; [cf. भूता.]<BR>—भूतोदन<BR>(˚त-ओद्˚), अस्, m. a dish of rice (eaten to counteract<BR>the influence of demons).<BR>—भूतोन्माद (˚त-उन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘demon-madness,’ a form of insanity pro-<BR>duced by the influence of evil spirits, (twenty kinds<BR>are enumerated.)<BR>—भूतोपदेश (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>referring to anything already occurring or existing.<BR>—भूतोपमा (˚त-उप्˚), f., Ved. comparison with<BR>a living being or animal.<BR>—भूतोपसृष्ट (˚त-<BR>उप्˚) or भूतोपहत (˚त-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessed<BR>by an evil spirit.<BR>—भूतोपहत-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having the mind possessed by evil beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतायन
भूतायन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूति|भूतिः
भूति, इस्, f. being, existence, any state of being;<BR>birth, production; well-being, welfare, prosperity,<BR>success, good fortune, wealth, riches, fortune, (अ-भू-<BR>ति, misfortune, calamity); Welfare personified (=<BR>Lakṣī) or = the wife of Ruci and mother of Manu<BR>Bhautya, or = the wife of Kavi and mother of Manu<BR>Bhautya; in this latter meaning also भूती, f.);<BR>power, grandeur, majesty, dignity; superhuman<BR>power as attainable by the practice of austerity and<BR>magical rites [cf. वि-भूति]; ornament, decorating<BR>elephants with many-coloured stripes (= गज-मण्-<BR>डन); ashes; fried meat; N. of various plants<BR>(= वृद्धि, = रोहिष-तृण, = भू-तृण); the<BR>rutting of elephants; (इस्), m., N. of a class of<BR>Manes; of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of a pupil (or son) of<BR>Aṅgiras and father of Manu Bhautya; of a Brāhman;<BR>[cf. Gr. φύ-σι-ς; Slav. infinitive by-ti = Lith. bú-ti,<BR>‘to be.’]<BR>—भूति-कर्मन्, अ, n. any auspicious or<BR>festive rite (e. g. any domestic ceremony performed<BR>at a birth, marriage, or the introduction of a pupil to<BR>his preceptor).<BR>—भूति-कलश, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>person (mentioned in Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VII. 26, &c.).<BR>—भूति-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desiring prosperity,<BR>desirous of wealth or aggrandisement, &c.; (अस्),<BR>m. a king's councillor, a minister of state; an epithet<BR>of Bṛhas-pati.<BR>—भूति-काल, अस्, m. a time of pros-<BR>perity or good fortune, an auspicious hour, a happy<BR>moment.<BR>—भूति-कीर्तन, अम्, n. ‘praise of pros-<BR>perity,’ N. of the twenty-ninth chapter of the Jñāna-<BR>khaṇḍa or second part of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—भूति-<BR>कील, अस्, m. a hole, pit, moat, ditch; a cellar, a<BR>place under ground for concealing wealth, &c.<BR>—भूति-कृत्, त्, m. ‘causing welfare,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of a class of Manes.<BR>—भूति-कृत्य, अम्,<BR>n. = भूति-कर्मन्, q. v.<BR>—भूति-गर्भ, अस्, m.<BR>a N. of the dramatic poet Bhava-bhūti.<BR>—भूति-<BR>तीर्था, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda.<BR>—भूति-द, अस्, m. ‘granting welfare,’ an<BR>epithet of Śiva; N. of a class of Manes.<BR>—भूति-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m. ‘fortune-given,’ N. of a man.<BR>—भू-<BR>ति-निधान, अम्, n. ‘receptacle of prosperity,’ the<BR>lunar mansion or Nakṣatra Dhaniṣṭhā.<BR>—भूति-<BR>भूषण, अस्, m. ‘adorned with ashes,’ an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—भूति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing welfare,<BR>prosperous, fortunate, doing well, affluent, happy.<BR>—भूति-मलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, soiled with ashes.<BR>—भूति-युवक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a tribe.<BR>—भूति-<BR>लय, N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—भूति-वर्मन्,<BR>आ, m., N. of a king of Prāg-jyotiṣa; of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—भूति-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘welfare-bringing,’ an<BR>epithet of Śiva; [cf. भूत-वाहन.]<BR>—भूति-शिव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भूति-सित, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>white with ashes.<BR>—भूति-सृज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, ‘welfare-<BR>creating,’ causing prosperity.<BR>—भूतीश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚ति-इश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place men-<BR>tioned in the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिक|भूतिकं|भूतिकः
भूतिक, अस्, अम्, m. n. the plant Ligusticum<BR>Ajowan; (अम्), n. Gentiana Cherayta; Andropogon<BR>Schœnanthus; a medicinal plant commonly called<BR>Kayaphal (= कत्-तृण); camphor (= घन-सार);<BR>[cf. द्राविड-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतीक|भूतीकं
भूतीक, अम्, n., n. of several plants, Gentiana<BR>Cherayta; Curcuma Zerumbet; = दीप्य; a kind<BR>of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत्वा
भूत्वा, ind. having been or become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम
भूम = भूमि (at the end of some comps, cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-c" target="_blank">Page0717-c+ 81</a>]<BR>उत्कृष्ट-भ्˚, उदक-भ्˚, उदग्-भ्˚, कवि-भ्˚,<BR>कृष्ण-भ्˚, पाण्डु-भ्˚; and occurring separately<BR>in the Vedic formula ध्रुवाय भूमाय स्वाहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमक
भूमक, a proper N. (?).<BR>—भूमक-तृतीया,<BR>f. epithet of the third day in a particular month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमन्
भूमन्, अ, n. (said to be fr. भू for बहु +<BR>इमन्), the earth, world; a territory, district, country,<BR>piece of ground [cf. भूमि, Lat. humus]; a being,<BR>the aggregate of all existing things; (आ), m. a great<BR>quantity, large number abundance, plenty, multitude,<BR>majority; wealth; N. of a son of Prati-hartṛ and<BR>father of Udgītha; (आ), f., Ved. a collection, assembly;<BR>(म्ना), inst. c. (Ved. भूना), for the most part,<BR>generally, usually, abundantly.<BR>—भूमानन्द-स-<BR>रस्वती (˚म-आन्˚), m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमन्यु
भूमन्यु, उस्, m., N. of a king, (also read<BR>सुमन्यु; cf. भुमन्यु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमय
2. भूमय (fr. भूमन्; for 1. भू-मय see<BR>P. 715, col. 3), Nom. P. भूमन्यति, &c., to aug-<BR>ment, increase, make abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमि|भूमिः
भूमि, इस्, f. (also भूमी, f., but this form is<BR>more commonly Ved., where occur nom. sing. भूमी,<BR>gen. भूम्यास्, loc. भूम्याम्), the earth, soil,<BR>ground; a territory, country, district; land, estate,<BR>domain; a place, site in general, situation, (often at<BR>the end of comps., cf. केश-भ्˚); position, posture,<BR>attitude; the floor of a house, story; a step, degree<BR>(metaphorically); the base of a triangle or of any<BR>geometrical figure; the part or character (of an actor<BR>in a play); a matter, object, subject [cf. विश्वास-<BR>भ्˚]; the tongue; (इस्), m., N. of a son of Yuyu-<BR>dhāna and father of Yugan-dhara; [cf. Lat. humus;<BR>Hib. aim.]<BR>—भूमि-कदम्ब, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>Kadamba; (also read भूमी-कदम्ब.)<BR>—भूमि-<BR>कन्दली, f. a species of plant (= कन्दली).<BR>—भूमि-<BR>कपाल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having the ground for a<BR>vessel or receptacle.<BR>—भूमि-कम्प, अस्, m. or<BR>भूमि-कम्पन, अम्, n. an earthquake.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>कुष्माण्ड, अस्, m. a species of plant (= विदारी).<BR>—भूमि-खण्ड, ‘earth-section,’ N. of the second<BR>book of the Padma-Purāṇa; [cf. भू-खण्ड.]<BR>—भूमि-खर्जूरिका or भूमि-खर्जूरी, f. a<BR>species of plam.<BR>—भूमि-गर्त, अस्, m. a pit or<BR>hole in the earth.<BR>—भूमि-गुहा, f. a hole in the<BR>earth.<BR>—भूमि-गृह, अम्, n. an under-ground<BR>chamber [cf. भू-गृह]; (अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. whose<BR>house is the earth (said of a dead person).<BR>—भूमि-<BR>चम्पक, अस्, m. the plant Kæmpferia Rotunda.<BR>—भूमि-चल, अस्, m. or भूमि-चलन, अम्, n.<BR>an earthquake.<BR>—भूमि-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘earth-born,’<BR>produced from the earth, sprung from the ground;<BR>(अस्), m. the planet Mars; a man; a plant (= भूमि-<BR>कदम्ब); an epithet of the demon Naraka; hell;<BR>(आ), f. an epithet of Sītā; (अम्), n. a species of<BR>vegetable (= गौर-सुवर्ण).<BR>—भूमिज-गुग्गु-<BR>लु, उस्, m. a species of bdellium.<BR>—भूमि-जम्बु,<BR>उस्, or भूमि-जम्बुका, or भूमि-जम्बू, ऊस्, f. a<BR>tree, = नादेयी; [cf. भू-जम्बू.]<BR>—भूमि-जीविन्,<BR>ई, m. ‘living by the soil, living on (the produce of)<BR>land,’ an agriculturalist, a Vaiśya or Hindū of the<BR>third or agricultural class.<BR>—भूमिञ्-जय, अस्, m.<BR>(भुमिम्, acc. of भूमि), ‘earth-conquering,’ N. of<BR>a son of Virāṭa.<BR>—भूमि-तल, अम्, n. the surface<BR>of the earth, the ground.<BR>—भूमि-तुण्डिक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a district.<BR>—भूमि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of<BR>earth, earthiness, earth (e. g. भूमित्वम् एति, he<BR>goes to or becomes earth).<BR>—भूमि-दान, अम्, n.<BR>donation of landed property.<BR>—भूमि-दुन्दुभि,<BR>इस्, m., Ved. ‘earth-drum,’ a pit or hole in the earth<BR>covered over with skins.<BR>—भूमि-दृंह, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. firmly fixed on the ground.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>देव, अस्, m. ‘earth-god,’ a Brāhman; (ई), f., N. of<BR>two women.<BR>—भूमि-धर, अस्, m. ‘earth-sup-<BR>porter,’ a mountain; a symbolical expression for the<BR>number seven [cf. कुल-पर्वत]; a king, prince.<BR>—भूमि-नाथ, अस्, m. ‘earth-lord,’ a king, prince.<BR>—भूमि-प, अस्, m. ‘earth-protector,’ a sovereign,<BR>king, prince; a Kṣatriya.<BR>—भूमि-पकष, अस्, m.<BR>a swift horse, a horse with good paces or of good<BR>breed.<BR>—भूमि-पति, इस्, m. ‘earth-lord,’ a king,<BR>prince.<BR>—भूमिपति-त्व, अम्, n. ‘earth-sovereignty,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-a" target="_blank">Page0718-a+ 81</a>]<BR>sovereignty, kingship, princedom.<BR>—भूमि-पाल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘earth-guardian,’ a king, prince.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>पाश, अस्, m., Ved. ‘earth-fetter,’ a plant.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>पिशाच, अस्, m. ‘earth-piśāca,’ the wine-palam or<BR>Palmyra tree, Borassus Flabelliformis.<BR>—भूमि-पु-<BR>त्र, अस्, m. ‘earth-son,’ the planet Mars; N. of a<BR>king.<BR>—भूमि-पुरन्दर, अस्, m. ‘earth-Indra,’<BR>an epithet of Dilīpa.<BR>—भूमि-भाग, अस्, m. a<BR>portion or plot of land, place, spot; [cf. भू-भाग.]<BR>—भूमि-भुज्, क्, m. ‘earth-possessor,’ a king,<BR>prince.<BR>—भूमि-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become earth;<BR>being on the ground.<BR>—भूमि-भृत्, त्, m. ‘earth-<BR>supporter,’ a king, prince; a mountain [cf. भू-<BR>भृत्].<BR>—भूमि-भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, differing from<BR>(what exists on) earth.<BR>—भूमि-मण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>‘earth-ornament,’ the plant Vallaris Dichotomus;<BR>(आ), f. Arabian jasmine.<BR>—भूमि-मण्डप-भू-<BR>षणा, f. the plant Gærtnera Racemosa.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing land, having land.<BR>—भूमि-मित्र, अस्, m. ‘friend of the country,’ N.<BR>of two kings.<BR>—भूमि-रक्षक, अस्, m. the<BR>guardian or protector of a country; a swift horse,<BR>horse of good breed.<BR>—भूमि-लाभ, अस्, m. ‘gain-<BR>ing or returning to earth,’ dying, death.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>लेपन, अम्, n. ‘earth-ointment,’ cow-dung.<BR>—भू-<BR>मि-लोक, अस्, m., Ved. the terrestrial world.<BR>—भू-<BR>मि-वर्धन, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘earth-increasing,’ a<BR>dead body, corpse.<BR>—भूमि-शय, अस्, आ, अम्, sleep-<BR>ing on the ground, lying or living on the ground,<BR>living in the earth; (अस्), m. any animal living in<BR>the ground or earth [cf. भू-शय]; (अस्), m. a<BR>wild pigeon (= अरण्य-चटक); N. of a king.<BR>—भूमि-शयन, अम्, n. or भूमि-शय्या, f. the<BR>act of sleeping on the (bare) ground.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, standing or remaining on the<BR>earth or on the ground; lying on the earth, (अम्बु<BR>भूमि-ष्ठम्, stagnant water); living or remain-<BR>ing in one's own country [cf. पर-भ्˚].<BR>—भू-<BR>मि-सत्त्र, अम्, n. an offering consisting of a dona-<BR>tion of land.<BR>—भूमि-सन्निवेश, अस्, m. the general<BR>appearance or configuration of a country.<BR>—भूमि-<BR>सम्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘earth-born, earth-produced,’<BR>produced on or from the earth; (आ), f. an epithet of<BR>Sītā.<BR>—भूमि-सव, अस्, m., Ved. one of the nine<BR>Vrātya-stomas.<BR>—भूमि-सुत, अस्, m. ‘earth-son,’<BR>the planet Mars.<BR>—भूमि-सेन, अस्, m., N. of one<BR>of the sons of the tenth Manu; of a Buddhist sage.<BR>—भूमि-स्तोम, अस्, m. ‘earth-stoma,’ N. of a<BR>Stoma.<BR>—भूमि-स्नु, उस्, m. an earth-worm.<BR>—भू-<BR>मि-स्पृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. touching the ground; blind;<BR>cripple, lame; (क्), m. a terrestrial being, man;<BR>mankind; an agriculturalist, a Vaiśya or Hindū of<BR>the third caste who cultivates the soil; a theif, one<BR>who creeps along the ground to carry off his plunder;<BR>[cf. भू-स्पृश्.]<BR>—भूमि-स्वामिन्, ई, m. ‘land-lord,’<BR>a king, prince.<BR>—भूमी-कदम्ब, see भूमि-क-<BR>दम्ब.<BR>—भूमी-कुरवक, a species of plant.<BR>—भूमीच्छा (˚मि-इच्˚), f. desire for the earth or<BR>for lying on the ground.<BR>—भूमीन्द्र (˚मि-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘earth-chief,’ a sovereign, king, prince.<BR>—भू-<BR>मी-पति, इस्, m. = भूमि-पति.<BR>—भूमी-भुज्, क्,<BR>m. = भूमि-भुज्.<BR>—भूमी-रुह्, ट्, or भूमी-रु-<BR>ह, अस्, m. ‘earth-growing,’ a plant, tree.<BR>—भूमी-<BR>श्वर (˚मि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘earth-lord,’ a king, prince.<BR>—भूमी-सह, अस्, m. a species of tree.<BR>—भूम्य्-<BR>अन्तर, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the next country;<BR>(अस्), m. the king of an adjacent country.<BR>—भूम्य्-<BR>आमलकी or भूम्य्-आली, f. the plant Flacourtia Cata-<BR>pharacta.<BR>—भूम्य्-आहुल्य, अम्, n. a species of shrub.<BR>—भूम्य्-एकदेश, अस्, m. one portion of terri-<BR>tory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0717-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिका
भूमिका, f. earth, ground, soil; a place, sport;<BR>the floor of a building [cf. मणि-भ्˚]; a story, flat<BR>roof of a house; a step, degree (as in the Yoga phil.);<BR>an actor's part, character in a play; theatrical dress,<BR>the costume of any character represented on the<BR>stage, change of costume (to represent different cha-<BR>racters); decorating images or temples, adorning<BR>gateways, decoration; a preface to a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम्य
भूम्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. भूमि), Ved. belonging<BR>to the earth, terrestrial; (Sāy. = भूमेर् अर्हस्, suited<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-b" target="_blank">Page0718-b+ 81</a>]<BR>to the earth, or अन्तरिक्षार्हस्, suited to the<BR>atmosphere.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूय|भूयं|भूयः
भूय, अम्, n. becoming, being, existence, con-<BR>dition, state, abstract state, (at the end of comps., cf.<BR>अमुत्र-भ्˚, आत्म-भ्˚, देव-भ्˚, ब्रह्म-भ्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्
1. भूयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (for 2. भूयस् see col. 3),<BR>becoming; (अस्), n. the act of becoming; [cf.<BR>ब्रह्म-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्
भूर्, ind. (originally = भूस्, nom. sing. of 2.<BR>भू), a mystical word (the first of the three Vyāhṛtis<BR>uttered by every Brāhman in commencing his daily<BR>prayers, see 2. भू, भुवस्, व्याहृति, and cf. Manu<BR>II. 76); the lowest of the seven lower worlds (=<BR>रसातल, q. v.); a spiritual son of Brahmā. (For<BR>comps. see under 2. भू, p. 715, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरि|भूरिः
भूरि, इस्, इस्, इ (according to some contracted fr.<BR>बहु-रै or बहु-रि), much, many, numerous,<BR>abundant, copious, frequent; great, large, strong,<BR>mighty; (इस्), m. an epithet of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Śiva; of Indra; N. of a man; of a son of Soma-<BR>datta (king of the Bālhīkas, cf. भौर); (इ), n.<BR>gold [cf. भौरिक]; (इ), ind. much, abundantly,<BR>exceedingly, often, frequently, repeatedly.<BR>—भूरि-<BR>कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, doing much, performing many<BR>exploits, very busy (Ved.); making many oblations.<BR>—भूरि-कालम्, ind. for a long time.<BR>—भूरि-<BR>गन्धा, f. a particular perfume (= पुरा).<BR>—भूरि-<BR>गम, अस्, m. ‘much-going,’ an ass.<BR>—भूरि-गु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ (गु = गो), Ved. having many oxen, rich<BR>in herds.<BR>—भूरि-चक्षस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. ‘much-<BR>seeing,’ affording manifold appearances or aspects<BR>(said of the sun).<BR>—भूरि-ज, आस्, m. pl., Ved. many<BR>(sons) born at the same time.<BR>—भूरि-जन्मन्, आ,<BR>आ, अ, Ved. having many births.<BR>—भूरि-ज्येष्ठ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of king Vi-cakṣus.<BR>—भूरि-<BR>तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more, more abundant, more nu-<BR>merous.<BR>—भूरि-ता, f. muchness, numerousness, mul-<BR>titude.<BR>—भूरि-तेजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, of great splendor<BR>or brightness, very glorious; (आस्), m., N. of a<BR>prince.<BR>—भूरि-तेजस, अस्, आ, अम्, possessing great<BR>splendor; (अस्), m. an epithet of fire.<BR>—भूरि-तोक,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having many children.<BR>—भूरि-द, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘much-giving,’ liberal, munificent.<BR>—भूरी-<BR>दक्षिण, अस्, आ, अम्, attended with rich presents or<BR>liberal rewards; bestowing large presents to Brāh-<BR>mans at a sacrifice, &c.; giving liberal rewards,<BR>liberal; (अम्), ind. with rich offerings or liberal<BR>presents.<BR>—भूरि-दा, आस्, आस्, अम्, Ved. ‘much-giv-<BR>ing,’ very liberal, munificent.<BR>—भूरि-दात्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. rich in gifts or weapons (rt. 1. दा or 3. दा).<BR>—भूरि-दान, अम्, n. great liberality, much-giving.<BR>—भूरि-दावन्, आ, वरी, अ, ‘much-giving,’ a muni-<BR>ficent giver, very liberal, (compar. भूरिदावत्-तर, a<BR>more munificent giver, cf. Pāṇini VIII. 2, 17, Vārt. 2.)<BR>—भूरि-दुग्धा, f. ‘having much milk,’ the plant<BR>Tragia Involucrata.<BR>—भूरि-द्युम्न, अस्, m. ‘pos-<BR>sessing great glory,’ N. of a pious prince (son of Vīra-<BR>dyumna); N. of the sons of two Manus, (also read<BR>भूरि-धामन्.)<BR>—भूरि-धन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>having much wealth, rich in property.<BR>—भूरि-धा-<BR>मन्, आ, म्नी, अ, possessing great splendor, splendid,<BR>bright; full of energy, having great might; (आ), m.,<BR>N. of a son of the ninth Manu.<BR>—भूरि-धायस्,<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. ‘much-nourishing,’ abundantly satis-<BR>fying, much-supporting (said of Parjanya and Soma).<BR>—भूरि-धार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘much-showering,’<BR>yielding abundant rays.<BR>—भूरि-निधन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having various terminations.<BR>—भूरि-पत्त्र, अस्, m.<BR>‘many-leaved,’ a species of Andropogon (= उखर्-<BR>वल).<BR>—भूरि-पलित-दा, f. [cf. पलित], a species<BR>of shrub (= पाण्डुर-फली).<BR>—भूरि-पाणि, इस्, इस्,<BR>इ, Ved. many-handed.<BR>—भूरि-पादात, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing many foot-soldiers, having much infantry.<BR>—भूरि-पाश, औ, m. du., Ved. ‘holders of many<BR>fetters,’ an epithet of Mitra and Varuṇa; (Sāy. =<BR>प्रभूत-बन्धन-साधन-पाशोपेतौ.)<BR>—भू-<BR>रि-पुष्पा, f. ‘many-blossomed,’ fennel, Anethum<BR>Sowa (= शत-पुष्पा).<BR>—भूरि-पोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>Ved. ‘much-nourishing,’ cherishing multitudes.<BR>—भू-<BR>रि-प्रयोग, अस्, आ, अम्, having many uses, variously<BR>used or applied, in common use; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">Page0718-c+ 76</a>]<BR>dictionary of synonyms by Padmanābha-datta.<BR>—भू-<BR>रिप्रयोग-त्व, अम्, n. the state of being much<BR>used, general applicability.<BR>—भूरि-प्रेमन्, आ, m.<BR>‘full of affection,’ the ruddy goose, Anas Casarca;<BR>[cf. चक्र-वाक.]<BR>—भूरि-फेना, f. ‘having much<BR>exudation,’ a species of plant commonly called Cher-<BR>maghās.<BR>—भूरि-बल, अस्, m. ‘having much<BR>strength,’ N. of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra; (आ), f. a<BR>species of plant (= अति-बला).<BR>—भूरि-भाग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having great good fortune, prosperous.<BR>—भूरि-भार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘much-weighted,’<BR>heavily laden.<BR>—भूरि-भोज, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>much enjoyment.<BR>—भूरि-मल्ली, f. a species of<BR>plant (= अम्ब-ष्ठा; cf. भूरि-मूलिका).<BR>—भू-<BR>रि-माय, अस्, m. ‘possessed of much deceit,’ a jackal.<BR>—भूरि-मूल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. ‘many-rooted,’<BR>rich in roots.<BR>—भूरि-मूलिका, f. ‘many-rooted,’ a<BR>species of plant (= अम्ब-ष्ठा).<BR>—भूरि-रस, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having much juice,’ the sugar-cane.<BR>—भूरि-<BR>रेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. ‘many-germed,’ rich in germ<BR>or seed, prolific, much-fructifying.<BR>—भूरि-लग्ना,<BR>f. the plant Clitoria Ternatea (having white flowers).<BR>—भूरि-लाभ, अस्, आ, अम्, having much profit,<BR>very profitable; (अस्), m. great gain.<BR>—भूरि-वर्-<BR>पस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. ‘many-shaped,’ presenting many<BR>appearances.<BR>—भूरि-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a minister<BR>or councillor; of a Brāhman.<BR>—भूरि-वार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. rich in gift; (Sāy. = यजमानैर् बहु-<BR>वारं वरणीय, cf. पुरु-वार.)<BR>—भूरि-विक्र-<BR>म, अस्, आ, अम्, having great valour, very brave.<BR>—भूरि-वियोग, अस्, आ, अम्, having many separa-<BR>tions, causing numerous separations.<BR>—भूरि-वृष्टि,<BR>इस्, f. excessive rain.<BR>—भूरि-वेतस, अस्, आ, अम्, hav-<BR>ing many canes or reeds, very reedy.<BR>—भूरि-शस्,<BR>ind. manifoldly, variously, in many ways.<BR>—भूरि-<BR>शृङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. many-horned.<BR>—भूरि-<BR>श्रम, अस्, m. great fatigue.<BR>—भूरि-श्रवस्, आस्,<BR>m. ‘very renowned,’ N. of a son of Soma-datta (king<BR>of the Bālhīkas).<BR>—भूरि-श्रेष्ठिक, N. of a<BR>building in Benares; (also read भूरि-श्रेष्ठक.)<BR>—भूरि-षह् or भूरि-षाह्, ट्, m., Ved. (a<BR>chariot) bearing or carrying much (Sāy. = भूरि-<BR>भारस्य सोढा).<BR>—भूरि-षेण, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>many armies,’ N. of a man; of a son of the tenth<BR>Manu; of the king Śaryāti.<BR>—भूरि-स्थात्र, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, Ved. having many stations, being at many<BR>places or spots.<BR>—भूरि-हन्, आ, m. ‘many-killer,’<BR>N. of an Asura.<BR>—भूर्य्-अक्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved.<BR>many-eyed.<BR>—भूर्य्-आसुति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. much-<BR>excited, much-exciting; (Sāy.) having much Soma<BR>poured forth (= बहुषु देशेषु सोम आसूयते or<BR>बहूनि सोमादि-हवींष्य् आसूयन्ते इति तादृशः).<BR>—भूर्य्-ओजस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. having great power,<BR>very vigorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिक
भूरिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्णु|भूष्णुः
भूष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, = भविष्णु, भवितृ,<BR>being, becoming, being or faring well; desiring<BR>happiness, wishing for wealth and prosperity (see<BR>Manu IV. 135).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूःखार
भूःखार भूःखार, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from<BR>Bokhara (as horses &c., cf. भुःखार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूक|भूकं|भूकः
भूक भूक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr.<BR>rt. 1. भू), a cavity, hole, chasm; the cavity from<BR>which a stream issues, the source of a stream, a<BR>spring; time; (अस्), m. darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकल|भूकलः
भूकल भूकल, अस्, m. a restive or un-<BR>manageable horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूताली
भूताली भूताली, f., N. of two plants (=<BR>भू-पाटली, मुसली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूना
भूना भूना, f., N. of a district; (for. भूना,<BR>inst. c. of भूमन्, see भूमन्, p. 717, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमि|भूमिः
भूमि भूमि, भूमी, &c. See p. 717, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिआण
भूमिआण भूमिआण and भूमीयाण, N. of<BR>two places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्
भूयस् 2. भूयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (according to<BR>Pāṇini VI. 4, 158, compar. of बहु, q. v.; for 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">Page0719-a+ 78</a>]<BR>भूयस् see p. 718, col. 2), more, more numerous,<BR>more abundant; greater, larger, mightier; more im-<BR>portant; much, many, numerous; very great, impor-<BR>tant; vehement, severe; abounding in, abundantly<BR>furnished with (with inst., e. g. गुणैर् भूयान्,<BR>abounding in qualities); (अस्), ind. more, most, very<BR>much, much, exceedingly, largely, over and above,<BR>still more, more and more, further on, further, be-<BR>sides, moreover, even; again, anew, afresh, fre-<BR>quently, repeatedly; भूयो भूयः, again and again;<BR>पूर्वम् — भूयः, first — next; in the first place —<BR>in the next place; (असा), ind. very much, exceed-<BR>ingly, beyond measure, excessively, in a high degree;<BR>mostly, generally, as a general rule; [cf. Hib. bhus,<BR>a sign of the comparative degree, always having ni<BR>before it, as ni bhus airde, ‘higher.’]<BR>—भूय-शस्,<BR>ind. mostly, generally, as a general rule, commonly;<BR>again, anew, afresh.<BR>—भूयस्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, or<BR>भूयस्-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. making or doing more;<BR>augmenting, increasing.<BR>—भूयस्-तरम् or भू-<BR>यस्-तराम्, ind. more, anew, afresh, again.<BR>—भू-<BR>यस्-त्व, अम्, n. ‘moreness,’ the being more or<BR>greater, muchness, a large quantity, abundance, mul-<BR>titude, manifoldness, multiplicity; majority, prepon-<BR>derance, surplus, surplusage, overplus.<BR>—भूयो-विद्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, knowing more, more learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्विन्
भूयस्विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. more numerous or<BR>abundant; superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठ|भूयिष्ठं
भूयिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of बहु), most,<BR>most numerous, most abundant; very abundant<BR>or numerous, many, much, very great, very, (भू-<BR>यिष्ठे निकटे, very near, in the closest proximity);<BR>chief, principal, most important; consisting principally<BR>of, chiefly filled with or characterized by (= प्राय,<BR>often at the end of comps., e. g. शूद्र-भ्˚, q. v.;<BR>अहङ्कार-दर्प-भूयिष्ठ, chiefly characterized<BR>by or filled with egotism and pride); nearly all,<BR>almost, (especially after a past passive part., e. g.<BR>गत-भूयिष्ठ, almost gone; cf. निर्वाण-भ्˚);<BR>(अम्), ind. for the most part, mostly, almost, chiefly;<BR>abundantly or numerously, in the highest degree,<BR>very much; (एन), ind. for the most part, mostly.<BR>—भूयिष्ठ-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. sharing princi-<BR>pally, enjoying the largest share, receiving most.<BR>—भूयिष्ठ-शस्, ind. in very large numbers, very<BR>numerously.<BR>भूरि भूरि. See p. 718, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिज्
भूरिज् भूरिज्, क्, f. the earth; (incorrectly<BR>for भुरिज्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज|भूर्जः|भूर्ज्ज
भूर्ज भूर्ज, अस्, m. a species of birch (the<BR>Bhoj or Bhojpatra tree, the bark of which is used<BR>for writing on); [cf. Old Germ. birca, bircha;<BR>Mod. Germ. birke; Engl. birch; Lith. berza-s.]<BR>—भूर्ज-कण्टक, अस्, m. a man of one of the<BR>mixed classes, the son of an outcast Brāhman by<BR>a woman of the same tribe (see Manu X. 21).<BR>—भूर्ज-पत्त्र, अस्, m. = भूर्ज above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्णि|भूर्णिः
भूर्णि भूर्णि, इस्, इस्, इ (probably fr. rt. भुर्,<BR>but said in Uṇādi-s. IV. 52. to be fr. rt. भृ), Ved.<BR>active, agile, moving restlessly, restless, wild, excited,<BR>irritated, (according to Sāy. = भर्तृ, भरण-<BR>शील, supporting, accustomed to bear); (इस्), f. the<BR>earth; a desert, a country ill-supplied with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्
भूष् भूष्, cl. 1. P. भूषति, बुभूष,<BR>भूषितुम्, to strive after, use efforts for,<BR>care for (with dat., Ved.); to adorn, decorate; (in<BR>the Veda a rt. भूष् is found, which is regarded by<BR>Sāy. as a form of 1. भू in the sense of ‘to obtain,<BR>attain;’ thus in Ṛg-veda IV. 16, 11. भूषात् =<BR>प्र-भवते, and in VIII. 92, 26. भूषसि = भ-<BR>वसि); cl. 10. or Caus. भूषयति (rarely A. -ते),<BR>भूषयाम्-आस, भूषयितुम्, to adorn, decorate,<BR>embellish, attire; to spread or strew over with (any-<BR>thing); to adorn one's self (A.); [cf. Hib. beosai-<BR>ghim, ‘I adorn.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषण|भूषणं|भूषणः
भूषण, अस्, ई, अम्, decorating, adorning; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of a Daitya; (अस्, अम्), m.<BR>n. ornament, decoration, embellishment (generally<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">Page0719-b+ 79</a>]<BR>अम्, n., often at the end of comps., cf. कर्ण-भ्˚;<BR>sometimes at the end of an adj. comp., e. g. कनक-<BR>भूषण, अस्, आ, अम्, decorated with gold); (अम्),<BR>n. ‘the act of decorating or adorning,’ N. of a work.<BR>—भूषण-ता, f. the being an ornament, ornature.<BR>—भूषण-सार-दर्पण, अस्, m. ‘mirror of<BR>the essence of decoration,’ N. of a commentary on<BR>the Vaiyākaraṇa-bhūṣaṇa.<BR>—भूषणेन्द्र-प्रभ<BR>(˚ण-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king of the Kinnaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषणीय
भूषणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be adorned, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषत्
भूषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. striving after; (Sāy.)<BR>adorning, ornamenting (= भूषयत्, अलङ्कुर्वत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषयत्
भूषयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, adorning, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषयितव्य
भूषयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be decorated or<BR>ornamented, to be adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषयित्वा
भूषयित्वा, ind. having adorned, having deco-<BR>rated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषा
भूषा, f. adorning, decorating, ornament, deco-<BR>ration; a jewel; [cf. कर्ण-भ्˚, बाहु-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषित|भूषितः
भूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned, decorated, orna-<BR>mented, embellished, garnished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषिन्
भूषिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. भूषा), adorned or deco-<BR>rated with (usually at the end of comps.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्य
भूष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be adorned or decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्णु|भूष्णुः
भूष्णु भूष्णु. See p. 718, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्तृण|भूस्तृणं|भूस्तृणः
भूस्तृण भू-स्-तृण. See p. 716, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृ
भृ भृ (allied to rt. धृ and to rt. हृ,<BR>which was probably evolved fr. rt. भृ), cl. 1.<BR>P. A. भरति, -ते, cl. 3. P. A. बिभर्ति, बिभृते<BR>(1st du. P. बिभृवस्, 3rd pl. बिभ्रति), Impf.<BR>अबिभर्, अबिभृत (3rd pl. अबिभरुस्), Pot. बि-<BR>भृयात्, बिभ्रीत, Impv. बिभर्तु, बिभृताम् (2nd<BR>sing. P. बिभृहि), Perf. बभार, बभ्रे (2nd sing.<BR>P. बभर्थ, 2nd du. P. बभृव by Pāṇ. VII. 2, 13,<BR>cf. Gram. 369), or बिभरां-चकार, बिभरां-<BR>चक्रे (also बिभराम्-आस, बिभराम्-बभूव),<BR>1st Fut. भर्ता, 2nd Fut. भरिष्यति, -ते, Aor.<BR>अभार्षीत्, अभृत (1st sing. अभार्षम्, 2nd<BR>du. अभार्ष्टम्), Prec. भ्रियात्, भृषीष्ट,<BR>Cond. अभरिष्यत्, अभरिष्यत (Vedic and ir-<BR>regular forms are Pres. भर्ति, 1st pl. बिभृमसि,<BR>Impf. अबिभ्रत्, बिभरत्, Perf. जभार, जभर्-<BR>थ, जभ्रुस्, A. जभ्रे, जभ्रिरे, जभरत्, ज-<BR>भर्तन, Aor. अभारिषम्, भर्षत्, अभार्),<BR>Inf. भर्तुम् (Ved. भर्तवे, अप-भर्तवै, भर्-<BR>तोस्, भरसे, भरध्यै), to bear, carry; to sup-<BR>port, maintain, keep, sustain, nourish, foster, cherish,<BR>protect, take care of; to hire, keep in one's pay,<BR>give wages or pay to (generally A.); to wear; to<BR>possess, have; to hold, contain, retain (as in the<BR>memory); to keep up, maintain; to endure, suffer;<BR>to carry to (any person or place), bring; to confer,<BR>bestow, give, produce; to fill, fill up, load; to carry<BR>away, take away, transport; to raise the voice, raise<BR>a sound (Ved.); to be borne along rapidly (A. Ved.,<BR>Lat. ferri); to take or carry away for one's self,<BR>acquire, gain (A. Ved.); to be borne upwards (as<BR>sound, A. Ved.). The above meanings of rt. भृ<BR>may be variously extended by connecting it with<BR>various nouns, e. g. गर्भम् भृ, to conceive,<BR>become pregnant [cf. गर्भं धृ under rt. धृ];<BR>श्मश्रु-लोम-नखानि भृ, to wear the hair, beard,<BR>and nails long, i. e. allow them to grow without cutting<BR>(Manu VI. 6); विभ्रमम् भृ, to make playful<BR>movements or to have the appearance of moving<BR>about; ऊर्जाम् भृ, to exert the strength; क्षितिम्<BR>भृ, to take care of, i. e. govern the earth: Pass.<BR>भ्रियते, Aor. अभारि (Ved. forms भरते, part.<BR>भुरमाण, बभ्राण, बिभ्रमाण): Caus. भा-<BR>रयति, -यितुम्, अबीभरत्, to cause to bear or<BR>support; to put out to hire, engage for hire: Desid.<BR>बुभूर्षति, -ते, बिभरिषति, -ते (Pāṇ. VII. 2,<BR>49), to wish to bear, to wish or intend to support or<BR>maintain [cf. बुभूर्षु]: Intens. बेभ्रीयते, बर्-<BR>भर्ति, बरीभर्ति (Ved. 3rd pl. भरिभ्रति, part.<BR>भरिभ्रत्), to bear repeatedly, to bear or carry<BR>hither and thither; to maintain continually; [cf.<BR>Zend bar, ‘to bear, bring:’ Gr. φέρ-ω, φέρ-μα,<BR>φέρ-ε-τρο-ω, φαρ-έ-τρα, φόρ-ο-ς, φορό-ς, φορ-ά,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">Page0719-c+ 81</a>]<BR>φορ-μό-ς, φόρ-το-ς, φερ-νή; φάρ-μα-κο-ν; φέρ-τερος,<BR>φέρ-ιστο-ς, φέρ-τα-το-ς; φέρ-β-ω, φορ-β-ή;<BR>φᾶρος; φωρ-ιαμός; δί-φρο-ς, δι-φθέρα: Lat. fero,<BR>fer in belli-fer, fer-cu-lu-m, fer-āx, for-du-s,<BR>far, far-īna, fer-ti-li-s, for(t)-s, for-tū-na, for-<BR>tu-itu-s; pro-bru-m, op-pro-br-iu-m (προ-φέρ-ειν),<BR>candela-bru-m; her-b-a, fi-b-ra, forb-ea: Goth.<BR>bair-an, ‘to bear;’ ga-baur, ‘tax;’ baur-ei or<BR>baur-thei, ‘a burden;’ ga-baur-th-s, ‘birth;’ bar-n,<BR>‘a child;’ ber-usyōs, ‘parents;’ barm-s, ‘womb;’<BR>baris, ‘barley;’ brigg-an, ‘to bring:’ Old Germ.<BR>bur-di, ‘a burden;’ bāra, ‘a barrow, bier:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. ber-an, ‘to bear;’ bearm, ‘womb;’ bearn,<BR>‘a child;’ byrdhen, ‘a burden;’ bring-an, ‘to<BR>bring:’ Slav. bra-ti, ‘to bear;’ bre†-me, ‘a load;’<BR>bra-kŭ, ‘wedlock:’ Boh. bra-ti, ‘to take;’ ber-nĕ,<BR>‘tax:’ Lith. bér-na-s, ‘a child, servant:’ Hib. beir-<BR>im, ‘I bear, carry.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्राण
बभ्राण, अस्, आ, अम् (Perf. part. A.), one who<BR>has borne, &c.; being borne (fr. the Pass.; according<BR>to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 1, 8, = सर्वैर् धार्य-<BR>माण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रत्|बिभ्रन्त्
बिभ्रत्, अत्, अती, अत् (Pres. part. P.), bearing,<BR>carrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्राण
बिभ्राण, अस्, आ, अम् (Pres. part. A.), bearing,<BR>carrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्
भृत्, त्, त्, त्, (at the end of comps.) bearing,<BR>carrying [cf. शस्त्रास्त्र-भ्˚], supporting, maintain-<BR>ing [cf. धर्म-भ्˚], nourishing, protecting [cf.<BR>क्षिति-भ्˚]; possessing, having, furnished or pro-<BR>vided with [cf. जन्म-भ्˚]; bringing, procuring,<BR>conferring; a bearer, maintainer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत|भृतः
भृत, अस्, आ, अम्, borne, carried, supported,<BR>maintained, cherished; hired, kept in pay, paid,<BR>(क्षीर-भृतः, a servant whose wages are paid<BR>with milk, Manu VIII. 231); possessed of, endowed<BR>with, having earned, acquired, gained; filled, full of;<BR>(अस्), m. a hireling, hired servant or labourer, mer-<BR>cenary.<BR>—भृत-भूति, इस्, इस्, इ, possessing power<BR>or prosperity, powerful, prosperous; smeared with<BR>ashes.<BR>—भृत-रन्ध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, filled up (as<BR>a hole or depression).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतक|भृतकः
भृतक, अस्, आ, अम्, hired, kept in pay, receiving<BR>wages; (अस्), m. a hired labourer, a servant.<BR>—भृ-<BR>तकाध्यापक (˚क-अध्˚), अस्, m. a hired teacher,<BR>one who gives instruction for pay.<BR>—भृतकाध्या-<BR>पित, अस्, आ, अम्, taught by a hired teacher; (अस्), m.<BR>a student who pays his teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृति|भृतिः
भृति, इस्, f. the act of bearing, carrying, sup-<BR>porting, maintaining, nourishing; bringing [cf.<BR>इध्म-भ्˚]; service for wages; nourishment, sup-<BR>port, maintenance, sustenance, food [cf. दुर्-भ्˚];<BR>wages, hire; capital, principal.<BR>—भृति-भुज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, enjoying or living on wages; (क्), m. a hired<BR>servant, labourer.<BR>—भृति-रूप, a reward given to<BR>a person in lieu of wages for the performance of a<BR>duty for which stipulated payment or hire is im-<BR>proper (as for the performance of a Śrāddha in<BR>behalf of another person).<BR>—भृत्य्-अध्यापन,<BR>अम्, n. instructing for wages, teaching (especially the<BR>Vedas) for hire.<BR>—भृत्य्-अन्न, अम्, n. wages and<BR>board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतिन्
भृतिन्, ई, इनी, इ, supporting, maintaining, fos-<BR>tering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्य|भृत्यः
भृत्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be nourished or main-<BR>tained; (अस्), m. one who is to be supported, a<BR>dependent, servant, (किम्-भृत्य, a bad servant),<BR>slave; subject; the servant of a king, a minister [cf.<BR>राज-भ्˚]; (आ), f. fostering, rearing; service, de-<BR>pendence; maintenance, support, sustenance, food;<BR>hire, wages.<BR>—भृत्य-काम-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, acting<BR>kindly to servants.<BR>—भृत्य-जन, अस्, m. a person<BR>to be supported, a dependent.<BR>—भृत्य-ता, f. or<BR>भृत्य-त्व, अम्, n. the condition of a servant, servi-<BR>tude, service, dependence.<BR>—भृत्य-भरण, अम्,<BR>n. maintaining or cherishing dependents or servants,<BR>&c.<BR>—भृत्य-भर्तृ, ता, m. one who maintains or<BR>supports dependents, the master of a family.<BR>—भृ-<BR>त्य-भाविन्, ई, इनी, इ, being or becoming a servant,<BR>about to become a dependent.<BR>—भृत्य-वर्ग,<BR>अस्, m. ‘servant-class,’ the whole number of any one's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">Page0720-a+ 76</a>]<BR>servants, assemblage of dependents, household.<BR>—भृत्य-वात्सल्य, अम्, n. kindness to depend-<BR>ents or servants.<BR>—भृत्य-वृत्ति, इस्, f. maintenance<BR>of servants or dependents (Manu XI. 7).<BR>—भृ-<BR>त्य-शालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having many servants.<BR>—भृ-<BR>त्याध्यापन (˚य-अध्˚), अम्, n. teaching the<BR>Veda for hire [cf. भृत्य्-अध्यापन].<BR>—१. भृ-<BR>त्या-भाव, अस्, m. a state of servitude or dependence.<BR> — 2. भृत्याभाव (˚य-अभ्˚), अस्, m. the absence<BR>of servants.<BR>—भृत्यी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भ-<BR>वितुम्, to become a servant, enter upon service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्याय
भृत्याय, Nom. A. भृत्यायते, &c., to behave<BR>like a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृथ
भृथ, Ved. the offering (of the Soma); the<BR>vessel in which the Soma is offered, (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda II. 14, 4, भृथे = सोमम् बि-<BR>भ्रति पात्रे or सोमस्य भरणे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृंश्
भृंश् भृंश् cl. 1. 10. P. भृंशति, भृंश-<BR>यति, &c., to speak; to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुंश|भृकुंशः
भृकुंश भृकुंश or भृकुंस or भृकुं-<BR>सक, अस्, m. a male actor or dancer in female attire<BR>[cf. भ्रूकुंश, भ्रुकुंश, भ्रकुंश].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुटि|भृकुटिः
भृकुटि भृ-कुटि, इस्, or भृ-कुटी, f. (cor-<BR>rupted fr. भ्रू-कुटि, see भ्रू), contraction or knit-<BR>ting of the eyebrow, a frown; (ई), f. a species of<BR>frog; (with Jainas) N. of a goddess executing the<BR>commands of the eighth Arhat of the present Ava-<BR>sarpiṇī; (इस्), m. (with Jainas) N. of the servant of<BR>the twentieth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī.<BR>—भृकुटि-मुख = भ्रुकुटि-मुख, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृक्ष्
भृक्ष् भृक्ष् or भ्रक्ष्, cl. 1. P. A.<BR>भृक्षति, -ते, भ्रक्षति, -ते, &c.,<BR>various reading for rt. भक्ष्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृग्
भृग् भृग्, an onomatopoetic word used<BR>to express the crackling sound of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगमात्रिक
भृगमात्रिक भृगमात्रिक, अस्, m. probably<BR>wrongly for मृग-मात्रिक or मृग-मतृक.<BR>See मृग-मातृका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगल
भृगल भृगल, see Kātyāyana's Śrauta-s.<BR>IX. 11, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगवाण
भृगवाण भृगवाण. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगु|भृगुः
भृगु भृगु, उस्, m., अवस्, m. pl. (fr. rt. 1. भ्राज्,<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्, to scorch; according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 127, 7, भृगवः = हविषाम्<BR>पापानां वा भ्रष्टारः, roasters or consumers of<BR>oblations or of sins), Ved., N. of a mythical race of<BR>beings (frequently mentioned in connection with Agni<BR>and classed in Naighaṇṭuka V. 5. with the Aṅgirasas,<BR>Atharvans, Ṛbhus, &c.; they are described in the<BR>Ṛg-veda as cherishing Fire brought to them by the<BR>Wind [Mātari-śvan], or as kindling Fire from the<BR>wood of attrition; in Ṛg-veda IV. 16, 20, and one<BR>or two other passages, they are said to fabricate<BR>chariots); the descendants of Bhṛgu; (उस्), m., N.<BR>of a Ṛṣi regarded as the ancestor of the whole race<BR>of Bhṛgus, (he is sometimes described as the off-<BR>spring of Prajā-pati, but in Manu 1. 35. is enumerated<BR>among the ten Maharṣis or primeval patriarchs<BR>created by the first Manu; according to Sāy., Varuṇa<BR>adopted him as his son, whence he is called Vāruṇi<BR>and is regarded as the author of Ṛg-veda IX. 65,<BR>X. 19); N. of one of the chief Brāhmanical families<BR>(the Aitaśayanas are said to belong to it); N. of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; of a son of Kavi; of one of the Prajā-patis<BR>(produced from Brahmā's skin); of one of the seven<BR>sages (an Adhvaryu at the Rāja-sūya of Soma, Hari-<BR>vaṃśa 1334); of the father of Cyavana and six<BR>others; of the father of Dhātṛ and Vidhātṛ; of the<BR>father of Śrī (by Khyāti); of the author of a Dharma-<BR>śāstra (who also communicated the Ganeśa-Purāṇa to<BR>Soma-kānta); N. of the son of Jamad-agni; of the<BR>Ṛṣi Jamad-agni himself; of Śukra or the planet<BR>Venus (called either Bhṛgu or the son of Bhṛgu;<BR>the day of Bhṛgu is the sixth day of the week, i. e.<BR>Friday); N. of Rudra (according to some); of a<BR>son of Artha-pati and uncle of the poet Bāṇa;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-b" target="_blank">Page0720-b+ 80</a>]<BR>table land, the level summit of a mountain; a<BR>declivity, slope, cliff, precipice [cf. भृगु-पतन].<BR>—भृगु-कच्छ, N. of a sacred place on the<BR>northern bank of the river Narma-dā; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the inhabitants of this place.<BR>—भृगु-ज or भृगु-<BR>तनय, अस्, m. ‘son of Bhṛgu,’ the planet Venus.<BR>—भृगु-तुङ्ग, अस्, m. ‘Bhṛgu's peak,’ N. of a<BR>sacred mountain in the Himālaya, (sometimes called<BR>भृगोस् तुङ्ग.)<BR>—भृगु-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of Bhṛgu,’ the planet Venus [cf. भृगु-ज, भृगु-<BR>पुत्र, भृगु-सुत]; an epithet of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-पतन, अम्, n. a fall from a precipice,<BR>&c.<BR>—भृगु-पति, इस्, m. ‘chief of the Bhṛgus,’<BR>an epithet of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-पात, अस्, m.<BR>precipitating one's self from a precipice.<BR>—भृगु-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. ‘son of Bhṛgu,’ the planet Venus.<BR>—भृगु-प्रस्रवण, ‘Bhṛgu's spring,’ N. of a<BR>mountain, probably = Bhṛgu-tuṅga.<BR>—भृगु-भू-<BR>मि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Aṅgiras (belonging to the<BR>family of the Bhṛgus; cf. भर्ग-भूमि, भार्ग-<BR>भूमि).<BR>—भृगु-मण्डल, अम्, n. (in astronomy)<BR>‘Bhṛgu's circle,’ N. of a Karaṇa, q. v.<BR>—भृगु-<BR>राक्षस, अस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi (said to have sacri-<BR>ficed men and cows).<BR>—भृगु-वंश, अस्, m. ‘race<BR>of Bhṛgu,’ N. of a family deriving their origin from<BR>Parśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-वल्ली, f., N. of the third<BR>Vallī in the Taittirīyopaniṣad.<BR>—भृगु-वार, अस्,<BR>m. the day of Venus, Friday.<BR>—भृगु-शार्दूल,<BR>अस्, m. ‘most excellent of the Bhṛgus,’ an epithet<BR>of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. ‘best<BR>of the Bhṛgus,’ epithet of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-<BR>सत्तम, अस्, m. ‘best of the Bhṛgus,’ epithet of<BR>Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-सुत, अस्, m. ‘Bhrigu's son,’<BR>the planet Venus or Śukra (who was preceptor of<BR>the Daityas); an epithet of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-<BR>सूनु, उस्, m. ‘Bhṛgu's son,’ the planet Venus.<BR>—भृगूद्वह (˚गु-उद्˚), अस्, m. ‘offspring of<BR>Bhṛgu,’ an epithet of Paraśu-rāma.<BR>—भृगु-अङ्गि-<BR>रस्, आस्, m., Ved., N. of the author of certain<BR>Atharva-veda hymns (supposed to avert diseases).<BR>—भृगु-अङ्गिरो-विद्, त्, त्, त्, knowing (the verses<BR>or hymns of) Bhṛgu and Aṅgiras (i. e. of the<BR>Atharvans and Aṅgirasas or Atharva-veda).<BR>—भृग्व्-<BR>ईश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्, n. ‘Tīrtha of Bhṛgu's lord,’ N.<BR>of a sacred bathing-place on the Narma-dā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगवाण
भृगवाण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. imitating Bhṛgu,<BR>acting like Bhṛgu, i. e. shining, glittering (Sāy. =<BR>भृगु-वद् आचरत् = दीप्यमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृग्वन्दीय
भृग्वन्दीय, अस्, m. a N. (probably wrong).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्ग|भृंग|भृङ्गं|भृंगः|भृङ्गः
भृङ्ग भृङ्ग, अस्, आ, ई, m. f. (probably fr.<BR>rt. भ्रम्, cf. भ्रमर; said in Uṇādi-s. I. 124.<BR>to be fr. rt. भृ), a species of large black bee, the<BR>humble bee; (अस्), m. = भृङ्गरोल, a species of<BR>wasp, either the common kind or the Vespa Solitaria;<BR>the fork-tailed shrike, Lanius Cærulescens; a bird,<BR>apparently a sort of shrike different from the pre-<BR>ceding; a libertine, catamite, lecher; the plant<BR>Eclipta Prostrata (= भृङ्ग-राज, मार्कव, केश-<BR>राज); = भृङ्गार, a golden vase or pitcher; (ई),<BR>f. a species of poisonous plant, = अति-विषा; (अम्),<BR>n. woody Cassia (= त्वक्-पत्त्र); the plant Eclipta<BR>Prostrata or Verbesina Prostrata; talc; [cf. पञ्च-<BR>भ्˚.]<BR>—भृङ्ग-ज, अम्, n. aloe wood or Agallo-<BR>chum; (आ), f. the plant Clerodendrum Siphonanthus<BR>(= भार्गी).<BR>—भृङ्ग-पर्णिका, f. small carda-<BR>moms.<BR>—भृङ्ग-प्रिया, f. ‘liked by bees,’ the plant<BR>Gærtnera Racemosa.<BR>—भृङ्ग-मारी, f. = भृङ्-<BR>गारि.<BR>—भृङ्ग-मूलिका, f. a species of plant (=<BR>भ्रमर-च्छल्ली).<BR>—भृङ्ग-रज, अस्, or भृङ्-<BR>ग-रजस्, आस्, m. the plant Eclipta Prostrata.<BR>—भृङ्ग-रस, अस्, m. the juice of the plant<BR>Eclipta Prostrata.<BR>—भृङ्ग-राज, अस्, m. ‘bee-<BR>king,’ a species of large bee, the humble bee; a<BR>species of bird (apparently the variety of shrike<BR>termed Malabar, Lanius Malabaricus); a spreading<BR>shrub, Eclipta Prostrata [cf. नील-भ्˚, पीत-भ्˚]; a<BR>kind of oblation or sacrifice.<BR>—भृङ्ग-राजक, अस्,<BR>m. a species of bird.<BR>—भृङ्गराज-रस, अस्, m.<BR>the juice of the plant Eclipta Prostrata.<BR>—भृङ्ग-<BR>वल्लभ, अस्, m. ‘favourite of bees,’ a species of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">Page0720-c+ 76</a>]<BR>Kadamba plant, Ligusticum Ajowan, = धारा-क-<BR>दम्ब and भूमि-कदमब; (आ), f. = भूमि-<BR>जम्बू.<BR>—भृङ्ग-वृक्ष, अस्, m. ‘bee-tree,’ per-<BR>haps = भृङ्ग-रजस्.<BR>—भृङ्ग-सोदर, अस्, m.<BR>the plant Eclipta Prostrata.<BR>—भृङ्गाधिप (˚ग-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘bee-chief,’ the queen of the bees.<BR>—भृङ्गानन्दा (˚ग-आन्˚), f. ‘bee-joy,’ the plant<BR>Jasminum Auriculatum (= यूथिका).<BR>—भृङ्गा-<BR>भीष्ट (˚ग-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘liked by bees,’ the<BR>Mango tree.<BR>—भृङ्गारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m. ‘bee-<BR>enemy,’ a species of flower growing in Mālwa (=<BR>केविका).<BR>—भृङ्गावली (˚ग-आव्˚), f. a line or flight<BR>of bees.<BR>—भृङ्गाह्व (˚ग-आह्˚), अस्, m. the plant<BR>Eclipta Prostrata; another plant, = जीवक; (आ), f.<BR>another plant (= भ्रमर-च्छल्ली).<BR>—भृङ्गी-<BR>फल, अस्, m. the hog-plum, Spondias Mangifera.<BR>—भृङ्गेष्टा (˚ग-इष्˚), f. ‘liked by bees,’ N.<BR>of several plants (= घृत-कुमारी, भार्गी, त-<BR>रुणी, काक-जम्बू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गक|भृंगकः|भृङ्गकः
भृङ्गक, अस्, m. the fork-tailed shrike; (at the<BR>end of an adj. comp.) = भृङ्ग, a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरिटि|भृंगरिटि|भृङ्गरिटिः
भृङ्गरिटि or भृङ्गरीटि, इस्, m. or भृङ्ग-<BR>रीट, अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's attendants; [cf.<BR>भृङ्गिन्, भृङ्गीरिटि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरोल|भृंगरोल|भृङ्गरोलः
भृङ्गरोल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. भृङ्ग and<BR>rt. रु, to cry), a kind of wasp; [cf. वरोल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गाय
भृङ्गाय, Nom. A. भृङ्गायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>become a bee, behave like a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गार|भृंगार|भृंगारं|भृङ्गारं|भृंगारः|भृङ्गारः
भृङ्गार, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>भृ), a golden pitcher or vase; a vase used at the<BR>inauguration of a king, (it might be made of any<BR>one of eight different substances, viz. gold, silver,<BR>brass, iron, earthenware, sandal-wood, crystal, or<BR>horn, and might be of eight differents forms); (अस्),<BR>m. = भृङ्ग-राज, the shrub Eclipta Prostrata; (ई),<BR>f. a cricket; (अम्), n. cloves; gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गारक
भृङ्गारक, अस्, m. = भृङ्गार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गारिका|भृंगारिका
भृङ्गारिका, f. = भृङ्गारी, a cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गारीट
भृङ्गारीट, अस्, m. = भृङ्गरीट under भृङ्-<BR>गरिटि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गि|भृङ्गिः
भृङ्गि, इस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's attendants;<BR>[cf. भृङ्गिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गिन्|भृंगिन्
भृङ्गिन्, ई, m. the Indian fig-tree; N. of one<BR>of Śiva's attendants [cf. भृङ्गरिटि, भृङ्गिरिटि];<BR>N. of a people; (इणी), f. a species of tree (= वटी).<BR>—भृङ्गीश (˚गि-ईश), ‘lord of the Bhṛṅgins,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गिरिटि|भृंगिरिटि|भृंगिरिटिः|भृङ्गिरिटिः
भृङ्गिरिटि or भृङ्गीरिटि or भृङ्गिरीटि or<BR>भृङ्गेरिटि, इस्, m. = भृङ्गरिटि, q. v.; an epithet<BR>of Śiva?; [cf. भृङ्गीश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्
भृज् भृज् (connected with rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्),<BR>cl. 1. A. भर्जते, बभृजे, भर्जितुम्,<BR>to fry, parch, roast: Caus. भर्जयति, -यितुम्, Aor.<BR>अबभर्जत्, अबीभृजत्: Desid. बिभर्जिषते:<BR>Intens. बरीभृज्यते, बर्भर्क्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्जन|भर्जनं|भर्ज्जन
भर्जन, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. भ्रज्जन], roasting,<BR>frying, baking; annihilating; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>roasting, frying, scorching, parching; a frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृक्त
भृक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, roasted, fried; [cf. Lat.<BR>frictus, frixus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृजायन
भृजायन भृजायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्ज्
भृज्ज् भृज्ज्, भृट्, ट्, ट्, (fr. rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्),<BR>frying, roasting, baking; [cf. बहु-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्ज
भृज्ज in उद-भ्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्जन|भृज्जनं|भृज्जनः
भृज्जन, अम्, n., Ved. a frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृड्
भृड् भृड्, cl. 6. P. भृडति, &c., to<BR>dive, plunge; [cf. rt. क्रुड्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृणीय
भृणीय भृणीय, भृणीयते, &c., Ved. a<BR>verb given in Naighaṇṭuka II. 12. and said to mean<BR>‘to be angry;’ [cf. rt. भ्री and हृणीय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृण्टिका|भृंटिका
भृण्टिका भृण्टिका. See भिरिण्टिका, p. 711.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृण्डि|भृंडि|भृंडिः|भृण्डिः
भृण्डि भृण्डि, a wave; (also read भण्डि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत|भृतः
भृत भृत, भृत्य, &c. See p. 719, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृम|भृमः
भृम भृम, अस्, m. (fr. rt. भ्रम्), Ved.<BR>erring, aberration, error, mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृमल
भृमल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. perplexed, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृमि|भृमिः
भृमि, इस्, इस्, इ, [cf. भ्रमि], Ved. whirling<BR>round, wandering about (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IV. 32,<BR>2, III. 62, 1, = भ्रमण-शील), active, quick, ener-<BR>getic (Sāy. on Ṛg-veda I. 31, 16, = भ्रामक =<BR>कर्म-निर्वाहक), sprightly, gay; (इस्), m. a<BR>whirlwind, hurricane, high wind, (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda II. 34, 1, either a moving cloud or a<BR>kind of lute); a whirlpool, eddy; (इस्), f., Ved.<BR>quickness, activity, agility.<BR>—भृम्य्-अश्व, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved., N. of a man [cf. भार्म्यश्व].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश्
भृश् भृश् (connected with rt. भ्रंश्),<BR>cl. 4. P. भृश्यति, to fall, fall down; cl. 6.<BR>P. भृशति, &c., to be strong or vehement (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश|भृशं
भृश, अस्, आ, अम् (probably fr. rt. भृश् with a<BR>sense ‘to be strong,’ or perhaps contracted fr. भूरि-<BR>शस्), powerful, mighty, strong, vehement, intense,<BR>much, exceeding, frequent; (अम्), ind. vehemently,<BR>strongly, intensely, in a high degree, much, very,<BR>exceedingly, excessively, violently, powerfully, greatly,<BR>extremely, eminently, in a superior manner, beauti-<BR>fully, better, often, repeatedly, quickly.<BR>—भृश-<BR>कोपन, अस्, आ, अम्, extremely passionate, very<BR>wrathful.<BR>—भृश-ता, f. violence, vehemence, inten-<BR>sity; [cf. भार्श्य.]<BR>—भृश-दारुण, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>very terrible or cruel.<BR>—भृश-दुःखित, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, very much afflicted, very unfortunate or unhappy.<BR>—भृश-पीडित, अस्, आ, अम्, very much afflicted.<BR>—भृश-विस्मित, अस्, आ, अम्, excessively astonished<BR>or perplexed.<BR>—भृश-शोक-वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>greatly increasing grief or augmenting sorrow.<BR>—भृश-संहृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, very delighted,<BR>very glad.<BR>—भृश-स्विद्, त्, त्, त्, perspiring violently.<BR>—भृशी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become<BR>vehement, to become very powerful or strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृशाय
भृशाय, Nom. A. भृशायते, &c., to become<BR>powerful, to be strong or vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्ट|भृष्टः
1. भृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रशिष्ठ
भ्रशिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, (superl.) most powerful,<BR>very strong or violent, very vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रशीयस्
भ्रशीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, (compar.) more powerful,<BR>stronger, more violent or vehement, very vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्ट|भृष्टः
भृष्ट 2. भृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्),<BR>fried, broiled, grilled, roasted, parched, scorched, baked;<BR>(अम्), n. roasted meat.<BR>—भृष्ट-कार, अस्, m. a<BR>preparer of roasted or fried meat.<BR>—भृष्टान्न<BR>(˚ट-अन्˚), अम्, n. rice boiled and then fried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टि|भृष्टिः
1. भृष्टि, इस्, f. the act of frying, broiling,<BR>roasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टि|भृष्टिः
भृष्टि 2. भृष्टि, इस्, f. (perhaps fr. rt. हृष्),<BR>Ved. a spike, point, top, corner, edge [cf. सहस्र-<BR>भ्˚, क्षुर-भ्˚, तिग्म-भ्˚, पिशङ्ग-भ्˚]; an<BR>empty or deserted cottage, a deserted garden (=<BR>शून्य-वाटी or शून्य-वाटिका).<BR>—भृष्टि-मत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, pronged, toothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भॄ
भॄ भॄ, cl. 9. P. भृणाति, बभार, &c.,<BR>to blame; to bear, nourish, maintain, support,<BR>hold [cf. rt. भृ]; to fry; to bend, be crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेक|भेकः
भेक भेक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. भी),<BR>a frog, (according to the Kathā-sarit-sāgara XX. 77,<BR>the inarticulate sounds uttered by frogs were the<BR>result of the curse of Agni, who was betrayed by<BR>them to the gods when he took refuge in the water);<BR>a cloud; a timid man (= भीरु; cf. भेल); (ई), f.<BR>a female frog; a small frog; a kind of creeper,<BR>Hydrocotyle Asiatica.<BR>—भेक-पर्णी, f. ‘frog-<BR>leaved,’ a plant (= मण्डूक-पर्णी).<BR>—भेक-<BR>भुज्, क्, m. ‘frog-eater,’ a serpent, snake.<BR>—भेक-<BR>शब्द, अस्, m. the croaking of frogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेकुरि
भेकुरि भेकुरि, इस्, f., Ved., N. of particular<BR>asterisms (according to Colebrooke ‘nymphs of the<BR>moon,’ cf. Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā XVIII. 40, Śatapatha-<BR>Brāhmaṇa IX. 4, 1, 9, where भेकुरि is explained<BR>by भाकुरि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेड|भेडः
भेड भेड, or भेडक, अस्, m. (said by some<BR>to be fr. rt. भिल् with change of ल् into ड्), a ram,<BR>sheep, (in this sense also written भेड्र; cf. एड);<BR>a raft, float [cf. भेल]; N. of a physician; of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">Page0721-b+ 79</a>]<BR>lexicographer; of a Ṛṣi; (ई), f. a ewe; N. of one<BR>of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda (associated with<BR>Eḍī and Sameḍī in Mahā-bh. Śalya-parva 2631).<BR>—भेड-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेडर
भेडर, अस्, m., N. of an Agra-hāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेड्र|भेड्रः
भेड्र. See भेड, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेतव्य
भेतव्य भेतव्य. See p. 712, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेत्तव्य
भेत्तव्य भेत्तव्य, भेत्तृ. See p. 711, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद|भेदः
भेद भेद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. भिद्), breaking,<BR>splitting, cleaving, dividing, separating, dissolving;<BR>bursting, tearing, rending, piercing, perforation;<BR>breaking in or through, breaking open; violation,<BR>dissolution; interruption, disturbance; breach, rup-<BR>ture, fracture [cf. पर्व-भ्˚]; a hurt, injury, wound;<BR>a slit, chasm, fissure, cleft, chap; division, separation,<BR>partition, part, portion; gaping, parting asunder [cf.<BR>हनु-भ्˚]; discrimination, discernment; distinction,<BR>difference, kind, sort, species, variety; change, alter-<BR>ation, modification [cf. मति-भ्˚]; divulging, dis-<BR>closure (of a secret), betrayal, treachery, treason<BR>[cf. रहस्य-भ्˚, मन्त्र-भ्˚]; dissension, em-<BR>broilment, disunion, disagreement, schism, making<BR>mischief, creating divisions (among confederates);<BR>seducing or enticing an ally to one's own party by<BR>sowing dissensions &c. (one of the four Upāyas or<BR>means of success against an opponent, see उपाय);<BR>defeat; (in philosophy) dualism, duality; (in medi-<BR>cine) evacuation of the bowels; (in astronomy) a<BR>particular separation of the stars; (कुक्षि-भेद, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. epithet of one of the modes in which an<BR>eclipse terminates); (in the drama according to the<BR>Sāhitya-darpaṇa) = संहति-भेदन, प्रोत्साहन;<BR>N. of a people (Ved.); N. of a man (see Atharva-<BR>veda XII. 4, 49); (औ), m. du. pudendum muliebre.<BR>—भेद-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, or भेद-कारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, or भेद-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, making a breach, breaking<BR>through, bursting asunder; causing separation, pro-<BR>ducing dissension or disunion, separating, disuniting.<BR>—भेद-तस्, ind. according to difference; discrimi-<BR>nately, according to peculiarities or diversities; sepa-<BR>rately, singly, individually, (opposed to युग-पद्.)<BR>—भेद-दृष्टि, इस्, f. viewing or holding the<BR>Universe and the Deity to be different and distinct.<BR>—भेद-धिक्कार, अस्, m. ‘refutation of duality,’<BR>N. of a treatise by Nṛ-siṃha Āśrama controverting<BR>the Nyāya philosophy from a Vedānta point of<BR>view.<BR>—भेदधिक्कार-सत्क्रिया, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Nārāyaṇa Āśrama on the Bheda-dhik-<BR>kāra.<BR>—भेद-प्रकाश, अस्, m. ‘manifestation of<BR>duality,’ N. of a refutation by Śaṅkara Miśra of the<BR>non-dualistic Vedānta theory from a Nyāya point of<BR>view.<BR>—भेद-प्रत्यय, अस्, m. belief in dualism<BR>(in opposition to the doctrine that every thing is<BR>God).<BR>—भेद-बुद्धि, इस्, f. perception or idea of<BR>a difference or distinction.<BR>—भेद-वादिन्, ई, m. one<BR>who maintains the doctrine that God and the Uni-<BR>verse are distinct.<BR>—भेद-विधि, इस्, m. the faculty<BR>of discriminating or discerning (between two different<BR>objects).<BR>—भेद-विभीषिका, f., N. of a philoso-<BR>phical work.<BR>—भेद-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, capable of<BR>being divided or disunited, seducible, corruptible.<BR>—भेदाभेद, औ, m. du. disagreement and agree-<BR>ment, disunion and union.<BR>—भेदोन्मुख (˚द-<BR>उन्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, just about to burst into blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदक|भेदकः
भेदक, अस्, इका, अम्, who or what breaks or<BR>breaks open or divides; breaking, breaking through,<BR>causing division or separation; piercing; a mischief-<BR>maker; a destroyer; one who breaks through or diverts<BR>(the course of a stream, cf. Manu III. 163); distin-<BR>guishing, discriminating, defining; a distinguisher;<BR>(अस्, अम्?), m. n. an adjective; (इका), f. the act of<BR>breaking asunder, destruction, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदन|भेदनं|भेदनः
भेदन, अस्, आ or ई (?), अम्, breaking, bursting,<BR>tearing, splitting, piercing, perforating, dividing, se-<BR>parating; loosening (as the feces, in medicine), dis-<BR>solving, cathartic, purgative; (अस्), m. a hog; a<BR>species of sorrel [cf. अम्ल-भ्˚]; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>breaking or breaking asunder, bursting, splitting,<BR>piercing, cutting up, ripping open, dissolving, loosen-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">Page0721-c+ 75</a>]<BR>ing, fracture, rupture; the act of dividing or sepa-<BR>rating, division, separation, discrimination, making a<BR>difference; disclosing, betraying [cf. रहस्य-भ्˚];<BR>dissension, disunion, discord, disagreement; Asa<BR>Fœtida; (in astronomy) passing through a constel-<BR>lation or asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदनक
भेदनक in घट-भ्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदनीय
भेदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken, frangible;<BR>capable of being split or cut open; fit to be separated<BR>or distinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदित|भेदितः
भेदित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), broken,<BR>divided, separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिन्
भेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, who or what breaks or divides<BR>or splits &c., breaking, splitting, dividing, opening,<BR>dissolving; interrupting, disturbing; piercing, per-<BR>forating; hurting, wounding; loosening (the bowels),<BR>cathartic; separating, distinguishing; separating from<BR>(with abl.); causing to flow (as juice); having a dis-<BR>tinction or division; (in philosophy) one who sepa-<BR>rates spirit and matter or holds the doctrine of<BR>dualism; causing dissension; (ई), m. a species of<BR>sorrel; the ratan; (इनी), f. (with Tāntrikas) N. of a<BR>particular Śakti.<BR>—भेदि-त्व, अम्, n. separation,<BR>division, parting asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिर|भेदिरं
भेदिर, अम्, n. = भिदिर, a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदुर|भेदुरं
भेदुर, अम्, n. = भिदुर, a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद्य|भेद्यं
भेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be broken or split, to be<BR>divided or pierced or cut; capable of being broken<BR>or divided &c., frangible, divisible, fragile; to be<BR>cut or opened (in medicine); to be disclosed or<BR>betrayed; to be separated or distinguished; to be<BR>defined; to be set at variance or disunited; to be<BR>seduced or led away; (अम्), n. a substantive.<BR>—भे-<BR>द्य-रोग, अस्, m. any disease treated by incision or<BR>cutting.<BR>—भेद्य-लिङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, distinguished<BR>by the gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद्यक
भेद्यक in उत्पल-भ्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेन|भेनः
भेन भेन, भेश. See under 4. भ,<BR>p. 694, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेंपुर
भेंपुर भेम्पुर, अम्, n., N. of a Grāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेय
भेय भेय. See p. 712, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेयपाल
भेयपाल भेयपाल (?), अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेर|भेरः
भेर भेर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. भी),<BR>= भेरी, a kettle-drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरि|भेरिः
भेरि, इस्, or भेरी, f. (the latter is the more usual<BR>form), a kettle-drum; [cf. आभेरी.]<BR>—भेरी-घ्नत्,<BR>अन्, m. ‘striking a kettle-drum,’ a kettle-drummer.<BR>—भेरी-भाङ्-कार. अस्, m., N. of a poet, (perhaps<BR>for भेरी-झाङ्-कार.)<BR>—भेरी-स्वन-महा-स्वना,<BR>f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरुण्ड|भेरुंड|भेरुण्डं|भेरुण्डः
भेरुण्ड भेरुण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, (connected with<BR>rt. 1. भी), terrible, formidable, fearful, awful, (also<BR>read भेरण्ड); (अस्), m. a bird, (perhaps a parti-<BR>cular species of bird, also read भेरण्ड, cf. भा-<BR>रण्ड); a species of beast of prey (wolf, jackal, or<BR>hyena); N. of a form of Śiva; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>goddess (= काली); N. of a Yakṣiṇī or female attend-<BR>ant on Durgā; (अम्), n. conception, impregnation,<BR>pregnancy, (in this sense perhaps fr. rt. भृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरुण्डक|भेरुंडक|भेरुंडकः|भेरुण्डकः
भेरुण्डक, अस्, m. a jackal [cf. फेरु].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेल|भेलं|भेलः
भेल भेल, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. भी), timid,<BR>timorous, fearful; foolish, ignorant, unwise, simple-<BR>minded; tall; active, agile; unsteady (literally or<BR>figuratively), inconstant; (अस्), m. a boat, skiff, float,<BR>raft; N. of a Ṛṣi (supposed to be the author of<BR>some medical works, cf. भेड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेलक|भेलकं|भेलकः
भेलक, अस्, अम्, m. n. = भेल, a boat, raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेलु
भेलु भेलु, a particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेलूपुरा
भेलूपुरा भेलूपुरा, f., N. of a suburb of<BR>Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेष्
भेष् भेष् [cf. rts. 1. भी, भ्यस्], cl. 1.<BR>P. A. भेषति, भेषते, &c., to fear,<BR>dread, be afraid; (according to others) to move, go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषज|भेषजं
भेषज भेषज, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. भिषज्),<BR>making well or healthy, sanative, curative, curing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">Page0722-a+ 78</a>]<BR>(Ved.); (अम्), n. a remedy or cure, remedy against<BR>(with gen.); any drug or medicament, medicine,<BR>physic [cf. आस्राव-भ्˚]; any spell or charm against<BR>diseases (as particular verses of the Atharva-veda); a<BR>kind of fennel, Nigella Indica; (according to Nai-<BR>ghaṇṭuka 1. 12) water.<BR>—भेषज-कल्प, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a chapter of the Aṣṭāṅga-hṛdaya-saṃhitā by<BR>Vāg-bhaṭa.<BR>—भेषज-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—भेषज-ता, f., Ved. curativeness, healing<BR>power.<BR>—भेषज-भक्षण, अम्, n. ‘drug-eat-<BR>ing,’ the act of taking medicine.<BR>—भेषजागार<BR>(˚ज-आग्˚), अम्, n. ‘medicine-room, drug-room,’ a<BR>druggist's or apothecary's shop.<BR>—भेषजाङ्ग (˚ज-<BR>अङ्˚), अम्, n. anything taken after medicine, any<BR>vehicle or medium in which medicine is administered<BR>(as water gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0721-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषज्य
भेषज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, curative, sanitary, sanative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष|भैक्षं
भैक्ष भैक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भिक्षा), living<BR>by alms, subsisting by charity; (अम्), n. asking alms,<BR>begging, mendicancy, (भैक्षं चर् or भै-<BR>क्षाय गम्, to go about begging, beg); anything<BR>obtained by begging, begged food, charity, alms.<BR>—भैक्ष-काल, अस्, m. ‘alms-time,’ the time for<BR>alms or for bringing home anything obtained as<BR>alms.<BR>—भैक्ष-चरण or भैक्ष-चर्य, अम्,<BR>n. or भैक्ष-चर्या, f. the going about begging,<BR>plying for alms, collecting alms, begging.<BR>—भै-<BR>क्ष-जीविका, f. living on alms, subsisting by begging,<BR>mendicancy.<BR>—भैक्ष-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, eating alms-<BR>food, living on alms; (क्), m. a mendicant.<BR>—भै-<BR>क्ष-वृत्ति, इस्, f. the living on alms, mendicancy;<BR>(इस्, इस्, इ), living by charity.<BR>—भैक्षान्न (˚ष-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. ‘alms-food,’ food obtained as alms,<BR>begged food.<BR>—भैक्षाशिन् (˚ष-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>eating alms-food or food obtained by begging; (ई),<BR>m. a mendicant.<BR>—भैक्षाश्य, अम्, n. (fr. the<BR>preceding), the living on alms, subsisting by charity.<BR>—भैक्षाहार (˚ष-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, eating<BR>begged food or food given in charity; (अस्), m. one<BR>living on charity (Manu XI. 257), a mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षक
भैक्षक (at the end of an adj. comp.) =<BR>भैक्ष, alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षुक|भैक्षुकं|भैक्षुकः
भैक्षुक, अम्, n. (fr. भिक्षुक), a number of<BR>mendicants, assemblage or collection of beggars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष्य|भैक्ष्यं
भैक्ष्य, an incorrect form for भैक्ष above.<BR>—भैक्ष्य-काल, भैक्ष्य-चर्य, भैक्ष्य-<BR>वृत्ति, see भैक्ष-काल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैदिक
भैदिक भैदिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भेद),<BR>frangible, liable to fracture (? Pāṇ. V. 1, 64).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैम
भैम भैम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भीम), relating<BR>to Bhīma; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of Bhīma;<BR>(ई), f. ‘the daughter of Bhīma,’ a patronymic of<BR>Damayantī; a festival on the eleventh day of Māgha,<BR>when ceremonies with तिल or sesamum are performed<BR>in honour of Bhīma; [cf. Lith. baime†, ‘terror.’]<BR>—भैम-प्रवीर, अस्, m. the bravest of the<BR>Bhaimas, the chief of the Bhaimas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमगव
भैमगव, अस्, m. (fr. भीम-गव), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमरथ
भैमरथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भीम-रथ),<BR>relating to Bhīma-ratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमसेनि|भैमसेनिः
भैमसेनि, इस्, m. (fr. भीम-सेन), a patro-<BR>nymic of Divo-dāsa, (also written भैमसीनि);<BR>of Ghaṭotkaca, (also written भैमिसेनि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमसेन्य|भैमसेन्यः
भैमसेन्य, अस्, m. (fr. भीम-सेन), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमायन
भैमायन, अस्, m. a patronymic (see Scholiast<BR>on Pāṇ. VI. 2, 34).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमि
भैमि, इस्, m. (fr. भीम), a patronymic of<BR>Ghaṭotkaca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरव|भैरवं|भैरवः
भैरव भैरव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भीरु), for-<BR>midable, awful, horrible, terrific, terrible, horrid;<BR>miserable; relating to Bhairava; (अस्), m. a form of<BR>Śiva, (eight forms of Bhairavas are enumerated, viz.<BR>महा-भ्˚, संहार-भ्˚, असिताङ्ग-भ्˚, रुरु-भ्˚,<BR>काल-भ्˚, क्रोध-भ्˚, ताम्र-चूड-भ्˚ or क-<BR>पाल-भ्˚, चन्द्र-चूड-भ्˚ or रुद्र-भ्˚; other<BR>names of these forms are sometimes given, e. g.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">Page0722-b+ 78</a>]<BR>विद्या-राज, काम-र्˚, नाग-र्˚, सच्छन्द-र्˚,<BR>लम्बित-र्˚, देव-र्˚, उग्र-र्˚, विघ्न-र्˚); a man<BR>representing Bhairava; a Śivagaṇādhipa; a son of<BR>Śiva by Tārā-vatī (who was wife of Candra-śekhara,<BR>king of Karavīra-pura); N. of a Nāga; of a Yakṣa;<BR>of the author of the Pheṭkāriṇī-tantra; of a teacher<BR>of the Haṭha-vidyā; of two kings; of a hunter; of<BR>a river; of a Rāga or musical mode calculated to<BR>excite emotions of terror; (ई), f. a particular form<BR>of Durgā; a girl of twelve years (representing that<BR>goddess at the Durgā festival); N. of a Rāgiṇī or of<BR>a particular scale in the Hindū musical system; (अम्),<BR>n. terror, horror, the property of exciting terror,<BR>terribleness; = भैरव-तन्त्र below.<BR>—भैरव-<BR>कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, causing terror, formidable.<BR>—भैरव-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra men-<BR>tioned in Kṛṣṇānanda's Tantra-sāra.<BR>—भैरव-<BR>तर्जक, अस्, m. ‘awful threatener,’ an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu (properly of Śiva).<BR>—भैरव-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the state of being Bhairava or a form of Śiva.<BR>—भैरव-दीक्षित-तिलक, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—भैरव-नाथ-तन्त्र, अम्, n. ‘Tantra<BR>of the lord of terror,’ N. of a Tantra.<BR>—भैरव-<BR>यातना, f. a purificatory torment inflicted by Śiva<BR>as presiding deity of Benares on those who die<BR>there, to render their spirits fit for absorption into<BR>the essence of the Supreme (whereas those who are<BR>punished by Yama have to return to mundane exist-<BR>ence).<BR>—भैरवाग्रतस् (˚व-अग्˚), ind. in the<BR>presence of Bhairava.<BR>—भैरवाचार्य (˚व-आच्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR>—भैरवानन्द (˚व-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Yogin.<BR>—भैरवेन्द्र<BR>(˚व-इन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—भैरवेश (˚व-<BR>ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of terror,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>(properly of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवीय
भैरवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Bhairava (as<BR>a Tantra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरिक
भैरिक, अस्, m., N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa by<BR>Satya-bhāmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज|भैषजं|भैषजः
भैषज भैषज, अस्, m. (fr. भेषज), a<BR>sort of quail, Perdix Chinensis; (आस्), m. pl. of the<BR>patronymic Bhaiṣajya below; (अम्), n. a drug,<BR>medicine, medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज्य|भैषज्यं
भैषज्य, अस्, m. the descendant of a physician;<BR>a patronymic from Bhiṣaj; (अम्), n. the adminis-<BR>tering of medicines and healing applications to the<BR>sick; curativeness, healing efficacy; a particular<BR>ceremony (performed as a remedy for sickness); any<BR>remedy, drug, medicine, medicament.<BR>—भैषज्य-<BR>गुरु-वैदूर्य-प्रभा, f., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—भैषज्य-रत्नावली, f., N. of a medical work.<BR>—भैषज्य-राज, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—भैषज्य-समुद्गत, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैष्णज
भैष्णज, आस्, m. pl. of the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैष्णज्य
भैष्णज्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Bhiṣṇaja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैष्मक
भैष्मक भैष्मक, अस्, m. (fr. भीष्मक),<BR>a patronymic; (ई), f. a patronymic of Rukmiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भो
भो भो. See भोस्, p. 723, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तव्य|भोक्तव्यं
भोक्तव्य भोक्तव्य, भोक्तृ, &c. See p. 713,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग|भोगः
भोग 1. भोग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. भुज्), any<BR>winding or curve, a ring, coil; winding; the ex-<BR>panded hood of a snake; a snake; the body; a par-<BR>ticular array, an army in column.<BR>—भोग-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. the state of being curved or winding, curvature,<BR>curvedness.<BR>—१. भोग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (for 2. see<BR>col. 3), furnished with windings or curves, having<BR>rings, ringed [cf. महा-भ्˚]; (आन्), m. a snake; a<BR>mountain; (अती), f. a female snake-demon; one of<BR>the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; the city of the<BR>snake-demons in the subterranean regions [cf. भो-<BR>गावती]; the sacred river of the snake-demons, or<BR>a Tīrtha in that river sacred to the serpent-king<BR>Vāsuki; N. of Ujjayinī in the Dvāpara age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिन्
1. भोगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, furnished with windings or<BR>curves, having windings or rings, curved, ringed [cf.<BR>महा-भ्˚]; (ई), m. a snake [cf. कृष्ण-भ्˚].<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-c" target="_blank">Page0722-c+ 80</a>]<BR>—भोगि-कान्त, अस्, m. ‘dear to snakes,’ air, wind.<BR>—भोगि-गन्धिका, f. a species of ichneumon<BR>plant.<BR>—भोगि-भुज्, क्, m. ‘eating snakes,’ an ich-<BR>neumon.<BR>—भोगि-वल्लभ, अम्, n. ‘beloved by<BR>snakes,’ sandal.<BR>—भोगीन्द्र (˚गि-इन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘king of snakes,’ an epithet of Ananta or Śeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग|भोगः
भोग 2. भोग, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. भुज्), en-<BR>joyment, fruition; eating; use, application; usufruct,<BR>the use of a deposit (Manu VIII. 149); utility,<BR>advantage, profitable aim or object; enjoyment (of<BR>women), sexual enjoyment; possessing, possession;<BR>ruling, governing, protecting, rule, government;<BR>cherishing, nourishing; suffering, experiencing; en-<BR>during, feeling, perception (of joy or sorrow), pleasure;<BR>suffering, passion; any object of enjoyment, that<BR>which is eaten, food; food offered to an idol;<BR>festivity, feasting, a repast, feast, banquet; income,<BR>revenue; gain, profit, produce; money, wealth;<BR>hire, the hire of dancing girls or courtezans, wages<BR>of prostitution; (in astronomy) the passing (of an<BR>asterism); the part of the ecliptic occupied by each<BR>of the 27 lunar mansions or Nakṣatras, i. e. 13°<BR>20° or 800°; (in arithmetic) the numerator of a<BR>fraction (?); N. of a preceptor.<BR>—भोग-कर, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, producing or affording enjoyment, procuring<BR>food or pleasure.<BR>—भोग-गुच्छ, अम्, n. hire of<BR>prostitution, price paid to harlots.<BR>—भोग-गृह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘pleasure-chamber,’ the inner or private<BR>apartments, women's apartments, zenana, harem;<BR>[cf. भोग-स्थान.]<BR>—भोग-ग्राम, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a village.<BR>—भोग-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, produced by<BR>enjoyment or by suffering.<BR>—भोग-दत्ता, f., N. of<BR>a woman.<BR>—भोग-दा, f. ‘granting enjoyment,’ N.<BR>of the goddess of the Piṅgalas.<BR>—भोग-देव, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having pleasure for a god (?),’ N. of a man<BR>(Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VIII. 531).<BR>—भोग-देह, अस्, m.<BR>‘the body of suffering,’ the subtle body which a<BR>dead person takes with him and with which, accord-<BR>ing to his works, he experiences either happiness or<BR>misery.<BR>—भोग-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भोग-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of possession,’ a person<BR>in actual possession (of anything), the governor or<BR>viceroy of a town or province.<BR>—भोग-पाल, a<BR>groom; [cf. भोगिक.]<BR>—भोग-पिशाचिका, f. hunger.<BR>—भोग-प्रस्थ, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—भोग-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—भोग-<BR>भुज्, क्, क्, क्, enjoying pleasures.<BR>—भोग-भूमि,<BR>इस्, f. ‘land of enjoyment,’ the place where people<BR>enjoy the reward of their works, Svarga or paradise,<BR>(opposed to कर्म-भूमि, ‘land of works.’)<BR>—भो-<BR>ग-भृतक, अस्, m. a servant who works only for<BR>maintenance.<BR>—भोग-मण्डप, अस्, m. the part of<BR>the temple of Jagan-nāth where the food to be pre-<BR>sented to the idol is cooked.<BR>—भोग-लाभ, अस्, m.<BR>acquisition of enjoyment or profit; the gain or profit<BR>made by the use of anything deposited or pledged;<BR>welfare.<BR>—२. भोग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (for 1. see<BR>col. 2), furnished with enjoyments, having enjoy-<BR>ment, delightful, pleasurable, enjoyable, affording or<BR>yielding enjoyment; happy, prosperous; (आन्), m.<BR>dancing, acting and singing; N. of Satya-bhāmā's<BR>residence (Hari-vaṃśa 8978); (अती), f., N. of a town;<BR>epithet of the night of the second lunar day.<BR>—भोग-वर्धन, N. of a country; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>its inhabitants.<BR>—भोग-वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a<BR>king; of a merchant.<BR>—भोग-वस्तु, उ, n. an object<BR>of enjoyment.<BR>—भोग-सद्मन्, अ, n. the abode of<BR>pleasure; the inner or women's apartments.<BR>—भो-<BR>ग-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भोग-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. the body as the seat of sensual enjoyment;<BR>the women's apartments.<BR>—भोगाधि (˚ग-आधि),<BR>इस्, m. a pledge or deposit which may be used until<BR>redeemed.<BR>—भोगान्त (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of<BR>enjoyment or of suffering.<BR>—भोगायतन (˚ग-आय्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a place of enjoyment or suffering.<BR>—भो-<BR>गार्ह (˚ग-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, fit for enjoyment, to<BR>be enjoyed or possessed; (अम्), n. property, wealth,<BR>money; [cf. भोग्य.]<BR>—भोगार्ह्य (˚ग-अर्˚),<BR>अम्, n. corn, grain.<BR>—भोगावली (˚ग-आव्˚), f. an<BR>encomiastic poem, the panegyric of professional<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-a" target="_blank">Page0723-a+ 81</a>]<BR>encomiasts or bards, eulogium.<BR>—भोगावास (˚ग-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of pleasure,’ the women's apart-<BR>ments; [cf. भोग-गृह.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिक|भोगिकः
भोगिक, अस्, m. a horse-keeper, groom (= भो-<BR>ग-पाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिन्
2. भोगिन्, ई, इनी, इ, enjoying, eating; using, pos-<BR>sessing; suffering, experiencing, undergoing; an<BR>enjoyer, possessor, &c.; full of enjoyments, devoted<BR>to enjoyments, indulging in sensual pleasures;<BR>wealthy, opulent; (ई), m. a voluptuary, a king,<BR>prince; the head man of a village; a barber; a<BR>person who accumulates money for a particular ex-<BR>penditure; (इनी), f. the concubine of a king or a<BR>wife not regularly consecrated with him; epithet of<BR>a kind of heroine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगीन
भोगीन, अस्, आ, अम्, at the end of a comp. [cf.<BR>मातृ-भोगीण].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्य|भोग्यं
भोग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, enjoyable, to be enjoyed, to<BR>be used, (in the sense ‘to be eaten,’ भोज्य is rather<BR>employed); to be endured or experienced; useful,<BR>profitable; (in astronomy) to be passed; (आ), f. a<BR>harlot, courtezan, prostitute; (अम्), n. what may be<BR>enjoyed, anything that may be possessed or used, an<BR>object of fruition, a possession, wealth, money; corn,<BR>grain.<BR>—भोग्य-ता, f. or भोग्य-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state of being used or possessed, usefulness, profit-<BR>ableness, enjoyableness.<BR>—भोग्याधि (˚य-आधि),<BR>इस्, m. = भोगाधि, p. 722, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज|भोजः
भोज, अस्, आ, अम्, bestowing enjoyment or<BR>pleasure, bountiful, liberal, (as an epithet of Indra<BR>or as the title of a king; Ved., Sāy. = फलस्य<BR>दातृ or रक्षितृ or पालयितृ); enjoying, leading<BR>a life of enjoyment or sensuality; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>country (= Patna and Bhāgalpur, cf. भोज-कट);<BR>N. of a celebrated sovereign of Malwa (supposed to<BR>have flourished about the end of the tenth century or<BR>beginning of the eleventh century, and to have been<BR>a great patron of learning, see भोज-देव, भोज-<BR>राज below); a king of the Bhojas (see below); N.<BR>of a king of Vidarbha (Raghu-v. VII. 1); N. of a<BR>son of Vasu-deva and Śānti-devā; of Kṛta-varman;<BR>of a son of Ujjendra and founder of Bhoja-purī; of<BR>a lexicographer; of an author of certain medical<BR>works; of a son of Kalaśa-deva; (आ), f. a princess of<BR>the Bhojas; N. of the wife of Vīra-vrata, (also read<BR>भोज्या); a cowherd; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>the descendants of Mahā-bhoja [cf. महा-भ्˚].<BR>—भोज-कट, अम्, n., N. of a town founded by<BR>Rukmin (Mahā-bh. Sabhā-p. 1166); the country<BR>of Bhoja, the present Bhojpur, or the vicinity of<BR>Patna and Bhāgalpur.<BR>—भोजकटीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to or coming from Bhoja-kaṭa; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>the inhabitants of Bhoja-kaṭa.<BR>—भोज-कन्या, f. a<BR>girl of the race of the Bhojas.<BR>—भोज-कुल-प्र-<BR>दीप, अस्, m. ‘the lamp of the race of Bhoja,’ epithet<BR>of a king of Vidarbha (Raghu-v. VII. 26).<BR>—भोज-<BR>दुहितृ, ता, f. a daughter of Bhoja, a princess or<BR>queen of the Bhojas [cf. भोज-पुत्री].<BR>—भोज-<BR>देव, अस्, m. king Bhoja (said to have been king of<BR>Dhārā in Malwa at the beginning of the eleventh<BR>century of our era; his capital being placed by some<BR>at Ujjayinī or Oujein; he was a great patron of<BR>literature, and is the reputed author of several works,<BR>e. g. the Yukti-kalpa-taru, Vyavahāra-samuccaya,<BR>Sarasvatī-kaṇṭhābharaṇa, and a commentary called<BR>Rāja-mārtaṇḍa on the Yoga-sūtras; cf. भोज-राज).<BR>—भोजदेव-शब्दानुशासन (˚द-अन्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a grammatical work (mentioned by Ujjvala-<BR>datta, Uṇādi-s. 1. 92).<BR>—भोज-नगर, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a town [cf. भोज-पुर].<BR>—भोज-नरेन्द्र<BR>(˚र-इन्˚), अस्, m. or भोज-नृपति, इस्, m. king<BR>Bhoja, = भोज-देव.<BR>—भोज-पति, इस्, m. the king<BR>of the Bhojas; king Bhoja (see भोज-देव); an<BR>epithet of Kaṃsa.<BR>—भोज-पुत्री, f. a daughter of<BR>Bhoja, a princess or queen of the Bhojas [cf. भोज-<BR>दुहितृ].<BR>—भोज-पुर, अम्, n. or भोज-पुरी, f.,<BR>N. of a town [cf. भोज-नगर].<BR>—भोज-प्र-<BR>बन्ध or भोज-राज-प्रबन्ध, अस्, m., N. of<BR>Ballāla's biography of Bhoja king of Dhārā.<BR>—भो-<BR>ज-राज, अस्, m. the king of the Bhojas; king Bhoja<BR>(said to be the author of several works, and described<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">Page0723-b+ 80</a>]<BR>as a poet, astronomer, lexicographer, and philosopher,<BR>cf. भोज-देव).<BR>—भोज-राजक-विवर्ग, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a work mentioned in the Śārṅga-dhara-pad-<BR>dhati.<BR>—भोजराज-वार्त्तिक, अम्, n., N. of a work<BR>mentioned in the Sāṅkhya-tattva-karumudī by Vācas-<BR>pati-miśra.<BR>—भोजराज-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the Yoga-sūtra by Patañjali (supposed<BR>to have been written under the patronage of king<BR>Bhoja).<BR>—भोजराजीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or<BR>coming from Bhoja-rāja.<BR>—भोजाधिप (˚ज-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘king of the Bhojas,’ an epithet of Kaṃsa;<BR>of Karṇa, the half brother of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>—भो-<BR>जाधिराज (˚ज-अध्˚), अस्, m. the king of the Bhojas.<BR>—भोजान्ता (˚ज-अन्˚), f., N. of a river.<BR>—भोजेन्-<BR>द्र (˚ज-इन्˚), अस्, m. the king of the Bhojas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजक
भोजक, अस्, आ, अम्, eating; (fr. the Caus.),<BR>giving to eat, causing to eat, nourishing; (अस्), m.<BR>one who gives to eat, (perhaps) a waiter at table;<BR>N. of a class of priests (or Sun-worshippers, supposed<BR>to be descended from the Magas by intermarriage<BR>with women of the Bhoja race).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजन|भोजनं|भोजनः
भोजन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing or giving to eat,<BR>feeding, nourishing; (अस्), m. an epithet of Śiva; N.<BR>of a river; (अम्), n. the act of giving to eat, feed-<BR>ing, nourishing, serving up or dressing food, (in these<BR>senses fr. the Caus.); the act of enjoying, using,<BR>eating, (in these and other senses fr. the simple rt.,<BR>cf. पर्ण-भ्˚); a meal, food, (कु-भोजन, bad<BR>food, indifferent, viands); anything given as sustenance<BR>or for enjoyment, anything enjoyed or used, property,<BR>possession; any object of enjoyment.<BR>—भोजन-<BR>काल, अस्, m. meal-time, dinner-time, supper-time.<BR>—भोजन-त्याग, अस्, m. ‘food-abandonment,’<BR>abstinence from food, fasting.<BR>—भोजन-भाण्ड,<BR>अम्, n. a dish of meat.<BR>—भोजन-भूमि, इस्, f.<BR>‘eating-place,’ a place for eating.<BR>—भोजन-विशे-<BR>ष, अस्, m. choice food, a dainty, delicacy.<BR>—भो-<BR>जन-वृत्ति, इस्, f. course or act of eating, a meal,<BR>food.<BR>—भोजन-वेला, f. meal-time, dinner-time,<BR>supper-time.<BR>—भोजन-व्यग्र, अस्, आ, अम्, occu-<BR>pied or engaged in eating; bewildered or strait-<BR>ened for want of food.<BR>—भोजन-व्यय, अस्, m.<BR>expense for food.<BR>—भोजनाधिकार (˚न-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. superintendence over food or provisions, the<BR>office of a master or overseer of the kitchen, commis-<BR>sariat, stewardship, charge of provender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनीय
भोजनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be eaten or enjoyed,<BR>eatable, edible; (fr. the Caus.), to be fed, to be<BR>made to eat or enjoy; (अम्), n. food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजयितव्य
भोजयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), to be<BR>made to eat, to be fed or nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजयितृ
भोजयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ (fr. the Caus), causing to<BR>enjoy or eat, feeding; one who makes another enjoy<BR>or eat; a promoter of enjoyment or amusement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजयित्वा
भोजयित्वा, ind. having caused to eat, having fed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजस्
भोजस्, Ved., in पुरु-भ्˚, विश्व-भ्˚; [cf. भो-<BR>जसे under rt. 3. भुज्, p. 713, col. 2.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजिक
भोजिक, अस्, m., N. of a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजिन्
भोजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, enjoying, eating; using, pos-<BR>sessing, &c. (at the end of comps., cf. अ-श्राद्ध-<BR>भ्˚, गृह-भ्˚, भुजङ्ग-भ्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्य|भोज्यं
भोज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be enjoyed or eaten,<BR>eatable, palatable [cf. प्रीति-भ्˚]; to be enjoyed<BR>carnally; to be used; to be suffered or experienced;<BR>(fr. the Caus.), to be made to eat, to be fed or<BR>nourished; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f. a<BR>princess of the Bhojas [cf. भोजा]; (अम्), n. anything<BR>to be enjoyed or eaten, food, (कु-भोज्य, bad food,<BR>indifferent viands); a dainty; a feast, a store of<BR>provisions, eatables; enjoyment, advantage, profit.<BR>—भोज्य-काल, अस्, m. eating-time, dinner-time,<BR>meal-time.<BR>—भोज्य-ता, f. or भोज्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>the condition of being eaten, the state of being food;<BR>भोज्यतां या, to become food.<BR>—भोज्य-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of food.<BR>—भोज्य-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m. ‘having its origin in food,’ chyle, chyme, the<BR>primary juice of the body [cf. रस].<BR>—भोज्योष्ण<BR>(˚य-उष्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, too hot to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोट|भोटः
भोट भोट or भोत, अस्, m., N. of a country,<BR>Bhoṭa (said to be the same as Tibet; cf. महा-भ्˚).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">Page0723-c+ 73</a>]<BR>—भोट-देश, अस्, m. the country of Bhoṭa.<BR>—भो-<BR>टाङ्ग (˚ट-अङ्˚), अस्, m., N. of a country, Bhootan.<BR>—भोटान्त (˚ट-अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of a country<BR>[cf. भोटाङ्ग].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटीय
भोटीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to Tibet, Tibetan.<BR>—भोटीय-कोशी, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौट्ट|भौट्टः
भौट्ट, अस्, m. a Tibetan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोमीरा
भोमीरा भोमीरा, f. coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलानाथ|भोलानाथः
भोलानाथ भोलानाथ (?), अस्, m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva; N. of a commentator on the Mugdha-<BR>bodha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलि|भोलिः
भोलि भोलि, इस्, m. a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोस्
भोस् भोस् (contracted fr. भवस् for भ-<BR>वन्, Sir! voc. sing. of 2. भवत्, q. v.; cf. भगोस्<BR>under भग-वत्, p. 696, col. 1), an interjection or<BR>vocative particle commonly used in addressing another<BR>person and generally translateable by ‘O!’ ‘Ho!’<BR>‘there!’ ‘Hallo!’ ‘Ah!’ ‘Alas!’ (before vowels and<BR>soft consonants भोस्, like भगोस् and अघोस्, is said<BR>to drop the final स्, but before vowels भोय् is also<BR>allowed, see Pāṇ. VIII. 3, 17, 18, 20, 22, Vopa-<BR>deva II. 49, 50; before hard consonants, भोस् or<BR>भोः is the form required, and भोः before a<BR>pause, but in the later literature भो is sometimes<BR>used where भोस् or भोः would be more correct;<BR>in Kathā-sarit-sāgara XVIII. 211, भोर् इति is against<BR>the rule; in Hari-vaṃśa 8301 भोस् occurs in the middle<BR>of a sentence, and in Bhāgavata-Purāṇa III. 23, 2,<BR>redundantly at the end; it is sometimes repeated,<BR>e. g. भो भो राजन् in Śakuntalā, p. 12; according<BR>to lexicographers it may be used as an interjection<BR>of sorrow and of interrogation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोहर
भोहर भोहर, अस्, m., N. of a poet men-<BR>tioned in the Śārṅga-dhara-paddhati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौगक
भौगक भौगक, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Bhogaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजकट
भौजकट भौजकट, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>or coming from Bhoja-kaṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजङ्ग|भौजंग
भौजङ्ग भौजङ्ग, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भुजङ्-ग),<BR>relating to a snake, snake-like, snaky, serpent-like,<BR>serpentine; (अम्), n., scil. भ, the serpent asterism,<BR>the Nakṣatra Āśleṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजि
भौजि भौजि, इस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Bhoja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजीय
भौजीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or coming from<BR>Bhauji.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौज्य
भौज्य, अम्, n., Ved. the rank of a king with<BR>the title of Bhoja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौट्ट|भौट्टः
भौट्ट भौट्ट. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौत|भौतः
भौत भौत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भूत), relating<BR>to existing beings; relating to or possessed by evil<BR>spirits, demoniacal, crazy, mad, silly; formed of the<BR>elements, elemental, material; (अस्), m. an attendant<BR>upon idols, a worshipper of demons and spirits, =<BR>देवल or देवलक, q. v.; (ई), f. ‘time of ghosts<BR>or spirits,’ night; (अम्), n. = भूतानां समूह,<BR>a collection or assemblage of Bhūtas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतक
भौतक, अस्, ई, अम्, = भौत, possessed by evil<BR>spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिक|भौतिकं|भौतिकः
भौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भूत), coming from<BR>or relating to existing beings, belonging to created<BR>beings, (भौतिक सर्ग, the creation of beings,<BR>the corporeal creation); relating or pertaining to<BR>evil spirits; possessed by evil spirits; formed of the<BR>elements, produced by the coarse or visible elements,<BR>relating to the elements, elemental, existent, material;<BR>(अस्), m. Śiva (fr. भूति, ashes ?); a sort of monk;<BR>(अम्), n. anything elemental or material; a pearl<BR>(probably for मौक्तिक).<BR>—भौतिक-मठ, अस्,<BR>m. a college of monks, monastery, convent.<BR>—भौ-<BR>तिक-विद्या, f. ‘spirit-science,’ sorcery, witchcraft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौत्य|भौत्यः
भौत्य, अस्, m. (fr. भूति), N. of a Manu; (अस्,<BR>ती, अम्), relating to the preceding Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौपाल|भौपालः
भौपाल भौपाल, अस्, m. (fr. भू-पाल),<BR>the son of a king, a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम|भौमः
भौम भौम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भूमि), be-<BR>longing or relating to the earth, dedicated to the<BR>earth; existing on or in the earth, produced or com-<BR>ing from the earth or ground, earthly, terrestrial,<BR>terrene; consisting or made of earth, earthy; com-<BR>ing from the land (as revenue &c.); relating to the<BR>planet Mars or to his day, falling on Tuesday, (in<BR>this sense fr. भौम, the planet Mars); (अस्), m.<BR>water; light; ambergris (= अम्बर); a red flower-<BR>ing Punar-navā; a metronymic of several persons;<BR>N. of a kind of supernatural being or spirit haunting<BR>the earth; of Atṛ; of the Daitya Naraka; of the<BR>planet Mars, (वारो भौमस्य, Tuesday); an epi-<BR>thet of the twenty-seventh Muhūrta; (ई), f. ‘produced<BR>from the earth,’ an epithet of Sītā; (अम्), n. any-<BR>thing coming from the earth, dust, &c.; a particular<BR>mode of sitting practised by Yogins; = भूमि, ground,<BR>floor, ceiling, (at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR>—भौ-<BR>म-चार, अस्, m. ‘the course of the planet Mars,’<BR>N. of the sixth chapter of Bhaṭṭotpala's commentary<BR>on Varāha-mihira's Bṛhat-saṃhitā.<BR>—भौम-दर्-<BR>शन-चार, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the Mīna-<BR>rāja-jātaka ascribed to Yavaneśvara.<BR>—भौम-<BR>देव-लिपि, इस्, f., N. of a kind of writing.<BR>—भौ-<BR>म-रत्न, अम्, n. coral.<BR>—भौम-वार, अस्, m.<BR>‘Mars-day,’ Tuesday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमक|भौमकः
भौमक, अस्, m. any animal living in the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमन|भौमनः
भौमन, अस्, m. an epithet of Viśva-karman,<BR>(for भौवन, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमिक|भौमिकः
भौमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, being or existing on the<BR>earth, earthly, earthy, terrestrial, terrene, belonging<BR>to any particular piece of ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम्य
भौम्य = भौमिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौर
भौर भौर, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Bhūri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिक|भौरिकः
भौरिक, अस्, m. the superintendent of gold in a<BR>royal treasury, a treasurer, (fr. भूरि, gold.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिकायणि
भौरिकायणि भौरिकायणि, इस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Bhuriki below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिकि
भौरिकि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR>—भौरिकि-वि-<BR>ध, अस्, आ, अम्, see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौलिकायनि
भौलिकायनि भौलिकायनि, इस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Bhauliki below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौलिकि
भौलिकि, इस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौलिङ्गि
भौलिङ्गि भौलिङ्गि, इस्, m. (fr. भू-लिङ्ग),<BR>a king of Bhū-liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवन|भौवनः
भौवन भौवन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भुवन),<BR>belonging to the world; (अस्), m. an epithet of Viśva-<BR>karman [cf. भौमन]; a son of Manthu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवनायन
भौवनायन, अस्, m. (fr. भुवन or भौ-<BR>वन), Ved. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवादिक
भौवादिक भौवादिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. 1.<BR>भू + आदि), belonging to that class of roots which<BR>begins with भू, i. e. belonging to the first class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवायन
भौवायन भौवायन, अस्, m. (fr. भुव),<BR>Ved. a patronymic; N. of Kapi-vana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्यस्
भ्यस् भ्यस्, cl. 1. A. भ्यसते, बभ्यसे,<BR>भ्यसितुम्, Ved. to fear, be afraid, trem-<BR>ble [cf. rt. 1. भी]: Caus. भ्यासयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अबिभ्यसत्, to cause to fear, frighten: Desid.<BR>बिभ्यसिषते: Intens. बाभ्यस्यते, बाभ्यस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश्
भ्रंश् भ्रंश् or भ्रश् (sometimes written<BR>भ्रंस्; cf. rt. भृश्), cl. 4. P. भ्रश्-<BR>यति (ep. also भ्रश्यते, &c.), cl. 1. A. भ्रंशते,<BR>बभ्रंश, बभ्रंशे, भ्रंशिष्यति, -ते, अभ्र-<BR>शत्, अभ्रंशिष्ट, भ्रंशितुम्, Indec. part. भ्रं-<BR>शितुआ or भ्रष्ट्वा, to fall, tumble, drop or fall<BR>down, fall out; to decline, decrease, decay, fade,<BR>disappear, vanish, to be ruined or lost; to fall from,<BR>stray from, be separated from, be deprived of, lose<BR>(with abl.); to run away, flee from (with abl.):<BR>Caus. भ्रंशयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबभ्रंशत्, to<BR>cause to fall, throw or cast down, precipitate; to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">Page0724-b+ 75</a>]<BR>ruin, overturn, expel; to cause to be lost, cause to<BR>disappear or vanish; to cause to be separated from,<BR>deprive of (with acc. of person and abl. of thing):<BR>Desid. बिभ्रंशिषति, -ते: Intens. बाभ्रश्यते,<BR>बाभ्रष्टि, बनीभ्रश्यते, बनीभ्रंशिति, बनी-<BR>भ्रंष्टि; [cf. Angl. Sax. hreosan, resosan, ‘to<BR>fall;’ arisan, ‘to rise:’ Goth. ur-risan, us-hris-<BR>jan, af-hrisjan, ‘to cast off.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश|भ्रंशः
भ्रंश, अस्, m. falling, falling off, a fall; de-<BR>clining, decline, decrease; decay, overthrow, destruc-<BR>tion, ruin (e. g. देश-भ्˚, ruin of a country); dis-<BR>appearance; running away; separating from, aban-<BR>doning, deserting; losing, loss [cf. जाति-भ्˚]; de-<BR>viating or straying from (propriety &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशथु|भ्रंशथुः
भ्रंशथु, उस्, m. = प्र-भ्रंशथु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशन
भ्रंशन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the simple rt. and<BR>Caus.), causing to fall, precipitating, throwing down;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of causing to fall, precipitating;<BR>falling from, being deprived of, losing (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशित
भ्रंशित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), made to<BR>fall, thrown down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशिन्
भ्रंशिन्, ई, इनी, इ, falling, tumbling, falling<BR>down, falling out, falling from or off, coming to<BR>ruin, decaying; causing to fall, ruining, annihilating;<BR>[cf. स्वार्थ-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्ट|भ्रष्टं
भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen, dropped, fallen<BR>down, fallen out or off; declined, decayed, ruined,<BR>disappeared, lost; fallen from, strayed from (with abl.,<BR>e. g. सार्थाद् भ्रष्ट उष्ट्रः, a camel strayed<BR>from a caravan); separated from, deprived of (with<BR>abl.); depraved, vicious, a backslider; (आ), f. a fallen<BR>or unchaste woman.<BR>—भ्रष्ट-क्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>one who has discontinued or omitted prescribed acts.<BR>—भ्रष्ट-गुद, अस्, आ, अम्, suffering from pro-<BR>lapsus ani.<BR>—भ्रष्ट-निद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, deprived<BR>of sleep.<BR>—भ्रष्ट-योग, अस्, आ, अम्, one who<BR>has fallen from devotion, a backslider.<BR>—भ्रष्ट-<BR>राज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from or deprived of a king-<BR>dom.<BR>—भ्रष्टाधिकार (˚ट-अध्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>fallen from office, deprived of office.<BR>—भ्रष्टा-<BR>धिकार-त्व, अम्, n. loss of office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टक
भ्रष्टक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश्य
भ्राश्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt. भ्रश् or fr. rt.<BR>भ्राश् ?), Ved. to be made to fall, to be struck down;<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda X. 116, 5, भ्रा-<BR>श्यानि = आयुधानि, ‘weapons,’ and connected with<BR>rt. भ्राश्, to shine.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंस्
भ्रंस् भ्रंस्. See rt. भ्रंश्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुंश|भ्रकुंशः
भ्रकुंश भ्रकुंश or भ्रकुंस, अस्, m. an<BR>actor in female apparel; [cf. भृकुंश, भ्रुकुंश,<BR>भ्रूकुंश.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुटि|भ्रकुटिः
भ्रकुटि भ्र-कुटि or भ्र-कुटी = भ्रू-कुटि,<BR>इस्, f. a contraction of the eyebrows, frown.<BR>—भ्र-<BR>कुटि-मुख, अम्, n. a face with contracted eyebrows,<BR>frowning face, (also written भृकुटी-मुख.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रक्ष्
भ्रक्ष् भ्रक्ष्. See rt. भृक्ष्, p. 720.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्
भ्रज् 1. भ्रज् in गिरि-भ्रज्, q. v.; (the word<BR>भ्रज् is thought to be fr. a lost rt. भ्रज् = Lat.<BR>frango.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्
भ्रज् 2. भ्रज्, f., Ved. (perhaps) stiffness;<BR>[cf. मृत-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्ज्
भ्रज्ज् 1. भ्रज्ज् (in the Dhātu-pāṭha writ-<BR>ten भ्रस्ज्; cf. rt. भृज्), cl. 6. P. A.<BR>भृज्जति, -ते (for भर्जते, see rt. भृज्), बभ्रज्ज,<BR>बभर्ज्ज, बभ्रज्जे, बभर्ज्जे, भ्रष्टा, भर्-<BR>ष्टा, भ्रक्ष्यति, -ते, भर्क्ष्यति, -ते, अभ्रा-<BR>क्षीत्, अभार्क्षीत्, अभ्रष्ट, अभर्ष्ट, भ्रष्-<BR>टुम्, भर्ष्टुम्, to fry, broil, grill, parch, scorch,<BR>roast (especially grain): Pass. भृज्ज्यते: Caus.<BR>भ्रज्जयति, भर्ज्जयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अब-<BR>भ्रज्जत्, to fry, roast: Desid. बिभ्रक्षति,<BR>-ते, बिभर्क्षति, -ते, बिभ्रज्जिषति, -ते [cf. बि-<BR>भ्रक्षु, बिभ्रज्जिषु]; Intens. बरीभृज्ज्यते,<BR>बाभ्रष्टि or बाभर्ष्टि (?); [cf. Gr. φρῡ́γ-ω,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">Page0724-c+ 79</a>]<BR>φρύγ-ανο-ν, φρύγ-ε-τρο-ν, φρυκ-τό-ς; Lat. frīg-0,<BR>frictus, frixus; Old Germ. briuwan = Angl. Sax.<BR>briwan = Old Iceland. brugga = Eng. brew; Hib.<BR>bruighim, ‘I boil, seeth.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्ट|भृष्टः
भृष्ट, भृष्टि, &c. See p. 721, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्ज्
2. भ्रज्ज्, भ्रट्, ट्, ट् (or भृट्, ट्, ट्, if fr.<BR>भृज्ज्, q. v.), frying, roasting, (at the end of a<BR>comp., e. g. धाना-भ्˚, roasting or parching grain,<BR>see Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 36.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्जन|भ्रज्जनं
भ्रज्जन, अम्, n. the act of frying, parching,<BR>roasting; [cf. भृज्जन, भर्जन.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टव्य
भ्रष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be fried, to be<BR>parched or roasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्ट्र
भ्रष्ट्र, अम्, n. a frying-pan, gridiron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं|भ्राष्ट्रः
भ्राष्ट्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. a frying-pan; (अस्),<BR>m. light, ether (in this sense probably to be con-<BR>nected with rt. भ्राश्); (अस्, ई, अम्), fried or cooked<BR>in a frying-pan.<BR>—भ्राष्ट्र-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, pro-<BR>duced or cooked in a frying-pan; (आ), f. a pan-cake<BR>made of rice-flour.<BR>—भ्राष्ट्रम्-इन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>heating the frying-pan, one who fries or cooks.<BR>—भ्राष्ट्र-व्रतिन्, ई, m. N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रक|भ्राष्ट्रकं|भ्राष्ट्रकः
भ्राष्ट्रक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रकि
भ्राष्ट्रकि, इस्, m., N. of a man, (also read<BR>भ्राष्ट्र-कृत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रण्
भ्रण् भ्रण् [cf. rts. भ्रम्, रण्], cl. 1.<BR>P. भ्रणति, बभ्राण, भ्रणितुम्, to<BR>sound, utter a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रभङ्ग|भ्रभंग|भ्रभंगः|भ्रभङ्गः
भ्रभङ्ग भ्र-भङ्ग, अस्, m. = भ्रू-भङ्ग<BR>under भ्रू, p. 726, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम्
भ्रम् भ्रम्, cl. 1. 4. P. (ep. also A.)<BR>भ्रमति (-ते), भ्राम्यति (-ते; accord-<BR>ing to Pāṇ. III. 1, 70, a form भ्रामति is admis-<BR>sible; the form भ्रम्यति is doubtful), बभ्राम<BR>(2nd sing. बभ्रमिथ or भ्रेमिथ, 3rd pl.<BR>बभ्रमुस् or भ्रेमुस्), भ्रमिष्यति, अभ्र-<BR>मीत्, भ्रमितुम् or भ्रान्तुम्, (perhaps orginally)<BR>to fly about humming (as insects); to roam or<BR>wander about, rove or ramble about, go or move<BR>about, (भिक्षाम् भ्रम्, to go about begging);<BR>to stroll, perambulate; to circulate, revolve, turn or<BR>whirl round, move in a circle or orbit, move round<BR>(as the stars &c.); to totter, stagger about, waver;<BR>to go astray, stray, deviate (from rectitude), err, be<BR>in error or mistake, be perplexed, be foolish or<BR>ignorant; to move to and fro, move unsteadily,<BR>flicker, flutter, vibrate, quiver (as the tongue, eyes,<BR>flames, &c.); to surround; to roam or wander<BR>through, go over (with acc., e. g. देशम् भ्रम्, to<BR>wander through a country): Caus. भ्रमयति,<BR>भ्रामयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबिभ्रमत्, to cause<BR>or make to wander, make to rove or roam; to<BR>cause to turn round or revolve; to whirl round,<BR>swing; to cause to roll or roll along or through;<BR>to cause to err, delude, perplex, embarrass, con-<BR>fuse, seduce; to cause to move to and fro, wave,<BR>brandish, agitate, vibrate: Pass. of Caus. भ्राम्-<BR>यते, to be made to wander or whirl, caused to err,<BR>made to go astray: Desid. बिभ्रमिषति: Intens.<BR>बम्भ्रम्यते, बम्भ्रमीति, बम्भ्रान्ति, to<BR>roam about repeatedly, move frequently to and fro,<BR>wander through; [cf. Gr. βρέμ-ω, ὑψι-βρεμ-έ-της,<BR>βρόμ-ο-ς, βρον-τή, βαβράζω, πεμφρηδών, φριμάσσομαι,<BR>φόρμιγξ, ῥέμβω;Lat. frem-o, frem-or,<BR>frem-itu-s; Old Germ. brem-an, bremo, briosa;<BR>Angl. Sax. bremman; Old Iceland. brim, ‘surf.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भ्रम्यमाण
बम्भ्रम्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, roaming or wan-<BR>dering about repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम|भ्रमः
भ्रम, अस्, m. roving or roaming about, wan-<BR>dering about; moving or going round, turning<BR>round, whirling, revolving, moving or going to and<BR>fro; straying, erring; a flickering flame (Ved.);<BR>a circular motion, whirl; a whirlpool, eddy; a<BR>potter's wheel; a lathe; a grindstone; giddiness,<BR>dizziness; wandering of mind; confusion, perplexity,<BR>error, mistake, aberration, misconception, misappre-<BR>hension, delusion [cf. स्थाणु-भ्˚]; a spring, foun-<BR>tain, watercourse; (आत्), ind. by an error or mistake.<BR>—भ्रम-त्व, अम्, n. whirling found, the being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">Page0725-a+ 81</a>]<BR>in error or mistake, erroneousness.<BR>—भ्रमासक्त<BR>(˚म-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘occupied in grinding,’ a knife-<BR>grinder, sword-cleaner, armourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमण|भ्रमणं
भ्रमण, अम्, n. (fr. the simple rt. or Caus.),<BR>the act of roaming, wandering about, travelling, tour-<BR>ing, a tour; turning round, whirling; revolution,<BR>the orbit (of a planet &c.); wavering, staggering,<BR>tottering, shaking about, unsteadiness, deviation<BR>(from rectitude); causing to go round or move<BR>about; erring, falling into error; giddiness, dizzi-<BR>ness; (ई), f. a sort of game (played by lovers, pro-<BR>bably consisting in circular movements or waltzes);<BR>a leech; N. of one of five Dhāraṇās or mental con-<BR>ceptions of the elements (viz. that of the wind; the<BR>others being स्तम्भिनी, earth; धारिणी, water; द-<BR>हनी, fire; and शोषिणी, ether).<BR>—भ्रमण-विल-<BR>सित, N. of a metre.<BR>—भ्रमणार्थे (˚ण-अर्˚),<BR>ind. for the sake of travelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमणीय
भ्रमणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be roamed about, to<BR>be wandered through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्
भ्रमत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, roaming, roving, prowl-<BR>ing, wandering, sauntering about, turning round,<BR>whirling, shaking, &c.<BR>—भ्रमत्-कुटी, f. a sort of<BR>umbrella, a concave mat carried on the head; [cf.<BR>जङ्गम-कुटी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रममाण
भ्रममाण, अस्, आ, अम्, wandering about,<BR>whirling round; being in error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमर|भ्रमरः
भ्रमर, अस्, m. a large black bee, a kind of<BR>humble bee, any bee; a lover, gallant, libertine; a<BR>young man; a potter's wheel; a particular position<BR>of the hand; N. of a man; (आ), f. = भ्रमर-<BR>च्छल्ली below; (ई), f. a bee; the plant Jatukā,<BR>q. v.; the plant Putra-dātrī, q. v.; (अम्), n. giddi-<BR>ness, vertigo, epilepsy.<BR>—भ्रमर-करण्डक,<BR>अस्, m. a small box containing bees (used by thieves<BR>to extinguish a candle-light by letting the bees<BR>escape), a dark lantern (?).<BR>—भ्रमर-कीट, अस्,<BR>m. a species of wasp that builds its nest in the<BR>corners of walls, doors, &c., Vespa Solitaria.<BR>—भ्र-<BR>मर-कुण्ड, N. of a sacred bathing-place on the<BR>mountain Nīla (mentioned in Raghu-nātha's Rasika-<BR>ramaṇa).<BR>—भ्रमर-च्छल्ली, f. a species of creeper<BR>(= भृङ्ग-मूलिका, भृङ्गाह्वा, भ्रमरा).<BR>—भ्रमर-पद, अम्, n. ‘bee-foot,’ a kind of<BR>metre, four times ¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘¯¯¯.<BR>—भ्रमर-प्रिय, अस्, m. ‘dear to bees,’ a par-<BR>ticular sort of Kadamba plant (= धारा-कदम्ब).<BR>—भ्रमर-बाधा, f. annoyance caused by a bee,<BR>molestation by a bee.<BR>—भ्रमर-मण्डल, अम्,<BR>n. a circle or swarm of bees.<BR>—भ्रमर-मारी, f.<BR>‘bee-killing,’ a particular plant or flower (growing<BR>in Malwa, = भृङ्ग-मारी, भ्रमरारि).<BR>—भ्र-<BR>मर-विलसित, अस्, आ, अम्, (a creeper, lotus, &c.)<BR>about which bees hover or sport; (अम्), n. the<BR>hovering or sporting of bees; (आ, अम्), f. n. a species<BR>of metre, four times ¯¯¯¯, ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯.<BR>—भ्र-<BR>मरातिथि (˚र-अत्˚), इस्, m. ‘bee-guest,’ the plant<BR>Michelia Champaka.<BR>—भ्रमरानन्द (˚र-आन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘bee-joy,’ N. of several plants, Mimusops<BR>Elengi, Gærtnera Racemosa (= अतिमुक्तक), the<BR>red-flowering globe amaranth (= रक्ताम्लान).<BR>—भ्रमराम्बा-क्षेत्र (˚र-अम्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of a district sacred to Durgā; [cf. भ्रामरी, अम्बा.]<BR>—भ्रमरारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m. ‘bee-enemy’ (=<BR>भ्रमर-मारी, q. v.).<BR>—भ्रमरालक (˚र-<BR>अल्˚), अस्, m. ‘bee-curl,’ a curl on the forehead.<BR>—भ्रमरावली (˚र-आव्˚), f. ‘bee-line,’ N. of a<BR>species of the Ati-śakkarī metre.<BR>—भ्रमराष्-<BR>टक (˚र-अष्˚), अम्, n. ‘eight verses on the bee,’<BR>N. of a collection of eight verses.<BR>—भ्रमरेष्ट<BR>(˚र-इष्˚), अस्, m. ‘loved by bees,’ a sort of Big-<BR>nonia; (आ), f. the plant Clerodendrum Siphonanthus<BR>(= भूमि-जम्बू, q. v.).<BR>—भ्रमरोत्सवा (˚र-<BR>उत्˚), f. ‘bee-delight,’ the plant Gærtnera Racemosa<BR>(= माधवी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरक|भ्रमरकः
भ्रमरक, अस्, m. a bee; a whirlpool; (अस्,<BR>अम्), m. n. a lock of hair or curl hanging down on<BR>the forehead; a humming-top; a ball for playing<BR>with; (इका), f. the act of wandering or straying in<BR>all directions.<BR>—भ्रमरिका-दृष्टि, इस्, f. a wan-<BR>dering glance (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमाय
भ्रमाय (fr. भ्रमत्, see Gaṇa Bhṛśādi to<BR>Pāṇ. III. 1, 12), Nom. A. भ्रमायते, &c., (pro-<BR>bably) to begin turning round or revolving; to roam<BR>about, become a vagabond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमि|भ्रमिः
भ्रमि, इस् (according to some also भ्रमी), f.<BR>whirling or turning round, turning about, going<BR>round, circulating, revolving [cf. संवत्सर-भ्˚];<BR>a potter's wheel, a turner's lathe; a whirlpool; a<BR>whirlwind; any circular arrangement of troops, a cir-<BR>cle formed by troops; an error, a mistake; N. of a<BR>daughter of Śiśu-māra and wife of Dhruva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमित
भ्रमित, अस्, आ, अम्, whirled round, made to<BR>go round, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमिन्
भ्रमिन्, ई, इणी, इ, roaming about, going round<BR>or about, whirling round, revolving, making a circuit,<BR>turning round (as the wind), erratic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्त|भ्रांत|भ्रान्तः
भ्रान्त, अस्, आ, अम्, roamed, wandered (some-<BR>times impersonally, e. g. तैर् भ्रान्तम्, it has<BR>been wandered by them; and even with acc., e. g.<BR>देशम् भ्रान्तम्, it has been wandered through a<BR>country); whirled round, turned round, revolved,<BR>rolled; confused, perplexed, bewildered, gone astray,<BR>mistaken, in error, blundering; roaming or wander-<BR>ing about, turning round, whirling, rolling, stagger-<BR>ing, flying or careering round and round (as a bird),<BR>moving to and fro; (अस्), m. an elephant in rut; a<BR>species of thorn-apple, = राज-धुस्तूरक; (अम्),<BR>n. roaming, wandering about, moving to and fro; a<BR>particular mode of fighting; error, mistake, delusion,<BR>blunder.<BR>—भ्रान्त-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, confused or<BR>perplexed in mind.<BR>—भ्रान्त-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ,<BR>confused in intellect, perplexed in mind, puzzled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्ति|भ्रांति|भ्रांतिः|भ्रान्तिः
भ्रान्ति, इस्, f. the act or state of wandering about,<BR>roaming, going round, flying about, turning round,<BR>revolution, whirling, rolling, a whirl or rapid rotary<BR>motion; confusion, perplexity, delirium [cf. मति-<BR>भ्˚]; error, going astray, mistake, delusion, false<BR>idea or supposition, wrong notion (e. g. पद्म-<BR>भ्रान्त्या, under the false idea of [its being] a lotus;<BR>भ्राह्मण-भ्रान्ति, the error of supposing [those<BR>works to be] Brāhmaṇas); unsteadiness; doubt, un-<BR>certainty.<BR>—भ्रान्ति-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing error<BR>or confusion.<BR>—भ्रान्ति-नाशन, अस्, m. ‘destroying<BR>error,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—भ्रान्ति-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, wandering or roaming about, whirling; erring,<BR>mistaken, being under a delusion, labouring under<BR>an error; entertaining a false notion; a particular<BR>figure of rhetoric (describing an error).<BR>—भ्रान्ति-<BR>हर, अस्, आ, अम्, taking away delusion, removing<BR>error; (अस्), m. a counsellor, minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्त्वा
भ्रान्त्वा, ind. having wandered about, having<BR>roamed through; having whirled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राम|भ्रामः
भ्राम, अस्, m. roaming about, wandering, un-<BR>steadiness, delusion, error, mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामक|भ्रामकः
भ्रामक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus. or fr.<BR>भ्रम), causing to whirl; causing error or mis-<BR>take, bewildering, perplexing, puzzling, deceitful,<BR>deceptive, false; (अस्), m. a sort of loadstone or<BR>magnet (so called from its causing iron to turn<BR>round); sun-flower, heliotrope; a deceiver, cheat,<BR>rogue; a jackal; (आ), f., N. of a particular plant<BR>(commonly called Laghu-dhāyaṭī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामण|भ्रामणं
भ्रामण, अम्, n. the act of causing to turn<BR>round, swinging or turning round; (ई), f. ‘the be-<BR>wilderer,’ N. of a female demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामयत्
भ्रामयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to turn round,<BR>whirling round, bewildering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामर|भ्रामरं|भ्रामरः
भ्रामर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भ्रमर), relating<BR>or belonging to a bee; (अस्, अम्), m. n. a kind of<BR>magnet or loadstone [cf. भ्रामक]; (अम्), n.<BR>whirling round; dancing round; vertigo, giddiness,<BR>epilepsy; honey; a village; a kind of coitus; (ई),<BR>f. an epithet of Durgā or Pārvatī (from her having<BR>assumed the form of a bee to contend with Mahi-<BR>ṣāsura ?); a Yoginī or female attendant on Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरिन्
भ्रामरिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. भ्रामर), whirling<BR>round, revolving; affected with vertigo, giddy; hav-<BR>ing epilepsy, epileptic; made of honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामिन्
भ्रामिन्, ई, इणी, इ, confused, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राम्यत्
भ्राम्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, roaming or rambling<BR>about, strolling about, perambulating; erring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राम्यमाण
भ्राम्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being caused to<BR>wander about, being made to whirl round, being<BR>caused to err or go astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमात्र
भ्रमात्र भ्रमात्र, a particular high num-<BR>ber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रश्
भ्रश् भ्रश्. See rt. भ्रंश्, p. 724, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रशिमन्
भ्रशिमन् भ्रशिमन्, आ, m. (fr. भृश), po-<BR>tency, mightiness, vehemence, violence, excessive-<BR>ness, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रशिष्ठ
भ्रशिष्ठ भ्रशिष्ठ, भ्रशीयस्. See under<BR>rt. भृश्, p. 721, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्ट|भ्रष्टं
भ्रष्ट भ्रष्ट, भ्रष्टक. See p. 724,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टव्य
भ्रष्टव्य भ्रष्टव्य, भ्रष्ट्र. See p. 724,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रस्ज्
भ्रस्ज् भ्रस्ज्. See rt. 1. भ्रज्ज्, p. 724,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज्
भ्राज् 1. भ्राज् (connected with rts. राज्,<BR>भ्राश्, भ्लाश्, भ्रेज्, भृज्), cl. 1. A.<BR>भ्राजते (Ved. and ep. also P. भ्राजति), बभ्राजे<BR>(बभ्राज) or भ्रेजे (3rd pl. बभ्राजिरे or भ्रे-<BR>जिरे, Pāṇ. VI. 4, 125), भ्राजिष्यते, अभ्राजिष्ट<BR>(Ved. अभ्राट्, अभ्राजि), भ्राजितुम्, to shine, glitter,<BR>gleam, glow, flash, beam, sparkle: Caus. भ्राज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अबभ्राजत्, अबिभ्रजत्, to<BR>make to shine, illuminate, irradiate: Desid. बिभ्रा-<BR>जिषते: Intens. बाभ्राज्यते, बाभ्राष्टि; [cf. Gr.<BR>φλέγ-ω, φλεγ-έ-θ-ω, φλέγ-μα, φλεγ-μονή, φλεγ-υρό-ς,<BR>φλύξ: Lat. fulg-e-o, fulg-ur, ful-vu-s, flag-<BR>ra-re, flam-ma for flag-ma, flā-men for flag-men,<BR>‘the kindler, i. e. priest:’ Goth. bairh-t-s, ‘mani-<BR>fest;’ bairhtei, ‘light:’ Angl. Sax. bearht, beorht,<BR>probably blāc, blœc-an, blīc-an: Old Germ.<BR>beraht, blanch, blich-an, blich, blic, blig: Engl.<BR>bright: Russ. blescu: Lith. blizg-ù, ‘I shine:’<BR>Scot. breagh, ‘shining, beautiful;’ breachad, boillsg,<BR>‘splendor;’ boillsgeach, ‘splendid.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज्
2. भ्राज्, भ्राट्, f. (Pāṇ. VIII. 2, 36), Ved. light,<BR>lustre, splendor, glitter; [cf. देव-भ्˚, न-भ्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज|भ्राजः
भ्राज, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, gleaming, glittering<BR>(Ved.); (अस्), m., N. of one of the seven suns; of<BR>a particular kind of fire (mentioned in Hari-vaṃśa,<BR>1. 10467); of a Gandharva protecting the Soma<BR>(Ved.); of a work composed in Ślokas and ascribed<BR>to Kātyāyana; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजक|भ्राजकं
भ्राजक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. the Caus.), causing<BR>to shine, illuminating, making bright (said of the<BR>digestive fire and bile as brightening the skin);<BR>(अम्), n. the bile, bilious humor, gall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजत्
भ्राजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shining, gleaming, glitter-<BR>ing.<BR>—भ्राजज्-जन्मन्, आनस्, m. pl., Ved. ‘having<BR>a brilliant native place or origin, brilliant form birth,’<BR>an epithet of the Maruts; (Sāy.) having brilliant<BR>forms (= दीप्त-शरीर).<BR>—भ्राजद्-ऋष्टि, अयस्,<BR>m. pl., Ved. ‘bright-weaponed’ (having bright<BR>gleams of lightning), an epithet of the Maruts;<BR>(Sāy. = दीप्यमानायुध.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजथु|भ्राजथुः
भ्राजथु, उस्, m. brilliance, splendor, glitter,<BR>beauty.<BR>—भ्राजथु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, shining,<BR>beautiful (said of a woman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजन|भ्राजनं
भ्राजन, अम्, n. (fr. the Caus.), the act of<BR>causing to shine, illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजमान
भ्राजमान, अस्, आ, अम्, shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजयत्
भ्राजयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, causing to shine, illu-<BR>minating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजस्
भ्राजस्, अस्, n., Ved. sparkling, glittering; [cf.<BR>अग्नि-भ्˚.]<BR>—भ्राजस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. spark-<BR>ling, glittering; containing the word भ्राजस्.<BR>—भ्रा-<BR>जस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. = भ्राजस्-वत् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिन्
भ्राजिन्, ई, इनी, इ, shining, gleaming, glittering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिर
भ्राजिर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a class of gods under<BR>the Manu Bhautya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्ठ
भ्राजिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. fr. rt. 1. भ्राज्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">Page0726-a+ 78</a>]<BR>shining very brightly, highly glittering or radiant;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a son of Ghṛta-pṛṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्णु|भ्राजिष्णुः
भ्राजिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, shining, gleaming, splen-<BR>did, radiant, elegant; (उस्), m. an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>of Śiva.<BR>—भ्राजिष्णु-ता, f. radiance, brightness,<BR>splendor, splendid appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिस्
भ्राजिस्, इस्, f. = भ्राजस्, p. 725.<BR>—भ्राजिष्-<BR>मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, splendid, shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजोभ्रादन्त्य
भ्राजोभ्रादन्त्य (?), आस्, m. pl., N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृ
भ्रातृ भ्रातृ, ता, m. (perhaps fr. rt. भृ,<BR>and originally meaning ‘a supporter’), a brother,<BR>uterine brother, own brother, (कु-भ्रातृ, a bad<BR>brother); an intimate friend or relation, a cousin or<BR>near relative in general, an intimate friend, (some-<BR>times used as a term of friendly address); (तरौ),<BR>m. du. brother and sister; [cf. Zend brātar: Gr.<BR>φράτηρ, φράτωρ, φρᾱτρ-ία, φρᾱ́τρ-α or φρή-τρη,<BR>φρατρίζ-ω, φρατριάζ-ω, φράτριοι θεοί: Lat. frāter,<BR>fraternu-s, frātr-ia, ‘a brother's wife:’ Umbr. frā-<BR>ter: Goth. brōthar, pl. bro-thra-hans, ‘brethren:’<BR>Angl. Sax. bródhor: Old Germ. bruodar: Slav.<BR>brātrŭ: Lith. broter-eli-s, a diminutive; bró-li-s,<BR>‘brother;’ brotù-szi-s, ‘a cousin:’ Old Pruss. bra-<BR>ti-s: Russ. brat: Hib. brathair.]<BR>—भ्रातुर्-<BR>जाया, f. (भ्रातुर्, gen. sing.), a brother's wife, sister-<BR>in-law.<BR>—भ्रातुष्-पुत्र, अस्, m. (भ्रातुष् for<BR>भ्रातुस्, gen. sing.), a brother's son, nephew; (ई),<BR>f. a brother's daughter, niece.<BR>—भ्रातृ-गन्धि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, or भ्रातृ-गन्धिक, अस्, आ, अम्, a brother<BR>only in appearance, having merely the name of<BR>brother.<BR>—भ्रातृ-ज, अस्, m. a brother's son; (आ),<BR>f. a brother's daughter.<BR>—भ्रातृ-जाया, f. a brother's<BR>wife, sister-in-law.<BR>—भ्रातृ-त्व, अम्, n. fraternity,<BR>brotherhood.<BR>—भ्रातृ-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, given by<BR>a brother; (अम्), n. anything given by a brother to<BR>a sister on her marriage.<BR>—भ्रातृ-द्वितीया, f. a<BR>festival on the second day in the light half of the<BR>month Kārttika (on which sisters give entertain-<BR>ments to brothers in commemoration of Yamunā's<BR>entertaining her brother Yama).<BR>—भ्रातृ-पत्नी, f.<BR>a brother's wife.<BR>—भ्रातृ-पद्म-वन, अम्, n. a<BR>group of lotus-like brethren.<BR>—भ्रातृ-पुत्र, अस्,<BR>m. a brother's son, nephew.<BR>—भ्रातृ-भगिन्यौ,<BR>du. a brother and sister.<BR>—भ्रातृ-मत्, आन्, अती,<BR>अत्, having a brother or brothers.<BR>—भ्रातृ-वधू,<BR>ऊस्, f. a brother's wife.<BR>—भ्रातृ-वल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>possessing a brother or brothers.<BR>—भ्रातृ-श्व-<BR>शुर, अस्, m. a husband's eldest brother.<BR>—भ्रातृ-<BR>सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—भ्रातृ-हत्या, f.<BR>fratricide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृक|भ्रातृकः
भ्रातृक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a brother, (at the<BR>end of a comp., cf. अ-भ्˚); coming from a brother,<BR>of or belonging to a brother, fraternal, brotherly (in<BR>this sense the fem. is ई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृव्य|भ्रातृव्यः
भ्रातृव्य, अस्, m. a brother's son, nephew,<BR>cousin; a rival, enemy, adversary; [cf. Lat. fra-<BR>trūelis.]<BR>—भ्रातृव्य-क्षयण, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>destroying rivals.<BR>—भ्रातृव्य-चातन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>scaring or frightening away rivals.<BR>—भ्रातृव्य-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having rivals.<BR>—भ्रातृव्य-<BR>हन्, हा, घ्नी, m. f. killing or striking down rivals<BR>(Atharva-veda X. 9, 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्र
भ्रात्र, अम्, n., Ved. brotherhood, fraternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रीय|भ्रात्रीयः
भ्रात्रीय or भ्रात्रेय, अस्, m. a (father's)<BR>brother's son, nephew; (अस्, आ, अम्), fraternal, be-<BR>longing or relating to a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्र्य|भ्रात्र्यं
भ्रात्र्य, अम्, n. = भ्रात्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्त|भ्रांत|भ्रान्तः
भ्रान्त भ्रान्त, भ्राम, भ्रामर, भ्राम्-<BR>यत्, &c. See p. 725, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश्
भ्राश् भ्राश् (connected with rts. 1.<BR>भ्राज्, भ्लाश्), cl. 1. 4. A. भ्राशते,<BR>भ्राश्यते (Ved. also P. भ्राश्यति), बभ्राशे or<BR>भ्रेशे (3rd pl. बभ्राशिरे or भ्रेशिरे, Pāṇ. VI.<BR>4, 125), भ्राशिष्यते, अभ्राशिष्ट, भ्राशितुम्,<BR>to shine, glitter, gleam, blaze: Caus. भ्राशयति,<BR>यितुम्, Aor. अबभ्राशत्, अबिभ्रशत् (Vopa-deva<BR>XVII. 3): Desid. बिभ्राशिषते: Intens. बाभ्राश्-<BR>यते, बाभ्राष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश्य
भ्राश्य भ्राश्य. See p. 724, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं|भ्राष्ट्रः
भ्राष्ट्र भ्राष्ट्र, भ्राष्ट्रक. See p. 724,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रेय
भ्राष्ट्रेय भ्राष्ट्रेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>family or race; (also भ्रास्त्रेय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रास्
भ्रास् भ्रास्, a various reading for rt.<BR>भ्राश्, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्री
भ्री भ्री, cl. 9. P. भ्रीणाति or भ्रिणाति,<BR>बिभ्राय, भ्रेष्यति, अभ्रसिहित्, भ्रे-<BR>तुम् (?), Ved. to be angry [cf. भृणीय^1]; to fear<BR>[cf. rt. 1. भी]; to bear, support, nourish [cf. rt.<BR>भृ]; to injure, hurt, (Sāy. = rt. हिंस्, ऋग्-वेद<BR>II. 28, 7.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 311-315.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुंश|भ्रुकुंशः
भ्रुकुंश भ्रुकुंश or भ्रुकुंस, अस्, m. =<BR>भ्रूकुंश, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुटि|भ्रुकुटिः
भ्रुकुटि भ्रु-कुटि, इस्, or भ्रु-कुटी, f. =<BR>भ्रू-कुटि under भ्रू.<BR>—भ्रुकुटि-बन्ध, अस्, m.<BR>knitting the brows, frowning, a frown.<BR>—भ्रुकुटी-<BR>मुख, अम्, n. a face with contracted eyebrows, a<BR>frowning face; (अस्, ई, अम्), having a frowning face;<BR>(अस्), m. a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुड्
भ्रुड् भ्रुड्, cl. 6. P. भ्रुडति, &c., to<BR>cover; to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुभङ्ग
भ्रुभङ्ग भ्रु-भङ्ग, अस्, m. = भ्रू-भङ्ग<BR>under भ्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुव
भ्रुव भ्रुव. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रू
भ्रू भ्रू, ऊस्, f. (said to be fr. rt. भ्रम्),<BR>an eyebrow, the brow; [cf. अग्रे-भ्˚, सु-भ्˚, भ्रौ-<BR>वेय; cf. also Zend brvat; Gr. ὀ-φρύ-ς; perhaps<BR>Lat. front(t)s = ὀφρυόεις; Old Germ. brāwa; Mod.<BR>Germ. braue; Angl. Sax. brœw; Engl. brow;<BR>Slav. brŭvĭ.]<BR>—भ्रू-कुटि, इस्, or भ्रू-कुटी, f. con-<BR>traction or knitting of the eyebrow, a frown, a look<BR>of displeasure; [cf. भृ-क्˚, भ्र-क्˚, भ्रु-क्˚.]<BR>—भ्रूकुटी-कुटिलानन (˚ल-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having a face wrinkled with frowns.<BR>—भ्रू-क्षे-<BR>प, अस्, m. contraction of the eyebrows, a frown.<BR>—भ्रूक्षेपालाप (˚प-आल्˚), अस्, m. the language<BR>of frowns.<BR>—भ्रू-चापाकृष्ट-मुक्त (˚प-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, drawn and discharged from the bow<BR>of the eyebrows (as a glance).<BR>—भ्रू-जाह, अम्,<BR>n. the root of the eyebrows (perhaps the inner side).<BR>—भ्रू-भङ्ग or भ्रू-भेद, अस्, m. contraction<BR>of the eyebrows, a frown.<BR>—भ्रूभेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>frowning, contracting or wrinkling the brow, attended<BR>with frowns.<BR>—भ्रू-मण्डल, अम्, n. the arch of<BR>the eyebrow.<BR>—भ्रू-मध्य, अम्, n. the interval<BR>between the eyebrows.<BR>—भ्रू-लता, f. ‘brow-<BR>creeper,’ a creeper-like eyebrow, an arched eyebrow<BR>(curving like a creeper).<BR>—भ्रू-विकार, अस्, m.<BR>‘change of the eyebrows,’ contracting the brow,<BR>frowning.<BR>—भ्रू-विक्षेप, अस्, m. contraction of<BR>the eyebrows, a frown.<BR>—भ्रू-विचेष्टित, अम्, n.<BR>playful movement of the eyebrows.<BR>—भ्रू-विलास,<BR>अस्, m. a playful or graceful motion of the eyebrows,<BR>play or contraction of the eyebrows, amorous play of<BR>the brows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुव
भ्रुव, अस्, आ, अम्, = भ्रू at the end of an adj.<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुंश|भ्रूकुंशः
भ्रूकुंश भ्रूकुंश or भ्रूकुंस, अस्, m. a<BR>male actor in female attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण्
भ्रूण् भ्रूण्, cl. 10. A. भ्रूणयते, &c.,<BR>to hope; to trust; to confide; to wish,<BR>desire; to fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण|भ्रूणः
भ्रूण भ्रूण, अस्, m. (fr. rt. भृ; perhaps<BR>for original भूर्ण), an embryo, fetus, unborn<BR>child; a child, boy; a pregnant woman (= गर्-<BR>भिणी); a Brāhman conversant with the Vedas (?);<BR>[cf. Gr. ἔμβρυον.]<BR>—भ्रूण-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, the<BR>killer of an embryo, one who occasions or procures<BR>abortion.<BR>—भ्रूण-हति, इस्, f. the killing of an<BR>embryo.<BR>—भ्रूण-हत्या, f. the killing of an em-<BR>bryo, procuring abortion; any sin equally heinous.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">Page0726-c+ 70</a>]<BR>—भ्रूण-हन्, आ, घ्नी, m. f. the killer of an<BR>embryo, one who procures abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रौणघ्न
भ्रौणघ्न, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. भ्रूण-हन्), re-<BR>lating to the killer of an embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रौणहत्य|भ्रौणहत्यं
भ्रौणहत्य, अम्, n. (fr. भ्रूण-हन्), =<BR>भ्रूण-हत्या, the killing of an embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेज्
भ्रेज् भ्रेज् (allied to rt. 1. भ्राज्), cl. 1.<BR>A. भ्रेजते, बिभ्रेजे, to shine, glitter,<BR>gleam, &c.: Caus. भ्रेजयति, -यितुम्, अबिभ्रेजत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष्
भ्रेष् भ्रेष् [cf. rts. भ्रंश्, ह्रेष्], cl.<BR>1. P. A. भ्रेषति, -ते, बिभ्रेष, बि-<BR>भ्रेषे, भ्रेषितुम्, to go, move; to totter, waver,<BR>slip, fall, make a false step; to fear; to be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष|भ्रेषः
भ्रेष, अस्, m. motion, going, proceeding; tot-<BR>tering, wavering, slipping, falling, declining or falling<BR>(from virtue), deviation (from rectitude), trespass,<BR>sin; loss, deprivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेषण|भ्रेषणं
भ्रेषण, अम्, n. the act of going, moving,<BR>tottering, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रौणघ्न
भ्रौणघ्न भ्रौणघ्न. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रौवेय
भ्रौवेय भ्रौवेय, अस्, m. (fr. भ्रू), a me-<BR>tronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लक्ष्
भ्लक्ष् भ्लक्ष् (various reading for rt.<BR>भक्ष्; cf. rt. भ्रक्ष्), cl. 1. P. A.<BR>भ्लक्षति, -ते, &c., to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लाश्
भ्लाश् भ्लाश् (connected with rt. भ्राश्),<BR>cl. 1. 4. A. भ्लाशते, भलाश्यते, ब-<BR>भ्लाशे or भलेशे (3rd pl. बभ्लाशिरे or भ्लेशिरे),<BR>भ्लाशितुम्, to shine, gleam, beam, glitter, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लास्
भ्लास् भ्लास्, a various reading for rt.<BR>भ्लाश् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लेष्
भ्लेष् भ्लेष्, cl. 1. P. A. भ्लेषति, -ते,<BR>&c., = rt. भ्रेष्, to go; to fear, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म 1. म, the twenty-fifth consonant of<BR>the Nāgarī alphabet and the nasal letter of the fifth<BR>or labial class, having the sound of the English म्.<BR> — 1. म-कार, अस्, m. the letter or sound म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म 2. म, अस्, m. (in prosody) a molossus<BR>or foot consisting of three long syllables.<BR>—२. म-<BR>कार, अस्, m. the foot called molossus.<BR>—मकार-<BR>विपुला, f., N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म 3. म, the singular base in all the cases<BR>except the nom. of the first personal pronoun and<BR>related to the verbal termination in the first person<BR>singular, (nom. अहम्, 1; acc. माम् or मा, me;<BR>inst. मया; dat. मह्यम् or मे; abl. मत् or<BR>मद्; gen. मम or मे; loc. मयि); at the<BR>beginning of a comp. the form मद् is used for the<BR>base, see 1. मद्; [cf. अहम्: Zend म: Gr. ἐμέ,<BR>ἐμ-ό-ς: Lat. me, me-u-s, mihi = Umbr. me-he:<BR>Goth. mi-s, ‘to me;’ mi-k, acc. ‘me:’ Slav. me,<BR>acc. ‘me:’ Lith. ma-n, ‘to me.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकत्
मकत्, a familiar diminutive of 3. म (according to<BR>the Bhāṣya on Pāṇ. I. 1. 29, e. g. मकत् पितृक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म 4. म, अस्, m. time, season; poison,<BR>venom; a magical or mystical formula; N. of the<BR>fourth note of the scale (abbreviated for मध्यम);<BR>the moon; N. of Brahmā; of Viṣṇu; of Śiva; of<BR>Yama; (आ), f. a mother; measure; light, lustre;<BR>knowledge, science; binding, fettering; death; a<BR>woman's waist; N. of Lakṣmī; (अम्), n. happiness,<BR>good fortune, welfare; water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंह्
मंह् मंह् [cf. rt. 1. मह्, महत्, &c.],<BR>cl. 1. A. मंहते, ममंहे, मंहितुम्;<BR>cl. 10. P. मंहयति, -यितुम्, Ved. to increase; to<BR>give, grant, bestow, offer, (sometimes with दानाय,<BR>to give as a present), honour; to speak; to shine,<BR>(in the last two senses cl. 1. is used in P. मं-<BR>हति, &c.): Intensive form in Ṛg-veda V. 27, 1,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">Page0727-a+ 78</a>]<BR>मामहे (or according to the Pada-pāṭha ममहे),<BR>part. मामहान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहना
मंहना, ind. (perhaps inst. c. fr. a form मं-<BR>हन् or मंहन), Ved. quickly, soon, promptly,<BR>willingly; (according to Sāy.) with greatness, great,<BR>praiseworthy; giving, granting, bestowing (= म-<BR>हत्त्वेन, महत्त्वेन or महिम्ना युक्त, पूज-<BR>नीय, दान, either as an adj. or subst.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहनीय
मंहनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. great, valuable,<BR>praiseworthy, worthy of honour; [cf. rt. 1. मह्,<BR>and see Nirukta III. 13, IV. 4.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहनेष्ठ
मंहने-ष्ठ or -ष्ठा (?), according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda X. 61, 1 = प्रदाने प्रवर्तमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहयत्
मंहयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, granting, giving, offer-<BR>ing.<BR>—मंहयद्-रयि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. granting<BR>riches, distributing wealth or treasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहयु
मंहयु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Caus.), Ved. wishing<BR>to grant or distribute, liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहिष्ठ
मंहिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very liberal; very<BR>mighty, very honourable, (Sāy. = अतिशयेन प्र-<BR>वृद्ध, अतिशयेन पूज्य, दातृ-तम); exceed-<BR>ingly abundant; [cf. Gr. μέγ-ιστο-ς; Goth. maists,<BR>‘most, greatest.’]<BR>—मंहिष्ठ-राति, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved.<BR>giving most abundantly, very bountiful, very rich,<BR>(Sāy. = प्रवृद्ध-धन or प्रवृद्ध-दान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंहीयस्
मंहीयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, giving more abundantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्
मक् मक्, ind., see Gaṇa Svar-ādi to Pāṇ.<BR>1. 1, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक
मक मक, अस्, अम्, m. n., see Gaṇa Ardhar-<BR>cādi to Pāṇ. II. 4, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकदत्त
मक-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकक
मकक मकक, अस्, m. in Atharva-veda<BR>VIII. 6, 12 (perhaps a particular kind of animal, or<BR>bleating, lowing, fr. rt. 2. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकत्
मकत् मकत्. See 3. म, p. 726, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकमकाय
मकमकाय मकमकाय (an onomatopo-<BR>etic verb), मकमकायते, &c., to croak (as a<BR>frog), to make a croaking noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकर|मकरः
मकर मकर, अस्, m. a kind of sea monster<BR>sometimes confounded with the crocodile, shark,<BR>dolphin, &c., (properly a fabulous animal regarded as<BR>the emblem of Kāma-deva, the god of love, cf.<BR>मकर-केतन below; also a symbol of the ninth<BR>Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī); N. of the tenth<BR>sign of the zodiac (Capricornus); the tenth arc of<BR>thirty degrees in any circle; a particular species of<BR>insect or other small animal; an array of troops in<BR>the form of a Makara (Manu VII. 187); an ear-ring<BR>in the shape of a Makara [cf. मकर-कुण्डल<BR>below]; the hands folded in the form of a Makara;<BR>one of the nine treasures of Kuvera; one of the<BR>eight treasures of the magic art called Padminī; a<BR>particular magical spell recited over weapons; N. of<BR>a mountain; (ई), f. the female of the sea monster<BR>Makara; N. of a river.<BR>—मकर-कटी, f., N. of a<BR>woman.<BR>—मकर-कुण्डल, अम्, n. an ear-ring<BR>shaped like a Makara.<BR>—मकर-केतन, अस्, or म-<BR>कर-केतु, उस्, or मकर-केतु-मत्, आन्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing the Makara for an emblem,’ or ‘having a fish<BR>on his banner,’ epithet of Kāma-deva, the god of<BR>love.<BR>—मकर-दंष्ट्रा, f. ‘Makara-toothed,’ N.<BR>of a woman.<BR>—मकर-ध्वज, अस्, m. ‘Makara-<BR>bannered,’ epithet of Kāma-deva, the god of love;<BR>a particular array of troops; a particular medical<BR>preparation (= रससिन्दूर-विशेष).<BR>—मकर-<BR>पाटक, अस्, m., N. of a village.<BR>—मकर-राशि, इस्,<BR>m. the sign of the Hindū zodiac corresponding with<BR>Capricornus.<BR>—मकर-विभूषण-केतन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘having the Makara for a characteristic ornament,’<BR>epithet of the god of love.<BR>—मकर-सङ्क्रमण,<BR>अम्, n. the passage of the sun from Sagittarius into<BR>Capricoruns.<BR>—मकर-सप्तमी, f., N. of the<BR>seventh day in the light half of the month Māgha<BR>(see माकरी सप्तमी under माकर).<BR>—मकरा-<BR>कर (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, m. ‘receptacle of Makaras,’ the<BR>ocean.<BR>—मकराकार (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, m. a variety of<BR>Cæsalpina Banducella (= षड्-ग्रन्थ).<BR>—मक-<BR>राक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘Makara-eyed,’ N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">Page0727-b+ 74</a>]<BR>Rākṣasa (son of Khara).<BR>—मकराङ्क (˚र-अङ्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘having the Makara for a symbol or mark,’<BR>epithet of the ocean; of the god of love.<BR>—मक-<BR>रानन (˚र-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's<BR>attendants.<BR>—मकरालय (˚र-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘Ma-<BR>kara-abode,’ epithet of the ocean; a symbolical ex-<BR>pression for the number four.<BR>—मकरावास (˚र-<BR>आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘Makara-abode,’ the ocean.<BR>—मक-<BR>राश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m. ‘whose horse is the Makara,’<BR>epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>—मकरी-पत्त्र, अम्, n. or<BR>मकरी-लेखा, f. the mark of a Makarī (on the<BR>face of Lakṣmī; cf. पत्त्र-भङ्ग, पत्त्र-लेखा).<BR>—मकरी-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरायण
मकरायण, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Makara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरिन्
मकरिन्, ई, m. ‘full of Makaras,’ epithet of the<BR>ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्द|मकरंदः|मकरन्दः
मकरन्द मकरन्द, अस्, m. the juice or<BR>nectar of flowers [cf. मरन्द], the honey of<BR>flowers; a species of jasmine; N. of various persons;<BR>of an astronomer; of a work (= कुसुमाञ्जलि-म-<BR>करन्द or सुपद्म-मकरन्द); the Indian<BR>cuckoo (= कोकिल); a bee; a species of fragrant<BR>Mango; (अम्), n. a filament (especially of the<BR>lotus-flower); N. of a pleasure-garden in Ujjayinī.<BR>—मकरन्द-कण, अस्, m. a drop or particle of<BR>flower-juice.<BR>—मकरन्दकणाय, Nom. A. -यते,<BR>to be like drops or particles of flower-juice.<BR>—मक-<BR>रन्द-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, rich in the juice of flowers;<BR>(अती), f. the flower of Bignonia Suaveolens.<BR>—मक-<BR>रन्द-विवृति, इस्, f., N. of a commentary by<BR>Citsukha Muni on the Nyāya-makaranda.<BR>—मक-<BR>रन्द-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्दिका
मकरन्दिका, f. a kind of metre, four times<BR>˘ ¯ ¯ ¯ ¯ ¯, ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ¯, ˘ ¯ ˘ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯; N. of a<BR>daughter of a Vidyā-dhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकष्टु
मकष्टु मकष्टु, उस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुआण
मकुआण मकुआण, अस्, m., N. of a race of<BR>kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुट|मकुटं
मकुट मकुट, अम्, n. = मुकुट, a head-<BR>dress, crown, tiara, crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुति|मकुतिः
मकुति मकुति, इस्, m. f. an edict or govern-<BR>ment order addressed to the Śūdras (= शूद्र-शा-<BR>सन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुर|मकुरः
मकुर मकुर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>मङ्क्, to adorn), a looking-glass, mirror; the stick<BR>or rod or handle of a potter's wheel; the tree Mimu-<BR>sops Elengi (= वकुल); a bud; Arabian jasmine;<BR>[cf. मुकुर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुराण
मकुराण, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुल|मकुलः
मकुल, अस्, अम्, m. n. the tree Mimusops Elengi;<BR>a bud; [cf. मुकुल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ट|मकुष्टः
मकुष्ट मकुष्ट or मकुष्टक, अस्, m. =<BR>मकुष्ठ below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ठ|मकुष्ठः
मकुष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, slow, going slowly, =<BR>मन्थर; (अस्), m. or मकुष्ठक, अस्, m. a<BR>species of kidney-bean or of rice; [cf. मुकुष्ठ,<BR>मपष्ट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकूलक|मकूलकः
मकूलक मकूलक, अस्, m. a species of<BR>medicinal plant (commonly called Danti, = मुकू-<BR>लक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकेरुक
मकेरुक मकेरुक, अस्, m. a kind of para-<BR>sitical worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्क्
मक्क् मक्क् [cf. rt. मस्क्], cl. 1. A. मक्-<BR>कते, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कल्ल|मक्कल्लः
मक्कल्ल मक्कल्ल, अस्, m. a dangerous abscess<BR>in the abdomen (peculiar to lying-in women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कुल|मक्कुलं|मक्कुलः
मक्कुल मक्कुल, अस्, m. red chalk (= शिला-<BR>जतु), a mineral substance considered variously to be<BR>chalk or benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कोल|मक्कोलः
मक्कोल, अस्, m. chalk, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष्
मक्ष् मक्ष् [cf. rt. म्रक्ष्], cl. 1. P.<BR>मक्षति, &c., to collect, heap, accumu-<BR>late; to be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष|मक्षः
मक्ष, अस्, m. or आ, f. a fly (Ved.; cf. मश,<BR>नील-म्˚, मधु-म्˚); (अस्), m. hypocrisy, the<BR>concealing of one's own defects; wrath; multitude<BR>(see म्रक्ष); [cf. Zend makhshi, ‘a fly:’ Gr.<BR>μυ-ῖ-α, ‘a fly;’ μοθ-ΐ-α: Lat. mus-ca: Old Germ.<BR>muc-ca, ‘a gnat:’ Angl. Sax. micge = Eng. midge:<BR>Old Norse my: Slav. mucha = Lith. musé, ‘a fly.’]<BR>—मक्ष-वीर्य, अस्, m. the plant Buchanania<BR>Latifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षिक|मक्षिकः
मक्षिक, अस्, आ, m. f. (said to be fr. rt. मश्,<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 153; cf. मशक), a fly, bee; [cf.<BR>निर्-म्˚, धेनु-म्˚, मधु-म्˚.]<BR>—मक्षिका-मल,<BR>अम्, n. ‘excretion of bees,’ wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षीका
मक्षीका, f. = मक्षिका above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षु
मक्षु मक्षु or मक्षू, ind. (properly a<BR>form in loc. pl. fr. rt. मंह्; cf. मङ्क्षु, मं-<BR>हना), Ved. quickly, rapidly, soon, promptly, imme-<BR>diately, directly, (in Ṛg-veda VIII. 26, 6, a form<BR>मक्षुभिः = शीघ्र-गमनैः occurs); (उस्), m.,<BR>N. of a man; [cf. Zend mashu, moshu; Lat.<BR>mox.]<BR>—मक्षुङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy.) = शीघ्रं गच्छन्, going quickly.<BR>—मक्षू-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very prompt,<BR>most prompt or quick, (Sāy. = शीघ्रतम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षूयु
मक्षूयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. quick, rapid, fleet,<BR>(Sāy. = शीघ्र-गन्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख्
मख् मख् or मङ्ख्, cl. 1. P. मखति,<BR>मङ्खति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख, अस्, आ, अम् (in some of its senses probably<BR>fr. a rt. मख् = 1. मह् or मंः, to worship),<BR>Ved. active, lively, sprightly, cheerful, free (said of<BR>the Maruts &c.; cf. अ-दुर्-म्˚); adorable, having<BR>sacrifices, honoured with oblations (Sāy. = मंह-<BR>नीय, महनीय, यज्ञ-वत्); (अस्), m. a sacrifice,<BR>sacrifical oblation, feast, festival [cf. 1. मह], any<BR>occasion of joy or festivity; (Ved.) a gift, wealth<BR>[? cf. मघ]; N. of a mythical being (supposed to<BR>be alluded to in Ṛg-veda IX. 101, 13, and in Vāja-<BR>saneyi-saṃhitā XXXVII. 7, 57, and in Śatapatha-<BR>Brāhmaṇa XIV. 1, 2, 17, where mention is made<BR>of मखस्य शिरः, the head of Makha, but in some<BR>of these passages मख is explained by यज्ञ and<BR>may mean ‘the victim’); [cf. Gr. μάχομαι, μάχαιρα,<BR>μαῖμαξ (fr. an Intens.), μαιμάκτης, μαιμακτήρια;<BR>Lat. macellum, mactare, mucro, maceria; Angl.<BR>Sax. méce; Old Norse mœkir.]<BR>—मख-क्रिया,<BR>f. a sacrificial rite.<BR>—मख-त्रातृ, ता, m. ‘pro-<BR>tector of [Viśvāmitra's] sacrifice,’ an epithet of Rāma-<BR>candra (son of Daśa-ratha).<BR>—मख-द्विष्, ट्, m.<BR>‘enemy of sacrifices,’ an evil being, demon, Rakṣas,<BR>(according to Malli-nātha = क्रतु-विघातक.)<BR>—मख-द्वेषिन्, ई, m. ‘enemy of [Dakṣa's]<BR>sacrifice,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मख-मय, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, containing or representing a sacrifice.<BR>—म-<BR>ख-वत्, आन्, m. having or performing sacrifices, a<BR>sacrificer; ‘companion of Makha,’ a word used in<BR>Śatapatha-Brāhmaṇa XIV. 1, 1, 13, to explain<BR>मघ-वत्, q. v.<BR>—मख-वह्नि, इस्, m. sacrificial<BR>fire.<BR>—मख-वेदी, f. a sacrificial altar.<BR>—मख-<BR>स्वामिन्, ई, m. ‘lord of sacrifice,’ N. of a commen-<BR>tator on the Drāhyāyaṇa-sūtras; (also read मघ-<BR>स्वामिन्.)<BR>—मख-हन्, आ, m., Ved. ‘killer of<BR>Makha,’ an epithet of Agni; of Indra; of Rudra.<BR>—मखांश-भाज् (˚ख-अं˚), क्, क्, क्, receiving a<BR>share of the sacrifice; (क्), m. a god.<BR>—मखाग्नि<BR>(˚ख-अग्˚), इस्, or मखानल (˚ख-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>sacrificial fire.<BR>—मखान्न (˚ख-अन्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘sacrificial food,’ the seed of Euryola Ferox.<BR>—म-<BR>खापेत (˚ख-अप्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>—मखालय (˚ख-आल्˚), अस्, m. a house or place<BR>for sacrifice.<BR>—मखासुहृद् (˚ख-अस्˚), त्, m.<BR>‘enemy of [Dakṣa's] sacrifice,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखस्य
मखस्य, Nom. P. A. मखस्यति, -ते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to be cheerful or sprightly; to wish to sacrifice;<BR>to wish to grant riches; (Sāy.) to wish for wealth,<BR>wish for honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखस्यु
मखस्यु, उस्, उस्, उ, cheerful, sprightly, merry,<BR>active, free; wishing to sacrifice; wishing for wealth,<BR>(Sāy. = यज्ञम् इच्छु, धन-काम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख्य
मख्य, a wrong form for मख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग|मगः
मग मग, अस्, m. a magian, a priest of<BR>the sun; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a country in Śāka-<BR>dvīpa inhabited chiefly by Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध|मगधः
मगध मगध, अस्, m. the country of the<BR>Magadhas, South Behār; a family bard or minstrel<BR>who sings the praises of a chief's ancestry in his<BR>presence; (आस्), m. pl. the people or the country of<BR>South Behār [cf. मागध]; (आ), f. the town of<BR>the Magadhas; long pepper.<BR>—मगध-देश, अस्,<BR>m. the country of Magadha.<BR>—मगध-पुरी, f.<BR>the city of Magadha.<BR>—मगध-प्रतिष्ठ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, dwelling in Magadha.<BR>—मगध-लिपि, इस्,<BR>f. the writing of Magadha.<BR>—मगध-वंश-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from the race of Magadha.<BR>—म-<BR>गधेश्वर (˚ध-इश्˚), अस्, m. a king of the Ma-<BR>gadhas; N. of Paran-tapa (Raghu-v. VI. 20); of<BR>Jarāsandha (one of the nine adversaries of Kṛṣṇa).<BR>—मगधोद्भव (˚ध-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, born in<BR>Magadha, growing in Magadha; (आ), f. long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगधीय
मगधीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or coming<BR>from Magadha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध्य
मगध्य, Nom. P. मगध्यति, &c., to sur-<BR>round; to serve, be a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगन्द|मगन्दः
मगन्द मगन्द, अस्, m. = कुसीदिन्, a usurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगल
मगल मगल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगव
मगव मगव, (with Buddhists) a parti-<BR>cular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगस
मगस मगस, आस्, m. pl., N. of the war-<BR>rior caste in Śāka-dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगु|मगुः
मगु मगु = मग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगुन्दी
मगुन्दी मगुन्दी, f., Ved., N. of a mythical<BR>being whose daughters are mentioned in Atharva-<BR>veda II. 14, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्न|मग्नः
मग्न मग्न. See under rt. मज्ज्, p. 729,<BR>col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ|मघः
मघ मघ, अम्, n. (fr. rt. मंह्), a gift,<BR>donation, present, reward [cf. क्रत्वा-म्˚, गो-म्˚];<BR>riches [cf. अश्वा-म्˚, तुवी-म्˚]; wealth, power, (in<BR>all the preceding senses Ved.); a kind of flower;<BR>(अस्), m. a particular drug or medicine, (in this sense<BR>also आ, f.); N. of one of the Dvīpas or divisions of<BR>the universe; of a country (Arrakan); pleasure; N.<BR>of the tenth or fifteenth Nakṣatra (containing five<BR>stars figured by a house, apparently α, γ, ζ, η, ν<BR>Leonis; in this sense often मघाः, pl.; cf. नक्-<BR>षत्र; मघा, like the other Nakṣatras, is some-<BR>times regarded as a wife of the moon); N. of the<BR>wife of Śiva; (आ, ई), f. a species of grain.<BR>—मघ-<BR>त्ति, इस्, f. (fr. मघ + दत्ति; cf. भग-त्ति), Ved.<BR>the giving of wealth, distribution of treasures, the<BR>giving and receiving of presents; (Sāy. = धन-<BR>दान, धन-लाभ.)<BR>—मघ-देय, अम्, n., Ved.<BR>the giving of presents.<BR>—मघ-रव, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Niṣāda.<BR>—मघ-व, अस्, m. = मघ-वन्,<BR>a N. of Indra.<BR>—मघ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, = मघ-<BR>वन् below.<BR>—मघवत्-त्व, अम्, n., Ved. libe-<BR>rality, munificence.<BR>—मघ-वन्, वा, घोनी, अत् (acc.<BR>sing. du. pl. m. मघवानम् मघवानौ मघो-<BR>नस्, inst. मघोना मघवभ्याम् मघवभिस्,<BR>dat. मघोने, मघवभ्याम्, &c., see Gram.<BR>155. c; the form मघ-वत् above may be option-<BR>ally used throughout), possessing gifts, rich, wealthy,<BR>distributing gifts (often as an epithet of the person<BR>who institutes a sacrifice and pays the priests), liberal,<BR>munificent; (आन्), m. an epithet of Indra (especially<BR>in the post-Vedic literature; cf. मही-म्˚, माघ-<BR>वत, माघवन); epithet of the chariot of the<BR>Aśvins (‘filled with treasures,’ Sāy. = धन-वत्);<BR>epithet of several gods; N. of a Vyāsa or arranger<BR>of the Purāṇas; of a Dānava; of the third Cakra-<BR>vartin in Bhārata; (वाना), m. du., Ved. epithet of the<BR>Aśvins, (Sāy. = हविर्-लक्षणान्नवन्तौ or ध-<BR>नवन्तौ); (ओनी), f. epithet of Uṣas, (Sāy. =<BR>धनवती.)<BR>—मघवन्-नगर, अम्, n. ‘Indra's<BR>city,’ N. of a town.<BR>—मघवन्-मुक्त-कुलिश,<BR>अस्, अम्, m. n. the thunderbolt hurled by Indra.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">Page0728-b+ 71</a>]<BR>—मघ-स्वामिन्, see मख-स्वामिन्.<BR>—मघा-<BR>त्रयोदशी, f. the thirteenth day in the dark half of<BR>the month Bhādra.<BR>—मघा-त्रयोदशी-श्राद्ध,<BR>अम्, n. a ceremony on the above-mentioned day.<BR>—मघा-भव, अस्, m. or मघा-भू, ऊस्, m.<BR>‘offspring of Maghā,’ the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ्नीप्रस्थ
मघ्नीप्रस्थ मघ्नी-प्रस्थ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्|मंक्
मङ्क् मङ्क् [cf. rt. वङ्क्], cl. 1. A. मङ्-<BR>कते, ममङ्के, मङ्किष्यते, अमङ्-<BR>किष्ट, मङ्कितुम्, to go, move; to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कु|मङ्कुः
मङ्कु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. shaking, vacillating, oscil-<BR>lating; (दुर्-मङ्कु, feeling no regret.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कणक
मङ्कणक मङ्कणक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Ṛṣi; of a Yakṣa (also read मचक्रुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कि
मङ्कि मङ्कि, इस्, m., N. of a man (men-<BR>tioned in the Mahā-bh. Śānti-p. 6589).<BR>—मङ्कि-<BR>गीत, अम्, n. ‘song of Maṅki,’ N. of the fifteenth<BR>chapter of the Pārtha Itihāsa-samuccaya, containing<BR>episodes from the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्किल|मंकिल|मंकिलः|मङ्किलः
मङ्किल मङ्किल, अस्, m. a forest confla-<BR>gration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कुर|मंकुर|मंकुरः|मङ्कुरः
मङ्कुर मङ्कुर, अस्, m. = मुकुर, a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्तव्य
मङ्क्तव्य मङ्क्तव्य, मङ्क्तृ, मङ्क्त्वा. See<BR>p. 729, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षण|मंक्षण|मंक्षणं|मङ्क्षणं
मङ्क्षण मङ्क्षण, अम्, n. armour for the<BR>legs or thighs, greaves; [cf. मङ्खुण, मत्कुण.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षु|मंक्षु
मङ्क्षु मङ्क्षु, ind. (= मक्षु, q. v.), im-<BR>mediately, directly, instantly, quickly; much, exceed-<BR>ingly; truly, really; (उस्), m., N. of a man [cf.<BR>मक्षु, माङ्क्षव्य].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

