मङ्ग्|मंग्
मङ्ग् मङ्ग् [cf. rt. मङ्क्], cl. 1. P. A.<BR>मङ्गति, &c., to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ग|मंग|मंगः|मङ्गः
मङ्ग मङ्ग, अस्, अम्, m. n. the head of a<BR>boat; (अस्), m. a mast or side of a ship [cf. मण्ड];<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a country in Śāka-dvīpa inha-<BR>bited chiefly by Brāhmans; [cf. मग and मृग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गिनी|मंगिनी
मङ्गिनी, f. a boat, ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल|मंगल|मङ्गलं|मङ्गलः
मङ्गल मङ्गल, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>मङ्ग्, Uṇādi-s. V. 70), happiness, felicity, good<BR>fortune, good luck, success, auspiciousness, prospe-<BR>rity, welfare, well-being, bliss, (in these and some<BR>other similar senses said to be also अस्, m.); any-<BR>thing regarded as auspicious or tending to a lucky<BR>issue, a good omen, an auspicious prayer, blessing,<BR>benediction, salutation; any auspicious or lucky<BR>object (as a dress, ornament, amulet, preservative);<BR>any happy or auspicious event (as a marriage &c.);<BR>a festival, festivity, rejoicing, solemnity, any solemn<BR>ceremony or religious service (as a thread-investi-<BR>ture &c.; cf. कौतुक-म्˚); any ancient custom; a<BR>good work; turmeric; N. of the capital of Udyāna;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of Agni; of the planet Mars; N. of a<BR>king belonging to the race of Manu; of a Buddha;<BR>of a poet; of a chief of the Cālukyas; (आ), f. a<BR>faithful wife; the white-flowering Dūrvā grass; the<BR>blue-flowering Dūrvā; a sort of Karañja; an epithet<BR>of Umā; of Dākṣyāyaṇī (as worshipped in Gayā);<BR>of the mother of the fifth Arhat of the present Ava-<BR>sarpiṇī, (according to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 41, मङ्गल may<BR>also have a fem. form in ई); (अस्, आ, अम्), lucky,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-c" target="_blank">Page0728-c+ 81</a>]<BR>fortunate, prosperous, auspicious, propitious, faring<BR>well or happily; brave.<BR>—मङ्गल-करण, अम्,<BR>n. ‘luck-causing, success-effecting,’ the act of reciting<BR>a prayer for success before the beginning of any<BR>enterprise.<BR>—मङ्गल-कारक, अस्, इका, अम्, or<BR>मङ्गल-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, causing welfare or pros-<BR>perity.<BR>—मङ्गल-कार्य, अम्, n. a festive occasion,<BR>solemnity (as a marriage &c.).<BR>—मङ्गल-कुठार-<BR>मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a door-keeper in the Dhūrta-<BR>nartaka by Sāma-rāja.<BR>—मङ्गल-क्षौम, अम्,<BR>n. a linen cloth worn at festivals.<BR>—मङ्गल-गिरि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘mountain of fortune,’ N. of a mountain.<BR>—मङ्गलगिरि-माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—मङ्गल-ग्रह, अस्, m. an auspicious planet;<BR>a lucky star.<BR>—मङ्गल-घट, अस्, m. ‘auspicious<BR>jar,’ a pot full of water offered to the gods on fes-<BR>tivals; N. of an elephant (Kathā-sarit-s. LI. 160).<BR>—मङ्गल-चण्डिका or मङ्गल-चण्डी, f., N. of<BR>a goddess, = Durgā (?).<BR>—मङ्गल-च्छाय, अस्, m.<BR>the tree Ficus Infectoria (= प्लक्ष).<BR>—मङ्गल-<BR>तूर्य, अम्, n. a musical instrument used at festivals;<BR>[cf. मङ्गलातोद्य.]<BR>—मङ्गल-देवता, f. a tute-<BR>lary deity; [cf. ब्रह्म-म्˚.]<BR>—मङ्गल-ध्वनि,<BR>इस्, m. an auspicious sound.<BR>—मङ्गल-पत्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. a leaf serving as an amulet.<BR>—मङ्गल-पाठक,<BR>अम्, n. ‘blessing-reciter,’ a professional well-wisher<BR>or panegyrist, a bard, encomiast.<BR>—मङ्गल-पाणि,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, having auspicious hands.<BR>—मङ्गल-पात्र,<BR>अम्, n. an auspicious vessel, a vessel containing<BR>auspicious objects.<BR>—मङ्गल-पुर, अम्, n. ‘city<BR>of properity,’ N. of a town; [cf. मङ्गल.]<BR>—मङ्गल-पुष्प, अम्, n. an auspicious flower.<BR>—मङ्गलपुष्प-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed of<BR>auspicious flowers (as a garland).<BR>—मङ्गल-पू-<BR>जित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured with a sacrificial fee or<BR>offering.<BR>—मङ्गल-प्रतिसर, अस्, m. any auspi-<BR>cious string or cord [cf. मङ्गल-सूत्र], the cord<BR>of an amulet.<BR>—मङ्गल-प्रद, अस्, आ, अम्, be-<BR>stowing welfare or prosperity, auspicious; (आ), f.<BR>turmeric.<BR>—मङ्गल-प्रस्थ, अस्, m. ‘auspicious-<BR>peak,’ N. of a mountain.<BR>—मङ्गल-मात्र-भू-<BR>षण, अस्, आ, अम्, only adorned with turmeric or<BR>with the Maṅgala-sūtra, q. v.<BR>—मङ्गल-वचस्,<BR>अस्, n. a benedictory or congratulatory word, auspi-<BR>cious expression, wishing joy, benediction, congratu-<BR>lation.<BR>—मङ्गल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, auspicious,<BR>happy, blessed; (अती), f., N. of a daughter of Tum-<BR>buru.<BR>—मङ्गल-वाद, अस्, m. benediction, wishing<BR>joy, benedictory expression; N. of a Nyāya work by<BR>Hari-rāma Tarka-vāg-īśa on the effect of benedic-<BR>tions.<BR>—मङ्गल-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, pronouncing a<BR>benediction, wishing joy, expressing congratulations,<BR>felicitating.<BR>—मङ्गल-वाद्य, अम्, n. a musical<BR>instrument played at festivals; [cf. मङ्गलातोद्य.]<BR>—मङ्गल-वार, अस्, m. ‘Mars-day,’ Tuesday.<BR>—मङ्गल-विधि, इस्, m. any auspicious ceremony<BR>or festive rite; preparations for a festival.<BR>—मङ्-<BR>गल-वृषभ, अस्, m. an auspicious ox or one<BR>promising good luck.<BR>—मङ्गल-शंसन, अम्, n.<BR>the act of wishing joy, uttering a benediction or<BR>congratulation.<BR>—मङ्गल-शब्द, अस्, m. an auspi-<BR>cious word, expression of congratulation, word of<BR>good omen, felicitation.<BR>—मङ्गल-सामन्, अ, n.<BR>an auspicious Sāman.<BR>—मङ्गल-सूत्र, अम्, n. the<BR>lucky thread, the marriage-string, (a string tied by<BR>the bridegroom round the neck of the bride and<BR>worn as long as the husband lives; in Upper India<BR>it is a string or piece of silk tied round the wrist and<BR>worn only during the marriage celebration).<BR>—मङ्-<BR>गल-स्नान, अम्, n. an auspicious ablution, any<BR>solemn ablution.<BR>—मङ्गलाक्षत (˚ल-अक्˚), आस्,<BR>m. pl. rice cast upon people by Brāhmans in bestow-<BR>ing a blessing at marriages &c.<BR>—मङ्गलागुरु<BR>(˚ल-अग्˚), उ, n. a species of Agallochum.<BR>—मङ्ग-<BR>लाचरण (˚ल-आच्˚), अम्, n. benediction, prayer for<BR>the success of anything, an auspicious introduction<BR>or form of words in praise of some deity &c. at the<BR>commencement of a written work or of any under-<BR>taking; pronouncing a blessing, wishing joy.<BR>—मङ्-<BR>गलाचार (˚ल-आच्˚), अस्, m. the repeating a prayer<BR>for success, wishing joy, pronouncing a blessing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">Page0729-a+ 79</a>]<BR>benediction, any auspicious ceremony or observance,<BR>pious usage.<BR>—मङ्गलाचार-युक्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>accompanied with a prayer for success or with good<BR>wishes, attended with benedictions or auspicious cere-<BR>monies.<BR>—मङ्गलातोद्य (˚ल-आत्˚), अम्, n. a drum<BR>beaten on festive occasions [cf. मङ्गल-तूर्य].<BR>—मङ्गलादेश-वृत्त (˚ल-आद्˚), अस्, m. a fortune-<BR>teller, professional panegyrist or well-wisher.<BR>—मङ्-<BR>गलायन (˚ल-अय्˚), अम्, n. an auspicious way, the<BR>way to happiness or prosperity; (अस्, आ, अम्), walking<BR>on the path of prosperity.<BR>—मङ्गलारम्भ (˚ल-<BR>आर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having auspicious commencements;<BR>(अस्), m. an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—मङ्गलार्थम्<BR>(˚ल-अर्˚), ind. for the sake of good fortune, for the<BR>sake of prosperity or happiness.<BR>—मङ्गलार्ह<BR>(˚ल-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of prosperity or happi-<BR>ness.<BR>—मङ्गलालम्भन (˚ल-आल्˚), अम्, n. touch-<BR>ing anything auspicious.<BR>—मङ्गलालय (˚ल-आल्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, dwelling in prosperity.<BR>—मङ्गला-<BR>वट (˚ल-अव्˚ or ˚ला-व˚), अम्, n., N. of a place<BR>of pilgrimage mentioned in the Kapila-saṃhitā.<BR>—मङ्गलावास (˚ल-आव्˚), अस्, m. ‘auspicious<BR>dwelling,’ a temple.<BR>—मङ्गला-व्रत, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>vow of Umā,’ N. of a chapter of the Kāśī-khaṇḍa<BR>of the Skanda-Purāṇa; (अस्), m. ‘devoted to Umā,’<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मङ्गला-शास्त्र, अम्, n. ‘the<BR>book of Umā,’ N. of a work mentioned in the<BR>Paramārtha-sāra by Abhinava-gupta.<BR>—मङ्गलाष्-<BR>टक (˚ल-अष्˚), eight lines of benediction pro-<BR>nounced for good luck by a Brāhman on a<BR>newly-wedded pair while a piece of silk is held<BR>between them.<BR>—मङ्गलाह्निक (˚ल-अह्˚), अम्, n.<BR>an auspicious ceremony performed daily, any daily<BR>religious rite for success.<BR>—मङ्गलेच्छु (˚ल-इच्˚),<BR>उस्, उस्, उ, wishing well, wishing joy, wishing pros-<BR>perity or happiness.<BR>—मङ्गलेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚ल-<BR>ईश्˚), अम्, n. ‘Tīrtha of the lord of prosperity,’ N.<BR>of a sacred bathing-place mentioned in the Revā-<BR>māhātmya division of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—मङ्ग-<BR>लोपेप्सा (˚ल-उप्˚), f. the wish or desire for pros-<BR>perity or happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलिक
मङ्गलिक, N. of the hymns of the eighteenth<BR>Kāṇḍa of the Atharva-veda (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलीय|मंगलीय
मङ्गलीय, अस्, आ, अम्, auspicious, fortunate,<BR>prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्य|मंगल्य|मङ्गल्यं|मङ्गल्यः
मङ्गल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, auspicious, propitious, for-<BR>tunate, lucky, happy, conferring happiness, pros-<BR>perous; beautiful, pleasing, agreeable; pious, pure,<BR>holy; (अस्), m., N. of several plants, a sort of pulse<BR>or lentil; the sacred fig-tree, Ficus Religiosa; Ægle<BR>Marmelos; = त्रायमाणा; the cocoa-nut tree, Fe-<BR>ronia Elephantum; a species of Karañja (= रीठा-<BR>करञ्ज); = जीवक; N. of a Nāga-rāja; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of several plants, a species of very fragrant sandal;<BR>a sort of Agallochum or aloe wood; Anethum Sowa,<BR>a sort of fennel; Mimosa Suma (= शमी); = अधः-<BR>पुष्पी; = प्रियङ्गु; = शङ्ख-पुष्पी; = मा-<BR>ष-पर्णी; = जीवन्ती, ऋद्धि, हरिद्रा; = दूर्वा;<BR>sweet flag, Acorus Calamus; a particular yellow pig-<BR>ment (= रोचना); a particular perfume (= चीडा);<BR>an epithet of Durgā; (अम्), n. water brought from<BR>various sacred places for the consecration of a king,<BR>&c.; sour curds; sandal-wood; a kind of Agallo-<BR>chum; gold; red lead.<BR>—मङ्गल्य-कुसुमा, f.<BR>‘having auspicious blossoms,’ a species of plant (=<BR>शङ्ख-पुष्पी).<BR>—मङ्गल्य-दण्ड, अस्, m. ‘hav-<BR>ing an auspicious staff,’ N. of a man.<BR>—मङ्गल्य-<BR>नामधेया, f. ‘having an auspicious name,’ a<BR>species of plant (= जीवन्ती).<BR>—मङ्गल्य-वस्तु,<BR>उ, n. any auspicious object or fortunate matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्यक|मंगल्यक|मंगल्यकः|मङ्गल्यकः
मङ्गल्यक, अस्, m. a sort of pulse or lentil,<BR>Cicer Lens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गुष
मङ्गुष मङ्गुष, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्घ्|मंघ्
मङ्घ् मङ्घ्, cl. 1. P. मङ्घति, &c., to<BR>adorn, decorate; A. मङ्घते, &c., to<BR>go, move, move quickly; to begin moving, start;<BR>to begin; to blame; to cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्
मच् मच् [cf. rts. मञ्च्, 1. मुच्, मुञ्च्],<BR>cl. 1. A. मचते, मेचे, मचितुम्, to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">Page0729-b+ 75</a>]<BR>cheat; to be wicked; to boast; to be vain or proud;<BR>to pound, grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मचकचातनी
मचकचातनी मचकचातनी, f. a species of<BR>plant (said to be = पटोलि; also read मेचकचा-<BR>तनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मचक्रुक
मचक्रुक मचक्रुक, अस्, m., N. of a Yakṣa<BR>and of a sacred spot, guarded by him, near the<BR>entrance to Kurukṣetra, (in Mahā-bh. Vana-p. 5079<BR>one edition has मङ्कणक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मचर्चिका|मचर्च्चिका
मचर्चिका मचर्चिका, f. (at the end of a<BR>comp.), excellence, anything excellent or good of its<BR>kind (e. g. गो-मचर्चिका, an excellent cow; cf. म-<BR>तल्लिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्चित्त
मच्चित्त मच्-चित्त. See p. 734, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्छ|मच्छः
मच्छ मच्छ, अस्, m. (corrupted fr. मत्स्य),<BR>a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्
मज् मज्. See निर्-मज्, p. 498, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मजमुदार
मजमुदार मजमुदार = مجموع دار; मज्-<BR>मूऽ-दार्, a record-keeper, document-holder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मजिरक
मजिरक मजिरक, अस्, m., N. of a man<BR>(Gaṇa Śivādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 112; cf. माजिरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्ज्
मज्ज् मज्ज् (in the Dhātu-pāṭha written<BR>मस्ज्), cl. 6. P. (ep. also A.) मज्जति,<BR>(-ते), ममज्ज (2nd sing. ममज्जिथ or म-<BR>मङ्क्थ), मङ्क्ष्यति (ep. also मज्जिष्यति),<BR>अमाङ्क्षीत् (ep. 2nd sing. अमज्जीस्; with particle<BR>मा, मज्जीस्), मङ्क्तुम् or मज्जितुम्, to sink (in<BR>water), dive, bathe, be submerged or immersed; to<BR>dip one's self, plunge, bathe, throw one's self into<BR>water; to sink down, sink under, sink into (with<BR>loc. or acc., e. g. तमो मज्जति, he sinks into dark-<BR>ness, Manu IV. 81); to be drowned, perish in<BR>water, perish; to sink into misfortune, become<BR>ruined; to despond, be disheartened: Caus. मज्ज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अममज्जत्, to cause to sink (in<BR>water), immerse, submerge, dip, bathe, cause to<BR>plunge or dive, drown, deluge, cause to perish, over-<BR>whelm: Desid. मिमङ्क्षति, मिमज्जिषति: In-<BR>tens. मामज्ज्यते, मामङ्क्ति; [cf. Lat. mergo:<BR>Lith. merkiu, ‘macero;’ mazgoju = Caus. मज्ज-<BR>यामि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्न|मग्नः
मग्न, अस्, आ, अम्, plunged, dived, immersed;<BR>sunk, drowned; absorbed; (अस्), m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्तव्य
मङ्क्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be dived or immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्तृ
मङ्क्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who dives or plunges,<BR>diving, plunging, bathing, performing ablutions;<BR>drowning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्त्वा
मङ्क्त्वा or मक्त्वा, ind. (Pāṇ. VI. 4, 32), hav-<BR>ing sunk or dived; having plunged; having im-<BR>mersed one's self; being plunged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्ज
मज्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, sinking, diving; [cf. उद-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जत्
मज्जत्, अन्, अन्ती or अती, अत्, sinking, drowning,<BR>dipping, bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन्
मज्जन्, आ, m. (said to be fr. rt. मज्ज् above,<BR>according to some for an original मर्जन्?), the<BR>marrow of the bones and flesh; the pith or sap of<BR>plants; (in the later medical system) the element or<BR>essential ingredient [cf. धातु] of the body which<BR>is produced from the bones and itself produces semen;<BR>[cf. Old Germ. marag; Angl. Sax. mearg, merg.]<BR>—मज्ज-कृत्, त्, n. ‘producing marrow,’ a bone.<BR>—मज्जन्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. marrowy, (op-<BR>posed to अ-मज्जक.)<BR>—मज्ज-समुद्भव, अम्,<BR>n. ‘produced from the marrow,’ semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन|मज्जनं|मज्जनः
मज्जन, अस्, m. ‘the diver,’ N. of a kind of<BR>supernatural being; N. of one of Śiva's attend-<BR>ants; (अम्), n. the act of sinking or sinking under<BR>water, diving, immersion; dipping, bathing, ablution;<BR>perishing in water, drowning; deluging; = मज्जन्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जयितृ
मज्जयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. one who causes to<BR>sink or plunge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जल
मज्जल, अस्, m., N. of one of Skanda's attend-<BR>ants, (also read मज्जान; cf. मज्जन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जस्
मज्जस्, अस्, n. = मज्जन्, marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जा
मज्जा, f. the marrow of the bones or flesh [cf.<BR>निर्-मज्ज]; pith, sap, the sap of plants.<BR>—मज्जा-<BR>गत, अस्, आ, अम्, seated in the marrow (as a<BR>disease).<BR>—मज्जा-ज, अस्, m. a species of bdellium<BR>(= भूमिज-गुग्गुलु).<BR>—मज्जा-मेह, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a particular disease of the urinary organs.<BR>—मज्जा-<BR>रजस्, अस्, n. a particular hell; bdellium.<BR>—मज्जा-<BR>रस, अस्, m. ‘marrow-secretion,’ semen virile.<BR>—मज्जा-सार, अम्, n. nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जान
मज्जान, अस्, m. = मज्जल, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जिका
मज्जिका, f. the female of the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जूक
मज्जूक, अस्, आ, अम्, repeatedly or habitually<BR>diving (used in Nirukta IX. 5. to explain the word<BR>मण्डूक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जूषा
मज्जूषा मज्जूषा, f. = मञ्जूषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्मना
मज्मना मज्मना, ind. (inst. case of a form<BR>मज्मन्; cf. मंहना), Ved. in one mass, to-<BR>gether, collectively, in one body, generally; with or<BR>by strength, by might, by intensity (Sāy. = बलेन,<BR>according to Naighaṇṭuka 11. 9. मज्मना = बल);<BR>[cf. Lat. magmentum.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च्|मंच्
मञ्च् मञ्च्, cl. 1. A. मञ्चते, &c., to<BR>cheat; to be wicked, &c. (= rts. मच्,<BR>1. मुच्, मुञ्च्); to hold; to grow high or tall; to<BR>adore; to shine; to go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च|मंच|मंचः|मञ्चः
मञ्च, अस्, m. a stage or platform supported by<BR>columns, a scaffold or temporary structure erected for<BR>spectators on festive occasions; an elevated shed<BR>raised on bamboos in a field (where a watchman is<BR>stationed to protect the crop from cattle, birds, &c.);<BR>a bedstead, couch, bed, sofa; a chair; a seat of<BR>state, throne; a pulpit.<BR>—मञ्च-मण्डप, अस्, m.<BR>a sort of temporary open shed standing upon bamboo<BR>posts; a platform erected for marriage ceremonies or<BR>other festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चक|मंचक|मंचकं|मञ्चकः
मञ्चक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a stage, platform, tem-<BR>porary scaffold erected on a house; a couch, bed;<BR>any frame or stand; a kind of brazier or stand for<BR>holding fire; (इका), f. = आसन्दी, a chair; a trough,<BR>tray.<BR>—मञ्चकाश्रय (˚क-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘bed-<BR>infesting,’ a bed-bug, house-bug.<BR>—मञ्चकासुर<BR>(˚क-अस्˚), अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—मञ्चकासुर-<BR>दुन्दुभि-वध, अस्, m., N. of a chapter of the<BR>Krīḍā-khaṇḍa of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चयाय्य
मञ्चयाय्य, अस्, m., N. of a brother of Cauṇḍa-<BR>pācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चुका
मञ्चुका in मदन-मञ्चुका, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्ज्|मंज्
मञ्ज् मञ्ज् (connected with rts. मार्ज्,<BR>मृज्), cl. 10. P. मञ्जयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>wipe, clean, cleanse, purify, wipe off; to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जर|मंजर|मंजरं|मञ्जरं
मञ्जर, अम्, n. a cluster of blossoms; a species<BR>of plant (= तिलक); a pearl; [cf. देव-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरि|मंजरि|मंजरिः|मञ्जरिः
मञ्जरि, इस्, or मञ्जरी, f. a cluster of blossoms;<BR>a compound pedicle or flower-stalk, a branching<BR>flower-stalk; a flower-bud; a shoot, sprout, sprig,<BR>stalk, (often at the end of titles of works, cf. प्र-<BR>दीप-म्˚); N. of a work by Bhaṭṭācārya-cūḍāmaṇi<BR>(abbreviated fr. the full title Nyāya-siddhānta-mañ-<BR>jarī); a parallel line or row; a species of plant (=<BR>तिलक); N. of a metre, four times ˘˘¯˘¯,<BR>˘˘˘¯˘¯¯˘¯; of another consisting of four lines<BR>of 12, 8, 16, and 20 syllables; a pearl; a creeper;<BR>= तुलसी, holy basil; [cf. Gr. μάργαρον, μαργαρίτης;<BR>Lat. margarita.]<BR>—मञ्जरी-चामर, अम्, n. a<BR>fan-like sprout.<BR>—मञ्जरी-नम्र, अस्, m. ‘bent<BR>down with clusters of flowers,’ the plant Calamus<BR>Rotang.<BR>—मञ्जरी-पिञ्जरित, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>pearls and gold.<BR>—मञ्जरी-प्रकाश or न्याय-<BR>सिद्धान्त-मञ्जरी-प्रकाश, अस्, m. a commen-<BR>tary by Bhāskara or Laugākṣi Bhāskara on the<BR>Nyāya-siddhānta-mañjarī (an elementary treatise on<BR>the Nyāya system).<BR>—मञ्जरी-सार or न्याय-सिद्-<BR>धान्त-मञ्जरी-सार, अम्, n. a commentary by<BR>Yādava Vyāsa on the Nyāya-siddhānta-mañjarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरिका
मञ्जरिका, f. = मञ्जरी in कटु-म्˚, पुष्प-<BR>म्˚; N. of a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरित|मंजरित
मञ्जरित, अस्, आ, अम्, having clusters of flowers<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">Page0730-a+ 81</a>]<BR>or branching flower-stalks; mounted on a stalk (as<BR>a bud &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जा|मंजा
मञ्जा, f. a cluster of blossoms, a branching flower-<BR>stalk; a creeper; = अजा, a she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जि|मंजि|मंजिः|मञ्जिः
मञ्जि, इस्, or मञ्जी, f. a cluster of blossoms, &c.<BR>[cf. अङ्गार-मञ्जी]; a creeper.<BR>—मञ्जि-फला, f.<BR>the plantain tree, Musa Sapientum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिका|मंजिका
मञ्जिका, f. a harlot, courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिमन्|मंजिमन्
मञ्जिमन्, आ, m. (fr. मञ्जु), beauty, loveliness,<BR>elegance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिष्ठ|मंजिष्ठ
मञ्जिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (probably superl. of<BR>मञ्जु, according to Pāṇ. fr. मञ्जि), bright red<BR>(as the Indian madder); (आ), f. Bengal or Indian<BR>madder, Rubia Mujista; [cf. माञ्जिष्ठ.]<BR>—मञ्-<BR>जिष्ठाभ (˚ठ-आभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the<BR>colour of Indian madder.<BR>—मञ्जिष्टा-मेह, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a disease in which the urine is of a light<BR>red colour.<BR>—मञ्जिष्ठा-मेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering<BR>from the above disease.<BR>—मञ्जिष्ठा-राग, अस्, m.<BR>the colour or dye of the Indian madder; an attach-<BR>ment charming and durable as the colour of the<BR>Indian madder, permanent attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जीर|मंजीर|मंजीरं|मंजीरः|मञ्जीरः
मञ्जीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. an ornament for the<BR>feet or toes, a ring, bangle, foot-oprnament, anklet;<BR>(अम्), n. a post round which the string of the churn-<BR>ing-stick passes; a metre, four times ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘˘<BR>¯˘¯˘¯; (आ), f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जीरक
मञ्जीरक, अस्, m. a proper N.; [cf. माञ्जीरक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जील|मंजील|मंजीलः|मञ्जीलः
मञ्जील, अस्, m. a village inhabited especially by<BR>washermen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जु|मंजु
मञ्जु, उस्, उस्, उ (perhaps corrupted fr. मनो-<BR>ज्ञ, but said to be fr. rt. मञ्ज्), beautiful, lovely,<BR>charming, pleasing, agreeable, sweet.<BR>—मञ्जु-कुल,<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मञ्जु-केशिन्, ई, m. ‘beautiful-<BR>haired,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—मञ्जु-<BR>गमन, अस्, आ, अम्, going beautifully or with<BR>graceful movements; (आ), f. a goose; a flamingo.<BR>—मञ्जु-गर्त, a N. of Nepal.<BR>—मञ्जु-गिर्, ईर्,<BR>ईर्, ईर्, having a charming voice, singing sweetly.<BR>—मञ्जु-गीति, इस्, f. a metre consisting of 29 + 30<BR>syllables.<BR>—मञ्जु-गुञ्ज, अस्, m. a charming murmur<BR>or humming.<BR>—मञ्जु-घोष, अस्, आ, अम्, having a<BR>sweet voice or cry, uttering a sweet sound; (अस्), m.<BR>= मञ्जु-श्री; N. of a deity worshipped by the<BR>Tāntrikas; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—मञ्जु-<BR>देव and मञ्जु-नाथ, अस्, m. = मञ्जु-श्री.<BR>—मञ्जु-नाशी, f. a beautiful woman (‘destroying<BR>or eclipsing other beautiful women?’); epithet of<BR>the wife of Indra; of Durgā; (perhaps for मञ्जु-<BR>नारी.)<BR>—मञ्जु-नेत्र, अम्, n. a beautiful eye; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्), lovely-eyed.<BR>—मञ्जु-पत्तन, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a town built by Mañju-śrī.<BR>—मञ्जु-पाठक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘repeating beautifully,’ a parrot.<BR>—मञ्जु-<BR>प्राण, अस्, m. an epithet of Brahmā.<BR>—मञ्जु-<BR>भद्र, अस्, m. = मञ्जु-श्री.<BR>—मञ्जु-भाषिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, sweetly speaking; (इणी), f. a particular metre.<BR>—मञ्जु-मञ्जीर, अस्, अम्, m. n. a beautiful foot-<BR>ornament.<BR>—मञ्जु-मती, f., N. of a princess.<BR>—मञ्जु-वक्त्र, अस्, आ, अम्, beautiful faced, lovely,<BR>handsome.<BR>—मञ्जु-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, speaking beauti-<BR>fully (as a parrot).<BR>—मञ्जु-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speak-<BR>ing delightfully; (इनी), f. a kind of metre, four<BR>times ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯; N. of a woman.<BR>—मञ्जु-श्री, ईस्, m., N. of one of the most cele-<BR>brated Bodhi-sattvas among the northern Buddhists.<BR>—मञ्जुश्री-परिपृच्छा, f., N. of a Buddhist work.<BR>—मञ्जुश्री-पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—मञ्जुश्री-मूल-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist<BR>work.<BR>—मञ्जुश्री-विक्रीडित, अम्, n., N. of a Bud-<BR>dhist work.<BR>—मञ्जु-सौरभ, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>metre, two lines of ˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯, ˘˘¯˘¯<BR>˘˘˘¯˘¯˘¯.<BR>—मञ्जु-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, sweet-<BR>sounding.<BR>—मञ्जु-स्वर, अस्, m. = मञ्जु-श्री;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), sounding or buzzing sweetly (as<BR>bees).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुल|मंजुल|मञ्जुलं|मञ्जुलः
मञ्जुल, अस्, आ, अम्, beautiful, pleasing, agreeable,<BR>charming, lovely, sweet, soft, melodious; (अस्), m.<BR>a species of water-hen or gallinule (= दात्यूह,<BR>जल-रङ्क, जल-रङ्कु); (आ), f., N. of a river;<BR>(अम्), n. a bower, arbour (= कुञ्ज); a spring, well,<BR>natural water-course or channel (= जलाञ्चल); the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">Page0730-b+ 71</a>]<BR>fruit of Ficus Oppositifolia, Vallisneria Octandra;<BR>variegated or the state of being variegated (= श-<BR>वल or शैवल?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुलिका
मञ्जुलिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जूषा|मंजूषा
मञ्जूषा मञ्जूषा, f. (sometimes written<BR>मञ्जुषा; according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 77, fr. rt.<BR>मज्ज्), a box, chest, case (for a bow &c.); recep-<BR>tacle, (sometimes at the end of titles of works,<BR>cf. धातु-न्याय-म्˚); a basket, large basket, ham-<BR>per; N. of a work by Nāgeśa (abridged from the full<BR>title Vaiyākaraṇa-siddhānta-mañjūṣā); N. of a com-<BR>mentary on a work called Jagadīśa-toṣiṇī; = मञ्-<BR>जिष्ठा, Bengal madder; a stone.<BR>—मञ्जूषा-<BR>कुञ्चिका, f. ‘key to the Mañjūṣā,’ N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Kṛṣṇa-mitra on Nāgeśa's Mañjūṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जूषक
मञ्जूषक, अस्, m., N. of a species of celestial<BR>flower; [cf. महा-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटक|मटकः
मटक मटक (formed fr. मृतक), a dead<BR>body, corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटची
मटची मटची, f. (probably) = मटती, hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटती
मटती मटती, f. hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटस्फटि|मटस्फटिः
मटस्फटि मटस्फटि, इस्, m. incipient arro-<BR>gance or pride (= दर्पारम्भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटामटाय
मटामटाय मटामटाय (an onomatopoetic<BR>verb), मटामटायति, &c., to make the sound<BR>Maṭā-maṭā; [cf. पट-पटा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटुतचण्डी
मटुतचण्डी मटुत-चण्डी, f., N. of a Rāk-<BR>ṣasī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मट्टक|मट्टकं
मट्टक मट्टक, अस्, m. = मडक, Eleusine<BR>Coracana; (अम्), n. the ridge or top of a roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मट्मट
मट्मट मट्मट, अस्, m., Ved. a species of<BR>demon or evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ्
मठ् मठ् [cf. rt. मण्ठ्], cl. 1. P. म-<BR>ठति, &c., to dwell, inhabit; to grind;<BR>to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ|मठं|मठः
मठ, अस्, अम्, m. n. (probably connected with<BR>the preceding rt.), a hut, cottage, especially the re-<BR>tired hut of an ascetic, a building inhabited by a<BR>devotee and his disciples, a small retired room occu-<BR>pied by a pupil, a pupil's cell; a cloister, convent,<BR>monastery, a school, college (especially for young<BR>Brāhmans prosecuting sacred studies); a temple; a<BR>carriage or cart drawn by oxen; (ई), f. a cell; a<BR>cloister.<BR>—मठ-केशव-धारिणी, f. epithet of<BR>Nandā the founder of the college of Keśava (Rāja-<BR>tar. V. 244).<BR>—मठ-स्थिति, इस्, इस्, इ, staying or<BR>residing in a college of priests.<BR>—मठाधिद्पति<BR>(˚ठ-अध्˚), इस्, or मठाध्यक्ष (˚ठ-अध्˚),<BR>अस्, m. the superintendent of a monastery, principal<BR>of a college, &c.<BR>—मठायतन (˚ठ-अय्˚), अम्,<BR>n. a monastery, convent, college.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठिका
मठिका, f. a hut, cottage; a cell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठर|मठरः
मठर मठर, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>मन्, and included in the Gaṇa Kaḍārādi, see Pāṇ.<BR>II. 2, 38), intoxicated; (perhaps) persisting in any-<BR>thing (with loc.); (अस्), m., N. of a man, (according<BR>to some) of a Muni; [cf. माठर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठोशीलोठिका
मठोशीलोठिका मठोशीलोठिका, f. (pro-<BR>bably) N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मडक|मडकः
मडक मडक, अस्, m. Eleusine Coracana<BR>[cf. मट्टक]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मडव
मडव मडव or मडव-राज्य, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a district in Kāśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड्डचन्द्र
मड्डचन्द्र मड्ड-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N. of a man<BR>(mentioned in Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VIII. 3416).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड्डु|मड्डुः
मड्डु मड्डु, उस्, or मड्डुक, अस्, m. a sort<BR>of drum; [cf. माड्डुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्
मण् मण्, cl. 1. P. मणति, ममाण, &c.,<BR>to sound, murmur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणि|मणिः
मणि, इस्, m. f. (usually m., said to be fr. rt. मण्,<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 117; a form मणी, f., is also given),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-c" target="_blank">Page0730-c+ 81</a>]<BR>a jewel, gem, precious stone (especially a pearl, bead,<BR>or other globular ornament); an ornament or amulet<BR>in general; anything excellent of its kind (e. g.<BR>खग-मणि, a jewel of a bird); a crystal [cf. काच-<BR>म्˚]; a magnet, loadstone; glans penis; clitoris;<BR>the fleshy excrescences or processes on the neck of a<BR>goat; = मणि-भन्ध, the wrist; a water-pot (=<BR>अलिञ्जर); N. of a Nāga; N. of a companion of<BR>Skanda (associated with Su-maṇi in Mahā-bh. Śalya-<BR>p. 2534); N. of a sage (in Mahā-bh. Sabhā-p. 442);<BR>of a son of Yuyudhāna (in Hari-vaṃśa 9207; also<BR>read तूणि); of a work (abridged from the full title<BR>of Tattva-cintāmaṇi, q. v.); of a collection of magical<BR>formulas; [cf. Gr. μάννος, μόννος; Lat. monile.]<BR>—मणि-कण्ठ, अस्, m. the blue jay or roller bird;<BR>N. of a Nāga.<BR>—मणिकण्ठक, अस्, m. a cock.<BR>—मणि-कर्ण, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, ‘jewel-eared,’<BR>having an ornament of any kind (as a mark) on the<BR>ear; (अस्), m., N. of a Śiva-liṅga in Kāma-rūpa;<BR>(ई), f. = मणि-करणिका below.<BR>—मणि-करणिका, f.,<BR>N. of a sacred pool or tank in Benares much fre-<BR>quented by pilgrims, (also written मणि-कर्णिकी);<BR>of a daughter of Caṇḍa-ghoṣa.<BR>—मणिकर्णिका-<BR>महिमन्, आ, m. and मणिकर्णिका-स्तोत्र, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of two works by Gaṅgā-dhara.<BR>—मणिकर्णिका-<BR>माहात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of the twenty-second chapter<BR>of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the Śiva-Purāṇa.<BR>—मणि-<BR>कर्णीश्वर (˚णी-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Śiva-liṅga at<BR>Benares.<BR>—मणिकर्णेश्वर (˚ण-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Śiva-liṅga in Kāma-rūpa.<BR>—मणि-काच, अस्, m.<BR>the feathered part of an arrow.<BR>—मणि-काञ्चन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a mountain (mentioned in Mahā-bhā-<BR>rata Bhīṣma-p. 426).<BR>—मणि-कानन, अम्, n. a<BR>wood or grove containing jewels; the neck, throat<BR>(as covered with jewels).<BR>—मणि-कार, अस्, m. a<BR>worker in precious stones, lapidary, jeweller; N. of<BR>the author of the work called Maṇi; of the author<BR>of the Nyāya-cintāmaṇi.<BR>—मणि-कुट्टिका, f. [cf.<BR>कुट्टक], N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on<BR>Skanda.<BR>—मणि-कुसुम, अस्, m., N. of a Jina.<BR>—मणि-कूट, अस्, m., N. of a mountain in Kāma-<BR>rūpa.<BR>—मणि-कृत्, त्, m. = मणि-कार.<BR>—मणि-<BR>केतु, उस्, m., N. of a particular comet or meteor.<BR>—मणि-गण, अस्, m. a multitude of pearls.<BR>—मणि-<BR>गुण-निकर, अस्, m. ‘a multitude of strings of pearls,’<BR>a species of the Ati-śakkarī metre, four times<BR>˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘, ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ˘ ¯.<BR>—मणि-ग्रीव, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘jewel-necked,’ wearing a necklace; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of a son of Kuvera.<BR>—मणि-चूड, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Vidyā-dhara; of a king of Sāketa-nagara (= रत्न-<BR>चूड); of a Nāga.<BR>—मणि-च्छिद्रा, f. ‘jewel-<BR>holed,’ N. of two medicinal herbs; = मेदा.<BR>—मणि-<BR>जला, ‘having jewel-like water,’ N. of a river.<BR>—मणि-तारक, अस्, m. ‘jewel-eyed’ [cf. तारक];<BR>the Indian crane.<BR>—मणि-दण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘jewel-<BR>handled,’ having a handle adorned with jewels.<BR>—म-<BR>णि-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—मणि-दर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a chief of the Yakṣas.<BR>—मणि-दर्पण,<BR>अस्, m. a mirror adorned with jewels or consisting of<BR>jewels; N. of a work on music.<BR>—मणि-दीधिति,<BR>इस्, f., N. of a work (abridged from the full title<BR>of Anumāna-maṇidīdhiti).<BR>—मणिदीधिति-गूढार्-<BR>थ-प्रकाशिका, f., N. of a commentary by Bhavā-<BR>nanda Siddhānta-vāg-īśa on the Maṇi-dīdhiti (said<BR>to be an epitome of the Dīdhiti).<BR>—मणि-दीप or<BR>मणि-दीपिक, अस्, m. ‘jewel-lamp,’ a lamp having<BR>jewels.<BR>—मणि-दोष, अस्, m. a flaw or defect in a<BR>jewel.<BR>—मणि-द्वीप, अस्, m. ‘jewel-island,’ N. of a<BR>mythical island in the ocean of nectar; the hood of<BR>the serpent Ananta.<BR>—मणि-धनु, उस्, m. ‘jewel-<BR>bow,’ a rain-bow; N. of a king, (also read मणि-<BR>धान or मणि-धाण्य.)<BR>—मणि-धनुस्, उस्,<BR>n. ‘jewel-bow,’ a rain-bow.<BR>—मणि-धर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having or wearing jewels or beads.<BR>—मणि-<BR>धान, see मणि-धनु above.<BR>—मणि-नाग, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a snake-demon; N. of a sacred bathing-<BR>place.<BR>—मणि-निर्यातन, अम्, n. the restitution of<BR>a jewel.<BR>—मणि-पद्म, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-<BR>sattva.<BR>—मणि-पर्वत, अस्, m. ‘jewel-mountain,’<BR>N. of a mythical mountain.<BR>—मणि-पाली, f. ‘jewel-<BR>keeper,’ a woman who has charge of pearls &c., a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-a" target="_blank">Page0731-a+ 81</a>]<BR>female keeper of jewels.<BR>—मणि-पुच्छी, f. ‘jewel-<BR>tailed,’ having jewels &c. on the tail; [cf. मणि-<BR>बाल.]<BR>—मणि-पुर, अम्, n. = मणि-पूर.<BR>—मणि-<BR>पुष्पक, अस्, m., N. of the conch-shell of Saha-<BR>deva (Bhagavad-gītā 1. 16).<BR>—मणि-पुष्पेश्वर<BR>(˚प-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's attendants.<BR>—मणि-पूर, अम्, n., N. of a town in Kaliṅga<BR>(situated on the sea-shore and the residence of<BR>Babhru-vāhana); the pit of the stomach or a mysti-<BR>cal circle on the navel; (अस्), m. the navel; a sort<BR>of bodice (worn by women and richly adorned with<BR>jewels).<BR>—मणिपूरक, अम्, n., N. of a mystical<BR>circle on the navel.<BR>—मणिपूर-पति, इस्, m., N.<BR>of king Babhru-vāhana.<BR>—मणिपूर-विभेदन,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a jewel.<BR>—मणिपूरेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m. = मणिपूर-पति; (also written मणिपु-<BR>रेश्वर.)<BR>—मणि-प्रदान, अम्, n., N. of the<BR>thirty-fourth chapter of the Sundara-kāṇḍa of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—मणि-प्रदीप, अस्, m. = मणि-दीप.<BR>—मणि-प्रभा, f. ‘jewel-splendor,’ N. of a par-<BR>ticular metre, the first line of which is ¯¯˘¯¯˘˘<BR>¯˘¯¯ and the second, third, and fourth ˘¯˘¯¯<BR>˘˘¯˘¯¯; of a lake.<BR>—मणि-प्रवेक, a most<BR>excellent jewel; [cf. प्रवेक.]<BR>—मणि-बन्ध,<BR>अस्, m. the fastening or putting on of jewels; the<BR>wrist (as the place on which jewels are fastened); a<BR>kind of metre, four times ¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘ [cf.<BR>मणि-मध्य]; N. of a mixed race.<BR>—मणि-<BR>बन्धन, अम्, n. the fastening on of jewels, a<BR>string of pearls, an ornament of pearls; the part of<BR>a ring or bracelet where the jewels are set; the wrist<BR>or fore-arm from the wrist to the elbow.<BR>—मणि-<BR>बाल, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘jewel-tailed’ or having jewel-like<BR>lumps on the tail, (according to Mahī-dhara on Vāja-<BR>saneyi-saṃhitā XXIV. 3 = मणि-शुद्ध-बाल or<BR>मणि-वर्ण-केश.)<BR>—मणि-बीज, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>jewel-like or pearl-like seeds,’ the pomegranate tree.<BR>—मणि-भद्र, अस्, m., N. of a king of the<BR>Yakṣas (the tutelary deity of travellers and mer-<BR>chants, probably another name for Kuvera); of a<BR>Jina or Jaina teacher (= पूर्व-यक्ष); of a<BR>brother of Kuvera; of a Śreṣṭhin; [cf. माणि-<BR>भद्र.]<BR>—मणिभद्रक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>race (in Mahā-bh. Bhīṣma-p. 2099; also read पारि-<BR>भद्रक); of a serpent-demon.<BR>—मणि-भव,<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the five Dhyāni-Buddhas.<BR>—मणि-भित्ति, इस्, f. ‘jewel-walled,’ N. of the palace<BR>of the serpent-demon Śeṣa.<BR>—मणि-भू, ऊस्, f. a<BR>floor inlaid with jewels.<BR>—मणि-भूमि, इस्, f. a floor<BR>inlaid with precious stones; a mine of jewels; [cf.<BR>कुट्टिम.]<BR>—मणि-भूमिका, f. a floor inlaid with<BR>jewels; (according to a Scholiast मणिभूमिका-<BR>कर्मन् = कृत्रिम-पुत्रिका-निर्माण.)<BR>—मणि-<BR>मञ्जरी, f. rows of jewels or pearls; a species of<BR>the Ati-dhṛti metre, four times ˘¯¯¯˘˘˘˘˘˘<BR>¯¯˘¯˘˘¯˘¯.<BR>—मणि-मण्डप, अस्, m. ‘jewel-<BR>palace, crystal-palace,’ N. of the residence of Śeṣa<BR>and of Nairṛta, the ruler of the south-west quarter.<BR>—मणि-मण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, set or studded with<BR>jewels or pearls.<BR>—मणि-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>or adorned with jewels, jewelled; (आन्), m. the sun;<BR>N. of a Yakṣa; of a servant of Śiva; of a Rakṣas;<BR>of a Nāga; of a king (who was Vṛtra in a former<BR>birth); of a mountain; of a place of pilgrimage;<BR>(अती), f., N. of a town of the Daityas; of a river.<BR>—मणि-मध्य, अम्, n., N. of a metre, four<BR>times ¯˘˘¯¯, ¯˘˘¯.<BR>—मणि-मन्थ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a mountain; (अम्), n. = माणिमन्थ, rock-<BR>salt.<BR>—मणि-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, formed or consisting<BR>of jewels, set or studded with gems, jewelled.<BR>—म-<BR>णिमय-भू, ऊस्, f. a floor made of gems, a jewelled<BR>floor; (उवस्), f. pl. jewelled floors.<BR>—मणि-महेश,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a place of pilgrimage mentioned in<BR>Raghu-nātha's Rasika-ramaṇa.<BR>—मणि-माला, f. a<BR>string of jewels or pearls, necklace of precious stones;<BR>a circular impression left by a bite (especially in<BR>amorous dalliance); lustre, splendor, beauty; epithet<BR>of Lakṣmī; a kind of metre, four times ¯¯˘˘¯¯<BR>¯¯˘˘¯¯.<BR>—मणि-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Nyāya-ratna.<BR>—मणि-मुक्ता, f., N. of a<BR>river.<BR>—मणि-मेखल, अस्, आ, अम्, girdled with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">Page0731-b+ 78</a>]<BR>gems, surrounded by jewels.<BR>—मणि-मेघ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a mountain.<BR>—मणि-यष्टि, इस्, m. f. a jewelled<BR>staff or stick.<BR>—मणि-रत, अस्, m., N. of a Bud-<BR>dhist teacher; (perhaps for मणि-रथ or मनो-<BR>रथ.)<BR>—मणि-रत्न, अम्, n. a jewel, gem,<BR>precious stone.<BR>—मणिरत्न-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>formed or consisting of jewels, jewelled.<BR>—मणि-<BR>रत्न-माला, f. ‘garland of jewels,’ N. of a philo-<BR>sophical treatise ascribed to Śaṅkarācārya.<BR>—मणि-<BR>रत्न-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, containing jewels, jewelled.<BR>—मणि-रथ, see मणि-रत.<BR>—मणि-राग, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘jewel-coloured,’ having the colour of a<BR>jewel; (अस्), m. ‘jewel-colour,’ the colour of jewels;<BR>a kind of metre, four times ¯˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯¯;<BR>(अम्), n. vermilion (= हिङ्गुल).<BR>—मणि-राज, अस्,<BR>m. ‘jewel-king, jewel-chief,’ (probably) a diamond<BR>[cf. मणीन्द्र].<BR>—मणि-राम, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author; of a commentator who lived in the begin-<BR>ning of this century.<BR>—मणि-लिङ्गेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of one of the eight Vīta-rāgas.<BR>—मणि-<BR>वर्मन्, आ, m., N. of a merchant.<BR>—मणि-वाल,<BR>see मणि-बाल.<BR>—मणि-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘jewel-<BR>bearer,’ an epithet of Kuśāmba (in Mahā-bh. Ādi-p.<BR>2363).<BR>—मणि-विशेष, अस्, m. a kind of jewel; an<BR>excellent jewel.<BR>—मणि-वीज, अम्, n. a pomegranate.<BR>—मणि-शङ्ख-शर्कर, अस्, आ, अम्, having jewel-<BR>like shells and gravel.<BR>—मणि-शर = मणि-सर.<BR>—मणि-शिला, f. a jewelled slab.<BR>—मणि-शृङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m. (probably) N. of the sun.<BR>—मणि-शैल, अस्,<BR>m. ‘jewel-mountain,’ N. of a mountain.<BR>—मणि-<BR>श्याम, अस्, आ, अम्, dark-blue like a jewel, i. e. like<BR>a sapphire; (according to a Scholiast मणि = इन्द्र-<BR>नील.)<BR>—मणि-सर, अस्, m. a string of pearls, an<BR>ornament of pearls, a necklace, (wrongly written<BR>मणि-शर.)<BR>—मणि-सार, N. of a work.<BR>—मणि-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n. a string of pearls.<BR>—मणि-सोपान,<BR>अम्, n. steps or stairs set with jewels, a jewelled<BR>staircase; a staff or stick set with jewels (?).<BR>—मणि-<BR>स्कन्ध, अस्, m., N. of a snake-demon.<BR>—मणि-<BR>स्तम्भ, अस्, m. a post or column set with jewels,<BR>a jewelled post or pillar.<BR>—मणि-स्रज्, क्, f. a garland<BR>of jewels.<BR>—मणि-हर्म्य, अम्, n. a jewelled palace,<BR>crystal-palace; N. of a particular palace.<BR>—मणीन्द्र<BR>(˚णि-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘jewel-chief,’ (probably) a diamond<BR>[cf. मणि-राज].<BR>—मणीश्वर-तीर्थ (˚णि-ईश्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—मण्य्-आलोक,<BR>N. of a commentary by Jaya-deva Tarkālaṅkāra on<BR>part of the Tattva-cintāmaṇī, (also called आलोक.)<BR>—मण्यालोक-कण्टकोद्धार (˚क-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘removing thorns from the Maṇy-āloka,’ N. of a<BR>commentary on the Maṇy-āloka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिक|मणिकं|मणिकः
मणिक, अस्, m. a jewel, gem, precious stone;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a water-jar or pitcher; (according<BR>to Sāy.) globular formations of flesh on an animal's<BR>shoulder; [cf. माणिक्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणित|मणितं
मणित, अम्, n. a murmuring sound, an inarticu-<BR>late sound said to be uttered at cohabitation, murmur<BR>libidinosum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिल
मणिल, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having fleshy excres-<BR>cences (as on the dew-lap &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिव|मणिवः
मणिव, अस्, आ, अम्, in अ-मणिव, (perhaps)<BR>‘having no jewels’ (opposed to सु-मणि, q. v.);<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a serpent-demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीचक|मणीचकं|मणीचकः
मणीचक, अस्, m. a king-fisher, halcyon; (अम्),<BR>n. a particular jewel, the moon-stone (probably a<BR>sort of crystal; cf. चन्द्र-कान्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीय
मणीय, Nom. A. मणीयते, &c., to become a<BR>jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीवक|मणीवकं
मणीवक, अम्, n. a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण
मण मण (fr. Arabic من a particular<BR>measure of grain by weight = 40 ser, mentioned by<BR>Hindū writers as used by the Turuṣkas or Muham-<BR>madans, a ‘maund.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणऊ
मणऊ मणऊ (fr. Arabic منع), N. of the<BR>seventh Yoga (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणि|मणिः
मणि मणि. See p. 730, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणित्थ
मणित्थ मणित्थ, अस्, m., N. of an astro-<BR>nomer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्टपी
मण्टपी मण्टपी, f. a species of pot-herb<BR>(= क्षुद्रोपोदकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्टि
मण्टि मण्टि, इस्, m., N. of a man; (pro-<BR>bably wrongly for माण्टि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ठ्|मंठ्
मण्ठ् मण्ठ्, cl. 1. A. मण्ठते, &c., to<BR>desire eagerly, long for; to remember<BR>with regret, to meditate sorrowfully, grieve for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ठ|मंठः|मण्ठः
मण्ठ मण्ठ, अस्, m. a sort of baked<BR>sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ठक
मण्ठक मण्ठक, a particular musical air;<BR>[cf. प्रति-म्˚, मण्डक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ड्|मंड्
मण्ड् मण्ड् (connected with rts. 2. मद्,<BR>मन्द्), cl. 1. P. मण्डति, ममण्ड,<BR>मण्डितुम्, to adorn one's self; cl. 1. A. मण्डते,<BR>&c., to clothe, dress; to surround, encompass; to<BR>divide, distribute; cl. 10. P. (ep. also A.) मण्ड-<BR>यति (-ते), -यितुम्, to adorn; to rejoice, exhilarate;<BR>[cf. Lat. mund-u-s, mund-are.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ड|मंडं|मण्डं|मंडः|मण्डः
मण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. (in Uṇādi-s. 1. 113. said<BR>to be fr. rt. मन्), that part of any fluid which<BR>rises and collects on the surface in the process of<BR>fermentation or while boiling; the scum or thick<BR>oily matter which forms on the surface of any liquor<BR>or liquid; the thick part of milk, cream, (दधि-ज<BR>मण्ड,) sour cream; cf. दधि-म्˚); the spirituous<BR>part of wine, &c.; the scum of boiled rice (or any<BR>grain); skimmings, scum, foam or forth in general;<BR>barm, ferment; gruel; the best part of anything,<BR>essence, pith (= सार); the head; (अस्), m. orna-<BR>ment, decoration; the castor-oil tree, Ricinus Com-<BR>munis [cf. अमण्ड]; a particular species of pot-<BR>herb; a frog [cf. मण्डूक]; (आ), f. the emblic<BR>myrobalan tree (= आमलकी); spirituous or vinous<BR>liquor, brandy; (अम्), n. (Ved.) an oar (? connected<BR>with मङ्ग).<BR>—मण्ड-करण, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man; [cf. माण्डकर्णि.]<BR>—मण्ड-चित्र, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the family of Maṇḍa-<BR>citra.<BR>—मण्ड-प, अस्, आ, अम्, drinking the scum<BR>of boiled rice or of any liquor, sipping cream, &c.;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. an open hall or temporary shed erected<BR>on festive occasions, (in this sense probably fr. मण्ड,<BR>an ornament, + 3. पा); a temple or building conse-<BR>crated to a deity; a pavilion, shed, tent; an arbour,<BR>bower; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (आ), f. a sort of pulse or<BR>leguminous plant (= निष्पावी).<BR>—मण्डप-क्षे-<BR>त्र, अम्, n., N. of a particular sacred district.<BR>—मण्-<BR>डप-प्रतिष्ठा, f. the consecration of a temple.<BR>—मण्ड-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of cream or<BR>from the scum of any liquid.<BR>—मण्ड-हारक,<BR>अस्, m. a distiller of spirits, &c.<BR>—मण्डोदक (˚ड-<BR>उद्˚), अम्, n. barm, yeast; the decorating of walls,<BR>floors, &c. on festive occasions; = चित्त-राग, mental<BR>excitement; (according to some) = चित्र-राग, varie-<BR>gated colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डक|मंडकः|मण्डकः
मण्डक, अस्, इका, अम्, a sort of thick gruel<BR>made of rice &c., (at the end of a comp., e. g.<BR>प्रिय-मण्डक, fond of this dish); (अस्), m. a<BR>sort of pastry or baked flour; a particular musical<BR>air [cf. मण्ठक]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>(also read मन्दक; cf. मण्डिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डन|मंडन|मण्डनं|मण्डनः
मण्डन, अस्, आ, अम्, adorning, dressing out,<BR>decorating; fond of ornament; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>man, = मण्डन-मिश्र below; (अम्), n. the act<BR>of adorning or decorating, bedecking one's self, de-<BR>coration, jewels, trinkets, (मण्डनं कुरुते, she<BR>adorns herself); ornament, embellishment; N. of a<BR>work.<BR>—मण्डन-कवि, इस्, m., N. of a Pandit.<BR>—मण्डन-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a philosopher<BR>(also called Sureśvarācārya and Viśva-rūpācārya).<BR>—मण्डनार्ह (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy of<BR>ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डनक
मण्डनक in मुख-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डपिक
मण्डपिक, अस्, m. or मण्डपिका, f. (fr. मण्ड-<BR>प above), a little pavilion; a small shed, shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डयन्त|मंडयंतः|मण्डयन्तः
मण्डयन्त, अस्, m. an ornament; an actor; an<BR>assembly of women; food; (ई), f. a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डिक
मण्डिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (also read<BR>शुण्डिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डित|मंडित|मण्डितः
मण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned, ornamented, deco-<BR>rated; (अस्), m. (with Jainas) N. of one of the<BR>eleven Gaṇādhipas; a Vāsiṣṭha.<BR>—मण्डित-पु-<BR>त्र, अस्, m. = मण्डित, N. of one of the eleven<BR>Gaṇādhipas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डप|मंडपः|मण्डपः
मण्डप मण्ड-प. See under मण्ड, p. 731,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डपूल
मण्डपूल मण्डपूल, boots with legs, high<BR>boots, jack-boots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डरी|मंडरी
मण्डरी मण्डरी, f. a sort of cricket; [cf.<BR>माण्डरिक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डल|मंडल|मण्डलं|मण्डलः
मण्डल मण्डल, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr.<BR>rt. मण्ड्), round; (अस्), m. a circular array of troops,<BR>an army drawn up in a circle; a species of snake; a<BR>dog; (अम्), n. a disk (especially the disk of the sun<BR>or moon); anything round (e. g. आदर्श-मण्ड-<BR>लम्, a mirror; चाप-मण्डलम्, the circular bend<BR>of a strung bow); a circle, globe, ball, orb, wheel,<BR>circumference, ring, (said to be also अस्, m.); the<BR>path or orbit of a heavenly body; a great circle (in<BR>astronomy); the visible horizon; a halo round the<BR>sun or moon; any circular figure or diagram; a sort<BR>of mystical diagram formed in summoning a divinity,<BR>&c.; a circular bandage (in surgery); a round mark<BR>(as a mark caused by a finger-nail, &c.); a parti-<BR>cular attitude or position of the feet in shooting; a<BR>district, arrondissement, territory, province (sometimes<BR>at the end of modern names as in Coro-mandal, the<BR>whole circle of territory over which one of the twelve<BR>emperors termed Cakra-vartins was supposed to have<BR>reigned in ancient times); a surrounding district or<BR>territory, the circle of a king's near and distant<BR>neighbours (with whom he must maintain political<BR>and diplomatic relations; four or six or ten or even<BR>twelve such neighbouring princes are enumerated);<BR>a multitude, assemblage, group, troop, collection,<BR>band, whole body, association, society, company,<BR>heap; a division of the Ṛg-veda, (the whole Saṃ-<BR>hitā of the Śākala school, which is the only extant<BR>Śākhā or recension of the Ṛg-veda, is divided into<BR>ten Maṇḍalas, and these into 85 Anuvākas or<BR>sections, and these again into 1017, or with the<BR>eleven additional hymns, into 1028 Sūktas or hymns,<BR>which again are divided into 10, 417 Ṛcs or verses,<BR>and these into 153, 826 Padas or words; the other<BR>method of division is into Aṣṭakas, Adhyāyas,<BR>Vargas, Ṛcs, and Padas; cf. वर्ग); a sort of<BR>cutaneous eruption or leprosy with circular spots, (in<BR>this sense also n. pl.); a sugar-ball, sweetmeat; a<BR>sort of perfume (= व्याघ्र-नख); a particular<BR>oblation or sacrifice; (ई), f. a circle, &c.; an assem-<BR>blage, company, corporate body, church, multitude,<BR>crowd; walking round, whirling, circular motion; a<BR>nest; bent grass, Panicum Dactylon (see दूर्वा).<BR>—मण्डल-कार्मुक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a circular<BR>bow or whose bow is bent; [cf. मण्डली-कृत.]<BR>—मण्डल-चिह्न, अम्, n. the sign or mark of a<BR>circle.<BR>—मण्डल-नृत्य, अम्, n. a circular dance<BR>(especially a dance like that said to have been<BR>danced by the Gopīs round Kṛṣṇa and his mistress<BR>Rādhā; also read मण्डली-नृत्य).<BR>—मण्डल-<BR>न्यास, अम्, n. the putting down or drawing a<BR>circle; मण्डल-न्यासं कृ, to describe a circle.<BR>—मण्डल-पत्त्रिका, f. a red-flowering Punar-<BR>navā.<BR>—मण्डल-पुच्छक, अस्, m. a species of<BR>insect.<BR>—मण्डल-ब्राह्मण, अम्, n., N. of an<BR>Upaniṣad.<BR>—मण्डल-भाग, अस्, m. part of a<BR>circle.<BR>—मण्डल-वट, अस्, m. an Indian fig-tree<BR>forming a circle; [cf. मण्डलिन्.]<BR>—मण्डल-वर्-<BR>तिन्, ई, m. the governor of a province, ruler of a<BR>small kingdom; [cf. चक्र-वर्तिन्.]<BR>—मण्डल-<BR>वर्ष, अम्, n. (probably) general rain extending<BR>over a whole country, lasting rain.<BR>—मण्डल-शस्,<BR>ind. by circles, in circles, in rings.<BR>—मण्डलाग्र<BR>(˚ल-अग्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, round-pointed, having a round<BR>point or end; (अस्), m. a bent or rounded sword, a<BR>scimitar, sabre; (अम्), n., scil. शस्त्र, a surgeon's<BR>circular knife.<BR>—मण्डलाधिप or मण्डलाधीश<BR>(˚ल-अध्˚), अस्, m. the lord of a district, ruler or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">Page0732-b+ 79</a>]<BR>governor of a province, king of a country, a monarch,<BR>emperor.<BR>—मण्डली-करण, अम्, n. the act of<BR>making round, rounding, gathering in a ball or<BR>circle, coiling, &c.<BR>—मण्डली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to make round, form into a circle or ball,<BR>form into a ring, coil.<BR>—मण्डली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>formed into a circle, made circular, rounded, curved,<BR>tense, bent (as a bow).<BR>—मण्डली-नृत्य = मण्-<BR>डल-नृत्य, q. v.<BR>—मण्डली-भू, cl. 1. P. -भ-<BR>वति, -भवितुम्, to become round, to form a circle.<BR>—मण्डली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become round, be-<BR>come circular or rounded, curved, bent (as a bow).<BR>—मण्डलेश (˚ल-ईश) or मण्डलेश्वर (˚ल-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m. the lord of a district, ruler or governor<BR>of a province.<BR>—मण्डलेश-त्व, अम्, n. rulership<BR>of a province, governorship.<BR>—मण्डलोत्तम (˚ल-<BR>उत्˚), अम्, n. the best or most excellent empire,<BR>principal kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलक|मंडलकं|मण्डलकं|मण्डलकः
मण्डलक, अम्, n. a disk; a circle; a district,<BR>province; a cutaneous disease, white leprosy with<BR>round spots; a circular array of troops; a group; a<BR>mirror; (अस्), m. a dog.<BR>—मण्डलक-राजन्, आ,<BR>m. the king of a small district or province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलय
मण्डलय, Nom. P. मण्डलयति, &c., to<BR>make round or circular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलाय
मण्डलाय, Nom. A. मण्डलायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>become a circle, form one's self into a circle or ring,<BR>coil one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलायमान
मण्डलायमान, अस्, आ, अम्, becoming circular,<BR>forming one's self into a circle or ring, coiling one's<BR>self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलायित|मंडलायित|मण्डलायितं
मण्डलायित, अस्, आ, अम्, formed into a circle or<BR>ring; round, circular, = वर्तुल?; (अम्), n. a ball,<BR>globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलित|मंडलित
मण्डलित, अस्, आ, अम्, made round or circular,<BR>(परि-मण्डलित, rounded, whirled round.)<BR>—मण्-<BR>डलित-हस्त-काण्ड, अस्, m. having a trunk formed<BR>in rings or circles (said of an elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिण्डलिन्
मिण्डलिन्, इ, इनी, इ, forming a circle or ring,<BR>made up into a coil or ball; possessing or ruling a<BR>country; (ई), m. ‘marked with round spots,’ a par-<BR>ticular kind of snake (= गो-नास); ‘ringed,’ any<BR>snake; the ruler of a district or province; a pole-cat;<BR>a cat; a dog; the Indian fig-tree [cf. मण्डल-<BR>वट]; the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डित|मंडित|मण्डितः
मण्डित मण्डित. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डु
मण्डु मण्डु, उस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi; [cf.<BR>माण्डव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डुक
मण्डुक in पङ्क-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूक|मंडूकः|मण्डूकः
मण्डूक मण्डूक, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>मण्ड्), a frog; N. of a particular breed of horses;<BR>the plant Calosanthes Indica; N. of a Ṛṣi; of a<BR>Nāga; (according to some) = गाढ-तेजस्?; (आ),<BR>f. the plant Rubia Munjista, = मञ्जिष्ठा; (ई), f.<BR>a female frog; N. of several plants (= मण्डूक-<BR>पर्णी); Hydrocotyle Asiatica; Polanisia Icosandra;<BR>Clerodendrum Siphonanthus; a particular shrub (com-<BR>monly called Khulakuḍī); a wanton woman; (अम्),<BR>n. a kind of coitus; (if मण्डूक occurs at the end of<BR>an adj. comp. the fem. ends in आ.)<BR>—मण्डूक-कुल,<BR>अम्, n. a collection or assemblage of frogs.<BR>—मण्-<BR>डूक-गति-लालस, अस्, आ, अम्, ardently desiring the<BR>gait of a frog.<BR>—मण्डूक-पर्ण, अस्, m., N. of<BR>several plants, Calosanthes Indica, = कपीतन; (ई),<BR>f. Rubia Munjista; Clerodendrum Siphonanthus;<BR>Polanisia Icosandra; Hydrocotyle Asiatica; a par-<BR>ticular shrub (commonly called Khulakuḍī).<BR>—मण्-<BR>डूकपर्णिका, f. = मण्डूक-पर्णी.<BR>—मण्डूक-<BR>प्लुति, इस्, f. ‘frog-leap,’ the passing over or skipping<BR>of several Sūtras and supplying from a previous Sūtra<BR>(in grammar).<BR>—मण्डूक-मातृ, ता, f. ‘the mother<BR>of frogs,’ the plant Clerodendrum Siphonanthus.<BR>—मण्डूक-योग, अस्, m. a particular kind of ab-<BR>stract meditation in which an ascetic sits motionless<BR>like a frog.<BR>—मण्डूकयोग-नियत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>intent upon the frog-meditation.<BR>—मण्डूकयोग-<BR>शयन, अम्, n. lying like a frog in deep medita-<BR>tion.<BR>—मण्डूक-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, lying like a frog.<BR>—मण्डूक-सरस, अम्, n. a frog-pond, pond<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">Page0732-c+ 72</a>]<BR>full of frogs [cf. Pāṇ. V. 4, 94].<BR>—मण्डूकानु-<BR>वृत्ति (˚क-अन्˚), इस्, f. ‘frog-course,’ skipping over<BR>or omitting at intervals; [cf. मण्डूक-प्लुति.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूर|मंडूरं|मण्डूरं
मण्डूर मण्डूर, अम्, n. rust of iron, scoriæ,<BR>dross.<BR>—मण्डूर-धाणिकी, f., Ved. a particular<BR>abusive and indelicate expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्
मत् मत् or मद्, abl. of 3. म, q. v. (serv-<BR>ing for the base of the singular number of the first<BR>personal pronoun at the beginning of compounds, the<BR>proper form in these cases being मद्, see 1. मद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कृत
मत्-कृत, मत्-पर, &c. See under 1. मद्,<BR>p. 734, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत|मतं|मतः
मत मत. See p. 740, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतङ्ग|मतंग|मतंगः|मतङ्गः
मतङ्ग मतङ्ग, अस्, m. (according to some<BR>fr. मतम् + ग, going wilfully), an elephant; a<BR>cloud; N. of a Muni (mentioned in Mahā-bh. Ādi-p.<BR>2925, &c.); of a Dānava; (आस्), m. pl. the family<BR>of this Muni.<BR>—मतङ्ग-ज, अस्, m. an elephant.<BR>—मतङ्गज-त्व, अम्, n. the being an elephant.<BR>—मतङ्ग-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-<BR>place (mentioned in the Śiva-Purāṇa).<BR>—मतङ्ग-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of a fabulous being.<BR>—मतङ्ग-<BR>पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—मतङ्ग-वापी, f.,<BR>N. of a sacred tank.<BR>—मतङ्ग-हतक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतङ्गिनी|मतंगिनी
मतङ्गिनी, f., N. of a daughter of Mandara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतल्लिका
मतल्लिका मतल्लिका, f. (at the end of a<BR>comp.), anything excellent of its kind [cf. मचर्-<BR>चिक, गो-म्˚]; a particular metre, four times ˘¯˘¯<BR>˘¯˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतल्ली
मतल्ली, f. = मतल्लिका, anything excellent of<BR>its kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतस्न
मतस्न मतस्न, ए, n. du., Ved., N. of<BR>certain internal organs of the body, (perhaps) the<BR>kidneys; (according to Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-<BR>saṃhitā XIX. 85) = हृदयोभय-पार्श्व-स्थे<BR>अस्थिनी, two bones situated on either side of the<BR>heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मति|मतिः
मति मति. See p. 740, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिनार
मतिनार मतिनार, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिल
मतिल मतिल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतीकृ
मतीकृ मती-कृ. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतुथ
मतुथ मतुथ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. मन्), an in-<BR>telligent person (= मेधाविन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतुल
मतुल मतुल, (with Buddhists) a parti-<BR>cular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्क|मत्कः
मत्क 1. मत्क, अस्, m. (for 2. see p. 734,<BR>col. 1), a bug, = मत्कुण below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुण|मत्कुणः
मत्कुण, अस्, m. a bug; a flea; a beardless man;<BR>an elephant without tusks; a small elephant; a<BR>buffalo; a cocoa-nut; (आ), f. pudendum (of a young<BR>girl, = अजात-लोम-भग); N. of a river; (अम्),<BR>n. armour for the thighs or legs, greaves (= जङ्घा-<BR>त्राण; cf. मङ्क्षण).<BR>—मत्कुणारि (˚ण-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. ‘bug-enemy,’ hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुणिका
मत्कुणिका or मत्कुलिका, f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्त|मत्तः
मत्त मत्त, मत्त-काल, मत्त-गामिनी, मत्-<BR>त-दन्तिन्, &c. See p. 734, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्य|मत्यं
मत्य 1. मत्य, अम्, n. (for 2. see p. 741), a<BR>harrow, roller; a club (perhaps with teeth, Ved.); har-<BR>rowing, rolling, making even or level; [cf. मदि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतीकृ
मती-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to harrow,<BR>roll, make even by rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स|मत्सः
मत्स मत्स, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मद्, to re-<BR>joice), = मत्स्य, a fish (‘the gay one’); the king of<BR>the Matsyas, (also read मत्स, q. v.); (ई), f. =<BR>मत्स्या, p. 733, col. 1.<BR>—मत्स-गण्ट, अस्, m. a<BR>kind of fish-sauce (= व्यञ्जन-विशेष; perhaps<BR>for मत्स-घण्ट, cf. मत्स्य-घण्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सर|मत्सरः
मत्सर, अस्, आ, अम् (according to Uṇādi-s. III.<BR>73. fr. rt. 2. मद्; according to others fr. मत् +<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-a" target="_blank">Page0733-a+ 81</a>]<BR>सृ), exhilarating, intoxicating (Ved.; according to<BR>Sāy. = तृप्ति-कर, तृप्ति-हेतु, satisfying); envious,<BR>grudging, jealous, hostile; selfish, self-interested; in-<BR>satiate, greedy, covetous; niggardly; wicked; (अस्),<BR>m. the exhilarater, i. e. Soma; envy, jealousy, en-<BR>mity, hostility; greediness after, selfish eagerness for<BR>or addiction to (with loc.); anger, passion; (अस्, आ),<BR>m. f. a gnat, musquito (usually fem.).<BR>—मत्सर-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. = मत्सर, exhilarating, in-<BR>toxicating, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda IX. 97,<BR>32 = मदकर-रस-युक्त, having intoxicating<BR>juice.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरिन्
मत्सरिन्, ई, इणी, इ, = मत्सर, exhilarating, in-<BR>toxicating (Ved., Sāy. = मदयितृ); envious, jealous,<BR>grudging; greedy after, selfishly eager for or addicted<BR>to (with loc.); wicked, depraved, bad.<BR>—मत्सरिन्-<BR>तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very exhilarating, very in-<BR>toxicating (Sāy. = अतिशयेन मदयितृ or मद-<BR>कारिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्य|मत्स्यः
मत्स्य, अस्, m. a fish (‘the gay one’); a parti-<BR>cular species of fish (probably the Sapharī); (in<BR>astronomy) the figure of a fish (= तिमि, q. v.); a<BR>king of the Matsyas (also called Matsa; cf. Mahā-bh.<BR>Virāṭa-p. 16, 18, 145, Ādi-p. 2393, 2396, where<BR>the name is applied to Virāṭa as having been found<BR>by fishermen, along with his sister Matsyā or Satya-<BR>vatī, in the body of the Apsaras Adrikā, metamorphosed<BR>into a fish); N. of a pupil of Deva-mitra Śākalya,<BR>(also read वात्स्य); a particular luminous appear-<BR>ance; (औ), m. du. the twelfth sign of the zodiac<BR>or Pisces (figured by two fish); (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people and country (mentioned in Manu II. 19. as<BR>forming part of the district called Brahmarṣi), the<BR>country of Virāṭa; (स्या or सी), f., N. of the sister<BR>of king Virāṭa; [cf. Hib. meas, ‘a fish;’ measach,<BR>‘fishy.’]<BR>—मत्स्य-करण्डिका, f. a fish-basket, any<BR>hamper or receptacle for fish.<BR>—मत्स्य-कूर्माद्य्-<BR>अवतारिन् (˚म-आद्˚), ई, m. ‘descending (and be-<BR>coming incarnate) as a fish, tortoise, &c.,’ an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>—मत्स्य-गन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>the smell of fish; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a race; (आ), f.<BR>epithet of Satya-vatī (mother of Vyāsa, also called<BR>Mīna-gandhā; see मत्स्य above); a species of<BR>aquatic plant (= लाङ्गली, जल-पिप्पली).<BR>—मत्स्य-<BR>घण्ट, अस्, m. a kind of fish-sauce or dish of fish;<BR>[cf. मत्स-गण्ट.]<BR>—मत्स्य-घात, अस्, m. the<BR>killing of fish, i. e. the occupation of a fisherman.<BR>—मत्स्य-घातिन्, ई, m. ‘fish-killer,’ a fisherman.<BR>—मत्स्य-जाल, अम्, n. a fishing net.<BR>—मत्स्य-<BR>जीवत्, अन्, or मत्स्य-जीविन्, ई, m. ‘living by fish,<BR>i. e. living by catching fish,’ a fisherman; [cf. मत्स्यो-<BR>पजीविन्.]<BR>—मत्स्य-देश, अस्, m. ‘the country<BR>Matsya,’ N. of a country mentioned in the Ratna-<BR>koṣa; [cf. मत्स्य.]<BR>—मत्स्य-द्वादशी or मत्स्य-<BR>द्वादशिका, f., N. of the twelfth day in one of the<BR>halves of the month Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>—मत्स्य-द्वीप,<BR>अस्, m. ‘fish-island,’ N. of a Dvīpa.<BR>—मत्स्य-धानी,<BR>f. ‘fish-holder,’ a fish-basket, a small basket used by<BR>fishermen, (also sometimes, but less accurately, applied<BR>to a kind of snare of reeds or grass which is left in<BR>the water and entangles the fish that swim with the<BR>current.)<BR>—मत्स्य-ध्वज, अस्, m. a fish-shaped<BR>standard; N. of a mountain in Kāma-rūpa.<BR>—मत्स्य-<BR>नाथ, अस्, m. ‘fish-lord,’ N. of a man (= मत्स्येन्-<BR>द्र, q. v.).<BR>—मत्स्य-नारी, f. ‘fish-woman, half<BR>fish, half woman,’ epithet of Satya-vatī.<BR>—मत्स्य-<BR>नाशक or मत्स्य-नाशन, अस्, m. ‘fish-destroyer,’<BR>a sea-eagle, ospray.<BR>—मत्स्य-पित्ता, f. ‘fish-bile,’ a<BR>species of medicinal plant (= कटु-रोहिणी; cf.<BR>मत्स्य-विन्ना).<BR>—मत्स्य-पुराण, अम्, n. ‘fish-<BR>Purāṇa,’ N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas, so<BR>called as communicated by Viṣṇu in the form of a<BR>fish to the seventh Manu, sometimes called Vaivas-<BR>vata; [cf. मत्स्यावतार.]<BR>—मत्स्य-प्रादुर्भाव,<BR>अस्, m. ‘fish-manifestation,’ N. of the thirty-sixth<BR>chapter of the Narasiṃha-Purāṇa; [cf. मत्स्याव-<BR>तार.]<BR>—मत्स्य-बन्ध, अस्, m. a fisherman.<BR>—मत्स्य-बन्धन, अम्, n. a fish-hook, angle;<BR>(ई), f. a fish-basket.<BR>—मत्स्य-बन्धिन्, ई, m. ‘fish-<BR>catching,’ an angler, fisherman; (इनी), f. a fish-<BR>basket (various reading for मत्स्य-बन्धनी).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-b" target="_blank">Page0733-b+ 79</a>]<BR>—मत्स्य-माधव, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—मत्स्य-रङ्क or मत्स्य-रङ्ग or मत्स्य-<BR>रङ्गक, अस्, m. a halcyon, king-fisher.<BR>—मत्स्य-<BR>राज, अस्, m. ‘fish-king,’ the fish Cyprinus Rohita;<BR>the king of the Matsyas.<BR>—मत्स्य-विद्, त्, त्, त्, know-<BR>ing fish, an ichthyologist.<BR>—मत्स्य-विन्ना, f. a plant<BR>(= कटुका).<BR>—मत्स्य-वेधन, अम्, ई, n. f. ‘fish-<BR>piercing,’ a fish-hook, angle; (ई), f. a cormorant.<BR>—मत्स्य-सगन्धिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a fish<BR>smell.<BR>—मत्स्य-सङ्घात, अस्, m. a multitude of<BR>fish, a shoal of young fry or small fish.<BR>—मत्स्य-सन्-<BR>तानिक, अस्, m. a particular dish of fish (eaten with<BR>condiments and oil).<BR>—मत्स्य-सूक्त, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a work mentioned in Kṛṣṇānanda's Tantra-sāra.<BR>—मत्स्य-हन्, आ, m., Ved. ‘fish-killer,’ a fisher-<BR>man.<BR>—मत्स्याक्षक (˚य-अक्˚), अस्, m. or मत्स्-<BR>याक्षका or मत्स्याक्षी, f. ‘fish-eyed (?),’ N. of a<BR>species of Soma plant; (according to some मत्स्-<BR>याक्षी and मत्स्याक्षिका = गण्ड-दूर्वा, accord-<BR>ing to others मत्स्याक्षी = हिलमोचिका, Hingcha<BR>Repens; मत्स्याक्षी is sometimes read मत्स्याङ्गी.)<BR>—मत्स्याद् (˚य-अद्), त्, त्, त्, or मत्स्याद (˚य-<BR>आद), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘fish-eating,’ feeding on fish.<BR>—मत्स्यादनी, f. = जल-पिप्पली, a particular plant.<BR>—मत्स्यावतार (˚य-अव्˚), अस्, m. ‘fish-descent,’<BR>N. of the first of the ten incarnations or manifesta-<BR>tions of Viṣṇu (during the reign of the seventh<BR>Manu, the whole earth, which had become corrupt,<BR>was destroyed by a flood, and all living beings<BR>perished, except the pious Manu himself, and the<BR>seven Ṛṣis, who were preserved by the help of<BR>Viṣṇu in the form of a fish, after having been di-<BR>rected by him to enter a large ship with the seeds<BR>of all existing things; while the ship floated, fastened<BR>to the fish, Manu entered into conversation with<BR>him, and his questions, with the replies of Viṣṇu,<BR>form the substance of the Matsya-Purāṇa, q. v.; in<BR>the Vana-parvan of the Mahā-bhārata, 1. 12746-<BR>12804, the fish is represented as an incarnation of<BR>Brahmā); N. of a division of the Khaṇḍa-praśasti,<BR>ascribed to Hanumat, treating of the ten manifesta-<BR>tions of Viṣṇu.<BR>—मत्स्यावतार-कथन, अम्, n.<BR>‘the tale or narration of the fish-descent,’ N. of the<BR>thirty-seventh chapter of the Uttara-khaṇḍa of the<BR>Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—मत्स्याशन (˚य-अश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘feeding on fishes,’ a halcyon, king-fisher.<BR>—मत्स्या-<BR>सुर (˚य-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘fish-Asura,’ N. of an Asura.<BR>—मत्स्यासुर-शैल-वध, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>ninety-second chapter of the Krīḍā-khaṇḍa or second<BR>part of the Gaṇeśa-Purāṇa.<BR>—मत्स्येन्द्र (˚य-इन्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a teacher of the Haṭha-vidyā.<BR>—मत्स्-<BR>येश्वर-तीर्थ (˚य-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—मत्स्योदरिन् (˚य-उद्˚), ई, m., N. of Matsya or<BR>Virāṭa as the brother of Matsyodarī.<BR>—मत्स्योदरी<BR>(˚य-उद्˚), f. a N. of Matsyā or Satya-vatī, who with<BR>her brother Matsya was found in the body of the<BR>Apsaras Adrikā metamorphosed into a fish, (also read<BR>मत्सोदरी); N. of a sacred bathing-place in Benares.<BR>—मत्स्योदरीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to the belly<BR>of a fish; (अस्), m. ‘son of Satya-vatī or Matsyodarī,’<BR>an epithet of Vyāsa.<BR>—मत्स्योपजीविन् (˚य-उप्˚), ई,<BR>m. ‘living by fish,’ a fisherman; [cf. मत्स्य-जीवत्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यक
मत्स्यक, अस्, m. a little fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सर|मत्सरः
मत्सर मत्सर. See p. 732, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्य|मत्स्यः
मत्स्य मत्स्य. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यण्डिका|मत्स्यंडिका
मत्स्यण्डिका मत्स्यण्डिका or मत्स्यण्डी, f.<BR>(corrupted fr. मधु-स्यन्दी?), granulated sugar,<BR>coarse or unrefined sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्
मथ् 1. मथ् (or मन्थ्, q. v.), cl. 1. 9. P.<BR>(ep. also A.) मथति (Ved. मथायति),<BR>मन्थति, मथ्नाति (-ते), ममन्थ or less usually<BR>ममाथ (2nd sing. ममन्थिथ, 3rd du. म-<BR>मन्थतुस् or less usually ममथतुस्, 3rd pl.<BR>ममन्थुस् or ममथुस्, Ved. मेथुस्, मेथिरे),<BR>मन्थिष्यति or मथिष्यति, अमन्थीत् (Ved.<BR>मथीत्), Inf. मन्थितुम् or मथितुम्, to rub<BR>together (Ved.); to stir, stir up, excite (in Ved.<BR>with अग्निम्, to excite fire by rubbing two pieces of<BR>wood together); to stir or whirl round, shake to-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">Page0733-c+ 79</a>]<BR>gether, shake, agitate; to churn, produce by churn-<BR>ing (sometimes with two acc., e. g. सुधां क्षीर-<BR>निधिम् मथ्नाति, he churns nectar out of the<BR>ocean of milk); to agitate, confuse; to crush, grind,<BR>pinch; to grind down, oppress, afflict, distress, trouble;<BR>to destroy, kill, annihilate, hurt; to tear off, dislocate,<BR>disjoint: Pass. मथ्यते (ep. also -ति), to be stirred<BR>up or churned, &c.: Caus. मन्थयति or less<BR>usually माथयति, -यितुम्, to cause to be stirred up<BR>or churned, &c.: Deside. मिमन्थिषति, मिमथि-<BR>षति: Intens. मामथ्यते, मामन्त्ति, मामन्-<BR>थीति, Impf. 3rd sing. अमामन्; [cf. Gr. μάτος,<BR>ματεύω, μανθάνω, μόθα-ς, μόθων, Προ-μηθ-εύ-ς =<BR>प्र-मन्थ-स्, q. v.; Lat. ment-ula; Slav. met-<BR>eźÇ, ‘tumult;’ Lith. met-uri-s, ment-ure, ‘a churn-<BR>ing-stick;’ Hib. muidhe, meadar, ‘a churn, milk-<BR>pail.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्
2. मथ्. See मथिन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ
मथ, अस्, m. = माथ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथक
मथक, अस्, m., N. of a man; (आस्), m. pl. his<BR>descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन्
मथन् (मथ्ना,) inst. c. sing.), a piece of wood<BR>for producing fire by attrition; friction, rubbing<BR>(Ved., Sāy. मथ्ना = प्रमाथनेन, लोडनेन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन|मथनं|मथनः
मथन, अस्, ई, अम्, rubbing; stirring round;<BR>churning; hurting, injuring, destroying; a destroyer<BR>[cf. पुर-म्˚, मधु-म्˚]; (अस्), m. the tree<BR>Premna Spinosa (the wood of which is used to<BR>produce fire by attrition); (अम्), n. the act of rub-<BR>bing, friction; the act of stirring round, churning<BR>[cf. अमृत-म्˚, मन्थन]; the act of hurting,<BR>injury, harsh treatment, destruction; N. of a weapon.<BR>—मथनाचल (˚न-अच्˚), अस्, m. the mountain<BR>(Mandara, q. v.) used as a churning-stick by the gods<BR>and Dānavas in churning the ocean of milk; [cf.<BR>मन्थ-शैल.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथि|मथिः
मथि, इस्, इस्, इ (at the end of a comp.), Ved.<BR>rubbing, churning, destroying, killing [cf. उरा-म्˚];<BR>(इस्), m. a churning-stick, any staff for stirring or<BR>churning; [cf. मथिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथित|मथितं
मथित, अस्, आ, अम्, stirred round, shaken about,<BR>churned, agitated; crushed, ground, pinched, nipped;<BR>oppressed, afflicted, distressed, anxious; destroyed,<BR>killed; dislocated, disjointed; (अस्), m., N. of a de-<BR>scendant of Yama (the reputed author of the hymn<BR>Ṛg-veda X. 19); (अम्), n. buttermilk without<BR>water, pure buttermilk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथितृ
मथितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who stirs or churns,<BR>one who destroys or annihilates, a destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथित्वा
मथित्वा or मन्थित्वा, ind. having stirred, hav-<BR>ing churned, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथिन्
मथिन्, मन्थास् (nom. voc. sing. मन्थास् fr. a<BR>base मन्थस्, the other strong cases fr. a base<BR>मन्थन्, acc. pl. and other weak cases fr. a base<BR>मथ्, middle cases fr. मथिन्, see Gram. 162;<BR>hence nom. pl. मन्थानस्, acc. pl. मथस्, inst.<BR>sing. du. pl. मथा, मथिभ्याम्, मथिभिस्), a<BR>churning-stick, churn-staff, any stick for stirring or<BR>churning; the penis; a thunderbolt; wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथीन
मथीन (said to be fr. मथिन् above), Nom. P.<BR>मथीनति, &c. (meaning doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्न
मथ्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. shaken about, agitated,<BR>whirled, (but मथ्ना in Ṛg-veda I. 181, 5, is<BR>regarded by Sāy. as inst. sing. of मथन् above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्नत्
मथ्नत्, अन्, अती, अत्, stirring round, shaking<BR>about, churning, agitating; oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्य
मथ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be rubbed, to be churned,<BR>to be extracted or produced by churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्यमान
मथ्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being stirred or churned,<BR>being rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्र
मथ्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. tearing or whirling<BR>along (Sāy. = मथन-शिल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ|मंथ|मंथः|मन्थः
मन्थ, मन्थ्य, &c. See under rt. मन्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथव्य
मथव्य मथव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., in Atharva-<BR>veda II. 35, 2, for मधव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथा
मथा मथा, ind., Ved. a Nidhana formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथात
मथात मथात, अम्, n., N. of a Sāman;<BR>[cf. ममाथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुर
मथुर मथुर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">Page0734-a+ 80</a>]<BR>1. मथ्), N. of a man; (आ), f., N. of an ancient town<BR>held in great honour as sacred to Kṛṣṇa (situated<BR>in the province of Agra on the right bank of the<BR>river Yamunā or Jumnā, not far from the hill Go-<BR>vardhana in Vṛndā-vana, the scene of the amours<BR>and exploits of Kṛṣṇa; it is described in Viṣṇu-<BR>Purāṇa XII. 1. as having been founded by Śatru-<BR>ghna; it was the birthplace of the god Kṛṣṇa, and<BR>under the modern name of Muttra is to this day<BR>the resort of crowds of devotees; according to Kul-<BR>lūka on Manu II. 19, the town forms part of a<BR>district, called Brahmarṣi, belonging to Śūrasena);<BR>N. of two other towns; [cf. माथुर, मधुरा.]<BR>—मथुरा-काण्ड, अम्, n., N. of a section of the<BR>Mantra-rahasya-prakāśikā.<BR>—मथुरा-नाथ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘lord of Mathurā,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa; N. of<BR>several men; (ई), f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>Tattva-cintāmaṇi by Mathurā-nātha.<BR>—मथुरा-<BR>निवेश, अस्, m., N. of the sixty-third chapter of the<BR>Uttara-kāṇḍa of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—मथुरा-मा-<BR>हात्म्य, अम्, n., N. of a part of the Vārāha-Purāṇa<BR>(containing an account of the city and temples of<BR>Mathurā).<BR>—मथुरा-सेतु, उस्, m. ‘the bridge of<BR>Mathurā,’ N. of a work.<BR>—मथुरेश (˚रा-ईश),<BR>अस्, m. ‘lord of Mathurā,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>N. of the author of the Śabda-ratnāvalī, a dictionary<BR>of synonyms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0733-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथूरा
मथूरा, f. = मथुरा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
मद् 1. मद् [cf. मत्, p. 732, col. 3], a form<BR>derived fr. मत्, abl. of 3. म, and serving for the<BR>base of the first personal pronoun in the singular<BR>number (especially at the beginning of compounds<BR>as follow).<BR>—मच्-चित्त, अस्, आ, अम्, having the mind<BR>(fixed) on me, thinking of me.<BR>—मच्-छरीर,<BR>अम्, n. (मद् + श्˚), my body.<BR>—मत्-कृत, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, made by me; uttered by me; (ए), ind. for the<BR>sake of me, on my account.<BR>—मत्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>better or more than mine.<BR>—मत्-तस्, ind. from me.<BR>—मत्-पर, अस्, आ, अम्, devoted to me.<BR>—मत्-<BR>पुत्र, अस्, m. the son of me, my son.<BR>—मत्-प्र-<BR>सूत, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from me.<BR>—मत्-सकाशे,<BR>ind. in my presence.<BR>—मत्-सखि, आ, m. my com-<BR>panion, my friend.<BR>—मत्-सन्देश, अस्, m. news of<BR>me, tidings of me.<BR>—मत्-समक्षम्, ind. in the<BR>presence of me, in my sight.<BR>—मत्-सादृश्य, अम्,<BR>n. the likeness or resemblance of me.<BR>—मद्-अर्थ,<BR>अस्, m. my purpose; (अम्), ind. for the sake of me.<BR>—मद्-देह, अम्, n. my body.<BR>—मद्-बन्धन-<BR>समुद्भव, अस्, आ, अम्, caused by the binding of<BR>me, i. e. by my bondage.<BR>—मद्-भक्त, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, devoted to me.<BR>—मद्-भू, cl. 1. P. मद्-<BR>भवति, &c., to become 1.<BR>—मद्रिक्, ind. (fr.<BR>मद्र्यञ्च्), Ved. to me, towards me (Sāy. = मद्-<BR>अभिमुखम्).<BR>—मद्र्यञ्च्, अङ्, द्रीची, अक् (fr. 1.<BR>मद् with अद्रि substituted for अद् and rt. अञ्च्),<BR>Ved. directed towards me, extending to me; (अक्),<BR>ind. towards me.<BR>—मद्र्यद्रिक्, ind., Ved. = म-<BR>द्रिक् (with reduplication of affix अद्रि; cf. तद्र्यञ्च्).<BR>—मद्-वचन, अम्, n. my word, my order;<BR>मद्-वचनात्, in my name, from me.<BR>—१. मद्-<BR>वत्, ind. like me; (for 2. मद्वत् see p. 736,<BR>col. 1.)<BR>—मद्-वर्गीण or मद्-वर्गीय or मद्-<BR>वर्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to my class or to my<BR>party, connected with or related to me.<BR>—मद्-<BR>विध, अस्, आ, अम्, like me, equal to me, of my<BR>sort or kind.<BR>—मद्-वियोग, अस्, m. separation from<BR>me.<BR>—मद्-विहीन, अस्, आ, अम्, separated from me.<BR>—मन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘consisting of me,’ full<BR>of me, like me, attached to me; come forth from<BR>me, proceeding from me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्क|मत्कः
2. मत्क, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 732, col. 3),<BR>mine, my.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदीय|मदीयं
मदीय, अस्, आ, अम्, mine, my own, belonging<BR>to me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्य|मद्यं
1. मद्य, Nom. P. मद्यति, &c., see Pāṇ. VII.<BR>2, 98. (For 2. मद्य see p. 735, col. 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
मद् 2. मद् [cf. rts. मन्द्, मुद्], cl. 4.<BR>P. (rarely A. in Ved.) माद्यति (-ते), म-<BR>माद, अमादीत्, मदितुम् (Vedic forms are मदति,<BR>मन्दति, -ते [see rt. मन्द्], मदेमहि, मत्सि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-b" target="_blank">Page0734-b+ 81</a>]<BR>ममत्सि, मत्स्व, ममद्धि, ममत्तु by Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 1, 192, ममत्तन, ममदस्, ममदन्,<BR>मत्सत्, मत्सति, अमत्त, अमत्सुस्, अमत्सत,<BR>अमन्दत, अमन्दीत्, see rt. मन्द्), to become<BR>drunk or inebriated, (perhaps originally madidum<BR>esse, to be moist); to be mad; to be drunk with joy,<BR>&c.; to revel, revel in, delight in (with inst., gen.,<BR>loc., and rarely acc.); to be glad, rejoice, be happy; to<BR>enjoy heavenly bliss; to be cheerful or gay; (Ved.)<BR>to gladden, delight, amuse, exhilarate, intoxicate,<BR>inspire, animate: Caus. मादयति, मदयति, -यि-<BR>तुम् (Ved. Inf. मादयध्यै), Aor. अमीमदत्,<BR>अममदत्, to intoxicate, inebriate, delight, exhi-<BR>larate, gladden, satisfy; A. (-ते), to be glad, rejoice,<BR>be pleased, be happy, delight in; to enjoy heavenly<BR>bliss: Desid. मिमदिषति: Intens. मामद्यते,<BR>मामत्ति; [cf. Gr. μαδ-αρό-ς, μαδ-ά-ω, μαδός,<BR>μαδίζω, μᾱνός; Lat. măd-e-o, măd-i-du-s, măd-<BR>e-sc-o, măde-facio, mā-na-re from mad-na-re;<BR>probably Goth. mat-s, mat-jan; Angl. Sax. mœte,<BR>mœt-an; Eng. mad; Hib. misge, ‘drunkenness;’<BR>Pers. مست mas-t from med-t.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्त|मत्तः
मत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicated, inebriated, drunk,<BR>(often used metaphorically, as ‘drunk with love, with<BR>joy, with pride, passion, &c.’); mad, insane, furious;<BR>in rut, ruttish (said of animals of all kinds, but espe-<BR>cially of an elephant); amorous, lustful, wanton;<BR>delighted, overjoyed, excited; proud, arrogant; (अस्),<BR>m. a drunkard; a madman; a furious elephant, an<BR>elephant in rut; a buffalo; the Indian cuckoo; a thorn-<BR>apple; N. of a Rākṣasa; (आ), f. any intoxicating<BR>drink, spirituous or vinous liquor; a particular metre,<BR>four times ¯¯¯¯, ˘˘˘˘¯¯.<BR>—मत्त-काल, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of Lāṭa.<BR>—मत्त-काशिनी, f. ‘ap-<BR>pearing intoxicated,’ a bewitching or wanton woman;<BR>(sometimes written मत्त-कासिनी and मत्त-का-<BR>षिणी.)<BR>—मत्त-क्रीडा, f. a kind of metre.<BR>—मत्त-<BR>गामिनी, f. ‘having the gait of an elephant in rut,’<BR>a woman with a rolling walk, a bewitching or wanton<BR>woman.<BR>—मत्त-दन्तिन्, ई, m. a furious elephant<BR>or one in rut.<BR>—मत्त-नाग, अस्, m. an elephant in<BR>rut; N. of an author.<BR>—मत्त-मयूर, अस्, m. an<BR>amorous peacock or one drunk with passion, a wild<BR>or excited peacock; (अम्), n. a kind of metre, four<BR>times ¯¯¯¯, ˘˘˘˘¯¯.<BR>—मत्तमयूरक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, behaving like an amorous peacock; (आस्),<BR>m. pl. epithet of a particular warrior-tribe.<BR>—मत्त-<BR>मातङ्ग-लीलाकर, a kind of metre.<BR>—मत्त-वा-<BR>रण, अस्, m. an elephant in rut, a furious elephant;<BR>(अस्, अम्), m. n. a fence against drunkards, &c., a<BR>fence or hedge round the house of a rich man; a<BR>turret, a little room on the top of a large building or<BR>palace; a veranda; a pavilion; = निर्-यूह, q. v.;<BR>(अम्), n. pounded betel-nuts.<BR>—मत्तवारण-वि-<BR>क्रम, अस्, m. the strength or might of a furious<BR>elephant.<BR>—मत्त-विलासिनी, f. a particular metre,<BR>four times ¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯.<BR>—मत्ताक्रीडा (˚त-आक्˚), f. a particular metre, four<BR>times ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯, ˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘¯.<BR>—मत्तालम्ब (˚त-आल्˚), अस्, m. a fence or hedge<BR>round the house of a rich man; [cf. मत्त-वारण.]<BR>—मत्तेभ-कुम्भ-परिणाहिन् (˚त-इभ्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, round as the frontal globes of an elephant in rut.<BR>—मत्तेभ-गमना (˚त-इभ्˚), f. a woman hav-<BR>ing the gait of an elephant in rut, a woman with a<BR>lounging or rolling walk; [cf. मत्त-गामिनी]<BR>—मत्तेभ-विक्रीडित, अम्, n., N. of a particular<BR>metre, four times ˘˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯¯¯˘<BR>¯¯˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तक
मत्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, somewhat drunk or inebri-<BR>ated, somewhat arrogant or proud; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>a Brāhman in Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VI. 339.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकीश|मत्तकीशः
मत्तकीश, अस्, m. (? fr. मत्तकी + ईश), an ele-<BR>phant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद|मदः
मद, अस्, m. intoxication, drunkenness, inebriety;<BR>madness, insanity, frenzy; ardent passion, lust, rut-<BR>tishness, rut (especially of an elephant), lascivious-<BR>ness, wantonness, sensual enjoyment; love, desire,<BR>passion, ardour, inspiration; delight, rapture, joy;<BR>pride, arrogance, presumption, conceit, petulance;<BR>any exhilarating or intoxicating drink, spirituous<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-c" target="_blank">Page0734-c+ 81</a>]<BR>liquor, wine; Soma; honey; the juice or ichor that<BR>exudes from an elephant's temples when in rut;<BR>semen virile; musk [cf. मृग-मद]; any beautiful<BR>object; a river; Intoxication or Insanity personified<BR>(a monster created by Cayavana, see Mahā-bh. Vana-<BR>p. 10389, Anuśāsana-p. 7317, 7322); N. of a son<BR>of Brahmā; of a Dānava; of a servant of Śiva;<BR>गृत्समदस्य मदः, N. of a Sāman; (ई), f.<BR>any drinking vessel, cup, &c. (= चषक-वस्तु);<BR>any agricultural implement, a plough, &c. (= कृ-<BR>षक-वस्तु).<BR>—मद-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, causing<BR>intoxication, making drunk, intoxicating.<BR>—मद-<BR>करिन्, ई, m. an elephant in rut.<BR>—मद-कल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, uttering low sounds of love; sounding softly,<BR>speaking indistinctly or like a drunkard, indistinct,<BR>inarticulate; ruttish, under the influence of rut (as<BR>an elephant); furious, mad; (अस्), m. an elephant.<BR>—मद-कारण, अम्, n. a cause of pride or arro-<BR>gance.<BR>—मद-कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or मद-कृत्, त्,<BR>त्, त्, making drunk, intoxicating<BR>—मद-कोहल,<BR>अस्, m. a bull set at liberty (at a festival and allowed<BR>to range about at will).<BR>—मद-गन्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>species of plant, = सप्त-च्छदा; (आ), f. an intoxi-<BR>cating beverage; hemp, Linum Usitatissimum (=<BR>अतसी).<BR>—मद-गमन, अस्, m. ‘having an excited<BR>or reeling gait,’ a buffalo.<BR>—मद-गुरु-पक्ष,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having wings heavy with honey (as<BR>bees).<BR>—मद-घ्नी, f. ‘destroying intoxication,’ a<BR>species of leguminous plant (= पूतिका).<BR>—मद-<BR>च्युत्, त्, त्, त्, distilling juice or ichor (as an elephant<BR>in rut), lustful, wanton, drunk; joy-bestowing, in-<BR>spiriting, gladdening, exhilarated by the Soma juice;<BR>destroying or overcoming pride, (according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda 1. 126, 4, 1. 51, 2 = शत्रूणां गर्-<BR>वस्य च्यावयितृ or मद-स्राविन्); (त्), m. an<BR>epithet of Indra; (ता), m. du., Ved. an epithet of the<BR>Aśvins.<BR>—मद-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. staggering<BR>or reeling with intoxication (Sāy. = मदार्थम्<BR>प्रेरित).<BR>—मद-जल, अम्, n. the juice of rut,<BR>the ichor of a ruttish elephant.<BR>—मद-ज्वर, अस्,<BR>m. the fever of passion; fever of pride or arrogance.<BR>—मद-द्विप, अस्, m. an elephant in rut.<BR>—मद-<BR>धार, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मद-पति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. lord of the Soma juice (epithet of Indra and<BR>Viṣṇu, Ṛg-veda VI. 69, 3).<BR>—मद-प्रयोग,<BR>अस्, m. the issue of the fluid from the temples of an<BR>elephant in rut.<BR>—मद-प्रसेक, अस्, m. or मद-<BR>प्रस्रवण, अम्, n. the oozing out or exudation of<BR>the juice from an elephant's temples (when in rut).<BR>—मद-भञ्जिन्, ई, इनी, इ, removing or dispelling<BR>(the effects of) intoxication; (इनी), f. the plant Aspa-<BR>ragus Racemosus.<BR>—मद-मत्ता, f. a particular<BR>metre.<BR>—मद-मुच्, क्, क्, क्, emitting or distilling<BR>juice, being in rut (as an elephant).<BR>—मद-मोहित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, infatuated by drunkenness or intoxication<BR>(Manu XI. 98), infatuated by pride.<BR>—मद-रक्त,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, affected with love, agitated by passion,<BR>amorous.<BR>—मद-राग, अस्, m. ‘affected by passion<BR>or by intoxication,’ the god of love; a drunken man;<BR>a cock.<BR>—मद-रुद्र-दत्त, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>author.<BR>—मद-लेखा, f. a line formed by the juice<BR>(exuding from an elephant's temples); a kind of<BR>metre, four times ¯¯¯˘˘¯¯; N. of a woman.<BR>—मद-वारि, n. the juice of rut, the ichor of a<BR>ruttish elephant.<BR>—मद-विक्षिप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, dis-<BR>tracted by passion, agitated by lust, in rut (as an<BR>elephant).<BR>—मद-विह्वल, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied<BR>with liquor, mad with lust or pride.<BR>—मद-वीर्य,<BR>अम्, n. the strength of passion; the heroism of love.<BR>—मद-वृद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. invigorated by<BR>Soma, exhilarated by the Soma juice.<BR>—मद-वृद्-<BR>धि, इस्, f. invigoration (caused) by Soma.<BR>—मद-<BR>वृन्द, अस्, m. ‘having a quantity of juice or ichor,’<BR>an elephant.<BR>—मद-शाक, अस्, m. Basella Cordi-<BR>folia.<BR>—मद-शौण्डक, अम्, n. nutmeg; (also<BR>written मद-सौण्डक.)<BR>—मद-सार, अस्, m.<BR>the cotton shrub.<BR>—मद-स्थल or मद-स्थान,<BR>अम्, n. ‘place of intoxication,’ a drinking-house,<BR>ale-house, dram-shop, tavern.<BR>—मद-स्राविन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, distilling juice as an elephant in rut.<BR>—मद-<BR>हस्तिनी, f. a species of Karañja (= महा-करञ्ज).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-a" target="_blank">Page0735-a+ 81</a>]<BR>—मद-हेतु, उस्, m. ‘cause of intoxication,’ the<BR>plant Grislea Tomentosa.<BR>—मदाकुल (˚द-आक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, agitated by passion, full of lust, furious<BR>with rut.<BR>—मदाघ (˚द-अघ), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man; (आस्), m. pl. his descendants.<BR>—मदाढ्य<BR>(˚द-आढ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, rich in wine or liquor, filled<BR>with wine, intoxicated, drunk; (अस्), m. the palmyra<BR>tree or palm which yields an intoxicating liquor; (आ),<BR>f. a red-flowering Barleria.<BR>—मदातङ्क (˚द-आत्˚),<BR>अस्, m. = मदात्यय below.<BR>—मदात्मानन्द<BR>(˚द-आत्म-आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—म-<BR>दात्यय (˚द-अत्˚), अस्, m. ‘passing off of wine,’<BR>disorder resulting from intoxication (as head-ache,<BR>crop-sickness, &c.); [cf. पानात्यय.]<BR>—मदान्ध<BR>(˚द-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, blind through drunkenness,<BR>blinded by intoxication, dead drunk, intoxicated;<BR>blinded by passion or pride, infatuated; dissolute,<BR>arrogant; (आ), f. a particular metre, four times<BR>¯ ¯ ¯ ˘ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ¯.<BR>—मदापनयन (˚द-अप्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the removal of intoxication.<BR>—मदाम्नात<BR>(˚द-आम्˚), अस्, m. a kettle-drum carried on an ele-<BR>phant.<BR>—मदाम्बर (˚द-अम्˚), अस्, m. the ele-<BR>phant of Indra; an elephant in rut.<BR>—मदालस<BR>(˚द-अल्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, lazy from drunkenness, languid<BR>with passion, indolent from pride, slothful; (आ), f.,<BR>N. of the daughter of the Gandharva Viśvā-vasu<BR>(carried off by the Daitya Pātāla-ketu and subse-<BR>quently the wife of Kuvalayāśva); N. of a work.<BR>—मदालापिन् (˚द-आल्˚), ई, m. ‘uttering sounds of<BR>love or of joy, singing delightfully,’ the Indian cuckoo<BR>or koil.<BR>—मदा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. intoxicated,<BR>drunk.<BR>—मदावस्था (˚द-अव्˚), f. a state of passion,<BR>wantonness, lustfulness, ruttishness, rut.<BR>—मदाह्व<BR>(˚द-आह्˚), अस्, m. musk.<BR>—मदे-रघु, उस्, उस्, उ<BR>(fr. the loc. मदे), Ved. eager with enthusiasm,<BR>enthusiastic, (according to Sāy. मदकरे धने<BR>गन्ता.)<BR>—मदोत्कट (˚द-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ex-<BR>cited by drink, intoxicated; excited by passion or<BR>lust, furious with passion; furious, mad, excited by<BR>pride, arrogant, haughty; under the influence of rut,<BR>ruttish (especially an elephant); (अस्), m. an elephant<BR>in rut; a dove; N. of a lion; (आ), f. an intoxicating<BR>beverage; N. of the goddess Dākṣāyaṇī as wor-<BR>shipped in Caitraratha.<BR>—मदोदग्र (˚द-उद्˚),<BR>or मदोद्धत (˚द-उद्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, excited with<BR>drink, intoxicated, excited with passion, furious;<BR>puffed up with pride, arrogant, haughty.<BR>—मदोन्-<BR>मत्त (˚द-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicated with passion<BR>or pride, furious.<BR>—मदोर्जित (˚द-ऊर्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, swollen with pride, haughty with arrogance.<BR>—मदोल्लापिन् (˚द-उल्˚), ई, m. the Indian cuckoo;<BR>[cf. मदालापिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदन|मदनः
मदन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the Caus.), intoxicating,<BR>maddening, delighting, &c.; (अस्), m. passion, love,<BR>sexual love, lust; N. of Kāma-deva, the god of love;<BR>a kind of embrace; the season of spring; a bee;<BR>bees-wax; N. of several plants, Vanguiera Spinosa<BR>[cf. मदन-कण्टक]; the thorn-apple, Datura<BR>Metel; Phaseolus Radiatus; Acacia Catechu; Alan-<BR>gium Hexapetalum; Mimusops Elengi; N. of several<BR>men [cf. भट्ट-म्˚, मदन-नृप, मदन-<BR>पाल, मदन-राज]; (आ, ई), f. any intoxicating<BR>drink, spirituous liquor; (ई), f. musk; a species of<BR>plant, = अति-मुक्तक; (अम्), n. the act of intoxi-<BR>cating or exhilarating; gladdening; (scil. अस्त्र), N.<BR>of a mythical weapon (‘the intoxicater, maddener’).<BR>—मदन-कण्टक, अस्, m. = मदन, the plant<BR>Vanguiera Spinosa.<BR>—मदन-काकु-रव, अस्, m.<BR>‘uttering low sounds of love,’ a pigeon, dove.<BR>—म-<BR>दन-क्लिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, pained by love.<BR>—म-<BR>दन-गृह, अम्, n. ‘abode of love,’ N. of a parti-<BR>cular Prākṛt metre.<BR>—मदन-गोपाल, अस्, m.<BR>‘herdsman of love,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa; N. of the<BR>preceptor of Vaikuṇṭha-purī, (also written simply<BR>गो-पाल.)<BR>—मदन-चतुर्दशी, f., N. of a festival<BR>in honour of Kāma-deva on the fourteenth day in<BR>the light half of the month Caitra.<BR>—मदन-त्र-<BR>योदशी, f., N. of a festival in honour of Kāma-deva<BR>on the thirteenth day of the light half of the month<BR>Caitra.<BR>—मदन-दंष्ट्रा, f., N. of a princess.<BR>—मदन-दमन, अस्, m. ‘Kāma-deva's subduer,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-b" target="_blank">Page0735-b+ 81</a>]<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मदन-दहन, अस्, m.<BR>‘Kāma-deva's burner or consumer,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva or Rudra; a symbolical expression for the<BR>number eleven.<BR>—मदन-द्वादशी, f. the twelfth<BR>day of the light half of the month Caitra (sacred to<BR>Kāma-deva).<BR>—मदन-नालिका, f. a faithless wife.<BR>—मदन-नृप, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Madana-vinoda glossary.<BR>—मदन-पक्षिन्, ई, m.<BR>‘spring-bird (?),’ a sort of raven.<BR>—मदन-पाठ-<BR>क, अस्, m. ‘announcer of spring,’ the Indian cuckoo.<BR>—मदन-पारिजात or मदन-परिजात, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a compendium of rules on morality and ritual<BR>compiled from older codes by Viśveśvara under the<BR>patronage of king Madana-pāla.<BR>—मदन-पाल,<BR>अस्, m. (sometimes simply मदन), N. of a king<BR>to whom several works are ascribed or under whose<BR>patronage they were composed; [cf. मदन-पारि-<BR>जात, मदन-विनोद, मदन-राज.]<BR>—मद-<BR>न-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—मदन-प्रभ,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Vidyā-dhara.<BR>—मदन-फल, अम्,<BR>n. the fruit of the plant Vanguiera Spinosa.<BR>—म-<BR>दन-बाधा, f. the pain or disquietude of love.<BR>—मदन-भवन, अम्, n. ‘abode of love or<BR>matrimony,’ a particular station or state of the<BR>heavenly bodies (in astrology); = मदनालय, q. v.<BR>—मदन-मञ्चुका, f., N. of a daughter of Ma-<BR>dana-vega and Kaliṅga-senā (the sixth Lambaka in<BR>the Kathā-sarit-sāgara is called after her).<BR>—मदन-<BR>मञ्जरी, f., N. of a woman; of a daughter of<BR>Dundubhi, king of the Yakṣas; of a kind of raven.<BR>—मदन-महोत्सव (˚हा-उत्˚), अस्, m. a great<BR>festival held in honour of Kāma-deva.<BR>—मदन-<BR>मालिनी, f., N. of a woman.<BR>—मदन-मिश्र, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man.<BR>—मदन-मोदक, a particular<BR>medicinal powder.<BR>—मदन-मोहन, अस्, m. ‘the<BR>infatuater of the god of love,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मदन-रत्न, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—म-<BR>दनरत्न-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a work ascribed<BR>to king Madana-siṃha.<BR>—मदन-राज, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a man.<BR>—मदन-रिपु, उस्, m. ‘Kāma-deva's<BR>enemy,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मदन-रेखा, f., N. of<BR>the supposed mother of Vikramāditya.<BR>—मदन-<BR>ललित, अम्, n. play of love, amorous sport or dalli-<BR>ance; (आ), f. a kind of metre, four times ¯¯¯¯<BR>˘˘˘˘˘¯¯¯˘˘˘¯.<BR>—मदन-लेख, अस्, आ,<BR>m. f. a love-letter; (आ), f., N. of a woman; of a<BR>daughter of Pratāpa-mukha, king of Vārāṇasī.<BR>—म-<BR>दन-वश, अस्, आ, अम्, subdued by or subject to<BR>love, in love.<BR>—मदन-वह्नि-शिखावली, f. the<BR>flame of the fire of love.<BR>—मदन-विनोद, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a glossary by Madana-nṛpa (composed<BR>under the patronage of Madana-pāla).<BR>—मदन-<BR>वेग, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Vidyā-dharas.<BR>—मदन-शलाका, f. a species of thrush, Turdus<BR>Salica (= सारिका); the female of the Indian cuckoo;<BR>an aphrodisiac.<BR>—मदन-शिखि-पीडा, f. the pain<BR>of the fire of love.<BR>—मदन-सारिका, f. = सारिका,<BR>Turdus Salica.<BR>—मदन-सिंह, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>king (said to be the author of the Madana-ratna-<BR>pradīpa).<BR>—मदन-सुन्दरी, f., N. of various<BR>women.<BR>—मदन-सेना, f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Vīra-bhaṭa, king of Tāmra-lipti; of a merchant's<BR>daughter.<BR>—मदन-हरा, f. (= मदन-गृह),<BR>N. of a particular Prākṛt metre.<BR>—मदनाग्रक<BR>(˚न-अग्˚), अस्, m. a species of grain, Paspalum<BR>Scrobiculatum (= कोद्रव).<BR>—मदनाङ्कुश (˚न-<BR>अङ्˚), अस्, m. the penis; a finger-nail; [cf. कामाङ्-<BR>कुश.]<BR>—मदनाचार्य (˚न-आच्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a certain preceptor.<BR>—मदनातुर (˚न-आत्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, love-sick, sick with love.<BR>—मदनादित्य<BR>(˚न-आद्˚), अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR>—मदनान्तक<BR>(˚न-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘Kāma-deva's destroyer,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva.<BR>—मदनायुध (˚न-आय्˚), अम्, n.<BR>pudendum muliebre.<BR>—मदनायुष (˚न-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a species of shrub (= काम-वृद्धि).<BR>—म-<BR>दनालय (˚न-आल्˚), अम्, n. ‘love-dwelling,’ pu-<BR>dendum muliebre; a lotus; a sovereign, prince; =<BR>मदन-भवन.<BR>—मदनावस्थ (˚न-अव्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, being in a state of love, enamoured, in<BR>love; (आ), f. the state of being in love, enamoured<BR>state, separation of lovers (?).<BR>—मदनेच्छा-फल<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">Page0735-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(˚न-इच्˚), अस्, m. a species of mango (= बद्ध-<BR>रसाल).<BR>—मदनोत्सव (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, m. Kāma-<BR>deva's festival, the Holi or vernal festival (held in<BR>the spring, in honour of the god of love); a parti-<BR>cular game; (आ), f. a courtezan of Svarga.<BR>—मदनोत्-<BR>सुक (˚न-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, pining or languid with<BR>love.<BR>—मदनोद्यान (˚न-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘love's<BR>garden,’ N. of a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनक|मदनकः
मदनक, अस्, m. the plant Artemisia Indica<BR>(said to be a transposition for दमनक, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनाय
मदनाय, Nom. A. मदनायते, &c., to be<BR>like Kāma-deva, to resemble the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनिका
मदनिका, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनीय
मदनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicating (used in Ni-<BR>rukta V. 1. to explain मद्य); causing love, exciting<BR>passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयत्|मदयन्त्
मदयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, intoxicating; exhilarating,<BR>delighting, gladdening; (अन्ती), f. Arabian jasmine;<BR>wild jasmine (= वन-मल्लिका); N. of the wife of<BR>Kalmāṣa-pāda or Mitra-saha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयन्तिका|मदयंतिका
मदयन्तिका, f. (fr. मदयन्ती), Arabian jas-<BR>mine; N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयितृ
मदयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, an intoxicater, maddener,<BR>delighter; intoxicating, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयितुनु
मदयितुनु, उस्, उस्, उ, intoxicating, exhilarating;<BR>maddening; gladdening; (उस्), m. the god of love;<BR>a distiller of spirituous liquor; a drunken man; a<BR>cloud; (उस्, उ), m. n. spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदामद
मदामद, अस्, आ, अम्, being in perpetual ex-<BR>citement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदार|मदारः
मदार, अस्, m. a hog; an elephant, an elephant<BR>in rut; = धूर्त, a thorn-apple, (according to some,<BR>‘a cheat, rogue’); a lover, libertine (= कामुक); a<BR>kind of perfume, (probably) musk; N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिन्
मदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. intoxicating; rejoicing,<BR>gladdening; delightful, lovely; [cf. मन्दिन्.]<BR>—म-<BR>दिन्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very intoxicating or<BR>exhilarating (as Soma); very gladdening; (Sāy. =<BR>मादयितृतम.)<BR>—मदिन्-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved.<BR>more intoxicating, more gladdening; very gladden-<BR>ing, &c.; (Sāy. = अत्यर्थम् मादयितृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिर|मदिरः
मदिर, अस्, आ, अम्, intoxicating; gladdening,<BR>delightful, lovely; (अस्), m. a species of red-flowering<BR>Khadira; (आ), f. spirituous liquor, any inebriating<BR>drink, wine, nectar; = मत्त-खञ्जन, a species of<BR>wagtail at the pairing season, a wagtail in general;<BR>a kind of metre; N. of one of the wives of Vasu-<BR>deva; an epithet of Durgā; N. of the mother of<BR>Kādambarī.<BR>—मदिराक्ष (˚र-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>‘having intoxicating or fascinating eyes,’ lovely-eyed;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a younger brother of Śatānīka; (ई),<BR>f. a fascinating woman.<BR>—मदिरा-गृह, अम्, n.<BR>a drinking-house, tavern, dram-shop, public-house.<BR>—मदिरायत-नयना (˚रा-आय्˚), f. a mistress<BR>with fascinating and long eyes.<BR>—मदिरा-वती, f.,<BR>N. of the thirteenth Lambaka in the Kathā-sarit-<BR>sāgara.<BR>—मदिरा-शाला, f. a drinking-house, dram-<BR>shop.<BR>—मदिराश्व (˚र-अश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Rājarṣi and of a king (son of Daśāśva and grand-<BR>son of Ikṣvāku, see Mahā-bh. Anuśāsana-p. 91).<BR>—मदिरा-सख, अस्, m. ‘friend of wine,’ the<BR>mango tree.<BR>—मदिरासव (˚र-आस्˚), अस्, m. any<BR>intoxicating beverage or spirituous liquor.<BR>—मदि-<BR>रेक्षण (˚र-ईक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having intoxicating or<BR>fascinating eyes; (आ), f. a fascinating woman.<BR>—म-<BR>दिरेक्षण-वल्लभा, f. a mistress with fascinating<BR>eyes, a fascinating woman.<BR>—मदिरोत्कट (˚रा-उत्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, excited or intoxicated with spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>—मदिरोन्मत्त (˚रा-उन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>drunk with wine or spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिष्ठ
मदिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. very intoxicating or<BR>exhilarating (as Soma); very gladdening or delightful;<BR>(आ), f. any intoxicating drink, spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिष्णु
मदिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ, a word used in Nirukta IV.<BR>12. to explain मन्दु, cheerful, joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदुघ
मदुघ, अस्, m., Ved., N. of a plant yielding<BR>honey or of a species of liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदेरु
मदेरु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. (according to Sāy.) either<BR>very much intoxicated or worthy of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्य|मद्यं
2. मद्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see p. 734, col. 1),<BR>intoxicating, exhilarating, gladdening, lovely; (अम्),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0736-a" target="_blank">Page0736-a+ 77</a>]<BR>n. any intoxicating drink, vinous or spirituous liquor,<BR>wine.<BR>—मद्य-कीट, अस्, m. a kind of insect or<BR>animalcule bred in vinegar, &c.<BR>—मद्य-द्रुम,<BR>अस्, m. a species of tree (= माड).<BR>—मद्य-प,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, a drunkard, a wine-drinker, one who<BR>drinks intoxicating liquor; (अस्), m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—मद्य-पङ्क, अस्, m. vinous liquor for distilling,<BR>mash.<BR>—मद्य-पान, अम्, n. the drinking of in-<BR>toxicating liquors; any intoxicating drink.<BR>—मद्य-<BR>पाशन (˚प-आश्˚), अम्, n. a drunkard's meal.<BR>—मद्य-पीत, अस्, आ, अम्, = पीत-मद्य, one who<BR>has drunk wine or spirits; drunk, intoxicated, a<BR>drunkard.<BR>—मद्य-पुष्पा, ई, f. Grislea Tomen-<BR>tosa (the blossoms of which are used in distilling).<BR>—मद्य-बीज, see मद्य-वीज below.<BR>—मद्य-<BR>भाजन, अम्, n. ‘a wine-glass,’ a vessel for drinking<BR>intoxicating liquors.<BR>—मद्य-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a<BR>vessel for intoxicating liquors.<BR>—मद्य-मण्ड, अस्,<BR>m. yeast, barm, froth.<BR>—मद्य-वासिनी, f. Grislea<BR>Tomentosa (the blossoms of which are used in dis-<BR>tilling).<BR>—मद्य-वीज, अम्, n. a drug used to<BR>procure fermentation, leaven; less of wine.<BR>—म-<BR>द्य-सन्धान, अम्, n. distillation of spirit.<BR>—म-<BR>द्यामोद (˚य-आम्˚), अस्, m. Mimusops Elengi.<BR>—मद्यासत्तक, अस्, m., N. of a man, (Rāja-<BR>taraṅgiṇī VIII. 276, perhaps for मद्यासक्तक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्र|मद्रः
मद्र, अम्, n. joy, happiness; (अस्), m. a country<BR>to the north-west of Hindūstan proper, the land of<BR>Madra; a king of Madra; N. of a son of Śivi<BR>the progenitor of the Madras; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a people; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of Raudrāśva; of<BR>a river; a personification of the first note or Mūr-<BR>chanā in the Gāndhāra-grāma; (ई), f. a princess of<BR>Madra.<BR>—मद्र-कार or मद्रङ्-कर, अस्, आ or<BR>ई, अम्, causing joy, giving delight, delighting.<BR>—म-<BR>द्र-कूल, cf. माद्रकूलक.<BR>—मद्र-गार, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a man, (also written मद्र-गारि.)<BR>—म-<BR>द्र-नगर, अम्, n. the city of the Madras.<BR>—म-<BR>द्र-नाभ, अस्, m. a particular mixed caste (Mahā-<BR>bh. Anuśāsana-p. 2585).<BR>—मद्र-प, अस्, m. the<BR>ruler of the Madras.<BR>—मद्र-बाणिज, अस्, m. a<BR>merchant who goes to Madra.<BR>—मद्र-सुता, f.<BR>‘daughter of the king of Madra,’ an epithet of Mādrī,<BR>the second wife of Pāṇḍu; [cf. माद्री.]<BR>—मद्रा-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to shear, shave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रक|मद्रकः
मद्रक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to or produced<BR>in Madra; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a degraded people in<BR>the Dakṣiṇāpatha; (अस्), m. a king of the Madras,<BR>an inhabitant of Madra; N. of a son of Śivi the<BR>progenitor of the Madra people; (इका), f. a Madra<BR>woman, (also माद्रिका, q. v.); (अम्), n., N. of a kind<BR>of song; a particular metre, four times ¯˘˘¯˘<BR>¯˘˘˘¯, ˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯˘˘˘¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्राय
मद्राय, Nom. P. A. मद्रायति, -ते, &c., to<BR>be glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वत्|मद्वन्त्
2. मद्वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (for 1. मद्-वत् see<BR>p. 734, col. 1), Ved. containing a form or derivative<BR>of rt. 2. मद्; intoxicating, gladdening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वन्
मद्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. addicted to intoxication,<BR>fond of enjoyment, giving enjoyment, intoxicating;<BR>(आ), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मददिन्
