मा
मा 1. मा, ind. (causing a following छ् to<BR>be changed to च्छ्, see Gram. 48. c), a particle of<BR>prohibition and of negation, usually translatable by<BR>‘not,’ or sometimes used as a conjunction and equi-<BR>valent to ‘that — not, lest, would that — not;’ [cf.<BR>the use of Gr. μή; Lat. ne.] मा is most com-<BR>monly employed in prohibition or deprecation, when<BR>it may be joined with the imperative (e. g. मा<BR>ब्रूहि, speak not; मा लज्जस्व, be not ashamed;<BR>मैवं वद, speak not thus); often also with the<BR>aorist, especially in later Sanskrit, when the augment<BR>is generally dropped (e. g. मा कृथाः, do not<BR>make; मा त्याक्षीः, do not abandon; मा शुचः,<BR>grieve not; मा भैषीः, fear not; मा नीनशः,<BR>destroy not; व्यथाम् मानुभूः, feel not pain;<BR>or with the sense ‘lest,’ as in Manu VIII. 15,<BR>धर्मो न हन्तव्यो मा नो धर्मो हतो व-<BR>धीत्, justice must not be destroyed, lest justice being<BR>destroyed destroy us); often with addition of the par-<BR>ticle स्म (e. g. मा स्म वादीः, speak not; मा स्म<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-b" target="_blank">Page0764-b+ 80</a>]<BR>गमः, go not); sometimes with the imperfect,<BR>the augment being still cut off (e. g. मा स्म<BR>भवत्, may he not become; मा स्म करोत्, let<BR>him not do; मैनम् अभिभाषथाः, do not<BR>speak to him, cf. Pāṇ. VI. 4, 74); occasionally, in<BR>epic poetry &c., with an aorist, without elision of<BR>the augment (e. g. मा कालस् त्वाम् अत्य्-अगात्, let<BR>not the season pass by thee; श्रद्धा नो मा व्य्-<BR>अगमत्, may faith not depart from us); not unfre-<BR>quently with the potential, in the sense of ‘wishing<BR>that anything may not happen’ (e. g. मा स्म<BR>जनयेत् पुत्रम् ईदृशम्, may she not bring forth<BR>such a son! मा यमम् पश्येयम्, may I not see<BR>Yama! मा कूर्याद् अकार्यम्, O that he may do<BR>nothing wrong!); and even with the precative (e. g.<BR>मा भूयात्, may it not be!); more rarely with the<BR>potential, in the sense of ‘prohibition’ (e. g. मा<BR>स्मैनम् प्रत्युदीक्षेथाः, do not look at him);<BR>sometimes with the future, in the sense of ‘lest,<BR>that — not’ (e. g. मा त्वां शप्स्ये, lest I curse thee,<BR>that I may not curse thee); even with the fut. pass.<BR>part. (मैवम् प्रार्थ्यम्, it must not be so re-<BR>quested); and even with the pres. part. (e. g. मा<BR>जीवन् यो दुःख-दग्धो जीवति, he ought not<BR>[to be] living who lives consumed by pain); some-<BR>times मा takes the place of the simple negative न<BR>(e. g. गच्छ वा मा वा, you can go or not go;<BR>मा जेतव्यः, he is not to be conquered; मा गन्-<BR>तुम् अर्हसि, thou oughtest not to go; कथम् मा<BR>भूत्, how may it not be); occasionally without a<BR>verb, which must be supplied from the context (e. g.<BR>मा शब्दम्, i. e. with ellipsis of कुरुत, do not<BR>make a noise; मा नाम रक्षिणः, may it not<BR>be the watchmen ! मैवम् or मा तावत्, not so,<BR>i. e. let it not be so; or with मा repeated, thus<BR>मा मा, मा मैवम्). In the Veda मा is some-<BR>times followed by the particle उ, blending with it<BR>into मो (e. g. Ṛg-veda V. 65, 6, मा मघोनः<BR>परि ख्यतम् मो अस्माकम् [पुत्रान्], deny us<BR>not who are rich in offerings, nor indeed our sons<BR>[according to Sāy. मो = मैव]; and Ṛg-veda 1.<BR>38, 6, मो षु वधीत् [Sāy. = सर्वथा वधम्<BR>मा कार्षीत्], let him not on any account destroy);<BR>[cf. Zend and Old Pers. mā; Gr. μή; perhaps Lat.<BR>ne.]<BR>—मा-चिर, अस्, आ, अम्, not long, short; (अम्),<BR>ind. without delay, shortly, quickly (generally after<BR>an impv. or before an aor. without augment, and<BR>sometimes for न-चिरम्, e. g. गच्छ मा-चिरम्<BR>or मा-चिरं गमः, go without delay; व्रजिष्-<BR>यामि मा-चिरम्, I will set forth without delay).<BR>—मा-विलम्बम् or मा-विलम्बितम्, ind. without<BR>delay, shortly, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा 2. मा, cl. 3. P. A. (in Ved. P.)<BR>मिमाति, मिमीते, ममे, मातुम्, to low,<BR>bellow, roar, bleat, sound, make any sound or cry<BR>(especially said of cows, calves, goats, &c.; according<BR>to Nirukta II. 9, मायुम् मिमाति = मायुं शब्दं<BR>करोति; cf. rt. मीम्, मीमयति, 2. मय, मयु,<BR>मयूर): part. of the Intens. मेम्यत्, in Ṛg-veda 1.<BR>162, 2, said to mean ‘bleating as a goat;’ (according<BR>to Sāy. = either हन्यमान, fr. rt. मी, or मेमे-<BR>शब्दं कुर्वत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
1. मायु. See p. 772, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा 3. मा, cl. 2. P. माति, cl. 3. A. मिमीते<BR>(3rd pl. मिमते, part. मिमान), Impf.<BR>अमिमीत (3rd pl. अमिमत), Pot. मिमीत, Impv.<BR>मिमीताम् (2nd sing. मिमीष्व, also P. मिमीहि;<BR>used according to Naigh. III. 19, याच्ञा-कर्मणि,<BR>in the act of praying); cl. 4. A. मायते, ममौ,<BR>ममे (3rd pl. ममिरे), मास्यति, -ते, अमासीत्,<BR>अमास्त, Prec. मेयात्, मासीष्ट, मातुम्, to<BR>measure, mete; to measure off, mark off, limit; to<BR>measure (by any standard), compare with, (तदीयैर्<BR>नयनैर् अमिमीत लोचने, she compared her eyes<BR>with theirs, Kumāra-s. V. 15); to measure across,<BR>measure or pass through, traverse (with अध्वनः,<BR>in Ṛg-veda 1. 146, 3; but according to Sāy. मिमान<BR>= सम्पादयितृ, making, causing); to measure out,<BR>apportion, deal out, impart, give, grant (e. g. in<BR>Ṛg-veda IV. 44, 6, नू नो रयिम् मिमाथाम् is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">Page0764-c+ 81</a>]<BR>said to mean ‘mete out opulence for us’); to pre-<BR>pare, arrange; to form, make, create, construct,<BR>build, effect (Ved.); to display, exhibit, show, dis-<BR>play one's self (e. g. in Ṛg-veda III. 29, 11, यद्<BR>अमिमीत मातरि is said to mean ‘when he has<BR>displayed himself in the maternal atmosphere or<BR>firmament,’ where, according to Sāy., तेजस् is to be<BR>understood); to correspond in measure, find measure<BR>or room in (cl. 2. with loc., e. g. ते यशो-राशिर्<BR>भुवन-त्रितयोदरे माति, thy mass of fame<BR>finds room in the interior of the three worlds); to<BR>infer, conclude: Pass. मीयते, Aor. अमायि, to be<BR>measured &c., to be inferred: Caus. मापयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अमीमपत्, to cause to be measured or<BR>built, to have measured out or prepared; to measure,<BR>mete off; to build, erect: Desid. P. A. मित्सति, -ते<BR>(Pāṇ. VII. 4, 54, 58): Intens. ममाति, मामेति,<BR>मेमीयते (Pāṇ. VI. 4, 66); [cf. Zend mā, ‘to<BR>measure or make;’ mā, f. ‘measure:’ Gr. μέ-τρο-ν,<BR>μέτρ-ιο-ς, μῑ-μέ-ο-μαι, μῑ́-μη-σις, μῖ-μ-ο-ς: Lat.<BR>mê-tâ-re, mê-tâ-ri, mê-ti-or, mensa, mensûra:<BR>Old Slav. me-ra: Lith. më-ra, ‘measure;’ ma-tú§-<BR>ti, ‘to measure;’ méta-s, ‘time, a year:’ Russ.<BR>mje-ra, ‘measure;’ mje-ritj, ‘to measure:’ Hib.<BR>mead, ‘a balance, a scale;’ meadaighim, ‘I weigh,<BR>balance, consider.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
4. मा, मास्, f. measure, (in the formula मा<BR>छन्दः, प्र-मा छन्दः, प्रति-मा छन्दः);<BR>Ved. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात
1. मात (at the end of comps. after a proper N.)<BR>= मातृ, (according to a Vārttika used only in voc.<BR>sing. For 2. मात see p. 768, col. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातय
मातय (fr. मातृ), Nom. P. मातयति, &c.;<BR>अममातत् = मातरम् आख्यत्, Schol. on Pāṇ. VII.<BR>4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माता
माता, f. = 1. मातृ, a mother, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माताली
माताली, f. (fr. माता + आली), ‘the mother's friend,’<BR>N. of a being attending on Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माति|मातिः
माति, इस्, f. measure; accurate knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुर
मातुर (fr. मातृ), a mother, (used at the end of<BR>comps.; cf. द्वै-म्˚, भाद्र-म्˚, Pāṇ. IV. 1, 115.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुल|मातुलः
मातुल, अस्, m. (fr. मातृ with change of र्<BR>into ल्), a maternal uncle; epithet of the solar year;<BR>the thorn-apple tree [cf. मातुल-पुत्रक]; a species<BR>of grain; a kind of snake [cf. मातुलाहि]; (आ or ई),<BR>f. the wife of a maternal uncle, maternal aunt;<BR>hemp, common Bengal Śan, a species of Crotolaria;<BR>(अस्, आ or ई, अम्), belonging to or existing in a<BR>maternal uncle.<BR>—मातुल-पुत्रक, अस्, m. the little<BR>son of a maternal uncle; the fruit of the thorn-apple.<BR>—मातुलाहि (˚ल-अहि˚), इस्, m. a kind of speckled or<BR>variegated snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलक|मातुलकः
मातुलक, अस्, m. maternal uncle (a more endear-<BR>ing term than मातुल); the thorn-apple; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), belonging to or coming from a maternal uncle<BR>(Pāṇ. IV. 2, 104).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलानी
मातुलानी, f. the wife of a maternal uncle; hemp,<BR>Crotolaria Juncea; a kind of pulse (= कलाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलेय|मातुलेयः
मातुलेय, अस्, m. the son of a maternal uncle, a<BR>cousin; (ई), f. a daughter of a maternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुल्य
मातुल्य, अम्, n. (perhaps) the house of a maternal<BR>uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृ
मातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a measurer (cf. धान्य-म्˚;<BR>in Nirukta XI. 5, the moon is called माता, ‘the<BR>measurer’); a maker, former, creator, arranger, pre-<BR>parer (Ved.); a knower, one who infers correctly or<BR>has true knowledge (= ज्ञातृ, प्र-मातृ); (ता),<BR>m., N. of a particular mixed caste; N. of an author;<BR>(ता), f. (nom. du. मात्ăरौ, nom. pl. मात्ăरस्,<BR>acc. pl. मातॄस्, see Gram. 129), the maker (of the<BR>child in the womb, cf. जा-मातृ); a mother (some-<BR>times at the end of adj. comps., e. g. कुन्ती-म्˚,<BR>having Kuntī for a mother, i. e. son of Kuntī);<BR>‘mother’ as a respectful term used in addressing<BR>females, near relatives, and elderly women generally;<BR>mother earth [cf. Ṛg-veda 1. 89, 4, V. 42, 16];<BR>a cow (= गो, a cow being sometimes called लोकस्य<BR>माता, mother of the world); space, ether, the firma-<BR>ment [cf. मातरि-श्वन्]; epithet of Lakṣmī (?);<BR>epithet of Durgā; N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in Siddha-<BR>pura (also read Siddha-vana) and Kāyāvarohaṇa;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0765-a" target="_blank">Page0765-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(तरा), du., Ved. the two parents, father and mother;<BR>epithet of heaven and earth; epithet of the two<BR>pieces of wood used in kindling fire (regarded as the<BR>parents of Agni, who is called द्वि-मातृ, having<BR>two mothers; in this sense also मातरस्, pl.);<BR>(तरस्), f. pl. the divine mothers or personified ener-<BR>gies of the principal deities (sometimes reckoned as<BR>seven in number, viz. Brāhmī or Brahmāṇī, Māhe-<BR>śvarī, Kaumārī, Vaiṣṇavaī, Vārāhī, Indrāṇī or Aindrī<BR>or Māhendrī, Cāmuṇḍā; sometimes eight, viz.<BR>Brāhmī, Māheśvarī, Raudrī, Vārāhī, Vaiṣṇavī,<BR>Kaumārī, Carma-muṇḍā, Kāla-saṅkarṣiṇī; some-<BR>times nine, viz. Brahmāṇī, Vaiṣṇavī, Raudrī, Vārāhī,<BR>Nārasiṃhikā, Kaumārī, Māhendrī, Cāmuṇḍā, Caṇ-<BR>ḍikā; sometimes sixteen, viz. Gaurī, Padmā, Śacī,<BR>Medhā, Sāvitrī, Vijayā, Jayā, Deva-senā, Svadhā,<BR>Svāhā, Śānti, Puṣṭi, Dhṛti, Tuṣṭi, Ātma-devatā,<BR>Kula-devatā; these divine mothers being closely<BR>connected with the worship of the god Śiva and<BR>attending on his son Skanda or Kārttikeya, to whom<BR>at first only seven Mātṛs were assigned, but in the<BR>later mythology an innumerable number, who are<BR>sometimes represented as having displaced the original<BR>divine mothers); N. of eight classes of female ances-<BR>tors or female Manes (mothers, grandmothers, great-<BR>grandmothers, paternal and maternal aunts, &c.);<BR>according to Naigh. 1. 13, मातरः = नदी, a river,<BR>[cf. Ṛg-veda III. 9, 2, where the waters are also<BR>called मातरः, mothers; cf. also 1. 34, 8, where the<BR>seven rivers, Gaṅgā &c., are called सप्त-मातृ;<BR>according to native lexicographers मातृ has also the<BR>following senses, वि-भूति, रेवती, आखुकर्णी, इन्-<BR>द्र-वारुणी, महा-श्रावणी, जटा-मांसी: cf. Gr.<BR>μήτηρ, Dor. μάτηρ; Lat. mater; Old Germ.<BR>muotar; Old Slav. mati; Lith. mote; Hib. ma-<BR>thair.]<BR>—मातर-पितरौ, m. du. mother and<BR>father, parents.<BR>—मातरि-पुरुष, अस्, m. a man<BR>(who acts or speaks) against his mother, a cowardly<BR>bully; [cf. पितरि-शूर.]<BR>—मातरि-श्व (fr. the<BR>next), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मातरि-श्वन्, आ, m.<BR>(according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda III. 29, 11, fr.<BR>मातरि = अन्तरिक्षे, in the atmosphere, + श्वसिति<BR>= चेष्टते, breathes or moves; or according to<BR>others fr. मातरि + rt. श्वि), N. of a divine being<BR>described in Ṛg-veda 1. 60, 1, &c. as bringing<BR>down the hidden Agni to the Bhṛgus, and identified<BR>by Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 93, 6, &c. with Vāyu, the<BR>Wind; N. of Agni himself, (according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda 1. 96, 4, so called as सर्वस्य जगतो<BR>निर्मातर्य् अन्तरिक्षे श्वसन् वर्तमाणः); air,<BR>wind, breeze (personified in Mahā-bh. Udyoga-p.<BR>3599 as son of Garuḍa); N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—माता-<BR>पितृ, तरौ, m. du. mother and father, parents; [cf.<BR>Pāṇ. VI. 3, 32.]<BR>—माता-पितृ-विहीन, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>bereft of father and mother, without father or mother.<BR>—माता-पुत्र, औ, m. du. mother and son.<BR>—माता-<BR>मह, अस्, m. a maternal grandfather; (ई), f. a<BR>maternal grandmother; (औ), m. du. a grandfather<BR>and grandmother on the mother's side; (आस्), m. pl.<BR>a mother's father, grandfather, and ancestors; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), = मातामहीय below.<BR>—मातामहीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, related or belonging to a maternal grandfather.<BR>—मातुः-श्वसृ or मातुः-स्वसृ, आ, f. a mother's<BR>sister, maternal aunt; [cf. मातृ-ष्वसृ.]<BR>—मातृ-<BR>क-च्छिद, अस्, m. ‘the cutter off of his mother's<BR>head,’ an epithet of Paraśu-Rāma.<BR>—मातृ-कृत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, done or performed towards a mother;<BR>done by a mother.<BR>—मातृ-केशट, अस्, m. a<BR>mother's brother, maternal uncle.<BR>—मातृ-गण, अस्,<BR>m. the assemblage of divine mothers (as worshipped<BR>in an especial manner in the western parts of India).<BR>—मातृ-गन्धिनी, f. ‘having but the smell (i. e.<BR>the name) of mother,’ an unnatural mother.<BR>—मा-<BR>तृ-गर्भ, अस्, m. a mother's womb.<BR>—मातृगर्-<BR>भ-स्थ, अस्, आ, अम्, being in the mother's womb.<BR>—मातृ-गामिन्, ई, m. ‘going to a mother,’ one<BR>who has committed incest with his mother.<BR>—मातृ-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मातृगुप्ताभि-<BR>षेणन (˚त-अभ्˚), अम्, n. an expedition against<BR>Mātṛ-gupta.<BR>—मातृ-गोत्र, अम्, n. a mother's<BR>family; (अस्, आ, अम्), belonging to a mother's family.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0765-b" target="_blank">Page0765-b+ 81</a>]<BR>—मातृ-ग्राम, अस्, m. the aggregate of mothers,<BR>i. e. the female sex, womankind; N. of a village.<BR>—मातृ-घात or मातृ-घातक, अस्, or मातृ-<BR>घातिन्, ई, or मातृ-घ्न, अस्, m. one who kills his<BR>mother, a matricide.<BR>—मातृ-घातुक, अस्, m. a<BR>matricide; an epithet of Indra.<BR>—मातृ-चक्र, अम्,<BR>n. a kind of mystical circle, an astrological figure;<BR>the circle or assemblage of divine mothers.<BR>—मातृ-<BR>चक्र-प्रमथन, अस्, m. ‘afflicter of the circle<BR>of divine mothers (?),’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—मा-<BR>तृ-चेट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मातृ-तम, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. very motherly or maternal (said of the<BR>waters; according to Sāy. = मातृ-वज् जगतां<BR>हित-कारिन्).<BR>—मातृ-तस्, ind. on the mother's side,<BR>in right of the mother.<BR>—मातृ-ता, f. maternity,<BR>the state of a mother, the being a mother.<BR>—मातृ-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—मातृ-दत्त, अस्,<BR>m. ‘mother-given,’ N. of a man; (आ), f., N. of a<BR>woman.<BR>—मातृ-दत्तीय, N. of a work.<BR>—मातृ-<BR>देव, अस्, m. having a mother for one's god.<BR>—मा-<BR>तृ-दोष, अस्, m. the defect or inferiority of a<BR>mother (who is of a lower caste, Manu X. 14).<BR>—मातृ-नन्दन, अस्, m. ‘mother's joy,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—मातृ-नामन्, अ, n., scil.<BR>सूक्त, epithet of a class of sacred texts in the<BR>Atharva-veda; (आ), m., N. of the reputed author and<BR>deity of these texts; (आ, म्नी, अ), named after the<BR>mother; [cf. पितृ-नामन्.]<BR>—मातृ-निवातम्, ind.<BR>to a mother's shelter or protection, to a mother's<BR>side (Pāṇ. VI. 2, 8).<BR>—मातृ-पक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to the mother, belonging to the maternal<BR>line.<BR>—मातृ-पालित, अस्, n., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—मातृ-पितृ-कृताभ्यास (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>trained or exercised by one's father and mother.<BR>—मातृ-पूजन, अम्, n. the worship of the divine<BR>mothers.<BR>—मातृ-बन्धु, उस्, m. a relation on the<BR>mother's side; (उ), n. blood relationship on the<BR>mother's side.<BR>—मातृ-बन्धू, ऊस्, f. a mother<BR>only in name, an unnatural mother; [cf. ब्रह्म-<BR>बन्धु.]<BR>—मातृ-बान्धव, अस्, m. a relation on<BR>the mother's side.<BR>—मातृ-भाव, अस्, m. the state<BR>or condition of a mother, maternity.<BR>—मातृ-भेद-<BR>तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—मातृ-भोगीण,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, fit or proper to be possessed by a<BR>mother; [cf. Scholiast on Pāṇ. V. 1, 9.]<BR>—मातृ-<BR>मण्डल, अम्, n. the assemblage or company of<BR>divine mothers.<BR>—मातृमण्डल-विद्, त्, m. a priest<BR>of the Mātṛs.<BR>—मातृ-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. pos-<BR>sessing a mother, accompanied by a mother, having<BR>a mother.<BR>—मातृ-मातृ, ता, f. ‘the mother of<BR>mothers,’ an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR>—मातृ-मुख,<BR>अस्, m. ‘mother-faced,’ a simple or foolish man,<BR>simpleton.<BR>—मातृ-मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, adorned<BR>by a mother.<BR>—मातृ-मोदक, N. of Uvaṭa's com-<BR>mentary on the Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā.<BR>—मातृ-यज्ञ<BR>or मातृ-याग, अस्, m. a sacrifice or oblation to the<BR>Mātṛs.<BR>—मातृ-वत्, ind. as a mother, like a mother,<BR>as towards a mother.<BR>—मातृ-वत्सल, अस्, m.<BR>‘mother-loving,’ an epithet of Kārttikeya.<BR>—मातृ-<BR>वध, अस्, m. the murder of a mother, matricide.<BR>—मातृ-वर्तिन्, ई, इनी, इ, behaving well to a<BR>mother, dutiful to one's mother; (ई), m. a proper N.<BR>—मातृ-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, carrying one's mother;<BR>(इनी), f. a kind of bird (= वल्गुला).<BR>—मातृ-विदू-<BR>षित, अस्, आ, अम्, tainted by the mother, inheriting<BR>a taint through the mother.<BR>—मातृ-शासित, अस्, m.<BR>a man who is led or guided by his mother, a sim-<BR>pleton.<BR>—मातृ-षष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम्, having a<BR>mother as a sixth person, six with a mother or inclu-<BR>sively of a mother.<BR>—मातृ-ष्वसृ, आ, f. (also in-<BR>correctly मातृ-स्वसृ), a mother's sister, maternal<BR>aunt.<BR>—मातृष्वसेय, अस्, m. the son of a maternal<BR>aunt, a mother's sister's son; (ई), f. a mother's<BR>sister's daughter, the daughter of a maternal aunt.<BR>—मातृ-ष्वस्रीय, अस्, m. a mother's sister's son,<BR>the son of a maternal aunt; (आ), f. a mother's sister's<BR>daughter.<BR>—मातृ-सिंही, f. the plant Justicia Gen-<BR>darussa.<BR>—मातृ-हन्, आ, m. (said to be Ved.),<BR>murderer of his own mother, a matricide.<BR>—मात्री-<BR>कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to adopt as a<BR>mother, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VII. 4, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृक|मातृकः
मातृक, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or belonging<BR>to a mother, maternal; (अस्), m. a maternal uncle;<BR>(आ), f. a mother; source, origin; a divine mother;<BR>a nurse; a grandmother; epithet of eight veins on<BR>both sides of the neck, (probably so called after the<BR>eight divine mothers); epithet of certain diagrams<BR>written in characters to which a magical power is<BR>ascribed; the aggregate of such characters or the<BR>alphabet employed in such a manner, (probably only<BR>the fourteen vowels with Anusvāra and Visarga were<BR>originally so called, after the sixteen divine mothers);<BR>a wooden peg driven into the ground for the support<BR>of the staff of Indra's banner (Ved.); an epithet of<BR>the Buddhist works included in the Abhidharma-<BR>piṭaka; N. of the wife of Aryaman; = करण.<BR>—मातृका-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of mystic<BR>characters.<BR>—मातृका-यन्त्र, अम्, n. a kind of<BR>mystical diagram.<BR>—मातृकार्णव (˚का-अर्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Tantra work.<BR>—मातृका-हृदय, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्र|मात्रं|मात्रः
मात्र, अम्, आ, n. f. (the feminine आ being the<BR>earlier and the more usual simple uncompounded<BR>form), measure, quantity, sum, size, duration, measure<BR>of any kind, whether of height, depth, breadth,<BR>length, distance, time, number, (commonly at the<BR>end of comps., and sometimes added redundantly;<BR>the form at the end of adjective comps. is generally<BR>deduced fr. मात्रा, f., while other comps. are<BR>assigned to मात्र; when compounded to express<BR>‘as long,’ a high, as broad, as thick, as deep, as<BR>wide, as great, &c.,’ i. e. having a certain measure<BR>or size, the fem. is usually in ई; when compounded<BR>with pass. participles, the fem. form is usually in आ:<BR>the following examples will serve to make the com-<BR>mon usage of this word clear,<BR>—अङ्गुल-मात्रम्, a<BR>finger's breadth; जानु-मात्रे, at the height of the<BR>knees; नर-मात्रे, at the depth of a man's length;<BR>क्रोश-मात्रे, at the distance of a kos; रेखा-मा-<BR>त्रम् अपि न व्यतीयुस्, they did not transgress even<BR>the breadth of a line; ताल-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, of<BR>the size of a palm; नग-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, large<BR>as a mountain; यव-मात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, of the size<BR>of a barleycorn; एतावन्-मात्र or तावन्-मात्र, as<BR>great as this, as large as this, so much; अर्थ-मा-<BR>त्रम्, a certain sum of money; वर्ष-मात्रम्,<BR>for the period of a year; वर्ष-मात्रेण, within<BR>a year's time; क्षण-मात्रम्, for the space of a<BR>moment, for an instant; भूमि-ष्ठ-मात्रतस्,<BR>from the first moment of setting foot upon the earth;<BR>शत-मात्रम्, a hundred in number, about a hun-<BR>dred); the full or simple measure of anything, the<BR>whole, the entire thing or class of things, the one<BR>thing and no more, the totality, (often in this sense<BR>at the end of comps. and equivalent to ‘mere, only,<BR>even, just,’ frequently, but not always, assuming the<BR>gender and number of the word with which it is<BR>compounded, e. g. नाम-मात्रम्, nothing but the<BR>name; मनुष्य-मात्रः कृपणः, a poor<BR>wretch who is a mere man; पदाति-मात्रः, a<BR>simple foot-soldier; उत्तर-मात्रम् न ददाति,<BR>he gives not even an answer; रति-मात्रम्, mere<BR>sensuality; वर्ष-मात्रम्, only a year; पाद-<BR>मात्रम्, a single Pāda; श्लोक-मात्रम्, a single<BR>verse; किञ्चिन्-मात्रम्, only a little; शब्द-मा-<BR>त्रेण, by mere sound; वचन-मात्रेण, by mere<BR>words; उक्त-मात्रे वचने, on the mere utterance<BR>of the speech; ग्रन्थ-मात्रे, only in books;<BR>ज्ञान-मात्रे, on the mere information; भुक्त-<BR>मात्रे, just after eating; दर्शन-मात्रम्, mere<BR>sight; जात-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, just born; न जीव-<BR>मात्रम्, not even a living germ; प्राण-धारन-<BR>मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्, barely sufficient for the support<BR>of life; यात्रा-मात्रम् भुञ्जीत, he should eat just<BR>enough for support; आघ्रात-मात्र, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>merely or barely smelt; ध्यात-मात्रोपगामिन्,<BR>coming merely when thought upon; क्षत्रिय-<BR>मात्रम्, a Kṣatriya in general; जीव-मात्रं न<BR>हिंसेत, one should not hurt any living thing;<BR>द्वार-मात्रेऽपि गोपुरम्, Gopura signifies a door<BR>in general; in these meanings एक is sometimes redun-<BR>dantly added, e. g. प्रणिपात-मात्रैक-शरणस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">Page0766-a+ 79</a>]<BR>one whose sole refuge is prostration of the body); a<BR>definite measure, standard, rule, (in these and the<BR>following senses usually आ, f.); the correct measure;<BR>moderation; a unit of measure, a foot; the lowest<BR>division of time, a moment; a prosodial instant, the<BR>unit in metre, the length of time required to pro-<BR>nounce a short syllable, the prosodial time of a short<BR>vowel, (in this sense usually आ, f.; a long vowel<BR>contains two Mātrās and a prolated vowel three);<BR>a measure of time in music; a minute portion, par-<BR>ticle, atom; a little, trifle; an element; the primitive<BR>and subtle type of elementary matter; matter, sub-<BR>stance, the material world, the world of sense (usually<BR>आ, f.); materials, property, goods, possessions, house-<BR>hold furniture, money, wealth, substance, means of<BR>subsistence, livelihood; the upper or horizontal limb<BR>of the Nāgarī characters; an ear-ring, jewel, orna-<BR>ment; (अया), ind. in small portions, in a slight<BR>degree, moderately; [cf. Gr. μέτρον.]<BR>—मात्रा-<BR>छन्दस्, अस्, or मात्रा-वृत्त, अम्, n. metre mea-<BR>sured only by the number of prosodial instants (a long<BR>vowel containing two Mātrās and a prolated vowel<BR>three), metre measured only by the time occupied<BR>in pronunciation without any particular reference to<BR>the kinds of feet.<BR>—मात्रा-भस्त्रा, f. a money-bag,<BR>purse.<BR>—मात्रार्ध (˚रा-अर्˚), अम्, n. half-measure,<BR>half of a prosodial instant.<BR>—मात्रा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>containing a particular measure.<BR>—मात्रा-वस्ति, इस्, m.<BR>an oily clyster.<BR>—मात्राशित (˚रा-आश्˚), अम्, n. eating<BR>moderately.<BR>—मात्राशितीय, अस्, आ, अम्, treating of<BR>moderate eating.<BR>—मात्राशिन् (˚रा-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>eating moderately.<BR>—मात्रा-सङ्ग, अस्, m. attach-<BR>ment to materials, regard for household possessions<BR>or utensils (Manu VI. 57).<BR>—मात्रा-समक, N. of<BR>a class of metres.<BR>—मात्रा-स्पर्श, अस्, m. material<BR>contact, the concurrence of material elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रक
मात्रक = मात्र at the end of comps. (e. g.<BR>छाया-मात्रक, lasting only as long as a shadow;<BR>मन्त्र-ब्राह्मण-मात्रकात्, from the Mantras<BR>and Brāhmaṇas alone; जात-मात्रक, just born);<BR>(इका), f. = मात्रा, the prosodial time of a short<BR>vowel, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रतस्
मात्रतस्, ind. = मात्रात्, मात्रे (at the end of<BR>comps., see under मात्र), from the first moment, at<BR>the moment of, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रिक
मात्रिक = मात्र at the end of comps.; (आ), f. a<BR>prosodial instant, a simple sound, see under मात्रक<BR>above; (अस्, आ, अम्), material, of the nature of matter,<BR>containing a short vowel (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रीय
मात्रीय, Nom. P. A. मात्रीयति, -ते, &c., to<BR>wish one's self a mother; to treat one as a mother<BR>(with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान, मापक, &c. See pp. 770, 771.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित|मितः
मित, मेय, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माउथ
माउथ माüथ, N. of a place; (also read<BR>माüणथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांश्चतु
मांश्चतु मांश्चतु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. (probably<BR>some colour), light yellow, dun-coloured (an epithet<BR>of Mitra or of a horse or horses; according to Sāy.<BR>on Ṛg-veda VII. 44, 3, = मन्यमानान् स्तुवतो<BR>जनांश् चेतयते जानाति यद्वा अभिमन्यमानांश्<BR>चातयते नाशयति यः, one who is mindful of his<BR>adorers, or destroying those that despise him; ac-<BR>cording to Naigh. 1. 14, मांश्चत्वः = अश्वाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांश्चत्व
मांश्चत्व, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. yellowish, (this word<BR>occurs with doubtful meaning in Ṛg-veda IX.<BR>97, 4.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांस्
मांस् मांस्, n. = मांस, flesh, meat, &c.<BR>(see below; मांस् is defective in nom. and acc. sing.<BR>and du., the inst. is मांसा, acc. pl. मांसि, inst.<BR>dat. abl. du. मान्भ्याम्, &c.).<BR>—मांस्-पचन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. used for cooking meat (said of a<BR>caldron).<BR>—मांस्-पाक, अस्, m. = मांस-पाक,<BR>q. v. (Pāṇ. VI. 1, 144).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांस|मांसं|मांसः
मांस, अम्, n. (said to be fr. rt. मन्; a fanciful<BR>derivation fr. मां स is given in Manu V. 55),<BR>flesh, meat, animal food, (according to some also अस्,<BR>m.); the flesh of fish; the fleshy part or pulp of<BR>fruit; (अस्), m., N. of a mixed caste (= मांस-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-b" target="_blank">Page0766-b+ 81</a>]<BR>विक्रेतृ, selling meat; cf. मांस-च्छेद); a<BR>worm; time; (ई), f. = जटा-मांसी, Nardostachys<BR>Jatamansi; a sort of drug; = मांस-च्छदा; [cf.<BR>Old Germ. môs, ‘food;’ Mod. Germ. Mus, Gemüse;<BR>Slav. manso; Lith. mēsa; Hib. maise, ‘food,<BR>victuals.’]<BR>—मांस-कच्छप, अस्, m. a fleshy<BR>abscess on the palate.<BR>—मांस-कन्दी, f. a fleshy<BR>protuberance or swelling of the flesh.<BR>—मांस-<BR>काम, अस्, आ, अम्, fond of meat or flesh.<BR>—मांस-<BR>कारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, flesh-making, flesh-preparing; (ई),<BR>n. blood.<BR>—मांस-खण्ड, अस्, अम्, m. n. a bit<BR>of flesh or meat.<BR>—मांस-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. flesh-<BR>swelling, a gland.<BR>—मांस-च्छदा, f. a species of<BR>plant.<BR>—मांस-च्छेद, अस्, ई, m. f. or मांस-<BR>च्छेदिन्, ई, m. ‘flesh-cutter,’ N. of a mixed caste.<BR>—मांस-ज, अम्, n. ‘flesh-born,’ the marrow of<BR>the flesh, adeps, fat.<BR>—मांस-तान, अस्, m. a polypus<BR>in the throat.<BR>—मांस-तेजस्, अस्, n. ‘flesh-marrow,’<BR>fat, adeps; [cf. मांस-ज.]<BR>—मांस-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>fleshiness, the being flesh; the derivation of the<BR>word मांस (Manu V. 55).<BR>—मांस-दग्ध, अम्,<BR>n. cauterizing of the flesh.<BR>—मांस-दलन, अस्,<BR>m. a plant, Amoora Rohitaka.<BR>—मांस-द्राविन्, ई,<BR>m. a species of sorrel, Rumex Vesicarius.<BR>—मांस-<BR>निर्यास, अस्, m. the hair of the body.<BR>—मांसन्-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत् (fr. Ved. मांसन्), fleshy.<BR>—मांस-<BR>प, अस्, m. ‘flesh-sucker,’ epithet of a Piśāca; of a<BR>Dānava.<BR>—मांस-पचन, अस्, ई, अम्, meat-cook-<BR>ing; (अम्), n. a vessel for cooking meat.<BR>—मांस-<BR>परिवर्जन, अम्, n. avoiding meat, abstaining<BR>from animal food.<BR>—मांस-परिविक्रयिन्, ई, m.<BR>a flesh-monger, dealer in flesh.<BR>—मांस-पाक,<BR>अस्, m. a kind of disease (destroying the mem-<BR>brum virile).<BR>—मांस-पिटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a<BR>basket of meat, a large quantity of flesh or meat.<BR>—मांस-पिण्ड-गृहीत-वदन, अस्, आ, अम्, car-<BR>rying a piece of flesh in the mouth.<BR>—मांस-पित्त,<BR>अम्, n. a bone.<BR>—मांस-पेशी, f. a piece of flesh;<BR>an epithet of the fetus from the eighth till the four-<BR>teenth day [cf. पेशी]; a muscle.<BR>—मांस-फला,<BR>f. the egg-plant, Solanum Melongena.<BR>—मांस-<BR>भक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, or मांस-भक्षक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, flesh-eating, carnivorous, eating meat; (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—मांस-भक्षण, अम्, n.<BR>the act of eating meat, eating animal food.<BR>—मांस-<BR>भिक्षा, f., Ved. begging for meat as alms, soliciting<BR>flesh as alms.<BR>—मांस-भुज्, क्, क्, क्, flesh-eating,<BR>eating meat.<BR>—मांस-भूतोदन (˚त-ओद्˚), अम्,<BR>n. ‘boiled rice mixed with meat,’ rice and meat.<BR>—मांस-भेत्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, flesh-cutting, inflict-<BR>ing a flesh-wound, piercing the flesh.<BR>—मांस-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of flesh; मांस-मयी<BR>पेशी, a piece of flesh.<BR>—मांस-मासा, f. a species of<BR>plant, = माष-पर्णी; (also read मांस-माषा.)<BR>—मांस-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having flesh in the<BR>mouth.<BR>—मांस-यूथ, अम्, n. a quantity of flesh.<BR>—मांस-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, flesh-born; (इस्), m. a<BR>creature of flesh and blood.<BR>—मांस-रस, अस्, m.<BR>meat-broth, soup.<BR>—मांस-रुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, fond of<BR>flesh, having a relish for animal food.<BR>—मांस-<BR>रोहिणी or मांस-रोही, f. a species of fragrant plant.<BR>—मांस-लता, f. ‘flesh-tendril,’ a wrinkle.<BR>—मांस-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having or possessing flesh.<BR>—मांस-<BR>विक्रय, अस्, m. the sale of meat.<BR>—मांस-विक्र-<BR>यिन्, ई, इणी, इ, or मांस-विक्रेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, selling<BR>meat, a meat-seller; (मांस-विक्रयिन् is used as a<BR>term of reproach for a low or vile person.)<BR>—मांस-<BR>वृद्धि, इस्, f. an increase or growth of flesh.<BR>—मांस-शील, अस्, आ, अम्, accustomed to eat meat;<BR>fleshy.<BR>—मांस-शोणित, अम्, n. flesh and blood.<BR>—मांस-शोणित-पङ्किन्, ई, इनी, इ, miry with flesh<BR>and blood.<BR>—मांस-सङ्घात, अस्, m. a swelling of<BR>the flesh.<BR>—मांस-सार, अस्, m. ‘flesh-essence, flesh-<BR>marrow,’ fat; (अस्, आ, अम्), having the flesh predo-<BR>minant among the seven constituent parts of the<BR>body.<BR>—मांस-स्नेह, अस्, m. ‘flesh-marrow,’ adeps,<BR>fat.<BR>—मांस-हासा, f. skin.<BR>—मांसाद् (˚स-अद्),<BR>त्, त्, त्, or मांसाद (˚स-अद or -आद), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>or मांसादिन् (˚स-आद्˚), ई, इनी, इ, flesh-eating, car-<BR>nivorous.<BR>—मांसार्गल (˚स-अर्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. a<BR>piece of flesh hanging from the mouth (of a lion<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">Page0766-c+ 74</a>]<BR>&c.).<BR>—मांसार्बुद (˚स-अर्˚), अस्, m. a kind of<BR>disease of the membrum virile.<BR>—मांसाशन (˚स-<BR>अश्˚), अम्, n. flesh-meat; the act of eating flesh-<BR>meat.<BR>—मांसाशि-त्व, अम्, n. the state of one who<BR>eats flesh, the devouring of flesh.<BR>—मांसाशिन् (˚स-<BR>आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ, eating flesh, living upon meat.<BR>—मांसाष्टका (˚स-अष्˚), f., N. of the eighth day<BR>in the dark half of the month Māgha (on which<BR>meat is offered to the Manes).<BR>—मांसाहार (˚स-<BR>आह्˚), अस्, m. animal food.<BR>—मांसएष्टा (˚स-इष्˚),<BR>f. a kind of bird, the flesh of which is considered a<BR>delicacy (= वल्गुला).<BR>—मांसोन्नति (˚स-उन्˚), इस्,<BR>f. a swelling of the flesh.<BR>—मांसोपजीविन् (˚स-<BR>उप्˚), ई, m. living by flesh, a dealer in meat.<BR>—मां-<BR>सौदन (˚स-ओद्˚), अस्, m. meat and boiled rice.<BR>—मांसौदनिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. the preceding),<BR>see Pāṇ. IV. 4, 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसल|मांसलं|मांसलः
मांसल, अस्, आ, अम्, fleshy; lusty, brawny, mus-<BR>cular; powerful, strong (sometimes applied to sound);<BR>pulpy (as fruit).<BR>—मांसल-फला, f. Solanum Me-<BR>longena; [cf. मांस-फला.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसिक|मांसिकः
मांसिक, अस्, आ, अम्, = मांसाय प्रभवति,<BR>see Gaṇa Santāpādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 101; (अस्), m. a<BR>butcher, a seller of meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसिका
मांसिका, f. (fr. मांसी), the plant Nardostachys<BR>Jatamansi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसिनी
मांसिनी, f. Nardostachys Jatamansi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसीय
मांसीय, Nom. P. मांसीयति, &c., Ved. to long<BR>for flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांस्पृष्ट
मांस्पृष्ट मां-स्पृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved., ac-<BR>cording to a Schol. a comp. fr. माम् + स्पृष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकन्द|माकंद|माकंदः|माकन्दः
माकन्द माकन्द, अस्, m. the mango tree;<BR>(ई), f. the Myrobalan tree, Myrobalan; N. of other<BR>plants (= Hindī माद्राणी, माकुनी); yellow sandal-<BR>wood, yellow sanders; N. of a city on the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकन्दक
माकन्दक, अस्, इका, अम्, belonging to the town<BR>Mākandī; (इका), f. = माकन्दी, the city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकन्दिक
माकन्दिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकर
माकर माकर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मकर),<BR>related or belonging to the sea-monster Makara;<BR>माकर आकर, ‘the mine of Makaras,’ the sea;<BR>माकरम् आसनम्, a particular posture in sitting;<BR>माकरो व्यूहः, a particular form of military array;<BR>माकरी सप्तमी = मकर-सप्तमी, the seventh<BR>day in the light half of the month Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकरन्द|माकरंद
माकरन्द माकरन्द, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मक-<BR>रन्द), coming from or consisting of the juice of<BR>flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकलि|माकलिः
माकलि माकलि, इस्, m. the moon; N. of<BR>Indra's charioteer; [cf. मातलि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकष्टेय
माकष्टेय माकष्टेय (fr. मकष्टु), a pa-<BR>tronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकारध्यान
माकारध्यान माकार-ध्यान, अम्, n. (pro-<BR>bably fr. I. मा + कार), a particular method of ab-<BR>stract meditation, kind of reverie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकिम्
माकिम् मा-किम्, see Gaṇa Cādi to Pāṇ. 1.<BR>4, 57; [cf. न-किम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकिस्
मा-किस्, ind., Ved. not (= Lat. ne, e. g. Ṛg-veda<BR>1. 147, 5, मा-किर् no दुरिताय धायीः, consign us<BR>not to misfortune); no one (= Lat. ne-quis, e. g.<BR>Ṛg-veda VIII. 5, 39, मा-किर् एना पथा गात्, let<BR>none proceed by that path; according to Sāy. अनेन<BR>मार्गेण अन्यो न गन्तुं शक्नोति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकीम्
मा-कीम्, ind., see Gaṇa Cādi to Pāṇ. 1. 4, 57,<BR>(according to Sāy.) = १. मा; [cf. न-कीम्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकी
माकी माकी, f. du., Ved. (Sāy.) = निर्मा-<BR>त्र्यौ भूत-जातस्य, the two creators or originators<BR>of all beings, (said of heaven and earth.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकीन
माकीन माकीन, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. 3. म), Ved.<BR>(according to Sāy.) my, mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकुलि|माकुलिः
माकुलि माकुलि, इस्, m. a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकोट
माकोट माकोट, N. of one of the places in<BR>which Dākṣāyaṇī is worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षव्य
माक्षव्य माक्षव्य, अस्, m. (fr. मक्षु),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">Page0767-a+ 77</a>]<BR>Ved. a patronymic, N. of a preceptor; [cf. मां-<BR>क्षव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिक|माक्षिकं|माक्षिकः
माक्षिक माक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मक्षिका),<BR>coming from or belonging to a bee; (अम्), n., scil.<BR>मधु, honey; a kind of honey-like mineral sub-<BR>stance or pyrites, (various kinds are described, see<BR>स्वर्ण-म्˚, रूप्य-म्˚, कांस्य-म्˚, विट्-म्˚); [cf.<BR>Old Germ. wahs, ‘wax;’ Angl. Sax. väx, vex, veax;<BR>Lith. waszka-s; Russ. vosk.]<BR>—माक्षिक-ज, अम्,<BR>n. ‘honey-born,’ bees’-wax.<BR>—माक्षिक-फल, अस्,<BR>m. a species of cocoa-nut (= मधु-नालिकेरिक).<BR>—माक्षिक-शर्करा, f. a kind of sugar, candied<BR>sugar.<BR>—माक्षिक-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N. of a place.<BR>—माक्षिकाश्रय (˚क-आश्˚), अम्, n. bees'-wax;<BR>honey-comb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षीक|माक्षीकं
माक्षीक, अम्, n. = माक्षिक, honey.<BR>—मा-<BR>क्षीक-धातु, उ, n. a kind of pyrites (described<BR>above).<BR>—माक्षिक-शर्करा, f. clarified sugar (=<BR>सिताखण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माख
माख माख, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मख), of or<BR>belonging to a sacrifice, sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागद्य
मागद्य मागद्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मगदिन्),<BR>see Gaṇa Pragadyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागध|मागधः
मागध मागध, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मगध),<BR>relating to or born in or living in or customary among<BR>the Magadhas or the Magadha country; मागधी<BR>भाषा, the Magadha language; (अस्), m. a king<BR>of the Magadhas; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people, the<BR>Magadhas; opprobrious epithet of a mixed caste<BR>(still numerous in Guzerat, and called the Bhāts),<BR>the son of a Kṣatriya mother and Vaiśya father,<BR>the poetical panegyrist of a king, a bard, minstrel<BR>(whose duty is to recite the praises of kings in their<BR>presence with allusions to their genealogy and the<BR>deeds of their ancestors, or to attend the march of<BR>an army and animate the soldiers by martial songs;<BR>frequently associated with सूत and वन्दिन्); N. of<BR>one of the seven sages in the fourteenth Manv-antara;<BR>of a son of Yadu; white cummin; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>the warrior-caste in Śākya-dvīpa; (आ), f. a princess<BR>of the Magadhas; long pepper; (ई), f. a princess of<BR>the Magadhas; the daughter of a Kṣatriya mother<BR>and Vaiśya father; the language of the Magadhas;<BR>N. of a river (= शोणा); Jasminum Auriculatum;<BR>long pepper; white cummin; anise or dill; a species<BR>of cardamoms (grown in Guzerat); refined sugar; a<BR>kind of metre (Ved.).<BR>—मागध-देशीय, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, belonging to or born in the land of the Ma-<BR>gadhas.<BR>—मागध-पुर, अम्, n. ‘the city of the<BR>Magadhas,’ N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागधक
मागधक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people; (इका),<BR>f. long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागधिक|मागधिकः
मागधिक, अस्, m. a prince of the Magadhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ|माघः
माघ माघ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मघा), related<BR>to the constellation Maghā; (अस्), m., scil. मास,<BR>the month Māgha which begins with the winter<BR>solstice (= January-February); N. of a poet (son of<BR>Dattaka and author of the Śiśupāla-vadha or Māgha-<BR>kāvya); (ई), f., scil. तिथि, the day of full moon in<BR>the month Māgha; Hingtsha Repens.<BR>—माघ-<BR>काव्य, अम्, n. the poem of Māgha, i. e. the Śiśu-<BR>pāla-vadha.<BR>—माघ-चैतन्य, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>author of the eighth book of the Kalpa-latā.<BR>—माघ-<BR>पाक्षिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to one of the two<BR>halves of the month Māgha.<BR>—माघ-माहात्म्य,<BR>अम्, n. ‘the majesty of the month Māgha,’ N. of a part<BR>of the Padma-Purāṇa.<BR>—माघ-स्नान, अम्, n. bathing<BR>or religious ablution in sacred pools &c. in the month<BR>of Māgha.<BR>—माघी-पक्ष-यजनीय, अम्, n. the<BR>first day of the month Phālguna; [cf. यजनीय.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ्य|माघ्यं
माघ्य, अम्, n. the flower of the Jasminum<BR>Multiflorum or Pubescens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघमा
माघमा माघमा, f. a female crab (= कर्-<BR>कटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघवत
माघवत माघवत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मघ-<BR>वत्), belonging to Indra; (ई), f., scil. दिश्, the east.<BR>—माघवत-चाप, अस्, m. the rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघवन|माघवनं
माघवन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मघ-वन्), belong-<BR>ing to Indra, ruled by Indra (Pāṇ. VI. 4, 128).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघोन
माघोन, अम्, n. liberality (Ved.); (ई), f., scil.<BR>दिश्, the east, the eastern quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्क्ष्|मांक्ष्
माङ्क्ष् माङ्क्ष् (connected with rt.<BR>काङ्क्ष्), cl. I. P. माङ्क्षति, माङ्-<BR>क्षितुम्, to wish, long for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्क्षव्य
माङ्क्षव्य माङ्क्षव्य, अस्, m. (fr. मङ्क्षु),<BR>a patronymic (Gaṇa Gargādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 105);<BR>माङ्क्षव्यायणी, f. (Gaṇa Lohitādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>1, 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गल
माङ्गल माङ्गल, अम्, n. (fr. मङ्गल), Ved.<BR>epithet of a particular liturgical formula addressed to<BR>the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गलि
माङ्गलि, इस्, m. a patronymic, N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गलिक|मांगलिक
माङ्गलिक, अस्, ई, अम्, auspicious, propitious,<BR>tending to good fortune, wishing for prosperity, in-<BR>dicating good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गलिका
माङ्गलिका, f. (fem. of an unused form माङ्ग-<BR>लक), N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गल्य|मांगल्य|माङ्गल्यं
माङ्गल्य, अस्, आ (?) , अम्, = मङ्गल्य, conferring<BR>happiness, auspicious; (अस्), m. Ægle Marmelos;<BR>(अम्), n. an auspicious thing, amulet; a benediction;<BR>an auspicious or festive ceremony, festivity, festival;<BR>prosperity, happiness, welfare, propitiousness.<BR>—माङ्-<BR>गल्य-मृदङ्ग, अस्, m. a tabour or drum beaten<BR>on festive occasions.<BR>—माङ्गल्यार्हा (˚य-अर्˚), f.<BR>a species of plant (= त्रायमाणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गुष्य
माङ्गुष्य माङ्गुष्य, अस्, m. (fr. मङ्गुष),<BR>a patronymic (Gaṇa Kurvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 151).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माच|माचः
माच माच, अस्, m. a way, road; [cf. मा-<BR>ठ, माथ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचल|माचलः
माचल माचल, अस्, m. (perhaps fr. 1. मा +<BR>चल), a thief, robber (= वन्दी-कार); a crocodile,<BR>&c. (= ग्राह); sickness, illness; [cf. करि-म्˚,<BR>गज-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचाकीय
माचाकीय माचाकीय, अस्, m., N. of a gram-<BR>marian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचाल
माचाल माचाल in पर्ण-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिका
माचिका माचिका, f. = मक्षिका, a fly [cf.<BR>गृह-म्˚]; a species of plant (= अम्ब-ष्ठा; cf.<BR>काक-म्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माची
माची in काक-म्˚ and ध्वाङ्क्ष-म्˚; cf. मा-<BR>चिका above.<BR>—माची-पत्त्र, अम्, n. a species of<BR>medicinal plant (= सुर-पर्ण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिरम्
माचिरम् मा-चिरम्. See p. 764, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजल|माजलः
माजल माजल, अस्, m. a kind of bird, the<BR>blue roller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजलपुर
माजल-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजिक
माजिक माजिक, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजिरक
माजिरक माजिरक, अस्, m. (fr. मजिरक),<BR>a patronymic (Gaṇa Śivādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 112).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजीज
माजीज माजीज, N. of a place; (also read<BR>माजुज and माजूज.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जिष्ठ|मांजिष्ठ|माञ्जिष्ठं
माञ्जिष्ठ माञ्जिष्ठ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मञ्जिष्-<BR>ठा), red as madder, red as the dye made from<BR>the Mañjiṣṭhā; (अम्), n. red, red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जिष्ठक
माञ्जिष्ठक or माञ्जिष्ठिक, अस्, ई, अम्, red<BR>as Bengal madder, dyed with madder, red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जीरक
माञ्जीरक माञ्जीरक, अस्, m. (fr. मञ्जीरक),<BR>a patronymic (Gaṇa Śivādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 112).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माटाम्रक|माटाम्रकः
माटाम्रक माटाम्रक, अस्, m. a species of<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माटियारि
माटियारि माटियारि or माटीयारि, N. of a<BR>city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठ|माठः
माठ माठ or माठ्य, अस्, m. a road; [cf.<BR>माथ, माच.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठर|माठरः
माठर माठर, अस्, m. (fr. मठर), a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">Page0767-c+ 73</a>]<BR>patronymic, a proper N.; = Vyāsa; N. of one of<BR>the sun's attendants; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(ई), f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठरक
माठरक, see Gaṇa Dhūmādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2,<BR>127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठरायण
माठरायण, अस्, m. a patronymic (Gaṇa Hari-<BR>tādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 100).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठर्य
माठर्य, अस्, m. (fr. मठर), a patronymic,<BR>see Schol. on Uṇādi-sūtras V. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठव्य
माठव्य माठव्य, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठी
माठी माठी, f. armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड्
माड् माड्, cl. I. P. A. माडति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to measure, weigh, (a various reading for<BR>rt. माह्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड|माडः
माड, अस्, m. measure, weight, quantity; a species<BR>of tree (= मद्य-द्रुम, also read माडा-द्रुम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माडव|माडवः
माडव माडव, अस्, m. a particular mixed<BR>caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माडार्य
माडार्य माडार्य (fr. मडार), see Gaṇa<BR>Pragadyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माडि|माडिः
माडि माडि, इस्, m. a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड्डुक|माड्डुकः
माड्डुक माड्डुक or माड्डुकिक, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. मड्डुक, q. v.), a drummer, player on the<BR>Maḍḍuka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माढि|माढिः
माढि माढि, इस्, f. = दल-स्नसा, the fibre<BR>or vein of a leaf (= पत्त्र-शिरा); the germ of<BR>leaves, the young leaf before it opens; honouring,<BR>respecting, reverencing, (in this sense fr. rt. मह्);<BR>dejection, sadness, affliction; poverty, indigence,<BR>manifestation of poverty, declaration of distress;<BR>anger, passion; a back or double tooth; the hem<BR>or border of a garment; N. of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माढी
माढी, f. = दन्त-शिरा, a back or double tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण
माण माण, अस्, m. a species of plant (=<BR>माणक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणक|माणकं|माणकः
माणक, अस्, m. a small shrub, Arum Indicum;<BR>the bulbous root of the Arum Indicum; [cf. मा-<BR>नक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव|माणवः
माणव माणव, अस्, m. a youth, lad, young-<BR>ster, (especially) a young Brāhman; a man, little<BR>man, manikin (used contemptuously); a pearl orna-<BR>ment of sixteen strings [cf. अर्ध-म्˚]; epithet of<BR>one of the nine treasures of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवक|माणवकः
माणवक, अस्, m. a lad or boy not exceeding<BR>sixteen years of age; a little man, dwarf, (माया-<BR>माणवको हरिः, Viṣṇu disguising himself under<BR>the form of a dwarf); a manikin (contemptuously);<BR>a silly or childish man, an ignorant or ridiculous<BR>man, (in the drama used as an epithet of the Vidū-<BR>shaka or jocose friend of the king); a pupil, scholar,<BR>religious student; a pearl ornament of a particular<BR>number of strings (e. g. of sixteen, twenty, or forty-<BR>eight strings); (इका), f. a young girl, damsel, wench;<BR>(अम्), n. = माणवक-क्रीड, a kind of metre, four<BR>times ¯ ˘ ˘ ¯ ¯ ˘ ˘ ¯.<BR>—माणवक-क्रीड, अम्, आ,<BR>n. f. ‘boy's play,’ N. of a kind of metre.<BR>—माण-<BR>वक-क्रीडनक or माणवक-क्रीडितक, अम्, n.<BR>= माणवक-क्रीड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवीन|माणवीनं
माणवीन, अस्, आ, अम्, proper for boys or lads,<BR>boyish, childish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव्य|माणव्यं
माणव्य, अम्, n. a multitude or company of boys<BR>or lads, boyhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणहल
माणहल माणहल, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिका
माणिका माणिका, f. a particular weight,<BR>= 2 Kuḍavas, = 1 Śarāva, = 8 Palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिकाम्बू
माणिकाम्बू माणिकाम्बू, ऊस्, f., N. of a<BR>woman, the mother of the Scholiast Viṭṭhala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिक्य|माणिक्यं
माणिक्य माणिक्य, अम्, n. a ruby [cf. रङ्ग-<BR>म्˚]; (अस्), m., N. of a man; (आ), f. a kind of<BR>small house-lizard.<BR>—माणिक्य-चन्द्र, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king of Tīra-bhukti.<BR>—माणिक्य-मय, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, made or consisting of rubies.<BR>—माणिक्य-मल्ल,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">Page0768-a+ 72</a>]<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king (patron of Manohara-śarman<BR>the commentator on the Śruta-bodha).<BR>—माणिक्य-<BR>मिश्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—माणिक्य-राय, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—माणिक्य-सूरि, इस्, m., N. of a<BR>Gujarāṭhī author and of other persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिचर
माणिचर माणिचर, अस्, m., Ved. (accord-<BR>ing to a commentator) the tutelary genius of the<BR>war-chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिचार
माणिचार, अस्, m. = माणिभद्र below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिपार
माणिपार माणिपार, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिपाल
माणिपाल माणिपाल, see Gaṇa Mahiṣyādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिपालिक
माणिपालिक, see Gaṇa Revatyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1,<BR>146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिबन्ध|माणिबंध|माणिबंधं|माणिबन्धं
माणिबन्ध माणिबन्ध, अम्, n. = माणि-<BR>मन्थ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिभद्र
माणिभद्र माणिभद्र = मणि-भद्र, a<BR>king of the Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिवर
माणिवर = माणिभद्र above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिमन्थ|माणिमंथ|माणिमंथं|माणिमन्थं
माणिमन्थ माणिमन्थ, अम्, n. (fr. मणि-<BR>मन्थ), salt brought from the mountain Maṇi-<BR>mantha, rock-salt, sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिमन्त
माणिमन्त, अम्, n. = माणिमन्थ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिरूप्यक
माणिरूप्यक माणिरूप्यक (fr. मणि + रूप्य),<BR>see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्टि|मांटि
माण्टि माण्टि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a teacher;<BR>(अयस्), m. pl., N. of his descendants; [cf. मण्टि,<BR>मेण्ठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्ड
माण्ड माण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डकर्णि
माण्डकर्णि माण्डकर्णि, इस्, m. (a patro-<BR>nymic fr. मण्ड-कर्ण), N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डप
माण्डप माण्डप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मण्डप),<BR>belonging to a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डरिक
माण्डरिक माण्डरिक (fr. मण्डर), see<BR>Gaṇa Aṅgulyādi to Pāṇ. V. 3, 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डलिक|मांडलिक|माण्डलिकः
माण्डलिक माण्डलिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मण्-<BR>डल), relating to a province, ruling a province;<BR>(अस्), m. the governor of a province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डव
माण्डव माण्डव, अम्, n. (fr. मण्डु), N. of<BR>a Sāman; एडम् माण्डवम्, N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डवी
माण्डवी, f. (fr. माण्डव्य below), N. of a<BR>daughter of Kuśa-dhvaja and wife of Bharata; a N.<BR>of Dākṣāyaṇī at Māṇḍavya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डव्य
माण्डव्य, अस्, m. (fr. मण्डु), a patronymic,<BR>N. of a teacher; (आस्), m. pl. the descendants of<BR>Māṇḍavya; N. of a people; (अस्, अम्), m. or n. (?),<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—माण्डव्य-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city on the Godā.<BR>—माण्डव्येश्वर (˚य-ईश्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR>—माण्डव्येश्वर-तीर्थ, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डव्यायन
माण्डव्यायन, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. माण्डव्य), a<BR>patronymic (Gaṇa Lohitādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूक
माण्डूक माण्डूक, आस्, m. pl. (fr. मण्डूक),<BR>N. of a school.<BR>—माण्डूकी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूकायन
माण्डूकायन, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR>—माण्-<BR>डूकायनी-पुत्र, अस्, m., N. of a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूकायनि
माण्डूकायनि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूकि
माण्डूकि, इस्, m. (fr. मण्डूक), a patronymic<BR>(Pāṇ. IV. 1, 119).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूकेय
माण्डूकेय, अस्, m. (fr. मण्डूक), a patronymic,<BR>N. of a teacher; (आस्), m. pl. his descendants; (अम्),<BR>n. the doctrine or teaching of Māṇḍūkeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूकेयीय
माण्डूकेयीय, relating to or connected with Māṇ-<BR>ḍūkeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डूक्य
माण्डूक्य, probably an adj. from माण्डूक.<BR>—माण्डूक्य-श्रुति, इस्, f. the Māṇḍukya revela-<BR>tion or teaching.<BR>—माण्डूक्योपनिषद् (˚य-उप्˚),<BR>त्, f., N. of a short but important Upaniṣad of the<BR>Atharva-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात
मात 2. मात, अस्, ई, m. f. (for 1. see p. 764,<BR>col. 3), Ved. a metronymic from Mati in Vāṅmātī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातङ्ग|मातंग|मातंगः|मातङ्गः
मातङ्ग मातङ्ग, अस्, m. (fr. मतङ्ग), an<BR>elephant; any large animal like an elephant; (at the<BR>end of comps.) anything the best of its kind (e. g.<BR>वलाहक-मातङ्गास्, ‘elephants of clouds,’ i. e. ‘best<BR>of clouds,’ an epithet of the Saṃvartaka clouds; cf.<BR>मातङ्ग-नक्र below); Ficus Religiosa; epithet<BR>of the twenty-fourth astronomical Yoga; a Cāṇḍāla,<BR>a man of the lowest rank, an outcast; a kind of<BR>Kirāta mountaineer, barbarian; N. of the servant of<BR>the seventh and of the twenty-fourth Arhat of the<BR>present Ava-sarpiṇī; of a Pratyeka-buddha; of an<BR>author; of a Nāga; (ई), f., N. of a mythical being<BR>regarded as progenitress of the whole elephant tribe;<BR>of a form of Durgā; of the wife of Vasiṣṭha.<BR>—मातङ्ग-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or belong-<BR>ing to an elephant, elephantine.<BR>—मातङ्ग-दिवा-<BR>कर, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—मातङ्ग-नक्र,<BR>अस्, m. a crocodile as large as an elephant.<BR>—मा-<BR>तङ्ग-मकर, अस्, m. a kind of marine monster.<BR>—मातङ्ग-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a Buddhist Sūtra.<BR>—मातङ्गोत्सङ्ग (˚ग-उत्˚), अस्, m. the back of<BR>an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातय
मातय मातय. See p. 764, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिपुरुष|मातरिपुरुषः
मातरिपुरुष मातरि-पुरुष, &c. See<BR>p. 765, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिश्व
मातरिश्व मातरि-श्व, मातरि-श्वन्. See<BR>p. 765, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातलि|मातलिः
मातलि मातलि, इस्, m., N. of Indra's<BR>charioteer, (said to be also read मातुलि.)<BR>—मातलि-<BR>सारथि, इस्, m. ‘having Mātali for his charioteer,’<BR>an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातलीय
मातलीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to or concerning<BR>Mātali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातली
मातली मातली, ई, m. (only found in the<BR>nom. sing. and without any case-ending, cf. पृथी),<BR>Ved., N. of a divine being associated with Yama and<BR>the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातवचस
मातवचस मातवचस, अस्, m., Ved. a patro-<BR>nymic from Mata-vacas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माता
माता माता. See p. 764, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातापितृ
मातापितृ माता-पितृ, माता-मह, &c. See<BR>p. 765, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माति|मातिः
माति माति, मातुर, &c. See p. 764,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुल|मातुलः
मातुल मातुल. See p. 764, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलङ्ग|मातुलंग
मातुलङ्ग मातुलङ्ग or मातुलिङ्ग or मा-<BR>तुलुङ्ग, अस्, m. (the original form is probably मा-<BR>तुलुङ्ग), a citron tree; (आ or ई), f. another species<BR>of citron tree, sweet lime; (अम्), n. a citron; (ac-<BR>cording to a commentator मातुलङ्ग = रुद्धक,<BR>perhaps for रुचक.)<BR>—मातुलुङ्ग-फल, अम्, n.<BR>the fruit of the above tree.<BR>—मातुलुङ्ग-रस, अस्,<BR>m. the juice of the above tree.<BR>—मातुलुङ्गासव<BR>(˚ग-आस्˚), अस्, m. a liquor distilled from the above<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलुङ्गक|मातुलुङ्गकः
मातुलुङ्गक, अस्, m. = मातुलुङ्ग; (इका), f.<BR>the wild citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलानी
मातुलानी मातुलानी. See p. 764, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृ
मातृ मातृ. See p. 764, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृक|मातृकः
मातृक मातृक. See p. 765, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्य
मात्य मात्य, see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्र|मात्रं|मात्रः
मात्र मात्र, मात्रक, मात्रिक. See p. 765,<BR>col. 3, and p. 766, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर
मात्सर मात्सर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मत्सर),<BR>selfish, envious, jealous, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सरिक
मात्सरिक, अस्, ई, अम्, envious, jealous, spiteful,<BR>malicious; showing envy or jealousy, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर्य|मात्सर्यं|मात्सर्य्य|मात्सर्य्यं
मात्सर्य, अम्, n. envy, jealousy, malice, spite,<BR>(मात्सर्यं कृ, to show jealousy); displeasure,<BR>dissatisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्य
मात्स्य मात्स्य, अस्, -सी (?) , अम् (fr. मत्स्य),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">Page0768-c+ 75</a>]<BR>fishy, coming from or belonging to a fish, fish-like<BR>(e. g. मात्स्यं रूपम्, a fish-like form, the form<BR>or shape of a fish); (अस्), m., N. of a king of the<BR>Matsyas; of a Ṛṣi.<BR>—मात्स्य-पुराण, अम्, n. =<BR>मत्स्य-पुराण, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यक
मात्स्यक, अस्, ई, अम्, = मात्स्य, fishy, relating<BR>to a fish; [cf. पौण्ड्र-म्˚; cf. also Hib. measach,<BR>‘fishy.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यगन्ध
मात्स्यगन्ध, आस्, m. pl. (fr. मत्स्य-गन्ध),<BR>N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यिक|मात्स्यिकः
मात्स्यिक, अस्, m. a fisherman; (wrongly read<BR>मात्सिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्येय
मात्स्येय, आस्, m. pl. the Matsya people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथ|माथः
माथ माथ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. मथ्), churn-<BR>ing, stirring; hurting, injuring, killing, destruction,<BR>annihilation; a way, road; [cf. माठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथव
माथव माथव, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic;<BR>[cf. माधव.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथितिक
माथितिक माथितिक, an adj. fr. मथित<BR>by Pāṇ. V. 3, 83, Vārttika 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथुर|माथुरः
माथुर माथुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मथुर),<BR>coming from or belonging to Mathurā, an inhabitant<BR>of Mathurā; composed by Mathura, related to Ma-<BR>thura; composed by Mathura-nātha (e. g. माथुरी<BR>टिप्पनी, the commentary of Mathura-nātha); (अस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Citra-gupta and of other persons;<BR>(अम्), n. the gate leading to Mathurā.<BR>—माथुर-<BR>देश्य, अस्, आ, अम्, coming from or belonging to<BR>the country of Mathurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथुरक
माथुरक, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of Ma-<BR>thurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद|मादः
माद माद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मद्), = मद,<BR>drunkenness, intoxication, stupor; joy, delight, exhi-<BR>laration; pride, passion.<BR>—मादानन्द (˚द-आन्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादक|मादकः
मादक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt. 2. मद्),<BR>intoxicating, causing intoxication, stupefying; exhi-<BR>larating, gladdening; (अस्), m. a gallinule (= दा-<BR>त्यूह).<BR>—मादक-त्व, अम्, n. the property or<BR>state of causing intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादन|मादनं|मादनः
मादन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt. 2. मद्),<BR>intoxicating, stupefying, maddening; gladdening,<BR>exhilarating; (अस्), m. the god of love; Vanguiera<BR>Spinosa; the thorn-apple; (ई), f., N. of two plants,<BR>= माकन्दी, = विजया; (अम्), n. the act of intoxi-<BR>cating, intoxication, inebriation; exhilaration, the act<BR>of delighting; cloves; ‘the stupefier,’ epithet of a<BR>mythical weapon, (in this sense also read मदन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादनीय|मादनीयं
मादनीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मादन above), intoxi-<BR>cating, inebriating; (अम्), n. an intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादयित्नु
मादयित्नु or मादयिष्णु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Caus.<BR>of rt. 2. मद्), Ved. intoxicating, inebriating; glad-<BR>dening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादायन
मादायन, अस्, m. (fr. मद), a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादिन्
मादिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. Caus. of rt. 2. मद्), intoxicat-<BR>ing, stupefying; gladdening; [cf. गन्ध-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादुघ
मादुघ मादुघ, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the<BR>plant called Madugha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादुर्णा
मादुर्णा मादुर्णा, f., N. of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृश्
मादृश् मादृश्, क्, क्, क् (fr. 3. म + 2. दृश्),<BR>like me, resembling me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृक्ष
मादृक्ष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. म + दृक्ष), =<BR>मादृश below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृश|मादृशः
मादृश, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 3. म + दृश), like me,<BR>resembling me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्य
माद्य माद्य, incorrectly for मान्द्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रक|माद्रकः
माद्रक माद्रक, अस्, m. (fr. मद्र), a<BR>prince of the Madras; (इका), f. a woman belonging<BR>to the Madra nation, (more properly मद्रिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रकूलक
माद्रकूलक (fr. मद्र-कूल), see Gaṇa Dhū-<BR>mādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रनगर
माद्र-नगर (fr. मद्र-नगर), see Scholiast<BR>on Pāṇ. VII. 3, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रवती
माद्रवती, f. ‘princess of the Madras,’ N. of the<BR>wife of Pari-kṣit; Mādrī the second wife of Pāṇḍu.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-a" target="_blank">Page0769-a+ 80</a>]<BR>—माद्रवती-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son of the Madra<BR>princess,’ epithet of either Nakula or Saha-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्री
माद्री, f. ‘princess of the Madras,’ N. of the<BR>second wife of Pāṇḍu and mother of the twins Na-<BR>kula and Saha-deva, (they were said to be the two<BR>youngest of the sons of Pāṇḍu, q. v., but were really<BR>the sons of Mādrī by the Aśvins, cf. नकुल, कुन्ती);<BR>the wife of Saha-deva; wife of Kroṣṭu; wife of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; a species of plant (= अति-विषा).<BR>—माद्रि-<BR>नन्दन, अस्, m. (माद्रि for माद्री to suit the<BR>metre, cf. कुन्ति-नन्दन), ‘son of Mādrī,’ epi-<BR>thet of either Nakula or Saha-deva.<BR>—माद्री-पति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘husband of Mādrī,’ epithet of Pāṇḍu.<BR>—माद्री-पृथा-पति, इस्, m. ‘husband of Mādrī<BR>and Pṛthā,’ N. of Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रेय|माद्रेयः
माद्रेय, अस्, m. ‘son of Mādrī,’ epithet of either<BR>Nakula or Saha-deva; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रुकस्थलक
माद्रुकस्थलक माद्रुकस्थलक (fr. मद्रु-<BR>क-स्थली), see Gaṇa Dhūmādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव|माधवः
माधव माधव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु), made<BR>of honey, honey-like, sweet; relating to spring,<BR>vernal; belonging or peculiar to the descendants<BR>of Madhu, i. e. the Yādavas, (माधवे ऽहनि, on a<BR>spring day; माधवी लक्ष्मीः, vernal beauty or,<BR>in Hari-vaṃśa 9597, the fortune of the Yādavas;<BR>माधवी देवी, N. of the earth); (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of the second month of spring; the month Vai-<BR>śākha (= April-May); spring; a son or descendant<BR>of Madhu, a man of the race of Yadu; an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa (Viṣṇu); of Paraśu-rāma (as an incarnation<BR>of Viṣṇu); of Indra; of a son of the third Manu;<BR>of one of the seven sages under Manu Bhautya; of<BR>another ancient sage; of a leader of the Pañca-rātra<BR>sect; of the author of the Rug-viniścaya; of the<BR>father of Dādābhāī and grandfather of the astrological<BR>writer Nārāyaṇa; of the father of the commentator<BR>Someśvara; of various other persons; Bassia Lati-<BR>folia or a species of leguminous plant, = कृष्ण-<BR>मुद्ग; (ई), f. honey-sugar, clayed or candied sugar;<BR>an intoxicating drink made of honey, mead; ‘spring-<BR>flower,’ Gærtnera Racemosa [cf. वासन्ती]; a kind<BR>of panic-grass; sacred basil; = मिसि (according to<BR>some, a sort of dentifrice); a procuress, bawd; afflu-<BR>ence in cattle or herds; a woman of the race of<BR>Madhu or Yadu (e. g. An-antā, wife of Janam-ejaya;<BR>Sampriyā, wife of Vidūratha; Kuntī, wife of Pāṇḍu);<BR>N. of Dākṣāyaṇī in Śrī-śaila; of Durgā; of a<BR>Mātṛ attending on Skanda; of a daughter of Yayāti;<BR>of a commentary (probably named after the author<BR>Mādhava); (अम्), n. sweetness; (in Schol. on Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 4, 129, a fem. form माधवा is given, agreeing<BR>with तनूः.)<BR>—माधव-कर, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>medical writer.<BR>—माधव-काल-निर्णय, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a work written by Mādhavācārya.<BR>—माधव-<BR>गुप्त, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—माधव-चरित, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—माधव-देव, अस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—माधव-निदान, अम्, n., N. of a work by<BR>Mādhava (= रुग्-विनिश्चय).<BR>—माधव-पण्डित,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a scholar.<BR>—माधव-प्राची, f., N.<BR>of a place.<BR>—माधव-भट्ट, अस्, m., N. of various<BR>persons (= माधवाचार्य).<BR>—माधव-भिक्षु,<BR>उस्, m. a proper N. (= माधवाश्रम).<BR>—मा-<BR>धव-मागध, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—माधव-<BR>यतीन्द्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—माधव-योगिन्,<BR>ई, m. a proper N.<BR>—माधव-रामानन्द-सरस्-<BR>वती (˚म-आन्˚), m., N. of the teacher of the com-<BR>mentator Śivānanda.<BR>—माधव-वल्ली, f. Gærtnera<BR>Racemosa.<BR>—माधव-श्री, ईस्, f. the beauty or glory<BR>of spring.<BR>—माधव-सिंह and माधव-सेन,<BR>अस्, m., N. of two kings.<BR>—माधव-सेना-राजन्,<BR>आ, m. ‘king of the army of spring’ or ‘of sweet-<BR>ness, N. of a king.<BR>—माधव-सोमयाजिन्, ई, m.<BR>a proper N. (= माधवाचार्य).<BR>—माधवाचार्य<BR>(˚व-आच्˚), अस्, m. ‘the learned Mādhava’ or ‘the<BR>teacher Mādhava,’ N. of a celebrated scholar, son of<BR>Māyaṇa and brother of Sāyaṇācārya and Bhoga-<BR>nātha, q. q. v. v., (he is sometimes called simply Mā-<BR>dhava, and regarded, together with Sāyaṇa, as, author<BR>of the celebrated commentary on the Ṛg-veda; also<BR>author of the Kāla-nirṇaya, of the Nyāya-mālā-vistara,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">Page0769-b+ 79</a>]<BR>of the commentary Parāśara-smṛti-vyākhyā, of the<BR>Saṅkṣepa-śaṅkara-vijaya, of the Sarva-darśana-saṅ-<BR>graha.)<BR>—माधवानन्द-काव्य (˚व-आन्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a poem by Nanda-paṇḍita.<BR>—माध-<BR>वानल (˚व-अन्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मा-<BR>धवानलाख्यान (˚व-अनल-आख्˚), अम्, n., N.<BR>of an erotic work by the above.<BR>—माधवाश्रम<BR>(˚व-आश्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—माधवी-लता, f.<BR>the creeper Gærtnera Racemosa (bearing white fra-<BR>grant flowers).<BR>—माधवी-वन, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>forest.<BR>—माधवेन्द्र-पुरी (˚व-इन्˚), m., N. of<BR>an author.<BR>—माधवेष्टा (˚व-इष्˚), f. a species<BR>of tuberous plant (= वाराही-कन्द); an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>—माधवोचित (˚व-उच्˚), अम्, n. a kind<BR>of perfume (= कक्कोलक).<BR>—माधवोद्भव<BR>(˚व-उद्˚), अस्, m. a species of plant (= राजादनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवक|माधवकः
माधवक, अस्, m. a spirituous liquor (prepared<BR>from honey or from the blossoms of the Bassia Lati-<BR>folia); (इका), f. Gærtnera Racemosa; a kind of<BR>metre, four times ˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯<BR>˘˘¯˘¯¯; N. of a woman; a female attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीय
माधवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging or<BR>devoted to Mādhava or to Mādhavācārya; composed<BR>by him.<BR>—माधवीय-धातु-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a<BR>treatise on Sanskrit roots by Sāyaṇa (dedicated to his<BR>brother Mādhava).<BR>—माधवीय-वेदार्थ-प्र-<BR>काश, N. of Sāyaṇa's commentary on the Ṛg-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव्य
माधव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Madhu,<BR>see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्व|माध्वः
1. माध्व, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु), sweet; (ई),<BR>f. a kind of spirituous liquor; = माधवी, Gærtnera<BR>Racemosa; = माधुर-कण्टक, a kind of fish;<BR>(ई), m. du., Ved. ‘possessing or loving sweetness,’ an<BR>epithet of the Aśvins; (Sāy.) = मधु-पूर्ण-पात्र-<BR>युक्तौ; (in this last sense perhaps fr. a base मा-<BR>ध्वि.)<BR>—माध्वी-मधुरा, f. a species of date<BR>(= मधुर-खर्जुरिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वक|माध्वकं
माध्वक, अम्, n. = माधवक, an intoxicating<BR>beverage prepared from honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्विक|माध्विकः
माध्विक, अस्, m. a person who collects honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीक|माध्वीकं
माध्वीक, अम्, n. a kind of intoxicating drink<BR>distilled from the blossoms of the Bassia Latifolia;<BR>wine, spirit distilled from grapes; [cf. मधु-म्˚.]<BR>—माध्वीक-फल, अस्, n. a species of cocoa-nut<BR>(= मधु-नालिकेरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुक|माधुकः
माधुक माधुक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधुक),<BR>coming from or belonging to the Madhuka tree;<BR>‘mead-maker,’ an epithet of the Maireyakas or of a<BR>particular mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकर
माधुकर माधुकर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु-<BR>कर), coming from a bee or from honey, belonging<BR>to a bee, resembling a bee, (माधुकरी वृत्तिः, a<BR>mode or course of life resembling that of a bee), be-<BR>longing to honey, &c.; (ई), f. gathering alms after the<BR>manner of a bee by going from door to door; alms<BR>obtained from five different places by the third class<BR>of religious mendicants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकर्णिक
माधुकर्णिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु-कर्ण),<BR>see Gaṇa Kumudādi 2. to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुच्छन्दस
माधुच्छन्दस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु-च्छन्-<BR>दस्), Ved. relating to or coming from Madhu-cchan-<BR>das; (अस्), m. a patronymic of Agha-marṣaṇa; of<BR>Jetṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुपर्किक
माधुपर्किक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु-पर्क),<BR>relating to the Madhu-parka; offered or presented<BR>as a token of respect to a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुमत
माधुमत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु-मत्), be-<BR>longing to or descended from Madhu-mat; (आस्), m.<BR>pl. the inhabitants of Kaśmīra; belonging to the<BR>river Madhu-matī, (माधुमतं जलम्, water<BR>from the Madhu-matī.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुमतक
माधुमतक (fr. मधु-मत्), see Gaṇa Kac-<BR>chādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूकर
माधूकर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधु-कर),<BR>gathered or collected after the manner of bees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर|माधुरं
माधुर माधुर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधुर),<BR>composed by Madhura; relating to Madhurā; (ई),<BR>f. sweetness, amiableness; mead; spirituous or vinous<BR>liquor; (अम्), n. the blossom of Jasminum Zambac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर्य|माधुर्यं|माधुर्य्य|माधुर्य्यं
माधुर्य, अस्, आ or -री (?), अम् (fr. मधुर),<BR>speaking sweetly or kindly; (अम्), n. sweetness,<BR>pleasantness, attractiveness, gracefulness; kindness,<BR>friendliness, amiability; (in rhetoric) the succession<BR>of single words in a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूक
माधूक माधूक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मधूक),<BR>made from Bassia Latifolia; (according to Kullūka)<BR>= मधुर-भाषिन्, sweetly speaking, kindly<BR>speaking; an epithet of the Maitreyakas (a mixed<BR>caste; cf. माधुक, col. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूची
माधूची माधूची, m. du., Ved. (probably<BR>formed after the analogy of माध्वी, see under<BR>1. माध्व, col. 2), an epithet of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूल
माधूल माधूल, अस्, m. (fr. मधूल), a<BR>patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्य
माध्य माध्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मध्य),<BR>middle, central, mid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यन्दिन|माध्यंदिन|माध्यन्दिनं|माध्यंदिनः
माध्यन्दिन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मध्यन्-दिन),<BR>Ved. belonging to midday, meridional, midday,<BR>(माध्यन्दिने सवने, at the midday rite); middle,<BR>central; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a branch of the Vājasa-<BR>neyins and of an astronomical school who fixed the<BR>starting-point of planetary movements at noon; (अम्),<BR>n., scil. तीर्थ, N. of a Tīrtha; [cf. माध्यन्दि-<BR>नीयक.]<BR>—माध्यन्दिन-युग, Ved. belonging<BR>to the midday oblation.<BR>—माध्यन्दिन-शाखा, f.<BR>the school of the Mādhyandinas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यन्दिनायन|माध्यंदिनायन
माध्यन्दिनायन, अस्, m. probably a patro-<BR>nymic, N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यन्दिनि|माध्यंदिनि
माध्यन्दिनि, इस्, m. a patronymic, N. of a<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यन्दिनीय|माध्यंदिनीय
माध्यन्दिनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, usual or customary<BR>at the midday oblation (Ved.); ‘belonging to the<BR>school of the Mādhyandinas,’ an epithet of Nārā-<BR>yaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यन्दिनीयक|माध्यंदिनीयक
माध्यन्दिनीयक, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यन्दिनेय|माध्यंदिनेय
माध्यन्दिनेय = माध्यन्दिन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यम|माध्यमं
माध्यम माध्यम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मध्यम),<BR>relating to the middle, middlemost, middle, central;<BR>middle-born; (आस्), m. pl. epithet of the Ṛṣis to<BR>whom the middle portion (Maṇḍala II — VII) of the<BR>Ṛg-veda Saṃhitā is attributed; N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमक
माध्यमक, अस्, इका, अम्, = माध्यमिक;<BR>(इका), f. epithet of the middle section of the Kā-<BR>ṭhaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमकेय
माध्यमकेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people, =<BR>मध्यमकेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमस्थ्य
माध्यमस्थ्य, अम्, n. (fr. मध्यम-स्थ),<BR>the state of standing or being in the middle, see<BR>Gaṇa Brāhmaṇādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 124; [cf. मा-<BR>ध्यस्थ्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमिक
माध्यमिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or belonging<BR>to the middle, middlemost, middle; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a Buddhist school; of a people in the central<BR>part of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमिनेय
माध्यमिनेय, अस्, m. (fr. मध्यमा), a<BR>metronymic, see Gaṇa Kalyāṇyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1,<BR>126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ|माध्यस्थं
माध्यस्थ माध्यस्थ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मध्य-<BR>स्थ), being in a middle state, indifferent, impartial,<BR>neutral; (अम्), n. middle state or condition; indif-<BR>ference, impartiality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ्य|माध्यस्थ्यं
माध्यस्थ्य, अम्, n. ‘the state of standing in<BR>the middle or between two,’ indifference, impartiality,<BR>neutrality; the office of umpire, mediation, inter-<BR>cession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्याह्निक
माध्याह्निक माध्याह्निक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>मध्याह्न), belonging to midday, taking place<BR>at noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्व|माध्वः
माध्व 2. माध्व, अस्, m. (for 1. see col. 2),<BR>an adherent of Madhva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्
मान् मान् (connected with rt. मन्), cl.<BR>1. P. मानति, &c., to honour, respect,<BR>revere, worship; cl. 10. P. मानयति, &c. (pro-<BR>perly Caus. of rt. मन्), to honour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान 1. मान, अस्, m. (fr. rt. मन्), opinion,<BR>conception, (also अम्, n.); a good opinion of one's<BR>self, conceit, self-reliance, self-confidence, arrogance,<BR>pride, haughtiness; honour, respect, consideration,<BR>(also exceptionally अम्, n.); regard for others, de-<BR>monstration of respect, paying honour; a wounded<BR>sense of honour; anger or indignation excited by<BR>jealousy (especially in women), female caprice, sulki-<BR>ness, hatred; object, purpose, will (Ved.); (in astro-<BR>logy) an epithet of the tenth house; a blockhead (?);<BR>an agent (?); a barbarian (?); N. of the father of<BR>Agastya (Ved.); (आस्), m. pl. the family or descend-<BR>ants of Māna (Ved.).<BR>—मान-कलह, अस्, m. any<BR>quarrel caused by pride or jealousy, rivalry, jealousy;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—मान-कलि, इस्, m.<BR>quarrelling or dissension caused by pride, mutual<BR>disdain or ill-will.<BR>—मान-कृत्, त्, त्, त्, showing<BR>honour or respect (to others).<BR>—मान-क्षति, इस्,<BR>f. a wound inflicted on the honour (of another),<BR>injury to reputation, wounding or hurting pride,<BR>humiliation.<BR>—मान-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. injury to<BR>honour or pride.<BR>—मान-तस्, ind. from honour,<BR>through honour, for honour's sake.<BR>—मान-तुङ्ग,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मान-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>haughtiness, arrogance, &c.; see 1. मान above.<BR> — 1. मान-द, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. मान + 2. द),<BR>giving honour, paying honour, showing respect;<BR>honour-giver, pride-inspirer, (a respectful mode of<BR>addressing husbands and lovers, usually in voc. sing.);<BR>(अस्), m. a mystical epithet of the letter आ; (आस्), m.<BR>pl., N. of a people [cf. माल-द]; (आ), f. epithet of<BR>the second Kalā or digit of the moon; (अम्), n.,<BR>scil. अस्त्र, epithet of a particular magical weapon.<BR> — 2. मान-द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मान + 3. द),<BR>destroying arrogance or pride.<BR>—मान-धन, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, rich in honour.<BR>—मान-ध्मात, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, puffed up with pride.<BR>—मान-पर, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, wholly addicted to pride, intensely proud, very<BR>arrogant (see पर); (आ), f., N. of a woman.<BR>—मान-परिखण्डन, अम्, n. loss of honour,<BR>wounding or offending pride, humiliation.<BR>—मान-<BR>प्राण, अस्, आ, अम्, one to whom honour is (as dear)<BR>as life, valuing honour or reputation as highly as life.<BR>—मान-भङ्ग, अस्, m. loss of honour, injury to<BR>reputation, humiliation.<BR>—मान-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, pos-<BR>sessing pride, (according to Malli-nātha = अहङ्-<BR>कारिन्.)<BR>—मान-मनोहर, N. of a work.<BR>—मा-<BR>नमनोहर-कर, अस्, m. the author of the above<BR>(= वाग्-ईश्वर).<BR>—मान-मय, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>particular article of luxury (?) mentioned in Hari-vaṃśa<BR>8455.<BR>—मान-महत्, आन्, अती, अत्, great in pride,<BR>extremely proud.<BR>—मान-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>honour or pride, proud, haughty, disdainful, high-<BR>spirited; (अती), f. a haughty or disdainful woman<BR>(angry from wounded pride or jealousy).<BR>—मान-<BR>वर्जिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—मान-<BR>वर्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, stripped of honour; humble,<BR>lowly; defamatory, slanderous, abusive.<BR>—मान-<BR>वर्धन, अस्, ई, अम्, enhancing honour, increasing<BR>respect.<BR>—मान-सार, अस्, m., N. of a king of<BR>Mālava.<BR>—मान-सिंह, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मा-<BR>न-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, destroying pride or honour,<BR>humbling, an humbler, abaser.<BR>—मानानन्द (˚न-<BR>आन्˚), अस्, m., N. of an author of a Durgā-mantra.<BR>—मानापमाने (˚न-अप्˚), n. du. honour and<BR>dishonour.<BR>—मानार्ह (˚न-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, worthy<BR>of honour, entitled to respect.<BR>—मानासक्त (˚न-<BR>आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, addicted to pride, haughty, arro-<BR>gant, proud.<BR>—मानोत्सेक-पराक्रम-व्यसनिन्<BR>(˚न-उत्˚), ई, इनी, इ, possessing pride, haughtiness,<BR>prowess, and intense diligence.<BR>—मानोन्नति (˚न-<BR>उन्˚), इस्, f. the height of honour, high honour,<BR>great respect.<BR>—मानोन्माद (˚न-उन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>the infatuation of pride, infatuated or insane arro-<BR>gance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानन|माननं
मानन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt. मन्),<BR>honouring, serving as a honorarium or token of<BR>respect; (आ, अम्), f. n. the act of honouring, paying<BR>honour, showing respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननीय|माननीयं
माननीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured, deserving<BR>honour from any one (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानयितव्य
मानयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be honoured or<BR>respected, deserving honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानयितृ
मानयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, honouring, respecting, an<BR>honourer, one who honours or respects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानित
मानित, अस्, आ, अम्, honoured, respected; (अम्),<BR>n. honouring, showing honour or respect, honour.<BR>—मानित-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन्. See s. v., p. 771, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्य|मान्यः
मान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be respected or honoured,<BR>worthy of honour, honourable, respectable, venerable,<BR>held in honour; a patronymic (Ved.); = मैत्रा-<BR>वरुणि, author of Ṛg-veda VIII. 56, (in the last two<BR>senses fr. मान, father of Agastya); (आ), f. Trigo-<BR>nella Corniculata, (wrongly for माल्या.)<BR>—मान्य-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. honourableness, respectability, worthiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान 2. मान, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. मा), a<BR>building, edifice, house, dwelling (Ved.); a prepara-<BR>tion, decoction, (perhaps used in this sense with<BR>reference to the Soma plant in Ṛg-veda X. 144, 5);<BR>(अम्), n. the act of forming or making (Ved.);<BR>form, appearance (Ved.); the act of measuring or<BR>meting, measure in general, dimension, computation<BR>of time, &c. (e. g. नृ-म्˚, a man's height; अन्तर-<BR>म्˚, difference of dimension; cf. तारका-म्˚, शत-<BR>म्˚, गिरि-म्˚, छन्दो-म्˚); any instrument for<BR>measuring, a measuring-rod, measure, rule, standard<BR>[cf. ऊर्ध्व-म्˚, कूट-म्˚]; (Ved.) a particular<BR>measure or weight (= कृष्णल or रक्तिका, a<BR>Guñjā seed; according to the commentators 100<BR>Mānas = 5 Palas or Paṇas, or, according to others,<BR>1/4 or 1/8 of a Khārī); likeness, resemblance (= उप-<BR>मान); proof, demonstration, means of proof (=<BR>प्र-माण, q. v.).<BR>—३. मान-द, अस्, आ, अम्, mea-<BR>suring.<BR>—मान-दण्ड, अस्, m. a measuring-rod.<BR>—मान-धानिका, f. = कर्कटी, a cucumber.<BR>—मा-<BR>नम्-पच, अस्, आ, अम्, see Schol. on Vopa-deva<BR>XXVI. 55; [cf. अल्पम्-प्˚, मितम्-प्˚.]<BR>—मान-<BR>योग, अस्, m. the correct mode of measuring and<BR>weighing (Manu IX. 330).<BR>—मान-रन्ध्रा, f. a<BR>kind of water-clock or clepsydra, a perforated copper<BR>vessel which, placed in water and gradually filling,<BR>serves to measure time, (according to some, मान-<BR>रन्ध्री; cf. ताम्री.)<BR>—मान-सूत्र, अम्, n. a<BR>measuring-cord [cf. प्रमाण-सूत्र]; a cord or<BR>chain of gold or some other material worn round<BR>the body.<BR>—मानाङ्गुल-महातन्त्र (˚न-अङ्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—मानाध्याय (˚न-<BR>अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘chapter on measurement’ (of time),<BR>N. of the fourteenth chapter of the Sūrya-siddhānta.<BR>—मानोन्मानिका (˚न-उन्˚), f., see Gaṇa Śāka-<BR>pārthivādi, Siddhānta-kaumudī on Pāṇ. II. 1, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानक|मानकं
मानक (at the end of an adj. comp.) = 2. मान,<BR>measure, &c.; (अस्, अम्), m. n. = माणक, Arum<BR>Indicum, a plant having an edible root; (इका), f. a<BR>particular spirituous or vinous liquor; = माणिका, a<BR>particular weight (= 2 Añjalis, = 8 Palas; according<BR>to others, the fourth or eighth part of a Khāri).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानःशिल
मानःशिल मानःशिल, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मनः-<BR>शिला), consisting of realgar or red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानन|माननं
मानन मानन, &c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव|मानवः
मानव मानव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मनु), de-<BR>scended from man or from Manu, belonging or<BR>proper to man or Manu, human; (Ved.) propitious<BR>to men; (अस्), m. a human being, man; a lad, boy,<BR>(for माणव, q. v.); a patronymic of Nābhā-<BR>nediṣṭha; of Śāryāta; of Cakṣus; of Nahuṣa;<BR>of Bhṛgu; of Su-dyumna; of Karūṣa; of Deva-<BR>hūti; (आस्), m. pl. the children of men, mankind;<BR>the subjects (of a king); N. of a school of the black<BR>Yajur-veda; (ई), f. a daughter of man or Manu, a<BR>woman; N. of a goddess (executing the commands<BR>of the eleventh Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī);<BR>N. of one of the eleven Vidyā-devīs; (अम्), n. a<BR>man's length (as a measure, Ved.); = मानव-<BR>कल्प-सूत्र, q. v.; N. of a Sāman; a particular<BR>mulct or fine; [cf. Goth. manna, fr. mannan,<BR>perhaps for manvan; Germ. Mann, ‘a man.’]<BR>—मानव-कल्प-सूत्र or मानव-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a well-known Sūtra work on Kalpa or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">Page0770-c+ 78</a>]<BR>ritual (see मनु).<BR>—मानव-देव, अस्, m. ‘man-<BR>god, god among men,’ a king, prince.<BR>—मानव-<BR>धर्म-शास्त्र, अम्, n., N. of the code of laws<BR>attributed to Manu (see मनु-संहिता).<BR>—मानव-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘man-lord,’ a king, sovereign.<BR>—मा-<BR>नवाचल (˚व-अच्˚), अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—मानवाद्य (˚व-आद्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Sāman.<BR>—मानवेन्द्र (˚व-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘man-chief, man-<BR>lord,’ a king.<BR>—मानवोत्तर (˚व-उत्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Sāman.<BR>—मानवोपपुराण (˚व-उप्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR>—मानवौघ (˚व-<BR>ओघ), with गुरु, epithet of a particular class of<BR>composers of mystical prayers [cf. the kindred words<BR>Divyaugha, Siddhaugha].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवस्य
मानवस्य, Nom. P. A. मानवस्यति, -ते, &c.,<BR>Ved. to act like men; (Sāy.) to wish for men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवस्यत्
मानवस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, acting like men;<BR>(Sāy.) wishing for men, i. e. priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवीय
मानवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, descended or derived from<BR>Manu; (अम्), n. a particular fine [cf. मानव].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवेय
मानवेय, अस्, आ, अम्, descended or derived from<BR>Manu; (अस्), m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव्य|मानव्यं
मानव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Manu, Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 1, 105; (आयनी), f., see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 18; (अम्),<BR>n. a number of boys, assemblage of youths, (for<BR>माणव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवर्तिक
मानवर्तिक मानवर्तिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a people; (also read मानवर्जक, मानवलक,<BR>गव-वर्तिल; cf. मालवर्ति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस मानस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मनस्), be-<BR>longing to the mind or spirit, mental, spiritual, (as<BR>opposed to शारीर, corporeal; मानसं तीर्थम्,<BR>a spiritual bathing-place or the lake Mānasa so called);<BR>expressed only in the mind (e. g. मानसं स्तोत्रम्,<BR>a silent hymn of praise), tacit, implied; present in<BR>the mind, only to be conceived in the mind, (आभ-<BR>रणैर् मानसैः, with every conceivable orna-<BR>ment); dwelling on the lake Mānasa, (in this sense<BR>fr. मानस, अम्, n. the lake Mānasa, see below);<BR>(अस्), m. a form of Viṣṇu; N. of a Nāga; of a<BR>class of ascetics; of a son of Vapuṣ-mat; of a pre-<BR>ceptor; (आस्), m. pl. a particular class of Manes<BR>(regarded as sons of Vasiṣṭha); epithet of the<BR>Vaiśyas in Śāka-dvīpa; (ई), f., N. of one of the<BR>sixteen Vidyā-devīs [cf. महा-मानसिका]; (अम्),<BR>n. the mental powers, mind, spirit, the seat or faculty<BR>of reason and feeling, heart, soul, (in these senses<BR>frequently at the end of a comp., cf. भय-सन्-<BR>त्रस्त-म्˚); tacit or implied consent (in law); N.<BR>of a sacred lake and place of pilgrimage on mount<BR>Kailāsa in the Himālaya mountains, (the native place<BR>of the wild geese or swans; constant allusions are<BR>made to this lake in Hindū poetry, and the Haṃsa<BR>or Rāja-haṃsa, a kind of wild goose, is described as<BR>migrating to its shores every year at the breeding<BR>season); a kind of salt.<BR>—मानस-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>frequenting lake Mānasa; (ई), m. a wild goose or<BR>swan.<BR>—मानस-जन्मन्, आ, m. ‘mind-born,’ the<BR>god of love; [cf. मनो-जन्मन्.]<BR>—मानस-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. thoughtfulness, spirituality, the belonging<BR>to spirit, fulfilment of anything in mere thought.<BR>—मानस-नयन, अम्, n. ‘guidance to the lake<BR>Mānasa,’ N. of a logical work by Jīvana.<BR>—मानस-<BR>नयन-प्रसादनी, f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>above work.<BR>—मानस-रुज्, क्, f., Ved. mental or<BR>spiritual disease.<BR>—मानस-वेग, अस्, आ, अम्, swift<BR>as spirit (i. e. thought); (अस्), m., N. of a king.<BR>—मानस-शुच्, क्, f., Ved. mental sorrow or grief.<BR>—मानस-सन्ताप, अस्, m. mental anguish, sorrow<BR>of heart.<BR>—मानसालय (˚स-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘dwelling<BR>on the lake Mānasa,’ a wild goose or swan; [cf.<BR>मानसौकस्.]<BR>—मानसोत्तर (˚स-उत्˚), अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a mountain range; [cf. उत्तर-मानस.]<BR>—मानसोल्लास (˚स-उल्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Vedānta<BR>work by Sureśvara Ācārya or Dakṣiṇa Ācārya, a<BR>disciple of Śaṅkara Ācārya.<BR>—मानसोल्लास-प्र-<BR>बन्ध and मानसोल्लास-वृत्तान्त and मान-<BR>सोल्लास-वृत्तान्त-विलास, अस्, m. names of commen-<BR>taries on the above work.<BR>—मानसौकस् (˚स-ओक्˚),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">Page0771-a+ 75</a>]<BR>आस्, आस्, अस्, dwelling on the lake Mānasa; (आस्), m.<BR>a wild goose or swan, the Rāja-haṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0770-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसायन
मानसायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Manas,<BR>see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसिक|मानसिकं|मानसिकः
मानसिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मनस् or fr. मा-<BR>नस), mental, spiritual; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस्य
मानस्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Manas, see<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 1, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस्कृत
मानस्कृत मानस्-कृत, अस्, m., Ved. (ac-<BR>cording to Mahī-dhara) = पूजाया अभिमानस्य<BR>वा कर्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस्थली
मानस्थली मान-स्थली, f., मानस्थलक,<BR>see Pāṇ. IV. 2, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानाङ्क
मानाङ्क मानाङ्क, अस्, m. (perhaps for मा-<BR>लाङ्क), N. of the author of the Vṛndā-vana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानायन
मानायन मानायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानाय्य
मानाय्य मानाय्य, मानाय्यायनी, see Gaṇa<BR>Gargādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 105, and Gaṇa Lohitādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिक
मानिक मानिक = मानिन् in पण्डित-म्˚,<BR>q. v. (For मानिका see मानक, p. 770, col. 2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानित
मानित मानित. See p. 770, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन् मानिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. rt. मन् or fr. 1.<BR>मान), thinking, being of opinion, (in these and<BR>the following senses often at the end of comps.);<BR>considering, regarding, taking for; fancying or ima-<BR>gining one's self, taking one's self for [cf. पण्डित-<BR>म्˚]; fancying that one possesses (e. g. क्षमता-<BR>मानिन्, fancying that one possesses ability); being<BR>regarded or taken for; honouring, esteeming highly;<BR>having a high opinion of one's self, proud, haughty,<BR>proud of anything (e. g. धनतो मानी नरः, a<BR>man proud of his wealth); maintaining one's honour,<BR>proud (in a good sense); highly honoured or esteemed;<BR>disdainful, angry, resentful, sulky; (ई), m. a lion;<BR>(इनी), f. an angry or disdainful woman or one<BR>offended with her lover; a species of odoriferous<BR>plant (= फली, i. e. प्रियङ्गु); N. of a daughter<BR>of Vidūra-stha and wife of Ṛājya-vardhana; a kind<BR>of metre, (probably incorrect for मालिनी.)<BR>—मानि-<BR>ता, f. or मानि-त्व, अम्, n. (at the end of a comp.) the<BR>fancying that one possesses, imagining or fancying one's<BR>self, taking one's self for (e. g. अज्ञाने ज्ञान-मानिता,<BR>the fancying when in ignorance that one has know-<BR>ledge); haughtiness, pride; honouring, paying respect;<BR>the being honoured, receiving honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्ध
मानिन्ध मानिन्ध, अस्, m., N. of an astro-<BR>nomer, (also read मनिन्ध; cf. मणित्थ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुतन्तव्य
मानुतन्तव्य मानुतन्तव्य, अस्, m. (fr. मनु-<BR>तन्तु), Ved. a patronymic of Aikādaśākṣa; [cf.<BR>मारुतन्तव्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष|मानुषः
मानुष मानुष, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मनुस्),<BR>human, belonging to mankind, appertaining to men;<BR>humane, kind, favourable or propitious to men; (अस्),<BR>m. a man, human being, (often at the end of comps.,<BR>and sometimes with fem. आ, cf. अ-म्˚, अति-म्˚; कार्य-<BR>म्˚, a human being in some sense of the word, incar-<BR>nate in human form); epithet of the signs of the<BR>zodiac Gemini, Virgo, and Libra; (ई), f. a woman;<BR>scil. चिकित्सा, a branch of medicine, the administering<BR>of drugs and herbs (as opposed to आसुरी and दैवी<BR>चिकित्सा); (अम्), n. the manner or ways of men,<BR>condition of man, humanity; the doings or actions<BR>of man, human action or effort, manhood; N. of a<BR>place.<BR>—मानुष-ता, f. or मानुष-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>humanity, the state or condition of man, manhood,<BR>manliness, human existence, man's estate.<BR>—मानु-<BR>ष-प्रधन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fighting for men,<BR>(used in Ṛg-veda 1. 52, 9. as an epithet of the<BR>Maruts).<BR>—मानुष-बुद्ध, अस्, m. a human<BR>Buddha, (opposed to ध्यानि-बुद्ध.)<BR>—मानु-<BR>ष-मांसाद (स-आद), अस्, आ, अम्, eating human<BR>flesh.<BR>—मानुष-राक्षस, अस्, m. a fiend in<BR>human form, a Rākṣasa-like man.<BR>—मानुष-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">Page0771-b+ 73</a>]<BR>लौकिक, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the world of men,<BR>proper for man, human.<BR>—मानुष-सम्भव, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, coming from a man, produced by men.<BR>—मानुषोपेत (˚ष-उप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, joined with<BR>human effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषक
मानुषक, अस्, ई, अम्, human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषीभू
मानुषी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become<BR>man, take human form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्य|मानुष्यं
मानुष्य, अम्, n. (fr. मनुष्य), the being a<BR>man, humanity, manhood, manliness, human nature,<BR>man's estate; (अस्, -षी, अम्), human, manly, belong-<BR>ing to man or humanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यक|मानुष्यकं
मानुष्यक, अस्, ई, अम्, human; (अम्), n. hu-<BR>manity, human condition, human nature; a multi-<BR>tude of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोज्ञक|मानोज्ञकं
मानोज्ञक मानोज्ञक, अम्, n. (fr. मनो-ज्ञ),<BR>beauty, agreeableness, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्तव्य
मान्तव्य मान्तव्य, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Mantu, see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्तव्यायनी
मान्तव्यायनी, f., see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्र
मान्त्र मान्त्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मन्त्र), Ved.<BR>proper or peculiar to Vedic texts, belonging to sacred<BR>texts, relating to mystical verses or spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रवर्णिक
मान्त्रवर्णिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मन्त्र-वर्ण),<BR>contained in the text of a Vedic hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रिक|मांत्रिक|मांत्रिकः|मान्त्रिकः
मान्त्रिक, अस्, m. (fr. मन्त्र), one who recites<BR>a text or spell, one conversant with spells or incan-<BR>tations, an enchanter, sorcerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रित
मान्त्रित मान्त्रित, आस्, m. pl. the descend-<BR>ants of Māntritya, see Pāṇ. IV. 2, III.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रित्य
मान्त्रित्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Mantrita,<BR>see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थ्|मांथ्
मान्थ् मान्थ्, cl. I. P. मान्थति, &c.,<BR>(according to Vopa-deva, Dhātu-pāṭha<BR>III. 9) = rt. मन्थ् or I. मथ्, to hurt, injure, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थ्य
मान्थ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, see Gaṇa Saṅkāśādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थरेषणि
मान्थरेषणि मान्थरेषणि, इस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Manthareṣaṇa, see Schol. on Pāṇ. II.<BR>4, 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थर्य|मांथर्य|मांथर्यं
मान्थर्य मान्थर्य, अम्, n. (fr. मन्थर),<BR>weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थाल
मान्थाल मान्थाल, अस्, m., Ved. a kind of<BR>animal, (according to Mahī-dhara) a species of mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द
मान्द मान्द, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. मन्द् or 2.<BR>मद्), Ved. ‘gladdening,’ an epithet of water in certain<BR>formularies; (अस्, ई, अम्), relating to the higher apsis<BR>of a planet's course; मान्दं कर्म, the process<BR>of correction for the apsis; मान्दम् फलम्, the<BR>equation of the apsis, (in these latter senses fr.<BR>मन्द, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्य|मांद्य|मांद्यं|मान्द्यं
मान्द्य, अम्, n. (fr. मन्द), slowness, sluggish-<BR>ness, laziness; stupidity, torpor; apathy; weakness;<BR>indisposition, illness, sickness; मान्द्यं कृ, to<BR>make one's self ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्र
मान्द्र (fr. मन्द्र), see Gaṇa Chattrādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 4, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्दार|मांदार|मांदारः|मान्दारः
मान्दार मान्दार or मान्दारव, अस्, m. a<BR>species of tree (= मन्दार; cf. मन्दारव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्दार्य
मान्दार्य मान्दार्य (fr. मन्दार), see Gaṇa<BR>Pragadyādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80; perhaps used as a<BR>proper N. in Ṛg-veda 1. 165, 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धातृ|मांधातृ
मान्धातृ मान्धातृ, ता, m. (according to<BR>some fr. माम्, ‘me,’ + धातृ, ‘a drinker,’ this king<BR>having once sucked Amṛta from the finger of Indra,<BR>who thereupon used the exclamation which afterwards<BR>became the prince's name), N. of a king (son of<BR>Yuvanāśva, author of Ṛg-veda X. 134; also read<BR>मन्धातृ, q. v.); N. of a sovereign in more<BR>recent times.<BR>—मान्धाता-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city; (also read मान्धात्ता-त्रिपुर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धात्र
मान्धात्र, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to Māndhātṛ;<BR>(अस्), m. a patronymic from Mandhātṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्ध्योद
मान्ध्योद मान्ध्योद, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्मथ
मान्मथ मान्मथ, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मन्म-<BR>थ), relating to or concerning love, excited by love,<BR>belonging to the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्य|मान्यः
मान्य मान्य. See p. 770, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्यमान
मान्यमान मान्यमान, अस्, m., Ved. a pa-<BR>tronymic from Manyamāna; according to Sāy. on<BR>Ṛg-veda VII. 18, 20, देवकं चिन् मान्यमानं<BR>जघन्थ may be translated, ‘thou hast slain Devaka<BR>the son of Manyamāna;’ according to others, ‘thou<BR>hast slain the god, the proud one.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्यव
मान्यव मान्यव, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to<BR>Manyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्यवती
मान्यवती मान्यवती, f., N. of a princess;<BR>(perhaps for माल्य-वती.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापक
मापक मापक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt.<BR>3. मा), serving for measuring or weighing, a<BR>measurer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापन|मापनं|मापनः
मापन, अस्, m. a pair of scales, balance; (आ), f.<BR>measuring; measuring or meting out, making a place<BR>for a sacrifice, measure; (अम्), n. the act of measur-<BR>ing; forming, making, formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापत्य|मापत्यः
मापत्य मापत्य, अम्, n. (perhaps fr. 1. मा<BR>+ अपत्य, i. e. not a child in the ordinary sense,<BR>cf. मनसि-ज; according to others fr. Caus. of rt.<BR>मे), a term applied to the god of love or Kāma-<BR>deva, (according to some, मापत्य, अस्, m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माबर
माबर माबर, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माम
माम माम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मम, gen. sing.<BR>of 3. म), mine, my; mother, uncle, (in this sense<BR>like तात, q. v., and commonly in voc. sing.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामक|मामकं|मामकः
मामक, अस्, इका or Ved. ई, अम्, my, mine;<BR>selfish, greedy, covetous; (अस्), m. a miser, niggard;<BR>a maternal uncle; (ई), f., N. of a Buddhist goddess;<BR>[cf. मामुखी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकीन|मामकीनं
मामकीन, अस्, आ, or ई (?), अम्, my, mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामतेय
मामतेय, अस्, m. (fr. ममता), a metronymic<BR>of Dīrgha-tamas; (also read सामन्तेय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामनसायति
मामनसायति मामनसायति, इस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामल्लदेवी
मामल्लदेवी मामल्ल-देवी, f., N. of the<BR>mother of Śrī-harṣa (author of the Naiṣadhīya-<BR>caritra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामिडि
मामिडि मामिडि, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामुखी
मामुखी मामुखी, f., N. of a Buddhist<BR>goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामुदगजनवी
मामुदगजनवी मामुद-गजनवी, m. =<BR>محمود غزنوي i. e. Mahmūd of Ghaznī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माम्पश्य|मांपश्य
माम्पश्य माम्-पश्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. माम्,<BR>acc. of अहम् + पश्य), Ved. regarding or looking<BR>at me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय|मायः
माय माय, अस्, आ, अम् (according to some<BR>fr. rt. 3. मा, according to others fr. rt. मन् + य),<BR>illusory, possessing magical powers or powers of illu-<BR>sion (said of Viṣṇu); (अस्), m. an illusionist, conjurer,<BR>juggler; an evil spirit, Asura; (आ), f. art, wisdom,<BR>(according to Naighaṇṭuka III. 9 = प्रज्ञा), extra-<BR>ordinary or supernatural power, wonderful power,<BR>(in these meanings only in the earlier language);<BR>illusion, trick, artifice, deceit, deception, fraud, jug-<BR>glery, sorcery, witchcraft; wickedness, villany; a<BR>political trick, diplomatic artifice; an illusory image<BR>or apparition, phantasm, phantom, anything unreal,<BR>anything which deceives the sight (e. g. सिंह-म्˚, a<BR>phantasm in the form of a lion, a phantom lion);<BR>philosophical illusion, idealism, unreality, (in the<BR>Sāṅkhya system applied to Prakṛti as the source of<BR>all apparent material objects); Illusion personified,<BR>(sometimes identified with Durgā as the authoress of<BR>spells, sometimes regarded as a daughter of Anṛta<BR>and Nirṛti or Nikṛti and mother of Mrityu or as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-a" target="_blank">Page0772-a+ 81</a>]<BR>daughter of Adharma); one of the four Pāśas or<BR>snares which entangle the soul (with Śaivas); pity,<BR>compassion; N. of the mother of Śākya-muni or<BR>Buddha; N. of two metres, four times ¯¯¯¯,<BR>¯˘˘¯¯˘˘¯¯, and ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯ twice<BR>alternately with ¯¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯; (= माया-<BR>पुरी), N. of a city; of the city Gayā; (आस्), f. pl.,<BR>Ved. ideal products of the mind.<BR>—माय-वत्, आन्,<BR>अती, अत्, Ved. = माया-वत्, q. v.<BR>—माया-कापालिक,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a particular drama.<BR>—माया-<BR>कार, अस्, or माया-कृत्, त्, m. ‘illusion-maker,’ a<BR>conjurer, juggler.<BR>—माया-चण, अस्, आ, अम् (see<BR>चण), skilled in illusion, famous for juggling; illu-<BR>sive, deceptive.<BR>—मायाचार (˚या-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>practising illusion or deceit, acting deceitfully, (op-<BR>posed to साधु-आचार.)<BR>—माया-जीविन्, ई, m. ‘living<BR>by illusion,’ a conjurer, juggler.<BR>—माया-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—मायात्मक (˚या-आत्˚), अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, consisting of illusion, essentially illusory.<BR>—माया-द, अस्, m. ‘giving or causing illusion,’ an<BR>alligator, crocodile.<BR>—माया-दर्शन, अम्, n., N.<BR>of a chapter of the Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa.<BR>—माया-देवी,<BR>f., N. of the mother of the Buddha κατ’ ἐξοχήν or<BR>Śākya-muni; of the wife of Pra-dyumna.<BR>—माया-<BR>देवी-सुत, अस्, m. ‘the son of Māyā-devī,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Śākya-muni.<BR>—माया-धर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>possessing illusion, skilled in magic, deceitful.<BR>—मा-<BR>यान्वित (˚या-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessing illusion,<BR>deceitful, guileful.<BR>—माया-पटु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ,<BR>skilled in illusion or magical arts, delusive, fraudulent.<BR>—माया-पति, इस्, m. ‘lord of illusion,’ a master<BR>in illusions, the husband of Illusion personified.<BR>—माया-पुर्, ऊर्, or माया-पुरी, f., N. of a city;<BR>[cf. माया.]<BR>—माया-प्रयोग, अस्, m. the application<BR>or employment of magic.<BR>—माया-फल, अम्, n. a<BR>gall-nut.<BR>—मायाभ्युदयन (˚या-अभ्˚), अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Kāyastha (Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VIII. 1819).<BR>—माया-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of illusion, formed of<BR>or creating illusion, illusive, illusory, deceptive, en-<BR>chanted, unreal, magical.<BR>—माया-माणवक, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, appearing magically as a boy or dwarf.<BR>—माया-मृग, अस्, m. an illusory antelope, a phan-<BR>tom deer.<BR>—माया-यन्त्र, अम्, n. enchantment.<BR>—मायायन्त्र-विमान, अस्, अम्, m. n. an en-<BR>chanted chariot, magical car.<BR>—माया-योग, अस्, m.<BR>the application or employment of illusion, employ-<BR>ment of magical arts.<BR>—माया-योधिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>fighting illusively or with deceitful artifices.<BR>—माया-<BR>रसिक, अस्, आ, अम्, taking pleasure in deceit, fond<BR>of illusion or deceit; [cf. माया-वसिक.]<BR>—माया-<BR>रावण, अस्, m. Rāvaṇa in an illusory or disguised<BR>form.<BR>—माया-वचन, अम्, n. a deceptive or hypo-<BR>critical speech.<BR>—माया-वटु, उस्, m., N. of a king<BR>of the Śavaras.<BR>—माया-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing<BR>powers of illusion, having magical powers, employing<BR>deceit, deceptive, illusory, unreal; skilled in magical<BR>arts; (आन्), m. an epithet of Kaṃsa; (अती), f., N. of<BR>the wife of Pra-dyumna; of the wife of a Vidyā-<BR>dhara; of a princess; of a particular magical art<BR>personified; of an authoress of certain magical incan-<BR>tations.<BR>—माया-वसिक, अस्, आ, अम्, practising de-<BR>ceit, deluding, a deceiver, cheat, (perhaps for माया-<BR>रसिक.)<BR>—माया-वाद, अस्, m. ‘the doctrine of<BR>illusion,’ a term applied to Buddhism.<BR>—मायावाद-<BR>सन्दूषणी, f. ‘destroyer of the doctrine of illusion,’<BR>N. of a controversial work against the non-dualistic<BR>doctrine of the Vedānta.<BR>—माया-विद्, त्, त्, त्, ‘illu-<BR>sion-knowing,’ experienced or skilled in magical arts.<BR>—माया-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing illusion or magical<BR>powers; employing deceit, using tricks, deluding or<BR>deceiving others; illusory, creating illusions; (ई), m.<BR>a magician, conjurer, juggler; a cat; N. of a son of<BR>Maya; (इ), n. a gall-nut.<BR>—माया-सुत, अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of Māyā,’ epithet of Śākya-muni or Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायायिन्
मायायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, = माया-विन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक, अस्, आ, अम्, illusory, creating illusion;<BR>practising deceit, deceiving others, deceitful, decep-<BR>tive, trickish; (अस्), m. a conjurer, juggler; (अम्), n.<BR>a gall-nut.<BR>—मायिक-भैरव, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिन्
मायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, possessing powers of illusion,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">Page0772-b+ 71</a>]<BR>having supernatural powers; illusory, unreal, decep-<BR>tive, subject to Māyā (said of the soul, cf. माया);<BR>(ई), m. a conjurer, juggler, magician; a cheat, de-<BR>ceiver; epithet of Brahmā; of Śiva; of Agni; of<BR>Kāma; (इ), n. magic, magical art [cf. दुर्-म्˚]; a<BR>gall-nut.<BR>—मायि-फल, अम्, n. a gall-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायेय
मायेय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. माया), see Gaṇa Nadyādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 4, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायण
मायण मायण, अस्, m., N. of the father of<BR>Mādhava and Sāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायव
मायव मायव, अस्, m. (fr. मयु or मायु),<BR>Ved. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायवत्|मायवन्त्
मायवत् माय-वत्. See col. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माया
माया माया. See under माय, p. 771.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकापालिक
मायाकापालिक माया-कापालिक, माया-कार,<BR>&c. See col. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाति|मायातिः
मायाति मायाति, इस्, m. = नर-बलि, the<BR>sacrifice or oblation to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक मायिक, मायिन्. See col. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
मायु 1. मायु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मा), Ved.<BR>the act of bleating, lowing, bellowing, roaring, yell-<BR>ing, braying, making any sound or cry; ‘the bleater<BR>or bellower,’ a kind of animal or epithet of a Kim-<BR>puruṣa [cf. मयु, मय, मयूर]; sometimes at<BR>the end of comps., [cf. अज-म्˚, ऊर्ध्व-म्˚, गो-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूक
मायूक, अस्, आ, अम् (probably for मायुक), bel-<BR>lowing, roaring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
मायु 2. मायु (probably fr. rt. 3. मा, to<BR>measure), = आदित्य, the sun, (according to Nirukta<BR>II. 9, XI. 42.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
मायु 3. मायु, उस्, उ, m. n. (in Uṇādi-s. I.<BR>1. said to be fr. rt. I. मि, to throw or scatter through<BR>the body), gall, bile, the bilious humor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुक
मायुक मायुक (according to Naigh. III.<BR>2) = ह्रस्व; [cf. प्र-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुराज|मायुराजः
मायुराज मायुराज, अस्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Kuvera [cf. मयु-राज]; N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूक
मायूक मायूक. See under 1. मायु above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूर|मायूरं
मायूर मायूर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मयूर), be-<BR>longing to or coming from a peacock; made of<BR>peacocks’ feathers; drawn by peacocks (said of a<BR>chariot); dear to peacocks; (ई), f. a species of plant,<BR>= अज-मोदा; (अम्), n. a flock of peacocks.<BR>—मा-<BR>यूर-कल्प, अस्, m., N. of a particular Kalpa or<BR>long period of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरक|मायूरकः
मायूरक, अस्, m. a peacock-catcher, one who<BR>catches wild peacocks either to tame them or in<BR>order to make various articles with their feathers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरकर्ण
मायूरकर्ण, अस्, m. (fr. मयूर-कर्ण), a<BR>patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरिक|मायूरिकः
मायूरिक, अस्, m. a fowler who catches peacocks,<BR>peacock-catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायोभव
मायोभव मायोभव or (more correctly)<BR>मायोभव्य, अम्, n. (fr. मयो-भू), Ved. well-<BR>being, enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय्य
माय्य माय्य. See पुरु-म्˚, p. 585, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्
मार् मार्, र्, र्, र् (fr. Caus. of rt. मृ), a<BR>killer, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार|मारः
मार, अस्, ई, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) killing,<BR>destroying, slaying; (अस्), m. death, pestilence (Ved.);<BR>slaying, killing; hindrance, obstruction, impediment,<BR>opposition; the god of love; the passion of love;<BR>(with Buddhists) the Destroyer, Evil One, Devil, (in<BR>this sense also आस्, m. pl.); the thorn-apple; (ई), f.<BR>a plague, pestilence, epidemic; Pestilence personified<BR>as the goddess of death, and identified with Durgā;<BR>[cf. अघ-मार, तृष्णा-म्˚, पशु-म्˚.]<BR>—मार-<BR>जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of Māra,’ N. of a Buddha.<BR>—मार-बीज, अम्, n. epithet of a particular magical<BR>formula.<BR>—मार-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, full of love, im-<BR>passioned, enamoured.<BR>—माराङ्क (˚र-अङ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">Page0772-c+ 74</a>]<BR>अम्, displaying tokens of love.<BR>—मारात्मक (˚र-<BR>आत्˚), अस्, इका, अम्, essentially destructive, murderous.<BR>—माराभिभु (˚र-अभ्˚), उस्, m. ‘overthrower of<BR>Māra,’ epithet of a Buddha.<BR>—मारारि (˚र-अरि),<BR>इस्, m. ‘the enemy of the god of love,’ N. of Śiva.<BR>—मारी-मृत, Ved. a spectre, apparition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारक|मारकः
मारक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>killing, slaying; (अस्), m. any deadly or pestilential<BR>disease, plague, pestilence; a slayer, destroyer, mur-<BR>derer, the god of death; a falcon, hawk; (इका), f.<BR>a plague, pestilence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकायिक
मारकायिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मार + काय), be-<BR>longing to the retinue or attendants of Māra (with<BR>Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारण|मारणं
मारण, अम्, n. the act of killing, slaying,<BR>slaughter, being killed, destruction; a magical cere-<BR>mony having for its object the destruction of an<BR>enemy; (scil. अस्त्र), ‘the slayer,’ epithet of certain<BR>mythical weapons; epithet of a particular process in<BR>reducing metals, calcination; a kind of poison [cf.<BR>मरण]; (ई), f. ‘the slayer,’ epithet of one of<BR>the nine Samidhs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारि|मारिः
मारि, इस्, f. any deadly disease, pestilence, plague;<BR>killing, slaying; ruin.<BR>—मारि-व्यसन-वारक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, averting plague and distress; (अस्), m. an<BR>epithet of Kumāra-pāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारित|मारितः
मारित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. the Caus.), killed, slain,<BR>destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिन्
मारिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. rt. मृ or fr. मार), dying;<BR>killing, a slayer, murderer (at the end of comps.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीय
मारीय, अस्, आ, अम्, belonging to the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुक
मारुक, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. dying, perishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्यमाण
मार्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being killed or destroyed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकत
मारकत मारकत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मरकत),<BR>of or belonging to an emerald, like an emerald,<BR>emerald-coloured, having any of the properties or<BR>qualities of an emerald.<BR>—मारकत-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>state or property of an emerald, emerald colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजातक|मारजातकः
मारजातक मारजातक, अस्, m. a cat (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारदाकार
मारदाकार मारदाकार, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारव
मारव मारव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मरु), desert,<BR>belonging to a wilderness or any wild, uncultivated<BR>region, living or being in a wilderness; (ई), f. epithet<BR>of a particular musical scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिच
मारिच मारिच, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मरिच), made<BR>of pepper, peppery; (with चूर्ण), ground or pounded<BR>pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिचिक|मारिचिकं
मारिचिक, अस्, आ, अम्, prepared or seasoned with<BR>pepper, peppered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारित|मारितः
मारित मारित. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिष|मारिषः
मारिष मारिष, अस्, m. (for मार्ष, q. v.),<BR>an honourable man, a respectable or venerable person,<BR>(in the voc. as a respectful mode of address, and in<BR>dramatic language sometimes applied to the manager<BR>or one of the principal actors); a species of pot-herb<BR>or vegetable, Amaranthus Oleraceus [cf. अल्प-मा-<BR>रिष, मार्षिक]; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(आ), f., N. of the mother of Dakṣa; of the wife of<BR>Śūra; of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारी
मारी मारी. See under मार, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच|मारीचः
मारीच मारीच, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging or<BR>relating to or composed by Marīci; (अस्), m. son of<BR>Marīci, a patronymic of Kaśyapa; N. of a Rākṣasa;<BR>a royal elephant; a species of plant, = कक्कोल; (ई),<BR>f., N. of a Buddhist goddess, the mother of Śākya-<BR>muni (= माया-देवी, q. v.); N. of an Apsaras;<BR>(अम्), n. a collection or grove of pepper plants, (in<BR>this sense fr. मरीच); N. of a commentary on the<BR>Siddhānta-śiromaṇi; [cf. मरीच.]<BR>—मारीचोपपु-<BR>राण (˚च-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीचि
मारीचि, इस्, m. a metronymic from Marīcī, see<BR>Gaṇa Bāhvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच्य
मारीच्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from Marīci, (used<BR>as an epithet of the Agni-ṣvāttas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुण्ड|मारुंड|मारुंडः|मारुण्डः
मारुण्ड मारुण्ड, अस्, m. a serpent's egg;<BR>cow-dung; a place spread with cow-dung; a road,<BR>way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुत|मारुतः
मारुत मारुत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मरुत्), of or<BR>belonging to the Maruts, proceeding from the Ma-<BR>ruts, relating to or consisting of the Maruts; belong-<BR>ing to air or wind, relating to or proceeding from<BR>wind, windy, aerial; (अस्), m. = मरुत्, air, wind;<BR>the god of the wind; breath, breathing; the wind<BR>in the body, vital air, one of the three humors of<BR>the body; the trunk of an elephant; N. of a Marut;<BR>a prince of the Maruts; a N. of Agni; (Ved.) a son<BR>of the Maruts; (Ved.) an epithet of Viṣṇu and of<BR>Rudra, &c.; (आस्), m. pl. the Maruts (regarded as<BR>children of Diti); N. of a people, (also read म-<BR>डक); (आ), f., N. of a woman; (ई), f., scil. दिश् or<BR>विदिश्, the north-west quarter; (अम्), n., scil.<BR>ऋक्ष or नक्षत्र, the constellation Svāti; N. of<BR>a Sāman; a burnt offering on conception (?).<BR>—मा-<BR>रुत-पूर्ण-रन्ध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, having cavities<BR>filled with wind (said of reeds).<BR>—मारुत-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, consisting or having the essence of wind,<BR>windy.<BR>—मारुत-व्रत, अम्, n. ‘wind-like duty,’<BR>penetrating everywhere (as a king by means of spies);<BR>—मारुत-सूनु, उस्, m. ‘son of the wind,’ epithet<BR>of Hanumat.<BR>—मारुतात्मज (˚त-आत्˚), अस्, m. ‘son<BR>of the wind,’ epithet of fire; of Hanumat.<BR>—मारु-<BR>तापह (˚त-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, expelling the wind of<BR>the body, removing windy humor; (अस्), m. Capparis<BR>Trifoliata.<BR>—मारुतापूर्ण (˚त-आप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>filled with wind.<BR>—मारुताशन (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, feeding on air alone, fasting; (अस्), m. a snake<BR>[cf. पवनाशन]; N. of one of Skanda's attendants;<BR>of a Dānava.<BR>—मारुताश्व (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>(perhaps) having horses rapid as the wind; (Sāy.) a<BR>patronymic from Marutāśva.<BR>—मारुतेश्वर-तीर्थ<BR>(˚त-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुति|मारुतिः
मारुति, इस्, m. (fr. मरुत् or मारुत), ‘son of<BR>the Maruts, son of the Wind,’ a patronymic of<BR>Dyutāna (Ved.); of Bhīma; of Hanumat.<BR>—मा-<BR>रुति-प्रष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, led on or preceded by<BR>Hanumat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतन्तव्य
मारुतन्तव्य मारुतन्तव्य for मानुतन्त-<BR>व्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुदेव
मारुदेव मारुदेव, N. of a mountain. See<BR>मरुद्-एव, p. 749, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुध
मारुध मारुध, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुवार
मारुवार मारुवार, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्क|मार्कः
मार्क मार्क, अस्, m. = मार्कव, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कट
मार्कट मार्कट, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मर्कट),<BR>apish, monkey-like.<BR>—मार्कट-पिपीलिका, f. a small<BR>black ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कटि
मार्कटि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Markaṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्ड|मार्कंड|मार्कंडः|मार्कण्डः
मार्कण्ड मार्कण्ड, अस्, m. = मार्कण्डेय<BR>below; (अस्, आ, अम्), composed by Mārkaṇḍa.<BR>—मार्कण्ड-पुराण, अम्, n. = मार्कण्डेय-<BR>पुराण.<BR>—मार्कण्डेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚ड-ईश्˚), अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डीय|मार्कण्डीयं
मार्कण्डीय, अम्, n. a species of shrub (= भूम्य्-<BR>आहुल्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डेय|मार्कंडेय|मार्कंडेयः|मार्कण्डेयः
मार्कण्डेय, अस्, m. a patronymic from Mṛ-<BR>kaṇḍu, (according to others also Mṛkaṇḍa); N. of<BR>an ancient sage (the reputed author or narrator of<BR>the Mārkaṇḍeya-Purāṇa); (आस्), m. pl. the descend-<BR>ants of Mārkaṇḍeya; (अम्), n. = मार्कण्डेयस्य<BR>तीर्थम्; (अस्, ई, अम्), delivered or composed by<BR>Mārkaṇḍeya.<BR>—मार्कण्डेय-पुराण, अम्, n., N.<BR>of one of the eighteen Purāṇas, (in this Purāṇa<BR>Jaimini, the pupil of Vyāsa, applies to Mārkaṇḍeya<BR>to be made acquainted with the nature of Vāsudeva<BR>or Kṛṣṇa, and for an explanation of some of the<BR>incidents of the Mahā-bhārata; the sage excuses<BR>himself, and refers Jaimini to some sapient birds of<BR>celestial origin, residing in the Vindhya mountains,<BR>and profoundly versed in the Vedas; these birds,<BR>whose chief is called Piṅgākṣa, answer Jaimini's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-b" target="_blank">Page0773-b+ 80</a>]<BR>questions and explain various difficult points, such as,<BR>‘Why was Vāsudeva born a mortal? How was it<BR>Draupadī became the wife of the five Pāṇḍus?’ &c.,<BR>&c. The answer to these inquiries and the addition<BR>of various legends constitute the bulk of this Purāṇa,<BR>and make it a kind of supplement to the Mahā-<BR>bhārata; it differs from all the other Purāṇas in its<BR>narrative rather than sectarial character.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कव|मार्कवः
मार्कव मार्कव, अस्, m. Eclipta Prostrata;<BR>(sometimes incorrectly spelt मार्कर; cf. मर्-<BR>कर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्
मार्ग् मार्ग् (connected with rts. मृग्,<BR>1. मृज्, but more properly to be regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. मार्ग below), cl. 1. 10. P. (ep. also<BR>cl. 1. A) मार्गति (-ते), मार्गयति, मार्गितुम्,<BR>मार्गयितुम्, to seek, seek for; to hunt after, chase;<BR>to search through, trace out; to seek after, seek to<BR>obtain, strive to attain; to follow after, strive after;<BR>to request, ask, beg, solicit anything from any one<BR>(with abl. of the person and acc. of the thing, or<BR>purchase or buy; to make or prepare a road (?); to<BR>with double acc.), to ask in marriage; to seek to<BR>go (?); to feather an arrow (?); to purify, adorn, (in<BR>this sense evidently for rt. मार्ज् = 1. मृज्, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग|मार्गः
मार्ग, अस्, m. (in some of its senses fr. मृग),<BR>hunting or tracing out game; following after, seek-<BR>ing, search, investigation, inquiry; the track of a<BR>wild animal, any track, path, road, way, (मार्गे,<BR>on the way, on the road; मध्ये मार्गे, in the<BR>middle of the way; मार्गं दा, with gen. of<BR>the person, to give up the way to any one, move<BR>out of any one's way; मार्गे प्रचलितः, he set<BR>out on his way); the path or course of a planet, of<BR>the wind, &c.; (in medicine) a way, passage, chan-<BR>nel, canal (in any part of the body); the intestinal<BR>canal, anus; a way, means, (विग्रह-मार्ग, a<BR>means of warfare); the right way, proper course;<BR>mode, manner, method, characteristic, usage, habit,<BR>custom, use, (अमार्गेण, in an unfair manner;<BR>मल्ल-मार्गाः, the usages of wrestlers; युद्ध-<BR>मार्ग, a mode of fighting, stratagem, manœuvre);<BR>a title or head in law, ground for litigation; style,<BR>diction; a high style of acting or dancing or singing<BR>(as opposed to a vulgar style); (in dramatic language)<BR>pointing out the way, indicating how anything is to<BR>take place; (in geometry) a section; (अस्, ई, अम्),<BR>coming from or belonging to wild animals, belonging<BR>to an antelope or deer, (in this sense fr. मृग);<BR>(अस्), m. musk [cf. मृग-मद]; the constellation<BR>Mṛga-śiras; the month Mārgaśīrṣa (November-<BR>December).<BR>—मार्ग-तोरण, अम्, n. a triumphal<BR>arch erected over a road.<BR>—मार्ग-दर्शक, अस्, m.<BR>‘way-shower,’ a guide.<BR>—मार्ग-दायिनी, f. ‘giving<BR>up the way,’ N. of Dākṣāyaṇī at Kedāra.<BR>—मार्ग-<BR>द्रङ्ग, अस्, m. a city or town on the road.<BR>—मार्ग-<BR>द्रुम, अस्, m. a tree growing by the way-side.<BR>—मार्ग-धेनु, उस्, m. or मार्ग-धेनुक, अम्,<BR>n. a Yojana, a measure of distance = 4000 fathoms<BR>or 4 Kos, above 8 miles, (perhaps originally a mile-<BR>stone representing a cow.)<BR>—मार्ग-प, अस्, or<BR>मार्ग-पति, इस्, m. ‘road-inspector,’ N. of a parti-<BR>cular official.<BR>—मार्ग-पथ, अस्, m. a course, road,<BR>path.<BR>—मार्ग-पाली, f. ‘road-protectress,’ N. of a<BR>goddess.<BR>—मार्ग-बन्धन, अम्, n. a road-<BR>obstruction, anything which blocks up a road, a bar-<BR>ricade.<BR>—मार्ग-मध्य-ग, अस्, आ, अम्, going in<BR>the middle of the road, being on the road.<BR>—मार्ग-<BR>रक्षक, अस्, m. a road-keeper, guard.<BR>—मार्ग-<BR>रोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, road-obstructing, blocking up a<BR>road.<BR>—मार्ग-वटी, f. epithet of the tutelary god-<BR>dess of travellers.<BR>—मार्ग-वशानुग (˚श-अन्˚) or<BR>मार्ग-वशायात (˚श-आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, remaining<BR>on the road, going or situated along the road.<BR>—मार्-<BR>ग-शाखिन्, ई, m. ‘way-side tree,’ a tree by the road-<BR>side.<BR>—मार्गशीर्ष, see col. 3.<BR>—मार्ग-शोधक,<BR>अस्, m. ‘road-clearer,’ a pioneer.<BR>—मार्ग-स्थ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, being on the road, a traveller.<BR>—मार्ग-<BR>हर्म्य, अम्, n. a mansion or palace on a high-road.<BR>—मार्गागत (˚ग-आग्˚) or मार्गायात (˚ग-आय्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, come from the road or a journey, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">Page0773-c+ 77</a>]<BR>traveller, wayfarer.<BR>—मार्गेश (˚ग-ईश˚), अस्, m. =<BR>मार्ग-प, col. 2.<BR>—मार्गैषिन् (˚ग-एष्˚), ई, इणी,<BR>इ, ‘road-seeking,’ searching for a road or path.<BR>—मार्गोपदिश् (˚ग-उप्˚), क्, m. ‘road-shower,’ a<BR>guide, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गक|मार्गकः
मार्गक, अस्, m. the month Mārgaśīrṣa; [cf.<BR>प्रति-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गण|मार्गणं|मार्गणः
मार्गण, अस्, ई, अम्, seeking, searching for; in-<BR>vestigating; begging, requiring, asking, desiring;<BR>(अस्), m. a beggar, solicitor, suppliant, mendicant;<BR>an arrow; a symbolical expression for the number<BR>five derived from the five arrows of the god of love;<BR>(अम्, आ), n. f. the act of seeking or searching for, inves-<BR>tigation; research, inquiry; the act of begging, soli-<BR>citation, affectionate solicitation or inquiry, (in some<BR>of these senses usually आ, f.)<BR>—मार्गण-ता, f. the<BR>being an arrow, the state or nature of an arrow;<BR>मार्गणतां गतः, become an arrow.<BR>—मार्गण-<BR>प्रिया, f., N. of a daughter of Prādhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गणक|मार्गणकः
मार्गणक, अस्, m. a beggar, solicitor, mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गमाण
मार्गमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, seeking, searching for,<BR>tracing out, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गयत्
मार्गयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, seeking, searching for,<BR>investigating, hunting after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिर|मार्गशिरः
मार्गशिर, अस्, or मार्गशिरस्, आस्, m. (fr.<BR>मृग-शिरस्), the month Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशीर्ष|मार्गशीर्षः
मार्गशीर्ष, अस्, ई, अम्, born under the constel-<BR>lation Mṛga-śiras; (with and without मास), N. of<BR>the month in which the full moon enters the con-<BR>stellation Mṛga-śiras, the tenth or (in later times)<BR>the first month in the year = November-December;<BR>(ई), f. (with and without पौर्णमासी), the day on<BR>which the full moon enters the constellation Mṛga-<BR>śiras, the fifteenth day of the first half of the month<BR>Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशीर्षक
मार्गशीर्षक, अस्, m. = मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गार
मार्गार, अस्, m., Ved. (according to Mahī-dhara)<BR>a patronymic from Mṛgāri; one who catches fish<BR>with his hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिक|मार्गिकः
मार्गिक, अस्, m. a hunter, huntsman; a traveller,<BR>wayfarer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गित|मार्गितं
मार्गित, अस्, आ, अम्, sought, searched, sought or<BR>inquired after, pursued, hunted after; desired, re-<BR>quired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गितव्य
मार्गितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be sought or sought<BR>after; to be searched through; to be striven after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिन्
मार्गिन्, ई, m. one who clears or guards the way,<BR>a pioneer, guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्य|मार्ग्यं
1. मार्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see under rt. मार्ज्<BR>below), to be sought or searched for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्यमाण
मार्ग्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being hunted after or<BR>searched for, being chased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गमर्षि
मार्गमर्षि मार्गमर्षि, इस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Viśvāmitra, (also read मार्दमर्षि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गमित्र
मार्गमित्र मार्गमित्र, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गयथ
मार्गयथ मार्गयथ, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गव|मार्गवः
मार्गव मार्गव, अस्, m. a particular mixed<BR>caste (born from a Niṣāda and an Ayogava female).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गवेय
मार्गवेय मार्गवेय, अस्, m., Ved. the patro-<BR>nymic or metronymic of a Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिर|मार्गशिरः
मार्गशिर मार्गशिर, मार्गशीर्ष. See<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गीयव
मार्गीयव मार्गीयव or मार्गीयवाद्य, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्
मार्ज् मार्ज्, cl. 10. P. मार्जयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to wipe, scour, cleanse, purify, (in these<BR>senses allied to rt. 1. मृज्, fr. which the derivatives<BR>below may be formed); to sound, make a parti-<BR>cular sound, (in this sense connected with rts. मर्च्,<BR>मर्व्, मञ्ज्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्य|मार्ग्यं
2. मार्ग्य, अस्, आ, अम् (properly fr. rt. 1. मृज्; for<BR>1. see above), to be wiped away or removed, to be<BR>scoured, to be cleansed or purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज|मार्जः|मार्ज्ज|मार्ज्जः
मार्ज, अस्, आ, अम्, cleaning, scouring; a cleaner,<BR>scourer [cf. अस्त्र-म्˚, शस्त्र-म्˚]; (अस्), m. an epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu; purification, cleansing; a washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जक
मार्जक, अस्, इका, अम्, cleansing, scouring, clean-<BR>ing, purifying; a cleaner, scourer, sweeper; (per-<BR>haps) = मार्जन, Symplocos Racemosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जन|मार्जनः|मार्ज्जन|मार्ज्जनं|मार्ज्जनः
मार्जन, अस्, ई, अम्, wiping away, cleansing,<BR>purifying, washing; (अस्), m. Symplocos Racemosa;<BR>(आ), f. washing, cleansing, purifying; the sound of a<BR>drum [cf. rt. मार्ज्]; (ई), f. a broom, besom, brush;<BR>N. of one of Durgā's female attendants; (अम्), n.<BR>the act of wiping or rubbing off; the act of cleaning,<BR>scouring, cleansing, sweeping; cleansing the person<BR>by wiping or bathing or rubbing it with unguents;<BR>the act of wiping away or effacing; (उच्छिष्ट-<BR>मार्जनम्, removing leavings.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जनीय|मार्जनीयः
मार्जनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleaned, to be<BR>cleansed or purified; to be swept or brushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जार|मार्जारः|मार्ज्जार
मार्जार, अस्, m. a cat, (probably so called from its<BR>habit of constantly cleaning itself); a polecat, civet-<BR>cat [cf. गन्ध-म्˚]; a wild cat, = अरण्य-मार्-<BR>जार; (ई), f. a female cat; a civet-cat; musk.<BR>—मार्जार-कण्ठ, अस्, m. ‘having the throat or<BR>cry of a cat,’ a peacock.<BR>—मार्जार-करण, अम्, n.<BR>a particular posture in sexual intercourse.<BR>—मार्जार-<BR>कर्णिका or मार्जार-कर्णी, f. ‘cat-eared,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Cāmuṇḍā.<BR>—मार्जार-गन्धा, f. a species<BR>of Mudga-parṇī or pulse, Phaseolus Trilobus.<BR>—मार्-<BR>जार-गन्धिका, f. = मुद्ग-पर्णी, q. v.<BR>—मार्-<BR>जार-लिङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having the nature or charac-<BR>teristics of a cat.<BR>—मार्जारी-क्रमण, अम्, n. a<BR>particular kind of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारक|मार्जारकः|मार्ज्जारक
मार्जारक, अस्, m. a cat; a peacock (so called<BR>from its cat-like cry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारि
मार्जारि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Saha-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारीय|मार्जारीयः|मार्ज्जारीय
मार्जारीय, अस्, m. a cat; a Śūdra; one who<BR>cleanses or purifies his body (= काय-शोधन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जाल|मार्जालः|मार्ज्जाल
मार्जाल, अस्, m. = मार्जार, a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जालीय|मार्जालीयः|मार्ज्जालीय
मार्जालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘fond of washing or ablu-<BR>tion, delighting in purification,’ an epithet of Śiva in<BR>Mahā-bh. Vana-p. 1628, (according to the Scholiast<BR>= शुद्ध-देह = किरात); (अस्), m. a cat; a Śūdra;<BR>scil. धिष्ण्य, a heap of earth to the right of the<BR>Vedi on which the sacrificial vessels are cleansed<BR>(Ved.); N. of the seventeenth Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जाल्य
मार्जाल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fond of washing or<BR>ablution, delighting in purification; (according to<BR>Sāy.) entitled to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जित|मार्ज्जित
मार्जित, अस्, आ, अम्, (see rt. 1. मृज्, with which<BR>this and the following may be connected), scoured,<BR>cleansed, purified, swept, brushed, adorned; (आ), f.<BR>curds with sugar and spice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टव्य
मार्ष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleansed, to be<BR>scoured or purified, to be swept or brushed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टि|मार्ष्टिः
मार्ष्टि, इस्, f. washing, cleaning, cleansing, puri-<BR>fying, cleansing the person or anointing it with oil;<BR>(इस्), m., N. of a son of Sāraṇa.<BR>—मार्ष्टि-मत्,<BR>आन्, m., N. of a son of Sāraṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्डाकव
मार्डाकव मार्डाकव, अस्, m. a patronymic<BR>from Mṛḍāku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्डाकवायन
मार्डाकवायन, अस्, m. a patronymic from Mār-<BR>ḍākava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्डीक
मार्डीक मार्डीक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. मृड्),<BR>Ved. gladdening, rejoicing; (अम्), n. compassion,<BR>grace, favour, (in this sense fr. मृडीक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ड्यर्थ
मार्ड्यर्थ मार्ड्यर्थ, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्तण्ड|मार्तंड|मार्तंडः|मार्तण्डः|मार्त्तण्ड|मार्त्तण्डः
मार्तण्ड मार्तण्ड, अस्, m. (fr. मृतण्ड,<BR>but the old form is probably मार्ताण्ड below), the<BR>sun, the sun-god, (sometimes used in titles of books;<BR>cf. छन्दो-म्˚, प्रमेय-कमल-म्˚); an Āditya;<BR>a symbolical expression for the number twelve; a<BR>hog, boar.<BR>—मार्तण्ड-तिलक-स्वामिन्, ई, m., N.<BR>of a preceptor.<BR>—मार्तण्ड-वल्लभा, f. ‘beloved of<BR>the sun,’ the plant Polanisia Icosandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ताण्ड
मार्ताण्ड, अस्, m. (fr. मृताण्ड), a bird (Ved.);<BR>‘the bird in the sky,’ the sun, a statue of the sun-god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्तवत्स
मार्तवत्स मार्तवत्स, अम्, n. (fr. मृत-<BR>वत्सा), Ved. born dead, still-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तिक|मार्तिक|मार्त्तिकः
मार्त्तिक मार्त्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मृत्तिका),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">Page0774-b+ 75</a>]<BR>made of clay or loam, earthen; (अस्), m. a kind of<BR>pitcher or earthenware vessel; the lid of a pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तिकावत
मार्त्तिकावत (fr. मृत्तिकावती), N. of a country;<BR>epithet of the king of that country; N. of a city;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; of a princely race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तिकावतक
मार्त्तिकावतक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to the country<BR>Mārttikāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्य
मार्त्य मार्त्य, अस्, आ (?) , अम् (fr. मर्त्य),<BR>mortal, corporeal; (अम्), n. the corporeal or mortal<BR>part, mortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्यव
मार्त्यव, अस्, ई, m. f. (fr. मृत्यु), a patronymic<BR>of Antaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्युञ्जय|मार्त्युंजय
मार्त्युञ्जय, अस्, ई, m. f. a patronymic from<BR>Mṛtyuñ-jaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्स्न
मार्त्स्न मार्त्स्न, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मृत्स्ना), Ved.<BR>ground fine or small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दङ्ग|मार्दंग|मार्दंगः|मार्दङ्गः|मार्द्दङ्ग|मार्द्दङ्गं
मार्दङ्ग मार्दङ्ग, अम्, n. (fr. मृदङ्ग),<BR>a city, town; (अस्), m. a drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दङ्गिक|मार्दंगिक|मार्दंगिकः|मार्दङ्गिकः|मार्द्दङ्गिक|मार्द्दङ्गिकः
मार्दङ्गिक, अस्, m. a drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दमर्षि
मार्दमर्षि मार्दमर्षि. See मार्गमर्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दव|मार्दवं|मार्द्दव|मार्द्दवं|मार्द्दवः
मार्दव मार्दव, अस्, m. (fr. मृदु), a patro-<BR>nymic; a particular mixed caste, (in this sense per-<BR>haps incorrectly for मार्गव); (अम्), n. softness, weak-<BR>ness, suppleness, pliancy, kindness, indulgence, gentle-<BR>ness, mildness, leniency, good nature; kindness or<BR>gentleness towards (with gen., e. g. मार्दवं सर्व-<BR>भूतानाम्, gentleness towards all living creatures).<BR>—मार्दव-भाव, अस्, m. the state of being soft<BR>or pliant, pliancy, suppleness.<BR>—मार्दवी-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>P. -करोति, &c., to make soft, make weak or indul-<BR>gent.<BR>—मार्दवी-कृता, f. made soft, weak, self-<BR>indulgent, lax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दवायन
मार्दवायन, अस्, m. (fr. मार्दव), a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्देय
मार्देय मार्देय, अस्, m. = मृदेर् अपत्यम्.<BR>—मार्देय-पुर, अम्, n., N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्वीक
मार्द्वीक मार्द्वीक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मृद्वीका),<BR>coming from or made of grapes; (अम्), n. wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष|मार्षः
मार्ष मार्ष, अस्, m. (fr. मर्ष), a vene-<BR>rable or honourable man, respectable person; a kind<BR>of vegetable; [cf. मारिष.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्षिक|मार्षिकः
मार्षिक, अस्, m. a kind of vegetable (= मा-<BR>रिष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टव्य
मार्ष्टव्य मार्ष्टव्य, मार्ष्टि. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल|मालं|मालः
माल माल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 3. मा),<BR>N. of a district (lying west and south-west of Ben-<BR>gal); a barbarian or mountaineer of a particular<BR>tribe; an epithet of Viṣṇu; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>barbarous tribe of people; (आ), f. a wreath, garland,<BR>chaplet, crown; a row, line (= पङ्क्ति, Kirātārju-<BR>nīya V. 9); a chain, string, rosary, necklace [cf.<BR>अक्ष-म्˚]; a collection, group [cf. नक्षत्र-म्˚];<BR>a series, regular succession, (नाम्नाम् माला, a col-<BR>lection of words arranged in order, a vocabulary, dic-<BR>tionary; cf. नाम-म्˚); (in rhetoric) a series of<BR>epithets, a string of similes; (in the drama) the<BR>offering of many things to obtain a wish; a streak,<BR>(तडिन्-माला, a flash of lightning); N. of a river;<BR>of a lexicon; of a metre containing two lines of<BR>¯¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘¯¯ and two of ˘¯˘¯¯˘˘¯˘<BR>¯¯ of another metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘,<BR>˘˘˘˘˘˘˘˘¯ [cf. स्रज्]; of a Prākṛt metre of<BR>twice 45 and 43+27 instants; (अम्), n. a field, a<BR>forest or wood near a village; deceit, fraud, artifice;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), low, base.<BR>—माल-चक्रक, अम्, n.<BR>the hip-joint.<BR>—माल-भञ्जिका, f. (माल for माला),<BR>‘breaking the garland,’ N. of a game.<BR>—माल-भा-<BR>रिन्, ई, इणी, इ (माल for माला), bearing or wearing<BR>a garland, having a chaplet or crown, garlanded.<BR>—माला-कण्ठ, अस्, m. the plant Achyranthes As-<BR>pera.<BR>—माला-कन्द, अस्, m. a species of bulbous<BR>plant.<BR>—माला-कर or माला-कार, अस्, m. a wreath-<BR>maker, garland-weaver, florist, gardener; the mixed<BR>caste of gardeners; N. of a son of Viśva-karman by<BR>a Śūdra woman or by Ghṛtācī; (ई), f. a woman<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">Page0774-c+ 81</a>]<BR>who weaves garlands, a wreath-maker.<BR>—माला-कुट-<BR>दन्ती, f., N. of a Rākṣasī.<BR>—माला-गुण, अस्, m.<BR>the string of a garland, a necklace.<BR>—मालागुण-<BR>परिक्षिप्ता, f. ‘invested with the marriage string,’<BR>a marriageable woman.<BR>—माला-गुणा, f., scil. लूता,<BR>a species of venomous spider.<BR>—माला-ग्रन्थि, इस्,<BR>m. = माला-दूर्वा, q. v.<BR>—मालाङ्क (˚ला-अङ्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king (the author of a commentary on<BR>the Mālatī-mādhava, and of the Vṛndā-vana).<BR>—मा-<BR>ला-तृण or मालातृणक, अम्, n. a fragrant grass,<BR>Andropogon Schœnanthus.<BR>—माला-दीपक, अम्, n.<BR>(in rhetoric) a particular figure of speech, a closely<BR>linked or connected climax.<BR>—माला-दूर्वा, f. a<BR>species of Dūrvā grass.<BR>—माला-धर, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having or wearing a garland, wearing a chaplet or<BR>crown, crowned; N. of a class of divine beings; N.<BR>of a man; (ई), f., N. of a Rākṣasī; (अम्), n. a<BR>species of the Aty-aṣṭi metre, four times ˘˘˘˘˘<BR>¯˘¯˘˘˘¯˘¯¯˘¯.<BR>—माला-प्रस्थ, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a city.<BR>—माला-फल, अम्, n. the seed of<BR>Elæocarpus Ganitrus (employed for rosaries).<BR>—माला-<BR>मनु, उस्, m., Ved. or माला-मन्त्र, अस्, m. a<BR>sacred text or saying written in the form of a wreath.<BR>—माला-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of garlands; con-<BR>sisting of lines or streaks in regular succession.<BR>—मालारिष्टा (˚ला-अर्˚), f. a species of plant (=<BR>पाची).<BR>—मालालिका or मालाली (˚ल-आल्˚), f. Trigo-<BR>nella Corniculata.<BR>—माला-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>a wreath or garland, garlanded, wreathed, crowned;<BR>(अती), f., N. of the wife of Upa-barhaṇa; of the<BR>wife of Kuśa-dhvaja.<BR>—मालोपमा (˚ला-उप्˚), f.<BR>‘string of comparisons,’ a particular figure in rhetoric<BR>(e. g. ‘heroism adds glory to thy character, as heat to<BR>the sun, the sun to the day, the day to the sky’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालक|मालकं|मालकः
मालक, अस्, m. the Nimb tree, Melia Semper-<BR>virens; a wood near a village; (आ), f. a garland;<BR>(अकी), f., see Gaṇa Gaurādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 41;<BR>(इका), f. = माला, a garland, &c.; a necklace; a row,<BR>series, collection of things arranged in a line; a<BR>species of jasmine (= सप्तला); linseed, Linum Usi-<BR>tatissimum [cf. नव-मालिका]; a kind of bird [cf.<BR>मालिक]; an intoxicating drink; a daughter; a<BR>palace; N. of a river; (अम्), n. a garland, &c., a<BR>ring; Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालय|मालयः
1. मालय (for 2. see p. 775, col. 1), Nom. P. मा-<BR>लयति (Aor. अममालत् = मालाम् आख्यत्), Schol.<BR>on Pāṇ. VII. 4, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाका
मालाका, f. = मालिका. See under मालक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालि|मालिः
मालि, इस्, इस्, इ, (at the end of comps.) wreathed,<BR>garlanded, crowned [cf. सु-म्˚]; (इस्), m., N. of a<BR>son of the Rākṣasa Su-keśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिक|मालिकः
मालिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. माला), relating or belong-<BR>ing to a garland; (अस्), m. a garland-maker, a<BR>gardener, florist; a painter, colourist, dyer; a species<BR>of bird; [cf. मालिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिका
मालिका, f. See under मालक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालित
मालित, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comps.) garlanded,<BR>crowned, encircled, encompassed, surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्
मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, garlanded, wearing a garland or<BR>chaplet, crowned; (at the end of comps.) wearing a<BR>garland or necklace of, crowned with, wreathed with,<BR>encircled by (e. g. नगरी चम्पक-मालिनी, a city<BR>encircled by Campaka trees; पृथिवी समुद्र-<BR>मालिनी, the sea-girt earth; cf. अंशु-म्˚, ऊर्मि-म्˚,<BR>किरीट-म्˚, मरीचि-म्˚, हेम-म्˚); (ई), m. a wreath-<BR>maker, garland-maker; a florist, gardener; N. of a<BR>son of the Rākṣasa Su-keśa [cf. मालि]; (इनी), f.<BR>the wife of a wreath-maker or gardener, a female<BR>florist; N. of a city (= चम्पा); N. of two plants<BR>(= अग्नि-शिखा and दुर्-आलभा); N. of a celestial<BR>maiden; of a divine Mātṛ (one of the seven Mātṛs<BR>of Skanda); an epithet of Durgā; N. of one of<BR>Durgā's female attendants; epithet of a girl seven<BR>years old (representing Durgā at the festival of that<BR>goddess); N. of a Rākṣasī, the mother of Vibhī-<BR>ṣaṇa; N. assumed by Draupadī (while resident<BR>with king Virāṭa, cf. Mahā-bh. Virāṭa-p. 246);<BR>N. of Śveta-karṇa's wife, daughter of Su-cāru;<BR>of the wife of Priya-vrata; of the wife of Ruci and<BR>mother of Manu Raucya; of the wife of Prasena-jit;<BR>of the celestial Ganges (= गङ्गा = मन्दाकिनी);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">Page0775-a+ 78</a>]<BR>of various other rivers; N. of various metres, four<BR>times ¯˘¯¯¯¯, four times ˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯<BR>˘¯, four times ˘˘˘˘˘˘¯¯, ¯˘¯¯˘¯¯; the<BR>personification of a particular musical mode; a poeti-<BR>cal stanza consisting of alternate verses or hemistichs<BR>of eight and seven syllables; it is especially used to<BR>conclude a section or canto.<BR>—मालिनी-तन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—मालिनी-विजय, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालीय
1. मालीय, Nom. P. मालीयति, &c., to wish one's<BR>self a garland, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालीय
2. मालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, destined or fitted or suited<BR>for a garland, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालेय|मालेयः
मालेय, अस्, m. (fr. मालि), a patronymic, = मालिन्,<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa; (आ), f. great cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्य|माल्यं
माल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, relating or belonging to a gar-<BR>land, &c., proper or fit for a garland; (अस्), m. a<BR>patronymic; (आ), f. the plant Trigonella Corniculata;<BR>(अम्), n. a wreath, garland, chaplet, crown; a flower.<BR>—माल्यगुणाय, Nom. A. (fr. माल्य-गुण), मा-<BR>ल्यगुणायते, &c., to become the string of a garland,<BR>to appear like a wreath, to become a garland.<BR>—माल्य-जीवक, अस्, m. one who lives by making<BR>or selling wreaths.<BR>—माल्य-पिण्डक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Nāga.<BR>—माल्य-पुष्प, अस्, m. a kind of hemp<BR>(= शण).<BR>—माल्य-पुष्पिका, f. a species of plant<BR>(= शण-पुष्पी).<BR>—माल्य-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, gar-<BR>landed, crowned, adorned with crowns or garlands;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a Rākṣasa, the son of Su-keśa; of<BR>one of Śiva's attendants; of a mountain or moun-<BR>tainous range (described as one of the smaller moun-<BR>tains of India proper, lying eastward of mount Meru);<BR>(अती), f., N. of a river.<BR>—माल्य-वृत्ति, इस्, m. one<BR>who subsists by making or selling garlands.<BR>—माल्या-<BR>पण (˚य-आप्˚), अस्, m. a market for the sale of<BR>wreaths or garlands, garland market, flower market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालकौश|मालकौशः
मालकौश मालकौश, अस्, m. = कौशिक, a<BR>particular Rāga or musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालति|मालतिः
मालति मालति, इस्, f. = मालती below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिका
मालतिका, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending<BR>upon Skanda; of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालती
मालती, f. Jasminum Grandiflorum (both the<BR>plant and its blossom; it bears fragrant white flowers<BR>which open towards evening); a species of plant (=<BR>विशल्या); Bignonia Suaveolens; a shrub, Echites<BR>Caryophyllata; a bud, blossom; a maid, virgin,<BR>young woman; moonshine, moonlight; night; N.<BR>of various metres, viz. four times ˘¯˘˘¯˘, four<BR>times ˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯, and four times ¯˘˘<BR>¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯¯; N. of a<BR>river; of a woman; of Kalyāṇa-malla's commentary<BR>on the Megha-dūta; (probably) = काच-मल, =<BR>मालती-तीर-ज.<BR>—मालती-क्षारक, अस्, m. (pro-<BR>bably) borax.<BR>—मालती-तीर-ज, अस्, m. borax (found<BR>on the bank of the Mālatī).<BR>—मालती-तीर-सम्-<BR>भव, अम्, n. white borax.<BR>—मालती-पत्त्रिका, f.<BR>= जाति-पत्त्री, the outer shell of a nutmeg.<BR>—मा-<BR>लती-फल, अम्, n. a nutmeg.<BR>—मालती-माधव,<BR>अम्, n. ‘Mālatī and Mādhava,’ N. of a celebrated<BR>drama by Bhava-bhūti (so called from the names of<BR>the heroine and hero).<BR>—मालती-माला, f. a garland<BR>of jasmine blossoms; N. of a lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालद
मालद मालद, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(also read मानद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालय|मालयः
मालय 2. मालय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मलय;<BR>for 1. मालय see p. 774, col. 3), coming from the<BR>Malaya mountains; (अस्), m. sandal-wood; N. of a<BR>son of Garuḍa; (अम्), n. the unguent prepared from<BR>sandal; a caravansary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालव|मालवः
मालव मालव, अस्, m., N. of a country<BR>(Malwa in central India); of a Rāga or particular<BR>scale in music; of a man; (आस्), m. pl. the inha-<BR>bitants of Malwa; (आ), f., N. of a river; (ई), f. a<BR>princess of the Mālavas; N. of the wife of Aśva-pati<BR>and progenitress of the Mālavas; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>Prākṛt metre, 16+12+16+12 instants; (अस्, ई,<BR>अम्), relating or belonging to the Mālavas.<BR>—मा-<BR>लव-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मालव-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">Page0775-b+ 69</a>]<BR>देश, अस्, m. the country of Mālava or Malwa.<BR>—मालव-नृपति, इस्, m. a king of Mālava.<BR>—मा-<BR>लव-रुद्र, अस्, m., N. of a poet.<BR>—मालव-वि-<BR>षय, अस्, m. the country of Mālava or Malwa.<BR>—मालव-श्री, ईस्, f., N. of a particular musical<BR>mode or scale.<BR>—मालवाधीश (˚व-अध्˚) or मा-<BR>लवेन्द्र (˚व-इन्˚), अस्, m. a king of Mālava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवक|मालवकः
मालवक, relating to the province of Mālava or<BR>Malwa; (अस्), m. the country of the Mālavas; a<BR>native of Mālava or Malwa; (इका), f. Ipomœa Tur-<BR>pethum; N. of a woman.<BR>—मालविकाग्निमित्र<BR>(˚का-अग्˚), अम्, n. ‘Mālavikā and Agnimitra,’ N. of<BR>a drama by Kālidāsa (so called from the names of<BR>the heroine and hero).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवीय
मालवीय, अस्, आ, अम्, native of or belonging to<BR>Mālava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालव्य
मालव्य, अस्, m. epithet of one of the Mahā-<BR>puruṣas born under particular constellations (Ved.);<BR>a prince of the Mālavas.<BR>—मालव्य-देश, N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवर्ति
मालवर्ति मालवर्ति, इस्, m., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालसी
मालसी मालसी, f., N. of a plant (com-<BR>monly called Keśapuṣṭa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालहायन
मालहायन मालहायन, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माला
माला माला. See under माल, p. 774.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालायन
मालायन मालायन, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्
मालिन् मालिन्, &c. See p. 774, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्द्य
मालिन्द्य मालिन्द्य, अस्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्य|मालिन्यं
मालिन्य मालिन्य, अम्, n. (fr. मलिन), foul-<BR>ness, uncleanness, dirtiness, pollution, defilement, im-<BR>purity; sinfulness; trouble, affliction; blackness,<BR>obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालु|मालुः
मालु मालु, उस्, m., N. of a particular<BR>mixed caste; N. of one of Śiva's attendants; (उस्),<BR>f. a species of creeper (= पत्त्र-वल्ली, पत्त्र-लता);<BR>a woman.<BR>—मालु-धान, अस्, m. a particular kind<BR>of snake; (ई), f. a species of creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुक
मालुक, अस्, m. Ocimum Sanctum; [cf. कृष्ण-<BR>मालुक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुद
मालुद मालुद, (with Buddhists) a parti-<BR>cular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूर|मालूरः
मालूर मालूर, अस्, m. a fruit tree, Ægle<BR>Marmelos; Feronia Elephantum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्ल|माल्लः
माल्ल माल्ल, अस्, m. (fr. मल्ल), N. of a<BR>particular mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्लवास्तव
माल्लवास्तव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मल्ल-वास्तु), see<BR>Schol. on Pāṇ. IV. 2, 120.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्लवी
माल्लवी, f. a wrestling or boxing match, exhibi-<BR>tion of wrestlers (= मल्ल-यात्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्व्य
माल्व्य माल्व्य, अम्, n. (fr. मल्व), foolish-<BR>ness, inconsiderateness, thoughtlessness, awkwardness,<BR>(opposed to धैर्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मावत्|मावन्त्
मावत् मा-वत्, ind., Ved. like me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माविलम्बम्
माविलम्बम् मा-विलम्बम्, मा-विलम्बितम्.<BR>See under 1. मा, p. 764.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मावेल्ल
मावेल्ल मावेल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a son of Vasu<BR>(prince of Cedi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मावेल्लक
मावेल्लक मावेल्लक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; (also read मावेलक, मावेल्वक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माशब्दिक|माशब्दिकः
माशब्दिक माशब्दिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मा-<BR>शब्दः, see 1. मा), commanding silence, prohibi-<BR>tive, prohibiting; a prohibitor, forbidder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष|माषः
माष माष, अस्, m. a bean, (the sing. is<BR>used for the plant, the pl. for the fruit); Phaseolus<BR>Radiatus, a valued kind of pulse having seeds marked<BR>with black and grey spots, (अकृष्टा माषाः,<BR>‘wild beans,’ epithet of a Ṛṣi-gaṇa, to whom Ṛg-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">Page0775-c+ 79</a>]<BR>veda IX. 86, 1. is ascribed); a particular weight of<BR>gold, &c. = 5 Kṛṣṇalas = (1/16) Suvarṇa, (the weight<BR>in common use is said to be about seventeen grains<BR>troy); a cutaneous eruption resembling beans; a<BR>fool, blockhead.<BR>—माष-तैल, अम्, n. an oily<BR>preparation from beans.<BR>—माष-पर्णी, f. a kind<BR>of leguminous shrub, Glycine Debilis (= पृश्नि-<BR>पर्णी).<BR>—माष-वर्धक, अस्, m. a goldsmith,<BR>jeweler.<BR>—माष-शराविन्, ई, m., N. of a man.<BR>—माष-शस्, ind. after the manner of a Māṣa,<BR>Māṣa-wise, Māṣa by Māṣa.<BR>—माषाज्य (˚ष-<BR>आज्˚), अम्, n. a dish of beans dressed or cooked with<BR>ghee.<BR>—माषाद (˚ष-अद˚) or ˚ष-आद), अस्, m.<BR>‘bean-eater,’ a tortoise.<BR>—माषाश (˚ष-आश˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘bean-eater,’ a horse.<BR>—माषोण or माषोन<BR>(˚ष-ऊन˚), अस्, आ, अम्, minus a Māṣa, lacking one<BR>Māṣa; see Gaṇa Giri-nadyādi to Pāṇ. VIII. 4, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषक|माषकः
माषक, अस्, m. a bean; a particular weight of<BR>gold, &c. = 7 or 8 Guñjās, = according to some,<BR>about 4(1/2) grains; (अस्, आ, अम्), amounting to or<BR>worth a particular number of Māṣas, (at the end of<BR>comps., cf. पञ्च-म्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषशरावि
माषशरावि, इस्, m. a patronymic, (probably fr.<BR>माष-शराविन्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषि
माषि, इस्, m. a patronymic from Māṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषिक
माषिक, अस्, ई, अम्, worth one Māṣa, amounting<BR>to or worth a particular number of Māṣas, (at the<BR>end of comps., cf. पञ्च-म्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषीण|माषीणं
माषीण, अस्, आ, अम्, sown with beans; (अम्), n.<BR>a bean field, a field producing black kidney-beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष्य|माष्यं
माष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fitted or suited for beans<BR>(= माषीण); amounting to or worth a particular<BR>number of Māṣas, (used in this sense at the end of<BR>comps. after numerals, &c., cf. द्वि-म्˚, अध्यर्ध-<BR>म्˚); (अम्), n. a field of kidney-beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्
मास् 1. मास्, आस्, n., Ved. = मांस्, flesh,<BR>meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्
मास् 2. मास्, आस्, m. (fr. rt. 3. मा; accord-<BR>ing to Pāṇini and Vopa-deva used in all cases except<BR>the nom. sing. du. pl. and acc. sing. du., according<BR>to the lexicographers and Garga also in the nom.<BR>sing.; inst. pl., Ved. माद्भिस्), the moon; a<BR>month; [cf. पूर्ण-म्˚, पुष्प-म्˚; cf. also Zend<BR>maoñh, ‘moon, month;’ maoñha, ‘moon:’ Gr.<BR>μήν for μήνς, Ion. μείς, μήν-η, μην-ιαῖο-ς, Æol.<BR>μῆνν-ος for μῆνσ-ος: Lat. mensis, Mena, men-<BR>struus; Goth. mena, menoth-s: Old Germ. ma-<BR>not: Angl. Sax. mona, monadh: Lith. menu,<BR>‘moon;’ ménesi-s, ‘month:’ Old Slav. mese-ci,<BR>‘moon, month.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास|मासं|मासः
मास, अस्, अम्, m. n. (but usually m.), the moon<BR>(cf. पूर्ण-म्˚; in this sense occurring in Ved. in<BR>the comp. सूर्य-मासा, sun and moon, see Ṛg-veda<BR>VIII. 83, 2, X. 64, 3, &c., where, however, मासा<BR>may be referred to 2. मास्); a month or the twelfth<BR>part of the Hindū year, (usually a lunar month con-<BR>sisting of thirty Tithis; there may be also a Saura or<BR>solar month, equal to the sun's passage through a<BR>sign of the zodiac, a Sāvana month consisting of<BR>thirty risings and settings of the sun, a Nakṣatra<BR>month regulated by the lunar asterisms, and a Bār-<BR>haspatya month depending on the motions of the<BR>planet Jupiter; the lunar month being of two kinds,<BR>as reckoned from the new or full moon, completes<BR>six modes of monthly computation); (मासे, after<BR>the lapse of a month); a symbolical expression for<BR>the number twelve; [cf. Lat. mensi-s; Hib. mios;<BR>Cambro-Brit. mis]<BR>—मास-कालिक, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>lasting for a month, available for a month, monthly;<BR>मासकालिकं वेतनम्, a month's wages.<BR>—मास-<BR>चारिक, अस्, आ, अम्, practising (anything) for a month.<BR>—मास-जात, अस्, आ, अम्, one month old.<BR>—मास-<BR>ज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, knowing the months; (अस्), m. a<BR>species of gallinule (= दात्यूह).<BR>—मास-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, monthly [cf. अर्ध-म्˚, संवत्सर-<BR>तम]; completing a full month (= मास-पूरण).<BR>—मास-ताल, अस्, आ, अम्, having time measured<BR>monthwise? (apparently applied to the sound of cym-<BR>bals &c., which lasts a long while).<BR>—मास-तुल्य,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, equal to a month or to a number of months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासत्रय
—मास-त्रय, अम्, n. three months.<BR>—मासत्र-<BR>यावधि (˚य-अव्˚), ind. for the space of three<BR>months.<BR>—मास-देय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be paid or<BR>discharged in a month (as a debt).<BR>—मास-धा,<BR>ind. by the month, monthly.<BR>—मास-पाक, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. maturing or producing results in a month.<BR>—मास-पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, a month before, a month<BR>earlier, (in this sense पूर्व has not the pronominal<BR>declension.)<BR>—मास-प्रमित, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘measured<BR>by months,’ occurring once a month; (अस्), m. new<BR>moon.<BR>—मास-प्रवेश, अस्, m. the beginning of a<BR>month.<BR>—मासप्रवेशानयन (˚श-आन्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of an astronomical work.<BR>—मास-भुक्ति, इस्, f.<BR>the (sun's) monthly course; [cf. पक्ष-भुक्ति.]<BR>—मास-मान, अस्, m. a year.<BR>—मास-वर्त्तिका,<BR>f. a species of wagtail (= सर्षपी).<BR>—मास-शस्,<BR>ind. by the month, monthly, month by month; for<BR>months.<BR>—मास-सञ्चयिक, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>provisions for a month.<BR>—मास-स्तोम, अस्, m., Ved.,<BR>N. of an Ekāha.<BR>—मासाधिप (˚स-अध्˚), अस्, and<BR>Ved. मासाधिपति (˚स-अध्˚), इस्, m. the regent<BR>or planet presiding over a month.<BR>—मासानुमा-<BR>सिक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मास + अनु-मास), performed<BR>from month to month, monthly.<BR>—मासान्त (˚स-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. the end of a month, day of new moon.<BR>—मासापवर्ग (˚स-अप्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. con-<BR>tinuing a month at the most.<BR>—मासावधिक (˚स-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a month as the limit, happen-<BR>ing in the period of a month at the latest.<BR>—मासा-<BR>हार (˚स-आह्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, taking food only once<BR>a month.<BR>—मासोपवास (˚स-उप्˚), अस्, m. fasting<BR>a whole month.<BR>—मासोपवासिनी (˚स-उप्˚), f. a<BR>woman who fasts a whole month; (ironically) a<BR>lascivious woman, procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासक|मासकः
मासक = मास, a month; [cf. चातुर्मासक.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासल|मासलः
मासल, अस्, m. a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासिक|मासिकं|मासिकः
मासिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (at the end of a comp.) re-<BR>lating or pertaining to a month [cf. अर्ध-म्˚];<BR>monthly, happening every month (e. g. मासिकं<BR>श्राद्धम्, a monthly Śrāddha; cf. अष्ट-म्˚);<BR>lasting or continuing for a month (e. g. मासिको<BR>व्याधिः, a sickness which continues for a month);<BR>performed or paid &c. within or after a month,<BR>payable in a month, to be restored in a month;<BR>engaged for a month or by the month (as a teacher,<BR>servant, &c.); dedicated to a particular month;<BR>(अम्), n. a particular Śrāddha or funeral rite per-<BR>formed every new moon.<BR>—मासिकान्न (˚क-अन्˚),<BR>अम्, n. the food given at a monthly oblation to the<BR>Manes (Manu XI. 157).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासीन
मासीन, अस्, आ, अम्, one month old; monthly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्य
मास्य, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comps.) a month<BR>old, lasting or continuing a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासन|मासनं
मासन मासन, अम्, n. Vernonia Anthelmin-<BR>thica; the seed of this plant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासर|मासरः
मासर मासर, अम्, n., Ved. a particular<BR>made dish, a mixture of the water in which rice and<BR>millet are boiled with yeast, grasses, &c.; (अस्), m.<BR>the meal of parched barley mixed with sour milk or<BR>buttermilk and covered with grass; the scum of<BR>boiled rice, rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासुरकर्ण
मासुरकर्ण मासुरकर्ण, अस्, m. a patro-<BR>nymic from Masura-karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासुरी
मासुरी मासुरी, f. a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासूर
मासूर मासूर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मसूर), of<BR>the shape of a lentil, lentil-shaped; consisting or<BR>made of lentils or pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माह्
माह् माह्, cl. 1. P. A. माहति, -ते, &c.,<BR>to measure, mete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहकस्थली
माहकस्थली माहक-स्थली, f., N. of a<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहकस्थलक
माहकस्थलक, pertaining to the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहकि
माहकि माहकि, इस्, m. (probably a patro-<BR>nymic fr. महक), N. of a preceptor; [cf. छन्-<BR>दोग-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहत
माहत माहत, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महत्), see<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">Page0776-b+ 79</a>]<BR>Gaṇa Utsādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 86; (अम्), n. great-<BR>ness (?), see Gaṇa Pṛthvādi to Pāṇ. V. 1, 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहन|माहनः
माहन माहन, अस्, m. a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहा
माहा माहा, f. a cow; [cf. महा, मही,<BR>माहेयी.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुल|माहाकुलः
माहाकुल माहाकुल or माहाकुलीन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम् (fr. महा-कुल), of noble family or lineage,<BR>nobly born, of illustrious descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाचमस्य
माहाचमस्य, अस्, m., Ved. a patronymic from<BR>Mahā-camasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाचित्ति
माहाचित्ति, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. महा-चित्त), see Gaṇa<BR>Sutaṅgamādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनिक
माहाजनिक or माहाजनीन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr.<BR>महा-जन), fit for or suitable to great persons; fit<BR>for merchants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्मिक
माहात्मिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महात्मन्), high-<BR>minded, magnanimous, noble, lofty, exalted, digni-<BR>fied, majestic; of great sanctity or honour; glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्म्य|माहात्म्यं
माहात्म्य, अम्, n. (fr. महात्मन्), greatness<BR>of soul, high-mindedness, magnanimity, exalted state<BR>or position, greatness, majesty, dignity; the peculiar<BR>efficacy or virtue of any divinity or sacred shrine; a<BR>work giving an account of the merits of any holy<BR>place or object; [cf. देवी-म्˚, भाव-नारायण-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहानद
माहानद, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-नद), relating<BR>to a great river, see Gaṇa Utsādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहानस
माहानस, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महानस), relating<BR>or belonging to a large carriage; belonging to a<BR>kitchen, &c.; see Gaṇa Utsādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहानामन
माहानामन or माहानामिक or माहानाम्-<BR>निक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-नाम्नी), Ved. relating to<BR>or connected with the Mahā-nāmnī verses; = महा-<BR>नाम्न्यो ब्रह्मचर्यम् अस्य, = महा-नाम्नीश्<BR>चरति or तासां व्रतं चरति [cf. महानाम्-<BR>निक]; माहानामिक or माहानाम्निक, अस्, m.<BR>a Brāhman versed in the above portion of the<BR>Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहापुत्रि
माहापुत्रि, इस्, इस्, इ (fr. महा-पुत्र), see Gaṇa<BR>Sutaṅgamādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाप्राण
माहाप्राण, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-प्राण), relat-<BR>ing to the hard breathing or aspirate, having the<BR>hard breathing, &c.; see Gaṇa Utsādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>1, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाभाग्य|माहाभाग्यं
माहाभाग्य, अम्, n. = महा-भाग्य, great<BR>good fortune, great prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहारजन
माहारजन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-रजन), dyed<BR>with saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराजिक
माहाराजिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-राज), attached<BR>or devoted to or honouring the reigning prince;<BR>imperial, fit for a great king, royal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराज्य|माहाराज्यं
माहाराज्य, अम्, n. (fr. महा-राज), the rank of<BR>a reigning prince or great sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराष्ट्र
माहाराष्ट्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-राष्ट्र),<BR>belonging to the Mahrattas or Marāṭhas; (ई), f. the<BR>Mahratta language, (more properly Marāṭhī.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहावार्त्तिक
माहावार्त्तिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-वार्त्तिक),<BR>familiar with Kātyāyana's Vārttikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाव्रती
माहाव्रती, f. (fr. महा-व्रत), the doctrine of<BR>the Pāśupatas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाव्रतीय
माहाव्रतीय, a wrong reading for महाव्रतीय,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्र|माहेंद्र|माहेन्द्रः
माहेन्द्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महेन्द्र), relating<BR>or belonging to great Indra (e. g. माहेन्द्रं ध-<BR>नुस्, great Indra's bow, i. e. the rainbow; माहेन्-<BR>द्रम् अम्भस्, great Indra's water, i. e. rain-water;<BR>माहेन्द्री दिश्, great Indra's region, i. e. the eastern<BR>quarter); fit or proper for mighty Indra; eastern,<BR>running or flowing eastward; (अस्), m. = शुभ-<BR>दण्ड-विशेष; a patronymic; epithet of the<BR>seventh Muhūrta; (ई), f. the energy of Indra, one<BR>of the seven divine Mātṛs and one of the Mātṛs of<BR>Skanda; a cow; (scil. दिश्), the east; (scil. ऋच्), a<BR>hymn in praise of Indra (Ved.).<BR>—माहेन्द्र-ज,<BR>आस्, m. pl. (with Jainas) N. of a class of gods.<BR>—मा-<BR>हेन्द्र-वाणी, f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेशी
माहेशी, f. (fr. महेश), a N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेश्वर|माहेश्वरः
माहेश्वर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महेश्वर), relating<BR>or belonging to the great lord Śiva; worshipping<BR>Śiva; (अस्), m. a worshipper of Śiva; (ई), f. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">Page0776-c+ 71</a>]<BR>energy of Śiva, one of the divine Mātṛs (= pārvatī<BR>or Durgā); N. of a river; a species of climbing<BR>plant (= यव-तिक्ता).<BR>—माहेश्वर-तन्त्र and<BR>माहेश्वरी-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—मा-<BR>हेश्वरोपपुराण (˚र-उप्˚), अम्, n., N. of an<BR>Upa-Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिक
माहिक माहिक, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(also read माहिष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिकीप्रस्थ
माहिकीप्रस्थ माहिकीप्रस्थ, N. of a village<BR>in the north of India; see also Schol. on Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहित्थि
माहित्थि माहित्थि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहित्य
माहित्य माहित्य, अस्, m. a patronymic from<BR>Mahita, see Gaṇa Gargādi to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 105;<BR>(माहितास्, m. pl., see Gaṇa Kaṇvādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 111.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहित्र
माहित्र माहित्र, अम्, n., scil. सूक्त, epithet<BR>of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 185 (beginning with the<BR>words महि त्रीणाम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिन|माहिनं
माहिन माहिन, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. मह्),<BR>Ved. great, exalted, joyful, joyous, gladsome, exhila-<BR>rated; giving pleasure, yielding enjoyment; an epi-<BR>thet of the place in which Soma is prepared; (अम्),<BR>n. sovereignty, dominion, kingdom.<BR>—माहिना-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. exhilarated, excited; endowed with<BR>might, mighty; (Sāy. = महिमोपेत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिर|माहिरः
माहिर माहिर, अस्, m. an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष
माहिष माहिष, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. महिष),<BR>coming from or belonging to a buffalo or buffalo cow;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a district; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; [cf. महिष.]<BR>—माहिष-स्थली, f., N.<BR>of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषक|माहिषकः
माहिषक, अस्, m. a buffalo herdsman, buffalo<BR>keeper; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषिक|माहिषिकः
माहिषिक, अस्, m. a buffalo herdsman, one who<BR>lives by keeping or breeding buffaloes; (said to<BR>mean) the paramour of an unchaste woman, one<BR>who lives by the prostitution of his wife; (आ or ई),<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्य|माहिष्यः
माहिष्य, अस्, m. a particular mixed caste, the<BR>son of a Kṣatriya father and a Vaiśya mother, (whose<BR>business is attendance on cattle with the practice of<BR>astronomy and music.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्मती
माहिष्मती माहिष्मती, f. of माहिष्मत<BR>(fr. महिष्मत्), N. of a city founded by Mahiṣ-<BR>mat or by Mucu-kunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्मतेयक
माहिष्मतेयक, see Gaṇa Kattryādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहीन
माहीन माहीन, अस्, m., Ved. (perhaps) a<BR>patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहीयत्व
माहीयत्व माहीयत्व, Ved. beginning with<BR>the word महीय-त्व (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहुरदत्त
माहुरदत्त माहुरदत्त, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहुल
माहुल माहुल, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्र|माहेंद्र|माहेन्द्रः
माहेन्द्र माहेन्द्र. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेय|माहेयः
माहेय माहेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मही), made<BR>of earth, earthen, relating to the earth, terrestrial;<BR>(अस्), m. the son of the earth, the planet Mars;<BR>coral; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (ई), f. a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेल
माहेल माहेल, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मि
मि 1. मि (in some of its senses connected<BR>with rt. 3. मा), cl. 5. P. A. मिनोति, मिनुते,<BR>ममौ or मिमाय, मिम्ये, मास्यति, -ते, अमासीत्,<BR>अमास्त, मातुम्, Ved. to fix or fasten in the earth;<BR>to found, establish; to erect, build; to measure; to<BR>judge, observe, perceive; to cast, throw, throw away<BR>or about, scatter; [cf. मयूख.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्
मित्, त्, f., Ved. a post (erected or fixed in the<BR>ground), a column; [cf. गर्त-म्˚, उप-म्˚, प्र-<BR>ति-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित|मितः
1. मित, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. fixed in the earth,<BR>founded, established; erected, built; cast, thrown,<BR>thrown away, scattered.<BR>—मित-ज्ञु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved.<BR>having well-compacted or firm knees; (Sāy. = सङ्-<BR>कुचित-जानु; मित-ज्ञुभिः = प्रह्वैर् जानुभिः,<BR>with bended knees.) — 1. मित-मेध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having firmly established strength or power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिति|मितिः
1. मिति, इस्, f., Ved. fixing, erecting, establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मि
मि 2. मि, cl. 9. P. A. मिनाति, मिनीते, &c.,<BR>= rt. 1. मी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिक्ष्
मिक्ष् मिक्ष् or मिमिक्ष् (thought by some<BR>to be desiderative forms fr. a lost rt. मिश्, contained<BR>in the words मिश्र, मिश्ल, but referred by native<BR>commentators to the rt. 1. मिह्, q. v.), मिमिक्षति,<BR>मिमिक्षुस्, मिमिक्षे, to mix, stir up, to give a<BR>relish to; (A.) to mix, be mixed: Caus. मेक्षयति,<BR>यितुम्, to stir up, mix, mingle; [cf. म्यक्ष्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिघ्
मिघ् मिघ् = rt. 1. मिह्, only in निमे-<BR>घमान, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. मेघ], Ved.<BR>emitting moisture; (Sāy. = न्यञ्चि अवाङ्मुखानि<BR>वृष्ट्य्-उदकानि सिञ्चत्, sprinkling down rain-<BR>water.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिचिता
मिचिता मिचिता, f., N. of a river; (various<BR>reading for निश्चिता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिच्छक
मिच्छक मिच्छक, अस्, m., N. of a Buddhist<BR>patriarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिछ्|मिच्छ्
मिछ् मिछ्, cl. 6. P. मिच्छति, मिमिच्छ,<BR>मिच्छितुम्, to annoy, hurt, pain; to<BR>obstruct, hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिञ्ज्
मिञ्ज् मिञ्ज्, cl. 10. P. मिञ्जयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to speak; to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिञ्जिकामिञ्जिक
मिञ्जिकामिञ्जिक मिञ्जिका-मिञ्जिक, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of two beings sprung from the seed of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिण्मिण
मिण्मिण मिण्मिण, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking<BR>indistinctly through the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्
मित् मित्. See under rt. 1. मि, p. 776,<BR>col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित|मितः
मित 2. मित, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. मा; for<BR>1. मित see above), measured, meted, measured<BR>off, measured out, containing a particular measure,<BR>measuring, (अक्षराणि षट्-त्रिंशद् गायत्री<BR>मिता, the Gāyatrī measuring or consisting of<BR>thirty-six syllables); defined, limited, bounded;<BR>measured, moderate, regular, scanty, frugal, sparing,<BR>little, brief, succinct^1, concise (e. g. मितं ददाति,<BR>he gives little or sparingly; मिता टीका, a concise<BR>commentary); examined, investigated, known, un-<BR>derstood; (अस्), m., N. of a divine being (associated<BR>with Sammita).<BR>—मितङ्-गम, अस्, आ, अम्, taking<BR>measured steps, going deliberately or slowly; (अस्,<BR>आ), m. f. an elephant.<BR>—२. मित-द्रु, उस्, उस्, उ, run-<BR>ning or moving in a measured manner (Sāy. = परि-<BR>मित-गति; but in Ṛg-veda VII. 7, 1, Sāy. explains<BR>मित-द्रु by दग्ध-द्रुम, consuming forests);<BR>(उस्), m. the ocean, sea.<BR>—मित-ध्वज, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a king.<BR>—मित-भाषितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, speaking<BR>in a measured or deliberate manner, speaking seldom<BR>or sparingly.<BR>—मित-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking<BR>little, seldom speaking; (इणी), f., N. of two concise<BR>commentaries.<BR>—मित-भुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, or मित-<BR>भुज्, क्, क्, क्, eating sparingly, moderate in diet,<BR>moderate, temperate.<BR>—मित-मति, इस्, इस्, इ, narrow-<BR>minded, having a contracted understanding.<BR>—२. मित-<BR>मेध, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having few sacrifices.<BR>—मि-<BR>तम्-पच, अस्, आ, अम्, cooking a measured portion<BR>of food, cooking little; cooking food by measure, a<BR>miser, sparing, niggardly, stingy, covetous; cooking<BR>little (as applied to a culinary utensil), small-sized;<BR>[cf. किम्-पच.]<BR>—मित-राविन्, ई, इणी, इ, roaring or<BR>sounding moderately or in a measured manner, (used<BR>in Nirukta XI. 13. to explain मरुत्; according to<BR>others a wrong reading for अ-म्˚, roaring beyond<BR>measure.)<BR>—मित-रोचिन्, used in Nirukta XI. 13. to<BR>explain मरुत्.<BR>—मित-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, of measured<BR>speech, speaking little, prudent or deliberate in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-b" target="_blank">Page0777-b+ 80</a>]<BR>speaking.<BR>—मित-व्ययिन्, ई, इनी, इ, one who mea-<BR>sures expenses, economical.<BR>—मित-शायिन्, ई, इनी, इ,<BR>sleeping little or sparingly.<BR>—मिताक्षर (˚त-अक्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, having measured syllables, composed in<BR>verse, metrical; short and comprehensive (as a<BR>speech); (आ), f., N. of various concise commentaries;<BR>of a celebrated commentary by Vijñāneśvara on<BR>Yājñavalkya's Dharma-śāstra; of a commentary by<BR>Hara-datta on the Gautama-smṛti; of a commentary<BR>by Nityānandāśrama on the Chāndogya Upaniṣad.<BR>—मिताक्षरा-कार, अस्, m. ‘author of the Mitā-<BR>kṣarā,’ an epithet of Vijñāneśvara.<BR>—मिताक्षरा-<BR>व्याख्यान, अम्, n., N. of a commentary by<BR>Lakṣmī-devī on Vijñāneśvara's Mitākṣarā.<BR>—मि-<BR>ताक्षरा-सिद्धान्त-सङ्ग्रह, अस्, m., N. of an<BR>abbreviation by Rādhā-manohara-śarman of Vijñā-<BR>neśvara's Mitākṣarā; (अस्, आ, अम्), speaking with<BR>caution, acting with circumspection.<BR>—मितार्थ (˚त-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. measured or accurate meaning; (अस्,<BR>आ, अम्,), of measured or restricted meaning.<BR>—मि-<BR>तार्थक (˚त-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, of measured mean-<BR>ing, speaking with caution; (अस्), m. a cautious<BR>envoy.<BR>—मितार्थ-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking<BR>words of well-weighed or measured import.<BR>—मिता-<BR>शन (˚त-अश्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, eating little or sparingly,<BR>moderate in diet, abstemious.<BR>—मिताहार (˚त-आह्˚),<BR>अस्, m. moderate food, scanty diet, moderation in<BR>eating; (अस्, आ, अम्), taking little food, sparing in<BR>diet.<BR>—मितोक्ति (˚त-उक्˚), इस्, m. moderate or in-<BR>frequent speech, speaking little.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिति|मितिः
2. मिति, इस्, f. (for 1. मिति see col. 1), measuring,<BR>measure, weight, value, quantity; determining; accu-<BR>rate knowledge [cf. माति]; proof, evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्वा
मित्वा, ind. having measured, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्र|मित्त्रं|मित्रं|मित्रः
मित्र 1. मित्र, अस्, m. (originally मित्त्र,<BR>fr. rt. 2. मिद्, or according to some fr. rt. मिथ् +<BR>त्र; cf. मेदिन्), a companion, associate, friend, (in<BR>this sense generally neut., except in Ved.; see अम्, n.<BR>below); N. of an Āditya or form of the sun (as a<BR>Vedic deity commonly associated with Varuṇa, both<BR>Mitra and Varuṇa being frequently invoked together<BR>with another of the Ādityas called Aryaman; Mitra<BR>is regarded in Ṛg-veda VIII. 47, 9, as son of Aditi;<BR>elsewhere he is called the deity of the constellation<BR>Anu-rādhā, and father of Ut-sarga: according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda 1. 89, 3, Mitra presides over the<BR>day as Varuṇa over the night; hence the closest con-<BR>nection subsists between these two deities, who are<BR>more frequently invoked together than Varuṇa is<BR>invoked singly; together they uphold and rule the<BR>earth and sky, together they guard the world, toge-<BR>ther they promote religious rites, avenge sin, and<BR>are the lords of truth and light; associated with<BR>Aryaman, they are represented as awful deities, haters,<BR>and dispellers of all falsehood; in only one hymn,<BR>Ṛg-veda III. 59, Mitra is celebrated alone, and is<BR>there described as calling men to activity, sustaining<BR>earth and sky, and beholding all creatures with un-<BR>winking eye; in Ṛg-veda VII. 61, 1, the sun is<BR>described as the eye of Mitra-Varuṇa); the sun;<BR>N. of a Marut; of a son of Vasiṣṭha; of the third<BR>Muhūrta; (आ), f., N. of an Apsaras, (also read<BR>चित्र); N. of the mother of Maitreya and Maitreyī;<BR>N. of one of the wives of Daśa-ratha, (cf. सु-<BR>मित्रा; according to some, in this sense मित्री);<BR>(अम्), n. a friend, (औरसम् मित्रम्, a friend con-<BR>nected by blood relationship); an ally, the next<BR>neighbour of a king; epithet of a mode of fighting,<BR>(also read भिन्न); friendship (Ved.).<BR>—मित्र-<BR>करण, अम्, n. the making of friends, making<BR>one's self friends.<BR>—मित्र-कर्मन्, अ, n. a friendly<BR>office.<BR>—मित्र-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, desirous of friends,<BR>wishing for friends.<BR>—मित्र-कार्य, अम्, n. the<BR>business of a friend, a friendly office, friendship.<BR>—मित्र-कृत्, त्, m. ‘friend-maker,’ N. of a son of<BR>the twelfth Manu.<BR>—मित्र-कृति, इस्, f., Ved. (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy.) a friendly office.<BR>—मित्र-कौस्तु-<BR>भ, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मित्र-क्रु or मित्र-क्रू,<BR>Ved. (probably) N. of an evil being; see Ṛg-veda<BR>X. 89, 14.<BR>—मित्र-गुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, protected by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-c" target="_blank">Page0777-c+ 81</a>]<BR>Mitra; (अस्), m., N. of a man.<BR>—मित्र-गुप्ति, इस्,<BR>f. protection of friends.<BR>—मित्र-घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>‘friend-killing,’ treacherous; (अस्), m., N. of a Rā-<BR>kṣasa; (आ), f., N. of a river, (also read चित्र-<BR>घ्नी.)<BR>—मित्र-ज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a demon (said<BR>to steal oblations).<BR>—मित्र-ता, f. or मित्र-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. friendship, friendliness, alliance, intimacy, (मि-<BR>त्रतां सम्प्राप्तः, one who has become a friend.)<BR>—मित्र-तूर्य, अम्, n., Ved. victory or triumph of<BR>friends.<BR>—मित्र-देव, अस्, m., N. of a man; of one<BR>of the sons of the twelfth Manu.<BR>—मित्र-द्रुह्,<BR>ध्रुक्, क्, क्, or -ध्रुट्, ट्, ट्, (see 2. द्रुह्) or मित्र-<BR>द्रोहिन्, ई, इणी, इ, seeking to injure a friend, the be-<BR>trayer of a friend, a false or treacherous friend; [cf.<BR>Zend mithra-druj.]<BR>—मित्र-द्रोह, अस्, m. injury<BR>or betrayal of a friend.<BR>—मित्र-द्विष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, or<BR>मित्र-द्वेषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, hating or injuring a friend;<BR>(ट्), m. a treacherous friend.<BR>—मित्र-धर्मन्, आ,<BR>m., N. of a demon (said to steal oblations).<BR>—मित्र-<BR>धा, ind., Ved. in a friendly manner.<BR>—मित्र-<BR>धित, अम्, n. or मित्र-धिति, इस्, f. or मित्र-धेय,<BR>अम्, n., Ved. a covenant or contract of friendship,<BR>friendly compact.<BR>—मित्र-पति, इस्, m., Ved. lord of<BR>friends or of friendship.<BR>—मित्र-पद, अम्, n.<BR>‘Mitra's place,’ N. of a particular locality.<BR>—मित्र-<BR>प्रतीक्षा, f. regard for a friend.<BR>—मित्र-बन्धु-<BR>हीन, अस्, आ, अम्, destitute of friends or relations.<BR>—मित्र-बाहु, उस्, m., N. of one of the sons of<BR>the twelfth Manu; of a son of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मित्र-<BR>भ, अम्, n., Ved. a friendly constellation, Mitra's<BR>Nakṣatra, i. e. Anu-rādhā.<BR>—मित्र-भानु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—मित्र-भाव, अस्, m. a state of<BR>friendship, friendliness, friendly disposition.<BR>—मित्र-<BR>भू, ऊस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मित्र-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved.<BR>entertaining or receiving a friend.<BR>—मित्र-भेद,<BR>अस्, m. separation of friends, breach of friendship;<BR>N. of the first book of the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—मित्र-<BR>महस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. (perhaps) having plenty of<BR>friends, rich in friends; having a friendly light,<BR>causing a favourable lustre; (Sāy.) = मित्राणाम्<BR>पूजक, अनुकूल-दीप्तिमत्, हितकारि-तेजस्, &c.<BR>—मित्र-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Vīra-mitrodaya.<BR>—मित्र-यज्ञ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>man.<BR>—मित्र-युज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. joining one's self<BR>to a friend, joining a friend to one's self; (क्), m.,<BR>N. of a man; (जस्), m. pl., N. of his descendants.<BR>—मित्र-युद्ध, अम्, n. a contest of friends, a<BR>strife or quarrel between friends, conflict of allies,<BR>feud.<BR>—मित्र-लब्धि, इस्, f. = मित्र-लाभ below.<BR>—मित्र-लाभ, अस्, m. acquisition of friends or of<BR>friendship, forming friendship; N. of the first book<BR>of the Hitopadeśa.<BR>—मित्र-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>friends, possessing friends; (आन्), m., N. of a demon<BR>(said to steal oblations); N. of a son of the twelfth<BR>Manu; of a son of Kṛṣṇa; (अती), f., N. of a<BR>daughter of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मित्र-वत्सल, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>affectionate towards friends, winning, captivating,<BR>engaging.<BR>—मित्र-वन, अम्, n. ‘Mitra's wood,’<BR>N. of a forest.<BR>—मित्र-वरण, अम्, n. choice of<BR>friends, the act of choosing of friends or acquaint-<BR>ances.<BR>—मित्र-वर्चस्, आस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मित्र-<BR>वर्ध, see Gaṇa Dhūmādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 127;<BR>[cf. मैत्रवर्धक.]<BR>—मित्र-वर्धन, अस्, ई,<BR>अम्, making friends prosperous, prospering friends<BR>(Ved.); N. of a demon (said to steal oblations).<BR>—मित्र-वर्ध्र, see Gaṇa Dhūmādi to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 127.<BR>—मित्र-वर्मन्, आ, m. a proper N.<BR>—मि-<BR>त्र-वाह, अस्, m., N. of a son of the twelfth Manu.<BR>—मित्र-विद्, त्, m. ‘a friend-knower,’ one who knows<BR>friends, (various reading for मन्त्र-विद्, a spy.)<BR>—मित्र-विन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘finding friends, acquir-<BR>ing friends,’ epithet of an Agni; (अस्), m., N. of a<BR>son of the twelfth Manu; of a son of Kṛṣṇa; of<BR>a preceptor; (आ), f. epithet of an Iṣṭi; N. of a wife<BR>of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मित्र-विषय, अस्, m. friendship.<BR>—मित्र-वैर, अम्, n., Ved. dissension among<BR>friends.<BR>—मित्र-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of various<BR>persons.<BR>—मित्र-शिस्, ईस्, ईस्, ईस् (शिस् fr. rt. शास्, cf.<BR>आशिस्), ruling over friends or allies; see Vopa-deva<BR>XXVI. 69.<BR>—मित्र-सप्तमी, f. epithet of the<BR>seventh day in the light half of the month Mārga-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">Page0778-a+ 80</a>]<BR>śīrṣa.<BR>—मित्र-सम्प्राप्ति, इस्, f. ‘acquistion of<BR>friends,’ N. of the second book of the Pañca-tantra.<BR>—मित्र-सह, अस्, आ, अम्, tolerant of friends, in-<BR>dulgent towards friends; (अस्), m., N. of a king,<BR>(also called कल्माष-पाद); N. of a Brāhman.<BR>—मित्र-साह, अस्, आ, अम्, = मित्र-सह above.<BR>—मित्र-साह्वया, f., N. of a divine being.<BR>—मि-<BR>त्र-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a son of the twelfth Manu;<BR>of a grandson of Kṛṣṇa; of a Buddhist; of a king<BR>of the Draviḍa country.<BR>—मित्र-हत्या, f. the mur-<BR>der of a friend.<BR>—मित्र-हन्, आ, m. one who kills<BR>or murders a friend; [cf. मित्र-घ्न.]<BR>—मित्र-<BR>हू = मित्रं ह्वयति, see Vopa-deva XXVI. 72.<BR>—मित्राख्य (˚र-आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, named after<BR>Mitra.<BR>—मित्राचार (˚र-आच्˚), अस्, m. treatment of<BR>friends, conduct to be observed towards a friend.<BR>—मित्रातिथि (˚र-अत्˚), इस्, m., Ved. a proper N.<BR>—मित्रानुग्रहण (˚र-अन्˚), अम्, n. the act of<BR>favouring friends or causing them prosperity.<BR>—मि-<BR>त्राभिद्रोह (˚र-अभ्˚), अस्, m. = मित्र-द्रोह,<BR>q. v.<BR>—मित्रा-वरुण, औ, m. du. Mitra and Varuṇa,<BR>see p. 777, under 1. मित्र; (मित्रा-वरुणयोर् अय-<BR>नम्, N. of a particular festival.)<BR>—मित्रावरुण-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. accompanied by Mitra and<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>—मित्रावरुणीय, अम्, n. the office of the<BR>Ṛtvij Mitrā-varuṇa.<BR>—मित्रा-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a<BR>son of Viśvā-vasu, king of the Siddhas.<BR>—मित्री-कृ,<BR>cl. 8. P. A.<BR>—करोति, -कुरुते, &c., to make a friend,<BR>make any one a friend, make any one friendly to<BR>one's self.<BR>—मित्री-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to<BR>become a friend, make friends with (with inst.).<BR>—मित्री-भूय, ind. becoming a friend or friendly.<BR>—मित्रेरु (˚र-ईरु˚), उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. (Sāy.)<BR>troubling friends, disturbing friends or friendly wor-<BR>shippers (= मित्राणां यजमानानाम् ईरयितृ, =<BR>मित्राणाम् बाधक).<BR>—मित्रेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), scil.<BR>हर, N. of a statue of Śiva erected by Mitra-śarman.<BR>—मित्रोदय (˚र-उद्˚), अस्, m. a friend's welfare,<BR>the success or prosperity of a friend; sunrise; N. of<BR>a work by Mitra-miśra on jurisprudence, (abbre-<BR>viated from वीर-म्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्र|मित्त्रं|मित्रं|मित्रः
2. मित्र, Nom. P. मित्रति, &c., to be friendly,<BR>act in a friendly manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रक
मित्रक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रय
मित्रय, Nom. P. मित्रयति, &c., (probably) to<BR>befriend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयु|मित्रयुः
मित्रयु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. मित्रय above), friendly-<BR>minded; winning or acquiring friends, attractive; =<BR>लोक-यात्राभिज्ञ, possessing worldly prudence, ac-<BR>quainted with the traditions and customs of mankind;<BR>(उस्), m. a friend; N. of a teacher; of a son of<BR>Divo-dāsa; (अवस्), m. pl., N. of a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्राय
मित्राय, Nom. A. मित्रायते, &c., (probably) to<BR>desire or wish for a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रायु
मित्रायु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. मित्राय above), desiring<BR>a friend, seeking friendship (Ved.); (उस्), m., N. of<BR>a son of Divo-dāsa, (also read मित्रेयु); N. of a<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रिन्
मित्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, Ved. befriended, having a friend;<BR>united by friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रिय
मित्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, friendly, coming from or<BR>relating to a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीय
मित्रीय, Nom. P. मित्रीयति, &c., to treat any<BR>one as a friend or companion, to seek to make a<BR>friend of any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीयत्
मित्रीयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming a friend, acting<BR>as a friend, deserving friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रिय
मित्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = मित्रिय; (at the end<BR>of a comp.) see Gaṇa Vargyādi to Pāṇ. VI. 2, 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्वा
मित्वा मित्वा. See p. 777, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्
मिथ् मिथ् (connected with rts. मेथ्,<BR>मिध्, मेध्, 1. मिद्, मेद्, मिल्), cl. 1.<BR>P. A. मेथति, मिथति, मेथते, &c., to meet or<BR>associate with; to unite, pair; to meet as rivals, be<BR>mutually antagonistic, wrangle, contradict, revile; to<BR>take hold of, grasp; to understand, perceive, know;<BR>to hurt, injure; to strike, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथत्या
मिथत्या, ind., Ved. alternately, emulously; (ac-<BR>cording to Sāy. मिथत्या is inst. c. of मिथति =<BR>हिंसा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथस्
मिथस्, ind. together, mutually, reciprocally, with<BR>each other, in common, to one another; from each<BR>other; between one another, secretly, privately, in<BR>secret; alternately, by turns.<BR>—मिथस्-तुर्, Ved.<BR>following closely on one another (as day and night),<BR>alternating, emulous, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda<BR>VI. 49, 3, मिथस्-तुरा = परस्परम् बाध-<BR>यन्त्यौ, mutually opposing each other.)<BR>—मिथ-<BR>स्पृध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, emulating or vying together,<BR>mutually emulous.<BR>—मिथो-अवद्य-प, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. mutually averting calamities.<BR>—मिथो-योध, अस्,<BR>m., Ved. hand to hand fighting with one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथु|मिथुः
मिथु, ind., Ved. falsely, wrongly, pervertedly,<BR>confusedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुन|मिथुनं|मिथुनः
मिथुन, अस्, आ, अम्, paired, forming a pair;<BR>(अस्), m., Ved. a pair (male and female, boy and<BR>girl, son and daughter), a twin couple, a brace,<BR>couple or pair in general, (in Ved. usually m. du.,<BR>e. g. सप्ती मिथुना, a pair of horses; गो-मिथुनौ,<BR>a pair of cows; in the later language mostly neut.);<BR>(अम्), n. a pair, couple, brace; twins; union, junction;<BR>congress of the sexes, pairing, cohabitation, copula-<BR>tion; the sign of the zodiac Gemini, or the third arc<BR>of 30° in a circle, (in this sense also अस्, m.); (in<BR>gram.) a root compounded with a preposition; a<BR>term applied to a particular kind of small statue at<BR>the entrance of a temple.<BR>—मिथुन-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>or मिथुन-भाव, अस्, m. the state of being a<BR>pair or forming a couple.<BR>—मिथुन-व्रतिन्, ई, इनी,<BR>इ, devoted to sexual cohabitation, practising copula-<BR>tion.<BR>—मिथुनी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to<BR>cause to pair or couple, effect the union of the sexes.<BR>—मिथुनी-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, coupling together, co-<BR>habiting, having sexual intercourse.<BR>—मिथुनी-भा-<BR>व, अस्, m. copulation, cohabitation, amorous incli-<BR>nation.<BR>—मिथुनी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to<BR>become paired, to be joined or united in couples, be<BR>arranged in pairs.<BR>—मिथुनी-भूय, ind. being<BR>joined in pairs, forming or uniting in couples.<BR>—मि-<BR>थुने-चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going in pairs, living in<BR>pairs; (अस्), m. the Cakra-vāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनाय
मिथुनाय, Nom. A. मिथुनायते, &c., to co-<BR>pulate, couple, pair, cohabit sexually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुया
मिथुया, ind., Ved. invertedly, distortedly, per-<BR>versely, falsely, incorrectly; [cf. मिथ्या below.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुस्
मिथुस्, ind., Ved. = मिथुया above, (मिथुर्<BR>भू, to turn out badly, fail); reciprocally, mutually<BR>(= मिथस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथूदृश्
मिथू-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, Ved. seen or appearing alter-<BR>nately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथो
मिथो, ind. = मिथस्, q. v., cf. Gaṇa Svarādi to<BR>Pāṇ. I. 1, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्या
मिथ्या, ind. (probably a contracted form for<BR>मिथुया above), invertedly, distortedly, contrarily,<BR>perversely, falsely, incorrectly, wrongly, improperly,<BR>(कथम् मयि मिथ्या प्रवर्तसे, why dost thou<BR>act improperly towards me ?); untruly, deceitfully,<BR>in a lying manner, (with वद्, वच्, ब्रू, to speak<BR>falsely, to make a false assertion); in vain; मिथ्या<BR>at the beginning of a comp. is often equivalent to an<BR>adj., and translatable by ‘false, untrue, sham, unjust,’<BR>&c.; Mithyā, Untruth, is personified as the wife of<BR>A-dharma.<BR>—मिथ्या-कर्मन्, अ, n. false act, failure.<BR>—मिथ्या-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, &c., to make false,<BR>falsify, utter a falsehood, contradict: Caus. P. -कार-<BR>यति, &c., to pronounce [a word] wrongly once:<BR>Caus. A. -कारयते, to pronounce wrongly over and<BR>over again; see Pāṇ. 1. 3, 71.<BR>—मिथ्या-कोप, अस्,<BR>m. feigned resentment, pretended anger.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>क्रय, अस्, m. a false price.<BR>—मिथ्या-ग्रह or<BR>मिथ्याग्रह (˚या-आग्˚), अस्, m. improper persist-<BR>ency, useless obstinacy.<BR>—मिथ्याचरत् (˚या-आच्˚),<BR>अन्, अन्ती, अत्, acting or practising falsehood.<BR>—मि-<BR>थ्या-चर्या, f. false behaviour, hypocrisy.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>चार (˚या-आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dealing falsely, per-<BR>versely; hypocritical, sanctimonious; (अस्), m. im-<BR>proper or incorrect conduct, wrong treatment (in<BR>medicine).<BR>—मिथ्या-जल्पित, अम्, n. a false report<BR>or rumour.<BR>—मिथ्या-ज्ञान, अम्, n. a false con-<BR>ception, misapprehension, error, mistake.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. falsity, unreality; illusion; (with Jainas)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">Page0778-c+ 78</a>]<BR>the lowest of the fourteen steps which lead to final<BR>emancipation; inversion; perversion (as one of the<BR>eighteen faults of a Jaina system).<BR>—मिथ्यात्विन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, being in a state of illusion.<BR>—मिथ्या-दर्-<BR>शन, अम्, n. a false appearance; false doctrine,<BR>heresy.<BR>—मिथ्या-दृष्टि, इस्, f. false doctrine, he-<BR>resy, denial of future existence, atheism.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>ध्यवसिति (˚या-अध्˚), इस्, f. ‘fruitless trouble,’<BR>epithet of a figure of speech expressing the impossi-<BR>bility of a thing by making it depend upon some<BR>impossible contingency (e. g. ‘only one who wears a<BR>crown of air can engage the affections of a harlot’).<BR>—मिथ्या-निरसन, अम्, n. denial by oath.<BR>—मिथ्या-पण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, one who makes a<BR>false pretence to learning, educated or learned only<BR>in appearance.<BR>—मिथ्यापवाद (˚या-अप्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a false accusation.<BR>—मिथ्या-पुरुष, अस्, m. a mere<BR>sham person, a man only in appearance.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>प्रतिज्ञ, अस्, आ, अम्, false to one's promise, faithless,<BR>treacherous.<BR>—मिथ्या-प्रवादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking<BR>falsely, lying.<BR>—मिथ्या-प्रवृत्ति, इस्, f. an erro-<BR>neous course of action, wrong function (of the senses),<BR>misdirected effort.<BR>—मिथ्या-प्रसुप्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>falsely or pretendedly asleep, feigning sleep.<BR>—मि-<BR>थ्या-फल, अम्, n. an imaginary or vain advantage<BR>or reward.<BR>—मिथ्याभिगृध्न (˚या-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, unjustly covetous.<BR>—मिथ्याभिधा (˚या-अभ्˚),<BR>f. a false name.<BR>—मिथ्याभिधान (˚या-अभ्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a false or untrue expression or assertion.<BR>—मिथ्याभियोग (˚या-अभ्˚), अस्, m. an unjust<BR>claim, a false accusation, groundless charge.<BR>—मि-<BR>थ्याभिशंसन, अम्, n. or मिथ्याभिशस्ति (˚या-<BR>अभ्˚), इस्, f. a false accusation.<BR>—मिथ्याभिशंसिन्<BR>(˚या-अभ्˚), ई, m. a false or unjust accuser.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>भिशाप, अस्, m. an unjust claim, false accusation;<BR>a false prediction.<BR>—मिथ्या-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति,<BR>&c., to be false, &c.<BR>—मिथ्या-मति, इस्, f. false<BR>opinion, error, ignorance, mistake.<BR>—मिथ्या-मान,<BR>अस्, m. false pride.<BR>—मिथ्या-योग, अस्, m. wrong<BR>use or employment.<BR>—मिथ्या-वदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्,<BR>speaking falsely.<BR>—मिथ्या-वध्यानुकीर्तन (˚य-<BR>अन्˚), अम्, n. the proclaiming that any one has been<BR>unjustly sentenced to death.<BR>—मिथ्या-वाक्य, अम्,<BR>n. an untruthful speech, falsehood, lie.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>वाच्, क्, क्, क्, whose words are false, untruthful, lying.<BR>—मिथ्या-वाद, अस्, m. false or untruthful speech,<BR>a falsehood, lie; declaring the falsehood of an accu-<BR>sation; (अस्, आ, अम्), speaking untruly, lying.<BR>—मि-<BR>थ्या-वादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, speaking untruly, lying, a<BR>liar; declaring an accusation to be false.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>वार्त्ता, f. false report.<BR>—मिथ्या-व्यापार, अस्, m.<BR>wrong occupation, meddling with another's affairs.<BR>—मिथ्य-साक्षिन्, ई, m. a false witness.<BR>—मिथ्या-<BR>साक्षि-प्रदातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, bringing forward false<BR>witnessess.<BR>—मिथ्याहार (˚या-आह्˚), अस्, m. impro-<BR>per nourishment, wrong diet.<BR>—मिथ्योत्तर (˚या-<BR>उत्˚), अम्, n. (in law) an untrue answer, false or<BR>prevaricating reply.<BR>—मिथ्योपचार (˚या-उप्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a feigned or pretended service or kindness; (in<BR>medicine) wrong treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथि|मिथिः
मिथि मिथि, इस्, m., N. of a son of Nimi<BR>and king of Mithilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथित
मिथित मिथित, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिल|मिथिलः
मिथिल मिथिल, अस्, m., N. of a king, the<BR>founder of Mithilā; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people,<BR>probably the inhabitants; (आ), f., N. of a city said to<BR>have been founded by Mithi or Mithila, (it was the<BR>capital of Videha or the modern Tirhut, and residence<BR>of king Janaka.)<BR>—मिथिलाधिपति (˚ला-अध्˚), इस्,<BR>m. lord of Mithilā, i. e. Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्या
मिथ्या मिथ्या. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्
मिद् 1. मिद्, cl. 1. P. A. मेदति, -ते, &c.,<BR>= rt. मिथ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्
मिद् 2. मिद् or मिन्द्, cl. 1. A. मेदते,<BR>मिमिदे, मेदिष्यति, अमिदत्, मेदितुम्;<BR>cl. 4. P. A. मेद्यति, -ते, मिमेद, मिमिदे, मेदिष्-<BR>यति, अमिदत्, मेदितुम्; cl. 10. P. मिन्दयति,<BR>मेदयति, &c., to become fat; to be unctuous or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">Page0779-a+ 71</a>]<BR>greasy; to liquefy, melt; to feel affection for any one,<BR>love [cf. मित्र, rt. स्निह्]; to rejoice (Ved. ?); Caus.<BR>मेदयति, -यितुम्, to fatten, make fat (Ved.); [cf.<BR>Gr. μειδάω: Old Germ. minna, minni, ‘love:’<BR>Lith. myliu, ‘I love;’ miêlas, ‘dear:’ Russ. milyĭ,<BR>‘kind, affable.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्न
मिन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, become fat, fat; unctuous;<BR>affectionately disposed towards any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्ध|मिद्धं
मिद्ध मिद्ध, अम्, n. sloth, indolence;<BR>sleepiness, torpor; dulness, heaviness of spirits or<BR>intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिध्
मिध् मिध्, cl. 1. P. A. मेधति, -ते,<BR>मेधितुम्, =rt. मिथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्दा
मिन्दा मिन्दा, f., Ved. a bodily defect,<BR>fault, blemish; [cf. Lat. menda.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्मिन|मिन्मिनः
मिन्मिन मिन्मिन = मिण्मिण, p. 777, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्व्
मिन्व् मिन्व् (connected with rts. निन्व्,<BR>सिन्व्), cl. 1. P. मिन्वति, &c., to<BR>sprinkle, moisten, water (= rt. पिन्व्); to worship,<BR>serve, gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमङ्क्षा|मिमंक्षा
मिमङ्क्षा मिमङ्क्षा, f. (fr. Desid. of rt.<BR>मज्ज्) the wish to plunge into water, desire of<BR>bathing or diving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमङ्क्षु
मिमङ्क्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, being about to plunge<BR>into water, desirous of bathing or diving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमत
मिमत मिमत, अस्, m. a proper N.; [cf.<BR>मैमत.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषा
मिमन्थिषा मिमन्थिषा, f. (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. मथ् or मन्थ्), the desire of stirring up or<BR>shaking, desire of destroying, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषु
मिमन्थिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to stir up,<BR>wishing or being about to shake or destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमर्दयिषु
मिमर्दयिषु मिमर्दयिषु or मिमर्दिषु,<BR>उस्, उस्, उ (fr. Desid. of rt. 1. मृद्), wishing to crush,<BR>being about to crush or grind to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमिक्ष
मिमिक्ष मिमिक्ष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Desid. of<BR>rt. 1. मिह्), Ved. mixed, mingled; (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VI. 34, 4, मिमिक्ष may =<BR>वृष्ट्य्-उदकानां सेक्तृ, the sprinkler of rain-<BR>waters.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमिक्षु|मिमिक्षुः
मिमिक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. mixed, mingled; being<BR>mixed, &c.; wishing to rain down, desirous of<BR>bestowing; (Sāy. = वर्षितुम् इच्छत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मियक्ष्
मियक्ष् मियक्ष्. See म्यक्ष्, p. 800, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मियेध|मियेधः
मियेध मियेध, अस्, m. food set before the<BR>gods, a sacrificial meal or oblation, (perhaps) = मेध,<BR>a sacrificial animal or victim, (according to Sāy. de-<BR>rived fr. मेध; cf. Zend myazda.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मियेध्य
मियेध्य, अस्, आ, अम्, partaking of or receiving<BR>the sacrificial food, worthy of the oblation; (Sāy. =<BR>मेधस्य यज्ञस्य योग्य or यज्ञार्ह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिरफ
मिरफ मिरफ, (with Buddhists) a parti-<BR>cular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिराखान
मिराखान मिरा-खान, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Paṭhān chief (खान = خان).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिरिका
मिरिका मिरिका, f. a species of plant, (con-<BR>nected with इरिका, q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिर्मिर
मिर्मिर मिर्मिर, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. a form मिर्<BR>= rt. 1. मिष्), Ved. (according to a commentator)<BR>blinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिल्
मिल् मिल् (thought by some to be ori-<BR>ginally a Nom. fr. a Prākṛt form मिल्ल<BR>= मिश्र), cl. 6. P. A. मिलति, -ते, मिमेल, मि-<BR>मिले, मेलितुम्, (generally P.) to unite, be united<BR>with, join, accompany; to meet together, come toge-<BR>ther; to meet, assemble, associate; to mix, combine,<BR>be present at; to be connected with; to meet or fall<BR>in with (with inst. or gen. or loc. of the person or<BR>with सह and inst.); to find; to meet, encounter,<BR>(द्वन्द्व-युद्धेन द्वौ मिलितौ, two persons<BR>met in single combat); to clash, impinge, concur;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">Page0779-b+ 76</a>]<BR>to happen, come to pass: Caus. मेलयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>cause to meet, bring together, assemble, convene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलत्
मिलत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, joining, accompanying;<BR>meeting; assembling; concurring, combining; hap-<BR>pening.<BR>—मिलद्-व्याध, अस्, आ, अम्, uniting with<BR>hunters, accompanied by huntsmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलन|मिलनं
मिलन, अम्, n. the act of mixing with, coming<BR>in contact with, associating with; concurring, en-<BR>countering, coalescing, meeting; contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलित|मिलितः
मिलित, अस्, आ, अम्, united, mixed, combined,<BR>connected; found, met, encountered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलित्वा
मिलित्वा, ind. having met together, having united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलिन्
मिलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, mixing with, combined with,<BR>provided with, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिला
मिला मिला in दुर्-मिला, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलिन्दक|मिलिंदक|मिलिंदकः|मिलिन्दकः
मिलिन्दक मिलिन्दक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलीमिलिन्
मिलीमिलिन् मिलीमिलिन्, ई, m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva (which is said to contain a Mantra addressed to<BR>Śiva, consisting of the following eighteen syllables,<BR>ॐ, रुद्र चीलि चीलि चिलि चिलि मिलि मिलि, ॐ स्वाहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिल्ला
मिल्ला मिल्ला, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्
मिश् मिश् (connected with rt. मश्), cl.<BR>1. P. मेशति, मेशितुम्, to make a noise,<BR>sound; to be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिशर
मिशर मिशर, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिशि|मिशिः
मिशि मिशि, इस्, or मिशी, f. Anethum Pan-<BR>mori and Anethum Sowa (= मिसि); common anise;<BR>Indian spikenard, Nardostachys Jatamansi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिशृष
मिशृष मिशृष, N. of a place (also<BR>written मिश्रिष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र्
मिश्र् मिश्र् or मिस्र् (probably a Nom.<BR>fr. मिश्र below), cl. 10. P. मिश्रयति,<BR>मिश्रापयति, &c., to mix, mingle, blend, combine,<BR>unite, mix with (with inst.); to add; [cf. Gr. μίσγ-ω,<BR>μίγ-νυ-μι, ἐ-μίγ-ην, ἐ-μίχθη-ν, μίγ-α, μίγ-δα, μίγ-δην,<BR>μιγ-άδες, μίξις: Lat. misc-e-o, mix-tu-s, mis-<BR>tu-s, mix-tû-ra, mis-tû-ra, mix-ti-o, mis-ti-o,<BR>misc-ellu-s, miscell-âneu-s: Old Germ. miscjan,<BR>misk-iu, ‘mix thou:’ Angl. Sax. miscan: Slav.<BR>mes-i-ti: Lith. misz-ti; misz-ini-s, ‘a mongrel;’<BR>maisz-y-ti, ‘to mix.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र|मिश्रं|मिश्रः
मिश्र, अस्, आ, अम्, (thought by some to be fr. a<BR>lost rt. मिश्, connected with मिक्ष्, desiderative of<BR>rt. 1. मिह्; by others referred to rt. मिश् above),<BR>mixed, mingled, blended, joined; mixed or blended<BR>with (with inst. or sometimes gen.), combined;<BR>associated, connected, (न मिश्रः स्यात् पापकृद्-<BR>भिः, one should not associate with the wicked);<BR>mixing, adulterating (e. g. mixing or adulterating<BR>corn); tangled, intertwined; manifold, diverse; (at<BR>the end of a comp.) having a mixture or mixed<BR>collection of anything, for the most part consisting<BR>of, consisting chiefly of (e. g. बदरी-मिश्रं का-<BR>ननम्, a forest consisting for the most part of<BR>Badarī trees; आर्य-विदग्ध-मिश्रास्, for the most<BR>part worthy and learned persons); (अस्), m. a respect-<BR>able person (cf. आर्य-म्˚; in this sense frequently<BR>used at the end or beginning of a proper name,<BR>especially that of a scholar, by way of respect, cf.<BR>कृष्ण-म्˚, भाव-म्˚, मधु-म्˚; and some-<BR>times used alone as an abbreviation for a name ending<BR>in मिश्र, e. g. मिश्र = मण्डन-मिश्र); N. of the<BR>author of the Karma-pradīpa and of various other<BR>persons; epithet of a kind of elephant; (अम्), n.<BR>mixing, mixture; a species of radish (= चाणक्य-<BR>मूलक).<BR>—मिश्र-केशव, अस्, m., N. of an author<BR>(= केशव-दास).<BR>—मिश्र-केशी, f., N. of an Apsaras.<BR>—मिश्र-चतुर्भुज, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मिश्र-<BR>ज, अस्, m. ‘of mixed birth or breed,’ a mule.<BR>—मिश्र-<BR>जाति, इस्, इस्, इ, being of mixed birth or breed, of<BR>mixed parentage, any one whose parents belong to<BR>different castes.<BR>—मिश्र-ता, f. mixedness, the being<BR>mixed, mixing, mingling.<BR>—मिश्र-दिन-कर, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a commentator on the Śiśupāla-badha.<BR>—मिश्र-धान्य, अस्, आ, अम्, made by mixing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">Page0779-c+ 79</a>]<BR>various kinds of grain; (अम्), n. mixed grain.<BR>—मि-<BR>श्र-पुष्पा, f. Trigonella Fœnum Græcum (= मे-<BR>थिका).<BR>—मिश्र-भाव, अस्, m., N. of the author<BR>of the Bhāva-prakāśa, a medical work, (also भाव,<BR>भाव-मिश्र.)<BR>—मिश्र-लटकन, अस्, m., N. of<BR>the father of Miśra-bhāva.<BR>—मिश्र-वर्ण, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, being of a mixed colour; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>black aloe wood (= कृष्णागुरु).<BR>—मिश्रवर्ण-<BR>फला, f. Solanum Melongena.<BR>—मिश्र-व्यवहार,<BR>अस्, m. (in arithmetic) investigation of mixture,<BR>ascertainment of composition (as principal and in-<BR>terest joined, &c.).<BR>—मिश्र-शब्द, अस्, m. a mule<BR>(= मिश्र-ज).<BR>—मिश्री-करण, अम्, n. the act of<BR>mixing, an ingredient, seasoning.<BR>—मिश्री-कृ, cl. 8.<BR>-करोति, &c., to make mixed, mix, mingle.<BR>—मिश्री-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. becoming mixed, mixing, mingling.<BR>—मिश्री-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become mixed, mix, intertwine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रक|मिश्रकं|मिश्रकः
मिश्रक, अस्, आ, अम्, mixing, adulterating, mingled,<BR>miscellaneous; mixed, adulterated; (अस्), m. a mixer<BR>or compounder; an adulterator of articles of com-<BR>merce, mixer of bad wares with good ones; (अम्),<BR>n. salt produced from salt soil; N. of a Tīrtha; of<BR>a grove or garden of paradise; a particular kind<BR>of song or singing.<BR>—मिश्रका-वण, अम्, n., N. of<BR>Indra's pleasure-grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रण|मिश्रणं
मिश्रण, अम्, n. the act of mixing, uniting; (in<BR>arithmetic) addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रणीय
मिश्रणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be mixed or mingled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रित|मिश्रितं
मिश्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, mixed, mingled, blended,<BR>united, joined; added; respected, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रिन्
मिश्रिन्, ई, m., N. of a Nāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रेया
मिश्रेया, f. (connected with मिशि, q. v.), Anethum<BR>Panmori or a species of anise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्ल
मिश्ल = मिश्र in आ-म्˚, नि-म्˚, सम्-म्˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्
मिष् 1. मिष् [cf. rt. मील्], cl. 6. P. मि-<BR>षति, मिमेष, मेषिष्यति, अमेषीत्,<BR>मेषितुम् (the simple rt. appears to be used only<BR>in the present participle), to open the eyes, have the<BR>eyes open; to look at, look at or look on unwil-<BR>lingly, look on angrily or with the eyes contracted,<BR>wink at (generally used in the present participle,<BR>the construction being that of a genitive absolute,<BR>e. g. मिषतो बन्धु-वर्गस्य, the whole number<BR>of relatives looking helplessly on, i. e. before their<BR>very eyes or in spite of them; मिषतां वः, in<BR>spite of you); to rival, contend with, resist, emulate;<BR>[cf. Gr. μῖσος perhaps also μύω: Lat. mico; per-<BR>haps nico, nic-to, fr. nimic-o, nimic-to = निमि-<BR>षामि: Russ. migaju, mischu, ‘I wink:’ Lith.<BR>mirkloju, ‘I wink;’ mêgmi, ‘I sleep.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष|मिषं|मिषः
मिष, अस्, m. rivalry, emulation, envy; (अम्), n.<BR>deceit, fraud, trick, illusion, false appearance (e. g.<BR>सूद-मिषं श्रितः, having assumed the form of<BR>a cook; दर्शन-मिषात्, under the pretext of<BR>seeing); [cf. मृषा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्
मिष् 2. मिष् (connected with rt. 3.<BR>मृष्), cl. 1. P. मेषति, मिमेष,<BR>मेषितुम्, to sprinkle, moisten, wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्ट|मिष्टं|मिष्टः
मिष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled, moistened; nice,<BR>savoury, dainty, delicate; sweet, sugary, (in this sense<BR>thought by some to be for 1. मृष्ट fr. rt. 1. मृज्, to<BR>cleanse); मिष्टम् पयस्, water; (अम्), n. a sweet-<BR>meat; a dainty or savoury dish.<BR>—मिष्ट-कर्त्रि,<BR>ता, त्री, तृ, a maker of dainties or delicacies, a<BR>skilful cook.<BR>—मिष्ट-पाचक, अस्, इका, अम्, cook-<BR>ing savoury food or delicacies.<BR>—मिष्ट-भुज्, क्, क्,<BR>क्, an eater of dainties, eating delicacies.<BR>—मिष्ट-<BR>वाक्य, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking pleasantly or agreeably.<BR>—मिष्टान्न (˚ट-अन्˚), अम्, n. sweet or savoury<BR>food, sweetmeats, sauce, gravy, seasoning, a mixture<BR>of sugar and acids &c. eaten with rice or bread.<BR>—मिष्टाशा (˚ट-आशा), f. desire for delicacies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषमिषाय
मिषमिषाय मिषमिषाय, Nom. A. मिष-<BR>मिषायते, &c. (an onomatopoetic word), to crackle,<BR>crepitate, make a crackling sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषि|मिषिः
मिषि मिषि, इस्, f. spikenard; fennel, &c.,<BR>= मिसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषिका
मिषिका, f. Nardostachys Jatamansi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिस्
मिस् मिस्, cl. 4. P. मिस्यति, &c., Ved.<BR>to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसर
मिसर मिसर, N. of a place, (perhaps =<BR>मिस्र्, Egypt; cf. मिशर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसरु
मिसरु, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसरूमिश्र
मिसरू-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of the author of the<BR>Vivāda-candra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसि|मिसिः
मिसि मिसि, इस्, f. a sort of fennel, Anethum<BR>Sowa; Anethum Panmori; common anise, Pimpi-<BR>nella Anisum; spikenard, Nardostachys Jatamansi;<BR>a sort of lovage; = अज-मोदा; = उशीरी; [cf. मिशि,<BR>मिषि.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिस्र्
मिस्र् मिस्र्. See मिश्र्, p. 779, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिह्
मिह् 1. मिह्, cl. 1. P. (in poetry also A.)<BR>मेहति (-ते), मिमेह, मेक्ष्यति, अमि-<BR>क्षत्, मेढुम्, to make water, void or pass urine,<BR>to rain down moisture, wet, moisten, sprinkle; to<BR>emit seed or seminal fluid (= रेतः-सेकं कृ):<BR>Caus. मेहयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अमीमिहत्, to cause<BR>to make water, &c.: Desid. मिमिक्षति, to wish<BR>to mix or stir up, to mix, unite, mix intimately [cf.<BR>मिक्ष्]: Intens. मेमेह्यते; [cf. Gr. ὀ-μιχ-έ-ω,<BR>ὤμιξα, ὄ-μιχ-μα, ὀμίχ-λη, ὀμίχλη, μοιχ-ό-ς, μοιχ-ά-ω,<BR>μιαίνω, μιορός: Lat. mi-n-g-o, mêj-o, mic-tu-s:<BR>Goth. maihstu-s, ‘dung:’ Angl. Sax. mig, mîge,<BR>mâh, migon: Mod. Germ. Mist: Iceland. mig:<BR>Lith. myz-u; mig-là, ‘mist:’ Slav. mĭg-la.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिह्
2. मिह्, ट्, f., Ved. mist, fog; falling of water;<BR>मिहो नपात्, the demon of the mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिका
मिहिका, f. mist, fog; frost, snow; [cf. महिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिर|मिहिरः
मिहिर, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. 1. 52. fr.<BR>rt. 1. मिह् above), the sun (= the Persian مهر); a<BR>cloud (as raining down moisture); wind, air; the<BR>moon; an old man, sage; N. of an author (an<BR>abbreviation of Varāha-mihira; cf. पद्म-म्˚).<BR>—मिहिर-कुल, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मिहिर-<BR>दत्त, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मिहिर-पुर, अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a city built by Mihira-kula.<BR>—मिहिर-रति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of a man (son of Bhaganarāya).<BR>—मिहि-<BR>रेश्वर (˚र-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a temple built by<BR>Mihira-kula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिराण|मिहिराणः
मिहिराण, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ|मीढं|मीढः
मीढ, अस्, आ, अम्, passed (as urine); urined,<BR>watered; (अम्), n., also मीऌह, अम्, n., Ved. a<BR>battle, combat, struggle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढुष
मीढुष, अस्, m., N. of a son of Indra by<BR>Paulomī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ्वस्
मीढ्वस्, आन्, असी, अस् (the declension follows that<BR>of a perf. part., e. g. acc. sing. masc. मीढ्वांसम्,<BR>dat. मीढुषे or मीऌहुषे, cf. Mahā-bh. Vana-p.<BR>1628, voc. Ved. मीढवस्), bountiful, liberal (applied<BR>to Rudra, Agni, Varuṇa, Mitra, Viṣṇu, Parjanya,<BR>and Indra); pouring forth seed (= रेतः-सेक्तृ),<BR>prolific (applied to a goat); N. of a son of Dakṣa.<BR>—मीढुष्-टम, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. most bountiful<BR>or liberal; (अस्), m. the sun; Śiva; a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिलारोप्य
मिहिलारोप्य मिहिलारोप्य, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>city in the south of India; [cf. महिलारोप्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
मी 1. मी, cl. 9. P. A. मीनाति, मीनीते (Ved.<BR>मिनाति), मिमाय (3rd du. मिम्यतुस्),<BR>मिम्ये, मास्यति, -ते, अमासीत्, अमास्त, मातुम्<BR>(Ved. forms मेष्ट, अमेषन्त, अमायि, Ved. inf.<BR>with प्र, -मियम्, -मिये, -मेतोस्; ind. part. -माय,<BR>cf. प्र-मी; chiefly Vedic), to lessen, diminish,<BR>reduce; to injure, destroy, kill; to violate, transgress;<BR>to annul, change, alter; to be lessened, disappear, be<BR>lost or destroyed; to stray, go astray; cl. 4. A. -मी-<BR>यते, to perish, be destroyed, die: Caus. मापयति,<BR>Aor. अमीमपत्, to cause to perish, destroy, kill,<BR>Pāṇ. VII. 4, 93: Desid. मित्सति, -ते, Pāṇ. VII. 4,<BR>54; [cf. Lat. pro-minere, e-minere, minere, pro-<BR>minare, e-minus, co-minus, minari.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
2. मी in मन्यु-मी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीत
मीत, अस्, आ, अम्, in प्र-मीत. See प्र-मी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीन|मीनः
मीन, अस्, m. (according to Uṇādi-s. III. 3. fr.<BR>rt. 1. मी above), a fish [cf. नड-म्˚]; the sign of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">Page0780-b+ 77</a>]<BR>the zodiac, Pisces; N. of a teacher of the Yoga<BR>system, = मीन-नाथ; (आ), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Uṣā and wife of Kaśyapa.<BR>—मीन-केतन, अस्, m.<BR>‘fish-bannered,’ an epithet of the god of love.<BR>—मीन-गन्धा. f. an epithet of Satya-vatī; [cf.<BR>मत्स्य-गन्धा.]<BR>—मीन-गोधिका, f. a pool, pond.<BR>—मीन-घातिन्, ई, m. ‘fish-killer,’ a fisherman; a<BR>crane.<BR>—मीन-ता, f. the state or condition of a fish.<BR>—मीन-धावन-तोय, अम्, n. water in which fish<BR>have been washed.<BR>—मीन-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>teacher of the Yoga system.<BR>—मीन-नेत्रा, f. a<BR>species of Dūrvā grass (= गण्ड-दूर्वा; cf. नेत्र-<BR>मीना).<BR>—मीन-रङ्क or मीन-रङ्ग, अस्, m. a<BR>kingfisher.<BR>—मीन-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मीन-राज, अस्, m. the king of the fishes; N. of<BR>an astrologer.<BR>—मीनराज-जातक, अम्, n., N. of<BR>an astrological work by Yavaneśvara.<BR>—मीन-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, possessing fish, abounding in fish.<BR>—मी-<BR>नाक्ष (˚न-अक्˚), अस्, m. ‘fish-eyed,’ N. of a<BR>Rākṣasa; (ई), f. a species of Soma plant, a kind of<BR>Dūrvā grass [cf. मत्स्याक्षी]; N. of a daughter of<BR>Kuvera.<BR>—मीनाघातिन् (˚न-आघ्˚), ई, m. = मीन-<BR>घातिन्, q. v.<BR>—मीनाण्ड (˚न-अण्˚), अम्, n. fish-<BR>spawn, roe, milt; (ई), f. moist or brown sugar.<BR>—मीनालय (˚न-आल्˚), अस्, m. ‘abode of fish,’ the<BR>sea, ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनर|मीनरः
मीनर, अस्, m. a kind of sea-monster (= मकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाम्रीण|मीनाम्रीणः
मीनाम्रीण, अस्, m. = दर्दुराम्र, a kind of<BR>sauce or condiment, fish-sauce; a wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
मी 3. मी, cl. 1. 10. P. मयति, माययति,<BR>&c., to go, move; to understand, know;<BR>[cf. Lat. meare, movere.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीडम्
मीडम् मीडम्, ind. in a low tone, softly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ|मीढं|मीढः
मीढ मीढ, मीढ्वस्, मीढुषे, मीऌहुषे,<BR>&c. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीन|मीनः
मीन मीन. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीम्
मीम् मीम्, cl. 1. P. मीमति, मीमितुम्,<BR>cl. 10. P. (or Caus.) मीमयति, -यितुम्,<BR>to go, move; to sound; [cf. rt. 2. मा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांस
मीमांस मीमांस, Desid. base of rt. मन्,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसक|मीमांसकः
मीमांसक, अस्, m. one who thinks over or<BR>reflects deeply upon, one who examines or proves;<BR>an examiner, investigator, prover; a follower of the<BR>Pūrva-mīmāṃsā system, (see below.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसन|मीमांसनं|मीमांसनः
मीमांसन, अस्, m. one who examines or proves,<BR>a tester, prover, examiner, investigator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसा
मीमांसा, f. reflection, consideration, opinion,<BR>investigation, examination, discussion, (काव्य-म्˚,<BR>the theory of poetry, art of poetry; N. of a work);<BR>‘examination (of the sacred text),’ N. of one of three<BR>great divisions of orthodox Hindū philosophy (divided<BR>like the Nyāya and Sāṅkhya into two systems, viz.<BR>the Pūrva-mīmāṃsā or Karma-mīmāṃsā founded by<BR>Jaimini, and the Uttara-mīmāṃsā or Brahma-mīmāṃsā<BR>or Śārīraka-mīmāṃsā by Bādarāyaṇa, the latter, how-<BR>ever, is more commonly called the Vedānta system,<BR>while the Pūrva-mīmāṃsā is usually called the<BR>Mīmāṃsā; though the Mīmāṃsā by Jaimini is classed<BR>among the six orthodox systems of philosophy, it<BR>does not concern itself like the others with the<BR>nature of soul, mind, and matter, but rather with a<BR>correct interpretation of the ritual of the Veda and<BR>the solution of doubts and discrepancies in regard to<BR>the Vedic texts caused by the discordant explanations<BR>of opposite schools; it may therefore be described as<BR>a critical commentary on the first or ritual portion<BR>of the Veda, and its only claim to the title of a<BR>philosophy consists in its philosophical method of<BR>interpretation, the topics being arranged according<BR>to particular categories, such as authoritativeness,<BR>indirect precept, &c., and treated according to a<BR>kind of logical sequence, which commences with<BR>the proposition to be discussed, the doubt arising<BR>about it, the Pūrva-pakṣa or primâ facie and wrong<BR>view of the question, the right argument or refuta-<BR>tion of the Pūrva-pakṣa, and the conclusion; see,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">Page0780-c+ 78</a>]<BR>moreover, पूर्व-मीमांसा: Jaimini, whose date is<BR>unknown, taught his system in twelve books, each<BR>book containing either four or eight chapters, and<BR>each chapter being subdivided into sections compris-<BR>ing one or more Sūtras; the oldest commentary on<BR>these obscure aphorisms being the Bhāṣya of Śabara-<BR>svāmin, explained by the great Mīmāṃsā authority<BR>Kumārila-svāmin or Kumārila-bhaṭṭa, and again elu-<BR>cidated by Mādhavācārya in the Jaiminīya-nyāya-<BR>mālā-vistara).<BR>—मीमांस-कृत्, त्, m. ‘the author of<BR>the Mīmāṃsā system,’ an epithet of Jaimini.<BR>—मी-<BR>मांसा-कौतूहल-वृत्ति, इस्, f., N. of a commen-<BR>tary by Vāsudeva Adhvarin (also called Vāsudeva<BR>Dīkṣita) on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtras of Jaimini.<BR>—मी-<BR>मांसा-कौस्तुभ, अस्, m., N. of a commentary by<BR>Khaṇḍa-deva on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtras of Jaimini.<BR>—मीमांसा-जीव-रक्षा, f., N. of a Mīmāṃsā<BR>work.<BR>—मीमांसा-तत्त्व-चन्द्रिका, f., N. of a<BR>work by Gopāla-bhaṭṭa on various Mīmāṃsā topics.<BR>—मीमांसा-तन्त्र-वार्त्तिक, अम्, n., N. of a com-<BR>mentary by Kumārila-svāmin on the Sūtras of Jai-<BR>mini.<BR>—मीमांसा-नय-विवेक, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>commentary by Bhavanātha-miśra on the Mīmāṃsā-<BR>sūtras of Jaimini.<BR>—मीमांसा-न्याय-प्रकाश, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a celebrated elementary work on the<BR>Mīmāṃsā system by Āpa-deva (son of Ananta-deva<BR>and pupil of Govinda).<BR>—मीमांसा-परिभाषा, f.,<BR>N. of an elementary treatise by Kṛṣṇa-dīkṣita on<BR>the Mīmāṃsā.<BR>—मीमांसा-भाष्य-विवरण, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a commentary by Kumāra-svāmin on a<BR>work entitled Mīmāṃsā-bhāṣya.<BR>—मीमांसार्थ-<BR>प्रदीप (˚सा-अर्˚), अस्, m., N. of a disquisition by<BR>Śaṅkara-śukla on the provableness of the Veda.<BR>—मी-<BR>मांसा-विधि-भूषण, अम्, n., N. of a Mīmāṃsā<BR>work by Gopāla-bhaṭṭa, written in refutation of<BR>the Vidhi-rasāyana.<BR>—मीमांसा-शिरोमणि, इस्, m.<BR>‘crest-gem of the Mīmāṃsā,’ epithet of an author,<BR>(also called Nīla-kaṇṭha.)<BR>—मीमांसा-सर्वस्व,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a work by Halāyudha.<BR>—मीमांसा-<BR>सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of the twelve books of aphorisms<BR>by Jaimini on the interpretation of the Veda; see<BR>मीमांसा, col. 2.<BR>—मीमांसा-स्तवक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a Mīmāṃsā work by Rāghavānanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसित्वा
मीमांसित्वा, ind. having considered or reflected<BR>upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांस्य
मीमांस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be thought over or<BR>reflected upon, to be examined or considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीर|मीरः
मीर मीर, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 1. मि,<BR>perhaps connected with rt. 1. मिह्), the sea, ocean;<BR>a particular part of a mountain; a limit, boundary;<BR>a drink, beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीरमीरसुत
मीरमीरसुत मीरमीर-सुत, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>मीरमीरा, f., N. of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मील्
मील् मील् (connected with rt. 1. मिष्,<BR>and perhaps originally a Nom.), cl. 1.<BR>P. मीलति, मिमील, मीलिष्यति, अमीलीत्, मीलितुम्,<BR>to close (the eyes), wink, twinkle, close or contract<BR>the eyelids; to close, be closed (as the eyes); to fade,<BR>disappear, vanish; to assemble, gather together, be col-<BR>lected (= rt. मिल् intransitively): Caus. मीलयति, Aor.<BR>अमिमीलत् and अमीमिलत्, to cause to close, close<BR>(applied to the blossom of flowers as well as to the<BR>eyes): Desid. मिमीलिषति: Intens. मेमील्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलत्
मीलत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, closing (as the eyes); wink-<BR>ing, twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलन|मीलनं
मीलन, अम्, n. the act of closing the eyes;<BR>winking, blinking, twinkling; the closing of a<BR>flower; (in rhetoric) a covert or concealed simile,<BR>see मीलित below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलयित्वा
मीलयित्वा, ind. having closed (as the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलिका
मीलिका in नील-मीलिक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलित|मीलितं
मीलित, अस्, आ, अम्, closed; twinkled; half opened,<BR>unblown, partly opened (as a young bud &c.); dis-<BR>appeared, vanished; assembled, gathered together;<BR>(अम्), n. a simile merely implied (e. g. क्षौम-<BR>वत्यो न लक्ष्यन्ते ज्योत्स्नायाम्, ‘clad in linen<BR>they are not perceived in the moonlight,’ where<BR>comparison between the whiteness of the linen and<BR>of the moonlight is implied.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीव्
मीव् 1. मीव्, cl. 1. P. मीवति, मीवितुम्,<BR>to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत|मूतः
1. मूत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see rt. 1. मू), moved,<BR>in काम-मूत, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीव्
मीव् 2. मीव् (connected with rt. पीव्),<BR>cl. 1. P. मीवति, मीवितुम्, to grow fat,<BR>to be large or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवग
मीवग मीवग, (with Buddhists) a parti-<BR>cular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवर|मीवरः
मीवर मीवर, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. rt. 1. मी),<BR>hurting, killing, hurtful, injurious, mischievous; vene-<BR>rable, worthy of esteem; (अस्), m. a general, leader<BR>of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवा
मीवा मीवा, f. (probably fr. 2. मी; said to<BR>be fr. 1. मी), the tape-worm, a worm generated in<BR>the intestines, Ascarides; air, wind, (in this sense<BR>also, according to some, मीवन्, आ, m.); = शीकर (?);<BR>= सार (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मु|मुः
मु मु, उस्, m. (fr. rt. 1. मू, q. v.), a bond,<BR>binding, confinement; an epithet of Śiva; final<BR>emancipation; a funeral pile; a reddish brown or<BR>tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुंसल
मुंसल मुंसल, N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकन्दक|मुकंदक|मुकंदकः|मुकन्दकः
मुकन्दक मुकन्दक, अस्, m. probably an<BR>error for सु-कन्दक, an onion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकय
मुकय मुकय, अस्, ई, m. f., see Pāṇ. IV.<BR>1, 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकाबिला
मुकाबिला मुकाबिला = مقابلة<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकारिणा
मुकारिणा मुकारिणा = مقارنة<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकु|मुकुः
मुकु मुकु, उस्, m. = मुक्ति, liberation; (an<BR>artificial word, formed fr. rt. 2. मुच्, to explain मु-<BR>कुन्-द, q. v., for which purpose others assume मु-<BR>कुम्, ind.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुट|मुकुटं
मुकुट मुकुट, अम्, n. a tiara, diadem,<BR>crown (said to be crescent-shaped; the किरीट being<BR>pointed, and the मौलि having three points); a<BR>crest; a peak, point, head [cf. त्रि-म्˚]; N. of a<BR>place; (अस्), m. a proper N. (contracted fr. राज-<BR>मुकुट); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people or of a race;<BR>(आ), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending upon<BR>Skanda; (ई), f. snapping the fingers (= मुचुटी,<BR>fr. rt. 2. मुच्).<BR>—मुकुट-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>sacred bathing-place.<BR>—मुकुटे-कार्षापण, अम्,<BR>n. epithet of a tax or tribute raised for a royal<BR>diadem (in the east of India).<BR>—मुकुटेश्वर (˚ट-<BR>ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of a king; (ई), f. a N. of Dā-<BR>kṣāyaṇī in Mākoṭa (Mukuṭa).<BR>—मुकुटेश्वर-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुटिन्
मुकुटिन्, ई, इनी, इ, crowned, wearing a diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुट्ट
मुकुट्ट मुकुट्ट, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(also read सुकुट्ट.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुण्टी
मुकुण्टी मुकुण्टी, f. a kind of weapon;<BR>(perhaps an error for सु-कुण्ठी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्द|मुकुंद|मुकुंदः|मुकुन्दः
मुकुन्द मुकुन्-द, अस्, m. (according to an<BR>artificial etymology, fr. मुकु, q. v., मुकुन्-द<BR>being said to mean ‘giver of liberation’), N. of<BR>Viṣṇu (sometimes transferred to Śiva); of a parti-<BR>cular treasure; a kind of precious stone; quicksilver;<BR>the resin of Boswellia Thurifera, gum olibanum; a<BR>kind of drum or kettle-drum; N. of various learned<BR>men (= गोविन्द, वाराहताजिक-मुकुन्द, मु-<BR>कुन्द-पण्डित); N. of a mountain.<BR>—मुकुन्द-<BR>देव, अस्, m., N. of various princes of Orissa (=<BR>वीर-म्˚).<BR>—मुकुन्द-प्रिय, अस्, m., N. of a certain<BR>teacher; of the father of the commentator Rāmā-<BR>nanda.<BR>—मुकुन्द-भट्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मुकुन्द-माला, f. ‘Mukunda-garland,’ N. of a<BR>prayer in twenty-two verses addressed to Mukunda<BR>(Viṣṇu).<BR>—मुकुन्द-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>Brāhman.<BR>—मुकुन्द-मुनि, इस्, or मुकुन्द-<BR>राज, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मुकुन्द-राम, अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">Page0781-b+ 76</a>]<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—मुकुन्द-शर्मन्, आ, m., N. of<BR>a scribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दक|मुकुंदकः|मुकुन्दकः
मुकुन्दक, अस्, m. a species of grain reckoned<BR>among the Ku-dhānyas; an onion (= सु-कुन्दक,<BR>सु-कन्दक; cf. मुकन्दक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दु|मुकुन्दुः
मुकुन्दु, उस्, m. = मुकुन्द, the resin of Bos-<BR>wellia Thurifera; gum olibanum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुम्
मुकुम् मुकुम्, ind. See मुकु, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुर|मुकुरः
मुकुर मुकुर, अस्, m. a mirror (= मकुर;<BR>cf. कर्ण-मुकुर, मति-म्˚); the stick or handle<BR>of a potter's wheel; Mimusops Elengi; Jasminum<BR>Zambac (= कुल-वृक्ष); a bud (= मुकुल<BR>below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुरित
मुकुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably) = मुकुलित<BR>below; see Gaṇa Tārakādi to Pāṇ. V. 2, 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुल|मुकुलं|मुकुलः
मुकुल मुकुल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (perhaps con-<BR>nected with rt. 2. मुच्), a bud, opening bud or<BR>calyx of a flower, (in these senses also written म-<BR>कुल, q. v.); anything shaped like a bud, (दशन-<BR>म्˚, a bud-like tooth); a bud-like junction or bring-<BR>ing together of the fingers of the hand, (in this sense<BR>only अस्, m.); the body; the soul or spirit; N. of<BR>a king; of another person; (अम्), n. a kind of<BR>metre, four times ¯ ¯ ¯ ˘ ˘ ¯.<BR>—मुकुलाग्र (˚ल-<BR>अग्˚), अम्, n. a particular surgical instrument with<BR>a bud-like point.<BR>—मुकुली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति,<BR>-कर्तुम्, to close (the hands) in the form of a bud.<BR>—मुकुली-कृत, अस्, आ, अम्, closed, shut (as a bud).<BR>—मुकुली-भाव, अस्, m. closing, being closed (as<BR>a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलय
मुकुलय, Nom. P. मुकुलयति, &c., to close,<BR>cause to close (the eyes, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलित
मुकुलित, अस्, आ, अम्, budded, having buds, blos-<BR>soming, full of blossoms; closed like a bud, half<BR>closed; half shut (as the eye), blinking, winking;<BR>closed, shut.<BR>—मुकुलिताक्ष (˚त-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>having half closed eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलिन्
मुकुलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, budding, budded, having buds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुष्ठ|मुकुष्ठः
मुकुष्ठ मुकुष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, = मन्थर;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of bean; [cf. मकुष्ठ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुष्ठक|मुकुष्ठकः
मुकुष्ठक, अस्, m. a species of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकूलक|मुकूलकः
मुकूलक मुकूलक, अस्, m. = मकूलक, a<BR>species of plant (commonly Danti).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त|मुक्तः
मुक्त मुक्त, मुक्ति, &c. See p. 782, col. 3,<BR>and p. 783, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्षीजा
मुक्षीजा मुक्षीजा, f. a net, snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख|मुखं|मुखः
मुख मुख, अम्, n. (said in Uṇādi-s. V.<BR>20. to be fr. rt. खन्, to dig, with the final rejected<BR>and मु prefixed), the mouth; the face, countenance,<BR>(in this sense often at the end of comps., e. g. भ्रू-<BR>कुटी-मुख, a frowning face; especially at the end<BR>of adj. comps. when the fem. is generally मुखी,<BR>e. g. सकलेन्दु-मुखी, a woman with a full moon-<BR>like face; cf. अश्रु-म्˚); the beak of a bird, snout<BR>or muzzle of any animal, (in these senses said to be<BR>also अस्, m.); a direction, quarter, (in this sense<BR>also often at the end of comps., e. g. आशा-मुख,<BR>दिङ्-मुख, quarter or region of space; अन्तर्-<BR>मुखम्, ind. in the direction of or towards the<BR>interior; and more frequently at the end of adj.<BR>comps. in the sense of ‘looking towards, facing,’<BR>when the fem. is generally -मुखी, cf. उभयतो-म्˚,<BR>अधो-म्˚, उदङ्-म्˚; मख-मुख, going to the<BR>sacrifice); opening, aperture, mouth of a vessel, &c.;<BR>entrance, egress (e. g. विन्ध्याटवी-मुखे, at the<BR>entrance of the Vindhya forest; स्वर्गस्य मुखम्,<BR>the entrance into heaven); the entrance to a house;<BR>the mouth or embouchure of a river; the fore part,<BR>front, van (of an army), head, top; the head, tip or<BR>point of anything, (स्तन-मुख, the tip or nipple<BR>of the breast; अङ्गुली-मुख, the tip of the finger;<BR>शर-मुख, the point of an arrow); the edge of<BR>any sharp instrument; surface, upper side (e. g.<BR>विष-कुम्भम् पयो-मुखम्, a vessel of poison<BR>with milk on the surface); the chief, principal, best,<BR>most excellent (e. g. नक्षत्राणाम् मुखं चन्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-c" target="_blank">Page0781-c+ 81</a>]<BR>द्रः, the moon is chief of the Nakṣatras); intro-<BR>duction, beginning, commencement, (often at the end<BR>of comps. when the fem. is -मुखा or -मुखी, but<BR>oftener the latter, e. g. गङ्गा-मुखीनां or गङ्गा-<BR>मुखानां सरिताम्, of the rivers beginning with<BR>the Ganges; महा-रथा जयद्रथ-मुखाः,<BR>the heroes beginning with Jayad-ratha, i. e. Jayad-<BR>ratha and the other heroes; cf. the use of आदि);<BR>the opening or previous incidents of a drama, the<BR>original cause or source of the action, the first act;<BR>(in algebra) the first term, the intial quantity of the<BR>progression; the apex or side opposite to the base<BR>of a mathematical figure; source, cause, occasion,<BR>ground; means, expedient; scripture, the Veda;<BR>sound (?); Artocarpus Locucha or Lakuca, (in this<BR>sense अस्, m.); (एन), ind. with reference to, according<BR>to.<BR>—मुख-कमल, अम्, n. ‘face-lotus,’ a lotus-<BR>like face.<BR>—मुख-खुर, अस्, m. ‘mouth-razor,’ a<BR>tooth.<BR>—मुख-गन्धक, अस्, m. ‘mouth-scent-<BR>ing,’ an onion.<BR>—मुख-घण्टा, f. ‘mouth-bell,’<BR>a particular sound made with the mouth (= हुल-<BR>हुली).<BR>—मुख-चन्द्र, अस्, m. ‘face-moon,’ a<BR>moon-like face, lovely face.<BR>—मुख-चपल, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘one whose mouth is ever moving,’ talkative,<BR>loquacious, garrulous; (आ), f. a kind of Āryā metre.<BR>—मुख-चपेटिका, f. a slap on the face, box on<BR>the ear; [cf. दुर्जन-म्˚.]<BR>—मुख-चीरी, f. the<BR>tongue.<BR>—मुख-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, produced from or<BR>in the mouth; (अस्), m. ‘mouth-born,’ a Brāhman,<BR>(so called as being sprung from the mouth of Brahmā;<BR>cf. Manu 1. 31.)<BR>—मुख-जाह, अम्, n. the root<BR>or point of issue of the mouth, the top of the<BR>pharynx.<BR>—१. मुख-तस्, ind. from or out of or at<BR>the mouth, in the mouth, in the face; at the head,<BR>in the front.<BR>—२. मुख-तस् = मुखे तस्यति, see<BR>Scholiast on Pāṇ. III. 4, 61.<BR>—मुख-दघ्न,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, reaching to the mouth.<BR>—मुख-दू-<BR>षण, अस्, m. ‘mouth-defiler,’ an onion.<BR>—मुख-<BR>दूषिका, f. ‘face-disfiguring,’ an eruption which dis-<BR>figures the face of young people.<BR>—मुख-धौता,<BR>f. a plant, Clerodendrum Siphonanthus.<BR>—मुख-<BR>नासिक, अम्, n. the mouth and nose.<BR>—मुख-<BR>निरीक्षक, अस्, m. ‘face-gazer,’ an idler, lazy<BR>person.<BR>—मुख-निवासिनी, f. ‘dwelling in the<BR>mouth,’ an epithet of Saravatī.<BR>—मुख-पट, अस्,<BR>m. ‘face-cloth,’ a veil.<BR>—मुख-पाक, अस्, m. in-<BR>flammation of the mouth.<BR>—मुख-पिण्ड, अस्, m.<BR>a lump or piece of food in the mouth, mouthful of<BR>food.<BR>—मुख-पूरण, अम्, n. filling the mouth,<BR>a mouthful of water, a mouthful in general.<BR>—मु-<BR>ख-प्रतिमुख, speech and reply (?).<BR>—मुख-<BR>प्रसाद, अस्, m. the light of the countenance,<BR>graciousness of aspect.<BR>—मुख-प्रिय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>pleasant in the mouth; (अस्), m. an orange.<BR>—मु-<BR>ख-प्रेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, or मुख-प्रेक्षिन्, ई,<BR>इणी, इ, observing or watching the face (to detect<BR>any one's intentions).<BR>—मुख-बन्ध, अस्, m. a<BR>preface.<BR>—मुख-बन्धन, अम्, n. ‘mouth-bind-<BR>ing,’ the fastening of an aperture, a lid, cover; an<BR>introduction, preface.<BR>—मुख-बहूरु-पज्-ज (˚हु-<BR>ऊर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, sprung from the mouth, arm, thigh,<BR>and foot (Manu. 1. 87).<BR>—मुख-बाहूरु-पाद-तस्<BR>(˚हु-ऊर्˚), ind. from the mouth, arms, thighs, and feet.<BR>—मुख-भूषण, अम्, n. ‘mouth-ornament,’<BR>betel; tin (?).<BR>—मुख-भेद, अस्, m. distortion<BR>of the face.<BR>—मुख-मण्डनक, अस्, m. a species<BR>of tree (= तिलक).<BR>—मुख-मण्डल, अम्, n.<BR>‘face-orb,’ the face, countenance.<BR>—मुख-मण्-<BR>डिका, f. a particular disease or the deity presiding<BR>over it; (also read मुख-मण्डिनिका.)<BR>—मुख-<BR>मण्डी, f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—मुख-माधुर्य, अम्, n. a particular disease of<BR>the phlegm.<BR>—मुख-मार्जन, अम्, n. washing or<BR>cleansing the mouth (after meals, &c.).<BR>—मुख-<BR>मोद, अस्, m. Hyperanthera Moringa.<BR>—मुखम्-<BR>पच, अस्, m. a beggar.<BR>—मुख-यन्त्रण, अम्, n.<BR>‘mouth-curb,’ the bit of a bridle.<BR>—मुख-राग,<BR>अस्, m. colour of the face.<BR>—मुख-रुज्, क्, f. or<BR>मुख-रोग, अस्, m. ‘mouth-disease,’ any disease<BR>of the mouth.<BR>—मुखरोगिक, अस्, आ, अम्, relating<BR>to mouth-disease.<BR>—मुख-रोगिन्, ई, इणी, इ, diseased<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-a" target="_blank">Page0782-a+ 81</a>]<BR>in the mouth.<BR>—मुख-लाङ्गल, अस्, m. ‘using the<BR>snout for a plough,’ a hog.<BR>—मुख-लेप, अस्, m.<BR>anointing the face, anointing the upper side (of a<BR>drum); a disease of the phlegmatic humor; [cf. आस्यो-<BR>पलेप]<BR>—मुख-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing a<BR>mouth, having a mouth.<BR>—मुख-वल्लभ, अस्, m.<BR>a pomegranate tree.<BR>—मुख-वाटिका, f. a species<BR>of plant (= अम्ब-ष्ठा).<BR>—मुख-वाद्य, अम्, n.<BR>a wind-instrument, any instrument of music sounded<BR>with the mouth; (in the worship of Śiva) a kind of<BR>musical sound made with the mouth (by striking it<BR>with the hand).<BR>—मुख-वास or मुख-वासन,<BR>अस्, m. ‘mouth-perfume,’ a perfume used to scent the<BR>breath; fragrant grass (= गन्ध-त्रिण).<BR>—मु-<BR>ख-विपुला, f. a kind of Āryā metre.<BR>—मुख-<BR>विलुण्ठिका, f. a she-goat.<BR>—मुख-विष्ठा, f. a<BR>species of cockroach.<BR>—मुख-व्यादान, अम्, n.<BR>the act of opening the mouth wide, gaping.<BR>—मु-<BR>ख-शफ, अस्, आ, अम्, foul-mouthed, scurrilous.<BR>—मुख-शुद्धि, इस्, f. cleanness of the face or<BR>mouth, cleansing or purifying the mouth (as by<BR>eating betel-nut, &c.).<BR>—मुख-शेष, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>having only the face left; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Rāhu.<BR>—मुख-शोधन, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘mouth-<BR>cleansing,’ cleansing the mouth; sharp, pungent;<BR>(अस्), m. pungency, sharp or pungent flavour; (अम्),<BR>n. the cleansing of the mouth; cinnamon.<BR>—मुख-<BR>शोधिन्, ई, इनी, इ, cleansing the mouth; (ई), m. a<BR>lime or citron, citron tree.<BR>—मुख-शोष, अस्, m.<BR>dryness of the mouth.<BR>—मुख-शोषिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>suffering from dryness of the mouth.<BR>—मुख-श्री,<BR>ईस्, f. beauty of countenance, a beautiful face.<BR>—मु-<BR>ख-ष्ठील, अस्, आ, अम् (probably for मुखा-<BR>ष्ठील), = मुख-शफ.<BR>—मुख-सम्भव,<BR>अस्, m. ‘mouth-born,’ a Brāhman; [cf. मुख-ज.],<BR>—मुख-सुख, अम्, n. ‘ease of pronunciation,’<BR>causing ease of pronunciation or facility of utterance.<BR>—मुख-सुर, अम्, n. ‘lip-nectar,’ the moisture<BR>of the lips.<BR>—मुख-स्राव, अस्, m. flow of saliva,<BR>salivation, saliva.<BR>—मुखाकार (˚ख-आक्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘form of the countenance,’ mien, look, appearance.<BR>—मुखाग्नि (˚ख-अग्˚), इस्, m. a forest conflagra-<BR>tion; a sort of goblin with a face of fire; fire put<BR>into the mouth of a corpse at the time of lighting<BR>the funeral pile; a sacrificial or consecrated fire; [cf.<BR>मुखोल्का.]<BR>—मुखाग्र (˚ख-अग्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>extremity of the mouth, extremity.<BR>—मुखानिल<BR>(˚ख-अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘mouth-wind,’ wind of the mouth,<BR>breath.<BR>—मुखामय (˚ख-आम्˚), अस्, m. disease of<BR>the mouth.<BR>—मुखामृत (˚ख-अम्˚), अम्, n. the<BR>nectar of the mouth or countenance, (a term used in<BR>flattering addresses.)<BR>—मुखार्चिस् (˚ख-अर्˚), इस्, n.<BR>‘mouth-flame,’ hot breath (?).<BR>—मुखार्जक (˚ख-<BR>अर्˚), अस्, m. a species of plant (= अर्जक).<BR>—मु-<BR>खासव (˚ख-आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘lip-moisture,’ nectar<BR>of the lips.<BR>—मुखास्त्र (˚ख-अस्˚), अस्, m. ‘mouth-<BR>armed,’ a crab.<BR>—मुखास्राव (˚ख-आस्˚), अस्, m.<BR>= mukha-srāva.<BR>—मुखी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति,<BR>-भवितुम्, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. III. 4, 61.<BR>—मु-<BR>खेन्दु (˚ख-इन्˚), उस्, m. a moon-like face, beau-<BR>tiful face.<BR>—मुखे-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. formed<BR>in the mouth.<BR>—मुखोत्कीर्ण (˚ख-उत्˚), अस्, m.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—मुखोल्का (˚ख-उल्˚), f. = मुखाग्नि,<BR>a forest fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखतीय|मुखतीयं
मुखतीय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. 1. मुख-तस्; cf.<BR>पार्श्वतीय), being in the mouth or in the front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखर|मुखरः
मुखर, अस्, आ, अम्, talkative, loquacious, gar-<BR>rulous, noisy, making any continuous or tedious<BR>sound (said of birds and bees and tinkling orna-<BR>ments, cf. उन्-म्˚); sounding, resonant or resound-<BR>ing with (at the end of a comp., e. g. प्रतिश्रुन्-<BR>मुखर, resonant with echoes); expressive of,<BR>(अवर्ण-मुखरा गिरः, voices expressive of re-<BR>proach); foul-mouthed, scurrilous, speaking harshly<BR>or abusively; ridiculing, mocking; (अस्), m. a crow;<BR>a conch shell; a leader, principal, chief, ringleader;<BR>N. of a Nāga; (ई), f. the bit of a bridle.<BR>—मु-<BR>खर-ता, f. talkativeness, garrulity, noisiness.<BR>—मु-<BR>खरी-करण, अम्, n. making resonant, speaking<BR>harshly, rallying, mocking.<BR>—मुखरी-कृ, cl. 8. P.<BR>-करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make resonant, cause to resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरक
मुखरक, अस्, m. a proper N.; (इका), f. =<BR>मुखरी, the bit of a bridle; talking, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरय
मुखरय, Nom. P. मुखरयति, -यितुम्, to<BR>make noisy or resonant; to notify, declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरित
मुखरित, अस्, आ, अम्, rendered noisy, made<BR>resonant, sounding, ringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखीय
मुखीय, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>being at the top or head, being foremost, being at<BR>the entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्य|मुख्यः
मुख्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being in or on the mouth or<BR>face; belonging to the mouth or face, coming from<BR>the mouth, &c.; being at the head or at the begin-<BR>ning, principal, chief, prime, primary, original, first,<BR>eminent, pre-eminent, first-rate, most excellent or<BR>important, original; (at the end of a comp.) the<BR>chief, most excellent among, first or best of (cf.<BR>द्विजाति-म्˚, द्विज-म्˚, मन्त्रि-म्˚, वार-मुख्या;<BR>sometimes even used like आदि, e. g. नारायणी-<BR>मुख्यम् मातृ-चक्रम्, the whole circle of Mātṛs<BR>beginning with Nārāyaṇī); (अस्), m. a leader, guide;<BR>N. of a tutelary deity presiding over one part of an<BR>astrological house which is divided into 81 or 63<BR>divisions or Padas; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a class of<BR>gods under Manu Sārvaṇi; (अम्), n. a principal or<BR>essential rite, chief ordinance; reading or teaching<BR>the Vedas; the month reckoned from new moon to<BR>new moon.<BR>—मुख्य-चान्द्र, the principal lunar<BR>month which ends with the conjunction (as opposed<BR>to the गौण-चान्द्र or secondary lunar month<BR>which ends with the opposition).<BR>—मुख्य-तस्,<BR>ind. principally, chiefly, particularly, especially, par<BR>excellence.<BR>—मुख्य-ता, f. or मुख्य-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. pre-eminence, the being best or chief, principal-<BR>ness, primacy, highest rank or position.<BR>—मुख्य-<BR>नृप, अस्, or मुख्य-राज्, ट्, m. a paramount<BR>sovereign, reigning monarch.<BR>—मुख्यमन्त्रि-ता,<BR>f. the office or rank of prime minister.<BR>—मुख्य-<BR>मन्त्रिन्, ई, m. a prime minister, chief councillor;<BR>[cf. मन्त्रि-मुख्य.]<BR>—मुख्य-शस्, ind. princi-<BR>pally, particularly, chiefly, before all, next.<BR>—मु-<BR>ख्यार्थ (˚य-अर्˚), अस्, m. primary meaning (of a<BR>word, as opposed to its गौणार्थ or secondary or<BR>metaphorical meaning), original sense, first signifi-<BR>cation; (अस्, आ, अम्), employed in or having the<BR>original sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखण्डी
मुखण्डी मुखण्डी, or मुखुण्डी, f. a kind<BR>of weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखुली
मुखुली मुखुली, f., N. of a Buddhist<BR>goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुगदस
मुगदस मुगदस, मुगदेमु, मुगल-स्था-<BR>न, names of places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुगूह|मुगूहः
मुगूह मुगूह, अस्, m. a species of gallinule<BR>(= दात्यूह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्ध|मुग्धः
मुग्ध मुग्ध, &c. See under rt. 1. मुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुङ्ग
मुङ्ग मुङ्ग, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुङ्गट
मुङ्गट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
मुच् 1. मुच् [cf. rt. मुञ्च्], cl. 1. A. मो-<BR>चते, मोचितुम्, = rt. मच्, q. v., to cheat,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
मुच् 2. मुच्, cl. 6. P. A. मुञ्चति, -ते,<BR>मुमोच, मुमुचे, मोक्ष्यति, -ते, अमु-<BR>चत्, अमुक्त (Vedic forms मुचन्ति, मुञ्चातु,<BR>मुमुच्रे, मुमोक्तु, मुमुगधि, मा मौक् =<BR>मा मुञ्च in Vājasaneyi-s. 1. 25, अमुमुक्तम्,<BR>मुमोचत, मुमोचति, मुमोचतम्, मुक्षत),<BR>मोक्तुम्, to loose, loosen, let loose, free, let go,<BR>release, liberate, (कण्ठम् मुञ्चति, he loosens his<BR>throat or voice, i. e. raises a cry; वनाय धेनुम्<BR>मुमोच, he let the cow go into the wood; प्राणान्<BR>मुच्, to let loose the breath of life, i. e. to deprive<BR>of life, kill); to set free, unloose, open; to let go,<BR>relinquish, abandon, forsake, leave, quit, put off,<BR>shake off, lay aside, give up, (देहम् मुञ्चति, he<BR>quits the body, i. e. dies; मुच्यतां विषादः, let<BR>despondency be shaken off); to give up, grant,<BR>bestow; to sacrifice; to set on one side, take away,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-c" target="_blank">Page0782-c+ 81</a>]<BR>set apart, except; to let go, discharge, emit, effuse,<BR>shed, send forth, send, throw, cast, fling, hurt, shoot,<BR>(वाणमयं वर्षम् मुमोच, he discharged a<BR>shower of arrows; इन्द्रो वज्रम् मोक्ष्यते, Indra<BR>will hurl his thunderbolt; कूटाद् आत्मानम् मुमोच,<BR>he threw himself down from a peak); to send away,<BR>dismiss; to spit out; to void; to emit sounds, utter;<BR>to put on (A.): Pass. मुच्यते (ep. also मुच्यति,<BR>2nd Fut. मोक्ष्यति), to be loosed, to be let loose<BR>or set free, to be released from (with abl. or some-<BR>times with inst., e. g. मुच्यते पातकैः, he is loosed<BR>from sins); to become loose, free or deliver one's<BR>self, escape, (यद्य् एतेभ्यो मुच्यसे, if thou deliver<BR>thyself from these men; न मे मोक्ष्यति जीवन्,<BR>he shall not escape from me alive); to abandon, to<BR>deviate or go astray from, (यदि धर्माद् न<BR>मुच्यते, if he go not astray from virtue): Caus.<BR>मोचयति, -ते, Aor. अमूमुचत्, मोचयितुम्, to<BR>cause to loose, cause to be liberated, cause to let go,<BR>cause to shed; to loose, unloose, set loose or free,<BR>set at large, liberate; to open (a road); to redeem<BR>from (with abl., Manu III. 37); to unyoke, unhar-<BR>ness, (अश्वान् मोचयति, he unyokes the horses);<BR>to let go, give away, bestow; to cause to give up or<BR>let go or discharge or shed; to gladden, delight,<BR>rejoice, yield enjoyment: Desid. of Caus. मुमोच-<BR>यिषति, Ved. to wish or intend to liberate, desire to<BR>be freed from (the bondage of existence, &c.):<BR>Desid. मुमुक्षति, -ते, to wish or be about to set<BR>free or let go or give up; to wish or be about to<BR>hurl, wish to cast, (वज्रम् मुमुक्षन्, being<BR>about to hurl a thunderbolt); to wish to free one's<BR>self or get loose; to desire final liberation or beati-<BR>tude [cf. rt. मोक्ष्, मोक्ष]: Intens. मोमोक्ति,<BR>मोमुच्यते; [cf. Gr. μύσσ-ω, μῦκ-ος, μυκτήρ, ἀπομυκτίζω,<BR>μύξα, Μυκάλη (?), Μυκήνη (?), μύξινος: Lat.<BR>mung-o, mucu-s, mûcêre, mûcor, mûcêdo: Slav.<BR>mok-na-ti, ‘to be wet;’ moc†iti, ‘to wet.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त|मुक्तः
मुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, loosened, loosed, let loose,<BR>set free, relaxed, (मुक्तैर् अवयवैः, with loos-<BR>ened or relaxed limbs); unloosed, opened, open [cf.<BR>मुक्त-हस्त]; redeemed, released, extricated, libe-<BR>rated, emancipated (from sin or from worldly exist-<BR>ence), finally happy, saved; abandoned, relinquished,<BR>quitted, left, put off, laid aside; given up; bestowed,<BR>granted, given; discharged, emitted, shed, thrown,<BR>cast, hurled, darted, shot, sent, sent forth, poured<BR>forth, (वर्णोदकैः काञ्चन-शृङ्ग-मुक्तैः,<BR>with coloured waters poured forth from golden vials);<BR>ejected, spit out; fallen; deprived; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>one of the seven sages under Manu Bhautya; N.<BR>of a cook in Rāja-taraṅgiṇī VII. 1635, &c.; (आ), f.,<BR>scil. दिश्, the quarter just quitted by the sun (e. g. if<BR>the sun be in the south, the south is said to be<BR>प्राप्तार्का, and the south-east मुक्ता); a pearl (as<BR>loosened or set free from the pearl-oyster shell); a<BR>courtezan, harlot; a species of plant, = रास्ना; (अम्),<BR>n. the spirit released from corporeal existence.<BR>—मुक्त-कच्छ, अस्, आ, अम्, letting the hem of<BR>the lower garment hang down or leaving it loose<BR>and untucked; (अस्), m. a Buddhist.<BR>—मुक्त-कञ्-<BR>चुक, अस्, m. a snake that has cast its slough.<BR>—मुक्त-कण्ठ, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, having a loos-<BR>ened or free throat, raising a cry, shrill; (अम्), ind.<BR>aloud.<BR>—मुक्त-कर, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्, open-handed,<BR>liberal, bountiful.<BR>—मुक्त-केश, अस्, आ, or ई, अम्,<BR>‘loose-haired,’ having flowing hair, having the hair<BR>dishevelled or hanging down.<BR>—मुक्त-चक्षुस्,<BR>उस्, उस्, उस्, having the eyes opened; (उस्), m. ‘cast-<BR>ing glances,’ a lion.<BR>—मुक्त-चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, one<BR>whose soul is liberated (from existence), emancipated.<BR>—मुक्त-ता, f. or मुक्त-त्व, अम्, n. emancipation,<BR>liberation, the being liberated from existence.<BR>—मु-<BR>क्त-ध्वनि, इस्, इस्, इ, giving out thunder (as a<BR>cloud).<BR>—मुक्त-निद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, freed from sleep,<BR>awakened.<BR>—मुक्त-निर्मोक, अस्, आ, अम्, = मुक्त-<BR>कञ्चुक, q. v.<BR>—मुक्त-फूत्कार, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>uttering a scream, screaming.<BR>—मुक्त-फूत्कृति,<BR>इस्, f. uttering a shriek, shrieking; hissing.<BR>—मुक्त-<BR>बन्धन, अस्, आ, अम्, released from bonds, freed<BR>from fetters.<BR>—मुक्त-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, one whose<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-a" target="_blank">Page0783-a+ 81</a>]<BR>soul is liberated, emancipated.<BR>—मुक्त-मण्डूक-<BR>कण्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having frogs croaking loudly<BR>(lit. with loosened throats).<BR>—मुक्त-मूर्धज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, = मुक्त-केश, q. v.<BR>—मुक्त-रोधो-<BR>नितम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, quitting the hip-like bank.<BR>—मुक्त-रोष, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has laid<BR>aside or relinquished anger.<BR>—मुक्त-लज्ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, casting away shame.<BR>—मुक्त-वसन, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one who has put off his clothes, going about<BR>naked; (अस्), m. an epithet of a Jaina ascetic.<BR>—मुक्त-व्यापार, अस्, आ, अम्, one who has re-<BR>signed an office or occupation.<BR>—मुक्त-संशय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, free from doubt, certain.<BR>—मुक्त-सङ्ग,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, free from worldly or selfish attachment,<BR>disinterested.<BR>—मुक्त-स्वामिन्, ई, m. ‘lord of eman-<BR>cipation,’ N. of a statue erected by a king (Rāja-<BR>taraṅgiṇī IV. 188).<BR>—मुक्त-हस्त, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>open-handed, liberal, easily parting with possessions,<BR>giving away, profuse; loosed, let go.<BR>—मुक्ता-कण,<BR>अस्, m. (for मुक्ता-कर्ण), a proper N.<BR>—मुक्ता-<BR>कलाप, अस्, m. an ornament made of strings of<BR>pearls, pearl necklace.<BR>—मुक्ताकार (˚ता-आक्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, having the look or appearance of a pearl.<BR>—मुक्ताकार-ता, f. the form of a pearl, likeness<BR>to a pearl.<BR>—मुक्ता-केशव, अस्, m., N. of a statue<BR>of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मुक्तागार (˚ता-अग्˚) or -आग्˚), अम्, n.<BR>‘pearl-abode,’ the pearl-oyster.<BR>—मुक्ता-गुण, अस्,<BR>m. a string of pearls; the excellence of a pearl, lustre<BR>or water of a pearl.<BR>—मुक्ता-जाल, अम्, n. an orna-<BR>ment of pearls, a string or multitude of pearls, a<BR>pearly zone; [cf. मुक्ता-फल-जाल.]<BR>—मुक्ता-<BR>जाल-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or consisting of pearls.<BR>—मुक्तात्मन् (˚त-आत्˚), आ, m. the emancipated<BR>soul, the soul released from matter; (आ, आ, अ), one<BR>whose soul is liberated, emancipated.<BR>—मुक्ता-दा-<BR>मन्, आ, m. a string of pearls.<BR>—मुक्ता-पटल,<BR>अम्, n. a mass of pearls.<BR>—मुक्तापीड (˚त-आप्˚),<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king; of a poet.<BR>—मुक्ता-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a mythical city in the Himālaya moun-<BR>tains.<BR>—मुक्ता-पुष्प, अस्, m. Jasminum Multi-<BR>florum or Pubescens.<BR>—मुक्ता-प्रसू, ऊस्, f. ‘pearl-<BR>bearing,’ mother of pearl, the pearl-oyster; [cf.<BR>मुक्ता-मातृ, मौक्तिक-प्रसवा.]<BR>—मुक्ता-प्रा-<BR>लम्ब, अस्, m. a string of pearls, pearl ornament,<BR>(also read मुक्ता-प्रलम्ब.)<BR>—मुक्ता-फल, अम्,<BR>n. a pearl; a species of flower; the fruit of the Lavalī<BR>plant, the custard apple; camphor; title of a work<BR>by Vopa-deva; N. of a king of the Śavaras.<BR>—मु-<BR>क्ताफल-केतु, उस्, m., N. of a king of the Vidyā-<BR>dharas.<BR>—मुक्ताफल-जाल, अम्, n. = मुक्ता-जाल.<BR>—मुक्ताफल-ध्वज, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मुक्ताफल-परीक्षा, f., N. of the eighty-first<BR>Adhyāya in the Varāha-brāhmaṇa-saṃhitā.<BR>—मुक्ता-<BR>फल-लता, f. a string of pearls; [cf. मुक्ता-लता.]<BR>—मुक्ता-मणि, इस्, m. ‘pearl-gem,’ a pearl; [cf.<BR>मुक्ता-रत्न.]<BR>—मुक्ता-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or<BR>consisting of pearls, pearly.<BR>—मुक्ता-मातृ, ता, f.<BR>mother of pearl, a pearl-oyster; [cf. मुक्ता-प्रसू.]<BR>—मुक्तामुक्त (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, loosed and<BR>not loosed (applied especially to weapons which may<BR>be wielded or hurled, as clubs, javelins, &c.).<BR>—मु-<BR>क्ताम्बर (˚त-अम्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one who has put<BR>off his clothes, naked; (अस्), m. an epithet of a Jaina<BR>ascetic; [cf. मुक्त-वसन.]<BR>—मुक्ता-रत्न, अम्,<BR>n. ‘pearl-gem,’ a pearl; [cf. मौक्तिक-रत्न.]<BR>—मुक्ता-लता, f. a string of pearls, pearl necklace;<BR>N. of a woman.<BR>—मुक्तावली (˚ता-आव्˚), f. a pearl<BR>necklace; N. of various works; of a dictionary; of<BR>a commentary on the Megha-dūta; of the wife of<BR>Candra-ketu.<BR>—मुक्तावली-प्रकाश, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a commentary by Dinakara-bhaṭṭa on the Nyāya-<BR>siddhānta-muktāvalī; of a commentary by Maṇi-<BR>rāma.<BR>—मुक्ता-शुक्ति, इस्, f. a pearl-oyster (= मौ-<BR>क्तिक-शुक्ति).<BR>—मुक्तासन (˚त-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>leaving a seat, rising from a seat; (अम्), n. the<BR>mode in which the emancipated are said to sit, a<BR>particular posture of ascetics (= सिद्धासन, q. v.).<BR>—मुक्ता-सेन, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Vidyā-<BR>dharas.<BR>—मुक्ता-स्थूल, अस्, आ, अम्, big as a pearl.<BR>—मुक्ता-स्फोट, अस्, आ, m. f. a pearl-oyster.<BR>—मु-<BR>क्ता-स्रज्, क्, f. a chaplet of pearls.<BR>—मुक्ता-हार,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">Page0783-b+ 79</a>]<BR>अस्, m. a string of pearls, pearl necklace.<BR>—मुक्ते-<BR>श्वर (˚त-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of a Liṅga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0782-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तक|मुक्तकं
मुक्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, detached, separate, inde-<BR>pendent; (अम्), n. a missile, any missile weapon;<BR>a separate or detached Śloka the meaning of which<BR>is complete in itself; simple prose (freed from all<BR>compound words); a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ति|मुक्तिः
मुक्ति, इस्, f. loosing, release, deliverance, liberation,<BR>setting free, becoming free, freedom, emancipation<BR>(e. g. दासत्व-मुक्ति, release from servitude; cf.<BR>शाप-म्˚); final liberation or emancipation, final<BR>beatitude, the delivery of the soul from the body<BR>and exemption from further transmigration, the re-<BR>absorption of the Jīvātman into the Paramātman or<BR>Supreme Soul of the universe; unloosing, opening;<BR>abandonment, putting off, giving up, leaving off;<BR>discharging (rain, a missile, &c.); throwing, casting,<BR>flinging, hurling, shooting, sending; discharge (of a<BR>debt, cf. ऋन-म्˚); N. of a divine being, the wife<BR>of Satya.<BR>—मुक्ति-क्षेत्र, अम्, n. a place where<BR>final emancipation is attainable; N. of a sacred place.<BR>—मुक्ति-ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. a book of precepts for<BR>the attainment of final emancipation.<BR>—मुक्ति-चिन्-<BR>तामणि-माहात्म्य, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—मुक्ति-<BR>पति, इस्, m. lord of bliss or beatitude.<BR>—मुक्ति-पुर,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Dvīpa.<BR>—मुक्ति-मण्डप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a temple.<BR>—मुक्ति-मती, f., N. of a river,<BR>(also read भुक्ति-मती and शुक्ति-मती.)<BR>—मुक्ति-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, m. the way of liberation, path to final<BR>emancipation.<BR>—मुक्ति-मुक्त, अस्, m. incense, frank-<BR>incense.<BR>—मुक्ति-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having freedom,<BR>freed from (with abl.).<BR>—मुक्ति-वाद, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a work.<BR>—मुक्ति-विचार, अस्, m., N. of a philoso-<BR>phical work.<BR>—मुक्ति-सेन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तिका
मुक्तिका, f., N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त्वा
मुक्त्वा, ind. having loosed or freed or let go, (मु-<BR>क्त्वा हासम्, having broken out into loud laughter);<BR>having left or abandoned, having resigned; having<BR>put on one side, having excepted, excepting, except,<BR>(युद्धम् मुक्त्वा नान्यद् अस्ति मे, except a<BR>battle there is nothing else for me); having discharged<BR>or shed, having thrown or flung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
3. मुच्, क्, क्, क्, (at the end of a comp.) freeing<BR>or delivering from [cf. अंहो-म्˚]; discharging, drop-<BR>ping, letting fall, emitting, throwing, shooting, sending,<BR>(शर-वृष्टि-मुच्, discharging showers of arrows;<BR>जल-लव-मुच्, letting fall drops of rain; cf. अ-म्˚,<BR>जल-म्˚, तोय-म्˚, पयो-म्˚, पर्ण-म्˚.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच
मुच, अस्, ई, अम्, in नख-मुच and अ-मुची, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचिर|मुचिरः
मुचिर, अस्, आ, अम्, liberal, munificent, generous [cf.<BR>मुक्त-हस्त]; (अस्), m. virtue; wind; a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्यमान
मुच्यमान, अस्, आ, अम्, being freed or released,<BR>being abandoned by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चत्
मुञ्चत्, अन्, अती, or अन्ती, अत्, or मुञ्चान, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, loosing, freeing; giving up, relinquishing; dis-<BR>charging, shooting, casting, shedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षत्
मुमुक्षत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, desiring emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षा
मुमुक्षा, f. desire of liberation or final eman-<BR>cipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षु|मुमुक्षुः
मुमुक्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of freeing, wish-<BR>ing to deliver or liberate; eager to be free (from<BR>mundane existence), striving after emancipation;<BR>wishing to let go or give up; wishing to emit or<BR>discharge; about to shoot; (उस्), m. a sage striving<BR>after emancipation.<BR>—मुमुक्षु-ता, f. or मुमु-<BR>क्षु-त्व, अम्, n. desire of liberation or of final<BR>emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुचान|मुमुचानः
मुमुचान, अस्, m. a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुचु
मुमुचु, उस्, m. (mentioned with Un-mucu and<BR>Pra-mucu), N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमोचयिषु
मुमोचयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, desirous of liberating,<BR>wishing to set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तव्य
मोक्तव्य, मोक्तृ, &c. See s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचक|मुचकः
मुचक मुचक, अस्, m. lac, gum-lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचि
मुचि मुचि, इस्, m., N. of a Cakra-vartin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचिलिन्द|मुचिलिंद|मुचिलिंदः|मुचिलिन्दः
मुचिलिन्द मुचिलिन्द, अस्, m. a species of<BR>flower; N. of a Nāga; of a Cakra-vartin; [cf.<BR>महा-म्˚.]<BR>—मुचिलिन्द-पर्वत, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a mythical mountain; [cf. महा-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचुकुन्द|मुचुकुंद|मुचुकुंदः|मुचुकुन्दः
मुचुकुन्द मुचुकुन्द, अस्, m. Pterospermum<BR>Suberifolium; N. of an ancient king (or Muni);<BR>N. of a son of Mandhāṛ (who asked the gods to<BR>grant him the enjoyment of long and unbroken<BR>sleep as a reward for the assistance he had rendered<BR>them in subduing the demons; the gods complied<BR>with his request, and decreed that whosoever disturbed<BR>him should be burnt to ashes by fire emanating from<BR>his body; Kṛṣṇa, in order to destroy Kāla-yavana,<BR>enticed him into the cave where Mucukunda was<BR>asleep, and the latter being thus roused cast upon<BR>Kāla-yavana an angry glance which reduced him<BR>to ashes; see translation of Viṣṇu-Purāṇa, p. 567);<BR>N. of a son of Yadu; of the father of Candra-bhāga;<BR>of a poet of Kaśmīra; of a Daitya.<BR>—मुचुकुन्द-<BR>प्रसादक, अस्, m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचुटी
मुचुटी मुचुटी, f. (fr. rt. 2. मुच्), snapping<BR>the fingers [cf. पुच्छटि]; the fist; a pair of forceps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुछ्
मुछ् मुछ्, cl. 1. P. मुच्छति, &c., a<BR>various reading for rt. युछ्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुज्
मुज् मुज्, cl. 1. P. मोजति, &c., and<BR>मुञ्ज्, cl. 1. P. मुञ्जति, &c., to sound,<BR>give out a particular sound; (according to Vopa-deva<BR>also) cl. 10. P. मोजयति, &c., and मुञ्जयति, &c.,<BR>to sound; to cleanse; [cf. rt. 1. मृज्: cf. also Gr.<BR>μύζ-ω, ἔ-μυ-σα, μυγ-μό-ς, μῡκ-ά-ο-μαι, μέμυκα;<BR>Lat. mugio.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्च्|मुंच्
मुञ्च् मुञ्च् (connected with rts. मञ्च्,<BR>म्रुञ्च्, म्लुञ्च्), cl. 1. P. मुञ्चति, &c.,<BR>to go, move; cl. 1. A. मुञ्चते, &c. = rt. मच्,<BR>q. v., to cheat, to be wicked, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चक|मुञ्चकः
मुञ्चक, अस्, m. a species of tree (= मुष्कक-<BR>वृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्ज्|मुंज्
मुञ्ज् मुञ्ज्. See rt. मुज् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्ज|मुंज|मुंजः|मुञ्जः
मुञ्ज, अस्, m. a sort of rush or grass, Saccharum<BR>Munja (which grows to the height of ten feet and<BR>is used to form the Brāhmanical mekhalā or girdle<BR>as well as in basket-work); the Brāhmanical girdle<BR>or the sacred cord of a Brāhman (as made of the<BR>Muñja grass, but in this sense the more proper form<BR>is मौञ्ज; cf. Manu II. 27, 42, 43); an arrow (?);<BR>N. of a person with the patronymic Sāma-śravasa;<BR>of a Brāhman; of a poet and king of Dhārā; of a<BR>prince of Campā.<BR>—मुञ्ज-केतु, उस्, m. a proper<BR>N.<BR>—मुञ्ज-केश, अस्, m. ‘rush-haired,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva; of Viṣṇu; of a king; of a teacher; of a dis-<BR>ciple of Vijitāsu.<BR>—मुञ्जकेश-वत्, आन्, m. ‘having<BR>rush-like hair,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मुञ्ज-केशिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, having rush-like hair; (ई), m. an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; a proper N.<BR>—मुञ्ज-ग्राम, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a village, (also read रम्य-ग्राम.)<BR>—मुञ्ज-<BR>नेजन, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (according to Sāy.) freed<BR>from grass or rushes (= तृणेन शोधित, अपगत-<BR>तृण).<BR>—मुञ्जन्-धय, अस्, ई, अम्, sucking rushes.<BR>—मुञ्ज-पृष्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a place on the<BR>Himālaya mountains.<BR>—मुञ्ज-बन्धन, अम्, n.<BR>investiture with the Brāhmanical girdle or cord.<BR>—मुञ्ज-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of Muñja grass.<BR>—मुञ्ज-मेखलिन्, ई, m. ‘Muñja-girdled,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Viṣṇu; of Śiva.<BR>—मुञ्ज-वट, N. of a<BR>place of pilgrimage; [cf. मुञ्जावट.]<BR>—मुञ्ज-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, overgrown with rushes, rushy; (आन्),<BR>m. epithet of a particular species of Soma plant; N.<BR>of a mountain of the Himālaya range.<BR>—मुञ्ज-<BR>वासस्, आस्, m. ‘rush-clothed,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मुञ्-<BR>जादित्य (˚ज-आद्˚), इस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मुञ्-<BR>जादिरि (˚ज-अद्˚), इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—मुञ्जा-<BR>वट (˚ज-अव्˚), N. of a place (= मुञ्ज-पृष्ठ).<BR>—मुञ्जी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to reduce<BR>to Muñja grass, i. e. to tear to shreds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जक
मुञ्जक, a various reading for मौञ्जक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जर|मुंजर|मुंजरं|मुञ्जरं
मुञ्जर, अम्, n. the fibrous root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जात
मुञ्जात, अस्, m. a species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जातक|मुञ्जातकः
मुञ्जातक, अस्, m. a species of tree; a kind of<BR>vegetable (= पुष्प-शाक-भेद); = मुञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जाल
मुञ्जाल, अस्, m., N. of an astronomer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0783-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुट्
मुट् मुट् (connected with rts. 1. मृद्, पुट्,<BR>पुण्ड्, पुड्, पुथ्), cl. 1. 6. 10. P. मोटति,<BR>मुटति, मोटयति, &c., to crush, grind, break, (see<BR>मोटक, मोटन); to blame, rebuke, (in this sense<BR>only cl. 6. मुटति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुट
मुट in निर्-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुड्
मुड् मुड्, cl. 1. P. मोडति, &c., = rt. मुट्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्
मुण् मुण्, cl. 6. P. मुणति, &c., to<BR>promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ट्|मुंट्
मुण्ट् मुण्ट्, cl. 1. P. मुण्टति, &c., = rt.<BR>मुट् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ठ्|मुंठ्
मुण्ठ् मुण्ठ्, cl. 1. A. मुण्ठते, &c., to<BR>run away; to protect, (पालने being<BR>given as a various reading for पलायने.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड्|मुंड्
मुण्ड् मुण्ड्, cl. 1. P. मुण्डति, &c., to<BR>grind, (in this sense = rt. मुट् and con-<BR>nected with rt. 1. मृद्); to shave, shear; cl. 1. A.<BR>मुण्डते, मुण्डितुम्, to be pure; to sink; [cf.<BR>Lat. mund-o, mundu-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड|मुंड|मुण्डं|मुण्डः
मुण्ड, अस्, आ, अम्, (perhaps connected with rt. 1.<BR>मृद्), shaved, bald, having no hair on the head;<BR>hornless, destitute of horns, having no horns (Ved.);<BR>stripped of top leaves or branches, lopped (as a tree);<BR>pointless, blunt; low, mean; (अस्), m. a man with<BR>a shaved head; a bald or shaven head, bald pate,<BR>shorn poll; the forehead; a tree stripped of its top<BR>branches, the trunk of a lopped tree, a pollard; a<BR>barber (= मुण्डक); N. of a king; of a Daitya;<BR>an epithet of Rāhu; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>(आ), f. a (close-shaved) female mendicant; a species<BR>of plant (= मुण्डीरिका); Bengal madder; (ई), f. a<BR>species of plant (= महा-श्रावणिका); N. of one<BR>of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda; (अम्), n. the<BR>head; iron [cf. मुण्ड-लोह, मुण्डायस]; myrrh.<BR>—मुण्ड-चणक, अस्, m. a kind of pulse (=<BR>कलाय).<BR>—मुण्ड-धान्य, अम्, n. a kind of grain<BR>(without awns; cf. मुण्ड-शालि).<BR>—मुण्ड-पृष्-<BR>ठ, N. of a place.<BR>—मुण्ड-फल, अस्, m. a cocoa-<BR>nut tree, (the fruit being one step towards a human<BR>head made by Viśvāmitra when he proposed attempt-<BR>ing a creation in opposition to that of Brahmā.)<BR>—मुण्ड-मण्डली, f. a number of shaven heads; a<BR>number of troops of an inferior description.<BR>—मुण्ड-<BR>माला, f. or मुण्डमाला-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tantra.<BR>—मुण्ड-मालिनी, f. a form of Durgā.<BR>—मुण्ड-लोह, अम्, n. iron; [cf. अष्ट-लोहक,<BR>मुण्डायस, मुण्डित.]<BR>—मुण्ड-वेदाङ्ग, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a serpent-demon.<BR>—मुण्ड-शालि, इस्, m.<BR>a species of rice.<BR>—मुण्डाख्या (˚ड-आख्˚), f. a<BR>species of plant (= महा-श्रावणिका).<BR>—मुण्डा-<BR>यस (˚ड-अय्˚), अम्, n. iron.<BR>—मुण्डासन<BR>(˚ड-आस्˚), अम्, n. a particular posture in sitting.<BR>—मुण्डेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚ड-ईश्˚), अम्, n., N. of<BR>a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डक|मुंडक|मुण्डकं|मुंडकः|मुण्डकः
मुण्डक, अस्, m. the lopped trunk or stem of a<BR>tree, a tree stripped of its branches; a shaver, barber;<BR>(इका), f. a species of plant; (अम्), n. the head; N.<BR>of the chapters into which the Muṇḍakopaniṣad is<BR>divided.<BR>—मुण्डकोपनिषद् (˚क-उप्˚), f., N. of<BR>a well-known Upaniṣad of the Atharva-veda (con-<BR>taining three short chapters or Muṇḍakas, each of<BR>which comprises two sections or Khaṇḍas, and said<BR>to take its name from the word मुण्ड because<BR>every one who comprehends its secret doctrine is<BR>‘shorn,’ i. e. liberated from all error, a similar idea<BR>being probably involved in the name of the Kṣuri-<BR>kopanishad or ‘Razor Upaniṣad:’ the Muṇḍaka<BR>is one of the most interesting of the numerous Upa-<BR>niṣads, on account of the reasons which it gives<BR>for the superiority of these works over the Veda and<BR>its ritual; thus, according to Muṇḍaka I. 4, there<BR>are two sciences, the higher and the inferior; the<BR>inferior is the knowledge of the Ṛg-veda, Yajur-<BR>veda, Sāma-veda, Atharva-veda, pronunciation, ritual,<BR>grammar, explanation of Vedic texts, prosody, and<BR>the astronomical calendar; but the higher knowledge<BR>is that by which the imperishable Brahma is com-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">Page0784-b+ 77</a>]<BR>prehended).<BR>—मुण्डकोपनिषद्-दीपिका, f., N. of<BR>a commentary on the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डन|मुंडन|मुंडनं|मुण्डनं
मुण्डन, अम्, n. shaving the head, tonsure;<BR>protecting, defending, [cf. rt. मुण्ठ्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डनक
मुण्डनक, अस्, m. a species of rice, = मुण्ड-<BR>शालि; (इका), f. in महा-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डय
मुण्डय, Nom. P. मुण्डयति, -यितुम्, to shave,<BR>shear, cut off the hair, shave the head closely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डार
मुण्डार, अम्, n., N. of a place at which the sun<BR>was worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डित|मुंडित|मुण्डितं
मुण्डित, अस्, आ, अम्, shaved, closely shaven, bald.<BR>shorn, lopped; (अम्), n. iron; [cf. मुण्ड-लोह.]<BR>—मुण्डित-शिरस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, shaven-headed, bald-<BR>pated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डितिका
मुण्डितिका, f. a species of plant, (commonly<BR>मुण्डीरी or मुण्डिनिका; cf. मुण्डन्क.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डिन्|मुंडिन्
मुण्डिन्, ई, इनी, इ, shaven, close-shaved, bald; horn-<BR>less, having no horns; (ई), m. an epithet of Śiva;<BR>a barber.<BR>—मुण्डीश्वर-तीर्थ (˚डि-ईश्˚), अम्, n.,<BR>N. of a Tīrtha; [cf. दण्डि-मुण्डीश्वर.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डिभ
मुण्डिभ, अस्, m., Ved. a proper N., (the author<BR>of Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā XXV. 9. is so called.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डीरिका
मुण्डीरिका, f. a species of plant (= मुण्डा =<BR>मुण्डितिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डीरी
मुण्डीरी, f. a species of plant (= श्रमणा, प्र-<BR>व्रजिता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुत्कल
मुत्कल मुत्कल, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुत्खलिन्
मुत्खलिन् मुत्खलिन्, ई, m., N. of a Deva-<BR>putra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुत्य|मुत्यं
मुत्य मुत्य, अम्, n. a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुथशिल
मुथशिल मुथशिल, (in astrology) N. of<BR>the third Yoga (= مُتّصِل).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
मुद् 1. मुद्, cl. 10. P. मोदयति, मोद-<BR>यितुम्, to mix, mingle, blend, unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
मुद् 2. मुद्, cl. 1. A. मोदते (ep. occa-<BR>sionally P. मोदति, &c.), मुमुदे, मो-<BR>दिष्यते, अमोदिष्ट, मोदितुम्, to be glad or<BR>joyous or happy, to rejoice, enjoy one's self, rejoice<BR>in, have pleasure in (with inst. or loc., e. g. पुत्र-<BR>पौत्रैर् मोदस्व, rejoice thou in children and<BR>children's children; तस्मिन् न मोदामहे, we do<BR>not take pleasure in that): Caus. मोदयति, अमू-<BR>मुदत्, मोदयितुम्, to rejoice, delight, give pleasure<BR>or joy, exhilarate, yield enjoyment; [cf. Lith. mu-<BR>drùs.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
3. मुद्, त्, f. joy, pleasure, delight, joyfulness,<BR>joyousness, gladness, happiness, rejoicing; Joy per-<BR>sonified as the daughter of Tuṣṭi (Contentment);<BR>intoxication; a species of medicinal plant (= वृद्-<BR>धि); a wife, woman (?).<BR>—मुद्-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>possessing joy, feeling or experiencing pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदकर
मुदकर, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदा
मुदा, f. pleasure, enjoyment, joy, gladness.<BR>—मु-<BR>दान्वित (˚दा-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, filled with joy,<BR>pleased, delighted.<BR>—मुदा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, rejoic-<BR>ing, glad, delighted; (अती), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>king Vidūratha.<BR>—मुदा-वसु, उस्, m., N. of a son<BR>of Prajāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदित|मुदितः
मुदित, अस्, आ, अम्, rejoiced, joyful, happy, de-<BR>lighted, glad; (अस्), m. epithet of a particular sort of<BR>servant; (आ), f. joy, gladness; (अम्), n. pleasure,<BR>happiness; a particular kind of sexual embrace.<BR>—मुदित-भद्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदिर|मुदिरः
मुदिर, अस्, m. a cloud; a lover, libertine; a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदी
मुदी, f. moonshine, moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्ग|मुद्गः
मुद्ग, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 2. मुद् above,<BR>Uṇādi-s. 1. 127), a sort of kidney-bean, Phaseolus<BR>Radiatus or Phaseolus Mungo (both the plant and<BR>its beans); a cover, covering, lid; a kind of sea-<BR>bird, (in this sense for मद्गु, q. v.)<BR>—मुद्ग-<BR>गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a city.<BR>—मुद्ग-पर्णी, f. a sort<BR>of kidney-bean, Phaseolus Trilobus.<BR>—मुद्ग-भुज्,<BR>क्, or मुद्ग-भोजिन्, ई, m. ‘eating Mudga-beans,’<BR>a horse.<BR>—मुद्ग-मोदक, अस्, m. a kind of sweet-<BR>meat or confectionery.<BR>—मुद्ग-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>having beans, &c.<BR>—मुद्गार्द्रकवट (˚ग-आर्˚),<BR>अस्, m. a kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गप
मुद्गप, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गर|मुद्गरं|मुद्गरः
मुद्गर, अस्, m. (probably connected with मुद्-<BR>ग), a hammer, mallet; a hammer-like weapon,<BR>mace; a staff weighted at the bottom with iron for<BR>breaking clods of earth; a kind of dumb-bell or<BR>club-like piece of wood used for exercising the arms;<BR>a bud (= कोरक); a species of jasmine, (also अम्,<BR>n. probably the blossom); N. of a Nāga; (अम्), n.<BR>a particular posture in sitting.<BR>—मुद्गर-गोमिन्,<BR>ई, m. a proper N.<BR>—मुद्गर-पर्णक, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Nāga.<BR>—मुद्गर-पिण्डक, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Nāga.<BR>—मुद्गराकार (˚र-आक्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>hammer-shaped, shaped like a mallet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गरक|मुद्गरकः
मुद्गरक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>a hammer; (अस्), m. Averrhoa Carambola; [cf.<BR>फल-मुद्गरिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गल|मुद्गलं|मुद्गलः
मुद्गल, अस्, m. (said to be fr. मुद्ग), N. of<BR>a Ṛṣi with the patronymic Bhārmyaśva, (said to<BR>be the author of Ṛg-veda X. 102); N. of a disciple<BR>of Śākalya; of a disciple of Deva-mitra; of a son of<BR>Viśvāmitra; of various persons; (आस्), m. pl. the<BR>descendants of Mudgala; N. of a people; (अम्), n. a<BR>species of grass (= रोहिष); N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गलानी
मुद्गलानी, f., Ved. the wife of Mudgala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गष्ट|मुद्गष्टः
मुद्गष्ट, अस्, m. a species of bean (= म-<BR>कुष्ठक, &c.; also spelt मुद्गष्ठ, मुद्-<BR>गष्टक, मुद्गष्ठक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्र
मुद्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. joyous, joyful, glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्ग|मुद्गः
मुद्ग मुद्ग. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्र
मुद्र मुद्र. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रा
मुद्रा मुद्रा, f. a seal or any instrument<BR>used for sealing or stamping, a seal-ring, signet-ring<BR>[cf. अङ्गुलि-म्˚], any ring; the stamp or impression<BR>made by a seal, &c., any stamp, print, impression,<BR>mark, form, (मुद्रां दा, to set or affix a seal to<BR>anything); type, lithograph; a stamped coin, cash;<BR>any coin or piece of money, a rupee; a medal; an<BR>image, sign, badge, token (especially a token of<BR>divine attributes impressed upon the body); shutting,<BR>closing (e. g. ओष्ठ-मुद्रा, closing of the lips,<BR>sealed lips); a mystery; a general N. for certain<BR>positions or intertwinings of the fingers commonly<BR>practised in devotion or religious worship and held<BR>to be symbolical [cf. तर्क-म्˚]; the natural expres-<BR>sion of things by words (in rhetoric), calling things<BR>by their right names.<BR>—मुद्रा-कर, अस्, m. a<BR>maker of seals, engraver, coiner.<BR>—मुद्राक्षर<BR>(˚रा-अक्˚), अम्, n. type, print.<BR>—मुद्राक्षेप<BR>(˚रा-आक्˚), अस्, m. taking away or removing a seal.<BR>—मुद्राङ्क or मुद्राङ्कित (˚रा-अङ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, stamped or marked with a seal, stamped, sealed,<BR>signed, marked, printed.<BR>—मुद्रा-बल, अम्, n.<BR>(with Buddhists) a particular high number.<BR>—मुद्रा-<BR>मार्ग, अस्, m. an aperture believed to exist on the<BR>crown of the head (through which the soul is said<BR>to escape at death, = ब्रह्म-रन्ध्र).<BR>—मुद्रा-<BR>यन्त्र, अम्, n. a printing-press.<BR>—मुद्रायन्त्रा-<BR>लय (˚र-आल्˚), अस्, अम्, m. n. a printing-office.<BR>—मुद्रा-रक्षक, अस्, m. the keeper of the seals.<BR>—मुद्रा-राक्षस, अम्, n. ‘the Rākṣasa and the<BR>ring,’ N. of a drama by Viśākha-datta.<BR>—मुद्रा-<BR>लिपि, इस्, f. print, lithograph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रण|मुद्रणं
मुद्रण, अम्, n. the act of sealing, sealing up,<BR>closing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रय
मुद्रय, Nom. P. मुद्रयति, मुद्रयितुम्, to<BR>seal, stamp, print, mark, impress a stamp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रिका
मुद्रिका, f. a little seal, seal; seal-ring, signet-<BR>ring [cf. अङ्गुलि-म्˚]; a stamp, impression; a stamped<BR>coin; a particular surgical instrument; a sealed or<BR>signed paper; N. of certain positions or intertwin-<BR>ings of the fingers practised in devotion, (see मुद्रा<BR>above.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रित|मुद्रितं
मुद्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, sealed, stamped, impressed,<BR>printed, marked, bearing the impress of anything;<BR>contracted, closed, sealed up; unblown (as a flower);<BR>arranged or intertwined in a particular form (said<BR>of the fingers of the hand, cf. मुद्रा).<BR>—मुद्रित-<BR>मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having the mouth closed, having<BR>the lips sealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0784-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुधा
मुधा मुधा, ind. (perhaps connected with<BR>rt. 1. मुह् and मूढ), in vain, uselessly, unprofit-<BR>ably, to no purpose, without any purpose or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनि|मुनिः
मुनि मुनि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. मन्,<BR>to think or perceive, Uṇādi-s. IV. 122; perhaps<BR>connected with μόνος, alone, whence the Eng. monk<BR>is said to be derived; cf. also μία fr. εἷς), impulse<BR>(Ved. ?); an inspired saint, holy man endowed with<BR>divine inspiration or one who has attained more or<BR>less of a divine nature by mortification and abstraction;<BR>a sage, seer, ascetic, devotee, monk; (especially) a<BR>recluse who lives alone and has taken the vow of<BR>silence [cf. मौन]; epithet of Agastya; of Vyāsa;<BR>of Pāṇini, &c. [cf. मुनि-त्रय]; of a Buddha or<BR>Arhat [cf. शाक्य-मुनि]; of a son of Kuru; of a<BR>son of Dyuti-mat, &c.; the internal monitor or<BR>conscience, (according to Kullūka on Manu VIII. 91<BR>= परमात्मन्, the Supreme Spirit); N. of various<BR>plants, Agati Grandiflora (= अगस्ति, अगस्त्य); Bu-<BR>chanania Latifolia; Butea Frondosa; Terminalia<BR>Catappa; the mango tree; Artemisia Indica; (अयस्),<BR>m. pl. ‘the celestial Munis, the seven Munis,’ an<BR>epithet of the seven stars of Ursa Major; a symbo-<BR>lical expression for the number seven; (इस् or मुनी),<BR>f. a female Muni; (इस्), f., N. of a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and wife of Kaśyapa, mother of a class of<BR>Gandharvas and Apsarasas, (see मौनेय.)<BR>—मुनि-<BR>केश, अस्, आ or ई, अम्, Ved. ‘monk-haired,’ wearing<BR>long hair like a Muni.<BR>—मुनि-खर्जूरिका, f. a<BR>species of date.<BR>—मुनि-चित, see Gaṇa Sutaṅgamādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR>—मुनि-च्छद, अस्, m. ‘seven-<BR>leaved,’ N. of a plant (= सप्त-च्छद).<BR>—मुनि-<BR>ज्ञान-ज्यन्त, अस्, m., N. of a scribe.<BR>—मुनि-<BR>तरु, उस्, m. Agati Grandiflora.<BR>—मुनि-ता, f. or<BR>मुनि-त्व, अम्, n. the state or character of a<BR>Muni, saintship, monkhood.<BR>—मुनि-त्रय, अम्,<BR>n. ‘the Muni-triad,’ i. e. Pāṇini, Kātyāyana, and<BR>Patañjali.<BR>—मुनि-देश, अस्, m., N. of a place.<BR>—मुनि-द्रुम, अस्, m. ‘the sage Agastya's tree,’<BR>Agati Grandiflora; Calosanthes Indica.<BR>—मुनि-निर्-<BR>मित, अस्, m. a species of plant (= डिण्डिश).<BR>—मुनि-<BR>पदी, f., see Gaṇa Kumbhapadyādi to Pāṇ. V. 4,<BR>139.<BR>—मुनि-परमपरा, f., Ved. a tradition<BR>handed down from one Muni to another in regular<BR>succession.<BR>—मुनि-पित्तल, अम्, n. copper.<BR>—मुनि-<BR>पुङ्गव, अस्, m. an eminent sage.<BR>—मुनि-पुत्र,<BR>अस्, m. Artemisia Indica.<BR>—मुनि-पुत्रक, अस्, m.<BR>a wagtail.<BR>—मुनि-पुष्पक, अम्, n. the blossom<BR>of Agati Grandiflora.<BR>—मुनि-पूग, अस्, m. Areca<BR>Triandra.<BR>—मुनि-भेषज, अम्, n. ‘sage's medi-<BR>cine,’ fasting; the fruit of the yellow Myrobalan;<BR>Agati Grandiflora; Terminalia Chebula or Citrina.<BR>—मुनि-मरण, अम्, n., N. of a district.<BR>—मुनि-<BR>वन, अम्, n. a hermit's grove, a wood inhabited by<BR>ascetics.<BR>—मुनि-वर, अस्, m. an excellent Muni,<BR>best of ascetics or holy sages.<BR>—मुनि-वाक्य, अम्,<BR>n. the saying or sentence of a holy sage.<BR>—मुनि-<BR>वीर्य, अस्, m., N. of a divine being reckoned<BR>among the Viśve Devāḥ.<BR>—मुनि-व्रत, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>observing the vow of a Muni, i. e. keeping perpetual<BR>silence.<BR>—मुनि-श्रेष्ठ, अस्, m. an excellent sage,<BR>eminent saint.<BR>—मुनि-सत्त्र, अम्, n., Ved., N. of<BR>an Iṣṭi, q. v.<BR>—मुनि-सुव्रत, अस्, m., N. of the<BR>twelfth Arhat of the past Ut-sarpiṇī; of the twen-<BR>tieth of the present Ava-sarpiṇī, (also called simply<BR>मुनि.)<BR>—मुनि-स्थल, see Gaṇa Kumudādi to<BR>Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80.<BR>—मुनि-स्थान, अम्, n. an abode<BR>of ascetics, the hermitage of a recluse or holy sage.<BR>—मुनि-हत, अस्, m. an epithet of king Puṣpa-<BR>mitra.<BR>—मुनीन्द्र (˚नि-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘chief of sages<BR>or ascetics,’ a great sage or ascetic; epithet of a<BR>Buddha; of Śākya-muni; of Bharata; of Śiva; of<BR>a Dānava.<BR>—मुनीन्द्र-ता, f. the rank of a great<BR>Muni.<BR>—मुनी-वती, f., see Gaṇa Śarādi to Pāṇ.<BR>VI. 3, 120.<BR>—मुनी-वह, see Scholiast on Pāṇ. VI.<BR>3, 121.<BR>—मुनीश (˚नि-ईश), अस्, m. ‘chief of sages<BR>or ascetics,’ a great sage or ascetic.<BR>—मुनीश्वर<BR>(˚नि-ईश्˚), अस्, m. ‘chief of sages or ascetics,’ a great<BR>sage or ascetic; an epithet of Viṣṇu; of Buddha;<BR>N. of a commentator on the Siddhānta-Śiromaṇi.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">Page0785-b+ 69</a>]<BR>—मुन्य्-अन्न, आनि, n. pl. the food of ascetics<BR>(consisting mostly of roots and fruits).<BR>—मुन्य्-<BR>अयन, अम्, n., N. of an Iṣṭi, q. v.<BR>—मुन्य्-<BR>आलय-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

