मुर|मुरं|मुरः
मुर, अस्, m., N. of a Daitya slain by Kṛṣṇa;<BR>(आ), f. a species of fragrant plant (named after the<BR>Daitya); said to be the N. of the wife of Nanda<BR>and mother of Candra-gupta; (अम्), n. encompass-<BR>ing, surrounding.<BR>—मुर-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of<BR>Mura,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-द,<BR>अस्, m. ‘Mura-cutting,’ the discus of Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-<BR>द्विष्, ट्, m. ‘foe of Mura,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-भिद्, त्, m. ‘cleaver of Mura,’ epi-<BR>thet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-मर्दन, अस्,<BR>m. ‘crusher of Mura,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-रिपु, उस्, m. ‘enemy of Mura,’ epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-वैरिन्, ई, m. ‘enemy<BR>of Mura,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुर-<BR>हन्, हा, m. ‘slayer of Mura,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुरारि (˚र-अरि), इस्, m. ‘enemy of<BR>Mura,’ epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; N. of the<BR>author of the Murāri-nāṭaka or Anargha-rāghava;<BR>N. of a commentary on the Kātantra grammar.<BR>—मुरारि-गुप्त, अस्, m., N. of a pupil of Caitanya.<BR>—मुरारि-नाटक, अम्, n., N. of a drama by Mu-<BR>rāri, = Anargha-rāghava.<BR>—मुरारि-भट्ट, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a teacher.<BR>—मुरारि-मिश्र, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>scholar, = Murāri (author of the Murāri-nāṭaka).<BR>—मुरारि-विजय, अस्, m., N. of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरगण्ड|मुरगंडः|मुरगण्डः
मुरगण्ड मुरगण्ड, अस्, m. an eruption on<BR>the face (= वरण्ड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरङ्गी
