मुरचीपत्तन
मुरचीपत्तन मुरची-पत्तन, N. of a town<BR>in the Dekhan, (also read मरीचि-पत्तन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरज|मुरजः
मुरज मुरज, अस्, m. (thought by some to<BR>be a comp. of मुर + ज), a kind of drum, tam-<BR>bourine; a Śloka artificially arranged in the form of<BR>a drum; (आ), f. a great drum; N. of Kuvera's wife.<BR>—मुरज-फल, अस्, m. the jack fruit tree, Arto-<BR>carpus Integrifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजक
मुरजक, अस्, m., N. of one of Śiva's attendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरण्ड|मुरण्डः
मुरण्ड मुरण्ड, अस्, m. a country to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">Page0785-c+ 74</a>]<BR>north-west of Hindūstān (called also Lampāka, and<BR>now Lamghan in Cabul); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a<BR>people; [cf. मुरुण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरन्दला|मुरंदला
मुरन्दला मुरन्दला, f., N. of a river (=<BR>मुरला; thought by some to be Narma-dā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरमण्ड
मुरमण्ड मुरमण्ड (probably incorrect)<BR>for मुरगण्ड, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरल|मुरलः
मुरल मुरल, अस्, m. (probably fr. rt. 4.<BR>मुर्), a species of fresh-water fish; a king of the<BR>Muralas; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (आ), f., N.<BR>of a river in the country of the Keralas, = मुरन्-<BR>दला, q. v.; (ई), f. a flute, pipe.<BR>—मुरली-धर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘flute-bearer,’ an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

