मुरुताणदेश मुरुताण-देश, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्छ्
मुर्छ् मुर्छ्, cl. 1. P. मूर्छति, मुमूर्छ,<BR>मूर्छिष्यति, अमूर्छीत्, मूर्छितुम्,<BR>to settle into a fixed or solid form, assume definite<BR>shape or substance, acquire consistency; to congeal,<BR>become dense, thicken, coagulate, stiffen; to become<BR>torpid or stupefied, become senseless, lose conscious-<BR>ness, faint away, swoon, be troubled in mind; to be<BR>infatuated; to increase, grow, become strong, gather<BR>strength, become stronger or more intense, acquire<BR>vehemence or power, be powerful or effectual, take<BR>effect, (मारुतस्य रंहः शिलोच्छये न मूर्-<BR>छति, the velocity of the wind has no power against<BR>a mountain); to be a match for; to be frequent;<BR>to fill, penetrate, pervade; to make to sound loudly,<BR>play loudly: Caus. मूर्छयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>settle into a fixed or solid form, give form to, form<BR>(Ved.); to congeal, curdle (Ved.); to stupefy, cause<BR>to faint, make senseless; to strengthen, augment;<BR>to excite; to cause to sound loudly, play (a musical<BR>instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ख|मूर्खः
मूर्ख, अस्, आ, अम्, stupid, foolish, silly, igno-<BR>rant, dull, unintelligent; inexperienced in (with loc.);<BR>(अस्), m. a fool, blockhead; a sort of bean, Phaseolus<BR>Radiatus.<BR>—मूर्ख-ता, f. or मूर्ख-त्व or<BR>मूर्ख-भूय, अम्, n. stupidity, folly, foolishness,<BR>dulness.<BR>—मूर्ख-भ्रातृक, अस्, m. one who has<BR>a foolish brother.<BR>—मूर्ख-मण्डल, अम्, n. a<BR>collection or assemblage of fools.<BR>—मूर्ख-व्यसनि-<BR>नायक, अस्, आ, अम्, having a foolish and vicious<BR>commander.<BR>—मूर्ख-शत, अम्, n. a hundred fools.<BR>—मूर्खी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become stupid or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खिमन्
मूर्खिमन्, आ, m. dulness, stupidity, folly (=<BR>मूर्ख-ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छत्
मूर्छत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, becoming senseless, faint-<BR>ing, swooning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छन
मूर्छन, अस्, ई, अम्, stupefying, causing insen-<BR>sibility (applied to one of the five arrows of Kāma-<BR>deva or Cupid); strengthening, augmenting, con-<BR>firming; (अम्, आ), n. f. fainting, swooning, syncope;<BR>vehemence, violence, prevalence, growth, increase,<BR>(in this sense usually अम्, n.); swelling or rising of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">Page0786-a+ 77</a>]<BR>sounds, an intonation, note, a tone or semitone in<BR>the musical scale, the seventh part of a Grāma or<BR>scale, (each Grāma or scale consisted of seven notes<BR>and contained also seven Mūrchanās); modulation,<BR>melody, (in these senses usually आ, f.); a particular<BR>process in metallic preparations, calcining quicksilver<BR>with sulphur, (in this sense only अम्, n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0785-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छयित्वा
मूर्छयित्वा, ind. having caused to thicken or<BR>coagulate, having curdled (Ved.); having augmented;<BR>having caused to sound loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छा
मूर्छा, f. fainting, loss of consciousness, a swoon,<BR>stupor; spiritual stupor or blindness, delusion, hallu-<BR>cination; the rising of sounds, diatonic scale; a par-<BR>ticular process in calcining metals.<BR>—मूर्छाक्षेप<BR>(˚छा-आक्˚), अस्, m. (in rhetoric) expressing vehement<BR>dissent or disapprobation by fainting.<BR>—मूर्छा-<BR>परीत, अस्, आ, अम्, overcome with faintness or<BR>swooning, fainting away, insensible, (according to a<BR>Scholiast = निश्चेतन.)<BR>—मूर्छा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्,<BR>suffering from faintness, swooning away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छाल|मूर्च्छालः
मूर्छाल, अस्, आ, अम्, fainting, fainted, swooning,<BR>insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छित|मूर्च्छितः
मूर्छित, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, rendered sense-<BR>less, fainted, fainting, insensible, bewildered, infatu-<BR>ated; intoxicated; stupid, ignorant; rendered vehe-<BR>ment or violent, intensified; grown, increased, aug-<BR>mented, swollen; rising upwards, lofty; filled with;<BR>calcined (as quicksilver; cf. मूर्छन); (अम्), n.<BR>epithet of a kind of song or air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त|मूर्त्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thickened, congealed, coagu-<BR>lated, curdled (Ved.); settled into any fixed shape,<BR>formed, substantial, solid, material, corporeal, em-<BR>bodied, incarnate; real (said of the practically useful<BR>division of time as opposed to the अ-मूर्त, the<BR>unreal or imaginary division); stupefied, unconscious,<BR>fainted, insensible.<BR>—मूर्त-त्व, अम्, n. the posses-<BR>sion of a form, embodiment, corporality, incarnate<BR>existence, materiality.<BR>—मूर्त-मात्र, अम्, n. that<BR>which is merely material, only corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ति|मूर्तिः|मूर्त्ति|मूर्त्तिः
मूर्ति, इस्, f. (often written मूर्त्ति), any solid<BR>body, any tangible or material form, (in philosophy)<BR>anything which has definite shape and limits (as<BR>earth, air, fire, water, and mind, but not आकाश,<BR>ether), a material element (especially as a component<BR>part of the human body), body, form, visible shape,<BR>matter, substance; embodiment, manifestation, in-<BR>carnation, personification, (मूर्तिर् धर्मस्य शाश्-<BR>वती, an eternal personification of justice; cf. तपो-<BR>म्˚); an image, statue, figure, form; beauty; N.<BR>of the first astrological house; N. of a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa and wife of Dharma; (इस्), m., N. of one<BR>of the sages under the tenth Manu; [cf. perhaps Gr.<BR>βρέτας, μορφή.]<BR>—मूर्ति-तस्, ind. from the form,<BR>bodily, substantially.<BR>—मूर्ति-त्व, अम्, n. the being<BR>or having a body, corporeity, embodiment, materiality,<BR>(मूर्तित्वे परिकल्पितः, made into bodily shape.)<BR>—मूर्ति-धर, अस्, आ, अम्, having a body, em-<BR>bodied, corporeal, incarnate.<BR>—मूर्ति-प, अस्, m.<BR>‘image-keeper,’ a priest who guards an idol.<BR>—मूर्ति-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. the state of assuming a solid form,<BR>corporeity.<BR>—मूर्ति-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having a<BR>material or bodily form, material, embodied, corpo-<BR>real, incarnate, personified [cf. ख-म्˚, विश्व-म्˚];<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a son of Kuśa; (अत्), n. a body.<BR>—मूर्ति-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, possessing a particular<BR>form.<BR>—मूर्ति-मात्रा, f. a particle of matter.<BR>—मूर्ति-लिङ्ग, perhaps = Prāg-jyotiṣa, the city of<BR>Naraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्भिणी
मुर्भिणी मुर्भिणी, f. a chafing-dish, small<BR>fire-place, fire-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्मुर|मुर्मुरः
मुर्मुर मुर्मुर, अस्, m. (an onomatopoetic<BR>word), a fire made of chaff, burning chaff; the god<BR>of love; N. of one of the horses of the sun; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्व्
मुर्व् मुर्व् [cf. rt. 1. मू], cl. 1. P. मूर्वति,<BR>मूर्वितुम्, to bind, tie; [cf. मूर्वा.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुल्
मुल् मुल् = rt. मूल्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुलालिन्
मुलालिन् मुलालिन्, ई, m. or मुलाली, f., Ved.<BR>(probably) a species of edible lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशटी
मुशटी मुशटी, मुशल, मुशलिका, मुशलिन्.<BR>See मुसटी, मुसल, मुसलिका, मुसलिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशल्लह
मुशल्लह मुशल्लह or मुसल्लह, an astro-<BR>logical term (مصالحة).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
मुष् 1. मुष्, cl. 1. P. मोषति, मोषि-<BR>तुम्, = rt. मष्, to kill, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
मुष् 2. मुष् [cf. rt. 1. मूष्], cl. 9. P.<BR>मुष्णाति (rarely cl. 6. P. मुषति), मु-<BR>मोष, मोषिष्यति, अमोषीत् (Ved. forms मो-<BR>षति, मोषथ, मुषायते), मोषितुम्, to steal,<BR>filch, pilfer, rob, plunder, seize, carry off; to steal,<BR>away, tear away, ravish; to captivate, enrapture; to<BR>surpass, excel; cl. 4. P. मुष्यति, मोषितुम्, = rt.<BR>मुस्, to break, destroy, (according to the commen-<BR>tator on Bhaṭṭi-kāvya XV. 16, where अमुषः is<BR>explained by खण्डितवान् असि): Pass. मुष्यते:<BR>Caus. मोषयति, Aor. अमूमुषत्: Desid. मु-<BR>मुषिषति, -षितुम्, see Pāṇ. I. 2, 8: Intens.<BR>मोमुष्यते, मोमोष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुषिषु|मुमुषिषुः
मुमुषिषु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to steal, intend-<BR>ing to rob; (उस्), m. a thief, robber.<BR>—मुमुषिषु-<BR>वत्, ind. like a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
3. मुष्, ट्, f. stealing, theft; (ट्, ट्, ट्), robbing,<BR>stealing, taking away (at the end of comps.); dis-<BR>pelling (darkness, &c.); surpassing, excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषक|मुषकः
मुषक, अस्, m. a mouse, = मूषक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषा
मुषा, f. = मूषा, a crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषि|मुषिः
मुषि, इस्, इस्, इ, stealing, &c. (in मनो-म्˚, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषित|मुषितं
मुषित, अस्, आ, अम्, stolen, robbed, plundered;<BR>stript; deceived, cheated; ravished, carried off, torn<BR>away, bereft of, deprived of, free from.<BR>—मुषित-<BR>चेतस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, bereft of sense, deprived of con-<BR>sciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषितक|मुषितकं
मुषितक, अस्, इका, अम्, stolen in a low or vile<BR>manner; (अम्), n. stolen property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषित्वा
मुषित्वा, ind. having stolen, having carried off, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषीवन्
मुषीवन्, आ, m. (मुषीवाणम्, acc. c.), Ved. a<BR>thief, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्क|मुष्कः
मुष्क, अस्, m. (perhaps originally ‘a little mouse,’<BR>fr. मुष् = 2. मूष् + क), a testicle; the scrotum;<BR>a species of tree (= मुषक); a muscular or<BR>stout person (= मांसल); a thief; a crowd, heap,<BR>quantity, multitude, mass; (औ), m. du. pudenda<BR>muliebria.<BR>—मुष्क-कच्छू, ऊस्, f. an eruption on<BR>the scrotum.<BR>—मुष्क-देश, अस्, m. the region of<BR>the scrotum.<BR>—मुष्क-द्वय, अम्, n. the two<BR>testicles.<BR>—मुष्क-भार, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. having<BR>large testicles, (Sāy. = प्रवृद्ध-मुष्क.)<BR>—मु-<BR>ष्क-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having testicles; an<BR>epithet of Indra as author of Ṛg-veda X. 38.<BR>—मुष्क-शून्य, अस्, m. ‘one who is without<BR>testicles,’ a castrated person, eunuch, guard of the<BR>women's apartments.<BR>—मुष्क-शोफ, अस्, m. swell-<BR>ing of the testicles.<BR>—मुष्क-स्रोतस्, अस्, n. the vas<BR>deferens (in anatomy).<BR>—मुष्काबर्ह (˚क-आब्˚),<BR>अस्, m., Ved. one who gelds or castrates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कक|मुष्ककः
मुष्कक, अस्, m. a species of tree (the ashes of<BR>which are used as a cautery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कर|मुष्करः
मुष्कर, अस्, आ, अम्, having testicles; (अस्), m.<BR>a man with large testicles; a species of small animal<BR>or insect (Atharva-veda VI. 14, 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्ट
मुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, a rare form for मुषित,<BR>q. v.; (अम्), n. theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टि|मुष्टिः
मुष्टि, इस्, m. f. stealing, filching, pilfering; the<BR>closed or clenched hand (perhaps originally ‘the<BR>hand closed to grasp anything stolen’); the fist,<BR>(गूढाङ्गुष्ठ-कृत-मुष्टि, the clenched fist<BR>with the thumbs turned in); a fistful, handful [cf.<BR>दर्भ-म्˚, कुश-म्˚, केश-म्˚, गाढ-म्˚]; a par-<BR>ticular measure (= a handful = 1 Pala); a hilt or<BR>handle (of a sword, &c.); a compendium, abridg-<BR>ment; (according to Mahī-dhara on Vājasaneyi-s.<BR>XXIII. 24) the penis (= लिङ्ग); [cf. Old Germ.<BR>fust; Angl. Sax. fyst.]<BR>—मुष्टि-करण, अम्, n.<BR>clenching the fist.<BR>—मुष्टि-ता, f. firmness of grasp.<BR>—मुष्टि-देश, अस्, m. the part of a bow which is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">Page0786-c+ 77</a>]<BR>grasped in the hand, the middle of a bow.<BR>—मु-<BR>ष्टि-द्यूत, अम्, n. a kind of game, odd or even,<BR>(commonly called पुरमुट्खेला.)<BR>—मुष्टिन्-<BR>धम, अस्, ई, अम्, blowing into the closed hand.<BR>—मुष्टिन्-धय, अस्, आ, अम्, sucking the fist<BR>or closed hand; (अस्), m. a child, boy.<BR>—मुष्टि-<BR>पात, अस्, m. pummelling, boxing.<BR>—मुष्टि-प्र-<BR>हार, अस्, m. a blow with the fist.<BR>—मुष्टि-बन्-<BR>ध, अस्, m. clenching the fist, closing the hand (in<BR>taking hold of anything); a handful.<BR>—मुष्टि-<BR>बन्धन, अम्, n. the act of clenching the fist.<BR>—मुष्टि-मुख, अस्, ई, अम्, having a fist-like face.<BR>—मुष्टि-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be measured or<BR>spanned with the hand, (मध्येन मुष्टि-मेयेन,<BR>with a waist which might be spanned with the<BR>fingers.)<BR>—मुष्टि-युद्ध, अम्, n. a fight with<BR>fists, pugilistic encounter.<BR>—मुष्टि-सङ्ग्राह-पी-<BR>डित, अस्, आ, अम्, squeezed by a grasp with the fist,<BR>griped.<BR>—मुष्टि-हत्या, f., Ved. a hand to hand<BR>engagement.<BR>—मुष्टि-हन्, आ, घ्नी, अ, Ved. fight-<BR>ing hand to hand (said of common soldiers as opposed<BR>to those who fought in chariots).<BR>—मुष्टी-कृ, cl.<BR>8. P. -करोति, &c., to close the hand, clench the fist.<BR>—मुष्टी-कृत्य, ind. having clenched the fist.<BR>—मुष्टी-मुष्टि, ind. fist to fist, hand to hand<BR>fighting, fisticuffs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिक|मुष्टिकः
मुष्टिक, अस्, m. a particular position of the<BR>hands; a goldsmith; N. of an Asura; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of an outcast race, = डोम्बास्; (आ), f. the fist,<BR>hand; (अम्), n. a fight with fists, pugilistic encounter,<BR>fisticuffs.<BR>—मुष्टिक-घ्न, अस्, m. ‘slayer of<BR>Muṣṭika,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—मुष्टिक-स्वस्-<BR>तिक, अस्, m. a particular position of the hands in<BR>dancing.<BR>—मुष्टिका-कथन, अम्, n. talking with<BR>the fingers.<BR>—मुष्टिकान्तक (˚क-अन्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘annihilator of Muṣṭika,’ an epithet of Bala-deva,<BR>the brother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्णत्
मुष्णत्, अन्, अती, अत्, stealing, robbing, taking<BR>away, depriving of; captivating; excelling, surpass-<BR>ing, eclipsing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्यमाण
मुष्यमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, being robbed, being<BR>plundered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तु|मुस्तुः
मुस्तु, उस्, m. f. = मुष्टि, the fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषल|मुषलः
मुषल मुषल, मुषल्य. See मुसल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्ठक|मुष्ठकः
मुष्ठक मुष्ठक, अस्, m. black mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्
मुस् मुस् [cf. rt. 2. मुष्, cl. 4], cl. 4. P.<BR>मुस्यति, &c., to break in pieces, cleave,<BR>divide, cut, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल|मुसलं|मुसलः
मुसल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (often spelt मुषल and<BR>less correctly मुशल), a pestle, a kind of wooden<BR>pestle used for cleaning rice; a mace, club, (चक्र-<BR>मुसलः सङ्ग्रामः, a battle fought with discuses<BR>and clubs); a particular surgical instrument; a par-<BR>ticular constellation; the twenty-second astronomical<BR>Yoga or division of the moon's path; N. of a son of<BR>Viśvāmitra; (ई), f. the plant Curculigo Orchioides;<BR>Salvinia Cucullata; the house-lizard.<BR>—मुसला-मु-<BR>सलि, ind. club against club.<BR>—मुसलायुध (˚ल-<BR>आय्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, club-armed; (अस्), m. an epithet of<BR>Bala-deva.<BR>—मुसली-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भ-<BR>वितुम्, to become a club.<BR>—मुसलोलूखल (˚ल-<BR>उल्˚), अम्, n. a pestle and mortar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलक
मुसलक, अस्, m., N. of a mountain; (इका), f. a<BR>common lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलित
मुसलित, अस्, आ, अम्, see Gaṇa Tārakādi to Pāṇ.<BR>V. 2, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलिन्
मुसलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, armed with a club; (ई), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; of Bala-deva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलीय
मुसलीय or मुसल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, deserving to be<BR>pounded to death or to be put to death with a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्र|मुस्रं
मुस्र, अम्, n. a pestle; a tear (in this sense =<BR>अश्रु, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसटी
मुसटी मुसटी, f. a white variety of Pani-<BR>cum Italicum, (also read मुशटी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल्लह
मुसल्लह मुसल्लह. See मुशल्लह, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसारगल्व
मुसारगल्व मुसारगल्व, coral or a kind of<BR>white coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0786-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त्
मुस्त् मुस्त्, cl. 10. P. मुस्तयति, मुस्त-<BR>यितुम्, to gather, collect, heap up, accu-<BR>mulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त|मुस्तं|मुस्तः
मुस्त, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. a species of grass,<BR>Cyperus Rotundus; (अम्), n. the root of the Musta<BR>grass; [cf. भद्र-म्˚.]<BR>—मुस्त-गिरि, इस्, m., N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR>—मुस्ताद (˚त-अद or ˚त-आद),<BR>अस्, m. ‘grass-eater,’ a hog, a wild boar.<BR>—मुस्ताभ<BR>(˚त-आभ्˚), अम्, n. a species of Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तक|मुस्तकः
मुस्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, m. f. n. a species of grass,<BR>Cyperus Rotundus; (अस्), m. a particular vegetable<BR>poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तु|मुस्तुः
मुस्तु मुस्तु. See p. 786, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्र|मुस्रं
मुस्र मुस्र. See p. 786, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह्
मुह् 1. मुह्, cl. 4. P. मुह्यति, मुमोह,<BR>मोहिष्यति or मोक्ष्यति, अमुहत्, मो-<BR>हितुम् or मोग्धुम् or मोढुम्, to become stupe-<BR>fied or unconscious, to be faint, lose consciousness,<BR>to be perplexed or embarrassed; to be disturbed in<BR>mind; to err or be mistaken; to be foolish or<BR>stupid or infatuated; to fail: Caus. मोहयति, -यि-<BR>तुम्, Aor. अमूमुहत्, to stupefy, bewilder, per-<BR>plex, infatuate, deprive of consciousness; to throw<BR>into disorder; to cause to err; to mistake (A., e. g.<BR>अध्वानम् मोहयन्ते, they mistake the way):<BR>Intens. मोमुह्यते, मोमोग्धि, मोमोढि, to be<BR>in great perplexity or greatly embarrassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्ध|मुग्धः
मुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, perplexed, stupid,<BR>ignorant; infatuated, enamoured; foolish, silly, sim-<BR>ple, mistaken, erring; inexperienced, artless, inno-<BR>cent, rendered attractive by youthful simplicity,<BR>charming, tender, lovely, beautiful; (आ), f. a young<BR>and beautiful female.<BR>—मुग्ध-कथा, f. a story<BR>of a fool, tale about a fool.<BR>—मुग्ध-ता, f. or<BR>मुग्ध-त्व, अम्, n. stupidity, silliness, ignorance;<BR>simplicity, artlessness, loveliness, charmingness, grace-<BR>fulness.<BR>—मुग्ध-दृश्, क्, क्, क्, lovely-eyed, hav-<BR>ing beautiful eyes.<BR>—मुग्ध-धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, or<BR>मुग्ध-बुद्धि, इस्, इस्, इ, silly, simple, a simpleton.<BR>—मुग्ध-बोध, अम्, n. ‘instructing the igno-<BR>rant’ (scil. व्याकरण), N. of a celebrated grammar<BR>by Vopa-deva (a grammarian who is supposed to<BR>have flourished in the thirteenth century, and who is<BR>regarded as a great authority in Bengal).<BR>—मुग्ध-<BR>बोध-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n. a supplement or appendix<BR>to the Mugdha-bodha.<BR>—मुग्धबोध-प्रदीप,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a commentary on the Mugdha-bodha.<BR>—मुग्धबोध-सम्बोधिनी, f., N. of a com-<BR>mentary on the Mugdha-bodha.<BR>—मुग्ध-बोधिनी,<BR>f., scil. टीका, N. of a commentary by Bharata-malla<BR>on the Amara-koṣa and of a commentary by Bha-<BR>rata-mallika (probably identical with the preceding<BR>author) on the Bhaṭṭi-kāvya.<BR>—मुग्ध-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. stupidity, simplicity, inexperience.<BR>—मुग्ध-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, perplexed, embarrassed, infatuated,<BR>mistaken.<BR>—मुग्धाक्षी (˚ध-अक्˚), f. a lovely-<BR>eyed woman.<BR>—मुग्धाग्रणी (˚ध-अग्˚), ईस्, m.<BR>the greatest of simpletons, the stupidest of the stupid.<BR>—मुग्धा-चक्र, अम्, n. a particular mystical<BR>circle.<BR>—मुग्धानन (˚ध-आन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>lovely-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह्
2. मुह्, क्, क्, क्, or ट्, ट्, ट्, perplexing, embarrass-<BR>ing, infatuating; [cf. मनो-मुह्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहिर|मुहिरः
मुहिर, अस्, आ, अम्, foolish, stupid; (अस्), m. a<BR>blockhead [cf. मुहेर]; ‘the bewilderer,’ epithet<BR>of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहु|मुहुः
मुहु, ind. = मुहुस्, Ved. suddenly, in a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुक|मुहुकं
मुहुक, अम्, n., Ved. a moment, instant; [cf.<BR>मुहूर्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुस्
मुहुस्, ind. (perhaps originally ‘in a bewildering<BR>manner’), suddenly, all at once, in a moment, in an<BR>instant (Ved.); for a moment, for a time, awhile;<BR>at every moment, repeatedly, constantly; मुहुस् —<BR>मुहुस्, at one moment — at another; at one time<BR> — at another; मुहुर् मुहुस्, at every moment,<BR>repeatedly, again and again, over and over again;<BR>on the other hand; [cf. पुनर्.]<BR>—मुहुर्-गीर्, ईर्,<BR>ईर्, ईर्, Ved. swallowing suddenly; (Sāy.) ever being<BR>hymned (= सर्वदा गीयमानः).<BR>—मुहुर्-भा-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">Page0787-b+ 79</a>]<BR>षा, f. or मुहुर्-वचस्, अस्, n. repeating what is<BR>said, repetition, tautology.<BR>—मुहुर्-भुज्, क्, m.<BR>‘constantly eating,’ a horse.<BR>—मुहुश्-चारिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, occurring repeatedly, recurring over and over again.<BR>—मुहुस्-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, loving or desiring<BR>again and again.<BR>—मुहुस्-तनैस्, ind. at repeated<BR>intervals, repeatedly, constantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्त, अस्, अम्, m. n. a moment, an instant,<BR>any short space of time, (मुहूर्तात्, after an instant,<BR>immediately, directly, at once; मुहूर्तेन, after an<BR>instant, after a little while; कु-मुहूर्त, an inau-<BR>spicious moment, cf. दुर्-म्˚, प्रति-म्˚); a particu-<BR>lar division of time (see Manu 1. 64); the thirtieth<BR>part of a day, a period of forty-eight minutes; (अस्),<BR>m. an astrologer; (आस्), m. pl. the Muhūrtas or<BR>Hours personified as the children of Muhūrtā; (आ),<BR>f., N. of a daughter of Dakṣa (wife of Dharma or<BR>Manu and mother of the Muhūrtas).<BR>—मुहूर्त-<BR>कल्प-द्रुम, अस्, m. and मुहूर्त-गण-पति,<BR>इस्, m., N. of works.<BR>—मुहूर्त-चिन्तामणि, इस्,<BR>m., N. of an astrological work by Rāma the son of<BR>Ananta.<BR>—मुहूर्त-ज, आस्, m. pl. children of Mu-<BR>hūrtā; [cf. मौहूर्तिक.]<BR>—मुहूर्त-तत्त्व, अम्,<BR>n., N. of a work.<BR>—मुहूर्त-दीपक, अस्, m., N.<BR>of an astrological work by Mahā-deva.<BR>—मुहूर्त-<BR>दीपिका, f., N. of a work.<BR>—मुहूर्त-मार्तण्ड,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an astrological work by Nārāyaṇa.<BR>—मुहूर्त-वल्लभा, f., N. of a commentary on<BR>the Muhūrta-mārtaṇḍa.<BR>—मुहूर्त-स्तोम, आस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of an Ekāha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्तक|मुहूर्तकः
मुहूर्तक = मुहूर्त, a moment, instant; an<BR>hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहेर|मुहेरः
मुहेर, अस्, m. = मुहिर, a fool, blockhead; [cf.<BR>perhaps Gr. μῶρο-ς; Lat. moru-s, mor-osu-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढ|मूढः
मूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, bewildered, per-<BR>plexed, confounded, confused [cf. दिङ्-म्˚], uncer-<BR>tain how to act; infatuated; stupid, dull, silly, foolish,<BR>simple, ignorant; mistaken, deceived, erring, gone<BR>astray or adrift; wrong, out of the right place (as<BR>the fetus in delivery), abortive; causing confusion,<BR>confounding; epithet of a particular position in the<BR>Yoga system; (अस्), m. a fool, blockhead, dolt, idiot;<BR>a sluggard; (आस्), m. pl. an epithet of the elements<BR>in the Sāṅkhya philosophy.<BR>—मूढ-गर्भ, अस्,<BR>m. difficult delivery; a dead fetus.<BR>—मूढ-<BR>ग्राह, अस्, m. a confused notion, misconception,<BR>infatuation.<BR>—मूढ-चक्षुर्-गद-च्छेतृ, ता, m.<BR>the remover of the defect of vision of the foolish.<BR>—मूढ-चेतन, अस्, आ, अम्, or मूढ-चेतस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, bewildered in mind, foolish, simple, silly.<BR>—मूढ-ता, f. or मूढ-त्व, अम्, n. stupidity,<BR>infatuation, bewilderment, confusion, simplicity, folly,<BR>ignorance; error, mistake, (ग्रन्थि-मूढता, mis-<BR>take or confusion in disentangling a knot.)<BR>—मूढ-<BR>धी, ईस्, ईस्, इ, or मूढ-बुद्धि, or मूढ-मति,<BR>इस्, इस्, इ, ‘silly-minded, ’ silly, simple, foolish.<BR>—मू-<BR>ढ-प्रभु, उस्, m. the chief of fools, a great<BR>blockhead.<BR>—मूढ-रथ, अस्, m., N. of a man;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of his descendants.<BR>—मूढ-वत्,<BR>ind. like a fool.<BR>—मूढ-सत्त्व, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘silly-<BR>minded,’ infatuated, insane.<BR>—मूढात्मन् (˚ढ-<BR>आत्˚), आ, आ, अ, bewildered or stupefied in mind, un-<BR>conscious, insensible, foolish, a fool.<BR>—मूढेश्वर<BR>(˚ढ-ईश्˚), अस्, m. the greatest of fools, a great sim-<BR>pleton, arrant blockhead; N. of an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुस्
मुहुस् मुहुस्. See col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्त मुहूर्त. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
मू 1. मू (connected with rts. मव्,<BR>मव्य्), cl. 1. A. मवते (sometimes P. -ति),<BR>to bind, tie, make fast: Caus. Aor. अमीमवत्:<BR>Desid. of Caus. मिमावयिषति, see Scholist on Pāṇ.<BR>VII. 4, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
2. मू, ऊस्, f. binding, tying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूक|मूकः
मूक, अस्, आ, अम्, dumb, silent, speechless, mute<BR>[cf. एड-म्˚, कल्ल-म्˚]; wretched, poor; (अस्), m.<BR>a mute; a poor man; N. of a Dānava; of a Nāga;<BR>[cf. Lat. mutus.]<BR>—मूक-ता, f. or मूक-त्व, अम्,<BR>n. dumbness, muteness, silence.<BR>—मूक-भाव, अस्,<BR>m. the state of being dumb, dumbness.<BR>—मूकाण्-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">Page0787-c+ 76</a>]<BR>डज (˚क-अण्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having the birds silent<BR>(said of a forest).<BR>—मूकाम्बिका (˚क-अम्˚), f. (per-<BR>haps) a form of Durgā; मूकाम्बिकायाः सदनम्,<BR>N. of a place.<BR>—मूकी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्-<BR>तुम्, to make dumb, render speechless, put to<BR>silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूकिमन्
मूकिमन्, आ, m. dumbness, muteness, silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत|मूतः
2. मूत, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see rt. 1. मीव्), bound,<BR>tied; woven; (अस्, अम्), m. n., Ved. a woven basket;<BR>a woven band of cloth or fillet.<BR>—मूत-कार्य, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, consisting of plaited work or basket work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूतक
मूतक, अम्, n., Ved. a little basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूकलराय
