मूचीप
मूचीप मूचीप, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people;<BR>[cf. मूतिब.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूजवत्|मूजवन्त्
मूजवत् मूज-वत्, आन्, m., N. of a moun-<BR>tain; (अन्तस्), m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूजालदेव
मूजालदेव मूजाल-देव, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढ|मूढः
मूढ मूढ, मूढ-चेतस्, &c. See col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत|मूतः
मूत 1. and 2. मूत. See under rt. 1. मीव्<BR>and rt. 1. मू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूतिब
मूतिब मूतिब, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र|मूत्रं
मूत्र मूत्र, अम्, n. (probably connected<BR>with rt. 1. मिह्; but according to Uṇādi-s. IV. 162.<BR>fr. rt. मुच्, to discharge; by others connected with<BR>rts. 1. मीव् and मिन्व्), the fluid secreted by the<BR>kidneys, urine.<BR>—मूत्र-कर, अस् ई, अम्, producing<BR>urine.<BR>—मूत्र-कृच्छ्र, अम्, n. painful discharge<BR>of urine in minute quantities, strangury; a class of<BR>urinary affections (of which eight kinds are enume-<BR>rated, including gravel, stone, &c.).<BR>—मूत्र-कृच्-<BR>छ्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ, labouring under painful discharge<BR>of urine, suffering from strangury.<BR>—मूत्र-कृत-<BR>वासस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. steeped or soaked in urine.<BR>—मूत्र-कोश, अस्, m. the scrotum.<BR>—मूत्र-<BR>क्षय, अस्, m. insufficient secretion of urine.<BR>—मू-<BR>त्र-ग्रन्थि, इस्, m. a knot or induration on the<BR>neck of the bladder.<BR>—मूत्र-घात = मूत्राघात,<BR>q. v.<BR>—मूत्र-जठर, अस्, अम्, m. n. swelling of<BR>the belly in consequence of retention of urine.<BR>—मू-<BR>त्र-दोष, अस्, m. urinary disease.<BR>—मूत्र-निरो-<BR>ध, अस्, m. obstruction or retention of urine.<BR>—मू-<BR>त्र-पतन, अस्, m. the civet cat.<BR>—मूत्र-पथ,<BR>अस्, m. the urinary passage.<BR>—मूत्र-परीक्षा, f.<BR>examination of urine, uroscopy; N. of a chapter of<BR>the Śārṅgadhara-saṃhitā.<BR>—मूत्र-पुट, अम्, n.<BR>‘urine-cavity,’ the lower belly.<BR>—मूत्र-पुरीष,<BR>अम्, n. urine and excrement.<BR>—मूत्र-प्रसेक, अस्,<BR>m. the urethra.<BR>—मूत्र-फला, f. Cucumis Utilissi-<BR>mus (= कर्कटी); another species of cucumber (=<BR>त्रपुषी).<BR>—मूत्र-भावित, अस्, आ, अम्, saturated<BR>with urine.<BR>—मूत्र-मार्ग, अस्, m. ‘urine-canal,’<BR>the urethra.<BR>—मूत्रमार्ग-निरोधन, अम्, n.<BR>obstruction of the urethra.<BR>—मूत्र-वर्धक, अस्,<BR>इका, अम्, increasing urine, diuretic.<BR>—मूत्र-वह,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, conveying urine.<BR>—मूत्र-विबन्ध-<BR>घ्न, अस्, ई, अम्, preventing suppression of urine,<BR>causing discharge of urine.<BR>—मूत्र-विष, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, poisonous with urine.<BR>—मूत्र-वृद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>copious secretion of urine.<BR>—मूत्र-शकृत्, त्, n.<BR>urine and excrement.<BR>—मूत्र-शुक्र, अम्, n. a<BR>disease in which semen and urine are ejected toge-<BR>ther.<BR>—मूत्र-शूल, अस्, m. urinary colic.<BR>—मूत्र-<BR>सङ्क्षय, अस्, m. insufficient secretion of urine<BR>(= मूत्र-क्षय).<BR>—मूत्र-सङ्ग, अस्, m. urinary<BR>obstruction, a painful and bloody discharge of urine.<BR>—मूत्र-सङ्गिन्, ई, इनी, इ, suffering from the<BR>above disease.<BR>—मूत्राघात (˚र-आघ्˚), अस्, m.<BR>affection of the urine, urinary disease (of which twelve<BR>or thirteen kinds are enumerated).<BR>—मूत्रातीत<BR>(˚र-अत्˚), अस्, m. ‘past the proper time for voiding<BR>urine,’ a particular kind of retention of urine.<BR>—मू-<BR>त्राशय (˚र-आश्˚), अस्, m. ‘urine-receptacle,’ the<BR>lower belly.<BR>—मूत्रासाद = मूत्रौक-साद, q. v.<BR>—मूत्रोत्सङ्ग (˚र-उत्˚) = मूत्र-सङ्ग, q. v.<BR>—मूत्रौक-साद (˚र-ओक्˚), अस्, m. a disease in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">Page0788-a+ 74</a>]<BR>which the urine assumes various colours and is voided<BR>with pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0787-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रय
मूत्रय, Nom. P. मूत्रयति, -यितुम्, to dis-<BR>charge urine; to make water against or upon (with<BR>acc.): Intens. मोमूत्र्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रल|मूत्रलं
मूत्रल, अस्, आ, अम्, promoting (the secretion of)<BR>urine, diuretic; (आ), f. Cucumis Utilissimus; another<BR>species of cucumber, = वालुकी; (अम्), n. a species<BR>of cucumber (= त्रपुष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रित|मूत्रितः
मूत्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, voided as urine, discharged<BR>like urine; soiled with urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र्य
मूत्र्य, अस्, आ, अम्, urinary, belonging or relating<BR>to urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर
मूर 1. मूर, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. = मूढ,<BR>stupefied, bewildered, stupid, dull, foolish; [cf. अ-म्˚,<BR>अ-प्रम्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर
मूर 2. मूर, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps fr. a form<BR>मू = rt. 1. मीव्), Ved. rushing, impetuous; (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy.) destroying killing (= मारक, fr. rt.<BR>मृ).<BR>—मूर-देव, अस्, m., Ved. epithet of a par-<BR>ticular kind of demon; (Sāy.) sporting in destruction<BR>(= मारण-क्रीड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर
मूर 3. मूर, अम्, n., Ved. = मूल, a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूरु
मूरु मूरु, N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ख|मूर्खः
मूर्ख मूर्ख. See P. 785, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खलिका
मूर्खलिका मूर्खलिका, f. an arrow in the<BR>form of a bird's heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्छन
मूर्छन मूर्छन. See p. 785, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ण|मूर्णः
मूर्ण मूर्ण. See under rt. मॄ, p. 793.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त|मूर्त्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त मूर्त, मूर्ति. See p. 786, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्
मूर्धन् मूर्धन्, आ, m. (in Uṇādi-s. 1. 158.<BR>said to be fr. rt. मुर्व्, to bind), the forehead, brow,<BR>skull; the head in general; a head, chief, leader,<BR>superior, (सर्वेषाम् भूतानाम् मूर्धा राजा, the<BR>king is the head of all creatures); the highest or<BR>foremost or most prominent part, surface, top, point,<BR>peak, summit, (पर्वतस्य मूर्धा, the top or<BR>peak of a mountain); ‘the summit,’ epithet of a<BR>particular spiritual condition with Buddhists; (in<BR>geometry) the base, (opposed to अग्र); मूर्ध्नि<BR>or मूर्धनि, at the head or highest point, at the<BR>beginning or commencement, in the front, (अतिष्-<BR>ठन् मनुजेन्द्राणाम् मूर्ध्नि, he stood at the<BR>head of the kings of men; सङ्ग्राम-मूर्धनि,<BR>in the front of the battle); before, above, over.<BR>—मूर्ध-कर्णी or मूर्ध-कर्परी, f. or मूर्-<BR>ध-खोल, अम्, n. a broad-brimmed hat (worn as<BR>a shelter from rain); an umbrella.<BR>—मूर्ध-ज,<BR>अस्, m. ‘head-born,’ the hair of the head, (in this<BR>sense usually आस्, m. pl.); the mane; N. of a king (a<BR>Cakra-vartin).<BR>—मूर्धज-राग, अस्, m. colouring<BR>or dyeing the hair.<BR>—मूर्ध-ज्योतिस्, इस्, n. = ब्रह्म-<BR>रन्ध्र, q. v.<BR>—मूर्ध-तस्, ind., Ved. upon the<BR>head.<BR>—मूर्ध-तैलिक, अस्, m., with वस्ति, epithet<BR>of a kind of Errhine for the head.<BR>—मूर्धन्-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing the word मूर्धन्;<BR>(आन्), m., N. of a Gandharva; of an Āṅgirasa or<BR>Vāma-devya, author of the hymn Ṛg-veda X. 88.<BR>—मूर्ध-पात, अस्, m. the splitting of the skull.<BR>—मूर्ध-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a lump upon the head<BR>(of an elephant in rut).<BR>—मूर्ध-पुष्प, अस्, m.<BR>the tree Mimosa Sirissa (शिरीष).<BR>—मूर्ध-रस,<BR>अस्, m. the scum of boiled rice, rice-water.<BR>—मूर्-<BR>ध-वेष्टन, अम्, n. a turban, fillet, diadem.<BR>—मूर्धान्त (˚ध-अन्˚), अस्, m. the crown of<BR>the head.<BR>—मूर्धाभिषिक्त (˚ध-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the head sprinkled, anointed, inaugu-<BR>rated, consecrated, installed; (अस्), m. a consecrated<BR>king; a man of the Kṣatriya or warrior caste; a<BR>royal counsellor, minister; = मूर्धावसिक्त below.<BR>—मूर्धाभिषेक (˚ध-अभ्˚), अस्, m. ‘head-<BR>sprinkling,’ the act of consecrating any one (as king),<BR>anointing, inaugurating.<BR>—मूर्धावसिक्त (˚ध-<BR>अव्˚), अस्, m. epithet of a particular mixed caste, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">Page0788-b+ 80</a>]<BR>son of a Brāhman father by a Kṣatriya mother; =<BR>मूर्धाभिषिक्त, a consecrated king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ध
मूर्ध = मूर्धन् (at the end of certain comps.,<BR>cf. द्वि-म्˚, त्रि-म्˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धक|मूर्द्धकः
मूर्धक, अस्, m. a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्य|मूर्द्धन्यः
मूर्धन्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being on or in the head,<BR>belonging to the head, capital; coming from the<BR>head or skull, cerebral (a term applied to a class of<BR>letters representing sounds formed high in the mouth<BR>or by keeping back the tip of the tongue as far as<BR>possible in the head and slightly turning it upwards,<BR>e. g. ऋ, ॠ, ट्, ठ्, ड्, ढ्, ण्, र्, ष्; these letters are<BR>sometimes called linguals); uppermost, highest, su-<BR>perior, pre-eminent; (आ), f., N. of the mother of<BR>Veda-śiras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ध्वन्
मूर्ध्वन्, आ, m. = मूर्धन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्वा|मूर्व्वा
मूर्वा मूर्वा, f. (according to some also<BR>मूर्वी, f.; probably fr. rt. मुर्व्), Sanseviera Rox-<BR>burghiana, a sort of creeper from the fibres of which<BR>bow-strings and the girdle of the Kṣatriyas are made,<BR>a sort of hemp for bow-strings; [cf. मौर्व.]<BR>—मूर्वा-मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made of Mūrvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्विका
मूर्विका, f. = मूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्
मूल् मूल् (more properly to be regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. मूल below), cl. 1. P.<BR>मूलति (according to Vopa-deva also A. -ते), मु-<BR>मूल, मूलितुम्, to be rooted or firm, stand fast,<BR>take or strike root: Caus. मूलयति (according to<BR>Vopa-deva also मोलयति), मूलयितुम्, Aor. अमू-<BR>मुलत्, to plant, transplant; to grow, sprout, shoot,<BR>germinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल|मूलं|मूलः
मूल, अम्, n. a root (literally and metaphorically);<BR>the root of any plant or tree, (मूलं कृ, to take or<BR>strike root); the root of Arum Campanulatum; the<BR>root of long pepper and of Costus Speciosus or Ara-<BR>bicus; basis, groundwork, beginning, origin, com-<BR>mencement, cause, (मूलाद् आरभ्य, having com-<BR>menced at the beginning); the bottom of anything,<BR>foot, (शैलस्य मूलम्, the foot of a mountain);<BR>basis, lower part, lower end, (वीणाया मूलम्, the<BR>lower end of a lute which rests against the body of<BR>a player); the end or juncture of anything by which<BR>it is joined to anything else [cf. बाहु-म्˚, कर्ण-<BR>म्˚]; outermost edge or border; original, original<BR>text of any work (as distinguished from the scholia<BR>or commentary); an old or hereditary servant or<BR>dependant, an aboriginal native or inhabitant; ori-<BR>ginal property, capital, principal, stock; a chief or<BR>capital city; square root; the twenty-fourth or,<BR>according to some, seventeenth or nineteenth lunar<BR>asterism containing eleven stars, (in this sense अस्,<BR>अम्, m. n.; cf. नक्षत्र); immediate neigh-<BR>bourhood or proximity; a copse, thicket; a vendor<BR>not a true owner, (according to Kullūka on Manu<BR>VIII. 202. मूलम् = अ-स्वामी विक्रेता); a particular<BR>position of the fingers [cf. मूल-बन्ध]; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Sadā-śiva; (आ), f. Asparagus Race-<BR>mosus; the asterism Mūla; (ई), f. a species of small<BR>house-lizard; (अस्, आ, अम्), original, first; own,<BR>proper, peculiar, (in Manu VII. 184. मूल is said<BR>to mean a king's own territory.)<BR>—मूल-कर्मन्,<BR>अ, n. ‘root-machination,’ magical employment of<BR>roots, magic; [cf. मूली-कर्मन्, मूल-कृत्.]<BR>—मूल-कार, अस्, m. the author of an original<BR>work.<BR>—मूल-कारण, अम्, n. first or original<BR>cause.<BR>—मूल-कारिका, f. a fire-place, furnace, oven.<BR>—मूल-कृच्छ्र, अस्, अम्, m. n. ‘root-austerity,’<BR>a kind of penance, living solely on roots.<BR>—मूल-<BR>कृत्, त्, त्, त्, Ved. preparing roots for magical uses.<BR>—मूल-केशर, अस्, m. a citron.<BR>—मूल-खा-<BR>नक, अस्, m. ‘root-digger,’ one who digs for roots,<BR>a collector of roots.<BR>—मूल-गुण, अस्, m. ‘root-<BR>multiplier,’ the coefficient of a root (in algebra).<BR>—मूलगुण-जाति, इस्, f. assimilation and reduction<BR>of the root's coefficient with a fraction.<BR>—मूल-<BR>ग्रन्थ, अस्, m. an original text; an epithet of<BR>the very words uttered by Śākya-muni.<BR>—मूल-<BR>च्छेद, अस्, m. ‘root-cutting,’ cutting away the<BR>roots, cutting up by the roots, uprooting.<BR>—मूल-ज,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, ‘root-born,’ growing from roots, pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-c" target="_blank">Page0788-c+ 81</a>]<BR>duced from a root, radical; formed at the roots of<BR>trees (as an ant-hill); (अस्), m. a plant growing<BR>from a root (as a lotus); (अम्), n. green ginger.<BR>—मूल-जाति, इस्, f. chief or principal origin; = मू-<BR>लगुण-जाति, col. 2.<BR>—मूल-तस्, ind. from the root,<BR>on the root, on the lower side (Ved.), (आ मूलतस्,<BR>from the root upwards, from the beginning.)<BR>—मू-<BR>ल-त्रिकोण, अम्, n. epithet of the third astrological<BR>house.<BR>—मूल-त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of<BR>a root, the being a root, the having a foundation or<BR>source in anything, (मूलत्वात् प्रजानां राजा<BR>स्कन्धः, the king is the stem through his subjects<BR>being the root; वेद-मूलत्व, the statement that<BR>the Veda is the original source of all knowledge;<BR>शास्त्र-मूलत्व, the being founded upon the Śās-<BR>tras.)<BR>—मूल-देव, अस्, m. = मूर-देव, an epithet<BR>of Kaṃsa [cf. मूल-भद्र]; N. of the murderer<BR>of Su-mitra the son of Agni-mitra; of an author; of<BR>a preceptor.<BR>—मूल-द्रव्य, अम्, n. original pro-<BR>perty, capital, principal, stock; [cf. मूल-धन.]<BR>—मूल-द्वार, अम्, n., Ved. principal door.<BR>—मू-<BR>ल-द्वारवती, f. the original or ancient Dvāra-vatī,<BR>the older part of that city; [cf. लघु-द्वारवती,<BR>मूल-नगर.]<BR>—मूल-धन, अम्, n. original<BR>property, capital.<BR>—मूल-धातु, उस्, m. lymph.<BR>—मूल-नगर, अम्, n. old town, (opposed to the<BR>suburbs or शाखा-नगर.)<BR>—मूल-नाश or मूल-<BR>नाशक, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मूल-निकृन्तन,<BR>अस्, ई, अम्, cutting away the roots, utterly destroying,<BR>destroying root and branch.<BR>—मूल-पर्णी, f. a<BR>species of plant (= मण्डूक-पर्णी).<BR>—मूल-पाक,<BR>अस्, m., see Pāṇ. VII. 3, 53.<BR>—मूल-पुरुष, अस्,<BR>m. the male representative of a family, the last<BR>male of a race.<BR>—मूल-पुलिश-सिद्धान्त, अस्,<BR>m. the original Siddhānta of Puliśa.<BR>—मूल-पुष्-<BR>कर, अम्, n. = पुष्कर-मूल, q. v.<BR>—मूल-पोती,<BR>f. a species of culinary plant (= पोतिका).<BR>—मूल-<BR>प्रकृति, इस्, f. (in phil.) the original root or germ<BR>out of which matter or all apparent forms are evolved,<BR>the primary cause or ‘originant;’ (अयस्), f. pl. the<BR>four principal sovereigns to be considered in time of<BR>war (viz. the Vi-jigīṣu, Ari, Madhyama, and Ud-<BR>āsīna; cf. प्र-कृति, शाखा-प्रकृति).<BR>—मूल-<BR>प्रणिहित, अस्, आ, अम्, (perhaps) placed under the<BR>surveillance or brought under the notice of old<BR>(thieves employed as spies; according to Kullūka on<BR>Manu IX. 269 = राज-नियुक्त-पुराण-चौर-<BR>वर्गे सावधान-भूताः).<BR>—मूल-फल-द, अस्,<BR>m. the Jaka or bread-fruit tree.<BR>—मूल-फलाशन<BR>(˚ल-अश्˚), अम्, n. feeding on roots and fruits.<BR>—मूल-<BR>बणिग्-धन, अम्, n. a merchant's original property<BR>or capital.<BR>—मूल-बन्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, (probably)<BR>having roots, deep-rooted; (अस्), m. a particular po-<BR>sition of the fingers.<BR>—मूल-बर्हण, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>Ved. tearing up by the roots, uprooting; (ई, अम्),<BR>f. n. the Nakṣatra Mūla; (अम्), n. the act of<BR>uprooting.<BR>—मूल-भद्र, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Kaṃsa, the uncle of Kṛṣṇa; [cf. मूल-देव.]<BR>—मूल-भव, अस्, आ, अम्, springing or growing<BR>from roots.<BR>—मूल-भार, अस्, m. a load of roots.<BR>—मूल-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become the root or<BR>original.<BR>—मूल-भृत्य, अस्, m. an old or here-<BR>ditary servant, one whose father, grandfather, &c.<BR>were servants before him, (opposed to आ-गन्तु.)<BR>—मूल-मन्त्र, अस्, m. an original or funda-<BR>mental text; an epithet of a particular sacred text.<BR>—मूल-माधव, N. of a place.<BR>—मूलमा-<BR>धव-तीथ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR>—मूल-मित्र, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मूल-रस,<BR>अस्, m. Sanseviera Zeylanica.<BR>—मूल-राज, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a king.<BR>—मूल-रामायण, अम्, n. the ori-<BR>ginal Rāmāyaṇa, i. e. Vālmīki's Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>—मूल-<BR>वचन, अम्, n. ‘primary word,’ an original text.<BR>—मूल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing edible roots;<BR>(perhaps) practising magic with roots.<BR>—मूल-वाप,<BR>अस्, m. one who plants roots.<BR>—मूल-वारिन्, ई, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—मूल-वित्त, अम्, n. ‘original property,’<BR>capital, principal.<BR>—मूल-विद्या, f. ‘principal science,’<BR>epithet of a particular Mantra (= द्वादशाक्षर,<BR>q. v.).<BR>—मूल-विनाशन, अम्, n. radical or entire<BR>destruction.<BR>—मूल-विभुज, अस्, आ, अम्, bending<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">Page0789-a+ 81</a>]<BR>down roots; (अस्), m. a chariot.<BR>—मूल-विरेचन,<BR>अम्, n. a purgative prepared from roots.<BR>—मूल-<BR>व्यसन-वृत्ति, इस्, f. the hereditary occupation of<BR>executing criminals (Manu X. 38).<BR>—मूल-व्रतिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, living exclusively on roots.<BR>—मूल-शकुन,<BR>अस्, m. (in augury) the first bird.<BR>—मूल-शाकट or<BR>मूल-शाकिन, अम्, n. a field planted with edible<BR>roots.<BR>—मूल-श्रीपति-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—मूल-सङ्घ, अस्, m. a society or sect.<BR>—मूल-सर्वास्तिवाद (˚व-अस्˚), आस्, m. pl., N. of<BR>a Buddhist school.<BR>—मूल-साधन, अम्, n. a chief<BR>instrument, principal expedient.<BR>—मूल-सूत्र, अम्,<BR>n. a principal Sūtra.<BR>—मूल-स्थल, अम्, n., N. of<BR>a place.<BR>—मूल-स्थान, अम्, n. principal place;<BR>foundation, base; the air, atmosphere; God; Mool-<BR>tan; (ई), f. an epithet of Gaurī.<BR>—मूलस्थान-<BR>तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha (= भास्कर).<BR>—मूल-स्थायिन्, ई, इनी, इ, existing from the begin-<BR>ning; (ई), m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मूल-स्रोतस्, अस्, n.<BR>the fountain-head of a river, principal current.<BR>—मूल-<BR>हर, अस्, आ, अम्, taking away the roots of anything,<BR>uprooting, utterly destroying, eradicating.<BR>—मूल-<BR>हर-त्व, अम्, n. the state of plucking up by the<BR>roots, eradicating, utter ruin.<BR>—मूलाधार (˚ल-<BR>आध्˚), अम्, n., scil. चक्र, epithet of a mystical<BR>circle situated above the generative organs; (accord-<BR>ing to a Scholiast) the navel.<BR>—मूलाभ (˚ल-आभ्˚),<BR>अम्, n. a radish.<BR>—मूलाभिधर्म-शास्त्र (˚ल-<BR>अभ्˚), अम्, n. the original Abhidharma-śāstra<BR>—मू-<BR>लायतन (˚ल-आय्˚), अम्, n. an original residence.<BR>—मूलाविद्या-विनाशक (˚ल-अव्˚), अस्, इका, अम्,<BR>(probably) destroying ignorance at its roots, eradi-<BR>cating ignorance.<BR>—मूलाशिन् (˚ल-आश्˚), ई, इनी, इ,<BR>‘root-eating,’ living upon roots.<BR>—मूलाह्वा (˚ल-<BR>आह्˚), अम्, n. a radish.<BR>—मूली-कर्मन्, अ, n. = मूल-<BR>कर्मन्, q. v.<BR>—मूली-भूत, अस्, आ, अम्, become a<BR>root, become a source or origin.<BR>—मूलोच्छेद (˚ल-<BR>उच्˚), अस्, m. cutting up the roots, utter destruction.<BR>—मूलोत्खात (˚ल-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, dug up by<BR>the roots, utterly destroyed; (अम्), n. digging up<BR>roots.<BR>—मूलोत्पाटन (˚ल-उत्˚), अम्, n. the digging<BR>up of roots.<BR>—मूलोत्पाटन-जीविन्, ई, m. one who<BR>lives by digging for roots (= मूल-खानक).<BR>—मू-<BR>लौषधि (˚ल-ओष्˚), इस्, f. a species of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलक|मूलकं|मूलकः
मूलक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of comps.)<BR>having roots, rooted in, springing from; born under<BR>the constellation Mūla; (अस्, अम्), m. n. an esculent<BR>root; a radish [cf. चाणक्य-म्˚, नेपाल-म्˚]; a<BR>sort of yam; (अस्), m. a kind of vegetable poison;<BR>N. of a prince, a son of Aśmaka; (इका), f. a root.<BR>—मूलक-पण, अस्, m. a handful or bunch of<BR>radishes, &c. (for sale).<BR>—मूलक-पर्णी, f. Moringa<BR>Pterygosperma.<BR>—मूलक-पोतिका, f. a radish.<BR>—मू-<BR>लक-मूला, f. the plant Lipeocercis Serrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलस
मूलस, अस्, आ, अम्, see Gaṇa Tṛṇādi to Pāṇ.<BR>IV. 2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिक|मूलिकः
मूलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, living on roots; radical,<BR>original; primary, principal; (अस्), m. an ascetic,<BR>devotee; (आ), f. a multitude or collection of roots.<BR>—मूलिकार्थ (˚क-अर्˚), अस्, m. a radical fact;<BR>[cf. योग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिन्
मूलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having a root or stock or origin,<BR>&c.; (ई), m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिन|मूलिनः
मूलिन, अस्, आ, अम्, having a root, growing from<BR>a root (not bulbous or tuberous; cf. फल-मूलिन);<BR>= मूल-कृत्, q. v.; (अस्), m. a plant, tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलेर|मूलेरः
मूलेर, अस्, m. a king; Indian spikenard, Nar-<BR>dostachys Jatamansi (= जटा-मांसी, जटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्य|मूल्यं
मूल्य, अस्, आ, अम्, being at the root; to be torn<BR>up by the roots, to be eradicated; to be bought<BR>for a price, to be bought, purchasable; (अम्), n. ori-<BR>ginal value; price, worth, value, a sum of money<BR>given as payment (e. g. दातुम् मूल्येन, to part<BR>with for a certain price, sell; दत्त्वा किञ्चिन् मूल्-<BR>येन, having given something in payment; मूल्-<BR>येन गृहीत, bought for a price); wages, salary,<BR>payment for service rendered; earnings, gain; =<BR>मूल, capital, principal; an article purchased.<BR>—मू-<BR>ल्य-करण, अम्, n. making the worth or value of<BR>anything, turning into money.<BR>—मूल्य-विवर्जित,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, devoid of price, priceless, invaluable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलाट
मूलाट मूलाट, मूलाटी, see Gaṇa Gaurādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्
मूष् 1. मूष् (= rt. 2. मुष्), cl. 1. P.<BR>मूषति, मूषितुम्, to steal, rob, plunder.<BR>2. मूष्, ट्, Ved. a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष|मूषः
मूष, अस्, आ or ई, m. f. a rat, mouse; (आ), f. a<BR>crucible, (said to be also अस्, m. and ई, f.); Lipeo-<BR>cercis Serrata; = गवाक्ष, a round window, air-<BR>hole; [cf. Gr. μῦς; Lat. mus, mus-culu-s, mus-<BR>cip-ula; Old Germ. mûs; Slav. mys-i.]<BR>—मू-<BR>षा-कर्णी, f. an aquatic plant, Salvinia Cucullata.<BR>—मूषा-तुत्थ, अम्, n. a kind of vitriol.<BR>—मू-<BR>षी-करण, अम्, n. melting in a crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषक|मूषकः
मूषक, अस्, m. a thief; a rat, mouse; a kind<BR>of metre; a particular part of the face; (आस्), m. pl.,<BR>N. of a people; (इका), f. a rat, mouse, a female rat<BR>or mouse; a species of leech; Salvinia Cucullata; a<BR>crucible; (अका), f. a rat, mouse, female rat.<BR>—मू-<BR>षक-कर्णिका or मूषक-कर्णी or मूषक-<BR>मारी, f. = मूषा-कर्णी, q. v.<BR>—मूषकाद (˚क-<BR>अद), अस्, m. ‘mouse-eater,’ N. of a Nāga.<BR>—मूष-<BR>काराति (˚क-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘mouse's foe,’ a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषण|मूषणं
मूषण, अम्, n. the act of stealing, pilfering,<BR>filching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषत्
मूषत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, stealing, filching, plun-<BR>dering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिक|मूषिकः
मूषिक, अस्, m. a thief, plunderer; a rat, mouse<BR>[cf. गन्ध-मूषिक, महा-मूषिक]; Mimosa<BR>Sirissa (= शिरीष); N. of a country (the part of<BR>the Malabar coast between Quilon and Cape Como-<BR>rin); (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people, (also read भू-<BR>षिक); (आ), f., see under मूषक.<BR>—मूषिक-<BR>निर्विशेष, अस्, आ, अम्, not differing from a mouse,<BR>the same as a mouse.<BR>—मूषिक-पर्णी, f. an<BR>aquatic plant, Salvinia Cucullata.<BR>—मूषिक-रथ,<BR>अस्, m. ‘rat-vehicled, riding on a rat,’ an epithet of<BR>Gaṇeśa (see गणेश, p. 279).<BR>—मूषिक-विषाण,<BR>अम्, n. a mouse's horn, i. e. an impossibility; [cf. शश-<BR>विषाण.]<BR>—मूषिक-स्थल, अम्, n. (probably) a<BR>mole-hill.<BR>—मूषिकाङ्क (˚क-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘cha-<BR>racterized by a rat,’ epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—मूषिकाञ्-<BR>चन (˚क-अञ्˚), अस्, m. ‘going on a rat,’ an epithet<BR>of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—मूषिकाद (˚क-अद˚) = मूषकाद.<BR>—मूषिका-दत्, अन्, अती, अत्, or मूषिका-दन्त,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, ‘mouse-toothed,’ having the teeth<BR>of a mouse.<BR>—मूषिकान्तकृत् (˚क-अन्˚), त्, m.<BR>‘mouse-destroyer,’ a cat.<BR>—मूषिकाराति = मूष-<BR>काराति.<BR>—मूषिकाह्वय (˚क-आह्˚), अस्, m. Salvinia<BR>Cucullata.<BR>—मूषिकोत्कर (˚क-उत्˚) or ˚का-उत्˚), अस्,<BR>m. a mole-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकका
मूषिकका or मूषिकिका, f. (diminutive of मू-<BR>षिका), a little rat or mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकार|मूषिकारः
मूषिकार, अस्, m. a male mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषित
मूषित, अस्, आ, अम्, stolen, &c. = मुषित, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिपर्णिका
मूषि-पर्णिका, f. = मूषिक-पर्णी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीक|मूषीकः
मूषीक, अस्, आ, m. f. = मूषिक, a rat, mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीककर्णी
—मूषीक-कर्णी, f. = मूषा-कर्णी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्यायण|मूष्यायणः
मूष्यायण मूष्यायण, अस्, आ, अम्, born of<BR>unknown parents, (probably for आमुष्यायण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूसरिःफ
मूसरिःफ मूसरिः-फ and मूसरीफ, अस्,<BR>m., N. of the fourth Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृ
मृ मृ, cl. 6. A., but in Perf., Futures, and<BR>Cond. only P. (ep. occasionally both P. and A.<BR>in all the tenses), म्रियते, ममार, मरिष्यति,<BR>अमृत, मृषीष्ट, मर्तुम् (epic forms म्रियति,<BR>म्रियन्ति, म्रियेयम्, म्रियेयुस्, मम्रे, मम्रिरे,<BR>Ved. forms मरति, मरते, मराति, अमरत्;<BR>the form मुमुरत्, Ṛg-veda VIII. 97, 3, is said<BR>by Sāy. to = मारयतु = विनाशयतु), to die, de-<BR>cease, depart from life: Pass. म्रियते (sometimes<BR>used impersonally with inst. c.), Perf. मम्रे, Aor.<BR>अमारि: Caus. मारयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अमीमरत्,<BR>to cause to die, kill, slay, put to death: Desid. मु-<BR>मूर्षति, to wish to die, be about to die, be at the<BR>point of death, face death: Intens. मेम्रीयते, मर्-<BR>मर्ति; [cf. Zend mar, ‘to die;’ mare-ta, ‘mortal;’<BR>maretan, ‘man:’ Gr. ἄ-μβρο-το-ς, ἀμ-βρόσ-ιο-ς, βρο-τό-ς,<BR>μορ-τό-ς, μαραίν-ω, μαρα-σ-μό-ς: Lat. mor-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-c" target="_blank">Page0789-c+ 81</a>]<BR>i-or-r, mor-(ti)-s, mor-tuu-us, mort-âli-s, mor-<BR>bu-s, mar-c-e-o, marc-e-sc-o, marc-i-du-s: Angl.<BR>Sax. uta-mœran, mordher, myrdhro, mordh:<BR>Goth. maur-th-r: Slav. mr-e-ti, ‘to die;’ mor-u,<BR>‘plague, death;’ s-mrĭ-tĭ, ‘death;’ mrĭ-tvu, ‘a<BR>dead man:’ Russ. u-miraju, ‘to die;’ mertvyi,<BR>‘dead;’ s-mer-tj, ‘death:’ Lith. mir-ti, ‘to die;’<BR>már-a-s, ‘plague;’ mórai, ‘bier;’ s-mer-ti, ‘death:’<BR>Hib. marbhaim, ‘I kill, slay;’ marbhan, ‘a corpse,<BR>dead body.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षा
मुमूर्षा, f. (fr. Desid.), desire of death, wishing<BR>to die, being at the point of death, impatience of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षु|मुमूर्षुः
मुमूर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to die, being about<BR>to die, being at the point of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत|मृतं
मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, dead, deceased, deathlike, tor-<BR>pid, useless; calcined, reduced (said of metals); (अम्),<BR>n. death, (मृतेभ्यः प्रमृतं यान्ति, they pass<BR>from death to death, i. e. from one death to another);<BR>= चैत्य, a grave; begging, food or alms obtained<BR>by begging.<BR>—मृत-कल्प, अस्, आ, अम्, almost dead,<BR>well-nigh dead, insensible, fainted.<BR>—मृत-गृह,<BR>अम्, n. ‘house of the dead,’ a grave.<BR>—मृत-चेल,<BR>अम्, n. the garments of the dead (worn by Caṇḍālas).<BR>—मृत-जीवन, अस्, ई, अम्, giving life to the dead,<BR>raising the dead to life.<BR>—मृत-दार, अस्, m. one<BR>whose wife is dead, a widower.<BR>—मृत-नाथ, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, one whose lord is dead.<BR>—मृत-निर्यातक,<BR>अस्, m. one who carries out dead bodies.<BR>—मृत-प,<BR>अस्, m. a person who guards a dead body.<BR>—मृत-<BR>पा, आस्, m. a person who watches a dead body, a<BR>man of the lowest caste who collects dead men's<BR>clothes, conveys dead bodies to the river side to be<BR>burnt, executes criminals, &c.; N. of an Asura.<BR>—मृत-पुत्र, अस्, m. one whose son is dead.<BR>—मृत-प्रज, अस्, आ, अम्, one whose children are<BR>dead.<BR>—मृत-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, well-nigh dead,<BR>almost dead.<BR>—मृत-भ्रज्, Ved. one who has lost<BR>the power of erection.<BR>—मृत-मत्त or मृत-<BR>मत्तक, अस्, m. a jackal.<BR>—मृत-मनस्, आस्, आस्,<BR>अस्, Ved. unconscious, insensible.<BR>—मृत-वत्, ind.<BR>like one dead.<BR>—मृत-वत्सा or मृत-वत्सिका, f.,<BR>Ved. whose offspring or first-born child dies.<BR>—मृत-<BR>वस्त्र-भृत्, त्, त्, त्, wearing a dead man's clothes.<BR>—मृत-वार्षिक, the period of the short rains<BR>(said to last twenty-four hours, while the वार्षिक<BR>last a month, and the दीर्घ-वार्षिक three months<BR>all but a day).<BR>—मृत-शङ्का, f. the fear entertained<BR>of a person being dead.<BR>—मृत-शब्द, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. report of any one's death.<BR>—मृत-संस्कार,<BR>अस्, m. funeral rites or ceremonies.<BR>—मृत-सञ्जी-<BR>वन, अस्, ई, अम्, reviving the dead, bringing the<BR>dead to life; (ई), f. the revival of a dead person, a<BR>Mantra for reviving the dead; (अम्), n. the revival<BR>of a dead person; bringing the dead to life.<BR>—मृत-<BR>सञ्जीविन्, ई, इनी, इ, reviving or giving life to the<BR>dead, bringing the dead to life; (इनी), f. epithet of<BR>a kind of formula; a species of shrub (= गोरक्ष-<BR>दुग्धा); N. of a commentary on Piṅgala's Chan-<BR>daḥ-śāstra.<BR>—मृत-सूतक, अम्, n. bringing forth a<BR>still-born child; (अस्), m. a term applied to quicksilver<BR>in a particular state.<BR>—मृत-स्नात, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>who has washed himself after a death or funeral,<BR>bathed after mourning; dying immediately after<BR>ablution.<BR>—मृत-स्नान, अम्, n. ablution after a<BR>death or funeral.<BR>—मृत-स्व-मोक्तृ, ता, m. ‘let-<BR>ting alone, i. e. not taking, the property of deceased<BR>person,’ an epithet of Kumāra-pāla.<BR>—मृत-हार,<BR>अस्, or मृत-हारिन्, ई, m. a carrier of the dead, one<BR>who bears a corpse to the funeral pile.<BR>—मृताङ्ग<BR>(˚त-अङ्˚), अम्, n. a dead body, corpse.<BR>—मृताङ्-<BR>गार (˚त-अङ्˚), अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मृताण्ड<BR>(˚त-अण्˚), अम्, n. a seemingly dead or lifeless egg<BR>(as opposed to a living egg or testicle; cf. मार्-<BR>ताण्ड, ‘a bird’ which is produced from the seemingly<BR>lifeless egg); (अस्), m. the sun; [cf. मृतण्ड.]<BR>—मृताधान (˚त-आध्˚), अम्, n. placing a dead<BR>body (on the funeral pile).<BR>—मृताशन (˚त-अश्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, living upon the dead.<BR>—मृताशौच<BR>(˚त-आश्˚), अम्, n. impurity contracted through the<BR>death of any one.<BR>—मृताहन् or मृताहस् (˚त-<BR>अह्˚), n. the day of any one's death.<BR>—मृतोत्थित<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-a" target="_blank">Page0790-a+ 81</a>]<BR>(˚त-उत्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, risen from the dead.<BR>—मृ-<BR>तोद्भव (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, m. the sea, ocean; (per-<BR>haps for अमृतोद्भव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0789-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतक|मृतकं|मृतकः
मृतक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a dead man, a corpse;<BR>(अम्), n. death, decease.<BR>—मृतकान्तक (˚क-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘consumer of corpses, demolisher of<BR>carcases,’ a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृति|मृतिः
मृति, इस्, f. death, dying; [cf. Lat. mors (mor-<BR>ti-s); Slav. s-mrĭ-tĭ; Lith. s-mèr-ti-s.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतिमन्
मृतिमन्, आ, m. mortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्यु|मृत्युः
मृत्यु, उस्, m. (ep. also f.), death, dying, decease,<BR>demise, (a hundred kinds of death are enumerated<BR>from disease or accident, and one natural kind from<BR>old age); Death personified, the god of death, Yama<BR>the judge of the dead; an epithet of Viṣṇu; N. of<BR>a son of A-dharma by Nir-ṛti; an epithet of Brahmā;<BR>N. of Māyā; of Kali; of a teacher; of Vyāsa in<BR>the sixth Dvāpara; of one of the eleven Rudras; of<BR>an Ekāha; of the eighth astrological house; of the<BR>seventeenth astrological Yoga; the god of love [cf.<BR>मार]; मृत्योर् हरः and मृत्योर् विकर्ण-भासे,<BR>names of Sāmans; अकाल-मृत्यु, ‘untimely death,’<BR>N. of a being attendant on Padma-pāṇi.<BR>—मृत्यु-<BR>कन्या, f. the goddess of death.<BR>—मृत्यु-जित्, त्, m.<BR>‘conqueror of death,’ N. of an author, (also called<BR>Mṛtyujid-bhaṭṭāraka); N. of a work by the same<BR>author.<BR>—मृत्युञ्-जय, अस्, आ, अम्, overcoming<BR>death; (अस्), m. ‘death-conqueror,’ an epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of an author.<BR>—मृत्युञ्जय-तीर्थ and<BR>मृत्यु-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of two Tīrthas.<BR>—मृत्यु-<BR>तूर्य, अम्, n. a kind of drum beaten at funeral<BR>ceremonies.<BR>—मृत्यु-द, अस्, आ, अम्, death-giving,<BR>fatal.<BR>—मृत्यु-दूत, अस्, m., Ved. ‘death-messen-<BR>ger,’ one who brings the news of a death.<BR>—मृत्यु-<BR>द्वार, अम्, n. death's door, the door that leads to<BR>death.<BR>—मृत्यु-नाशक, अस्, m. ‘death-averter,’<BR>quicksilver.<BR>—मृत्यु-नाशन, अम्, n. ‘death-de-<BR>stroying,’ the drink of immortality.<BR>—मृत्यु-पथ,<BR>अस्, m. a way or path leading to death.<BR>—मृत्यु-पा,<BR>आस्, m. ‘death-quaffing,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मृत्यु-<BR>पाश, अस्, m. death's noose (these are variously rec-<BR>koned at 101 or even more than 1000 in number).<BR>—मृत्यु-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘death-flowered,’ the<BR>sugar cane (so called because it dies after the loss of<BR>its flowers).<BR>—मृत्यु-प्रतिबद्ध, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>subject or liable to death.<BR>—मृत्यु-फल, अस्, m.<BR>a species of cucumber, = महा-काल = महाकाल-<BR>फल; (आ or ई), f. the plantain, Musa Sapientum;<BR>(अम्), n. a sort of fruit considered as poisonous.<BR>—मृत्यु-बन्धु, उस्, m., Ved. ‘companion of<BR>death,’ a man.<BR>—मृत्यु-बीज, see मृत्यु-वीज.<BR>—मृत्यु-भङ्गुरक, अस्, m. a drum beaten at<BR>funeral ceremonies.<BR>—मृत्यु-भय, अम्, n. danger<BR>or peril of death; fear of death.<BR>—मृत्यु-भीत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, afraid of death.<BR>—मृत्यु-भृत्य, अस्,<BR>m. a servant of death; (figuratively) sickness, ma-<BR>lady, disease.<BR>—मृत्यु-मत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having<BR>death, subject to death.<BR>—मृत्यु-मार, अस्, m.<BR>(with Buddhists), N. of one of the four Māras or<BR>devils.<BR>—मृत्यु-मृत्यु, उस्, m. the death of death,<BR>i. e. a remover or preventer of death.<BR>—मृत्यु-<BR>राज्, ट्, m. ‘death-king,’ the god of death, Yama.<BR>—मृत्यु-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, death-formed, having the<BR>form of death; (इणी), f. mystical epithet of the letter श्.<BR>—मृत्यु-लङ्घनोपनिषद् (˚न-उप्˚), त्, f., N.<BR>of an Upaniṣad.<BR>—मृत्यु-लोक, अस्, m. ‘death-<BR>world,’ the world of death (the fifth of the seven<BR>worlds), the world of the dead, abode of Yama.<BR>—मृत्यु-वञ्चन, अस्, m. ‘death-cheater,’ an epi-<BR>thet of Śiva; a raven, carrion-crow; Ægle Mar-<BR>melos.<BR>—मृत्यु-वीज, अस्, m. ‘dying after the<BR>production of seed,’ a bamboo, bamboo-cane.<BR>—मृत्यु-सञ्जीवन, अस्, ई, अम्, restoring from<BR>death to life, making alive again [cf. मृत-सञ्जी-<BR>वन]; (ई), f., N. of a section of the Tantra-sāra.<BR>—मृत्यु-सात्, ind. to death, to the power of death;<BR>मृत्यु-सात् कृ, to deliver any one over to death.<BR>—मृत्यु-सुत, आस्, m. pl., Ved. ‘death's sons,’ epi-<BR>thet of a class of Ketus.<BR>—मृत्यु-सूति, इस्, f. ‘dying<BR>in bringing forth,’ a female crab.<BR>—मृत्यु-सेना, f.<BR>the army of the god of death.<BR>—मृत्यु-हेतु, उस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">Page0790-b+ 77</a>]<BR>m. cause of death; मृत्यु-हेतवे, dat. c. for the<BR>sake of death, in order to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युक
मृत्युक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comps.) =<BR>मृत्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रियमाण
म्रियमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, dying, departing from<BR>life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृकण्ड
मृकण्ड मृकण्ड, अस्, or मृकण्डु, उस्, m.,<BR>N. of an ancient sage, the father of Mārkaṇḍeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्ष्
मृक्ष् मृक्ष् = rt. म्रक्ष्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्ष
मृक्ष, अस्, m., Ved. (perhaps) a curry-comb,<BR>comb or any instrument for scraping; (according to<BR>Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VIII. 66, 3) purifying, cleansing;<BR>rubbed, cleansed (= शोधक, प्र-क्षालित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्षकनाटक
मृक्षक-नाटक, अम्, n., N. of a Nāṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्षिणी
मृक्षिणी, f. (perhaps fr. rt. म्रक्ष्, in the sense<BR>of ‘tearing up the ground’), Ved. (perhaps) a rapid<BR>stream, torrent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्
मृग् मृग् (more properly to be regarded<BR>as a Nom. fr. मृग), cl. 4. P., 10. A.<BR>मृग्यति, मृगयते (ep. also P. -ति), &c., to<BR>chase, hunt, pursue; to seek, search for, seek after;<BR>to investigate, examine; to strive for, aim at; to<BR>visit; to desire or request or beg anything (acc.)<BR>from another (abl., gen., or with सकाशात्); अन्तर्<BR>मृग्, to examine or investigate inwardly, i. e. in<BR>the mind: Pass. मृग्यते, to be searched or sought<BR>after, to be pursued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग|मृगः
मृग, अस्, m. a wild beast; an animal in general,<BR>any quadruped, a deer, stag, antelope, musk-deer;<BR>game in general; the spots on the moon represented<BR>as a hare or antelope; the celestial antelope or the<BR>Nakṣatra Mṛga-śiras; the sign of the zodiac Ca-<BR>pricorn (or the tenth arc of 30° in a circle); an<BR>elephant characterized by particular marks (one of<BR>the three classes of elephants); a particular kind of<BR>large bird (Ved.); epithet of a demon or of Vṛtra<BR>in the form of a deer slain by Indra (Ved.); N. of a<BR>celestial being or tutelary divinity occupying a parti-<BR>cular place in an astrological house divided into eighty-<BR>one compartments (Ved.); epithet of a particular<BR>class of men whose conduct in coitus resembles that<BR>of the roebuck; N. of the district in Śāka-dvīpa<BR>inhabited principally by Brāhmans, (also read मङ्ग,<BR>cf. मग); = मृग-नाभि, musk; the month Mār-<BR>gaśīrṣa; a particular Aja-pāla sacrifice; seeking,<BR>search (= मार्गण); pursuit, hunting, chase; re-<BR>search, inquiry, investigation; asking, soliciting, beg-<BR>ging; (ई), f. a female deer or antelope, doe; N. of<BR>the mythical progenitress of the antelopes; epithet<BR>of a particular class of women; a particular metre,<BR>four times ¯˘¯; demoniacal possession, epilepsy.<BR>—मृग-काक, औ, m. du. a deer and a crow.<BR>—मृग-कानन, अम्, n. a forest abounding in<BR>game; a park, preserve; [cf. मृगारण्य, मृ-<BR>गया-वन.]<BR>—मृग-क्षीर, अम्, n. antelope's<BR>milk, doe's milk.<BR>—मृग-गामिनी, f. a kind of<BR>medicinal substance (= विडङ्गा).<BR>—मृग-ग्र-<BR>हण, अम्, n. the capture of a deer.<BR>—मृग-चर्-<BR>मीय, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मृग-चर्या, f.<BR>the acting like a deer (a kind of penance, see मृग-<BR>चारिन् below).<BR>—मृग-चारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting like<BR>a deer (as certain devotees; cf. गो-चारिन्, which<BR>appears to mean ‘acting like a cow, using the mouth<BR>instead of the hands’).<BR>—मृग-चैटक, अस्, m. (?),<BR>a wild cat, pole-cat.<BR>—मृग-जम्बुक, औ, m. du.<BR>a deer and a jackal.<BR>—मृग-जल, अम्, n. ‘deer-<BR>water,’ mirage; see मृग-तृष्.<BR>—मृगजल-<BR>स्नान, अम्, n. bathing in the unreal waters of a<BR>mirage, (a term for any impossibility.)<BR>—मृग-जाति,<BR>अयस्, f. pl. the deer species, whole race of deer.<BR>—मृग-जालिका, f. a net for snaring game.<BR>—मृग-<BR>जीवन, अस्, m. one who lives by hunting, a hunter,<BR>huntsman.<BR>—मृग-तीर्थ, अम्, n., Ved. ‘animal<BR>track,’ epithet of the path by which the priests at<BR>the end of the Savana leave the sacred place to attend<BR>to their bodily wants.<BR>—मृग-तृष्, ट्, or मृग-<BR>तृषा, or मृग-तृष्णा, or मृग-तृष्णि, इस्, or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-c" target="_blank">Page0790-c+ 81</a>]<BR>मृग-तृष्णिका, f. ‘deer-thirst,’ mirage, vapour<BR>floating over sands or deserts, fancied appearance of<BR>water in deserts.<BR>—मृग-तोय, अम्, n. the water<BR>of a mirage.<BR>—मृग-त्व, अम्, n. the being a deer<BR>or antelope, the state or condition of a deer.<BR>—मृग-<BR>दंश or मृग-दंशक, अस्, m. ‘animal-biter,’<BR>a hunting-dog, dog.<BR>—मृग-दाव, अस्, m. a wood<BR>for game, park, preserve.<BR>—मृग-दृश्, क्, f. ‘deer-<BR>eyed,’ a woman with eyes like an antelope's; (क्),<BR>m. the sign of the zodiac Capricorn.<BR>—मृग-द्युत्,<BR>त्, त्, त् (see 1. द्युत्, p. 437), attacking a deer, a<BR>hunter.<BR>—मृग-द्यू, ऊस्, ऊस्, उ, delighting or tak-<BR>ing pleasure in deer; (ऊस्), m. a hunter.<BR>—मृग-<BR>द्विज, आस्, m. pl. beasts and birds.<BR>—मृग-धर,<BR>अस्, m. ‘bearing deer-like marks,’ the moon (which,<BR>according to the Hindūs, is spotted like a deer or a<BR>hare); N. of a minister of Prasena-jit.<BR>—मृग-<BR>धूम, N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—मृग-धूर्त or मृग-<BR>धूर्तक, अस्, m. ‘animal-deceiver,’ a jackal.<BR>—मृ-<BR>ग-नयना, f. a fawn-eyed woman.<BR>—मृग-नाभि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘deer's navel,’ musk; a musk-deer; [cf.<BR>नाभि.]<BR>—मृगनाभि-जा, f. musk.<BR>—मृगनाभि-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, made or consisting of musk.<BR>—मृग-निर्मोक-वसन, अस्, आ, अम्, clothed in<BR>the cast-off skin of a deer.<BR>—मृग-नेत्र, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, having the Nakṣatra Mṛga for a leader, re-<BR>lating to this Nakṣatra; (आ), f. ‘fawn-eyed,’ a woman<BR>with eyes like an antelope's.<BR>—मृग-पक्षिन्,<BR>इणस्, m. pl. beasts and birds.<BR>—मृग-पति, इस्, m.<BR>‘lord of the beasts,’ a lion; a tiger; a roebuck.<BR>—मृग-पद, अम्, n. a deer's foot, deer's track<BR>(= मृग्याः पदम्).<BR>—मृग-पालिका, f. a musk-<BR>deer.<BR>—मृग-पिप्लु, उस्, m. ‘deer-marked,’ the<BR>moon.<BR>—मृग-पोत or मृग-पोतक, अस्, m. a<BR>young deer, fawn.<BR>—मृग-प्रभु, उस्, m. ‘lord<BR>of the beasts,’ the lion.<BR>—मृग-प्रेक्षिन्, ई, इणी,<BR>इ, looking at (anything) like a deer, having the eyes<BR>of a deer; [cf. वृक-प्˚.]<BR>—मृग-बधाजीव<BR>(˚ध-आज्˚), अस्, m. ‘living by killing deer,’ a deer-<BR>killer, hunter.<BR>—मृग-बन्धिनी, f. a net for snar-<BR>ing game or for confining deer.<BR>—मृग-बालक,<BR>अस्, m. a young deer.<BR>—मृग-भक्षा, f. Nardo-<BR>stachys Jatamansi.<BR>—मृग-भोजनी, f. coloquintida,<BR>colocynth, bitter apple.<BR>—मृग-मद, अस्, m.<BR>musk.<BR>—मृगमद-वासा, f. a musk-bag.<BR>—मृ-<BR>ग-मन्द, अस्, m. epithet of a class of elephants;<BR>(आ), f. the mythical progenitress of lions, Sṛmaras,<BR>and Camaras; [cf. मृग-वती.]<BR>—मृग-मन्द्र,<BR>अस्, m. epithet of a class of elephants.<BR>—मृग-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, coming from or consisting of<BR>wild animals.<BR>—मृग-मांस, अम्, n. deer's flesh,<BR>venison.<BR>—मृग-मातृका, f. a species of wild<BR>animal; a doe.<BR>—मृग-मास, अस्, m. the month<BR>Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>—मृग-मुख, अस्, m. the sign of<BR>the zodiac Capricorn; [cf. मृगास्य.]<BR>—मृग-<BR>यूथ, अम्, n. a herd of deer.<BR>—मृगयूथ-प,<BR>अस्, m. lord of the herd of deer.<BR>—मृग-रसा, f. a<BR>species of plant (= मृगादनी, सह-देवी).<BR>—मृ-<BR>ग-राज्, ट्, m. ‘king of the beasts,’ a lion, the sign<BR>of the zodiac Leo; a tiger.<BR>—मृग-राज, अस्, m.<BR>‘king of the beasts,’ a lion, the sign of the zodiac<BR>Leo; a tiger; the moon.<BR>—मृगराज-धारिन्, ई,<BR>m. (probably) the moon; ‘lion-shaped,’ the sign of<BR>the zodiac Leo.<BR>—मृगराज-लक्ष्मन्, आ, आ, अ,<BR>‘characterized by the lion (or the moon),’ bearing<BR>that surname (= सिंह-चिह्न).<BR>—मृग-राटिका, f.<BR>a species of medicinal plant (= जीवन्ती).<BR>—मृग-<BR>रिपु, उस्, m. ‘the enemy of wild animals,’ the lion.<BR>—मृग-रूपिन्, ई, इणी, इ, ‘deer-shaped,’ being in<BR>the form of an antelope.<BR>—मृग-रोम-ज, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, ‘produced from animal's hair,’ woollen.<BR>—मृ-<BR>ग-लक्ष्मन्, आ, or मृग-लाञ्छन, अस्, m.<BR>‘spotted like a deer,’ the moon.<BR>—मृगलाञ्छन-<BR>ज, अस्, m. ‘son of the moon,’ the planet Mercury.<BR>—मृग-लेखा, f. the deer-like streak on the moon.<BR>—मृग-लोचन, अस्, m. ‘deer-eyed,’ the moon;<BR>(आ or ई), f. a woman with eyes like an antelope's.<BR>—मृग-वती, f., N. of the mythical progenitress<BR>of the bears and Sṛmaras.<BR>—मृग-वधाजीव<BR>(˚ध-आज्˚), अस्, m. ‘one who lives by killing wild<BR>animals,’ a huntsman.<BR>—मृग-वन, अम्, n. a forest<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-a" target="_blank">Page0791-a+ 81</a>]<BR>abounding in wild animals, a park, preserve.<BR>—मृ-<BR>गवन-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-<BR>place on the Narmadā river.<BR>—मृग-वल्लभ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘liked by deer,’ a species of grass (= कुन्दर),<BR>—मृग-वाहन, अस्, m. ‘having a deer for a<BR>vehicle,’ epithet of Vāyu, god of the wind (who is<BR>sometimes represented mounted on an antelope),<BR>air, wind.<BR>—मृग-वीथी, f. ‘deer-track,’ an epithet<BR>of that portion of the moon's course which includes<BR>the constellations Śravaṇā, Śata-bhiṣaj, and Pūrva-<BR>bhadra-padā; [cf. मृगाख्य.]<BR>—मृग-वैणिक,<BR>अम्, n. epithet of a particular posture in sitting.<BR>—मृग-व्याध, अस्, m. a hunter of wild animals,<BR>huntsman; the dog-star or Sirius; an epithet of<BR>Śiva; N. of one of the eleven Rudras.<BR>—मृग-<BR>व्याध-सर्प-शूकर, आस्, m. pl. the deer, hunter,<BR>snake, and boar.<BR>—मृग-व्याधीय, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>relating to the hunter and the deer.<BR>—मृग-<BR>व्याल-निषेवित, अस्, आ, अम्, infested by wild beasts<BR>and serpents.<BR>—मृग-शायिका, f. the lying or re-<BR>clining posture of an antelope (e. g. शयीत मृग-<BR>शायिकाम्, let him lie as still as an antelope).<BR>—मृ-<BR>ग-शाव, अस्, m. a young deer, fawn.<BR>—मृग-<BR>शावक, अस्, m. = मृग-शाव.<BR>—मृगशावाक्ष<BR>(˚व-अक्˚), अस्, ई, अम्, ‘fawn-eyed,’ having eyes<BR>like those of a young deer or fawn.<BR>—मृग-<BR>शिर, अस्, आ, m. f. the Nakṣatra Mṛga-śiras, (see<BR>नक्षत्र.)<BR>—मृग-शिरस्, अस्, n., N. of the tenth<BR>or, according to some, third or fifth Nakṣatra or<BR>lunar mansion (containing three stars, one of which<BR>is λ Orionis and figured by an antelope's head; see<BR>नक्षत्र); (आस्, आस्, अस्), born under the Nakṣatra<BR>Mṛga-śiras; (आस्), m., scil. हस्त, a particular posi-<BR>tion of the hands.<BR>—मृग-शीर्ष, अम्, n. the con-<BR>stellation Mṛga-śiras, (according to some also अस्, आ,<BR>m. f.); (अस्, आ, अम्), born under the constellation Mṛga-<BR>śiras; (अस्), m., scil. मास, the month Mārgaśīrṣa;<BR>scil. हस्त, epithet of a particular position of the<BR>hands, (also मृग-शीर्षक.)<BR>—मृग-शीर्षन्, आ,<BR>m. the constellation Mṛga-śiras.<BR>—मृग-शूकर,<BR>औ, m. du. a deer and a boar.<BR>—मृग-शृङ्ग, अम्,<BR>n. a stag's horn.<BR>—मृग-शृङ्ग-व्रतिन्, इनस्, m.<BR>pl., N. of a particular sect.<BR>—मृग-श्रेष्ठ, अस्,<BR>m. ‘best of beasts, chief of animals,’ a tiger.<BR>—मृ-<BR>ग-सक्थ, अम्, n. = मृगस्य सक्थि, Pāṇ. V. 4,<BR>98.<BR>—मृग-सत्तम, अस्, m. the best of antelopes.<BR>—मृग-सत्त्र, अम्, n., Ved., N. of a festival<BR>lasting nineteen days.<BR>—मृग-हन्, आ, m. ‘deer-<BR>slayer,’ a huntsman.<BR>—मृगाक्षी (˚ग-अक्˚), f. a<BR>fawn-eyed woman, a woman with eyes like an ante-<BR>lope's; coloquintida, colocynth; = त्रि-यामा.<BR>—मृ-<BR>गाखर (˚ग-आख्˚), अस्, m., Ved. the lair or den<BR>of a wild beast, the hole of any wild animal.<BR>—मृ-<BR>गाख्य (˚ग-आख्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, named after the<BR>deer, (मृगाख्या, वीथी, a portion of the moon's<BR>course which comprises three constellations beginning<BR>with Maitra.)<BR>—मृगाङ्क (˚ग-अङ्˚), अस्, m. ‘deer-<BR>spotted, spotted like a deer,’ the moon; camphor;<BR>the wind [cf. मृग-वाहन]; N. of a sword (in<BR>Kathā-sarit-s. X. 45); of a man.<BR>—मृगाङ्क-दत्त,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a son of Amara-datta (king of Ayodhyā);<BR>of the father of Aruṇa-datta.<BR>—मृगाङ्कदत्तीय,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, relating to Mṛgāṅka-datta.<BR>—मृ-<BR>गाङ्क-रस, अस्, m. epithet of a kind of formula.<BR>—मृगाङ्क-लेखा, f., N. of the daughter of a<BR>king of the Vidyā-dharas.<BR>—मृगाङ्क-वती, f., N.<BR>of the wife of Dharma-dhvaja, king of Ujjayinī; of<BR>the wife of Mṛgāṅka-sena.<BR>—मृगाङ्क-सेन, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a king of the Vidyā-dharas.<BR>—मृगाङ्-<BR>गना (˚ग-अङ्˚), f. a female deer, doe.<BR>—मृगाजिन<BR>(˚ग-अज्˚), अम्, n. a deer-skin.<BR>—मृगाजीव (˚ग-<BR>आज्˚), अस्, m. ‘subsisting by wild animals,’ a hunts-<BR>man; a hyena.<BR>—मृगाटवी (˚ग-अट्˚), f. = मृग-<BR>कानन, q. v.<BR>—मृगाण्ड-जा (˚ग-अण्˚), f. musk.<BR>—मृगाद् (˚ग-अद्), त्, m. ‘animal-devourer,’ a<BR>tiger.<BR>—मृगादन (˚ग-अद्˚), अस्, m. ‘animal-<BR>devourer,’ a hyena; a hunting leopard; (ई), f. colo-<BR>quintida, colocynth (= इन्द्र-वारुणी).<BR>—मृगा-<BR>धिप (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्, m. ‘king of animals,’ a lion.<BR>—मृगाधिपत्य (˚ग-आध्˚), अम्, n. dominion<BR>over wild animals.<BR>—मृगाधिराज (˚ग-अध्˚), अस्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-b" target="_blank">Page0791-b+ 81</a>]<BR>m. = मृगाधिप.<BR>—मृगान्तक (˚ग-अन्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘animal-destroyer,’ a cheeta or hunting leopard.<BR>—मृगाराति (˚ग-अर्˚), इस्, m. ‘enemy of wild<BR>animals,’ a lion; a dog.<BR>—मृगारि (˚ग-अरि), इस्, m.<BR>‘enemy of wild animals,’ a lion; a tiger; a dog,<BR>hound; a species of Moringa with red blossoms (=<BR>रक्त-शिग्रु; cf. मार्गार).<BR>—मृगा-वती, f., N. of<BR>Dākṣāyaṇī on the Yamunā; N. of several princesses.<BR>—मृगावती-चरित्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR>—मृ-<BR>गाविध् (˚ग-आव्˚), त्, m. a deer-killer, huntsman.<BR>—मृगास्य (˚ग-आस्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, ‘deer-faced,’<BR>having the head or face of an antelope; (अस्), m.<BR>the sign of the zodiac Capricorn; [cf. मृग-<BR>मुख.]<BR>—मृगी-कुण्ड, N. of a Tīrtha.<BR>—मृगी-<BR>त्व, अम्, n. the state or condition of a female deer<BR>or doe.<BR>—मृगी-दृश्, क्, f. ‘deer-eyed, fawn-eyed,’<BR>a woman with eyes like an antelope's.<BR>—मृगी-<BR>पति, इस्, m. ‘husband of Mṛgī,’ an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मृगी-लोचना, f. ‘fawn-eyed,’ a woman<BR>with eyes like an antelope's.<BR>—मृगेक्षण (˚ग-<BR>ईक्˚), अम्, n. the eye of an antelope or fawn, an eye<BR>like a deer's (आ), f. ‘fawn-eyed,’ a woman with<BR>eyes like an antelope's coloquintida, colocynth.<BR>—मृगेन्द्र (˚ग-इन्˚), अस्, m. ‘king of beasts,’ a<BR>lion; the sign of the zodiac Leo; a tiger; a parti-<BR>cular metre, four times ˘¯˘; N. of an author;<BR>(अम्), n., N. of Mṛgendra's work; of a Tantra.<BR>—मृगेन्द्र-चटक, अस्, m. a hawk, falcon.<BR>—मृगेन्द्र-ता, f. lordship over the beasts, do-<BR>minion over wild animals.<BR>—मृगेन्द्र-मुख,<BR>अम्, n. a lion's mouth; a particular metre, four times<BR>˘˘˘˘¯˘˘¯˘¯˘¯¯.<BR>—मृगेन्द्र-वृषभ,<BR>औ, m. du. a lion and a bull.<BR>—मृगेन्द्राणी, f.<BR>Gendarussa Vulgaris (= अटरूषक; cf. सिंही).<BR>—मृगेन्द्रासन (˚र-आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘lion's seat,’<BR>a throne; [cf. सिंहासन.]<BR>—मृगेन्द्रास्य (˚र-<BR>आस्˚), अस्, m. ‘lion-faced,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मृगेर्वारु (˚ग-इर्˚), coloquintida, colocynth;<BR>a species of animal; a white deer (?).<BR>—मृगेर्वा-<BR>रुक (˚ग-इर्˚), a species of animal (said to dwell<BR>in holes or caves).<BR>—मृगेश्वर (˚ग-ईश्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘lord of beasts,’ a lion; the sign of the zodiac Leo.<BR>—मृगेष्ट (˚ग-इष्˚), अस्, m. a species of jasmine.<BR>—मृगैर्वारु or मृगैर्वारुक (˚ग-एर्˚) =<BR>मृगेर्वारु.<BR>—मृगोत्तम (˚ग-उत्˚), अस्, m. best<BR>of antelopes, a beautiful antelope or deer; (अम्), n.<BR>the Nakṣatra Mṛga-śiras.<BR>—मृगोत्तमाङ्ग (˚ग-<BR>उत्˚), अम्, n. ‘antelope-head,’ the Nakṣatra Mṛga-<BR>śiras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

