मृगया
मृगया, f. hunting, the chase; the Chase per-<BR>sonified as one of the attendants of Revanta.<BR>—मृ-<BR>गया-यान, अम्, n. the going out to hunt, a hunting<BR>expedition.<BR>—मृगयारण्य (˚या-अर्˚) or मृगया-<BR>वन, अम्, n. a forest prepared or suited for hunting,<BR>a park, preserve; [cf. मृग-कानन.]<BR>—मृगया-<BR>शील, अस्, आ, अम्, accustomed to the chase, attached<BR>to hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

