मृच् मृच्, क्, f. (fr. rt. मर्च्), Ved. threaten-<BR>ing; injury; a snare; [cf. अ-मृक्त.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृचय
मृचय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (perhaps) liable to<BR>destruction or decay, transitory, going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृच्चय|मृच्चयः
मृच्चय मृच्-चय, मृच्-छकटिका. See<BR>under 2. मृद्, p. 792, col. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृछ्
मृछ् मृछ् or मर्छ्, cl. 6. A. मृच्छते,<BR>&c., to pass away, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्
मृज् 1. मृज् [cf. rts. मार्ज्, मृश्], cl. 2.<BR>P. मार्ष्टि (ep. also A. मार्ष्टे, 3rd pl.<BR>मृजन्ति or मार्जन्ति; Ved. 3rd sing. मृजति, -ते),<BR>Impf. अमार्ट् (3rd pl. अमृजन् or अमार्जन्), Impv.<BR>मार्ष्टु (2nd sing. मृड्ढि), ममार्ज (3rd pl.<BR>ममृजुस् or ममार्जुस्), मार्जिष्यति or मार्क्ष्-<BR>यति (Ved. म्रक्ष्यते), अमार्जीत् or अमार्क्षीत्<BR>(Ved. अमृक्षत्), मार्जितुम् or मार्ष्टुम्, to wipe,<BR>rub, cleanse, clean, purify, wash off, clear away; to rub,<BR>stroke; to make smooth or glossy, curry (as a horse);<BR>to deck, adorn, make ready; (A.) to wipe off (impu-<BR>rity from one's self) upon some one else (loc. c.);<BR>to go (Ved.); cl. 1. P. मर्जति, मृञ्जति, &c., to<BR>sound, (in this sense connected with rts. मुज्, मुञ्ज्,<BR>cf. rt. मार्ज्); cl. 10. P. A. or Caus. मार्जयति, -ते<BR>(Ved. मर्जयति, -ते), -यितुम्, to wipe off; to wash<BR>or cleanse one's self (in this sense only A.), purify<BR>one's self, become purified; to adorn; to move<BR>about, (according to Sāy. on Ṛg-veda VII. 39, 3.<BR>मर्जयन्त = परिचर्यन्ते): Pass. मृज्यते, Aor.<BR>अमार्जि, to be wiped or washed, &c.: Caus. मार्ज-<BR>यति, -यितुम्, Aor. अममार्जत् or अमीमृजत्, to<BR>cause to wipe or cleanse, &c.: Desid. मिमार्जिषति<BR>or मिमृक्षति: Intens. मरीमृज्यते (Ved. मर्-<BR>मृज्यते), मरीमार्ष्टि, मरिमार्ष्टि, मर्मार्-<BR>ष्टि, to rub or wipe off repeatedly, to keep rubbing<BR>or wiping off; (A.) to be continually cleansing one's<BR>self; [cf. Zend marez, ‘to wipe:’ Gr. ἀμέλγ-ω,<BR>ἄμελξις, ἀμολγεύ-ς, ἀμολγαῖο-ς, ἀμέργ-ω, ἀμοργός,<BR>ἀμόργη, ὀμόργ-νυ-μι, ὄμοργ-μα, γλάγος (for<BR>μλάγος), γάλα, γάλακτος (for μλακτο): Lat.<BR>mulg-e-o, mulc-tu-s, mulctra, mulctru-m, merg-a,<BR>merg-e(t)s, mulier, lac (for mlac): Old Germ.<BR>milch-u, ‘I milk:’ Goth. miluks, ‘milk:’ Angl.<BR>Sax. meoluc, meolc, melcan, mearc, mearcian,<BR>ge-mearc: Slav. mlz-a: Lith. melz-u: perhaps Hib.<BR>breugaim, ‘I soothe;’ bleaghaim, ‘I milk.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जित|मार्ज्जित
मार्जित, अस्, आ, अम् (equally to be connected with<BR>rt. मार्ज्), wiped, cleansed, purified, clean, smooth,<BR>bright; washed away, removed; rubbed, smeared,<BR>besmeared, &c.; see मार्जित, p. 774, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्
2. मृज्, ट्, ट्, ट्, (at the end of a comp.) wiping,<BR>rubbing; wiping off or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज|मृजः
मृज, अस्, m. a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृजत्
मृजत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, wiping away, cleansing,<BR>effacing, (also प्र-मृजत्, Kirātārj. III. 4, 3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृजा
मृजा, f. wiping, cleansing, washing, purifying,<BR>purification, ablution; purity, cleanliness; a pure<BR>skin, clear complexion; complexion.<BR>—मृजा-न-<BR>गर, अम्, n., N. of a town.<BR>—मृजान्वय (˚जा-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, possessing or endowed with clean-<BR>liness, cleansed, clean.<BR>—मृजा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, pos-<BR>sessed of cleanliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृजित
मृजित, अस्, आ, अम्, wiped, wiped away, rubbed<BR>off, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्य|मृज्यं
मृज्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be cleansed, to be purified;<BR>to be wiped away or removed (= 2. मार्ग्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
1. मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 793, col. 1),<BR>washed, cleansed, clean, pure; smeared, besmeared;<BR>prepared, dressed, savoury, (मृष्टम् अन्नम्, deli-<BR>cate food, dainties; cf. मिष्ट); (अम्), n. pepper.<BR>—मृष्ट-गन्ध, अस्, m. (probably) an agreeable<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">Page0792-a+ 77</a>]<BR>or appetizing smell or savour.<BR>—मृष्टगन्ध-<BR>पवन, अस्, m. a fragrant breeze.<BR>—मृष्ट-तम,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, exceedingly delicate or savoury.<BR>—मृ-<BR>ष्ट-लुञ्चित, अस्, आ, अम्, torn up (as a root) and<BR>washed.<BR>—मृष्ट-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. containing<BR>a form of rt. 1. मृज्.<BR>—मृष्ट-वाक्य, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>speaking sweetly (= मिष्ट-वाक्य).<BR>—मृष्ट-<BR>सलिल, अस्, आ, अम्, having bright or pure water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0791-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टि|मृष्टिः
1. मृष्टि, इस्, f. (for 2. see p. 793, col. 1), cleans-<BR>ing, cleaning, preparation, dressing (of food, Manu<BR>III. 255); a savoury repast, (according to Kullūka<BR>= अन्नादेः संस्कार-विशेष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टेरुक|मृष्टेरुकः
मृष्टेरुक, अस्, आ, अम्, eating dainties or deli-<BR>cacies, luxurious, selfish; liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड्
मृड् मृड् (Ved. मृऌ), cl. 6. 9. P. मृ-<BR>डति, मृड्नाति, ममर्ड, मर्डिष्यति,<BR>अमर्डीत्, मर्डितुम् (Ved. cl. 6. P. मृऌअति, cl.<BR>10. P. मृऌअयति, &c.), to be gracious or favour-<BR>able, be gracious towards (with dat.); to forgive, par-<BR>don, spare; to treat graciously, rejoice, delight, make<BR>happy; to rejoice, be delighted or happy: Caus.<BR>मर्डयति, -यितुम्, Aor. अमीमृडत् or अममर्-<BR>डत्: Desid. मिमर्डिषति: Intens. मरीमृड्यते,<BR>मरीमर्ट्टि; [cf. Gr. μείλ-ια, μείλιχο-ς, μειλίχ-ιο-ς,<BR>μει-λιχ-ίη, μειλίσσω, μειλ-εῖν: Lat. blan-<BR>dus: Goth. mild-s, ‘affectionate:’ Old Germ. mil-<BR>ti, ‘mild:’ Slav. mil-ŭ, ‘pitiable;’ mil-ovati, ‘to<BR>pity;’ mil-ostĭ, ‘pity:’ Lith. myl-iu; meilù-s,<BR>‘lovely;’ méile, ‘love.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड|मृडः
मृड, अस्, आ, अम् [cf. मृदु, col. 3], showing<BR>mercy, gracious (Ved.); (अस्), m. a N. of Agni or<BR>Fire; of Śiva; (आ, ई), f. an epithet of Pārvatī [cf.<BR>मृडानी]; (अम्), n., scil. हिरण्य, a particular<BR>weight of gold (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडन|मृडनं
मृडन, अम्, n. the act of showing grace or<BR>favour, making happy, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडय
मृडय, अस्, आ, अम्, showing grace or mercy;<BR>अ-मृडय, unmerciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडाकु
मृडाकु, उस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडानी
मृडानी, f. the wife of Mṛḍa or Śiva, i. e. Pār-<BR>vatī.<BR>—मृडानी-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडितृ
मृडितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, Ved. = मर्डितृ, one who<BR>shows favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडीक|मृडीकः
मृडीक, अस्, m. ‘gracious,’ N. of Śiva; a fish;<BR>(according to some) an antelope, [cf. मृग.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृळयत्
मृऌअयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. showing grace or<BR>favour, favouring.<BR>—मृऌअयत्-तम, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>Ved. exceedingly gracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृळयाकु
मृऌअयाकु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. gracious, kindly dis-<BR>posed, showing grace, making happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृळीक
मृऌईक, अम्, n., Ved. grace, mercy, kindness;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a Vāsiṣṭha, author of the hymns<BR>Ṛg-veda IX. 97, 25-27, and X. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडङ्कण|मृडङ्कणः
मृडङ्कण मृडङ्कण, अस्, m. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. IV. 24. fr. rt. मृड्), a child, boy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्
मृण् मृण् (connected with rts. मृ,<BR>मॄ), cl. 6. P. मृणति, ममर्ण,<BR>मृणितुम्, to kill, slay; [cf. Gr. μάρναμαι.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणाल|मृणालं|मृणालः
मृणाल मृणाल, अस्, अम्, m. n. (said to be<BR>also ई, f.), the edible fibrous root of some kinds of<BR>lotus, a lotus fibre or small fibre attached to the stalk<BR>of a water-lily; (ई), f. a lotus fibre; (अम्), n. the<BR>root of the fragrant grass Andropogon Muricatus.<BR>—मृणाल-भङ्ग, अस्, m. the fracture of a lotus<BR>fibre.<BR>—मृणाल-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing lotus<BR>fibres or roots.<BR>—मृणाल-सूत्र, अम्, n. the fibre<BR>of a lotus stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालक
मृणालक, अस्, आ, अम्, (at the end of comps.) =<BR>मृणाल; (इका), f. the edible root of a lotus; a<BR>proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालिन्
मृणालिन्, ई, m. a lotus; (इनी), f. a lotus plant;<BR>a group of lotuses; a place where lotuses grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्मय
मृण्मय मृण्-मय, incorrectly for मृन्-<BR>मय under 2. मृद्, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत|मृतं
मृत मृत. See under rt. मृ, p. 789, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतण्ड|मृतंडः|मृतण्डः
मृतण्ड मृतण्ड, अस्, m., N. of the father<BR>of the sun; the sun; [cf. मृताण्ड, मार्तण्ड.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतामद|मृतामदं|मृतामदः
मृतामद मृतामद, अम्, n. blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतालक|मृतालकं
मृतालक मृतालक or मृत्ताल or मृत्ता-<BR>लक, अम्, n. (probably connected with 2. मृद्),<BR>a kind of loam or clay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्कर|मृत्करः
मृत्कर मृत्-कर. See under 2. मृद् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्यव
मृत्यव मृत्यव, probably incorrect for<BR>मृत्-पच below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्यु|मृत्युः
मृत्यु मृत्यु. See p. 790, col. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्सा
मृत्सा मृत्सा, मृत्स्न. See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
मृद् 1. मृद् [cf. rts. म्रद्, मृड्], cl. 9. P.<BR>मृद्नाति (ep. also A. मृद्नीते), cl. 1. P.<BR>मर्दति (ep. also A. -ते), ममर्द (3rd pl. ममृ-<BR>दुस् or ममर्दुस्), ममृदे, मर्दिष्यति, अमर्-<BR>दीत्, मर्दितुम्, to press, squeeze; to grind, pound,<BR>bruise, reduce to powder, pulverize; to crush, dash<BR>to pieces, trample upon, treat harshly, lay waste; to<BR>overcome, surpass; to rub, stroke, wipe, (हस्तेन<BR>ममृदे ललाटम्, he wiped his forehead with his<BR>hand); to rub against, touch, graze, pass through (as<BR>a constellation, in astronomy); to rub away, wipe<BR>away, destroy; (according to Naigh. II. 14) to go,<BR>(in this sense cl. 1. P.): Pass. मृद्यते, to be<BR>pressed or ground, &c.: Caus. मर्दयति, -यितुम्,<BR>Aor. अममर्दत् or अमीमृदत्, to press or squeeze<BR>hard, to crush, break, trample upon, tread under foot,<BR>oppress, treat harshly, wear out, torment, plague,<BR>destroy, kill; to rub; to cause to be trampled upon,<BR>&c.: Desid. मिमर्दिषति, to desire to crush, wish<BR>to pound; to be about to crush, &c.: Intens. मरी-<BR>मृद्यते, मरीमर्त्ति, &c.; [cf. Gr. ἀ-μέρδ-ω,<BR>μύλ-η, μέλδ-ω, ἀ-μαλδ-ύν-ω, ἄ-μαλο-ς: Lat. mord-<BR>e-o, mand-o, mol-o, mol-a, malleus (for mar-<BR>deus): Goth. malvja, ‘I pound;’ mala, ‘I grind;’<BR>malo, ‘a moth:’ Angl. Sax. s-melte, ‘to melt;’<BR>malt, meltan, miltan, smeortan: Old Germ.<BR>smilzu; smylt, ‘serene, calm;’ malz, smerzan:<BR>Lith. malù, ‘I grind;’ mald-inu, mal-inu, ‘I<BR>cause to be ground;’ molj, ‘a moth:’ Hib. meilim,<BR>‘I grind;’ millim, ‘I spoil, ruin.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्तिका
मृत्तिका, f. earth, clay, loam; fresh earth; a<BR>kind of fragrant earth.<BR>—मृत्तिका-वती, f., N. of a<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्सा
मृत्सा, f. good earth or clay; earth, clay; a kind<BR>of fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्स्न|मृत्स्नं|मृत्स्नः
मृत्स्न, अस्, अम्, m. n. dust, powder; (आ), f.<BR>good earth or clay; a kind of fragrant earth; clay;<BR>[cf. मार्त्स्न.]<BR>—मृत्स्ना-भाण्डक, अम्, n. a<BR>kind of earthen vessel (= उष्ट्रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
2. मृद्, त्, f. earth, soil, clay, loam; a piece of<BR>earth, lump of clay; a mound of earth; a kind of<BR>fragrant earth; [cf. पाण्डु-म्˚.]<BR>—मृच्-चय, अस्, m.<BR>a heap of earth.<BR>—मृच्-छकटिका, f. (i. e. मृत् +<BR>शकटिका), a small cart made of clay, toy-cart; (आ, अम्),<BR>f. n., N. of a celebrated drama (supposed to be the oldest<BR>Sanskrit play extant) by king Śūdraka.<BR>—मृच्छ-<BR>कटिका-सेतु, उस्, m., N. of a commentary by Lallā-<BR>dīkṣita on the above drama.<BR>—मृच्-छिला-मय,<BR>अस्, ई, अम् (i. e. मृत् + शिला + मय), made of clay<BR>and stone.<BR>—मृत्-कण, a small lump or clod of<BR>earth or clay.<BR>—मृत्कण-ता, f. the state of a clod<BR>of earth.<BR>—मृत्-कर, अस्, m. a worker in clay,<BR>potter.<BR>—मृत्-कांस्य, अम्, n. an earthen pitcher,<BR>earthen vessel.<BR>—मृत्-किरा, f. ‘earth-scattering,’ an<BR>earth-worm; a species of cricket.<BR>—मृत्-खलिनी,<BR>f. a species of plant (= चर्म-कशा).<BR>—मृत्-पच,<BR>अस्, m. a baker of clay, potter.<BR>—मृत्-पात्र, अम्,<BR>n. a vessel of clay, earthen vessel, earthenware.<BR>—मृत्-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a clod of earth, lump of clay.<BR>—मृत्पिण्ड-तस्, ind. from a lump of clay.<BR>—मृत्-<BR>प्रक्षेप, scattering earth over anything (as a<BR>means of purification, Manu V. 125).<BR>—मृत्-फली,<BR>f. Costus Speciosus or Arabicus.<BR>—मृद्-आह्वया, f.<BR>a species of fragrant earth.<BR>—मृद्-ग, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>being in the earth, growing in clay; (अस्), m. a<BR>species of fish.<BR>—मृद्-घट, अस्, m. an earthen pot<BR>or pitcher.<BR>—मृद्-भाण्ड, अम्, n. a vessel of clay,<BR>earthen pot, earthenware.<BR>—मृद्-भाण्डावशेषम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-c" target="_blank">Page0792-c+ 81</a>]<BR>(˚ड-अव्˚), ind. so that only an earthen vessel is left.<BR>—मृद्-वारि-शुचि, इस्, इस्, इ, purified with earth and<BR>water (Manu V. 106).<BR>—मृन्-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>made of earth or clay, earthen; मृन्-मयम्<BR>पात्रम्, an earthenware vessel.<BR>—मृन्-मरु, उस्,<BR>m. a stone, rock (?).<BR>—मृल्-लोष्ट, अम्, n. a lump<BR>of clay, clod of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदव|मृदवं
मृदव, अम्, n. (fr. मृदु), contrasting excel-<BR>lence or merit of any kind with demerit (in drama-<BR>tical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदा
मृदा, f., Ved. = 2. मृद्; [cf. probably Lat.<BR>merda; Goth. mulda; Angl. Sax. molde.]<BR>—मृ-<BR>दा-कर, अस्, m. a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदित|मृदितः
मृदित, अस्, आ, अम्, pressed, squeezed; crushed,<BR>bruised, pounded, ground, trampled upon, trampled<BR>down, laid waste; rubbed; (अम्), n. a particular<BR>disease of the membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदिनी
मृदिनी, f. good earth or soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदु|मृदुः
मृदु, उस्, उस् or वी, उ (compar. म्रदीयस्, su-<BR>perl. म्रदिष्ठ, q. q. v. v.; cf. rt. म्रद्, from<BR>which in Uṇādi-s. 1. 29. मृदु is said to be de-<BR>rived), ‘easily pressed or squeezed,’ soft, tender, sup-<BR>ple, flexible, pliant; mild, gentle; weak, moderate;<BR>blunt; slow; (उस्), m. the planet Saturn [cf. मन्द];<BR>N. of a king; (वी), f. a vine with red grapes [cf. मृ-<BR>द्वीका]; (उ), n. softness, mildness, gentleness; [cf.<BR>Gr. βραδύς (fr. μραδύς like βροτό-ς fr. μροτό-ς);<BR>Lat. bardus, mollis (fr. molvis for modvis or<BR>morvis), mollities, mollīre, blandus; Old Germ.<BR>milti; Mod. Germ., Angl. Sax., and Eng. mild;<BR>Russ. molodyĭ, ‘young;’ Hib. meirbh, ‘slow,<BR>tedious, weak.’]<BR>—मृदु-कृष्णायस, अम्, n. ‘soft-<BR>iron,’ lead.<BR>—मृदु-कोष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, having<BR>relaxed bowels, relaxed, easily affected by medicine.<BR>—मृदु-क्रिया, f. the act of softening, mollify-<BR>ing.<BR>—मृदु-गण, अस्, m. = मृदु-वर्ग below.<BR>—मृदु-गन्धिक, अस्, m. a species of plant.<BR>—मृदु-गमन, अस्, आ, अम्, going softly, having<BR>a soft or gentle gait; (आ), f. a goose or female swan.<BR>—मृदु-गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going softly, having a<BR>soft or gentle gait.<BR>—मृदु-चर्मिन्, ई, m. a species<BR>of birch tree (= चर्मिन्).<BR>—मृदु-चाप, अस्, m.,<BR>N. of a Dānava.<BR>—मृदु-च्छद, अस्, m. a species<BR>of birch tree; a kind of mountain Pīlu tree.<BR>—मृदु-<BR>जातीय, अस्, आ, अम्, somewhat soft, slightly weak.<BR>—मृदु-ता, f. or मृदु-त्व, अम्, n. softness,<BR>gentleness, tenderness, mildness, weakness; मृदु-<BR>तां गम् or व्रज्, to become mild or weak, be<BR>appeased.<BR>—मृदु-ताल, अस्, m. a species of tree<BR>(= श्री-ताल).<BR>—मृदु-तीक्ष्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, soft and<BR>violent, gentle and harsh, (used as an epithet of the<BR>two Nakṣatras Kṛttikā and Vi-śākhā.)<BR>—मृदु-<BR>त्वच्, क्, or मृदु-त्वच, अस्, m. ‘having a soft<BR>bark,’ a species of birch tree.<BR>—मृदु-पत्त्र, अस्,<BR>m. ‘soft-leafed,’ a rush, reed.<BR>—मृदु-परुष-<BR>गुण, औ, m. du. ‘the qualities of mild and harsh,’<BR>mildness and harshness.<BR>—मृदु-पर्वक, अस्, m.<BR>or मृदु-पर्वन्, अ, n. ‘soft-jointed,’ a reed, cane.<BR>—मृदु-पाणि, इस्, इस्, इ, ‘soft-handed,’ having a<BR>delicate hand.<BR>—मृदु-पीठक, अस्, m. a kind of<BR>sheat-fish, silurus.<BR>—मृदु-पुष्प, अस्, m. ‘having<BR>soft flowers,’ Acacia Sirissa (= शिरीष).<BR>—मृदु-<BR>पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, commencing softly, friendly at<BR>first, gentle, tender; (अम्), ind. mildly or friendly<BR>at first, gently, tenderly, blandly, softly, coaxingly.<BR>—मृदु-प्रयत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. (to be pro-<BR>nounced) with a gentle effort.<BR>—मृदु-प्रिय, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—मृदु-प्रौढ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, full of gentleness; mild and haughty.<BR>—मृदु-<BR>फल, अस्, m. ‘having soft fruit,’ N. of various<BR>plants (= विकङ्कत, विकण्टक, मधु-नालिके-<BR>रक).<BR>—मृदु-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ, speaking sweetly.<BR>—मृदु-मृत्स्न, अस्, आ, अम्, consisting of soft or<BR>fine particles or atoms.<BR>—मृदु-रोम-वत्, आन्, or<BR>मृदु-लोमक, अस्, m. ‘having soft hair,’ a hare.<BR>—मृदु-वर्ग, अस्, m. the group of Nakṣatras<BR>called मृदु (viz. Anu-rādhā, Citrā, Revatī, and<BR>Mṛga-śiras).<BR>—मृदु-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, ‘soft-voiced,’<BR>mild in speech.<BR>—मृदु-वात, अस्, m. a gentle<BR>breeze, zephyr.<BR>—मृदु-विद्, त्, m., N. of a son of<BR>Śvaphalka.<BR>—मृदु-स्पर्श, अस्, आ, अम्, soft to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">Page0793-a+ 74</a>]<BR>touch, soft.<BR>—मृदु-हृदय, अस्, आ, अम्, tender-<BR>hearted, kind.<BR>—मृदूत्पल^1 (˚दु-उत्˚), अम्, n.<BR>the blue lotus, Nymphæa Cyanea.<BR>—मृद्व्-अङ्ग,<BR>अस्, आ or ई, अम्, ‘tender-limbed,’ delicately formed;<BR>(ई), f. a delicate woman; (अम्), n. tin.<BR>—मृद्व्-<BR>अवग्रह, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. easily indicating the<BR>division of the members of a compound.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/322, batch 311-315. note: confuses utphala for utpala "lotus".<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0792-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुक
मृदुक, अस्, आ, अम्, soft, tender, gentle; (अम्),<BR>ind. softly, gently, tenderly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुर
मृदुर, अस्, m., N. of a son of Śvaphalka, (also<BR>read मुदर.)<BR>—मृदुर-स्वन, see under भि-<BR>दुर-स्वन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुल|मृदुलं
मृदुल, अस्, आ, अम्, soft, tender, mild, gentle;<BR>(अम्), n. water; Amyris Agallocha (= अ-गुरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदूअस्
मृदू-अस्, cl. 2. P. मृद्व्-अस्ति, &c., to be or<BR>become soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदूभाव
मृदू-भाव, अस्, m. the becoming soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदूभू
मृदू-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, &c., to become soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्यमन
मृद्यमन, अस्, आ, अम्, being crushed or bruised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्वीका
मृद्वीका, f. a vine; a bunch of grapes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्कुरु|मृदंकुरुः|मृदङ्कुरुः
मृदङ्कुरु मृदङ्कुरु, उस्, or मृदङ्कुर, अस्,<BR>m. the green pigeon, Columba Hariala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्ग|मृदंग|मृदंगः|मृदङ्गः
मृदङ्ग मृदङ्ग, अस्, m. (according to<BR>Uṇādi-s. 1. 120. fr. rt. 1. मृद्), a kind of drum,<BR>tabour; noise, din; a bamboo cane; (ई), f. a species<BR>of plant (= घोषातकी).<BR>—मृदङ्ग-फल, अस्,<BR>m. the jack or bread-fruit tree.<BR>—मृदङ्ग-फ-<BR>लिनी, f. = मृदङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्गक|मृदंगक
मृदङ्गक, अम्, n. a kind of metre, four times<BR>¯ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ˘ ˘ ¯ ˘ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯ ˘ ¯.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदर
मृदर मृदर, अस्, आ, अम् (perhaps fr. rt. 1.<BR>मृद्, said to be fr. rt. मृ), sporting, sportive;<BR>passing quickly away, transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदानी
मृदानी मृदानी, incorrect for मृडानी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदि
मृदि मृदि. See मार्देय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुन्नक|मृदुन्नकं
मृदुन्नक मृदुन्नक, अम्, n. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुर
मृदुर मृदुर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध्
मृध् 1. मृध्, cl. 1. P. A. मर्धति, -ते,<BR>मर्धितुम्, (Ved.) to kill, injure, hurt;<BR>to contemn, neglect, forget, disregard, be disgusted<BR>with (with acc.); to be moist; to moisten; [cf. pro-<BR>bably Gr. μαλθακός; Goth. maurthr; Angl. Sax.<BR>mordher, mordhor; Old Germ. multjan.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध्
2. मृध्, त्, f., Ved. (according to Sāy.) combat,<BR>fight, battle; one who contemns or injures; an ad-<BR>versary, foe, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध|मृधं
मृध, अम्, n. combat, fight, war, battle; (said<BR>to be also अस्, m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृधस्
मृधस्, अस्, n., Ved. war, battle; contempt, indif-<BR>ference; मृधस्-कृ, to disdain, contemn, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध्र
मृध्र, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. one who injures, an<BR>enemy; (आणि), n. pl. disdain, contempt, abuse,<BR>insult, contumely.<BR>—मृध्र-वाच्, क्, क्, क्, Ved.<BR>speaking injuriously or contumeliously, insulting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृन्मय
मृन्मय मृन्-मय, मृल्-लोष्ट, &c. See<BR>under 2. मृद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृळ्
मृळ् मृऌ, Ved. See under rt. मृड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृश्
मृश् 1. मृश् (often confounded with<BR>rt. 1. मृष्), cl. 6. P. मृशति (some-<BR>times also A. मृशते), ममर्श, मर्क्ष्यति or<BR>म्रक्ष्यति, अमृक्षत् or अमार्क्षीत् or अम्रा-<BR>क्षीत्, मर्ष्टुम् or म्रष्टुम्, to touch, stroke,<BR>handle; to rub, rub off; to touch (mentally), con-<BR>sider, reflect, deliberate; [cf. Lat. mulc-e-o, (pro-<BR>bably also) mulc-o: perhaps Hib. mear, ‘a finger,<BR>toe;’ mearacht, ‘fingering or touching a musical<BR>instrument.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृश्
2. मृश्, क्, क्, क्, (at the end of comps.) one who<BR>strokes or touches, a stroker, (see Gram. 181.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
2. मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. and 3. see under<BR>rts. 1. मृज् and 3. मृष्), touched, stroked, rubbed,<BR>handled; considered, reflected upon, deliberated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टि|मृष्टिः
2. मृष्टि, इस्, f. (for 1. and 3. see p. 792, col. 1,<BR>and this page, col. 2), touching, stroking, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृशय
मृशय मृशय for मृचय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
मृष् 1. मृष् (often confounded with<BR>rt. 1. मृश्), cl. 4. P. A. मृष्यति, -ते<BR>(rarely cl. 1. P. A. मर्षति, -ते), ममर्ष, म-<BR>मृषे, मर्षिष्यति, -ते, अमर्षीत् (ep. अमृ-<BR>षत्), अमर्षिष्ट, मर्षितुम्, to bear, endure,<BR>suffer; to permit, let, allow; to bear patiently, (मु-<BR>हूर्तम् मृष्यताम्, have patience for a moment);<BR>to forget, let slip (from the mind), neglect; to par-<BR>don, forgive, excuse; cl. 10. P. A. or Caus. मर्ष-<BR>यति, -ते (according to Vopa-deva also मृषयति,<BR>-ते), -यितुम्, Aor. अमीमृषत् or अममर्षत्,<BR>अमीमृषत or अममर्षत, to bear, suffer;<BR>endure, tolerate, allow, put up with; to forgive,<BR>excuse, pardon; [cf. Goth. marzjan; Old Germ.<BR>marrjan; Angl. Sax. myrran.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
2. मृष्, ट्, ट्, ट्, (at the end of comps.) one who<BR>bears or endures, bearing, (see Gram. 181.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषा
मृषा, ind. (probably an old inst. fr. a form<BR>मृष, and perhaps meaning originally ‘with for-<BR>getfulness’), in vain, to no purpose, uselessly; wrongly,<BR>incorrectly, falsely, untruly, untruthfully, lyingly,<BR>feignedly, (sometimes used like a substantive, e. g.<BR>वर्जनीयम् मृषा बुधैः, untruthfulness is to<BR>be avoided by the wise); मृषा कृ, to act falsely,<BR>feign; Mṛṣā, as ‘Untruth,’ is personfied as the wife<BR>of A-dharma.<BR>—मृषा-ज्ञान, अम्, n. false or spu-<BR>rious knowledge, ignorance, folly.<BR>—मृषा-त्व,<BR>अम्, n. incorrectness, falsity.<BR>—मृषा-दान, अम्,<BR>n. ‘false gift,’ feigned or insincere promise of a gift.<BR>—मृषा-दृष्टि, इस्, इस्, इ, having a false view or<BR>opinion.<BR>—मृषाध्यायिन् (˚षा-अध्˚), ई, m. a<BR>species of crane, Ardea Nivea, (compared to a reli-<BR>gious hypocrite, hence its names तापस, दाम्भिक,<BR>तीर्थ-सेविन्.)<BR>—मृषानुशासिन् (˚षा-अन्˚), ई, इनी,<BR>इ, punishing unjustly.<BR>—मृषा-भाषिन्, ई, इणी, इ,<BR>speaking falsely or untruthfully, a liar.<BR>—मृषार्-<BR>थक (˚षा-अर्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having a false<BR>sense or meaning, untrue, absurd; (अम्), n. an<BR>impossibility, absurdity (as a rabbit's horn, &c.).<BR>—मृषा-वाच्, क्, f. an untrue or satirical speech,<BR>sarcasm, irony.<BR>—मृषा-वाद, अस्, m. an untrue<BR>speech, lie; sarcasm, irony; (अस्, आ, अम्), speaking<BR>falsely or untruthfully, a liar.<BR>—मृषा-वादिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, speaking falsely or untruthfully, a liar; (ई),<BR>m. one who brings forward an unjust or unfounded<BR>charge, a false accuser.<BR>—मृषोद्य (˚षा-उद्˚),<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, speaking untruthfully, lying, a liar; (अम्),<BR>n. untruthfulness, lying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषाय
मृषाय (fr. मृषा), Nom. A. मृषायते,<BR>&c., to err, be mistaken, hold a wrong notion or<BR>opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषित
मृषित in अप-मृषित, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
मृष् 3. मृष् (connected with rt. 2.<BR>मिष्), cl. 1. P. मर्षति, ममर्ष,<BR>मर्षितुम्, to sprinkle, pour out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
3. मृष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टि|मृष्टिः
3. मृष्टि, इस्, f. (for 1. and 2. see under rts.<BR>1. मृज् and 1. मृश्), sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषालक|मृषालकः
मृषालक मृषालक, अस्, m. the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
मृष्ट मृष्ट. See under rts. 1. मृज्, 1. मृश्,<BR>and 3. मृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मॄ
मॄ मॄ (connected with rts. मृ and<BR>मृण्), cl. 9. P. मृणाति, ममार, मरिष्-<BR>यति, अमारीत्, मर्तुम्, Ved. to bruise, smash, crush,<BR>break; kill, hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ण|मूर्णः
मूर्ण, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed, broken; = 2. मूत,<BR>bound; [cf. rt. मुर्व्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मे
मे मे, cl. 1. A. मयते, ममे, मास्यते,<BR>अमास्त, मातुम्, to change, exchange, barter:<BR>Caus. मापयति, -यितुम्, to cross over, (perhaps fr.<BR>rt. 3. मा): Desid. मित्सते: Intens. मेमीयते,<BR>मामेति, मामाति; [cf. Gr. ἀ-μείβ-ω, ἀμείβ-ο-μαι,<BR>ἀ-μεύ-σα-οθαι, παρ-αμείβ-εινμ ἀμοιβή, μοῖ-το-ς:<BR>Lat. me-a-re, mov-e-o, mô-tu-s, mô-tio, mô-men-<BR>tu-m, mu-ta-re, mû-tuu-s, communis, munus:<BR>Goth. maithms, maidjan, ga-mains: Angl. Sax.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">Page0793-c+ 77</a>]<BR>madhm, mane, man, ge-mœne: Slav. me-na,<BR>‘change:’ Lith. mai-na-s, ‘exchange;’ mainý-ti,<BR>‘to change, exchange.’]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापयान
मापयान, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. the Caus.), crossing<BR>over (fr. rt. 3. मा ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेक|मेकः
मेक मेक, अस्, m. (probably onomato-<BR>poetic), a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकल|मेकलः
मेकल मेकल, अस्, m., N. of a mountain;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people, (also wrongly read<BR>मेलक); (आ), f., N. of a river (= मेकल-कन्-<BR>यका).<BR>—मेकल-कन्यका or मेकल-कन्या, f.<BR>‘daughter of Mekala,’ an epithet of the Narmadā<BR>river.<BR>—मेकलकन्यका-तट, N. of a district.<BR>—मेकलाद्रि (˚ल-अद्˚), इस्, m. the Mekala moun-<BR>tain.<BR>—मेकलाद्रि-जा, f. ‘sprung from the Mekala<BR>mountain,’ an epithet of the Narmadā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेक्षण|मेक्षणं
मेक्षण मेक्षण, अम्, n. (fr. मिक्ष्), Ved.<BR>a wooden stick or spoon for stirring up the Caru or<BR>taking small portions from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखला
मेखला मेखला, f. a girdle, belt, waist-belt,<BR>(in one or two instances अस् or अम्, m. or n.); the<BR>zone of a woman; the triple zone worn by the first<BR>three classes, (according to Manu II. 42. that of a<BR>Brāhman ought to be of मुञ्ज, that of a Kṣatriya<BR>of मूर्वा, that of the Vaiśya of शण or hemp);<BR>the girth of a horse; a band or fillet; anything<BR>girding or surrounding [cf. सागर-म्˚]; a sword-<BR>belt, baldric; a sword-knot or string fastened to the<BR>hilt; the place of the girdle, the hips; the cords or<BR>lines drawn round an altar, or on the four sides of<BR>the hole in which sacrificial fire is offered; the edge<BR>or slope of a mountain [cf. नि-तम्ब]; Hemionitis<BR>Cordifolia; N. of a place; of a woman; of the<BR>Narmadā river, [cf. मेकला.]<BR>—मेखल-कन्-<BR>यका = मेकल-कन्यका, q. v.<BR>—मेखला-पद,<BR>अम्, n. the place of the girdle, the hips.<BR>—मेखला-<BR>बन्ध, अस्, m. investiture with the girdle; the<BR>rites connected with such investiture.<BR>—मेखला-वत्,<BR>आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. having a girdle or belt, wearing a<BR>fillet.<BR>—मेखला-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. wearing a<BR>girdle.<BR>—मेखली-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्,<BR>to put on a girdle, to put on the sacrificial string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलाल|मेखलालः
मेखलाल, अस्, m. ‘having a girdle,’ epithet of<BR>Śiva; (according to a Scholiast = मेखलयालङ्-<BR>कृत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलिक
मेखलिक, अस्, आ, अम्, wearing a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलिन्
मेखलिन्, ई, इनी, इ, wearing a girdle; (ई), m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; a Brāhmanical student or youth<BR>who, previous to his marriage, wears a girdle suited<BR>to his caste, Brahma-cārin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघ्
मेघ् मेघ् = rt. मिघ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघ|मेघः
मेघ, अस्, m. a cloud, (काल-म्˚, a black cloud);<BR>cloudy weather; a mass, multitude; a fragrant grass,<BR>Cyperus Rotundus; N. of one of the six Rāgas or<BR>musical scales; of a Rākṣasa; of the father of the<BR>fifth Arhat of the present Ava-sarpiṇī; of a poet,<BR>(also read मेच); of a mountain; (अम्), n. talc;<BR>[cf. Gr. ὀ-μίχ-λη; Goth. milh-ma, ‘a cloud;’<BR>Lith. mig-la, ‘a mist.’]<BR>—मेघ-कफ, अस्, m.<BR>‘cloud-phlegm,’ hail.<BR>—मेघ-कर्णा, f., N. of one<BR>of the Mātṛs attending on Skanda.<BR>—मेघ-काल,<BR>m. ‘cloud-time,’ the rainy season.<BR>—मेघ-कूटा-<BR>भिगर्जितेश्वर (˚ट-अभ्˚, ˚त-ईश्˚), अस्, m., N. of<BR>a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—मेघ-गम्भीर, अस्, आ, अम्,<BR>deep as (the rumbling of) a cloud.<BR>—मेघ-गर्-<BR>जन, अम्, n. ‘cloud-rumbling,’ thundering, thunder.<BR>—मेघ-गिरि, इस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—मे-<BR>घङ्-कर, अस्, ई, अम्, ‘cloud-making,’ producing<BR>clouds.<BR>—मेघ-चिन्तक, अस्, m. ‘anxious for<BR>clouds,’ the Cātaka bird (supposed to drink only<BR>rain-water, and therefore naturally eager for rainy<BR>weather).<BR>—मेघ-ज, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘cloud-born,’<BR>coming from the clouds; (अस्), m. a large pearl.<BR>—मेघ-जाल, अम्, n. ‘cloud-collection,’ a mass<BR>of clouds, thick clouds; talc.<BR>—मेघ-जीवक<BR>or मेघ-जीवन, अस्, m. ‘living on clouds,’ the<BR>Cātaka bird.<BR>—मेघ-ज्योतिस्, इस्, n. (according to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-a" target="_blank">Page0794-a+ 81</a>]<BR>the Amara-koṣa, इस्, m.), ‘cloud-light,’ a flash of<BR>lightning, the fire produced from lighting.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>डम्बर, अस्, m. thunder; [cf. मेघाडम्बर.]<BR>—मेघ-तरु, उस्, m., Ved. ‘cloud-tree,’ a parti-<BR>cular form of cloud.<BR>—मेघ-तिमिर, अम्, n. ‘cloud-<BR>darkness,’ darkness resulting from a clouded sky,<BR>cloudy or rainy weather.<BR>—मेघ-त्व, अम्, n. the<BR>being a cloud, the state of a cloud, cloudiness; मे-<BR>घत्वम् उप-गम्, to become a cloud.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>दीप, अस्, m. ‘cloud-light,’ lightning.<BR>—मेघ-दुन्-<BR>दुभि, इस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR>—मेघ-दुन्दुभि-<BR>स्वर-राज, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—मेघ-दूत,<BR>अस्, m. ‘cloud-messenger,’ N. of a celebrated poem<BR>by Kālidāsa.<BR>—मेघदूत-पाद-समस्या, f., N.<BR>of a work.<BR>—मेघदूताभिध (˚त-अभ्˚), अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, entitled ‘cloud-messenger.’<BR>—मेघ-द्वार, अम्,<BR>n. ‘cloud-gate,’ heaven, the sky, ether.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>नाद, अस्, m. ‘cloud-noise,’ sound of rain, thunder;<BR>(अस्, आ, अम्), sounding or rumbling like thunder,<BR>making a noise like thunder; (अस्), m. an epithet<BR>of Varuṇa; N. of one of the attendants of Skanda;<BR>of a Dānava; of a son of Rāvaṇa, afterwards called<BR>Indra-jit, as having conquered Indra (see Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>Uttara-kāṇḍa XXXIV); of a frog; Amaranthus Po-<BR>lygonoides; the Palāśa tree, Butea Frondosa.<BR>—मे-<BR>घनाद-जित्, त्, m. ‘conqueror of Megha-nāda or<BR>Indra-jit, son of Rāvaṇa,’ an epithet of Lakṣamaṇa,<BR>the favourite brother of Rāma (the account of his<BR>fighting and killing Indra-jit is in Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>Yuddha-kāṇḍa LXVII-LXX).<BR>—मेघनाद-तीर्थ,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place on the Narmadā<BR>river.<BR>—मेघनादानुलासिन् (˚द-अन्˚), ई, m. ‘re-<BR>joicing in the rumbling of thunder-clouds,’ a peacock.<BR>—मेघ-नादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, sounding or making a<BR>noise like thunder; crying with joy at the appear-<BR>ance of clouds; (ई), m., N. of a Dānava.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>नामन्, आ, m. ‘cloud-named,’ a fragrant grass, Cy-<BR>perus Rotundus.<BR>—मेघ-निर्घोष, अस्, m. the<BR>rumbling of clouds, thunder; (अस्, आ, अम्), sounding<BR>or making a noise like thunder.<BR>—मेघ-पङ्क्ति,<BR>इस्, f. a line or succession of clouds.<BR>—मेघ-पर्-<BR>वत, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—मेघ-पाली, f.<BR>a proper N.<BR>—मेघ-पुष्प, अम्, n. ‘cloud-<BR>blossom,’ water; river-water; hail; (अस्), m., N. of<BR>one of the four horses of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मे-<BR>घ-पृष्ठ, अस्, m., N. of a son of Ghṛta-<BR>pṛṣṭha.<BR>—मेघ-प्रदीप, अस्, m., N. of a work.<BR>—मेघ-प्रवाह, अस्, m., N. of one of the<BR>attendants of Skanda.<BR>—मेघ-प्रसव, अस्, m.<BR>‘cloud-offspring,’ water.<BR>—मेघ-बद्ध, अस्, m.<BR>epithet of a particular formula.<BR>—मेघ-बल, अस्,<BR>m. a proper N.<BR>—मेघ-भगीरथ-ठक्कुर,<BR>अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मेघ-भूति, इस्, m. a<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>—मेघ-मञ्जरी, f., N. of a daughter<BR>of king Vijaya-pāla.<BR>—मेघ-मठ, अस्, m., N. of<BR>a monastery or college built by and named after<BR>Megha-vāhana.<BR>—मेघ-मण्डल, अम्, n. the<BR>sphere of the clouds, region of the clouds, firma-<BR>ment, atmosphere.<BR>—मेघ-मय, अस्, ई, अम्,<BR>formed or consisting of clouds, cloudy.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>माल, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘cloud-wreathed, cloud-capt,’<BR>crowned with clouds; (अस्), m., N. of a mountain;<BR>of a Rākṣasa; of a son of Kalki by Ramā; (आ), f. a<BR>line or succession of clouds, gathering of clouds; N.<BR>of a work by Ketali-kīrtti treating of the astrological<BR>significance of various kinds of clouds; of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attending upon Skanda.<BR>—मेघ-मालिन्, ई,<BR>इनी, इ, cloud-wreathed; (ई), m., N. of one of<BR>Skanda's attendants; of an Asura; of a king.<BR>—मे-<BR>घ-योनि, इस्, m. ‘cloud-source,’ smoke, fog.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>रव, अस्, m. ‘cloud-noise,’ thunder; (अस्, आ, अम्),<BR>thundering like a cloud; (आ), f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attending upon Skanda.<BR>—मेघ-राग, अस्,<BR>m. the musical scale Megha (being supposed capable<BR>of bringing down rain from heaven).<BR>—मेघ-राज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—मेघ-राजि, इस्, or मे-<BR>घ-राजी, f. a line of clouds.<BR>—मेघ-राव, अस्, m.<BR>‘cloud-sounding,’ a kind of water-bird.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>रेखा or मेघ-लेखा, f. a line of clouds.<BR>—१. मे-<BR>घ-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, enveloped in clouds, overcast<BR>with clouds; (आन्), m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—२. मे-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-b" target="_blank">Page0794-b+ 80</a>]<BR>घ-वत्, ind. like a cloud.<BR>—मेघ-वन, N. of<BR>an Agra-hāra named after Megha-vāhana.<BR>—मेघ-<BR>वपुस्, उस्, m. ‘cloud-form,’ a mass of clouds which<BR>appear to assume some shape.<BR>—मेघ-वर्ण, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, ‘cloud-coloured,’ having the hue of a cloud;<BR>(अस्), m., N. of a man; of a crow in the Hitopadeśa;<BR>(आ), f. the indigo plant.<BR>—मेघ-वर्त्मन्, अ, n.<BR>‘cloud-path,’ the atmosphere, sky.<BR>—मेघ-वह्नि,<BR>इस्, m. ‘cloud-fire,’ lightning.<BR>—मेघ-वासस्, आस्,<BR>आस्, अस्, ‘cloud-robed,’ clad in clouds; (आस्), m., N.<BR>of a Daitya.<BR>—मेघ-वाहन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘having<BR>clouds for a vehicle,’ riding upon the clouds; (अस्),<BR>m. an epithet of Indra; of Śiva; N. of a king; of<BR>a king of Kaśmīra; of the twenty-second Kalpa.<BR>—मेघ-वाहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, riding upon a cloud;<BR>(इनी), f., N. of one of the Mātṛs attending upon<BR>Skanda, (also read मेष-वाहिनी.)<BR>—मेघ-वितान,<BR>अस्, m., Ved. ‘cloud-canopy,’ an expanded mass of<BR>clouds, a sky overcast with clouds; (अम्), n. a par-<BR>ticular metre, four times ˘˘¯˘˘¯˘˘¯¯.<BR>—मे-<BR>घ-विस्फूर्जित, अम्, n. the rumbling of clouds,<BR>thundering; thunder; (आ), f., scil. वृत्ति, a parti-<BR>cular metre, four times ˘¯¯¯¯¯, ˘˘˘˘˘¯, ¯˘<BR>¯¯˘¯¯, (in this sense also अम्, n.)<BR>—मेघ-<BR>वृन्द, अम्, n. a mass of clouds.<BR>—मेघ-वेग,<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मेघ-वेश्मन्, अ, n. ‘cloud-<BR>abode,’ the sky, atmosphere.<BR>—मेघ-श्याम, अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, dark as a cloud.<BR>—मेघ-सख, अस्, m.<BR>‘cloud-friend,’ N. of a mountain.<BR>—मेघ-सङ्-<BR>घात, अस्, m. an assemblage or multitude of clouds.<BR>—मेघ-सन्देश, अस्, m. = मेघ-दूत, q. v.<BR>—मेघ-सन्धि, इस्, m., N. of a king of Magadha.<BR>—मेघ-सम्भव, अस्, m. ‘cloud-produced,’ N.<BR>of a Nāga.<BR>—मेघ-सार, अस्, m. ‘cloud-essence,’ a<BR>kind of camphor (= चीन-कर्पूर).<BR>—मेघ-सु-<BR>हृद्, त्, m. ‘cloud-friend,’ a peacock (described as<BR>delighting in the rainy season).<BR>—मेघ-स्तनित,<BR>अम्, n. ‘cloud-rumbling,’ thunder.<BR>—मेघस्तनि-<BR>तोद्भव (˚त-उद्˚), अस्, m. Asteracantha Longi-<BR>folia.<BR>—मेघ-स्वन, अस्, आ, अम्, ‘cloud-sounding,’<BR>loud as a (thunder) cloud; (आ), f., N. of one of the<BR>Mātṛs attending upon Skanda.<BR>—मेघ-स्वर or<BR>मेघस्वर-राज, अस्, m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—मे-<BR>घ-स्वाति, इस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मेघ-ह्राद,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, shouting or roaring like a thunder-cloud.<BR>—मेघाख्य (˚घ-आख्˚), अस्, m., N. of a Persian<BR>king, (also read मेघाक्ष; = Prākṛt mehākkho);<BR>(अम्), n. Cyperus Rotundus; talc.<BR>—मेघागम<BR>(˚घ-आग्˚), अस्, m. ‘approach of clouds,’ the rainy<BR>season.<BR>—मेघाच्छन्न or मेघाच्छादित (˚घ-<BR>आच्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, overspread with clouds, covered<BR>with clouds, clouded.<BR>—मेघाटोप (˚घ-आट्˚), अस्,<BR>m. ‘cloud-swelling,’ a dense cloud.<BR>—मेघाडम्-<BR>बर (˚घ-आड्˚), अस्, m. ‘cloud-drum,’ thunder;<BR>[cf. मेघ-डम्बर.]<BR>—मेघानन्दा (˚घ-आन्˚),<BR>f. ‘rejoicing in clouds,’ a kind of crane.<BR>—मेघा-<BR>नन्दिन् (˚घ-आन्˚), ई, m. ‘rejoicing in clouds,’ a<BR>peacock; [cf. मेघ-सुहृद्.]<BR>—मेघान्त (˚घ-<BR>अन्˚), अस्, m. ‘coming at the end of the rainy season,’<BR>the autumn.<BR>—मेघारि (˚घ-अरि), इस्, m. ‘cloud-<BR>enemy,’ the wind.<BR>—मेघावतत (˚घ-अव्˚), अस्,<BR>आ, अम्, overspread with clouds, overcast.<BR>—मेघावली<BR>(˚घ-आव्˚), f., N. of a princess.<BR>—मेघास्थि (˚घ-<BR>अस्˚), इ, n. ‘cloud-bone,’ hail.<BR>—मेघास्पद (˚घ-<BR>आस्˚), अम्, n. ‘cloud-region,’ the atmosphere, sky,<BR>ether, heaven.<BR>—मेघेश्वर-तीर्थ (˚घ-ईश्˚),<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Tīrtha on the Revā or Narmadā<BR>river.<BR>—मेघोदक (˚घ-उद्˚), अम्, n. ‘cloud-<BR>water,’ rain.<BR>—मेघोदय (˚घ-उद्˚), अस्, m.<BR>‘cloud-rising,’ rising clouds.<BR>—मेघौन्मुख्य<BR>(˚घ-औ˚), अम्, n. the act of looking up eagerly<BR>or longing for clouds (said of a peacock).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0793-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघय
मेघय, Nom. P. मेघयति, -यितुम्, to make<BR>cloudy, cause cloudy weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघयत्
मेघयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. making cloudy;<BR>(अन्ती), f., N. of one of the seven Kṛttikās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघाय
मेघाय, Nom. A. मेघायते, -यितुम्, Ved. to<BR>form clouds, become cloudy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघ्य
मेघ्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. being in the clouds;<BR>according to Pāṇ. मेघ्य at the end of a comp.<BR>= मेघम् अर्हति or मेघ इव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैघ
मैघ, अस्, ई, अम्, belonging to the clouds,<BR>cloudy; descended from clouds (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेङ्गनाथ
मेङ्गनाथ मेङ्ग-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>race (?).<BR>—मेङ्गनाथ-भट्ट, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेच
मेच मेच, अस्, m., N. of a poet; [cf. मेघ.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचक|मेचकं|मेचकः
मेचक मेचक, अस्, आ, अम् (said to be fr. rt.<BR>मच्), dark-blue, dark-coloured, black; (अस्), m.<BR>dark-blue colour, black; blackness; an eye of a<BR>peacock's tail; a teat, nipple; smoke; a cloud; Mo-<BR>ringa Pterygosperma; a kind of gem; (अम्), n.<BR>darkness; sulphuret of antimony.<BR>—मेचकापगा<BR>(˚क-अप्˚), f. ‘dark-blue river,’ an epithet of the<BR>Yamunā.<BR>—मेचकाभिधा (˚क-अभ्˚), f. a species<BR>of creeper (= पाताल-गरुडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचकचातनी
मेचकचातनी मेचकचातनी, f. a various<BR>reading for मचकचातनी, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचुरुदि
मेचुरुदि मेचुरुदि (?), N. of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेट्
मेट् मेट् (= rt. म्रेट्), cl. 1. P. मेटति,<BR>मेटितुम्, to be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेटुला
मेटुला मेटुला, f. the myrobalan tree (=<BR>आमलकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेठ|मेठः
मेठ मेठ, अस्, m. an elephant keeper [cf.<BR>मेण्ड]; an elephant driver (= यन्तृ); a ram<BR>[cf. मेढर].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेठि|मेठिः
मेठि मेठि, मेठी. See मेथि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेड्
मेड् मेड्, cl. 1. P. मेडति, &c., = rt. मेट्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेडि
मेडि मेडि or मेऌइ, इस्, m., Ved. crackling,<BR>emitting sparks, rustling (said of wind, fire, &c.);<BR>any jingling or murmuring sound; (a reading मेडवस्<BR>is given for the pl. मेडयस्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढी
मेढी मेढी, f. See मेथि below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्र|मेढ्रः
मेढ्र मेढ्र, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. मिह् + त्र;<BR>according to native lexicographers also अस्, m.), mem-<BR>brum virile, the penis; (अस्), m. a ram; [cf. मी-<BR>ढ्वस्, मेण्ढ, मेष.]<BR>—मेढ्र-चर्मन्, अ,<BR>n. or मेढ्र-त्वच्, क्, f. the fore-skin, prepuce.<BR>—मेढ्र-ज, अस्, m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मेढ्र-<BR>रोग, अस्, m. venereal disease.<BR>—मेढ्र-शृङ्गी, f.<BR>Odina Pennata (= मेष-शृङ्गी, said to be a<BR>milky plant, the fruit of which is crooked and there-<BR>fore like a ram's horn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्रक|मेढ्रकः
मेढ्रक, अस्, m. the penis; a ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ढ|मेंढ|मेंढः|मेण्ढः
मेण्ढ, अस्, m. (formed fr. मेढ्र above), a<BR>ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ढक|मेंढक|मेंढकः|मेण्ढकः
मेण्ढक, अस्, m. a ram; a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ढ्र|मेंढ्र|मेंढ्रः|मेण्ढ्रः
मेण्ढ्र, अस्, m. = मेण्ढ above; membrum<BR>virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ठ|मेंठ|मेंठः|मेण्ठः
मेण्ठ मेण्ठ, अस्, m. an elephant keeper or<BR>feeder (= मेठ); N. of a poet (= भर्तृ-मेण्-<BR>ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ड|मेंड|मेंडः|मेण्डः
मेण्ड, अस्, m. an elephant keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेतार्य
मेतार्य मेतार्य, अस्, m. (with Jainas) N. of<BR>one of the eleven Gaṇādhipas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेतृ
मेतृ मेतृ, ता, m. (fr. rt. 1. मि), Ved. one<BR>who erects a column; (but according to Sāy. on Ṛg-<BR>veda IV. 6, 2, मेता is f. and = स्थूणा, a column,<BR>pillar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथ्
मेथ् मेथ् (connected with rt. मिथ्,<BR>q. v.), cl. 1. P. A. मेथति, -ते, मेथि-<BR>तुम्, to meet; (A.) to meet one another, associate;<BR>to reproach, revile; to strike, hurt, kill; to know,<BR>understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथि|मेथिः
मेथि, इस्, m. (perhaps connected with rt. 1. मि),<BR>a pillar, post; a pillar in the middle of a threshing-<BR>floor to which oxen are bound, any central body,<BR>(also written मेधि, मेधी, मेढी, मेठि, मेठी,<BR>f.; मेढी-भूत or मेधी-भूत, forming a solid<BR>pillar or centre); a post to which cattle are tied; a<BR>prop for supporting the shafts of a carriage; (ई), f. =<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">Page0795-a+ 77</a>]<BR>मेथिका.<BR>—मेथि-ष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. standing<BR>at the post to which cattle are bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0794-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथिका
मेथिका or मेथिनी, f. a sort of grass, Trigondella<BR>Fœnum Græcum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद्
मेद् मेद् = rt. 1. मिद्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद|मेदः
मेद मेद, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मिद्), fat (=<BR>मेदस् below); a species of plant (= अलम्बुषा);<BR>a particular mixed caste (the son of a Vaideha by a<BR>Kārāvara female); N. of a serpent-demon; (आ), f.<BR>a root resembling ginger (said to be one of the<BR>eight principal medicines, used especially in cases of<BR>fever and consumption); (ई), f., see Gaṇa Gaurādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 1, 41.<BR>—मेद-ज, अस्, m. a species of<BR>bdellium (= भूमिज-गुग्गुलु).<BR>—मेद-पाट, N.<BR>of a place.<BR>—मेद-पाठ, अस्, m., N. of a branch<BR>of the Vatsa family.<BR>—मेद-भिल्ल, अस्, m., N. of a<BR>degraded tribe.<BR>—मेद-शिरस्, आस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मेदोद्भवा (˚द-उद्˚), f. = मेदा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदक|मेदकः
मेदक, अस्, m. spirituous liquor used for dis-<BR>tillation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदन
मेदन, अम्, n., Ved. the act of fattening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्
मेदस्, अस्, n. fat, marrow, lymph (as one of the<BR>seven Dhātus or constituent elements of the body,<BR>and supposed to be a serous or adipose secretion that<BR>spreads amongst the muscular or fleshy fibres, per-<BR>forming the same functions to the flesh that the<BR>marrow of the bones performs to them; in Hindū<BR>physiology its proper seat is said to be the abdomen);<BR>vigour, energy (Ved.); corpulence; excessive fatness,<BR>morbid or unnatural corpulence (= मेद-दोष); a<BR>mystical term for the letter व्; [cf. perhaps Gr. μῡε-<BR>λό-ς for μεδυλό-ς; Lat. medulla for medusla or<BR>medurla.]<BR>—मेदः-पुच्छ or मेदः-पुच्छक,<BR>अस्, m. the fat-tailed sheep.<BR>—मेदः-सार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, one in whom the Dhātu fat predominates; (आ),<BR>f. = मेदा.<BR>—मेदस्-कृत्, त्, n. ‘fat-producing,’ the<BR>body, flesh.<BR>—मेदस्-तेजस्, अस्, n. ‘strength of the<BR>Medas,’ bone.<BR>—मेदस्-पिण्ड, अस्, m. a lump of<BR>fat.<BR>—मेदस्-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. possessed of fat,<BR>fat.<BR>—मेदस्-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, ‘having Medas,’ corpu-<BR>lent, fat; robust, stout, strong.<BR>—मेदो-गण्ड, अस्, m.,<BR>Ved. a kind of fatty excrescence.<BR>—मेदो-ग्रन्थि, इस्,<BR>m. a lump or knot of fat, a fatty tumor.<BR>—मेदो-ज,<BR>अम्, n. ‘produced by Medas,’ bone.<BR>—मेदो-धरा,<BR>f. a membrane in the abdomen containing the fat,<BR>the omentum.<BR>—मेदो-ऽर्बुद, अम्, n. a fatty tumor<BR>unattended with pain.<BR>—मेदो-वती, f. = मेदा.<BR>—मेदो-वह, अम्, n. (in anatomy) a vessel con-<BR>veying fat, a lymphatic.<BR>—मेदो-वृद्धि, इस्, f.<BR>increase of fat, corpulence; enlargement of the<BR>scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिन्
मेदिन्, ई, इनी, इ, Ved. associated with another as<BR>a friend or companion [cf. मित्र]; a partner, con-<BR>federate, ally; (Sāy.) having Medas, possessing<BR>vigour or energy, = मेदसा युक्त = बलवत्; (इनी),<BR>f. the earth, land, soil, ground, landed property;<BR>spot, place [cf. युद्ध-म्˚]; Gmelina Arborea; =<BR>मेदा, q. v.; N. of a lexicon; (sometimes in comps.<BR>spelt मेदिनि.)<BR>—मेदिनी-कोष, N. of a lexicon.<BR>—मेदिनी-ज, अस्, m., Ved. ‘earth-born,’ the planet<BR>Mars.<BR>—मेदिनी-द्रव, अस्, m. dust.<BR>—मेदिनी-पति,<BR>इस्, m. ‘lord of the earth or of the country,’ a prince,<BR>king.<BR>—मेदिनीश (˚नी-ईश), अस्, m. ‘lord of the<BR>earth or of the country,’ a prince, king; (अम्), n.,<BR>scil. तन्त्र, N. of a Tantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुर|मेदुरः
मेदुर, अस्, आ, अम्, fat; smooth, soft, bland, unc-<BR>tuous; thick, dense; (with inst. or at the end of a<BR>comp.) thick with, as thick as, full of, covered with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुरित
मेदुरित, अस्, आ, अम्, thick, thickened, made<BR>dense; unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद्य
मेद्य, अस्, आ, अम्, fat; thick, consistent, (opposed<BR>to द्रव.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिनी
मेदिनी मेदिनी, f. See under मेदिन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुर|मेदुरः
मेदुर मेदुर. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्
मेध् मेध् (= rts. मिध्, मिथ्), cl. 1. P.<BR>A. मेधति, -ते, &c., to meet, associate,<BR>accompany; to hurt, kill, immolate; to revile; to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">Page0795-b+ 81</a>]<BR>understand: Caus. मेधयति, -यितुम्, to cause to<BR>understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध|मेधः
मेध, अस्, आ, अम्, one who kills or immolates;<BR>(अस्), m. (also अम्, n. in Ved.), the juice of meat,<BR>broth, nourishing or strengthening drink (Ved.);<BR>marrow (especially of the sacrificial victim), sap, pith,<BR>essence (Ved.); a sacrificial animal, victim; an animal<BR>sacrifice; an offering, oblation, sacrifice in general;<BR>N. of the reputed author of Vājasaneyi-saṃhitā, 33,<BR>92; N. of a son of Priya-vrata; see Gaṇa Pacādi<BR>to Pāṇ. III. 1, 134; (आ), f. vitality, strength, vigour,<BR>power, ability (Ved.); mental vigour or power, un-<BR>derstanding, intelligence, intellect, prudence, wisdom;<BR>retentiveness, memory; Intelligence personified as<BR>the wife of Dharma and daughter of Dakṣa; a<BR>form of Dākṣāyaṇī in Kaśmīra; a form of Saras-<BR>vatī; a symbolical expression for the letter ध्;<BR>(according to native authorities also) a sacrifice;<BR>(according to Naigh. II. 10) = धन; (आस्), f. pl.<BR>the products of the understanding, ideas, perceptions,<BR>thoughts, opinions.<BR>—मेध-ज, अस्, m. ‘sacrifice-<BR>born,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—मेध-पति, इस्, m.,<BR>Ved. ‘lord of sacrifice,’ Rudra.<BR>—मेध-साति, इस्,<BR>f., Ved. (perhaps) expression of devotion, service or<BR>worship of the gods; (according to Sāy.) the receiv-<BR>ing or giving of the oblation.<BR>—मेधा-कार, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, Ved. inspiring mental power, causing intelli-<BR>gence, bestowing wisdom.<BR>—मेधा-कृत्, त्, त्, त्,<BR>causing mental power or intelligence; (त्), m. a<BR>species of culinary plant (= सितावर).<BR>—मेधा-<BR>चक्र, अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मेधा-जनन, अस्,<BR>ई, अम्, productive of wisdom; (Ved.) N. of a rite<BR>(and of its appropriate sacred text) for producing<BR>mental and bodily strength in a new-born child or<BR>in a youth.<BR>—मेधा-जित्, त्, m. an epithet of Kātyā-<BR>yana.<BR>—मेधातिथि (˚धा-अत्˚), इस्, m., N. of a<BR>Kāṇva (author of the hymns Ṛg-veda 1. 12 — 23,<BR>VIII. 1, &c.; cf. मेध्यातिथि); of the father of<BR>Kaṇva; of a son of Manu Svāyambhuva; of one<BR>of the seven sages under Manu Sāvarṇa; of a son<BR>of Priya-vrata; of a lawyer or commentator on the<BR>Mānava-dharma-śāstra; of a river; a parrot [cf.<BR>मेधा-विन्].<BR>—मेधा-रुद्र, अस्, m. an epithet of<BR>Kālidāsa.<BR>—मेधा-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, possessing wis-<BR>dom, intelligent, wise; (अती), f. a species of plant (=<BR>महा-ज्योतिष्मती); a proper N.<BR>—मेधा-वर,<BR>अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मेधावि-ता, f. cleverness,<BR>prudence, judiciousness.<BR>—मेधा-विन्, ई, इनी, इ, pos-<BR>sessed of mental power, intelligent, intellectual, wise,<BR>judicious, endowed with sound judgment, having a<BR>good memory; (ई), m. a learned man, sage, teacher,<BR>Pandit; a parrot [cf. मेधातिथि]; an intoxicating<BR>beverage, (in this sense perhaps an error for मा-<BR>धवी); N. of a Brāhman; of a king (son of<BR>Su-naya and father of Nṛpañ-jaya); of a son of<BR>Bhavya and of a Varṣa named after him; an epithet<BR>of Vyāḍi; (इनी), f. epithet of the wife of Brahmā.<BR>—मेधा-सूक्त, अम्, n. epithet of a particular Vedic<BR>hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधयु
मेधयु, उस्, उस्, उ, Ved. full of sap or marrow,<BR>strong, powerful; (Sāy.) = सङ्ग्रामेच्छु, eager for<BR>war, or = यज्ञ-क्रमणेच्छु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधस्
मेधस्, अस्, n. = मेध, a sacrifice (Ved.); (आस्),<BR>m., N. of a son of Manu Svāyambhuva; of a son of<BR>Priya-vrata; (आस्, आस्, अस्), at the end of an adj.<BR>comp. = मेधा, intelligence, knowledge, understand-<BR>ing (e. g. आत्म-मेधस्, knowing or understanding<BR>the Supreme Spirit); [cf. अल्प-म्˚, दुर्-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधस
मेधस, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधा
मेधा. See under मेध above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधिर|मेधिरः
मेधिर, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मेधा), Ved. wise, in-<BR>telligent, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधिष्ठ|मेधिष्ठः
मेधिष्ठ, अस्, आ, अम् (superl. of मेधा-विन्),<BR>wisest, most intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधीयस्
मेधीयस्, आन्, असी, अस् (compar. of मेधा-विन्),<BR>wiser, more intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्य|मेध्यं|मेध्यः
मेध्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. मेध), full of sap,<BR>vigorous, mighty (Ved.); fresh, uninjured (Ved.);<BR>belonging to a sacrifice; fit for a sacrifice or oblation,<BR>free from blemish (as a victim); clean, purified, pure<BR>(not defiling by contact or by being eaten); = मे-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">Page0795-c+ 74</a>]<BR>धिर, wise, intelligent, (in this sense fr. मेधा;<BR>according to Pāṇ. = मेधायाम् भवः; = मेधाम्<BR>अर्हति.)<BR>—मेध्य-तम, अस्, आ, अम्, most pure,<BR>purest.<BR>—मेध्य-तर, अस्, आ, अम्, more pure,<BR>purer.<BR>—मेध्य-ता, f. or मेध्य-त्व, अम्, n.<BR>purity, (especially) ceremonial purity.<BR>—मेध्य-<BR>मन्दिर, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मेध्य-<BR>मय, अस्, ई, अम्, consisting of pure matter.<BR>—मे-<BR>ध्यातिथि (˚य-अत्˚), इस्, m., N. of a Ṛṣi (a Kāṇva<BR>and author of Ṛg-veda VIII. 1, 3-29, IX. 41-43).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधि|मेधिः
मेधि मेधि, मेधी. See मेथि, p. 794, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेना
मेना मेना, f. a woman (Ved.); the female<BR>of any animal (Ved.); speech, = वाच् (Ved.); (ac-<BR>cording to Mādhava) the sound of thunder; (accord-<BR>ing to Sāy.) N. of the daughter of Vṛṣaṇ-aśva (the<BR>latter being sometimes called Mena); N. of an<BR>Apsaras (wife of Hima-vat and mother of Pārvatī);<BR>of a river.<BR>—मेना-जा, f. ‘daughter of Menā,’ Pār-<BR>vatī.<BR>—मेना-धव, अस्, m. ‘husband of Menā,’<BR>Hima-vat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनका
मेनका, f., N. of the daughter of Vṛṣaṇ-aśva;<BR>of an Apsaras (wife of Hima-vat).<BR>—मेनकात्मजा<BR>(˚का-आत्˚), f. ‘daughter of Menakā,’ Pārvatī.<BR>—मे-<BR>नका-प्राणेश, अस्, m. ‘husband of Menakā,’ Hima-<BR>vat.<BR>—मेनका-हित, अम्, n., N. of a Rāsaka or<BR>kind of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनि
मेनि, इस्, f., Ved. a missile weapon, a thunder-<BR>bolt; a various reading for मेना, speech (Naighaṇ-<BR>ṭuka 1. 11).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनिला
मेनिला, f., N. of a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनुल
मेनुल, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाद|मेनादः
मेनाद मे-नाद, अस्, आ, अम्, making the<BR>sound मे; (अस्), m. a goat; a cat; a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनि
मेनि मेनि. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेन्धिका|मेंधिका
मेन्धिका मेन्धिका or मेन्धी, f. a plant,<BR>Lawsonia Alba (a reddish dye is extracted from its<BR>leaves, used for staining the palms of the hands, the<BR>tips and nails of the fingers, and the soles of the<BR>feet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेप्
मेप् मेप्, cl. 1. P. मेपति, मेपितुम्, to<BR>go, move; to worship (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेब्
मेब् मेब् (= rt. मेव्), cl. 1. A. मेबते,<BR>मेबितुम्, to worship, serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेम
मेम मेम, (with Buddhists) a particular<BR>high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेमिष
मेमिष मेमिष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. Intens. of<BR>rt. 1. मिष्), Ved. in अति-म्˚, opening the eyes<BR>wide, staring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेय
मेय मेय, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 3. मा), to be<BR>measured, measurable, to be spanned [cf. मुष्टि-<BR>म्˚]; capable of being estimated, discernible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरक|मेरकः
मेरक मेरक, अस्, m., N. of an enemy of<BR>Viṣṇu; a seat covered with bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरु|मेरुः
मेरु मेरु, उस्, m. (in Uṇādi-s. IV. 101,<BR>said to be fr. rt. 1. मि), N. of a fabulous mountain<BR>regarded as the Olympus of Hindū mythology, (it is<BR>said to form the central point of Jambu-dvīpa, all<BR>the planets revolving round it, and is compared to<BR>the cup or seed-vessel of a lotus, the leaves of which<BR>are formed by the different Dvīpas; its height is<BR>said to be 84, 000 Yojanas, 16, 000 of which are<BR>below the surface of the earth; its shape is variously<BR>described, as square, conical, spherical, or spiral, and<BR>its four faces are variously coloured, being white<BR>towards the east, yellow to the south, black to the<BR>west, and red to the north; the river Ganges falls<BR>from heaven on its summit, and flows thence to the<BR>surrounding worlds in four streams; the regents of<BR>the four points of the compass occupy the corres-<BR>ponding faces of the mountain, the whole of which<BR>consists of gold and gems; its summit is the resi-<BR>dence of Brahmā, and a place of meeting for the<BR>gods, Ṛṣis, Gandharvas, &c.; when not regarded<BR>as a fabulous mountain, it appears to mean the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">Page0796-a+ 79</a>]<BR>highland of Tartary north of the Himālaya); the<BR>central or most prominent bead in a rosary, large<BR>middle gem of a necklace; the most prominent<BR>finger-joint in certain positions of the fingers; N. of<BR>a Cakra-vartin; of a person mentioned in Rāja-<BR>taraṅgiṇī VIII. 1418; epithet of a particular kind<BR>of temple; N. of the palace of Gāndhārī, one of<BR>the wives of Kṛṣṇa; (उस्), f., N. of the wife of<BR>Nābhi and mother of Ṛṣabha.<BR>—मेरु-कल्प, अस्,<BR>m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—मेरु-कूट, अस्, अम्, m. n.<BR>the summit of Meru; (अस्), m., N. of a Buddha.<BR>—मेरु-तन्त्र, अम्, n., N. of a Tantra.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>तुङ्ग, अस्, m., N. of a Jaina.<BR>—मेरु-दुहितृ, ता,<BR>f. the daughter of Meru.<BR>—मेरु-दृश्वन्, आ, आ or<BR>अरी, अ, one who has seen or visited Meru.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>देवी, f., N. of a daughter of Meru (wife of Nābhi<BR>and mother of Ṛṣabha, who was an incarnation of<BR>Viṣṇu).<BR>—मेरु-धामन्, आ, m. ‘having Meru for<BR>a habitation,’ an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—मेरु-ध्वज,<BR>अस्, m., N. of a king.<BR>—मेरु-नन्द, अस्, m., N.<BR>of a son of Sva-rocis.<BR>—मेरु-पर्वत, अस्, m. the<BR>mountain Meru.<BR>—मेरु-पुत्री, f. a daughter of<BR>Meru.<BR>—मेरु-पृष्ठ, अम्, n. the summit of<BR>Meru; heaven, the sky.<BR>—मेरु-प्रभ, अस्, आ,<BR>अम्, resembling Meru; shining like Meru.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>प्रभ-वन, अम्, n., N. of a forest.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>प्रस्तार, अस्, m. a term for a representation of all<BR>the possible combinations of a metre having a fancied<BR>resemblance to mount Meru.<BR>—मेरु-बल-प्र-<BR>मर्दिन्, ई, m., N. of a king of the Yakṣas.<BR>—मेरु-भूत, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>मन्दर, अस्, m., N. of a mountain.<BR>—मेरु-म-<BR>हीभृत्, त्, m. mount Meru.<BR>—मेरु-यन्त्र, अम्,<BR>n. (in mathematics) a figure shaped like a spindle.<BR>—मेरु-वर्धन, अस्, m. a proper N.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>वर्ष, अम्, n., N. of a Varṣa.<BR>—मेरु-व्रज,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a city.<BR>—मेरु-शिखर-धर-कु-<BR>मार-भूत, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>श्री-गर्भ, अस्, m., N. of a Bodhi-sattva.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>सावर्ण, अस्, or मेरु-सावर्णि, इस्, m. a general N.<BR>for the last four of the fourteen Manus.<BR>—मेरु-<BR>सुसम्भव, अस्, m., N. of a king of the Kum-<BR>bhāṇḍas.<BR>—मेर्व्-अद्रि-कर्णिका, f. ‘having the<BR>Meru mountain for a seed-vessel,’ the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0795-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुक|मेरुकः
मेरुक, अस्, m. fragrant resin, incense; N. of a<BR>district in the north-east of Madhya-deśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुटू
मेरुटू मेरुटू, (with Buddhists) a parti-<BR>cular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुदु
मेरुदु, (with Buddhists) a particular high<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुण्डा
मेरुण्डा मेरुण्डा, f. a particular goddess,<BR>(probably incorrect for भेरुण्डा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेल|मेलः
मेल मेल, अस्, आ, m. f. (fr. rt. मिल्), meeting,<BR>coming together, union, intercourse; an assembly,<BR>company, society; (in modern dialects) a large con-<BR>course of people collected at stated periods for reli-<BR>gious or commercial purposes; a fair; (आ), f. a<BR>musical scale; (with Buddhists) a particular high<BR>number; any black substance used for writing, ink-<BR>powder, ink, (in this and the following senses pro-<BR>bably connected with Gr. μέλας); antimony, eye-<BR>salve; the indigo plant.<BR>—मेला-नन्द, अस्, आ, m. f.<BR>an ink-bottle; [cf. मेला-मन्दा below.]<BR>—मेला-<BR>नन्दाय, Nom. A. मेलानन्दायते, &c., to be-<BR>come an ink-bottle.<BR>—मेलान्धु, उस्, f. (? m.) or<BR>मेलान्धुक (˚ला-अन्˚), अस्, m. an ink-bottle.<BR>—मे-<BR>ला-मन्दा, f. an ink-bottle.<BR>—मेलाम्बु, उस्, m. an<BR>ink-bottle; (probably for मेलान्धु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलक|मेलकः
मेलक, अस्, m. meeting, union, coming together,<BR>intercourse; a congress, assembly, a company [cf.<BR>नटक-म्˚]; मेलकं कृ, to assemble together;<BR>ग्रह-मेलक, a conjunction of the planets.<BR>—मे-<BR>लक-लवण, अम्, n. a kind of salt (= मृत्तिका-<BR>लवण; cf. क्षार-मेलक, क्षार-मृत्तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलन|मेलनं
मेलन, अम्, n. the act of meeting, union, coming<BR>together, junction, assembling, associating with; an<BR>encounter; mixing with, mixture; adding to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलयत्
मेलयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत् (fr. the Caus.), causing to<BR>be mixed or added to, mixing, adding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलापक|मेलापकः
मेलापक, अस्, m. (fr. the Caus.), uniting, bring-<BR>ing together; conjunction (of planets).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलायन|मेलायनं
मेलायन, अम्, n. mixing together, combination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलु
मेलु and मेलुद, (with Buddhists) a particular<BR>high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेव्
मेव् मेव् (= rts. म्लेव्, मेब्), cl. 1. A.<BR>मेवते, मेवितुम्, to worship, serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेवाड
मेवाड मेवाड, अस्, m., N. of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेवार्य
मेवार्य मेवार्य for मेतार्य, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेशिका
मेशिका मेशिका in काल-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेशी
मेशी मेशी, f., Ved. epithet of water in a<BR>particular formula, (also read मेषी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेष|मेषः
मेष मेष, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मिष्; accord-<BR>ing to some fr. rt. 1. मिष्), a ram, wether, sheep,<BR>(in Ved. applied also to a fleece or anything woollen);<BR>the sign of the zodiac Aries, or the first arc of 30°<BR>in a circle; a kind of drug; a species of plant [cf.<BR>मेष-कुसुम, मेष-पुष्पा]; N. of a demon<BR>said to possess children; (आ), f. a kind of carda-<BR>moms; (ई), f. an ewe; Nardostachys Jatamansi;<BR>Dalbergia Ougeinensis; [cf. काल-म्˚.]<BR>—मेष-<BR>कम्बल, अस्, m. a sheep's fleece or woollen dress<BR>serving for an outer garment, a woollen rug or<BR>blanket.<BR>—मेष-कुसुम, अस्, m. Cassia Tora; [cf.<BR>मेषाक्षि-कुसुम.]<BR>—मेष-पाल or मेष-पा-<BR>लक, अस्, m. a shepherd.<BR>—मेष-पुष्पा, f. a<BR>species of plant.<BR>—मेष-मांस, अम्, n. the flesh<BR>of sheep, mutton.<BR>—मेष-यूथ, अम्, n. a flock<BR>of sheep.<BR>—मेष-लोचन, अस्, m. Cassia Tora.<BR>—मेष-वल्ली, f. Odina Pinnata.<BR>—मेष-वाहिन्,<BR>ई, इनी, इ, riding on a ram; (इनी), f., N. of one of<BR>the Mātṛs attending on Skanda, (also read मेघ-<BR>वाहिनी.)<BR>—मेष-विषाणिका, f. = मेष-शृङ्गी,<BR>q. v.<BR>—मेष-शृङ्ग, अस्, m. a species of tree<BR>(enumerated among the द्रुमाणां राजानः); a<BR>species of poisonous plant; (ई), f. Odina Pinnata.<BR>—मेष-हृत्, त्, m., N. of a son of Garuḍa, (also<BR>read मेघ-हृत्.)<BR>—मेषाक्षि-कुसुम (˚ष-<BR>अक्˚), अस्, m. Cassia Tora.<BR>—मेषाण्ड (˚ष-अण्˚),<BR>अस्, m. ‘having ram's testicles,’ an epithet of Indra.<BR>—मेषान्त्री (˚ष-अन्˚), f. a species of plant (=<BR>अजान्त्री, छगलान्त्री).<BR>—मेषालु (˚ष-आलु), उस्,<BR>m. a species of plant (= वर्वरा).<BR>—मेषाह्वय<BR>(˚ष-आह्˚), अस्, m. Cassia Tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषक|मेषकः
मेषक, अस्, m. a species of vegetable, = जीव-<BR>शाक; (इका), f. an ewe; [cf. काल-मेषिका.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषाय
मेषाय, Nom. A. मेषायते, &c., to act like a<BR>goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषायित
मेषायित, अस्, आ, अम्, acting like a ram or goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषूरण
मेषूरण मेषूरण, अम्, n. (a word bor-<BR>rowed fr. the Gr. μεσουράνημα), epithet of the<BR>tenth astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेह|मेहः
मेह मेह, अस्, m. (according to some also)<BR>अम्, n. (fr. rt. 1. मिह्), making water; urine, (मे-<BR>हं कृ, to make water; अ-मेह, retention of<BR>urine); urinary disease, excessive flow of urine, dia-<BR>betes; a ram (= मेष); a goat; [cf. Gr. μοιχός.]<BR>—मेह-घ्नी, f. ‘curing diabetes,’ Indian saffron.<BR>—मेह-हाट, N. of a place; [cf. मेद-पाट.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहत्
मेहत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, urining, passing urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहत्नू
मेहत्नू, ऊस्, f., Ved., N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहन|मेहनं|मेहनः
मेहन, अम्, n. the act of passing urine; mem-<BR>brum virile, the penis; the urinary duct; urine;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of tree, = मुष्कक; (आ), f.<BR>(according to some) = महिला, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहना
मेहना, ind., Ved. (lit. in streams), abundantly.<BR>—मेहना-वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, Ved. bestowing abun-<BR>dantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहिन्
मेहिन्, ई, इनी, इ, (at the end of comps.) making<BR>water; suffering from a particular urinary disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैघ
मैघ मैघ. See p. 794, col. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र|मैत्रं|मैत्रः
मैत्र मैत्र, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. 1. मित्र), coming<BR>or derived from a friend, given by a friend, of or<BR>belonging to a friend; friendly, amicable, well-dis-<BR>posed, kind, benevolent, affectionate; of or belonging<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">Page0796-c+ 81</a>]<BR>to the god Mitra, q. v.; (अस्), m. ‘a friend to all<BR>creatures,’ a Brāhman who has arrived at the highest<BR>state of human perfection; a particular mixed caste<BR>or degraded tribe (the offspring of an outcast<BR>Vaiśya, Manu X. 23; cf. मैत्रेयक); scil. सन्-<BR>धि, an alliance grounded on good-will; epithet of<BR>the twelfth astrological Yoga; the anus, fundament;<BR>a man's N. much used in grammatical examples [cf.<BR>चैत्र and the Latin Caius]; N. of a preceptor;<BR>(ई), f. (according to native authorities f. of मैत्र्य),<BR>friendship, friendliness, good-will, (in the Buddhist<BR>system) universal charity, love; friendship for, good-<BR>will towards (with loc.); association, intimate con-<BR>nection, union, contact; Benevolence personified<BR>(daughter of Dakṣa and wife of Dharma); the<BR>Nakṣatra Anu-rādhā; (अम्), n. friendship; the<BR>Nakṣatra Anu-rādhā presided over by Mitra; a<BR>prayer addressed to Mitra early in the morning;<BR>evacuation of excrement presided over by Mitra,<BR>(मैत्रं कृ, to discharge excrement, see Manu<BR>IV. 152); N. of a Sūtra work; (in Ved. said to be)<BR>= 1. मित्र, a friend.<BR>—मैत्र-कन्यक, अस्, m. a<BR>proper N.<BR>—मैत्र-ता, f. friendship, friendliness,<BR>benevolence, kindness.<BR>—मैत्र-भ, अम्, n., N.<BR>of the Nakṣatra Anu-rādhā.<BR>—मैत्र-शाखा, f.,<BR>N. of a school.<BR>—मैत्र-सूत्र, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Sūtra work.<BR>—मैत्राक्ष-ज्योतिक (˚र-अक्˚), अस्,<BR>m., N. of a particular class of evil beings or demons<BR>who feed on purulent carcases (Manu XII. 72).<BR>—मैत्री-नाथ, अस्, m., N. of an author.<BR>—मैत्री-<BR>पूर्व, अस्, आ, अम्, preceded by friendship.<BR>—मैत्री-<BR>बल, अस्, आ, अम्, whose strength is benevolence;<BR>(अस्), m. epithet of a Buddha; N. of a king (re-<BR>garded as an incarnation of Śākya-muni).<BR>—मैत्री-<BR>भाव, अस्, m. state of friendliness, friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रक|मैत्रकं
मैत्रक, अम्, n. friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रवर्धक
मैत्रवर्धक (fr. मित्र-वर्ध; also read<BR>मैत्रवर्ध्रक, fr. मित्र-वर्ध्र), see Gaṇa<BR>Dhūmādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्राबार्हस्पत्य
मैत्राबार्हस्पत्य, Ved. belonging or pertain-<BR>ing to Mitra and Bṛhas-pati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रायण
मैत्रायण, अम्, n. (fr. मैत्र + अयन), be-<BR>nevolence; (अस्), m. a patronymic, see Gaṇa Naḍādi<BR>to Pāṇ. IV. 1. 89, (in this sense fr. 1. मित्र); N.<BR>of the author of a Gṛhya-sūtra; (आस्), m. pl., N. of<BR>a school (named after Maitri); (ई), f., N. of the<BR>mother of Pūrṇa; of a female teacher.<BR>—मैत्रा-<BR>यण-गृह्य-पद्धति, इस्, f., N. of a work by<BR>Prathama-puruṣa on the sixteen Saṃskāras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रायणक
मैत्रायणक, see Gaṇa Arīhaṇāid to Pāṇ. IV.<BR>2, 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रायणि
मैत्रायणि or मैत्रायणी, N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रायणीय
मैत्रायणीय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a school.<BR>—मै-<BR>त्रायणीय-परिशिष्ट, अम्, n., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रायण्य
मैत्रायण्य, अस्, m. a patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुण|मैत्रावरुणः
मैत्रावरुण, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. descended or<BR>derived from Mitra and Varuṇa, of or belonging to<BR>them; (अस्), m. a patronymic (see Ṛg-veda VII.<BR>33, 11); of Agastya; of Vālmīki; epithet of one of<BR>the officiating priests (the first assistant of the Hotṛ,<BR>who was also called Pra-śāstṛ; cf. कोकिल-म्˚).<BR>—मैत्रावरुण-श्रुति, इस्, f., N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुणि|मैत्रावरुणिः
मैत्रावरुणि, इस्, m. the son of Mitra and<BR>Varuṇa, a patronymic of Mānya or Agastya; of<BR>Vasiṣṭha; of Vālmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुणीय
मैत्रावरुणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. relating to<BR>the Maitrāvaruṇa Ṛtvij; (अम्), n. the office of the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रि
मैत्रि, इस्, m., Ved., N. of a teacher (from whom<BR>the Maitry-upaniṣad derives its title).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रिक
मैत्रिक, अम्, n. (fr. 1. मित्र or मैत्र), a<BR>friendly office, (used at the end of an adj. comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रिन्
मैत्रिन्, ई, इणी, इ (fr. मैत्र), friendly, benevo-<BR>lent, a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेय|मैत्रेयः
मैत्रेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मैत्री), friendly, re-<BR>lating to a friend, benevolent; (अस्), m. (fr. मि-<BR>त्रयु), a patronymic of Kauṣārava; of Glāva,<BR>(according to a Scholiast a metronymic fr. मित्रा);<BR>N. of a Bodhi-sattva and future Buddha; of the<BR>Vidūṣaka in the Mṛc-chakaṭikā; of a grammarian<BR>(= मैत्रेय-रक्षित); a particular mixed caste,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">Page0797-a+ 74</a>]<BR>= मैत्रेयक; (ई), f., N. of an Upaniṣad (pro-<BR>bably as composed by Maitri); of the wife of Yājña-<BR>valkya; of certain other women.<BR>—मैत्रेय-रक्-<BR>षित, अस्, m., N. of a grammarian.<BR>—मैत्रेय-<BR>वन, अम्, n., N. of a forest.<BR>—मैत्रेय-सूत्र,<BR>अम्, n., N. of a Sūtra work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0796-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेयक|मैत्रेयकः
मैत्रेयक, अस्, m., N. of a particular mixed<BR>caste or degraded tribe (the offspring of a Vaideha<BR>father by an Ayogavī, whose business is to praise<BR>great men and announce the dawn by ringing a bell,<BR>Manu X. 33); (इका), f. descent from Mitrayu;<BR>a contest between friends or allies (= मित्र-युद्-<BR>ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र्य|मैत्र्यं
मैत्र्य, अम्, n. friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथिल|मैथिलः
मैथिल मैथिल, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or be-<BR>longing to Mithilā; (अस्), m. a king of Mithilā;<BR>(आस्), m. pl. the people of Mithilā; (ई), f. an epithet<BR>of Sītā (daughter of Janaka, king of Mithilā).<BR>—मै-<BR>थिल-वाचस्-पति, इस्, m. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथिलिक
मैथिलिक, आस्, m. pl. the inhabitants of Mithilā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथिलेय
मैथिलेय, अस्, m. a metronymic from Maithilī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुन|मैथुनं
मैथुन मैथुन, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मिथुन),<BR>paired, coupled, forming a pair or one of each sex;<BR>united by marriage; relating or belonging to copu-<BR>lation, (मैथुनं वासस्, a garment worn during<BR>sexual intercourse); entered into (as a marriage)<BR>for the sake of cohabitation; (अम्), n. copulation,<BR>coitus, sexual intercourse or connection; union, con-<BR>nection; marriage, matrimony, (at the end of an<BR>adj. comp. मैथुन forms its fem. in आ.)<BR>—मै-<BR>थुन-गत, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged in copulation.<BR>—मैथुन-ज्वर, अस्, m. the excitement of sexual<BR>passion.<BR>—मैथुन-धर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, cohabiting,<BR>copulating.<BR>—मैथुन-वैराग्य, अम्, n. abstinence<BR>from sexual indulgence.<BR>—मैथुनी-भाव, अस्, m.<BR>(fr. मैथुनी-भू), copulation, sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुनिक
मैथुनिक (at the end of a comp.) = मैथु-<BR>निन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुनिका
मैथुनिका, f. union by marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुनिन्
मैथुनिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having sexual intercourse,<BR>sexually united; (ई), m. one who has had sexual<BR>connection with a woman; Ardea Sibirica, [cf.<BR>कामिन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुन्य
मैथुन्य, अस्, आ or -नी (?), अम्, proceeding<BR>from sexual passion, caused by the desire for sexual<BR>union; relating to copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैधातिथ
मैधातिथ मैधातिथ, अस्, ई, अम्, Ved. re-<BR>lating to Medhātithi; (अम्), n., N. of a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैधाव
मैधाव, अस्, m. (fr. मेधा-विन्), the son of<BR>a wise man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैधावक|मैधावकं
मैधावक, अम्, n. (fr. मेधा-विन्), intelli-<BR>gence, prudence, wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैध्यातिथ
मैध्यातिथ, अम्, n. (fr. मेध्यातिथि), N. of<BR>a Sāman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाक|मैनाकः
मैनाक मैनाक, अस्, m. (fr. मेना), N. of a<BR>mountain (son of Hima-vat by Menā or Menakā,<BR>and said to have alone retained his wings when Indra<BR>clipped those of the other mountains; according to<BR>some this mountain was situated between the southern<BR>point of the Indian peninsula and Laṅkā); N. of a<BR>Daitya.<BR>—मैनाक-स्वसृ, सा, f. ‘sister of Maināka,’<BR>an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाल|मैनालः
मैनाल मैनाल or मैनिक, अस्, m. (fr.<BR>मीन), a fisher, fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनेय
मैनेय मैनेय, आस्, m. pl., N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्द|मैंद|मैंदः|मैन्दः
मैन्द मैन्द, अस्, m., N. of an ape or<BR>monkey-demon killed by Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—मैन्द-मर्-<BR>दन, अस्, or मैन्द-हन्, हा, m. ‘killer of<BR>Mainda,’ an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैमत
मैमत मैमत and मैमतायन, अस्, and<BR>मैमतायनि, इस्, m. (fr. मिमत), patronymics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरव
मैरव मैरव, अस्, ई, अम्, relating or be-<BR>longing to mount Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरावण
मैरावण मैरावण, अस्, m., N. of an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरेय|मैरेयं|मैरेयः
मैरेय मैरेय, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according to<BR>the lexicographers only अम्, n.), a kind of intoxi-<BR>cating drink (extracted from the blossoms of the<BR>Lythrum Fructicosum, with sugar, &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरेयक|मैरेयकं|मैरेयकः
मैरेयक, अस्, अम्, m. n. = मैरेय above;<BR>(आस्), m. pl., N. of a mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैलिन्द|मैलिंद|मैलिंदः|मैलिन्दः
मैलिन्द मैलिन्द, अस्, m. a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैश्रधान्य
मैश्रधान्य मैश्रधान्य, अम्, n. (fr. मिश्र-<BR>धान्य), a dish prepared by mixing various kinds<BR>of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैहिक
मैहिक मैहिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मेह), relat-<BR>ing to urinary disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मो
मो मो (मा + उ), Ved. and not, nor, not<BR>indeed (see under 1. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक|मोकं
मोक मोक, अम्, n. (fr. rt. 2. मुच्), the cast-<BR>off skin of an animal [cf. निर्-म्˚]; (ई), f., Ved. night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तव्य
मोक्तव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be set free or released<BR>or liberated; to be let go or given up or delivered;<BR>to be flung or hurled, to be wielded, to be sent (as<BR>a missile).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तुकाम
मोक्तु-काम, अस्, आ, अम्, wishing to let go, de-<BR>siring to shoot or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तृ
मोक्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, a releaser, liberator, deliverer,<BR>rescuer, saviour; one who pays or discharges (a debt),<BR>a payer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष्
मोक्ष् मोक्ष्, cl. 1. P. A. मोक्षति, -ते<BR>(more properly to be regarded as an<BR>anomalous Desid. fr. rt. 2. मुच्), to set free, liberate;<BR>to free one's self from or wish to do so (A.); cl. 10.<BR>P. (ep. also A.) मोक्षयति (-यते), -यितुम् (perhaps<BR>to be regarded as a Nom. fr. मोक्ष below), to free,<BR>set free, set at liberty, liberate, emancipate; to set<BR>free from (with abl.); to detach, extract; to loose,<BR>untie, undo; to wrest away, wrest from (with abl.);<BR>to shed, cause to flow; to cast, hurl, fling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमोक्षयिषु
मुमोक्षयिषु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid.),<BR>wishing to set free, desiring to liberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष|मोक्षः
मोक्ष, अस्, m. emancipation, deliverance, free-<BR>dom, liberation, escape, release; release from worldly<BR>existence, final emancipation, eternal bliss resulting<BR>from the soul's final liberation and its exemption from<BR>further transmigration; death; epithet of particular<BR>sacred hymns conducive to final emancipation; de-<BR>livery, discharge; the act of loosing, loosening,<BR>untying, unbinding, undoing, solving, (प्रश्न-म्˚,<BR>the settling of a question); acquittance of an obli-<BR>gation; (in astronomy) the liberation of an obscured<BR>planet, end of an eclipse, the last contact or separa-<BR>tion of the eclipsed and eclipsing bodies; shedding,<BR>causing to flow; the act of discharging, casting,<BR>flinging, shooting; strewing, scattering; separating,<BR>falling off, falling down; a species of tree (=<BR>मुष्कक).<BR>—मोक्ष-काङ्क्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, de-<BR>sirous of liberation or final emancipation.<BR>—मोक्ष-<BR>क्रिया-समाचार, अस्, आ, अम्, affording a method<BR>for effecting liberation.<BR>—मोक्ष-ज्ञान, अम्, n.<BR>knowledge of the beatitude attained through final<BR>emancipation.<BR>—मोक्ष-तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a<BR>Tīrtha.<BR>—मोक्ष-दा, f., N. of a female ascetic.<BR>—मोक्ष-देव, अस्, m. an epithet applied to<BR>Hiouen-thsang.<BR>—मोक्ष-द्वार, अम्, n. ‘gate of<BR>emancipation,’ an epithet of the sun.<BR>—मोक्ष-<BR>धर्म, अस्, m. law or rule of emancipation.<BR>—मोक्षधर्म-पर्वन्, अ, n. ‘section relating<BR>to the law or rules of emancipation,’ N. of a section<BR>of the twelfth book of the Mahā-bhārata, from<BR>Adhyāya 174 to the end.<BR>—मोक्षधर्मार्थ-<BR>दीपिका (˚म-अर्˚), f., N. of a commentary on the<BR>preceding section of the Mahā-bhārata.<BR>—मोक्ष-<BR>पुरी, f. ‘city of emancipation,’ an epithet of the<BR>city of Kāñcī.<BR>—मोक्ष-भाज्, क्, क्, क्, receiving<BR>final emancipation.<BR>—मोक्ष-महा-परिषद्, त्, f.<BR>‘great emancipation-assembly,’ the great Buddhist<BR>general council.<BR>—मोक्ष-मार्ग, अस्, m. ‘path of<BR>emancipation,’ N. of a Jaina work.<BR>—मोक्ष-<BR>लक्ष्मी-विलास, अस्, m., N. of a temple.<BR>—मोक्ष-<BR>वत्, आन्, अती, अत्, having final emancipation, con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">Page0797-c+ 79</a>]<BR>nected with eternal bliss.<BR>—मोक्ष-विंशक, अम्, n.<BR>‘twenty verses on emancipation,’ epithet of the verses<BR>Hari-vaṃśa 14348 sqq.<BR>—मोक्ष-शास्त्र, अम्, n.<BR>the doctrine of final emancipation.<BR>—मोक्ष-सा-<BR>धन, अम्, n. means of emancipation.<BR>—मोक्षान्-<BR>तरङ्-ग (˚ष-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, nearest or next<BR>to final emancipation.<BR>—मोक्षोपाय (˚ष-उप्˚),<BR>अस्, m. means of emancipation; a sage, saint, de-<BR>votee (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षक|मोक्षकः
मोक्षक, अस्, इका, अम्, (at the end of a comp.)<BR>setting at liberty, freeing, delivering, emancipating;<BR>(अस्), m. a species of tree; one who looses or unties<BR>or sets free, a deliverer, liberator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षण|मोक्षणं
मोक्षण, अस्, ई, अम्, liberating, emancipating;<BR>(अम्), n. the act of loosing, loosening; emancipa-<BR>tion, releasing, rescuing, setting at liberty, liberation;<BR>letting go, giving up, resigning, abandoning, desert-<BR>ing; squandering; shedding, causing to flow; [cf.<BR>रक्त-म्˚.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षणीय
मोक्षणीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be let go or liberated,<BR>to be given up or resigned, to be disregarded or<BR>neglected, (अ-मोक्षणीय, inevitable.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षमाण
मोक्षमाण, अस्, आ, अम्, setting free, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षयत्
मोक्षयत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, setting free, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षयितृ
मोक्षयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who frees or libe-<BR>rates, a liberator, emancipator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षाय
मोक्षाय, Nom. A. मोक्षायते, -यितुम्, to<BR>become emancipated, tend to emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षित
मोक्षित, अस्, आ, अम्, set free, let go, liberated,<BR>allowed to be at large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षिन्
मोक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, striving after emancipation;<BR>emancipated, redeemed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष्य
मोक्ष्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be set free or liberated;<BR>to be saved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोग|मोगः
मोग मोग, अस्, m. the chicken-pox or<BR>some similar disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघ|मोघं|मोघः
मोघ मोघ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. मुह्),<BR>vain, useless, aimless, fruitless, unprofitable, (अमो-<BR>घातिथि, a guest who does not come causelessly or<BR>uselessly); left, abandoned; idle; (अस्), m. an en-<BR>closure, hedge, fence; (आ), f. the trumpet flower,<BR>Bignonia Suaveolens; a species of plant, the seeds of<BR>which are used as a vermifuge, = विडङ्ग; (अम्), ind.<BR>in vain, uselessly.<BR>—मोघ-कर्मन्, आ, आ, अ, one<BR>whose actions are fruitless or unavailing, observing<BR>useless ceremonies.<BR>—मोघ-ज्ञान, अस्, आ, अम्, one<BR>whose knowledge is useless or unavailing, cultivating<BR>any but religious wisdom.<BR>—मोघ-ता, f. vainness,<BR>uselessness, aimlessness, erringness, (अ-मोघतया<BR>युतम् अस्त्रम्, a weapon endowed with unerring-<BR>ness, Kirātārj. VI. 40); idleness.<BR>—मोघ-पुष्पा,<BR>f. a barren woman.<BR>—मोघ-हासिन्, ई, इनी, इ, laugh-<BR>ing without any cause or occasion.<BR>—मोघाश<BR>(˚घ-आश्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, one whose hopes are vain.<BR>—मोघी-कृ, cl. 8. P. -करोति, -कर्तुम्, to make<BR>vain, render useless, foil, frustrate, baffle, disappoint.<BR>—मोघी-भू, cl. 1. P. -भवति, -भवितुम्, to<BR>become useless or aimless, be foiled.<BR>—मोघी-भूत,<BR>अस्, आ, अम्, become useless, rendered vain, foiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघोलि|मोघोलिः
मोघोलि, इस्, m. an enclosure, hedge, fence; [cf.<BR>मोघ above.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच|मोचं|मोचः
मोच मोच, अस्, m. (fr. rt. 2. मुच्), Mo-<BR>ringa Pterygosperma; (probably) the plantain tree,<BR>Musa Sapientum; (आ), f. Musa Sapientum (= क-<BR>दली, रम्भा); the cotton shrub; the indigo plant;<BR>(ई), f. Hingtscha Repens [cf. हिल-मोची]; (अम्), n. a<BR>plantain, banana (the fruit).<BR>—मोच-निर्यास or मो-<BR>च-रस or मोच-सार or मोच-स्राव, अस्, or मोच-<BR>स्रुत्, त्, m. the resin of Gossampinus Ramphii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचक|मोचकः
मोचक, अस्, इका, अम् (fr. Caus. of rt. 2. मुच्),<BR>liberating, emancipating; (अस्), m. a liberator, one<BR>who has abandoned all worldly passion and desire,<BR>an ascetic, devotee; Moringa Pterygosperma; the<BR>plantain tree, Musa Sapientum; (इका), f. Musa<BR>Sapientum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचन|मोचनं
मोचन, अस्, ई, अम्, releasing, freeing from;<BR>casting, darting; (ई), f. a species of plant, = कण्ट-<BR>कारी; (अम्), n. the act of releasing, liberating,<BR>liberation, emancipation, setting free, loosing, (ऋण-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">Page0798-a+ 76</a>]<BR>मोचन, the releasing from a debt, paying a debt<BR>for any one); the act of unyoking, unharnessing;<BR>letting loose, discharging, emitting.<BR>—मोचन-पट्-<BR>टक, ‘clearing-cloth,’ a filter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0797-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचनिका
मोचनिका, f. a proper N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचनीय
मोचनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be released or set free,<BR>to be let loose; to be resigned or given up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचयितव्य
मोचयितव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be set free or re-<BR>leased, (sometimes with inst. of the thing from which<BR>there is release); capable of being set at liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचयितृ
मोचयितृ, ता, त्री, तृ, freeing, setting free, re-<BR>leasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचयित्वा
मोचयित्वा, ind. having freed or loosed, having<BR>unharnessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचाट|मोचाटः
मोचाट, अस्, m. the pith or heart of the banana<BR>tree; the fruit of the banana; a kind of pungent<BR>seed, Nigella Indica; sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचि
मोचि in हिल-म्˚, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचित
मोचित, अस्, आ, अम्, caused to be released, set at<BR>liberty, emancipated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचिन्
मोचिन्, ई, इनी, इ, setting free, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच्य
मोच्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be set free or released; to<BR>be given up or restored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचिक|मोचिकः
मोचिक मोचिक, अस्, m. a leather manu-<BR>facturer, shoe-maker, &c.; [cf. Hindī موچي]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटक|मोटकं|मोटकः
मोटक मोटक, अस्, अम्, m. n. (fr. rt. मुट्),<BR>a globule, pill; मोटकं नेत्र-रोगाणाम्, a pill to<BR>be used as a remedy against ophthalmia; (अस्), m.,<BR>N. of an author; (ई), f., N. of a Rāgiṇī; (अम्), n.<BR>a broken or crushed leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MW72&page=0798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mw72" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटन|मोटनं|मोटनः
